export const STREAMS = ["MFA press conferences (LECTERN v2)", "MND press conferences and statements (LECTERN v2)", "TAO press conferences and statements (LECTERN v2)"];
export const STATEMENTS = [[0,"2015-01-05","Hua Chunying","","The Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the US held a flag-raising ceremony on the New Year's Day. What is China's comment on that?","We are resolutely opposed to the so-called flag-raising ceremony staged by Taiwan's office in the US, and have lodged solemn representations with the American side. The Chinese side requests the American side to adhere to the one-China policy and the principles established by the three China-US joint communiqués, act with discretion when dealing with Taiwan-related issues and avoid the recurrence of similar incident.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1225723.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-01-06","Hong Lei","","DPRK's Supreme Leader Kim Jong-un said in his New Year's address that the DPRK and the ROK should actively engage in dialogue, negotiation and communication, and that the DPRK can resume stalled high-level meetings if the ROK authorities sincerely want to improve relations through talks. ROK President Park Geun-hye reportedly said on January 2 that the ROK government will take concrete steps to prepare for the…","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the liberation of the Korean Peninsula. At the outset of the New Year, the DPRK and the ROK conveyed to each other positive messages concerning bilateral relations. The Chinese side welcomes that. As a close neighbor to the Korean Peninsula, the Chinese side always supports the DPRK and the ROK in improving relations through dialogue and advancing reconciliation and cooperation so as to achieve peaceful reunification with their own efforts. It is hoped that under the current circumstances, both parties can have larger interests in mind, seize the opportunity, take concrete measures and work hard to improve bilateral relations and safeguard regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1225965.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the first press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office in 2015. I wish you all good health, smooth work, and all the best in the new year. Now I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Regarding the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council launching joint research on connecting the common economic development of the two sides with regional economic cooperation, is there any new progress recently? In addition, the by-election for chairperson of the Kuomintang will be held this weekend. May I ask whether the mainland side has any expectations for the incoming Kuomintang chairperson?","On the first question, for some time now, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council have maintained close communication on the preparatory work for launching joint research on linking the co-development of cross-Strait economies with regional economic cooperation. There will be further news soon.\nOn the second question, since 2008, through the joint efforts of the Kuomintang (KMT) and the Communist Party of China and of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and on the common political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations have opened a new chapter of peaceful development. This has brought stability to the Taiwan Strait area and well-being to people on both sides, and has won unanimous affirmation from compatriots on both sides and the international community. We hope that once the new chairperson of the Kuomintang is smoothly elected, both sides can consolidate the existing political foundation, maintain positive interaction, move in the same direction, and continue to work for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","I have two questions. First, please introduce the basic situation and main characteristics of cross-Strait economic cooperation and exchanges in 2014. Second, more and more Taiwan media are purchasing mainland variety show copyrights, and more and more Taiwan entertainers and ordinary people are appearing on mainland variety shows. How does the spokesperson evaluate the vibrant cross-Strait exchanges taking place…","On the first question: at the last press conference, the spokesperson already introduced to everyone the overall situation of cross-Strait relations in 2014. Here I would like to introduce the basic situation and main features of cross-Strait economic cooperation in 2014.\nOver the past year, cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation continued to deepen, mainly reflected in the following points:\nFirst, cross-Strait bilateral trade grew steadily. In 2014, cross-Strait trade totaled US$198.31 billion, an increase of 0.6% over 2013. Of this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$46.28 billion, and imports from Taiwan were US$152.03 billion. The mainland's trade deficit with Taiwan reached US$105.77 billion.\nSecond, the results of cross-Strait economic cooperation benefiting people's livelihoods became more evident. The total number of regular cross-Strait passenger flights rose from 828 to 840 per week, and the total number of cargo flights rose from 68 to 84 per week. The number of mainland passenger destinations increased to 55, and the number of cargo destinations increased to 10. The cross-Strait customs electronic information exchange system went online, greatly improving the efficiency of cross-Strait customs clearance. The proportion of renminbi settlement in cross-Strait trade gradually increased, and Taiwan financial institutions continued to add branches on the mainland, bringing more convenience to cross-Strait enterprises and people.\nThird, cross-Strait industrial cooperation deepened further. The seven industrial cooperation working groups of the Cross-Strait CEO Summit made positive progress in their respective fields, and pilot industrial cooperation projects achieved new results. The Cross-Strait Forum on Information Industry and Technology Standards has so far reached 288 points of consensus across nine industrial fields and published 31 cross-Strait common standards.\nFourth, the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation continued to advance. Follow-up consultations under the ECFA, including on goods trade and dispute settlement agreements, continued. The two sides signed the “Cross-Strait Meteorological Cooperation Agreement” and the “Cross-Strait Earthquake Monitoring Cooperation Agreement,” have begun consultations on transit for mainland tourists, and communicated further on matters that make exchanges between people on both sides more convenient. The competent authorities of both sides reached consensus on promoting negotiations on an environmental protection cooperation agreement and an agreement on civil aviation flight standards and airworthiness cooperation. On food safety, which compatriots on both sides care about, relevant authorities on both sides have maintained exchanges and communication.\nFifth, cross-Strait agricultural cooperation continued to deepen. The mainland actively brought the role of the market into play and introduced convenient customs clearance and inspection and quarantine measures, promoting wider sales channels for Taiwan agricultural products on the mainland and improving trade facilitation.\nWe hope that in the new year, cross-Strait economic cooperation will continue to expand and deepen, achieve more results, and that more compatriots on both sides will become participants in, promoters of, and beneficiaries of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation.\nOn the second question: I have also noted the recent cross-Strait exchange of variety shows. Their leading role in modern cultural fashion, and their depiction of the lifestyles and aesthetic preferences of contemporary compatriots on both sides, are notable. I think the reason this phenomenon has become so popular on both sides is that we are all Chinese people, sharing a common way of thinking, common culture, and common aesthetic tastes. We also hope that such platforms can continue to serve as important channels for communication, exchange, mutual understanding, and mutual trust between compatriots on both sides, especially young people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697460.htm"],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","I have two questions. First, as avian influenza continues to spread in Taiwan, can the two sides establish a joint prevention and control mechanism for avian influenza? Second, according to Taiwan media reports, Tsai Ing-wen will restart the “Committee on China Affairs” to explore changes in the cross-Strait situation. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","First question: the two sides have signed a medical and health cooperation agreement, and recently the liaison windows of both sides have been in close contact regarding the avian influenza outbreak in Taiwan. According to our understanding from the competent business authorities, the mainland has not recently imported poultry or livestock products from Taiwan. Relevant parties will implement the cross-strait agreements and make every effort to properly carry out prevention and control management, safeguarding the health rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond question: as everyone knows, our policy toward the DPP is very clear, and our position of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is also very clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","The Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone was announced to launch at the end of last year. Will there be investment-facilitation policies for Taiwan businesses in 2015?","The spokesperson already gave a brief introduction to the relevant situation at the last press conference; for specifics, you may further inquire with the Fujian provincial authorities. Recently, the State Council issued a notice requiring the promotion of the replicable reform and innovation achievements of the Shanghai Pilot Free Trade Zone. This will help promote the orderly and free flow of cross-Strait factors, the efficient allocation of resources, and the deep integration of markets. It will bring more convenience and more business opportunities to market participants, including Taiwan businesses, in investment management, trade supervision, financial innovation, and in-process and ex-post supervision, thereby providing new opportunities for deepening cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","On January 12, the Civil Aviation Administration of China announced that new air routes would be opened, but relevant Taiwan authorities believe this may threaten Taiwan's air defense security. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Last night, in response to a question from a Taiwanese reporter, a spokesperson for the National Civil Aviation Administration of China explained the relevant situation regarding the CAAC announcement on January 12 that the southeast coast maritime flight route would be put into use starting March 5 this year. Some reporters may not yet have seen it, so I would like to brief you on the relevant content here. The CAAC spokesperson said in response to questions: The southeast coast maritime flight route (M503 route) about to be put into operation is a routine task of mainland civil aviation airspace management. In 2007, it completed the design and evaluation of this route in cooperation with aviation experts from the United States and other countries, and it was approved by the International Civil Aviation Organization. The operational precision, safety and reliability of this route conform to international standards, and air traffic control departments have formulated relevant operational technical measures and emergency response procedures. Its three connecting lines are necessary passages connecting the M503 route with the departure and arrival routes of three coastal cities on the mainland. During actual operation, air traffic control departments will strengthen communication with adjacent control areas to fully guarantee operational safety. In an emergency, aircraft will be kept to the west of the route and will not deviate eastward.\nThis route is located within the Shanghai Flight Information Region on the mainland. Once opened, it will mainly be used to ease the pressure of rapid growth in flights in the Shanghai area and the Pearl River Delta, to be used in pairs with the A470 route, to improve flight safety, reduce flight delays, protect passenger rights and interests, and meet the needs of air transport development in the Asia-Pacific region. It is in line with the overall interests of all parties.\nThe CAAC spokesperson also said that cross-Strait civil aviation has always maintained smooth communication channels. Previously, at the request of the Taiwan side, both sides had held two rounds of communication on this route. In future operations, we will continue to maintain good communication and cooperation to jointly safeguard the achievements of cross-Strait air transport development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697439.htm"],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","My two questions both relate to the new air route. First, the mainland's Civil Aviation Administration emphasized that in emergency situations, aircraft will be kept to the west of the route and will not deviate eastward. What emergency situations might these include? Since they are emergencies, how can it be technically ensured that the route will not deviate? Second, the main reason Taiwan's side gives for…","Your first question involves some very specific technical matters, so please direct it to the competent aviation authorities.\nSecond, according to the information from the Civil Aviation Administration that I just quoted, this new route lies within the Shanghai Flight Information Region of the mainland, and managing it is a routine part of mainland airspace management. Its opening is indeed necessary for the economic development of the mainland and the development of its civil aviation. From a professional and economic perspective, if everyone puts themselves in others' shoes, this should be understandable. Therefore, we also hope that Taiwan society will have a bit more understanding and a bit less suspicion. As for whether both sides can continue to communicate, the relevant explanation just now made clear that the two sides have already conducted two rounds of communication, and communication will continue during future operations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The leaders of the two cross-Strait associations held a formal round of talks last year. Will new agreements be signed in cross-Strait association negotiations in 2015?","In February last year, the Tenth Round of Talks between the two associations planned several topics for the next round of consultations between both sides. As I understand it, the discussions on these topics are continuing. As for the specific time, location and arrangements for the leaders’ meeting of the two associations this year, these should be determined by the associations through consultation, based on progress in the business consultations on these topics. We can optimistically expect that new agreements should be signed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","You mentioned that cross-Strait industrial cooperation has achieved many results in recent years. Please introduce what plans there are this year for bridging cross-Strait industries.","Since 2008, the bridge-building meetings organized by relevant cross-Strait industry associations, with broad participation from enterprises, have played a positive role in advancing cross-Strait industrial cooperation. In the new year, both sides have agreed to hold bridge-building meetings in industry fields including communications, displays, vehicles, LED, renewable energy, biomedicine and pharmaceuticals, exhibition services, and e-commerce, to advance and expand cross-Strait industrial exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697432.htm"],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","On January 1 of this year, the Taiwan Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States held a flag-raising ceremony. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already made a statement on this. The Taiwan Affairs Office has also conveyed our position and attitude to the Taiwan side. We firmly oppose any words or deeds that violate the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Cross-Strait personnel exchanges remained active throughout 2014. Please introduce the basic situation of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions in 2014.","Overall, cross-Strait personnel exchanges and various forms of exchange showed good momentum last year, and the situation of large-scale cross-Strait exchanges continued to consolidate and develop. This is mainly reflected in three aspects:\nFirst, the scale of cross-Strait personnel exchanges continued to expand. Throughout the year, the total number of cross-Strait personnel exchanges was 9.411 million person-times, up 16.52% year on year, again hitting a historic high. Among them, 5.366 million person-times were Taiwan residents coming to the mainland, and 4.046 million person-times were mainland residents traveling to Taiwan. Mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism reached 3.22 million person-times, up 47% year on year.\nSecond, platforms for exchanges between cross-Strait youth and grassroots people continued to increase. Cross-Strait youth exchanges flourished, and inter-university and student exchanges expanded and deepened. The 6th Straits Forum focused on creating a series of cross-Strait grassroots exchange platforms, such as the Cross-Strait Community Governance Forum, the Cross-Strait Youth New Media and Cultural Creative Forum, and cross-Strait same-name village activities, which were widely welcomed.\nThird, relevant mainland authorities further provided convenience for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interaction. Five additional Taiwan compatriot visa application points were added at ports, bringing the cumulative total to 41. Ten new cities were opened for individual travel to Taiwan, bringing the cumulative total to 36.\nIn the new year, we will continue to expand and deepen cross-Strait exchanges in all fields, especially strengthen communication and exchanges among all sectors and strata of society across the Strait, and continue to help Taiwan youth study, work, and start businesses on the mainland. We will increase mutual understanding and trust, adopt more targeted policy measures, let more Taiwan grassroots people share in the fruits of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continue working to bring the hearts of compatriots on both sides closer together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697457.htm"],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Last year, the two cross-strait associations held a first working-level negotiation in Beijing on the issue of transit for mainland tourists. The Straits Exchange Foundation said it hopes the mainland side will put forward a feasible plan as soon as possible. When can it be put forward? Regarding new mainland air routes, could the spokesperson say whether this will affect the issue of transit for mainland tourists?","The first question: Regarding the transit of mainland residents through Taiwan and the communication on further facilitating exchanges between compatriots on both sides, the two associations have held the first working-level consultation. In the consultation, everyone fully exchanged views and put forward their respective considerations. It is my understanding that the two sides are currently maintaining contact so as to hold a second working-level consultation at an appropriate time.\nThe second question: The announcement that the M503 route will soon be put into operation and the consultation on mainland tourists transiting through Taiwan and further facilitating exchanges between compatriots on both sides are two unrelated issues and should not affect each other.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Previously, Xiong Jie, a professor in the Department of Political Science at New York University, gave a media interview in which he said that the mainland's Taiwan policy needs to change its thinking, and should not blindly make concessions, otherwise the DPP would think it can gain more benefits by opposing the mainland. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this view?","We generally do not comment on the various views that some scholars have expressed about cross-Strait relations. But I would like to say that, setting aside his personal views, over the years, especially since 2008, the creation of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has of course relied on the efforts of both sides of the Strait and of the KMT and the CCP, on the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, and even more on the positive policies both sides have implemented to improve and develop cross-Strait relations. So in terms of the achievements of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, the mainland's policy measures have been effective. Why would they need to change? Second, at the last press conference we already gave a dedicated explanation of the dividends of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations. The mainland adheres to the policy of peaceful development and implements policy measures that benefit compatriots on both sides, and these cannot be simply summed up with the words “giving concessions” (让利). Why do we do this? Because compatriots on both sides are brothers, and we act in the spirit of one family across the Strait, genuinely implementing such policies. I think these policies are visible and tangible to everyone, and anyone who wants to exploit them may not be able to.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","Recently Taiwan’s military released a calendar that, for the first time, includes Zuo Quan, a general of the Eighth Route Army who fought in the War of Resistance. How do you evaluate this?","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War. The bloody, fierce struggle of 70 years ago was a national war of resistance. At the critical moment when the nation faced mortal danger, all Chinese sons and daughters united to jointly resist external aggression, and only then was that victory of the national war of resistance achieved. Today, commemorative activities held in various forms across the two sides of the Taiwan Strait help enhance the shared historical understanding of compatriots on both sides. Perhaps everyone has also noticed that among the names of anti-Japanese war heroes previously published by the Ministry of Civil Affairs, many were Kuomintang generals. We must remember history, and even more, we must cherish the good situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations and strive together to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","环球时报环球网记者","Regarding the by-election for chairperson of the Kuomintang: on January 17, the KMT is about to elect a new party chairperson in a by-election. At that time, will General Secretary Xi Jinping of the CPC Central Committee follow precedent and send a congratulatory telegram to the newly elected KMT chairperson?","Since 2008, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, along with their leaders, have maintained positive interaction and formed some constructive and beneficial practices. These good practices should of course continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150114_8697924.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter’s question about the continued spread of avian influenza in Taiwan, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said at the regular press conference on January 14 that the two sides have signed a medical and health cooperation agreement, and that recently the working liaison channels of both sides have kept in close contact about the avian influenza epidemic in Taiwan. According to the competent business authorities, the mainland has not imported livestock and poultry products from Taiwan recently. The relevant parties will implement the cross-Strait agreement and do their utmost to carry out epidemic prevention and control, safeguarding the health rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697436.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to questions at the regular press conference on January 14 about the by-election for chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, scheduled for January 17, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said: Since 2008, through the joint efforts of the KMT and the CPC and of compatriots on both sides, and on the common political basis of opposing “Taiwan independence” and upholding the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations have opened a new situation of peaceful development. This has brought stability to the Taiwan Strait area and well-being to people on both sides, and has also won unanimous affirmation from compatriots on both sides and the international community. We hope that after the new chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang is smoothly chosen, the two parties can consolidate the existing political foundation, maintain positive interaction, move toward each other, and continue to work for the advancement of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150114_8697454.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua.net, Beijing, January 21 dispatch: TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 21st, said that last November, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun and Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council Chairperson Wang Yu-chi met in Beijing and exchanged views on cross-Strait relations and livelihood issues in Kinmen. To further advance related work, the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council are studying and planning a visit by Zhang Zhijun to Kinmen in early February. If there is definite news, it will be released in a timely manner.\nEarlier, the Taiwan side’s Mainland Affairs Council said it would invite Zhang Zhijun to visit Kinmen in early February.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150121_8776140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Regarding Director Zhang Zhijun's upcoming visit to Kinmen, have the specific time and arrangements been determined?","At the invitation of Wang Yu-chi, Chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, will visit Kinmen on February 7 and 8. The two sides will hold a working meeting between the heads of their respective cross-Strait affairs authorities, exchanging views on the situation in cross-Strait relations this year and related issues, including further discussion and promotion of livelihood issues related to Kinmen. During his visit to Kinmen, Director Zhang will also meet with Kinmen County Magistrate Chen Fu-hai, hold discussions with representatives from all sectors of Kinmen, visit grassroots residents to learn about the living conditions of Kinmen villagers, and listen to the opinions and suggestions of all sectors of Kinmen on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150128_8856180.htm"],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","环球时报、环球网记者","The DPP recently reactivated the so-called \"China Affairs Committee,\" and Tsai Ing-wen proposed \"three adherences\" and \"three beneficials\" for advancing cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have said many times that our policy toward the DPP is consistent and clear, and our position of firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” is unwavering. Since 2008, the series of achievements in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been made on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” The anchor for the stable development of cross-Strait relations is the “1992 Consensus,” and this is the crux of the matter. Only if the DPP conforms to the trend of history and public opinion and abandons its “Taiwan independence” position can it find a way out in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150128_8856177.htm"],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Has renewed consultation between the two sides on the M503 route begun? What is the situation?","On January 16, the mainland already sent an invitation to the Taiwan side through the civil aviation “small two-meetings” channel, hoping that the air traffic control departments on both sides would further communicate on technical issues in the use of the M503 route. Such communication should help the Taiwan side objectively, realistically and comprehensively understand the mainland's opening of this new route. I am not aware of the specific status of the consultations at present, and if there is news, we will disclose it to everyone in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun attended the Cross-Strait Agriculture and Fisheries Symposium in Pingtan, Fujian. Please introduce what results were achieved.","Director Zhang Zhijun listened carefully on January 20 in the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, Fujian Province, to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan fishermen and farmers on cross-Strait agricultural and fisheries exchange and cooperation. Media on both sides of the Strait extensively reported on the matter, and we thank everyone for their enthusiastic participation in this event. I want to stress that the Taiwan Affairs Office attaches great importance to the opinions and suggestions raised by Taiwan fishermen and farmers. We will actively coordinate with relevant departments to study and resolve the practical issues of concern to Taiwan fishermen and farmers, and create favorable conditions for expanding cross-Strait agricultural and fisheries exchange and cooperation. Of course, we also hope the Taiwan side will take concrete actions, move toward us, and work together to promote better cross-Strait agricultural and fisheries exchange and cooperation, bringing more convenience and well-being to Taiwan fishermen and farmers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","We understand that representatives of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen have put forward a series of proposals, including simplifying the quarantine procedures for Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products shipped to the mainland. May I ask what attitude the Taiwan Affairs Office takes on this?","Without a doubt, over the years we have been working hard to provide all kinds of convenience for the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, including convenience in inspection and quarantine and customs clearance. Relevant departments on both sides have also repeatedly discussed these issues within the framework of the agreements between the two associations. Frankly speaking, some issues require continued efforts from the mainland side, while others are restrictions arising from Taiwan's policies and regulations. That is why I emphasized just now that both sides should take concrete actions and move toward each other, creating a favorable policy environment and conditions so that Taiwan's farmers and fishermen can sell their agricultural and fishery products to the mainland better and faster, thereby increasing their well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","First question: this year marks the 70th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance against Japan, and the mainland will hold a military parade. Will the mainland invite veterans of the KMT’s anti-Japanese war, civilian figures, and even KMT Chairman Chu Li-luan to attend such activities? Second question: after being elected KMT chairman, Chu Li-luan mentioned in his reply telegram to General Secretary Xi…","The first question: This year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. The mainland side will hold grand commemorative and celebratory activities. As for the specific timing and methods of these commemorative and celebratory activities, including the scope of invited personnel, I do not currently have specific information to release.\nThe second question: The Kuomintang and its leaders, and the Communist Party and its leaders, have maintained good interaction over these years, promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations on the common basis of opposing “Taiwan independence” and upholding the “1992 Consensus.” This good interaction should be maintained. In the congratulatory messages exchanged between General Secretary Xi Jinping and Chairman Hung Lu-chin, I believe there are three points worthy of close attention. First, both sides highly appraised the good situation of peaceful development of cross-strait relations opened since 2008, and both believe that compatriots on both sides have benefited greatly. Second, both sides expressed the need to consolidate the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Third, both sides also expressed confidence and hope that they can continue to make greater efforts to advance peaceful development of cross-strait relations and benefit people on both sides.\nAs for enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides and narrowing the psychological distance between them, achieving heart-to-heart harmony, this has long been the direction of the mainland’s policy efforts. To this end, we have also taken relevant measures in exchanges across various fields between the two sides. Of course, because the two sides have been isolated for so many years, some estrangement and misunderstanding are inevitable. I think this will require a relatively long process and time. But we believe that compatriots on both sides are brothers and sisters, that there are no knots that cannot be untied, and that the day when heart-to-heart harmony is achieved is not out of reach, as long as we strengthen communication and mutual understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","I have two questions. First, following Director Zhang's visit to Pingtan, the TAO will actively coordinate with relevant departments to resolve practical problems of concern to Taiwan's farmers and fishermen. What specifically do these practical problems refer to? Have steps been taken to resolve them? Second, the TAO and the MAC have recently begun jointly studying preparatory work in Beijing for connecting…","The cross-Strait agriculture and fisheries symposium was open, and relevant opinions and suggestions were widely reported by media on both sides. These included how to make the quarantine, inspection, and customs clearance of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products more convenient; how to reduce or waive taxes and fees; how to ensure the safety of imported products; and how to further leverage market mechanisms to expand imports of agricultural and fishery products. Some of these issues have in fact been actively promoted by the TAO all along, and the relevant measures need to be further improved. Some issues naturally require coordinating with relevant departments to actively promote, and all of this requires a process. Therefore, Director Zhang said that with the continuous development of cross-Strait relations, the practical concerns of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen will eventually find solutions.\nSecond question: As we have already announced, responsible persons of the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan have recently communicated on preparatory work for launching joint research, and the two sides have exchanged views on the goals, principles, topics, and steps for launching joint research.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan's relevant authorities said they hope to open individual travel to Taiwan for 10 more mainland cities. What is the mainland's consideration on this?","Since mainland residents were allowed to travel to Taiwan in 2008, such travel has increased exchanges and mutual understanding between the peoples on both sides and has also promoted the growth of Taiwan's economy and the incomes of its people, and it has been broadly recognized by people on both sides. We note that Taiwan's industry hopes to further increase the cities open to individual travel by mainland residents to Taiwan, and we will study this request. Whatever is conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, we will actively promote.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150128_8856160.htm"],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","The 7th regular meeting of the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee will be held soon. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant information.","In accordance with Article 11 of the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait, and after consultation between ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) in Taiwan, the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee (ECC) will hold its seventh regular meeting in Taipei on January 29. Mr. Zheng Lizhong, Executive Vice President of ARATS and mainland convener of the ECC and chief representative, and Ms. Gao Yan, Vice Minister of Commerce, will lead the mainland delegation to the ECC to attend the meeting. The regular meeting will review the implementation of the framework agreement since it took effect, including the implementation of the Early Harvest Program under the framework agreement and the progress of the work of six working groups on trade in goods, trade in services, investment, dispute settlement, industrial cooperation, and customs cooperation, as well as the establishment of offices by economic and trade associations of the two sides in each other’s territory. It will also discuss the negotiation process for follow-up agreements. Meanwhile, both sides will exchange views on further expanding and deepening cross-strait economic cooperation, on their respective economic development situations and economic policies, and on other related issues, and arrange the next stage of work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150128_8856173.htm"],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾三立电视台记者","I would like to ask: after Taiwan's food oil safety crisis, 235 food manufacturers were banned from exporting to the mainland, and it has now been more than four months. Taiwan's side hopes the ban will be lifted before the Lunar New Year. Is this possible?","On January 23, experts from the cross-Strait food safety competent authorities, under the arrangements of the two associations, held a cross-Strait food safety exchange meeting in Beijing. At this meeting, both sides agreed to further study and negotiate the improvement of information notification and follow-up handling mechanisms for major food safety incidents, strengthen technical exchanges on cross-Strait food safety standards, encourage the creation of platforms in various forms, and reached consensus on the follow-up handling mechanism for the recent oil product safety incident in Taiwan. It is understood that after the oil product safety incident in Taiwan, relevant mainland departments, based on information and data publicly released by the Taiwan side, temporarily suspended imports of certain Taiwan products. This was a necessary preventive measure taken to safeguard the health rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. Our hearts are alike; if we consider it from each other’s position, I think everyone can understand. After the Taiwan side provides new assessment materials to us, relevant mainland departments will actively and appropriately resolve the follow-up issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","Recently, Taiwan’s economic authorities released a set of data showing that in 2014, the number of projects approved by Taiwan for mainland investment in Taiwan declined year-on-year. Outside observers generally believe this is related to the suspension of the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement. May I ask: with the services trade agreement suspended, will there be consultations this year to promote this…","As I have said before, after rapid development, cross-Strait trade and investment have entered a “new normal.” At the same time, the decline in the share of mainland investment in Taiwan is also to some extent related to the delay in the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement. For a long time we have encouraged mainland enterprises with the conditions and capability to invest in Taiwan, which can increase tax revenue for Taiwan and create jobs, forming a virtuous cycle of economic exchange and cooperation across the Strait that benefits both sides. We hope the Taiwan side will further reduce restrictions on mainland investment, so that both sides can make new efforts to further expand and deepen economic cooperation across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","Could the spokesperson introduce the recent preparations for the KMT-CPC Forum? Is it possible to hold it before the Lunar New Year? Will Chu Li-luan, the newly elected Kuomintang chairman, be invited to visit the mainland?","Everyone has been paying close attention to this issue for a long time, and I have responded to it several times. We believe that over the years, the Straits Forum on cross-Strait economic, trade and cultural exchanges has not only played an important role in promoting the development of relations between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party and cross-Strait relations, but has also widely included participants from all sectors of cross-Strait society, enhanced mutual communication and understanding among compatriots on both sides, promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and produced more than 100 joint proposals during the forum, most of which have been implemented. Such a good platform for exchange should naturally continue. To this end, relevant departments of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party have also maintained communication, and when there is specific news, we will release it to everyone in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","At this year's Taiwan work conference, it was specifically mentioned that we will actively advance consultations on follow-up issues under the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement. Is there a concrete timetable? Regarding benefiting more people, that is, letting Taiwan residents feel the benefits, how will this be done?","Once the results of the follow-up ECFA negotiations are reached, they can further benefit the people of Taiwan and effectively let more Taiwan residents feel the benefits. More Taiwan products will enter the mainland through tariff reductions and zero tariffs, and more Taiwanese small and medium-sized enterprises and service industries will come to the mainland to develop and grow. How could people not feel it? There is no doubt that they will feel it. Our attitude and policy in actively promoting the follow-up ECFA negotiations are very clear. Of course, we hope to reach an agreement as early as possible, but frankly speaking, this also depends on Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","We were delighted to see that Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Wang Yu-chi will meet in Kinmen on February 7 to 8. My question is, why did the two sides choose Kinmen as the venue?","Last November, during the meeting in Beijing between Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Wang Yu-chi, the two exchanged views on the situation in cross-Strait relations and related issues, including promoting work concerning the livelihood of Kinmen. This is a very important consideration behind holding this \"Zhang-Wang meeting\" in Kinmen. We believe that during Director Zhang's visit to Kinmen, he will take \"stability, development, and livelihood\" as the main axis. We believe that through pragmatic and candid communication between the heads of cross-Strait affairs authorities, and sincere interaction with people from all walks of life in Kinmen, we can certainly provide momentum for continuing to advance cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","I would like to ask a lighter and warmer topic, about cross-Strait marriages. When people talk about cross-Strait marriages, the term “mainland brides” usually comes up. But in recent years the number of “mainland grooms” has also been growing. Recently, Taiwan's civil affairs authorities published data showing that in 2014, among newly married cross-Strait families, more than 720 couples were Taiwanese women…","I think this situation reflects the improvement and progress of exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait and the development of cross-Strait marriages. As you may also know, in the early days, most cross-Strait marriages were one-directional, and many were made for livelihood reasons. As cross-Strait exchanges have expanded and deepened over these years, and as the mainland's economy has developed, its society has progressed, and living standards have risen, today's cross-Strait marriages are based on love and carry a special charm. We hope that young people across the Strait will have broader contact and understanding through exchange, entrepreneurship, and study. Not all of them will necessarily marry, but they can certainly form friendships.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201501/t20150128_8856502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-01-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a question from a reporter about the recent cross-Strait agriculture and fisheries symposium, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said at the regular press conference on January 28 that on January 20, Director Zhang Zhijun carefully listened to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan farmers and fishermen on cross-Strait agriculture and fisheries exchanges and cooperation at the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone in Fujian. The TAO attaches great importance to the opinions and suggestions raised by Taiwan farmers and fishermen. We will actively coordinate with relevant departments to study and resolve the practical issues of concern to Taiwan farmers and fishermen, and create favorable conditions for expanding cross-Strait agriculture and fisheries exchanges and cooperation. We hope the Taiwan side will also take concrete actions, meet us halfway, and work together to promote better development of cross-Strait agriculture and fisheries exchanges and cooperation, bringing more convenience and well-being to Taiwan farmers and fishermen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201501/t20150128_8856175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-01-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first is on the military parade commemorating the 70th anniversary of the victory in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression. Retired PLA Major General Luo Yuan suggested that there should be a veteran square in the parade, consisting of veterans from the Kuomintang who took part in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression. What is…","On the first question, I have already said that I am sorry that I do not have any new information to share. As to your second question, spokespersons of the Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have both responded to this issue. Neither of the two kinds of interpretations that you have mentioned, whether the construction is targeting the Diaoyu Islands or the construction is targeting Taiwan, is correct.\nWe think that under the background of peaceful development in cross-strait relations, it goes against the good momentum of development in cross-strait relations to hype up the so-called military threat from the mainland against Taiwan.\nAnd I’d like to make an additional comment. Some foreign commentators are really prone to hype up the legitimate activities of the Chinese military. Indeed, they have gone out of their way to hype up such topics. But they will not win applause by doing so.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-01/29/content_4567609.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-01-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A number of senior military officers from the Kuomintang fought the Japanese during the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression. And later in the civil war, they fought with the Communist Party of China. Recently, the body of the deceased Kuomintang Major General Zhang Lingfu, who used to be the commander of the 74th Division of the Kuomintang Party, has triggered a lot of controversy and…","I think they are actually the same question. The histories of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the Chinese People’s War of Liberation are quite clear. I’m not going to comment on certain individuals in the history.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-01/29/content_4567609.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-01-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Earlier there was a question about the construction on the Nanji Islands, and you said that the construction was not directed at the Diaoyu Islands which are known in Japan as the Senkaku Islands, and it was also not directed against Taiwan. Can you tell us the purpose of the construction?","I have said that the construction on the Nanji Islands is a legitimate activity conducted within Chinese territory, and there is no necessity to over-interpret such construction.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-01/29/content_4567609.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2015-02-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to remarks made by Ko Wen-je, Mayor of Taipei, in a recent interview with the U.S. magazine Foreign Policy, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 2nd in response to a question: The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not relations between two states. This has an indisputable legal basis and factual foundation. The bottom line of cross-Strait relations must not be challenged. Any words or deeds detrimental to cross-Strait relations go against the wishes of compatriots on both sides and harm their interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150202_8909610.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua net, Beijing, February 5 (Electric) (Reporter Chen Jianxing): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 5th in response to questions that, according to the understanding of the Civil Aviation Administration of China, relevant parties in Taiwan have issued an invitation, and the mainland civil aviation authority will send personnel to Taiwan in the capacity of the civil aviation 'small two-meeting' to participate in assisting the investigation of the TransAsia Airways crash accident in Taiwan. At present, the civil aviation side is contacting the Taiwan side through existing communication mechanisms and channels and is urgently handling related matters.\nMa Xiaoguang said that, based on the consensus reached by the competent investigation authorities of cross-Strait civil aviation accidents, both sides have established a communication mechanism for the investigation of cross-Strait civil aircraft accidents and incident symptoms, and have mutually invited each other to participate in investigations of major air disaster accidents involving the other side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150205_8949965.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 5 (reporter Chen Jianxing): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, told reporters on the 5th that Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office had originally planned to visit Kinmen on the 7th and 8th. On the 4th, a Taiwan TransAsia Airways aircraft crashed into a river, causing heavy casualties among compatriots on both sides. At present, both sides need to concentrate their efforts on handling the aftermath. After consultation between both sides, the timing of Director Zhang’s visit to Kinmen will be postponed.\nMa Xiaoguang said that on the 4th, a TransAsia Airways aircraft flying from Taipei to Kinmen crashed into a river, causing heavy casualties among compatriots on both sides. So far, 32 compatriots have died and 15 have been injured, and we feel deeply distressed. Eleven compatriots remain missing, and search and rescue work is continuing. Their safety concerns compatriots on both sides. At present, compatriots on both sides are following closely the progress of search and rescue, and both sides need to concentrate their efforts on handling the aftermath. We hope the Taiwan side will continue to make every effort to urgently search for the missing and properly handle the related aftermath. After consultation between both sides, the timing of Director Zhang’s visit to Kinmen will be postponed. Meanwhile, both sides will further communicate on issues concerning cross-Strait relations. We will release the relevant arrangements in a timely manner once they are determined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150205_8949971.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","On February 11 at 10:00 a.m., the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first briefed on the follow-up handling of the Taiwan TransAsia Airways airliner crash, and on the situation of TAO and ARATS leaders visiting Taiwan compatriots in many places to offer condolences and goodwill ahead of the Spring Festival. He then answered reporters'…","Dear media friends, good morning. First, I will brief you on two items. The first concerns the handling of the TransAsia Airways passenger aircraft crash in Taiwan.\nOn February 4, a TransAsia Airways passenger aircraft crashed in Taiwan. The bad news shocked and grieved compatriots on both sides of the Strait. As of now, this air disaster has killed 40 compatriots from both sides, injured 15, and left 3 missing, including 26 mainland tourists killed, 3 injured, and 2 missing. We express deep condolences to the deceased and sincere sympathy to the injured and the families of the deceased.\nAfter the accident, General Secretary Xi Jinping immediately issued an important instruction, requiring that the relevant situation be grasped accurately as soon as possible, that active assistance be provided for the treatment of the injured, and that work on comforting the families and handling aftermath be done well. Premier Li Keqiang also issued instructions on the rescue work.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office, the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), the Ministry of Transport, the Civil Aviation Administration, the National Tourism Administration, as well as Fujian Province and Xiamen City, all immediately activated emergency response mechanisms for sudden incidents and are working fully on information briefings, comforting families, and other aftermath work. Over recent days, the TAO and the SEF have maintained close contact with Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation (Taiwan) to learn about the accident and the progress of search and rescue, to facilitate the swift travel of mainland tourists' families to Taiwan, and to properly handle the aftermath. The SEF, the Haixia Tourism Association, Fujian Province, and Xiamen City have successively sent work teams to Taiwan to learn on the spot about rescue conditions, visit the injured, comfort the families of mainland victims, and assist with the handling of the victims' remains, insurance claims, and other aftermath matters. Through contact between the SEF and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation, three mainland civil aviation accident investigation experts arrived in Taiwan on February 8 to take part in the investigation of the cause of the accident.\nAt present, the search for the missing continues, and one of the three injured mainland tourists has been discharged from hospital. In Taiwan, Buddhist ceremonies and memorial services have been held for the deceased, and the remains are being handled in turn according to the wishes of the families. Insurance claims, communication, and explanation procedures have been initiated, and the cause of the accident is under investigation and analysis. We will continue to maintain close communication with relevant parties in Taiwan and assist in properly handling the follow-up work.\nThe second item: on the eve of the Spring Festival, the heads of the TAO and the SEF will divide into six teams and visit Taiwan compatriot groups, including Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan students, and mainland spouses, in 11 provinces and municipalities. They will learn about these compatriots' production, business, study, employment, and daily lives on the mainland, and listen to their views and suggestions on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and on improving and developing cross-Strait relations.\nNow I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150211_9012706.htm"],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Taiwan’s MAC stated that the “Zhang–Wang meeting,” originally scheduled for February 7 and 8 in Kinmen, has been postponed. Apart from the Fuxing air disaster, the main reason is that the two sides across the Strait did not reach agreement on the M503 route. Could the spokesperson explain whether this is really the case?","After the TransAsia Airways passenger plane crashed into a river, causing heavy casualties among people on both sides of the Strait, including mainland tourists and fellow townspeople from Kinmen, human life is at stake. In such circumstances, fully organizing rescue and concentrating efforts on aftermath work is the top priority for the competent cross-Strait authorities on both sides. Although the preparations for Director Zhang Zhijun’s visit to Kinmen were basically ready, we and the Mainland Affairs Council agreed to postpone the visit, with everything placed first on rescue and aftermath work. This approach reflects our people-centered governing philosophy and also accords with human sentiment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council Minister Wang Yu-chi (王郁琦) suddenly resigned yesterday. May I ask what comment the Taiwan Affairs Office has on this? In addition, the Zhang-Wang meeting, originally scheduled for early February, has now been confirmed as unable to take place. Will this bring new variables to cross-Strait relations?","We have noted the relevant reports. We will not comment on personnel changes on Taiwan's side. Since last year, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council have established a regular communication and liaison working mechanism. The heads of the cross-Strait affairs authorities have visited each other and met several times, exchanging views on the situation in cross-Strait relations and several important issues within them. This is a new progress in cross-Strait exchanges. It has played a positive role in maintaining the overall stability of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and keeping it on the correct course, and it has also been unanimously recognized by compatriots on both sides and the international community. We believe personnel changes should not affect the operation of the mechanism. We hope the relevant mechanism will continue to play a positive role in promoting the development of cross-Strait relations. Regarding Director Zhang's visit to Kinmen, we hope both sides can continue to maintain communication.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150211_9012702.htm"],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","After the Fuxing air crash, some people worried that it might affect the plan for this year’s Spring Festival cross-Strait charter flights. Please introduce the relevant situation and the current approval status.","After consultation between the civil aviation “small two associations” (the cross-Strait aviation industry associations), cross-Strait airlines may arrange Spring Festival additional flights between February 5 and March 5, and the total number of additional flights is not restricted. At present, this plan has not changed in any way. As far as I understand, as of February 9, the mainland civil aviation authorities had approved 593 additional flight applications submitted by cross-Strait airlines, of which 493 were from mainland airlines and 100 were from Taiwan airlines.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","It is reported that the Taiwan side has approved the application of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits to set up an office in Taiwan. Please have the spokesperson confirm this. In addition, please introduce the latest progress on cross-Strait economic and trade groups establishing offices in each other's areas.","In accordance with the relevant provisions of ECFA, both sides are actively promoting the establishment of offices by cross-Strait economic and trade associations. The first batch, the China Chamber of Commerce for the Import and Export of Machinery and Electronic Products, has set up an office in Taipei, and the Taiwan External Trade Development Council has set up six representative offices in six cities, including Shanghai and Beijing. As the second batch, the Suzhou (Kunshan) representative office of the Taiwan Region Electrical and Electronic Industry Trade Association was formally unveiled in July 2014, and its Dongguan representative office is also speeding up its approval procedures. At the same time, the Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Exchange Association of the mainland had its application to set up an office in Taiwan approved on January 23 of this year. We wish these two institutions smooth unveiling and the start of operations this year, so that they can play their due role in promoting cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone construction symposium was recently held in Fujian. Please introduce the relevant situation of the symposium and the outcomes achieved.","In December 2014, the State Council approved the establishment of a free trade pilot zone in Fujian. At present, relevant departments are conducting in-depth research on the specific plans and policy measures for the Fujian pilot free trade zone. To further give play to Fujian's special advantages and role in cross-Strait economic cooperation, and to ensure that the policies for the Fujian FTZ are formulated more pragmatically and with greater targeting on the basis of fully understanding the wishes of Taiwan compatriots, Fujian Province convened a symposium on the construction of the Fujian Free Trade Demonstration Zone on February 3, inviting Taiwanese business people and scholars and experts from 20 sectors, including finance, shipping, commerce and trade, tourism, cultural and creative industries, healthcare, accounting, construction, and publishing. At the symposium, the Taiwanese participants put forward a series of targeted and constructive suggestions on expanding Taiwan business investment, improving customs clearance efficiency, facilitating travel for Taiwan compatriots, and deepening industrial linkages. We believe that such symposiums and exchanges help us understand the interests and concerns of Taiwan's business sector and are conducive to Taiwan compatriots better sharing in Fujian's development opportunities in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150211_9012693.htm"],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","After the crash of Taiwan’s TransAsia Airways, there has been news that mainland airlines offer better pay and working conditions, so many pilots of Taiwan airlines have been poached by the mainland, which has become a concern for Taiwan’s aviation industry. May I ask whether the TAO, together with relevant departments, will introduce regulations and consider restricting the mainland’s hiring of Taiwan-origin pilots?","We have noted that some Taiwan media have made such claims. We believe these claims are irresponsible and also an attempt to evade responsibility. It is understood that in recent years, at the request of the Taiwan side and according to the wishes of Taiwan pilots themselves, mainland airlines operating cross-Strait routes have recruited a limited number of Taiwan pilots. Meanwhile, airlines in Japan, South Korea, Vietnam, and even the Middle East have also hired Taiwan pilots. The movement of professionals and technical personnel of all kinds across the Strait conforms to market rules and individual choice, and should be viewed with a normal, ordinary mindset.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Over this period, both sides have been communicating about the new air routes, but there is still no consensus yet. Will both sides continue to communicate about the new air routes? Is there still a possibility that the mainland will withdraw its plan to open the new air routes on March 5? If communication on the new air routes does not reach a consensus, will it affect the arrangements for the next meeting of…","We have already given complete explanations on the relevant issue many times. The mainland side has repeatedly communicated and explained the matter to the Taiwan side through the civil aviation “mini two-conference” channel, and has shown much goodwill, including the operational measure of having aircraft offset to the west. In addition, I would like to emphasize several points again. The M503 route is set within the Shanghai Flight Information Region, not within the Taipei Flight Information Region, and it has been approved by the International Civil Aviation Organization. This route keeps a sufficient safety distance from the Taipei Flight Information Region and will not affect the current use of airspace in that region. To ensure flight safety, the mainland has formulated relevant operational technical measures and emergency response procedures, and the air traffic control departments on both sides maintain close communication and cooperation. Therefore, I believe the doubts on the Taiwan side can be resolved.\nIn addition, we have repeatedly stressed that the opening of the new M503 route is to meet the need, after the mainland's economic and social development, to promptly divert traffic from very busy and congested air routes. Therefore, opening the new route is necessary and very urgent. We therefore still hope that, through communication between the two sides, the Taiwan side can more fully understand the circumstances of the mainland's opening of the new route, view them objectively, and make use of this route to facilitate personnel exchanges across the two sides and promote the development of civil aviation on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the third \"Zhang-Wang Meeting,\" originally scheduled to be held in Kinmen, has on its agenda the topic of drawing water from the mainland to Kinmen. Please introduce the current status of the Kinmen water diversion project from the mainland.","The mainland is deeply concerned about Kinmen's water shortage and has been actively promoting the Fujian water supply project to Kinmen. In June 2013, ARATS and SEF reached a shared understanding on resolving Kinmen's water issue at the ninth round of talks. Since then, relevant units in Fujian Province have communicated with the Taiwan side many times. We hope that relevant units on both sides will continue working together, strive to sign the water supply contract as early as possible, begin construction of the project, and ease Kinmen's water shortage at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新京报记者","This afternoon, TransAsia Airways will hold a compensation explanation meeting regarding the air crash accident. I would like to ask what assistance the Taiwan Affairs Office will provide to the families of mainland victims on compensation issues? My second question is for the spokesperson: will Wang Yu-chi’s resignation have some impact on the mutual establishment of representative offices between the two…","Taking up the second question first: the discussions on the various issues the two sides are working to resolve, including the discussions on the two organizations establishing offices in each other's territory, are still ongoing. On the first question, regarding the principles of compensation, after we conveyed the wishes of the mainland families and after coordination between the two sides, the Taiwan side has made a principled decision to pay the same compensation as for the same flight. As for the specific follow-up matters, we will continue to convey the reasonable wishes and demands of the mainland families and assist the Taiwan side in jointly handling the follow-up work of compensation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee recently held its meeting successfully and, for the first time, added a cross-Strait small and medium enterprise cooperation working group. What role will this play in future cross-Strait SME cooperation?","The Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee and its subordinate working groups are institutions authorized under the framework of the two associations (两会), and they promote economic cooperation across all fields between the two sides based on the ECFA agreement. At this regular meeting, the SME Cooperation Working Group was placed under the Committee for the first time. Through communication and consultation between the relevant parties on both sides, it will certainly have a positive impact on cross-Strait SME cooperation and play its due role.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志记者","May I ask the spokesperson: after Taiwan's local “Nine-in-One” elections, will the mainland still maintain high-level personnel exchange visits to Taiwan? Which provincial and municipal leaders will visit Taiwan for exchanges this year?","Our guidelines and policies for advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will not change, and we will continue to take various measures to promote exchanges and cooperation among personnel at all levels and in all fields across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Last year, cross-Strait relations changed greatly, especially after the “Nine-in-One” elections. Please have the spokesperson look ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2015. What are the mainland's expectations?","We will not change our policy of promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and at the same time we are closely following a series of new changes and new developments in Taiwan's political situation. We believe that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has brought peace dividends and tangible economic benefits to compatriots on both sides, and remains the mainstream public opinion among the people on both sides. Therefore we have the confidence and determination to keep overcoming difficulties and moving forward, to continue advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and to benefit compatriots on both sides with more achievements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中央社记者","Since taking office, Ko Wen-je has made statements and taken actions on cross-Strait relations. Does the TAO have any comment on them?","On matters concerning the foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the positioning of cross-Strait relations, we have stated our position and attitude many times over a period of time. As for some remarks by individual Taiwan political figures, I will not respond to them one by one here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Since Taiwan opened tourism to mainland visitors in 2008, tourism safety incidents have occurred from time to time. Spokesperson, will the Taiwan Affairs Office urge the relevant authorities in Taiwan to comprehensively improve the tourism safety environment?","In recent years, mainland residents' tourism to Taiwan has maintained an overall development trend that is positive, orderly, and healthy. Of course, during this process, some safety incidents have occurred, including some major safety incidents. Based on the 《Agreement Between the Two Sides of the Strait on Mainland Residents Traveling to Taiwan for Tourism》 and its supplementary and amended clauses, the tourism authorities on both sides have established a liaison mechanism through the tourism “small two associations.” We will use this mechanism to require the Taiwan side to take further measures to improve safety in relation to mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Last year's “anti-service trade” movement in Taiwan had a certain impact on cross-Strait relations. Recently, according to investigations by Taiwan prosecutors, Lin Fei-fan and Chen Wei-ting have both been indicted. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's view?","We will not comment on matters occurring within Taiwan.\nFriends, as ten thousand horses gallop to bid farewell to the old year, three rams usher in a prosperous new spring. As the Yiwei Spring Festival approaches, we extend our warmest wishes to the journalist friends present, to the media you represent, and to the audiences behind them: may you be full of joy and cheer. This concludes the press conference. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201502/t20150211_9012621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter's question about doubts raised on the Taiwan side by the M503 route, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said at the regular press conference on February 11: We have already given complete explanations of the relevant situation many times. The mainland side has communicated with and explained this issue to the Taiwan side many times through the civil aviation \"small two associations\" channel, and has shown much goodwill, including adopting operational measures such as offsetting aircraft westward. The M503 route is set within the Shanghai Flight Information Region, not within the Taipei Flight Information Region, and has been approved by the International Civil Aviation Organization. The route is at a sufficient safe distance from the Taipei Flight Information Region and will not affect the current use of that area. To ensure flight safety, the mainland has formulated relevant operational technical measures and emergency response procedures, and the air traffic control departments on both sides of the Strait maintain close communication and cooperation. Therefore, the doubts on the Taiwan side should be resolvable.\nMa Xiaoguang reiterated that the launch of the new M503 route is meant to address the need to divert traffic, as the air routes have become very busy and congested with the mainland's economic and social development. Its opening is necessary and very urgent. We hope the Taiwan side can more fully understand and objectively view the relevant situation, and use this route to further facilitate personnel exchanges across the Strait and promote the development of civil aviation on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150211_9012698.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated at the regular press conference on February 11: On the eve of the Spring Festival, heads of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Straits Exchange Foundation will travel in six groups to 11 provinces and municipalities to visit Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan students, mainland spouses and other Taiwan compatriot groups, to learn about their situation in production, business, study, employment and daily life on the mainland, and to listen to their opinions and suggestions on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and on improving and developing cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150211_9012705.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-02-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 16 (reporter Zha Wenye) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on February 16 when asked to comment on the Taiwan side's announcement that Xia Liyan will succeed as chair of the Mainland Affairs Council: We have noted the relevant reports. Since last year, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council have established a regular liaison and communication mechanism on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” achieving mutual visits between the heads of the responsible departments for cross-Strait affairs on both sides, which has played an important role in advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we hope both sides will work together to safeguard and consolidate the “1992 Consensus,” continue to advance liaison and communication between the two departments, interact positively, move in the same direction, continue to promote new progress in cross-Strait relations, and bring more achievements that benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201502/t20150217_9065468.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-02-26","Hong Lei","","Reports said that the Taiwan's representative office in the United States has changed its car plates to the new ones issued by the US State Department. What is China's comment? Has China lodged representations with the US side?","The US side issued new car plates to the Taiwan's representative office in the United States, but this kind of plate is not diplomatic one. We have asked the US side to strictly follow the one-China policy and the principles of the three joint communiques, abide by the international law, avoid developing official ties with Taiwan, and make sure that the name, nature, function and activities of the Taiwan's representative office in the United States are non-official ones so as to avoid any negative impact on China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1240873.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-02-27","Hong Lei","","Reports say that Taiwan has heightened its security alert due to the security threat suspectedly released by the Islamic State on the internet. What is your comment on that?","The threat to world peace and security posed by international terrorism is spreading lately. China firmly opposes all forms of terrorism and is willing to cooperate with the international community on counter-terrorism.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1241296.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-03-10","Fan Liqing","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","During a recent visit to Hong Kong, KMT Chairman Chu Li-lun said that the KMT would continue the “1992 Consensus” and KMT-CPC exchanges, and that it is only natural for the KMT chairman to travel to the mainland to take part in the KMT-CPC forum. What is the mainland's attitude toward this? Fan Liqing made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 10 (reporter Zhao Bo) — Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 10th when asked: We have noted Chairman Eric Chu's remarks in Hong Kong, and we welcome him to visit the mainland when convenient.\nShe said that in recent years, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China have worked to increase mutual trust on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” maintained positive interaction, promoted the development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait, safeguarded peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides. The positive and beneficial practices in exchanges between the two parties should continue. We are willing to work with the Kuomintang to move in the same direction and push forward relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait steadily.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150310_9237341.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","We noticed that on the eve of the Spring Festival, leaders of the TAO and the ARATS separately visited Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople and listened to their opinions and suggestions. Could you introduce the situation of this visit?","This Spring Festival, on the eve of the Year of the Sheep Spring Festival, Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, ARATS Chairman Chen Deming and other leaders respectively led Taiwan Affairs Office and ARATS working groups to visit and extend greetings to 42 Taiwan-funded enterprises and several schools in 11 provinces and municipalities across East, North, South, Central and Southwest China. They held 23 symposiums and engaged face to face with nearly 450 Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan students and mainland spouses of Taiwan compatriots. While extending New Year wishes and greetings, they gained a detailed understanding of the production and operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises, the living conditions of Taiwan compatriots, and the difficulties and problems they encountered, and listened to the aspirations and suggestions of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots for developing cross-Strait relations.\nFrom the overall situation, Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots are settling into entrepreneurship, work, study and life on the mainland smoothly, with the care, support and assistance of governments and relevant departments at all levels. Amid considerable downward pressure on the economy, the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople still have confidence in developing and upgrading their enterprises on the mainland. Some Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots also raised specific problems they have encountered in running enterprises on the mainland and in study and life. We attach great importance to these, are actively studying them, and strive to resolve them step by step.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250777.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾中天电视台记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed in his March 4 speech that the “1992 Consensus” is the foundation of exchanges between the two sides. In response, the DPP proposed “three beneficials and three adherences.” What comments does the mainland have on this? Many Taiwan businesspeople are worried about Document No. 62, and six major Taiwan industrial and commercial groups have submitted a petition asking that the…","Since 2008, the reason cross-Strait relations have taken the road of peaceful development and achieved a series of important results is mainly that both sides have adhered to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” The core of this foundation is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. As long as this point is recognized, there will be no obstacle to exchanges between the mainland and any party or group in Taiwan.\nOn the second question: The mainland recently issued documents requiring the clean-up of preferential investment and tax policies. This is a measure for deepening reform, optimizing the investment environment, and improving investment policy on the mainland, and it is not aimed at Taiwan businesses. We will continue to work to create a fairer competitive environment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and, as always, protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesses in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech on cross-Strait relations on March 4. Spokesperson, what important policy information does this speech contain, and what guiding significance does it have for advancing the development of cross-Strait relations?","On the afternoon of March 4, Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, President of the State, and Chairman of the Central Military Commission, delivered an important speech on cross-Strait relations while visiting members of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, and the Taiwan Democratic Autonomous League attending the Third Session of the 12th National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, and while attending their group meeting. He proposed “four unwavering commitments,” which have attracted wide attention from all sectors across the Strait and produced positive responses. The main spirit contained therein is:\nFirst, it emphasizes unwaveringly taking the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and stresses that the fruits of peaceful development need to be jointly safeguarded by compatriots on both sides.\nSecond, it emphasizes the importance of the common political foundation of both sides of the Strait adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” It also emphasizes that the core of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” lies in recognizing that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. It stresses that “Taiwan independence” is the greatest obstacle to peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and must be resolutely opposed and contained. On this point, the mainland's position is clear and consistent, and there will never be any change.\nThird, it expresses the sincere goodwill of the mainland in pursuing well-being for compatriots on both sides, and points out that this is the starting point and goal of our development of cross-Strait relations.\nFourth, it calls on compatriots on both sides to join hands and work together to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nGeneral Secretary Xi's important speech accurately grasped the new changes in the situation in the Taiwan Strait and took a comprehensive view of the overall situation with a long-term perspective. It demonstrated the confidence and determination of the mainland to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, had strong pertinence, and pointed out the direction for promoting work on Taiwan and expanding the path of cross-Strait relations development in the coming period.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250814.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, KMT Chairman Eric Chu said that as KMT chairman, attending the KMT-CPC Forum on the mainland is a very natural thing. I would like to ask the spokesperson for comment.","We have noted Chairman Zhu Lilun's remarks in Hong Kong, and we responded yesterday. We welcome Chairman Zhu Lilun to visit the mainland at a convenient time. In recent years, the Communist Party and the Kuomintang, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have worked to enhance mutual trust and maintain positive interaction. This has promoted the development of relations between the two parties and cross-strait relations, maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area, and enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides. The positive and beneficial practices formed in exchanges between the two parties should continue, and we are willing to work with the Kuomintang to jointly promote steady progress in the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.\nThe Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Culture Forum has been held nine times and has played an important role in promoting the development of relations between the two parties and cross-strait relations. It should continue. Regarding the specific arrangements for holding the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Culture Forum, relevant parties of the two parties have remained in communication. If there is definite news, we will release it promptly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾东森电视台记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je recently told the media that he will send a letter to the Shanghai Municipal Government, expressing willingness to hold the Taipei–Shanghai “Twin City Forum” again this year. However, Ko Wen-je has never made clear his attitude toward the “1992 Consensus,” seemingly taking an evasive approach. I wonder what the mainland's attitude is? Will it only proceed after Ko Wen-je clearly states his…","We have noted the relevant reports. We believe that since 2008, on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus,” the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has achieved a series of important results, which have been affirmed and welcomed by people on both sides of the Strait and the international community. Only by upholding and safeguarding this political foundation can exchanges and cooperation between the two sides of the Strait, and between cities across the Strait, go steadily and far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250807.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","福建厦门卫视记者","Reportedly, the Taiwan fishing boat “Xiang Fu Chun” recently lost contact with 11 mainland fishing workers aboard. Spokesperson, does the TAO know the situation?","On March 9, after we learned of the news that the Taiwanese fishing vessel “Xiang Fu Chun” had lost contact in the sea 1300 nautical miles east of Argentina, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) immediately sent a letter to Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) to verify the situation, expressing deep concern over the whereabouts of the missing vessel and all the fishermen aboard, including 11 mainland fishermen. Taiwan's SEF has replied confirming that the loss of contact did occur. According to our understanding, the China Maritime Search and Rescue Center has actively coordinated with the relevant parties to make every effort in the search and rescue. We also hope the relevant Taiwan authorities will make every effort to search and find the missing vessel and the fishermen as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250754.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾《中国时报》记者","We noted that Foreign Minister Wang Yi mentioned at the NPC press conference the other day that a grand military parade will be held this year to mark the 70th anniversary of victory in the war against fascism, and that invitations will be sent to the relevant national leaders and international organizations. Whoever sincerely comes is welcome. Does this also mean that, apart from Chu Li-lun, the mainland has…","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and of the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland. The mainland will solemnly hold a series of commemorative activities. Victory in the War of Resistance was a victory of the entire nation, and we welcome Taiwan compatriots to take part in the commemorative activities. We hope that through commemorating the victory in the war, compatriots on both sides will remember history, cherish the memory of the martyrs, unite and work together with one heart, and jointly commit to advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250793.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","The Boao Forum for Asia will be held at the end of March. According to Taiwan media, General Secretary Xi Jinping will meet Vincent Siew at that time. Please confirm.","As I understand it, Mr. Vincent Siew will attend the annual conference of the Boao Forum for Asia held in Hainan at the end of March this year in his capacity as honorary chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation; specific activities are still being arranged through communication.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Kao Yu-jen, former Speaker of the Taiwan Provincial Assembly, said in a recent interview that a cross-Strait peace forum is currently being negotiated with the mainland side, probably in May or June. Please confirm.","As far as I understand, the specific arrangements for holding the Cross-Strait Peace Forum are still under communication between the relevant parties on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾《联合报》记者","A few days ago, some National People's Congress deputies proposed putting the revision of the “Law on the Protection of Investments by Taiwan Compatriots” on the agenda. The revision of its “Implementing Rules” began two years ago. When will the revision be completed? This year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance. Are there any commemorative activities that the mainland is holding…","First question. Since its promulgation and entry into force, the Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots and its Implementing Rules have played an important role in protecting the lawful rights and interests of investment by Taiwan compatriots and in promoting economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. In 2012, the two organizations signed the Cross-Strait Agreement on Investment Protection and Promotion, which, together with the Investment Protection Law, continues to provide legal safeguards for protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Regarding the problems Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots encounter in all aspects of business and production on the mainland, we will forward them to the relevant departments for handling, and protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesses in accordance with the law.\nSecond question: the series of activities commemorating the War of Resistance is still being planned. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait, by jointly commemorating the victory in the War of Resistance, will remember history, honor the martyrs, stand together in unity, and work to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","中新社记者","Relevant Taiwan authorities recently penalized six universities in Taiwan and required that they not invite mainland personnel to visit Taiwan for exchanges within six months. What is your view?","Academic and other exchange activities between universities on both sides of the Strait help enhance mutual understanding and also promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. We hope relevant parties in Taiwan will create a favorable environment and conditions for exchanges between cross-strait universities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150311_9250746.htm"],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾《旺报》记者","The M503 route incident has basically come to an end. Will it be possible for Director Zhang Zhijun to visit Taiwan and hold a “Zhang-Xia meeting”?","Mutual visits and meetings between the heads of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan are an important part of the normalized communication mechanism that the two departments have established. Because of the TransAsia Airways crash on February 4, Director Zhang Zhijun’s originally scheduled visit to Kinmen was postponed. Regarding when Director Zhang will visit Taiwan and meet with the Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council have remained in communication.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾工商时报记者","Last year, the Mainland Affairs Council and the Taiwan Affairs Office reached a consensus to communicate on the part concerning both sides' participation in regional economic integration. May I ask how the communication is going at present? In addition, a Taiwanese scholar recently published an article proposing that \"civil-to-civil dialogue\" be launched. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office is prepared…","On the first question, further expanding exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and promoting economic integration is conducive to creating better conditions for Taiwan’s participation in regional economic cooperation. At present, the two sides have exchanged views on preparations for jointly studying the alignment of cross-Strait economic common development with the regional economic cooperation process, and will continue follow-up communication.\nOn the second question, as I have already answered, the most important reason cross-Strait relations have moved onto the path of peaceful development since 2008 and achieved a series of important results is that both sides adhere to the shared political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” The core of this foundation is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. As long as one recognizes this point, there will be no obstacle to exchanges between the mainland and any political party or group in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","We have noticed that the “Belt and Road” strategic concept has become a buzzword at this year’s two sessions. Will the Taiwan Affairs Office help Taiwan share in this strategic opportunity?","We are willing to listen to the opinions and views of people from all walks of life in Taiwan on this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-11","Fan Liqing","台湾TVBS电视台记者","We have seen recently that both Lin Yifu, a member of the CPPCC, and Lei Jun, a National People's Congress deputy, have made remarks on issues concerning Taiwan youth. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office has any clear work priorities or newer views on Taiwan youth issues this year?","Cross-Strait youth are the future of cross-Strait relations. We have always attached great importance to cross-Strait youth exchanges, and we are willing to further provide more help and create better conditions for Taiwan youth friends to visit, exchange, study, live and start businesses on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150311_9251552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-03-18","Hong Lei","","With regard to the 1969 map of the Diaoyu Dao posted on the Japanese Foreign Ministry website, you have made some comments yesterday and I wonder whether you have anything more to say today?","This 1969 map tells us two things: first, the Diaoyu Dao is an integral part of China, or a part of Taiwan to be specific; second, it is a historical fact that Japan invaded and occupied Taiwan and stole the Diaoyu Dao.\nThis map of \"Fujian Province and Taiwan Province\" is from the Provincial Atlas of the People's Republic of China. In order to draw a complete picture of Fujian Province and Taiwan Province, the northern part of Fujian, southern part of Taiwan and the Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated waters are extended beyond the sheet line of the map in the. form of \"border break\", serving as a powerful evidence that the Diaoyu Dao is a part of China.\nChina is the first country to discover the Diaoyu Dao and has exercised long-term effective administration over it. Dozens of Chinese maps drawn in the Ming and Qing dynasties explicitly marked the Diaoyu Dao as Chinese territory. Before the Sino-Japanese war of 1894, the name of \"Dioyu Dao\" was widely used in maps drawn by western countries, with clear marks showing that it belongs to China. After the war in 1894, Japan imposed long-time colonial rule over Taiwan and its affiliated islands including the Diaoyu Dao, which explains the change to the name of the Diaoyu Dao on relevant maps. After the Second World War, the Diaoyu Dao was given back to China following relevant international legal instrument. Be it Japan's colonial rule or its repercussions on map-drawing, nothing can change the fact that the Diaoyu Dao belongs to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1246655.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201503/t20150318_5412139.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","After the closing of the two sessions on March 15, Premier Li Keqiang told reporters that Taiwan businesspeople should be given a “reassurance pill.” How will the cross-Strait economic and trade policies benefiting Taiwan proposed by Premier Li Keqiang be implemented?","Premier Li Keqiang's message giving Taiwan businesspeople a \"reassurance pill\" fully shows that the policies and direction of the mainland in supporting and encouraging the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises have not changed. The Taiwan Affairs Office will work with relevant departments to further strengthen the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and continue the follow-up consultations on ECFA; further intensify efforts to protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesspeople in accordance with the law and promote the revision of the \"Measures for the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots\" and its implementing rules; further promote the implementation of policies that allow Taiwan-invested enterprises to enjoy the various support policies for enterprise operation and development on the mainland; further support Taiwan small and medium-sized enterprises in investing and developing on the mainland; and encourage Taiwan youth to start businesses and find employment on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150325_9401064.htm"],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","台湾中天电视台记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou went to Singapore yesterday to pay respects to Mr. Lee Kuan Yew. Please talk about Lee Kuan Yew’s contribution to cross-Strait relations.","Mr. Lee Kuan Yew, during his lifetime, adhered to the One-China policy and made positive and beneficial efforts to promote the development of cross-Strait relations. We hope all parties will properly handle the matter of Taiwan personages attending the condolences in accordance with the One-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","香港中评社记者","Mr. Hsiao Wan-chang recently said that Kinmen has a rich Minnan culture that inherits the essence of Chinese culture, and that Kinmen can serve as a platform for integrating cross-strait cultural exchanges. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Minnan culture is a folk culture shared by the people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and an important part of Chinese culture. Building a Minnan cultural exchange platform helps compatriots on both sides understand each other, deepens their bonds, and allows them to join hands in passing on and promoting Chinese culture. We welcome Kinmen playing a greater role in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150325_9401044.htm"],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","First, the AIIB has become a focus of attention in all sectors, and many scholars have called on Taiwan to proactively join and share in the opportunities. What is the spokesperson's response? Second, the Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference is about to be held. Please introduce which guests from Taiwan will attend and which important activities they will take part in. Thank you.","The first question: It is understood that the relevant parties are carrying out preparatory work for the establishment of the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank in accordance with the memorandum of understanding on its establishment. The second question: Mr. Vincent Siew, Honorary Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan (Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation), will lead a delegation to attend the Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference this year, and relevant activities are being arranged.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","中国台湾网记者","Li Jianhua, Party Secretary of the Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region, is leading a delegation on a visit to Taiwan. Which other provincial-level leaders will visit Taiwan for exchanges this year?","At the invitation of the Central Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, Li Jianhua, Secretary of the CPC Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region Committee, led a delegation to visit and exchange in Taiwan from March 24 to 30. It is understood that the delegation will take \"Cross-Strait Families Are One · Working Together Toward the Future\" as its theme, highlight Ningxia's resource characteristics, and carry out a series of exchange activities. These include a forum on economic, trade, and cultural cooperation and exchange, a minority ethnic plaza arts and friendship gathering, and a Ningxia tourism and cultural product exhibition. The delegation will also exchange views with relevant KMT figures, visit grassroots associations in Taiwan, and visit Taiwan's cultural institutions, science parks, and farm households. We wish Secretary Li Jianhua's visit complete success.\nWe will continue to promote exchanges between the two sides at all levels and in all fields, and relevant news will be communicated to everyone in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","新华社记者","The Political Bureau meeting of the CPC Central Committee yesterday adopted the overall plan for the Fujian Free Trade Zone. Could the spokesperson introduce what specific measures the Fujian Free Trade Zone has for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation?","The overall plan for the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone was reviewed and approved by the central government on March 24. We believe that the construction of the Fujian Free Trade Zone will help promote the liberalization and facilitation of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation. We will also, as always, encourage Taiwan compatriots to start businesses and develop on the mainland and share in mainland development opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","台湾东森电视台记者","I have two questions. First, we know the Taipei-Shanghai “Twin City Forum” is based on the “1992 Consensus,” but Taipei Mayor Ke Wenzhe only said that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” which seems to be somewhat avoiding the “1992 Consensus.” What is the mainland’s attitude toward this? Second, many Taiwan businesses have recently reported that the “mini three links” between Xiamen and Kinmen have, it…","On the first question: we also noticed the report you mentioned. Since 2008, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” both sides of the Strait have promoted a series of important achievements in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We hope all sectors in Taiwan will work with us to safeguard the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Upholding the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family” is conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nOn the second question: as we understand it, the overall operation of the “Small Three Links” is normal. Regarding imports of goods, the situation reported by Taiwan businesspeople may be due to certain regions implementing more standardized regulatory policies. Governing the country according to law and creating a more unified and fair market environment is the general trend. At the same time, we will give full consideration to the reasonable demands of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","福建海峡卫视记者","Many people are concerned about Tsai Ing-wen's attitude toward the “1992 Consensus.” If Tsai Ing-wen is elected and does not recognize the “1992 Consensus,” what serious consequences would follow?","I will not comment on hypothetical questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","福建东南卫视记者","First, MAC Chairman Xia Liyan earlier revealed that he did not rule out meeting Director Zhang Zhijun in April. May I ask the spokesperson whether a specific timetable for the “Zhang-Xia meeting” has been set, and whether it is scheduled for April? Second, the ceremony to worship the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum in Xi'an is approaching this year. What is the current preparation status of the various items involving…","Question one: Regarding the meeting between Director Zhang Zhijun and Minister Shih Li-yan of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council are still in communication about arrangements. Once confirmed, we will release the information promptly.\nQuestion two: Xuanyuan Huangdi is one of the cultural ancestors of the Chinese nation. The annual Qingming ancestral sacrifice ceremony is a grand occasion where descendants of the Yan and Huang emperors at home and abroad remember their ancestors, trace their origins, and carry forward the national spirit. We welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan, especially young people from Taiwan, to attend the ancestral sacrifice ceremony and promote cultural exchange across the Strait.\nQuestion three: For many years, telecom fraud has caused major financial and psychological losses to people on both sides of the Strait, including damage to trust between people. Therefore, after the Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance was signed and implemented, police on both sides have strengthened cooperation to jointly combat cross-Strait crime, with one key focus being the fight against telecom fraud crimes. To date, the two sides have jointly dismantled nearly 400 criminal gangs across the Strait and in third places, and arrested more than 6,300 criminal suspects. As long as such criminal activities exist, police on both sides will continue to join hands to combat cross-border telecom fraud, actively recover stolen funds, and protect the property security of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","福建厦门卫视记者","Earlier, Taiwan media reported that the eleventh round of talks between the leaders of the two sides' associations may be held in March this year. Please confirm.","Under the established practice of institutionalized consultations between the two associations, the 11th round of talks between the leaders of the two associations will be held on the mainland. At present, the two associations are communicating on the time, venue and agenda of this meeting, and will release the details promptly once they are determined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","福建海峡导报记者","Recently, DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen, responding to remarks by former AIT Executive Director Stephen Young, said that cross-strait relations must be kept peaceful and stable, and that she will make every effort to maintain the status quo. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our policy toward the DPP is clear. We have pointed out many times that since 2008, the most important reason cross-Strait relations have been able to move onto a path of peaceful development and achieve a series of important results is that both sides adhere to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” The core of this foundation is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. As long as this point is recognized, there is no obstacle for any Taiwan party or group to engage with the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150325_9401061.htm"],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Former AIT Executive Director Raymond Greene believes that Tsai Ing-wen “should have some policies on cross-strait relations.” Is this view the result of communication between China and the US? Also, what is the TAO's view of such a statement?","Since 2008, cross-Strait relations have embarked on a path of peaceful development and achieved a series of important results. These have received strong support from compatriots on both sides and recognition from the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","台湾《联合报》记者","I would like to know whether Taiwan has any opportunity to participate in the construction of the \"Belt and Road\" through the AIIB? What methods or channels do Taiwanese businesses have for participating in Belt and Road construction?","On the question of Taiwan’s participation in the “Belt and Road” construction, we are willing to hear the opinions and suggestions of people from all sectors in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","香港中评社记者","We know that recently, in counties and cities governed by the DPP, as well as in Taipei City, which is governed by independent Ko Wen-je, “cross-Strait affairs groups” have been successively established to handle cross-Strait exchange matters. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Our policy toward the DPP is consistent and clear. We have repeatedly pointed out that the series of achievements in peaceful development of cross-Strait relations were attained on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” We have consistently held a positive attitude toward exchanges in all areas across the Taiwan Strait, including exchanges between counties and cities. We hope that through various cross-Strait cooperation and exchanges, we can safeguard the political foundation of peaceful cross-Strait development and maintain the favorable situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201503/t20150325_9401844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-03-25","Fan Liqing","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to reports that many people in Taiwan make a living through telephone fraud targeting the mainland, Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to questions at the regular press conference on March 25: For many years, telecom fraud has caused major financial and mental losses to people on both sides of the Strait, and has also damaged trust between people. Therefore, after the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance” was signed and implemented, police on both sides of the Strait have strengthened cooperation to jointly combat cross-Strait crimes, with one key focus being the crackdown on telecom fraud. To date, the two sides have jointly dismantled nearly 400 criminal gangs involving both sides of the Strait and third places, and arrested more than 6,300 criminal suspects.\nFan Liqing said that as long as such criminal activity exists, police on both sides of the Strait will continue to join hands to crack down on cross-border telecom fraud, ensure the property security of people on both sides of the Strait, actively recover stolen funds, and give a fair deal to the people who were defrauded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150325_9401040.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-03-26","Geng Yansheng","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the mainland has opened a new flight route M503 on the west side of the median line of the Taiwan Strait. Because the new route is quite close to the median line of the Strait, there are a lot of discussions or even suspicions on this new flight route in Taiwan.\nPreviously, we have heard a lot of comments from mainland civil aviation authorities and Taiwan Affairs Office. So regarding the opening of the…","The M503 flight route is within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. Opening such a flight route is a routine work in its air space management of China’s civil aviation department. And relevant work is conducted in accordance with the conventions of the International Civil Aviation Organization.\nThis is an open route for civil aviation, which means that aviation companies from both Taiwan and foreign countries can apply for using this flight pass. So the opening of this new route means opening a new passage of peace in the air space.\nAnd after the opening of this new flight route, the military activities conducted by both the mainland and Taiwan are required to keep at a safe distance from this route to ensure its smooth operation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-03/26/content_4576980.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-03-26","Geng Yansheng","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I’m sorry I have yet another question about the military parade. Will the contributions of other countries and militaries that contributed to Japan’s defeat in the Asian theater such as the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Great Britain and others, be reflected in China’s preparations and in the actual commemorations and parade? And also is there any chance that the military officials from Taiwan will be…","As to the work related to Taiwan, I’d like you to refer the question to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. And in answering the previous questions on the military parade, I have mentioned the countries that we are going to invite to take part in the parade. And the countries you mentioned just now are within the countries that we are going to invite to take part in the military parade.\nI want to emphasize that this year’s military parade is special in the sense that it is not only China that will take part in the parade, and it is actually an international event. And we are inviting the leaders of other countries to observe the military parade and we are also inviting the militaries of other countries to send their own contingents or teams to take part in and observe the military parade.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-03/26/content_4576980.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2015-03-31","Hua Chunying","","Media reports say that the DPRK wants to join the AIIB, but China says no. Can you confirm this? Taiwan has applied to join the AIIB. On what conditions will China allow Taiwan to join?","On your first question, I am not aware of that. The AIIB is an open and inclusive multilateral development institution, and all parties are welcome to join. Concerning Taiwan's application, problems like \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" should be prevented from emerging.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1250815.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-03-31","Fan Liqing","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 31 (reporter Zha Wenye) — On March 31, Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions about remarks made by Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je, who expressed his views on cross-Strait relations in an interview, saying: We have noted the relevant reports. Since 2008, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” both sides of the Strait have promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and achieved a series of important results. Mayor Ko’s statement is conducive to exchanges and cooperation between Taipei and mainland cities, including Shanghai. We appreciate it.\nFan Liqing also said that regarding the “Twin City Forum” to be held by Shanghai and Taipei, Shanghai will maintain communication with Taipei.\nMayor Ko Wen-je expressed his views on cross-Strait relations in an interview on the 30th. Ko Wen-je said that no one in today’s world believes there are “two Chinas,” so “one China” is not a problem; that both sides should respect the agreements they have signed in the past and the history of their interactions; and that, on the existing political foundation and in the spirit that “cross-Strait families are one family,” they should promote exchanges, increase goodwill, and let the people on both sides pursue a better common future, with mutual understanding, mutual knowledge, mutual respect and mutual cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201503/t20150331_9463095.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-04-01","Hua Chunying","","What position does China hold on Taiwan's application for the AIIB membership?","The Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has replied to Taiwan's application for the AIIB membership this morning. He said that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has received the letter of intent from Taiwan, and has forwarded it to the interim multilateral secretariat of the AIIB. The AIIB is open and inclusive, and we welcome Taiwan's participation under an appropriate name.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1251275.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-04-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Taiwan side has clearly expressed its intention to join the AIIB. What attitude does the mainland take toward this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 1 (reporter Chen Jianxing) —\nMa Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on April 1 that the TAO has received a letter of intent from the Taiwan side and forwarded it to the AIIB Multilateral Interim Secretariat. The AIIB is open and inclusive, and we welcome Taiwan's participation in the AIIB under an appropriate name.\nOn the afternoon of March 31, the authority in charge of financial affairs of the Taiwan authorities issued a press release saying that the Taiwan side has submitted a letter of intent, and the Mainland Affairs Council asked the TAO to forward it to the AIIB Multilateral Interim Secretariat to apply to join the AIIB.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150402_9478697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The TAO affirmed Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je’s remarks in a recent interview. If the DPP said the same thing, could civil exchanges between the DPP and the mainland then proceed?","Xinhua Net, Beijing, April 3 (reporter Zha Wenye).\nMa Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to this on the 3rd.\nMa Xiaoguang said that our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. We have always made adherence to the “1992 Consensus” the basis and precondition for exchanges with Taiwan’s authorities and political parties, and its core is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. The DPP’s insistence on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position of “one side, one country” is the fundamental obstacle to its exchanges with us. Only if the DPP abandons its “Taiwan independence” separatist position can it truly safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150403_9500796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-04-08","Hua Chunying","","According to media reports, the Japanese minister in charge of territorial issues said on April 7 that the Japanese government has compiled about 500 historical records proving Japan' s control over the \"Senkaku Islands\" starting before WWII, with the aim of telling people in and outside Japan that the islands are integral parts of Japan. What is China's comment on this?","Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have been China's inherent territory since ancient times. There are innumerable historical materials and records from home and abroad to prove that. China is the first to have discovered Diaoyu Dao and has exercised long-term and effective governance over the island. Diaoyu Dao has been clearly marked on maps dating back to the Ming and Qing dynasties. Before the Sino-Japanese War of 1894-1895, the name of Diaoyu Dao had been widely recognized by western countries who clearly defined Diaoyu Dao as China's territory on their maps. Taiwan and its affiliated islands, including Diaoyu Dao were put under the colonial rule of Japan for a long time in the wake of the Sino-Japanese War of 1894-1895. Diaoyu Dao was returned to China in accordance with relevant legal instruments after WWII. Japan, who struggles to deliberately misinterpret the materials it has got in disregard of the integrity of history, can by no means change the fact that Diaoyu Dao belongs to China. The Japanese side recently made a fuss about a 1969 Chinese map, which in the end served as a strong proof that Diaoyu Dao is a part of China. I would like to advise the Japanese side to be cautious with the records they are about to release, otherwise they may find themselves in another self-defeating scenario.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1253140.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-04-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter's question about whether Chao Tien-lin, Director of the DPP's “China Affairs Department,” visiting the mainland recently means that formal interaction between the DPP and the CPC has begun, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 8th that Chao Tien-lin visited as a member of the Straits Exchange Foundation's board delegation, and that this has nothing to do with…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 8 (reporter Zha Wenye)\nHe said that in June 2008, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan resumed consultations and exchanges on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” and the two bodies plan some routine exchange activities every year. The composition of this visiting delegation of SEF directors and supervisors was based on a list provided by the SEF. Mr. Zhao Tianlin participated in the delegation as a director of the foundation and a member of the delegation. His identity and title in the visit are clear, and it has nothing to do with DPP-CPC exchanges.\nMa Xiaoguang reiterated that as long as the DPP does not abandon its separatist “Taiwan independence” position of “one side, one country,” we will not hold party-to-party exchanges with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150408_9530888.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency Beijing, April 10 (reporter Chen Binhua) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee, said on the 10th that, after consultation between relevant parties of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum will be held in Shanghai on May 3.\nThe spokesperson explained that this forum focuses on small and medium-sized enterprises, young people and grassroots people, aiming to deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, build consensus, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and further bring well-being to people on both sides of the Strait. At the forum, representatives of the KMT, the CPC and other Taiwan political parties, relevant departments on both sides, and representatives from small and medium-sized enterprises, young people, grassroots communities, the economic, trade and technology sectors, and the cultural and educational sectors will attend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150410_9545547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency Beijing, April 10 (reporter Chen Jianxing): On April 9, the DPP held the second meeting of its \"China Affairs Committee,\" at which DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen stated, \"The DPP's basic principle for handling cross-Strait relations is to maintain the cross-Strait status quo, that is, the status quo of maintaining peace in the Taiwan Strait and sustaining the stable development of cross-Strait relations.\" Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on April 10 and commenting on this, stressed that the key is to safeguard the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nMa Xiaoguang said that since 2008, on the political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" cross-Strait relations have maintained a situation of peaceful development and achieved a series of important results, which have been affirmed and welcomed by people on both sides of the Strait and by the international community.\nHe pointed out that the key to safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is for both sides to adhere to the political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposition to \"Taiwan independence.\" The core is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and this is the anchor of cross-Strait relations. If one insists on the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position of \"one side, one country,\" it will inevitably undermine the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and cause cross-Strait relations to become turbulent and unstable, and there are historical lessons in this regard.\nMa Xiaoguang said that he hopes compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together to safeguard the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, keep cross-Strait relations on the correct course of peaceful development, and bring benefits to the people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150410_9549691.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-04-13","Hong Lei","","First, the US cyber security firm \"FireEye\" said that hackers from China have been launching cyber attacks against some countries in the past decade. Does China have any comment on this? Second, why does China refuse Taiwan's application to the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank for prospective founding membership?","On your first question, I'd like to emphasize that the Chinese government resolutely forbids and cracks down on all forms of hacker attacks. This position is consistent and clear. Hacker attack is a global issue which requires cooperative response from the international community rather than groundless finger-pointing and suspicion.\nOn your second question, today the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has made the position clear. I have nothing new to offer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1254246.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: China Review News Agency previously relayed that persons involved in the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank's multilateral interim secretariat said that Taiwan and others had not become prospective founding members, but could still become new members in the future. Request that the TAO confirm this.","Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on April 13 in response to a question that, after checking with the relevant parties, the China Review News Agency report is true. The AIIB is an international multilateral development institution that is open and inclusive, and Taiwan is welcome to participate under an appropriate name. Recently, we have also noted the views Taiwan has expressed on the manner and name of its participation. We are willing to continue listening to views from all sides in order to properly resolve the issue of Taiwan's participation in the AIIB. We believe that the relevant parties will positively consider the issue of Taiwan's participation in the AIIB when they negotiate the articles of association in the future. We believe that through pragmatic consultation, a way can be found for Taiwan to participate in the AIIB under an appropriate name.\nEarlier, the Hong Kong-based China Review News Agency reported the following:\nAccording to relevant personnel at the AIIB Multilateral Interim Secretariat, as learned by this agency's correspondent in Beijing, after 22 regional countries jointly signed the “Memorandum on the Establishment of the AIIB” at the end of last October, the preparation of the AIIB formally entered a multilateral process. In line with international practice, prospective founding members are negotiating the AIIB's articles of association, and the procedures and rules applicable to the accession of new members are still under consultation.\nThe AIIB is an open and inclusive international multilateral institution. It does not preclude Taiwan or other parties that have not become prospective founding members from becoming members of the AIIB in the future.\nRegarding the various concerns Taiwan has expressed, we believe the relevant parties will take them into consideration in the process of formulating the articles of association, and the mainland side will also make efforts in this regard.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150413_9560994.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. I am now glad to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","KMT Chairman Eric Chu will lead a delegation to attend the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum in Shanghai. He also said that regarding a “Xi-Chu meeting,” they are still further understanding and discussing it. What considerations does the Mainland have on this?","We welcome KMT Chairman Eric Chu leading a delegation to attend the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Culture Forum. We will strengthen communication with the Chinese Kuomintang and make arrangements for Chairman Chu's attendance at the forum and related activities. We hope that through this visit, exchanges between the KMT and the CPC will be maintained, positive interaction will be promoted, and together we can push forward the relations between the two parties and across the Strait steadily.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150415_9584097.htm"],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","I have two questions. First, the seminar “Review and Outlook on the Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations” will be held in Nanjing later this month. Please introduce the relevant details of this forum. Second, this year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance Against Fascism, and both sides of the Strait will hold commemorative activities. Recently, relevant Taiwan authorities…","On the first question: On April 29, 2005, leaders of the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang held talks for the first time in 60 years, jointly issuing the \"Common Vision for Peaceful Development across the Taiwan Strait,\" which established the common political foundation of the two parties of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" and created important conditions for the historic turn in cross-Strait relations since 2008 and the opening of a new phase of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nLooking back at history and looking ahead to the future, the Haixia Research Center of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Kuomintang's Center for Political Studies Foundation plan to jointly hold, in late April in Nanjing, a photo exhibition marking the tenth anniversary of the release of the \"Common Vision for Peaceful Development across the Taiwan Strait,\" and to convene a seminar titled \"Review and Prospects of Peaceful Development in Cross-Strait Relations.\"\nOn the second question, we have stated our position and provided explanations on multiple occasions regarding compatriots on both sides of the Strait commemorating the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. We hope that through commemorative activities, compatriots on both sides will remember history, honor the martyrs, unite as one, join hands and hearts, and work together to advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150415_9584093.htm"],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Taiwan submitted an application to join the AIIB on March 31. Why has Taiwan's application to become a founding member of the AIIB not succeeded? Is it because of the name? What name does the mainland hope for?","First, I want to reiterate that our welcome for Taiwan's participation in the AIIB under an appropriate name has not changed. The AIIB is an open and inclusive international multilateral development institution. We believe that relevant parties, when negotiating the charter in the future, will give positive consideration to the question of Taiwan's participation in the AIIB. We believe that through pragmatic consultation, a way can be found for Taiwan to participate in the AIIB under an appropriate name. In this process, we are willing to continue listening to constructive views from all sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150415_9584092.htm"],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","I have two questions. First, ten years ago the “Hu-Lien Meeting” put forward five visions, and currently only the vision of “promoting an end to hostilities and reaching a peace agreement” remains unrealized. May I ask the spokesperson for comment? Second, Tsai Ing-wen said, “The DPP's basic principle for handling cross-strait relations is to maintain the cross-strait status quo.” Responding to General Secretary…","Looking back at the ten years since the release of the “Common Vision for Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations,” cross-Strait relations have made substantial progress, especially in cross-Strait economic cooperation and exchanges in other fields, as well as in cross-Strait consultations and negotiations, all of which have yielded fruitful results. We advocate developing cross-Strait relations in an order of easy first and difficult later, step by step. At the same time, we also believe that some long-standing political issues between the two sides ultimately cannot be avoided, so we are willing, within the framework of one China, to gradually create conditions and seek ways to resolve these political difficulties.\nSecond, regarding the remarks of the DPP leader, we have already responded. I wish to reiterate that the key to maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is for both sides to establish a political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” The core is recognizing that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China; this is the anchor of cross-Strait relations. If they insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position of “one country on each side,” it will inevitably be impossible to find a way out in cross-Strait relations. This is not a new topic, but history that occurred between 2000 and 2008, and the lesson is not far off. Therefore, we hope that compatriots on both sides can attach great importance to safeguarding the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and through joint efforts, maintain the good situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, benefiting the people on both sides with more achievements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The Cross-Strait Youth Scholars Forum recently concluded. What topics did this year’s forum focus on? What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","The Cross-Strait Young Scholars Seminar is being held in Sanya, Hainan. This is an exchange activity for young scholars across the Strait organized by the National Taiwan Studies Association, and it has drawn the attention of media and public opinion on both sides. Holding such an event helps enhance mutual understanding among young people across the Strait, helps build consensus on continuing to develop the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and enables young people on both sides to more actively devote themselves to improving and developing cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","You just mentioned that you believe that through pragmatic consultation, a way can be found for Taiwan to participate in the AIIB under an appropriate name. Does this mean there are still some difficulties for Taiwan’s participation in the AIIB now? If so, what are these difficulties? In addition, through what channels will the pragmatic consultation take place? Third question: Earlier, Director Zhang’s visit to…","One question concerns the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB), and I have already explained it to everyone. As I understand it, the prospective founding members are negotiating the AIIB's articles of agreement, and the relevant procedures and rules applicable to new members joining are still under consultation. I would like to stress that our attitude of welcoming Taiwan's participation under an appropriate name has not changed.\nThe second question: as everyone knows, since last year the Taiwan Affairs Office (TAO) and the Mainland Affairs Council (MAC) have established a regular liaison and communication mechanism. The establishment of this mechanism is very rare and very valuable, and it has played an important role in promoting steady development of cross-Strait relations and in enabling effective communication between the two sides to resolve many matters of concern to people on both sides. Meetings between the heads of the two agencies are, of course, an important component of this working mechanism, and the TAO and MAC have maintained close communication regarding a meeting between Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Xia Liyan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志记者","It is reported that Wang Xiankui, Party Secretary of Heilongjiang Province, will soon lead a delegation to visit Taiwan. Please introduce the relevant information.","At the invitation of the Central Committee of the Kuomintang, Wang Xiankui, Secretary of the Heilongjiang Provincial Party Committee, will lead a delegation to Taiwan from April 19 to 25, 2015, for exchanges. It is understood that the delegation will hold a series of exchange activities, including an exchange forum with all sectors of Taiwan, a Heilongjiang Ice and Snow Culture and Folk Customs Scenic Exhibition, visits to Taiwan's grassroots associations, visits to Taiwan's cultural and museum institutions, and inspections of Taiwan's science parks and high-tech enterprises. Through these activities, the delegation aims to promote exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in culture, economy and trade, science and technology, tourism and other fields. We wish Secretary Wang Xiankui a smooth and successful visit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","Regarding the seminar “Review and Outlook of Cross-Strait Relations' Peaceful Development,” which people from Taiwan will attend? Will the issue of signing a cross-Strait peace agreement be discussed?","Regarding the attendees and the specific issues the seminar will discuss, both sides are still communicating on arrangements. We will release the details promptly once they are confirmed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","The 5th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong Economic Daily Financial Summit Forum will be held in Taipei on April 22. This forum has been successfully held four times, and this session's participants will number more than 700. I would like to ask the spokesperson for his evaluation of this forum.","The “Three Economics Forum,” jointly organized by the economic daily newspapers of both sides of the Strait and Hong Kong, has, as I understand it, reached its fifth session. It is an important platform where the media serve as a bridge, widely inviting people from all walks of life to discuss cross-Strait economic cooperation and development. This session will be held in Taipei. It is understood that Li Yafei, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, and Vice President of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, will attend and deliver a speech at the opening ceremony. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, we hope this session can build consensus to further promote cross-Strait economic cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","When KMT Chairman Eric Chu leads a delegation to the mainland to participate in the KMT-CPC Forum, will General Secretary Xi meet with him? Another question concerns Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je, who, when asked about the “1992 Consensus” in a recent media interview, proposed a “1-5” new viewpoint. What is your response?","The relevant sides of both parties will plan and arrange for Chairman Chu’s attendance at the forum and related activities. Once the arrangements are confirmed, we will release them in a timely manner.\nAs for your second question, we have already given a formal response. Regarding Mayor Ko Wen-je’s statement that no one in the world believes there are “two Chinas,” and that “one China” is not an issue, and his statement that he respects the agreements already signed between the two sides and the history of exchanges and interactions, and that on the existing political foundation, in keeping with the concept that the two sides are one family, he seeks to promote exchanges, increase goodwill, and pursue a common good future for the people on both sides, we affirm these positive remarks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Apart from the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum you just introduced, what other important cross-Strait exchange activities are there recently? Another question: the pilot cities for the fifth batch of individual tourism to Taiwan by mainland residents were launched today. Please introduce the overall situation of mainland individual tourism to Taiwan at present.","First question: Recently, exchange activities in all fields across the two sides have continued to be lively. Today, the fifth batch of individual tourism to Taiwan from 11 mainland cities officially launched. April 21 is a very special day: it is the third day of the third lunar month. Xinzheng in Henan will hold the Yiwei Year Yellow Emperor Hometown Ancestor Worship Ceremony, inviting compatriots from both sides to seek their roots, pay respects to their ancestors, and share the bonds of kinship from common origins. On the same day, Guizhou, Hainan, and other places will also hold “Third Day of the Third Month” festival events, with ethnic minority compatriots from both sides celebrating the traditional festival together. In late April, the fifth Cross-Strait Cultural and Creative Industries Exhibition, the second Cross-Strait Small Theatre Arts Festival, and the second Cross-Strait Cultural Heritage Festival, jointly held by both sides, will open successively in Taiwan. From April 24 to 30, the Cross-Strait Chinese Martial Arts Forum will also be held in Taiwan. I believe it will bring a fresh and visually delightful feast, promote martial arts exchanges across the Strait, and carry forward traditional Chinese culture.\nSecond question: After the fifth batch of mainland cities opened to individual tourism to Taiwan, our overall judgment, and our belief, is that mainland residents’ tourism to Taiwan will continue to maintain a positive, healthy, and orderly development trend. We hope that mainland residents’ tourism to Taiwan will further enhance communication and understanding between people on both sides, and will also provide appropriate assistance to Taiwan’s economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150415_9584059.htm"],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Regarding the 11th high-level meeting of the two cross-Strait associations, the SEF side hopes to target the end of April. Is this time point feasible, or should it be decided only after the KMT-CCP forum is held?","Regarding the 11th round of cross-Strait talks, as far as I know, ARATS and SEF have maintained communication and contact all along. From April 7 to 10, while SEF Chairman Lin Zhongsen led a delegation of SEF directors and supervisors on a visit to the mainland, ARATS President Chen Deming also met with him, and the two sides exchanged views on preparations for holding the 11th round of talks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150415_9584523.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","At the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council on April 15, spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions, saying that since last year, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council have established a regular contact and communication mechanism, which has played an important role in promoting the steady development of cross-Strait relations and in enabling both sides to effectively communicate and resolve many matters of concern to people on both sides. The meeting between the heads of the two departments is an important component of this working mechanism, and the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council have been in close communication all along regarding the meeting between Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairman Hsia Li-yan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150415_9584062.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-04-24","Hong Lei","","It is reported that General Secretary Xi Jinping will meet with Chairman Eric Chu of the Kuomintang (KMT) party next month. Please confirm that. What will be discussed by the two sides? How will the meeting affect the relationship between the two parties?","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Work Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) has released the relevant information today. As agreed by the CPC and the KMT, KMT Chairman Eric Chu will lead a delegation to Beijing after attending in Shanghai the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum scheduled for May 3. Leaders of the CPC and the KMT will exchange views on party-to-party interactions and relations across the Taiwan Strait. This will be an important event in the two parties' high-level exchanges.\nAfter the press conference, journalists asked the following questions:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1257625.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","(Xinhua) Beijing, April 24 — (Reporter: Zha Wenye) Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Work Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, said on the 24th that, following consultation between relevant parties of the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, Kuomintang Chairman Chu Li-lun will attend the 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Culture Forum in Shanghai on May 3, and will then lead the Kuomintang's mainland delegation to Beijing. At that time, the leaders of the two parties will exchange views on party-to-party exchanges and cross-strait relations. This is an important event in high-level exchanges between the two parties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150424_9655031.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, hello. The press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Premier Li Keqiang and Chairman Yu Zhengsheng recently said, in a symposium with representatives of Taiwan-funded enterprises, that the mainland's preferential policies for Taiwan businesses will not change, and that it will continue to support and encourage Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop on the mainland. How will the TAO implement the spirit of these remarks?","Recently, at a symposium with some heads of Taiwan-funded enterprises held in Xiamen, Premier Li Keqiang said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are closely connected, like brothers and sisters in one big family. Our preferential policies for Taiwanese businesses will not change; policies already formulated and contracts already signed will remain valid, and there is no question of retroactivity. When he held a symposium with representatives of Taiwanese entrepreneurs in Nanjing recently, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng also stressed that the policies and direction of the mainland supporting and encouraging the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises will not change, that support and encouragement for the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises will continue, and that the lawful rights and interests of Taiwanese businesses will be protected in accordance with the law. After these remarks were delivered, Taiwanese businesses in various places responded enthusiastically, feeling reassured as if they had taken a “peace-of-mind pill,” and believing these remarks embody the policy concept of “cross-Strait relations as one family,” strengthening their confidence to further develop their careers on the mainland. The Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office will earnestly implement the spirit of the remarks by the central leaders and, together with the relevant departments and localities, create a better environment and conditions for the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150429_9696156.htm"],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Please introduce the activities recently held jointly by relevant parties of the KMT and the CPC to commemorate the tenth anniversary of the release of the “Common Vision for Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations.”","On April 25, in Nanjing, Jiangsu, the Research Center for Cross-Strait Relations of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Chiang Ching-kuo Foundation for International Scholarly Exchange [placeholder]","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150429_9696147.htm"],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Today marks the 22nd anniversary of the Wang-Koo Talks and the 10th anniversary of the \"Hu-Lien meeting.\" Ma Ying-jeou will re-emphasize the \"1992 Consensus\" and \"one China, each with its own interpretation\" at the Mainland Affairs Council. What is your comment on this? In addition, under the current new circumstances in cross-Strait relations, is it possible for the \"1992 Consensus\" to be further deepened?","First question: Twenty-two years ago, the Wang-Koo talks held on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” opened a mechanism for institutionalized cross-Strait consultation, set a model of equal cross-Strait consultation, and marked a historic and important step in cross-Strait relations.\nTwenty-two years of practice in cross-Strait relations since the Wang-Koo talks have proven that to maintain the good momentum of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the key is to consolidate the political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” With this foundation, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop, the rights and well-being of compatriots on both sides can be safeguarded and enhanced, and all kinds of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation can continue to expand and deepen. If this foundation is undermined, mutual trust across the Strait will no longer exist, cross-Strait relations will return to the old path of turmoil and instability, and the fruits of peaceful development will also be lost. History enlightens reality and also points to the future; this is the most important enlightenment of the Wang-Koo talks for compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question: Since 2008, through the joint efforts of the KMT, the CPC and both sides of the Strait, and on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” compatriots on both sides have together opened a new situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, achieved a series of important results, and been affirmed and welcomed by compatriots on both sides and the international community. As long as this common political foundation continues to be upheld, the path of cross-Strait relations will become broader, and it will also bring more well-being to compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150429_9696145.htm"],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen recently said, “The DPP’s basic principle for handling cross-Strait relations is to maintain the cross-Strait status quo.” A DPP spokesperson stated that the so-called maintaining of the cross-Strait status quo refers to the status quo of 2015, not the status quo of 1992. What is your comment on this? What exactly is the current status of cross-Strait relations?","Since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not been reunified, the fact that both the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has never changed. Since 2008, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-strait relations have achieved peaceful development. This is the current state of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150429_9696134.htm"],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","A strong earthquake has just occurred in Nepal. As of now, more than 100 Taiwan tourists remain stranded in Nepal, and more than 20 are missing. Will the mainland consider cooperating with the relevant Taiwan authorities to provide assistance to Taiwan compatriots stranded in Nepal?","After the Nepal earthquake, the mainland urgently activated its emergency mechanism. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are bound by blood, and we are willing to provide necessary assistance to Taiwan compatriots in Nepal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently, CSRC Vice Chairman Jiang Yang said in Taiwan that relevant mainland departments are studying the opening of the \"Shanghai-Taiwan Connect.\" Please introduce the relevant situation and the mainland's position on cross-Strait financial cooperation.","The Shanghai-Hong Kong Stock Connect has been implemented smoothly, and the “Shanghai-Taiwan Connect” has recently drawn much discussion. We hope that, when conditions are ripe, by deepening cross-strait capital market cooperation we can provide a new platform for Taiwan compatriots to share in the fruits of mainland economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","Next week, leaders of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party will meet. Please introduce the significance of this meeting in the history of KMT–CPC exchanges, and the arrangements for Chu Li-lun’s itinerary in Beijing. When the leaders of both parties met in 2005, the two sides issued a joint press release. Will one be issued at this meeting?","A meeting between the leaders of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China is of great significance for maintaining exchanges between the two parties, enhancing positive interaction, and advancing the steady development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait. At present, preparations for the relevant itinerary are being carried out at full speed. We and the relevant parties in the Kuomintang will strengthen communication and finalize the details of each activity. The Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China broadly agree on safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait, promoting common development, enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, opposing “Taiwan independence,” upholding the “1992 Consensus,” and resolutely taking the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We expect and believe that a meeting between the leaders of the two parties will exchange views extensively and in depth on exchanges between the two parties and cross-Strait relations, and will certainly achieve positive results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201504/t20150429_9696151.htm"],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","Reportedly, Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's confidant and former Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda will successively lead delegations to visit Taiwan. What is your view?","As is well known, our position on the issue of interactions between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and Taiwan is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Recently, some scholars have said that the era of cross-Strait “concessions” is over. Does this mean the mainland will no longer “concede benefits” to Taiwan?","Over more than 20 years of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, mutually complementary and mutually beneficial results have been achieved, and business circles and the general public on both sides have broadly benefited. Starting from the concept that “cross-Strait families are one family,” the mainland has shown goodwill toward Taiwan compatriots in cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation. As the reform of the mainland's economic system deepens, greater emphasis will be placed on institutional innovation, and the various reasonable preferential policies for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises developing on the mainland will continue to be implemented.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","On May 4, Chairman Eric Chu may propose, when meeting General Secretary Xi Jinping, a political position to deepen the connotations of the “1992 Consensus,” thereby outlining a new vision for the development of cross-Strait relations. What views and expectations do you have on this?","In fact, I already answered this question just now. We believe that we must consolidate and safeguard the common political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” When this political foundation is maintained, the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will become broader and broader, the well-being of people on both sides will continue to increase, and the prospects for cross-Strait relations will become ever brighter.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","The four free trade zones of Shanghai, Guangdong, Tianjin and Fujian are currently being built at full speed. Shanghai's free trade zone has issued new policies to advance the establishment of a Taiwan small and medium-sized enterprise commodity center. Tianjin has also introduced new policies allowing Taiwan investors to register companies directly with Taiwan compatriot permits. Do you think that, with the…","The mainland’s measures to establish free trade zones have drawn wide attention from Taiwan compatriots and aroused eager expectations from Taiwan’s business and industry circles, including small and medium-sized enterprises. We believe that as the construction of the free trade zones continues to improve, and as the achievements of institutional innovation continue to accumulate, they will certainly create new opportunities and open new space for cross-Strait economic cooperation, including cooperation between small and medium-sized enterprises on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201504/t20150429_9696542.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-04-30","Hong Lei","N/A — opening announcement (no press Q)","","As agreed by China and the EU, State Councilor Yang Jiechi will host the 5th China-EU High-Level Strategic Dialogue from May 5 to 6 together with Federica Mogherini, EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy and Vice President of the European Commission during the latter's visit to China. This dialogue falls on the 40th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the EU as an integral part of relevant celebrations. The two sides will take this opportunity to look back on and ahead to China-EU relations, and exchange views on international and regional hotspot issues of common interest. It is believed that this dialogue will promote strategic mutual trust and enhance pragmatic cooperation between the two parties, and create favorable conditions for the development of China-EU partnership for peace, growth, reform and civilization.\nHere are updates on China's disaster-relief assistance to Nepal and protection of Chinese citizens there.\nChina's International Rescue Team is racing against time to search and rescue survivors. They will make 100% of efforts as long as there exists 1% of hope.\nThe medical team sent by China has carried out rescue and treatment work in Nepal in an orderly way. The team has received over 400 injured Nepalis, 14 of whom suffer from serious wounds. A new medical and disease prevention team consisting of 59 members arrived in Nepal at 4 p.m. April 29 local time, assisting and guiding Nepal to prevent any epidemic after the disaster. They will also help Nepal train 1,000 disease prevention personnel.\n120 out of the 186 tons of Chinese government's first batch of emergency relief supplies have reached Nepal, and the left will be delivered today and tomorrow. The second batch of 800 tents sent by the Red Cross Society of China has arrived in Nepal on three cargo planes this noon local time. The Chinese military will also dispatch helicopters at the request of the Nepali government to help transport the injured and other personnel.\nUnder the coordination of the Foreign Ministry, the Civil Aviation Administration of China and the Chinese Embassy in Nepal, Air China, China Eastern Airlines, China Southern Airlines and Sichuan Airlines have arranged 30 flights and taken back over 3,700 Chinese citizens from Nepal against all odds since April 26. We will continue to dispatch civil flights to pick up Chinese citizens in Nepal based on the situation there.\nFrom April 25 to 5 p.m. April 29, the Foreign Ministry has received 408 calls concerning the Nepali earthquake through the 12308 consular protection hot-line. 2,209 Chinese are involved, including 17 from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. We are happy to learn that the number of Chinese citizens dialing 12308 because of the Nepali earthquake has sharply decreased in the past two days. 11 calls were received from 5 p.m. April 28 to the same time the next day, which means that most of the Chinese citizens in Nepal have received effective assistance. The Foreign Ministry and the Chinese Embassy in Nepal will continue to follow closely the information of Chinese citizens trapped in Nepal, provide them with all necessary assistance and coordinate with departments concerned on the follow-up work.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1259920.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[1,"2015-05-09","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","The 2015 “China Military Power Report” released by the U.S. Department of Defense disregards the facts and continues to peddle the hackneyed “China military threat” narrative. It makes groundless accusations on issues including China’s national defense and military development strategic intent, the development of its military services, space, cyberspace, military transparency, and Taiwan. In particular, it ignores China’s positive efforts to safeguard peace and stability in the international and regional situation and to develop China-U.S. relations and the relations between the two militaries, and it wantonly distorts China’s peaceful development strategy, its foreign policy, and its rights-protection operations in the East China Sea and the South China Sea. China firmly opposes this.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues an independent foreign policy of peace and a defensive national defense policy. The purpose of China’s strengthening of national defense is to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity, and to guarantee the country’s peaceful development. The Chinese military actively participates in international security cooperation and has always been a firm force for safeguarding world peace. China’s rights-protection operations concerning territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests are justified, reasonable, and lawful, and are beyond reproach. No one should be casting aspersions on them.\nFor many years the U.S. side has issued so-called “China military power reports,” which have seriously undermined mutual trust and run counter to the important consensus reached by the two heads of state on building a new model of major-country relations and a new model of military-to-military relations between China and the United States. We demand that the U.S. side immediately take measures to stop words and deeds that are detrimental to China-U.S. relations and to mutual trust between the two militaries, and that it use concrete actions to promote the healthy and stable development of China-U.S. relations and relations between the two militaries. We will respond further at an appropriate time.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2015-05/09/content_4601871.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","新华社记者","The 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum proposed expanding exchanges among young people across the Strait and creating conditions for cross-Strait young students in areas such as study, internships, entrepreneurship and employment. What specific measures and arrangements will follow?","Promoting expanded exchanges among young people across the Strait is a direction we have consistently and actively worked toward. Relevant departments on the mainland and localities across the country have created many favorable conditions for young people across the Strait in areas such as innovation, entrepreneurship, employment, schooling, and internships, and have also done a great deal of work. We hope that young people on both sides can realize their life dreams amid the tide of mass entrepreneurship and innovation.\nIt is understood that many localities will soon hold a series of exchange activities themed on cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and innovation. For example, Beijing is holding the “Beijing-Taiwan Youth Entrepreneurship Season” series of activities; the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Association, in cooperation with universities in Taiwan and Shanghai, is providing internship and employment opportunities for young Taiwanese studying in Taiwan and Shanghai; Tianjin, Jiangxi Province, and other places will add cross-Strait youth exchange activities to the cross-Strait economic and trade events held this year. Our office is also actively promoting the holding of inspection and discussion activities to promote cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796175.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","台湾中天电视台记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen plans to visit the United States at the end of this month to present her cross-Strait narrative and set out her views on maintaining the cross-Strait status quo. What is your view on this?","Maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area hinges on upholding the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” We firmly oppose anyone engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally, in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796192.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","福建海峡卫视记者","The Straits Forum has been held six times so far, usually in June each year. Has the date for this year's Straits Forum been set? What is the progress?","The Seventh Straits Forum is scheduled to be held in Fujian from June 13 for one week. Preparations are proceeding smoothly. This year's Straits Forum will center on engaging young people and serving the grassroots, and has planned 17 activities in four sections—the forum conference, and cross-Strait youth, grassroots, and economic and trade exchanges—co-hosted by 76 entities from both sides of the Strait. These activities will incorporate current hot topics of concern on both sides, such as the “Belt and Road,” free trade zone construction, “Internet Plus,” and ecological civilization, to promote exchanges within the same industries. There will also be exchanges between villages with the same name, youth entrepreneurship competitions, a Common Homeland Forum, a cross-Strait carnival for persons with disabilities, community interaction, exchanges on folk temple and ancestral connections, and vocational education exchanges, so that the forum and its activities truly serve the grassroots and young people and promote exchanges between grassroots people and youth on both sides.\nWe welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan, especially young people and grassroots friends, to participate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796167.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The 10th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum recommended strengthening cross-Strait agricultural and fisheries cooperation while increasing e-commerce channels to help Taiwan agricultural products expand into the mainland market. How will this be implemented?","The mainland side has consistently and actively helped Taiwan's agricultural products expand into the mainland market. At present, some well-known mainland e-commerce enterprises, such as Taobao and Benlai Life, have already established purchasing and sales cooperation with local Taiwan producers, and mainland consumers can already buy Taiwan agricultural products online. In the future, we will continue to encourage and support e-commerce enterprises in connecting with Taiwan production areas, carrying out cooperation, and jointly creating win-win outcomes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","台湾东森电视台记者","Taiwan media have reported that a “Zhang-Xia meeting” will be held in Kinmen at the end of this month, with TAO Director Zhang Zhijun and MAC Chairperson Xia Liyan meeting. Please confirm.","Visits and meetings between the heads of the TAO and Taiwan’s MAC are an important part of the regular communication mechanism between the two departments. Regarding the meeting between Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Xia Liyan, the TAO and the MAC have been maintaining communication, and we will release information at the first opportunity once there is news.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","福建厦门卫视记者","Reports say some experts have suggested piloting card-style Taiwan compatriot permits first in Xiamen. Is this feasible? What new measures will be taken to further facilitate exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait?","Promoting personnel exchanges between the two sides of the Strait is conducive to the development of cross-Strait relations. In recent years, in order to facilitate personnel exchanges between the two sides, relevant mainland authorities have successively introduced a series of policy measures regarding Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, achieving good results. In recent years, the scale of cross-Strait personnel exchanges has expanded every year; in 2014 it already exceeded 9 million person-trips, reaching 9.411 million person-trips. Within this expanding situation, we have also noted that some Taiwan compatriots have expressed the hope that the documents for crossing the Strait could be made more convenient. To this end, relevant authorities are working urgently to study positive measures, and we believe they will be introduced at an appropriate time..","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796164.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","It is reported that this month, the Cross-Strait Small and Medium Enterprises Cooperation and Innovative Development Forum will be held in Kaohsiung as part of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit. Why was Kaohsiung chosen to host it? What arrangements are planned for this forum?","It is understood that after the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit successfully held its annual meeting in Taipei, Taiwan in 2014, many business people in southern Taiwan proposed that the Summit hold activities in central and southern Taiwan, so that enterprises there, especially small and medium-sized enterprises, would have the opportunity to participate. To this end, the two sides of the Summit agreed that the Summit will hold the “Cross-Strait SME Cooperation and Innovative Development Forum” in Kaohsiung on May 21 to 22. Mr. Sheng Huaren, vice chairman of the Summit on the mainland side, will lead more than 100 mainland SME leaders to Taiwan to attend the forum, and discuss with Taiwan counterparts topics such as incubation and nurturing of cross-Strait SMEs, cooperation, and enhancing innovation and design capabilities, striving to realize “jointly building cooperation mechanisms and working together for innovative development.” We hope the forum can build new bridges for cross-Strait SME cooperation and promote better development of cross-Strait SMEs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796172.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","香港中评社记者","At the “Xi-Zhu meeting,” General Secretary Xi put forward that the two sides should not only seek common ground while reserving differences, but should also strive to converge commonalities and manage differences. Please further explain this.","Since 2008, the facts of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations show that both sides, by upholding the common political foundation, facing matters pragmatically, and resolving practical problems through consultation, have achieved a series of important results in improving and developing cross-Strait relations. This process is one of seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and also one of accumulating common ground while resolving differences. Differences that exist across the Strait should not affect cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The two sides should communicate and exchange more, and jointly safeguard the overall situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nDuring the visit of Chairman Chu Li-luan, both the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China agreed that the two sides should adhere to the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and agreed on the political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Both sides stated that the two parties and the two sides should properly handle cross-Strait differences, respect each other, manage disagreements, and avoid disrupting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The two parties can explore difficult issues in cross-Strait relations and seek ways to resolve them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796197.htm"],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","福建海峡导报记者","Recently a “toxic tea” controversy erupted in Taiwan involving several well-known chain tea merchants. Are there related enterprises on the mainland that have been affected?","We have seen the relevant reports. The competent mainland authorities will, through the liaison and consultation mechanism under the framework of the cross-Strait food safety agreement, promptly grasp information and carry out supervision and management.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-13","Fan Liqing","台湾TVBS记者","The State Council issued Document No. 62 last year, and many Taiwan businesspeople worried that their investment rights and interests would be harmed. Yesterday the State Council issued Document No. 25, which can be said to have reassured Taiwan businesspeople. Please introduce the specific content of Document No. 25.","Recently, Premier Li Keqiang and Chairman Yu Zhengsheng both made clear in discussions with Taiwan businesspeople that the mainland's policy direction of supporting and encouraging the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises will not change. On May 11, the \"Notice of the State Council on Matters Related to Preferential Policies Such as Taxation\" (Guo Fa [2015] No. 25) was issued. It clearly stipulates that preferential policies such as taxation formulated uniformly by the state must be implemented item by item. Preferential policies already introduced by various regions and departments that have a stipulated time limit shall be implemented in accordance with that time limit. Where there is no stipulated time limit but adjustment is genuinely necessary, local governments and relevant departments shall set up a transition period under the principle of controlling the pace and ensuring stability, and continue to implement the policies during the transition period. Preferential policies in contracts already signed between localities and enterprises remain valid. Portions already realized are not retroactive. These provisions apply to Taiwan-funded enterprises and fully demonstrate the mainland's high regard for the rights and interests of Taiwan-funded enterprises. We believe they can dispel the doubts of Taiwan businesspeople and strengthen their confidence in developing on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150513_9796382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150513_9796179.htm"],[2,"2015-05-15","Fan Liqing","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 15 (reporter Zha Wenye) — TAO spokesperson Fan Liqing said on the 15th: At the invitation of Hsia Li-yan, Chairman of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, plans to visit Kinmen from May 23 to 24. The two sides will hold a meeting between the heads of cross-Strait affairs authorities to exchange views on the situation in cross-Strait relations and related issues, including livelihood issues concerning Kinmen.\nDuring his stay in Kinmen, Director Zhang Zhijun will also meet with Chen Fu-hai, the county magistrate, hold a symposium with representatives from all sectors of Kinmen, visit grassroots residents, learn about the lives of Kinmen residents, and listen to the opinions and suggestions of all sectors of Kinmen on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150515_9815140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-20","Fan Liqing","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhuanet, Beijing, May 20 (Reporter Zha Wenye): Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 20th, saying that the reports by certain Taiwan media that the mainland would help handle Taiwan's nuclear waste do not accord with the facts. This matter is not included in the agenda for the upcoming exchange of views between the head of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the head of the Mainland Affairs Council on the Taiwan side.\nShe said that the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Nuclear Power Safety Cooperation” that the two sides previously signed does not involve this matter either.\nAt the invitation of Hsia Li-yan, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council on the Taiwan side, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, will visit Kinmen from May 23 to 24, and the two sides will hold a working meeting between the heads of the cross-Strait affairs competent authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150521_9856886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Fan Liqing first introduced the outcomes of Director Zhang Zhijun’s visit to Kinmen and his meeting with Hsia Li-yan, Minister of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council. She then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone. Last weekend, our office director Zhang Zhijun successfully visited Kinmen. Let me first introduce to you the details of Director Zhang's visit and the positive results it achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","On February 11, 2014, the TAO and Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council established a communication mechanism on the basis of adherence to the “1992 Consensus.” In more than a year, the heads of the two departments have held two formal meetings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899569.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","At the meeting between the two sides last November, livelihood issues including water supply to Kinmen were discussed. Afterward, both sides agreed that Director Zhang Zhijun would be invited to visit Kinmen and inspect the situation there on site. On May 23 and 24, Director Zhang Zhijun led a delegation to Kinmen and held the third meeting between the heads of the two sides’ cross-Strait affairs authorities with Mainland Affairs Council Minister Hsia Li-yan. They exchanged views on the current situation in cross-Strait relations, policies, and relevant issues in advancing the development of cross-Strait relations, and reached positive consensus. Director Zhang also inspected the Tianpu Reservoir on site to learn about the progress of the project diverting water from the mainland to Kinmen. He visited the Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Distillery, Gongtang (sweets) and Kinmen kitchen-knife stores, among others, and held a symposium with Kinmen industry representatives, positively responding to issues of local concern.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","On the afternoon of May 23, Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Xia held a meeting lasting more than two hours. Both sides stressed that they must grasp the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain the resolve and confidence to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, earnestly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and continue to make new progress in cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” so that compatriots on both sides, especially grassroots people, benefit more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","The two sides reached a number of positive consensuses, which have been introduced in detail in the joint press conference and press release after the meeting, so I will not repeat them one by one here. I will only stress several main points. First, strengthen communication between the two sides' departments, continue to advance institutionalized cross-Strait consultations, hold the 11th meeting of the two sides' leaders as early as possible, and complete discussions on relevant topics and sign agreements as soon as possible. Second, further strengthen cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and create conditions for this. Third, expand and deepen exchanges across the Strait in economic, youth, and grassroots fields; promote discussions on the “mainland tourist transit” arrangement and strive to reach agreement by mid-year; and consult further on facilitating travel for compatriots on both sides, striving for progress. Fourth, the two sides exchanged views on issues of concern to each side and enhanced mutual understanding. In addition, the two sides also reached consensus on promoting water supply from Fujian to Kinmen and on strengthening and improving exchange and cooperation measures between Kinmen and Fujian. These outcomes and consensus are of great significance for further enhancing mutual trust across the Strait, deepening exchange and cooperation, effectively resolving livelihood issues, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Director Zhang's visit to Kinmen has drawn high attention from both sides of the Strait and the international community, and was warmly welcomed by the local people of Kinmen. The successful holding of this “Zhang-Xia Meeting” also shows that the communication mechanism between the two departments, the TAO and the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council, established on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” is operating well, and that the institutional development of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations continues to deepen, which has positive significance for stabilizing and developing cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, during Director Zhang Zhijun’s visit to Kinmen, local residents of Kinmen also raised some issues of concern and hoped the mainland side could help resolve them. Besides water supply from Fujian to Kinmen, they also proposed that the mainland give the “mini three links” more room for development, such as shortening customs clearance times for goods and opening direct air routes between Kinmen and the…","As just introduced, Director Zhang Zhijun's visit to Kinmen included an on-site inspection of Tianpu Reservoir and visits to the Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Distillery and the Gongtang and Gangdao shops. He actively responded to local concerns such as water supply from Fujian to Kinmen, fully demonstrating our high attention to Kinmen's livelihood issues and our sincerity in seeking well-being for grassroots compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nRegarding shortening cargo clearance time: recently, mainland customs authorities launched a special rectification of illegal and irregular practices in small-scale trade with Taiwan. We will fully consider the concerns of businesses on both sides and promote the standardized and healthy development of small-scale trade with Taiwan.\nRegarding opening direct flights from Kinmen to the mainland: Kinmen is already a passenger route point across the Strait, and there are no policy obstacles to flights between Kinmen and mainland points. Airlines on both sides may apply for flight frequencies in accordance with relevant regulations.\nWe welcome and actively support Kinmen's further close people-to-people exchanges with Xiamen and Fujian and the deepening of mutually beneficial cooperation, and we will work tirelessly together to improve cross-Strait livelihoods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899556.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen will visit the United States at the end of this month and articulate her so-called “maintaining the cross-Strait status quo” position. Some Taiwan public opinion holds that if the DPP and the U.S. side reach agreement on the so-called “cross-Strait status quo,” the mainland side may adjust its relevant views. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity are not divisible. Since 2008, cross-Strait relations have achieved peaceful development on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” This is the current state of cross-Strait relations. As for the DPP’s call to “maintain the cross-Strait status quo,” all sectors of Taiwan society are now asking: what exactly is the “cross-Strait status quo” that the DPP refers to? This is something they need to give a clear answer to.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899565.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","新华社记者","Kinmen has many cross-Strait marriage families, and the mainland spouses in these families are also very concerned about their rights and interests in Taiwan. When Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairman Xia Li-yan met in Kinmen, did they touch on this issue?","During Director Zhang's meeting with Chairman Xia, both sides discussed policy issues concerning people's livelihood. Director Zhang said that we are highly concerned about the legitimate rights and interests of mainland spouses in Taiwan. Some of Taiwan's regulations in this regard are overly harsh, such as restricting mainland spouses' parents from going to Taiwan to join their children, restricting eligibility for public office, and restricting employment. Mainland spouses are also family members of Taiwan compatriots, and we hope the Taiwan side will take active measures to genuinely address the appeals of mainland spouses. Director Zhang also expressed the hope that the Taiwan side would adjust relevant policies toward mainland students studying for degrees in Taiwan, including adjusting the “three limits and six nots” (三限六不) and discriminatory policies such as those on medical care. He hopes both sides will support expanded youth exchanges across the Strait and provide assistance to young people studying, interning, working and starting businesses on the other side.\nRegarding the strict review and restriction policies the Taiwan side applies to mainland capital, Director Zhang said he hopes the Taiwan side will adopt an open and positive attitude toward mainland capital, so as to help create win-win outcomes together.\nChairman Xia said the Taiwan side takes the above concerns of the mainland side seriously, and that the relevant issues are under study and being addressed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899561.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","福建《海峡导报》记者","When Director Chang Chih-chun recently visited Kinmen, he expressed hope that Kinmen would not develop a gambling industry, as otherwise the “mini three links” would certainly be affected. What further explanation does the spokesperson have on this?","On this issue, we have clearly stated our position on multiple occasions: the mainland strictly prohibits gambling. The “Measures for the Administration of Mainland Residents' Travel to the Taiwan Region” and the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Tourism for Mainland Residents to Taiwan” both stipulate that tour guides and tour operators must not be induced or organized to take part in gambling or other related activities. The mainland side will not allow residents to gamble in Taiwan; this is very clear. The mainland sincerely hopes, and will continue to promote, the healthy and stable development and steady expansion of cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation in Kinmen. When Director Zhang Zhijun visited Kinmen and held a symposium with industry representatives there, he also clearly expressed the mainland's sincerity. We do not wish to see Kinmen's tourism market, which has great potential, affected by the gaming industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899559.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","香港大公报大公网记者","Democratic Progressive Party Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen said yesterday that if the Democratic Progressive Party is in power, it will not give up sovereignty over the South China Sea, and she advocates resolving the South China Sea issue peacefully under international law. Ma Ying-jeou also proposed a \"South China Sea Peace Initiative\" on the same day and made five appeals. May I ask the spokesperson for your…","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have an obligation to jointly safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and to maintain peace and stability in the South China Sea region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","Just now the spokesperson introduced the positive outcomes achieved by the “Zhang-Xia meeting” and mentioned the issue of “transit of mainland tour groups,” saying efforts would be made to reach consensus by mid-year. Could the spokesperson share what specific plans there are in this regard?","Regarding the issue of “transit of mainland tourists” and further facilitating travel between compatriots on both sides, ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) have held two working consultations and one internal communication, achieving positive results. The two sides will continue to consult and make joint efforts to reach agreement by mid-year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","新京报记者","During Director Zhang Zhijun’s visit to Kinmen, the two sides reached consensus on water supply. Could you introduce the specific water supply plan in detail?","The mainland is very concerned about Kinmen's water shortage and has actively promoted the supply of water from Fujian to Kinmen. In June 2013, ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) reached common understandings on resolving Kinmen's water use problem at their ninth round of talks. Since then, relevant units in Fujian Province have held multiple rounds of communication with the Taiwan side, and the operating units on both sides have basically reached consensus on related matters. After Director Zhang and Chairperson Hsia Li-yan met and exchanged views, both sides agreed that the process should be accelerated. We hope the relevant units on both sides will sign the water supply and use contract as soon as possible and start construction of the project at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","中国国际广播电台记者","Second question: the Cross-Strait Small and Medium Enterprises Cooperation and Innovation Development Forum was recently held in Kaohsiung. Please introduce the outcomes achieved at this forum.","It is understood that the “Cross-Strait SME Cooperation and Innovation Development Forum,” held in Kaohsiung on May 21–22, was the first time the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit built a platform for SME exchange and cooperation in southern Taiwan. This is a very meaningful event.\nSheng Huaren, vice chairman of the Mainland Entrepreneurs Summit, introduced the mainland’s economic situation and development plans at the forum and expressed sincerity in promoting cross-Strait joint development. Representatives unanimously agreed that cross-Strait SMEs each have their own advantages in capital, technology, talent, and markets, and should join hands in innovation, improve cooperation platforms and mechanisms, jointly expand markets, and create win-win outcomes.\nThe Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will also continue to promote exchange and cooperation among cross-Strait SMEs. It has already planned to hold a “Cross-Strait SME Cooperation, Investment and Creative Products Exhibition and Negotiation Fair” during this November’s Zijin Mountain Summit, continuing to build bridges and provide assistance for the development of cross-Strait SMEs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201505/t20150527_9899555.htm"],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","台湾《中国时报》记者","May I ask the spokesperson: at the Kinmen “Zhang-Xia Meeting,” Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, also invited Xia Liyan, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, to visit the mainland. When will Xia Liyan visit the mainland? In addition, what is the progress of the “Twin City Forum” between Shanghai and Taipei, and is it possible to invite Mayor Ke Wenzhe to visit Shanghai? Thank you.","Chairman Hsia Li-yan has already said he will visit the mainland when it is convenient. The two departments will continue to communicate and consult on the specific schedule.\nOn the second question, Shanghai and Taipei have been in close communication on this, and information will be released once preparations are ready.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-05-27","Fan Liqing","台湾东森电视台记者","Yesterday the mainland issued the white paper “China's Military Strategy,” which also touched on the Taiwan issue. Could the spokesperson tell us how cross-strait relations will change after the release of the white paper? Will the two sides strengthen cooperation?","Regarding the white paper “China's Military Strategy,” the Ministry of National Defense gave a very detailed explanation at yesterday's press conference, which you may refer to.\nOur position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. In recent years, cross-Strait relations have shown a good situation of peaceful development, which has benefited the well-being of people on both sides and is conducive to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Our policy of promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will not change, and our resolve to curb “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes will not waver.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201505/t20150527_9899777.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to Taiwan media reports, DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen, during her visit to the United States, wrote in the Wall Street Journal that “a more stable, consistent and sustainable relationship with China” will be the focus of her governance, and that she wants to “engage comprehensively and on principled terms with China.” What is the TAO's comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in responding to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 3 (reporter Li Hanfang): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd: Our policy toward the DPP is clear and will not change. Opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the foundation of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Denying this foundation and persisting in the separatist “one country on each side” position of “Taiwan independence” will find no way out in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150603_9948750.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-06-05","Hong Lei","","According to media reports, during the visit of Tsai Ing-wen, the head of Taiwan's Democratic Progressive Party to the US, the US said that it would develop non-official relations with Taiwan and support the security of Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this?","The Chinese side holds a consistent and clear position on the Taiwan Question. We are staunchly opposed to anyone's engagement in \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities in any form on international occasions. It is hoped that the US side would abide by the one-China policy and the three joint communiqués between China and the US, stay firmly against \"Taiwan independence\", refrain from sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" forces, and make tangible efforts to support the peaceful development of the cross-Straits relations and the steady growth of China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1270836.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 10, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first introduced the progress of preparations for the 7th Straits Forum, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Strait.","Good morning, everyone. First, I would like to introduce the relevant situation of the Straits Forum to you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","At present, all preparations for the 7th Straits Forum are in place, and the forum congress will be held on June 14. Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, will attend the Straits Forum. Kuomintang Vice Chairman Hau Lung-bin, People First Party Secretary-General Chin Chin-sheng, New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming, Non-Partisan Solidarity Union Chairman Lin Ping-kun, relevant Taiwan county and city magistrates, county and city council speakers, representatives of Taiwan host units, and people from all walks of life, nearly 10,000 people in total, have been invited to attend this forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","This forum pays more attention to youth development and places greater emphasis on serving the grassroots. First, it is closer to the concerns and needs of cross-strait youth, and will hold activities including the exhibition of achievements from the Cross-Strait College Students Youth Creative Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition and the Youth New Media Cultural and Creative Forum, as well as multiple projects such as micro-films, healthy growth, entrepreneurship and “Internet+,” and summits on the integrated development of art education and new media. It has also invited Taiwan youth to Fujian to take part in the cross-strait youth cycling event “Riding the Most Beautiful Fujian.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005921.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Second, designing grassroots and folk-flavored activity projects such as villages sharing the same name and common ancestry, and folk religious culture. The scope of participation by grassroots groups on both sides of the Strait has continued to expand. For example, the number of Taiwan vendors participating in cross-Strait characteristic temple fairs has expanded from seven major night markets in five cities last year to 15 counties and cities, and mainland vendors have expanded from the Minnan Xiamen-Zhangzhou-Quanzhou area to nine prefecture-level cities in Fujian. A variety of colorful interactive activities have been arranged, including the Straits Forum Evening folk art performances, a cross-Strait food night market, a cross-Strait cultural and creative supermarket, and the “Children's Play Garden.” A new cross-Strait Disability Exchange Carnival has been added, inviting more than 20 Taiwan civil organizations and charities that assist persons with disabilities to participate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Third, closely following the trends in cross-Strait economic development, we have actively introduced hot topics of concern to society on both sides, and have made “Innovation and Cooperation in the Cross-Strait Free Trade Zone” the theme of this year's Cross-Strait Common Home Forum, to promote exchanges among industry peers across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear media friends, the Straits Forum has become a grand event for civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. You are welcome to go and cover it. We hope that through your pens and cameras you will report more on the stories of exchanges among grassroots people on both sides, their enthusiasm for participation, and the results of cooperation, so as to continue injecting positive energy into the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen has concluded her visit to the United States. Regarding the remarks she made on cross-Strait relations during her stay in the U.S., what evaluation does the spokesperson have?","We firmly oppose anyone carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally in any form. Our policy toward the DPP is clear and consistent. The DPP leader said all sorts of things about cross-Strait relations during this visit to the United States, but did not clearly address the most core issue. Opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and its core lies in recognizing that both the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. Cross-Strait relations are not a relationship between two countries. What the DPP most needs to answer clearly is: what is the relationship between the two sides of the Strait?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The first batch of Mainland undergraduates who studied in Taiwan will graduate this month, and many of them will return to the Mainland to seek employment and work. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Also, will you continue to encourage Mainland students to study in Taiwan?","Since the mainland opened degree-program study in Taiwan to mainland students in 2010, the first batch of mainland students studying in Taiwan will graduate this year. We sincerely hope that after they return to the mainland, they can all find positions where they can make use of their expertise, and that their intelligence and talents can be fully deployed in the development and construction of the mainland. We also hope they can both look up at the stars and keep their feet on the ground, and build their own careers in life. Of course, we also hope they will bring back the experiences and insights they gained from studying in Taiwan, continue to strengthen their ties with Taiwanese classmates, and contribute to cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. Our policy and attitude of encouraging and supporting cross-Strait educational exchange and cooperation have not changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","The China-South Korea Free Trade Agreement (FTA) was recently signed, and mainstream opinion in Taiwan holds that it will impact Taiwan’s economy and trade, and hopes that both sides of the Strait can quickly negotiate and sign follow-up ECFA agreements, such as on trade in goods. What attitude does the mainland hold on this?","We have stated before that our attitude toward continuously advancing the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation, and toward promoting the follow-up consultations on ECFA such as the trade in goods agreement, has been consistent and positive. We hope to continue strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and let Taiwan compatriots be the first to share the opportunities of the mainland market. In economic cooperation and development, moving one step ahead may allow one to seize more opportunities, while artificial obstruction and interference can only cause more opportunities to be lost. We hope that both sides will work together, move toward each other, take each other's concerns into account, reach an agreement at an early date, and enable the people of both sides to gain more tangible benefits on the basis of the ECFA Early Harvest Program.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005918.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The first Taiwan Business Development Forum was held in Zhangzhou, and one of its themes involved the transformation and upgrading of Taiwan-invested enterprises. Will the TAO take specific measures to help Taiwan businesses achieve transformation and upgrading?","In fact, we have been taking various measures to help and guide Taiwan-invested enterprises achieve transformation and upgrading on the mainland. These measures include a series of policies issued by local governments and relevant parties, as well as a series of lectures and guidance activities that the TAO has directed the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises to organize. This work will continue, and we will keep increasing our efforts, ultimately enabling Taiwan-invested enterprises to achieve sustainable and healthy development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Summer vacation is coming soon. Spokesperson, what important cross-Strait exchange activities have been planned and arranged recently, including those for the summer?","Amid the overall situation of continued peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations, personnel exchanges across the Strait and cooperation and exchanges in economic, cultural and other fields have further expanded and deepened. Since June, exchange activities across the Strait organized by relevant groups, institutions and local bodies have entered their busy season. According to information, in addition to the Straits Forum, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, together with relevant parties, will hold cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment inspection and discussion events in Shanghai, Hangzhou, Fuzhou and other places from June 8 to 11. Relevant mainland localities will exchange with Taiwan delegations on youth entrepreneurship and employment guidance policies, support measures and successful cases, explore cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment experiences, promote exchanges among cross-Strait entrepreneurship guidance institutions, and encourage Taiwan youth to start businesses and find jobs on the mainland.\nSeveral localities will hold Taiwan-related economic and trade events successively in July and August. Following the Chongqing Taiwan Week and the Yuntai Meeting, these will include the 8th Tianjin–Taiwan Investment Cooperation Negotiation Conference and the 2015 Tianjin·Taiwan Famous Products Expo, the 21st Lanzhou Investment and Trade Negotiation Fair, and the 14th Liaoning Taiwan Week.\nIn cultural exchanges, the “Connecting with the Silk Road, Holding Hands with Ningxia” series of activities will be held from July 7 to 16, and the “Cross-Strait Campus Classics Concert” will be held in Shanghai on July 18.\nIn educational exchanges, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots will hold the “Thousand-Person Summer Camp for Taiwan Compatriot Youth.” The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait will hold the “Chinese Culture Summer Study Camp” and a cross-Strait seminar on traditional culture education in universities. Peking University and Jilin University will hold summer schools and study camps, and the China Education International Exchange Association will hold the “Cross-Strait Youth Leaders Study Camp.” The “Yushan Program” of the China Association for Science and Technology and the “Taiwan University Students’ Zhongguancun Science Park Internship Camp” of the China Productivity Center will also offer Taiwan students valuable opportunities to intern on the mainland.\nIn sports exchanges, the 7th Xiamen–Kinmen Cross-Strait Swim, scheduled for August 1, has attracted more than 200 swimmers from both sides of the Strait.\nIn tourism exchanges, the “Chinese Civilization·Passing the Torch” mainland study tour for young students of Taiwan tertiary tourism programs will be held during the summer vacation, with a scale of nearly 500 people.\nIn folk belief exchanges, from June 6 to 17, the “Divine Image of the Shennong Emperor Ancestral Temple Tours Taiwan to Bestow Blessings” activity is taking place in Taiwan. On June 22, the “2015 (Yiwei Year) Public Ceremony to Honor Fuxi, Ancestor of Chinese Civilization” will be held in Tianshui, Gansu.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005914.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The Taipei office of the Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Exchange Association of the Ministry of Commerce will officially open its signboard in Taipei on the 16th of this month. What are the main functions of this office? Will it provide some positive help in promoting cross-Strait services trade and goods trade? Thank you.","The second economic and trade institution from the mainland to set up an office in Taiwan was arranged through consultation under the ECFA agreement, within the framework of the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee. Its functions and positioning are very clear and should be said to be consistent with those of the first office. I believe that the further increase and expansion of mutual office establishments by cross-Strait economic and trade institutions will play an important role in connecting economic and trade circles on both sides, facilitating exchanges of cross-Strait economic and trade policies and information, and jointly offering suggestions for deepening cross-Strait economic cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","What kind of platform does the Straits Forum hope to build for young people across the Strait?","I have just introduced the content related to youth exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the platform-building for cross-Strait youth cooperation in the various activities of this Straits Forum. You may have noticed that for some time, we have attached great importance to exchanges among cross-Strait youth and have taken some measures to provide further policy convenience for Taiwan youth to study, work and start businesses on the mainland. Moreover, we have also begun to organize and implement inspection activities for cross-Strait youth to start businesses and find jobs, to build more platforms for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to start businesses and find jobs. With these efforts, together with the active participation of cross-Strait youth, cross-Strait youth exchanges will certainly rise to a new level.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","香港文汇报记者","During Tsai Ing-wen's visit to Washington, senior U.S. officials met with Tsai Ing-wen one after another in their offices. What comment does the TAO have on this U.S. action?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position on this. We believe that some of the arrangements made by the US side are contrary to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The US side should genuinely abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and do more things that are conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005936.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Could the spokesperson tell us: the AIIB's articles of association will be published at the end of this month. Is there a more specific arrangement regarding the name and form of Taiwan's participation?","The articles of association of the AIIB are being drafted, and I do not know the specific details well. However, you may have noticed that we have repeatedly reaffirmed our welcome for Taiwan to join the AIIB under an appropriate designation. At the “Zhang-Xia meeting” recently held in Kinmen, both sides further exchanged views on this matter. We believe that through communication and consultation, the relevant issues will be properly handled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公报大公网记者","“Hong Kong independence” figure Chen Yun recently went to Taiwan to promote his “Hong Kong independence” remarks and colluded with certain “Taiwan independence” figures. Some public opinion is worried about this convergence of “Hong Kong independence” and “Taiwan independence.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment?","We firmly oppose any words and actions that attempt to undermine Hong Kong's political development, prosperity and stability, and cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Taiwan relations. This is our attitude and position.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","You just emphasized that we oppose anyone engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally. May I ask: in the TAO’s view, which of Tsai Ing-wen’s words and actions during her visit to the United States crossed the mainland’s bottom line? In addition, you just said that Tsai Ing-wen did not make the core issues clear; now Tsai has not mentioned the “1992 Consensus” and has only said that on…","I have already expressed an overall view just now. Here I want to emphasize that the “1992 Consensus” is a consensus reached in 1992 through the authorized representatives of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), through the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchange of letters, and it cannot be narrowed to a consensus between the KMT and the CCP. At the same time, the “1992 Consensus” is by no means an abstract concept, nor a historical term; it embodies both sides' basic attitude toward upholding the one-China principle. It is precisely because of this basic attitude that the two sides were able to seek common ground while setting aside differences, shelve disputes, and carry out consultations. It is also precisely because of this basic attitude that, since 2008, cross-Strait relations have been able to open new horizons on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and achieve a series of important progress. Peaceful development is not water without a source or a tree without roots. If the core meaning of this foundation is shaken, there can be no peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations. Therefore, the DPP needs to give a clear answer to compatriots on both sides: what is the relationship between the two sides of the Strait, what is the foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations, and how to maintain peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005927.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Statistics show that over the past six years, mainland capital investment in Taiwan has exceeded US$1 billion, which also demonstrates many positive effects of mainland investment in Taiwan. However, there is indeed a lot of inequality in two-way cross-strait investment. May I ask whether the two sides will further consult on the unequal treatment faced by mainland capital investing in Taiwan?","Promoting economic exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait is our consistent attitude and position, and mainland enterprises investing in Taiwan are also an important component of cross-Strait economic cooperation. Recently, when Director Zhang Zhijun met with Chairman Hsia Li-yan in Kinmen, both sides expressed their intention to further strengthen cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation and to create favorable conditions for this. Therefore, we hope the Taiwan side will, in keeping with this spirit, gradually remove the many unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, so that cross-Strait economic and trade relations can quickly move toward normalization, institutionalization, and liberalization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","香港文汇报记者","Some Taiwanese businesspeople have reported that they are very willing to participate in Belt and Road construction, but they struggle to find counterpart departments on the mainland. Which departments should they contact?","We welcome broad participation by Taiwanese businesses in the construction of the “Belt and Road.” This attitude is clear, and the policy is clear. The vision and action plan for the “Belt and Road” have now been issued, and there are responsible competent authorities. If Taiwanese businesses have consultation needs, they may inquire with the relevant competent authorities or local competent authorities. If they have specific wishes, they may also convey them to the TAO, and we are willing to pass them along and build bridges and make connections.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Tsai Ing-wen did not mention the “1992 Consensus,” but when she visited the US she said that if the DPP had the opportunity, it would continue to advance cross-Strait exchanges, including institutionalized talks between heads of cross-Strait affairs agencies. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Thank you.","We have stated on many occasions that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is built on opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and adhering to the \"1992 Consensus.\" The regular communication mechanism between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council is also built on the recognition of the \"1992 Consensus.\" Please everyone take note of this situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报团结网记者","We are paying close attention to the issue of mainland students. Some time ago, relevant officials of Taiwan’s education authorities said that Taiwan’s “three restrictions and six no’s” policy toward mainland students may be gradually abolished, retaining only two items. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The \"three restrictions and six non-s\" policy has indeed seriously harmed the rights and interests of mainland students studying in Taiwan. We of course hope that the Taiwan side can take practical measures to lift these unreasonable restrictions as soon as possible, provide mainland students studying in Taiwan with reasonable treatment, and safeguard and protect their due rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","In recent years, a number of Cross-Strait Exchange Bases have been established in various localities. It is my understanding that some new ones have recently been set up as well. Could the spokesperson please introduce the situation in this regard?","To create more platforms for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council decided in June this year to add six Cross-Strait Exchange Bases, namely: Xiwangmu Palace in Jingchuan, Gansu Province; the Huangdi Hometown in Xinzheng, Henan Province; Lingshan in Wuxi, Jiangsu Province; Xuedoushan in Fenghua, Zhejiang Province; the museum of the “National Southwest Associated University” in Yunnan Province; and the Qu Yuan Hometown Cultural Park in Zigui, Hubei Province. As of now, there are 43 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases, providing more options for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to look back on history, savor culture, and share family affection during their exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150610_10005917.htm"],[2,"2015-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Some media reported that this year’s Cross-Strait Peace Forum may be cancelled due to electoral factors. Please confirm whether it will be cancelled, and what the reason for the cancellation is.","The Cross-Strait Peace Forum was jointly initiated by 14 cross-Strait civil groups and academic institutions. According to my understanding from relevant mainland units, at the request of the Taiwan organizers, the second Cross-Strait Peace Forum is planned to be postponed, and the specific date will be determined through consultation between both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150610_10006286.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18 (reporter Li Hanfang). Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on June 18, regarding the implementation of the policy of exempting Taiwan residents from endorsements for travel to the mainland and issuing card-format Taiwan compatriot permits, that the introduction of this measure demonstrates the mainland’s sincere concept and service purpose of caring for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and doing practical and good things for them. We believe the implementation of this measure will provide greater convenience for cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, and will help compatriots on both sides draw ever closer.\nHe said that on May 4 this year, General Secretary Xi Jinping, meeting with Chu Li-luan, Chairman of the Kuomintang, said, “We will implement further measures to facilitate travel between compatriots on both sides at an appropriate time.” On June 14, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng announced at the opening ceremony of the 7th Straits Forum that the mainland would exempt Taiwan residents from endorsements for travel to the mainland and would implement card-format Taiwan compatriot permits at an appropriate time.\nAccording to the Decision of the State Council on Amending the 《Administrative Measures for Travel of Chinese Citizens to the Taiwan Region》, starting July 1, Taiwan residents holding valid Mainland Travel Permits may travel to the mainland through open ports and stay or reside in the mainland without applying for endorsements. It is expected that card-format Taiwan compatriot permits will be implemented on a pilot basis this year. At that point, Taiwan residents will be able to enter and exit through ports with self-service verification facilities, making travel even more convenient.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150618_10066394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18 (reporter Zha Wenye) — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to comments on June 18 regarding the Kuomintang Central Standing Committee’s approval of the nomination of Hung Hsiu-chu as its candidate for the 2016 Taiwan presidential election, said: We have noted the relevant reports. We do not interfere in or comment on Taiwan’s elections. We hope that, on the basis of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will continue to be maintained, and cross-Strait relations will continue to advance peacefully.\nHe said that any political party or individual in Taiwan, as long as they oppose “Taiwan independence,” endorse the “1992 Consensus,” and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, is welcome.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150618_10066395.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalists, good morning. Today’s press conference now begins. I am willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The spokesperson previously introduced that the 7th Straits Forum paid more attention to youth development, emphasized serving the grassroots, and more closely followed the trend of cross-Strait economic development. The forum has now concluded. What results did this forum achieve in the above areas?","The 7th Straits Forum concluded on June 19 and achieved a series of fruitful results. I will briefly introduce some policy “highlights” in four areas:\nFirst, new measures were introduced to facilitate exchanges and travel between people on both sides. At the Forum's plenary session, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng announced that residents of Taiwan will be exempt from visa requirements for travel to the mainland, and that card-format Taiwan compatriot travel permits will be implemented at an appropriate time. This will provide more convenience for exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides and has been warmly welcomed by them.\nSecond, a new platform for employment and entrepreneurship for young people across the Strait was established. More than 1,000 representatives of cross-Strait youth groups, entrepreneurs, and students participated in the various youth activities organized by this Forum. Fujian Province issued the “Opinions on Encouraging and Supporting Taiwan Youth in Starting Businesses and Finding Employment in Fujian,” which provides support to Taiwan youth coming to Fujian to start businesses and find jobs in nine areas. Zhou Haijiang, vice chairman of the All-China Federation of Industry and Commerce and president of Hodo Group, announced at the Forum's plenary session the establishment of the “Chain Brand Hodo Entrepreneurship Fund” with a total amount of RMB 100 million to support Taiwan youth in starting businesses on the mainland. The Fujian Provincial Committee of the Communist Youth League and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone initiated the founding of the Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Alliance, which currently has 186 cross-Strait youth startups settled in it, of which 130 are Taiwanese civic and institutional organizations that have signed agreements to settle in, covering tourism, cultural and creative industries, agriculture, the Internet of Things, and many other fields. The Cross-Strait Youth Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Maker Base was unveiled in Haicang, Xiamen, where 15 enterprises have completed registration and 27 more are in the process of registering. Taiwan youth in the base will enjoy a series of preferential policies.\nThird, exchanges among grassroots communities across the Strait have become deeper. Fujian has established friendship ties with more than 50 pairs of villages in Taiwan that share the same name and ancestry. This year, six pairs of cross-Strait villages and neighborhood committees have signed cooperation agreements to promote joint community governance and construction across the Strait. Public-welfare organizations on both sides have set up a cross-Strait youth psychology expert think tank and established a linkage mechanism for major disaster response among cross-Strait public-welfare institutions. Persons with disabilities from both sides held exchange activities at the Forum for the first time, and the temple fairs with distinctive cross-Strait features attracted a total of 700,000 participants.\nFourth, new channels for mutually beneficial cross-Strait economic cooperation were opened. The State Food and Drug Administration announced that the acceptance and approval of registration applications for Taiwan-made Chinese herbal medicines that have been on the market in Taiwan for more than 20 years, as well as the filing of some Taiwan-made Class I medical devices, will be entrusted to the Fujian Provincial Food and Drug Administration, to facilitate Taiwan-made Chinese herbal medicines and medical devices entering the mainland market. In connection with the construction of the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone, Fujian Province has issued a series of policies and measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, such as raising the subsidy standard for Taiwan farmers' entrepreneurship parks starting in 2015. In addition, during this Straits Forum, 25 science, technology and economic cooperation projects, 20 tea trade and cooperation projects, and 11 cross-Strait film and television cooperation projects were signed, and two pairs of banks in Xiamen and Taiwan signed a cooperation agreement on cross-border renminbi business to promote cross-border internet financial cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150624_10105316.htm"],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The Central Standing Committee of the Kuomintang recently approved the nomination of Hung Hsiu-chu as the KMT's candidate for Taiwan's 2016 presidential election. What is the spokesperson's comment on Hung Hsiu-chu's cross-Strait position?","As everyone knows, we do not interfere in Taiwan’s elections. Since 2008, both sides across the Taiwan Strait have promoted a new situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations and achieved a series of important results. The key lies in establishing the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Its core is recognition that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. We hope that on this basis, peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will be maintained, and peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will continue to advance. Any political party or individual in Taiwan that opposes “Taiwan independence,” endorses the “1992 Consensus,” and adheres to the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is welcome.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150624_10105327.htm"],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Regarding the implementation of visa-free entry for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland and the implementation of card-style Taiwan compatriot permits within this year, some remarks on the island say the purpose of this policy is to make “Taiwan Hong Kong-ized” and Taiwan residents “mainland citizens.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","In recent days, the \"Decision of the State Council on Amending the Measures for the Administration of Travel by Chinese Citizens to Taiwan,\" the statement and Q&A by the responsible person of the National Immigration Administration of the Ministry of Public Security, have given a detailed and clear account of the policy measures and implementing rules for exempting Taiwan compatriots from visa requirements when traveling to the mainland and for issuing card-format Taiwan compatriot travel permits. Everyone can consult the relevant Xinhua News Agency reports. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We are implementing this policy to further facilitate exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides and to promote exchanges among them. It serves the well-being of the people on both sides. It has therefore been widely welcomed by people on both sides, especially the broad mass of Taiwan people, and has been highly praised by Taiwan's mainstream media.\nI must point out that the card-format Taiwan compatriot travel permit is an electronic upgrade of the current paper Taiwan compatriot travel permit, which is valid for 5 years. The name of the document, \"Taiwan Residents Travel Permit to and from the Mainland,\" has not changed, and its function as an entry-exit document has not changed; its validity period remains 5 years. Once the card-format permit is issued, Taiwan residents will be able to use it for self-service entry and exit, making travel even more convenient.\nAs for any measures that help exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides, \"Taiwan independence\" politicians are terrified and extremely resentful. However, their misleading remarks that distort basic facts also greatly underestimate the judgment of the Taiwan people, and therefore are not worth refuting, or even worth a smile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150624_10105326.htm"],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The mainland side has already proposed inviting some KMT veterans to attend the September 3 military parade. Are these KMT veterans referring to those on the mainland, or do they broadly include KMT veterans in Taiwan? Some retired generals in Taiwan may also attend, but the Taiwan military has begun to gently discourage them from coming. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's view?","Yesterday, at a press conference held by the State Council Information Office, responsible officials of the relevant departments introduced the arrangements for the mainland's activities marking the 70th anniversary of the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan and the world anti-fascist war. The Taiwan Affairs Office has repeatedly pointed out and emphasized that the victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan was a great victory of the entire nation, and both the battlefields behind enemy lines and the front battlefields played an important role. Under new historical conditions, we hope that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will, by jointly commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance, remember the martyrs, keep history in mind, carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, safeguard its achievements, unite and work together in common cause, and jointly commit to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. As for the specific arrangements of some related activities, they will be announced in due course once determined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","The Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) between the two sides will reach its fifth anniversary of signing at the end of this month. Could the spokesperson introduce the results achieved over these five years?","Five years since the signing of ECFA, positive progress has been made in the early harvest of goods trade, the early harvest of services trade, investment protection and promotion, industrial cooperation, customs cooperation, cooperation among small and medium-sized enterprises, and the mutual establishment of representative offices by economic and trade associations, as well as in the negotiation of follow-up agreements. This has brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and has also produced mutually beneficial results for cross-Strait economic cooperation.\nEarly-harvest products under the ECFA goods trade agreement have all been reduced to zero tariffs since January 1, 2013. As of the end of March 2015, the mainland had imported from Taiwan goods enjoying ECFA tariff preferences worth a cumulative US$38 billion, with tariffs reduced or exempted by RMB 14.15 billion. According to Taiwan customs statistics, the mainland had exported to Taiwan goods enjoying ECFA tariff preferences worth a cumulative US$6.47 billion, enjoying tariff preferences of NT$7.28 billion (about US$240 million). 46 Taiwanese financial enterprises and 321 non-financial enterprises have used early-harvest preferential policies to provide services on the mainland, while 3 mainland financial enterprises and 141 non-financial enterprises have used early-harvest preferential policies to provide services in Taiwan. The Industrial Cooperation Working Group under the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Committee has eight industry subgroups, covering automobiles, wireless cities, cold chain logistics, displays, LED lighting, textiles, pharmaceuticals, and e-commerce, to advance pilot projects and major cooperation projects. The cross-Strait customs electronic information exchange system has gone online, and customs clearance efficiency for goods across the Strait has improved substantially. The two sides' customs authorities have also jointly resolved some cases in which ECFA preferential tariff rates could not be applied due to third-party trade, enabling more operators to benefit from ECFA. Since 2011, exports to the mainland of goods on Taiwan's early-harvest list have increased year by year, with export growth rates consistently well above the growth rate of overall goods exports. Among them, exports to the mainland of early-harvest products from the petrochemical, textile, and machinery manufacturing industries have continued to grow, and exports of major agricultural products to the mainland have increased enormously.\nAt present, within the ECFA follow-up agreements, both sides have signed the Cross-Strait Agreement on Investment Protection and Promotion, the Cross-Strait Customs Cooperation Agreement, and the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services; negotiations on the cross-Strait goods trade and dispute settlement agreements have also made progress to varying degrees. We hope both sides will work together, meet each other halfway, and as soon as possible complete the entry-into-force procedures for signed agreements and the negotiation of the various follow-up agreements, so as to create more opportunities for mutually beneficial cooperation for compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150624_10105321.htm"],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","At last month's “Zhang-Xia Meeting,” Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, and Xia Li-yan, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, reached eight points of consensus, including issues related to “mainland tourists transiting” through Taiwan. What is the current progress?","At present, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) are holding consultations in Taipei on the topic of “mainland residents transiting through Taiwan and further facilitating exchanges between compatriots on both sides.” We hope both sides can, on the basis of the consensus reached at the meeting of the heads of cross-Strait affairs authorities, move toward each other and push for early progress in these consultations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The consensus reached by Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairman Hsia Li-yan includes starting the 11th leaders’ meeting of the two associations as early as possible, and launching the project to supply water from Fujian to Kinmen. Please introduce the progress on these two issues.","Regarding the 11th meeting between the leaders of the two associations, both sides have maintained close contact and communication and are already actively preparing for the relevant issues. We hope the two associations will work together, achieve results, make arrangements, and strive to hold the 11th meeting as soon as possible and sign new agreements.\nRegarding the water supply to Kinmen: During his visit to Kinmen, Director Zhang inspected the water receiving point of the Kinmen water supply project, namely the Tianpu Reservoir, demonstrating that the mainland will advance this work with the attitude and sincerity of “we are one family, drinking from the same river.” It is understood that the two sides' operating units will hold the next round of consultations after completing their respective procedures, striving to sign the water supply contract as early as possible and to start construction of the project as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港文汇报记者","Recently, Ma Ying-jeou said that regarding the mutual establishment of offices across the Strait, the mainland holds a defensive attitude and worries that Taiwan has political intentions. How do you comment on this?","In the more than two years since the two associations began talks on establishing liaison offices in each other’s territory, important progress has been made. The two sides have reached basic consensus on the purposes, positioning, and main functions of the offices, and have also achieved considerable results on the main content of the agreement text. We still adhere to our consistent attitude and hope that both sides will continue active communication and move toward the goal of completing the consultations as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾三立电视台记者","I would like to ask the spokesperson: you just mentioned that the card-style Taiwan compatriot permit is a redesign of the paper Taiwan compatriot permit valid for five years, and that the name has not changed. I would like to further ask whether it has added functions that are more convenient for people, and what the functional differences are from before?","I suggest you consult the specific implementing departments on professional questions. As I understand it, compared with paper documents, it is more portable, and in the future it can also be used for self-service clearance. Of course, I also noted that the head of the public security authorities pointed out in his remarks that the design of this card-format document follows current international standards, and it can be said to conform to the development trend of travel documents today and their corresponding functions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan’s reaction to Chairman Yu Zhengsheng’s announcement that Taiwan compatriots will be exempt from visa endorsements and that a card-format Taiwan compatriot permit will be introduced in due course seemed somewhat caught off guard. Does this mean there is a problem with the liaison and communication mechanism between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council?","Providing convenience for exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is our consistent policy position, and over the years we have successively introduced a series of positive measures to this end. In accordance with the wishes and demands of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, we recently announced the implementation of this policy. We believe it will provide greater convenience for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and for exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and it will also help bring compatriots on both sides ever closer together. At the same time, we also hope that both sides will move toward each other, so that exchanges between compatriots on both sides become smoother and more convenient.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中国网记者","Around September 3, a symposium commemorating the victory in the War of Resistance will be held for compatriots from Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan and relevant overseas personages, and an international academic seminar will be held on major issues concerning the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the world’s anti-fascist war. May I ask the spokesperson: will the Taiwan Affairs Office…","As I understand it, preparations for the activity you mentioned are underway, and we will announce it at an appropriate time once there is a definite date. One thing is certain: we welcome Taiwan compatriots and people from all walks of life, including veterans who took part in the War of Resistance and their relatives and descendants, to come to the mainland to participate in the relevant commemorative activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201506/t20150624_10105645.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-06-25","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","My question is also about the military parade to be held on September 3. During the press conference held by the Information Office of the State Council several days ago, it is said that the veterans of the Nationalist Party will be invited to take part in the parade. Does this mean that the veterans of the Nationalist Party in Taiwan will be invited to take part in the military parade? If they will be invited,…","The armed forces of the Nationalist Party had played an important role in the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression. Some veterans of the Nationalist Party will be invited to take part in the military parade. As to the specific arrangements, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council answered this question yesterday.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-06/25/content_4591733.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-06-25","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On the activities to commemorate the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression in September, will people from Taiwan be invited to attend the activities? If you have issued invitation to people from Taiwan, have you got any response from those people?","About inviting people from Taiwan to attend the commemorative activities, please refer to competent authorities for information.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-06/25/content_4591733.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-06-25","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On June 18, the U.S. Senate passed the Defense Budget Request for Fiscal Year 2016, which includes an additional item of inviting Taiwan to take part in military exercises. May I know your response and your comment on that?\nSecondly, we have learnt that the Liaoning aircraft carrier has gone on training at sea. Please tell us the contents of the Liaoning aircraft carrier’s training mission this time and what…","On the first question, we are firmly opposed to any country developing military ties with Taiwan in any form, and this position is consistent and clear.\nWe urge the U.S. to observe the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, take a prudent attitude in dealing with the Taiwan issue and take concrete actions in maintaining the overall interests of China-US state-to-state and military-to-military relations.\nOn the issue of the Liaoning aircraft carrier’s training at sea, I do not have any information to release.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-06/25/content_4591733.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2015-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhuanet, Beijing, June 28 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — A dust explosion at a facility in New Taipei, Taiwan, injured four mainland residents. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang told Xinhua reporters on the morning of the 28th that ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation will remain in contact and, together with relevant parties, assist the families of the injured mainland residents in traveling to Taiwan. On the evening of the 27th, a fire broke out during an event at the Formosa Fun Coast in New Taipei City, causing a combustible dust explosion that has so far left 516 people injured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150628_10130047.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 29 (reporter Chen Jianxing): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 29th, saying that the AIIB Agreement embodies the consensus among prospective founding members. We are pleased to see the AIIB handle the issue of Taiwan's accession in accordance with its Agreement. Continued communication between the two sides helps to better resolve the issue of Taiwan's accession to the AIIB.\nThe AIIB Agreement was signed in Beijing on the 29th. A reporter asked Ma Xiaoguang about the mainland's further considerations regarding Taiwan joining the AIIB in the future, and Ma gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201506/t20150629_10139776.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-07-06","Hua Chunying","","Ma Ying-jeou was quoted as saying that the Kuomintang was mainly responsible for the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. What's your comment on this? Which party do you think played the decisive role in the war, the Communist Party or the Kuomintang?","The great victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was won thanks to the united struggle of all compatriots of the Chinese nation and should be commemorated and remembered by all Chinese people.\nIn the recent press conference held by the State Council Information Office, officials from related departments briefed on the specific arrangements for the activities commemorating the 70th anniversary of the end of the World Anti-Fascist War and the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. By holding such commemorations, we hope to join the rest of the world to remember history, recall the martyrs, cherish peace and open up to the future.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1278960.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-07-08","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, while attending a seminar on the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, Taiwan leader Ma Ying-jeou stated that China resumed its sovereignty over islands in the South China Sea according to relevant international legal documents including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender.…","China's sovereignty and relevant claims of rights in the South China Sea are formed in the long course of history based on international legal grounds. After the Second World War, the then Chinese government made great efforts in taking back the South China Sea islands and safeguarding China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in the South China Sea. Since the founding of the PRC, the Chinese government has been committed to safeguarding China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in the South China Sea, and made active contribution to upholding peace, stability and freedom of navigation in the South China Sea.\nIn the current context, Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Straits have the responsibility and obligation to jointly safeguard our territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1279708.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-07-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 24 (Reporter Chen Jianxing): In response to Lee Teng-hui's recent public speech in Japan advocating “Taiwan independence,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 24th when answering reporters' questions: We firmly oppose any country providing a stage for “Taiwan independence” activities, and we are deeply dissatisfied with Japan for allowing Lee Teng-hui to make a visit to Japan.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Lee Teng-hui publicly made “Taiwan independence” remarks, glorified Japan's colonial rule over Taiwan, and falsely claimed that the Diaoyu Islands belong to Japan, which was unanimously condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. His despicable words and deeds have made compatriots on both sides even more clearly see the extreme harmfulness of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to the overall interests of the Chinese nation, and they will surely be spurned by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201507/t20150727_10337581.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-08-03","Fan Liqing","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (reporter Zha Wenye) -- Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responding on the 3rd to remarks by Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je on the \"1992 Consensus,\" said: We have noted the relevant reports. The core meaning of the \"1992 Consensus\" is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Cross-strait exchanges are not international exchanges. Since 2008, on the basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" both sides have promoted a series of important achievements in the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. As long as both sides uphold the existing political foundation, cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, including exchanges between Shanghai and Taipei, will certainly make positive progress.\nTaipei Mayor Ko Wen-je, in an interview with relevant media on the 3rd, said that he understands and respects the mainland's position that the \"1992 Consensus\" is the basis for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. He also said that exchanges between Taipei and Shanghai are exchanges between cross-strait cities. The Taipei municipal government's Mainland Affairs Group handles mainland affairs, while a separate International Affairs Group handles foreign matters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201508/t20150803_10393757.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-08-07","Fan Liqing","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The leader of the People First Party has announced participation in Taiwan's 2016 election. May I ask whether the mainland still invites him to attend the September 3 commemorative events marking the 70th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance? Fan Liqing gave the above response when asked.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 7 (Reporter Zhao Bo): Fan Liqing, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to questions on the 7th: “We do not interfere in Taiwan's elections.” Invitations to Taiwan-related personnel to attend events held in the mainland are also handled in this manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201508/t20150810_10439732.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-08-21","Fan Liqing","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question: some people on the island believe that this year’s Shanghai–Taipei “Twin City Forum” has formed a new model of cross-strait exchanges, and that the mainland no longer insists that Taiwan must accept the “1992 Consensus” as a political precondition. What is your comment? Fan Liqing made the above remarks in response to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 21 (dateline). Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Fan Liqing said on the 21st that adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This is our consistent position and it will not change.\nFan Liqing said that during the Shanghai-Taipei “Twin City Forum,” Shanghai municipal leaders stated that they must firmly adhere to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and actively promote anything that benefits the well-being of the people on both sides of the Strait. Mayor Ko Wen-je said that he has consistently upheld the spirit that both sides of the Strait are one family, and the principles of mutual understanding, mutual respect, and mutual cooperation. He hopes to promote exchanges on the existing political foundation shared by both sides and to promote peaceful development across the Strait. He will not refuse anything that benefits the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201508/t20150822_10526404.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-08-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","During the parade, the veterans of the Communist Party and the Kuomintang Party will be reviewed together. What is the significance of such an arrangement and how can we carry forward the spirit of the Anti-aggression War?","During the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the press conferences of the Information Office of the State Council, relevant spokespersons have responded to similar questions. The victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression is a victory for the whole Chinese nation. I have noticed that when the vehicles carrying the veterans of both the Communist Party and the Kuomintang Party passed the Tiananmen Square during the dress rehearsal on Aug.23, many people rose to their feet voluntarily. They either saluted or applauded to the veterans to pay their tribute to them.\nAnd I think this fully demonstrated all Chinese people’s respect and admiration for the veterans. In this new historical period, I hope that through commemorating the victory together, compatriots from across the Taiwan Strait can carry forward the spirit of the Anti-aggression War, keep the history in mind, cherish the memory of the martyrs and join hands to make contributions to the peaceful development of relations across the Taiwan Strait and also to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-08/27/content_4616171.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-08-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lian Zhan, the former Honorary Chairman of the Kuomintang Party, expressed his willingness to attend the military parade to be held on Sept 3. His reason was that he attached great importance to the historical significance of the anti-aggression war and he also wished that the peaceful development of the relationship across the Taiwan Strait could be maintained. But, Hao Bocun, the other high-ranking KMT official…","During the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, the forces led by the Communist Party and the Kuomintang Party of China undertook the combat tasks in the backstage battlefield and in the center stage battlefield respectively. They supported and cooperated with each other to form a strategic momentum of all-out resistance against Japanese aggression. By advocating the establishment of the United National Front against Japanese Aggression and leading its army and people to establish the broad backstage battlefield. The Communist Party of China has made great sacrifice to the victory of the Anti-Aggression War and played a vital role.\nTherefore, we regard the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression as a victory for the whole Chinese nation. We welcome compatriots from Taiwan to join relevant commemorative activities.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-08/27/content_4616171.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-08-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It was mentioned that Lian Zhan will attend the parade on Sept. 3 as a civilian. Will he be arranged on the reviewing stand?","As I have just mentioned, we welcome compatriots from Taiwan to take part in relevant commemorative activities. As for the specifics, I’d like to advise you to refer to my colleagues in the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-08/27/content_4616171.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2015-08-28","Fan Liqing","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question about media reports that Lien Chan, former chairman of the KMT, will go to Beijing to attend the commemorative activities for the 70th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance, and will meet General Secretary Xi Jinping during this period, and asked for confirmation: TAO spokesperson Fan Liqing responded on the 28th: We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to attend…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 28 (reporter Li Hanfang).\nFan Liqing said: This year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland. The mainland side will hold a series of grand commemorative activities. It is understood that former Chairman of the Kuomintang Lien Chan, veterans of the War of Resistance and representatives of their bereaved families, representatives of Taiwan-born anti-Japanese War heroes and their bereaved families, and representatives of all sectors of Taiwan society will be invited to attend the commemorative activities.\nVictory in the War of Resistance was a victory for the entire nation, and all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, made enormous sacrifices for it. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait, by commemorating the victory in the War of Resistance, will remember history, honor the martyrs, carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, and work together to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201508/t20150828_10569219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-08-28","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 28 (reporter Li Hanfang): On the afternoon of the 27th, a tourist bus carrying mainland tourists was involved in a traffic accident in Pingtung County, Taiwan, killing one mainland tourist and injuring 15 others. Fan Liqing, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, told reporters on the 28th: “We mourn the deceased mainland tourist and extend our sympathy to the injured.”\nShe said that upon learning of the accident, the Taiwan Affairs Office, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, and the National Tourism Administration immediately activated emergency response mechanisms, verified the casualties, communicated with the Taiwan side, and demanded that the Taiwan side do its utmost to treat the injured. They also helped families travel to Taiwan as soon as possible to visit, and properly handled insurance claims and other follow-up matters. “We will continue to follow the progress of this matter and hope the injured tourists recover soon.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201508/t20150828_10569816.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-09-03","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After cutting 300,000 personnel, China still has the world's largest military. Why still maintain such a large scale?","As a large developing country, China still faces diverse and complex security threats. Survival security and development security, and traditional and non-traditional security threats, are intertwined. The tasks of safeguarding national unity, territorial integrity and development interests are arduous and heavy. At the same time, our military also undertakes non-war military operations such as emergency rescue and disaster relief, international peacekeeping and international rescue. We also have to deal with threats from regional terrorism, separatism and extremism. Therefore, our military needs to maintain a certain scale, which is entirely for defensive purposes. We will not follow the old path of “a strong country seeks hegemony.” We will never seek hegemony and never engage in expansion. Some countries deliberately hype the “China threat,” which runs counter to objective facts and is irresponsible.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2015-09/03/content_4617698.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2015-09-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO Spokesperson Responds on Inviting People from Taiwan's All Sectors to Attend Commemorative Activities for the 70th Anniversary of the Victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War\nOn September 4, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to the invitation to people from all sectors in Taiwan to attend commemorative activities for the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War that the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was the first complete victory of China's resistance to foreign invasion in modern times, and it made a major contribution to the victory of the world anti-fascist war. Commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance is to remember history, honor the martyrs, cherish peace, and create the future.\nThe victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan was a victory of the great unity of the Chinese nation. The Kuomintang and the Communist Party cooperated to establish the Anti-Japanese National United Front. All Chinese sons and daughters, regardless of party, nationality, class, or region, united against the common enemy and shared the national crisis. Countless predecessors advanced courageously, facing death without flinching, and defended national sovereignty and national dignity with their blood and lives. The frontal battlefield and the enemy-rear battlefield coordinated with each other and fought together, and a large number of heroes who stirred the nation emerged. The anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots was an important component of the all-nation war of resistance; it paid enormous sacrifices for the victory of the war and made important contributions. All the martyrs who bravely gave their lives for the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan will always be remembered by history.\nOn September 2, General Secretary Xi Jinping especially pointed out in his speech at the ceremony awarding the commemorative medal for the 70th anniversary of the victory of the War of Resistance: during the 14 years of resistance against Japanese militarist aggression, and especially the 8 years of all-out war of resistance, amid arduous years, all Chinese sons and daughters united as one and built a common resolve to resist external aggression and save the nation from perishing, writing a magnificent epic that moved heaven and earth and stirred the nation. Many anti-Japanese martyrs and heroes emerged, including Yang Jingyu, Zhao Shangzhi, Zuo Quan, Peng Xuefeng, Tong Linge, Zhao Dengyu, Zhang Zhongren, and Dai Anlan, as well as the “Five Heroes of Langya Mountain” of the Eighth Route Army, the “Liu Laozhuang Company” of the New Fourth Army, the eight female soldiers of the Northeast Anti-Japanese United Army, and the “Eight Hundred Heroes” of the Nationalist army, along with many other groups of heroes. Whether on the frontal battlefield or the enemy-rear battlefield, whether fighting directly or providing support from the rear, all who took part in the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression are war heroes and national heroes.\nIn the September 3 military parade, the vehicle formations of veterans of the War of Resistance, children of heroes, and model supporters of the front included both veteran fighters of the Chinese Communist Party and veteran fighters of the Kuomintang. People gave warm applause to all of them.\nIn commemorating the victory of the war, we must learn from history to better understand peace and firmly resolve to safeguard peace. General Secretary Xi Jinping solemnly declared that the mainland of China will cut its armed forces by 300,000 personnel, fully demonstrating our sincerity and determination in pursuing and safeguarding peace.\nThe participation of people from all sectors of Taiwan in commemorative activities helps compatriots on both sides, from the height of the overall interests of the entire nation, to remember the lessons of history and carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance. Strengthening communication under the current cross-Strait situation and continuing to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is important.\nWe know that compatriots on both sides still have differences over the historical evaluation of the War of Resistance and other issues, but these should not affect the process and atmosphere of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Facing these differences, scholars from both sides can strengthen exchanges and discussions through the approach of “sharing historical materials and compiling history together,” seeking common ground while reserving differences, and gradually resolving disagreements.\nSeventy years ago, all Chinese sons and daughters, regardless of party, united as one to resist external aggression, writing a magnificent chapter of all-nation resistance. Seventy years later, we have even more reason to believe that compatriots on both sides can overcome all prejudice and differences, focus on the overall situation and future of national rejuvenation, work together with one heart, continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. This is also the historical responsibility that all responsible political parties and political figures on both sides of the Strait should shoulder.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150905_10608592.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","It is reported that the mainland military will hold live-fire exercises in the Taiwan Strait from September 11 to 13, which has aroused concern across all sectors of Taiwan. Please ask the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office to explain or respond.","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 10th to the question of the mainland military conducting live-fire exercises in the Taiwan Strait, saying: This training was arranged according to the annual plan. Ma Xiaoguang said: It is understood that recently, units of the Fujian Military Region will conduct a routine live-fire shooting training in nearshore waters. This training was arranged according to the annual plan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150911_10650690.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning! After a summer vacation, it has been a long time. I will host today’s press conference, and first I would like to extend my greetings to all of you. Next, I am willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Starting July 1, the mainland began exempting Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland from visa endorsement. Yesterday the Ministry of Public Security issued a notice that card-format Taiwan compatriot permits will be fully implemented. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On September 15, the mainland public security authorities issued an announcement that starting September 21, the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit will be fully implemented. Public security organs at or above the county level began accepting applications, and the issuance of the booklet-format permit ceased. Public security authorities in various places may reissue or renew five-year-valid card-format Taiwan compatriot permits for Taiwan residents on the mainland. Booklet-format Taiwan compatriot permits that remain valid may continue to be used without endorsement, and their holders may also apply to renew them for card-format permits. In addition, ports with permit-processing agencies will continue to provide one-time valid Taiwan compatriot permit services for Taiwan residents who arrive directly at the port without a valid permit. After the full implementation of the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit, we believe travel between Taiwan residents and the mainland will become more convenient, and stays and residence on the mainland will be easier. We also believe that this measure facilitating exchanges between compatriots on both sides will have a profound impact on the future development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681545.htm"],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The spokesperson is asked: Cross-Strait exchanges have remained active since the beginning of this year. What important cross-Strait exchange activities will there be in the coming period?","At present, cross-Strait exchanges maintain a good momentum of development, with exchange activities flourishing in all fields. It is understood that in September, the following will be held: the Taiwan Week in Wuhan, Hubei; the Cross-Strait Information Industry and Technology Standards Forum; the Western Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cooperation Exchange Conference; the Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum; and the 8th Cross-Strait Choral Festival. In addition, a series of commemorative activities marking the 130th anniversary of Liu Mingchuan's appointment as the first Governor of Taiwan will be held in Hefei, Anhui Province, Liu's hometown, where people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait will jointly commemorate this forerunner who made outstanding contributions to defending national dignity, maintaining the territorial integrity of the country, and building Taiwan.\nEntering October, the following will also be held: the Hunan-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cooperation Exchange Conference; the 2015 Cross-Strait Chinese Character Art Festival; the 8th Straits Forum on Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Expo and Trading Fair; the Strait Baseball Exchange Match, which young people love; the Cross-Strait Science and Technology Service Industry Development Cooperation Forum; the 2015 Tianjin-Taiwan Higher Education Summit Forum; and the 4th World Business Congress, among other events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681542.htm"],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","I would like to ask: Chairman Xi is about to meet US President Obama. I wonder whether the Taiwan question will come up at the “Xi-Obama meeting,” whether more messages will be released on the Taiwan question, and whether a fourth joint communiqué is possible?","The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in US-China relations. We believe that the heads of state of the two countries will exchange views on important issues of mutual concern.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681551.htm"],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Lien Chan came to the mainland to attend the September 3 military parade, but after returning to Taiwan he was criticized by all sectors of Taiwan. What is the TAO's view on this matter?","On September 4, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office already issued a statement on the matter of Taiwan's various sectors participating in commemorative activities marking the 70th anniversary of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the Victory of the World Anti-Fascist War, clearly stating our position and attitude. Here, I must also point out that the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was a victory of great unity of the Chinese nation. This is the most basic and undeniable fact. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should, from the height of the interests of the entire nation, keep the lessons of history in mind, promote the spirit of the War of Resistance and the national spirit, and cherish the hard-won achievements of cross-Strait relations. On the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we should continue to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and devote ourselves to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. This is what commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance across the Strait should entail.\nTo be sure, compatriots on both sides of the Strait still have differences in their assessments of the history of the War of Resistance and other matters. These differences have existed for a long time, and everyone cannot deny that, with the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations in recent years, these differences have been narrowing and the areas of mutual overlap have been expanding. Both sides can perfectly well manage these differences properly, and in particular should not allow them to cause unnecessary impact on the process and atmosphere of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Any approach that expands and intensifies differences is unhelpful and unwise.\nIt is especially necessary for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to be vigilant against the attempts of “Taiwan independence” forces to deny the achievements of the Chinese nation's War of Resistance, to erase the contributions made by Taiwan compatriots in resisting Japanese colonial rule and in the victory of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, to sow discord between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and to undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Curbing the spread of the “Taiwan independence” view of history and curbing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme is the historical responsibility that all responsible political parties and political figures on both sides of the Strait should first bear.\n70 years ago, all Chinese sons and daughters, regardless of party affiliation, united as one to jointly resist external aggression and wrote a magnificent chapter of the nation's War of Resistance. We have every reason to believe that 70 years from now, with the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides of the Strait will ultimately be able to overcome prejudices and differences, and jointly open up a new situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681548.htm"],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","If the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” were lost, could the liaison and communication mechanism between the two sides' cross-Strait affairs authorities, as well as the consultation mechanism between ARATS and SEF, still be maintained?","We have pointed out on many occasions that the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations did not fall from the sky; they are built on the common political foundation of both sides' recognition and adherence to the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” In May 2008, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan exchanged letters and agreed to resume exchanges and negotiations between the two organizations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” In February 2014, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council likewise established a regular liaison and communication mechanism between the two departments on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” If the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” were gone, the political mutual trust built on this foundation and the related institutionalized consultation mechanisms would collapse.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681553.htm"],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Dengue fever in Taiwan continues to intensify. What impact will this have on mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan? What measures will the mainland take to jointly prevent the epidemic from spreading? Second question: according to media reports, at the launch of his new book, *New. Taiwan’s Position*, Lee Teng-hui claimed yesterday that he has never advocated “Taiwan independence,” because Taiwan is already “de…","On the first question, we have also noted that a serious dengue fever outbreak has erupted in southern Taiwan, with infections approaching ten thousand and dozens dead. The mainland’s National Tourism Administration has issued travel advisories. This is to maintain normal order in cross-Strait exchanges and to safeguard the vital rights and interests of mainland tourists. Through the cross-Strait Agreement on Medical and Health Cooperation, a mechanism for mutual notification of major epidemic information has been established. If necessary, this mechanism will be activated to play a role in joint epidemic prevention.\nOn the second question, Lee Teng-hui’s recent series of words and deeds fully exposes his muddled view of history, his shameful colonial and subservient mentality, and his vicious intent to stubbornly uphold “Taiwan independence” positions, undermine the development of cross-Strait relations, and drive a wedge between the feelings of compatriots on both sides. This has aroused strong indignation among compatriots on both sides. History has proven, and will continue to prove, that those who sell out national interests will never come to a good end and will ultimately be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Today a mainstream Taiwan media outlet released a public opinion poll on cross-Strait relations, in which, asked about their views on cross-Strait relations, the answer “maintain the status quo indefinitely” reached a new high in recent years. How does the spokesperson interpret this poll result?","Taiwan's public opinion polls come in all kinds, and we never comment on specific polls. What we see is that supporting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations remains the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. We also believe that as long as we adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will become broader and broader.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","What is the actual schedule currently for the “Zhang-Xia meeting” (张夏会)? How is the preparation for Chairman Chen Deming's visit to Taiwan in the second half of the year going? Second question: Since the Taiwan issue is an important topic of the “Xi-Obama meeting,” is it possible that President Xi Jinping will ask President Obama to take a tougher stance on the Taiwan issue at the Xi-Obama meeting?","On the second question, I have already answered it just now. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs will continue to keep everyone informed of relevant news regarding President Xi Jinping's visit to the United States, so please keep an eye on it.\nOn the first question: regarding the meeting between the heads of the competent cross-Strait authorities of both sides, the two sides are in communication, and it will be announced in a timely manner once agreed. As for the visit to Taiwan by Chen Deming, President of the Straits Exchange Foundation, leading the SEF Economic, Trade and Technology Exchange Delegation, this is arranged in accordance with the annual reciprocal exchange plan of the two organizations, and the two organizations are communicating on the specific timing and itinerary.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen recently said that if the DPP takes power in the future, it will absolutely not reduce the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office assess this?","Only by upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" can cross-Strait relations maintain peaceful and stable development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Some individuals in Taiwan claim that the cross-Strait tax agreement will cause Taiwanese workers on the mainland to be pursued for tax evasion, and that Taiwan’s relevant authorities providing labor data to the mainland will also harm their interests. Please explain.","This is pure nonsense. The purpose of signing the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Avoidance of Double Taxation and Enhancement of Tax Cooperation” is precisely to prevent and eliminate double taxation, safeguard the lawful rights and interests of taxpayers, and further deepen cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges.\nOn the question of information exchange: the cross-Strait tax agreement refers to the common practices of international tax cooperation and places particular emphasis on addressing the concerns of Taiwan compatriots. It stipulates that information exchange does not apply retroactively, that information is provided only in specific cases, and that exchanged information shall not be used for purposes other than taxation, among other things. The mainland tax authorities will carry out information exchange with the Taiwan side in accordance with the above provisions. I think, as the saying goes, rumors stop with the wise, so clarification is very necessary.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Will the next \"Zhang-Xia Meeting\" be able to reach a consensus on \"transit of mainland tourists\"?","The issue of “mainland tourist transit” and further facilitating exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is in fact the complete content of this topic. Both sides should move toward each other, make joint efforts, reach consensus as soon as possible, and make arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen may lead some DPP-affiliated public officials to attend Taiwan's \"Double Ten\" National Day celebrations. Do you think this move has symbolic significance?","I note that Taiwan public opinion has quite a few questions about this; you would be better off asking the parties concerned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报团结网记者","The Fuzhou New Area was recently established. Spokesperson, what role will it play in cross-Strait exchanges, especially cross-Strait economic exchanges?","Recently, the State Council approved the establishment of the Fuzhou New Area and assigned it many important functions, one of which requires building the Fuzhou New Area into an important platform for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are following this closely. The Taiwan Affairs Office will, in accordance with the State Council’s requirements, actively support this and coordinate with relevant departments to advance the implementation of the relevant policies and measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","DPP Chairperson Cai Yingwen has consistently said on cross-Strait relations that if she is elected in the future, she will still “maintain the status quo,” and she completely avoids mentioning the “1992 Consensus.” The spokesperson just mentioned that without the “1992 Consensus” across the Strait, many things would collapse. Would the mainland consider “maintaining the status quo” equivalent to acknowledging the…","Maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations requires, above all, upholding the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” whose core is recognizing that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Upholding this political foundation, cross-Strait relations can forge ahead through the waves without losing their way. Otherwise, cross-Strait relations will inevitably drift off course, be battered by wind and rain, and even run aground. Therefore, the “1992 Consensus” holds a foundational position in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it determines the two paths and two prospects for cross-Strait relations. On this fundamental question, any responsible political party must give a clear answer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150916_10681724.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150916_10681554.htm"],[0,"2015-09-18","Hong Lei","","A military coup was staged in Burkina Faso. What is China’s comment on this? It is one of the three countries in Africa that have “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. With the formation of the new military government, is there now a opportunity for China to establish diplomatic ties with Burkina Faso?","The Chinese side has been following the situation in Burkina Faso, and hopes that all parties can proceed from the fundamental interests of the state and the people, resolve political disputes through dialogue and consultation, restore normal order as soon as possible, and ensure national stability and development.\nAfter the press conference, the follow question was raised: It is reported that the Israeli police clashed with Palestinian protesters in Al-Aqsa mosque of Jerusalem. How does China comment on this? What is your position on the current situation between Palestine and Israel?\nHong Lei said that China pays great attention to this, and urges Israel and Palestine, Israel in particular, to exercise maximum restraint and avoid escalation of the tension. It is disconcerting to see the continuous clashes between Israel and Palestine in recent days. It is a proven fact that containing violence through violence can only lead to the cycle of violence and additional confrontation and hatred between the two parties. China once again urges the Israeli and Palestinian sides to take effective measures to rebuild trust and strive for the early resumption of peace talks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1298026.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-09-25","Hong Lei","","According to media reports, Tsai Ing-wen, chief of the Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan, plans to visit Japan early October. What’s your comment? Will China lodge any representations with Japan over this?","We are deeply concerned about and firmly opposed to Tsai Ing-wen’s visit to Japan. It is hoped that Japan would stick to the one-China principle, honor its commitment to China on the Taiwan Question, and leave no room for those who may spread the “Taiwan independence” ideas in whatever name and under whatever pretext.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1300569.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1300489.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. I will host today's press conference and am willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Could you introduce the recent 11th business communication under the Cross-Strait Trade in Goods Agreement?","From September 28 to 29, the 11th operational consultation on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods was held in Beijing. During this round, both sides reconfirmed the overall goals of the negotiations and the tariff reduction arrangements, fully communicated their respective concerns, and further exchanged views on the principles of market opening negotiations. Both sides expressed a positive attitude toward accelerating the follow-up negotiations on the Trade in Goods Agreement, hoping to complete it by the end of this year. Both sides also stated that they will continue to advance follow-up work and hold the next round of consultations as soon as possible. We hope that both sides will work together, move toward each other, continue to promote the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation on the basis of mutual benefit, strive to conclude the Trade in Goods Agreement at an early date, and enhance the well-being of the peoples and businesses on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768884.htm"],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","The card-type Taiwan compatriot permit has caused controversy in Taiwan. The Mainland Affairs Council said the mainland fully implemented the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit without fully informing the Taiwan side in advance. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond?","Implementing the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit is a further convenience measure we have taken in response to the wishes and demands of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, in accordance with the relevant management regulations on Taiwan residents' travel to the mainland. Since late June, the relevant competent departments and the Taiwan Affairs Office have explained it in detail and comprehensively through various channels. I would like to reiterate that the card-format permit is an electronic upgrade of the currently valid five-year paper Taiwan compatriot permit. The name of the document, “Taiwan Residents' Travel Permit to the Mainland,” has not changed; its entry and exit function has not changed; the personal information registered has not increased; and the validity period remains five years. Moreover, Taiwan residents holding the card-format permit can also complete entry and exit through self-service, further facilitating carrying and keeping the document. For such a convenient, beneficial, and positive measure, both sides of the Strait should welcome it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The Straits Cross-Strait Cultural Expo has been held seven times in Xiamen. May I ask the spokesperson what new features the 8th Straits Cross-Strait Cultural Expo will have, and what the current state of preparations is?","The Straits Cultural Industries Fair is sponsored by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Culture, and the State Administration of Press, Publication, Radio, Film and Television, and is hosted by the Fujian Provincial People's Government, the Xiamen Municipal People's Government, and the Asia-Pacific Cultural and Creative Industry Association of Taiwan. It has been held eight times since 2008. This year's fair is scheduled for October 30 to November 2 at the Xiamen International Conference and Exhibition Center. It is understood that this session of the fair will continue to uphold the purpose of \"promoting Chinese culture and advancing the integration of cross-Strait cultural markets,\" and will continue to play its active role as an important platform for connecting cross-Strait cultural industries. Preparatory work is underway at a brisk pace by the Xiamen authorities. We look forward to this session of the fair achieving new results in exchange and cooperation in the cross-Strait cultural industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","How many Taiwan residents have begun using the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit? Did you communicate with the Mainland Affairs Council through the institutionalized liaison channels between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council beforehand?","First question: according to our understanding, from the start of the pilot work on July 6 through September 29, relevant departments issued a total of 238,000 card-format Taiwan compatriot permits. Second question: as I have already answered just now, we have explained this through multiple channels and on multiple occasions. Please refer to the statements of the relevant Taiwan authorities, which should give you a clear answer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The cross-Strait Aviation Safety Agreement and Tax Agreement have been signed for a full month but have not yet taken effect. Will they repeat the fate of the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement? What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Second question: Super Typhoon Dujuan (杜鹃) has had a major impact on transportation, including flights, Taiwan Railway and high-speed rail. Will this affect mainland…","At the 11th meeting of the two associations, both sides signed the Agreement on Avoidance of Double Taxation and Strengthening of Tax Cooperation Across the Taiwan Strait, and the Agreement on Civil Aviation Flight Safety and Airworthiness Cooperation Across the Taiwan Strait. According to the agreements, they will formally take effect after both sides complete their respective procedures. It is understood that both sides are still carrying out their respective procedures. Of course, we hope these agreements can complete the relevant procedures smoothly and take effect as soon as possible, so as to play a positive role in deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and benefiting people on both sides.\nAs for the second question, we noted that this typhoon caused considerable losses in Taiwan, and we express our concern and sympathy. As for whether it will affect mainland tourists visiting Taiwan during the “National Day Golden Week,” please direct your question to the competent authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","During the “Xi-Obama meeting,” President Obama reaffirmed the “One China” policy based on the “three Sino-US joint communiqués” and the “Taiwan Relations Act.” We would like to know how the mainland views this US statement. The second question: Tsai Ing-wen recently launched the “New Southbound Policy,” and some interpret it as her intention to reduce reliance on the mainland market. How does the mainland view…","First question: On September 25, President Xi Jinping held talks with US President Obama in Washington. President Xi stressed that the Chinese nation is highly sensitive to issues concerning China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. He hopes the US side will abide by the relevant commitments and not support any actions aimed at undermining China's unification and stability. President Obama reaffirmed that the US adheres to the one-China policy and to the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and that this position will not change. He also stressed that the US does not support \"Taiwan independence.\" The two heads of state reconfirmed their respective positions and attitudes on the handling of the Taiwan question. This helps the international community consolidate and strengthen the one-China framework, and it also shows that \"Taiwan independence\" has no room to exist internationally.\nSecond question: As for this hypothetical statement, we do not comment on it in principle. But everyone should know that the so-called \"Southbound Policy\" is nothing new. Taiwan society already has a public consensus on how well it worked back then.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768904.htm"],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen plans to visit Japan in October. What comment do you have?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position. We firmly oppose anyone engaging in \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities internationally in any form, and opposing any attempt to undermine and provoke cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768896.htm"],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently responded to Obama's statement on the Taiwan issue, saying that what the United States refers to is its own “one China” policy. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Is the “one China” policy the United States refers to consistent with China's “one China” policy?","As I have just said, the Chinese and US leaders reaffirmed and confirmed their position and attitude on the Taiwan issue, which helps the international community consolidate the one-China framework. The international community generally adheres to the one-China policy and handles Taiwan-related affairs in accordance with the one-China principle. “Taiwan independence” has no space whatsoever internationally, and we will not allow “Taiwan independence” forces to undermine or split China's sovereignty and territorial integrity in any form. I think this is the most important point.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","The mainland's implementation of card-style Taiwan compatriot permits seems to have caused some questions and hype in Taiwan, and some Taiwan public opinion believes the mainland's approach to Taiwan work has seemingly changed. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our policy of advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and benefiting compatriots on both sides is consistent and clear, and it has not changed. The measures exempting Taiwan residents from travel endorsement requirements for visiting the mainland, and implementing the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit, have been widely welcomed by the Taiwan public. We understand that the feedback from broad Taiwan compatriots is positive. As for certain forces that, aiming to obstruct exchanges between people on both sides, engage in negative hype about this, such efforts are unpopular and difficult to succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768880.htm"],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","First question: Is there a timetable for the fourth meeting between the heads of the two sides' cross-Strait affairs authorities, which has attracted wide attention from all sectors? Second question: On the 25th of next month will mark the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's Retrocession, so will the mainland hold commemorative activities for it?","Regarding the visit of Chairperson Hsia Li-yan and his meeting with Director Zhang Zhijun, the two sides are coordinating arrangements, and there should be news soon. The cross-Strait affairs authorities and responsible officials of both sides, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” maintaining contact, exchanges and communication helps enhance mutual understanding and mutual trust, continues to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and jointly safeguards the overall situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At that time, both sides will exchange views on issues such as advancing the development of cross-Strait relations.\nAs for the second question: this year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 70th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, and all Chinese sons and daughters, after bloody fighting, not only won the War of Resistance but also freed Taiwan from Japanese colonial rule and returned it to the embrace of the motherland. At that time, relevant mainland departments will hold activities commemorating the 70th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201509/t20150930_10768831.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter's question about the mainland's commemorative activities for the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the regular press conference on September 30 that this year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, and all sons and daughters of China, through bloody battles, not only won victory in the war of resistance but also freed Taiwan from Japanese colonial rule and returned it to the embrace of the motherland. At that time, relevant departments on the mainland will hold commemorative activities marking the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768866.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Is there a timetable for the fourth meeting between the heads of the two sides’ cross-Strait affairs authorities, which has drawn wide attention from all sectors?","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the regular press conference on September 30, in response to a question, that the visit of Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council Chairperson Xia Liyan and his meeting with Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office are being arranged through communication between the two sides, and there should be news soon. Cross-Strait affairs authorities and officials of both sides maintaining contact, communication and exchange on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus\" helps enhance mutual understanding, strengthen mutual trust, continue to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and jointly safeguard the overall situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At that time, the two sides will exchange views on issues such as advancing the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201509/t20150930_10768872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office said that, after communication and consultation between the competent cross-Strait authorities of both sides, Xia Liyan, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council on the Taiwan side, will lead a delegation to visit Guangzhou and Dongguan from October 13 to 15. During this period, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, will hold a working meeting with Xia Liyan to exchange views on issues such as advancing the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151001_10771594.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-10-19","Hua Chunying","","In its latest trade policy communication released recently, the European Commission said that it would explore launching negotiations on two-way investment with Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","The Chinese side does not object non-official trade and cultural exchanges between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic relations with China, but opposes the development of official ties in any form. It is hoped that the EU side would continue to honor its commitment to the one-China principle, deal with Taiwan-related issues with prudence and refrain from having any form of official contacts or exchanges with Taiwan in any capacity, or signing any official agreement that has sovereignty implications.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1307341.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1307223.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on October 28, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. The newly appointed spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning, and welcome to the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Today's press conference is hosted by me. First, let me introduce myself: my name is An Fengshan, and I currently serve as Deputy Director of the News Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Today is my first time stepping onto the press briefing podium, but because I have worked in the News Bureau for a long time, I am actually an old friend who has known you journalists for many years. I hope that in my new post I can strengthen communication and exchanges with you all and do press briefing work well. First, I will release a piece of news.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","The 2015 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijinshan Summit will be held in Nanjing from November 3 to 4. This is the third annual meeting since the cross-strait entrepreneurs summit association was established. The theme is “Innovating Cooperation Models and Promoting Industrial Integration.” Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, will attend the summit and deliver a speech. More than 850 cross-strait business leaders, heads of business organizations, small and medium-sized enterprise owners, and finance and economics scholars will attend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926619.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","This summit will highlight the focus on small and medium-sized enterprises, young people and grassroots people, guide cross-Strait enterprises to jointly participate in the construction of the Belt and Road, and promote cross-Strait small and medium-sized enterprises and young people to accelerate their pace of innovation and entrepreneurship. The summit's seven industrial cooperation promotion groups are: the macroeconomy group, the energy, petrochemical and equipment group, the finance group, the information and home appliances group, the growth-oriented and small and medium-sized enterprises group, the cultural and creative group, and the biotechnology and healthcare group. At the summit, thematic forums or sub-forums will be held to exchange views on deepening cross-Strait industrial cooperation, put forward suggestions, and advance cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","An on-site exchange meeting encouraging Taiwanese youth to start businesses and find employment on the mainland was recently held in Xiamen, and 12 Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases were established. Please introduce the relevant situation.","In the mainland’s nationwide wave of “mass entrepreneurship and innovation,” localities, enterprises, and industrial parks, drawing on their own characteristics and advantages, have actively created conditions and successively issued policies and measures to support and encourage Taiwan youth to come to the mainland for employment and entrepreneurship. They have built a batch of distinctive and relatively mature cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment platforms. To promote these positive practices, further summarize experience, and facilitate exchange, a Symposium on Encouraging Taiwan Youth to Work and Start Businesses on the Mainland was held in Xiamen, Fujian, on October 15 to 16. Taiwan Affairs Offices of 14 provinces and municipalities, including Beijing, Tianjin, Shanghai, Jiangsu, and Guangdong, and heads of Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases attended. During the meeting, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council granted plaques to 12 Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases.\nThese 12 Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases are located at: Beijing Zhongguancun Startup Street; Shanghai Jinshan Industrial Zone; Shanghai Hui Guang Optoelectronics Co., Ltd.; Qilin Cross-Strait Small and Medium Enterprise Innovation Park in Nanjing, Jiangsu; Kunshan Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Park; Taiwan Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Service Center in Wenzhou, Zhejiang; Yunqi Town in Hangzhou, Zhejiang; Fuzhou Strait Creative Industry Park, Fujian; Xiamen Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship and Innovation Maker Base, Fujian; Xiamen Yipin Witkey Maker Space, Fujian; Taiwan Youth Entrepreneurship Base in Dongxihu District, Hubei; and Taiwan Hi-Tech Park at Songshan Lake, Dongguan, Guangdong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926615.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Media reported that Chen Deming, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, will visit Taiwan in early November. Could the spokesperson introduce the main itinerary, theme, and related content of Chairman Chen's visit? The second question: the 25th is the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's Retrocession, and both sides of the Strait have held commemorative activities in different forms. May I ask the spokesperson,…","First question. Under this year's high-level exchange and visit plan of the two associations, Chen Deming, Chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS), will lead an ARATS economic, trade and technology exchange delegation to visit Taiwan within the year. The delegation will inspect representative cultural and creative enterprises, technology parks and enterprises in relevant Taiwan counties and cities, and hold discussions with important Taiwan business groups and associations, Mainland-invested enterprises in Taiwan, youth entrepreneurship organizations, and elderly care institutions. The specific timing and itinerary are still under discussion between the two associations and have not yet been determined.\nSecond question. October 25 this year marks the 70th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. To commemorate this important historical moment, relevant Mainland departments have held a series of commemorative events. It is of great significance for compatriots on both sides to jointly remember historical lessons, cherish the memory of the martyrs and their merits, promote the spirit of the War of Resistance, seek peace and development together, and work with one heart toward realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The restoration of Taiwan was a victory achieved through the joint struggle of compatriots on both sides. This history shows that no matter how many hardships compatriots on both sides have endured and no matter how long they have been separated, no force can tear us apart, because we have always been one family. The current development of cross-Strait relations is at an important juncture. Compatriots on both sides should uphold the common political foundation and firmly follow the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We must not allow the hard-won peace across the Taiwan Strait and the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations to be lost.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926618.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Please assess this: KMT 2016 presidential candidate Eric Chu will visit the United States in early November. His trip and the cross-Strait policy he has proposed are based on the “1992 Consensus, One China with Respective Interpretations.”","Our position on Taiwan's exchanges with foreign countries is consistent and clear. We hope relevant countries will properly handle related matters in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, met with Hsia Li-yan, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, in Guangzhou on the 14th and reached a number of points of consensus. This meeting took place as Taiwan's elections approach, at an important juncture where cross-Strait relations face a choice of path. May I ask the spokesperson for its evaluation?","On the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan have established a regular liaison and communication mechanism. Mutual visits and meetings between the heads of the two departments are an important part of this mechanism. We want to emphasize that adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is an important foundation for establishing this regular liaison and communication mechanism between the two departments, and it is also a necessary condition for the mechanism to operate normally. We therefore hope that both sides of the Strait will continue to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on this common basis.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926616.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen said that regarding Taiwan's restoration, people have two kinds of feelings: one is national pride and self-confidence, and the other is memories that rise and fall with the times. She said both sides should acknowledge differences and respect and tolerate each other. What is your view?","The restoration of Taiwan is an achievement of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, in winning the victory of the War of Resistance against Japan, and it is the pride and glory of the Chinese nation. The viewpoint you just mentioned, which calls for \"understanding and tolerance,\" is nothing more than a \"Taiwan independence\" view of history that contradicts historical facts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926617.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen recently visited Japan, and it is reported that she met with Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe. How does the spokesperson assess Tsai’s visit?","On this matter, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position. We firmly oppose anyone engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally in any way, and undermining or provoking cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","This is also about the 70th anniversary of the War of Resistance Against Japan. Recently, the Taiwan Chinese Nation Anti-Japanese War Commemoration Association was established in Taipei. According to the introduction, the association will actively cooperate with relevant parties on the mainland to jointly build an anti-war museum. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","I am not aware of the situation you just mentioned. Victory in the War of Resistance was the result of the united and hard-fought struggle of the entire Chinese nation. Our purpose in commemorating the 70th anniversary of the victory is to remember the lessons of history, cherish the merits of the martyrs, carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, and work together for peaceful development. We hope that both sides of the Strait will, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” strengthen exchanges and communication, resolve prejudices and differences, and work together for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Spokesperson, what attitude does the mainland hold toward Taiwan's wish to join the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB)? Has any progress been made in this regard? In addition, this month ARATS Chairman Chen Deming led a Taiwan business “Belt and Road” inspection group to Shaanxi and other places. Please introduce the relevant situation.","We have repeatedly expressed our welcome for Taiwan joining the AIIB, and we are glad to see the AIIB handle Taiwan’s accession in accordance with its Articles of Agreement. Continued communication across the Strait helps to better resolve related issues.\nOn the second question, from October 16 to 22, Chen Deming, Chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS), led the ‘Belt and Road’ Taiwan Business Western Tour delegation on an inspection visit to Shaanxi, Gansu, and Ningxia. Responsible persons of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and nearly 30 Taiwan business association presidents and Taiwan business representatives participated. Through on-site inspections, Taiwan businesspeople gained a deeper understanding of economic and social development in the western region, its cost advantages in resources and production factors, and the enormous potential and market space brought by the ‘Belt and Road’ development strategy. The TAO and ARATS will continue to help Taiwan business friends better understand the ‘Belt and Road’ strategy, and jointly seek transformation opportunities and share development opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201510/t20151028_10926612.htm"],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","In the 2016 election, the KMT replaced Hung Hsiu-chu with Chu Li-lun as its candidate. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office view Chu Li-lun's cross-Strait policy?","We do not intervene in or comment on Taiwan's elections. As far as cross-Strait relations are concerned, since 2005, and especially since 2008, the KMT and the CPC, on the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" have promoted important and positive progress in party-to-party relations and cross-Strait relations. Cross-Strait relations are once again at an important juncture. We hope the two parties will continue on this common political foundation, consolidate and enhance political mutual trust, adhere to the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continue to work unremittingly to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","First question: recently there has been widespread speculation in Taiwan that relevant mainland authorities will reduce mainland tourists visiting Taiwan before the elections at the end of the year. Please confirm. If so, what is the proportion of the reduction? Second question: regarding the Taiwan Affairs Office anti-corruption issue, the Fifth Central Inspection Tour recently released some information. I…","Regarding your first question, on the decline in Mainland tourists to Taiwan, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office already explained this at the press conference held after the Guangzhou \"Zhang-Xia Meeting.\" Because the situation in Taiwan is currently in a special and sensitive period and society's atmosphere is highly politicized, Mainland travel agencies will also consider their own interests, and travelers to Taiwan will also consider the travel environment and their own rights and interests. Judging from past experience, these conditions have affected Mainland residents' willingness to travel to Taiwan to varying degrees. We also hope that a healthy and orderly environment for Mainland residents' travel to Taiwan can be maintained, and that the rights and interests of Mainland tourists can be valued and guaranteed.\nOn the second question, in accordance with the unified arrangements of the central government, the Fifth Central Inspection Team conducted a special inspection of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee from June 30 to August 30, 2015. On October 19, the inspection team fed back the inspection situation to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee, pointed out problems in party conduct and clean governance construction, and put forward rectification requirements. Relevant information has been made public. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee attaches great importance to the feedback and opinions of the inspection team; it will take this special inspection as an opportunity to earnestly carry out the various rectification tasks in accordance with the problems fed back by the central inspection team and the rectification opinions put forward, placing them at the political height of comprehensively and strictly governing the Party, resolutely and unswervingly advancing party conduct and clean governance construction and the fight against corruption, so that rectification work becomes an important impetus for further strengthening team building and advancing work concerning Taiwan, and makes a contribution to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Taiwan is actively seeking to join the second round of TPP membership. Taiwan's “Minister of Economic Affairs” said that if the 12 member states agree, the mainland's attitude still needs to be considered. What comment do you have on this?","Regarding Taiwan's desire to participate in regional economic cooperation, we have repeatedly stated our position and attitude.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","新京报记者","On the 27th, Taiwan’s side released its 2015 military power report, claiming that the mainland plans to have the capability to attack Taiwan before 2020. What is your response?","The peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is conducive to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and it also accords with the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides. Under the new circumstances of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, hyping up the so-called mainland military threat to Taiwan or the mainland’s military strength is neither in line with the facts, nor conducive to political mutual trust across the Strait, and even less in keeping with the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","人民日报海外版记者","Both sides of the Strait commemorate Taiwan's Restoration, yet the DPP has gone to great lengths to avoid it, and has hyped the so-called “undetermined status of Taiwan” theory in the Treaty of San Francisco, seeking a so-called international legal basis for “Taiwan independence.” How do you view this?","As I have just said, the Restoration of Taiwan is an achievement of all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, in winning the victory of the War of Resistance, and it is a source of pride and glory for the Chinese nation. Any attempt by “Taiwan independence” elements to deny that Taiwan is part of China is futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The Fifth Plenary Session of the 18th Central Committee is convening, focusing on studying the economic development plan for the next stage, the 13th Five-Year Plan. Taiwan's side pays close attention to this. May I ask the spokesperson: what impact will this have on future cross-strait economic cooperation?","From October 26 to 29, the Fifth Plenary Session of the 18th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was held in Beijing. This plenary session will study proposals on formulating the 13th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development and plan China's development path for the next five years. The session is still underway; please follow the information released by the plenary session.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台声杂志社记者","Recently, the “mass entrepreneurship and innovation” activity week has been underway, which is a very good platform, especially for the younger generation. May I ask, in the process of cross-Strait youth exchanges and serving Taiwan businesspeople’s employment and entrepreneurship, what relevant policies are there?","We have always attached great importance to cross-Strait youth exchanges, and have actively created conditions and built platforms to promote and expand cross-Strait youth exchanges and cooperation. We have provided room for broad Taiwan youth to study, work, start businesses, and develop on the mainland, and created good conditions for them to join the tide of \"mass entrepreneurship and innovation\" on the mainland and realize their life dreams. To this end, we have also built a number of cross-Strait youth exchange brands that cross-Strait youth are happy to take part in and that have broad influence, including the 12 cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship bases I mentioned just now. Next, we will continue to optimize the environment and improve conditions, focus on providing room for cross-Strait youth in employment and entrepreneurship, and continue to provide support and assistance for cross-Strait youth exchange, cooperation, and employment and entrepreneurship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾“中央社”记者","When Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairman Hsia Li-yan met earlier, Chairman Hsia personally invited Director Zhang to visit Taiwan next year. Later, Chairman Hsia said he would need to see the situation in Taiwan next year, especially public opinion next year and the views of the newly elected leader. What is the spokesperson's comment on this point?","When the heads of the competent cross-Strait authorities met in Guangzhou, Chairman Hsia Li-yan (Xia Liyan) invited Director Zhang Zhijun to visit Taiwan again. Director Zhang expressed thanks for this and said he is willing to consider it at an appropriate time. At present, the two sides have not further contacted each other on this matter. As I just mentioned, the regular contact and communication mechanism established between the competent cross-Strait authorities of both sides, including reciprocal visits by heads, is built on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" We hope that both sides of the Strait can jointly uphold this foundation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","Does Beijing have plans to establish channels of contact with the Tsai Ing-wen camp to facilitate the exchange and transmission of information between the two sides?","Our policy toward the DPP is clear and consistent. Since 2008, the reason cross-Strait relations have achieved a good situation of peaceful development and a series of important results lies in the common political foundation of both sides adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” The core of this foundation is recognizing that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that cross-Strait relations are not relations between two countries. As long as this is recognized, there is no obstacle for any Taiwan political party or group to deal with the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-10-28","An Fengshan","团结报团结网记者","The 2nd Cross-Strait Design Awards for Four Regions, the “Huacan Award,” will be presented next month in Pingtan, Fujian. Please introduce the relevant information.","It is understood that the Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, the China Higher Education Association and other units will hold, on November 3 at the Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Park in the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone in Fujian, the award ceremony of the Second “Huacan Award” together with the Sixth Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Forum. Since 2010, the Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee has initiated and successfully held five consecutive “Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Forums,” which have received good response on both sides of the Strait. This session's forum takes “互·融” (encouraging and promoting exchanges between students and young designers across the Strait, collaborative design, and co-creating the future) as its theme, and invites about 500 participants, including guests from relevant parties on both sides, cultural and creative personnel, well-known enterprise figures, young designers and university students. The award ceremony of the “Huacan Award” will be held at the forum. The “Huacan Award” is a comprehensive design competition aimed at discovering and promoting young designers from the two sides of the Strait and Hong Kong and Macao. We wish this forum complete success.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201510/t20151028_10926550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-10-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to foreign media, Commander of the Chinese People's Liberation Army Navy (PLAN) Admiral Wu Shengli will have a video conversation with the US Chief of Naval Operations and they will probably mention the USS Lassen's entering into the waters within 12 nautical miles of China's islands and reefs in the South China Sea. Can you verify this information?\nSecondly, the Taiwanese military published a report…","For the first question, Admiral Wu Shengli, the PLA Navy commander, will have a video conversation with the US Chief of Naval Operations (CNO) Adm. John Richardson on Oct. 29, which is tonight, through the MND hotline, and express China's solemn stance to the US side on the USS Lassen's unilateral intrusion into offshore waters of relevant islands and reefs of the Nansha Islands in the South China Sea.\nThis will also be the first such conversation after the signing of new annexes to the two confidence-building mechanisms between China's MND and the US DOD in September this year.\nOn your second question, the spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has stated China's position.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-10/29/content_4626549.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2015-11-02","Hua Chunying","","The Taiwan authorities reportedly released a statement on October 31 concerning the award rendered on October 29 by the Arbitral Tribunal established at the request of the Philippines on jurisdiction and admissibility of the South China Sea arbitration, saying that it would neither recognize nor accept the award. What is your comment on that?","I have noted the relevant report. I want to stress that Chinese people from both sides of the Straits have the responsibility and obligation to jointly uphold territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests of the country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1311236.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1311150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-11-04","Hua Chunying","","Leaders across the Taiwan Straits will meet in Singapore on November 7. Why did they choose to meet in Singapore?","Zhang Zhijun, head of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has given a press interview on the meeting between leaders across the Taiwan Straits scheduled for November 7 in Singapore. I would like to refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for the specifics.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1311992.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1311866.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-11-04","Hua Chunying","","The Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan said today that the mainland is seeking to influence the outcome of the election in Taiwan by holding the meeting of leaders acorss the Straits. What is your reaction to that?","I would like to refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for specifics concerning the meeting of leaders across the Taiwan Straits. I want to point out that peaceful development of cross-Straits relations serves the interests of the two sides across the Straits as well as peace and stability of the region and world at large.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1311992.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1311866.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-11-07","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Taiwan will hold elections next year, and now there are more than 70 days until voting. Why is the Mainland considering a meeting between the leaders of both sides at this time? Zhang Zhijun made the above remarks in response to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Singapore, November 7 (reporters Chen Binhua and Zhao Bo): Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions here on the 7th, saying that the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office has repeatedly stated that we do not interfere in Taiwan's elections, and what we care about is that cross-Strait relations develop in the right direction.\nCPC General Secretary and President Xi Jinping met with Taiwan's leader Ma Ying-jeou in Singapore on the afternoon of the 7th to exchange views on further advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This was the first meeting between leaders of the two sides since 1949.\nAfter the meeting, the Taiwan Affairs Office held a press conference to answer questions from reporters present.\nZhang Zhijun said, \"We value the lessons that the 66 years of cross-Strait relations offer people, and we value the future of cross-Strait relations. As Xi Jinping pointed out in the meeting, as long as something is beneficial to enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, as long as it is beneficial to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and as long as it is beneficial to safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation, both sides should make the utmost effort to do it and do it well.\"\nA reporter also asked: identity and title have long been a problem troubling leaders' meetings across the Strait; how was this problem resolved for this meeting between the two leaders?\nZhang Zhijun replied that a meeting between the leaders of the two sides has been our consistent position, and we have stated this attitude on multiple occasions. We proposed this idea as far back as 20 years ago. Since 2008, on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposition to \"Taiwan independence,\" the two sides have opened up a path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, achieving fruitful results that created favorable conditions for a meeting of the leaders. At the same time, political differences still exist between the two sides. Therefore, through communication, the two sides agreed that the meeting would use the identities and titles of the leaders of the two sides, addressing each other as \"Mr.\" This is a pragmatic arrangement made in accordance with the one-China principle while cross-Strait political differences have not yet been fully resolved, and it also reflects the spirit of setting aside disputes and mutual respect.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151108_10993722.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Not long ago, the leaders on both sides of the Strait met for the first time in 66 years and reached positive consensus. What role will this consensus play in promoting the development of cross-Strait relations?","The meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait turned a historic page in cross-Strait relations and opened new space for the future development of cross-Strait relations. During the meeting, both leaders affirmed the important achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008. They held that the “1992 Consensus” should continue to be upheld, the common political foundation consolidated, peaceful development of cross-Strait relations promoted, peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait maintained, communication and dialogue strengthened, exchanges across the Strait expanded, cooperation deepened, mutually beneficial win-win outcomes realized, and benefits brought to the people on both sides. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all descendants of Yan and Huang. They should join hands and cooperate, committed to revitalizing China and to national rejuvenation. This important consensus points the way for compatriots on both sides in terms of the direction, foundation, path, and goals for the development of cross-Strait relations, and it is of great significance for the long-term development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe positive outcomes of this meeting have laid a firmer foundation for future exchanges and interactions at all levels across the Strait, for exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and for the stable and healthy development of cross-Strait relations. They have opened new space and injected new impetus. This also fully shows that, on the basis of the one-China principle, the two sides are fully able, through establishing and strengthening high-level communication, to increase mutual trust, clarify direction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and work toward the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","The cross-Strait leaders' meeting achieved positive outcomes. Could you introduce how these positive outcomes will be implemented in future cross-Strait exchanges?","In the meeting between the leaders of the two sides, in response to issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots, General Secretary Xi Jinping clearly stated that we are willing to share mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first. The two sides can strengthen macro-policy communication, give full play to their respective strengths, expand the space for economic cooperation, enlarge the common pie of interests, and increase the benefits and sense of gain for compatriots on both sides. On issues including the Agreement on Trade in Goods, the mutual establishment of offices by the two organizations, Taiwan compatriots' participation in the construction of the Belt and Road, and Taiwan's joining the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank in an appropriate manner, we have expressed a positive attitude. Whatever benefits the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides, whatever promotes the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and whatever safeguards the overall interests of the Chinese nation, both sides should make the greatest efforts to do and do well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100111.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Some opinion in Taiwan holds that the rise of the mainland's “red supply chain” has impacted some of Taiwan's industries. Please share the spokesperson's views on the economic competition and cooperation between the two sides of the Strait.","Economic exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait are characterized by cooperation outweighing competition. The two sides complement each other’s strengths, benefit mutually, and have brought real benefits to compatriots on both sides. We believe the space for future development remains very broad. Recently, at the 2015 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit held in Nanjing, entrepreneurs from both sides unanimously called on businesses across the Strait to join hands, inject new momentum into industrial cooperation across the Strait, and, on the basis of mutual trust and mutual benefit, continue to deepen industrial exchanges and cooperation, leading enterprises on both sides toward building a Chinese national industrial chain, so as to enhance the competitiveness and influence of the Chinese nation’s economy in the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","The international counterterrorism situation is currently grave. When former U.S. President Obama spoke of partners in joint counterterrorism efforts, he included Taiwan. Does the mainland have plans to cooperate with Taiwan on counterterrorism?","On the question of international counter-terrorism cooperation, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated our position on several occasions.\nRegarding cross-Strait counter-terrorism cooperation, under the Agreement on Cross-Strait Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance, the police forces on both sides have in recent years continued to strengthen communication on cooperation in combating crime, and combating terrorism-related crimes is also a category of such cooperation. We hope that both sides can continue to work together and join hands to combat all kinds of criminal activities, including violent terrorism, to safeguard the lives and property of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","If the DPP had taken power in Taiwan in 2016, would the spokesperson say there would still be meetings between the leaders of the two sides?","This is a hypothetical question, and I will not respond.\nBut I want to stress that adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and its core lies in recognizing that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China and that cross-Strait relations are not a relationship between two countries. The leaders of both sides met in Singapore and jointly confirmed the “1992 Consensus,” which further consolidated the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and is conducive to safeguarding the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe “1992 Consensus” has been clearly authorized and endorsed by the relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, and it enjoys broad support from public opinion on both sides. We hope that all parties and groups in Taiwan can face the “1992 Consensus” squarely. Regardless of which party or group it is, and regardless of what it advocated in the past, as long as it acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and endorses its core meaning, we are willing to engage with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100108.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Recently, relevant figures in the KMT said that amendments should be passed as soon as possible to shorten the years required for mainland spouses to obtain Taiwan ID cards, and to include mainland students in the national health insurance, among other amendment drafts. The DPP said that because the mainland still harbors hostility toward Taiwan, mainland spouses' acquisition of ID cards must necessarily be…","The discriminatory treatment that mainland spouses and mainland students studying in Taiwan encounter in Taiwan has long gone unresolved. I believe everyone is clear about where the resistance lies. The DPP ignores the legitimate rights and interests of cross-Strait marriage families, disrupting the normal lives of these families and causing them pain, and harming the emotional bonds between compatriots on both sides. This approach is not popular with the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100103.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","You just mentioned that when the leaders of the two sides met, they discussed advancing the cross-Strait goods trade agreement. Could you introduce the situation at the 12th round of business communication on the cross-Strait goods trade agreement recently held in Taipei? What are the next work plans in this regard?","From November 21 to 23, the 12th operational consultation on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods was held in Taipei. Both sides comprehensively reviewed and sorted out the progress of the negotiations on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods, and conducted in-depth discussions on issues on which agreement had not previously been reached. Through the joint efforts of the cross-Strait negotiation teams, this round of negotiations made positive progress. On the text portion, the two sides reached consensus on all provisions of the chapters on rules of origin, customs procedures, and sanitary and phytosanitary measures, as well as on the implementing procedures for rules of origin listed as an annex. They reached agreement on some divergent provisions of the trade remedies chapter, and on product-specific rules of origin for most products. On the market access portion, the two sides further clarified the overall objectives of the Trade in Goods Agreement and the principles for tariff reduction arrangements, and exchanged views in depth on the issue of normalization and on specific product lists. The two sides will continue to work together to strive to complete the negotiations on the Trade in Goods Agreement as soon as possible. The two sides have also tentatively agreed to hold the 13th operational consultation on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods in mid-to-late December.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100106.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Now, the implementation of the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement is still being delayed. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Strengthening cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation is conducive to advancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and the benefits it brings are plain for all to see. Therefore, we hope the agreements already signed can take effect and be implemented as soon as possible, to benefit the people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Two questions. First, it is reported that the Straits Exchange Foundation and ARATS will hold a conference in Taipei on the 30th on the effectiveness of cross-Strait agreements and their promotion. I would like the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation. Second, on October 29, the Permanent Court of Arbitration in The Hague issued a preliminary ruling in the South China Sea arbitration case, and on the…","Regarding your first question, the two associations are preparing for a summary meeting on the implementation results of cross-Strait agreements. The meeting will be held in Taipei on November 30 and will mainly review the implementation of the various cross-Strait agreements over the past more than seven years, and systematically summarize the achievements these agreements have made in advancing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nRegarding your second question, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position. The Nansha Islands and their adjacent waters are China’s inherent territory. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation is a shared responsibility of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","It is rumored that recently a young Taiwanese singer, Lu Guangzhong, was cancelled from performing on the mainland because he took part in opposition to the Cross-Strait Service Trade Agreement. Can you confirm this report? Does taking part in opposition to the Cross-Strait Service Trade Agreement equate to being a “Taiwan independence” separatist? In addition, recently some public figures have often labeled…","I am not aware of the specific situation you mentioned. What I want to emphasize is that our attitude of supporting exchanges between the two sides in all fields is clear and positive, and at the same time our firm position of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Recent media reports indicate that from November 21 to February 29 next year, the daily quota for mainland group tourists traveling to Taiwan will be temporarily increased to 8,000 people. Could the spokesperson confirm this and provide specific details? In addition, what is the overall situation of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan up to now?","The change in the quota for mainland tourists to Taiwan that you mentioned should have been stated by the relevant Taiwan authorities. We hope that an environment for the healthy and orderly development of mainland tourism to Taiwan can be maintained, and that the rights and interests of mainland tourists are valued and protected. As for the overall situation of mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan, as is customary, we will sort out and summarize exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait by the end of the year, and at that time we will respond to the relevant questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","《台声》杂志记者","When the leaders of both sides met, General Secretary Xi Jinping said that more opportunities and better conditions should be provided for cross-Strait youth to study, find employment, start businesses, and exchange. How will the spokesperson implement this? What work have we already done in this area?","As the mainland's economy has grown rapidly and cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges have deepened, more and more young Taiwanese have chosen to develop their careers on the mainland, and we welcome this. Over the years, many places and relevant departments on the mainland have introduced a series of policies to actively support young Taiwanese in studying, finding employment, and starting businesses on the mainland. For example: pilot programs for Taiwan residents to take employment in public institutions have been launched in 6 provinces and municipalities including Fujian; more than 30 professional qualification examinations, including those for physicians and lawyers, have been gradually opened to Taiwan compatriots; and channels for Taiwan youth to find employment and start businesses on the mainland have been expanded. In addition, Taiwan students studying at mainland universities who take entrepreneurship training during their graduating academic year may also enjoy corresponding training subsidies, in accordance with the relevant regulations for mainland university graduates. Zhejiang, Fujian, Guangdong and other places have issued policies specifically encouraging Taiwan youth to intern, find employment, and start businesses. Since the beginning of this year, several localities have successively held symposiums and forums on the theme of cross-Strait youth cooperation and development to explore collaboration. Thirteen Straits Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases of various forms have been established.\nNext, we will continue to improve relevant policies and measures, and support localities in building cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship cooperation platforms that suit their own industrial characteristics and advantages, seeking truth from facts, in order to create better conditions for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100107.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Has there been any substantive progress between the two sides of the Strait on Taiwan's accession to the AIIB?","On the issue of Taiwan joining the AIIB, at the recent meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Strait, General Secretary Xi Jinping clearly stated that we are willing to first share the opportunities of mainland development with Taiwan compatriots, welcome Taiwan compatriots to participate in the construction of the Belt and Road, and also welcome Taiwan joining the AIIB in an appropriate manner. We believe these issues will be properly handled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","台湾三立电视台记者","Regarding the “Xi-Ma meeting,” The Economist published a column arguing that this represents a concession by the mainland on sovereignty issues. Ma Ying-jeou also wrote to USA Today a couple of days ago, putting forward corresponding views. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","I have not heard of the article you mentioned. What I want to emphasize is that the meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Strait is a major event of milestone significance in the history of cross-Strait relations. Both sides, with a mutually respectful and constructive attitude, candidly exchanged views on themes such as advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly working toward national rejuvenation, reached positive consensus, and opened a historic new page in cross-Strait relations. During the meeting of the leaders, the two sides exchanged views on relevant issues, and General Secretary Xi also expressed the Mainland side's consistent position, attitude and proposals. General Secretary Xi pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” is important because it embodies the “one China” principle and clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. It shows that the Mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, that cross-Strait relations are not a state-to-state relationship, and that they are not “one China, one Taiwan.” Although the two sides have not yet been reunified, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided. The two sides belong to one country, and compatriots on both sides belong to the Chinese nation. This historical fact and legal basis have never changed and cannot change.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151125_11100109.htm"],[2,"2015-11-25","An Fengshan","团结报团结网记者","At the recent meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Strait, General Secretary Xi proposed that the two sides share historical materials and jointly write history. What further measures will the mainland take in this regard? What significance will this have for the development of cross-Strait relations?","Having cross-Strait experts and scholars share materials related to the War of Resistance and jointly study its history, and strengthening cooperation in this regard, helps us keep the lessons of history in mind, safeguard the fruits of the War of Resistance, carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, and jointly pursue peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will promote this in line with the spirit of General Secretary Xi's speech.\nThank you all for attending today's press conference. Thank you, and we will see you at the next one.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201511/t20151125_11100220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-11-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","It is reported that on October 13, the mainland side released two Taiwan intelligence personnel who had been detained, Chu Kung-hsun and Hsu Chang-kuo, and arranged for them to return to Taiwan. Subsequently, the Taiwan side paroled Lee Chih-hao, a subject of a “communist espionage case.” Can the TAO confirm this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 30 (reporter Zha Wenye) — An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, on the 30th responded to questions and introduced the relevant circumstances of the parole granted in October this year by mainland judicial authorities to two Taiwan spies.\nAn Fengshan said: It is understood that Zhu Gongxun and Xu Zhangguo, who engaged in espionage activities against the mainland, seriously endangered the mainland's security interests and were severely punished by the relevant judicial authorities in accordance with law. As of October this year, Zhu Gongxun and Xu Zhangguo had served many years of their sentences and met the relevant conditions for parole under the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, and the relevant judicial authorities granted them parole in accordance with law. The parole of Li Zhihao is a matter for the relevant Taiwan departments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201511/t20151130_11134684.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2015-12-15","Hong Lei","","US congressional sources said that the US is getting ready to approve the sale of guided missile frigates to Taiwan before the end of this month. Has China already warned the United States not to do so?","The Chinese side firmly opposes any arms sale from the US to Taiwan. This position is solid, clear and consistent. I would like to reiterate that the arms sale from the US to Taiwan constitutes a grave breach of the principle of the three joint communiqués between China and the US, especially that of the August 17 Communiqué, interfere in China's domestic affairs and undermine the peaceful development of cross-Straits relations and China-US relations. The Chinese side strongly urges the US side to fully recognize how sensitive and harmful the arms sales can be, stick to its commitments, stop selling arms to Taiwan, and contribute to the overall interests of China-US ties and the peaceful development of cross-Straits relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1324515.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1324481.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 16, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first announced policy measures to expand opening, allowing Taiwan residents to apply to establish individual industrial and commercial households on the mainland, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues in cross-Strait relations.","Dear journalists, good morning! Today’s press conference is hosted by me. First, I would like to announce a favorable policy measure to everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Starting January 1, 2016, relevant mainland authorities will further expand and relax the industry fields, geographic scope and operating conditions under which Taiwan residents may apply to set up individual industrial and commercial households on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259955.htm"],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","At the end of 2011, guided by our sincere wish to let Taiwan compatriots first share in the development opportunities on the mainland, we first opened to Taiwan residents the application to establish individual industrial and commercial households in nine provinces and municipalities, including Beijing and Shanghai, as well as in the Cross-Strait Agricultural Cooperation Pilot Zones and Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Parks established on the mainland. As of the end of November 2015, Taiwan residents had established more than 3,500 individual industrial and commercial households on the mainland. At present, these individual households are generally doing well, and many of them have grown and expanded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Over the past four years, as the mainland's economy and society have continued to develop, exchange and cooperation between the two sides in economic and other fields have continued to expand and deepen, and the desire of broad Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan's young friends, to seek development opportunities on the mainland has continued to grow. The State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Administration for Industry and Commerce, together with relevant departments, after careful research, decided to further expand the opening up to allow Taiwan residents to apply to establish individually owned businesses on the mainland. The relevant policy document was officially issued yesterday (December 15).","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","I believe this newly introduced policy measure will provide more entrepreneurial opportunities and development space for Taiwan's grassroots people, especially Taiwan's young friends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","At the previous meeting of the leaders of the two sides across the Strait, consensus was reached that both sides would establish a hotline. What progress has been made?","At the recent meeting between the leaders of the two sides, both sides agreed to establish a cross-Strait hotline, first set up between the heads of the competent cross-Strait affairs authorities of both sides. Establishing a cross-Strait hotline helps both sides strengthen exchange and dialogue, enhance political mutual trust, and, through equal consultation and active discussion, promote the resolution of various difficult issues between the two sides. It also helps manage and control differences and disagreements, enables timely communication, avoids miscalculation, and handles urgent matters. As far as we understand, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council are actively consulting on the specific arrangements. Once they are determined, we will release them to everyone in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259935.htm"],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","It has been reported that the United States is about to announce a $1 billion arms sale to Taiwan. What is your comment, spokesperson?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs expressed our stern position yesterday. We firmly oppose any country selling weapons, arms and equipment, or technology to Taiwan in any form or under any pretext. This position is consistent, clear, and firm. All parties should fully recognize that opposing “Taiwan independence,” upholding the “1992 Consensus,” and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations are the fundamental guarantees of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. At the same time, we also hope the Taiwan side will cherish the hard-won favorable situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and do more things that are conducive to improving and developing cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259931.htm"],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Reportedly, TSMC, Taiwan's leading wafer manufacturer, plans to invest in and build factories on the mainland, which has drawn attention. What is the mainland's attitude?","With the development of the mainland's economy and the continuous improvement of people's living standards, the mainland has become the world's largest and fastest-growing integrated circuit market. In 2013 and 2014, annual imports each exceeded 200 billion US dollars. A batch of internationally renowned enterprises, such as Samsung and Intel, have already invested in and set up factories on the mainland, fully demonstrating that the mainland's integrated circuit industry has enormous development potential and market space. As for Taiwan's integrated circuit enterprises investing on the mainland, we of course also take a positive and welcoming attitude, and hope that Taiwan enterprises will share the development opportunities on the mainland and achieve mutual benefit and win-win results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259920.htm"],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","Reports say Taiwan's tourism sector hopes to further increase the number of pilot cities for individual mainland tourist travel to Taiwan. Taiwan's competent authorities have said that after next year's elections, they will launch cross-Strait consultations on this as appropriate. What is the mainland's attitude?","Since the launch of individual travel by mainland residents to Taiwan in June 2011, 47 cities, including Beijing and Shanghai, have opened this business. As of September 2015, the cumulative total had reached 2,917,800 person-trips (291.78万), maintaining a rapid pace of development, promoting exchanges between the peoples on both sides, and being widely welcomed. We hope individual travel to Taiwan will develop in a healthy and orderly manner. Next, we will handle related matters as appropriate, based on the situation of cross-Strait relations and the demand of the cross-Strait tourism market.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259919.htm"],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The first question: Recently, some within the DPP have again advocated “freezing independence.” Spokesperson, if the DPP were to “freeze independence,” would Tsai Ing-wen's “maintaining the status quo” no longer be just empty words? The second question: The World Internet Conference opened today, and Terry Gou and others from Taiwan were invited to attend. Spokesperson, what room is there for future cross-Strait…","On the first question: “Taiwan independence” has no way out and does not win hearts and minds. We take a positive view of any words or deeds by DPP figures that move in the direction of abandoning the “Taiwan independence” party platform. On the second question: At this very moment, the Second World Internet Conference is being held in Wuzhen, Zhejiang. As an important component of the conference, the inaugural Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao Internet Development Forum will be held this afternoon. More than 400 senior media professionals, experts, scholars, and business people from both sides of the Strait and from Hong Kong and Macao will discuss topics such as the development and cooperation of e-commerce and the integration and transformation of media. We hope that both sides of the Strait can work together to build up and strengthen e-commerce, and that media on both sides can actively lead the development trend of new media, continue to play a positive role in promoting mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides and fostering friendly feelings, and fulfill their social responsibilities. At the same time, we also hope that the cultural and media sectors on both sides can join hands to create a new type of media industry with Chinese cultural characteristics, jointly promote Chinese culture, and jointly meet global competition and challenges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾三立电视台记者","TSMC has confirmed it will set up a plant in Nanjing, and it is said the mainland side has offered some preferential treatment. Could you specify what preferential measures are included? Second question: today, media reported that Hung Hsiu-chu may visit Beijing in the coming days and meet General Secretary Xi. Hung Hsiu-chu has just denied this rumor. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s response to this rumor?","The first question: Including Taiwan-funded enterprises, foreign enterprises investing on the mainland increasingly value the market opportunities on the mainland. Our policies on enterprise investment are open and transparent. Relevant departments and localities will do the related service work in accordance with the law.\nThe second question: As I understand it, Hung Hsiu-chu, former Vice Chairperson of the Chinese Kuomintang, at the invitation of the Cross-Strait Marriage and Family Association, will come to the mainland in the near future to take part in activities organized by the association and attend events such as the Mazu circuit procession in Kunshan. Our position of not interfering in Taiwan’s elections has been consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","It is reported that the \"small three links\" route from Huangqi in Fujian to Matsu will open. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","Huangqi in Fujian and Matsu are separated by only a narrow strip of water, and civilian exchanges between the two places have long been very close. Residents of Matsu have had a pressing need for a sea passenger route to and from Huangqi. Through joint efforts by relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, the Huangqi-Matsu passenger route will open in the near future, to facilitate personnel exchanges between the Fuzhou area and Matsu. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","The results of Taiwan's 2015 character-of-the-year vote were recently announced, and “换” (change) became this year's character of the year. What is the spokesperson's view?","We note that this is an annual selection of Chinese characters on affairs within Taiwan, organized by the United Daily News. Of course, we do not comment on Taiwan's internal affairs. What we want to emphasize is that the situation of peaceful development of cross-strait relations cannot be changed, the common political foundation for peaceful development of cross-strait relations cannot be changed, the shared pursuit of mutual benefit and win-win outcomes across the Strait cannot be changed, and the grand goal of compatriots on both sides of the Strait joining hands to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation cannot be changed either.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","First question: Ma Ying-jeou's delegation originally planned to inspect Taiping Island before December 12, but it was later changed to be carried out by others. What comments does the spokesperson have? Second question: according to Taiwan media reports, proposals to include mainland students studying in Taiwan in Taiwan's National Health Insurance and to shorten the years required for mainland spouses to obtain…","First question: The South China Sea Islands and their adjacent waters are China’s inherent territory. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation, is a common responsibility of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Our attitude and position on this are very clear.\nSecond question: Mainland spouses and mainland students studying in Taiwan have long been subjected to unfair discrimination in Taiwan. After years of appeals, far-sighted people in Taiwan and relevant Taiwan authorities have taken notice and begun to address the issue. But as everyone can see, the DPP, the “Taiwan Solidarity Union,” and some “Taiwan independence” forces, out of narrow partisan interest, have gone to great lengths to obstruct, undermine and interfere, so that the problem has been difficult to resolve for a long time. One cannot, on the one hand, tout democracy and human rights, and on the other hand deprive compatriots of their rightful interests. Such touting is self-contradictory. So, what the DPP does next will be watched closely by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","This week, Xiamen Port took the lead in realizing the regular transport of Taiwan vehicles into Fujian. What were the main considerations? Are there plans and a timetable for Fujian vehicles to enter Taiwan, or for cross-Strait vehicles to reach each other's other regions?","Because Fujian and Taiwan have very close relations both historically and in reality, encouraging and supporting exchanges between the two places is our established policy. At present, Taiwan vehicles entering Fujian has been partially realized. As for when Fujian vehicles will be able to go to Taiwan next, that still depends on Taiwan's policies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公报大公网记者","Some Taiwan media previously reported that the two sides carried out the so-called first \"prisoner swap\" in October, and that the person Taiwan released, Li Zhihao, is a Hong Kong resident. Please confirm. Thank you.","Regarding the parole of persons engaged in espionage activities, our Office's spokesperson already explained the relevant situation on November 30. The parole of Lee Chih-hao was handled by the relevant Taiwan authorities, and I am not aware of the relevant details.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","The first question: This afternoon, Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office will meet with Chen Fu-hai, magistrate of Kinmen County. What issues will the two be concerned about? Some media have commented that this meeting is meant to rescue Kinmen's electoral fortunes. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? The second question: Tsinghua Unigroup recently announced plans to acquire stakes in…","First question: It is understood that Kinmen County Magistrate Chen Fuhai will travel to Beijing from December 15 to 18 to attend a series of Taiwan county and city economic and trade exchange activities. During this period, Director Zhang Zhijun will meet with Magistrate Chen Fuhai and his delegation to exchange views on livelihood issues in Kinmen. We do not interfere in Taiwan's elections; this position is consistent, as is well known.\nSecond question: Regarding Unigroup's plan to invest in and acquire shares of a Taiwan semiconductor packaging and testing company, this is merely a simple corporate act and should not be politicized. Cross-Strait enterprises carry out independent cooperation in accordance with market rules, which is conducive to achieving mutual benefit and win-win outcomes. I would also like to stress that 20 years of development practice has proven that cross-Strait economic cooperation is complementary and mutually beneficial. It is not one side swallowing up the other, nor one side buying up and controlling the other. The benefits of cross-Strait economic cooperation for mainland enterprises are obvious, and the benefits it brings to Taiwan are equally countable. For example, Taiwan has obtained huge trade surpluses, Taiwan's GDP has maintained a certain scale of growth, and Taiwan's enterprises and industries have upgraded and transformed, with the mainland playing the most important role as Taiwan's economic hinterland. The trend of cross-Strait economic cooperation cannot be stopped, and it does not shift according to human will. We hope Taiwan society can fairly, objectively and rationally return to the economic dimension itself, and view cross-Strait economic cooperation, including cross-Strait industrial cooperation and cross-Strait mutual investment. Only then will it truly benefit the development of Taiwan's industries, the development of Taiwan's economy, and the well-being of the Taiwan people. Practice is the sole criterion for testing truth. Let time judge all of this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151216_11260237.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151216_11259907.htm"],[0,"2015-12-17","Hong Lei","","Regarding the US arms sale to Taiwan, China has decided to impose sanctions on Raytheon and Lockheed Martin, two involved companies. Can you provide more details on the sanction measures?","The involvement of US enterprises in the arms sale to Taiwan severely undermines China's sovereignty and security interests. The Chinese government and enterprises will not conduct cooperation or business with such enterprises.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1325380.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1325267.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-12-17","Hong Lei","","How will the US announcement of arms sale to Taiwan impact China-US ties?","No one can shake the firm will of the Chinese government and people to defend their national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to oppose foreign interference. China urges the US to live up to the clear commitment it has made in the three joint communiques, revoke the arms sale plan, stop military contact with Taiwan, and do more to advance the overall interests of China-US ties and peaceful development of cross-Straits relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1325380.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1325267.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2015-12-29","Lu Kang","","Taiwan said that it will consult with the Japanese side on the issue of comfort women. Will the Chinese side lodge representations with the Japanese side?","During the Second World War, the Japanese militarists forcibly recruited comfort women from different places in China, committing a severe crime against humanity. We urge the Japanese side to assume its responsibility, respect the concerns of the victims, and properly handle relevant issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1328578.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1328542.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 30, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first announced the relevant situation regarding the official launch today of the cross-Strait hotline, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Strait.","Dear media friends, good morning. The press conference now begins. First, I will announce an important piece of news.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Establishing a cross-Strait hotline was an important consensus reached by the leaders of both sides when they met in Singapore on November 7. Since that meeting, the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council have maintained close communication on the arrangements for setting up the hotline, which was officially put into operation today. Just now, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun and MAC Chairperson Hsia Li-yan made their first phone call via the cross-Strait hotline. Both sides affirmed that over the past year, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” the two agencies maintained communication and healthy interaction and promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations to achieve positive results. Especially in recent period, they have earnestly implemented the important consensus reached at the meeting of the leaders of both sides, and the results continue to emerge. We hope that in the future the two agencies, on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” will strive to maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and do more good deeds and seek more well-being for the peoples on both sides. Director Zhang Zhijun and Chairperson Hsia Li-yan also exchanged New Year greetings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344727.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen recently made some statements about the “1992 Consensus” at policy forums, debates and other occasions. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","In 1992, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan were authorized to consult on how to express adherence to the one-China principle in cross-Strait affairs negotiations. Through the Hong Kong talks in October of that year and a series of subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, they reached a consensus that each side would orally express that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle,” which was later summarized as the “1992 Consensus.” Its core meaning is that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and that cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations, thereby clearly defining the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. The reaching of the “1992 Consensus” was authorized by both sides across the Strait. Whether in the negotiation process or in the content of the consensus, it is very clear, has a complete historical record, and is beyond doubt.\nThe “1992 Consensus” is not only the common political foundation for cross-Strait consultations and negotiations; since 2008 it has also become the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It is precisely because of this foundation that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has achieved a series of important results, that peace and stability have been maintained in the Taiwan Strait area, and that people on both sides of the Strait have been able to share the dividends of peace. It is precisely because of this foundation that cross-Strait relations can continue to improve and develop, bringing real benefits to compatriots on both sides. At present, the key to maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is to acknowledge the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognize its core meaning. If the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation that acts as the sea-stabilizing divine needle, is lost, the institutionalized communication mechanisms across the Strait will inevitably be affected and may even collapse, and the boat of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will face huge waves and may even capsize completely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344660.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Relevant parties on both sides recently announced that they will expand the provinces and scale of the pilot program allowing mainland students to study in Taiwan through the “zhuanshengben” (upgrade-to-bachelor's) track. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To implement the outcomes of the meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Strait and promote cross-Strait education exchanges, relevant parties on the mainland have decided to take positive measures to further expand the opening of the “ZHUANSHENGBEN” (junior-college-to-bachelor's) track for mainland students studying in Taiwan, starting from 2016. First, Beijing, Shanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Liaoning, and Hubei, six additional provinces and municipalities, will be added as pilot provinces. Together with Guangdong and Fujian, which were already designated as pilot provinces in 2013, the number of pilot provinces will reach eight. Second, the enrollment quota will increase from the current 1,000 to 1,500. To ensure the smooth implementation of this work, the two sides' relevant parties recently held consultations, and the liaison units responsible for affairs related to mainland students studying in Taiwan are currently communicating and coordinating on specific details, to ensure that this good deed is done well.\nOver the years, under the new circumstances of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, cross-Strait education exchanges and cooperation have achieved positive results. We hope the Taiwan side will earnestly improve the environment for cross-Strait education exchanges and safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan. Both sides should work together to promote the healthy and orderly development of mainland students studying in Taiwan and create a good environment for exchanges and cooperation among young students across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344649.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","First question: Tsai Ing-wen has long denied the “1992 Consensus,” but this time she mentioned the historical fact of the 1992 cross-Strait talks, and spoke of mutual understanding across the Strait and seeking common ground while setting aside differences. What comments do you have on this? Second question: Hsu Hsin-liang recently said in an interview that if the “1992 Consensus” conforms to the “constitutional…","On the relevant questions concerning the “1992 Consensus,” I have just given a comprehensive and clear explanation and answer. In 1992, between the two associations, there was not only a process of talks; the consensus reached and its connotations are clear and unambiguous. The “1992 Consensus” is beyond question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Regarding those in Taiwan who make money investing on the mainland while funding “Taiwan independence” activities, what attitude does the mainland take?","We support and encourage cross-strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields to achieve mutual benefit and win-win outcomes. But we will never allow a small number of people to make money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and undermining cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344655.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, scholars and experts from both sides jointly issued an initiative recommending Xi Jinping and Ma Ying-jeou as candidates for the 2016 \"Nobel Peace Prize.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","This is a spontaneous, grassroots act. It shows that the outcomes and significance of the meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have deeply resonated with the public and are widely welcomed, and it also shows that the two peoples on both sides highly endorse the situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations since 2008. As for the hypothetical question, we will not respond.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","At the 2015 Cross-Strait Chinese Character Festival, co-hosted by media on both sides of the Strait, the character “和” (harmony) was selected as the Chinese character of the year for 2015 across the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Since 2008, on the common political basis of both sides upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides across the Strait have put cross-Strait relations on the path of peaceful development and achieved fruitful results. This path has won broad support from compatriots on both sides, because it accords with the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides for peace, stability and development, and conforms to their common interests. At present, cross-Strait relations are at an important juncture. The character “和” (he, meaning harmony and peace) truly reflects the cherishing by people on both sides of the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations over the past eight years, and their sincere hopes for the future of such development. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to safeguard the political foundation and correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and maintain the situation of peaceful development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344644.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央人民广播电台记者","The Central Economic Work Conference held recently proposed helping enterprises reduce costs, including lowering social insurance contributions. Does this apply to Taiwan-invested enterprises?","We attach great importance to issues that directly affect the vital interests of Taiwan-funded enterprises, such as reducing operating costs and improving the business environment. The Central Economic Work Conference clearly stated that one of the important measures for economic work in 2016 is helping enterprises reduce costs, one element of which is lowering social insurance contributions and studying the streamlining and consolidation of the “five social insurances and one housing fund.” This is a major benefit for the broad mass of Taiwan-funded enterprises. The Taiwan Affairs Office will, in accordance with the relevant arrangements, work with the relevant departments to do well the work concerning the “five social insurances and one housing fund” for Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201512/t20151230_11344646.htm"],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently said that he does not rule out visiting the mainland after leaving office. What response does the mainland have to this?","We support exchanges and interactions at all levels and in all fields across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank was established on December 25. Is there any more specific plan or arrangement regarding Taiwan joining the AIIB? Another question: Japan and South Korea reached an agreement on the “comfort women” issue on the 28th. Ma Ying-jeou also demanded yesterday that Japan apologize and compensate Taiwan on this matter. On the historical issue of the “comfort women,” do you think…","First question: we have repeatedly stated that we welcome Taiwan joining the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) in an appropriate manner, and this attitude has not changed.\nSecond question: the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on this. During World War II, Japanese militarism forcibly conscripted “comfort women” across various parts of China and committed grave crimes against humanity. We urge Japan to genuinely bear its responsibility, respect the concerns of the victims, and properly handle the relevant issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2015-12-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Some in Taiwan have proposed revising the history curriculum guidelines to delete the word “forced” from “were forced to become comfort women.” What is the spokesperson's view on this?","Any history curriculum outline should respect historical facts and should not be distorted for the sake of one party's private interests or for some political purpose.\n2015 is about to pass and 2016 is approaching us. As the New Year is about to arrive, on behalf of the Press Bureau of the TAO, I extend New Year's greetings to media friends and wish everyone good health, smooth work, a happy family, and all the best in 2016!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201512/t20151230_11345139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2015-12-31","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have a question about the recent U.S. weapon sales to Taiwan. The Chinese government was very angry with the new weapon sales to Taiwan by the United States. But the Taiwanese government says that China aims more than a thousand missiles at Taiwan, and, therefore, it needs to defend itself. Why doesn’t China withdraw these missiles aiming at Taiwan if it really wants to maintain peace and stability in the…","China’s position of promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations has been consistent and clear. I would like to stress that China is firmly opposed to arms sale to Taiwan by any country.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-12/31/content_4634720.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2015-12-31","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Returning to the issue of Taiwan arms sales. At the time the Chinese government and defense ministry said that the Chinese side planed to retaliate against companies that were involved in the technology being transferred to Taiwan. Can you give us details on what sort of sanctions have been taken? What companies have been sanctioned and anything else? Thank you.","The Ministry of Foreign Affair and the Ministry of National Defense of China both issued statement, expressing China’s solemn stance on the U.S. arms sales to Taiwan.\nAs to the details of the question that you have raised, please refer to relevant authorities of the government.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2015-12/31/content_4634720.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2016-01-06","Hua Chunying","","First, it is reported that Indonesia and China are cooperating to stop religious extremists from illegally entering Indonesia. Why is that? Can you confirm whether or not Indonesian counter-terrorism officials have come to China to investigate relevant case? Second, do you have any comment on Taiwan and Japan holding consultations on the issue of comfort women?","On your first question, the Chinese side attaches great importance to safeguarding Chinese citizens’ rights and interests to legally enter and exit the country, and has enhanced cooperation on law enforcement with countries around the world including Indonesia to combat transnational crimes. We will work with countries concerned in the region to firmly crack down on illegal immigration and human smuggling that violate international conventions and law. As for Indonesian officials’ investigation in China, I have no relevant information at the moment.\nOn your second question, China’s position on the issue of comfort women is very clear. We believe that the Japanese side should properly deal with the relevant issue in an honest and responsible manner. Our position on Taiwan’s external contact is consistent.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1329999.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1329896.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-01-15","Hong Lei","","Taiwan will hold the election on January 16. How will China handle the cross-Straits relations?","The spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already made our position clear regarding the election and the cross-Straits relations. I want to stress that we stick to the One China Principle, oppose \"Taiwan independence\", \"two Chinas\", \"one China, one Taiwan\". This policy remains unchanged and will not change regardless of what happens in Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1332038.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1332010.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-01-16","Not identified in source","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Voting is underway in Taiwan's elections. How does the mainland view the election results that are about to be announced? The spokesperson made the above remarks in answering questions.\nWhat is your view of the Chou Tzu-yu incident? It is said that Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council has communicated with the Taiwan Affairs Office on this matter; please confirm. The spokesperson said that since 2008, on the…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 16 (reporter Chen Jianxing): A spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 16th: We have long made clear that we do not intervene in Taiwan's elections; what we are concerned about is cross-Strait relations.\nHe said that some political forces in Taiwan are exploiting individual incidents in civilian exchanges across the Strait to sow discord between the peoples on both sides, and compatriots on both sides must remain highly vigilant. In communication with Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, the Taiwan Affairs Office conveyed our consistent position and attitude.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160116_11366650.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-01-18","Hong Lei","","Tsai Ing-wen, candidate of the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) won the election in Taiwan. How will it impact the cross-Straits relations? How would the mainland react if Tsai Ing-wen pursued \"Taiwan Independence\" after taking office?","Head of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already made a statement on the election in Taiwan.\nThe Taiwan question falls within China's internal affairs. There is only one China in the world. Both the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. China's sovereignty and territorial integrity brook no division. This basic fact and consensus of the international community will not be changed by the result of the election in Taiwan. The Chinese government sticks to the one-China principle and opposes \"Taiwan independence\", \"two Chinas\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\". This position remains unchanged and will not change regardless of what happens in Taiwan. On such a major issue as safeguarding state sovereignty and territorial integrity, the Chinese government has rock-solid determination and never tolerates any separatist activities aiming at \"Taiwan independence\". We hope and believe that the international community will adhere to the one-China principle, stand against any forms of \"Taiwan independence\" and support, with concrete actions, the peaceful development of the cross-Straits relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1332584.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1332505.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-01-18","Hong Lei","","It is reported that former US Deputy Secretary of State William Burns is inTaiwan for meetings with Taiwan politicians. What is China's comment on that?","The Chinese side has expressed concerns with the US side. I would like to reiterate that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Taiwan affairs are China's internal affairs. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China policy, uphold the principle enshrined in the three joint communiqués between China and the US, honor its commitment against \"Taiwan independence\", speak and act cautiously, refrain from interfering in China's internal affairs in any form, and make more efforts to facilitate the steady growth of China-US relations and the peaceful development of the cross-Straits relations, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1332584.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1332505.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-01-21","Hong Lei","","US Deputy Secretary of State Antony Blinken is in Beijing for a visit. Who will meet with him? Will the bilateral discussion mainly focus on issues about the DPRK and Taiwan?","US Deputy Secretary of State Blinken is in China on January 20 and 21 to co-host the interim Strategic Security Dialogue with Executive Vice Foreign Minister Zhang Yesui. The two sides will exchange views on China-US relations, strategic security, comprehensive security and other issues of common interest.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1333741.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1333693.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-01-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Tsai Ing-wen recently said in an interview with Taiwan media: “In 1992, the two sides' associations conducted communication and consultation with a political mindset of mutual understanding and seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and reached a number of common perceptions and understandings. I understand and respect this historical fact,” and “The status quo and achievements…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 21 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — In response to remarks Tsai Ing-wen recently made in an interview with Taiwanese media, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 21st in response to questions that only by upholding the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations advance steadily and go far.\nMa Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions: We have noted the relevant reports.\nHe said that since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and cannot change.\nHe pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and its core meaning is that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Only by continuing to uphold and safeguard this common political foundation can the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations advance steadily and go far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160121_11371098.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Today's briefing now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","2015 has passed, and many major events have occurred in cross-Strait relations. I would like you to evaluate the progress of cross-Strait relations in 2015, and also look ahead: in which direction will cross-Strait relations develop in 2016?","In 2015, cross-Strait relations advanced steadily and achieved new and important progress. First, the leaders of the two sides met for the first time in 66 years, a historic breakthrough in cross-Strait political exchanges that reached a new high. Second, the liaison and communication mechanism between the two sides' competent authorities for cross-Strait affairs operated effectively, playing an important role in promoting exchanges and cooperation across all fields. Third, the two sides' cross-Strait Association and Straits Exchange Foundation signed new agreements, adding new achievements to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Fourth, cross-Strait trade and investment developed steadily and economic cooperation continued to deepen. Total cross-Strait trade reached US$188.56 billion; the mainland approved 2,962 Taiwan-funded projects, with actual use of Taiwan investment of US$1.54 billion; and 95 investment projects and enterprises going to Taiwan, with investment amounting to US$436 million, were approved by the relevant mainland competent authorities. The project to supply water from Fujian to the Kinmen area officially began construction. Cross-Strait cooperation in cold chain logistics, LED lighting, e-commerce and other industries made new progress, and cooperation among small and medium-sized enterprises advanced steadily. The mainland actively used market forces to further promote Taiwan agricultural and fishery products' entry into the mainland market. It expanded the opening to Taiwan residents to apply to set up individually owned businesses on the mainland. It established 21 Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Bases and 1 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Demonstration Site, and encouraged qualified state-owned enterprises, private enterprises and Taiwan-funded enterprises to provide positions for Taiwan youth to intern and find employment. Fifth, cross-Strait personnel exchanges expanded steadily, and exchanges in all fields continued to maintain good momentum. Total cross-Strait personnel exchanges reached 9.8561 million person-times, up 4.73% year on year. Of these, Taiwan residents coming to the mainland numbered 5.4986 million person-times, up 2.47% year on year, and mainland residents traveling to Taiwan numbered 4.3575 million person-times, up 7.73% year on year. It is projected that mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism will reach 3.4 million person-times for the year, again reaching a historic high. The mainland remains Taiwan's largest inbound tourism market. The mainland implemented multiple-entry permits for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and card-type Taiwan compatriot travel permits. It expanded the opening of cities for individual travel to Taiwan and of travel agencies organizing group tours to Taiwan. The total number of regular cross-Strait passenger flights increased from 840 flights per week to 890 flights per week. A direct sea route from Fujian's Huangqi to Taiwan's Matsu was opened. Suzhou was added as a mail processing center for cross-Strait postal mail. The opening was further expanded for mainland students to study in Taiwan through the \"upgrade from junior college to bachelor's program\" track. Leading officials from relevant provinces and municipalities were continuously encouraged to visit Taiwan for exchanges, providing new platforms for culture, arts, education, folk customs, grassroots and youth exchanges across the Strait. Sixth, compatriots on both sides commemorated the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the restoration of Taiwan in their own ways. Looking back on history and cherishing the memory of the fallen, they more deeply understood that the mainland and Taiwan are an inseparable community of shared destiny. The relevant parties on both sides strengthened communication and coordination, jointly combated crime, handled cross-Strait corporate rights disputes and major emergencies involving people on both sides, and worked to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides and maintain the healthy order of cross-Strait exchanges and contacts.\nThe new achievements in cross-Strait relations in 2015 fully demonstrate that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is a correct path of mutual benefit and cooperation that benefits compatriots on both sides, and that adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" is the \"stabilizing needle\" for maintaining peace across the Strait and advancing the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations.\nAt present, although major changes have occurred in the situation on the island of Taiwan, the legal and factual reality that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has not changed and cannot change. On the major principled issues of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, our will is as firm as a rock and our position is consistent. In the new year, we will continue to implement the central government's basic policies on Taiwan affairs, adhere to the \"1992 Consensus,\" resolutely oppose any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activity, work together with compatriots on both sides to maintain the common political foundation across the Strait, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, safeguard the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, and maintain the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376019.htm"],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","TAO Director Zhang Zhijun recently met with U.S. Executive Deputy Secretary of State Blinken. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On January 21, Director Zhang Zhijun met with US Deputy Secretary of State Blinken in Beijing and, responding to questions, introduced the current situation in the Taiwan Strait and cross-Strait relations. Director Zhang said that over the past eight years, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides across the Strait have forged a path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This favorable situation needs to be cherished all the more. Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear, and it will not change because of the results of elections in Taiwan. We will continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and firmly uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Director Zhang stressed that recent changes in the situation on the island have brought uncertainty to the development of cross-Strait relations, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait face challenges. The US side should continue to abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly respect China's major concerns, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to reports, the head of Taiwan’s economic authority recently said that negotiations on the cross-Strait Trade in Goods Agreement will be suspended. What is the mainland’s attitude on this?","Since March 2011, the cross-Strait negotiating teams have held 12 rounds of business communication on the cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods. In this process, the mainland side, adhering to the principles of mutual benefit and win-win results, has made active efforts to advance the interests of compatriots on both sides. As for the next steps in negotiations, that depends on communication between the two sides and the state of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Ker Chien-ming, convener of the DPP caucus in Taiwan, recently said that the DPP advocates resuming negotiations on the cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office comment on this?","First, we believe that the political foundation on which the two associations were authorized to negotiate, and the authority of the agreements they reached, should be safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376016.htm"],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","There are rumors that the mainland may tighten its quota for travel to Taiwan. Is this restriction order real?","First, I must clarify that relevant mainland authorities have never set quotas for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan; quotas are a unilateral practice of the Taiwan side. We hope that a healthy and orderly environment for travel to Taiwan will be maintained, and that the rights and interests of mainland tourists will be respected and protected. As for changes in the number of travelers to Taiwan, that is a market behavior that depends on the wishes of travel agencies and tourists. Next, we will handle relevant matters as circumstances warrant, based on the state of cross-Strait relations and the demand in the cross-Strait tourism market.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376015.htm"],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Recently, several hundred thousand mainland netizens expressed their positions on Facebook, making the meme battle between netizens across the two sides of the Strait a hot topic. What is the spokesperson’s view of this unconventional form of exchange?","I also saw this news in the media. I believe that young people on both sides of the Strait should strengthen exchanges, enhance mutual communication and understanding through exchanges, continuously deepen their correct understanding of cross-Strait relations, and continuously foster the national sentiment of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Two questions. First, Tsai Ing-wen recently made some statements about the 1992 cross-Strait talks; I would like to ask the spokesperson for comment. Second, the mainland is planning to pilot opening transit services for mainland residents through Taoyuan Airport in Taiwan. May I ask what specific progress has been made on transit for mainland tourists? Thank you.","The first question: Since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and cannot change. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and its core meaning is that both sides belong to one China. Only by continuing to uphold and safeguard this common political foundation can the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations proceed steadily and go far.\nRegarding the question of opening pilot cities for the transit of mainland tourists, ARATS and SEF are communicating on the relevant preparatory work. It can be implemented as soon as the preparations are ready.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","After Taiwan's elections, the political situation has undergone some new changes. Will this affect the newly opened cross-Strait hotline? Will the communication mechanism established between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council be interrupted?","We have stressed many times that the achievements of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations are built on the common political foundation of both sides upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Only by maintaining this political foundation can the achievements of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations avoid being lost. If this anchor is shaken, cross-Strait relations will inevitably be impacted. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376018.htm"],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","I would like to ask the spokesperson two questions. Taiwan leader Ma Ying-jeou may recently visit Taiping Island. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s view on this matter? In addition, cold damage occurred in central and southern Taiwan last week. What is the current status of cross-Strait milkfish contract farming?","First question: China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation, is the common responsibility and obligation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond question: A few days ago, an extreme polar cold wave affected agricultural and fishery production on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and caused certain damage, and we are deeply concerned about this.\nIn recent years, we have been actively promoting the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland through market mechanisms, expanding the scope of beneficiaries. As for the contract farming of milkfish, to my understanding it is being carried out by civil enterprises on both sides, and I do not yet have specific knowledge of the particular situation you mentioned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","On the issue of transit for mainland tourists: three cities are currently open. Which cities will be opened in the next wave, and when? Has the mainland agreed to decouple the transit of mainland tourists from the issue of further facilitating people-to-people exchanges across the Strait? Another question: the AIIB has officially begun operations. Will Taiwan have a chance to join this year, in the first half? If…","First, regarding transit for mainland tourists: the pilot opening of transit for mainland tourists is intended to implement the outcomes of the meeting between the leaders of the two sides, and also to facilitate exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait and help the development of cross-Strait aviation. We chose the three cities of Nanchang, Kunming, and Chongqing because they are popular cities for outbound tourism in the mainland's central and western regions. This is a decision made by relevant mainland competent departments after comprehensively considering various factors.\nWhether to further expand the opening in the next step will be determined in light of the operation of the first batch of pilot openings and the broader environment of cross-Strait relations.\nFinally, I would like to point out that “continuing to consult on opening other, more convenient new air routes” was already a stated item in the Supplementary Cross-Strait Air Transport Agreement, and is also a complete part of the issue of “transit for mainland tourists and facilitating exchanges between people on both sides.” It is necessary to reduce the cost of exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, enhance the attractiveness of “transit for mainland tourists,” break through capacity bottlenecks, and avoid safety risks, so it is reasonable. We hope both sides will move toward each other, and both can maintain a positive and open attitude and take practical measures to facilitate exchanges between the peoples on both sides. This is my answer to your first question.\nAs for the second question, we have repeatedly stated that we welcome Taiwan's participation in the AIIB in an appropriate manner, and this position has not changed. We believe that the AIIB, as a newly established international organization, will handle the issue of Taiwan's accession in accordance with the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the AIIB's articles of association.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","While Director Zhang Zhijun was meeting with the US Deputy Secretary of State, a former US Deputy Secretary of State also went to Taiwan and met with senior political figures there. Some experts point out that Tsai Ing-wen's frequent interactions with senior US and Japanese officials aim to internationalize the Taiwan question and reduce Taiwan's economic and political ties with the mainland. What response does…","The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We hope the US side will abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, and earnestly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. At the same time, we also emphasize that “Taiwan independence” has no international space. The attempt to expand so-called international space by damaging cross-Strait relations is unrealistic, and it runs counter to the overall pattern of the international community adhering to the one-China policy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","About three and a half months remain before Tsai Ing-wen takes office on May 20. May I ask you: during this transition period, will you watch what she says and how she acts? In addition, if Tsai Ing-wen never acknowledges the “1992 Consensus,” will cross-strait economic and trade relations be the first to be affected?","The development of cross-Strait relations over the past more than 20 years has fully proven that if we uphold the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” the prospects for cross-Strait relations are bright. Conversely, the ship of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will encounter huge waves and may even capsize completely. Everyone is very clear on this point.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Has a cross-Strait hotline been activated since the elections until today? The second question concerns the South China Sea. Apart from the possibility that Ma Ying-jeou will land on Taiping Island tomorrow, what is the Taiwan Affairs Office's evaluation of Tsai Ing-wen's South China Sea position? Third question: a few days after Taiwan's elections, CCTV broadcast a PLA military exercise on the southeast coast,…","On the hotline: Adherence to the “1992 Consensus” is an important basis for the establishment of the liaison and communication mechanism between the cross-Strait affairs competent authorities, and also a necessary condition for its normal operation. The cross-Strait hotline is used to communicate on major and urgent matters in cross-Strait relations, and is used when both sides agree it is necessary. So far, I am not aware of any recent use of the hotline.\nOn the second question: China has indisputable sovereignty over the islands of the South China Sea. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Compatriots on both sides have a responsibility to jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nOn the third question: The Ministry of National Defense has already explained the relevant situation. I also need to point out that the foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is adherence to the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” With this foundation, the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can be maintained, and its prospects will be bright. If this foundation is undermined, as I mentioned just now, the ship of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will encounter raging waves and may even capsize completely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Not long ago, it was announced that Gong Qinggai, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, had been placed under investigation. Why was this announced at this particular juncture? Will it affect the future development of cross-Strait relations?","Obviously you have also noticed media reports, including those by Phoenix Television, which should answer your question. What I want to say is that Gong Qinggai is suspected of serious violations of discipline and is under organizational investigation; the CCDI website has already released the news. The Central Taiwan Affairs Office firmly supports the central decision, will take this as a warning, self-discipline to a high standard, solidly carry out rectification following inspection, and unwaveringly advance Party conduct and clean governance and the fight against corruption.\nIncidentally, our office's rectification progress following inspection will be announced to the public in the near future, and everyone is welcome to supervise.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201601/t20160127_11376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said at the regular press conference on January 27 in response to questions: We have stated many times that we welcome Taiwan's participation in the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) in an appropriate manner, and this attitude has not changed. We believe that the AIIB, as a newly established international organization, will handle Taiwan's accession to the AIIB in accordance with the One-China principle and the relevant provisions of the AIIB's articles of association.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376013.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-01-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to questions about whether Ma Ying-jeou may land on Taiping Island and about the evaluation of Tsai Ing-wen's South China Sea claims, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated at the regular press conference on January 27 in response to questions: China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands. The two sides of the Strait belong to one China. Compatriots on both sides have the responsibility to jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201601/t20160127_11376014.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-01-28","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan's leader Ma Ying-jeou visited Taiping Dao today and issued a statement. What is your comment?","The Nansha Islands have historically been China's territory. Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Straits share the responsibility to protect the ancestral property of the Chinese nation.\nThe Chinese government has been committed to making the South China Sea a sea of peace, friendship and cooperation, and will continue to make positive efforts to safeguard navigation freedom, peace and stability, and prosperity and development of the South China Sea.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1336013.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1335975.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-02-05","Lu Kang","","Recently there have been a number of cyber attacks on Taiwan \"President\" Tsai Ing-wen's Facebook page that appeared to be coming from mainland Chinese users. Some speculate that the Chinese government is potentially supporting those attacks. What is your response to the speculation?","First I must say that Taiwan is a part of China. We hope that when talking about sovereignty-related issues, rhetoric would be chosen in line with the one-China principle.\nI wonder whether there is any evidence to support the speculation you mentioned. We have heard a great variety of speculations concerning cyber security. We don't have that much time to spend our efforts commenting on each and every groundless allegation or hearsay like that.\nThe Regular Press Conference of the Foreign Ministry will be adjourned from February 8 to 12 for the Spring Festival vacation, and resumed on February 15 (Monday). During the adjournment, the Spokesperson's Office of the Chinese Foreign Ministry will take your questions by phone.\nToday's press conference is the last one that we have in the Chinese lunar year of goat. Wish you all a happy lunar new year! We also hope that friends from the foreign press would share with us the happiness of Spring Festival.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1338870.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1338806.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-02-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 6 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, in an interview with Xinhua reporters on the morning of the 6th, expressed concern and sympathy regarding the earthquake disaster in southern Taiwan. He said that from 6:00 a.m. on the 6th, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) has been in contact with the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) by telephone to learn about the earthquake damage and express sympathy. ARATS will soon formally send a letter to the SEF stating that, if the Taiwan side needs it, the mainland is willing to provide disaster relief assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160206_11384209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-02-16","Hong Lei","","Dolkun Isa, head of the World Uyghur Congress (WUC), has been refused permission to visit Taiwan. He said that it is because the Chinese government has put pressure on Taiwan. Can you confirm that?","Dolkun Isa is wanted by the International Criminal Police Organization and China. He is suspected of organizing and carrying out a series of explosions, murders, robberies and other severe criminal activities as well as violent terrorist activities. He has been supporting violent terrorist activities by the East Turkistan Islamic Movement and East Turkistan terrorists with fund and training. Terrorism is our common enemy. Fighting against terrorism is a consensus shared by all.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1340925.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1340906.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-02-22","Hua Chunying","","The regional election in Taiwan at the beginning of this year has led to changes of the political landscape in Taiwan. Will Foreign Minister Wang Yi require the US side to reaffirm its opposition to \"Taiwan independence\"?","The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive question in China-US relations. The US should honor its commitment to the one-China policy, the three China-US joint communiqués and opposing \"Taiwan independence\". It must not send any wrong message to \"Taiwan independence\" forces. Rather, it should support the peaceful development of cross-Straits relations through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1342276.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1342231.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear friends from the media, good morning. Welcome to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I will be hosting today's press conference. Now, I am glad to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","新华社记者","After Taiwan’s presidential election earlier this year, public opinion has paid close attention to how the mainland will interact with the DPP authorities about to take office. May I ask the spokesperson, based on the current situation, what adjustments will the mainland make to its Taiwan policy after 5·20? Is it possible for the two sides to communicate before 5·20? What are the preconditions for communication?","Our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We will adhere to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence,” continue to advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and strive to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Without the “1992 Consensus” as the anchor, the ship of peaceful cross-Strait development would encounter huge waves and could even capsize completely. We have said many times that regardless of which party or group in Taiwan, and whatever it advocated in the past, as long as it acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizes the core meaning that both sides belong to one China, we are willing to engage with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394366.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","The competent authorities on cross-Strait affairs have established a regular communication mechanism. Is it possible for the heads of the Taiwan Affairs Office and Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council to meet before May 20?","In February 2014, the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council established a liaison and communication mechanism on the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which has played an active role in promoting exchanges and cooperation across all cross-strait fields. Meetings between the heads of the two departments are an important component of this mechanism. In several earlier meetings, both sides emphasized that, on the common basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” they would continue to promote exchanges and cooperation in all cross-strait fields and the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. As for another meeting between the heads of the two departments, both sides are currently actively assessing it and maintaining communication.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394362.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The KMT is conducting a by-election for its party chairman. What is the spokesperson's comment on this by-election and on the candidates?","The election of the Chairperson of the Kuomintang is an internal affair of the Kuomintang, and we will not comment on it.\nWe hope that the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang will continue, on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to work together to safeguard and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to bring benefits to the compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394364.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","A DPP legislator in Taiwan has proposed abolishing the portraits of Sun Yat-sen hung in schools or government agencies. What impact do you think this will have on cross-Strait relations?","We have noted the relevant reports. Mr. Sun Yat-sen was a great pioneer of China's modern democratic revolution, who pursued national unification and the revival of China throughout his life, and he is revered by all Chinese descendants. The move by DPP figures can be described as “Sima Zhao's intention is known to all passersby.” We have also noted that Taiwan public opinion has pointed out that this is yet another move that “undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the status quo of peaceful development of cross-strait relations” and “de-Sinicizes” Taiwan, and it should arouse high vigilance among compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394359.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Minister of Commerce Gao Hucheng said on the 23rd that he hopes the Taiwan side will bring the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement into effect as soon as possible. Otherwise, it will not be a matter of rising early and arriving late to the market; we may not even make it to the late market. What is the spokesperson’s view on this? Second question: what is your view of the “Draft Regulations on Supervision of…","We have repeatedly stated our position on the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement. The basis for cross-Strait consultations and negotiations must not be undermined, and the authority of the agreements negotiated and signed under the authorization of the two associations should be upheld. It is abnormal that the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement has been stalled for a long time in Taiwan and has still not taken effect. The greatest harm falls on Taiwan’s industry and ordinary people.\nOn the second question: the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not a “state-to-state” relationship. We have repeatedly stated that the basis for cross-Strait consultations and negotiations must not be undermined, and the authority of agreements signed under the authorization of the two associations should be upheld.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","中新社记者","In his new book, Lee Teng-hui claimed that “the Diaoyu Islands belong to Japan” and vigorously promoted “Taiwan independence.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The new book by Lee Teng-hui is filled with blatant “Taiwan independence” claims, treasonous words and deeds, and a colonial and servile mentality. It once again exposes his obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” stance and his essence as an enemy of compatriots on both sides and the Chinese nation, and it has been strongly condemned by compatriots on both sides.\nI would like to emphasize that since 1949, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. We will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan away from China under any name or in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394357.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","We note that Tsai Ing-wen has for some time not publicly denied the “1992 Consensus,” and she has also proposed promoting cross-Strait relations under the existing “constitutional system.” May I ask whether the mainland side will give a green light to exchanges between the DPP and the CPC on this basis? The second question: there have recently been reports that the mainland has banned television stations and…","On the first question: We have repeatedly and clearly stated that the “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. If the “1992 Consensus,” this pillar that steadies the seas, is shaken, cross-Strait relations will inevitably be impacted. We have also said many times that regardless of which party or group in Taiwan it is, as long as it acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and endorses the core meaning that both sides belong to one China, we are willing to engage with it.\nOn the second question: I am not aware of the specific circumstances. What I want to emphasize is that the relevant mainland authorities will handle the introduction and broadcast of overseas TV programs in accordance with law and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, recently there have been cases of mainland tourists’ applications being approved without queuing, and even quotas going unused. Please confirm this. In addition, Taiwan’s tourism operators are worried that the number of visitors to Taiwan continues to be sluggish, so they demand that Tsai Ing-wen fulfill her promises. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Changes in the number of visitors to Taiwan are a market behavior, mainly determined by the willingness of travel agencies and tourists. We hope that a healthy and orderly environment for mainland tourism to Taiwan can be maintained, and that the legitimate rights and interests of mainland tourists can be valued and protected. In the next step, we will handle this according to the development of the cross-Strait situation and changes in cross-Strait tourism market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","Mainland tourist transit to Taiwan officially began on February 1. Will other cities be opened further? Is there a timetable, and how do you estimate the benefits?","The pilot for transit of mainland tour groups began on February 1, and it has been less than a month. The next steps will depend on the actual operation of the trial transit and the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","The Cross-Strait Industrial Matchmaking Program was launched in 2008. Some enterprises are worried about whether Cross-Strait industrial matchmaking projects will continue after May 20. Please clarify.","In recent years, against the background of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, relevant cross-Strait institutions have held cross-Strait industry exchange activities every year. As for next steps, relevant parties on both sides are currently in contact regarding the related arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Please explain: what is the relationship between Deputy Director Chen Yuanfeng’s recent visit to Taiwan and future KMT exchanges?","Deputy Director Chen Yuanfeng took advantage of the Spring Festival period, in line with practice in recent years, to visit some old friends in Taiwan. As for KMT-CPC exchanges, I have just clearly stated that we hope the Kuomintang and the Communist Party will continue to work together, on the shared political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to maintain and advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and benefit the people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","You just mentioned that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. May I ask whether, before 5·20, the mainland and the DPP would communicate through a second channel to find a balance point acceptable to both sides?","Our policy toward the DPP is consistent and clear. As I have just emphasized, upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Any party or group in Taiwan, as long as it can acknowledge the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognize the core meaning that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, we are willing to engage with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","人民日报记者","Please, what is the mainland's attitude toward the follow-up negotiations on the cross-Strait trade in goods agreement?","On the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus,” the cross-Strait negotiation teams have carried out 12 rounds of business communication on the goods trade agreement since March 2011. As for the next steps in negotiations, both sides are currently communicating, and there will be results soon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394360.htm"],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, a Taiwanese legislator hoped to change \"Mainland China\" to \"Chinese Beijing\" at some international occasions, saying that this would keep Taiwan from being belittled. The mainland has consistently promoted exchanges between young people across the Taiwan Strait, but some young people in Taiwan have moved toward a more \"pro-independence\" stance. What is your view on this?","First, our position in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is firm and unwavering. On Taiwan’s external exchanges and Taiwan-related issues in international affairs, our position has been consistent and clear: handle them in accordance with the one-China principle. On cross-Strait youth exchanges: for various reasons, some people on the island, especially the younger generation, may hold some vague understandings of the mainland and of cross-Strait relations. We are willing to narrow the psychological distance across the Strait with sincerity, goodwill and kinship, and achieve heart-to-heart understanding. We are also willing to strengthen exchanges in all fields and expand cross-Strait cooperation, and through deepening the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, to promote mutual understanding and emotional integration between people on both sides, especially the younger generation, deepen their correct understanding of cross-Strait relations, and strengthen the national sentiment that compatriots on both sides are one family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Not long ago the TAO and the China Development Bank signed a cooperation agreement to promote cross-strait economic development. What substantive help will this agreement provide to cross-strait economic development, including the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland?","On February 5, the TAO and the China Development Bank signed the “Cooperation Agreement on Promoting the Integrated Development of Cross-Strait Economies” in Beijing. This is the third cooperation between the TAO and the CDB, and another strong measure to support cross-strait economic and trade cooperation in the new situation. We believe this will play a positive role in promoting cross-strait financial exchanges and cooperation and in promoting the integrated development of the cross-strait economies. Relevant information has already been reported by the media, and you may refer to it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","At the start of the New Year, an earthquake occurred in southern Taiwan, which has concerned mainland people deeply. General Secretary Xi Jinping (习近平) and all sectors of mainland society are paying close attention. May I ask you to introduce how the mainland has conveyed its love and care to people on the island of Taiwan?","At dawn on February 6, a magnitude 6.7 earthquake struck southern Taiwan, causing major casualties and property losses. General Secretary Xi Jinping and Premier Li Keqiang delivered speeches, expressing deep mourning for the victims, sincere sympathy for the injured compatriots, and stating their willingness to provide assistance in all respects.\nSocial circles across the mainland are also deeply concerned, expressing their sympathy and desire to help, and actively donating. Preliminary statistics show that the total donations have exceeded 20 million yuan. Specific details were extensively reported by media on both sides of the Taiwan Strait some time ago.\nNatural disasters are merciless, but compatriots have love. We sincerely wish that the Taiwan compatriots affected by the disaster will soon heal the wounds of the earthquake and rebuild their homes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台","Reports say the mainland has deployed fighter jets on Yongxing Island in the Xisha (Paracel) Islands, which has raised concern in Taiwan that the mainland may change the overall military balance in the South China Sea. Please respond to this.","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has previously stated our solemn position on the relevant issue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201602/t20160224_11394383.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-02-24","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question: The DPP caucus resolved a party-version “Draft Cross-Strait Agreement Oversight Act,” which will use the name “Taiwan Area and Mainland Area” in its title. Some Taiwan public opinion holds that this reflects a gesture of goodwill toward the mainland. What is your comment?","Anfeng Shan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on February 24 at the regular press conference in response to a question: The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not “state-to-state” relations. Our position on cross-Strait agreement consultations and negotiations is also very clear. The basis of cross-Strait agreement consultations and negotiations must not be undermined, and the authority of agreements reached by the two associations under authorized consultations should be upheld and respected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201602/t20160224_11394365.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-03-11","Hong Lei","","The US State Department said in a statement on March 10 that the US government had authorized the sale of two US Navy frigates to Taiwan for US$ 190 million, subject to congressional approval. What is China's response to that?","The Chinese side has lodged representations with the US State Department about the relevant report and asked the US side for clarification. The US State Department said that no plan has been made recently on arms sales to Taiwan, and that it has not issued any statement about selling arms to Taiwan. I want to stress that the Chinese side is resolutely opposed to arms sales by the US to Taiwan. This position is consistent, firm and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1347202.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1347124.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-03-15","Lu Kang","","The party formed through the merger of Japan's opposition Democratic Party and Ishin no To will be named Minshin To, the namesake of Taiwan's Democratic Progressive Party. What is your comment?","We have no comment on that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1347923.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1347899.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-03-17","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said today in response to a question that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has issued a statement on the restoration of China–Gambia diplomatic relations. We adhere to the one-China principle, and the policy of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has not changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160317_11412601.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-03-21","Hua Chunying","","US President Barack Obama signed a bill on March 18, asking the US Secretary of State to develop a strategy to obtain observer status for Taiwan in the International Criminal Police Organization (Interpol). What is your comment?","Interpol is an intergovernmental organization made up of sovereign states. Eligibility of membership is clearly stated in its legal materials. China always deals with Taiwan's participation in international organizations in line with the one-China principle, and this position is clear and consistent. Chinese mainland and relevant sides have made practical arrangements for how Taiwan would participate in Interpol's cooperation on combating criminal offenses. Such arrangements have been proved effective.\nThe Taiwan issue is China's domestic affair. China urges the US to abide by the one-China policy and principles enshrined in the three communiques between China and the US, and refrain from supporting Taiwan to join any international organization so as not to hurt Cross-Straits relations and China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1349416.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1349368.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-03-21","Hua Chunying","","The Taiwan side said today that China's restoration of diplomatic ties with Gambia was to put pressure on Tsai Ing-wen. Did the mainland do this to impose pressure on Tsai Ing-wen?","My colleague has taken this question last week. The time for China's restoration of diplomatic ties with Gambia was set upon consultation. It has been long since Gambia severed its so called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. China and Gambia's restoration of diplomatic relations does not target anyone.\nI also want to emphasize that there is only one China in the world. Mainland and Taiwan belong to one same China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity shall not be undermined. The Chinese government is committed to developing friendly and cooperative relations with all countries based on the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one-China principle. We always deal with Taiwan's relations with others following the one-China principle, and object to activities aiming to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China and one Taiwan\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1349416.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1349368.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-03-23","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan authorities today invited some foreign media to Taiping Dao. Is China concerned about this? Do you think this is appropriate? The Philippines has also invited foreign journalists to some islands and reefs quite often, and why doesn't China allow foreign media to visit Chinese islands and reefs?","Nansha Islands are China's inherent territory. Chinese people across the Strait have the responsibility to uphold the heritage of the Chinese nation.\nI see you are very interested in whether China would organize foreign journalists to visit the Nansha Islands. Relevant islands and reefs are still under construction. When the condition is ripe, we will consider inviting foreign journalists to visit the islands and reefs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1350212.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1350108.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-03-24","Hua Chunying","","According to media reports, Taiwan authorities published a position paper on its South China Sea policy on March 21. Besides on March 23, some academic institutions in Taiwan submitted a proposal to the arbitration tribunal in the Hague, stressing that Taiping Dao meets the definition of island according to UNCLOS and is therefore eligible for possessing exclusive economic zone, continental shelf and other…","First of all I'd like to reiterate that China is consistent and clear on its non-acceptance and non-participation in the South China Sea arbitration case initiated by the Philippines.\nThe Nansha Islands including Taiping Dao have been China's territory since ancient times. Chinese people have long been living and working there continuously. China takes the Nansha Islands as a whole when claiming maritime rights and interests, and Chinese people across the Strait all have the responsibility to safeguard the property handed down from our ancestors. China is firmly against attempts of the Philippines to unilaterally deny China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in the South China Sea through arbitration.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1350552.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1350452.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, members of the press. Thank you all for attending the Taiwan Affairs Office's regular press conference. I will be moderating today's press conference. I now welcome your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Relevant parties in Taiwan are currently reviewing the “Draft Cross-Strait Agreement Supervision Act.” Some Taiwan public opinion holds that if this act passes, it will be a goodwill gesture to the Mainland. What is the Mainland's attitude?","We have repeatedly stated that the basis of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations must not be damaged, and that the authority of the consultations conducted by the two authorized associations and of the agreements reached should be upheld. We oppose any act that undermines the basis of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations, interferes with or obstructs the relevant processes, or artificially creates obstacles to the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160330_11423444.htm"],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","央视海峡两岸记者","May I ask the spokesperson: after the DPP won the 2016 Taiwan election, how is the communication liaison mechanism between the TAO and the MAC functioning?","In 2014, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” established a communication mechanism including meetings between the heads of the two agencies, which has played a positive role in promoting exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait. At present, this mechanism, which is built on the “1992 Consensus,” is still operating effectively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Ms. Hung Hsiu-chu was recently elected Chairperson of the Kuomintang, becoming the first female chairperson in the Kuomintang’s century-long history. I would like to ask the spokesperson: will the mainland side invite Hung Hsiu-chu to visit the mainland in the near future? In addition, Hung Hsiu-chu has said she will continue to hold the KMT-CPC Forum. Will the forum be held this year? What role can the…","On the night Ms. Hung Hsiu-chu was elected Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent her a congratulatory message, and Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu replied afterward. Both sides reviewed the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008 and reached positive consensus on continuing to uphold the great righteousness of the nation, adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" consolidating the foundation of mutual trust, strengthening exchanges and interaction, jointly maintaining the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations, and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nAs for the specific plans and arrangements for the operation of the platform between the two parties and exchanges and interactions at all levels in the future, both sides will further communicate and consult, actively promote them, and jointly maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160330_11423445.htm"],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently the Taiwan side opened Taiping Island to foreign media for coverage. What is the mainland's view?","Our basic position on the South China Sea issue is clear and consistent. China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands and their adjacent waters. The two sides of the Strait both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides have a shared obligation to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Taiwan media reported that recently, at the 20th anniversary celebration of the China Youth Exchange Association, Ma Ying-jeou gave remarks with Taiwan Affairs Office personnel present, and some media speculated this would become a new model of cross-Strait exchange. Is this the case, spokesperson?","The actual situation at the time was that, when attending the event, TAO personnel were not present at the same time as relevant personnel from Taiwan. We have made no changes to our policies or practices regarding cross-strait exchange activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","I would like to ask the spokesperson: what measures will the mainland take next to enable Taiwanese businesses and Taiwan-invested enterprises to better participate in the construction of the 13th Five-Year Plan, so that compatriots on both sides can share the development opportunities and dividends of the 13th Five-Year Plan? Second question: I would like to ask the spokesperson to introduce the features and…","Regarding the first question, the 13th Five-Year Plan Outline clearly sets out the guiding ideology, main goals, development concepts and major measures for the mainland’s economic and social development during the 13th Five-Year Plan period. Over the next five years, the mainland will follow the new development concepts of innovation, coordination, green development, openness and sharing, adapt to the new normal of economic development, adhere to development as the top priority, and, while moderately expanding aggregate demand, accelerate structural reform, especially supply-side structural reform, maintain medium-to-high growth, and move toward the medium-to-high end. Within the 13th Five-Year Plan lies a historic opportunity that Taiwan can take advantage of. Both sides should innovate their cooperation concepts and methods, and deepen cross-Strait economic cooperation in a mutually beneficial, win-win manner, enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nRegarding the second question, the Cross-Strait Trade Fair (“台交会”) has been held many times and has played a positive role in advancing cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation. As for the specific situation of this session, I suggest you inquire with the relevant authorities in Fujian or check the official website of the “台交会.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160330_11423443.htm"],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Reportedly, Taiwan's New Power Party recently proposed a “draft amendment to the Referendum Act,” saying it would lower the threshold for proposing referendums. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. The party’s position is clear to everyone. We firmly oppose any force using so-called law amendments to open the door wide for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. Regarding certain forces in Taiwan that repeatedly play this trick, undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and obstructing the development of cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides should remain highly vigilant.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160330_11423441.htm"],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen recently said in an exclusive interview with the China Times that she hopes the mainland side can show a bit more goodwill before “5·20.” What is the mainland's comment? Second question: Taiwan's “Minister of Justice” Luo Yingxue (罗莹雪) recently visited the mainland. We are more concerned about whether the two sides have reached further consensus on the repatriation of major economic…","Regarding the first question, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun has already stated our position and attitude when he recently accepted an interview with Taiwanese journalists. Director Zhang said that the mainland side’s goodwill has been stated very clearly: our adherence to the “1992 Consensus” is both our principle and our goodwill. Our attitude toward the “1992 Consensus,” and how to define the nature of cross-Strait relations, are the touchstone and standard for judging whether there is goodwill. Only by clarifying the nature of cross-Strait relations can the future of cross-Strait relations be seen clearly.\nRegarding the second question, Ms. Lo Ying-hsueh’s visit this time was an operational exchange conducted under the framework of the “Agreement on Joint Crackdown on Crime and Judicial Mutual Assistance Across the Taiwan Strait.” At the invitation of the liaison for the judicial mutual assistance agreement of the Supreme People’s Procuratorate, Ms. Lo, in the name of the Taiwan side’s chief adviser to the agreement, led a delegation of 10 people to visit Beijing and Shanghai from March 28 to April 1. During the visit, they will conduct operational and academic exchanges with mainland law enforcement and judicial authorities and research institutions, and visit the Shanghai Pilot Free Trade Zone, the Shanghai Juvenile Correctional Institution, and other sites. Relevant parties on both sides will exchange views on the issues of greatest concern to both sides in the current implementation of the agreement, such as jointly combating telecommunications fraud and drug crime, and the return of property defrauded from mainland residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","According to reports in Taiwan media, Taiwan tourism operators estimate that tourism revenue from mainland visitors to Taiwan this year will show negative growth for the first time. What expectations do you have for the future development of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan? Second question: the Fujian Free Trade Zone was inaugurated nearly a year ago. In the coming year, will the Taiwan Affairs Office support…","On the first question, regarding travel by mainland residents to Taiwan, we have already explained on many occasions and stated our position and attitude.\nOn the second question, we have always supported Fujian and Xiamen's free trade zones in using their geographic advantages to develop economic, trade and exchange and cooperation relations with Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The Panama Canal expansion will be completed in June, and the Panamanian government has invited leaders from both sides of the Strait to attend. What is the mainland's attitude?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on this. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","At the Boao Forum for Asia held recently, Vincent Siew, Honorary Chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation in Taiwan, said that alternation of political parties is the norm in Taiwan and should not be allowed to hinder cross-Strait relations. How do you view the prospects for cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation after “5·20”?","When Premier Li Keqiang met with Mr. Hsiao Wan-chang at Boao, he already made our position clear. The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The key to peaceful cross-Strait development lies in acknowledging the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and endorsing its core meaning that both sides belong to one China. Only by upholding and safeguarding this political foundation can cross-Strait relations advance steadily and go far. Our major policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We will continue to firmly uphold the “1992 Consensus” as the common political foundation, oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, continue to facilitate exchanges and contacts in all fields across the Strait, and benefit the people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","The Qingming ceremony to offer sacrifices to the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan in the Bingshen year is about to be held. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","The Bingshen-year Qingming public sacrificial ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi will be solemnly held on April 4, the Qingming Festival, at the Mausoleum of the Yellow Emperor in Huangling County, Shaanxi Province. This sacrificial event is co-hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, and the People's Government of Shaanxi Province. Under the theme of “Being mindful of the end and remembering the distant, inheriting civilization,” and using the public sacrificial ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi and a series of exchange activities as its vehicle, it aims to inherit and promote China's excellent traditional culture, inspire the national pride of Chinese descendants, and strengthen national cohesion. Taiwan public figures including Zhan Chunbai, former vice chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, and Yu Muming, chairman of the New Party, along with more than 200 grassroots residents from Taichung, New Taipei, Nantou, and other counties and cities, will jointly attend the public sacrificial ceremony.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","人民日报社记者","May I ask whether the cross-strait agreement on trade in goods can still be negotiated before “5·20”? If the DPP's attitude toward the “1992 Consensus” has not changed, will there still be an opportunity to negotiate the trade-in-goods agreement after “5·20”?","As we have previously introduced, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” the negotiating teams of the two associations have conducted twelve rounds of working-level communication on the Agreement on Trade in Goods and made positive progress. In this process, the mainland side has demonstrated our utmost goodwill. As for the next round of negotiations, it will depend on the development of cross-Strait relations and the state of communication between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","All forms of institutionalized cross-Strait consultation are conducted on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” If the new leader of Taiwan's authorities still does not recognize the “1992 Consensus” after “5·20,” institutionalized cross-Strait consultation will inevitably be affected?","The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by acknowledging the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and identifying with its core meaning can cross-Strait relations maintain peaceful and stable development. If this political foundation is damaged, all aspects of the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will be affected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","香港大公报、大公网记者","If the newly elected leader of Taiwan's authorities expresses on “May 20,” in her own way, recognition that both sides belong to one China, or that cross-Strait relations are not “state-to-state relations,” can the model of meetings between the leaders of both sides still continue?","The basis and content of last year's meeting between the leaders on both sides are well known. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the 1992 Consensus and recognizes the core meaning that both sides belong to one China, we are willing to engage with any party or group in Taiwan, regardless of which party or group it is and regardless of what it advocated in the past.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","On the Taiwan side today, Ma Ying-jeou and Tsai Ing-wen held a closed-door meeting. Ma Ying-jeou’s term is also nearing its end. May I ask the spokesperson how you evaluate the decisions Ma Ying-jeou made on cross-Strait relations during his time in office? What role do you expect him to play in cross-Strait exchanges after he leaves office, particularly in exchanges between the KMT and the CPC?","As for Taiwan’s internal affairs, I will not comment. As for cross-Strait relations, since 2008 the two sides of the Strait and their compatriots, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” have opened a new situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations and achieved a series of important results, which have brought substantial benefits to compatriots on both sides. This is clearly seen by the people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Earlier, there were reports in Taiwan that Tsai Ing-wen, the newly elected leader of the Taiwan region, may appoint former “Legislative Yuan President” Wang Jinping as chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation. Do you think that the green camp’s leader employing a figure from the blue camp to serve as the bridge across the Strait at present is done with goodwill?","I will not respond to hypothetical questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","中新社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, 41 mainland fishermen were recently detained by Taiwan law enforcement personnel while fishing near Dongsha. What comment does the TAO have?","After learning of the relevant situation, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits immediately activated the emergency contact mechanism between the two associations, sought information from and verified the situation with the Straits Exchange Foundation, and at the same time asked that relevant parties be coordinated to handle this incident properly, ensure the safety of the lives and property of the aforementioned fishermen, and return the people and boats as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201603/t20160330_11423447.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-03-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to DPP Chairperson Tsai Ing-wen's recent remarks in an interview that she hopes the mainland side will show more goodwill before “5.20,” An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on March 30 at the regular press conference when asked: Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently expressed our position when interviewed by Taiwan reporters. Director Zhang said that the mainland's goodwill has been stated very clearly; adherence to the “1992 Consensus” is both our principle and our goodwill. The attitude toward the “1992 Consensus,” and how to define the nature of cross-Strait relations, is the touchstone and standard for judging whether there is goodwill. Only when the nature of cross-Strait relations is made clear can the future of cross-Strait relations be seen clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201603/t20160330_11423446.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2016-03-31","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On 28th this month, the Defense Ministry of Japan deployed a coastal monitoring force on the Yonaguni Island. And right after that, on 29th, the New Security Law of Japan also took effect. Mr. spokesman, how would you comment on this series of actions by Japan?","You’ve raised a very good question. Actually, we indeed noticed that recently, the Japanese side had been very active in the military arena. We also noticed that Japan had loudly accused China of the so-called militarization on the islands and reefs in the South China Sea. And it was quite delighted to do so. But today, let’s see what Japan did on the Yonaguni Island, which is just 100 kilometers and more from Taiwan of China and also the Diaoyu Islands. I also noticed that, according to media report, there were only two policemen and ten rounds of ammunition on the Island in the past.\nBut now, Japan suddenly deployed additional 150 self-defense force personnel and it also said that for the next step it would deploy a rapid reaction infantry regiment. So while the Japanese side constantly accused other side, how would it account for its own actions? Japan also liked to take “freedom of navigation” as an excuse to accuse other side. The South China Sea is very broad. If China’s deployment of necessary defense facilities on its islands and reefs is blamed for “undermining freedom of navigation”, what should Japan’s action be called when it strengthened military deployment around the narrow Yonaguni-Iriomote Channel, which is an international water channel connecting the East China Sea and the West Pacific?\nAs for the New Security Law of Japan, we have noticed that, from the initial discussion to the development and implementation of the New Security Law, Japan has been facing a lot of questioning and opposition. In history, the Japanese militarists brought terrible disasters to the international community, particularly to the nations and people in Asia. In recent years, Japan substantially adjusted its military and security policies to break the limit of the Peace Constitution. Whether Japan will repeat the mistake in history, I think, is worthy of all parties’ vigilance.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2016-03/31/content_4648193.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-03-31","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Ma Yingjiu, the leader of Taiwan region, and later, its foreign department, invited foreign media to visit the Taiping Island in the South China Sea for media coverage. How would you comment, in the perspective of the PLA, on such an action? Since the Taiping Island is open to foreign media for visit and media coverage, when will the mainland open such islands as the Nansha Islands and the Xisha Islands to…","My colleague in the Taiwan Affairs Office answered your first question yesterday, so I will not reiterate here. Your second question, as I understand, is about how overseas reporters as well as those from Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao apply for permission to make media coverage on the Nansha Islands or the Xisha Islands. From the perspective of personnel management, the reporters from Taiwan should apply for that to the Taiwan Affairs Office, and foreign reporters should apply for that to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. But from the perspective of location management, the Nansha Islands or the Xisha Islands are within the jurisdiction of Sansha City of Hainan Province. So if you have such needs, I suggest that you apply to relevant departments of Sansha City of Hainan Province","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2016-03/31/content_4648193.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2016-04-07","Lu Kang","","Reports by the Taiwan media said that China will organize a reporting trip by foreign journalists to Yongxing Dao in May. Please confirm.","You may have noted the response given by staff of the press center of Sansha City, Hainan Province. They said they have noted the online report but have not been informed of any reporting trip by foreign journalists to Yongxing Dao. They also said that if foreign journalists want to visit Yongxing Dao, they can file applications to the information department of Hainan Provincial Party Committee.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1353880.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1353849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-07","Lu Kang","","Over the past few years, there have been frequent confrontations between fishing boats from China, the Philippines, Malaysia, Vietnam and the Taiwan region. Some of them have involved China's coast guard authorities and even the military. Chinese fishermen have found themselves in danger when fishing in disputed waters. What is the Chinese government planning to do to avoid tensions in the future, in particular…","I will take your second question first. There is no such thing as what you said.\nOn your first question, fishery disputes are not exclusive to this area. The Chinese government attaches great importance to fishery management and directs Chinese fishermen to conduct fishing operations in accordance with laws and regulations. Fishery cooperation is an important part of mutually beneficial cooperation between China and neighboring countries including coastal countries in the South China Sea. A very good approach of resolving disputes through friendly consultation has been developed over time. As for the disputes you mentioned, China and relevant countries are trying to solve them through friendly consultation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1353880.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1353849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-12","Lu Kang","","Regarding the Taiwanese who were repatriated from Kenya to Chinese mainland, the Taiwan authorities said that these people were forced back to China by the Kenyan police. Why were they sent back to the mainland?","Commitment to the one-China principle is the prerequisite and basis for China's relations with other countries. We commend the Kenyan government for consistently sticking to the one-China principle. As for cross-Straits matters, I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1355004.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1354944.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-13","Lu Kang","","Regarding the Taiwanese that have been deported from Kenya to China, China’s Ministry of Public Security also issued a statement. These Taiwanese have been acquitted by the Kenyan court of fraud, then why did China still want them back to the mainland?","Maybe you need to look further into this. Not only did China’s Ministry of Public Security make a statement this morning, senior officials from Kenya’s Interior Ministry also made statements on this case. It is not right to say that these people are not guilty at all. They are real suspects.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1355368.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1355241.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","人民日报记者","Yesterday, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun and Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council Chairperson Xia Liyan held a call through the cross-Strait hotline. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","On the afternoon of April 12, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, at the invitation of Xia Liyan, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council on the Taiwan side, held a communication via the cross-Strait hotline. The two sides discussed the recent arrest by our public security authorities of a group of criminal suspects, including Taiwan residents, on suspicion of telecommunications fraud, and exchanged views on issues related to cross-Strait relations.\nZhang Zhijun briefed Xia Liyan on the background and related circumstances of the case, saying that in recent years new forms of illegal and criminal activity on telecommunications networks have been rampant. Telecommunications fraud suspects from Taiwan have set up dens overseas to carry out fraud against mainland residents, and such activity has persisted despite repeated crackdowns and grown increasingly severe, causing enormous financial losses to mainland residents and extremely serious harm. These criminals must be brought to justice in order to effectively safeguard the rights and interests of the broad public, especially the victims. The mainland side has already given Taiwan's side a preliminary briefing on the relevant situation.\nZhang Zhijun stressed that cross-Strait relations are currently at an important juncture, and that compatriots on both sides and the international community are paying close attention to the future direction of cross-Strait relations. The mainland's major policies toward Taiwan have not changed. Over the past eight years, the reason cross-Strait relations have been able to maintain peaceful development and achieve positive results lies in the key fact that both sides have adhered to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This common political foundation is an important component of the current state of cross-Strait relations. Negating this political foundation would inevitably lead to a change in the status quo of cross-Strait relations. We hope the Taiwan side will cherish and safeguard the situation and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” and continue along the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433113.htm"],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Regarding the deportation of Taiwan telecom fraud suspects from Kenya to the mainland, Taiwan is paying close attention to this matter and believes the mainland's approach may undermine the “1992 Consensus.” What is your view? Will the mainland allow visits to these individuals?","I understand this matter has been the focus of attention in island media and public opinion over the past couple of days, and all parties are following it closely. So I would like to hear what other questions everyone has about it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","中国网记者","What role has the cross-Strait hotline played in handling urgent cross-Strait matters? Are there other communication mechanisms between the two sides to respond to the occurrence of similar situations?","This morning, the Ministry of Public Security issued a press release regarding the Taiwan criminal suspects in telecom fraud who were brought back to Taiwan from Kenya. I would like to provide further information on this case.\nFirst, according to information obtained from the relevant departments: On November 29, 2014, Kenyan police discovered a large number of electronic communication devices suspected of being used for telecom fraud crimes in a residence locally, and arrested 48 mainland criminal suspects and 28 Taiwan criminal suspects, successfully breaking up a telecom fraud crime ring. The ring set up a fraud den in Nairobi, the capital of Kenya, made online phone calls to 9 provinces and municipalities including Beijing, Jiangsu, Hunan and Sichuan, and impersonated public security, procuratorial and judicial authorities on the mainland to carry out extensive fraud, defrauding more than 100 people of over 6 million yuan. On April 8, 2016, Kenyan police again arrested 19 mainland criminal suspects and 22 Taiwan criminal suspects suspected of calling mainland China to carry out fraud. After review by Kenyan law enforcement authorities, it was decided to repatriate 77 of the above persons, mainland Chinese and Taiwan criminal suspects, to mainland China. The first batch of 10 criminal suspects was brought back on April 9, and the second batch of 67 criminal suspects was brought back on the morning of April 13. Among the two batches, a total of 45 Taiwan criminal suspects were involved.\nSecond, many people on the mainland have suffered greatly in this case. Many elderly people, teachers, students, migrant workers, laid-off workers and others were defrauded. Some retired elderly people who toiled all their lives had their lifetime savings swindled away, leaving them penniless and in dire straits; some had the “life-saving money” they had scraped together for a sick family member’s treatment stolen; some young students had their college tuition stolen. For example, a woman in Jilin jumped to her death after her husband’s death compensation was stolen, and a vegetable farmer surnamed Xiong committed suicide in front of an Agricultural Bank branch after his lifetime savings were stolen. Public authorities have also been defrauded: in December 2015, Taiwan criminal suspects impersonating public security, procuratorial and judicial authorities tricked an economic development zone in a certain city out of more than 100 million yuan in shantytown redevelopment funds and migrant workers’ wages, the largest single amount defrauded on the mainland to date. Preliminary statistics show that in recent years, more than 10 billion yuan of proceeds from telecom fraud each year has been moved from the mainland to Taiwan by swindlers, and only 200,000 yuan has been recovered to date. These fraudulent acts have caused many families to lose everything and many businesses to close or go bankrupt, inflicting enormous physical and psychological harm on the victims, and some have even been driven to desperate ends. The victims deeply loathe these fraudulent acts. I hope the Taiwan side will consider this matter from the perspective of the victims.\nThird, since the Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance was signed, public security organs on the mainland and the Taiwan police have worked closely together to continuously combat cross-border and cross-Strait telecom fraud crimes, achieving positive results. At the same time, some problems that cannot be ignored should also be noted: because the two sides handle criminal suspects separately, many Taiwan telecom fraud suspects with extensive records have not received due punishment, and the proceeds of their crimes have long been unable to be recovered. Many Taiwan criminal suspects were released immediately after being escorted back to Taiwan, and some set up fraud dens abroad again shortly afterward and resumed their crimes. These circumstances have allowed telecom fraud rings with Taiwan criminal suspects as their core to persist despite repeated crackdowns, causing huge economic losses to people on the mainland, leaving the lawful rights and interests of the victims without effective protection. People on the mainland are extremely dissatisfied with this and strongly demand that Taiwan fraud criminals be severely cracked down on and the hard-earned money stolen from victims be recovered.\nFourth, because these criminals committed their crimes overseas, all the victims are residents of the mainland, and the mainland naturally has jurisdiction. Moreover, the countries concerned are our diplomatic partners. In order to thoroughly establish the facts of all cases, and in accordance with the principle of facilitating investigation, our judicial authorities will strictly carry out investigative work against the Taiwan criminal suspects in accordance with the law, and the lawful rights and interests of the relevant criminal suspects will be safeguarded in accordance with the law.\nFifth, the relevant parties on both sides have carried out several rounds of communication on this case. On the afternoon of April 12, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to a request and held a cross-Strait hotline call with Xia Liyan, Chairperson of the Taiwan side’s Mainland Affairs Council. Director Zhang Zhijun introduced the background of the incident, the relevant circumstances and our stance to Xia Liyan. In addition, the relevant mainland authorities have already provided preliminary notification to the Taiwan side of the relevant information through the channels of the cross-Strait joint crime-fighting and judicial mutual assistance agreement framework. The second batch of criminal suspects was brought back on the morning of April 13, and the relevant mainland authorities also promptly notified the Taiwan side. Future developments in this case will also be promptly communicated to the Taiwan side. At the same time, Taiwan police and judicial departments will be invited to come to the mainland to discuss joint crackdown on cross-border and cross-Strait telecom fraud crimes, in order to further strengthen cooperation and effectively protect the interests and well-being of people on both sides.\nThe above is the basic situation of this case. I believe that, having heard this introduction, everyone should be very clear about which side in this case is the victim and which side is the perpetrator. We will handle this case strictly in accordance with the relevant provisions of national laws and regulations, and effectively safeguard the property security and lawful rights and interests of the people. This is a responsible attitude toward the people and is conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to the peace and contentment of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433111.htm"],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, whether to cancel or change the form and content of the KMT-CPC Forum has sparked discussion within the KMT and in Taiwan society. What is the mainland's attitude on this?","Over the past decade, the operation of the platforms of the KMT and the CPC and exchanges and interactions at all levels have played an active and important role in advancing party-to-party relations and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. In the future, both sides will further communicate and consult, actively promote, and continuously improve, continuing to maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nReporter from China Radio International: Recently, public opinion has claimed that the mainland side repeatedly stresses the “1992 Consensus,” and since the DPP cannot avoid it, it should seek to interpret the “1992 Consensus” in its own way, which might open up the stalemate in cross-Strait relations after May 20. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?\nWe have already stated very clearly that the core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that cross-Strait relations are not “relations between states,” thereby clearly defining the nature of cross-Strait relations. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizes the core meaning that both sides belong to one China, the two sides have a common political foundation and can maintain positive interaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, AIIB President Jin Liqun pointed out that for Taiwan to join the AIIB it must apply through the mainland. Taiwan has rejected this, and Taiwan joining the AIIB amounts to a dead end. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's response?","We have repeatedly stated our position on the question of Taiwan joining the AIIB. We believe the AIIB will handle the question of Taiwan’s accession in accordance with the one-China principle and the relevant AIIB rules.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","Previously, the American Foreign Policy Council released a report calling on the mainland not to use force to resolve the Taiwan question, and stating that it would stand on Taiwan's side. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? On the other hand, senior US officials have been actively shuttling between the two sides of the Strait. Some public opinion holds that this is carrying messages, while others…","I will not comment on the think tank's report. What I want to stress is that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Only by upholding and safeguarding this foundation can cross-strait relations move steadily and go far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou landed on Pengjia Islet on April 9 to erect a monument for peace in the East China Sea. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this? The Straits Forum, which is dedicated to cross-Strait civil exchanges, has been held seven times, and this year is the eighth. Does the spokesperson have any information to disclose?","On your first question, regarding the Diaoyu Islands issue, we have stated our position and attitude many times. The Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands are inherent territory of China. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a responsibility to jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to protect the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nOn your second question, the 8th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian from June 11, lasting one week. Current preparatory work is progressing smoothly. Themed “Expanding Civil Exchange and Promoting Integrated Development,” with an emphasis on youth and grassroots exchange, this forum has arranged four major sections: the Forum Plenary, Youth Exchange, Grassroots Exchange, and Economic and Trade Exchange, with 19 events. This forum is co-hosted by 77 units from both sides of the Strait. In youth exchange, this forum focuses on employment and entrepreneurship issues for young people, designing the Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship and Innovation Competition, a new-media cultural and creative forum, the “Benefiting Youth Run,” and other activities, and widely invites young people from Taiwan to participate. In grassroots exchange, centered on livelihood issues of common concern to both sides of the Strait, arrangements include a workers' forum, a women's forum, and distinctive temple fairs and other activities. We warmly welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan, especially young friends and grassroots residents, to attend this year's forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433104.htm"],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","The five-year contract farming of milkfish between the mainland and Xuejia in Tainan has expired and will not be renewed this year. May I ask the spokesperson: is there political influence? Will the mainland's attitude toward cross-strait economic and trade cooperation change?","I believe everyone is aware that the head of the Taiwan Milkfish Aquaculture Association recently said that, affected by the cold currents, fry prices on the island have soared this year, so the previous contract farming prices cannot be sustained, and therefore Taiwan's contract farmers announced they would suspend milkfish contract farming this year. He also expressed gratitude for the efforts made by relevant parties on the mainland to improve the livelihoods of Xuejia fishermen. We will continue to promote agricultural and fishery cooperation across the Strait on the basis of mutual benefit and reciprocity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Lin Zhongsen, Chairman of the Taiwan Straits Exchange Foundation, originally planned to visit the mainland last week, but was suddenly halted by Taiwan’s legislature. Public opinion holds that institutionalized consultation across the Strait is an important sign of the normalization of cross-Strait relations, and the cancellation of Lin Zhongsen’s visit to the mainland means that institutionalized consultation…","Since 2008, ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan have, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” restored the institutionalized consultation and reciprocal visit mechanism between the two organizations, which has played an important role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This time, the heads of the two organizations had planned to meet in Xiamen to exchange views on issues of concern to both sides. However, due to reasons on the Taiwan side, the SEF cancelled this visit. We do not wish to see the normal exchanges between the two organizations disrupted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433108.htm"],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Taiwan's legislature recently deleted, in preliminary review, the provision on “not allowed to unilaterally stamp images on the cover of passports,” which means a green light for so-called “Taiwan national passport stickers.” May I ask the spokesperson for views on this?","We have made it clear for a long time that we firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","香港大公报大公网记者","The DPP recently passed its party version of the “Draft Regulations on Supervision of Cross-Strait Agreements.” Some analysts hold that, in the name of improving the supervision mechanism, the “regulations” in fact obstruct and undermine cross-Strait relations and are by no means well-intentioned. May I ask the spokesperson: if these regulations are passed by Taiwan’s legislature, does that mean consultations…","We have repeatedly made clear that the basis for cross-Strait consultations and negotiations must not be damaged, and the authority of the authorized consultations and agreement signing by the two associations should be upheld. We firmly oppose any act that undermines the basis of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations, interferes with the consultation and negotiation process, or artificially creates obstacles to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","There is news that this year’s Straits Forum intends to invite Hung Hsiu-chu, the new Kuomintang chairwoman, to attend. Can the spokesperson confirm this news?","I have just introduced the basic situation of this year’s Straits Forum. As for the question you raised, specific arrangements in this regard are still being planned and discussed, and will be announced in a timely manner once determined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","Recently, on Facebook, a popular community website in Taiwan, some so-called “independence” social media campaigns were launched in the names of Taiwan's counties and cities. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? In addition, recently, Democratic Progressive Party figures have called for a “pardon” of former Taiwan leader Chen Shui-bian. What is your comment on this?","First question: firmly opposing any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity is our firm position. As for some actions by netizens on the island, they also demonstrate from the opposite side the illusory and unrealistic nature of “Taiwan independence.”\nSecond question: we do not comment on Taiwan’s internal affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Can family members visit these 45 Taiwanese people who were sent to the mainland? Does the mainland accept consultation with the Taiwan side?","Earlier, when I introduced the situation, I already stated that the mainland welcomes the Taiwan side to send people, and that the two sides are communicating and consulting within the framework of the cross-Strait agreement on jointly combating crime. The specific matters are currently being discussed by both sides. As for the issue of family visits, we will handle it in accordance with the relevant procedures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Recently, Ma Ying-jeou met with Tsai Ing-wen, and it is reported that cross-Strait relations were not touched upon during the meeting. A similar situation occurred at the DPP's extraordinary national congress. Some Taiwan scholars believe that the DPP avoids the cross-Strait issue, stalls and waits for changes, and cannot promote positive interaction in cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our position and attitude on cross-Strait relations are clear and consistent. The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of the development of cross-Strait relations. Only by upholding and safeguarding this common political foundation can cross-Strait relations advance steadily and go far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160413_11433125.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, whether to cancel the previous form of the KMT-CPC Forum or change its form and content has prompted discussion within the Kuomintang and in Taiwan’s society. What attitude does the mainland hold on this?","TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said at the regular press conference on April 13 in response to questions: Over the past decade, the operation of the KMT-CPC platform and exchanges and interactions at all levels have played a positive and important role in promoting relations between the two parties and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. In the future, both sides will further communicate, consult, actively promote, and continuously improve, and continue to safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433109.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Some public opinion recently stated that the mainland has repeatedly emphasized the “1992 Consensus”; since the DPP cannot avoid it, it should strive to interpret the “1992 Consensus” in its own way, which might open up 5?","The deadlock in cross-strait relations after 20: how does the spokesperson evaluate it? Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions at the regular press conference on April 13, saying: we have made it very clear that the core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that cross-strait relations are not “state-to-state relations,” thereby clearly defining the nature of cross-strait relations. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the 1992 Consensus and endorses the core meaning that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, the two sides will have a common political foundation and can maintain positive interaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160413_11433110.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-04-15","Lu Kang","","Taiwan said that Malaysia is going to deport 52 Taiwan criminal suspects to the mainland. Please confirm. Does the case have anything to do with Kenya's sending of Taiwan wire fraud suspects to the mainland?","You may have noticed that the Ministry of Public Security has issued rather detailed information about the Kenyan government's deportation of criminal suspects to the mainland. Issues relating to the cross-Straits relations are not diplomatic issues. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council also communicated with Taiwan through cross-Straits channels. I would point you to competent authorities of China for specifics concerning the case you asked, and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for issues relating to the cross-Straits relations.\nI would like to reiterate that the one-China principle is the prerequisite and basis for China's relations with other countries. We fully commend those governments that stay committed to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1355862.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1355831.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-04-16","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 16 (reporter Zhao Bo) — Regarding the Taiwan side's release of telecom fraud suspects deported from Malaysia, An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 16th when asked: The Taiwan side's action will only encourage increasingly rampant cross-border telecom fraud crimes. It is a disregard for and renewed harm to the rights and interests of numerous victims, and it damages the cooperation between the two sides in jointly combating crime.\nHe said he hopes the Taiwan side will immediately correct its mistake, eliminate the bad impact, and ensure that the criminal suspects are seriously pursued and receive due punishment. He hopes the Taiwan side will prove, through concrete actions, its respect for and protection of the legitimate rights and interests of victims, so as to avoid causing greater harm to the joint anti-crime cooperation between the two sides and to the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160416_11435329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-04-18","Lu Kang","","Last week, the Malaysian government deported a group of wire fraud suspects to Taiwan. Taiwan officials later set them free. Is the mainland upset about this? Did you protest with the Malaysian side?","Regarding the cross-Straits relations that this issue touches upon, you may have noticed that the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council issued a statement during the weekend.\nI also want to stress that one-China principle is an important political prerequisite for bilateral relations between China and other countries around the world. Relations between China and Malaysia are developing in an all-round way. We believe that effective cooperation between the two sides in law enforcement and security on cracking down on cross-border crimes will serve the fundamental interests of the two sides.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1356427.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1356370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-18","Lu Kang","","It is reported that Taiwan invited experts on international law and physical geography to visit Taiping Dao of China's Nansha Islands. Leader of the Taiwan region Ma Ying-jeou reiterated that islands in the South China Sea belong to China, and the nine-dash-line shall be interpreted in accordance with the international law in existence when the lines were drawn instead of the United Nations Convention on the Law…","Like what I have said, China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands including Taiping Dao and their adjacent waters. China's sovereignty and relevant rights over the South China Sea were formed over the long course of history and are fully backed by historical and jurisprudential evidence.\nThe final settlement of territorial issues, regardless of what mechanisms and procedures are undergone, including a resort to a third party, has to be based on state will and be agreed upon by parties directly concerned through negotiation.\nThe Chinese people from both sides of the Straits share similar views on the relevant issue and jointly bear the honorable mission of protecting the heritage of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1356427.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1356370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-19","Hua Chunying","","The Japanese government publicized 750 documents on its website proving that Diaoyu Dao and \"Takeshima\" are Japan's \"inherent territory\", the second time Japan has done so since last year. What is China's comment?","Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. China's sovereignty over Diaoyu Dao is fully backed by historical and jurisprudential evidence. Before the First Sino-Japanese War, the name Diaoyu Dao was widely used in maps made by western countries with clear marks showing that Diaoyu Dao belonged to China. After the War, Japan exercised colonial rule over Taiwan and its affiliated islands including Diaoyu Dao for a long time. Following the end of the Second World War, Diaoyu Dao was returned to China pursuant to relevant legal documents. Japan pieced up a distorted history by picking some information here and garbling some documents there. This will by no means change the fact that Diaoyu Dao is part of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1356858.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201604/t20160419_5413464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-04-26","Hua Chunying","","Do you have more details about the Taiwan fishing boat detained by the Japanese government on April 25?","We have seen the report and are trying to learn more about that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1358635.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1358589.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","新华社记者","In two days, on April 29, is both the 11th anniversary of the release of the “Common Vision for Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations” jointly issued by the leaders of the Communist Party and the KMT, and the 23rd anniversary of the signing of relevant agreements by both sides of the Wang-Koo talks. What lessons does this hold for the future development of cross-Strait relations under the current…","Twenty-three years ago, the Wang-Koo talks held on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” opened an institutionalized mechanism for cross-Strait consultation and marked a historic and important step in cross-Strait relations. Practice has proven that to maintain the direction and good momentum of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the key is to consolidate the common political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” With this foundation, cross-Strait relations can continue to move forward, and the rights and well-being of compatriots on both sides can be safeguarded and enhanced. If this foundation is undermined, cross-Strait relations will return to the old path of turmoil and instability, and the fruits of peaceful development will be lost.\nEleven years ago, at an important moment when cross-Strait relations faced a choice of path, the leaders of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China held a historic meeting on April 29, 2005, and jointly issued the “Common Vision for Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations,” pointing out a bright path for cross-Strait relations. Since 2008, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the KMT, the CPC, both sides of the Strait, and compatriots on both sides have worked together to implement the “Common Vision,” and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has yielded fruitful results. This situation was hard-won and must be cherished all the more. At present, cross-Strait relations have once again reached an important juncture in choosing direction and path. We hope to continue to uphold the common political foundation, maintain the correct direction and good momentum of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and safeguard the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445341.htm"],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","中央人民广播电台记者","Could the spokesperson say whether, without the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” mechanisms such as the communication mechanism between the TAO and Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, and the consultation mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, would be interrupted?","On May 26, 2008, the Straits Exchange Foundation sent a letter to the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, expressing its willingness to resume talks between the two associations as soon as possible on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” On May 29, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits replied to the Straits Exchange Foundation, expressing its willingness to resume talks on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” On June 12, the two associations resumed talks that had been suspended for nearly ten years, and the next day they signed cross-Strait agreements. Over the past eight years, the two associations held 11 rounds of talks and signed 23 agreements, which played an important role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nIn 2014, the Taiwan Affairs Office (TAO) and the Mainland Affairs Council (MAC) established a regular liaison and communication mechanism on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” They properly handled some major sensitive issues in cross-Strait relations and played a positive role in maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait.\nIt can thus be seen that the reason the TAO and the MAC were able to establish a liaison and communication mechanism, and the reason the two associations were able to resume talks and sign agreements, is that both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus” as their common political foundation. It can be said that the “1992 Consensus” is both the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and an important component of the status quo in cross-Strait relations. If this political foundation were negated, the status quo in cross-Strait relations would inevitably change. Only by continuing to uphold this important foundation, the “1992 Consensus,” can the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and its good momentum be maintained.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445340.htm"],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","The DPP is currently advancing the review of the draft “Transitional Justice Promotion Regulations.” I would like to ask the spokesperson for a comment.","This matter has attracted great attention and vigilance from all sides. We note that Taiwan public opinion believes the purpose of this is to further advance “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence-ization.” On this issue, our position is consistent and clear: we firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Tsai Ing-wen received a briefing at the MAC this morning. I would like to ask whether the mainland has any message it hopes to convey to her at this time?","The TAO and the MAC, on the basis of the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” have established a regularized liaison and communication mechanism, with the heads of the two departments meeting and making reciprocal visits. The “1992 Consensus” is an important foundation for the establishment of the liaison and communication mechanism between the two departments, and a necessary condition for this mechanism to operate normally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","On the afternoon of April 25, a mainland tour bus overturned in Taiwan, drawing concern from people on both sides of the Strait. I would like to ask the spokesperson to explain the relevant details of this accident to us.","On April 25, a tour bus carrying 26 mainland tourists collided with another vehicle inside Miaoli County, Taiwan, resulting in the unfortunate death of the Taiwanese driver, serious injuries to the Taiwanese tour guide, and varying degrees of injury to the 26 mainland tourists. We express our condolences for the deceased Taiwanese driver, extend our sympathy to the injured mainland tourists and the Taiwanese tour guide, and wish them an early recovery. Upon learning of the accident, the National Tourism Administration has maintained contact with the Taiwan side through the cross-Strait “small two associations” tourism channel and is handling the related follow-up work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","The “Chinese Language Dictionary,” jointly compiled by both sides of the Strait, was recently officially published. I would like the spokesperson to introduce the detailed situation. How do you evaluate it? What are your expectations for future exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in related fields?","The cross-Strait joint compilation of Chinese language reference works was launched in early 2010, led respectively by the mainland editorial committee and the Taiwan side's Chinese Culture Promotion Association. The \"Great Chinese Language Dictionary\" is one of the important achievements; the Taiwan edition was formally published recently, and the electronic version of the mainland edition will be released in July of this year, with the paper edition to be published and distributed in 2018. In addition, the two sides have jointly built and launched the \"Chinese Language Knowledge Base\" website, published a series of achievements such as the \"Common Words Dictionary for Both Sides of the Strait,\" and held multiple sessions of cross-Strait university student Chinese calligraphy art exchange summer camps and other activities.\nJoint compilation of Chinese language reference works by both sides of the Strait is a good beginning for jointly inheriting and carrying forward the Chinese language and script. A basic exchange and cooperation mechanism has now taken shape. We hope both sides will continue to advance this work and achieve more results. We will continue to provide active assistance to promote and deepen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in language and script, facilitate communication between compatriots on both sides, and create favorable conditions for inheriting and carrying forward Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445335.htm"],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Today, Taiwan's legislature is reviewing the draft amendment to the Referendum Act. Some public opinion holds that this move may provide a legal basis for “Taiwan independence” forces to promote a referendum on “constitution-making.” What is your view?","There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are indivisible. We firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, and oppose “Taiwan independence” forces attempting to separate Taiwan from China under any name or by any means, including through so-called “referendums,” “constitution-making,” “constitutional amendments,” and similar methods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445339.htm"],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Are there any more Taiwan telecom fraud suspects to be extradited from other countries to the mainland in the near future?","I am not very familiar with this information. Relevant parties on both sides have carried out cooperation through the channels of the Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance. You may inquire with the relevant liaison unit under the agreement.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","On the issue of telecom fraud cases, we have seen on television the tragic experiences of many mainland victims, and we feel deeply for them. Recently, including mainland friends online and those we have encountered around us, there is great hatred toward the conduct of Taiwan fraudsters, and their impression of Taiwan has changed somewhat. May I ask, will the change in mainland compatriots' impression of Taiwan…","I think the attitude toward this matter should be to deal with the specific issue on its merits and to put ourselves in others' shoes. This is a cross-border, cross-Strait telecom fraud criminal case. As everyone knows, telecom fraud has caused serious property losses and physical and psychological harm to people on both sides of the Strait. It can be said that compatriots on both sides have a strong desire to see these criminals brought to justice. Strengthening cooperation across the Strait within the framework of the Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance, so as to jointly combat crime, accords with the common wishes of compatriots on both sides. As for our attitude of supporting and encouraging cross-Strait civil exchanges, it is clear and consistent, and it will not change.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","The Taiwan Industrial Association recently put forward three proposals for deepening cross-Strait economic cooperation, hoping that after the DPP takes office it will build a dialogue and interaction model acceptable to both sides and continue to promote cross-Strait economic cooperation. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Since 2008, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” both sides across the Strait have promoted the institutionalization of cross-strait economic cooperation and made positive progress. Only by adhering to the “1992 Consensus” as the common political foundation can we truly respond to the expectations of the business community and create a favorable environment and conditions for cross-strait economic cooperation. If this foundation is undermined, the atmosphere of exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait will inevitably be affected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","After the Kenya case, the Taiwan Legislative Yuan issued a statement, initiated by the DPP and the New Power Party caucus, and lodged a protest. I would like to ask the spokesperson what comment you have on this statement.","As I just said, telecom fraud is a criminal act that people on both sides of the Strait deeply loathe. It has caused serious property losses and physical and psychological harm to compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides strongly demand that the criminals be brought to justice. We will handle this case strictly in accordance with the relevant provisions of national laws and regulations, and earnestly safeguard the property security and legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.\nAs for the so-called “statement” you mentioned, it completely ignores the facts, fails to distinguish right from wrong, disregards the rights of the victims, and even contains obvious “one country on each side” content. It is intended to undermine the cross-Strait status quo and create cross-Strait confrontation. This both runs counter to the wishes of compatriots on both sides and undermines the foundation of cross-Strait cooperation in combating crime and of the development of cross-Strait relations. It will naturally be opposed by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","The U.S. House Foreign Affairs Committee recently reaffirmed that the U.S. “Taiwan Relations Act” and the “Six Assurances” to Taiwan are the cornerstones of U.S.-Taiwan relations. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no interference from foreign forces. The US side should honor its commitments to adhere to the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, oppose “Taiwan independence,” handle Taiwan-related issues properly, and do more that is conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445337.htm"],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, relevant personnel from Taiwan's justice authorities came to the mainland to negotiate joint crackdown on telecom fraud across the Taiwan Strait. What progress has been made? In addition, the head of the education and culture authorities appointed by the Taiwan side, who has a strong ideological orientation, has not yet taken office but already demands “abolishing the fine-tuned curriculum guidelines.”…","First question: On April 21, under the framework of the “Agreement Between the Two Sides of the Strait on Jointly Combating Crime and Mutual Judicial Assistance,” the cross-Strait agreement working group held consultations on cooperation to combat cross-border telecommunications fraud. Both sides exchanged information on telecommunications fraud cases in Kenya and Malaysia and communicated on assisting in case investigations, deepening the cooperative approaches to combating cross-border telecommunications fraud, and other matters of mutual concern.\nA responsible person of the Ministry of Public Security said that strengthening law enforcement cooperation and jointly combating crime accords with the wishes of the people on both sides of the Strait. Both sides should work together, on the principles of being conducive to combating crime, effectively protecting the interests of victims, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, to resolutely crack down on telecommunications fraud. No matter where telecommunications fraud criminals flee, they must be fully pursued, brought to justice and severely punished according to law.\nBoth sides agreed that, on the basis of preserving the existing achievements of the cross-Strait joint crime-fighting agreement, they should further explore specific ways to deepen cooperation in response to new developments in cross-border telecommunications fraud crimes. Both sides agreed to assist each other in verifying the identities and related information of suspects, arresting fugitives and recovering stolen funds involved in cases, and to maintain communication on subsequent assistance in case investigations and related matters.\nRelevant parties also arranged for the Taiwan consultation delegation to visit the Haidian District Detention Center in Beijing on-site, to learn about the investigation and trial of cross-Strait criminal suspects and the detention environment. They expressed that they would treat cross-Strait criminal suspects equally, fully guarantee the various rights they enjoy under the law, and assist in arranging family visits and other matters in accordance with the law.\nMany people on both sides of the Strait have felt the pain of telecommunications fraud firsthand. This type of fraud not only steals money but can even cost lives. Some ordinary mainland people, after being defrauded, have lost everything, and some have even taken their own lives. Many ordinary Taiwan people have also suffered from it. I believe that telecommunications fraud is something everyone on both sides of the Strait opposes. Putting ourselves in others' shoes, both sides should strengthen hand-in-hand cooperation, resolutely crack down on cross-border telecommunications fraud so that the rights and interests of victims can be protected, and never allow these criminals to escape justice.\nYour second question: We will not comment on specific personnel arrangements on the island. As far as cross-Strait relations are concerned, since 2008, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait exchanges in the fields of culture and education have developed vigorously, with remarkable results. We hope this good situation can be maintained, so as to enhance mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, foster common feelings, and jointly promote Chinese culture. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should remain highly vigilant against the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities of some people who attempt to push “de-Sinicization” in the fields of culture and education and to sever the blood ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","On the first question: the Taiwan Pingtung-registered fishing vessel Dong Sheng Ji No. 16, which belongs to the Liuqiu Township, was recently intercepted and seized by a Japanese government vessel while operating in the high seas near Okinotorishima Reef. May I ask the spokesperson, what is the mainland's comment on the seizure of the Taiwan fishing vessel? The second question: Zhang Zhijun, Director of the…","Regarding your first question, we are highly concerned about it. Protecting the lawful rights and interests of fishermen on both sides of the Strait in relevant waters is a shared responsibility of both sides.\nRegarding your second question, I think the mainland’s economic development and transformation and upgrading provide very significant and good market opportunities for a broad range of enterprises, including Taiwan businesses. We will, in combination with the full implementation of the outline of the 13th Five-Year Plan, actively help Taiwan-funded enterprises with transformation and upgrading and, at the same time, help Taiwan enterprises participate in the mainland’s Belt and Road construction in appropriate ways.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","In recent days, some mainland media and think tanks conducted a poll on cross-Strait relations that specifically posed hypothetical questions about “armed unification.” What is the spokesperson's comment? The second poll concerns Taiwan: a Taiwan think tank published a poll yesterday showing that 52% of people oppose the “1992 Consensus.” How does the spokesperson view this?","Regarding your first question, I will not comment on specific public opinion polls. Our major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will uphold the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, promote the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, narrow the psychological distance across the Strait, and enhance compatriots' understanding of the community of shared destiny across the Strait. At the same time, we also firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will never allow a repeat of the historical tragedy of national division.\nRegarding your second question, likewise, I will not comment on specific opinion polls. But the position and background of the so-called polling organization you mentioned are very clear to everyone. What I want to emphasize is that there is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are indivisible. The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It is on this basis that cross-Strait relations have opened a new situation of peaceful development. If this foundation is undermined, all achievements in the various areas of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will be affected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","台声杂志记者","April 26 marks the 7th anniversary of the signing of the Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance. Please introduce the achievements of cross-Strait cooperation over these seven years.","April 26 marks the 7th anniversary of the signing of the Agreement on Joint Crackdown on Crime and Judicial Mutual Assistance across the Taiwan Strait. Over these 7 years, under the broader environment of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, law enforcement departments on both sides have closely cooperated within the framework of the agreement, cracked many widely watched cases involving cross-Strait telecom fraud, drugs, and pyramid schemes, mutually repatriated a number of wanted fugitives, and carried out a series of judicial mutual assistance cooperation in investigation and evidence collection. They have contributed to protecting the well-being of people on both sides, maintaining order in cross-Strait exchanges, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. I believe these achievements are plain to see for compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","香港大公报大公网记者","A mainland scholar recently suggested that if the DPP takes power, cross-Strait relations may fall into a so-called “cold peace” and cold dialogue. How does the spokesperson understand this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor that steadies the seas for cross-Strait relations. If this political foundation can be upheld, cross-Strait relations can advance steadily and far. If this foundation is damaged, political mutual trust across the Taiwan Strait will cease to exist, and cross-Strait relations will inevitably be impacted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","团结报记者","Chairman Yu Zhengsheng recently attended the congress of the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and said that Taiwan businesspeople have made many contributions to the mainland's economic development. Under the new circumstances, will the mainland's policies toward Taiwan businesspeople change?","The mainland's policy of supporting and encouraging Taiwan businesses to develop on the mainland is clear and consistent, and it will not change.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Recently, a Taiwan delegation was asked to leave an international steel conference it was attending in Belgium. This incident has caused heated discussion on the island, and some figures in the Green camp have taken the opportunity to stir up trouble in cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","It is my understanding that the meeting you mentioned, held on the afternoon of April 18, was a roundtable of an intergovernmental nature. We respect relevant international organizations and institutions, and handle Taiwan-related issues in accordance with their charters and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","Recently, Hu Sheng-cheng, an academician of “Academia Sinica” who is regarded as one of Tsai Ing-wen's mentors, stated that Tsai Ing-wen's inaugural address will likely not mention the “1992 Consensus,” and that she may continue to promote cross-Strait relations through some formulation implicitly based on the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus,” with content that all relevant parties can accept. What is the…","The “1992 Consensus” is both the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and an important component of the cross-Strait status quo. Acknowledging the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing the core meaning that both sides of the Strait belong to one China gives the two sides a common political foundation, so that they can maintain positive interaction. If this political foundation is denied, it would mean changing the status quo of cross-Strait relations. On the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations, persistently taking a vague, evasive approach or playing word games is entirely meaningless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201604/t20160427_11445344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to calls by Taiwan's incoming heads of the education and culture departments and others to “abolish the fine-tuned curriculum guidelines,” Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan told a regular press conference on April 27 that since 2008, on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait exchanges in the cultural and educational fields have flourished, with very significant results. We hope this positive situation can be maintained, so as to enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, warm our shared feelings, and jointly promote Chinese culture. The compilation of textbooks should respect history and respect facts. Compatriots on both sides should remain highly vigilant against certain “Taiwan independence” separatist activities that attempt to promote “de-Sinicization” in the cultural and educational fields and to sever the blood ties between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445336.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-04-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","At the regular press conference on April 27, An Fengshan, spokesperson of the TAO of the State Council, responding to questions, introduced progress in joint cross-strait efforts to combat cross-border telecom fraud crimes.\nAn Fengshan said that on April 21, under the framework of the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance,” the cross-strait agreement working groups consulted on cooperation in combating cross-border telecom fraud crimes. They mutually notified each other of telecom fraud cases in Kenya and Malaysia, and communicated on assisting in case investigations, on ways to deepen cooperation in combating cross-border telecom fraud, and on other matters of mutual concern. Both sides believe that, on the basis of preserving the existing achievements of the joint crime-fighting agreement, they should further explore specific ways to deepen cooperation in response to new developments in cross-border telecom fraud crimes. Both sides agreed to assist each other in verifying the identities of suspects and related information, arresting fugitives, and recovering stolen funds, and to remain in communication on follow-up assistance in case handling. The relevant parties stated that they will treat cross-strait criminal suspects equally, fully guarantee the rights they enjoy under the law, and assist in arranging family visits and similar matters in accordance with the law.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that many people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have personal pain from telecom fraud, and such fraud not only takes money but can also take lives. Some ordinary people on the mainland have lost everything after being deceived, and some have even taken their own lives. Many ordinary people in Taiwan have also suffered from it. Telecom fraud crimes should be, on both sides of the Strait, “a rat crossing the street that everyone shouts to beat.” Putting ourselves in each other's shoes, the two sides should strengthen hand-in-hand cooperation, resolutely crack down on cross-border telecom fraud, so that the rights and interests of victims can be protected, and absolutely not allow these criminals to escape justice.\nIn addition, regarding the so-called “statement” recently issued by Taiwan's legislature on the Kenyan telecom fraud cases, An Fengshan said in response that this so-called “statement” completely ignores the facts, does not distinguish right from wrong, disregards the rights and interests of victims, and even contains obvious “one side, one country” content. It intends to undermine the cross-strait status quo and create cross-strait confrontation. This not only runs against the wishes of compatriots on both sides, but also damages the basis for cross-strait joint crime-fighting cooperation and for the development of cross-strait relations, and it will naturally be opposed by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160427_11445338.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-04-29","Hua Chunying","","Japanese Foreign Minister Fumio Kishida said yesterday that the Japanese side has lodged a protest with Taipei for not recognizing waters off Okinotori as Japan's Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ). He said that Okinotori's status as an island has been established under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS). Japan cannot accept Taiwan's position. What is China's comment?","Okinotori is an isolated rock in the West Pacific far away from the homeland of Japan. As prescribed in the UNCLOS, rocks like Okinotori which cannot sustain human habitation or economic life of their own shall have no exclusive economic zone nor continental shelf. In April, 2012, the Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf gave its recommendations in regard to the submission made by Japan on the limits of its outer continental shelf,not recognizing Japan's claim of an outer continental shelf based on Okinotori. Japan has violated the UNCLOS by categorizing Okinotori as \"island\" for the purpose of claiming for EEZ and continental shelf based on that. China does not recognize the illegal assertion by Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1360007.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1359806.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-04-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 30 (reporter Zhao Bo): Regarding the mainland public security organs’ repatriation on the 30th from Malaysia of a group of cross-strait offenders suspected of telecom fraud, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, in an interview with reporters, said: At present, cross-strait offenders engaged in cross-border telecom fraud crimes overseas are extremely rampant. They have seriously infringed on the personal and property safety of mainland residents. The broad public is deeply resentful of this and strongly demands intensified crackdowns, stern punishment of telecom fraud crimes, and no tolerance for criminals escaping justice.\nIt is understood that mainland police promptly informed the Taiwan side of the relevant circumstances of the suspects repatriated from Malaysia to Taiwan, and invited the Taiwan side to send personnel to the mainland as soon as possible to jointly handle the cases. This shows that the cross-strait mutual judicial assistance and crime-fighting liaison mechanism is operating in an orderly manner, and that the preliminary consensus reached at the April 21 meeting of the cross-strait agreement working group is being put into practice, demonstrating the mainland side’s pragmatic attitude of cooperation within the framework of the agreement.\nIn recent years, police on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have worked closely together and achieved positive results in continuously cracking down on cross-border telecom fraud. At the same time, cooperation between the two sides also faces some new problems, such as the two sides separately investigating criminal suspects, which is not conducive to forming a complete chain of evidence and recovering stolen funds, and not conducive to punishing crimes in accordance with the law and protecting the rights and interests of victims. We believe that, within the framework of the agreement and guided by the principles of being conducive to combating crime, protecting the interests of victims, achieving judicial fairness, and promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations, the two sides on both sides can continuously improve and deepen cooperation methods for combating cross-border telecom fraud, effectively protect the lawful rights and interests of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard peace and stability in cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201604/t20160430_11447699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 6 (reporter Zha Wenye): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 6th. He said that Ms. Chen Fengfuzhen, Director-General of the World Health Organization, sent a letter that day to the head of the health authority on the Taiwan side, inviting Taiwan to attend this year's World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that our position on Taiwan's participation in international organization activities is clear and consistent: it must be under the one-China principle, with reasonable and appropriate arrangements made through cross-Strait consultation. Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly since 2009 is a special arrangement made on the political basis that both sides of the Strait adhere to the “1992 Consensus.” This year, the Taiwan side has repeatedly expressed its wish to continue attending. We have taken this seriously and made arrangements, which fully reflects the mainland side's sincere desire to continue maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and is also a goodwill gesture from the mainland side.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that if the political foundation of cross-Strait relations is undermined in the future, the above arrangements will be difficult to sustain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160506_11452488.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-05-11","Lu Kang","","The Democratic Progressive Party of Taiwan will send Lin Tzou-yien, incoming head of public health authorities to participate in the World Health Assembly (WHA). Taiwan also claimed that the one-China principle cited by the WHO in its invitation letter has no connection with Taiwan's participation in the WHA. Taiwan's participation does not mean that it accepts the position spelt out in the invitation letter. In…","The WHO Director-General has sent a letter to authorities in charge of public health in Taiwan, inviting Taiwan to attend this year's WHA as an observer under the designation of \"Chinese Taipei\". This is a special arrangement we make for the peaceful development of cross-Straits ties and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots under the premise of the one-China principle. It fully showcases our sincere wishes to sustain the peaceful development of cross-Straits ties and our good will. I want to make it clear that the one-China principle is the prerequisite and necessary basis for Taiwan to take part in activities organized by international organizations. In this connection, we commend the WHO for sticking to the one-China principle, and will continue to deal with Taiwan's participation in the WHA in accordance with the principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1362394.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1362338.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","The new DPP authorities in Taiwan recently issued a “four-point statement” regarding Taiwan’s participation in the WHA, saying that the one-China principle based on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 has nothing to do with Taiwan’s participation in the WHA, that this matter is “political interference,” and lodged a protest. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment?","The one-China principle is universally recognized by the international community. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1 both embody this principle, and their authority is beyond question. The WHO, as a specialized agency of the United Nations, reaffirming this is only natural.\nSince 2008, both sides of the Strait, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” have continuously enhanced political mutual trust and opened a new chapter of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations. Against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, starting in 2009 Taiwan was able to participate in the World Health Assembly. This was a special arrangement made under the one-China principle. Challenging the one-China principle that is universally recognized by the international community, the related arrangements will be difficult to sustain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455638.htm"],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The People's Daily recently published a commentator article, “Not Recognizing the ‘1992 Consensus’ Is Undermining the Common Political Foundation of Cross-Strait Relations,” which outside observers regard as an escalation of warnings and an ultimatum to Taiwan's newly elected leader. May I ask whether this represents the official position of the mainland? In addition, if Tsai Ing-wen does not recognize the “1992…","For some time, we have stated our position and attitude on major cross-Strait issues on many occasions. In particular, we have systematically explained and expounded the extreme importance of the political foundation of peaceful cross-Strait relations, and the prospects that the two possible paths could bring. This reflects our sincere wish to continue advancing peaceful cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” At present, cross-Strait relations are at an important juncture, and the ball is in the hands of Taiwan’s new ruling authorities. People will wait and see where they go from here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455637.htm"],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台中国新闻记者","Taiwan may soon send a special case team to take part in the second round of cross-strait joint consultations on combating fraud crimes. Could you introduce the relevant situation to us, especially what goals this round of consultations aims to achieve?","The competent authorities on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will hold working group talks on cooperation in combating telecom fraud under the \"Agreement on Mutual Assistance in Combating Crime and Judicial Assistance between the Two Sides of the Taiwan Strait\" in Zhuhai from May 12 to 14. The competent business departments of both sides will report relevant developments to media friends in a timely manner. Building on the consensus reached in the first round of working group consultations on April 21, the mainland side will continue to deepen cross-strait cooperation in jointly combating telecom fraud crimes, guided by the principles of being conducive to combating crime, protecting the interests of victims, achieving judicial justice and social fairness, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.\nIn recent years, the implementation of the Agreement on Mutual Assistance in Combating Crime and Judicial Assistance has yielded fruitful results. It has safeguarded the well-being of people on both sides and social order, and has brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. We do not wish to see the achievements in all areas of the peaceful development of cross-strait relations affected by damage to the \"1992 Consensus,\" which is the common political foundation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","According to reports, U.S. Deputy Assistant Secretary of State Dong Yunshang (董云裳) recently told Taiwan media in an exclusive interview that there cannot be any form of deadlock or crisis across the Strait, and she believes Tsai Ing-wen has been “consistent in word and deed” to date and has “done very well.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Since 2008, both sides of the Strait, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have opened a new chapter of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area, which accords with the common wishes and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, and has received high praise from the international community. We hope this status quo can continue. We have repeatedly emphasized that our major policy toward Taiwan will not change due to changes in Taiwan's political situation. For some time now, it has been clear to everyone who has been working to uphold the common political foundation across the Strait and the overall situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and who has been undermining the common political foundation and changing the cross-Strait status quo, who is building bridges and who is tearing them down. If some people cannot see even this clearly, and even encourage the latter, that is truly not a wise move.\nWe must reiterate that if a cross-Strait deadlock or a crisis results, the responsibility shall be borne by those who change the status quo.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455636.htm"],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Have arrangements not been made for family members of the 45 Taiwan telecom fraud suspects repatriated to the mainland from Kenya to visit them? When will they be able to come to the mainland to visit?","It is understood that the relevant departments have received a request from the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan for family members of criminal suspects to visit. Under the premise of conforming to our relevant regulations, family visits will be received after May 15. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (海协会) has promptly notified the Straits Exchange Foundation of the relevant situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Because the WHO invitation letter sent to Taiwan this year for the first time contains the text of Resolution 2758, some DPP figures have advocated that Taiwan’s delegation to this year’s World Health Assembly should enter the venue to protest. What comment do you have on this?","Regarding the principles for handling Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly, and the broader background of why Taiwan has been able to participate since 2009 — namely, that the peaceful development path of cross-Strait relations was opened on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” — I have already explained this very clearly just now; it is an objective reality. As for what consequences would result if anyone tried to challenge the one-China principle, they should make their own assessment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently, a “Belt and Road” Taiwan Business Western Tour delegation visited the mainland. There are reports that many Taiwanese enterprises want to use the “Belt and Road” to expand business opportunities and seek development. May I ask the spokesperson whether the TAO will provide more support to Taiwanese businesses with such intentions in the future?","You may have noticed that the TAO and ARATS have been actively creating convenient conditions for the broad Taiwanese business community to take part in the mainland's “Belt and Road” construction. Starting from the second half of last year, ARATS Chairman Chen Deming and Executive Vice Chairman Zheng Lizhong each led Taiwanese business inspection delegations to inspect cities along the Belt and Road. Last year they went to Shaanxi, Gansu, Ningxia, Yunnan and Guizhou. From May 8 to 14 this year, Chairman Chen again led a Taiwanese business inspection delegation to inspect Sichuan, Chongqing and Guangxi. The activity is currently ongoing, and it is understood that more than 20 Taiwanese business representatives are taking part. It is expected that in June this year Chairman Chen will also lead an inspection delegation to Xinjiang and other places.\nThe reason we organize such intensive inspections for Taiwanese business friends is mainly to let them understand firsthand the important construction projects related to the “Belt and Road” in the relevant provinces and cities, and to hear local introductions to the relevant plans for economic and social development during the 13th Five-Year Plan period. This provides them with first-hand material for grasping the planning for participation in the “Belt and Road” construction. As everyone knows, the construction of the “Belt and Road” is a very important measure in our opening up and a rare opportunity. We therefore sincerely hope that Taiwanese businesses can give full play to and make good use of their own advantages, find the right positioning, become familiar with the situation, and actively participate. We hope they will find business opportunities suited to themselves in future trade and investment, business management and services, so as to achieve mutual benefit and win-win results and share in the opportunities brought by the mainland's development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455631.htm"],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","In nine days it will be “5·20.” The framework of Tsai Ing-wen’s inaugural address is roughly complete. After the KMT, which supported the “1992 Consensus,” has stepped down, her inaugural address should not mention the “1992 Consensus”; she will only acknowledge the “1992 Talks.” May I ask for the spokesperson’s views on this?","We have made it very clear that the “1992 Consensus” has been the foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008 and constitutes an important part of the current state of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. To maintain the status quo, one should of course accept this foundation. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizes its core meaning, the two sides can engage in exchanges and positive interaction, and cross-Strait relations can continue to move forward. Our requirements are reasonable, because we have not raised any new demands on Taiwan’s newly elected leader beyond those made since 2008. We have repeatedly reiterated that our major policy toward Taiwan will not change with changes in Taiwan’s political situation. We sincerely hope that cross-Strait relations can continue to develop along the bright road paved on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which is also the expectation of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","This year, media have repeatedly reported that cross-Strait flights are being reduced every week. May I ask the spokesperson, will this affect the future development of direct cross-Strait flights, and will the two sides take corresponding measures? After the DPP takes office, if it does not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” can the two so-called “little” associations continue to operate?","First, the specific operation of cross-Strait flights and the number of flights are determined by market rules. Under the relevant cross-Strait agreements, this is itself a market arrangement, so everyone should view it with a calm mind. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Taiwan’s prospective “Premier” Lin Chuan recently said that joining the “Belt and Road” requires first resolving Taiwan’s international positioning. May I ask how the mainland will resolve the positioning issue in the process of Taiwan joining the “Belt and Road”? If cross-Strait relations change in the future, would this affect Taiwan businesses’ participation in the “Belt and Road”?","I am not clear on the specific background and implications of his remark, so I am not in a position to comment. The “Belt and Road” is the mainland's strategy of opening up to the outside world on its own initiative, and it does not seem to have much to do with international issues. In addition, you mentioned Taiwan's international status. I have repeatedly cited UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and the one-China principle just now.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Taiwan’s highest leader, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou, is about to step down. Over these eight years, the Ma administration promoted the signing of 23 agreements between the two sides, actively advanced cross-Strait exchanges, and on the South China Sea issue, Mr. Ma also upheld the position of defending sovereignty. May I ask the spokesperson: what is the mainland’s assessment of Ma Ying-jeou’s eight years?","Over these 8 years, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” cross-Strait relations opened a new chapter of peaceful development. The two sides built political mutual trust, carried out positive interactions, signed 23 agreements, advanced cross-Strait economic cooperation and exchanges in all fields, and reduced friction and internal attrition between the two sides in foreign affairs. Therefore, these 8 years of cross-Strait development have won broad support from compatriots on both sides and general affirmation from the international community. This is plain for all to see, cannot be denied, and will be written into history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455635.htm"],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","The Director of the Media Relations Office of the US State Department recently pointed out that the United States still adheres to the one-China principle based on the three China-US joint communiqués and the Taiwan Relations Act. A spokesperson of the State Department's Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs then added that the future of cross-Strait relations will be decided by the people on both sides. What…","Abiding by the commitments made on the basis of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués is the cornerstone of the development of China-US relations. The US and the entire international community highly affirm the achievements of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations over these eight years, and all hope that this peaceful development and the situation of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait can be sustained. At the same time, the important reason this situation took shape is that both sides adhered to the “1992 Consensus.” Therefore, whether this situation can continue in the future depends on whether both sides can keep upholding the “1992 Consensus.” Everyone is very clear on this principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","First question: after May 20, if the DPP authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” will it affect this year's Straits Forum? Second question: a recent poll shows that more than half of the Taiwan public supports sending telecom fraud suspects to the mainland for trial. What is your assessment of this shift in public opinion?","First question: preparations for the Straits Forum are progressing smoothly. As everyone knows, the Straits Forum is a platform that we built after 2008, with grassroots people on both sides of the Strait as its main participants. We will continue to advance civil exchanges and cooperation across the Strait; this policy will not change. Therefore, the Straits Forum will not be affected by any such factors.\nSecond question: regarding the handling of cross-border telecom fraud cases, a great deal has already been introduced at previous press conferences. Of course, your point that half of the Taiwan public expresses support is, I think, to be expected. As everyone knows, the victims of these criminal activities are all mainland residents, and their losses have been extremely severe; some have even paid with their lives. Handling this on the mainland is reasonable, lawful and proper, so people's hearts are alike. As I just mentioned, the second round of consultations is about to take place. I believe that, along the correct direction, cooperation between the two sides on jointly combating fraud crimes will also gradually advance in a healthy and orderly manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On April 29, Taiwan's legislature passed a motion, proposed by DPP lawmakers, requiring Taiwan's education authorities to revoke the micro-adjusted curriculum guidelines. Given that the DPP is now impatiently pushing to forcibly revoke the micro-adjusted curriculum guidelines, what is the spokesperson's view?","We have said many times that the compilation of textbooks should respect history and respect facts. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are trying to continue promoting “de-Sinicization” separatist activities in the field of culture and education, using the “Taiwan independence” view of history to poison the younger generation in Taiwan and sever the blood ties between compatriots on both sides. They think they have sown what they call “dragon seeds,” but what they will reap can only be “fleas.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The WHA invitation letter issued by the World Health Organization was addressed to the then head of the health department, Chiang Ping-huang. However, since the WHA was held on May 23 and the newly appointed head of the health department, Lin Tzou-yan, has registered to attend, it is rumored that the mainland side will strictly review the content of Tsai Ing-wen’s inaugural address of May 20 before deciding…","First question: Since 2009, the WHO has made special arrangements for Taiwan's participation in accordance with the one-China principle. This year, the WHO sent the invitation letter to the current head of Taiwan's health authority, which is in line with past practice. On May 6, WHO Director-General Dr. Margaret Chan wrote to the head of the health authority on the Taiwan side, inviting Taiwan to attend this year's World Health Assembly under the name \"Chinese Taipei\" as an observer. It is understood that the Taiwan side has replied. We believe the World Health Organization will handle this in accordance with the spirit of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and relevant WHA resolutions.\nSecond question: Let us first review an important speech that General Secretary Xi Jinping gave at the two sessions of the National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference on March 5 this year. General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed that our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent and will not change because of changes in Taiwan's political situation. We will uphold the political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus\" and continue to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. He also specifically emphasized that we will continue to advance exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, deepen the integrated economic and social development across the Taiwan Strait, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, bring compatriots' hearts closer, and strengthen recognition of the community of shared destiny. I think it follows from this that the policy content of the mainland's Taiwan policy, which places hopes on the Taiwan people, is obvious and needs no doubt.\nFor some time, we have repeatedly appealed for upholding the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, precisely to respond to the earnest expectations of compatriots on both sides for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We believe that supporting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations remains the mainstream public opinion of people on both sides. Therefore, we sincerely hope that cross-Strait relations will continue to develop on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus,\" that the well-being of compatriots on both sides will keep increasing, that emotional ties will keep deepening, and that mutual benefit and win-win outcomes will be achieved through exchange and cooperation.\nBut as everyone knows, the fact that cross-Strait relations have achieved the series of results they have today is inseparable from the \"1992 Consensus.\" Therefore, to maintain the status quo, we must first uphold this common political foundation; we cannot take only the fruit while refusing to tend the roots. I think the vast majority of compatriots in Taiwan should be able to understand this.\nThe results of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations still need to be jointly safeguarded by compatriots on both sides, and the prospects for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations also need to be jointly created by compatriots on both sides. Therefore, in advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and implementing our Taiwan policy, we will always work together with the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nAs for the specific cases you mentioned, such as the situation of the cross-border telecom fraud crimes just mentioned, as other journalist friends cited from Taiwan media polls, more than half of the Taiwan public supports mainland authorities handling the case. I think that some people on the island who oppose it do so out of partisan self-interest and political private gain, so it is not surprising that they oppose it. I have also often thought: in the face of the blood and tears of these victims, how can anyone use pan-political tactics to turn such criminal cases into political confrontation? I find this hard to understand. I think that people and forces who put politics above everything are so indifferent to the safety of mainland compatriots' lives and property; how could you then expect them to safeguard the interests of the Taiwan people at critical moments?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160511_11455646.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160511_11455633.htm"],[0,"2016-05-18","Hong Lei","","The US House of Representatives passed a resolution on the afternoon of May 16 local time, saying that the Taiwan Relations Act and the six assurances together form the cornerstone of US relations with Taiwan. What is your comment on that?","We firmly oppose the resolution passed by the US House of Representatives. Taiwan affairs belong to China's domestic affairs. The so-called Taiwan Relations Act unilaterally made by the US and the relevant assurances constitute a grave breach of the one-China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués between China and the US, and interfere in China's domestic affairs. The Chinese government has long been expressing its opposition. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués, honor its commitment to opposing \"Taiwan independence\", immediately revoke the resolution and take effective measures to eliminate the adverse impact.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1364549.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1364451.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-05-20","Hua Chunying","","Do you have any comment on the inauguration speech by Tsai Ing-wen?","The head of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will issue a statement on Tsai Ing-wen's speech this morning, so stay tuned.\nI want to stress that the one-China principle has been widely recognized by the international community. It is also the political basis and prerequisite for the development of relations between China and other countries in the world. No matter how the political situation in Taiwan changes, the Chinese government will not alter its commitment to the one-China principle and its opposition to \"Taiwan independence\", \"two Chinas\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\".\nYou may have noted that the Russian Foreign Ministry stated yesterday that there is but one China in the world, and that it opposes all forms of \"Taiwan independence\". We highly commend the Russian side for that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1365237.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1365177.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-05-20","Hua Chunying","","Tsai Ing-wen said in her speech that she would deepen cooperation with Japan, the US and other democracies. Japan has also expressed its welcome. What is your comment on that?","As I just said, the one-China principle is an important political basis and prerequisite for the development of relations between China and the rest of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1365237.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1365177.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-05-20","Hua Chunying","","Tsai Ing-wen also said that she would try to lift Taiwan's profile in international trade and economic cooperation, and improve relations with other democracies. How does Beijing feel about such efforts?","We hold a consistent and clear position on Taiwan's external contacts. The one-China principle is an important political foundation and prerequisite for the development of China's relations with other countries. We have no objection to the unofficial business exchanges between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic ties with us, but firmly oppose their official engagement and agreement that implies sovereignty or is of official nature. As for Taiwan's participation in multilateral trade arrangements, there must be pragmatic discussions between both sides of the Taiwan Straits on the premise of not creating \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1365237.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1365177.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-05-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 21 (reporter Zha Wenye) — In response to the question of whether the liaison and communication mechanism between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council can continue to operate now that the DPP is in power in Taiwan, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on May 21 in response to a question: Only upon confirming adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” the common political foundation that embodies the one-China principle, can the liaison and communication mechanism between the two departments continue.\nMa Xiaoguang said: In February 2014, the heads of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council met in Nanjing and decided to establish a regular liaison and communication mechanism between the two departments on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Over more than two years, the two departments have actively interacted, held five working-level meetings, established a cross-Strait hotline, maintained close communication, and properly handled many complex and sensitive issues, which has been widely recognized by all sectors on both sides. The operation of the liaison and communication mechanism helps both sides communicate promptly on developments, avoid miscalculation, manage differences, and build understanding and mutual trust, making some “impossibilities” in cross-Strait relations a reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160521_11463274.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-05-24","Hua Chunying","","On May 23, the Taiwan authority said that \"it does not take a particular stance in legal terms\" on whether Okinotori is an island or a reef. It is commented that the new Taiwan administration has gone backwards on the issue of Okinotori, undermining the rights and interests of Taiwan fishermen. How do you comment?","Okinotori is an isolated reef in the west Pacific distant from the Japanese soil. Pursuant to the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), Okinotori cannot have the exclusive economic zone and the continental shelf. Waters off 12 nautical miles of it are high seas, where all countries are entitled to freedoms on the high seas such as fishing and so forth. On April 2012, the Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf (CLCS) adopted the recommendations in regard to the submission made by Japan on the outer limits of its continental shelf, rebuffing Japan's illegal claims based on Okinotori.\nI also want to point out that the above-water area of Okinotori is less than 10 square meters at high tide, or no bigger than two beds as some people put it. Japan's illegal and greedy claim of jurisdiction over 700,000 square kilometers merely based on two beds constitutes a grave encroachment on the high seas and international seabed area, and also puts international interests at great danger. Japan repeatedly declares itself as a champion of international law, and we hope it would live up to its own words and abide by the law.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1366103.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1366070.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-05-25","Hua Chunying","","Hong Kong media reported that Taiwan has appointed its so-called \"ambassador to the US\". What is your comment?","The international community in general follows the \"one China\" policy. Taiwan can only have non-official and non-governmental relations with the US. Therefore, the role and position of Taiwan's institutions and persons in charge is very clear. We oppose any attempt to create \"two Chinas\", \"one China, one Taiwan\" and \"Taiwan independence\". It is hoped that the relevant country would stick to the \"one China\" principle, and must not allow Taiwan institutions and officials to engage in activities incompatible with their role and position.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1366744.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1366444.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Does the mainland consider Tsai Ing-wen's “May 20 speech” to be “unsatisfactory but tolerable,” and will it “listen to her words and observe her actions”?","The statement on the current state of cross-Strait relations issued on May 20 by the head of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the head of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already clearly expressed our solemn position.\nThe speech given by the new leader of the Taiwan authorities on May 20 adopted an ambiguous attitude on the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations, which is the greatest concern of compatriots on both sides. It did not explicitly acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” or endorse its core meaning, and it did not propose specific measures to ensure the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations. I want to emphasize that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China; cross-Strait relations are not relations between two countries. Questions of principle concerning the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations are a “required question” that cannot be avoided, and there is no room for ambiguity.\nAs the head of the Taiwan Affairs Office's statement pointed out, different choices of path determine different prospects. Whether to uphold the common political foundation embodying the one-China principle, or to push the “two-state theory” and “one side, one country” “Taiwan independence” separatist proposition; whether to continue on the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, or to repeat the mistake of provoking tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait; whether to enhance the emotional bonds and well-being of compatriots on both sides, or to sever the spiritual ties between compatriots and harm their fundamental interests. On these major questions, the Taiwan authorities must give a clear answer through concrete actions, and accept the test of history and the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466776.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","In her May 20 inauguration speech, Tsai Ing-wen repeatedly mentioned that Taiwan would launch the “New Southbound Policy,” and hoped Taiwan could take part in future multilateral and bilateral economic cooperation and free trade negotiations, breaking away from its current dependence on a single market. I wonder what the spokesperson's comment is?","Everyone should still remember that, during the Lee Teng-hui and Chen Shui-bian periods, the so-called \"Southward Policy\" was forcibly promoted. This kind of practice, which served political purposes and went against economic laws, caused enormous harm to the interests of many Taiwan businesses and had adverse effects on Taiwan's economy. The lesson is not far away.\nAs for Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation, if the one-China principle cannot be upheld and political mutual trust no longer exists, it will inevitably have adverse effects. If one attempts to carry out \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities internationally, creating \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan,\" this path simply will not work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466770.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","In her May 20 inaugural speech, Tsai Ing-wen mentioned that the ruling parties on both sides of the Strait should put down the “historical baggage,” start positive dialogue, and benefit the people on both sides. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Everyone is very clear about the history of the Democratic Progressive Party. This party adheres to the “Taiwan independence” position and has documents advocating “Taiwan independence.” This is an obstacle to developing relations with the mainland that the DPP created itself. Clearly, it is the DPP that needs to put down its historical baggage.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466772.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan’s legislature originally planned to pass, at preliminary review, an amendment to the “Referendum Act” which, in addition to adding “referendum on territorial change” to the matters subject to national referendum, newly added a provision that any cross-Strait political consultations must be approved by national referendum, both before and after the exchange of documents, in order to take effect.…","“Taiwan independence” is the greatest scourge to peace in the Taiwan Strait and to the stable development of cross-Strait relations. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” means there can be no peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose any force using so-called “legal amendment” or other pretexts to carry out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. No one should attempt to test our determination and ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466774.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","When Tsai Ing-wen took office on May 20, she did not explicitly acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” Will the mainland abandon the so-called tacit understanding across the Strait on “diplomatic truce”?","We treat Taiwan’s external contacts in accordance with the One-China Principle, and firmly oppose any act that attempts to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international arena. The One-China Principle is generally recognized by the international community. If anyone attempts to carry out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally, or to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan,” it will certainly not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466771.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's education authorities recently announced that they will abolish the “curriculum fine-tuning” passed in 2014. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","I have just reiterated the remarks made on May 20 by the heads of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. They make it very clear that different paths lead to different prospects. If the DPP authorities write their own “answer” with the latter choice, they must bear the consequences that follow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","It is reported that the Taiwan authorities will withdraw complaints against 126 people involved in the “Sunflower Student Movement.” The members of the 2014 “Sunflower Student Movement” occupied Taiwan's legislature because they opposed the Cross-Strait Service Trade Agreement. May I ask the spokesperson what the Taiwan Affairs Office's evaluation is of the new Taiwan authorities doing this so soon after taking…","We note that some public opinion on the island has raised questions: what impact will this approach to handling the matter have on Taiwan's society, both now and in the future?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 8th Straits Forum will be held in Xiamen on the 11th of next month. Please introduce the latest preparations.","Preparations for the 8th Straits Forum are progressing smoothly. The forum congress will be held on June 12.\nThe theme of this forum is “Expanding Civil Exchanges and Promoting Integrated Development.” It will continue to present the characteristics of being “civil, grassroots, and broad-based,” and its activities will be closer to the concerns and needs of young people and grassroots people on both sides of the Strait.\nFirst, activities are designed around employment, entrepreneurship, livelihood services, and other issues of common concern to cross-Strait youth and grassroots people. For example, new activities have been added, such as the “Working Across the Strait, Creating the Future” Youth Innovation Pioneers Forum and Taiwan professional talent matching, to provide platforms and broaden channels for Taiwan youth to work in Fujian.\nSecond, centered on themes such as the construction of the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone and the core area of the Maritime Silk Road, activities are designed to share development opportunities for compatriots on both sides. Activities such as the Cross-Strait Think Tank Forum, the Straits Financial Forum, and the Common Home Forum will be held to promote exchanges and cooperation between relevant industries and townships and villages on both sides, and to explore issues such as joint governance and joint construction.\nThird, interactive sharing and experiential exchange are highlighted. The forum congress has added a dialogue session with well-known young entrepreneurs from both sides of the Strait. Activities such as matching of namesake villages, ancestral homeland culture, and characteristic townships will invite Taiwan youth, farmers, and clan members to visit places such as namesake and common-ancestor villages, Taiwan youth innovation bases, and farmers' entrepreneurship parks for experiential exchange. The Workers' Forum will showcase civil inventions from both sides of the Strait and hold skills competitions and technological innovation exchanges. The Women's Forum will bring together young women college students from both sides to compete on the same stage. The Public Welfare Forum will arrange for Taiwan youth students to enter communities in groups to exchange volunteer service experience with local youth.\nWe welcome journalists to visit and report. The Straits Forum News Center accepts journalist registration applications from May 10 to 31. Relevant registration information can be found on the official website of the Straits Forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466769.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou has left office. What is the mainland's evaluation of Ma's conduct on cross-strait relations over the past eight years? Will he be invited to the mainland? Will there be a second “Xi-Ma meeting”? Thank you.","Since 2008, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides across the Strait have created the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advanced exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, enhanced the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides, maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and brought cross-Strait relations to their best situation since 1949. In particular, through the joint efforts of both sides, the first meeting between the leaders of the two sides in 66 years was realized, a milestone in the development of cross-Strait relations. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou, as leader of the Taiwan authorities, made efforts and contributions to this.\nThe situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been hard-won and must be jointly safeguarded by compatriots on both sides. We welcome and hope that all far-sighted people who care about and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will continue to play a positive role as before, contributing their wisdom and strength.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466773.htm"],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The Taiwan side has noted that the mainland has suspended the communication and consultation mechanisms between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council, as well as between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Straits Interchange Foundation. On the 23rd, it also announced stricter quarantine inspections for citrus fruits imported from Taiwan. Is there a risk that the Cross-Strait Agreement on…","In November 1992, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), each authorized to do so, reached a consensus that each side would orally express that both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle. In May 2008, after the two associations confirmed the “1992 Consensus” through exchanges of letters and telegrams, the two sides resumed contacts and consultations and negotiations. Over the past eight years, the two associations successively signed 23 agreements, which enhanced the interests and well-being of cross-Strait residents and promoted exchanges and cooperation in all fields. It can thus be seen that the achievement of these results is inseparable from the two sides' adherence to the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Only by affirming the political basis that embodies the one-China principle can the results of institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges be ensured to remain unaffected.\nAs for some of the individual cases you mentioned, such as the investment protection agreement, as everyone knows, as early as 1994 we formulated the “Law on Protection of Investments by Taiwan Compatriots,” and later the two sides also signed an investment protection agreement. Our protection of the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesses is consistent and clear, and will not change.\nAs for the question concerning quarantine and inspection of citrus imported from Taiwan, to my understanding, since February of this year, mainland inspection and quarantine departments have on multiple occasions intercepted citrus canker bacteria in citrus fruit shipped from Taiwan to the mainland. This bacterium is a quarantine pest of concern to the mainland. As everyone knows, citrus cultivation is also an important fruit industry on the mainland, so the mainland's quality inspection departments issued warning notices to all ports in order to prevent this pest from entering the mainland through cargo. The purpose of this measure is to protect the mainland's ecological security and agricultural production security.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Regarding the WHA, Taiwan may submit a so-called written “protest letter.” Can the mainland accept this? In addition, will both sides hold talks as they have in the past?","We have stressed many times that Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly is a special arrangement made under the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志记者","Recently, Tung Chen-yuan, spokesperson for Taiwan's Executive Yuan, said that regarding the question of whether Okinotorishima is a “reef” or an “island,” Taiwan does not adopt any specific legal position and will await a United Nations ruling. What is the spokesperson's view on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated its position on the Okinotori Reef issue. Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters, and we will, as always, safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of cross-Strait fishermen in the relevant waters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Earlier, when the TAO responded to Tsai Ing-wen's May 20 speech, it described it as an “unfinished answer sheet,” and outside interpretations said this means there will be a “make-up exam.” May I ask roughly how long such a “make-up exam” period would be? That is, roughly how long is the period of “listening to their words and observing their deeds”? Another question: recently, a former TAO leader with the rank…","I will combine your questions into one answer. We do not comment on individual remarks. The May 20 remarks by the head of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have already made our stern position clear. Please take note.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","The first question: In her “5.20” speech, Tsai Ing-wen specifically cited the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” as one of the bases for handling cross-Strait affairs. I would like to ask what the TAO's response is? The second question: We have noted that the Tsai Ing-wen authorities have changed the title “representative in the United States” to “ambassador to…","First question: this shows that everyone has noticed that the new leader of the Taiwan authorities merely reiterated the existing position of Taiwan’s current regulations, and still avoided the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations. If we want to ensure that the existing institutionalized exchange mechanisms and the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations are not affected, we must confirm with the mainland a common political foundation that embodies the one-China principle.\nSecond question: the international community generally adheres to the one-China policy. The status and identity of Taiwan’s institutions in the United States and of their heads are very clearly defined. We firmly oppose any act of creating “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international arena.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Before 5.20, many Taiwan products were seized by Fujian customs under the “mini three links.” Now, in her 5.20 speech, Tsai Ing-wen did not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” May I ask whether the “mini three links” will therefore be aborted?","I do not know the specifics of the so-called “seizure” you mention. But as I just said, since 2008, the institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges and the achievements in all areas have been built on the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Therefore, only by confirming this common political foundation can these achievements remain unaffected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201605/t20160525_11466675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-05-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to reporters’ questions, including whether agreements already signed between the two sides would become invalid, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said at the regular press conference on May 25 in response to questions: In November 1992, the Straits Exchange Foundation of the mainland and the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan (SEF), authorized to do so, reached a consensus that each side orally expresses that both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle. In May 2008, after the two associations confirmed the “1992 Consensus” through exchanges of letters and telegrams, the two sides resumed contact and negotiations. Over these eight years, the two associations signed 23 agreements in succession, which enhanced the interests and well-being of people on both sides and promoted exchanges and cooperation in all fields. The achievement of these results is inseparable from both sides adhering to the foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only by confirming the political foundation embodying the one-China principle can the results of institutionalized exchanges across the Strait be ensured against impact.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201605/t20160525_11466775.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2016-05-26","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen assumed office as the leader of Taiwan region. In her inaugural speech, she didn’t clearly recognize the 1992 Consensus and acknowledge its core essence. Rumor has it that the PLA is going to hold large-scale military exercises aiming at deterring \"Taiwan independence\" forces. What is your comment?","On the question you have raised, like what was said by the head of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on May 20, we are today as determined as ever and more capable to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will resolutely contain any action and attempt by the secessionists for “Taiwan independence\".","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2016-05/26/content_4665371.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-05-26","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After assuming office in Taiwan region on May 20th, the Tsai Ing-wen administration expressed that it would not hold an official stance on whether the Japanese-called Okinotorishima should be an “island” or a “reef”, which is remarkably different from the former Ma Ying-jeou administration’s stance on the issue. So, if the Tsai Ing-wen administration changes its stance and waives Taiwan’s claim to the sovereignty…","Our policy and position on this kind of issue is consistent and known to all. It is the common responsibility of the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2016-05/26/content_4665371.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2016-06-06","Hong Lei","","The completion ceremony of the Panama Canal expansion project will be held on June 26. Head of the Taiwan authorities will attend the ceremony. Has the mainland received Panama's invitation? Will the mainland send anyone to the ceremony?","The one-China principle is the prerequisite for China to develop and handle relations with other countries in the World. It is also a universally recognized principle. We hope that the relevant country will deal with Taiwan-related issues with prudence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1370122.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1369911.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-06-14","Lu Kang","","I have two questions on China-US relations. The Dalai Lama is on a visit in Washington. He said that he might meet with US President Barack Obama this week. Has China warned the US not to meet with him? Leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen will be visiting the US on her way to and from Panama. We don't know whom she is meeting, but has the Chinese side warned the US government not to arrange any high-level…","Your two questions all come down to the fundamental one-China policy. I can tell you for sure that the US government made serious commitments on sticking to the one-China policy.\nOn Taiwan-related issues, the US side made it clear that it would follow the one-China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués between China and the US. So in response to your second question, we ask the US government to honor its commitments and deal with the relevant matters in accordance with the one-China policy, and not to offer any chance to any separatist forces that try to create \"two Chinas\", \"one China, one Taiwan\" or split China.\nBack to your first question, the US government also made solemn commitments. It acknowledges that there is only one China, that Tibet is an inseparable part of China and will never recognize the so-called Tibetan government in exile. Under the cloak of religion, the 14th Dalai Lama peddles his political ambitions of dividing China all around the world. We ask all countries and governments not to give him any room to carry out such campaigns, even less risking arousing the firm opposition from the 1.3 billion Chinese people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1372136.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1372056.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-06-14","Lu Kang","","The Cambodian government arrested 27 Chinese from the mainland and Taiwan suspected of telecommunication fraud. Has the Chinese government been in touch with the Cambodian government? Did you ask them to repatriate the suspects to China?","This case involves the law enforcement cooperation between Cambodia and China. I will get more information on the specifics of this case. As you may know, there have been several cases of this kind recently. The Chinese government holds a very clear position on this issue, and always hopes to carry out law enforcement cooperation with relevant countries in compliance with international law and the one-China policy. We also highly commend the positive efforts by relevant countries on this issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1372136.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1372056.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","新华社记者","According to relevant reports, the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently referred to the mainland as a neighbor during a casual exchange with the media. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are one family. Cross-Strait relations are not relations between states, so they are absolutely not a “neighbor” relationship either.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483770.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Some Taiwan public opinion holds that, as cross-Strait relations change and a series of news events ferment, some anti-Taiwan sentiment has emerged among Mainland civilians this year, which should be taken seriously. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. Therefore, there is no so-called “anti-Taiwan” sentiment among the mainland public as you describe; there are only strong calls to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483764.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","福建海峡之声广播电台记者","There have been many reports and comments on the candidate for chairperson of Taiwan’s Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), and there is also much attention on how the future cross-Strait consultation and liaison mechanisms will operate. What is the mainland’s attitude on this?","Our position and sincerity in promoting cross-Strait consultations and negotiations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” have not changed. Whether the consultation and liaison mechanisms between the two associations can be maintained depends on whether the Straits Exchange Foundation can be authorized to confirm to the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483769.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Ma Ying-jeou had planned to travel to Hong Kong today to attend an event and deliver a speech, but the Taiwan authorities ultimately rejected his application, on the grounds that Hong Kong is a sensitive, high-risk area. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have noted the relevant reports.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","It is understood that a batch of cross-Strait exchange bases has recently been added. Could you introduce the relevant situation?","In order to create more cross-Strait exchange and cooperation platforms and provide compatriots on both sides of the Strait with more opportunities to revisit history, savor culture, enjoy family reunions, and achieve integrated development, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council recently decided to add six new Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Bases to the existing 43: Huangshan in Anhui; the Wudian Traditional Street in Jinjiang, Fujian Province; the birthplace of Zhu Xi in Youxi, Sanming; Zhu Xi's hometown in Wuyi Mountain, Nanping; the Zhang Family Marshal's Residence Museum in Liaoning; and the Tianhou Temple in Tianjin. We welcome compatriots from Taiwan and people from all walks of life to visit these exchange bases for sightseeing, exchange, and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483762.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Some media reported that the New Power Party caucus in Taiwan recently proposed so-called “constitutional amendment” motions, including abolishing the provincial government and eliminating the “one country, two areas” formulation. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity is a blatant provocation and sabotage of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If anyone attempts, through so-called “constitutional amendment” or other means, to split Taiwan away from China, they will only be smashed head-on and bleed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483768.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","At the 8th Straits Forum, Taiwan participants proposed that the mainland further expand its opening to Taiwan in small-scale trade, including raising the amount of small-scale trade and opening more ports. What is the mainland's attitude on this?","Small-scale trade with Taiwan is a beneficial supplement to cross-Strait trade and has long played an important role in promoting direct cross-Strait commerce. At present, small-scale trade with Taiwan, because of its fast and convenient features, still plays a unique and positive role in promoting cross-Strait agricultural trade, serving the production and operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland, and facilitating exchanges among grassroots people on both sides. We believe the relevant authorities will pay attention to these concerns and actively consider promoting the healthy and steady development of small-scale trade, further strengthening civilian economic and trade exchanges across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483766.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","At present, communication between the Mainland Affairs Council and the Taiwan Affairs Office, the SEF, and ARATS has essentially been interrupted, but the DPP government is willing to launch Track II communication. May I ask whether the mainland is willing to engage in Track II communication? In the past, during the Chen Shui-bian administration, when consultations between the SEF and ARATS were interrupted, both…","First question: We have always stressed the importance of the \"1992 Consensus\" because it embodies the one-China principle and clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations: the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and the two sides are not a relationship between two countries. This is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The new leader of the Taiwan authorities has so far taken an ambiguous attitude on the nature of cross-Strait relations. If we are to ensure the existing institutionalized exchange mechanisms across the Strait and the achievements of peaceful development, the political foundation embodying the one-China principle must be confirmed.\nYour second question, regarding the Hung Su-chu incident: we note that this incident has been unanimously condemned by all sectors. The causes and background of this incident are indeed worth everyone's reflection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Recently, Yu Zhengsheng, Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, stated at the opening ceremony of the Straits Forum that maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait requires continuously expanding exchanges between the peoples across the Strait. The more complex the situation in cross-Strait…","Safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait hinges on adhering to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” firmly opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and also on continuously expanding exchanges between the people on both sides. It is understood that a series of exchange activities between the people on both sides will be held in the near future in fields such as culture, education, youth, and religion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","经济日报记者","Taiwan media recently reported a sharp drop in mainland tour groups visiting Taiwan, and predicted that after entering July, the total number of mainland tour group visitors to Taiwan each day will be even lower. May I ask the spokesperson for views on this?","Since 2008, against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, mainland tourists' travel to Taiwan has continued to develop rapidly and healthily. As is well known, since this year, the situation on the island and the broader cross-Strait relations have changed, which has caused concern among mainland operators and tourists and thereby reduced their willingness to travel to Taiwan. As for the specific changes in travel to Taiwan, these are mainly market behavior, depending on the willingness of enterprises and tourists. Relevant mainland authorities have never set quotas for mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan; quotas are a unilateral practice of the Taiwan side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Earlier, the mainland side said that Tsai Ing-wen's answer sheet was incomplete. I would like to ask the spokesperson how you assess Tsai Ing-wen's answers on the answer sheet over this past month. In addition, I would like to ask: official exchanges between the two sides across the Strait are now suspended. What are the main priorities of the Taiwan Affairs Office for the current and coming period?","The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. To ensure that the existing institutionalized cross-Strait exchange mechanisms and the achievements of peaceful development are not affected, the key is to confirm the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle.\nRegarding the second question, we will continue to uphold the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose and curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, continue to advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","Recently, mainland spouses in Taiwan seeking to obtain identity documents have had the waiting period shortened from six years to four. In response, the chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council said, “Lenient in daily life, strict in identity.” This morning, the Internal Administration Committee of the Legislative Yuan did not recognize the decision that had been passed in the earlier initial review. What are…","As for your first question, the discriminatory treatment that mainland spouses encounter in Taiwan, and the failure to safeguard their legitimate rights and interests, which has long gone unresolved, are, I believe, very clear to everyone regarding the obstacles involved. The DPP has disregarded the legitimate rights and interests of cross-Strait marriages and families and has repeatedly obstructed them for political purposes, which is unpopular. Mainland spouses are also relatives of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the Taiwan side can adjust and amend outdated discriminatory regulations as soon as possible and genuinely attend to the reasonable demands of mainland spouses.\nAs for your second question, we have always handled Taiwan’s external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose any act in the international arena that creates “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","At the Taiwan youth symposium of this Straits Forum, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng had a warm conversation with Taiwan youth, hoping they would develop better and live better on the Mainland. May I ask the spokesperson what other expectations there are for the Taiwan youth group?","As Chairman Yu Zhengsheng pointed out at this year's Straits Forum, the future responsibility for cross-Strait relations rests on the shoulders of young people on both sides of the Strait, and safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait requires sustained efforts by young people on both sides. We warmly welcome young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to pursue their aspirations. We are willing to create more conditions for their study, employment, entrepreneurship and exchanges on the mainland, and to build better platforms, so that young people on both sides have more contact and exchange, enhance mutual understanding, draw closer in heart, foster harmony of national sentiment, and deepen a correct understanding of cross-Strait relations. They can become good friends and good partners who strive together and walk hand in hand, and even more so become promoters, builders and defenders of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, jointly contributing to a bright future for cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483765.htm"],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","中新社记者","I have two questions to ask. First, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng mentioned at the opening ceremony of the Straits Forum that he attaches great importance to the proposal by Taiwan compatriots for more convenient travel to the mainland, and that implementation measures will be issued soon. May I ask what specific measures the spokesperson can share? Second, Taiwan media have reported that the KMT Youth Work Committee…","We attach great importance to the suggestion from Taiwan compatriots that travel within the mainland become more convenient. We understand that civil aviation authorities have equipped nearly 1,000 self-service check-in and self-service ticketing devices capable of reading Taiwan Compatriot Permits at 34 airports with heavy traffic of Taiwan compatriots, including Beijing, Shanghai and Guangzhou. Meanwhile, railway authorities are also working to resolve self-service ticket purchase and collection with card-type Taiwan Compatriot Permits. In addition, relevant departments will continue to study adding ports where one-time Taiwan Compatriot Permits can be issued on arrival.\nRegarding your second question: the Youth Work General Association of the Kuomintang of China delegation will visit the mainland from June 20 to 25, and Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, will meet with the delegation. The main content of the visit is exchanges with the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League of China, the All-China Youth Federation, and youth federations of relevant provinces and cities on youth work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council Chairperson Zhang Xiaoyue said on the 13th that they still have not been able to have any interaction with TAO Director Zhang Zhijun. Can the spokesperson confirm this? Will the heads of the cross-Strait affairs authorities continue to interact via the cross-Strait hotline in the future?","The communication mechanism between the cross-Strait affairs authorities of both sides and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between the two associations are both built on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only when the political foundation embodying the one-China principle is confirmed can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","At the 8th Straits Film and Television Season held recently in Xiamen, “Nirvana in Fire” was voted the mainland TV series most popular with Taiwan residents. More and more Taiwan residents now enjoy mainland TV dramas. How do you view this cultural phenomenon?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language and culture. It is a good thing for compatriots on both sides to increase mutual understanding and exchanges through all kinds of channels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","We note that Kaohsiung will hold a Harbor Cities Forum in September this year. Chen Chu said that if the mainland is willing, she is ready to lead a delegation to the mainland to invite some harbor cities, such as Xiamen and Tianjin. What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. Only with a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations can normal exchanges between the two sides be facilitated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160615_11483731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter's question about discriminatory treatment that mainland spouses encounter in Taiwan, State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan stated at the regular press conference on June 15: The fact that mainland spouses encounter discriminatory treatment in Taiwan, with their lawful rights and interests unprotected and this problem long unresolved, I believe everyone is very clear about the obstacles involved. The DPP, disregarding the lawful rights and interests of cross-Strait marriages and families, has repeatedly obstructed them for political purposes, which is not supported by the public. Mainland spouses are also family members of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the Taiwan side can adjust and amend these outdated discriminatory provisions as soon as possible, and genuinely address the reasonable demands of mainland spouses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483763.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-15","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question: At the opening ceremony of the Straits Forum, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng mentioned that the mainland attaches great importance to the proposals put forward by Taiwan compatriots for more convenient travel on the mainland, and that implementing measures will be issued as soon as possible in the near future. What specific measures will there be?","An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the regular press conference on June 15 in response to questions that we attach great importance to the suggestion from Taiwan compatriots that travel on the mainland be made more convenient. We understand that the civil aviation authorities have equipped nearly 1,000 self-service check-in and ticketing kiosks capable of reading Taiwan Compatriot Permits at 34 airports with high concentrations of Taiwan compatriot traffic, including Beijing, Shanghai, and Guangzhou. Meanwhile, the railway authorities are also working to resolve the issue of enabling self-service ticket purchase and collection with card-type Taiwan Compatriot Permits. In addition, relevant departments will continue to study adding ports of entry where a one-time-valid Taiwan Compatriot Permit can be issued on arrival.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160615_11483767.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-06-20","Hua Chunying","","First, Indonesian Vice President said that Indonesia is determined to assert its exclusive right to the Natuna Islands where there has been a run of skirmishes between Indonesian navy ships and Chinese fishing vessels. Have you noticed these remarks? Second, the Cambodian police plans to repatriate all the 27 telecom fraud suspects from the mainland and Taiwan based on the \"one China\" policy. Do you know the…","We have stated our position over the weekend on Indonesian navy vessels harassing and shooting Chinese fishing boats and fishermen. This took place in waters which are Chinese fishermen's traditional fishing grounds and where China and Indonesia have overlapping claims for maritime rights and interests. The Indonesian vessels that harassed and shot Chinese fishing boats with a willful resort to force put the life and property of Chinese fishermen in danger and violated international laws including UNCLOS and the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea (DOC). China strongly protests and condemns the abuse of force. China urges the Indonesian side to stop taking actions that complicate, exacerbate the dispute and undermine regional peace and stability, and handle the fishery issue at sea in a constructive way.\nChina has no territorial sovereignty dispute with Indonesia. Yet the two countries have overlapping claims for maritime rights and interests over some part of the South China Sea. The two sides have normal communication channels, and it is hoped that they will step up communication in a friendly and constructive way and properly settle relevant issue.\nOn your second question, we commend the Cambodian side for handling relevant issue based on the \"one China\" principle. You may ask competent authorities for the specifics of this case and the communication across the Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1373744.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1373583.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-06-24","Hua Chunying","","The Cambodian government will deport over 20 telecom fraud suspects from the mainland and Taiwan to China today. Will China appreciate that?","We have noted the statement by the Cambodian side which says that it will handle the relevant issue in accordance with the one-China principle. We hereby express our appreciation. The relevant department of China will work and communicate closely with its Cambodian counterpart to properly address this issue, and safeguard the rights and interests of victims in the telecom fraud cases.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1375206.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1375085.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-06-25","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 25 (reporter Zha Wenye) — In response to the Taiwan side's Mainland Affairs Council stating that it has lodged a protest through cross-Strait communication channels over Cambodia's deportation of Taiwan telecom fraud suspects to the mainland, An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 25th in response to questions that after May 20, because the Taiwan side has failed to confirm the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle as the common political foundation, the cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms have been suspended.\nAn Fengshan said that cracking down on telecom fraud crimes in accordance with the law and protecting the rights and interests of victims is a matter of course, and it enjoys the support of the broad masses of people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160625_11491242.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-06-28","Hong Lei","","台湾当局领导人在参观巴拿马运河时，在留言簿上署名自称“President of TAIWAN（ROC）”，意为“台湾（中华民国）总统”。你对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1375871.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","新华社记者","We noted that the spokesperson stated in response to a question on June 25 that “the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms have come to a standstill.” Could the spokesperson explain what caused this situation?","“Cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms” refer to the regularized liaison and communication mechanism established between the Taiwan Affairs Office (TAO) and Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council (MAC), and the consultation and negotiation mechanism established between the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and Taiwan’s Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF).\nAs everyone knows, the fruitful achievements of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations since 2008 did not fall from the sky. The liaison and communication mechanism between the TAO and the MAC, and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between ARATS and SEF, were both built on the political foundation that both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus.”\nHere, I would like to share some specific facts. On May 26, 2008, SEF sent a letter to ARATS stating that it “hopes that both associations can resume institutionalized consultations as soon as possible on the basis of the ‘1992 Consensus.’” After receiving the letter, on May 29, ARATS replied to SEF, stating that “our association agrees with the views in your association’s letter and will resume exchanges and consultations and negotiations between the two associations as soon as possible on the basis of the ‘1992 Consensus.’” The correspondence between the two sides is black and white, and clearly on record. It was on this basis that on June 12, the two sides resumed the cross-Strait talks between the two associations, which had been suspended for nearly ten years. Over the following eight years, these led to 11 rounds of talks and 23 agreements between the two associations.\nIn February 2014, the heads of the TAO and the MAC met in Nanjing and decided to establish a regularized liaison and communication mechanism between the two agencies on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” At the meeting, Director Zhang Zhijun specifically stressed that the “1992 Consensus” is the basis of the regularized liaison and communication mechanism between the two agencies; without this basis, the mechanism could not have been established; and even if it had been established, if the basis were undermined, the mechanism would collapse. In a press release issued on February 11, the MAC also clearly stated: “The MAC stresses that the ‘1992 Consensus’ is the key core of cross-Strait institutionalized consultation and interaction.” Afterward, the heads of the two agencies met and visited each other many times, and both sides emphasized that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for continuing to advance cross-Strait relations.\nThese facts are sufficient to show that the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and the basis and prerequisite on which cross-Strait institutionalized liaison mechanisms were established. I want to stress that the mainland’s position of advancing institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges on this basis and safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has never changed, and its attitude has always been consistent. What has changed this situation is the Taiwan side. The new ruling authorities in Taiwan have so far not acknowledged the “1992 Consensus” or identified with its core meaning. This has undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait interaction and led to the suspension of the liaison and communication mechanism between the TAO and the MAC, and of the consultation and negotiation mechanism between ARATS and SEF. The responsibility lies entirely with the Taiwan side. People cannot help but ask: why does the Taiwan side want to change the status quo of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations that has existed since 2008? What is its purpose?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160629_11495074.htm"],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","厦门卫视记者","Around this year’s May 20, the Taiwan side has repeatedly stated that it respects the historical fact that the two associations reached certain common understandings and tacit understandings through consultation in 1992. The key point of this historical fact is “seeking common ground while shelving differences.” Why can the mainland not accept this expression?","The Taiwan side has consistently taken an ambiguous attitude on the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations, which compatriots on both sides care about most, and has not explicitly acknowledged the “1992 Consensus” and its core meaning. For some time, compatriots on both sides have been asking: the Taiwan side says it respects the common understandings and tacit agreements reached through consultations between the two associations in 1992. What exactly are these so-called “common understandings”? The key to this historical fact lies in “seeking common ground while shelving differences”; what is the “common” in “seeking common ground”? The Taiwan side should explain these points clearly and make them plain. Only when clear and correct statements are made about the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations and the basis for their development can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160629_11495073.htm"],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","中新社记者","According to reports, Raymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan, currently said that the mainland’s decision to suspend or halt exchanges and communication with Taiwan is an “unfortunate” matter. He also mentioned the “1992 Understanding” that Koo Chen-fu once spoke of, and considers whether to use “1992 Understanding” or “1992 Consensus” to be a question that both sides of the Strait must…","The “1992 Consensus” is the consensus reached in 1992 between the Mainland's ARATS and Taiwan's SEF on how to express “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” The SEF's expression was: “In the process of working together to seek national unification across the Taiwan Strait, while both sides adhere to the one-China principle, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.” ARATS' expression was: Both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive to seek national unification. However, in the consultations on cross-Strait affairs, the political meaning of one China is not involved.” Thus, both sides at that time expressed the position that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” Its basic facts and entire process are very clear and beyond doubt.\nIt is precisely because of the fact that consensus was reached in 1992 that the 1993 Koo-Wang talks took place. Everyone can look at the “Record of the Koo-Wang Talks” published by the SEF at that time. After 2000, Mr. Koo Chen-fu repeatedly stated that the historical significance of the “1992 Consensus” should be taken seriously. This is also a historical fact that no one can deny or distort.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160629_11495072.htm"],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台","I have two questions. The first concerns the “1992 Consensus.” The new authorities on the Taiwan side may hope that, after the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) installs a new board of directors, the SEF will recognize the “1992 Consensus” in order to communicate with the mainland side. Will the mainland side accept this? The second question: when Tsai Ing-wen was active in Panama, she signed her name in English…","Your first question, regarding the choice of chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, I already answered at the last press conference. Our position and sincerity in promoting cross-Strait consultations and negotiations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” have not changed. Whether the consultation and contact mechanism between the two bodies can be maintained depends crucially on whether the SEF can obtain authorization to confirm to ARATS its adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle.\nYour second question: we have consistently handled Taiwan’s external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose any act attempting to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international arena.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","The spokesperson just said that the “cross-Strait communication and liaison mechanism has come to a standstill.” Will the Taipei-Shanghai Twin City Forum and this year's KMT-CPC Forum be affected? When will they be held?","The political foundation and good situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations should be cherished and maintained. As for the Shanghai-Taipei “Twin City Forum” you mentioned, communication should be conducted between the Shanghai and Taipei municipal authorities. As for the operation of the KMT-CPC exchange platform, both sides have been actively communicating.\nTaiwan's “Want Daily” reporter: The ARATS-SEF liaison mechanism has been suspended, but the interaction between the two “small associations,” the Mainland's Association for Relations across the Taiwan Strait tourism exchanges (SHTA) and the Taiwan Strait Tourism Association (TSTA), remains to be observed. Will the Mainland's SHTA send representatives to the tourism forum to be held in Hualien in mid-August?\nWe have stated many times that the fruitful results of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008 were all achieved on the basis that both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus.” Only by confirming the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle can the institutionalized exchange results across the Strait be kept unaffected. We will also continue to work to safeguard the rights and interests of people on both sides in exchanges and interactions, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. As for the specific question you asked, I suggest consulting the competent tourism authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者提问","Continuing the previous question: the TAO has for the first time confirmed that the cross-Strait communication mechanism has stalled. However, the MAC recently said it hopes both sides can open the door to dialogue on jointly combating crime, and that political factors should not be used to obstruct cross-Strait cooperation on combating crime. What is the spokesperson’s response?","Regarding the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanism, I have already answered very clearly. As for the cross-Strait joint crime-fighting cooperation mechanism: on the 24th, regarding Cambodia’s repatriation to the mainland of some cross-Strait telecom fraud suspects, the mainland public security authorities have already issued a press release, and the TAO spokesperson has also made a statement on this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","First question: Regarding Tsai Ing-wen's performance over the more than one month since she took office, some scholars on the island analyze that externally, Tsai is playing a “humiliation card,” and domestically she is implementing “Taiwan independence” internal policies, and that Tsai's cross-Strait policy is “anti-China while slowing independence.” May I ask the spokesperson for his comment? Second question:…","On your first question: to ensure the institutionalized cross-Strait exchange mechanisms and the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, it is necessary to affirm the political foundation embodying the one-China principle. On this fundamental issue, using double-dealing tactics or adopting an ambiguous attitude in language and wording would be of no help.\nOn your second question, the international community has already reached clear conclusions regarding that period of history of World War II. The people of Taiwan were also victims of the aggressive war waged by Japanese militarism at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Recently some people on the Taiwan side have proposed that the KMT and CPC first sign a peace agreement. I don't know if this is feasible?","Since 2005, the KMT and the CPC, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have, together with compatriots on both sides of the Strait, opened a new chapter of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations and promoted a series of important achievements. Regarding the long-standing political differences between the two sides, we have repeatedly stated clearly that we are willing to consult with the Taiwan side on the basis of the one-China principle to explore solutions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","中国日报记者","Some media have reported that when Tsai Ing-wen visited Panama, Panamanian President Mr. Varela first wrote “China (Taiwan)” on Facebook, and later revised it to “Republic of China (Taiwan).” Is the spokesperson aware of this? What is the mainland's response?","The mainland has always handled Taiwan's external exchanges in accordance with the One-China Principle. We firmly oppose any force that engages in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally, or that promotes “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","The Taiwan legislature recently scheduled the review of draft amendments, including the “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area,” and gave preliminary approval to the version of the DPP's amendment motion. The years required for mainland spouses to obtain ID cards remain unchanged at six, and they are additionally required to possess “basic knowledge of civic rights…","Mainland spouses in Taiwan face discriminatory treatment, and their lawful rights and interests are not protected, and this has long gone unresolved. Where the obstacles lie, I believe everyone will see more clearly through this matter. Such practices are not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Who will head the Straits Exchange Foundation in Taiwan has been a constant topic. Wang Jin-pyng, James Soong, Hsu Hsin-liang and others have been mentioned successively. There is also news saying that “Wang Jin-pyng is on Beijing's blacklist.” May I ask the spokesperson for comment? How does the mainland side view the role the Straits Exchange Foundation needs to play under DPP rule?","I will not comment on specific candidates. If the achievements of institutionalized cross-strait exchanges are to be secured, the Straits Exchange Foundation needs authorization to confirm to the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201606/t20160629_11495077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter's question about the current interaction between the cross-Strait industry “mini-associations,” State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan stated at the regular press conference on June 29: As we have said many times, the fruitful results of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008 were all achieved on the basis of both sides adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” Only by affirming the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle can the results of institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges be ensured. We will also continue to work to safeguard the rights and interests of cross-Strait residents in exchanges and interaction, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160629_11495070.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-06-29","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Regarding reporters’ questions about Tsai Ing-wen’s recent activities in Panama, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, at the regular press conference on June 29, responded to questions by saying that we have consistently treated Taiwan’s external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose any conduct that attempts to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” internationally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201606/t20160629_11495071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2016-06-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Freedom Times of Taiwan, the Taiwan military has announced a plan to build 12 naval ships and the timing is from 2018 to 2040 with a total budget of 470 billion New Taiwan dollars or about 15 billion US dollars. What is the comment from the mainland?","To recognize the 1992 Consensus and maintain peaceful development of cross-strait relations is conducive to peace and stability cross the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan independence secessionist forces and their activities are the gravest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan side should do more to improve and develop cross-strait relations.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2016-06/30/content_4685792.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-06-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, a news report from the PLA Daily said that a motorized infantry brigade of the 1st Group Army under the PLA Eastern Theatre Command has been reformed and upgraded to a new rapid-response combat force with wings. It is commented by Hong Kong media that this is aiming at deterring the “Taiwan independence” forces. What is your comment?","It is a sacred mission for the Chinese PLA to safeguard the sovereignty and territorial integrity of the country. To report on the efforts to strengthen the national defense and armed forces building is quite a normal phenomenon.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/Press/2016-06/30/content_4685792.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2016-07-05","Hong Lei","","Taiwan’s department dealing with foreign affairs said on July 4 that Taiwan has prepared for various scenarios of the South China Sea arbitration case and will look into the ruling after it comes out. But Taiwan will not make any compromise. What’s your response?","The Chinese people across the Taiwan Strait should make concerted efforts to uphold the common rights and interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1377843.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1377677.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-07-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","BEIJING, July 6 (Xinhua) (Reporter Zha Wenye) Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang told reporters on the 6th that in recent days, some southern provinces have suffered severe floods and other natural disasters, and the Kuomintang and people from all walks of life in Taiwan have expressed concern and condolences through various channels. We express our gratitude for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160707_11501261.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-07-07","Hong Lei","","According to media reports, during Tsai Ing-wen’s transit stop in the US, she got in touch with US congressmen in different ways and talked to US government officials and congress leaders on the phone. What’s your comment?","We consistently handle Taiwan’s engagement with foreign countries following the one-China principle, and firmly oppose any official exchange or contact between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. We are strongly dissatisfied with and strongly opposed to the US government officials and congressmen having contact with Tsai Ing-wen, and have lodged solemn representations with the US side. We urge the US to abide by the one-China policy and the three China-US joint communiques and honor its commitment of opposing “Taiwan independence”, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, and stop having any official contact with Taiwan or sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” forces so as not to compromise China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1378321.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1378307.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-07-08","Hong Lei","","The US Senate passed a bill on July 6 reaffirming that the Taiwan Relations Act and the six assurances are the bedrock of Taiwan-US relations. The US House of Representatives had also approved relevant bills in May. What’s your comment?","Taiwan affairs fall entirely within China’s domestic affairs. By unilaterally enacting the “Taiwan Relations Act” and offering relevant “assurances” to Taiwan, the US has interfered in China’s domestic affairs in severe breach of the one-China policy and the three joint communiques between China and the US. We are firmly opposed to the passing of relevant bills by the US senate and the house of representatives. We demand the US side adhere to the one-China policy, the three China-US joint communiques and its commitment of opposing “Taiwan independence”, rescind relevant bills immediately, maintain the China-US relations with concrete efforts and not send any wrong signal to the separatist forces touting “Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1378753.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1378698.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-07-08","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 8 (reporter Zha Wenye): Typhoon Nepartak, the first typhoon of this year, made landfall in Taiwan on the morning of the 8th, causing casualties and property losses in eastern and south-central Taiwan. In response, a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said: We are deeply concerned about the disaster suffered in Taiwan, and we extend our condolences to the affected people. We sincerely hope that the affected people will soon restore normal production and living order.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160708_11503806.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-07-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Taiwan authorities issued a statement on the South China Sea arbitration case, expressing a position of absolute non-acceptance. What is the TAO’s response?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 12 (reporter Qi Xianghui): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 12th in response to questions that compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a responsibility to jointly safeguard the territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in the South China Sea, and to jointly safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Ma Xiaoguang said that the Chinese government and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have already issued statements expressing the relevant positions. I want to emphasize that compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a responsibility to jointly safeguard the territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in the South China Sea, and to jointly safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160712_11506775.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-07-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 19 (reporter Zha Wenye) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th that at noon today, a mainland tour group organized by Liaoning Overseas International Travel Agency Co., Ltd. was involved in a serious traffic accident and fire in Taoyuan, Taiwan, a major accident that killed 24 mainland tourists, along with the tour guide and driver, for a total of 26 deaths.\nUpon receiving the news, the Taiwan Affairs Office immediately activated the emergency response mechanism for cross-Strait emergencies. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan, as well as the Cross-Strait Tourism Exchange Association and the Taiwan Straits Cross-Strait Tourism Association, urgently contacted each other to understand and verify the situation, and required the relevant Taiwan authorities to fully handle the matter, investigate the cause of the accident, properly handle the aftermath, strengthen safety management, and prevent further safety accidents. We are highly concerned about the life and property safety of mainland compatriots, and relevant departments will send a working group to Taiwan to assist the families in handling the aftermath.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160719_11513262.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-07-20","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 20 (reporters Zha Wenye and Qi Xianghui). In response to questions on the 20th, a spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office said that after a major vehicle fire accident occurred in Taiwan on July 19, Premier Li Keqiang gave an important instruction requiring the Taiwan Affairs Office, the National Tourism Administration and other departments to quickly understand the situation and properly handle the aftermath. The Taiwan Affairs Office, the National Tourism Administration, the Liaoning Provincial Government and other relevant parties activated emergency response mechanisms at the first opportunity. In accordance with the instructions of the central leadership, they verified the situation, contacted and notified family members, activated emergency contact windows to maintain communication with Taiwan, and quickly organized a working group to travel to Taiwan. At present, the working group led by the Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Association for Tourism Exchanges departed at noon on the 20th, and the Liaoning Provincial working group will also arrive in Taiwan in the evening. Arrangements for family members to travel to Taiwan are also under way. We will work closely with the relevant departments and the working group in the field to keep in close contact and do our utmost to properly handle all aftermath matters.\nThe spokesperson said that we deeply regret the large number of deaths caused by this accident. The relevant authorities in Taiwan should quickly find out the cause and responsibility of the accident, properly handle follow-up matters, and safeguard the rights and interests of the victims' families. They should take effective measures to strengthen safety management, eliminate safety hazards, and ensure the safety of life and property of tourists traveling to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160720_11514382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-07-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 22 (reporters Liu Huan and Qi Xianghui). In response to statements by Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan authorities, on the “1992 Consensus” and cross-Strait communication channels in an interview with the U.S. newspaper The Washington Post, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on July 22 that safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the mainstream public opinion in both societies across the Strait. Only by adhering to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and its core meaning that both sides belong to one China can the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations be ensured.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the liaison and communication mechanism between the Taiwan Affairs Office and Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between ARATS and SEF, were both established on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only by confirming a political foundation that embodies the one-China principle can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160722_11516637.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2016-07-28","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","General Fan Changlong, vice chairman of China’s Central Military Commission, said when meeting with U.S. National Security Adviser Susan Rice that the Chinese military will act as a staunch pillar for safeguarding national territorial sovereignty and security. Admiral Wu Shengli, commander of the PLA Navy, also stressed that the sovereignty, rights and interests in the South China Sea are China’s core interests…","On the first question, China has sovereignty over the islands and reefs of the South China Sea and their adjacent waters. It is the sure responsibility of the Chinese military to safeguard the national sovereignty security, territorial integrity as well as maritime interests and rights.\nOn the South China Sea Air Defense Identification Zone (ADIZ), we have reiterated our position on numerous occasions that it is within the sovereign rights of a country to establish the ADIZ. As to whether or when to establish such a zone, it depends on whether China is facing security threats from the air, and it also depends on the level of the threat.\nOn the Huangyan Island, the Huangyan Island is an inherent territory of China. China has the right to take measures to safeguard its sovereignty and security, and deal with various threats.\nOn the second question about the Military Court’s verdict on the Guo Boxiong case, the trial of the Guo Boxiong case in accordance with law fully demonstrates the firm resolve of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping as the General Secretary to administer the military according to law and enforce strict discipline. It also demonstrates the strong will of the Party Central Committee and the Central Military Commission to punish corruption. The handling of the case has been given a positive response among the rank and file, and is of great significance for deterring corrupt behavior, boosting morale, and protecting the image of the armed forces.\nThe trial and sentencing of Guo Boxiong has again demonstrated that there will be no place for corrupt individuals in the military, and no Party member is above the law or Party discipline. Cases of corruption in the military, whoever is involved , regardless of his or her rank, will be dealt with without toleration.\nOn the question concerning the Taiping Island, China enjoys sovereignty over the islands and reefs of the South China Sea and their adjacent waters. It is the common responsibility of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits to safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2016-07/28/content_4703118.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2016-07-29","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 29 dispatch (reporter Zhao Bo): TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said on the 29th that the relevant Taiwan authorities today released the latest investigation findings on the “7·19” major vehicle fire accident, and we are highly concerned about it.\nAn Fengshan said that after this major accident occurred, we repeatedly asked the relevant Taiwan authorities to quickly establish the cause and responsibility of the accident, in order to console the victims and their families. Today, the Cross-Strait Tourism Association again expressed serious concern through the Taiwan Tourism Association, demanding that the Taiwan side promptly report on the progress of the accident investigation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201607/t20160729_11523638.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-08-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Relevant Taiwan authorities have publicly written to the President of the ICAO Council, requesting to attend the 39th ICAO Assembly. What is the mainland's attitude on this?","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on August 4: Our position on Taiwan's participation in international organizations and activities is clear and consistent: it must be arranged through cross-Strait consultations under the one-China principle. Since 2008, on the political foundation of both sides of the Strait upholding the “1992 Consensus,” against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and without creating “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan,” the mainland side has, through cross-Strait consultations, made special and pragmatic arrangements for Taiwan's participation in international organizations and activities.\nBecause the new Taiwan authorities have so far not acknowledged the “1992 Consensus” or endorsed its core meaning, the cross-Strait communication and liaison mechanisms have stalled, and the responsibility lies entirely with the Taiwan side. Only by confirming the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges continue, and only then will it be possible for the two sides to consult on Taiwan's participation in international organization activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201608/t20160804_11529014.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-08-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The Taiwan authorities’ Mainland Affairs Council said it has, through cross-Strait communication channels, lodged a protest with the mainland over the return of five Taiwan telecom fraud suspects from Kenya to the mainland. Please confirm. Ma Xiaoguang responded: The 40 telecom fraud suspects handed over by Kenya this time, including five Taiwan residents, belong to the same case as the 36 people repatriated in…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 8 (reporter Zhao Bo). In response to the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan's statement that it has lodged a protest with the mainland side through cross-Strait communication channels over the escort back to mainland China of five Taiwanese telecom fraud suspects from Kenya, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 8th in response to a question that cracking down on telecom fraud in accordance with the law enjoys the support of the public on both sides; the Taiwan side should make concrete efforts to restore the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms.\nMa Xiaoguang said that regarding the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms, we have stated on many occasions that because the Taiwan authorities have failed to confirm the “1992 Consensus,” the common political foundation embodying the one-China principle, the liaison, communication and negotiation mechanisms between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, and between ARATS and SEF, have come to a standstill. The Taiwan side should face this fact and make concrete efforts to restore the operation of these mechanisms.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201608/t20160808_11531895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-08-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 12 (reporter Liu Huan): In response to the announcement by Shanghai and Taipei that they will hold a “Twin City Forum” in late August, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 12th in response to questions: “We have said many times that upholding the ‘1992 Consensus,’ which embodies the one-China principle, as the political foundation is what allows cross-Strait relations of peaceful development to be maintained. As long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and cross-Strait city exchanges, we hold a positive and open attitude toward cross-Strait city exchanges.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201608/t20160812_11536263.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-08-22","Lu Kang","","Taiwan UN Alliance President and former head of Taiwan's defense authorities Michael Tsai reportedly urged Tsai Ing-wen to write to UN Secretary-General Ban Ki-moon and ask for Taiwan's participation in the UN as a new \"member state\". The official in charge of Taiwan's foreign affairs responded on August 18 that the Taiwan authorities will continue to push for meaningful participation at UN-related agencies but…","As we all know, the UN is an inter-governmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Only sovereign states can apply for UN membership. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. It has been recognized by the international community. The government and people of China are firmly opposed to any form of \"Taiwan independence\". Any attempt to challenge the one-China principle, and create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will not prevail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1390779.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1390695.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-08-25","Lu Kang","","A Taiwan leader will go to the Vatican next month. I am wondering if China has lodged a protest with the Vatican or potentially with Italy? Secondly, Donald Trump has once again threatened that he would hit China with tariff and trade cases if he's elected US president. Do you have a response to that?","On your first question, the one-China principle is widely recognized by the international community. It is our long-standing stance in dealing with Taiwan's interaction with foreign countries. We hope that the relevant country will handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence.\nOn your second question, it is our opinion that the positive, stable and sound relationship, especially the mutually beneficial cooperation between China and the US in trade has brought enormous benefits to people from both sides. We believe that the future leader of the US, whoever it will be, will continue to take mutually beneficial cooperation as their basic policy toward China in the interests of the US and its people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1391901.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1391785.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2016-08-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The decision by Indian government to deploy the Brahmos supersonic cruise missile along the China-India border may pose security threats to heartland of China, including the Yunnan Province and the Tibet Autonomous Region. What kind of counter-measures will the Chinese military have?\nDuring the Han Kuang Exercise conducted by the military of Taiwan, there are video clips showing the simulated confrontational…","I have already responded to your first question.\nOn the basis of the 1992 Consensus, maintaining peaceful development of cross-strait relations is the fundamental guarantee for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan independence secessionist forces and their activities are the gravest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nAfter the press conference, the spokesperson responded to a question concerning the Chinese side providing personnel training to Syria. This year, the Chinese military will provide medical and nursing training to the Syrian side in China.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2016-08/25/content_4719535.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2016-09-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 6 (reporter Qi Xianghui): The film “Love Crab Encounter,” a movie based on real-life cross-strait exchange activities, held its premiere on the 6th at the National Committee Hall of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference in Beijing.\n“Love Crab Encounter” is drawn from a real story that occurred during Shanghai Ocean University’s efforts to help Miaoli County, Taiwan, raise hairy crabs. Since 2011, Shanghai Ocean University has organized 16 batches of scientific and technical expert teams to be stationed in Miaoli to provide technical guidance, successfully establishing the “Miaoli model” suited to raising hairy crabs in Taiwan. Over four years, Shanghai provided more than 1.6 million high-quality crab fry to Miaoli. The number of crab-farming households in Miaoli reached 103, with a crab-farming water area of 450 hectares, and the cumulative output value exceeded NT$300 million, while boosting Miaoli County’s tourism revenue by more than NT$200 million.\nShanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office Director Li Wenhui gave a speech, saying that “Love Crab Encounter” is a beautiful wave that has surged forth since 2008 amid the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and the great tide of cross-strait exchange. He expressed the hope that the film’s release will enhance understanding and trust between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and create more “fate” (yuan).\nMa Xiaoguang, Director of the Information Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that “Love Crab Encounter” is a feature film based on cross-strait exchange activities. It is a beneficial attempt to reflect, through film, young people across the Taiwan Strait exchanging and cooperating and communicating from the heart, together gaining a good career and love. He expressed the hope that more people will pay attention to the wonderful cross-strait stories and to the lives of young people across the Strait.\nAt the premiere, the film’s creative team and main actors talked about their creative experiences and about the experiences of performers on both sides of the Strait working together with one heart and encouraging one another during filming.\nIt is reported that the film will be released to the public starting September 15.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160907_11561954.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-10","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","This afternoon, relevant parties in Taiwan announced the investigation results of the “7.19” tour bus fire incident. A spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said: We strongly condemn this deliberately created, vicious criminal case, and express strong indignation at such conduct, which is utterly devoid of conscience and humanity.\nSince the “7.19” incident occurred, we have repeatedly stated our position on how it should be handled, demanding that relevant parties in Taiwan thoroughly investigate the causes and responsibility of the accident and give an account to the victims and their families. This vicious incident, as well as some words and deeds on the island that have harmed the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, have seriously affected mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan.\nGoing forward, relevant mainland authorities will continue to urge the Taiwan side to properly handle follow-up matters such as compensation, and will fully assist the families in handling related affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160910_11565756.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The DPP has been in power for more than 100 days. How do you comment on the DPP authorities' mainland policy and on the development of cross-Strait relations now and in the future?","Since May 20 of this year, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" and do not recognize that both sides belong to one China. They have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation across the Strait, causing the institutionalized cross-Strait exchange mechanisms to stall and severely impacting the good momentum and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations that had continued for eight years. Compatriots on both sides, especially the Taiwan public, are worried about the prospects for cross-Strait relations.\nCompatriots on both sides are one family, a community of shared destiny linked by blood. We must grasp the future of cross-Strait relations by recognizing the trend of historical development. Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to maintain peace across the Strait, promote common development, and benefit compatriots on both sides. Adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and to the common political foundation embodying the one-China principle, and continuing on the correct path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, best accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides. \"Taiwan independence\" has no way out; any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct will certainly meet firm opposition from all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation and will inevitably end in complete failure. On the issue of upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, our will is as firm as a rock, and our attitude has always been consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160914_11570149.htm"],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said in Kinmen that without the Kinmen-Xiamen “Small Three Links” there would be no cross-Strait exchanges today. She called on both sides, starting from the historical experience of the “Small Three Links,” to uphold peaceful cross-Strait exchanges, shelve disputes, seek common ground while setting aside differences, interact in good faith, and pursue greater well-being for the people on…","“Small Three Links” refers only to exchanges between Kinmen, Matsu, and the coastal areas of Fujian. Those familiar with this history are well aware that the DPP authorities at the time agreed to open them only under strong appeals from the Taiwan public and active advocacy by figures from Kinmen and Matsu, and under pressure. Genuine mutual trust and constructive dialogue between the two sides, and the realization of comprehensive, direct, two-way “Three Links” across the Strait, came only after 2008, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Historical facts have fully demonstrated that only by upholding the “1992 Consensus” as the political foundation and endorsing its core meaning that both sides belong to one China can we genuinely set disputes aside, seek common ground while reserving differences, engage in constructive dialogue and good-faith interaction, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Recently, some political forces on the island have been agitating for Taiwan to join the United Nations. What attitude does the mainland take on this?","The United Nations is an international organization composed of sovereign states and adheres to the one-China policy. Taiwan is part of China. Before 2008, Lee Teng-hui and Chen Shui-bian manipulated “UN entry” and “UN entry referendums,” and both failed; the historical lesson is not distant. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces attempting to make an issue of the UN question in order to challenge the one-China policy that the international community generally adheres to will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160914_11570147.htm"],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Recently, the number of mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan has dropped sharply. On the 12th of this month, Taiwan tourism industry representatives held a large demonstration, expressing their concerns and demands to the Taiwan authorities. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","As is well known, mainland residents’ tourism to Taiwan showed a good momentum of development in past years. Since May this year, the Taiwan authorities’ refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” has damaged the hard-won situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and the effects have been felt in many respects. The recent decline in mainland residents’ travel to Taiwan is one reflection of this. We noted that Taiwan’s tourism industry recently took to the streets to clearly express their voices and wishes. The root of the damage to the interests of Taiwan’s tourism-related industries is clear to everyone: only the one who tied the bell can untie it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","After the DPP took office, the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan did indeed drop sharply. The Taiwan Tourism Association has already gone to large mainland cities such as Nanjing to attract mainland tourists to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second question: Tsai Ing-wen invited James Soong to attend this year's APEC leaders' meeting, and reports say the mainland side has vetoed it. Could…","First question: Regarding the decline in the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan and the damage to the interests of Taiwan's tourism-related businesses, we have already stated our position. Clearly, relying on so-called “promotion” cannot solve the fundamental problem. As we have said before, only the one who tied the bell can untie it.\nSecond question: Taiwan-side personnel attending APEC-related events should comply with the provisions of the relevant memorandum of understanding of APCE.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社中评网记者","Reports indicate that recently, the New Power Party and DPP legislators have invited the Dalai Lama to visit Taiwan, and claimed they would arrange for him to deliver a speech at the Legislative Yuan. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","As everyone knows, the Dalai Lama has long used a religious cloak to carry out activities aimed at splitting the country. We firmly oppose any form of activity by the Dalai Lama in Taiwan. Some forces in Taiwan intend to collude with “Tibet independence” forces and deliberately create incidents, which will inevitably have a serious impact on cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160914_11570140.htm"],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress recently adopted amendments to the Law on the Protection of Investments by Taiwan Compatriots. What impact will this have on Taiwan businesspeople investing in the mainland? In addition, will the Investment Protection Law and its implementing rules be further amended in the future?","On September 3, the 22nd session of the 12th Standing Committee of the National People's Congress deliberated and adopted the amendment to the Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots. This amendment was a special revision carried out within the time limit and according to the requirements set by the decision of the NPC Standing Committee authorizing it. Under the relevant rules, approval items for the establishment and change of Taiwan-funded enterprises outside the negative list will be changed to filing-based management. In other words, Taiwan-funded enterprises will be subject to a management model of pre-establishment national treatment plus a negative list. This will create a fairer, more stable and more transparent legal environment for Taiwan investors. Once it takes effect, for Taiwan compatriots investing on the mainland, first, openness will be higher and the fields open to investment access will be broader. Taiwan-funded investment projects that do not involve the negative list will not require approval, and only filing will be needed to complete establishment and change procedures. Second, the degree of convenience will be greatly enhanced. Filing procedures will be substantially simplified, and processing times will be greatly shortened. As reform deepens, the Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots and its implementing rules will be further revised and improved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Feng Ming-chu, former director of the National Palace Museum in Taipei, was invited to serve as an adviser to the Beijing Palace Museum Research Institute. Some people claim she violated relevant Taiwan regulations and call for an investigation. What is your comment on this?","Clearly this is purely academic exchange. As we understand it, the Palace Museum Research Institute is a non-establishment institution set up by the Palace Museum for academic research and exchange. It brings together well-known experts and scholars at home and abroad to jointly build an open, high-end academic platform. We respect the willingness of cultural institutions and individuals on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to cooperate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","The International Civil Aviation Assembly is about to convene at the end of this month. The Mainland Affairs Council has previously stated that it hopes the two sides can consult jointly and hopes the mainland will show goodwill. What is the mainland's current attitude toward Taiwan's participation in the International Civil Aviation Assembly? Second question: The DPP has recently been actively pushing so-called…","First question: The premise for Taiwan’s participation in international organization activities is the one-China principle, with arrangements made through cross-Strait consultation. At present, the Taiwan authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, causing the cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms to stall and making relevant issues impossible to address.\nSecond question: Regarding the so-called issue of pursuing party assets, there are all kinds of comments on the island. We are closely following developments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan prosecutors announced the investigation results of the serious fire incident involving the Liaoning tour group. May I ask whether relevant compensation matters have been initiated? In addition, some public opinion on the island holds that this incident not only seriously impacted the island's tourism industry, but that the Taiwan authorities' various actions afterward were also intended to…","After the Taiwan side announced the results of the investigation into the \"7·19\" incident, we expressed our position at the first opportunity. Clearly, this is a heinous criminal case that is outrageous. This serious criminal case, together with certain words and deeds that have appeared on the island in recent times and harmed the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, has seriously affected mainland residents' travel to Taiwan. Going forward, we will continue to urge the relevant parties in Taiwan to properly handle compensation for the families of the victims, and to assist in handling other related follow-up matters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On September 12, the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan sent a letter to the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits notifying it of personnel changes, but the letter did not mention the “1992 Consensus.” How does the spokesperson evaluate this? When will there be new progress in the communication mechanism between the two cross-Strait associations, which is currently suspended?","Chairman Chen Deming already responded in writing that day. On September 12, ARATS did receive a letter from SEF. Clearly, there is no “secret password” in it, and people from all walks of life in Taiwan have expressed great disappointment. The “1992 Consensus” cannot be bypassed. Only if the Taiwan authorities formally authorize SEF to confirm to ARATS that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle, can the consultation and liaison mechanism between the two organizations continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","In an interview a few days ago, Director Zhang Zhijun of the Taiwan Affairs Office mentioned that this year's Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum will continue to be held, but there will be some new changes in form. I have two questions. First, roughly when and where will this year's forum be held? Second, what does the new form refer to?","First question: the platform operations of the KMT and the CPC, and exchanges and interactions at all levels, have played an important role in advancing relations between the two parties and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Under the new circumstances, this platform can continue to play a positive role in keeping cross-Strait relations on the right direction, so we attach great importance to it.\nAs for the specific manner of platform operations between the KMT and the CPC and related specific matters, both sides are still communicating, and we will release further news in a timely manner.\nSecond question: over the past more than ten years, the KMT-CPC exchange platform has united people from all walks of life on both sides, promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, continuously deepened its content, continuously enriched its connotations, and constantly innovated its forms. In the future it will further keep pace with the times, be closer to the Taiwan public, and better match the needs of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","Regarding Tsai Ing-wen’s May 20 inaugural speech, the TAO once said, “This is an unfinished answer sheet.” I would like to ask the spokesperson whether the mainland has set a deadline for this “answer sheet”?","I have already answered this. Where cross-strait relations will go and how they should proceed—whether to continue on the correct path of peaceful development of cross-strait relations, adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and benefiting the people on both sides, or the opposite—depends on the Taiwan authorities’ whim.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Yesterday, Tsai Ing-wen, in meeting Bo Ruiguang, chairman of the American Institute in Taiwan who is about to leave office, said that she thanked the United States for its continued arms sales to Taiwan over the years, that Taiwan is willing to continue to serve as a trustworthy security partner of the United States in the region, and looks forward to strengthening US-Taiwan military relations in the future. What…","We have always opposed external forces interfering in Taiwan affairs; this position is consistent and clear. We also advise the Taiwan authorities that the choice that truly safeguards peace in the Taiwan Strait and is truly beneficial to Taiwan's future is to return to the correct path of peaceful development of cross-strait relations. There is no other way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公报、大公网记者","The Kuomintang of China held its 19th National Congress on the 4th. Party Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu proposed deepening the “1992 Consensus” and promoting the signing of a cross-Strait peace agreement to end the state of hostility between the two sides. What is the mainland's response to this? Will the KMT and the CPC further communicate on related issues in the future?","As I just said, we are willing, on the common political foundation of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" to continue to maintain and develop inter-party exchanges with the KMT, jointly enhance mutual trust, and deepen exchanges and cooperation. On April 29, 2005, the leaders of the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang jointly issued the \"Common Vision for Peaceful Development of Cross-Strait Relations.\" This document proposed \"promoting the termination of hostilities between the two sides of the Strait and the conclusion of a peace agreement.\" Since then, we have repeatedly set out our position and proposals on many important occasions. Anything that benefits the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides and the Chinese nation should be vigorously promoted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160914_11570148.htm"],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","With the institutionalized cross-Strait consultation mechanism now at a standstill, will the implementation of the agreements already reached between the two associations be affected?","The current cross-Strait liaison and consultation mechanisms have come to a standstill, which has both prevented new cross-Strait agreements from being signed and inevitably affected the implementation of existing agreements. As I said just now, only the one who tied the bell can untie it. Only when the Straits Exchange Foundation is authorized to confirm with the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” the common political foundation embodying the one-China principle, can the liaison and consultation mechanisms authorized by the two bodies be continued.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","《团结报》记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office and the China Council for the Promotion of International Trade recently jointly issued the “Notice on Further Promoting the Use of Arbitration by Taiwan-Invested Enterprises to Resolve Economic and Trade Disputes.” Could you introduce this situation?","Everyone has already noted the related information we published on the website of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. I would like to make one further explanation here. Recently, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the China Council for the Promotion of International Trade jointly issued the “Notice on Further Promoting Taiwan-Invested Enterprises' Use of Arbitration to Resolve Economic and Trade Disputes,” requiring Taiwan Affairs Offices and Councils for the Promotion of International Trade at all levels to give full play to the role of arbitration in protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, proactively guide Taiwan-invested enterprises to strengthen contract awareness and arbitration awareness, and help Taiwan-invested enterprises use arbitration to protect their legitimate rights and interests according to law, so as to safeguard the stable development of cross-Strait economic and trade relations in accordance with the law. This is an important measure by the two departments to implement the spirit of comprehensively advancing the rule of law, to use the rule of law to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and to protect the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots according to law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","In a few days, several county magistrates and mayors from counties and cities governed by the KMT (the “Blue camp”) in Taiwan will visit Beijing. They hope the mainland side will allow mainland tourists to visit counties and cities that recognize the “1992 Consensus.” I would like to ask what the Taiwan Affairs Office thinks about this matter.","Our attitude and position are consistent. As long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of exchanges between cities on both sides, exchanges between the mainland and Taiwan's counties and cities can proceed smoothly.\nTomorrow is the Mid-Autumn Festival, a traditional Chinese festival. On behalf of the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, I extend festive greetings to everyone. May you have a happy Mid-Autumn Festival, a happy family life, and prosperity in your lives and careers. Thank you all!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160914_11570156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On September 17, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions: At the invitation of the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, a delegation of county and city heads from Taiwan, composed of the heads of New Taipei City, Hsinchu County, Miaoli County, Nantou County, Hualien County, Taitung County, Kinmen County, and Lienchiang County, visited Beijing today to discuss exchange and cooperation with the mainland in areas such as economy, culture, and tourism. It is understood that some members of the delegation will also visit and exchange views with other provinces and municipalities on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160917_11570578.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 18 (reporter Zhao Bo) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, told reporters on the 18th that the mainland side will adopt eight measures to promote exchanges with eight Taiwan counties and cities.\nMa Xiaoguang said that on the morning of the 18th, Zhang Zhijun, director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, held a discussion in Beijing with the Taiwan county and city heads delegation composed of eight counties and cities, namely New Taipei City, Hsinchu County, Miaoli County, Nantou County, Hualien County, Taitung County, Kinmen County and Lienchiang County, to exchange views on advancing cross-Strait county and city exchanges under the new situation. Zhang Zhijun said, “We will unwaveringly adhere to the political foundation of the ‘1992 Consensus,’ firmly oppose and curb ‘Taiwan independence,’ safeguard and continue to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continuously enhance the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.” We take a positive attitude toward mainland departments and cities strengthening exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan counties and cities that firmly support the ‘1992 Consensus’ and make efforts to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The eight Taiwan county and city heads said they would continue to adhere to the ‘1992 Consensus,’ work to maintain the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including cross-Strait county and city exchanges. They put forward suggestions on promoting exchanges between their counties and cities and the mainland. To this end, the mainland side will promote the following measures:\n1. Welcome and support the holding of agricultural specialty product exhibitions and promotion events by the eight Taiwan counties and cities on the mainland.\n2. Promote mainland enterprises to visit the eight Taiwan counties and cities to conduct inspections and negotiate procurement of agricultural specialty products.\n3. Welcome and support the eight Taiwan counties and cities in forming a tourism promotion alliance, jointly designing tourism products, establishing liaison channels with tourism authorities in various mainland localities, and holding tourism promotion events on the mainland.\n4. Actively promote mainland departments and cities to strengthen exchanges and cooperation with the eight Taiwan counties and cities in green industries, high-tech industries, smart cities and other fields.\n5. Encourage and support mainland departments and cities to actively strengthen cultural and humanities exchanges with the eight Taiwan counties and cities, and promote cross-Strait cultural and creative industry cooperation.\n6. Promote and expand communication between mainland departments and cities and youth in the eight Taiwan counties and cities, and provide convenience and create favorable conditions for Taiwan youth to intern, find jobs and start businesses on the mainland.\n7. Further expand the scale of economic, trade and personnel exchanges between coastal areas of Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu.\n8. Support mainland departments and localities in strengthening contacts with the eight Taiwan counties and cities, expanding exchanges, raising the level of cooperation, and solving practical problems of concern to the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160918_11571873.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-09-19","Lu Kang","","It is known that a Hong Kong citizen was killed in a car accident in Ireland. How will the Foreign Ministry help his families to bring his body back to Hong Kong?","I need to get more information on this case. As a principle and what we have been doing over the years, you may also know that for any overseas Chinese citizen, including those from Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan, if they are caught in an emergency and are in need of consular protection, assistance and service from the central government, they can always count on China's diplomatic missions overseas to deliver timely assistance and honor due responsibilities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1398638.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1398541.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-09-21","Lu Kang","","63 telecom fraud suspects including several from Taiwan were escorted from Cambodia back to China's mainland yesterday. Taiwan expressed regret over this. Do you have any comment?","It is not our remit to comment on the remarks made by Taiwan. You may ask the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for the official position.\nRegarding the specific case, the Chinese side highly applauds and appreciates Cambodia for sticking to the one-China policy and cooperating with China to crack down on cross-border crimes, including telecom fraud.\nThe Chinese Ministry of Public Security has released information on this case. Relevant authorities of China will deal with these suspects in accordance with law. This will help us crack the case, deliver an effective blow to crimes and protect the legitimate rights and interests of the victims. We believe this will be understood and supported by the Chinese people across the Strait and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1399373.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1399311.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-09-23","Lu Kang","","First, Taiwan was not invited to the assembly meeting of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) despite the fact that it attended such meeting in 2013. What is your comment? Second, according to a statement released by Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, the mainland may face serious consequences for its unilateral actions if it does not open dialogue with Taiwan. What is your response to that?","The first question is easy to answer. The ICAO and its arrangement of relevant meetings are all under the UN framework. As a specialized organ of the UN, the ICAO only allows sovereign states to participate in its events.\nAs we all know, as an integral part of China, Taiwan is not eligible to participate in such event. As we said earlier, the two sides once made certain temporary arrangement through consultation pursuant to the one-China principle, but such arrangement can not serve as a precedent. Regarding Taiwan’s participation in international events, we hold a clear stance that this can only be negotiated across the Strait based on the one-China principle.\nOn your second question, I would like to refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council as it falls out of the remit of foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1400068.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1400041.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-09-23","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to the Taiwan authorities’ protest over not receiving an invitation to this session of the International Civil Aviation Assembly, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to a question on September 23, said:\nOn Taiwan’s participation in international organization activities, our position is consistent and clear: in accordance with the one-China principle, the matter is to be handled through cross-Strait consultations. In 2013, Taiwan attended the 38th International Civil Aviation Assembly under the name “Chinese Taipei Civil Aviation Administration” as a guest of the President of the Council. This was an individual arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations, against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations maintained on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” It should also be pointed out that Taiwan has always had smooth channels for obtaining data and information on international aviation safety.\nSince the beginning of this year, major changes have taken place in the island’s political situation. To date, the DPP authorities have still refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, and caused the cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms to stall. As a result, Taiwan cannot attend. This situation was entirely caused by the DPP authorities.\nWhat the DPP authorities need to do is reflect on why Taiwan could attend three years ago but cannot now, rather than harshly criticizing the mainland and misleading the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160923_11577656.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Since May 20 this year, the Taiwan authorities have refused to accept the \"1992 Consensus\" on the one hand, while on the other hand repeatedly claiming that cross-Strait exchanges should not be subject to preconditions. What is your comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” and the one-China principle it embodies are objective facts consistent with the legal principles and reality of cross-Strait relations, not a premise artificially added. This consensus was reached by both sides through communication and consultation, seeking common ground while setting aside differences. It was not unilaterally imposed on Taiwan by us. When the two sides deal with each other, they must first clarify the nature of their relationship. The crux of so-called “no preconditions” is not acknowledging that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, that is, not abandoning the positions of the “two-state theory” and “one side, one country.” The DPP authorities’ unilateral undermining of the common political foundation across the Strait, in effect, imposes their denial of the consensus on the mainland. That is what actually sets preconditions for cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581729.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, a visiting delegation from Taiwan’s counties and cities came to the mainland. The mainland will adopt eight measures to promote exchanges and cooperation with these eight counties and cities. How will the spokesperson implement these measures going forward? Does this mean the mainland is adopting differentiated policies toward Taiwan’s blue and green camps? Thank you.","Not long ago, a delegation of county and city heads from Taiwan visited the mainland and stated that they would continue to support the “1992 Consensus.” We responded positively and proposed eight measures to further promote the strengthening of exchanges and cooperation between relevant mainland departments and cities and these eight counties and cities. Our determination and sincerity to advance exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait and to benefit compatriots on both sides will not change. As long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and county and city exchanges, and is willing to contribute to enhancing the well-being and kinship of compatriots on both sides, we all take a positive attitude.\nIt is understood that relevant parties on the mainland and in the eight Taiwan counties and cities are planning arrangements to hold a specialty agricultural products exhibition and tourism promotion event for the eight Taiwan counties and cities on the mainland within this year. Relevant mainland enterprises are also planning to visit the eight counties and cities to inspect and negotiate the procurement of agricultural products.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581727.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","央视记者","On October 10, Tsai Ing-wen will deliver her “Double Ten” speech. Some media analyze that in this speech, Tsai has failed to submit a qualified answer sheet on cross-Strait relations. How does the spokesperson respond?","Since May 20 of this year, the good momentum and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, which had lasted eight years, have been severely impacted, and the vital interests of Taiwan's people have been harmed. The crux of this situation and where responsibility lies are clear to everyone.\nPractice in both the positive and negative aspects of cross-Strait relations has proven that different path choices determine different prospects. The key to maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations lies in adhering to the “1992 Consensus” as its political foundation. Whatever the leader of the Taiwan authorities says, this hurdle cannot be bypassed.\nOur major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus” as the political foundation, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence,” firmly uphold the one-China principle, further expand exchanges and visits between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, advance exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and build a community of shared destiny across the Taiwan Strait. We believe that no force can stop the historical process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581730.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan and China's southeastern coastal regions have repeatedly been ravaged by typhoons. Can the spokesperson say whether the two sides can strengthen relevant cooperation on disaster reduction and prevention to address typhoons and other natural disasters?","Recently, several typhoons with strong destructive power have successively affected parts of both sides of the Strait, causing major losses of life and property to residents on both sides. We have been following this closely and extend our sincere condolences to the affected compatriots. As we understand it, during the impact of Typhoon “Nepartak” and Typhoon “Meranti” on Taiwan and the mainland this year, meteorological professionals on both sides communicated and exchanged information in real time through instant messaging software. We actively support anything that helps compatriots on both sides jointly do a good job in meteorological disaster prevention and mitigation, and that promotes the livelihoods and well-being of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581724.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Three DPP legislators have successively been unable to obtain Hong Kong entry permits. The “green” legislators believe this is blocking anything “green.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","We respect the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government's handling of entry and exit affairs for persons from abroad in accordance with the Basic Law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Could you tell us what the overall situation is for Taiwanese-invested enterprises operating on the mainland at present? Under the new circumstances of implementing the 13th Five-Year Plan on the mainland, what opportunities exist for the transformation and upgrading of Taiwanese-invested enterprises?","At present, the overall production and operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland are generally stable. With the reform dividends and market space that the mainland continues to release, the development of Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland generally shows a trend of structural transformation, technological upgrading, and capital increases and equity expansion. Taiwan businesspeople’s investment on the mainland continues to grow.\nAccording to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, in the first eight months of this year, the mainland newly approved 2,392 Taiwan-funded projects (excluding those transferred through third locations), up 23.93% year on year; actual use of Taiwan capital was US$1.491 billion, up 33.09% year on year.\nAt present, the mainland is implementing the 13th Five-Year Plan and deepening the construction of the Belt and Road; advancing the coordinated development of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei, the Yangtze River Economic Belt, the Western Development, and the revitalization of the old industrial base in Northeast China; and other strategies. We hope that the transformation and upgrading of Taiwan enterprises will align precisely with these strategies and achieve greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581722.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","国际台记者","Taiwan claims that its pursuit of participation in the International Civil Aviation Organization Assembly is based on responsibility for international aviation flight safety. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Regarding the issue of Taiwan not being invited to participate in the 39th Assembly of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), the DPP authorities should deeply reflect on why Taiwan was able to participate three years ago but not this year, rather than hurling accusations at the mainland, misleading public opinion, or even using Taiwan's flight safety as a pretext to mislead Taiwan's people. I solemnly state here that the mainland has always attached importance to the needs of Taiwan compatriots in the field of civil aviation and will continue to provide relevant information to the Taiwan side. It can be said that Taiwan's channels for obtaining ICAO standards, recommended practices and related materials are unimpeded, and this information is complete and comprehensive. Taiwan has convenient flight connections with many cities around the world. Facts prove that Taiwan's aviation safety and its air exchanges with other regions have no connection with whether Taiwan participates in the ICAO Assembly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581726.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","This year marks the 30th anniversary of the DPP's founding. How do you assess the impact of the party's governance in Taiwan on cross-Strait relations?","As is well known, the DPP has long held to the \"Taiwan independence\" party platform and insisted on the separatist position of \"one side, one country.\" It has undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, incited cross-Strait confrontation, and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges. As a result, the good momentum and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations since 2008 have been seriously impacted, and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots have been harmed. It can be said that if the DPP does not abandon \"Taiwan independence,\" it will be difficult to find a way out in cross-Strait relations. Whether it pursues radical \"Taiwan independence\" or so-called gradual, soft \"Taiwan independence,\" it is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160928_11581728.htm"],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报提问","In Taiwan’s 2018 county and city magistrate elections, if the blue and green counties and cities are reshuffled at that time, will the eight policies for the eight counties and cities be adjusted? Second, the Taipei Palace Museum recently decided to remove the replicas of the Twelve Zodiac Animal Heads donated by Jackie Chan. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office evaluate this?","On the first question: the key to cross-Strait county and city exchanges is to have a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of county and city exchanges. Having this understanding helps the interaction, exchange and cooperation between the two sides.\nOn the second question, everyone has noticed that Mr. Jackie Chan's side has made a public response, stating that the donation they conveyed reflects an attitude of \"respecting civilization and protecting culture.\" Whether the National Palace Museum in Taipei respects such an attitude, or has other purposes, I believe everyone will form their own public judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","The Taiwan Solidarity Union recently suggested that the Taiwan authorities should invite people such as the Dalai Lama or Rebiya Kadeer to visit Taiwan, and did not rule out the TSU sending an invitation letter. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Regarding the impact and harm that inviting figures such as the Dalai Lama and Rebiya Kadeer to engage in activities in Taiwan could have on cross-Strait relations, I already made our position clear in my previous statement. The political stance and political nature of the “Taiwan Solidarity Union” are clear to everyone, so it is no surprise that they would utter such wild talk. What matters is that Taiwan's ruling authorities do not misjudge the situation and do not allow themselves to be led by the nose by the “urgent independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The visits to the mainland by the eight Taiwan county and city magistrates achieved fruitful results. Some Green Camp representatives alleged that these magistrates are “Blue Eight slaves selling out Taiwan.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","The eight county and city magistrates who visited have already made rebuttals and clarifications. I think that those who are clear remain clear and those who are muddled remain muddled. Although the behavior of throwing dirt on others reflects the political nature of these politicians, it still cannot solve the practical interests that the people of Taiwan care about.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding Taiwan's participation in the International Civil Aviation Organization Assembly, some commentators say that if Taiwan insists on not recognizing the “1992 Consensus,” its room to participate in international affairs will continue to be affected. How do you evaluate this?","There is no doubt that the \"1992 Consensus\" is both an important political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and an important basis for both sides to build mutual trust and carry out positive interaction. Without this foundation, mutual trust between the two sides and all the achievements of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations will inevitably be affected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Former Taiwan leader Lee Teng-hui recently agitated for so-called “constitutional reform,” clamoring to lead Taiwan toward “normalization as a state.” What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","There is a fashionable political term in Taiwan now: \"those pretending to sleep cannot be woken.\" I think Lee Teng-hui is the one who, lost in the dream of \"Taiwan independence,\" cannot be woken. But the general trend of world development and the general trend of cross-Strait development have destined that what he does can only be a futile dream. If a response is necessary, I would quote a line from the Tang dynasty poet Du Fu: \"Your kind's bodies and names will both perish, yet the rivers will flow on for ten thousand ages.\" Of course, what matters is that compatriots on both sides may not have forgotten that during Chen Shui-bian's time in power, he attempted to change Taiwan's status as part of China through means such as \"constitutional revision\" and \"referendums,\" and suffered a shameful defeat. If anyone still wants to inherit the mantle of Lee Teng-hui and Chen Shui-bian, the outcome will not be good, and everyone can foresee this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Xie Xuehong, co-founder of the Taiwan Communist Party and also co-founder of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, was packaged by some “Taiwan independence” organizations on the island as a “Taiwan independence” pioneer, and even had a monument erected to her. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","As many of you may know, Xie Xuehong was also a member of the Communist Party of China. Her struggle to resist Japanese colonial rule and to achieve the reunification of the motherland is a spirit that cannot be erased and must not be distorted. “Taiwan independence” forces attempt to make political capital out of this and mislead Taiwan’s residents, but this only exposes the distortion of their mindset and the clumsiness of their methods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Since September, protests have continued on the island of Taiwan, with many Taiwan residents taking to the streets to express dissatisfaction with the ruling authorities. For example, tourism operators directly shouted for the “1992 Consensus”—“we want work, we want to survive.” Can this be understood as public opinion exerting pressure on the Taiwan authorities? May I ask for the spokesperson’s views on this?","I think, in a word, these ordinary people of Taiwan and the businesspeople from all walks of life who are struggling to make a living have taken to the streets to express their voices and dissatisfaction. In fact, they are already using their feet to vote on the Taiwan authorities' cross-Strait policies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201609/t20160928_11581788.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: In an open letter to DPP members, Tsai Ing-wen made remarks such as “vigorously resist China’s pressure.” What is your comment?","TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 30th in response to questions that the trend of history is vast and irresistible. National reunification is the historical inevitability of the Chinese nation's march toward great rejuvenation, and no “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme can succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201609/t20160930_11583681.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-05","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Regarding the Taiwan side’s announcement of its APEC attendance candidates, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan stated in response to questions on October 5: Our position on this question has already been made very clear. Taiwan-side personnel attending APEC-related activities must comply with the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161005_11584310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-06","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: In an exclusive interview with the Wall Street Journal, Tsai Ing-wen discussed her views on cross-Strait relations. What is your comment?","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan stated in response to questions on October 6: The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Our will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock. The political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, cannot be shaken, and our position opposing any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities is unwavering. No force and no person should underestimate the firm resolve of the more than 1.3 billion people on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161006_11584370.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Regarding the content on cross-Strait relations in the leader of the Taiwan authorities’ “Double Ten” speech, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on October 10 as follows:\n“The ‘1992 Consensus’ and the one-China principle it embodies accord with the legal principles and reality of cross-Strait relations, and they are the cornerstone for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Whether one accepts the ‘1992 Consensus’ is the touchstone for testing whether the Taiwan authorities’ leader’s so-called ‘goodwill’ is genuine. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the ‘1992 Consensus’ and endorses its core meaning, the two sides across the Strait can consult on an equal footing and interact positively, and compatriots on both sides can look forward to a bright future for cross-Strait relations. Denying the ‘1992 Consensus,’ inciting cross-Strait confrontation, and severing the economic, social, and cultural ties across the Strait is a dead-end path.\nWe reiterate once again that our sincere goodwill to push for the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the ‘1992 Consensus’ will not change; our solemn commitment to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, welfare for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation will not be abandoned; and our resolute will to firmly oppose and deter ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist acts will not waver. The tide of history is vast and mighty: those who follow it prosper, and those who defy it perish. With the prosperity and progress of the mainland as its foundation, and the strong public will of more than 1.3 billion Chinese people as its backing, no force can stop the historical march toward national reunification and national rejuvenation.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161010_11588116.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-10-11","Geng Shuang","","The Taiwan leader talked about Taiwan's foreign exchanges and participation in international activities in a speech delivered on October 10. Do you have any response?","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has responded to questions on cross-Straits relations.\nRegarding Taiwan's foreign exchanges and participation in international activities as you asked, I would like to emphasize that there is but one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China whose sovereignty and territorial integrity brook no division. This is the international consensus.\nIn dealing with issues about Taiwan's foreign exchanges and participation in international activities, our consistent position is adhering to the one-China principle and opposing \"Taiwan independence\", \"two Chinas\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1404820.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1404796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Earlier, Director Zhang Zhijun (张志军) and the spokesperson both said that exchanges and interactions between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party would take new forms. Does the spokesperson have further news on this? Will the Straits Economic, Trade and Culture Forum be held again this year?","Since 2006, the Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Forum, co-hosted by relevant departments of the KMT and the CPC, has been successfully held 10 times. It is an important platform for exchanges and dialogue between the two parties and has played an important role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nUnder the new circumstances of cross-Strait relations, after consultation between relevant departments of the two parties, it was decided that this year they will jointly support several civil groups from both sides in co-hosting the “Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum.” It is understood that the forum will be held in Beijing from November 2 to 3. About 200 representative figures from all sectors of society from both sides, social elites, and heads of associations are expected to attend. They will conduct thematic discussions and exchanges in five groups (politics, economy, culture, society, and youth) on important issues in the development of cross-Strait relations. We hope that thoughtful people from all sectors on both sides will offer constructive advice and suggestions at the forum. We also hope that journalist friends will enthusiastically sign up to cover it.\nIn addition, relevant departments of the KMT and the CPC will continue to maintain communication regarding other exchange activities between the two parties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161012_11590884.htm"],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","福建海峡之声记者","What recent interactions have there been between the KMT and the CPC? Besides the Peace Development Forum just mentioned, will the KMT also send a delegation to visit?","The operation of the KMT-CPC platform and the exchanges and interactions at all levels have played an important role in advancing relations between the two parties and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Under the new circumstances, the KMT and the CPC will continue to maintain contact and communication on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” They will strengthen exchanges and interaction, and continue to play a positive role in maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nAs for the visit of the Kuomintang delegation you mentioned, the relevant parties on both sides are still in communication. If there is definite news, it will be announced promptly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161012_11590883.htm"],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","新华社记者","In her “5.20” inaugural address, Tsai Ing-wen made statements about cross-Strait relations, and the Taiwan Affairs Office once commented that this was an unfinished answer sheet. During the just-passed “Double Ten,” Tsai Ing-wen made new statements about cross-Strait relations. Regarding this statement, do you think she has completed her answer sheet? If so, how many points would you give her?","On October 10, the TAO spokesperson already stated our position and attitude on this matter. The causes of and responsibility for the suspension of institutionalized cross-Strait exchange mechanisms, the obstruction of the positive momentum of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the impact on the achievements of peaceful development in all areas, and the damage to the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, are clear to everyone.\nPeaceful development of cross-Strait relations is a correct path to safeguard peace across the Strait, promote common development, and benefit compatriots on both sides. To safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the key lies in adhering to the common political basis of the ‘1992 Consensus.’ On the fundamental questions of the political basis for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait relations, there is no room for ambiguity. This is also a ‘compulsory question’ that cannot be evaded no matter how much fancy talk or procrastination is used.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161012_11590855.htm"],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","PFP Chairman James Soong intends to attend the APEC meeting to be held in Peru next month on behalf of Tsai Ing-wen, but some mainland scholars now believe this does not comply with the provisions of the Memorandum of Understanding and may not be able to go ahead. How does the TAO comment on this?","On this issue, our position has been made very clear: Taiwan personnel attending APEC-related activities should comply with the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","According to Taiwan media, Tsai Ing-wen recently said in an interview with Japanese media that she does not rule out holding a Taiwan-Japan maritime affairs cooperation dialogue this month, and that they would discuss the “Okinotori Reef dispute.” May I ask how the spokesperson views this?","Our position and attitude on Taiwan's external exchanges have been consistent and clear. As for the Okinotorishima issue, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","台湾中天记者","You just mentioned the Cross-Strait Peace Development Forum. During this forum, will General Secretary Xi Jinping and Kuomintang Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu be arranged to meet?","It is understood that the specific schedule of the forum is still being arranged.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Currently, the Taiwan authorities do not recognize the “1992 Consensus.” What is your comment on Tsai Ing-wen's statement that she would respect the historical fact of the 1992 talks between the two sides' associations?","In fact, as I indicated just now in answering the previous question, the “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Whether one accepts the “1992 Consensus,” and whether one can correctly recognize the nature of cross-Strait relations, is the touchstone for testing the so-called “goodwill” of the leader of the Taiwan authorities. On major issues concerning the future of cross-Strait relations and the fate of our compatriots, the Taiwan authorities should answer with concrete actions, and should also accept the test of history and the people. Goodwill must be demonstrated through action, not merely spoken.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊","At the “Double Ten” events, Tsai Ing-wen proposed facing up to the existence of what she calls Taiwan's “regime.” This is the first time a DPP leader has raised this issue. However, public opinion on both sides of the Strait holds that, without the foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” this in fact openly expresses her “two-state theory” thinking of “one side, one country; two Chinas.” What is the spokesperson's…","Our position on cross-Strait relations is very clear. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not a “state-to-state” relationship. As for the long-standing political differences between the two sides, our position is that we do not wish them to be passed down from generation to generation; they should be addressed through consultations between the two sides on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","The so-called “Taiwan Congress Tibet Caucus,” established within Taiwan's legislature on the 7th, is chaired by Lin Chang-tso of the New Power Party. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this?","Our position on this is very clear. Certain political forces on the island that stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and treat the mainland as an enemy intend to merge with “Tibet independence” forces and deliberately create incidents, which will inevitably damage cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","央视记者","Mainland basketball star Yao Ming (姚明) recently visited Taiwan and was pursued by young people on the island. Some media say this visit was based on the institutionalized exchange platform of the “Twin City Forum” between Shanghai and Taipei. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","It is my understanding that Yao Ming's trip to Taiwan is to take part in the “Strait Cup Basketball Invitational Tournament” jointly held by Shanghai Municipality and Taipei City, which is a purely sports exchange activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","The director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office recently visited the magistrate of Miaoli County. Will Taiwan Affairs Offices of other mainland provinces and cities also visit and exchange with the KMT-led counties and cities in Taiwan?","Our attitude and sincerity in actively supporting exchange and cooperation in all areas across the Taiwan Strait have not changed. As for specific exchange activities, you may inquire with the relevant provincial and municipal authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","The first question: It is understood that Taiwan is actively applying to attend this year's INTERPOL General Assembly. May I ask what attitude the mainland takes on this? The second question: During the just-concluded National Day holiday, the number of mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan dropped sharply. May I ask how the spokesperson views this?","First question: The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. We have consistently adhered to the one-China principle in handling Taiwan's external exchanges and its participation in international organization activities, and we firmly oppose interference by foreign forces.\nSecond question: We have answered this several times at press conferences. Everyone is very clear about the reasons for the decline in the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan and the damage to the interests of Taiwan's tourism-related industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","After Tsai Ing-wen's “Double Ten” speech, some mainland public opinion said that she has lost the opportunity to avoid confrontation with the mainland. How do you assess future cross-Strait relations? Because some mainland scholars say that cross-Strait relations have now entered a period of “cold confrontation,” do you agree with this view? Apart from “cold confrontation,” do you think there is any opportunity…","We have said that different path choices will determine different prospects. Will it be to uphold the “1992 Consensus” as the political foundation embodying the one-China principle, or to pursue the “two-state theory” and the separatist “Taiwan independence” proposition of “one side, one country”? Will it be to continue on the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, or to re-stir tension and turmoil across the Strait? Will it be to enhance the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides, or to harm the fundamental interests of compatriots and sever the emotional ties across the Strait? These are major questions of right and wrong concerning the future of cross-Strait relations and the destiny of compatriots, and a correct choice must be made. Where cross-Strait relations go depends on a single thought of the leader of the Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161012_11590854.htm"],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Zhuang Nu, a giant of the Chinese-language lyrics world, passed away on the 11th. Mr. Zhuang was a Taiwanese and also a son-in-law of Chongqing, and left behind more than 3,000 widely loved lyrics in his lifetime. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of the role Mr. Zhuang played in promoting cross-Strait music and cultural exchanges?","Mr. Zhuang Nu is a renowned master of lyrics on both sides of the Strait. In his lifetime he created thousands of popular Chinese songs that are widely sung throughout the Chinese-speaking world. Songs such as “Story of a Small Town,” “Sweet as Honey,” and “Walking Along the Ridge” are probably familiar to everyone. The person has passed, but the songs live on. We hope the elder walks on well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","First question: the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently responded to Tsai Ing-wen’s speech, saying it hopes the mainland side will once again seriously consider, that there is no need for unnecessary doubts and suspicions, and especially not to misjudge the situation. How do you evaluate these remarks? Second question: there is news that the first cross-Strait telecommunications industry matchmaking…","On the first question, our position has been stated very clearly. Achieving national reunification is the historical inevitability of the Chinese nation's march toward great rejuvenation. Do not misjudge the situation. It is precisely the Taiwan authorities who are mistakenly walking onto the evil path of “Taiwan independence” and separatism. On the second question, it is understood that the cross-Strait communication exchange seminar to be held soon is a civilian exchange activity organized by cross-Strait industry associations, not a bridge-building meeting. In addition, it was the Taiwan side that proposed not holding this activity again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","央视记者","In response to the content of Tsai Ing-wen's speech on the 10th, a US Department of Defense official said that peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait are in line with long-term US interests, and what matters is that both sides of the Strait work toward the common goal of sustained peace and stability. The US statement did not give Tsai Ing-wen clear support. How does the spokesperson view this issue?","We have already stated our position and attitude on the current state of cross-strait relations very clearly. We hope the US side will continue to abide by the one-China policy and the commitments made in the three US-China joint communiqués, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","香港大公报记者","There is exactly one month until the 150th anniversary of the birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen. Given the current situation in cross-Strait relations, may I ask the spokesperson whether the mainland has plans to invite people from the Taiwan side, or to hold related commemorative events jointly with the Taiwan side?","On this question, we already gave an answer at the last press conference. November 12 this year marks the 150th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's birth. At that time the Mainland will hold a series of commemorative activities, and Taiwan compatriots are also welcome to take part.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","A pro-independence figure on the island said at a seminar that maintaining the status quo and not accepting the “1992 Consensus” means Taiwan is not part of China, and that logically this amounts to Taiwan “independence.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","I think the one who should answer this question is the leader of the Taiwan authorities herself: what exactly is the so-called “status quo” she claims to be maintaining?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","Continuing the question of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council recently said that if mainland tourism to Taiwan were differentiated by blue and green, it would intensify the antagonism between the peoples on both sides of the Strait. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","Regarding exchanges and cooperation between relevant mainland parties and certain counties and cities in Taiwan, we have already expressed our attitude and given explanations on many occasions. Our attitude is very clear: regardless of which county or city in Taiwan it is, as long as it has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of the nature of cross-Strait county and city exchanges, we take a positive attitude. As for the so-called “political tourism” that the Taiwan side has mentioned, this claim is extremely absurd and not worth refuting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-12","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Tsai Ing-wen has repeatedly said that Taiwan will not yield to pressure from the mainland. But public opinion on both sides of the Strait holds that this reflects her playing the “sorrow card,” using it to incite and stir up hatred toward the mainland in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","Regarding the recent series of statements on cross-Strait relations by the leader of the Taiwan authorities, some analysts on the island have made a very valid point: her “four noes and one absence.” The “four noes” are empty, merely said to different audiences and different listeners. But the “one absence” is a fact, namely that she has not accepted the “1992 Consensus.” We state clearly that the “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161012_11590885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-10-24","Lu Kang","","First, during President Duterte's visit last week, Vice Foreign Minister Liu Zhenmin said that Huangyan Dao was not touched upon. Now there are reports saying that Philippine fishermen can fish in Huangyan Dao very soon. What is your response? Second, regarding more than 20 Asian sailors, including some from the mainland and Taiwan who were kidnapped by Somali pirates, how did the Foreign Ministry rescue them?…","On your first question, President Duterte's visit last week was a historic one. In the past five years, China-Philippine relations were held back due to reasons known to all. The two sides demonstrated enough political willingness and exchanged views on resuming and improving bilateral relations in an all-round way, further enhancing cooperation, and controlling disputes. I can tell you that the two sides talked a lot and agreed a lot on a wide range of subjects. As for the specific issue you asked concerning the South China Sea, President Xi told President Duterte that for the most part of bilateral relations since China and the Philippines established diplomatic ties, the two sides were able to properly control disputes through bilateral dialogues on the South China Sea issue. Such successful practice can be repeated and the political wisdom it exhibited worth carrying forward. It is an important basis for China and the Philippines to develop their relations in a sound and steady way. With this basis, the two sides can have candid exchange of views on everything, manage disputes and give full play to cooperation. I also want to point out for you that in the joint statement issued during President Duterte's visit, the two sides made clear that they will remain in consultation on the South China Sea issue and other concerns. I can assure you that relevant issues between China and the Philippines will be properly settled as long as the two sides keep their political willingness going on.\nOn your second question, yesterday, the Foreign Ministry has given details about these 26 crew members rescued after spending more than 4 years as hostages to Somalia pirates. There were Chinese fishermen from both the mainland and Taiwan.\nIt is up to the State Council Office for Taiwan Affairs to answer cross-Straits-related issues, as the Spokesperson of the Office just did this morning. He said that in accordance with the choice made by the Taiwan fisherman and the requests made by his family members, the Taiwan fisherman will travel to Guangzhuo from Nairobi along with other fishermen from the mainland. His family members will take him back to Taiwan from Guangzhou.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1408253.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1408215.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-10-24","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan said on October 24 that 26 surviving crew members of the Omani-registered Taiwanese fishing vessel NAHAM 3, which had been held hostage by Somali pirates for four and a half years, were safely rescued on the 22nd. Among them, 9 mainland crew members and 1 Taiwanese crew member will return to the motherland escorted by a working group of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The NAHAM 3 fishing vessel was hijacked by Somali pirates in March 2012, with 29 crew members aboard from China, the Philippines, Indonesia, Vietnam and Cambodia. Three of them died unfortunately during the hijacking, including 1 mainland crew member and 1 Taiwanese crew member.\nThe spokesperson said that, in accordance with the wishes of the rescued Taiwanese crew member Shen Ruizhang himself and the commission of his family, Shen will return to Guangzhou from Nairobi, the capital of Kenya, on the same flight as the mainland crew members, and his family will collect him from Guangzhou to return to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161024_11601166.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-24","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan said on October 24 that Hung Hsiu-chu, Chairwoman of the Kuomintang, will lead a Kuomintang mainland delegation to visit Nanjing and Beijing from October 30 to November 3, and that both sides are communicating about arrangements for the activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161024_11601175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-24","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question: Relevant parties in Taiwan have made remarks on the eligibility of certain incoming Hong Kong SAR legislators, and these incoming legislators have also traveled to Taiwan to engage in activities colluding with “Taiwan independence” forces. What is your view?","An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on October 24 in response to questions:\nWe are paying close attention to this. Since Hong Kong's return to the motherland, the “one country, two systems” principle, “Hong Kong people governing Hong Kong,” and a high degree of autonomy have been comprehensively and accurately implemented. The Basic Law and the Constitution have been strictly followed, which has won high affirmation from all sectors in Hong Kong and the international community.\nWe firmly oppose the words and deeds of the Taiwan authorities that interfere with the implementation of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong and undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability. Diehard “Taiwan independence” elements colluding with “Hong Kong independence” elements to split the country will be opposed by compatriots on both sides and will certainly not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161024_11601767.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-10-25","Lu Kang","","Has the Chinese fishermen who were rescued from the Somali pirates arrived in China?","Yesterday, we have given you details on their rescue. The latest information we have is that of the 10 Chinese fishermen (9 from the mainland and 1 from Taiwan), 9 have arrived at Guangzhou this morning, except one who needs to stay put for medical treatments because of health reasons. He will be escorted back by the working group of the Foreign Ministry once he gets better.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1408663.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1408596.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-10-25","Lu Kang","","First, about the Somali hostage incident, according to the BBC, former Taiwan elected representatives who were part of the rescue operation said that they paid a huge amount of ransom for the release of the Taiwan fisherman. What is your response? Did China pay ransom? Can you tell us more about the operation? Second, Philippine President Duterte kicked off his visit to Japan today. Japan hopes that President…","On your first question, we have offered all the information we have on the rescue of the hostages. I want to reiterate that regardless of multiple difficulties and complex factors, the Chinese government always puts the safety of the hostages in the first place and has been making unremitting efforts to that end. Today, most of the hostages can return home safely. That is one thing we should value more and feel more relieved about.\nConcerning President Duterte's visit to Japan, we wish for healthy, positive and cooperative relations among all countries, especially between our neighbors. Such relations should be conducive to regional peace, stability and development, instead of the opposite. Considering that the South China Sea situation has cooled down, and China and the Philippines are committed to restoring ties and enhancing cooperation, it is better if other parties can help consolidate such a positive trend by doing and saying the right things.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1408663.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1408596.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","新华社记者","KMT Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu is about to visit the mainland. As is customary, the leaders of the KMT and the CPC should meet and express views on cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Meetings between leaders of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China have been held for many years. In 2005, at a critical moment when cross-Strait relations faced a choice of path, the leaders of the two parties held a historic meeting, confirming the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” pointing out a bright path for cross-Strait relations, and also reaching a consensus on establishing a regular communication platform between the two parties. Since then, the two parties have maintained high-level interaction, making positive contributions to promoting the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, meetings between leaders of the two parties, which continue high-level interaction and consolidate the common political foundation, are of great positive significance for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the interests and welfare of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604529.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","A major part of Hung Hsiu-chu's trip to the mainland this time is to attend the Cross-Strait Peace and Development Forum held in Beijing from November 2 to 3. Could you introduce the current preparations for the forum, and what agenda items and topics it includes?","The Cross-Strait Peace Development Forum will be held in Beijing from November 2 to 3. This session of the Forum is co-hosted by 20 civil organizations from both sides of the Strait. The mainland co-hosts are: the Cross-Strait Relations Research Center, the National Taiwan Studies Association, the China Industrial Economics Federation, the China Productivity Center Association, the Chinese Culture Exchange Association, the China Culture Institute, the China Social Work Federation, the Chinese Society for Higher Education, the All-China Youth Federation, and the China Young Entrepreneurs Association. The Taiwan co-hosts are: the Institute for National Policy Research, the 21st Century Foundation, the Industry and Commerce Development Research Association, the Taiwan Listed and OTC Companies Association, the Taiwan Television Drama Production Industry Federation, the Chinese Publishing Foundation, the Taiwan Federation of Labor, the Taiwan Farmers' Association, the Youth Development Foundation, and the Cross-Strait Public Affairs Association. As we understand it, as of now, more than 240 elites and association heads from all sectors on both sides have registered to attend the Forum, and more than 280 media reporters have registered to cover it. Preparations for the Forum are progressing smoothly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604526.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the preparations for the cross-Strait entrepreneurs summit.","The Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit is a very important civil exchange platform where business and economic circles on both sides exchange views and hold seminars on macroeconomic and industrial development trends, and promote enterprise matching and cooperation. It is understood that this year's annual meeting of the Summit will be held in Kinmen and Xiamen from November 6 to 7. The opening ceremony and keynote speeches will be held in Kinmen, and the thematic forums and closing ceremony will be held in Xiamen. The annual meeting takes “Enterprise Innovation and Cooperation, Integrated Development of Industries” as its theme, and will set up seven thematic forums of industrial cooperation promotion groups to conduct in-depth discussions on cooperation in relevant industrial fields across the Strait, SME exchanges, and youth employment and entrepreneurship. Guests will include well-known industry entrepreneurs, experts and scholars from both sides, as well as SME representatives and young entrepreneurs. We hope that industry circles on both sides will, through the Summit platform, continue to promote innovative cooperation and youth employment and entrepreneurship, share experiences, and plan development together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604525.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","福建海峡之声广播电台记者","The crew members from both sides of the Taiwan Strait aboard the Omani-registered Taiwanese fishing vessel NAHAM3, which had been hijacked by pirates, have all been rescued. This matter has also drawn the concern of people on both sides of the Strait. According to our understanding, the Straits Exchange Foundation played a very active role in this process. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant…","On the 24th, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office has already given a preliminary account of the situation. On March 26, 2012, the fishing vessel was hijacked by Somali pirates in the Gulf of Aden. The relevant mainland authorities attached great importance to this and actively launched rescue efforts. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) wrote to the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) in Taiwan several times, asking it to verify crew information, convey family members' appeals, and urge the Taiwan side to press the shipowner to take effective measures to handle the rescue, but it did not receive active cooperation.\nLife is priceless, and human feeling is warm. Although the hijacking took place thousands of miles away, and information was obstructed and communication channels were lacking, making the rescue work extremely difficult, the Chinese government did not abandon its duty to protect every citizen, and made enormous efforts to rescue the hijacked crew. Authorized by the relevant parties and entrusted by the families of the cross-Strait fishing workers, ARATS actively carried out its work, coordinating closely with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other relevant parties and international institutions. After more than four years of arduous mediation, the 26 surviving crew members were finally rescued successfully.\nIn the early morning of the 25th, the rescued mainland crew members and Taiwan crew members, accompanied by a working group composed of personnel from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and ARATS, safely returned to Guangzhou. On the 26th, the Taiwan crew member Shen Ruizhang left Guangzhou and returned to Taiwan. Shen Ruizhang and his family expressed sincere gratitude for the mainland's full-scale rescue and proper care.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604524.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Hung Hsiu-chu recently had a dinner meeting with former KMT Chairman Ma Ying-jeou, and there seems to have been some dispute over the topics of “1992 Consensus, one China with each side expressing its own interpretation” and “1992 Consensus, one China with both sides expressing the same interpretation.” What is the mainland's view on the so-called “one China, each side with its own interpretation” and “one China,…","Since 2008, the KMT and the CPC and the two sides of the Strait have promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, opened a brand-new situation, and achieved a series of important results. The key to these achievements lies in both sides establishing the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” The core of this foundation is that both sides recognize that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. So we also hope that, on this basis, the KMT and the CPC can continue to build mutual trust, maintain good-faith communication and positive interaction, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continue working together to increase the well-being of the people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604528.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Taiwan’s prospective “President of the Judicial Yuan,” Hsu Tsung-li, recently said that cross-Strait relations are a “special state-to-state relationship,” which sparked controversy on the island. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Regarding cross-Strait relations, our position is very clear. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's sacred territory and has never been a country. This is the basic fact and legal foundation of cross-Strait relations, recognized by the international community. This has never changed and can never change.\nThe mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. The fallacy of the “two-state theory” has long been denounced by compatriots on both sides and by the international community. History has proven, and will continue to prove, that no one and no force that attempts to pursue so-called “de jure Taiwan independence” in any form will succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604523.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Recently, a Taiwan female entertainer, Chen Ai-lin, went to the mainland to film a production. Mainland netizens discovered that she had previously said things like “Taiwan is my country, and I don’t mind not earning RMB,” and as a result she was replaced in the role. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have repeatedly reiterated that our position of supporting and encouraging cross-Strait cultural exchanges is clear and consistent. At the same time, our position of firmly opposing any form of “Taiwan independence” separatism is also unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸栏目记者","Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, civilian exchanges and contacts across the Strait remain fairly close, and various localities are holding cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Cross-Strait economic, trade, and exchange cooperation is conducive to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In recent times, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities remain brisk. The Tianjin-Taiwan Conference, the Shandong-Taiwan Conference, the Zhejiang Taiwan Week, the Jiangxi-Taiwan Conference, the Chongqing Taiwan Week, the Anhui-Taiwan Investment Cooperation Matchmaking Conference, the Huai’an Taiwan Business Forum in Jiangsu Province, and others have already been held, with participation from all sectors of society across the Strait, including representatives of Taiwan’s industry and commerce groups and enterprise heads, youth, and grassroots people, and have reached many concrete outcomes, reflecting the strong aspiration and enthusiasm of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for sustained exchange and cooperation.\nIt is also learned that Beijing, Sichuan, Hubei, Hunan and other places will also soon hold cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Among them, the 13th Hubei?Wuhan Taiwan Week will be held in Wuhan, Xiangyang, Yichang, Shennongjia Forest District and other places from November 14 to 18. At that time, nearly 1,000 people, including representatives of Taiwan youth, women, labor unions, and grassroots people, heads of Taiwan social organizations and industrial and commercial enterprises, and experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait, will participate in a total of 18 events. During this period, the first Cross-Strait Youth Donghu Forum will have nearly 400 youth representatives from both sides of the Strait, individuals who have succeeded in entrepreneurship and innovation, as well as youth groups and university student representatives, who will engage in exchanges on themes such as entrepreneurship and innovation, internships and employment, and common development.\nIn addition, the 9th Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Expo and Trade Fair will be held in Xiamen from November 4 to 7. It will be held under the principles of “highlighting the Cross-Strait, highlighting industry, highlighting investment, and highlighting trade,” featuring various forms of activities such as an expo and trade fair, forums and matchmaking events, and award ceremonies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604521.htm"],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","First question: the Council of Indigenous Peoples of Taiwan recently stated that, during the Hangzhou Cultural Expo, the organizers required the removal of the full titles of government agencies, so it withdrew from the event. Will this impact cross-Strait exchanges? Second question: in the future, mainland students in Taiwan may be included in the National Health Insurance, but they must pay the full premium in…","First question: As we understand it, the organizer of this event has already issued an explanation on this matter, and relevant media on the island have reported on the organizer's explanation. Since the Cross-Strait Cultural and Creative Boutique Exhibition at the Hangzhou Cultural and Creative Industries Expo was first held jointly by both sides, it has been participated in through civil exchange. This year, because the Taiwanese exhibitors violated the long-standing tacit understanding of civil exchange during booth setup, displaying so-called “official logos” and “institutional names,” which was inconsistent with the expo's consistent practice. After repeated communication between the organizer and the Taiwanese exhibitors failed, the organizer removed the relevant logos. We welcome and support exchanges and cooperation between civil sectors across the Strait, and we also hope that similar incidents will not happen again.\nSecond question, regarding the inclusion of mainland students in Taiwan in the National Health Insurance program. Regarding the discriminatory policies that mainland students have encountered in Taiwan, our office has repeatedly stated our position on related issues at previous press conferences. We also note that the Taiwan side has taken measures to improve medical conditions for mainland students in Taiwan, and we hope the Taiwan side will further abolish discriminatory policies that affect the rights and interests of mainland students. In addition, I must point out that Taiwanese students studying at universities on the mainland have been included in the urban resident basic medical insurance scheme on the mainland since September 2013, enjoying the same basic medical insurance benefits as local mainland students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Yesterday was Taiwan's Restoration Day. Every year the island holds commemorative events, but a Green camp legislator recently proposed deleting the budget for related events next year. What is the spokesperson's comment?","This year marks the 71st anniversary of the Chinese people's victory in the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, and also the 71st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration to the motherland. The anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots was an important component of the nationwide war of resistance, and Taiwan's restoration is a victory achieved through the joint struggle of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. The history of Taiwan's restoration proves that, although compatriots on both sides of the Strait have experienced all kinds of hardships and separation, no force can separate the two sides, because we are one family. Budgets can be deleted, but this history cannot be erased.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","First, regarding Hong Xiuzhu's upcoming visit to the mainland, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council stated that cross-Strait exchanges should have no political preconditions, and should be conducted in accordance with the provisions of the Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area; only through existing mechanisms and normal communication and dialogue can the rights and…","First question: What is meant by “preset preconditions”? What is meant by “existing mechanisms”? In fact, everyone is very clear about this. It is precisely because the Taiwan authorities unilaterally undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, imposed their denial of the “1992 Consensus” on the mainland, and set preconditions and obstacles for cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, that the existing cross-Strait communication and liaison mechanisms have stalled. Therefore, only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing the core meaning that both sides belong to one China can the two sides communicate in good faith and interact positively under the existing mechanisms, jointly benefiting compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question: Our attitude toward Taiwan's external exchanges is very clear. The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We hope the US side will abide by its commitments to adhere to the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Reports say the Kuomintang was not invited to attend the Cross-Strait Forum for Peaceful Development to be held next week, and some Taiwan media have used this to hype the relationship between the KMT and the mainland. Please introduce the relevant situation.","As I just introduced, this Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum was jointly organized by multiple cross-Strait civil groups. The invitation of guests from the Taiwan side to attend was handled by the Taiwan host units; for specifics, you may inquire with them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","You just mentioned the entrepreneurs’ summit about to be held in Xiamen and Kinmen. We have also noted that Kinmen County Magistrate Chen Fu-hai recently said that Kinmen has no “Taiwan independence” and is the best practice field of the “1992 Consensus,” and he also hopes to promote cooperation with Xiamen. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this remark?","We are pleased to see, and actively support, personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields between Kinmen and Xiamen and Fujian, and we jointly work for the well-being of people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","A Taiwan research institution on the mainland recently stated that the mainland's new position toward the DPP authorities is the 12-character guideline of “hold the bottom line, exert pressure, show goodwill.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","We have noted that recently some experts and scholars, out of concern for the development of cross-Strait relations, have expressed personal views. We have repeatedly stressed that our major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent, and will not change with changes in Taiwan's political situation. Our will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock. Our attitude of insisting on the common political foundation embodying the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” will not change, and our position of firmly opposing any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity is unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","香港凤凰卫视记者","May I ask the spokesperson: regarding the two young Hong Kong lawmakers-elect, their oaths involved some insulting remarks against China, and afterwards the Taiwan side expressed concern. Subsequently, these two individuals were invited to give speeches at universities in Taiwan, and spoke about some “Hong Kong independence” issues. What comment does the spokesperson make on this?","On the 24th, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office already stated our position on this. We firmly oppose the conduct of those separatist forces on the island who persistently insist on “Taiwan independence” colluding with “Hong Kong independence” elements in an attempt to split the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office has granted plaques to dozens of cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites. We recently noted that a Taiwan Youth Entrepreneurship Station was also officially established in Beijing with a plaque. May I ask, what new measures will the spokesperson take in promoting cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship?","In recent years, amid the mainland's “mass entrepreneurship and innovation” wave, all kinds of cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship platforms have emerged. I think this is a win-win, multiple-win good thing for both sides. The youth entrepreneurship bases and youth employment and entrepreneurship demonstration sites that the Taiwan Affairs Office has promoted in various places are mainly intended to encourage cross-Strait youth to start businesses, find employment and develop together, to build better platforms, and at the same time to explore better experiences. In the future, we will continue to create a better environment for cross-Strait youth employment, entrepreneurship and common development, and strive to achieve a win-win goal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸栏目记者","There is news that Taiwan will set up an early-warning radar on Taiping Island and may share the intelligence with the United States in the future. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","Our basic position on the South China Sea issue is very clear, and we have explained it on many occasions in the past. If some people on the island seek to rely on foreign powers to strengthen their own position in order to engage in cross-Strait confrontation, this will have a negative impact on cross-Strait peace and stability. We hope the Taiwan side will abandon this “Taiwan independence” and hostile mindset, return to the position of the “1992 Consensus,” and jointly safeguard cross-Strait peace and stability for the benefit of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","香港电台记者","Regarding the Hong Kong incoming legislators who went to Taiwan to attend exchange activities, how are they related to “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence”? Please give your evaluation.","The activities they participated in on the island and the remarks they made at the scene are clear to everyone. Therefore, we firmly oppose this practice of merging “Hong Kong independence” with “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201610/t20161026_11604530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-10-26","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a question from a reporter about the Taiwan side's decision to amend laws so that mainland students in Taiwan can join Taiwan's health insurance, but must pay the full premium themselves, TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said at the regular press conference on October 26 that we have stated our position many times on the discriminatory policies mainland students face in Taiwan. We have noted the measures the Taiwan side has taken to improve medical conditions for mainland students in Taiwan, and we hope the Taiwan side will further cancel discriminatory policies that affect the rights and interests of mainland students.\nI must also point out that Taiwan students studying at mainland universities have been included in the urban resident basic medical insurance scheme since September 2013, and enjoy the same basic medical insurance benefits as local mainland students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201610/t20161026_11604522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Regarding the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress's interpretation of Article 104 of the Hong Kong Basic Law, the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said that it is closely following the state of freedom and democracy in Hong Kong and called on the mainland to keep its commitments to Hong Kong. What comment do you have on this?","At the regular press conference on November 8, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions, saying that the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, in accordance with the provisions of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, interpreted Article 104 of that Law; a responsible person of the National People's Congress has already issued an explanation, and a spokesperson of the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council has also made a statement. We firmly oppose relevant parties in Taiwan commenting on this, confusing right and wrong, and deliberately misleading people. Relevant parties in Taiwan should stop any words and deeds that interfere with the implementation of \"one country, two systems\" in Hong Kong and undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161108_11617563.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","On November 1, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with a visiting delegation led by Hung Hsiu-chu, Chairperson of the Chinese Nationalist Party (Kuomintang). This meeting drew wide attention from all sectors on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the significance of this meeting.","General Secretary Xi Jinping’s meeting with the delegation of the Chinese Kuomintang led by Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu is an important meeting between the leaders of the two parties under the complex and severe situation facing cross-strait relations, and it is of great significance for exchanges between the two parties and for the development of cross-strait relations.\nDuring the meeting, the leaders of the two parties exchanged views on advancing cross-strait relations, fully affirmed the historical contributions of the two parties to the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and once again affirmed the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” They agreed that the Communist Party and the Kuomintang should continue to consolidate this foundation, enhance political mutual trust, and safeguard the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They will further give play to the role of the exchange and communication mechanism between the two parties, promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation in economic, cultural, social, and other fields, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. This meeting has drawn wide attention from compatriots on both sides and from the international community, and it has had a positive impact on advancing relations between the two parties and on guiding cross-strait relations in the new situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626255.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Much public opinion holds that the recently held Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum provided a good platform for elite exchanges across the Strait. How does the spokesperson view this?","The Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum, co-hosted by 20 civil organizations from both sides of the Strait, was successfully held in Beijing from November 2 to 3. Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, met with some participating delegates and the heads of the organizing units of the forum. More than 240 elites from all walks of life on both sides and heads of associations attended the forum. They actively engaged in exchanges and dialogue around important issues in the development of cross-Strait relations, offered suggestions, and pooled wisdom, reflecting the shared voice of compatriots on both sides in upholding the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At the closing ceremony of the forum, a batch of important 2017 cross-Strait exchange activities and cooperation projects planned by relevant mainland units and localities were released. They were openly open to registration from all sectors in Taiwan and produced a good response.\nWe will work with relevant parties to actively promote the implementation of the constructive views and suggestions put forward at the forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626254.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","We noted that, regarding the mainland's activities commemorating the 150th anniversary of Sun Yat-sen's birth, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said Sun Yat-sen founded the “Republic of China,” and that the mainland's commemorative activities should be “faithful to historical facts.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Mr. Sun Yat-sen was a great national hero, a great patriot, and a great pioneer of China’s democratic revolution, revered by all Chinese sons and daughters. Under new historical conditions, compatriots on both sides of the Strait should inherit Mr. Sun’s resolute pursuit of national reunification and the revitalization of China, jointly safeguard peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and join hands to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. That is the best commemoration of Mr. Sun.\nAs for “being faithful to historical facts,” compatriots on both sides see very clearly: who has abandoned the core values of Sun Yat-sen’s thought? Who has been vigorously carrying out “de-Sun Yat-sen-ization” in the political, social and cultural fields? Who has violated Sun Yat-sen’s posthumous teachings and condoned words and deeds on the island that split the country and the nation? On the one hand refusing to recognize or commemorate Sun Yat-sen, and on the other hand carping about commemorative activities for him, is truly the greatest joke under heaven.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626249.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2016 annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, held recently in Kinmen and Xiamen, had distinctive features. I would like to ask the spokesperson how he assesses the results achieved at the summit.","The 2016 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Annual Meeting opened in Kinmen on November 6 and closed in Xiamen on November 7. Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the meeting in Xiamen and delivered an address. More than 900 business people from both sides of the Strait eagerly attended, and journalists also actively participated in coverage. Participants held in-depth discussions around the theme of “Enterprise Innovation and Cooperation, Integrated Industrial Development,” reached several points of consensus, and signed 16 cooperation agreements and memoranda of cooperation. After the meeting, a joint press release was issued, calling on entrepreneurs from both sides to join hands, strengthen communication and exchanges between enterprises across the Strait, vigorously promote innovation cooperation between enterprises and economic integration across the Strait, and pursue the common interests of businesses on both sides and the long-term well-being of people across the Strait. We believe that the implementation of the summit's outcomes will play a positive role in promoting economic and social integration across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626253.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","First question: According to reports, Tsai Ing-wen recently attended an event commemorating Taiwanese veterans. Because Taiwanese veterans included Taiwanese soldiers serving in the Japanese army during World War II, this move has drawn much questioning. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Second question: Soong Chu-yu said that on this trip to attend the APEC meeting, he would have natural interactions…","On the first question, the history of the Second World War has long been settled. The crimes of the Japanese invaders who launched the war of aggression against China and the Pacific War have been nailed to the pillar of historical shame. The Taiwanese soldiers who were forced to take part in the war of aggression under Japanese colonial rule are also victims of Japanese militarism. What needs even more emphasis is that the standards for judging justice and injustice, aggression and anti-aggression, colonialism and anti-colonialism in history must not be confused, let alone denied. Any remarks that uphold the “Taiwan independence” view of history, disregard historical facts, attempt to glorify Japan’s colonial rule over Taiwan, or attempt to justify the aggression crimes of Japanese militarists will certainly be unanimously condemned by compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question, upholding the “1992 Consensus” is the foundation for the stable and peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the basis for positive interaction between the two sides. The Taiwan authorities’ refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle as its political foundation, means that substantive positive interaction between the two sides would be impossible. As for Taiwan-side personnel attending APEC meetings, we have said many times that this must comply with the one-China principle and the provisions of the relevant memorandum of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626248.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The Ministry of Justice recently announced that it will further expand the scope of civil litigation representation that Taiwan residents holding mainland lawyer licenses may engage in on the mainland. What significance does this have for serving compatriots on both sides of the Strait?","Recently, the Ministry of Justice decided to expand the scope of civil litigation representation that Taiwan residents who have obtained mainland legal professional qualifications and mainland lawyer practice certificates may undertake on the mainland, covering cases involving Taiwan residents and legal entities. Building on the 2008 opening of litigation related to Taiwan marriage and inheritance, new areas have been added: civil litigation related to Taiwan contract disputes, intellectual property disputes, company, securities, insurance, and negotiable instrument matters, as well as cases applying special procedures related to the above cases. The scope has been expanded to 237 types of civil cases in five major categories. For specific details, the Ministry of Justice issued a press release on November 14 to explain, and everyone is invited to refer to it. This further expansion of openness is a positive response by the mainland side to the demands of Taiwan compatriots, upholding the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family.” We believe this will help Taiwan legal professionals further participate in the service market for cross-Strait legal affairs, integrate into the mainland's rule-of-law development process, and serve Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Before PFP Chairman James Soong attended APEC, at an event commemorating Mr. Sun Yat-sen, he reiterated the PFP's position of “one China on both sides of the Strait, opposing ‘Taiwan independence.’” What is the spokesperson's view of this statement made before his trip?","We note that the People First Party has stated that “one China across the Strait, opposing Taiwan independence” has been the party's consistent position. We hope the People First Party will continue to uphold this position and maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161116_11626251.htm"],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The Taiwan Competitiveness Forum recently released a survey showing that under the current cross-Strait situation, the proportion of Taiwan residents who identify themselves as Chinese rose from 46.8% in the first half of the year to 52%, and 86% of respondents agree that they are part of the Chinese nation. I would like to ask the spokesperson: under the current cross-Strait situation, the rate of Chinese…","We do not comment on specific public opinion polls on the island. But I want to say that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are blood-related brothers and sisters, and the two sides are a community of shared destiny. As long as we curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and hold to the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, then through the continuous deepening of exchange and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, compatriots on both sides will grow closer and closer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","After Trump was elected U.S. President, the TPP, which Taiwan was actively seeking to join, has basically been “stillborn.” If Tsai Ing-wen's focus shifts to RCEP, what is the mainland's attitude on this?","If the one-China principle cannot be upheld, if political mutual trust across the Strait no longer exists, and if the institutionalization of cross-strait economic cooperation is delayed, this will inevitably have adverse effects on the question of Taiwan's side participating in regional economic cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","First, recently Taiwan media reported that toys imported from the mainland to Taiwan emitted the sound “Taiwan is China's largest island.” Chang Hsiao-yueh, Chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, said that it is inappropriate for the mainland to do this. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment? Second, a retired Taiwanese general took part in the mainland's commemoration of the 150th anniversary of…","On the first question: Taiwan Island is China's largest island, which is common knowledge around the world. On the second question: as I said just now, Dr. Sun Yat-sen is a great figure revered by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Some DPP politicians stubbornly hold “Taiwan independence” positions, incite hostility and confrontation across the Strait, use political pretexts to interfere with cross-Strait exchanges, suppress Taiwan participants in cross-Strait exchanges, and create a “chilling effect.” This also exposes that their professed so-called freedom and democracy is extremely hypocritical. Yesterday, Director Zhang Zhijun responded to reporters' questions while participating in exchange activities in Wuhan. Our attitude and feelings on this matter can be summed up in eight characters: “If one wants to pin a crime on someone, one will never lack excuses.” On the third question, I currently have no information on this to release.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","We note that the Cross-Strait Peace and Development Forum has for the first time established a youth group, and at its closing ceremony, more than 40 projects focused on cross-Strait youth exchanges were announced. In addition, the “Wuhan?Taiwan Week” in Hubei has also specifically set up a youth agenda. All of this shows how vibrant exchanges between young people across the Strait are. Could the spokesperson…","As you pointed out in your question, strengthening youth exchanges is an important field and a key direction in our promotion of cross-Strait exchanges. In recent years we have not only actively promoted cross-Strait youth exchanges, but have also actively provided more convenient conditions for Taiwan youth to work, live, intern, start businesses, study and more on the mainland. Without a doubt, youth are the future of the Chinese nation and the future of cross-Strait relations. Only when young people across the Strait exchange closely, understand each other, share more common interests and reduce estrangement can the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations be more than just empty words.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Reportedly, in the first three quarters of this year the mainland remained the world's largest source market for outbound tourism, bringing more foreign exchange income to destinations around the world than in previous years, yet only the Taiwan region has decreased rather than increased. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","As everyone knows, from 2008 for some time, mainland residents' travel to Taiwan showed a healthy and good development trend, but since “5?20” this development trend has been affected, for reasons that are widely known. I believe everyone is clear on how to resolve the crux of the problem. As we have always said, the one who tied the knot must be the one to untie it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","We recently noted that an assessment report from a Taiwan security agency points out that the incoming new US President Trump has the opportunity to expand US arms sales to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I will not make specific comments on the various statements on the island about the policy direction of the newly elected US President Trump and his new administration. What I want to point out is that developing long-term, healthy and stable China-US relations serves the fundamental interests of both peoples and is the common expectation of the international community. The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We hope the new US administration will abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","In view of the current complex situation in cross-Strait relations, some mainland scholars have recently suggested formulating detailed rules for the “Anti-Secession Law” or legislating to pursue criminal liability for acts of secession, so as to deter “Taiwan independence” forces. Does the mainland have such considerations?","The “Anti-Secession Law” is a law that firmly safeguards national sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposes and contains “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and maintains peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is also a law that promotes the development of cross-Strait relations and advances national reunification. It is the concentrated expression of the Central Government's major policy toward Taiwan and the common will of the entire Chinese people. It shows that we are making the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, and it also shows the firm resolve of the entire Chinese people that they will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","Recently, at a meeting of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, several participants said that the Taiwan Strait issue is not a problem the mainland urgently needs to address at this stage, that the mainland may still have expectations of Tsai Ing-wen, that at this stage the mainland mainly divides Taiwan's internal politics through differentiated treatment, and that the trend of “cold peace” or “cold confrontation”…","We generally do not comment on the various specific views within Taiwan, but I strongly feel that some “in-house” think tanks on the island, out of various political biases, are unwilling to face the objective development of the mainland, and therefore cannot reach correct and objective conclusions involving the mainland. Here I must reiterate: our sincere goodwill in promoting the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” will not change; our solemn commitment to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation will not be abandoned; our firm will to resolutely oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct will not waver. No force can stop the historical march toward national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161116_11626281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-11-21","Geng Shuang","","The Xinhua News Agency has issued news releases about all the meetings between President Xi Jinping and leaders of other countries on the sidelines of the APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting except the one with Prime Minister Abe. According to the Taiwan media, James Soong also met with President Xi Jinping, but we have not seen any official readout. Are these two meetings different from others?","As I said, President Xi Jinping had a brief conversation with Prime Minister Abe on the sidelines of the APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting.\nAs for President Xi Jinping's meeting with Mr. Soong, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has their statement on that. I have nothing more to offer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1417190.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1417148.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-11-23","Geng Shuang","","The website of Taiwan's \"Foreign Ministry\" updated its column about Mainland's restriction on Taiwan's activities in the international arena. What is your comment on that?","I am not aware of the updates you mentioned. As for issues about the space for Taiwan's international activities, we have been stressing that they must be handled in accordance with the one China principle. That is also the consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1418010.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1417974.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-11-25","Geng Shuang","","Hong Kong customs inspected and detained a Singapore-bound cargo ship from Taiwan, as they found armoured vehicles on board. As Taiwan and Singapore have a long established military relationship, was the seizure of the armoured vehicles ordered by Beijing? Was this Beijing expressing its displeasure with Singapore for its military relationship with Taiwan?","We have noted the relevant report, and are checking on that. In the Hong Kong SAR, the entry and exit of foreign personnel and cargo should follow relevant laws of Hong Kong. I also want to reiterate that the Chinese government is firmly opposed to any forms of official interaction between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with us, military exchanges and cooperation included.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1418891.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1418796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-11-28","Geng Shuang","","The nine Singapore-bound armoured vehicles seized by Hong Kong customs last week were said to have come back from a military exercise in Taiwan. Has the Chinese side lodged representations with the Singaporean side?","The Chinese side has lodged representations with the Singaporean side, asking them to act in strict accordance with relevant laws of the Hong Kong SAR and cooperate with the SAR government to properly deal with follow-up matters. The Chinese side is firmly opposed to any forms of official interaction between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with us, military exchanges and cooperation included. We require the Singaporean government to stick to the one China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1419412.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1419307.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-11-29","Geng Shuang","","The Taiwan authorities have again taken foreign journalists down to visit Taiping Dao. With Taiwan being part of China, does China think that Taiwan also has an obligation to maintain Chinese sovereignty in the South China Sea?","As we have been saying, the Nansha Islands including Taiping Dao are an inherent part of China. The Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Straits have the obligation to preserve ancestral property.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1419810.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1419752.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-11-30","Geng Shuang","","According to the Ministry of Public Security, the Chinese police brought back 74 telecoms fraud suspects from Malaysia on November 29, 21 Taiwanese suspects included. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on that?","The Chinese side highly commends and thanks the Malaysian side for its adherence to the one China policy and collaboration with China in combatting cross-border crimes, such as telecoms fraud. Competent Chinese authorities will deal with those suspects in accordance with the law. It will help ascertain the facts, recover the ill-gotten money, punish the wrongdoing and safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of the victims. We believe it will be understood and supported by compartriots from both sides of the Taiwan Straits and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1420109.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1420568.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2016-11-30","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Last week, the Hong Kong Customs seized 9 armored personnel carriers (APCs) being sent back from Taiwan to Singapore after they participated military drills in Taiwan. Taiwan and Singapore have a long military relationship. Has the Chinese military spoken to the Singaporean military about this and offered Singapore military training facilities in the mainland of China so that Singapore no longer has to train its…","My colleagues from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs as well as the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have already answered this question. Here, I’d like to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. We firmly oppose to any country’s official and military contacts in any form with Taiwan.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2016-12/01/content_4765258.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2016-11/30/content_4765238.htm",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-11-30","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Global Times reported on Monday that the Singaporean side announced in 2012 that Singapore would like to cut off its military cooperation program code-named “Star Light” with the Taiwan. Could you please confirm whether the Singaporean side has reached any agreement with China or made any commitment to China to stop its “Star Light” cooperation program with Taiwan? The second question is that, recently,…","I have already answered your first question a moment ago. With regards to the report you mentioned written by the Global Times, since I know that the journalist from the Global Times is also present here, I suggest you exchange views with her on that report after the press conference. Your second question is about the reform on national defense and the military. I have also noticed that in society and especially on the Internet, there are a lot of remarks and comments on the military reform, but most of them are just speculations or guesses. The relevant authorities of the military will disclose the information about the progress of the reform in due course.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2016-12/01/content_4765258.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2016-11/30/content_4765238.htm",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-11-30","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the “Coast Guard Administration” and “the Navy” of Taiwan conducted a humanitarian assistance exercise near the Taiping Island of the Nansha Islands. What is your comment on this exercise?","The Nansha Islands, including the Taiping Island, are inherent territory of China. The Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have the responsibility to jointly safeguard the territory and property left by our common ancestors. And we will keep a close watch on the moves of relevant parties on the Taiping Island.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2016-12/01/content_4765258.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2016-11/30/content_4765238.htm",0,1,1,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Chen Yingzhen, the renowned Taiwanese writer and pro-unification figure, passed away in Beijing on the 22nd. Has the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed condolences? Also, what is your assessment of Mr. Chen Yingzhen?","Chen Ying-zhen, founding chairman of the Taiwan China Unification League and honorary vice chairman of the Chinese Writers Association, passed away in Beijing on November 22, 2016, due to illness. The Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council express deep mourning and sincere condolences to his family.\nMr. Chen Ying-zhen was a loyal patriot, an outstanding representative of Taiwan compatriots, a famous writer, and an outstanding leader and theorist of the Taiwan patriotic reunification camp. He steadfastly pursued national reunification, created many excellent literary works and literary criticism, praised the patriotic and home-loving traditions of Taiwan compatriots, exposed the absurdity and harm of \"Taiwan independence\", and called on Taiwan compatriots to devote themselves to the great cause of national reunification. His lofty convictions and brilliant character will inspire compatriots on both sides of the Strait to keep moving forward.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161130_11640062.htm"],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","According to reports, the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently said that the mainland should positively understand the “goodwill” of Taiwan's side in its words and actions, and should not make excessive negative interpretations or criticisms. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Since May 20 this year, the new ruling authorities in Taiwan have refused to accept the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermining the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This has led to the interruption of cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms, stagnation of the institutionalization of economic cooperation, a slowdown in exchanges and cooperation in various fields, and harm to the immediate interests and emotional bonds of compatriots on both sides. At the same time, “Taiwan independence” forces have repeatedly made moves of “de-Sinicization” in politics, economy, society, culture, education, and other fields, attempting to weaken or sever Taiwan society's connection to Chinese culture. Can these actions be what they proclaim as “goodwill”?\nWe have said many times that whether one accepts the “1992 Consensus” concerns the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations and is the touchstone for testing whether the Taiwan authorities' so-called “goodwill” is genuine. Turning away from the political foundation that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and treating the two sides as a “state-to-state relationship,” naturally leaves no room for any “goodwill.” Pursuing “Taiwan independence” under the pretext of “Taiwan's internal development,” with the goal of “de-Sinicization,” will inevitably meet firm opposition from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161130_11640109.htm"],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","It is reported that relevant mainland enterprises recently visited eight counties and cities in Taiwan to inspect and negotiate the procurement of agricultural products. Please introduce the relevant situation.","At the invitation of eight counties and cities in Taiwan, the All-China Federation of Supply and Marketing Cooperatives led relevant mainland associations and enterprises to visit Taiwan from November 21 to 28 to inspect and negotiate agricultural product cooperation. Both sides pragmatically explored issues such as establishing sales channels, building brands and stabilizing supply sources, and reached a consensus to carry out regular cooperation on a market-based mechanism. Mainland enterprises expressed their intention to purchase 3,000 tons of Taiwan fruit, and both sides are actively communicating about purchases of other product categories, with prospects of achieving more results.\nAs long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and exchanges between counties and cities, and is willing to contribute efforts to enhancing the well-being and kinship of compatriots on both sides, we take a positive attitude.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161130_11639959.htm"],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","According to reports, after “5?20” this year, the number of mainland students going to Taiwan to study has dropped sharply. What comment does the spokesperson have on this? What attitude does the mainland currently take toward mainland students studying in Taiwan?","Whether to study in Taiwan is an autonomous choice of students and their parents. As we understand it, political changes in Taiwan this May have impacted the momentum of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and Taiwan's educational environment has also been affected. These factors have deeply worried mainland students and their parents, and have directly affected their willingness to study in Taiwan. I want to point out that some forces in Taiwan carrying out “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in the field of education will inevitably worsen the environment for cross-Strait educational exchanges. We hope that cross-Strait educational exchanges can develop healthily under good conditions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161130_11639958.htm"],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","There are reports that some figures in Taiwan’s business community have taken posts such as “Zizheng” (senior adviser) and have come under pressure from the mainland side. Is this true?","I am not aware of the situation you described. We do not comment on or interfere with specific personnel matters on the island. We hope that business and industry people across Taiwan will uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” support the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and participate in and promote cross-strait economic exchanges and cooperation through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Liu Chao-hsuan, Chairman of the Chinese Culture Foundation of Taiwan, announced his resignation on the 23rd. Previously, the Democratic Progressive Party had, it can be said, exerted all its “primordial force” trying to seize the Chinese Culture Foundation. Outsiders are worried that the DPP intends to repeat its old tactics, “taking the Chinese out of Chinese culture after seizing it.” In addition, there are…","We have noted the relevant reports and also noted the doubts expressed by Taiwan public opinion on this. Will this organization continue to uphold and promote Chinese culture, or will it pursue “de-Sinicization” and “removing Chinese culture”? We are following this closely, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are also watching and waiting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, the Golden Horse Awards in Taiwan concluded. At this Golden Horse, most of the awards went to mainland performers and directors. I want to ask: in the current cold state of cross-Strait relations, the Golden Horse still treats everyone equally. What is your view of this situation? What are your expectations for cross-Strait film exchanges?","We have noted this situation. We support and encourage the film circles on both sides to strengthen exchanges, learn from each other, make up for each other's shortcomings, enhance mutual understanding, jointly promote Chinese culture, and make the Chinese nation's film industry stronger and bigger. I believe this is also the voice of filmmakers on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Taiwan’s TransAsia Airways recently announced that it will suspend flights and dissolve. Public opinion holds that the sharp decline in mainland tourists to Taiwan was the last straw that broke TransAsia Airways. What is the spokesperson’s comment? In addition, yesterday the Civil Aviation Administration of China released arrangements for cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights for 2017 and said that the…","On the first question, we have noted that Taiwan's TransAsia Airways has suspended operations, and we have also noted that there are various analyses and commentaries from different angles within Taiwan regarding the reasons for the company's suspension. On the second question, due to changes in the situation in Taiwan this year, the business-level meeting between the competent authorities on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to discuss strengthening cross-strait civil aviation transport cooperation has not been held again. Taking into account the travel needs of people on both sides of the Strait to travel and return home for the holidays, the two sides' agreed contacts have made relevant arrangements regarding Spring Festival extra flights through an exchange of letters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","First question: Hong Kong customs recently seized nine Singaporean armored vehicles that had participated in military training in Taiwan, and the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council has also responded to this. How does the mainland Taiwan Affairs Office evaluate this? Second question: media recently reported that Hung Hsiu-chu will visit the United States after Trump takes office. How does the mainland view this?","On the first question, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude, and I have no new information to provide.\nOn the second question, our position on Taiwan's external activities is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The South China Sea sovereignty issue is one that both sides of the Strait care deeply about, and Taiwan's “Coast Guard Administration” and other relevant parties held a humanitarian rescue drill yesterday in the waters near Taiping Island in the South China Sea. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on this?","The Nansha Islands, including Taiping Island, are China's inherent territory, and Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have a responsibility to jointly safeguard this ancestral property. We will closely monitor the actions of relevant parties involving Taiping Island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","Could the spokesperson say whether the Taiwan authorities have made contact with the mainland about joining the RCEP? If Taiwan is willing to join the RCEP and the “Belt and Road” strategy, what is the mainland's attitude?","Regarding Taiwan's participation in regional economic integration: In the past, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” and against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, we expressed willingness to explore feasible ways to strengthen cross-Strait economic cooperation and Taiwan's participation in regional economic integration, and the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council made contact on this matter. But as everyone can see, after “5?20,” the situation has changed. If the one-China principle cannot be upheld, political mutual trust across the Strait will no longer exist, and the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation will be delayed, this will inevitably have an adverse impact on this issue. As for the “Belt and Road,” we have stated many times that we welcome Taiwan's industrial, commercial, and business circles to participate in the construction of the Belt and Road.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201611/t20161130_11640012.htm"],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公报大公网记者","Recently there have been reports that “Hong Kong independence” figures who had their Legislative Council membership revoked plan to write to Tsai Ing-wen asking her to intervene in Hong Kong affairs. In addition, a DPP legislator has proposed that the Taiwan authorities pay more attention to Hong Kong affairs. Moreover, the Mainland Affairs Council has recently made frequent remarks on Hong Kong affairs. What is…","What you have raised once again shows that \"Hong Kong independence\" elements and \"Taiwan independence\" forces are colluding in an attempt to stir up trouble in Hong Kong. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially those in Hong Kong, must remain highly vigilant. The words and deeds of Leung Sung-hang, Yau Wai-ching and others run counter to Hong Kong's mainstream public opinion and to the fundamental interests of Hong Kong residents, and relevant parties in Taiwan are lending them support. What exactly do they intend? We advise the Taiwan side not to comment on Hong Kong issues, not to interfere with the implementation of \"one country, two systems\" in Hong Kong, and not to undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","We note that the so-called “cases of mainland China obstructing Taiwan’s international space” on the Taiwan authorities’ foreign affairs department website, after being blank for eight years, were relaunched on November 22. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The international community handles Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle. Violating this principle, the matters cited on that website will certainly not work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","The Chinese Air Force recently organized air units to conduct training in the far seas of the Western Pacific according to plan, and some Taiwan media hyped that “mainland fighter jets circling Taiwan once is putting pressure on Taiwan.” How do you view this issue?","As I understand it, the PLA's recent training in relevant airspace in the Western Pacific was a routine arrangement within the annual plan. For specific details, you may consult the Ministry of National Defense.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","On the grounds that diabolo is Chinese culture, a DPP legislator recently questioned whether promoting diabolo amounts to “helping the mainland’s united front work.” What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","I believe everyone has noticed that “Shifang chelling” has recently become a major super joke in Taiwan’s political circles and public opinion. Is it satirical? Behind the satire is a reflection of the spiritual split of those who are the driving force behind “de-Sinicization.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声记者","Recently, some pan-Green elected representatives proposed inviting the Dalai Lama to visit Taiwan, claiming it would “make the mainland jump up and down and act irrationally.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have repeatedly reaffirmed that we firmly oppose the Dalai Lama's activities in Taiwan in any form. If certain people or forces try to exploit this matter to deliberately create incidents, it will inevitably cause serious damage to cross-Strait relations, and they must bear the responsibility they should bear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","These past two days, Taiwan and Japan have been holding negotiations on an economic partnership agreement, but cross-Strait negotiations on trade in goods have come to a complete standstill. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? In addition, regarding the mainland's procurement from the eight Blue-camp counties and cities: some on the island have pointed out that there are also Blue-camp townships within…","I have already addressed the second question: as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of county- and city-level exchanges, we all hold a positive attitude.\nRegarding the first question, we firmly oppose Taiwan and our diplomatic partners developing official relations and signing agreements with sovereignty implications. This is our consistent position. As for the stalling of the cross-Strait trade in goods agreement, I think that as time goes by, cross-Strait compatriots, especially Taiwan compatriots, will increasingly feel that, for political reasons, the Taiwan side has lost a precious opportunity for prosperous development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Mr. Yu Keli, former director of the Taiwan Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, recently said in a media interview that during Ma Ying-jeou’s administration, political relations across the Strait actually regressed, and the KMT authorities gave up the long-term goal of unification. Does this mean the mainland’s evaluation of Ma Ying-jeou has changed?","We will not comment on the personal views of scholars.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Media recently reported that Soong Chu-yu, Taiwan's representative to APEC, pointed out that his meeting with President Xi Jinping at the APEC summit lasted only one minute, not the ten minutes they claimed. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's view on this?","In fact, I have already explained this issue, and I want to stress three points. First, General Secretary Xi Jinping and Soong Chu-yu only exchanged natural, brief pleasantries. Second, the situation this year differs greatly from the situation after 2008 up until last year, and I believe everyone has noticed this. Third, the basis for improving and developing cross-Strait relations is adherence to the “1992 Consensus.” Because the Taiwan authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” positive interaction between the two sides is impossible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-11-30","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","According to media reports, Malaysia sent more than 20 Taiwanese telecom fraud suspects to the mainland yesterday. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council again called for seeking a solution together with the mainland. How does the TAO respond?","You may have already noticed that on November 29, our public security organs escorted back from Malaysia a group of telecom fraud suspects, including 21 Taiwan residents. For specific details, you may inquire with the relevant authorities. What I want to say is that, as in the past, this was a criminal gang composed mainly of Taiwan residents, with victims all being mainland people. Therefore, in order to punish crime according to law and protect the rights and interests of the victims, the mainland brought the suspects back for handling; everyone should be able to understand this. The MAC should consider why, since May 20, personnel from the two sides' police departments have not met or had contact again on cooperation in combating crime. Why have these Taiwan telecom fraud suspects repeatedly been treated leniently, so that victims' rights and interests cannot be protected? What they should reflect on even more is Taiwan's relevant regulations and Taiwan's political culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201611/t20161130_11640158.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-01","Geng Shuang","","Some sources in Taiwan said that China is approaching the Dominican Republic for the possibility of opening official ties with the Latin American country. Can you confirm this and give us more details?","There is but one China in the world. That is the consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1420605.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1420479.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-02","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that US lawmakers are considering putting in the National Defence Authorization Act for the 2017 fiscal year military exchanges between Taiwan and US officials. What is China's comment on that? Will that affect China-US relations?","We are severely concerned about this report.\nThe Chinese side strongly opposes any form of official interaction and military contact between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.\nThe Chinese side urges the US to abide by the one China policy and principles of the three joint communiqués, deal with the Taiwan question in a prudent manner, and avoid backsliding and damaging the larger interests of China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1420977.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1420901.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-03","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 3 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — In response to the phone call between U.S. President-elect Trump and Tsai Ing-wen, An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 3rd that the head of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on this. Small maneuvers on the Taiwan side cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the pattern of the international community's general recognition of one China. Our position of adhering to the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” is firm and unwavering. We have firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capacity to contain any form of “Taiwan independence,” and we will continue to advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161203_11642733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","About US President-elect Trump's phone call with Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen, you said on Saturday you have lodged representations with the relevant US side. Can you tell us exactly whom did you lodge the representations with? Is it the US government or the Trump transition team? How did they respond? How is the Chinese government's relationship with the Trump team at the moment? Do you have smooth contact with them?","Foreign Minister Wang Yi, Spokesperson of the Chinese Foreign Ministry and Spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office have already stated China's solemn stance on this matter over the weekend. As to what you asked, I can tell you that the Chinese side has lodged solemn representations with the relevant party on the US side both in Beijing and Washington. China has got its message across to the world as a whole with regard to Taiwan-related issues. The US side, President-elect Trump's team included, is also fully aware of China's solemn attitude on the issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Did you see Trump's tweets today? How do you respond?","I have answered a similar question. I believe you can understand China's position clearly through the remarks made by Foreign Minister Wang Yi, spokespersons of the Foreign Ministry and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. The sound and steady development of China-US relations serves the common interests of both peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Will Mr. Trump's call with Tsai Ing-wen change China's view of him?","I know that American media have made multiple comments on Mr. Trump's words and deeds during his campaign and after his election as the US president. But on China's part, we never comment on other countries' politicians and their personalities. What we are interested in commenting is his policies, especially the ones concerning China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Foreign Minister Wang Yi spoke about the call as a petty trick by Taiwan. Can you give some insight into the Foreign Ministry's view as to what motivated this call? Was this an inadvertent miscalculation or something more deliberate is at play?","I just answered a similar question. Instead of conjecturing about the considerations behind what was said and done, we only state our position on what was said and done.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","You spoke about the difference between Trump's statements and the policies he might pursue once he takes office in January. To what extent do his statements now have any predictive value in what he might do as President? Do you expect that his tweets suggest a tougher line on policies towards China? Do these tweets have any value in China as China assesses how it will pursue its relationship with the US after…","I did not say about differentiating what Mr. Trump says and does now with his future policies as president. This is your own judgment. What I said is that instead of conjecturing about the considerations behind what was said and done by President-elect Trump and his team, we only comment on things that have happened.\nAs we have been saying and as you all know, Taiwan-related issues remain the most significant and sensitive part in China-US relations. China-US relations have been moving forward for nearly 40 years since the establishment of diplomatic ties. The one-China policy and the basic principles embodied in the three joint communiqués between China and the US remain a solid political premise of the sound and steady development of bilateral relations and mutually beneficial cooperation. China-US relations and mutually beneficial cooperation will embark on a brighter future only if the two countries hold fast to this political premise.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Trump is likely to continue with this rhetoric. How do you actually assess these words and at what point will you change your position?","As I have said, we only state our position on concrete facts and China-related issues that are already there. Regarding President-elect Trump's call with Tsai Ing-wen, China's solemn position has been made clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Did the US notify China of Trump's call with the Taiwanese leader in advance?","The world knows clear the position held by the Chinese government on Taiwan-related issues. And I believe that President-elect Trump and his team are also aware of this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","How serious is Trump's call with Tsai Ing-wen? Were Trump to consider continuing some kind of dialogue with the Taiwan leader and changing the established protocol, what might the consequences be?","China's solemn position has been made clear right after the phone call.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","What is your reaction to reports that this call was planned weeks in advance?","As I said, we have already stated our solemn position on what has happened. China's firm stance and attitude on Taiwan-related issues is known to all, including President-elect Trump and his team I think.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Is China planning to punish the Tsai administration? Is China going to take further measures against the US apart from representations?","On your first question, I'd refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council as it's out of the remit of the foreign ministry.\nOn your second question, as we have been saying clearly, Taiwan-related issues remain the most important and sensitive part of China-US relations. The one-China principle serves as a solid political premise of the continuous, sound and steady development of China-US relations and mutually beneficial cooperation. We have presented our firm position to the relevant party in the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","Why shouldn't two democratically elected leaders speak on the phone?","I think your question is flawed.\nFirst of all, you may ask the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council about how Taiwan elects its leader and how the mainland views this.\nYou asked about why they shouldn't speak on the phone. If we look at remarks made by Foreign Minister Wang Yi, spokespersons of the Foreign Ministry and the Taiwan Affairs Office, we know clearly that the one-China principle is a consensus of the international community and a solid political premise on which other countries develop ties and conduct mutually beneficial cooperation with China. The one-China principle is not a hollow concept, and there are specific meanings attached to it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","关于美国当选总统特朗普与台湾地区领导人蔡英文通话，外交部发言人周六表示已向美国有关方面提出严正交涉。中方交涉对象是美国现任政府还是特朗普团队？美方是如何回应的？中方和特朗普过渡团队的关系如何，沟通是否顺畅？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","特朗普同蔡英文通话后又在社交媒体上发文，质疑中国货币政策，指责中国故意贬低人民币汇率、对美国进口产品征收高额关税并在南海建立庞大军事设施。中方对此作何解读、有何回应？中方认为他此举是个人背景导致的失误，还是美国新一届政府对华政策发生重大改变的信号？中方是否仍然认为特朗普是能被中国政府信任、能在未来四年开展合作的总统？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","特朗普和蔡英文通话是否会改变中方对特朗普的看法？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","王毅外长将特朗普和蔡英文通话称为“台湾方面搞的一个小动作”，你认为是什么动机促成上述通话？是无心之过还是有意为之？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","你提到要将特朗普的言行和他执政后所采取的政策进行区分，他现在的言行在多大程度上可以用来预测美国政府未来对华政策？他在社交发文是否表明他将对华采取更强硬的政策？这对于中方评估对美新政府政策有何价值？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","特朗普看来会持续发表这种言论，中方如何评估他的这些言论，在何时会改变立场？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","关于美国当选总统特朗普与台湾领导人通话事，中方事前是否得到美方通知？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","关于特朗普与蔡英文通话事，目前局势究竟有多严重？如果特朗普团队考虑继续同台湾地区领导人对话并考虑改变现状，你认为将造成何种后果？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","有报道称，特朗普与蔡英文通话是从几周前开始筹划的。你对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","中方是否会惩戒台湾当局？除了严正交涉外，中方还将对美方采取哪些措施？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-05","Lu Kang","","为何两位民选领导人不能通话？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1421494.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1421442.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2016-12-07","Lu Kang","","Tsai Ing-wen said to the US media yesterday that her phone call with Trump did not signal any change in policies and that everybody valued regional stability. What's your response?","I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for comments on what was said by certain people in Taiwan. Regarding US President-elect Trump's call with Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen, we have made multiple statements of our position here. There is no need for me to repeat.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1422213.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1422151.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-07","Lu Kang","","It is reported that the Chinese government has asked the US government to prevent Taiwan leader from making a stop-over in the US on her way to Nicaragua. Do you have anything to say on this?","I believe China's position is well known to all. As we have been saying on this podium, there is only one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing China and Taiwan is only part of China. This is a consensus reached by the international community, and also an important political pre-condition if other countries intend to grow ties and carry out mutually beneficial cooperation with China. Only on this premise can we grow smooth ties with relevant countries and move forward mutually beneficial cooperation. The so-called transit diplomacy is only a petty trick played by the Taiwan leader, whose hidden political agenda should be clear to all.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1422213.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1422151.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-09","Lu Kang","","The US Congress on Thursday passed the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017, incorporating for the first time contents on enhancing direct senior military exchanges with Taiwan. What is your response?","The Taiwan issue is a matter of principle bearing on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is also the most important and sensitive issue for China-US relations. China firmly opposes any official contact and military exchanges between the US and Taiwan or the US arms sales to Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear and well-known to the international community.\nSince the two houses of the US Congress raised such proposal separately early this year, we have on many occasions lodged solemn representations with the US side on these negative contents concerning China. Here I want to reiterate that China urges the US to abide by the one China policy and the principles of the three joint communique as well as its pledges, approach the Taiwan issue with prudence, and never go back on its historical commitments so as to avoid disturbance to the overall China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1422924.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1422879.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-09","Lu Kang","","Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen said today that Taiwan will staunchly defend its territorial sovereignty in the South China Sea and will not compromise sovereignty and the legitimate rights of the Republic of China. She also proposed to carry out seismic monitoring and climate change cooperation with neighboring countries with Taiping Dao as the center. Do you have any response?","Remarks made by political figures in Taiwan fall out of the remit of the foreign ministry. You may ask the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for comments.\nOn the South China Sea issue, I want to point out that China's historical rights and interests in the South China Sea are assets handed down from our ancestors, and the Chinese people across the Taiwan Strait share the responsibility to defend and preserve it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1422924.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1422879.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2016-12-09","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US House of Representatives and Senate recently passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017,” which for the first time includes content promoting high-level US-Taiwan military exchanges. What comment does the Chinese Ministry of National Defense have?","The U.S. Congress, disregarding the overall state of China-U.S. relations, has voted to pass the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017,” which contains negative provisions concerning China, including military exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. The Chinese Ministry of National Defense firmly opposes this.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and involves China’s core interests. China firmly opposes any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and Taiwan, and opposes U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. The U.S. Congress has forcibly turned back the wheel of history by pushing military exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. This practice interferes in China’s internal affairs, undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and damages China’s sovereignty and security interests. In the end it will also necessarily harm the interests of the United States itself.\nAs early as 1999, the U.S. Congress passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2000,” which restricted exchanges between the Chinese and U.S. militaries in 12 areas and artificially created legal obstacles to China-U.S. military relations. Today, the U.S. Congress has again passed a bill advocating exchanges between senior officers and civilian officials of the United States and Taiwan. This practice reflects the stubborn Cold War mentality and zero-sum thinking of certain people in the U.S. Congress. We urge the U.S. side to recognize the situation, immediately take effective measures to correct its mistake, and avoid further damage to China-U.S. relations and to relations between the two militaries.\nIt must be stressed that the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatists to undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity with the help of foreign forces will not succeed. They will only strengthen the resolve, confidence, and capability of the Chinese military to contain “Taiwan independence” and to advance the process of national reunification.\nWe reserve the right to take further measures.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2016-12/09/content_4766161.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2016-12-12","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that on December 11, US President-elect Donald Trump said in an interview that he fully understands the one China policy, but knows not why they have to be bound by it unless they make a deal with China having to do with other things, including trade. What is your response to that?","We have seen the relevant report, and we are seriously concerned about his words. The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and touches our core interests. Adherence to the one China principle serves as the political foundation for the development of China-US ties. If this foundation is wobbled and weakened, then there is no possibility for the two countries to grow their relations in a sound and steady way and cooperate on key areas. We urge the new US administration and leadership to be fully aware of the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question, stick to the one China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués, and approach Taiwan-related issues with prudence so as to avoid any serious disruption and harm to the overall interests of the China-US relationship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423512.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-12","Geng Shuang","","Mr. Trump said in an interview that his phone call with Tsai Ing-wen on December 2 was a very short one put into him. He questioned why should some other nation be able to say he can't take a call and thought it would have been very disrespectful not taking it. What is your comment on that?","As for the phone call, we have already made our position clear on many occasions. I would like to reiterate that the one China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations, and if this foundation is compromised, the sound and steady development of the bilateral relationship will be out of the question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423512.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-12","Geng Shuang","","Can you give us more specifics on the consequences of not sticking to the one China principle? What will happen if Donald Trump, for example, insists on direct leader-to-leader contact with Taiwan, and continues with these sorts of statements?","Our position on the Taiwan question is already very clear. Adherence to the one China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués is what the US promised us. We hope they can honor this promise. To stay true to this promise and properly deal with the Taiwan question is also a prerequisite for the sustained, steady, and sound development of China-US relations. The realization of the latter certainly relies on the fulfillment of the former.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423512.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-12","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that after the phone call between Trump and Tsai, the People's Liberation Army of China sent a bomber to fly over the South China Sea. What is the Foreign Ministry's response to this?","You need to ask the competent authorities for the specifics.\nChina has indisputable sovereignty over islands in the South China Sea and the adjacent waters. There is nothing wrong about carrying out normal activities within one's sovereignty.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423512.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-12","Geng Shuang","","Some reports say that the Taiwan leadership is planning to visit the US. What is your response?","We have noted these reports. We believe the US is well aware of our position on the Taiwan question, and we expect them to deal with it properly.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423512.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-13","Geng Shuang","","First, US President-elect Trump has tapped ExxonMobil CEO Rex Tillerson as the Secretary of State. What is your comment? Second, the US Defense Department said that China flew its H-6 bomber along the \"Nine-Dash line\" after Trump spoke with Tsai Ing-wen by phone. It is interpreted by some people in the US as a warning in response to Trump's remarks on China. What is your comment?","On your first question, we have noted the relevant reports. It is in the fundamental interests of the Chinese and American people if the two countries continue to develop their relationship in a sound and steady way. China is willing to work with the US Secretary of State, whoever it is, to move forward China-US relations at a new starting point.\nOn your second question, Chinese military aircrafts have been carrying out normal flight operations in the relevant airspace over the South China Sea, which we hope can be perceived correctly by the relevant party.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1423851.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1423773.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-14","Geng Shuang","","Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense of the US said that Taiwan should increase its defense spending to deal with the growing military threat from China. What is your comment?","China opposes any official contacts and military connections between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US side to stick to the one China policy and the principles of the three joint communiqués, and approach the Taiwan question with prudence so as to avoid unnecessary disruptions to the overall interests of the China-US relationship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1424188.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1424151.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-14","Geng Shuang","","An unidentified official of the National Development and Reform Commission reportedly said that China will soon punish a US car-maker for monopolistic behaviors. Can you confirm and do you have any details on this? Some people speculated that this is China seeking retaliation against US President-elect Trump's comments on Taiwan recently. What is your response?","I have no details to offer. If you would like to know more, you can ask the competent authorities. In principle, as we have been saying, China welcomes investment and business operations by foreign companies, including US companies in China. At the same time, it goes without saying that they must obey Chinese laws and regulations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1424188.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1424151.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","新华社记者","It is reported that U.S. President-elect Trump, in a recent interview, said he fully understands the one-China policy, but does not understand why the United States must be bound by the one-China policy, unless the United States and China reach an agreement on trade and other issues. What is your comment?","The Foreign Ministry spokesperson has already stated our position and attitude on this matter. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and involves China’s core interests. Adhering to the one-China principle is the political foundation for developing China-U.S. relations and the cornerstone of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. If this foundation is disturbed and undermined, the healthy and stable development of China-U.S. relations will be out of the question, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait will inevitably suffer serious shocks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161214_11653356.htm"],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","I would like to continue with the question of Trump's remarks involving the One-China policy. We note that after he made these remarks, within Taiwan, including some elected representatives of the DPP and the New Power Party, raised the question of whether the so-called “status quo” proposed by Tsai Ing-wen is also outdated, and whether Taiwan can be free of the One-China framework. May I ask the spokesperson for…","This remark fully exposes the essence of some political forces on the island, who are single-mindedly seeking “Taiwan independence” separatism, and their impatient mindset in pursuit of their “Taiwan independence” dream. What I want to stress is that there is only one China in the world; the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This has an indisputable legal basis and factual foundation, and it is also a reality recognized by the international community. Our position of adhering to the one-China principle and opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatism is firm and unwavering. On the issues of opposing “Taiwan independence” and opposing separatism, we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability. Facts will tell these people that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161214_11653355.htm"],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","I have two questions. Following the previous question: if Trump makes similar remarks in the future, will this affect our policies toward Taiwan? Second question: the character “变” (change) was chosen as the 2016 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year, while the character “苦” (bitter) became Taiwan’s Character of the Year. What is the spokesperson’s comment on these selection results?","Our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent, and the one-China principle is our basic guideline. Regarding your second question, the cross-Strait media selection of the annual Chinese character has been held for several years. This year there was one selected jointly by media on both sides, and also one selected by Taiwan media alone. This year's characters, such as “变” (change) for the two sides of the Strait and “苦” (bitter) for Taiwan, in fact reflect the tangible feelings of people on both sides about the development of cross-Strait relations and changes in the situation on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","央视海峡两岸记者","Reportedly, Tsai Ing-wen may transit the United States during her visit to Central and South America in early January next year. Spokesperson, what attitude does the mainland take on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on this. We have always handled Taiwan's external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose any attempt to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international arena.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161214_11653354.htm"],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","According to reports, a mainland scholar recently said that, on the basis of not violating the connotation of the one-China principle, the two sides across the Taiwan Strait could seek a new consensus beyond the “1992 Consensus,” and suggested that under certain conditions, the two sides could engage in contact that conveys messages and is controllable. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's attitude toward this?","Our position and attitude on upholding the one-China principle are consistent, clear, and unwavering. We stress the importance of the “1992 Consensus” for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations because the core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Only with this clarified can the two sides have a common political foundation and be able to engage in contact and interaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","中新社记者","The Haibawang Group recently issued a statement expressing firm support for both sides of the Strait belonging to one China. Some public opinion holds that the mainland, in implementing punishment of Taiwan businesspeople who support “Taiwan independence,” has begun to implement “differential treatment” against Taiwan businesses. The Taiwan authorities said they do not wish to see political factors interfere with…","You mention this matter. We understand that during recent food safety inspections on the mainland, relevant localities found obvious problems with products of the Haibawang company, and ordered the company to rectify in accordance with the law, and imposed penalties in accordance with relevant regulations. We have always attached importance to, and actively taken measures to protect, the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesses. At the same time, the production and business operations of Taiwan businesses should also comply with mainland laws and regulations. Here, I must reiterate that our attitude of encouraging and supporting Taiwan investment has not changed, but we will never allow a small number of people who make money on the mainland to support \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","According to reports, the two chambers of the US Congress recently each passed the 2017 National Defense Authorization Act, which includes provisions on exchanges between senior US and Taiwan military officers and officials. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of National Defense have already expressed our solemn position on this. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between our diplomatic partners and Taiwan. Our position on this is clear and consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","There are two questions. First, reports say that recently Wu Lipei, an adviser to Tsai Ing-wen's office, said in a meeting with Ye Wanghui, an adviser to a former US vice president, that he does not oppose using Taiwan as a chess piece to pressure the mainland, as long as the United States gives Taiwan preferential treatment in politics and economics. How does the mainland view such conduct by some people on the…","Your first question: Some forces on the island that stubbornly hold the \"Taiwan independence\" position and are hostile to the mainland, in order to realize their so-called \"Taiwan independence\" dream, have not hesitated to sell themselves out and rely on external powers for strength, willingly serving as bargaining chips and pawns for external forces to restrain and contain China. Such a mindset is truly one of \"not feeling shame but taking pride in it.\"\nYour second question: Yesterday was the National Memorial Day for the Victims of the Nanjing Massacre. We keep the national martyrs in our hearts and vow never to forget. That War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression was a nationwide war in which all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, fought bitterly and paid a tremendous national sacrifice. I believe the blood of the victims was not shed in vain, and history will also forever remember the martyrs who sacrificed for victory in the War of Resistance. Under the current cross-Strait situation, I think compatriots on both sides jointly commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance, remembering that history, and carrying forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, helps us join hands to jointly oppose all acts of splitting the country, and to jointly realize the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of our nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","联合报记者","Later this month, the eight Blue-camp counties and cities will hold an agricultural products exhibition in Beijing. I wonder what results the Taiwan Affairs Office hopes this exhibition will achieve? If Taiwan farmers in green-camp-governed counties and cities who endorse the “1992 Consensus” also wish to take part, what is the mainland's attitude?","Regarding the exhibition and sales of local specialty agricultural products and tourism promotion activities in the eight counties and cities, to my understanding, this activity is currently being prepared. The two sides also hope to use the holding of this activity to explore carrying out regular exchanges and cooperation under market mechanisms.\nAs for your following question, we have already stated our position on multiple occasions: regardless of which county or city in Taiwan, as long as it has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and county-city exchanges, and is willing to contribute efforts to enhance the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, we all hold a positive attitude.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan authorities, recently again stressed “transitional justice” at an event, stating that its essence is pursuing truth and reconciliation. What is the spokesperson's view on this?","I will not comment much on Taiwan's internal affairs. I think there has already been a lot of evaluation and discussion on this matter on the island. What is just and unjust cannot be decided by oneself alone; history will render its own verdict.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","大公报、大公网记者","Recently, some “Hong Kong independence” elements went to Taiwan to “spread independence,” and Taiwan residents reacted strongly, denouncing them as traitors and telling them to go back to Hong Kong. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Any form of “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” runs counter to the common will of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan and Hong Kong, and runs counter to the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. It should naturally be firmly opposed by all Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the issue of lifting restrictions on Japanese foods affected by the nuclear disaster has continued to flare up on the island. While the DPP authorities tout being “nuclear-free,” they are promoting imports of Japanese foods affected by the nuclear disaster, harming the interests of Taiwan residents. Some commentators have pointed out that the Taiwan authorities are turning down the mainland's sincere…","I think that on this matter, people from all sectors on the island have already made many criticisms and comments about the authorities’ mindset and practices, so I will not comment further.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","I have two questions. First, on food safety: Taiwan has recently considered lifting restrictions on food from Japan's Fukushima nuclear radiation zone. Has the Taiwan Affairs Office given any risk advice to the relevant authorities, or suggested reducing food imports from Taiwan? Second, in response to Trump's remarks and a series of small maneuvers by the Taiwan authorities, some experts have suggested refining…","Regarding food safety issues, we have always attached great importance. Relevant departments on the mainland will take necessary measures to safeguard the rights and interests of mainland consumers and protect the safety of people's lives and health.\nAs for your second question, our major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We adhere to the one-China principle, and our firm opposition to “Taiwan independence” is unwavering. The “Anti-Secession Law” is a law that both defends national territorial sovereignty and opposes and contains “Taiwan independence,” while also promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing national reunification. This law is a concentrated expression of the central government's major policies toward Taiwan and the will of all our people. It also reflects our consistent position of making the utmost sincerity and the greatest efforts to achieve peaceful reunification, and it demonstrates our firm resolve to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to resolutely oppose and contain any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We have noted that the controversy surrounding Taiwan's \"Academia Historica\" has continued to flare up in recent days. A Kuomintang legislator recently pointed out that the new rules not only prohibit scholars from the mainland, Hong Kong, and Macau from consulting materials, but also block Taiwanese scholars who wish to consult materials from the Chiang Kai-shek and Chiang Ching-kuo era. May I ask the…","We have also noted the relevant reports. As for the political factors behind this matter, I believe everyone can see very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","The Taiwan side recently said that compensation work for the 23 victims of the Liaoning tour group bus fire accident has been completed, but the family of one victim still refuses to settle. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation, and whether there are further safety measures for tourism to Taiwan?","When the incident occurred, the mainland side was highly concerned about the safety of the lives and property of mainland compatriots. On the one hand, we demanded that the Taiwan side quickly determine the cause and responsibility of the incident and handle the aftermath well; at the same time, we also demanded that the Taiwan side strengthen safety management and effectively protect the lives and property of mainland tourists in Taiwan. Regarding the handling of the aftermath, we respect the wishes of the families of the mainland victims. As for the follow-up arrangements you mentioned, I need to make further inquiries with other departments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","台声杂志社记者","Recently, a Taiwan fishing vessel, the “Jin Rui Yi No. 88,” capsized in heavy waves in the waters off Fugui Cape in New Taipei City. As of the morning of the 13th, media reports said that 2 mainland fishermen who fell into the water had been successfully rescued, but 5 people remain missing, including 3 mainland fishermen. May I ask whether the spokesperson has further information on this incident? In addition,…","As we understand it, after the incident, the China Maritime Search and Rescue Center and Fujian authorities promptly kept in contact with relevant Taiwan parties to learn about the search and rescue situation. According to information from relevant parties, there were 8 crew members on board in total. Two mainland crew members have been rescued, the Taiwanese captain died, and 5 crew members are still missing, including 3 mainland crew members. We hope the relevant Taiwan authorities will step up search and rescue efforts to locate the missing personnel as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","台湾中央通讯社记者","On the 6th, Tsai Ing-wen told US media that her phone call with Trump on the 2nd was meant to express Taiwan's respect for the US election and to congratulate him on being elected US president, and should not be interpreted as indicating a significant change in policy. She also emphasized that we all value stability in this region, and that good Taiwan-US relations are definitely conducive to peace and stability…","Regarding this matter, I have already made a very clear statement earlier. I want to emphasize again that our position of adhering to the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is unwavering. On the issues of opposing “Taiwan independence” and separatism, we have firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161214_11653363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions at the regular press conference on December 14, said that December 13 is the National Memorial Day for Victims of the Nanjing Massacre. The national dead are kept in our hearts, and we vow never to forget them. The War of Resistance against Japan was a nationwide war fought in blood by all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, at tremendous national sacrifice. The blood of the Chinese people who died will not have been shed in vain, and history will forever remember the martyrs who sacrificed for victory in the War of Resistance against Japan.\nAn Fengshan said that under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides jointly commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance, remembering that history, and carrying forward the spirit of the War of Resistance helps us join hands to jointly oppose all acts that split the country, and to jointly realize peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of our nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161214_11653350.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-14","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","At the regular press conference on December 14, An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions, stating: Recently, when relevant local authorities on the mainland conducted food safety inspections, they found obvious problems with the products of the Taiwan company Hai Ba Wang, and in accordance with the law ordered the company to rectify and imposed penalties in accordance with relevant regulations. We have always attached importance to and actively taken measures to protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan businesspeople; at the same time, the production and business operations of Taiwan businesspeople should also comply with relevant mainland laws and regulations.\nAn Fengshan emphasized: Our attitude of encouraging and supporting Taiwan businesspeople's investment remains unchanged, but we will never allow a small number of people who make money on the mainland to support \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161214_11653353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-15","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday French Foreign Minister said that Trump's comments on Taiwan were not very \"smart\". Do you agree with this comment?","Some countries have reaffirmed their commitment to the one China principle recently. We commend them for that. I want to reiterate that there is but one China in the world. Taiwan is a part of China. The government of the People's Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing China. Adherence to the one China principle is the prerequisite and foundation for friendly cooperation between China and other countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1424544.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1424499.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-19","Hua Chunying","","US President Obama advised President-elect Trump to be deliberate when making any change to the one-China policy, as the Taiwan question is crucial to China. Changing the one-China policy may push China to make significant response and he has to think through what the consequences are. We also noticed that German Chancellor Angela Merkel, French Foreign Minister Jean-Marc Ayrault and Australian Foreign Minister…","The one-China principle is a widely recognized consensus of the international community, and also the precondition and foundation for China to develop ties with other countries.\nThe Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China’s core interests. It is the most important and sensitive part in China-US relations. We hope that the relevant US party can fully understand the extreme importance and sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China policy and honor its commitment in the three joint China-US communiqués and handle Taiwan-related issues in a deliberate and proper way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425479.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425293.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-19","Hua Chunying","","US President-elect Trump previously questioned the one-China policy. But one of his aides said recently that since Trump is yet to assume the office, what he said does not mean that he is going to revisit the one-China policy upheld by the US right now. What is your comment on that? Do you think that the Trump team has somehow softened its position on the one-China policy?","I have already answered the question. Widely recognized by the international community, the one-China principle is the prerequisite and basis for the development of relations between China and other countries. The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is related to China's core interests, and remains a very sensitive and important issue in China-US relations. We hope that the US side will fully recognize the importance and sensitivity of the Taiwan question, uphold the one-China policy, abide by its commitment in the three joint communiqués and deal with Taiwan-related issues with prudence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425479.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425293.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-20","Hua Chunying","","Today the Taiwan authorities announced Tsai Ing-wen's visit to Central America next month without giving details about any transit stops in the US, as the final decision is yet to be made. Has the Chinese government recently been in contact with the US side to ask them not to allow Tsai Ing-wen to transit through the US?","The one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community, as well as our long-standing principle in dealing with issues about Taiwan's foreign interaction. We hope that the relevant country will approach Taiwan-related issues with prudence.\nAs for the Taiwan leader's possible transit stop in the US, I think her real intention is self-evident. We hope that the US side will abide by the one-China policy and principles established in the three joint communiqués, not allow her to transit through the US, refrain from sending any wrong signal to the Taiwan independence forces, and maintain the overall interests of China-US relations as well as peace and stability of the Taiwan Straits with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425745.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425658.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-20","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter's question: Taiwan's legislature recently passed in initial review an amendment draft of the Referendum Act, which sharply lowers the thresholds for all referendums. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 20 (reporter Zha Wenye) — An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 20th: After consultation between relevant parties of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, the two parties will hold a dialogue and exchange event in Beijing on December 23 to exchange views on issues related to the two parties and cross-Strait relations, actively implement the consensus reached at the meeting of the leaders of the two parties, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and maintain stability in the Taiwan Strait and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nIn addition,\nAn Fengshan responded to questions: We firmly oppose any force, in any way, including through so-called “legislation” or “amendment of laws,” carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities or opening the door for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161221_11659022.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","The government of Sao Tome and Principe reportedly issued a statement on December 20, declaring to sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan as of date. What is China's comment?","We note that the government of Sao Tome and Principe issued a statement on December 20 local time, announcing its decision to cut the so-called \"diplomatic\" ties with Taiwan. China appreciates and welcomes Sao Tome and Principe's return to the right track of the one-China principle.\nThe one-China principle bears on China's core interests and the feelings of over 1.3 billion Chinese people. It is also the prerequisite and political foundation for China to maintain and develop friendly and cooperative relations with other countries in the world. It has become the common aspiration of the international community and the trend of the times to adhere to the one-China principle. China is ready to develop friendly and cooperative relations with all countries on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence and the one-China principle.\nAs is known to all, the 26th Session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 in October 1971, making it clear that the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing China. The one-China principle recognized in the Resolution has become the general consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","Has the Chinese government promised financial aid to the government of Sao Tome and Principe to get it to ditch diplomatic ties with Taiwan? If you have offered money, can you give us an idea of how much? Also, when will the Chinese ambassador arrive in Sao Tome and Principe?","That is imaginative. I want to reiterate that the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing China. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle recognized in UN Resolution 2758 has become the general consensus of the international community. I believe that by cutting off \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan, the government of Sao Tome and Principe demonstrates its recognition of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","Sao Tome and Principe's decision leaves Taiwan with only 21 states having \"diplomatic relations\" with it, and 12 of them are from Latin America and the Caribbean. Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen will travel to several Central American countries in the near future. Is China in talks with any of those countries in Latin America and the Caribbean to talk them into adopting the one-China policy?","The one-China principle is the prerequisite and political foundation for China to maintain and develop friendly and cooperative relations with other countries in the world. It has become the common aspiration of the international community and the trend of the times to adhere to the one-China principle. China is ready to develop friendly and cooperative relations with all countries on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence and the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","Among all the states that have \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan, the Vatican is the one that is obviously intended to improve relations with China. Any new development in the negotiation between the Vatican and China on improving relations?","We have repeatedly said that we are ready to have constructive dialogues with the Vatican in accordance with the relevant principle. The line of communication between the two sides is smooth and effective. We will continue to make concerted efforts with the Vatican to move ahead with the improvement of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","Although Beijing has never openly recognized the idea of \"diplomatic truce\" brought up by the Ma Ying-jeou administration, it did not snatch countries having \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan over the past 8 years, which can be taken as acquiescence to \"diplomatic truce\". China is yet to establish official ties with Sao Tome and Principe, but analysts say that the era of \"diplomatic truce\" is over. What is your…","I would point you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for questions about cross-Straits relations. What I want to highlight is that there is but one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Chinese government stays committed to developing friendly and cooperative relations with countries around the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence and the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-21","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan blamed Beijing for luring Sao Tome and Principe to break up with it, and expressed strong dissatisfaction. What is your response?","I have been clear enough on this issue. There is but one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The one-China principle recognized in Resolution 2758 has become the general consensus of the international community. I believe that by cutting off \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan, the government of Sao Tome and Principe demonstrates its recognition of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1425994.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1425931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-21","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter's question: What is your comment on the statement by the governments of São Tomé and Príncipe deciding to sever so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 21 (reporter Zha Wenye). Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions on the 21st, said that the Foreign Ministry spokesperson has already stated our position and attitude on this matter. Our position of adhering to the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” is firm and unwavering, and will surely gain increasingly broad recognition and support from the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161221_11659085.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-22","Hua Chunying","","The Taiwan authorities said it can no longer satisfy Sao Tome and Principe's enormous need for financial aids, thus leaving Beijing an opportunity to wield dollar diplomacy over Sao Tome and Principe and get it to terminate ties with Taiwan. Taiwan is strongly discontent with that. What is China's response?","The one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community. It has become the common aspiration of the international community and the trend of the times. We appreciate and welcome Sao Tome and Principe's return to the right track of the one-China principle. It shows that justice will prevail.\nHow can the recognition of the one-China principle be bought with money?! The Chinese government never trades in its principles. As for remarks made by some specific figure from Taiwan, I can only say that they are assuming that others all harbour the same hidden agenda as they do.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426297.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426258.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-22","Hua Chunying","","The US State Department spokesperson said yesterday that both sides across the Taiwan Straits should promote peace and stability of their relations through dialogue, and urged all concerned parties to engage in a productive dialogue to avoid destabilizing cross-Straits relations. How does China respond?","I would point you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for questions about the cross-Straits relations. I want to stress that the one-China principle is not only the prerequisite and political foundation for China to develop relations with other countries but also the bedrock for peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits or the peaceful development of the cross-Straits relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426297.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426258.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-23","Hua Chunying","","Sao Tome and Principe has recently severed ties with Taiwan. Does China have a strategy for encouraging other \"diplomatic allies\" of Taiwan to abandon Taiwan and switch ties to Beijing?","I find your choice of words, like \"strategy\" and \"abandon\" interesting. Sao Tome and Principe's Prime Minister Patrice Trovoada told the journalists yesterday that breaking relations with Taiwan was the most correct decision for Sao Tome and Principe who has a commitment to the people to improve their living conditions. He also referred to the mainland as a very important strategic partner. I think the Prime Minister was telling a profound idea in plain words, that is, the one-China principle and win-win cooperation between China and Africa for common development is gaining momentum. If there is any strategy, that is to develop friendly and cooperative relations with other countries based on the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence and the one-China principle, conduct cooperation with other countries based on mutual respect, equal treatment and win-win spirit for the well-being of people from both sides and for the economic and social development of other countries. I will avail myself of the opportunity to commend the leader of Sao Tome and Principe for his remarks, and express our appreciation and welcome to the country's return to the right track of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426589.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426523.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-26","Hua Chunying","","US President Barack Obama signed into law the US National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017, which included a section on senior military exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this?","We are firmly against the Taiwan-related contents in the US act and have lodged solemn representations with the US. We are strongly discontent with the US for signing this act.\nThe Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territory integrity and falls entirely within China's domestic affairs. Although the Taiwan-related content in the US Act has no legal binding force, it still severely violates the three joint communiqués and interferes in China's domestic affairs. China will by no means accept this. We urge the US side to honor its commitment on the Taiwan question, put an end to military exchanges with and arms sales to Taiwan and avoid undermining China-US relations or cross-Straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426902.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-26","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan said that China's aircraft carrier Liaoning sailed through waters to the south of Taiwan today, please confirm. It is heard that Liaoning may head towards the South China Sea in the future. Could you provide more specific information?","According to Spokesperson Liang Yang of the PLA Navy,the Liaoning aircraft carrier battle group has set off for the Western Pacific on December 24 where it will take part in an open-sea exercise as part of an annual routine exercise plan. As for where else will the group head, I would refer you to the PLA Navy spokesperson.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426902.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-26","Hua Chunying","","You just stated that foreign ministers of China and Sao Tome and Principe signed a joint communiqué to resume bilateral relations, economic ties and trade included. How large will the bilateral economic and trade cooperation get? Many see Sao Tome and Principe's switch to Beijing as an end to the \"diplomatic truce\" between the mainland and Taiwan, and I am wondering what's your take on this?","On your first question, as I have said, the resumption of diplomatic ties between China and Sao Tome and Principe accords with the trend of the times and will of the people. We welcome Sao Tome and Principe's return to the big family of China-Africa friendly cooperation. We stand ready to act in accordance with the principle of win-win cooperation and common development, and carry out friendly and mutually beneficial cooperation with Sao Tome and Principe in various fiends with agriculture, fishery and tourism as the priority under the framework of the Forum on China-Africa Cooperation and the Forum for Economic and Trade Cooperation between China and Portuguese-Speaking Countries. The two countries are unequivocally positive about cooperation. And the scale of future cooperation depends on how specifically it is carried out.\nOn your second question, there is only one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing China, and Taiwan is an integrated part of the Chinese territory. The Chinese government is committed to growing friendly cooperative ties with other countries following the five principles of peaceful coexistence and the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426902.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-26","Hua Chunying","","After passing through the Miyako Strait, the Chinese aircraft carrier went on sailing southwest, which has raised concerns among some countries including Japan. What is the purpose of this training? Is it meant to target US President-elect Trump's attitude towards Taiwan?","Like I said, the PLA Navy spokesperson has put it clear that the training of the Liaoning group is part of the annual routine exercises.\nYou mentioned that some countries have expressed concerns about the purpose of this training. I don't think there is any need to read too much into it, such as assuming that it is targeted against anyone. I have seen a lot of reports including some carried by the Japanese media saying that the only way for Japan to reach consensus on any policy, action and public opinion is to make it target against China. But on the Chinese part, we develop policies and take actions according to our own needs. Relevant training by the Chinese side complies with international law and practices, and the Liaoning aircraft carrier is entitled to the freedom of navigation and overflight under international law. And we hope that all parties will respe ct this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1426902.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1426849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-26","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a question on the comment regarding the restoration of China–São Tomé and Príncipe diplomatic relations on December 26, after the government of São Tomé and Príncipe announced on December 21 that it was severing so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 26 —\nDoes this mean that the mainland is ending its “diplomatic truce” toward Taiwan? Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to a query on the 26th, said that the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already made our position and attitude clear. We have always handled Taiwan's external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle. Any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” is doomed to fail. The historical trend cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161226_11663338.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-27","Hua Chunying","","China's diplomacy has recently scored some major achievements: normalization of relations with Norway, Mongolia's commitment of no more Dalai's visits, Sao Tome and Principe's cutting ties with Taiwan and resuming relations with China yesterday. Bloomberg describes this as China's \"diplomatic hat trick\", and some US media say that China is making remarkable strides diplomatically using its economic power as a…","To start with, I'd like to thank relevant media for their interest in and acknowledgment of China's diplomacy. Speaking of economic power, as the largest developing country in the world, we are certainly not the most economically powerful yet. Thanks to our relations with other countries featuring mutual respect, equal treatment and win-win cooperation based on the five principles of peaceful coexistence, China's diplomacy is projecting a proactive and pioneering landscape. At the same time, China has the resolve and capability to safeguard its own core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1427046.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201612/t20161227_5414319.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-27","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan said that the Liaoning aircraft carrier is heading to Hainan Island. Do you know the details of where it is heading?","You may ask the Chinese military for details.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1427046.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201612/t20161227_5414319.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2016-12-28","Hua Chunying","","Interchange Association Japan, a non-governmental institution responsible for exchanges with Taiwan, will change its name to “Japan-Taiwan Exchange Association”from January 1. Do you have any comment?","China holds a consistent and clear position on the Taiwan question. We are firmly against any attempt to create “two Chinas”, or “one China, one Taiwan”, and are strongly discontent with Japan’s negative moves concerning the Taiwan question. China urges Japan to abide by principles enshrined in the China-Japan joint statement and its commitment to China, stick to the one-China principle, properly deal with Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from sending wrong signals to the Taiwan administration and the international community or causing new disruptions to China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1427260.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201612/t20161228_5414325.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear media friends, good morning, and welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office's last regular press conference of 2016. Thank you for your hard work! I am now willing to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Please describe the outcomes of the KMT-CPC dialogue and exchange activities held on December 23. In addition, what further plans are there to advance KMT-CPC exchanges in the next phase?","This dialogue and exchange event between the KMT and the CPC is an important measure to implement the important consensus reached at the meeting between General Secretary Xi Jinping and KMT Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu, and to improve and innovate the exchange platform between the two parties in response to the new situation. Both sides reviewed the course of the KMT and CPC jointly promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, focusing on three topics in their dialogue and exchange: inter-party exchanges at the grassroots level, cross-Strait youth and grassroots exchanges, and the protection of the rights and interests of people on both sides. They reached eight important consensuses through this, and achieved positive results. The content of these eight consensuses has been explained in detail in the event's press release. Here I will mainly introduce four aspects of the results:\nFirst, both sides stated that they will continue to uphold the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” Second, jointly strengthen and deepen exchanges between the two parties, including continuing to hold meetings between the leaders of the two parties, supporting the holding of the Cross-Strait Forum for Peaceful Development, improving and strengthening the working mechanism of the KMT and CPC for safeguarding the rights and interests of people on both sides, launching a dialogue and exchange mechanism between the two parties, and deepening inter-party exchanges at the grassroots level. Third, actively promote exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Taiwan Strait. Expand exchanges between young people and grassroots people on both sides; study and improve relevant policies for Taiwan youth to study, intern, seek employment, and start businesses on the mainland; and promote exchanges and cooperation in agriculture and fisheries, small and medium-sized enterprises, tourism, and other areas across the Strait. Fourth, continuously enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides. Actively support relevant counties, cities, townships, and grassroots associations in Taiwan that recognize the “1992 Consensus” in carrying out cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nOn the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the KMT and the CPC will continue to maintain close communication, give play to the role of the two parties' exchange mechanisms, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, implement the consensus reached at the meeting of the two parties' leaders and the concrete results of the two parties' dialogue and exchange, and work together to enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides and to safeguard and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161228_11665597.htm"],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","中新社记者","It is reported that the exhibition, sales and tourism promotion event for agricultural specialty products from eight counties and cities in Taiwan, held in Beijing recently, was very lively. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From December 24 to 26, the Taiwan Eight Counties and Cities Agricultural and Specialty Products Exhibition, Sales, and Tourism Promotion and Negotiation Fair was held in Beijing. More than 130 businesses from eight Taiwan counties and cities—New Taipei, Hsinchu, Miaoli, Hualien, Nantou, Taitung, Kinmen, and Lienchiang—brought their distinctive agricultural and specialty products to the exhibition. Beijing residents responded enthusiastically, and many people arrived early to wait for the venue to open. Sales at the exhibition booths were brisk, with many products sold out, and all exhibitors achieved satisfactory sales results and expressed anticipation for continued events in the future. It is also reported that, with a view to long-term cooperation, four procurement signing and tourism matchmaking negotiation sessions were held during the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161228_11665592.htm"],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","国际台记者","Tsai Ing-wen said that the mainland continues to suppress Taiwan's “international space” and that this has nothing to do with who governs Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Everyone has seen that since 2008, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides have promoted peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Against this backdrop, the two sides avoided unnecessary internal friction in handling foreign affairs. But since 5.20 this year, the situation of cross-Strait relations has changed. Because the DPP authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides belong to one China, they have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations and the political mutual trust between the two sides. This has severely impacted the good situation and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The impact is multifaceted, and I believe everyone can feel it. We have always handled Taiwan's external affairs in accordance with the one-China principle. Any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” is doomed to fail. The trend of history is irresistible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161228_11665596.htm"],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","A mainland scholar recently said that, on the basis of the one-China principle, the two sides across the Taiwan Strait could seek a new consensus beyond the “1992 Consensus.” Recently, a Taiwan scholar also proposed that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one Chinese nation” could become a new consensus for both sides. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","This is the personal view of a scholar. We have also noted that opinions on this topic have recently been diverse. What I want to stress is that our position of adhering to the one-China principle has been consistent, clear and unwavering. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China do the two sides have a common political foundation. The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” lies in recognizing that the two sides of the Strait belong to one China. Its importance lies in clearly defining the nature of cross-Strait relations, showing that the two sides are not a relationship between two countries. No matter what wording is used, it must not deviate from the core understanding that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. This core cannot be replaced. Only by returning to this position can the two sides have a common political foundation, and only then can they engage and interact and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161228_11665594.htm"],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Since May of this year, Taiwan's new ruling authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides belong to one China. This has undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and cross-Strait relations have since undergone a major shift from the active exchanges and cooperation of the previous eight years. Some commentators…","In fact, the causes of and responsibility for the current state of cross-Strait relations are clear to everyone. We adhere to the one-China principle, and our position of opposing “Taiwan independence” is unwavering. The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. If the Taiwan authorities truly have goodwill and sincerity in improving cross-Strait relations, they should return to the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” Only then can the two sides of the Strait engage and interact, and only then will cross-Strait relations have room to improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","Taiwan’s same-sex marriage equality bill recently passed its first reading, and same-sex marriage is formally moving toward legalization. The mainland has always encouraged and supported cross-Strait marriages and marriages between the two sides. If a same-sex couple from the mainland marries their Taiwanese partner in Taiwan, does the mainland recognize the legal validity of that marriage? Can they hold the…","Regarding Taiwan’s internal affairs, I will not comment. As for the legal matters involved in the question you raised, you should consult the relevant legal authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Regarding the recent routine training of the PLA Navy and Air Force, a former US Speaker of the House and important adviser to Trump recently said that the United States does not encourage Taiwan “independence,” but will never sit idly by if the mainland uses force against Taiwan under any circumstances. Public opinion on both sides of the Strait holds that this remark challenges China's “Anti-Secession Law.”…","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is China's internal affair and the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We hope the US side will abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","The Liaoning aircraft carrier passed through the first island chain, and Taiwan's side is very nervous. What is the spokesperson's evaluation? Another question: Recently, middle school students in Taiwan performed in Nazi uniforms on their school anniversary, provoking strong criticism from all sectors of Taiwan society. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","Regarding your first question, the spokesperson of the Navy has already given a specific explanation. On December 24 this year, the Liaoning carrier group of the People's Liberation Army Navy went to the western Pacific for far-seas training, which was organized and carried out according to the annual training plan.\nRegarding your second question, many comments have already been made on this issue on the island. I need to point out that Nazism in Germany and militarism in Japan were both the chief culprits of the profound disasters of World War II, and they should be unanimously condemned and repudiated by all humankind. If double standards are applied in historical judgment, and distortions and misleading are deliberately carried out in the fields of culture and education, this will only cause a spiritual void and confusion of values in society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","The US 2017 fiscal year National Defense Authorization Act included, for the first time, content on high-level US-Taiwan military exchanges. It is reported that in the future, US officials at the rank of assistant secretary and above, as well as active-duty generals and officers, may visit Taiwan, and the head of Taiwan's defense department may also break through the restrictions on visiting the United States.…","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on this. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is also the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan, and we firmly oppose US arms sales to Taiwan. This position is clear and consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","Chang Hsiao-yueh, Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, said in response to the issue of the new cross-Strait consensus that it must return to the “Constitution of the Republic of China.” What comments does the spokesperson have? In addition, after São Tomé and Príncipe established diplomatic relations with the mainland, some mainland media commented that if the Tsai administration continues to deviate from…","On your first question, regarding the so-called new consensus, I have already responded to this just now. Since May 20 this year, the Taiwan side has repeatedly said that the two sides should carry out dialogue and develop relations on the basis of “seeking common ground while setting aside differences.” Compatriots on both sides are actually asking: what exactly is the “common” in the “common ground” the Taiwan side refers to, and what exactly is the “shared understanding across the Strait” it speaks of? The Taiwan authorities ultimately need to make clear and explain these fundamental principles: the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations and the foundation for their development. Only by returning to recognizing the “1992 Consensus” and acknowledging the common political foundation that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development.\nOn your second question, our position on Taiwan's external exchanges is very clear. We adhere to the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence”; this position is unwavering and will certainly gain increasingly broad recognition and support from the international community. Any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Wang Zaixi, former deputy director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that the possibility of peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait is becoming smaller and smaller. How do you view his remarks? Another survey shows that if the mainland uses armed force against Taiwan, 66% of Taiwan’s people believe the Taiwan military cannot resist. How do you view this report?","Your first question: Since May 20 this year, cross-Strait relations have undergone major changes, which many experts and scholars are following closely and on which they have expressed their own views. What I want to emphasize is that our position of firmly upholding the one-China principle and resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is clear and consistent. We will, with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. At the same time, our position of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering, and we will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to separate Taiwan from China in any form or under any name.\nAs for the second question, I will not comment on specific public opinion polls on the island. But peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the greatest guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, while “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities are the greatest threat to cross-Strait peace and stability, and “using force to resist unification” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201612/t20161228_11665593.htm"],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the blue-camp counties and cities jointly organized groups to come to the mainland again and launched 20 blue tourism routes. However, the Taiwan authorities, on the grounds that the follow-up scouting groups of the eight counties and cities that visited Taiwan were “unnatural and overly politicized,” threatened to conduct strict reviews. What is the spokesperson's comment?","It is understood that relevant industries on both sides of the Strait are in negotiations and communication. We also hope such inspection activities will not be subject to unnecessary interference or obstruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","香港大公报大公网记者","Recently, media reported that the “Taiwan independence” New Power Party invited several so-called “self-determination faction” legislators from Hong Kong to attend relevant forums in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s response?","We have repeatedly stated our solemn position at previous press conferences. A small handful of “Taiwan independence” forces attempting to collude with “Hong Kong independence” to split the country will never succeed. As the saying goes, in this small globe, a few flies that hit the wall will only end up with bloody heads.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","Li Ta-wei, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities, said that Taiwan will make new friends and has a “pocket list.” Outsiders believe this means Taiwan wants to poach on the mainland's turf. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Any scheme to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" internationally is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","中评社记者","First question: regarding the dialogue and exchange mechanism between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party, will it be held once every few months? Or will it be held alternately on both sides of the Strait? Second question: the Taiwan Affairs Office once announced that card-type Taiwan compatriot permits could be used for self-service check-in and self-service ticket purchase at major mainland airports and…","The specific operation of the future Kuomintang-CPC dialogue and exchange platform requires further communication and consultation between the two sides.\nYour second question concerns the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit. This is a measure introduced by the mainland's public security authorities to respond to the wishes and demands of the broad Taiwan compatriot community and to facilitate them. Further improvements will follow. For specific arrangements and progress, I suggest you consult the public security authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Among the counties and cities governed by the Green camp in Taiwan, some residents who support the “1992 Consensus” have expressed hope to strengthen exchanges with the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have said that as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of exchanges between counties and cities on both sides, and is willing to contribute to promoting the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, we take a positive attitude. Among the results of the KMT-CPC dialogue and exchange activities I just announced, one item is that we will actively support Taiwan counties, cities, townships, and grassroots groups that recognize the “1992 Consensus” in carrying out cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation recently adjusted its secretary-general appointment, and part of next year's budget has been frozen and reduced. What is the spokesperson's view on this? In addition, what level of communication is currently maintained between the two organizations?","Since May 20 this year, because the Taiwan authorities do not recognize the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides belong to one China, the communication and consultation mechanism between the two organizations has come to a standstill. The reasons for this and where responsibility lies are clear to everyone. The Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) can only restore the continuity of the communication and negotiation mechanism between the two organizations if it receives clear authorization to confirm to ARATS that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, as the common political foundation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Taiwan has pushed an amendment to the “Referendum Act” and originally planned to include “change of territory” in it. Some public opinion holds that if this happens, it would be a substantive step by the Taiwan authorities from covert “Taiwan independence” toward overt “independence.” How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should maintain a high level of vigilance against any words or deeds that split the country. We firmly oppose anyone, any organization, or any political party at any time and in any way splitting any piece of Chinese territory away from China.\nIn a few days, 2016 will draw to a close and we will welcome the new 2017. Over the past year, the situation in Taiwan has undergone major changes, cross-Strait relations have once again been clouded, and the situation and achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations have also suffered serious shocks. Nevertheless, just as Director Zhang Zhijun said in his speech at the KMT-CPC dialogue and exchange event on December 23, although cross-Strait relations have encountered setbacks and new difficulties and risks, hope remains and the future is promising. As long as compatriots on both sides of the Strait recognize the trend of the times, unite, and adhere to the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the “dark clouds” hanging over the Taiwan Strait will eventually disperse. As Shelley wrote in a poem, “If winter comes, can spring be far behind?”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2016-12-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/closing)","","Taking this opportunity, once again I thank all media friends for your hard work and effort over the past year in promoting the development of cross-strait relations! I wish everyone, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait, a new year of good fortune in all things, happiness and peace. See you again next year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201612/t20161228_11665568.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2016-12-29","Hua Chunying","","According to Taiwan's \"foreign ministry\", Tsai Ing-wen will pass through the US when she visits Latin America. How do you comment on this?","The one-China policy is a consensus shared by the international community, and also a principle of how we handle Taiwan's engagement with foreign countries. We hope that relevant countries can carefully address Taiwan-related issues. As to the Taiwan leader's transit in the US, I believe her real intention is clear to all. We hope that the US side can follow the one-China policy and the three joint communiques, disallow the Taiwan leader's transit in the US, refrain from sending any wrong signal to the pro-independence force in Taiwan, and take concrete steps to uphold the overall interests of China-US relations and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1427498.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1427478.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2016-12-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The National Interest website of the United States reported on December 18 that China sent a H-6 long-range bomber to patrol the South Pacific area. Comments said that it is China’s way to make threat and express displeasure. Could you please confirm that? Secondly, recently the US President signed the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017, in which the military exchanges between the US and…","On your first question, the relevant reports are fabricated stories.\nOn your second question, we are resolutely against the Taiwan-related contents in the US National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017, and we have lodged solemn representations to the US. We are strongly discontent with the US for the signing of the Act.\nThe Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and is entirely China’s domestic affair. The above-mentioned US Act severely violates the three joint communiqués between China and the US, and interferes with China’s domestic affairs. China will by no means accept it. We urge the US side to abide by its commitments to the Chinese side on the Taiwan question and put an end to the military exchanges and arms sales to Taiwan, so as to avoid undermining the relations between the two countries and the two militaries, as well as the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait .\nYou mentioned the US’s decision to set up a propaganda center against China and Russia, I do not think it is a pure military issue. However, I have noticed that even some experts in Western counties also have doubts on such a decision.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2016-12/30/content_4768597.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-12-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the Aircraft Carrier Liaoning’s formation navigated through the south of Taiwan’s air-defense identification zone and joined forces with the South China Sea Fleet to conduct training and exercise. Taiwan said it would conduct close monitor and reconnaissance and other measures as a response. What is your comment?\nThere are also some media reports from Taiwan saying that the relevant training and…","According to my knowledge, the recent training of the Aircraft Carrier Liaoning’s formation in the West Pacific and other waters were all conducted according to the training plan, and the activities of relevant parties will not affect the normal navigation and training of the formation.\nYour second question is on the recent training and exercise by the PLA Navy and Air Force, in which the Taiwan question was also mentioned. We have a consistent and clear-cut policy and position on the Taiwan question. As for the relevant exercise and training activities conducted by the PLA recently, we have stated publicly again and again that these are regular and routine arrangements according to the training plan. Relevant training and exercises will help the PLA enhance its capability of deterring the Taiwan secessionist forces and safeguarding China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and are conducive to maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2016-12/30/content_4768597.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2016-12-29","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Over a month ago, a batch of armored personnel carriers (APCs) of the Singapore were seized by the Hong Kong Customs. The Singaporean side once voiced its hope for the return of these APCs at an early date. Have these APCs been returned to the Singaporean side after more than a month of coordination?\nThe second question is about the training of Aircraft Carrier Liaoning in the West Pacific. Taiwan’s “Defense…","About your first question, I do not have any new information to share at this moment.\nAbout your second question, we have stated many times that the training conducted by the Aircraft Carrier Liaoning and its formation is a routine arrangement within the PLA’s annual training program, and the areas for training include the waters of the West Pacific and other offshore waters.\nAbout the details of the training, the competent departments will release relevant information in due course.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2016-12/30/content_4768597.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-01-03","Geng Shuang","","On New Year's Eve, Trump was asked whether he would meet Taiwan's leader Tsai Ing-wen after taking the office. His answer was unclear and did not rule out the possibility of meeting her. Are you concerned? Have you been in touch with the Trump transition team to make China's position clear?","We keep stressing that the Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive one in China-US relations. We urge the US side to fully recognize the sensitivity of the question, stick to the one China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, cautiously and prudently approach Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from having any official contacts and exchanges with Taiwan. This position is very clear and explicit.\nAs for the second part of your question, China stays in touch with the Trump transition team. I believe his team is fully aware of our position on relevant issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1428102.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1428075.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-03","Geng Shuang","","Today, Japan's \"de facto embassy in Taiwan\" officially changed its name. The \"de facto Japanese ambassador to Taiwan\" said at the name-changing ceremony that currently Japan-Taiwan relations are at their best, and they should take further steps to develop a good relationship. Has China already lodged a protest with the Japanese side? How concerned is China about Japan's relationship with Taiwan?","First, I need to correct one thing. There is no so-called \"embassy\" or \"ambassador\", even though you prefixed \"de facto\" to them.\nWe firmly oppose all attempts to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\". We are strongly dissatisfied with the negative moves Japan has taken in the Taiwan question. My knowledge is that we have lodged representations with the Japanese side. China urges Japan to remain committed to the principles established in China-Japan Joint Declaration and the promises it has made to China, adhere to the one China principle, properly deal with Taiwan-related issues, and avoid sending wrong signals to the Taiwan authorities and the international community, nor causing new trouble for China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1428102.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1428075.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-04","Geng Shuang","","The so-called Taiwan \"Foreign Ministry\" yesterday expressed regret at and dissatisfaction with the deportation by the Vietnamese government of four Taiwanese suspected of transnational telecommunications fraud to the mainland on January 1. What is your response to that?","China and Vietnam have close cooperation on combatting cross-border crimes such as telecoms fraud. If you are interested in the specific case, you may contact the public security organ for an answer. Since remarks made by the Taiwan authorities do not belong to foreign affairs, I would point you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for the mainland's official position on that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1428274.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1428237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-04","Geng Shuang","","According to media reports, China will send its Liaoning aircraft carrier which is now training in the South China Sea to sail northward through the Taiwan Straits and circle around Taiwan during or after Tsai Ing-wen's visit to Central America, for the purpose of intimidating Taiwan. What is your comment?","I wonder where you get this piece of information. Yesterday I responded to a similar question. As for the specifics concerning the training of the Liaoning aircraft carrier, you can ask the military for more if interested. What I can tell you is that the carrier and accompanying ships are testing weapons and equipment and running exercises in the relevant waters of the South China Sea in accordance with their plan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1428274.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1428237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-06","Geng Shuang","","Is China behind the abortion of Greenland Trade Minister's planned visit to Taiwan last November?","We stand firmly against any forms of official contact and interaction between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic ties with us. The Chinese side appreciates Denmark's adherence to the one China principle. As Denmark's autonomous constituent country, Greenland should follow the foreign policy upheld by Denmark.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1428756.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1428721.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-09","Lu Kang","","On Sunday morning, Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen met with Senator Ted Cruz and Governor of Texas Greg Abbott during her transit in the US. What is your take on this?","I have taken note of relevant reports. I want to reiterate that we are firmly opposed to the Taiwan leader's contact with any US officials in any form and engagement in actions that disrupt and undermine China-US relations during the so-called transit. We once again urge relevant people from the US to abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three Joint Communiqués, and cautiously handle Taiwan-related issues so as not to harm the overall interests of China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1429155.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1429111.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-01-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 9 (reporter Qi Xianghui) — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 9th in response to a question: Mr. Qin Jinsheng, Secretary-General of the People First Party, has unfortunately passed away, and we deeply regret it and extend our condolences.\nIn answering reporters' questions, Ma Xiaoguang said: Secretary-General Qin Jinsheng devoted himself for a long time to promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and made great contributions to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Zhang Zhijun, Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Work Office, has already sent a telegram of condolence to Mr. Qin's family, expressing deep mourning for Mr. Qin's passing and extending sympathy to his family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201701/t20170109_11674022.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning, and welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office’s first press conference of 2017. At the beginning of the new year, on behalf of the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, I extend sincere greetings to all of you, and wish you smooth work, good health, a happy family, and success in all your endeavors in the new year. I will now take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","2016 has just passed. How do you evaluate the development of cross-Strait relations over the past year, and could you also look ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2017?","When we talk about cross-Strait relations in 2016, people will naturally think of the character \"change\" (“变”), which was recently selected as the annual character by mainland and Taiwan media, and also of the character \"bitter\" (“苦”), selected by Taiwan media as the annual character for Taiwan. The single character \"change\" summarizes how cross-Strait relations changed in 2016, while the single character \"bitter\" expresses Taiwan residents' personal feelings about the impact and consequences of that change.\nIn 2016, the political situation in Taiwan underwent major changes, and the situation in cross-Strait relations became more complex and grave.\nThe new Taiwan authorities refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" and did not recognize that both sides belong to one China. This undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, interrupted the communication and consultation and negotiation mechanisms across the Strait, affected achievements in all areas, and harmed the immediate interests of Taiwan residents. At the same time, \"Taiwan independence\" forces frequently carried out \"de-Sinicization\" activities, seriously threatening peace and stability across the Strait. Safeguarding the political foundation embodying the one-China principle, protecting the achievements of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area became the primary task for compatriots on both sides.\nIn the face of the new and complex situation, we have firmly and unwaveringly adhered to the central government's basic policies on Taiwan affairs and united compatriots on both sides to continue on the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. General Secretary Xi Jinping has made several important speeches, setting out the principled position of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, declaring the firm will and determination to oppose and contain any form of \"Taiwan independence,\" and expressing the sincere attitude of promoting civilian exchanges and cooperation across the Strait and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, thereby pointing the direction for the development of cross-Strait relations.\nOver the past year, we responded to challenges, pushed forward through difficulties, adopted effective policy measures, firmly opposed and contained all forms of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and waged resolute struggle against actions that undermine the common political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and seek to weaken and sever the ties between the peoples on both sides. We united Taiwan compatriots and all parties and groups in Taiwan that recognize that both sides belong to one China, carried out exchanges and dialogue, and strove to safeguard and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We continued to promote civilian exchanges and cooperation across all fields, advanced integrated economic and social development across the Strait, optimized policy environments for Taiwan youth and Taiwan residents to study, intern, work, start businesses, and live on the mainland, and continuously built a community of shared destiny across the Strait.\nLooking back at 2016, the changes in cross-Strait relations profoundly reveal that only by upholding the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, can cross-Strait relations advance steadily over the long term and can compatriots on both sides share in the well-being; abandoning this political foundation would cast dark clouds over the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots. It fully demonstrates that safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism is the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan compatriots; that strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, fostering kinship, and achieving mutually beneficial win-win outcomes is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides; and that any attempt to sever kinship ties or weaken and cut off the connections between Taiwan and the mainland is unpopular.\nLooking ahead to 2017, uncertainties and risks and challenges facing the development of cross-Strait relations have increased. We will continue to adhere to the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, and maintain the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We will firmly oppose any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area. We will study and introduce policy measures that facilitate Taiwan compatriots' study, employment, entrepreneurship and life on the mainland, advance the common interests of compatriots on both sides, and strengthen emotional bonds. Compatriots on both sides are participants, promoters, and beneficiaries of cross-Strait relations. We believe that with the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, we will certainly be able to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly contribute to realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201701/t20170111_11676209.htm"],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","At her year-end 2016 press conference, Tsai Ing-wen recently said that the mainland is stepping back, one step at a time, to the old path of dividing, suppressing, threatening and intimidating Taiwan. She also said she hopes the two sides can sit down and talk to find a way to solve the problems. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","Since May 20, 2016, we have stated many times that our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan will not change with shifts in Taiwan’s political situation, including uniting compatriots on both sides to continue the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations; adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and firmly safeguarding the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations; and continuing to advance exchanges across all fields across the Strait, deepening economic and social integration and development, and enhancing the well-being and kinship of compatriots. We have said this, and we have done this. But after the new ruling authorities in Taiwan took office, they have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” do not recognize that both sides belong to one China, undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, tolerated all kinds of “de-Sinicization” “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, weakened the common interests and ties of compatriots on both sides, and insisted on heading back to the old path of confrontation before 2008. So, who is walking the main road, who is trying to take the old road or even a wrong path, the facts are very clear. The DPP authorities cannot shirk responsibility for the current unfavorable situation in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","Recently, some Taiwan media reported that thousands of Taiwan enterprises have withdrawn from Dongguan. Dongguan once had more than 5,000 Taiwan-funded enterprises, which has now fallen to about 2,000, and the remaining Taiwan-funded enterprises are mainly engaged in traditional processing trade. Is this true?","According to our understanding, the relevant reports seriously deviate from the facts. Dongguan is one of the first places where Taiwan businesspeople entered the mainland and one of the most densely invested regions. Since 2008, the total number of Taiwan-funded enterprises in Dongguan has remained stable at over 3,400. As of the end of November 2016, there were 3,438 Taiwan-funded enterprises operating normally across the city. These enterprises are mainly in high-tech manufacturing; electronics and communications manufacturing, metal products, electrical machinery manufacturing, and special equipment manufacturing account for 53.8% of the total number of Taiwan-funded enterprises. In recent years, Taiwan businesspeople’s investment in Dongguan has continued to grow, with good momentum. In 2016, Dongguan newly signed 93 Taiwan-funded projects, with contracted use of Taiwan capital totaling US$313 million and actual use of Taiwan capital totaling US$287 million. We will, as always, continue to support Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in sustained and healthy development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","Could you briefly introduce the basic situation and main characteristics of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation over the past year, and what are your expectations for cross-Strait economic cooperation and exchanges in the new year?","In 2016, despite major changes in the situation on Taiwan and in cross-Strait relations, with the institutionalized consultation mechanisms between the two sides at a standstill and the environment for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation hit hard, through the joint efforts of cross-Strait business communities and compatriots on both sides, economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait remained generally stable and made positive progress. First, Taiwan investment in the mainland grew steadily. According to Ministry of Commerce statistics, from January to November 2016, the mainland approved 3,072 Taiwan-invested projects, a year-on-year increase of 19.58%; actual Taiwan capital utilized was US$1.687 billion, a year-on-year increase of 16.97%. The growth rates of Taiwan-invested projects and of actual Taiwan capital utilized were higher than the growth rates of foreign-invested projects and of foreign capital utilized in the mainland over the same period. A batch of key cross-Strait cooperative Taiwan-invested projects settled in the mainland and are progressing smoothly. Second, cross-Strait trade declined slightly but remained basically stable. From January to November 2016, cross-Strait trade totaled US$161.38 billion, a year-on-year decrease of 4.9%, a smaller decline than the drop in the mainland's overall foreign trade over the same period. The mainland remains Taiwan's largest trading partner, largest export market, and largest source of trade surplus. Third, the environment for young people from Taiwan to work and start businesses on the mainland kept improving, with more internship and employment opportunities. Taiwan businesses actively took part in the construction of the \"Belt and Road\" and eagerly positioned themselves and expanded markets.\nThe above situation shows that the mainland market holds valuable opportunities and remains the best choice for Taiwan business communities to operate and develop their enterprises. Economic cooperation across the Strait is mutually beneficial and has broad prospects, and cannot be blocked or weakened by any force.\nIn 2017, the mainland will continue to introduce a series of measures to deepen reform and expand opening up, including policy opinions on further expanding and attracting foreign investment, including Taiwan investment, and will also adopt further measures to lower enterprises' production and tax costs. These will all provide broader room for Taiwan investment and cross-Strait economic cooperation. Promoting integrated economic and social development across the Strait accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We will, guided by the concept that \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" share mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots. We hope that Taiwan business communities and Taiwan residents will firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" uphold the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and join hands to lift cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation to a new level.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Please introduce the basic situation of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2016, and what considerations there are for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in 2017 under the present circumstances.","In 2016, cross-Strait personnel exchanges continued at a certain scale, but some new changes emerged. According to incomplete statistics, Taiwan residents traveled to the mainland 5.73 million person-times, an increase of 300,000 person-times over 2015, a year-on-year increase of 4.2%. Mainland residents traveled to Taiwan 3.61 million person-times, nearly 800,000 person-times fewer than in 2015. Mainland resident tourism to Taiwan decreased 14.4% year on year, the first decline in eight years. Regarding the one-increase, one-decrease pattern in cross-Strait people-to-people travel figures, commentators argue that it was clearly affected by factors such as changes in the situation in Taiwan. The mainland has continued to adhere to its established major policies toward Taiwan, which has increased its appeal to Taiwan compatriots. However, changes in the Taiwan authorities' mainland policy have worsened the atmosphere for cross-Strait exchanges and affected the enthusiasm and willingness of mainland residents to travel to Taiwan.\nIn the past year, civil exchanges in all areas across the Strait continued to develop and showed “four more” characteristics. First, more fields of cross-Strait exchange and more points of contact between people on both sides. Second, more exchange activities at the grassroots level and among young people on both sides. Third, more experiential, interactive, and participatory exchange activities. Fourth, more and more Taiwan youth and students coming to the mainland for exchanges and internships to seek development opportunities. Civil exchanges across the Strait have deepened mutual understanding and kinship between compatriots on both sides, demonstrating the strong public will of compatriots on both sides to continue on the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nIn the new year, we will, as always, actively support and promote the expansion and strengthening of exchanges and cooperation in all sectors and fields across the Strait, and strive to give more Taiwan people and youth more opportunities and channels to participate in cross-Strait exchanges. We will take concrete measures to earnestly solve the practical problems faced by Taiwan residents in studying, interning, working, and living on the mainland, and create more convenient conditions for them to pursue their careers on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Reportedly, an archive recently released by relevant Taiwan authorities shows that Chiang Kai-shek once stated in his early years: “The legal status and sovereignty of Taiwan, before the peace conference with Japan is concluded, is merely the nature of a trusteeship territory of our country.” This matter has aroused widespread attention on the island. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of Chinese territory. This fact is beyond question. Attempts by “Taiwan independence” forces to make an issue of this are futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","There are reports that the mainland will treat Taiwan businesses differently in their investment and operations on the mainland according to their political positions. May I ask the TAO whether this is true? In addition, what is the TAO's attitude toward the development of Taiwan businesses on the mainland over the coming period?","For a long time, Taiwan business people and Taiwan-funded enterprises have made positive contributions to promoting cross-strait economic cooperation and the development of cross-strait relations. It is understood that the production and operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland are generally stable, and Taiwan investment on the mainland continues to grow. We have consistently encouraged and supported Taiwan-funded enterprises in producing and operating on the mainland, and we earnestly safeguard their lawful rights and interests. In recent years, localities and departments across the mainland have taken active measures to help Taiwan-funded enterprises transform and upgrade, and to help Taiwan business people solve practical problems they encounter in production and daily life on the mainland. This has been recognized by Taiwan business people.\nWe have stated many times that the vast majority of Taiwan business people oppose “Taiwan independence” and support the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Our attitude of strengthening cross-strait economic cooperation and encouraging and supporting Taiwan investment has not changed. At the same time, we will never allow a small number of people who make money on the mainland to support “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and undermine cross-strait relations. Going forward, guided by the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we will study and introduce relevant policies and measures, and actively promote the faster granting of equal treatment to Taiwan enterprises and mainland enterprises in investment and economic cooperation, so that more Taiwan compatriots can share in the development opportunities and achievements of the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201701/t20170111_11676206.htm"],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On the first question: dissatisfied with the DPP and the Tsai Ing-wen authorities' large-scale \"Taiwan independence\" actions or their tolerance of them, on New Year's Day a group of Taiwan residents from Nantou who support reunification of the motherland held a flag-raising ceremony in Ershui Township, Changhua, raising the flag of the People's Republic of China and the flag of the Communist Party of China. How…","On the first question: Realizing national reunification and national rejuvenation at an early date is the shared aspiration of all Chinese descendants at home and abroad. For any words or deeds on the island of Taiwan that oppose “Taiwan independence,” support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and endorse national reunification, we express affirmation and support.\nOn the second question: For a long time, we have actively encouraged exchange and cooperation between cultural and arts circles across the Strait, and have provided many policy conveniences for this. As long as exchange activities are normal and healthy, there is no so-called problem of “blocking, interference, and obstruction.” On the contrary, in recent years, there have been constant reports of mainland performing-arts personnel facing various restrictions and difficulties during visits, exchanges, filming, and performances in Taiwan, and even to this day mainland performing-arts personnel still cannot hold commercial performances in Taiwan. So I want to say that before holding up a mirror to others, one should first look at one’s own clothes and hat.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Taiwan’s largest social networking site recently held a vote on “What is the thing Taiwan people regret most in 2016?” 59% of respondents chose “voting for the DPP,” believing the DPP has not brought Taiwan’s people the good life they expected. What is the spokesperson’s view?","I think, since this is such a painful topic, it is better left for Taiwan netizens to comment on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","On the first question: Tsai Ing-wen said during a transit in the United States that the U.S. is continuing to persuade the mainland to resume dialogue and communication with Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's view? On the second question: some opposition legislators from Hong Kong recently attended an event in Taiwan at the invitation of the New Power Party, which triggered protests from the public in both Taiwan…","First question: I think everyone has noticed that the US side has consistently expressed appreciation for the efforts of both sides across the Strait, from 2008 until before May 20 of last year, to engage in dialogue and consultation and to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan region. I think US personnel should also understand that the basis for launching and sustaining this dialogue and interaction mechanism is that both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus.” Therefore, as long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and accepts the core meaning that both sides belong to one China, resuming cross-Strait dialogue and negotiation is not a problem. If the new ruling authorities in Taiwan cannot return to the right track, but instead go to foreign powers to file complaints, I think it will be of no help.\nSecond question: On this question, our spokesperson has already stated our position many times. “Hong Kong independence” elements are colluding with “Taiwan independence” forces, attempting to split the country and undermine Hong Kong's “one country, two systems” and its prosperity and stability. Such schemes are doomed to fail and are unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","May I ask the spokesperson: there is a rumor that this morning the aircraft carrier Liaoning passed through the Taiwan Strait. Outside observers believe this timing, coinciding with Tsai Ing-wen's overseas trip, was intended as intimidation. What is your assessment?","As we previously explained in response to questions, starting December 24, 2016, the PLA Navy's Liaoning carrier group conducted far-seas training in the waters of the western Pacific. This training was organized in accordance with the annual training plan. As for the situation you just mentioned, I cannot confirm it at present. If you are interested, you may inquire with the Ministry of National Defense and the Navy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Former Taiwan Vice President Wu Den-yih recently announced his candidacy for chairman of the KMT. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","We have also noted the situation of the Kuomintang chairmanship election. This is the internal affair of the Kuomintang, and we will not comment on it. What I want to emphasize is that since 2005, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, on the common political basis of opposing 'Taiwan independence' and adhering to the '1992 Consensus,' have established inter-party exchange relations. Since 2008, the Kuomintang has again governed Taiwan, and on this common basis, both sides have jointly promoted cross-Strait relations into a new situation of peaceful development. Therefore, in the future, we are willing to work with the Kuomintang to continue strengthening communication and positive interaction on this common political basis, to maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area, and to enhance the well-being of the peoples on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The “Small Three Links” (小三通) between Fujian and Taiwan has just marked its 16th anniversary. Passenger traffic last year exceeded 1.8 million person-trips, again reaching a new high. However, in the face of new changes in cross-Strait relations, the industry also has some concerns about the future of the “Small Three Links.” What is the spokesperson’s evaluation?","Our attitude of supporting the “three links” (“三通”) across the Strait is clear. As you just said, since the opening of the “small three links” (“小三通”), especially since 2008, they have played a very important role in the flow of people and goods across the Strait. In the future, as long as the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations does not further deteriorate, I think they should still be able to operate normally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The consumer confidence index for the four places across the Taiwan Strait released recently shows that the confidence index for the Taiwan region has declined, with all sub-indicators showing pessimism, and it ranks last. Some scholars have pointed out that the deterioration of cross-strait relations has had a great impact on Taiwan's economy. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","We will not comment on the scholars’ views or on certain internal situations in Taiwan. Far-sighted people in Taiwan and relatively fair-minded public opinion in Taiwan both believe that healthy and good cross-Strait relations are vital to Taiwan’s economic development and social stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","How does the mainland view Tsai Ing-wen's interactions with some pro-Taiwan figures in the United States during her transit through Houston?","The Foreign Ministry spokesperson has already stated our position. We firmly oppose any form of official contact between countries that have diplomatic ties with us and the Taiwan authorities, and we firmly oppose words and deeds that create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” internationally. We hope relevant persons on the US side will abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related matters prudently and appropriately, so as not to undermine the overall China-US relationship and further impact Taiwan Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Recently, a group in Japan calling itself a “friend of Taiwan” launched a petition campaign titled “Taiwan 2020 Tokyo,” aiming to support Taiwan participating in the 2020 Tokyo Olympics under the “Taiwan” name. On the island, some groups have also held a so-called competition for composing the anthem for the 2020 Tokyo Olympics Taiwan flag team. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The Olympics have long since resolved a series of related issues concerning Taiwan's participation. The Tokyo Olympics should strictly abide by the relevant Olympic rules, avoid creating complications, and not use political factors to interfere with the conduct of sporting events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","Some media recently reported that, amid the continued deterioration of cross-strait relations, the mainland may intend to gradually reduce or even suspend air and sea links across the Taiwan Strait, including “mini three links” and “big three links,” after 2017. Please confirm this.","We have stated many times that everyone is clear about our position and attitude on cross-Strait relations. As for the speculative remarks in Taiwan media that you mentioned, I will not comment here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Regarding Tsai Ing-wen’s trip this time, many media outlets believe that during this visit Tsai proactively clarified pro-green media reports about a meeting with Trump, did not meet with Trump or members of his team, and her overall performance was calm and restrained. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","I think this kind of meeting should never have happened at all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201701/t20170111_11676225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-01-12","Lu Kang","","The Nigerian government has recently closed Taiwan office in Nigeria and asked Taipei to move its office from Abuja, the capital city. During Foreign Minister Wang Yi's visit to Nigeria on January 11, foreign ministers of the two countries signed a joint statement on upholding the one-China policy, in which the Nigerian side reaffirmed its commitment to the one-China policy. Do you have any further comment on that?","As you said, the Nigerian government has recently made a political decision and taken a series of decisive measures against Taiwan office's violation of the one-China principle. It ordered Taiwan to rename its office, remove it from the capital, reduce its staff and have it disempowered. Nigerian government officials and institutions are also forbidden from having official contact with Taiwan. All these measures help settle the legacy issue that bears on the political mutual trust between China and Nigeria once and for all, and remove the stumbling blocks obstructing the sound development of bilateral relations.\nIn the joint statement signed by foreign ministers of China and Nigeria yesterday, the Nigerian government reaffirmed that the one-China policy is at the core of the bilateral strategic partnership, recognized that there is but one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China, while Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, promised not to have official relationship or official contact with Taiwan and underscored its support for China's reunification efforts. The Chinese side highly commends Nigeria's adherence to the one-China principle. It proves once again that the one-China principle meets the trend of the times and the shared aspiration of the people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430128.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430096.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-12","Lu Kang","","Commentary said that it is another action taken by the mainland to limit Taiwan's international activities following its restoration of diplomatic ties with Sao Tome and Principe. Is that true?","There is but one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Based on the one-China principle, countries like Sao Tome and Principe and Nigeria have come to a right political decision which lays a solid foundation and broadens the horizon for their political mutual trust and mutually beneficial cooperation with China as well as people's well-being. It serves the fundamental interests of people of relevant countries, complies with the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, and conforms to the international community's consensus and the trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430128.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430096.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-12","Lu Kang","","Taiwan said that it had never established \"diplomatic ties\" with Nigeria. China and Nigeria were misleading the international community by announcing the termination of \"diplomatic relations\" between Nigeria and Taiwan. Taiwan is in solemn protest against that. What is your response to that? Does China expect to see more countries joining Nigeria in requesting the closure of Taiwan offices in their countries?","On your first question, I would point you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for comments on Taiwan's response. It is not about foreign affairs.\nOn your second question, adherence to the one-China principle is an important political prerequisite for the development of relations between China and the rest of the world. China will point out with the slightest hesitation any violation of the principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430128.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430096.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-12","Lu Kang","","In his Senate hearing, Mr. Tillerson talked about the US commitments to Taiwan under the Taiwan Relations Act and the Six Issues Accord, saying that the US needs to reaffirm and live up to those commitments. But he also said the US has no plans to alter its one-China policy. What is China's view on his two-sided remarks?","Do you also think this is contradictory? (The journalist nodded.)\nI agree with you, and this is indeed contradictory. The so-called Taiwan Relations Act and \"the Six Assurances\" of the US are in serious violation of the US commitment to the one-China policy it made on the basis of the three China-US joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430128.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430096.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-13","Lu Kang","","It is said that the Chinese government would give back Singapore's armoured vehicles only if Singapore promised to cut off all forms of formal communication with Taiwan including military activities. Can you confirm that? It is also said that those vehicles have been handed over to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Can you confirm that?","On your first question, I want to reiterate China's position on that. First, all countries must abide by and honor their commitment to the one-China principle. This is the political prerequisite for the development of relations between China and the rest of the world. Second, countries should fully observe the law and regulation of the Hong Kong SAR.\nI would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for your second question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430511.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430401.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-16","Hua Chunying","","昨天蔡英文结束了对中美洲的“访问”，期间两次“过境”美国。但她没有见特朗普过渡团队的任何成员，也未与美政府成员有正式接触，尽管她确实见了个别政客并参访了推特总部。中方对奥巴马政府以及特朗普过渡团队成员没有会见蔡英文是否感到满意？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430903.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430855.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-01-16","Hua Chunying","","特朗普上周接受《华尔街日报》采访时称，一个中国政策可以谈判。中方是否就此事向特朗普过渡团队提出了交涉？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1430903.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1430855.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-01-18","Hua Chunying","","First, we notice that Vice Foreign Minister Liu Zhenmin met with Singaporean Permanent Secretary yesterday in Singapore, and they agreed to hold a meeting of the Joint Council for Bilateral Cooperation between China and Singapore next month. Does China plan to return the nine armored vehicles of Singapore detained in Hong Kong before the meeting? What are China's considerations? Second, You Xikun, former chief of…","For your first question, Liu Zhenmin, Vice Foreign Minister of China and Chee Wee Kiong, Permanent Secretary for Foreign Affairs of Singapore, held the tenth diplomatic consultation in Singapore on January 17th. The two sides exchanged views on bilateral relations, East Asian cooperation and other regional and international issues of common concern. The Joint Council for Bilateral Cooperation between China and Singapore you mentioned is a high-level cooperation mechanism between the two countries. The two sides keep close communication to find a proper time for a meeting of the joint council. The meeting has nothing to do with the armored vehicles. As I said yesterday when answering the question raised by a Taiwan journalist, the Hong Kong SAR government is handling this case in accordance with relevant laws and regulations.\nFor your second question, our position is very clear. China opposes any moves by the Taiwan authority for whatever excuses to send people to the U.S. to conduct activities that will disturb or undermine Sino-U.S. relations. We once again urge relevant parties in the U.S. to allow no delegation sent by the Taiwan authority to attend the inauguration ceremony of the president, and not to have any official contact with Taiwan. This message has been delivered to the sitting US administration and the Trump transition team.\nFor your third question, I have already answered similar questions. We noticed Prime Minister May's speech yesterday. We pay close attention to how the negotiation between the UK and the EU will play out, and hope the two sides can reach a win-win agreement through negotiation. China always supports the European integration process, and at the same time attaches great importance to the position and role of the UK. We are ready to further strengthen practical cooperation with the UK across the board for win-win outcomes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1431615.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1431555.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-19","Hua Chunying","","Tsai Ing-wen confirmed today that the Taiwan delegation will attend President-elect Trump's inauguration ceremony. What is China's comment on that?","I have answered this yesterday. We oppose any moves by the Taiwan authority for whatever excuses to send people to the U.S. to conduct activities that will disturb or undermine Sino-U.S. relations. We once again urge relevant parties in the U.S. to allow no delegation sent by the Taiwan authority to attend the inauguration ceremony of the president, and not to have any official contact with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1431978.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1431928.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-20","Hua Chunying","","There are reports that Yu Shyi-kun, former head of the Taiwan administrative organ, is now in the US for the inauguration ceremony of President Trump. What is China's comment on that?","I noticed that the U.S. government has reiterated many times that it only invites diplomatic envoys posted in the country to attend the presidential inauguration ceremony, and does not invite or encourage other countries or regions to send delegations to the ceremony. By blatantly hyping up the attendance of the so-called official delegation of Taiwan to the ceremony upon invitation, some people in Taiwan plot to disturb and undermine Sino-U.S. relations. We have for many times expressed our firm opposition to this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1432311.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1432226.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-20","Hua Chunying","","Kyodo news reported that Japan's Self-Defense Forces is planning a table-top exercise that would simulate a conflict between China and Taiwan. What is your comment?","I have seen relevant reports. For some people in Japan, it seems that the last thing they want is peace. We must solemnly stress that the Taiwan question, as part of China's domestic affairs, bears on the core interests of China. We hope that Japan can watch its words and steps on Taiwan-related issues, strictly abide by the principles in the four political documents between China and Japan, and avoid sending any wrong signal to the Taiwan-independent forces nor undermining regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1432311.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1432226.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-23","Hua Chunying","","What is China's expectation for the China-US relationship after Trump's inauguration? Does China have any expectation or demand for the new US administration on the Taiwan question and territorial issues such as the South China Sea?","History and practice have shown that a sound and stable China-US relationship serves the fundamental interests of the two countries and peoples, and contributes to the peace, stability and development of the Asia-Pacific and beyond. Despite some disagreements, China and the US share important interests in a wide range of areas. The two sides should respect each other's core interests and major concerns, approach and manage the disagreements in a constructive way so that they will not affect the overall relations between the two countries. We will work with the new US administration to secure sound and steady growth of bilateral relations in keeping with the principle of non-conflict, non-confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation.\nOn issues of territory, you all know that China holds a firm position on issues concerning its sovereignty and territory. We hope that the Chinese and American sides will respect each other's core interests and major concerns, approach and manage the disagreements in a constructive way to prevent them from disrupting the overall bilateral relations.\nOn the Taiwan question, I want to stress that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. Any US administration has the obligation to honor the commitment made by successive Republican and Democratic administrations to upholding the one-China policy, abiding by the three joint communiqués with China and strictly confining its relations with Taiwan to unofficial scope.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1433035.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1432971.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-25","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan's Central News Agency quoted Burkina Faso's Foreign Minister Barry as saying that people and companies with links to Beijing have been making offers worth of over 50 billion dollars for the country to dump Taiwan and switch recognition to Beijing, but Burkina Faso will not cut off the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. What is China's comment?","We noticed the report. This is absurd and fake.\nI would like to emphasize that the one-China principle, which bears on China's core interests and the feelings of the 1.3 billion Chinese people, can never be bought with money, and the Chinese Government will never trade on issues relating to the one China principle. The one-China principle, which is the prerequisite and cornerstone for China to develop its relations with all other countries, has become the general consensus of the international community, the will of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1434394.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1433835.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-01-25","Hua Chunying","","香港特区政府日前决定归还此前扣留的新加坡装甲车。这是特区政府独立作出的决定还是中央政府的授意？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1434394.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1433835.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-01-26","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan's Central News Agency quoted Burkina Faso's Foreign Minister Barry as saying that people and companies with links to Beijing have been making offers worth of over 50 billion dollars for the country to dump Taiwan and switch recognition to Beijing, but Burkina Faso will not cut off the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. What is China's comment?","We noticed the report. This is absurd and fake.\nI would like to emphasize that the one-China principle, which bears on China's core interests and the feelings of the 1.3 billion Chinese people, can never be bought with money, and the Chinese Government will never trade on issues relating to the one China principle. The one-China principle, which is the prerequisite and cornerstone for China to develop its relations with all other countries, has become the general consensus of the international community, the will of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1434397.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1434327.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear media reporters, good morning! Just after the Spring Festival, thank you all for taking time out of your busy schedules to attend the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. I am glad to answer your questions below.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","中新社记者","The 2017 Taiwan Work Conference proposed studying and introducing policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' study, employment, entrepreneurship, and daily life on the mainland. Could you introduce the relevant considerations and plans? Will these policy measures give Taiwan compatriots “national treatment”?","The 2017 Taiwan Work Conference held on January 20 called for research into and introduction of policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' study, employment, entrepreneurship, and life on the mainland. It is understood that these policy measures involve many aspects for Taiwan residents on the mainland, including employment and professional practice, social security, and convenience of daily life. Relevant departments are studying them according to the requirements of the conference, and once they mature, they will be announced and implemented one after another. We believe the introduction of these measures will create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots' development on the mainland and promote the integrated economic and social development of both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","Recently, a mainland tour group was involved in a car accident in Kaohsiung that injured 21 tourists, once again drawing attention to safety concerns about travel to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's view?","On February 4, a tour bus carrying 26 mainland tourists from Zhejiang crashed into a culvert in Kaohsiung, Taiwan, injuring 21 tourists. The relevant mainland authorities are highly concerned about this accident. The Taiwan Affairs Office and the Straits Exchange Foundation expressed sympathy to the injured, and together with the relevant parties, through cross-Strait civil tourism organizations, actively handled the aftermath. After the injured were sent to hospital for treatment, currently only one tour leader with more serious injuries remains under observation in hospital, and the other 25 tourists returned to the mainland on the afternoon of February 6.\nWe deeply regret and are seriously concerned about the repeated accidents that harm the lives and property of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan. We attach great importance to the safety of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan, and hope the relevant Taiwan authorities will effectively take concrete measures, strengthen safety management, eliminate safety hazards, protect the lives and property of mainland tourists in Taiwan, and provide a better tourism environment and conditions for mainland tourists.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","新华社记者","According to media reports, Tsai Ing-wen recently said at a Taiwan businesspeople's Spring Festival gathering that both sides should jointly chart a new model of cross-Strait interaction with new thinking and approaches. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. No matter how it is phrased, and whatever vocabulary is used, including so-called “new thinking,” “new approaches” or “new models,” the key is still to affirm the core understanding that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Only by acknowledging the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing the core meaning that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can the two sides engage in contact and interaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170208_11694495.htm"],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Tsai Ing-wen said at a Spring Festival gathering that both sides of the Strait should eliminate political interference and jointly safeguard the rights and interests of Taiwan businesspeople. Tien Hung-mao, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), said he hopes the mainland will not interfere with the operations of Taiwan-invested enterprises based on untrue rumors. What is the spokesperson's comment on…","We have consistently encouraged and supported the production and business operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland, attached great importance to protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland, and actively helped Taiwan businesspeople resolve practical difficulties and problems they encounter in production and daily life, supporting the legitimate operations and better development of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises on the mainland. We did so in the past and will continue to do so in the future.\nLooking back over the years, who has been obstructing and interfering with cross-Strait economic cooperation and Taiwan businesspeople’s investment on the mainland? I believe everyone sees this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","At the earlier Taiwan business fellowship meeting, Cai Yingwen said the second half of the year might be a good time for her to propose new cross-Strait policies. Please respond to this. Another question: US President Trump is now actively encouraging companies to invest in the United States, and Guo Taiming, chairman of the Foxconn Group, has also stated that he will strengthen investment in the US. Does the…","Regarding your first question, I think our position and attitude have been expressed very clearly. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can cross-Strait relations have a chance to return to the correct path of peaceful development.\nRegarding your second question, the current reform and opening up on the mainland holds enormous business opportunities and broad prospects for development and space. We will, as always, welcome and encourage the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople to invest, start businesses, and develop on the mainland, and will provide them with more convenience and opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Reportedly, some DPP members are preparing a proposal to remove the portraits of Sun Yat-sen and Chiang Kai-shek from New Taiwan dollar banknotes. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Since last year's “5.20,” this kind of crude farce has occurred from time to time on the island. As for the political scheme behind it, I would like to repeat a line we used at a previous press conference: “Sima Zhao's intention is known to every passerby.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","The 2017 Taiwan work conference has recently been held. Outside analysts believe this meeting conveyed signals from the mainland side to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to continue advancing civil exchanges and cooperation across all fields, and that the so-called “military reunification” was not included on the timetable. May I ask for the spokesperson’s views on this?","Our basic position on the Taiwan question is very clear and consistent. We adhere to the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.” We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. At the same time, our determination to safeguard the territorial integrity and sovereignty of the country is unwavering, and we will never allow “Taiwan independence” forces to split Taiwan from China in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","According to reports by Taiwan media, since the second half of last year the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan has fallen sharply, repeatedly hitting new lows, and businesses are suffering greatly. There is news that Taiwan's transportation authorities intend to relax restrictions on independent travel by mainland visitors, including raising the daily quota from 5,000 to 6,000 people, extending the…","Judging from the statistics over the past year, the number of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan has indeed declined. I believe that people from all walks of life can see very clearly the reasons behind this decline. Only the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations can resolve the problem; other approaches are like climbing a tree to catch fish.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","According to a recent public opinion poll released by Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, as many as 68.9% of respondents believe the mainland government is not very friendly toward Taiwan's authorities, a new high in nine years. What views does the spokesperson have?","Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear, and fully reflects our sincere goodwill in seeking peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation. In particular, since 2008, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides have opened a new era of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and compatriots on both sides have benefited together. I believe Taiwan compatriots should have deep feelings about this.\nSince May 20 of last year, however, because the Taiwan authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides belong to one China, they have undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, made the situation in the Taiwan Strait more complex and grave, affected the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and its achievements in all areas, and harmed the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. I believe that, whatever pretext may be offered, the Taiwan authorities cannot shirk responsibility for creating this situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","香港凤凰卫视记者","Yesterday, at the launch ceremony for Taiwan’s fighter aircraft manufacturing, Cai Yingwen said this is the first step in developing Taiwan’s so-called “defense industry,” and that “defense autonomy” is no longer “only hearing the stairs” (creak). What is the spokesperson’s assessment of this? In addition, Cambodian President Hun Sen recently said that Taiwan’s flag is not allowed in Cambodia and no official…","Your first question. Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee for maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, while pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nYour second question: the international community generally handles Taiwan-related affairs in accordance with the one-China policy, avoiding the creation of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” I think this is a natural matter.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","台湾《联合报》记者","The Japanese newspaper *Yomiuri Shimbun* reported that the mainland is currently considering amending the *Anti-Secession Law* or formulating a “National Unification Law,” and that the *Anti-Secession Law* may amend the conditions for using force against Taiwan. I wonder if you can confirm this report.","As we all know, on March 14, 2005, the Third Session of the 10th National People's Congress adopted the Anti-Secession Law. In the twelve years since the law was promulgated and implemented, it has played a very important role in opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The current situation in cross-Strait relations is complex and grave. We will continue to use the rule of law to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and we will never allow anyone, any organization, or any political party to split any part of China's territory from China at any time or in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the Taiwan People's Communist Party, which advocates the “1992 Consensus” and the One-China principle, was recently established in Tainan, drawing attention from outside. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","I do not comment on matters internal to Taiwan. We have stated many times that for any words or deeds on the island that oppose “Taiwan independence” and support the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and favor national reunification, we express agreement and support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","This year marks the 30th anniversary of Taiwan's opening of visits to the mainland by veterans. Looking back on the 30 years since the restoration of cross-Strait personnel exchanges, what lessons and reflections do you think this process offers both sides?","Looking back at the 30 years of cross-Strait exchanges and development, it should be clear that cross-Strait exchange is an unstoppable tide of the times, and the kinship of compatriots is something no force can tear apart or sever. Over these 30 years, the mainland side has consistently taken various measures to advance cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, driving cross-Strait relations into a new situation of peaceful development. However, since last year, although the various practices of Taiwan’s new ruling authorities have undermined the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and affected the atmosphere of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, they cannot block the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, foster harmonious kinship, and achieve mutually beneficial win-win outcomes.\nThe more complex the situation in the Taiwan Strait, the more we need to strengthen civil exchanges and cooperation in all fields. Through civil exchanges and cooperation, a strong public opinion will keep gathering and being displayed that opposes “Taiwan independence” and upholds the political foundation and correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We hope compatriots on both sides will, through strengthened exchanges and cooperation, make their feelings more harmonious, deepen exchanges and cooperation, and together contribute their efforts to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Two questions. First, this year marks the 70th anniversary of the “2·28 Incident.” Will the mainland side hold related commemorative activities? Second, the Taiwan Solidarity Union recently announced that it plans to invite Rebiya Kadeer to visit Taiwan in March and hopes to arrange a meeting between her and Tsai Ing-wen. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Your first question. According to our understanding, relevant mainland departments will hold a series of commemorative activities at that time.\nSecond question: as everyone knows, Rebiya is an ethnic separatist and a leading figure of the “East Turkistan” separatist forces. We firmly oppose Rebiya engaging in any activity in Taiwan in any form. “Taiwan independence” forces inviting such a figure to visit Taiwan, with the intention of creating trouble, will inevitably damage cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-08","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We have noted that the list for the re-elected so-called “Cabinet” of the Taiwan authorities was recently released, with Tsai Ing-wen’s cousin, Lin Mei-chu, appointed head of the Taiwan authorities’ labor department. This has once again sparked controversy on the island, and many people have criticized Tsai Ing-wen for “royal family” rule, and mocked that Taiwan may also see a “girlfriends’ gate” type of…","Regarding your first question, I will not comment on this internal personnel change in Taiwan. I think the people on the island of Taiwan have their own public judgment.\nRegarding your second question, our position is very clear: we firmly oppose conflating “refugee” and related issues with overseas Tibetans.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170208_11694475.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-02-09","Lu Kang","","This week, the Asia Society issued a report of experts from both Republicans and Democrats on China relations. It made a number of recommendations, including sticking to the one-China principle but taking a tougher line with China on certain issues. What is your reaction to that report?","We have repeatedly elaborated on China's principled position on the Taiwan question. It remains unchanged. The US should continue to uphold the one-China policy, adhere to principles established in the three joint communiqués between China and the US, and properly deal with Taiwan-related issues.\nThe report you mentioned covers a broad range of aspects of the China-US relationship. It shows that after nearly 40 years of growth, the relationship is now defined by common interests that converge more than ever before and by the extensive scope and great potential for cooperation. It echoes with our view that China and the US share extensive common interests and special responsibilities, and should expand cooperation and properly manage differences. That is the only way in which the relationship can truly deliver tangible benefits to people of the two countries and the rest of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1437227.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1437184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-02-10","Lu Kang","","Let us take a look at the one-China principle from a more positive angle. Previous analysis said that the Taiwan question was like a stumbling block between China and the new US administration. Now that the stumbling block has been removed, can we expect positive things for the bilateral relationship in the future?","China and the US take up nearly 1/4 of the world's population and about 1/3 of the world economy. Our two-way trade accounts for 1/5 of the world total. To develop a long-term, healthy and steady cooperative relationship between China and the US meets the fundamental interests of the people of our two countries, and the shared aspiration of the international community.\nI stressed that the one-China principle is the political foundation for the China-US relationship. It is vital for the healthy and steady growth of this relationship to firmly safeguard this political foundation. We hope the US side will properly handle issues related to Taiwan in keeping with the one-China policy and the three joint communiqués between China and the US, to ensure that the larger picture of the relationship is free from interruptions.\nTogether with the US, we will act in accordance with what our leaders have agreed to in their phone call, strengthen communication and cooperation to make our relationship a more fruitful one and better serve the interests of the people of both and all countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1437570.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1437497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-02-15","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that three Taiwan \"legislators\" are visiting India, and that a proposal was made by them to upgrade Taiwan office in India. Media reports say that by receiving the Taiwan delegation, India is \"taking revenge on China\". What is China's comment? Has China lodged representations with the Indian side?","We have long been opposing all forms of official contact and interactions between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China, as well as their mutual deployment of official institutions. This position is consistent and clear-cut.\nThe Indian side has made commitments on Taiwan-related issues. It is hoped that the Indian side will respect and understand China's core concerns, uphold the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and work with China to maintain the sound and steady growth of China-India relations. It is learnt that the Chinese side has lodged solemn representations with the Indian side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1438808.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1438768.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-02-15","Geng Shuang","","Further to what you said about China lodging representations, what exactly is it about? Is it about the Taiwan \"legislators\" visiting India, or about their proposal to upgrade Taiwan office in India? Why did China lodge the representations?","China's representations are related to what you said. The reason behind China's representations is obvious. We have been asking countries that have diplomatic relations with us to honor their commitment to the one-China principle. We also urged the Indian side in the representations to stick to the one-China principle and take concrete steps to maintain the sound and steady growth of China-India relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1438808.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1438768.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-02-15","Geng Shuang","","In what way has India violated the one-China principle?","As I said, we are firmly opposed to any forms of official contact and interactions between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. Those who are visiting India are so-called \"legislators\" from Taiwan. Their title says it all.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1438808.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1438768.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-02-17","Geng Shuang","","Former director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) said yesterday that US Marine Corps will be posted at the new AIT compound in Taipei as a symbolic expression of the US commitment to Taiwan. What is China's response to that?","We have just seen the report and have to get more information on that. I want to point out that the Chinese side opposes all forms of official contact and military interactions between the US and Taiwan. We hope that the US will abide by the one-China policy and principles prescribed in the three joint communiqués between China and the US, and properly deal with Taiwan-related issues in a prudent manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1439482.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1439397.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 22, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Everyone, good morning. Welcome to today's regular press conference of the TAO. I am happy to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","新华社记者","At the Chinese New Year get-together organized recently by the Taiwan Business Association, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun said that he would actively consider some proposals raised by Taiwan businesspeople for development on the mainland. May I ask whether there are specific plans and measures in this regard at present?","Director Zhang Zhijun has already stated very clearly in his speech at the Spring Festival gathering hosted by the Taiwan Enterprises Association. We will continue to adhere to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” share mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, study and introduce relevant policies and measures, create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots’ internships, employment, entrepreneurship and development on the mainland, and further promote integrated economic and social development across the Taiwan Strait and enhance compatriots’ kinship and well-being.\nRegarding some problems and demands that Taiwan businesspeople have raised about production and operations on the mainland, such as establishing a Taiwan businesspeople’s private bank to help Taiwan businesses and enterprises develop, and Taiwan businesspeople participating in the construction of the “Belt and Road” and assisting Taiwan enterprises in developing e-commerce and expanding the mainland’s domestic market, the TAO attaches great importance to these and is actively working with relevant departments to draft relevant policies and measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705914.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸栏目记者","We have noted that this month, tour bus traffic accidents have occurred one after another in Taiwan, and the safety of travel to Taiwan has drawn everyone's attention. What views does the spokesperson have on this?","We also note that in recent days, a series of tourist safety accidents has occurred in Taiwan. On February 13, a tour bus overturned in Taipei City, Taiwan, killing 33 Taiwan compatriots and injuring 12. After the accident, relevant departments on the mainland expressed deep concern. Responsible persons of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits both expressed deep condolences to the compatriots who died in this accident, and also sincerely extended sympathy to the injured compatriots and the families of the relevant persons.\nNot long before this accident, on February 4, a tour bus carrying 26 Zhejiang tourists collided with a culvert in Kaohsiung, injuring 21 tourists. On February 17, another tour bus full of mainland tourists emitted thick smoke from its rear while traveling during a trip in Taiwan; fortunately, there were no casualties. In addition, the incident of a mainland tourist's vehicle catching fire on July 19 of last year is probably still fresh in everyone's memory and lingers in their minds.\nWe are deeply concerned about the series of safety accidents during tourism in Taiwan. We also attach great importance to the safety of mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan. Human life is at stake. The relevant authorities in Taiwan should reflect seriously on what causes such problems to recur, and then take practical and effective measures to strengthen safety management, eliminate safety hazards, protect tourists' lives and property, and provide better travel environments and conditions for tourists.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705913.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Reportedly, the outbreak of highly pathogenic H5N6 avian influenza in Taiwan is continuing to expand. Spokesperson, how does the mainland prevent and control the spread of this type of outbreak?","It is understood that the mainland's inspection and quarantine authorities have been closely following recent epidemic situations in Taiwan through relevant channels. At present, the mainland has no trade in importing live poultry from Taiwan. To prevent the spread of the epidemic, the inspection and quarantine authorities have taken effective measures: closely monitoring the dynamics of the epidemic, strictly controlling quarantine at entry points, strengthening coordinated epidemic prevention and control, and preventing animal products from epidemic areas from entering illegally. At the same time, the inspection and quarantine authorities are making relevant quarantine technical preparations and strengthening port detection and defense capabilities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705912.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Reportedly, Taiwan's economic authority has dissolved the ECFA group and merged its related business. What is the TAO's comment?","The reason this issue you raised has drawn wide attention on the island, I think, is mainly that it reflects concern in Taiwan’s business community and public opinion about the current direction and future prospects of cross-Strait relations.\nSince 2008, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides’ associations have signed 23 agreements, including the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA), which promoted exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait and brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. However, since May 20, 2016, because the Taiwan authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides belong to one China, they have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation across the Strait. This has brought the cross-Strait communication, consultation and negotiation mechanisms to a standstill, affected the implementation of cross-Strait agreements, and harmed the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan’s business community. I believe this situation is one that business circles on both sides of the Strait do not wish to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","央视中国新闻记者","We noted that the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently published a set of data: from January to November 2016, the number of mainland personnel who went to Taiwan for economic and trade exchanges was 205,000 person-times, a year-on-year decrease of 24.8%, a very large decline. I would like to ask the spokesperson what comment you have on this decrease in numbers?","When the TAO spokesperson reviewed and took stock of cross-strait exchanges for 2016 in January, some basic points were already set out. According to statistics, in 2016 mainland residents made 3.6462 million trips to Taiwan, a decrease of 711,300 trips compared with 2015. Among them, mainland residents’ tourism to Taiwan declined for the first time since it was opened in 2008. In the same year, Taiwan residents made 5.73 million trips to the mainland, an increase of 300,000 trips compared with 2015. Regarding the one rise and one fall in cross-strait exchange figures, some commentators have argued that this in fact reflects the influence of many factors, including changes in the situation in Taiwan. The mainland has continued to uphold its established major policies toward Taiwan, which has enhanced their appeal to Taiwan compatriots, whereas changes in Taiwan authorities’ mainland policy have worsened the environment and atmosphere for cross-strait exchanges and affected mainland tourists’ enthusiasm and willingness to visit Taiwan. I think the changes in public sentiment reflected in this set of figures, one rising and one falling, are worth reflecting on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705910.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","台湾中天记者","Spanish government authorities decided to extradite all Taiwan-registered suspects involved in telecom fraud to the mainland, and several Taiwan departments, including the Mainland Affairs Council, have expressed protest. What is the mainland’s view?","Telecom fraud seriously harms the lawful rights and interests of victims, is deeply loathed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and has aroused public indignation. We have stated our position on the handling of Taiwanese suspects in cross-border telecom fraud on many occasions. I want to reiterate that, because the victims and the evidence are all on the mainland, all these suspects will be repatriated in accordance with the law and the entire case will be handled by us. This helps effectively combat telecom fraud and genuinely protect the rights and interests of victims. This approach has won widespread approval from people on both sides of the Strait and from the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705909.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Yeh Chu-lan, the newly appointed chairwoman of Taiwan's tourism association, requested on the 13th to visit the Taipei office of the Cross-Strait Tourism Exchange Association, and said that if she had the opportunity, she would very much like to visit the mainland, but she has not yet received a reply. Yeh Chu-lan believes this may be related to her personal party inclination. How does the spokesperson comment?","As everyone knows, the Straits Tourism Association (海旅会) is a civil trade association that provides services to the tourism sector and tourists on both sides of the Strait. We believe that matters of operations can be handled properly by its Taipei office on its own. I want to stress that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Our position of upholding the One-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism has been consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, recently Taiwan’s military carried out exercises simulating a mainland “decapitation operation” against Taiwan. How does the spokesperson evaluate this? Second, recently DPP legislator Kuo Cheng-liang said in an interview that Tsai Ing-wen’s proposal to handle cross-Strait relations according to the so-called “Constitution” and the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the…","Your first question: We have always been committed to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We have said many times that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, while \"Taiwan independence\" forces and their separatist activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If you are not pursuing \"Taiwan independence,\" what is there to fear? So the Taiwan authorities should still recognize the situation and return to the foundation of the \"1992 Consensus.\" Only then can they truly safeguard cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nYour second question: Our basic position on cross-Strait relations is very clear. Adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the basis for cross-Strait contact and interaction, and also the \"touchstone\" for testing the good faith the Taiwan authorities claim to have. Only when the Taiwan authorities return to the position of acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus\" and recognizing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can the two sides have a political foundation for interaction, engage in contact and interaction, and allow cross-Strait relations to return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen will take over as chairperson of the Chinese Culture Foundation next month. Some media vividly described it as Tsai Ing-wen taking “China” (中华) and then “removing China” (去中华). I wonder what the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment is on this? Is there still any possibility of exchanges with the Chinese Culture Foundation in the future?","We also noted this report. Whether this organization will in the future uphold promoting Chinese culture or pursue “de-Sinicization,” compatriots on both sides of the Strait will wait and see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","国际台记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, Kuomintang Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu recently told a Hong Kong media outlet that cross-Strait relations cannot be limited to economic topics, that political topics must also be discussed, and that a peace agreement should be used to eliminate the state of hostility between the two sides and seek lasting peace in the future. What is the spokesperson's view on this?","Under the one-China principle, formally ending the state of hostility between the two sides through cross-Strait consultations and reaching a peace agreement is our consistent position and proposition. On matters that conform to the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, both sides should actively promote them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Yang Sudi, former Director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office, has revealed that after AIT's new Taipei facility is completed and opened this year, the U.S. side will deploy Marines to be stationed there for security maintenance. What is the spokesperson's view on this? Second question: a former commander of the Taiwan Navy wrote a post saying that military circles speculate the U.S. military…","Regarding your first question, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs already stated our solemn position on February 17. Regarding your second question, this is a speculative report based on flimsy evidence. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. We firmly oppose any country selling arms to Taiwan or engaging in military cooperation with Taiwan; this position is well known.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","In previous years, Taiwan was able to attend the WHA and the ICAO meetings. Taiwan industry insiders are worried that this year Taiwan may no longer be able to attend these meetings. I would like to ask what the mainland's attitude is. Second question: Tsai Ing-wen mentioned that new cross-Strait policies may emerge in the second half of the year. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's view on her remarks?","Regarding your first question, our position on Taiwan's participation in international organization activities is very clear: under the one-China principle, arrangements shall be made through cross-Strait consultation.\nRegarding your second question, we already answered it at the last press conference. Our position is very clear: only when the Taiwan authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China will the two sides have a common political foundation, and only then will cross-Strait relations have a chance to return to the correct track of peaceful development. There is no other path than this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the Cai Yingwen authorities’ policy of launching the manufacturing of fighter jets has triggered questions. Some officials in Taiwan’s defense departments have pointed out that maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the key to safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait, while putting resources into manufacturing weapons squeezes the budgets of other civilian…","As I said earlier, the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Any act of “resisting unification by force” will certainly meet firm opposition from compatriots on both sides and is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705911.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the February 28 Incident. Every year around February 28, some people on the island of Taiwan use the occasion to hype it up. Recently, at a cross-Strait youth forum in Taipei, young people from both sides of the Strait jointly called on the relevant parties in Taiwan to face historical facts and promote ethnic integration. May I ask what attitude the spokesperson holds on this?","The February 28 Incident (2.28 Incident) that occurred 70 years ago was a righteous action by Taiwan compatriots to resist authoritarian rule and fight for basic rights, and part of the Chinese people's struggle for liberation. For a long time, this incident has been exploited with ulterior motives by some “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces on the island. They distort historical facts, stir up provincial-origin conflicts, tear apart Taiwan's ethnic groups, create social antagonism, and champion their “Taiwan independence” secessionist activities. Their intentions are extremely base.]","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170222_11705906.htm"],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","香港凤凰卫视记者","Continuing from the 2.28 issue just now: Last time you mentioned that the mainland would hold some commemorative activities. What commemorative activities will there be?","According to our understanding, on the morning of the 23rd, the Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League will hold a symposium in Beijing marking the 70th anniversary of the February 28 Uprising of the Taiwan people. You may inquire with the organizing unit about the specific arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","Recently we noticed that the leaders of two heavyweight Taiwan-related think tanks on the mainland have both been replaced, including the Taiwan Studies Institute of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences and the National Association of Taiwan Studies, and the current leaders of both think tanks have backgrounds in international relations research. Outside analysis holds that this means the mainland may consider…","This is the normal turnover and personnel adjustment of a Taiwan-related research institution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-02-22","An Fengshan","央视记者","On the evening of the 15th, Chen Chien-jen, Vice President of Taiwan's leader Tsai Ing-wen, attended a fundraising dinner held by a \"Taiwan independence\" organization, where he publicly stated that their goal is to make Taiwan a so-called \"normal country.\" May I ask what comment the spokesperson would make on this?","We have consistently and clearly stated that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s sacred territory, and that it has never been a country. We adhere to the one-China principle, and our position of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism is unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201702/t20170222_11705927.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2017-02-23","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Japanese government intended to revise its defense guidelines at an earlier date. Analysts pointed out that the purpose was to clear the way for Japan to deploy the THAAD system and the land-based Aegis missile defense system. What is your comment? Secondly, could you please update us on the first domestically-built aircraft carrier of China? It is said that the first domestically-built…","On the first question, we have noticed relevant report. Due to historical reasons, moves taken by Japan in the fields of military and security have always been followed closely by its Asian neighbors and the international community. We urge Japan to take history as a mirror, observe its commitment to the path of peaceful development, and do more to improve mutual trust with its neighbors and contribute more to regional peace and stability.\nOn the second question, people from all walks of life have been paying close attention to the development of China’s domestically-built aircraft carrier, and I share their interests as well. My colleagues have released information on the aircraft carrier on many occasions. I have no further information to offer right now.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2017-02/24/content_4773549.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-02-23","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to recent Taiwan media reports, former director of the Taibei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) said that when the new AIT building was completed and put into use in Taibei this year, the US side would send members of the Marine Corps to provide security protection to the venue. He also said it would be a symbol of the US commitment to Taiwan. What is your comment?","We have noticed relevant report, and we are consistently opposed to any form of official exchange and military contact between the US and Taiwan.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2017-02/24/content_4773549.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-02-23","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","There were reports that the US was intending to sell the THAAD system to Taiwan. Recently, Taiwan’s military denied those reports. Experts from the mainland commented that if Taiwan deployed the THAAD system, it would create a condition for the mainland to unify the country by force. What is your comment?","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already answered the question. It needs to be emphasized that the Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and touches our core interests. We are firmly opposed to any official or military contact between the US and Taiwan.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/HomePicture/2017-02/24/content_4773549.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-02-24","Geng Shuang","","Do you think Mnuchin is going to be an easier person to work with?","Treasury Secretary Mnuchin has been in office for a just few days. China looks forward to working with him and jointly moving forward China-US economic and trade ties and delivering benefits to the two peoples.\nAfter the press conference, the following question was raised: the National Institute for Defense Studies of the Japanese Ministry of Defense published its China Security Report 2017-the Dynamics of China-Taiwan Relationship written by experts in their own names. The report regards Taiwan as a state entity along with the mainland. What is your comment?\nGeng Shuang said that we have noted relevant reports and have lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side. I want to stress that the Taiwan question is China's domestic affairs and bears on China's core interests. We urge Japan to practice relevant principles and spirits enshrined in the four political document including China-Japan Joint Statement and honor its pledge on the \"one China\" principle with concrete actions, exercise prudence on Taiwan-related issues, refrain from sending any wrong signals to the Taiwan-independence forces and undermining regional peace and stability, and avoid creating new obstacles for the improvement of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1441435.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1441374.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-02-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions today, saying that Comrade Zheng Lizhong was removed from positions such as member of the Standing Committee of the 12th National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference for personal reasons, and that the relevant circumstances do not involve his performance of duties or work in the Central TAO, the State Council TAO, or the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201702/t20170227_11709628.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-03-06","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan announced today that the \"Association of East Asian Relations\" will change its name to the \"Association of Taiwan-Japan Relations.\" What is your comment on that?","I am not aware of the latest development. But we have expressed our position on other similar moves. The Chinese side holds a consistent and clear stance on the Taiwan question. We are resolutely opposed to any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\". The Chinese side urges the Japanese side to honor its commitment, adhere to the one China policy and properly deal with Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the four political documents including the China-Japan Joint Statement.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1443498.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1443469.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-03-20","Hua Chunying","","美方官员称特朗普政府正酝酿对台大规模军售计划，中方是否已就此向美方提出交涉？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1447096.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-03-27","Hua Chunying","","据报道，25日，日本总务副大臣赤间二郎访问台北，并出席“日本台湾交流协会”主办的日本文化宣介活动。有报道称，赤间此访系1972年以来日本访台的最高级别官员。中方对此有何评论？日方此举是否将给中日关系造成负面冲击？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201703/t20170327_5414650.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-03-29","Lu Kang","","According to media reports, on March 27, a woman, who seemed to be from Taiwan, was allowed entry at the Tokyo Haneda Airport holding a passport attached with a \"Republic of Taiwan\" sticker. What is your comment?","Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has responded to this issue from the perspective of cross-Straits relations.\nFrom the perspective of the foreign ministry, I want to state that the Chinese government opposes all forms of acts to seek \"Taiwan independence\" and that upholding the \"one China\" principle is a consensus broadly recognized by the international community. If some individual country plays petty tricks over this issue, it only further proves that it is at odds with the mainstream international consensus. The Chinese people remains highly vigilant. The Chinese side has lodged representations with the Japanese side over the relevant issue, asking the Japanese side to strictly stick to their commitments and not give any chance or space to any acts by those who seek \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1449905.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1449855.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-03-29","Lu Kang","","The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council responded today to the case of a Taiwan resident named Li Mingzhe being investigated by authorities of the mainland. Do you know his location and who is doing the investigation?","This question does not concern diplomacy. Affairs in the mainland, Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan are all internal affairs of China. Therefore questions over these affairs are not within our remit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1449905.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1449855.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Please introduce the relevant situation of the public memorial ceremony for the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum about to be held in Shaanxi. Which Taiwan guests will attend? Thank you.","Xuanyuan Huangdi is the cultural progenitor of the Chinese nation. Holding a public sacrifice to Xuanyuan Huangdi at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum during Qingming is a traditional grand event for Chinese descendants to “trace origins, seek roots, and forge the soul.” The “Ding You (2017) Public Sacrifice Ceremony to Xuanyuan Huangdi,” co-hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the State Council Overseas Chinese Affairs Office and the People's Government of Shaanxi Province, will be held solemnly on April 4 (Qingming Festival) at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum on Qiao Mountain in Huangling County, Yan'an City, Shaanxi Province. On that occasion, Mr. Chen Zhenxiang, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Mr. Yu Muming, Chairman of the New Party, and more than 200 grassroots residents and young students from central and southern Taiwan will jointly attend. We welcome friends from all walks of life in Taiwan to attend this grand ceremony, honor ancestors, revere forebears, and jointly inherit and promote Chinese culture. We also welcome the media friends present to go and cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201703/t20170329_11734563.htm"],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","We understand that the head of Taiwan's department in charge of external affairs recently said that cross-Strait relations are not “foreign relations,” and the head of the Mainland Affairs Council also said that “cross-Strait relations are just cross-Strait relations,” and that cross-Strait agreements are not “international agreements.” What is the spokesperson's comment? Thank you.","We have seen the relevant reports. The nature of cross-Strait relations is clear. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not relations between two countries. Only with a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations can there be any talk of improving and developing them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201703/t20170329_11734566.htm"],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","Reportedly, Chen Deming, Chairman of the ARATS, recently said that if he visits Taiwan, his identity should be an authorized representative of “two institutions of one country still governed separately.” Could the spokesperson further explain this?","Our basic position and propositions on cross-Strait relations are clear and have not changed. We will continue to implement the central government's major policy guidelines toward Taiwan, adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, firmly oppose and contain any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Reports say that Taiwan resident Lee Ming-che disappeared after entering Guangdong from Macau. Is the spokesperson aware of the situation? Thank you.","It is understood that Taiwan resident Lee Ming-che, suspected of engaging in activities that endanger national security, has been under investigation by relevant authorities and is currently in good physical condition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201703/t20170329_11734561.htm"],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","We note that Japan's Parliamentary Vice-Minister for Internal Affairs and Communications, Akama Jiro, recently visited Taiwan, and we also note that Japan has recently taken a series of actions related to Taiwan. How does the mainland view this matter? Thank you.","The Taiwan question involves China’s core interests and absolutely does not allow any challenge. The visit to Taiwan by a current Japanese vice minister seriously violates the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and we firmly oppose it. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already lodged stern representations regarding Japan’s recent wrongful conduct on Taiwan-related issues. I must point out that on the one hand the Taiwan authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” while on the other hand they attempt to challenge the one-China framework in foreign affairs. The more of these small maneuvers there are, the greater the backlash will be.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201703/t20170329_11734564.htm"],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","It is understood that relevant mainland authorities have issued opinions on applying probation under the law and community corrections to Taiwan residents who are being tried on the mainland for crimes. Please introduce the relevant situation. Thank you.","Thank you for your attention to this issue. On December 15, 2016, the Supreme People’s Court, the Supreme People’s Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice jointly issued the “Opinions on Issues Concerning the Lawful Application of Probation to Taiwan Residents Tried in the Mainland for Crimes and the Implementation of Community Corrections.” Taking into account actual cases involving Taiwan, these Opinions make special arrangements for the application of probation and community corrections to Taiwan residents tried in the mainland for crimes. Taiwan residents sentenced to control, parole, or suspension of execution outside prison that is subject to community corrections may also refer to these Opinions. The issuance of these Opinions is a positive response by the mainland side to the demands of Taiwan compatriots and helps protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. If you would like to learn more, please consult the competent authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","You just mentioned that Lee Ming-che's physical condition is good. May I ask where he is being detained? In which city? Because his wife wants to pass some money and medicine to him, I wonder whether these items can be delivered to him? On humanitarian grounds, could his wife be allowed to come to the mainland to visit him? Has ARATS received any letter from SEF? Thank you.","The TAO has noted some of the demands of Taiwan families. As for the relevant circumstances of the Lee Ming-che case, what I know at present is what was just disclosed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","I would like to follow up on the Lee Ming-che matter. How long will his investigation last? Will his family in Taiwan be notified, or can he hire a lawyer? Where exactly is he, and will the two sides consult on this? In addition, because the Lee Ming-che case has drawn much attention in Taiwan, it has made some people worry that their personal safety could be affected if they come to the mainland. Could you…","First, I must clarify that the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots who come to the mainland to engage in normal activities are guaranteed. We govern the country according to law and will not arbitrarily impose personal restrictive measures on Taiwan compatriots, so Taiwan compatriots can rest assured on this point: when they come to the mainland, their basic rights and interests are fully protected. Regarding Lee Ming-che's case, because he is suspected of engaging in activities that endanger national security, the investigation into him is being handled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","At the recently concluded two sessions, we saw that Premier Li Keqiang and Director Zhang Zhijun both mentioned providing more convenience for Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, in studying, working, starting businesses, and living on the mainland. May I ask the spokesperson how these convenience measures or policies are progressing? Thank you.","I think you have already seen that the Taiwan Affairs Office has granted plaques establishing 53 bases and demonstration sites for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland for employment and entrepreneurship, and many localities have also introduced all kinds of support policies covering startup funding, coaching and training, use of business premises, and many other aspects. Next, our relevant departments are also working hard to study and introduce measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwan youth, in coming to the mainland for schooling, employment, work, and daily life. These measures will be announced and implemented one after another within the year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","We have noted that Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen recently said at a public event that she hopes to establish an upgraded strategic partnership with the United States, and she also said that arms sales to Taiwan are an important pillar of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson’s comment on such remarks? Thank you.","First, we firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military exchange between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with us. There is no doubt about this. I would point out that as the gap in overall strength between the two sides of the Strait keeps widening, if the Taiwan authorities try to buy weapons from foreign countries, develop offensive weapons, or even put forward bluffing so-called military strategies to shield their erroneous political line, there is no way out. Engaging in an arms race with the mainland can only harm the well-being and interests of Taiwan compatriots. The fundamental guarantee for cross-Strait relations and the peaceful development of the Taiwan Strait is to oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” and adhere to the “1992 Consensus.” Therefore, we hope the Taiwan side will return to this correct track.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. Recently, a poll in Taiwan showed that the proportion of supporters of “Taiwan independence” has hit a ten-year low, and that among the surveyed young people aged 20 to 29, more than half want to come to the mainland to develop. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","Regarding a public opinion poll on Taiwan and the public opinion trend it shows, I want to make two points. First, this again shows that “Taiwan independence” runs counter to the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots and to the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, has no future, and therefore inevitably fails to win the support of the people of Taiwan. It also reflects the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan compatriots, which opposes “Taiwan independence” and supports the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Second, after 30 years of reform and opening up, the mainland has become the world's second-largest economy, providing a huge market and boundless potential for Taiwan compatriots who come to the mainland to develop their careers. Moreover, we have consistently pursued policies supporting cross-Strait economic cooperation and promoting cross-Strait economic and social integration, so it is not surprising at all that young people in Taiwan are willing to come to the mainland to develop. This shows that only compatriots on both sides of the Strait are a true community of shared destiny.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Recently we noticed that some Taiwan \"pro-independence\" advocates question the statement in the Cairo Declaration issued during World War II that \"Taiwan shall be restored to China.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","Taiwan has been a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory since ancient times. In 1895, Japanese militarists forcibly seized Taiwan through an unequal treaty and colonially ruled the Taiwanese people for as long as 50 years. With the victory of the Chinese people and the world anti-fascist alliance in World War II, and through a series of international documents such as the “Cairo Declaration” and the “Potsdam Proclamation,” Taiwan returned to the embrace of the motherland. This is beyond doubt.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Two questions for the spokesperson. Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan region, succeeded to the post of chairperson of the Chinese Cultural Association this month, and she has said she will strengthen cultural exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? The second question: at the Boao Forum, Vice Premier of the State Council Zhang Gaoli said that policies for economic…","Let me first address the first question. We have noted that not long ago the leadership of the Chinese Culture Promotion Association underwent changes. What understanding and attitude the new leadership and new leader of this association have toward Chinese culture is something that people from all walks of life across the Strait will watch closely.\nAs for the second question, you may have noticed that last year we revised the “Taiwan Compatriot Investment Protection Law,” reformed the management system, and implemented pre-establishment national treatment plus a negative list management model for Taiwan-funded enterprises. At the beginning of this year, the State Council issued Document No. 5, which set out 20 measures to expand opening to the outside world and actively use foreign investment. As I understand it, relevant departments are currently revising the Catalogue of Industries for Foreign Investment to further relax market access, and to treat domestic and foreign enterprises equally in areas such as standard certification, investment recognition, and procurement access. I want to emphasize that these policies fully and without reservation apply to Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","At an ice hockey match held in Taipei a few days ago, athletes from both sides of the Taiwan Strait came into conflict on the field. How does the spokesperson evaluate this incident of conflict? Second question: yesterday Director Zhang Zhijun said at the council meeting of ARATS that the challenges facing cross-Strait relations have increased and interference has multiplied. How does the spokesperson interpret…","First question: Such an incident should not have happened, and it is also something we do not wish to see. Any sporting event, including athletes on the field and spectators at the venue, should display good conduct, and no situation contrary to the spirit of sport should occur.\nSecond question: Yesterday, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) held the 4th plenary meeting of its 3rd council, and Director Zhang Zhijun delivered a speech. My understanding is that when Director Zhang said that cross-Strait relations face increased challenges and interference, he was primarily referring to the fact that since 2008, the common political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations established by both sides has been damaged since May 20 of last year. Because this foundation has been damaged, the “Taiwan independence” forces on the island and their activities have grown restless and frequent. If this were allowed to continue, the harm and impact it would bring to cross-Strait relations, to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and even to Taiwan's future, I think everyone is quite clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Recently, a reporter from Global Times, when entering the country at Haneda Airport in Tokyo, Japan, found that a woman’s “passport” bore a sticker reading “Taiwan Country,” and she was allowed entry by the Japanese side. What is the spokesperson’s view on this? Second question: recently, former Taiwan Vice President Annette Lu planned to visit Thailand, but Thailand refused to issue her a visa. What is the…","I will answer the second question first: the international community generally adheres to the one-China policy and handles Taiwan-related affairs on that basis.\nAs for the first question, as far as I understand, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already made stern representations to the Japanese side regarding a series of recent erroneous practices on Taiwan-related issues. That such an absurd thing as you describe has happened shows how deeply the “Taiwan independence” brainwashing has poisoned some Taiwan youth. But I think that no matter how far she travels around the world, I am afraid there is no place called “Taiwan Country.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","What I would like to ask is: While Taiwan compatriots enjoy the benefits brought by cross-Strait economic and social integrated development, what obligations should they also uphold? Thank you.","There is no doubt that Taiwan compatriots who live, work, start businesses, or study on the mainland must of course abide by local laws and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The spokesperson of the Straits Exchange Foundation said that if Chairman Chen Deming visits Taiwan, there will be no issue of foreign nationality status, and once again said that meetings between the heads of the two cross-Strait associations should not presuppose political preconditions. How do you evaluate this remark?","First, since Chairman Chen's trip to Taiwan involves no issue of foreign nationality status, you should say it loudly: both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and we are not a relationship between two countries. Second, throughout history, no negotiation or consultation has been without objectives, without direction, and without a common foundation. I remind the gentlemen of the SEF and the MAC to pay attention: on May 26, 2008, the SEF sent a letter to the ARATS agreeing to resume cross-Strait consultations as soon as possible on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” On February 11, 2014, the heads of the cross-Strait affairs competent authorities of both sides met in Nanjing and jointly stated that they would advance cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” and the Taiwan Affairs Office and the MAC established a regular liaison and communication mechanism. These facts are all black and white in writing, all spoken openly, and all can be verified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201703/t20170329_11734565.htm"],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Two questions. First, recently there have been many calls for “armed unification” from mainland netizens. May I ask the spokesperson: in the face of the grim and complex cross-Strait situation, how will the mainland maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations? Second, the 70th World Health Assembly will be held in May in Geneva, Switzerland, and all sectors in Taiwan are very concerned about…","Regarding the first question, we have already clearly explained it many times. We will continue to implement the Central Committee's major policies toward Taiwan, continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, and firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We will make our greatest efforts and with the utmost sincerity strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will also never allow “Taiwan independence” forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means.\nRegarding the second question, our position has also been stated very clearly: the issue of Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations must be arranged through cross-Strait consultations under the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Some public opinion on the island holds that the “Taiwan Boutique Exhibition” organized by the Taipei World Trade Center may find it difficult to continue on the mainland. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Thank you.","We have stated our basic position on cross-strait economic and trade cooperation very clearly. As for the specific details of the projects you mentioned, I am not familiar with them. But I can introduce that in the past, when inviting Taiwan business and industry groups to the mainland for exhibition and sales events, localities made relevant arrangements based on their own actual conditions and needs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the Kaohsiung District Prosecutors Office and the Kaohsiung Fifth Coast Guard Team recently joined forces to arrest 20 mainland fishermen in the waters off Dongsha. What response does the spokesperson have?","Regarding the arrest and detention by Taiwan's side of a fishing boat registered in Hong Kong and the mainland fishermen aboard, after the incident occurred, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) immediately contacted relevant Taiwanese civil organizations to learn the situation, expressed concern, and made representations. It also entrusted relevant Taiwanese civil organizations to visit the mainland crew members detained in Taiwan. The relevant Taiwanese authorities should respect the fact that fishermen from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, including those from Hong Kong and Macao, have long operated in traditional fishing grounds, stop treating them in this brutal manner, guarantee their lives and property, and release the people and the boat as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-03-29","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","First question: recently, the various parties and caucuses on the island have been squabbling bitterly over the review of the “Cross-Strait Agreement Oversight Act.” What is the spokesperson's comment? Second question: some commentators believe that the “security law” and “anti-infiltration law” that the Tsai Ing-wen authorities originally planned to draft amounted to “green terror,” and that the DPP intended to…","On the second question, I think your comment is very apt. Of course, using certain political means or political reasons to restrict cross-Strait exchanges, and to put pressure on Taiwan people engaged in cross-Strait exchanges, runs counter to the wishes of compatriots on both sides who call for stronger exchanges, and is also unpopular.\nAs for the “Cross-Strait Agreement Oversight Act,” we have stated our position many times. We oppose any act that undermines the basis of cross-Strait negotiations, interferes with or obstructs the negotiation process, or artificially creates obstacles to the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201703/t20170329_11734572.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2017-03-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports by Taiwan media Storm on March 27, starting this year, the first phase of the “Han Guang Exercise”, which is a computer-aided tabletop exercise, has been extended from five days to four weeks. It is also reported that starting from this month, services of the Taiwan military have started their computer-enabled tabletop exercises. In May, the so-called general staff headquarters of the Taiwan…","To recognize the 1992 Consensus and maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is conducive to the stability of the Taiwan Straits. The “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces and their activities are the biggest threat to the peace and stability in the Taiwan Straits. Any scheme to refuse the reunification by force is doomed to failure.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/DefenseNews/2017-03/31/content_4777094.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","国际台记者","A responsible official of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council recently said that the cross-Strait hotline has stalled because the mainland has no willingness and is one-sidedly refusing to communicate. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is an important basis for the establishment of the liaison and communication mechanism between the cross-strait affairs authorities of both sides, and it is a necessary condition for this mechanism to function normally. Since May 20, 2016, the Taiwan authorities have not recognized the “1992 Consensus” and have not agreed that the two sides belong to one China. This has undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and caused the interruption of the cross-strait liaison, communication, and consultation and negotiation mechanisms. The reasons and responsibility for this are very clear to everyone. The statement from the Taiwan side that you mentioned is a typical case of asking a question you already know the answer to, “knowingly playing dumb.” If the Taiwan authorities truly sincerely want to improve cross-strait relations, they should acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” recognize that both sides belong to one China, and return to the common political foundation of both sides. Only then can institutionalized cross-strait exchanges continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744562.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","新华社记者","According to reports, Taiwan's tourism industry figures recently said that the reduction in mainland visitors to Taiwan has stopped expanding, and mainland tourism to Taiwan is expected to gradually recover. What is the spokesperson's view?","I will not comment on the various claims within the industry. Everyone has seen that since May last year, the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan has dropped significantly, and tourism safety incidents have also occurred frequently. Relevant authorities in Taiwan should reflect earnestly on this. We have said many times that only the person who tied the bell can untie it (解铃还需系铃人). Only by truly finding the root of the problem can a solution be found.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744555.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","I would like to ask about the situation of the Lee Ming-che case. Did ARATS receive the medicine that Mrs. Lee handed over, and if so, was it passed on to Lee Ming-che? We are also very concerned about Lee Ming-che’s physical condition. Is he being detained in Guangdong? Mrs. Lee hoped to come to the mainland to visit him, but before boarding the plane she found that her Taiwan compatriot travel permit had been…","You have raised several questions. I know this matter has been heavily hyped on the island recently and everyone is paying close attention, so I would like to give a concentrated reply.\nRegarding the situation of Taiwan resident Lee Ming-che, who is under investigation by the relevant mainland authorities in accordance with law on suspicion of engaging in activities endangering national security, our office's spokesperson has issued statements to the outside world on March 29 and April 9.\nSince May 20 of last year, the cross-Strait liaison, communication, and consultation and negotiation mechanisms have been at a standstill; everyone is clear about the reasons and the responsibility. Under such special circumstances, in order to attend to the concerns of Lee Ming-che's family and on humanitarian grounds, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits entrusted a relevant Taiwan group, namely the Straits Exchange Services Center, to inform Lee Ming-che's wife of the relevant situation, and also forwarded handwritten letters from Lee Ming-che to his parents and wife. Some groups and individuals in Taiwan with ulterior motives have seized the opportunity to attack the mainland, create incidents, and interfere with the relevant mainland departments handling the case in accordance with law. Their aims will not succeed.\nHere, I would like to reiterate that this case concerns Lee Ming-che, who is under investigation by the relevant authorities in accordance with law on suspicion of engaging in activities endangering national security. The relevant mainland side is handling the case in accordance with law, and will protect the lawful rights and interests of the party concerned in accordance with law. If incidents are deliberately created with the intention of interfering with law-based case handling, this will only further complicate the issue and harm the interests of the party concerned. Relevant parties in Taiwan deliberately steer this case toward cross-Strait relations and maliciously attack the mainland, stoking the flames. This will only add insult to injury to cross-Strait relations, which are already extremely grave at present.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","A responsible person of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently said that “cross-Strait relations are cross-Strait relations,” and welcomed Chen Deming, Chairman of ARATS, to visit Taiwan in his capacity as Chairman of ARATS. The SEF has already extended an invitation for this. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this?","The mainland side's basic position and proposition of adhering to the one-China principle are clear; they have not changed and will not change. Regarding the issue of consultation and interaction between the two associations, we have stated many times that only when SEF is authorized to confirm to ARATS that it adheres to the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle can the liaison mechanism between the two associations be restarted and the heads of the two associations engage in exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744560.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","Yesterday, Mainland Affairs Council Chairperson Chang Hsiao-yueh mentioned that the mainland side has still not provided the Taiwan side with the details of the Lee Ming-che case in accordance with the agreements signed between the two sides and existing mechanisms. May I ask whether this means that the 23 agreements signed with the mainland during the Ma Ying-jeou period, including the cross-Strait agreement on…","The Cross-Strait Agreement on Joint Crime-Fighting and Judicial Mutual Assistance has played a positive role for many years, and this is plain to see. The agreement has clearly defined scope of application and operating procedures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744559.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Earlier this month, the Taipei District Court concluded the case of the “3.18” Sunflower Student Movement's occupation of the Legislative Yuan. The 22 defendants involved were found not guilty, which caused a huge shock on the island. Some Taiwan media and political figures have said that the DPP has opened the convenient door of “protesting against officials is justified, rebellion is not a crime.” What is the…","We note that this case has caused widespread controversy on the island. We also see that there are many in-depth and insightful commentaries on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","Will Director Li Wenhui of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office, who is set to travel to Taipei on the 14th, study the issue of this year's “Twin City Forum”? Please introduce the preparations for the “Twin City Forum.”","We have repeatedly stated that, as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, we hold a positive and open attitude toward cross-Strait city exchanges. As for this year's “Twin City Forum,” communication needs to take place between the Shanghai Municipality and the Taipei City government.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, regarding this China-US leaders' meeting, Taiwan authorities said the outcome was no surprise and matched what Taiwan had anticipated. What comment does the spokesperson have? Second, recently the fisheries departments of Taiwan and relevant Japanese authorities held a fisheries working group meeting. Taiwan asked Japan to recognize the fishing rights of Taiwanese fishermen around…","Regarding your first question, Foreign Minister Wang Yi has already given a detailed account of the meeting between the Chinese and US heads of state at Mar-a-Lago. For specific questions, I suggest you ask the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\nRegarding your second question, on the issue of Okinotorishima, the mainland’s position is very clear, and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","The establishment of the Xiong'an New Area in Hebei has drawn much attention. Spokesperson, will Taiwan businesses have the opportunity to participate in related construction and share in this policy dividend?","The establishment of the Xiong'an New Area in Hebei is a major decision and deployment to further advance the coordinated development of Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei. Whether enterprises are domestic or foreign, as long as their development direction conforms to the industrial plan of the new area, they can find their place to develop in accordance with the laws of the market economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744557.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","We have noted that this year, mainland dramas have drawn attention from young people in Taiwan and have won both praise and popularity. We have also seen that, according to Taiwan media reports, the Taiwan Chinese Television System (CTS) recently received a warning letter from Taiwan's National Communications Commission because its ratio of locally produced programming from January to March did not meet the…","I will not comment on the relevant practices on the island. Civilian exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, and the integrated economic and social development of both sides, serve the common interests of compatriots on both sides and are an unstoppable trend. Artificially erecting obstacles runs directly counter to the wishes and needs of compatriots on both sides to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","福建《海峡导报》记者","I have a question about exchanges. Mazu is a shared faith of people on both sides of the Strait. Recently, some “pro-independence” people on the island seem to be engaging in cultural severance, claiming that Mazu belief is a tool of KMT rule and that Taiwan people who come to the mainland to worship Mazu are more likely to be subjected to “united front” work. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this view?","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and Chinese culture is the common spiritual home of compatriots on both sides, just as we Chinese descendants all call ourselves descendants of Yan and Huang. Mazu has several million believers in Taiwan, and is a faith shared by believers on both sides. These are our common history, common culture, and common blood ties, and they are also our common roots and soul. Trying to play \"de-Sinicization\" tricks on this issue, with the aim of severing the connection between Taiwan and Chinese culture, is akin to trying to lift oneself off the Earth by pulling one's own hair—it is utterly futile and will certainly be opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170412_11744554.htm"],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Hsu Hsin-liang, Chairman of the Taiwan Asia-Pacific Peace Foundation, said that the opportunity to break the deadlock in the Taiwan Strait has always existed and that there is a chance for a thaw in the second half of the year. Does the spokesperson think his view is too optimistic?","The root cause of the current deadlock in cross-strait relations is clear to everyone. To break the current deadlock, untying this knot is actually quite simple: the Taiwan authorities need to genuinely show sincerity, acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” recognize that both sides belong to one China, and return to the common political foundation shared by both sides. Only then can the two sides engage in contact and interaction, and only then will cross-strait relations have a chance to return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","团结报、团结网记者","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the full-scale outbreak of the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. We have learned that Yu Mu-ming, Chairman of the Taiwan New Party, will attend the Yangtze River Anti-War Memorial Tour organized by the Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang next week. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of the relevant situation?…","I am not aware of the specific activity you mentioned. We have stated many times in the past that victory in the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was the result of the whole Chinese nation's resistance war, including compatriots in Taiwan. Commemorating the war helps compatriots on both sides of the Strait remember history, honor martyrs, and carry forward the spirit of the resistance war, and together promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We note that Taiwan’s “National Development Council” is drafting the “Foreign Professional Talent Recruitment and Employment Act,” which preliminarily plans to make it applicable to foreign talent as well as professional talent from Hong Kong and Macau. What views does the spokesperson have on this?","Our position of upholding the one-China principle is clear and consistent, as is well known.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","A media commentary article pointed out that a batch of new “Taiwan independence” forces are currently stirring, and that vigilance is needed against the convergence of old and new “Taiwan independence” forces, which would undermine the normal development of cross-Strait relations. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","The comment you cited does indeed reflect the concern of people on both sides of the Strait about the merging of old and new “Taiwan independence” forces on the island, which endangers the development of cross-Strait relations. As everyone knows, “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities are the greatest threat to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We therefore hope that compatriots on both sides can join hands to build an iron wall against “Taiwan independence” and to deter “independence,” so as to prevent “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities from bringing profound disaster to compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","经济日报记者","Since April 10, Taiwan residents have been able to enter and exit through Macau using their Taiwan Compatriot Permits, a move welcomed by the Taiwan public. May I ask the spokesperson, what specific measures to facilitate exchanges for Taiwan compatriots will be introduced next?","Starting April 10, 2017, the Macao SAR Government added the Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents as a travel document for entering and leaving Macao. I believe this measure will further facilitate Taiwan residents' travel to Macao, Hong Kong and the mainland, and promote personnel exchanges and cooperation between Macao and Taiwan. As for measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' travel to the mainland and their study, employment and daily life on the mainland, regions and departments across the mainland have been actively working to advance them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","I would like to ask whether the medicines Lee Ming-che needs can be delivered to him?","Just now, when I introduced the situation, I said that, in order to address the concerns of Li Ming-che's family, out of humanitarian considerations, ARATS entrusted the Taiwan Strait Cross-Strait Exchange Service Center with notifying Li Ming-che's wife of the relevant situation, and could also pass along the family's relevant belongings. However, up to now, ARATS has not received any belongings from the family of the person concerned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Second question. According to reports, Taiwan authorities are attempting to rename their offices in the United States and Japan by adding the word “Taiwan.” The US side regards this as undermining the status quo. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The international community has always handled Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the One-China principle, to prevent the emergence of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-12","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","Spokesperson, you just emphasized that the Straits Exchange Foundation (ARATS) did not receive the items that the families of the concerned parties wished to deliver. However, Taiwan’s Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) said it had already sent the medicine to the ARATS on the mainland and asked ARATS to pass it on. What is the current status of the medicine?","It is understood that the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits has not contacted the Straits Exchange Foundation about this matter. As I said earlier, the ARATS has still not received any items from the family members of the parties concerned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170412_11744575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-04-18","Lu Kang","","In a written answer approved at a Japanese Cabinet meeting on April 14 in response to questions raised by a lawmaker from the opposition Democratic Progressive Party, the Japanese government said that the beneficial and appropriate contents of Adolf Hitler's autobiography \"Mein Kampf\" (\"My Struggle\") could be used in a way that adheres to the spirit of the basic education law, among other conditions. What is your…","The world knows perfectly well what kind of a book \"Mein Kampf\" is. The Japanese government agreed that some contents of such a book could be used in the textbooks for teenage students. No wonder that it has caused great concern among people inside Japan. Fascism and militarism, as the root causes of the WWII, must be exposed, criticized and eradicated once for all. On historical issues that concern the principle of right and wrong, there is no room for the slightest ambiguity and obscurity. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect upon and learn from historical lessons, educate its young people with the right view of history, unequivocally guard against and oppose poisonous thoughts of war, and win trust from its Asian neighbors and the international community with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1454650.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1454513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-04-19","Lu Kang","","A Chinese tourist who tried to seek political asylum in Taiwan was deported back to the mainland. Does the central government welcome this move by the Taiwan authorities?","I have to remind you again that this is China's domestic affair, and I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1454907.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1454827.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-04-25","Geng Shuang","","The World Health Assembly will be held from 22 to 31 May. Will the Chinese government allow Taiwan to attend?","My colleagues answered similar questions before. When dealing with issues related to Taiwan's activities in the international arena, we always adhere to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1456730.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1456660.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Since the “5.20” last year, the cross-Strait communication mechanisms have been at a standstill. But recently we have also seen the Taiwan side repeatedly express hope to resume dialogue and interaction between the two sides as soon as possible, and some public opinion holds that this is sending goodwill to the mainland. What is your comment on this?","From 2008 until May 20, 2016, cross-Strait relations achieved fruitful results in peaceful development on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” (“九二共识”). The contact and communication mechanism between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council, and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Straits Interchange Foundation, functioned smoothly and communicated without obstruction. They played a positive role in safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, promoting institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, enhancing the well-being of people on both sides, and improving and developing cross-Strait relations.\nI want to emphasize that the mainland side has always hoped to uphold the important foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and to maintain the positive momentum of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations. No one cherishes the hard-won achievements created jointly by compatriots on both sides of the Strait more than we do. However, since May 20 last year, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not identify with its core meaning, undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait interaction and causing the cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms to stall. This is a situation we do not wish to see. The reason the “1992 Consensus” became the basis for cross-Strait consultation and dialogue is that it clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations. This is a goodwill signal exchanged by both sides, and it is also the touchstone for testing whether the Taiwan authorities' so-called “goodwill” is genuine. The Hundred Parables Sutra (《百喻经》) contains a story called the “Parable of the Three-Story House” (“三重楼喻”): a man sees a neighbor's three-story house, tall, spacious and splendid, and longs for one like it. He asks a carpenter to build one for him, but wants only the third floor and not the two below. In the end, because it lacked a foundation, the house was never completed. The Taiwan authorities, on the one hand, undermine the common political foundation across the Strait and, on the other, put on a posture of wanting to resume communication and dialogue between the two sides. How is this any different from that man? No excuse can justify denying the “1992 Consensus.” If there is genuine sincerity in restoring the cross-Strait communication and contact mechanisms, they should return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754535.htm"],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","It is reported that Lien Chan, former chairman of the Kuomintang, will soon visit the mainland. Please introduce the purpose of this trip and whether he will meet with high-level mainland officials.","It is understood that Mr. Lien Chan and his delegation plan to travel to Shaanxi soon to worship ancestors, and have been invited to attend the “Cross-Strait Compatriots' Folk Ancestor Worship Ceremony at the Hometown of Shennong Yandi” held in Shanxi. In addition, they will visit relevant provinces and municipalities in Ningxia and Zhejiang. Director Zhang Zhijun of the Central Taiwan Affairs Office will meet with Mr. Lien.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754534.htm"],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","A Taiwan authority recently said that in order to return funds from mainland telecom fraud, it hopes the two sides will negotiate a mechanism for returning stolen funds as soon as possible. What is the mainland’s attitude?","Combating telecom fraud and helping to return criminal proceeds are key priorities under the cross-Strait agreement on joint crime-fighting and judicial mutual assistance. Since the agreement took effect, this work, which protects the vital interests of people on both sides of the Strait, has not stopped. To date, the competent authorities on both sides have assisted each other in returning 11 sums of criminal proceeds, totaling more than RMB 6.8 million. We hope the relevant Taiwan authorities will promptly return the lawful property of victims on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754533.htm"],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","This morning we saw the latest news that the mainland's second aircraft carrier has been launched. Earlier, when the first carrier, the Liaoning, sailed around Taiwan, it drew great attention in Taiwan. I would like to ask: in the future, will carriers sailing around the waters surrounding Taiwan become a routine training activity? The second question: “5.20” is approaching, and Tsai Ing-wen's administration will…","On the first question, I have just seen this important news as well. I am proud of the great achievements our country has made in national defense and military modernization. This helps enhance our ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to protect China's major core interests. For other specific information, please inquire with the Ministry of National Defense.\nOn the second question, we have already responded to this many times. The eight years since 2008, during which peaceful development of cross-Strait relations achieved a situation and results widely endorsed by compatriots on both sides, were because both sides share the important political foundation of jointly opposing “Taiwan independence” and upholding the “1992 Consensus.” Today, on the major choice concerning the future of cross-Strait relations, I believe compatriots on both sides are also paying close attention. In fact, how the new ruling authorities in Taiwan answer this exam paper is very clear to them. No reason can serve as an excuse for denying the “1992 Consensus.” Only by returning to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can peaceful development of cross-Strait relations continue steadily and go far along the correct path opened in the past.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","It is reported that mainland resident Zhang Xiangzhong, who left his tour group in Taiwan while traveling there with a group, has already left Taiwan with his original tour group. How will the follow-up to this matter be handled? Another question: Taiwan’s Tsai Ing-wen authorities broke the 54-year convention by downgrading the Koxinga memorial ceremony. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Recently, a mainland tourist deviated from a tour group on their own during a trip to Taiwan. The Cross-Strait Tourism Exchange Association requested that the relevant Taiwan authorities send the tourist back in accordance with the cross-Strait tourism agreement. It is understood that the tourist has since returned with the group to Xiamen. The relevant tourism authorities and the mainland travel agency have questioned and investigated the tourist and the tour group’s guide. The competent authorities will handle this incident of leaving the group in accordance with relevant regulations.\nTaking this opportunity, I would also like to tell everyone that the “Administrative Measures on Mainland Residents’ Travel to Taiwan,” jointly revised by the National Tourism Administration, the Ministry of Public Security and the Taiwan Affairs Office, was published on April 13. We hope mainland tourists will strictly abide by the relevant regulations when traveling to Taiwan.\nOn the second question, in 1661 Zheng Chenggong expelled the Dutch colonists, recovered the treasure island of Taiwan, and made historic contributions to the development of Taiwan. He was revered by the Taiwan public as the “Sacred King of Taiwan” and is regarded by Chinese people at home and abroad as a national hero. Today, temples to Prince Yanping are found throughout Taiwan, and the deeds of “Guoxingye” (Koxinga) are passed down. Could a few “de-Sinicization” gestures possibly erase this?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","I would like to ask about the SEF's recent invitation of a Taiwan business delegation to visit Kinmen. It is said this has drawn concern from relevant mainland parties, and I would like to ask the spokesperson about it.","As you may have noticed, yesterday the Taiwan Enterprises Association issued a statement saying that this was not an activity organized by the association, but a spontaneous act by individual Taiwanese businesspeople. Since it was spontaneous, the Taiwan Affairs Office has no comment. I want to clarify one point: our attitude toward cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation has always been consistent. Since May 20 last year, who has been obstructing Taiwanese businesspeople from investing on the mainland by exerting various political pressures, and who has been desperately trying, in defiance of economic laws, to weaken and sever the economic ties between Taiwan compatriots and the mainland, everyone can see very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, several mainland provinces and cities have begun fully accepting applications for electronic Taiwan travel permits from the 24th of this month. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Electronizing the Mainland Residents’ Permit for Travel to Taiwan is a new measure by public security authorities to facilitate travel to Taiwan by mainland residents and to enhance the anti-counterfeiting effectiveness of the document. The new version of the document was first piloted in Fujian Province on December 26, 2016, and has been well received by society. Under the unified deployment of the Ministry of Public Security, public security entry-exit administration agencies in various localities began accepting applications for electronic Permits for Travel to Taiwan from April 24 of this year. At present, the vast majority of localities have successfully launched the service. A few localities, due to large-scale system debugging and upgrades, will complete the launch before May 30.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754529.htm"],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","When CCTV reported on the Asian Table Tennis Championships on April 11, it changed the name of the Taiwan delegation from “Chinese Taipei” to “China Taipei.” Why was this change made? Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council Chair Zhang Xiaoyue (张小月) said that Taiwan does not accept the mainland's unilateral “belittling.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our relevant policy is consistent and has not changed. This time, the Taiwan table tennis team came to the mainland to compete, which was arranged in accordance with the spirit of the agreement reached between the two sides’ Olympic committees. I want to emphasize that mainland media have always reported on Taiwan-related matters in accordance with the one-China principle, and there is no question of “belittling” Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","First question: Taiwan’s “Han Kuang” military exercises will be held in late May, returning to Penghu after 20 years to practice amphibious landing operations. It is reported that Tsai Ing-wen will go to review them. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? Second question: the Green-camp polling foundation in Taiwan recently released a poll showing that nearly 60 percent of the public is dissatisfied with the…","First question: The cornerstone for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. The Taiwan authorities' pursuit of armed confrontation is doomed to have no way out.\nSecond question: We do not make specific comments on the various opinion polls on the island of Taiwan. What I want to express is that Taiwan's economic development and social stability cannot be separated from positive and healthy cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","联合报记者","First question: I would like to learn about the case of Lee Ming-che. Has the Straits Exchange Foundation received the medicine? Is Lee Ming-che’s physical condition still good? Is Lee Ming-che currently detained in Zhuhai, Guangdong? What exactly is the reason? Second question: the World Health Assembly is about to convene, and Taiwan has still not received an invitation. Will it still receive one? If not, why not?","On the first question: Li Ming-che, a Taiwan resident, is suspected of engaging in activities endangering national security, and the case-handling authority is investigating in accordance with the law; the case is still under investigation. We have explained the relevant situation on multiple occasions. Here I would like to reiterate three points: First, Li Ming-che is currently in good physical condition, and medical care is assured; he has also clearly explained the relevant situation in his letters to family members. Second, the case-handling authority protects the lawful rights and interests of the persons involved in accordance with the law. Third, the mainland has consistently and actively supported and encouraged personnel exchanges across the Strait; to this end, we have adopted convenience measures including issuing card-format Taiwan compatriot permits and providing visa-free entry for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. At present, more than 5 million Taiwan compatriots travel to the mainland each year. As long as Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland to engage in normal activities, their rights and interests will be protected in accordance with the law.\nOn the second question, regarding Taiwan's participation in the activities of international organizations, we have stated on many occasions that arrangements should be made through cross-Strait consultation under the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754531.htm"],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Recently, on the island of Taiwan, “pandering to Japan” and “de-Chinafication” behaviors have coexisted, such as the downgrading of the Zheng Chenggong (郑成功) memorial ceremony and the decapitation of the bronze statue of Hatta Yoichi (八田与一), which have triggered a series of controversies on the island. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","For a long time, “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have misled Taiwan residents with the “imperial subject” view of history and the “Taiwan independence” view of history, distorted value concepts, and caused serious social antagonism. To borrow a line from Taiwan media to comment: “Those who sow hatred will inevitably be consumed by hatred.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","First question: Hau Lung-pin, a candidate for the next chairmanship of the KMT vice chairmanship, recently said in an interview that if elected he would deepen KMT-CPC exchanges and proposed establishing a KMT representative office on the mainland. May I ask the spokesperson for comment? Second question: Ma Ying-jeou, former leader of Taiwan, recently said in a campus speech that peace is the minimum requirement…","First question: As for elections on the island, we do not comment. We are willing to enhance mutual trust and strengthen communication and interaction with the Kuomintang on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” jointly commit to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond question: Realizing national reunification is the common aspiration of Chinese people at home and abroad, and a historical inevitability for the Chinese nation's march toward great rejuvenation. Taiwan's future is tied to national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots cannot be separated from the prosperity of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","I have two questions. First, the Belt and Road Forum will be held in Beijing in mid-May. I would like to ask the spokesperson whether Taiwan will send representatives or organizations to participate.","The Belt and Road International Cooperation Summit Forum is an international event, and the representatives of various countries attending the forum were invited by the host organizers. We have stated many times that we welcome Taiwanese businesspeople to participate in the construction of the Belt and Road and share development opportunities. This position has not changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","At the recent 2017 Xiamen Industrial Expo and the 21st Cross-Strait Trade Fair, industry representatives from both sides said that cross-Strait manufacturing should innovate in areas of cooperation and jointly develop the smart manufacturing market. Does the spokesperson have particular fields in which the mainland especially encourages Taiwanese businesses to invest, as it advances industry-academia-research…","The mainland side has consistently encouraged and supported Taiwan businesses investing on the mainland, and encouraged and supported cross-Strait economic cooperation and economic and social integration. Before May 20 last year, the competent departments of both sides had, under the framework of the Economic Cooperation Committee (经合会), made policy coordination and related arrangements on strengthening cross-Strait industrial cooperation pilot projects. As I understand it, many Taiwan businesses investing on the mainland have now actively invested in smart manufacturing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the Shanghai Taiwan-Funded Enterprises Association held a job fair in Taipei, attracting tens of thousands of people to seek employment. The venue was lively, which was unexpected. Some media have commented that Taiwan's economy has continued to sag and cannot escape its economic predicament, and that young people in Taiwan wish to go to the mainland, where there is a vast world, to build their careers…","The mainland is not only the ancestral homeland of Taiwan compatriots but also the solid hinterland for Taiwan’s economic development. In recent years, the mainland’s economic development and social progress have been thriving and advancing at a remarkable pace, with growing appeal to Taiwan people, especially Taiwan’s young people. We are glad to see more Taiwan youth come to the mainland to study, find employment, work, and start businesses, and we are willing to provide them with various conveniences. We believe that Taiwan youth’s willingness to develop on the mainland and to exchange with young people there will certainly have a positive effect on the future development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","The Chairman of the American Institute in Taiwan, Mo Jian, recently arrived in Taiwan, which has prompted many associations. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second question: The Taipei World University Games is about to be held. Will Taiwan residents be allowed to enter the stadium carrying the “Blue Sky with White Sun and Red Earth” flag?","First, we do not object to civil, non-governmental economic and cultural exchanges between Taiwan and foreign countries, but we firmly oppose any official-level interaction between the Taiwan authorities and countries that have diplomatic relations with China.\nSecond, the World University Games is a sports event organized by the International University Sports Federation, and the handling of Taiwan-related issues must follow the relevant provisions of the International Olympic Committee. Sports events of this kind held in Taiwan should not be subject to artificial political interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Second question: regarding the issue of mainland tourists who left their tour group just now, some commentary in Taiwan holds that the Taiwan authorities did not accept their stranded status in order to avoid aggravating the current sluggish cross-Strait relations, and that it is a gesture of goodwill toward the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Under the agreement on mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, for tourists who violate relevant regulations, neither side may refuse to send them back or refuse to accept them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声电台记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that U.S. arms sales to Taiwan are an important pillar of stability in the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? In addition, may I ask the spokesperson: Does the mainland have any specific policies to facilitate the development of Taiwan youth on the mainland?","Let me first answer your second question. Our policy is open. Next, we will further study and provide more convenient policy measures. I think it will not take long before everyone receives good news.\nOn the second question, the cornerstone for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” activities, not any foreign arms sales to Taiwan. Therefore, to truly improve and develop cross-Strait relations, we should earnestly return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” There is no other way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","First, the Taiwan administrative authorities plan to amend the measures for permits for people from the mainland to enter the Taiwan region, which would bring former mainland party, government, and military personnel who have left office under control. What is your comment on this? Second, could you provide some information on the 9th Straits Forum?","Regarding your first question: the Taiwan authorities’ actions are not conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and represent a historical step backward. Regarding your second question: as I understand it, this year’s Straits Forum will be held in Xiamen in mid-June, and preparations are proceeding in an orderly manner. We will announce specific information at an appropriate time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201704/t20170426_11754546.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-04-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on April 26 at the regular press conference, in response to a question, that recently a mainland tourist deserted a tour group without permission while traveling in Taiwan. The Straits Tourism Exchange Association requested that relevant Taiwan authorities return the tourist in accordance with the cross-Strait tourism agreement. It is understood that this tourist has recently returned to Xiamen with the tour group. Relevant tourism authorities and the mainland travel agency have questioned the tourist and the tour group leader. The authorities will handle this group-departure incident in accordance with relevant regulations.\nMa said that the “Administrative Measures for Mainland Residents' Travel to Taiwan Region,” jointly revised by the National Tourism Administration, the Ministry of Public Security, and the TAO, were promulgated on April 13. He hoped mainland tourists would strictly abide by the relevant rules when traveling to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170426_11754532.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2017-04-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We have seen online that many netizens have been voting on the name of the new aircraft carrier that has just been launched. During the voting, some people named this carrier “Taiwan,” and some named it “Shandong.” May I ask whether the name of this aircraft carrier has been decided? Second, some experts have mentioned that the launch of this new aircraft carrier has changed the situation in the Taiwan Strait.…","Regarding the first question: you mentioned that some people online conducted a vote on the name of the aircraft carrier. I feel this should be a spontaneous act by netizens, because I have noticed that some people have named this carrier \"Pipi Shrimp,\" and quite a few people voted in favor. Our military has corresponding regulations for naming naval vessels, and names are usually announced when the vessel is handed over and commissioned.\nRegarding the second question, the training waters for the aircraft carrier are determined according to the needs of the situation and mission.\nRegarding the third question, as I have just said, the relevant Chinese authorities will comprehensively consider various factors and plan the development of the aircraft carrier as a whole.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2017-04/27/content_4779393.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2017-04-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On the day China's second aircraft carrier was launched, Taiwanese media reported that Li Hsi-ming, who was about to take over as “Chief of the General Staff of the Ministry of National Defense” in Taiwan, confirmed on the morning of the 26th in the Taiwan “Legislative Yuan” that two second-hand Perry-class frigates the Taiwan military purchased from the United States would arrive in Taiwan simultaneously in May.…","On this question, I would like to say two things. First, we have always firmly opposed any country selling weapons to Taiwan. Second, any attempt to “use force to resist reunification” is doomed to fail.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2017-04/27/content_4779393.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2017-04-27","Yang Yujun","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","An official said Lockheed Martin will sell F-35 fighters to Taiwan. What response does China have? In addition, if this becomes reality, would it affect China-US relations?","On this kind of question, as I said earlier, we firmly oppose any country selling weapons to Taiwan.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2017-04/27/content_4779393.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2017-04-28","Geng Shuang","","President Trump was asked yesterday about his attitude towards another potential call with Taiwan's Tsai Ing-wen. This is after Tsai Ing-wen appeared not to rule out another phone call with President Trump. However, President Trump appeared to express no interest in this, saying that it would create problems for China. In other words, he basically rebuffed this suggestion from Tsai Ing-wen. Is this a position of…","We've noted the US reply, which we believe the Taiwan side should have also noted. We always oppose official exchanges in any form between the Taiwan side and countries that have diplomatic ties with China. This position is very clear and resolute.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1457731.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1457688.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-04-28","Geng Shuang","","During the election, President Trump criticized China. After he won the election, he took the phone call from Tsai Ing-wen. All these raised concern in China. It seems that recently, President Trump has realized that China and President Xi are his good friend. The bilateral relationship seems to be at the moment very close and cooperative. President Trump appears to have realized that this is also in his…","The China-US relationship is one of the most consequential bilateral relationships not only for the two countries but also for the world. Your question is a big one and it may take an hour to answer it. (laughs) Here I will be brief.\nChina's attitude is clear and consistent. We are always ready to develop a sound and steady relationship with the US on the basis of mutual respect and win-win cooperation. Since President Trump took office, President Xi Jinping has stayed in close contact with him through various means, and they have established good working relations as well as personal friendship, which is significant for the development of bilateral relations. At present, the two sides are following through the important agreements reached between the two presidents and developing the relationship along the right track.\nThe importance of the China-US relationship has gone beyond the bilateral scope. A good and sound China-US relationship serves the interests of not only the two countries but also the Asia-Pacific region and the whole world. We are always ready to work with the US to push forward sound and steady development of our relationship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1457731.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1457688.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, April 28 (reporter Liu Huan) — In response to questions from foreign media on April 27 concerning cross-Strait relations and other issues during Tsai Ing-wen's exclusive interview with Reuters, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded: Since “5·20” last year, the most fundamental change in cross-Strait relations has been the destruction of the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Whoever destroyed this foundation should be held responsible for the current impasse in cross-Strait relations. The DPP authorities not only refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, but also tolerate and support a series of “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” activities on the island, obstruct cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and incite opposition in public opinion across the Strait. This is the greatest obstacle to the current development of cross-Strait relations, and compatriots on both sides see this clearly.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that our major policies toward Taiwan are consistent and clear. We adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and strive to safeguard and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, but we will never allow the nation to be split. This is the common will and firm determination of more than 1.3 billion Chinese people. The only way for the Taiwan authorities to resolve the current impasse in cross-Strait relations is to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and recognize one China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201704/t20170428_11756192.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-03","Geng Shuang","","The Kimberley Process (KP) intersessional meeting was held in Perth, Australia on May 1. According to the Australian media, tension rose at the meeting because there was a delegation invited from Taiwan. It is also said that the Australian Department of Foreign Affairs raised this issue with the Chinese ambassador. Can you tell us anything about the Chinese government's perspective on this, and what possibly the…","Our position on Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations is clear and consistent, and that is to follow the one-China principle. The understanding was reached between China and the KP in 2003 when the process was inaugurated that Taiwan provisionally executes the Kimberley Process Certification Scheme (KPCS) in the name of the rough diamond-trading entity of Chinese Taipei. However, Taiwan is neither the participant nor observer of KP, and shall not attend meetings of its working groups or committees.\nBefore the intersessional meeting, the host unilaterally decided to invite Taiwan to attend as a \"guest\" of the Chair, which violated relevant rules of the process. The Chinese side lodged repeated representations with the host before the meeting, but China's reasonable concerns were not respected. Most KP participants and its committees and working groups also clearly voiced their disapproval of the host's practice. It is confusing and regrettable that the host was completely indifferent and held on to its own view.\nChina's expression of concerns about the issue and relevant arrangements at the meeting was in line with the rules of procedure and was perfectly reasonable and fair. China's position and concerns were also echoed and supported by many other participants at the meeting.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1458633.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1458578.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-05-06","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 6 (reporter Qi Xianghui): Regarding the incident in which relevant Taiwan authorities shot and injured mainland fishermen early this morning, TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said on the 6th that, in view of the frequent incidents in recent period in which relevant Taiwan authorities have detained mainland fishing boats, we have repeatedly stressed that the Taiwan side should respect the fact that fishermen from both sides operate in traditional fishing grounds, respect the rights and interests of mainland fishermen engaged in normal production and operations, and stop the practice of detaining mainland fishing boats without cause. However, this morning an incident still occurred in which mainland fishermen were shot and injured, which is outrageous. We demand that the Taiwan side immediately conduct a strict investigation and punishment of this incident, release the people and boats as soon as possible, and prevent such incidents from happening again.\nOn the morning of the 6th, when relevant Taiwan authorities were seizing mainland fishing boats in waters near the Penghu Islands, they fired rubber bullets, injuring two mainland fishermen. The two injured have been sent to relevant hospitals in Penghu for treatment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170506_11760225.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-08","Geng Shuang","","The deadline for online registration of this year's World Health Assembly (WHA) is coming soon, and Taiwan has yet to receive any invitation. Recently, the US and Canada expressed their support for Taiwan's continued participation in the WHA as an observer. There are comments saying that politics should not overtop public health. What is China's comment on that?","As we have said many times, the one-China principle must be followed when dealing with Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations.\nYou mentioned that relevant countries expressed their support for Taiwan's continued participation in the WHA as an observer. As far as I know, only some individual countries are making irresponsible remarks on this issue. We are firmly against such remarks. In fact, most countries support the handling of the issue in keeping with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1459639.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1459609.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-05-08","Geng Shuang","","US Secretary of State Rex Tillerson stated recently that the US made it clear to the ROK, Japan, China and Russia that denuclearization of the Peninsula is a shared objective. It is not about regime change, not about regime collapse, not about an accelerated reunification of the Peninsula, and not about looking for an excuse to cross the 38th Parallel, but to let the DPRK know that only denuclearization can bring…","We have noted the remarks by Secretary Tillerson, the principles he mentioned and the commitment of the US to promoting denuclearization of the Peninsula. Under the current circumstances, the message sent by the US about solving problems through dialogue and consultation is of positive significance and worth serious consideration by relevant parties.\nThe US is one of the main parties directly involved in the nuclear issue of the Korean Peninsula. Together with the international community, China always expects and encourages the US to play a constructive role in the peaceful settlement of the issue. We hope the US can, based on the above-mentioned positions, strengthen contact with the DPRK to gradually seek consensus and build preliminary mutual trust. We are ready to join hands with the US and other relevant parties to continue to work for the peaceful settlement of the nuclear issue through dialogue and consultation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1459639.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1459609.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-05-08","Geng Shuang","","According to a Taiwan official, a fishing boat from Guangdong province was seized Saturday by a Taiwan patrol. Can you confirm this? Is the mainland handling this case?","Your question is about cross-Straits affairs. As far as I know, the spokesperson from the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already made comments on that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1459639.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1459609.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-05-08","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 8 (reporter Li Hanfang): Spokesperson An Fengshan of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, in an interview with reporters on the 8th concerning issues related to Taiwan at the World Health Assembly, said that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and have placed obstacles in the way of Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly. The responsibility for Taiwan’s inability to attend this year lies entirely with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nHe said that since 2009, Taiwan has for 8 consecutive years participated in the World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei.” This was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations during the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides on the two sides of the Strait adhered to, embodying the one-China principle. However, because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to date have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and the core meaning that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, they have undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, causing the cross-Strait communication and consultation mechanisms to stall. The premise and basis for Taiwan’s participation no longer exist, and the arrangement that lasted 8 years is no longer sustainable.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that the World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations and must handle issues related to Taiwan at the World Health Assembly in accordance with the one-China principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, has placed obstacles in the way of Taiwan’s participation. The responsibility for Taiwan’s inability to attend this year lies entirely with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nHe said that the mainland side has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and we have adopted multiple measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in the health sector. On the basis of adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” the Straits Exchange Foundation on the mainland side and the Straits Exchange Foundation on the Taiwan side have signed the Cross-Strait Agreement on Medicine and Health Cooperation, the Cross-Strait Food Safety Agreement, the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement and others, and have built multiple platforms for exchange and cooperation. At the same time, under the one-China principle, we have also made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan’s participation in global health affairs. Taiwan experts may attend relevant WHO technical meetings and activities, and the WHO may also send experts to Taiwan for guidance when needed. These arrangements ensure that whether public health emergencies occur on the island or internationally, Taiwan can respond promptly and effectively. As for why Taiwan cannot attend this year’s World Health Assembly, this is a question the Democratic Progressive Party authorities need to reflect on. Any attempt to shirk responsibility or shift the focus will not succeed.\nAn Fengshan reiterated that on the question of Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations, our position is clear and consistent: it must be arranged through cross-Strait consultation under the one-China principle. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities should recognize reality and return as soon as possible to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only then can institutionalized cross-Strait interaction continue, and only then will it be possible for both sides to consult on Taiwan’s participation in international organizations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170508_11761265.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-09","Geng Shuang","","The registration for the 70th World Health Assembly (WHA) has ended, yet Taiwan has not received any invitation. For many times it claimed that the mainland used health issues to \"exert political pressure\", and that the absence of Taiwan will \"damage the well-being of the people in Taiwan\" and \"leave a loophole in the global epidemic prevention network\". What is your comment on that?","Yesterday the spokesperson from the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already expressed China's position. As we have stressed many times, the one-China principle must be followed when dealing with Taiwan's participation in activities held by international organizations. The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations. The UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1 provided legal grounds for dealing with the above-mentioned issue.\nWhen dealing with Taiwan's participation at the WHA, the WHO secretariat acts in strict accordance with UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1 as well as the one-China principle. Most countries around the world express understanding and support for China's stance on this issue. It has been proven that only by recognizing the one-China principle, can arrangements for Taiwan's participation be made through cross-Straits consultation. It is useless to court foreign support.\nI would like to stress that the central government of China has made proper arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs in line with the one-China principle. Within the framework of the International Health Regulations (2005), there are sound channels and mechanism for Taiwan to exchange information with the WHO and countries around the world. Experts from Taiwan can participate in WHO-related technical meetings while the WHO may also send experts to Taiwan for guidance when needed. These arrangements ensure timely and effective responses from Taiwan in case of public health emergencies either in Taiwan or in other places around the world. Claims that \"people's right to health will be damaged\" and \"there will be a loophole in the global epidemic prevention network\" are not true.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1460040.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1459976.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-05-09","Geng Shuang","","Today the Taiwan authorities say that the Taiwan \"Health Minister\" is going anyway to the WHA, and he is leading a delegation to Geneva. Has the Chinese government been in touch with the Swiss government to ask the government to deny their entry?","I have just elaborated on China's position on Taiwan's participation at this year's WHA. I would like to stress that whatever measures the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities are going to take, they are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1460040.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1459976.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 10, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson An Fengshan first introduced the situation in which relevant mainland departments are actively studying and introducing policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues in cross-Strait relations.","For many years, the mainland side has actively promoted exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, continuously introduced policy measures benefiting the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and enhanced compatriots' kinship and well-being. Compatriots on both sides are brothers and sisters with a shared destiny, one family whose blood is thicker than water. No matter how cross-Strait relations change, bringing well-being to compatriots on both sides has always been the focus and foothold of our development of cross-Strait relations.\nIn recent years, as personnel exchanges across the Strait have grown closer, many Taiwan friends have developed new expectations and demands for greater convenience in living and working on the mainland. The relevant departments on the mainland have conscientiously implemented the important instructions of General Secretary Xi, actively studied and issued relevant policy measures, and provided more convenience for Taiwan compatriots to study, find employment, start businesses and live on the mainland. It is understood that over a period of time, the relevant departments have successively announced a batch of new policy measures, mainly in the following aspects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","First, mainland railway and civil aviation departments have announced upgrades to self-service equipment so that Taiwan compatriots can buy tickets, collect tickets, and check in on their own. In recent years, with the vigorous development of convenience measures by railway, civil aviation, and other departments, self-service equipment has greatly facilitated travel for mainland residents. However, the relevant self-service equipment did not support the Taiwan Compatriot Permit, so Taiwan compatriots taking trains, planes, and other public transportation on the mainland could not enjoy the convenience of self-service equipment. Even when buying train tickets online, they could only queue at manual windows or counters to collect their tickets. To facilitate travel on the mainland for Taiwan compatriots, China Railway Corporation has, by optimizing and adjusting its railway ticketing system and installing and upgrading self-service ticket purchase and collection machines, among other measures, successively launched self-service ticket purchase and collection services for Taiwan compatriots at railway stations in Beijing, Tianjin, Shanghai, Guangdong, Hunan, Fujian, and other places. Next, it will continue to take corresponding measures according to demand to facilitate travel for Taiwan compatriots. The Civil Aviation Administration of China has also stated that, after preparatory work, nearly 800 self-service ticketing devices at major airports nationwide already support manual entry of the Taiwan Compatriot Permit for ticket purchase, and the upgrade of nearly 1,700 self-service check-in devices to automatically read the Taiwan Compatriot Permit is being accelerated, with self-service check-in for Taiwan compatriots expected to be achieved within this year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778495.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Second, the Ministry of Education and other departments have revised and improved the relevant rules on Taiwan students studying in the mainland. To solve practical problems that Taiwan students encounter when attending mainland universities and seeking employment after graduation, the Ministry of Education and five other departments revised the rules on enrolling students from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan in ordinary higher education institutions last December. The revision standardizes management and services such as enrollment and teaching, and safeguards the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan students. It explicitly requires institutions that enroll Taiwan students to register their student status and establish their files, resolving file management and use issues when Taiwan students remain in the mainland to work after graduation. At the same time, the Examination Center of the Ministry of Education published a new syllabus for the joint entrance examination for students from Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and overseas Chinese, to make the examination content more scientific.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Third, opening the National Social Science Fund to Taiwanese researchers working on the mainland. For a long time, Taiwanese scholars on the mainland have hoped to apply for national-level fund projects and obtain project funding and other support, but they have been unable to apply due to their non-mainland-resident status. In recent years, as cross-Strait science and technology exchanges have grown increasingly frequent, the Ministry of Science and Technology and the National Natural Science Foundation of China have stated that national science and technology programs, including the National Natural Science Foundation of China, the National Key Research and Development Program, and the National Science and Technology Major Projects, have gradually been opened to Taiwanese researchers working on the mainland. This time, the National Planning Office of Philosophy and Social Sciences stated that it will also open applications for all categories of National Social Science Fund projects to Taiwanese researchers working at universities and research institutes on the mainland, covering 26 first-level disciplines; projects in the three separately listed disciplines, including education, will also accept applications at the same time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Fourth, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security is expanding the pilot areas for employment of Taiwan compatriots in public institutions on the mainland. The Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security has decided that, on the basis of the six provinces and municipalities already opened (Fujian, Jiangsu, Tianjin, Shanghai, Zhejiang and Hubei), six more provinces, municipalities and autonomous regions (Beijing, Hebei, Shandong, Guangdong, Guangxi and Hainan) will be added as pilot areas open to Taiwan residents for employment in public institutions. Taiwan residents may take up employment in public institutions such as universities and public hospitals in the pilot areas.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Fifth, the Ministry of Justice has decided to further expand the opening of legal services to Taiwan. The geographic scope in which Taiwan law firms may establish representative offices in the mainland will expand from the current cities of Fuzhou and Xiamen in Fujian Province to all of Fujian Province, Shanghai, Jiangsu Province, Zhejiang Province and Guangdong Province. Taiwan law firms that have already established representative offices in the mainland, and whose representative offices have been in existence for three years or more, are allowed to form joint operations (联营) with mainland law firms in Fujian Province, Shanghai, Jiangsu Province, Zhejiang Province and Guangdong Province, where their representative offices are located. Law firms in the above provinces and municipalities are allowed to hire Taiwan-licensed lawyers as legal counsel to the firm, to provide consultation services on Taiwan law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","In addition, to encourage and support young people from Taiwan to work and start businesses on the mainland, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council issued relevant regulations last year, guiding localities to provide support in areas such as start-up capital, financing, and use of office space. As of the end of 2016, 53 cross-strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites on the mainland had collectively hosted or served nearly 1,200 Taiwan-funded enterprises, attracted more than 6,000 Taiwan youths to intern, find employment, and start businesses, and more than 17,000 Taiwan youths participated in various internship, employment, entrepreneurship, and innovation exchange activities organized by the bases or demonstration sites.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","The series of policy measures described above demonstrates that the mainland welcomes more Taiwan compatriots to take part in cross-Strait exchanges and provides them with a stage on which to display their talents and realize their aspirations. This is a vivid embodiment of the concept that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. It is understood that the relevant authorities will also introduce more policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots’ study, employment, entrepreneurship and daily life in the mainland, based on the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","新华社记者","The launch ceremony of “Taiwan Businesses Go E-commerce” and the online launch of the “JD·Taiwan Enterprise Premium Products Hall” were recently held in Jiangsu, drawing wide attention from Taiwan businesses. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","On the morning of May 8, 2017, the launch ceremony of “Taiwan Businesses Go E-commerce” and the online opening of the “JD.com · Taiwan Enterprise Products Hall” were held in Suqian, Jiangsu Province. The All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, presidents of Taiwan business associations in various localities, and more than 350 Taiwanese business representatives who have set up shop in the “JD.com · Taiwan Enterprise Products Hall” enthusiastically attended the event. Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, attended the online opening ceremony and delivered remarks. Director Zhang said: For a long time, governments at all levels on the mainland and the broad masses of Taiwanese businesspeople have been very concerned about how Taiwan-invested enterprises, in the process of transformation and upgrading, can combine Taiwanese businesses' participation in e-commerce with opening domestic sales channels for enterprise products, in order to promote the sustained and healthy development of enterprises. He said: Through the efforts of all sides, this matter has finally been accomplished, and the broad masses of Taiwanese businesspeople have boarded the express train to the vast domestic market. This will more precisely help enterprises continuously accumulate and cultivate new momentum for innovation. We hope that Taiwanese business friends can seize opportunities, actively explore and forge ahead, take root on the mainland, and achieve greater development. Relevant reports have already been published by the media, and everyone may refer to them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Could the spokesperson briefly introduce the current preparations for the 9th Straits Forum?","The 9th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian from June 17 for one week, and preparations are progressing smoothly. This forum is co-hosted by 80 units in total, 40 from the mainland and 40 from Taiwan. Under the theme of “Expanding People-to-People Exchanges and Deepening Integrated Development,” the forum continues to focus on and serve young people and grassroots groups across the Taiwan Strait, and has arranged 21 activities in four major sections: the forum plenary, youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, and economic and trade exchanges.\nIn the youth exchange section, centered on creative entrepreneurship, experiential exchanges, and related content, this forum will newly hold activities such as the Straits Forum Golden Idea Creative Competition and the New Generation Leadership Training Camp, striving to create more opportunities for Taiwan youth to study, live, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland. In the grassroots exchange section, we will continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges in fields such as folk beliefs, marriage and family, community public welfare, and traditional culture, and newly hold activities such as the Fujian-Taiwan Academy Cultural Exchange Forum and the Fujian-Taiwan Relations Archival Photo Exhibition, deepening interaction between grassroots people across the Strait and jointly passing on the excellent Chinese culture. In the economic and trade exchange section, we will add to the cross-Strait characteristic temple fairs an economic, trade, and tourism promotion and exchange meeting for Taiwan counties and cities, promote matchmaking and industrial cooperation between relevant cross-Strait counties and cities, and hold exchange and matchmaking activities in relevant industries across the Strait such as science and technology, health, and vocational education, enhancing the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nWe warmly welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan, especially young people and grassroots friends, to attend the activities of this forum. We also welcome media friends from both sides of the Strait to cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778491.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾《联合报》记者","Taiwan did not receive an invitation on the final day of registration for the World Health Assembly, and the Mainland Affairs Council expressed protest against mainland obstruction. Taiwan's “health minister” plans to travel to Switzerland to exchange views with other countries. May I ask whether the mainland will also obstruct this?","On the issue of the World Health Assembly, our office's spokesperson stated our position and attitude on May 8. I would like to reiterate that the World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations. In accordance with the one-China principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1, it is only natural to handle Taiwan-related matters at the World Health Assembly. The DPP authorities' refusal to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, has eliminated the premise and basis for Taiwan's participation. The responsibility for the Taiwan region not being able to attend this year lies entirely with the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities need to ask themselves in good conscience why Taiwan could attend the World Health Assembly over the past eight years but not this year, rather than persistently shirking responsibility, shifting focus, and misleading and deceiving Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778493.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","It has been reported that the mainland recently added six Cross-Strait exchange bases. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Since 2009, our office has approved the establishment of 49 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 20 provinces and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian. To create more cross-Strait exchange and cooperation platforms and give compatriots on both sides more opportunities to look back at history, savor culture, share familial affection and develop together, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council recently approved the establishment of six new Cross-Strait Exchange Bases at: the Beichuan County Earthquake Ruins Protection Zone in Mianyang City, Sichuan Province; the Historical Museum of the Army Military Academy (Lujun Jiangwutang) in Yunnan Province; Bao Gong Park in Hefei City, Anhui Province; the Yandi (Emperor Yan) Mausoleum in Gaoping City, Shanxi Province; the China Ceramics Museum in Jingdezhen City, Jiangxi Province; and the Dingguang Buddha Cultural Park in Wuping County, Fujian Province. The establishment of these bases fully took into account local cultural resource characteristics and the state of cross-Strait exchanges, and fully displays the kinship of compatriots on both sides who share the same roots and origins. For example, the newly established Cross-Strait Exchange Base at the Beichuan County Earthquake Ruins Protection Zone in Mianyang City, Sichuan, aims to promote the spirit of mutual support and blood-is-thicker-than-water solidarity that compatriots on both sides displayed in fighting the “5·12” Wenchuan earthquake. We welcome Taiwan compatriots and people from all walks of life to visit these exchange bases for sightseeing, exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778490.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","Continuing the WHA issue: The mainland believes that the responsibility for Taiwan's inability to attend this year's WHA meeting lies with the Democratic Progressive Party government's refusal to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus.\" However, both the Democratic Progressive Party and the Mainland Affairs Council have responded that the mainland's move may cause cross-Strait relations to drift further apart. May I ask…","Regarding some statements from Taiwan, we have previously explained that two-way information exchange between Taiwan and the WHO is unobstructed. The channels for Taiwan to participate in WHO professional and technical activities, obtain relevant data in fields such as health and epidemic prevention, and report relevant situations have also always been unobstructed and effective. Taiwan experts can attend WHO-related technical meetings and activities, and when needed, the WHO and experts can also travel to Taiwan for guidance. The above arrangements ensure that whether a public health emergency occurs on the island or internationally, Taiwan can respond promptly and effectively. Anyone with discerning eyes can see that the health of Taiwan’s people and whether Taiwan attends the World Health Assembly are two different matters. This is merely a pretext the DPP authorities use to shirk responsibility. As for why Taiwan cannot attend this year’s World Health Assembly, this is a question the DPP authorities need to reflect on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Reportedly, the mainland brand music program “The Voice of China” recently held its first open talent search in Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have?","It is understood that the music program “The Voice of China,” which is deeply followed and loved by audiences on both sides of the Strait, will begin its second season. Open auditions will be held in Taiwan for the first time from May 3 to May 27, with six regional preliminary contests planned in Taipei, Hsinchu, Hualien and other places. Winning contestants selected through the semifinals and finals will go to Shanghai to take part in the next stage of competition. Registration for the event is currently very enthusiastic. The three preliminary auditions already held have seen more than 1,000 participants, and the on-site atmosphere has been very lively. We are pleased to see music lovers on both sides of the Strait, especially young people, use this event platform to join hands in letting music dreams take flight and deepen mutual understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","福建《海峡导报》记者","With “5.20” approaching, Tsai Ing-wen recently put forward her so-called “three new” cross-Strait interaction proposal of “new situation, new questionnaire, and new model.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this proposal?","Since “5.20” last year, the situation on the island has undergone major changes, impacting cross-Strait relations. We adhere to the One-China Principle; our firm resolve and will to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism will not change, and our sincerity and goodwill in safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and benefiting compatriots on both sides will not change either.\nThe root cause of the changes in cross-Strait relations at present lies in the fact that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, unilaterally undermining the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations. It can be said that the current problems in cross-Strait relations were created single-handedly by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, and that responsibility cannot be shirked by them. This is also a fact that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities cannot conceal or divert attention from, no matter how many new phrases they use. To change the current state of cross-Strait relations, the only way is to clearly answer the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations and acknowledge that both sides belong to one China. Only then can both sides engage in constructive interaction, and only then can cross-Strait relations develop in a sustained and healthy manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778494.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","May I ask a question? Recently, the Taiwan “Coast Guard Administration” injured mainland fishermen. Some Taiwan reports hold that May is the mainland's fishing moratorium period, but fishermen still take risks to go out fishing, which affected the rights and interests of Taiwan fishermen and led to this incident. Does the spokesperson have any comment on this?","On May 6, the day the incident occurred, we already expressed our position and attitude on this matter, demanding that the Taiwan side immediately and strictly investigate the matter, release the people and boats as soon as possible, and prevent such incidents from happening again. Here, I want to emphasize four words: put yourself in their shoes. For many years, the mainland side has provided safeguards for the normal operations of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, maintained good operating order, protected the lives and property of fishermen on both sides, and done a great deal of work. The mainland side has always treated Taiwan fishermen with fraternal friendship. We have set up reception facilities for Taiwan fishermen in many coastal areas, providing shelter from wind, supplies, emergency repairs, rescue, and other assistance to Taiwan fishing boats and fishermen. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are blood brothers. Putting yourself in their shoes, the Taiwan side should stop treating mainland fishermen in brutal and dangerous ways and ensure the lives and property of the fishermen concerned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170510_11778492.htm"],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","This year, cross-Strait relations have been full of espionage intrigue. Following the case involving mainland students in Taiwan, a serving Taiwanese major general has now become involved in a “espionage case.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","I am not aware of the situation you mention. Recently, the Taiwan side has repeatedly hyped such topics. I wonder what the intention is?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Lin Jin-chang, the newly appointed Secretary-General of the Chinese Culture General Association, said in an interview last week that Chinese culture is an ancient and long-standing civilization, and a large part of Taiwan's culture comes from Chinese culture. There are many cultural projects on which both sides can cooperate, and the association will also help expand participation. What is the spokesperson's…","We have stated many times that Chinese culture is the shared spiritual home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and our common roots and soul. Not long ago, after the leadership of the Chinese Culture Association changed, compatriots on both sides have been waiting and watching to see how the association's new leaders and new leadership understand Chinese culture, and what concrete actions they will take regarding cross-Strait cultural exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","We note that recently Tsai Ing-wen has repeatedly made unfriendly remarks on cross-Strait relations, and the Taiwan authorities have adopted relatively harsh measures on cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's view? Does the spokesperson think cross-Strait relations will further deteriorate in the future? In addition, when Tsai Ing-wen recently accepted an interview, she compared Taiwan's “New…","The current deadlock in cross-Strait relations and the predicament facing Taiwan both stem from the fact that after the DPP authorities took office, they did not acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" and did not accept that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, thereby undermining the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The current state of cross-Strait relations is enough to prove that the so-called \"maintaining the status quo\" claimed by the Taiwan authorities is simply a lie and empty talk. To break the current deadlock and untie this knot, the key is to return to the common political foundation that both sides of the Strait belong to one China; there is no other way. We have stressed that different paths lead to different prospects for development. If the Taiwan authorities choose to return to the old path of conflict and confrontation, this runs counter to the hopes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations.\nAs for your second question, regarding Taiwan's \"New Southbound Policy,\" our position has been stated on many occasions. Practices that violate the laws of economic development and are driven purely by political considerations will only harm Taiwan's economy and the interests of Taiwan businesspeople.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","Returning to the WHA issue: Spokesperson, cross-Strait relations have been sluggish for a long time. Will they really continue to slide because of the WHA, escalating from cold confrontation to hot confrontation?","On the issue of the WHA, our spokesperson's statement of May 8 has already made our position very clear. Regarding Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations, our position is very clear and consistent: it must be arranged through cross-Strait consultations under the one-China principle. The responsibility for Taiwan's inability to attend the World Health Assembly this time is very clear. The DPP authorities should recognize reality and return at an early date to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only in this way can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges be sustained, and only then will it be possible for both sides to consult on the issue of Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","On the 5th, Taiwan authorities' leader Tsai Ing-wen, when accepting a joint interview with media from six Southeast Asian countries, used \"China\" to refer to \"mainland China.\" How does the spokesperson view this change?","Our position on the positioning of cross-Strait relations is very clear: there is only one China, the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations. This objective fact cannot be changed by anyone who denies it or deliberately evades it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Li Li-chen (李丽珍), Deputy Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan, recently said that since last year’s “5.20” until now, the Straits Exchange Foundation has not sent a delegation to visit the mainland, and hopes it can visit the mainland in the second half of this year. What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","On the question of cross-Strait exchanges and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between the two associations, our position is very clear: the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan must be authorized to confirm to the mainland its adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Only then will it be possible for the two sides to resume exchanges and consultations and negotiations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","July 7 this year marks the 80th anniversary of the Marco Polo Bridge Incident. According to Taiwan media, the Taiwan authorities have in the past held commemorative special exhibitions and other activities at the Military History Museum of the Taiwan military on the “July 7 Incident” anniversaries ending in 5 or 0, but this year they will suspend them. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this decision by the…","The Marco Polo Bridge Incident broke out on July 7, 1937, opening the curtain on the Chinese nation's all-out War of Resistance. This inspiring history is of great significance to compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and to the Chinese nation as a whole. Without the all-nation resistance war, there would have been no return of Taiwan to the motherland. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should forever remember this history and commemorate it together. To forget history means to betray it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Recently, a “Taiwan sign” was added to the “Blue Sky with White Sun” landscape at the Twin Oaks estate in Washington. Some KMT legislators described this as “Twin Oaks changing color.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The international community generally adheres to the one-China policy. Any small trick that violates the one-China principle is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-10","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","I'd like to ask: Premier Li Keqiang recently visited the Foxconn technology park in Zhengzhou and discussed the direction of “mass entrepreneurship and innovation” with Terry Gou. Because Gou had just traveled to the United States, outside commentators say this shows that Hon Hai Group's global layout is closely watched by both China and the United States. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have also seen the relevant reports. As for specific enterprises' investment decisions, we will not comment. What I want to say is that the mainland's economic development has been positive over the long term, and the prospects for Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland are broad, as all Taiwan businesspeople can plainly see. At the same time, our position of supporting Taiwan-invested enterprises in taking root and developing on the mainland has been consistent and clear. We will continue to adopt relevant positive measures to create a more favorable environment for the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170510_11778512.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-16","Hua Chunying","","中国与越南昨天签署了联合公报，其中，越方重申坚定奉行一个中国政策，支持两岸关系和平发展与中国统一大业，坚决反对任何形式的“台独”分裂活动，不同台湾发展任何官方关系。由于越南是台湾“新南向”政策的重点国家之一，有分析认为，中越签署这份联合公报是中方逐步全面防堵“新南向”政策的举措。中方对此有何看法？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1462257.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-16","Hua Chunying","","这份联合公报中的相关内容和台湾“新南向”政策的关系是什么？会对“新南向”政策产生什么影响？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1462257.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-17","Hua Chunying","","台湾方面今天证实，斐济已于近日撤销驻台湾贸易旅游代表处，还有消息称，斐济官员赴台协助处理了相关事宜。你是否知情？斐济驻台代表处撤销是否与大陆施压有关？是否表明两岸“外交战”再起？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1462735.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-17","Hua Chunying","","据报道，台湾当局17日举行仪式，宣布台对日交流窗口“亚东关系协会”自即日起更名为“台湾日本关系协会”。“日本台湾交流协会”代表沼田干夫参加。请问中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1462735.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2017-05-18","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: the East Asian Relations Association, Taiwan's window for exchanges with Japan, was renamed the “Taiwan-Japan Relations Association” on May 17. What is the mainland's attitude toward this? An Fengshan gave the above response when asked.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 18 (reporter Zhao Bo): Regarding the renaming of Taiwan's exchange window with Japan, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on the 18th, pointing out that any attempt to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail.\nHe said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position on this and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side. I want to emphasize that any attempt to create incidents internationally and to engage in “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” is futile and doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170518_11784833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-19","Hua Chunying","","台湾今年未获邀参加世界卫生大会，但是仍计划派出“卫生福利部长”率团赴瑞士日内瓦，打算在当地举行国际记者会，向世卫组织提交书面抗议信函，并与一些国家代表举行双边或多边会谈。中方对此有何评论？是否会阻挠这些行为甚至要求瑞士不让台湾代表团入境？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1463533.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-19","Hua Chunying","","中美军机危险接近的频率越来越高，中国政府是否将采取措施降低这种频率？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1463533.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2017-05-19","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19 — State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions on the current state of cross-Strait relations on the 19th, said that on the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations, which concerns the destiny of compatriots on both sides, there is no room for ambiguity.\nAn Fengshan said that over the past year, the situation in the Taiwan Strait has undergone major changes, cross-Strait relations have become increasingly tense, the fruits of peaceful development have been lost, and the vital interests of compatriots have been harmed. This situation was entirely created by the DPP authorities alone. The DPP authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” do not accept that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and evade the core question of the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. This has undermined the common political foundation across the Strait and damaged the good momentum of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Facts have again proven that if we adhere to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can grow ever broader. Conversely, if this foundation is destroyed, cross-Strait relations will return to the old path of turmoil and instability.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China cannot be changed, and the one-China principle widely upheld by the international community cannot be challenged. We will firmly adhere to the one-China principle, resolutely uphold the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” and absolutely not tolerate any form of “Taiwan independence” separatism. Compatriots on both sides should join hands to defend the foundation, contain “Taiwan independence,” safeguard the fruits of peaceful development, enhance the well-being of compatriots, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170519_11785841.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-21","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, May 21 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — On May 20, Wu Dun-yih was elected Chairman of the Kuomintang. TAO spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on the 21st: We hope that under the leadership of its new party chairman, the Kuomintang will continue to adhere to the \"1992 Consensus\" and firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence.\" We hope the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China will grasp the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on their common political foundation.\nAn Fengshan said that on May 20, General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee Xi Jinping sent a telegram to Mr. Wu Dun-yih congratulating him on his election as Chairman of the Kuomintang, and Mr. Wu sent a reply thanking him. For many years, the Kuomintang and the CPC, on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" have continuously increased mutual trust, played an important role in opening up and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and achieved fruitful results. We hope that under the leadership of its new party chairman, the Kuomintang will continue to adhere to the \"1992 Consensus\" and firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence.\" We hope both sides will maintain communication, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, grasp the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, continue to enhance the well-being and kinship of compatriots on both sides, and jointly strive for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170521_11786001.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-05-22","Hua Chunying","","因为两岸关系的原因，台湾多年来首次不能参与世界卫生大会。中方对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1464038.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-23","Hua Chunying","","台湾“行政院陆委会主委”张小月22日称，有些国家被中国大陆胁迫签署以一个中国原则参与“一带一路”合作的协议，目的是向大陆申请低息贷款。“陆委会”还称中方通过“一带一路”国际合作高峰论坛发布联合公报宣传一个中国原则，借此对台湾施压。你对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1464446.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-05-23","Hua Chunying","","世卫大会已作出决定，不将涉台提案列入大会补充议程。请问你对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1464446.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 25, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan first announced relevant information about the celebration meeting for the 10th anniversary of the founding of the National Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises, held in Beijing on the 24th, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I will first announce a piece of news: On May 24, the National Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises held a celebration meeting in Beijing marking its 10th anniversary. More than 400 people attended, including members of the national federation, Taiwan business representatives, and heads of important Taiwan industrial and commercial groups. General Secretary Xi Jinping of the CPC Central Committee sent a congratulatory letter, extending warm congratulations and sincere greetings to all members of the national federation and to the broad base of Taiwan businesspeople. Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, met with Taiwan business representatives attending the celebration and delivered a speech. General Secretary Xi's congratulatory letter and Chairman Yu's speech fully reflect the high importance and heartfelt care given to the national federation and the broad base of Taiwan businesspeople. They also point the way forward for the development of the national federation. They reflect the mainland's clear and consistent policy on Taiwan, and they express our policy position of promoting economic and social integration across the Strait under the new circumstances, and of welcoming and supporting Taiwan compatriots in developing on the mainland.\nFirst, we will adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, keep deepening economic and social integration across the Strait, enhance the welfare and kinship of compatriots on both sides, and unite Taiwan compatriots to jointly build a community of shared destiny across the Strait.\nSecond, on the path to achieving the “Two Centenary Goals,” we hope that Taiwan compatriots broadly can catch the fast train of mainland development. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to invest and start businesses. We will continue to provide more favorable conditions for the development of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland, so that Taiwan compatriots can more deeply feel that people on both sides of the Strait are one family and one kin.\nThird, we hope that the national federation and the broad base of Taiwan businesspeople will carry forward the spirit of being pioneers and taking responsibility, adhere to the One China principle, widely unite Taiwan compatriots, and make greater contributions to maintaining and advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, promoting economic and social integration across the Strait, and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170525_11789426.htm"],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Hello, spokesperson. On the day Wu Tun-yih (吴敦义) was elected Chairman of the Kuomintang, the leaders of the KMT and the CPC exchanged telegrams, and their contents attracted attention. May I ask what comment the spokesperson has on the expression regarding the “1992 Consensus” in Wu Tun-yih’s reply telegram?","Everyone knows that in 1992, with authorization from both sides across the Strait, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) reached, through consultations and exchanges of letters and telegrams, a consensus in which each side orally expressed that both sides across the Strait adhere to the one-China principle, later called the “1992 Consensus.” The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is recognition that both sides belong to one China. Its importance lies in clearly defining the nature of cross-Strait relations, showing that the two sides are not a state-to-state relationship. The “1992 Consensus” laid an important foundation for institutionalized cross-Strait consultations and became an important component of the common political foundation for exchanges between the Kuomintang (KMT) and the CPC and for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. If you are interested in this history, you may consult the relevant content on the historical origins of the “1992 Consensus” on the website of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170525_11789424.htm"],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Chang Hsiao-yueh, Chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently claimed that she has long recognized the fact that mainland China has risen, but that Taiwan cannot therefore surrender or be willing to become a part of it. May I ask the spokesperson for his evaluation of this remark?","The mainland's comprehensive national strength keeps rising, and its international influence grows by the day; this is the reality of international politics. What you mentioned, the views of some people on the Taiwan side, clearly reflects a matter of position and mindset. If one can change one's position and mindset, the world will be broader. As long as people acknowledge that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, compatriots on both sides can work hand in hand, pursue common development, share development opportunities, and share the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. This is the good fortune of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","According to some overseas Taiwanese businesspeople, since last year, relevant Taiwan institutions have firmly demanded that they not take part in mainland exchange activities. I would like to ask the spokesperson for comment on this.","These calls reflect the strong dissatisfaction of Taiwan businesspeople overseas with these measures of the Taiwan authorities. These actions by the Taiwan authorities run counter to the shared wishes and practical needs of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for strengthened exchanges and cooperation, and they are unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","I have two questions. First, regarding this year's Universiade in Taipei, why does the mainland not take part in the team events and only take part in the individual events? Is this arrangement made so as not to give the DPP “government” a false impression? Second, what is the progress of the Lee Ming-che case?","Regarding your first question: it is understood that the China University Sports Federation has sent an intention registration form to the organizing committee of the Taipei World University Games (Universiade). Other relevant matters have not yet been determined. The Taipei Universiade is scheduled for August 19 to August 30, which overlaps with the National Games of China, scheduled for August 27 to September 8; this is an objective fact. As for the relevant external analyses and views you mentioned, I will not comment.\nRegarding your second question: it is understood that after the case-handling unit completes its investigation in accordance with the law, it will release information to the public in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","The 70th World Health Assembly opened in Geneva on the 22nd. The World Health Assembly refused to invite Taiwan’s region to attend, but the head of Taiwan’s health department still led a delegation to Geneva in an attempt to attend. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation? Second question: One year after Tsai Ing-wen took office, polls from various sources show rising public dissatisfaction in Taiwan, yet the Tsai…","Regarding your first question, the reason Taiwan cannot attend the World Health Assembly this year was explained at our last press conference. The international community generally recognizes the one-China principle; UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1 both embody this principle, and its authority is beyond question. As a specialized agency of the United Nations, the WHO handling Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the above principles is only natural. We hope the World Health Assembly will not be disrupted.\nRegarding your second question, on the relevant public opinion polls on the island, I will not comment. The conduct of political figures is clear to ordinary people, and the public naturally has its own yardstick in their hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Taiwan is currently holding the “Han Kuang Exercise,” which for the first time simulated attacks and raids on a mainland aircraft carrier. Did the TAO have prior knowledge of this? In addition, some experts believe that the Tsai “government” deliberately raised cross-Strait military tensions this time. Is it possible for cross-Strait relations to escalate from cold confrontation to hot confrontation?","We have repeatedly stressed that peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and Taiwan's future depend on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The Taiwan authorities' “using force to resist reunification” has no way out. They should abandon the “Taiwan independence” position, discard hostile thinking, and return to the common political foundation of acknowledging the “1992 Consensus.” Only in this way can the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations truly be safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","I'd like to ask the spokesperson: on the 31st, SEF extended a Dragon Boat Festival invitation to Taiwanese businesspeople. Yesterday, at the tenth anniversary event of the Taiwan Enterprise Federation, many Taiwanese businesspeople did not indicate they would attend, and those who did respond said the two organizations have now lost their functionality and they are unwilling to attend. How does the spokesperson…","Your two questions are in fact one question. Yesterday, at the celebration meeting marking the 10th anniversary of the founding of the Taiwan Enterprises Association (台企联), its side already responded to this. The Taiwan Enterprises Association is the most influential and representative civil organization of mainland Taiwanese businesspeople. Over the past decade, the Association has united a broad base of Taiwanese businesspeople, worked to promote cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, helped Taiwanese businesspeople and enterprises develop better, and made positive contributions to advancing the development of cross-Strait relations. As to what will benefit the development of Taiwanese businesspeople themselves and what will benefit the development of cross-Strait relations, members of the Association and the broad base of Taiwanese businesspeople naturally have their own judgments and will voice their own opinions. The Taiwan authorities should listen more closely to their voices.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","Two questions. First, Chairman Yu Zhengsheng stated at the tenth anniversary conference of the Taiwan Enterprises Association that any act attempting to change the “1992 Consensus” and any political position supporting “Taiwan independence” are unacceptable, and any disguised “Taiwan independence” will ultimately fail. Does this indicate that the mainland side believes the DPP authorities' current policy line is…","First question: “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, including radical “de jure Taiwan independence,” gradual and soft “Taiwan independence,” and “Taiwan independence” activities that seek to de-Sinicize under the guise of “constitutional amendment” or “amending laws.” We firmly oppose all of these.\nSecond question: Our position and attitude on actively promoting relations between the Chinese Communist Party and the Kuomintang have been consistent. The current cross-Strait situation is complex and severe. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to continue communication with the Kuomintang, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, grasp the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, continue to enhance the well-being and kinship of compatriots on both sides, and work together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","央视记者","Recently, some Taiwan public opinion has argued that because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” Taiwan will have no way to join the “Belt and Road” initiative, and Taiwanese businesses will miss Belt and Road opportunities. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this?","Since May 20 last year, because the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" the regular liaison and communication mechanism and the consultation and negotiation mechanism between the two sides have been interrupted, and the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation has also stalled. The vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait have been harmed, and the interests of the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople and many of their development opportunities have been wasted. These are things we do not wish to see.\nWe have stated many times that we welcome Taiwan's business and industrial circles participating in the Belt and Road Initiative in appropriate ways. Yesterday, at the celebration of the 10th anniversary of the Taiwan Enterprises Association, Director Zhang Zhijun said that we are promoting the establishment of industrial parks closely related to the Belt and Road Initiative in relevant provinces and cities, and actively encouraging and assisting Taiwan businesses to move in, forming new concentrations of Taiwan investment. We actively support Taiwan-funded enterprises in using the \"China-Europe Railway Express\" to sell their goods to Central Asia and Europe, further expanding overseas markets. We are also organizing Taiwan-funded enterprises from the eastern coastal areas to visit the central and western regions to explore business opportunities, and have achieved some positive results. In the past two years, we have organized Taiwan businesspeople many times to visit provinces and cities along the Belt and Road routes, and some Taiwan businesspeople have already found business opportunities locally and begun investing and operating there. In the future, we will continue to advance this work and let the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople share in the opportunities of mainland economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170525_11789423.htm"],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, the DPP authorities transferred Mongolian and Tibetan affairs, which under the Ma Ying-jeou administration had been planned to be managed by the Mainland Affairs Council, to the foreign affairs department for handling. What is the spokesperson’s view?","We will not comment on Taiwan’s internal adjustments, but we firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts that use internal adjustments as a pretext to pursue “de-Sinicization.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","It has been one year since Taiwan's leader Tsai Ing-wen took office. How does the spokesperson assess the changes in cross-Strait relations over this past year?","On May 19, our office's spokesperson already gave a response in our reply to an external inquiry. Over the past year, the situation in the Taiwan Strait has undergone major changes. The current cross-Strait situation is complex and grave. The mechanisms for cross-Strait communication and consultation and for negotiations have been interrupted, exchanges and cooperation in all fields have been affected to varying degrees, and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides have been seriously harmed. This is something no one wishes to see. The root cause of the current cross-Strait stalemate is that after the DPP authorities took office, they refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and did not recognize that both sides belong to one China, unilaterally undermining the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Yet rather than considering how to change the current stalemate in cross-Strait relations, the DPP authorities have allowed and promoted “de-Sinicization” and other “Taiwan independence” separatist activities on the island, obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and incited opposing public opinion on both sides. This is the greatest obstacle to the current development of cross-Strait relations.\nOur major policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We will continue to uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, work to maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and, together with compatriots on both sides, firmly oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. The Taiwan authorities should keep in mind the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, positively respond to the expectations of compatriots on both sides for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and confirm the common political foundation that embodies the one-China principle. This is the only right path to resolving the current stalemate in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170525_11789422.htm"],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","We note that Wu Dun-yih was recently elected KMT chairman. Some Taiwanese scholars have reminded that the KMT should let young people in Taiwan truly understand the relationship between Taiwan and the mainland and its future development in order to move toward 2020. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this? In addition, according to Taiwanese media reports, the Fiji Trade and Tourism Office in Taiwan…","Regarding your first question: Youth is the future and hope of society, and a brighter future for cross-Strait relations also needs young people from both sides to build together. We have consistently encouraged young people across the Strait to strengthen exchanges and communication, and we are also willing to provide more opportunities for the broad masses of young Taiwanese to study, work, start businesses, and develop on the mainland. The purpose is to help young people on both sides strengthen mutual understanding, deepen their knowledge of Chinese history and culture, improve their correct understanding of cross-Strait relations, and work together to advance the development of cross-Strait relations.\nRegarding your second question, concerning Fiji, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position. The one-China principle is widely upheld by the international community; it reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","团结报记者","Reports indicate that the Taiwan military authorities will change generals' official mobile phone numbers before the end of July, as a strategy to prevent so-called “espionage.” What does the Taiwan Affairs Office think of this?","The Taiwan side hypes this kind of topic every so often. I don't know what the motive behind it is.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","台湾中央通讯社","Yesterday, the “constitutional interpretation case” on same-sex marriage in Taiwan reached a conclusion. Taiwan hopes to set a precedent in Asia by legally protecting same-sex marriage. I would like to ask the spokesperson: if in the future a mainland resident and a same-sex partner from Taiwan marry in Taiwan, will the mainland recognize the legal effect of such a marriage?","I have seen related reports involving cross-Strait marriage issues. I suggest you consult the relevant professional departments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","There is currently a view on the island that the mainland keeps “magnetically attracting” Taiwan talent, mainly in order to obtain Taiwan's technology. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Under market economy conditions, the flow of production factors, including the flow of talent, is a normal phenomenon. We welcome broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to study, work, and start businesses, to share in the mainland's development opportunities and achieve greater development. At the same time, we have also been strengthening protection in areas such as intellectual property rights, to provide a fair environment for a broad range of market entities, including Taiwan businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","台湾三立新闻记者","After being elected, Wu Den-yih mentioned that if the KMT returns to power, it will certainly respect the “1992 Consensus.” People generally interpret this “respect” as leaving considerable room for imagination. We would like to ask the Taiwan Affairs Office how it evaluates this new KMT leader, and whether the “KMT-CPC Forum” is truly a good occasion for the two parties to meet?","On the understanding and position regarding the “1992 Consensus,” I have already answered earlier. Our position on actively promoting KMT–CPC relations is very clear. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the KMT and the CPC will continue to maintain communication and strengthen exchanges and dialogue. Relevant parties of the two parties have been maintaining communication all along. Regarding the specific matters of exchanges between the two parties that you mentioned, we will announce them promptly once there is definite news.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Taiwan's New Power Party recently advocated placing the Taiwan MAC, currently under the Interior Committee, among the ministries supervised by the Foreign Affairs Committee. What is the spokesperson's comment?","If the Taiwan side attempts to pursue “Taiwan independence” small moves of de-Sinicization through internal adjustments, we firmly oppose them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Second question: Chang Hsiao-yueh, Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that many countries, in order to apply for low-interest loans from the mainland, were coerced into recognizing the one-China principle in order to join the “Belt and Road,” which is different from the “1992 Consensus, each side with its own interpretation of one China,” and therefore must never be accepted. What is…","The Belt and Road Initiative is an open and inclusive development platform, to which countries around the world actively respond, hoping to find business opportunities and achieve win-win cooperation. The one-China principle is generally recognized by the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle has become the consensus of more and more countries and international organizations; this is the reality of today's world economy and international politics. I think it is precisely the DPP authorities themselves who are out of touch with reality. Some people in Taiwan really should pull their heads out of the sand, open their eyes and look at the outside world, rather than continuing to anesthetize themselves and fool themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","香港大公报、大公网记者","Recently, MAC Chairperson Chang Hsiao-yueh made many statements about cross-Strait relations, including one that Taiwan is not part of mainland China. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","Our position is very clear: there is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This historical fact cannot be denied. The international community generally adheres to the one-China principle, and this is also not to be challenged.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201705/t20170525_11789421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-25","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a reporter's question about cross-Strait exchanges between the KMT and the CPC following Wu Den-yih's election as chairman of the Kuomintang, An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the regular press conference on May 25 in response to questions: The mainland side's position and attitude in actively promoting relations between the two parties have been consistent. Cross-Strait relations are currently in a complex and grim situation. We are willing to continue communication with the Kuomintang on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and dialogue, to grasp the correct direction for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and to continuously enhance the welfare and kinship of compatriots on both sides, working together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Relevant departments of the two parties have maintained communication. As for specific matters of exchanges between the two parties, we will announce them in a timely manner once there is definite news.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170525_11789425.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-05-26","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 26 (reporter Zhao Bo) — An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 26th in response to a question: The national security authorities have learned that Taiwan resident Lee Ming-che, on suspicion of “subversion of state power,” has been arrested in accordance with law by the state security authorities of Hunan Province in recent days, with approval from the procuratorate.\nAn Fengshan said: The investigation by national security authorities has found that since 2012, Lee Ming-che has frequently entered the mainland for activities, colluded with relevant persons on the mainland, drafted action programs, established an illegal organization, and planned and implemented activities to subvert our state power. On March 19, 2017, national security authorities took compulsory measures in accordance with law against Lee Ming-che, who had entered the mainland for activities. After interrogation, Lee Ming-che and others confessed without reservation to engaging in activities that endanger our national security, and the judicial authorities will handle the case in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201705/t20170526_11790356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 3 dispatch (reporter Chen Jianxing): In response to heavy rainfall sweeping across the whole island of Taiwan, with many areas flooded and causing casualties and property losses, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 3rd: We are highly concerned about the safety of life and property of Taiwan compatriots, we mourn those who died, extend sympathy to affected residents, and will continue to follow the disaster situation.\nAccording to Taiwan's meteorological authorities, affected by the southwesterly flow and a stationary front, torrential rain has hit various parts of the island since the 2nd, causing road collapses, bridge breakages, flooding and other disasters, which have resulted in casualties. Rainfall is still ongoing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170603_11793951.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 3 (reporter Chen Jianxing): According to reports, in a hotel attack in Manila, the Philippines, which occurred on the 2nd, four Taiwan compatriots were killed. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 3rd, saying: We express our condolences for the Taiwan compatriots who died in the Philippines. We are willing to provide any necessary assistance.\nIn the early morning of the 2nd, the “Manila Resorts World” hotel was attacked. The gunman involved fired shots and used gasoline to set fire to the tables, causing a fire and serious casualties. Local police, in their search, found 36 bodies of victims.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170603_11793952.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-06-07","Hua Chunying","","The above-mentioned report also claimed that the US opposes any unilateral change to the status quo in the Taiwan Straits by either side and does not support \"Taiwan independence\" and maintains a one-China policy that is based on the three joint communiqués and the \"Taiwan Relations Act (TRA)\". It also mentioned that, consistent with the \"TRA\", the US has contributed to peace and stability in the Taiwan Straits,…","China's stance on the Taiwan question has been consistent and clear-cut. The so-called \"Taiwan Relations Act\" unilaterally enacted by the US severely violates the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués. The Chinese government has firmly opposed it all along.\nChina requires the US to honor the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, cease arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan and cautiously handle Taiwan-related issues, so as not to hurt the overall interests of China-US relations and cross-Straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1468550.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1468506.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-06-07","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On June 7, Beijing time, the US Department of Defense released its 2017 “Annual Report on Military and Security Developments Involving the People's Republic of China,” which makes irresponsible comments on China's national defense and military development, hypes the so-called “China military threat,” and speculates about cross-Strait relations and the situation in the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this.\nChina firmly pursues the path of peaceful development and firmly adheres to a defensive national defense policy. In recent years, the Chinese military has actively carried out overseas military missions such as peacekeeping, escort, and disaster relief, provided more public security goods, and has won widespread praise from the international community. China does not engage in military expansion or seek spheres of influence, and it has always been a firm force for maintaining world peace.\nOn the issues of the East China Sea and the South China Sea, China firmly defends national sovereignty and security and firmly maintains regional peace and stability. The US has strengthened its military deployments in the region and frequently sent warships and aircraft on close-in reconnaissance, creating tense conditions in the region.\nChina's national defense spending has always been open and transparent, and the reform of the Chinese military, the development of its weapons and equipment, and the building of its cyberspace defense capabilities are legitimate and reasonable. The accusations in the US report are pure speculation.\nWe note that the US report devotes a special section to China-US military relations. The development of healthy and stable military relations between the two sides serves the common interests of both and requires joint efforts from both. We hope the US will view China's national defense and military development rationally and objectively, move in the same direction as China, earnestly implement the important consensus reached by the leaders of the two countries, and do more useful work for the development of military relations.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2017-06/07/content_4796155.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2017-06-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je recently gave an interview to the media, expressing some views on this year's “Twin-City Forum” and on cross-Strait relations. What comment does the spokesperson have? Ma Xiaoguang made the above statement on this.\nReporters also asked: According to convention, this year's “Twin-City Forum” should be held in Shanghai; what considerations are there at present? In response, Ma Xiaoguang said…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 10 (reporter Chen Jianxing): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 10th: We have noted media reports on the exclusive interview with Taipei Mayor Ke Wenzhe. As long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of exchanges between cross-Strait cities, we maintain a positive and open attitude toward interactions between cross-Strait cities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170610_11798295.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 13 (Reporter Qi Xianghui) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to questions on the 13th: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has issued a statement on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Pakistan. There is only one China in the world. Adhering to the One China principle is the broad consensus of the international community, and the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Pakistan reflects the wishes of the people and the trend of the times.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the One China principle, is the anchor for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus\" and recognizing its core meaning that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct path of peaceful development. The Taiwan authorities should recognize the objective trend and make a wise choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170613_11799869.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-06-14","Lu Kang","","Yesterday, the announcement of the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Panama grabbed international attention. The Chinese leaders and Foreign Minister Wang Yi have all spoken on this. I am wondering whether you as the Spokesperson have anything more to say.","We have noted the extensive reports at home and abroad on the official establishment of diplomatic ties at the ambassadorial level between the People's Republic of China and the Republic of Panama. The international media commented a lot on this, and the Foreign Ministry Spokesperson's Office also received a lot of inquiries on this issue. Here, I would like to reaffirm China's position.\nOn June 13, Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Isabel Saint Malo de Alvarado, Panama's Vice President and Foreign Minister, signed in Beijing a joint communique on the establishment of diplomatic relations between the People's Republic of China and the Republic of Panama on behalf of their respective government. According to the communique, the Chinese and Panamanian governments have decided to recognize each other and establish diplomatic relations at the ambassadorial level effective from the date of signature of the communique.\nThere is but one China in the world. The Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. These are historical facts as well as well-acknowledged norms guiding international relations.\nPanama is an important Latin American country. The amicable exchanges between the Chinese and Panamanian people date back a long way. The Chinese people have profound friendship with the Panamanian people. The Panamanian government acknowledges the one China principle and promises to stick to it. It chooses to cut off the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan and establishes diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China, which is a right choice that meets the trend of our times and the wishes of our people. China highly commends that.\nOn the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one China principle, China stands ready to develop and deepen all-around friendly cooperation with Panama and deliver more benefits to the two countries and peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470265.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470213.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-14","Lu Kang","","Does the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Panama means the end of the \"diplomatic truce\" across the Straits? Will the mainland establish or resume diplomatic relations with more countries which have the so-called diplomatic ties with Taiwan? Will there be any major adjustments in the policies of the Chinese central government towards Taiwan?","As for your last question, I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nThe one China principle is the major principled position which concerns China's core interests and the feelings of the 1.3 billion Chinese people. It is also the prerequisite and the political basis for China to maintain and develop friendly cooperative relations with other countries in the world. The Chinese government stays committed to developing friendly cooperative relations with other countries in the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one China principle.\nLooking around the world, China's circle of friends is growing bigger and bigger. Refusing to recognize the 1992 Consensus will end up nowhere. Only by coming back to the right track set in the 1992 Consensus and recognizing that both sides across the Taiwan Straits belong to the one and same China can there be preconditions and basis for the peaceful development of the cross-Straits relations and can the common aspiration of the people across the Straits for pursuing common development, sharing opportunities and jointly scoring glorious achievements be realized.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470265.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470213.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-14","Lu Kang","","The US State Department officials said that the US opposes any unilateral action by either side across the Straits to change the status quo of the Taiwan Straits, urging concerned parties to engage in dialogues and avoid escalatory and destabilizing moves. What is your comment? Also, Taiwan officials said that before Panama announced its decision to establish diplomatic ties with China, Taiwan asked the US to…","First of all, the one China policy is an open pledge made by the US government since the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the US. Second, the past experience has shown that only by sticking to the 1992 Consensus, which incorporates the one China principle, can we create a favorable condition for the existence of stability, peace and positive interactions across the Straits. Any deviation from the 1992 Consensus will only result in greater instability across the Straits. We believe the US side is very clear about that.\nAs for whether or not the Panamanian government had any contact with the US government, I don't have any information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470265.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470213.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first introduced the relevant situation for the 9th Straits Forum, which will be held in Fujian from June 17 to 23. He then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends. The press conference now begins. First, I will introduce some information about the Straits Forum.\nThe 9th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian from June 17 to 23, and the forum's main conference will be held in Xiamen on June 18. Preparatory work is now in place. Yu Zhengsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, will attend the Straits Forum. Hung Hsiu-chu, Chairperson of the Kuomintang; representatives of political parties such as the People First Party, the New Party, and the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union; representatives of relevant counties and cities in Taiwan and Taiwan-side organizers; and more than 8,000 people from all walks of life in Taiwan will be invited to attend this forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","This forum adheres to its positioning of being “civilian in nature, grassroots in character, and broad in scope.” Centered on the theme of “expanding civilian exchanges and deepening integrated development,” it has carefully planned and designed more than 30 related activities, which display the following features:\nFirst, it brings together the wisdom of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. For the first time, it set up an online platform to openly solicit proposals for Straits Forum activities from the Taiwan public, held a “Golden Ideas” competition for the Straits Forum, and selected outstanding Taiwan creative proposals for inclusion in the event arrangements.\nSecond, it expands the sectors and fields of exchange. Guided by public needs, it designed activities around the “three major brands” of workers, youth, and women; the “four major ties” of surname kinship groups, hometown associations, folk beliefs, and mainland spouses; the “five major fields” of culture, education, healthcare, law, and business and industry; and the “six major grassroots organizations” of agriculture, fisheries, water conservancy, township and village neighborhood committees, community associations, and public welfare and charity. It continues to expand the sectors and fields of exchange and provides platforms for cross-strait exchange and cooperation.\nThird, it continues to serve youth entrepreneurship and innovation. It held the Straits Youth Forum, the 7th session of the New Youth New Generation Leadership Training Camp, and cross-strait talent exchange and matching events, invited Taiwan youth to take part in experiential exchanges, offered employment, internship, and startup positions to Taiwan youth, and served cross-strait youth, especially Taiwan youth, in coming to the mainland to work and start businesses.\nFourth, it reviews the achievements of cross-strait exchanges and looks ahead to integrated development. This year marks the 30th anniversary of the breaking of the isolation between the two sides and the opening of civilian exchanges. Economic and social integrated development across the Taiwan Strait has become the direction for deepening cross-strait exchange and cooperation. The forum grasps the two key words “30th anniversary” and “integrated development,” and in its event arrangements, through the accounts of those who experienced these events, reviews history together and looks toward the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801043.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","After Wu Den-yih was elected Chairman of the Kuomintang, he stated that he firmly opposes “Taiwan independence” and advocates the “1992 Consensus” and “one China, each with its own interpretation.” The “1992 Consensus” of “one China, each with its own interpretation” will not be expressed as “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” How does the spokesperson comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is the recognition that both sides belong to one China. It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations, showing that the two sides are not a relationship between two countries. For many years, the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang have, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” advanced the peaceful development of relations between the two parties and across the Strait, achieving fruitful results. We are willing to continue communication with the Kuomintang on this common political foundation, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, and work together to enhance the well-being of people on both sides and to maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801040.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","According to reports, DPP caucus convener Ker Chien-ming said that the “Taiwan independence party platform” has become the greatest obstacle to cross-Strait exchanges, and that amending the “party platform” is a practical and feasible approach. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. The DPP holds to the “Taiwan independence” party platform and insists on the separatist position of “one side, one country.” This is the fundamental obstacle to this party’s dealings with us. Only by abandoning the “Taiwan independence” party platform and changing its “Taiwan independence” stance can the DPP possibly improve relations with the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801039.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","It is reported that the so-called “Hong Kong Democracy Concern Alliance,” formed by multiple elected representatives in Taiwan's legislature, including Huang Kuo-chang, was recently established, and several Hong Kong legislators traveled to Taiwan to attend related events, which has caused controversy. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","We firmly oppose the collusion of “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” forces to interfere with the implementation of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong, meddle in Hong Kong's internal affairs, and undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability. This scheme and conduct are unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801036.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","At last month's press conference, the spokesperson introduced a batch of newly issued policy measures that facilitate Taiwan compatriots. Will the spokesperson announce any new measures in the near future?","Over a period of time, we have successively announced a batch of policy measures to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots studying, working, starting businesses and living on the mainland. We already introduced the relevant measures at the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference on May 10. It is understood that the relevant departments are still actively studying new policy measures, and some measures are expected to be issued in the near future. The main ones are:\n1. Taiwan residents employed on the mainland will enjoy the right to contribute to and use the housing provident fund. The Ministry of Housing and Urban-Rural Development is actively conducting research together with relevant departments. Building on the experience of localities such as Fujian and Shanghai, it will soon issue a nationwide policy that clearly provides that Taiwan compatriots employed on the mainland enjoy housing provident fund benefits on an equal footing, supporting them in contributing to and using the housing provident fund, improving their ability to buy or rent housing, and helping them settle down and feel secure on the mainland.\n2. Taiwan residents who live, work and study on the mainland may participate in social insurance on the mainland. To further clarify and standardize the rules on Taiwan residents’ participation in social insurance on the mainland, and to safeguard the social insurance rights of Taiwan residents who live, work and study on the mainland, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security is studying and formulating policy documents on Taiwan residents’ participation in social insurance on the mainland. Policies on Taiwan compatriots who live on the mainland but are neither studying nor employed, participating in urban resident basic medical insurance, will also be studied together. It is understood that the relevant policy documents are currently being solicited for opinions from relevant State Council departments and localities, and will be issued and implemented at an appropriate time after further refinement.\n3. The Ministry of Finance and the Ministry of Education will add a scholarship program of higher honorary status for Taiwan students at mainland universities. On the basis of the existing scholarships for Taiwan students at universities, the Ministry of Finance is studying, together with the Ministry of Education, adding awards of higher honorary status for Taiwan students studying on the mainland, which are planned to be formally implemented starting from the autumn semester of 2017.\n4. The National Tourism Administration has required tourist accommodation enterprises to provide more convenient travel accommodation services for Taiwan compatriots. Recently, the National Tourism Administration issued a document requiring local tourism administrative departments to strengthen policy guidance, and requiring tourist accommodation enterprises to strictly abide by national laws, regulations and relevant policy provisions, not to set obstacles to check-in for Taiwan compatriots for any unjustified reason, and to strictly standardize service standards and improve service awareness, so as to provide Taiwan compatriots with higher-quality and more convenient accommodation services.\n5. The banking industry will improve small-amount credit card services for Taiwan compatriots. To address the high threshold for Taiwan compatriots applying for credit cards, under the guidance of the China Banking Regulatory Commission, some banks have adjusted or plan to adjust their credit card policies for Taiwan compatriots. For example, the head office of the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China has issued a new version of the “Personal Customer Credit Management Measures.” For Taiwan compatriots applying for credit cards, apart from the age requirement of being between 25 and 65 years old, the other access conditions are the same as for mainland citizens. Banks may score customers based on internal rating models and grant credit limits of 3,000 to 20,000 yuan based on those scores. At the same time, some banks have also issued notices requiring frontline staff to further raise their level of professional competence and service awareness in cross-Strait financial business.\nIn addition, it is understood that to do a good job in employment services for Taiwan students graduating from mainland universities this year, the Ministry of Education is studying relevant policies. For eligible mainland university graduates who are willing to work on the mainland, employment agreements will be issued to them, along with the National Employment Registration Certificate for Ordinary Higher Education Graduates (Undergraduate and Junior College) or the National Employment Registration Certificate for Postgraduate Graduates, further providing policy convenience for Taiwan students studying on the mainland to find employment after graduation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801041.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","The mainland's announcement of establishing diplomatic relations with Panama this time: may I ask the spokesperson, which is more important, cross-Strait relations or one more diplomatic partner for the mainland? Does the mainland subjectively wish to follow the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations? On the second question: Tainan Mayor Lai Ching-te said “friendly to China and love Taiwan,”…","On the first question, regarding the China-Pakistan establishment of diplomatic relations: There is only one China in the world, and adhering to the one-China principle is the common understanding of the international community. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Pakistan is the will of the people and the trend of the times. Everyone remembers that between 2008 and May 20 of last year, on the common political basis of opposing 'Taiwan independence' and adhering to the '1992 Consensus,' the two sides across the Strait opened a new era of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, including reducing friction between the two sides in foreign affairs. Last year, after major changes occurred in Taiwan's political situation, we stated on multiple occasions that our basic policy toward Taiwan would not change, and that our position and attitude of pursuing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the political basis of opposing 'Taiwan independence' and adhering to the '1992 Consensus' would not change either. However, since May 20 last year, the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been undermined, and the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations to date have been seriously impacted. Who is changing the status quo of cross-Strait relations, and who is not sincere about pursuing the path of peaceful development, the responsibility is very clear.\nI would like to stress once again that the '1992 Consensus,' which embodies the one-China principle, is the anchor of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by acknowledging the '1992 Consensus' and recognizing its core meaning that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct direction of peaceful development. The Taiwan authorities should recognize the objective trend and make a wise choice.\nOn the second question, regarding the situation you mentioned, we have noted the relevant reports in Taiwan's media. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not relations between countries. Whatever the claims, the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations must be made clear. On the one hand holding the position of 'Taiwan independence,' and on the other hand loudly talking about 'affinity and friendliness,' is self-contradictory. If DPP figures truly have sincerity in improving and developing cross-Strait relations, they should change course not only in words but also in actions, and thoroughly abandon the position of 'Taiwan independence.'","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801042.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the travel of mainland personnel for exchanges to Taiwan has been strictly controlled by the Taiwan authorities. The spokesperson of the Mainland Affairs Council said that it would pay attention to four categories of situations regarding mainland personnel's exchanges to Taiwan, and that the mainland's refusal to receive Taiwan official personnel is what hinders cross-strait exchanges. What is the…","We have consistently and actively encouraged and supported civil exchanges and cooperation across all fields across the Taiwan Strait; this is well known and plain to see. Since the DPP authorities took office, their practices of interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation have continually escalated; this is also plain to see. Yet they turn the tables and blame us. In my view, this is merely a sign of their guilty conscience.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801038.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Taiwan's well-known documentary director Chi Po-lin recently died in a plane crash. Has the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed condolences?","Mr. Qi Bolin was a famous Taiwan film director who for many years actively took part in cross-strait film and television exchanges and cooperation and paid attention to ecological and environmental protection, leaving a deep impression on all of us. We mourn the untimely passing of Mr. Qi Bolin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Continuing the Panama issue: after Panama and Taiwan “severed diplomatic ties,” a Taiwanese media personality claimed that the mainland provided Panama with an interest-free loan of US$3 billion. I would like to ask the spokesperson whether this is true. The spokesperson has consistently stressed that cross-Strait relations can develop peacefully only on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” If the current DPP…","On the first question, I think everyone has seen the \"China-Pakistan Joint Communiqué\" on the establishment of diplomatic relations, and has also seen Foreign Minister Wang Yi's remarks. They state very clearly that there was no exchange of so-called \"commercial interests\" of any kind. Of course, for further details, you may inquire with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\nOn the second question, as is well known, we have always treated Taiwan's external dealings in accordance with the one-China principle. We also hope the Taiwan authorities will make a wise choice on the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and lay a lasting foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视记者","Continuing the question of the Taiwan–Panama “severing of diplomatic ties,” the leader of Taiwan's authorities has harshly “attacked” it, stating that Taiwan will reassess the cross-Strait situation and will not yield under threat. How does the spokesperson respond to this? In addition, some public opinion reports argue that this approach may cause the hearts of people on both sides to drift further apart. What…","Let me answer the second question first. As we have said before, as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of the nature of exchanges between cities across the Strait, we maintain a positive and open attitude toward exchanges and interactions between cities on both sides.\nTurning to the first question, the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Pakistan is the trend of the times, as I have just explained. On the question of public sentiment, don’t you think that undermining the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the main reason why the hearts of people on both sides are growing farther apart? In fact, returning cross-Strait relations to the right direction is, for the Taiwan authorities, a matter of a single thought. We hope they will recognize the objective trend of events and make a wise choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Last week, Ko Wen-je gave an interview expressing some views on cross-Strait relations and the “Twin-City Forum,” and the spokesperson also responded accordingly. May I ask the spokesperson: under the current circumstances, are Ko Wen-je's remarks worth the DPP authorities and DPP figures learning from? In addition, Ko also said in the interview that the goal should not merely be to maintain the status quo but to…","Regarding the views expressed by Mayor Ko Wen-je in his media interview, I have already responded earlier. As for the DPP’s policies, our position on the DPP’s policies is clear and consistent. As long as the DPP does not abandon its “Taiwan independence” separatist stance of “one side, one country,” we will not engage in exchanges with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","It is understood that the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will hold the 2017 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Seminar. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","As I understand it, in order to support Taiwan youth in coming to the mainland for internships, employment, and entrepreneurship, after consultation at the summit of both sides, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will hold the 2017 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Seminar in Dongguan, Guangdong Province, on July 7–8. The seminar takes “Chase Dreams, Create the Future” as its theme, and includes segments on policy introductions for employment and entrepreneurship, experience sharing, promotion of job opportunities, and interaction among cross-Strait youth. Its purpose is to help Taiwan youth connect with mainland enterprises and find opportunities to develop on the mainland. Chairman Zeng Peiyan and Chairman Xiao Wanchang of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, leaders of some cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites, and representatives of cross-Strait young entrepreneurs and Taiwan youth students will attend the seminar. Please continue to follow this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170614_11801037.htm"],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently released a public opinion poll showing that 45% of Taiwan residents believe that cross-strait exchanges are proceeding too slowly. The Mainland Affairs Council believes that these results are related to the recent overall cross-strait situation and the mainland's restrictive and tightening measures on personnel exchanges with Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's…","I think that compared with before “5.20,” the perception that the pace of exchanges has slowed among the Taiwan public may be true, but the cause has been completely reversed, black made white. It is not mainland restrictions. As I just said, since last “5.20,” because the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been undermined, the situation of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation has been impacted, and the Taiwan authorities have, openly and covertly, increased restrictions on mainland personnel traveling to Taiwan and controls over Taiwan compatriots' exchanges to the mainland. These facts are clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Since taking office, the DPP authorities have continuously made small moves to “de-Sinicize” and promote cultural “Taiwan independence.” But this year at the Dragon Boat Festival, the DPP for the first time formed a team to take part in the dragon boat race. What is your comment?","This shows that “de-Sinicization” cannot be eliminated. The two sides of the Strait are blood-related brothers, and Taiwan compatriots also belong to the Chinese nation, descendants of the Yan and Huang emperors. We share the same culture and the same customs. After all, one cannot say that the Dragon Boat Festival and Qu Yuan are not Chinese!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The pan-green media outlet Beautiful Island Electronic Journal recently released a new poll showing that Tsai Ing-wen advocates the so-called “maintaining the status quo” in cross-Strait relations, but as many as 54.4% of Taiwan residents believe that Tsai's so-called “maintaining the status quo” actually tends toward pursuing “Taiwan independence.” What is the spokesperson's view on this?","We do not comment on specific polls in Taiwan. However, I believe the results of this kind of poll should prompt compatriots on both sides of the Strait to reflect. Is it, as they say, “maintaining the status quo” and safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, or is it a departure from this goal, pushing and manipulating, openly and covertly, some gradual “de-Sinicization” “Taiwan independence” activities? I believe compatriots on both sides of the Strait see this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The 9th Straits Forum is about to be held in Fujian. Some Taiwan media have pointed out that this year's Straits Forum should become a link for the stable development of cross-Strait economic and trade relations. The cross-Strait economic and trade issue most worthy of attention and discussion at the Straits Forum is undoubtedly how Taiwan businesses can take part in the “Belt and Road.” What is the…","Media have all kinds of remarks, and asking me to evaluate them may also exceed my ability. I think that from the introduction I just gave about the Straits Forum, you should understand that the Straits Forum is a platform for broad grassroots exchanges between the two sides of the Strait. Over the eight years since the forum was held, it has launched a series of policy measures to promote cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields. More important and more precious, it has built a great stage for grassroots people across the Strait to exchange with each other and enhance mutual understanding. Economic and trade exchanges are important; they are compatriots on both sides holding hands. But communication of hearts is even more important; it is compatriots on both sides with hearts connected. Therefore, I suggest that media friends, in reporting on the Straits Forum, focus more on the stories of grassroots exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, to promote heart-to-heart understanding among people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Second question: We know this year marks the 80th anniversary of the “July 7 Incident.” There is news that the KMT is planning related commemorative activities. I would like to ask whether the mainland side has any plans in this regard, and whether it would take the form of a joint cross-Strait commemoration.","On July 7, 1937, the \"Marco Polo Bridge Incident\" broke out, thereby opening the historic chapter of the Chinese nation's all-out War of Resistance. This heroic and tragic history carries very important and special significance for compatriots on both sides of the Strait and for the Chinese nation as a whole. It can be said that without the national resistance as a whole, there would have been no return of Taiwan. Under new historical conditions, compatriots on both sides of the Strait, in commemorating the War of Resistance, should not only forever remember this history, but also work together toward the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, so as to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, we have seen relevant parties in Taiwan say that Taiwan is a victim of drugs, and that most of Taiwan’s drugs come from the mainland into Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment on his remarks?","As for where Taiwan's drugs come from, I am not aware of it. But I want to emphasize that the mainland resolutely combats drug crime, including drug crime involving both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We will severely punish drug criminals and, under any circumstances, take effective measures without leniency. This is unequivocal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","May I ask the spokesperson: as summer approaches, this is usually the peak season for exchanges among young people across the Strait. What plans are there for summer exchanges among young people on both sides, including university students?","Indeed, the summer vacation is the peak season for exchanges between young people across the Strait, especially university students. This summer, exchanges between young people on both sides will be rich and colorful. In addition to mutual visits, seminars, and summer camps, a major highlight this summer is that Taiwan students will come to the mainland for internships and experiential exchanges, and the scale and number of participants will increase substantially. I hope you will pay attention to the relevant activities at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170614_11801071.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-06-15","Lu Kang","","Yesterday, the so-called \"Foreign Ministry of Taiwan\" said that due to the pressure from China, the so-called Foreign Representative Offices of Taiwan in five countries that don't have the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan have been requested to change their names. The five offices are located in Nigeria, the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, Jordan and Ecuador respectively. Among these countries, Nigeria…","Our position on this cannot be more clear-cut. Adhering to the one China principle conforms to the trend of our times and the wishes of the international community. It serves as an important political prerequisite and basis for China to establish diplomatic relations and develop friendly cooperation with other countries around the world. The Chinese government highly commends relevant countries for adhering to the one China principle while handling the Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470574.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-15","Lu Kang","","How does China view its future relations with Panama after establishing diplomatic relations with it? It is reported that following the severing of the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" between Taiwan and Panama and the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Panama, the Panamanian students who are studying on scholarships in Taiwan may find it difficult to finish their studies. What are the comments of the…","The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Panama opens up broad prospects for bilateral cooperation across the board. The Chinese side stands ready to strengthen exchanges with the Panamanian side, including the friendly exchanges in education and people-to-people and cultural exchanges. We have taken note of the fact that the Panamanian students studying in Taiwan on scholarships may encounter some difficulties. We welcome them to study in the mainland and will provide needed and timely assistance to them. As for other Panamanian students in Taiwan, we are also willing to offer assistance to them on the basis of respecting their own will. In the future, we will offer scholarships to Panamanian students in China every year.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470574.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-15","Lu Kang","","Yesterday the US Secretary of State Rex Tillerson said at the Congress that the United States adheres to the one China principle while it also will honor all the commitments it has made to Taiwan. He mentioned that whether the one China policy is still sustainable in the next fifty is a complex topic which is under discussion on the part of the US side. What is your comment?","First of all, I have noted that the US Secretary of State Rex Tillerson stated that the Trump administration will firmly stick to the one China policy. The one China principle is a political basis for the China-US relationship, which is clearly stipulated in the three China-US joint communiques. Since President Donald Trump took office, the top leaders of the United States including President Donald Trump and Secretary of State Rex Tillerson, when meeting with the Chinese side, have all explicitly pointed out that the United States will stick to the one China policy. We urge the US side to stick to its pledges made in the three joint communiques, and properly deal with Taiwan-relation issues with prudence. After all, the one China principle has become a universally acknowledged norms governing international relations and it is also the important prerequisite for any other country to develop friendly relations and conduct win-win cooperation with China. We believe that the US side is quite clear about this.\nRegarding why Secretary of State Rex Tillerson mentioned the next fifty years, it has to be explained by the US side. I have also noted that some people in Taiwan are getting some illusions because of these words. If these people cannot put into perspective the trend of the development in the next fifty years, I suggest look back at the past fifty years. Recognizing the trend of the international situation, the development trajectory of the China-US relations, and the great rejuvenation process of the Chinese nation, and comparing the past fifty years with the present, they can gain a correct understanding of the future.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470574.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-16","Lu Kang","","It is reported that ROK President Moon Jae-in said during a speech marking the 17th anniversary of the June 15 Joint Declaration that if the DPRK stops making additional nuclear and missile provocations, the ROK can come to dialogue with the DPRK without conditions. The two sides will be able to comprehensively discuss complete dismantlement of the DPRK nukes and the establishment of a peace regime on the Korean…","We have noted relevant reports and welcome these positive messages released by the DPRK and the ROK. Descending from the same nationality, if the ROK and the DPRK could improve their relations and move forward reconciliation and cooperation, it would serve the fundamental interests of the two sides and contribute to regional peace and development. Under the current circumstances, we hope that the two sides continue to demonstrate good faith, commit themselves to reconciliation and cooperation, and play a positive role in alleviating tensions on the Peninsula and resuming dialogues and consultations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1470941.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1470893.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-20","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan and Panama still have a free trade agreement. What does China think about this?","Last week, China and Panama established diplomatic relations. The Panamanian side has stated explicitly in the communique that it recognizes the one China principle and promises that it will not have any form of official contacts or develop any form of official relations with Taiwan. The attitude of the Panamanian side on this is quite clear-cut.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1471820.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1471704.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-20","Geng Shuang","","Does a free trade agreement constitute diplomatic ties between Taiwan and Panama?","What I want to tell you is that the Panamanian side has promised that it will not have any form of official contacts or develop any form of official relations with Taiwan. What are official contacts and what are official relations? This cannot be clearer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1471820.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1471704.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-21","Geng Shuang","","With regard to the severing of the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" between Panama and Taiwan, Susan Thornton, acting assistant secretary of the US State Department's Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs, stated on June 20 local time that the United States follows closely the peace and stability across the Taiwan straits. It is very important for the two sides across the straits to have unimpeded channels for…","As for the statements made by the United states, just now you said that they are repetitive. Then I think I am allowed to repeat our position which has been stated earlier. Is it all right?\nWe strongly urge the United States to abide by the one China principle and the principles stipulated in the three Sino-US joint communiques and properly handle Taiwan-related issues. The one China principle constitutes the political basis for China-US relations. We hope that the United States can properly handle relevant issues on the basis of this principle.\nAs for the communication between the mainland and Taiwan, I would refer you to competent authorities since this is not a diplomatic question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1472219.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1472124.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-21","Geng Shuang","","Will the Taiwan-related issues be discussed in the upcoming China-US Diplomatic and Security Dialogue?","We have stated that the two sides will have an in-depth exchange of views on China-US relations and the international and regional hot-spots of mutual concern at the upcoming China-US Diplomatic and Security Dialogue. It is self-evident that what important issues are incorporated in the China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1472219.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1472124.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-22","Geng Shuang","","Panamanian President Juan Carlos Varela said, when giving an interview in Washington D.C. on June 21 that, he once told Taiwan that Panama would switch its stance once the \"diplomatic truce\" across the straits ended. Later on when learning about the end of \"diplomatic truce\", he made the right decision to establish diplomatic relations with China. Varela is the first to clearly state the \"diplomatic truce\" has…","You speak Spanish? Quite good pronunciation. (The journalist nodded and smiled.)\nThe one China principle concerns China's core interests and the feelings of the 1.3 billion Chinese people. Staying committed to the one China principle and developing friendly cooperative relations with other countries in the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence is the consistent position of the Chinese government. We will continue to uphold this position in developing friendly cooperative relations with other countries in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1472471.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1472449.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-26","Geng Shuang","","A flotilla with aircraft carrier Liaoning set out for a training mission yesterday. The aircraft carrier is expected to travel all the way south through the Taiwan Straits to Hong Kong for public display, as part of the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the return of Hong Kong. Can you tell us more about that?","I suggest that you ask the Chinese military for more about the aircraft carrier.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1473268.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1473208.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-27","Lu Kang","","Following the changing of the name of Taiwan's trade office in Dubai, its trade mission in Ecuador has recently changed its name from \"the Commercial Office of the Republic of China (Taiwan)\" to \"the Commercial Office of Taipei\". Taiwan said that China exerted pressure on several countries who are not Taiwan's allies to have the names of Taiwan's representative offices changed. How do you respond to that?","The Chinese government highly commends the Ecuadorian government for dealing with Taiwan-related issues in line with the one-China principle. What it proves once and again is that upholding the one-China principle has become a shared view and an irreversible trend of the international community. It has nothing to do with the Chinese government putting pressure on others.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1473592.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1473513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. I will host today's press conference and will now take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The mainland side keeps stressing the importance of the “1992 Consensus,” while there are various views on the “1992 Consensus” on the island. I would like the spokesperson to again explain the origin, specific meaning, and important significance of the “1992 Consensus.”","In November 1992, the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) on the mainland side and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation through the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams reached a consensus that each side would verbally express that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” The SEF's expression was: “In the process of working together to seek national unification across the Taiwan Strait, while both sides adhere to the one-China principle, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.” The Mainland's Association for Relations across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) expressed it as: “Both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive to seek national unification. However, in the consultations on cross-Strait affairs, the political meaning of one China is not involved.” Thus, both sides at that time expressed the position that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.”\nThe reason the “1992 Consensus” is important is that its core meaning is recognition that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, not “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations, showing that the two sides are not a state-to-state relationship. This is a matter of fundamental principle in the development of cross-Strait relations, and a major question of principle that the Taiwan authorities cannot evade.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170628_11809891.htm"],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","It is reported that the Taiwan authorities have recently taken measures to restrict mainland personnel from visiting Taiwan for exchanges, and have said that the mainland’s publicity about measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots is empty and untrue united front tactics. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","It is understood that some mainland delegations and personnel recently encountered obstacles in visiting Taiwan.\nFor many years, we have actively promoted personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, facilitated civilian exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, taken concrete measures, and continuously advanced economic and social integrated development across the Strait, to enhance the kinship and well-being of people on both sides. In recent times, relevant departments, adhering to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” have listened carefully to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan compatriots and successively introduced a series of policy measures. These create better learning environments for Taiwan compatriots in the mainland, create more job opportunities, and provide more convenience in daily life and social security, so that they can enjoy basically the same treatment as mainland residents. These policies are real and tangible, genuinely respond to the demands of Taiwan compatriots, and have therefore won broad recognition from Taiwan compatriots. In the future, we will continue, as always, to do practical and good things for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nIn contrast, the DPP authorities, since 5.20 last year, have not only unilaterally undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-strait relations, but also, on the island, tolerated and abetted “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and used various means to obstruct cross-strait exchange and cooperation and incite opposition in cross-strait public opinion. People cannot help but ask: over this past year, what good has the DPP authorities done for the people on both sides of the Strait? What practical things have they done for mainland compatriots in Taiwan? The answer is clearly: nothing.\nThis year marks the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-strait exchanges. The 30 years of history fully demonstrate that exchange, cooperation, and development are the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The doors that have been opened cannot be closed again. Any act that goes against the tide will ultimately only anger the people and lose their trust, and will be like lifting a rock only to drop it on one’s own foot.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Overseas Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople have repeatedly reported, and Taiwan media have also reported, that relevant Taiwan authorities groundlessly obstruct overseas Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople from participating in cross-Strait exchange activities, and personally attack and intimidate some leaders of Taiwan compatriot associations and overseas Taiwan business associations. What is…","Since 2008, against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, overseas compatriots from both sides have further strengthened exchanges, jointly promoted Chinese culture, and made efforts to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhance the overall interests of the Chinese nation. However, since “5.20” of last year, the DPP authorities have repeatedly used various means to restrict and suppress overseas Taiwan compatriots' participation in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This is yet another conclusive proof of their obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges. Their approach will only further lose the hearts of overseas compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170628_11809892.htm"],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","A draft of Taiwan's education curriculum guidelines was recently made public. It revises history instruction by discussing Chinese history within the context of East Asian history. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this?","The history of Taiwan is the history of the Chinese nation’s growth and reproduction, the history of Chinese culture spreading and flourishing, the history of generations of Chinese people developing and building the treasure island and jointly resisting foreign colonial rule, and it is naturally an organic component of Chinese history. The “Taiwan independence” forces have increasingly carried out “de-Sinicization” separatist activities in the fields of culture and education, attempting to use the “Taiwan independence” view of history to continue poisoning the younger generation in Taiwan and thereby wipe out the Chinese national consciousness of Taiwan compatriots. This has aroused strong indignation among the people of Taiwan. In the historical trend of national reunification and national rejuvenation, such reckless behavior is nothing more than a mantis trying to stop a chariot.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170628_11809890.htm"],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Relevant Taiwan authorities recently expressed condolences over the June 24 Maoxian landslide incident. How does the spokesperson respond?","We thank all sectors of Taiwan for their concern and sympathy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","This year marks the 20th anniversary of Hong Kong's return to China. A responsible official of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently made irresponsible comments about the implementation of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The practice of the 20 years since Hong Kong’s return fully proves that “one country, two systems” is not only the best solution to the historical issue of Hong Kong, but also the best institutional arrangement for maintaining Hong Kong’s long-term prosperity and stability after its return. We firmly oppose anyone interfering with the implementation of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong in any form, and undermining Hong Kong’s prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170628_11809888.htm"],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","I have two questions. First, regarding the return of Hong Kong: it is rumored that the “Liaoning” aircraft carrier formation will go to Hong Kong, and Taiwan may be rather worried whether the “Liaoning” will pass through the Taiwan Strait. Please verify this. Second, the National Intelligence Law was passed by the National People’s Congress some time ago, and Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council is worried that this…","On the first question, please direct your inquiry to the Ministry of National Defense. On the second question, the mainland administers in accordance with the law. While safeguarding national security, we will also protect the lawful rights and interests of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","According to reports in Taiwan media, the mainland side is about to launch a second-generation card-format Taiwan compatriot permit, with the permit number reportedly becoming 18 digits, consistent with the number of digits in the mainland resident identity card number. May I ask the spokesperson whether this policy is under consideration, and if so, when it is expected to be announced?","Thank you for your attention. As far as I understand, since the full implementation of the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit, the relevant authorities have issued more than 1.8 million of them to Taiwan compatriots. They have been well received by the broad base of Taiwan compatriots for their convenience in carrying and for the ease of entry and exit. However, a number of Taiwanese friends residing on the mainland have also told us that, even with the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit, they still encounter some inconveniences when using public service systems in various localities and industries. We attach great importance to this and are actively studying solutions.\nChina Politics and Economy Weekly / Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Weekly reporter: The pre-meeting notice of the Organizing Committee of the 9th Straits Forum said that guests and groups attending this forum would include members of Taiwan's Kuomintang (KMT)... wait","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS新闻记者","The Shanghai–Taipei “Twin City Forum” is about to take place. Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je, after the “four mutuals,” has now proposed mutual understanding, hoping that through exchanges among civil society, businesses and young people across the Strait, an opportunity can be found to ease cross-strait relations. What are the spokesperson’s comments?","On July 2, the “2017 Shanghai–Taipei City Forum” will be held in Shanghai. As I understand it, Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je will lead a delegation to Shanghai to attend the forum. We have repeatedly stated that as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, we maintain a positive and open attitude toward exchanges and interactions between cross-Strait cities. We also wish the Shanghai–Taipei “Twin City Forum” the expected results in deepening exchange and cooperation between the two cities in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Lin Chuan, head of Taiwan's Executive Yuan, recently said in an interview with Japanese media that if the One-China Principle means eliminating Taiwan, most people in Taiwan would not accept it. What is the spokesperson's comment?","This argument is logically muddled. Since 1949, although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and can never change. Before unification, in handling cross-Strait affairs, and especially in cross-Strait negotiations, adhering to the one-China principle means upholding that there is only one China in the world, that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are not to be divided. As for the long-standing political differences between the two sides, we have consistently held that they can be resolved through equal consultation on the basis of one China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170628_11809889.htm"],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Tainan Mayor Lai Ching-te, while visiting the United States, declared that a cross-Strait peace agreement does not help peace, stated that his “Taiwan independence” position has not changed, and pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and “pro-China” are not contradictory, and that Taiwan can still extend a hand of friendship. What is your comment?","If a peace agreement does not help peace, does insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position of “one country on each side” help peace? Clearly not. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Constantly claiming to be “pro-China,” does Taiwan then exclude itself from “China”? So, once again: only if the DPP abandons its “Taiwan independence” position can it truly find a way out in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","Two questions. First, Japan recently said it welcomes Taiwan joining the TPP. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second, some analysts point out that the Taiwan authorities may push the so-called “UN entry” issue at the UN General Assembly in September as one of their countermeasures to the “Taiwan-Ba diplomatic break.” What is the spokesperson’s response?","First question: Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on adherence to the one-China principle. Second question: The United Nations is composed of sovereign states and has long adhered to the one-China policy. Before 2008, Lee Teng-hui and Chen Shui-bian manipulated “UN entry” and “UN entry referendums,” and both met with failure; the lessons of history are fresh. Anyone who attempts to challenge UN General Assembly resolutions and the one-China policy upheld by the international community is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","A recent poll released on the island shows that public dissatisfaction with Tsai Ing-wen has reached 63%, hitting a new low. In response, Hu Wenqi, deputy director of the Culture and Communication Committee of the Kuomintang, said that the public has seen through the tricks Tsai Ing-wen has used during more than a year in office. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","We will not comment on matters within Taiwan. Today I would also like to stress two points: First, opposing “Taiwan independence” and supporting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations remains the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. Second, a healthy, stable, win-win cross-Strait relationship is crucial to Taiwan’s economic development and social stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Recently, eight US federal senators jointly wrote to US President Trump, demanding that he immediately submit the arms sale notification for Taiwan to Congress. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have consistently and firmly opposed any of our diplomatic partners developing military relations with Taiwan or selling weapons to Taiwan. This position is firm and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Cross-Strait relations have seen many twists and turns over the past year. May I ask the spokesperson whether the mainland's major policy guidelines and specific policies toward Taiwan have changed to date?","We have repeatedly emphasized that our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan have not changed. We will continue, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to unite the broad Taiwan compatriots and walk the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. On this issue, everyone should understand that after 5.20 last year, who undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, who has been doing everything possible to weaken the ties between compatriots on both sides in economic, social, and cultural terms, who is changing the status quo, and who is maintaining it? I think the answer is very clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","We noted that Panama announced on the 13th of this month that it would establish diplomatic relations with mainland China and sever all official relations with the Taiwan authorities. Meanwhile, Annette Lu recently told U.S. media that Taiwan's greatest mistake and tragedy was its past policy of “Han and bandits cannot coexist” (汉贼不两立). She also questioned why other countries must sever ties with Taiwan when they…","It seems that on questions of cross-Strait relations and national reunification, these DPP figures really need to brush up on their basic knowledge. The one-China principle is a policy widely upheld by the international community, and adhering to the one-China principle is also the general trend. Therefore, the DPP and the Taiwan authorities should recognize the objective trend and make a wise choice, particularly on the political foundation that matters for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, the Taiwan MAC said that the mainland's frequent criticism of Taiwan's side as “cultural Taiwan independence” deliberately creates cross-Strait opposition and does not help improve relations. What is the spokesperson's response?","Whoever overtly or covertly promotes “cultural Taiwan independence”—people are doing it, and heaven is watching. If you feel wronged, then openly declare your opposition to “Taiwan independence,” and openly stop those “de-Sinicization” acts that incite and stir up antagonism between the peoples on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-06-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Please have the spokesperson evaluate the development of Hong Kong-Taiwan relations over the past 20 years.","Over the twenty years since Hong Kong's return to China, the Hong Kong SAR Government, in accordance with the Basic Law and the central government's basic principles and policies on handling Hong Kong-related Taiwan affairs, has adopted policies and measures favorable to civil exchanges between Hong Kong and Taiwan. It has actively handled Taiwan-related affairs within its autonomy and, under the approval, guidance or authorization of the central government, properly handled matters in Hong Kong-Taiwan relations involving national sovereignty and cross-Strait relations, promoting civil exchanges and economic and trade relations between the two places. Maintaining Hong Kong's prosperity and stability and promoting the healthy development of Hong Kong-Taiwan relations is the shared wish of all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201706/t20170628_11809826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-06-29","Lu Kang","","There is a bill moving to the US Senate that would allow US Navy vessels to dock at Taiwan ports. What's your comment on that?","I believe you know fairly well China's position on the Taiwan question. We are strongly concerned about and firmly opposed to the bill approved by the Senate Armed Services Committee. We have lodged solemn representations with the US side about its erroneous actions on Taiwan-related issues. I have to stress once again that the Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and belongs to China's domestic affairs. Taiwan-related contents in the aforementioned bill severely violate the three joint communiqués between China and the US, and constitute interference in China's domestic affairs. China by no means accepts that. We urge the US to honor its commitment on the Taiwan question, immediately stop military contact and arms sale to Taiwan, and avoid causing damage to the bilateral relationship and bilateral cooperation in a broader range of areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474166.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474127.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-06-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","During its training mission, will the Liaoning aircraft carrier task group pass through the Taiwan Strait?","The training mission of the Liaoning aircraft carrier task group is a routine one within the annual training plan. Relevant information has been released by the PLA Navy recently and I have no more to add.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-06/30/content_4784138.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2017-06/29/content_4784102.htm",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-06-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. Senate Committee on Armed Services deliberated and passed its National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2018 on June 28th. One of its terms is quoted as saying that the U.S. would reestablish regular ports of call by the U.S. Navy at suitable ports in Taiwan and permit the U.S. Pacific Command to receive ports of call by Taiwan. What is your comment on that?","We are always firmly opposed to any form of official contact and military interaction between Taiwan and the U.S. We urge the American side to abide by its commitment to the Chinese side with regard to the Taiwan question, and stop military contacts with Taiwan, so as not to cause damage to the relations between the two militaries and the two countries as well as to the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-06/30/content_4784138.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2017-06/29/content_4784102.htm",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-06-30","Lu Kang","N/A — opening announcement (no press Q)","","At the invitation of President Donald Tusk of the European Council, President Jean-Claude Juncker of the European Commission, and President Antonio Tajani of the European Parliament, Vice-chairman of the CPPCC National Committee and Minister of Science and Technology Wan Gang will attend the funeral held by the EU for former German Chancellor Helmut Kohl in Strasbourg, France on July 1, as the special envoy of President Xi Jinping.\nMr. Kohl was an eminent statesman. President Xi Jinping said, in his message of condolences to German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier on the passing of Mr. Kohl, that Mr. Kohl had devoted himself to promoting China-Germany and China-EU dialogue and cooperation. He had made positive contribution to the development of China-Germany relations and had been understanding and supportive of the Chinese people's endeavor for complete national reunification. The Chinese people will never forget this old friend of them.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474637.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-30","Lu Kang","","The US has approved US$ 1.4 billion worth of arms sales to Taiwan, but has also emphasized that there is no change to its longstanding \"one China\" policy. What is China's comment on that?","On June 30, the US government announced to sell US$ 1.4 billion worth of arms to Taiwan. The Chinese side lodged representations with the US side both in Beijing and in Washington.\nThe Chinese side pointed out that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. By selling arms to Taiwan, the US has severely violated international law, basic norms governing international relations and the three China-US joint communiqués, and jeopardized China's sovereignty and security interests. The Chinese side firmly opposes that.\nThe Chinese side stressed that the Chinese government and people will never waver in their will and determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and fend against external interference. We strongly urge the US side to honor its solemn commitments in the three China-US joint communiqués, cancel its arms sales plan, and stop its military contact with Taiwan, so as not to cause further damage to China-US relations and bilateral cooperation in major areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474637.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-30","Lu Kang","","Over the last few days, China-US relationship has gone from being quite positive since the meeting at Mar-a-lago to having more and more uncertainties because of the arms sales to Taiwan and the sanctions on Chinese companies due to the Korean nuclear issue. Next week, President Xi Jinping and President Donald Trump are going to meet at the G20 Hamburg Summit. Do you believe that we are in a new period of turmoil…","Consensus reached by leaders of China and the US at their Mar-a-lago meeting reflects the common interests of the two sides, and points in the right direction of China-US relations. On our part, we definitely hope to keep the momentum going and even build it up, however, as you have said, erroneous actions by the US over the recent period of time, its proposed arms sales to Taiwan in particular, run counter to the important consensus at the Mar-a-lago meeting, the overall trend of the China-US relationship, and the interests of the US itself.\nAs I just said when answering the question about US arms sales, we hope that the US will correct mistakes, bring the bilateral relationship back to the track of sound, steady and sustained growth, and avoid negatively affecting bilateral cooperation in major areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474637.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-30","Lu Kang","","You said that you hope the US side will change its course to avoid negatively affecting other areas of cooperation. Is the Chinese side contemplating any specific retaliatory measures and what specific areas could be negatively affected?","We have been stressing that a sound and steady China-US relationship serves the interests of both sides. Wrong actions taken by the US on the Taiwan question which bears on China's core interests go against the consensus reached by leaders of the two countries at Mar-a-lago. On an issue as important as this, wrong actions by the US will affect bilateral cooperation in major areas. We have lodged representations with the US about that in both Beijing and Washington, asking them to correct their mistakes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474637.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-06-30","Lu Kang","","Did China protest both about the arms sales and about sanctions on China?","By \"sanctions on China\", are you referring to the \"long-arm jurisdiction\" exercised by the US? (Journalist nodded) We have lodged solemn representations with the US about its wrong actions including the arms sales to Taiwan and the \"long-arm jurisdiction\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1474637.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-06-30","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On June 29, the US government notified Congress of its decision to sell weapons and equipment to Taiwan worth a total of about 1.4 billion US dollars. The Chinese Ministry of National Defense expresses firm opposition and strong dissatisfaction.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, involves China's core interests, and is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-US relations. China firmly opposes any foreign government selling weapons to Taiwan. The US side's conduct seriously violates the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the principles of the “August 17” Communiqué, blatantly interferes in China's internal affairs, damages China's sovereignty and security interests, and harms the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe position of the Chinese military on safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and clear. We strongly urge the US side to abide by the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, revoke the relevant arms sales projects to Taiwan, and stop selling weapons to Taiwan and military contacts between the US and Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to China-US military relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2017-06/30/content_4784266.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2017-06-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter's question: the US Senate Armed Services Committee recently approved a resolution allowing warships to regularly dock at Taiwan's ports, and the US State Department approved the first arms sale to Taiwan since Trump took office. What comment do you have?","XINHUA, Beijing, June 30 (Reporter Liu Huan)\nTAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on June 30 in response to questions: The Foreign Ministry and the Ministry of National Defense have already stated our solemn position on this. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between Taiwan and the United States, and firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan on any pretext. Any act that relies on foreign powers to strengthen oneself and undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait will surely reap its own bitter fruit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201706/t20170630_11811306.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-07-03","Geng Shuang","","In recent days, the US has taken a series of moves including arms sales to Taiwan, sanctions on Chinese individuals and entities and the US warship's entry into China's territorial waters off the Xisha Islands. We know that President Xi Jinping spoke to President Trump this morning, could you tell us whether President Xi made China's position on some of the issues clear to President Trump?","This morning, President Xi Jinping had a telephone conversation with President Donald Trump as agreed. The Chinese side has issued a press release on this and you can refer to it on the website of the Foreign Ministry.\nDuring this conversation, the two sides have exchanged views on China-US relations, the upcoming G20 Summit in Hamburg and some other issues. President Xi pointed out that recently, the bilateral relations, while having achieved important progress, are also affected by some negative factors. The Chinese side has explicitly stated its positions to the United States. The two sides should stay committed to the general direction of the growth of China-US relations, uphold the principles of mutual respect and mutual benefit, focus on cooperation and properly handle and manage differences so as to promote the solid progress of China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1475054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474965.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-03","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that China's aircraft carrier Liaoning entered Taiwan's Air Defense Identification Zone (ADIZ) on Saturday afternoon. Taiwan's military said it would continuously monitor the movements of Liaoning and launch responsive measures. Separately, reports from Japan say that a PLA naval ship entered Japanese territorial waters through the Tsugaru strait of Hokkaido yesterday, and the Japanese side has…","On your first question about the aircraft carrier Liaoning, the spokesperson of the Chinese Navy Liang Yang introduced relevant information on July 2. As approved by the Central Military Commission, the Chinese naval formation including aircraft carrier Liaoning, which is performing cross maneuver training tasks, will visit Hong Kong SAR in early July in celebration of the 20th anniversary of the People's Liberation Army (PLA) being stationed in HKSAR. As for what the Taiwanese side said about it, this is not a diplomatic question, thus should be referred to competent authorities.\nOn your second question, I am not aware of what you said about Chinese naval ship entering Japan's territorial waters. I will refer you to the military if you are interested. I do like to emphasize that China's naval vessels operate in relevant waters in accordance with international law.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1475054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1474965.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-07-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 12 (Reporter Zha Wenye): In response to the matter that, regarding the new high school social studies curriculum guidelines the Taiwan authorities are about to roll out no longer mentioning the Cairo Declaration, and relevant official websites having removed the related content, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 12th by saying that any scheme attempting to change the status of Taiwan as part of China is doomed to fail.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the Cairo Declaration is an important international document of the world anti-fascist war. The Cairo Declaration clearly stipulates that Japan shall return to China territories it stole from China, such as Manchuria, Taiwan, and the Penghu Islands. The Potsdam Proclamation, signed by the United States, the United Kingdom and China, and later joined by the Soviet Union, clearly declares: \"The terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.\" This became the basis in international law for Japan's surrender and for China's recovery of lost territories such as Taiwan and the Penghu Islands.\nMa Xiaoguang emphasized that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, which has indisputable historical fact and legal basis, and is also widely recognized by the international community. Any scheme attempting to change the status of Taiwan as part of China is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201707/t20170712_11817717.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-07-13","Geng Shuang","","I have an historical question relating to the Cairo Declaration jointly issued by China, the US and the UK in 1943. This Declaration is not going to be included in the curriculum guidelines for social studies of senior high schools in Taiwan in the future. There is a view that this is an attempt by the Taiwanese side to advance the so-called \"uncertain status of Taiwan\" theory. Does the mainland think the Cairo…","It is true that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has made remarks on this. But since you have asked about the legal status of the Cairo Declaration, I will reply to your question.\nTaiwan is an indispensable part of China's territory, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity brook no division. The Cairo Declaration has set crucial international legal basis for China to regain Taiwan and its affiliated islands seized and stolen by the Japanese militarism after World War II. It is an important document universally recognized as part of international law and a major outcome of the world anti-fascist war, which laid down the key foundation of after-war international order for the international community and is of far-reaching historical significance and highly relevant.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1477718.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1477627.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-14","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday Tsai Ing-wen tweeted that she was honored to receive Paraguayan President Horacio Cartes on his so-called \"state visit\" to Taiwan and the two sides inked new agreements on economic cooperation and visa-free travel for tourists. How do you comment on that?","The one china principle is the general consensus among the international community. Any attempts to create \"two China\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\" will certainly meet firm opposition of all Chinese people, and it is not in line with the fundamental interests of the Taiwanese people.\nWe hope the Taiwan authorities can make a correct assessment of the situation and return to the 1992 consensus as soon as possible, and do no more things that are against the trend of the times and the will of the people.\nWe would also like to advise certain people in Taiwan to open their eyes to see the world, place themselves in a right position, stop being a frog in a well and deceiving themselves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1477975.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1477885.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-17","Lu Kang","","On July 14, the House of Representatives of the US Congress passed the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2018 which asks the US Defense Secretary to look into the feasibility of reestablishing port calls between the US and Taiwanese navies. What is your comment?","The National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2018 passed by the House of Representatives of the US Congress includes some negative contents, directing the Pentagon to submit a report to the Congress on the feasibility of reestablishing port calls between the US and Taiwanese navies. Relevant contents go against the one China policy of the US and the principles of the three joint communiques between China and the US and interfere in China's domestic affairs. China has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nI must reiterate that it is China's consistent position to firmly oppose any official contacts and military exchanges between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US to fully recognize the gravity of the relevant clauses in the Act. The US should not allow the Act with the relevant clauses to become law, nor turn back the wheel of history lest it should harm the general interests of China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1478246.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1478201.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-20","Lu Kang","","With regard to the China-US Comprehensive Economic Dialogue yesterday held in Washington, how will this Dialogue affect bilateral relations? Will recent diplomatic cases, like the US arms sale to Taiwan, its maneuvers in the South China Sea, and sanctions on Chinese companies and individuals because of the Iranian nuclear issue, impede bilateral economic and trade cooperation?","As I said yesterday, in accordance with the consensus reached between the two leaders, on July 19, the first round of China-US Comprehensive Economic Dialogue was held in Washington, the US, co-chaired by Vice Premier Wang Yang of the State Council and US Treasury Secretary Steven T. Mnuchin and Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross. China and the US have released relevant information, including detailed account of their dialogues. You can refer to that.\nThe two sides held in-depth discussions on China-US trade and investment, the 100-Day Plan and One-Year Plan for economic cooperation, global economy and governance, macro-economic policy and finance, and agriculture. Extensive consensus was reached. The two sides also agreed to cooperate constructively on narrowing trade deficits.\nThe two sides agree that this round of dialogue was innovative, pragmatic and constructive, the most important achievement being setting a right direction for China-US economic cooperation. That is the two sides should uphold win-win cooperation as a basic principle for developing bilateral business ties, take dialogue and consultation as basic methods to resolve differences, and sustain communication on major economic policies as a fundamental way of carrying out cooperative dialogues, which laid a solid foundation for future cooperation.\nI said that the US Treasury Department also released relevant information. Treasury Secretary Mnuchin and Commerce Secretary Ross spoke highly of the positive progress achieved by bilateral economic cooperation in some important areas since the Mar-a-lago meeting, especially since the announcement of the 100-Day Plan. They expressed that the US stands ready to work with China to implement the important consensus reached between the two leaders.\nAs for your second question, in response to these issues besetting China-US relations as a result of the erroneous steps the US has taken on issues concerning China's core interests, whether it is the Taiwan-related issue, or the \"long-arm jurisdiction\" imposed on Chinese enterprises, or maritime issues, we have made our positions clear. I sense that your logic is that the development of China-US relations depends on the two sides working together towards the same direction. A China-US relationship that grows in a sound and steady way serves the common interests of the two sides. All the wrong moves taken by the US on relevant issues, as you enumerated in your question, are not conducive to sustaining a favorable environment for China and the US to carry out mutually beneficial cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1479101.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1479037.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-20","Lu Kang","","According to reports, the Cambodian government has detained more than 30 telecom fraud suspects, of which 7 are apparently from Taiwan. I was wondering if you can confirm that and say China has requested those suspects be sent to the mainland? Secondly, there are reports that Egyptian officials have imprisoned several dozens of Chinese. Can you give more details?","On your first question, we support the Cambodian government in carrying out law enforcement activities in accordance with its domestic laws.\nOn your second question, as my colleague has said, we are following the development of the relevant situation. Consular officials from the Chinese Embassy in Egypt have paid consular visits. We consistently ask Chinese citizens overseas to abide by the laws, regulations and rules of the countries they reside in and not to engage in activities that do not suit their residence status.\nAs announced last week, the promotion event for Inner Mongolia will be held here tomorrow at 3:30 pm themed Open China: Magnificent Inner Mongolia Inviting Friends around the Globe. Foreign Minister Wang Yi will address the event. The Party Secretary of the Inner Mongolian Autonomous Region Li Jiheng and chairperson Bu Xiaolin will respectively deliver speeches and presentations. Foreign diplomatic envoys and representatives will also be invited to make remarks and interact with other guests.\nWe look forward to your participation in and coverage of this event.\nThe regular press conference of the Foreign Ministry will be adjourned tomorrow. The Office of the Foreign Ministry Spokesperson's Office will take phone calls and faxes as usual.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1479101.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1479037.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-07-20","MND Information Bureau (国防部新闻局; no named spokesperson)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","Question: According to a report in Taiwan's “China Times,” during the passage of the Liaoning carrier group through the Taiwan Strait, a US Navy destroyer also entered the Taiwan Strait and tracked the Chinese formation throughout. Please confirm.\nOffice of the News Bureau, Ministry of National Defense: We noted the relevant report. The Chinese military maintains full monitoring and effective handling of the situation in the relevant waters.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2017-07/20/content_4786290.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2017-07-27","Lu Kang","","The Cambodian government has deported to China Chinese nationals who are suspected of involvement in telecoms fraud cases. Taiwan said that some people are from Taiwan and should be sent back to Taiwan instead of the mainland. What is your response to this?","China highly commends Cambodia's cooperation with China to crack down on cross-border crimes including telecoms scams. China and Cambodia have been in close communication and cooperation in this field. As for Taiwan's response, it is not a diplomatic issue. I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs' Office of the State Council for the mainland's response.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1480581.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1480533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-27","Lu Kang","","On July 26, Foxconn Chairman Terry Guo announced that he will invest $10 billion to open a new plant in the US. How does China view this investment? Considering that Foxconn hires almost 1 million people in China, do you worry this may cause an erosion in China's employment opportunities?","At the Foreign Ministry's press briefing, we could not give specific comments on each and every commercial behavior.\nAs for Taiwan's investment in the mainland, it is also outside the remit of the Foreign Ministry. I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs' Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1480581.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1480533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-07-27","Lu Kang","","The latest edition of Indian Today carried a Chinese map on its cover which does not include Taiwan and Xizang. What is your response?","Do you really think this kind of tricks is worth your time and attention?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1480581.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1480533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-07-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Guo Taiming, Chairman of the Foxconn Group, announced at the White House that it will invest 10 billion US dollars to build a factory in Wisconsin. How does the mainland view this investment? Foxconn employs about 1 million workers in the mainland. Is the mainland concerned that Foxconn’s response to “Made in America” will affect job opportunities for mainland employees?","We have noted the relevant reports.\nAccording to our understanding, the Foxconn Group has continued to expand its investment in the mainland this year, and its existing enterprises have not been affected.\nTaiwanese businesses generally believe that the mainland's economic development has a long-term positive outlook and that the prospects for Taiwan-invested enterprises are broad. At the same time, our position of supporting Taiwan-invested enterprises' roots and development on the mainland has been consistent and clear, and we will continue to take positive measures to create a favorable environment for the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201707/t20170727_11824732.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-08-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 9 (reporter Zha Wenye): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 9th that after the strong earthquake in Jiuzhaigou County, Aba Tibetan and Qiang Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan Province, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) activated emergency mechanisms overnight and contacted the Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office to verify whether any Taiwan compatriots had been killed, injured or trapped. The Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office quickly made arrangements for this work and implemented them. As of now, there have been no reports of Taiwan compatriots being killed, injured or trapped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201708/t20170809_11828669.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-08-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on August 9 that after the strong earthquake in Jiuzhaigou County, Aba Tibetan and Qiang Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan Province, all sectors of Taiwan expressed concern and sympathy in various forms. The Central Committee of the Kuomintang of China sent a telegram expressing sympathy, hoping that the people in the disaster area will overcome their difficulties and complete post-disaster reconstruction as soon as possible. Some Taiwan-invested enterprises actively donated money and donated food and supplies to the disaster area to support local disaster relief work. We express our thanks for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201708/t20170809_11828769.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-08-15","Hua Chunying","","In a jointly signed article on the Wall Street Journal, the US Secretary of State Rex Tillerson and Secretary of Defense Jim Mattis said that, diplomacy is their preferred means of changing the DPRK's course of action. The object of their peaceful pressure campaign is the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula. The U.S. has no interest in regime change or accelerated reunification of Korea. They do not seek an…","We have noted the relevant report and Secretary of State Rex Tillerson and Secretary of Defense Jim Mattis's positive remarks on commitment to diplomatic settlement of the Korean Peninsula issue. We hope the US side can translate the relevant positive remarks into its DPRK-related policy, and also call upon the DPRK to respond to the positive signal sent by the US.\nChina's position on the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue remains consistent and clear-cut. We have always stayed committed to denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula, upholding peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula and solving the issue through dialogue and negotiation,for which we have made enormous efforts for a long time. We have always maintained that security issue is the core of the Korean Peninsula issue, and the DPRK and the US hold the key to the solution. We hope that the relevant parties can take seriously the Chinese-initiated \"suspension for suspension\" proposal, accommodate each other's reasonable security concerns and find a breakthrough for peaceful solution of the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue through talks. China will continue to implement the relevant UN Security Council resolutions comprehensively and faithfully, and as usual play a positive and constructive role in promoting the peaceful settlement of the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue through diplomatic means. We also hope other relevant parties can join our efforts for the shared goal.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1484923.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1484830.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-08-16","Hua Chunying","","Did the two sides discuss the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue? Did Joseph Dunford meet with other leaders?","Also, Chief of the CMC Joint Staff Department Fang Fenghui and Joseph Dunford exchanged views on the issues of mutual concern, including the Taiwan issue, the South China Sea issue, and the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue. They also jointly signed the Framework Document of the Dialogue Mechanism of the Joint Staff Departments Between the Chinese and the US Militaries. As to the other meetings during Joseph Dunford's visit, I will refer you to the Ministry of National Defense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1485231.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1485207.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-08-18","Hua Chunying","","On August 17, a van rammed into crowds of pedestrians at Placa Catalunya in the downtown of Barcelona, killing at least 13and injuring more than 100. Spanish Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy Brey called the van rampage an \"terrorist attack\". How do you respond to that? Has any Chinese citizen been injured?","The Chinese side strongly condemns the terrorist attack that happened in Barcelona, Spain,deeply mourns the victims and expresses sincere condolences to the injured and the bereaved families. President Xi Jinping and Premier Li Keqiang have sent a message of condolences to King Felipe VI of Spain and Spanish Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy Brey respectively.\nAfter the attack happened, China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Chinese Embassy in Spain and the Chinese Consulate General in Barcelona have immediately launched the emergency mechanism, issued an security alert and closely followed the development of the situation. According to our information, by far, two Taiwanese compatriots were severely hurt and sent to hospital for urgent treatment. One Hong Kong compatriot was slightly injured and has been discharged from hospital. There is no other report of casualties of Chinese nationals. The Chinese Consulate General in Barcelona has sent officials to visit the Taiwanese compatriots who are treated for heavy injuries. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Chinese Consulate General in Barcelona will continue to closely follow the evolution of the situation and offer necessary assistance to those injured.\nI would like to reiterate that China firmly opposes all forms of terrorism, steadfastly supports Spain in fighting terrorism and upholding national security and stability, and stands ready to reinforce counter-terrorist efforts with Spain and other members of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1485818.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1485770.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-08-18","Hua Chunying","","17日，一辆厢式货车在巴塞罗那市中心加泰罗尼亚广场附近冲撞行人，造成至少13人死亡，100余人受伤。西班牙首相拉霍伊称事件是恐怖袭击事件。中方对此有何评论？是否有中国公民在事件中伤亡？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1485818.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1485770.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2017-08-20","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 20: The Chinese Kuomintang held its 20th National Congress on the 20th and adopted a new policy platform. In response to a question about the content on cross-Strait relations in the new policy platform, TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said the same day that in 2005 the KMT and the CPC reached five common visions for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, establishing the common political foundation that both sides uphold the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence.” On this basis, the two parties strengthened exchanges and interaction, advanced peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and achieved fruitful results.\nAn Fengshan said that at present, the situation in cross-Strait relations is complex and grave. We are willing to maintain communication and strengthen dialogue with the KMT on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and opposing “Taiwan independence,” so as to jointly maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201708/t20170820_11832987.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-08-21","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 21 (reporter Zhao Bo) — TAO spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions on the 21st, said that the New Party, since its founding 24 years ago, has consistently advocated peaceful reunification of the two sides, firmly upheld one China, and opposed “Taiwan independence,” which we highly appreciate.\nOn August 20, the New Party held a celebration for its 24th anniversary and put forward a new line and new discourse for the New Party. New Party Chairman Yu Muming stated, “We must press forward toward peaceful reunification and the revitalization of China.”\nAn Fengshan pointed out that we are willing to maintain communication and strengthen dialogue with all Taiwan political parties, groups, organizations and individuals that uphold the one-China principle, support the reunification of the motherland and oppose “Taiwan independence,” including the New Party, to jointly advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and jointly pursue the peaceful reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201708/t20170821_11833421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-08-22","Hua Chunying","","The so-called \"Defense Minister\" of Taiwan is going to Central America but will stop in New York and Los Angeles. Has China required the US not to engage in any kind of official meeting during those stopovers?","I have noted the relevant report. The Chinese side is always handling the foreign exchanges of Taiwan in accordance with the one China principle and we firmly oppose the countries that have established diplomatic relations with China to conduct any form of official contact or have any form of military relationship with Taiwan. Our position in this respect is clear-cut and consistent and we believe the US is quite clear about this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1486601.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1486512.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-08-31","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Since May 20, 2016, times for the PLA aircraft’s circling Taiwan have been constantly increasing. Especially in mid August this year, there were three times of such kind of military maneuvers within one week. Thus, some media in Taiwan said that the Mainland China is preparing to attack the Taiwan island, and others called on the Mainland China to exercise restraint and calm. Would you please brief us on this?…","On your first question, as for the Chinese military aircraft’s training exercises you have mentioned, we have learned that such operations are routine training conducted by the PLA Air Force.\nOn your second question, China’s policy and position on the Korean Peninsula is consistent and clear, and there is no need for me to repeat here. However, I’d like to stress that along the China-DPRK border, the Chinese frontier defense troops are maintaining normal status of combat readiness and they are conducting normal training.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-08/31/content_4790489.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-09-11","Geng Shuang","N/A — opening announcement (no press Q)","","The 72nd session of the United Nations (UN) General Assembly will open at the UN headquarters in New York on September 12 and the General Debate will kick off on September 19. Foreign Minister Wang Yi will head a delegation to attend the General Debate, during which he will give a full account of China's stances and propositions on the current international landscape and major international and regional issues and demonstrate China's firm resolve to stand ready to work with the other UN member states to uphold world peace and stability and promote development and prosperity.\nPrior to attending the General Debate, at the invitation of Minister of Foreign Affairs Manuel González Sanz of Costa Rica and Vice President and Minister of Foreign Affairs Isabel de Saint Malo de Alvarado of Panama, Foreign Minister Wang Yi will pay official visits to Costa Rica and Panama from September 14 to 17. The Chinese side will exchange views with both countries on bilateral relations and issues of common interest.\nDuring his visit to Costa Rica, Foreign Minister Wang Yi will meet with President Luis Guillermo Solís Rivera and hold talks with Foreign Minister Manuel González Sanz. Over the past decade since the establishment of China-Costa Rica diplomatic ties, the bilateral relations have achieved rapid growth. The two countries have established the strategic partnership of equality, mutual trust and win-win cooperation, formulated the Joint Action Plan on China-Costa Rica Cooperation (2016-2020) and witnessed the steady deepening of exchanges and cooperation across the board. We are convinced that with the concerted efforts of the two sides, China-Costa Rica relations will continue flourishing and accomplishing greater new development.\nDuring his visit to Panama, Foreign Minister Wang Yi will meet with President Juan Carlos Varela and co-chair the first political consultation between the foreign ministries of the two countries with Vice President and Foreign Minister Isabel de Saint Malo de Alvarado. The two sides will hold the unveiling ceremony for the Chinese Embassy in Panama. Panama is an important country in Latin America and the friendship between the people of China and Panama dates back to a long time ago. In recent years, the relations between China and Latin American and Caribbean countries have witnessed great development and the exchanges and cooperation between China and Panama have also been on the increase. In June this year, the government of Panama, by accepting and pledging to adhere to the One China principle, severed the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan and established the diplomatic ties with the People's Republic of China. This is in compliance with the trend of the times and the aspirations of the people and opens a new historic chapter in China-Panama relations. The Chinese side stands ready to closely join hands with Panama to make the bilateral relations get off to a fast start and achieve steady and long-term development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1491953.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1491867.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Ladies and gentlemen of the press, good morning. After a long summer break, I am very pleased to see you again here. Welcome to all of you attending this morning's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I am now glad to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","Could the spokesperson briefly introduce the relevant situation of this summer's cross-strait exchange activities?","This summer, cross-Strait exchange activities have had many highlights: cultural, sports and educational exchanges have been colorful, and grassroots exchanges have been broad and deep. In addition to the brand exchange activities in various fields and sectors that have been held for many years, some new exchange activities have also had a positive impact. There are two major highlights. First, cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges have yielded rich results. Taiwan business and industry circles and Taiwan-funded enterprises have signed multiple investment and economic cooperation agreements with relevant local authorities, demonstrating Taiwan businesspeople’s expectations and confidence in the prospects of mainland development and investment opportunities. Second, in cross-Strait youth exchanges, the forms and content of experiential and interactive activities have become more diverse, guidance activities for cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment have been rich and varied, and Taiwan youth have been enthusiastic about internships on the mainland. According to incomplete statistics, more than 4,000 Taiwan student youths interned at enterprises and public institutions across the mainland this summer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842527.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","新华社记者","The Lee Ming-che case was heard on September 11 in Yueyang, Hunan, attracting attention on the island. I would like to ask the spokesperson for comments on this matter.","On September 11, the Yueyang Intermediate People’s Court publicly opened a hearing in accordance with the law in the case of Peng Yuhua, a mainland resident, and Lee Ming-che, a Taiwan resident, for subversion of state power. Throughout the investigation and trial of this case, the mainland authorities handling the case strictly followed the law and legal procedures, and the litigation rights of the defendants and their families were fully protected and guaranteed. The mainland authorities handling the case notified the defendants’ families in accordance with the law to attend the trial as observers. After the trial, at the request of the defendants’ families, the court arranged for Lee Ming-che to meet with his mother and wife. The Yueyang Intermediate People’s Court broadcast the relevant trial proceedings in full, through video and text and images, on Sina Weibo, and mainland media, including Xinhua News Agency, reported on the trial after it concluded. Some Taiwanese media also reported on the trial throughout.\nThe first-instance judgment in this case has been concluded, and the court will announce the verdict at a date to be chosen later. It must be stressed that the mainland is a society governed by law. Anyone in the mainland must abide by legal provisions and social public order, and anyone who violates the law will be held accountable under the law. Any attempt to use this case for political manipulation, to influence or defame the mainland’s handling of the case in accordance with the law, or to attack the mainland’s political and legal system is futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842529.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","中新社记者","This year marks 30 years since the opening of cross-Strait exchanges. What is the spokesperson's assessment of cross-Strait exchanges over the past 30 years, and what commemorative activities does the mainland have planned?","As early as 1979, the mainland took the lead in advocating the opening of cross-Strait exchanges. The Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress issued the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan,” calling for the early implementation of postal and direct transport links, direct contact among compatriots, visiting relatives and friends, and sightseeing and exchanges. Through the unremitting efforts of compatriots on both sides, by 1987 the long-standing isolation between the two sides had been broken, and the door to cross-Strait exchanges and travel was opened. Over the past 30 years, cross-Strait exchanges have grown from nothing to something, from few to many, from indirect to direct, and from one-way to two-way, continuously expanding and deepening into a comprehensive, multi-level pattern. Cross-Strait personnel exchanges and economic, cultural, and social ties have reached an unprecedented level, laying a profound foundation for and providing strong impetus to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe achievements of 30 years of cross-Strait exchanges have been hard-won. They embody the heartfelt efforts and sacrifice of countless compatriots on both sides and need to be jointly cherished and safeguarded by compatriots on both sides. Since May of last year, despite complex changes in the situation on Taiwan and in cross-Strait relations, we have continued to advance exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, continuously deepened economic and social integrated development across the Strait, and promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn the occasion of the 30th anniversary of the start of cross-Strait exchanges, localities and departments are holding commemorative activities in various forms. On September 5, Hong Kong held the “Cross-Strait Exchanges 30th Anniversary Commemorative Conference.” On September 20, the “Cross-Strait Kinship, One Family” theme evening and the 2017 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival, aimed at reviewing 30 years of Jiangsu-Taiwan exchange and cooperation, will be held in Kunshan, Jiangsu. It is understood that academic institutions in Beijing and Shanghai will also hold commemorative seminars in October on the theme of 30 years of cross-Strait exchanges and relations. We believe that the trend of cross-Strait exchanges continuing to move forward is something no force can stop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842532.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","What is the mainland's view of Lai Ching-te leading Taiwan's new administrative team? Lai Ching-te previously said he supports “Taiwan independence,” but he has also said “pro-China, love Taiwan.” The Mainland Affairs Council said that Lai Ching-te's taking office will not affect Taiwan's cross-Strait policy. What are your expectations for Taiwan's new administrative team? A further question: at the APEC Economic…","On your first question, Director Zhang Zhijun already stated our position on this matter during the Beijing-Taipei Science and Technology Forum on September 8. Regardless of how personnel changes in the Taiwan authorities turn out, what we value and watch is their mainland policy. In terms of cross-Strait relations, the most important question the Democratic Progressive Party authorities need to answer is: what is the nature of cross-Strait relations? Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development.\nOn your second question, regarding Taiwan’s participation in APEC activities, it should be handled in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions of the APEC memorandum of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","It is reported that the 2017 “The Voice of China” will hold related activities in Taipei. I would like the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation. Second question: The latest public opinion poll in Taiwan shows that more than 70% of the public believe the mainland’s importance to Taiwan’s development is continuously increasing, and 73% of the public support the Taiwan authorities adjusting their…","On your first question, as we understand it, the 2017 \"China New Voice Shanghai-Taipei Music Festival\" will be held on September 24 at the athletics field of National Taiwan University. Young singers from both sides of the Strait will perform together on the same stage, and young people across the Strait will once again come together in the name of music to share the joy brought by musical dreams. We welcome young people from both sides of the Strait to participate in and follow this event.\nOn your second question, we do not comment on specific polls on the island. We have repeatedly stated that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to promote peace across the Strait, advance development across the Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides, that it conforms to the common interests of compatriots on both sides, and that maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is also the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. Since last year, compatriots on both sides have seen very clearly the causes of, and responsibility for, the tension in cross-Strait relations and the damage to the interests of compatriots on both sides. If the Taiwan authorities truly keep the well-being of the Taiwan public in mind, they should actively respond to the needs of the public, return to the common basis of the \"1992 Consensus,\" and only then can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development, and compatriots on both sides will be able to share the benefits together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently issued a press release stating that the Lee Ming-che case concerns the human rights image of the mainland and will also affect cross-Strait development. It therefore calls on the mainland to handle the case after the trial in a manner consistent with universal human rights values. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Regarding the Li Mingzhe case, I already gave a basic explanation when answering the earlier question from a reporter. I need to stress again that the mainland is a society governed by the rule of law. Anyone on the mainland must abide by the mainland's laws and regulations and public social order, and if someone violates the law, they will be held accountable under the law. We also clearly emphasize that anyone who attempts to use this case for political manipulation or to attack the mainland's political and legal system will be wasting their effort.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","中央电视台记者","Over the recent period, we have seen that, under the unanimous opposition of all sectors in Taiwan, Taiwan's education authorities have not been able to lower the proportion of classical Chinese in Taiwan's senior high school Chinese textbooks as originally planned. May I ask for your comments on this?","For some time, a force in Taiwan has been persistently manipulating issues such as the curriculum guidelines and textbooks, which has met strong opposition from all sectors of Taiwan society. We have repeatedly stated that Chinese culture is the common spiritual home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and is the common root and soul of us across the Strait.\nI remember that when we were small, our parents and teachers taught us to memorize 300 Tang poems, because “a person with books in their belly has a radiant bearing.” Why do we study classical Chinese? As a passage online puts it, when we see a beautiful scene before us, we can exclaim, “The sunset glow and a lone duck fly together; autumn waters merge with the vast sky in one color,” rather than only saying, “Wow, how beautiful.” When we want to express our personal aspirations, we can say, “Worry before the world worries; rejoice only after the world rejoices,” rather than thinking only about climbing the ranks and getting rich. When we encounter entanglements in love, we can sigh, “If life were only like the first meeting, why would autumn wind sadden the painted fan? Lightly changing an old friend's heart, yet claiming the old friend's heart changes easily,” rather than only saying, “Lan shou xiang gu (‘blue-thin mushrooms’).” So I think these outstanding traditional Chinese cultures, after thousands of years of quiet influence, have been internalized as part of the humanistic spirit and temperament of every Chinese person, becoming part of the genes of every one of us Chinese. Looking back at the recent controversy on the island over the proportion of classical Chinese in high school Chinese-language courses, most public opinion on the island holds that this is not simply a “classical versus vernacular” dispute, but another “de-Sinicization” move in the cultural and educational fields by certain forces on the island. Therefore, I must emphasize once again that carrying out “de-Sinicization” in education and culture, attempting to sever Taiwan's blood ties with Chinese culture, will only harm Taiwan society and poison the younger generation of Taiwan. Doing so is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842528.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","台湾《旺报》记者","Taiwan's security authorities recently released a report on mainland military strength, proposing that there are seven possible scenarios for the mainland to use force against Taiwan. How does the spokesperson evaluate this report? I would also like to ask about retired Taiwan general Hsu Li-nung (许历农), who announced on September 3 that he would no longer be “anti-communist” and should not oppose for the sake of…","On your first question: peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee for maintaining peace and stability across the Strait, while “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities are the greatest obstacle, creating a serious threat to peace and stability across the Strait. Therefore, what the Taiwan side should do is abandon the “Taiwan independence” proposition and separatist thinking and return to the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Only then can it truly safeguard peace and stability in cross-Strait relations.\nOn your second question, we have also noted the open letter from Mr. Xu. Realizing national reunification is the common aspiration of Chinese people at home and abroad. The tremendous achievements in the mainland's economic and social development, as well as the historic changes in cross-Strait relations, have also led more and more far-sighted people on the island to recognize that cross-Strait reunification is the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","经济日报记者","2017 marks the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait exchanges. I would like the spokesperson to review the important results of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges in recent years.","Cross-Strait trade has continued to grow in the first half of this year, reaching US$87.49 billion. In addition, the mainland approved 1,688 projects with Taiwanese investment, and the actual amount of Taiwan investment utilized was US$1.19 billion. Our position of continuing to promote economic exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait has been consistent and is also very clear. We have been actively helping Taiwanese companies upgrade and transform, helping them reduce operating costs on the mainland and solve financing difficulties. In addition, we are actively promoting basic equal treatment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and mainland enterprises, creating better conditions and environment for Taiwan compatriots to share the development opportunities and achievements of the mainland. We believe that economic exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait are mutually beneficial, win-win, and have broad prospects, and that no force can stop them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","海峡之声电台记者","It is our understanding that a mainland medical team recently provided emergency treatment in Chad, Africa, to a young Taiwanese woman who suddenly fell critically ill. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","As we understand it, at the end of August this year, a Taiwan female employee surnamed Liu at a Taiwan-invested hotel in Chad suddenly fell seriously ill. After failing to be saved at a local hospital, she later asked the 12th batch of the Chinese medical team assisting Chad for help. The medical team provided emergency treatment. When the blood supply was insufficient, the team leader voluntarily donated blood, which pulled this Taiwan compatriot back from danger; she has recently returned to Taiwan to recuperate. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, a family whose blood runs thicker than water. No matter where Taiwan compatriots are overseas, and no matter what difficulties they encounter, we are willing to provide assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842526.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","广东深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, Taiwan's external affairs authorities recently revealed that during this year's UN General Assembly they chose not to submit the proposal requested by the “allies.” Public opinion outside holds that this was to avoid provoking the mainland before the 19th CPC National Congress. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second, outside parties are paying particular attention to how the 19th…","Your first question: the United Nations is an international organization made up of sovereign states, and it adheres to the One China policy. Any act that challenges the One China principle, which is universally recognized by the international community, is bound to fail. Your second question: our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We will continue to uphold the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the One China principle, firmly safeguard the common political foundation for peaceful development across the Taiwan Strait, oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" and defend territorial integrity and sovereignty. At the same time, we will actively promote exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, advance the integrated economic and social development of both sides, and bring benefits to compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Some public opinion holds that recent signs in cross-Strait exchanges indicate that the mainland's policies on cross-Strait exchanges have loosened. Is this true?","What you describe is an interpretation by certain media. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and agreeing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can the institutionalized cross-Strait exchange mechanisms continue. On this point of principle, our position will not waver in the slightest.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842530.htm"],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","The Ninth BRICS Leaders’ Meeting was held in Xiamen from September 3 to 5. Some commentators have pointed out that if Taiwan can seize the BRICS opportunity and improve cross-Strait relations, Taiwan’s economy could gain enormous room for development; otherwise its prospects will be quite grim. How does the spokesperson evaluate this? Second, the draft party platform of the Kuomintang’s 8·20 Party Congress has…","Your first question: The BRICS Leaders' Xiamen Meeting concluded successfully on September 5. During the meeting, several heads of Taiwan-invested enterprises were invited to attend the business forum activities as representatives of Fujian enterprises. We believe that the in-depth development of cooperation between the mainland and BRICS countries will provide more development opportunities for Taiwan-invested enterprises.\nYour second question: The Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson already responded to this on August 20, and I can repeat it here. In 2005, the KMT and the CPC reached five common visions for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, establishing the common political foundation that both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence.” On this basis, the two parties strengthened exchange activities, promoted peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and achieved fruitful results. The current situation in cross-Strait relations is complex and grave. We are willing to maintain communication with the KMT on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China principle, and opposition to “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen dialogue and jointly promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","We note that the mainland's “new four great inventions” have recently continued to attract public attention on the island of Taiwan, including some reflections. If one does not face up to the mainland's development, Taiwan cannot correctly find its own future. What comments does the spokesperson have on this call from all sectors of the island?","As you mentioned, the mainland's “New Four Great Inventions” reflect achievements that have attracted worldwide attention over the years through reform and opening up and a series of economic developments. The development of the mainland's economy and society has also provided broad room and prospects for economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. We certainly hope that both sides can join hands to develop together and progress together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","At the Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum on the 8th of this month, economist Lin Yifu, through an analysis of per capita GDP data, showed that he hopes Taiwan will not miss the opportunity to take off together with the mainland, and will not continue to pursue the wrong “New Southbound Policy.” Do you agree with this?","We have stated many times that the economies on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese economy, and that economic exchange and cooperation across the Strait is a mutually beneficial, win-win good thing that benefits both sides. Therefore, we are willing to share the mainland’s development opportunities and achievements with Taiwan compatriots, in order to realize common development. However, taking actions that violate the laws of economic development for the sake of political self-interest will only cause damage to Taiwan’s economy and the interests of Taiwanese businesspeople.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, Taiwan media reported that, as the mainland advances cross-Strait economic and social integration, the mainland may in the future open up space for political participation for Taiwan residents living on the mainland, including allowing Taiwan residents to take part in elections or hold public office. I would like the spokesperson to confirm this news.","For many years, the mainland has actively promoted personnel exchanges between the two sides and exchange and cooperation in various fields across the Strait, advancing the integrated development of cross-Strait economies and societies and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. In the future we will continue to uphold the concept that both sides of the Strait are one family, share the mainland's development opportunities and achievements with Taiwan compatriots, and introduce various policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' study, internships, employment, entrepreneurship, and life and development on the mainland, benefiting Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊","Recently, Taiwan's representative to the United States, Gao Shuo-tai, compared cross-Strait relations to a relationship between neighbors in remarks to American media. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Cross-Strait relations are by no means state-to-state relations, and of course they are not a “neighbor” relationship either.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan media claimed that the American Institute in Taiwan has been contacting relevant parties in Taiwan and plans to begin providing replenishment operations for US warships in waters off Taiwan starting in 2018. What evaluation does the spokesperson have?","We have stated many times that we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between Taiwan and the United States. This position is clear and consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Since May 20 last year, the number of times PLA aircraft have flown around Taiwan has continued to increase. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","I think we have answered this question before. This is a planned, routine training exercise.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170913_11842547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","In response to a question from a Taiwan journalist on whether Lai Ching-te's assumption of the post of head of Taiwan's executive branch would affect cross-Strait relations, An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the regular press conference on September 13 in response to inquiries that Director Zhang Zhijun had already answered this question on September 8 while attending the Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum. We do not care about personnel changes on the Taiwan authorities' side; what we value and attend to is their mainland policy. On cross-Strait relations, the question the DPP authorities most need to answer is what exactly the nature of cross-Strait relations is. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170913_11842531.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-09-20","Lu Kang","","According to reports, an earthquake measuring 7.1 on the Richter scale has rocked central Mexico on September 19, killing at least 200 people. Is any Chinese national killed or injured in this earthquake?","China is following the information about the strong earthquake that struck Mexico and caused major casualties. We deeply mourn for the victims and express our sincere condolences to the bereaved families, the Mexican government and the people of the earthquake-hit area. We believe that the brave and tenacious Mexican people will surely rise above the disaster and rebuild their homeland soon.\nThe Chinese government pays high attention to the safety of Chinese nationals in Mexico, and the Chinese diplomatic missions in Mexico have launched emergency consular protection mechanism. According to the information we have at this time, some Taiwan compatriots have been stranded and one injured after the earthquake. The Chinese Foreign Ministry and Chinese diplomatic missions in Mexico will continue closely following the situation of the disaster and provide necessary assistance to Chinese nationals.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1494956.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1494927.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-09-22","Lu Kang","","Can you give us more details about the casualties of and the treatment and rescue efforts for the Chinese nationals following the earthquake in Mexico?","I said the Chinese government has been closely following the security situation of the Chinese nationals in the earthquake in Mexico the other day. The Mexican side has confirmed to the Chinese Embassy in Mexico that three out of the five Taiwan compatriots trapped under the debris of the collapsed buildings in the downtown of Mexico City have been killed and the remaining two still missing. We deeply mourns the victims and extend sincere condolences to the bereaved families. By far, the rescue efforts are going on. The Chinese Foreign Ministry and the Chinese Embassy to Mexico will continue closely following the development of the situation of the disaster and provide necessary assistance to Chinese nationals.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1495913.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1495923.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-09-25","Lu Kang","","Yesterday the China Central Television (CCTV) covered the news that the Chinese embassies in the Caribbean countries assisted the transfer of the Chinese citizens in the hurricane-hit areas in Dominica. Up to now, how many Chinese citizens have been properly resettled?","Recently, the Caribbean island nation Dominica took a direct hit from Hurricane Maria, which caused the paralysis of local transportation and communications, shutdown of airports and a scarcity of goods supplies. The Chinese government expressed condolences to the hurricane-struck Dominica and immediately launched the emergent humanitarian response mechanism. We will provide emergent humanitarian assistance as soon as possible.\nThe Chinese government is highly concerned about the security of the Chinese citizens in Dominica. Following the hurricane, the Foreign Ministry immediately activated the emergency response mechanism to coordinate the Chinese Embassy in Dominica and Chinese embassies in the neighboring countries of Dominica to take measures to offer emergent assistance to the transfer of Chinese nationals in Dominica.\nThanks to the concerted efforts of the Chinese embassies in Dominica, Antigua and Barbuda, Barbados and Trinidad and Tobago, as of the evening of September 22 local time, the first batch of 158 Chinese citizens, including two Taiwan compatriots and a just one-month-old baby, have been emergently transferred to Antigua and Barbuda and properly resettled. Now the transfer of relevant people is still intensively underway.\nHereby I would like to avail myself of this opportunity to express our heartfelt thanks to the assistance and support provided by relevant countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1496727.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1496591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台中国新闻记者","We noticed that the DPP recently held its “National Congress,” at which Tsai Ing-wen proposed forming a new discourse to define the party's direction and route in the new era. How does the spokesperson respond to this statement?","As everyone knows, our policy and guidelines toward Taiwan are consistent and clear. Only when the DPP abandons its “Taiwan independence” stance can it find a way out on cross-Strait relations. We have repeatedly reaffirmed that the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations; only by upholding the political foundation that embodies the one-China principle can the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations be maintained.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847607.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Reportedly, Lai Ching-te, the newly appointed head of Taiwan's executive authority, recently stated during a question-and-answer session before the Legislative Yuan that Taiwan is a “sovereign and independent country” and that the two sides are not subordinate to each other. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations, nor are they “one China, one Taiwan.” Taiwan, as an inalienable part of Chinese territory, has never been a country and will never become one. The mainland firmly opposes any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist words and deeds, will never allow the historical tragedy of national division to recur, and those who engage in “Taiwan independence” separatism will surely reap the bitter fruit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847605.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","We note that at the DPP's National Congress held on the 24th, Tsai Ing-wen raised issues related to reform of the “constitutional system,” which has drawn attention in Taiwan society. How do you view this issue?","We will closely watch the relevant developments. I wish to reiterate that the red lines of cross-Strait relations are very clear, and our determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847603.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","厦门卫视记者","The recent Meizhou Mazu statue procession received attention in Taiwan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To meet the strong wishes of the broad Taiwanese Mazu believers, at the invitation of Taiwan's Hon Hai Group, Banqiao Cihui Temple in New Taipei City, and the Taiwan Mazu Association, the Mazu statue of the Meizhou Ancestral Temple in Fujian will conduct a 17-day tour in Taiwan from September 23 to October 9. This tour is another major event in civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. The tour covers ten counties and cities, including Taipei, New Taipei, Keelung, Taoyuan, Hsinchu, Miaoli, Chiayi, Yunlin, Changhua, and Taichung, and encompasses 89 temples in Taiwan, the largest number of temples visited in any tour so far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847600.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","May I ask whether the conflict that broke out at “The Voice of China” event held in Taiwan will affect future cross-strait cultural exchanges? Will it affect the future performances of cross-strait artists in Taiwan or on the mainland? Lai Ching-te mentioned hoping this matter will not affect cross-strait relations. How do you respond?","The brand music program “The Voice of China,” which is popular with audiences on both sides of the Strait, was invited to Taiwan for the third time to hold music exchange activities, and was welcomed and anticipated by Taiwan students and youth. We are pleased to see young people across the Strait come together in the name of music and share the joy brought by musical dreams. But a few days ago, when this music event was held in Taiwan, it was organizedly attacked by some people carrying “Taiwan independence” flags and slogans, attracting attention from all sectors and drawing criticism and questions from public opinion on the island.\nThis year marks the 30th year of cross-Strait exchanges. The 30 years of cross-Strait relations fully demonstrate that, although there have been various twists and turns, the desire of people on both sides, including the vast majority of Taiwan compatriots, for exchange and cooperation is a historical trend that cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","The cross-Strait industrial cooperation zone was recently inaugurated in Guangxi. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","To help Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises expand new development space on the mainland, on September 15 the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce, unveiled and established the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone in the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region. This cooperation zone is “one zone, three parks,” comprising the Fangchenggang Industrial Park, the Chongzuo Industrial Park and the Qinzhou Industrial Park. We believe the establishment of the cooperation zone will provide greater business opportunities for the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847602.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Two questions. First, regarding the incident involving “The Voice of China,” some Taiwan public opinion holds that it constitutes “cultural united front” work. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office view this claim? Second, regarding the proportion of classical Chinese texts in Taiwan high school Chinese language courses: the proportion was reversed, and it was ultimately decided that it would be reduced by 10%,…","On the first question: as everyone can see, this is a simple and normal music exchange activity that young people on both sides of the Strait enjoy, and it has already been held three times in Taiwan. I think those who politicize this event out of proportion may lack confidence or be driven by a particular ideological bias. To call it “cultural united front work” is baseless and ignores the facts.\nOn the second question: for some time, “Taiwan independence” forces have been tampering with curriculum outlines and textbooks, which has met with questioning and opposition from most conscientious circles in Taiwan's education and culture and from public opinion. The approach of Taiwan's education authorities will only turn Taiwan's education into a victim of political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","In early July, the Ministry of Education announced that it would relax the standards for Taiwan high school graduates to apply to mainland universities based on their General Scholastic Ability Test scores. The threshold for admission was lowered from the previous standard to the same standard for all. The follow-up impact has included raising concern in Taiwan society about whether there will be an exodus of…","The Ministry of Education adopted this measure to create more convenient conditions for Taiwan youth to study on the mainland, aiming to further promote exchanges between cross-Strait youth and in the cross-Strait education sector. As for the worry that this may cause an “exodus wave,” I think it is an entirely unnecessary concern, perhaps an overly rich imagination, because after all, the number of students recruited is limited.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","We note that after Singapore Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong's recent visit to China, he once again reiterated Singapore's opposition to “Taiwan independence” and adherence to the one-China principle. There are also reports that Singapore's “Starlight Program,” under which Singapore sends soldiers to Taiwan for training, may come to an end. What is the spokesperson's response?","Not long ago, the leaders of China and Singapore held a meeting, and the relevant content has been reported in the news. With the rise of the mainland's international status and the expansion of its influence, the international community's adherence to the one-China framework has increasingly consolidated, and “Taiwan independence” separatism has no room at all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Recently, an earthquake occurred in Mexico, and the Chinese Embassy in Mexico carried out rescue operations for Taiwanese compatriots who were trapped. Taiwanese media analyzed that the mainland has recently strengthened emergency relief services for Taiwanese residents overseas, and has intentionally implemented the \"nationalization\" of Taiwanese compatriots internationally. What is the spokesperson's comment on…","Safeguarding the rights and interests of overseas Chinese, including those of Taiwan compatriots, has always been the guiding principle and practice of our embassies and consulates abroad. After the strong earthquake in Mexico this time, when the Chinese Embassy received a call for help and learned that five Taiwan compatriots were trapped and missing, it immediately asked the relevant Mexican departments to make every effort to rescue them. Within the 72-hour golden rescue window, the embassy closely followed the rescue progress and visited the relatives of the trapped Taiwan compatriots many times. On September 22, it was confirmed by the relevant Mexican departments and the relatives of the Taiwan compatriots that all five trapped Taiwan compatriots had unfortunately died. Here, we express deep condolences to the deceased Taiwan compatriots and sincere sympathy to their families. Taiwan compatriots are our own flesh and blood. Our embassy in Mexico is willing to further assist the relevant relatives of the Taiwan compatriots in properly handling the aftermath.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201709/t20170927_11847599.htm"],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, former Taiwan leader Lee Teng-hui said that the mainland's united front work toward Taiwan has allied with Taiwan's “black societies” (organized crime). Last weekend a clash broke out at the “The Voice of China” event, and some Taiwan media outlets and netizens said that “black society” elements are involved in Taiwan's pro-unification groups and demanded that the Taiwan authorities investigate and…","Let me first address the “Voice of China” incident. I have also noted that the Taiwan media are asking: Who stirred up this conflict? Who is behind it? Who is trying to politicize this normal music exchange activity? I think everyone has an answer in their hearts.\nAs for Lee Teng-hui, the “godfather of Taiwan independence,” I believe that his recent move to use this occasion to attack Taiwan's unification-leaning camp and people who support cross-Strait exchanges and reunification is nothing more than an attempt to further create a “green terror,” and his intentions are extremely sinister. As everyone knows, Lee Teng-hui's time in office was a period when black-gold politics ran rampant in Taiwan's political arena. Who the “gangsters” are, everyone knows full well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Two questions. First, on the 24th the DPP held its “National Congress.” In remarks made as party chairperson, Tsai Ing-wen said that the rise of mainland China is a situation the whole world must now face with caution, and that emotional hatred or blind appeasement cannot honestly confront the development of mainland China's rise. How does the spokesperson evaluate this? Second, calls to pardon Chen Shui-bian…","I will answer the second question first: we do not comment on judicial cases in Taiwan. Everyone will wait and see what judicial values the DPP and the Taiwan authorities uphold.\nTurning to the first question: since 1949, and especially over the 40 years of reform and opening up, the mainland's development and progress have achieved remarkable accomplishments that have also won the growing recognition of more and more Taiwan compatriots. The era in which “Taiwan independence” forces could get by by smearing the mainland and creating confrontation and hatred is becoming increasingly unsustainable. Fundamentally, the key factor determining the direction of cross-Strait relations is the development and progress of the mainland. We will continue to maintain our own momentum of development, advance the cause of socialism with Chinese characteristics to achieve new accomplishments, and realize the Chinese Dream of a prosperous country, national rejuvenation and people's happiness. In this process, we will continue to implement the central government's major policies toward Taiwan, firmly uphold the “1992 Consensus” political foundation and the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resolutely curb any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, uphold the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, actively advance exchange and cooperation in all fields of cross-Strait civil society, promote and deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait economies and societies, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, and work hand in hand to build a community of shared destiny across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We note that four days after the Lee Ming-che case hearing, the Taiwan authorities also handed down the so-called “mainland student espionage case” verdict. What is your response?","We are highly concerned about the safety and lawful rights and interests of mainland residents in Taiwan, and we firmly oppose interference with and obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges on any pretext or by any means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国网记者","Recently some voices on the island have said that the decline in mainland tourists makes it urgent to save Taiwan's tourism industry. How does the spokesperson evaluate this view? On the other hand, the National Day Golden Week is coming up. What advice does the spokesperson have for mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan?","Since last year, the number of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism has continued to drop sharply. The reasons are well known, and we have analyzed them several times at previous press conferences; please refer to them. This year, the National Day and Mid-Autumn Festival holidays coincide, so the National Tourism Administration has released a holiday travel guide. As far as I understand, from October 1 to 8, domestic tourist trips are expected to reach 710 million person-trips, and outbound tourism will also see a small peak. Where to travel is a decision mainland residents make for themselves, taking into account various factors.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报《两岸经合》周刊记者","Recently Taiwan media reported that the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Zijin Mountain Summit will be held in November. Please confirm this and introduce the relevant situation.","The Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit is a very important civil platform where business and economic circles on both sides of the Strait exchange views, hold discussions, and carry out cooperation. In recent years, the Summit has played an important role in gathering the strength of cross-Strait entrepreneurs, promoting cross-Strait industrial cooperation and cooperation among small and medium-sized enterprises, and jointly advancing cross-Strait economic cooperation. Regarding the arrangements for this year's Summit annual meeting, as far as I understand, both sides are currently communicating about specific arrangements, and once they are settled, they will be announced promptly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","联合早报记者","Recently, much public opinion has pointed out that after the 19th Party Congress, the mainland may have placed the resolution of the Taiwan question on its agenda. Please comment on this claim.","I wish to reiterate once again that our major policy principles on Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will continue to uphold the “1992 Consensus,” safeguard the political foundation and correct direction of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We are also willing to continue expanding cross-Strait exchanges, promote the integrated economic and social development across the Strait, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides, build a community of shared destiny across the Strait, and, in the process of uniting Taiwan compatriots and jointly realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, achieve the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Will the controversy over “The Voice of China” affect our policy of actively promoting cross-Strait youth exchanges? As the summer boom in cross-Strait youth exchanges comes to an end, are there any major upcoming cross-Strait youth exchange activities you could introduce to us?","As I said just now, the policies and measures we support and encourage for exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, especially between young students across the Strait, will not change. We also believe that the public will and trend toward cross-Strait exchange and cooperation will not change either. As you said, during the summer vacation, cross-Strait exchanges, especially youth and student exchange activities, reached a peak. Next, around the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait exchanges, relevant mainland departments and localities will also hold a series of exchange activities. We will notify everyone promptly of any important events so that you can cover them, and we will also promptly disclose important information through this platform.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","The U.S. House and Senate have successively passed the National Defense Authorization Act, which contains content on the possibility of U.S. and Taiwanese warships mutually docking. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and is also the most important and most sensitive issue in China-U.S. relations. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","大公报、大公网记者","Tsai Ing-wen said that \"emotional hatred or blind appeasement cannot face up to China's rise and development.\" How does the spokesperson interpret the hatred and appeasement referred to in this remark?","I have already responded at length. I think circumstances are stronger than people: the mainland's development and progress are also attracting the attention of more and more Taiwan compatriots. Under this trend, mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides of the Strait can only grow fuller, and the positive factors accumulated through peaceful development will keep increasing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Will the “KMT-CPC Forum” continue to be held this year? Will the format of the “KMT-CPC Forum” change in the future?","We have stated many times that the Kuomintang and the Communist Party will, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” continue to maintain communication, strengthen exchanges, and jointly safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201709/t20170927_11847608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-09-28","Lu Kang","","A couple of days ago, you said that the first batch of Chinese citizens in Dominica have been transferred after the hurricane struck Dominica. Can you give us more details on this?","Under the coordination of China's Foreign Ministry, over the past few days, the Chinese embassies in Dominica, Antigua and Barbuda and Barbados have been assisting the transfer of the Chinese nationals in Dominica and relevant efforts have achieved remarkable progress. After the first batch of 158 people were successfully transferred to Antigua and Barbuda by ship on the evening of September 22 local time, the second batch of 306 people arrived in Antigua and Barbuda by ship on September 25. In addition, another 23 Chinese compatriots arrived in Barbados by taking the naval vessels of Barbados Coast Guards. Up to now, 487 people have been transferred from Dominica, including one Macao compatriot and two Taiwan compatriots. All relevant people have been properly resettled under the assistance of the Chinese embassies in relevant countries. To date, the Chinese nationals with the willingness to be transferred that the Chinese Embassy in Dominica can get in touch with have all been transferred from Dominica.\nHereby I would like to once again extend my heartfelt thanks to the assistance provided by relevant countries and the strenuous efforts made by all.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1498012.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1497848.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","As the 19th CPC National Congress will be held in October, what achievements have been made by China in deepening national defense and military reform so far? Is there any plan of pushing forward the major work of the reform in the next phase?\nChinese Defense Minister Chang Wanquan met with visiting Singaporean Defense Minister Ng Eng Hen in Beijing on September 21. Analysts say that Singapore is likely to stop…","Aiming at achieving the ‘Two Centenary Goals’ and realizing the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, the CPC Central Committee, the Central Military Commission (CMC) and President Xi Jinping, who is also chairman of the CMC, have made the important strategic decision to deepen the national defense and military reform.\nAs the reform has entered the implementation stage, changes of historical significance have taken place in military leadership & management system; substantial breakthroughs have been made in the reform of commanding system for joint operations; a solid step has been taken in the reform of force scale, structure and composition; a critical development has been achieved in the reform of joint logistics support; and, a systematic restructuring of military academies, scientific research institutions and training institutions has been completed. Besides, major progress has been made in the development of supporting policies and mechanisms as well as the civil-military integrated development. Now the Chinese military takes on a new look featuring new mechanisms, a new structure and a new pattern of development.\nThe meeting between Gen. Chang Wanquan and Mr. Ng Eng Hen has already been covered by media. In recent years, we have seen a generally smooth development of the mil-to-mil relations between China and Singapore. The two sides have conducted a series of cooperation including high-level exchanges, defense policy dialogues, joint training activities, mutual naval port calls, and intercollegiate exchanges among others. Mutual understanding has been deepened with many fruits of practical cooperation. The Chinese side is willing to work with the Singaporean side and create more favorable conditions for the development of a more mature mil-to-mil relations between the two countries.\nI also want to stress here that Taiwan is an indispensable part of China, and we firmly oppose any country to conduct any form of official exchange or military contact with Taiwan.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-09/28/content_4793398.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Since May 20 last year, we have seen more and more PLA aircrafts circling around the Taiwan Island. Some Taiwan media analyze that this is a warning to the Taiwan authority, and some people in Taiwan regard it as a military threat from the mainland of China which is worrisome . What is your comment?","For your question, there are three points I want to make. Firstly, Taiwan is a part of China, and this is the precondition and basis for me to answer the question. Secondly, the relevant air force training is part of the annual training plan of the PLA air force, and similar trainings will continue in the future. Thirdly, for those people who feel worried, I want to say, there is no need to fear or worry as long as one does not seek ‘Taiwan independence’.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-09/28/content_4793398.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-09-29","Lu Kang","","Yesterday, Susan Thornton, the Acting Assistant Secretary of the US State Department, told a hearing of the Senate Committee on Banking, Housing and Urban Affairs that the pressure campaign of the United States is aimed at bringing the DPRK back to the negotiating table. Meanwhile, the US has been clear about its strategy towards the DPRK. The US does not seek the regime change or collapse of the DPRK. The US…","We have taken note of Ms. Thornton's statement. Recently, relevant parties have consecutively sent the positive signals that the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue, in the final analysis, should be resolved politically through dialogue and consultation. We hold an encouraging attitude to this. The Chinese side agrees with the Four Nos promise which has been reiterated by the US side many times. We hope that the US side can translate these commitments into concrete actions and that the DPRK can work for the shared goal. We hope that relevant parties can demonstrate utmost sincerity to accumulate conditions for dialogue and create opportunities for peace talks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1498369.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1498267.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-10-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 10 (reporter Chen Jianxing): In response to the content on cross-Strait relations in the “Double Ten” speech of the leader of the Taiwan authorities, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 10th: We have noted that the speech repeated some of the earlier statements. We have stated our position and attitude on cross-Strait relations many times. Regardless of what model or proposition the Taiwan authorities put forward, the key is to clarify the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations and to confirm the core recognition that Taiwan and the mainland both belong to one China.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that this year marks 30 years since cross-Strait exchanges began. The achievements of cross-Strait exchanges over the past 30 years have been hard-won, and their lessons are extremely precious. The most important lesson is that only by adhering to the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully and stably, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation advance smoothly, and the well-being of compatriots on both sides continue to grow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201710/t20171010_11850114.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-10-11","Hua Chunying","","Yesterday the president of Spain's autonomous region of Catalonia offered a dialogue with the Spanish government before implementing the Declaration of Independence. Given China's investment in Catalonia and the fact that Spain is an important partner of China in the Belt and Road Initiative, is this political crisis a matter of concern for China?","We have noted the relevant situation in Catalonia of Spain. China has said multiple times that this is Spain's internal affairs. We believe the Spanish government and people can properly handle the issue and uphold national unity and prosperity. Spain is a friendly country of China, and we will continue to develop friendly cooperation with it by upholding the principle of respecting each other's sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in each other's internal affairs.\nRegarding your question of whether the Chinese side is concerned that this will affect the trade and investment between China and Spain in the future, I don't think we need to worry about it. As I said just now, we believe the Spanish government and people can properly handle the relevant issue and uphold national unity, stability and prosperity. As a friendly nation of Spain, China is willing to keep upholding the principle of mutual respect and reciprocity to develop mutually beneficial cooperation with Spain in various fields, including the fields of trade, investment and finance.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1500871.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1500839.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-12","Hua Chunying","","Recently, the president of Spain's Catalan autonomous region said in an address at the Catalan parliament that the region had won the right to be independent as a result of the referendum, but would suspend the independence declaration and seek a dialogue with the Spanish government. What is your comment?","The Chinese side closely follows the relevant situation in Catalonia, understands and supports the effort of the Spanish government to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity and believes the Spanish side is capable of safeguarding the social order and civil rights and interests in accordance with law. China and Spain are friendly countries. We will continue to develop friendly cooperation with Spain by upholding the principle of respecting each other's sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in each other's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1501196.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1501156.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-13","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, US House Foreign Affairs Committee passed the Taiwan Travel Act on October 12, which calls for the complete lifting of restrictions on high-level visits between the US and Taiwan. How do you comment on that?","We have noted the relevant reports. I have to stress once again that the relevant bill has severely violated the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiques and constituted interference in China's internal affairs. We are firmly opposed to this.\nThe Chinese side urges the US side to comply with the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiques and cautiously handle the Taiwan question, not to engage in any official exchange and contact with Taiwan or send any wrong message to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists least the larger picture of the China-US relations should be disrupted and undermined.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1501588.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1501525.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-13","Hua Chunying","","It is reported that on October 11, Spanish Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy sent a written order to the president of the Catalan autonomous region, which formally requested the government of the Catalan autonomous region to confirm whether it has declared the independence of Catalonia by October 16 at 8:00 GMT. If the independence is confirmed, the Spanish government will give the Catalan government an additional…","I have stated the position of the Chinese side at request over the past two days. The Chinese government understands and supports the effort of the Spanish government to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity. We hope and believe the Spanish government and people are capable of finding a proper solution under the framework of law and order to uphold national solidarity and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1501588.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1501525.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-10-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 15 (reporter Chen Jianxing). In response to the accident on the morning of the 15th in which falling rocks at the Three Gorges scenic area in Yichang, Hubei, killed three Taiwan tourists, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions: We express deep condolences to the compatriots who died and extend our sympathy to their families. The Straits Exchange Association and the Straits Tourism Exchange Association will form a working group and send personnel to the scene to assist in handling the aftermath.\nMa Xiaoguang said that after receiving the relevant information, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Straits Exchange Association attached great importance to the matter and immediately activated the emergency response mechanism for sudden incidents involving Taiwan. They verified the full situation through the tourism authorities and the local Taiwan Affairs Offices, and reported the known casualty situation to the Taiwan Travel Association through the Straits Tourism Exchange Association.\nHe said that the latest information held by the Yichang Taiwan Affairs Office is that the accident involved a tour group of Dong Sheng Travel Agency of Taiwan, with 45 Taiwan compatriots in total. The accident caused 3 deaths and 2 minor injuries. Apart from one Taiwanese tour guide who remains at the hospital to assist with related matters, the other 39 Taiwan compatriots are resting on the boat.\nMa Xiaoguang said that over the years, we have, in accordance with relevant regulations and policies, properly handled every sudden incident involving the lives and property of compatriots on both sides through emergency response mechanisms. We will spare no effort to guide and coordinate the relevant departments and localities to properly handle this sudden incident and safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201710/t20171015_11852569.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-10-16","Lu Kang","","In about 45 minutes time, it can be the deadline for the leader of Catalonia to declare or not declare independence. Should he choose to declare independence, he can't probably count on support from Europe. Can he count on support from China?","China's position remains unchanged on the issue of Catalonia. I would like to reiterate that the Chinese government understands and supports the efforts made by the Spanish government to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity. We believe that the Spanish side is capable of safeguarding the social order and civil rights and interests in accordance with law.\nChina and Spain have friendly relations. We will continue developing friendly cooperation with Spain in various fields in the principle of respecting each other's sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in each other's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1502004.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1501973.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-10-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports in Taiwan, a US Army Lieutenant Colonel recently claimed that China was seeking to set up a military base in the Pacific island country of Micronesia to cut off US power projection to the Asia-Pacific region. Could you please confirm this?","This report is pure fabrication and not worth refuting.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-10/27/content_4795905.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-10-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, we have seen some speculation in Taiwan's media that the PLA may strengthen its combat flight patrol surrounding the Taiwan Island in the future to increase military pressure on Taiwan. Could you please comment on this?","Taiwan is a part of China. The PLA will carry out routine training according to its annual plan. We have reiterated repeatedly that we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and utmost efforts. At the same time, we are capable and confident and have methods to maintain the unity, sovereignty security and territorial integrity of the motherland.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-10/27/content_4795905.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2017-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: What is your comment on Tsai Ing-wen's speech at the “Thirty-Year Review and Prospects of Cross-Strait Exchanges” seminar?","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 26th in response to a question:\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations and is the key to ensuring their peaceful development.\nOur attitude toward exchanges with all Taiwan political parties is open, and our standards are consistent. Once the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” is acknowledged and both sides recognize that they belong to one China, the two sides can engage in dialogue and consult on resolving problems of concern to compatriots on both sides, and there will be no obstacle to any Taiwan political party or group engaging with the mainland. The course of development of cross-Strait relations has fully proved this. Therefore, only by returning to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations clear the clouds and open new prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201710/t20171026_11857530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-10-27","Geng Shuang","","Tsai Ing-wen will be visiting three of Taiwan's allies in the Pacific from tomorrow, during which she will transit via Hawaii and Guam. Has China expressed any concerns or lodged any representations with the United States about these transits?","The one-China principle is a consensus widely shared by the international community and the principle we have always upheld in handling Taiwan's external exchanges.\nOn your question about the \"transit\" of the leader of the Taiwan region, the true purpose of her so-called \"transit\" is self-evident. We hope the US will abide by the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiques, deny her \"transit\", refrain from sending any wrong message to the Taiwan independence forces and uphold the larger interests of China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability. The Chinese side has lodged stern representations with the US side on this matter.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1505355.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1505306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-30","Hua Chunying","","Recently, the Catalonian autonomous region's parliament voted to pass the motion for \"independence\" and declared the \"establishment of an independent state\". The Spanish government said it would invoke Article 155 of the constitution as a firm response. What's your comment on this?","China's position on this issue has been consistent and unequivocal. We think it falls within Spain's internal affairs. We understand and support the Spanish government's effort to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity, oppose the act of splitting the country and undermining the rule of law, and believe Spain is capable of upholding the social order and safeguarding the rights and interests of its citizens.\nChina and Spain are friendly countries. We will continue to develop friendly cooperation in various fields with Spain following the principle of mutual respect for each other's sovereignty and territorial integrity and mutual non-interference in each other's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1505871.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1505857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-30","Hua Chunying","","A question on what happened in Catalonia. Do you think the current situation could harm Chinese investment or business in Catalonia? Will China issue a travel warning to Chinese citizens traveling to Catalonia?","We think what's happening in Catalonia is Spain's internal affairs. We understand and support the Spanish government's effort to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity, oppose the act of splitting the country and undermining the rule of law, and believe Spain is capable of upholding the social order and safeguarding the rights and interests of its citizens under the framework of law and system. We will continue to develop friendly cooperation in various fields with Spain following the principle of mutual respect for each other's sovereignty and territorial integrity and mutual non-interference in each other's internal affairs.\nRegarding whether we will advise Chinese citizens not to travel to a certain region for the time being, the relevant Chinese diplomatic missions will issue such information as needed. I have no information in this respect by far.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1505871.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1505857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-10-30","Hua Chunying","","Since last Friday, Spain's central government has taken over Catalonia. Has the Chinese government been in touch with the Spanish government or Embassy about this question? Have you received any pressure in condemning the Catalonian \"independence\"?","China and Spain are friendly countries. We have been maintaining close communication on various kinds of issues, especially issues of our respective and mutual concern.\nThe international community has been closely following the situation in Catalonia. We have noted the remarks from various parties of the international community, and the Chinese side is also paying great attention. We hope and believe the Spanish side is capable of upholding the social order and safeguarding the rights and interests of its citizens under the framework of law and system. I would like to reiterate that we understand and support the Spanish government's effort to uphold national unity, ethnic solidarity and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1505871.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1505857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 30 (reporter Zhao Bo) — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 30th, introduced that the Ministry of Justice has issued Order No. 136 and Announcement No. 176. Starting November 1, 2017, the scope within which Taiwan residents who have obtained mainland lawyer professional qualifications and mainland lawyer practice certificates may represent cross-Strait civil cases in the mainland will be expanded to five major categories and 237 items.\nIn response to a reporter’s inquiry about the Ministry of Justice’s issuance of the “Decision on Amending the ‘Measures for the Administration of Taiwan Residents Who Have Obtained National Legal Professional Qualifications Practicing as Lawyers in the Mainland’,” Ma Xiaoguang gave the above introduction. He said that the expansion of scope is based on the cross-Strait marriage and inheritance litigation business opened in 2008, with the addition of cross-Strait contract disputes, intellectual property disputes, civil litigation related to companies, securities, insurance, negotiable instruments, and other matters, as well as special procedure cases related to the above cases.\nMa Xiaoguang said that this opening measure will create better development opportunities and broader development space for the broad masses of Taiwan legal professionals, especially young and middle-aged legal practitioners, to work and start businesses in the mainland, and will provide a stronger rule-of-law guarantee for deepening exchange and cooperation in all fields across the Strait and for protecting the legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201710/t20171030_11859946.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-10-31","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, the Cambodian Immigration Department said that it has handed over 61 Chinese nationals, including 19 from Taiwan, to the mainland, who were involved in extorting money over the internet and by phone in Cambodia. What is your comment?","China highly commends and appreciates the Cambodian side for its adherence to the one China policy and its cooperation with China on cracking down cross-border crimes, including telecom frauds. China and Cambodia have been in close communication and cooperation in this field.\nThe relevant department in China will handle suspects across the Taiwan Strait in accordance with law which will help get to the bottom of this case, effectively fight crimes, and protect the legitimate rights and interests of the victims. We believe we will have the understanding and support of people across the Taiwan Strait and the international community.\nAs for the specifics of the case, the relevant competent department in China has released related information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1506230.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1506202.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, October 31 (reporter Zha Wenye). Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on October 31, said that the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit is an important civilian exchange platform through which economic circles on both sides exchange views and discuss macroeconomic conditions and industrial development trends and promote business matching and cooperation. As agreed by both sides of the summit, the 2017 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit will be held in Nanjing from November 6 to 7.\nMa Xiaoguang said that this year's annual meeting will take “Cross-Strait Industrial Integration: New Situation, New Business Opportunities and New Ideas” as its theme. It will hold activities including an opening ceremony, keynote speeches, seven thematic forums and a closing ceremony, and conduct in-depth discussions on cross-Strait cooperation in relevant industries, youth employment and entrepreneurship, and other issues. Some 600 people, including well-known entrepreneurs from both sides, heads of business associations, representatives of small and medium-sized enterprises, young entrepreneurs and experts and scholars, will attend. This summit is the first major cross-Strait civilian exchange event held after the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, and attendees will offer suggestions on expanding cross-Strait economic cooperation, achieving mutual benefit and win-win results, and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides under the new circumstances.\nDuring this year's annual meeting of the summit, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit and the National Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises will also hold a sales exhibition of Taiwan-funded enterprise products on the mainland, to showcase the development course and fruitful achievements of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland over the 30 years of civilian economic and trade exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. The exhibition consists of two parts, a display of development achievements and a sales exhibition of enterprise products, with nearly 700 Taiwan enterprises and their products from all over the mainland participating. Preparations are currently proceeding in an orderly manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171101_11860938.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-11-13","Geng Shuang","","The UN Climate Change Conference is now underway in Bonn, Germany. It is reported that Lee Ying-yuan, head of the Chinese Taipei delegation and also the so-called \"minister of the Environmental Protection Agency of Taiwan\" was denied access to the conference because of intervention from the Chinese mainland. What is your response? Second, Soong Chu-yu (James Soong), representing the Chinese Taipei at the APEC…","On your first question, I think you must be very clear with our consistent and clear position on Taiwan's participation in international activities, which is that the one-China principle must be observed.\nOn your second question, Taiwan's participation in APEC must accord with the one-China principle and the relevant APEC MOU. I want to stress that the improvement of the cross-Straits relations must be based on adhering to the 1992 Consensus which reflects the one-China principle. The Taiwan authority's denial of the historical fact of the 1992 Consensus and refusal to recognize that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China, has created some obstacles for interactions between the two sides.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1510216.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1510045.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-11-14","Geng Shuang","","Why did China block Taiwan from participating in the UN Climate Change Conference in Germany?","I already gave my answer yesterday. On the issue of Taiwan's participation in international events, China's position is very clear; that is, the one-China principle must be upheld.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1510671.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1510412.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The report of the 19th Party Congress proposed gradually providing Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland. We have also noted that some related beneficial measures have recently been introduced on the mainland. Please introduce the relevant situation.","This year, we have successively introduced a series of policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots’ study, entrepreneurship, employment and daily life on the mainland. For example, we issued 20 measures to further expand opening up, to further support Taiwan-funded enterprises in investing on the mainland; we established cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones, encouraging Taiwan-funded enterprises to expand into central and western regions and to take part in the Belt and Road Initiative; we promoted “Taiwan businesses going online” to help Taiwan-funded enterprises expand domestic sales; we provided convenience for Taiwan compatriots in purchasing and collecting tickets for civil aviation flights and high-speed rail travel; we relaxed the geographic restrictions on employment of Taiwan compatriots in mainland public institutions; we opened the National Social Science Fund to Taiwan researchers employed on the mainland; and we expanded the scope of practice for Taiwan residents who have obtained mainland lawyer professional qualifications, among other measures.\nRecently, relevant departments have successively introduced three policy measures to facilitate Taiwan students’ study and employment on the mainland. First, starting October 1 this year, Taiwan high school graduates who score at or above the standard level in all subjects of the General Scholastic Ability Test in Taiwan may apply directly to more than 200 mainland universities, namely the universities that enroll overseas Chinese and students from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. Information on university admissions can be obtained through the universities’ admissions websites and the mainland university admissions information website for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan students run by the Cross-Strait Admissions Service Center.\nSecond, the Ministry of Education recently required local governments and universities to provide targeted employment guidance and consultation for Taiwan graduates on the mainland, and to issue employment agreements and employment registration certificates to Taiwan graduates who wish to work and meet the conditions.\nThird, the Ministry of Finance and the Ministry of Education revised the administrative measures for scholarships for Taiwan students, dividing Taiwan student scholarships into three categories—undergraduate and junior college, master’s, and doctoral—and adding a Special Prize above the original first, second and third prizes, with an award amount equal to that of the National Scholarship. The amounts and number of awards at each level have been substantially increased.\nNext, we will work with relevant departments to fully implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, continue to study and introduce relevant policy measures, and gradually provide Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in study, entrepreneurship, employment and daily life on the mainland, promote the integrated development of cross-Strait economic and social life, and enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171115_11867624.htm"],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","央视“中国新闻”记者","Some time ago, Lu Li-an, a Taiwan-born delegate to the 19th Party Congress, and her family had their household registration cancelled by the Taiwan side. What is the spokesperson's comment on this matter?","Professor Lu Lian is a native-born compatriot from Taiwan Province. Through her own observation and reflection, she chose to join the Communist Party of China. As a party representative attending the 19th Party Congress, she said in an interview with reporters that she takes pride in being a daughter of Taiwan and is proud to be born Chinese, and she hopes that compatriots in Taiwan and fellow villagers on the island will take part in the great cause of jointly realizing the Chinese Dream. She also said that the distance between people's hearts and some misunderstandings can be dissolved. Her views have won wide recognition and affirmation from compatriots on both sides of the Strait; no matter what measures the Taiwan side takes, they cannot diminish her love for her hometown and for the Chinese mainland. Whether or not she has household registration in Taiwan, the mainland and Taiwan are both her home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171115_11867622.htm"],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","央视“海峡两岸”记者","Reportedly, Taiwan's relevant authorities will study and formulate the so-called “International Criminal Judicial Mutual Assistance Act.” In the future, criminal judicial assistance requests between Taiwan and the mainland, Hong Kong and Macao will apply its relevant provisions. What is your comment?","I am not yet familiar with the specific details of this bill. What I want to emphasize is that there is only one China; the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and related affairs must be handled strictly in accordance with this principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171115_11867621.htm"],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","We noted that the report to the 19th Party Congress on Taiwan policy did not clearly mention “integrated economic and social development across the Taiwan Strait.” I would like to ask the spokesperson what considerations lay behind this?","The policy statements in the report of the 19th Party Congress on deepening and expanding cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation fully reflect General Secretary Xi Jinping’s thinking on promoting the integrated economic and social development of both sides. We will earnestly implement them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","During the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit recently held in Nanjing, a product exhibition for Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland was held, which had positive influence and good results. Please introduce the relevant situation.","This year marks thirty years since cross-Strait exchanges began. To fully showcase the development course and achievements of Taiwanese businesses investing and building enterprises in the mainland, during the Cross-Strait CEO Summit, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises held a product exhibition of Taiwan-invested enterprises in Nanjing, Jiangsu. The exhibition consists of two parts: a product exhibition of Taiwan-invested enterprises, and a 30-year development achievement exhibition of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises in the mainland. Within an exhibition hall of 38,000 square meters, it brought together nearly 700 outstanding Taiwan-invested enterprises from 31 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the central government on the mainland. Their products cover all industries, fields, and categories in which Taiwanese businesses have invested in the mainland, with several thousand products on display. These include special exhibition areas featuring more than 100 heavyweight Taiwan-invested enterprise representatives and carefully designed displays by Taiwan youth innovation and entrepreneurship companies. The achievement exhibition reviewed the course of Taiwanese businesses crossing the Strait, riding the express train of mainland economic development, and continuously growing stronger. It recounted the moving stories of Taiwanese businesses growing from nothing to something and from small to large, and showed the bright prospects of Taiwanese businesses' continued development in the mainland and of cross-Strait cooperation for mutual benefit.\nThe holding of this exhibition has drawn high attention from economic circles on both sides of the Strait. Media from both sides, including the media friends present here, have conducted extensive coverage, which has produced a positive impact.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171115_11867623.htm"],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","We have noted that some people in Taiwan's Green camp have misunderstandings about the mainland's proposal to gradually provide Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots and to enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. They believe this is “united front” work or “small favors.” Does the spokesperson have any comment on this? Second question: We noted that Soong Chu-yu recently…","On the first question: our advancement of the relevant measures is entirely based on the concept of \"cross-Strait families are one family\". It conforms to the needs of Taiwan compatriots to study, live, start businesses and find employment on the Mainland, and fully reflects their voices. Any prejudice is untenable, and any misunderstanding and doubt are also unnecessary.\nOn the second question: I am not aware of the specific situation you mention, but everyone has seen that since the political situation in Taiwan changed last year, the DPP authorities have been using a rope to tie up the hands and feet of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. That rope destroys the political foundation of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, namely the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle. Therefore, only by cutting this rope can cross-Strait relations turn for the better and show bright prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","You just mentioned mainland scholarships. Previously, some print media reported that the first condition for applying for the scholarship is to acknowledge One China, otherwise the school will cancel your eligibility. Please confirm this. Second question: after Trump took office, on his first visit to China, President Xi hoped the US side could adhere to the One-China principle and prevent interference in…","On the first question, I think everyone knows that scholarships are certainly awarded to students who possess both virtue and talent and who excel in both character and studies. On the second question, adhering to the One-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, the political foundation for developing China-US relations, and the cornerstone of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The US side's adherence to the One-China principle accords with the common interests of both China and the United States.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","After the 19th Party Congress, Taiwan youths represented by Wang Yu-ching, who is pursuing a doctorate at Peking University, have successively expressed in recent days their wish to apply to join the Communist Party of China. What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","For this question, please consult the relevant competent authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","After the TPP was restructured into the CPTPP, the head of Taiwan's economic department attending the APEC meeting in Vietnam said that once the CPTPP takes effect, Taiwan will strive to join in the second batch. What is your view?","Our consistent position is clear and definite. We firmly oppose any of our diplomatic partners signing with Taiwan any agreement that carries sovereign implications and is of an official nature.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","The UN climate conference currently being held in Germany: representatives of Taiwan-related departments were unable to gain entry. It is rumored that this was due to pressure from the mainland side. How does the spokesperson respond?","On the question of Taiwan's participation in international organizations, our position is clear and consistent: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, through cross-Strait consultations. The reality is that because the Taiwan side refuses to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” the communication mechanisms between the two sides have stalled, making it impossible to address related issues. This is the crux of the problem. The Taiwan side should not turn the tables and should instead engage in serious self-reflection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Some Taiwan students in the mainland have applied to join the Communist Party. I would like to ask whether these Taiwan students must give up their Taiwan household registration in order to join. The Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation say that these students will be fined if they join. What is the spokesperson’s view?","Regarding the matter of Taiwan students applying to join the Communist Party of China that you mentioned, please inquire with the relevant departments. Based on my personal observation, realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has been the great dream of all Chinese people since modern times. Through long and unremitting efforts, the Communist Party of China has united and led the people of all ethnic groups in China, ushering in the great leap of the Chinese nation from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, and opening a bright prospect for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Some Taiwan compatriots who live, work and study on the mainland have personally experienced the earth-shaking changes and have increased their admiration for and identification with the Communist Party of China. I think this is quite natural. As for some of the practices of the Taiwan authorities, I believe they should abandon their hostile mindset, readily accept good advice, and respect the choices of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Reports say that Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, at the APEC meeting, suggested that Soong Chu-yu convey to Tsai Ing-wen that a “Xi-Tsai meeting” be held to resolve cross-Strait issues. Everyone now knows this seems unlikely. May I ask the spokesperson: what conditions would the two sides need to create to make a “Xi-Tsai meeting” possible?","First, the issue of cross-Strait relations is a matter among Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, and it should be resolved by Chinese people on both sides sitting down on a common basis and through equal consultation. Second, as you said, if the Taiwan side truly has sincerity in breaking the political deadlock and developing cross-Strait relations, it should take concrete action, acknowledge the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus,” and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. This is the key to the problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The Taiwan authorities' education department, disregarding strong opposition from all sectors on the island, has accelerated “de-Sinicization” moves in education. Recently it removed the classical text “Preface to the General History of Taiwan” from its recommended readings, triggering a new round of controversy. May I ask the spokesperson for comment? Second question: although relevant Taiwan authorities said…","First, as you noted in your question, these “de-Sinicization” moves have actually triggered social conflict and wide controversy within Taiwan, and they are unpopular. Chinese culture is a precious common treasure of the people on both sides of the Strait. Incredibly, some people are throwing away the treasures in their own homes, and in the end it is the welfare of Taiwan compatriots and the foundation of Taiwan society's future development that are harmed.\nSecond, regarding mainland residents traveling to Taiwan: indeed, we have recently received feedback from some tourists to Taiwan, who feel that there are more steps in applying for entry procedures and that the required procedures have become more cumbersome. I believe that since the Taiwan authorities have repeatedly stated verbally that they welcome mainland tourists to Taiwan, they should simplify the relevant procedures and provide convenience for them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently intentionally \"transited\" through Hawaii and Guam in the United States. What is your comment?","On this issue, our position has been consistent and clear. The one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, and all countries that have diplomatic relations with us should properly handle the Taiwan question on the basis of the one-China principle. Any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” in the international arena will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently published an op-ed in a Malaysian newspaper, calling out to the mainland from afar, urging the mainland to use its wisdom to talk with Taiwan. She also reiterated that since taking office last year, the Taiwan authorities have consistently released goodwill toward the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of these remarks?","Rather than shouting from afar, it is better to engage in direct dialogue. The authorities in Taiwan know full well where the key and the code for cross-Strait dialogue lie. All goodwill and sincerity should be tested against the “1992 Consensus” as the touchstone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Reports say that a Taiwan resident recently traveled to Vladivostok, Russia, for tourism through the Hunchun Port in Jilin. Because he exited using a mainland temporary passport, after returning to Taiwan, the Taiwan authorities cancelled his Taiwan household registration. May I ask the spokesperson for comment on this?","It is understood that issuing a passport valid for one trip to Taiwan residents who join China-Russia border group tours is a convenience measure provided for Taiwan residents taking part in border tourism on the mainland. Applying for it does not require establishing a household registration on the mainland as a precondition. In recent years, thousands of Taiwan compatriots have obtained this document.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","This year marks the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait exchanges. We have seen that commemorative events have recently been held in various places on both sides, in Taipei as well as in Xiamen. May I ask the spokesperson how you evaluate this extraordinary course of cross-Strait relations over these 30 years? What enlightening significance does it have for promoting the peaceful development of…","Regarding the extraordinary course of the 30 years since cross-Strait exchanges began, if there are any enlightenments, I think there are at least four:\nFirst, from the perspective of the course of historical development, everyone can see that the Mainland has always been the promoter of the development of cross-Strait relations. Over these 30 years, we have taken the initiative to introduce policies and measures to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At that time, the opening of exchanges was also inspired by our new-era policy of peaceful reunification, and compatriots on both sides were able to open the door that had been closed for 38 years.\nSecond, adhering to the one-China principle is the precondition for cross-Strait relations to develop smoothly. Conversely, cross-Strait relations will encounter twists, turns and setbacks.\nThird, the \"Taiwan independence\" forces have always stood on the opposite side of the development of cross-Strait relations. They use every means to interfere with, obstruct and oppose the development of cross-Strait relations and exchanges among compatriots on both sides. Therefore, to safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, we must jointly oppose \"Taiwan independence.\"\nFourth, it once again confirms that \"cross-Strait families are one family.\" Compatriots on both sides are flesh-and-blood brothers; we are all members of the Chinese nation. Therefore, people on both sides should exchange and cooperate. This is the trend of history. No matter how the cross-Strait situation changes, it cannot be stopped, and it will continue to develop with irresistible momentum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-15","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The 19th Party Congress report proposed acknowledging the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus,” and Tsai Ing-wen made a similar statement in her “5.20” speech last year. Therefore, some public opinion on the island believes this could become a new starting point for cross-Strait consensus. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment? Second question: A former head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department said that…","On the first question, we are talking about acknowledging the historical fact of the \"1992 Consensus.\" The leader of the Taiwan authorities talks about recognizing the historical fact of the \"1992 Talks.\" The difference of two characters is very significant. On this matter, she should make clear what consensus was reached at the \"1992 Talks\" and what the core meaning of that consensus is. Therefore, on this question she should continue to complete her answer sheet, that is, clearly state that she acknowledges the historical fact of the \"1992 Consensus\" and recognizes that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China.\nOn the second question, we generally do not comment on personal remarks. But everyone also recognizes that, with the continuous prosperity and progress of the Mainland, and with our continuous release and expression of goodwill in cross-Strait policy, more and more Taiwan compatriots, including some far-sighted Taiwanese figures, have deeply embraced the concept of \"cross-Strait families are one family\" and are willing to take part in the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. I think this is a good thing. As for resuming consultation and dialogue between the two sides, the basis must of course be the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle.\nThe failure of the Catalonia independence referendum fully shows that safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the supreme national interest, whether in the East or the West. Pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" is therefore doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171115_11867620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-11-17","Geng Shuang","","美国候任国防部亚太助理部长薛瑞福16日在为美参议院军事委员会听证会准备的证词中表示，美国有自己的“一个中国”政策，而美台军舰互访完全符合美国的一中政策。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1511665.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-11-20","Lu Kang","","The Victoria's Secret Fashion Show is happening tonight in Shanghai. Two of the guests, according to US media reports, have been denied their visas. One of them, a US singer, failed to get her visa probably because she wore a Taiwanese \"flag\"over her shoulders at a 2015 concert in Taiwan. The other one, a US model, once made a gesture on social media that some people interpreted as being insulting to Asian…","I'm not aware of the details you mentioned. As we said before, as a principle, we welcome foreign citizens to China for normal trade, tourism and cultural activities, and we have been issuing visas to the eligible applicants. In the meanwhile, I have to point out that, just like all other countries, China is entitled to independently decide whether to issue a visa to foreign citizens or not in accordance with its domestic laws and policies as a sovereign country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1512276.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1512312.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-11-21","Lu Kang","","According to the Australian media, negotiations between Australia and the Taiwan authority on a \"free trade agreement\"have been on hold for many years because of pressure from the Chinese mainland and Australia's reluctance to offend the mainland. What is your response? Some members of the Australian parliament believed that though Australia has already signed a Free Trade Agreement (FTA) with the Chinese…","We firmly oppose any official contacts and exchanges between the countries having diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan authority. We firmly oppose their negotiating and signing of any official agreements with sovereign implications as well. We hope that the relevant country will fully grasp how sensitive and complicated the Taiwan issue is, stick to the one-China principle, and properly handle the relevant issue with caution.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1512680.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1512685.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-11-23","Lu Kang","","First, as far as we learn, China and the Vatican plan to hold two joint art exhibitions next year. The Vatican calls it the \"diplomacy of art\", which some compare to Richard Nixon's Ping-Pong diplomacy preceding his visit to China in 1972. How do you respond to such comparison? Second, according to reports, the Chinese government has recently banned tourist groups from traveling to the Vatican and Palau. Some…","I have not heard of what you mentioned in your second question.\nOn your first question, I have noted the relevant reports. We are not aware of the details by far. China's position on how to develop its relations with the Vatican is consistent and clear. China is willing to continue to have constructive dialogue with the Vatican and advance the improvement of the relations between the two sides on principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1513437.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1513447.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2017-11-24","Wu Qian","深圳卫视直通港澳台","I am a reporter from Shenzhen Satellite TV's Direct Broadcast to Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. I would like to ask Vice Mayor Liu Yingzi about volunteers for the Military World Games. How many volunteers will this edition of the Military World Games recruit? What are the sources and composition of the volunteers? We all know that the volunteer service for the Military World Games mainly serves military athletes…","Wuhan is a city of volunteers, with a million university students, and volunteer service has a broad mass base in this city. The Wuhan Military World Games plans to recruit 50,000 event volunteers. They will mainly come from troops and officers and soldiers, mature volunteer organizations, and university students in the Wuhan area. We will also recruit some international volunteers. In addition, we have at least 200,000 city volunteers.\nVolunteer service for the Military World Games has three characteristics. The first is having a “military flavor.” The Military World Games’ greatest feature is “military flavor.” Most of the volunteers serving the military athletes come from troops and military academies. At the same time, for non-military volunteers, we also hope they will have the spirit of soldiers, the same ability to endure hardship and fight hard battles, and the quality of strictly observing discipline. The second is greater professionalism. The “professional” feature will be reflected in three aspects. One is selecting the best from the best during recruitment, choosing outstanding volunteers with relevant expertise and experience in city volunteer work. The second is systematic training, including training on the Military World Games, the spirit of volunteering, and job-specific skills. The third is practical drills. Starting in 2016, large-scale cultural and sports events in Wuhan have been incorporated into the “Accompanying the Military Games” series of activities, and every event has been a live exercise. The third feature is greater fashion. We believe volunteering is not only dedication but also a lifestyle that young people pursue. The slogan for Wuhan Military World Games volunteers is “Make volunteering a fashion.” In our volunteer culture, there will be more fashionable elements that young people like.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2017-11/24/content_4798328.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2017-11-29","Geng Shuang","","Lee Ming-che was sentenced to five years in jail for \"subverting state power\". The US and the EU have called on China to release him at an early date so that he could be reunited with his family. How do you respond to that?","The spokesperson with the Office for Taiwan Affairs of the State Council already gave a fairly adequate response to this question. I would like to stress that China is a country governed by law, and we hope relevant parties will respect China's judicial sovereignty rather than interfere in China's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1515157.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1515042.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear media friends, good morning. I will now take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","央视记者","The latest public opinion poll from Taiwan media shows that public opinion on the island has undergone a major shift: the proportion supporting unification has risen, the proportion leaning toward “Taiwan independence” has fallen, impressions of the mainland have become more positive, and many people have an increasingly strong willingness to work and study on the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment on…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters with a shared destiny, one family bound by blood. The great achievements the mainland has made and the policies it pursues toward Taiwan have led more and more Taiwan residents to recognize that our efforts to promote the well-being of Taiwan compatriots are sincere; that compatriots on both sides form a community of shared destiny; that the mainland's development is not a threat to Taiwan but an opportunity; and that “Taiwan independence” harms the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. Maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, expanding economic and cultural exchanges across the Strait, and advancing integrated economic and social development across the Strait are conducive to enhancing Taiwan's own well-being. We believe that as the mainland prospers and advances, this trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171129_11874036.htm"],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The grand final of the first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League will soon be held in Shenzhen. Please introduce the relevant situation. Recently, what other important sports exchange activities have there been between the two sides of the Strait? Please also introduce them.","The grand final of the first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League will be held in Shenzhen, Guangdong, from December 1 to 6. Teams from 32 primary, secondary, and tertiary schools on both sides of the Strait will take part, with 64 games in total. Since the league started this year, from the preliminary round to the re-match and then to the grand final, it has spanned many cities on both sides of the Strait and drawn participation from more than 100 primary, secondary, and tertiary schools on both sides. It is a youth baseball event that has received wide attention, and a grand festival of cross-Strait youth sports exchange. Shenzhen has made all the necessary preparations and has put forward the slogan “A Great City, Great Sport,” and welcomes the baseball boys from both sides of the Strait!\nIn addition, it is our understanding that the final of the first Cross-Strait Martial Arts Exchange Competition will be held in Beijing on December 2. The competition will combine online and on-site competition. As of now, more than 5,000 people from Beijing, Tianjin, Hebei, and other provinces and municipalities, as well as Taiwan, have registered, and more than 10,000 are expected to take part by the end of the event. Of these, nearly 100 teams with about 800 people from Taiwan have signed up. The online platform has received 150,000 likes and endorsements, and 120 Taiwan athletes have advanced to the final stage. At that time, they will gather in the capital with martial artists from across the mainland to exchange skills, make friends through martial arts, and jointly promote traditional Chinese martial arts culture and Chinese martial ethics.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171129_11874037.htm"],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The Kuang-fu case has recently drawn attention on the island. Some voices on the island question whether the Kuang-fu company made large investments on the mainland and transferred a large amount of assets to the mainland. Is the spokesperson aware of the relevant situation?","I am not aware of the situation you describe. We have also noticed that the Qingfu case, which has been hyped up on the island recently, can only have its truth found within Taiwan itself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan media reported that at the Cross-Strait Young Scholars Forum held in Shanghai, Taiwanese scholars attending collectively avoided Lu Li-an's welcoming remarks. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of this situation?","Some reports by individual Taiwan media are irresponsible and have ulterior motives. We understand that on November 18, the Taiwan Research Center of Fudan University and the Taiwan Research Institute in Shanghai jointly held the Cross-Strait Young Scholars Forum and the Third Young Scholars Forum of Fudan University. More than ten experts and scholars from National Taiwan University, National Chengchi University, National Cheng Kung University, and the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research attended. Cross-Strait scholars conducted discussions on topics such as “the 19th Party Congress’s policy statements on Taiwan and their impact on cross-Strait relations,” with lively interaction and a good atmosphere. During the event, some Taiwan scholars did not attend the opening ceremony or the group photo, but there was no so-called “collective avoidance.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The Lee Ming-che case received its first-instance verdict yesterday in Hunan, attracting great attention from island media. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this matter?","On the morning of November 28, the Yueyang Intermediate People’s Court in Hunan Province, in accordance with the law, handed down a first-instance verdict in the case of Peng Yuhua and Li Mingzhe for subversion of state power. Peng and Li both stated in court that they accept the verdict and will not appeal. The court arranged for live video footage of the trial and sentencing to be broadcast throughout. After the verdict, the court arranged for the two defendants to meet separately with their families.\nI must point out that in the investigation and trial of this case, mainland law enforcement authorities strictly followed the law and legal procedures, and handed down the verdict strictly based on the facts, nature, circumstances and degree of social harm of the crimes, fully protecting the lawful rights and interests of the defendants.\nI must stress once again that the mainland is a society governed by the rule of law. Any organization or individual in the mainland must respect and abide by the mainland’s laws and social public order, and those who violate the law will be held accountable. Any attempt to use this case for political hype or to stir up hostility between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171129_11874034.htm"],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Li Mingzhe should be the first Taiwan person sentenced for the crime of subverting state power. In addition to a five-year fixed-term sentence, he was also deprived of political rights for two years. May I ask the spokesperson: what political rights do Taiwan residents enjoy on the mainland? Second question: After the verdict, the Taiwan side said it was “completely unacceptable” and that “the verdict seriously…","Regarding the trial and verdict in the Lee Ming-che case, I would like to stress several more points. First, Lee Ming-che committed the crime of subverting state power. The facts of the crime are clear, the evidence is conclusive and sufficient, and the acts were organized, planned, and carried out. Some people in Taiwan ignore the facts and blindly attack the mainland, and that is what seriously harms cross-Strait relations. Whether Lee Ming-che's actions endangered the security and stability of the mainland should be determined by mainland law, not by the subjective prejudices of the Taiwan authorities and certain political organizations.\nSecond, mutual respect for each side's choice of development path and social system is the basic bottom line for developing cross-Strait relations. We respect Taiwan's existing social system and the way of life of Taiwan compatriots, but this does not mean that the Taiwan side may impose its political ideas on the mainland, nor does it mean that some individuals in Taiwan may arbitrarily violate mainland law under the banner of “democracy and freedom.” I believe the vast majority of Taiwan residents will have this kind of “empathy.”\nThird, for historical reasons, the two sides have chosen different development paths. As for how things are going in Taiwan society under DPP authorities, I believe Taiwan residents have their own first-hand experience and judgment. On the mainland, under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, socialism with Chinese characteristics has achieved accomplishments that have drawn worldwide attention. Political, economic, social, cultural, and ecological civilization construction has advanced across the board, people's living standards have improved greatly, and international standing and influence have risen markedly. The Chinese nation has made a great leap from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, and is closer to the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation than at any time in history. Facts have proven that the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics that we follow best serves the fundamental interests of the broad masses of the people, enjoys their sincere support, and has led more and more Taiwan compatriots to view the mainland with an objective and rational perspective.\nAt present, we are working hard, following the development blueprint drawn up at the 19th Party Congress, to achieve the two centenary goals and, by the middle of this century, build a modern socialist country that is prosperous, strong, democratic, culturally advanced, harmonious, and beautiful. We are confident about the future development of cross-Strait relations.\nAs for the other question you raised, according to regulations, Taiwan compatriots holding valid documents may travel to the mainland normally. The reason some individuals cannot enter should be clear to them. Here I still want to emphasize that when Lee Ming-che's family members traveled to Yueyang to attend the sentencing, the Taiwan side had accompanying personnel.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The cross-Strait “Three Financial Regulators” meeting mechanism, that is, the regulatory cooperation meeting among the banking, securities, futures, and insurance regulators, has been suspended for nearly two years. Recently, a responsible person of Taiwan's relevant authorities said that dialogue across the Strait could be conducted on the principle of equality, without restriction to form or venue. May I ask…","I have not heard of any arrangement of the kind you mentioned. Last year, major changes took place in Taiwan's political situation, and the cross-Strait communication, consultation and negotiation mechanisms were interrupted. Exchanges between the heads of cross-Strait financial regulatory authorities were also affected and impacted. The reasons are well known.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171129_11874032.htm"],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Recently, some media on the island have hyped the so-called “PLA aircraft circling Taiwan four times a week” issue. After checking the data, one will find that the “circling Taiwan” claim is quite far-fetched. How does the spokesperson view this practice of artificially creating cross-strait tension?","It is understood that the recent activities of PLA military aircraft were planned, routine training. For specific questions, please consult the Ministry of National Defense. I believe the greatest guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is opposing “Taiwan independence,” adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” and pursuing the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","We note that the Taiwanese flight attendant of Xiamen Airlines has recently officially begun flying, marking the first batch of trainees from the Taiwan Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Base officially entering the workforce. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this?","In recent years we have taken various measures to actively provide convenience for compatriots in Taiwan, especially young people from Taiwan, to study, start businesses, find jobs and live on the mainland. I think Xiamen Airlines actively implemented the central government's policies toward Taiwan, and took the lead in putting into service the flight attendants it recruited from Taiwan. This is a development worth welcoming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The third Cross-Strait Media Summit Beijing was recently held in Beijing. We have noted that journalists from both sides of the Strait jointly recalled and reviewed the 30-year course of cross-Strait news exchange. May I ask the spokesperson for your evaluation of the 30th anniversary of cross-Strait news exchange? What are your expectations for future cross-Strait news exchange?","This year marks 30 years since cross-Strait exchanges began, and of course also 30 years since cross-Strait news exchanges began. Over these 30 years, cross-Strait news exchanges have grown from nothing to something and from small to large, from one-way to two-way. Exchange channels have gradually widened, content has continuously been enriched, and forms have become increasingly diverse. Good results of cooperation have been achieved in many areas, including personnel exchanges, mutual visits, exchange of articles, supply of content and layouts, joint reporting, cooperative filming, program imports, and talent development. Under the new circumstances of cross-Strait relations, especially in the era of converged media, we hope that media professionals on both sides of the Strait will take the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation as their direction, report cross-Strait information more promptly and objectively, continuously enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, report more on stories of exchange and cooperation among compatriots, promote heartfelt connection between compatriots on both sides, better jointly promote Chinese culture, strengthen and enlarge the discourse power of the Chinese nation, and create a favorable public opinion environment for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201711/t20171129_11874033.htm"],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The cross-Strait high school Chinese-language textbooks jointly compiled by the Cross-Strait Cultural Development Research Center of Fujian Normal University, the School of Literature of Fujian Normal University, and the Taiwan Chinese Cultural Education Association have been used by high schools in Taipei since this semester, and have been welcomed by teachers and students. However, some “Taiwan independence”…","The so-called “united front” claim is baseless. Cross-strait culture shares the same roots and origins, and the profound Chinese culture has taken deep root on both sides of the Strait and is gaining increasingly broad recognition around the world. Against this backdrop, in recent years exchanges and cooperation in education across the Strait have continued to strengthen and achieved some gratifying results. We affirm and support anything that helps jointly inherit and promote excellent Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the Lee Ming-che case, after the verdict some analysts in Taiwan argued that it sends a very tough signal from the mainland toward Taiwan. How do you view such commentary?","First, we govern the country according to law, and the trial of Lee Ming-che’s (李明哲) case fully reflected the spirit of governing the country by law. Second, I must reiterate that the various policies toward Taiwan determined by the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China have not changed, and we will continue to implement them in all areas of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, during the visit of the President of Panama to China, he said that the establishment of diplomatic ties between Panama and China would set an example for Taiwan's so-called “diplomatic allies” in Latin America. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","The One-China principle is a general consensus of the international community. Adhering to the One-China principle is also what the people want and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The 54th Golden Horse Awards ceremony was held in Taipei on November 25. Mainland filmmakers won several important awards. Some commentators point out that interaction between the two sides in the film industry continues, while political relations have stalled or even regressed because the Taiwan authorities have never acknowledged the “1992 Consensus.” What is the spokesperson’s evaluation?","In recent years, as the mainland’s cultural undertakings have continued to develop and progress, it is no longer news that mainland films win awards at various international and regional film exhibitions and festival events. Our attitude is consistent: we encourage cross-Strait cultural exchanges, we are pleased to see cross-Strait filmmakers strengthen exchanges and deepen understanding, and we jointly promote Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, in a speech at Soochow University, Ma Ying-jeou said that unification is not decided by politicians but must be decided by the people on both sides of the Strait. How do you view this statement?","Achieving reunification across the Taiwan Strait is the common aspiration of all Chinese people and fundamental to the interests of the Chinese nation. Of course, we believe the people are the driving force of history, so on the question of national reunification, we place our hopes in the people of Taiwan. At the same time, I think Taiwan's political figures should at the very least not engage in acts that obstruct reunification, and certainly not engage in acts that split the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The Taiwan legislature voted to abolish the so-called “Organic Act of the Mongolian and Tibetan Affairs Commission.” Commentators say this is another new step toward “de-Sinicization.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Cross-Strait relations are not a “state-to-state relationship.” This legal basis and this reality cannot be changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Second question: recently we saw that the Ministry of Commerce released statistical data showing that from January to September this year, Taiwan businesses’ investment in the mainland grew substantially, up 37% year on year. However, the relevant Taiwan statistics show the opposite. May I ask for your comment?","Since the 18th National Congress, the mainland has deepened reform and expanded opening up, and has introduced a series of policies and measures to encourage and support Taiwan businesses and enterprises in developing on the mainland. These have created favorable conditions for Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest, start businesses, and put down roots on the mainland, and have opened up new space. As a result, Taiwan business investment has continued to maintain good momentum. Regarding the discrepancies in the statistical data you mentioned, they may be related to inconsistencies in the statistical methods of the two sides. For specific business questions, please consult the commerce authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Randall Schriver, the incoming US Assistant Secretary of Defense for Asia-Pacific Affairs, recently said that the United States has its own “One China Policy,” and that the reciprocal visits of US and Taiwan warships fully conform to the US “One China policy.” What is the spokesperson's comment? In addition, Japan is currently pushing forward the CPTPP with full force, and rumor on the island has it that the Tsai…","First question: Adhering to the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, the political foundation for developing China-US relations, and the cornerstone of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The US side's adherence to the one-China principle is in the common interest of both China and the United States. We firmly oppose the development of US-Taiwan military relations. People on the US side should fully recognize that the Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations, and should not do anything that undermines the overall situation of China-US relations.\nSecond question: We firmly oppose any of our diplomatic partners developing official exchanges with Taiwan or signing agreements of a sovereign implication and official nature. As for certain matters in Taiwan's domestic economic policy, we will not comment. I think the Taiwan public and public opinion have their own comments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-11-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Not long ago, Yu Weiguo, Party Secretary and Governor of Fujian Province, said that Fujian will take the lead in promoting basically equal treatment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and mainland enterprises, and for Taiwan residents and mainland residents. May I ask the spokesperson whether Fujian will become a pilot area for equal treatment of cross-Strait residents in the future?","At present, localities and departments are thoroughly implementing the spirit of the 19th Party Congress work on Taiwan. In particular, they are gradually providing Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment and living on the mainland, enhancing the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and advancing the integrated economic and social development of both sides of the Strait. The Fujian Provincial Party Committee and Provincial Government have taken the lead in implementing this and are at the forefront. We support them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201711/t20171129_11874030.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2017-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan military claimed on Nov. 23 that such PLA military aircraft as H-6K bombers conducted a far-sea training exercise crossing over the “island chain” and some aircraft returned to their home base from their original flight course after passing over the Bashi Channel and flying to the Western Pacific. Taiwan military’s vessels and aircraft followed and monitored the whole process according to regulations.…","I have answered this question many times. Taiwan is a part of China. The training as you mentioned is within the annual training plan. Similar training will be conducted in future.\nI also noted that you had mentioned the word “island chain” several times in your question. I want to emphasize here that no chain can chain China.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-11/30/content_4798766.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","First, the Chinese military aircraft conducted frequent distant waters training recently and circled Taiwan. The Taiwan military claimed that some military aircraft of China’s mainland entered the air defense identification zone of Taiwan and flew away shortly afterwards. Could you please confirm?\nSecond, officials from the U.S.Department of Defensesaid that two days before U.S. President Trump’s visit to China,…","As to your first question, I have made our stance very clear and I would not restate it.\nAbout your second question, it is a normal practice for China to develop missiles as scheduled and it is not against any specific country, region or target. We always follow our national defense policy which is defensive in nature and a military strategy of active defense. We develop weapons and armament only to meet our need of national security.\nAbout the THAAD question, actually China’s stance of firmly opposing the deployment of the THAAD system has never changed. Recently, the diplomatic branches of the two countries have reached consensus on discussing issues related to the THAAD system. I should say it is up to the doer to undo the knot. And the fundamental solution to the issue is to stop deploying the THAAD system and remove the equipment. And the Chinese military will take its due measures to firmly safeguard national security.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-11/30/content_4798766.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2017-12-07","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, December 7 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan told reporters on the 7th that Yu Muming, Chairman of the New Party, at the invitation of the party, will lead a New Party delegation to the mainland, visiting Beijing, Nanjing, and Shanghai successively from December 9 to 16, to hold discussions and exchanges with the mainland on promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, jointly pursuing the peaceful reunification of the motherland, and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171207_11876888.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-12-08","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, on December 7, Taiwan and the Philippines signed seven cooperation documents, including one on investment protection agreement. The Philippines is the first to sign such agreement among those whom Taiwan's \"New Southward Policy\" is targeted. What's your comment on this? It is reported that China has lodged representations with the Philippines for this reason. Can you confirm that?","China sees no objection to a country that has diplomatic ties with China conducting normal economic, trade and people-to-people exchanges with Taiwan, but does firmly oppose it conducting with Taiwan any form of official engagement or signing any agreement or cooperation document with sovereign implication.\nWe express grave concern over the signing of the investment protection agreement and other cooperation documents that are obviously official in character between the relevant Philippine authority and the Taiwan authority. China has lodged representation with the Philippine side. We hope the Philippines will abide by the one-China principle and avoid having the Taiwan-related issue undermine the larger picture of China-Philippines relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346213.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1517837.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-11","Lu Kang","","According to media reports, a Chinese diplomat in the United States on Friday said that if the US military has ships that visit Taiwan as authorized in the 2018 US defense bill, then China would take Taiwan by force. Does China stand by this?","The position of the Chinese government on the Taiwan issue, which I believe you and all the journalists here are quite clear about, is consistent and clear. We will continue adhering to the policy of \"peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" in an effort to advance the peaceful development of cross-straits relations and promote the process of peaceful reunification of our motherland. Meanwhile, we will firmly uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity and never tolerate the recurrence of the historical tragedy of national division.\nI also want to stress that China always opposes official exchanges and military contact of any form between the United States and Taiwan. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and three China-US joint communiqués and the US must prudentially and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1518491.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1518396.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-13","Lu Kang","","According to reports, yesterday US Secretary of State Tillerson specifically said that the US has talked to China about the need to secure the DPRK’s nuclear weapons in the event of a collapsed state or some huge upheaval. The US troops would go into the DPRK to secure these weapons with the pledge to retreat to the ROK after securing these weapons. What is China’s position on this? How did China respond to what…","Regarding the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue, while keeping firmly in mind the goal of denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula, we always stay committed to upholding peace and stability of the Peninsula and resolving the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue through dialogue and negotiation. It is based on this consistent position that we have been explicitly emphasizing in our communication and coordination with various parties that no war or conflict is allowed on the Korean Peninsula. This position is very clear.\nAs to the specifics of Secretary of State Tillerson’s remarks you just mentioned, I wonder whether you remember that the US reaffirmed their “Four Nos” promise several times, namely, not seeking a regime change, not seeking a collapse of the regime, not seeking an accelerated reunification of the peninsula and not seeking an excuse to send the US military north of the 38th Parallel.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1519191.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1519154.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear journalist friends, hello. Welcome to today's regular press conference of the TAO. I am happy to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","新华社记者","A New Party delegation is currently visiting the mainland. Could the spokesperson introduce the main situation and outcomes of this trip?","At the invitation of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Affairs Office, on December 9, Yu Mu-ming, Chairman of the New Party, led a New Party mainland visiting delegation to Beijing, Nanjing, and Shanghai. On December 11, Yu Zhengsheng, Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, met with the visiting delegation and expressed appreciation for the New Party's clear attitude and firm stance since its founding: consistently upholding the One China principle, advocating peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait, actively promoting cross-Strait exchanges, and resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence.” Chairman Yu introduced relevant information on the 19th CPC National Congress and expounded the Taiwan policies and our position on major cross-Strait issues determined by the 19th Congress.\nDuring their stay in Beijing, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office held a discussion with the visiting delegation. Both sides conducted in-depth exchanges on promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, working together for peaceful reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Both sides agreed that they must firmly uphold the One China principle, resolutely oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist actions, strive to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification, and jointly work toward the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Both sides agreed to establish and improve a liaison and communication mechanism, and to promptly exchange views and study major issues concerning relations between the two parties and cross-Strait relations, in order to build consensus. Both sides will uphold the concept of “both sides of the Strait are one family,” strive to promote exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, strengthen services for compatriots on both sides, and promptly communicate and handle matters involving the rights and interests of the public. They will further expand cross-Strait youth exchanges and create convenient conditions for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland. Together they will promote Chinese culture and foster spiritual connection among compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nEngaging in dialogue and exchanges with parties, groups, and individuals in Taiwan that uphold the One China principle and the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” in order to maintain and advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, is our consistent position. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, the CPC Central Taiwan Affairs Office strengthening dialogue and exchanges with the New Party, and enhancing mutual trust, is of positive significance for promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171213_11878743.htm"],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","中新社记者","You just introduced the exchanges with the New Party. Could you again introduce the exchanges with the Kuomintang and other parties on the island?","For a long time, we and the Kuomintang have maintained regular contact and exchanges on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Just yesterday, our office received a delegation from the Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Association of China led by Zeng Wenpei, Standing Committee member of the Kuomintang Central Committee and chairman of the association. The delegation had 24 members, including 21 members of the Kuomintang Central Committee and 3 party representatives.\nZhang Zhijun, Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, met with the delegation, briefed them on the 19th CPC National Congress, and focused on explaining the main spirit of the 19th CPC National Congress regarding Taiwan work. Zhang Zhijun also exchanged views with the delegation on further strengthening exchanges and cooperation between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party. Both sides hope that the two parties will maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn the same day, Liu Jieyi, Deputy Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, also met with all members of the delegation. Liu Jieyi said that the mainland side actively encourages grassroots and young people across both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchanges, and will continue to take measures in keeping with the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” gradually providing Taiwan compatriots studying, starting businesses, working and living on the mainland with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots. He hoped that young elites of the Kuomintang would play a positive role in promoting exchanges among cross-Strait youth and other sectors.\nIn addition, the leader of the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union will also hold exchanges with our office in the near future to exchange views on matters related to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171213_11878742.htm"],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently the Taiwan legislature passed partial amendments to the so-called “Referendum Act.” Please give your assessment.","We have repeatedly stated that we firmly oppose any force, in any manner, including through so-called referendums, engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities or opening the door for them. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should remain highly vigilant.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171213_11878740.htm"],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Reports say the Chinese minister to the United States recently stated that the day a US warship arrives in Kaohsiung is the day the PLA will use force to unify Taiwan. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant position and attitude?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on this. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan. I must emphasize that any conduct that presumes on foreign support to advance its own interests and seeks to harm China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity will certainly be jointly opposed by all Chinese people and will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171213_11878737.htm"],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Recently, Taiwanese media reported that personnel of the mainland’s Taiwan Affairs system who travel to Taiwan were all required to sign a so-called “binding agreement” agreeing to the so-called “four nots” principle: during their stay in Taiwan they must not make political statements, must not accept media interviews, must not engage in so-called united front activities, and must not meet privately with…","Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, the mainland side, adhering to the concept of “Cross-Strait families are one family,” continues to actively promote civil exchange and cooperation across the Strait in all fields, enhancing the kinship and welfare of compatriots on both sides. In contrast, the DPP authorities have consistently used political reasons to interfere with and restrict cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, creating obstacles to exchanges and inciting hostility and confrontation across the Strait. Comparing the two, everyone should see very clearly who is upholding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and who is interfering with and undermining it.\nThis year marks the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait exchanges. The development over these thirty years shows that the desire for exchange, cooperation and development is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides, the wish of the people, and the trend of the times. It is something that no person or force can easily stop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Since the 19th Party Congress, PLA military aircraft have frequently conducted drills around Taiwan. Given the current insufficient political mutual trust across the Taiwan Strait, should military mutual trust mechanisms across the Strait be established first to avoid accidental conflict?","We have stated repeatedly that the recent mainland military aircraft activities are planned, routine training. As for the question you raised afterward: as is well known, the current political impasse in cross-Strait relations is due to the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and to recognize that both sides belong to one China, so that the foundation and premise of the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms no longer exist. “If the skin is gone, where can the fur attach?” Under these circumstances, establishing military mutual trust mechanisms through cross-Strait negotiations is out of the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","The Taiwan legislature recently passed the “Act on Promoting Transitional Justice,” which has caused wide controversy on the island. What is your assessment?","We have also noted that this matter has sparked wide controversy in Taiwan society. I must emphasize here that we firmly oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, including “de-Sinicization” activities carried out under various pretexts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171213_11878739.htm"],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","The Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League recently concluded its 10th National Congress, at which Su Hui was elected Chairperson of the 10th Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League. She stated that she would implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" and be a promoter of the peaceful reunification of the…","As everyone knows, the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League is a democratic party composed of Taiwan-origin people residing on the mainland, which has long taken the peaceful reunification of the motherland as its goal. Here, we also congratulate Chairman Su Hui on his election. We also hope that the Taiwan League can continue to give play to its distinctive features and advantages, unite broad Taiwan compatriots, jointly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and advance the development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","Taiwan's 2017 character-of-the-year vote results are out, and “茫” (mang, meaning confused or vague) has become the new character of the year. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","We have also noted this selection result. As commentary within Taiwan has put it, this result also reflects the genuine feelings of Taiwan residents over the past year, and their genuine feelings about cross-Strait relations and the future development of Taiwan. There is an old Chinese saying, \"People do things, and heaven watches.\" The common people have their own scales in their hearts. What kind of influence and consequences the words and deeds of the Taiwan authorities and the DPP have brought to Taiwan society and its people, we believe, the people of Taiwan have their own feelings and judgments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan middle schools' use of Chinese-language textbooks co-compiled by both sides of the Strait has come under pressure from the Green camp. What is your comment?","Cross-Strait culture shares common roots and origins. Education circles on both sides of the Strait jointly compiling Chinese-language textbooks helps both sides jointly inherit and carry forward excellent traditional Chinese culture. What crime is there in this?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Some Taiwan media reported that Fujian will introduce relevant policy measures to provide corresponding subsidies to Taiwan compatriots who come to Fujian for the first time or take up employment in Fujian, and to award exemplary Taiwan youth entrepreneurship teams. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of the relevant situation?","I am not aware of the situation you mention. As the province closest to Taiwan, Fujian has in recent years taken the lead in introducing a number of policies and measures to encourage and support Taiwanese youth to work and start businesses in Fujian. It provides policy support for Taiwanese youth's employment and entrepreneurship, creates a good environment, and helps resolve some existing difficulties and problems, in order to enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nGoing forward, we will continue to implement the spirit of the 19th Party Congress, study and introduce policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, and gradually provide Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in study, entrepreneurship, employment and daily life on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We noted that New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming said that Taiwan has suffered severe internal attrition in recent years while the mainland has continued to develop and grow; in the past, people hoped for the Taiwanese people, but now some Taiwanese hope more for the mainland. How does the spokesperson view this statement and this change?","Realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people. The key factor determining the direction of cross-Strait relations is the development and progress of the mainland of China. Under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, the cause of socialism with Chinese characteristics has achieved world-renowned accomplishments. The Chinese nation has ushered in a great leap from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, and it is closer than at any period in history to the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Currently, under the magnificent blueprint outlined by the 19th Party Congress, we are working hard to achieve the “two centenary goals” and to build, by the mid-21st century, a modern socialist country that is prosperous, strong, democratic, culturally advanced, harmonious and beautiful. We are full of confidence in the future.\nThe development and construction achievements of the mainland in recent years, and the sincerity and goodwill shown in its policies toward Taiwan, combined with the current comparison of cross-Strait development, have led more and more Taiwan people to view the mainland with an objective and rational outlook. This has enabled Taiwan people to realize that the mainland's policies and attitudes toward Taiwan are sincere; that mainland development is an opportunity for Taiwan rather than a threat; and that promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is beneficial to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, while pursuing “Taiwan independence” would harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. I believe that as the mainland continues to develop and progress, this trend will continue to develop further.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-13","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that there is currently regular contact and communication with the KMT. May I ask whether a KMT-CPC forum could be held soon? In addition, will KMT Chairman Wu Den-yih also, following the example of New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming, lead a KMT delegation to visit the mainland?","When I was introducing our exchanges with the KMT and other parties on the island just now, I also mentioned that for a long time, the CPC and the Kuomintang have maintained contact and communication, strengthened exchanges and dialogue, and jointly promoted the development of relations between the two parties and cross-Strait relations on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” This has safeguarded peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and enhanced the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. As for the specific situation you mentioned, I do not have information on it at present. If there is definite news, we will release it promptly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171213_11878736.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-12-14","Lu Kang","","US President Donald Trump signed into law the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2018, which considers the possibility of port visit to Taiwan by US military ships among other non-legally binding provisions. Do you have a comment on that law?","Although those Taiwan-related clauses of this act are not legally binding, they severely violate the one China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiques and constitute an interference in China's internal affairs. China always firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the US government.\nWe need to reiterate that the one China principle serves as the political foundation of China-US relations. China firmly opposes all forms of official exchange and military contact between the US and Taiwan as well as the US arms sales to Taiwan. We urge the US to fully recognize the severity of the damage the Taiwan-related clauses may cause and properly handle the Taiwan-related issue in accordance with the one China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiques lest it should jeopardize the larger interests of China-US cooperation and cross-straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1519590.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1519511.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-14","Lu Kang","","据报道，美国总统特朗普签署了“2018财年国防授权法案”，其中包含“评估美台军舰互访的可能性”等没有约束力的涉台条款。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1519590.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1519511.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2017-12-18","Hua Chunying","","According to media reports, on December 16, the Spanish court made the ruling that the 121 telecommunication fraud suspects from mainland and Taiwan that were arrested in Spain at the end of last year will be extradited to China. The court said that Spain accepts the one-China principle. What is your comment on this?","The Chinese side welcomes the above-mentioned ruling made by the Spanish court. This is an important outcome of the cooperation conducted by China and Spain in combating crimes in accordance with the extradition treaty. China highly appreciates that the Spanish side adheres to the one-China principle and decided to extradite the Taiwan suspects to China. The police from China and Spain maintain close cooperation in jointly combating China-related telecommunication fraud crimes. We are willing to work with the Spanish side to earnestly safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of the people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1520413.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1520324.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-18","Hua Chunying","","It is reported that on the map of the people's dictionary published by Japan's Iwanami bookstore, Taiwan is marked as a province of the People's Republic of China. The \"Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office\" in Japan asks Iwanami bookstore to correct this mistake. What is your comment?","Isn't Taiwan a province of China? It is known to us that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1520413.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1520324.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-19","Hua Chunying","","The US National Security Strategic Report mentioned \"we will maintain our strong ties with Taiwan in accordance with our one-China policy\". What is your comment on this?","The position held by the Chinese government on the Taiwan issue is consistent and clear-cut. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués and properly handle the Taiwan-related issues, thus avoiding disturbing the overall picture of China-US cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1520766.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1520714.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-12-19","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter’s question: Regarding the search of the residences of four New Party members, including Wang Bing-zhong, by Taiwan’s police and investigation departments on the 19th and the taking away of the people, what is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 19 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions, said: We are highly attentive to this matter. As is well known, the New Party has consistently adhered to the one-China principle, firmly opposed “Taiwan independence,” advocated peaceful reunification of the two sides, and actively upheld and promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We highly appreciate this. For some time, the Taiwan authorities have shielded and condoned “Taiwan independence” separatists, and have adopted various means to arbitrarily suppress and persecute forces and individuals who advocate peaceful reunification across the Strait. We solemnly condemn this and are closely following relevant developments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171219_11880812.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-21","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 21 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions on the 21st, said: The Kenya cross-border telecom fraud case was publicly pronounced in a first-instance judgment in accordance with law by the Beijing No. 2 Intermediate People's Court on the 21st, and the judicial authority has released the relevant judgment information. During investigation and trial, the mainland judicial authorities strictly observed legal provisions and statutory procedures and fully guaranteed the defendants' litigation rights. Judgments were made in accordance with the law, based on the facts, nature, circumstances, and degree of social harm of the crimes. After the verdict was announced, relevant parties arranged a meeting with the family members who attended the hearing, at their request.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that for some time, telecom fraud cases led by criminal elements from Taiwan have occurred frequently. Compatriots on both sides have suffered greatly, and people on both sides of the Strait detest them deeply. The mainland judicial authorities' apprehension and prosecution of cross-border telecom fraud criminals is a righteous act that accords with popular will and protects rights. It has been fully affirmed and recognized by compatriots on both sides, and has also gained understanding and support from the international community. The mainland side, adhering to the position that it is conducive to fighting crime, conducive to safeguarding judicial justice, and conducive to protecting the rights and interests of victims, will resolutely punish telecom fraud crimes so as to effectively safeguard the interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171221_11881947.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2017-12-22","Hua Chunying","","According to media reports, yesterday, the ROK police uncovered a telecommunication fraud group which is composed of 51 people in Jeju Island. Most of them come from Taiwan and their targets include people from the mainland. Over the past one year and a half, the number of Taiwan telecommunication fraud suspects sent to the mainland by foreign countries is over 200. Does China hope that these suspects can be sent…","We have taken note of the relevant report. According to our information, this case is under investigation now. The Chinese Consulate-General in Jeju Island has contacted the ROK police to learn more about this case and verify the identities of the people involved.\nIn principle, we always require the countries that have established diplomatic ties with China to deal with the Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1521677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1521608.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-25","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, on December 21, a Taiwan official addressed the United Nations Internet Governance Forum (IGF) by video conferencing, which triggered protests from the representative of the Chinese mainland. What's your comment on this?","Our position is consistent and clear. The Taiwan region's participation in the activities of international organizations must abide by the one-China principle. The United Nations Internet Governance Forum is a mechanism for discussing internet governance under the UN framework. The Forum's Secretariat strictly follows the UN General Assembly's Resolution 2758 and observes the one-China principle.\nI shall also point out that any attempt to seek Taiwan independence on the international stage will end in nothing but failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1521984.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1521946.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2017-12-25","Hua Chunying","","According to Taiwan media, the Swedish Foreign Minister said when answering inquiries at the Riksdag that she is supportive of Taiwan's meaningful participation as a non-state actor in international organizations and is willing to continuously endorse Taiwan's attendance at expert meetings in the fields such as aviation security. On Taiwan's participation in the World Health Organization (WHO), she said that she…","I believe that when answering the question from the Taiwan \"Central News Agency\" just now, I have made our position clear on the issue of this sort. With regard to the participation of Taiwan as a region of China in the activities of international organizations, China's position on adhering to the one-China principle is consistent and clear. The Taiwan question belongs to China's internal affairs, and China firmly opposes other country in making irresponsible remarks in that regard.\nBefore we wrap up today's press conference, I have some sad news to tell you.\nYou may have learned that Mr. Ezzat Shahrour, the Beijing Bureau Chief for Al Jazeera Arabic, passed away on December 23 in Beijing due to illness. Mr. Ezzat Shahrour, who spent more than 20 years living and working in China, made positive contributions to helping people across the Arab world to better understand China and promoting China-Arab friendship. We express our deep sadness and grief over the passing of Mr. Ezzat Shahrour and sincere condolence to his family and relatives. The relevant Chinese department stands ready to help his family at this difficult time.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1521984.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1521946.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear journalist friends, good morning! Welcome to the TAO regular press conference. I am happy to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently four New Party figures were forcibly investigated by Taiwan's police and investigation departments, who searched their residences and took the individuals away. The Taiwan Affairs Office immediately expressed a solemn position, but Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council expressed dissatisfaction with this. What is the spokesperson's comment?","On the day of the incident, our office has already expressed a firm condemnation. Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of all Chinese people and lies at the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We highly commend the Taiwan political parties, groups, and individuals who uphold the one-China principle, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” advocate peaceful reunification of the two sides, and actively uphold and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The Taiwan authorities’ shielding and condoning of “Taiwan independence” separatists, and their suppression and persecution of forces and individuals advocating peaceful reunification, undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and naturally provoke strong indignation and shared opposition among people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171227_11884423.htm"],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Public opinion generally holds that recently, the Taiwan authorities have restricted cross-Strait exchanges in various ways, stirred up hostility between the two sides, suppressed and persecuted forces and individuals on the island who advocate peaceful unification, greatly lowered the threshold for referendums, and let “Taiwan independence” forces clamor for a “Taiwan independence constitutional amendment.”…","We have noted that Taiwan’s side has been very active recently. Everyone has seen that since May 20 of last year, because the Taiwan authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not recognize that both sides belong to one China, they have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation of cross-strait relations. This has had a severe impact on cross-strait relations, making the current situation increasingly complex and severe. Rather than considering how to improve cross-strait relations, the Taiwan authorities have persisted obstinately. On the one hand, they indulge and support “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island and carry out “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. On the other hand, they suppress and persecute forces and individuals on the island who support cross-strait exchanges and cooperation and advocate peaceful development and peaceful reunification of cross-strait relations. They interfere with and obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, incite hostility and confrontation between the two sides, and undermine the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. I must emphasize that any force, in any form, that pursues “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and practices will certainly be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides and will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171227_11884424.htm"],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中央电视台中国新闻记者","We have a question regarding the sentencing in the “Kenya fraud case.” After the sentencing of this case, public opinion in Taiwan is concerned about whether Taiwanese prisoners serving sentences can return to Taiwan to serve them. May I ask the spokesperson: what is the mainland's attitude on this issue?","In recent years, Taiwanese telecom fraud criminals have set up bases overseas and carried out telecom fraud against people on the mainland on a rampant scale, seriously harming the personal and property safety of mainland residents. Residents of the mainland deeply loathe this and have expressed that such criminals should be severely punished, that justice should be done for the victims, and that the legitimate rights and interests of mainland residents and victims should be earnestly protected. In fact, it is not only mainland residents; people in Taiwan also suffer greatly from telecom fraud. Everyone hopes these telecom fraud criminals will be brought to justice. However, what we see is that telecom fraud crimes on the island of Taiwan are growing increasingly severe. These telecom fraud criminals “defraud the world,” yet on the island they are treated leniently and do not receive due punishment. I have seen reports in Taiwanese media stating that, according to Taiwan’s statistics, from 2011 to October 2016, a total of 49,000 person-times were prosecuted on suspicion of telecom fraud. However, only 8 people were sentenced to more than five years in prison, less than two ten-thousandths. Not to mention that last year, 20 Taiwanese telecom fraud suspects brought back from Malaysia were announced as released on the spot at the airport. This scene, I believe, has left a very deep impression on everyone. What Taiwan should reflect on is why cross-border telecom fraud activities in Taiwan have been banned repeatedly yet continue to grow more severe. Where exactly does the problem lie?\nAs for the question you just raised, relevant departments on the mainland will handle it based on a position that is conducive to combating crime, conducive to safeguarding judicial fairness, and conducive to protecting the rights and interests of victims. Specific questions may be directed to the relevant departments for inquiry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171227_11884422.htm"],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Reportedly, KMT Vice Chairman Tseng Yung-chuan originally planned to visit the mainland in the near future, but his application was rejected by the Taiwan authorities and he cancelled the trip. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The current situation in cross-Strait relations is becoming more complicated and grim. The KMT and the CPC, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” strengthening exchange and cooperation helps maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promotes the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhances the well-being of compatriots on both sides. Yet the Taiwan authorities, on the one hand, restrict cross-Strait exchanges themselves, and on the other hand deprive others of the right to exchange. This practice of interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges does not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171227_11884419.htm"],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","I would like to verify: is the KMT-CPC Forum scheduled to be held in March or April of next year? Is there any new progress now? Does the fact that no KMT-CPC Forum was held this year mean that relations between the KMT and the CPC are not as close as before? In addition, KMT Chairman 吴敦义 recently attended an event where, when the crowd shouted “peaceful reunification,” he said that “peaceful reunification” is…","On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the Kuomintang and the Communist Party have maintained regular contact and communication. As for the specific circumstances of the forum you mentioned, the information will be made public once it is confirmed. As for your second question, the mainland’s position and attitude on resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the peaceful reunification of the motherland are very clear and consistent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台","First, could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation regarding the housing provident fund benefits available to Taiwan residents living on the mainland? In addition, some people are concerned that for personnel who do not plan to buy a house on the mainland, housing provident fund contributions may cause a certain degree of trouble for their benefits. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","To gradually realize equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland, as for mainland compatriots, relevant departments recently jointly issued the “Opinions on Housing Provident Fund Benefits for Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Compatriots Employed on the Mainland.” The specific contents of the above provisions can be viewed on the website of the Ministry of Housing and Urban-Rural Development.\nHere I would like to emphasize again: Taiwan compatriots employed on the mainland may all pay into the housing provident fund in accordance with relevant regulations. The individual contribution portion of the housing provident fund belongs to the employee personally and will not add extra expense, and it can be withdrawn and used through various channels. If you do not plan to buy a house on the mainland, you can also withdraw the housing provident fund to pay rent. The rights of Taiwan compatriots to withdraw and use the housing provident fund will be effectively protected. This is a good thing that benefits the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201712/t20171227_11884418.htm"],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台","Recently, Taiwan released its “National Defense Report White Paper,” which emphasized so-called “asymmetric” operations. A DPP legislator said that Taiwan now has the capability for one soldier to carry an explosive pack and blow up one mainland tank. We would like to know how the mainland views this statement.","We have repeatedly and clearly stated that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Under the current reality of increasingly lopsided strength between the two sides, pursuing confrontation and “refusing unification by force” has no way out. Only if the Taiwan side abandons the “Taiwan independence” position and hostile mindset can it truly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","According to reports, the mainland internet company Toutiao has used internet technology to help Taiwanese veterans find relatives on the mainland, and there have already been many successful cases. Please introduce the relevant situation.","With the rapid development of the internet, it has now become the “fourth link” connecting compatriots on both sides of the Strait, following the postal, air and trade links across the Strait. It has strengthened the family bonds of compatriots on both sides and enhanced their interests and welfare. We understand that Toutiao, a mainland internet company, has cooperated with Taiwanese media and, through precise internet push technology, published information seeking relatives for Taiwanese veterans, helping Taiwanese veterans find mainland relatives they had been separated from for many years. To date, more than 40 pieces of relevant information have been published, and 19 Taiwanese veterans have successfully been reunited with their mainland relatives. Tomorrow, that is, December 28, Toutiao will hold a launch event for the cross-Strait family-search project in Beijing. Reporters are welcome to attend and cover it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2018 Spring Festival is approaching again. Could you introduce the plans for cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights this year?","It is understood that, to meet the travel needs of cross-Strait passengers, especially the need of Taiwan compatriots to return home for the Spring Festival, cross-Strait business and technical personnel recently confirmed the arrangements for Spring Festival extra flights in 2018. Both sides agreed that cross-Strait airlines will arrange Spring Festival extra flights during the period from February 2 to March 2, 2018. The total number of extra flights is not restricted; only certain busy mainland airports have caps, namely round-trip flights of 16 for Beijing, 162 for Shanghai Pudong, 11 for Guangzhou, 23 for Shenzhen, and 44 for Hangzhou. Both sides plan to approve the first batch of Spring Festival extra flights before January 3, 2018, to facilitate passengers' seat booking and itinerary planning.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Kunshan has long been an important center of Taiwanese manufacturing. Recently, a suspension order caused many Taiwanese businesspeople great concern. Although it was later stated that it was only a notice and would not be implemented, facing increasingly strict environmental protection requirements, will the TAO take measures to guide Taiwanese businesses in upgrading and improving their operations?","After inquiring with Kunshan’s authorities, we understand that the relevant notice you mentioned has not been implemented. Next, the local government will strengthen monitoring of the relevant polluting enterprises, require enterprises to strictly implement their primary responsibility as pollution-discharging entities, strengthen the construction and operational management of pollution treatment facilities, and fulfill responsibilities for pollution control, emission reduction, and environmental risk prevention. We hope the relevant Taiwan enterprises can understand and support the measures taken by Kunshan’s municipal government to control pollution and protect the environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Regarding the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit. Besides air and high-speed rail travel, ticket purchase and ticket collection, what further convenience measures will there be in the future? How many card-type Taiwan compatriot permits have been reissued so far, according to statistics?","To provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland, the mainland began implementing a visa-free policy for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland on July 1, 2015, and from September 21, fully implemented the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit. Taiwan compatriots have generally given positive reviews of the substantial improvement in functionality and convenience of the card-type Taiwan compatriot permit, and the number of people applying for or exchanging for the card-type permit is increasing. It is understood that the relevant mainland departments have so far issued 2.69 million card-type Taiwan compatriot permits. In the next step, we will earnestly study ways to address the problem that the Taiwan compatriot permit cannot be recognized when relying on electronic and network technologies to provide social services, so as to provide more convenience for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视","Recently, Taiwan achieved “gate-crashing” via video at a certain UN meeting. What is your response to this incident?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on this. As is well known, the United Nations is an international organization composed of sovereign states, and it adheres to the one-China policy. Taiwan, using this abnormal means, is provoking the one-China principle generally upheld by the international community, attempting to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” in the international arena, and it thinks it has achieved something, amusing itself on the island. In reality, this is like a mayfly trying to shake a tree; it cannot in the slightest shake the one-China framework of the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报","Recently, media reported that the first phase of the project to pipe water from the mainland to Kinmen has been completed. Does the spokesperson have relevant information? Please comment on what significance this cross-strait people's livelihood project has for cross-strait relations.","Since the Fujian-to-Kinmen water supply project contract was officially signed on July 20, 2015, the mainland side has consistently promoted construction with the attitude and sincerity of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, sharing one river.” It is understood that the main works of the mainland section of the project have already been completed. We hope the Kinmen side will speed up construction so that water can be delivered as early as next year, benefiting the broad masses of Kinmen residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中国台湾网","Recently, the 2017 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year poll results were released, and the character “創” (chuang, meaning “create”) was selected as the new Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year. What is the spokesperson's evaluation? Second question: the renowned poet Yu Guangzhong passed away in Kaohsiung, Taiwan, on December 14. Mr. Yu created many poems. How does the spokesperson evaluate the role…","Your first question: the cross-Strait character of the year, jointly selected by media on both sides, is “创” (create). Previously, the character of the year selected by Taiwan's own media was “茫” (vast/confused). Comparing the two, one stands for entrepreneurship and innovation, facing the future with pioneering and enterprise; the other stands for confusion and vagueness, feeling lost when facing the future. This can also be seen as a true reflection of the personal experiences and feelings of people on both sides of the Strait in 2017, which is about to end.\nYour second question, regarding the passing of Mr. Yu Guangzhong: our office's spokesperson already expressed condolences the following day. Although Mr. Yu has passed away, his poems full of national sentiment, such as 《乡愁》, 《风铃》, 《寻李白》 and 《乡愁四韵》, will be recited by the world, and his active participation in cross-Strait cultural exchanges and his opposition to the cultural “Taiwan independence” activities will also be praised by later generations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","人民政协报记者","At the cross-Strait youth officials forum held in Taiwan on the 24th, affected by the incident involving Wang Bingzhong of the New Party, Taiwanese students did not dare to interact with mainland students, fearing that interacting with mainland students would lead to persecution under the so-called “National Security Law.” This incident has already triggered a chilling effect on the island. What is the…","I want to emphasize again that any actions to suppress or persecute forces and individuals who advocate peaceful reunification of the two sides will inevitably provoke strong indignation and joint opposition from the people on both sides of the Strait, and they cannot stop the trend of exchanges and interactions between the people of both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中评社记者","On the 17th, 18th, and 20th of this month, the PLA sent military aircraft to fly around Taiwan on consecutive days, and on the 17th released a propaganda video titled 《绕岛巡航》. May I ask the spokesperson what these moves signify? Will circling-the-island flights become routine going forward? In addition, New Party Chairman Yu Muming said yesterday that he will establish a “New Party Service Committee” to connect…","On your first question, the Ministry of National Defense and the TAO press conferences have repeatedly made clear that this is a planned, routine training exercise, and everyone will gradually get used to it. On your second question, we welcome and support the New Party playing a greater role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and serving compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Reports say that Didi Chuxing, China's largest ride-hailing platform, has begun recruiting drivers in Taiwan to join passenger services. Can the spokesperson confirm this? Does the spokesperson welcome this development?","I am not very familiar with this situation. Didi Chuxing is a one-stop, diversified travel platform that emerged on the mainland in the internet economy era, and many mainland residents have enjoyed convenient travel services through it. Strengthening cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in the internet economy helps advance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. It is a mutually beneficial, win-win matter and should be viewed with an even mind.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","团结报记者","In the past month, eight democratic parties successively held national congresses and elected new leaderships. The democratic parties have long been committed to promoting the great cause of peaceful reunification of the motherland. What expectations and views does the spokesperson have on the democratic parties’ future role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations?","We extend our congratulations to the new leadership teams of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, the Taiwan League, and other democratic parties following their leadership transitions. We also hope and believe that the democratic parties can continue to give play to their respective characteristics and strengths, unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","中国日报记者","After PLA aircraft resumed far-seas training, the DPP authorities became very nervous. Some Taiwan media have reported that Tsai Ing-wen will hold a year-end press conference at the end of this month, where she will certainly speak of so-called “defense autonomy.” In addition, some Taiwan officials have claimed that Tsai Ing-wen will transit through the United States again in January next year. What comment does…","First question: I have already answered this just now. Only peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can fundamentally safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Adopting confrontational practices of “resisting unification by force” is of no benefit to peace and stability across the Strait.\nSecond question: we have always handled Taiwan’s external activities in accordance with the one-China principle.\nYour third question: I recall that the Taiwan Affairs Office’s earlier press conference answered this. It is a long-term plan for transportation infrastructure construction in the outline of the “13th Five-Year Plan.” Such planning is conducive to the layout of the railway network and to improving railway service capacity, and it also helps the economic and social development of the areas along the lines, benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that Taiwan is a “contributor to regional security and stability,” but slandered the mainland by claiming that the mainland’s increasingly frequent military activities in East Asia have caused some impact on the security and stability of the surrounding region. What is the spokesperson’s response?","Only the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait; pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism means there will be no peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2017-12-27","An Fengshan","环球网","We note that the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently announced it will reduce the limit on the number of Mainland tour group members for the “mini three links” from 5 to 3, and relax some provisions on Mainland spouses' relatives visiting Taiwan for family visits. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","Since last year's 5·20, because the Taiwan authorities do not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and do not accept that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, they have undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. This has caused serious impact on cross-Strait relations and affected all aspects of them. The Taiwan side should recognize the crux of the problem and adopt practical and effective measures to provide a better environment and conditions for cross-Strait exchanges.\nThank you all! Today is the last regular press conference of this year. In a few days we will welcome 2018. Over the past year, all of you reporter friends have worked busily and hard. Here, I also wish you all in advance good health, smooth work and everything going well in the new year!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201712/t20171227_11884416.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2017-12-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Taiwan defense authority published the so-called “National Defense Report 2017” on December 26th, which is the first one published by the Tsai Ing-wen administration. The report detailed the number of times the PLA Air Force had drilled near the island and listed for the first time the process of the US arms sales to Taiwan, hyping up the US-Taiwan military cooperation. What is your comment?","First of all, I’d like to point out that Taiwan is a part of China, therefore, there is no such a thing as the so-called “National Defense Report”. China firmly opposes any form of official contacts between Taiwan and the US, and China is willing to do its utmost with maximum sincerity to achieve the outcome of peaceful reunification of the Mainland and Taiwan.\nHowever, we must sternly warn the \"Taiwan independence\" forces that China’s determination to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity is unshakeable, and any attempt to rely on foreign forces or any attempt to resist the reunification by military force will be in vain. The only right choice is sticking to the 1992 Consensus and maintaining the peaceful development of cross-straits relation, and by so doing can peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits be guaranteed.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-12/29/content_4801034.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-12-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The PLA Daily carried the report about a missile brigade of the Rocket Force and it had attracted the attention from Taiwan press. The Central Agency of Taiwan reported on December 25th that the strategic missile forces of the former Second Artillery Force used to be hidden in remote mountains, which had a poor performance in mobility and was vulnerable to attacks. However, the article on the PLA Daily shows that…","The PLA Rocket Force is the major strategic deterrence force of the nation, and a strategic pillar of China’s status as a major power and also the cornerstone for maintaining national security. With technological progress, it is normal and necessary for the Rocket Force to develop and upgrade its weaponry and equipment, which is also a common measure taken by various countries in modernizing their armed forces. The PLA Rocket Force’s modernization of its weaponry and equipment focuses on the improvement and upgrading of strategic deterrence and real combat capabilities. It is out of the need for safeguarding national security and it is not targeting any country or specific target. We adhere to the path of peaceful development and firmly follow a defensive national defense policy. We hope that all countries can view China’s development of national defense in an objective manner.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-12/29/content_4801034.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2017-12-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Since mid November, the PLA’s warship and aircraft have conducted frequent training exercises in East Asia, during which the PLA Air Force’s aircraft circled around Taiwan for many times. Although the mainland said these were routine drills, the Taiwan authority pointed out recently that related drills had, to a certain extent, undermined the regional security and stability. What is your response?","Taiwan is a part of China. The related training activities conducted by the naval and air forces of the PLA are routine arrangements under the annual training plans, and we will continue to carry out such kind of training. The training activities in high seas by the naval and air forces of the PLA are becoming increasingly regular, which conforms to relevant international laws and practices. The development of China’s armed forces is a boost for the peaceful and stable force in the region.\nThe objective of these far-sea training is to enhance the Chinese military’s capacity of carrying out missions in the new era to better safeguard national security and maintain peace and stability in the region and the world at large.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2017-12/29/content_4801034.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2017-12-29","Hua Chunying","","The US said it felt disappointed at China allowing oil export to the DPRK. Do you have any further comments on that?","I believe I have just now made myself quite clear. First, China has been comprehensively and strictly implementing the Security Council resolutions and condones no violations of these resolutions by any Chinese citizen and company. Second, any act of violation, once found and proven, will be dealt with seriously in accordance with laws and regulation. Not a single case of violation should get away with it. Third, regarding the specific cases recently reported by some media, like what I said to the Taiwan \"Central News Agency\", the Chinese side launched investigation immediately after learning the relevant reports. What is described in these reports turns out to be untrue. The hyped-up media reports are not conducive to building mutual trust and conducting cooperation between all parties on the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue. Fourth, all sides should comprehensively implement relevant resolutions in entirety, and make positive efforts to maintain peace and stability of the Korean Peninsula and the region at large, advance the Peninsula denuclearization process, and promote a settlement of the issue through dialogue and negotiation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1522875.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1522838.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-01-11","Lu Kang","","What are China's comments on the US House of Representatives' recent passing of the Taiwan Travel Act?","We have taken note of relevant reports. I must stress once again that the act severely violates the one-China policy and principles in the three China-US joint communiqués and interferes in China's internal affairs. We express firm opposition to it.\nThe Chinese side urges the US side to abide by the one-China policy and principles in the three China-US joint communiqués, prudently handle the Taiwan issue, refrain from engaging in any form of official exchange or contact with Taiwan or sending any wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and take concrete actions to uphold the larger picture of China-US relations and the China-US cooperation in international affairs.\nAfter the press conference, the following question was raised: according to our information, the spokesperson of the National Iranian Tanker Company said that China did not help to rescue those missing Iranian crewmen in the oil tanker collision accident off the coast of the East China Sea. Though having a lot of firefighting equipment and personnel near the burning tanker, China is not using them. What's your comment?\nSpokesperson Lu Kang said that such remarks are totally contrary to the facts.\nSince the accident happened, the Chinese government has attached great importance to it and made all-out efforts to conduct maritime search and rescue for the shipwrecked crew. China maintains communication with the Iranian Embassy in China. The China Maritime Search and Rescue Center has coordinated and dispatched a large number of rescue forces to engage in the search and rescue efforts on the spot in a scientific and effective manner. The wrecked ship that carries 130,000 tons of condensate oil is still burning and exploding. Meanwhile, the sea conditions are rough in the waters where the accident took place, and you can well imagine how difficult and dangerous the rescue is. When faced with security threats, the Chinese rescuers approached the tanker at the risk of their lives many times to search, rescue and fight the fire at close range. At the same time, China has been coordinating with the rescue teams from Japan and the ROK.\nA case involving human life must be treated with the utmost care. This is how we perceive this matter and we also act exactly in that vein. We hope that the relevant sides will learn about their information through official channels including the China Maritime Search and Rescue Center and not readily believe information from other channels, lest that should disrupt and negatively affect the rescue efforts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1525118.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1525034.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-01-12","Lu Kang","","According to reports, recently, in an e-mail survey sent to its members and on the registration page of its mobile phone app, Marriott Hotel listed Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and Tibet as \"countries\". Reports said that some Chinese departments have taken measures in response to the global hotel chain's behavior and initiated an investigation on that. What is your comment?","I believe you have all noted the relevant situation. You may have also noted that the Chinese competent authorities have dealt with that and the head of the corporation you mentioned has made a public apology. I would like to stress that Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and Tibet are all parts of China, and this is the objective fact as well as the consensus of the international community.\nWe welcome foreign corporations' investment and operation in China. Meanwhile, they should respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by China's laws and respect Chinese people's national feelings. This is the minimum requirement for any enterprise to invest, operate and conduct cooperation in another country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1525480.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1525355.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 17, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang first summarized the development of cross-Strait relations in 2017 and looked ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2018, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues in cross-Strait relations.","Ladies and gentlemen of the media, good morning. Welcome to the first press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office in 2018. On behalf of the News Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, and on behalf of my fellow spokesperson Mr. An Fengshan, I extend New Year greetings to you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","In 2017, the situation in cross-Strait relations became even more complex and grave. The Taiwan authorities refuse to accept the “1992 Consensus,” tolerate and indulge “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence” activities, and obstruct cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. “Taiwan independence” forces clamor for “referendums” and “constitutional revision,” stirring up hostility across the Strait, undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180117_11894600.htm"],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Facing a complex and severe situation, we thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thought on work concerning Taiwan, comprehensively carry out the decisions and arrangements of the central authorities, firmly grasp the correct direction of cross-Strait relations, strive to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” take forceful measures, and resolutely oppose and contain all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. We will strengthen exchanges and dialogue with political parties, groups, and individuals on the island that recognize the “1992 Consensus” and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and unite compatriots on both sides to jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We insist on doing good deeds and practical things for Taiwan compatriots. We have introduced more than 20 policy measures: expanding the enrollment of Taiwan students, relaxing admission standards, and adding scholarships; expanding the industries and regions where Taiwan compatriots may work on the Mainland, adding professional qualification examination programs, and opening applications for the National Social Science Fund; expanding the scope of practice for Taiwan residents who have obtained Mainland lawyer qualifications; adding self-service ticket vending machines for ID-card-style Taiwan Compatriot Permits at more than 200 railway stations and all civil airports nationwide; and solving the problem of Taiwan compatriots paying into and using the housing provident fund on the Mainland. We have provided more than 12,000 internship and employment positions for Taiwan youth, and cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship bases and employment and entrepreneurship demonstration sites have cumulatively hosted or served more than 1,400 Taiwan enterprises and teams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We continue to deepen cross-Strait economic cooperation. General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter on the 10th anniversary of the founding of the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, fully reflecting the high importance and heartfelt care given to Taiwanese businesspeople and strengthening their confidence in putting down roots and developing in the mainland. We held a product fair for Taiwan-invested enterprises in the mainland, showcasing the development process and achievements of Taiwanese businesses in the mainland over more than 30 years. We promoted “Taiwanese businesses going online” and helped Taiwanese enterprises expand into the mainland domestic market. We established the Guangxi and Sichuan Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zones to provide platforms for Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to develop in the central and western regions and to participate in the construction of the “Belt and Road.” A batch of large Taiwanese corporate and major projects achieved new progress in investment and construction, and cooperation in agriculture and finance across the Strait continued to expand. In 2017, cross-Strait trade reached US$199.39 billion, up 11.3 percent year on year, setting a new historical high. The actual use of Taiwan capital (including from third places) in the mainland was US$4.73 billion, up 30.9 percent year on year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We vigorously promote exchanges across all fields between the two sides of the Strait. We held the 9th Straits Forum, the 2017 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit at Purple Mountain, the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance against Japan History Symposium, and the 3rd Cross-Strait Media Summit in Beijing. Compatriots on both sides jointly commemorated the 30th anniversary of cross-Strait exchanges; grassroots exchanges produced many highlights, youth exchanges developed innovatively, and exchanges in culture, education, marriage, sports, religion and folk beliefs, labor unions, farmers’ and fishermen’s associations, and ethnic minorities were rich and varied. Mainland film and television programs, variety shows, online literature, online shopping, mobile payment, and shared services have been sought after by the island’s public, especially young people. The first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League drew wide attention, with online clicks reaching 530 million in just the six days of the finals alone. The Mazu statue from the Meizhou Zumiao temple in Fujian toured Taiwan, causing a sensation across the island, with nearly 5 million believers paying homage. Cross-Strait personnel exchanges have been continuous; in 2017 they reached 8.78 million trips, of which 5.87 million were trips by Taiwan residents to the mainland, a year-on-year increase of 2.49% and another record high.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Looking ahead to 2018, the complex factors facing cross-Strait relations have increased, and risks and challenges have grown; but we have full confidence and ability to meet challenges, grasp the direction, and push cross-Strait relations to continue to overcome difficulties and move forward.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We will thoroughly implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, fully implement the central government's major policies and work deployments toward Taiwan, adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and firmly oppose and deter any form of \"Taiwan independence\" secession. We will actively expand cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, continuously deepen the integrated economic and social development across the Strait, uphold the concept that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,\" take the lead in sharing the opportunities of mainland development with Taiwan compatriots, gradually provide them with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, working, and living on the mainland, and promote the joint promotion of Chinese culture by compatriots on both sides. We will closely unite compatriots on both sides, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Regarding the mainland's activation of M503 northbound and three connecting routes, the Taiwan authorities claimed that this move violates the “consensus” reached between the two sides in 2015, is a “unilateral” and “one-sided” activation, and affects Taiwan's flight safety. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The M503 northbound route and related connecting routes began operating on January 4. The Civil Aviation Administration of China's website has already introduced the relevant situation, and when I previously answered reporters' questions in writing, I also explained its necessity. Here, I would like to express several further views:\nFirst, the airspace on the west side of the Taiwan Strait is a major air traffic corridor linking the Yangtze River Delta with the Pearl River Delta, as well as Hong Kong, Macao, and Southeast Asia, and cross-Strait direct air routes also pass through this area. Opening the M503 northbound route and connecting routes is intended to ease the pressure of rapidly growing flights in this area, ensure flight safety, reduce flight delays, protect passengers' rights, and meet the needs of air transport development in the Asia-Pacific region. It is also conducive to improving cross-Strait flight operations, further facilitating exchanges between people on both sides, and is in line with the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nIn recent years, flights in this region have grown rapidly, traffic density has been extremely high, and delays have become increasingly serious. Without the northbound route, flights from Southeast Asia and Hong Kong and Macao heading north through the Yangtze River Delta are seriously affected. Without the related connecting routes in use, flights have always been constrained in diverting traffic from route A470. According to statistics, in 2017 the average delay for flights from Hong Kong to Shanghai Pudong reached 103 minutes, an increase of 5.1% over the same period in 2016, and the average on-time rate on this route was only 46%. Starting the M503 northbound route and related connecting routes will effectively relieve the traffic pressure on existing routes.\nSecond, the M503 route lies entirely on the side of the Taiwan Strait close to the mainland, within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. Establishing and activating this route is a routine task of mainland civil aviation airspace management and an internal affair of the mainland. It does not involve Taiwan's routes or waypoints, so there is absolutely no question of unilateral opening.\nThird, before this route was activated in March 2015, the mainland side fully considered Taiwan's concerns and communicated with the Taiwan side. In those communications, the mainland side stated that when opening the M503 northbound route and related connecting routes in the future, it would notify the Taiwan side in advance. However, this does not mean that opening the route requires Taiwan's consent. Even so, before the mainland activated the M503 northbound and related connecting routes on January 4, we also notified the Taiwan side. The Taiwan side's claim that the mainland violated the consensus reached by both sides in 2015 is completely inconsistent with the facts.\nFourth, since the southbound route of M503 was activated, its overall operation has been safe and stable, and airlines from Hong Kong, Macao, and Southeast Asia have widely participated, effectively playing the role of international civil aviation routes. Since the northbound route and connecting routes were opened, an average of 27 flights have operated per day, which fully demonstrates the safety and reliability of this route. There is no issue affecting flight safety in Taiwan.\nFinally, I must once again point out that the Taiwan side should view this matter correctly and not use it as an opportunity to make an issue of it, or interfere with or undermine cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180117_11894599.htm"],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","We have noted that a netizen recently reported that a TV drama starring Taiwanese actress Lin Xinru was temporarily removed from the broadcasting platform. In response, Lin Xinru issued a statement saying that she has always supported peaceful coexistence and friendly development across the Strait, and that in the past, she has never supported, and in the future will never support, any acts or remarks of 'Taiwan…","We have noted this matter. We believe the relevant parties will objectively assess it and handle it properly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180117_11894596.htm"],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","We noted that the U.S. House of Representatives recently passed the so-called “Taiwan Travel Act,” which advocates mutual visits by officials at all levels between the U.S. and Taiwan. I would like to ask the spokesperson how you respond to this.","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated its position on this. I want to stress that the relevant US bill seriously violates the one-China principle established by the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose it. We advise the Taiwan side not to rely on foreign powers to elevate itself, lest it bring fire upon itself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180117_11894598.htm"],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, “independence” groups on the island held a press conference announcing that they would start a referendum signature drive to apply to participate in the 2020 Tokyo Olympics and all international sports events under the name “Taiwan.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The International Olympic Committee has clear rules on Taiwan’s participation in the Olympics. The “Olympic model” is a principle jointly followed by international sports organizations and sports circles on both sides of the Strait. Any political scheme and action attempting to change the name is doomed to be a farce that cannot succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180117_11894597.htm"],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","A recent public opinion poll released by Taiwan's Commonwealth Magazine (《天下》) shows that the proportion of people who consider themselves both Taiwanese and Chinese has reached a record high, and the integration of cross-Strait cultures and the rise of the mainland economy have also led Taiwan residents to identify with the mainland. On the other hand, we see that since May 20 of the year before last, the Taiwan…","Regarding these two questions, I have noted the relevant reports, and I agree with the comment you made in your question. The broad mass of Taiwan compatriots opposes “Taiwan independence” and supports the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. As our policies toward Taiwan keep producing results, and as the mainland continues to develop and progress, we will certainly be able to unite the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, jointly safeguard and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and work together toward the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","First, we noted that Tsai Ing-wen, at her year-end press conference, put forward the “new three no's” for cross-Strait relations: cross-Strait relations will not run wild, will not freeze, and will not return to the old path. What is the spokesperson's assessment? Second, we recently noticed that the electronic questionnaire of the Marriott Hotel listed Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and Tibet within the scope of…","Let me answer your second question first. The relevant departments have already stated their position on the relevant incident and handled it. The relevant enterprises have also carried out rectification. As is well known, Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of Chinese territory, and the one-China principle is the basic guideline for the international community in handling Taiwan-related affairs. Enterprises that invest and operate on the mainland should all abide by Chinese law.\nOn your first question, the actual situation is that since May 20, 2016, because the Taiwan authorities have refused to accept the “1992 Consensus” and do not acknowledge that the two sides belong to one China, the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations has been seriously damaged. This has caused cross-strait relations to be in a politically deadlocked situation, which is well known. Of course, the future depends on whether Taiwan's side will readily heed good advice and return to the common foundation of the “1992 Consensus” to work with us for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, or whether it will move in the opposite direction and escalate even further. This depends on the Taiwan side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, the New Party Service Committee, recently announced to serve Taiwan compatriots doing business and studying on the mainland, was established. New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming said it would only help those who identify themselves as Chinese descendants and oppose “Taiwan independence.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Our attitude has been consistent and clear. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen dialogue and cooperation with all parties, groups, and individuals in Taiwan who recognize this foundation and concept, to jointly safeguard and enhance the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, and to jointly safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, recently there have been more and more calls for “armed unification” of Taiwan. Tsai Ing-wen said on one occasion recently that she believes the mainland will not use force against Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have? The other question concerns the M503 route. The US side has said it hopes the mainland will not undermine this status quo and hopes both sides can develop relations…","Second question: The spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already responded to the US side's statement, and I have nothing new to add. This route was approved by the International Civil Aviation Organization after scientific and professional demonstration. We still need to believe in science and believe in ICAO.\nFirst question: Everyone knows that our major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent, and they have not changed. The reason for the recent rise in \"armed unification\" rhetoric, I think, is mainly the increasingly rampant variety of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities on the island. We are willing to make our greatest efforts and sincerity to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will also never tolerate \"Taiwan independence\" and will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist forces to split China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","We note that in the last few days of 2017, a cross-Strait industrial cooperation park was established in Sichuan, which can be said to have added another new platform for cross-Strait industrial cooperation. Could the spokesperson introduce the overall progress of cross-Strait industrial cooperation in 2017? In addition, could the spokesperson also introduce the overall operating situation of the main Taiwan…","First, let me correct something: there is no dedicated Taiwanese investment zone. In the more than thirty years since Taiwanese businesses began investing on the mainland, they have been able to go to any place where laws and regulations permit. Of course, based on the current situation, they are mainly concentrated in the Yangtze River Delta, the Pearl River Delta, the Bohai Rim region, and places such as Hubei, Sichuan and Chongqing. But in recent years, with the mainland's economic reform, economic transformation and even expanded opening-up, Taiwanese investment has shown a trend of shifting toward the central and western regions.\nAs for the cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones you mentioned, you may have already noticed that, to help Taiwan-funded enterprises shift toward the central and western regions and to help Taiwanese businesses take part in the Belt and Road construction, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, together with the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce, established Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zones in Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region and Sichuan Province in September and December 2017, respectively. The cooperation zone in Guangxi includes three industrial parks: Fangchenggang, Chongzuo and Qinzhou. The cooperation zone in Sichuan includes three industrial parks: Chengdu, Deyang and Meishan. At present, Guangxi and Sichuan have both issued specific policy measures and are working to speed up the construction of the cooperation zones. The transportation, location and cost advantages of the cooperation zones have also attracted a large number of Taiwan-funded enterprises to visit. As far as I know, many Taiwan-funded enterprises have already settled in the cooperation zones and begun to develop there.\nIn the future, we will continue to guide, support and promote the construction of the cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones, and open new development space for Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to reports, the DPP authorities will continue to increase the defense budget, and it is estimated that by 2025 Taiwan’s annual budget will increase by at least 20%. Some commentators believe this reflects that the DPP authorities will engage in an arms race with the mainland and attempt to “resist unification by force.” Some analysts also believe that cross-Strait relations in 2018 will be full of…","We have repeatedly and clearly stated that “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan authorities, on the one hand, flatly refuse to accept the “1992 Consensus” and undermine the political foundation of cross-Strait relations, while on the other hand recklessly expanding their armaments, which will only aggravate tensions in the Taiwan Strait. Military confrontation has no way out. Only by returning to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be truly safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Two questions. First, regarding the pollution restriction order implemented in Kunshan, which affected some Taiwanese businesses: as the mainland increasingly attaches importance to a Beautiful China and to the environment, will the mainland conduct new coordination or communication with Taiwanese businesses in the new year? Second, Taiwanese media recently reported that regarding this year’s Shanghai-Taipei Twin…","First, this is already old news. As everyone knows, one important task of the mainland’s economic work this year is controlling air pollution. Taiwan also faces serious localized air pollution. I believe that broad enterprises, including Taiwan-funded enterprises, can understand the mainland’s pollution control measures.\nIn addition, some provinces and cities have adopted pollution-restriction measures during periods when pollution may be concentrated. Fundamentally, these measures ultimately benefit enterprises’ transformation and upgrading and help them keep pace with the mainland’s economic restructuring, so that they can achieve greater development.\nAs for the Twin City Forum, as everyone knows, the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum is an exchange activity between cities across the Taiwan Strait, and its specific matters are to be discussed by the Shanghai and Taipei municipal governments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","May I ask the spokesperson: The mainland previously stated that it would formulate policy measures to facilitate the life of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, including studying changing the Taiwan compatriot permit to an 18-digit number. What is the progress of this measure? Is it possible to implement it in 2018?","As everyone knows, gradually providing Taiwan compatriots who study, start businesses, seek employment, and live on the mainland with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots is our established policy, which has been written into the report of the 19th National Congress. Building on the more than twenty policy measures adopted last year, we will also work with relevant departments to continue introducing new policy measures this year. As for the inconvenience you mentioned that Taiwan compatriots encounter when using certain public services on the mainland with their Taiwan Compatriot Permits, as I understand it, the relevant departments are working to compile and study the issue. Once there is definite news, we will announce it promptly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","January 13 marks the 30th anniversary of the death of Chiang Ching-kuo, the late leader of Taiwan. We noted that the Kuomintang has held multiple commemorative events in a high-profile manner, and there are voices within the party calling to “find the next Chiang Ching-kuo.” What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","Mr. Chiang Ching-kuo adhered to one China, opposed “Taiwan independence,” pursued national reunification, and made certain efforts to ease cross-Strait relations. We are willing to maintain communication with the Kuomintang on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” strengthen exchanges and dialogue, jointly safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, and jointly maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, some DPP lawmakers proposed amending Taiwan's so-called “Criminal Law” to explicitly designate the mainland as an “enemy.” Some public opinion in Taiwan holds that this is an attempt to switch concepts, blurring the clear provisions in Taiwan's existing laws that both sides of the Strait belong to one country, and that it is part of “legal Taiwan independence.” What is the spokesperson's view of such…","We are closely following developments. We oppose all kinds of activities aimed at “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-17","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报、团结网记者","Taisheng Furniture, a well-known Taiwanese company that set up a factory in Dongguan, announced it would halt production starting the 21st. Taiwan media reported that \"Taiwanese businesses may become historical terms.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","If the cessation of production by one company made Taiwan businesspeople a thing of the past, that would be rather alarmist. If you saw the achievements exhibition of Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-invested enterprises recently held in Nanjing, Jiangsu, you would be amazed by the development achievements of Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland. As for the specific matter you mentioned, some rumors do not match the actual situation. As I understand it, Dongguan Taisheng Furniture Co., Ltd. has not stopped production permanently. Rather, the enterprise is actively responding to market changes and undergoing a temporary restructuring and production suspension. Once its new domestic-sales production line is upgraded and adjusted, it will rehire the relevant employees and resume production.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180117_11894595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-01-19","Lu Kang","","Yesterday, the police of Poland arrested 48 Taiwanese and 2 Polish suspects in telecom fraud, allegedly swindling 2.3 million US dollars from Chinese citizens. Will China ask the Polish side to hand over the Taiwanese suspects?","We have noted relevant reports. This is still an ongoing investigation. China attaches high importance to protecting the legitimate rights and interests of its citizens and stands ready to coordinate with other countries to jointly fight against cross-border crimes including fraud.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1527187.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1527119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Tsai Ing-wen, the local leader of Taiwan, said this week that she could not rule out the possibility that China would reunify with Taiwan by use of arms. What is your response to this? Second, the Liaoning aircraft carrier battle group sailed twice through the Taiwan Strait this month. Will you comment on that?","On your first question, we have the utmost sincerity to strive for peaceful reunification, but we would never allow Taiwan to be separated from China.\nWith regard to your second question, recently, the Liaoning aircraft carrier battle group conducted a cross-region maneuver according to the annual training plan. The purpose of the training is to test the performance of the weapons and equipment, and the training level of the troops.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-01/26/content_4803345.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently, TAO and ARATS leaders visited several places on the mainland to visit and extend condolences to Taiwan businesspeople, students, and compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On the eve of the Spring Festival, Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Deputy Directors Liu Jieyi and Long Mingbiao; Assistant to the Director Zhou Ning; and Chen Deming, Chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait, divided into five groups and went to 12 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Beijing, Shanghai, Fujian, Henan, Hebei, Guangdong, Guangxi, Jiangxi, Anhui, Jiangsu, Shaanxi and Gansu. They visited Taiwan-funded enterprises, schools, communities and Taiwanese families, and extended greetings to Taiwanese businesspeople and officials, Taiwanese teachers and students, Taiwanese journalists and other groups of Taiwan compatriots. They learned about compatriots’ work, study, life and business operations on the mainland, investigated the implementation of more than 20 convenience policies introduced last year, and listened to opinions and suggestions.\nDuring these visits and greetings, Taiwanese businesspeople, students and compatriots generally reported that the conditions for working, studying and living on the mainland are getting better and better, which has further strengthened their confidence in developing here. We attach great importance to certain specific issues raised by some Taiwan compatriots. We will work with the relevant departments and localities to earnestly implement the 19th Party Congress’s call to “gradually provide Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment and living on the mainland,” and will continue to introduce policy measures of greater intensity and higher value.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913536.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","During the recent visit and condolences by leaders of the Taiwan Affairs Office, some Taiwan compatriots and students raised concerns. For example: Can Taiwanese youth working on the mainland take out loans to buy housing? Can convenience be provided for Taiwanese students to obtain a Chinese medicine practitioner license on the mainland? Can a dedicated job fair be held for Taiwanese youth seeking employment on…","Taiwan residents working in the mainland may, in accordance with local regulations, apply for commercial loans to buy homes, and may also pay into the housing provident fund under relevant regulations and then apply for housing provident fund personal housing loans. Taiwanese students studying at mainland universities may take the National Medical Practitioner Qualification Examination on the same terms as mainland students. These two specific issues have been resolved in terms of policy.\nIn recent years, various regions and relevant parties, based on the actual needs of Taiwanese youth, have actively provided convenience for them to find employment in the mainland. For example, the Shanghai Taiwan-Invested Enterprises Association has repeatedly held recruitment expos in Taipei, Wenzhou City has also held talent matching events for Taiwanese youth, and at the cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship seminar hosted by the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, job positions were specially provided for Taiwanese youth to choose from. In the future, we will continue to support such events and further open up channels for Taiwanese youth to find employment in the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently gave an exclusive interview. When asked whether the mainland would use force against Taiwan, she said “no one will rule out this possibility,” and that it depends on whether the mainland side is rational. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Since May 20, 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to accept the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermining the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. On the island, they have tolerated and indulged “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence” activities, obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and suppressed and persecuted parties, groups and individuals who support the development of cross-Strait relations and peaceful reunification. “Taiwan independence” forces have agitated for a referendum to “amend the constitution,” stirring up cross-Strait hostility and undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At present, the complex and severe situation in cross-Strait relations is entirely the responsibility of the Taiwan authorities.\nAlthough the complex factors and risks and challenges facing cross-Strait relations have increased, we have full confidence and capability to meet challenges, grasp the direction, and push cross-Strait relations to keep moving forward despite difficulties. We will continue to adhere to the policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and utmost effort. At the same time, we resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, have firm resolve, sufficient confidence and adequate capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist plots, and will never tolerate a repeat of the historical tragedy of national division.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913535.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","We note that on the 29th, the Taiwan side said it would not approve the Spring Festival extra flights for 176 flights of China Eastern Airlines and Xiamen Airlines, resulting in infringement of the rights and interests of 50,000 passengers, most of whom are Taiwan businesspeople. What is the spokesperson’s response?","The Taiwan authorities, citing the use by China Eastern Airlines and Xiamen Airlines of the M503 route and its connecting route as a pretext, have ignored public opinion and insisted on their course, obstructing the approval of 176 Spring Festival extra flights planned by the two airlines. The National Civil Aviation Administration of China issued written statements on January 19 and January 30, respectively, to condemn this. On January 29, as the Taiwan side’s final approval deadline approached, China Eastern Airlines and Xiamen Airlines, under compulsion, had no choice but on January 30 to announce follow-up service measures, including flight cancellations and free refunds. The unreasonable actions of the Taiwan authorities have caused inconvenience to tens of thousands of travelers, created difficulties for many cross-strait families reuniting for the Spring Festival, and inflicted harm on the feelings of people on both sides. All consequences arising from this must be borne by the Taiwan authorities.\nThe cross-strait Spring Festival extra flights are a benefit measure launched by the mainland side in keeping with the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family.” Over more than a decade, the routes and flights of the Spring Festival extra flights have continuously expanded and increased, meeting the needs of cross-strait people for travel during the Spring Festival and of Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year, and they have been warmly welcomed by compatriots on both sides. In 2017, the scale of cross-strait personnel exchanges continued to expand, and the number of Taiwan compatriots studying, starting businesses, working and living on the mainland continued to increase. Based on the actual needs of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots returning home for the New Year and of cross-strait exchanges during the Spring Festival, mainland aviation authorities and airlines, despite severe shortages of airport slots, time slots, and capacity, overcame difficulties, actively organized support, and made efforts to arrange additional flights. The Taiwan authorities, however, linked the Spring Festival extra flights to the unrelated matter of opening the M503 northbound and connecting routes, and, without hesitation, took Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots as hostages to carry out so-called “retaliation” against mainland airlines. This seriously harms the rights of cross-strait people, especially Taiwan people, to return home for the holiday, seriously departs from the humanitarian needs of countless families and travelers, is extremely unreasonable, and is not supported by the public.\nThe Spring Festival is a traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and tens of thousands of compatriots in Taiwan urgently need to return home. Since the Taiwan authorities did not approve the Spring Festival extra flights of China Eastern and Xiamen Airlines, the relevant departments on the mainland will do their utmost to adopt other measures to help them return home for the holiday. For Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots who cannot go home and remain on the mainland for the holiday, the relevant departments on the mainland will also take good care of them so that they can have a good New Year on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913533.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Chang Hsiao-yueh, chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, said at a year-end press conference recently that this year's work priorities include reviewing and revising relevant regulations to avoid exchanges with mainland “united front” or political purposes. Public opinion holds that this means the Taiwan authorities will further restrict cross-strait exchanges. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Smearing normal cross-strait exchanges as “united front work” is a long-standing tactic of the Democratic Progressive Party and its authorities. Their continued escalation and restriction of cross-strait exchanges is going down a backward path. The wish of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, foster harmonious contacts, and achieve mutually beneficial win-win outcomes cannot be stopped. If the Taiwan authorities take cross-strait exchanges as a target, insist on escalating cross-strait confrontation, and worsen cross-strait relations, they will surely meet the joint opposition of compatriots on both sides and will ultimately reap the consequences themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913534.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that other measures will be taken regarding the cancellation of extra flights. Please elaborate on what measures will be taken. Is it possible to approve China Airlines' application for extra flights? Also, will the mainland side increase capacity to help Taiwan compatriots travel from Xiamen via the “Mini Three Links” back to Taiwan?","First, the Taiwan authorities, on the one hand, unscrupulously infringe on the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses and compatriots, and on the other hand shift responsibility, \"passing the buck\" to the mainland. Is this practice moral? The correct approach is for the Taiwan authorities to promptly agree to the Spring Festival additional flight plans of China Eastern and Xiamen Airlines. After that, if there is still a need, additional flight plans may be considered. As for other measures, the mainland civil aviation authorities, airlines and relevant localities will introduce them successively. You may have noticed that Fujian Province has already arranged to increase passenger ferry services from Pingtan to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Relevant authorities in Taiwan say that the W122 and W123 air routes are too close to the terminal airspace of Kinmen and Matsu, which could lead to an aerial close approach or collision between aircraft from the two sides and cause a flight safety problem. May I ask the spokesperson for comment on this?","This is a very good question. I have been waiting for everyone to ask it, and I am glad to explain it in detail.\nAs I understand it, regarding the connecting routes, when they were originally designed they already maintained safe separation distances from the routes between Kinmen, Matsu and Taiwan, so they will not affect the safety of the Kinmen and Matsu routes to and from Taiwan. To explain further in professional technical terms: under the rules of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), air traffic controllers should provide vertical separation and lateral separation according to the conditions of instrument flight rules. If either kind of separation is provided, both aircraft are considered safe. In fact, flights on routes W122 and W123, and flights taking off and landing at Kinmen and Matsu, both have lateral separation and vertical separation at the same time.\nAccording to the routes designed and published for Fuzhou, Xiamen, Kinmen and Matsu, the minimum lateral separation between route W123 and the Taiwan side's route W6, and between route W122 and Taiwan's route W8, is 33 kilometers and 23 kilometers respectively. Such separations are far greater than the lateral separation standard stipulated by ICAO. In terms of vertical altitude, the flight altitude difference between flights bound for Xiamen and flights bound for Kinmen exceeds 1,000 meters, and the flight altitude difference between flights bound for Fuzhou and flights bound for Matsu exceeds 3,000 meters. Both far exceed the vertical separation standard stipulated by ICAO. Therefore, the connecting routes are safe.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913531.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","Recently, a Taiwanese female student studying at a mainland university posted a micro-video on her social media platform titled “A Taiwanese girl wanders through a fifth-tier city on the mainland,” in which she talks about her impressions of life in northwestern cities and of mainland poverty alleviation work. The video quickly drew attention on both sides of the Strait, with over 20 million views. What is the…","Allowing impoverished people and impoverished areas to enter a moderately prosperous society together with the whole nation is a solemn commitment of our Party. The prosperity and development of the mainland have brought continuous improvements in people's living standards. Since the 18th Party Congress, the Party and government have implemented the development philosophy of putting the people at the center, and placed poverty alleviation in a prominent position in governing the country. Over the past five years, the battle against poverty has achieved decisive progress: more than 60 million impoverished people have achieved stable poverty exit, and the poverty incidence has dropped from 10.2% to below 4%. The appearance of impoverished areas has also undergone enormous changes. It is only natural that Taiwan youth spread and share this change with what they have seen with their own eyes and experienced firsthand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The Taiwan authorities recently again called on both sides of the Strait to negotiate the M503 route as soon as possible, without political preconditions. Some public opinion holds that the Taiwan side hopes to use this matter to restart institutionalized cross-Strait negotiations. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have repeatedly reiterated that the M503 route is an international civil aviation route open to the outside world. It lies entirely on the side of the Taiwan Strait close to the mainland, within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. Establishing and operating this route is a routine task of mainland civil aviation airspace management. The M503 route has undergone reliability demonstrations by multiple experts, has been approved by the International Civil Aviation Organization, and has been assigned a designator. Therefore, the accuracy, safety and reliability of the route’s operation all conform to International Civil Aviation Organization standards, and there is no question of flight safety requiring consultation.\nSince the realization of cross-Strait direct air links in 2009, the air traffic control departments on both sides have established a coordination and notification mechanism, and its operation has been smooth. The mainland regional air traffic control department and the Taiwan air traffic control department will maintain technical communication to ensure the safe operation of the M503 route.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201801/t20180131_11913532.htm"],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Following up on M503, Chang Hsiao-yueh (Zhang Xiaoyue), Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, said at the year-end press conference that temporarily withholding approval for additional flights was the “most minor punishment.” Yesterday, personnel of Taiwan’s Civil Aviation Administration also said that in the future it would depend on the goodwill of the other side to decide whether regular…","What is the so-called “most minor punishment”? Who is being punished? I think Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots feel as though they are drinking icy water, each drop cutting into their hearts. If the Taiwan side dares to further set its sights on regular cross-Strait flights, destroying the direct cross-Strait flight arrangements that compatriots on both sides have worked hard for since 2008, then they will be sinners for all time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, a polling agency in Taiwan released poll results showing that about 60 percent of the public is dissatisfied with Tsai Ing-wen's performance on cross-Strait policy, a new high since she took office. What comment does the spokesperson have on this? Second question: Some media reported that the Vatican recently sent a delegation to mainland China, which has prompted outside speculation about so-called…","We generally do not comment on specific Taiwan public opinion polls. But I think everyone has noticed that since May 20, 2016, cross-Strait relations have indeed undergone enormous changes. The situation of peaceful development has been seriously impacted, and its achievements have also been damaged, thus harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. I think the root cause of this situation is still the cross-Strait policy of the DPP authorities. Therefore, it is understandable that dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents has increased.\nSecond question: the one-China principle is the basic principle for us in handling Taiwan's external activities, and also an important political foundation for developing our relations with countries around the world. As for the specific issues in China-Vatican relations, please consult the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","At present, mainland spouses in Taiwan generally do not receive fair treatment. According to our understanding, mainland spouses without children who wish to obtain long-term residence permits in Taiwan mostly have to go through an interview with the Taiwan authorities, and some spouses have reported that the whole process is very unfair: the interview gives only one chance, and if they fail to pass, they may be…","In recent years, as cross-Strait exchanges have developed, cross-Strait marriages and families have also continued to increase. As I understand it, there are already 400,000 cross-Strait marriage families. These mainland spouses are both relatives on the mainland and relatives of Taiwan compatriots. Therefore, treating them with the attitude of family members is entirely appropriate. But it is very regrettable that what we see is the DPP authorities' long-standing discrimination against and restriction of the various rights of mainland spouses in Taiwan. Some regulations, such as the interview system you mentioned, are in effect near-humiliating measures and are extremely inhumane. So I think it is natural that they have provoked strong opposition from the broad community of mainland spouses. The Taiwan authorities should change these unreasonable practices as soon as possible, so that the so-called freedom, democracy and human rights that they tout and keep on their lips do not continue to become a laughingstock to the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","In an interview recently, Tsai Ing-wen spoke at length about so-called “Taiwan values,” which has made “Taiwan values” a hot topic of discussion on the island. What is the spokesperson’s view on so-called “Taiwan values”?","Has everyone not noticed what the so-called “Taiwan values” she speaks of actually are? Even Ko Wen-je has been left “utterly baffled.” If I must offer a view, I believe that if so-called “Taiwan values” means separating Taiwan culture from Chinese culture and setting them against each other, separating the well-being of Taiwan's people from the overall interests of the Chinese nation and setting them against each other, handing Taiwan's future and destiny over to outsiders, and willingly serving as a pawn to contain China, then such “values” are not a blessing for Taiwan, but a disaster for Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently the mainland uncovered a major military espionage case involving Taiwan. Please introduce the relevant circumstances and progress of this case.","It is understood that the case has already been brought to prosecution by the People's Procuratorate of Suzhou City, Jiangsu Province. For specific information, you may inquire with the handling authorities. I want to stress that whoever commits criminal acts endangering national security will be punished according to law, regardless of who they are.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","The Xiamen Entry-Exit Inspection and Quarantine Bureau recently said that this year it will adhere to pioneering and experimenting first, strengthen innovation in the inspection and quarantine mechanism for Taiwan, and strive to establish a special supervision zone for inspection and quarantine between Xiamen and Kinmen. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","The Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone, including the Xiamen area, is pioneering reform and opening up on a trial basis in deepening reform and expanding opening. This is conducive to promoting economic and trade cooperation between Jinmen and Xiamen, and even between the two sides of the Strait, and we welcome this. As for the specific situation, you may inquire with the relevant local authorities and the Free Trade Zone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志社记者","The 71st World Health Assembly will be held in Geneva, Switzerland, in May this year. On January 29, the head of Taiwan's health authority said Taiwan will not give up any opportunity, and that this year's efforts are stronger than last year's. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","Our position on Taiwan's participation in international organizations is consistent and clear, and we have explained it many times: the one-China principle must be upheld, and the matter must be handled through cross-Strait consultation. From 2009 to 2016, against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and on the common political foundation of both sides opposing “Taiwan independence” and upholding the “1992 Consensus,” Taiwan participated in the World Health Assembly for eight consecutive years. Last year, for well-known reasons, Taiwan was not invited again. I think the Taiwan side should think carefully about why it could participate in the past but cannot now. In fact, the bright path is right in front of you, and no one needs to point it out.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Returning to the M503 route issue: we found that Tsai Ing-wen herself posted protests on her social networking site right away, and at the same time the Taiwan authorities’ overseas representatives delivered more than 120 letters around the world to “lodge complaints abroad” with the international community. Some public opinion holds that the Taiwan authorities’ actions are mainly aimed at hyping the M503 route…","The Taiwan authorities have been sending letters abroad around the world, one-sidedly promoting their views. I think this is using the occasion to make political capital. “Complaining to foreign powers” is of no help.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Continuing from the earlier question about cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights: because mainland airlines' Spring Festival extra flights have been obstructed, it has become difficult for many Taiwan compatriots to return home for the New Year. Some mainland netizens have said they would like to postpone their plans to travel to Taiwan and leave their air tickets for Taiwan-funded enterprise personnel and…","On the first question, I believe the words and deeds of our mainland netizens reflect their fraternal feelings toward Taiwan compatriots and their concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” They stand in stark contrast to certain unreasonable actions of the Taiwan authorities.\nOn the second question, we do not comment on matters within Taiwan. But the reality is that since May 20, 2016, because the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been undermined, and the overall political and social environment on the island has changed, the willingness of mainland residents to travel to Taiwan has been affected. The healthy and stable development momentum of mainland residents’ tourism to Taiwan, which had lasted for many years, has been disrupted, and the interests of some Taiwan operators have also been harmed. I believe that only the one who tied the bell can untie it. The Taiwan authorities should take concrete action to improve cross-Strait relations, especially by returning to the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","US Taiwan Strait issues expert Bonnie Glaser believes that the main variable in the Taiwan Strait situation this year is Tsai Ing-wen's policies, because Tsai is currently under enormous pressure on the island and her poll approval ratings are very low. What is the spokesperson's view on this?","As for the remarks of certain American scholars, we generally do not comment. Since the beginning of this year, we have pointed out several times the complex and grave situation facing cross-Strait relations, and have also set out our policies and guidelines toward Taiwan for the future. In short, our major policies toward Taiwan will not change. As for where cross-Strait relations go from here, of course it depends on the remarks and actions of the Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-01-31","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报团结网记者","It is understood that the eight measures for entry and exit convenience introduced by the Ministry of Public Security starting February 1 will officially take effect. Please ask the spokesperson: with the implementation of this policy, what impact will it have on travel to Taiwan, which has been cooling?","To further improve the way administration is conducted, raise the level of public services, and increase the people's sense of gain, public security authorities have recently introduced a number of convenience measures. By simplifying application materials, streamlining document procedures, and facilitating port clearance, among other means, they aim to further provide convenience for the broad public in going abroad, traveling, visiting relatives, studying, and working. As for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, as I said just now, this fundamentally depends on the overall situation of cross-Strait relations and the atmosphere on the island.\nThis press conference is now concluded. As the Spring Festival is approaching, on behalf of the Information Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, I extend my Spring Festival greetings to everyone, and wish you all success in everything, good health, and smooth work. I especially wish the Taiwan media reporters present a smooth trip home to visit family for the Spring Festival.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201801/t20180131_11913522.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-02-07","Geng Shuang","","The Chinese mainland has offered to send help after the earthquake in Taiwan. Has Taiwan responded to this offer?","The earthquake that hit the Taiwan region is not a diplomatic question. Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has issued a statement on the earthquake that shook Hualian, Taiwan. You could check that on the website.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1532736.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1532721.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-02-07","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 7 (reporters Zhao Bo and Shi Longhong): TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said on the 7th, in response to a question, that late on February 6, a strong earthquake struck Hualien County in Taiwan, causing heavy casualties and property losses. Relevant parties on the mainland are highly concerned. The TAO and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) urgently activated the emergency response mechanism for cross-strait emergencies to learn about the disaster and the rescue situation. On the morning of February 7, TAO Director Zhang Zhijun held an urgent phone call with Hualien County Magistrate Fu Kun-chi, and ARATS Chairman Chen Deming called relevant parties in Hualien County. They expressed profound mourning for the Taiwan compatriots who died in the earthquake, sincere sympathy for the injured and affected Taiwan compatriots, and willingness to provide disaster relief assistance, including dispatching rescue teams.\nAn Fengshan said that after the earthquake, relevant parties on the mainland urgently sought to learn, through various channels, about mainland tourists, mainland students studying in Taiwan, and mainland spouses living in the disaster area. According to information received, apart from a few mainland tourists being injured, no deaths have been reported so far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180207_11922428.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-02-09","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, the US Senate Committee on Foreign Relations advanced the Taiwan Travel Act the other day, after US House of Representatives passed the bill. The bill encourages the US government to lift restrictions on high-level exchanges between the US and Taiwan. What is your comment?","The relevant provisions in the Act, though not legally binding, still gravely violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. If becoming law, it would severely disrupt China-US and the cross-Straits relations. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to that, and has lodged stern representations with the US.\nThe one-China principle is the political basis for China-US relations. We urge the US to honor its pledges made to China on the Taiwan issue, stop advancing the bill, properly deal with Taiwan-related issues, and ensure steady development of China-US and the cross-Straits relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1533682.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1533521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-02-09","Geng Shuang","","After the earthquake in Hualien, Taiwan, some Japanese senior officials conveyed their condolences while addressing Taiwan politicians in their so-called \"official\" titles. What is your comment? Have you lodged representations with the Japaneseside?","After the strong earthquake rocked Hualien, Taiwan, every heart on the mainland is throbbing with the suffering of Hualien. Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already sent condolences to our compatriots in the affected areas in Hualien, and offered to send rescue teams and provide all necessary assistance.\nI must stress that Japan's \"one China, one Taiwan\" attempt under the cloak of disaster relief violated the one-China principle and went against its commitments on Taiwan-related issues. China is strongly dissatisfied with that and has lodged stern representations with the Japanese side.\nWe urge the Japanese side to faithfully abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and immediately correct its wrongdoings so as to avoid any new disturbance to China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1533682.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1533521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-02-12","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 12 (reporter Liu Huan): TAO spokesperson An Fengshan said on the 12th that since the Hualien strong earthquake, relevant mainland authorities and all sectors of society have shown great concern. The TAO, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, the Red Cross Society of China, the China Earthquake Association and other relevant parties, as well as the Beijing Municipality, Fujian Province, Guangdong Province, the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region and other localities, promptly expressed condolences to the disaster-stricken compatriots through various means, and mourned the compatriots who died on both sides. The TAO has maintained close contact and communication with relevant Taiwan parties and Hualien County, promptly learned of the progress of disaster relief, and coordinated relevant parties to prepare to travel to Taiwan for rescue at any time and to provide rescue equipment. Relevant mainland parties, localities and Taiwan-invested enterprises have eagerly donated money and goods to support disaster-stricken compatriots in getting through the difficulties and rebuilding their homes as soon as possible. According to incomplete statistics, a total of RMB 20.875 million has been donated.\nAn Fengshan said that in this earthquake, 9 mainland tourists died and 6 mainland tourists were injured. The TAO and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits attached great importance to this and, together with the Ministry of Public Security, the National Tourism Administration and relevant provinces and municipalities, quickly activated emergency mechanisms, promptly verified information on the dead and injured, urgently opened a “green channel,” and expedited entry and exit documents for the families of casualties and for those who had lost their documents, fully assisting the families of the deceased tourists in traveling to Taiwan to handle the aftermath. The Cross-Strait Tourism Exchange Association and the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office also dispatched working groups to accompany the families to Taiwan and assist with handling aftermath matters.\nFinally, An Fengshan said that relevant Taiwan parties, the Hualien County Government and rescue personnel have fully carried out search and rescue operations, and have shown concern for and provided assistance to the injured mainland tourists and the families of the deceased. We express our thanks for this, and hope that the aftermath for the deceased tourists will be properly handled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180212_11924630.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan first introduced the issuance of the \"Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic, Cultural Exchange and Cooperation,\" and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO's first regular press conference after the Spring Festival. I will first release one piece of information:","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Since the 18th Party Congress, we have successively introduced a series of policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots in studying, starting businesses, working, and living on the mainland, which have played an important role in promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation. The 19th Party Congress proposed that, upholding the concept that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,\" we are willing to take the lead in sharing the opportunities of mainland development with Taiwan compatriots, and will expand cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation for mutual benefit. To thoroughly implement the spirit of the 19th Party Congress and General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thinking on Taiwan work, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the National Development and Reform Commission, after consultation with the Central Organization Department and 29 other departments, issued and implemented the \"Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation\" (hereinafter the \"Several Measures\") on February 28 (i.e., today).","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180228_11928563.htm"],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","A total of 31 specific measures were introduced this time, of which 12 measures involve accelerating equal treatment of Taiwan-invested enterprises with mainland enterprises. These mainly include clarifying that Taiwan-invested enterprises enjoy the same treatment as mainland enterprises in participating in \"Made in China 2025,\" enjoying tax preferential policies, participating in national key research and development programs, infrastructure construction, government procurement, and mixed-ownership reform of state-owned enterprises; clarifying the land use of Taiwan-invested enterprises, relocation to the central and western regions and northeastern region, and the relevant policies available to Taiwan-invested agricultural enterprises; and supporting deeper financial cooperation between businesspeople on both sides in areas such as small-value payments, credit reference services, and syndicated loans. In addition, 19 measures involve gradually providing Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland. These mainly include opening 134 national professional qualification examinations to Taiwan compatriots, providing more convenience for Taiwan people to obtain professional qualifications and find employment on the mainland, allowing Taiwan compatriots to apply for the \"Thousand Talents Plan,\" the \"Ten Thousand Talents Program,\" and various fund projects, participating in the Chinese fine traditional culture inheritance and development project and award programs and honorary title selections, joining professional associations and industry associations, participating in grassroots work on the mainland, and relaxing market access restrictions for Taiwan film, television, and books.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","To summarize, these 31 measures have three main features. First, the measures introduced this time revolve around major national action plans and national key R&D program projects, providing Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland enterprises and mainland compatriots. For example, Taiwan-invested enterprises participating in the “Made in China 2025” action plan are subject to the same policies as mainland enterprises. Second, they are tailor-made. During the drafting of the Several Measures (若干措施), the special circumstances and needs of Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots were fully taken into account, and widespread concerns of Taiwan enterprises and compatriots were addressed with highly targeted solutions. For example, the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zones will continue to be established in central and western China and the northeast; Taiwan-invested enterprises are encouraged to relocate and participate in the Belt and Road initiative; and market opening in radio and television program production will be expanded. Third, the benefits are broad. The Several Measures cover multiple fields, including industry, finance and taxation, land use, finance, employment, education, culture, healthcare, and film and television. The scale of opening, breadth of scope, and number of departments involved are unprecedented, and they will substantially expand the scope of benefits and the sense of gain for Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","These measures will bring huge opportunities and tangible benefits to Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan compatriots. For Taiwan-funded enterprises, the measures will help them reduce production and operating costs, accelerate transformation and upgrading, expand the domestic market, gain more business opportunities, and achieve greater development. For Taiwan compatriots, the measures will provide more convenience for studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland, create better conditions, and promote cross-Strait compatriots’ joint promotion of Chinese culture and deeper spiritual affinity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will continue to uphold the concept of “Cross-Strait Compatriots Are One Family,” work with the National Development and Reform Commission and other relevant departments to strengthen policy implementation, assess implementation effects, and, as needed, study and formulate more policy measures to expand and deepen economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, and continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","新华社记者","May I ask the spokesperson: under the current circumstances, what were the main considerations behind issuing the \"Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation\"? What is its important significance?","The issuance of the “Several Measures” is an important embodiment of conscientiously implementing General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thinking on work toward Taiwan and the spirit of the 19th CPC National Congress. The “Several Measures” strive to provide Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots with treatment equal to that of mainland enterprises and mainland compatriots. They will bring tangible benefits to Taiwan enterprises investing and doing business on the mainland and to broad Taiwan compatriots developing on the mainland, reflecting our sincere wish to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and highlighting the important concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family.” The issuance of the “Several Measures” owes much to the collective efforts and joint support of relevant departments, demonstrating the determination and sincerity of all relevant mainland parties to coordinate and do concrete good deeds for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople. Implementing the “Several Measures” will help further expand and deepen cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, achieve mutual benefit, and continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180228_11928562.htm"],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","中央电视台中国新闻记者","Before the Spring Festival, an earthquake occurred in Hualien, Taiwan. Could you briefly introduce the specific situation of condolences and donations from all parties on the mainland, and the handling of post-disaster affairs for mainland tourists?","After the “2·6” earthquake in Hualien, Taiwan, relevant parties and all sectors of society on the mainland expressed deep concern. Zhang Zhijun, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, immediately expressed condolences to the affected people and said that the mainland was willing to provide all necessary assistance. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, the Red Cross Society of China, the China Seismological Society, and other relevant parties, as well as several provinces, municipalities, and autonomous regions, quickly expressed condolences and mourning to the affected compatriots and the compatriots on both sides of the Strait who died, and expressed their willingness to provide all necessary assistance and donations, including rescue equipment. According to incomplete statistics, relevant mainland parties, institutions and enterprises in Taiwan, some provinces, municipalities, and autonomous regions, and Taiwan-funded enterprises have donated a total of RMB 23.075 million.\nThis earthquake killed 9 mainland tourists and injured 6. Relevant mainland parties attach great importance to this, activated emergency mechanisms, opened a “green channel,” and provided comprehensive assistance to family members of the deceased tourists traveling to Taiwan. The Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office also dispatched a working group to Taiwan to assist the families in handling post-disaster matters. Relevant Taiwan authorities, the Hualien County Government, and the relevant units involved in the rescue have also made positive efforts in rescue and treatment, in assisting in caring for the injured mainland tourists, and in caring for the families of the deceased, and we appreciate this.\nIt is understood that the bodies of the two mainland victims whose identities were finally confirmed were removed on the afternoon of the 25th. Relevant mainland insurance companies have initiated claims settlement procedures, and we also hope that relevant Taiwan authorities will properly handle the post-disaster arrangements for the victims in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180228_11928559.htm"],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","After the Hualien earthquake, Cai Yingwen thanked all parties on the mainland for their condolences and donations in a Facebook post written in simplified characters. In addition, at the Taiwan business community’s Spring Festival gathering, when she mentioned cross-Strait policy, Cai Yingwen’s attitude also showed signs of a so-called “shift from hard to soft.” Some public opinion believes this sends a goodwill…","We have noted the relevant reports you mentioned. As everyone knows, the crux of the current political impasse across the Strait lies in the damage done to the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We have stated on many occasions that whether one acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and recognizes that both sides of the Strait belong to one China is the touchstone for testing whether the Taiwan authorities sincerely want to improve cross-Strait relations.\nTo our understanding, it is indeed the case that recently some delegations from Taiwan Affairs Offices of mainland provinces and municipalities seeking to visit Taiwan have not been approved by the relevant Taiwan authorities on various pretexts. The Taiwan authorities' practice of obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation appears to run counter to the so-called goodwill they profess to advance the development of cross-Strait relations. Therefore, whether cross-Strait relations can truly improve depends not on oral expressions of goodwill, but on concrete action.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180228_11928561.htm"],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Tsai Ing-wen mentioned at a New Year's gala evening last night that Taiwan's position on maintaining the status quo in cross-strait relations will not change. But she also said that maintaining the status quo in cross-strait relations is not a unilateral responsibility, and that she hopes both sides will work together to achieve it. What is your assessment of her remarks? In addition, Taiwan's senior leadership…","On your first question, everyone can see clearly that since 2008, through the joint efforts of both sides of the Strait and compatriots on both sides, a brand-new situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has been created, and compatriots on both sides have shared its benefits. Since “5.20” in 2016, because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and to recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, they have unilaterally undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. In other words, the status quo has already been undermined by the Taiwan side. Under the current circumstances, our position of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle, and opposing “Taiwan independence” is very clear. Rather than talking empty words about maintaining the status quo, the Taiwan side should consider how to return to the correct track of the “1992 Consensus,” so that cross-Strait relations can once again move toward the broad road of peaceful development.\nOn your second question, we do not comment on personnel changes within Taiwan. What we care about is whether the cross-Strait policy of the Taiwan authorities can return to the correct track of the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","国际台记者","This Spring Festival, because the Taiwan authorities did not approve extra flights for two mainland airlines, air tickets to Taiwan were in short supply. May I ask the spokesperson what measures the mainland side has taken to help Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots return home for the holiday? In addition, for those Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots who could not go home and stayed in the…","Before the Spring Festival, because the Taiwan authorities refused to approve additional Spring Festival flights for China Eastern and Xiamen Airlines, relevant parties on the mainland took various measures to fully ensure that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots on the mainland could return home for the holiday. In strengthening transport capacity scheduling and transportation support, China Eastern and Xiamen Airlines promptly issued notices via SMS, email and other means, informing passengers of the policies for free refund, change and rebooking to minimize passengers' losses as much as possible. In addition, Shanghai, Fujian and other places have also improved their emergency additional-flight systems, and dispatched aviation and shipping capacity, especially strengthening the capacity of the “mini three links” routes. During the seven-day Spring Festival, from February 15 to February 21, a total of 42,300 passenger trips were carried through the “mini three links” and other maritime passenger routes, an increase of 17.32% over the same period last year. To promptly resolve difficulties Taiwan compatriots encountered on their journey home, all localities have also actively provided travel services: they launched 24-hour hotlines for Taiwan compatriots returning home, set up Taiwan compatriot service desks at airports and ports, and provided warm services such as tea, medicine and free internet access in waiting areas for Taiwan compatriots. Additionally, it is understood that this year many Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots chose to stay on the mainland for the New Year, and some Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan officials brought their relatives to the mainland for reunions. Relevant departments in various localities also visited Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople who stayed on the mainland for the New Year, bringing New Year goods and festive greetings, and celebrated the Spring Festival with them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201802/t20180228_11928560.htm"],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Today is the 71st anniversary of the “2·28 Incident.” We know the “2·28 Incident” had a major impact in Taiwan, especially the “anti-China” attitudes of the Green camp toward the mainland. What is the mainland's view of “2·28” now?","Today marks the 71st anniversary of the “2·28 Incident.” The mainland's position on the “2·28 Incident” is very clear. We believe the “2·28 Incident” was a just action by Taiwan compatriots opposing autocratic rule and fighting for basic rights, and part of the Chinese people's struggle for liberation. What we oppose is any distortion of historical facts, or any attempt to use this incident to agitate for and promote “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","After the Hualien earthquake, a Fujian reporter stationed in Taiwan was asked by relevant Taiwan authorities to correct his report, because he disclosed that Japanese rescue teams were worried about danger and therefore did not enter the affected building. The authorities did not rule out revoking his press credentials in Taiwan. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of the situation and what is your…","As we understand it, after the recent Hualien earthquake in Taiwan, mainland resident correspondents in Taiwan rushed to the earthquake site overnight at the first moment, and for several consecutive days reported timely and objective information on the disaster and relief efforts for mainland audiences. The professional competence and dedication of our resident correspondents deserve recognition. In addition, the resident correspondents voluntarily donated NT$150,000 to the affected areas, offering their own modest contribution to the disaster-stricken people. Reporting truthfully and objectively about Taiwan, promoting kinship and mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides, is the mission and original aspiration of mainland journalists reporting in Taiwan. I want to stress here that the objective and impartial reporting of mainland journalists in Taiwan should be respected, and the legitimate rights and interests and good environment they should enjoy while reporting in Taiwan should be effectively guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","Reports say the KMT-CPC Forum will be held in late April. Could you introduce the current preparations for the KMT-CPC Forum?","Since 2005, exchanges and cooperation between our side and the Kuomintang have been strengthened on the political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and the achievements are plain for all to see. As for the specific arrangements for this year's forum, we have maintained communication and contact with the KMT and other relevant parties. When there is definite news, we will announce it in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","According to reports, the honorary chairman of the Zhangzhou Taiwan Business Association recently said in an interview while attending an event in Taiwan that he would do his utmost to support the decisions of the DPP authorities. Some mainland netizens pointed out that this person is a “two-faced Taiwan businessman.” The current chairman of the Zhangzhou Taiwan Business Association publicly stated on this matter…","We have noted the relevant reports, and we have also noted the formal statement made on this matter by the current president of the Zhangzhou Taiwan Business Association.\nOur position and attitude on this issue are very clear. We welcome Taiwan businesspeople to invest and start businesses on the mainland, but at the same time, we will never allow a small number of people to earn money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” and undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","It is understood that after the Hualien earthquake, the Taiwan authorities refused to let mainland rescue teams enter Taiwan, but welcomed a Japanese rescue team. However, the Japanese rescue team entered the disaster area but did not enter the rescue sites, which has sparked controversy. What is the spokesperson’s view on this incident?","After the Hualien earthquake, all sectors on the mainland expressed concern and condolences, stated their willingness to provide all necessary assistance, and actively made donations. The reason the mainland side and mainland compatriots did this has no other purpose or consideration; it is simply because compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, with kinship of blood thicker than water.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","We note that a delegation composed of some members of the US House of Representatives and Senate recently visited Taiwan and met with Tsai Ing-wen, who said she hopes US-Taiwan relations can reach a higher level. May I ask for the spokesperson's assessment?","We have stated many times that we firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and Taiwan, and we also firmly oppose the United States selling arms to Taiwan on any pretext. This position and attitude are very clear. We also advise the Taiwan side not to rely on foreign powers to assert itself, or else it will reap what it sows.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","The Year of the Dog spring couplets that Ma Ying-jeou personally calligraphed and printed to give to the public before the Spring Festival have sparked discussion on both sides of the Strait. They were snapped up by Taiwan residents and have also proved popular with mainland netizens. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Spring couplets that embody excellent traditional Chinese culture should always be loved by people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","台声杂志社记者","According to reports in Taiwan media, on February 25 former Taiwan leader Ma Ying-jeou stated in an interview that cross-Strait relations are currently in a state of cold confrontation with a grave situation, and said that the conditions for cross-Strait unification are not yet ripe. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this?","In fact, everyone can see very clearly that the current situation in cross-Strait relations is grave. The fundamental cause lies in the fact that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only when the Taiwan side returns to the track of the \"1992 Consensus\" can cross-Strait relations return to a virtuous cycle of peaceful development. As for resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the peaceful reunification of the motherland, this is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants and an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Therefore, we will continue to adhere to the policy of \"peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems,\" actively promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","中国华艺广播公司记者","During the Spring Festival, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council repeatedly promoted the \"Taiwan businessman Mr. Zhang\" hotline, but people discovered that the hotline is located in Taiwan, so Taiwanese businesspeople must call across the sea to make inquiries. If Taiwanese businesspeople truly want to understand investment policies on the mainland, through what proper channels should they seek this information?","At previous press conferences we have also said many times that the mainland has done a great deal of work to provide Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment and developing their careers on the mainland. This includes providing relevant employment, entrepreneurship and investment information, holding various job fairs, publishing relevant information on websites, and providing relevant information to employment teams at entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites, among other things. All of this can be found on the relevant websites.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Recently, Taiwan media revealed that an expert at a U.S. think tank claimed that U.S. President Trump would declare the Taiwan Strait international waters. Some Taiwan media have also jumped on the bandwagon, hyping that this could further counter the mainland threat. May I ask the spokesperson what views it has on this?","I have not seen the statement you mention. But internationally, there is indeed a force that has always wanted to stir up trouble in the Taiwan Strait in order to profit from it and contain China’s rise, and such small maneuvers have never stopped. As for cross-Strait relations, we have always said that the two sides are flesh-and-blood brothers. As the ancient saying goes, “Brothers may squabble within the family, but they unite to resist outside insults.” Over the past 100-odd years, the Chinese nation has endured suffering and rises and falls, and now we have finally welcomed a precious opportunity for national rejuvenation. We are closer than ever in history to the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. At this moment, we should be even more united, as brothers, in creating brilliance together. But some people in Taiwan do not pursue this and instead go against the trend, serving as pawns for outsiders to contain China’s rise, even at the cost of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, gambling with the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Would this not be painful to those close to us and delightful to our enemies?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","The CCTV Spring Festival Gala skit “Going Home” was starred by three Taiwan actors. Some Taiwan public opinion criticized that this skit has a “united front” flavor. In addition, regarding the lines and character images, a writer published an article saying it is somewhat discriminatory against Taiwanese people, which also caused some discussion. May I ask how the spokesperson views this?","This year's CCTV Spring Festival Gala sketch “Going Home” should be said to have touched the hearts of many viewers on both sides of the Strait. I also learned from later media interviews that this sketch was created based on the personal experiences of the two Taiwanese actors who performed in it. In the words of the Taiwanese actors themselves, the purpose of this program was to let both sides of the Strait know that we are all of the Chinese nation. Some people on the island say they do not understand the feeling of going home, which in fact is because they do not understand their own roots. So I think: for literary and artistic works that reflect the homesickness of wanderers, if one interprets them as “united front” work or discrimination, I can only say that if one wears “green”-tinted glasses, then the whole world looks “green.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Recently, some Taiwan media, noting that developments in Taiwan in the Wuxu Year of the Dog remain full of challenges and uncertainty, offered Taiwan three wishes for the Year of the Dog: first, social harmony; second, economic prosperity; third, peace across the Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment? On the second question: a 2018 large-scale survey of public opinion in Taiwan recently published by Taiwan…","Regarding your first question, I think the three wishes mentioned there are also the shared wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. However, one situation worth noting is that a reverse current of “Taiwan independence” separatism on the island is stirring, constantly agitating for so-called referendums and “constitutional amendment,” inciting hostility and confrontation between compatriots on both sides. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and it is also a realistic threat to our shared good wishes across the Strait.\nRegarding your second question, we will not comment on specific public opinion polls on the island. Compatriots on both sides are one family, and seeking well-being for compatriots on both sides has always been the starting point and end point of the mainland's development of cross-Strait relations. Last year marked the 30th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait exchanges, and the 30 years of development of cross-Strait relations have also fully proven that the mainland side has consistently promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, while “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to cross-Strait relations. The one-China principle is an important cornerstone for ensuring the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It is our common wish for people on both sides of the Strait to exchange, cooperate, and develop; this is what people's hearts desire and the general trend of the times.\nThis year marks the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up on the mainland. The achievements of the mainland's 40 years of reform and opening up are plain for all to see, and the various policies toward Taiwan promoted by the mainland in recent years that benefit the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots have stood the test of time. Comparing the current situation in Taiwan society with the words and deeds of the Taiwan authorities, I think it is only natural that more Taiwan residents would reach such a judgment and make such a choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-02-28","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Dong Yunshang, the nominee for Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs, recently stated before the US Congress that a US official website removed the flag of the so-called “Republic of China” because the US does not recognize Taiwan as a “sovereign and independent state.” What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","The One-China principle is the political foundation for the development of China-U.S. relations and the basic guideline for both sides in handling Taiwan-related affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201802/t20180228_11928558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-03-01","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, an Australian scholar's book entitled \"Silent Invasion: China's Influence in Australia\" was published in Australia on February 26. The Australian business community and academic institutions have criticized the book as inventing stories for malicious sensationalization, condemning the author for poisoning Australia-China relations for achieving fame. What's your comment on that?","We have noted relevant reports and that there is much criticism of the author and denunciation of the book. I would like to say that China has remained committed to conducting friendly exchange and practical cooperation with other countries based on such principles as mutual respect and non-interference in each other's internal affairs. Certain individual's malicious hyping up and slander on China are completely meaningless and good for nothing. Just as an ancient Chinese poem said, \"despite the incessant cry of apes from the banks, the swift boat has already sailed through thousands of hills\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1538767.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1538703.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-03-01","Hua Chunying","","The US Senate has passed the Taiwan Travel Act. What is China's comment on this?","Some of the act's clauses, though not legally binding, still severely violate the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués between China and the US. China is strongly dissatisfied with that and also firmly opposes it. We have lodged stern representations with the US side.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of the China-US relationship. We urge the US side to adhere to the one-China policy and honor the commitments it made in the three joint communiqués, stop pursuing any official ties with Taiwan or improving its current relations with Taiwan in any substantive way. It must handle Taiwan-related issues properly and cautiously so as to avoid causing any major disruption or damage to the China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1538767.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1538703.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-03-02","Hua Chunying","","China Daily said today that if the US was to pass the new bill which will encourage high-level exchanges between the US and Taiwan, including at official level, this might trigger the Anti-Secession Law which would allow Beijing to use force to stop Taiwan from attempting an independence. Is this a view that you agree with?","We usually make no comment on the opinions made by the media. I already made clear China's stern position on this issue yesterday. I would like to stress again that the one-China principle is the political foundation of the China-US relationship. We urge the US side to adhere to the one-China policy and honor the commitments it made in the three joint communiqués, stop pursuing any official ties with Taiwan or improving its current relations with Taiwan in any substantive way. It must handle Taiwan-related issues cautiously and properly so as to avoid causing any major disruption or damage to the China-US relations.\nThank you for joining us today. Wish you a happy Lantern Festival!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1539127.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1539018.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-03-02","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 2 — In response to the US Senate's passage of the “Taiwan Travel Act,” TAO spokesperson 安峰山 said in response to a question on the 2nd: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position and attitude on this. I want to emphasize that the US Congress's passage of a series of Taiwan-related bills seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose them. We also warn Taiwan: do not rely on foreign powers to elevate yourselves, or you will only be playing with fire and burning yourselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180302_11929473.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-03-06","Geng Shuang","","Some African countries still have the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. What effort has China made to win back these African countries and establish diplomatic relations with them?","The one-China principle is the widespread consensus of the international community and adhering to this principle also represents the trend of the times. China is willing to develop friendly relations and conduct cooperation with all the other countries around the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1539946.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1539886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-03-06","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, the DPRK leader Kim Jong-un \"unusually\" met with the special delegation sent by the ROK to Pyongyang and said that the two sides will write a new chapter of national reunification. The Korean Central News Agency said that the US should not make misjudgment on DPRK's willingness to hold negotiations with it. What is your comment on this?","Just as I said yesterday, the ROK sent a special delegation to the DPRK to exchange views on relevant issues and China believes that this is good news. We have also noted the positive media reports on the ROK special delegation's visit to the DPRK.\nChina always maintains that the DPRK-ROK interactions should bring about the ones between all relevant parties, including between the DPRK and the US and the dialogue during the Pyeongchang Winter Olympic Games should continue as a regular one, and that the efforts to improve the DPRK-ROK relations should lead to the concerted ones that will realize the denuclearization and achieve the lasting peace of the Peninsula. China stands ready to make efforts and play a positive role to this end.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1539946.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1539886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-03-16","Lu Kang","","According to reports, the US government has said that it has yet to decide whether to go ahead and sign the Taiwan Travel Act. But the bill could automatically become law on Saturday. I would like to ask if that does become a US law, how would China respond?","We have made clear our position on this issue many times. I bet even if I don't repeat it, you already know by heart the position of the Chinese government.\nThe relevant clauses of the act mentioned by you, though not legally binding, still severely violate the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués between China and the US. China is strongly dissatisfied with that and also firmly opposes it. We have lodged stern representations with the US side.\nI must reiterate that the one-China principle is the political foundation of the China-US relationship. We urge the US side to adhere to the one-China policy and honor the commitments it made in the three joint communiqués, stop pursuing any official ties with Taiwan or improving its current relations with Taiwan in any substantive way. It must handle Taiwan-related issues properly and cautiously so as to avoid causing any major disruption or damage to the China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1543040.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1542945.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-03-17","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On March 16, local time, the U.S. side signed the \"Taiwan Travel Act,\" and the Chinese military resolutely opposes it.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Although the relevant provisions of this act are not legally binding, they seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, interfere in China's internal affairs, and damage the atmosphere for the development of China-U.S. and China-U.S. military-to-military relations. China demands that the U.S. side keep its commitments and correct its mistakes, not implement the relevant provisions of the above act, stop official exchanges between the U.S. and Taiwan, stop military contacts between the U.S. and Taiwan, and stop arms sales to Taiwan, so as to avoid causing serious damage to China-U.S. relations, the military-to-military relationship between the two countries, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2018-03/17/content_4807061.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2018-03-18","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 18 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — In response to a question about the U.S. signing of the “Taiwan Relations Reinforcement Act,” An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 18th that some provisions of this act seriously violate the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and send a grave and erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We firmly oppose this. I also solemnly warn the Taiwan authorities once again: those who rely on foreign backing to wield influence will surely bring disaster upon themselves.\nIn answering reporters’ questions, An Fengshan pointed out that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other departments have already stated our firm opposition to the U.S. signing of the “Taiwan Relations Reinforcement Act” and have lodged stern representations with the U.S. side. Although the provisions of this act are not legally binding, they seriously violate the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, send a grave and erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and cause serious impact on the complex and severe situation in cross-Strait relations and on peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose this. I also solemnly warn the Taiwan authorities once again: those who rely on foreign backing to wield influence will surely bring disaster upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180318_11934381.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-20","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 20 (reporter Zha Wenye) — According to media reports, Lai Ching-te, head of the executive branch of the Taiwan authorities, claimed on the 20th that Taiwan is a “sovereign and independent country,” and that the fact of “Taiwan's sovereign independence” will not change because of outside influence. An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response that this blatant “Taiwan independence” rhetoric is a serious provocation to cross-Strait relations and will certainly reap what it sows.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory and has never been, and never will be, a country. We firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. All acts and schemes to split the country are doomed to fail and will be condemned by the people and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180320_11935353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-03-21","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State Alex N. Wong of the Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs is currently visiting Taiwan. He is going to address a meeting tonight which will also be attended by Tsai Ing-wen. Is the Chinese government upset at the fact that a US official is visiting Taiwan so soon after the US side signed into law the \"Taiwan Travel Act\"?","China firmly opposes the so-called \"Taiwan Travel Act\" and has lodged stern representations with the US side regarding the situation you just mentioned. We urge the US to abide by the the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués between China and the US, stop pursuing official exchanges and contacts in any form with Taiwan, and cautiously and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid causing severe damage to the China-US relations and cross-Straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1544122.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1544125.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-03-22","Hua Chunying","","A senior US diplomat gave a speech yesterday in Taipei, in which he said that \"Taiwan-US relations\" had never been stronger and he praised Taiwan as a \"model\" for the Indo-Pacific region. The Taiwan authorities announced today that another senior US official will be visiting this week from the Commerce Department. What is your response to the comments yesterday and this second visit in a week by a senior US…","Yesterday I already made clear China's stance on the recent contacts between the US and Taiwan. I want to stress again that the Taiwan issue concerns China's core interests and is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations, and the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China policy and the three joint communiqués, stop pursuing any official ties with Taiwan or elevating its current relations with Taiwan in any substantive way and handle Taiwan-related issues cautiously and properly so as to avoid causing any major damage to the China-US relations and cross-Straits peace and stability.\nI would also like to remind those who want to play the \"Taiwan card\" or have any other attempt that they need to attentively read and study President Xi Jinping's important remarks delivered at the closing ceremony of the First Session of the 13th National People's Congress (NPC), in particular the part that involves China's attitude on upholding its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Not a single inch of our great motherland could be ceded from China. We hope relevant persons will speak and act with caution on the Taiwan issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1544674.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1544556.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone. Thank you for attending the TAO regular press conference held this morning. I am willing to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","新华社记者","The “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots” have been formally issued and implemented for one month and have drawn wide attention. I would like to ask the spokesperson how implementation work will be carried out going forward, and what progress has been made so far?","Today marks one month since the “31 Measures” were issued. The “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation,” implemented since their release on February 28, have drawn close attention from all sectors on both sides of the Strait and widespread praise from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. These measures are a concrete embodiment of implementing the spirit of the 19th Party Congress and General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thinking on work toward Taiwan. They genuinely respond to the demands and expectations of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises, fully reflect our adherence to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and our sincerity in taking the lead in sharing the mainland's development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, accelerating the provision of equal treatment, and doing good and practical things for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. Localities and relevant departments are actively promoting the implementation of the various measures, striving to make these good things happen so that Taiwan compatriots truly benefit.\nAt present, the implementation of the 31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots is being rolled out in full, and progress has already been made on some measures. For example, regarding the eligibility of certain cross-Strait cultural projects for inclusion in the resource pool of the Chinese Cultural Centers Overseas project, relevant departments have clarified that Taiwan compatriots may submit applications through the Chinese Culture Friendship Association. Themed activities in which cross-Strait cultural and creative institutions and artists jointly promote Chinese culture overseas are also being arranged. As for the implementation in localities, here are a few examples. In Shanghai, Jiangsu, Fujian and other areas where Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises are concentrated and cross-Strait exchange and cooperation are in-depth, a number of pilot measures have been implemented and have achieved initial results. According to our understanding, Shanghai has put 12 equal-treatment measures into effect, including encouraging Taiwan-invested enterprises to participate in major Shanghai construction projects, reducing taxes for high-tech Taiwan-invested enterprises, and allowing pilot project cooperation in cross-Strait economic cooperation and financial institution cooperation. Kunshan City in Jiangsu has 17 measures that have been or are being implemented, including 42 Taiwan-invested headquarters enterprises receiving cumulative local awards of 83.03 million yuan, leading agricultural enterprises at all levels receiving subsidies of 700,000 yuan and project support funds of 1 million yuan, and Taiwanese construction companies directly participating in the preliminary design of the Kunshan Zhonghuan Expressway. Fujian Province has 22 measures that have been or are being promoted, including 39 high-tech Taiwan-invested enterprises enjoying tax preferential policies in total, the implementation of 33 Fujian-Taiwan science and technology cooperation projects, of which 4 projects are led by Taiwanese experts, and Changhua Bank's Fuzhou branch and Cooperative Bank's Fuzhou branch participating in syndicated loans for projects, among other things.\nIn the future, we will continue to carefully study new situations, actively respond to the demands of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises, successively introduce more policy measures, expand and deepen cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, and continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937832.htm"],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中央人民广播电台记者","We note that in his important speech at the closing ceremony of the “Two Sessions,” President Xi Jinping comprehensively expounded the policies and principles toward Taiwan, and issued a stern warning to the “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities. How does the spokesperson interpret this?","Cross-Strait relations are becoming more complex and grim. The Taiwan authorities refuse to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, tolerate and abet \"de-Sinicization\" and \"gradual Taiwan independence,\" and obstruct and interfere with cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Separatist \"Taiwan independence\" forces on the island are stepping up efforts to push the so-called \"Taiwan name-rectification referendum,\" which is aimed at splitting the country. Certain external forces are attempting to play the \"Taiwan card,\" creating difficulties for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. These actions endanger the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nFaced with this complex and grim situation, we resolutely implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thinking on work concerning Taiwan and the Party Central Committee's major policies on Taiwan work, and we firmly oppose and contain any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes and actions. We will never tolerate \"Taiwan independence\" forces undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait or interfering with the process of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. All acts and schemes to split the country are doomed to fail and will be condemned by the people and punished by history!\nThe peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to safeguarding peace across the Strait, promoting common development, and benefiting compatriots on both sides, and it is also a bright road leading to peaceful reunification. We must adhere to the one-China principle, uphold the \"1992 Consensus,\" advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, expand economic, cultural and exchange and cooperation across the Strait, share the opportunities of mainland development with Taiwan compatriots, enhance the well-being of compatriots, and promote heart-to-heart connection among compatriots on both sides. We recently issued 31 measures to promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, and we are accelerating the provision of equal treatment to Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan compatriots. We will also continue to do practical things and good things for compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, resolutely advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and solidly push forward the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937833.htm"],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","You just mentioned that the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots” issued by the mainland have received wide praise from the public on the island, but the Taiwan authorities have come up with “four directions” and “eight strategies” as a passive response, claiming the 31 measures are “in name benefiting Taiwan” but in fact benefit the mainland, and that about half of the measures are old ones. What is the…","For many years, in response to the demands and expectations of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, we have upheld the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and have continuously promoted pilot implementation by relevant localities and fields first, providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses. The “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” recently introduced not only extend the pilot practices comprehensively, but also include many new policies, new measures, and new content. This is a policy measure that the mainland has taken the initiative to introduce to benefit Taiwan compatriots, and it has been warmly welcomed and generally affirmed by Taiwan compatriots: “the common people keep a scale in their hearts.” Yet the Taiwan side not only has failed to meet us halfway, but has instead come up with so-called “countermeasures,” which in fact aim to further restrict the opportunities and space for broad Taiwan compatriots to develop on the mainland, harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses. The DPP authorities should actively respond to the demands of Taiwan residents, respect the desire of people on both sides of the Strait to deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, respect market rules, and respect the choices of Taiwan compatriots. If they go in the opposite direction, they will only put themselves in a more passive position.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937831.htm"],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Huang Zhihan, as well as Royce, Chairman of the US House Committee on Foreign Affairs, successively visited Taiwan. With the Taiwan-US defense industry cooperation conference that may be held in Taiwan in May, and the completion of the new AIT building in June, the US may send even higher-level officials to visit Taiwan. What is…","Our relevant departments have already expressed our solemn position and attitude on this. The US side should abide by and uphold its commitment to the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and not conduct any form of official exchanges or contact with the Taiwan side. Any external force attempting to play the “Taiwan card” is bound to fail. Doing so harms the interests of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and is also a form of deceiving Taiwan compatriots. We also solemnly warn the Taiwan authorities that relying on outside backing to put on airs will only bring fire upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937828.htm"],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中国国际广播电台记者","The “2020 Tokyo Olympics Taiwan name-change referendum” promoted by pro-“Taiwan independence” forces on the island has recently passed proposal review and will enter the petition signature stage. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","We have noted that this matter has already caused widespread concern and vigilance on the island. A very small number of people in Taiwan are manipulating the so-called “name-rectification referendum,” tearing apart Taiwan society, harming the interests of compatriots, and provoking cross-Strait relations, and their true intention is not in the wine. I want to stress that any political scheme to pursue “Taiwan independence” separation through “referendum” or “name-rectification” is extremely dangerous and is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937830.htm"],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中天电视台记者","Former MAC Chairperson Chang Hsiao-yueh has formally taken over as Chairperson of the SEF, and she has said that she hopes to meet with ARATS Chairman Chen Deming at an appropriate time, on the basis of equality, reciprocity, and dignity. The SEF has sent a letter notifying ARATS, but has not yet received a response from ARATS. When will the mainland respond to the SEF?","We will not comment on personnel changes within Taiwan. The causes and crux of the current political deadlock across the Strait are in fact clear to everyone. What we care about is whether the Taiwan authorities' cross-Strait policy can return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","香港中评社中评网记者","We understand that the Taiwan film “Johnny Ke” is about to be released on the mainland. Recently, netizens have pointed out that one of the film's lead actors, Ke Yu-lun, has previously made “Taiwan independence” statements and actions, and supported his father, film director Ke Yi-cheng's “Taiwan independence” stance and the New Power Party in Taiwan. Spokesperson, are you aware of the relevant situation, and…","According to our understanding, the competent authorities are already aware of the situation you mentioned, and have stated that they will not allow films involving Taiwan entertainers who hold “Taiwan independence” positions or engage in “Taiwan independence” words and deeds to be screened on the mainland. If these Taiwan entertainers recognize the errors and harm of “Taiwan independence” and change their thinking and actions, we welcome that. At present, the screening of this film on the mainland has been put on hold.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, Taiwan businessman Li Jung-fu published a newspaper apology for his improper remarks made at the Straits Exchange Foundation's Spring Festival gathering, stating that he firmly opposes “Taiwan independence,” firmly supports the “1992 Consensus” and “one China across the Strait,” and hopes for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted the relevant statement. We support Taiwan-funded enterprises investing and developing on the mainland, and we also hope and believe that the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople will shoulder their social responsibility, promote cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, support the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, and promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","Kuan Chung-ming, president-elect of National Taiwan University, was alleged to have visited the mainland 28 times from 2005 until now, and was therefore investigated. What is your view of the storm that the NTU president case has caused in Taiwan?","I am not aware of the specific situation you mentioned. What I understand is that Xiamen University, in response to an inquiry letter from the acting president of National Taiwan University, explained the relevant situation by letter. Mr. Guan Minzhong was once hired by the School of Economics of Xiamen University as a visiting professor, but he did not teach and received no remuneration. Professor Guan did not hold a teaching post at Xiamen University, did not offer professional courses, did not serve as a supervisor for master's or doctoral students, and did not receive any pay.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","Is it possible for the KMT-CPC Forum to be held in late April, and if so, where will it be held? Second question: Director Liu Jieyi has just held talks with Chu Li-lun in Shanghai. How will these talks help in holding the Cross-Strait Peace Forum or the KMT-CPC Forum?","First, regarding the forum you mentioned, the mainland side has maintained communication and consultation with relevant parties, including the Kuomintang, and when there is a definite outcome we will announce it in a timely manner.\nSecond, regarding the visit of Mayor Eric Chu to the mainland: from March 21 to 26, New Taipei City Mayor Eric Chu led a New Taipei City delegation to visit Jiangsu, Shanghai and other places. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the State Council, met Mr. Eric Chu in Shanghai, and the main leaders of the relevant provinces and cities also separately met Chu and his party locally. Both sides exchanged in-depth views on adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” promoting the development of cross-Strait relations, and strengthening cross-Strait urban exchange and cooperation. For specific details, you may refer to the press release issued after the meeting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","厦门卫视记者","It is reported that the Beijing High People's Court will announce the second-instance verdict in the Kenya telecom fraud case today. Please introduce the relevant situation.","According to information from the relevant departments, the Kenyan cross-border telecom fraud case was publicly pronounced today in accordance with the law by the Beijing Higher People's Court in its second-instance trial. In the course of the trial, judicial authorities strictly observed legal provisions and statutory procedures, fully safeguarded the procedural rights enjoyed by the defendants, and rendered the judgment in accordance with the law. Specific details may be inquired of the adjudicating authorities. I want to emphasize again that the Mainland side brings cross-border telecom fraud criminals to justice, which has been fully affirmed and recognized by compatriots on both sides and has also received understanding and support from the international community. We will continue, adhering to the position that is conducive to combating crime, conducive to maintaining judicial fairness, and conducive to protecting the rights and interests of victims, to punish telecom fraud crimes in accordance with the law, and will never allow any criminal to escape justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","After Director Liu Jieyi met with New Taipei Mayor Chu Li-lun in Shanghai, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council issued a press release stating that it hopes the two sides can communicate without preconditions, which is the only way to ensure the rights of the public and resolve disputes. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","As I said earlier, Mayor Chu Li-luan’s visit is for cross-Strait city exchange.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","In his speech, Taipei Mayor Chu Li-lun said that upholding the “1992 Consensus” has been the consistent position of the Kuomintang, but its meaning is somewhat different. Some voices within Taiwan interpret it as still implying the issue of “One China, each side with its own interpretation.” May I ask the Taiwan Affairs Office for its comment on this? Lai Ching-te said that this means there is no consensus…","The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Since 2005, the KMT and the CPC, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have moved toward each other and jointly promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We are also willing to work with the KMT, on the basis of continuing to uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and safeguard the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","We have noticed that many Taiwan businesspeople are very worried that a China-US trade war is about to break out and may bring problems to their industries. In response to these concerns, Chen Deming, chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait, said on the 25th at the 2018 annual meeting of the China Development High-Level Forum that the trade war will certainly have some impact on Taiwan,…","On the China-U.S. trade issue, the relevant departments have already stated our position. ARATS Chairman Chen Deming also expressed our attitude of protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses when interviewed by reporters. We support Taiwan-funded enterprises putting down roots and developing on the mainland. This attitude is very clear. We are actively implementing the ‘Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,’ from which Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan compatriots will benefit. The investment and development prospects of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland are bright.\nIn addition, the mainland is the world’s second-largest economy. Its economy has entered a stage of high-quality development, its domestic market is huge, and the mainland firmly supports and promotes the process of economic globalization, which has been widely welcomed by the international community. Our future development potential is enormous. So we believe Taiwan-funded enterprises and broad Taiwan compatriots will continue to be optimistic about the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently, officials from the U.S. Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs visited Taiwan, and the American Institute in Taiwan will also relocate. Some Taiwan media have speculated that a U.S. Navy unit may be stationed at the new AIT site. How do you evaluate this?","Our principled position on this issue has been stated many times. The United States should honor its commitments to the one-China policy and the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués, and not develop any form of official exchanges or contacts with Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We noted that Kaohsiung Mayor Chen Chu recently said, during her visit to the United States, that the current development of cross-Strait relations is regrettable, and that she is worried that if the two sides do not communicate or interact, ... She also said that the two sides should open up exchanges, communicate continuously, understand each other, appreciate each other’s differences, and seek common ground…","As I just said, the causes and crux of the political deadlock across the Taiwan Strait are well known. The statement you mentioned is purely feigning confusion while knowing full well, and is an argument that puts the cart before the horse. Rather than talking at length about openness, exchanges, and communication, it would be better to return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” which is the only way to bring cross-Strait relations back to the bright path of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","海峡卫视记者","We know that after the “two sessions” ended, Comrade Liu Jieyi became the new Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, and at a time when the United States is trying to provoke a trade war against China, is there a new approach to the mainland's Taiwan policy?","On March 21, the official websites of the CPC Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office officially published the CPC Central Committee's decision to appoint comrade Liu Jieyi as Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. At present, socialism with Chinese characteristics has entered a new era, and cross-Strait relations also face a new and complex situation. Taiwan affairs work must also show new vitality and new achievements. Our Taiwan affairs system will earnestly study and implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress and General Secretary Xi Jinping's important thinking on Taiwan work, resolutely implement the central government's policies and arrangements on Taiwan, continue to adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” separatism, firmly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","A domestic poll on 31 measures shows that the attitudes of Taiwan's so-called “natural independence” generation aged 18–29 are undergoing a major shift, with 60% of young people saying they are willing to develop their careers on the mainland. May I ask the spokesperson for an assessment?","We generally do not comment on public opinion polls on the island. The mainland's development changes with each passing day, and its achievements are plain for all to see. We sincerely care for Taiwan compatriots, and I think more and more Taiwan compatriots will recognize that the mainland is an opportunity for Taiwan, not a threat or a challenge. Moreover, as cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation deepen, more and more Taiwan compatriots have gradually increased their understanding of the real situation on the mainland and their correct cognition of cross-Strait relations. They have begun to recognize that cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and the integrated development of cross-Strait economies and societies, conform to the common interests of compatriots on both sides, whereas pursuing “Taiwan independence” will only bring disaster to compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中国日报记者","Recently, US President Trump signed the “Taiwan Travel Act,” and a China-US trade war is about to break out. In this sensitive situation, mainstream mainland media have recently published a series of articles on “armed reunification.” Some commentators believe this signals that the mainland does not rule out “armed reunification.” What comments do you have on this?","Our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. At the same time, our determination to safeguard national territorial sovereignty is firm and unwavering, and we will never allow any “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-03-28","An Fengshan","中新社记者","The 2018 Boao Forum for Asia will be held next month. Has the Taiwan side received an invitation? Will high-level cross-Strait meetings be arranged during this period?","It is understood that this year's Boao Forum for Asia will be held in Boao, Hainan, from April 8 to 11, and Mr. Xiao Wanchang will attend this year's annual meeting in his capacity as Honorary Chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation. The specific arrangements are still under discussion.\nAfter the press conference ended, the spokesperson, responding to further questions from reporters, introduced relevant information about the upcoming Qingming ceremony to publicly honor the Yellow Emperor, to be held in Shaanxi. The “2018 Wuxu Year Qingming Public Ceremony to Honor the Xuanyuan Yellow Emperor” will be held on April 5 at the Mausoleum of the Yellow Emperor in Shaanxi. Qingming is a traditional festival of the Chinese nation for honoring the dead and remembering ancestors. The public ceremony will take as its theme “tracing origins, seeking roots, uniting hearts, and forging the soul,” calling on all descendants of the Chinese nation not to forget their roots and to jointly inherit traditional Chinese culture. More than 200 Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life, including former Chinese Kuomintang Chairwoman Hong Xiuzhu and New Party Chairman Yu Muming, will attend the public ceremony.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201803/t20180328_11937820.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201803/t20180328_11937826.htm"],[1,"2018-03-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After Donald Trump signed the Taiwan Travel Act, Taiwan's Kaohsiung Mayor Chen Ju visited the US and Alex Wong, deputy assistant secretary in the Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs at the US Department of State visited Taiwan. The Taiwanese authorities were thrilled for the visits. How do you comment on the so-called “exchange”? At the same time, we noticed that the Liaoning aircraft carrier sailed across…","We firmly oppose any forms of official exchanges or military contact carried out by any country, including the US, with Taiwan. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. No one, no force, nor any actions can stop China from realizing its complete reunification and national rejuvenation. The Chinese military has the firm determination, full confidence and sufficient capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-03/30/content_4808301.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-03-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Admiral Harris, Commander of the U.S. Pacific Command, recently made a comment that he thought the U.S. should continue to sell arms to Taiwan on a regular basis. What is your comment on that？ Japan’s Liberal Democratic Party put forward at a meeting on national security investigation on March 20 that Japan should upgrade the Izumo helicopter destroyer into an aircraft carrier and introduce the F-35B stealth…","China is firmly opposed to any arms sale to Taiwan by any country. We urge the U.S. to observe the one-China principle as well as the Three Joint Communiqués between China and the U.S., and stop promoting its arms sales to Taiwan. The PLA is in combat readiness and on high alert to safeguard China’s unification, national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. Any attempt to resist unification through military means is doomed to failure. As for the second question, because of historical and realistic reasons, Japan’s movements in military and security areas have always been under close attention of its Asian neighbors and the international community, especially Japan’s development of offensive weapons beyond its purely defensive defense demands. It is worthy of keeping much more alert of this movement of Japan. We urge the Japanese side to take history as a mirror, do more things conducive to enhancing mutual trust with its neighboring countries, and regional peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-03/30/content_4808301.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2018-04-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 2 (reporter Zha Wenye): Lai Ching-te, head of the executive branch of the Taiwan authorities, recently again openly claimed that he is indeed a “Taiwan independence” worker, that he has always advocated Taiwan’s “sovereign independence,” and that the “1992 Consensus” has absolutely no consensus. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 2nd that Lai Ching-te obstinately insists on the “Taiwan independence” position, has repeatedly and openly made “Taiwan independence” remarks, arrogantly challenges the status quo of cross-Strait relations, seriously provokes mainstream public opinion across the Strait, endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and endangers the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots. This is very dangerous, and also an overreach beyond one’s own capacity.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and it can never split from the motherland. We firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. All acts and schemes to split the country are doomed to fail and will ultimately be condemned by the people and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180402_11939293.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-04-09","Geng Shuang","","Taiwanese media reported that the US administration has approved the marketing license that would allow American manufacturers to sell technologies to Taiwan for the building of submarines. And a separate report said that the incoming US National Security Adviser John Bolton might visit Taiwan in June. Does China have any comment on either report?","I will answer your two questions together. We have noted relevant reports. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US ties. We firmly oppose the US side carrying out any official exchange and arms-sales with Taiwan. This position remains consistent, clear and firm. We urge the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, avoid having official contacts with Taiwan or trying to improve their relations in substantive ways, and stop military contacts and arms-sales with Taiwan so that China-US relations and peace and stability across the Straits will not be severely damaged.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1549249.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1549169.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-04-09","Geng Shuang","","Recently the Philippines handed over to the Chinese mainland 78 telecom fraud suspects from Taiwan arrested in its law enforcement operations. What is China's comment?","China and the Philippines have all along maintained close communication and cooperation in fighting against telecom and Internet fraud. China applauds and appreciates the Philippines' support and cooperation in this respect.\nIn regard to the specifics of the case, I would like to refer you to the competent authorities. I shall point out that the victims of the criminal acts committed by these lawbreakers abroad are all Chinese citizens from the mainland. As such, the mainland surely has judicial jurisdiction over that. We highly commend the Philippine government's adherence to the one-China principle in handling this issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1549249.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1549169.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-04-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, Taiwan's defense authorities said the US State Department recently announced approval of a “marketing license” for Taiwan's submarines, and Taiwan believes this helps enhance its defense capabilities and maintain Taiwan-US friendly relations. What comment does the Ministry of National Defense have on this?","China's position of firmly opposing U.S. arms sales to Taiwan is clear and consistent. Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. China requires the U.S. side to abide by the one-China policy and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to stop all forms of U.S.-Taiwan military contacts and all forms of arms sales to Taiwan. The Chinese military has the capability and determination to defeat any attempt to split the country, and will take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2018-04/09/content_4809013.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2018-04-10","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, on Monday, a Taiwanese navy flotilla docked in Nicaragua. What is China's comment?","There is only one China in the world, and this is the universal consensus among the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle is the trend of the world today. We believe all countries around the globe will accept this consensus and embrace the trend.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1549527.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1549493.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Could the spokesperson introduce the latest situation regarding the implementation of the \"31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots\" by localities and departments?","At the last press conference (March 28), we introduced the implementation status one month after the release and implementation of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”\nIn recent days, localities and departments have continued to step up efforts to advance implementation of the 31 measures. New progress includes: in cultural exchange, relevant departments are actively studying specific implementation measures for bringing Taiwan compatriots into the scope of cultural-sector award selections. In finance, the Working Committee on Taiwan-Funded Banks of the China Banking Association, the China Development Bank, and mainland Taiwan-funded banks have strengthened cooperation; so far, 2 syndicated loan pilot projects have successfully landed, with a total project amount of RMB 630 million, and the total participation amount of Taiwan-funded banks is RMB 55 million. In social exchange, Fujian, Jiangsu, Shandong and other provinces are carrying out work to enable Taiwan compatriots to be considered for local model workers; in some places, award recipients have already been selected and will be publicized according to the selection procedures.\nWenzhou City, Zhejiang Province, has implemented 24 measures on equal treatment for Taiwan enterprises and compatriots, including: Taiwan-related institutions and personnel participating in national key R&D programme projects enjoy the same policies as mainland institutions and personnel; Taiwan intellectual property converted on the mainland is protected and incentivized; and Taiwan-funded enterprises are supported in participating in infrastructure construction, with related projects able to negotiate cooperation directly with the competent industry authorities, among others.\nXiamen City, Fujian Province, yesterday (April 10) formally promulgated and issued the 《Several Measures on Further Deepening Economic, Social and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Xiamen and Taiwan》. It introduced 60 specific measures in five areas: economic exchange and cooperation between Xiamen and Taiwan; social and cultural exchange and cooperation; Taiwan compatriots' study and internships in Xiamen; employment and entrepreneurship; and residence and daily life. Among these 60 measures, the content of the “31 measures” has been fully implemented in Xiamen. At the same time, combined with Xiamen's actual conditions, new content beyond the “31 measures” has been added, covering equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots in studying, interning, employment, entrepreneurship, residence, daily life, medical care, transportation, and other areas, and also involving preferential policies for Taiwan-funded enterprises on opening of industry access, coexistence of industrial standards, and funding support, so as to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots' lives in Xiamen across a wider scope and more levels, and to create conditions for Taiwan enterprises to develop better and faster in Xiamen. You may have already noticed that yesterday (April 10) afternoon, relevant Xiamen municipal authorities held a media briefing and gave a detailed introduction; the specific provisions can be checked on the Xiamen municipal government website.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941949.htm"],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","When will this year's Straits Forum be held? How is the preparation going? This year the Straits Forum enters its tenth year. May I ask the spokesperson how you assess the role the Straits Forum has played in the development of cross-Strait relations?","It is understood that the 10th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in mid-to-late June. This will be the first large-scale cross-Strait exchange activity held since the 19th Party Congress. The organizers on both sides have already begun preparatory work. As a new attempt, this year’s forum will open online registration in mid-April. Please pay attention to the “Straits Forum Official Website” for specific registration times and details.\nThe Straits Forum has been going for ten years and has reached an important milestone for review and looking to the future. Over the past ten years, adhering to the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family” and to its positioning of being “civil, grassroots, and broad-based,” this platform has fully played its role in expanding and deepening civil exchanges across the Strait, promoting Chinese culture, facilitating the integrated economic and social development of both sides, and promoting spiritual connection among compatriots on both sides. Under the new circumstances, this forum will continue to center on the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and will carry out exchange activities with more diverse content, richer forms, and broader participation, so as to build a common public foundation for maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe organizers on both sides sincerely welcome and look forward to the participation of compatriots on both sides, and we also welcome media friends from both sides of the Strait to cover the event on site.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941946.htm"],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社中评网记者","Recently, “Taiwan independence” organizations held a forum in Taipei, which was attended by representatives of several overseas anti-China and “Hong Kong independence” organizations. Hong Kong scholar Benny Tai openly advocated “Hong Kong independence” at the forum, which has provoked strong condemnation from all sectors of Hong Kong public opinion. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Both Hong Kong and Taiwan are part of China's territory. “Taiwan independence,” “Hong Kong independence” and other separatist forces collude with each other, openly advocate “independence and nation-building,” and attempt to endanger national sovereignty and territorial integrity, harm national interests, and harm the interests of the people in Hong Kong and Taiwan. This is unpopular and is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The mainland will further open to the outside world. What opportunities will opening up bring to Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan compatriots?","As everyone has noted, in the keynote speech at this year's Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference, General Secretary Xi Jinping announced major new measures to expand China's opening up. These measures equally apply to Taiwan-invested enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","We know that at the end of this month, the “Wang-Koo Talks” will mark their 25th anniversary. Given the current state of cross-Strait relations, what lessons and significance do the “Wang-Koo Talks” hold?","The \"Wang-Koo Talks\" held twenty-five years ago accorded with the historical trend of cross-Strait relations development, opened the precedent of high-level cross-Strait contact, dialogue, and equal consultation, embodied the spirit of replacing confrontation with dialogue and promoting cooperation through consultation, highlighted the important status of the \"1992 Consensus\" as the basis for cross-Strait consultation, and took an important historic step in cross-Strait relations. The Wang-Koo Talks and the tortuous course of cross-Strait relations since then demonstrate that, to maintain the correct direction and good momentum of improving and developing cross-Strait relations, the key is to consolidate the common political foundation of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and adhering to the \"1992 Consensus.\" With this foundation, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop, and the rights and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait can be safeguarded and enhanced. If this foundation is undermined, mutual trust across the Strait will cease to exist, cross-Strait relations will return to the old path of turbulence and instability, and the achievements of peaceful development will be lost.\nUnder the current circumstances of cross-Strait relations, firmly upholding the political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus\" and adhering to the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the best commemoration of the Wang-Koo Talks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941945.htm"],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, the “Happy Island Alliance” was established in Kaohsiung, Taiwan, and said it would promote a so-called “independence referendum” to be held on April 6 next year. What is the spokesperson's response?","I will give them ten words: “A mayfly trying to shake a giant tree—how laughable its self-overestimation.” Every inch of our great motherland’s territory absolutely cannot and absolutely will not be separated from China. History has proven and will continue to prove that any separatist scheme of “Taiwan independence” carried out through “referendums” or “name rectification” is doomed to fail. If they dare to take a reckless gamble, it will only bring “hardship and misery” to Taiwan, not any “joy.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941948.htm"],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Reports indicate that when the new AIT Taipei office building is completed in June this year, Bolton, the newly appointed White House National Security Adviser, may visit Taiwan. In addition, the US State Department has announced the marketing approval for Taiwan's submarine “indigenously built” program, and the Taiwan authorities have said that this US move will help regional security and stability. What is the…","In response to the two questions you raised, our relevant departments have repeatedly expressed our solemn position and attitude. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan, and we firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan under any pretext. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. Any attempt to play the ‘Taiwan card’ is futile. External forces playing the ‘Taiwan card’ harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the overall interests of the Chinese nation, but going too far will also harm their own interests. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and touches the national feelings of 1.3 billion Chinese people. On the issue of safeguarding core national interests, we will not show the slightest vagueness. At the same time, we once again warn the Taiwan authorities: relying on foreign powers to bolster themselves will surely set themselves on fire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941947.htm"],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, head of Taiwan's executive authority, made several improper remarks on cross-Strait relations, negated the “1992 Consensus,” and called himself a “Taiwan independence worker.” Tsai Ing-wen, leader of Taiwan, has neither affirmed nor denied this. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Lai Ching-te, in his capacity as head of the Taiwan administrative authority, has repeatedly and openly made “Taiwan independence” remarks, arrogantly challenged the status quo of cross-Strait relations, seriously provoked mainstream public opinion across the Strait, endangered peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and endangered the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. The nature is very grave and the impact extremely adverse. His “Taiwan independence” remarks, and any support for and tolerance of such remarks, are extremely dangerous.\nI wish to emphasize once again that “Taiwan independence” runs counter to the trend of historical development and defies the will of Chinese descendants; it also seriously harms the interests of compatriots on both sides. It is an act of overestimating oneself and is bound to fail. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","According to reports, in response to China-US trade friction, the Taiwan authorities will control steel imports from the mainland, by clarifying so-called “Chinese content,” in order to win tariff exemptions for Taiwan's steel exports to the United States. Going forward, relevant Taiwan companies must obtain transport permits to import five major categories of steel from the mainland. What is the spokesperson's…","We oppose any act that attempts to restrict cross-Strait economic cooperation and sacrifices the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Cross-Strait economic cooperation is mutually beneficial. The mainland is Taiwan's largest trading partner and its largest source of trade surplus. The mainland is continuing to promote a brand-new pattern of openness, using high-level opening to drive high-quality development. This will bring new development opportunities to Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan compatriots, and will open broader prospects and provide stronger impetus for cross-Strait economic cooperation. Therefore, no one who attempts to block the pace of cross-Strait economic cooperation can succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Regarding Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” remarks, Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan region, said in an interview that these were Lai Ching-te's personal opinions, and that she is very satisfied with Lai Ching-te's actual performance. May I ask the spokesperson for comment? In addition, regarding the US-China trade war, Tsai Ing-wen said, “Do not underestimate the 23 million people; Taiwan is also a player…","On the first question, I once again emphasize that Lai Ching-te's \"Taiwan independence\" advocacy is no longer so-called \"personal freedom of speech\", so his wild \"Taiwan independence\" remarks, as well as any echoing, condoning or supporting of such remarks, are extremely dangerous.\nOn the second question, I have not seen detailed reports. In economic terms, cross-Strait economic cooperation is inseparable. If some people in Taiwan try to take advantage of the China-U.S. trade friction to do something not entirely aboveboard, I think the result can only be lifting a rock only to drop it on their own feet. At the same time, we must again stress that the Taiwan authorities must return to the correct track of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, so as to avoid being reduced to the status of \"chess pieces\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Reports say that a poll released recently by the Taiwan Democracy Foundation shows that if the mainland uses force, 70% of young people in Taiwan are “willing to fight for Taiwan.” How does the spokesperson view such a poll?","Everyone knows well the background, political leanings, and motives of this polling institution. Public opinion on the island holds that this misleading poll it produced is more like a piece of propaganda material, and so it is not worth commenting on.\nI want to point out that, in the current situation where the DPP authorities are undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait relations, tolerating and condoning “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, stepping up the creation of cross-Strait confrontation, and stirring up feelings among people on both sides, leading to an increasingly complex and grim situation in cross-Strait relations, the political motive behind this institution's release of this so-called poll is extremely dangerous. They stage-manage things themselves and do not hesitate to use the lives and fortunes of Taiwan's young people as stakes in “Taiwan independence,” indulging their own desires. It is a flagrant act of “playing with fire.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Are you aware of the circumstances in which Taiwan’s “Minister of the Interior” Yeh Chun-jung lectured at Zhejiang University while he was a professor at National Taiwan University? Another question: yesterday General Secretary Xi Jinping met Siew Wan-chang in Boao, and he specifically mentioned that the mainland’s economic development should record the Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the…","On the first question: over the years, teachers on both sides of the Strait have carried out academic exchanges in various forms. Such exchanges have promoted and expanded cross-Strait educational exchanges. Both sides should support and encourage such good practices, rather than obstructing and restricting them as the Taiwan authorities have done.\nOn the second question: yesterday morning, Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, met with Vincent Siew, honorary chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation, and his delegation at the Boao Forum for Asia and delivered an important speech. Media on both sides of the Strait gave full coverage to General Secretary Xi’s speech, and public opinion on both sides has given it high praise. The mainland has consistently supported and protected Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan compatriots in investing and developing businesses on the mainland. Our policy is consistent and continuous.\nGoing forward, we believe that as we further expand opening up and as our economic development rises to a higher quality level, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses that grasp the pulse of the mainland’s economic development will certainly achieve greater and better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“TVBS”记者","Continuing the previous topic: regarding the meeting held during the Boao Forum, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council responded that it hopes the mainland will carry out political reform and democratization, and will abandon one-sided political positions as a precondition for cross-Strait exchanges. What views does the spokesperson have on this?","Everyone has noticed that yesterday General Secretary Xi’s remarks while meeting Xiao Wanchang and his delegation declared our policy position of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” and pursuing a bright prospect for cross-Strait relations. They highly affirmed the contributions of Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to mainland development, expressed the sentiment that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” and conveyed our willingness to keep sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, deepening cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and our sincere goodwill in letting the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots gain real benefits. They also made clear that the Taiwan question concerns the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and hoped that compatriots on both sides would share the national righteousness, jointly advance the process of peacefully achieving national reunification, and jointly realize the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. General Secretary Xi’s remarks were sincere and forceful, and have won wide acclaim among compatriots on both sides.\nThe so-called response from Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council describes the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” as “a unilateral political proposition of the mainland.” It attempts to use the so-called “respecting the choice of Taiwan public opinion regarding cross-Strait relations and Taiwan’s future development” to lend cover to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and it makes unwarranted remarks about the mainland’s development path, distorting facts and confusing the public. It is not worth refuting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, Lee Ching-yu visited Hunan to see Lee Ming-che, and after returning to Taiwan said that Lee Ming-che's freedom of speech and communication had been deprived and restricted while he was serving his sentence on the mainland. What is the spokesperson's comment?","It is our understanding that the claim made by Lee Ching-yu that Lee Ming-che's \"right to speak\" and \"right to communicate\" have been deprived or restricted is seriously inconsistent with the actual situation. The Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, the Prison Law, and administrative regulations such as the Ministry of Justice's Provisions on Meetings and Communications for Offenders contain specific and clear provisions on the various lawful rights of persons serving sentences. Since Lee Ming-che entered prison to serve his sentence, the prison administration authorities have strictly ensured, in accordance with law and regulations, his rights to meetings, communication, rest and other rights. At present, Lee Ming-che is in good physical and mental condition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国国际广播电台记者","We note that although cross-Strait relations have changed over the past year or so, the number of Taiwan youth who study, start businesses, work, or live on the mainland, or who wish to come to the mainland to develop, is increasing. Among them, the number of students who have successfully applied to study at mainland universities has increased two to three times compared with last year, and all are…","We noted that this year the number of Taiwan students applying to study at mainland universities has clearly risen, and applications to famous mainland universities have multiplied. This shows that the development and opportunities on the mainland are increasingly attractive to Taiwan’s young people, and that our convenience measures providing Taiwan youth with equal treatment in studying, living, and working on the mainland are increasingly welcomed by Taiwan’s young people. This trend will continue to develop. Here, I sincerely wish that all Taiwan students who have applied will achieve their wish of entering the mainland universities of their choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Yesterday, Chen Ming-tong, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, mentioned at an event that among the 31 measures recently launched by the mainland to benefit Taiwan, 10 are related to Taiwan businesspeople. But he also reminded Taiwan businesspeople that the mainland often has cases of “inconsistency between words and deeds,” so they should manage risks themselves. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's response?","Whoever is inconsistent in word and deed on promoting cross-Strait exchanges and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides should ask themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央人民广播电台记者","During the just-past Qingming Festival, former KMT Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu attended the “Wuxu Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi,” serving as one of the chief sacrificers, and met and held talks with Taiwan Affairs Office Director Liu Jieyi. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this cross-Strait Qingming memorial event?","Regarding the relevant situation of Director Liu Jieyi meeting former KMT Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu and New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming, we have already issued a news release; please refer to it. What I want to say here is that the Qingming public ceremony commemorating Xuanyuan Huangdi is an activity with broad influence among compatriots on both sides of the Strait and overseas Chinese. The Yellow Emperor is the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation, and the Huangdi Mausoleum is the spiritual symbol of Chinese civilization. Compatriots on both sides jointly paying respects at the Huangdi Mausoleum reflects their shared remembrance of the ancestor of the Chinese nation and their commitment to Chinese spirit and Chinese roots. We hope compatriots on both sides will together promote Chinese culture, rally Chinese spirit, enhance heart-to-heart connection, and jointly strive for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","I have two questions. First, again regarding remarks by Chen Mingtong: he recently said that, on the definition of cross-Strait relations, the Taiwan side defines them according to its so-called current “constitution” and the “Regulations on Cross-Strait People’s Relations,” and he believes these two provisions have already answered how cross-Strait relations are defined. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation?","On the first question: since you also know that the relevant Taiwan authorities’ regulations are within the “one China” framework, you should clearly answer the nature of cross-strait relations, clearly affirm that both sides belong to one China, that the two sides are not a state-to-state relationship, and clearly uphold the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社中评网记者","The Philippines recently deported to the mainland 78 Taiwan-origin telecom fraud suspects it had arrested, and Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council expressed protest. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","For specific circumstances, please consult the competent authorities. I want to emphasize that cross-Strait telecom fraud crimes are deeply hated by people on both sides and have aroused public outrage. Therefore, we will continue, in accordance with the position of being conducive to combating crime, safeguarding judicial justice, and protecting the rights and interests of victims, to punish telecom fraud criminal activities according to law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","A referendum proposal titled “Participating in the International Olympics and International Sports Events under the Full Name Taiwan” was approved for review on March 23. If enough signatures are gathered by the end of September, it could be held at the end of the year. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","On this issue, our attitude was already stated at the last press conference. I reiterate that a very small number of people in Taiwan are manipulating the so-called “name-rectification referendum,” tearing apart Taiwan society, harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and provoking cross-Strait relations. Any political scheme to pursue “Taiwan independence” and division through “referendums” or “name rectification” is extremely dangerous and will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Five branches of the Bank of China in Shanghai, Jiangsu, Fujian, Shenzhen and Suzhou will recruit a small number of Taiwan fresh graduates who are studying on the mainland. Subsequently, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council claimed that Taiwan residents taking up posts at the Bank of China are suspected of so-called \"illegality.\" May I ask the spokesperson for comments on this? On the second question, the Second…","First question: The Bank of China recruits Taiwan graduates studying on the mainland and provides them with job opportunities, which has been widely welcomed by Taiwan students. The Taiwan authorities, however, have blown the matter out of all proportion, made large-scale threats, and obstructed it. They fail to realize that what they are strangling is the opportunity for Taiwan youth to realize their own development, and what they are harming is the interests of Taiwan youth.\nSecond question: Baseball is a sporting event that cross-Strait youth enjoy watching. Following the first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League held last year, this sports exchange activity has been warmly welcomed by cross-Strait youth, and viewership and online click-through rates have set records for cross-Strait exchange activities. From April 3 to 9 this year, the Beijing leg of the second Cross-Strait Student Baseball League was held. This year, the number of participating teams increased from 8 to 10 in each group, so there were 20 teams in total. After three days and 24 games, the leg champions of the mainland university and Taiwan university groups in the A and B divisions were decided. The A-division champions were Xiamen University and Wanneng University of Science and Technology, and the B-division champions were Guangdong Technology College of Industry and Commerce and Hsinchu Tsing Hua University. After the games, the teams were also ranked by points; these points will be carried into the Taichung leg to be held in July as the final results for advancing to the grand final. We therefore sincerely hope that the broad media will continue to follow this event with enthusiasm.\nI must point out that holding the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League helps cross-Strait youth deepen mutual understanding and build friendships, becoming good teammates, good partners and good brothers. Cross-Strait students who devote themselves to the baseball league both pour out youthful passion and inject vitality into exchanges between compatriots on both sides. We therefore wish this event ever greater success.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180411_11941944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On the morning of April 10, Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, met in Boao, Hainan, with Hsiao Wan-chang, Honorary Chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation of Taiwan, and his delegation, who had come to attend the 2018 Annual Conference of the Boao Forum for Asia.\nAt the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office on April 11, spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions, said: General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Mr. Hsiao Wan-chang, Honorary Chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation of Taiwan, and his delegation in Boao, and delivered an important speech. The media on both sides of the Strait gave full coverage, and public opinion on both sides has also given it high praise. General Secretary Xi declared our policy position of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" and pursuing bright prospects for the development of cross-Strait relations. He highly affirmed the contributions of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises to the mainland's development, and expressed that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.\" We are willing to continue sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, deepening economic, cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, and bringing real and tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises through sincere goodwill. He also made clear that the Taiwan question concerns the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and expressed the hope that compatriots on both sides will share the great responsibility of the nation, jointly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and together realize the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. General Secretary Xi's speech was sincere and forceful, and it won wide acclaim from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180411_11941950.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: It is reported that from 8:00 to 24:00 on April 18, the PLA will conduct live-fire military exercises in waters of the Taiwan Strait. Public opinion on both sides of the Strait generally believes this is a warning from the mainland aimed at recent “Taiwan independence” remarks by Lai Ching-te, head of Taiwan's executive authority, and at the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities pursued by…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 13 (reporter Zhao Bo): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 13th in response to a question: We have repeatedly stated our firm opposition to “Taiwan independence.” I would like to reiterate that we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and action, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180413_11943066.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-04-17","Hua Chunying","","Do you have any comment on the visit by the Taiwanese \"President\" to Swaziland tomorrow? Is the planned military exercise a response to this?","I must correct your mistake because what you said is wrong. There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. What you mentioned is the head of the Taiwan region.\nI only want to stress that there is but one China in the world. This is not only an objective fact and common sense but also the general consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1551802.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1551717.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-04-18","Hua Chunying","","Are there any details you can give us on the current drills in the Taiwan Straits? There are reports saying that they are larger than previous ones. What's your comment?","I would like to refer you to the military or Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for this question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1552217.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1552116.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-04-18","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, the head of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen started her visit to Swaziland yesterday, her first \"visit to Africa\" since taking office. Do you have any further reaction to that?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an indispensable part of China's territory. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government that represents China. This is not only recognized by the relevant UN resolution, but also constitutes the universal consensus of the overwhelming majority of countries around the world.\nThe China-Africa Comprehensive Strategic Cooperative Partnership is maintaining a sound momentum of development now. The upcoming Forum on China-Africa Cooperation (FOCAC) summit in Beijing this September will surely set off a new surge of China-Africa cooperation. The Gambia and Sao Tome and Principe's return to the big family of China-Africa friendly cooperation fully indicates that the one-China principle is an irresistible trend that meets the aspiration of all people. We sincerely hope that the relevant African country will get a clear understanding of the general trend of the world and join our big family of China-Africa friendly cooperation at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1552217.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1552116.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-04-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Air Force has recently organized multiple types and numbers of aircraft to “circumnavigate the island” on patrol in succession, and will continue to organize aircraft to “circumnavigate the island” to test real combat capability. Public opinion holds that, in addition to the military exercises of the 18th in the Taiwan Strait, this is a further warning from the mainland to Lai Ching-te, head…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 19 (reporter Zhao Bo) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th in response to questions about air force fighter jets “circling the island on patrol”: “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the greatest realistic threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and compatriots on both sides should remain highly vigilant. We firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and conduct. Any scheme attempting to split Taiwan from China is doomed to failure. No one or force should underestimate our determination and firm capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180419_11945990.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce the latest developments in localities and departments implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”","Since the release of the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation,” all localities and relevant departments have actively promoted their implementation, achieving positive progress. We have already given detailed briefings at the press conference twice in succession. Today, I will give a few more examples to introduce the latest developments:\nThe second “Talents Gather, Shanghai Chases Dreams” Taiwan Outstanding Doctoral (Graduate) Students and Shanghai Universities Exchange Meeting was held in Shanghai on April 20, attracting 70 outstanding Taiwanese doctoral (graduate) students from 18 universities, including Fudan University, Tongji University and Shanghai Jiao Tong University. The positions offered by Shanghai universities generally carry annual salaries of around 200,000 to 300,000 yuan. For high-end talent, there are even salaries of one million yuan per year, along with research startup funds of 300,000 yuan and housing relocation subsidies of up to 1.5 million yuan.\nThe fourth “Innovation and Entrepreneurship, Dreams Built in Wenzhou” Taiwan Youth Talent Matching Meeting was held in Beijing on April 21. Targeting Taiwanese students at well-known universities in Beijing, the meeting introduced Wenzhou's entrepreneurship and employment environment and talent网 platform, attracting them to pursue their careers in Wenzhou. 86 enterprises and institutions in Wenzhou jointly offered nearly 600 quality job vacancies, which were welcomed by Taiwanese students in Beijing.\nKunshan City held a meeting on promoting the implementation of the “31 Measures” on April 13, centrally releasing a series of documents issued by Kunshan granting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises treatment equal to that of mainland counterparts. It also paid out rewards and bonuses to leading Taiwan-invested enterprises at all levels, enterprises recognized for listing or going public, and headquarters enterprises. It awarded the honorary titles of “Red Banner Women's Day Flag Bearer” (individual) and “Red Banner Women's Day Collective” to three Taiwanese women and to the Kunshan Taiwan Business Association's Women's Association, respectively, and commended the Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises that had received the honorary titles of Model Worker, May Day Labor Certificate and May Day Labor Medal in recent years. These awards are among the highest social honors on the mainland and fully affirm the outstanding contributions of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises to mainland development.\nThe 2018 Cross-Strait Intelligent Equipment Manufacturing Zhengzhou Forum, hosted by the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, was held on April 16. Cross-Strait business operators conducted in-depth discussions on the theme “Intelligent Equipment Manufacturing Connects Both Sides of the Strait and Leads the Future” and achieved positive outcomes. The first of the 31 measures is “Taiwan-invested enterprises participating in the ‘Made in China 2025’ action plan shall be subject to the same policies as mainland enterprises,” providing tax, investment and other support to Taiwan businesspeople who establish high-end manufacturing, intelligent manufacturing, green manufacturing and other enterprises on the mainland. According to our understanding, 2 Taiwan-invested enterprises have entered the green manufacturing list of “Made in China 2025,” one Taiwan-invested enterprise factory has been designated as an intelligent manufacturing pilot demonstration project, and 2 more Taiwan-invested enterprises have joined the Industrial Internet Industry Alliance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948532.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The “Guiding Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Hainan in Comprehensively Deepening Reform and Opening Up” were recently released. They explicitly propose to “strengthen cooperation with the Taiwan region in education, healthcare, modern agriculture, and the protection and development of marine resources,” and also allow “technical and skilled personnel from the Taiwan…","Benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait is the starting point and goal of our development of cross-Strait relations. Under the new circumstances across the Strait, the mainland is willing to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with compatriots in Taiwan, and has successively introduced a series of policy measures providing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises with equal treatment for studying, starting businesses, finding employment and living in the mainland, thereby enhancing the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The recently issued \"Guiding Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Hainan in Comprehensively Deepening Reform and Opening Up\" assigns a new mission of reform and opening up to Hainan's special economic zone. This major deployment provides a rare opportunity for Qiong-Taiwan cooperation and will help further promote cross-Strait economic, cultural and exchange and cooperation. It is both a manifestation of the mainland's further deepening of reform and expansion of opening up, and a microcosm of our implementation of the spirit of the 19th Party Congress and the concept of \"cross-Strait one family.\" The Taiwan Affairs Office will resolutely implement the spirit of the Guiding Opinions, take measures such as implementing the \"31 Measures\" in Hainan as a starting point, support and coordinate Hainan Province and relevant parties in strengthening policy alignment and drafting new measures, strengthen Qiong-Taiwan cooperation, and encourage relevant sectors in Taiwan to take part in development in Hainan's fields of education, healthcare, health and elderly care, modern agriculture, and marine resource protection and development. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, to study, intern and carry out various exchanges in Hainan, and welcome Taiwan technical and skilled personnel to find employment and start businesses in Hainan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948533.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, regarding the claim that the mainland’s military exercises were aimed at Lai Qingde’s “Taiwan independence” remarks, Cai Yingwen recently responded that Lai Qingde showed his “pragmatic” side, and that the DPP authorities’ cross-Strait policy position is clear: “maintain the status quo,” and Lai Qingde is the same. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The message conveyed by the PLA military exercises is very clear. We have firm resolve, full confidence and sufficient capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme or action and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. If “Taiwan independence” forces continue to act recklessly, we will take further action.\nSince 1949, although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and never will. From May 20, 2008 to May 20, 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations achieved peaceful development. This is the current state of cross-Strait relations.\nAfter the DPP authorities came to power, they undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, condoned and abetted “Taiwan independence” separatist activities of “de-Sinicization,” interfered with and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, created cross-Strait confrontation, undermined the hard-won situation and achievements of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and caused cross-Strait relations to regress. Lai Ching-te’s “Taiwan independence” remarks further constitute blatant provocation against peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities must bear this responsibility.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948543.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡导报记者","Continuing the topic of the military exercises just mentioned, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the mainland’s military drills are pressure on Taiwan, create confrontation, and seek to provoke tension across the Strait and in the region, and that this is inconsistent with the mainland’s efforts to promote heart-to-heart connection across the Strait. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","“Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the greatest real threat to peace and stability across the Strait, and they harm the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots. The series of actions we have taken target the “Taiwan independence” forces on the island and their activities, in order to prevent the well-being of the Taiwan people from being harmed by “Taiwan independence” schemes. The DPP authorities should not confuse public perception.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, sharing common blood, common culture, common ties, and common vision. We are a community of shared destiny as close as blood and water. The true spiritual unity of compatriots on both sides lies first in a shared recognition of Chinese culture and the Chinese nation. What undermines this spiritual unity is precisely the “de-Sinicization” activities promoted by a small number of “Taiwan independence” forces on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948531.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","In response to the mainland’s military exercises, a spokesperson for the U.S. State Department said the United States opposes any action by either side to change the status quo, including any use of force or other forms of action. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and we firmly oppose any interference by external forces.\nThe PLA's military exercises target “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist words and deeds. They are meant to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in cross-Strait relations, and safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Since May 20, 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” do not recognize that both sides belong to one China, undermined the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and let “Taiwan independence” separatist activities run unchecked and tolerated them. This is what is changing the status quo.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948530.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","You just mentioned that if “Taiwan independence” remarks or activities continue, the mainland will take further action. Does “further action” mean the use of force? Second question: we noticed that the PLA Air Force recently launched a promotional video in the Minnan dialect. Please explain the considerations behind it.","The relevant Minnan-language video was released by the air force; please ask them about the specifics.\nRegarding your first question, I reiterate that the signals sent by the PLA's series of military exercises are clear and unambiguous. We have the greatest sincerity and make the greatest efforts to pursue the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we absolutely do not tolerate “Taiwan independence,” and we will not allow “Taiwan independence” forces to separate Taiwan from China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Some media reported that Wu Tun-yih is expected to fill out forms this week to apply to the DPP authorities to come to the Mainland to attend the “KMT-CPC Forum.” What is the current progress of the “KMT-CPC Forum”? Will it be held in mid-to-late May?","Since 2005, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have carried out extensive exchanges at many levels and achieved positive results. Regarding the specific arrangements for exchange activities between the two parties, the relevant departments of both parties are in close communication. Communication is smooth. If there is definite news, we will release it in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, because Taiwan will hold its “nine-in-one” elections at the end of the year, there are rumors that the mainland side will suspend issuing Mainland Residents' Travel Permits to Taiwan and will reduce group tour permits for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan after September. Please confirm this.","As everyone knows, the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermine the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and hurt the feelings of mainland compatriots. As a result, over the past two years the willingness of mainland residents to travel to Taiwan has continued to decline, and the numbers have steadily dropped. Regarding the rumor you mentioned, I cannot confirm it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Reportedly, Taiwan's authorities, under the pretext of “jointly building global epidemic prevention and security,” are seeking international support and trying to take part in the World Health Assembly. What is your comment?","On the question of Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations, we have stated our position many times: it must be arranged reasonably through cross-Strait consultations, under the one-China principle.\nFrom 2009 to 2016, under the one-China principle, and against the backdrop of recognizing the “1992 Consensus” and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, Taiwan participated in the World Health Assembly through cross-Strait consultations. However, after the DPP authorities came to power, the reasons why Taiwan could no longer attend the World Health Assembly are well known. Nonetheless, under the arrangement reached between us and the World Health Organization, Taiwan can fully and promptly obtain information in areas such as global health and epidemic prevention, and Taiwanese experts may also attend relevant WHO technical meetings and activities. According to incomplete statistics, from 2013 to 2017, Taiwan sent 58 people to attend 34 WHO technical meetings. In 2009, 2013, 2014 and 2017, Taiwan reported a total of 24 confirmed H1N1 influenza cases and 5 cases of human infection with H7N9 avian influenza to the WHO.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948527.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Former AIT Taipei Office Director Yang Su-ti recently said that a U.S. Marine Corps guard detachment will be stationed at the new AIT Taipei site for security. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and our Office have both repeatedly expressed our solemn position. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Last week, Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, separately met with Hualien County Magistrate Fu Kun-chi and Nantou County Magistrate Lin Ming-chen. May I ask whether this is a continuation of expanding exchanges with the “blue eight counties,” or whether there is a possibility in the future of building other “twin-city forums” beyond Taipei and Shanghai? Second question: Taiwan's defense authorities…","We have consistently upheld the concept that “Both sides of the Strait are one family,” promoting exchanges and cooperation in all fields between the two sides and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. As long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of exchanges between Taiwan counties and cities and the mainland, there is no problem with any Taiwan county or city exchanging with us.\nRegarding your second question, “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the greatest realistic threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the only way to improve cross-Strait relations. Any scheme involving armed confrontation is destined to have no way out.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电台总台国广记者","The Taiwan authorities, citing academic exchanges Guan Zhongmin conducted at mainland universities, strongly obstructed him from serving as president of National Taiwan University, while Wu Maokun, president of National Dong Hwa University in Taiwan, who had given lectures at many mainland universities and served as an adviser to relevant mainland institutions, was nonetheless appointed head of Taiwan’s education…","In the three decades of cross-Strait exchanges, many Taiwan experts and scholars have come to the mainland to engage in cross-Strait education and academic exchanges, and have held honorary positions or given lectures in relevant professional fields on the mainland. This is normal exchange activity, done openly and above board, and it benefits both sides. The DPP authorities, however, apply double standards, restrict cross-Strait exchanges, and suppress people who take part in them. This is not popular with the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently the situation on the Korean Peninsula has begun to ease, but cross-Strait atmosphere is tense because of the “Taiwan independence” issue. Taiwan may hold the Han Kuang Exercise in June, and AIT may have a U.S. Marine Corps guard detachment take up security duties in June. This seems to symbolize that the Taiwan Strait is becoming a new “powder keg.” What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","We have repeatedly said that, for reasons well known to all, cross-Strait relations and the situation in the Taiwan Strait have become increasingly severe and complex. This responsibility lies with the cross-Strait policies of the DPP authorities and the increasingly rampant separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces, and of course it is also related to foreign forces attempting to play the “Taiwan card.” We have the confidence and ability to safeguard the overall situation of cross-Strait relations, grasp the future direction of cross-Strait relations, defeat all acts that provoke cross-Strait relations, unite broad Taiwan compatriots, overcome difficulties, eliminate interference, and pursue the bright prospect of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","It is reported that, affected by the China–U.S. “trade war,” the Taiwan authorities’ finance department announced on the 16th an anti-subsidy and anti-dumping investigation into five steel products from the mainland. Spokesperson, will the mainland take corresponding countermeasures?","The mainland is Taiwan's largest trading partner and the largest source of its trade surplus. Cross-Strait economic cooperation is mutually beneficial, and cross-Strait industrial cooperation is inseparable. A considerable share of the five categories of steel products covered by the Taiwan authorities' “double anti” investigation are produced by Taiwan-invested factories on the mainland. The DPP authorities' approach hides undisclosed aims, and it harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948529.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The Taiwan education authorities recently sent letters to public universities requiring a thorough investigation of the 2019 plans of various universities for official overseas assignments and travel to the mainland. Many professors worry this will affect academic exchanges across the Strait. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Combining this with the earlier response, I would like to stress again that no retrograde action can stop the broad trend of cross-Strait relations development. What the Taiwan authorities are blocking is the steps of Taiwan teachers heading west, but what it may lead to is a further contraction of Taiwan’s higher education sector.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","According to Taiwan media reports, on the 25th about 40 KMT representatives came to Beijing to visit the Taiwan Affairs Office, and Director Liu Jieyi will meet them. Please confirm. Second question: What is your view on cooperation between the China Zhi Gong Party on the mainland and in Taiwan?","The Cross-Strait Business Representatives Association of the Kuomintang's Taiwan-invested businesses recently sent a delegation to visit Beijing. Its itinerary includes a visit to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, and we will release information in a timely manner when that takes place.\nOn the second question, exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan's parties, sectors and groups that oppose “Taiwan independence,” recognize the “1992 Consensus,” and advocate developing cross-Strait relations are our consistent policy. I am not familiar with the specific cooperative relationship with this organization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","First question: We noted that the Taiwan Affairs Office's official Weibo account “Cross-Strait Relations 0808” was launched recently and, within just a few days, has published a series of messages related to cross-Strait relations. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant details of this Weibo account? Second question: Chang Chen, a well-known Taiwan actor who serves as a jury member at the 71st Cannes Film…","To further advance government information disclosure and increase channels for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to learn about the central government's policies toward Taiwan and the relevant work of the Taiwan Affairs Office, we opened an official account on the Sina Weibo platform on March 27. Its content covers three sections: “Authoritative Releases,” “Government News,” and “Serving Taiwan Compatriots.” It is currently in the testing phase of system and product operations. Even so, 31 pieces of relevant information have been published, the number of followers has exceeded 510,000, and the total reading volume has reached 2.494 million. We welcome media friends and netizens on both sides of the Strait to follow us.\nOn the second question, we have also noted the relevant reports. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, and we hope that far-sighted people in the film circles on both sides will take responsibility for promoting the development of the cross-Strait film industry and play a positive role in bringing Chinese culture to the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948526.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","On the afternoon of the 23rd, the Taiwan Competitiveness Forum released a 2018 first-half identity survey of Taiwan residents. The results showed that more than 86% of residents identify as members of the Chinese nation, nearly 52% consider themselves Chinese, and more than 60% believe the two sides will unify in the future. What is the spokesperson's view of these survey results?","We have also noted this public opinion poll. What I want to express is that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese; we carry the blood of the Chinese nation and spiritually uphold the roots of Chinese culture. Even during the period of Japanese colonial rule, countless patriotic and righteous Taiwanese people proved with their blood and lives that they were Chinese and descendants of the Chinese nation. Therefore, there is no such thing as “natural independence”; there is only “man-made independence.”\nOver the past forty years of reform and opening up, the tremendous achievements of the rapid development and progress of the mainland, together with the cross-Strait policies we have pursued, have led more and more Taiwan compatriots to recognize that the mainland’s care for Taiwan compatriots is sincere, that Taiwan’s future cannot be separated from the mainland, and that “Taiwan independence” harms the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. They have also come to recognize that advancing the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peaceful reunification of the motherland accords with the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and is also in the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots. Therefore, I believe this trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201804/t20180425_11948528.htm"],[2,"2018-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","The Taiwan authorities recently solicited public comments on a new design plan for the “Taiwan Residents' Identity Card.” Adjustments to the relevant requirements have been questioned by public opinion as yet another move toward “soft Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization.” How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","We have stated many times that we firmly oppose any scheme of “de-Sinicization.” The DPP authorities' practice has already been questioned by the people of the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201804/t20180425_11948547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports in Taiwan, the PLA Air Force recently sent several types of aircraft to patrol around the island. Would you please specify which island this “island” refers to? What is the significance of the frequent exercises conducted by the PLA near Taiwan?","Recently, the PLA Air Force dispatched multiple types of warplanes to carry out real combat training exercises in the airspace over the sea to further enhance the capability of safeguarding China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The island the PLA warplanes patrolled around is, of course, China’s Taiwan Island.\nThe “Taiwan independence” secessionist activities pose the largest realistic threat to the peace and stability of the cross-strait relations and cause damage to the fundamental interests of the Taiwan compatriots. The series of actions we have taken are targeting the “Taiwan independence” forces and their activities, and are to protect the well-being of the people in Taiwan from being undermined by the “Taiwan independence” conspiracy. If the “Taiwan independence” forces continue to act recklessly, we will take further actions.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, Taiwan’s military held naval and air force exercise in waters off eastern Taiwan in April and Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan region, boarded a destroyer to review the exercise. In addition, the Taiwan authorities announced recently that it would conduct the Han Kuang military exercise. Some analysts believe that this is the attempt of the Taiwan authorities to counter the mainland.…","We will strive for the bright prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. However, it must be pointed out that all ‘Taiwan independence’ secessionist activities are doomed to failure and any attempt to resist reunification by the use of force will get Taiwan nowhere.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Defense Ministers' Meeting of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) Member States was held recently in Beijing. Could you please brief us on the meeting and its achievements? The second question is that, according to today’s media reports, two B-52 strategic bombers of the US Air Force flied through the Bashi Channel to the area near the Dongsha Islands in the South China Sea and returned on April 24.…","The 15th Defense Ministers' Meeting of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) Member States was held in Beijing from April 23 to 24. This was the first meeting of the SCO defense ministers held after the SCO’s enlargement. The meeting is themed as “building a community with shared future and seeking development through innovation and cooperation”.\nPresident Xi Jinping met with the defense ministers during the meeting, fully affirming the positive contribution made by the SCO defense and security cooperation to the maintenance of regional security and stability.\nThe defense ministers conducted in-depth exchanges of views on international and regional security situation, further enhancement of the SCO member states’ pragmatic cooperation in defense and security fields, and other issues of common concern, and reached broad consensus. They also attended the opening ceremony of the 5th \"Fanfare for Peace\" Military Tattoo of the SCO and watched the first performance.\nThe meeting has scored many achievements: Firstly, a joint communiqué was issued and the meeting minutes were signed, affirming the important role of the defense and security cooperation as the cornerstone of SCO’s sound development, reiterating the strong resolve of the SCO member states to jointly strike the Three Forces and safeguard regional peace, security and stability.\nSecondly, it announced the establishment of the expert working group for the Defense Ministers' Meeting of the SCO Member States and reached important consensus on further improving and developing the military cooperation among SCO members.\nThirdly, it awarded medals of “strengthening friendship and cooperation” to the representatives from SCO member states who had made outstanding contribution to the SCO defense and security cooperation.\nWe will work with other SCO member states to achieve more pragmatic and effective results in military security cooperation.\nOn your second question, the situation is under the control of the Chinese military. The PLA will, as always, firmly safeguard its national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","First, the newly issued military doctrine altered a lot of articles closely related to the interests of the service personnel. But, some are doubtful that a few units might make subordinate policies or regulations misusing the good-faithed doctrine. What can be done to ensure that the new doctrine will be strictly followed? Second, 9 years after the last fleet review, the PLA Navy held another one in mid April,…","The Central Committee of the CPC, the CMC and President Xi cared a lot about the welfare of servicepersons. The recent amendment to the doctrines includes more scientific and humanistic regulations on certain affairs concerning the vital interests of servicepersons. To ensure the delivery of the doctrines’ benefits, the Training and Administration Department of the CMC has made comprehensive arrangements for the implementation of the new doctrines and ordered units at all levels to resolutely abolish any local policies or regulations inconsistent with the doctrines and will carry out constant inspection and supervision. All persons and cases violating the doctrines will be dealt with immediately, so that the authority and solemnity of the doctrines can be well preserved.\nThe main purpose of the fleet review is to show the great achievements that have been scored since the 18th National Congress of the CPC in the development of the People’s Navy, the latest achievements in the Navy’s efforts to carry out real combat training, the new image of the Navy in building a strong Navy through reform, the resolve to safeguard China’s sovereignty, security and development interests, and the support from the officers and men of the PLA Navy for President Xi Jinping as the core of the Central Committee of the CPC. This fleet review is not directed against any specific country or target; nor is it related to the situation around China.\nThe fighting capabilities of the Liaoning Aircraft Carrier should be improved through training and tested by real combat.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Stephen M. Young, former director of the Taipei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT), said to the media recently that the US would very likely to station Marine Corps to guard its new compound of the AIT in Taipei, which is to be open in June. What’s your comment?","We firmly oppose official exchanges and military contact between the US and Taiwan in any form. The Chinese military has firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to defeat all attempts aiming to split our country .","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-04-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","You just mentioned that the Chinese Mainland will take counter measures in response to any further actions by the ‘Taiwan independence’ secessionist force. Some analysts say that the Chinese Mainland will stop only at the level of flexing its military muscles. What is your comment?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China and the Chinese military has sent a clear and consistent message on this. We have strong resolve, full confidence and sufficient capability to defeat any secessionist attempt and safeguard our national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-04/27/content_4811291.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2018-04-27","Hua Chunying","","The US Air Force said that B-52 bomber aircraft conducted missions in what they say was the vicinity of the South China Sea. Taiwan media report that they actually did fly over the South China Sea. The Defense Ministry made a response yesterday. Do you have more details about this?","I would refer you to the Defense Ministry.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1555315.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1555158.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-01","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: the Dominican Republic government announced it is severing so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan, and China has established diplomatic relations with the Dominican Republic. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 1 (reporter Zhao Bo): Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on the 1st, saying that adhering to the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Dominican Republic is what people's hearts desire and the general trend of the times.\nAn Fengshan made the above remarks in answering questions.\nAn Fengshan said that on the morning of May 1 in Beijing, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi signed the \"Joint Communiqué of the People's Republic of China and the Dominican Republic on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations\" with Dominican Foreign Minister Vargas. From the date the communiqué was signed, the People's Republic of China and the Dominican Republic mutually recognize each other and establish ambassador-level diplomatic relations. Adhering to the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Dominican Republic is what people's hearts desire and the general trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180501_11950081.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-05-02","Hua Chunying","","The Taiwan side claimed that the mainland used vast financial incentives to lure the Dominican Republic to sever \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world. The Government of the People's Republic of China is the only legal government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. It is completely in line with international law and norms guiding international relations for the Dominican Republic to sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan region and establish diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China. It also serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the people in the two countries. Everything involved is logical, rightful and aboveboard. There is no lure or deal to speak of.\nChina's establishment of diplomatic ties with the Dominican Republic is conditioned on only one premise, which is the recognition and adherence to the one-China principle, a position that has been declared by the Dominican side in the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the People's Republic of China and the Dominican Republic and their public statements. So the time and conditions are all there for it to happen. We believe that the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the Dominican Republic will open up broad prospects for the all-around friendly cooperation between the two countries. This is another testament to the fact that adherence to the one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community. It corresponds with the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1556224.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1556160.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-03","Hua Chunying","","In response to Taiwan's accusation that the Dominican Republic cut off their \"diplomatic ties\" in exchange for vast cash assistance, President Danilo Medina of the Dominican Republic said that China established diplomatic relations with his country with no strings attached. They were following the trend of the history. The Dominican Republic cannot be expected to forever stay out of a diplomatic relationship with…","We have noted these positive statements made by President Medina. China highly commends the unanimous support of the Dominican Republic's governing and opposition parties and all walks of life to the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and that country. There is only one China in the world. The Government of the People's Republic of China is the only legal government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Forty-seven years ago, the one-China principle was incorporated by the UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. Today, it has become a well-recognized principle for international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. The establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the Dominican Republic is another testament to the fact that the one-China principle is the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times. No efforts will succeed in trying to stop the rolling wheels of history.\nWe believe that after the establishment of diplomatic ties, more bilateral cooperation potential will be unleashed, which will bring unprecedented opportunities to the development of the Dominican Republic and tangible interests and benefits to the two peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1556501.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1556448.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-04","Hua Chunying","","President Danilo Medina of the Dominican Republic said yesterday that they hope the Chinese mainland will admit Dominican students studying in Taiwan with scholarships. Will the Chinese mainland admit them ?","China cares a lot about the Dominican scholarship receivers who are now studying in Taiwan. As long as they wish to study in the mainland, we will admit them. I believe that the mainland will become a warm new home for them.\nTaking the establishment of diplomatic ties as a new starting point, China is willing to expand our people-to-people and cultural exchanges, including promoting cooperation between universities so as to offer more convenience to our young students for their study in and visit to the other country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1556810.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1556738.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-07","Geng Shuang","","The Weibo account of the US Embassy in China made comments today that it objected to the letter of the China Civil Aviation Administration which asked foreign air carriers to change their identification of the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions, compelling private firms to use specific language of political nature. What's your reaction to this?","I already responded to this issue yesterday. I can restate my answer if you need it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1557299.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1557246.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-07","Geng Shuang","","Can you make a response to the comments by the US Embassy?","Whatever the US side says or does will never change the objective fact that there is only one China in the world and the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions are all inalienable parts of China's territory. China will continue to handle its relations with other countries in accordance with the one-China principle. In the meantime, we have to point out that foreign enterprises operating in China should respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by China's law and respect the national feeling of the Chinese people. This is the basic principle for them to follow when doing business here.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1557299.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1557246.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-07","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, the registration for the 71st World Health Assembly (WHA) will end today, and Taiwan has yet to receive an invitation. The WHA invited Taiwan for eight consecutive years from 2009 to 2016. What is your comment on it?","The one-China principle represents the universal consensus shared by the international community. The WHA must adhere to the one-China principle which has been endorsed by the UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and the WHA Resolution 25.1 when handling the Taiwan-related issues.\nThe Taiwan region attended the WHA in the name of \"Chinese Taipei\" as an observer for eight consecutive years from 2009 to 2016. This was a special arrangement made by cross-Strait consultations based on mutual adherence to the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP)'s refusal to acknowledge the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle undermines the political foundation for the Taiwan region to attend the WHA. If Taiwan does not receive the invitation this year, the DPP is the one to blame.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1557299.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1557246.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-07","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 7 (reporter Zhao Bo). TAO spokesperson An Fengshan, in an interview with reporters on the 7th on Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly (WHA), said that the reason Taiwan region still cannot attend the World Health Assembly this year is that the DPP authorities so far refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. The political basis for Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly does not exist, and the responsibility for its inability to attend lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nAn Fengshan said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. Our position on Taiwan region's participation in international organization activities has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations, and it should naturally handle Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly in accordance with the one-China principle established by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1.\nHe pointed out that from 2009 to 2016, Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly for eight consecutive years under the name “Chinese Taipei,” as an observer. This was a special arrangement reached through cross-Strait consultations, against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides adhere to as embodying the one-China principle. This fully shows that only by returning to the common political basis of the “1992 Consensus” can institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges continue, and only then can the two sides consult on Taiwan region's participation in international organization activities.\nAn Fengshan said that the mainland has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and has adopted multiple measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in the health field. Under the one-China principle, we have made proper arrangements for Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs. Under arrangements we have reached with the World Health Organization, experts from Taiwan region may attend WHO-related technical meetings and activities in an appropriate capacity, and the WHO may send experts to Taiwan for guidance when needed. These arrangements ensure that whether a public health emergency occurs on the island or internationally, Taiwan region can respond promptly and effectively. They reflect the mainland's goodwill and sincerity in addressing the health concerns of Taiwan compatriots.\nHe also said that under current circumstances, the DPP authorities should reflect on why Taiwan region still cannot attend the World Health Assembly this year, as it could not last year, rather than shirk responsibility, shift the focus, and mislead Taiwan residents and the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180507_11952573.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-05-08","Geng Shuang","","I know you commented yesterday on Taiwan and the World Health Assembly (WHA) issue. Did China ask the World Health Organization (WHO) not to invite Taiwan to the next WHA?","Taiwan is not a member of the WHO. Besides, it has no invitation. There is no wonder that it cannot attend the WHA.\nJust as I said yesterday, the Taiwan region's attendance at the WHA in the name of \"Chinese Taipei\" as an observer for eight consecutive years was a special arrangement made by cross-Straits consultations based on mutual adherence to the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP)'s refusal to acknowledge the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle undermines the political foundation for the Taiwan region to attend the WHA. If Taiwan is not invited this year, the DPP is the one to blame.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1557639.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1557583.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-08","Geng Shuang","","Can you clarify whether China has had any type of communication with the WHO in relation to Taiwan's participation this year?","As a member of the WHO, China remains close communication with the Secretariat and other members of the WHO.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1557639.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1557583.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-11","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, the Catholic Archbishop of Taiwan has said that he would like to invite the Pope to visit Taiwan next year. If such a visit did take place, what impact might this have on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Vatican?","I have not seen the report mentioned by you. There is only one China in the world. The one-China principle is a universal consensus shared by the international community. Accepting this principle conforms to the trend of the times and reflects the will of the people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1558711.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1558642.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","After the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots” were issued, they attracted a great deal of attention from Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the latest progress in localities and departments implementing the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots.”","We have previously introduced to you the implementation of the “31 Measures” since their release. Recently, localities and departments have continued to step up efforts to implement the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.” I will introduce several new developments to you.\nIn credit cooperation, the Shanghai Credit Information Services Co., Ltd., under the People’s Bank of China Credit Reference Center, has launched a joint business with the Taiwan Credit Information Center, the “Taiwan Region Credit Report Inquiry System.” This service provides mainland financial institutions with credit record inquiry services for enterprises and individuals in Taiwan, helping Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots resolve financing problems on the mainland.\nIn the field of high-tech cooperation, Jiangsu Province actively supports Taiwan-invested enterprises in applying for high-tech enterprise status and provincial science and technology plan projects. Taiwan-invested enterprises in Jiangsu that meet the conditions enjoy the same treatment under policies such as the comprehensive universal award and subsidy for enterprise technological transformation. At present, nearly 700 Taiwan-invested enterprises across the province have been recognized as high-tech enterprises and enjoy the 15% enterprise income tax preference. Two Taiwan-invested enterprises have successively received support from Jiangsu’s special fund for the transformation of scientific and technological achievements, and a total of 9.5 million yuan has been approved for payment.\nIn terms of policy subsidies, two Taiwan-invested food enterprises in Heilongjiang Province enjoy the same provincial livestock farming subsidies under the “two cattle and one pig” (dairy cows, beef cattle and hogs) policy, receiving subsidies at the provincial, municipal and county levels totaling 226 million yuan and 95 million yuan respectively.\nAs of April 20, 24 of the “31 Measures” have been implemented in Hubei Province. In terms of employment and recruitment, since the release of the “31 Measures,” Hubei Province has accelerated the implementation of the “Thousand Posts to Welcome Taiwan Youth” program. At present, 27 universities have provided 582 formal teaching positions, and a number of major enterprises in the province such as Huagong Technology, together with Taiwan-invested enterprises operating in Hubei, have provided 2,068 internship and employment positions.\nIn the selection of honorary titles for Taiwan compatriots, Fujian, Shandong, Jiangsu and Hubei commended a group of Taiwan compatriots during this year’s May Day holiday. Fujian Province and Shandong Province selected five and one Taiwan compatriots respectively as 2018 provincial model workers. Jiangsu Province awarded one Taiwan compatriot the “May Day Labor Honor Medal.” Hubei Province awarded several Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan the title of “March 8 Red Banner Bearer,” the title of 2018 provincial model worker, and the 2018 Hubei Youth “May Fourth” Medal, and several other Taiwan compatriots received various honors at the prefecture and municipal levels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955399.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","海峡之声电台记者","This year marks the tenth anniversary of the Wenchuan earthquake. The “Taiwan Compatriots in Sichuan” event was held recently, and public opinion has recalled the scenes when compatriots on both sides of the Strait joined hands to overcome the disaster after the earthquake. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","This year marks the tenth anniversary of the Sichuan Wenchuan major earthquake. Ten years ago, when the earthquake disaster occurred, countless Taiwan compatriots reached out to the people in the Sichuan disaster areas, whether in rescue, disaster relief or post-disaster reconstruction, expressing their care and providing help in various ways. The love among compatriots is deeply moving. From May 10 to 14, Sichuan Province held a special event titled \"'5·12' Wenchuan Major Earthquake 10th Anniversary Taiwan Compatriots' Sichuan Tour.\" More than 50 Taiwan personalities, representatives of various sectors of charitable individuals, representatives of donating enterprises and social organizations, and media people attended the event, including Fu Kun-chi (傅崐萁), County Magistrate of Hualien, Ou Chin-te (欧晋德), former Deputy Mayor of Taipei who led the rescue team to the disaster area in those years, and Kao Chin-su-mei (高金素梅), a Taiwan legislator. They visited Taiwan compatriot-assisted reconstruction projects in Dujiangyan, Mianyang, Deyang and other places, and saw that the areas hit by the disaster in those years had been completely renewed, and felt even more the spirit of the disaster-stricken people rebuilding their homes with high spirits and drive. At the event, County Magistrate Fu Kun-chi said that when Hualien County suffered an earthquake disaster in February this year, compatriots on the mainland likewise expressed their mutual support and friendship to the people of the disaster area. The mutual support of compatriots on both sides fully embodies the principle that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.\" As long as Chinese people on both sides of the Strait unite and work together, no difficulties or hardships can be overcome.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955394.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, some mainland media published an article suggesting that a list of “Taiwan independence” figures be published and that they be punished according to law, with those whose conduct is extremely egregious subjected to global wanted notices. It is reported that relevant mainland departments have begun collecting such a list. May I ask whether this is true?","Reunification across the Taiwan Strait is an irresistible historical trend. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that cannot succeed, and “Taiwan independence” diehards will only bring disaster to the Taiwan compatriots. Whatever has been done leaves traces. “Taiwan independence” diehards should not think that what they have said and done can leave no trace like a boat passing over water. Any obstinate and unrepentant “Taiwan independence” diehard will certainly be condemned by the people and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","What is your view on the recent apology by Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je over his remarks that “cross-Strait families are one family,” and his subsequent clarification of the matter? Also, Tsai Ing-wen is about to reach the second anniversary of taking office. Is the mainland still waiting for her answer sheet? In an earlier interview she said that the fact of the “1992 Talks” exists but that she cannot compromise on…","On your two questions. On the first question, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office has previously made a statement on this. We have also noted that the recent remarks by Mr. Ko Wen-je in an interview have caused much controversy on the island. We have said that any scheme to sow discord and create antagonism between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is bound to fail. Using the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides as material for political games is also unpopular.\nOn the second question, since “5·20” in 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, tolerated and abetted “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence,” obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and caused the current tense and confrontational state of cross-Strait relations. The responsibility lies with the DPP authorities. Compatriots on both sides firmly oppose this. Facing the current complex and grave situation in cross-Strait relations, we adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly oppose and deter any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and actions, continue to expand cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and will keep working to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peacefully achieving national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955397.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","The spokesperson previously said that if “Taiwan independence” forces continue to act recklessly, the mainland will take further action. Recently, the PLA Air Force conducted two-way patrol flights circling Taiwan island, achieving a new breakthrough in the island-circling patrol model. Is this one of the further actions the spokesperson referred to? In addition, in light of recent remarks and conduct by Tsai…","At the last press conference, we already made clear that the PLA military exercises and the air force's flights around the island convey a very clear and explicit message. They are a strong warning against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, and demonstrate our determination and capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to contain any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. “Taiwan independence” has no way out.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","It is reported that the first Cross-Strait Rural Revitalization Forum, hosted by Cross-Strait Relations magazine and other units, will be held in Ningbo, Zhejiang. Please introduce the situation.","It is reported that the First Cross-Strait Rural Revitalization Forum, themed “Cross-Strait Families Are One, Rural Areas Revitalize Together,” aimed at promoting excellent cross-Strait rural culture and common development of cross-Strait rural areas, was held from May 16 to 18 in Ninghai County, Ningbo City, Zhejiang Province. The forum was guided by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and jointly hosted by the 《两岸关系》 magazine, the Ningbo Municipal Agricultural and Rural Affairs Office, and the Taiwan Affairs Office. More than a hundred Taiwan compatriots, including former KMT Vice Chairman 林政则, will attend the forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955393.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","经济日报记者","Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation regarding the cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites that the TAO has newly established recently, as well as those set up previously.","To help Taiwan youth develop on the mainland, and in keeping with the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we encourage and support relevant parties to build platforms and explore experience. In recent years, a large number of platforms serving Taiwan youth in employment and entrepreneurship have emerged in various localities. Recently, after extensive selection, the Taiwan Affairs Office newly established 22 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases and Demonstration Sites in 15 provinces and municipalities, including Tianjin, Shanghai, and Fujian. These bases and demonstration sites each have their own characteristics. Some focus on providing platforms for Taiwan youth to take internships and find jobs on the mainland, and some are exploring and innovating in training Taiwan youth for employment and entrepreneurship. They will work hard to provide services for Taiwan youth in exchange, training, internships, employment, and entrepreneurship on the mainland, and to create a better development environment.\nPreviously, since 2015, the Taiwan Affairs Office has successively granted plaques to establish 53 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases and Demonstration Sites in 12 provinces and municipalities, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Liaoning. Adding these 22, the total is 75. According to statistics, as of the end of 2017, these entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites had housed or served about 1,900 Taiwan-funded enterprises and teams in total, and nearly 9,000 Taiwan youth had interned, found employment, or started businesses there (counted by person-time), with more than 50,000 person-times taking part in exchange activities organized by the bases and demonstration sites. They have gradually become a bridge for youth exchange across the Strait and an important vehicle for Taiwan youth to intern, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955410.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","May I ask the spokesperson: Regarding the Quanzhou military exercises, the aircraft circling Taiwan, and the Dominican Republic's severing of so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan, is the mainland taking these actions in response to Lai Ching-te's pragmatic “Taiwan independence” theory? Second question, regarding a meeting between cross-Strait leaders: Tsai Ing-wen said that the two sides could sit down…","On the first question: as I already said when answering the earlier reporter's question, the measures we have taken are aimed at delivering a strong warning against the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities.\nSince 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and cannot change. From 2008 to 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations achieved peaceful development. However, since the DPP authorities came to power, they have undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, tolerated and indulged “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence” activities, and obstructed and interfered with cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They have created cross-Strait confrontation, destroyed the hard-won situation and achievements of peaceful development across the Strait, harmed the interests of compatriots on both sides, and caused cross-Strait relations to regress. Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” remarks have further openly provoked peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Therefore, the responsibility for the current regression of cross-Strait relations lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nOn the second question: we have always said that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Its nature is completely different from the Korean issue. Everyone has also seen that from 2008 to 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which upholds the one-China principle and opposes “Taiwan independence,” and under the joint efforts of both sides and compatriots on both sides, against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the leaders of the two sides held a historic meeting on November 7, 2015. However, since the DPP authorities came to power, they have undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, which has led to the regression of cross-Strait relations. So we say that the responsibility lies with the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955395.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","The 10th Straits Forum is about to be held in Fujian. May I ask the spokesperson how the preparations for the forum are going? What new highlights does this session have? Second question: the first cross-Strait joint-venture consumer finance company recently received formal approval to begin preparatory work in Xiamen. May I ask the spokesperson, does this mean that cross-Strait financial cooperation has further…","The 10th Straits Forum will hold its forum conference on June 6. At the previous press conference, we introduced the relevant preparations for the Straits Forum. The preparatory work is currently advancing in an intense and orderly manner.\nOn the second question, promoting cross-Strait financial cooperation has always been our consistent position. Our recently issued “31 Measures” also contain relevant content on strengthening cross-Strait financial cooperation. I believe that the implementation and concrete advancement of the “31 Measures” will provide broader room for development in cross-Strait financial cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾《中国时报》记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je stressed on the 10th that the tone of “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family” that he advocates will not change. But he also pointed out that Taiwan's society is being held hostage by 6% of people with obvious “blue” or “green” coloring. Recently, some Taiwan scholars have called on the remaining 94% silent majority to awaken, using a “colorless” awakening to break the “blue-green” combat…","We have noted the phenomenon you mentioned. As for the thinking and actions of Taiwan people in facing the current chaotic situation in Taiwan's domestic politics and the complex and severe state of cross-Strait relations, we will not comment. As far as cross-Strait relations are concerned, our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and promote peaceful reunification, with the aim of enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. I think time will reveal people's hearts. The development and progress of the mainland in recent years, and the policy measures we have consistently introduced to benefit compatriots on both sides, have allowed more and more Taiwan people to feel our genuine sincerity toward Taiwan compatriots, and also to feel that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and exchanges and cooperation in all fields are beneficial to ordinary Taiwan people. At the same time, we also recognize that the development and progress of the mainland are opportunities for Taiwan, not challenges, and certainly not threats. What truly threatens and challenges the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots is “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. Therefore, we will take any necessary measures to oppose and contain the separatist schemes and actions of “Taiwan independence,” in order to prevent the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots from being harmed. So, in the face of such development of cross-Strait relations, more and more Taiwan compatriots will gradually awaken and understand these truths, and will then be able to join compatriots on the mainland in jointly promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","After his recent talks with Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, Premier Li Keqiang noted that both sides of China and Japan confirmed their adherence to the \"four political documents,\" established various principles, and properly handled sensitive issues such as history and Taiwan. We have noted that Kishi Nobuo, a Liberal Democratic Party lawmaker and younger brother of Shinzo Abe, temporarily cancelled his trip…","Your first question further demonstrates that the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community, and that it is the trend of the times.\nSecond, I am not familiar with the report you mentioned. What I want to say is that since 2005, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the KMT and the CPC have jointly advanced the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The core meaning of this common foundation is that both sides of the Strait belong to one China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾东森新闻云记者","What is the current preparation status of the KMT-CPC Forum? Could you please explain?","Relevant parties of the KMT and CPC have been maintaining smooth communication on carrying out inter-party exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","According to reports, although the DPP authorities still have not received an invitation to the World Health Assembly, the DPP has nonetheless decided to lead a delegation to Geneva to tag along at the meeting in order to gain international attention. What is the spokesperson's evaluation? Thank you.","Our spokespersons have previously explained our position and attitude. From 2009 to 2016, on the basis of both sides' adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and through cross-Strait consultations, and in accordance with the arrangements reached between us and the WHO, Taiwan participated in the World Health Assembly for eight consecutive years under the name “Chinese Taipei” and as an observer. This was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The reason Taiwan cannot attend this year is that the DPP authorities still refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” so the basis and prerequisites for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly no longer exist. Therefore, the responsibility for its inability to attend lies with the DPP authorities.\nUnder the current circumstances, what the Taiwan authorities should actually reflect on is why Taiwan has been unable to attend the World Health Assembly for two consecutive years, rather than shirking responsibility, shifting the focus, and misleading Taiwan's public and the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","大公网记者","The “Hong Kong independence” organization “Hong Kong National Front” claims that it has established a so-called formal alliance with the “Taiwan independence” organization “Islanders Against China United,” and threatens to “forcibly split China.” What is the spokesperson's response?","“Taiwan independence” forces and some “Hong Kong independence” forces are colluding with each other, attempting to endanger national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to harm the vital interests of compatriots. Doing so is unpopular and will never succeed. Moreover, by doing so, they are essentially tearing off the so-called “freedom, democracy and human rights” cloak they have draped over themselves, exposing their true face of splitting the country and harming the interests of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Following the ban on teachers from the island teaching on the mainland, the DPP authorities have once again reiterated in the cultural and educational sphere that in the future, books authorized by the mainland for publication in Taiwan may all have to undergo review by the Taiwan authorities before they can be published. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","For a long time, we have consistently advocated and promoted exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, so that compatriots on both sides can understand each other and develop together. We recently issued the “31 Measures” to promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait and to speed up granting Taiwan compatriots equal treatment. These have been warmly welcomed and praised by broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, which also shows that this is what the people want. Yet the DPP authorities, instead of thinking about how to conform to public sentiment and do good things that benefit compatriots on both sides, are doing the opposite, constantly placing obstacles in the way of normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. What they restrict is the opportunity for Taiwan compatriots to obtain greater, bigger and better development, and what they harm is the interests of Taiwan compatriots themselves. Doing this is not supported by the people. To use an analogy: one side is building bridges and laying roads, while the other is destroying roads and tearing down bridges. Comparing the two, the difference is clear; who is safeguarding the interests of compatriots and who is harming their well-being is plain to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180516_11955396.htm"],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","On the 10th, the House Armed Services Committee of the US House of Representatives passed the so-called “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2019” draft, which advocates that the US should assist the Taiwan authorities in strengthening Taiwan's defense capabilities to counter the mainland. Meanwhile, the “US-Taiwan Defense Industry Forum” recently took place in Kaohsiung. According to Taiwanese…","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan, and firmly oppose US arms sales to Taiwan. This position is consistent and very clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We have noted that Taiwan's internal affairs authorities plan to amend the Regulations on Mainland Residents Traveling to Taiwan for Sightseeing, reducing the deposit requirement for individual and group tourist travel by mainland residents from the current NT$200,000 to NT$100,000. What is the spokesperson's view? Second question: 马英九, former leader of the Taiwan region, was charged in the “leaking secrets…","First question: Mainland tourists’ willingness and numbers to travel to Taiwan have both declined. What is the reason? As everyone knows, the side in Taiwan should consider how to work hard on resolving the crux problems. Second question: On affairs on the island, I will not comment. But I think Taiwan compatriots will have their own public judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾“中央社”记者","Taiwan’s Da Ai Television recently aired a new drama called “Heart of the Wisdom Child.” It was taken off the air shortly after its broadcast last week, reportedly because the storyline glorifies the Japanese colonial era. The mainland seems to have expressed concern about this. Please respond.","We also note that after the trailer for this TV drama was released, it was immediately and unanimously condemned by netizens on both sides of the Strait. Any practice that glorifies wars of aggression and champions colonial rule will naturally be opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","中央广电总台央广记者","Taiwan's relevant authorities recently announced a ban on the Taiwan military's use of mainland-brand smartphones, with Xiaomi and Huawei both placed on the blacklist. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have always said that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee for maintaining peace in the Taiwan Strait and promoting common development. In fact, many matters across the Strait come down to a question of position and mindset. If one holds a hostile mindset and wears green-tinted glasses, one cannot see the prospects for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by thoroughly discarding the “Taiwan independence” position and the hostile mindset can peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations truly be achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","环球网记者","We noticed that a T-shirt sold by the American brand GAP outside China bears a truncated map of China on which Taiwan has been erased. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","Earlier, a spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated clearly in response to a reporter's question that foreign companies operating in China should respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by China's laws, and respect the national sentiments of the Chinese people. This is the most basic requirement for doing business here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","中国日报记者","Tsai Ing-wen's governance has faced continuous difficulties over the past two years, and her approval ratings in local polls keep falling. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We do not comment on specific polls on the island; these are matters for the island's public to judge for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-16","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","A U.S. senator warned today that Paraguay may be the next country to “sever ties” with Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's view?","We have said many times that the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180516_11955430.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-05-18","Lu Kang","","According to reports, on May 16, US Senator Marco Rubio said at a hearing of the Senate Foreign Relations Committee that Paraguay may be the next country to cut off its \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. The spokesperson of the US State Department recently said that the Dominican Republic's severing of its \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan unilaterally changed the status quo and was not conducive to upholding regional…","China stands ready to develop friendly cooperative relations with other countries around the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one-China principle. Since last year, China has established diplomatic ties with Panama and the Dominican Republic. It once again demonstrates that the one-China principle has been universally acknowledged and endorsed by the international community. As a principle of righteousness, it corresponds with the will of the people and the irresistible trend of the times.\nWe are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to the above-mentioned remarks by the US side. The US established diplomatic ties with the People's Republic of China in 1979 and acknowledged in the three China-US Joint Communiques that there is only one China in the world and that the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole China. So, it baffles us as to why the US side wants to prevent other countries from recognizing the one-China principle and normalizing relations with the People's Republic of China? We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle, honor the clauses and its commitments in the three China-US Joint Communiques, refrain from making irresponsible remarks at other countries' decisions to develop ties with China, and stop exploiting cross-Straits relations to interfere in China's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1560672.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1560574.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-18","Lu Kang","","According to reports, recently, the Spanish side repatriated two Taiwanese telecom fraud suspects to the mainland. The Taiwanese department in charge of its so-called foreign affairs voiced strong protest over this, claiming that the mainland \"forcibly interfered in and imposed pressure on\" Spain's court trial process. What is your comment?","China highly appreciates the Spanish government's adherence to the one-China principle when handling the Taiwan-related issues. We are pleased to see that with the deepening of political mutual trust and solid progress in practical cooperation between China and Spain, more fruitful outcomes have been achieved in cooperation on combating crimes and conducting joint law enforcement operations.\nAs to some comments made by certain people in Taiwan, it falls within China's internal affairs and I would refer you to the competent authority, namely, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1560672.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1560574.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-05-22","Lu Kang","","The World Health Assembly (WHA) this year has decided not to include the Taiwan-related proposal in its supplementary agenda. What's your comment?","This year's WHA resolutely and neatly refused to incorporate into its supplementary agenda the so-called proposal of \"inviting Taiwan to attend the WHA as an observer\". This decision safeguards the dignity of the relevant resolutions of the UN General Assembly and the WHA, fully testifying to the fact that the one-China principle is the shared aspiration of the international community and the trend of the times. China welcomes this. I would like to reiterate that the Chinese government is willing to properly handle the issue of the Taiwan region's participation in the activities of international organizations in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1561528.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1561452.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-22","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","(Xinhua) Beijing, May 22 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, on May 22, responded to a reporter's question about the World Health Assembly's decision not to include the invitation of Taiwan region in this year's supplementary agenda, saying: The one-China principle is the broad consensus of the international community. The WHO, as a specialized agency of the United Nations, handles Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle established by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1, and we highly appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180523_11957975.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-05-25","Lu Kang","","Burkina Faso announced last night that it was cutting off ties with Taiwan. When will the Chinese government open an embassy in Ouagadougou? Will China offer financial aids and preferential loans to Burkina Faso?","The government of Burkina Faso yesterday issued a statement on severing the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. The Chinese Foreign Ministry has immediately made clear China's attitude. We appreciate this move. We believe that the decision by the government of Burkina Faso is in the interests of its people and testifies to the one-China principle that is universally recognized by the international community. This is a correct decision made by the Burkina Faso government, in keeping with the trend of the times and the world.\nChina has always stayed committed to developing friendly cooperative relations with countries around the globe on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence and the one-China principle. You may not need to feel surprised if a country that stays committed to the one-China principle in keeping with the trend of the times and the world establishes diplomatic ties with China.\nRegarding whether China will offer assistance to the government of Burkina Faso, I would like to stress that this decision made by the Burkina Faso government independently is first of all a political decision, a correct one that conforms to the trend of the world. Speaking of any friendly country, China is willing to conduct mutually beneficial cooperation with it on the basis of mutual respect, equality and win-win results. China and African countries have conducted a lot of mutually beneficial cooperation under the framework of the China-Africa Cooperation Forum. If China and Burkina Faso establish diplomatic ties some day, we will carry out such cooperation under the same framework. We believe this is good to both sides.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1562652.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1562568.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-26","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 26 (reporter Zha Wenye). In response to Burkina Faso's announcement that it is severing so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan and restoring ties with China, TAO spokesperson An Fengshan told reporters on the 26th in response to questions: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has issued a statement on the restoration of China-Burkina Faso relations. Burkina Faso's restoration of ties with China is a correct choice made according to its own national and people's interests. The facts once again prove that adherence to the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180526_11959043.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-05-29","Hua Chunying","","In response to the resumption of diplomatic ties between China and Burkina Faso, Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed that the Taiwan authorities would not compete with the mainland in the so-called \"checkbook diplomacy\". What is your comment?","The Taiwan authorities' allegation that the mainland conducts \"checkbook diplomacy\" is entirely a groundless slander.\nThere is only one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government that represents the whole of China and Taiwan is an inseparable part of the Chinese territory. This not only has been enshrined by the United Nations' resolution but also represents the universal consensus of the overwhelming majority of the countries around the globe. The Chinese government never allowed, does not allow and will never allow the one-China principle to be traded away. Anyone with global vision and common sense knows this fully well.\nBurkina Faso's severing of the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan and resumption of diplomatic ties with the People's Republic of China is a correct political decision. It is independently made by the government of Burkina Faso. It is a right thing that most countries in the world have already done. It conforms to international law and the norms governing international relations. It serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the two peoples. It keeps up with the trend of the times. Last but not least, it has won the support of both ruling and opposition parties as well as people of various circles in Burkina Faso. We have noted that President Karim Démé of Le point focal de la République populaire de Chine in Burkina Faso said that his country has made a major decision that is conducive to its development in the future. Burkina Faso needs a serious and strategic cooperative partner with international influence, and China is exactly such a partner. Burkina Faso's newspaper Le Pays also commented that time will prove that President Roch Marc Christian Kaboré has made a correct decision.\nBurkina Faso's recognition of and commitment to the one-China principle as well as its resumption of diplomatic ties with China without any prerequisite have come along in an open and aboveboard manner. Now Burkina Faso has returned to the big family for China-Africa friendship as it should. The fact has again proved that adhering to the one-China principle represents the universal consensus of the international community, corresponds with the irresistible trend of the times and meets the shared aspirations of the people. Certain people with tunnel vision should refrain from self-deception.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1563568.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1563482.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporter friends, good morning. Welcome to everyone attending the regular press conference held by the Taiwan Affairs Office this morning. I am willing to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","新华社记者","At recent press conferences, the spokesperson has repeatedly introduced the situation in various areas of the mainland in promoting the implementation of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” and there have been continuous new developments in this area. Could the spokesperson introduce the latest situation today?","Since the 31 measures to promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation were issued and implemented in February this year, various localities and departments have been pressing ahead with implementation at a rapid pace, and they will soon be fully implemented. Many of these measures have already produced results, allowing Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to enjoy tangible benefits. We have already introduced the relevant implementation progress several times at previous press conferences. Shanghai, Fujian, Guangdong, Zhejiang, Jiangsu, and other provinces and municipalities where Taiwan enterprises and compatriots are relatively concentrated have already launched, or are successively launching, detailed implementation rules tailored to local conditions. This is accelerating the implementation of policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, so that Taiwan compatriots and enterprises will have more opportunities and broader room to develop on the mainland. Here, I would like to introduce several new examples of progress in implementation.\nIn professional qualification examinations: among the professional qualification examinations newly opened to Taiwan compatriots this time, for the qualifications of nondestructive testing personnel for civil nuclear safety equipment, operators of civil nuclear facilities, and registered nuclear safety engineers, Taiwan compatriots may apply to take the examinations under the current examination rules. For the banking professional qualification examination, Taiwan compatriots may register to take the examination in the second half of 2018. For Taiwan compatriots applying for the entry-exit quarantine handling personnel qualification examination, the General Administration of Customs will announce specific arrangements in the near future. For professional qualification examinations previously opened to Taiwan compatriots, such as the patent agent qualification, the performance brokerage personnel qualification, and the engineering consulting (investment) professional and technical personnel qualification examinations, Taiwan compatriots may continue to register under current regulations.\nIn participation in government procurement: Fujian Province has no market access threshold for Taiwan-invested enterprises in the procurement field, and encourages them to take part in government procurement. Across the province, procurement included 1,303 branded automobiles produced by Taiwan-invested enterprises, worth RMB 155 million, and the province’s banking system procured nearly 30,000 monitors produced by Taiwan-invested enterprises.\nIn high-tech cooperation: Taiwan-invested enterprises in Zhejiang Province may participate in the province’s “machine replacement” demonstration projects, enterprise technology center programs, and evaluations of outstanding industrial new products and new technologies, and enjoy the same policies as other enterprises in the province. 83 Taiwan-invested high-tech enterprises in Zhejiang enjoy the 15% enterprise income tax rate.\nIn agricultural cooperation: a Taiwan-invested enterprise in Guizhou was recognized as a national key leading enterprise for agricultural industrialization and as a key leading enterprise for agricultural industrialization in Guizhou Province, and the company has successively received more than RMB 16 million in support funds at various levels. A Taiwan-invested enterprise in Fujian was recognized as a key leading enterprise for agricultural industrialization in Fujian Province, and has successively received more than RMB 4 million in project support, including financial loan interest subsidies, comprehensive agricultural development, and integration of the primary, secondary, and tertiary industries.\nIn the future, based on the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots, we will continue to introduce more policy measures that give Taiwan compatriots and enterprises equal treatment, and continuously enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960291.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the preparations for the 10th Straits Forum. What highlights does this session of the Straits Forum have?","The 10th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in early June this year. The forum conference will be held in Xiamen on June 6, and activities will be carried out successively across Fujian over a period of one week. At present, preparations for the forum are basically in place. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, will attend and deliver an important speech. Representatives of relevant Taiwan political parties, county and city representatives, and several thousand people from all walks of life in Taiwan will attend the forum activities. The overall scale is comparable to last year.\nThis forum will be a grand occasion for civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. The forum is divided into four major sections: youth exchange, grassroots exchange, cultural exchange and economic exchange, with 69 activities planned. The activities cover youth creative competitions, workers' skills, social welfare, film and television exchanges, caring for the next generation, economy and finance, cross-Strait marriages, traditional culture, community governance, and distinctive temple fairs, among many other areas. The content is more diverse than before, the forms are richer, and participation from all sectors will be broader. People from all walks of life in Taiwan and grassroots residents are full of anticipation for attending this forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960287.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","人民日报海外版记者","After Burkina Faso declared on May 24 that it was severing so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan, the Taiwan authorities claimed this was caused by the mainland’s “dollar diplomacy.” Tsai Ing-wen also said that the mainland’s suppression of Taiwan has challenged Taiwan’s bottom line and that Taiwan will no longer tolerate it. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. The restoration of diplomatic relations between China and Burkina Faso is a correct choice made by Burkina Faso based on its own national and people's interests. As for some people on the island falsely claiming \"dollar diplomacy\", this is entirely groundless, self-deceiving, and judging others by one's own heart. What the DPP authorities themselves have done is worth asking themselves.\nPeaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to safeguard peace across the Strait, promote common development, and benefit compatriots on both sides, and it is also the only correct choice for the DPP authorities. The root cause of the current political deadlock in cross-Strait relations is well known. If the DPP authorities acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" as soon as possible and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, cross-Strait relations will return to the correct direction of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960290.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Recently, Kuomintang Chairman Wu Den-yih rarely stated clearly his position on cross-Strait unification at an internal party meeting, emphasizing that Taiwan’s “Additional Articles of the Constitution” “ultimately take national unification as the principle.” Tsai Ing-wen, however, claimed that unification cannot be the only option for Taiwan’s young people. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Achieving national reunification has always been the shared goal of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and a sacred common aspiration and responsibility of all Chinese people. From 2008 to 2016, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and through the joint efforts of both sides and compatriots on both sides, a new era of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations was opened, and compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, gained real benefits from it. We hope that all sectors across the Strait will work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and contribute their efforts to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960289.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Regarding Taiwan losing two “diplomatic allies” within a single month, Tsai Ing-wen said it would not yield again. The Taiwan authorities will strictly review mainland visiting delegations to Taiwan, and it is reported that 10 mainland officials who applied to attend the Straits Forum were refused. What is the spokesperson's response to this? In addition, will the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum continue to be held?…","You asked three questions. Regarding the Straits Forum activities you mentioned: the Straits Forum is currently the largest and most widely participated civil exchange activity across the Taiwan Strait, with the greatest number of participants. It is also an important platform for strengthening exchange and mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides. The forum has now been held for ten sessions. Over the past decade it has been widely welcomed by grassroots people on both sides, who have continued to take part enthusiastically, deepening mutual understanding and family ties through exchange. I therefore believe that strengthening exchange and cooperation is the shared wish of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities, for political purposes, are obstructing and suppressing this civil exchange, which runs against popular sentiment.\nAs for your second question, as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-strait relations and of exchanges between counties and cities across the Strait, our attitude toward cross-strait county and city exchanges has been consistent and clear.\nAs for your third question, relevant departments of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party have maintained smooth communication on party-to-party exchange activities all along. The two parties will strengthen contact on the common basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” continue to promote the well-being of compatriots, and advance the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Some people on the island have promoted holding a so-called “Olympic name-correction referendum,” attempting to change the name in order to participate in the Tokyo Olympics. The International Olympic Committee has already sent a letter to the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee expressing concern about this, and demanding that Taiwan abide by the relevant agreements and that it will not approve any renaming moves.…","It is understood that, in response to some people in Taiwan promoting a so-called “Olympic name-change referendum,” the International Olympic Committee on May 5 sent a letter to the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee, requiring it to abide by the IOC’s resolutions and regulations on Taiwan’s participation in competitions, namely the “Olympic Model,” and expressly stated that it would not consider approving any change to its existing name.\nOver the years, under the “Olympic Model,” Taiwan’s athletes have been able to take part in international sporting events, including the Olympic Games, demonstrating good competitive standards and sportsmanship and winning gold and silver medals, which is a source of pride for all Chinese people on both sides. Pushing a so-called “Olympic name-change referendum” is in fact only about satisfying the selfish interests of a very small number of extreme “Taiwan independence” diehards on the island. It harms the interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and sacrifices the competitive opportunities of Taiwan’s athletes. This will certainly be opposed by the international community and by compatriots on both sides, and will ultimately only backfire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960286.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","福建海峡导报记者","The relevant Taiwan authorities have already changed the term “Huaqiao” (overseas Chinese) in relevant administrative regulations to “Qiaomin” (overseas nationals), and claimed that this uses a relatively neutral term to encompass terms such as “Huazu” (Chinese ethnic group) and “Taiwan qiao.” Some public opinion questions whether, compared with the mainland, which has long devoted itself to protecting overseas…","Overseas Chinese are overseas Chinese. The DPP authorities’ manipulation of so-called “renaming” is in effect “de-Sinicization,” and they have put themselves on the opposite side of overseas Chinese. This practice can neither change the Chinese national identity of overseas Chinese nor win the recognition of the broad body of overseas Chinese.\nI would also like to stress that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are brothers of one blood, flesh and bone. For a long time, safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas, including overseas Chinese from Taiwan, has been our unshirkable responsibility and consistent practice, and it has been highly affirmed and praised by Taiwan compatriots. Our relevant agencies will continue to strengthen contact with Taiwan compatriots and overseas Chinese abroad, shelter them from wind and rain in critical moments, relieve their worries and difficulties, and help them solve practical problems.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960285.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","台湾《联合报》记者","There have been recent reports that if the Taiwan authorities continue to use punitive intimidation that leaves Taiwan businesspeople, teachers, and students working on the mainland unable to go home, the mainland is considering issuing mainland identity cards to these Taiwan people. Does the Taiwan Affairs Office have such considerations? The second question: Recently, foreign media coined a new term, the…","Regarding your first question, we have seen the relevant reports. Being one family across the Strait and strengthening exchange and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides, and it also benefits the interests and well-being of compatriots. The DPP authorities ignore the actual needs and vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, and disregard the people’s pursuit of a better life; they wantonly accuse and interfere with cross-Strait exchanges. I think the concerns raised by these scholars are understandable.\nRegarding your second question, I will not comment on the meaning of the term you mentioned. I think that, with regard to cross-Strait relations alone, the vigorous development and tremendous progress that the mainland has achieved over several decades of reform and opening up have been gradually changing Taiwan compatriots’ stereotypes of the mainland, and the mainland has continuously introduced measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots, which have been welcomed by more and more Taiwan compatriots. I think that the growing number of Taiwan people, especially grassroots people and some young people, who are willing to come to the mainland to study, exchange, start businesses, find employment, develop and live is also a concrete manifestation of this.\nI recall that at the time of the 19th National Congress last year, Lu Li-an, a Taiwan-born daughter, attracted wide attention on the island. When the island’s media discussed the “Lu Li-an phenomenon,” some commentary said that cross-Strait relations had entered an era of competition between systems and talent. At the previous press conference, I recall a reporter also asked about the phenomenon of the so-called “colorless awakening” on the island. In fact, in the face of the blue-green struggle and confrontation on the island, some island commentators also believe that the Kuomintang, the DPP and the Communist Party should compete with each other to see who loves Taiwan more, so that ordinary people have more choices.\nIn fact, whether a system or a political party is attractive depends on whether it can always take the people’s aspirations for and pursuit of a better life as its own goal of struggle, whether it can bring tangible benefits to ordinary people, whether it can provide them with better development opportunities and greater development space, and at the same time bring the people a brighter hope and vision. Apart from these things, shouting empty slogans such as “loving Taiwan,” or flaunting so-called “universal values,” is of no real help and cannot fool the eyes of ordinary people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the first “National Reunification and National Rejuvenation” seminar was held in Wuhan, attracting attention from public opinion on the island. Could the spokesperson briefly introduce the relevant content of the meeting? In addition, some commentators believe that the mainland has begun to unilaterally promote the process of national reunification. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","This seminar was sponsored by Central China Normal University and the Hubei Provincial Association for the Promotion of Cross-Strait Exchanges, under the theme “Jointly Seek National Reunification, Work Hand in Hand for National Rejuvenation.” Dai Bingguo, president of the National Taiwan Studies Association, attended and delivered a speech. Nearly one hundred experts and scholars from universities and research institutions on both sides of the Strait attended. The meeting pointed out that national reunification and national rejuvenation are mutually complementary. We must continue to resolutely oppose all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and prevent external forces from harming the overall interests of the Chinese nation. We must firmly take the path of peaceful development of cross-strait relations, actively advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and accumulate strength and create conditions for achieving reunification during national rejuvenation.\nI want to emphasize that advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland and realizing the reunification of the country is an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will strive to promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, steadily advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and create an even better future for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","After the restoration of China–Burkina Faso diplomatic relations, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said it will strictly review visits to Taiwan by officials at all levels of the mainland government and related personnel, and expand investigations into mainland entities that have set up bases in Taiwan under various names. What is your comment?","We have also repeatedly stressed that expanding cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations conform to the common wishes and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We have therefore consistently upheld the concept of “both sides of the Strait are one family,” continuously expanded and deepened cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and solidly advanced and implemented the “31 Measures,” with the aim of providing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses with more and better development opportunities and doing practical good deeds for them. By contrast, the DPP authorities keep inventing various reasons to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, constantly setting up barriers. In effect, they are restricting Taiwan compatriots' more and better development opportunities and harming their fundamental interests. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan compatriots can gain more and better benefits and well-being; this is a truth everyone knows. The DPP authorities' current approach is in effect going backward; it does good things for Taiwan compatriots badly, and it will inevitably meet the joint opposition of compatriots on both sides. For some time, in their performance on cross-Strait relations, which side has truly been full of confidence, building bridges, paving roads and opening up exchanges, and which side has inwardly been uneasy, building high walls and dams and pursuing “closing the country off”? I think ordinary people can see this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201805/t20180530_11960288.htm"],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Tsai Ing-wen has been in office for two years. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of the changes in cross-strait relations over these two years? Mainland Affairs Council Chairman Chen Ming-tong recently said that the failure of the Tsai authorities to manage cross-strait relations should not be blamed on not acknowledging the “1992 Consensus.” What is the spokesperson’s response?","At the last press conference, I already gave a basic answer to your first question. Since the DPP came to power on May 20, 2016, it has refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle. This has undermined the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations, condoned and tolerated \"de-Sinicization\" and \"gradual Taiwan independence,\" and obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, causing the current tension and confrontation in cross-Strait relations. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait firmly oppose this.\nFaced with the current complex and severe situation in cross-Strait relations, the mainland's policies toward Taiwan are consistent and clear. We will continue to adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and firmly oppose and deter any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes and actions. At the same time, we will continue to deepen and expand cross-Strait economic, cultural and exchange and cooperation, unite compatriots in Taiwan to jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.\nOn your second question: since 2016, the crux of the current political impasse in cross-Strait relations lies precisely in the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" whose core meaning is recognition that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Therefore, whether the DPP authorities can take a clear position and attitude, acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China is something people are watching closely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The State Council has recently released a plan to further deepen reform and opening-up of the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone, which will focus on strengthening Fujian-Taiwan financial cooperation. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","We actively promote deeper financial exchange and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan. The deepening reform and opening-up plan for the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone proposes a large number of pilot policy measures targeting Taiwan in the financial field, including supporting qualified Taiwan-funded financial institutions in the Free Trade Zone to conduct underwriting business in the interbank bond market, and exploring the establishment of a mutual recognition mechanism for credit information products with Taiwan. These measures will bring new opportunities for Taiwan financial enterprises to share in the achievements of the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone and to deepen financial cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan.\nThis year marks the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up. Measures such as the mainland's accelerated construction of free trade zones, expanded opening of the service sector, and relaxed market access in the financial industry also apply to Taiwan-funded enterprises. These measures will further provide Taiwan-funded enterprises with rare opportunities and broad development prospects to share in the mainland's development achievements. We will also continue to introduce policy measures for deepening reform and expanding opening up, so that Taiwan compatriots can take the lead in sharing the opportunities and achievements of the mainland's development more widely and to a greater extent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Two questions. First, we note that on the 24th, local time, the US House of Representatives voted to pass the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2019,” which advocates so-called “US-Taiwan military exchanges.” Recently, a US Congressman has also proposed the so-called “Taiwan Defense Assessment Committee Act.” May I ask for the spokesperson's comment? Second question: Lee Teng-hui will travel to…","Your first question: The Taiwan question concerns China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Therefore, we firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.\nYour second question: Regarding the practice of certain individuals on the island who glorify colonial rule and promote aggressive war and militarism, compatriots on both sides of the Strait will firmly oppose it and jointly condemn it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央广记者","It is understood that 15 mainland subsidiaries of Taiwan-invested enterprises plan to list on the A-share market. What is the spokesperson's comment?","With deepening reform and expanded opening-up, the mainland's economic development prospects will become ever broader, and more and more enterprises are willing to list on the mainland to share in the opportunities and achievements of its development. I believe this is a trend that accords with market rules.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, according to Taiwan media reports, the principals of two Taiwan secondary schools were “concerned” about by relevant departments of the Taiwan authorities for writing recommendation letters for graduates to study in the mainland and for making remarks about Taiwan students studying in the mainland. What is your comment?","In recent years, with the development and progress of the mainland and the series of convenience measures we have introduced for the benefit of Taiwan compatriots, more and more young people from Taiwan are willing to come to the mainland to develop. This is a good thing. Taiwanese students hope to study at mainland universities in pursuit of better personal opportunities and to realize their life dreams, and parents also hope their children can have a better educational opportunity. This is both a matter of human sentiment and a trend of the times. Youth is the future and hope of the nation. Failing to provide young people with better opportunities, higher platforms and greater space for development, and instead setting all kinds of obstacles and obstructing and restricting young people's development, will only hurt and lose the hearts of young people.\nWe have consistently encouraged exchange and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, including educational exchange. In the future we will also continue to introduce more and stronger measures to provide better conditions and create more opportunities for Taiwan's young students to study, intern, work and start businesses on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-05-30","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Within one month, the Dominican Republic and Burkina Faso successively severed so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities. May I ask the spokesperson whether efforts in the diplomatic field will continue to be intensified in the future?","We have said it before: the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201805/t20180530_11960283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-06-01","Hua Chunying","","Swaziland is now the last country on the African continent to have the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. Do you have any particular message for Swaziland? Do you have any advice for them?","We have been sending out very clear message in recent days. The one-China principle corresponds with the trend of the times and meets the shared aspirations of the people. As you can see, more and more countries have developed across-the-board friendly cooperative relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle and achieved tangible progress. Swaziland is surely welcome to join the big family of China-Africa cooperation at an early date so that we can take a group photo of the whole family of China-Africa cooperation. Indeed, this all depends on Swaziland itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1564980.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1564868.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-05","Hua Chunying","","Does China have any comments regarding reports that the US military is considering sailing a warship through the Taiwan Strait?","We have repeatedly emphasized that the Taiwan issue is the most important and sensitive one sitting at the core of the China-US relationship. The US should strictly adhere to the one-China principle and the three joint Communiqués and prudently handle the Taiwan issue so as to avoid harming bilateral ties and cross-Straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1566054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1565977.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-05","Hua Chunying","","The Australian Foreign Minister recently criticized China for pressuring the airline Qantas to change how it refers to Taiwan on its website, saying that the activities of private companies should not be subject to political pressure. What is China's comment?","I have noted relevant reports. There is only one China in the world and Hong Kong, Taiwan and Macao have always been parts of China. This is an objective fact, a common sense as well as the general consensus of the international community. The relevant issue is not a general procedural or technical one. What the relevant Chinese department has asked for is based on the consistent and firm position held by the Chinese government on the one-China principle and is thus legal and legitimate. It has nothing to do with the so-called \"political inference\" or \"political pressure\". All companies operating in China should abide by the Chinese laws and regulations and respect and follow the one-China principle. That is the least they must do.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1566054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1565977.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-12","Geng Shuang","","据报道，6月12日，“美在台协会”台北办事处举行新址落成仪式。美国务院负责教育文化事务的助卿罗伊斯等出席。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1568094.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Today's press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","At several previous press conferences, the spokesperson introduced the new progress made by various localities and departments in implementing the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots.” Today, please ask the spokesperson to introduce some new developments.","Thank you all for your attention to the implementation of the “31 Measures.” On June 1, Shanghai issued the “Implementation Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Shanghai and Taiwan,” comprising 55 articles, of which 28 cover the economic field and 27 cover the cultural and social fields. These include content that corresponds to the implementation of the “31 Measures” in Shanghai, as well as measures under which Shanghai's public policies are opened ahead of other places, and measures with Shanghai characteristics. For example, they support Taiwan-funded enterprises in establishing headquarters, financial institutions, operations centers, procurement centers, and logistics centers in Shanghai; support Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the China International Import Expo to be held in Shanghai this December for display, sales, and procurement; support Shanghai Taiwan-funded enterprises in raising financing through equity custody trading institutions; support Taiwan professional and technical personnel coming to Shanghai for employment; provide talent support policies that give them the same treatment as local residents; and, for young Taiwan people coming to Shanghai to start businesses, innovate, and find jobs, provide subsidies for rent of startup premises during the early stage of their ventures and interest subsidies on guaranteed startup loans.\nOn June 6, Fujian Province issued its implementation opinions on carrying out the “31 Measures,” comprising 66 specific measures in four areas: expanding Fujian-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation, supporting Taiwan compatriots in internships, employment, and entrepreneurship in Fujian, deepening Fujian-Taiwan cultural exchanges, and facilitating Taiwan compatriots' settlement and livelihood in Fujian. Of these, 37 correspond to implementing the “31 Measures,” 24 are pilot measures that Fujian is trying out first, and another 5 replicate and promote relevant pilot policies. These 66 measures cover preferential policies for Taiwan-funded enterprises in areas such as industry access, financial services, funding support, and customs facilitation, and also involve equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots in study, internships, employment, entrepreneurship, residence, daily life, labor protection, medical care, transportation, and other areas in Fujian, as well as various measures deepening cultural exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan. For example, Taiwan-funded enterprises may participate in franchised operation projects in public service fields such as Fujian's expressways, rail transit, port transportation, and urban inland waterway improvement. Taiwan compatriots who come to Fujian for employment and entrepreneurship enjoy, in accordance with regulations, the same employment and entrepreneurship preferential policies as Fujian residents. Taiwan compatriots working in Fujian may participate in the “five social insurances and one housing provident fund” in accordance with regulations, and enjoy the same labor protection as local residents. Qualified financial institutions from Taiwan may apply, in accordance with regulations, to establish banks, life insurance companies, and other institutions in Fujian with a 51% or greater shareholding. Newly established Taiwan-funded enterprises in the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone may register in the same way as mainland enterprises; Taiwan professional and technical personnel holding accounting, planning, construction, consulting, finance, medical, tourism, and other professional licenses issued by relevant institutions in Taiwan may, within the scope permitted by their certificates, conduct corresponding business in the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone in accordance with relevant regulations. It is also understood that several other provinces and cities are actively drafting relevant implementation measures.\nIn professional qualification examinations, there has also been new progress in implementing the “31 Measures.” First, on May 31, the China Securities Association, the China Futures Association, and the Asset Management Association of China each issued specific measures for the 29th article of the “31 Measures,” stating clearly that “Taiwan compatriots who have obtained the corresponding qualifications in Taiwan need only pass the mainland's laws and regulations examination when applying for securities, futures, or fund practice qualifications on the mainland, and do not need to take the professional knowledge examination,” and set out detailed provisions on how Taiwan compatriots may obtain practice qualifications, application conditions, and application procedures. Going forward, Taiwan compatriots who meet the conditions may, in accordance with the specific requirements and procedures published by the three associations, take the relevant examinations and apply for practice or professional qualifications respectively. Second, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs is organizing the revision of regulations and rules on the management of fishing crew, and will publish before the end of June the specific method by which Taiwan compatriots may register for the fishing crew professional qualification examination. Starting January 1 next year, Taiwan compatriots may use the 《Taiwan Residents' Travel Permit to Mainland China》 to apply for fishing crew certificate-related services. Third, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism recently issued the 《Notice on Organizing the Implementation of the 2018 National Tour Guide Qualification Examination》, and the 2018 National Tour Guide Qualification Examination will be held between November and December this year. Taiwan compatriots may register for the examination in any province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the central government on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965183.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The 10th Straits Forum recently concluded in Fujian. Please ask the spokesperson to evaluate the role the Straits Forum has played over the past ten years. In addition, please introduce the outcomes achieved at the 10th Straits Forum.","The Straits Forum has now been held for ten years since its founding. Over these ten years, adhering to the concept of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family” and to its positioning of being “civil, grassroots and broadly based,” this platform has fully played its active role in expanding and deepening civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, jointly promoting Chinese culture, boosting the integrated economic and social development of both sides, and promoting spiritual affinity. It has become an important platform for uniting compatriots on both sides in the shared public opinion of maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe 10th Straits Forum closed on June 11, with more than 8,000 people from all walks of life in Taiwan attending this grand event. Under the current cross-Strait situation, the successful holding of the Straits Forum, the largest civil exchange activity across the Taiwan Strait, is of great significance and has produced a wide and positive impact. First, it further highlighted the direction of continuing to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, delivered an important speech at the forum’s main session, expounding the policies for maintaining and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations under the new situation. Representatives from all walks of life on both sides unanimously agreed that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path, and that compatriots on both sides should unswervingly continue along it and keep overcoming difficulties and moving forward. Second, it further gathered public opinion and encouraged and strengthened the confidence of compatriots on both sides to expand and deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family” became the most frequently used phrase during the forum. Despite interference and obstruction from some people on the island, the enthusiasm of Taiwan's people to participate in this forum remained high, and Taiwan youth signed up more actively than before. For the first time, this forum opened online registration to Taiwan's people, and the 300 slots for “first-time attendees” were snapped up instantly. Third, the various activities of the forum and the positive energy it conveyed for promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and enhancing the fraternal bond and well-being of compatriots have drawn great attention. A total of 142 media outlets and 785 journalists from both sides covered this event, of which 55 Taiwanese media outlets and 86 journalists participated in forum coverage, issuing more than 1,000 articles (items and pieces). The live stream of the “Ten-Year Story Collection” exceeded 10 million clicks, and the total readership of related topics on Sina Weibo reached nearly 15 million. Fourth, this forum once again became an important platform for releasing policies and seeing them take effect. During the forum, Fujian Province released 66 policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, and Xiamen City held a talent matching meeting at this forum, offering 2,653 employment and entrepreneurship internship positions to talent and youth from various fields in Taiwan. These drew wide attention and positive reviews. Fifth, this forum produced a batch of new achievements in advancing civil exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait. During the forum, civil sectors, fields and industries on both sides, including science and technology, talent, public welfare, communities, finance, health care, and farmland water conservancy, signed more than 80 cooperation projects (agreements). Nearly 100 pairs of community associations, townships, villages, neighborhoods and communities across both sides reached consensus on exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965180.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","U.S. Assistant Secretary of State for Educational and Cultural Affairs Royce recently visited Taiwan to attend the completion ceremony of the new building of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has lodged stern representations with the US side. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and contacts between the United States and Taiwan. The US side should earnestly abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, so as not to harm China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. The DPP authorities relying on foreign powers to bolster themselves will only further undermine cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965173.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Reports say the DPP authorities are supporting “Taiwan independence” groups in co-signing and launching several referendum proposals targeting the five-star red flag and Taiwan’s participation in international organizations. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment?","Recently, the International Olympic Committee has issued a stern warning regarding Taiwan's push for a so-called “Olympic name-correction referendum.” The DPP authorities have not repented; they continue to incite populism, manipulate referendums, and deliberately provoke the one-China principle, recklessly undermining the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations. Such playing with fire will surely backfire and further harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965175.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","大文传媒集团全媒体记者","Recently, a think tank in Taiwan's pro-green camp proposed that the Taiwan authorities could lease Taiping Island in the Nansha Islands to the U.S. military under the name of “humanitarian rescue.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","This proposal is very dangerous. Any words or deeds that harm the interests of the Chinese nation will be condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently reiterated that the relevant measures to strictly review mainland groups and individuals visiting Taiwan are only aimed at officials at all levels on the mainland, and that Taiwan still welcomes ordinary mainland tourists. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We have repeatedly expressed our firm opposition to the DPP authorities' restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges. We believe that strengthening exchanges and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities keep fabricating all kinds of excuses to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, worsening the atmosphere of cross-Strait exchanges. Ultimately, it is the well-being of Taiwan compatriots that suffers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","It is reported that the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Association recently went to Taiwan to hold the 2nd Talent Recruitment Fair and achieved considerable results. Please introduce the relevant information.","It is understood that on June 2, the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Association held the second Talent Recruitment Expo in Taipei, striving to provide more positions, more opportunities and better services for Taiwan youth seeking employment in Shanghai, while building a stage for Taiwan youth to showcase their strengths and charm and realize their dreams. For this recruitment expo, the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Association organized 125 well-known Taiwan-invested enterprises in Shanghai to exhibit in Taiwan, offering nearly 2,000 job vacancies across multiple industries including education and training, financial investment, and chain services. Compared with the recruitment event first held last year, this added more than 1,000 positions. At the recruitment fair site, a “one-stop” recruitment method combining “traditional job fairs + the internet” was used for the first time, providing online and offline services for Taiwan youth attending interviews.\nAccording to statistics, the recruitment fair had 15,860 visits by job seekers throughout the day, a 50% increase over last year, and 6,200 résumés were received. 286 Taiwan youth reached employment intentions with recruiting companies on site, and some other applicants will take part in follow-up interviews with the companies. That is the basic situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Yesterday the US-North Korea leaders' summit reached a consensus in which the DPRK committed to strive for the complete denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula, which is tantamount to removing the fuse of the North Korean nuclear crisis. At the same time, however, cross-Strait relations continue to be tense. May I ask the spokesperson whether the mainland is worried that the Taiwan Strait issue will become the…","I listened carefully to your question, and I am curious about the logic behind connecting these two matters. If you are referring to the recent reports in Taiwan media that so-called “national security” figures in Taiwan and scholars in the Green camp have claimed that, after the situation on the Korean Peninsula stabilizes, the United States will further interfere in the Taiwan Strait to support the DPP authorities, then I can tell them that this is a wishful misjudgment of the international situation, and also a deliberate misleading of the Taiwan public. As everyone knows, “Taiwan independence” forces are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and a grave harm to the interests of Taiwan compatriots and the overall interests of the Chinese nation. We have the firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and never allow the historical tragedy of national division to repeat itself. No one should underestimate our resolve and strength.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","In the current East Asian situation, a glimmer of peace has appeared on the Korean Peninsula, while the situation in the Taiwan Strait is gradually heating up. Does the mainland hope that the next meeting between the leaders across the Strait could clear the clouds and reveal the sun?","Everyone has noticed that yesterday the Ministry of Foreign Affairs already stated the Chinese government’s position and attitude regarding the Korean Peninsula-US summit talks. The Taiwan issue is entirely China’s internal affair, and its nature is completely different from that of the Korea-US relationship. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations. On November 7, 2015, the leaders of both sides, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” held a historic meeting, demonstrating that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have the ability and wisdom to resolve their own problems. However, after the DPP authorities took office, they refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and caused serious regression in cross-Strait relations. Whether the clouds can part and the sun shine on cross-Strait relations depends critically on the DPP authorities’ attitude toward the common political foundation across the Strait. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” as early as possible and recognizing that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965172.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","At the recent Straits Forum, KMT Vice Chairman Hao Longbin proposed the new “Three Links” of future cross-Strait study, marriage and employment. What is the spokesperson's response to this?","As everyone knows, with the close exchanges across the Strait, marriages between compatriots on both sides are increasingly common. In recent years the mainland has actively introduced relevant policies to provide convenience and equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to study and work. The mainland side has already taken the lead. If the so-called “new three links” in the true sense, both two-way and comprehensive, are to be realized, I believe the Taiwan authorities need to make efforts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","Reports say Tsai Ing-wen may visit Paraguay in August, transiting through the United States, and some members of the U.S. Congress have proposed inviting Tsai Ing-wen to deliver a speech to Congress. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on this?","We have consistently adhered to the one-China principle in handling Taiwan’s external contacts. We firmly oppose any act that attempts to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” internationally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, New Party youth members Wang Bingzhong, Hou Hanting and Lin Mingzheng applied to travel to the mainland to attend the 10th Straits Forum, but were obstructed by Taiwan's authorities. What is your comment?","Everyone knows that for some time, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have stopped at nothing in suppressing people who advocate cross-Strait unification. Just now we saw news that the DPP authorities are trying to prosecute them under the so-called “crime of endangering security.” I think such a monstrous act will certainly be unanimously opposed and condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Of course, it cannot stop the common public will of people from all walks of life on both sides to exchange and cooperate, nor the historical trend of the continuous development of cross-Strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","US Secretary of Defense Mattis publicly stated on June 2 that the US Department of Defense will continue to cooperate with Taiwan and provide necessary arms and defense services to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","This is an old question, and both the Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have already responded. I reiterate that we firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and Taiwan. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, so as not to damage China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Recently, Taiwan's fruit has had a bumper harvest but sales have been poor, causing prices to plummet. In particular, bananas are in surplus, and many banana farmers are watching helplessly as the fruits of their labor rot in the fields. Some public opinion on the island holds that improving cross-strait relations is the fundamental solution. What is the spokesperson's comment on this phenomenon?","Everyone knows that from 2008 to 2016, the two sides, on the basis of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” jointly worked for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, including smooth procurement cooperation for Taiwan agricultural products by the mainland, from which compatriots on both sides, especially those in Taiwan, benefited. But after the DPP came to power, it refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” condoned and indulged “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence” activities, restricted cross-Strait exchanges, and arbitrarily weakened the various links between compatriots on both sides of the Strait that had been so hard to establish. As a result, all aspects of the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations have been damaged, which inevitably harms the interests of Taiwan compatriots. “Scooping hot water to stop it boiling is not as effective as removing the firewood.” If the DPP authorities took a clear position on acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” as a matter of principle, many problems in cross-Strait exchanges would be readily resolved. That cross-Strait relations being good means Taiwan compatriots will be well off is a simple and plain truth.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965171.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Faced with Taiwan's economic predicament, former Taiwan leader Ma Ying-jeou recently suggested at an event that the Tsai Ing-wen authorities restart the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement to help Taiwan join regional economic integration. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Facts have proven that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct direction. On the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” both sides jointly advance matters, including cross-Strait economic cooperation, through consultation and negotiation, which is a path of mutual benefit and win-win outcomes. Of course, cross-Strait consultations are currently stalled and signed agreements are difficult to bring into effect; the responsibility lies with the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","We have noted that recently, in southern Taiwan, which is known as the \"iron ballot box\" of the Democratic Progressive Party, some original supporters of the Democratic Progressive Party have hung banners reading \"If the DPP does not fall, Taiwan will not prosper,\" expressing the dissatisfaction of the Taiwanese people with the current cross-Strait policy of the Taiwan authorities. May I ask for the…","As I said just now, when cross-strait relations are good, Taiwan compatriots will be well off, and they can obtain more benefits and well-being. I think it is entirely understandable that when their interests and well-being are harmed, they express their inner anger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The 10th Straits Forum: the Xiamen matchmaking meeting on employment, entrepreneurship, and internship and practice opportunities for Taiwan talent was held in Xiamen on the 9th, attracting more than 300 Taiwan professionals and students to attend. This matchmaking meeting, for the first time, introduced a supporting summer internship plan for Taiwan students, meeting the multi-channel training needs of Taiwan…","Thank you for raising this topic. I will also briefly introduce the relevant situation of this year's summer internships for Taiwan students.\nThis year we continued to implement the \"Third Taiwan Youth Summer Internship Program.\" After coordination with relevant departments, localities and enterprises, about 600 summer internship places were provided for Taiwan youth. This internship activity has three characteristics in terms of job distribution. First, the job locations are fairly widely distributed, with positions available in first- and second-tier cities from the Northeast to South China. Second, there are many industry categories, with positions covering several popular industries such as finance and internet, as well as Taiwan's advantageous industries such as design and cultural creativity. Third, the types of enterprises are comprehensive, including headquarters of large state-owned enterprises, startups, and small and medium-sized private enterprises, all of which have posted positions.\nOn May 14, Taiwan students began logging into the \"Youth Community\" platform of China Taiwan Network to submit resumes. As of June 5, a total of 550 Taiwan students had submitted resumes. Among these 550 Taiwan students, more than 340 are studying at universities in Taiwan. At present, enterprises are conducting resume screening and interviews. This is only a small part. In addition, our relevant departments, localities and enterprises have also each launched summer internship programs targeting Taiwan youth. It is expected that this year's internships by Taiwan students in the Mainland will once again be a lively scene.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180613_11965179.htm"],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Recently, a researcher at a US think tank claimed that if the US sends warships through the Taiwan Strait, it can remind China and the whole world that the Taiwan Strait is international waters. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-U.S. relations. The U.S. side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, so as not to damage China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We understand that, out of fear of a so-called “wave of diplomatic severances,” the Taiwan authorities have recently been in frequent contact with so-called “allies,” but often receive requests from them for help with economic development. What views does the spokesperson have on this?","This shows two points. First, the One China principle is the trend of the times and the will of the people. Second, it is the DPP authorities who are engaging in “dollar diplomacy.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Because cross-Strait relations have cooled, enthusiasm among mainland tourists for traveling to Taiwan has sharply declined. Relevant Taiwan authorities recently launched a series of preferential measures for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, but still failed to raise the appeal of Taiwan for mainland tourists. May I ask the spokesperson for an evaluation?","We have said many times that mainland residents' travel to Taiwan once had a positive and healthy momentum of development. The reasons for the sharp decline in the scale and number of mainland visitors to Taiwan today are well known. Therefore, the one who tied the bell must untie it. As we have said, when cross-strait relations are good, Taiwan compatriots will do well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180613_11965156.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-06-19","Geng Shuang","","Firstly, is Chairman Kim Jong Un's visit directly related to the DPRK-US summit in Singapore? Will he meet with President Xi Jinping and inform President Xi of the DPRK-US summit? What is the purpose of his visit? Secondly, two Japanese airlines changed \"Taiwan\" to \"Taiwan, China'' on their official websites. In response, the Taiwanese authorities lodged stern protests to the two companies through the \"Taipei…","Please keep closely following Chairman Kim Jong Un's visit to China. The Chinese side will release relevant information in a timely manner and we will get a clearer picture by then.\nWith regard to your second question, we have made clear our position many times. There is only one China in the world and Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan have always been parts of China. This is an objective fact, a common sense as well as the general consensus of the international community.\nThe foreign enterprises operating in China should respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by China's laws and respect the national feelings of the Chinese people. This is the basic requirement for any foreign company doing business in China.\nI urge the Taiwanese authorities to refrain from attempting to kick against the pricks and hold back the trend of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1569968.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1569911.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-26","Lu Kang","","In a recent interview with AFP, leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen said that the mainland was putting \"immense pressure\" on Taiwan and called on the international community to constrain China, saying that we need to work together to reaffirm our values on democracy and freedom in order to constrain China and also minimize \"the expansion of hegemonic influence\". I wonder if you have any reaction to that?","As we said on many occasions, Taiwan is part of China. What was said by certain person in Taiwan falls within China's internal affairs, and we won't give specific reaction to that here at the Foreign Ministry. I would like to refer you to the competent department of the Chinese government that is in charge of the Taiwan affairs.\nI shall point out in principle that we hope certain people in Taiwan could correctly understand the development trend of China and its national unity as well as the evolvement of international circumstance and stop moving further down the wrong path. It won't work even if they try to bank on foreign forces to build themselves up.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1572054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1572000.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends. The press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","We know that since the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” were introduced, localities and departments have actively promoted them and achieved some results. Could the spokesperson please introduce the latest progress on the “31 Measures”?","Since the “31 Measures to Benefit Taiwan Compatriots” were issued and put into effect, all regions and departments have been pushing implementation with great urgency, and many provinces and cities have issued local implementation rules tailored to their conditions, including Shanghai's “55 Measures,” Fujian Province's “66 Measures,” and Xiamen's “60 Measures,” among others. Many of these measures have already produced real results. Here, I would like to introduce several new developments.\nFirst, provinces and cities continue to roll out upgraded measures. On June 19, Ningbo City issued and put into effect the “Several Measures on Further Deepening Economic, Social and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Ningbo and Taiwan,” comprising 80 specific measures covering support for Taiwan compatriots' investment, promotion of trade with Taiwan and social and cultural exchanges and cooperation, facilitation of study, internships, employment, entrepreneurship, residence, and daily life for Taiwan compatriots locally, among other areas. In supporting Taiwan compatriots' investment and actively promoting trade with Taiwan, it is made clear that Taiwan-funded enterprises can fully enjoy all kinds of industrial support policies in Ningbo; Taiwan-funded enterprises are encouraged to list on the mainland's main board, SME board, and ChiNext, and to be listed on the New Third Board and the Ningbo Equity Exchange Center; and facilitation measures such as “one-stop inspection and quarantine” and “green channels” are provided at the Ningbo port. In financial services, it is made clear that Taiwan-funded enterprises are allowed to raise funds from overseas through loans, bond issuance, and other forms, and Taiwan-funded enterprises established in the Ningbo export processing zone may be granted general VAT taxpayer status. In employment and entrepreneurship, Taiwan talent coming to Ningbo for employment and entrepreneurship enjoy the same treatment under local talent recruitment, training, and service guarantee policies; qualified law firms from Taiwan may set up representative offices in Ningbo; and Ningbo will provide no fewer than 1,000 jobs for Taiwan compatriots each year. In living conditions, school-age children and adolescents from Taiwan receive compulsory education on the same terms as citizens; Taiwan compatriots and their families in Ningbo enjoy the same medical treatment as Ningbo residents; and public cultural venues at all levels are open to Taiwan compatriots free of charge, among others.\nIn addition, some provinces and cities are, in light of the actual needs of local Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan compatriots, working urgently to formulate specific local implementation guidelines for the “31 Measures,” and these are expected to be released one after another in the near future.\nSecond, we support Taiwan groups and individuals in participating in cultural and artistic activities that the mainland holds overseas. From May to June, the China Cultural Relations Association held the “China Cultural and Creative Products Exhibition Week” at the Chinese Cultural Centre in Madrid and the Chinese Cultural Centre in Malta, with cultural and creative institutions and artists from both sides of the Strait jointly exhibiting and showcasing the innovative achievements of cross-Strait cultural and creative industries. This is a positive step in promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly promote Chinese culture overseas.\nThird, we further implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots. On June 14, the China Television Artists Association announced that, in accordance with the relevant content of the “31 Measures,” the 29th China Television Golden Eagle Award this year will include Taiwan actors in the selection of the Favorite Male and Female Actor awards, giving them the same eligibility to compete as mainland actors. On June 21, the National Office for Philosophy and Social Sciences announced the results of the 2018 National Social Science Fund annual and youth projects. Taiwan researchers working on the mainland who met the application requirements applied for 157 projects, of which 58 were approved after review; these projects are concentrated in history, sociology, ethnic affairs, journalism, and linguistics, among other fields.\nFourth, we provide more job and employment opportunities for Taiwan compatriots. On June 15, the Fujian Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, the Department of Education, and the China Overseas Talent Market jointly held a Fujian Province special matching event for Taiwan teachers. 65 universities in Fujian released demand for 536 positions for recruiting Taiwan teachers; 337 Taiwan PhD holders were interviewed on site, and 260 résumés were received. Of these, 68 Taiwan PhD holders were invited to assessment interviews, 47 passed the interviews, and they will sign onboarding agreements with the relevant universities in the near future.\nGoing forward, our steps to promote exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait will not stop, and our sincere goodwill toward seeking well-being for compatriots on both sides will not change. Next, some regions and fields will make new progress in trying out equal treatment first, new breakthroughs will be made in promoting joint development of cross-Strait industries, and Taiwan compatriots will have greater opportunities and broader horizons for development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969492.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","What important cross-strait exchange activities are planned for the next stage, including during the summer vacation?","Every summer is the peak season for civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, and this year the activity is even more intense. To further expand and deepen economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, and to enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, all sectors on both sides will launch a series of rich and colorful exchange activities with many highlights.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, localities will, based on their actual conditions, successively hold a series of economic exchange activities related to Taiwan. In July, Tianjin will hold the 11th Tianjin-Taiwan Conference, Guizhou Province will hold the 6th Guizhou-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cooperation Symposium, and Hubei Province will hold the 15th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week.\nIn cultural exchanges, first, Zhejiang, Shaanxi, Guangdong and other places will hold branded activities such as “Connected to Qiantang: Cross-Strait Cultural Friendship Tour” and “Taiwan History Teachers’ Chinese Culture Study Camp.” Second, Yunnan, Hunan, Beijing, Shanghai, Guizhou and other places will hold cultural activities such as “Cross-Strait University Students’ Photography Journey along the Ancient Tea Horse Road,” “Cross-Strait Youth Literature Camp,” “Cross-Strait Youth Chinese Folk Music Exchange Performance,” “Connected by Youth — Cross-Strait Youth Journey Through China,” and “Qian-Taiwan Intangible Cultural Heritage Traditional Craft Workshop,” promoting the joint inheritance of Chinese culture by compatriots on both sides.\nIn youth exchanges, apart from the summer internship activities for Taiwan youth organized by the Taiwan Affairs Office, which were already introduced at the previous press conference, 20 mainland financial institutions have provided 800 summer internship positions for Taiwan students, and all places have now been filled. The “2018 Thousand Taiwan Compatriot Youth Summer Camp,” sponsored by the All-China Taiwan Compatriots Federation, will be held in early July, with more than 1,000 Taiwan youth going to over 20 provinces and municipalities to take part. The “Beijing Summit on Cross-Strait Youth Exchange and Cooperation” will be held in Beijing in July, including a forum on the theme of cross-Strait youth exchange and cooperation, a cross-Strait college students’ vocational skills competition, and other activities, and about 1,600 young people from both sides are expected to attend. The “13th Cross-Strait Youth Festival and 6th Strait Youth Festival” will be held in Fuzhou, Fujian Province, in early to mid-August, with more than 30 sub-events planned, involving nearly 2,000 young people from both sides, including 1,000 Taiwan youth.\nIn sports exchanges, last year the first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League and the first Cross-Strait Wushu Exchange Conference were successfully held, drawing wide attention and welcome from compatriots on both sides. This year we will continue to organize large-scale youth sports exchange activities across the Strait, such as baseball and wushu.\nIn addition, a batch of cross-Strait exchange activities in diverse forms and lively styles will be successively held in news, education, science and technology, communities, ethnic minority affairs and many other fields. This fully demonstrates that the public desire on both sides for exchange and cooperation cannot be stopped by anyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969491.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to reports, Tsai Ing-wen recently said that Taiwan faces pressure from the mainland to change Taiwan's way of life and to compress Taiwan's international space, and hopes the international community will constrain the mainland. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The remarks of the leader of the Taiwan authorities confuse the public and have no factual basis. Their purpose is to create hostility between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to rely on outside forces to bolster their own standing, and to further escalate cross-Strait confrontation. Such schemes will not succeed. The blood ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait cannot be driven apart, and attempts to contain the Chinese nation's march toward great rejuvenation are even more an overestimation of one's own capabilities.\nIt is well known that it is the DPP authorities who have undermined the hard-won good situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, which compatriots on both sides worked together to achieve. Our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent: we unwaveringly adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” and we are firm and unambiguous in opposing and containing “Taiwan independence.” Upholding the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we respect Taiwan's existing social system and the way of life of Taiwan compatriots, and we take the lead in sharing the mainland's development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots. The series of policy measures we have introduced, which provide Taiwan compatriots with equal treatment in studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland, have enhanced the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and provided Taiwan compatriots with more and better opportunities and platforms to realize their life aspirations. Today, the strong attention that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots pay to the mainland's development and progress, and their welcome of the “31 Measures,” stand in sharp contrast to how deep their concern is about the DPP's cross-Strait policy, how great their disappointment is with the DPP's governance, and how high their dissatisfaction is with the island's economic and livelihood conditions. What the reasons are, everyone can think carefully about.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969488.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","It has been reported that Chen Chu recently stated publicly that Tsai Ing-wen insists on the “1992 No Consensus.” How does the spokesperson comment on this?","In November 1992, after the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) reached the “1992 Consensus,” which no one can deny under any pretext. The “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-strait relations and is the key to ensuring the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. At this time, the leader of the Taiwan authorities once again disregarded facts and loudly denied the “1992 Consensus.” Compatriots on both sides must remain highly vigilant about what political purpose lies behind this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969471.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","It is reported that several cross-Strait exchange bases have recently been newly established. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","Since 2009, our office has approved the establishment of 60 Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 21 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian. Recently, we have also approved the establishment of six new Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Bases. They are: Youli City in Anyang, Henan Province; the hometown of Zheng Chenggong in Nan'an, Fujian Province; the Straits Youth Exchange Camp in Fuzhou, Fujian Province; the Chiyou Jiuli City in Chongqing Municipality; the Songshan Anti-Japanese War Site in Longling County, Baoshan, Yunnan Province; and the Genghis Khan Mausoleum in Ordos, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region. The establishment of these exchange bases, which comprehensively considers local cultural resource characteristics and the state of cross-Strait exchanges, has provided a platform for compatriots on both sides to look back on history, savor culture, share close family feelings, and pursue common development opportunities, and it fully demonstrates the shared kinship and common roots of compatriots on both sides. Currently, there are 66 Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Bases, and we sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots and people from all walks of life to visit these exchange bases for sightseeing, exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969468.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The “New Power Party” recently held a press conference saying that the Taiwan legislature should amend the “Referendum Act” to add content such as territorial change to the referendum options. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have stressed many times that we firmly oppose any force, in any way, including through so-called “legislation and amendments,” carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities or opening a convenient door for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. “Taiwan independence” is a dead-end path that harms the interests of Taiwan compatriots. We warn the “Taiwan independence” forces not to play with fire and burn themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The PLA Navy recently organized a ship formation to conduct cross-zone training around Taiwan. Is this a further warning from the mainland against “Taiwan independence” separatist activities on the island?","Regarding these training activities by the PLA Navy, the military has already expressed our position and attitude. I would like to reiterate that we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and action, to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and we will absolutely not tolerate “Taiwan independence” forces undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait or interfering with the process of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201806/t20180627_11969470.htm"],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","June 26 is International Day Against Drug Abuse. It is reported that public security organs recently cracked a series of drug cases involving Taiwan. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","Recently, public security authorities cracked several major cross-Strait drug crime cases, destroying multiple drug crime gangs made up mainly of Taiwanese criminals that harmed compatriots on both sides. Fujian police successively destroyed three cross-Strait drug smuggling gangs, arrested 11 Taiwanese criminal suspects, and seized various types of drugs and a large amount of drug money, effectively striking at the arrogance of Taiwan-related drug crime and safeguarding the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Wang Ping-chung and other members of the New Party's youth wing were indicted by Taiwan's authorities on the so-called charge of “obstructing national security,” and the “indictment” also involves relevant mainland departments. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","This so-called “indictment” is full of absurd claims. The relevant allegations are entirely fabricated and have ulterior motives, which fully exposes the political nature of the DPP authorities: they tolerate and indulge “Taiwan independence” separatist acts while suppressing Taiwan people who advocate unification. Realizing national reunification is the fundamental interest of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and a historical inevitability for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The force for unification cannot be suppressed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Reports indicate that a reporter from Dongnan Satellite Television recently applied through the proper procedures to be stationed in Taiwan for reporting, but was rejected by the Taiwan authorities. Is the Taiwan Affairs Office aware of this situation? What is your comment?","It is understood that the application by reporters from Southeast TV for a resident reporting post in Taiwan was indeed unreasonably rejected by the DPP authorities, creating a bad precedent since the two sides began exchanging resident reporters.\nFor a long time, mainland reporters in Taiwan have played a bridging and linking role, through a large number of objective and fair reports, in increasing mutual understanding and warm kinship among compatriots on both sides, and especially in helping mainland residents better understand Taiwan. The legitimate rights and interests of mainland reporters should be protected, and their news-gathering work in Taiwan should be respected. For some time, the DPP authorities have used various means to restrict and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and they have now gone further by erecting obstacles to cross-Strait news exchanges. These practices do not win popular support and must be exposed and condemned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","It is reported that former KMT Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu will soon be invited to attend the first “Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum” in Hangzhou. Please confirm.","The first Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, co-hosted by the Taiwan Zhonghua Qingyan Peace Education Foundation and relevant mainland units, will be held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, on July 8. Hong Xiuzhu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang and Chairperson of the Zhonghua Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, will travel to Hangzhou to attend the forum-related activities and make a visit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Following up on Tsai Ing-wen's interview with AFP: she said “China is an expansionist hegemon” and called on the international community to stand up and constrain it, yet she still said she is willing to meet mainland leaders. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's response? Second question: The Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation was recently succeeded by Yao Jen-to, who is a core aide of Tsai…","First question: I have already stated our position on this just now. Everyone does not think her proposal for a meeting has much substance. I think compatriots and public opinion on both sides are skeptical.\nSecond question: regarding personnel changes within Taiwan's internal circles, we will not comment. Since this person is said to be “best at communication,” he should know what the passcode for communication between the two associations across the Strait is.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, Taiwan \"pro-independence\" groups plan to mobilize the public to hold a referendum on \"banning the display of the five-star red flag\" in Taiwan, and the DPP also seems poised to echo this. What is the TAO's view on this?","At our previous press conference, we already responded to this issue. We believe that manipulating such a referendum is, in essence, using the interests of the Taiwan people as a stake to challenge the one-China principle and create cross-Strait confrontation. This act of playing with fire will inevitably backfire on its perpetrators.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Taiwan’s Secretary-General of the National Security Council encouraged the public to refuse to fly on airlines that list Taiwan as part of China, and he believes such moves will not change the positioning of cross-Strait relations. What comment does the spokesperson have?","There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is a part of China’s sacred territory, and adhering to the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities are going against the tide, and even use the interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses as stakes in a gamble. This approach is futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","At the third Beijing-Taipei Scholars' Joint Research Conference held last weekend, in discussing the understanding of the “one country, two systems” Taiwan model, scholars present pointed out that matters including regime transformation, the handling of political symbols, Taiwan's international space, military issues and maritime jurisdiction will differ from Hong Kong. What comments does the spokesperson have?…","We will not comment on the various views that scholars raised at the seminar. What I want to say is that “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. The scientific concept of “one country, two systems” has been elaborated in detail by several generations of central leaders; it respects history and reality, and is the best way to fully accommodate the interests of all parties and achieve national reunification. In recent years, General Secretary Xi Jinping has further emphasized that “the concrete realization of ‘one country, two systems’ in Taiwan will fully consider Taiwan's actual conditions and fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and it is an arrangement that can fully take into account the interests of Taiwan compatriots,” which is “three fullys.” General Secretary Xi also further pointed out that “the national reunification we pursue is not merely unification in form; what is more important is the spiritual convergence of compatriots on both sides.” We have full confidence in this. We believe that in the process of advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and promoting peaceful reunification of the motherland, more and more Taiwan compatriots will recognize and accept “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Yesterday, the director of the Washington-based Center for Strategic and International Studies published an article stating that Taiwan, as an important partner of the US in the Pacific, will take part in US naval exercises being conducted in the Solomon Islands. How does the TAO respond?","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any form of military ties between our diplomatic partners and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","On the 22nd, the mainland's Ministry of Commerce issued an announcement deciding to impose anti-dumping duties on imports of styrene originating in Taiwan. Could the spokesperson provide further clarification on this?","It is understood that, based on applications submitted by mainland industry operators, on June 22 the Ministry of Commerce issued a notice ruling that styrene originating from South Korea, the United States, and the Taiwan region is being dumped, and decided to impose anti-dumping duties on these products. This ruling was made in accordance with relevant mainland laws and regulations and the relevant rules of the World Trade Organization. For specific details, please consult the Ministry of Commerce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","Tsai Ing-wen's recent interview with foreign media was the most hardline in her wording since taking office. Coupled with various signs across the Strait recently, does this mean that the cross-Strait situation will gradually escalate? Please comment.","Where cross-Strait relations go is up to the Taiwan authorities. We hope they will not misjudge the situation or miscalculate the trend, and will not keep going further down a wrong path that runs against the interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","We have noted that some Western media have repeatedly hyped the cyberattacks Taiwan has suffered from the mainland over the past two years. Taiwan's authorities have said Taiwan has become a training ground for mainland cyber forces. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","This kind of report has no factual basis and is not worth refuting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, this year’s summer tourism peak season on the island was far below previous years, the worst in thirty years. Some Taiwan media analyze that the sharp freeze in cross-Strait relations has led to a drop in the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We have said many times that when cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan compatriots will be well off. As I just said, what are the causes of the various grievances that the Taiwan public feels today in their social life in Taiwan? Everyone should think about this carefully. Therefore, we hope the DPP authorities will remove as early as possible the artificial obstacles set up in the development of cross-Strait relations and cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and truly consider the lives and interests of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The Guangzhou Intermediate People's Court recently sentenced to heavy prison terms 29 Taiwan-national fraud suspects who had been repatriated to the mainland. This is the second time the mainland side has sentenced Taiwan-national fraud suspects to heavy prison terms. What is the spokesperson's evaluation? The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council stated that if the criminal gang is to be dismantled, judicial…","We have repeatedly stressed that telecom fraud cases led by Taiwan criminals occur frequently, causing deep suffering to compatriots on both sides, and we deeply loathe them. We will absolutely not allow criminals to escape justice. We will apprehend cross-border telecom fraud criminals and bring them to justice in accordance with law. This conforms to public will, has won high affirmation and wide recognition from compatriots on both sides, and has received full understanding and strong support from the international community.\nI want to emphasize that the mainland's position on punishing telecom fraud crimes in accordance with law has remained consistent. Its attitude is firm and unwavering, and it will continue to take resolute measures to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","We know that U.S. Congressman Rohrabacher introduced a resolution last week calling on the United States and Taiwan to restore so-called “diplomatic relations” and to recognize Taiwan as a “sovereign and independent state.” The Taiwan authorities responded, “Thank you very much.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an objective reality with a solid legal basis, and it is a common understanding of the international community. But there are always some who overestimate themselves and attempt to challenge the one-China principle that the international community generally observes. Such discordant noises cannot stop the historical trend of the one-China principle being further deepened in the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-06-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The Taiwan Public Opinion Foundation recently released a poll showing that 49% of Taiwan adults hold a favorable view of the mainland, and for the first time those with favorable views have surpassed those with unfavorable views. Yu Ying-lung, chairman of the foundation, described this as a historic shift. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","We have noted this public opinion poll, and we have explained our position and attitude on the related issues on many occasions. We believe that, with the development and progress of the mainland and with our various cross-Strait policy measures taking root in people's hearts, more and more Taiwan compatriots will take part in the process of developing cross-Strait relations, contributing their efforts to steadily advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. This trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201806/t20180627_11969526.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-06-28","Lu Kang","","It is reported that China has rejected the request from the United States to discuss China's position on the listing of Taiwan on airline websites. Why was the request for meeting rejected?","The Civil Aviation Administration of China has made clear China's position on this issue. We have also repeated our position many times. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. It is a fact acknowledged by the international community, and it is also common sense. The one-China principle is a must-have foundation for any development of relations and cooperation between China and the rest of the world. Respecting China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and observing China's laws is a fundamental principle that foreign enterprises operating in China must follow. On this issue, China's position is clear-cut, firm and consistent.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1572644.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1572535.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-28","Lu Kang","","Can you confirm that there was a request from the US side to discuss the issue of listing Taiwan as part of China?","The US government and companies know very well the Chinese government's position on the Taiwan issue. Our position has never changed and remains consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1572644.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1572535.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-06-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","General Mattis, Secretary of Defense of the United States is visiting China from June 26 to 28. What are the consensuses reached between China and US during this visit? And what is your comment on his first visit as the Secretary of Defense of the United States?","At the invitation of General Wei Fenghe, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense of China, General Mattis paid an official visit to China from June 26 to 28. President Xi Jinping met with Mattis. General Wei Fenghe, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense of China, General Xu Qiliang, member of the Political Bureau of CPC Central Committee and Vice Chairman of Central Military Commission and Yang Jiechi, member of the Political Bureau of CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of Central Leading Group of Foreign Affairs also met with him.\nBoth sides had in-depth exchange of views on topics of mutual interest such as international and regional situation, bilateral relations between the countries and the two militaries, Korean peninsula issue, Taiwan, maritime security and other issues. Important consensuses were reached on strengthening exchanges between the two militaries at all levels, enhancing mutual trust, deepening practical cooperation and managing risks and challenges. The visit was fruitful and constructive.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-06/29/content_4818078.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-06-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","You have mentioned that during the US Secretary of Defense James Mattis’ visit to China, the two sides have talked on topics of Taiwan issue. Can you tell us what information has the Chinese side conveyed to the US side? A scholar of a think tank of the pan-Green groups within Taiwan has suggested renting a part of the Taiping Island to the US in the name of the humanitarian aid. What is your comment on…","About Secretary Mattis’ visit to China, the media have given full coverage yesterday. Needless to say, China and the US have different views on some issues. It must be pointed out, however, that the common interests of China and the US far outweigh their differences, and the opportunities for cooperation far outweigh the challenges. China is willing to work together with the US to expand common interests of both sides, properly handle contradictions and differences, manage and control risks and challenges, walk in the direction of mutual respect and win-win cooperation between the two militaries, and promote the mil-to-mil relations as an important stabilizer for the development of relations between the two countries.\nAs for the proposal you mentioned on the Taiping Island, I think it is very dangerous. Any words and deeds that harm the interests of the Chinese nation will be firmly opposed by all Chinese of both sides of the Taiwan Straits. The Chinese PLA will resolutely safeguard China's sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.\nOn the high-tech issue, China has always adhered to the principles of independence, self-reliance and independent innovation in developing its weapons and equipment, and has mainly relied on its own efforts to conduct research and production. We have the wisdom and ability to research and develop the weapons and equipment needed to maintain national security, as the past history has proved. It is and will be the same at present and in the future.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-06/29/content_4818078.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-06-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The senate of the United States has approved the 2018 National Defense Authorization Act in June, in which the US Armed Forces is encouraged to participate in some of Taiwan’s military exercises. It also suggests that the US Secretary of Defense James Mattis to suspend the invitation for China to participate in the RIMPAC Exercise until it can proved that China has stopped the construction of the islands in the…","Taiwan is a part of China. We are firmly opposed to any form of official exchanges and military contacts between any country and Taiwan. This position is clear and definite. What needs to be stressed is that there is no way out to bank on foreign forces to build themselves up, and it is impossible to contain China with Taiwan. We urge the US side to deal with the Taiwan-related issues cautiously or it might shoot itself in the foot. As for the participation of the Pacific Rim Exercise, we have already shown the Chinese military’s stance on this issue, so I will not repeat here.\nAnd for your second question, China is concerned about the Malabar 2018 naval exercise held by the US, Japan and India. China believes that the military cooperation of relevant countries should be conducive to regional peace and stability and not target at any third country.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-06/29/content_4818078.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-06-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's United Daily News reported that last week, the guided-missile destroyer Jinan and frigate Huanggang of the Chinese PLA Navy sailed southward through the eastern waters of Taiwan, headed west from the Bashi Channel and lingered in the southwestern waters of Taiwan. Taiwan media said it was the first time that the PLA had sent a type 052C destroyer, known as the “Chinese Aegis”, to carry out such a…","I have three points to make concerning this issue.\nFirst, Taiwan is a part of China. To safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is a sacred mission of the PLA.\nSecond, necessary actions taken by us are aiming at the secessionist forces within Taiwan, in order to prevent the welfare of the Taiwan people from being harmed by the “Taiwan independence” plot.\nThird, we will organize and carry out relevant training and actions according to the development and change of situation across the Taiwan straits.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-06/29/content_4818078.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-06-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports by Taiwan media, China’s HQ-9 missile system appeared again on the Yongxing Island days ago. The Foreign Ministry of Vietnam made a response on June 15, asking China to withdraw the illegal military deployment on the island. What is your comment on this issue?","The Xisha Islands is Chinese territory, and it is fully just and reasonable to deploy necessary defense facilities on the Islands.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-06/29/content_4818078.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2018-06-29","Lu Kang","","According to reports, the US officials revealed that the Department of State has applied to dispatch the Marine Corps to defend the new building of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT). If the application was approved, it would be the first time for the Marine Corps to be sent to Taiwan for relevant missions. Because the Marine Corps are usually dispatched to the countries that have established diplomatic ties…","We have responded to relevant questions. The one-China principle is the political foundation for China-US relations. The US should honor its commitment to the one-China principle and refrain from any official ties or military exchanges with Taiwan. The US side is quite clear about China's position in this regard and knows that it should speak and act cautiously when it comes to this matter lest it should impact the overall picture of China-US ties.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1572946.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1572824.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-06-29","Lu Kang","","The US Embassy in China on June 28 released a statement, saying that China has rebuffed the US' request to discuss the demand that American airlines should change the listing of \"Taiwan\" into \"Taiwan, China\". What's your comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. This is an objective fact and common sense, something universally recognized by the international community. The relevant notice issued by the Civil Aviation Administration of China demonstrates the Chinese government's consistent and firm position on the issue of the one China principle, and the relevant demand is completely legitimate and lawful.\nForeign enterprises are welcome to invest and operate in China. In the meantime, they should respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by Chinese laws and respect the national feelings of the Chinese people.\nI shall stress again that the one China principle is the political foundation for China-US relations, something not negotiable. The US government should have urged the relevant enterprises to observe the one China principle and rectify the relevant websites as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1572946.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1572824.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-04","Lu Kang","","A US chip company Micron accused a Chinese state-backed company on the mainland as well as a company from Taiwan of stealing technology. The Fuzhou Intermediate People's Court yesterday banned Micron from selling some of its chip products. Does the timing of this court ruling of temporarily barring Micron sales have anything to do with the current China-US trade tensions?","According to my understanding, this is an individual commercial case on the intellectual property rights protection. As to the specifics, I may refer you to the competent authority.\nI would like to emphasize two points here. Firstly, China is a country under the rule of law and we act in strict accordance with the law. We provide equal protection for all enterprises, be they Chinese or foreign ones, state-owned or private. Secondly, China is always committed to creating a law-based and enabling business environment for Chinese and foreign companies alike.\nAs to whether this has anything to do with China-US trade frictions, I do not think there is any necessary link between them.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1573983.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1573904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-05","Lu Kang","","India's flag carrier airline Air India has decided to change the reference of \"Taiwan\" into \"Chinese Taipei\" on its website. Two months ago China's civil aviation authority sent a formal communication to several airlines, including the Indian one. What is your comment on this? Did the Chinese Foreign Ministry also raise the matter with India?","The Chinese government's position on this issue cannot be more clear-cut, and India and other countries around the world are quite clear about it. By taking the relevant step, Air India shows respect for the objective fact that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China, which is also the common sense and international consensus.\nI want to stress once again that it is the basic requirement for any foreign enterprise operating in China to respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by China's laws and respect the national feelings of the Chinese people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1574293.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1574188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-07-06","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 6 dispatch: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan said on July 6 that Lien Chan, former chairman of the Kuomintang and chairman of the Cross-Strait Peace and Development Foundation, will lead a delegation of Taiwan public figures to visit Beijing from July 12 to 14. After that, Lien Chan and his delegation will also visit Liaoning, Jilin, and Zhejiang.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201807/t20180706_11972296.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-07-09","Hua Chunying","","Firstly, last week the DPRK and the US held the high-level meeting in Pyongyang. After US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo left Pyongyang, the DPRK state media issued hard-line comments, criticizing the attitude and position of the US side. Quite a few US political figures believe that the change in the DPRK's position has something to do with China. US Senator Lindsey Graham said there is no doubt that it is China…","With regard to your first question, we have also noted that after Secretary of State Mike Pompeo's visit to the DPRK, there seems to be some differences between the statements made by the two sides. The Chinese side has been stressing that we hope that the DPRK and the US can strengthen dialogue and consultation, follow through on the consensus and outcomes of the summit in Singapore and move forward the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula and political settlement process of the Korean Peninsula issue in the right direction and strive to achieve steady progress in this aspect. Just now you said that some people in the US associated the inconsistency of the statements made by the DPRK and the US after their high-level meeting with China's role in the Korean Peninsula issue. I believe that it does not make any sense. China's attitude on this issue is consistent and clear-cut. We will continue to play a positive role in and make constructive contributions to realizing the denuclearization of the Peninsula and achieving the long-lasting peace and stability of the region.\nRegarding your second question, China has closely followed and knows fully well the whole process of the US warships' sailing through the Taiwan Strait. We have expressed our concerns to the US side on this. It must be pointed out that the Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and it is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués and prudently and properly handle the Taiwan-related issues, lest it should undermine China-US ties and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1575371.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1575317.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-09","Hua Chunying","","Firstly, regarding the rescue operation in Thailand, does China have any specific request in terms of expanding the research? Are you asking a timetable to try to find all the missing people? Secondly, as to the Taiwan Straits mission by the US Navy, does China see any relation between this action and the current tension over trade tariffs?","Regarding your first question, just now I have briefed you on the relevant information. A joint working group comprised of China's Foreign Ministry, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism and the Ministry of Transport has been staying in close communication with the Thai side. We have asked the Thai side to expand their searching area under the sea and mobilize all resources to increase search frequency. The Thai side made it clear that their search efforts will not cease until every missing Chinese tourist is found.\nWith regard to your second question, I have made clear China's position just now. I can give you a principled response. The sound and steady development of China-US relations, the proper handling of differences in the spirit of mutual respect and the expansion of cooperation under the principle of mutual benefit serve the common interests of our two countries and represent the shared aspirations of the international community. We hope that the US side can respect China's core interests and major concerns and meet the Chinese side halfway.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1575371.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1575317.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-07-16","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, July 16 (reporters Zhao Bo and Shi Longhong) — An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 16th that since the “31 Measures” (the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation”) were issued and implemented, all regions and departments have been stepping up efforts to push implementation, and recently relevant provinces and cities have successively issued specific implementation measures tailored to local conditions.\nAn Fengshan said that on July 3, Tianjin issued and implemented the “Several Measures on Further Deepening Economic, Social and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Tianjin and Taiwan,” covering a total of 52 specific measures in cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, social and cultural exchange and cooperation, Taiwan compatriots studying, interning, working, and starting businesses in Tianjin, and daily life in Tianjin. Among them, it specifies that Taiwan-funded enterprises may obtain industrial land through long-term leasing, a combination of leasing and transfer, leasing followed by transfer, and flexible-term transfer; Taiwan-funded enterprises may invest in the elderly care services sector, and elderly care institutions’ electricity, water, gas and heating are priced at residential living rates, with equal tax and other preferential policies; enterprises founded by Taiwan compatriots in Tianjin may apply to be designated as “Thousand Enterprises, Ten Thousand People” enterprises, and where a selected enterprise’s R&D platform is upgraded to the national level, it is granted a special fund of 500,000 to 1 million yuan; for Taiwanese university graduates founding enterprises in Tianjin, a one-year job subsidy and a three-year social insurance subsidy are granted; for Taiwanese university graduates who obtain business licenses in Tianjin and conduct normal production and business operations in leased premises, a rent subsidy of 1,800 yuan per month for up to 24 months is granted; Taiwanese students enjoy the same treatment as Tianjin citizens during compulsory education; Taiwan compatriots who have lived in Tianjin for one year or more enjoy the same treatment as local hukou holders in purchasing housing in the city, including eligibility and mortgage loans, and so on.\nOn July 8, Zhejiang Province issued and implemented the “Implementation Opinions of Zhejiang Province on Implementing the ‘Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,’” covering a total of 76 specific measures in investment cooperation, technological innovation, employment and entrepreneurship, cultural exchange, and living arrangements. Among them, it specifies that Taiwan-funded enterprises may enjoy the relevant treatment Zhejiang extends to support the operation and development of private and foreign-invested enterprises, and may equally enjoy the various support funds established at the provincial and local levels and the preferential policies introduced; for Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan compatriots who contribute to science and technology innovation and the transformation and use of achievements in Zhejiang, those who meet the conditions may be recommended to participate in the provincial Science and Technology Award evaluation in accordance with regulations; Taiwan compatriots interning, working, and starting businesses in Zhejiang enjoy equal access to internship subsidies, employment subsidies, one-time entrepreneurship subsidies, entrepreneurship-driven employment subsidies, entrepreneurship guarantee loans and interest subsidies, and other support policies; Taiwan compatriots may enjoy the same public cultural service treatment as Zhejiang residents, and public cultural facilities at all levels in Zhejiang open to Taiwan compatriots free of charge or at preferential rates according to their functions, characteristics and relevant regulations; Taiwan compatriot investors and the children of Taiwan compatriots lawfully employed in Zhejiang who live together with them there may, in accordance with relevant regulations, enter kindergartens and primary and secondary schools in their localities and enjoy the same treatment as local students, and so on.\nOn July 9, Hubei Province published and implemented the “Implementation Opinions on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” covering 62 specific measures in four areas: promoting economic cooperation, encouraging entrepreneurship and employment, strengthening cultural exchange, and facilitating residence and daily life. In promoting economic cooperation, it sets out specific measures to accelerate the transfer of Taiwan-funded enterprises to Hubei’s industries and to promote their transformation and upgrading, and makes concrete arrangements for funding support, encouraging technological innovation, industrial guidance, factor supply, and financing and guarantees. In encouraging entrepreneurship and employment, it sets out specific provisions on platform construction, funding support, tax and venue rent reductions, and vocational training for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, starting businesses in Hubei; Taiwan compatriots working in Hubei may take 53 professional and technical personnel vocational qualification examinations and 81 skilled personnel vocational qualification examinations, and Taiwan compatriots coming to Hubei to work in medicine, law, teaching and other professions, and participating in various provincial talent recruitment programs, also enjoy equal qualification treatment. In strengthening cultural exchange, it sets out provisions and explanations on Taiwan compatriots’ participation in cultural and social science awards, applying for related research projects, participating in intellectual property cooperation, and taking part in grassroots community work. In facilitating residence and daily life, it sets out provisions on equal qualifications and treatment for Taiwan compatriots in Hubei in medical care, schooling, tourism and travel, providing more convenience for their residence and daily life in Hubei.\nOn July 6, Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province issued the “Several Measures on Deepening Economic, Social and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Kunshan and Taiwan,” covering 68 specific measures in five areas: investment and economic cooperation, financial innovation cooperation, social and cultural exchange, Taiwan compatriots studying, interning, working, and starting businesses in Kunshan, and Taiwan compatriots’ residence and daily life in Kunshan. Apart from the “31 Measures” being fully implemented in Kunshan, another 26 pilot measures with local characteristics have been added. These measures fully draw on and further expand the effective practices of Kunshan over the five years since the establishment of the Kunshan Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone, reflecting the greatest possible extension of local reform and development achievements to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. On expanded measures, they explicitly support Taiwan enterprises in adopting dual-innovation models such as “joint incubation,” provide support policies for Taiwan-funded e-commerce enterprises, support Taiwan enterprises in participating in international trade fairs, strengthen financial and fiscal support for Taiwan-funded enterprises, expand opening of the financial sector to Taiwan capital, explore new cooperation models with innovative Taiwan-funded enterprises in government procurement, and encourage state-owned enterprises to purchase Taiwanese cultural, sports and other products and services. On equal treatment, they specify that Taiwan compatriots who have obtained employment permits in Kunshan and do not own housing may purchase one apartment as a family unit; Taiwan compatriots in Kunshan and their families enjoy the same healthcare services as Kunshan residents; qualifying Taiwan compatriots and their parents admitted to elderly care institutions enjoy the same treatment as elderly people with local hukou; cross-Strait professional and technical titles are supported for recognition by comparison; and equal treatment is granted in establishing wholly foreign-owned medical institutions, investing in modern agriculture, and in policy support for Taiwan youth starting businesses in Kunshan. In addition, Kunshan has simultaneously issued the “Three-Year Upgrading Project Implementation Plan for Promoting Kunshan-Taiwan Integrated Development (2018–2020),” aiming within three years to build Kunshan into a demonstration zone for cross-Strait deep integrated development, with the closest industrial cooperation, the deepest social and cultural exchange, and the most comprehensive implementation of “same-city treatment.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201807/t20180716_12036139.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-07-18","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council Minister Chen Ming-tong is in Washington. He is going to speak at a think tank and meet some US senior officials from the administration. It appears to be the first \"cabinet-level\" official from Taiwan to visit the US. What is your response to that? Will China do anything if US officials meet with him?","Our position on the issue of exchanges between the US and Taiwan remains clear and consistent. We firmly oppose official interactions between the US and Taiwan in any form and urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, prudently handle the Taiwan issue and uphold the larger picture of the China-US relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1578409.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201807/t20180718_5416445.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-19","Hua Chunying","","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council Minister Chen Ming-tong appealed at a symposium in Washington that Taiwan and the mainland have practical communications and dialogue to seek internal agreement. Official from the US Department of Defense said that Taiwan is an important partner for the US' Indo-Pacific strategy. What is your response?","I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for comments on Chen's remarks regarding cross-Straits relations. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and prudently handle the Taiwan issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1578759.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1578645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-19","Hua Chunying","","Some US airlines, including the United Airlines, the Delta Airlines and the American Airlines have not yet complied with the Chinese government's directive to refer to Taiwan as Chinese Taiwan by July 25th. Are the US and China in talks to resolve this issue? What punitive actions will China take if they do not comply?","China's Civil Aviation Administration held a press briefing on July 13 on the latest development of the relevant issue. China's position is quite clear. Foreign enterprises operating in China shall respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and abide by Chinese laws and regulations. The same can be said for Chinese enterprises operating in other countries. Moreover, one China is a basic fact and international consensus.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1578759.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1578645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-24","Geng Shuang","","明天是中国政府要求外国航空公司将官网上对台湾的称谓改为“中国台湾”的最后期限，但一些美国航空公司尚未更改。中方是否与美航空公司进行过沟通？中美政府是否就此沟通？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1579863.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2018-07-24","Geng Shuang","","如果一些外国航空公司没有按中方要求更改网站上对台湾的标注，中方将对其采取什么反制措施？是否会禁止其使用中国的机场？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1579863.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","American Airlines and Delta Airlines have both removed references to Taiwan as a country on the website. But they have not gone so far to say \"Taiwan, China\" like other airlines. Is the Chinese government satisfied with this approach?","We noted that some positive developments have taken place and acknowledge the corrections made by relevant foreign airlines.\nChina is willing to share development opportunities with foreign enterprises and they are welcome to invest and operate in China. In the meantime, we also hope that when doing business in China, they will respect China's laws and regulations and sovereignty and territorial integrity, and respect the Chinese people's feelings. Indeed, we will ensure their lawful rights and interests in accordance with the law and create a level playing field for them to do business in China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","The US Congress has reached a compromise on the draft bill of National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2019 that includes several propositions aimed at China, like strengthening defense ties with Taiwan and studying China's \"coercive activities\" in the South China Sea. What is your response to this?","The Chinese side expresses strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to the China-related provisions in the above-mentioned bill and has lodged stern representations with the US side on many occasions. If the relevant content passes into law, it will severely undermine the mutual trust between China and the US and jeopardize our exchanges and communication in relevant fields as well as cross-straits peace and stability. We urge the US side to discard the outdated cold-war and zero-sum mentality, immediately delete the relevant negative content and uphold rather than disrupt the steady development of the relations between the two countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","The East Asian Olympic Committee (EAOC) revoked Taichung city's right to host the East Asian Youth Games in 2019. Spokesperson of the US Department of State said that it supports Taiwan's participation in international organizations whose members are not restricted to countries, and that the mainland and Taiwan should have productive talks as soon as possible to avoid escalation of tension. What's your reaction…","The Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council already made an elaborate response to this issue of the EAOC revoking Taichung city's right to host the East Asian Youth Games in 2019.\nRegarding the remarks by the US Department of State, I shall say that the one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community and adhering to the principle is the political foundation for the steady development of China-US relations. We urge the US side to comply with the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and properly handle relevant Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","Today is the deadline for the foreign airlines to change the way they label Taiwan on their websites. What consequences will they face if they don't change their websites?","Like I just said, we noted that some positive developments have taken place in this regard and we acknowledge the corrections made by relevant foreign airlines.\nI also stressed that for foreign companies operating in China, they should respect China's laws and regulations as well as its sovereignty and territorial integrity, and respect the Chinese people's feelings.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","Regarding the Civil Aviation Administration of China's demand that foreign airlines should change their reference to Taiwan, the US Embassy in China said it opposed China's attempt to force private businesses into using certain terms with political implications. What' your response?","We already stated our position many times these two days. Adhering to the one-China principle is the political foundation for the steady development of China-US relations. We hope the US government will urge the relevant enterprises to comply with the one-China principle rather than put a drag on that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-25","Geng Shuang","","You just said many foreign airlines have changed the way Taiwan is labeled on their websites. Are there any airlines at the moment which in the Chinese government's view are not in keeping with the way that you would have them referred to Taiwan?","It was the Chinese competent authority that issued a notice asking foreign airlines to correct their websites. So I will refer you to the competent authority if you are interested in knowing how changes should be made on their references to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580228.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-07-25","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 25 (Reporter Chen Jianxing) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, answering questions on the 25th, pointed out that the East Asian Olympic Committees decided to cancel the 2019 East Asian Youth Games because some political forces and “Taiwan independence” elements in Taiwan, with the connivance of the DPP authorities, promoted the so-called “Tokyo Olympics name-correction referendum,” openly challenging the “Olympic model” and exposing the 2019 East Asian Youth Games in Taichung to enormous political risk and political interference. We have always opposed political interference in sports, and have repeatedly expressed our firm opposition to the so-called “name-correction referendum” provocation. The IOC has also paid close attention and wrote to the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee to state its position. The “Olympic model” must be upheld and maintained; this is a consensus in the international sports community. Cancelling the 2019 East Asian Youth Games in Taichung was a correct decision by the East Asian Olympic Committees.\nHe said that the reasons Taichung City lost the hosting rights for this Games are very clear. The root cause is that the DPP authorities, for their own narrow political interests, disregarded the interests of Taiwan athletes, the sports community and the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and ignored our repeated reminders by insisting on indulging the so-called “name-correction referendum” and its challenge to the “Olympic model.” Regarding the East Asian Olympic Committees' decision to cancel the Taichung City East Asian Youth Games, the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces that promoted the so-called “referendum” cannot escape blame. Confusing public opinion and diverting attention will be of no use; they must bear full responsibility for their words and deeds.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that we have repeatedly urged the DPP authorities not to take actions that challenge the one-China principle, undermine cross-strait relations, harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots, or harm the interests of the Chinese nation. Yet they have turned a deaf ear. Recently, the DPP authorities have obstructed and restricted cross-strait exchanges even more aggressively. Mainland exchange delegations visiting Taiwan have repeatedly been banned and restricted, and Taiwan civil groups and university and high school students coming to the mainland for cultural and sports exchanges have repeatedly been subjected to suppression and intimidation by the DPP authorities. We once again urge the DPP authorities to return to the path of peaceful cross-strait development based on the “1992 Consensus”; not to harm and sacrifice the interests of Taiwan's ordinary people again for narrow political gain; not to keep stirring up hostility between compatriots on both sides or escalating cross-strait confrontation; and not to rely on foreign backing to overrate themselves, harbor illusions, or persist in their delusions.\nAn Fengshan said that we have always actively supported and worked to promote cross-strait civil sports exchanges, and we welcome Taiwan's participation in international sports activities in accordance with the “Olympic model.” When athletes from both sides achieve good results in international competitions, it is a glory for all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. Cross-strait civil sports exchanges have maintained a good momentum of development for many years; in exchanges and cooperation they have promoted the popularization of sports, the promotion of sporting spirit, and the raising of competitive sports standards on both sides. We will, as always, vigorously support the continued expansion and deepening of exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait, including sports exchanges, and add positive energy to the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201807/t20180725_12039804.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-07-25","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","It is reported that the head of Taiwan authorities’ foreign affairs department, Wu Chao-hsi, recently gave an interview to the American CNN, in which he expressed views on cross-Strait relations and US-Taiwan relations. He said that “Taiwan survives on its own, outside China,” and that without continued US military support, Taiwan could easily be “forcibly occupied” by the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s…","(Xinhua) Beijing, July 25 — Spokesperson An Fengshan of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council responded to questions on the 25th, saying that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory. This is the consensus of the international community, and no force can ever change it. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and we absolutely will not tolerate, and firmly oppose, interference by external forces. The DPP authorities, attempting to rely on foreign powers to boost their own standing, will only aggravate the turbulence and instability of the situation across the Taiwan Strait and bring Taiwan to a dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201807/t20180726_12040013.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-07-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","During the regular press conference last month, the spokesperson mentioned that the counter-terrorism joint military exercise among member states’ militaries of Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) was to be held in Russia in August. Could you please brief us on the latest development? Recently, the US Congress has reached a compromise on the draft bill of National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year…","The SCO will hold the Peace Mission 2018 joint military drill from August 22 to 29 in No. 255 Comprehensive Training Field in Chebarkul, Chelyabinsk, Russia. The theme of the drill is “Preparation and Cooperation on Counter-terrorism Among SCO Member States’ Militaries”. The main subjects include field reconnaissance, joint fire strike, counter-terrorism operations in residential settlements. The PLA will send 743 officers and men to participate. This is a routine military drill within the framework of the SCO, which has been playing a positive role in deepening defense and security cooperation among member states, enhancing capacity in tackling new threats and challenges and also safeguarding regional peace and stability.\nOn the second question, we have noted relevant information. What needs to be stressed is that Taiwan is an integral part of China. We firmly oppose any official contacts and military exchanges in any form between any country and Taiwan. This position is clear and consistent. There is no way out only relying on other countries and any attempt to make use of Taiwan to contain China is doomed to failure. We urge the US side to keep its commitment to One-China Policy and relevant propositions in the three joint communiqués between China and US and handle Taiwan-related issues properly and cautiously so as not to harm the state-to-state and the mil-to-mil relationship between China and the US and the cross-strait peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-07/26/content_4820785.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-07-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to the Taiwan media, the so-called Taiwan’s defense ministry said that, from July 20 to 21, a total of nearly 50 ships of the PLA Navy passed through the Taiwan straits at high speed. The Taiwan media speculated that this move was to guard against typhoon. What is your comment on that?","The PLA has recently organized live-fire confrontational exercises in relevant waters and airspace. It is a normal arrangement for the ships of the PLA Navy to navigate through the Taiwan Straits. There is no need to overinterpret.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-07/26/content_4820785.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-07-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Days ago, the US former Secretary of Defense Ashton Carter said in his speech in Taiwan that Taiwan will play an important role in the Indo-Pacific strategy of the US, claiming that there is a large space for military cooperation between the US and Taiwan. What is your comment on that?","We have noticed relevant reports. I’d like to reiterate and stress that Taiwan is part of China，and the Taiwan issue concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is the most important and most sensitive core issue in the China-US relations. We firmly oppose any official contacts and military exchanges in any form between any country and Taiwan. We urge the US side to keep its commitment to the ”one-China” principle and provisions of the three Joint Communiqués between China and the US, and to stop making irresponsible remarks and taking provocative actions, so as not to harm the state-to-state and mil-to-mil relations between China and the US and cross-straits peace and stability.\nThe Taiwan side should also be fully aware of the situation that there is no way out to rely on foreign countries, and it should give up the “Taiwan independence” fantasy and confrontational mentality, and do more things to improve the relations between the mainland and Taiwan. The PLA will take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard China’s national sovereignty, territorial integrity and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-07/26/content_4820785.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2018-07-27","Geng Shuang","","According to German media, Germany is preparing for the first time to prevent the takeover of a German company by Chinese investors for strategic reasons. The Chinese company is called Yantai Taihai and the German company is Leifeld Metal, which produces parts for cars and planes well as well nuclear equipment. What's your comment?","We noted relevant reports and are paying attention to this. In recent years, China and Germany have been working to deepen bilateral relations and maintain a sound momentum for two-way investments, which plays a positive role in promoting the economic development and employment of the two countries.\nIn face of rising protectionism and unilateralism, China and Germany, as two major economies in the world, have the responsibility to uphold free trade and multilateralism, boost the bilateral high-standard and mutually beneficial cooperation through two-way opening up, and inject positive energy to sustaining an open world economy. We hope the German side can treat Chinese investment objectively and provide open and fair market access and stable institutional framework for Chinese companies to invest in Germany.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1580976.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1580892.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-30","Geng Shuang","","First, the Taiwan side submitted a petition for the East Asian Youth Games hosting rights today. Will the Chinese mainland try to block that again in the East Asian Olympic Committee (EAOC) or take other countermeasures? Second, according to Taiwan media reports, the mainland's delegation headed to relevant APEC events, who refused to enter Taiwan due to delayed entry permit, has now returned to the mainland.…","I would take your second question first. There has been customary practices for people from Chinese Taiwan and mainland to participate in the APEC activities hosted by each other over the years. The Taiwan side's violation of the established practices hindered the mainland delegation's participation in the Digital Innovation Forum of the APEC Business Advisory Council (ABAC) and the Taiwan side is fully to blame for the consequence. The fact and nature of this incident are very clear. The Taiwan side's attempt to confuse the public, distort the fact and shirk responsibility with relevant remarks is doomed to fail. We hope the Chinese Taipei will earnestly reflect upon what it did and correct its wrongdoing in concrete actions.\nWith regard to your first question, I would refer you to the competent authority. What I need to point out here is that Taiwan's participation in international activities should always abide by the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1581484.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1581384.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-07-30","Geng Shuang","","Firstly, does China have a view on how free and fair elections were? Secondly, what does China make of possible US responsive visa restrictions and EU possible responsive sanctions with regard to how this election was run?","I have just answered similar questions. The National Assembly election is Cambodia's domestic affairs. China sincerely congratulates Cambodia on the successful running of the sixth National Assembly Election and the CPP led by Chairman Hun Sen on winning the election. We hope that under the leadership of the forthcoming National Assembly and government, the Cambodian people will make greater achievement in their national development.\nMeanwhile, we also hope that the international community could play a constructive role in helping Cambodia maintain stability and achieve development.\nAfter the press conference, the following question is raised: The Vietnamese government has allowed some Taiwan businessmen to hang the so-called \"blue sky-white sun\" flag in their factories due to their worries over security. What's your comment?\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. China firmly opposes all forms of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and has lodged stern representations with Vietnam. The Vietnamese side has ordered relevant enterprises to rectify their wrongdoings.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1581484.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1581384.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-07-30","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 30 (reporter Shi Longhong): An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on July 30 that since the “Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation Across the Taiwan Strait” (hereinafter the “31 Measures”) were issued and came into effect, more than a dozen provinces, municipalities and regions, including Shanghai, Tianjin, Fujian and Xiamen, have issued detailed measures for implementation. Recently, Guangdong, Shenzhen, Hangzhou and Huai'an have also successively issued specific implementing measures tailored to local conditions.\n—On July 26, Guangdong Province issued and implemented the “Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Guangdong and Taiwan,” comprising 13 sections and 48 specific measures.\nIn terms of focusing on “equal treatment,” Taiwan-invested enterprises may participate in infrastructure construction in Guangdong Province's energy, transport, water conservancy, environmental protection, municipal public utilities and other projects through franchising; they may, on equal terms with Guangdong enterprises and other capital, participate in cooperative construction of transport infrastructure PPP projects by governments at all levels in the province; they may, on equal terms, use the province's land guarantee and preferential measures; and Taiwan compatriots may take part in various honor evaluations in Guangdong Province, such as Model Workers and “Three-Eight” Red Banner Bearers.\nIn terms of sharing the “Guangdong dividend,” Guangdong will take the lead in sharing with Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots the series of favorable policies and development opportunities that Guangdong has implemented in recent years, including innovation-driven development, expanded opening to the outside world, and support for the real economy. It will focus on supporting Taiwan-invested enterprises in carrying out digital, networked, intelligent and green technological upgrading, and increase support for Taiwan-invested R&D institutions. The business scope for Taiwan compatriots applying to register individual industrial and commercial households in Guangdong Province will follow the treatment for Hong Kong and Macao residents, covering 135 items.\nIn terms of focusing on “Guangdong-Taiwan integration,” it will expand and deepen exchanges and cooperation between Guangdong and Taiwan in all fields, covering industry, fiscal and taxation, land, finance, education, culture, healthcare and more. It will focus on supporting the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises in emerging pillar manufacturing industries such as next-generation information technology, high-end intelligent equipment, and the marine economy, and it will emphasize strengthening civil exchanges in culture and academia.\nIn responding to the demands of “Taiwan compatriots,” eligible Taiwan-invested enterprises may apply to participate in Guangdong Province government procurement activities, and may apply, on the same terms as Guangdong enterprises, for inclusion in the Guangdong Province innovative products list to enjoy government procurement incentive measures. Taiwan compatriots may use their Taiwan Compatriot Permits to register and log in to government and public service information systems and platforms such as “China Public Recruitment Network” and “Guangdong Employment Network.”\n—On July 24, Shenzhen released the “Compilation of Shenzhen Policies Implementing the ‘31 Measures,’” covering 99 policies in 18 categories, including development and reform policies, fiscal funds and government procurement policies, economic, trade and informatization policies, science and innovation policies, state-owned assets policies, financial policies, and tax policies. These basically cover the various equal-treatment policy measures for Taiwan compatriots studying, starting businesses, working and living in Shenzhen. The policies released this time have a clear inclusive character. In enterprise development, talent recruitment, and science and technology innovation policies, they describe relevant provisions on Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots enjoying tax preferences, participating in national key R&D programme projects, infrastructure construction, government procurement, applying for various fund projects, and so on, and are committed to creating a stable, fair, transparent and predictable business environment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots. Shenzhen municipality also specially notes that the 2018 municipal-level special fiscal fund budget in Shenzhen reached RMB 25.737 billion, with 54 special funds covering more than 200 funding directions, and that eligible Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots may apply through the prescribed procedures.\n—On July 17, Hangzhou municipality, Zhejiang Province, issued and implemented the “Implementation Opinions on Further Deepening Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Hangzhou and Taiwan,” covering investment, employment, study, daily life and other areas, with 60 specific measures in total.\nIn terms of sharing Hangzhou's advantageous industrial development opportunities, Taiwan-invested enterprises are encouraged and supported to take part in major action plans such as the construction of the “Greater Bay Area,” research programmes, and platform construction; to set up investment parks and industrial cooperation zones and to locate in characteristic towns, makerspaces and other entrepreneurship and innovation bases; to take part in urban infrastructure, “rural revitalization” construction, and mixed-ownership reform of state-owned enterprises; to jointly train research teams and technical talent. Major projects enjoy “one-project-one-discussion” support policies, and they enjoy equal treatment in intellectual property commercialization, organizing conferences and exhibitions, financial credit, and other areas.\nIn terms of helping Taiwan youth integrate into Hangzhou's development, Taiwan teenagers are encouraged to travel to Hangzhou for study tours. Taiwan university students may apply for internships at more than 600 trainee bases and receive internship subsidies, and those who come to Hangzhou to start businesses or find employment may apply for funding of up to RMB 200,000 and small guaranteed loans of up to RMB 300,000. Taiwan youth may take part in free vocational skills training and dedicated job fairs in Hangzhou, and they enjoy equal treatment in applying for various talent programmes.\nIn terms of conveniences in daily life, in addition to purchasing commercial housing, Taiwan compatriots may apply for public rental housing and youth talent stations; they may enjoy discounts on urban public transport and sightseeing attractions, as well as free services in areas such as public culture and legal consultation; they can receive fast and efficient service in handling social security, medical insurance, the housing provident fund and other matters; and Taiwan compatriots and their family members studying, working or living in Hangzhou can obtain a “big package” of convenience services by applying for a Hangzhou Citizen Card.\n—On July 23, Huai'an municipality, Jiangsu Province, issued the “Implementation Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Huai'an and Taiwan,” comprising 58 specific measures in five areas.\nIn terms of promoting economic and trade cooperation between Huai'an and Taiwan, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in Huai'an are supported in taking part in the construction of the “one zone, two belts and one hub,” and enjoy equal treatment in more areas, such as project attraction, participation in infrastructure construction, government procurement, science and technology R&D, import tax preferences, and industrial land preferences.\nIn terms of helping Taiwan compatriots start businesses, Taiwan compatriots starting businesses in Huai'an are assisted under the “six uniformities”: when Taiwan compatriots set up small and micro enterprises, they are uniformly provided a “green channel”; they are uniformly charged administrative and public institution fees at the lower limit; they are uniformly given free entrepreneurship training; they are uniformly given tax preferences; they are uniformly given access to the city's public service platforms and science and technology R&D platforms; and they are uniformly given assisted financial services.\nIn terms of building a high ground for Taiwan talent, Taiwan professionals who independently apply through Huai'an municipality and are selected for the national “Thousand Talents Plan” or “Ten Thousand Talents Plan,” Taiwan talent employed or starting businesses at enterprises and institutions in Huai'an, and Taiwan talent selected for the innovation and entrepreneurship urgently needed talent projects under the “Northern Jiangsu Plan” and “Huaishang Talent Plan” are all given financial subsidies according to certain standards. Those who qualify equally enjoy housing and rental subsidies, training, medical examinations, recuperation and other service benefits.\nIn terms of deepening exchanges between Huai'an and Taiwan, the measures establish special funds, help Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots apply for cultural projects and funds at all levels, give play to the role of the Taiwan Business College, encourage Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots to take part in social development, and strengthen social and cultural exchange and cooperation between Huai'an and Taiwan.\nIn terms of optimizing services for Taiwan businesspeople, innovative service measures are provided for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots in handling administrative affairs, children's school enrollment, medical care, home purchase, social security, travel, honorary title selection, mediation of Taiwan-related commercial cases, and handling of labor disputes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201807/t20180730_12041973.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-07-31","Geng Shuang","","There is information that Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen is going to visit Paraguay and Belize next month, and she plans to \"transit\" in the US during the trip. Does China have any comment on that?","The one-China principle represents the universal consensus of the international community. Any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\" will be opposed by all Chinese people and it does not serve the fundamental interests of the people in Taiwan. We urge the Taiwan authorities to get a clear understanding of the situation, come back to the \"1992 consensus\" as soon as possible and refrain from taking any actions that go against the trend of the times and run counter to the will of the people.\nAs to the so-called \"stopover\" made by the Taiwan leader in the United States, the Chinese side has made clear its position many times and lodged stern representations with the US side. We are always opposed to arranging such kind of \"stopover\" on the part of the US and other countries that have established diplomatic ties with China. This position is consistent and firm.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China policy and the principles stipulated by the three China-US joint communiqués, not to allow the Taiwan leader to \"transit\", refrain from sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" force and uphold the overall picture of China-US ties and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1581940.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1581787.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-02","Geng Shuang","","The US Senate passed the 2019 National Defense Authorization Act, which is set to reinforce Taiwan's defense capability and expand joint training, arms sales and high-level military exchanges with Taiwan. It also advises the US Department of Defense to advance military exercises with Taiwan. What's your comment?","The Chinese side has already made clear its position before, and lodged stern representations with the US side for many times. We urge the US to discard the outdated cold-war and zero-sum mentality, stop allowing the bill that contains negative China-related content to pass into law and refrain from implementing the relevant clauses, lest it should undermine the China-US relations and the cooperation in key areas.\nAs to the Taiwan-related issues, I shall stress again that the Taiwan issue concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is the most important and sensitive issue at the core of China-US relations. We firmly oppose any official exchange and military contact between Taiwan and any country. We demand that the US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués to properly handle the Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1582646.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1582552.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-03","Geng Shuang","","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with his Japanese counterpart Taro Kono in Singapore yesterday. We learned from the information issued by the two sides that both China and Japan remain positive towards the improvement of bilateral relations. Can you give us more details on that?","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with his Japanese counterpart Taro Kono on the sidelines of the Foreign Ministers' Meetings on East Asia Cooperation in Singapore. We released the relevant information yesterday.\nChina and Japan are important neighbors. China always attaches great importance to its ties with Japan. As State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said when meeting with Foreign Minister Taro Kono yesterday, the two sides must earnestly cement the political foundation for bilateral relations, which has been enshrined in the four political documents, and properly handle sensitive issues related to history and Taiwan. This is the overarching precondition for the improvement and development of China-Japan relations. Foreign Minister Taro Kono said that the Japanese side is willing to make greater efforts to implement the consensus reached by the leaders of the two countries so as to lay the groundwork for the sustained improvement and development of China-Japan relations.\nWe hope that the Japanese side can translate its positive remarks on its ties with China into actions, contribute more to the improvement and development of China-Japan relations and move forward our bilateral ties along the right track.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1583054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1582927.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The US Senate recently passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2019,” which supports strengthening Taiwan’s defense capabilities, expanding joint training, arms sales, and high-level military exchanges, and the Taiwan authorities have expressed gratitude. What is your comment? Apart from stating that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already set forth our position and attitude on this, Ma…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (reporters 石龙洪 and 赵博) — TAO spokesperson 马晓光 said in response to a question on the 3rd: The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is also the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities seek to rely on foreign powers to elevate themselves. This will only make the situation in the Taiwan Strait more tense and turbulent, and cross-Strait relations more complicated and grim.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180803_12043490.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-08-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 8 -- On August 3, the State Council announced a decision on canceling a batch of administrative licensing items and other matters, including canceling the employment permit item for Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao personnel in the mainland. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, briefed on the relevant situation on August 8.\nMa Xiaoguang said that, to implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and gradually provide Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland compatriots in studying, starting businesses, finding employment, and living on the mainland, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security and other relevant departments, conducted active research, carefully listened to the opinions and suggestions of a broad range of Taiwan compatriots, and, with the approval of the State Council after it was submitted for approval, decided to cancel the relevant regulations requiring Taiwan residents to obtain employment permits for working on the mainland. From now on, Taiwan residents working on the mainland will be like mainland residents and no longer need to apply for the special \"Employment Permit for Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Personnel.\"\nHe said that Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland may use a business license, labor contract, wage payment voucher, or social insurance contribution record as proof of employment, and enjoy all labor and social security rights under the law. After becoming unemployed, they may register as unemployed in accordance with regulations and enjoy public employment services. Next, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security will, as required by the State Council, promptly issue supporting policy measures for Taiwan residents' employment on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180808_12044780.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-08-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, August 13 — A fire broke out in the early morning of August 13 at a hospital in Xinzhuang District, New Taipei City, Taiwan. The accident has caused 9 deaths and more than ten people with serious and minor injuries. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said that we are deeply saddened by this accident, extend our condolences to the Taiwan compatriots who died in the tragedy, and sincerely express sympathy to the families of the deceased and the injured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180813_12046845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-08-14","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On August 13, local time in the United States, the US side signed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2019.” The provisions of this act concerning China are full of Cold War mentality, play up China-US confrontation, interfere in China's internal affairs, violate the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, undermine the atmosphere for the development of China-US and China-US military-to-military relations, and damage mutual trust and cooperation between China and the United States. The Chinese armed forces firmly oppose this and have lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nTaiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-US relations. We firmly oppose any country carrying out any form of official exchanges or military contacts with Taiwan. This position is firm and clear. We will never allow anyone, at any time or in any form, to split Taiwan from China.\nA person without trustworthiness cannot stand, and a country without trustworthiness will decline. We urge the US side to honor its commitments to China on the Taiwan question, abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently, so as not to harm China-US and China-US military-to-military relations or peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2018-08/14/content_4823075.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2018-08-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 13 (reporter: Liu Huan). Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 13th that since the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation” (hereinafter the “31 Measures”) were issued and implemented, all localities and departments have been stepping up implementation and continuously made positive progress. Recently, relevant departments and provinces, municipalities and autonomous regions have successively issued specific implementation measures.\n——On July 30, the National Art Fund introduced specific measures to implement the “31 Measures” provision that “Taiwan compatriots may apply for National Art Fund projects.” With the approval of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism, the National Art Fund officially announced the specific measure “The National Art Fund will open project applications to Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan arts workers who work and study in the Chinese mainland”:\nIn 2019, the National Art Fund will open applications for the Young Art Creative Talent Support Project to Taiwan arts workers who are employed by mainland art units and institutions, or employed or enrolled at higher education institutions, with an employment or enrollment term of more than one year, and who are under 40 years of age. The scope of support covers creative talent in drama and quyi (traditional Chinese narrative performing arts) scriptwriting, music composition, dance and dance-drama choreography, stage performance, fine arts, calligraphy, photography, and arts and crafts. At the same time, the Art Fund will also encourage mainland art units and institutions to cooperate with Taiwan art institutions in applying for support for stage art creation, communication and promotion projects, and for arts talent training. Projects in which mainland art units and institutions apply to hold performances and exhibitions in Taiwan will receive special attention.\n——On August 2, the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region issued and implemented the “Several Measures on Promoting Guangxi-Taiwan Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” comprehensively implementing the “31 Measures.” Covering six areas (promoting investment and economic cooperation; promoting study, entrepreneurship and employment; facilitating residence and daily life; deepening social and cultural exchanges and cooperation; and advancing the construction of cooperation zones), it sets out 80 measures to promote Guangxi-Taiwan economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, providing Taiwan compatriots in Guangxi with treatment equal to that of Guangxi residents in investment, entrepreneurship, employment, study and daily life.\nFirst, highlight Guangxi's advantages. Centering on Guangxi's development positioning and strategic priorities, the measures bring together the Western Development policy, the coastal opening policy, the ethnic autonomy policy and the border-area opening policy that Guangxi enjoys, and provide equal treatment to Taiwan enterprises and compatriots in cross-border labor, tax, and open cooperation policies.\nSecond, highlight policy innovation. Among the measures, especially in the areas of investment and living convenience and open cooperation, and in industrial funds, open cooperation, administrative approval, talent recruitment, youth entrepreneurship and the business environment, preferential treatment is provided to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises for starting businesses and developing in Guangxi.\nThird, give priority to helping Taiwan youth find employment and start businesses. Targeted support measures are set out for Taiwan youth coming to Guangxi to start businesses or find jobs, and for the recruitment of Taiwan talent, including employment subsidy policies for university graduates, entrepreneurship guarantee loan policies, and preferential measures for moving into entrepreneurship incubation platforms. Taiwan compatriots are encouraged to take part in the “Beautiful Guangxi” rural revitalization initiative and to develop modern characteristic agriculture, achieving mutual benefit and win-win results.\nFourth, align with the preferential policies of the cooperation zones. In setting up investment industry funds, investment promotion rewards, processing trade, cross-border labor and related areas, relevant preferential support policies are extended to the Guangxi Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone, encouraging Taiwan-invested enterprises to accelerate their concentration in the cooperation zone, creating a demonstration effect that spreads from points to areas and promoting high-starting, high-level development of the cooperation zone.\nThe issuance of these “Several Measures” will help Taiwan-invested enterprises in Guangxi simplify approval procedures, reduce operating costs, accelerate transformation and upgrading, and better participate in Guangxi's economic and social development and in the construction of the “Belt and Road.” They will bring greater convenience to Taiwan compatriots for employment, entrepreneurship, study and daily life in Guangxi, and create better conditions and broader space for them.\n——On August 8, Nanjing City issued the “Several Measures on Deepening Services Enabling Taiwan Compatriots Coming to Nanjing to Study, Work, Travel and Live Well,” proposing 75 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots.\nIn terms of studying well, a “Jinling Trial Flight Plan” for Taiwan youth coming to Nanjing will be set up, providing a 1,000 yuan round-trip transportation subsidy to Taiwan university students enrolled in Taiwan who complete an internship of more than three months locally.\nIn terms of working well, 41 measures have been formulated across five areas: employment, entrepreneurship, talent, investment, and platform services. These include a one-time 1,000 yuan interview subsidy for university graduates, and permitting qualified Taiwan teachers to work in kindergartens and regular senior high schools. Taiwan talent is encouraged to apply for the “Start-up Nanjing” Talent Plan; those selected for the top technology experts gathering plan receive project funding of up to 10 million yuan and follow-up investment of up to 100 million yuan. Those selected for the innovative entrepreneur cultivation plan receive interest subsidies on loans for up to five years, with total loans not exceeding 30 million yuan, as well as rent reductions for makerspaces, awards for R&D institution recognition, and subsidies for overseas training. Taiwan compatriots who do not own housing in Nanjing and rent a home may apply for a rental subsidy for three years in accordance with the rules. Those selected for the high-level entrepreneurial talent introduction plan receive start-up support of 500,000 to 1.5 million yuan, three years of rent-free talent apartments of 100 square meters, and three years of rent-free entrepreneurship premises of 100 square meters. These measures cover the relevant policies of Nanjing's construction of an internationally influential innovation city.\nIn terms of traveling well, a “Jinling Filial Piety Plan” for Taiwan youth will be set up: for Taiwan youth under 35 who have studied, worked or started businesses in Nanjing for more than one consecutive year, if they invite their parents to visit Nanjing, a 1,000 yuan round-trip transportation subsidy will be provided. When Taiwan compatriots first come to Nanjing, they may apply for a citizen transportation card free of charge, and when using transportation with the card they enjoy the same discounts as Nanjing citizens.\nIn terms of living well, 20 specific measures include enjoying the same treatment as Nanjing citizens in paying the housing provident fund, purchasing housing, medical and health services, and participating in social insurance; being able to apply for small-amount credit cards; and participating in various honor selections in Nanjing.\n——On July 30, Guangzhou City issued the “Several Measures on Further Deepening Guangzhou-Taiwan Economic, Social and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” comprehensively implementing the “31 Measures.” Covering four areas (deepening Guangzhou-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation; promoting Guangzhou-Taiwan social and cultural exchanges; supporting Taiwan compatriots in studying, working and starting businesses in Guangzhou; and facilitating Taiwan compatriots' residence and daily life in Guangzhou), it proposes 60 specific measures.\nFirst, make a concerted effort to encourage Taiwan youth to innovate and start businesses. Each year, at least 1,200 job positions and 300 internship positions will be provided for Taiwan university students, and after graduation, Taiwan university students who come to Guangzhou will receive an internship subsidy of no less than 1,500 yuan per person per month. Taiwan youth are encouraged and supported to take part in competitions such as the “Qingchuang Cup” Guangzhou Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition, and qualifying winning projects may receive entrepreneurship project funding of up to 200,000 yuan. Taiwan professional talent is supported in applying for Guangzhou City Talent Green Cards, among other measures.\nSecond, actively support the transformation, upgrading and technological innovation of Taiwan-invested enterprises. An annual fund of 10 million yuan for “Transformation and Upgrading of Taiwan-Invested Enterprises and Innovation and Entrepreneurship of Taiwan Youth” will be established to support the transformation and upgrading and technical renovation of Taiwan-invested enterprises, as well as the settlement of Taiwan youth entrepreneurial teams. Qualifying Taiwan-invested enterprises will be actively cultivated and guided to apply for recognition as “small giant” technology innovation enterprises and high-tech enterprises, and will receive subsidies and awards. Local Taiwan-invested high-tech enterprises that meet the requirements may enjoy high-tech enterprise tax preferences, among other measures.\nThird, comprehensively optimize the investment and business environment for Taiwan-invested enterprises. Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises are encouraged to share the development opportunities of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, the National Independent Innovation Demonstration Zone and the Nansha Free Trade Pilot Zone, and to invest in Guangzhou's ten key development fields and eleven key projects. Taiwan financial institutions are supported in pioneering green finance reform and innovation. Investors from Taiwan may enjoy the “Cross-Border Service” for fast settlement in Guangzhou, among other measures.\nFourth, continually facilitate the residence and daily life of Taiwan compatriots in Guangzhou. Taiwan compatriots working in Guangzhou are supported in participating in the “Five Social Insurances and One Housing Fund” in accordance with the rules and enjoying related labor security benefits. Qualifying Taiwan compatriots are supported in applying for Guangzhou public rental housing in accordance with the rules. Taiwan compatriots are given the same treatment as Guangzhou residents when entering various public cultural service venues, among other measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180814_12046906.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-08-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 14 dispatch: Recently, the U.S. “2019 National Defense Authorization Act” was signed into law by U.S. President Trump. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 14th: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other relevant departments have already stated our position and attitude on this. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and Taiwan region, and we firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. We urge the U.S. side not to implement the negative Taiwan-related provisions of the above act, so as to avoid damage to the overall situation of China-U.S. relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We also warn the DPP authorities that relying on foreign powers to bolster themselves will inevitably harm the interests of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180814_12047281.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-08-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to reports, Taiwan's education authority's curriculum review committee recently approved the senior high school history curriculum, incorporating Chinese history into East Asian history. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 15 (reporter Zhao Bo): TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 15th, said that since the DPP authorities took office, they have undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait relations and have supported and condoned all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. If the relevant reports are true, forcibly revising the senior high school history curriculum and incorporating Chinese history into East Asian history is yet another proof of “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct in the education field. It not only poisons the younger generation in Taiwan, but also further undermines cross-Strait relations and aggravates cross-Strait confrontation.\nHe also pointed out that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, compatriots on both sides belong to the Chinese nation, and Taiwan culture is an inseparable part of Chinese culture. No “de-Sinicization” conduct can sever the historical and cultural ties across the Strait. This reckless and retrograde conduct by the DPP authorities has met with strong opposition from Taiwan society. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities that forget their ancestors and roots will certainly meet stronger containment and blows from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180815_12047573.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-08-17","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","At 8 p.m. Beijing time on August 17, the US Department of Defense released its 2018 “China Military and Security Developments Report,” which distorts China's strategic intentions, exaggerates the so-called “China military threat,” and makes baseless remarks about cross-Strait relations and the situation in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese military firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nChina firmly follows the path of peaceful development and firmly adheres to a defensive national defense policy. It has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a guardian of international order. In recent years, the Chinese military has increasingly carried out overseas missions such as peacekeeping, escort, and disaster relief, shouldering more international responsibilities within its capacity and providing more public security goods. Its contributions and efforts have won widespread praise from the international community.\nThe Chinese military strengthens its modernization to safeguard the country's sovereignty, security, and development interests, and to safeguard world peace, stability, and prosperity. The reform of the Chinese military, the development of its weapons and equipment, and the building of its cyberspace defense capabilities are legitimate and reasonable. The accusations in the US report are pure speculation.\nTaiwan is part of China; this is an indisputable fact. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence. The Chinese military will, as always, firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nChina's position on maritime issues is consistent and clear. China is committed to resolving disputes with the countries concerned peacefully through direct negotiations. China's peaceful construction activities on the islands and reefs of the South China Sea are the legitimate right of a sovereign state; apart from meeting necessary national defense needs, they serve civilian needs, so that China can better fulfill its international responsibilities and obligations. The US, under the banner of “freedom of navigation,” has frequently sent warships and aircraft to the South China Sea to provoke and create tension. That is the real threat to regional peace and stability.\nThe United States' annual release of the so-called “China Military and Security Developments Report” undermines mutual trust between China and the US and does not serve the common interests of both sides. We demand that the US side abandon Cold War thinking, view China's national defense and military development objectively and rationally, stop releasing such reports, and take concrete actions to maintain the stable development of relations between the two militaries.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2018-08/17/content_4823028.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2018-08-20","Lu Kang","","Taiwan's leader Tsai Ing-wen has visited NASA's space center. What is your comment?","With regard to the Taiwan's leader exploiting all kinds of excuses to justify her foreign trips and separatist activities, the Chinese side has made its stern position clear to relevant countries that we oppose offering convenience and avenue for such activities.\nAs for the specific case you mentioned, I can tell you unequivocally that we have made clear our stern position to the US side. We urge the US to stick to the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués. The Taiwan separatist forces should not be aided nor have any space on the international stage. We firmly oppose any country that has diplomatic ties with China engaging in any official interaction with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1586627.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1586521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-21","Lu Kang","","China and El Salvador established diplomatic relations today. What is your comment?","This morning, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Foreign Minister of El Salvador Carlos Castaneda, on behalf of the two governments, inked the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the People's Republic of China and the Republic of El Salvador in Beijing. The two governments decided to recognize each other and establish the diplomatic relations at ambassadorial level as of the day the Joint Communiqué was signed.\nThere is only one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. This is a historical fact and a well-recognized norm governing international relations.\nEl Salvador is an important country in Central America. The government of El Salvador recognizes and promises to abide by the one-China principle. It has severed the so-called diplomatic ties with Taiwan and established diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China. This is a right choice made in accordance with the trend of the times and the will of the people. The Chinese side highly appreciates that.\nOn the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one-China principle, China is willing to enhance friendly cooperation with El Salvador in various areas so as to deliver benefits to the two countries and two peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1587065.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1586959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-21","Lu Kang","","First, Taiwan believes that \"money diplomacy\" is at play behind the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador. What is the response from the Foreign Ministry Spokesperson? Second, earlier this year, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi expressed the hope that no country in Africa will be absent from the family photo of the FOCAC Beijing Summit. So, will Swaziland attend this summit?","Regarding the first question, I believe that you know the details of the joint press conference held by State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Foreign Minister Castaneda this morning. It is for the competent department of the central government to respond to the remarks made by those in Taiwan, not the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. That said, I still want to emphasize that the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador is a political decision. It is by no means a so-called \"bargaining chip\" as imagined by some people in Taiwan. The Salvadoran government made the political decision to establish diplomatic relations with China without any economic preconditions because it identifies with the one-China principle. China highly appreciates this position of the Salvadoran side.\nI also want to remind those people in Taiwan that to establish and develop normal and friendly relations with the People's Republic of China is the trend of the times and the will of the people. They should learn to recognize this overwhelming trend and stop trying to explain everything away in terms of money.\nYou mentioned that there is still one African country that has not given up its so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. We have repeatedly stated that the Chinese government is always ready to forge friendly and cooperative ties with all countries in the world on the basis of the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one-China principle. We believe that such a relationship is in the interest of each other and we hope that the relevant country could clearly discern the trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1587065.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1586959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-08-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On August 21, the Government of the Republic of El Salvador announced that it would sever so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan, and China and El Salvador established diplomatic relations. Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities made accusations against the mainland in response. What is the TAO’s comment on this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in his answer.","Beijing, August 21 (Xinhua) — Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council said on the 21st, in response to a question, that the DPP authorities' attempt to cover up the truth, divert attention, escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and undermine cross-Strait relations is bound to fail; their attempt to sow discord and create trouble internationally is even more of an overestimation of their own abilities.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already issued a statement on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador. The establishment of China-El Salvador diplomatic relations is a correct decision made by El Salvador in accordance with the interests of its country and people. The overwhelming majority of countries in the world have already made the same decision. Facts have repeatedly proven that adhering to the one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community, reflects the wishes of the people, and represents the trend of the times.\nMa Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's sacred territory. Any attempt to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or to pursue “Taiwan independence” has no way out and will certainly be firmly opposed by the entire Chinese people. The DPP authorities' attempt to cover up the truth, divert attention, escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and undermine cross-Strait relations is bound to fail; their attempt to sow discord and create trouble internationally is even more of an overestimation of their own abilities. We once again advise the DPP authorities not to do anything that harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Acting against the tide is doomed to be futile. The only right choice is to return as soon as possible to the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations based on the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180821_12050019.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-08-22","Lu Kang","","The US State Department said that the US is deeply disappointed by El Salvador's decision to break its \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan in favor of China and is reviewing its relationship with El Salvador as a result. It accuses China of unilaterally altering the status quo and urges China to abstain from coercion that would jeopardize the people of Taiwan. The US Ambassador to El Salvador said that this will impact…","An independent sovereign state has the right to determine its own foreign relations. This is true both for China and El Salvador. We two countries established ties on the basis of the one-China principle. This corresponds to the trend of the times and the development of the international situation. It conforms with international law and basic norms governing international relations, serves the fundamental interests of the two countries and two peoples, and will not affect our respective relations with other countries.\nThe Salvadoran government made the same right choice as the UN and other 177 countries. Others are in no position to interfere in it or even try to deter it. The US established its diplomatic ties with China almost 40 years ago. But now, it is threatening another sovereign country not to recognize the one-China principle and develop normal relations with China while allowing Tsai Ing-wen to stop over and attend activities in the US. The Chinese people is firmly opposed to these unreasonable actions. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, put into perspective the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and El Salvador, cautiously and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and make sure that no wrong signal is sent out to the Taiwan independent forces so as to avoid damaging China-US cooperation and cross-strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1587407.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1587320.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-24","Lu Kang","","A US senator has said that he is preparing a legislation to force Taiwan allies to stay with Taiwan and not change their so-called \"diplomatic ties\" to China. Do you have any comment on this?","While some US politicians are making these jarring noises on the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and El Salvador, the President and government of El Salvador have made public statements, declaring that their decision meets the trend of the times and the fundamental interests of the Salvadoran people. I am convinced that the Salvadoran people knows the best what is in their own interests.\nWe hope that the relevant country could respect other sovereign states' right to choose and formulate their foreign policies and stop interfering in other countries' domestic affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1588050.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1587984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-27","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, a \"lawmaker\" from Taiwan's Democratic Progressive Party said on social media that it was because the mainland accepted El Salvador's request to provide over 27 billion dollars that El Salvador established diplomatic relations with the mainland. What is your comment?","China and El Salvador established diplomatic relations on the basis of the one-China principle, which accords with the international law and basic norms governing international relations. It is justified and aboveboard. The Salvadorian government just made the same right choice as the UN and other 177 countries already did. The one-China principle is by no means a bargaining chip, and will never become one.\nWhen establishing diplomatic relations with China, the Salvadorian side never proposed any economic preconditions. There is no such thing as the so-called \"bargaining\". The relevant person who claimed the so-called \"checkbook diplomacy\" is fabricating something out of thin air, deceiving himself and judging others by himself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1588564.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1588439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-08-28","Hua Chunying","","Former Commander-in-Chief of the US Pacific Command Dennis Cutler Blair recently said that both Taiwan and Japan took the Chinese People's Liberation Army's activities in international waters near their \"territory\" as a threat. Taiwan should try to conduct simulated attacks to improve its combat readiness while the aircraft carrier Liaoning sails nearby. What's your comment?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. I wonder whether this former senior official from the US military is trying to help or harm the Taiwan side by offering such advice? If you are interested in what military implications his advice may have, I would advise you to follow what our defense ministry will say at their press briefing the day after tomorrow.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1589014.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1588848.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-08-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 28 (reporter: Liu Huan). Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 28th that recently, all localities and departments have continuously stepped up efforts to implement the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation” (hereinafter the “31 Measures”), and have made positive progress. Recently, Jiangxi Province, Shandong Province, Chongqing Municipality and Fuzhou City have issued specific implementation measures suited to local conditions.\n——On August 8, the “Implementation Measures for Jiangxi Province's Implementation of the ‘Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation’” were officially issued, with a total of 60 specific measures, providing Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots in Jiangxi with treatment equal to local residents in investment, entrepreneurship, employment, study and daily life.\nFirst, respond practically to demands. Clear rules and preferences are set for issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, such as children's schooling and medical services. Enrollment of Taiwan students in Jiangxi is arranged by the education department, giving them the same admission treatment as local students; they take Jiangxi's secondary school entrance examinations and the general college entrance examinations and enjoy preferential bonus-point policies. Taiwan compatriots and their family members enjoy equal medical and health services, and a “green channel” will be opened for them, among other measures.\nSecond, add a number of new measures. Building on the implementation of the “31 Measures,” the effort to benefit Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots has been increased, with 24 new measures added. In attracting talent, the recruitment of Taiwan-invested enterprises and the cultivation of high-level talent are included in the scope of applications for Jiangxi Province's “Double Thousand Plan” for introducing and cultivating high-level innovation and entrepreneurship talent; qualifying projects are recommended for support from the provincial talent innovation and entrepreneurship guidance fund. In expanding markets, local Taiwan-invested export enterprises are supported in making full use of rules-of-origin preferences to open international markets, among other measures.\nThird, highlight Jiangxi's characteristics. Regularly, in conjunction with activities such as the “Precision Service for Taiwan Enterprises Month,” the “Hundred Banks Enter Thousand Enterprises” targeted financial assistance programs will hold government-bank-enterprise matchmaking meetings for Taiwan enterprises. Qualifying Taiwan enterprises will be included in the scope of recognition for “Jiangxi Famous Brand Products”; local Taiwan enterprises are helped to ship exports via the Gan-Europe freight train; Taiwan compatriots who live long-term in Jiangxi may use their Taiwan compatriot permits to obtain local annual tourism passes, and qualifying Taiwan compatriots may enjoy free or half-price admission to scenic spots, among other measures.\nFourth, increase opening-up. Services are strengthened in creating a tax and business environment and establishing a Jiangxi Cross-Strait Commercial Arbitration Center, among other areas. Businesspeople from Taiwan are given priority in invitations to participate in special investment promotion activities of Jiangxi state-owned enterprises, and key projects are selected each year for introduction to Taiwan businesspeople. In addition, new clear provisions have been made regarding home-purchase eligibility for Taiwan compatriots, the “Five Social Insurances and One Housing Fund,” and other matters.\n——On August 15, Shandong Province issued and implemented the “Several Measures on Promoting Lu-Taiwan Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” covering three areas, economic cooperation, cultural exchanges, and study, entrepreneurship, employment and daily life of Taiwan compatriots in Shandong, with 56 specific measures in total.\nIn promoting Lu-Taiwan economic cooperation, regional headquarters and functional headquarters of newly established Taiwan-invested enterprises that are reviewed and recognized will receive a one-time reward of 5 million yuan from the Shandong provincial government; Taiwan private capital is supported in jointly establishing equity investment funds and industrial investment funds with state-owned capital in Shandong, and Taiwan-invested enterprises are supported in participating in infrastructure construction such as Shandong expressways and rail transit through franchise operation; Taiwan scientific researchers employed by units within Shandong Province may serve as provincial science and technology program project leaders, enjoying the same policies as Shandong researchers.\nIn cultural exchange and cooperation, Taiwan compatriots, universities, research institutions and civil associations are encouraged to take part in undertaking Shandong cultural projects and cultural industry projects, enjoying the same industrial policies as local enterprises; scholarships and grants are added to attract Taiwan students to study at Shandong universities; Shandong's literary and arts troupes and research institutions may hire Taiwan literary and arts workers and Taiwan youth for employment, teaching and study; and high-level talent in Taiwan Confucian studies is actively attracted to Shandong to carry out Confucian research and dissemination work.\nIn facilitating life and protecting the rights and interests that Taiwan compatriots should enjoy, the schooling of Taiwan compatriots' children and medical practice by Taiwan compatriots are coordinated and managed, and Taiwan compatriots are clearly guaranteed equal treatment in paying and using the housing provident fund, purchasing self-use housing, taking professional qualification examinations, and various living services.\nShandong Province will also soon issue local legislative regulations to protect and promote the investment rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, clarifying and guaranteeing the rights that Taiwan compatriots should enjoy at the legal level.\nIn addition, Weifang City in Shandong Province issued and implemented 80 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots on August 6, striving to create more convenience and provide more preferences for Taiwan businesspeople to invest and start businesses, for Taiwan enterprises to transform and upgrade, for Taiwan compatriots to live, and for Taiwan youth to find jobs and start businesses.\n——On August 21, Chongqing Municipality issued and implemented the “Several Measures on Promoting Yu-Taiwan Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” covering five areas: economic exchanges and cooperation; social and cultural exchanges and cooperation; study and internship, employment and entrepreneurship, and residence and daily life for Taiwan compatriots locally, with 58 measures in total.\nIn economic exchanges and cooperation, local Taiwan enterprises are supported in listing on the Chongqing regional equity market in accordance with the law; the Chongqing Equities Transfer Center is supported in providing services for Taiwan enterprises' non-public offerings and transfers of enterprise shares; Taiwan enterprises are encouraged to transfer to Chongqing industries and participate in the construction of the “Belt and Road” and the development of the Yangtze River Economic Belt; and cooperation on intellectual property protection between Chongqing and Taiwan is strengthened, protecting the intellectual property of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises.\nIn social and cultural exchanges and cooperation, Taiwan compatriots are encouraged to carry out cultural exchange activities combined with Chongqing's outstanding cultural heritage and take part in the protection and transmission of intangible cultural heritage projects; Taiwan compatriots are supported in enjoying public cultural services on an equal footing, and encouraged to found various cultural enterprises and enjoy related local policies on an equal footing; and cross-Strait scientific research institutions, higher education institutions and enterprises are encouraged to establish cross-Strait cooperative research and development institutions.\nIn study and internship for Taiwan compatriots, a Chongqing-Taiwan talent training cooperation mechanism is established, encouraging high-quality Taiwan vocational schools to cooperate with Chongqing vocational schools and vocational education institutions in carrying out vocational skills training and joint talent cultivation; the children of Taiwan compatriots pay the same tuition as the children of local residents and enjoy the policy of reduced score requirements for admission in the high school entrance examination.\nIn employment and entrepreneurship for Taiwan compatriots, professional talent from Taiwan is encouraged and assisted in applying for the national “Thousand Talents Plan” and “Ten Thousand Talents Plan” and Chongqing key talent projects; Taiwan compatriots are supported in investing in local medical institutions and opening individual clinics in accordance with the law; Taiwan youth start-up enterprises are supported in moving into various youth innovation spaces and listing on the Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Board; and Taiwan compatriots are supported in founding elderly care service institutions.\nIn residence and daily life for Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan compatriots who live long-term locally are supported in participating in community services, sitting in on local CPPCC meetings, and joining community organizations; a liaison window is set up at the Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office to provide emergency assistance to local Taiwan compatriots, and a “green channel” for emergency assistance is opened at designated hospitals.\n——On August 12, Fuzhou City issued the “Implementation Opinions on Carrying Out the ‘Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,’” covering four areas with 68 specific measures.\nIn economic and trade cooperation, for newly established Taiwan-invested enterprises that conform to Fuzhou's industrial plan and environmental protection plan and whose annual actual Taiwan capital paid-in amount reaches US$5 million or more, a reward is given at 1.5% of the actual paid-in amount converted to renminbi, with a maximum reward of 10 million yuan; Taiwan enterprises apply the relevant land-use policies on the same basis as local enterprises; and Taiwan enterprises may participate in franchise projects in public service fields such as Fuzhou expressways and rail transit, among others.\nIn internships, employment and entrepreneurship, each year a “Rooted in Rong City” competition for outstanding entrepreneurial projects is held, selecting 10% of outstanding Taiwan youth entrepreneurial projects; Taiwan compatriots holding a bachelor's degree or above (including from Taiwan universities) may apply for relevant public institution positions in Fuzhou; and a Fuzhou Taiwan Talent Service Workstation is established to provide services for high-level Taiwan talent, among others.\nIn culture and exchanges, local Taiwan compatriots are encouraged to take part in projects such as cultural heritage protection and other projects for the inheritance and development of excellent Chinese culture; Taiwan compatriots are encouraged and supported in applying to establish privately run museums, among others.\nIn settling down and working in peace, local Taiwan compatriots may enjoy same-city treatment; in down payment ratios, time limits for handling, and loan applications for purchasing self-occupied housing, they enjoy equal treatment. Taiwan compatriots working in Fuzhou may participate in the “Five Social Insurances and One Housing Fund” in accordance with the rules and enjoy the same labor security and medical and health services as local residents; Taiwan compatriots may be evaluated for Fuzhou municipal model workers, “May Fourth Youth Medals,” “March 8th Red Banner Bearers,” outstanding representatives of employment and entrepreneurship, honorary citizens and other honorary titles.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201808/t20180828_12052551.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-08-30","Hua Chunying","","In response to the Civil Aviation Administration of China's demand to classify \"Taiwan\" as \"Taiwan, China\", the United Airlines' website shows that mainland, Taiwan and Hong Kong can be selected as locations according to the currency. The spokesperson of the department in Taiwan in charge of so-called \"foreign affairs\" expressed appreciation for such \"flexible workaround\". What is your comment?","I would refer you to the Civil Aviation Administration for details as they are in charge of this specific issue.\nI just want to stress that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. This is the objective fact, common sense and international consensus. It lays out a basic principle for foreign companies operating in China to follow. However flexible they may try to get, there is simply no way to sidestep the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1589844.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1589700.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-08-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Dennis Blair, retired commander of the former U.S. Pacific Command, wrote a signed article saying that Japan and Taiwan should not continue to intercept the Chinese military’s vessels and aircraft. Instead, they should engage in the tit-for-tat reciprocal actions. He suggested Japan and Taiwan patrol the coastal areas of the Chinese mainland or launch simulated attacks on the aircraft carrier Liaoning…","The suggestions mentioned above provoke cross-Strait military confrontation and destroy the China-Japan relationship. They are irresponsible and also very dangerous. Taiwan is an integral part of China. Any attempt by Taiwan to resist reunification through force and violence is overrated and will get Taiwan nowhere.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-08/31/content_4823736.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2018-09-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Some Taiwan operators have said that if Taiwan residents apply for residence permits in the mainland, they may in the future have to pay global individual income tax in the mainland. Please explain. Ma Xiaoguang said that he noted the relevant situation and gave the above response.","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180901_12054018.htm","",1,3,2,""],[0,"2018-09-05","Hua Chunying","","It is reported that the Nauru side has created much hassle for the Chinese delegation attending the 30th Pacific Islands Forum in that country. Could you talk a bit more about that?","The 30th Pacific Islands Forum (PIF) Leaders Session with Forum Dialogue Partners was held on September 4 in Nauru, a country that has the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities. At the invitation of the PIF Secretariat, China attended the meeting as a Forum Dialogue Partner.\nHowever, the host country Nauru went against international practices and the PIF regulations and staged a despicable farce. Before the meeting, Nauru asked the Chinese delegation to travel on regular passports. After many PIF members and the Chinese side lodged representations and said that they would boycott the meeting, Nauru had to agree with the Chinese delegation's request to visit on diplomatic passports. During the meeting, Nauru disrespected international practices again and obstructed the Chinese delegation's speech. The Chinese side immediately lodged stern representations and walked out of the meeting in protest. Many delegations from other attending countries also left the meeting to express their strong dissatisfaction with Nauru.\nIt must be pointed out that the one-China principle is part of the well-recognized norms governing international relations and a consensus shared by the international community. Any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will be rejected and is doomed to fail. Our advice for Nauru is that it should have a clear grasp of the overarching trend, correct its mistakes and stop working against the trend of the times.\nChina attaches importance to its relations with the Pacific Islands countries and the PIF and will continue to strengthen friendly exchanges and practical cooperation with the Pacific Islands countries on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1592240.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1592093.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-09-05","Hua Chunying","","据报道，日前在瑙鲁举行的第30届太平洋岛国论坛会期间，瑙鲁方面曾多方干扰中方代表团与会，请问你能否介绍有关情况?","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1592240.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1592093.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2018-09-10","Geng Shuang","","据报道，美国国务院上周宣布召回驻多米尼加、萨尔瓦多和巴拿马三国高级外交官。三国此前都已与台湾“断交”并与中华人民共和国建交。中方对此有何回应？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1593694.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2018-09-11","Geng Shuang","","据台湾媒体报道，日前，日本一右翼组织代表脚踢台南的慰安妇铜像。你对此有何评论？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1594045.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Regarding the mainland’s issuance of residence permits to Taiwan residents, the DPP authorities claim this is a unilateral mainland “united front” move affecting Taiwan’s “security,” and are drafting so-called “countermeasures.” What comment do you have on this?","Issuing Taiwan Resident Residence Permits is a good thing that facilitates Taiwan compatriots in studying, working, and living on the mainland. The purpose of introducing this policy is to implement General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important exposition on work concerning Taiwan, to act in accordance with the principle of “governing for the people,” to implement the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” to resolutely and unswervingly seek well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and to do good deeds and practical things for Taiwan compatriots. It is an important step in taking the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and implementing “equal treatment,” and it is a concrete measure that actively responds to the demands of broad Taiwan compatriots, relieves the difficulties and problems of Taiwan compatriots, and genuinely resolves practical difficulties and problems that have troubled Taiwan compatriots for many years. It should be explained that:\n1. The Taiwan Resident Residence Permit is different from the mainland resident identity card. The Taiwan Resident Residence Permit is an identity document used by Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. It aims to address the convenience of daily life matters such as food, clothing, housing, and transportation for Taiwan compatriots in studying, working, and living on the mainland, and does not involve any adjustment of political rights and obligations. 2. Applying for a Taiwan Resident Residence Permit does not require holding a mainland household registration, nor does it require giving up one’s Taiwan household registration. 3. The application for a Taiwan Resident Residence Permit fully adopts the principle of voluntariness; whether to apply is entirely up to Taiwan compatriots themselves, and there are no mandatory requirements.\nIn sum, the significance of this policy lies in convenience and benefit to the people: allowing permit holders from Taiwan to enjoy the three rights, six basic public services, and nine conveniences provided by the state and their place of residence, and to enjoy equal treatment. No matter what good things the mainland does for Taiwan compatriots, the DPP authorities will deliberately distort, slander, restrict, and obstruct them; this is determined by the very nature of the DPP.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058926.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","Please introduce the latest progress and highlights of localities and departments in implementing the \"31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.\"","Since the \"Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation\" (i.e., the \"31 Measures\") were issued and implemented, various regions and departments have continued to accelerate their efforts to implement them, and continuous positive progress has been made. During the summer, we have already introduced four times the specific implementation measures issued by relevant departments and provinces and municipalities. Today, I would like to introduce some new developments to everyone.\nOn September 3, Sichuan Province issued and implemented the \"Several Measures on Promoting Sichuan-Taiwan Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,\" comprising 70 specific measures that provide Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as local residents in expanding economic and trade cooperation, providing policy support, and strengthening people-to-people and cultural exchanges. On August 28, Huzhou City in Zhejiang Province issued the \"Implementing Measures of Huzhou City for Carrying Out the 'Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,'\" introducing 60 specific measures in four areas: investment and economic and trade cooperation, entrepreneurship and employment, cultural exchanges, and living conditions. On September 10, Zhuhai City in Guangdong Province issued the \"Several Measures on Promoting Zhuhai-Taiwan Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,\" introducing 52 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots in four areas: deepening economic and trade cooperation, promoting social and cultural exchanges, supporting Taiwan compatriots in studying, interning, employment, and entrepreneurship, and facilitating their residence and daily life.\nIn addition, in terms of cross-Strait film and television exchanges and cooperation, the number of Taiwan personalities participating in mainland radio and television programs has increased. Radio and television administrative departments in Beijing, Shanghai, Xinjiang, and other places have received intentions for co-production from multiple production companies, and a number of Taiwan production companies are actively preparing to co-produce TV dramas and TV documentaries with the mainland. In terms of Taiwan compatriots joining mainland professional industry associations, several Taiwan compatriots have successively joined the China Writers Association, the China Artists Association, and the China Dramatists Association, participating in mainland cultural development and cross-Strait cultural exchanges. In terms of making it convenient for Taiwan compatriots to apply for jobs on the mainland, recruitment websites such as Zhaopin, 51job, and 58.com have opened interfaces for Taiwan, and Taiwan compatriots can register and log in directly with their mobile phone numbers and enjoy the same job-seeking and employment environment as mainland compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058924.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Reports say that the so-called “Olympic name-correction referendum,” promoted by “Taiwan independence” forces on the island, has reached the signature threshold, and the DPP authorities have provided considerable support. What is your comment?","The IOC has clear provisions on Taiwan's participation in the Olympic Games. The “Olympic model” is a principle that international sports organizations and sports circles on both sides of the Strait follow together. A very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island, with the support and tolerance of the DPP authorities, have ignored the solemn warnings of the IOC and the East Asian Olympic Committee and stubbornly pushed ahead, escalating the “Olympic name-change referendum.” In the end, this will only sacrifice the competition opportunities of Taiwan's athletes and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058922.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","After the residence permit is introduced, will the function of the Taiwan Compatriot Permit be weakened? The residence permit has a validity period of five years. If Taiwan compatriots return to Taiwan or go to work and live in other provinces or cities on the mainland within five years, will they need to reapply for the permit? In addition, will there be situations where holders of residence permits cannot enjoy…","I would like to clarify one point here: the Taiwan residence permit is an identity document that facilitates Taiwan compatriots in studying, working and living on the mainland, while the Taiwan Compatriot Permit is a travel document for Taiwan compatriots traveling to and from the mainland. The residence permit and the Taiwan Compatriot Permit are two documents that exist side by side; the residence permit does not replace the Taiwan Compatriot Permit. After the residence permit officially takes effect, it will not affect the original functions of the Taiwan Compatriot Permit, nor will it affect the rights and interests Taiwan compatriots previously enjoyed with the Taiwan Compatriot Permit.\nDuring the validity period of the residence permit, if a Taiwan compatriot returns to Taiwan and then returns to their mainland residence or relocates, the permit remains valid. The various rights, public services and conveniences provided by the state and carried on the residence permit can be enjoyed in all provinces and municipalities on the mainland and will not be affected by geographic location. Rights, public services and conveniences provided by the place of residence are handled according to the regulations of each locality when outside the place of residence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","The Taiwan authorities claim that the mainland, through issuing residence permits, is collecting personal data and fingerprint information of Taiwan residents. What is the spokesperson’s response?","The Taiwan residence permits issued this time have built-in chips and registered fingerprints, mainly for the convenience of using the documents and for preventing impersonation. In the information age, such practices are very common; mainland residents' ID cards also have similar requirements. On the one hand, this approach can effectively use existing resident ID card readers for rapid verification, enabling permit holders to conveniently take trains and airplanes, check into hotels, and handle financial business. On the other hand, it can also prevent the documents from being impersonated by people with ulterior motives, which would harm the rights and interests of permit holders. At the same time, the chip technology used in the residence permits is very advanced and can effectively protect the personal information stored on the chip from being stolen or leaked. Taiwan compatriots may rest assured on this point.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058925.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Since residence permit applications began on September 1, roughly how many Taiwan residents have applied for residence permits? The second question: Previously, after the typhoon and earthquake in Japan, many Taiwan compatriots received assistance from mainland embassy personnel abroad to get out of difficulty, which caused much discussion in Taiwan. Many people in Taiwan feel that the relevant Taiwan…","On the first question, after the “Measures for the Application and Issuance of Residence Permits for Residents of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan” were announced, they were warmly welcomed and affirmed by a broad range of Taiwan compatriots, and reactions in all quarters have been very enthusiastic. Since the “Measures” took concrete effect on September 1, Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life, including Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan officials, young Taiwan entrepreneurs, Taiwan teachers and Taiwan students, have been very eager to apply. In some places there have even been instances of “grabbing the first spot,” and in some places a family of nine and two brothers’ families have applied together. According to incomplete statistics, as of September 10, in just 10 days, more than 22,000 Taiwan compatriots had applied for residence permits. This also fully shows that the Taiwan residence permit is a truly beneficial policy that serves the people and is widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the second question, I have also seen related reports from the island. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and my Consulate General in Osaka have already introduced the specific circumstances at that time, and some of the Taiwan compatriots involved have also explained the matter through social media. I think that at such a critical moment, it is clear who was quietly doing things for Taiwan compatriots and who was shirking responsibility, spreading rumors and slandering others. The clear will be clear, and the murky will be murky. I want to stress that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. No matter where Taiwan compatriots are overseas and no matter what difficulties they encounter, the motherland is their firm backing. We will provide assistance, shelter them from wind and rain at critical moments, relieve their worries and help them resolve their practical problems.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Please spokesperson introduce the relevant cross-Strait exchange activities this summer. Thank you.","To further expand and deepen economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, a series of colorful exchange activities with notable highlights have been launched this summer by all sectors on both sides. In terms of economic and trade exchanges, since July this year, eight provinces and municipalities, namely Tianjin, Gansu, Guizhou, Hubei, Beijing, Jiangxi, Shandong and Hebei, have successively held Taiwan-related economic and trade exchange activities. More than 4,000 person-times from Taiwan's industrial and commercial circles attended, and over 190 Taiwan-invested business projects and agreements were signed, with a contract value of over 75 billion yuan, playing a positive role in expanding and deepening economic exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait. Next, from September 12 to 17, Zhejiang Province will hold the 2018 Zhejiang-Taiwan Cooperation Week, which will be attended by Taiwan political and business figures including Wu Boxiong, Jiang Bingkun, Wang Wenyuan and Lai Zhengyi. From September 27 to 28, the 15th Cross-Strait Forum on Information Industry and Technology Standards will be held in various places in Anhui. Relevant institutions, well-known enterprises, and experts and scholars from both sides will conduct practical discussions on cooperation in technology standards across ten fields, including mobile communications and intelligent manufacturing. Journalist friends are welcome to cover the event at that time.\nIn youth exchanges, our office organized more than 300 Taiwan students studying on the mainland and some students from universities in Taiwan to carry out summer internships at multiple large state-owned enterprises and well-known private enterprises across the mainland. The ARATS invited 739 Taiwanese young students in 16 batches to participate in Chinese culture study camps in various places on the mainland. The All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises organized more than 290 Taiwanese university students to visit and exchange in Beijing, Shanghai and other places. More than 760 Taiwanese young people took summer internship positions offered by 20 financial institutions on the mainland. In July, activities including the Cross-Strait Youth Exchange and Cooperation Beijing Summit, the 2018 Thousand-Person Summer Camp for Taiwan Compatriot Youth, the final of the 3rd Beijing-Taiwan Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition, and the Taiwan Youth New Economy Study Camp were successfully held in Beijing. Guangzhou, Kunshan and other places also actively organized Taiwanese university students to carry out summer internships locally.\nIn cultural exchanges, the “Seminar on Education on the History of the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance and Inheritance of the Anti-War Spirit” was held in Wuhan, Hubei, with nearly 300 attendees, including retired generals, experts and scholars from both sides, and university and secondary school students from both sides. Activities including the “Forum Commemorating the 30th Anniversary of Cross-Strait Publishing Exchanges,” “Qiantang Cross-Strait Cultural Friendship Tour,” “Cultural Study Camp for Taiwan History Teachers in Chinese Culture,” “Cross-Strait Youth Hui Culture Exchange Month,” “Hunan Cultural Journey,” and “Cross-Strait University Students' Photography Journey along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road” were successfully held in various places.\nIn sports exchanges, from July 18 to 24, the Cross-Strait Sports Exchange Games were held in Beijing. A total of 4,000 people from both sides of the Strait, including 1,800 Taiwanese young students and members of the public, took part in the competition, the largest civil sports exchange activity across the Taiwan Strait to date. The 2nd Cross-Strait Wushu Exchange Conference and the Cross-Strait (Dezhou) Bajiquan Skills Exchange Conference were held in Shijiazhuang, Hebei, and Dezhou, Shandong, respectively. The 2018 “5th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao University Student Sports Exchange Games” was held at Fudan University in Shanghai, with 1,200 university students from both sides participating. The second round of the 2nd Cross-Strait Student Baseball League (Taiwan) was held in Taichung, with more than 270 student baseball players from 10 mainland universities traveling to Taiwan to compete.\nIn addition, in education, science and technology, community, ethnic minority and many other fields, a large number of exchange activities in diverse forms and lively formats have also been successively held.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","环球时报环球网记者","We note that in response to the establishment of China–El Salvador diplomatic relations, the US has recently taken a series of so-called “pro-Taiwan” measures, hoping to help Taiwan consolidate its “diplomatic allies,” and the DPP authorities have expressed gratitude for the US approach. What comment do you have on this?","On the question of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador, in response to groundless accusations from the United States, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has repeatedly stated its position. I would like to reiterate that the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador is a correct decision made by El Salvador in accordance with its own national and people's interests. The remarks and actions of the United States crudely interfere in the internal affairs of other countries, and also seriously violate the one-China policy and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués that it has committed to. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers to boost their own standing, will ultimately reap the bitter fruit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058917.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","香港大公文汇传媒集团全媒体记者","According to reports, Chen Shui-bian recently said in an interview with Japanese media that, facing the mainland's strong pressure, Taiwan should hold a referendum as soon as possible, and he stated that Taiwan “does not want to become part of China.” What comment do you have?","The two sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. This historical and legal fact is beyond doubt and absolutely not permitted to change. Chen Shui-bian, while in office in Taiwan, stubbornly pursued the evil path of “Taiwan independence,” and in the end was ruined in reputation and career, forced to admit that “‘Taiwan independence’ cannot be done, and that is that.” Now, however, he is again inciting the DPP authorities to “do what is known to be impossible,” which is truly absurd and laughable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058919.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Recently, an incident in which representatives of a Japanese right-wing organization kicked a bronze statue of “comfort women” on Taiwan island has drawn public attention and angered the Taiwan public, who have denounced Japan and demanded an apology. What comment does the spokesperson have on this incident?","We have also noted that this matter has already aroused public indignation on the island. Such clownish antics will, of course, meet with unanimous condemnation and joint boycott by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The forcible recruitment of “comfort women” was a grave crime against humanity committed by Japanese militarism during World War II. Those who distort historical facts, seek to justify Japanese militarism's brutality, or even glorify its acts of aggression are challenging the moral bottom line of humanity. I think that attitudes on matters of right and wrong are both a touchstone for various political figures and a mirror that reveals the good and evil of human nature.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","海峡卫视记者","Some young Taiwanese who have come to the Mainland to develop have proposed the “Six Principles for Taiwan Youth in the New Era,” including “rely on yourself, stay grounded, do not speculate, develop together, promote integration, and embrace the future.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have also noted that in recent years, as the mainland has developed and progressed, and as we have continually introduced policies and measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, more and more Taiwan youth have chosen to come to the mainland to develop. While realizing their life aspirations, they have also linked their personal futures with the development of the times and with the future and destiny of the country and nation. This is commendable. The “six principles for Taiwan youth in the new era” you just mentioned reflect the genuine feelings of Taiwan youth developing on the mainland. They include the tangible sense of gain from enjoying the various measures the mainland offers to Taiwan, as well as their pragmatic and enterprising side, and they also contain their beautiful aspirations for the future. We are glad to see more Taiwan youth come to the mainland to develop, and we will continue to introduce more measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots to help Taiwan youth achieve greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","中央广电总台央视“中国新闻”记者","Recently, the “pro-independence” group “Happy Island Alliance” (“喜乐岛联盟”) held a press conference advocating changing the “Republic of China” to “Taiwan” through a referendum, and stated that it will mobilize 100,000 people to march on October 20. What comments do you have on this?","Not a single inch of the motherland's territory can ever be, or ever will be, split away from China. We will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” forces stirring up trouble, and no “Taiwan independence” scheme will succeed. “Taiwan independence” will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots, not happiness and joy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058921.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","北京日报记者","Lai Ching-te, head of Taiwan's executive branch, recently declared that next year policy will be set to promote English as Taiwan's second “official language,” making Taiwan a so-called “bilingual country.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","No matter what tricks the DPP authorities play with the various policies they are currently pursuing on the island, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they stop the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","At the start of the school year in September, Taiwan’s MAC sent a letter to Taiwan’s education authorities and universities, stating that it has established a “Taiwanese students studying in mainland China zone” and asking universities to remind students to pay attention to the risks of developing careers on the mainland. Commentators on the island believe this move is full of political implications. What is the…","As I mentioned in answering the previous question, many young students in Taiwan now choose to study at mainland schools in order to find better development opportunities and larger development space and to realize their life dreams. This reflects both the aspirations of the people and the trend of the times. Youth are the future and hope of the nation and society. What we should do is provide young people with better opportunities and create greater space for their development. If artificial obstacles are set up to obstruct and restrict young people's greater development opportunities, this will only hurt young people and drive their hearts away.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Please spokesperson introduce the achievements of the cross-Strait youth innovation bases and demonstration sites. Thank you.","To help Taiwan youth come to the mainland for internships, employment, and entrepreneurship, since 2015 the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has granted plaques to establish 76 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases and Demonstration Sites in 20 provinces and municipalities. These bases and demonstration sites take diverse forms. Some are industrial parks, makerspaces, or enterprises, while others are universities, media organizations, or social groups. They play an active role in providing Taiwan youth with employment and entrepreneurship guidance, training, and policy interpretation; helping them connect with markets, resources, and internship and job opportunities; providing entrepreneurship financing support; and offering supporting services in policy and legal consultation, patent and technology applications, and financial and tax consulting. In particular, some of the bases and demonstration sites are operated by Taiwan youth, who have consistently introduced the mainland’s employment and entrepreneurship environment to young people on the island and helped Taiwan youth develop in local areas, doing much to promote cross-Strait youth exchange and cooperation. According to statistics, as of the first half of 2018, more than 10,000 Taiwan youth had interned, worked, or started businesses at these bases and demonstration sites, and more than 70,000 person-times of Taiwan youth had participated in various exchange activities they hosted. Meanwhile, with the support of local governments, these bases and demonstration sites have become important platforms for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland, and a preliminary concentration of Taiwan youth has formed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180912_12058923.htm"],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","There is news that, in response to the residence permit policy introduced by the mainland, the Taiwan authorities have launched so-called “law amendments” that will penalize Taiwan compatriots who apply for residence permits. What comment does the spokesperson have on this? Another question: The Mainland Affairs Council claims that by exchanging personal financial information of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan…","As I mentioned at the beginning, on matters concerning the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, the mainland side has always adhered to the concept of “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” listened carefully to the voices of Taiwan compatriots, actively responded to their demands, and done practical good deeds for them. Yet some people in Taiwan always look at this with disapproval and, with a confrontational mindset and contrarian psychology, harshly criticize it. The DPP authorities have repeatedly threatened, intimidated, obstructed and restricted, which in effect spoils good things for Taiwan compatriots.\nOn your second question, as far as I understand, the tax status and tax obligations of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are determined under the newly revised Individual Income Tax Law, its Implementing Regulations and related normative documents. Interpretation authority rests with the competent tax authorities, so for specific matters, I suggest you consult the competent authorities.\nI want to emphasize that whether one applies for a Taiwan Residence Permit and the relevant tax rules have no corresponding relationship. Taiwan compatriots will not change their tax status or tax obligations on the mainland merely because they applied for the Taiwan Residence Permit, nor will they bear an obligation to pay tax on global income in the mainland merely because they received the permit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","环球网记者","First question: Soong Chu-yu, chairman of the People First Party, recently stated publicly that he has told the office of Taiwan's leader that he has no intention of again serving as Taiwan's representative at the APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting. There are reports that Morris Chang, founder of TSMC, will attend this year's APEC. Could the spokesperson comment on this? Second question: To address the difficulties…","Regarding Taiwan's participation in APEC-related activities, our position is very clear: it must conform to the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding. This has been our consistent position.\nOn the second question, I recall that not long ago, Director Liu Jieyi, when accepting media interviews at the water supply ceremony in Kinmen, said that both sides of the Strait are one family, and there should be free, mutual and frequent exchanges, with ever closer ties. It should not be limited to the \"Three Links\"; it should be fully opened.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","新华社记者","On September 6, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council published a so-called “Report on the Results of Responding to the Mainland's 31 Measures Targeting Taiwan,” claiming that the “31 Measures” are united front measures of the mainland, that they lure Taiwan residents with benefits, and that there has been no obvious impact since implementation. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Two sentences. The first: “The hearts of the common people have a scale.” Whether the series of measures launched by the mainland are good or bad for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, and whether they are opportunities or so-called challenges and risks, I believe that broad Taiwan compatriots and enterprises understand this very clearly.\nThe second: “The eyes of the masses are bright as snow.” This year we not only launched the “31 measures,” but also realized water supply to Kinmen, canceled the employment permits for Taiwan residents coming to work on the mainland, and issued residence permits to Taiwan residents. Who is doing good deeds for Taiwan compatriots and who is undermining their good deeds—Taiwan compatriots will make their own judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","北京日报记者","Some media report that Eswatini, the only country that did not send representatives to the China-Africa forum, is preparing to establish diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China and sever its so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. Please share the spokesperson's view.","The one-China principle is the broad consensus of the international community, and also the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-12","An Fengshan","台湾东森新闻云记者","Some time ago, because of the so-called “name-correction referendum,” the East Asian Youth Games that were originally scheduled to be held in Taichung next year were cancelled. Now Taiwan wants to hold a sporting event called the Asia-Pacific Youth Games. What is the spokesperson's view? If the mainland is invited to send a delegation to attend, will the mainland send participants?","I have not heard of the sports event you mentioned. It should not be a sports event recognized by international sports organizations. Adhering to the Olympic model recognized by the international community is the fundamental way to safeguard the interests of Taiwan athletes and the sports community. Attempting to use sports events to seek political gains and achieve political aims will ultimately be futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180912_12058957.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-09-13","Geng Shuang","","据报道，台湾官员称，中国和梵蒂冈将很快就相互承认达成协议。中方能否证实？对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1594827.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2018-09-16","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","(Xinhua) Beijing, September 16 — Spokesperson An Fengshan of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council responded to questions on the 16th, saying that, according to our understanding from relevant departments, for some time Taiwan's intelligence agencies have targeted the mainland, vigorously stepping up intelligence theft and infiltration and sabotage activities. For this reason, national security organs have organized special crackdown operations. We demand that relevant Taiwan authorities immediately stop their infiltration and sabotage activities against the mainland, so as to avoid further harm to the increasingly complex and severe cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180916_12060510.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-09-25","Geng Shuang","","据报道，9月25日美国国防部下属防务安全局通知美国会，计划向台湾出售总值约3.3亿美元的武器装备，包括军机零部件和相关后勤支持等。请问中方对此有何评论?","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1598527.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[1,"2018-09-25","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reported that the US is selling weapons and equipment to Taiwan worth about US$330 million in total, including aircraft parts and related support systems. What comment does the Chinese military have?","On September 25, the US government notified Congress of its decision to sell weapons and equipment to Taiwan worth a total of about 330 million US dollars. The Chinese military expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. We firmly oppose US arms sales to Taiwan. The US side's conduct seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, interferes in China's internal affairs, damages China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously undermines the relations between the two countries' armed forces and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe determination and will of the Chinese military to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity are firm and unwavering. We strongly demand that the US side strictly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately revoke the relevant arms sales projects to Taiwan, and stop selling weapons to Taiwan and military contacts between the US and Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to China-US military relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2018-09/25/content_4825699.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2018-09-26","Geng Shuang","","关于上周末中国与梵蒂冈签署的协议，你能否透露更多细节？协议中是否提到了梵蒂冈与台湾的关系？是否制定了中国希望梵蒂冈与台湾“断交”并与大陆建交的时间表？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1599062.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the latest progress made by localities and departments in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”","After we issued the “31 measures” in February to promote cross-Strait economic, cultural exchanges and cooperation, all regions and departments have earnestly and comprehensively implemented them and successively rolled out specific measures. To date, 30 localities in 13 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities have issued additional specific measures tailored to their own regions and departments, which have been widely recognized and welcomed by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. Here I would like to introduce the latest progress in several provinces and cities.\nOn September 12, Jiangsu Province issued the “Implementing Opinions on Deepening Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Jiangsu and Taiwan,” covering four areas, namely supporting the quality improvement and efficiency enhancement of Taiwan-invested enterprises, expanding talent exchanges and cooperation between Jiangsu and Taiwan, deepening social and cultural integration between the two sides, and providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots who come to Jiangsu to study, work, start businesses or live, for a total of 76 measures. On the same day, Yancheng City in Jiangsu Province also issued “Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Yancheng and Taiwan,” which offer 50 specific measures in three areas: promoting economic and trade cooperation between Yancheng and Taiwan, enhancing people-to-people exchanges between the two sides, and creating convenient living conditions for Taiwan compatriots.\nOn September 15, Shaanxi Province published the “Implementing Opinions on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation between Shaanxi and Taiwan,” which offer 60 specific measures covering economic cooperation, cultural exchanges, encouragement of entrepreneurship and employment, and convenience in study and daily life between Shaanxi and Taiwan.\nOn September 13, Jiaxing City in Zhejiang Province issued the “Implementing Measures for Jiaxing City to Carry Out the Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation,” which include 48 measures in three areas: vigorously promoting the construction of high-quality Taiwan-invested industrial clusters, encouraging and supporting Taiwan compatriots to start businesses and undertake innovation in Jiaxing, and working to create an environment in which Taiwan compatriots can settle and thrive.\nOn September 19, Xiamen City in Fujian Province, building on its previously issued “60 measures,” further formulated detailed implementation rules. After each measure, it specifies the concrete policy, application requirements, documents to be submitted, the responsible unit's contact person and telephone number, and the service procedures. This greatly facilitates Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in looking up, understanding and handling related business.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180926_12095493.htm"],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广新闻记者","Several recent Taiwan opinion polls show that the proportion of people dissatisfied with the DPP authorities’ cross-Strait policy has risen sharply, and the proportion supporting cross-Strait unification has reached a new high. Island public opinion shows a trend of “unification rising, independence falling.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","As for the specific opinion polls, I will not comment.\nWhat I want to make clear here is that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are a community of shared destiny bound by blood and flesh. Upholding the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we have continuously introduced a series of policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, including the “31 Measures,” water supply to Kinmen, the abolition of work permits for Taiwan residents coming to the mainland, and the issuance of residence permits to Taiwan residents. We have taken the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, providing Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland compatriots in study, employment, entrepreneurship and daily life. We strive to do practical things, good things and things that solve difficulties, and this has been widely praised by Taiwan compatriots. Following the will of the people naturally wins the hearts of the people.\nAs the mainland develops and progresses, and as our policies toward Taiwan achieve results and increasingly win hearts and minds, more and more Taiwan compatriots see the mainland as the path to advancing their interests and welfare and realizing their life goals, and recognize that achieving national reunification accords with the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180926_12095490.htm"],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen said that the mainland has been creating “fake news” during Taiwan’s local elections, causing social division in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have always refrained from interfering in elections in the Taiwan region. At every election, the DPP and its authorities, in order to cover up their poor governance and divert public criticism, always try every means to spread rumors and smear the mainland. By manipulating hostility and antagonism toward the mainland, they damage cross-Strait relations and seek electoral gains. This is their habitual political manipulation, and it fully exposes their political nature. It is precisely these statements and practices of the DPP authorities that create and spread “fake news.”\nHere, let me cite a recent example. At the previous press conference, a journalist asked about the rescue of passengers stranded at Kansai Airport during the windstorm disaster in Japan. At that time I only offered a brief comment: “The clear will remain clear, and the murky will remain murky.”\nIn fact, at that time the DPP authorities, certain political figures on the island, and specific media, in order to conceal their embarrassment over failing to promptly rescue stranded Taiwan compatriots, deliberately distorted the facts and diverted attention. Some posted photos online claiming that the airport’s connecting bridge had collapsed and outside vehicles could not get in at all; it was later shown that the photos had been deliberately cropped to conceal the fact that passage was in fact possible. Others claimed that the airport authorities did not allow outside vehicles to enter, so the mainland’s dispatch of vehicles to pick up people was false news; yet they did not mention that our Consulate General in Osaka, through consultations with Kansai Airport and coordination with the airport authorities, specially arranged six batches of buses to take Chinese passengers from the airport to an assembly point outside, after which our consulate arranged shuttle buses to transport the passengers to downtown Osaka.\nThe purpose of doing so is to cover up a basic fact: 1,044 Chinese passengers were quickly, safely, and smoothly evacuated with the help of our Consulate General in Osaka, including 32 Taiwan compatriots. Over the years, who has been quietly doing good deeds for Taiwan compatriots and who has been undermining their good deeds: I believe Taiwan compatriots have their own sense of judgment in their hearts. Deceiving and misleading the Taiwan public through deceptive tactics is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180926_12095488.htm"],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","新华社记者","According to reports, Taiwan's executive authority recently made clear that it will impose controls on Taiwan residents who apply for mainland residence permits, including restricting their rights on the island. What is your comment?","We have repeatedly stated that the Taiwan Residence Permit was issued to meet the needs of the broad Taiwan compatriots. It is a measure to facilitate Taiwan compatriots studying, working and living on the mainland, and it does not involve any adjustment of the political rights and obligations of Taiwan residents. Taiwan compatriots applying for the residence permit do not need to give up their Taiwan ID cards or household registration, nor do they need to have mainland household registration. Moreover, the application for the Taiwan Residence Permit fully follows the principle of voluntariness; whether to apply is entirely up to Taiwan compatriots themselves, with no mandatory requirements. This policy, which benefits the people and provides convenience, positively responds to the demands of the broad Taiwan compatriots, conforms to public sentiment, wins hearts, and has been widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots.\nWe introduced this policy as a further extension of the “31 measures” previously introduced, to provide Taiwan compatriots studying, working and living on the mainland with treatment equal to that of mainland residents, and to create more convenient conditions for the broad Taiwan compatriots to share in the development opportunities of the mainland. Facts prove that we are constantly striving to do real things, good things, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. In sharp contrast, the DPP authorities ignore the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, continuously obstruct and intimidate them, and out of narrow party interests and unspeakable political purposes, keep spoiling good deeds for Taiwan compatriots. This further exposes their true nature, and they can only lose the hearts of the people even further.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180926_12095492.htm"],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","I would like to ask two questions. The first question: the mainland recently cracked more than one hundred Taiwan espionage cases. Reports have emerged that Taiwanese intelligence personnel have targeted mainland students in Taiwan, using money and sexual enticement to collect intelligence. The Mainland Affairs Council has called this “totally fabricated.” Please comment and respond to this matter. Will this…","Regarding your first question, we have previously stated our position on this matter. For some time, Taiwan’s espionage and intelligence agencies have targeted the mainland, carrying out extensive intelligence theft and infiltration and sabotage activities. The national security organs organized the special operation “2018—雷霆” and cracked more than a hundred Taiwan espionage cases. The state has laws, and these illegal activities will surely be severely punished in accordance with the law. What we are doing is entirely acting in accordance with the law, to safeguard national security, to maintain the normal order of cross-Strait exchanges, and to protect the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. The facts speak louder than words. Some Taiwan departments are evading the facts, confusing right and wrong, and even turning the tables. This only proves that they have a guilty conscience.\nI also want to stress here that the mainland has consistently and actively supported cross-Strait educational exchanges and cooperation, and we encourage young students on both sides to interact more. But Taiwan’s espionage and intelligence agencies have used despicable means to reach out to young mainland students studying in Taiwan who are inexperienced in the ways of the world. This has seriously harmed the interests of mainland students and seriously undermined cross-Strait educational exchanges. We demand that relevant Taiwan authorities immediately stop any infiltration and sabotage activities that endanger national security, and effectively guarantee the personal safety of mainland students.\nAs for your second question, the one-China principle is the basic principle guiding our handling of Taiwan’s external relations, and it is also an important political foundation for developing our relations with countries around the world. As for the China-Vatican relationship, I suggest you ask the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180926_12095491.htm"],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","The spokesperson just mentioned the conveniences of residence permits. I would also like you to give concrete examples of the conveniences Taiwan residents enjoy after applying for residence permits.","The \"Measures for Application and Issuance of Residence Permits for Residents of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan\" have been widely welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots since their release, and they have generated strong repercussions. Since the Measures took effect on September 1, applications have been very enthusiastic among Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life, including Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan officials, Taiwan youth, Taiwan teachers and Taiwan students. After receiving their residence permits, some Taiwan compatriots used self-service devices at railway stations to buy train tickets with WeChat Pay. Some used airport self-service ticketing and check-in to board flights smoothly. Some joined social insurance locally and collected and activated their social security cards. Others completed mainland mobile phone network registration, and so on.\nWhat I want to say is that making things convenient for the people and benefiting the people, so that permit-holding Taiwan compatriots can enjoy the \"three rights, six basic public services and nine conveniences\" provided by the state and their place of residence, and enjoy the same treatment as mainland residents, is the purpose of this policy. I believe more and more Taiwan compatriots will genuinely feel the convenience and benefits this good policy brings them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","台湾TVBS记者","On September 25, the U.S. government notified Congress of its decision to sell arms and equipment to Taiwan worth approximately US$330 million in total. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Regarding this matter, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of National Defense have both stated our solemn position. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the Taiwan region and the United States, and firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region under any pretext. I must emphasize once again that any act that relies on foreign backing to assert itself and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will inevitably reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","I have two questions. First, recently some media reported that the mainland is considering relaxing the qualifications for Taiwan compatriots to apply for residence permits. For example, relaxing the residence time requirement, so that one can apply with only a marriage certificate and an employment certificate. In addition, in response to the registration controls adopted by relevant Taiwan authorities, the…","Regarding your first question, on residence permits: The purpose of issuing residence permits to Taiwan residents is to provide convenience to Taiwan compatriots. Under the Measures for the Application and Issuance of Residence Permits for Residents of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, Taiwan residents who have lived on the mainland for more than six months and provide the corresponding supporting documents may apply voluntarily. During the application process, public security organs in various localities will handle each case according to the specific circumstances of Taiwan compatriots and try their best to meet their application needs.\nRegarding your second question, this exposes that some people in the DPP, on the one hand, tolerate and condone “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, while on the other hand, they crack down on and persecute Taiwan people who advocate unification. Such practices will certainly be opposed and condemned by people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Two questions. First question: In Bob Woodward's new book, “Fear: Trump in the White House,” it is revealed that Trump once questioned what benefit the United States would gain from protecting Taiwan. The Taiwan authorities, in response, stressed that the United States is Taiwan's most important ally. Could the spokesperson respond to this? Second question: Stephen Young (司徒文), former director of the American…","On the first question, we have always stressed that Taiwan's future and destiny are tied to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, national reunification, and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Reunification is an irresistible historical trend. Any act that opposes this historical tide and seeks to rely on foreign powers to enhance its own standing will ultimately harm the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nAs for your second question, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and we firmly oppose any interference by external forces. Taiwan's future should be decided jointly by all 1.3 billion-plus Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. We will make the greatest sincerity and the greatest efforts to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. At the same time, our determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering. We absolutely will not allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China in any form or under any name.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","中新社记者","The island's first park themed on “commemorating ‘Taiwan independence’ figure” Huang Chao-tang recently officially opened for use. Chen Chu and others attended the opening ceremony. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Erecting monuments and writing biographies for so-called \"Taiwan independence\" elements once again exposes the true face of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities in Taiwan, who support and indulge \"Taiwan independence.\" I want to stress that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead-end road that cannot be traveled, and it will only lead the people of Taiwan into the abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Recently, media reported that the Taiwan Army Command decided to invest NT$1.66 billion (16.6 億新台币) to build new bases in Taichung and Taitung, and claimed this is to guard against a sudden attack by the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s view on this?","We have always stressed that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the fundamental guarantee for maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This is a principle that everyone understands very well. Any attempt to resort to armed confrontation is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","The head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department has repeatedly contributed articles to foreign media, seeking to open the door for Taiwan at the United Nations. What is your assessment?","The United Nations is composed of sovereign states and adheres to the one-China principle. Any attempt to challenge the one-China principle internationally is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","经济日报记者","Recently, the 2018 Straits Science and Technology Forum and the 2018 Cross-Strait New Economy Forum were held one after another. We can see that cooperation between the two sides in science, technology, and economic and trade fields continues to advance and deepen. May I ask the spokesperson what new measures the mainland will take next to promote cross-Strait industrial exchange and cooperation?","Not long ago, the Second Cross-Strait New Economy Forum, co-hosted by Xinhua News Agency and media under the Taiwan Want Want China Group, was held in Beijing, bringing together more than 100 business leaders and financial experts from both sides of the Strait to discuss the theme of new opportunities for cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation in the new era. Cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation has unique and unmatched advantages, and Taiwan businesses should seize the new opportunities brought by the mainland's industrial transformation and upgrading, coordinated regional development, and high-level opening up, and usher in broader development space.\nThe mainland has always upheld the concept that \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" and has successively introduced a series of policies and measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, including the \"31 Measures,\" the cancellation of the employment permit for Taiwan compatriots, and the issuance of residence permits for Taiwan residents, sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first, and providing Taiwan compatriots with the same treatment as mainland compatriots in studying, finding employment, starting businesses, and living on the mainland, doing practical things and good deeds for Taiwan compatriots. We also hope that Taiwan's business and industrial circles, while riding the mainland's fast-track development and participating in cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation to realize their own business development, will be willing to shoulder responsibility, firmly maintain correct positions, actively exert their influence, and, together with mainland compatriots, use practical actions to safeguard and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","After El Salvador and other countries severed ties with Taiwan, the United States recalled its ambassadors to three Latin American countries. A U.S. State Department spokesperson recently said that it maintains close unofficial relations with Taipei and develops relations with Beijing, which applies to the United States but may not apply to other countries. What is the spokesperson’s response to the U.S. statement?","In response to the groundless accusations by the US over the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on multiple occasions. I would like to reiterate that the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador is the correct decision made by El Salvador in accordance with the fundamental interests of its country and people. The relevant US remarks and actions brutally interfere in another country's internal affairs; they are also a typical double standard, and they seriously violate the US commitments to the one-China policy and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","On the 87th anniversary of the September 18 Incident, New Party Chairman Jaw Shaw-kong posted on Facebook on the 18th to commemorate the date. He lamented that under “de-Sinicization” education, Taiwan's people now hold distorted views of history. He said that those who intend to destroy a nation must first destroy its history; those who forget their ancestors and bring calamity upon their descendants will…","We all know that Chinese history and Chinese culture are the common roots and soul of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities support and tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and in the fields of history, culture and education they carry out this gradual “de-Sinicization” “Taiwan independence” campaign, which in effect is digging up the roots and pulling out the soul. This reckless conduct, which forgets one's ancestors, certainly deserves condemnation and opposition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Two questions. First, over the past two years, as mainland universities have continued to rise in international rankings, more and more Taiwan youths have chosen to study at mainland universities. I would like the spokesperson to introduce the situation of Taiwan youths coming to the mainland to study this year. Second, a Taiwan media outlet recently reported that during the mainland's targeted poverty…","On the first question, from this year's enrollment situation, Taiwan students have applied to Mainland universities very enthusiastically. Mainland universities have actively taken measures to expand their enrollment of Taiwan students, and the number admitted has grown considerably compared with previous years. At present, the relevant universities have completed their preparations and will strive to provide convenient study and living conditions for Taiwan students. We have consistently supported exchanges among cross-Strait youth and adopted a series of measures to build platforms, create conditions and provide convenience for Taiwan youth to study, intern, find employment and start businesses in the Mainland. In the future we will continue to introduce and improve relevant policies, and welcome Taiwan students to study and develop in the Mainland, embark on a new journey in life and realize their life ideals.\nOn your second question, the report of the 19th CPC National Congress explicitly stated that by 2020 we must complete the task of eliminating poverty. Poverty alleviation work is now entering a critical stage. In the Mainland's poverty alleviation and poverty reduction work, Taiwan businesses have also played an active role. Not long ago, the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Department of the China Journalists Association jointly organized a cross-Strait joint reporting trip on targeted poverty alleviation, visiting Gansu to report on local poverty alleviation work. Some of the journalists present also took part in this reporting activity and filed extensive coverage. You may refer to it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-09-26","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, the mainland palace drama “Story of Yanxi Palace” has been popular with Taiwan audiences, and data says the drama's clicks in Taiwan exceeded 100 million. How does the spokesperson evaluate the phenomenon of mainland film and television programs becoming hugely popular in Taiwan?","Chinese culture is inherently connected across the Strait. Exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all areas, including culture, film and television, and entertainment, play an important role in increasing mutual understanding among compatriots, strengthening kinship ties, and achieving spiritual connection. The two sides are fundamentally one family, and Chinese culture is the common spiritual home of compatriots on both sides. This is something no “de-Sinicization” conduct on the island can sever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201809/t20180926_12095513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-09-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the US announced a $330 million arms sale to Taiwan. Though it’s mainly composed of components and the scale and total number are not big，analysts held that this would become a regular arrangement in the future. What’s your comment?","We have expressed our firm opposition to the US arms sale to Taiwan. It is not about the number but about the nature of the action. Taiwan is a part of China. The Taiwan question matters on China’s core interests. The US action has violated the one-China principle and the three Joint Communiques between China and the US. It is an interference into China's domestic affairs. It undermined China’s sovereignty and security interests and severely damaged China-US military relations and bilateral ties as well as peace and security across the Taiwan Straits. I want to stress that any attempts to contain China with Taiwan or to resist reunification through force are surely to fail.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-09/28/content_4825833.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-09-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Does the Chinese military have any plan to put sanctions on the US enterprises that sell arms to Taiwan?","We have stated our position on the unreasonable sanctions on China by the US side. As for whether we will have any sanctions on related US enterprises, I advice you to refer to competent authorities.\nFew days later, the 5th Chinese Memorial Day will fall on September 30th. Martyrs represent a nation’s backbone and spirit. They are the carrier and incarnation of our national spirit. We’ve made a video clip to commemorate the Chinese Memorial Day. (http://vv.chinamil.com.cn/asset/category3/2018/09/27/asset_336537.mp4) Let us remember the history, cherish the memory of our revolutionary martyrs, stay true with the original self, and keep moving on.\nHere concludes today’s press conference! Thank you!","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2018-09/28/content_4825833.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2018-09-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 27 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — In response to recent announcements by relevant authorities in Taiwan that they have revised regulations to further restrict personnel exchanges and interaction across the Taiwan Strait, An Fengshan, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 27th in response to a question: Expanding and deepening cross-Strait exchanges is the will of the people and the trend of the times. The DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest and inconfessable political purposes, are turning back the wheel of history, continuously placing obstacles to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interaction, further undermining the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, harming the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, and going against the will and wishes of the people. The DPP authorities' reckless actions can only further lose them popular support.\nAn Fengshan said: We will continue, guided by the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” to expand and deepen economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, promote personnel exchanges across the Strait, do practical things, good deeds, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, enhance common interests, promote heart-to-heart understanding, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, overcome difficulties and eliminate interference together, advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and push forward the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201809/t20180927_12096028.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 10 — In response to remarks concerning cross-Strait relations in the “Double Ten” speech of the leader of the Taiwan authorities, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 10th in response to a question: The leader’s speech is full of “two-state theory” separatist fallacies and confrontational thinking aimed at the mainland, exposing a sinister intent to cooperate with Western anti-China forces in containing the mainland. Such hostile provocative remarks further prove that the DPP authorities are the makers of cross-Strait conflict and the saboteurs of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They will only further worsen cross-Strait relations and drag Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the legal fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China and that Taiwan is part of China cannot be changed by anyone or any force. Any separatist scheme or action that relies on foreign powers to bolster itself, escalates confrontation, attempts to undermine cross-Strait relations, or changes Taiwan’s status can only humiliate itself and will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181010_12099405.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-10-15","Lu Kang","","The US leader recently claimed that the Chinese side has threatened the stability across the Taiwan Strait by persuading three Latin American countries to sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan. What is your comment?","We have stated our position on this issue on many occasions. The relevant accusations made by the US side are nothing but calling white black and confusing right and wrong. Here I would like to stress three points as follows:\nFirstly, there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. This is the general consensus shared by the international community. China has established diplomatic relations with the relevant countries on the basis of the one-China principle, which is a sovereign right enjoyed by China and the relevant countries as sovereign states. It also fully conforms to the international law and the basic norms governing international relations, corresponds with the irresistible trend of history and the times, and meets the aspirations of the people. As early as nearly four decades ago, the United States established diplomatic ties with China in accordance with the one-China principle, but now it points fingers at or even flagrantly hinders other countries when they did the same. This does not make any sense.\nSecondly, it is the \"Taiwan independence\" forces and their separatist activities that pose the biggest threat to the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities in Taiwan are trying to undermine the status quo that the two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same country and the relations across the Strait are not state-to-state relations, which not only hinders the peaceful development of the cross-straits relations but also erodes regional peace and stability. The international community should say no to this. By severing their relations and making a clean break with the Taiwan authorities who are undermining the status quo across the Strait, the relevant countries have upheld the international consensus of the one-China principle and played a positive role in maintaining cross-straits peace and stability.\nThirdly, I have to point out that the US side recently took a string of wrong actions on the Taiwan issue, including allowing the leader of the Taiwan region to make \"stopovers\" in the US and announcing the plan of arms sales to Taiwan. Such acts have severely violated the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, emboldened the \"Taiwan independence\" forces and harmed China-US relations as well as cross-straits peace and stability.\nThe Chinese side urges the US side to correct its mistakes, stop any official and military ties with and arms sales to the Taiwan region, stop harassing those countries that have already established or hope to establish diplomatic ties with China, and earnestly restrain the \"Taiwan independence\" forces to avoid harming China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nDue to scheduling reasons, the regular press conferences of the Foreign Ministry on October 16 (Tuesday) and October 17 (Wednesday) will start at 2:30 p.m. at the same venue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1604154.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1604105.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-10-17","Lu Kang","","It is reported that on October 15, US research vessel Thomas G. Thompson docked at the port of Kaohsiung. Although this ship is part of the US Navy assets, it has been used by non-governmental organizations. What is your comment?","We have noted relevant reports and are expressing our grave concerns to the US side.\nI would like to reiterate that the Chinese side is firmly opposed to any form of military ties between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop any form of official exchanges and military ties with Taiwan and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1604874.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1604812.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently we have seen that various localities and departments on the mainland have successively issued specific measures to implement the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots.” Could you introduce the latest situation?","In February this year, after the “31 measures” to promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait were introduced, all departments and regions earnestly and comprehensively implemented them. Recently, five more localities, in light of their own actual conditions, have introduced specific implementation measures. To date, 35 localities in 16 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities have introduced specific implementation measures.\nOn September 29, Guizhou Province issued the 《Implementation Opinions on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Guizhou and Taiwan》, with 64 articles in total; on October 15, Liaoning Province issued the 《Implementation Opinions of Liaoning Province on Implementing the 〈Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation across the Taiwan Strait〉》, with 52 articles in total; on October 15, Anhui Province announced the 《Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Anhui and Taiwan》, with 55 articles in total; on October 12, Suzhou City of Jiangsu Province issued the 《Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Suzhou and Taiwan》, with 55 articles in total. The new measures introduced by the above localities not only fully implement the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots,” but also highlight local characteristics and policy innovations. They provide many policy supports to Taiwan-funded enterprises in the local area in fields such as industry, finance and taxation, land use, and finance; and in areas involving employment, education, culture, and healthcare, they provide Taiwan compatriots with equal treatment, and they resolve hot-button issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots, such as applying for credit cards, housing provident fund, children's enrollment in school, applying for motor vehicle driver's licenses, and medical services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102019.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council stated that most of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” issued by the mainland are “empty promises” and “say one thing and do another.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","For some time, we have continuously rolled out a series of policies and measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, including the “31 Measures for Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” providing water supply to Kinmen, abolishing the work permit for Taiwan residents coming to the mainland for employment, and issuing Residence Permits for Taiwan Residents. We have taken the lead in sharing development opportunities on the mainland with Taiwan compatriots and provided Taiwan compatriots studying, starting businesses, working, and living on the mainland the same treatment as mainland compatriots. We have worked to get things done, do good deeds, and solve difficulties, which has been widely welcomed and well received by Taiwan compatriots.\nSince the release of the “31 Measures,” various departments and regions have continued to advance policy implementation, and as I just introduced, new progress has continuously been made. Many Taiwan-funded enterprises enjoy tax preferences and capital subsidies and participate in R&D programs, government procurement, and infrastructure construction projects. Many Taiwan compatriots have obtained various qualification certificates, employment positions, awards and commendations, and honorary titles. This year, the number of Taiwan students applying to mainland universities has multiplied, and many Taiwan students have received admission notices, scholarships, and grants as they wished. Taiwan compatriots studying, working, and living on the mainland all feel that food, clothing, housing, and transportation have become more convenient. Facts speak louder than words. The DPP authorities have used intimidation, punishment, and other means to obstruct Taiwan compatriots from enjoying equal treatment and to restrict them from obtaining greater and better development opportunities. Now they have turned black into white, misled public opinion, and further undermined the good deeds done for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. As the saying goes, the sky is not the highest; the human heart is the highest. The DPP authorities' practice of going against the will of the Taiwan people will only harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and will only further lose public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102018.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央广电台记者","Lai Ching-te, head of Taiwan’s executive department, recently said he hopes to use the China-US trade friction to get mainland Taiwan-invested enterprises to return to Taiwan to invest. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","Regarding the China-U.S. trade issue, relevant departments have repeatedly stated our attitude and position. What I want to say is that our support for Taiwan-invested enterprises' continued development on the mainland is consistent and clear. As we understand it, the overall production and operations of Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland are currently good. Broad numbers of Taiwan businesspeople are optimistic about the opportunities, vast market capacity, and market potential of the mainland's sustained economic development. A batch of new Taiwan-invested projects with high technology content and large investment scale are under construction, and many existing Taiwan-invested enterprises have successively increased capital and expanded production. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from January to August this year, the mainland approved 3,265 Taiwan-invested projects, a year-on-year increase of 29.6%. We will continue to release the dividends of reform and opening up, further expand opening to the outside world, continuously optimize the business environment, and create more opportunities and broader space for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102015.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The “Belt and Road” initiative has reached its fifth anniversary. What achievements have Taiwan-invested enterprises made in participating in Belt and Road construction?","The Belt and Road Initiative has made major progress over the past five years. The volume of trade in goods between the mainland and countries along the Belt and Road has cumulatively exceeded 5 trillion US dollars, direct investment has cumulatively exceeded 60 billion US dollars, and China-Europe freight trains have cumulatively exceeded 10,000 trips. Broad masses of Taiwan businesses have also directly benefited from the Belt and Road Initiative. Some products made by Taiwan-invested enterprises are shipped to Europe via China-Europe freight trains, which has opened larger markets for relevant businesses and created a stable and efficient new logistics channel. Some Taiwan-invested enterprises cooperate with mainland enterprises and, by providing electrical equipment and supporting services, jointly participate in the construction of infrastructure projects such as coal-fired power plants and combined-cycle power stations in multiple countries along the Belt and Road. Some Taiwan-invested banks also cooperate with mainland banks, providing project financing and bringing more business to Taiwan-invested banks. We will continue to encourage and support Taiwan-invested enterprises to cooperate with mainland enterprises in participating in Belt and Road projects, and to continuously expand the scope and fields of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102013.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","According to reports, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council required the mainland visiting delegation to meet with MAC officials, causing some local Taiwan Affairs Office personnel to be forced to cancel their trips to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle. This undermines the existing political foundation of cross-Strait relations and has directly led to the interruption of cross-Strait communication and liaison mechanisms. Under these circumstances, it is inconvenient for Taiwan Affairs Office personnel to meet with people from the Mainland Affairs Council. The Mainland Affairs Council should reflect on why officials responsible for cross-Strait affairs from both sides could meet between 2008 and 2016, but cannot do so now. Instead of pretending to be confused while knowing full well what is going on, and setting new obstacles to cross-Strait civil exchanges through nearly unreasonable pestering, it should face the matter squarely. Such political maneuvering will not win hearts and cannot stop the pace of cross-Strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102012.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","According to media reports, the U.S. Navy plans to dispatch warships to the South China Sea and the Taiwan Strait in November for so-called “military operations to demonstrate force.” What is the spokesperson’s response?","We have noted the relevant reports. On South China Sea-related issues, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of National Defense have stated our solemn position many times. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and involves China's core interests. Our determination and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity are unwavering. We advise the relevant parties to act prudently so as not to damage peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan's Central Election Commission recently approved the so-called “Olympic renaming referendum” and will bind it to the year-end “Nine-in-One” elections. What is your comment?","We have repeatedly stated that the “Olympic model” is a principle that international sports organizations and sports figures on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should jointly follow. Trying to use the “Olympic name-rectification referendum” to seek “name rectification” is nothing but a farcical self-deception. A very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island, for their own selfish interests and under the laissez-faire tolerance of the DPP authorities, have ignored the solemn warnings of the International Olympic Committee and the East Asian Olympic Committees, and have stubbornly pushed for this referendum. In the end, what will be harmed is only the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan athletes. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will remain vigilant, cherish the rights and interests they currently enjoy, and not let a few grains of rat dung spoil the whole pot of porridge.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102017.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The draft revision of the Referendum Act proposed by Taiwan's New Power Party lists \"territorial change\" and the formulation of a so-called \"new constitution\" among the matters applicable to referendums. What is the TAO's comment on this?","We firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities carried out through so-called “referendum legislation amendments” or any other means. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Taiwan has never been a country and will never become one in the future. “Taiwan independence” is a “dead end” that will only lead Taiwan's people into an abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181017_12102016.htm"],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Two questions. First, on the 16th, a research vessel reportedly belonging to the U.S. Office of Naval Research called at Kaohsiung port for resupply and crew change for the fourth time this year, and is expected to leave port on the evening of the 18th. What comment does the spokesperson have? Second, last month, Typhoon “Yanzi” severely hit Japan and caused the closure of Kansai Airport. The mainland's consulate…","On the first question: we have noted the relevant reports. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange or military contact between the United States and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.\nOn the second question: the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and our Consulate General in Osaka already provided the relevant details at the first opportunity. At the previous two press conferences, my colleague Mr. An Fengshan also explained the relevant details quite clearly. The facts are these: through consultation with the Kansai Airport side, our Osaka Consulate General coordinated with the airport to dispatch buses to transport 1,044 cross-strait passengers, including 32 Taiwan compatriots, from the airport to an assembly point outside. The consulate then arranged vehicles to take the passengers to downtown Osaka. This basic fact cannot be denied by anyone or refuted by any sophistry. As for why Taiwan people criticize and condemn relevant Taiwan authorities, I think this is a matter they themselves should reflect on deeply. In short, “those who are clear remain clear, and those who are muddy remain muddy.” Using this incident to keep making political hay, slandering the mainland, and trying to divert public attention and escape various predicaments will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The first China International Import Expo will open in Shanghai on November 5. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan businesses and enterprises.","The first China International Import Expo will be held in Shanghai from November 5 to 10, 2018. This is a major measure by which we take the initiative to open our market to the world on the occasion of the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up. Preparatory work is underway. Over these 40 years, a large number of Taiwan compatriots have actively joined the tide of reform and opening up and taken part in the economic development and various construction undertakings of the mainland. While achieving their own development and growth, they have also made important contributions to the economic and social development of the mainland. Therefore, we sincerely welcome Taiwan businesses and enterprises to take part in the CIIE. According to my preliminary understanding, 72 Taiwan businesses and enterprises have so far registered to exhibit, distributed across five exhibition areas—electronics, smart technology, medical care, food, and services—with a total exhibition area of 2,253 square meters. For the overall overview and relevant information about the Expo, please visit the official CIIE website.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","In the November Taiwan local elections, many Taiwan businesspeople are preparing to return to vote, some traveling in groups of three or five, and they all hope for voting charter flights, or charter flights combining voting and the Spring Festival. Will the Taiwan Affairs Office provide assistance? Second question: I have noticed that at entry and exit, immigration officers, security personnel, and quarantine…","I will first answer the second question: there is no such notice. “Taiwan residents,” “Taiwan compatriots,” and “Taiwan's public” are all terms I have used interchangeably at press conferences, so please do not overthink this and do not let “people with ulterior motives” exploit it to make political arguments.\nRegarding the first question, we have said many times that we do not interfere in Taiwan's elections. If Taiwan businesspeople are willing to return home to vote, we will provide convenience; they may raise the request with the local Taiwan business association, and we will provide assistance within our capacity where possible. As for the Spring Festival charter flights you mentioned, let me say something on this. The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation and a time for family reunions. I would like to state here that we will, as always, continue to take positive measures to provide convenience for cross-Strait people's travel during next year's Spring Festival, especially for Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year. We hope the DPP authorities will change the unreasonable practice this Spring Festival of obstructing mainland civil aviation charter flights, stop deliberately setting up obstacles, and stop harming the basic rights of Taiwan compatriots to go home for the New Year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Last week, when the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to Tsai Ing-wen's “Double Ten speech,” it mentioned that the speech was full of “two-state theory.” May I ask whether this is already a characterization of Tsai Ing-wen? In addition, in response to Tsai Ing-wen's inauguration speech, the Taiwan Affairs Office said it was an unfinished answer sheet. May I ask whether this answer sheet has been collected? Second…","Regarding the relevant remarks of Taiwan's leader, I already gave a written response on October 10. I would like to reiterate here that the speech by Taiwan's leader is replete with the separatist fallacy of the \"two-state theory\" and confrontational thinking directed against the Mainland, exposing its sinister intention to cooperate with Western anti-China forces and contain the Mainland. Such hostile provocative remarks further prove that the DPP authorities are the creators of cross-Strait confrontation and the destroyers of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and will only further worsen cross-Strait relations and bring Taiwan to an even more dangerous situation. The Mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China cannot be changed by anyone or any force. Any separatist scheme and conduct that relies on foreign powers to elevate itself, escalates confrontation, attempts to undermine cross-Strait relations and change Taiwan's status can only bring humiliation upon itself and will never succeed. Improvement and development of cross-Strait relations is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides, and \"only the person who tied the knot can untie it.\" We hope the DPP authorities will awaken, repent, abandon the old and embrace the new, and return to the common political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" which is the only way to open up a future vision for the development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn the second question, I think this logic is a \"ghost logic\" of deranged thinking, a logic that cuts oneself off from the Chinese people and the Chinese nation; it is no exaggeration to say that it betrays national interests. As everyone knows, compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all descendants of Yan and Huang; the histories of the Yangtze and the Yellow River are the shared history of us compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, when asked “why not require the United States to establish diplomatic relations with Taiwan,” Lai Ching-te said that this is a very good suggestion, that it will be conveyed to the United States, and that efforts can be made in this direction. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Hearing these words, I feel this is a person who is dreaming and speaking nonsense. Such nonsense is not worth further comment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The “Cross-Strait Online New Media Mainland Tour” will be launched in the near future. This is the first important news exchange activity held with cross-strait online new media as the main body. Please introduce the relevant situation. Second question: the Taiwan Grassroots Influence Cultural and Educational Foundation released survey results on the 8th regarding the 31 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots on…","First question. The first Cross-Strait New Media Joint Interview and Reporting Activity will officially launch tomorrow, that is, the morning of October 18, at the Taiwan Hall. More than 100 new media practitioners from both sides will take part. The activity will focus on the achievements of 40 years of reform and opening up, and on the achievements of continuously expanding and deepening cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, to tell the common stories of people on both sides. The activity starts in Beijing and will also go to Tianjin, Shanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang and Guangdong, lasting 16 days. Because this is an important first-ever attempt at cross-Strait news exchange that uses new media as the reporting subject and communication platform, I sincerely wish this activity smooth and complete success.\nSecond question. We do not comment on specific polls in Taiwan. Taking into account the situation reflected in various Taiwan public opinions during this period, there is no doubt that the series of policies benefiting Taiwan since the “31 measures” has produced increasing influence among the Taiwan public. Therefore, their willingness to develop on the mainland has further increased. I think what is right, we will continue to uphold. We are now solidly and earnestly implementing relevant policies and measures, to bring more convenience to Taiwan compatriots and increase their sense of gain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently the Taiwan authorities indicated that relevant regulations have been revised, explicitly restricting Taiwan compatriots who apply for Mainland residence permits from taking civil service examinations, joining the military police or military academies, running in county or city magistrate elections, or holding other public office in the future. What is the spokesperson's comment?","As I have repeatedly stated just now, the starting point of a series of policies, including the residence permit policy and the “31 measures” and so on, is to provide more convenience for Taiwan compatriots to live, work, study, find employment and start businesses on the mainland, and to gradually provide them with treatment equal to that of mainland compatriots. This embodies the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and is our sincere effort to do real things, good things, and solve real problems for Taiwan compatriots. For things that benefit Taiwan compatriots like these, the DPP authorities should have moved in the same direction and joined in the good cause together. But very regrettably, they have adopted political manipulation tactics that go in the opposite direction, continually intimidating, restricting and even punishing Taiwan compatriots who develop careers on the mainland. Such practices are truly unpopular, and we hope they will earnestly reflect on this.\nI would also like to reiterate here that the Taiwan residence permit was issued in response to the needs of broad Taiwan compatriots. It is a measure to facilitate Taiwan compatriots studying, working and living on the mainland, and does not involve any adjustment of the political rights and obligations of Taiwan residents. Taiwan compatriots applying for the residence permit do not need to give up their Taiwan ID cards or household registration, nor do they need to hold mainland household registration. Application for the Taiwan residence permit is entirely voluntary, with no mandatory requirements. Therefore, with this policy, we have fully considered the current special circumstances of cross-Strait relations and the possible concerns of Taiwan compatriots. But very regrettably, the DPP authorities are still scheming to spoil good things for Taiwan compatriots. We have also said many times that ordinary people have their own scales in their hearts. What effect the Taiwan authorities' practices will ultimately produce, I believe, is self-evident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","According to reports, the leaders of Taiwan’s three so-called “diplomatic allies,” Guatemala, Honduras and Haiti, did not mention Taiwan in their remarks at the general debate of the recent UN General Assembly. In particular, Haiti recently accepted a loan of 150 million US dollars from Taiwan. Island media used the word “rare” to describe this change. We note that these three Central American countries are the…","We have said many times that the One-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, and also reflects the aspirations of the people and the trend of the times. As for the specific question of China developing bilateral relations with other countries, please ask the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Recently, Taiwan authorities are preparing to amend relevant cross-Strait regulations. Regarding fines for unauthorized mainland capital, which were previously NT$120,000 to NT$600,000, they will be adjusted to NT$50,000 to NT$25 million, a substantial increase. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","I think everyone should understand one principle: mainland enterprises investing in Taiwan benefit Taiwan's economic and social development and will inevitably contribute to creating jobs and increasing income for Taiwan residents. So this is a good thing. Of course, the DPP authorities' consistent logic is to oppose anything that benefits Taiwan compatriots. Therefore, we hope the DPP authorities can soon remove the handcuffs and shackles on mainland capital and further give play to mainland capital's contribution to Taiwan's society, economy, and people's livelihood. This is the correct direction and approach.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng, Deputy Chairperson of the MAC, said that the mainland's “tightening and suppression” of Hong Kong has “eroded” freedom of speech and freedom of the press in Hong Kong. What is the spokesperson's response?","Since Hong Kong's return to the motherland, “one country, two systems,” “Hong Kong people governing Hong Kong,” and a high degree of autonomy have maintained prosperity and stability; this is a fact that is plain for all to see. The DPP authorities really have no qualification to make irresponsible remarks on this issue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Regarding exchange visits by Taiwan primary and secondary school teachers and students to the mainland, the MAC recently asked the education authorities to call on schools not to become \"tools of united front work.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","To imagine normal exchanges between cross-Strait youth and the education sector as “united front” work shows that the DPP's thinking has gone wrong and its logic has gone wrong. Because this is a confrontational mindset and a confused logic, we cannot accept such slander and labeling, and neither can cross-Strait educators and primary and secondary school teachers and students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台海峡两岸记者","Continuing on the issue of mainland capital, there have recently been reports that the DPP authorities may target Taiwan businesses, plan to comprehensively tighten cross-Strait capital flows, and conduct strict reviews of Taiwan businesses. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","If this news is true, we advise the DPP authorities that they absolutely must not do this, as it will hurt the hearts of Taiwan businesspeople. Water can carry a boat, but it can also capsize it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181017_12102020.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-10-23","Hua Chunying","","The US navy warships yesterday sailed through the Taiwan Strait. Does China consider this a provocative move by the United States?","The Chinese side has been closely monitoring from start to end the passage by the US warships through the Taiwan Strait. We have expressed our concern to the US side. The Taiwan issue concerns the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China. It is the most important and sensitive issue amid China-US relations. We urge the US to observe the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid undermining China-US relations and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1606490.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201810/t20181023_5416753.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-10-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We noticed that there were some ups and downs recently in the mil-to-mil relationship between China and the US. Last month, a US warship entered the neighboring waters of the reefs of China and the US Secretary of Defense cancelled his visit to China for the diplomatic and security dialogue. Meanwhile, Chinese Defense Minister and US Secretary of Defense held a meeting in Singapore and the US Secretary of Defense…","China-US military-to-military relationship is an important component of the overall relationship. A sound and stable military relationship is in the interests of both sides and it calls for efforts from both sides. The Chinese side believes that win-win cooperation is the only right path towards lasting growth in bilateral ties. Building mutual trust is the best glue for more profound contacts between the two countries. Upholding mutual-respect and inclusiveness is the right approach to resolving differences and frictions. The military-to-military relationship is generally stable. Nevertheless, there are also some negative factors. I must say China’s position on Taiwan and the South China Sea remains unchanged. The Chinese military’s determination to safeguard national sovereignty and development interests is rock-solid.\nA few days ago, State Councilor and Defense Minister Wei Fenghe held a positive and constructive meeting with Secretary James Mattis in Singapore. Secretary Mattis once again invited Minister Wei to visit the US during their meeting. China and US defense establishments are working closely on the visit. We hope the US side can work with the Chinese side towards the same direction, implement agreements reached by the two heads of state, enhance communication and trust, strengthen cooperation and control risks so as to push the military-to-military relationship into a stabilizer for the overall relationship.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-10/25/content_4827867.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-10-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US military is planning to send warships to conduct so-called “military operation to demonstrate force” in the Taiwan Straits and the South China Sea in November. There are many reports on this and what is your comment?","We have noticed related reports. China’s position on Taiwan and the South China Sea remains unchanged. The Chinese military’s determination to safeguard national sovereignty and regional peace and stability is rock-solid. Your question reminds me of the recent CCTV special program called “Pingyu Jinren” which is about President Xi’s quotes in his speeches and reports. In one episode, it says President Xi quoted many times the poem “From whichever direction the winds leap, I remain strong, though dealt many a blow.” I think this can be the answer to your question.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-10/25/content_4827867.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-10-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It’s reported that two US warships sailed through the Taiwan Strait from south to north on October 22. The Taiwan defense department said that the US warships routinely passed through the international waters in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","The spokesperson from China’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated China’s solemn position on this issue. The Chinese PLA knows best all the details of the passage of the US vessels and is fully aware and prepared for all movements of the vessels.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-10/25/content_4827867.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2018-10-29","Lu Kang","","Regarding the three principles guiding China-Japan relations proposed by Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, you just said that China welcomes that. Does that mean China has agreed to accept the three principles?","As to Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's visit, I would advise you to give a thorough reading of the readouts of Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's meetings and talks with President Xi Jinping, Premier Li Keqiang and Chairman of the NPC Standing Committee Li Zhanshu. It has been made clear in those readouts that the Chinese and Japanese sides have reached a high degree of consensus on planning for and further deepening China-Japan relations. The two sides confirmed that we will abide by all principles embedded in the four China-Japan political documents, properly handle the issue of history and the Taiwan issue, and maintain the political foundation of our bilateral relations. We will take concrete actions to implement the political consensus of being cooperative partners rather than threats to each other and supporting each other's peaceful development, and manage differences in a constructive manner. In the spirit of taking history as a mirror and facing forward to the future, we will promote new progress after the bilateral relations return to the right track.\nThe two sides also agreed to strengthen high-level guidance for China-Japan relations and conduct practical cooperation at a higher level, promote cooperation in such areas as scientific and technological innovation, energy conservation and environmental protection, health care and old-age care, fiscal and financial sectors, and step up people-to-people exchanges. Under the current international circumstances, we will jointly uphold free trade, oppose protectionism and promote the economic integration of the Asia-Pacific region through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1608076.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-10-31","Lu Kang","","According to reports, Taiwan's so-called \"deputy defense minister\" traveled this late October to Maryland, the US to attend the US-Taiwan Defense Industry Conference. Officials from the US Department of Defense also attended and spoke at the conference. What's your comment?","China is firmly opposed to any forms of official exchanges and military contacts between the US and Taiwan. This stance remains consistent and clear. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop its official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan, and stop selling arms to Taiwan. We hope that the US could prudently handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid any harm to China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1608884.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1608783.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央广记者","Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the latest progress made by localities and departments in implementing the “31 Measures” benefiting Taiwan compatriots.","The “31 Measures” have been issued and implemented for eight months, and at each press conference we have introduced new progress in their implementation. In the half month after the October 17 press conference, five more localities and one central state-owned enterprise rolled out specific implementation measures.\nOn October 19, Hunan Province issued the “Implementation Opinions on Deepening Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Hunan and Taiwan,” with 59 articles in total; on October 23, Beijing Municipality issued “Several Measures on Deepening Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Beijing and Taiwan,” with 55 articles in total; on October 18, the city of Changzhou in Jiangsu Province issued “Implementation Opinions on Deepening Economic, Social and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Changzhou and Taiwan,” with 36 articles in total; on October 19, the city of Longyan in Fujian Province issued “Implementation Opinions on Deepening Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Longyan and Taiwan,” with 46 articles in total; and on October 23, the city of Zhangzhou in Fujian Province issued “Opinions on Promoting Economic, Social and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation between Zhangzhou and Taiwan,” with 58 articles in total.\nIn addition, on October 26, China International Technical Intellectual Cooperation Corporation formulated implementation opinions for the “31 Measures,” with 38 measures in total. It was also the first central state-owned enterprise to promulgate specific implementation measures. Zhongzhi is the only central state-owned enterprise whose main business is human resources and intellectual services. In its implementation opinions, the company gave full play to its strength and influence in professional human resources services, accelerated the implementation of services benefiting Taiwan in key business sectors and regions, served Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to innovate and start businesses, and promoted cross-Strait business and cultural exchange.\nTo date, 40 localities in 18 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, as well as one central state-owned enterprise, have introduced specific measures. These measures will further ensure the comprehensive implementation of the “31 Measures” and provide more equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots according to local conditions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107904.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security publicly solicited public comments on the Interim Measures for Social Insurance Participation by Residents of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan on the Mainland. Could the spokesperson explain the situation?","To safeguard the social insurance rights of Taiwan compatriots who live, work, and study on the mainland, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security has drafted the “Interim Measures on Social Insurance Participation by Residents of Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan in the Mainland (Draft for Public Comment).” The scope of application of the Interim Measures covers Taiwan compatriots who are formally or flexibly employed on the mainland, as well as those who live on the mainland but are not employed, and university students, among others. These Measures will address the “double enrollment” issue that Taiwan compatriots have long been concerned about. They provide that Taiwan compatriots who have already enrolled in relevant social insurance in Taiwan and continue to maintain those social insurance relationships may, with a certificate issued by the authorized agency, not participate in pension insurance and unemployment insurance on the mainland.\nThe Interim Measures are currently being solicited for public comment. After they are finalized, the relevant policies and implementing rules will be officially released. We hope everyone will continue to follow this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107900.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently publicly attacked the mainland's political system and development model, shifting responsibility for damaging cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","At present, cross-Strait relations are complicated and grave. The head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council made outrageous remarks and wantonly provoked at a seminar, which will only further heighten cross-Strait tension and confrontation. Who is deliberately provoking trouble and creating cross-Strait confrontation? I believe compatriots on both sides can see very clearly.\nUnder the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China, we have firmly adhered to the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics, persisted in reform and opening up, and achieved brilliant accomplishments recognized worldwide. No one may make groundless statements or slander and smear them.\nUnder DPP rule, what the social situation on Taiwan is really like can be found in the indignation of the island's military, civil servants and teachers, the helplessness of farmers and fishermen, the distress of intellectuals, the worries of the business community, and the outcries of young people who are going west to the mainland. So I will not comment further.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107903.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","On the 20th of this month, the “Happy Island Alliance” held in Taipei a so-called “anti-annexation name-rectification referendum” event. On the same day, the DPP held another march in Kaohsiung. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","We firmly oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” provocations. Any conduct that stirs up cross-Strait confrontation, heightens hostility toward the mainland, or worsens cross-Strait relations will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots, and facts have proven that it is also unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107902.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce the relevant situation of the upcoming 11th Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Exposition and Trade Fair.","The 11th Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industries Expo and Fair will be held from November 2 to 5 at the Xiamen International Conference and Exhibition Center. It is understood that this year's expo will feature five exhibition areas: provinces and cities alongside leading cultural enterprises, arts and crafts, creative design, digital content and film and television, and cultural and creative tourism, with a total area of over 70,000 square meters and nearly 3,500 booths. For the first time, a Taiwan Life Pavilion has been set up, and the number of Taiwan enterprises exhibiting is close to 1,000, continuing to grow compared with previous years.\nSince its founding in 2008, the Straits Cross-Strait Cultural Expo has become an important platform for promoting cultural industry exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, win-win cooperation, cultural exchange and cooperation, and investment and trade, and it has achieved positive results. This year's expo will launch more than 40 events and over 30 sub-venues, presenting many new highlights. On behalf of the organizers, I welcome media friends to visit and report on the event at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107898.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On the 22nd of this month, two U.S. warships transited the Taiwan Strait, and Taiwan's authorities responded that they “welcome all efforts conducive to regional security and stability.” What is your comment?","Everyone has already noticed that the Foreign Ministry and the Ministry of National Defense have stated our attitude and position on this. The Taiwan question concerns China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange or military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear. Here I must once again emphasize: those who lean on foreign powers to bolster themselves and collude with external forces to undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will surely reap what they sow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the New Party held commemorative events marking the 73rd anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, declaring that “Taiwan independence” cannot erase history, and warned the DPP authorities that whoever agrees to U.S. military exercises in the Taiwan Strait is a traitor to Taiwan. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland in 1945 was a victory won through the joint resistance of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and external forces are absolutely not allowed to interfere. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have the full capability and wisdom to eliminate external interference and keep the destiny of the nation firmly in their own hands. The New Party has consistently advocated peaceful reunification of both sides of the Strait, adhering to one China and opposing “Taiwan independence,” which embodies the great righteousness of the nation. We highly appreciate this and firmly support it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201810/t20181031_12107901.htm"],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department recently claimed in an exclusive interview with German media: “When Beijing cannot handle its internal problems, it uses Taiwan to divert attention.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","I think this is blatant distortion of black and white and fabrication to mislead the public. As everyone can see, after 40 years of reform and opening up, today's mainland enjoys economic prosperity, social stability, improved living standards for the people, and unprecedented unity among all ethnic groups across the country. We are full of confidence in working united to realize the two centenary goals and the Chinese Dream of national rejuvenation.\nI actually think that the DPP authorities, who now fail to put their internal affairs in order and are relying on foreign powers to enhance their own standing, are trying to shift the focus of internal pressure by provoking cross-Strait relations. So I would ask them to reflect on their own conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The head of Taiwan's Investigation Bureau previously said that in Taiwan's year-end elections, the mainland is providing “financial support” to certain specific candidates. I wonder how the spokesperson views this?","I have already clarified in writing that we have never interfered in Taiwan’s elections. This is not just talk; over more than a decade, the facts have proven it. I think the accusation you mentioned is pure slander and complete fabrication and defamation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","May I ask whether the spokesperson has further clarification on cross-Strait flight arrangements for mid-to-late November? I have also heard that some flights in Yangzhou have been cancelled. Please explain this part.","As I understand it, at the strong request of a large number of members and Taiwan compatriots, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises recently invited airlines from both sides of the Strait to communicate on the issue of return air tickets for Taiwan compatriots. They agreed on specific operating methods for group purchases of tickets for Taiwan compatriots returning home until the Spring Festival of 2019, and these have been published. For details, you may consult the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises. As for the flight cancellations you mentioned, if this information is true, I think that at a time when a large number of Taiwan compatriots are willing to return home to vote, everyone will see clearly who is depriving Taiwan compatriots of the qualification to exercise their legitimate rights, and who is trying to influence Taiwan's elections.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","At the first cross-Strait civil roundtable forum, successfully held the day before yesterday, many Taiwan businesspeople raised that, amid China-US economic and trade frictions, export-oriented Taiwan businesses have suffered serious losses. They also hope the mainland will adjust its policies to reduce or exempt Taiwan businesses' taxes and fees. What is the spokesperson's comment?","At the first Cross-Strait Civil Roundtable Forum, held on October 29 in Beijing and co-hosted by the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots and the Taiwan Cross-Strait Roundtable Forum Association, representatives from civil sectors on both sides of the Strait conducted in-depth discussions on promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, providing development opportunities for Taiwan youth on the mainland, and other issues, and issued a “Joint Initiative.”\nI believe everyone has learned from relevant news reports and on-the-ground interviews that, in response to the voices and concerns expressed by Taiwan compatriots, we issued the “31 measures” in February this year, and subsequently canceled the employment permits for Taiwan residents on the mainland and issued residence permits to Taiwan compatriots. This series of measures is also aimed at enabling Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies to enjoy equal treatment in response to changes in the external situation. At the same time, we are now accelerating the expansion of opening up and deepening reform, and have issued a series of economic and trade measures. These measures also apply to Taiwan investors and industrial and commercial enterprises. Of course, we will continue to create a better business environment through expanded opening up and deepened reform, and create conditions for the development of Taiwan businesses on the mainland. I think this is the greatest policy support and assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾ETTODAY新闻云记者","Yesterday, news drew the attention of people on both sides of the Strait: the writer Mr. Jin Yong has passed away. How does the spokesperson evaluate the influence of his literary works across the Strait?","Yesterday, like everyone else, I was shocked to learn of the passing of Mr. Jin Yong and felt deep grief. For a generation like mine, Jin Yong's novels grew up with us; probably few university students and young intellectuals of that time had not read Jin Yong's novels. Mr. Jin Yong is a great writer respected by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. He wrote 15 magnificent works, and I noted that netizens summarized them as 'Snow flies across the sky, shooting the white deer; laughing at the books, the divine hero leans on the jade mandarin ducks.'\nMr. Jin Yong used his creative work to open another aesthetic realm for Chinese literature and to expand the connotation of traditional Chinese culture, so it is our unshirkable responsibility, as compatriots on both sides, to commemorate him. We should jointly promote Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","It is reported that more than 200 Taiwan suspects involved in the Spanish cross-border telecom fraud case have, by applying for political asylum, temporarily avoided repatriation to the mainland, while the Mainland Affairs Council said that the Taiwan authorities respect all possible remedies, and relevant agencies will provide assistance within the necessary scope. May I ask for the spokesperson’s response?","We have noted the relevant reports. We firmly crack down on all kinds of telecom fraud and, in accordance with law, apprehend cross-border telecom fraud criminals and bring them to justice, protecting the property security of people on both sides of the Strait. This is our firm position. It has won high praise from compatriots on both sides and full understanding and strong support from the international community. The DPP authorities should not disregard the legitimate rights of victims, nor should they indulge and support a small number of people with ulterior motives who, under the banner of so-called “human rights,” try to help criminals evade legal sanction. This can only continue to harm compatriots on both sides and the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","At the first Cross-Strait Civil Roundtable Forum held recently, cultural exchange was an important topic. We also noted that many representatives from the film and television industry attended that day, and that two cross-Strait co-produced film and television series signed agreements. May I ask the spokesperson: what further measures will be introduced to promote cross-Strait film and television cultural exchange?","We have consistently supported the active strengthening of cooperation between the film and television sectors across the Taiwan Strait. The “31 measures” policy issued on February 28 included three provisions providing policy support for Taiwan film and television practitioners to develop in the mainland, and these three measures have now been implemented one after another. On this premise, we will of course continue to encourage the film and television sectors on both sides to strengthen cooperation. One important direction of cooperation is to encourage them to co-produce films and television series, jointly promote Chinese culture, and, through literature and art, promote mutual understanding and spiritual affinity among people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to reports, the head of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that a so-called internal public opinion poll shows that islanders support barring holders of mainland residence permits from running for county or city magistrate and as public representatives. The MAC is drafting relevant bills to restrict the right to be elected of those who obtain mainland residence permits. What is the…","We have emphasized many times that the Taiwan residence permit was issued to meet the needs of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. It is a measure to facilitate Taiwan compatriots studying, living, and working on the mainland, and does not involve any adjustment of Taiwan residents' political rights and obligations.\nThe DPP authorities have consistently ignored the immediate interests and practical needs of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and have continually escalated so-called “countermeasures.” Now they want to further restrict their political rights. Such conduct, which harms the economic interests of cross-Strait compatriots and further harms the political rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","A recent poll on the island showed that nearly 60% of Taiwan residents identify themselves as Chinese, and nearly 90% identify themselves as members of the Chinese nation, reaching a new high in recent years. The polling agency believes this result shows that the DPP authorities' “de-Sinicization” has completely failed. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I will not comment on specific polls on the island. However, I want to reiterate that changes in some political and identity inclinations among the Taiwan public at least show one thing: the brilliant achievements of mainland economic and social development, and our Taiwan policy, have taken root in people’s hearts. This has led more and more Taiwan compatriots to recognize that the mainland is the opportunity and the future for increasing their interests and well-being and realizing their life ideals. So I personally believe this trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志社记者","Recently, the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge opened to traffic, drawing much discussion among the public on the island, who expressed envy and wondered when the cross-Strait bridge would be built after water is supplied to Kinmen. What comment does the spokesperson have on the public discussion on the island?","Everyone understands that the construction and opening of the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge is an important measure to deepen the integration of Hong Kong, Macao, and the mainland and to deepen the development of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area. It will play an important role in facilitating travel between Hong Kong, Macao, and the mainland, and in deepening economic cooperation and mutual benefit between these places. Of course, people easily think of the Taiwan Strait and hope that one day a similar bridge can be built to span both sides, so that a chasm becomes a smooth path. I think that as cross-Strait relations develop, this day should not be an unreachable dream.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the “Mazu Cultural Gazetteer,” compiled over more than eight years by more than 40 experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait, was announced as completed. This is the first specialized work on Mazu culture jointly compiled by both sides, totaling 4 volumes and 3.57 million characters. How does the spokesperson evaluate the role this work plays in promoting cultural exchanges across the Strait?","Mazu culture is a shared belief of many people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and a strong bond connecting the feelings of compatriots on both sides. The publication of such a document will certainly play its due role in promoting mutual communication and emotional connection among Mazu believers on both sides, and in jointly promoting Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","During his visit to China this month, Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe again reaffirmed the position on the Taiwan region question stated in the 1972 Japan–China Joint Communiqué. This leaves the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, who like to play the “Japan card,” with nothing to play. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this?","The Japanese side has repeatedly stated that it will continue to abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents and the relevant commitments it has made to China. We hope the Japanese side will keep its word, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and genuinely safeguard the political foundation for the healthy development of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-10-31","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je said that for the next 15 years there will be no cross-Strait relations, only the Taiwan issue under US-China confrontation. Does the spokesperson agree?","We will not comment on individual remarks. But I think that advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland is a shared wish and a shared responsibility of compatriots on both sides. Our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. We have the confidence, the means, and the capability to improve and develop cross-Strait relations by containing “Taiwan independence,” by safeguarding the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and by expanding and deepening exchanges and cooperation across the Strait in economic, cultural and other fields. This will benefit compatriots on both sides, and we will work together to achieve the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201810/t20181031_12107896.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-11-08","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, the El Salvador President said on November 7 that China will give his country financial aids for social and technological projects. Can you confirm that? Doesn't this sound like the \"dollar diplomacy\" that Taiwan is always accusing the Chinese side of practicing when it tries to win over its \"allies\"?","First of all I have to emphasize that China's support and assistance for El Salvador don't bear the slightest resemblance to the so-called \"dollar diplomacy\" as Taiwan alleged.\nOn November 1, President Xi Jinping held talks with El Salvadoran President Salvador Sanchez Ceren in Beijing. We issued a detailed news release then. President Xi Jinping stressed that the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and El Salvador conforms to the historical trend and is in line with the fundamental and long-term interests of the two countries. China stands ready to work together with El Salvador to steadily and rapidly advance the friendly exchanges and cooperation between the two countries for the benefit of the two peoples. The Chinese side is willing to cooperate with the Salvadoran side in infrastructure and other fields under the principle of government offering guidance, enterprises as the main player, market operation, win-win results and mutual benefit, and support competent Chinese enterprises in investing in El Salvador. The Chinese side is willing to provide support to El Salvador in education, medical care, water supply, disaster prevention, etc. It is also willing to provide more scholarships to El Salvador, strengthen cooperation in human resources training, and list El Salvador as a destination for outbound Chinese tourist groups. The friendly exchanges and cooperation between China and El Salvador are rapidly progressing.\nAs to reports you cited as saying that China will provide financial aids to El Salvador, I want to stress once again that China-El Salvador relations are based on political principles and aimed for common development. In the spirit of friendship between the two countries and South-South cooperation, China is willing to provide assistance for the economic and social development of El Salvador as its capacity allows. The assistance will focus on El Salvador's urgent livelihood needs, such as food and water supply equipment for disaster-stricken areas and learning devices for poor students so as to benefit the society and ordinary people in El Salvador.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1611573.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2018-11-14","Hua Chunying","","I have two questions. First, US Vice President Mike Pence will attend APEC and has plans to hold a meeting with Taiwan's APEC representative. Is this acceptable within the bounds of the relevant MOU, or is this an instance of the US side sending a wrong signal to the Taiwan authorities? Second, after a coup in Fiji in 2006, many Western countries withdrew their involvement in Fiji, but China stepped up its…","Your first question involves two aspects: Taiwan's participation in the APEC events and the exchanges between the US and Taiwan. Adhering to the one-China principle and observing the stipulations in the relevant MOU is the basis and prerequisite for Taiwan's participation in APEC. Any party should abide by the one-China principle instead of playing any tricks. Regarding the exchanges between the US and Taiwan, our position is also very firm. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and refrain from having any form of official exchanges with Taiwan.\nYou also mentioned China-Fiji relations. First of all, in response to your viewpoint, I want to make clear that China never believes that a certain country or region should become the sphere of influence of another country or several countries. We maintain that all countries, big or small, are all equal. All countries should refrain from interfering in other countries' domestic affairs and fully respect the development path chosen by other countries as well as their right to independently decide with which countries they will develop ties and conduct cooperation.\nYesterday, the Foreign Ministry gave a press briefing on President Xi Jinping's attendance at the 26th APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting, his state visits to Papua New Guinea, Brunei and the Philippines and his meetings with the leaders from the Pacific Island countries that have established diplomatic ties with China. Vice Foreign Minister Zheng Zeguang answered the questions in a detailed way raised by journalists on the Pacific Island countries. I only want to stress one point. China's ties with Fiji and other Pacific Island countries are South-South cooperation as well as the mutual support and assistance between developing countries. We hope that the general election in Fiji can be held smoothly. We hope to develop friendly and cooperative relations with Fiji and other Pacific Island countries under the principles of mutual respect, equality, mutual benefit and non-interference in each other's domestic affairs. We believe that President Xi Jinping's upcoming meetings with the leaders from the Pacific Island countries that have established diplomatic ties with China in Papua New Guinea will map out new blueprint and open up new prospects for the growth of China's ties with Fiji and other Pacific Island countries going forward.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1613116.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1613056.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Please introduce the progress in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.” It is reported that some local public institutions have opened public recruitment to Taiwan compatriots. In response, Taiwan’s MAC said it will examine whether these positions endanger Taiwan’s security and will investigate and handle them if necessary. What is your comment on this?","Since the “31 Measures” were issued and implemented, all regions and departments have earnestly and comprehensively carried them out and have successively introduced specific measures. Since late October, three more localities, Henan Province, Qingdao City in Shandong Province, and Shaoxing City in Zhejiang Province, have introduced concrete measures for implementation. To date, 43 localities in 19 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities have, based on local conditions, introduced specific methods to implement the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”\nThe Ministry of Water Resources has also introduced specific methods for the water resources aspects of the “31 Measures.” First, to implement “Taiwan-funded enterprises may participate in water infrastructure construction through franchise operations,” it encourages Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in the construction and operation of water conservancy projects, and the Ministry has simplified related administrative approvals to create a favorable environment for Taiwan-funded enterprises to enter the market. Second, regarding Taiwan residents taking occupational qualification examinations, it has designated the Fujian Water Conservancy and Electric Power Vocational Skills College and the Zhejiang Water Conservancy and Hydropower Cadre School as pilot appraisal stations for Taiwan residents taking the national occupational qualification examination for water facility operation and maintenance personnel. In addition, the Ministry of Water Resources is working to finalize the “Interim Provisions on the Occupational Qualification System for Water Engineering Quality Inspectors,” which will specify the requirements for Taiwan residents to take the examination.\nIn the process of local and departmental implementation of the 31 Measures, some local public institutions have hired Taiwan compatriots through public recruitment and similar methods. This is a concrete expression of providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, and has been welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities, however, have obstructed this and continually raised the stakes, depriving the Taiwan public of their rights to employment and development and of their aspiration for a better life. This can only further alienate the hearts of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181114_12112701.htm"],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said the mainland will regulate the participation of Taiwan residents in social insurance on the mainland; only pension and unemployment insurance are exempted, while medical insurance is retained. In effect, this increases the burden of “double enrollment” in insurance for Taiwan compatriots across the Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The statement by the Mainland Affairs Council is nothing but confusing the public, misleading public opinion, and deceiving the people of Taiwan. Taiwan residents participating in social insurance on the mainland do not create any increased personal burden, and it is conducive to enhancing the personal rights and interests and safeguarding of Taiwan compatriots. The relevant policy is already explained very clearly in the Interim Measures on Taiwan Residents' Participation in Social Insurance on the Mainland.\nAllow me to specify this here. Taiwan residents participating in mainland social insurance fall into five categories: pension insurance, unemployment insurance, work-related injury insurance, maternity insurance and medical insurance. According to the Interim Measures, first, Taiwan residents who have already participated in social insurance in Taiwan and continue to retain their social insurance relationship there may choose not to participate in pension and unemployment insurance on the mainland. Second, work-related injury and maternity insurance are paid entirely by mainland employers, with no contribution required from individuals. Third, medical insurance contributions are paid jointly by mainland employers and individuals, but the entirety of the individual contributions and a portion of the employer contributions are credited to the insured person's individual account, which belongs entirely to the Taiwan compatriot for personal use. Moreover, the balance in the insured Taiwan compatriot's account can be withdrawn in a lump sum when the basic medical insurance relationship is terminated, and if the insured person dies, the account can be inherited in accordance with the law. All of this fully demonstrates that the relevant policy not only does not increase the burden on Taiwan compatriots, but is instead conducive to enhancing their personal rights and interests and safeguards.\nI want to emphasize that the “31 Measures” we introduced reflect the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait as one family.” They aim to provide more favorable conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to live, work, and start businesses and innovate on the mainland, and to share in the mainland's development opportunities. This is beneficial to compatriots on both sides and has been widely praised by Taiwan compatriots. However, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities keep fabricating all kinds of rumors to deceive the Taiwanese public and restrict Taiwan compatriots from gaining greater and better development opportunities, in order to achieve their aim of undermining cross-Strait relations. These actions harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181114_12112702.htm"],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The first China International Import Expo has successfully concluded. The mainland has announced the national strategy for the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta, and Taiwan businesses have welcomed this new opening-up opportunity. What is your comment?","When General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a keynote speech at the opening ceremony of the first China International Import Expo, he noted that China will support the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta region and elevate it to a national strategy, focus on implementing the new development philosophy, build a modern economic system, advance deeper reform and higher-level opening to the outside world from a higher starting point, and coordinate with the Belt and Road Initiative, the coordinated development of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei, the development of the Yangtze River Economic Belt, and the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, to improve the spatial layout of China's reform and opening-up. The mainland's policies and measures to deepen reform and expand opening up will enable Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to share the opportunities and achievements of the mainland's development to a greater extent and in a wider scope.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181114_12112703.htm"],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the participation of Taiwan enterprises in the first China International Import Expo.","The first China International Import Expo (CIIE) specially set up a Taiwan exhibition area within the China Pavilion, themed “Taiwan? Qin,” which derives from and embodies the concept that “Both sides of the Strait are one family,” to showcase the achievements of cross-Strait economic cooperation over the 40 years of reform and opening up. During the CIIE, the Taiwan exhibition area attracted large numbers of visitors, and the Taiwan enterprises and products on display were also widely welcomed. Cross-Strait enterprises signed a batch of purchase orders, demonstrating the enormous potential of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. It is understood that some Taiwan enterprises have already begun registering to exhibit at next year's CIIE.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently emphasized, at a seminar marking the third anniversary of the meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, the importance of the \"1992 Consensus\" for the development of cross-Strait relations. He proposed maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the principles of \"not excluding unification, not supporting 'Taiwan independence,' and not using force.\"…","The one-China principle is the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. Realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants and the fundamental interest of the Chinese nation.\nThe 2015 meeting between the leaders of the two sides consolidated and deepened the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, opened a historic page in cross-Strait relations, and has milestone significance. Under the current situation of cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides should jointly uphold the correct path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","Taiwan's \"Nine-in-One\" elections are about to be held, and the DPP authorities claim that the mainland is interfering in and suppressing Taiwan, and are advocating that Taiwan's people resist the mainland. What is the comment?","The DPP authorities deliberately create estrangement between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, raise hostility, and damage cross-Strait relations in order to gain electoral benefit. Attempting to repeatedly deceive the broad Taiwan public with such practices underestimates the judgment of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Taiwan authorities sent TSMC founder Morris Chang as their representative to attend this year's APEC summit. May I ask the spokesperson whether the mainland leader will meet with Morris Chang, and if a meeting takes place, what topics would be discussed?","Regarding the question you asked, I currently have no information on this. We have also stated on multiple occasions that the question of Taiwan's participation in APEC-related activities should comply with the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Regarding Taiwan's “nine-in-one” elections, some candidates have said that the mainland provided funds to secretly assist specific candidates. Please clarify.","As everyone knows, we never interfere in Taiwan's elections. This claim is entirely groundless and fabricated out of thin air. We ask Taiwan compatriots not to believe it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","Recently, local governments across the mainland have successively announced institutional adjustments. In some provinces, such as Fujian, the Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office has been merged with the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office to form the Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office. However, Beijing and Shanghai still maintain separate municipal Taiwan Affairs Offices and Hong Kong and Macao Affairs…","Thank you for your concern about our work on Taiwan affairs. Deepening the reform of local Party and government institutions is an important measure for advancing the modernization of the national governance system and governance capacity. As I understand it, in this institutional reform, some provinces have adjusted the structure of their Taiwan Affairs Offices in light of local realities.\nI want to stress that no matter how they are adjusted, all levels of Taiwan Affairs Offices will continue to adhere to the central government's major policies on Taiwan, work to promote the development of cross-Strait relations and the peaceful process of national reunification, and, as always, wholeheartedly serve Taiwan compatriots and help them resolve their difficulties. Taiwan Affairs Offices will always be a home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","There has been widespread speculation recently that the National Palace Museum in Taipei will undergo renovation, and that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities plan to move these cultural relics south to the “Nanyuan” (Southern Branch) for exhibition. This is obviously a move made for the sake of elections. The DPP is “de-Sinicizing” on one hand, while on the other hand it wants to use these Chinese…","We have seen the relevant reports, and we have also seen criticism and questioning from Taiwan’s cultural circles and people from all walks of life. I believe the purpose of the DPP authorities in doing this is clear, and Taiwan public opinion has already passed judgment on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je recently said that the issue of “unification and independence” has overshadowed Taiwan for more than 20 years. He also said that “unification and independence” is a false issue, because the United States will not allow Taiwan to “become independent” at this stage, nor will it allow the mainland and Taiwan to unify. Please give the Taiwan Affairs Office's response.","Our policies, positions and attitudes—adhering to the one-China principle, opposing “Taiwan independence,” promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and advancing the process of peacefully achieving national reunification—are clear and consistent. Regarding some people and matters in Taiwan’s elections, we will not comment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《联合报》记者","In this election in Taiwan, a total of 10 referendum proposals were held concurrently. I wonder what the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment is on this? In addition, one of these referendum proposals is the “Olympic name-correction referendum.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have repeatedly stated our position on the so-called “Olympic name-rectification referendum.” We have also noted that many groups and individuals on the island who care about the immediate interests of Taiwan athletes have expressed concern and opposition. They believe the so-called “Olympic name-rectification referendum” is a “gamble bound to lose,” a political manipulation that stakes the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and that it is in fact harmful to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that the mainland is waging so-called \"Three Warfares\" against Taiwan through new technology, new networks and new media, using \"false information\" to attack the Taiwan authorities. What is your response?","Her remarks themselves are fake news and fake information, not worth refuting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The online shopping festival “Double Eleven” is popular not only on the mainland but has also sparked a craze in Taiwan. The Industrial Economics and Knowledge Center of the Taiwan Institute for Information Industry recently conducted a survey on netizens’ intentions to shop during “Double Eleven” and found that 63.5% of netizens plan to take part in this year’s “Double Eleven,” continuing to rise from 57.1% in…","Over the weekend that just passed, several mainland e-commerce platforms held “Double Eleven” shopping events, which received enthusiastic responses from people and enterprises on both sides of the Strait. We have noted that Taiwan residents and Taiwan e-commerce businesses actively participated, and many Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland put products on offer and carried out promotions. On the world's largest online trade platform, Taiwan compatriots are both consumers and sellers. This has played a positive role in stimulating consumption in Taiwan and expanding export trade. Therefore, this is a matter of mutual benefit and win-win for both sides across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","On October 31, Raymond Greene (郦英杰), Director of the Taipei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan, declared at his first press conference after taking office that the US has an obligation to support Taiwan in maintaining sufficient self-defense capabilities to counter coercion. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region, and the development of military ties in any form. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, and to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181114_12112704.htm"],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报团结网记者","Little more than a month remains until the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan.” Will the mainland hold commemorative activities?","On New Year's Day 1979, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress issued the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan,” solemnly declaring the major policy of striving for peaceful reunification of the motherland and clearly setting forth a series of policy measures for developing cross-Strait relations and promoting the process of peaceful reunification. Over the past forty years, through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, many of the policy propositions put forward in the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan” have become reality. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides should work together to uphold the political foundation and correct path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resolutely oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, carry on the past and open up the future, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","I would like to ask again about the Taiwan regional elections. The vote is coming up soon. Some voices on the island say that at this stage, in the face of various provocations from the Green camp, the mainland must keep its composure; otherwise it may fall into the DPP's trap and push the election situation in Taiwan in an unfavorable direction. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Thank you for your concern, but we will not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾三立电视台记者","During the recent cross-Strait debate, Ke Wenzhe promoted the message of “cross-Strait as one family.” Yao Wenzhi repeatedly said he was “pro-China,” and Ke Wenzhe said he was being labeled as “red.” Another opponent, Ding Shouzhong, said he deceives blue, deceives green, and deceives Beijing. Ke Wenzhe said that in fact he simply does not want to see cross-Strait relations as tense as they are now. How do you…","As I just said, our policy on Taiwan is clear. We carry out cross-Strait city exchanges on the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, and our attitude and position are also clear. I stress again that regarding people and events in island elections, we will not comment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Just now, reporters also raised the issue of the “three no's” principle mentioned by Ma Ying-jeou, and Tsai Ing-wen also responded, saying “absolutely do not accept cross-strait unification.” What is the spokesperson's comment? Second, regarding the cross-strait Zijin Mountain Summit, does the spokesperson have any latest information to share with everyone?","Regarding your first question, I already answered it just now, and you may consider it carefully. As for the second question, regarding the annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, as far as I know, the host units on both sides are in close communication. There is confirmed news, and it will be released in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Defense Minister Wei Fenghe said at the press conference after the second round of the China-US Diplomatic and Security Dialogue that if Taiwan splits from China, China will, as the United States did in its Civil War, defend national sovereignty at any cost. The US side said it opposes any unilateral action aimed at changing the status quo, including resorting to force or coercion. What is the spokesperson's…","Since 2016, who has unilaterally undermined the political foundation and the good situation of peaceful cross-Strait relations, and who has damaged the achievements of peaceful cross-Strait relations? In fact, Americans should be clear about this. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and involves China’s core interests. Our determination and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity are unwavering. We will never allow any person, any organization, or any political party to split any piece of Chinese territory away from China, at any time, in any way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan's “Nine-in-One” elections will be held next week. Some media reported that on the eve of the elections, Taiwan's authorities may conduct live-fire exercises in the waters around Taiping Island. How does the spokesperson respond to this?","I believe that all the moves, statements and conduct related to the election will be judged by Taiwan's voters themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Recently, because Li Mingzhe was transferred between facilities twice, his wife has been unable to visit him, and some people in Taiwan are very worried about him. May I ask whether the spokesperson has information on his current situation?","According to our understanding, Li Mingzhe was transferred back to Chishan Prison in Hunan on October 28, 2018. Regarding family visits, the prison has, through appropriate means, explained to his family members the reasons why visits are temporarily not possible this time. Since Li Mingzhe began serving his sentence, the prison has consistently handled family visits in accordance with the law. His family members have also visited him many times, and visits will continue to be arranged in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","Last week, when two frigates that Taiwan purchased from the United States were commissioned, the Taiwan military said on Facebook that it has high hopes for this warship. It said it would not only work hard on combat readiness training, but also that it feels it is fully prepared. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","We have said many times that the important guarantees for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are upholding the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Any attempt to rely on force to confront is without a future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-14","Ma Xiaoguang","美联社记者","Regarding Taiwan's so-called “Olympic name-change referendum,” the Taiwan Affairs Office previously said that Taiwan would “swallow the bitter fruit.” What is the specific meaning of “bitter fruit”? Will the mainland ask the International Olympic Committee to impose sanctions?","As you may have noticed, the International Olympic Committee has repeatedly indicated to the Taiwan side its opposition to changing the name, and we have also repeatedly stated our position. Moreover, recently, sports circles and people from all walks of life on the island have also said that the eligibility and rights of Taiwan athletes to compete should not be used as political bets.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181114_12112709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 25 (Reporter Chen Jianxing): The results of Taiwan's “Nine-in-One” local elections were announced on the 25th. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions: We have noted the results of this election. The results reflect the strong desire of the broad Taiwan public to continue sharing the “dividends” of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to improve economic livelihoods. We will continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, and walk the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. On the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, we welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to participate in cross-Strait city exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181125_12115704.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","BEIJING, Nov. 25 (Xinhua) (Reporter Chen Jianxing) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 25th that the failure of the so-called “Olympic name-change referendum” shows that gambling with the interests of Taiwan athletes is unpopular, and that “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181125_12115705.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Please introduce the latest progress in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.” Localities and departments have successively rolled out specific measures. What highlights do these measures have? Please give examples of the results achieved.","Since late November, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, Wuhan City in Hubei Province, Dongguan City in Guangdong Province, and Wuxi and Yangzhou cities in Jiangsu Province have also rolled out specific measures implementing the \"31 Measures.\" To date, 49 localities in 20 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities have introduced specific implementation measures based on local conditions. Among the specific measures rolled out by various regions and departments, many have local characteristics, have made a strong impression, and have drawn wide attention and praise. For example, Beijing clearly stipulates that Taiwan-invested enterprises in the Zhongguancun Demonstration Zone are encouraged to obtain bank loans by pledging intellectual property rights, and projects that pass review may receive corresponding subsidies; Shanghai clearly stipulates that it supports Taiwan-invested enterprises in participating in the display, sales and procurement activities of the China International Import Expo; Jiangsu clearly stipulates that it regularly holds the \"Zifeng Award\" selection activity targeting Taiwan-invested enterprises, and award-winning enterprises may enjoy relevant industrial policy support; Fujian clearly stipulates that it implements a \"source management, port clearance\" model for rapid clearance of Fujian-Taiwan goods, and expands the scope of recognition of third-party test results for Taiwan imported goods; Guizhou clearly stipulates that it supports Taiwan-invested enterprises in participating in the development of Guizhou's big data electronic information industry and in the strategic action of \"Healthy Guizhou\"; Inner Mongolia clearly stipulates that it supports Taiwan-invested enterprises in participating in the construction of the \"China-Mongolia-Russia Economic Corridor\" and in key exhibitions in the autonomous region, such as the China-Mongolia Expo.\nAt present, the implementation and advancement of the \"31 Measures\" have achieved remarkable results. I can group and illustrate them with examples.\n1. In the fields of culture, education and science and technology, Fujian Province and the National Natural Science Foundation of China jointly established the \"Cross-Strait Science and Technology Cooperation Joint Fund,\" which approved 107 projects with funding of 273 million yuan, and more than 130 Taiwan scientists participated in project research.\n2. In terms of Taiwan compatriots' participation in various honorary awards, dozens of Taiwan compatriots in Hubei, Jiangsu and Jiangxi have already been awarded local honorary titles such as \"Three-Eight Red Banner Pacesetter,\" \"May Day Labor Honor Medal\" and \"Youth May Fourth Medal.\"\n3. In cross-strait film and television cooperation, restrictions on the number of Taiwan personnel that mainland radio and television programs and TV series productions may hire have been lifted. Restrictions on the proportion of key creative personnel, mainland elements and investment ratios for cross-strait co-produced TV series have all been removed. Taiwan personnel are actively participating in the production of mainland radio and television programs. Radio and television authorities in Beijing, Shanghai, Xinjiang and other places have received letters of intent from many cross-strait production companies for co-produced TV series and documentaries. Several Taiwan production companies are actively preparing cross-strait co-produced films.\n4. In terms of financial support, Fujian has seen five Taiwan-invested projects, including Huajiacai, receive special subsidies totaling 18.3 million yuan and technology transformation fund investments of 460 million yuan. The Cross-Strait Joint Research and Development Center for Integrated Optoelectronic Technology, jointly established by both sides, and the Southeast Automobile Research Institute received a combined 16.3 million yuan in funding. Three Taiwan companies in Jiangsu, including Huiju Pharmaceutical in Haimen, received provincial science and technology achievement transformation special funds, totaling 17.5 million yuan in science and technology funding.\n5. In participating in public infrastructure construction, the Taiwan company Advantech Technology reached a strategic cooperation agreement with the Kunshan Jiaofa Group and will provide professional solutions for intelligent transportation in Kunshan. Six projects are currently in the design stage and will be implemented locally by optimizing government procurement processes and promoting products of Taiwan-invested enterprises.\n6. In agriculture, Taiwan companies such as Xianhuo Juice and Boli Foods were selected as provincial key leading agricultural industrialization enterprises in Jiangsu. Three Taiwan-invested agricultural enterprises in Fujian, including Jichen Agriculture and Forestry Technology, enjoy agricultural machinery purchase subsidies, and 13 agricultural machinery products from Taiwan companies have been included in the agricultural machinery purchase subsidy product catalogue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117394.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","After the “nine-in-one” elections, Tsai Ing-wen, when resigning as chairperson of the DPP, said that over the past three years Taiwan has been on the right path and will continue to adhere to the existing course. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Since taking office, the DPP authorities have unilaterally undermined the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, supported and tolerated all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, obstructed and restricted exchanges and cooperation between people on both sides, relied on foreign powers to enhance their own standing, and repeatedly put forward separatist fallacies full of the “two-state theory” as well as confrontational statements and actions against the mainland. This has raised hostility across the Strait, made the situation in cross-Strait relations complex and grave, and seriously harmed the interests of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities should reflect deeply, heed the strong desire of the Taiwan people to continue sharing the “dividends” of peaceful cross-Strait development and to improve their economic livelihoods, and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and to the correct path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by abandoning the “Taiwan independence” position and recognizing the “1992 Consensus” can the DPP and its authorities find a way out in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117392.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","In this Taiwan county and city magistrate election, Kaohsiung also “turned upside down.” Han Kuo-yu (韩国瑜) again proposed recognizing the “1992 Consensus,” hoping to sell Kaohsiung’s agricultural products and help the local tourism industry. What is the mainland’s response to his proposal?","The \"1992 Consensus\" is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be safeguarded and enhanced. On the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of cross-Strait city exchanges, we welcome more counties and cities in Taiwan, including Kaohsiung, to take part in cross-Strait city exchanges and cooperation, so as to jointly enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nFacts have proven that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides should expand personnel exchanges, deepen economic and trade interactions, and strengthen exchanges in culture and other fields, so as to benefit from exchanges and cooperation and achieve greater and better development. Yesterday everyone also saw good news: mainland tourism operators have already organized groups to travel to Kaohsiung, and I think this is a good start. At the same time, I must also point out that over the past two-plus years, what has truly affected cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and obstructed Taiwan compatriots from benefiting is the obstacles set up by the DPP authorities. The sooner these obstacles are removed, the greater the benefit to Taiwan compatriots, and the easier it will be for them to realize their pursuit of economic development and improved livelihoods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117393.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","Continuing on the “nine-in-one” elections: everyone has seen the election results. What impact will the election results have on cross-Strait relations? Will the mainland's Taiwan policy be adjusted?","We have seen the election results and stated our position to the outside world in the early hours of that same day. Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. We will continue to uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and to oppose “Taiwan independence.” We will keep expanding and deepening cross-Strait economic, cultural and other exchanges and cooperation, and steadfastly work for the well-being of compatriots on both sides. We will continue to uphold the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and take the lead in sharing with Taiwan compatriots the opportunities and achievements of mainland development. We will gradually provide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses with better development opportunities and greater development space, so that Taiwan compatriots gain more tangible benefits and achieve greater and better development. We will unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117395.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2018 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting will be held in Xiamen. Could the spokesperson introduce the preparations?","Since its establishment in 2013, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit has held five annual meetings. The organizers of the summit, adhering to the purpose of “deepening cross-Strait industrial integration and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations,” have fully leveraged the advantage of the summit as the most important civil exchange and cooperation platform for business circles across the Strait, continuously promoted close connections between business circles on both sides, and played a positive role in promoting industrial cooperation across the Strait and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nAfter consultation, this year’s annual summit will be held in Xiamen from December 3 to 5, with the theme: “New measures for integration, new business opportunities shared.” Activities will include an opening ceremony, keynote speeches, eight thematic forums, and a closing ceremony. Approximately 1,100 attendees in total, including well-known entrepreneurs across the Strait, heads of business organizations, and representatives of small and medium-sized enterprises and young entrepreneurs, will take part. Here, on behalf of the organizers, I warmly welcome everyone to go there to cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117391.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Last year's first Cross-Strait Students Baseball League drew great attention. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant details of this year's second Cross-Strait Students Baseball League?","The first Cross-Strait Student Baseball League, successfully held last year, drew strong response and high praise on both sides of the Strait, especially among young students, and became a widely followed cross-Strait sports exchange event for youth. A year has passed, and the grand final of the second Cross-Strait Student Baseball League will be held in Shenzhen, Guangdong, from December 1 to 8. As I understand it, after nearly a year of qualifying rounds and stage competitions, and selection across more than 200 primary, secondary, and tertiary schools on both sides of the Strait, the scale of this year's grand final has been further expanded: the number of participating teams has increased from 32 to 42, and a U10 age group has been added. The number of matches has increased from 64 last year to 100. There are 888 players from both sides of the Strait in total, of whom 441 are from 20 Taiwan-region teams, representing 10 counties and cities across the island.\nPreparations for the event are currently being pushed forward, and Shenzhen City is also ready. We look forward to the baseball youngsters on both sides of the Strait adding further brilliance to this sports exchange festival for cross-Strait youth. Likewise, on behalf of the host organizers, I also welcome everyone to visit and cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201811/t20181128_12117390.htm"],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Shanghai and Taipei have each announced that they will hold a Twin City Forum in Taipei next month. Please introduce the relevant situation.","We have clearly stated that, on the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of city exchanges across the Strait, we hope to continuously strengthen exchanges and cooperation between cities on both sides, and we also welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to participate, jointly enhancing the affection and well-being of people on both sides.\nAs everyone knows, the ‘Shanghai-Taipei City Forum’ has been held alternately in Shanghai and Taipei every year since 2010, and it has become a established practice and an important platform for exchanges between the two cities and between compatriots on both sides. Over these years, the forum has reached many points of consensus on economy, culture, technology, society, sports, urban management, and other topics, and has achieved positive results in enhancing the well-being of residents in both places. We hope this forum can be held smoothly on the island, further deepen exchanges between Shanghai and Taiwan in all fields, and enhance the interests and well-being of residents in both places.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Before the “Nine-in-One” elections, the DPP played the “unification versus independence” card, saying that “fake news” and “fake polls” flooded the election campaign. But judging from the election results, the so-called “unification versus independence” card did not work. How does the spokesperson assess this?","I have repeatedly said that we do not evaluate Taiwan's elections and do not interfere. But I have also said here many times that recently, some people and forces at home and abroad have spread all kinds of rumors, slandered and smeared the mainland, sought to manufacture a sense of victimhood, stir up confrontation, and seek electoral gains, and sabotage cross-Strait relations. Facts have fully proven that they underestimated the judgment of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","What is your comment on the outcome of this “Olympic name-rectification referendum”? Where is Lee Ming-che currently detained, and when can his wife meet with him again?","First question: as you may have noticed, we stated on the morning of the 25th that the so-called “Olympic name-correction referendum” case was defeated. This shows that gambling with the interests of Taiwanese athletes is unpopular, and that “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail.\nSecond question: as I introduced at the previous two press conferences, Li Mingzhe is still in Chishan Prison in Hunan. I also said that since he entered prison, visits have never been a problem. His family members have visited him in the past, and in the future, at an appropriate time, the prison authorities will again make visiting arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Continuing the previous question about the referendum on renaming for the Tokyo Olympics: because of the referendum on renaming for the Tokyo Olympics, Taichung City was stripped of its right to host the first East Asian Youth Games. Now that the referendum on renaming for the Tokyo Olympics has been rejected, it is reported that Lu Shiow-yan, the Kuomintang mayor-elect of Taichung City, has said that after…","The cancellation of the 2019 Taichung East Asian Youth Games was a collective decision made by the East Asian Olympic Committees Council.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾ETtoday新闻云记者","The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum is tentatively scheduled for December 20. When Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je was recently asked whether he would again mention “both sides of the Strait are one family,” he said: Ko Wen-je is still Ko Wen-je, Taipei is still Taipei, and the Twin City Forum is still the Twin City Forum. Compared with Kaohsiung mayor-elect Han Kuo-yu, who acknowledged the “1992 Consensus,” should Ko Wen-je…","As long as there is a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of the nature of city-to-city exchanges across the Strait, we welcome exchanges between cities on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","At present, the average number of tourists visiting Taiwan is less than 5,000 per day. Now the “Blue camp” holds 15 seats among counties and cities. Do you expect the number of visitors to Taiwan to increase?","As I just said, due to changes in the situation on the island, and on the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-strait relations and of cross-strait urban exchanges, cross-strait urban exchanges should in the future be broader in scope and larger in scale. But I have also said that the fundamental factor affecting and obstructing cross-strait exchanges over the past two years is the restrictive policies of the DPP authorities. Whether the expectations everyone has now can be implemented smoothly still needs to be observed. Conversely, the earlier this obstacle is removed, the sooner compatriots on both sides of the Strait will benefit from exchanges and interactions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","The large-scale exhibition commemorating the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up, now underway, has attracted wide attention. Please introduce the content in the exhibition related to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and how you evaluate the participation of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in the process of reform and opening up on the mainland.","The “Great Transformation: Exhibition Celebrating the 40th Anniversary of Reform and Opening Up” is being held at the National Museum of China and has attracted wide attention and enthusiastic responses. In the fourth exhibition zone, “Historic Transformation,” through focusing on the major events, important matters, and happy occasions in the development of cross-Strait relations over the past 40 years, and through rich historical photographs, texts, videos, and physical scenes, it clearly outlines the process by which compatriots from Taiwan have actively participated in reform and opening up and promoted the development of cross-Strait relations. Some high-tech products of Taiwanese enterprises are also featured in the exhibition. I am also pleased to see that the Taiwanese media present here have reported on the exhibition.\nWhat I want to say here is that over the 40 years of reform and opening up, the mainland has increasingly become a fertile ground where Taiwan compatriots can invest, start businesses, and live and work in peace. While achieving their own development and growth, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises have also made important contributions to the economic and social development of the mainland. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have joined hands and worked together in the great historical current of reform and opening up, helping each other through hardship and moving forward, and have written a magnificent chapter. In the future, we are willing to continue sharing the opportunities and achievements of the mainland's development with Taiwan compatriots, further deepen cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation, and let Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises obtain more real benefits and greater, better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We know that the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan” was issued 40 years ago, and it can be said that it opened the ice-breaking situation across the Strait. Now that the “nine-in-one” elections on the island have just concluded, and the stalemate across the Strait seems to see a glimmer of dawn, may I ask the spokesperson: in the context of the new era, will the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan” be given new…","As I said last time, the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” published 40 years ago, solemnly declared our major policy for striving for the peaceful reunification of the motherland. Over these 40 years, as everyone has seen, some of the policy propositions in the 《告台湾同胞书》 have become reality, and through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, the overall picture of cross-Strait relations has undergone profound historic changes. Of course, under the new situation of cross-Strait relations, we will continue to uphold the central government’s major policies on Taiwan work, unite Taiwan compatriots to strive together, and continue to advance the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, at the APEC meeting held this month, U.S. Vice President Mike Pence, when meeting with Morris Chang, a representative from Taiwan, mentioned that cooperation between Taiwan and the United States is the best option, and the Taiwan side proposed a so-called Taiwan-U.S. free trade agreement. May I ask for your response to this?","We have repeatedly reiterated that we firmly oppose any form of official contact between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and Taiwan. This is our consistent position. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already lodged serious representations with the relevant parties on this matter. Participation by Taiwan-side personnel in APEC meetings must conform to the one-China principle and the provisions of the relevant memorandum of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Recently, media reported that Han Guoyu, the KMT-affiliated mayor-elect of Kaohsiung, said in an interview that the “1992 Consensus” is his view of cross-Strait relations. May I ask the spokesperson how you view Han Guoyu's statement on cross-Strait relations? In addition, the term “1992 Consensus” and similar terms have now become hot search terms on the island; Kaohsiung residents' searches for “1992 Consensus”…","We have repeatedly reaffirmed that the “1992 Consensus” is the foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it is also a consensus reached through authorization by both sides. With this consensus, cross-Strait relations can continue to improve and develop, and the interests of compatriots on both sides can achieve mutual benefit and win-win outcomes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志社记者","On November 26, the mainland published a list of one hundred outstanding contributors to reform and opening up to be commended, and Mr. Lin Yifu, as the only Taiwan-born compatriot selected, has been included. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","As I mentioned just now, during the 40 years of reform and opening up, compatriots from Taiwan made important contributions to the mainland’s reform, opening up and socioeconomic development. I think Mr. Lin Yifu (林毅夫) is a typical representative of them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Second question. You just mentioned fake news, which reminds me that before the election, rumors were widely circulated in Taiwan that the mainland would start banning the Golden Horse Awards next year. Please confirm this.","You may have noticed that we have officially clarified that the news report you mentioned from a media outlet with a particular stance was a blatant fake news story. Of course, the Golden Horse Awards are a platform for film professionals on both sides of the Strait to exchange ideas, and compatriots on both sides should cherish it together. This time, some political forces used cross-Strait film exchange activities to make \"Taiwan independence\" remarks and create political incidents. I believe such conduct is unpopular and has been condemned by public opinion on the island. Therefore, we hope that film and television circles and people from all sectors on both sides of the Strait will work together to do more things that promote film and television exchanges across the Strait and jointly resist such disruptive words and deeds.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Kuomintang Chairman Wu Dunyi has not been able to visit the mainland since he was elected last year. With the major shifts in the island’s political landscape after this “Nine-in-One” election, will a meeting between the leaders of the KMT and the CPC be put on the agenda?","We are willing to strengthen exchanges and dialogue with all Taiwan political parties that adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” to jointly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan region, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and advance the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-11-28","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","All 15 newly elected KMT county and city magistrates have explicitly stated that they uphold the “1992 Consensus” and will engage in cross-Strait exchanges to boost the economy. Recently, Lai Ching-te, head of the Taiwan authorities’ executive branch, claimed that because the newly elected KMT county and city magistrates have won public support, the Taiwan executive branch will respect it if they use the “1992…","I would like to say that if they are truly willing to accept good advice, they should return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and return to the correct path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201811/t20181128_12117402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-11-29","Geng Shuang","","The US Navy has sent two warships through the Taiwan Strait on Wednesday. What is China's response?","The Chinese side has been closely monitoring from start to end the passage by the US warships through the Taiwan Strait. We have expressed our concern to the US side.\nThe Taiwan issue concerns the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China. It is the most important and sensitive issue in the China-US relations. We urge the US to observe the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid undermining China-US relations and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1617471.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1617387.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2018-11-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Two US navy ships sailed through the Taiwan Strait on Nov. 28. It’s the third time this year. Has the National Defense Ministry of China expressed concern about this with the US government?","The Chinese military is aware of the sailing of the US ships across the Taiwan Straits and all movements of the US ships. We hope the US side can abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three Sino-US Joint Communiques, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues so as not to undermine China-US relations and peace and stability in the region. The Chinese military will remain on high alert and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-11/30/content_4830790.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-11-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, the Defense Strategy Committee, which is made up of people from across the political spectrum in the United States, said in a report to the U.S. Congress in the middle of this month that the American military's deterrent capability is weakening and once China \"attacks Taiwan\", the US seems unable to use its military pressure to \"force China to stop\". What is your comment? My second…","The relevant report of the U.S. has deliberately instigated antagonism between the mainland and Taiwan and hyped up confrontation between China and the United States, to which we are firmly opposed. The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, as well as its core interests. It is the most important and sensitive core issue in China-U.S. relationship. The Chinese military is firm in its resolve and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nOn the second question, the visit is part of an annual plan. In recent years, exchanges and cooperation between Chinese and Japanese defense authorities have made some progress. We hope the Japanese side can work together with the Chinese side to follow the improving momentum of bilateral relations, strengthen defense exchanges and cooperation, properly handle differences and provide positive energy for the sustained and stable development of bilateral relations and regional peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-11/30/content_4830790.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-11-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan media reported that the so-called Taiwanese military will conduct a ground shooting exercise in waters around the Taiping Island in the South China Sea from November 30th to December 1st, and it might also test-fire US-made air defense missiles. What is your comment?","We are aware of related movement. I want to stress that China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands and their related waters and that the Chinese people across the straits share the common responsibility to safeguard the assets left by our ancestors.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-11/30/content_4830790.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Good morning, friends from the media. I will first release one piece of information. On December 10, Chiang Pin-kung, the Taiwan-side vice chairman of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, former vice chairman of the Kuomintang, and former chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, unfortunately passed away. We are deeply saddened and reluctant to see him go. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council; Zhang Zhijun, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Association; and former chairmen Chen Yunlin and Chen Deming, among others, have sent condolence telegrams to Mr. Chiang’s family, expressing profound mourning and sincere sympathy. On December 8, after learning that Mr. Chiang had been hospitalized due to illness, relevant mainland authorities expressed concern and offered sympathy at the earliest opportunity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Mr. Chiang Pin-kung has consistently upheld the “1992 Consensus” and opposed “Taiwan independence.” For a long time he has tirelessly traveled back and forth across the Strait, racking his brains to advance economic and other cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and to promote the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations, making great contributions. In particular, during his tenures as Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang and as Chairman of SEF, he played an active role in improving relations between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, advancing institutionalized consultation between the two associations and achieving results, enhancing the livelihoods and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. His contributions have earned the broad praise and respect of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122032.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The annual meeting of the 2018 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit has just concluded in Xiamen. Spokesperson, how do you evaluate the outcomes of the summit?","From December 3 to 5, the 2018 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Annual Meeting was held in Xiamen. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, attended the summit and delivered an important speech. Cross-Strait public opinion highly praised Chairman Wang Yang’s important speech, holding that the speech proclaimed the mainland’s policies toward Taiwan and reflected the mainland’s efforts to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and its sincere goodwill in taking the lead in sharing mainland opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and benefiting compatriots on both sides. At the same time, the speech actively responded to the appeals of the broad Taiwan public for economic development, improved livelihoods, and stronger cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and gave Taiwan businesses operating on the mainland a “reassurance pill.”\nSince its establishment in 2013, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit has held five annual meetings, fully leveraging its advantage as a civil platform for cross-Strait business exchanges and cooperation, continuously promoting close connections between business circles on both sides, and playing an important role in promoting cross-Strait industrial cooperation, enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nRegistration for this annual meeting was enthusiastic among business people from both sides of the Strait. About 1,400 representatives of entrepreneurs, business and industry groups, small and medium-sized enterprises, and youth from both sides attended, a record high. The annual meeting yielded fruitful results: after lively discussions, the eight working groups reached multiple points of consensus, and 36 projects were signed in areas including electronics and information, biomedicine, finance, agriculture, cultural and creative industries, services, small and medium-sized enterprises, and youth employment and entrepreneurship. This fully reflects the summit’s influence and cohesion, and shows that cross-Strait economic cooperation benefits both sides’ enterprises and compatriots, and that business circles on both sides are increasingly moving from benefiting from cooperation toward concrete implementation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122030.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the latest progress in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” and give examples of the results achieved by localities and departments in promoting implementation.","In recent times, Hebei Province, Hainan Province, Dalian City in Liaoning Province, Zhoushan City in Zhejiang Province, Jieyang City in Guangdong Province, Taizhou City in Jiangsu Province and other places have also introduced specific measures to implement the “31 Measures.” So far, 55 localities in 22 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities have formulated specific implementation methods in light of local conditions, and Taiwan compatriots have further benefited from them.\nXiamen City in Fujian Province was among the first cities to introduce specific measures, and the results of implementation have been very notable. In the past six months, Xiamen has newly certified 37 Taiwan-invested high-tech enterprises, which enjoy reduced enterprise income tax for high-tech enterprises; subsidies under the special fund for Taiwan-invested enterprises’ transformation and upgrading to intelligent manufacturing have exceeded 10 million yuan; funding for municipal-level technology centers of Taiwan-invested enterprises has reached 3.2 million yuan; Dong Ya Machinery became the first Taiwan-invested enterprise in Xiamen to enjoy a land-transfer contract priced at 70% of the transaction price; the first wholly Taiwan-owned performing arts enterprise in Fujian Province and three Taiwan-invested intellectual property service institutions have settled in the Xiamen area of the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone; goods of Top Victory Electronics exported by China-Europe Railway Express received certification from Poland, achieving mutual recognition of customs supervision between the two sides’ customs authorities, and so on. This year Xiamen also assisted more than 500 Taiwan students in internships and trainee positions in Xiamen, and established scholarships for Taiwan primary and secondary school students; township and street communities in every city and the cross-Strait mediation committees can provide free people’s mediation services to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises; the first batch of 15 Taiwan youths moved into municipal public rental housing, 66 Taiwan compatriots serve as community director assistants locally, and more than a thousand Taiwan compatriots aged 64 and above enjoy preferential convenience on public transportation in the city.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122029.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said in Penghu that he hopes the SEF and ARATS can resume dialogue. What is your response?","Cross-Strait consultation and dialogue are an important means and method for promoting the development of cross-Strait relations. Resolving specific problems in cross-Strait exchanges through consultation and dialogue, to benefit compatriots on both sides, is our consistent position. But as everyone knows, cross-Strait consultation and dialogue are built on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” After 2016, the reasons and the responsibility for the inability of the two sides to hold dialogue are clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan baker Wu Pao-chun recently said he supports the “1992 Consensus” and takes pride in being Chinese, but he has been attacked by “Taiwan independence” forces on the island. In particular, Tsai Ing-wen called this “political oppression,” and claimed that this kind of threat is the reason for the regression of cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family bound by blood, and Taiwan people are also Chinese. The “1992 Consensus” is the foundation of cross-Strait relations. Master Wu’s statement expresses a correct understanding and normal feelings. Meanwhile, the frenzied assault on him by Green camp politicians and “Taiwan independence” forces is political distortion and political persecution. This matter once again shows that, faced with the urgent demands of Taiwan people to improve their economic livelihoods and cross-Strait relations, the DPP authorities show no self-reflection; they repeatedly attempt to manufacture sentimentality and incite confrontation through political manipulation, and now they are trying to shift focus and relieve pressure. I think people on both sides of the Strait need not dance along with it. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to achieve greater and better development. Deepening cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation, increasing common interests, and promoting spiritual harmony: this policy has not changed, and we will continue to do it well in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Tsai Ing-wen stated that the Taiwan authorities take a positive and open attitude toward exchanges between cross-Strait cities, but do not want any political precondition. Chen Ming-tong, chair of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that he is pleased to see counties and cities governed by the Blue camp establish “cross-Strait working groups,” but that placing the political foundation of cross-Strait…","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It is the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that single-handedly created the controversy. Their so-called “no political precondition” is in fact premised on negating the “1992 Consensus.” The DPP authorities' cross-Strait policy obstructs the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations and seriously harms the interests of Taiwan compatriots; it is a dead end that cannot be traversed.\nRegarding cross-Strait city exchanges, we have stated repeatedly that as long as there is a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, cooperation between cities on both sides can show broad prospects. As long as it benefits the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, we will strive to promote it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","广东深圳卫视记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said that the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” emphasized by the mainland are actually a “belittling” of Taiwan, and that Taiwan’s cross-Strait policy will not change. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Its core meaning is adherence to the one-China principle, which clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be safeguarded and enhanced. If the DPP authorities ignore the strong desire of the Taiwan public to improve the economy and people's livelihoods and to develop cross-Strait relations, and continue to defy public opinion and refuse to change course, they will only fall into an increasingly passive position.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122031.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Reports say that the US Senate recently passed a draft of the Asia Reassurance Initiative Act, whose Taiwan-related provisions include regular arms sales to Taiwan and encouraging senior US officials to visit Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Relevant bills passed by the U.S. Congress that contain Taiwan-related content seriously violate the One China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués. We firmly oppose them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122027.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Some Taiwan media reported that the head of Taiwan’s financial regulator and a responsible official of the mainland’s China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission exchanged views recently during the annual meeting of the Basel Committee in Abu Dhabi. Taiwan media described this as a “breakthrough in cross-strait finance.” Please confirm this.","As far as I know, the relevant reports are inaccurate. The two sides have not carried out any substantive exchanges. As is well known, since 2016 the political obstacles affecting exchanges between civil servants on both sides have not been removed, and the responsibility lies with the Taiwan side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Please spokesperson introduce the ongoing exchange and promotion activities of the Straits Industrial Cooperation Zone.","Since 2017, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with relevant departments, has successively established three Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zones in Guangxi, Sichuan, and Hubei, to help Taiwan-invested enterprises participate in the construction of the \"Belt and Road\" and support them in sharing the development opportunities of the central and western regions. Taiwan-invested businesses have generally welcomed this and hope to learn more about the investment environment and relevant policies of the cooperation zones.\nTo this end, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the Ministry of Commerce, held a Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone exchange and promotion event in Kunshan, Jiangsu, on December 11 and 12. Relevant departments, the governments of the localities where the cooperation zones are located, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, presidents of Taiwan-invested enterprise associations from some provinces and municipalities, the Taiwan Electrical and Electronic Manufacturers' Association, and representatives of well-known enterprises such as Foxconn, a total of more than 300 people, attended the promotion meeting to exchange views on advancing the construction of the cooperation zones. The three cooperation zones made professional presentations around the questions of greatest concern to Taiwan-invested businesses, and experts and scholars present gave special introductions and interpretations on the policies of the Great Western Development, the opportunities and challenges facing Taiwan businesses in central China's development, and the new role of Taiwan businesses in the mainland's two-way, east-west mutually supportive open pattern. Taiwan business representatives also shared their experiences of investing and developing in the cooperation zones. We believe that, with the joint efforts of all parties, the cooperation zones will become a new platform for Taiwan businesses to develop better and bigger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","It is understood that the Shandong Province “Regulations on the Protection of Taiwan Compatriot Investment” will officially take effect on January 1, 2019. These are the first local regulations on the treatment and rights protection of Taiwan compatriot investment since the 19th Party Congress. Could you please introduce the relevant situation?","On November 30, the Standing Committee of the Shandong Provincial People's Congress deliberated and adopted the Shandong Provincial Regulations on Protecting Investment by Taiwan Compatriots, which will formally take effect on January 1, 2019. These Regulations are the first provincial-level local regulation on promoting investment by Taiwan compatriots and protecting their rights and interests since the 19th CPC National Congress, and a concrete measure to implement the \"31 Measures.\" They introduce many new provisions on the investment treatment, livelihood security and rights protection of Taiwan compatriots and their invested enterprises, giving Taiwan businesses investing in Shandong a more comprehensive and specific legal guarantee. For example, they encourage and support Taiwan compatriots to participate in Shandong's economic construction and provide preferences and convenience in accordance with national and Shandong provincial regulations. They also stipulate that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots enjoy \"equal treatment\" in consumption in daily life, children's schooling, social insurance and many other areas. They further clarify the entities responsible for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses, the working mechanisms, and the avenues for resolution when their lawful rights and interests are infringed. It can be said that they provide comprehensive and detailed responses to issues of high concern to Taiwan businesses. We believe the promulgation of these Regulations will have a further driving effect, optimize the investment environment for Taiwan businesses in the Mainland, effectively safeguard the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, and enhance the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently a TV drama called 《Happy Family》 has ranked first in ratings on the mainland. This work involved a Taiwan company, and Taiwan directors and actors took part in its creation and production. It is the first work to achieve such good results after the mainland introduced the “31 measures.” I would like to ask about the mainland’s attitude, and what promotion measures will follow?","As everyone knows, guided by the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” we have introduced the “31 Measures” to promote further cultural exchange across the Strait. Three of these measures specifically provide for expanded opening in cross-Strait film and television exchange and cooperation. It can be said that as these policies have been put into effect and implemented, we have already seen concrete results. Just as the drama “A Happy Family” that this gentleman mentioned just now: I have also noticed that the director and main actors of this film and television work are all from Taiwan, a phenomenon that never occurred in the past. This also fully reflects that after the “31 Measures” were introduced, Taiwan performing artists are willing to come to the mainland to develop, promoting cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation. Through cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, everyone can together portray the moving stories that happen in contemporary China and across the Strait, and jointly promote Chinese culture.\nI look forward to, and also believe, that more and more excellent works co-created across the Strait, like “A Happy Family,” will have an increasingly large influence across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","The day before yesterday, Lai Feng-wei, the Penghu County magistrate-elect, visited the Taiwan Affairs Office and hoped that the Taiwan Affairs Office could assist with Penghu's tourism and tourism exchanges. Afterward, Mr. Lai said that the Taiwan Affairs Office had set up a dedicated liaison window. Could this become a new model of cooperation for future Kuomintang county and city magistrates to exchange on the…","On December 10, Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, met with Lin Bingkun, Chairman of the Taiwan Non-Partisan Solidarity Union, and Lai Feng-wei, the Penghu County Magistrate-elect, and their delegation. The two sides exchanged views on exchange and cooperation between the mainland and Penghu County. The guests put forward suggestions on mainland tourists traveling to Penghu and on the sale of agricultural products. Our attitude is that we will actively promote anything that is beneficial to the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","I would like to ask about follow-up matters following the passing of Mr. Jiang Bingkun. Will the mainland’s official side send personnel to Taiwan to express condolences? In addition, rumors suggest the candidate may be former Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation Chen Yunlin. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","What I can tell everyone now is that regarding the follow-up funeral arrangements for Mr. Chiang Pin-kung, the relevant parties will make appropriate arrangements after communicating with Mr. Chiang’s family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","After the “nine-in-one” elections, more than ten enterprises said they would invest in Kaohsiung. Will the mainland encourage enterprises to invest in Kaohsiung?","Regarding mainland enterprises investing in Taiwan: in 2009, the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits reached relevant consensus, after which the Taiwan side made open permits. However, for a long time, mainland investment in Taiwan has not lived up to expectations, and many restrictive conditions remain. I have said before that mainland investment in Taiwan and two-way cross-Strait investment are both beneficial to people on both sides, but because mainland capital has had its “hands and feet bound,” it can only “dance in shackles.” As I mentioned last time, although the desire on all sides to improve economic livelihoods and develop cross-Strait relations is unprecedentedly strong, since 2016 many unreasonable policies and measures restricting cross-Strait exchanges remain in place. Therefore, we believe that while the mainland makes efforts, the Taiwan side should review and relax unreasonable policies as soon as possible, including those restricting mainland capital.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","I would like to follow up on the question about Wu Pao-chun. It is reported that the matter began when mainland netizens attacked Wu for selling “Taiwan independence” bread in Shanghai. Wu Pao-chun subsequently issued a statement saying that he is Chinese and supports the “1992 Consensus,” and was then attacked by “Taiwan independence” forces on the island. What can the two sides of the Strait do to reduce…","First, let me correct something. If you look into it further, the source of this matter was that some remarks made by Master Wu on the island were distorted by “Taiwan independence” forces or media holding a particular position, and were portrayed as expressions of a “Taiwan independence” stance, which then drew the attention of mainland netizens. So the matter was not provoked by mainland netizens.\nSecond, if you trace the source of some of the so-called disharmonious or even opposing remarks that now appear online, you can consider this: why were there not such voices before 2016, and why have they multiplied after 2016? The root cause is still the so-called “de-Sinicization” pursued by the DPP authorities, which has poisoned the younger generation in Taiwan, distorted the values of the Taiwan public, and caused the atmosphere of cross-Strait relations to deteriorate, thereby triggering some emotions among mainland netizens. The DPP authorities are the ones who started it. Only the person who tied the knot can untie it. To fundamentally resolve this issue, the DPP authorities must change their mistaken cross-Strait policy of confrontation.\nI want to stress that the mainland has always upheld the concept of “cross-Strait compatriots are one family” and has promoted economic, social and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. In cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, compatriots on both sides have further enhanced mutual understanding, increased communication and reached a meeting of minds. On this matter, I believe the public on both sides of the Strait will not dance along with it. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to develop, and our policy and attitude of promoting economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait have never changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Please spokesperson introduce the features and results of the second Cross-Strait Student Baseball League.","With the active participation of more than 200 baseball teams from primary, secondary and tertiary schools on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and the concern and support of all sectors of society on both sides, the second Cross-Strait Student Baseball League full-year competition recently concluded successfully in Shenzhen. This competition showed several new features:\nFirst, the scale of the competition is larger. This year, 42 teams with 888 people entered the finals, an increase of 10 teams and 214 people over last year. Second, the geographic scope of participation is broader. Teams from 10 counties and cities in Taiwan, including Taipei, Taichung and Tainan, took part, an increase of 3 counties and cities over last year. Third, the competition groups are more complete. On top of the five groups from last year, new groups were added, achieving full coverage of groups. Fourth, the content of exchanges is richer. Beyond the competition, arrangements were made for Taiwan primary and secondary school athletes to visit Shenzhen residents’ homes and for young people from both sides to co-produce short videos. Fifth, the duration is longer. The final competition lasted 8 days, the short video contest lasted 20 days, and the exchange period was greatly extended. Sixth, the reach is wider. This time, the National Taiwan Sport University worked with the competition organizing committee and sent a team of 14 students to record and broadcast 12 games of the university Division A competition. These will be aired on the official website and new media platforms of the National Taiwan Sport University, so that more young people will get to know and understand this competition.\nHere I wish the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League continued success and hope that young people on both sides of the Strait can become good friends and good partners through sports competition and exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181212_12122028.htm"],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","At the end of the 2018 year, the results of the Taiwan Character of the Year selection were recently announced, with the character “翻” (“turn over”) coming out on top. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","We have noted the relevant reports. The votes of Taiwan’s voters have already shown everything.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Huawei has sponsored the “Christmas City” event held by the New Taipei City government for three consecutive years, which has been questioned by DPP lawmakers. Taiwan's security authorities have also said there are so-called “security risks.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","This kind of practice, carried out for political purposes and undermining normal cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides and is unpopular. In fact, public opinion in Taiwan has also strongly condemned it in the past two days.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","This year marks the tenth anniversary of the opening of the “Three Links” across the Strait. Please evaluate the role of the “Three Links” over the past decade in enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","The year 2008 saw cross-Strait relations achieve a historic turning point and open up a new situation of peaceful development. The Straits Exchange Foundation and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation resumed consultations and negotiations on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" Through the signing of relevant agreements by the two organizations, direct cross-Strait air transport, direct shipping and direct postal services were formally implemented, Mainland enterprises realized investment in Taiwan, and the comprehensive, direct and two-way \"Three Links\" that compatriots on both sides had long anticipated were realized.\nOver the past decade, the \"Three Links\" have promoted the flow of people, goods and capital across the Strait, realized a \"one-day living circle\" across the Strait, greatly facilitated exchanges between people on both sides, and played an important role in advancing the common interests of compatriots on both sides and promoting heart-to-heart connection, with Taiwan's public also benefiting. At the same time, this fully demonstrates that by adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" cross-Strait exchange and cooperation can continue to deepen, cross-Strait relations have broad prospects for development, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be safeguarded and enhanced.\nHowever, it is regrettable that the DPP authorities have undermined the foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations; Mainland residents' travel to Taiwan, which is built on the \"Three Links,\" has been affected; the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation has been damaged; and the interests and well-being of Taiwan's public have been harmed. We once again advise the DPP authorities to return to the common political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" which is the only way to fundamentally improve cross-Strait relations, continuously expand the spillover effects of the \"Three Links,\" and enable more people on both sides, especially the Taiwan public, to enjoy the fruits of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Li Hsi-chou and others established in Taipei the so-called “Formosa Republic Association,” and claimed it is the first right-wing political group in Taiwan's history to advocate “Taiwan independence.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The first group advocating “Taiwan independence”? That is probably an overstatement on their part. What I want to stress is that we firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and “Taiwan independence” has no future. We urge these “Taiwan independence” forces to recognize the trend of the times, abandon their “Taiwan independence” stance and position, and stop doing things that harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots and the interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","January 1 next year marks the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan.” When is the commemorative meeting expected to be held? Will there be new Taiwan policies? Please also have the spokesperson evaluate the role of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan” over these forty years.","Since the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan” was issued forty years ago, it has played a historic and guiding role in the development of cross-Strait relations. I reviewed and summarized this at the previous two press conferences. As for your question on whether there will be a commemorative conference, I currently have no information on this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Taiwan’s “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” has now issued an order to its “overseas offices” to change the identifying text on their Facebook official pages to the English word “TAIWAN.” May I ask the spokesperson, do you think this is another “de-Chinafication” move by the DPP authorities?","No matter what tricks are played or what means are used, the fact that Taiwan is part of China cannot be changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-12","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","We noted that a Green camp legislator demanded that the Taiwan authorities supervise and bar some institutions in Taiwan from using communications and security equipment manufactured on the mainland, and that board members of public-sector institutions cannot even use mainland-made mobile phones and WeChat. What is the spokesperson's comment?","As far as we know, mainland communications equipment is used around the world, and we have not heard of any insecurity it has brought to any country or region. We firmly oppose using various political pretexts and for various political purposes to interfere with and undermine normal economic, trade, and cooperative exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. This not only harms the interests of mainland enterprises but also harms the interests of Taiwan consumers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181212_12122039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2018-12-14","Lu Kang","","On December 7, the Canadian Foreign Minister said that Canada is giving consideration to a foreign investment protection agreement with Taiwan. On December 13, the economic and trade dialogue between Canada and Taiwan was held in Taipei. Analysts say that Canada is now playing \"the Taiwan card\" to hold the mainland in restraint. What's your comment?","Regarding China's position on the Taiwan issue, I believe that all the countries in the world are very clear about that. If, as you said earlier, the Canadian side did try to play the \"Taiwan card\", then it has miscalculated the situation so much that it will only end up hurting itself.\nDue to scheduling reasons, the Foreign Ministry's regular press conference on December 17 (Monday) will start at 14:00 at the same venue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1622128.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. I will first release a piece of information. Recently, the CPC Central Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office newly approved five cross-Strait exchange bases: Lizhuang Ancient Town in Yibin, Sichuan; Linshui Palace in Gutian, Ningde, Fujian; Huiju Plaza in Kunshan, Jiangsu; the Memorial Museum of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression in Beijing; and the Taiwan Hall in Beijing. Each of the newly established exchange bases has its own distinctive features. They are both important local cultural assets and carry the shared historical memory and cultural heritage of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Since 2009, our office has successively approved the establishment of 66 cross-Strait exchange bases in 22 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian, which have played a positive role in expanding and deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Together with the 5 newly approved this time, the coverage of exchange bases has further expanded. We welcome compatriots from Taiwan to visit and tour these exchange bases and carry out exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126340.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","In addition, as the year draws to a close and the new year begins, I know everyone is deeply concerned about the views of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council on the situation of cross-strait relations over the past year, and their outlook for the situation in the new year. We will provide a detailed introduction at our next press conference. Now I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” have been issued and implemented for nearly a year. What achievements has the spokesperson seen? Also, how do you assess the role of the “31 Measures” in promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation?","Since the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” were issued and implemented, all localities and departments have actively promoted policy implementation, achieving positive results in expanding and deepening economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, and bringing tangible convenience for Taiwan compatriots to achieve greater and better development on the mainland. Since February this year, at every press conference we have introduced the relevant situation. To date, the mainland has formulated specific measures for implementing the “31 Measures” in 60 localities across 22 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, covering all provincial-level administrative regions in the eastern region, most provincial-level administrative regions in the central, western and northeastern regions, and all separately planned cities. Among them, many localities, based on local conditions, have taken the lead in pilot programs, providing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises with treatment equal to that of local residents and enterprises.\nOver the past year, according to incomplete statistics, more than 1,000 Taiwan enterprises have enjoyed various tax preferences such as High and New Technology Enterprise status; more than 100 Taiwan enterprises have received special funds supporting industrial transformation and upgrading, green manufacturing, intelligent manufacturing, and similar areas; some outstanding Taiwan enterprises have successfully won government procurement projects such as the Beijing New Airport, the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge, and the large-scale light show “Impression West Lake” in Hangzhou; more than 800 Taiwan compatriots have obtained professional qualifications in several popular industries; and more than 100 Taiwan compatriots have received various honors such as the “May Day Labor Medal” and “Model Worker” from various localities. This year, the number of Taiwan students applying to mainland universities and the number of Taiwan young people coming to the mainland for employment and internships, as well as the number of newly added Taiwan enterprises served by mainland employment and entrepreneurship service agencies, have all maintained double-digit growth. More and more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, especially Taiwan students and young people, are choosing to come to the mainland to develop and realize their life aspirations.\nGoing forward, we will continue to address issues of common concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, timely study and introduce more new measures, and provide more convenience and better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126335.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The Implementing Regulations of the Individual Income Tax Law will take effect on January 1 of next year, and include provisions on the collection of tax on overseas income that Taiwan businesses are concerned about. Could the spokesperson please explain?","It is understood that the Implementation Regulations of the Individual Income Tax Law, which will officially take effect on January 1, 2019, make further preferential arrangements for the taxation of overseas income of overseas individuals, including Taiwan residents. Taiwan compatriots can enjoy these new provisions.\nBefore the revision of the Individual Income Tax Law, the preferential period for overseas individuals, including Taiwan compatriots, on overseas income paid from overseas was five years. That is, for individuals who have no residence in the mainland but have lived there for more than one year and less than five years, only income within the mainland and overseas income paid from within the mainland were subject to individual income tax. The current Implementation Regulations further extend this five-year preferential period to six years. At the same time, they add the provision that if an individual without residence leaves for more than 30 days in a single trip, the six-year residence period is recalculated, which in substance provides more favorable arrangements for the cumulative calculation of time residing within the mainland.\nIn the new round of reform and opening up, the mainland's business environment will be further optimized. Taiwan-invested enterprises will face broader development space, and Taiwan compatriots investing, living, working, and starting businesses on the mainland will also enjoy better conditions and treatment.\nHere, I invite everyone to review together the untrue statements that the DPP authorities have made about the new tax law for some time, and then look at the facts now. This shows that they constantly create false information and mislead the public, creating misunderstandings and estrangement between Taiwan compatriots and the mainland, and obstructing Taiwan compatriots from achieving greater and better development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126341.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently said that the mainland's demand that Taiwan accept the “1992 Consensus” is intended to eliminate the so-called “Republic of China.” What is the spokesperson's response?","In November 1992, the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) and the Taiwan-side Straits Exchange Foundation were authorized to reach a consensus that each side would orally express its adherence to the one-China principle, which is the \"1992 Consensus.\" This is a consensus confirmed by both sides of the Taiwan Strait, not a so-called \"political precondition\" imposed by one side on the other. Since 1949, although the two sides have been separated and in confrontation, with political differences between them, both sides have long maintained one basic position: the Chinese mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have not been divided. The core of the \"1992 Consensus\" is the shared understanding that the one-China principle is upheld, which clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations. This not only conforms to objective facts and to each side's own stipulations, but also allowed difficult differences to be temporarily set aside, built the most basic mutual trust between the two sides, and in turn opened the door to cross-Strait exchanges and dialogue on the basis of equal consultation.\nSince the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities took office, they have refused to accept the one-China principle and have distorted and slandered the \"1992 Consensus\" with various pretexts and sophistries, causing the cross-Strait consultation door to close, damaging the achievements of peaceful cross-Strait development, and severely harming the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. After Taiwan's \"nine-in-one\" local elections, more and more Taiwan people have come to recognize that the \"1992 Consensus\" is closely tied to their desire for economic development and improved livelihoods, and is as important as water and air. They have recognized that the DPP authorities' undermining of the \"1992 Consensus\" and creation of cross-Strait tension and confrontation stem entirely from narrow partisan interest. We urge the DPP authorities to abandon their separatist stance, stop words and actions that undermine cross-Strait relations, return to the common political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" and stop being an enemy of the public will of people on both sides of the Strait to improve cross-Strait relations, and of Taiwan compatriots' wish for better economic livelihoods and a better life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126336.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","In a media interview before taking office, Kaohsiung Mayor Han Guoyu raised a new cross-Strait discourse calling on the DPP’s central leadership to follow the localities. What is your response to this? In addition, in an interview after taking office, Han Guoyu mentioned hoping to build a new “Twin City Forum” mainly with southern mainland cities. What attitude does the Taiwan Affairs Office hold on this?","I will answer the second question first. We have always taken an active and open attitude toward cross-Strait city exchanges. On the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, we welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to work together for the well-being of cross-Strait compatriots. Our attitude is open and consistent.\nReturning to the first question, it is clear that whoever’s policies are good, and who can bring tangible benefits that let Taiwan people live well, Taiwan people will follow those policies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Since August of this year, a large-scale African swine fever outbreak has occurred on the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council has said it issued notices to the mainland three times to learn about the development of the epidemic but received no response. The mainland also did not notify Taiwan of the African swine fever outbreak as required by the Cross-Strait Agreement on Cooperation in Agricultural Product…","First, let me correct something: this is not a large-scale epidemic. Since the African swine fever outbreak was discovered on the mainland in August this year, relevant departments and regions have taken effective measures and strictly carried out disposal of the outbreak. At present, the epidemic has become stable and is generally under control. The measures and results of the Chinese government in epidemic prevention and control have been affirmed by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.\nThe two sides of the Taiwan Strait have signed the “Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement,” which is used to resolve the notification of food safety and agricultural product safety information involving cross-Strait trade. Taiwan has long not imported pork from the mainland, so this African swine fever notification does not apply to the above agreement. Nevertheless, in 2004, after an avian influenza outbreak occurred on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the two sides, through communication, determined that the Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Association and Taiwan's Foundation for Rural Development, a legal-person foundation, would serve as the non-governmental channel for exchanging epidemic information on non-trade agricultural products and for exchanges on epidemic prevention and control. However, in 2017, the personnel of the aforementioned Taiwan-related foundation were replaced and its business was transformed, causing contact between the two sides to be interrupted.\nSince the African swine fever outbreak, relevant mainland departments have consistently followed the principles of “timeliness, openness and transparency” in releasing epidemic information, and have promptly notified international and regional organizations such as the World Organisation for Animal Health, as well as relevant countries and regions. As a member of the World Organisation for Animal Health, Taiwan can obtain animal epidemic information in a timely manner. As for why the channel between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, and between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Straits Exchange Association, was interrupted, I think the reasons are well known.\nHere, I must also stress that since the outbreak, mainland customs has strengthened port prevention and control publicity through means such as entering mobile phones, passenger cabins and train carriages, reminding passengers to comply with the relevant regulations at the entry point. So far, 35,000 publicity leaflets and 60 million prompt messages have been distributed.\nHere, I must also point out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have recently fabricated some false claims, asserting that the mainland is \"concealing the epidemic\" and \"losing control of epidemic prevention.\" These are entirely false accusations, deliberate hype, and using the issue to make a point, with the intention of inciting dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents toward the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126339.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The Taipei Zoo, where the mainland-gifted giant pandas “Tuan Tuan” and “Yuan Yuan” live, said recently that its request to send staff to the mainland to attend this year's giant panda annual exchange activities was refused for the first time, which is suspected to be for political reasons. Could you please explain the situation?","It is understood that the Cross-Strait and Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Symposium on Giant Panda Conservation and Education has been held five times since 2009, forming an effective non-governmental consultation mechanism that specifically discusses giant panda cooperation among Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. The sixth session will be held in Beijing in 2019, and we welcome the Taipei Zoo to send representatives at that time to discuss giant panda protection and breeding cooperation.\nHere I want to clarify certain media reports. The “International Conference on Giant Panda Conservation and Breeding cum 2018 Annual Meeting of the Giant Panda Breeding Technical Committee,” held for the first time this year, is not a meeting that all institutions that have previously attended the cross-Strait and Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan symposia I just mentioned could fully attend. These are two different meetings, and I clarify this here.\nOur position is clear to everyone. Gifting giant pandas to the people of Taiwan was proposed by the mainland side on its own initiative, in order to foster cross-Strait compatriot affection and enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides. We will continue to support cross-Strait exchange and cooperation on giant panda conservation. The giant pandas “Tuan Tuan” and “Yuan Yuan” entered the Taipei Zoo; counting on fingers, it has been 10 years, and they are loved by Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan children. Their second-generation offspring, “Yuan Zai,” is also 5 years old this year. Many Taiwan compatriots are very concerned about the breeding of “Yuan Zai,” and mainland compatriots are concerned too. As far as I understand, experts from both sides are actively carrying out technical exchanges and assessments, and exploring follow-up breeding cooperation. Like everyone, I look forward to “Yuan Zai” having happy news as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Please spokesperson introduce to us the specifics of the newly established cross-Strait exchange bases.","The five newly established cross-Strait exchange bases, as I already introduced at the start of this press conference.\nAs I just said, from 2009 until now, in order to expand cross-Strait exchanges, the Taiwan Affairs Office has approved the establishment of 71 cross-Strait exchange bases across mainland regions. Some of these bases are places where compatriots on both sides share historical memories, some embody the cultural values of Chinese civilization, and some are historically famous cultural and tourist destinations. In recent years, the cross-Strait exchange bases have fully played their role in expanding exchanges. Many Taiwan compatriots are willing to visit these places when coming to the mainland, many cross-Strait exchange activities are held at the bases, and some bases also serve the function of receiving Taiwan youth for internships and entrepreneurship on the mainland. Using cross-Strait exchange bases to carry out exchange activities is an approach and platform we hope will gain the attention and support of compatriots on both sides, and will further give play to their role in strengthening the emotional bonds of compatriots on both sides and promoting heart-to-heart connection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently responded to cross-Strait city exchanges with several points, saying that city exchanges should be handled through official communication between the two sides and should not have political preconditions, and that requirements such as joint review and approval for Taiwan county and city visits to the mainland for exchanges are needed. What comments does the…","We have seen media reports. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good, and only then can the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots be safeguarded and enhanced. Over the past two years and more, the cross-Strait policies of the DPP authorities have undermined the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and seriously harmed the interests of Taiwan compatriots. At present, in the face of the strong desire of the Taiwan public to improve economic livelihoods and develop cross-Strait relations, we hope they will no longer gamble with the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and will stop obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201812/t20181226_12126338.htm"],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","How does the spokesperson evaluate the currently held Shanghai–Taipei “Twin City Forum”?","As we have introduced several times before, the “Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” has achieved a series of positive results since its founding. This year's “Twin City Forum” was held in Taipei, themed on “circular economy,” and three memoranda of exchange and cooperation were signed, further enhancing the kinship and well-being of the people of the two cities. This fully shows that as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-strait relations and cross-strait city exchanges, exchanges and cooperation between cross-strait cities can advance steadily and far, and show broad prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je said that the “1992 Consensus” and “cross-Strait families are one” have been labeled. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. A correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of cross-Strait city exchanges is the basis for carrying out cross-Strait urban exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, a recent poll shows that more than 60% of Taiwan residents support developing cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Meanwhile, in the recent Taiwan “nine-in-one” local elections, Han Guoyu loudly called for support of the “1992 Consensus” and won the recognition of most Taiwan residents. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","We generally do not comment on specific Taiwan opinion polls. But I think everyone has noticed a trend. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It bears on whether cross-Strait relations can develop steadily and go far, and it also concerns the vital rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. It is as important as water and air. After more than two years of tense and complex changes in cross-Strait relations, more and more Taiwan compatriots have come to recognize the importance and value of the “1992 Consensus” to their own vital interests. This helps compatriots on both sides jointly maintain the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” and jointly create a bright future of mutually beneficial, win-win cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","With barely more than a month until the 2019 Spring Festival, mainland Taiwan compatriots are very concerned about the status of Spring Festival charter flights. Can the spokesperson introduce the preparations? How many airlines will operate this year, and how many additional Spring Festival flights will there be?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. Arranging Spring Festival extra flights is to facilitate exchanges between the two sides, especially to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots returning home to celebrate the New Year. Over the years, the two sides have already formed effective and practical operating methods for this. At present, the mainland side has completed its preliminary preparations and has provided the Taiwan civil aviation authorities with the mainland airlines' demand for extra flights, which will provide positive assurance for cross-Strait exchanges during next year's Spring Festival, especially for Taiwan compatriots returning home to celebrate the New Year. I believe specific news will be announced very soon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Miaoli County Magistrate Hsu Yao-chang recently proposed following the earlier “Blue camp eight counties and cities” model to bring about a visit to Beijing by the “Blue camp 15 counties and cities,” to promote cross-Strait economic and trade development and improve cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment?","As I said just now, on the basis of a correct understanding of the nature of cross-strait relations and cross-strait city exchanges, we will carry out exchanges and cooperation with more counties and cities in Taiwan, continue to promote exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Taiwan Strait, including exchanges between counties and cities, and strive to expand the benefits and sense of gain for Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, former SEF Chairman Chen Yunlin traveled to Taiwan to pay respects to Mr. Chiang Pin-kung, hoping to meet his old friend Lien Chan on the way, but was obstructed by the Taiwan authorities. May I ask the spokesperson how he evaluates the Taiwan authorities' approach of allowing only “public” exchanges and no “private” friendship?","During Mr. Chen Yunlin’s visit to Taiwan to mourn Mr. Chiang Pin-kung, he hoped to have the opportunity to visit some old friends who have made important contributions to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This is both basic courtesy and a matter of human sentiment. But for reasons everyone knows, he was unable to do so, and we also regret this. I think some people in Taiwan are full of “political cells” and have become “political animals.” They do not understand what it means for “lofty mountains and flowing waters to meet a kindred spirit,” and they do not believe that “true feeling exists in the human world.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","In his speech at the celebration of the 40th anniversary of reform and opening up on December 18, General Secretary Xi Jinping mentioned Taiwan three times, and his formulation on the Taiwan question has also caused much discussion. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech, set against the historical backdrop of 40 years of reform and opening up, reviewed and summarized the achievements made in Taiwan work, and highly praised the historic changes and historic breakthroughs in cross-Strait relations. It profoundly elaborated the Central Committee's policies and principles toward Taiwan and its stance on major cross-Strait issues, pointing out that realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people and lies at the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. It made clear our firm adherence to the One-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and to consolidating and developing the foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It declared our political resolve and strong capability to oppose and deter “Taiwan independence” and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It stressed the sincere goodwill of deepening cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation for the benefit of compatriots on both sides, reflecting the people-centered concept of our policy toward Taiwan.\nGeneral Secretary Xi's important speech points the way forward for Taiwan work and cross-Strait relations in the new era. It accords with popular sentiment and public expectations, will inspire compatriots on both sides to work hand in hand, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","After the \"nine-in-one\" elections in Taiwan, many county and city governments in central and southern Taiwan that have hog farming are eagerly anticipating that mainland tourists will be able to travel to Taiwan. May I ask whether the mainland has prepared relevant contingency plans on the issue of African swine fever prevention and control, to prevent the African swine fever virus from spreading to Taiwan?","You may not be very familiar with some internationally common customs functions. In principle, customs at each location only manage imports, and exports are handled by the customs at the place of entry. As I said earlier, mainland customs has already strengthened guidance for tourists traveling to Taiwan through a variety of measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Reports say that some mainland visitors or mainland spouses who arrive at Taoyuan Airport are still found, during customs clearance, to be carrying pork or pork products in their luggage, and African swine fever virus was detected in some of these products, and they were penalized. These mainland visitors or spouses say they did not see any reports on African swine fever in the mainland and did not know about it,…","As I just introduced, the mainland customs authorities have made efforts. As for the individual tourists you mentioned, that is their personal conduct. The claim that these punished people say they did not understand the publicity is a one-sided account from the media and cannot serve as a basis for judgment.\nNone of us wants to see the related epidemic harm the immediate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. Although communication between the two sides' public authorities through relevant channels cannot currently function normally due to reasons on the Taiwan side, we still hope both sides will each make efforts, strengthen epidemic prevention and control, and reduce harm to the rights and interests of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Under current regulations on the island, if a mainland spouse of a Taiwan resident cannot obtain custody of their minor biological children who hold Taiwan household registration after divorce, they cannot continue to reside in Taiwan. Recently, Taiwan media reported that Taiwan's interior authorities will revise the relevant regulations and relax the conditions. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this?","We have said many times that, for a long time, mainland spouses in Taiwan have been subject to unfair and even discriminatory treatment. This phenomenon is unreasonable and inhumane. We have repeatedly called for giving them reasonable and normal treatment and safeguarding their rights and interests. If the situation you mention is true, it is a step toward a more humane direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2018-12-26","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","According to Taiwan media reports, PLA military aircraft and warships recently entered the Bashi Channel to conduct long-distance deep-sea training. Taiwan media said this is the PLA's first related action since the “Nine-in-One” elections and in nearly half a year. What is the spokesperson's view?","As I understand it, the relevant training is a routine arrangement within the PLA’s annual plan. Before this press conference ends, I sincerely wish everyone a happy New Year 2019, good health and everything going well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201812/t20181226_12126351.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2018-12-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media in Taiwan said that a PLAAF aircraft flying around Taiwan this month carried combat warheads. And Taiwan’s defense agency also said that the real combat capabilities of mainland China are advancing rapidly. What’s your comment?","You mentioned that Taiwan’s defense agency said that PLA’s real combat capabilities were advancing rapidly. As for my comment, I should say I agree with that. I noticed that in the media report, Taiwan’s defense agency also said that this move deserved alert from Taiwan. I want to stress that it is a dead end to deny reunification by using force.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-12/27/content_4833087.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2018-12-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports from Taiwan, PLA aircraft of multiple types flew over the Bashi Strait to the west Pacific on December 18. Some media in Taiwan said that it was PLA’s another flying operation around Taiwan after half a year’s interval. What is your comment? Some media in the U.S. reported that China conducted in late November the first test flight of its JL-3 submarine-launched intercontinental…","On the first question, I have three points to make. First, it is PLA’s duty to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and protect national security. Second, the relevant training is a regular arrangement of our annual training plan. Third, we will conduct similar training in the future.\nOn the second question, I have no information to release.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2018-12/27/content_4833087.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-01-02","Lu Kang","","In President Xi Jinping's speech made at the 40th anniversary of issuing Message to Compatriots in Taiwan, he said that China makes no promise to renounce the use of force and reserves the option to take all necessary measures against the external forces which try to undermine the reunification process. What specifically do these external forces refer to?","I am glad that you have followed President Xi Jinping's important speech this morning for the 40th anniversary of issuing Message to Compatriots in Taiwan which comprehensively reviews the breakthroughs and progress made by cross-Straits relations over seven decades since the founding of the PRC, especially since the implementation of the principle of peaceful reunification. President Xi Jinping expounded on China's major policies and propositions to move forward China's peaceful reunification for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in the new era. I hope that you could have a comprehensive understanding of President Xi Jinping's speech.\nPresident Xi Jinping also made it very clear in his speech that adherence to the one-China principle is a consensus shared by the international community. The international community generally understands and supports the just cause of the Chinese people in opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and realizing national reunification. President Xi Jinping made the message explicitly clear in his speech. We make no promise to renounce the use of force. This does not target compatriots in Taiwan, but the interference of external forces and the very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their activities. In fact, you should note that China's stance on this has never changed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1626635.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1626567.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-01-02","Lu Kang","","The US \"Asia Reassurance Initiative Act of 2018\" was signed into law. The Act includes Taiwan-related contents that are not legally binding, like asking for stronger official exchanges and military ties between the US and Taiwan. What is your comment?","The above-mentioned Act seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiques, and grossly interferes in China's internal affairs. The Chinese side expresses strong dissatisfaction with and resolute opposition to the US insisting on signing the Act into law and has already made stern representations with the US.\nI would like to remind the US side of the speech made by President Xi Jinping at the 40th anniversary of issuing Message to Compatriots in Taiwan. He stressed solemnly that the Taiwan question belongs to China's internal affairs, concerns China's core interests and the national bond of the Chinese people and allows no interference from the outside.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiques. The US must not implement the relevant contents of the Act and should carefully handle the Taiwan-related issues in a cautious manner so as not to impair the overall situation of the China-US relations and cross-Straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1626635.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1626567.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-01-14","Hua Chunying","","It is reported that the US has agreed to allow some military enterprises to export their technology to support Taiwan's Indigenous Defense Submarine (IDS) program. Many US, European, Japanese and Indian companies have expressed their willingness to participate in the program. What is your comment?","China firmly opposes arms sales to Taiwan by any country and military links in any form between any country and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the US and other relevant countries to keep in mind the sensitivity and graveness of this issue, earnestly abide by the one-China principle, not to permit relevant enterprises from participating in Taiwan's Indigenous Defense Submarine (IDS) program in any form, stop having any military links with Taiwan, and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid severely undermining their bilateral relations with China and peace and stability across the Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1629365.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1629296.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-01-16","Hua Chunying","","The Defense Intelligence Agency of the US issued a report on China's military power, saying that Beijing's attempt to \"eventually compel Taiwan's reunification with the mainland\" has served as the primary driver for China's military modernization. China is rapidly building a robust, lethal force, with capabilities spanning ground, air, maritime, space and information domains, designed to enable China to impose…","We have noted the report entitled \"Assessment on US Defense Implications of China's Expanding Global Access\" recently issued by the US Department of Defense and this report just published by the Defense Intelligence Agency. We still need some time to study these reports in an in-depth and meticulous manner, but I can give you an initial response:\nThese reports by the US side made unwarranted speculations and comments on China's development path, strategic intention and national defense, showing no respect to facts and teeming with the Cold War mindset and zero-sum game mentality. The baseless speculations they contain are highly ridiculous and unprofessional. China is firmly opposed to that. We believe that the sound and steady development of military ties between the two sides will benefit not only the two countries but also the whole world. We hope that the US military could view China's development in a rational, objective and correct way and maintain the larger picture of China-US state-to-state and mil-to-mil relations with concrete actions.\nI want to further emphasize a few points:\nFirst, China is committed to the path of peaceful development. China develops its national defense strength independently in commensurate with the growth of its national power, the purpose of which is to better safeguard its own sovereignty, security and development interests and maintain global and regional peace and stability.\nSecond, China is a role model in observing regional and international rules. We maintain that interests shall be protected by rules, not by weapons. In fact, as you may have all noted, even for a country as militarily powerful as the US, it cannot have its way in everything it does. We hope that the US side could also respect and observe international rules, instead of finding or even fabricating various excuses to develop greater lethal force for the purpose of more military strength.\nThird, the Taiwan question belongs to China's internal affairs. Just like what General Secretary Xi Jinping said in his speech to commemorate the 40th anniversary of issuing Message to Compatriots in Taiwan, we are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, strive for peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and greatest efforts, but will leave no room for any form of separatist activities. We urge the US to abide by the one China policy and maintain the larger picture of China-US relations as well the peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.\nFourth, I also want to remind certain people in the US that peace and development is the trend of the times and the aspiration of all people. If these people only care about burying their heads down to find traps or are even busy digging pits, instead of looking up at the stars, sooner or later they will fall into the traps and pits of their own making.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1629984.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1629918.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang introduced the development of cross-Strait relations and Taiwan work in 2018, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO's first press conference of 2019. I extend New Year greetings to you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","2018 was a year in which compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait worked hand in hand to push cross-Strait relations forward through difficulties. Facing the complex and severe situation in the Taiwan Strait, we thoroughly implemented the spirit of the 19th Party Congress and General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan work, carried out the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee, acted proactively and effectively, pursued progress while maintaining stability, united the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and led cross-Strait relations in the right direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132596.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and we firmly oppose and contain all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. We will strengthen dialogue and exchanges with parties and groups on the island that recognize the “1992 Consensus” and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, uniting compatriots on both sides to jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities' retrograde moves to promote “de-Sinicization” in education, culture and other fields have been widely opposed by enlightened people on the island, and the so-called “Olympic name-correction referendum” was defeated. Our circle of international friends is growing larger, and the one-China principle is increasingly gaining international recognition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We are mindful of the interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and have adopted a series of policies and measures that benefit them widely, doing practical things, good deeds, and solving difficult problems for Taiwan compatriots. We issued the \"31 Measures\" to promote economic, cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, issued residence permits to Taiwan residents, abolished employment permits for Taiwan residents, and realized water supply from the mainland to Kinmen. We have taken new steps in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first and gradually providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. With specific implementation measures introduced in 65 localities across 24 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities and their subordinate cities and counties, more than 2,000 Taiwan-funded enterprises have enjoyed tax preferences for high-tech enterprises and other categories, more than 100 Taiwan-funded enterprises have received special funds for industrial transformation and upgrading, green manufacturing, intelligent manufacturing and other areas, a number of high-quality Taiwan-funded enterprises have won bids for several large government procurement projects, more than 800 Taiwan compatriots have obtained occupational qualifications in many popular mainland industries, and more than 100 Taiwan compatriots have received various honorary titles. The number of cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites has increased by 23 this year, bringing the cumulative total to 76. They host or serve about 2,000 Taiwan-funded enterprises and teams in total, and more than 10,000 Taiwan youth are pursuing their dreams there. Various enterprises and institutions provided more than 25,000 employment and internship opportunities for Taiwan youth this year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","We continue to deepen cross-Strait economic cooperation and various exchanges. Cross-Strait economic and trade ties are becoming ever closer, exchanges and interactions in all fields continue to expand and deepen, and more Taiwan compatriots come to the Mainland to find employment, start businesses, study and live. Cross-Strait trade has once again reached a new historical high, with total annual trade of 226.2 billion US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 13.2%. Taiwanese investment has steadily increased, with a total of 4,911 Taiwanese-invested projects approved throughout the year, a year-on-year increase of 41.8%. As of the end of 2018, cumulatively 107,190 Taiwan-invested projects had been approved, accounting for 11.2% of the total number of projects using foreign capital in practice. 73 Taiwanese enterprises participated in the first China International Import Expo, and the number of Taiwan industrial and commercial circles attending the annual Cross-Strait CEO Summit exceeded previous years. In 2018, cross-Strait personnel exchanges exceeded 9.05 million person-times, a year-on-year increase of 3.2%. Among them, Taiwan compatriot visits to the Mainland exceeded 6 million person-times for the first time, and the number of \"first-time visitors\" reached 400,000, both setting historical highs. As of the end of 2018, Taiwan residents had made a cumulative total of more than 100 million visits to the Mainland. This year, more than 8,000 Taiwan grassroots people enthusiastically took part in the 10th Straits Forum. More than 1,800 people participated in the Cross-Strait Youth Games, and the second Cross-Strait Student Baseball League continued to stir up a new wave of enthusiasm. The number of Taiwan students applying to Mainland universities has also multiplied.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","2019 marks the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China and the 40th anniversary of the NPC Standing Committee's issuance of the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan” and the proposal of the policy of peaceful reunification. At the beginning of the new year, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech, “Working Together to Realize the Great Rejuvenation of the Chinese Nation and Advance the Peaceful Reunification of the Motherland,” which provides the fundamental guidance and action guide for carrying out Taiwan work in the new era. We will thoroughly study and fully implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Although cross-Strait relations will not always go smoothly, and “Taiwan independence” forces will continue to provoke trouble, we are fully capable of overcoming various risks and challenges. We believe that in the new year, exchanges between compatriots on both sides will become even more active, cooperation will become even closer, and kinship will deepen further. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together with one heart to continue promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","May I ask the spokesperson: what is the important significance of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech at the commemoration of the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Taiwan Compatriots” for leading cross-Strait relations in the new era and advancing work on Taiwan?","General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech comprehensively elaborates our major policy propositions for promoting the peaceful reunification of the motherland from the standpoint of the new era and on the great journey of national rejuvenation. It is of epoch-making significance, is the programmatic document guiding Taiwan work in the new era, and is the fundamental guideline and action plan for doing Taiwan work in the new era.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping’s speech comprehensively reviewed the major achievements in Taiwan work and cross-Strait relations, profoundly revealed the inner connection between Taiwan’s future and destiny and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and clearly demonstrated the historical trend of cross-Strait relations’ development and the inevitability of the motherland’s reunification. The five major policy propositions put forward in the speech scientifically answer the epochal question of how, in the new era, to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to unite Taiwan compatriots in working together toward national rejuvenation and the peaceful reunification of the motherland. They enrich the important content of the basic strategy of “one country, two systems” and of advancing national reunification in the new era. They clearly express the firm opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism and to interference by external forces, and clearly draw an inviolable red line. They fully demonstrate our determination and sincerity in promoting peaceful reunification, fully consider and respond to the needs and concerns of Taiwan compatriots, and fully reflect concern for and care about the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, pointing the way forward for cross-Strait relations in the new era.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech has great guiding significance for further strengthening our confidence and continuing to unite all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, in working together for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and the completion of the great cause of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and it will certainly have a far-reaching impact.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132594.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","In his important speech at the commemoration marking the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” General Secretary Xi Jinping pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” — “both sides of the Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national reunification” — adds “seeking national reunification” to the “1992 Consensus.” Does the spokesperson believe this means the connotation of the “1992…","In November 1992, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), through talks in Hong Kong and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, reached a consensus that each side would express orally that \"both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.\" The SEF's formulation is: \"In the process of working together across the Taiwan Strait to seek national reunification, although both sides adhere to the principle of one China, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.\" The ARATS formulation is: \"Both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive to achieve national reunification. However, in cross-Strait negotiations on practical matters, the political meaning of one China is not involved.\" It can thus be seen that adhering to the one-China principle and jointly striving for national reunification is the inherent meaning of the \"1992 Consensus.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132593.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Tsai Ing-wen refuses to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and she hopes that others on the island will not acknowledge it either. She says the “1992 Consensus” is “one country, two systems.” What views does the spokesperson have on this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and shows that both sides, in their efforts to seek national reunification, adhere to the one-China principle. “One country, two systems” is the institutional arrangement after national reunification is achieved. DPP authority leaders deliberately conflate the two, deliberately misleading the Taiwan public. Cross-Strait relations being good is what allows Taiwan compatriots to do well, but for those people and forces who turn back the wheel of history and act against the tide, when cross-Strait relations are good, their days are not necessarily easy. Therefore, their wanton denial of the “1992 Consensus” and slander of “one country, two systems” further expose their separatist stance, and further expose their aim of undermining cross-Strait relations by escalating confrontation and hostility in order to seek personal gain. We believe compatriots on both sides, especially the broad Taiwan compatriots, will not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132592.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","According to reports, after the 40th anniversary commemoration of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” a spokesperson of the US White House National Security Council said that the US “rejects the plan and threat of military intimidation against the people of Taiwan,” and called on the mainland to “stop oppressing Taiwan” and resume dialogue with the Taiwan authorities. The DPP authorities said they will…","First, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. It concerns China's core interests and the national sentiments of the Chinese people, and matters concerning China must be decided by the Chinese people themselves; no external interference will be tolerated. Second, our basic policy toward Taiwan is “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” We wish to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence,” and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. There is no so-called “intimidating the Taiwan people by force” or “oppressing Taiwan” issue here. US personnel should not irresponsibly sow discord in the feelings of people on both sides of the Strait. US personnel turn a blind eye to the words and deeds of the DPP authorities that undermine the political foundation of cross-Strait relations and heighten hostility across the Strait, while constantly issuing erroneous messages, which can only further undermine peace and stability across the Strait. Third, the DPP authorities are relying on foreign backing to assert themselves, which the Taiwan compatriots will not accept, and the compatriots on both sides of the Strait will not accept either, so they will inevitably reap what they have sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132591.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Taiwan's so-called “Justice Investigation Bureau” recently obtained the Mainland's consent to set up a “justice secretary” in Hong Kong. It is said this is the first time someone from the bureau will work at an overseas base. What is the spokesperson's comment?","First, the relevant reports do not conform to the facts. According to the relevant consensus between Hong Kong and Taiwan, the Hong Kong “Taipei Economic and Cultural Office” has not established a position of “legal secretary,” and there is no so-called “obtaining approval from the mainland side.” Relevant Taiwan institutions should earnestly abide by the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region and relevant laws, and act within their prescribed scope of duties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The Regulations for the Implementation of the Individual Income Tax Law took effect on January 1. Taiwan-side authorities have said that the mainland has included anti-tax-avoidance provisions in the new tax law, and that if Taiwan compatriots apply for Taiwan residence permits on the basis of having a lawful and stable residence on the mainland, they may be determined to be “tax residents,” which would expose…","It is understood that the anti-tax-avoidance provisions added to the Individual Income Tax Law and its Implementing Regulations are a universally applicable tax policy. Such rules are common in the tax legislation of major countries and regions around the world, including Taiwan.\nTaiwan compatriots working and doing business in the Mainland enjoy the same tax obligations and rights as compatriots from Hong Kong and Macao. There is no so-called \"higher risk.\" Let me further clarify some questions about the new tax law that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses are concerned about. First, the \"lawful and stable residence\" that Taiwan compatriots must show when applying for a residence permit is not equivalent to \"having a residence\" under the Individual Income Tax Law. Taiwan compatriots have lawful and stable residences in the Mainland, but if, after the reasons such as study, work or visiting relatives have ceased, they return to Taiwan, they are in principle regarded as individuals without a residence and are not thereby determined to be tax residents of the Mainland.\nSecond, this individual income tax reform continues and optimizes the preferential policies in the original implementing regulations of the tax law. For individuals without a residence who stay within the Mainland for less than 6 years, foreign-source income paid from outside the Mainland is exempt from taxation.\nThird, this reform fully implements a tax system that combines comprehensive and categorical income taxation, raises the tax threshold, adjusts the tax rate schedule, and adds special additional deductions, further reducing the tax burden on Taiwan compatriots working and living in the Mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190116_12132590.htm"],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","I have two questions. First, the Industrial Technology Research Institute in Taiwan announced that its internal employees are prohibited from using Huawei phones and computers. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second, the Governor of Fujian announced that in 2019 it will actively promote the new “Four Links” with Kinmen and Matsu, namely water, electricity, gas and bridge connections. I would like to know your…","On the first question: we firmly oppose such practices that undermine normal cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation for political purposes, because they not only harm the interests of mainland enterprises but also seriously harm the interests of Taiwan consumers. Such practices cater to certain foreign forces and willingly serve as their “pawns,” and are unpopular.\nOn the second question: General Secretary Xi Jinping, in his important speech on January 2, starting from the kindly sentiment of kinship, “when relatives wish each other well, Chinese must help Chinese,” proposed deepening the integration and development across the Strait, continuing to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and promoting the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. He put forward a series of policy propositions, proposed that “cross-Strait exchanges should be fully connected,” and proposed that “Kinmen and Matsu may take the lead in achieving water, electricity, gas, and bridge connections with the coastal areas of Fujian.” The Fujian authorities are earnestly implementing the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech and will actively advance the relevant work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, Taiwan region leader Tsai Ing-wen, at an event, falsely claimed that each year two to three million mainlanders visit Taiwan, some of whom may use exchange activities as cover to probe or collect intelligence, and that since 2018 Taiwan's relevant authorities have arrested 174 people on grounds of endangering security, including mainland tourists. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities keep fabricating and piling up baseless charges, obstructing and undermining normal cross-Strait exchanges, intimidating Taiwan residents, escalating cross-Strait confrontation, and inciting cross-Strait hostility. This vile conduct is unpopular and will certainly be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Some media have reported that around the Spring Festival, mainland tourists traveling to the Kaohsiung and Taichung areas are expected to increase significantly, by at least 20 percent, with Kaohsiung showing an even more pronounced rise. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Mainland tourists have seen the positive changes in Kaohsiung, and have also noted that the relevant officials of Kaohsiung City have a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of exchanges between cross-Strait cities. Therefore, the increase in the number of visitors to Kaohsiung around the Spring Festival is natural and within expectations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The Taiwan authorities have obstructed exchanges between Taiwan counties and cities and the mainland through various means, and Kaohsiung City has been the first to be affected. At the same time, Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu has continuously stressed the “1992 Consensus” and the importance of cross-Strait exchanges. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","We have repeatedly stated that as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and the nature of cross-Strait city exchanges, we hold a positive and open attitude toward cross-Strait city exchanges. On this basis, we are also willing to welcome and support more Taiwan counties and cities taking part in cross-Strait city exchanges, promote the kinship and well-being of people on both sides of the Strait, and expand the range of beneficiaries and the sense of gain among compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. At the same time, it must be pointed out that some structural factors and fundamental root causes restricting cross-Strait exchanges and travel since 2016 have not yet been eliminated. We have noted recent confrontations on the island over whether to hold exchanges and whether to disallow them. I believe that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will judge which is good for cross-Strait relations and which is beneficial to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots themselves, and will make correct judgments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Chang Ya-chung has announced his candidacy for leader of Taiwan's region. Some commentators believe the pro-unification camp will have a greater voice in Taiwan's future elections. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We never comment on affairs on the island of Taiwan, especially matters concerning elections. What I want to emphasize is that our policy toward Taiwan is “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” For groups and individuals on the island that advocate unification, we are willing to engage in exchanges, contacts, and to strengthen dialogue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","After General Secretary Xi Jinping put forward the “five-point proposition” on Taiwan work, Tsai Ing-wen stressed that cross-Strait exchanges must be conducted by “governments” or authorized institutions sitting down to talk, which conflicts to some extent with the mainland's “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan. How does the spokesperson comment?","I have already made comments and refutations just now. Since 2016, why have institutionalized cross-Strait exchanges and consultation mechanisms been interrupted? It is because the DPP authorities unilaterally undermined the common political foundation for cross-Strait consultations. They refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle and deny the “1992 Consensus.” This is the fundamental crux. Everyone is very clear about this reason.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Ma Ying-jeou, in an exclusive interview, was asked whether he might visit mainland China after the restrictions are lifted on May 20, and he said that this possibility cannot be ruled out. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this?","While serving as leader of the Taiwan region, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou adhered to the “1992 Consensus,” opposed “Taiwan independence,” promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and achieved positive results. We are willing to strengthen exchanges with political parties, groups and individuals on Taiwan that adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and to widely exchange views on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Haicang District in Xiamen has opened more than 30 vacancies for community deputy director positions this year. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed that, after consultations among relevant agencies, it has determined that 43 Taiwan residents who currently hold grassroots administrative posts on the mainland have, in principle, violated the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area…","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan always works against the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots. That is my comment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Taiwan politicians keep hyping the African swine fever epidemic issue. Tsai Ing-wen has repeatedly mentioned at events the slander that the mainland deliberately let African swine fever spread to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I already answered this question directly and in detail at the last press conference. Recently, a responsible official of the mainland's agricultural authorities also explained again to the public the prevention and control of African swine fever. Everyone can check the Ministry of Agriculture's website.\nI want to stress that the mainland has always followed the principles of “timeliness, openness, and transparency” in releasing epidemic information, and has promptly reported to international regional organizations such as the World Organisation for Animal Health. The measures and results of the Chinese government in epidemic prevention and control have been fully affirmed by international professional organizations such as the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations and by the international community. Taiwan, as a member of the World Organisation for Animal Health, can obtain relevant information through existing channels, and there are no obstacles or restrictions whatsoever.\nAs a province neighboring Taiwan, Fujian Province has strictly implemented epidemic reporting, testing and screening, quarantine supervision, restrictions on the transport of live hogs and their products from epidemic areas, and supervision of hog slaughter, among other prevention and control measures. It has resolutely handled outbreaks and firmly prevented the spread of the epidemic. For example, the epidemics in Chengxiang District of Putian City, Youxi County of Sanming City, and Yanping District of Nanping City have all been effectively handled. At the same time, Fujian Province has organized comprehensive screening and increased testing in areas where no epidemic zones have occurred. The results of the inspections found no African swine fever outbreaks outside the areas I just mentioned. In epidemic prevention and control, the DPP authorities should do their own job well, rather than exploit the issue, shift blame to the mainland, and make political capital.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","《台声》杂志社记者","Recently, New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming said he is willing to take the lead in conducting political consultations with the mainland. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of other political parties or groups on the island that have expressed willingness to conduct political consultations with the mainland?","The New Party has consistently advocated peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait, firmly supports one China, and opposes “Taiwan independence.” We highly appreciate this. We are willing, on the basis of the one-China principle, to hold dialogue and communication with Taiwan's parties, groups and individuals, including the New Party, on cross-Strait political issues and issues related to advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, so as to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly pursue peaceful reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","Please spokesperson introduce the policy on opening to Taiwan residents the application for qualifications to teach at mainland primary and secondary schools.","Recently, the Ministry of Education, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, and the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council jointly issued the “Notice on Issues Concerning Applications by Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Residents for Primary and Secondary School Teacher Qualifications in the Mainland.” Taiwan compatriots who meet the conditions and who study, work, and live in the mainland may, using a Taiwan residence permit or a Taiwan Compatriot Travel Permit for Mainland Travel with a five-year validity period (commonly known as the “five-year valid” Taiwan compatriot permit), apply to take the primary and secondary school teacher qualification examination and be certified as primary or secondary school teachers.\nThis is another favorable policy that relevant mainland authorities have introduced, after the “31 Measures,” to implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots. In particular, it responds to the needs of Taiwanese students who are already studying teacher-training majors in the mainland, and it has strong practical relevance. The examination date for this year's first-half qualification exam is set for March 9. Registration runs from January 15 to 18. Specific details can be checked on the China Education Examinations Network and on the Ministry of Education's official new media account “Weiyan Education.” We welcome eligible Taiwan compatriots to register actively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities recently said they “welcome the entry into force of the CPTPP” and expressed hope that the CPTPP would begin accepting new members, including Taiwan, as soon as possible. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have repeatedly made clear that Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on adherence to the one-China principle. We firmly oppose any agreements with sovereignty implications and official nature being signed between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with us.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the progress of the 2019 Spring Festival charter flights.","On December 26, 2018, the civil aviation authorities on both sides of the Strait each issued press releases confirming the air transport arrangements for extra flights during the 2019 Spring Festival and other periods. According to the relevant arrangements, on January 10 the civil aviation authorities on both sides approved all applications by cross-Strait airlines for Spring Festival extra flights; this year there are 528 flights in total.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen, when she served as head of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the “1992 Consensus” is “one China, each with its own interpretation,” but now she says there is no “1992 Consensus.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have noted the media reports. I think this reflects, to some extent, questions about the political conduct and integrity of some Taiwan political figures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Recently, KMT legislator Chiang Wan-an publicly supported the so-called “Four Musts” put forward by Taiwan's leader in his New Year's Day address, and later clarified that he supports the “1992 Consensus.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","I would like to reiterate that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of that development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190116_12132608.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-01-25","Hua Chunying","","First, the US military confirmed that two US military vessels sailed through the Taiwan Strait on Thursday. The US side claimed that it was a normal passage that conforms with the international law. But we have noted that the US has been sending its military vessels through the Taiwan Strait at a higher frequency. What is your response to the US actions and remarks? Second, on Thursday, speaking at the World…","On your first question, China paid close attention to and monitored from start to end the passage of the US military vessels through the Taiwan Strait. We have expressed our concerns to the US side. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive one for China-US relations. We urge the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues to avoid damaging China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability.\nYou said that the US military vessels have made more frequent passages through the Taiwan Strait, while the US side claimed that these passages are normal and compliant with the international law. I want to make a comparison here and would like to invite you to envision a scenario with me. Suppose that a family has two courtyards, a smaller one lying in front of a large one, divided by a passage which could be used by passersby to come through for convenience's sake. However, if there is someone who frequents this passage just to issue provocative words or make provocative moves, or even attempt to threaten or endanger the safety of the family and make them discomfort, then how would you feel? We hope that the US side will exercise caution on this issue.\nOn your second question, I have seen relevant reports. In today's world, it is very easy to tell who is opening the door and paving roads and who is closing the door and building walls. Therefore, it is meaningless and worthless to refute these words made by certain individual that call white black and confuse right and wrong. Living in this era where globalization is advancing further on all fronts, only by seeing things in a dynamic way and taking in things with an open and inclusive mind can a country find greater development space for itself and its relations with other countries. We hope that the relevant people on the US side can set right their attitude, broaden their horizon, and view China's development in an objective, reasonable and correct way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1632577.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1632526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","厦门卫视记者","With the Spring Festival approaching, what measures has the mainland taken to help Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots return home for the New Year?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. In order to make cross-Strait exchanges among the public, especially the return of Taiwan compatriots home for the New Year, more convenient during the Spring Festival, relevant parties on the Mainland have already launched Spring Festival travel work. According to our understanding, Mainland airlines have already begun relevant work in accordance with the arrangements for cross-Strait Spring Festival additional flights in 2019 and are providing full support. This year's Spring Festival travel work began on January 22, and as we understand it, overall operations are currently running smoothly.\nFujian Province is an important transit point for Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year, and every year it handles a large volume of Spring Festival travel for Taiwan compatriots. This year, relevant departments in Fujian Province have actively taken measures to fully implement online ticket sales and strengthen seamless connections between water and land transport, providing convenient services for Taiwan compatriots returning home. In terms of sea passenger transport, cross-Strait sea passenger traffic between Fujian and Taiwan is expected to reach 220,000 person-times, a year-on-year increase of 3%. In terms of air passenger transport, in addition to the fixed flights operating 72 round trips per week between Fujian and Taiwan, Xiamen Airlines has also specially added 110 additional flights from Xiamen, Fuzhou, Quanzhou, Hangzhou and Changsha to Taipei and Kaohsiung, adding capacity of more than 10,000 person-times. During the Spring Festival travel period, Xiamen Airlines also presents passengers with gifts such as New Year red envelopes, commemorative coins and candy gift boxes, and on some flights has specially assigned Taiwan-born flight attendants to deliver fine New Year wishes to Taiwan compatriots returning home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136867.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the maiden voyage of the Kaohsiung–Pingtan (Fujian) fast ferry took place, and Kaohsiung products have also been rapidly delivered. Han Kuo-yu said he is willing to come to the mainland for further discussions on cooperation, and Taichung Mayor Lu Shiow-yen will also soon travel to Hong Kong to discuss the sale of fruit to the mainland via Hong Kong. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have stated many times that as long as there is a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of exchanges between cities across the Strait, we are willing to carry out exchange and cooperation with more counties and cities in Taiwan, to together enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Recently, enterprises in Pingtan, Fujian, purchased more than 700 tons of agricultural and industrial products worth over 15 million yuan from Kaohsiung. We are also pleased to see agricultural products from Taichung City sold on the mainland.\nWe will continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and continue to expand and deepen cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, so as to bring well-being to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136865.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","Recently, Taiwan authorities have strictly inspected pork products carried by mainland travelers to Taiwan at entry ports. What is the comment? In addition, how will the mainland strengthen publicity and guidance for travelers to Taiwan?","On this issue, I would point out several things. First, the mainland attaches great importance to the prevention and control of African swine fever. Based on laws and regulations such as the Law on Animal Epidemic Prevention, the Regulations on Emergency Response to Major Animal Epidemics, and the Regulations on the Administration of Pig Slaughter, it strictly implements measures for epidemic screening, testing, and disposal, and standardizes pig slaughter and circulation. At present, the epidemic is not spreading.\nSecond, relevant parties on the mainland have further strengthened publicity to passengers traveling between the two sides through airlines, ports of entry, and travel agencies. The mainland civil aviation authority has notified airlines operating cross-strait routes to strengthen control of pork products and to publicize reminders to passengers. The Ministry of Culture and Tourism has issued a travel reminder in the “Travel Tips” column of its official website, reminding mainland tourists not to illegally carry meat products into Taiwan. The General Administration of Customs and the Ministry of Transport have also strengthened publicity and inspection at ports of entry and exit. Responding to animal epidemics concerns the well-being of people on both sides, and we are willing to make active efforts to get this right.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","The Taiwan executive authority said it will publish a list of mainland technology companies whose products are banned for use by Taiwan public servants, and that this list will be continuously updated. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment?","We have stated many times that we firmly oppose the DPP authorities' practice of undermining normal cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation for political purposes. Against the backdrop of increasingly close cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges, this move not only harms the interests of mainland enterprises, but will also seriously harm the interests of Taiwan consumers and of many supply-chain manufacturers in Taiwan, thereby affecting Taiwan's own economic development. This practice of creating divisions and harming the rights and interests of Taiwan residents is unpopular. We will closely monitor it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136862.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently declared publicly that the time has come for Taiwan to formulate a so-called “new constitution.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Lai Ching-te himself previously claimed to be a “Taiwan independence worker,” and now his “Taiwan independence” face is even more fully exposed. I must stress that promoting “de jure Taiwan independence” under the name of so-called “constitution-making” will only push Taiwan into a dangerous abyss and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and we will never sit idly by.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136863.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","At a recent New Year press conference, Chen Ming-tong, Chairman of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, claimed that he would implement the so-called “democratic defense network,” perfect the security defense mechanism, and, when meeting with Han Kuo-yu, demanded restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The DPP authorities, disregarding the strong desire of the broad Taiwan public to develop cross-Strait relations and improve the economy and people's livelihoods, have continuously heightened cross-Strait confrontation and restricted cross-Strait exchanges, further exposing their essence of being hostile to the interests of the Taiwan public. Whether they set up “defense lines” or weave “networks,” they cannot stop the steps of cross-Strait compatriots to draw closer, to become more intimate in reality, and to go well. In the end, they can only entangle themselves like silkworms in their own cocoons and be spurned by the broad Taiwan compatriots.\nThe mainland and Taiwan belong to one China. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. By adhering to this principle, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop, and Taiwan compatriots can benefit from it. We will continue to unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, remove interference, expand and deepen economic exchanges and cooperation, including exchanges between cross-Strait cities, enhance the interests and well-being of the Taiwan public, and promote the spiritual connection of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136864.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The MAC claims it will arrange for two mainland residents who are stranded in Taiwan to leave for a third location, and then apply to come to Taiwan under the name of \"professional exchange.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. This is a malicious act by the DPP authorities to create a pretext and provoke cross-Strait relations. We are closely monitoring developments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The U.S. Navy announced that two warships transited the Taiwan Strait on January 24. On the same day, several PLA aircraft flew over the Bashi Channel and then returned, and three warships were active in waters east of Taiwan. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question concerns China's core interests, and we firmly oppose any external interference. We have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201901/t20190130_12136861.htm"],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中评社记者","On January 22 local time, the US House of Representatives voted to pass a bill requiring the US Secretary of State to study strategies to help Taiwan regain observer status at the World Health Organization. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. As for Taiwan's participation in activities of the WHO and other international organizations, it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Only by recognizing the one-China principle can arrangements for Taiwan's participation in WHO activities be made through cross-Strait consultations. Relying on foreign powers to raise one's own standing leads nowhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen has frequently engaged with Taiwan’s military and promoted the “mainland threat theory,” attempting to pursue “independence” by force and to resist unification by force. How does the spokesperson assess this?","In a word: using force to resist unification is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Last year, the TV drama “Story of Yanxi Palace” was a hit on the island and became the island’s top traffic draw. Recently, media reports revealed that this drama was also included in the island’s 2019 university subject competence test. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","I think compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, and Chinese culture is our common root and soul. In recent years, excellent mainland film and television dramas have been highly sought after by audiences in Taiwan and have had a wide influence. This is a natural thing. As for what you mentioned about the General Scholastic Ability Test (學測), I think it is also following hot topics.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","We note that Tsai Ing-wen, the leader of the Taiwan region, once again wrote to the Pope. In the letter, she falsely claimed that “the mainland suppresses and belittles Taiwan,” promoted the so-called “four musts,” accused the mainland of “not abandoning the threat of force,” and finally boasted of having a spirit of peace. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","In recent times, the leaders of the DPP authorities have, one moment, pretended to be “Popeye” playing an internet celebrity, and the next moment played the “leading lady” crying foul abroad, constantly raising cross-Strait antagonism, inciting hostility between the two sides, obstructing exchanges and cooperation between the peoples on both sides, and undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Anyone can see that they perform so zealously, even at the cost of the interests of the Taiwan people, purely for self-interest and party interest.\nThe Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. We have always treated Taiwan compatriots well; Chinese do not fight Chinese. If we have deterred anyone, it is of course the “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest scourge to the fundamental interests of the Taiwan people and the greatest threat to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. If anyone wants to take it personally, they will only humiliate themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Taiwan media reported that the Mainland Affairs Council has banned some radio programs from broadcasting the remarks of Taiwan reporters stationed in Beijing, on the grounds that these reporters' ideology has become “leaning toward China.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The relevant video has already been broadcast online, and I believe everyone has seen it. The reporters concerned have already mounted forceful questioning and strong rebuttals. This incident once again reflects that the Mainland Affairs Council and the DPP authorities have stopped at nothing in undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台声杂志社记者","On January 25, the famous Taiwan writer Lin Qingxuan passed away, and several of his essays were selected for mainland primary and secondary school textbooks. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Mr. Lin Qingxuan is a well-known writer admired on both sides of the Strait. He actively engaged in cross-Strait cultural exchanges, visited more than 300 cities on the mainland, and was a close friend of many mainland writers. Mr. Lin's broad-minded and serene character, and his faith in and adherence to Chinese wisdom and Chinese culture, found expression in a fresh and pure aesthetic style that has deeply remained in the memory of readers on both sides of the Strait. On his passing, I would like to express my grief with the line \"A cup of turbid wine to see off the clear delights.\" I hope that after his passing, exchanges in the cultural and artistic circles of both sides of the Strait will become ever closer, and that Chinese culture will be further promoted and carried forward on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Straits Exchange Foundation Chairperson Zhang Xiaoyue recently said that even though the two sides currently hold different political positions, she believes cross-Strait cultural exchanges should become more frequent and in-depth, and she hopes to have the opportunity to visit, in person, schools on the mainland attended by the children of Taiwan businesspeople. May I ask what response the TAO has to this?","I believe everyone has noticed that Ms. Chang Hsiao-yueh's statement does not seem to match what the Mainland Affairs Council and the DPP authorities have been doing. As for the institutionalized consultation and exchange mechanism between the two associations, it has stalled since the DPP took office, and I believe everyone knows clearly why. So I also hope that the SEF will urge the DPP authorities to return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” as soon as possible, so that her wish to visit the mainland can be realized at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","Recently Tsai Ing-wen attended a Lunar New Year gathering for Mainland spouses hosted by the Straits Exchange Foundation and mentioned that in the past few years some improvements were made on issues related to Mainland spouses in advancing policy and amending laws. How does the spokesperson comment on this remark?","As is well known, for a long time the DPP and its authorities have imposed many unreasonable and even inhumane restrictions on the rights of mainland spouses, including unreasonable restrictions on their right to work, their right of residence, and even their rights to vote and to stand for election. Where the so-called “improvement” claim comes from, I do not know. If the DPP authorities truly intend to make improvements, they should act at once and remove, as early as possible, the various unreasonable restrictions imposed on mainland spouses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Second question: Just yesterday, Xiamen and Kinmen again connected, and around the principle of “connecting everything that should be connected,” proposed deepening the construction of the “Xiamen-Kinmen Common Living Circle” in the new year. What is the spokesperson's comment? In which areas do you think Xiamen and Kinmen can still pilot first?","From January 27 to 30, Kinmen County Magistrate Yang Zhenwu led a delegation to Fujian for exchanges and a visit, and discussed with relevant parties in Fujian promoting connections for water, gas, electricity and bridges between the two places, as well as exchanges between counties and cities. Our attitude is open. As long as something benefits the kinship and well-being of compatriots across the Taiwan Strait, we are willing to actively promote it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Following up on the question: data on export orders released by Taiwan’s administration last week show that total orders from the mainland, Hong Kong and Macau reached NT$130.23 billion, a record high, up 6.2% from 2017. What is the spokesperson’s view of this data?","I think this reflects two points. First, it shows that cross-Strait economic and trade relations are already inseparable, with you in me and me in you: united, both sides prosper; divided, both sides suffer. This cannot be changed by any person’s will or by any means of interference or sabotage. Second, it also shows that over these years, as the mainland has developed and prospered, as it has continuously introduced policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, and as it has continuously launched measures to expand opening and deepen reform, we have created a good environment and conditions for Taiwan businesses to develop in the mainland and for cross-Strait economic and trade prosperity. Of course, we sincerely hope, and are also willing, to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, so that Taiwan compatriots can achieve greater and better development in the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Second question: McDonald’s previously mislabeled Taiwan in an advertisement in the Taiwan region, and afterward urgently issued a statement saying it has always adhered to the one-China position, yet Taiwan’s foreign affairs department expressed dissatisfaction because of this. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, which has an indisputable factual and legal basis. Enterprises investing and operating in China should respect this fact and abide by China’s laws.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊","Follow-up question: In responding to remarks by Lai Ching-te and others on “constitutional reform to rectify the name,” the newly elected DPP chairman said the DPP will not be absent when it comes to facing the “Taiwan independence movement.” What is the spokesperson’s view?","This once again exposes that the DPP is a disruptor of cross-Strait relations and a troublemaker for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We issue a serious warning: if they dare to promote all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, we will never sit idly by.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-01-30","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Second question: Cheng Li-chiun, head of Taiwan's culture authority, was recently slapped by someone dissatisfied with “de-Chiang-ization.” Some reports revealed that Cheng Li-chiun supports cultural “Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization,” yet her family has long invested on the mainland. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have seen this report, and we have noted that Taiwan public opinion holds that the DPP authorities should reflect on why such a slap incident occurred.\nAs for the second layer of your question, our position and attitude are very clear and very firm. We will not allow anyone or any enterprise to earn money on the mainland on the one hand while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities on the other and undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201901/t20190130_12136879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-02-20","Geng Shuang","","The Nicaraguan government says it has received a 100 million dollar loan from Taiwan. Beijing and Taipei frequently trade accusations of \"dollar diplomacy\". Does this in the Chinese government's eyes count as \"dollar diplomacy\" from Taiwan trying to ensure that Nicaragua maintains diplomatic ties with Taipei?","China is committed to developing relations with other countries on the basis of the one-China principle and the five principles of peaceful coexistence. We hope all countries can recognize the one-China principle, which is a consensus among members of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1639566.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1639502.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-02-22","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Chen Ming-tong, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently claimed that if people from all sectors of Taiwan go to the mainland to participate in democratic consultation, they would violate the “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area.” He also named New Party Chairman Jaw Shaw-kong and threatened him with “do not test the penalty with your…","XINHUA, Beijing, February 22 — TAO spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on the 22nd: Some people in the DPP authorities readily wield big sticks to suppress political parties and individuals who support unification. This fully exposes their essence of harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and acting against the tide of history. They cannot stop the historical trend of cross-Strait relations moving forward.\nAn Fengshan said that General Secretary Xi Jinping solemnly proposed that, \"On the common political foundation of adhering to the '1992 Consensus' and opposing 'Taiwan independence,' political parties and sectors on both sides of the Strait nominate representative figures to conduct extensive and in-depth democratic consultation on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, and reach institutional arrangements for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\" Democratic consultation is the correct direction for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it accords with public opinion on both sides and the trend of the times. We warmly welcome representative figures from all Taiwan political parties and sectors to participate actively, offer suggestions, and jointly advance this effort.\nAn Fengshan pointed out that Chairman Yu Mu-ming said, \"I am willing to take the lead in consulting with the mainland to seek a peaceful development mechanism toward unification and ensure peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait,\" which demonstrates a sense of national righteousness and mission.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190222_12141842.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-02-26","Lu Kang","","Two US warships yesterday sailed through the Taiwan Strait, which I believe is something like the fourth or fifth mission by US warships through the Taiwan Strait in the last couple of months. Has China complained to the United States about this latest sailing?","The Chinese side has made clear its position many times and expressed its concerns to the US side. We are firmly opposed to these provocative actions by the US side which are not conducive to the peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as well as the China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1641180.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1641120.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office held this morning. The Spring Festival has just passed, and I wish everyone a happy New Year. Now I am glad to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","新华社记者","I have two questions. First, the mainland's proposal to “explore a ‘two systems’ plan for Taiwan” has prompted Taiwan public opinion to pay attention to and discuss “one country, two systems,” but some people on the island still have doubts about “one country, two systems.” Please elaborate further. Second, Tsai Ing-wen recently accepted an interview with foreign media, slandering and attacking the mainland for…","On the first question: compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China have not been divided and cannot be divided. This is an indisputable fact with a sufficient legal basis. National rejuvenation and national reunification are the trend of the times and a matter of great righteousness. The motherland must be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified; this is the historical verdict on the development of cross-Strait relations and an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in the new era. The future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should work together to seek national reunification and heal historical wounds.\n“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and is the best way to achieve national reunification. It fully takes into account the realities in Taiwan and is conducive to the long-term stability and security of Taiwan after reunification. “One country, two systems” reflects our greatest goodwill and care for Taiwan compatriots and will inevitably bring Taiwan compatriots greater development opportunities and better living conditions. After peaceful reunification, Taiwan will enjoy lasting peace and its people will live and work in contentment. With a strong motherland to rely on, the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be better, their development space will be greater, and they will stand taller and be more confident internationally, enjoying greater security and dignity.\nDifferences in systems are not an obstacle to reunification, much less an excuse for division. The proposal of “one country, two systems” was originally meant to take account of the realities in Taiwan and to safeguard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. General Secretary Xi Jinping has pointed out that the specific form of realizing “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities in Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, and fully accommodate the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. On the premise of safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests, after peaceful reunification, the social systems and way of life of Taiwan compatriots will be fully respected, and their private property, religious beliefs and lawful rights and interests will be fully protected.\nOn the second question, the claims of “oppression” and “threats” are a complete distortion of the facts, designed to confuse people. Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. We have consistently done practical things, good things and things that resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, resolutely safeguarded and continuously enhanced the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and helped them achieve greater and better development. The DPP authorities, by contrast, stand in opposition to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and are doing exactly the opposite.\nWe resolutely oppose and deter “Taiwan independence” precisely to safeguard the common interests of all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots, because “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest harm to the fundamental interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. On this matter of principle, which concerns the fundamental interests of the nation and its compatriots, our position is firm and unwavering.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142930.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142936.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","I have two questions. First, Fujian Province plans to supply electricity to Kinmen and Matsu and has launched relevant projects to supply water to Matsu. Please introduce the relevant situation. What considerations and plans are there for the next step? Second, according to reports, Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu will visit Xiamen and other places in the near future, and some blue-camp mayors have also announced they…","On the first question: General Secretary Xi, in his important speech at the symposium marking the 40th anniversary of the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan,” proposed that relatives should wish well for relatives, that Chinese should help Chinese, and that cross-Strait relations should achieve full connectivity. This means smoother trade and economic cooperation, infrastructure connectivity, energy and resource interchange, and common industry standards. He also proposed that water, electricity, gas, and bridge connections between Kinmen and Matsu and the coastal areas of Fujian could be realized first. This reflects our development philosophy of “putting the people first.” It focuses on the common development of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. By sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, working for their well-being, helping to solve practical economic and livelihood problems, we aim to provide better and more development conditions for Taiwan compatriots.\nThe people of Kinmen and Matsu have long hoped that the mainland could help resolve difficulties such as shortages of water and electricity, and they have repeatedly expressed their appeals for gas and bridge connections. Our position on these needs is very clear: the mainland is willing to make every effort to create opportunities and provide conditions for them to achieve greater and better development. Relevant departments in Fujian Province have preliminarily completed research and planning for supplying electricity to Kinmen and Matsu and water to Matsu, and have made preparatory arrangements. We will also continue to take active steps to accelerate the construction of gas and bridge connections between Fujian’s coastal areas and Kinmen and Matsu, and to promote integrated development across the Strait.\nOn the second question: we welcome and support cross-Strait city exchanges and cooperation in various forms on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” and jointly enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Recently, several Taiwan county and city heads have led delegations to visit the mainland and carry out exchanges and cooperation with relevant mainland cities, achieving positive results. We welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to join in. As long as both sides work together, overcome obstacles, and actively promote exchanges and cooperation, more tangible benefits can be brought to Taiwan compatriots.\nYou also mentioned that public opinion on the island hopes the mainland will include content on cross-Strait city exchanges in the “31 measures.” We believe that all sectors on the island are actively offering suggestions on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This reflects the strong desire of Taiwan compatriots to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and achieve common development, and their concern for and support of the mainland’s policies to benefit Taiwan compatriots. In recent years, we have listened carefully to the voices of Taiwan compatriots, and many of the policy measures we have introduced to benefit them have responded positively to their appeals and played a role in enhancing their well-being. The prospects for promoting exchanges and cooperation, including cross-Strait city exchanges, are broad, and there is still much to be done. However, there are also some well-known artificial obstacles. We hope that compatriots on both sides can work together to remove these obstacles, and continuously expand the scope of benefits and their sense of gain from strengthened exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142932.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142933.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","人民日报海外版记者","The “31 Measures” to promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation will mark their first anniversary tomorrow. What achievements have the “31 Measures” produced over this past year? What further measures to deepen implementation will follow?","Last year, on February 28, also here, we officially issued the “Several Measures on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation Across the Taiwan Strait.” The promulgation and implementation of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” reflects our sincere willingness to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and also highlights the important concept of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family.”\nOver the year since the “31 Measures” were implemented, they have brought tangible benefits to Taiwanese enterprises’ investment and business operations on the mainland and to Taiwan compatriots’ development on the mainland, and have achieved good results. First, they have improved the convenience for Taiwan compatriots to study, work, and live in various parts of the mainland; second, “equal treatment” for Taiwan compatriots has been implemented in a wider scope and in more fields; third, Taiwan compatriots have a greater sense of participation, gain, and integration, which has further promoted the integrated economic and social development of both sides of the Strait.\nTo date, 72 localities on the mainland, including 25 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, have each formulated specific implementation measures, covering all provinces in the eastern region, most provinces in the central, western and northeastern regions, and all separately planned cities. Many localities have published implementation rules that include policy interpretations, procedures, and contact telephone numbers, basically achieving “every provision has a case, every item has a result.” Some localities, in light of their own circumstances, have taken the lead in pilot programs, providing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises with more equal treatment alongside local residents and enterprises. Over the past year, according to incomplete statistics, more than 2,000 Taiwanese enterprises have enjoyed various tax preferences, such as those for high-and-new technology enterprises; more than 100 Taiwanese enterprises have received special funds supporting industrial transformation and upgrading, green manufacturing, intelligent manufacturing and other areas; a number of outstanding Taiwanese enterprises have won government procurement projects, including Beijing New Airport, the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge, the Wuhan Tianxingzhou Yangtze River Bridge, and the Hangzhou city landmark light show; more than 800 Taiwan compatriots have obtained qualifications in several popular professions; and more than 100 Taiwan compatriots have received honorary titles from various localities, such as the “May Day Labor Medal,” “March 8 Red Banner Bearer,” and “May Fourth Youth Medal.” In 2018, the number of Taiwan students applying to mainland universities, the number of Taiwan youth coming to the mainland for employment, and the number of newly added Taiwanese enterprises served by mainland employment and entrepreneurship service institutions all maintained double-digit growth. More and more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises, especially Taiwan students and Taiwan youth, are choosing to develop on the mainland to realize their life ambitions.\nGoing forward, we will thoroughly implement the important speech of General Secretary Xi, “continue to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises.” We will continue, together with relevant departments and localities, to carry out the implementation of the “31 Measures” with a “hammer-on-the-nail” spirit, promptly coordinate and resolve issues of common concern to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises, study and introduce more measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, and provide more convenient conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises to develop on the mainland, so that Taiwan compatriots gain more of a sense of benefit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142935.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Recently, KMT Chairman Wu Den-yih and others have raised the topic of a cross-Strait peace agreement. The DPP and its authorities oppose this, claiming they will “amend the law” to set a high threshold for negotiating and signing a cross-Strait peace agreement, requiring “dual review and dual referendum.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and also lies in their common interests. Anything that is conducive to the fundamental interests of compatriots across the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation should be vigorously promoted. Any issue that is conducive to safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait, conducive to advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and conducive to advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland can be jointly explored by both sides of the Strait and by all sectors of society. On the basis of the one-China principle, both sides of the Strait, all political parties, and people from all walks of life should, with a responsible attitude toward the nation and future generations, pool wisdom, bring their creativity into play, seek common ground while reserving differences, and strive to resolve political confrontation at an early date and achieve lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, disregarding the desire of Taiwan residents for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and for mutual benefit and win-win outcomes, are going against this trend and obstructing it at every turn. They will only harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and ruin Taiwan’s future and prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142934.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Two questions. First, the director of the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office recently visited Taipei, and a visit he had been invited to make to central and southern Taiwan was reportedly blocked. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council claimed that mainland TAO officials who come to Taiwan mostly have political aims and should not be allowed to “walk around thoroughly” in Taiwan. What is your comment on this?…","On your first question, during his visit to Taiwan, Li Wenhui, Director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office, had no contact whatsoever with Chen Ming-tong. How could he have made such a statement? This is not the first time such fabrication of facts out of nothing has occurred.\nThe purpose of Taiwan Affairs Office personnel from various places visiting Taiwan is to promote exchange and cooperation between compatriots on both sides and to enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots; they go there to do good deeds. During this year's Spring Festival, in order to let Taiwan compatriots better celebrate the Chinese nation's traditional festival, many local Taiwan Affairs Offices took the lead in organizing various cultural, tourism and folk activities to be displayed and performed in Taiwan, enriching the festive life of Taiwan compatriots, and these were welcomed and well received by Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan compatriots have seen these measures with their own eyes and kept them in mind. The Taiwan authorities setting obstacles to their visits to Taiwan is undermining good deeds for Taiwan compatriots. Certain personnel in relevant departments, including the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, have repeatedly spoken abusive words and obstructed cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, arousing public indignation on both sides of the Strait.\nOn your second question, book recommenders and book recommendations are part of the book content, selected by publishers and authors, which is a normal common practice. The DPP authorities' interference only concerns the routine book publishing of publishers and authors; they exploit the issue to slander and smear the Mainland. What is their intention? It is well known.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142929.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","央视中国新闻记者","The Ministry of Education recently announced that starting this year, the standards for Taiwan high school graduates applying to mainland universities will be adjusted again. Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation.","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,3,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","The Taiwan MAC recently said that the Taiwan community's assistant director employed in Haicang District, Xiamen, committed a so-called “principled violation of law.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","In recent years, more and more Taiwan youth have come to the mainland to study, work, and start businesses. We have also successively introduced a series of policies to provide more convenience for Taiwan students studying on the mainland and more opportunities for Taiwan youth to make the most of their strengths. Some localities, based on local conditions, have adopted innovative measures. For example, Haicang District of Xiamen City has hired Taiwan compatriots as community director assistants to help the local area, from a professional perspective, carry out rural revitalization and community construction work; this is one beneficial exploration among them.\nAs is well known, residents’ committees and villagers’ committees on the mainland are both grassroots self-governing organizations. These Taiwan compatriot community director assistants sign labor contracts with local enterprises, take part in community work, and enjoy the same treatment and social security as other employees. The so-called “illegality” accusations by relevant Taiwan authorities are groundless and utterly untenable. You may recall that last year some Taiwan youth applied for positions at the Bank of China, and the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council went so far as to accuse these Taiwan youth of “illegality” on the pretext that the Bank of China is a public institution on the mainland. For years, tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots have worked at public institutions such as mainland universities and hospitals, as well as in grassroots communities, state-owned enterprises, and financial institutions such as state-owned commercial banks. Does the DPP authorities really insist on breaking their rice bowls, cutting off their livelihoods, and ruining their well-being? What is the intention behind arbitrarily obstructing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth from studying, working, and starting businesses on the mainland and seeking better development opportunities?\nWe will, as always, work for the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, provide better space for development for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to work and start businesses and to chase, build, and realize their dreams, and will firmly safeguard their legitimate rights and interests. The DPP authorities should not repeatedly obstruct and interfere with normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, cut off Taiwan youth’s employment and development opportunities, or make unwarranted difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. That will never win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142931.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","中新社记者","The \"Outline Development Plan for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area\" was recently released. What business opportunities will it bring to Taiwan businesspeople?","Recently, the CPC Central Committee and the State Council issued the “Outline Development Plan for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area,” which points out that the Greater Bay Area is both a new attempt to promote the formation of a new pattern of comprehensive opening in the new era and a new practice in advancing the cause of “one country, two systems.” The Greater Bay Area, along with major strategies such as the coordinated development of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei, the construction of the Yangtze River Economic Belt, the integration of the Yangtze River Delta, and the Hainan Free Trade Pilot Zone, will provide more development opportunities for Taiwan businesses on the mainland and create a favorable development environment. They will help give full play to the advantages of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in areas such as science and technology innovation, and strengthen deep integration between industry, academia and research across the Strait. We actively welcome and support broad Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in participating in these major strategies and achieving better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","February 28 marks the first anniversary of the release and implementation of the “31 Measures.” The Cross-Strait Internet Exchange Committee of the Internet Society of China is about to release a mobile service application product called “31 Measures.” Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","In order to better provide high-quality cross-Strait information services to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, the Cross-Strait Internet Exchange Committee, on the first anniversary of the implementation of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” developed an app named “31条” which will be officially released today.\nThe product currently performs three main functions: aggregating cross-Strait information, releasing authoritative information, and interactive community Q&A. It centrally displays the implementation rules and latest information for the “31 Measures” in 72 localities on the mainland, including 25 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, and answers questions from netizens. The “31条” APP is the first authoritative mobile application platform providing cross-Strait information services. It will be gradually listed on major internet app markets, and its content and service functions will continue to be improved. We welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, to download and use it, and to offer suggestions for improvement.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142927.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Tomorrow is the “February 28” commemoration day. Taiwan independence forces on the island have recently been hyping the “February 28” issue again. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Tomorrow marks the 72nd anniversary of the “2·28 Incident.” We have also noted that whenever this time comes around, some Green camp politicians and “Taiwan independence” forces on the island become restless, deliberately distort historical facts, stir up ethnic antagonism, divide Taiwan society, and worsen cross-Strait relations. They do this only for their own electoral interests and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, which run directly counter to the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","It is understood that the Higher People's Court of Fujian Province recently published the “Measures on Further Leveraging Judicial Functions to Promote Cross-Strait Economic, Cultural Exchange and Cooperation.” Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the relevant details.","On February 22, the Fujian Provincial High People’s Court issued the “Several Measures on Further Giving Play to Judicial Functions to Promote Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation.” Centered on ensuring that Taiwan compatriots share mainland development opportunities first, the “Measures” set out 59 measures in four areas: fully playing the function of protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots; effectively safeguarding the equal litigation rights of Taiwan compatriots; actively improving litigation service mechanisms for Taiwan compatriots; and supporting Taiwan compatriots’ orderly participation in judicial matters. They basically cover all fields and aspects of judicial work related to Taiwan.\nThe “Measures” are an important step taken by Fujian courts, on the basis of comprehensively summarizing useful experience in past judicial work involving Taiwan, to actively respond to the judicial demands of Taiwan compatriots and effectively safeguard their legitimate rights and interests. They will provide more adequate and favorable judicial guarantees for the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots investing, starting businesses, studying and living in Fujian.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","The World Internet Conference recently took place in Spain. At first, Taiwan’s authorities refused to attend because the registration website referred to them as “Taiwan: a province of China”; after they protested, their protest was rejected. Pro-green Taiwanese media claimed that the World Mobile Communications Conference is one of the world’s most important communications industry gatherings, and that Taiwan’s…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China, which is a fact recognized by the international community. Adhering to the One-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, and also reflects the aspirations of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","On the 25th, two more U.S. warships were reported to have transited the Taiwan Strait. Some foreign media say this shows support for Taiwan. How do you respond?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position on this issue. The Taiwan question concerns our country's core interests, and we firmly oppose any external interference. We have firm resolve, full confidence and sufficient capacity to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","台湾旺报记者","Recently, when the mainland was reviewing the draft Foreign Investment Law, Zhang Zhijun, Chairman of ARATS, mentioned treating Taiwan capital as “special domestic capital.” May I ask whether there are more specific further ideas or supporting regulations at present?","Investments by Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are subject to the Provisions on the Protection of Investments by Taiwan Compatriots and their Implementing Rules. Since reform and opening up, the mainland has always been a fertile ground for investment for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, while achieving their own development and growth, have also made important contributions to the economic and social development of the mainland. In the current process of deepening reform, expanding opening up, and achieving high-quality development, we will continue to welcome, encourage and protect Taiwan compatriots' investment on the mainland, share in the mainland's development opportunities, and achieve greater and better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, regarding the upgrade program for Taiwan Air Force's F-16V fighters, the U.S. side plans to deliver the first four units by the end of March. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The Taiwan question concerns China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201902/t20190227_12142928.htm"],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","台湾三立电视台记者","Many KMT-governed counties and cities want to hold exchanges with the mainland. In the future, if DPP-governed counties and cities set aside political baggage and show goodwill, will the mainland likewise respond with equal goodwill?","We have consistently stressed that as long as one has a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and of city exchanges across the Strait, we welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to take part in cross-Strait city exchanges and to jointly enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","人民日报记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that Taiwan's record-setting agricultural exports to the mainland in 2018 were the result of the joint efforts of the DPP authorities and the private sector. What comment do you have on this?","The mainland has always been concerned about the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwan's farmers and fishermen, and has actively done real good deeds and solved difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. In sharing the mainland's development opportunities, Taiwan's farmers and fishermen should not be absent and should have a greater sense of gain. Facing the many obstacles set up by the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities, we have made our utmost efforts and actively taken measures to address the difficulties of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen and help them expand into the mainland market. When agricultural products in Taiwan are unsold, we have promptly extended a helping hand to counties and cities that made requests, helping Taiwan's farmers and fishermen get through hard times and gain tangible benefits. Last year, compatriots on both sides of the Strait worked together to overcome difficulties created by the DPP authorities and achieved results, which is a concrete illustration of “both sides of the Strait are one family.”\nWho is doing good for compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and who is sabotaging their good deeds, Taiwan compatriots have their own gauge in their hearts. People on the island are asking whether the DPP authorities have ever done anything good to enhance the well-being and kinship of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The answer is very clear. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait can continue to work together, remove obstacles, and create better conditions for enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","A game in Taiwan called “Huan Yuan” (还愿, “Fulfilling a Vow”) was recently banned on the mainland. Please introduce the specific situation.","I am not familiar with the video game you mentioned. The mainland manages the internet and electronic products in accordance with law and regulation, which is entirely normal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","人民日报海外网记者","Taiwan's “Premier” Su Tseng-chang recently declared that he would fight the mainland even with a broom, and the head of Taiwan's defense department, Yen Teh-fa, also claimed this demonstrates the determination to fight a defensive battle. What comment does the spokesperson have on this? Second question: Taiwan's relevant authorities released statistics for January showing that mainland investment in Taiwan was…","Your first question: recently, some \"prominent figures\" in Taiwan have frequently issued hostile and provocative remarks, constantly inciting cross-Strait hostility, escalating cross-Strait confrontation, and worsening cross-Strait relations. In order to gain a meager electoral advantage, they have not hesitated to push Taiwan Strait peace and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots to the brink of danger. As the island's public opinion has criticized, their conduct is like \"a blind man riding a blind horse toward a deep pool at midnight.\" This further proves that the DPP authorities are the instigators of cross-Strait conflict, the disruptors of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the harmers of the interests of the Taiwan people.\nWe are willing, with the utmost sincerity and by making the greatest efforts, to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait. At the same time, we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist scheme or action, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nYour second question: at the first press conference after this year's New Year's Day, we already released a summary of cross-Strait personnel exchanges, trade and economic exchanges, two-way investment, and other topics for 2018. Expanding and deepening exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait is our consistent policy position, because it accords with the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides and with the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots. In fact, over the years we have worked hard to promote this work, and in particular last year we introduced the \"31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,\" launched the Taiwan residence permit, abolished employment permits for Taiwan residents, realized water supply to Kinmen, and a series of other measures. The purpose is to promote exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides and to advance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. By contrast, the DPP authorities have consistently engaged in obstructing and interfering with cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Despite these numerous obstacles, through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, cross-Strait personnel exchanges, trade and economic exchanges, and exchanges and cooperation in various fields last year still reached historic highs. I believe the reason for such achievements is that this reflects the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides and accords with their common interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the Taiwan authorities decided to push for amendments to relevant regulations to extend the controlled period for retired senior officials traveling to the mainland. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","As I mentioned in answering the previous question, we are actively promoting exchanges and cooperation between the two sides across all fields and working to enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Meanwhile, the DPP authorities are doing everything they can to set up various obstacles, obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and undermining good things for Taiwan compatriots. I believe the people of Taiwan clearly understand who is actually doing things that benefit ordinary people in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-02-27","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Fu Jen Catholic University recently issued a faculty notice stating that some students reported to the Taiwan Affairs Office that certain teachers on campus were instilling and promoting personal ideology in class. The faculty notice also said that, as a result, the mainland has asked the university to reduce the enrollment quota for mainland students. Regarding this matter, the DPP authorities responded with a…","The Taiwan side has a responsibility to provide a normal learning environment for students from the mainland studying in Taiwan and to ensure that their basic rights during their time in Taiwan are not subject to any interference or harm. Otherwise, it will only undermine exchange and cooperation in the field of cross-Strait education.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201902/t20190227_12142923.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-02-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, two US military vessels sailed across the Taiwan Strait again after last month’s operation, and this is the fifth operation in the past eight months. Foreign media considered these actions as the support for Taiwan. Do you have any comment? My second question is that some Japanese media reported that Japan’s defense ministry has invited many foreign countries including China to the ship parade of…","The Chinese side is fully aware of all the moves of relevant US military vessels and keeps high alert to these moves all the time. And here I want to reiterate that Taiwan is a part of China; the Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is also the most important and sensitive issue in the China-US relationship. We urge the US side to abide by the ‘One China Principle’ and the Three China-US Joint Communiques, and carefully handle the Taiwan -related issues.\nAs for your second question, in line with the improving bilateral ties between China and Japan, the two sides will have a series of exchanges and interactions in defense and security areas this year such as the productive experts' meeting for the direct hotline of the Maritime and Air Liaison Mechanism. As for the specific exchanges and programs, we will keep communication with the Japanese side and release information in due course. We are currently preparing for activities celebrating the 70th anniversary of the founding of the PLA Navy , and we will release relevant information according to the progress in our preparations.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-02/28/content_4836995.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-03-11","Lu Kang","","The US Ambassador-at-Large for International Religious Freedom, Sam Brownback, has been in Hong Kong last week and he is currently in Taiwan. He has made some very strong comments critical of China in both places, including criticizing China's treatment of Uyghurs in Xinjiang. What is your reaction?","Your question touches on two aspects. First of all, I want to stress again that China firmly opposes any official contacts between the US government and Taiwan. This position is rock firm.\nSecondly, we have noted these wrong remarks made by the relevant person. We deplore and firmly oppose that and have made stern representations with the US side. The Chinese government protects its citizens' freedom of religious belief in accordance with law and people of all ethnic groups in China fully enjoy their right to freedom of religious belief in accordance with law. The Chinese side consistently opposes the US side cooking up or using the so-called religious issues to interfere in other countries' internal affairs. We urge the US side to face squarely and respect basic facts, cast aside prejudice, choose its words and actions carefully, view China's religious policies and freedom of religious belief in an objective way, stop using the so-called religious issues to interfere in China's internal affairs.\nThis person in question mentioned the so-called issues in Xinjiang. I want to say that the affairs of Xinjiang are China's internal affairs. Xinjiang set up the vocational and educational training centers as a preventive counter-terrorism and de-radicalisation measure. They are not the so-called \"re-education camps\" claimed by the US. Facts have proven that the measures taken in Xinjiang to counter terrorism and maintain stability enjoy extensive support from all ethnic groups in Xinjiang. We urge the US side to discard its double standards on counter-terrorism and counter-separatism, stop using Xinjiang-related issues to interfere in China's domestic affairs, and contribute to enhancing mutual trust and cooperation between China and the US, instead of the contrary.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1644609.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-03-12","Lu Kang","","The US Ambassador-at-Large for International Religious Freedom Sam Brownback, who is still in Taiwan on a visit, held a press conference today with the wife of Li Mingzhe, the Taiwanese activist who has been jailed in China. Brownback called on China to immediately release Li Mingzhe and said this case is of serious concern to Washington. Is China prepared to release him because of the concern of the US?","I want to make two brief points. First, as I said explicitly here yesterday, China firmly opposes any official contacts between the US and China's Taiwan region. This unshakable position remains unchanged. We hope that the US government will strictly abide by the one-China policy.\nSecond, the individual case you mentioned is between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. It belongs to China's internal affairs and others have no right to meddle in it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1644890.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-03-12","Lu Kang","","Tsai Ing-wen will next week visit three of Taiwan's diplomatic allies in the Pacific, namely Palau, Nauru and the Marshall Islands. Taiwanese officials say the government is currently in talks with the US side on her stopovers in the US territories, presumably Guam or Hawaii. Has the Chinese government already warned the US government not to allow Tsai Ing-wen to stop over in US territory?","The one-China principle is a consensus shared by the international community. Any attempts to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China one Taiwan\" will be strongly opposed by all the Chinese people. The fundamental interests of the people in China's Taiwan region will not be served in that way.\nAs for the activities planned by Tsai Ing-wen and Taiwan-independence forces inside Taiwan, the official from the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already said unequivocally that we hope that the authority in Taiwan will grasp the trend and understand the situation correctly, come back to the 1992 consensus at an early date, and stop working against the trend and the popular wish.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1644890.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-03-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 12 (reporter Zhao Bo): On March 11–12, the “Indo-Pacific Region Civil Society Dialogue on Defending Religious Freedom” was held in Taiwan, and Brownback, U.S. State Department Ambassador-at-Large for International Religious Freedom, attended. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan, responding to questions on the 12th, said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on this. I must reiterate: we firmly oppose any form of official exchange between any country that has diplomatic ties with us and Taiwan, and this position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190313_12147970.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-13","An Fengshan","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 12 (Xinhua). In response to questions about the proposal by Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities to counter the \"one country, two systems\" Taiwan plan, which has further worsened cross-Strait relations, An Fengshan, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 12th: Recently, the various actions of Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities are in essence undermining the prospects for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resisting the great trend toward peaceful reunification of the two sides, and seeking \"Taiwan independence\" and separation. Their constant wanton attacks on the mainland, their deception of the Taiwan public, their incitement of hostility across the Strait, and their escalation of confrontation and worsening of cross-Strait relations are using the interests and well-being of the Taiwan public as a stake to gain electoral advantage. They are entirely driven by personal and party interests. The Mainland Affairs Council has gone even further, setting up obstacles everywhere and standing against the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, trying hard to block compatriots on both sides from moving closer and making solid progress. This is nothing but a praying mantis trying to stop a chariot, an act of overestimating one's own strength.\nAn Fengshan emphasized once again that \"peaceful reunification, one country, two systems\" is our consistent basic policy. The specific form of \"one country, two systems\" in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, will fully absorb the opinions and suggestions from all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and will fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. Any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist act that goes against the tide cannot stop the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190313_12147971.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-03-19","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan's \"diplomatic ally\" Solomon Islands will soon hold elections. Is it China's hope that the new administration severs ties with Taiwan? Has the Chinese side initiated contact with the Solomon Islands?","The one-China principle is a consensus of the international community. The Chinese government develops friendly and cooperative relationships with other countries on the basis of the one-China principle and the five principles of peaceful coexistence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1646704.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1646623.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-03-21","Geng Shuang","","Tsai Ing-wen will \"stop over\" in Hawaii on her \"diplomatic tour\" next week. Has China already complained to the US about this?","The one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. Any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will be opposed by all Chinese people.\nAs to the so-called \"stopover\" issue of the Taiwan leader in the US, China has stated its position repeatedly and lodged stern representations with the US side. We firmly oppose the arrangement of such \"stopovers\" by the US or any other country having diplomatic ties with China. This position is clear and resolute.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, not to allow Tsai Ing-wen to \"stop over\", refrain from sending out any wrong signal to Taiwan-independence forces, and to uphold China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1647428.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1647334.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-03-22","Geng Shuang","","Bloomberg News reported that the US government has given approval to Taiwan's request to buy more than 60 F-16 fighter jets, according to people familiar with the matter. I wonder if you have any comment on that?","China resolutely opposes US arms sales to Taiwan, and this position remains consistent and firm. We have lodged stern representations to the US. We urge the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive and harmful nature of the relevant issue, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 communiqué, to stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, and carefully and prudently handle the Taiwan-related issues lest it should seriously damage the cooperation between China and the US in important areas and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1647752.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1647631.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-03-25","Geng Shuang","","A US warship and a US Coast Guard ship sailed through Taiwan Strait yesterday. What is your reaction to that?","China has paid close attention to and monitored from start to end the passage of the US military vessels through the Taiwan Strait. We have made representations to the US side. We urge the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid damaging China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1648178.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1648138.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-03-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. Navy destroyer USS Wilbur and the Coast Guard cutter Bertholf transited the Taiwan Strait on the 24th. What is your comment on this?","We are clear about the situation of the relevant US vessel transiting the Taiwan Strait, and its movements have been under our full control throughout. China has expressed its concerns to the US side.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-US relations. We demand that the US abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and avoid undermining China-US relations, military-to-military relations between the two countries, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. The PLA will remain on high alert at all times and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/TopStories/4838223.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/qwfb/4838204.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO's regular press conference. I am glad to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu recently led a delegation to visit Hong Kong, Macau, Shenzhen and Xiamen. What results have been achieved? What is the significance for future cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation?","Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu's trip has recently been a focus of attention in cross-Strait and Hong Kong and Macau media. From March 22 to 28, Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu led a Kaohsiung municipal delegation to visit Hong Kong, Macau, Shenzhen, Xiamen and other places for city exchange and cooperation. The trip not only achieved phased, fruitful results in economy and trade, tourism, and culture and education, but also reached a preliminary consensus on building an institutionalized platform for city exchanges and establishing a long-term exchange mechanism, showing broad prospects for future exchange and cooperation with Kaohsiung.\nMayor Han Kuo-yu and his delegation learned about the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, visited the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge, the Shenzhen Qianhai development zone, the Xiamen Haicang automated container terminal, high-tech enterprises, and youth entrepreneurship bases, and engaged in extensive exchanges on urban construction and people's livelihood development. In particular, the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area is a new attempt to promote a new pattern of all-round opening-up in the new era, containing enormous development opportunities and unlimited business potential. Participating in this major strategy will provide very broad space for deepening future exchange and cooperation.\nIn economic and trade procurement, the mayor's delegation signed a large number of agricultural and fishery product procurement agreements on a market-oriented basis. The amount signed during their stays in Shenzhen and Xiamen reached 400 million yuan, more than 500 million yuan in Hong Kong, and 160 million yuan in Macau. Shenzhen coordinated to give priority to Kaohsiung in renting stalls at the Haijixing agricultural wholesale market, where stalls are in very high demand, to sell Kaohsiung agricultural products. Xiamen invited Kaohsiung to send delegations to participate in trade and cultural exhibitions held annually, such as the “Straits Forum,” the “Investment and Trade Fair,” the “Travel Expo,” the “Industrial Expo,” and the “Cultural Expo.”\nIn culture and education exchanges, Shenzhen will provide 200 youth internship and employment positions to Kaohsiung every year, and Shenzhen Polytechnic will provide 20 student enrollment quotas to Kaohsiung every year. In November this year, Xiamen will hold the 12th Cross-Strait Fude Culture Festival in Kaohsiung, and hold an activity in which a Minnan-language choir visits Kaohsiung. The two places will continue folk, customary, clan, community and youth exchanges, enriching residents' cultural life and increasing mutual understanding and affection.\nIn tourism cooperation, Xiamen will promptly push to resume the “Zhongyuan Star” ro-ro ferry service on the Xiamen-Kaohsiung route, and will promptly push to open cruise flights between Xiamen and Kaohsiung. Shenzhen and Xiamen will operate on a market-oriented mechanism, encouraging travel agencies to organize tourists to visit Kaohsiung. Xiamen will soon organize 8,000 tourists to travel to Kaohsiung in batches. In addition, Xiamen Airlines will again recruit 200 cabin crew members in Taiwan this year, of which 100 will be recruited specifically from Kaohsiung.\nIn establishing mechanisms, an institutionalized city exchange platform between Shenzhen and Kaohsiung will be built to comprehensively strengthen exchanges and cooperation in economy, culture, education, sports, science and technology, and other fields between the two places, and both sides agreed to hold forums jointly at appropriate times. An institutionalized city exchange platform between Xiamen and Kaohsiung's port will be built, focusing on hot topics such as port city cooperation, in-depth industrial exchange, convention and tourism cooperation, and urban management innovation, and negotiating to hold city forums to promote exchange and cooperation between the two cities and benefit the residents of both places.\nThese outcomes are a concrete embodiment of “cross-Strait families are one family,” of close affection and mutual support, and a vivid portrayal of cross-Strait integrated development, working together and developing together. They fully demonstrate that, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait city exchange and cooperation has broad prospects. The continuing progress of the mainland's economy and society releases enormous development opportunities and dividends, which we are willing to share with more Taiwan compatriots. We welcome and support more cross-Strait cities in strengthening exchange and cooperation on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” learning from one another and developing hand in hand, so that Taiwan compatriots can gain more and the well-being of compatriots on both sides continues to increase. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together, adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence” and secession, overcome man-made interference and obstacles, actively promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly create a bright future for integrated development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151782.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","人民日报记者","We noted that the Supreme People's Court has just issued the “Several Measures on Providing Judicial Services for Deepening Cross-Strait Integrated Development.” Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","Yesterday, that is March 26, the Supreme People’s Court issued the “Several Measures on Providing Judicial Services for Deepening Cross-Strait Integrated Development.” This is a major measure to implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan.” It is a specialized, comprehensive, and inclusive set of Taiwan-related policy measures in the judicial field, and it is also the first systematic and normative set of measures issued by the Supreme People’s Court to comprehensively and equally protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in accordance with the law.\nThe “Several Measures,” grounded in deepening cross-strait integrated development and providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, put forward 36 measures in four major areas. First, adhere to fair and efficient judicial work and protect the substantive and procedural rights of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in accordance with the law. Second, improve convenience and benefit measures throughout the entire process of cases involving Taiwan, providing high-quality and convenient judicial services to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Third, gradually expand the participation of Taiwan compatriots in judicial work, creating better conditions for the broad body of Taiwan compatriots to take part in national rule-of-law construction. Fourth, strengthen the organizational structure for trial and enforcement work related to Taiwan, and continuously raise management and support standards. For specific details, the Supreme People’s Court held a special press conference yesterday to provide a detailed introduction, and everyone may also consult the Supreme People’s Court website.\nThe “Several Measures” actively respond to the needs and concerns of Taiwan compatriots and demonstrate the determination and sincerity of the judicial organs to do practical, good, and helpful work for Taiwan compatriots and to resolve their difficulties. As comprehensive rule of law advances in the new era, and with the joint efforts of all localities and departments, the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will be better protected, and their sense of gain from the justice system will continue to grow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151781.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping emphasized during this year's “Two Sessions” that we must strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, implement the people-centered development philosophy in Taiwan work, and continue to study and introduce measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots. How will this be implemented? Please also introduce recent new progress by localities and departments in implementing the “31…","During this year's “Two Sessions,” General Secretary Xi Jinping, on March 10 when he took part in the deliberations of the Fujian delegation, issued important instructions on doing well the work toward Taiwan in the new era, which carry important guiding significance. General Secretary Xi stressed that we must explore new paths for the integrated development of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. Work toward Taiwan must both focus on the overall situation and trends and pay attention to implementation in concrete and meticulous detail. Cross-Strait exchanges should be connected wherever possible, enhancing the connectivity of trade and economic cooperation, of infrastructure, of resources and energy, and of industry standards, and Fujian should be built into the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises landing on the mainland. We must strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, expand cultural exchanges, reach into the hearts of Taiwan compatriots, and enhance and deepen Taiwan compatriots' understanding of and emotional attachment to the nation and the country. In work toward Taiwan, we must implement the development philosophy centered on the people, treat Taiwan compatriots equally, and serve Taiwan compatriots for their benefit just as we serve the people of the mainland. We have introduced the “31 measures benefiting Taiwan,” which have achieved notable results, and Taiwan compatriots are all beneficiaries. We must implement these measures in place, listen to the voices of Taiwan compatriots, study what further policies and measures benefiting Taiwan and its people can be introduced, and make every effort to do whatever can be done. Premier Li Keqiang, when answering reporters' questions during the “Two Sessions,” also pointed out that the “31 measures” must be solidly implemented in place, and that new initiatives should also be added during this process.\nWe will fully implement the important remarks of General Secretary Xi Jinping, adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, explore new paths for the integrated development of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, promote common development across the Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nIn implementing the “31 measures” in concrete and meticulous detail, all regions and departments have continued to push forward actively. Here are a few more examples.\nIn financial services, the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone in Fujian Province has taken the lead in offering credit inquiry services for Taiwan. As of the end of 2018, it had processed 194 inquiries for Taiwan compatriots' credit reports and issued loans totaling RMB 45.66 million. Recently, the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone issued “financial credit certificates” for the first time to 16 Taiwan-funded businesses and Taiwan compatriots. Certificate holders can handle multiple financial businesses, including loans, guarantees, and credit lines, at local financial institutions, and enjoy certain conveniences and preferential treatment.\nIn cultural cooperation and exchanges, the “Maritime Silk Road — Eastern Life Aesthetics Exhibition,” jointly planned by cultural institutions on both sides of the Strait, has been selected by the Chinese Cultural Center in Seoul and will travel to South Korea for performances. Cultural institutions and artists from both sides will join hands to showcase the finest of Chinese arts and crafts and jointly promote excellent Chinese culture.\nIn terms of Taiwan compatriots being eligible for various honors and awards, on the eve of International Women's Day (March 8), more than ten Taiwan compatriots were jointly awarded the honorary title of “March 8th Red Banner Bearer” by Fujian, Shanghai, Guangxi, Anhui, Guangzhou, Nanjing, and other places. On March 12, it was officially announced that Taiwanese employees working on the mainland will be included in the scope of local labor model and other honorary title selections. This helps Taiwan compatriots share in the development opportunities on the mainland and enjoy equal treatment on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151783.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Recently, a website registered in Taiwan that introduced content related to the “31 measures” benefiting Taiwan was blocked by the Taiwan authorities, and its registration was canceled. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The original intention of our introduction of the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” was to respond to the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots, to solve some practical problems they encounter in studying, working, living and starting businesses on the mainland, to share the development opportunities of the mainland with Taiwan compatriots, and to provide them with equal treatment, offering more opportunities and convenience for the development of Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, on the mainland. Since the implementation of the “31 Measures,” many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises have obtained tangible benefits from them, and therefore they have also received wide attention and welcome. Many Taiwan compatriots have expressed the hope of learning more about the specific contents of the “31 Measures” and the actual implementation of the “31 Measures” in various localities. We also hope to expand the number of beneficiaries of the “31 Measures,” so that Taiwan compatriots can know more and make better choices, and obtain greater development.\nThe “Attention to the 31 Measures” website provides information services for the development of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. I believe Taiwan compatriots who have browsed this website are very clear about it: it is an information aggregation website on the specific contents of the “31 Measures” and the actual implementation of the “31 Measures” by various localities and departments, actually intended to facilitate Taiwan compatriots with a \"one-stop\" understanding and provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities closed this website on a trumped-up charge. Does the Democratic Progressive Party regard letting Taiwan compatriots know and understand more useful and beneficial information as a \"sin\"? The real reason for these actions by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities is that they are afraid: afraid that the improvement of cross-Strait relations will progress well, afraid that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will grow closer, afraid that Taiwan residents will see through their true colors, and see through their true intention of deliberately creating hostility, antagonism and hatred for the sake of party self-interest. That is why they want to use this method of \"covering the eyes\" and \"stopping the ears\" to cut off the channels through which Taiwan residents obtain information for development, block their access to understanding the real mainland and cross-Strait relations, and obstruct their opportunities for better and greater development. The actions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have increasingly placed them on the opposite side of the interests of Taiwan residents, and they are moving further and further away.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151778.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Taiwan compatriots who travel or reside overseas are very concerned about whether relevant mainland institutions can provide consular protection and services. Could the spokesperson please explain?","Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. We have consistently attached great importance to safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas, and we have helped them resolve difficulties in times of crisis. For many years, we have actively carried out consular protection and assistance for Taiwan compatriots overseas. This includes providing emergency protection and assistance to Taiwan compatriots during major emergencies or when the situation in certain countries becomes unstable; assisting in handling cases of Taiwanese fishing boats in cross-sea fishing disputes, as well as civil disputes and economic and criminal cases involving Taiwan in other countries; providing assistance to Taiwan compatriots affected by natural disasters or other accidents abroad; and providing services such as handling travel documents, certification of documents and credit, and searching for relatives and friends for Taiwan compatriots living overseas.\nDuring the Two Sessions this year, State Councilor Wang Yi said at a press conference that we are actively building a Chinese overseas security system, so that everyone can travel abroad with greater peace of mind. In 2019, we will continue to roll out new consular measures to protect, serve, and benefit the people. Taiwan compatriots overseas are, of course, objects of consular protection and assistance from us. No matter where they are in the world, if Taiwan compatriots encounter an emergency, they can seek consular protection and assistance through the following four channels.\nFirst, they can call the 12308 hotline immediately. To dial the “12308” hotline from overseas, use +86-10-12308. You may also call the backup number +86-10-59913991. If the emergency involves a threat to personal safety, after the call connects, you can dial 0 and then 9 to go directly to a human operator.\nSecond, they can directly call the consular protection and document consultation telephone numbers published by overseas embassies and consulates.\nThird, they can download and use the “MFA 12308” mobile app.\nFourth, they can obtain consular protection and assistance information from the MFA and overseas embassies and consulates in real time through the WeChat official account “Consular Express.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151777.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","Mayor Han Kuo-yu’s visit to the mainland was received at a very high level. Will other county and city heads who come to the mainland in the future receive the same treatment?","As I just said, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” we hold a positive and open attitude toward promoting exchanges between cities across the Strait. We hope to continuously strengthen exchanges and cooperation between cities across the Strait, and we welcome more Taiwan counties and cities to take part, so as to jointly advance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","香港凤凰卫视记者","I have two questions. First, during his visit to Hong Kong and Macao, 韩国瑜 entered the Liaison Office of the Central People's Government in the Hong Kong SAR, making him the first local leader from Taiwan to enter the Liaison Office. 蔡英文 said this is creating an atmosphere of “one country, two systems.” How does the spokesperson respond? Second, during his visit to the United States, Taipei Mayor 柯文哲 put forward…","Regarding your first question: During Mayor Han’s visit, the directors of the Liaison Offices of the Central People’s Government in Hong Kong and Macau each met with him. This is both normal courtesy toward guests and reflects the mainland’s importance attached to Mayor Han’s visit. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities and some “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” forces distorted and slandered this, fully exposing their intention to obstruct cross-Strait and Hong Kong and Macau exchanges and cooperation and to harm the interests and well-being of compatriots.\nSince the return of Hong Kong and Macau to the motherland, the practice of “one country, two systems” has achieved success recognized around the world, and no one and no force can distort or erase this.\nRegarding your second question, our principled position is very clear: there is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. The one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","The State Council recently published the “Decision on Canceling and Delegating a Batch of Administrative Licensing Matters,” which includes two administrative licensing matters directly related to Taiwan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The State Council recently issued the Decision on Canceling and Delegating a Batch of Administrative Licensing Items. It includes two administrative licensing items that directly concern Taiwan: first, the approval for issuing ship-boarding work permits for Taiwan labor personnel is canceled; second, for exhibition projects held within the mainland that are co-organized by institutions from Hong Kong, Macao, or Taiwan, approval is canceled and replaced with filing-based management.\nCanceling the approval of these two Taiwan-related administrative licenses is an important measure to thoroughly implement the spirit of the important speech General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered at the commemoration of the 40th anniversary of the “Message to Compatriots in Taiwan,” and to deepen the reform of “streamlining administration, delegating power, and improving services.” It helps simplify the application process for Taiwan labor personnel to work aboard ships, further promoting labor cooperation among cross-Strait fishing vessel crews; it also facilitates institutions from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan holding exhibitions in mainland China, further enhancing the convenience of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges.\nGoing forward, we will continue to uphold the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” do practical things, good things, and things that solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, and ensure that all measures benefiting Taiwan are implemented in practice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151795.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Regarding Fujian’s hiring of Taiwanese village chiefs as executive directors of village committees or residents’ committees, and its hiring of Taiwanese youth as rural science and technology special commissioners, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said this is suspected of violating relevant regulations and is under investigation. Public opinion holds that the DPP authorities have recently increasingly…","The DPP authorities' open suppression of and intimidation toward Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland is becoming increasingly common. At the last press conference, I explained the suppression by the DPP authorities of a Taiwan compatriot who was hired as an assistant community director in Haicang District, Xiamen, and now there are further examples.\nIt is understood that in order to support Taiwan technology personnel in innovation and entrepreneurship, Zhangpu County in Zhangzhou, Fujian, specially hired a group of Taiwan compatriots who invested and started businesses locally, enabling them to provide rural technology services while engaged in their own businesses, which provides them with greater development opportunities. In addition, Pingtan in Fujian has also hired a group of Taiwan compatriots to serve as executive directors of local village and neighborhood committees, engaging in community management, industrial development, humanistic education, medical care, volunteer services, and other work. These are all good deeds that provide opportunities and convenience for Taiwan compatriots to develop on the mainland, yet the DPP authorities threaten and intimidate them with so-called \"illegality\" accusations, which is not popular with the people.\nI want to stress that cross-Strait exchanges have been open for more than 30 years, and personnel exchanges and economic, cultural, and social ties across the Strait have reached an unprecedented level. This has laid a deep foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and has also increased the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We follow the shared wish of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchange and cooperation, and the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots to obtain better development opportunities. We continuously introduce policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and providing equal treatment, which have been welcomed and affirmed by broad Taiwan compatriots. Yet the DPP authorities stand against the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and out of partisan self-interest, place obstacles everywhere. By doing so, they are undermining Taiwan compatriots' right to a better life and obstructing Taiwan residents' opportunities to achieve greater and better development for themselves.\nTaiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood kin. Regardless of the interference and obstruction encountered, exchange and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait must not stop, must not be cut off, and must not be reduced. We will continue to strengthen and promote exchange and cooperation among civil society on both sides of the Strait, and on the basis of further implementing the \"31 Measures,\" we will continue to introduce more policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, striving to bring compatriots on both sides closer together and make cross-Strait relations develop more solidly and better, continuously enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201903/t20190327_12151779.htm"],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Qingming Festival is approaching, and Huangling County in Shaanxi Province will hold the Xuanyuan Huangdi Ceremony of the Jihai Year. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The “Ji-hai Year Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi” will be held on April 5 at the Qiaoshan Sacrifice Square in Huangling County, Shaanxi Province. Liu Chao-hsuan, Chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Culture Sustainable Development Foundation, New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming, and more than 300 Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life will attend the public memorial ceremony.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Reports say that recently, the chairman of Spring Airlines visited Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu and expressed hope to increase Spring Airlines flights to and from Kaohsiung. What attitude does the Taiwan Affairs Office take toward this?","We have also noted the relevant reports. We attach great importance to the proposals and demands put forward by cross-strait aviation operators that are conducive to increasing personnel exchanges across the Strait, and we will, in light of actual needs, actively study them together with the relevant departments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Taiwan media reported that Soong Chu-yu, Chairman of the People First Party, will visit the mainland next month. Please confirm this and introduce related information.","The KMT adheres to one China and opposes “Taiwan independence,” and we maintain contact and communication with the KMT.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","台声杂志记者","The National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (the “Two Sessions”) deliberated and passed the *Foreign Investment Law*, and Premier Li Keqiang stated that investment from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan may refer to or be treated in accordance with the *Foreign Investment Law*. May I ask the spokesperson whether the relevant laws on investment from Hong Kong, Macao, and…","Protecting the investment rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law has always been our consistent policy. We have consistently taken effective measures to create a favorable development environment for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots investing and starting businesses on the mainland. For Taiwan compatriots investing on the mainland, the Taiwan Compatriot Investment Protection Law and its implementing rules apply first; where that law and its implementing rules do not provide, other laws and regulations such as the Foreign Investment Law may be applied by reference. In addition, some long-standing and effective institutional arrangements and certain practical measures may continue to be used. We will also introduce more policies benefiting Taiwan, create a better rule-of-law environment, and enable Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses to receive equal treatment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots and the National Working Committee for Young Pioneers co-sponsored a cross-Strait youth exchange event at a primary school in Taipei. Some Taiwan media claimed that this was a Communist Youth League “united front” infiltrating a Taiwan primary school. The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that it does not want cross-Strait exchanges to become a mainland…","Young people are the future of cross-Strait relations. We attach great importance to cross-Strait youth exchanges and have taken active measures to continuously advance mutual understanding and friendship between young people on both sides. The DPP authorities view such exchanges, which benefit cross-Strait cooperation, through tinted glasses, criticizing and obstructing them and creating confrontation. This is not popular with the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Lin Youshi, a Taiwan-origin member of the CPPCC, delivered a speech at this year’s CPPCC plenary session during the “Two Sessions” titled “Adhere to the One-China Principle, Enrich the Practice of Peaceful Reunification, and Warmly Look Forward to the Arrival of Cross-Strait Reunification,” which drew attention on both sides of the Strait. Yet the Taiwan authorities want to punish him and have threatened to…","Ms. Ling Yoshi herself has already strongly refuted the DPP authorities' repression. The DPP authorities' conduct once again exposes their essence of undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resisting the trend of national reunification, and seeking “Taiwan independence” and division.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","Han Kuo-yu's visit to the mainland drew criticism and questioning from Taiwan's authorities. Now many Blue-camp county and city magistrates on the island worry that Taiwan's authorities may no longer approve their exchanges with the mainland. What views does the spokesperson have?","As I said earlier, while upholding the “1992 Consensus,” we hold a positive and open attitude toward promoting exchanges between cities across the Taiwan Strait. We hope more Taiwan counties and cities will join in, so as to jointly promote the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities' obstruction and restriction of matters that are conducive to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides will not win public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-03-27","An Fengshan","环球网记者","I have two questions. First, recently Taiwanese entertainer Ouyang Nana was questioned for supporting “Taiwan independence.” She subsequently stated that she is Chinese and firmly supports the one-China principle, yet this drew verbal attacks from some pan-green netizens and media on the island. What is the spokesperson’s evaluation of this? Second, Tsai Ing-wen, who is currently visiting so-called “allied”…","As for your first question, we have also seen that a few days ago Ouyang Nana gave an exclusive interview to CCTV, and her entertainment activities on the mainland are proceeding normally. Recently, quite a few mainland media outlets have published rational and objective analyses and commentaries on this matter, which you may refer to. Some political figures on the island have taken the opportunity to stir up trouble and create confrontation, which only shows that their mentality is very unhealthy.\nAs for your second question, we have seen that Mayor Han Kuo-yu's exchange visit this time was groundlessly criticized by the DPP authorities and some “Taiwan independence” forces. At the same time, we have also seen that more Taiwan public opinion has criticized and denounced these accusations. The more the DPP authorities obstruct and interfere with cross-Strait urban exchanges and cooperation, the more they expose their true face of harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots out of partisan and private interests.\nOn one side, people are working hard to get things done and grow the economy; on the other, people do nothing good and only drag their feet, or even turn back the clock. One side works hard to benefit the people, while the other stands opposite the people's interests and keeps destroying their chances to gain benefits. Without comparison, there is no harm. The DPP authorities' actions amount to volunteering themselves for a clear comparison, revealing the characters “小” (petty) and “私” (selfish) in their hearts. I believe such conduct will only make more and more Taiwan people open their eyes and clearly recognize their true face.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201903/t20190327_12151792.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-03-28","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan's President Tsai Ing-wen said yesterday that Taiwan was seeking new purchases of tanks and US fighter jets, and Washington was \"responding positively\". Do you have any comment on those developments?","First I need to correct you on the title of Tsai Ing-wen. She is the leader of the Taiwan Region. The so-called title of \"president\" is never recognized by China. I am sure you know that very well.\nThere have been many similar questions. Here I will reiterate our consistent, unequivocal and firm opposition to US arms sales to Taiwan. China has lodged stern representations to the US on this issue. We urge the US to fully realize the high degree of sensitivity and severe impact of this issue, honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, in particular the August 17 communique, stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan, and prudently and properly handle issues relating to the region for the sake of China-US cooperation in key areas and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1649338.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1649303.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We noticed that there were frequent contacts between the United States and Taiwan in the military field. Some media reports say that a high-level military delegation from Taiwan is visiting the United States and the US might sell F-16V fighters to Taiwan. Meanwhile, two US ships sailed through the Taiwan Strait recently, and the US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said that the United Stated will take more moves to…","There is only one China in the world. Both the mainland and Taiwan belong to China and the People’s Republic of China is the only legitimate government of China. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity allows no division. And my answer to your question is based on this fact.\nWe noticed that the United States took a number of moves related to Taiwan. We are opposed to US’ arms sales to Taiwan and US military contacts with Taiwan. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and it concerns China’s core interests and the national bond of the Chinese people and allows no interference from the outside. The One-China Principle is a universal consensus of the international community and it is also the political foundation of the China-US relationship. Words or deeds that break the One-China Policy will undermine the China-US relationship. These are dangerous moves that serve neither the interests of China nor those of the United States.\nWe also noticed the separatist remarks of some people in Taiwan. Here I want to stress that reunification is a trend of history and Taiwan’s secessionist movement is a counter current and a dead end. The One-China Principle is the political base of the cross-strait relations. Taiwan’s future lies in reunification and the well-being of the compatriots in Taiwan hinges on national rejuvenation. Those people and forces that instigate confrontations across the strait and blindly court foreign support have very little understanding of the greater good and will receive no support from the people.\nThe motherland must be and will be reunified. We will strive for peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and greatest efforts. However, against the interference of the external forces and the \"Taiwan Independence\" separatists, we will take all necessary measure to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and protect peace and stability across the strait.\nThe motherland must be and will be reunified. We will take all necessary measure to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and protect peace and stability across the strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-03/28/content_4838457.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have a question from one of our followers whose cyber name is Nanhai. Western countries such as the US always talk about China’s defense expenditure and hype up “China Threat”. As for this kind of cliché issues, how can China respond to them in a more convincing way?","Thank you and your follower for the question. I want to clarify one thing first. It is a country’s domestic and foreign policy rather than its defense expenditure that decides whether it is a threat to others or not. China follows a defense policy that is defensive in nature and stays committed to the path of peaceful development. The growth in China’s military strength is also growth in global force for peace.\nNow let us analyze the issue in details. The total amount of China’s defense expenditure is big, but we have some specific conditions. First, China has a very complicated geopolitical environment. It is yet to realize national reunification and has arduous tasks in safeguarding national sovereignty and security. Second, China is and will take more international responsibilities and obligations and providing more public security products to the world. All these responsibilities also cost a lot of our budget. Third, the new revolution in military affairs in the world is accelerating. Like other countries, China also wants to follow the trend and make some accomplishments. Fourth, China is a populous country. If we look at the defense expenditure per capita and the proportion of China’s defense expenditure in its GDP, we can see both numbers are at low levels in the world.\nTo conclude, I want to say China’s defense policy is clear and its defense expenditure is moderate and reasonable. In the mosaic of fluctuating international situations, Chinese military will always be a staunch force in protecting national sovereignty and security and maintaining world peace and stability.\nPlease pass my question to “Nanhai”, asking him whether my response is convincing or not.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-03/28/content_4838457.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-04-01","Geng Shuang","","According to Reuters, on Sunday Taiwan scrambled aircraft to \"drive away\" two Chinese fighter jets that flew past the \"middle line\" in the Taiwan Strait. Can you confirm this information?","I'm not aware of what you mentioned. I would like to refer you to the relevant authority.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1650338.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1650254.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-04-02","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan earlier said that its planes warned off the mainland's military aircraft that crossed the \"middle line\" in the Taiwan Strait last weekend, and that the move from Beijing was a provocation. US National Security Adviser John Bolton wrote on his Twitter yesterday that \"the Chinese military provocations won't win any hearts or minds in Taiwan, and the Taiwan Relations Act and our commitment are clear.\" I'm…","I'd refer you to the competent authorities if you'd like to know more about the PLA fighter jets flying past the \"middle line\" of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Taiwan leader made comments and tweeted about this. Her ridiculous words are pure nonsense and indeed infuriating. But since this is not a diplomatic matter, I believe the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council is better suited to answering your question.\nHowever, in response to the US comments, I must say a few words. China's position on the Taiwan question has been consistent and clear-cut. The so-called Taiwan Relations Act unilaterally rolled out by the US runs counter to the basic norms governing international relations and the three China-US joint communiques. China has been firmly against it from the start. We urge the relevant individuals in the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiques, and make efforts to advance our bilateral relations and cross-strait peace and stability instead of doing the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1650723.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1650630.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-04-04","Geng Shuang","","According to media reports, the spokesperson of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) in Taipei said on April 3 that the US government has stationed officials including active military personnel at the AIT since 2005. On the same day, a spokesperson of the US State Department said the US follows the one-China policy and that the security of the AIT is maintained by a small US unit and a larger group of local…","We have noted relevant reports. The US has made unequivocal commitments on keeping non-official relations with Taiwan. China firmly opposes any forms of official and military ties between the US and Taiwan. We have made clear our stern position to the US many times.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The US sending military personnel to Taiwan under whatever pretext constitutes a violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, which will inevitably have a negative impact on the bilateral relations. We urge the US to honor its commitments, strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, correct its wrongdoing and exercise caution and prudence when handling Taiwan-related issues to avoid serious damage to China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1651487.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1651415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-04-10","Lu Kang","","The Dalai Lama has been admitted to hospital with a lung infection. What's the Foreign Ministry's comment on this? Does China have a plan to appoint a successor to the Dalai Lama in China? My second question, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State David Meale is scheduled to speak in Taiwan tonight at the American Institute in Taiwan. Are you aware of this and what is China's view on the US government…","Let me take your second question first. China opposes any official contacts between the US and Taiwan. We believe that this severely violates the One-China commitment the US has made and its obligations under the three China-US Joint Communiques. We demand that the US not take such wrong move.\nRegarding the first question, first, we are not aware of what you said about the physical condition of the 14th Dalai Lama. Second, in China's history, clear rules have been established concerning the reincarnation of the living Buddha. Reincarnation of living Buddhas, as a unique institution of inheritance in Tibetan Buddhism, comes with a set range of rituals and conventions. The Chinese government implements the policy of freedom of religious belief. The reincarnation system is respected and protected by such legal instruments as Regulations on Religious Affairs and Measures on the Management of the Reincarnation of Living Buddhas.\nThe institution of reincarnation of the Dalai Lama has been in existence for several hundred years. The 14th Dalai Lama himself was found and recognized following religious rituals and historical conventions and his succession was approved by the then central government. Therefore reincarnation of living Buddhas including the Dalai Lama must comply with Chinese laws and regulations and follow religious rituals and historical conventions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1653187.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1653078.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 10, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO press conference. Now, I am happy to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen once again put forward the so-called “defending sovereignty” rhetoric, and claimed that “the whole world will support Taiwan in resisting pressure from the mainland.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","There is only one China. Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations, a common consensus of the international community, and indeed the will of the people and the trend of history.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. Guided by the concept of “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family” and the spirit of close kinship and mutual goodwill (亲望亲好), we continue to do real things, good things, and things that solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, unite compatriots on both sides to oppose “Taiwan independence,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots. The purpose is to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides. By contrast, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces defy the common wishes and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, constantly create estrangement and confrontation, and obstruct Taiwan compatriots from seeking greater and better development opportunities. This is what undermines cross-Strait relations and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait.\nFor some time now, they have repeatedly made statements full of “two-state theory,” escalating provocations and creating incidents. Externally, they lean on foreign powers to bolster their standing; internally, they intimidate the Taiwanese people. This has met with unanimous opposition from compatriots on both sides. If they feel pressure, that pressure comes from compatriots on both sides opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguarding common interests. When faced with pressure caused by their own reckless actions, they are destined to be a lonely minority.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155384.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to reports, on March 31 two PLA aircraft flew over the so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” Taiwan's authorities reacted strongly, saying the “act undermines the status quo across the Strait.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","It is understood that this is a normal arrangement within the PLA's annual training plan.\\nThere is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will not be allowed to be divided. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the sacred duty of the Chinese People's Liberation Army and the fundamental interest of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common responsibility of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155380.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","Reportedly, the Taiwan authorities plan to revise the “Hong Kong and Macau Relations Act” to restrict county and city heads and political appointees from exchanges in Hong Kong and Macau. Pan-Green politicians have recently attacked county and city heads who visited the mainland, and one even said, “If people only strive for food and warmth, how are they any different from ‘pigs, dogs, poultry and beasts’?” What…","Over the years, urban exchanges across the Strait have grown increasingly close, bringing tangible benefits and more and better development opportunities to Taiwan compatriots.\nTaiwan compatriots have the right to pursue a better life. Taiwan compatriots hope to strengthen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, develop the economy, improve livelihoods, and look forward to a better life and greater development. This is where their interests lie. When Taiwan county and city magistrates come to the Mainland, they are responding to the needs of the people and seeking outlets for the labor achievements of Taiwan compatriots.\nWe adhere to the concept of \"cross-Strait families are one family,\" actively promote urban exchanges across the Strait, and strive to expand the benefits and sense of gain for Taiwan compatriots. In cross-Strait urban exchanges, the labor, wisdom and sweat of the Taiwan people are transformed, through the bonds of affection between compatriots on both sides, into solid gains and a better life.\nIn sharp contrast, the DPP authorities, out of narrow party interests, have used various means to interfere with and restrict cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, engaged in extensive political manipulation, and harmed the interests of Taiwan compatriots. They not only obstruct Taiwan people's pursuit of a better life, but also make abusive remarks, even comparing them to \"beasts.\" This fully shows that they have no concern for the hardships of the people and no regard for the well-being of ordinary people in their hearts. It exposes their consistent stance of trampling on the interests of the people, and in the end they will only be abandoned by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155385.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","After the Taiwan interior authorities imposed fines on two Taiwan residents who served as assistant community directors in Xiamen, they recently also required another batch of community assistants who signed labor contracts with mainland enterprises to explain their situation. This has caused more concern among Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","Who cannot find an excuse for a charge they wish to bring? We have already stated our position on this issue several times at press conferences. I would like to reiterate that using so-called “illegal” accusations, threats and intimidation against Taiwan youth, and depriving them of the right to find satisfactory jobs, seek better development and realize their own value, is cutting off the employment and development opportunities of Taiwan's young people. Those who are hostile to young people will never come to a good end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155381.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Taiwan MAC recently said that Taiwanese youth have a low success rate in starting businesses on the mainland, and that going to the mainland to start a business requires awareness of risk. What comment does the spokesperson have?","All along, in line with the shared desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, and with the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots for more development opportunities, we have continuously introduced policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, providing them with more and better development opportunities.\nYouth is the hope and future of the nation. We attach great importance to the demands of Taiwan's young people and have continuously provided better conditions and greater scope for Taiwan youth to study, work, and start businesses on the Chinese mainland. Since 2015, we have granted plaques to establish 76 cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites in 20 provinces and municipalities, which have housed or served about 2,000 Taiwan enterprises and teams in total. More than 10,000 Taiwan youths have cumulatively interned, found employment, or started businesses at these bases and sites, and more than 70,000 person-times of Taiwan youths have participated in various exchange activities held by the bases and sites. In 2018, the number of Taiwan students applying to mainland universities, the number of Taiwan youths coming to the mainland for employment and internships, and the number of newly added Taiwan enterprises served by mainland employment and entrepreneurship institutions all maintained double-digit growth. More and more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, especially Taiwan students and youths, choose to develop on the mainland to realize their life aspirations. In fact, many Taiwan youths' entrepreneurial projects on the mainland have been developing very well, such as Jiangsu Huixing Intelligent Technology, Shanghai Zhixiang Wang (Carton King), Suzhou Beimian (Cup Noodle), Beijing Taotao Xi, and Kunshan Majie Electronics Co., Ltd., which won the Youth Entrepreneurship Enterprise Award of the Jiangsu Zifeng Award. These are all crystallizations of Taiwan youths' entrepreneurial dreams.\nWhat I want to ask the DPP authorities here is: why, after you took office, have Taiwan youths increasingly fallen into distress and bewilderment and come to feel that there is no hope? If the DPP authorities continue to trample on the people's well-being, then neither suppressing and obstructing Taiwan compatriots nor slandering and smearing the mainland will stop the growing number of Taiwan youths who come to the mainland to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155382.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视记者","Recently, a sub-event of the 3rd Cross-Strait Student Baseball League was held in Beijing. The first two editions were warmly welcomed by students on both sides of the Strait. Could the spokesperson introduce the situation for this edition?","From April 3 to 9, the sub-leg of the Third Cross-Strait Student Baseball League was held in Beijing. This year, the number of participating teams increased from 10 in the first edition to 24. In addition to the university Division A and Division B, women's baseball was included for the first time. After 3 days and 34 games, the champions of the sub-leg for the university teams from the mainland and Taiwan were determined in the Division A, Division B, and women's divisions.\nSince the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League was launched three years ago, it has drawn attention and affection from young people on both sides of the Strait. Through competition and exchange, players from both sides have deepened their understanding and friendship, and have been willing to become good friends and partners who are united, caring, and striving forward together. Recently, Director Liu Jieyi of the Taiwan Affairs Office met with player representatives from both sides, encouraged them, and welcomed Taiwanese youth to regard the mainland as the place where their youthful dreams begin, and invited young people from both sides to pursue, build, and realize their dreams together. We wish this event continued success with each edition, and we also hope that media friends will continue to pay attention to this competition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Taiwan’s Executive Yuan recently passed a draft amendment to the Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area, which stipulates that cross-Strait agreements on political issues must undergo dual legislative review and a referendum. The procedure is complex and the threshold extremely high. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Today, as the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation shows a bright prospect, exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides are becoming ever broader and their contacts ever closer, and the force of joining hands to realize national rejuvenation is growing ever stronger. In the process of national rejuvenation, the broad Taiwan compatriots certainly cannot be absent. We are willing to be the first to share with Taiwan compatriots the opportunities of mainland development, and are willing to introduce more preferential policies so that Taiwan compatriots can enjoy the same treatment as mainland compatriots in investing and starting businesses, working and studying, and living and residing on the mainland, benefiting Taiwan compatriots just as we serve the mainland's people. By contrast, the DPP authorities, for the sake of their party's and their own private interests, defy the shared wish of compatriots on both sides for peace and development, deliberately undermine the process of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and harm the vital interests of the people. But their conduct cannot stop the historical tide of cross-Strait relations moving forward.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190410_12155383.htm"],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The Shanghai Stock Exchange’s STAR Market has recently officially launched. Among the first nine enterprises accepted for listing on the STAR Market, one is a Taiwan-invested enterprise. It is not ruled out that more Taiwanese high-tech companies will list on the STAR Market in the future. May I ask the spokesperson for comment on this?","There is no reason for compatriots on both sides of the Strait not to integrate, develop together, and share in development. Strengthening economic cooperation across the Strait, with mutual benefit, serves the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We have always supported Taiwan-funded enterprises listing on the mainland, and we hope that Taiwan-funded enterprises can better share in mainland development opportunities through listing there. There are no policy obstacles to Taiwan-funded enterprises listing on the STAR Market, and they enjoy the same treatment as mainland enterprises. To date, more than 30 Taiwan-funded enterprises have listed on the mainland A-share market and raised funds. Since 2016, a total of 10 Taiwan-funded enterprises have listed on the mainland A-share market, raising about 35 billion yuan. These listings have both provided the funds needed for the companies’ growth and expansion and given their brand image a clear boost, and more and more Taiwan-funded enterprises are choosing to list on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Shao Ziping, a well-known Taiwanese law professor, had his household registration cancelled by the Taiwan authorities after obtaining a mainland ID card. What is the spokesperson’s view?","We have noted the relevant reports. In recent years, exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait have become increasingly close, yet the DPP authorities not only cling to the old and outdated, but have gone further, constantly setting up obstacles. In matters involving the interests of compatriots on both sides, they keep digging trenches, building walls, and cutting roads, seriously harming the interests of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","In an interview on an online livestream, Lai Ching-te said that “Taiwan independence” as advocated by the DPP is what defends Taiwan’s “sovereignty.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? Second question: a Japanese media outlet has recently been serializing “The Secret Memoirs of Lee Teng-hui,” which mentions that in the 1990s, across the two sides of the Strait, there were mysterious phone calls and…","On the first question: Lai Ching-te’s remarks completely twist right and wrong. We have repeatedly refuted his stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” position and his open “Taiwan independence” statements. If he continues to fan the flames of “Taiwan independence” for his own private gain, it will be extremely dangerous.\nI want to stress again that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory, and it will never be able to split away from the motherland. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the second question: I am not aware of the situation you describe. Regarding contact, communication, and negotiations across the Taiwan Strait, our position has been consistent and clear: they should be conducted on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","On the issue of mainland military aircraft flying over the “median line of the Taiwan Strait,” the spokesperson just said it was a normal arrangement under the annual plan. Will there be more in the future? Tsai Ing-wen said she would “drive them away at the first opportunity”; are you not worried about an accidental exchange of fire? Second question: nine people were convicted in the Hong Kong “Occupy Central”…","On the first question, I have just answered: this is a normal arrangement within the PLA's annual training plan. As for the DPP authorities' leader's wild talk, it only shows that she is fierce in manner but weak inside. We also solemnly warn her: do not play with fire, and don't even think about it.\nOn the second question, Hong Kong is a society governed by the rule of law, where everyone is equal before the law. Those who disrupt public order and harm the public interest should be punished according to law. By contrast, in Taiwan, corrupt officials escape justice, and those who smash and loot claim that “rebellion is justified.” Therefore, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council has no qualifications whatsoever to spout nonsense here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On April 3, the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) confirmed for the first time that since 2005, active-duty military personnel, including U.S. Marines, have been stationed at AIT's current site, and that security at the new building will follow the current site. What response does the spokesperson have?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already conveyed our solemn position to the US side. I must stress once again that we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contact between the United States and Taiwan. The US side should keep its promises, correct its wrong practices, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness in strict accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, so as not to damage China-US relations or the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Simplo Technology chairman Song Fuxiang recently said in an interview, “We have never done business on the mainland, because we could not make money.” Netizens pointed out that the company has factories and subsidiaries in many places on the mainland, and called it “two-faced.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. It is understood that Simplo Technology has made investments in Jiangsu, Shanghai, Chongqing and other places since 2001. We have repeatedly reaffirmed that we welcome Taiwan businesspeople to invest and do business on the mainland, but absolutely do not allow anyone to make money on the mainland while undermining cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","A WHO spokesperson recently stated in a reply letter to Taiwan media that, without an understanding reached across the Strait, the World Health Assembly this year will still not extend an invitation to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations must be arranged appropriately through cross-Strait consultation under the one-China principle. The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. Therefore, the premise and basis for Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly no longer exist, and the relevant arrangements naturally cannot be sustained.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu, while answering questions at the city council, said that Jack Ma, founder of the Alibaba Group, has sent a letter expressing his desire to visit Kaohsiung, Taiwan, and that at that time he would also hold a face-to-face discussion with young friends in Kaohsiung. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","As I have just said, youth are the hope and future of a nation. We have always endeavored to provide cross-Strait youth exchanges and the development and growth of Taiwan's young people with better opportunities, broader platforms, and greater space. On the journey of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, Taiwan's young people should not be absent. We hope that young friends across the Taiwan Strait can obtain better development opportunities, strengthen their exchanges, realize their dreams, and create brilliance together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","On the 8th, an expert meeting on African swine fever was held in Beijing, but no representatives from Taiwan were invited. The head of Taiwan’s “Council of Agriculture” said this was due to interference from mainland China. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s response?","It is our understanding that this meeting of the prevention and control working group was hosted by the World Organisation for Animal Health in Beijing.\nFor some time, the DPP authorities have repeatedly used the prevention and control of African swine fever to make political capital, with the aim of further undermining cross-Strait relations. The mainland side has consistently released relevant information in accordance with the principles of \"timeliness, openness and transparency,\" and maintains close cooperation and smooth information channels with the World Organisation for Animal Health. If the Taiwan side wishes to learn about relevant circumstances, it can fully obtain complete information.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","During this year's Qingming period, many places on both sides of the Strait held ceremonies honoring the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan. Many of these ceremonies were jointly attended by people from both sides. Could the spokesperson talk about the significance of people from all walks of life on both sides jointly worshipping the Yellow Emperor?","The Yellow Emperor is the cultural progenitor of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides jointly worshipping our ancestors reflects their shared remembrance of the ancestor of the Chinese nation, and reflects adherence to the Chinese spirit and the roots of the Chinese nation. We hope compatriots on both sides will jointly promote Chinese culture, gather the Chinese spirit, strengthen spiritual affinity, and work together to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Some “Taiwan independence” figures on the island claim that mainland cyber troops want to acquire some Taiwan social media fan pages for propaganda. Is the spokesperson aware of this information, and how do you respond?","The relevant information recently circulating on the island is clearly fake news staged by its own creators. Those who fabricate such fake news do so entirely to find excuses for escalating cross-Strait confrontation, and it cannot fool the broad masses of Taiwan’s residents. Such crude acts of fabricating, selling, and peddling fakes clearly underestimate the judgment of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-10","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Taiwan media reported that the London School of Economics, Tsai Ing-wen’s alma mater, corrected an error in the map artwork on its campus that had labeled mainland China and Taiwan separately, labeling Taiwan as part of China. Taiwan’s foreign affairs department sent a letter of protest, and Tsai Ing-wen even declared, “We will not disappear from the face of the earth.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","As I said just now, the One-China Principle is a basic norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community, so all Taiwan-related affairs should be handled in accordance with the One-China Principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190410_12155396.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 16 — In response to the DPP authorities’ slander concerning the Eastern Theater Command of the People’s Liberation Army dispatching sea and air forces to patrol around Taiwan island and conduct joint exercises, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 16th in response to questions: The PLA’s recent training and exercises are normal arrangements within the annual plan, aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguarding the common interests of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities deceive and mislead the Taiwan public, taking the opportunity to stir up hostility across the Strait and escalate cross-Strait confrontation. Their schemes to continue undermining cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will not succeed. No person or force should underestimate our firm resolve and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190416_12156946.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-04-17","Lu Kang","","Regarding this Masood Azhar issue, you just said it is moving towards settlement. Can you please elaborate you have a timeline or are you in touch with parties? Is there a kind of formula you are working on for the solution of this?","First, you correctly quoted me as saying that things are moving towards settlement, which is true. Second, on ongoing discussions at the 1267 Committee, just as I said, there are explicit rules of procedure and disciplinary regulations when it comes to the internal consultations at the Security Council and its subsidiary bodies. As a member of the Security Council, China should abide by the rules and regulations faithfully.\nThe following question was raised after the press conference: media reports say the US has recently approved a package of arms sales worth 500 million US dollars for Taiwan, which includes fighter jets pilot training and maintenance services. I wonder if you have any comment?\nThe US arms sales to Taiwan constitutes a serious violation of the three China-US joint communiques, in particular the August 17 communique. It is interference in China's internal affairs and infringement upon China's sovereignty and security interests. China firmly opposes it and has lodged solemn representations to the US side.\nI must emphasize that the Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. We urge the US to honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, cancel this planned arms sales to Taiwan, stop selling arms to and military ties with Taiwan before serious damage is caused in our bilateral cooperation in important areas and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1655318.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-04-24","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On April 15, the US State Department approved an arms sale to Taiwan worth US$500 million and notified Congress. The Chinese military expressed firm opposition to this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. China firmly opposes any country selling weapons to Taiwan and firmly opposes any country conducting military contacts with Taiwan. The US side's conduct seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, interferes in China's internal affairs, undermines China's sovereignty and security interests, poisons the atmosphere for the development of China-US military relations, seriously disrupts cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is completely wrong and also very dangerous.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, involves China's core interests, and is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. Relying on foreign powers to bolster oneself leads nowhere, and using Taiwan to contain China is bound to be futile. China requests that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately cancel the relevant arms sales projects to Taiwan, and halt arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military contacts, so as not to cause further damage to China-US military relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese military has the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2019-04/24/content_4840191.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning! Today's press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","When will this year’s Straits Forum be held? What is the status of preparations?","The 11th Straits Forum will open in Fujian Province on June 15, with concentrated activities lasting one week. Themed “Expanding Civil Exchanges and Deepening Integrated Development,” this forum will continue to focus on and serve grassroots people and young groups, and arranges the main conference activities as well as 33 activities across four sections. Among them, the youth exchange section provides more opportunities and a larger stage for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams. The grassroots exchange section deepens mutual trust and emotional identification between compatriots on both sides. The cultural exchange section promotes the creative transformation and innovative development of Chinese culture. The economic and trade exchange section expands the industries and fields of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and shares development opportunities. Preparations are progressing smoothly.\nThe Straits Forum has gone through ten years; the number of host units has increased from 54 entities from both sides at the outset to 82 this year, and the number of Taiwan compatriots who have participated in forum activities has reached over a hundred thousand person-times. The facts show that continuing to hold the Straits Forum well accords with the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides for more exchanges and more mutual visits.\nIn 2018, the Straits Forum opened online registration for the first time, aiming to give Taiwan compatriots who wish to learn about the mainland and the Straits Forum an opportunity to experience it firsthand. At that time, Taiwan compatriots registered very enthusiastically, and the response after participation was also very positive. Online registration for this year’s forum opened a few days ago on the forum’s official website. To meet the needs of the broad Taiwan compatriot community, the quota has been increased to 500 people, and the registration period runs from April 15 to May 10. We welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to take an active part in this forum, and we also welcome media friends from both sides to report on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159197.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Yilan County Magistrate Lin Tzu-miao recently led a delegation to visit Jiangsu and Shanghai. Please introduce recent exchanges of Taiwan counties and cities with the mainland.","From April 18 to 20, Lin Tzu-miao, Magistrate of Yilan County, Rao Ching-ling, Magistrate of Taitung County, and representatives of Hualien County led a delegation to Shanghai for a visit and exchange. They held tourism and agricultural product promotion events and held talks with relevant local parties on cooperation. Earlier, from April 16 to 18, Magistrate Lin Tzu-miao also led a delegation to Jiangsu for a visit and related promotional events. The above three counties and cities reached more than 10 cooperation outcomes with relevant parties in Jiangsu and Shanghai on tourism, agricultural cooperation and procurement of agricultural products, building a bridge for institutionalized exchange and cooperation between the two places. It is also reported that Lin Ming-chen, Magistrate of Nantou County, is currently leading a delegation on a visit and exchange in Nanjing, Jiangsu. Several other Taiwan counties and cities are also discussing visits for exchanges at appropriate times.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, connected by blood and close to each other. Compatriots in Taiwan hope to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, develop the economy, improve livelihoods, and hope for a better life and greater development; this is in their interest. Taiwan county and city heads coming to the mainland accords with the needs of the public. We are willing, on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” to continue carrying out exchanges and cooperation in all fields with Taiwan counties and cities, to enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159195.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen stated in an interview that she does not accept the “1992 Consensus,” insists on so-called “sovereign independence,” and said that her “maintaining the status quo” means maintaining the so-called status quo of “independence and self-determination.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The remarks by this DPP authority leader are self-incriminating. They expose the deliberate intention to overturn the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and to undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This fully shows that the DPP authorities are the creators of cross-Strait conflict, the destroyers of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the perpetrators harming the interests of the Taiwan people.\nThere is only one China; Taiwan and the mainland both belong to one China; China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and are not to be divided. This is the status quo of cross-Strait relations and an objective fact widely recognized by the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159196.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","During his visit to the United States, Han Kuo-yu recently said: “Taiwan’s ‘defense’ relies on the US, its technology relies on Japan, and its market relies on the mainland.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for improving and developing cross-Strait relations, and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest real threat to the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations. Promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is in the fundamental interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and cross-Strait affairs are family matters of compatriots on both sides, which should be discussed and handled by family members. We hope that all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots, will follow the historical trend, shoulder the national responsibility together, firmly hold the destiny of the nation in their own hands, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, People First Party Chairman James Soong led a delegation to visit Hong Kong and Macau, and in both places met with the Liaison Offices of the Central People's Government and with their respective directors. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the mainland arranged this trip in order to carry out “united front” work and eliminate so-called “Taiwan sovereignty.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","People First Party Chairman James Soong led a delegation to visit Hong Kong and Macao. The heads of the Liaison Offices of the Central People's Government in Hong Kong and Macao each met with them. This is normal exchange.\nThe DPP authorities distorted and slandered this, which fully exposes their scheme to obstruct cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao exchanges and cooperation and to harm the interests and well-being of compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159194.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's Apple Daily reported recently that Taiwan-invested enterprise Want Want Group received large government subsidies on the mainland and that some are trying to “hype and smear” the company. Want Want Group has issued a statement refuting this. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The political stance of the media outlet that published this news is well known to everyone. At this time, the motive behind its publication is also clear to everyone. We have also noted that the Want Want Group has already issued a public statement to clarify the matter and refute the false claims. Here, I must point out that over the years, we have encouraged and supported Taiwan-funded enterprises in investing and developing businesses on the mainland, and have taken active measures to provide them with all kinds of convenience, equal treatment, and opportunities to share in mainland development, helping them achieve greater and better development on the mainland. Our policies are inclusive. In accordance with law and regulations, we treat all Taiwan enterprises equally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The U.S. State Department recently approved an arms sale to Taiwan worth 500 million U.S. dollars. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position on this. Let me stress again that the Taiwan question concerns China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to Taiwan and firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159190.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The head of the American Institute in Taiwan recently said in Taiwan that the mainland has intensified the dissemination of so-called \"false information\" to exert influence on Taiwan, including influencing the \"elections,\" and that the United States will continue security consultations with Taiwan to help Taiwan develop effective deterrence. May I ask the spokesperson for your comment on this?","We have stressed many times that we have never interfered in Taiwan's elections. The DPP authorities are accustomed to spreading slanders and fabricating smears against the mainland. Now some people in the United States are parroting the groundless claims of the DPP authorities, which is irresponsible. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190424_12159192.htm"],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The mainland scholar Li Yi, residing in the United States, who had been invited to visit Taiwan, was recently expelled from Taiwan by the Taiwan authorities. Tsai Ing-wen said, \"Persons from the mainland who come to Taiwan and who promote 'one country, two systems' or 'unification by force' should be subject to control measures, and when necessary, be denied entry.\" May I ask the spokesperson for your response?","I am not familiar with the background of Mr. Li Yi's participation in this event. What I want to stress here is that we advocate “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” For some time, the DPP authorities have constantly obstructed and restricted exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides, suppressed voices calling for cross-Strait reunification, and heightened cross-Strait confrontation, exposing their true face of seeking the private interests of one party and pursuing “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","It is reported that another batch of Taiwan village and township chiefs recently signed twinning exchange agreements with the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that the competent authorities would investigate and deal with this. The Taiwan Ministry of the Interior recently released a video threatening that village and township chiefs who go to the mainland to sign agreements may be fined…","Exchanges and contacts at the grassroots level across the Strait, which enhance understanding and mutual learning, are good for compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities disregard the wishes and needs of grassroots people, and repeatedly obstruct and restrict cross-Strait civil exchanges and cooperation—banning this today, penalizing that tomorrow. Their intentions are malicious, they do not win popular support, and of course they will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","On the 21st, the Fuzhou area of the China (Fujian) Pilot Free Trade Zone marked the fourth anniversary of its launch. Over the past four years, trade in goods between Fuzhou's free trade area and Taiwan has grown steadily, service trade with Taiwan has been opened further, and cross-Strait exchange and entrepreneurship bases have developed in clusters. May I ask for the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","The Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone was established for Taiwan and bears the important mission of strengthening economic cooperation across the Taiwan Strait. Since the Fuzhou Area was officially launched on April 21, 2015, it has achieved notable results in promoting trade in goods and services with Taiwan, advanced manufacturing cooperation across the Strait, financial cooperation with Taiwan, cross-Strait personnel exchanges, and the concentrated development of Taiwan youth innovation and entrepreneurship bases. The relevant person in charge recently accepted an interview with Xinhua News Agency and gave a detailed introduction.\nWhat I want to say here is that over the years, the Fujian FTZ has not only been bold in exploring expanded opening-up and deepening reform, but has also made achievements in implementing equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. This is instructive for exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development within the framework of the FTZ strategy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公文汇传媒集团全媒体记者","Before the Legislative Yuan in Taiwan reviewed the draft amendment to the *Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area*, Chen Ming-tong, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council in Taiwan, said in an interview with a green media outlet that “there are many possibilities between the two sides, such as the EU, the Commonwealth, or diplomatic recognition.” However, when…","In principle, we do not comment on remarks made in a personal capacity. But everyone knows that both sides of the Strait belong to one China; this is not a relationship between two countries. I think he should study the relevant regulations on the Taiwan side carefully, and not spread remarks carrying the implication of a “two-state theory.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊","According to Taiwan media reports, the Mainland Affairs Council recently drafted an administrative order to be issued in the second half of the year, requiring Taiwan residents who obtain mainland residence permits to report proactively, otherwise they will be fined. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our issuing residence permits to Taiwan compatriots is to meet their needs and to make it easier for them to live, study, and work on the mainland. This is a good thing that benefits Taiwan and its people, and it has been welcomed by the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities are unwilling to see compatriots on both sides come closer, visit relatives, and get along well. Out of narrow party interest, they restrict one thing today and punish another tomorrow, acting against the interests of Taiwan compatriots everywhere and destroying good things for them. Such practices are unpopular, and their schemes will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that in the 2020 “election,” Kuomintang candidates successively showed up as Han Kuo-yu and Terry Gou, and that she does not believe the mainland did not interfere. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","As I said earlier, we neither interfere in nor comment on Taiwan’s elections. The claim of “mainland interference” is pure nonsense with ulterior motives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Guo Tai-ming (郭台铭), the well-known entrepreneur who has already announced he will run in the 2020 election, recently said, “Democracy cannot fill your stomach. Tsai Ing-wen’s blindly treating the mainland as an enemy is not democracy, but populism.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Peaceful development of cross-strait relations conforms to the common interests of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities, under various pretexts, stir up confrontation and incite hostility across the Strait in order to serve the narrow private interests of one party. Compatriots in Taiwan see this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Taiwan's executive authority recently issued the “Principles for Restricting the Use of Products Harmful to Cybersecurity.” Some analysts argue that this move by the Taiwan authorities targets mainland products by setting a purchase-ban principle. How does the spokesperson view this?","Practice over the years has fully proven that strengthening economic cooperation across the Strait, with mutual benefit, can bring tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. But the DPP authorities, going against the will of the people, have done the opposite, attempting to blockade and restrict the mainland's high-tech industries. This approach, which puts political aims first and violates economic laws, ultimately harms the interests of Taiwan compatriots themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The 2019 Beijing International Horticultural Exhibition will be held on the 29th of this month. Please introduce the participation of the Taiwan region.","The 2019 Beijing International Horticultural Exhibition will be held in Yanqing District, Beijing, on April 29. At the invitation of the Beijing Expo Bureau, the Taiwan Flower Industry Development Association participated as an exhibitor in the design and installation of the Taiwan exhibition garden. The Taiwan exhibition garden covers 2,000 square meters and is divided into six major landscape nodes: Toward the Mountain Path, Orchid Area, Path of Time, Sun Moon Lake, In the Farmland, and Mountain Summit. The exhibition garden is highly distinctive of Taiwan and captivating.\nWe welcome broad compatriots from Taiwan and media friends to visit the Expo, tour it, interview, report, and join in this grand occasion together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The draft amendment to the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” recently passed by Taiwan's Executive Yuan would add a provision that “political agreements negotiated across the Strait must be reviewed twice by the legislature and be subject to a referendum,” and would stipulate that they “may not be used as items of the agreement.” According to Taiwan media, the…","Peaceful development of cross-strait relations is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and lies in the shared interests of compatriots on both sides. Everything that benefits the interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation should be vigorously promoted. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, for the narrow self-interest of their party, defy the shared wish of compatriots on both sides for peace and development and resort to any means to sabotage the process of peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Doing so will only harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and bury Taiwan's future and prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201904/t20190424_12159191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-04-25","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Since Trump took office, the US has made arms sale to Taiwan multiple times. And it seems to be normalized. What is your comment？","We have already stated our position on many occasions on the US’ arms sale to Taiwan. I want to stress that China is firmly opposed to any country’s arms sale to Taiwan or any official contact or military ties with Taiwan in any form. The US’ arms sale to Taiwan severely violates the One-China Principle and regulations of the Three Joint Communiqués between China and the United States. It is utterly wrong and dangerous. I also want to stress that it is doomed to fail to contain China with Taiwan and there is no way out to rely on other countries. Relevant parties should recognize the main trend today as well as the overall interests of the Chinese nation. The future of Taiwan lies in reunification and welfare of the Taiwan compatriots lie in national rejuvenation.","","http://eng.chinamil.com.cn/view/2019-04/25/content_9489162.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-04-25","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan “Central News Agency” reported that PLA military aircraft flew through the Bashi Straits on April 15th to carry out blue water training. Joseph Wu, the head of Taiwan liaison department, said that when Taiwan and the American Association in Taiwan (AIT) celebrated the 40th anniversary of the “Taiwan Relations Act”, the PLA conducted targeted military training. He added, \"we will not bow to bullying.\" May I…","The PLA’s training and exercises are aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintaining peace and stability across the Straits, and protecting common interests of the compatriots across the straits. The DPP authorities took this opportunity to stir up, raise cross-strait confrontation, and to rely on the US. The attempt will not succeed.\nIf there are no further questions, here concludes today’s press conference. Thank you.","","http://eng.chinamil.com.cn/view/2019-04/25/content_9489162.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2019-04-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 25 dispatch: In response to the DPP authorities' smearing of the Hong Kong court's ruling in the \"Occupy Central\" case, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 25th in response to a question: The illegal \"Occupy Central,\" which lasted 79 days, seriously undermined the rule of law in the Hong Kong SAR and caused serious harm to Hong Kong's prosperity and stability and to the normal order of life of Hong Kong residents. The central government firmly supports the Hong Kong SAR in punishing the main organizers and planners of the illegal \"Occupy Central\" in accordance with the law. The DPP authorities, disregarding Hong Kong's rule of law and making irresponsible comments on Hong Kong affairs, are yet another manifestation of their habit of confusing right and wrong and turning black into white.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201904/t20190425_12159814.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-04-29","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday two US warships sailed through the Taiwan Strait. What is the Chinese government's reaction to this?","China closely followed and monitored from start to end the US warships' sailing through the Taiwan Strait and has expressed concerns to the US side. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive element in China-US relations. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and prudently and properly handle issues related to Taiwan to avoid negative impact on China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1659619.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1659475.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-05-06","Geng Shuang","","Registration for the 72nd World Health Assembly (WHA) will close today and Taiwan has not received an invitation. It has claimed on many occasions that its absence will affect the heath welfare of people in Taiwan and cause a gap in international epidemic prevention. Do you have a comment?","China's position on the Taiwan region's participation in international organizations, including the World Health Organization (WHO) is consistent and clear. It must be arranged pursuant to the one-China principle. This is also an important principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nFrom 2009 to 2016, the Taiwan region participated in the WHA as an observer under the name of \"Chinese Taipei\" for eight consecutive years. That was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultation on the basis of the 1992 consensus, which embodies the one-China principle. This principle represents the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations as well as the political basis for the special arrangement for Taiwan's participation in the WHA. However, the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP), since taking power in 2016, has been putting political calculations above the Taiwan people's welfare and entrenching itself in the secessionist position of \"Taiwan independence\", thus undermining the political foundation for the region's participation in the WHA. In a move to uphold the one-China principle and the solemnity and authority of UNGA and WHA resolutions, China has decided not to allow Taiwan's participation in this year's WHA.\nThe central government of China attaches high importance to the health welfare of Taiwan compatriots and has made proper arrangements regarding the region's participation in international health affairs on the precondition of the one-China principle. According to arrangements between China and the WHO, medical experts from Taiwan can attend WHO technical meetings and WHO experts can travel to Taiwan to conduct studies or provide assistance when such needs arise. The Taiwan region has timely access to information on global public health emergencies released by the WHO and information can also flow readily the other way. With these arrangements in place, Taiwan is able to cope promptly and effectively with local or global public health emergencies. Therefore it is a false claim that Taiwan's absence from the WHA will cause a gap in international epidemic prevention. It is nothing but the DPP's lie and pretext in an attempt to attend the WHA.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1661163.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1661103.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-05-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 6 dispatch: In response to the fact that the registration deadline for the 72nd World Health Assembly will close on the 6th, and that Taiwan will be unable to attend the World Health Assembly, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the same day in response to a question that the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already explained our position. We have stressed on many occasions that the question of the Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that from 2009 to 2016, for eight consecutive years, the Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei.” This was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides adhered to as embodying the one-China principle. Since the DPP authorities came to power in May 2016, they have obstinately clung to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and refused to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This has undermined the political basis for cross-Strait consultations and caused the Taiwan region to be unable to continue participating in the World Health Assembly. This situation was entirely created by the DPP authorities.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the mainland side has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. On the premise of the one-China principle, it has adopted a number of measures to promote cross-Strait cooperation and exchanges in the health sector, and has made proper arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs, reflecting the goodwill and care of the mainland side toward Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their party's own interests, place political scheming above the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, create and escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. They will inevitably meet with opposition from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190507_12162449.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-05-08","Geng Shuang","","The US House of Representatives yesterday passed a bill reaffirming the US commitment to Taiwan, which will now presumably be sent to the Senate to be passed into law. Has China asked the US not to pass the bill?","The bill is a grave violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and a gross interference in China's domestic affairs. China objects it resolutely and has lodged stern representations to the US side.\nWe urge the US to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques by stopping Congress to review and pass the bill and properly handling Taiwan-related issues to prevent severe damages to bilateral cooperation in key areas and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1661701.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1661695.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-05-09","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On May 3, Beijing time, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2019 “China Military and Security Developments Report.” Disregarding facts, confusing right and wrong, distorting China's strategic intentions, it passes baseless comments on China's normal national defense and military development, and makes wanton remarks about China's legitimate actions in safeguarding sovereignty and security interests. The Chinese military firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development, firmly pursues a defensive national defense policy, does not engage in military expansion, and does not seek spheres of influence. It has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a maintainer of international order. The Chinese military is committed to providing more public security goods to the international community, and the growth of China's military strength is the growth of the forces for world peace, a fact that is plain for all to see.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China. China's great cause of reunification must be realized, and it certainly will be realized. China requires the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness. The Chinese military has firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nChina's position on maritime issues is consistent and clear. China is committed to resolving disputes peacefully with the countries concerned through direct negotiations and consultations. Facts have proven that the regional countries have the confidence, wisdom, and capability to properly handle differences, maintain peace, and promote prosperity. By contrast, the U.S. side says it wants to maintain peace and stability, yet in practice it keeps strengthening its forward military presence and frequently sends warships and aircraft to the South China Sea to provoke, seriously harming the security interests of coastal states and undermining regional peace and stability.\nThe U.S. side has for many consecutive years published so-called “China Military and Security Developments Reports,” which damage mutual trust between China and the U.S. and poison the atmosphere of relations between the two countries and the two militaries. Right and wrong will eventually be clear, and justice will remain in people's hearts. We demand that the U.S. side view China's national defense and military development objectively and rationally, stop publishing relevant reports, and maintain the stable development of military-to-military relations and China-U.S. relations through concrete actions.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2019-05/09/content_4841454.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2019-05-14","Geng Shuang","","Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the CPPCC, delivered remarks to Taiwan media in the fourth Cross-Strait Media Summit in Beijing. Do you have any comment on his remarks?","Is that a diplomatic question? (The journalist laughed.)\nIf not, I'd refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1663358.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1663262.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends! Welcome to the TAO press conference. I now take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We understand that former Kuomintang Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu recently led a delegation to the mainland for a visit and exchange. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From May 12 to 15, Ms. Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang and chairperson of the Zhonghua Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, led a delegation of representatives from various sectors of Taiwan to visit Beijing. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, met with Hung Hsiu-chu and her delegation, and the Cross-Strait Relations Research Center and the Zhonghua Qingyan Peace Education Foundation jointly held a symposium titled “Cross-Strait Relations and National Rejuvenation.”\nBoth sides conducted in-depth exchanges of views on issues of common concern, including cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, engaged in consultative dialogue, and put forward six joint initiatives: working together to achieve national rejuvenation, consolidating the common political foundation, deepening cross-Strait integration and development, strengthening cross-Strait grassroots exchanges, promoting cross-Strait youth exchanges, and deepening cross-Strait cultural exchanges.\nIn the initiatives, both sides pointed out that adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” are the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Upholding this foundation enables cross-Strait relations to keep developing and the well-being of compatriots on both sides to keep growing. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and people of insight on both sides should cherish and safeguard this foundation even more, strengthen exchanges, interaction, dialogue and consultation, and jointly safeguard the overall situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe initiatives also hold that realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is a common dream of compatriots on both sides. In the process of national rejuvenation, Taiwan compatriots should not and will not be absent. The initiatives call on compatriots on both sides to join hands and work together to push cross-Strait relations in the right direction and to strive unremittingly to realize the dream of national rejuvenation together.\nThe initiatives also proposed to actively promote the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation, work hard to promote the full connectivity of cross-Strait transportation and communications, build a cross-Strait common market, and strengthen the Chinese nation’s economy. They support Taiwan counties, cities, groups and individuals who recognize the “1992 Consensus” in deepening exchanges and cooperation with the mainland, expanding sales of Taiwan’s agricultural and fishery products on the mainland, and strengthening cross-Strait tourism cooperation. They help Taiwan youth come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams. They oppose all forms of “de-Sinicization” and “cultural Taiwan independence” activities, enhance cultural and national identity among compatriots on both sides with Chinese culture and the Chinese nation, and promote spiritual connection.\nOn January 2 this year, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at a symposium marking the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” pointing out the direction for cross-Strait relations in the new era. We are willing, on the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to engage in diverse and wide-ranging consultation and dialogue with political parties, groups and individuals in Taiwan, accumulating common understanding while setting aside differences. As long as compatriots on both sides join forces and work together, we will surely move toward the broad road of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, peaceful reunification of the motherland, and great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165176.htm"],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Yesterday the Taiwan Affairs Office and China Development Bank signed an agreement on financial cooperation. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","On May 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the China Development Bank signed in Beijing the “Agreement on Supporting the Development of Taiwan-Invested Enterprises and Promoting Development Financial Cooperation for Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation.” Under this cooperation agreement, the China Development Bank will provide an indicative cooperation financing total of no less than RMB 60 billion over the next four years, strengthen comprehensive financial services and provide financial support in areas such as high-quality cross-Strait industrial development cooperation, investment and business establishment and upgrading of Taiwan-invested enterprises, and cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and innovation cooperation, to promote integrated development across the Strait.\nIn 2005, 2012 and 2016, both sides had signed financing cooperation agreements three times. To date, the China Development Bank has cumulatively disbursed more than RMB 185 billion in loans to Taiwan-invested projects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the latest progress made by localities and departments in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”","In recent times, localities and departments have actively implemented the people-centered development philosophy, upheld the concept of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family,” and continued to implement the “31 Measures to Benefit Taiwan Compatriots.” Recently, Heilongjiang Province, Yunnan Province, Shenyang City in Liaoning Province, and Wenzhou City in Zhejiang Province have also each introduced specific measures to implement the “31 Measures.” To date, 80 localities, including 27 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, have issued concrete implementation measures in light of local conditions, further enhancing Taiwan compatriots’ sense of benefit and honor.\nThe policy core of the “31 Measures” is to provide Taiwan compatriots who live, study, work, or start businesses in the mainland with equal treatment. Starting May 1, the Comprehensive Plan for Reducing Social Insurance Contribution Rates, implemented on the mainland, lowered social insurance contribution rates and adjusted contribution bases. In accordance with the spirit of the “31 Measures,” Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots on the mainland equally enjoy the relevant policies and benefit directly.\nIn addition, in implementing measures allowing Taiwan compatriots to take professional qualification examinations, the Ministry of Justice on April 28 issued professional qualification certificates in Xiamen City to 26 Taiwan residents who passed the 2018 National Unified Legal Professional Qualification Examination.\nIn terms of Taiwan compatriots being eligible for various honors and awards, around May Day and Youth Day (May 4), Beijing, Shanghai, Fujian, Hainan, Hubei, Hunan and other places have already conferred honorary titles such as model worker, “May 1st Labor Medal,” and “May 4th Youth Medal” on a number of Taiwan compatriots.\nIn encouraging Taiwan compatriots to participate in the inheritance of intangible cultural heritage, the Fujian-Taiwan local opera *Ada Sao* (阿搭嫂), jointly performed by the Xiamen Jinlian Shenggaoja Opera Troupe and the Youth Troupe of the Taiwan Theatre Academy, began performances today at the 12th China Arts Festival in Shanghai. The production blends three opera genres, Gaojia opera, Hakka opera, and Gezai opera, and is a meaningful attempt at integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan local opera arts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165175.htm"],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","As you just mentioned, the Ministry of Justice recently held a ceremony in Xiamen to issue legal professional qualification certificates to Taiwan residents. Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the basic situation of Taiwan residents taking the mainland's national judicial examination.","Earlier, we introduced at a press conference that on March 26 this year, the Supreme People’s Court issued the “Several Measures on Providing Judicial Services for Deepening Cross-Strait Integrated Development,” which proposes 36 judicial measures benefiting Taiwan in four areas. These explicitly call for gradually expanding Taiwan compatriots’ participation in the judiciary, so as to create better conditions for the broad Taiwan compatriots to contribute to national rule-of-law construction.\nHere, I would like to review with everyone the basic situation of Taiwan residents taking the national judicial examination. In 2008, the Ministry of Justice promulgated the “Several Provisions on Taiwan Residents’ Participation in the National Judicial Examination,” and specifically set up centralized examination zones for Taiwan residents in Xiamen and Shenzhen to provide convenient services for Taiwan residents taking the examination. In 2018, the reconstituted Ministry of Justice formulated and issued the “Measures for Implementing the National Unified Legal Professional Qualification Examination,” again clarifying that Taiwan residents may take the National Unified Legal Professional Qualification Examination, continuing the principle that Taiwan residents and mainland residents take the examination in the same way, under the same standards, and on equal terms. The first National Unified Legal Professional Qualification Examination, held in September 2018, coincided with the tenth anniversary of Taiwan residents taking this examination, and the number of Taiwan examinees who passed increased substantially compared with previous years. To date, thousands of person-times have registered for the examination, and several hundred people have been granted legal professional qualifications. The Ministry of Justice has also successively introduced four legal service opening-up policies toward Taiwan, including expanded scope of practice.\nWe will, as always, safeguard the right to practice of Taiwan compatriots who have obtained mainland lawyer professional qualifications, provide broad space and a platform for Taiwan legal youth to put their learning into practice, actively take part in mainland rule-of-law construction, and participate in the construction of cross-Strait legal services and “Belt and Road” legal services, providing ample room and a stage for advancing cross-Strait economic and social integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165174.htm"],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the 4th Cross-Strait Media Summit was held in Beijing, and the DPP authorities pressured Taiwanese media personnel who attended the summit. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","The 4th Cross-Strait Media Summit Beijing was held in Beijing from May 9 to 12, with more than 160 media leaders, heads of journalism schools, and experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait in attendance, reflecting the shared desire of mainstream media on both sides to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nWang Yang, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, met with the participants, expounded the mainland's policies toward Taiwan, introduced the general trend of cross-Strait relations, and expressed our position of implementing General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech of January 2, adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" and promoting cross-Strait relations in the right direction. He hopes that cross-Strait media will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, fulfill their social responsibilities well, and jointly play a role in communicating between people on both sides of the Strait, promoting Chinese culture, and deepening emotional bonds, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.\nCross-Strait news exchange plays an important role in enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides. The reason the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces obstruct and smear it is that they fear that, as compatriots on both sides deepen their understanding of each other, they will recognize the political essence of their pursuit of narrow party interests and see through their schemes to undermine cross-Strait relations. Therefore, it is not surprising that they do this, and it will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165173.htm"],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Terry Gou (Guo Taiming) recently said, “I 100% agree that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China.” He also said in an interview, “I will not say ‘the 1992 Consensus’ unless it is paired with ‘one China, respective interpretations,’” and that Beijing should “find a peaceful foundation for resolving cross-Strait issues.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and China’s sovereignty and territory are not to be divided.\nThe “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Both sides have stated that the two sides belong to one China and jointly strive for national reunification. The “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations, showing that the two sides are not a state-to-state relationship.\nThe mainland and Taiwan are a community of shared destiny, sharing weal and woe. Taiwan’s future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Upholding the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of peaceful national reunification are a matter of national righteousness and serve the common interests of compatriots on both sides. On the long-standing political differences across the Strait, in the process of compatriots on both sides working together toward unification, both sides should, with a sense of responsibility to the nation and to future generations, explore solutions together on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Two questions. First, the US House of Representatives recently passed the so-called “Taiwan Assurance Act of 2019,” which requires normalization of arms sales to Taiwan, and the DPP authorities have expressed gratitude for it. What impact will this act have on cross-Strait relations? Second, it is reported that the number of mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan during this year's May Day holiday increased…","Regarding the first question, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position. We firmly oppose U.S. interference in China’s internal affairs. The U.S. side should abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We also warn the DPP authorities once again: pursuing “Taiwan independence” by placing one’s bets on foreign forces is unreliable. Relying on foreign powers to bolster oneself will inevitably bring retribution upon oneself.\nRegarding the second question, after the “nine-in-one” elections on the island last year, more and more counties and cities have expressed support for the “1992 Consensus,” and mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan have shown clear signs of recovery. In particular, the launch of regular flights from Shanghai to Penghu and the resumption of the Xiamen-Kaohsiung sea route have greatly facilitated mainland tourists traveling to the central and southern counties and cities of Taiwan. On May 8, 9, and 11, after the May Day holiday, three more cruise voyages full of tourists departed from Xiamen for Penghu and Kaohsiung.\nCompatriots on both sides are one family, and the affection between compatriots on both sides is the driving force behind mainland residents’ travel to Taiwan and a bond that enhances the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good. As long as we adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” whether through tourism to Taiwan or exchanges between counties and cities, we can continuously bring tangible benefits to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165172.htm"],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The Taiwan referendum authority recently held a hearing on the so-called “Peaceful Neutrality Referendum” proposed by Lu Hsiu-lien. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are inviolable. We firmly oppose any act that attempts to challenge the One-China principle or undermine cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, could the spokesperson introduce the relevant circumstances of Mr. Wang Jinping's recent visit to Fujian to pay respects to ancestors? Second, regarding China-US trade frictions, some voices on the island believe Taiwan may benefit from this. The head of Taiwan's economic affairs department recently said that the China-US trade dispute is affecting companies' deployment, which has…","The first question. From May 6 to 8, Wang Jin-pyng, Honorary Chairman of the Taiwan Wang Clan Association, led his family members and clan members to his ancestral home in Zhangzhou, Fujian, to offer sacrifices to ancestors and exchange views with local clan members. In Xiamen, he paid tribute to the national hero Zheng Chenggong, and also visited the Taiwan Youth Entrepreneurship Base and Taiwan-funded enterprises and held discussions with Taiwanese businesspeople. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, met with Mr. Wang Jin-pyng, and the two sides exchanged views on promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” and working to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Mr. Wang Jin-pyng said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all part of the Chinese nation, and that Chinese sons and daughters are one family. The “1992 Consensus” has laid a solid foundation for the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations, and “Taiwan independence” simply will not work. Compatriots on both sides should keep pace with the times, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and work for the prosperity of the Chinese nation. You have all seen these developments through media reports.\nMr. Wang Jin-pyng's return with his family and clan members to offer sacrifices to ancestors and pay tribute to Zheng Chenggong demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same ancestry and blood ties, and reflects the Taiwan Wang clan's inheritance of traditional Chinese culture and its sense of attachment to the nation and family. Over the years, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation have become increasingly extensive, contacts among compatriots have grown ever closer, family bonds among compatriots have deepened, and mutual understanding has grown increasingly harmonious. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to return to the mainland to take part in various forms of exchange activities, and we welcome more Taiwan compatriots to participate in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe second question. Over the forty years of reform and opening up, the mainland's economic and social development has achieved tremendous success, becoming the world's second-largest economy and largest market. Our economic development has enormous strategic depth, resilience, and sustained, strong domestic demand, and enterprises from around the world remain optimistic about the mainland as an investment destination.\nNo matter how the external environment changes, our attitude of supporting the continued development of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland has been consistent and clear. We have gradually adopted a number of measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises, and we will continue to introduce and improve relevant policies in the future, expand opening up, optimize the business environment, and create more opportunities and broader space for the development of Taiwanese enterprises on the mainland.\nCorporate investment follows economic laws, and economic laws are what ultimately decide it. Some people in Taiwan attempt to use the current China-US trade frictions to weaken the economic ties between the two sides of the Strait. Their wishful thinking will only come to nothing, and the great tide and trend of cross-Strait economic cooperation cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Taiwan’s “Legislative Yuan” recently passed amendments to the relevant regulations, and Ma Ying-jeou, Wu Den-yih and others, who had planned to visit the mainland this year, may be unable to make the trip. What is the spokesperson’s comment? In addition, regarding the KMT-CPC Forum, what is the current state of consultations between the mainland and the Kuomintang?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have engaged in exchanges and dialogue through various forms, strengthened communication and cooperation, and played an important role in improving and developing cross-Strait relations and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots. For some time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, out of narrow partisan self-interest, have continually set up obstacles to personnel exchanges across the Strait, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots. Such practices are unpopular. We are willing, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to continue deepening exchanges and contacts with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals, and to work together with compatriots in Taiwan to push cross-Strait relations in the right direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Since 2002, the China Association for Science and Technology has launched the “Yushan Plan” for youth exchanges between Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, inviting Taiwan students to intern in Beijing and Nanjing every year. However, Taiwan’s “Ministry of Education” recently sent a letter to National Taiwan University and National Chengchi University, requiring the two schools to take down online announcements of this…","We have commented on and criticized such words and deeds of the DPP authorities many times. For some time now, they have gone to all lengths to obstruct normal exchanges in all fields across the Strait. Their methods are very ugly and their faces are very vile. They describe normal cross-Strait exchanges as \"United Front infiltration\" of Taiwan; they describe voices on the island criticizing their poor governance as \"fake information and fake news\"; and they describe the Mainland side's measures that do good deeds and practical things for Taiwan compatriots as \"threats\" to Taiwan. This is a complete distortion of black and white. I believe broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize, through this series of actions by the DPP authorities, their essence: pursuing the narrow private interests of one party and its individuals, and grabbing electoral benefits even at the cost of undermining cross-Strait relations and harming the interests of the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Tsai Ing-wen has recently frequently entered military camps in Taiwan, attempting to seek “independence” through force, and has made public clamors promoting “Taiwan independence,” such as “If you want independence and not unification, vote for Tsai Ing-wen.” How does the spokesperson comment?","We have repeatedly criticized the words and deeds of “Taiwan independence” by the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces. We will never tolerate “Taiwan independence,” and our stance on this is unequivocal. I want to emphasize that the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the safeguarding and protection of the common interests of compatriots on both sides must adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence.” Any conduct that runs counter to this will be in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, as the island's elections have heated up, the DPP authorities have begun strictly investigating so-called Taiwan media outlets that are “on the same path” as the mainland, including their reporting and related content. What views does the spokesperson have?","As I just said, this is a despicable act by the DPP authorities, who are trying to undermine cross-Strait relations and pursue the narrow private interests of one party and one individual. Cross-Strait news exchange has made outstanding contributions to the development of cross-Strait relations, and it has played an irreplaceable role in conveying the feelings of people on both sides and enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots. It is precisely out of fear of the media’s role that the DPP authorities have reached out with a dark hand to suppress media outlets and figures on the island that uphold justice, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and advocate developing cross-Strait relations. Such practices will ultimately not succeed, because compatriots in Taiwan have the basic judgment to tell right from wrong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","DPP authorities recently said that Taiwan residents who shop on Taobao may have their personal data collected, which could then be used to influence and manipulate their voting behavior. What views does the spokesperson have?","This is a completely groundless, black-and-white-reversing, and highly irresponsible statement. This is exactly what the DPP authorities are doing: they not only tighten all kinds of control within the island, divide Taiwan society, and suppress people who advocate developing cross-Strait relations, creating a so-called “green terror,” but also attempt to shift focus and frame others, desperately inciting cross-Strait confrontation and raising hostility between the two sides. I believe compatriots on both sides of the Strait will not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently, the head of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said that they have preliminarily learned that 100,000 Taiwan compatriots have obtained mainland residence permits, and that a registration mechanism will be established in the future. For those who do not report, they plan to impose fines of NT$10,000 to NT$50,000. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We have said many times that the issuance of Taiwan residence permits is intended to facilitate life, work, and study for Taiwan compatriots in the mainland, and to provide them with equal treatment. This also responds positively to the long-standing demands of Taiwan compatriots, and aims to resolve the practical difficulties and specific problems that trouble Taiwan compatriots. The core function of issuing Taiwan residence permits is to enjoy equal treatment. Therefore, Taiwan compatriots holding this document can enjoy 3 rights, 6 basic public services, and 9 conveniences provided by the state and their place of residence, which is good news for the broad Taiwan compatriots. We have introduced the specifics before, and everyone can look them up. But as everyone has seen, on the one hand the mainland is doing good deeds for Taiwan compatriots, while on the other hand the DPP authorities are undermining the good deeds for Taiwan compatriots, and even go so far as to punish Taiwan compatriots for this. I believe the people see this very clearly, and such practices will ultimately only further lose popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","This time, Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairwoman of the KMT, came to the mainland, and both sides held a joint discussion and put forward six initiatives. How will these six initiatives be implemented, and how will their results be tracked? Another question: Ms. Hung Hsiu-chu is the first Taiwan guest invited through the method of democratic consultation and democratic dialogue. Will the second invitee be New Party…","As for your third question, I have already stated my clear position and views. I think these Taiwan media outlets, which are motivated by the original aspiration to improve and develop cross-Strait relations, should hold their heads high, since evil cannot prevail over righteousness.\nAs for your first two questions, I will answer them together. In this exchange, at the symposium, some specific opinions and suggestions were raised that are conducive to the development of cross-Strait relations and to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, including some of the content of the Six Major Initiatives. Some of these we are already actively working to implement, and some we will study carefully. We hope people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait will join together to break through the layers of obstruction and restrictions imposed by the Taiwan authorities and jointly create the conditions for realizing these initiatives. I reaffirm that we are willing, on the political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to carry out dialogue and consultation in diverse forms and with broad content with Taiwan’s political parties, groups and individuals, to seek common ground while reconciling differences, build consensus, and we will continue to work toward this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190515_12165195.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The US House of Representatives recently voted to pass the “Taiwan Assurance Act of 2019” and the resolution “Reaffirming US Commitments to Taiwan and to Implementing the Taiwan Relations Act,” advocating the normalization of arms sales to Taiwan and implementation of the “Taiwan Travel Act.” The DPP authorities have expressed gratitude. What is your comment on this?","At the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office on May 15,\nspokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions, saying that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our position on this. We firmly oppose US interference in China's internal affairs. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop damaging peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities once again: pursuing “Taiwan independence” by betting on foreign forces is unreliable, and relying on foreign powers to boost oneself will surely bring its own punishment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190515_12165171.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-05-21","Lu Kang","","The 72nd World Health Assembly (WHA) has decided not to include a Taiwan-related proposal into its provisional agenda. Would you like to comment on that?","This year the WHA has again refused to include the so-called proposal of \"inviting Taiwan to attend the WHA as an observer\" in the conference's provisional agenda. This decision, consistent with provisions of relevant resolutions of the UNGA and the WHA, is a further testament that the one-China principle is an overriding trend with wide support that cannot be challenged. I would like to reiterate that the participation of China's Taiwan region in the activities of international organizations must and can only be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1665346.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1665274.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-05-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 22: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 22nd that Yu Mu-ming, chairman of the New Party and honorary chairman of the New Chinese Sons and Daughters Society, will lead a delegation of Taiwan personages from all sectors to visit Guangdong, Shanghai, Jiangsu, Beijing and other places from May 24 to 30. During their stay in Beijing, personages from all sectors across the Strait will hold dialogues and consultations on cross-Strait relations and national rejuvenation and exchange views in depth.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that General Secretary Xi Jinping, in his important speech at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” said that in the process of the Chinese nation’s march toward great rejuvenation, Taiwan compatriots will certainly not be absent. We will, together with personages from all sectors on the island, jointly explore practices of integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and peaceful reunification, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly pursue the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190522_12167175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-05-23","Lu Kang","","Tanzanian officials said a major port project backed by China has stalled and accused the Chinese side of unfair treatment. Is the foreign ministry aware of this and does it have any comment on the accusations? Also, the US military said it sent two warships through the Taiwan Strait on Wednesday. What's the ministry's comment on that?","On your first question, I just saw relevant reports. You may be aware that backward infrastructure and lack of funds are the main bottlenecks of Africa's independent development. As a friend and partner of African countries, China has been doing its best in conducting cooperation on infrastructure, investment and financing with Africa. Also, we have carried out feasibility studies to ensure the socio-economic benefits and sustainable development of projects. The Chinese government will continue to support Chinese businesses in participating in infrastructure construction, including the port project in Tanzania you mentioned, in accordance with market principles.\nRegarding your second question, the Chinese side has been closely monitoring from start to end the passage by the US warships through the Taiwan Strait. We have raised concerns to the US side. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive one in China-US relations. We urge the US to observe the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid negative impacts on China-US relations and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1666065.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1665967.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-05-27","Lu Kang","","The US National Security Adviser John Bolton, according to Taiwan's \"foreign ministry\", had talks recently with his Taiwanese \"counterpart\", the first time since 1979 there has been such a high-level contact between US government officials and Taiwanese officials. Has China already complained about this meeting to the US?","Before answering your question, I need to correct you on one point. In light of the US government's explicit recognition of the government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal representative of China and its commitment that it only maintains unofficial exchange with Taiwan, Mr. David Lee is by no means the \"counterpart\" of Mr. Bolton.\nAs to the incident you referred to, China deplores and strongly objects to that. As we have repeatedly stated, the one-China principle is the political basis for China-US relations. We are firmly against the US engaging in any official contact with Taiwan in whatever form and under whatever pretext. We also stand resolutely against any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\". This is our clear and consistent position. Once again we urge the US side to honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop having official exchange or upgrading substantive relations with Taiwan, and prudently and properly handle issues relating to it to avoid affecting China-US relations and bilateral cooperation in key areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1666925.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1666906.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-05-28","Lu Kang","","Recently there have been reports on a warming relationship between Taiwan and the US. For instance, US warships sailed through the Taiwan Strait; the Coordination Council for North American Affairs (CCNAA) was renamed the Taiwan Council for US Affairs (TCUSA); Taiwan's security chief David Lee met with US National Security Adviser John Bolton. Since the phrase \"maximum pressure\" has been frequently used in the…","You know the Chinese government's position very well.\nLet me reiterate that the one-China principle is the political basis for the development of China-US relations in the past four decades. Only when the US strictly abides by this principle and the three joint communiques can there be sound development in bilateral relations and good cooperation on important issues. The US knows that very well. Therefore, regarding the recent wrong moves relating to Taiwan, China has stated its solemn position to the US side and urged it to honor its commitment under the bilateral political framework to avoid disrupting our relationship and cooperation in key areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1667291.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1667286.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-05-28","An Fengshan","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A Taiwan external-affairs department said that Li Ta-wei, head of its security agency, recently visited the United States and met with U.S. National Security Advisor John Bolton. Do you have any comment on this? An Fengshan said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position on this, and then made the above comment.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 28: State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson An Fengshan responded to questions on the 28th, pointing out that the One-China Principle is a universally recognized norm of international relations and the political foundation of China-US relations. Any remarks and actions that undermine the One-China Principle are tantamount to shaking the foundations of China-US relations. They do not conform to the fundamental interests of the two countries and are also extremely dangerous, and we firmly oppose them. We warn the DPP authorities once again that “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. Any attempt to inflate oneself by relying on foreign powers will be futile and will surely reap the bitter fruit of one's own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190528_12168932.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to everyone attending this morning's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I am glad to take your questions below.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Tsai Ing-wen's administration has been in power for three years. How does the spokesperson assess cross-Strait relations over these three years?","Since May 20, 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. They have supported and condoned all kinds of “Taiwan independence” activities, obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and relied on foreign support to assert themselves. They have repeatedly put forward all kinds of divisive remarks filled with the “two-state theory,” arbitrarily attacked the mainland, incited hostility across the Strait, and escalated confrontation across the Strait. This has not only worsened cross-Strait relations and made the situation in the Taiwan Strait more complex and grim, but has also seriously damaged the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nOver the past three years, in the face of the various provocations and sabotage by the Taiwan authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, we have unwaveringly adhered to the major policy guidelines for work on Taiwan. We have resolutely implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan, firmly upheld the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and resolutely opposed and contained any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and acts. At the same time, we have actively implemented the people-centered development philosophy, upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and worked hard to expand civil exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait. We have continuously rolled out a series of policies and measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, including the “31 Measures,” water supply to Kinmen, and the issuance of Residence Permits for Taiwan Residents, promoting cross-Strait integration and development and the spiritual connection of compatriots. The future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation. We will unite broad Taiwan compatriots to overcome difficulties together with us, remove obstacles, and work hard to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and steadily advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. This is something no person and no force can stop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190529_12169176.htm"],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed that it was because the mainland proposed the “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan that she stated her position clearly, and that she was not being provocative. Tsai also said that the mainland is constantly influencing Taiwan through suppression, and that the 2020 “election” may be Taiwan's last election. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China. China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided and brook no division. The fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and brooks no change. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to unification, much less a pretext for division. Any words or deeds that attempt to change the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China are a serious provocation against the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nWhenever there is an election on the island, the DPP and its authority leaders always use the tactic of inciting cross-Strait hostility, escalating cross-Strait confrontation, intensifying conflicts and worsening cross-Strait relations, and adopt the deliberate-provocation “pengci” (staged-collision) tactic to provoke the mainland. This is their habitual routine, aimed at creating hostility and confrontation to win votes through deception. However, lies and trickery will always be exposed and seen through. Looking back at the period from 2008 to 2016, when there were large-scale exchanges and cooperation across the Strait and a scene of peaceful development and stability and tranquility, and comparing it with the increasingly complex and severe situation in the Taiwan Strait since the DPP came to power in 2016, who caused it is self-evident. In the face of facts, do the DPP and its authority leaders still want to continue deceiving people with this method of fabricating things out of nothing and sensationalist rhetoric?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190529_12169175.htm"],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the latest progress made by localities and departments in implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots.”","All localities and departments have been continuously implementing the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” and have recently achieved some new results. Let me give a few examples.\nIn the past month, Shandong Province has successively and intensively issued specific implementing opinions on the “31 Measures” in Jinan, Yantai, Tai'an, Zaozhuang, Liaocheng, Jining and several other localities, implementing the “31 Measures” in detail across the Qilu region and providing more convenience and greater support for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises developing in Shandong.\nIn financial cooperation, Fubon Hwa Yi Bank was approved to prepare for credit card business, becoming the first Taiwan-funded bank on the mainland approved for this business. This will provide stronger support for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland to enjoy more financial services.\nIn supporting the development of Taiwan youth, the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office recently released a summer internship position list for Taiwan youth, offering 1,000 excellent positions to Taiwan youth willing to intern in Jiangsu. The positions cover state-owned enterprises, public institutions, private enterprises, Taiwan-funded enterprises and social public welfare organizations, including many well-known enterprises and departments, and span more than 30 industries and fields such as finance, law, healthcare, and news media.\nIn opening various mainland award programs to Taiwan compatriots, the Chinese Poetry Research Institute recently announced the list of winners of the inaugural “Qu Yuan Poetics Award.” The awards ceremony will be held in Jingzhou, Hubei on June 3, and Taiwan scholars won the “Poetics Essay Award” among them. This is a concrete manifestation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly carrying out research on Chinese history and culture and working together to promote excellent traditional Chinese culture. We believe that more Taiwan compatriots, like mainland compatriots, who have achieved outstanding results in their professional fields and made significant contributions will receive corresponding recognition, encouragement and commendation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190529_12169177.htm"],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","中新社记者","New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming recently led a delegation on a visit and exchange on the mainland. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","From May 24 to 30, Yu Mu-ming, chairman of the New Party and honorary chairman of the New Chinese Sons and Daughters Association, led a delegation of representatives from all walks of life in Taiwan to visit Guangdong, Shanghai, Jiangsu and Beijing. Li Xi, Party Secretary of Guangdong Provincial Committee, Li Qiang, Party Secretary of Shanghai Municipal Committee, and Wu Zhenglong, Governor of Jiangsu Province, respectively met with Yu Mu-ming and his party. Yu Mu-ming’s delegation also paid respects at the Huanghuagang Mausoleum of the Seventy-Two Martyrs in Guangzhou and the Sun Yat-sen Mausoleum in Nanjing, visited some Taiwanese enterprises and entrepreneurship bases for Taiwanese youth, held discussions with Taiwanese students and businesspeople, and learned about cross-Strait economic cooperation and the work, living and study conditions of Taiwan compatriots locally. This morning, people from all walks of life across the Strait held dialogue and consultation in Beijing on topics related to cross-Strait relations and national rejuvenation, and exchanged views in depth. We will release relevant details in a timely manner. During the stay in Beijing, other important activities will also take place, and they will be announced in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190529_12169178.htm"],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","It is reported that Guangdong will hold activities soon for Taiwan businesses participating in the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in seizing and sharing the development opportunities of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, deepen cross-strait integrated development, and promote economic, cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, the theme event \"Taiwan Businesses Come Together, Integrate into the Greater Bay Area\" will be held in Guangdong from June 3 to 5. Relevant departments, Guangdong provincial leaders, the chairpersons of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit from both sides, representatives of Taiwan business groups and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and Taiwan youth representatives, about 300 people in total, will attend the event. Holding this event is a positive response to Taiwan compatriots' and Taiwan-funded enterprises' close attention to, and eager hopes of participating in, the construction of the Greater Bay Area. It will explain in detail the development plan and related policies of the Greater Bay Area to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Representatives of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will visit Greater Bay Area cities including Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Zhuhai, Foshan and Dongguan, and will also see on the ground major development platforms such as Qianhai and the Hengqin New Area. We hope this event will help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises gain a deeper understanding of the Greater Bay Area, integrate into it, share its opportunities, pursue development together, and create win-win outcomes together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201905/t20190529_12169174.htm"],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","The United States has recently moved to contain and suppress Huawei. Has this affected some Taiwan-invested enterprises in the mainland and Taiwan-related supply chain enterprises? Outside observers have noted that TSMC, one of Huawei’s suppliers, has said it has not stopped supplying Huawei. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We also noted that the supplier list Huawei published earlier includes quite a few Taiwan companies. It can be said that Huawei’s achievements also owe something to the contributions of these Taiwan companies. Huawei’s cooperation with relevant Taiwan companies helps leverage complementary advantages among enterprises, achieves a strong alliance, and plays a positive role in the common economic development of both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently the United States has constantly played the “Taiwan card.” The DPP authorities have explicitly stated that they are willing to be part of the U.S. Indo-Pacific strategy, and they keep treating the mainland as a “hypothetical enemy” and staging various military exercises. The U.S. and Taiwan singing from the same songbook has provoked resentment among mainland netizens, and has again stirred a wave of…","We have repeatedly and clearly stated that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region, and will not allow foreign forces to play the “Taiwan card” to harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities that pursuing “Taiwan independence” by placing bets on foreign forces is unreliable. Any conduct that relies on foreign powers to gain standing, sows discord internationally, escalates cross-Strait confrontation, creates hostility among compatriots and worsens cross-Strait relations will ultimately reap its own bitter fruit. No person or force should underestimate our determination and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","The Tsai authorities have been very active recently. After extending exit restrictions on Ma Ying-jeou and Wu Den-yih earlier, they have now stepped up restrictions on retired generals traveling to the mainland for activities. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have carried out exchanges, dialogue, communication and cooperation through various forms, playing an important role in improving and developing cross-Strait relations and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. For some time now, the DPP authorities, out of the narrow private interests of one party and its individuals, have used various pretexts to restrict cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions, and have suppressed Taiwan figures who take part in cross-Strait exchanges. This runs counter to the desire of Taiwan's public to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and also seriously harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We are willing, on the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\", to continue deepening exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, and to work together with broad Taiwan compatriots to push cross-Strait relations in the right direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","Since 2002, the China Association for Science and Technology has launched the “Yushan Plan” for youth exchanges among Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao, inviting Taiwan university students to intern in Beijing every summer vacation. This year, Taiwan's education authorities sent letters requiring National Taiwan University and National Chengchi University to take down the announcements of these programs. Please give…","Cross-Strait educational exchange and cooperation is an important component of exchange and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, and it concerns the interests and well-being of young people on both sides. We have always actively supported and encouraged strengthening exchange and cooperation in education across the Strait, enhancing mutual understanding among young people on both sides, and creating better conditions and greater space for Taiwan students to study, intern, work, and live on the mainland. However, the DPP authorities have obstructed Taiwan youth's development on the mainland and cross-Strait educational exchanges, distorted and smeared them, and deliberately sabotaged cross-Strait educational exchanges. What they are harming is the development opportunities and well-being of Taiwan's young people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","Taiwan recently passed a dedicated same-sex marriage law. Is the mainland considering legalizing same-sex marriage?","We have noted reports on the island. The mainland practices a marriage system in which one man and one woman form a married couple.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities renamed the “North American Affairs Council” the “Taiwan-U.S. Affairs Council,” and the DPP authorities believe this move symbolizes close Taiwan-U.S. relations. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Yesterday, our office's spokesperson, in the form of answering reporters' questions, clearly stated our solemn position on the relevant issues. The one-China principle is a norm generally recognized by the international community and an important political foundation of China-US relations. Any remarks and actions that undermine the one-China principle would shake the foundations of China-US relations, do not conform to the fundamental interests of the two countries, and are very dangerous words and deeds. We firmly oppose them. We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities again: “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. Any attempt to rely on foreign backing to throw one's weight around has no way out and will surely bring self-inflicted disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","台湾“中央社”记者","Taiwan region leader Tsai Ing-wen recently met with so-called “democracy activists.” What is the TAO's view?","Only the people of the mainland have the most say on the mainland’s political, economic, and social development. Under the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China, we have firmly followed the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics, persisted in reform and opening up, and achieved remarkable accomplishments that have attracted worldwide attention. These cannot be negated by character assassination and slander. The DPP authorities’ continued escalation of cross-Strait confrontation and conduct undermining cross-Strait relations are unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","台湾中天电视台记者","The DPP authorities recently plan to amend relevant regulations under which individuals or parties who participate in democratic consultation on the mainland would be subject to the so-called “treason offense.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's response?","We have stated many times that democratic consultation is the correct direction for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it accords with the wishes of people on both sides and the trend of the times. Whatever is conducive to the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation should be actively promoted. On the basis of the one-China principle, political parties and people from all walks of life on both sides have the right and the responsibility to express their views, conduct consultations, and build consensus through democratic consultation. The DPP authorities scheme to create “one country on each side” and deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation and hostility. Such conduct cannot stop the tide of cross-Strait relations moving forward. By continually suppressing parties and personages in Taiwan that advocate peaceful reunification, they undermine the fundamental interests of the Taiwan people and the future of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Hong Kong media report that the mainland plans to build a “One Country, Two Systems” museum in Beijing, which will include a Taiwan pavilion. Please verify this.","I am not currently aware of the relevant information regarding the establishment of a museum that you mentioned. What I want to emphasize is that we advocate “peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems.” “Peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems” is the best way to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve national reunification. “One Country, Two Systems” is meant to take into account the realities of Taiwan and safeguard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and it embodies the goodwill and care of the mainland toward the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The specific form in which “One Country, Two Systems” would be realized in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan’s actual circumstances, will fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides, and will also fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","人民日报海外网记者","Kaohsiung Mayor Han Kuo-yu said that many DPP members very much want to go to the mainland to see its progress and development, but they are “stuck” due to the DPP party label, party discipline and electoral pressure. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","We do not comment on remarks by people on the island. Good cross-strait relations are the only way for Taiwan to do well, and only then can the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots be safeguarded and enhanced. Our attitude toward contacts with DPP figures is very clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","Two US Navy vessels again transited the Taiwan Strait this month. A spokesperson for the US Seventh Fleet said that these ships' transit through the Taiwan Strait demonstrates US commitment to a free and open Indo-Pacific. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position on this matter, and relevant departments have lodged serious representations with the US side. The Taiwan question concerns China's core interests, and we firmly oppose any external interference. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-05-29","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Media recently reported that after an event on the 23rd, the president-elect of El Salvador's vice presidency claimed that after taking office, El Salvador does not rule out restoring so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities. What response does the spokesperson have?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a recognized norm of the international community and a common consensus of the international community, and it is also the fundamental basis on which China establishes and develops relations with any country. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Saudi Arabia was the correct choice. It conforms to the trend of historical development and to the fundamental interests of both countries and their peoples.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201905/t20190529_12169205.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We noticed a series of moves by the US side on Taiwan related issues. For example, the US House of Representatives passed an act to reassure the US commitments to Taiwan, US military warships frequently sailed through the Taiwan Strait, the top National Security Council officials met with each other for the first time and there were high-profile activities held to commemorate the 40th anniversary of the so called…","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affairs and it has to do with China’s core interests and it has a direct bearing on the Chinese people’s feelings. Therefore it brooks no foreign interference.\nRecently the US side frequently plays the Taiwan card in an attempt to use Taiwan to contain China, which is merely wishful thinking. The “One China” principle is widely accepted by international community and also serves as the pivotal political foundation of the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the US. The US side is playing with fire. It seriously hurts the advancement of the China and US state-to-state and mil-to-mil ties and it seriously undermines peace and stability across the Strait.\nWe also noticed the separatist rhetoric and acts by the DPP authorities. It must be pointed out that the so called “Taiwan Independence” is the biggest threat plaguing the peace and stability across the Strait. It is also the biggest menace hurting the fundamental interests of the Taiwan people. By upholding the principle of “peaceful reunification” and the “One Country, Two Systems”, we advance the peaceful development of the cross Strait relations and promote the cause of peaceful reunification of the motherland. That said, we steadfastly oppose any attempt and move aiming at separating the country. Attempting independence by using force is doomed to fail. Seeking “Taiwan Independence” or placing all the bets on a foreign power does not and will not work. One will only swallow the bitter fruit if he or she panders to foreign powers in an attempt to increase his or her own importance.\nThe PLA is fully determined, confident and capable in defeating any separatist act to safeguard the integrity of territory and sovereignty.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-05/30/content_4842691.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, on May 7, the US House of Representatives passed the Taiwan Assurance Act, which said Taiwan is an important partner in the US Indo-Pacific strategy and the arms sale to Taiwan should be normalized. What is your comment? Second, the quasi aircraft carrier Izumo of the Japanese Self-Defense Force has been active in the South China Sea region this month, and it has interacted with…","For your first question, Taiwan is part of China and its future cannot be guaranteed by someone else.\nFor your second question, we have noticed the relevant developments of the Japanese quasi aircraft carrier Izumo in the South China Sea region. Due to historical and realistic reason, the moves by the Japanese side in the military security field are closely followed by Asian neighbors and the International community. It is our hope that the Japanese side can take history as a lesson and abide by their commitment to a path of peaceful development, do more to enhance mutual trust with neighboring countries and contribute to regional stability, rather than the opposite.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-05/30/content_4842691.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Thank you. I have two questions. In recent days, Taiwan has conducted a series of military exercises, and there is one today. I think it is landing on the beach exercise. I just wonder if the PLA is paying attention to these exercises and if you have comments or observations? As for my second question, recently the Australian navy was sailing in the South China Sea, and some of the helicopter pilots were reported…","For your first question, we have noticed relevant moves. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with our utmost sincerity and efforts. However, it must be pointed out that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end and there is no way out to engage in armed confrontation.\nOn the second question, the accusations are not true. We hope the Australia side could reflect on their own deeds before pointing fingers at others. Chinese fishermen are entitled to operate according to the law within the waters administered by China, and to the freedom of navigation and fishing in the high seas.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-05/30/content_4842691.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-06-03","Geng Shuang","","China's Defense Minister Wei Fenghe said on Sunday at the Shangri-La Dialogue in Singapore that if anyone dares to split Taiwan from China, the Chinese military has no choice but to fight at all costs. In this regard, does China assume the situation in the Taiwan Strait is somehow worsening right now? If so, what factors have done such a negative impact?","First, in his remarks, State Councilor and Defense Minister Wei Fenghe made clear China's position on the Taiwan question, which has been consistent and firm all along.\nSecond, his remarks were in response to the wrong comments on Taiwan-related issues by Acting US Defense Secretary Shanahan at the Shangri-La Dialogue.\nThird, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. This is a universal consensus of the international community.\nFourth, China has the determination, the will and the capability to realize the complete reunification of our country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1669120.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1669065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-06-03","Geng Shuang","","US Senator Cory Gardner, Chairman of the US Senate Foreign Relations Subcommittee on East Asia, the Pacific, and International Cybersecurity Policy, said recently that he hopes to invite Tsai Ing-wen to speak at the US Congress and that he will continue to push the \"TAIPEI Act\". Chinese State Councilor and Defense Minister Wei Fenghe has given a strong response to the recent developments implying warming…","You seem to have a lot of considerations on this issue.\nFirst, the remarks by the certain US Senator are a grave violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, which we strongly reject.\nSecond, there is only one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal representative of the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a universal consensus of the international community.\nThird, we are firmly against any official exchange between the US and Taiwan and any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\". This has been our clear and consistent position. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and act prudently to prevent damages to bilateral relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nAs to whether China will grab the so-called \"diplomatic allies\" of Taiwan, frankly, do we really need to do that? China develops friendly and cooperative relations with all countries based on the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and the one-China principle. In fact, the one-China principle has become a norm of international relations and the trend of the times which the vast majority of countries choose to follow. As such, do you think we need to make additional efforts on that?\nOn your second concern, as we stated repeatedly, we welcome foreign companies to invest and do business in China, but they must comply with Chinese laws and regulations and respect Chinese people's sentiment. Our position is clear-cut. The relevant companies know it very well.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1669120.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1669065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-06-06","Geng Shuang","","It is reported that the US has plans to sell two billion dollars worth of weapons to Taiwan, including tanks and other weaponry. What's the foreign ministry's view on this and how would such an action affect ongoing trade negotiations?","We note the relevant reports and express serious concerns on the moves of the US side. China firmly, consistently and unequivocally opposes US arms sales to Taiwan. We urge the US to fully realize the high degree of sensitivity and severe impact of this issue and honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques. It needs to stop selling arms to or having military ties with Taiwan, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly and avoid serious damage to bilateral relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nRegarding China-US trade frictions and consultations, China has issued two White Papers, offering a full and accurate elaboration on our position. I won't repeat them here, but I'd like to advise the US once again to grasp the situation, return to the right track and meet China halfway as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1670288.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1670229.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-06-12","Geng Shuang","","For some time certain people in the US have been accusing China of taking advantage of the US in trade and economic cooperation, preaching the \"decoupling\" from China. What's your response to this?","\"Decoupling\" is a very dangerous and irresponsible argument produced by a small number of people in the US, who cling to the cold-war mindset and zero-sum game mentality. Such viewpoint runs contrary to the win-win nature of China-US relations, disregards the people's will for friendly exchange and does not conform to the trend of the times for progress and development. It will in no way gain support or succeed.\nSince China and the US established diplomatic ties four decades ago, our relationship has been mutually beneficial and our interests have become highly complementary and deeply interwoven. We are now each other's biggest trading partner and important investment destination. Almost all American big companies do business in China and all American states have cooperation with China. China and the US now have 50 pairs of sister states/provinces and 277 pairs of sister cities. Over 14,000 visits are made by flight across the Pacific every day. The sales revenue of American companies in China topped $700 billion and their profits reached over $50 billion in the year 2017 alone. Before decoupling the two economies, first you need to ask these businesses, provinces, states and people in the two countries whether they agree to it or not.\nAs two biggest economies in the world, both China and the US play important roles in global industrial chain, supply chain and value chain. A forced decoupling will surely disrupt the existing world economic chain, undermine global industrial labour division and lead to chaos in global market, which is the last thing the stakeholders want to see.\nWe advise certain people in the US to reflect upon what they did, abandon ideological prejudices, stop making outdated and biased remarks, and do not try to reverse the wheel of history.\nIt has been proved in the past and present that China and the US, as two major countries, stand to benefit from cooperation and lose from confrontation. Cooperation is the best choice for both sides. We hope that the US will meet China half way to expand cooperation on the basis of mutual benefit and manage differences on the basis of mutual respect, jointly advance the China-US relations featuring coordination, cooperation and stability to bring more benefits to the two peoples and the rest of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1671670.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1671546.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalists, good morning. Welcome to the TAO regular press conference. I am now willing to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","福建厦门卫视记者","The 11th Straits Forum is about to be held in Xiamen. Please introduce the preparations. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently banned and restricted relevant Taiwan individuals and groups from attending the Straits Forum. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The 11th Straits Forum will open in Fujian Province on June 15, with more than 60 events held over a one-week period. The forum's main session will be held in Xiamen City on the morning of June 16. This edition of the forum is jointly organized by more than 80 units and associations from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and preparatory work is currently advancing in an orderly way. The Office of the Organizing Committee of the Straits Forum will hold a press conference in Xiamen on June 14, where everyone can learn more.\nAt present, more than 10,000 members of the public from various counties, cities and sectors in Taiwan have registered to attend the Straits Forum, exceeding the scale of previous editions. This fully demonstrates that the Straits Forum adheres to its positioning of being “civil, grassroots and broadly based,” actively promotes cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and promotes spiritual kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and it has won general recognition and wide welcome from the broad masses of Taiwan's people. The bone-and-blood kinship of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait cannot be severed, and strengthening cross-Strait exchange and cooperation is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides, with a strong and profound foundation of public opinion.\nThe DPP authorities' unreasonable obstruction exposes their fear of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation moving forward in a good way. It cannot affect the successful holding of the Straits Forum. We also advise the DPP authorities not to go against the trend of the times, not to turn back the wheel of history, and not to become a stumbling block to civil exchanges across the Strait or harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots; otherwise, they will only be condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173360.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","中新社记者","Could the spokesperson introduce the latest progress in implementing the \"31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots\" by localities and departments?","Localities and departments continue to implement and advance the “31 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots,” continuously achieving new results. Recently, Fujian Province, in thoroughly implementing General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on Fujian's work toward Taiwan, issued the “Implementation Opinions on Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait.” These opinions propose deepening Fujian-Taiwan industrial integration, raising the level of trade facilitation, carrying out “small four-links” docking and negotiations, creating a livable and workable living environment, creating better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to develop in Fujian, supporting Taiwan compatriots' participation in rural revitalization, and other content. They further implement and refine the provision of equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, serving them as well as mainland residents are served, so as to benefit Taiwan compatriots. In addition, Zigong City in Sichuan Province and Weihai City in Shandong Province have also issued specific implementation opinions on the “31 Measures,” continuing to provide more equal treatment to Taiwan enterprises and compatriots and to share mainland development opportunities with them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173359.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, some members of the U.S. Senate proposed inviting Tsai Ing-wen to deliver a speech to the U.S. Congress. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position on this. Certain individuals on the US side have repeatedly made irresponsible remarks, which seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose them. At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The US side should handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness, and should not send wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.\nAt the same time, we also warn the DPP authorities not to underestimate the mainland's resolve and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Any attempt to rely on foreign backing to throw its weight around and undermine cross-Strait relations will certainly fail, and will only reap the bitter fruit of its own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173356.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Recently, Minister of National Defense and State Councilor Wei Fenghe said at the Shangri-La Dialogue that if anyone dares to split Taiwan from China, the Chinese military will certainly fight at all costs and will resolutely defend national unification at any price. May I ask whether this means the mainland has made preparations for “forceful unification”?","The remarks by State Councilor and Minister of National Defense General Wei Fenghe at the Shangri-La Dialogue clearly expressed our firm position of upholding the reunification of the motherland. The motherland must and will be reunified; this is a historical conclusion of the seventy-year development of cross-Strait relations and an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in the new era. Compatriots on both sides are blood-related brothers and a community of shared destiny. We are willing to make the greatest efforts, with the utmost sincerity, to pursue and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. At the same time, our determination and will to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity are unwavering, and we will absolutely not tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatist forces splitting the country. We reserve the option of taking all necessary measures, which is aimed at external forces’ interference and the separatist activities of a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists, and is by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173357.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","At a recent press conference, Terry Gou said the TAO “manipulates” some Taiwan media to guide Taiwan's regional elections. What comment does the spokesperson have?","This claim is groundless. The common political basis for our exchanges with all Taiwan parties, groups, and people is adherence to the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” We have always refrained from interfering in Taiwan's elections, and we oppose any words or actions that slander and smear the mainland or undermine cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","海峡卫视记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je recently accepted an interview and made a positive statement on cross-Strait relations. What is the spokesperson's comment? What is the current status of preparations for the \"Twin City Forum\"?","We have noted the relevant reports. Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je has taken a positive view of cross-Strait relations and advocated that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” He has stated that both sides should respect the agreements previously signed and the history of their interactions, and on the existing political foundation continue to promote the development of cross-Strait relations and jointly pursue a better future for the peoples on both sides. He has said that as long as it is conducive to enhancing the well-being of both peoples and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, they will make their utmost efforts. We express our appreciation for this.\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, compatriots on both sides are one family, and matters across the Strait are family affairs of compatriots on both sides. As long as people have a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” cross-Strait relations can improve and develop, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be improved and guaranteed. Regarding this year’s arrangements for the “Shanghai-Taipei City Forum,” the Shanghai Municipal Government and the Taipei City Government will communicate with each other.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173358.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, the Hong Kong “amendment of laws” has caused controversy among some Hong Kong residents. The DPP authorities said they oppose it, and Terry Gou proposed that the failure of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong can be seen from the “anti-amendment” movement. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have?","Regarding the demonstration you mentioned and the situation in which some participants stormed the Hong Kong SAR Legislative Council after the demonstration ended, the Hong Kong SAR government has already responded. We have repeatedly emphasized that “one country, two systems” is the best solution to the Hong Kong question and the best system for Hong Kong’s long-term prosperity and stability after its return to China. Since Hong Kong returned to the motherland, it has maintained long-term prosperity and stability; the practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong has achieved world-renowned success, which is an undeniable objective fact. The specific form in which “one country, two systems” is realized in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan’s actual conditions, fully listen to the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities, disregarding facts, reversing right and wrong, deliberately vilifying “one country, two systems,” and undermining the development of cross-Strait relations, have ulterior motives and will ultimately fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Summer vacation is approaching. Under the current cross-Strait situation, has civil cross-Strait exchange been affected? What large-scale cross-Strait exchange activities are scheduled in the near future?","In recent times, the DPP authorities have stepped up efforts to obstruct and restrict normal cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, deliberately provoking and sabotaging cross-Strait exchange activities and creating vicious incidents. But they cannot stop the enthusiasm of people on both sides of the Strait for exchanges. Recently, a series of cross-Strait exchange activities have been successfully held across various localities.\nFor example, the “Second Cross-Strait University Rowing Culture Study Camp” was held in Xi'an, Shaanxi, from April 14 to 22, with 308 teachers and students from 14 universities across both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong and Macao participating. The “Three Good Strait Cup” Cross-Strait Middle School Basketball Invitational Tournament was held in Shanghai from April 27 to May 1. The “Connected by Qilu” Cross-Strait Culture and Tourism Friendship Tour was held in Shandong from May 22 to 29, with about 350 guests from cross-Strait cultural and tourism sectors attending. From May 28 to June 2, the “Ancient Charm, Modern Brilliance: Harmony Across the Strait” Jiangsu-Taiwan Children's Choir Music Gathering was held in Jiangsu Province, with more than 400 primary and middle school students from Jiangsu and Taiwan making friends through song and carrying out rich activities such as choral concerts and campus study-buddy exchanges. From May 18 to 22, the 21st Straits Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Fair was held in Fuzhou, with more than 1,100 Taiwanese business and industry personnel participating. From June 3 to 5, the “Taiwan Businesses Together, Integrating into the Greater Bay Area” theme event was held in Guangdong, with more than 230 Taiwanese business and industry personnel attending, learning in detail about the development plan and related policies of the Greater Bay Area and seeking new business opportunities.\nRegardless of how the situation across the Strait changes, we will continue to advance cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in all civil fields and deepen the integrated development of economies and societies across the Strait. We will also hold a series of exchange activities during the summer. For example, the Chengdu leg of the Third Cross-Strait Student Baseball League will be held in late June, with 24 cross-Strait student baseball teams competing and about 600 participants. This is the first time the league has been held in a mainland city other than Beijing and Shenzhen. In mid-July, the “Youth Bonds Across the Strait—Cross-Strait Youth Visit to Shanghai” event will also be held in Shanghai, with 100 young students majoring in art design and tourism management from both sides of the Strait experiencing in depth the style and essence of Shanghai culture and learning about the development of the mainland's cultural tourism industry. In addition, the Cross-Strait New Kinetic Energy Conversion Summit Forum, the Tianjin-Taiwan Meeting, the Yuntai Meeting, the Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week and others will also be held successively in the near future. We welcome Taiwanese business and industry personnel to participate actively and gain new development opportunities from them. Mainland relevant institutions and enterprises will also carry out summer internship activities for Taiwan youth, creating more opportunities for young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to chase, pursue and realize their dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190612_12173355.htm"],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Recently the Ministry of Public Security, in cooperation with Spanish police, collectively extradited a batch of Taiwan telecom fraud suspects to the mainland. Please explain the relevant situation, spokesperson. In addition, Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council again accused the mainland, saying that the mainland should cooperate with relevant parties in Taiwan to jointly investigate in order to dismantle the…","The relevant Spanish authorities adhere to the one-China principle and properly handle Taiwan-related cases. As is well known, for some time, telecom fraud cases led by Taiwanese criminals have occurred frequently, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait have suffered greatly and deeply resent them. The mainland side resolutely cracks down on all kinds of telecom fraud crimes. In accordance with the position that it is conducive to combating crime, upholding judicial justice, and protecting the rights and interests of victims, it has apprehended cross-border telecom fraud criminals according to law and brought them to justice. This has won high recognition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait and has also gained general understanding and strong support from the international community. Who has disregarded the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides and placed obstacles in the way of jointly fighting cross-Strait crime? I believe justice will be evident in people's hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","After obstructing island students from participating in the “Jade Mountain Program” for youth exchange among Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan launched by the China Association for Science and Technology, the DPP authorities have now begun investigating research personnel working on the mainland. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","The mainland side has consistently and actively worked to create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to share in the mainland's development opportunities and to benefit them. Yet the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have fabricated all kinds of pretexts to keep causing trouble, placing obstacles at every turn, and even wantonly fabricating charges to threaten and intimidate. This stands against Taiwan compatriots, undermines the right of Taiwan people to pursue a better life, and obstructs Taiwan compatriots from realizing greater and better development opportunities of their own, and will only further harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nRecently, the conduct of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities can be described in four sentences: for their own selfish interests, they obstruct cross-Strait exchanges; they cause the decline of all industries; they harm the well-being of the masses. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities now fear most cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields and interactions among the people, because when compatriots on both sides of the Strait come closer, understand each other better, and grow more mutually understanding and affectionate, the lies they deliberately spread to create hostility and hatred between the two sides will collapse of their own accord, and their schemes to manufacture tension and confrontation across the Strait for electoral gain will be exposed and seen through. I think that those with crooked hearts who plot cleverly will in the end only harm themselves, and what they will destroy is not only the Democratic Progressive Party and its authorities, but also the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the future of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","Guangdong recently held an event titled “Taiwan Businesses Come Together, Integrate into the Greater Bay Area.” Regarding Taiwan businesses' wish to actively integrate into the construction of the Greater Bay Area, what positive measures and responses does the mainland have?","At the previous press conference I had already introduced the relevant situation of this event. The “Taiwan Businesses Come Together, Integrate into the Greater Bay Area” theme event was held in Guangdong from June 3 to 5. The purpose of the event is to support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in seizing and sharing the development opportunities of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, deepen integrated development across the Strait, and promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation between the two sides.\nBroad Taiwan businesspeople are pioneers and beneficiaries of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and they will certainly also be participants in and beneficiaries of the construction of the Greater Bay Area. The construction of the Greater Bay Area provides new major opportunities for the transformation, upgrading and sustainable development of Taiwan-invested enterprises. We hope that broad Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises can display the spirit of “daring to be first under heaven” that they showed when they came to the mainland to invest and do business at the beginning of reform and opening up. While achieving better development for themselves, they can share the great glory of the motherland's prosperity and strength, and make new contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","On June 1, the US Department of Defense released a strategy report claiming that it has long been committed to assessing Taiwan's defense needs in order to help Taiwan enhance its survivability. On the same day, at the Shangri-La Dialogue held in Singapore, the US Acting Secretary of Defense said that the US will continue to fulfill its obligations under the “Taiwan Relations Act,” providing Taiwan with the…","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our solemn position regarding the relevant US report. Recently at the Shangri-La Dialogue, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense General Wei Fenghe also issued a stern warning against foreign forces interfering in China's internal affairs and meddling in the Taiwan question. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the US and Taiwan; this position is consistent and clear. We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities once again: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and relying on foreign powers to inflate one's own weight will only bring self-inflicted harm.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","The U.S. Department of Defense recently released its “Indo-Pacific Strategy Report,” listing Taiwan as a “country.” How does the TAO comment on this? In addition, there has been a lot of recent military exchange between the United States and Taiwan. Has this exceeded the bottom line of the one-China principle on the mainland?","There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and Taiwan has never been a country. This fact has never changed and will not be allowed to change. Our position on any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and Taiwan is very clear: we firmly oppose it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","人民日报海外网记者","Solomon Islands media reported that the Solomon Islands Foreign Minister pointed out that within 100 days a decision will be made on whether to sever diplomatic ties with Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. Conforming to this trend of the times is the choice of the vast majority of countries in the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-12","An Fengshan","环球网记者","Media on the island recently reported that the Taiwan military plans to advance the deployment of “Thunderbolt-2000” multiple rocket launchers to Kinmen and Matsu, and claimed that the rocket launchers can carry nerve gas warheads and can strike mainland coastal cities. How does the spokesperson view this?","Pursuing armed confrontation and seeking “independence” through military means has no way out. In particular, deliberately spreading crazy rhetoric about chemical weapons will certainly be condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190612_12173353.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-06-25","Geng Shuang","","The Xinhua News Agency released the readout of Vice Premier Liu He's telephone conversation with USTR Robert Lighthizer. Does that mean China and the US have restarted the trade talks? Can you confirm that President Xi Jinping will meet with President Trump on Saturday? According to reports, the US is suspending its arms sales to Taiwan to avoid escalation of tensions ahead of the two leaders'meeting and…","The Xinhua News Agency released the readout of Vice Premier Liu He's telephone conversation upon invitation with the US side and I have nothing more to add.\nRegarding the upcoming meeting between Chinese and US heads of state at the G20 Osaka Summit, as far as I know, the teams from both sides are in communication on scheduling the meeting. As to the measures related to Taiwan and Hong Kong by the US, I think the US side knows China's position very well. Taiwan and Hong Kong-related issues are China's internal affairs and we firmly oppose US interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1675600.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1675511.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson An Fengshan answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporter friends, good morning! Welcome to everyone attending this morning’s Taiwan Affairs Office regular press conference. I am now willing to answer your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the results achieved at the 11th Straits Forum, which concluded recently. In addition, the DPP authorities distorted, slandered, restricted, and obstructed this forum. What is the spokesperson's comment?","From June 15 to 21, 83 institutions and social organizations from both sides of the Taiwan Strait successfully held the 11th Straits Forum in Fujian. This was a major gathering to expand civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and deepen integrated development under new circumstances. Although the DPP authorities obstructed this forum in every way, as Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee Political Bureau and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, pointed out at the forum's plenary session: the general trend of exchange and integration among the people on both sides cannot be suppressed by any force; the confidence and determination of compatriots on both sides to safeguard national reunification cannot be shaken by any force; the cultural bond of common roots and origins among the people on both sides cannot be severed by any force; and the aspiration of people from all walks of life on both sides to join hands in realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation cannot be blocked by any force. The characteristics and achievements of this forum are mainly reflected in the following aspects:\nFirst, participation reached an unprecedented scale and a broader scope. Taiwan compatriots attending the Straits Forum came from more than 30 sectors, with over 10,000 people, a record high. Of them, 20% were visiting the mainland for the first time, 40% were attending the Straits Forum for the first time, and 51% were grassroots residents from central and southern Taiwan. The number of participants in many events exceeded that of previous forums.\nSecond, the forum focused on youth needs and served youth development. Taiwan youth accounted for more than 50% of the attendees at this forum. Taiwan youth have a strong desire to come to the mainland to exchange and develop their careers, and the diverse activities of this forum responded to their needs. More than 300 Taiwan talents, including 125 holders of doctoral degrees, attended the Landing First Home Forum. The Xiamen talent matching event offered 2,300 jobs to Taiwan youth. Talent institutions on both sides reached more than 80 cooperation intentions.\nThird, cooperation spanned diverse fields, and the results were more abundant. During the forum, a number of investment, trade, industry cooperation, and grassroots exchange agreements were signed. For example, during the Mazu Cultural Week, 15 projects were signed; at the Guan Di Culture Festival, 20 projects were signed on site; the Common Home Forum launched the trial operation of the Pingtan cross-strait agricultural and fishery product trading platform, attracting more than 30 Taiwan businesses and mainland purchasers; the Science and Technology Experts Forum signed 32 cross-strait academic exchange and science and technology cooperation projects; and more than 50 projects on Fujian-Taiwan characteristic towns and townships and integrated development of modern agriculture were matched, with cooperation agreements signed. Discussions on promoting the \"New Four Links\" and the Xiamen-Kinmen \"Small Four Links,\" and Fujian's introduction of policy measures to explore new paths for cross-strait integrated development, were also highlights of this forum.\nFourth, compatriots drew closer together, and their feelings grew warmer. This forum was filled with the fellowship of \"cross-strait families are one family.\" More than 2,000 cross-strait clan members gathered at the Straits Ordinary People's Forum and sang \"We Are All One Family.\" More than 600 Taiwan villagers from villages sharing the same name returned to their ancestral home to pay respects to their ancestors. 200 frontline worker representatives from both sides gathered at the Workers' Forum to exchange skills. Cross-strait college students and families performed classic pieces together on stage, and family representatives from both sides told stories of passing down family traditions.\nThe forum drew wide attention, and its influence multiplied. According to incomplete statistics, online and social media outlets on the island reported on it 1,600 times, with 76,000 comments and nearly 160,000 likes. Online discussion on the island was twice that of the previous forum, attention was ten times that of the same period last year, and video views were 20 times last year's, reaching 3.04 million. Social media users on the island engaged in 3.5 million interactions on the forum's topics.\nThe successful holding of this Straits Forum once again shows that expanding civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and deepening cross-strait integrated development is the shared aspiration of the people on both sides. The DPP authorities are acting against this trend, slandering and smearing, which does not win popular support and is doomed to fail in the end. The great force and historical trend that the people on both sides have gathered to advance cross-strait relations cannot be stopped by any person or any force.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190626_12177774.htm"],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","福建东南卫视记者","Fujian Province is working to build Pingtan into a pilot zone for the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to settle on the mainland. Please introduce the relevant information.","In recent years, Fujian Province and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone have actively taken measures to pioneer cooperation with Taiwan, continuously optimizing the business and living environment. The fast maritime passenger and cargo roll-on/roll-off routes from Pingtan to Taichung and Taipei have played a positive role in facilitating travel between Fujian and Taiwan, and between people on both sides of the Strait. As the level of trade facilitation with Taiwan in Pingtan continues to improve, the barriers and costs for Taiwan-funded enterprises entering the mainland market are also continuing to fall, and development opportunities keep increasing. This has attracted many Taiwan compatriots and young Taiwanese to live, start businesses, and find work in Pingtan.\nOn June 16, the Management Committee of the Fujian Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone issued the “Implementation Rules for Exploring New Paths for Integrated Cross-Strait Development.” The rules propose “36 measures” to build a pioneer zone as the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland. The main contents include: enhancing smooth economic and trade cooperation, advancing infrastructure connectivity, accelerating the connection of energy and resources, and deepening the alignment of industry standards; implementing equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in detail; promoting equalization of public services for Taiwan compatriots; strengthening cross-strait grassroots governance exchange and cooperation; and expanding civil exchange and contact across the Strait. These measures will provide more convenience and better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to achieve greater and better development in Pingtan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190626_12177770.htm"],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","福建海峡卫视记者","What progress has been made in promoting the “small four links” and “all-possible links” between Kinmen and Matsu and the Fujian coast?","At the commemorative event on January 2 this year marking the 40th anniversary of the \"Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,\" General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech stating that relatives wish each other well, Chinese should help Chinese, and across-Strait exchanges should be fully connected (应通尽通). Trade and economic cooperation, infrastructure connectivity, energy and resource exchange, and common industry standards should be promoted, and water, electricity, gas, and bridge links between Kinmen and Matsu and the coastal areas of Fujian can be realized first.\nResidents of Kinmen and Matsu have long hoped that the mainland would help resolve difficulties such as shortages of water and electricity, and have repeatedly expressed their demands for gas and bridge links. Our position is clear: for these needs, the mainland is willing to do everything possible to create opportunities and provide conditions for them to achieve greater and better development. Last August, the Fujian water supply project to Kinmen overcame many difficulties and officially began supplying water. So far, Fujian has steadily supplied Kinmen with more than 3 million tons of water, resolving the water shortage that Kinmen's residents had long faced.\nRegarding the follow-up water, electricity, gas, and bridge links, mainland authorities and Fujian Province have been actively carrying out work. We are doing everything we can to advance these in a pragmatic way, and interim progress has already been achieved. On water supply to Matsu, in 2002, during Matsu's water shortage, Fujian had already set a precedent of emergency water supply by ship. As long as Matsu has demand, we can supply water at any time. On electricity, the head of the State Grid Fujian Company has publicly explained the plan for electricity links between Kinmen, Matsu, and the mainland, and technical preparations are in place to achieve safe, stable, and environmentally friendly power supply. On gas, relevant enterprises on both sides of the Strait have carried out preliminary communication and coordination, and two options, ship-borne gas supply and pipeline gas supply, have preliminarily taken shape. On bridge links, mainland experts and enterprises have conducted in-depth research, and relevant planning is advancing. As long as conditions are in place, enterprises and industry associations on both sides of the Strait can further engage in consultations to accelerate the implementation of projects that bring real benefits to compatriots on both sides.\nWe will continue to fully implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech, adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, further study and introduce new measures, and continuously deepen integrated economic and social development across the Strait. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together, remove obstacles, and realize \"all-round connectivity\" across the Strait as soon as possible, continuously enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190626_12177772.htm"],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","香港中评社记者","“New Power Party” figure Huang Guochang and others recently initiated a so-called “Reject Red Media” march. Cai Yingwen said this would raise vigilance against “mainland infiltration of Taiwan’s media,” and that the authorities would combine legislative and administrative measures with international cooperation to remove so-called “erroneous and false information” from Taiwan society. What is the spokesperson’s…","Both sides of the Strait understand very clearly that when cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good, and only when compatriots on both sides come closer and become more like relatives can cross-Strait relations develop solidly and well. We have been promoting stronger cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides and deepening their kinship ties, which accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides and with the overall interests of the Chinese nation. Over the years, the positive role played by cross-Strait media in this regard is, I believe, plain for all to see. At present, more than 10 mainstream media outlets from each side maintain resident reporters on the other side, and many news reporters travel back and forth across the Strait to conduct interviews and reporting and to carry out news exchanges, opening a very precious window for people on both sides to understand each other.\nThe mainland and Taiwan are close at hand, yet a shallow strait divides us into two sides. Although cross-Strait exchanges have gone on for more than 30 years, very few mainland residents have actually visited the island of Taiwan, and a considerable number of Taiwan residents have never been to the mainland. For them to truly understand the real other side, they cannot do without objective reporting by cross-Strait media. The importance of cross-Strait media and news exchange is self-evident. We call cross-Strait media the bridge and link between the two sides because they can enhance mutual understanding and harmonious kinship among compatriots on both sides. For many years, we have actively encouraged and supported cross-Strait news exchanges.\nThe DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces fear that the two sides will come closer and develop well, and fear that compatriots on both sides will come to know each other and build harmonious kinship, because this would cause the hostile illusions they have deliberately created across the Strait to collapse on their own. Therefore, they want to use means of “tearing down bridges” and “destroying roads” to prevent mutual understanding across the Strait and sever the kinship ties between compatriots on both sides. They regard media that can objectively report on the mainland and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations as thorns in their side, smearing them and labeling them “red,” inciting attacks against them, and now even openly reaching out with black hands to suppress and persecute them, escalating cross-Strait confrontation. Their actions have met with strong opposition and condemnation from people on both sides, and their schemes will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan's “Legislative Yuan” recently passed the so-called “amendment to the National Security Act,” which increases penalties for so-called “spying for the mainland” and incorporates “treason offenses.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities are scheming to create “one side, one country,” deliberately stirring up hostility across the Strait and escalating cross-Strait confrontation. Such conduct will certainly be condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","香港凤凰卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen and some DPP political figures have made various so-called responses to Hong Kong’s law amendments, and Chu Li-luh and Terry Gou have recently also said Taiwan will not take “one country, two systems” as an option. What is your response?","At our last press conference, we had already answered similar questions. We have repeatedly emphasized that “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” fully takes Taiwan's actual situation into account and is the best way to achieve national reunification. The specific form of “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan's actual circumstances, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","台湾东森电视台记者","The Hong Kong “anti-extradition bill” incident has gradually affected Taiwan. The DPP's previously sluggish electoral prospects have improved. How does the mainland view this development?","We do not comment on Taiwan’s elections. Regarding the amendments to the law by the Hong Kong SAR government, the State Council Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, and our office have all already stated our principled position. We firmly oppose anyone who makes irresponsible remarks about Hong Kong affairs or issues false statements. Any scheme to create chaos in Hong Kong and to disrupt and undermine Hong Kong’s prosperity and stability will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Two questions. First, it is reported that the 16th Hubei?Wuhan Taiwan Week is about to be held. Please introduce the relevant situation. Second, the 2019 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held in Shanghai on July 4, and Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je will lead a delegation to attend the forum. Please introduce this.","Your first question: The 16th Hubei?Wuhan Taiwan Week will be held in Hubei from July 8 to 12. Themed “New Era, New Momentum, New Integration,” this Taiwan Week aims to promote economic and social integration between Hubei and Taiwan, let Taiwan compatriots share in Hubei's strategic development opportunities, promote spiritual connection among compatriots, and push forward high-quality development in Hubei in the new era. It will focus on high-tech industries such as electronic information, intelligent manufacturing, biomedicine, and energy conservation and environmental protection, as well as emerging industries such as financial service innovation and cultural and creative industries. It will carry out a series of activities, including economic and trade cooperation, youth exchanges, grassroots interaction, and cultural exchanges. On that occasion, about 800 guests will attend the activities, including well-known figures from all sectors in Taiwan, youth and grassroots representatives, heads of relevant Taiwan organizations, the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and heads of Taiwan associations in various localities, and cross-Strait experts and scholars. Members of the news media are welcome to interview and report on them.\nYour second question: It is understood that, after consultation between Shanghai and Taipei, the “2019 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” will be held in Shanghai on July 4. The “Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” is hosted alternately by the Shanghai and Taipei municipal governments, and has become an important institutionalized exchange platform between the two cities. It has achieved a series of positive results in promoting exchanges and cooperation in all fields between the two cities and in enhancing the livelihood and well-being of residents of both places. We have also repeatedly stressed that as long as there is a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations and cross-Strait city exchanges, cross-Strait city exchanges can progress steadily and go far, show broad prospects, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","北京日报记者","Taiwan's well-known media personality Huang Zhixian was “besieged” by “Taiwan independence” elements after giving a speech supporting cross-strait reunification at the Straits Forum. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council declared that it will collect information and handle the matter according to law. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","The motherland must be and will inevitably be reunified. This is the historical conclusion of the 70-year development of cross-Strait relations, and also an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” fully takes into account Taiwan's realities; it is the best way to achieve national reunification, and it conforms to the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities' wanton suppression and persecution of groups and individuals who oppose “Taiwan independence” and advocate reunification is unpopular, and will inevitably arouse strong indignation among people on both sides of the Strait. We strongly condemn it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","台湾联合报记者","The Solomon Islands expects to send a delegation to visit the mainland in the near future and will also visit Taipei to discuss relations with Taiwan. What is your comment?","The One-China principle is a norm of international relations, a general consensus of the international community, and the only correct choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Experts say that Taiwan residents may serve as arbitrators on the mainland, and that Taiwan businesspeople should better understand this, as it is very helpful for protecting their rights. Please introduce the situation of Taiwan professionals serving as arbitrators at mainland arbitration institutions.","Arbitration, as an important means of resolving civil and commercial disputes, has unique advantages of professionalism, speed and low cost, and is especially advantageous in resolving investment and trade disputes. We have always advocated that Taiwanese businesses protect their own rights and interests through the arbitration mechanism. Since 1998, more than 40 arbitration commissions, including the China International Economic and Trade Arbitration Commission, the China Maritime Arbitration Commission, the Cross-Strait Arbitration Center, and arbitration commissions in Shanghai, Beijing, Guangzhou and Xiamen, have successively appointed nearly 100 Taiwanese arbitrators. Some Taiwanese arbitrators have formally handled arbitration cases. The appointment of Taiwanese professionals as arbitrators by mainland arbitration institutions has played a positive role in protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, improving the investment environment, and promoting exchanges between cross-Strait arbitration institutions and personnel.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190626_12177771.htm"],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","台湾中国时报记者","Yesterday, maiden voyage launch ceremonies were held at Cijin in Kaohsiung and at Dongtou Port in Wenzhou. The organizers said these were launch ceremonies for “mini three links.” The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council called it a political fraud designed to create a false impression of making a fortune across the Strait. What is the TAO's comment?","For some time now, whenever something is beneficial to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, the DPP authorities have always tried every means to obstruct and restrict it, and engaged in political manipulation. Their underlying intent is self-evident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","新华社记者","Public opinion holds that the DPP authorities, by attempting to amend laws to gradually sever cross-Strait ties, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and incite fear and hostility toward the mainland in Taiwan’s society, are engaging in what can be called “Taiwan independence through amending laws.” This causes enormous harm and a grave impact. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","For the narrow private interests of one party, the DPP authorities violate the shared wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, cooperation, and development. They are increasingly obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, as well as dialogue and communication among parties, groups, and individuals on both sides, attempting to place obstacles in the way of compatriots on both sides growing closer and of cross-Strait relations developing steadily and well. When the great Way prevails, people's hearts turn toward it, and it cannot be stopped. Any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme that provokes or creates antagonism between compatriots on both sides is doomed to fail. Compatriots on both sides should join hands with one heart, remove interference, firmly push cross-Strait relations forward through difficulties, and jointly create a bright future for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","中新社记者","For some time, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has, in various ways, obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges, slandered and vilified the mainland, and continuously escalated cross-Strait confrontation, undermining cross-Strait relations. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on this, and how will it respond?","The Mainland Affairs Council is the competent authority for mainland affairs under the Taiwan authorities, and it should rightly help promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. But for some time, the Mainland Affairs Council has arbitrarily denied the “1992 Consensus,” viciously attacked the mainland's political system and development path, restricted and undermined normal civil exchanges across the Strait, maliciously deterred Taiwan residents from participating in cross-strait exchanges, openly interfered in Hong Kong affairs, and willingly served as the “pawn” of anti-China forces, repeatedly provoking trouble and creating cross-strait confrontation. The nature of these actions is extremely bad.\nWe have repeatedly stressed that any attempt to create confrontation, escalate opposition, or incite hostility is futile, and cannot stop the general trend of the development of cross-strait relations. We advise the Mainland Affairs Council to recognize the trend of history, respond to the strong desire of Taiwan compatriots for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, change course, and avoid causing greater shocks to peace in the Taiwan Strait. If it persists in going its own way, it will only put itself in an even more passive position and will ultimately be severely punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201906/t20190626_12177773.htm"],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","中国台湾网记者","It is understood that the “Rongrong & Yunji Taiwan Pavilion” recently went online on mainland e-commerce platforms, attracting attention from cross-Strait netizens. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To meet the needs of compatriots on both sides and better leverage the role of cross-Strait e-commerce platforms, the “Rongrong & Yunji Taiwan Pavilion” launch ceremony, hosted by China Taiwan Network and Rongrong Haohuo and Yunji, was held in Hangzhou on June 20. At present, the “Rongrong & Yunji Taiwan Pavilion” has launched dozens of Taiwan-origin products. Going forward, the quantity, quality, and transaction volume of Taiwan products and services will continue to rise on mainland e-commerce platforms, and “Rongrong” will share more high-quality cross-Strait products and service information with compatriots on both sides.\nThe internet is one of the most direct and convenient channels for bringing compatriots on both sides closer and promoting cross-Strait economic cooperation. Taiwan’s high-quality products and services entering the mainland through e-commerce platforms can help Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland broaden markets and achieve precise connection with consumers; this is an important embodiment of the principle that everything that can be connected should be connected across the Strait. Cooperation between cross-Strait e-commerce enterprises continues to strengthen, which will further leverage the strong complementarity of the two sides’ economies, promote economic integration across the Strait, and deepen integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","团结报记者","There are reports that Tsai Ing-wen plans to visit some Central American countries in July and take the opportunity to transit through the United States. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","We have repeatedly and clearly stated that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. We firmly oppose any attempt to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international arena. Any attempt or conduct that relies on foreign powers to elevate itself and undermine cross-Strait relations will only bring its own bitter consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please spokesperson introduce the relevant activities of Taiwan Day at the World Horticultural Expo on June 29.","According to the overall event plan of the Beijing International Horticultural Exposition, all 31 provinces, municipalities and autonomous regions across the country, as well as Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, will hold theme days. The Taiwan theme day activities will be held on June 29 at the Lawn Theater and Tongxing Plaza in the Beijing Horticultural Expo park, co-hosted by the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, the Taiwan Association, the governments of Taichung, New Taipei, Kaohsiung and other counties and cities, and the Taiwan Area Flower Development Association, among others, mainly including promotion of agricultural specialty products and cultural performances. It is understood that at that time, Linghu Rongda, deputy mayor of Taichung, will lead a Taichung City delegation of 20 people, along with more than 100 Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriot representatives in Beijing, to attend. Media and friends from all walks of life are welcome to attend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-06-26","An Fengshan","人民日报海外网记者","Randall Schriver, U.S. Assistant Secretary of Defense for Indo-Pacific Security Affairs, recently claimed that the United States expects China to interfere in Taiwan's 2020 election, and that the United States will directly help Taiwan strengthen its response capabilities. Some media believe this amounts to openly acknowledging that the United States is intervening in Taiwan's “election.” What is the…","We have always refrained from intervening in Taiwan’s elections, and we oppose any external forces interfering in Taiwan’s elections, and we firmly oppose any words or deeds that frame and smear the mainland. The US side should instead examine its own words and deeds and respond to media questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201906/t20190626_12177800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-06-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US Department of Defense (DOD) released the Indo-Pacific Strategy Report on June 1st. It is the first systematic exposition of the Indo-Pacific strategy by the US DOD. It is worth noting that when the Report talks about China, on the one hand, it directly links the US economic relationship with China with the security precautions against China; on the other hand, it shows that the US is ready to take more…","We have taken note of this report from the US side and we are firmly opposed to its negative contents concerning China. Here, I would like to make three points.\nFirst, no strategy should go against the times. The trend of the world is mighty and overwhelming. Those who follow it will prosper while those who resist will perish. Peace, development and win-win cooperation are the trends of our times. Any strategy that is closed and exclusive, which is against the general trends, is doomed to failure.\nSecond, no strategy should harm the well-being of people all over the world. China upholds that all countries, while seeking their own interests, should also pursue common benefits and jointly build a community of shared future. A strategy would not have international support unless it reflects the aspirations and common interests of people throughout the world. Any strategy that only satisfies the interests of one party will have little support and will hurt the interests of all in the end.\nFinally, no strategy should underscore the confrontation side of relations. Facts have proved that confrontation cannot solve problems while dialogue provides a solution. Some countries have strengthened military presence, hyped up military competition, and promoted military confrontation. These actions will only escalate tensions and undermines world peace.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-06/27/content_4844628.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-06-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, when attending this year’s Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) Summit, President Xi Jinping mentioned that it is our common aspiration to build an Asia where countries enjoy mutual respect and trust. This statement is rarely seen in the previous statements of China’s security outlook. How do you interpret the new statement of China’s security…","On your first question. On June 15, President Xi delivered a speech at the 5th CICA Summit and proposed to build an Asia where countries enjoy mutual respect and trust, and an Asia that is secure and stable, growing and prosperous, open and inclusive, cooperative and creative. This major initiative is in line with the trend of the times, in the interests of relevant countries and reflects the aspirations of the people. It will be an important consensus leading the future development of CICA and play a positive role in promoting regional peace and stability. As to why we initiate the forum of military academy superintendents of CICA member states, I think the forum will help improve exchanges on military doctrine, theory and culture, and enhance understanding and trust. Exchanges of military academies on topics such as military education can help service members, especially young officers, from different member states to build and carry on friendship. We believe the inaugural forum will be a successful one with the joint efforts of all participants and add new impetus to the development of CICA.\nOn your second question, we have also noticed the remarks of relevant officials from the US side. Some people in the US still hold the Cold War mentality. They keep exaggerating the strategic competition between China and the US, and provoking confrontation between the Chinese mainland and Taiwan. We are strongly opposed to that.\nI want to reaffirm that the world is big enough to accommodate the common development and interests of both China and the US. The path of peaceful development is China’s long-term policy, and China is always a contributor to world peace, global development and international order. China has no intention to follow the beaten path of big power seeking hegemony and repeat the big power confrontation in the Cold War period. China has no intention to compete for the alleged world dominance with the US. I want to reaffirm that Taiwan matters on China's core interests and the national bond of the Chinese people. It allows no interference from foreign countries. China will resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe also want to urge some people in the US to have a lucid understanding of the situation, abandon the Cold War mentality, respect the basic facts and come back to senses. We urge them to stop hyping up the strategic competition between China and the US, stop misleading the world, media and themselves, and also stop interfering into China’s domestic affairs. Instead, they should take concrete actions to promote a sound and stable relations between the two countries and the two militaries.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-06/27/content_4844628.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-06-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reports said that the Liaoning aircraft carrier group of the PLA Navy returned to its home port through the Taiwan Strait on June 25th. During this training, the aircraft carrier group sailed close to the Guam. Could you please brief us on the training of the aircraft carrier group? Did the aircraft carrier group approach the Guam?","According to the annual training plan, the Liaoning aircraft carrier group conducted a trans-regional ocean-going maneuver and training in recent days. The purposeistestingthe performance of weapons and equipment and improving the troops’ training level, so as to further enhance the aircraft carrier group’s capabilities to fulfill missions and tasks.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-06/27/content_4844628.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-06-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to media reports from the US, when the Liaoning aircraft carrier group entered the South China Sea on June 18th, a US P-8A anti-submarine patrol aircraft took off from Singapore and followed the Liaoning aircraft carrier group. After that mission, theP-8A also circled around Taiwan. What’s your comment? Second, two Canadian military vessels transited through the Taiwan…","On your first question, we were clear about the moves of the US military aircraft and maintained high alert during the process. We are strongly opposed to the US military’s provocative actions in the Taiwan Strait and the South China Sea.\nOn your second question, we were clear about the transit of Canadian vessels through the Taiwan Strait and monitored the vessels for the whole process.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-06/27/content_4844628.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-07-01","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, Tsai Ing-wen will be transiting the US twice this month for a total of four days, which may be the longest time she has ever spent in the US. Has the Chinese government already complained to the US about this? Is China asking the US not to allow Tsai Ing-wen to transit the US?","China always opposes official interactions between the US and Taiwan. This position is firm, consistent and clear. We urge the US to honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, not allow Tsai to transit and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan to prevent damaging China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China has expressed concerns and lodged stern representations to the US side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1677414.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1677331.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-02","Geng Shuang","","据报道，美国官员称，中国在南海进行了一系列反舰弹道导弹试验。中方能否确认？对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1677771.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2019-07-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to Taiwan media, the program “夜问打权” hosted by well-known Taiwan host Huang Chih-hsien was suspended under pressure from the DPP authorities. What is the spokesperson's view?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 2 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 2nd in response to questions: Taiwan host Huang Zhixian insists that both sides belong to one China, advocates cross-Strait unification, and opposes “Taiwan independence.” In the program “Night Questions, Fight for Power” (夜问打权), she openly promoted this position and stance, which has been broadly affirmed by discerning people on the island. Recently, Ms. Huang has repeatedly been subjected to unreasonable attacks by “Taiwan independence” forces, and the program “Night Questions, Fight for Power” was suspended under pressure from the DPP authorities, which has aroused strong indignation among compatriots on both sides. We strongly condemn the conduct of the DPP authorities.\nMa Xiaoguang made the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201907/t20190702_12179802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-07-03","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday Taiwan announced a one-year extension of its trial program concerning visa-free entry to Taiwan for Russian nationals. I wonder if the Foreign Ministry has any comment on that?","As China's comprehensive strategic partner of coordination, Russia fully understands the sensitive nature of issues relating to Taiwan. We trust the Russian side to properly handle relevant issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1678295.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1678143.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-04","Geng Shuang","","It has been reported that there will be progress in the US government's work plan to sell 66 fighter jets to Taiwan. What's your response?","As we repeatedly stated, China consistently opposes official interactions and military ties between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US to honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop arms sales to and cut its military ties with Taiwan, and prudently and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan to avoid affecting China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1678570.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1678463.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-09","Geng Shuang","","The US State Department has approved a $2.2 billion arms sale package to Taiwan. Has the Chinese government already complained to the US about this?","The US arms sale to Taiwan gravely violates international law and basic norms in international relations, seriously breaches the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, flagrantly interferes in China's domestic affairs and harms China's sovereignty and security interests. China deplores and resolutely opposes it. We have lodged stern representations with the US.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. No one should underestimate the Chinese government and people's will and resolve to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity against foreign interference. We urge the US to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, cancel this arms sale immediately and stop military ties with Taiwan to prevent further damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1679792.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1679787.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-09","Geng Shuang","","How will the US arms sale to Taiwan affect China-US military exchange?","We urge the US to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, cancel this arms sale immediately and stop military ties with Taiwan to prevent further damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nMil-to-mil relations are an important component of bilateral ties. It goes without saying that China-US military relations cannot be free from influence of overall relations. As to the current China-US military ties and their future trajectory, I will refer you to the Ministry of National Defense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1679792.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1679787.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-07-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: according to reports, relevant departments of the DPP authorities recently launched “election inspections,” listing mainland enterprises’ purchases of Taiwan agricultural products as a key target of so-called “search and report,” which has caused doubts and backlash among Taiwan farmers and fishers. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in his answer.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 9 (reporter Zhao Bo) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 9th in response to a question: The DPP authorities’ reckless actions, which are hostile to the interests of the people, will inevitably place them even further in a position of being condemned by thousands, and they will ultimately be abandoned by the Taiwan people.\nHe also pointed out that the sale of agricultural products concerns the vital interests of Taiwan’s broad farming population. Over many years, guided by the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” we have actively helped Taiwan’s farmers expand the mainland market and resolve difficulties in selling agricultural products, which has been warmly welcomed by Taiwan’s broad public. The mainland has already become the largest export market for Taiwan’s agricultural products.\nMa Xiaoguang said that in order to reap electoral gains, the DPP authorities have continually used various means to create hostility across the Strait and undermine cross-Strait relations. Now they have extended their black hand to agricultural procurement, directly harming the interests of Taiwan’s farmers and fishermen. This has provoked strong indignation from Taiwan’s farmers’ associations and fishermen’s associations, and unanimous condemnation from the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201907/t20190709_12182231.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-07-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 9 (reporter Zhao Bo). In response to the U.S. State Department’s recent approval of the sale to Taiwan of weapons and equipment worth a total of about US$2.2 billion, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 9th, saying that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position on this. This U.S. move crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs and seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose it. The U.S. side should immediately revoke the relevant arms sales plan to Taiwan and stop sending serious wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nMa Xiaoguang also said that we once again solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any conduct that relies on foreign powers to elevate its position and escalate confrontation will surely bring disaster upon itself and reap bitter consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201907/t20190709_12182233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-07-11","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On July 9, the US State Department approved a arms sale to Taiwan worth about US$2.22 billion, including M1A2 tanks and “Stinger” air defense missiles, and the US Department of Defense has notified Congress of this. The Chinese military expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. China's position of firm opposition to US arms sales to Taiwan is clear and consistent. The US side's erroneous actions seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué, interfere in China's internal affairs, undermine China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously endanger the development of China-US relations and of military relations between the two militaries, and seriously harm peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair, concerns China's core interests and the national sentiment of the Chinese people, and brooks no foreign interference. China urges the US side to honor its commitments, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately cancel the aforementioned arms sales plan to Taiwan, and halt all forms of US-Taiwan military contacts, so as not to cause further damage to China-US military relations. The Chinese military has the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, and will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2019-07/11/content_4845629.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2019-07-12","Geng Shuang","","Taiwanese \"president\" Tsai Ing-wen is on a two-day visit to the US. What does the foreign ministry think about the visit given the recent arms sale from the US to Taiwan?","I'm afraid I need to correct you on this: we call her the leader of the Taiwan region, and there is no so-called \"president\" in that region.\nRegarding the \"transit\" of the leader of the Taiwan region in the US, we have made clear our solemn position. Here I'd like to emphasize this again. China opposes official exchange between the US and Taiwan. This position is firm and clear. We have made stern representations to the US side.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiques, not allow Tsai Ing-wen's transit and stop the official exchange with Taiwan. It must no longer provide any platform for the separatists to advocate \"Taiwan Independence\". It needs to deal with Taiwan-related issues properly and with caution to avoid damaging China-US relationship and peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.\nAs we stated, China's position on US arms sales to Taiwan is also stern. We urge the US to cancel the arms sales immediately and cut its military ties with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1680717.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1680672.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-07-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 12 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 12th in response to questions about Tsai Ing-wen's “transit” through the United States: Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities, for the narrow private interests of their party and themselves, attempt to use external forces to challenge the one-China principle, seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and seek political gain from it. No force should underestimate our determination and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities disregard the safety and well-being of the Taiwan people, rely on foreign backing to throw their weight around, and willingly serve as chess pieces for external forces interfering in China's internal affairs. They also misjudge the situation and depart from popular sentiment, and they will not escape being repudiated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201907/t20190712_12183368.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","","On Friday evening, you announced that the Chinese government will put sanctions on US companies that sell weapons to Taiwan. Can you give us any more details about that? For example, which companies specifically you will sanction? How the sanctions will work? Is there a timetable?","By selling arms to Taiwan, the US seriously violates international law and the basic norms governing international relations. It breaches the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and undermines China's sovereignty and national security. To safeguard China's national interests, we will impose sanctions on US companies that participate in the above-mentioned arms sale to Taiwan. The Chinese government and Chinese businesses will not engage in cooperation or commercial exchanges with the US companies involved.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","","On China's sanctions on US companies participating in the arms sale to Taiwan, which companies are on the list? When will the sanctions start? Tsai Ing-wen gave some remarks on the \"one country, two systems\" policy and cross-strait relations during her \"transit\" in New York. I wonder what's your comment on that? Yesterday, Financial Times reported that Chief Executive Carrie Lam of Hong Kong expressed her…","How many questions did you ask?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","Journalist","Okay.","On your first question, US arms sales to Taiwan gravely violates international law and basic norms of international relations, seriously breaches the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and undermines China's sovereignty and national security.\nTo uphold China's national interests, we will impose sanctions on US companies participating in the above-mentioned arms sale. The Chinese government and Chinese businesses will not engage in cooperation or commercial exchanges with the US companies involved. I'm afraid I cannot tell you more details at the moment. But I can assure you, we Chinese always keep our word.\nOn your second question, Tsai Ing-wen let loose of much nonsense about cross-strait relations and the \"one country, two systems\" policy. But I will restrain myself here as this is not a diplomatic issue. I refer you to my colleagues in the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council.\nAs a spokesperson of the foreign ministry, I can tell you that the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. The Taiwan authority, wearing a mask of democracy, is seeking pretexts for its so-called \"independence\" agenda by misleading others and reaping sympathies. In fact, its true intention has long been seen through by the world.\nThere is no dignity at all when you are slavishly dependent on others, thinking this may bring you some recognition. It won't bring you anything more than a doomed fate.\nOn your third question, I have not heard of that. I can assure you the central government firmly supports the Hong Kong SAR government and Chief Executive Carrie Lam in administering the region according to law.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","","上周五晚上，中方发布了将对参与售台武器的美国企业实施制裁的消息，你能否进一步介绍有关情况？比如说都有哪些美国公司将受到制裁？中方将如何实施制裁？何时启动制裁？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","","关于中方宣布制裁对台军售的美国企业一事，你能否透露究竟涉及哪些美国企业？何时实施制裁？蔡英文在“过境”美国纽约时就香港“一国两制”和两岸关系发表言论。你对此有何评论？昨天，英国《金融时报》报道称，香港特首林郑月娥曾多次向中央政府要求辞职，但中央政府拒绝了。你能否证实？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-15","Geng Shuang","","三个。\n你下次一个个地问，省得我听乱了。\n记者：好。（笑）\n关于第一个问题，美方向台湾出售武器严重违反国际法和国际关系基本准则，严重违反一个中国原则和中美三个联合公报的规定，损害了中国主权和国家安全。\n为了维护国家利益，中方将对参与售台武器的美国企业实施制裁。中国政府和中国企业将不会同这些美国企业开展合作和商业往来，具体细节目前我不便透露。但请你相信，中国人一向讲求言必信、行必果。\n关于第二个问题，蔡英文在纽约期间，就两岸关系以及“一国两制”大放厥词。但我还是要克制一点，因为这毕竟不是外交问题，我把它留给国台办和港澳办的同事去回应。\n作为外交部发言人，我可以告诉你，一个中国原则是国际普遍共识。台方试图戴上民主的面具，在国际上混淆视听，骗取同情，为自己制造“台独”寻找借口，它的真实面目世人早已看穿。\n另外还要再说一句，挟洋自重、仰人鼻息，有失尊严，也注定是死路一条。\n关于第三个问题，我没听到过你说的这种情况。我能告诉你的是，…","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681206.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201907/t20190715_5417767.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-16","Geng Shuang","","You said yesterday you didn't have any details at present about the sanctions that China is going to put on the US companies which sell weapons to Taiwan. I was wondering if you have further details today, again specifically about which companies might be targeted?","(The spokesperson turned to the journalist who raised the question.) Do you need me to repeat what I said in response to the same question yesterday?\n(The journalist smiled and shook his head.) If you don't, let's just move on.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681503.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1681470.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-17","Geng Shuang","","Czech media reported that China has taken countermeasures against the anti-China actions of the municipal government and mayor of Prague. Can you confirm that and what's your comment?","Recently the municipal government and mayor of Prague have behaved very badly on Taiwan- and Tibet-related issues that concern China's sovereignty and core interests. What they did has severely hurt the sentiments of the Chinese people and undermined the good atmosphere for bilateral relations, in particular sub-national communication and cooperation. This is why the relevant parties and individual in Prague are unwelcome to the Chinese people. We advise the Prague municipal government and certain politician to correct their wrongdoing as soon as possible and not to recklessly damage the overall China-Czech relations. Otherwise, their own interests will be harmed at the end of the day.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1681711.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1681695.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-19","Geng Shuang","","First question, the European Parliament passed a motion on July 18, which asks the Hong Kong SAR government to withdraw the amendment bill and release the arrested protesters. I wonder if you have any comment? Second, some Hong Kong protesters are reportedly seeking sanctuary in the Taiwan region and the US. Leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen said those friends from Hong Kong would be treated in an…","Didn't you ask the first question or something very similar yesterday?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682201.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682125.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-19","Geng Shuang","Journalist","I did mention the US.","Our position is very clear: we firmly oppose interference in Hong Kong affiars and China's internal affairs by any foreign government, organization or individual.\nI'd still refer you to the competent authority for the comments of some people in Taiwan. But since you are so interested in it, there's something more I have to say. I advise some people in Taiwan to not be so hypocritically \"generous\", as they are now in a pitiable plight themselves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682201.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682125.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday an attack took place in Yuen Long Metro Station in Hong Kong. The Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan also condemned the Hong Kong government, saying that specific violent groups in Hong Kong are controlled by Beijing, and that they believe this incident will draw world attention. Do you have any response to that?","Regarding the incident took place in Hong Kong yesterday, both the Office of Hong Kong and Macao Affairs of the State Council and the Liaison Office of the Central People's Government in the Hong Kong SAR made responses to that, which represent the position of the central government. The Hong Kong SAR government also made a statement. I'd refer you to that.\nI'd like to reiterate that the behaviors of some radical protesters have crossed the bottom line of the \"one country, two systems\" principle. This is intolerable. We firmly support the SAR government in taking all necessary measures according to law to ensure the safety of central government institutions in Hong Kong, uphold the rule of law in Hong Kong and punish the criminals. And I'd like to reiterate that we firmly oppose any foreign interference in and any wanton accusations on Hong Kong's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","First question, the CCTV reported yesterday that Chinese enterprises are seeking new purchases of US agricultural products. Is China making good on promises to buy more US agricultural products as the US required? Do you have more details about this, for example, the number of purchases? Second, foreign scholars said that white-clad men \"indiscriminately\" attacked people at the Yuen Long MTR station in Hong Kong…","Regarding your first question, the Xinhua News Agency has released information. There is a line in it that \"our journalists have learned from relevant party\", and I believe it refers to the authoritative department. That press release is very detailed and I don't think I have any more to add. If you are interested in the China-US talks, you may keep following that since the Chinese side will release relevant information in due course.\nAs to the so-called \"attack\" in Hong Kong as you mentioned, our attitude is very clear. We oppose all illegal, violent behaviors and the central government always supports the Hong Kong police in handling relevant situation in accordance with law. This position is consistent.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan's \"Foreign Minister\" Joseph Wu has called for genuine election in Hong Kong while in transit in Denver, the US. Do you have any comments on this?","First of all, I have to correct you that we never recognize the so-called \"foreign minister\" you mentioned. I believe you are fully aware of this and please stop calling him that next time.\nRegarding the absurd remarks on Hong Kong affairs by certain individual in Taiwan, like I just said in my answer to questions from Hong Kong journalists, this is not a diplomatic question and I'm not in the position to answer that.\nI would like to advise certain people in Taiwan to stop grandstanding on hot issues and making irresponsible remarks on Hong Kong affairs. Such tricks are doomed to fail.\nAs to the so-called \"transit\", China's position is also very clear. We firmly oppose any official contact between the US and Taiwan in whatever form. We also stated our stern position against the \"transit\" in the US of the leader of the Taiwan region previously. I won't go into details for that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","是的，都想问。\n首先，日本参议院选举是日本内政，我们不作评论。其次，日本修宪问题也是日本内政，但是由于历史原因，这一问题受到国际社会特别是亚洲邻国高度关注。我们希望日方坚持走和平发展道路，以实际行动取信于亚洲邻国和国际社会。\n至于中日关系，中日互为重要近邻。在前不久刚刚结束的G20大阪峰会期间，两国领导人一致积极评价当前中日关系改善发展的良好势头，认为中日都进入发展的新时代，双方共同利益和共同关切日益增多，两国关系面临新的发展机遇。双方应共同致力于构建契合新时代要求的中日关系。我们希望中日双方能共同为此作出努力。\n问：昨天，香港新界元朗地铁站发生了袭击事件，台湾民进党也谴责港府，称事件凸显香港特定的暴力团体已经受到了北京当局的控制，相信这一事件会引起国际社会的关注。中方对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","第一，央视昨天报道称，中国的企业准备向美方采购新一批农产品。中方是应美方要求来兑现恢复采购农产品的承诺吗？有没有相关资料，诸如采购数量等？第二，有国际学者称昨天香港元朗地铁站发生了袭击事件，有人身穿白色衣服“无差别”地攻击站内市民。对此，国际学者称发生了“恐袭”，台湾民进党也谴责了港府的做法，这一事件引起了国际社会的关注。请问中方有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-22","Geng Shuang","","台湾“外长”吴钊燮在美国丹佛过境期间呼吁香港进行普选。你对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1682558.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1682511.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-07-25","Hua Chunying","","A US warship again sailed through the Taiwan Strait yesterday and today. I wonder if you have any comment?","China closely monitored from start to end the passage of the US warship through the Taiwan Strait. We have expressed concerns to the US side. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive one in China-US relations. We urge the US to observe the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiques and deal with Taiwan-related issues properly and with caution so that they won't undermine China-US relationship and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1683397.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1683377.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-30","Hua Chunying","","First question, when responding to a Hong Kong-related question in the Economic Club of Washington D.C., US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said that protests are appropriate, and that they often see protests in the United States. He hopes the Chinese government will do the right thing and respect the agreements that are in place with respect to Hong Kong. What's your comment? What are the agreements he refers to?…","On your first question, first of all, you mentioned Mr. Pompeo said that they often see protests in the US. I was wondering if he is happy to see those violent radicals using iron batons and lethal weapons to attack the police in the US, too? Maybe it will be a chance for the US to show its democracy? What do you think of that?\nI think Mr. Pompeo obviously failed to put himself in a right position. I'm afraid he still regards himself as the CIA chief. He said the recent violent incidents in Hong Kong are appropriate because, as you all know, they are somehow the work of the US.\nLet us think about what has happened. According to public reports, at the end of February and the beginning of March, the then US Consul-General in Hong Kong blatantly criticized the Hong Kong SAR government's bill amendment and the \"one country, two systems\" principle and interfered in Hong Kong affairs. In March, US Vice President Mike Pence met with Hong Kong opposition lobbyists. In May, Pompeo met with Hong Kong opposition and made irresponsible remarks on the amendment matter. In June, Speaker of the US House of Representatives Nancy Pelosi even called the demonstrations in Hong Kong \"a beautiful sight to behold\". Some members of US Congress once again proposed the Hong Kong Human Rights and Democracy Act. In July, Pence, Pompeo and Bolton met with opposition personnel. In the scenes revealed on media, we saw some American faces among the violent demonstrators in Hong Kong. We even saw the national flag of the US on some occasions. We all have this question: what role has the US played in Hong Kong recently? The US owes the world an explanation.\nThe US has to be clear that we are talking about Hong Kong. It is China's Hong Kong. Like we stressed many times, the Chinese government will never allow any foreign forces to have a hand in Hong Kong affairs. Neither will we allow them to mess up Hong Kong. The central government firmly supports the SAR government in governing Hong Kong in accordance with law and support Hong Kong police in strictly punishing violent criminals to uphold security and stability in Hong Kong. Those who play fire will only get themselves burned. There have been so many lessons in history. We advise the US to immediately stop playing the dangerous game of pulling chestnut out of fire.\nOn your second question, Spokesperson Yang Guang of the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council has made a clear and comprehensive statement on the \"one country, two systems\" principle. I'd like to say this to the relevant persons you mentioned in Taiwan: only through peaceful reunification and the \"one country, two systems\" principle can we have a brighter future. This is what we all believe in.\nI'll leave your third question to the competent authority of the Chinese side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1684560.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1684475.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-31","Hua Chunying","","First question, China's Ministry of Culture and Tourism just released this information. In view of the current cross-strait relations, it decided to suspend the individual travel of residents of 47 mainland cities to Taiwan from August 1. Taiwan media say this is related to Tsai Ing-wen's recent transit in the US and her blatant remarks on the recent protests in Hong Kong. What is your comment on that? Second…","On your first question, Taiwan is part of China, and cross-strait affairs are not diplomatic matters. I'd refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nOn your second question, I don't know which people in Hong Kong think my comments yesterday are double standards. What I said is objective. I make judgments and comments based on facts.\nOn your third question, I have seen relevant reports and twitter. Hmm. How interesting.\nWe all know who has been flip-flopping in the trade talks over the past year or so. In contrast, China's position remains consistent. The Chinese and American negotiating teams are now in Shanghai for trade talks. I'm not aware of the latest information you mentioned. It just doesn't make any sense if the US tries to exert maximum pressure at this particular time. In fact, it's useless to ask others to take pills when the US is ill itself. I believe the US needs to show more sincerity and good faith on this issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685017.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1684951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-31","Hua Chunying","","First, why does the mainland decide to suspend individual trips to Taiwan at this time? Does it have anything to do with the China-US trade talks? Second, the US said it would possibly respond to American companies' requests for supplying Huawei next week. Is China concerned that an unsuccessful round of talks today will affect cooperation between Huawei and American companies?","On your first question, like I said, I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nRegarding your second question, we noted a growing number of American companies recently said they want to supply Huawei. Also, Huawei said on many occasions that they are fully confident in their business. I'm confident, too. It's the US, not China, that gets anxious and concerned now.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685017.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1684951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-07-31","Hua Chunying","","We've seen a recent ban for individual travels to Taiwan. I wonder if you have any comment on that?","Like I said, this is a cross-strait affair. I would refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685017.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1684951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-08-01","Hua Chunying","","The Fijian government recently demanded that the \"trade mission\"of the Taiwan authority to Fiji change its name into \"Taipei Trade Office in Fiji\", asked it to remove the plaque with its original name and took back its diplomatic license plates. Now none of Taiwan's \"missions\" to countries other than its \"diplomatic allies\" have \"the Republic of China\" or \"Taiwan\" in their names. Can you comment on that?","I think the Fijian government has done a very right thing. China highly applauds the Fijian government for dealing with Taiwan-related issues according to the one-China principle. This again proves that following the one-China principle is an internationally popular trend.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685342.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1685306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-08-01","Hua Chunying","","Yesterday several journalists asked you about the travel restrictions on individual mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan. And you referred them to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Could you let us know why those travel restrictions were put in place?","I really appreciate your professionalism and hope I can help you, but I just can't overstep my authority and speak for them. You may still need to ask the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for cross-strait affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685342.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1685306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-08-01","Hua Chunying","","Tsai Ing-wen said that this decision is a strategic mistake. I was wondering whether China has a comment on that?","The history will eventually prove who is on the right side and who has done it wrong.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1685342.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1685306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-08-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 1 — In response to a recent announcement on the official website of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism that, starting August 1, the pilot program for individual travel to Taiwan by mainland residents in 47 cities would be suspended, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 1st, saying that the pilot program for individual travel to Taiwan by mainland residents was launched in 2011. It is a positive measure to expand personnel exchanges across the Strait against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Over the years, travel to Taiwan by mainland residents has had a positive effect in promoting Taiwan’s tourism and related industries. The DPP authorities have continuously advanced “Taiwan independence” activities, constantly incited hostility toward the mainland, and stirred up cross-Strait confrontation, seriously undermining the foundation and conditions for the pilot program for individual travel to Taiwan by mainland residents.\nMa Xiaoguang said that he believes compatriots on both sides of the Strait all hope that cross-Strait relations will soon return to the correct track of peaceful development, and that travel to Taiwan by mainland residents can resume normal and healthy development as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190801_12189164.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-08-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 13 (reporter Zha Wenye): In response to questions about remarks on Hong Kong made by DPP Chairman Cho Jung-tai on the 12th, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 13th: Cho Jung-tai’s latest outburst is an attempt to fan the flames of Hong Kong’s recent situation and stir up chaos in Hong Kong; his attempts to slander and attack the mainland, vilify “one country, two systems,” and incite populism on the island to seek electoral gains will all fail.\nMa Xiaoguang said the situation in Hong Kong has recently been complex and grave, and the DPP and its authorities have played an extremely disgraceful role in it. We must warn the DPP and its authorities to immediately withdraw their black hands reaching into Hong Kong, or they will surely reap the consequences.\nMa Xiaoguang said that, with the firm support of the central government, the Hong Kong SAR government and all sectors of society are fully capable of stopping violence, restoring order, and maintaining Hong Kong’s long-term prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190814_12192374.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-08-19","Geng Shuang","","The US said on Sunday that the government had approved a proposed deal to sell $8 billion worth of F-16V fighter jets to Taiwan. They would officially notify the congress of the deal. I wonder if China has any comment on that?","We've seen relevant media reports. China has recently made solemn representations with the US on the planned sales of F-16V fighter jets to Taiwan on many occasions. I shall stress once again that the US arms sales to Taiwan severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués especially the August 17 Communiqué. They constitute severe interference in China's internal affairs and undermine China's sovereignty and security interests. China firmly opposes that.\nI must stress that the Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. China has a firm resolve to uphold its sovereignty and security. China urges the US to fully recognize the highly harmful nature of the arms sales to Taiwan, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, immediately cancel the planned arms sales, and stop selling weapons and military contact with Taiwan. Otherwise, the US will have to bear all the consequences. China will take necessary measures to safeguard its interests in accordance with the development of the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1689960.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1689910.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-08-19","Geng Shuang","","据报道，美方8月18日向媒体表示，美行政当局已批准向台湾出售价值80亿美元的一批F-16V战机。美方将就此正式通知美国国会。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1689960.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1689910.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2019-08-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 19 (reporter Zha Wenye) — In response to a DPP statement saying that Tsai Ing-wen and relevant units had ordered that certain Hong Kong residents be given “individual assistance” to travel to Taiwan by way of “humanitarian rescue,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th in response to questions: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to stop undermining the rule of law in the Hong Kong SAR, stop interfering in Hong Kong affairs, and not tolerate lawbreakers in any way.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, disregarding facts and reversing right and wrong, are not only covering up the crimes of a small number of violent radicals in Hong Kong and fueling their arrogance as they harm Hong Kong, but also openly claim to provide them sanctuary, making Taiwan a “safe haven for fugitives.” Where does this leave the safety and welfare of the people of Taiwan? No one is above the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190819_12194068.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-08-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 19 — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded on the 19th to the matter of the U.S. plan to sell F-16V fighter jets to Taiwan, saying that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side. This U.S. move brutally interferes in China's internal affairs and seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously damaging China-U.S. relations, cross-Strait relations, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose it. The U.S. side should immediately cancel the relevant arms sales plan and stop sending serious wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. No force should underestimate our determination and ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nMa Xiaoguang said that Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities, who harm the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, have not hesitated to act as the U.S.'s “pawn” and pay a hefty “protection fee” to the United States. In the end, they will only become “discarded pawns” and be nailed forever to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190819_12194223.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-08-21","Geng Shuang","","On August 21 Beijing time, the US Department of Defense officially notified the Congress that it's going to sell $8 billion worth of 66 F-16 fighter jets and provide relevant equipment and support to Taiwan. What's your comment?","I already made clear the Chinese government's solemn position on this matter the other day. Our position remains unchanged.\nThe US arms sales to Taiwan severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués especially the August 17 Communiqué. They constitute severe interference in China's internal affairs and undermine China's sovereignty and security interests. China firmly opposes that and has lodged serious representations and protests to the US side. China will take every necessary measure to safeguard its interests, including sanctioning American companies involved in the arms sale this time.\nI must point out that the Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. China has a firm resolve to uphold its sovereignty, unity and security. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, immediately cancel the planned arms sales, and stop selling weapons to and cut its military contact with Taiwan. Otherwise, the US will have to bear all the consequences.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1690680.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1690592.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-08-21","Geng Shuang","","People say that China is facing a lot of pressure or bargaining chips that America uses on China, from the Hong Kong protests to the Taiwan arms sales and even the Huawei issue. On top of that is the economic pain that the tariffs are causing to China, from the slowest economic growth in 27 years, to what Trump says \"millions of jobs having been lost and thousands of factories relocating out of China\". We all…","As I said earlier, the China-US relationship is one of the most important bilateral relationships in the world. A healthy and stable China-US relationship not only serves the interests of both countries, but also meets the aspiration of the international community. We hope the US will work with China to meet each other halfway and act on our presidents' consensus to advance a relationship featuring coordination, cooperation and stability.\nAt the same time, we also hope the US could view China's development fairly and deepen cooperation with China. We hope it will cast aside the Cold-War and zero-sum game mentality. If the US remains entrenched in the outdated mentality, I am afraid China-US relations will continue to hit some bumps in the road from time to time.\nThe past four decades of China-US diplomatic relations offer this important inspiration: our two countries could see beyond ideological differences and form partnerships that benefit the people of our two countries and beyond. We do hope the US could see this point.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1690680.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1690592.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-08-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 21: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 21st to the passing of Mr. Yang Liyu, retired honorary professor at Xidong University (西东大学) in the United States, saying: Mr. Yang Liyu devoted his life to cross-Strait relations and advocated the peaceful reunification of the country unswervingly. He worked tirelessly to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, opposed the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence,” and did not fear slander. We deeply mourn Mr. Yang's passing. Though he is gone, his spirit endures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190821_12195034.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-08-22","Geng Shuang","","Western officials have told the Wall Street Journal they are concerned thatcounter-demonstrations overseas being held against violent activities in Hong Kong, including in the UK and Australia, may have been organized or encouraged by China's local diplomatic missions. Do you have a comment?","I guess you weren't here the other day? I already gave my answer. Do you need me to repeat that for you?\nYou may note that recently in some foreign cities, overseas Chinese, including Chinese students, have taken to the street to express their aspiration and appeal in support of the motherland's national unity and upholding prosperity and stability in Hong Kong.\nFirst, it is totally understandable and reasonable for Chinese students and other Chinese citizens overseas to express indignation and opposition against such words and deeds that attempt to separate China and smear its image.\nSecond, we also hope overseas Chinese can express their patriotism in a rational way and protect themselves from harm.\nThird, the Chinese government asks overseas Chinese to observe local laws and regulations. In the meantime, we hope relevant countries can understand and respect their legal activities and protect their lawful rights and interests.\nIn addition, you said these activities were organized by Chinese diplomatic missions overseas. But I can tell you clearly that the biggest appeal of the 1.4 Chinese people, including the Hong Kong compatriots, is to stop violence, end the chaos and restore order and their biggest aspiration is to uphold Hong Kong's prosperity and stability. This is the common will of the 1.4 billion Chinese. Do you think it is something that can be organized or manipulated?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1691074.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1691020.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-08-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 22 (reporter Zhao Bo): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded again on the 22nd to the U.S. sale of F-16V fighter jets to Taiwan: The United States, disregarding China’s strong opposition, insists on arms sales to Taiwan, brutally interferes in China’s internal affairs, arbitrarily violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously damages China-U.S. relations, and openly undermines cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We once again urge the United States to immediately stop arms sales to Taiwan and immediately stop supporting the vicious acts of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, disregarding the well-being and interests of Taiwan compatriots and their lives, have sold themselves out and submitted to outside powers, shamelessly, and insist on driving the 23 million people of Taiwan onto a road of no return. They will surely face the punishment of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201908/t20190822_12195391.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-08-23","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On August 18, US President Trump, responding to a media question, said he had approved an arms sale to Taiwan worth US$8 billion for F-16V fighter jets. The Chinese military expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged solemn representations and protests with the US side.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. The US arms sales to Taiwan seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously interfere in China's internal affairs, seriously undermine China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously endanger the development of China-US relations and of military relations between the two militaries, and seriously harm peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. They are completely wrong and also very dangerous.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and brooks no foreign interference. No scheme to split China can succeed, and any underestimation of the resolve and will of the Chinese military is extremely dangerous. China requests that the US side fully recognize the grave harm of the issue of arms sales to Taiwan, see the situation clearly, immediately cancel the above arms sales plan to Taiwan, and immediately halt US-Taiwan military contacts, so as not to cause serious damage to China-US military relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese military has the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, to firmly defend national sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity, and to firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2019-08/23/content_4848818.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2019-08-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On August 20, the U.S. Department of State announced the approval of selling 66 F-16V fighters worth $8 billion to Taiwan, and the Ministry of National Defense has also responded to this. What impact will Taiwan’s introduction of such advanced fighter planes have on the military strength of the two sides across the Taiwan Strait?","We have issued a statement on this matter. We know that the “One-China\" Principle is the political foundation of China-US relations, and the United States have made a solemn commitment to China on the Taiwan question. However, it is a regret that the United States has been trying to contain China with Taiwan, repeatedly violating the “One-China\" Principle and the three Joint Communiques of China and the United States. It has neither international credibility nor justice to speak of. We must point out that the sale of arms by the United States to Taiwan will not change the irreversible trend of China’s reunification, nor the comparison of strength of the two sides across the Strait. It will only send a wrong signal to the Taiwan “independence forces” and bring danger to the Taiwan Strait.\nWe have the staunch will, full confidence and capacity to defeat any form of external interference and separatist activities of Taiwan “independence forces”. We will take all necessary measures to safeguard our own interests, and will firmly safeguard the sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity of our country and the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait at all costs. All the consequences of US arms sales to Taiwan should be borne by the US side.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-08/29/content_4849335.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-08-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lately, China has twice said it will impose sanctions on the US companies involved in arms sales to Taiwan. There are those who argue that the US companies involved have only limited cooperation with China, thus the sanctions might only have limited effectiveness. What’s your comment on that? Could you please brief us on the details of the sanctions for the next step?","The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and brooks no external interference. Any attempt to divide China is unlikely to succeed, and any underestimation of the determination and will of the Chinese military is extremely dangerous. The Chinese side urges the US side to fully realize the serious harm caused by the US arms sales to Taiwan, understand the situation clearly, immediately cancel the above-mentioned arms sales plan to Taiwan and stop its military contacts with Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to China-US military relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan straits.\nWhat needs to be stressed is that we will take all necessary measures to maintain our own interests, firmly safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity at all costs, and firmly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan straits.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-08/29/content_4849335.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-09-02","Geng Shuang","","The Solomon Islands government is expected to reach a decision this week about establishing diplomatic ties with Beijing and cutting its ties with Taiwan. Can you give us any details you may have of the Chinese government's meetings with representatives from the Solomon Islands? And when you might expect a decision to be made as to when China and the Solomon Islands would establish diplomatic relations?","As is known to all, there is but one China in the world. The Chinese government stands ready to develop friendly and cooperative relations with countries around the globe on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1693811.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1693739.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 3 (reporter Shi Longhong): In response to Taiwan media reports that the MAC recently preliminarily determined that certain Taiwan groups' participation in the cross-Strait youth “financial services exchange” activities was illegal, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to a question on the 3rd, pointed out that with the economic and social development of the mainland, more and more Taiwan youth hope to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams. To help Taiwan youth realize their life dreams, all sectors on the mainland are actively working out ways to create better conditions and provide more convenience for Taiwan youth to intern, find employment, and start businesses and innovate on the mainland. This is doing good deeds and practical work for Taiwan youth.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, however, have fabricated all kinds of excuses to keep obstructing, setting up barriers everywhere, and even threatening and intimidating, creating a “green terror,” which seriously harms the vital interests of Taiwan youth. This approach is unpopular and is destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190903_12198592.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-05","Geng Shuang","","The Solomon Islands government was considering whether to establish relations with China or maintain relations with Taiwan. It has decided that the country will establish diplomatic relations with China. So have the two sides decided to establish diplomatic relations?","As is known to all, there is but one China in the world. The Chinese government stands ready to develop friendly and cooperative relations with countries around the world on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1694950.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1694892.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-06","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan has warned the Solomon Islands that it should not switch its diplomatic ties to China because if it did so, it risks a debt trap by relying on China. I wonder if you have a response to that?","I responded to similar questions these two days repeatedly. Let me reiterate that there is but one China in the world. The Chinese government stands ready to develop friendly and cooperative relations with countries around the world on the basis of the one-China principle.\nAs to this nonsense of certain individual or department in Taiwan, I would advise you to ask the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for comments.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1695338.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1695288.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-10","Hua Chunying","","The Solomon Islands' foreign minister is currently in Taiwan. In a press conference in Taipei yesterday, he said everything was normal in the relations between Solomon Islands and Taiwan. Has China invited the Solomon Islands' foreign minister to visit Beijing? Does China have a timetable for when China and the Solomon Islands may establish diplomatic relations?","As is known to you all, there is only one China. The one-China principle is an international consensus and an overwhelmingly supported historical trend. The correct choice is to follow this trend, which has already been done by most of the countries. China is ready to develop friendship and cooperation with all countries following the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1696514.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1696371.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-10","Hua Chunying","","所罗门群岛外长正在台湾访问。昨天他在台北举行记者会时称，所罗门群岛与台湾的关系一切正常。请问中方是否邀请所外长来京访问？关于中所建交事宜，中方是否有时间表？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1696514.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1696371.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-09-11","Hua Chunying","","Yesterday a Canadian warship sailed through the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any response to that?","We are well aware of this. The Chinese side does not oppose normal passage by foreign military vessels through the Taiwan Strait. But why did the Canadian side deliberately make a high-profile announcement of it? We hope the Canadian side will demonstrate respect for China's sovereignty and security through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1696968.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1696903.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning! It is very pleasant to meet you all again today. I will host this press conference. Now I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Spokesperson, in recent period, what new progress have the mainland's localities and departments made in advancing the implementation of the “31 Measures”?","Recently, departments at all levels have continued to implement the “31 Measures,” steadily producing new results. So far, 99 localities, including 28 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, have issued specific implementation opinions in light of local conditions. Jilin Province has issued 36 implementing measures, and Chengdu in Sichuan Province has issued 54 implementation opinions. Beijing and other places have also published implementing rules that explain in detail the application requirements, handling procedures, responsible units, and contact telephone numbers for each measure, providing more convenience for compatriots in Taiwan to benefit from the relevant measures.\nIn cross-strait credit reporting cooperation, Fujian Pinshang Credit Co., Ltd. signed a comprehensive strategic cooperation agreement with the Chinese Credit Reporting Agency of Taiwan, further advancing the integration of civil credit reporting across the Taiwan Strait.\nIn promoting academic exchange and mutual learning between the two sides of the Strait, on July 11, the Center for Chinese Social Science Evaluation of Nanjing University announced that 30 academic journals in the humanities and social sciences from Taiwan, covering 15 disciplines, have been included in the source journal catalogue of the Chinese Social Sciences Citation Index database. This will create favorable conditions for incorporating the academic achievements of Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland into the work evaluation system.\nIn promoting cross-strait cultural and artistic exchange, preliminary statistics show that the National Art Fund has received 12 applications for cooperative projects with institutions or units in the Taiwan region, and 19 artists from Taiwan have applied for the Young Artist Creative Talent Program. On August 19, the “China Impressions—China World Heritage Cultural and Creative Design Products Exhibition,” jointly organized by the Chinese Culture Promotion Association and multiple parties including design companies from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, opened at the Chinese Cultural Center in Seoul. The exhibition was curated by a team from Taiwan and gathered more than 120 sets of Chinese intangible cultural heritage cultural and creative products, including ceramic tea sets, stationery and home décor, designed and made by artists from both sides of the Strait, reflecting the rich results of the joint efforts of both sides to inherit and promote Chinese culture.\nIn making life and residence more convenient for Taiwan compatriots, the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office launched a special public rental housing allocation program for Taiwan compatriots in Beijing, with 40 housing units raised in the first batch.\nGoing forward, we will continue, together with relevant departments and localities, to ensure the sustained implementation of the “31 Measures,” promptly coordinate the resolution of issues of common concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, and provide more convenience and better conditions for their development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200831.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the recent situation of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and exchanges in other fields. What are your expectations for the various cross-Strait exchange activities in the second half of the year?","Strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is conducive to deepening mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, fostering kinship, and is in line with the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Although the DPP authorities have obstructed in every way, they cannot stop Taiwan compatriots' enthusiasm for participating in cross-Strait exchanges and sharing the development opportunities of the mainland. Since the beginning of this year, the number of Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland has continued to grow steadily. Especially after entering the summer vacation, cross-Strait exchanges have also entered their peak season. Hebei, Beijing, Shandong, Henan and other provinces and municipalities have successfully held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities, and reached a number of cross-Strait economic cooperation projects. The \"Strait Cup\" 2019 Basketball Invitational Tournament, hosted by the Taipei City Sports Bureau, the Shanghai Municipal Sports Bureau and others, kicked off in Taipei, with more than 1,000 young players competing fiercely in men's and women's divisions for universities, senior high schools and junior high schools. From August 25 to 30, the 3rd Cross-Strait Student Baseball League was held in Taichung and Changhua, with more than 600 athletes from 23 cross-Strait university baseball teams competing. On August 28, the 2019 Cross-Strait Bagua Boxing Skills Exchange Conference opened in Dezhou, Shandong, with more than 800 Bagua boxing masters from both sides of the Strait making friends through martial arts and jointly promoting traditional Chinese culture.\nNext, Zhejiang, Guizhou, Sichuan, Guangxi, Chongqing and other provinces and regions will successively hold cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. On September 17, the 2019 Zhejiang-Taiwan Cooperation Week, themed \"Sharing Opportunities, Integrated Development,\" will open in Hangzhou, and more than 50 economic and trade events will be held in Hangzhou, Ningbo, Wenzhou, Jiaxing and other cities to promote industrial matching and cooperation between Zhejiang and Taiwan. In the second half of this year, many provinces and regions will also hold a series of diverse and lively cross-Strait exchange activities in sports, youth, culture, folk beliefs and other fields. This fully shows that the mainstream public will of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for exchanges and cooperation cannot be stopped by anyone or any force.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","We have noted that, regarding the recent situation in Hong Kong, Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities have constantly interfered. They not only attack the mainland and vilify “one country, two systems,” but also openly invite the ringleaders of the chaos in Hong Kong to visit Taiwan and provide shelter for violent radicals. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have pointed out many times that the DPP authorities have played a most inglorious role in the recent Hong Kong situation. They have fanned the flames and added fuel to the fire, colluding with “Hong Kong independence” forces in an attempt to create chaos in Hong Kong and undermine “one country, two systems.” They keep seizing opportunities to attack and slander the mainland, stir up populism on the island, create an anti-China and China-fearing atmosphere, and seek electoral gains. Recently, they have even disregarded the security and welfare of Taiwan's residents by openly inviting “Hong Kong independence” elements to visit Taiwan and providing sanctuary to violent radicals, making Taiwan a “safe haven for fugitives” and opening the door to bringing disaster and chaos to Taiwan.\nWe once again solemnly warn the DPP authorities: immediately withdraw the black hand reaching out toward Hong Kong, stop interfering in Hong Kong affairs, stop condoning and sheltering violent radicals, and stop acts that undermine cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200833.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The Taiwan legislature will push forward the so-called “amendment on Chinese Communist Party agents,” which, in the name of endangering security, would strictly restrict Taiwan individuals and institutions from making propaganda for the mainland, issuing relevant statements, or attending conferences held on the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","For some time now, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces, for the sake of their own party and personal interests, have comprehensively incited cross-Strait confrontation, manufactured hostility across the Strait, and spared no effort in attacking parties, groups, and individuals holding different positions. They have intimidated and punished Taiwan residents who participate in cross-Strait exchanges on the basis of fabricated charges and restrained critical public opinion, creating a \"green terror\" and a \"chilling effect,\" which have triggered strong skepticism and widespread opposition in public opinion on the island.\nRather than reflect on themselves, they misjudge the situation and go further, once again attempting to revise the relevant regulations, further exposing their \"Taiwan independence\" nature. We note that public opinion on the island calls this the \"new martial law act,\" which pinpoints the crux of the problem. If their scheme succeeds, cross-Strait relations will regress to the era of martial law on Taiwan, and the situation in the Taiwan Strait will once again fall into tension and turmoil. The basic rights of Taiwan residents will be stripped away, and they will once again live in fear, where any misstep brings punishment. So, who is seriously threatening the \"free and democratic way of life\" of Taiwan residents? The answer is clear.\nThose who play with fire will perish by it. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that they must rein in the cliff's edge.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200834.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Which Taiwan guests have been invited to attend the celebrations of the 70th anniversary of National Day? The Mainland Affairs Council recently called on Taiwan residents not to travel to the mainland to take part in National Day-related activities, and stated that if public or military personnel engage in so-called improper conduct on the mainland, they will be punished. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China. We will hold a series of celebratory events, and at that time we will invite representatives of compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, and overseas Chinese, to join in the grand occasion. Compatriots from Taiwan are part of the Chinese nation and certainly cannot be absent from the process of the Chinese nation's march toward great rejuvenation. The DPP authorities' suppression of cross-Strait exchange activities cannot stop the historical trend of compatriots on both sides of the Strait working hand in hand and in unity to realize the Chinese Dream together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200832.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The New Party recently published its “One Country, Two Systems Plan for Taiwan” at a party anniversary event. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Since its founding 26 years ago, the New Party has consistently advocated peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait, firmly supports the One-China principle, and opposes “Taiwan independence,” which we highly appreciate. We are willing to hold dialogue and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and individuals, including the New Party, that adhere to the One-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence,” on issues concerning the advancement of the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200830.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","As the new high school semester began in Taiwan, the history textbooks compiled according to the “new curriculum guidelines” of the education department of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities officially went into use. Some public opinion on the island holds that this “new curriculum guideline” is “de-Sinicizing” at every turn and is a manifestation of “Taiwan independence” in the field of education. What…","Since the DPP authorities came to power, they have continuously advanced all kinds of “Taiwan independence” activities. This time, they have introduced a new curriculum outline filled with “de-Sinicization” and “Taiwan independence” content. This not only poisons the younger generation in Taiwan, but further undermines cross-Strait relations and aggravates cross-Strait confrontation.\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides belong to the Chinese nation. No one can deprive Taiwan compatriots of their rights as children of China. Any act of “de-Sinicization” cannot sever the historical ties across the Strait and cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities, acting contrary to the trend and forgetting their ancestry, have already met strong opposition from Taiwan society and will continue to meet even stronger containment and blows from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200828.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Two questions. First, Mr. Wang Jinping, former chairman of the Taiwan China Unification League and former chairman of the China Foundation, passed away on the 7th of this month. What is the spokesperson's assessment of Mr. Wang Jinping's role in the development of cross-Strait relations? Second, after the announcement that the mainland would this year suspend mainland films and personnel from participating in the…","Mr. Wang Jinping, former chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Unification League, passed away on September 7, 2019 after medical treatment failed.\nMr. Wang Jinping was a loyal patriot, an outstanding representative of Taiwan compatriots, and an outstanding leader, educator, and social activist in the patriotic unification camp of Taiwan compatriots. He unwaveringly pushed for the reunification of the motherland, firmly opposed “Taiwan independence,” firmly opposed foreign forces’ interference in China’s internal affairs, actively pursued social progress, fairness, and justice, and devoted tremendous effort to the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation. The Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office express deep mourning at his passing.\nSecond question: The DPP authorities have continually created incidents that undermine cross-Strait relations, and some Taiwan political forces have used cross-Strait exchange activities to make “Taiwan independence” remarks, undermining cross-Strait exchanges. The mainland film industry has suspended participation in the 2019 Golden Horse Film Festival. The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces cannot escape blame for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台海峡两岸记者","The head of Taiwan’s economic department said the direct impact of the China–U.S. trade friction on Taiwan is very limited, and that investment returning to Taiwan this year will exceed NT$800 billion. What is your evaluation?","Compared with the direct experience of broad Taiwan compatriots regarding the economy, livelihoods and actual life, will people believe the so-called \"reflux\" figures released by the DPP authorities?\nOver the years, Taiwan businesses in the Mainland have achieved very good development, which has also made important contributions to the well-being of compatriots on the island. At present, Taiwan businesses' operations in the Mainland are generally stable, and investment continues to increase. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from January to July this year, the Mainland approved a total of 3,078 Taiwan-invested projects (excluding those via third places), a year-on-year increase of 21.3%, and actually used 1.22 billion US dollars of Taiwan capital, a year-on-year increase of 49.1%.\nI want to further point out that in the first half of this year, amid a complex world economic environment, the Mainland's GDP grew 6.3% year on year. The economy operated generally steadily, making progress while maintaining stability, and continued to maintain its long-term positive fundamentals. The Mainland has a complete industrial system, complete infrastructure, abundant financial capital, and strong industrial and supply chains. The output of more than 200 major industrial products ranks first in the world, and this year it is also expected to become the world's largest consumer goods retail market. With the continuous growth of the Mainland's economic scale, the continuous optimization of its economic structure, and the continuous emergence of new demands, we believe this will bring greater development space to Taiwan businesses and compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190911_12200829.htm"],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Lin Shu-hao, the American basketball player of Chinese descent whose parents are from Taiwan and who has drawn the attention of fans on both sides of the Strait, recently signed with the Beijing Shougang club and will take part in the Chinese Men's Basketball Professional League. May I ask the spokesperson for views on this?","Lin Shu-hao, the player of Chinese-American descent, is deeply loved by fans on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We welcome him to come to Beijing to play basketball.\nIn recent years, the Chinese Basketball Association has specifically introduced relevant policies to create opportunities for Taiwan players to participate in professional leagues on the mainland. According to our understanding, seven players from the Taiwan region have been registered for the new CBA season. We welcome more Taiwan athletes to develop on the mainland in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾旺报记者","Terry Gou recently said, during a tea gathering with Japanese media, that the two sides of the Strait are “two independent political entities.” What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? In addition, the Shanghai Stock Exchange recently adjusted the Shanghai-Hong Kong Stock Connect list, and FIH, a subsidiary under Hon Hai (Foxconn), was removed. What is the spokesperson's view?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan and the mainland both belong to one China, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will not be allowed to be divided. This is a basic legal fact and a reality recognized by the international community. On the question of improving and developing cross-Strait relations, adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and opposing “Taiwan independence,” cross-Strait relations will improve and develop, and the interests of compatriots on both sides will be safeguarded and enhanced. Conversely, cross-Strait relations will be damaged, the situation in the Taiwan Strait will become turbulent, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be harmed.\nOn the second question, according to information from the relevant business departments, Foxconn (富智康) was removed by Hang Seng Indexes Company from the Hang Seng Composite Large and Mid Cap Index. Under the relevant rules of the Shanghai-Hong Kong Stock Connect, the stock was accordingly removed from the Stock Connect list as well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","A professor at Academia Sinica in Taiwan holds a position at Renmin University of China, and was asked to resign after the Mainland Affairs Council said he violated the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area.” What impact will this have on Taiwan teachers coming to the mainland to teach?","In recent times, everyone has seen very clearly that the DPP authorities, disregarding the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides for the development of cross-Strait relations, have increasingly interfered with cross-Strait exchange activities and restricted Taiwan residents from studying, working, seeking employment, and starting businesses on the mainland. They restrict Taiwan university students from interning on the mainland, restrict retired senior officials, retired generals, and primary and secondary school teachers in Taiwan from exchanges on the mainland, penalize Taiwan university teachers and research institute scholars who teach on the mainland, and penalize young Taiwanese who served as assistant community directors in Xiamen. Such examples are numerous. A single falling leaf reveals autumn; if these actions are allowed to continue, I fear that Taiwan compatriots will live in days in which they cannot be free from fear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Following the suspension of individual travel to Taiwan, will group travel to Taiwan also be restricted?","The DPP authorities keep stirring up “Taiwan independence” activities, continually inciting hostility toward the Mainland, provoking cross-Strait confrontation, worsening the atmosphere of cross-Strait exchanges, and hurting the feelings of Mainland compatriots. It is inevitable that this will affect the willingness of Mainland residents to travel to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","团结报记者","During the summer vacation, a large number of young Taiwan students come to the mainland to study, intern and exchange. What is the spokesperson’s view on the prospects of cross-Strait youth exchanges against the backdrop of the Tsai Ing-wen authorities restricting cross-Strait exchanges?","Cutting water with a sword only makes it flow more. Wanting cooperation and exchange is the shared wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and no one can stop it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻记者","Li Meng-ju, political adviser to Fangliao Township in Pingtung County, Taiwan, has been out of contact for three weeks after traveling to Hong Kong. Please explain the situation.","It is understood that Lee Meng-chu has been placed under investigation in accordance with the law on suspicion of engaging in criminal activities that endanger national security.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Foreign media reported that Wu Chao-hsieh, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department, recently said that Taiwan’s military is formulating new defensive and offensive strategies against the mainland, including content such as “air strikes on Fujian.” Although the relevant Taiwan authorities have denied this, it has still aroused strong attention on the island. What is your evaluation?","I have also seen that relevant authorities in Taiwan came out to deny this, calling it “fake news.” I think this matter shows everyone where Taiwan’s “fake news” actually originates and how it is manufactured through “export for domestic sale” (出口转内销). It is a vivid case. I hope media on both sides of the Strait will pay close attention and carefully dissect it.\nI want to stress that “Taiwan independence” has always been the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It seriously harms the interests of compatriots on both sides and runs counter to the trend of historical development. It is a dead end, a road to failure. If “Taiwan independence” is pushed forward and relies on force for support, it is destined to fail all the faster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Reports that the Solomon Islands may sever ties with Taiwan have circulated for months. How does the spokesperson view the Solomon Islands' so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan at present?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. Following this trend of the times is the choice of the vast majority of countries. At present we have established and maintain diplomatic relations with 178 countries, and this trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港大公文汇全传媒记者","When the Hong Kong “troublemakers” and “Hong Kong independence” elements went to the DPP headquarters, many Taiwan residents held five-star red flags to protest, criticizing “Hong Kong independence” as a dead end. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have said many times that “Hong Kong independence” and “Taiwan independence” are both cancers, seriously harming the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and of Hong Kong, and harming the overall interests of the Chinese nation. If the “two independences” are allowed to merge, they will not only harm Hong Kong but will eventually harm Taiwan too. I believe the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots see this clearly and will resolutely resist it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recent developments in Hong Kong have led some Western forces and certain forces on the island to claim that “one country, two systems” has failed, and even to treat “one country, two systems” as a monster. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have said many times that “One Country, Two Systems” is a scientific concept for resolving the question of national reunification. It respects history and reality, takes into account the interests of all parties, and for Taiwan, it is the best choice. In exploring the “One Country, Two Systems” plan for Taiwan, General Secretary Xi Jinping has also explicitly emphasized the “three fullys”: it will fully consider the actual situation in Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors across the Strait, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. I believe that as time goes on, more and more Taiwan residents will be able to correctly view, understand, and ultimately accept “One Country, Two Systems.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","In response to the decline in mainland tourists visiting Taiwan, which has harmed local tourism, the DPP authorities said they would adopt a series of subsidies and preferential measures, hoping to make up for the decline in mainland tourists with markets from Japan, South Korea and the “New Southbound” region. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have explained many times the reasons for the decline in mainland tourists visiting Taiwan. The root cause lies in the DPP authorities undermining the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and disrupting the good situation of peaceful development across the Taiwan Strait. Recently, they have continuously incited confrontation, hostility and antagonism and advanced various “Taiwan independence” activities. This point is beyond doubt.\nI want to emphasize once again that when cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan compatriots will be well off. Compatriots on both sides sincerely hope that cross-Strait relations can return to the correct track of peaceful development as soon as possible, so that tourism to Taiwan can also return as soon as possible to a healthy, positive and normal development, and jointly enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that Taiwan-invested enterprises' development on the mainland shows a year-on-year growth trend. We have also noted that the Foxconn plant in Zhengzhou was recently pointed out for allegedly violating relevant labor laws. Has the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises encountered some bottlenecks and difficulties?","We do not need to draw too many associations from this individual case, and we will not comment on the individual case. All enterprises' production and business activities should abide by the relevant laws and regulations, and the relevant departments and localities will also handle matters in accordance with law and regulations. I must also stress that in today's complex international economic environment, the scenery on the mainland side remains very good. We will continue to adhere to our policy of encouraging Taiwan compatriots to invest, provide them with good services, and safeguard their rights and interests. We hope that through the continuous expansion and deepening of cross-Strait economic cooperation, compatriots on both sides will all share in the benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190911_12200845.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","According to reports, on September 16, the Solomon Islands' Caucus Meeting decided to sever \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan and establish diplomatic relationship with China, with 27 votes for shifting ties, zero against and six abstentions. The government's cabinet adopted this decision on the same day. What's your comment on the decision of the Solomon Islands' government? When will China officially establish…","China highly commends the decision of the Solomon Islands' government to recognize the one-China principle and sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities. We support the Solomon Islands in making such an important decision as a sovereign and independent country.\nThere is but one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government that represents the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. These are basic facts and the universal consensus of the international community. On the basis of the one-China principle, China has established official diplomatic relationships with 178 countries.\nThe decision of the Solomon Islands' government made with 27 votes for and zero against to recognize the one-China principle and establish diplomatic ties with China again fully testifies to the fact that the one-China principle meets the shared aspiration of the people and constitutes an irresistible trend of the times.\nWe welcome the Solomon Islands' integration into the big family of China-Pacific Island countries cooperation on the basis of the one-China principle at an early date by standing on the right side of history and seizing the historical opportunity. We stand ready to work with the Solomon Islands to open up broad prospects for our bilateral relations.\nAs to when China will officially establish diplomatic ties with the Solomon Islands, I'd like to quote a Chinese proverb, \"everything comes naturally at the right time\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","First, do you have an exact date for when China and the Solomon Islands will formally sign the agreement to establish diplomatic relations? Second, the Taiwanese authorities had provided \"financial support\" for the Solomon Islands. The Solomon Islands government had been having discussions with China about replacing that financial support. So the money that came from Taiwan will now come from China's mainland.…","Your questions, as I can sense, are so skillful with careful wording.\nAs to your first question, I understand it represents your good wish that China will establish diplomatic ties with the Solomon Islands at an early date. Like I just said, \"everything comes naturally at the right time\".\nRegarding the economic support you mentioned, I noticed what certain people in Taiwan said at a press conference the other day. The remarks fully reveal how they've presumed others' behavior by their own pattern. Indeed, those used to \"dollar diplomacy\" may not understand that certain principles cannot be bought with money, neither can trust.\nThe government of the Solomon Islands decided to recognize the one-China principle and establish diplomatic ties with China. It again fully testifies to the fact that the one-China principle meets the shared aspiration of the people and constitutes an irresistible trend of the times.\nWe're convinced that the establishment and development of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China, the world's second largest economy with more than 1.4 billion people and a bright future, will surely bring unprecedented development opportunities for the Solomon Islands. We stand ready to work with it to open up broad prospects for our bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","According to media reports, the Solomon Islands has decided to establish diplomatic relations with China. We noted that the Taiwan authorities said that China's financing and infrastructure assistance to Pacific Island countries is not often substantiated and may cause heavy debt burdens on the recipients. What's your comment on that?","China highly appreciates the Solomon Islands government's decision to recognize the one-China principle, sever the so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan authorities and to establish ties with China. We support this important decision by the Solomon Islands as a sovereign and independent country. It is further proof that the one-China principle is the overriding trend of the times recognized by people all over the world.\nChina and Pacific Island countries are all developing nations. In conducting cooperation with these countries, China always upholds justice while pursuing shared interests. We have also provided much assistance to the best of our capabilities. Chinese assistance to these countries is an integral part of South-South cooperation. It has four distinct features. First, equality. We fully respect the will of the recipients, offer assistance to their needs, do not interfere in their internal affairs and never attach any political strings. Second, practicality. All projects are scientifically sound, taking into full consideration their actual effects and fiscal sustainability. Third, openness. Our assistance is not against any third party. We aim to make the pie of cooperation bigger instead of engaging in a zero-sum game. Fourth, sustainability. Following the idea of teaching a person to fish rather than simply giving him a fish, we attach importance to helping the recipients enhance their self-reliant sustainable development capabilities.\nGuided by these principles, China has helped Pacific Island countries build more than 100 sets of projects such as international conference centers, roads, office buildings, schools and hospitals. We have provided scholarships to more than 5,000 students and trained more than 7,000 professionals. These measures have given a strong boost to these countries' socioeconomic development and people's welfare, gaining unanimous welcome and appreciation of local governments and peoples.\nIn conducting cooperation, from selection of projects to investment and financing projects, decisions are made prudently with mutual agreement after risk analysis and feasibility studies. China offers loans based on the will of recipient countries to areas where they are most needed. When our cooperative partners face debt difficulties, we always seek proper solutions through friendly consultations. So far, not a single country has fallen into a debt crisis because of cooperation with China.\nI must point out that the remarks by Taiwan authorities are fictitious slandering. They are presuming other's behavior by their own pattern. The Pacific Island countries, with eyes wide open, are in the best position to say whether Chinese assistance is good or bad.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","据报道，9月16日，所罗门群岛执政党团会议以27票支持、0票反对、6票弃权的结果表决通过与台湾“断交”、与中国建交的最终决定。同日，所政府召开内阁会议通过上述决定。中方对所罗门群岛政府这一决定有何评论？中国何时与所正式建交？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","第一个问题，你是否能确认所罗门群岛与中国签署建交协议的准确日期？第二个问题，据报道，台湾当局此前已为所罗门群岛提供了“财政支持”，所方已经同大陆探讨如何代替台湾向所提供经济援助，以使得原来由台湾当局提供的经济援助能够由大陆继续提供。你能够透露吗？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2019-09-17","Hua Chunying","","近期，英国前议员加洛韦在接受采访时表示，一些外国组织在香港示威活动中进行幕后干预。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698607.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698578.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2019-09-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, September 17 (Xinhua) — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, on September 17, commenting on the Solomon Islands government's decision to sever so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities and establish diplomatic ties with China, said that the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already made a statement on this. The Solomon Islands made the right decision based on its own national and people's interests, and we express our high appreciation. Facts have repeatedly proven that adhering to the one-China principle is the will of the people, the trend of the times, and irresistible.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that what we must emphasize is that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is a sacred part of China's territory. This is a basic fact and a general consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities' claims of “dollar diplomacy” and “political suppression” are complete lies that deceive oneself and others, aimed at diverting attention. Their attempts to sow discord and stir up trouble internationally are even more presumptuous. Past, present and future, we will absolutely never trade in the one-China principle! Anyone with international vision and common sense understands this clearly.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the damage to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and to the achievements of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the responsibility of the DPP authorities. To truly safeguard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, returning to the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the only correct choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190917_12202190.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-18","Geng Shuang","","On September 17, the spokesperson of the US Department of State said that they are disappointed by the Solomon Islands' decision to sever its \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan and Beijing's continued campaign to squeeze Taiwan's international space and change the cross-strait status quo. Following the Solomon Islands' decision to establish diplomatic ties with China, US Vice President Mike Pence refused to meet the…","There is but one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. These are basic facts and the universal consensus of the international community. On the basis of the one-China principle, China has established official diplomatic relationships with 178 countries.\nChina highly commends the decision of the Solomon Islands' government to recognize the one-China principle and sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities. We support the Solomon Islands in making such an important decision as a sovereign and independent country.\nThe US established diplomatic ties with China on the basis of the one-China principle back in 1979. Does this put it in a position to criticize a sovereign country's decision to establish diplomatic relationship with China based on the one-China principle? Isn't it interfering in the domestic affairs of the Solomon Islands? The international community sees it clearly.\nAs to Vice President Pence's refusal to meet with the leader of the Solomon Islands, you should ask the US side. If it truly cares for the Pacific Island countries, it should take more concrete measures to help them develop the economy and improve livelihood, rather than wantonly wield the big stick of sanctions and grossly interfere in their internal affairs.\nWe urge the US to respect other countries' sovereign rights in independently deciding their internal and foreign affairs, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues to avoid severe harms to China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1698946.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1698901.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-19","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan's ally Tuvalu has elected a new prime minister. I wonder if China is reaching out to that country's government to talk about opening relations?","China's position is consistent and clear. We stand ready to develop friendly cooperative relations with countries around the globe on the basis of the one-China principle and the Five Principles of Peaceful Co-existence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1699375.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1699291.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-20","Geng Shuang","","On September 20, the Kiribati government announced in a statement its decision to recognize the one-China principle, sever its \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan authorities and resume diplomatic relations with China. What's your comment?","China highly commends the decision by the government of Kiribati to recognize the one-China principle, sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities and re-establish its diplomatic relations with China. We support Kiribati in making such an important decision as a sovereign and independent country.\nThere is but one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. These facts are recognized by UN resolution and constitute the universal consensus of the international community. On the basis of the one-China principle, China has established official diplomatic relationships with 178 countries. Recently, Pacific Island countries including the Solomon Islands and Kiribati decided to recognize the one-China principle, sever \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities and establish or re-establish diplomatic relationships with China. This again fully shows that the one-China principle meets the shared aspiration of the people and is an irresistible trend of the times.\nThe relations between China and Pacific Island countries maintain a momentum for rapid development. Despite setbacks in the relations between China and Kiribati, the two peoples have long-cherished friendship towards each other. We welcome Kiribati's early return to the big family of China-Pacific Island countries for cooperation on the basis of the one-China principle. We stand ready to work with Kiribati to turn a new page in our bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1699827.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1699656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-20","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan says that China has managed to win back Kiribati by offering a large amount of money to buy aircraft and ships for Kiribati, is this true?","After the Solomon Islands decided to sever the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with the Taiwan authorities, certain people in Taiwan also tried to mislead the public with similar rhetoric.\nI'd like to reiterate that such remarks by certain individuals in Taiwan again fully reveal how they've presumed others' behavior by their own pattern. Indeed, those used to \"dollar diplomacy\" may not understand that principles cannot be bought with money, neither can trust.\nThe government of Kiribati's decision to recognize the one-China principle and resume diplomatic relationship with China again shows that the one-China principle meets the shared aspiration of the people and is an irresistible trend of the times.\nWe're convinced that the resumption and development of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China, the world's second largest economy with more than 1.4 billion people and a bright future, will surely bring unprecedented development opportunities for Kiribati. We stand ready to work with it to turn a new page in our bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1699827.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1699656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, September 20 (Xinhua) — Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 20th, in response to a question about the Government of Kiribati's decision to sever so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities and restore diplomatic relations with China, that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's sacred territory. This is a fundamental fact that has never changed and cannot be changed, and it is also a common consensus of the international community. We highly appreciate the Government and people of Kiribati for following the trend of history and making the correct decision to join the ranks of the 178 countries in the world that have formal diplomatic relations with China. The DPP authorities' various groundless accusations against the Government of Kiribati contradict what they have said to Kiribati in the past, and are an extremely disrespectful expression toward the country and people of Kiribati.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the habitual practice of the DPP authorities is to weave lies in order to divert attention and deceive the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. They did this in the past, and they will do so again in the future. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have already seen this clearly. Only by adhering to the one-China principle can cross-Strait relations improve and develop, and only then can Taiwan compatriots obtain better livelihood and well-being, greater room for development, and greater security and dignity.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the international community generally and firmly adheres to the one-China principle. The DPP authorities' attempt to rely on slander and smears to shake the international community's firm adherence to one China is absolutely impossible to achieve.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190920_12203272.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-23","Geng Shuang","","Now that China has reestablished ties with Kiribati. Is China planning to reopen the space tracking station it had there that was closed down in 2003?","Michael, I need to correct you. The Kiribati government announced last week that it severed the so-called \"diplomatic ties\" with Taiwan authorities and expressed the will to resume diplomatic relations with the Chinese side. But our two countries have yet to reestablish diplomatic relations.\nI take it that you really hope to see us resuming relations soon. Thank you for your interest and good wishes.\nAs I used to say here, sooner or later, whatever will be, will be. Please remain patient for the time being.\nI'd like to reiterate that China is committed to developing friendly cooperative relations with other countries on the basis of the one-China principle. We look forward to reestablishing diplomatic relations with Kiribati and turning a new page in our bilateral relations. We believe this will bring benefits to the two peoples and is conducive to peace, stability, development and prosperity of the Pacific Island region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1700483.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1700436.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-23","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 23 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 23rd regarding the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Solomon Islands, saying: The establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the Solomon Islands is the correct decision made by the government and people of the Solomon Islands. Adhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. 179 countries have followed the trend of the times and established formal diplomatic relations with us, and this historical trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190923_12204079.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-25","Geng Shuang","","According to reports, on August 30, then US National Security Adviser John Bolton declassified a memo dated 1982, which was sent by then U.S. President Ronald Reagan to his Secretary of State George P. Shultz and Secretary of Defense Caspar Weinberger after the August 17 Communiqué was signed. The document said that the quality and quantity of the arms provided to Taiwan depend entirely on the threat posed by…","The Shanghai Communiqué of 1972, the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations of 1979, and the August 17 Communiqué in 1982 established the guiding principle for China and the US to handle bilateral relations, including the Taiwan question. In particular, the August 17 Communiqué sets out clear provisions on US arms sales to Taiwan. The US explicitly states that it does not seek to carry out a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan, that its arms sales to Taiwan will not exceed, either in qualitative or in quantitative terms, the level of those supplied in recent years since the establishment of diplomatic relations between the United States and China, and that it intends gradually to reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution. As facts have shown, US arms sales to Taiwan seriously breach the three joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, go against the commitment made by the US itself, and seriously undermine China-US relations.\nThe unilateral and internal memo you mentioned is a serious breach of the one-China principle, the three joint communiqués and basic norms governing international relations. It is completely wrong and null and void. The US should abide by the three joint communiqués, not some unilateral memo.\nWe strongly urge the US side to stay true to its solemn commitment to China, abide by the one-China principle and the three communiqués, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop arms sales to Taiwan, and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan, to prevent new disruption and damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1701592.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1701570.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-09-25","Geng Shuang","","The government of the Marshall Islands has within the last thirty minutes just issued a statement expressing its support for Taiwan and criticism of China. The Marshall Islands' president said that China's attempts to expand its influence in the Pacific Island region should be of great concern to democratic countries. Can you tell us is the Chinese government currently discussing with the Marshall Islands whether…","First, there is but one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a consensus of the international community. Adhering to this principle is an irresistible trend of the times with wide recognition. We are convinced that more and more countries will join the ranks of those supporting the one-China principle. I would like to reiterate that China stands ready to develop friendly cooperative relations with other countries on the basis of the one-China principle.\nAs to China expanding influence in the Pacific Island region, we have stated repeatedly that our cooperation with Pacific Island countries is based on mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit. It has brought tangible interests to Pacific Island countries and is welcomed by the their governments and peoples. Any fair-minded people will not fail to see the plain facts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1701592.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1701570.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning! I will host today's press conference. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","After the pilot program for individual tourism by mainland residents to Taiwan was suspended, the magistrates of Kinmen, Matsu, and Penghu counties visited the Taiwan Affairs Office in August. The mainland's immigration and exit-entry administration recently announced that it would resume accepting applications for individual tourism visa endorsements under the “mini three links” from some mainland cities. Please…","For reasons known to all, starting August 1, the relevant mainland authorities have suspended the pilot program for individual tourism to Taiwan by residents of 47 mainland cities. This does not involve the policy on individual tourism to Kinmen, Matsu, and Penghu by residents of the 20 cities in the Haixi region. The entry-exit administration authorities of these 20 cities will continue to accept applications from local residents for individual tourism visas to Kinmen, Matsu, and Penghu.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205167.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please have the spokesperson tell us about recent important cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities?","Recently, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities have featured many highlights. From September 16 to 22, the 2019 Zhejiang-Taiwan Cooperation Week was held in Hangzhou and other places. More than 1,500 people attended, including Guo Jinlong and Mr. Vincent Siew, the chairpersons of the two sides of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, and 32 cooperation projects were reached, with total investment of about RMB 32.2 billion. From September 17 to 19, the 2019 Guizhou-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Forum was held in Guiyang. Taiwanese business and industry representatives enthusiastically attended, and 16 cooperation projects were reached, with investment of about RMB 2.5 billion. From September 23 to 26, the 15th Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum was held in Nanning, reaching 11 cooperation projects with investment of RMB 10.86 billion. During the same period, the 2019 China Western Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Cooperation and Exchange Fair was held in Chengdu, Sichuan, reaching 21 cooperation projects with investment of nearly RMB 2 billion. This fully demonstrates that, amid the current complex global economic environment, the mainland's economic scale continues to grow, its structure keeps being optimized, its market is more open, and new demand keeps emerging, so it remains the best choice for Taiwanese investment.\nNext, in mid-October and early November, the 11th Chongqing-Taiwan Week and the 18th China (Suzhou) Electronic Information Expo will also be held in Chongqing and Suzhou, respectively. We welcome broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to take part, seize new development opportunities, and achieve greater and better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205169.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the 16th Cross-Strait Forum on Information Industry and Technology Standards was held in Hsinchu, Taiwan. Please have the spokesperson introduce the achievements of this forum. What cooperation achievements have the two sides cumulatively made in this area?","On September 17–18, the China Communications Standards Association, the China Electronic Industry Standardization Technical Association, and the Taiwan Huaju Industry Common Standards Promotion Foundation jointly held the 16th Cross-Strait Forum on Information Industry and Technology Standards in Hsinchu, Taiwan. Nearly 300 representatives from the cross-Strait information and communications industry attended. The forum released 6 common standards in relevant fields, 1 case compilation, and 1 industry white paper, and reached 31 points of consensus, making new efforts to promote “common industry standards across the Strait.”\nSince the Standards Forum began sixteen sessions ago, it has cumulatively released 65 common standards, 5 case compilations, and 2 industry white papers, reached 453 points of consensus, and signed 14 cooperation memoranda. It has become an important platform for cross-Strait cooperation on information industry and technology standards and has exerted a positive influence on promoting exchange, cooperation, and integrated development in related fields across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205168.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视记者","The National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises recently issued a statement calling on cross-Strait airlines to add flights on cross-Strait routes in early next year and offer preferential fares, to facilitate Taiwan compatriots returning home. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","It is understood that, at the strong request of members and Taiwan compatriots, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises recently appealed to cross-Strait airlines to add flights on cross-Strait routes early next year and offer preferential fares, among other measures, to facilitate the return of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople to Taiwan. We fully understand the feelings of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that cross-Strait airlines and relevant units will, based on the timing and route conditions, do their utmost to guarantee capacity and offer as many preferential fares as possible, to meet the needs of the broad Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205166.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","It is reported that the government of the Solomon Islands has decided to sever its so-called \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan and establish diplomatic ties with China. U.S. officials have questioned whether the mainland \"instigated\" the Solomon Islands' diplomatic shift and changed the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, and reiterated support for Taiwan's so-called \"international space.\" May I ask the…","We have repeatedly stated that adhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations, a universal consensus of the international community, and the political foundation of China-US relations. The US side established diplomatic relations with China in 1979 on the basis of the one-China principle. US personnel criticize sovereign countries for establishing diplomatic relations with China; by openly playing “double standards” in this way, do they not feel embarrassed?\nSince 2016, the DPP authorities have unilaterally negated the “1992 Consensus,” promoted “Taiwan independence” activities, incited hostility across the Strait, created confrontation across the Strait, and undermined cross-Strait relations. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait see this very clearly. Is it only US personnel who are “turning a blind eye”?\nThe US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions and commitments of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues appropriately, and avoid seriously harming China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205164.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, personnel of Taiwan's office in New York were recently invited by the US to take part in related meetings hosted by the US at the United Nations, and the DPP authorities called this a “major breakthrough.” May I ask for the spokesperson's evaluation?","It is understood that this meeting is not on the agenda of the UN General Assembly. The DPP authorities are using it to make political hay and boast about themselves, in order to deceive the people of Taiwan. The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is part of China and is not qualified to join. The UN has long adhered to the one-China principle in handling Taiwan-related matters, including the entry of people from Taiwan into relevant UN venues. This has not changed and will not change.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, the DPP authorities recently said that because they were “suppressed” by the mainland, they cannot attend the ICAO Assembly held in Montreal, Canada, and that this would affect flight safety. What comment does the spokesperson have? Second, it is reported that Tsai Ing-wen recently said the mainland is most afraid of three things about Taiwan: first, that Taiwanese people unite;…","On the first question: Taiwan is part of China. On the issue of Taiwan's participation in international organizations, including activities of the International Civil Aviation Organization, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. We believe that the ICAO and relevant countries will properly handle Taiwan-related issues that may arise during this year's assembly in accordance with the one-China principle.\nThe mainland has always attached importance to the needs of Taiwan compatriots in the field of civil aviation, and the channels for the Taiwan side to obtain ICAO standards and recommended practices and related materials are open. Flight connections between Taiwan and many cities around the world are also convenient. Facts prove that Taiwan's aviation safety and its air links with other regions have no connection with whether the DPP authorities participate in the ICAO Assembly.\nOn the second question: the remarks by the leader of the DPP authorities completely turn black into white. Their purpose is very clear: to serve electoral needs, create an atmosphere of \"anti-China\" and \"fear of China,\" and pursue narrow party interests. Not worth refuting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190925_12205163.htm"],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Three questions. First, today the Daxing International Airport held its opening ceremony. Which cross-strait airlines or Taiwan airlines will move to Daxing Airport in the future? Second, besides Li Meng-chu, Taiwan scholar Tsai Chin-shu was reportedly detained in Fuzhou for over a year on “national security grounds.” What is the current status of Li Meng-chu and Tsai Chin-shu? Third, Lee Ming-che's father has…","On the first question: the Beijing Daxing International Airport has officially begun operations. This is another achievement in our economic and livelihood development and civil aviation construction. The airport project has also been hailed as one of the \"Seven Modern Wonders of the World.\" I note that it has also been enthusiastically received by Taiwan media and netizens. According to arrangements by the civil aviation authorities, airlines in the Taiwan region may freely choose whether to station at Daxing Airport. For specific circumstances, please consult the civil aviation authorities further.\nOn the second question, as we understand it, Tsai Chin-shu, on suspicion of engaging in activities endangering national security, was placed under investigation by relevant mainland authorities in July 2018 in accordance with law. The relevant mainland authorities have notified Tsai Chin-shu's family, and the so-called \"disappearance\" issue reported by some media does not exist. The relevant authorities have strictly handled the case in accordance with the law and, as provided by law, safeguarded Tsai Chin-shu's various lawful rights.\nOn the third question, regarding Li Mingzhe's relatives, his mother and wife visited Li Mingzhe at the Chishan Prison in Hunan yesterday. As for his application to return to Taiwan to attend a funeral, it does not conform to relevant legal provisions, and the prison authorities have explained the detailed circumstances to the family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping recently stated at the conference marking the 70th anniversary of the founding of the CPPCC that we must adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” expand exchanges and interactions with political parties, groups, social organizations, and personages from all walks of life in Taiwan, promote deeper integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, and resolutely oppose…","General Secretary Xi's speech at the central work conference on the CPPCC has pointed the direction and path for further advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of national reunification. We must study and comprehend it carefully, thoroughly implement the spirit of the General Secretary's important speech, unite broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots, strive to promote integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, promote emotional and spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides, and thereby advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Reports say the DPP and some groups on the island will soon launch a so-called “Taiwan-Hong Kong Mass March” in Taipei in response to the protests in Hong Kong. What comment does the spokesperson have?","In the past three months, radical protests and violent assaults in Hong Kong have seriously undermined the overall prosperity and stability of Hong Kong, seriously challenged the rule of law and social order in Hong Kong, and seriously touched the principled bottom line of \"one country, two systems.\" A small number of radical elements have continuously carried out violent activities, and some have even openly advocated \"Hong Kong independence,\" arousing strong indignation among Chinese people at home and abroad. At present, \"stopping violence and restoring order\" has become the broadest consensus across all sectors of Hong Kong society.\nThe DPP authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces, in order to profit for private gain, disregard the well-being of the people of Hong Kong and Taiwan, stir up trouble, fan the flames, and their intention to sow chaos in Hong Kong is plain to see. This latest clamor from a relevant DPP official is yet another clear proof of their meddling in Hong Kong affairs and their attempt to stir up chaos there, a self-confession without need of exposure.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces once again: stop interfering in Hong Kong affairs and stop acts that undermine cross-Strait relations. Those who attempt to pull chestnuts out of the fire will certainly burn themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The DPP authorities recently said they will revise the “Measures on Permits for Taiwan Region Civil Servants and Persons of Specific Status to Enter the Mainland Area.” This means that in the future, public officials on the island, even if merely transiting through the mainland, will have to apply in advance and report afterward. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Cross-strait exchanges have been open for more than thirty years, yet the DPP authorities are still doing things that undermine cross-strait exchanges and harm the interests of the people. As long as this political nature does not change, they will inevitably lose the people's support step by step.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","According to foreign media reports, U.S. Vice President Pence personally called Solomon Islands Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare to try to prevent the country from “severing ties” with Taiwan. After this attempt failed, Pence refused to meet with him at the UN General Assembly, and some U.S. lawmakers also threatened to halt aid to the Solomon Islands. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. The blatant interference by the U.S. side in China's internal affairs runs against popular sentiment. The U.S. side should earnestly abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions and commitments of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Please, how does the spokesperson evaluate cross-Strait relations over the past 70 years?","The 70 years of cross-strait relations are a history in which compatriots on both sides broke through isolation, and exchanges and cooperation as well as mutual visits grew ever broader and closer. By the end of 2018, there had been 135 million cross-strait trips, of which more than 100 million were trips by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland. In 2018, the scale of cross-strait trade reached US$226.25 billion. As of July 2019, the mainland had approved more than 110,000 Taiwan-invested projects, and cumulative actual use of Taiwan capital exceeded US$69 billion. Guided by the development philosophy that puts the people first, we have continuously introduced policies that benefit Taiwan and its people, providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots who come to the mainland to live, work, study and start businesses, and taking the lead in letting Taiwan compatriots share the opportunities of mainland development, which has promoted the integrated development of both sides and the spiritual connection of compatriots on both sides. The 70 years of cross-strait relations are also a history of equal consultation on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and improving and developing cross-strait relations. Since 2008, the two sides have signed 23 agreements, achieved full, direct, two-way “three links” (trade, transport and postal links), and implemented the Early Harvest Program under the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement, bringing real benefits to compatriots on both sides. By the end of 2018, the mainland had cumulatively reduced or exempted tariffs of about NT$155.2 billion, and 56 Taiwan financial enterprises and 1,033 non-financial enterprises had used the Early Harvest preferential policies to provide services on the mainland. Leaders of the two sides have held a historic meeting, and political interaction has reached a new high. The 70 years of cross-strait relations are also a history of opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, firmly safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nThe development of cross-strait relations fully demonstrates that Taiwan is part of China, and that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, a historical and legal fact that no person or force can change! Compatriots on both sides are Chinese; the natural bonds of kinship, mutual support in times of need, and national identity are something no person or force can change! The trend toward peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the historical tide of cross-strait relations moving forward cannot be stopped by any person or force! The historical trend of a strong country, national rejuvenation and cross-strait reunification is even more unstoppable by any person or force!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央广记者","Taiwan's external exchange department recently said that it will consider increasing so-called “foreign aid funds” for Nauru, Tuvalu, the Marshall Islands, Palau and other countries in order to stably maintain relations. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The actions of Taiwan’s relevant authorities precisely show who is engaging in “checkbook diplomacy.” I want to emphasize that adhering to the one-China principle is the trend of history and the will of the people, and it is unstoppable. More and more countries in the world are choosing to establish diplomatic relations with us, and this trend will continue to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻记者","Which Taiwan personalities have been invited to, or confirmed to, attend the National Day military parade and celebration? Are any Taiwan personalities performing in or watching the arts gala?","National Day is a grand festival that brings Chinese people at home and abroad together. We will invite Taiwan compatriots to join the celebrations, and Taiwan compatriots will take part in several important events during the National Day period.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-25","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","I have two questions. First, Hong Kong director Du Qifeng withdrew from the jury of the Golden Horse Awards. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Second, a Hong Kong University student studying in Taiwan posted a poster in his dormitory supporting the “anti-extradition” movement, which led to a clash with his mainland roommate. What are the spokesperson's thoughts on this?","First question: the reasons why the mainland film industry suspended participation in the 2019 Golden Horse Film Festival are well known. On this matter I have pointed out that the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces bear unavoidable responsibility. Some people in Taiwan are using this as an opening to stir up trouble, which is entirely about confusing public perception.\nSecond question: it is understood that recently some Hong Kong students studying at universities in Taiwan have openly posted stickers and slogans on campus supporting violent activities in Hong Kong. We firmly oppose anyone who agitates for or supports violent and illegal activities in Hong Kong. We hope relevant universities in Taiwan will stop such acts that champion violent and illegal activities, and avoid any impact on the normal studies and lives of mainland students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201909/t20190925_12205161.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-26","Geng Shuang","","First, the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee and the House Foreign Relations Committee passed the Hong Kong Human Rights and Democracy Act. What's your comment? Second, the US Senate Committee on Foreign Relations passed the Taiwan Allies International Protection and Enhancement Initiative (TAIPEI) Act, which proposes to reduce ties with countries that have severed or is considering severing \"diplomatic…","In the early hours of this morning, the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee and the House Foreign Relations Committee passed the Hong Kong Human Rights and Democracy Act. The Chinese side has immediately made response to that, which is available on the website of the foreign ministry. Have you seen that? If necessary, I will repeat our response.\nBy passing the relevant act, the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee and the House Foreign Relations Committee have blatantly backed the Hong Kong violent radicals up and grossly interfered in China's internal affairs. China expresses strong indignation and firm opposition to that.\nSince Hong Kong's return, the policies of \"one country, two systems\", Hong Kong people governing Hong Kong and a high degree of autonomy have been implemented, and Hong Kong residents' rights and freedoms have been fully safeguarded in accordance with law. However, recent developments over the past three months or so have veered off the normal track. With the instigation and indulgence of external forces and anti-China forces attempting to destabilize Hong Kong, radical forces and violent offenders in Hong Kong flagrantly disrupted social order, vandalized public facilities, attacked the police and left a trail of smashed or burned items all over the city. These behaviors have gone far beyond the scope of marches or assemblies. They trampled on the bottom line of morality, crossed the bottom line of rule of law, and challenged the bottom line of \"one country, two systems\". Ending violence and chaos and restoring order has become the widest consensus and the strongest appeal of all social sectors in Hong Kong. The Chinese central government firmly supports the SAR government in governing by law, supports the Hong Kong police in strict and just law enforcement, and supports the Hong Kong judicial organs in bringing violent criminals to justice according to law.\nIn disregard of the vile behavior of Hong Kong's radical and violent forces, the appeal from various sectors of the Hong Kong society, and the basic norms governing international relations, the US Senate Foreign Affairs Committee and the House Foreign Affairs Committee insisted on reviewing and passing the above-mentioned Hong Kong-related bill and openly endorsed Hong Kong's radical and violent forces. Such behavior is a gross interference in China's domestic affairs, which fully reveals the ill intentions of some people in the United States to mess up Hong Kong and contain China's development.\nIt must be pointed out that Hong Kong's prosperity and stability are in the interests of all parties, including the United States. The United States has more than 80,000 citizens, over 1,300 companies and a large amount of investment in Hong Kong. The passing of the bill by the US Senate and the House Foreign Affairs Committees will only embolden Hong Kong's radical and violent forces, and further mess up Hong Kong. It will harm the interests of both China and the US. No one should underestimate China's firm resolve and determination to safeguard its national sovereignty, security and development interests, to implement \"one country, two systems\", and to safeguard Hong Kong's prosperity and stability. Any attempt by the US to harm China's interests will be met with forceful fightback.\nI stress again that China strongly urges certain people in the US Congress to grasp the situation, immediately stop advancing the bill regarding Hong Kong and interfering in Hong Kong's affairs to avoid further damaging China-US relations.\nRegarding the passing of the TAIPEI Act by the Senate Foreign Affairs Committee, I would like to point out that the relevant act seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and the international law and basic norms governing international relations, and grossly interferes in China's internal affairs. China firmly opposes it. The one-China principle is the popular trend of the times and the general consensus of the international community. There are 179 countries in the world that have established diplomatic relations with China. The United States has established diplomatic relations with China as early as 40 years ago. Now it is obstructing other sovereign countries' development of normal state-to-state relations with China. This is simply unreasonable and illogical.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, immediately stop reviewing and pushing through the negative act on Taiwan, and prudentially and carefully handle the Taiwan-related issues so as not to damage China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.\nAs for the series of negative US moves you mentioned, you may want to read State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi's speech at a dinner hosted by several American institutions on the evening of September 24. The speech expounded China's position and proposition on developing China-US relations, and I think you would like to read it carefully.\nWhat I want to say here is that we hope the US will meet China halfway, jointly manage differences with mutual respect, and expand cooperation on the basis of mutual benefit to advance our relations featuring coordination, cooperation and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1702256.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1702197.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-09-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We noticed that at the news conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council yesterday, the spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said that the upcoming National Day is a grand festival for all the Chinese people at home and abroad. Taiwan compatriots will also participate in several important events. The military parade demonstrates China’s great achievements in national defense building. Many Taiwan compatriots…","As was mentioned by the spokesperson from the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, this year marks the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People’s Republic of China. The state will host a number of commemorative activities and compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan will be invited to join us for the celebration. The Taiwan compatriots are part of the Chinese nation and should not be absent in the process of realizing the great rejuvenation of China. The PLA is a staunch force to safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity, and also a strong force to prevent secession and combat the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2019-09/27/content_4851488.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2019-09/26/content_4851445.htm",0,1,1,""],[2,"2019-09-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to reports, the United States recently declassified a memorandum that then-U.S. President Reagan in 1982 sent to former Secretary of State Shultz and former Secretary of Defense Weinberger after the signing of the “August 17 Communiqué,” which states that Taiwan’s defense capability relative to mainland China, both in quantity and performance, should be maintained. What is your comment on this? Ma…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 26 (reporter Chen Jianxing) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 26th about the so-called memorandum on arms sales to Taiwan that the U.S. side declassified, stating that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. U.S. arms sales to Taiwan will only embolden the arrogance of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and will further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position on this matter. The so-called memorandum unilaterally produced within the United States seriously violates the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and seriously violates the basic norms of international relations. It is entirely wrong and invalid.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides. We are willing to make our utmost efforts and act with the greatest sincerity to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, while our determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering! China must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. This historical trend cannot be stopped by anyone or any force!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190926_12205402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-09-27","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan media reported that a staffer from the Taipei office in New York attended a meeting on religious issues held by the US at UN headquarters, and called it a \"diplomatic breakthrough\". What's your comment on this?","The meeting you mentioned is not a UN meeting. It is merely a side event held by the US at a UN venue. Certain individual from the Taipei office in New York degraded herself by sneaking into the UN. And yet this is being hyped up as a \"diplomatic breakthrough\". Such an underhand ploy will only become a laughing stock.\nThe UN has reiterated time and again that it handles issues relating to Taiwan in accordance with UNGA Resolution 2758. The vast majority of UN member countries stay committed to the one-China principle. Taiwan authorities' scheming will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1702916.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1702880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-09-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 27 — TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded on the 27th to the U.S. Senate Foreign Relations Committee's passage of the so-called “Taipei Act,” saying that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs spokesperson has already stated our position on this. The U.S. Senate Foreign Relations Committee's review and passage of the so-called “Taipei Act” seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, and we firmly oppose it.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. We strongly urge the U.S. side to recognize the situation, immediately stop promoting the relevant negative bills, and immediately stop meddling in the Taiwan question, so as not to further damage China-U.S. relations and harm peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that China must be unified, and it will certainly be unified. No person or force can stop this historical trend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190927_12205850.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-09-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, September 29 — Responding to the DPP's passage of the so-called \"Resolution on Social Co-Existence, Generational Win-Win,\" Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 29th that this so-called \"resolution\" fully exposes the DPP's true colors of obstinately clinging to a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position and deliberately undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It fully proves that the DPP and its authorities are troublemakers for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, dividers of harmony within island society, and destroyers of the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Its purpose is to inflame cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, to suppress the calls of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots to improve and develop cross-Strait relations, and to maliciously manipulate cross-Strait issues to seek electoral self-interest.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end and will only bring profound harm to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan is the Taiwan of all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan's future is to be decided jointly by all Chinese people. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities in any form. The DPP's \"independence\" obsession will never die, and it will ultimately be abandoned by the irresistible tide of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201909/t20190930_12206184.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-10-08","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan media reported that Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and Deputy Prime Minister Taro Aso sent congratulatory messages respectively to Taiwan's economic and cultural office in Fukuoka, Japan on its celebratory event and referred to Taiwan as the \"Republic of China\". What's your comment?","We noted that the Japanese government has openly stated that this is fake news and reiterated its commitment to the 1972 China-Japan Joint Communiqué on issues regarding Taiwan.\nThere is only one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory.\nI advise certain people in Taiwan to stop making what they deem clever moves that will only lead to humiliation. It couldn't be nice to get a slap in the face.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1706154.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1706148.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-10-10","Geng Shuang","","Yesterday Beijing announced its decision to end sister-city relations with Prague, Czech. Do you have a comment on this?","Since November 2018, major officials from the new Prague city government, disregarding basic norms governing international relations, international consensus and China's solemn position and strong opposition, repeatedly made erroneous moves and inappropriate remarks on major issues concerning China's core interests such as topics regarding Taiwan and Tibet. They were grossly interfering in China's internal affairs, openly challenging Prague's sister-city relations with Beijing, and seriously undermining the political precondition and foundation for exchanges between the two cities. In light of the negative impact produced by the above, Beijing has announced its decision to end the sister-city relationship with Prague and suspend all official interactions.\nWe have noted that people with insight from all sectors in Czech, including political leaders such as President Zeman, have condemned the wrong moves of the Prague city government. I would like to stress that continued progress in the China-Czech strategic partnership on the basis of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit serves the interests of both sides. We hope the Prague city government will recognize and correct its mistake as soon as possible and work to create conditions for resumption of exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1706849.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1706831.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-10-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","BEIJING, October 11 (Xinhua) (Reporters Li Hanfang and Shi Longhong) — In response to remarks on cross-Strait relations made on October 10 by the leader of the DPP authorities, Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 11th that this speech is full of confrontational thinking and hostile awareness. It attempts to create an atmosphere of hostility toward the mainland by smearing and attacking “one country, two systems,” to suppress mainstream public opinion on the island, which hopes for economic development, improved livelihoods, and easing of cross-Strait relations, and to seek electoral gains.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that this speech turns black into white. It describes the efforts of all Chinese people to pursue peaceful reunification, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and maintain the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations as a so-called “threat” to Taiwan, caters to Western anti-China forces, and describes the mainland's development and progress and the process of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation as a so-called “challenge” to regional stability and peace. Once again, this exposes the essence of “Taiwan independence” of the DPP authorities: creating cross-Strait confrontation and conflict, undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, going against the mainstream public opinion on the island, which seeks security and good governance, and standing against the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.\nHe emphasized that we warn the DPP authorities: confrontation has no way out, and seeking “Taiwan independence” is an even more dead end. “Taiwan independence” is a serious threat to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The trend of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the historical tide of cross-Strait relations moving forward cannot be blocked by anyone or any force. Those who harm the interests of the people, go against public opinion, or move against the current will certainly be abandoned by the course of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191011_12208755.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Today's press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","What new progress has been made by various localities and departments in implementing the “31 measures”? Is it possible that the mainland will introduce new measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots in the near future?","We have repeatedly introduced to everyone that various localities and departments continue to implement the “31 Measures” in detail. Recently, Guilin City in the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, Dezhou City in Shandong Province, and Suining City in Sichuan Province each issued specific implementation opinions. As of now, 102 localities on the mainland have issued specific implementation opinions for the “31 Measures” in light of local conditions, including 28 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the central government, 12 sub-provincial cities, 57 prefecture-level cities, 1 municipal district and 4 county-level localities, providing more comprehensive equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to develop on the mainland. The implementation of the “31 Measures” has continuously expanded its coverage and achieved new results.\nAdhering to the development philosophy of putting the people first, providing more favorable conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to live, work, and start businesses and innovate on the mainland, and sharing the development opportunities of the mainland is a policy we have long upheld and consistently pursued. We will continue to widely listen to and carefully study the demands of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, strive to do practical things, good things, and solve difficult problems for Taiwan compatriots, promote the integrated development of the two sides of the Strait and the spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides, so that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will have a greater sense of gain, honor, and happiness, and help Taiwan compatriots realize their yearning for a better life.\nReporter from Voice of the Strait Radio: Please introduce the current preparations for this year's annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit.\nSince its establishment in 2013, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit has held six annual meetings, continuously promoting exchange and dialogue between business circles on both sides of the Strait and close connections, and has played a positive role in promoting economic exchange and cooperation across the Strait and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe 2019 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit will be held in Nanjing from November 3 to 5. This year's summit annual meeting takes “Deepening Integrated Development, Building a Common Market” as its theme, and will feature activities such as an opening ceremony, keynote speeches, a series of thematic forums, and a concluding session for the conference. About 1,000 participants, including well-known entrepreneurs from both sides of the Strait, heads of business associations, small and medium-sized enterprises, and young entrepreneurs, will attend. At present, preparations are proceeding in an orderly manner. On behalf of the host organizers, I also warmly welcome media friends from both sides of the Strait to visit and report on the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210209.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210210.htm"],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","It is understood that the mainland recently established four new cross-Strait exchange bases. Please introduce the relevant information.","To create more platforms for cross-strait exchange and cooperation, and to give compatriots on both sides more opportunities to revisit history, appreciate culture, share family ties, and develop together, the Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office recently approved four new Cross-Strait Exchange Bases at four locations: Dachen Island in Jiaojiang District, Taizhou, Zhejiang; the General Zhang Zizhong Memorial Hall in Yicheng City, Xiangyang, Hubei; the Fujian Xiamen (Jimei) Min-Taiwan Study Tour Base in Fujian; and the former site of the Battle of Kunlun Pass in Nanning, Guangxi. Each of these four exchange bases has its own distinctive features. Some carry history shared by compatriots on both sides, and others serve as important venues for youth exchange across the Strait. They have already played an important role in cross-strait exchange and cooperation. We have consistently advocated strengthening cross-strait exchange and civil contact, and we warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange at these bases.\nSince 2009, the Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office have successively approved the establishment of 75 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 23 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei, and Fujian. The establishment of these bases has played an important role in expanding cross-strait exchange and cooperation, deepening cross-strait integrated development, and achieving heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210208.htm"],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 12th Straits Forum Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Exposition and Trade Fair is about to be held. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 12th Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industries Expo and Trade Fair will be held at the Xiamen International Conference and Exhibition Center from November 1 to 4, 2019. It has been announced that this year's Expo will feature five major sections: Provincial and Municipal Famous Enterprises, Crafts and Art, Creative Design, Digital Film and Television, and Cultural and Creative Tourism. The total exhibition area is 75,000 square meters, with about 3,500 booths set up, of which Taiwanese enterprise booths account for one-third. Eight themed pavilions for Taiwan's cultural and creative industries have been carefully built. For the first time, a Taiwan Premium Exhibition Area of more than 6,500 square meters has been set up, covering various Taiwanese exhibitors with distinctive features, highlighting the achievements of Cross-Strait integration and enhancing the practical effectiveness of cultural and economic connections across the Strait.\nSince its founding in 2008, the Cross-Strait Expo has promoted cultural industry exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, achieved win-win results, and become an important platform for cultural exchange, cooperation, and investment and trade across the Taiwan Strait, with positive outcomes. This year's Expo is co-hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism, the National Radio and Television Administration, and the People's Government of Fujian Province. More than 30 events and 27 sub-venues will be organized. On behalf of the host organizations, I extend a warm welcome and sincere invitation to the media friends attending to cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央电视台记者","Recently, Taiwan's economic authorities said that even if the mainland were to terminate the ECFA, the impact on Taiwan's foreign trade would not exceed 5%. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The signing of the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait conformed to the objective needs of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, and was the inevitable result of more than 30 years of mutually complementary, mutually beneficial and integrated development of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges. Since ECFA was signed, positive progress has been made in the early harvest for trade in goods, the early harvest for trade in services, investment protection and promotion, industrial cooperation, customs cooperation, and cooperation on small and medium-sized enterprises, bringing tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. Taking the ECFA early harvest as an example: as of the end of June 2019, in the field of trade in goods, the mainland had cumulatively reduced or exempted tariffs on Taiwan by approximately RMB 37.53 billion (375.3亿元人民币), far exceeding the tariff reductions and exemptions enjoyed by mainland exports to Taiwan. In the field of trade in services, a total of 56 Taiwanese financial enterprises and 1,158 non-financial enterprises used the early harvest preferential policies to provide services on the mainland, and 41 Taiwanese films were approved for import into the mainland.\nThe follow-up ECFA agreement on trade in services was signed but did not take effect, and negotiations on the trade in goods agreement were forced to be interrupted. Everyone is very clear about the reasons, and everyone knows full well where the responsibility lies. As to what role the implementation of ECFA and its early harvest projects has played in Taiwan's economic development, how deep their impact has been on Taiwan's business community, and how much they have enhanced the well-being of the public, I believe everyone has a public judgment. ECFA was hard won. The DPP authorities, in order to grab electoral advantage, distort the facts and deliberately belittle and smear ECFA's role, once again exposing the political nature of their disregard for and willful harm to the well-being of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Reportedly, after Hong Kong implemented the “Prohibition on Face Covering Regulation,” the DPP authorities, disregarding that the island also has relevant regulations prohibiting masked protests, have wantonly attacked and slandered the HKSAR government. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The Hong Kong SAR Government has formulated and implemented the *Prohibition on Face Masks Regulation*. It is lawful, reasonable and sensible, conducive to stopping violence and chaos and restoring order, and is extremely necessary. The implementation of this regulation does not affect the rights and freedoms enjoyed by Hong Kong residents under the law, including the freedom of procession and assembly. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities seek to undermine the prosperity and stability of the Hong Kong SAR and to take political advantage from it. This scheme will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210205.htm"],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","Recently, a special seminar on the Taiwan Strait passage and the Kinmen–Matsu bridge project was held in Fuzhou. Experts from both sides of the Strait formed a preliminary plan for the bridges from Fuzhou to Matsu and from Xiamen to Kinmen. Taiwan’s MAC has claimed that this move is intended to “divide” Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","On October 13, a special seminar on the Taiwan Strait Passage and the Kinmen Bridge was held in Fuzhou. Scholars and experts from both sides of the Strait exchanged views and discussed topics including the construction model and economic benefits of the Taiwan Strait passage project, as well as bridge-linking plans for Fuzhou to Matsu and Xiamen to Kinmen, and shared research findings.\nOn January 2 of this year, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” proposing that cross-Strait links should be made fully accessible, and clearly stating that Kinmen and Matsu could take the lead in achieving water, electricity, gas and bridge connections with coastal areas of Fujian. We intend to serve Taiwan compatriots just as we serve mainland compatriots. The Fuzhou–Matsu and Xiamen–Kinmen bridges are important components of the “Taiwan Strait Passage.” Advancing the bridge-linking projects is an important measure to practice the people-centered development philosophy and respond to the livelihood demands of residents of Kinmen and Matsu. It helps Taiwan compatriots share the development opportunities on the mainland and promotes the integrated economic and social development of both sides. Relevant mainland authorities have fully launched preliminary research and demonstration work for the Rongma Bridge and the Xiamen–Kinmen Bridge. Far-sighted people on both sides have offered advice and suggestions on this matter; promoting early bridge construction is aimed at benefiting compatriots on both sides.\nAs for the DPP authorities, they have unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations, tried every means to obstruct economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, stood against the interests of the broad Taiwan compatriots, and deliberately restricted the development of Kinmen and Matsu. Such a mindset and such practices are not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210207.htm"],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Morris Chang will attend the APEC meeting for the third time this year, and outsiders expect him to meet with the leaders of China and the United States. What is the spokesperson's view?","On the question of Taiwan's participation in APEC-related activities, our position has always been very clear: it must comply with the One-China Principle and the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Some Taiwan businesspeople have reported difficulties with labeling for goods exported to the mainland. What is the spokesperson's view?","Our management policies on certificates of origin and on labels for imported and exported goods in cross-Strait trade have been in place for many years and have not changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Han Kuo-yu recently proposed a “cross-Strait policy white paper,” which mentions that there are currently no conditions for so-called unification or “independence,” and that this generation has no right to restrict the choices of the next generation. New Party Chairman Yu Mu-ming criticized this statement as evading the issue. What is the spokesperson’s view?","Our position on Taiwan policy is clear and explicit. Here I want to stress two points again. First, adherence to the one-China principle is the political foundation of cross-strait relations. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. We have repeatedly stated that adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and opposing “Taiwan independence,” will lead to the improvement and development of cross-strait relations, and the interests of Taiwan compatriots will be safeguarded and enhanced. Conversely, cross-strait relations will be damaged, the situation in the Taiwan Strait will become turbulent, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be harmed. Second, Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation. Realizing the reunification of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait at an early date is the shared wish of Chinese people at home and abroad. We are willing to continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen issued a statement on the 10th that was full of rhetoric such as \"the mainland threatens Taiwan and challenges regional stability and peace,\" and vigorously incited hatred toward the mainland. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","Regarding the speech delivered by the leader of the DPP authorities on October 10, we have already stated our position in writing. Here I want to further emphasize that this speech is brimming with confrontation and hostility. It attempts to slander and attack “One Country, Two Systems” in order to create an atmosphere of hatred toward the mainland, suppresses the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that hopes for economic development, improved livelihoods, and easing of cross-Strait relations, and seeks electoral self-interest. This speech turns black into white: it describes all the efforts of Chinese people to pursue peaceful reunification, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and maintain peaceful development of cross-Strait relations as a so-called “threat” to Taiwan. It caters to Western anti-China forces and describes the mainland's development and progress, and the process of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, as a so-called “challenge” to regional stability and peace. Once again, it exposes the “Taiwan independence” nature of the DPP authorities, which manufactures cross-Strait confrontation and conflict, undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, defies the mainstream public opinion on the island that seeks stability and good governance, and is hostile to the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.\nWe warn the DPP authorities once again: confrontation has no way out, and seeking “Taiwan independence” is an even more dead-end path. Those who harm the people's interests, defy public opinion, and go against the tide will all be abandoned by the trend of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","It is understood that, to meet the needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople who wish to return home, mainland civil aviation technical personnel communicated with the relevant parties in Taiwan about Spring Festival extra flights for 2020, but no reply has been received so far. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","Over the years, cross-Strait exchanges and visits have grown increasingly close, and the number of people traveling back and forth has continued to rise. Under the current circumstances, where resources such as airport slots and airlift capacity are very tight, the mainland’s civil aviation authorities and airlines have tried their best to add flights to the cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights and to provide the greatest possible support. We hope the Taiwan side will face the needs of Taiwan compatriots to return home and respond positively as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Reportedly, the number of mainland tourists visiting Taiwan during this year’s National Day “Golden Week” holiday is the lowest in 11 years, only one-third of the previous level. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","According to statistics, during the 2019 National Day “Golden Week” holiday, the number of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan fell sharply year on year. The reasons for the decline in mainland residents' travel to Taiwan are well known: the DPP authorities have constantly fanned “Taiwan independence” activities, continuously stirred up hostility toward the mainland, worsened the atmosphere for cross-Strait exchanges, and hurt the feelings of mainland compatriots; it inevitably affected the willingness of mainland people to travel to Taiwan. When cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good. Family affection between compatriots on both sides is the driving force behind mainland residents' travel to Taiwan. We believe that compatriots on both sides hope that cross-Strait relations will return to the correct track of peaceful development as soon as possible, and that mainland residents' travel to Taiwan can quickly return to normal and healthy development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191016_12210206.htm"],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Some Taiwanese media reported that the Taiwan authorities wrote to the President of INTERPOL in late January seeking to take part in this year’s INTERPOL General Assembly as an observer, but have not received a response to date. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: The Taiwan Interior Ministry recently issued a document slandering Hong Kong police as “black police,” claiming these “black police”…","On the first question: INTERPOL is an intergovernmental international organization, and Taiwan is not qualified to join it. Our position on Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations is clear and consistent: it must be handled through cross-strait consultation, in accordance with the One-China Principle and the charters of the international organizations concerned.\nOn the second question: facts have proven that the news circulating on Taiwan’s internet that Hong Kong police would move to Taiwan is an outright false rumor. For such a false message that violates basic common sense, the person in charge of the relevant department of the DPP authorities treated it as a treasure and hyped it up on the website, making himself a political joke. He smeared law enforcement officers who maintain law and order and protect the safety of people’s lives and property as “black police,” which is the same as his use of his personal authority to openly shield scandals such as the “private cigarette case” and the “high-speed rail lost cash case.” This shows that in his heart there is only party interest and no legal justice. Who is “black” and who is “white” is plain to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Regarding Sun Xiaoya, Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs at the U.S. Department of State, who recently traveled to Taiwan to attend the so-called “Pacific Dialogue,” what comment does the spokesperson have?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and tolerates no interference from any external force. The DPP has put together such a meeting only because it wants, through this small maneuver, to conceal the failure of its cross-Strait policy and its predicament in foreign affairs, and merely to dupe some votes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","A Hong Kong esports player was recently removed from a competition by the organizers for promoting “Hong Kong independence.” The U.S. NBA, over inappropriate remarks involving Hong Kong by a Rockets general manager, was boycotted by its mainland partners. Tsai Ing-wen said she would join all fans and players in safeguarding the values of “democracy” and “freedom.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Advocating “Hong Kong independence” and supporting violent activities has nothing to do with so-called “democracy and freedom”; rather, it openly undermines the rule of law in the Hong Kong SAR. Such inversion of right and wrong is nothing more than an attempt to grab electoral benefits, and Taiwan’s public sees this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","A mainland tourist angrily tore up a National Taiwan University poster supporting the Hong Kong rioters and was forcibly expelled by Taiwan authorities. What is the spokesperson's response?","The radical demonstrations and illegal violent activities taking place in Hong Kong have aroused strong indignation among Hong Kong citizens and Chinese people at home and abroad. Openly advocating “Hong Kong independence” and supporting illegal violent activities on Taiwan campuses will inevitably meet with strong opposition and resistance from all Chinese sons and daughters who care about and cherish Hong Kong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Taiwan's Ministry of the Interior statistics show that the number of cross-Strait marriages in 2018 set a record low since statistics began, indicating a trend of sharp decline. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Mainland spouses living in Taiwan have long been treated unreasonably in many respects, including acquisition of identity, employment rights and interests, and recognition of academic qualifications, causing harm to several hundred thousand cross-Strait marriage families. The DPP authorities should face the reasonable demands of cross-Strait marriage families and cancel, as soon as possible, the discriminatory and exclusionary policies targeting mainland spouses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","A responsible official of Taiwan’s defense department recently revealed in the United States that a so-called “overall defense concept” has been formulated targeting the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s assessment?","We have answered questions of this kind many times at press conferences. The greatest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait is the “Taiwan independence” forces and their secessionist activities. Confronting them with arms is a path that cannot be taken; it is a dead end. If it is merely to whistle in the dark to bolster one's courage, then it would be better not to walk the night road at all, and to return to the correct track of peaceful development of cross-strait relations based on the “1992 Consensus.” Only then will the situation in the Taiwan Strait and cross-strait relations take on an atmosphere of peace, tranquility, harmony and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-16","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","A hot term recently circulating on the island is \"dried mango,\" which uses a homophone to refer to the so-called \"sense of national demise.\" The Blue and Green camps accuse each other of hyping this topic. Some scholars have also questioned whether the \"dried mango\" tactic can actually conceal an unflattering \"report card.\" May I ask the spokesperson for your comment?","Everyone has noticed that, as Taiwan media have pointed out, this “mango dried” is a “poisoned wine” that flows with “green blood.” The DPP and its authorities deliberately hype this topic and create this atmosphere in order to incite cross-strait confrontation, create cross-strait hostility, and mobilize for elections to reap electoral gains. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, will not be fooled by this deceptive trick and will not dance along with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191016_12210219.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-10-23","Hua Chunying","","Regarding the case of a murder suspect Chan Tong-kai, the Hong Kong SAR has asked Taiwan to take him to Taiwan for trial. However, Hong Kong has rejected Taiwan's offer to send a delegation to bring him back to Taiwan. Do you have any explanations to why Hong Kong would take that position?","This is not a diplomatic matter. The Hong Kong SAR government will properly handle it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1710130.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201910/t20191023_5418162.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-10-24","Hua Chunying","","Yesterday Prime Minister Abe asked Vice President Wang Qishan to provide assistance to the case of the detained Japanese professor in China. I wonder if you have any specific information on that?","I can share some information on Vice President Wang Qishan's meeting with Prime Minister Shinzo Abe. As President Xi Jinping's special envoy, Vice President Wang Qishan paid a friendly visit to Japan and met with Prime Minister Abe yesterday.\nVice President Wang said that in June this year, President Xi and Prime Minister Abe reached important consensus on fostering a China-Japan relationship in keeping with the need of the new era, ushering in new development opportunities to bilateral relations. The two sides need to abide by principles set by the four political documents between China and Japan and properly handle historical issues and the question of Taiwan, so that our bilateral relations can progress along the track of peace, friendship and cooperation.\nPrime Minister Abe said that Japan and China are deepening economic and trade cooperation, and that both countries are shouldering major responsibilities to peace and prosperity in Asia and the world. Both Japan and China are stepping into their new eras. The Osaka summit between two leaders brought bilateral relations fully back to normal, promising immense potential for future cooperation. The Japanese side looks forward to President Xi's state visit in spring next year. Japan will properly handle sensitive issues including those relating to Taiwan. The Japanese side stands ready to work with China for a future-oriented, vibrant relationship.\nAs to the case you mentioned, I commented a few days ago. The Japanese side knows that very well. The Chinese side lawfully handles the case involving a foreign citizen who has broken Chinese law. Pursuant to the Agreement on Consular Relations Between China and Japan, the Chinese side has offered necessary assistance to the Japanese side in fulfilling consular duties.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1710515.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201910/t20191024_5418168.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-10-25","Hua Chunying","N/A — opening announcement (no press Q)","","Invited by Prime Minister Aripov of Uzbekistan and Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha of Thailand, from November 1 to 5, Premier Li Keqiang will attend the 18th Meeting of the SCO Council of Heads of Government in Tashkent, Uzbekistan, pay an official visit to Uzbekistan, attend the 22nd China-ASEAN Summit, the 22nd ASEAN Plus China, Japan and ROK Summit and the 14th East Asia Summit in Bangkok, Thailand, and pay an official visit to Thailand.\nIn his speech on October 24, US Vice President Pence intentionally misrepresented China's social system, human rights and religious conditions, and wantonly criticized China's domestic and foreign policies. These remarks, just like those in his speech last October, are full of political bias and lies, and reveal nothing but his arrogance and hypocrisy. China expresses strong indignation and firm opposition to them.\nSince the People's Republic of China was founded 70 years ago, the Chinese people, under the leadership of the CPC, have found a development path in line with the country's national realities and achieved great progress to the amazement of the world. China has made historic leaps from finding its feet to becoming prosperous and strong. More than 800 million Chinese people have been lifted out of poverty. China now has the world's largest number of middle-incomers. China's economic growth rate has been leading major world economies and it has been contributing over 30% to world economic growth for many consecutive years. China is now the world's second largest economy, the largest industrial nation, and the largest trader in goods. History and facts have illustrated that the path China chose is the right one that enjoys support and endorsement of the Chinese people. We have every confidence in this path and will press ahead for greater victory while committed to socialism with Chinese characteristics. No force could prevent the Chinese people and nation in their way forward.\nThe most important criteria on China's human rights situation is whether the Chinese people are satisfied. As the country advances in leaps and bounds, the Chinese people have an increasingly stronger sense of happiness and fulfillment. Our government attaches high importance to protecting and advancing human rights. During the past over four decades of reform and opening-up, China's human rights cause has seen tremendous progress that has been recognized by the world. The Chinese people now enjoy unprecedented rights and freedoms. This is a fact that no one can deny except for those obsessed with prejudice. Nearly 200 million Chinese practice various religions, of which more than 20 million are Muslim. Chinese people of all ethnic groups enjoy full religious freedom in accordance with law.\nThe Chinese government resolutely safeguards national sovereignty, security and development interests. Issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are all China's domestic affairs where no external forces shall interfere. A handful of US politicians headed by Mr. Pence are distorting facts with wanton accusations and slanders to meddle in China's internal affairs with an attempt to disrupt China's stability and development. However, just as dark clouds cannot block the sunshine, lies cannot cover truth. The Chinese people do not believe in fallacy. Nor are we afraid of evil forces. Any attempt at undermining China's national unity, ethnic solidarity and social stability or pinning blames on China will end up nowhere and is bound to be rejected by history.\nChina is committed to reform and opening up and to protecting intellectual property rights. Our policy aiming to create a favorable environment for foreign investment will not change. Our policy dedicated to protecting foreign businesses' lawful rights and interests will not change. All foreign companies abiding by Chinese laws and regulations enjoy full business autonomy in their operation. There is no such thing as enterprises being \"coerced\".\nChina's foreign policy is aboveboard as always. China pursues an independent foreign policy of peace, a path of peaceful development, a new type of international relations and a community with a shared future for mankind. China never advances its own interests at the expense of others, and its development will never pose a threat to any country. China never seeks hegemony or expansion. That's exactly why we have so many friends all over the world. Some people's attempts to wantonly label China or drive a wedge between China and other countries will never succeed. Such attempts will bring nothing but shame on those people themselves.\nWhile arbitrarily accusing and lecturing other countries, Mr. Pence and his like have turned a blind eye to serious domestic problems in the US and tried to cover their own political malpractice by smearing other countries to divert public attention in the US. From the PRISM program to frequent, severe shootings, from extensive racial discrimination to obvious wealth gap, from arbitrary sanctions and use of force on other countries to wanton withdrawals from international agreements and treaties, there are so many cases in point proving that the US has become notorious for lack of moral principles and credibility. We advise some people in the US to carefully examine themselves in the mirror, get fully aware of their own problems and mind their own business. They should cease talking utter nonsense and stop playing mutually detrimental tricks as soon as possible.\nChina's position on China-US relations is consistent and clear. Our bilateral relationship is not zero-sum, where two countries stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. For China and the US, the right thing to do is have mutual respect and seek common grounds. China-US relationship is currently in a critical stage. We urge the US to consider the fundamental interests of both countries and peoples, respect the truth, correct wrongs, and stop making irresponsible remarks and damaging bilateral relations, trust and cooperation. It needs to follow the consensus established by the two leaders, act on the basic tone of coordination, cooperation and stability, manage differences with mutual respect, expand mutually beneficial cooperation, and work for steady progress in China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1710842.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201910/t20191025_5418174.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear media friends, good morning! Welcome to the press conference. I will now take questions from you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The 2019 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit at Purple Mountain is about to be held. What are the features of this year's summit?","The 2019 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit will be held in Nanjing from November 3 to 5, and cross-Strait entrepreneurs have registered enthusiastically to attend this session of the summit. At present, more than 40 central state-owned enterprises and a group of well-known private enterprises have registered to attend, and the heads of major Taiwan industrial and commercial groups as well as a group of heavyweight entrepreneurs have also completed registration. During the summit, cross-Strait industrial exchange and cooperation agreements and project signings will also be held, and the cooperation outcomes are expected to exceed those of previous sessions. This session of the summit will also host an exhibition on the construction of the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Park and the \"Belt and Road\" parks, and an exhibition of achievements of the Jiangsu Province Taiwan Youth Internship, Employment and Entrepreneurship program.\nIt is worth mentioning that all localities and departments in Jiangsu attach great importance to the implementation of the \"31 Measures,\" and a series of concrete results have already been achieved. Across the province, nearly 1,100 Taiwan-funded enterprises have enjoyed the preferential corporate income tax policies for high-tech enterprises, with a total reduction of 3.13 billion yuan in enterprise income tax. The Huai'an Shilian Chemical Electronic Specialty Chemicals project, the Huai'an Qingding Precision Electronic Multilayer Flexible Circuit Board project, and the Nanjing TSMC project have been designated as major projects of Jiangsu Province for 2019 and will receive equal preferential policy support. To provide more convenience for Taiwan youths to realize their dreams on the mainland, this year Jiangsu launched the \"2019 Jiangsu Province Taiwan Youth Internship Special Support Plan,\" and the total number of Taiwan interns in Jiangsu has exceeded one thousand; 122 outstanding Taiwan youth representatives received scholarships and student aid. Life for Taiwan compatriots in Jiangsu has become more convenient: nearly 10,000 Taiwan students are studying in primary, secondary and tertiary schools of all kinds in Jiangsu, 92 hospitals in the province have been designated as medical institutions for Taiwan businesspeople, and more than 3,300 Taiwan compatriots in Jiangsu participate in the basic pension insurance for enterprise employees. This year, 6 Taiwan compatriots have been awarded the Jiangsu Province \"May 1st Labor Medal,\" and 30 Taiwan-funded enterprises have received the Jiangsu Province \"Zifeng Award\" from the Jiangsu Provincial People's Government.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213892.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","After Chen Tong-chia was released from prison upon completing his sentence and said he was willing to go to Taiwan to surrender, the DPP authorities' attitude and statements on handling this case have been inconsistent and have changed repeatedly, full of political manipulation. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Everyone has noticed that the Hong Kong SAR government has issued multiple statements on this matter and is handling the relevant incident. The DPP authorities should stop engaging in political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213896.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Given public attention to whether the ECFA will face termination when it expires after ten years next year, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council recently said it does not wish to see the mainland stop implementing cross-strait agreements for political reasons. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Since the signing of ECFA, the mainland side has earnestly fulfilled its commitments to ensure the smooth entry into force and implementation of ECFA. As of the end of June 2019, for early harvest products in goods trade, the mainland has cumulatively reduced or exempted tariffs on Taiwan goods by 37.53 billion yuan. It is especially worth pointing out that the early harvest product list has brought tangible and great benefits to small and medium-sized enterprises and to farmers and fishermen on the island. From 2010 to 2018, Taiwan's agricultural product exports to the mainland under the early harvest list grew threefold, and the mainland has become the largest market for Taiwan's agricultural exports.\nThe tariff reduction arrangements and opening measures under the early harvest plan account for only a small part of cross-Strait trade and market opening. Regrettably, for reasons that are well known, the ECFA Subsequent Agreement on Trade in Services has not taken effect after signing, negotiations on the goods trade agreement were forced to be interrupted, and ECFA has been unable to benefit more Taiwan compatriots. Who is working for the well-being of compatriots and businesses on both sides, and who is harming the interests of compatriots and businesses on both sides in order to seek political gain, is plain to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that its poll shows 27.7% of respondents support so-called Taiwan “independence,” and 89.3% of respondents do not agree with “one country, two systems.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The Mainland Affairs Council is choosing to publish and sensationalize this so-called opinion poll at the current moment. Everyone is surely clear about its purpose. Everyone is also clear about the Mainland Affairs Council's capacity to manufacture data. Attempting to raise confrontation between the two sides of the Strait in order to gain electoral advantage will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213894.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Some green media outlets have recently been hyping that, because the Golden Horse Awards and Golden Rooster Awards overlap this year, the mainland's suspension of films and personnel traveling to Taiwan to attend the Golden Horse Awards is a “suppression” act. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have repeatedly stated that the DPP authorities' continued creation of incidents that undermine cross-Strait relations and interfere with cross-Strait exchanges is the sole and fundamental reason the mainland film industry suspended its participation in the 2019 Golden Horse Film Festival.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","According to reports, Rene Liu (刘若英) and other Taiwan filmmakers and related works have been shortlisted for this year's Golden Rooster Awards. This is the first time since the release and implementation of the “31 Measures” that Taiwan filmmakers and co-produced works have registered for and been shortlisted for the Golden Rooster Awards. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The China Film Golden Rooster Awards were established in 1981. They are a national awards event sponsored by the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles and the China Film Association, and are known as the “experts’ award” of Chinese cinema. Since 2005, film professionals from Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan have been eligible to compete for the China Film Golden Rooster Awards, and over the years, several Taiwan film professionals have won awards and received nominations.\nThat Taiwan film professionals and their works competed for and received nominations for the Golden Rooster Awards this year is yet another manifestation of implementing the relevant measures in the “31 measures” encouraging co-production of films and television series across the Strait and “supporting the inclusion of Taiwan in nominations for all kinds of award programs in the economic, scientific, cultural, and social fields.” We congratulate them on receiving nominations. The mainland side will, as always, encourage film professionals on both sides of the Strait to strengthen cooperation, promote the common development of the film and television industries across the Strait, build up and strengthen the film industry that belongs to the Chinese nation, and jointly promote Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213893.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Yesterday, the DPP caucus in Taiwan's legislature temporarily changed the agenda and sent several “Chinese Communist Party agent bills” to the Internal Administration Committee after the first reading. Under the DPP's version, Taiwan residents who attend meetings on the mainland or sign relevant statements in the future could face prison terms of up to three years. What is the spokesperson's view? In addition,…","The so-called amendment of the “Chinese Communist Party agents” law is a revival of the “White Terror.” Its purpose is to comprehensively incite cross-Strait confrontation and create hostility across the Strait, to persecute parties, groups and individuals who hold different positions, to intimidate and punish Taiwan residents who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, and to muzzle critical public opinion on the island. It is entirely driven by the private interests of one party and one individual, and has already met strong opposition from all sectors of Taiwan society. We once again warn the DPP authorities: they must pull back from the brink.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Two questions. First, Han Kuo-yu and Tsai Ing-wen have recently each made statements on cross-Strait relations. What is your view of their remarks? Second, the mainland has signed a “Defense Exchange and Security Cooperation Agreement” with Singapore. Will the mainland demand that Singapore terminate its “Starlight Program” with Taiwan?","I will answer the second question first: regarding national defense exchanges and security cooperation between China and New Zealand, please direct your inquiry to the Ministry of National Defense. On Taiwan-related issues, our position is consistent and clear: we firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China.\nOn the first question: there is only one China in the world, the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are not divided and are not divisible. Within this framework, the two sides of the Strait should adhere to the \"1992 Consensus,\" uphold the sentiment of kinship and compatriot affection to promote exchange and cooperation in all fields, and resolve their differences and problems through equal consultation. I believe this is the correct way for cross-Strait relations to be handled. The history of cross-Strait relations has provided examples of this from both positive and negative perspectives. Any responsible political figure in Taiwan should truthfully tell Taiwan's young people the real situation and the reasoning behind it: only on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus\" can cross-Strait relations develop sustainably over the long term and create win-win outcomes for both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have frequently interfered with exchanges between schools across the Strait, and the Mainland Affairs Council and the education department have also claimed they will study a notification mechanism for schools at all levels going to the mainland for exchanges. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Recently, the “black hand” with which the DPP seeks to obstruct and restrict cross-strait exchanges and cooperation has reached into campuses. They frequently make statements and use various pretexts to interfere with and restrict normal exchanges between cross-strait schools, attempting to deprive Taiwanese teachers and students of their exchange rights and thereby harm their interests. Strengthening civil exchanges and personnel contacts across the Strait is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides and the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. This is something no force can block or confine.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213895.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻记者","The Beijing Xiangshan Forum has just concluded. The Mainland Affairs Council says the Xiangshan Forum has become a “venue for criticizing the U.S. and intimidating Taiwan.” What is your assessment?","The Mainland Affairs Council's statement is complete nonsense. Since its founding in 2006, the Beijing Xiangshan Forum has held nine sessions. It has become the highest-level and largest-scale “Track 1.5” security dialogue platform hosted by the mainland. It has achieved the goals of enhancing security mutual trust, communicating policy positions, leading security dialogue and promoting exchanges and cooperation, and it helps countries in the region increase mutual understanding and trust and reduce misunderstanding and miscalculation.\nThe mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and maintaining peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” is the guarantee of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” is what safeguards peace in the Taiwan Strait, safeguards the prosperity and stability of the Asia-Pacific region, and safeguards the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides. I must correct the erroneous statement of the Mainland Affairs Council: opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” is not intimidation of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","After Taiwan was successively \"severed\" by the Solomon Islands and Kiribati, Saint Vincent and the Grenadines recently also turned on a red light. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Adhering to the One-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, it reflects the wishes of the people and the trend of history, and this trend will continue to develop. For specifics, please direct your inquiries to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Two questions. First, after the DPP authorities took office, they altered history curricula, which has sparked dissatisfaction on the island. What is the spokesperson's evaluation? Second, US Vice President Pence made pro-Taiwan remarks on the 24th, saying he would stand with Taiwan, and Taiwan's foreign contact department expressed gratitude. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Let me first address the first question. The so-called “new curriculum guidelines” launched under the lead of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces forget their roots, glorify colonial rule, attempt to sever the historical and cultural ties across the Strait, and are full of “de-Sinicization” content. They not only poison the younger generation in Taiwan but further undermine cross-Strait relations and intensify cross-Strait confrontation, and they will inevitably meet strong opposition from Taiwan society.\nOn the second question, regarding this speech by Mr. Pence of the United States, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already set out our position in full. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers to elevate themselves and willing to act as pawns, are contemptible. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no interference by foreign forces. We hope the U.S. side will earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues appropriately, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","On October 24, two mainland vessels and 28 crew members were detained by the Taiwan authorities on the pretext of “crossing the boundary.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We are following the development of the incident. The relevant Taiwan authorities should protect the legitimate rights and interests of the parties concerned and handle the matter properly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","Recently, Lee Teng-hui has sought to pursue so-called “Taiwan independence” and “constitutional reform” by supporting Tsai Ing-wen's re-election. What is the spokesperson's assessment of this? Second question: regarding the revision of the curriculum, the head of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently argued that the revision of Taiwan's primary and secondary school history textbooks is not government-led…","Let me answer the second question first: The Mainland Affairs Council's explanation is a cover-up and an excuse, a case of “protesting too much.” In the “Taiwan independence” activities that have been carefully planned and gradually promoted under the banner of “de-Sinicization,” the DPP and its authorities are the masterminds behind the scenes. Their sophistry and denials are useless, and everyone can see this very clearly.\nReturning to the first question, we have repeatedly stated that we firmly oppose altering Taiwan's status as part of China through so-called “constitutional revision,” “renaming,” or similar means. Lee Teng-hui's proposition has touched the bottom line of all Chinese people, and it is impossible for it to succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The “Double Eleven” shopping festival is approaching, and the newly launched online shopping platform “Taobao Taiwan” has recently officially entered the island. The DPP authorities claim this is Mainland capital circumventing restrictions to seize the market and that it must be investigated and stopped. What is the spokesperson's assessment?","Since the “Double Eleven” e-commerce shopping festival was first launched in 2009, November 11 has become a nationwide shopping feast each year, and it has won enthusiastic response and active participation from Taiwan residents and businesses. This time, “Taobao Taiwan” went online in Taiwan to provide local services to Taiwan residents and businesses, and offers consumers many discounts during this year's “Double Eleven.” We are glad to see Taiwan residents gain real benefits and interests.\nThe DPP authorities have never taken the people's interests seriously. At every turn they cut off roads, dig pits, and build walls. Apart from harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, this will have no effect whatsoever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《旺报》记者","Today the US Senate passed the “Taipei Act,” requiring the US executive branch to take proactive action to support Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We firmly oppose the U.S. side's use of a series of so-called Taiwan-related acts to interfere in the Taiwan question and in China's internal affairs. This position is clear and consistent. The Taiwan authorities' pursuit of so-called “diplomatic” relations is nothing but a fool's dream and can never be realized. The United States is playing the “Taiwan card,” and the DPP authorities are willing to serve as its pawn. In the end, what is harmed is peace in the Taiwan Strait region and the interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","We note that China's business environment has risen to 31st place globally. What opportunities will this bring for Taiwan businesses?","I have also noted this news. Further improvement of the business environment on the mainland helps us further expand opening up and attract more foreign businesses and investment to develop on the mainland. Of course, this also includes providing better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to invest and start businesses on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The State Council recently published the revised contents of the “Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Insurance Companies” and the “Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Banks.” Do these revisions apply to Taiwan-funded financial enterprises, and what impact will they have on Taiwan-funded financial services?","On October 15, the State Council announced its decision to amend the Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Insurance Companies and the Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Banks. Through this revision, the market access conditions for foreign-funded insurance companies and foreign banks have been relaxed, which will further accelerate the process of opening up the financial sector. For example, the revised Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Insurance Companies lower the conditions for applying to establish foreign-funded insurance companies on the mainland and eliminate the requirement that a foreign insurance company have been engaged in the insurance business for 30 years. The revised Regulations on the Administration of Foreign-Funded Banks lower the threshold for establishing wholly foreign-owned banks and Sino-foreign joint venture banks, and relax business restrictions on foreign banks.\nThe above opening measures apply equally to Taiwan-funded financial institutions, and will provide a rare opportunity for Taiwan-funded financial institutions to share in the mainland's development gains.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201910/t20191030_12213897.htm"],[2,"2019-10-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","I have two questions. First, Taiwan's “Investigation Bureau” recently said that two posts on Facebook involving Tsai Ing-wen were “fake news,” that their publishers are mainland individuals, and that it will ask Facebook to take them down, while using the occasion to continue accusing and attacking the mainland. What comments does the spokesperson have? Second, please introduce the progress of preparations…","First question: As we understand it, these two items of news originated from a personal fan page and are the author's personal observations and interpretations of Taiwan society. The DPP and its authorities, in order to manipulate elections and divert public criticism, always direct their arrows toward the mainland and fabricate rumors and smear it; this is their habitual tactic.\nSecond question: Preparations for the second China International Import Expo (CIIE) are proceeding in an orderly manner. This year, Taiwan enterprises have registered to exhibit with great enthusiasm, and the number has increased substantially compared with last year. We are willing to promote the products of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the large platform of the CIIE, provide convenience for expanding the domestic market for Taiwan products, and strive to ensure that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises participating in the exhibition gain tangible benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201910/t20191030_12213890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-10-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have 3 questions. First, according to media reports, the second aircraft carrier was painted with the hull number recently. Does this mean it will be commissioned soon? Can you confirm that? Second, according to Japanese Kyodo News Agency’s report on October 29, China and Russia are talking about building an alliance between the two countries. The former US house speaker said to Fox News on October 27 that if…","For your first question, China's second aircraft carrier is carrying out various tests as planned and steady progress is being made in the tests. The time for commissioning depends on its construction progress and tests.\nFor your second question, China pursues an independent foreign policy of peace. The China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination in the new era features non-alliance, non-confrontation and is not targeted against any third country. It is an example of the new model of international relations featuring mutual respect, equality, justice and win-win cooperation. It is completely different from the military alliance between some other countries. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. China firmly opposes irresponsible remarks by the US side.\nFor your third question, in addition to independent research and development of weaponry and equipment, China also pursues active military technological cooperation with friendly countries, which is not targeted at any third party. It is beneficial to regional and global peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-11/01/content_4854325.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-10-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first is that some officials from Taiwan said that the Beijing Xiangshan Forum has become a platform to criticize the US and intimidate Taiwan, and it cannot help improve security in the Asian Pacific but undermine regional peace. What’s your response to that? The second question is that according to media reports, Taiwan plans to purchase 66 F-16V fighters from the United States, and a…","On your first question, the comment from Taiwan is not consistent with facts. Since its inception in 2006, the Beijing Xiangshan forum has been successfully held 9 times. The Forum has been growing in terms of its size, level, influence and fame. It is now the largest and highest-level track 1.5 security dialogue hosted by China. It has helped countries enhance trust, coordinate policies, promote security dialogue and strengthen cooperation.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. Following the 1992 Consensus and safeguarding peaceful development is a guarantee for peace and stability across the Strait. The \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their activities are the biggest threat to the peace and stability across the Strait. National reunification is the right course and separatist movement is a dead end. Taiwan should get a clear understanding of its situation, abandon Taiwan “independence” and confrontation, stop its irresponsible remarks and make more contributions to the improvement and development of the relationship across the Strait.\nMaintaining peace and stability in the Asian Pacific is in the common interests of regional countries, and calls for the wisdom and strength from all countries. We need more dialogues instead of confrontations, and we need cooperation to achieve harmony. We need more platforms like the Beijing Xiangshan Forum to help regional countries to strengthen mutual trust and reduce misunderstanding and misjudgment.\nFor your second question, we are firmly opposed to any arms sale by any country to Taiwan. Any attempt of using force to resist reunification is doomed to fail.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-11/01/content_4854325.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2019-11-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 4 (reporter Li Hanfang): Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 4th that just as cross-Strait business communities and compatriots on both sides were deeply encouraged and warmly welcomed the “26 measures” for benefiting Taiwan compatriots announced by the mainland, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council rushed to hold forth and smear them, further exposing their dark mentality of being hostile to the interests of the broad Taiwan compatriots.\nMa Xiaoguang said that more than a year ago, when the mainland announced the “31 measures” for benefiting Taiwan compatriots, the Mainland Affairs Council and the DPP authorities vilified them in every way. The facts are that the “31 measures” were warmly welcomed by the broad Taiwan compatriots, and more and more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have benefited from them. We continue to introduce new “26 measures” for benefiting Taiwan compatriots in order to further respond to the demands of Taiwan compatriots, so that they can share the mainland's development opportunities in a wider scope and wider areas, and hope they develop better and gain greater benefits. In contrast, the DPP authorities turn a deaf ear to the calls of the public and are blind to the suffering of ordinary people. Apart from fabricating rumors and smearing, they resort to intimidation and punishment, constantly setting obstacles to the Taiwan compatriots' access to benefits and well-being, and undermining the good deeds for Taiwan compatriots at every turn. The remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council are not surprising. It is conceivable that the more we do good deeds, do practical things, and solve difficulties for the interests of Taiwan compatriots, the higher they will jump. In their minds, there is only political manipulation for the sake of one party, with no regard for the well-being of the people.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, with close ties and mutual affection. Where the people wish to go, government policy will follow. As long as something is conducive to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, we will persistently keep doing it. The DPP authorities cannot block the “31 measures,” and they likewise cannot block the “26 measures.” Whoever is hostile to the interests of the broad Taiwan compatriots will ultimately be abandoned by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191104_12215363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 7 (reporter Chen Jianxing): In response to Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities' recent claim that the mainland's “26 measures” are meant to “force” Taiwan to accept the “‘One Country, Two Systems’ Taiwan plan,” Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answering reporters' questions on the 7th, said that the DPP authorities are deliberately confusing public opinion and deceiving the people. This further exposes that they care only about party self-interest and completely disregard the interests of the Taiwan people. The common people have their own scales in their hearts. The DPP authorities' sinister intent in political manipulation will not succeed.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that following the “31 measures,” on November 4 the mainland introduced another set of “26 measures” benefiting Taiwan compatriots and the people, which is another concrete manifestation of our implementation of the people-centered development philosophy in our work on Taiwan. We continue to provide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises with more equal treatment and share mainland development opportunities with them, enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. These measures have been widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191107_12216346.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear media friends, good morning! The press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The Fourth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China decided on a special provision stating “adhere to and improve the “one country, two systems” institutional system and advance the peaceful reunification of the motherland.” Please interpret this and explain how it will be implemented.","The “Decision of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Several Major Issues Concerning Upholding and Improving the Socialist System with Chinese Characteristics and Advancing the Modernization of the National Governance System and Governance Capacity,” adopted by the Fourth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, makes “upholding and improving the ‘one country, two systems’ institutional system and advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland” an important component of the major strategic task for the whole Party of upholding and improving the socialist system with Chinese characteristics and advancing the modernization of the national governance system and governance capacity. It clarifies the goals and tasks of upholding and improving the ‘one country, two systems’ institutional system and advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland in the new era. It fully demonstrates the strong institutional advantages of upholding ‘one country, two systems’ and advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland, and provides a solid institutional guarantee for advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland in the new era.\nWe must thoroughly study, understand, and implement the decision of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee, comprehensively implement Comrade Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan, and especially the spirit of his important speech of January 2 this year. We must give full play to the institutional advantages of socialism with Chinese characteristics, work hard to do well the work concerning Taiwan in the new era, advance cross-Strait relations of peaceful development, and firmly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nWe will adhere to the development philosophy of putting the people first, and starting from the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people, we will continuously improve institutional arrangements and policy measures that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We will continue to provide equal treatment over a wider scope and in more fields for Taiwan compatriots to study, live, work, and start businesses and innovate on the mainland, and create more favorable conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to broadly participate in the mainland's economic construction and to share the mainland's development opportunities first. We will actively promote the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation, build a common cross-Strait market, and strengthen top-level design in promoting cross-Strait “connectivity of everything possible” and the “small four links” between Fujian's coastal areas and Kinmen and Matsu, and introduce relevant policies.\nWe will continue to adhere to the policy of placing hope in the Taiwan people, and as always respect, care for, unite with, and rely on Taiwan compatriots. We will expand civil exchanges, enhance mutual understanding, narrow psychological distances, and achieve heartfelt agreement, and we will unite broad Taiwan compatriots to jointly oppose “Taiwan independence” and promote unification.\nWe will continue to engage in dialogue and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” conduct extensive exchanges of views on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, seek social consensus, and gradually resolve the long-standing political differences across the Strait by seeking common ground while setting aside differences, so as to reach institutional arrangements for peaceful development across the Strait.\nIn the 70 years since the founding of New China, through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, the situation in the Taiwan Strait has moved from tense confrontation to easing and improvement, and then onto the path of peaceful development. Cross-Strait relations have continuously achieved breakthrough progress, and the community of shared destiny across the Strait has become an increasingly vivid reality. Today we are closer than at any time in history to, and more confident and capable of, achieving the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and we are better able and better positioned to advance the reunification of the motherland. The Taiwan question arose from the weakness and turmoil of the nation, and it will also come to an end with the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217881.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","Recently, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with relevant departments, issued the “26 measures,” which have sparked heated public debate. What is the background and significance of the current issuance of the “26 measures”? The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are hyping this topic to peddle a sense of “national collapse.” What is your view on this?","We have issued the “26 Measures” to further promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation. Their purpose is to implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech of January 2, to improve the institutional arrangements and policy measures that promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, so that more Taiwan compatriots can be the first to share the mainland's development opportunities, and to provide more equal treatment for Taiwanese businesses and enterprises.\nThe purpose of the “26 Measures” is a continuation of the “31 Measures,” and both embody the people-centered development philosophy in our Taiwan work, treating Taiwan compatriots equally, and benefiting Taiwan compatriots in the same way we serve the people on the mainland.\nThe “26 Measures” include 13 measures providing equal treatment to Taiwanese enterprises, covering the equal participation of Taiwan-funded enterprises in investment and construction in major technology equipment, 5G, circular economy, civil aviation, theme parks, new types of financial organizations and other areas, equal access to financing, trade remedies, export credit insurance, import and export facilitation, standard setting and other policies, and support for the construction of cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration points. They also include 13 measures providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots, offering greater convenience and support to Taiwan compatriots in areas such as consular protection, agricultural cooperation, transportation, communication fees, eligibility for home purchases, culture and sports, professional title evaluation, and categorized recruitment examinations.\nThe “26 Measures” are all “real and substantial” measures that bring greater development opportunities and greater interests and well-being to Taiwan compatriots. This is a good thing for enhancing the interests of Taiwan compatriots. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities should keep the cold and hardships of Taiwan compatriots in mind, and should not interpret these measures through an overly politicized lens, much less intimidate or punish Taiwan compatriots. Doing so does not conform to the will of the people. If they really want to engage in political maneuvering, they should understand that the interests of the people and the will of the people are the greatest politics.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217880.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Regarding the “26 Measures” proposing that Taiwan-funded enterprises may participate in the construction and application of the mainland's 5G networks, Taiwan's National Communications Commission (NCC) said it does not approve of Taiwan operators going to the mainland to participate in 5G construction, and proposed numerous restrictions. What is the spokesperson's comment?","As the new generation of mobile communication technology, 5G has attracted high attention around the world. The mainland's information and communications market is enormous, and the prospects for 5G industry development are broad, which will bring new and huge business opportunities to Taiwan-related enterprises. Where the market and opportunities lie, I believe Taiwan businesses have their own judgment. We welcome Taiwan-funded enterprises to take part in the construction and application of 5G networks on the mainland and to share in the development opportunities of 5G.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","According to reports, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said that since the release and implementation of the “31 Measures,” their actual impact on Taiwan has not been obvious, and also said that recently Taiwan businesses have returned to Taiwan in large numbers to invest, while investment on the mainland has decreased and the number of people working on the mainland will also decrease. What is the…","Since the “31 Measures” were issued more than a year ago, 102 localities, in light of their actual conditions, have successively formulated specific implementation opinions, providing equal treatment and more convenient conditions for the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Many Taiwan-funded enterprises have obtained “real gold and silver” benefits in areas such as tax preferences, capital subsidies, participation in major action plans and R&D projects, and participation in infrastructure construction. Many Taiwan compatriots have gained more opportunities and conveniences in professional qualification examinations, applications for various funds and talent programs, receiving honorary titles, employment, and daily life.\nIn the first three quarters of this year, the number of Taiwan business investment projects on the mainland and the actual amount used increased year on year by 11.2% and 39.6%, respectively. This shows that the mainland remains the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to invest and build businesses. The mainland's market capacity is large enough, its workforce is highly skilled enough, its industrial conditions are good enough, and its government is dedicated and accountable enough. Any enterprise that respects reality and is willing to seize opportunities will acknowledge this. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to come to the mainland to develop and share in its development opportunities and dividends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217876.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The “26 Measures” propose that Taiwan compatriots may seek consular protection and assistance at our overseas embassies and consulates, and apply for travel documents. What travel documents can Taiwan compatriots currently apply for? The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan says the mainland is using this to belittle Taiwan’s so-called “sovereignty.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. Safeguarding the lawful and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas is our unshirkable responsibility. Looking back at recent years: when war broke out in Libya, when an earthquake struck New Zealand, and when flood disasters hit Japan, the lives and property of Taiwan compatriots were threatened, and they were isolated and helpless, even at their wits’ end. Extending a helping hand was, for us, an unshirkable duty. “Compatriots, compatriots, born of the same mother’s milk” is the meaning of compatriot. Likewise, when Taiwan compatriots traveling, studying, living, or working abroad encounter difficulties such as lost documents, our overseas embassies and consulates will naturally provide assistance. Faced with such acts of compatriot assistance, the DPP authorities still make idle talk and unwarranted accusations. We must ask: do they still have the interests of the Taiwan people in mind? Of course, this disregard for the common people in their words and deeds has been consistent, and it is not surprising at all. Our work to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots overseas will not stop because of this. In the future we will do even better and work even harder.\nAs for specific questions about Taiwan compatriots applying for travel documents and handling procedures at Chinese embassies and consulates abroad, please refer to the relevant content of the “26 Measures,” and you may also refer to the websites of our overseas embassies and consulates or call the consular protection consultation hotline publicly announced by China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217877.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","It is reported that the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) is expected to be signed next year, while the DPP says Taiwan has little chance of participating in the future. Some public opinion on the island holds that this will affect Taiwan’s export trade. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","From 2008 to 2016, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” both sides across the Strait promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and achieved fruitful results in all areas. In fact, on the question of connecting cross-Strait economic cooperation with the regional economic integration process, Taiwan once had opportunities, but the DPP authorities single-handedly undermined this situation. With the imminent signing and implementation of the RCEP, the adverse consequences of the DPP authorities' undermining of cross-Strait relations and harming of Taiwan's economy will further become apparent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The second China International Import Expo has concluded. Please spokesperson introduce the participation of Taiwan enterprises.","From November 5 to 10, the Second China International Import Expo was successfully held in Shanghai. During the expo, a total of 124 Taiwan enterprises took part in the commercial exhibition, an increase of 72 percent over last year. The exhibited products were spread across all seven exhibition zones: technology and lifestyle, automobiles, equipment, medical devices and healthcare, quality living, services trade, and food and agricultural products.\nTo further assist Taiwan enterprises in opening the mainland market, the TAO, together with relevant departments of the Ministry of Commerce, also held a promotion and matchmaking event for well-known Taiwan food products. It attracted more than 70 well-known Taiwan food companies, several mainland e-commerce platforms, and more than 60 offline food agents and distributors from Fujian, Guangdong, Shanghai, Hubei, and other provinces and municipalities. At the matchmaking event, mainland e-commerce companies signed strategic cooperation agreements with several Taiwan enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please spokesperson introduce the achievements of the 2019 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit.","From November 4 to 5, the 2019 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit was successfully held in Nanjing. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the summit, delivered an important speech, and publicly announced the “26 Measures” to benefit Taiwan compatriots. Political and business circles on both sides of the Strait spoke highly of Chairman Wang Yang's important speech, holding that the speech fully reflects the mainland's sincere willingness to wholeheartedly do practical good deeds and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. It will surely provide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises with greater convenience and support in developing on the mainland, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and promote the integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe number of participants at this summit was a record high, with more than 1,300 well-known entrepreneurs from both sides of the Strait, heads of business organizations, small and medium-sized enterprise and young entrepreneurs, and experts and scholars attending. Centering on the theme “Deepening Integrated Development and Building a Common Market,” they engaged in exchanges and discussions and achieved fruitful results. Enterprises from both sides of the Strait reached 47 cooperation agreements in fields including agriculture, energy, electronics, pharmaceuticals, finance, intelligent manufacturing, cultural and creative industries and services, and small and medium-sized enterprises, with an intended contract value of RMB 15.521 billion. This fully demonstrates that the trend of cross-Strait economic exchange and integration cannot be suppressed by any force, the bonds of kinship rooted in the common origins of people on both sides of the Strait cannot be severed by any force, and the expansion and deepening of exchange and cooperation among all sectors across the Strait cannot be blocked by any force either.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","On the eve of next year's Spring Festival, which coincides with two elections in the Taiwan region, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople hope the operating hours of the extended Spring Festival charter flights can be prolonged, but this has been refused by Taiwan's civil aviation authorities. Some public opinion on the island questions whether the DPP authorities intend to obstruct Taiwan businesspeople…","Recently, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises and Taiwan business associations in relevant regions asked the civil aviation authorities to extend the execution period of the 2020 Spring Festival extra flights. Because the eve of next year's Spring Festival coincides with two elections in Taiwan, large numbers of mainland-based Taiwan compatriots will be traveling across the Strait at that time, and they hope the extra flights can be extended to fully meet the needs of Taiwan compatriots returning home.\nWe believe the suggestion by the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises and the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to extend the execution period of the 2020 Spring Festival extra flights is reasonable, and we are also willing to do our utmost to provide assistance. Although the Spring Festival travel rush is the busiest period for mainland air transport, the mainland civil aviation authorities have overcome difficulties to actively respond to the demands of Taiwan compatriots, encouraging cross-Strait airlines to provide various conveniences for Taiwan compatriots returning home. At the same time, they have repeatedly communicated with the Taiwan side about appropriately extending the execution period of the Spring Festival extra flights.\nAccording to our understanding, the Taiwan civil aviation authorities have clearly refused to extend the execution period of the Spring Festival extra flights. We truly do not understand the DPP authorities' disregard for public demands and their indifference to the needs of Taiwan compatriots to return home. We hope they will listen more to the feedback of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots, adopt an attitude and approach that meet public expectations, and stop deliberately setting obstacles that affect the smooth return home of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217874.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, U.S. Secretary of State Mike Pompeo recently said that, in order to normalize relations with mainland China and resolve the Taiwan question peacefully, the United States has for a long time \"downgraded\" its relations with Taiwan, and that this amounts to abandoning American values, Western democracy, and so on. May I ask what the spokesperson's comment is on this?","As everyone has noticed, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has comprehensively and systematically stated our solemn position.\nI want to emphasize here that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and this is an internationally recognized, iron-clad fact that cannot be changed by certain US politicians on the basis of their own prejudices and faulty logic. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately, and avoid damaging China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217872.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Spokesperson, what are the main features of the “26 Measures” compared with the “31 Measures” issued earlier?","Regarding the “26 Measures,” media on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have given them full and extensive coverage. I would like to take this opportunity to offer some further interpretation.\nThe “26 Measures” both follow in the same line as the “31 Measures” in letting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises share development opportunities and in providing them with equal treatment. They also have the following new features:\nFirst, they closely follow hot spots in economic and social development. For example, Article 2 focuses on 5G, a hot industrial topic, and will actively support cross-Strait enterprises in exchanging and cooperating on the 5G industry, welcoming Taiwan-funded enterprises to take part in mainland 5G construction and share mainland 5G business opportunities. Article 9 makes clear that Taiwan-funded enterprises may apply to competent authorities under law for trade remedy measures, and enjoy the same protection from these trade remedy measures as mainland enterprises, to safeguard their own legitimate rights and interests. Article 16 focuses on new transportation formats that have emerged on the mainland in recent years, such as ride-hailing, shared bicycles and shared cars, providing Taiwan compatriots with more travel options and convenience for business trips, visiting relatives and commuting to work on the mainland.\nSecond, they further respond to the key concerns of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. For example, Article 8 addresses problems facing Taiwan-funded enterprises, especially small and micro Taiwan-funded enterprises, such as difficulty and high cost of financing, and proposes solutions in applying for government-backed financing guarantee funds and expanding direct financing channels. Article 10 supports Taiwan-funded enterprises in equally using short-term export credit insurance, medium- and long-term export credit insurance, and overseas investment insurance products, to secure export payment collection and reduce overseas investment risk. Article 23, to meet the aspiration of Taiwan students to attend university on the mainland, will continue to optimize the distribution of institutions and majors, raise the proportion of institutions in the central and western regions, and create more learning opportunities and a better learning environment for Taiwan students who come to study on the mainland.\nThird, their substantive value has been further raised. For example, Article 1 supports Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating equally in major technical equipment and in the construction of the four types of “centers,” to help Taiwan-funded enterprises accelerate research and innovation and integrate into high-quality development. Article 21 supports Taiwan compatriots engaged in professional technical work in taking part in professional title evaluations, and recognizes the projects they have taken part in in Taiwan, the achievements they have obtained, and the years they have worked in technical jobs.\nFourth, the scope of beneficiaries has been further expanded. Article 13 targets Taiwan youth and will help the 76 cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites enjoy more preferential policies. Article 14 targets overseas Taiwan compatriots: within its scope of responsibilities, it will actively assist Taiwan compatriots who encounter sudden safety incidents such as natural disasters or accidents overseas, and will also handle applications for various travel documents and other matters for overseas Taiwan compatriots. Articles 25 and 26 target Taiwan athletes and coaches, and will create a better environment and conditions for them to take part in sports competitions and professional leagues on the mainland and to carry out study and exchange activities.\nFifth, they fully reflect pioneering and trial implementation. For example, Article 17 actively implements General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important instruction to “strive to build Fujian into the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to land,” and carries out pilot work in Fujian on communication tariff preferences, giving tariff preferences to Taiwan compatriots using mainland mobile telephone services.\nThe specific content can be read in more detail by everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191113_12217879.htm"],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Retired Taiwan Normal University professor Shi Zhengping (施正屏) is reportedly been out of contact on the mainland since last August and is currently detained in Beijing. Others, including Cai Jinshu (蔡金树) and Li Mengju (李孟居) before him, have also “lost contact,” yet no specific charges have been stated. Please explain.","The three cases you cited all involve individuals engaged in activities suspected of endangering national security, and they were placed under investigation by the competent mainland authorities in accordance with the law. As we understand it, the relevant authorities are handling these cases strictly according to law, have notified the families of all three individuals, and are protecting their various lawful rights as provided by law. The cases of 蔡金树 and 施正屏 have entered the trial process. The mainland has consistently cracked down on criminal activities that endanger national security in accordance with the law. This is normal law enforcement.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Your Mandarin version of the 26 measures mentions content about sports competitions and athletes. May I ask the spokesperson: if Taiwan athletes wish to develop on the mainland, can they join the national team? Do they need to give up their Taiwan nationality?","As I just introduced, Articles 25 and 26 of the “26 Measures” clearly stipulate that we welcome Taiwan athletes to take part in national sports competitions and professional leagues on the mainland. Taiwan athletes may participate in mainland professional leagues such as football, basketball, table tennis, and Go in the capacity of domestic reinforcements (内援). Qualified Taiwan sports teams and clubs may also take part in relevant professional leagues on the mainland. The mainland sports authorities will revise the management measures for athletes' technical grades. For Taiwan athletes and sports enthusiasts who take part in mainland sports competitions, reach the corresponding sports technical grade standards, and apply, the mainland individual sports associations will award them technical grade certificates.\nAs for the question you raised, it is not clearly stipulated in the “26 Measures” and is not within the policy scope of the “26 Measures.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","The two sides of the Strait give different accounts of the extension of next year's Lunar New Year charter flights. Taiwan's Civil Aeronautics Administration and the Mainland Affairs Council claim that the mainland's account does not match the facts, and that arrangements for cross-Strait Lunar New Year charter flights have been handled through customary contact. Could the spokesperson introduce the status of…","There is currently no question of differing accounts. The facts are only one. Regarding the request by Taiwan compatriots returning from the mainland to extend the Spring Festival charter flight schedule in 2020, the Taiwan civil aviation authority has clearly refused, a settled matter with no room for each side to tell its own story. If the Taiwan side says it has not refused and is still considering, that is of course welcome, and we hope they will agree with our civil aviation authorities on specific timing as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾ETToday东森新闻云记者","Continuing with the question of the “26 measures”: earlier, Taiwan’s economic authorities said the content relating to the “26 measures” was “deception,” and the Taiwan side will put forward a so-called countermeasure within two weeks, and will also conduct stricter reviews of Taiwan businesses investing on the mainland. May I ask for the spokesperson’s response to this?","Whether it is deception is not for any one person to decide; it is for the broad Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots who have benefited to decide. If we talk about deception, what truly deceives the Taiwan public is their confusing, slandering, and smearing of the “26 Measures” from every angle. Since they think the “26 Measures” are empty and not frightening, why did they formulate so many so-called countermeasures to counter them? This logic is obviously self-contradictory. The DPP authorities' use of so-called “response measures” to impose restrictive measures on Taiwan compatriots harms the interests of the Taiwan public and spoils good things for Taiwan compatriots. Their approach runs counter to the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots and will not win their recognition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报两岸经合周刊记者","The Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival is about to be held. Spokesperson, roughly how many Taiwan filmmakers will take part in this festival?","I do not have information on this at the moment. The Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival is organized by the China Film Association. Please direct your specific questions to them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","First question: on the 11th, a Hong Kong police officer fired at a rioter who had seized a police service firearm. Tsai Ing-wen used this to accuse the Hong Kong government of shooting at unarmed people, and also said she hopes Taiwan can become a benchmark for Hong Kong. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: Wu Chao-hsu, head of Taiwan’s department responsible for external affairs, recently…","Let me answer the first question first. In fact, the DPP authorities have been playing politics with the Hong Kong situation from the very beginning. I advise them to read the complete statements from the Hong Kong SAR Government and the police carefully, to open their eyes and take a good look at the images of rioters setting ordinary citizens on fire in the streets, and not to keep confusing right and wrong and muddying the waters for political self-interest. What they should do is immediately withdraw the black hand reaching out toward Hong Kong.\nOn the second question, Wu Zhaoxie's remarks are complete nonsense, close to talking nonsense. Amid the current complex world economic situation, the mainland's economic development outlook remains excellent, and this is not something that Wu Zhaoxie and his ilk can talk down. By contrast, the DPP authorities gloss over and conceal the economic difficulties on the island, and completely ignore the actual feelings of Taiwan people and the actual decline of Taiwan's economy and people's livelihoods. We firmly adhere to the policy of peaceful reunification. The DPP authorities keep promoting \"Taiwan independence\" activities, stirring up cross-Strait hostility and creating cross-Strait confrontation, which is the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Recently, in order to gain electoral benefits, they keep weaving various lies to intimidate, threaten and mislead Taiwan people. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must remain highly vigilant and not be easily misled by them.\nQuestion from a reporter of Hong Kong's China Review News Agency: Recently, Ma Ying-jeou said at the Oxford Union that Taiwan should keep open options on the question of unification, and that unification dialogue should be conducted only on the premise that the Taiwan people are well prepared. What is the spokesperson's response to this?\nRealizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of the Chinese people and the fundamental interest of the Chinese nation. We will continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","环球时报、环球网记者","The DPP authorities recently released so-called data stating that Taiwan’s GDP growth in the third quarter continued to rank first among the “Four Asian Tigers.” Cai Yingwen also said that it was because, after more than three years in office, she worked hard to change the economic structure and transform industries, which made Taiwan first among the “Four Little Dragons.” What is the spokesperson’s response to…","Regarding some people’s remarks and actions, we note that public opinion on the island has already expressed disapproval of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ practice of selectively releasing data. The state of Taiwan’s economy and people’s livelihoods, and Taiwan residents’ own direct experience, are the most convincing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","\"Double 11\" has just passed. How does the spokesperson view the current integrated development of e-commerce across the Taiwan Strait?","The “Double Eleven” e-commerce shopping festival grows more popular every year, reflecting the strong consumption capacity of mainland residents. Statistics show that in 2018, total retail sales of consumer goods in mainland China already exceeded 38 trillion, of which online retail sales of physical goods exceeded 7 trillion yuan. According to media reports, during this year's “Double Eleven,” Taiwan became the region with the largest growth in purchase amounts. The rapidly developing mainland e-commerce market can both provide convenient services to Taiwan compatriots and create major business opportunities for Taiwan enterprises. We are pleased to see Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises make full use of this platform to further expand e-commerce cooperation and achieve greater and better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The head of Taiwan’s indigenous affairs department recently said that when Taiwan’s indigenous peoples exchange with the mainland, they should not call themselves “ethnic minorities” but “indigenous peoples.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan’s Indigenous peoples are an important and inseparable part of the big family of the Chinese nation. Indigenous compatriots on both sides of the Strait have for years actively carried out exchanges and cooperation, sharing the dividends of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the achievements of integrated development across the Strait. Some people in the DPP authorities manipulate this issue, stirring up feelings between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, with sinister intentions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191113_12217905.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-11-15","Geng Shuang","","A US congressional advisory body yesterday made some suggestions that Congress should suspend the special economic status of Hong Kong if China decides to send troops in. There were also recommendations for the United States to offer more support to Taiwan. What is your reaction to this congressional report?","The committee you mentioned is deeply entrenched in prejudice against China. Its reports are rarely based on facts. I have no interest in commenting.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1716261.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201911/t20191115_5418264.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-11-18","Geng Shuang","","China sailed a group of carrier ships into the Taiwan Strait on Sunday. The group was trailed by US and Japanese ships. What is the purpose of this operation and has China been in cooperation or communication with US and Japanese counterparts regarding this exercise?","Perhaps you have noticed that the PLA Navy spokesperson already responded to this. I'd refer you to them if you are interested.\nBut I wonder why is the fuss over a normal and regular exercise of China's fleet at its own doorstep? The relevant activity complies with international law and international practice. We urge relevant sides to stop actions that interfere with China's normal military operations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1716772.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201911/t20191118_5418269.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-11-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Lai Ching-te (赖清德) recently declared that he is a “pragmatic Taiwan independence worker,” and said that Taiwan is already a “sovereign and independent country” and that Taiwan’s future will be decided by 23 million people. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Ma Xiaoguang (马晓光) gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 21 — In response to a question about the “Taiwan independence” remarks recently made by Lai Ching-te, deputy to Tsai Ing-wen, who is seeking re-election in 2020, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 21st that Lai has repeatedly claimed to be a “Taiwan independence worker,” which has drawn strong condemnation from all sectors on both sides of the Strait. At this moment he has once again blatantly clamored for “Taiwan independence,” attempting to hype up and escalate cross-Strait confrontation and recklessly challenging peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This once again fully exposes that, in pursuit of political and electoral gain, he is willing to harm the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, and it also completely tears off the mask of the so-called non-provocation of the DPP authorities.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The motherland must be and will inevitably be reunified; this is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people, and no one and no force can stop it. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that cannot succeed; it will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan and will certainly be firmly opposed by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191121_12219877.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-11-22","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan's \"foreign minister\" today said that China had promised aid and investment to several former allies to Taiwan, but that money hasn't come. The \"foreign minister\" also said that China is exporting corruption and authoritarianism to these countries. Do you have a response?","I should correct you first. We do not recognize the so-called \"foreign minister\" of Taiwan. I hope you will get the terms right next time.\nAs to your question, I can tell you that the one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community and commitment to this principle is a widely recognized norm in international relations. We stand ready to develop friendly cooperative relations with the rest of the world on the basis of the one-China principle.\nI want to say that we have friendly cooperation with many countries on the basis of mutual benefit. Such cooperation is in the interests of not only China, but also those countries themselves. With tangible benefits delivered, such cooperation will continue to be welcomed by the local people. It just cannot be discredited by any attacks or slanders.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1718137.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201911/t20191122_5418294.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on November 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. The new spokesperson Zhu Fenglian hosted a press conference for the first time and answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalists, good morning!\nWelcome, everyone, to the press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I am Zhu Fenglian.\n(In Hokkien) I am a Hakka from Guangdong, and I would first like to greet our Taiwanese compatriots!\n(In Hakka) I am very glad to have the opportunity to serve Taiwanese compatriots from this press conference podium, so that Taiwanese compatriots can learn more about our policies and our work!\nI also hope that together with you, dear journalists, we can help compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait understand, in a timely, accurate, comprehensive and objective manner, the mainland’s policies and positions toward Taiwan, and enhance understanding, mutual comprehension and trust between compatriots on both sides!\nNow, please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The “31 Measures” propose accelerating equal treatment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and mainland enterprises in the fields of investment and economic cooperation. Over the past year or so, what major R&D projects and infrastructure construction have Taiwan businesses and enterprises taken part in? What achievements have been made in the construction of cross-Strait cooperation zones and in agricultural…","Over the past year or more, Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises have gained many opportunities, and have obtained tangible benefits, in participating in major economic action plans and R&D projects and in participating in infrastructure construction.\nFirst, in participating in infrastructure construction and government procurement. Amid fierce competition, the valve products of the Taiwan-funded company Shanghai Guanlong won the bid for the Beijing Daxing International Airport construction project. Taiwan's CECI Engineering Consultants directly participated in the preliminary design of the Kunshan Zhonghuan Expressway. Fujian Province encourages Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in government procurement, and has already procured automobiles and displays produced by Taiwan-funded enterprises such as Dongnan Motor and Foxconn's Coretronic. Second, in participating in major economic action plans and R&D projects. Coretronic Technology obtained industrial transformation and upgrading fund support, and Advantech, AUO and other Taiwan-funded enterprises were included in the green manufacturing list. A Xiamen Yujing Optoelectronics factory was designated as a smart manufacturing pilot demonstration project. Foxconn, Inventec and others participated in the Industrial Internet Industry Alliance guided by the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology. Third, in the construction of cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones. The Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, the Ministry of Commerce and others, successively established cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones in Sichuan, Guangxi and Hubei. Relevant localities have also issued various policies that provide Taiwan-funded enterprises with a range of preferences in land use, labor, financing and other areas. Fourth, in agricultural cooperation. Taiwan-funded agricultural enterprises in Guizhou, Fujian and other places were recognized as key leading enterprises in agricultural industrialization, and received total support funds of more than 20 million yuan from all levels of government over the past three years. Sixteen agricultural machinery products produced by Taiwan-funded enterprises in Fujian were included in the agricultural machinery purchase subsidy product catalog, with subsidy funds totaling 112 million yuan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221343.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","It is understood that activities for Taiwan businesses participating in the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta will be held soon. Please introduce the relevant information.","From December 4 to 5, activities for Taiwan businesspeople to participate in the integration of the Yangtze River Delta region, themed “Taiwan Businesses Unite in the Yangtze River Delta, Cross-Strait Shared New Opportunities,” will be held in Shanghai. The purpose of these activities is to support Taiwan businesspeople in participating in the Yangtze River Delta regional integration development strategy, to help Taiwan businesspeople further understand relevant policies and measures, to better share in the development opportunities and achievements of the mainland, to promote cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and to deepen cross-Strait integration and development. Relevant competent authorities, responsible officials from Shanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang and Anhui provinces and municipalities, the two chairpersons of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan business representatives, totaling more than 500 people, will attend the activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed that 700 billion in funds has flowed back from Taiwan businesses. How does the spokesperson view this?","I have noted the relevant reports. In fact, where Taiwan businesses invest and where they deploy is not decided by the DPP authorities. Judging from the main data for the first three quarters of this year, the mainland economy has continued to operate within a reasonable range, maintaining an overall trend of steady development with progress, and its development prospects remain consistently promising. Facts speak louder than words. Taiwan businesses and enterprises will have their own judgment about which place has a better business environment and is more conducive to their long-term development, and I believe they will make wise choices.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","After the “26 Measures” were launched this month, what progress has been made in implementing them?","The “26 Measures” were issued and implemented on November 4, and localities and departments are accelerating the implementation of the measures.\nFujian Province has carried out pilot programs in some areas and has already achieved some concrete progress. For example, Taiwan-funded enterprises such as Guanjie (冠捷), Jianlin (建霖), Liuhe Machinery (六和机械), and Dongnan Motors (东南汽车) have established national-level or provincial-level industrial design centers and enterprise technology centers. Fujian Province provided capital increase incentives totaling 11 million yuan to three Taiwan-funded enterprises, including Qimei (奇美), and also set up a special fund for trade remedies to provide relief for the export trade of Taiwan-funded enterprises. It has also provided cumulative export business risk coverage of nearly 10 billion US dollars for Taiwan-funded enterprises such as Cankun (灿坤). The Xiamen Municipal Financial Affairs Office provided financing guarantees for 11 Taiwan-funded enterprises, totaling 76 million yuan, and also launched the Taiwan enterprise section of the Straits Equity Exchange Center.\nA few days ago, Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province released 20 distinctive measures serving Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, covering support for Taiwan-funded enterprises' on-site transformation, technology benefiting Taiwan, talent cultivation, and other areas.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","What is most closely related to the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots is equal treatment in studying, starting businesses, finding employment and living on the mainland. May I ask what new results have been achieved in this regard since the “31 measures” were issued and implemented more than a year ago?","Over the past year and more, as the “31 measures” have been implemented in ever more concrete detail, Taiwan compatriots have found it increasingly convenient to study, work and live in all parts of the mainland, and they enjoy equal treatment in a wider range of areas and fields.\nFirst, regarding professional qualification examinations. Last year we opened 134 professional qualification examinations. According to incomplete statistics, more than 800 Taiwan compatriots obtained professional qualifications in several popular industries.\nFor example, the first national unified legal professional qualification examination was held last September, with 573 Taiwan examinees registering, and 81 of them passed and obtained legal professional qualification certificates. The mainland tourism market is very hot: domestic travel reached 5.5 billion trips last year, so there is a shortage of tour guides. Many Taiwan compatriots seized this opportunity promptly; last year 133 Taiwan compatriots registered for the tour guide professional qualification examination, and 48 of them successfully obtained tour guide certificates. This year, the number of registrants has increased to more than 180.\nIn January this year, the education authorities issued a policy allowing Taiwan residents who study, work and live on the mainland to apply to take the primary and secondary school teacher qualification examination; after certification, they can obtain primary and secondary school teacher qualifications. Afterward, 80 Taiwan compatriots registered for the March examination; 10 passed the written test, and 7 passed the interview and obtained teacher qualification certificates. The second examination this year is underway, and I will provide the relevant data to everyone in a timely manner. It can be seen that these professional qualification examinations in popular industries are quite competitive and fairly difficult. We hope that Taiwan youth who aspire to sit these examinations will work hard, prepare carefully, and we look forward to seeing more Taiwan compatriots gain benefits this year.\nSecond, regarding employment in mainland public institutions. On the basis of pilot programs allowing Taiwan compatriots to work in public institutions in 12 provinces and municipalities, including Fujian, Tianjin, Jiangsu and Shanghai, the free trade pilot zones in five provinces — Liaoning, Henan, Chongqing, Sichuan and Shaanxi — have also been included in the pilot scope. At present, more than 1,600 Taiwan teachers work at more than 200 universities on the mainland.\nThird, regarding applications to participate in major national talent programs. So far, 72 Taiwan professionals have been selected for the national “Thousand Talents Plan.” Taiwan researchers working on the mainland submitted 157 projects to the 2018 annual and youth programs of the National Social Science Fund, of which 58 were approved. The National Art Fund received 12 applications for cooperative projects with institutions or entities in Taiwan, and 19 Taiwan artists applied for the young artist creation talent program.\nFourth, regarding the inclusion of academic achievements obtained in Taiwan in evaluation systems. In July this year, the Center for Chinese Social Science Evaluation at Nanjing University included 30 Taiwan humanities and social science academic journals across 15 disciplines in its catalogue of source journals for the Chinese Social Sciences Citation Index (CSSCI) database. The relevant work is operating normally, and feedback from all sides has been good. This is very good news for Taiwan youth working in public institutions or universities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221339.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The mainland recently released the results of the Fourth National Economic Census. Although the number of Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao-invested enterprises increased from 97,000 at the end of 2013 to 119,000, their share of all enterprises declined from 1.2% to 0.6%. How does the spokesperson interpret this?","The results of the Fourth National Economic Census show that over the past five years, the total number of enterprise legal person units was 18.57 million, an increase of 126.2%. Among them, mainland enterprises numbered 18.348 million, accounting for 98.8%; enterprises invested in by Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao numbered 119,000, accounting for 0.6%; and foreign-invested enterprises numbered 103,000, accounting for 0.6%. This reflects a new situation in which the mainland's business environment continues to improve and all types of market entities are growing in large numbers simultaneously. It also reflects the strength and economic vitality of mainland enterprises, and shows that our market pie has grown bigger.\nThe mainland was in the past, is now, and will continue to be the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to invest and build businesses. According to data compiled by the Ministry of Commerce, from January to October this year, the mainland approved 4,350 Taiwan-funded projects, a year-on-year increase of 10.9%, and actually utilized 1.5 billion US dollars of Taiwan capital, a year-on-year increase of 35%. We will continue to actively create conditions for Taiwan compatriots to broadly participate in the mainland's economic construction, provide policy guidance for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to participate in major national development strategies, and build more channels and platforms. The Taiwan businesses event about to be held in Shanghai, just mentioned, falls within this category.\nWe will also actively advance the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation, build a cross-Strait common market, and promote the full interconnection of the two sides. We will further implement and refine the “31 measures” and the “26 measures,” continuing to share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises and providing them with equal treatment. We hope Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises can leverage their own strengths, catch the express train of the mainland's expanding domestic demand market, and achieve greater development of their own while integrating into the mainland's rapid development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221336.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","After the “26 Measures” were introduced, Taiwan's sports community paid close attention to content related to cross-Strait sports exchanges. Have detailed implementation measures been issued in this area?","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,3,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Reports say that the Taiwan cargo ship “Chang Xin” collided with an unidentified vessel and sank in waters at the mouth of the Min River in Fujian on November 20, and two Taiwanese crew members are still missing. Could the spokesperson please introduce the latest situation?","We have been closely following this situation. We understand that at 21:50 on November 20, a cargo ship from Guangdong collided with the Taiwan cargo ship ‘Changxin’ (苌薪号) about 0.66 nautical miles south of Chuanshi Island at the mouth of the Min River in Fuzhou City, Fujian Province. The ‘Changxin’ took on water and sank, causing nine crew members on board (six Taiwanese crew and three Indonesian crew) to fall into the water.\nUpon receiving the news, the Fujian Provincial Maritime Search and Rescue Center immediately activated its emergency plan and dispatched helicopters and search and rescue vessels to carry out full-scale search and rescue operations. At dawn on the 21st, seven crew members were rescued and properly settled. Two Taiwanese crew members are missing, and one crew member’s body was found on the evening of the 22nd. We have just received word that another body was found this morning, and its identity is still being confirmed. The relevant departments are currently investigating the vessel involved and the cause of the accident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","On the first question: this year, film industry personalities from Taiwan participated in the evaluation of the 32nd China Golden Rooster Awards and received nominations. This is the first time since the “31 Measures” were implemented that Taiwan filmmakers and co-produced works have registered for and been shortlisted for the Golden Rooster Awards. May I ask the spokesperson what achievements Taiwan compatriots…","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,3,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221338.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221341.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾ETToday东森新闻云记者","Wang Liqiang, who calls himself a so-called “Chinese spy,” stated in Australia that China Innovation Investment, a Hong Kong-listed company, provided funding in Taiwan to influence the elections, and that the company’s head, Xiang Xin, and his wife were recently restricted from leaving Taiwan by sea and air. What is the spokesperson’s response?","On this matter, our spokesperson already responded at the first opportunity on the 23rd of this month, and the Jing'an Branch of the Shanghai Municipal Public Security Bureau issued a briefing on the relevant situation on the 23rd. Wang Liqiang is a fugitive involved in the case. Because he is suspected of fraud, the public security organs have opened a criminal investigation against him, and the so-called passport of the People’s Republic of China and Hong Kong permanent resident identity card he held are both forged documents. The public security organs are still conducting further investigation into this case.\nIn fact, the facts are very clear: “swindler turned spy” is an absurd script full of holes, concocted by anti-China forces. The DPP authorities, tying themselves to a fraudster and extensively engaging in political manipulation, aim to create the illusion of so-called “mainland interference in Taiwan's elections” in order to seek improper electoral gains. They attempt to deceive Taiwan residents with lies, which seriously underestimates the rationality and judgment of Taiwan residents. Taiwan public opinion has already raised many doubts about this DPP scheme, which shows that this electoral trick by the DPP authorities has already failed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","There is news that some members of the US Congress are preparing to introduce the so-called “Taiwan Sovereignty Symbols Act.” What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this? In recent years, the US has continuously put forward so-called “pro-Taiwan” bills and shows a trend of gradually closer ties with Taiwan. How will the mainland respond?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no external interference. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, Han Kuo-yu said that as long as the mainland has not given up the use of force to resolve the Taiwan question, there are no conditions for signing a peace agreement across the Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides and the common interest of compatriots on both sides. On the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” reaching institutional arrangements to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nWe have stressed many times that we are willing, with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. We do not commit to renouncing the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is aimed at foreign interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist activities, and is by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots. We compatriots on both sides of the Strait must seek peace together, safeguard peace together, and share peace together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Chen Mingzhong, former adviser to the Taiwan Political Victims Mutual Aid Association and former chairman of the Xiachao Alliance, passed away in Shanghai on November 21. May I ask the spokesperson for your evaluation of Mr. Chen Mingzhong's role in the development of cross-strait relations?","Chen Ming-chung, former adviser of the Taiwan Political Victims Mutual Aid Association and former president of the Xiachao United Association, died in Shanghai on November 21, 2019, after medical treatment failed due to illness. The Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office express deep mourning.\nMr. Chen Ming-chung was a loyal patriot, a shining model of the Taiwan people's resistance against colonialism and oppression, and an outstanding representative of Taiwan's patriotic unification camp. He devoted his entire life to the lofty cause of realizing the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. His patriotic sentiments are worth remembering forever by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221332.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The DPP has put forward a draft “anti-infiltration law” in Taiwan's legislature that would impose more restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges. What is the spokesperson's comment?","This year, the DPP authorities, by manipulating so-called “Chinese Communist Party agent” law amendments and the like, have continuously incited cross-Strait confrontation and created hostility between the two sides, which has been strongly opposed by all sectors of Taiwan society. Now they are hyping the so-called “anti-infiltration law.” Regardless of how the tactics change, the purpose is to suppress parties, groups, and individuals on the island that hold different positions, to intimidate and punish Taiwan people participating in cross-Strait exchanges, and to create a “green terror” in Taiwan society. The DPP authorities seek to gain electoral advantage through this, and it will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that the situation in Hong Kong highlights the importance of the United States and Taiwan jointly defending so-called “democracy and freedom” values. What comment does the spokesperson have?","“One Country, Two Systems” is the best solution to the Hong Kong issue left over from history, and the best institutional arrangement for keeping Hong Kong prosperous and stable over the long term. We now see more and more Hong Kong citizens stepping forward, not wanting Hong Kong to descend into further chaos, and hoping to halt violence, restore order. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers to bolster their own standing, keep meddling in Hong Kong affairs to seek political gain. Their intention will not succeed.\nWe will continue to implement the central government’s major policies on Taiwan work, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","According to reports, 30 Taiwan compatriots who served as assistants to mainland community directors were punished by Taiwan authorities, then filed administrative lawsuits, all of which were recently rejected by Taiwan’s Ministry of the Interior. The DPP authorities also claimed that they will continue to investigate so-called “illegal” cases of Taiwan residents taking up such posts on the mainland. What is the…","In recent years, in line with the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots, we have provided them with more and better development opportunities and helped them overcome practical difficulties in finding employment, which has been widely affirmed and welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. Tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots work at mainland universities, research institutions, hospitals, and various enterprises and institutions, as I touched on earlier when introducing the “31 Measures.”\nRegarding the suppression and punishment by the DPP authorities of Taiwanese youth working in Haicang District, Xiamen, we have repeatedly explained the situation and stated our position. Some of these Taiwanese youth came to work in Haicang: some were hired by local enterprises, signed labor contracts, and served as assistants to community directors, engaging in community construction, modern agriculture, traditional culture protection, rural education revitalization, and volunteer services; others were employed by the Straits Urban-Rural Development Foundation and provided services to communities as “community builders.” What we offer these youth is employment opportunities, and what these youth seek is also better development for themselves. For such a simple matter, the DPP authorities still set up barriers everywhere and constantly threaten and intimidate them with so-called “illegality.” In doing so, they are in effect smashing these Taiwanese youth's rice bowls.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201911/t20191127_12221334.htm"],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报海外网记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently released a campaign video whose main theme was opposition to “one country, two systems” and inciting Taiwan residents not to trust the mainland. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We never interfere in Taiwan’s elections. The DPP authorities ignore the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, deliberately stir up cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Their actions aim to deceive Taiwan’s people and seek electoral self-interest. We believe Taiwan compatriots will see through their electoral tricks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Some people in Taiwan believe that the Xiangxin couple, who were “accused” by Wang Liqiang, may have engaged in so-called “espionage” or “infiltration.” Since this coincides with Taiwan's elections, the Taiwan side may take some coercive measures. May I ask the spokesperson for a response?","I have seen the relevant reports, the statement from the Zhongchuang Investment Company, and the questions raised in Taiwan public opinion about the DPP authorities’ so-called “detention” this time. We are highly concerned about the safety and lawful rights and interests of mainland residents and Hong Kong and Macao residents in Taiwan, and we warn the DPP authorities not to act recklessly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Under the current situation in Hong Kong, the Taiwan authorities want to take the opportunity to recruit Hong Kong teachers and students. What is your response?","We have seen relevant reports. Some students studying at universities in Hong Kong may want to transfer to study in Taiwan, which precisely shows that the radical and violent criminal acts in Hong Kong have seriously harmed these students' right to normal study. Stopping violence, quelling chaos, and restoring order is the most urgent task in Hong Kong at present. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to stop meddling in Hong Kong affairs and stop political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Some Huawei phones label Taiwan as “China Taiwan,” and the Taiwan authorities forced telecom operators to stop selling these Huawei phones. What comment does the spokesperson have?","This practice by the DPP authorities of undermining normal cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges for political purposes harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides and is not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently the Taipei City side said it will sign a sister-city agreement with Prague, Czech Republic, using the title “Taiwan Taipei City.” What is the spokesperson's comment? Will this affect the holding of the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum and cross-Strait exchanges?","Our position on Taiwan's participation in foreign-related activities has been consistent and clear, and our attitude toward cross-Strait city exchanges is also very clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201911/t20191127_12221363.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-11-28","Geng Shuang","","Recent media reports claimed that in 2017, Panama's then president Varela received large amounts of assistance from the Chinese government in exchange for establishing ties with China. Taiwan said that the mainland often uses assistance to lure corrupt officials to put personal gains before national interests. Could you comment on that?","China and Panama established diplomatic relationship on the basis of the one-China principle, which is consistent with international law and basic norms governing international relations. It is in keeping with the trend of the times and people's aspirations. Last year, the Panama government published the full text of 26 agreements signed with China, including the Joint Communique on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between China and Panama. It fully shows that the whole process was open and transparent and the two sides have nothing to hide. The Panama side also stated on many occasions that establishing relations with China was a political decision entirely based on the one-China principle.\nSince relations were established, China has provided assistance to Panama's socioeconomic development to the best of our capabilities. We offered support to projects such as the Amador Convention Center and the Colon Secure City project. They are designed to benefit the Panama people, not any political party or individual. There is no secret funneling of funds or backdoor dealing of any kind. It is the Taiwan authority that engages in dollar diplomacy and interests transmission. Its allegation of \"assistance for diplomacy\", presuming others by Taiwan's own pattern, is pure fabrication to console itself and to fool others.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1719976.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1719929.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2019-11-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The first domestically-built aircraft carrier of China recently passed through the Taiwan Straits. Some analysts say that this aircraft carrier might be deployed in Sanya, a move that might have an impact on the regional situation. Do you have any comments?","On Nov 17, China’s second aircraft-carrier successfully passed through the Taiwan Straits to carry out scientific research tests and routine training in the South China Sea. It is a regular arrangement for an aircraft carrier to conduct cross-sea maneuvers in the process of its construction. Similar routine exercises will be organized as planned in the future.\nWhere the Chinese navy deploys the domestically-made aircraft carrier is determined by national security threats and defense needs. It has nothing to do with the regional situation and does not target any specific target, country or region.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-11/29/content_4855898.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-11-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","China’s domestically-built aircraft carrier passed through the Taiwan Straits and anchored at Sanya Military Port this month. Does this mean that it will be commissioned soon?","China’s second aircraft carrier is conducting various trials according to plan and we are making steady progress. The date of commissioning will be decided by the progress in its construction and trials.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-11/29/content_4855898.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-11-28","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","This month, China's second aircraft carrier passed through the Taiwan Strait. The outside world is interested in China's future plan for aircraft carriers. What is the military's consideration on this? Second question, the spokesperson pointed out that the actions of the US warships pose threats to service members on the two countries' naval vessels. Does this mean that the increasing provocations by the United…","On the first question, developing aircraft carriers is a major strategic decision based on our national security and overall development. We will plan the development of aircraft carriers in accordance with our economic and social development and the needs of national defense and military build-up.\nOn the second question, despite warnings from the Chinese side, US warships and aircraft repeatedly and deliberately trespassed into neighboring waters and airspace of China’s islands and reefs in the South China Sea. These actions jeopardize regional peace and stability, undermine China’s sovereignty and security, and endanger the safety of the front-line service members of both sides. These are very dangerous provocations. We urge the US side immediately stop such operations that harm China's interests. The Chinese military has always been on high alert and will take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard our national sovereignty, security and development interests.\nIf there are no more questions, here concludes this month’s regular press conference. Thank you!","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-11/29/content_4855898.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2019-12-02","Hua Chunying","","I was wondering if the foreign ministry could confirm that citizens from Belize and Taiwan were detained recently specifically for their involvement in the Hong Kong protests?","I refer you to relevant authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201912/t20191202_5418326.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-12-04","Hua Chunying","","It is reported that El Salvador's President Bukele is on a state visit in China. Can you give more information?","At the invitation of President Xi Jinping, El Salvador's President Bukele is paying a state visit to China from December 1 to 6. Yesterday, President Xi Jinping held fruitful talks with President Bukele. The two sides released a joint statement. The two presidents witnessed the signing of cooperation agreements in science and technology, agriculture, trade, investment, tourism, sports, etc.\nBy establishing and developing diplomatic relations, China and El Salvador opened the door of cooperation. President Bukele's visit to China is monumental in our bilateral relationship as it elevates the relationship to a new historical starting point and gives it a brighter prospect. Progress in our exchange and cooperation in the past year or so has also proven that the establishment of diplomatic ties serves the fundamental interests of both peoples. As President Bukele pointed out, it hasn't been long since we established diplomatic ties, but we have great potentials and we are fully capable of becoming good friends and partners. He believes that developing relations with China, a great nation and a sincere friend, will bring development opportunities to El Salvador and tangible benefits to its people. El Salvador is committed to developing long-term, friendly relations with China. The Salvadorean side reiterated that it fully observes the one-China principle and supports China's peaceful reunification. The bilateral cooperation agreements signed during President Bukele's visit will break new ground for mutually beneficial cooperation in the future. China looks forward to closer ties with El Salvador and broader cooperation. Specifically, we welcome more Salvadorean friends from various sectors to visit China.\nSome friends from El Salvador visited China after our two countries established diplomatic relations. They viewed China as a mystery before they came but were fascinated after they arrived. I believe a lot of foreign friends share the same feeling. China is a big country. You will not get to know the real China if you don't set foot on this land and only read biased reports by some Western media. Only when you are actually here will you see how modern, open and friendly China is, which is totally different from certain Western media's description. In this sense, it is very important to step up people-to-people exchange.\nIn yesterday's talks, the Chinese leader extended an invitation to Salvadoreans, welcoming them to visit China and see the country with their own eyes. As our two peoples share closer ties and greater mutual trust, I believe the people foundation for our relationship will be even more solid. Our relations will grow in a long-term, sound and stable manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1721507.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201912/t20191204_5418338.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-12-09","Hua Chunying","","Defense Secretary Mark Esper said today's revisionist powers China and Russia are seeking \"veto power\" over the economic and security decisions of smaller nations. China tripled its annual military spending since 2002 with estimates close to 250 billion dollars last year. Beijing continues to violate the sovereignty of Indo Pacific Nations. He still plans to shift the American military's focus to competing with…","According to public information, the US military budget for 2019 tops $716 billion, more than double that of 2002, accounting for over 40% of the world's total military expenditure and equivalent to the total of the nine countries next to the US. The US defense budget accounts for 3.5% of its GDP in 2019, while China's annual defense expenditure accounted for less than 2% of its GDP in the past 30 years, which is lower than not only the world's major countries, but also the world average of 2.6%. China's per capita military spending is even lower, only accounting for 1/22 of America's, one ninth of Britain's and one fifth of Japan's. With hundreds of military bases around the world, the United States has been war-free for only 16 of its 240-plus years of existence. The US has imposed \"regime change\", instigated \"color revolutions\" and exerted maximum pressure, thus causing regional instability and untold suffering for the people in Iraq, Afghanistan, Syria and Venezuela. The list goes on.\nI want to stress that China adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. The development of China's national defense strength is out of the need to safeguard China's national unity, territorial integrity and development interests, as well as international and regional peace and security. We pursue an independent foreign policy of peace. We believe that all countries, big or small, are equal. We never interfere in the internal affairs of other countries, and oppose the practice of the big and strong bullying the small and weak and the imposition of one's own will on others. China has never threatened, intimidated or extorted others. Such practices are not to our liking, nor are we good at them. The biggest threat to world peace and stability is precisely unilateralism and bullying, which undermine the current international order and challenge the norms governing international relations. We urge the US to abandon the outdated cold-war, zero-sum mentality and refrain from seeking and making enemies everywhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/201912/t20191209_693000.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201912/t20191209_5418356.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office held a special press conference on the “26 measures” in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian presided, and together with Zheng Chiping, Deputy Director of the Foreign Investment Department of the National Development and Reform Commission; Xu Jie, Deputy Director of the Office of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the Ministry of Science…","Good morning, esteemed journalist friends. Welcome to the press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. On November 4, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, together with the National Development and Reform Commission, after consulting with the Central Organization Department and 20 other departments, issued the “Several Measures on Further Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation” (referred to as the “26 Measures”). After the release of the “26 Measures,” they were warmly welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses. To help everyone better understand the specific details of the “26 Measures,” today we have specially invited Zheng Chiping, Deputy Director of the Foreign Capital Department of the National Development and Reform Commission; Xu Jie, Deputy Director of the Office for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the Ministry of Science and Technology; Li Yubing, Deputy Director of the Standards Innovation Department of the State Administration for Market Regulation; and Chen Binhua, Deputy Director of the Economic Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, to explain in detail the 13 measures in the “26 Measures” that provide equal treatment to Taiwanese enterprises. Now, please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Since the “26 measures” were introduced last month, we have seen many reports introducing them. Today is a press conference explaining the “26 measures” in detail. Please briefly outline the general situation of the 13 measures among the “26 measures” that provide equal treatment to Taiwan enterprises, and what were the main considerations behind introducing these measures? What are their highlights?","These 13 measures further respond to the demands and expectations of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. The main consideration is to provide more development opportunities and equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, further encourage Taiwan enterprises to participate in the mainland's high-quality development and high-tech innovation, help Taiwan enterprises accelerate technological innovation, reduce overall costs, seize development opportunities, and achieve better development.\nThese 13 measures are in philosophical continuity with the 12 measures concerning Taiwan enterprises in the “31 measures” we issued last year. They embody the concept of “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and reflect equal treatment for all. At the same time, they keep pace with the times, expand the scope of beneficiaries, and increase their substance. In summary, there are three highlights:\nFirst, they closely follow hot spots in economic and social development. For example, Article 2 focuses on the hot industry of 5G, and will actively support cross-Strait enterprises in carrying out exchanges and cooperation in the 5G industry, welcome Taiwan-invested enterprises to take part in mainland 5G construction, and share in 5G business opportunities on the mainland.\nSecond, they respond to key concerns of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. For example, Article 8 targets the difficulties in financing and high financing costs faced by Taiwan enterprises, especially small and medium-sized Taiwan enterprises, and proposes solutions in areas such as applying for government-backed financing guarantee funds and expanding direct financing channels.\nThird, their substance has been further increased. For example, Article 1 supports Taiwan enterprises in participating equally in major technical equipment and the construction of the “four types” of centers, helping Taiwan enterprises accelerate technological innovation and integrate into high-quality development.\nSince the release of the “26 measures,” the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the National Development and Reform Commission have deployed implementation work with relevant departments and localities, and related implementation and supporting work is being pushed forward. For example, relevant departments in Fujian Province will hold a policy briefing in the near future to clarify the specific plans for some measures. Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province has introduced 20 new measures to serve Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, providing more equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. Next, we will implement all measures in detail, turn good intentions into good results, and let Taiwan compatriots and enterprises gain more tangible benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","We note that Article 1 of the “26 Measures” states that Taiwan-invested enterprises may equally participate in the R&D, innovation, testing and evaluation, and demonstration application system construction of major technical equipment, and may equally participate in the construction of industrial innovation centers, engineering research centers, enterprise technology centers, and industrial design centers. Please…","Please let Deputy Director-General Zheng Chiping answer this question.\nZheng Chiping: The mainland has a complete range of industrial categories, its manufacturing scale has consistently ranked first in the world, and its industrial technology level is rising rapidly. To promote high-quality development of mainland manufacturing, relevant departments have issued a series of policy measures and management methods to guide and support various market entities in giving full play to their respective strengths and participating on an equal footing in major technical equipment development, construction of enterprise technology centers, and other areas. At present, the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, and other departments have certified 25 batches of national enterprise technology centers and 110 national-level industrial design centers. They are also actively promoting the building of systems for R&D and innovation of major technical equipment, testing and evaluation, and demonstration and application, as well as the layout and construction of national industrial innovation centers and national engineering research centers.\nWe treat Taiwan-funded enterprises equally in participating in the development of major mainland equipment, construction of enterprise technology centers, and so on. At present, some Taiwan-funded enterprises have taken the lead, actively participating and enjoying preferential policies such as the full refund of value-added tax. For example, Fujian Jielian Electronics Co., Ltd. was certified as a national enterprise technology center, and Xiamen Jianlin Health Furniture Co., Ltd. was selected for the third batch of national-level industrial design centers.\nWe welcome more Taiwan-funded enterprises to contact the provincial development and reform commissions, industry and information authorities, and other relevant departments in their locations, in accordance with their own development needs and national policy requirements, to take the lead in or participate in related work. They can make full use of the mainland's vast market and development opportunities to enhance their technological innovation capacity and market competitiveness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","We note that Article 11 of the “26 Measures” states: “To promote fast and convenient customs clearance for Taiwan's goods imported into the mainland, and to support the development of the cross-Strait third-party testing and inspection market, customs authorities are studying and formulating a management system for accepting the results of third-party inspection institutions.” May I ask when this management…","To further promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, to facilitate the rapid customs clearance of goods imported from Taiwan into the mainland, and to support the development of third-party testing and inspection markets across the Strait, mainland customs is accelerating the improvement of its early warning and rapid response supervision system for quality and safety risks of imported and exported goods, and is studying and formulating a management system for the recognition of results from third-party inspection institutions.\nAt present, the recognition system has been solicited for comments within a certain scope, and mainland customs will further refine it based on the feedback and promote its issuance as soon as possible. When conditions are ripe, test results issued by qualified Taiwan third-party testing and appraisal institutions may be recognized by mainland customs.\nOnce this system is implemented, mainland customs will reduce the inspection rate for related goods from Taiwan, further improving the convenience of goods exported from Taiwan to the mainland. It will also help promote the development of cross-Strait third-party testing and inspection markets, giving Taiwan’s relevant testing and inspection institutions the opportunity to obtain more business.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191211_12224785.htm"],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","The “Interim Measures on Social Insurance Participation by Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Residents in the Mainland” have now been officially issued. Participation in mainland social insurance concerns the immediate practical interests of Taiwan compatriots. What concrete benefits will Taiwan compatriots gain from it?","On December 3, officials from the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security and the National Healthcare Security Administration already gave a detailed introduction and interpretation of the background and related circumstances of the Interim Measures. Here, I will mainly explain what concrete benefits Taiwan compatriots who live, work, start businesses, and study on the mainland can obtain.\nFirst, it must be made clear that the social insurance system is a social welfare benefit provided by the state. The issuance of the Interim Measures is a systematic arrangement to implement the 19th Party Congress's proposal to gradually provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, and it is also a concrete measure implementing General Secretary Xi Jinping's important proposal on promoting the sharing of social security and public resources across the Taiwan Strait. This means that Taiwan compatriots who are employed, reside, or attend school on the mainland can, like mainland residents, enjoy the relevant welfare benefits provided by the state.\nThe Interim Measures give thorough consideration to the personnel covered by the Taiwan compatriots, achieving full coverage for Taiwan compatriots participating in insurance on the mainland. They apply not only to Taiwan compatriots employed in various forms, including with units, in flexible employment, and self-employed, but also to unemployed Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland and Taiwan students attending mainland universities. For Taiwan compatriots participating in the urban and rural residents' basic pension insurance and urban and rural residents' basic medical insurance on the mainland, governments at all levels on the mainland will provide corresponding fiscal subsidies in accordance with regulations, ensuring the social security level of insured Taiwan compatriots.\nTaking into account the practical needs of reducing the contribution burden on Taiwan compatriots and of returning to Taiwan to work and study, the Interim Measures make special arrangements for Taiwan compatriots participating in social insurance on the mainland. If a Taiwan compatriot does not choose to be insured both on the mainland and in Taiwan, they may, upon providing a certificate issued by the relevant authorized institution, not participate in pension insurance and unemployment insurance on the mainland. This effectively resolves the issue of double enrollment that Taiwan compatriots are concerned about. If a Taiwan compatriot leaves the mainland before meeting the prescribed conditions for receiving a pension, they may choose to keep their account and continue contributions when they again work or reside on the mainland, or they may choose to have the social insurance relationship terminated by submitting a written application and withdraw the balance in their individual social insurance account in one lump sum.\nThe Interim Measures further explicitly provide that Taiwan compatriots enjoy the right to participate in five types of social insurance. Among them, maternity insurance and work-related injury insurance are paid by mainland employers, and Taiwan compatriots participating in insurance need not pay any personal contributions at all. This effectively and substantially expands the scope and strength of social security coverage for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191211_12224784.htm"],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Article 11 of the “26 measures” proposes to “promote cooperation on food, agricultural product, and consumer product safety supervision across the Taiwan Strait.” However, some people on the island question whether this cooperation can be implemented given that the cross-strait consultation mechanism is currently at a standstill. Can this problem be resolved?","To improve customs clearance efficiency, shorten clearance time, and reduce corporate logistics costs, on November 1 the General Administration of Customs issued and implemented the “Announcement on Promoting Facilitation Measures for Accepting Certification Results for Imported Auto Parts.” Under it, for imported auto parts from Taiwan that fall under the 8 HS codes in Chapter 8708 of the Import and Export Tariff and involve 3C certification, customs may directly accept the certificates issued by certification bodies during inspection, and in principle will no longer conduct sample testing.\nFor reasons that are well known, the institutionalized consultation mechanism across the Strait has stalled, but our steps to promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait have not stopped. Promoting cooperation between the two sides on food safety, agricultural product quarantine, and consumer product safety supervision is a concrete measure that benefits compatriots on both sides and related industries, and the mainland side will implement it earnestly. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to remove artificial obstacles created in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and truly enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","We note that Article 6 of the measures mentions supporting qualified Taiwan financial institutions and enterprises in initiating or participating in the establishment of new types of financial organizations, such as micro-credit companies, financing leasing companies, and financing guarantee companies, in areas where Taiwan-funded enterprises are concentrated. What concrete measures do we currently have in this…","At present, Taiwan-funded financial institutions have set up seven financing leasing companies on the mainland, and these companies are operating well. The China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission has issued the Regulations on the Supervision and Administration of Financing Guarantee Companies, and is formulating the Interim Measures for the Supervision and Administration of Microcredit Company Business Operations and the Interim Measures for the Supervision and Administration of Financing Leasing Business Operations. The above policy documents will treat equally sponsors, including Taiwan-funded enterprises, who establish microcredit companies, financing guarantee companies, financing leasing companies and other new types of financial organizations in accordance with relevant regulations. Going forward, the China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission will further improve its market regulatory system, actively support qualified Taiwan financial institutions and enterprises in initiating or participating in the establishment of microcredit companies, financing leasing companies and financing guarantee companies, optimize services, and promote the integrated development of the cross-Strait financial industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Article 2 of the “26 Measures” mentions that Taiwan-funded enterprises may, on market principles, participate in the research and development, standard formulation, product testing, and network construction of the mainland's fifth-generation mobile communications technology. What new opportunities will the 5G industry bring to relevant Taiwan enterprises?","The mainland's 5G market has broad prospects, and cross-Strait enterprises already have a good foundation for cooperation in areas such as standard-setting and technical testing. The “26 measures” just issued include measures supporting Taiwan-invested enterprises' participation in the mainland's 5G development. We hope cross-Strait enterprises will take a long-term view, strengthen their confidence, continue to adhere to the principles of complementary advantages, mutual benefit and win-win results, and jointly build a globalized 5G industrial chain, promoting the healthy development of the global mobile communications industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","The DPP claims that the mainland issuing the “26 measures” at this time is suspected of interfering in Taiwan's elections. What is your response? Second question: The draft “anti-infiltration law” has entered the second reading procedure in the Taiwan legislature. Will this move reduce the willingness of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan youth to go to the mainland to do business and seek employment?","On the first question: we have never interfered in Taiwan's elections. Earlier, at a press conference, we introduced the five major features of the “26 measures,” including that they focus closely on hot spots in economic and social development, further respond to the major concerns of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, have further increased substantive value, further expanded the range of beneficiaries, and reflect a willingness to try new approaches first. The reason these features appear is that, in formulating the “26 measures,” we conducted thorough investigation and research and extensively and carefully listened to the appeals of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses. Among the “26 measures,” some are to be replicated and promoted to more places after being piloted in certain localities first, and some target emerging industry sectors that certain Taiwan businesses are especially concerned about and eager to take part in. Whether what some people on the island call a so-called “declaration” is a substantive breakthrough, let the facts speak for themselves.\nOn the second question, we have noted that for some time, the DPP authorities have continuously engaged in political manipulation through means such as “amending laws,” stirring up hostility across the Strait and restricting and suppressing normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. In practice, this has already caused Taiwan people, especially Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan students, to feel anxious and see danger everywhere. No matter how the DPP authorities change their tactics, their aim is to intimidate and punish Taiwan people who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, and they have already created a “green terror” in Taiwan society. They seek to use this to obtain private political gain, and it does not win the hearts of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland’s “13th Five-Year Plan” mentions expanding personnel exchanges across the Strait and improving policy measures for the treatment of Taiwan compatriots. Since last year, the “31 measures” and the “26 measures” have continued to be introduced. Recently, some Taiwan scholars have suggested that the mainland not “neglect” Taiwan when drafting its “14th Five-Year Plan.” Will the mainland, when drafting…","Thank you for following our series of policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots. Upholding the people-centered development philosophy, and responding to the shared desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, as well as the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots for more development opportunities, we have continuously introduced a series of policy measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, such as the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures.” These measures share mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and provide more equal treatment, and they have been widely welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office will continue to improve institutional arrangements and policy measures that promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integration and development, and safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. In formulating the “14th Five-Year Plan,” we will actively convey the demands of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to relevant parties.\nWe sincerely thank the responsible comrades from the relevant departments who attended today's press conference to answer questions of common concern, and we also thank the journalists present for their attention to the implementation of the “26 Measures.” At the next press conference, we will continue to invite responsible comrades from the relevant ministries to explain in detail the 13 measures in the “26 Measures” that involve providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots. We hope everyone will continue to give them attention and support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191211_12224801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2019-12-13","Hua Chunying","","In his speech at the Center for Strategic and International Studies on December 12, US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asia and the Pacific David Stilwell said the US has provided enormous assistance to China's development over the past decades but they are disappointed that China responded to their good faith with aggressive and consistent bad faith. What's your comment?","We read Mr. Stilwell's remarks. Frankly we cannot agree with him. What he said was not the truth. And attempting to use it to justify wrong US China policies won't work.\nFirst, the fundamental reason for China's achievements in the past seven decades is that under the leadership of the CPC, the Chinese people found a development path that suits our national condition. Our great achievements were made with our people's diligence and wisdom. They were not charity offered by anyone.\nSecond, cooperation between China and the US is mutually beneficial instead of benefiting only one side. Since our two countries established diplomatic ties 40 years ago, our bilateral cooperation has been expanding and delivering huge benefits to the two peoples. The US gained a lot from this process, which I believe American people from various sectors can all feel.\nThird, Mr. Stilwell talked many times about America's \"good faith\", but we don't feel \"good faith\" when the US wantonly restricts and oppresses China in economy, trade, science, technology and people-to-people exchange. We don't feel \"good faith\" when the US smears and attacks China on Hong Kong, Taiwan, Xinjiang, Tibet, human rights and other issues relating to China's core interests including territorial sovereignty and national dignity. And we don't feel \"good faith\" when the US slanders China's social system, development path and cooperation with other countries under various pretexts. We should definitely make strong responses to the wrong words and deeds that undermine China's sovereignty, security and development interests.\nFourth, the root cause of serious difficulties and challenges in China-US relations is that the US cannot objectively view and adapt to the fact that China is developing rapidly. Like State Councilor Wang Yi said this morning at the Symposium on the International Situation and China's Foreign Relations in 2019, US erroneous words and deeds originate from its wrong perception of China and its outlook on China has gone astray. If the US truly wants to develop a China-US relationship that is \"good, rich and mutually beneficial\", it should match its words with deeds instead of being two-faced.\nI'd like to reiterate that China's policy on the US is clear and consistent. We are committed to developing a China-US relationship featuring non-confrontation, non-conflict, mutual respect and win-win cooperation, but such a relationship takes efforts from both sides. Once again we urge the US to reject the outdated Cold-War mindset, reflect on and correct its mistakes, return to reason, view and handle China-US relations in a correct manner, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, undermining China's interests or smearing China, so that our bilateral relationship can return to the right track.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1724378.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201912/t20191213_5418380.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-12-16","Geng Shuang","","CPJ, Committee to Protect Journalists, released a report today about China's influence and operations in Hong Kong and Taiwan and how it is threatening press freedoms. Specifically the report details China using its commercial power as well as visa denials to wield this influence. Can you respond to the allegations in this report?","I haven't read this report, but it is not the first time for institutions like that one to publish such reports. Those false words are not even worth refuting. Anyone with an objective and fair mind has a clear judgment on press freedoms in China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1724891.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/201912/t20191216_5418386.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2019-12-23","Geng Shuang","","The US National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2020 has been signed into law. There are negative contents distorting and smearing China's military development, issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang, and prohibiting purchase of some Chinese products. Does China have a comment?","We deplore the US obstinate moves to pass and sign the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2020, which contain negative elements on China. China has lodged solemn representations. We urge the US to discard the Cold-War mentality and ideological prejudice, view China's development and China-US relations in an objective and rational manner, and not implement clauses with negative contents regarding China, lest it should affect overall China-US relations and bilateral cooperation in important areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1727131.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1727079.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office held the second special press conference on the “26 Measures” in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian presided, and together with Yang Shu, Executive Deputy Director of the Consular Protection Center of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs; Wang Zhiwei, Deputy Director of the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs Office of the Ministry of Education;…","Good morning, dear journalist friends. Welcome to today's press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. We have specially invited Yang Shu, Executive Deputy Director of the Consular Protection Center of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs; Wang Zhiwei, Deputy Director of the Office for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the Ministry of Education; Li Jinsheng, Deputy Director-General of the Department of Professional and Technical Personnel Management of the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security; Man Hongwei, Inspector of the Office for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism; and Wu Jian, Director of the Office for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the General Administration of Sport of China, to introduce in detail the 13 measures concerning the provision of equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots contained in the “Several Measures on Further Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation.” Now, please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Article 18 of the “26 Measures” stipulates that Taiwan compatriots holding Taiwan residence permits enjoy the same treatment as mainland residents in terms of eligibility to purchase housing. Please explain. In addition, Shanghai recently launched 300 public rental housing units for Taiwan youth in the form of public housing. Will this model be extended to other parts of the mainland in the future?","In recent years, the Ministry of Housing and Urban-Rural Development and other departments have continuously issued relevant policies to address the housing needs of the broad Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan compatriots who hold a Taiwan Residence Permit and work or study on the mainland may, in accordance with the relevant policy provisions and based on their own actual needs, purchase commercial housing for self-occupation and personal use. At the same time, some cities on the mainland have implemented purchase restrictions on housing; when Taiwan compatriots buy homes in these cities, they must, like mainland residents, comply with the local policy provisions.\nIn addition to purchasing homes, Taiwan compatriots can in fact also rent public rental housing on the mainland, which we commonly call public rental housing (gonzu fang). Public rental housing is a type of policy-guaranteed housing, mainly intended to address the housing difficulties of people who have long lived, worked, and lived their lives in the local area. Shanghai's special provision of 300 units of public rental housing for Taiwan youth in Shanghai this time is a good thing and a practical measure. It is understood that, in terms of application conditions, residents from both sides of the Strait are treated the same; that is, applicants without Shanghai household registration must hold a residence permit and have paid social insurance.\nIn fact, everyone can pay attention to the fact that among the specific implementation opinions of the “31 measures” issued by 102 localities, many directly involve measures allowing Taiwan compatriots employed locally to apply for public rental housing, for example in Beijing, Guangzhou, Xiamen, and other places. It is understood that at present, 38 and 16 Taiwan compatriots who meet the conditions have respectively applied for local public rental housing in Beijing and Xiamen, and Guangzhou has made available 1,000 talent apartments for Taiwan compatriots who meet the conditions to apply for. Doing good things for Taiwan compatriots, of course, the more the better, and we will actively support and encourage them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","We note that Article 15 of the “26 measures” proposes that Taiwan compatriots may apply to become members of farmers' professional cooperatives, and may also apply for agricultural basic construction projects and fiscal projects that meet the conditions. Please explain the situation in detail.","The development of farmers is an area to which we pay special attention. A farmer professional cooperative is a mutual-aid economic organization that broad masses of farmers establish voluntarily and manage democratically on the basis of household contracted management. It is an effective organizational form for linking smallholder farmers organically with modern agricultural development. After years of development, the product types of farmer professional cooperatives have become increasingly diverse, their cooperative content has continuously expanded, and they have played an important role in leading industrial development and protecting farmers' rights and interests.\nCompatriots from Taiwan may apply to become members of farmer professional cooperatives, share development opportunities on the Mainland, and enjoy equal treatment, which provides favorable conditions for them to achieve better development on the Mainland. In this regard, Fujian Province took the lead in 2014 by cultivating the Zhangping Yongfu Minmin Yuan Highland Tea Production, Marketing and Sales Professional Cooperative, founded by Taiwan farmers, into the Mainland's first provincial-level farmer professional cooperative with Taiwan farmers as its main body, and this year it granted a special fund subsidy of 300,000 yuan.\nBuilding on the pilot experience in Fujian and other places, this measure extends the policy of allowing Taiwan compatriots to apply to become members of farmer professional cooperatives to all parts of the Mainland. After Taiwan compatriots apply to become members of farmer professional cooperatives, they will have more options and conveniences in terms of capital contribution methods, business operations and experience sharing. This will promote mutual learning and resource sharing in cross-strait farmers' organizational management experience, and mutually reinforce and jointly develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Less than a month remains until the Spring Festival, the traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and Taiwan compatriots returning home are very concerned about the status of cross-Strait extra flights. May I ask the spokesperson: How far has the arrangement of cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights for 2020 progressed, and what other arrangements still need to be made?","Yesterday, the cross-Strait civil aviation authorities confirmed and publicly announced the arrangements for the additional flights for the 2020 Spring Festival. Both sides plan to approve all additional flight plans before December 31, 2019, so that passengers can book seats and plan their travel.\nEarlier, at the request of the National Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, local Taiwan affairs associations, and many compatriots, the mainland aviation authorities repeatedly suggested to the Taiwan aviation authorities that they fully meet the reasonable demands of the broad Taiwan compatriots to return home in early January. After repeated communication, we secured the result that both sides' airlines will add flights on January 9 and 10, so that the broad Taiwan compatriots can return home smoothly. Next, we will continue to coordinate with the mainland civil aviation authorities to actively provide assurance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视记者","Could you further introduce what the mainland has done in providing consular protection and assistance to Taiwan compatriots, and in handling travel document applications?\nYang Shu: We have always attached great importance to safeguarding the safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas, and we actively carry out consular protection and assistance work, providing positive help to…","I would like to share one more case, which happened this month. On December 3, while attending activities of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the National People's Congress and visiting Paris, France, ARATS (Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits) Chairman Zhang Zhijun happened to meet a Taiwanese tour group. During the conversation, group member Mr. Ge mentioned that he planned to leave Paris the next morning and transfer through Fuzhou back to Taiwan. However, his Taiwan compatriot travel permit and other documents had been stolen, and he was very distressed, worried that this would affect his onward itinerary, and hoped to receive help. Chairman Zhang immediately introduced to him the content of Article 14 of the “26 Measures” and helped him contact our embassy in France. Staff in the consular department of the embassy handled the matter with urgency, promptly verified the relevant information and quickly processed travel documents for Mr. Ge, helping him smoothly return to Taiwan. Mr. Ge was very grateful and felt that this policy measure was truly practical.\nIn fact, as everyone can see, from handling travel documents and certifying documents and credentials, to assisting in handling foreign civil disputes involving Taiwan compatriots as well as economic and criminal cases, to major emergencies such as earthquakes, floods and the evacuation of citizens, relevant departments on the mainland and our overseas embassies and consulates have always stood behind Taiwan compatriots, helping them solve their problems.\nWe hope that Taiwan compatriot friends traveling and living overseas will remember one sentence: compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family; wherever you are, if you have something happen, dial 12308.\n(Hokkien) If there is a problem overseas, be sure to remember 12308.\n(Hakka) If something happens when you go abroad, call 12308 as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Since the DPP authorities came to power, they have comprehensively restricted cross-strait exchanges for the sake of their own party. They have stirred up a “green terror” on the island, and have falsely accused the “26 measures,” normal cross-strait exchanges and other activities of “interfering in Taiwan's elections,” and have repeatedly publicly defamed and attacked the mainland. What is your comment on this?","We have stated many times that we have never interfered in Taiwan's elections, and we firmly oppose any words or deeds that frame or smear the mainland.\nWhat we care about is the prospects for the development of cross-Strait relations and the interests and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots. We adhere to the people-centered philosophy of development. Starting from the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots residents, we have in recent years successively introduced measures that benefit Taiwan, including the “31 Measures,” the Taiwan Residence Permit, the “26 Measures,” and the Interim Measures on Taiwan Residents' Participation in Social Insurance on the Mainland. We have realized the supply of water from Fujian to Kinmen, and held forums on Taiwan businesses' participation in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, the integration of the Yangtze River Delta region, the Belt and Road construction, and other initiatives. These efforts create favorable conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to share development opportunities on the mainland over a wider scope and in broader fields, and provide more equal treatment. They are widely welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nIn contrast, over the past more than three years, the DPP authorities, for the sake of their own party's narrow interests, have constantly come up with new tricks, trying to divide Taiwan society and create hostility across the Strait. They have reached out to cross-Strait exchanges and targeted the people on the island. At every turn they tear down bridges, cut roads, dig pits, and erect walls, and by every means they block Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises from coming to the mainland for exchange and development, undermining their good interests. When Taiwan compatriots apply for residence permits or come to the mainland to intern or work, they threaten them with “illegality” and warn of control and punishment. When Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises take advantage of the equal treatment provided under the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures,” they confuse public opinion and falsely label it as “accepting united front work” or “being infiltrated.” They play political tricks and undermine the “Golden Horse Awards,” a platform for cross-Strait film and television exchange. They worsen the atmosphere of cross-Strait tourism cooperation and arrest so-called “spies” everywhere, causing mainland tourists to feel uneasy and treating travel to Taiwan as a “dangerous journey.”\nUnder the “green terror” created by the DPP authorities, Taiwan's businesspeople feel panic. The so-called “amendments on Chinese Communist Party agents” and the “anti-infiltration law” leave them unable to work with peace of mind or return home with a sense of security. Retired officials and retired generals feel panic, as restrictions on their exchanges with the mainland keep multiplying and they are often subjected to heavy penalties. Teachers and students feel panic: taking part in normal cross-Strait school exchange activities means being closely monitored by so-called “platforms.” Tourism operators feel panic: not only have their livelihoods been smashed, but they may also frequently be summoned for questioning by prosecutorial and investigative authorities. The media feel panic: anyone who dares to criticize or supervise the DPP authorities may be labeled as “selling out Taiwan.” It can be said that over the past year or more, Taiwan society has been in a state of desolation, with “green terror” shrouding the entire island, and one wave barely subsides before another rises. As long as one holds a position different from the DPP's, one may face overwhelming suppression.\nThe facts are clear: escalating cross-Strait confrontation and undermining cross-Strait relations are the consistent playbook of the DPP authorities in manipulating elections. They have no concern whatsoever for people's well-being. For the sake of electoral self-interest, they are willing to harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, deprive Taiwan compatriots of the opportunity to choose, and restrict the space for Taiwan compatriots' development. This fully exposes the DPP authorities' malicious intent and base nature. Over these years, the situation across the Taiwan Strait has been complex and grave, and Taiwan compatriots have not been living well, feeling distressed and anxious about the future. The fundamental reason lies precisely here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191225_12227923.htm"],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","After the suspension of “free independent travel” by mainland residents to Taiwan on August 1, it has caused a major impact on the livelihoods of 2 million households in Taiwan’s tourism industry. When will individual travel by mainland tourists to Taiwan be allowed again?","The reasons why individual travel by Mainland residents to Taiwan was suspended are clear to everyone. Compatriots on both sides hope cross-Strait relations can return to the right track as soon as possible, and that Mainland residents' travel to Taiwan can return to normal, healthy development as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The results of the 2019 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year selection were announced recently, with the character “困” (trapped) selected. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The annual Chinese character selection activity for the Taiwan Strait, initiated by the Xiamen Haicang Taiwan Investment Zone together with media from both sides of the Strait, has been held for 12 years since 2008. Each year, the selected Chinese character of the year reflects the development and changes in cross-Strait relations and the trends in public opinion on both sides. Looking at this year, cross-Strait relations have become increasingly complex and severe. For the sake of its own party's narrow interests, the DPP authorities have pushed all kinds of “Taiwan independence” activities, have escalated their obstruction of personnel exchanges across the Strait and exchanges in all fields, have continuously heightened cross-Strait hostility, have created cross-Strait confrontation, have seriously undermined cross-Strait relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and have seriously harmed the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots. Therefore, the character “困” (trapped/distress) appropriately reflects the deep concern of compatriots on both sides about cross-Strait relations and their strong indignation at the DPP authorities' reckless actions.\nWe hope that compatriots on both sides will work together to remove obstacles as soon as possible, push cross-Strait relations back onto the right track, and jointly create a bright future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","At her first campaign platform event on December 18, Tsai Ing-wen put forward “four recognitions” regarding cross-Strait relations. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The so-called “four recognitions” she proposed completely reverse black and white and confuse right and wrong. We suggest that everyone read it the other way around: It is the DPP authorities who unilaterally deny the ‘1992 Consensus’ and undermine cross-Strait relations. It is the DPP authorities who restrict cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesses, and Taiwan’s economic development space. It is the DPP authorities who rely on foreign backing and beg for so-called ‘protection’ from anti-China forces with the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents. And it is still the DPP authorities who incite cross-Strait confrontation, raise cross-Strait hostility, create a ‘green terror,’ and seek to fully control Taiwan’s society.\nRecently, the DPP authorities and ‘Taiwan independence’ forces have repeatedly used certain incidents in exchanges between compatriots on both sides to create trouble, using a ‘bait-and-hook’ approach to stir up emotions on the island, incite cross-Strait hostility, and gain electoral advantage for themselves. Compatriots on both sides should remain highly alert and not be taken in.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The spokesperson just mentioned some “green terror” moves by the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities are currently pushing the Anti-Infiltration Act and plan to have it passed by the legislature at the end of this month. What comment does the spokesperson have?","For the sake of one party’s political self-interest, the DPP authorities have taken a great step backward for democracy, completely disregarding the well-being and interests of the Taiwan public, and have forcibly engaged in political manipulation through so-called ‘legal amendment’ measures. The impact is extremely bad and the harm is extremely serious.\nWe note that in recent days, people from all walks of life in Taiwan have expressed strong condemnation and firm opposition. Once this law passes, parties, groups, and individuals whose positions differ from the DPP, media daring to criticize the DPP, Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to study or work, and people participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation may all have baseless labels pinned on them, be hit with ‘sticks in the dark,’ and be subjected to arbitrary investigation, fines, and even criminal imprisonment.\nThe DPP authorities, forcing through an evil law and acting in a perverse manner, creating a ‘green terror,’ banning and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and raising cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, will ultimately reap the bitter fruit of their own actions and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191225_12227922.htm"],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The U.S. side recently signed the FY2020 National Defense Authorization Act into law. The Act supports arms sales to Taiwan, expands high-level military officer exchanges and military exchanges with Taiwan, and requires U.S. intelligence agencies to submit reports on mainland “interference or sabotage” of Taiwan's elections after the Taiwan regional elections. The DPP authorities have expressed gratitude for…","The Foreign Affairs Committee of the National People's Congress and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have already expressed a solemn position on this. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The bill you mentioned contains content concerning Taiwan that seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously damages China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and publicly interferes in elections in the Taiwan region. We firmly oppose it.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding peace in the Taiwan Strait and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and for the sake of electoral self-interest, have done everything they can to smear and attack the mainland, and are fawningly cozying up to anti-China forces in the United States, which is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191225_12227921.htm"],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Could the spokesperson say: recently, Taiwanese internet celebrity Potter Wang co-produced a film with Tsai Ing-wen, which sparked controversy. What is your view? Will such disputes affect civil exchanges across the Strait?","We have made specific inquiries, and this is purely a commercial act by the enterprise itself. We hope everyone will not bring cross-Strait political differences into civil exchanges across the Strait, so that civil exchanges across the Strait can proceed smoothly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","Article 14 of the “26 measures” states that Taiwan residents may apply for travel documents at mainland overseas embassies and consulates. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council has said that even applying for a one-time mainland passport may result in the cancellation of one's Taiwan household registration. May I ask for a response?","The DPP authorities have always made remarks like these that disregard the welfare of the people; it is not surprising.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2019-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Some individual members of the US House recently proposed a bill requiring that the director of the American Institute in Taiwan be confirmed by the Senate, which would be equivalent to a non-portfolio ambassador. What is the spokesperson's view?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The United States can only maintain civil, unofficial relations with Taiwan, and the U.S. side is very clear about this. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. As for the DPP authorities, they are accustomed to fawning and clinging to others, and are not worth commenting on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/201912/t20191225_12227941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2019-12-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Just now, you mentioned the US President has signed the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) for Fiscal Year 2020. The act involves containment on China in many places, and has negative provisions on Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang. Do you have any comment?","On December 20th , local time, the US side signed the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2020. The contents on China in the Act are full of Cold War mindsets and hyping up competition between the US and China and the so called “China Military Threat”. It also contains negative provisions on Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang. This Act severely interferes in China’s domestic affairs and violates the One China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués. It also undermines the relations between China and the United States and the mil-mil relationship, and hurts mutual trust and cooperation between the two sides. The Chinese military is firmly opposed to this Act, and the Chinese side has already lodged solemn representations to the US side.\nChina follows the path of peaceful development and a defensive national defense policy. We stay as determined as ever to safeguard world peace, contribute to global development, and uphold international order. The development of China’s military forces is to protect China’s sovereignty, security and development interests and to address various security threats. Its growth will boost the force for peace in the world. The Chinese military is shouldering greater international responsibilities and providing more public security goods, which have been seen by all the peace-loving nations and peoples and praised by the international community.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question concerns China’s internal affairs and core interests, bears upon the national bond of the Chinese people and allows no external interference. We are firmly opposed to any country to conduct any kind of official exchanges or military contacts with Taiwan. We’ll never allow anyone to separate Taiwan from China at any time in any form. The US side should abandon the illusion to contain China with Taiwan.\nThe US side openly meddles in Hong Kong and Xinjiang, interferes in China’s internal affairs with various kinds of excuses, disrupts prosperity and stability in Hong Kong and smears China’s counter-terrorism and de-extremization efforts. These actions severely violate international laws and the basic norms governing international relations. They are very mean and evil. All attempts by the US side to contain China’s development will be of no effect and will only hurt the US in the end.\nWe urge the US side to abandon the Cold War mindset and the hegemonic logic, stop interfere in China’s internal affairs and not put into practice the negative provisions related to China in the Act, and take concrete actions to protect the overall relations and the mil-to-mil relationship.\nAs for Xinjiang, I’d like to add a few words. Recently, CGTN has made two English documentaries on China’s counter-terrorism efforts in Xinjiang. You may take the DVDs of the two documentaries after the press conference.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-12/27/content_4857655.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-12-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Retired Lieutenant General Wang Hongguang, former deputy commander of the PLA Nanjing Military Area Command, said at a symposium in Beijing on last Saturday that if the mainland launches an attack on Taiwan, the PLA can soon capture the Dongying Island, Dongsha Islands and Penghu Islands. Do you agree with Lieutenant General Wang's remarks? Does this run counter to the concept of \"Peaceful Reunification and One…","I will not comment on the personal views of experts and scholars. As a matter of principle, we follow the policy of peaceful reunification. We expect compatriots across the Taiwan Straits to jointly oppose and contain \"Taiwan Independence”, safeguard peace and stability across the straits, and jointly promote peaceful development of cross-straits relations and the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-12/27/content_4857655.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-12-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's military signed three quotation and acceptance documents with the US for arms purchase including F-16V fighter jets on December 13, indicating that the three arms purchase plans have entered the implementation phase. What’s your comment on that?","China is firmly opposed to arms sale to Taiwan by any foreign countries. Containing China through Taiwan will be of no effect and relying on foreign support will also be a dead end.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-12/27/content_4857655.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2019-12-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to think tank reports from Taiwan, by the year 2030, the PLA will have four aircraft carrier battle groups. In addition, the commissioning of China’s first home-made aircraft carrier Shandong is also closely watched by media in Taiwanese. Do you have any response to the concerns from Taiwan for the aircraft carriers?","On the future development of the aircraft carriers, we will make overall decisions based on the national security needs and equipment development.\nWe follow the policy of peaceful reunification and urge the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits to jointly oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” and protect peace and stability across the Straits, promote peaceful development of the cross-strait relations and push forward the peaceful reunification of China.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2019-12/27/content_4857655.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2019-12-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 31 (electronic dispatch). In response to the Taiwan legislature's passage on December 31 of the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act,” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to questions: In pursuit of political and electoral gain, the DPP authorities have extensively engaged in “green terror,” undermined cross-Strait exchanges and interaction, manufactured hostility and confrontation across the Strait, hurt the feelings of the peoples on both sides, and seriously damaged the well-being and interests of Taiwan residents. People from all sectors on the island strongly condemn and firmly oppose the reckless actions of the DPP authorities, and they express deep concern about the consequences of the DPP authorities' undermining of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said: We warn the DPP authorities that the feeling of blood being thicker than water and of mutual support between compatriots on both sides of the Strait cannot be changed by any force. The trend of shared destiny and close exchange and cooperation among compatriots on both sides cannot be stopped by any force. Acting against the will of the people, deliberately creating cross-Strait antagonism and provoking confrontation will surely bring them the consequences of their own actions. We believe that broad Taiwan compatriots will distinguish right from wrong and understand what is just, jointly overcome interference, and work hand in hand with mainland compatriots to create a bright future for cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/201912/t20191231_12229465.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesman for the Central Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in an interview on January 11 regarding the results of the Taiwan region’s elections:\nOur major policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” adhere to the one-China principle, resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and actions, and resolutely advance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nPeaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to promote common development across the Strait and benefit compatriots on both sides, and it requires the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides to advance. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with Taiwan compatriots to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200111_12231917.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-01-14","Geng Shuang","","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi has wrapped up his visit to Africa and will soon be back to Beijing. How do you comment on his first visit in the new year?","Africa has been the destination for Chinese foreign ministers' first overseas visits each year, and State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang's visit this time marks the 30th consecutive year of this practice. The unique tradition fully reflects the special friendship China and Africa have long cherished through weal and woe. It also shows that developing friendly and cooperative relations with African countries has been China's basic policy and unswerving strategic choice in foreign affairs.\nThe profound friendship between China and Africa has been and will remain unbreakable no matter how the international landscape changes or what others say. China will always stand firmly with our African brothers.\nDuring his visit, State Councilor Wang Yi exchanged views and reached broad consensus with African leaders and foreign ministers on consolidating bilateral relations and deepening mutually beneficial cooperation. Both sides noted the need to speed up the implementation of the outcomes of the FOCAC Beijing Summit, promote high quality BRI development and deepen practical cooperation in various fields. Both sides agreed that China-Africa relationship is at its historical best with promising cooperation in the future. The China-Africa cooperation will continue to take the lead in international cooperation with Africa.\nFacing the complex and fluid international landscape, both sides vowed to continue to strengthen strategic communication and cooperation, jointly uphold multilateralism and basic norms governing international relations, oppose unilateralism and bullying behavior, reject foreign interference, firmly stand on the right side of history and justice, and stand for the common interests of developing countries. The two sides reaffirmed that they will continue to firmly support each other on issues concerning each other's core interests. African leaders and foreign ministers clearly reiterated their commitment to the one-China principle and that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory.\nTaking State Councilor Wang Yi's visit as an opportunity, China stands ready to work with Africa to cement our traditional friendship, enhance the quality and efficiency of our practical cooperation, strengthen international coordination and cooperation and jointly build a closer community with a shared future for China and Africa.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1732174.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200114_5418506.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-15","Geng Shuang","","Does the foreign ministry have any comment on what was said by the leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen in a BBC interview that Taiwan is already independent and has a separate identity from China?","I will refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council for cross-Strait issues. What I can tell you is that there is but one China in the world. The People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. And the one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1732612.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200115_5418512.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, friends of the media. Welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office's first press conference of the New Year. I will be moderating today's press conference. I now take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","At the turn of the year, please summarize the development of cross-Strait relations in 2019 and look ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2020.","In 2019, facing a complex and severe situation across the Taiwan Strait, we thoroughly implemented the important speech General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the \"Message to Compatriots in Taiwan,\" as well as the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China. We resolutely carried out the Central Committee's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work, pushed cross-Strait relations forward despite difficulties, and made solid progress in our work on Taiwan.\nWe adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and resolutely combat and curb all forms of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, safeguarding the overall peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait area. Centered on the theme of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and benefiting compatriots on both sides, we held dialogues with political parties, groups, and individuals on the island that recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" and support peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. These dialogues produced multiple points of consensus, including strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepening cross-Strait integrated development, jointly opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and working together to advance the peaceful unification process. We also issued joint initiatives, and cross-Strait democratic consultation took an important step forward.\nIn our work on Taiwan, we apply the development philosophy centered on the people, serving Taiwan compatriots as we serve the people on the mainland, benefiting Taiwan compatriots, continuously deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and constantly enriching and improving relevant institutional arrangements and policy measures. Building on the implementation of the \"31 Measures\" and the measures serving Taiwan compatriots in the judicial field, we introduced the \"26 Measures,\" which carry greater weight and benefit a wider range of people. We also issued policies and measures opening participation of Taiwan compatriots in mainland social insurance, providing Taiwan compatriots with consistent treatment and allowing them to share the development opportunities of the mainland, thereby enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. We actively explored building a cross-Strait common market, launched preliminary work on the \"small four links\" between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu, and promoted six common standards among relevant cross-Strait industry associations.\nFrom January to November 2019, cross-Strait trade totaled 207.06 billion US dollars, and the mainland remained Taiwan's largest export market. Taiwan businesses and enterprises continued to have confidence in the mainland's economic development and business environment, with direct investment by Taiwan businesses in the mainland up 26.8% year on year, and the number of Taiwan-invested projects up 7.9% year on year. As of the end of November 2019, a cumulative total of 111,955 Taiwan-invested projects had been approved. Preliminary statistics show that in 2019, cross-Strait personnel exchanges totaled about 9 million trips, with more than 6 million trips by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland. Despite constant interference and obstruction from the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces, exchange and cooperation among compatriots on both sides maintained momentum and remained active.\n2020 is the year of wrapping up the goal of building a moderately prosperous society in all respects. On the basis of achieving the first centenary goal, we will embark on a new journey toward building a modern socialist country in all respects. Although the situation across the Taiwan Strait continues to be complex and severe, we have sufficient confidence and capability to overcome various risks and challenges. Fundamentally, the key factor determining the direction of cross-Strait relations is the development and progress of the mainland. We will continue to thoroughly implement the important speeches of General Secretary Xi Jinping and the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee, adhere to the basic policy of \"peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,\" adhere to the one-China principle, firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely oppose any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist plots and acts, resolutely enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233154.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Please briefly introduce the basic situation of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields in 2019, as well as the plans for 2020.","In 2019, the strong expectations of compatriots in Taiwan for strengthened cross-Strait exchange and cooperation stood in sharp contrast to the restrictions and suppression imposed by the DPP authorities; the momentum of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields stood in sharp contrast to the reckless actions of the DPP authorities. We have continued to introduce a series of policy measures to further promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, providing more convenience for Taiwan compatriots who study, work, and live on the mainland, actively encouraging and supporting civil exchange and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, and holding a series of cross-Strait exchange activities welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. Cross-Strait exchanges between compatriots have withstood severe tests and remained basically stable, with the total volume of cross-Strait personnel exchanges maintained at about 9 million person-trips.\nIn the new year, we will continue to promote exchange and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, as we always have, doing practical things, good things, and resolving difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, promoting the joint inheritance and carrying forward of China's excellent traditional culture by compatriots on both sides, and enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233146.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Please briefly introduce the basic situation of cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation in 2019, and your expectations for cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation in 2020.","In 2019, against the backdrop of the Mainland deepening reform, expanding opening up, and continuously optimizing the business environment, all regions and departments made concerted efforts to implement the \"31 Measures\" in detail, and the Taiwan Affairs Office, the National Development and Reform Commission and other departments further issued the \"26 Measures\", promoting new progress in cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation. Last year, cross-Strait trade once again exceeded 200 billion US dollars. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, cross-Strait trade from January to November totaled 207.06 billion US dollars. Taiwanese investment in the Mainland continued to grow. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from January to November, the Mainland approved a total of 4,765 Taiwanese-invested projects, a year-on-year increase of 7.9%; actual use of Taiwan capital reached 1.52 billion US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 26.8%; investment fields further extended from manufacturing to the service industry. In addition, Guangxi, Sichuan, Hubei and other places accelerated the construction of cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones, providing new platforms for Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to develop in the central and western regions. The construction of cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites was further improved. We actively organized Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to participate in national major development strategies such as the \"Belt and Road\" initiative, the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, and the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta region, and made new progress.\nIn the new year, we will continue to expand cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, and continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233147.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","In the recent election of Taiwan's leader, Tsai Ing-wen was re-elected. What impact will this result have on the future direction of cross-Strait relations? With the DPP continuing to govern, what is the overall consideration of the mainland's policy toward Taiwan?","On the evening of January 11, the TAO spokesperson already issued a statement on the results of the Taiwan regional election. Here I emphasize three points again:\nFirst, Taiwan's regional elections cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. Regardless of the results of the Taiwan regional elections, our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan will not change. Regardless of how the political situation in Taiwan changes, peaceful development of cross-Strait relations remains the voice and public opinion of the broad Taiwan compatriots on the island. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, will allow cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be safeguarded and enhanced. Conversely, cross-Strait relations will be undermined, the situation in the Taiwan Strait will become turbulent, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be harmed.\nSecond, national rejuvenation and national reunification are the trend of the times and cannot be blocked by anyone or any force. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for various forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. Confrontation leads nowhere, and “Taiwan independence” is an even more certain dead end. We have firm resolve, full confidence and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. We will never allow anyone, any organization, any political party, at any time, in any form, to separate any piece of Chinese territory from China.\nThird, we maintain a high degree of strategic confidence and strategic resolve in implementing the central government's major policy guidelines toward Taiwan. We will continue to adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” uphold the one-China principle, continue to unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233151.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","After winning the election, Tsai Ing-wen proposed the so-called \"peace, parity, democracy, and dialogue\" as the key to restarting positive interaction and achieving long-term stable development across the Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Since the Democratic Progressive Party authorities took office in 2016, they have refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" unilaterally undermined the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, supported and condoned \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, relied on foreign backing to assert themselves, and repeatedly put forward separatist rhetoric replete with the \"two-state theory,\" wantonly attacked the mainland, incited hostility across the Strait, and escalated cross-Strait confrontation. This is the fundamental reason why cross-Strait relations have deteriorated, negotiations and dialogue have been interrupted, and the situation across the Taiwan Strait has become more complex and grave. Here, I make four responses:\nFirst, adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, is the unshakable foundation for the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations. \"It is easier to shake a mountain than to shake the '1992 Consensus.'\"\nSecond, \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest calamity to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and must be resolutely curbed.\nThird, the trend toward peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the historical tide of cross-Strait relations moving forward cannot be blocked by anyone or any force.\nFourth, Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation. Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan's future shall be determined jointly by all Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233150.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视记者","After her election victory, Tsai Ing-wen claimed that this election demonstrated the rejection of \"one country, two systems\" and insistence on the so-called \"sovereignty and free democracy\" way of life. What is the spokesperson's comment?","For 40 years, “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” has been the basic policy toward Taiwan that we have consistently upheld. Guided by this basic policy, we broke the state of isolation between the two sides of the Strait, opened cross-Strait consultations and negotiations, realized the “three direct links” across the Strait, and formed a great situation of large-scale exchanges and cooperation among compatriots on both sides, profoundly changing the historical face of cross-Strait relations.\nDifferent systems are not an obstacle to unification, much less a pretext for separation. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification. Peaceful reunification best serves the overall interests of compatriots on both sides and the Chinese nation; “one country, two systems” best accommodates reality, respects differences, and safeguards the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The specific form in which “one country, two systems” is realized in Taiwan will fully consider Taiwan's actual conditions, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nDuring the election process in Taiwan this time, the leader of the DPP authorities deliberately framed and smeared the mainland, stoked hostility toward the mainland, created estrangement, opposition, and confrontation among compatriots on both sides, and sought political self-interest. This damages the development opportunities and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Public opinion on the island is concerned about whether the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA), which will soon reach its tenth anniversary, will be terminated after Tsai Ing-wen wins re-election. What is the spokesperson's view?","We have stated many times that since the signing of ECFA, the mainland side has earnestly fulfilled its commitments and ensured the smooth entry into force and implementation of ECFA. As of the end of September 2019, for products under the Early Harvest list for trade in goods, the mainland had cumulatively reduced or exempted tariffs on Taiwan by 38.88 billion yuan. The Early Harvest product list has brought tangible benefits to small and medium-sized enterprises and farmers on the island. From 2010 to 2019, Taiwan’s exports of agricultural products to the mainland under the Early Harvest list grew by more than 2 times, and the mainland has become Taiwan’s largest export market for agricultural products. Regrettably, for well-known reasons, the follow-up Agreement on Trade in Services under ECFA failed to take effect, and negotiations on the trade in goods agreement were forced to be interrupted, so ECFA cannot benefit more Taiwan compatriots.\nWhat I want to stress here is that ECFA was won with difficulty, and I believe compatriots on both sides do not wish to see this important achievement lost.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Outside observers have noted that after the KMT's defeat in this election, voices have emerged within the party calling for a review of cross-Strait policy, arguing that the “1992 Consensus” has been distorted by the DPP and that the KMT needs to reconsider its cross-Strait policy positioning. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","The “1992 Consensus” is the anchor of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Since 2005, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have strengthened exchanges and cooperation, promoted peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and achieved fruitful results. Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is built on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” All political parties, groups, and individuals on the island that oppose “Taiwan independence” and support peaceful development of cross-Strait relations should cherish it all the more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","If the DPP authorities, on the one hand, do not abandon their “Taiwan independence” position, and on the other hand, under public pressure, make some “easing” gestures in cross-Strait relations, will the mainland respond positively?","Confrontation leads nowhere, and “Taiwan independence” is an even more dead-end path. We have also repeatedly reaffirmed that, on the basis of the one-China principle, there are no obstacles to exchanges between any political party or group in Taiwan and us.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200115_12233148.htm"],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","First question: In this election, the “mango dried” effect was extended, and voter turnout among voters under 30 surged. Some people believe that the younger generation does not agree with the KMT's cross-Strait line and the “1992 Consensus,” and that Taiwan's young people are growing further away from the mainland. Will the mainland's policy toward Taiwan youth change? Second question: please introduce the…","First question: The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and sets the parameters for the issues we must address in consultations and negotiations. Compatriots on both sides are Chinese; the mainland and Taiwan are not a “state-to-state” relationship. If cross-Strait dialogue, consultation and the development of cross-Strait relations were not built on the “1992 Consensus,” major problems would arise. Therefore, the “1992 Consensus” is unshakable. Since 2016, guided by the concept that “across the Strait we are one family,” we have continuously introduced a series of policy measures to provide Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, with equal treatment for coming to the mainland and enjoying the opportunities of mainland development. Over these years, more and more Taiwan youth have come to the mainland to study, work, find employment and start businesses. This shows that our policies are effective and are aimed in the right direction. Otherwise, why would the DPP authorities be so terrified of and resentful toward the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures”? We have always held that young people are the future of the Chinese nation, and that young people on both sides of the Strait should engage in more exchange and communication. We will never give up on Taiwan’s young people. Through sustained exchanges and the continuous introduction of a series of policy measures, we will create conditions for young people on both sides to deepen mutual understanding, to gain a correct understanding of cross-Strait relations, and to gain a more objective and accurate understanding of the mainland. I believe that, through “persistent effort and sustained commitment,” compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including their young people, will move closer and closer together.\nSecond question: Relevant departments on the mainland attach great importance to safeguarding the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and have repeatedly and promptly briefed relevant Taiwan authorities on the latest pandemic prevention and control situation. On January 13 and 14, experts from Taiwan visited Wuhan for on-site inspections, comprehensively examining pandemic prevention and control, emergency response, medical treatment, pathogen detection and related issues. They also held exchanges with mainland experts who took part in the epidemic prevention and control and patient treatment, consulted on prevention and treatment information, and visited the laboratories of disease control agencies and the medical institutions treating cases on site. The Taiwan medical experts expressed their heartfelt thanks for the mainland’s reception. We understand that they will return to Taiwan this afternoon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","After Tsai Ing-wen's election victory, calls for “using force to unify Taiwan” rose quickly on mainland internet platforms. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I have already reiterated on several occasions that our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan are consistent and clear, and will not change. I would like to remind the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces that they should seriously reflect on why, in recent years, more and more voices calling for “military unification” have emerged among the mainland’s civilian population. This has been forced out by their reckless and perverse conduct. They should think carefully about where they intend to lead Taiwan and cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The Taiwan legislature passed the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” on December 31 last year. According to Taiwan media reports, the Tsai Ing-wen authorities will officially promulgate the “Anti-Infiltration Act” today. What is the spokesperson’s view?","The “Anti-Infiltration Act” is an out-and-out “bad law.” It restricts the free will of Taiwan compatriots and deprives Taiwan compatriots of the right to engage in cross-strait exchanges. This “bad law” may harm things for a time, but it cannot stop the will and the trend of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait who want to exchange, cooperate, and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","The first question: the mainland has proposed that, toward Taiwan, it will adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” But at present many people on the island reject “one country, two systems.” How does the spokesperson view this? The second question: In this election, Tsai Ing-wen was elected with a high number of votes. Facing new public opinion in Taiwan, will the…","I have already answered the first question very comprehensively just now. I believe that with the further development and progress of the mainland, and as compatriots on both sides increasingly draw closer, become more intimate, move in reality, and go well, more and more people on the island will objectively view and understand “one country, two systems.”\nSecond question: Since 2016, facing the severe and complex situation across the Taiwan Strait, and facing the retrogressive actions of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, we have always united the broad Taiwan compatriots to overcome difficulties and obstacles, actively exerted the influence of our Taiwan policy, promoted peace and stability in cross-Strait relations, and safeguarded the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. This policy will not change, and we will continue to carry it out. As everyone knows, the pilot program for individual tourism by mainland residents to Taiwan was launched against the backdrop of peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations. We hope cross-Strait relations will return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","经济日报记者","In December last year, the Standing Committee of the 13th National People's Congress passed the revised *Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots*, which formally took effect on January 1 this year. May I ask the spokesperson what specific impact this will have on investment by Taiwan compatriots in the mainland?","Since the “Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots” was enacted and implemented in 1994, it has played a positive role in protecting the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in accordance with law, and in encouraging and promoting investment in the mainland by Taiwan compatriots. The amendment to the “Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots” that the National People's Congress Standing Committee has now carried out, which you mentioned, has, in accordance with the principles and spirit of the Foreign Investment Law, abolished the approval and filing management system for the establishment of Taiwan-funded enterprises. This ensures that Taiwan compatriots' investment simultaneously enjoys institutional dividends. This will provide more opportunities and create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to ride the wave of the mainland's comprehensive deepening of reform and further expansion of opening up, and to achieve greater development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland has consistently stressed the need to advance cross-Strait political consultations. To improve cross-Strait relations, how does the mainland plan to address the question of Taiwan's status, which the Taiwan people are concerned about, over the next four years?","First, I must point out that the foundation for improving and developing cross-Strait relations is adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This consensus originates from each side’s own stipulations; it was not imposed unilaterally by the mainland on Taiwan. We also understand that there are inherent political differences between the two sides, and some new issues have arisen in the course of cross-Strait relations. On these issues, we advocate finding solutions through equal consultation under the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","I have two questions. First, Tsai Ing-wen won this election. Could you analyze the reasons why young people in Taiwan supported Tsai Ing-wen? Second, regarding cross-Strait interaction: after the election concluded on the 11th, both sides across the Strait mentioned “peace.” The mainland side often says the two sides are one family, but it is not right for a family to go a long time without talking. Can the two…","I fully understand your concern about the current situation across the Strait. Let me answer the second question first. As you said, peace is precious; everyone yearns for peace, and Chinese do not fight Chinese. But regarding what you mentioned, that “a family does not speak to each other,” we must first acknowledge that we are one family. As long as we acknowledge that we are one family, I think other issues can all be easily discussed.\nReturning to the first question, we have repeatedly stated that regarding elections in the Taiwan region, we do not intervene and we do not comment. One election in the Taiwan region cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. As for how to further do work among Taiwan's young people in the future, and how to improve its targeting and their sense of gain, we will continue to make efforts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","The website of the American magazine *Foreign Policy* recently published an article stating that Taiwan’s “fake news” comes from within Taiwan itself, not from the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? Second question: Zhang Yazhong, Chancellor of the Sun Yat-sen School in Taiwan, announced on the 13th that he will run for chairman of the Kuomintang, and he also said that if he cannot create peace…","On the first question: foreign media have finally had someone say things that accord with the facts, which shows that not all of them lack professional ethics. Facts prove that the “fake news” on the island was jointly fabricated by the DPP authorities, “Taiwan independence” forces and foreign anti-China forces, who are in cahoots with one another, with the thief crying “stop, thief!”\nOn the second question: we will not comment on matters within Taiwan, especially internal party affairs.\nBeijing Daily reporter: I have two questions. Tsai Ing-wen, when meeting Li Yingjie, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office, said that Taiwan-US relations have been upgraded to “global partners,” and that over the next four years, in security cooperation, Taiwan and the US will continue to strengthen Taiwan's self-defense capabilities. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second, public opinion generally holds that Tsai Ing-wen won the election by playing the “anti-China card” against the backdrop of the Hong Kong turmoil. What is the spokesperson's comment?\nOn the first question: Taiwan is part of China, and Taiwan's participation in international affairs must and can only be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The one-China principle is the fundamental premise and political foundation for China to develop relations with all countries, including the United States, and is also the common understanding of the international community. If the DPP authorities continue to rely on foreign powers to bolster themselves and indulge in subjective illusions, in the end it will only be “a spring dream.”\nOn the second question: we do not comment on Taiwan's elections. Media on both sides of the Strait have already carried fairly full and detailed analyses of this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Some Taiwanese youth on the mainland have reported that, worried about being implicated in Taiwan's “anti-infiltration law,” many mainland investors are taking a wait-and-see attitude toward investing in Taiwanese youth startups, and some have already decided to withdraw their earlier investments. What is the spokesperson's comment? Another question: Please briefly introduce the main situation of handling…","To answer the first question first: if what you describe is accurate, it can only further prove that the “Anti-Infiltration Act” is an out-and-out “bad law” that is undermining good things for Taiwan’s youth. We will continue to implement the various measures benefiting Taiwan. Whoever sincerely helps Taiwan’s young people and provides them with development opportunities and space, and whoever keeps harming their vital interests, they will ultimately understand.\nSecond, according to incomplete statistics, in 2019 the relevant departments and localities across the country reported a total of 109 Taiwan-related emergency incidents to the Taiwan Affairs Office, including 43 maritime Taiwan-related emergency incidents, 15 accidents such as tourism and traffic accidents, 11 emergency rescue cases, 3 natural disasters, 2 criminal cases, and 35 cases of Taiwan compatriots committing suicide or dying of illness on the mainland. As mentioned just now, among these 109 Taiwan-related emergency incidents, 44 people died, 17 were injured and 7 went missing. The Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the relevant departments and localities, handled all of these incidents properly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Second question: after the implementation of the “Anti-Infiltration Act,” Taiwan people now going to the Mainland to develop is like “taking a risk.” Although the Mainland keeps releasing measures for Taiwan, civil exchanges will still be affected. How will the Mainland respond?","What I want to tell you is that no matter how the situation across the Taiwan Strait changes, our policies and measures to promote civilian exchanges across the Strait will not stop, will not be cut off, and will not be reduced. On this basis, as for how to counter the damage that the “Anti-Infiltration Act” does to cross-Strait exchanges, I believe Taiwan compatriots must first “save themselves.” I do not believe Taiwan compatriots will allow themselves to be bound hand and foot by such an “evil law.” You may appeal to compatriots on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","To follow up on the question of “individual travel”: After Taiwan's elections ended, the impact was not only a sharp decline in Taiwan's tourism-related stocks, but also affected many cross-Strait families. Recently, a mainland journalist complained on social media that during their posting in Taiwan, their spouse could not come to Taiwan to visit relatives. What is the mainland's response to help those affected…","First, the reason that spouses of mainland reporters stationed in Taiwan cannot visit Taiwan for family reunions is the restrictions imposed by the Taiwan authorities. I suggest that everyone appeal to the Taiwan authorities to promptly allow reporters' spouses to visit Taiwan. As for the Taiwanese reporters stationed on the mainland, if your spouses come to visit, the Taiwan Affairs Office will resolutely provide assistance, without any hesitation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外网记者","Recently, news emerged on the island that the New Party may be dissolved. At its meeting on the 13th, the New Party resolved to oppose dissolution, arguing that its line has not been wrong and that its party chairman, Yu Mu-ming, will hand over the post when his term expires. The New Party has also said it insists on “peaceful unification to protect Taiwan” (和统保台), and that its determination to advocate peaceful…","We have repeatedly expressed that the New Party and Chairman Yu Muming have long adhered to the one-China principle, opposed “Taiwan independence,” advocated cross-Strait unification, and made important contributions to promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We sincerely admire this. Going forward, we will continue to maintain contact and strengthen communication with all groups, parties, and individuals on the island that oppose “Taiwan independence” and advocate improving and developing cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Second question: With the Spring Festival approaching, what measures has the mainland taken to help Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots return home for the New Year?","Cross-Strait Spring Festival charter flights have started. Cross-Strait airlines applied for a total of 306 additional flights under the 2020 Spring Festival plan: 242 from mainland airlines and 64 from Taiwan airlines. The mainland civil aviation authorities completed all approvals at the end of December 2019. At present, mainland airlines and some maritime and other transport departments are actively carrying out related work, and are fully assisting cross-Strait compatriots’ travel during the Spring Festival, especially the broad number of Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","A scholar, speaking at the Global Times annual conference late last year, asked why efforts to win popular support and do mass work have failed among Taiwan compatriots. Has the mainland studied at which link the problem occurred?","I will not comment on the scholar’s remarks. Placing our hopes in the Taiwan people is a policy we have consistently upheld. Since the 18th Party Congress, and especially since 2016, we have adhered to a people-centered development philosophy and the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” and have introduced a series of policy measures conducive to winning popular support. These have made progress and produced results. The journalists present have long traveled back and forth across both sides to conduct interviews, and you have come into contact with people and events more concretely and comprehensively than I have. We should look at the big picture. One or two elections in Taiwan will not decide the future. As everyone can recall, over the past 40 years cross-Strait relations have moved forward amid difficulties and twists. Difficulties have always existed, but everyone should have confidence. No matter how many difficulties and challenges we encounter, we can respond to them and overcome them, and we always maintain confidence and resolve.\nThe press conference ends here. In 10 days the Gengzi Spring Festival will arrive. On behalf of all colleagues of the Taiwan Affairs Office Press Bureau, I extend early New Year greetings to the cross-Strait media journalists and your families. I wish you good health, smooth work and a happy family in the new year. Thank you all again for coming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202001/t20200115_12233155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-01-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 16: In response to Tsai Ing-wen’s recent remarks on cross-Strait relations in an interview with the BBC, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 16th: Taiwan has never been a country; Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China. Anyone who attempts to challenge this iron-clad fact will only be battered and bloodied and end up in utter disgrace.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We warn the leaders of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not to inflate their own importance or misjudge the situation, and not to further create tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait, which would drag Taiwan into a dangerous situation. Our resolve to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock. No one, no organization, no political party, at any time and in any form, will be allowed to split off any piece of Chinese territory from China!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202001/t20200116_12233599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-01-17","Geng Shuang","","Taiwan announced that a US warship sailed through the Taiwan Strait on Thursday. Do you have a comment?","China paid close attention to and monitored from start to end the passage of the US military vessel through the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations as it bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, prudently and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan to avoid harming China-US relations and affecting peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1733473.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200117_5418524.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-20","Geng Shuang","","Can you share with us any new details on how China is coordinating with other countries to prevent the spread of the new coronavirus?","You may have noted that the Chinese health authorities have released relevant information on the prevention and control of pneumonia outbreak caused by the new coronavirus. You may refer to that.\nHere I want to stress that since the outbreak, China has taken proactive measures to handle it in a serious and professional manner. We have worked to formulate strict prevention and control schemes, spared no effort to treat the patients, properly managed close contacts, carried out in-depth epidemiological investigations, released the information on epidemic prevention and control in a timely manner, and launched campaigns to raise awareness of the disease.\nAt the same time, China has informed the World Health Organization, relevant nations, regional organizations, and its Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions of the outbreak in a timely manner and maintained close communication with them. We have shared with the WHO the information on the genome sequence of the new coronavirus as soon as possible. After receiving notification of cases from relevant countries, China has taken that seriously and stayed in close communication with all parties through bilateral and multilateral channels, while strengthening cooperation with all-out efforts to deal with them.\nWe hope other countries can immediately inform the Chinese side of suspected imported cases through official channels with a view to better prevention and control. We will work with all parties to jointly tackle the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1734309.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200120_5418530.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-20","Geng Shuang","","Recently, Japan, Thailand and the ROK all reported cases of the infection by new coronavirus. It is the peak season for the Spring Festival travel rush in China, and many people are concerned about it. What measures will China take to prevent the outbreak from spreading around the world?","According to what I learned from relevant authorities, Japan, Thailand and the ROK have informed China of confirmed cases of new coronavirus infections. China has maintained close communication and cooperation with these countries on treatment, prevention and control.\nAs for what measures China will take to prevent the spread of the epidemic, I can tell you that the Wuhan government has taken measures to control the flow of people leaving the city. I would refer you to competent authorities and relevant local governments for more details.\nI would like to emphasize once again that after the outbreak of the new coronavirus-caused pneumonia in Wuhan, relevant Chinese authorities have informed the WHO, relevant nations, regional organizations, as well as China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner and stayed in close communication with them.\nAt the same time, relevant departments of the Chinese side have also disclosed information and briefed the public on the developments of the epidemic in a timely manner. We will work with all parties to jointly tackle the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1734309.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200120_5418530.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-21","Geng Shuang","","The WHO said they are holding an emergency meeting about the coronavirus outbreak. We want to know if China's sending representatives, and if so, who?","After the outbreak of pneumonia caused by the novel coronavirus, the Chinese government has attached high importance and made comprehensive deployment on prevention and control.\nActing with openness, transparency and a high sense of responsibility towards global health security, Chinese authorities shared information of the epidemic with the WHO, relevant nations and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner, including the genome sequence of the new coronavirus.\nAs far as I know, upon invitation from the WHO, China will join other affected countries at an International Health Regulations (IHR) Emergency Committee meeting on the night of January 22 Beijing time. Relevant countries, the WHO and experts will share information and come up with a science-based evaluation at the meeting.\nChina will continue to deepen international cooperation and work in concert with the international community to deal with the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1734624.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200121_5418536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-21","Geng Shuang","","Given that now there there's confirmed human-to-human transmission of the coronavirus, is China stepping up prevention or control in outbound Chinese travelers from Wuhan?","Like I said yesterday, the Wuhan government has taken measures to control the flow of people leaving the city. The latest news is that they have stepped up control over the flow of people leaving or entering Wuhan. I'd refer you to the competent and local authorities for more details.\nI'd like to stress again that Chinese authorities, acting with a high sense of responsibility, shared information of the epidemic with the WHO, relevant nations and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner. After receiving notification of cases from relevant countries, China has taken it seriously and stayed in close communication with all parties through bilateral and multilateral channels, while strengthening cooperation with all-out efforts to deal with them. We will work with all parties to jointly tackle the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1734624.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200121_5418536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-21","Geng Shuang","","In light of the recent developments over the past 24 hours, will China be enforcing any more checks at airports or any other places where people would be leaving China for destinations in foreign countries in order to reduce risk of spreading this virus? You talked about restrictions on people entering and leaving Wuhan, what kind of advice is China giving to people thinking about going to Wuhan for the Chinese…","I'll leave these questions to the competent authorities.\nWhat I can tell you is that we have formulated comprehensive, strict prevention and control schemes in response to the pneumonia outbreak caused by the novel coronavirus. We are determined to curb any momentum of spreading.\nLike I said earlier, Chinese authorities, acting with a high sense of responsibility, shared information of the epidemic with the WHO, relevant nations and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner. We will work with all parties to jointly tackle the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1734624.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200121_5418536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-22","Geng Shuang","","Do you think Taiwan's exclusion from the WHO in the current situation in any way impairs its ability to respond to the coronavirus outbreak? Taiwan has called for the WHO to allow space for Taiwan's participation. I wonder if you have any response to that?","No one cares more about the health and wellbeing of our compatriots in Taiwan than China's central government does. After the pneumonia outbreak caused by the novel coronavirus took place in Wuhan, the National Health Commission notified the Taiwan region in a timely and prompt manner. From January 13 to 14, as requested by relevant authorities in Taiwan, experts from the Taiwan region went to Wuhan to see our work on prevention and control, medical treatment and pathogen detection. They also had discussions with experts in the mainland who participated in related medical work. The Taiwan experts expressed heartfelt appreciation for their reception in the mainland.\nAs we repeatedly stressed, Taiwan's participation in international organization activities must be arranged in a fair and reasonable manner following the one-China principle after cross-strait consultations. Based on the arrangement made by China and the WHO, medical experts from the Taiwan region can attend relevant technical meetings at the WHO, and the WHO can send experts to Taiwan to inspect or assist when necessary. The Taiwan region has timely access to WHO's information on global public health emergencies, and any emergency happening in the Taiwan region can be reported to the WHO in time. Those arrangements ensure that the Taiwan region can handle public health emergencies in a timely and effective manner regardless of where they may take place.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1735126.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200122_5418542.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-22","Geng Shuang","","I wonder if you have an update on whether or not China will impose travel restrictions given the increasing number of foreign countries reporting cases of pneumonia caused by the new coronavirus?","At this morning's press conference at the State Council Information Office, officials from the National Health Commission gave a thorough account of prevention and control measures concerning the pneumonia outbreak caused by the new coronavirus and answered questions from the press. I have nothing further to update you at the moment.\nI'd like to stress that acting with openness, transparency and a high sense of responsibility towards global health security, Chinese authorities shared information of the epidemic with the WHO, relevant nations and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner. While stepping up efforts to contain the outbreak, we will deepen international cooperation and work together with the international community to deal with the epidemic and safeguard regional and global health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1735126.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200122_5418542.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-23","Geng Shuang","","Regarding the pneumonia epidemic caused by the novel coronavirus (nCoV), the WHO has decided to postpone a decision on whether or not to declare a global health emergency. I wonder what is the foreign ministry's response? Is China in favor of declaring such an emergency?","On the night of January 22 Beijing time, in the form of telephone conference, the WHO convened the first Emergency Committee meeting in response to the pneumonia caused by the novel coronavirus.\nAfter the meeting, WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus didn't declare the nCoV a global health emergency.\nAs I know, parties concerned will stay in close communication and coordination on evaluation and possible adjustment of prevention and control measures. The committee plans to hold another meeting later.\nActing with openness, transparency and a high sense of responsibility to global health security, Chinese authorities will continue to share information of the epidemic with the WHO, relevant nations and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions in a timely manner. We believe the WHO Emergency Committee will have fair, fact-based and reasonable evaluation and judgment on the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1735680.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200123_5418548.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-01-23","Geng Shuang","","A statement was recently released by a coalition in Sao Tome and Principe consisting of the the Democratic Convergence Party, The Force for Democratic Change Movement and the Union of Democrats for Citizenship and Development. It clarifies that the \"congratulations\" from former President Fradique de Menezes to recently elected Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen were not true at all, a piece of fake news that was…","We noted this statement and commend this coalition in Sao Tome and Principe for reaffirming its commitment to the one-China principle and clarifying the truth.\nThe one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. In the past three years or so after China and San Tome and Principe resumed diplomatic ties, our bilateral relations have developed smoothly and our cooperation has benefited both peoples. The attempt to undermine our friendly relations will never succeed.\nWe advise the DPP authority to give up those pathetic tricks that fool only themselves and make them a laughing stock of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1735680.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202001/t20200123_5418548.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-02-02","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Wuhan, February 1 (Xinhua): Since the outbreak of the novel coronavirus pneumonia epidemic, media on both sides of the Strait have been deeply concerned about the situation of Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan. On February 1, the head of the Wuhan Taiwan Affairs Office accepted a media interview on the Taiwan-related work of epidemic prevention and control in Wuhan.\nThe head of the Wuhan Taiwan Affairs Office said that under the unified command of the municipal and provincial epidemic prevention and control headquarters, and under the specific guidance of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Fujian Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, we have, guided by the principle of attaching great importance to and caring for the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, actively carried out Taiwan-related epidemic prevention and control work. We have promptly kept track of the situation of Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan, responded in a timely manner to their needs, released prevention and control information through various channels, and proactively provided them with epidemic prevention services and assistance with daily life.\nAfter the city's announcement on January 23 of outbound traffic control measures, the municipal and district Taiwan Affairs Offices and the Wuhan Taiwan Business Association actively coordinated and, at the first opportunity, contacted airlines and others to ascertain the number and basic information of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Wuhan due to flight cancellations. Regarding the Taiwan compatriots known to be stranded in Wuhan, each district Taiwan Affairs Office contacted them one by one by phone to ask about their health and to understand their various needs. At the same time, we established a daily information reporting system on epidemic prevention for Taiwan compatriots, and made all preparations for emergency response at any time.\nDuring the quarantine period, the municipal and district Taiwan Affairs Offices and the Wuhan Taiwan Business Association used phone calls, WeChat groups, WeChat official accounts, QQ groups, and other channels to promptly pass epidemic prevention and control information to Taiwan compatriots and their relatives, help Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan understand the situation and protect themselves, and actively calm and steady the emotions of Taiwan compatriots remaining in Wuhan. We separately set up consultation hotlines for Taiwan compatriots, and announced them through WeChat groups and WeChat official accounts to receive requests for help and consultation. In recent days, district Taiwan Affairs Offices have worked through the street and community work mechanisms to help Taiwan compatriots with epidemic prevention and control, and have visited and offered condolences in communities where Taiwan businesspeople live in concentrated numbers. They delivered anti-inflammatory medicines, masks, disinfectant, and other medical protective supplies in more than ten batches, promptly resolving the shortages faced by some Taiwan compatriots whose household supplies were insufficient.\nAccording to information currently available, there are about 476 Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan. Among the Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan, there were 3 suspected cases, and 1 has been confirmed. All of them were promptly taken for medical treatment and nucleic acid testing with the assistance of the Taiwan Affairs Office, and the confirmed Taiwan compatriot has been arranged for hospitalization. Most Taiwan compatriots remaining in Wuhan understand the current epidemic prevention and control measures and, together with the general public of Wuhan, are cooperating actively to minimize going out and to strengthen self-protection. Some Taiwan compatriots need to return to Taiwan as soon as possible due to work or family needs. We attach great importance to this and are actively helping to resolve it.\nSeveral Taiwan-invested enterprises and kind-hearted Taiwan compatriots have expressed their willingness to fulfill their social responsibility, contribute their love, and support the epidemic prevention efforts in Wuhan. Our office will work with the Wuhan Taiwan Business Association to assist with donations from Taiwan enterprises and compatriots and will publish statistics in due course. Here, we sincerely thank Taiwan compatriots and enterprises for their support and dedication to epidemic prevention work.\nThe head of the Wuhan Taiwan Affairs Office emphasized that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We will further raise our level of service, continue to strengthen care for Taiwan compatriots in Wuhan, and promptly address their needs and difficulties. We hope that Taiwan compatriots, together with the citizens of Wuhan, will overcome the hardships of the times together and jointly win the battle against the epidemic.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200207_12240002.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 4 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding on the 4th to Taiwan-related issues concerning the novel coronavirus pneumonia epidemic, said: We have always cared about the health and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan, and there is no obstacle to Taiwan obtaining epidemic information.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that after the novel coronavirus pneumonia epidemic broke out, from the standpoint of attaching great importance to the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots, the mainland repeatedly and promptly notified Taiwan of the latest epidemic prevention and control information. In particular, it notified Taiwan of information on the mainland's sharing of the novel coronavirus gene sequence with the WHO and on ways to obtain the relevant gene sequence, and it immediately notified Taiwan of relevant information on Taiwan compatriots diagnosed on the mainland. At the request of Taiwan's disease control authorities, the mainland arranged for Taiwan epidemic prevention experts to visit Wuhan for on-site inspection. Both sides strengthened communication, which played a positive role in jointly carrying out epidemic prevention and control.\nMa Xiaoguang said that doing epidemic prevention and control well is directly related to the safety of compatriots on both sides and is the most important and urgent matter at present. The DPP authorities should stop all political hype and political manipulation using the epidemic as a pretext, and stop interfering with epidemic prevention and control work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200204_12238273.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 4: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, on February 4, responding to questions about Lai Ching-te's visit to the United States, said that the One-China Principle is the fundamental premise and political foundation for China's development of relations with all countries, including the United States. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between our diplomatic allies and Taiwan. The US side should abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. We warn the DPP authorities once again that “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. Anyone or any force that tries to inflate their own weight by relying on foreign powers will surely reap the bitter fruit of their own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200204_12238375.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, February 5 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said in an interview on February 5 that, under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee and the united efforts of the people of all ethnic groups across the country, the epidemic prevention and control work for the novel coronavirus pneumonia is proceeding in an orderly manner. The Taiwan work system resolutely implements the Party Central Committee’s requirement to attach great importance to and show concern for the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, places the safety and health of the people first, treats Taiwan compatriots equally, and earnestly carries out epidemic prevention and control work.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan affairs work agencies of relevant provinces and municipalities have set up epidemic prevention and control leading groups. Local Taiwan Affairs Offices have proactively strengthened contact with Taiwan compatriots, Taiwanese enterprises and Taiwan-funded enterprise associations in their localities; some have carried out “one-on-one” services, promptly learned about conditions, carried out epidemic prevention publicity, shown greater care for and attention to Taiwan compatriots, promptly learned about their needs and difficulties, and worked to coordinate the resolution of practical problems. Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are actively cooperating with local epidemic prevention and control work. Currently, three Taiwan compatriots on the mainland have been confirmed as cases and two are suspected cases; all have been promptly arranged for medical treatment. On February 3, we assisted in arranging for the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei for various reasons to return to Taiwan on a China Eastern Airlines Spring Festival extra flight. We are working urgently to make return arrangements for other Taiwan compatriots in Hubei who wish to return to Taiwan.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that in this epidemic prevention work, from the very beginning the mainland side has adhered to a high level of attention to the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, has maintained communication with relevant parties in Taiwan, arranged for Taiwan experts to conduct on-site inspections in Wuhan, and has continuously provided timely information and relevant materials. As of February 4, the mainland side had notified the Taiwan side of epidemic information 36 times in total, and the Taiwan side had notified us 15 times.\nMa Xiaoguang said that sharing weal and woe and helping one another in times of hardship are traditional Chinese virtues, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are blood brothers and sisters and a community with a shared destiny. Whether it is the care and support that local governments and the public on the mainland show for Taiwan compatriots in their localities, or the support that all sectors of Taiwan society show for the mainland’s fight against the epidemic, or Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises voluntarily donating money and goods to express their love, all demonstrate the fraternal bond of blood being thicker than water and the family affection of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that epidemic prevention and control is the top priority of current work. Local Taiwan affairs work agencies will further diligently and solidly carry out epidemic prevention and control work related to Taiwan affairs, and relevant parties will continue to maintain communication and coordination such as information sharing on cross-Strait epidemic prevention work. In accordance with epidemic prevention and control needs, we will manage and serve cross-Strait personnel exchanges well. For Taiwan compatriots returning to the mainland from Taiwan for work or study after the Spring Festival holiday, we will strengthen epidemic prevention and control publicity and carry out quarantine and health protection work. For Taiwan-funded enterprises resuming production, we will actively provide services to ensure that epidemic prevention and control work and production and business operations proceed normally and in an orderly manner. We hope that relevant parties in Taiwan will properly handle the matter of mainland students in Taiwan returning to Taiwan and safeguard their health, schooling and other rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200205_12238674.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 6 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding on February 6 to questions about Lai Ching-te's visit to the United States and his contacts with the US side, said: We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. Lai Ching-te's visit to the US, his seeking to meet US officials and members of Congress, and his use of these occasions to carry out despicable schemes of “Taiwan independence” and national division have been spurned by all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200206_12239468.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 6. Title: Epidemics Are Merciless, but Compatriots Show Love: Governments and All Walks of Life Across the Mainland Show Concern for and Care of Taiwan Compatriots\nXinhua reporter\nSince the outbreak of the novel coronavirus (2019-nCoV) pneumonia epidemic, the Mainland side has attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, treated Taiwan compatriots equally, provided timely care, and actively provided services to Taiwan-invested enterprises, ensuring that epidemic prevention and control work and production and business operations proceed normally and in an orderly manner.\nMa Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that the Taiwan Affairs Office and the relevant provincial and municipal Taiwan affairs work bodies have set up epidemic prevention and control leading small groups. Local Taiwan Affairs Offices have proactively strengthened contact with local Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan-invested enterprise associations; some have provided “one-on-one” services, promptly learned about the situation, carried out epidemic prevention publicity, enhanced care for Taiwan compatriots, promptly learned about their needs and difficulties, and worked to coordinate solutions to practical problems. Taiwan compatriots on the Mainland who were confirmed or suspected to have the illness have all been promptly arranged for medical treatment.\nIn Hubei, where the epidemic was most severe, the provincial Taiwan Affairs Office implemented a daily reporting system on information about Taiwan compatriots, directed the province's Taiwan Affairs Office system to contact and connect with each Taiwan compatriot in Hubei, and promptly compiled information on their health status, willingness to return home and other matters. It organized the Taiwan Affairs Office system and guided local Taiwan-invested enterprise associations to carry out “one-on-one” services, conduct home visits or telephone condolences, and donate protective supplies such as masks and disinfectant. It sent letters of condolence to Taiwan compatriots across the province and promptly provided assistance to those with special difficulties who requested it.\nAfter coordination among many parties and careful preparation, on February 3 the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots who had been stranded in Hubei for various reasons returned to Taiwan on a China Eastern Airlines Spring Festival additional flight. “At present, about 900 Taiwan compatriots in Hubei have requested assistance in returning to Taiwan. In recent days, we have been intensively counting and contacting Taiwan compatriots applying to return to Taiwan. The relevant information has been fully collected, and Taiwan compatriots in some remote counties and cities have already gathered with the assistance of local epidemic prevention and control command headquarters,” said Xing Junzhi, deputy director of the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office.\nIn Zhejiang, the Wenzhou Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office and the municipal Taiwan-invested enterprise association immediately published epidemic prevention announcements and personal hygiene and epidemic prevention knowledge via WeChat groups, provided free delivery of disinfectant, and helped Taiwan compatriots purchase protective supplies.\n“Most Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots in Wenzhou have returned to Taiwan for the New Year. At present, about 30 members of the Taiwan businesspeople association in Wenzhou and their family members are all equipped with masks and other protective supplies, and there have been no cases of Taiwan businesspeople, compatriots or family members being infected or quarantined,” said Zhang Xianqing, president of the Wenzhou Municipal Taiwan-Invested Enterprise Association. “The municipal Taiwan Affairs Office often calls us to learn about our daily lives, asks whether we have any difficulties needing help, and encourages us to support and look after one another.”\nZhang Xianqing said that daily life has not been greatly affected, that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots in Wenzhou feel relatively reassured, and that they currently have no intention of returning to Taiwan and are willing to stay in Wenzhou to avoid increasing risk through movement. “If we work together with one heart, we will certainly overcome the epidemic and restore normal production and daily life.”\n“Epidemic prevention and control requires early detection, early reporting, early isolation and early treatment, and it also requires calming people's hearts and warming people's hearts,” said Chen Wei, secretary-general of the Beijing Municipal Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League. He said that the Beijing Municipal Committee and the Hubei Provincial Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League and Beijing Forestry University jointly carried out a public-emergency mental health micro-course activity.\nStarting February 2, 14 faculty members from the Psychology Department of Beijing Forestry University successively opened live-streaming rooms on WeChat to teach Taiwan compatriots knowledge related to responding to the epidemic and to provide free remote psychological assistance. Nearly 500 people have watched the courses.\nAfter the Spring Festival, more and more Taiwan compatriots returned to their places of work. Six to seven tenths of the more than 300 members of the Hangzhou Municipal Taiwan-Invested Enterprise Association have already returned to Hangzhou. President Zhou Baohua said that members are mainly quarantining and working from home, preparing to resume work and business. Taiwan compatriots in Hangzhou have received considerable substantive help and spiritual comfort, and everyone's mindset is relatively stable.\n“As of February 1, there were 98 Taiwan businesspeople in Hunan in total,” said Quan Guanghui, director of the Economic Division of the Hunan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office. “As some Taiwan-invested enterprises resume work, some Taiwan businesspeople will gradually return to Hunan. We will contact each of them one by one to learn about their health conditions, actual difficulties and needs.”\nChen Junren, chairman of Changsha Tongli Xingye Real Estate Development Co., Ltd., said: “Before the New Year, the municipal Taiwan Affairs Office went to the enterprise specifically to show concern for everyone's health and urged us to pay attention to safety. After the New Year, both the provincial and municipal Taiwan Affairs Offices sent messages asking whether we plan to return to Hunan soon, saying that if we need anything, we should contact them immediately. These measures are heartwarming.”\n“Some colleagues have already returned to Taiyuan, and the municipal Taiwan Affairs Office follows developments every day and reminds us to strengthen personal protection,” said Wang Wenjie, a Taiwan businessman in Shanxi. He said the Taiwan businesspeople WeChat group he belongs to has 46 members, and relevant information is released promptly. “We have confidence in the Mainland's success in halting the epidemic.”\nAffected by the epidemic, Taiwan-invested enterprises face development difficulties. Taiwan Affairs Offices across the Mainland have proactively strengthened contact with local Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan-invested enterprise associations, promptly learned about the needs and difficulties of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, and worked to coordinate solutions to practical problems.\nIn Jiangsu, the provincial Taiwan Affairs Office issued a notice to help resolve difficulties faced by Taiwan-invested enterprises in epidemic prevention, employment, financing, orders, logistics and other areas, helped Taiwan-invested enterprises make full and proper use of support policies, and promptly assisted Taiwan-invested enterprises whose international trade contracts could not be performed on schedule or at all due to the epidemic. Through the provincial Council for the Promotion of International Trade, it issued relevant factual certificates of force majeure to reduce enterprises' losses. It also issued the “Legal Guidance Recommendations on Production and Business Operations of Taiwan-Invested Enterprises during the Epidemic” for reference by Taiwan-invested enterprises, covering three aspects: labor employment, commercial contracts and common issues in contract performance, and epidemic prevention and safety management.\n“Officials from the Taiwan Affairs Office, the Industry and Information Bureau, the subdistrict office and others often convey epidemic prevention policies and measures through WeChat, phone calls and visits, and guide us in doing epidemic prevention in the factory area and personal protection. We are very grateful for the government's concern!” said Shi Jikun, assistant general manager of Inventec (Nanjing) Technology Co., Ltd.\nOn the 2nd, Suzhou municipality published the “Ten Policies on Responding to the Novel Coronavirus Pneumonia Epidemic and Supporting Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises in Overcoming Difficulties Together,” which help enterprises jointly overcome hardships in areas such as expanding financial support, stabilizing the workforce, and reducing enterprise burdens. “These policies also apply to Taiwan-invested enterprises, which greatly encourages Taiwan businesspeople. I believe everyone can get through the difficulties,” said Cai Hanxin, a Taiwan businessman in Kunshan.\nEpidemics are merciless, but compatriots show love. Sharing hardship together and looking out for one another are the traditional virtues of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are blood-related brothers and sisters, a community of shared destiny. Whether it is the concern and care shown by governments and the public across the Mainland toward Taiwan compatriots, or the support from all walks of life on the island for the Mainland's fight against the epidemic and the voluntary donations of money and goods by Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to express their love, both demonstrate the fraternal bonds thicker than water and the familial kinship of cross-Strait families as one. (Writing reporter: Liu Huan; contributing reporters: Yu Pei, Zhang Yujie, Luo Xin, Duan Jingjing, Xi Yue, Lu Huadong, Lü Mengqi, Wang Xuetao)","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200218_12244404.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a reporter's question, some people on the Taiwan side claimed that they had a priority order for which Taiwan compatriots should be brought back first. Ma Xiaoguang said: The Taiwan side demanded a priority ranking for Taiwan compatriots' flight seats, which prevented the China Eastern Airlines aircraft from implementing the transport plan in a timely manner. In fact, the time for concentrated…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 6 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in an interview with reporters on the 6th that after the first batch of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei were successfully transported home on February 3, subsequent transport arrangements have been repeatedly obstructed by the Taiwan authorities, so the transport plans that China Eastern had scheduled for the 5th and 6th have still not been carried out.\nMa Xiaoguang said that after the novel coronavirus pneumonia outbreak, many Taiwan compatriots in Hubei who had planned to return to Taiwan for the Spring Festival, as well as Taiwan compatriots who had come to Hubei temporarily to visit relatives, on business, or for tourism, were stranded locally because flights were cancelled and routes suspended. Some Taiwan compatriots needed to return to Taiwan for work, school, medical treatment, and family reunions, and asked local Taiwan Affairs Offices for assistance. After careful assessment, and with full consideration of the actual needs of the stranded Taiwan compatriots, the relevant parties decided, under the overall arrangements for local epidemic prevention and control, to have China Eastern Airlines arrange transport by way of extra cross-Strait Spring Festival flights. On February 3, the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots returned to Taiwan safely.\nMa Xiaoguang said that in the first transport operation, out of responsibility for the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots, and in accordance with Hubei Province's relevant epidemic prevention and control requirements, each Taiwan compatriot made a written commitment before returning to Taiwan that they had had no contact with confirmed or suspected cases of novel coronavirus pneumonia within the past 14 days, and agreed to accept local epidemic prevention measures after returning to Taiwan. Before leaving home in Wuhan, after arriving at the airport, and before boarding, each of these compatriots had their body temperature measured three times to screen for fever. The relevant authorities in Hubei Province and Wuhan City, as well as customs, border inspection, and other departments, carefully and meticulously assisted Taiwan compatriots in returning home. Of the 250 passengers originally booked, 1 was advised to stay behind after showing fever symptoms during screening, and 2 could not board because their documents were not in order. All 247 passengers met the conditions for entry into Taiwan, and all completed clearance and entered that same evening. The following day, the Taiwan side even expressed approval of this transport operation. But in the past two days, the Taiwan authorities have suddenly changed their attitude, repeatedly delaying the return of Taiwan compatriots on various pretexts, and have groundlessly accused relevant parties on the mainland, turning a good deed done to serve Taiwan compatriots into unreasonable political hype on the island.\nRegarding the reasons why China Eastern's subsequent planned transport could not be carried out, Ma Xiaoguang said that on February 4, China Eastern submitted to Taiwan's civil aviation authority a plan to operate 2 flights each on the evenings of February 5 and 6, transporting about 890 Taiwan compatriots in total, but did not receive confirmation of cooperation from the other side. The Taiwan side said it has “limited capacity to accommodate,” and that “it is absolutely impossible to continuously accommodate and settle 890 people within two days.” We believe this should not be a reason to refuse the return of Taiwan compatriots from Hubei. First, the Taiwan side once loudly claimed it would take back Taiwan compatriots in Hubei, and publicly stated it would “make full preparations.” Second, even if Taiwan's epidemic prevention measures were insufficiently prepared, it could fully have gradually settled returning personnel while intensifying its preparations. Its current approach of comprehensively blocking transport, not allowing even a single flight through, completely disregards the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, and this is hard to justify. Taiwan compatriots in Hubei feel deeply disappointed about this, and believe that the Taiwan side's attitude and approach are chilling.\nMa Xiaoguang said that despite obstruction by the Taiwan authorities, relevant parties in Hubei have still, true to their original intention, provided assistance services to Taiwan compatriots. As of 8 a.m. on February 6, 979 Taiwan compatriots had applied for help returning home, and the full list was submitted to the Taiwan side through cross-Strait civil aviation channels at 9 a.m. On this basis, China Eastern proposed to Taiwan's civil aviation authority a transport plan of 2 flights each on the 6th and 7th and 1 flight on the 8th, to meet the return needs of Taiwan compatriots as soon as possible. But as of the evening of the 6th, the Taiwan side was still delaying on various pretexts.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that, amid the heavy burden of epidemic prevention and control, the efforts by all relevant parties on the mainland to transport Taiwan compatriots in Hubei back home reflect sincere care and humanitarian concern for Taiwan compatriots, and absolutely will not allow some Taiwan politicians to fabricate rumors, smear, or make baseless attacks. Some people in Taiwan have gone from saying one thing and meaning another to hurling insults over the arrangements for Taiwan compatriots' return, which fully exposes their vile disregard for the interests of Taiwan compatriots. The Taiwan side should immediately stop all political manipulation, promptly confirm its cooperation with China Eastern's transport arrangements, and provide the necessary conditions for Taiwan compatriots in Hubei to return home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200207_12239517.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 7: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in an interview with reporters on the 7th that this morning, the leader of the DPP authorities continued to argue, claiming that “the principles of giving priority to the vulnerable and giving priority to quarantine must be implemented,” attempting to mislead public opinion, shirk responsibility, and continue to delay and obstruct Taiwan compatriots in Hubei from returning home. We must refute and clarify this to set the record straight.\nFirst, regarding whether the arrangements for the first batch of Taiwan compatriots' return home took care of the “vulnerable.” The Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, on the basis of statistical surveys, drew up the overall arrangements for transporting Taiwan compatriots home, and Taiwan's demands were all within our considerations. Because the epidemic in Wuhan is severe, and taking into account factors such as timing and geography, the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots transported were all those stranded in Wuhan, and all of them personally asked the local Taiwan Affairs Office for assistance and urgently needed to return to Taiwan. Among them, temporary visitors to Wuhan, minors under 18 traveling with family, known chronic disease patients, and people over 60 accounted for more than half. Therefore, claims such as the list being “not as expected” and that “the order agreed upon was not followed, and the vulnerable and those needing special handling did not make it onto the first flight home” are completely disregarding facts and making unreasonable arguments. If the subsequent transport work had proceeded smoothly as planned, all Taiwan compatriots with needs, including those in other parts of Hubei, should now all have returned to Taiwan. On the contrary, it is precisely because the Taiwan side has repeatedly delayed and obstructed with all kinds of excuses that nearly 1,000 Taiwan compatriots' return home has been blocked, and even the “vulnerable” have not been spared. The Taiwan side repeatedly claims to care for the vulnerable; it should promptly cooperate with us to complete the subsequent transport operations, and not use the excuse of “giving priority to some over others” to delay again and again.\nSecond, regarding whether the mainland's quarantine work was thorough. The Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office and the Wuhan Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office have repeatedly explained publicly that Hubei's relevant authorities, with a high degree of responsibility for the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots, conducted comprehensive quarantine screening of the first batch of Taiwan compatriots boarding flights back to Taiwan, and strictly implemented local testing requirements at every procedure and link. All boarding passengers underwent three body temperature checks before and after boarding with no abnormalities and wore masks throughout. None of the passengers boarding had fever or similar conditions. The vehicles going to the airport were fully disinfected before passengers boarded, and the drivers and accompanying staff also had their body temperatures checked and wore masks throughout, in line with epidemic prevention requirements. The above situation was explained to the Taiwan side before the China Eastern flight took off on the 3rd. Hyping up one case of fever among the 247 Taiwan compatriots after they returned to Taiwan, and then claiming that the mainland “caused difficulties for quarantine,” is completely untenable.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the epidemic in Hubei and Wuhan remains extremely severe, and we are deeply concerned about the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots who have been stranded here for a long time. We call on the DPP authorities not to ignore the interests of the relevant Taiwan compatriots any longer, not to continue to argue and make things difficult with any excuse, and to confirm their cooperation with the China Eastern transport arrangements so that Taiwan compatriots in Hubei can return home as soon as possible.\nHe also said that we serve Taiwan compatriots wholeheartedly and with full effort, and we will not allow Taiwan politicians to fabricate rumors, slander, or make baseless attacks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200207_12240108.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On February 9, the PLA Eastern Theater Command organized naval and air forces to conduct combat readiness patrols. Authoritative sources believe this is a warning against Lai Ching-te’s sneaky visit to the United States for collusive activities. Please explain. Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks on this matter.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 10th in response to a question: Leaders of the DPP authorities have recently repeatedly made separatist remarks with “two-state theory” implications, adopted a posture of increasing cross-Strait confrontation, intensified planning of new Taiwan-US collusion, and used this opportunity to seek “independence” and openly carry out dangerous provocations. The relevant actions of the Chinese People’s Liberation Army are to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We advise the DPP authorities not to play with fire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200210_12241054.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 14 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, on the 14th commented on erroneous “Taiwan independence” remarks made by Yu Xikun, saying that Yu Xikun, head of Taiwan's legislative body, used the COVID-19 epidemic to spout nonsense, openly advocated “Taiwan independence,” hurt compatriots' feelings, and undermined cross-Strait relations, once again exposing the delusion of a very small number of people on the island to “use the epidemic to promote independence.” Faced with the epidemic, these people do not think about how to protect the lives and common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait; instead, they spread political virus, create cross-Strait confrontation, and obstruct mutual care and assistance among compatriots on both sides. They have lost basic conscience, and they are disgraceful.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, a road that cannot be taken, and will only bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan. Some politicians, inflated with self-importance and moving against the tide, disregard the well-being and safety of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and will only end up bloodied and battered.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200214_12243335.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 14 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 14th: Since the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, we have always placed the lives and health of the people first. Regions, departments and the broad masses have united and worked hard to fight the epidemic. The Taiwan work system attaches great importance to and cares about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, actively provides epidemic prevention services and living assistance to Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, carefully treats Taiwan compatriots who fall ill, and through extra flights during the Spring Festival transported some Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei back home. It has assisted Taiwan-funded enterprises in all regions to resume work and production in an orderly way. Many Taiwan compatriots have demonstrated the righteousness of being in the same boat and have donated funds and supplies to contribute to epidemic control.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces are exploiting this epidemic to profit from the crisis, engaging in extensive political manipulation, continuously escalating cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and recklessly worsening the atmosphere of cross-Strait relations, fully exposing their ugliness to the core.\nThey keep putting forward cold-blooded measures full of discrimination and disregarding the rights and interests of the people, even violating basic morality and human ethics, and separating cross-Strait marriages and families. This fully exposes the hypocrisy of their so-called “democracy,” “human rights,” and “humanitarianism.”\nOn the issue of Taiwan compatriots returning from Hubei, they are insincere in what they say. They keep fabricating excuses such as insufficient epidemic prevention capacity to obstruct and delay, so that nearly a thousand Taiwan compatriots are still blocked from returning, and the delay has now exceeded 10 days. Could it be that after so many days they still cannot arrange epidemic prevention measures that would let these compatriots return? This fully exposes their purpose: to delay as long as they can, and to delay for as long as they like. When Taiwan compatriots return is not in their consideration at all. For their own political interests they are willing to sacrifice the life and health of Taiwan compatriots, with no basic human conscience.\nThey manipulate public opinion, suppress criticism of groups and individuals on the island, and use Green camp politicians, Green media, and the internet armies they keep to fabricate and spread false information and rumors, attacking and slandering the mainland. This fully exposes their dark mentality of using the epidemic to stir up a new round of “anti-China and anti-Chinese” sentiment.\nThey remain silent about the on-site inspection of Wuhan by Taiwan's epidemic prevention experts in early January, and silent about the mainland's multiple notifications of the epidemic to the Taiwan side. They refuse to admit that they can obtain epidemic and related technical information from the mainland and the WHO in a timely manner. They maliciously fabricate names for the epidemic and recklessly attack the WHO for adhering to the one-China principle, and they fabricate the rumor that the Taiwan side broke the one-China principle to participate in WHO activities. These fully expose that their hyping of the issue of participation in WHO activities has nothing to do with epidemic prevention needs, and has nothing to do with public health and safety. It is entirely a political calculation, seizing the opportunity to seek “independence.”\nThey rely on foreign backing to assert themselves, attempting to use the epidemic to incite “Taiwan independence” consciousness. This fully exposes the plot of “using the epidemic to seek independence.”\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that “Taiwan independence” acts harm the feelings and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. They are a political plague even more “poisonous” than the virus. We have the ability and confidence to win the battle to contain the epidemic, and we have even greater determination and ability to defeat all kinds of “Taiwan independence” activities. The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces, persisting stubbornly in their course, will surely reap what they have sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200214_12243476.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to reporters' questions, the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention agency stated on the afternoon and evening of the 14th that on February 9 the two sides had reached a consensus that China Airlines would operate the flight to transport the 121 people on the “priority return list” proposed by the Taiwan side, but the mainland side suddenly reneged and demanded that 979 people be transported on five…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 15 — On February 3, the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots in Hubei boarded China Eastern’s Spring Festival extra flight to return home, but subsequent transport has so far not been implemented, drawing close attention from both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities recently accused the mainland side of refusing cooperation, causing the transport arrangements to “fall apart.” What exactly happened, and why have Taiwan compatriots in Hubei still been unable to return home? On the 15th, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, gave an interview to reporters and laid out the facts of the matter.\nMa Xiaoguang said that on February 6, I introduced the situation in which China Eastern’s transport plan had been blocked, pointing out that the Taiwan side had repeatedly used excuses to delay the return of compatriots and kept making groundless accusations against the mainland, turning a good deed—our efforts to overcome various difficulties to serve Taiwan compatriots—into unreasonable political hype. In the days since, the Taiwan side has not only continued to obstruct and delay compatriots’ return home, but its populism and political manipulation has escalated, even resorting to fabrication and rumor-mongering to cover up the truth.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the above is the full process of communications through cross-Strait civil aviation channels up to now. The facts make clear that what the head of Taiwan’s epidemic prevention agency said is entirely false. Both sides have been communicating about China Eastern’s transport arrangements all along. Clearly, on February 6 China Eastern proposed a complete plan to transport Taiwan compatriots, yet the Taiwan side repeatedly blocked and delayed it under various pretexts, and on February 9 it changed its position and proposed that China Airlines operate the flight. Where is the “mainland reneging” supposed to have come from? It was also this same person who declared that a new COVID-19 confirmed case had appeared among the first batch of compatriots returning to Taiwan, which triggered hype on the island and became the Taiwan side’s pretext for blocking the return home of compatriots in Hubei. However, the Wuhan Taiwan Affairs Office, based on specific and conclusive facts it had gathered, found that the confirmed case announced by the Taiwan side had many doubtful points that neither conform to medical norms nor make obvious sense, and therefore raised seven questions. This Taiwan epidemic prevention official has every responsibility to explain the facts to the public honestly, yet from February 8 until now, apart from hedging and evasion, he has remained silent on the seven questions. This Taiwan compatriot was declared a confirmed case yet was not informed, was not sent to hospital for isolation treatment, and was not subjected to measures different from other passengers on the same flight. Who could believe such a strange thing? Yet it is precisely this case, full of doubtful points, that the Taiwan side has made a big fuss about, using it as a reason to block China Eastern’s flight. Only after repeated demands from the mainland side did the Taiwan side, on the 13th, provide some information about this case. If it really was a confirmed COVID-19 case, how much harm would a delay of 10 days in providing relevant information cause to other passengers on the same flight and to Hubei’s epidemic prevention efforts? Just the other day, this same Taiwan epidemic prevention official, disregarding basic humanitarian spirit, announced that children of cross-Strait marriages and families would not be allowed to return home. This cold-blooded decision not only brings greater disruption and obstruction to the return of Taiwan compatriots in Hubei, but also causes harm to many Taiwan families.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the “priority for the vulnerable” claimed by the Taiwan side is in fact a pretext for delaying China Eastern’s flight. In reality, among the first 247 compatriots to return home, we have already taken into account the elderly, children and adolescents, and patients with chronic illnesses, and 98 people were given priority transport. We have also said that transporting them as quickly as possible is the greatest priority, in line with the interests of every Taiwan compatriot who needs to return home quickly. Now everyone can see very clearly that the Taiwan side dragged its feet until the 9th before proposing a “priority list” of 121 people, long after it had delayed China Eastern’s earlier flight arrangements. So where does “priority” come from? Moreover, among the 979 Taiwan compatriots China Eastern planned to transport, nearly 85% were temporary residents in Hubei, nearly 400 were minors under 18 or elderly people over 60, and nearly 80 were patients with chronic illnesses. The list of 121 proposed by the Taiwan side took none of these circumstances into account and cannot truly reflect the actual urgent needs of compatriots in Hubei. As for the Taiwan side’s claim that epidemic-prevention “reception capacity is limited,” it should not forget that on January 30 the DPP authorities themselves said they would bring back Taiwan compatriots in Hubei and declared with confidence that they “would make full preparations.” Why, a few days later, did they instead use “insufficient reception capacity” as a pretext for rejecting China Eastern’s transport? “Insufficient reception capacity” is a problem that must be resolved first and is not difficult to resolve. Ten days have passed with no result, which is hard to believe. Is it a lack of will? A lack of ability? Or something else? We have proposed that the Taiwan side accelerate the expansion of epidemic-prevention reception facilities while not completely suspending the transport of returning compatriots. This fully takes into account the greatest concern of compatriots in Hubei who urgently need to return home, and is also based on understanding and consideration for the island’s public. We have proposed that the Taiwan side produce an exact timetable for completing its epidemic-prevention arrangements, to facilitate orderly arrangements for the subsequent transport of compatriots in Hubei. This is also reasonable, yet the Taiwan side has so far avoided the matter. What is the real reason? It should explain clearly.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that on the matter of transporting compatriots in Hubei back home, the facts are clear. The Taiwan side first used “epidemic prevention first,” “vulnerable people first,” and insufficient epidemic-prevention capacity as pretexts, then later raised unrelated complications by proposing that China Airlines carry out the transport. They keep looking for excuses and changing tactics to delay and obstruct China Eastern from carrying out the transport. Who truly cares about and helps Taiwan compatriots, and who is pushing hard to delay and block, constantly creating side issues—right and wrong are clear and obvious to all. In fact, the Taiwan side’s various excuses and pretexts all serve to delay transport and obstruct compatriots’ return home. Trying to use lies to shirk responsibility and cover up their own contradictory words and actions will not work. Facts are a mirror that reflects their inner thoughts and true face. In the end, the DPP authorities have never taken the interests of Taiwan compatriots to heart. They never intended to let compatriots in Hubei return quickly, but have done everything they can to block them, delaying wherever they can, obstructing wherever they can, and dragging things out for as long as they can. Starting from genuine concern for Taiwan compatriots’ health and welfare and sincere help for them, the mainland side has long made all arrangements for transporting compatriots in Hubei home, and these compatriots are anxiously waiting. We urge the DPP authorities not to place their own narrow interests above the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and to promptly agree to China Eastern’s transport so that compatriots in Hubei can return home safely and soon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200215_12243729.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-20","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 19. Title: The DPP authorities should stop blocking the way for Taiwan compatriots to return home\nBy Xinhua reporter\nThe first batch of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei took an extra China Eastern flight home about two weeks ago. However, because of obstruction and delays by the DPP authorities, China Eastern's follow-up transport plan has been held up until now. A few days ago, a spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office restored the facts in more than three thousand words and exposed the many lies of the DPP authorities. Faced with the question “Do they really want Taiwan compatriots to go home or not?”, the DPP authorities still resorted to a “stalling tactic.” Under pressure from compatriots on both sides of the Strait calling for the stranded Taiwan compatriots in Hubei to be brought back as soon as possible, the head of the Taiwan epidemic prevention agency recently declared that China Airlines “can carry out the mission at any time,” and accused the mainland of “delay and non-cooperation.” Continuing to play such tricks of deception that turn right into wrong is truly cold-blooded to the core!\nTo block the route home for the stranded Taiwan compatriots in Hubei, the DPP authorities have gone to great lengths, fabricating untenable pretexts such as “epidemic prevention first,” “the vulnerable first,” and “insufficient epidemic prevention capacity,” and they have also raised the unreasonable demand that China Airlines must carry out the transport, adding complications. Anyone who understands the situation can see that these are malicious obstructions and political manipulation. They are not only refusing to let Taiwan compatriots go home, they are also treating Taiwan compatriots as a “political card,” using them to smear and attack the mainland, stir up cross-Strait hostility, and seek to profit from the chaos. Put simply, the DPP authorities are willing to sacrifice the health and basic rights of the people for their own political interests, which fully exposes their selfish, vicious, and bloodthirsty political nature.\nAmong the 979 Taiwan compatriots waiting to return home, nearly 80 have chronic illnesses, and nearly 400 are over 60 years old or are children under 18. Over the past half month, they have been anxious, suffering, and disappointed; how painful it is to feel unable to return home. Some Taiwan students stranded in Hubei have written to the leaders of the DPP authorities to appeal: “I want to go home, I want to go to school,” “I hope I can go home soon to finish my homework and prepare for the new semester,” “I hope you can give us a road home”... Their words are sincere and enough to move any listener. Can the DPP leaders hear the cries written in these immature handwriting lines, or do they simply not want to listen and cannot be bothered? The head of the Taiwan authorities' epidemic prevention agency still responded with cold, bureaucratic boilerplate, as if nothing mattered. People can find the answer in that.\nThe truth of the facts cannot be disputed; justice and warmth are in people's hearts. We warn the DPP authorities that placing the private interests of one party above the interests of the people, and being full of deception and scheming, is not only shameful but is destined to be rejected by public opinion and punished by history. Hubei and China Eastern have long been fully prepared. If the DPP authorities still have a shred of human decency, they should immediately stop their political calculations, agree to China Eastern's transport as soon as possible, and allow the anxiously waiting Taiwan compatriots to set out on the road home sooner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200220_12245187.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to reports, on the 21st the Taiwan legislature passed a so-called “joint statement” that disregards the one-China principle and relevant provisions of international organizations, and raises the unreasonable demand that the World Health Organization (WHO) “accept Taiwan’s participation in WHO operations in a complete and unimpeded institutionalized manner.” What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 21 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 21st in response to a question: Regarding the Taiwan-related issue at the World Health Organization, we have repeatedly stated our principled position clearly, comprehensively and systematically. In fact, on the basis of the one-China principle, medical and health experts from the Taiwan region of China participate in technical activities of the WHO in an individual capacity, and there is no obstacle to the Taiwan region obtaining public health information published by the WHO, including the information on this COVID-19 epidemic. Therefore, the reason the DPP authorities repeatedly hype the WHO's Taiwan-related issue, and even attack the WHO and make unreasonable demands that violate the relevant rules of international organizations, is precisely to engage in political manipulation. The scheme by some people in Taiwan's legislature to push a so-called “declaration” with ulterior motives, using the epidemic to seek independence, will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200221_12246077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-02-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 21 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding on the 21st to Wu Cheng-tien’s assumption of the post of New Party chairman, said: Since its founding, the New Party has consistently and firmly supported one China, opposed ‘Taiwan independence,’ and advocated peaceful reunification of the two sides. Mr. Yu Mu-ming made efforts and devoted much energy to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations during his tenure as New Party chairman, and we highly appreciate this. We believe that under the leadership of the new party chairman, Mr. Wu Cheng-tien, the New Party can continue to make positive contributions to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nZhu Fenglian said that we will continue to maintain communication with all Taiwan parties, groups, and individuals that oppose ‘Taiwan independence’ and advocate improving and developing cross-Strait relations, including the New Party, strengthen dialogue, jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly seek the peaceful reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200221_12246112.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-02-24","Zhao Lijian","","First question, recently Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders said in an interview that if he becomes president of the US, he would not sit by and allow invasions to take place if China takes military action against Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this? Second question, you said that as long as we reporters do objective coverage, the foreign ministry will continue to support our work. My question is, what then can…","To answer your first question, we noted relevant reports. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs and no foreign country has the right to interfere. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and prudently handle issues relating to Taiwan so as to avoid causing harm to China-US relations and peace and stability across the strait.\nRegarding your second question, instead of pestering the foreign ministry spokesperson, you should ask WSJ why it hasn't made public apologies and who should be responsible for the insulting article.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1748946.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202002/t20200224_5418644.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 26: In response to recent fallacies, such as those advanced by Democratic Progressive Party figure Tsai Chi-chang and others, who advocated adjusting the cross-Strait discourse to the so-called “Republic of China, Taiwan,” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on February 26: These “Taiwan independence” statements expose the sinister intentions of certain people on the island to promote “gradual Taiwan independence” and escalate cross-Strait hostility and confrontation. The essence of this scheme is to benefit one party’s private interests at the expense of the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, which is a complete deception of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and international public opinion.\nZhu Fenglian stressed: The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is an immutable fact that will not change. “Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history and a dead end. We call on Taiwan compatriots to join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” and safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202002/t20200226_12248241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-02-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Following a joint air-sea combat-readiness patrol on February 9, the PLA conducted joint exercises in waters southeast of Taiwan on February 10. A person in charge of the Taiwan administrative department complained that the mainland, in time of the COVID-19 outbreak, still flew military aircraft around Taiwan, which caused concerns among Taiwan people and undermined regional peace. What’s your comment?","The Spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has released information on this issue. I want to emphasize that the combat-readiness patrol and joint exercises conducted by the PLA are aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and protecting the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. These operations are targeted specifically at “Taiwan independence” forces and their secessionist activities.\nTaiwan is a part of China. We warn the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) of Taiwan not to play with fire. Any attempt to secede Taiwan from China is doomed to fail.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2020-03/01/content_4861321.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2020-02/28/content_4861262.htm",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-02-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Senator Bernie Sanders, one of the US Democratic presidential candidates, said in an interview that he “will not stand by” if China decided to take military actions against Taiwan. What’s your comment?","The Taiwan question belongs to China's internal affairs, and brooks no foreign interference. Those actions fueling cross-strait hostility and confrontation will only bring disasters to the compatriots in Taiwan. Any attempt to resist reunification by force is doomed to failure. Containing China with Taiwan will not work. The PLA has the firm will, full confidence and sufficient capabilities to safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2020-03/01/content_4861321.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2020-02/28/content_4861262.htm",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-03-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 4. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on March 4: Because of repeated obstruction by the DPP authorities, 1,148 Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei who urgently need to return home still cannot go home. Su Tseng-chang recently publicly spread the “Su-style lie” again, continuing to disregard facts and reverse right and wrong, falsely claiming that “the bottleneck is on the mainland side.” One really wonders whether the world still knows the meaning of the word “shame.”\nZhu Fenglian said: Since the epidemic broke out, on the one hand, the mainland has fully taken care of the lives and epidemic prevention needs of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. On the other hand, it has fully considered the actual needs and homecoming wishes of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei, and actively arranged for China Eastern Airlines to transport the first batch of 247 Taiwan compatriots back to Taiwan on February 3. On February 5, and on many occasions thereafter, it proposed reasonable arrangements to transport other Taiwan compatriots who had requested to return home as soon as possible, including arrangements proposed by cross-strait airlines jointly operating temporary flights, to meet the eager wish of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei to return home. However, the DPP authorities, time and again, changed their excuses, kept setting up obstacles, and repeatedly delayed and obstructed. On February 15, our office's spokesperson disclosed in detail the whole process of the mainland's continuous transport arrangements and unremitting efforts to make transport possible, and the specifics are clear and the facts are plain. That the DPP authorities keep using various excuses to stop China Eastern's follow-up transport is obvious to all. Su Tseng-chang himself once publicly said that not letting those in Hubei go back was because the island lacked capacity for epidemic prevention and accommodation. What is more, the DPP authorities put the 1,148 Taiwan compatriots who hoped to return for employment, study, family reunion, and other purposes onto a so-called “annotated control list,” completely blocking the way home for Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei. The facts repeatedly prove that the DPP authorities simply do not want Taiwan compatriots in Hubei to go home. The obstruction on the return path of Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei, the “bottleneck,” lies in the hands of these DPP politicians.\nZhu Fenglian emphasized: Su Tseng-chang attempts to divert attention and shift responsibility with self-contradictory lies, which seriously underestimates the intelligence of the broad Taiwan compatriots. We urge him to have at least a basic moral bottom line, to stop talking nonsense, and to stop spreading rumors and making trouble. We ask him: Dare you say that you will immediately agree to let these 1,148 Taiwan compatriots return home?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200304_12251516.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-03-05","Zhao Lijian","","Reports say the US House of Representatives recently passed the \"Taiwan Allies International Protection and Enhancement Initiative (TAIPEI) Act of 2019\". The act puts out that the government should consider \"increasing or decreasing the United States Government's economic, security, or diplomatic engagement with another nation as a result of an action taken by that nation to either strengthen or undermine ties…","This Act is in serious violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques. It goes against international law and basic norms governing international relations. China is firmly against it. The one-China principle is the prevailing trend recognized by international consensus. Altogether 180 countries have established diplomatic relations with China. The US itself established diplomatic ties with China on the basis of the one-China principle more than 40 years ago. However, now it is going against the trend of the times by thwarting other sovereign nations' pursuit of normal relations with China. This cannot be justified.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, comply with international law and basic norms governing international relations, take concrete measures to prevent the Act from becoming law, and handle issues relating to Taiwan prudently to avoid serious damages to bilateral relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1752564.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202003/t20200305_5418690.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-03-05","Zhao Lijian","","Joseph Wu made comments today accusing China of forcing the Malaysian state of Sarawak to reinstate a travel ban against visitors from Taiwan. They had previously canceled the ban. Do you have a comment about this accusation?","China opposes politicizing epidemic prevention and control measures. We hold Taiwan compatriots' health and welfare dear to heart. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities' political maneuvering over the outbreak is just despicable.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1752564.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202003/t20200305_5418690.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-03-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 5. On the 5th, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to the recent passage by the US House of Representatives of the so-called “Taipei Act,” said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed a solemn position on the House's passage of Taiwan-related legislation. US congressional Taiwan-related bills that openly obstruct other countries from establishing diplomatic relations with China and help Taiwan expand its so-called “international space” are utterly unreasonable. We firmly oppose any interference by the US in China's internal affairs in any form and any undermining of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that, over the recent period, the US Congress has repeatedly and again and again manipulated so-called Taiwan-related bills. This will only stir up more trouble across the Taiwan Strait, create more troubles for China-US relations, and ultimately harm the interests of the US itself.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities always try to use this kind of form to rely on foreigners to enhance their own standing. The result will only intensify tension and turmoil in cross-Strait relations and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200305_12252093.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-03-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 7 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 7th: We have noted the result of the by-election for chairman of the Kuomintang. For many years, the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have consolidated mutual trust, engaged in positive interaction, actively promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhanced the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. The current situation in cross-Strait relations is complex and severe. We hope that the Kuomintang, under the leadership of Chairman Chiang Chi-chen, will cherish and maintain the existing political foundation of the two parties, play its role as a bridge and link in cross-Strait communication, and work toward maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the interests and well-being of compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200307_12253222.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-03-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 12 — In response to the recent release by the U.S. Department of State of its “2019 Country Reports on Human Rights Practices,” which mentions that the mainland attempts to “manipulate” Taiwan's media through commercial pressure and restricts Taiwan journalists' reporting, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 12th that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed a solemn position on the U.S. Department of State report. The content of the report concerning cross-Strait news exchanges is entirely fabricated, distorts right and wrong, and is maliciously slanderous.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that news exchange across the Strait is a bridge and link that enhances mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides and promotes Chinese culture; it is a matter between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We have always supported, and will continue to actively support, media exchange and cooperation across the Strait, and we provide convenient working conditions for Taiwan journalists reporting in the mainland. The U.S. report is full of lies that go against basic facts and common sense and is full of political bias, which precisely exposes the unspeakable and ulterior political intentions of some U.S. politicians.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities, by every means, restrict cross-Strait media exchanges, intimidate and suppress Taiwan media that hold different positions, and collude with Western anti-China forces to fabricate the rumor of “mainland manipulation of Taiwan media.” The United States, acting as an accomplice of the DPP authorities, is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200312_12255379.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-03-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 13 —\nTaiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, in an interview on the 13th, said that the Taiwan affairs system and relevant departments and localities have thoroughly implemented the important speech spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the meeting on coordinating the advancement of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control and economic and social development. Under the guidance of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities have taken a series of concrete measures to actively assist Taiwan-funded enterprises in resuming work and production in an orderly manner while doing a good job of epidemic prevention and control.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office has implemented 10 support measures from the local government to help Taiwan enterprises resume work and production, resolving difficulties in epidemic prevention supplies, supply chains and logistics, and labor, and increasing financial support. The Fujian Provincial Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office, together with relevant financial institutions, set up for the first time a special loan quota of 2 billion yuan for Fujian's key Taiwan enterprise emergency fund. Taiwan Affairs Offices in many places, including Shanghai, Zhejiang, Anhui, Shandong, Guangdong, Chongqing, Sichuan, Tianjin, Liaoning, Jiangxi, and Shenzhen, have actively carried out various types of assistance work, coordinating the resolution of practical difficulties faced by Taiwan enterprises in resuming work and production, and ensuring that Taiwan enterprises equally enjoy the various relief policies and measures introduced by the central and local governments in response to the epidemic. According to incomplete statistics, as of March 10, the work-resumption rate of Taiwan-funded industrial enterprises above designated size in mainland Taiwan-funded concentration areas exceeded 90%, and Taiwan-funded industrial enterprises above designated size in places such as Fujian had all resumed work and production.\nZhu Fenglian said that recently, a batch of major Taiwan-funded projects has successively settled in Fujian, Jiangsu, and other places through remote video signing and other methods, with a total amount exceeding 15 billion yuan, showing that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises continue to be optimistic about the prospects for development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200313_12255599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-03-18","Geng Shuang","","With regard to China's countermeasures, does that affect the journalists working in Taiwan?","The details are all there in our statement. You may read it more carefully.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1757799.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1757637.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-03-19","Geng Shuang","","According to media reports, the Haitian government ordered Taiwan's representative Liu Bangzhi to leave the country within 72 hours after he got into a fierce argument with President Jovenel Moise. What's your comment?","We noted media reports on that. The overwhelming majority of countries in the world recognize the one-China principle, which is a basic norm governing international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. In recent years, some of the Latin American and Caribbean countries, for instance Panama, the Dominican Republic and El Salvador, followed the historical trend and established diplomatic relations with China based on the one-China principle. China's cooperation with these countries, featuring mutual benefit and mutual respect, has yielded fruitful results and brought tangible benefits to their people. This stands in sharp contrast to the situation of Haiti and other \"allies\" of Taiwan, who know better than anyone how things stand.\nI want to stress once again that there is no way out for the Taiwan authorities to pursue \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\". I believe relevant countries can be soberly aware that only an early recognition of the one-China principle is the right choice that meets the fundamental and long-term interests of their own people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1758235.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1758148.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-03-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 19 (electronic dispatch) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, in an interview with reporters on the 19th, said that because of reasons on the Taiwan side, the rights and interests of mainland students registered at universities in Taiwan have been harmed, and the Taiwan authorities and relevant universities in Taiwan should take responsibility in earnest and properly resolve the relevant problems.\nIt is understood that at present more than 8,300 mainland students are registered at universities in Taiwan for degree programs. After the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic, the DPP authorities' measures restricting mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan have continuously escalated, and the relevant schools have also failed to make proper arrangements for mainland students to return to campus. Starting February 6, the DPP authorities fully suspended mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, so mainland students were unable to return to Taiwan's universities before the start of the semester. At the same time, Taiwan's universities gradually began their normal semesters from late February to early March, yet still required mainland students to pay tuition and register on time. Some universities did not take seriously the problems caused by mainland students being unable to return and the resulting academic arrangements, and did not adopt necessary and effective measures to resolve them; some schools even asked mainland students to defer their enrollment by one semester after collecting their tuition fees.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the relevant departments on the mainland attach great importance to the obstacles mainland students face in returning to study and the related problems arising from them. More than 8,300 mainland students have student status at Taiwan's universities; most must stay in Taiwan for four to seven years, and a small number face completing their studies in Taiwan this year. They have a legitimate right to return to school as scheduled. When Taiwan's universities on the island can still open normally, it is obviously unreasonable for the Taiwan side to prevent these mainland students from returning to school, which seriously harms the legitimate rights and interests of more than 8,300 mainland students studying in Taiwan. Relevant universities in Taiwan have not fought for the mainland students' due right to return to school, and some universities have been negligent in resolving the problems that mainland students face because their return is blocked, causing mainland students' studies to be delayed and even affecting their normal graduation and employment, seriously harming mainland students' rights and interests. Recently, the broad mass of mainland students have strongly demanded that relevant parties in Taiwan face up to their legitimate rights and demands, correct unreasonable practices and remedy the missing arrangements. Their demands are reasonable and legitimate, and their rights and interests should be protected.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that the DPP authorities and the relevant universities on the island should safeguard the right of mainland students to return to school and study, and should not one-sidedly emphasize epidemic prevention at the expense of mainland students' right to return to school. They must change unreasonable restrictions targeting mainland students, provide necessary guarantees for mainland students' return, and reasonably arrange necessary epidemic prevention measures for mainland students' return. Where mainland students are forced to be unable to return or to defer their return, the relevant universities in Taiwan should take the students' demands seriously, make thoughtful arrangements, adopt due remedial measures, and reasonably address the concerns of mainland students, so that their studies are not affected and they do not suffer economic losses.\nIt is understood that, affected by the epidemic, Taiwan students who are registered at universities on the mainland for degree programs have not yet returned to campus. The mainland's education authorities will, in accordance with the unified deployment of epidemic prevention and control work, decide in a timely manner the opening dates of universities in various regions, and the relevant universities have made arrangements for pre-enrollment epidemic prevention, academic arrangements and related matters. Taiwan students, like mainland students, will carry out all teaching requirements and epidemic prevention measures according to the unified arrangements of their schools.\nZhu Fenglian said that although the epidemic has had some impact on mainland economic and social life, the mainland side, as always, attaches importance to caring for Taiwan students, and relevant departments and localities will continue to do related work so that Taiwan students can study and plan their future on the mainland with greater peace of mind and assurance after the epidemic ends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200319_12257576.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-03-24","Geng Shuang","Reuters","The Taiwan authorities said they asked the WHO for more information on the coronavirus including the risk of human-to-human transmission in late December, but they got no answer. Is this because China pressured the WHO not to deal with Taiwan?","If I remember it right, the Spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has made a response to similar questions.\nTo be brief, the attempt for political play-up or manipulation under the pretext of this pandemic will not succeed. We believe that the WHO will properly resolve the relevant matter, as it always does, in accordance with the one-China principle and Resolution 2758 of the UN General Assembly.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1760477.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202003/t20200324_5418755.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-03-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 24 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 24th, in response to questions, that Su Tseng-chang once again shamelessly spread the “Su-style lies,” openly fabricating rumors that the mainland was “concealing the epidemic.” This performance of using lies to incite discrimination and hatred once again exposes his vicious nature to the world.\nZhu Fenglian said that over the past two-plus months, mainland people have united and fought hard against the epidemic, and the achievements are universally recognized; they have bought precious time for epidemic prevention around the world. At the same time, we have always adhered to a highly responsible attitude toward the health and well-being of the people of Taiwan, and from the very beginning we have notified relevant parties in Taiwan of epidemic information, including specifically notifying them of the mainland's sharing of novel coronavirus gene sequences with the WHO and of ways to obtain the relevant gene sequences. As of March 24, such notifications had been issued 101 times. The DPP authorities have never dared to tell these truths to the people of Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the “Su-style lies” have repeatedly been slapped in the face by facts. The epidemic situation in Taiwan is intensifying. We advise the DPP authorities, Su Tseng-chang, and others like him to immediately stop spreading political viruses. Using the epidemic to continually “stoke fires” and escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and worsening the atmosphere of cross-Strait relations, is both shameless and disgusting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200324_12259157.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-03-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 24 — Responding to the so-called “Taiwan-US Epidemic Prevention Partnership Joint Statement” recently issued by Taiwan’s foreign affairs department and the “American Institute in Taiwan,” which the DPP authorities and some media on the island have hyped, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 24th in response to a question: The so-called “joint statement” issued by Taiwan and the US once again exposes the despicable conduct and political scheme of the DPP authorities to “use the epidemic to seek independence” by exploiting the COVID-19 pandemic. It holds the health and well-being of Taiwan’s people hostage and forces them onto a mistaken path of “relying on foreign powers to bolster oneself” and confrontation with the mainland.\nZhu Fenglian said that we support the international community’s joint efforts to strengthen cooperation in defeating the epidemic, but we firmly oppose using this as a pretext to pursue “Taiwan independence” or play the “Taiwan card” through unnecessary tricks. Relations between Taiwan and the United States must be handled under the one-China principle. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between Taiwan and the US.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200324_12259176.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-03-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media reports, on the evening of March 16, a PLA KJ-500 early warning aircraft and J-11fighter jets approached the \"middle line of the Taiwan Strait\" for night flight training in the southwestern sea of Taiwan, and Taiwan fighter planes took off to respond. Some media said that the PLA's move was very rare, showing that its capabilities to counter “Taiwan independence” were not affected by the…","Taiwan is an integral part of China. The combat-readiness patrol and joint exercises conducted by the PLA are aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and protecting the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. These operations are targeted specifically at “Taiwan independence” forces and their secessionist activities.\nIt should be pointed out that, recently, the US has continued to take negative actions on Taiwan, including allowing Tainan City Mayor Lai Ching-te a visit to the US, the passing of the so-called “Taiwan Allies International Protection and Enhancement Initiative (TAIPEI) Act” by the US Congress, and repeated dispatching of warships across the Taiwan Strait. Relevant US practices have seriously interfered in China's internal affairs, seriously undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits, severely poisoned China-US military relations, and sent wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces. These actions are extremely dangerous. China has expressed its strong dissatisfaction and resolute opposition.\nThe PLA has the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capabilities to thwart all secessionist activities and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-03/27/content_4862776.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-03-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports on March 15 from the Central News Agency (CNA) of Taiwan, the Institute for National Defense and Security Research (INDSR) in Taiwan recently released a report, stating that Wuhan is an important location for the military industry on the Chinese mainland, a place with strategic importance in weapon development and also a pilot demonstration zone for civil-militaryintegration strategy. The…","What I can tell you is that the PLA's determination, will, and ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not be shaken by any force or disturbed in any way.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-03/27/content_4862776.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-03-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, March 26 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, in an interview on the 26th, said that the so-called statement issued by Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council on March 24 seriously violates the facts, completely turns black into white and confuses the public.\nZhu Fenglian said that over the past two-plus months, we have adhered to an open, transparent and responsible attitude, promptly notified the World Health Organization and relevant countries and regions of epidemic information, and adopted the most comprehensive, strictest and most thorough prevention and control measures. This has bought valuable time for the international community’s fight against the epidemic, and the international community has already reached consensus on this. As of March 25, 90 press conferences of the State Council Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism had been held to brief domestic and foreign audiences on the epidemic; more than 20 international expert video conferences had been held to share treatment plans and epidemic prevention experience with the whole world; in addition, assistance was provided to the international community’s fight against the epidemic through dispatching medical expert teams and providing materials and technical assistance, which has been fully recognized by the WHO and the international community. May I ask the DPP authorities: during the epidemic prevention process, did you receive epidemic-related information from the mainland and the WHO? Did you benefit from the experience provided by the mainland?\nZhu Fenglian said that from the very beginning, the mainland, in a spirit of attaching great importance to the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, has maintained communication with relevant parties in Taiwan. On January 3, we activated the cross-Strait emergency public health event notification mechanism and promptly notified Taiwan’s disease control authorities of epidemic information on the mainland. On January 12, we specially notified relevant parties in Taiwan of information about the mainland’s sharing of the novel coronavirus gene sequence with the WHO and the ways to obtain the relevant gene sequence. From January 12 to 14, we specially arranged for Taiwan experts to visit Wuhan on site to learn about the diagnosis, treatment and handling of confirmed novel coronavirus pneumonia patients. On January 16, the Taiwan health experts who took part in the visit stated clearly at a press conference held on the island that during this trip they were informed by the mainland of two family cluster infection incidents and of the information that close contacts needed to be quarantined. From February 5 to March 8, we successively shared 26 key technical documents with Taiwan, including the “Diagnosis and Treatment Protocol for Novel Coronavirus Pneumonia,” the “Prevention and Control Protocol for Novel Coronavirus Pneumonia,” and the “Nursing Standards for Severe and Critical Novel Coronavirus Pneumonia Patients.” As of March 24, the mainland had notified Taiwan of epidemic information 101 times in total. The facts that the mainland promptly notified, issued warnings and provided prevention experience are crystal clear. May I ask the DPP authorities: why do you not tell the Taiwan public these facts?\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the epidemic situation in Taiwan is still developing, and voices on the island keep questioning that the DPP authorities’ “political double standards” have created a breach in the island’s epidemic prevention. Some DPP politicians keep spreading rumors and smearing and attacking the mainland in an attempt to shift responsibility. This is an extremely immoral and dishonorable act. We must ask the DPP authorities: you have consistently refused to disclose the movement trajectories of confirmed cases and the names of hospitals where infections occurred — is this not transparency? You have continuously punished ordinary people for releasing true epidemic information — is this not repression? You still use travel-restriction measures to stop Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei from returning home — is this not discrimination? You have disregarded the WHO’s rules and maliciously fabricated and used stigmatizing names for the epidemic — is this not incitement of hatred? The DPP authorities must examine their own consciences!\nZhu Fenglian stressed that shifting focus and shirking responsibility does not help epidemic prevention and control on the island, and that fabrication, slander and political manipulation will only create hatred and ultimately harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots. The conduct of the DPP authorities is neither kind nor generous, and they indeed should examine their own consciences carefully.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200326_12259911.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-03-27","Geng Shuang","SCMP","First, the US President signed the Taiwan Allies International Protection and Enhancement Initiative (TAIPEI) Act. Do you have any comment? Second, G20 pledged $5 trillion in global stimulus funding, how will that be shared by its member states? What is the share for China? How does China hope to see this funding be spent?","Regarding your first question, the so-called TAIPEI Act seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques. It goes against international law and basic norms governing international relations and constitutes interference in China's domestic affairs. China deplores and rejects it.\nAltogether 180 countries have established diplomatic relations with China. The US itself established diplomatic ties with China on the basis of the one-China principle 41 years ago. The above-mentioned Act, however, calls for blocking other sovereign states from developing normal state-to-state relations with China, which is the logic of flagrant hegemonism.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity as well as China's core interests. The determination and resolution of the Chinese government and people to safeguard their core interests are firm as rock.\nWe strongly urge the US to correct its mistake, refrain from implementing this act and obstructing other countries' pursuit of relations with China. Otherwise, it will be met with resolute countermeasures from the Chinese side.\nOn your second question, last night, the G20 leaders held a successful Extraordinary G20 Leaders' Summit on COVID-19. A statement was issued after the meeting, saying that the G20 is injecting more than $5 trillion into the global economy as part of targeted fiscal policies, economic measures and guarantee programs to offset the social, economic and financial impact of the pandemic. They have drawn much attention and been commended by the international community.\nSince the outbreak of COVID-19, the Chinese government has made all-out efforts to combat the epidemic, and introduced a series of fiscal and financial policies to stabilize the economy and employment and ensure people's livelihood. On the fiscal front, Chinese finance authorities at all levels have allocated more than RMB 121 billion for epidemic prevention and control, and will cut taxes and fees by an extra more than RMB 1 trillion this year, or about $159.3 billion in total. In the financial sector, we have injected more than RMB 1.3 trillion, or about $184.8 billion worth of liquidity and relending and rediscount into the market. What the fiscal and monetary policy involves is worth about $344.1 billion in total. These measures are yielding positive results, providing strong support for epidemic response and the recovery of the economy, and playing an important role in ensuring the smooth socio-economic operation.\nOne last point I would like to stress is that the $5 trillion mentioned in the statement is a sum of the policy measures taken and to be taken by G20 countries. The measures taken and to be taken by the Chinese side, as I talked about earlier, are also an important part of the global efforts to tackle the pandemic and stabilize the economy. The figure concerning the Chinese side is the sum of what has been and will be put in place altogether.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1762834.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202003/t20200327_5418770.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-03-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 28 -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the US signing into law the so-called \"Taipei Act of 2019,\" said that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other departments have clearly stated China's firm opposition to the US signing the \"Taipei Act of 2019,\" and have lodged solemn representations with the US.\nZhu Fenglian said there is only one China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. 180 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China, and the US established diplomatic relations with China more than 40 years ago on the basis of the one-China principle. Now the US has signed a bill obstructing other sovereign states from developing normal state relations with China. This is utterly unreasonable and self-contradictory, and it violates international law and the basic norms of international relations.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that China's national unification and national rejuvenation are the trend of history, and no force can stop them. \"Taiwan independence\" is a countercurrent of history and a dead end, and it will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200328_12260348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-03-30","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Taiwan's Joseph Wu commented that he would invite reporters from New York Times, Washington Post and Wall Street Journal to be stationed in Taiwan, a free and democratic \"country\". Will China help facilitate such a move?","You should know that Taiwan is not a country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1763695.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202003/t20200330_5418774.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 30 (dateline). Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 30th, saying that we deeply mourn the untimely passing of Mr. Hao Baicun and Mr. Wang Wenxie, and extend sincere condolences to their families. Mr. Hao Baicun and Mr. Wang Wenxie had deep feelings for the nation, firmly opposed “Taiwan independence,” devoted themselves to national reunification, made great contributions to the development of cross-Strait relations, and earned wide praise and respect from compatriots on both sides.\nZhu Fenglian said that although they have passed away, their nobility lives on. We hope that compatriots on both sides will work hand in hand, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and work toward realizing national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200330_12260973.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 31 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on March 31, said that in order to implement the spirit of central government policy toward Taiwan and help outstanding Taiwan students and athletes realize their wish to study at mainland universities, the Ministry of Education, the General Administration of Sport and the China Association for Science and Technology recently jointly issued the “Notice on Doing Well in the Recommended Admission of Outstanding Overseas Chinese and Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Students (Athletes) to Ordinary Universities.”\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that under the notice, Taiwan students who participate in and win an award in any one of five competitions, including the International Mathematical Olympiad, International Physics Olympiad, International Chemistry Olympiad, International Biology Olympiad and International Informatics Olympiad, or Taiwan athletes who place in the top three at the National Games, the Asian Games (Summer), the Asian Winter Games, the Summer Olympic Games or the Winter Olympic Games, may apply to mainland universities and, after assessment by the universities, be granted recommended admission to undergraduate programs.\nZhu Fenglian said that Taiwan students and athletes who wish to learn more about the eligibility requirements, eligibility review, recommendation procedures and other details can check the admissions websites of the relevant universities. We sincerely welcome Taiwan students and athletes who meet the requirements and are willing to come to the mainland to study and pursue further education.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202003/t20200331_12261391.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-01","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Taiwan donated 10 million masks to the US and other countries. What's your comment? Second question, some Chinese supermarkets, gyms, bars, hotels and SPA houses refuse to serve foreigners citing the pandemic as the reason. Some say this is retaliation to Chinese nationals being demonized overseas. What's your comment?","On your first question about Taiwan's donation of masks, if my memory serves me right, when the epidemic first broke out in China's mainland, Taiwan authorities banned the export of masks. Now as we can see, the situation in the US is very severe, Chinese provinces, cities and businesses have been providing assistance to the American people. If the Taiwan region can and wants to help, I believe we are all glad to see it. But if anyone in Taiwan seeks to politicize the pandemic, I would advise them to think twice and act prudently.\nOn your second question, I haven't heard of anything like that. As you know, when COVID-19 first hit China, a handful of Western politicians demonized and stigmatized China in their words, leading to injustice and discrimination against Chinese and Asians overseas. We the Chinese believe in not doing to others what you don't want others to do to you. That's why we stand firmly against and don't allow discriminatory behavior targeting foreigners.\nYou mentioned some facilities like gyms and SPA parlors refuse to serve foreigners. I don't think such facilities are open at this special time amid the pandemic. The Chinese people welcome foreign friends with kindness, warmth and generosity. But at this extraordinary time, there are regulations at government and community levels to ensure public health security. We hope foreign nationals living in China could understand, support and cooperate with relevant regulations. This is both for their own health and safety and public health security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1764777.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202004/t20200401_5418785.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-04-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 1: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on April 1 in response to a question: Regarding Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly, some Taiwanese media have spread false reports based on rumor. The spokesperson of our embassy in Japan has issued a statement sternly refuting the false information. What I want to reiterate is that Taiwan-related issues at the WHO must be handled under the one-China principle; there is no other way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200401_12261649.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-04-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 1 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding on the 1st, said: Recently, Su Tseng-chang has repeatedly raised the “Taiwan independence” pitch, and his “Taiwan independence” nature has been fully exposed. If Su Tseng-chang insists on going his own way, continuing to provoke and create cross-Strait confrontation and seriously undermining cross-Strait relations, he will ultimately only push the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots into a dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200401_12261715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-03","Hua Chunying","Shenzhen TV","Taiwan decides to donate 2 million masks to the US. In response, a spokesperson for the State Department said that \"Taiwan is not just a democratic success story, but a true friend in times of need, for which the American people are deeply grateful.\" What is your comment?","I have noted the heated exchanges between the US and Taiwan in recent days. It seems that the US has really let its standard fall, as 2 million masks are enough to make Taiwan a model of democracy and a \"true friend\". I have noticed that Jack Ma Foundation and Alibaba Foundation donated 1 million masks and 500,000 testing kits to the US. And Huawei, a Chinese company targeted by unwarranted US suppression, is making generous donations to the American people. It appears on a list of appreciated donors released by New York Governor Andrew Cuomo. Some provinces, cities and enterprises in China have also extended a helping hand to the American people, and the US has purchased a fairly large amount of medical supplies from China. How will the US comment on this?\nIt goes without saying that we should all help each other out during his extraordinary period with the spreading pandemic. However, if someone attempts to take advantage of and politicize the situation to undermine China's core interests, they'd better think twice.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1765751.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1765719.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-04-03","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Are China and the US having talks about allowing Taiwan greater access to WHO and on if China will permit Taiwan to attend the World Health Assembly as an observer this year?","The US government and the Taiwan region are fully aware that WHO members must be sovereign countries. According to arrangement between China and WHO, medical and health experts in the Taiwan region can, on the precondition of the one-China principle, participate in WHO's technical activities in their own capacity. With International Health Regulations (IHR) focal point in the Taiwan region, it has no problem at all in accessing WHO information on global public health emergencies, including notifications and cooperation on epidemics. I hope certain people will refrain from politicizing the pandemic.\nThe following questions were posed after the regular press conference:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1765751.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1765719.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-04-03","Hua Chunying","","据报道，针对台湾将向美捐赠200万只口罩，美国务院发言人称，台湾不仅是民主的典范，也是美国共患难的真朋友，美国人民对此深表感谢。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1765751.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1765719.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2020-04-03","Hua Chunying","","中美双方是否讨论过允许台湾更大程度地参与世卫组织活动，并允许其以观察员身份参加今年的世卫大会？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1765751.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1765719.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2020-04-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 3. In response to the so-called “Epidemic Prevention Cooperation Joint Statement” recently issued by the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the Czech Republic” and the Czech Economic and Cultural Office, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd in response to questions: The DPP authorities are playing these small tricks not for the health and well-being of Taiwan residents, but to “use the epidemic to seek independence” (以疫谋独). Their scheme will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200403_12262527.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-09","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The head of the WHO has accused Taiwan of making racist attacks against him. Do you agree with this accusation?","China opposes any attempt to use the epidemic for purpose of politicization or stigmatization, and strongly condemns the personal attacks and racist words and deeds against WHO DG Tedros.\nUnder the leadership of DG Tedros, the WHO has played an important role in assisting countries' responses to the epidemic and promoting international anti-epidemic cooperation by actively fulfilling its responsibilities and upholding an objective, science-based and unbiased stance, which has been widely recognized and highly praised by the international community. China supports the WHO in continuing to play a leading role in global anti-epidemic cooperation.\nSince the outbreak of COVID-19, the DPP authorities in Taiwan have been doing all they can to make reckless political maneuvers and hype up Taiwan's participation in the WHO and the World Health Assembly. Their real intention is to seek independence under the pretext of the pandemic. We are firmly opposed to that. Their scheme will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1767935.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1767872.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-04-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 9 dispatch: TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 9th, said that regarding Taiwan-related issues at the WHO, we have repeatedly stated our position. The DPP authorities, using any means to “seek independence through the epidemic,” have viciously attacked the WHO and its head, and tolerated green-camp online troops in spreading racially discriminatory remarks at will. We strongly condemn this.\nZhu Fenglian said we urge the DPP authorities to immediately stop political manipulation. Their attempt to use the epidemic to undermine the one-China principle and to seek WHO membership will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200409_12264050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-10","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","The US State Department spokesperson said on April 9 that the US is \"deeply disturbed that Taiwan's information was withheld from the global health community, as reflected in the WHO's January 14 statement that there was no indication of human-to-human transmission.\" She also claimed that \"the WHO once again chose politics over public health,\" and the WHO's actions \"cost time and lives.\" What is your comment?","I responded to a similar question yesterday. Since the US has refused to let go of this issue and kept trying to confuse public opinion on it, I would like to make a few more comments.\nFirst, the novel coronavirus is a novel virus, which means it takes time for us to research it, know it and draw conclusions accordingly. This is a science-based process. On January 20, a high-level expert group of the National Health Commission of China announced the confirmation of human-to-human transmission. The WHO sent a team on a field trip to Wuhan from January 20 to 21. Dr. Gauden Galea, WHO Representative in China, said on January 21 that the latest information showed that the virus has been passed to some extent from person to person. We can see that at the earliest time possible, the WHO released authoritative information based on China's confirmation of \"human-to-human transmission\" and its field visits. In fact, no responsible countries or organizations will jump to conclusions without sufficient and valid evidence.\nSecond, the US claims that the international community failed to get information from the Taiwan region. This is not true. As people in the Taiwan region share a bond of kinship with us, no one cares more about their health and well-being than the Chinese central government. After the epidemic broke out, the National Health Commission of China promptly informed the Taiwan region of the situation. In mid-January, at the request of the relevant departments in the Taiwan region, experts from the Taiwan region paid a field visit to Wuhan and had discussions with mainland experts. Taiwan medical experts expressed sincere thanks to the mainland for the reception.\nWHO is a specialized UN agency composed of sovereign states. Taiwan's participation in the activities of WHO and other international organizations needs to be arranged in a reasonable and appropriate manner after cross-straits consultations under the one-China principle. According to the agreement reached between China and the WHO, there is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region, so it can obtain timely information on global public health emergencies released by the WHO, and report its public health emergency information to the WHO in a timely manner as well. Health experts from the Taiwan region can attend WHO technical meetings, and WHO experts can visit the Taiwan region if necessary for field trips or to provide assistance. These arrangements ensure that the Taiwan region can respond to public health emergencies in a timely and effective manner wherever these emergencies occur.\nThird, since the outbreak of COVID-19, the WHO has been holding an objective, scientific and impartial position, performing its duties, and making enormous efforts to assist countries in response to the pandemic and to promote international cooperation, which has been widely recognized and highly praised by the international community. The US State Department Spokesperson made fact-distorting comments to shift the blame, which won't be helpful to ease the current situation in the US or to facilitate international anti-epidemic cooperation. Her words will only damage the credibility, image and interests of the US. We urge the US side to respect the facts and international public opinion, and focus on containing the epidemics at home. China will, as always, firmly support the WHO in fulfilling its duties and leading global anti-epidemic cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1768338.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1768268.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","BEIJING, April 10 (Xinhua) -- Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 10th in response to questions that since the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, the mainland, in a spirit of being highly responsible for the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, has promptly shared epidemic information and prevention and control experience with relevant parties in Taiwan, carefully looked after the living and epidemic prevention needs of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, devoted itself to the service of Taiwan compatriots who are stranded, made every effort to treat Taiwan compatriots who fell ill, worked hard to help Taiwan compatriots who needed to return to Taiwan do so safely and smoothly as early as possible, actively assisted Taiwan-invested enterprises in enjoying policy support from various localities, and orderly resumed work and production. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises have shown the great national righteousness of sharing the same boat in adversity, enthusiastically donated funds and materials for epidemic prevention and control, and actively participated in treatment, aid, and volunteer services on the mainland, conveying the love of compatriots in various ways. These are all concrete manifestations of \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" and they demonstrate the positive energy of the community of shared destiny across the Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said that at present, the staged results of epidemic prevention and control on the mainland have been further consolidated, and the order of economic and social operations is recovering quickly, which compatriots on both sides of the Strait can feel. However, the DPP authorities keep attacking and smearing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland and attacking and smearing the mainland. They let no topic pass, constantly fabricating lies in an attempt to create conflict and opposition between compatriots. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait may recall: to date, what good words have they said about Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan-invested enterprises, mainland students in Taiwan, and spouses from the mainland, and what good deeds have they done? When it comes to the mainland and cross-Strait relations, what comes out of their mouths is nothing but abuse, and what they raise is nothing but provocation. At present, there are many pressing problems on Taiwan in responding to the epidemic, responding to the reasonable demands of the public, and solving the practical difficulties of the public, such as how to meet the demand for face masks on Taiwan, how to allow Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei to reunite with their families as soon as possible, how to effectively control the spread of the epidemic, and how to solve the livelihood difficulties faced by the public... Solving these problems, which concern the interests and well-being of the people of Taiwan, is where the DPP authorities should direct their energy. Fabricating lies and inciting hatred cannot solve these problems, nor can it divert the public's attention.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities should focus their minds on the interests of the public, let people on Taiwan live in peace, let Taiwan residents who wish to return home do so smoothly, and let the broad Taiwan compatriots no longer suffer from the epidemic or be troubled by livelihood problems. Their political tricks of fabricating lies and smearing others should come to an end!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200410_12264245.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-15","Zhao Lijian","AFP","According to the Chinese embassy in France, Taiwan authorities used the word \"nigger\" to attack WHO Director-General Tedros. This is a serious allegation. Could you tell us on which occasion the Taiwan authorities used this term?","Why not go and ask the Taiwan authorities? The word is a racist slur. No country will tolerate such an expression.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1770103.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1770018.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-04-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 17 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, told reporters on the 17th in response to questions that the DPP authorities claim Taiwan's epidemic prevention department sent a letter to the WHO on December 31 last year to “sound the alarm” that the COVID-19 virus was “human-to-human” transmissible, and that the WHO did not make this information public to the world. These claims are completely inconsistent with the facts.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that since the COVID-19 outbreak, we have promptly notified the WHO and relevant countries and regions of epidemic information. On December 31 last year, the Wuhan Municipal Health Commission first published the “Briefing on the Current Pneumonia Epidemic in Our City” on its official website, reporting 27 cases and clearly stating that isolation and treatment measures had been taken. This both made epidemic information public to society at large and to the international community, reflecting our consistent attitude of openness, transparency and responsibility in handling the epidemic. The WHO also learned of the relevant situation that same day. It can be said that the information released by the Wuhan Health Commission played a key role in the WHO's immediate decision to form incident management support teams at three levels of the organization starting January 1 and to enter an emergency state for epidemic response.\nZhu Fenglian said that the December 31 email the Taiwan side refers to merely quoted the content published by the Wuhan Health Commission, with no other information; in other words, the information published by the Wuhan Health Commission was the sole source of the content of the Taiwan side's email. On December 31 last year, Taiwan's health authority also sent a letter to the National Health Commission to inquire about the information published by the Wuhan Health Commission, and the National Health Commission replied in writing through the liaison channel under the cross-Strait medical and health cooperation agreement, asking them to refer to the situation briefing published by the Wuhan Health Commission. The facts are clear: the mainland side published the information first, and Taiwan's health authority then relayed it; there was no so-called case of the Taiwan side reporting to the WHO first. The Taiwan side's email also did not mention “human-to-human” transmission; its main purpose was to inquire with the WHO about the situation. Taiwan's health authority issued press releases on January 4 and 6 stating “there is no obvious human-to-human transmission or infection of medical personnel.” Yet after March 15, the Taiwan side repackaged the relayed December 31 email as the first “alarm” message. Viewed from the perspective of “sounding the alarm,” this email merely proves that the Wuhan Health Commission released information to the public and the international community at the earliest moment. It is evident that the DPP authorities' hype is a false proposition, aimed at making political hay. Some foreign politicians have jumped on the bandwagon, spreading and repeating falsehoods to attack the mainland and the WHO, which is entirely malicious.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Taiwan side claims it cannot communicate with the WHO, but this email proves that claim is untrue. Taiwan's health institutions can obtain information published by the WHO in a timely manner and directly update information to the WHO through the liaison channels under the framework of the WHO's International Health Regulations. Taiwan's medical and health experts have always participated in WHO meetings in appropriate capacities. From early 2019 to March 2020, 24 Taiwan experts participated in WHO-organized technical meetings in 16 batches. The mainland side arranged for Taiwan experts to conduct on-site inspections in Wuhan from January 12 to 14 to learn about the diagnosis and treatment of confirmed COVID-19 patients and epidemic response. As of April 13, the mainland side had notified the Taiwan side of epidemic information 127 times. The DPP authorities have repeatedly evaded these facts and remained silent, have never honestly explained the situation to the public on the island, have continuously hyped a so-called “epidemic prevention gap,” and are now massively hyping the “email alarm.” This shows that their intent is not public health epidemic prevention. In fact, none of this is hard to understand: by doing this, the DPP authorities are simply continuing to expose their political aim of “using the epidemic to seek independence.”\nZhu Fenglian stressed that the WHO is a specialized agency of the United Nations composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is part of China, and its participation in international activities such as the WHO must be handled under the one-China principle. The DPP authorities' hyping of the Taiwan issue at the WHO, attempting to “use the epidemic to seek independence,” will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200417_12266749.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-04-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Hong Kong police recently arrested Jimmy Lai, Lee Cheuk-yan, and others suspected of organizing and participating in unauthorized assemblies. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have taken the opportunity to make accusations and hype the matter. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 21 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 21st, stating that the Hong Kong police took lawful arrest actions against persons suspected of \"organizing and participating in unauthorized assemblies,\" which reflects the rule of law principle that laws must be observed and violations must be pursued. The Democratic Progressive Party and other \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces seized on this to make accusations and hype the matter, distorting right and wrong, once again exposing their \"Taiwan independence\" nature of meddling in Hong Kong affairs, seeking political gain, and attempting to split the country.\nZhu Fenglian said: We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs is unpopular, and \"Taiwan independence\" and any political scheme attempting to split the motherland will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200421_12268177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-23","Geng Shuang","Phoenix TV","US Secretary of State Pompeo said at a press availability that China is \"exploiting the world's focus on COVID-19 crisis by continuing its provocative behavior\", including eroding Hong Kong's autonomy, exerting military pressure on Taiwan and coercing its neighbors in the South China Sea. What's China's response?","I want to stress that China will always resolutely safeguard its sovereignty, security and development interests, no matter what, no matter when.\nMatters relating to Taiwan and Hong Kong are China's internal affairs which allow no interference from external forces. China' sovereignty over the islands and reefs in the South China Sea and their adjacent waters is based on sufficient historical and jurisprudential evidence. In the meantime, we are committed to resolving differences with parties directly concerned through dialogue and consultation.\nSome people in the US want to replace facts with rumors and lies and sow discords among neighbors. Such attempts will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1772783.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202004/t20200423_5418860.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-04-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 27 — In response to Taiwan media reports that the mainland's Seventh National Population Census would require mainland spouses to provide data on their families in Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said this infringes personal privacy rights. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded on the 27th that these claims completely distort the facts, have ulterior motives, and attempt to undermine cross-Strait relations.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that, according to relevant laws and regulations, the State Council decided to conduct the Seventh National Population Census in 2020, with the standard reference time being 0:00 on November 1, 2020. Taiwan residents living on the mainland fall within the scope of the census; Taiwan residents not living on the mainland do not fall within its scope.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200427_12270323.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-04-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 28 — Regarding certain “Taiwan independence” organizations on the island pushing a so-called “constitution-making referendum,” which has completed the first stage of signature collection, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded on the 28th, pointing out: What the “Taiwan independence” organizations aim to achieve with a so-called “constitution-making referendum” is something everyone knows well. “Taiwan independence” is a counter-current of history and a dead end.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that “Taiwan independence” separatist activities severely damage the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, seriously threaten peace in the Taiwan Strait, and will only push Taiwan toward an extremely dangerous abyss and bring profound disaster to broad Taiwan compatriots. We have the firm will, full confidence, and ample capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. We will never allow anyone, any organization, or any party, at any time, in any form, to split any piece of Chinese territory away from China!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200428_12270456.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-04-30","Geng Shuang","De Telegraaf","This week the Netherlands trade and investment office in Taipei changed its name into the Netherlands office in Taipei. What's your comment on this issue?","I understand that the Chinese embassy in the Netherlands has responded to that. You may read their statement.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. China firmly opposes any official ties between the Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic ties with China, not to mention the establishment of any official agencies in Taiwan. Our position has been clear and consistent. We urge the Netherlands to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, properly handle issues related to Taiwan, correct its wrongdoing and uphold bilateral relations through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1775332.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202004/t20200430_5418885.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-04-30","Geng Shuang","","本周，“荷兰在台贸易暨投资办事处”更名为“荷兰在台办事处”。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1775332.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202004/t20200430_5418885.shtml",0,3,0,""],[1,"2020-04-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan \"defense officials\" recently claimed that the PLA has threatened the island by offensive words and show of force. They said that Taiwan is well prepared for any potential war between the two sides across the Strait. What is your comment?","Taiwan is an integral part of China. The PLA organized related military operations to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and protect the well-being of compatriots in Taiwan from \"Taiwan independence\" attempts. They are not targeted at the compatriots in Taiwan, but at a small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their activities. I should emphasize that any attempt to resist reunification with force is doomed to failure and will damage the interests of the Chinese nation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-05/04/content_4864649.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to reports, the DPP authorities have penalized 37 Taiwan compatriots who took up posts on the mainland on the grounds of violating the Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area, and another 88 people are under investigation. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 30 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 30th, saying that the DPP authorities repeatedly use so-called “illegal” accusations to threaten and intimidate, continuously escalating a “green terror” and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges, which seriously harms the vital interests of the people of Taiwan. This vicious practice of intimidation and arbitrary punishment is unpopular, has been and will continue to be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said, “We have noted the relevant reports. Recently, the DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated charges to suppress and punish Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland, depriving young people in Taiwan of the opportunity to achieve greater and better development. We will, as always, warmly welcome and firmly support Taiwan youth in developing on the mainland, and help them find a stage on the mainland where they can make use of their expertise and realize their dreams.”\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the mainland authorities have required Hong Kong and Taiwan entertainers to “declare their patriotism” and guarantee “political correctness” for ten years, failing which audio-visual platforms and film and television companies may not hire them. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed that political factors should not be introduced into literary, artistic and film and television creation. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment?\nZhu Fenglian said that these claims are pure fabrication. We have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait film and television exchanges and welcome Taiwan performers to develop on the mainland. We support more Taiwan performing artists in sharing opportunities in the development of the mainland’s cultural industry, realizing their dreams, and jointly promoting the prosperous development of cross-Strait cultural undertakings. At the same time, we do not allow a small number of people to earn money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and we do not want the healthy development of cross-Strait film and television exchanges to be polluted politically by “Taiwan independence” forces.\nShe said that the DPP authorities and a small group of “Taiwan independence” forces have continuously spread false information and fabricated lies in the field of cross-Strait film and television exchanges, with the aim of disrupting cross-Strait exchanges and deliberately creating contradictions and estrangement between compatriots.\nA reporter asked: Regarding the case of paint being thrown at Lin Rong-ji in Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council said that if mainland involvement is confirmed, it will be severely punished under the “Anti-Infiltration Act.” Some DPP elected representatives said it should be handled as a so-called “security” incident. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment?\nZhu Fenglian said that behind this farce, who is planning and manipulating it politically, everyone can now see very clearly. Forces of “Hong Kong independence” and “Taiwan independence” are colluding, with the aim of creating chaos in Hong Kong, causing trouble for the mainland, further worsening cross-Strait relations, and bringing turmoil to Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200430_12271305.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 30 — Regarding the DPP authorities' following Western politicians in unreasonably hyping the investigation into the origins of the COVID-19 virus, Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 30th: The foreign ministry spokesperson recently gave an exclusive media interview, refuting and countering with facts the absurdity of Western politicians manipulating this issue and expressing the position of the central government. The mainland's epidemic information and anti-epidemic measures have been open and transparent; we have promptly and comprehensively released the timeline of epidemic reports, and have repeatedly and publicly explained in detail the notifications of epidemic information to relevant parties in Taiwan, the prevention and control experience shared, and the invitations to Taiwan health experts for on-site inspections. Claiming that the mainland is concealing the epidemic is a complete reversal of black and white.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities have constantly fabricated all kinds of rumors to slander and attack the mainland, and now openly echo anti-China Western politicians, willingly serving as pawns, further exposing to the world their ugly essence of \"using the epidemic to pursue independence.\" Practicing \"anti-China and hatred of China\" will inevitably degenerate into \"anti-intellectualism,\" which can only add to the ridicule.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202004/t20200430_12271312.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-06","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","Will China support the EU's resolution at the World Health Assembly for an independent review into the lessons learned of the health response? And our second question is, Taiwan has said that the WHO would allow it to participate in the World Health Assembly this month. Will China allow this?","On the issue of a review, as I just said, since the outbreak of COVID-19, China has been working closely with WHO in an open, transparent and responsible manner and supporting the global response with concrete actions. We stand ready to continue joint efforts with the international community to ramp up cooperation in fighting the pandemic. We support summarizing and reviewing the epidemic response at an appropriate time to advance international health cooperation and improve the global public health security governance so that we can deal with similar challenges better in the future.\nWhat we oppose is the so-called investigation chanted by politicians in a few countries out of domestic political calculations based on the presumption of guilt. What we oppose is political maneuvers of the pandemic, which run counter to the original mission of scientific research and disrupt the concerted international response. China's position is clear-cut. We are completely above-board and have nothing to hide. We hope the international community will render active support to WHO's work.\nOn the Taiwan region's participation in WHO activities, China's position is clear and consistent. It must be handled according to the one-China principle. Under this precondition, China's Central Government has made proper arrangement for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs, which ensures that the region can deal with local or global public health emergencies in a timely and effective manner. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, the DPP authorities have been engaging in political manipulation and constant hype-up over the issue of Taiwan's participation in WHO and WHA. The real intention is very clear. They are taking advantage of the virus to seek independence. We firmly reject this futile attempt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1776657.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200506_5418890.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: the Taiwan authorities' foreign affairs department recently claimed that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 of 1971 only resolved the question of China's representation and has nothing to do with Taiwan, and that it did not confer on China the power to represent the people of Taiwan in international settings, and that the WHO should allow Taiwan to fully participate in the organization and the…","Beijing, May 7 (Xinhua) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on May 7, pointing out that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, causing the political basis for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly to no longer exist. The responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped the issue of participating in the WHA amid the COVID-19 epidemic. This is not a genuine concern for public health, but a political scheme. For some people in the United States to openly support Taiwan's accession to the World Health Organization is to politicize epidemic prevention issues and send a serious wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” forces. We firmly oppose it.\nMa Xiaoguang said that recently, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have concocted various pretexts and hyped the so-called issue of Taiwan's participation in the WHO, attempting to take advantage of the epidemic to make mischief and challenge the one-China principle internationally. We have repeatedly stated our solemn position on this.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, a fact that no person or force can change. In 1945, the Chinese people, together with the peoples of other countries around the world, achieved the great victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and Taiwan was subsequently restored and returned to the embrace of the motherland. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, have clearly and unmistakably confirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan. Since 1949, although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that in 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, recognizing the People's Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all the Chinese people. This thoroughly resolved the question of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally and procedurally, and fully reflects the one-China principle upheld by the United Nations. There is only one China, Taiwan is part of China, and the question of Taiwan joining the United Nations simply does not exist. Taiwan's participation in international organization activities, including WHO activities, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The United Nations has repeatedly reaffirmed that it will continue to handle the Taiwan question in accordance with General Assembly Resolution 2758. The WHO, as a specialized agency of the United Nations composed of sovereign states, abides by the resolutions of the General Assembly, and WHA Resolution 25.1 reaffirmed General Assembly Resolution 2758. These are iron-clad facts that admit of no doubt.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200507_12272629.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-08","Hua Chunying","China News Service","The spokesperson for Taiwan's so-called \"Foreign Ministry\" said that a resolution adopted by the UN in 1971 resolved only \"the problem of China's representation,\" but not \"the issue of Taiwan,\" and it did not give China the right to represent people in Taiwan on international occasions. The WHO should shake off the control of the Chinese government and let Taiwan participate fully in the global fight against the…","The Taiwan authorities are just playing the trick of replacing concept to realize his purpose of confounding the public.\nIn October 1971, the United Nations General Assembly adopted at its 26th session Resolution 2758, recognizing the People's Republic of China (PRC) as the sole legitimate government representing the whole of China. The resolution, fully demonstrating the one China principle that the UN is committed to, has solved once and for all the issue of China's representation in the UN politically, de jure and procedure-wise.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the PRC. This is the consensus of the international community. The UN has reiterated multiple times that it will stick to Resolution 2758 in dealing with the Taiwan issue. The WHO, as a special agency of the UN, should observe UNGA resolutions. Resolution 25.1 of the World Health Assembly reaffirmed the UNGA Resolution 2758 and clarified the issue of China's representation in the WHO.\nWhat was said by the spokesperson simply exposed the DPP's devious motive to use the current outbreak to seek \"Taiwan independence\". It is definitely not for the health and welfare of people in Taiwan that the Taiwan authority has been ostensibly trying to join the WHO and the WHA. They are doing this for sheer political gains. But they will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1777215.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200508_5418900.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, some people on the island said that for the sake of national rejuvenation, the mainland will not only refrain from reclaiming Taiwan but will also tolerate Taiwan's “independence” or “quasi-independence.” The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the mainland should abandon unilateral political preconditions, abandon intimidation and suppression, and work with Taiwan to jointly promote…","Beijing, May 8 (Xinhua) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on May 8, pointed out that on the road toward the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, we are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and to safeguard the prospects for peaceful reunification across the Strait. We have the firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and we will never allow anyone, any organization, any political party, at any time, in any form, to split off any part of Chinese territory from China.\nMa Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions. He said that the reunification of the motherland is an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. National reunification and national rejuvenation are also the trend of history, which no force can stop.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that we adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” adhere to the one-China principle, continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the unshakable political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. The peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is built on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus,” and all political parties, groups and individuals on the island who oppose “Taiwan independence” and support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations should cherish it all the more. We will continue to conduct dialogue and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and individuals on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200508_12272898.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-05-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to reports, a DPP legislator has proposed amending the “Act Governing Relations Between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” to delete the text relating to “national reunification,” reflecting the so-called “national jurisdiction extends only to Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, Matsu and their affiliated islands.” May I ask for your comment on this?\nMa Xiaoguang made the above remarks in…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 9 dispatch: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to a question on the 9th: We solemnly warn the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces not to underestimate the firm will and determination of the 1.4 billion Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200509_12273145.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-11","Zhao Lijian","China Review News Agency","New Zealand's Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Winston Peters said the other day that New Zealand would support Taiwan's request for an observer role at the World Health Assembly. Peters also said that previous discussions with senior Chinese officials gave him confidence there would be no pushback to New Zealand's decision. What is your response?","Such erroneous remarks on the New Zealand side severely violate the one-China principle. China deplores and opposes them and has lodged representations with the New Zealand side.\nOn the Taiwan region's participation in WHO activities, China's position is clear and consistent. The one-China principle must be observed. Based on this principle, the central government of China has made proper arrangements for Taiwan region's participation in global health events, which ensures that the Taiwan region can promptly and effectively respond to local and global public health incidents. The Taiwan authorities chose to play up its so-called participation in WHO events and return to the WHA at this moment. The timing reveals its true motive, which is to use the current outbreak to seek \"Taiwan independence\". It is out-and-out political manipulation.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-New Zealand relations. It is the fundamental underpinning of the progress achieved in bilateral relations since the establishment of diplomatic ties. China urges New Zealand to strictly abide by the one-China principle and immediately stop its wrong actions on Taiwan-related issues to avoid damaging bilateral relations.\nAs for Peters claiming that he has been assured by the Chinese leadership that there would be no pushback to New Zealand's decision, I wonder how he came to that assumption? I want to point out that China is committed to developing friendly cooperative relations with New Zealand based on mutual respect and equality. But we are firmly resolved to uphold our sovereignty, independence and territorial integrity. No one should entertain any illusion when it comes to matters concerning China's core interests. We hope that certain people in New Zealand will stop spreading rumors and creating trouble and work to enhance instead of undermining bilateral mutual trust and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1777953.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200511_5418905.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-11","Zhao Lijian","The Globe and Mail","In addition to New Zealand, several Western countries are also calling for Taiwan's inclusion as an observer at the World Health Assembly. What's your comment?","China's position on issues relating to the Taiwan region in WHO is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1777953.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200511_5418905.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-12","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Joseph Wu made mention of a 2005 memorandum of understanding signed between China and WHO over the Taiwan region's participation in the organization. Media reports said that the MOU set Taiwan down as part of China. We're wondering if you could give us any more details about the said MOU and whether this still applies to Taiwan currently?","I'd like to stress two points.\nFirst, there is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. There is no need for China to \"set Taiwan down as part of China\" by signing an MOU with any international organization.\nSecond, there is no secrecy at all with the MOU signed between the Chinese government and WHO in 2005. You can find it online. Based on its provisions, under the one-China principle, participation in WHO technical activities by technical experts in the Taiwan region is unimpeded. Since 2019, 16 groups of 24 medical and health experts from the region have taken part in WHO technical activities.\nThe Taiwan authorities are trying to hype up the MOU signed years ago in another show of political maneuvering under the pretext of the pandemic. This is nothing but a futile attempt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1778378.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200512_5418910.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-13","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Regarding the French government's plan to sell weapons to Taiwan, I understand the foreign ministry firmly opposes that and demands the French side withdraw its plan, but the French company just refuted China's criticism. I wonder what's your response to that?","Our position is consistent and clear: we firmly oppose other countries selling arms to the Taiwan region or conducting military exchange with it. We have expressed grave concerns to the French side.\nOnce again we urge the French side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and withdraw its arms sales plan to avoid more damage to China-France relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1778769.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200513_5418914.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-13","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","A US government commission has said that the WHO's exclusion of Taiwan has led to more lives being lost in the pandemic. Do you have any comment on this?","I believe you were referring to the US China Economic and Security Review Commission. Its reports are always distorting facts and full of bias.\nChina's position on the Taiwan region's participation in WHO activities is clear and consistent. It must be handled according to the one-China principle. Under this precondition, China's Central Government has made proper arrangement for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs, which ensures that the region can deal with local or global public health emergencies in a timely and effective manner. The Taiwan region is never excluded from the WHO global anti-epidemic system.\nSince the outbreak of COVID-19, the DPP authorities in Taiwan have been doing all they can to make reckless political maneuvers and hype up Taiwan's participation in WHO and the World Health Assembly. Their real intention is to solicit foreign support and seek independence under the pretext of the pandemic. We are firmly opposed to that. Their scheme will never succeed.\nChina urges relevant side in the US to abide by the one-China principle and stop backing the Taiwan authorities' political maneuvering to seek independence under the disguise of epidemic response, so as to avoid disrupting global solidarity and cooperation against the pandemic.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1778769.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200513_5418914.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 13 — In response to a recent incident in which an associate professor at Taichung Yuan University publicly made discriminatory remarks against mainland students and attacked the mainland in class, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan and its education authorities expressed support for him. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 13th: We have noted the relevant reports. A man surnamed Zhao (招某) publicly spread discriminatory and aggressive political remarks in class, seriously violating academic ethics and professional morality. The facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive. The Mainland Affairs Council and the education authorities ignored the facts and disregarded right and wrong, and openly defended him, further confirming that they are the “black umbrella” for the “anti-China, anti-Chinese” sentiment in Taiwan society.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that precisely such words and deeds, together with the DPP authorities’ partiality and tolerance, have worsened the educational exchanges across the Strait and the normal, healthy learning environment that mainland students should enjoy when studying in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200513_12274259.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-14","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","We understand countries including Swaziland and Nicaragua have put forward to WHO a proposal on inviting Taiwan to attend this year's WHA as an observer. A few countries are doing everything they can to push for discussions of this proposal at the WHA. I wonder if China has a comment?","The 73rd WHA will be held on May 18 to 19. Due to the COVID-19 pandemic, it will be virtual. According to WHO Executive Board consensus, this year's agenda will be significantly reduced to cover only essential items like the COVID-19 pandemic and Executive Board election. This reflects the shared sincere wish of member states to focus on international cooperation on COVID-19 at this WHA.\nChina opposes the so-called proposal by a few countries including Swaziland on inviting the Taiwan region to attend this WHA as an observer. The Taiwan region's participation in the WHA must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is also a fundamental principle enshrined in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. Based on this principle, the Central Government of China has made proper arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs, which ensures that the region can promptly and effectively respond to local and global public health incidents. Therefore the region is by no means a so-called \"gap\" in global anti-epidemic efforts. The WHA has for many consecutive years rejected a handful of countries' proposals relating to the Taiwan region, demonstrating the shared international commitment to the one-China principle.\nI would like to reiterate that the few countries who are insisting on discussing the proposal relating to the Taiwan region are only seeking to severely disrupt this WHA and undermine global anti-pandemic cooperation. The international community including China stands firmly against this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1779190.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200514_5418920.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-14","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","On May 13, a US State Department spokesperson said in an emailed press statement that WHO Director General Tedros has the authority to invite Taiwan to participate as an observer and we call on him to do so. From 2009 to 2016, Taiwan was invited by former WHO DG Margaret Chan to attend the WHA as an observer. But after the DPP won the election in 2016, the WHA unilaterally stopped the invitation. Taiwan's…","There is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inseparable part of China's territory. As a specialized agency of the UN, the WHO should deal with Taiwan-related issues in strict accordance with the one-China principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. No legal basis can be found in WHO's Constitution or the WHA's Rules of Procedure to justify the participation of a region of a sovereign state in the WHA.\nFrom 2009 to 2016, through cross-strait consultations and on the basis that both adhere to the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle, China's Central government made special arrangements for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA as an observer. In the past, the WHO director general invited Taiwan to participate as an observer on the precondition of no objection from all WHO member states, but that does not constitute a precedent.\nSince the DPP came to power, it has obstinately adhered to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence\" and refused to recognize that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in WHO has ceased to exist. That foundation was unilaterally abandoned by the DPP authorities, who are the only one to blame for the region now being unable to take part in the WHA. The DPP understands this only too well. It goes without saying that with China and the vast majority of members firmly opposed to the participation of the Taiwan region, the WHO DG could not issue an invitation.\nAccording to the consensus reached by the WHO Executive Board, this year's agenda will be significantly reduced to cover only essential items like the COVID-19 pandemic and Executive Board election. This reflects the shared wish of member states to focus on international cooperation on COVID-19 at this WHA. I would like to reiterate that the one-China principle is a consensus of the international community and the overriding trend of the times. The WHA has long made a final decision on issues relating to the Taiwan region. The few countries who are insisting on discussing the proposal relating to the Taiwan region are only seeking to severely disrupt this WHA and undermine global anti-pandemic cooperation. The international community including China stand firmly against this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1779190.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200514_5418920.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-14","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US navy said today it has sailed a destroyer through the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment on this?","China closely and fully monitored the US navy vessel sailing through the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the US side will properly deal with the relevant issue and play a constructive role in upholding regional peace and stability, instead of the contrary.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1779190.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200514_5418920.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-15","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","We understand that the DPP authorities are soliciting support for Taiwan's participation in the 73rd World Health Assembly, claiming there will be a \"gap\" in global anti-epidemic efforts if Taiwan is not able to participate. A handful of countries including the US are asking the WHO to invite the Taiwan region to attend as an observer and pushing for WHA discussions of this proposal. I wonder if you have any comment?","Lately I have commented repeatedly on the so-called participation of the Taiwan region in the WHA. Since COVID-19 broke out, Taiwan's DPP authorities have been busy making political manipulation and hyping up so-called \"Taiwan's participation in the WHA\" on international occasions. Their true intention is to seek independence under the pretext of the pandemic with the help of some Western countries. We firmly oppose their futile attempts.\nThe participation of the Taiwan region, which is part of China, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is also a fundamental principle enshrined in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. Since the DPP came to power in 2016, it has obstinately adhered to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence\" and refused to recognize that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in WHO has ceased to exist. The DPP authorities are the only party to blame for the region being unable to take part in the WHA. The DPP understands that only too well.\nThe Chinese Central Government always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. In January, the Central Government hosted Taiwan experts traveling to Wuhan to observe epidemic containment efforts on the ground. As of May 15, the Central Government has sent 152 notifications on COVID-19 to the Taiwan region. Since 2019, under the one-China principle, altogether 24 Taiwan experts in 16 groups have participated in WHO technical activities. The claim of a \"gap\" in global anti-epidemic efforts is simply not true, as Taiwan has unimpeded access to epidemic information.\nAccording to the consensus reached by the WHO Executive Board, this year's agenda will cover only essential items like the COVID-19 pandemic and Executive Board election. This reflects the shared wish of member states to focus on international cooperation on COVID-19 at this WHA. The WHA has for many consecutive years rejected a handful of countries' proposals relating to the Taiwan region, demonstrating the shared international commitment to the one-China principle, an overriding trend that cannot be challenged. The few countries that insist on discussing the proposal relating to the Taiwan region are only aiming to politicize the health issue to seek selfish political gains even at the expense of hijacking the WHA and undermining global anti-pandemic cooperation. Their attempt will inevitably disrupt the WHA proceedings and international cooperation, which will be firmly rejected by the vast majority of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1779579.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200515_5418923.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-15","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company is going to invest $12 billion in the United States to build a new factory. Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said this is an important move at a time China when China is competing to dominate cutting-edge technology and control critical industries. Does China believe this investment is another part of US strategy to delink the Chinese and US economies?","As a general rule, we don't comment on the production or business layout of any company.\nWe have said many times that cooperation between China and the US in various fields like economy, trade and investment is in nature mutually beneficial. We stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. Decoupling or severing relations will lead nowhere. We urge the US to abandon the obsolete Cold War and zero-sum game mindset and correctly view exchanges and cooperation with China in the fields of science and technology, economy and trade, and work to enhance China-US mutual trust and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1779579.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202005/t20200515_5418923.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-05-15","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reported the French government plans to sell weapons to Taiwan. What comment does the Ministry of National Defense have?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. China firmly opposes any country selling weapons to Taiwan and firmly opposes any country conducting military contacts with Taiwan. China demands that France immediately cancel the relevant arms sales projects to Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to relations between the two countries and their militaries. The Chinese military has firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-05/15/content_4865145.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2020-05-19","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","The President of the 73rd WHA announced that the proposal submitted by Taiwan's \"diplomatic allies\" to invite the region to participate in the WHA as an observer will not be discussed at this meeting, and relevant issues will be left for discussion at the Assembly's resumed session in the second half of this year. What is China's comment?","On May 18, the President of the 73rd WHA announced that the meeting would not discuss the proposal put forward by some countries to \"invite Taiwan to participate in the WHA as an observer\". The Taiwan authorities and some countries failed to promote the Taiwan-related proposal at the WHA. This once again shows that seeking \"Taiwan independence\" is like walking into a blind alley; it goes against the will of the people to hype up Taiwan-related proposals at the WHA.\nIn the context of the ongoing global spread of COVID-19, focusing on international cooperation against the pandemic is the common expectation of the majority of WHO member states for this meeting. Against the strong will of the vast majority of WHO member states, the DPP authorities and some countries are bent on pushing the Taiwan-related proposal in an attempt to disrupt the proceedings of the assembly and undermine international cooperation against the pandemic. It fully exposes their true intention of putting political considerations above international public health security.\nThe vast majority of WHO member states uphold the authority of the UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1 and adhere to impartiality and justice. China highly commends that.\nThe people in the Taiwan region are our compatriots. The Central Government of China takes all necessary measures to ensure the health and well-being of our Taiwan compatriots. After COVID-19 broke out, we invited health experts from the Taiwan region, before inviting anyone else outside the mainland, to visit Wuhan, Hubei province to see the situation on the ground, and we have given the Taiwan region 152 updates about the COVID-19 outbreak. Based on the one-China principle, the Central Government of China has made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. There are no obstacles for Taiwan experts to participate in WHO's technical activities. Since 2019, a total of 24 health experts in 16 groups have participated in WHO's technical activities. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region so it can obtain timely information on global public health emergencies released by the WHO and report its public health emergency information to the WHO in a timely manner as well. All channels of information on epidemic prevention and control are unimpeded and effective, a guarantee for the Taiwan region to respond in a timely and effective manner to public health incidents on the island or elsewhere in the world. The so-called \"international epidemic prevention gap\" is just an excuse for the DPP authorities to seek independence under the pretext of the epidemics, which has already been seen through by the international community long ago.\nWe urge the DPP authorities to acknowledge the facts and not go further down the wrong path of seeking independence. Thinking that relying on some external forces will improve their odds of breaking the universally-recognized one-China principle is just a pipe dream. We also urge some countries not to misjudge China's determination and ability to safeguard its core interests and national reunification. They should immediately change course and stop any action that challenges the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1780716.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1780583.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The President of the 73rd World Health Assembly announced that the meeting will not discuss the Taiwan-related proposal submitted by Taiwan's so-called “allies.” What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th in response to a question that the relevant decisions of the 73rd World Health Assembly once again show that “Taiwan independence” has no way out, and that hyping Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly does not win popular support. The One China principle is the consensus of the international community, in keeping with popular sentiment and the trend of the times. There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, the iron-clad facts are beyond question, and the iron-clad principle cannot be shaken.\nHe said that it must be pointed out that the mainland has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan. We not only promote exchanges and cooperation in the health field across the Taiwan Strait, but also uphold the One China principle in international affairs, and have adopted multiple measures to make appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region’s participation in global health affairs. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, the channels through which the Taiwan side has obtained various epidemic prevention and control information and support have been smooth and effective. As of May 18, the mainland had notified Taiwan of epidemic information and shared technical materials a total of 155 times. Since 2019 alone, 24 health experts from the Taiwan region, in 16 groups, have participated in technical activities of the WHO, including briefings on the epidemic situation by the WHO Secretariat and research-related meetings. The lie about a so-called “international epidemic prevention gap” is merely a pretext for the DPP authorities to “use the epidemic to seek independence.” It cannot withstand the facts and is not worth refuting.\nMa Xiaoguang said that from 2009 to 2016, the Taiwan region was able to participate in the World Health Assembly under the name “Chinese Taipei” with observer status. This was a special arrangement made through cross-strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides upheld as embodying the One China principle. After the DPP took office in May 2016, it stubbornly clung to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-strait consultations. The Taiwan region has been unable to participate in the World Health Assembly for four consecutive years, and the responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities. Their practice of interfering with the proceedings of the World Health Assembly and undermining international cooperation on epidemic prevention fully exposes the true face of the DPP authorities, who place their own political interests in “Taiwan independence” above public health and safety.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that we advise the DPP authorities not to go further and further down the wrong path. Any act that challenges the One China principle will inevitably end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200519_12275933.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-20","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","First question, on Tuesday, US Secretary of State Pompeo sent a congratulatory message to Tsai Ing-wen on the commencement of her second term. He called her \"Taiwan's President\" and acclaimed Taiwan as a \"force for good\" and a reliable \"partner\". This is the first time in decades for a US secretary of state to publicly congratulate the leader of the Taiwan region on starting a new term. I wonder what is China's…","Regarding what you said in your first question, a foreign ministry statement was released.\nOn May 20, in his statement to congratulate Tsai Ing-wen's assumption of office as the leader of the Taiwan region, US Secretary of State Pompeo called her \"Taiwan's President\" and boasted about the \"partnership\" between the US and Taiwan. Some other US officials and politicians also sent congratulatory videos to Tsai. These practices by the US side are in serious violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and constitute grave interference in China's internal affairs. China deplores and condemns them.\nThere's only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. As the China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations clearly stipulates, \"The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\" The above-mentioned US practices seriously violate the one-China principle, the three China-US joint communiqués and the US government's own commitment. They have sent a wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and gravely undermined the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as the bilateral relations between China and the US.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. The Chinese government and people are determined in opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposing external interference and realizing national reunification. We solemnly inform the US that \"Taiwan independence\" will only lead to a dead end, and attempts to condone and support \"Taiwan independence\" are doomed to fail. Practices that undermine China's core interests and intervene in China's domestic affairs will be met with forceful fightback, which will not to the slightest extent impede the historical trend of China's reunification. We urge the US to immediately correct its mistakes, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, cut its official ties with Taiwan, and stop upgrading substantive relations with Taiwan, interfering in China's internal affairs and undermining the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as China-US bilateral relations.\nChina will take necessary measures in response to the US erroneous practices, and the consequences will be borne by the US side.\nAs for your second question, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council stated our position on the statement made by the leader of the DPP authorities on May 20.\nI'd like to stress that there's only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing international trend. Attempts to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1780978.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1780914.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-20","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","There have been some global responses to President Trump's letter to WHO Director-General Tedros. Canadian Prime Minister said that Canada will continue to support WHO. Spokesperson for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy at European Commission said that this is the time for solidarity, not the time for finger-pointing or undermining multilateral cooperation. The EU backs the WHO in its efforts to contain and…","I noted those responses you mentioned from all over the world. It is not difficult to see that the international community does not agree with the US fact-distorting and self-contradictory actions that aim to shift the blame and responsibility to others and undermine international cooperation on COVID-19 response. Those fallacies in the US leader's letter have been pointed out and cleared up by us many times. Here I just want to list some of its basic mistakes.\nThe letter said that \"Taiwanese authorities had communicated information to the WHO indicating human-to-human transmission of a new virus\". The fact is, the email sent from the Taiwan region to WHO on December 31 was mainly about requesting information from WHO, without any mention of \"human-to-human transmission\".\nThe letter said that on January 21, the Chinese leader pressured Director-General Tedros. This is pure fiction. As has been clarified by both China and WHO, the Chinese leader and Director-General Tedros didn't even have a phone call on January 21.\nThe letter criticized Director-General Tedros for praising China for its transparency and setting a new standard for outbreak control. The US side seems to have forgotten that its leader has publicly commended on China's outbreak response on many occasions. On January 25, President Trump tweeted that China has been working very hard to contain the coronavirus, and the United States greatly appreciates its efforts and transparency. On March 13, President Trump told journalists that the data China shared was helpful for the U.S. efforts against the epidemic.\nThe list of US disinformation, lies and rumors goes on and on. There is simply not enough time for me to enumerate them all. But the public is a fair judge. The international community will determine the credibility of this letter.\nLet us just revisit the timeline here. The US had only one confirmed case when Wuhan was put under lockdown on January 23. The US official tally for the confirmed cases was 11 when it closed its borders on February 2 to all Chinese citizens as well as foreigners who had been to China in the previous 14 days. The US had 1,264 cases when it declared national emergency on March 13. The number surpassed 10,000 on March 19 and 100,000 on March 27. When the lockdown in Wuhan was lifted on April 8, there were 400,000 confirmed cases in the US. Today, the US has more than 1.57 million confirmed cases and over 90,000 death tolls. We mourn for the lost lives and wish the US people will defeat the outbreak as early as possible. But for those US politicians spending all their time on political maneuvering, the responsibility is too heavy to shake off.\nChina upholds the vision of building a community with a shared future for mankind and puts the people and their lives first. China takes it as its responsibility to ensure not just the life and health of its own citizens, but also global public health. We have taken the most comprehensive, rigorous and thorough measures, and every family and every citizen nationwide have been contributing their strength in this fight against COVID-19. After making painstaking efforts and enormous sacrifice, we have turned the tide. We have been acting with openness, transparency and responsibility, and providing epidemic updates to WHO and relevant countries including the US in a timely fashion. We shared the genome sequence at the earliest possible time. We shared control and treatment experience with the world without reservation. We have done everything in our power to support and assist countries in need. On May 18, President Xi Jinping delivered a speech via videolink at the opening ceremony of the 73rd World Health Assembly and put forward important proposals and measures on international cooperation in response to COVID-19. China firmly supports WHO's leading role in the global response, because to support WHO is to support international cooperation and to support saving lives. Practices of unilateralism, selfishness, evading responsibility, and even coercing and intimidating WHO, are indifference toward lives, challenges to humanitarianism, and disruption of international cooperation on COVID-19 response.\nThe US should commit itself to securing an early victory against the virus instead of issuing an \"ultimatum\" to the very international organization spearheading the global response. We advise some US politicians reflect on their actions, stop political maneuvering and focus on saving more lives.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1780978.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1780914.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20. On May 20, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions about the cross-strait content of the DPP authorities' leader's “May 20” speech, said: At present, the situation in cross-strait relations is complex and grave. The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and unilaterally undermine the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Some politicians create cross-strait confrontation, obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and attempt to sever Taiwan's relationship with the mainland both geographically and legally. They step up collusion with external forces to undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait, “seeking independence through the epidemic.” A very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists clamor for so-called “law amendments” and “referendums,” scheming for “de jure Taiwan independence.” All of this seriously harms the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, seriously harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that the reunification of the motherland is the historical inevitability of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and no person or force can stop it. “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent and a dead end. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and we are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will absolutely not leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form. We have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will absolutely not tolerate any act that splits the country, and we will absolutely not tolerate any external force interfering in China's internal affairs.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we will continue to unite the broad Taiwan compatriots and work together to promote exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, strengthen the emotional bonds between them, and deepen cross-strait integrated development. We actively help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses on the mainland overcome difficulties and resume work and production, and support Taiwan compatriots in gaining more development opportunities and a greater sense of gain on the mainland. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals, and to continue dialogue and consultation on cross-strait relations and the future of the nation, and to strive together to promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, advance the peaceful reunification of the motherland, and realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThat morning, Tsai Ing-wen was inaugurated in Taipei as leader of the new term of the Taiwan authorities, beginning her second term.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200520_12276191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-05-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On May 19, U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo issued a statement on the U.S. State Department website and on his personal Twitter account congratulating Tsai Ing-wen on her inauguration for a second term. The DPP authorities expressed gratitude. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 20th in response to questions: We urge the United States side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, observe the basic norms of international relations, and stop any form of official exchanges with the Taiwan region.\nMa Xiaoguang made the above statement in answering questions. He said that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. We have firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to thwart any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes. We will take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and continue to advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200520_12276240.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-05-21","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US government has notified Congress of a possible sale of advanced torpedoes to Taiwan worth around $180 million. What's the foreign ministry's comment on this?","China firmly opposes US arms sales to Taiwan. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan, lest it should further harm China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1781212.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1781210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-05-21","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo once again attacked China's political system at a press conference on May 20, vilifying and tarnishing China on COVID-19, Taiwan, Hong Kong and other issues. What is China's comment?","Mr. Pompeo lied again as he normally does. He really is second to none at being an extremely irresponsible politician. But the international community has already seen through the set of lies he tries to sell.\nRegarding the pandemic, as the US Secretary of State, Pompeo owes the world clear answers to the following questions: Why didn't the US government take strong containment measures during the long period from January to March? Why did it for a long time argue against the practice of wearing masks? Why did it fail to curb the rapid rising trend of the epidemics in the US? Pompeo has the responsibility to give explicit explanations to the international community.\nOn the issues related to the Taiwan region and Hong Kong, Pompeo should first figure out the territorial scope of the US and stop poking his nose into China's internal affairs, otherwise his attempts will be countered.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1781212.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1781210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-05-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 21 — In response to the US State Department's recent approval of a US$180 million arms sale to Taiwan, TAO spokesperson 马晓光 said in response to a question on the 21st: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to China's Taiwan region and oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan, including military contacts. The DPP authorities have repeatedly used the hard-earned money of Taiwan taxpayers to buy American weapons. This will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200521_12276556.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-05-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The third session of the 13th National People's Congress deliberated the “Decision of the National People's Congress on Establishing and Improving the Legal System and Enforcement Mechanisms for Safeguarding National Security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (Draft).” The DPP authorities made baseless accusations and malicious attacks. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on this? Ma…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 22 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 22nd, saying: We advise the DPP and its authorities to immediately stop their wanton attacks and irresponsible remarks on the bills under review by the National People’s Congress, and to stop their political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs. We also hope that certain political forces on the island will distinguish right from wrong and do more that is conducive to the prosperity and stability of Hong Kong and to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nHe said that establishing and improving, at the national level, the legal system and enforcement mechanisms for the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region to safeguard national security is very necessary and important. Its purpose is to firmly safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, maintain the long-term prosperity and stability of Hong Kong, and ensure that the policy of “one country, two systems” does not change, does not waver, and that its implementation does not deviate or become distorted.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that for some time, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have colluded with “Hong Kong independence” forces and international anti-China forces. Using the controversy over the extradition-law amendments and other pretexts, they have extensively interfered in Hong Kong affairs, created incidents, fanned the “anti-China, Hong Kong-disrupting” activities, slandered and attacked “one country, two systems,” and served as a cover for “Taiwan independence” separatism. Their schemes will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200522_12276846.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-05-24","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On May 20, the US State Department announced that it had approved the sale to Taiwan of weapons, including torpedoes, worth up to 180 million US dollars. This US move seriously violates the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, and China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nAt present, cross-Strait relations are complex and grave. Taiwan regional leader Tsai Ing-wen refuses to accept the “1992 Consensus” and attempts to rely on foreign backing to enhance her own standing. She is aggravating cross-Strait antagonism and damaging cross-Strait relations. In this situation, the US has openly announced a new round of arms sales to Taiwan. This sends a seriously wrong signal to the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. It seriously damages China's sovereignty and security, seriously endangers peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harms the development of China-US military-to-military relations.\nNational rejuvenation and national reunification are the people's aspiration and the trend of the times, and no person or force can stop them. We strongly urge the US side to immediately halt arms sales to Taiwan and immediately halt US-Taiwan military ties, so as to avoid further damage to China-US military relations. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-05/24/content_4865675.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2020-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reported that China's 2020 national budget allocates national defense expenditure up 6.6% over the previous year. Please have the spokesperson introduce the considerations behind this arrangement.","President Xi has profoundly pointed out that “coordinating development and security, strengthening a sense of crisis, and remaining alert in times of peace are a major principle for our Party in governing the country.” China adheres to balancing development with security and to unifying national wealth with military strength. It insists on coordinated development of national defense construction and economic construction, and reasonably determines the scale and structure of national defense spending based on the country's economic development level and national defense needs. In other words, when we consider the national defense budget, we have two ledgers in hand: we must calculate the economic ledger, and even more so the security ledger.\nRecently, our country has faced some new risks and challenges in the field of national security. Internationally, hegemonism and power politics occasionally resurface, unilateralism prevails in some countries, geopolitical risks are rising, and the international security system and order have been impacted. It can be said that the world is not at peace. Domestically, security threats are diverse and complex, the struggle against separatism is more severe, and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, relying on foreign backing to reinforce their own position, are going further and further down the road of separatism. Our national territorial security and overseas interests also face some real threats. On national security issues, we must keep a clear head, remain alert in times of peace, and be prepared to avoid disaster.\nThe growth of national defense spending is also a need for the Chinese military to fulfill more international responsibilities. As the Chinese military grows stronger, the international community's expectations that it provide more public security goods are also rising. The Chinese military actively supports UN peacekeeping operations; it has dispatched 35 batches of naval escort task groups to the Gulf of Aden and waters off Somalia to carry out regular escort missions, and it actively takes part in international disaster relief, earning widespread acclaim from the international community. Keeping national defense spending growing at a moderate and stable pace will help the Chinese military practice the major concept of a community with a shared future for mankind, actively fulfill the international responsibilities of a major-country military, and make more contributions to building a lasting peace and a world of universal security.\nChina firmly follows the path of peaceful development and firmly adheres to a defensive national defense policy. China's national defense spending is open and transparent, and its spending level is reasonable and appropriate. Compared with the needs for safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, compared with the needs for fulfilling the international responsibilities and obligations of a major country, and compared with the needs of its own construction and development, China's national defense spending still falls far short. It is entirely reasonable and necessary for China's national defense spending to grow moderately and steadily.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-05/26/content_4866019.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2020-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The government work report submitted to the Third Session of the 13th National People's Congress for deliberation points out that we must adhere to the major principles and policies on Taiwan work and resolutely oppose and deter “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. Recently, the US Secretary of State issued a statement congratulating the leader of Taiwan on taking office, and the US State Department also…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, concerns China's core interests and the national sentiment of 1.4 billion Chinese people, and brooks no foreign interference. The US side's actions seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously interfere in China's internal affairs, seriously endanger the development of China-US relations and of military relations between the two militaries, and seriously harm peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. They are extremely wrong and also very dangerous.\nNational rejuvenation and national reunification are the will of the people and the trend of the times. At present, cross-Strait relations face a complex and grave situation. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to accept the “1992 Consensus” and seek to rely on foreign powers to bolster themselves and to pursue “independence” through force. Such conduct runs counter to national righteousness, seriously harms the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and will certainly be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.\nIt must be pointed out that pursuing “Taiwan independence” means a dead end, and pursuing armed confrontation means self-destruction. We will never allow anyone, any organization, any political party, at any time or in any form, to split off any piece of Chinese territory from China! The Chinese People's Liberation Army has the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-05/26/content_4866019.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2020-05-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 28 — In response to Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities repeatedly making irresponsible remarks about the National People’s Congress decision on Hong Kong-related matters, turning a blind eye to the illegal acts of Hong Kong’s black-clad violent elements, and threatening to carry out so-called “rescue operations,” Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 28th, pointed out that the prosperity and stability of Hong Kong brook no interference or sabotage by any separatist forces. We warn the DPP authorities to stop profiteering from the turmoil and stirring up trouble. Bringing black-clad violent forces into Taiwan will only harm the people of Taiwan and is like lifting a rock only to drop it on one’s own feet.\nMa Xiaoguang said in response to questions, “Regarding the National People’s Congress decision on Hong Kong-related matters, we have already expressed our stern position earlier. I want to emphasize that the prosperity and stability of Hong Kong brook no interference or sabotage by any separatist forces. For some time, ‘Taiwan independence’ and ‘Hong Kong independence’ forces have colluded with each other, attempting to create chaos in Hong Kong and split the motherland, which has aroused shared indignation and resolute opposition among Chinese people at home and abroad. The DPP authorities have distorted the facts and vilified the National People’s Congress decision on Hong Kong-related matters with wild attacks, once again exposing their sinister intention to manipulate the Hong Kong situation, attack ‘one country, two systems,’ and seek ‘Taiwan independence’ separatism, seriously harming the interests and well-being of compatriots in Hong Kong and Taiwan.”\nMa Xiaoguang said, “The series of illegal acts by radical violent elements should be punished in accordance with the law. Our prevention, suppression, and punishment of illegal and criminal acts endangering national security are aimed at better safeguarding the life and property safety, basic rights, and freedoms of Hong Kong residents, and better implementing ‘one country, two systems.’ We warn the DPP authorities to stop profiteering from the turmoil and stirring up trouble. Bringing black-clad violent forces into Taiwan will only harm the people of Taiwan and is like lifting a rock only to drop it on one’s own feet.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200528_12278230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-05-29","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Tsai Ing-wen took office as the leader of Taiwan on May 20. On May 21, the US State Department approved the sale of an estimated $180 million worth of MK-48 Heavy Weight Torpedoes and related equipment and technology to Taiwan. What’s your comment?","China firmly opposes the sale of arms by the US to Taiwan. The wrong action of the US seriously violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, the one-China principle and regulations of the three China-US joint communiqués. It is a grave interference in China’s internal affairs and greatly undermines the relations between China and the US and the military-to-military relationship. It harms the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and is extremely dangerous. We urge the US to stop selling arms to Taiwan immediately, stop developing any form of official relations with Taiwan, and do not send wrong messages to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-06/01/content_4866094.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-05-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 29th the mainland held a symposium marking the 15th anniversary of the implementation of the “Anti-Secession Law.” What considerations lie behind this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks when answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 30 (electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 30th, said that resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of the Chinese people and all the sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. Fifteen years ago, when “Taiwan independence” separatist activities were rampant on the island, the National People's Congress formulated and implemented the Anti-Secession Law, a concentrated expression of the national will and the interests of the people. Over the 15 years since the law took effect, it has played an important role in curbing “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland. It has provided a solid legal guarantee for safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, promoting the development of cross-Strait relations, and protecting the well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the situation across the Taiwan Strait is currently complex and grave. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces keep up a stream of provocations, which seriously harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and seriously challenge our bottom line of safeguarding national sovereignty, territorial integrity, and development interests. On the morning of the 29th, a symposium marking the 15th anniversary of the Anti-Secession Law was solemnly held in the Great Hall of the People. Li Zhanshu, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, delivered an important speech. It fully demonstrated our firm resolve to curb and combat “Taiwan independence” separatism, our constant commitment to safeguarding the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and our confidence that the complete reunification of the motherland will be achieved.\nMa Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Any “Taiwan independence” separatist activity is illegal and null and void. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to break the law, they will be severely punished. Any attempt by external forces to interfere in China's internal affairs or to split Taiwan from China is doomed to fail.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the motherland must be and will certainly be reunified. This is a historical verdict and an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will continue to thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work. We will adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and to the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle. We will strive with the utmost sincerity and effort for the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will not leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the grave harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, see the trend clearly, seize opportunities, and join us in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200530_12278536.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-05-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, May 30 — After the National People's Congress adopted the decision on legislation concerning Hong Kong, the Taiwan legislature issued a so-called “statement,” which, while wantonly attacking, claimed it would “rescue Hong Kong people” and promote relevant “legislation” and administrative measures. TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 30th, said that these schemes of the Taiwan legislature will not succeed; by interfering in Hong Kong affairs, it will surely reap what it has sown.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the purpose of the NPC's legislation concerning Hong Kong is to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, ensure Hong Kong's long-term prosperity and stability, and ensure the sound and steady implementation of “one country, two systems.” It targets external forces, separatist forces and violent terrorist forces that endanger national security, and protects the various rights and freedoms that Hong Kong residents enjoy under the law.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities and some politicians on the island have time and again distorted facts, twisted right and wrong, and wrongly accused the legislation concerning Hong Kong, precisely because that legislation is meant to cut off the black hands that link “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” in disrupting and splitting Hong Kong.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the Taiwan legislature's issuance of a so-called “statement” and its promotion of so-called “legislation” and administrative measures to provide “rescue” to the chaos-makers in Hong Kong constitute open protection for lawless violent forces, further exposing its political nature of creating chaos in Hong Kong, attacking “one country, two systems,” and seeking “Taiwan independence.” Its schemes will not succeed; by interfering in Hong Kong affairs, it will surely reap what it has sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202005/t20200530_12278537.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-06-09","Hua Chunying","AFP","The Taiwan authorities said that it warned off Chinese fighter jets that flew near southwest Taiwan today. Can you confirm this and do you have any response to that statement?","I'm not aware of that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1787390.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202006/t20200609_5419004.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-06-11","Hua Chunying","","Media reports say a US C-40A transport jet flew over the Taiwan region on June 9. Do you have any comment on that?","China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this move by the US, which gravely violates international law and basic norms governing international relations. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and immediately stop such unlawful and provocative behaviors. China will take all necessary measures to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1787995.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202006/t20200611_5419015.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-06-11","Hua Chunying","","涉港国安立法是否会对香港的互联网进行限制？中方是否会出于维护国家安全而禁止一些手机应用或网站在香港使用？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1787995.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202006/t20200611_5419015.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2020-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 11 — In response to media reports that on June 9 a US military C-40A transport aircraft flew over Taiwan, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 11th that the flight of US military aircraft over Taiwan damages our sovereignty, security, and development interests, violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, and is an illegal act and a serious provocation. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to infringe upon China’s sovereignty and security, undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, have brought disaster to the security and well-being of the people on the island. We strongly condemn this. We have the determination, will, and capability to firmly safeguard our national sovereignty, security, and development interests. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities not to misjudge the situation, and not to underestimate the firm will and determination of the entire Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to immediately stop the above actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200611_12281145.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 12 – In response to some “Taiwan independence” parties and groups on the island who have recently continuously clamored for “constitutional amendment” and “renaming,” and attempted to push for the drafting of a so-called “new constitution,” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 12th, pointing out: In the recent period, the DPP authorities have intensified their collusion with external forces to undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, continuously provoking cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, which has caused cross-Strait relations to become more complex and severe. A small handful of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island, blinded by the lure of power and profit, have taken the opportunity to make trouble, loudly clamoring for and intensifying a series of activities to pursue “independence.” They are attempting to push cross-Strait relations to the brink of danger and push Taiwan compatriots into an abyss of disaster.\nZhu Fenglian said that “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest obstacle to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Their conduct runs counter to the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, and it is destined to fail. We solemnly warn these “Taiwan independence” diehards to pull back from the brink, and that anyone who dares to defy the law will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200612_12281271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-06-15","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that on June 9, a U.S. Navy C-40 transport aircraft flew across Taiwan Island. What is your comment on this?","US military aircraft flew over Chinese territory without China's permission, seriously violating China's territorial sovereignty and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This is extremely wrong and dangerous. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop all acts that provoke China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China, and any approach of “using Taiwan to contain China” or relying on foreign backing to boost one's own standing leads nowhere. The PLA has firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and it will resolutely thwart any scheme to create “one China, one Taiwan.”","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/qwfb/4866733.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2020-06-18","Zhao Lijian","CGTN","US President Trump signed into law the \"Uyghur Human Rights Policy Act of 2020\", according to which President Trump needs to submit a report and a sanction list to Congress 180 days after the law comes into force. What is your comment?","The Foreign Ministry, the NPC Foreign Affairs Committee, the CPPCC Foreign Affairs Committee and the Standing Committee of the People's Congress of Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region have all issued statements in response to this. The United States signed into law the so-called \"Uyghur Human Rights Policy Act of 2020\". This so-called Act deliberately denigrates the human rights conditions in China's Xinjiang, viciously attacks the Chinese government's Xinjiang policy, blatantly violates international law and basic norms governing international relations, and grossly interferes in China's internal affairs. The Chinese government and people express strong indignation and firm opposition to this.\nXinjiang-related issues are not issues about human rights, ethnicity or religion at all, but about combating violent terrorism and separatism. Xinjiang once suffered deeply from extremism, violent terrorism and separatism, which jeopardized the safety and property of the people there. Xinjiang has taken a series of measures to combat these activities and prevent their re-occurrence, in an approach of addressing both the symptoms and root causes of the problem. The measures taken are in compliance with Chinese laws. They are also China's concrete steps in implementing the international counter-terrorism and de-radicalization initiatives, including the UN Global Counter-Terrorism Strategy and the Plan of Action to Prevent Violent Extremism.\nThe measures carried out in Xinjiang have effectively curbed the rising and frequent occurrences of violent terrorist activities, safeguarded national unity and security to the greatest extent possible, and protected the fundamental rights of the people of all ethnic groups in Xinjiang, including their rights to life, health and development. Over the past three years and more, there has not been a single violent terrorist case in Xinjiang. People of different ethnic groups and religious beliefs in Xinjiang live together as equals, enjoy unity and harmony, and lead a peaceful and stable life. China's policy in Xinjiang has been positively recognized across the international community.\nTerrorism and extremism are common enemies of human society. Countries' efforts in fighting terrorism and extremism should not be judged by different yardsticks, still less deliberately distorted in violation of international justice and human conscience. The so-called Act of the US side, by disregarding facts and distorting truth, seeks to stigmatize Xinjiang's measures against terrorism, separatism and radicalization, and applies double standards on counter-terrorism. The Act further reveals the ill intention of the US side to undermine China's sovereignty and security, sow discord among the ethnic groups in China, harm Xinjiang's prosperity and stability, and contain China's development.\nWe hereby warn the US side that Xinjiang affairs are purely China's internal affairs that allow no foreign interference. The Chinese government and people are resolute in safeguarding China's sovereignty, security and development interests. Once again, we urge the US side to immediately redress the mistake, and stop using this Xinjiang-related Act to harm China's interests and interfere in China's internal affairs. Otherwise, China will respond resolutely, and the United States must bear all the consequences arising therefrom.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1790023.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202006/t20200618_5419040.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-06-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Recently, relevant Taiwan authorities published the first batch of overseas students permitted to return to Taiwan, which did not include mainland students studying in Taiwan, and continued to ban the children of mainland spouses from returning to Taiwan. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 18th, pointed out that the DPP authorities should face squarely the reasonable needs of mainland students and cross-Strait marriage families, respect their legitimate requests to return to Taiwan for study and family reunion, and cancel discriminatory measures as soon as possible.\nZhu Fenglian said that regarding the return to school of mainland students studying in Taiwan and the return to Taiwan of children from cross-Strait marriage families, we have stressed many times that their rights and interests should be respected and protected. Since the outbreak of the epidemic, the DPP authorities have deliberately adopted discriminatory measures against some Taiwan compatriots returning from the mainland, mainland students studying in Taiwan, and children from cross-Strait marriage families, seriously harming their legitimate rights and interests. This political manipulation, which departs from a humanitarian stance, has already been criticized by fair-minded public opinion on the island and by people from all sectors of society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200618_12282060.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 19 dispatch: Regarding the so-called “Hong Kong Humanitarian Assistance and Care Action Project” recently announced by the DPP authorities, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 19th, said that the DPP authorities’ so-called “assistance action” once again exposes its political scheme to meddle in Hong Kong affairs and undermine Hong Kong’s prosperity and stability. Providing shelter to “black violence” and Hong Kong-disrupting elements and bringing them onto the island will only continue to harm the people of Taiwan. The scheme of “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” converging to undermine “one country, two systems” and split the country will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200619_12282408.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, June 19 — The Cross-Strait Discourse Group of the Chinese Kuomintang Reform Committee recently put forward a mainland policy proposal, which has been submitted to the plenary session of the Reform Committee for discussion. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 19th, in response to questions, that we have noted that the Chinese Kuomintang is discussing its party's mainland policy. It must be stressed that although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation for mutual trust, exchanges and cooperation between the Communist Party of China and the Chinese Kuomintang. Over the years, the two parties have, on this basis, promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhanced the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and achieved positive results.\nShe pointed out that the current situation in cross-Strait relations is complex and grave. We hope the Chinese Kuomintang will distinguish right from wrong, adhere to a positive mainland policy, cherish and uphold the existing political foundation of the two parties, properly handle political differences across the Strait, move in the same direction, and continue to work with us to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots. If the party abandons the correct principles it has long upheld and departs from the basic principles concerning cross-Strait relations, it will not only damage the foundation of mutual trust, but will also create obstacles to exchanges and cooperation between the two parties and across the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200619_12282410.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 22 — In response to the pre-recorded video speech delivered by the leader of the DPP authorities at the \"2020 Copenhagen Democracy Summit\" a few days ago, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 22nd in response to questions: The leader of the DPP authorities, using the platform of certain non-governmental organizations and under the banner of \"democracy,\" engaged in ulterior political manipulation and pointed fingers at Hong Kong affairs. This once again exposes its political nature of seeking \"independence\" internationally, on various occasions and under various pretexts. We advise the DPP authorities to abandon their \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist schemes and stop seeking so-called \"diplomatic breakthroughs\" internationally. We also urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and not provide any stage or convenience for the DPP authorities to seek \"independence\" internationally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200622_12282890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 22 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 22nd, saying that recently, Su Tseng-chang, head of the Taiwan executive authority, took advantage of the United States’ release of the so-called “China Military Power Report” to viciously attack the mainland, stir up cross-Strait confrontation, and deliberately conflate “Taiwan independence” with Taiwan. This once again exposed his stubborn essence of pursuing “independence.”\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are members of one family, bound by blood. Chinese do not fight Chinese. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort. Our refusal to promise that we will renounce the use of force, and our reservation of the option to take all necessary measures, are aimed at external interference and at the very few “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist acts. They are by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots. “Taiwan independence” is the common enemy of compatriots on both sides and will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan’s 23 million people.\nZhu Fenglian said that a very small number of “Taiwan independence” figures on the island keep pursuing “independence” and provoking, and attempt to use this to hold Taiwan society hostage. She believes that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots can see through their vicious conduct and will never allow their schemes to succeed. Only when compatriots on both sides unite to resolutely contain “Taiwan independence” separatism can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be maintained and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots be protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200622_12282891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-06-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 22 — In response to media reports that on the 22nd the Ishigaki City Council of Okinawa Prefecture, Japan, passed a resolution changing the so-called “administrative district” name of the Diaoyu Islands, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated on the 22nd in response to questions: On this issue, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position. I must stress again: the Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands have been China's inherent territory since ancient times, and China has indisputable sovereignty over them. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China and should jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200622_12282894.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-06-23","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","On June 17, The American Prospect published a long report on Taiwan funding of think tanks. It disclosed that the five think tanks—the Hudson Institute, the Center for Strategic and International Studies, the Brookings Institution, the Center for American Progress and the Center for a New American Security received funding from the Taiwan authorities and produced policy papers pushing for expanded arms sales and…","I noted relevant reports and you need to ask those US think tanks.\nI want to stress that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and the universal consensus of the international community. China firmly opposes US military ties with and arms sales to Taiwan, and the signing of any trade agreement of sovereign implication between the US and Taiwanese businesses. The US should abide by the one-China principle and three China-US joint communiques and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues to avoid harming China-US relations and cross-straits peace and stability. The relevant US think tanks should conduct their studies in a fair and objective manner and make more reasonable voices.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1791668.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202006/t20200623_5419055.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-06-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US and Taiwan have had close interactions this month. A US transport plane flew over the Taiwan island for the first time, and its destroyers passed through the Taiwan Strait again. The US Defense Secretary Mark Esper even tweeted that America would remain committed to a “democratic Taiwan”. What’s your comment on that?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Taiwan affairs are purely China’s internal affairs that brook no external interference. The US’ frequent playing of the so-called Taiwan card in an attempt to harm China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity in the “sausage-slicing” approach is a sheer pipe dream. The PLA has been on high alert, and has the firm resolve, full confidence and sufficient capabilities to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-06/24/content_4867191.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-06-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 30 — In response to the DPP authorities' vicious attacks and slanders against the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for its vote to adopt the Hong Kong national security law, and their threat to launch so-called “assistance projects,” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on June 30, saying that the Hong Kong national security law clearly stipulates four categories of crimes that seriously endanger national security and their punishments, and it will certainly cut off the black hand of the DPP authorities who are disrupting Hong Kong. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any attempt by any person or force to damage national sovereignty, security and development interests, or to undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability, is futile and will certainly bring about its own downfall.\nZhu Fenglian said that the 20th Session of the 13th National People's Congress Standing Committee voted to adopt the Law of the People's Republic of China on Safeguarding National Security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and we firmly support and endorse the implementation of the Hong Kong national security law.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the Hong Kong national security law aims to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, and to ensure the long-term stable implementation of “one country, two systems” and the prosperity and stability of Hong Kong. The DPP authorities pretentiously jumped out to pass judgment on the Hong Kong national security law, openly distorting facts and reversing right and wrong, attempting to continue colluding with the troublemakers of Hong Kong and endangering national security. This once again exposes their sinister intention to meddle in Hong Kong affairs, create chaos in Hong Kong, and pursue “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202006/t20200630_12284131.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-07-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The DPP authorities recently said that mainland media's recording or producing programs in Taiwan is suspected of being “illegal,” revoked the press cards and entry permits of two mainland-stationed reporters, and said they would investigate the situation of mainland media stationed in Taiwan. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 3 (Xinhua). In response to questions on the 3rd, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, pointed out that the DPP authorities have brutally and unreasonably suppressed the normal news reporting activities of mainland media and their resident reporters, exposing the hypocrisy of their so-called \"freedom of the press.\"\nZhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering questions. She said that we have noted the relevant reports and are closely following the developments.\nZhu Fenglian said that exchange of news across the Strait is an important bridge for disseminating information across the Strait, enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, and promoting emotional integration. For a long time, mainland reporters in Taiwan have played an important bridging and connecting role through a large number of objective and fair reports, in particular in helping mainland compatriots better understand Taiwan. The legitimate rights and interests of mainland reporters should be protected, and their reporting work in Taiwan should be respected.\nShe said that for some time, the DPP authorities have restricted and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation by various means, and now they have directed their spearhead at the normal news reporting of mainland media in Taiwan. This seriously interferes with the resident news coverage of mainland media and seriously harms the legitimate rights and interests of mainland reporters. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop their unreasonable practices. Otherwise, all consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200703_12284467.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-07-06","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","Following WHO's last update on the timeline of its response to COVID-19, chairman of the China Task Force in the US House of Representatives Michael McCaul said that the WHO is finally admitting to the world the truth - the CCP never reported the virus outbreak to the WHO. Do you have any comment? Has China reported the outbreak to the WHO?","The allegation by the US side is totally untrue.\nAs a State Party to the International Health Regulations (2005), China has been acting in an open, transparent and responsible manner, earnestly implementing its duties and obligations under the IHR, and timely sharing COVID-19 information with the WHO, relevant countries, regional organizations, and China's Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions. The timelines published by the Chinese government and the WHO have clearly shown that China shared information with the international community in a timely and transparent fashion. On December 31, 2019, the Wuhan Municipal Health Commission released a statement on the situation of pneumonia in the city on its official website. China reported to the WHO at the earliest time possible. This fact cannot be clearer.\nBy telling lies and spreading disinformation, certain US politicians aim to frame China and the WHO for their own political agenda. We urge them to respect facts and stop political maneuvering.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1795337.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200706_5419090.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-07-06","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","Somalia reaffirmed its commitment to the one-China principle and condemned Taiwan for undermining Somalia's sovereignty and territorial integrity in a statement issued by its presidential office. Earlier reports said the Taiwan authorities and Somaliland in northwest Somalia had decided to set up \"representative offices\" for each other and had appointed representatives for each other. What is China's comment?","We noticed and appreciate that the Somali government reaffirmed its adherence to the one-China principle and condemned Taiwan for undermining Somalia's sovereignty and territorial integrity. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and an international consensus. China firmly opposes the establishment of official institutions or any form of official exchange between the Taiwan authorities and Somaliland. The Democratic Progressive Party has gone frantic in search of whatever support it could get, but it will never succeed in trying to stage separatist activities in the international arena.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1795337.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200706_5419090.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-07-07","Zhao Lijian","CRI","The ninth ministerial meeting of the China-Arab States Cooperation Forum (CASCF) was successfully held via videolink yesterday. Faced with severe challenges brought by COVID-19 and in terms of economic recovery, China and Arab states face significant external pressure. What is China's consideration behind holding this meeting in such context? What outcomes have been achieved in China-Arab practical cooperation…","The ninth ministerial meeting of the China-Arab States Cooperation Forum was successfully held via videolink last night. President Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter to the meeting. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Jordan's Minister of Foreign Affairs and Expatriates Ayman Safadi co-chaired the meeting and delivered keynote and concluding remarks. The meeting was addressed by the Arab League Secretary-General and foreign ministers of all the 21 AL member states.\nIt was no easy feat to hold this meeting. As COVID-19 wreaks havoc around the world, the future of all mankind and the destinies of all countries are unprecedentedly intertwined. The advent of this pandemic affected China and all Arab states and forced the cancellation or postponement of many institutional meetings between Arab states. Despite all these, both sides made joint efforts to overcome difficulties and hold this meeting as scheduled. This meeting bears far-reaching significance as it reflects the determination of China and Arab states to fight COVID-19 and advance China-Arab strategic partnership together.\nAfter discussions, three outcome documents were reached, namely the joint statement of China and Arab states on solidarity against COVID-19, the Amman declaration of the ninth ministerial meeting of the China-Arab States Cooperation Forum, and the execution plan for 2020-2022 of the China-Arab Cooperation Forum.\nThrough the joint statement of China and Arab states on solidarity against COVID-19, China and Arab states have gathered collective strength to fight the epidemics and tide over the difficulties together. Both sides stressed that solidarity and cooperation is the most powerful weapon for the international community to defeat the epidemics, and called for the building of a community with a shared future and a community for health between China and Arab states in the joint fight against COVID-19. Both sides underlined the importance of multilateralism, the need to further strengthen and improve the UN-centered global governance system, support the key leading role of WHO, and call on international community to strengthen coordination and form synergy, and stand against discrimination against any specific country, region, ethnic group or individual. China is ready to continue providing assistance to Arab states in fighting the epidemics.\nThe adoption of the Amman declaration demonstrates the political will of China and Arab states to support each other and share weal and woe. At the last ministerial meeting, President Xi Jinping put forward the initiative of \"jointly building a China-Arab community with a shared future for a new era\", which became a bilateral consensus. The two sides agreed to hold a China-Arab summit at an appropriate time and included the topic of building a China-Arab community with a shared future into the agenda of the summit.\nThe Arab states emphasized that they support China's position on Hong Kong-related matters, support China's efforts to safeguard national security under the framework of \"one country, two systems\" and oppose foreign interference in China's internal affairs. They support China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, adhere to the one-China principle and oppose \"Taiwan independence\" in all forms. They support China's preventive counter-terrorism measures and de-radicalization efforts. They oppose anti-China separatist activities carried out by extremist, separatist and terrorist forces.\nThrough the execution plan for 2020-2022, China and Arab states have mapped out practical cooperation and common development in the future. The two sides have reached 107 cooperation measures in 20 areas, including politics, economy, energy, production capacity, science, technology and health.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1795735.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200707_5419095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-07-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 7 (Dateline): In response to the baseless accusations by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities regarding the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government's publication of the “Implementation Rules for Article 43 of the Law of the People's Republic of China on Safeguarding National Security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region,” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 7th: The DPP authorities are guilty of a guilty conscience. Their criticism of the Hong Kong National Security Law and the Implementation Rules, and their wanton slander, once again expose their sinister intent to meddle in Hong Kong affairs, bring chaos to Hong Kong, and seek “Taiwan independence.” Any attempt to interfere in Hong Kong affairs, attack “one country, two systems,” or split the country is doomed to fail.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the Hong Kong National Security Law is an important measure to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests, maintain the long-term prosperity and stability of Hong Kong, and ensure that “one country, two systems” proceeds steadily and far. It will certainly strike effectively against disruptors of Hong Kong and separatist forces, and effectively prevent and control national security risks. It is very necessary and timely for the Hong Kong SAR Government to issue and implement the Implementation Rules.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200707_12285016.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-07-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 10 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 10th in response to questions: After consultation between relevant parties in Shanghai and Taipei, the “2020 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” will be held via videoconference on July 22. Over the years, Shanghai and Taipei have carried out exchanges and cooperation in urban construction and governance, reaching many points of consensus and enhancing the livelihood well-being and mutual understanding of residents of both cities. Cross-Strait city exchanges and cooperation advancing along the correct track are conducive to enhancing the well-being of people on both sides and sharing the dividends of mutually beneficial cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200710_12285469.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-07-14","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","According to a press release from the Defense Security Cooperation Agency (DSCA) of the US Department of Defense on July 9, the US State Department has approved a request from Taiwan to recertify its Patriot Advanced Capability-3 missiles for an estimated cost of $620 million. Lockheed Martin would be the prime contractor for this sale. What is your comment?","China firmly opposes US arms sales to Taiwan and urges the US to honor its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and stop selling arms to and having military ties with Taiwan to avoid further damage to China-US bilateral relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nIn order to safeguard our national interests, China has decided to take necessary measures and impose sanctions on the prime contractor for this sale Lockheed Martin.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1797731.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200714_5419120.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-07-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 14. In response to the US State Department's approval of a $620 million arms sale case for Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 14th: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China, and we oppose any form of military ties between Taiwan and the United States. The DPP authorities' “using arms to seek independence” will not succeed; it will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and bring greater disaster to the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200714_12286075.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-07-15","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On July 9, US local time, the Defense Security Cooperation Agency (DSCA) of the US Department of Defense issued a statement saying that the US State Department has approved the re-certification of a sale to Taiwan of Patriot-3 missiles worth a total of $620 million. The US side's move openly violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously damages China's sovereignty and security, and crudely interferes in China's internal affairs. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. China's position on the Taiwan question has been consistent and clear. China will never allow anyone, any organization or any country to separate Taiwan from the motherland by any means. All schemes that go against the trend of history, create “one China, one Taiwan,” or split China will be firmly opposed by all Chinese descendants, including all overseas Chinese. China strongly demands that the US immediately stop selling weapons to Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to China-US relations and military-to-military relations. We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities: reunification of the motherland is the great righteousness of the nation and the aspiration of the people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Relying on foreign powers to enhance one's own standing leads nowhere, and seeking “independence” through force is a dead end.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-07/15/content_4868206.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2020-07-16","Hua Chunying","ITV","A question about Taiwan. Today the Taiwanese military held drills rehearsing for a Chinese invasion. President Xi has said that unification is his aim. What is the position of the government on that today and is there a timetable for unifying China and Taiwan?","You should ask the Defense Ministry on questions about military drills. I've seen reports commenting that Taiwan wants to flex its muscle through holding military drills. If Taiwan really thinks that way, then it is hugely overestimating its strength.\nChina is rock-firm in safeguarding its sovereignty and security. Reunification of the People's Republic of China is the inevitable trend. Any force that seeks to separate China needs to be clear-minded about this. The 1.4 billion Chinese people will not allow an inch of the territory to be taken away.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202007/t20200716_693294.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200716_5419130.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-07-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to a statement by US Secretary of State Pompeo on the South China Sea issue, Taiwan's external affairs authorities claimed that they enjoy rights under international law and the law of the sea over the Nansha Islands and their surrounding waters. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above remarks.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 16: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 16th in response to a question: China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands and their adjacent waters. In response to erroneous remarks from the US side, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has repeatedly set out its position and refuted them. The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and should jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200716_12286544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-07-17","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","Taiwan said that its top representative to Hong Kong has returned home due to \"unnecessary political obstacles\". Some local media reported he refused to sign a statement endorsing \"one China\". We are wondering if China has comments on this?","I am not aware of the situation. There is only one China in the world, a fact and an international consensus. How can some in Taiwan call it an \"unnecessary political obstacle\"?\n********************************************\nBefore letting you go, I want to, with great pleasure, introduce to you my new colleague Wang Wenbin, new Spokesperson of the Foreign Ministry and Deputy Director General of the Information Department.\nDeputy Director General Wang Wenbin has been engaged in diplomatic work for 27 years. He once worked in the Information Department, Department of Western European Affairs, Policy Planning Department and General Office of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, as well as the Chinese diplomatic missions in Senegal, Cameroon and Mauritius. He served as China's Ambassador to Tunisia from 2017 to 2020. Deputy Director General Wang Wenbin is a seasoned diplomat and good communicator. I believe that he will soon become friend with all Chinese and foreign journalists. I believe our friends from the press will support Deputy Director General Wang Wenbin as they have supported me and all previous spokespersons. Now I'll give the floor to him.\nFriends from the press, good afternoon! Thank you, Director General Hua Chunying, for introducing me today. It is my great pleasure and honor to meet you all at this podium. As Director General Hua said, I have been serving as a diplomat for 27 years, but I am a new hand as a Spokesperson of the Foreign Ministry. I will do my best to learn from my predecessors and communicate with our journalist friends sincerely. I will introduce China's foreign policy and diplomatic visions to you in a timely and accurate manner so as to enhance mutual understanding and friendship between the Chinese people and the rest of the world. In the days to come, I will take each and every of your questions seriously and facilitate your work to the best of my capability. At the same time, I look also forward to your understanding and support. Because of the epidemic, I'm afraid I won't be able to shake hands with you one by one today, but I believe we'll have many more opportunities to talk with each other in the future. Thank you!\nDeputy Director-General Wang Wenbin will host the regular press conference starting from next week. We look forward to your participation and questions. That's the end of today's press conference. Have a nice weekend.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346839.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200717_5419134.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-07-23","Wang Wenbin","CRI","According Japanese media, the Japanese government on July 22 decided to conduct consultations with China, including the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions, and the ROK on relaxing restrictions on entry of personnel. Do you have any comment?","We welcome Japan’s decision to take science-based and proper measures to properly handle the entry and exit of personnel in light of development of the epidemic situation. Against the backdrop of maintaining ongoing epidemic control measures, the gradual resumption of the exchange of essential personnel between China and Japan will help the two countries accelerate resumption of work and production, promote economic recovery and guarantee stable and unfettered industrial and supply chains.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1800221.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200723_5419155.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 24 — In response to the DPP authorities' foreign affairs department expressing “thanks” on July 24 for remarks on Taiwan made by U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo on the 23rd, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 24th when asked: Regarding the remarks of U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has fully expounded the Chinese government's position. As for the Taiwan question he mentioned, I must emphasize that Taiwan is part of China, and Taiwan has never been a country. We demand that the U.S. government adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. “Taiwan independence” has no way out. No matter in what way, under what name, or by what means the DPP authorities attempt to seek “independence,” they will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200724_12287700.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-07-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to reports, amid rumors that the mainland recently destroyed Buddhist books, including those published by Taiwanese religious groups, the MAC stated that this is of no help to cross-Strait relations. What is the comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 27 — In response to the Mainland Affairs Council’s claim that some Taiwanese students studying on the mainland who wanted to transfer back to Taiwan recently, due to the epidemic and other reasons, were obstructed by mainland schools, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 27th: As we understand it, mainland universities have not received any transfer applications from Taiwanese students.\nZhu Fenglian said that after arduous efforts by all sides, the mainland’s prevention and control of the COVID-19 epidemic has achieved major results, and the epidemic has been effectively controlled. We have always attached importance to the health, study and life of Taiwanese students. At present, none of the Taiwanese students studying on the mainland has been infected, and conditions are stable in all respects.\nZhu Fenglian replied that the relevant claims do not conform to the facts. The mainland protects citizens’ freedom of religious belief in accordance with the law; it protects lawfully published religious books in accordance with the law, and protects the publication and distribution on the mainland of books by religious figures from Taiwan; at the same time, it investigates and punishes illegally published and printed publications in accordance with the law.\nZhu Fenglian said that for many years, the publication and distribution on the mainland, in accordance with the law, of books by Taiwanese religious figures or groups has been smooth. We will continue to support cross-Strait religious and cultural exchanges and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200727_12287880.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-07-30","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","US Defense Secretary Mark Esper said in a recent speech that China is undermining international rules and taking malicious and coercive actions. He also said that China’s aggressive activities including military drills targeting the Taiwan region in the East China Sea and the South China Sea will increase the risk of miscalculation. What’s your comment?","The remarks from the US side about China are groundless and unreasonable, full of arrogance, bias, attacks and smears. We are firmly opposed to these remarks.\nIt is a well-known fact that the US always bends international rules as it sees fit and is aggressively pursuing \"America first\" and unilateral bullism. Unlike the US, who has withdrawn from many international organizations and treaties, China is taking solid actions to fulfill its international responsibilities and obligations and joined the Arms Trade Treaty (ATT) on the same day the US announced its withdrawal from the World Health Organization (WHO).\nThe US has held and bragged about some highly-targeted military exercises in the Indo-Pacific region, deployed game-changing weapons and equipment to the region, and even openly pursued an alliance against China.\nWe urge the US to stop undermining world peace and regional stability, and stop sowing discord among countries.\nRecently, the US has strengthened its military contacts with the Taiwan region, promoted arms sales to Taiwan and floated possible joint military training with Taiwan. These actions have sent extremely wrong messages to the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities. These are the latest moves from the US that violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués.\nThese attempts to contain China with Taiwan interfere in China's internal affairs and undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. They are completely wrong and extremely dangerous.\nThe US should realize that China must and will be reunified, and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation must and will be achieved.\nWe can always seek wisdom from the past to enlighten the days to come. The past has proved that both China and the US would gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. In the future, a community with a shared future and diversity is the only prospect for human development.\nWe hope that the US can abandon the Cold War mindset and zero-sum concept, view China-US relationship and the military-to-military relationship in a rational way, stop the negative words and deeds, and do meaningful things to improve bilateral ties and mil-mil relationship and protect the common interests of China and the US.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2020-08/01/content_4869055.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-07-30","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","We have noticed that the US and the Taiwan region have been continuously strengthening military exchanges recently. The US Department of State has just approved a new arms sale to Taiwan worth 620 million US dollars, which was acclaimed as a helpful move to “maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the region” by Taiwan’s defense authorities. At the same time, a promotional video of the US Special…","In regard to the US announcement of a new round of arms sales to Taiwan, China has stated its solemn position and imposed sanctions on Lockheed Martin, the main contractor of the arms sale.\nThe US sending military personnel to Taiwan for exercises and exchanges has seriously violated the fundamental principles of international relations and the political commitment the US has made to China. It has a severe negative impact on bilateral relations and mil-mil relationship between China and the US, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It has sent a wrong message to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and is a deliberate provocation. The Chinese side has expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to it and has lodged solemn representations to the US side. We urge the US side to immediately correct its mistake, stop its official and military contacts of any form with Taiwan, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and promise that no similar incident would occur again.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. The future of Taiwan lies in reunification and the welfare of the Taiwan compatriots lies in national rejuvenation. There is no way out for Taiwan to bank on foreign support, and it is doomed to be futile for the US to contain China with Taiwan. We have the firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to thwart any form of external interference and separatist attempts for \"Taiwan independence\". And we will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2020-08/01/content_4869055.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-07-30","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the Japanese government issued the Defense of Japan 2020 (Annual White Paper), claiming that China's military development lacks transparency, China has unilaterally changed the status quo in the East China Sea and the South China Sea, and China has used anti-pandemic assistance as a pretext to seek its own political interests. It also described the cross-Strait relations as “China-Taiwan” relations.…","On July 14, the Japanese side released the Defense of Japan 2020 white paper and its contents related to China are inconsistent with facts. The white paper made irresponsible remarks on China’s national defense and military development and exaggerated the so-called military threat of China. It distorted facts and discredited China on issues such as the South China Sea, the East China Sea and China’s pandemic response, and made extremely irresponsible remarks on the Taiwan question. We are strongly dissatisfied and firmly opposed to these contents and have lodged solemn representations to the Japanese side.\nAt present, China-Japan relationship is in a critical period of improvement and development. We urge the Japanese side to take history as a mirror and look to the future, and stop making wrong remarks. Following the strategic consensus reached by the leaders of the two countries, the Japanese side should work with the Chinese side towards the same goal, jointly promote a constructive bilateral security relationship, and make positive efforts to enhance mutual political and security trust, safeguard regional peace and stability, and promote the continuous improvement and development of China-Japan relationship.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2020-08/01/content_4869055.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-07-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 30 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 30th in response to questions that Mr. Mao Zhulun, former chairman of the Chinese Unification Promotion Alliance, and Mr. Wang Xiaobo, former vice chairman and former editor-in-chief of the Straits Review, held a sense of national righteousness and steadfastly promoted the reunification of the motherland, and their firm opposition to “Taiwan independence” is admirable. We express our deep sorrow at their passing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200730_12288323.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-07-31","Wang Wenbin","NHK","US Secretary of State Pompeo released a statement yesterday offering condolences on the passing of Lee Teng-hui on behalf of the American people. Do you have a response to that?","I noticed the news. Taiwan independence is a dead end. No individual or force could hold back the historical trend of reunification and revitalization of the Chinese nation. We urge the relevant country to adhere to the one-China principle, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid sending out any wrong signal to Taiwan independence forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1803070.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202007/t20200731_5419185.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-07-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 31 electronic dispatch: Regarding the death of Lee Teng-hui, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 31st: I have seen this news. I want to stress that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that cannot succeed. The historical trend of national reunification and national rejuvenation cannot be blocked by anyone or any force!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202007/t20200731_12288361.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Mr. Wang Xiaobo, former Vice Chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Unification Alliance and a well-known scholar, has passed away, and the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed condolences that same day. What is the assessment of Mr. Wang Xiaobo's role in the development of cross-Strait relations? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response when answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 3rd that Mr. Wang Xiaobo, former vice chairman of the Taiwan China Unification League, passed away on July 30, 2020, after his illness proved beyond medical treatment. The Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office once again express deep mourning.\nMa Xiaoguang said that Mr. Wang Xiaobo was a loyal patriot, an outstanding representative of Taiwan compatriots, and an outstanding leader and theorist and social activist in the Taiwan compatriot patriotic unification camp. Born into a family of revolutionary martyrs, he unswervingly promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the peaceful reunification of the motherland, firmly opposed “Taiwan independence,” firmly opposed foreign forces interfering in China's internal affairs, tirelessly pursued social progress and fairness and justice, and devoted his life to the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation. His lofty convictions and patriotic devotion will inspire compatriots on both sides of the Strait to keep striving to complete the great cause of reunifying the nation and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. I must once again stress that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that cannot be traversed. National reunification and national rejuvenation are the trend of history and the will of the people, and no person or force can stop them. All patriotic and unification forces will be inscribed on the historical monument of national reunification and national rejuvenation, and all “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will be drowned in the historical torrent of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200803_12288789.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-05","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","The American Institute in Taiwan said on August 5 that Health and Human Services Secretary Alex Azar is going to lead a delegation to visit Taiwan in the coming days. Do you have any comment?","China firmly opposes any official interactions between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. China has made stern representations with the US side both in Beijing and in Washington.\nFor the China-US relationship, the Taiwan question is one of the utmost importance with the highest level of sensitivity, and the one-China principle is the political foundation. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, stop making official interactions of any kind with Taiwan, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, and not to send any wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" elements to avoid severe damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. I want to stress that the one-China principle is universally recognized by the international community. Any attempt to ignore, deny or challenge that principle is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202008/t20200805_693322.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202008/t20200805_5419200.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 5 dispatch: In response to reports that US Secretary of Health and Human Services Azar would visit Taiwan in the near future, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 5th in response to a question: The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external force is allowed to interfere. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose official exchanges between the United States and the Taiwan region of China.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing and willing to serve as pawns, colluding with the US side to obtain political self-interest and damaging the common interests of compatriots on both sides, are very dangerous and will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200805_12289091.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-06","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Regarding the US Health and Human Services Secretary Alex Azar's upcoming visit to Taiwan, we are wondering if China plans any measures in response to this?","I stated China's position yesterday. China firmly opposes any official interactions between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, and stop making official interactions of any kind with Taiwan. Any attempt to ignore, deny or challenge the one-China principle is doomed to fail. China will take firm countermeasures in response to the US wrong move.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1804582.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 6 — Taiwan’s education authorities recently announced the reopening of Taiwan to some overseas students for study, but excluded students from the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the mainland was obstructing mainland students from returning to Taiwan. TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on this on the 6th, saying that the statements by the DPP authorities are completely fabricated and have ulterior motives.\nMa Xiaoguang said that since the outbreak of the epidemic, we have attached great importance to the problem of mainland students being blocked from returning to Taiwan to study, supported mainland students in safeguarding their legitimate rights and interests, and promptly helped resolve practical problems related to mainland students going to Taiwan. However, for political self-interest, the DPP authorities have consistently adopted discriminatory measures specifically targeting mainland students studying in Taiwan, used various pretexts to engage in political manipulation, and repeatedly created obstacles to block mainland students from returning to Taiwan to study. On August 5, the DPP authorities announced the reopening of Taiwan to overseas students other than fresh graduates, yet excluded mainland students alone. This once again seriously harmed the legitimate rights and interests of mainland students.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities’ vicious conduct of hurting the feelings of compatriots and creating cross-Strait confrontation has already drawn questioning and criticism from public opinion on the island. Their practice of slander and malicious discrimination will ultimately only backfire on themselves. We advise the DPP authorities to face public opinion squarely and genuinely respect and safeguard the legitimate rights of mainland students to study in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200806_12289282.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-07","Wang Wenbin","TASS","My question is about US Health and Human Services Secretary Alex Azar's visit to Taiwan. It would be the highest level trip since 1979. My question is what China's response could be if the US will continue such official contacts with Taipei?","I took a similar question yesterday. We urge the US to correct its mistake, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and stop official ties with Taiwan in any form. China will take firm countermeasures in response the wrongdoing of the US side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1804839.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1804743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-07","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","On your first question, is there any updates on visa extension for Chinese journalists in the US? The Foreign Correspondents' Club of Hong Kong issued a statement on June 6, calling on the Chinese and US governments not to use journalists' visas as a weapon in dealing with international disputes. Do you have any comment? Second question, it is reported that the US plans to sell arms to Taiwan again, this time at…","As for what's been going on in the media sector between China and the US, the facts and the right and wrong cannot be clearer. The US side provoked first, and China only took necessary and reciprocal countermeasures to the US unreasonable suppression of the Chinese media outlets working in the US. What China has done is legitimate and justified self defense. The US has been ratcheting up its pressure on the Chinese media from registering them as \"foreign agents\" to enlisting them as \"foreign missions\", from refusing visas to more than 20 Chinese journalists to imposing de facto expulsion on Chinese journalists working in the US. And now, its discriminatory and restrictive visa policy means that all the Chinese journalists stationed in the US, including those stationed in the UN, can only have visas with a validity length of 3 months, thus causing great disruption and inconvenience to their normal reporting there.\nThe US side should immediately redress its mistakes, stop its political discrimination and unjustified suppression against Chinese media and journalists, and guarantee that the safety, property, press freedom and other legitimate rights and interests of these Chinese journalists will not be violated and their normal reporting activities not affected. If the US refuses to correct its course and insists on taking more wrong steps, China is faced with no other choice but doing what is necessary and legitimate to safeguard its rights and interests.\nThat said, China's commitment to the basic state policy of opening-up has not changed and will never change. We welcome media from all over the world, including those from the US, to work and report in China in accordance with laws and regulations, and we will continue to assist them in doing their job here.\nRegarding your second question, US arms sales to Taiwan seriously breach the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communique, which severely undermines China's sovereignty and security interests, and gravely violates basic norms of international relations. China firmly opposes this.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. China has firm resolve in upholding its sovereignty and security. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan, lest it should gravely harm China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1804839.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1804743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-10","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","Alex Azar, the United States Health and Human Services Secretary, arrived in Taiwan and kicked off his visit yesterday. He met with Tsai Ing-wen this morning and plans to meet more officials. What is your comment?","China consistently and firmly opposes any official interactions between the US and Taiwan and has made stern representations with the US side over this issue.\nI'd like to reiterate that for the China-US relationship, the Taiwan question is one of the utmost importance with the highest level of sensitivity, and the one-China principle is its political foundation. What the US has done contravened its own promises on the question. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three joint communiques, stop having official interactions of any kind with Taiwan, make no attempts to change the nature of its relationship with Taiwan, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly to avoid severe damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346856.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1805214.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-10","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","First question, you just announced some sanctions against US officials. Are they effective today? Second question, Hong Kong media tycoon Jimmy Lai was arrested today in Hong Kong under the national security law for suspected collusion with foreign forces. Can the foreign ministry specify in what ways did Lai collude with foreign forces? Third question, Chinese fighter jets crossed the median line of the Taiwan…","On your first question, these sanctions take effect as of today.\nOn your second question, Hong Kong is governed by rule of law. We support SAR law enforcement authorities in discharging their duties in accordance with law.\nOn your third question, I would refer you to the defense department.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346856.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1805214.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 10 dispatch: In response to remarks by the DPP authorities and some political forces on the island about the Hong Kong SAR police’s lawful arrest of Jimmy Lai and others, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 10th, said that the DPP authorities have long meddled in Hong Kong affairs, supported and incited black violence forces, and viciously attacked “one country, two systems,” with the aim of disrupting Hong Kong and seeking “independence.” It is only natural for the Hong Kong SAR government to handle lawbreakers according to law, and interference will not be tolerated. Any conduct that violates the Hong Kong National Security Law will surely be subject to legal accountability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200810_12289734.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-12","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","US Health and Human Services Secretary Alex Azar said in a speech at National Taiwan University on August 11: \"The Chinese Communist Party had the chance to warn the world and work with the world on battling the virus. But they chose not to...the People's Republic of China did not live up to the binding obligations it had under the International Health Regulations, betraying the cooperative spirit we need for…","We must repeat this solemn message to the US side again that China firmly opposes official exchanges between the US and Taiwan under whatever pretext. On issues concerning China's core interests, certain individuals in the US must not have any illusions or imagine they can get away with inappropriate behaviors. Those playing with fire will end up burning themselves badly.\nWe also remind the DPP authorities in Taiwan to stop pursuing its misguided course. A dead end will meet them if they so willingly choose to act like self-important puppets with strings in foreign hands and seriously believe that they have a chance at independence by taking advantage of the epidemic.\nWith regard to COVID-19, we've released the timeline showing clearly China's effective response. Since the very beginning of the outbreak, China has been acting in an open, transparent, and responsible manner and earnestly fulfilling its duties and obligations under the International Health Regulations. With the most comprehensive, stringent, and thorough measures, we contained the spread of the virus while engaging in international cooperation in prevention and control. Putting people and life front and center, the Chinese government's epidemic response can stand the test of time and history. China's tremendous sacrifice for and contribution to the global fight has been witnessed by all.\nTurning to the US, confirmed cases passed five million and deaths over 160,000. In the face of such a grave situation, the principal US health official, instead of manning the front-line and devoting himself entirely to bringing the virus under control, has walked out on the millions of people suffering at home, all for a political posturing faraway in Taiwan. I wonder if this official knew that during his three-day visit, more than 150,000 new cases were confirmed in the US and over 2,000 lives lost. Their ridiculous stunts this time just make us more convinced that for them, American people's lives are nothing compared with their selfish political gains.\nSecretary Azar, I'm afraid, is directly responsible for the unchecked spreading of the epidemic in the US. We wonder why he is so blatant to even speak ill of China's anti-epidemic efforts. If he entered a world competition of \"who performed the worst in managing this epidemic\", he will almost surely come out on top. He lashed out against China because he wanted to make China a scapegoat to cover for US officials' incompetence. Stopping these political shows and focusing on saving American lives, this is what he should do as the health secretary. Azar claimed that if this virus had emerged in a place like the United States, it might have been snuffed out easily. We can't wait to see him working wonders and bringing the epidemic situation at home under control as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1805964.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1805875.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-12","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","A question regarding the proposed visit by the mayor of Prague to Taiwan. He will be joined by the Czech senate president. Do you have any comment on the proposed visit?","China consistently opposes official exchanges between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China.\nI also want to stress that the renewal and reunification of the Chinese nation is an unstoppable trend. Anyone who attempts to resist this trend and to split China is doomed to fail and their names will go down in history as anathema.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1805964.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1805875.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 12: In response to reports that U.S. Health and Human Services Secretary Azar met with Tsai Ing-wen during his visit to Taiwan, and that Taiwan and the United States signed a so-called “Memorandum of Understanding on Health Care Cooperation,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 12th in response to a question: Secretary Azar's visit to Taiwan violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose it. The DPP authorities are using this to make political capital, “using the epidemic to seek independence,” which is nothing but a farce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200812_12290008.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-08-12","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 12 — In response to the unwarranted accusations made on the 12th by the leader of the DPP authorities regarding the National Security Law for Hong Kong and the measures the HKSAR government has taken in accordance with the law, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated in reply to questions: The formulation and implementation of the Hong Kong National Security Law, and the HKSAR government's taking of measures against lawbreakers in accordance with the law, aim to crack down on illegal and criminal activities, safeguard the rule of law and order, prosperity and stability in Hong Kong, uphold the country's sovereignty, security and development interests, protect the freedom and human rights of the broad Hong Kong public, and safeguard the long-term stable operation of “one country, two systems.” This is a just act, lawful and reasonable.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, under various banners and in the name of various pretexts, have meddled in Hong Kong affairs, supported and colluded with “Hong Kong independence” forces and disruptive elements, and incited, and even participated in, activities that undermine Hong Kong's prosperity and stability and split the country. The relevant remarks of the DPP authorities once again expose their evil intentions: so-called democracy and freedom are false, while disrupting Hong Kong and pursuing “independence” are real. We advise the DPP authorities to immediately stop their political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs and not to go further down the dead end of disrupting Hong Kong and pursuing “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200812_12290009.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-08-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 12th, DPP authority leaders delivered a pre-recorded speech at a video conference hosted by a US think tank, claiming in the name of “liberty and democracy” that they would strengthen Taiwan-US relations. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response when answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 13 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 13th in response to questions: Taiwan is part of China, and we firmly oppose any countries that have diplomatic relations with China developing official relations with the Taiwan region. For a long time, the DPP authorities have used some non-governmental organization platforms, under the guise of “democracy and freedom,” to maliciously attack the mainland, recklessly undermine cross-Strait relations, and create hostility and hatred among compatriots on both sides. This conduct of serving as a pawn of Western anti-China forces and harming the interests of compatriots on both sides is contemptible, and it is even harder to use to deceive the world and gain a false reputation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200813_12290192.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-14","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","The Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People's Liberation Army has recently carried out combat exercises. From the Foreign Ministry's standpoint, what signals do you think such exercises have sent out?","The Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Eastern Theater Command has already issued a press release on their exercises. I can give you some information.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Eastern Theater Command recently systematically sent troops from multiple military branches into multiple directions and organized consecutive, realistic drills in the Taiwan Straits and its northern and southern ends. The drills further tested and improved the troops' joint combat capability. Recently, a certain major country has been continuously making negative moves on the Taiwan question, which has sent seriously wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces and severely threatened peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits. Taiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of Chinese territory, and the patrol and exercise activities by the PLA are necessary operations aimed at the current security situation in the region and safeguarding national sovereignty. The troops will always be on high alert, take any necessary measures, resolutely counter any provocative actions that could result in \"Taiwan independence\" and separate the country, and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1806529.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202008/t20200814_5419235.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-17","Zhao Lijian","AFP","First, do you have any comment on Taiwan finalizing a deal to buy dozens of F-16 fighter jets from the US? Second, police in Nigeria said that four Chinese workers have been freed after they were kidnapped from a quarry. Do you have any details on the kidnapping and the rescue process?","On your first question, China consistently and firmly opposes US arms sales to Taiwan. US arms sales to Taiwan seriously breach the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. It severely undermines China's sovereignty and security interests and gravely violates the basic norms of international relations. China stated its solemn position and made a firm response after the US announced the sale of 66 F-16V fighter jets to Taiwan in August 2019.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. China has firm resolve in upholding its sovereignty and security. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan, lest it should gravely harm China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability.\nWith regard to your second question, on August 15 local time, with the joint efforts of relevant parties, four kidnapped Chinese nationals in Nigeria were rescued. China will continue to take all necessary measures to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of our citizens overseas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1806940.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1806917.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-18","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Do you have any response on Taiwan opening a representative office in Somaliland?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community. China firmly opposes the establishment of official institutions or any form of official exchanges between Taiwan and Somaliland. The Democratic Progressive Party's frantic search of support for its separatist activities in the international arena will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1807193.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1807178.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-19","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Youth Daily","On August 18, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Federal Republic of Somalia condemned in a statement Taiwan's attempts to infringe on the sovereignty of Somali and violate its territorial integrity. It has been reported earlier that Taiwan's representative office in Somaliland has been officially inaugurated. What's China's comment?","The DPP authorities' pursuit of its separatist agenda on the international stage has no chance of success and will be despised by the world. I stress once again: there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm of international relations and a consensus of the international community. Here is a word of advice for whom it may concern: don't make the mistake of seeking wiggle room where there is none. Those going against the trend to challenge the one-China principle will get burned and swallow the bitter fruit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1807490.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1807468.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-20","Zhao Lijian","AFP","First, US President Trump called Jimmy Lai \"a brave man\" and expressed his support for Jimmy Lai who was briefly detained last week under the Hong Kong national security law. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment? Second, officials in Taiwan said that Chinese hackers infiltrated at least ten \"government agencies\" in Taiwan and gained access to around 6,000 email accounts attempting to steal data. What is…","On your first question, the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council has issued remarks on the Hong Kong police's lawful detention of the pertinent personnel. China is a country ruled by law, and Hong Kong is a society upholding the rule of law. The SAR law enforcement authorities fulfill their duties according to law. There's no room for any doubt.\nOn your second question, the DPP authorities' accusation is nothing but a vicious slander to instigate cross-strait confrontation and to seek political gains out of selfish motives.\nI'd like to tell you that China is a staunch defender of cyber security and also one of the victims of cyber attacks. In accordance with law, we've been cracking down on such attacks launched inside China or using China's cyber infrastructure. Our position on this issue is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1807885.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202008/t20200820_5419255.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-20","Zhao Lijian","AFP","There was a photo of Chinese Ambassador to Kiribati at a local welcoming ceremony circulating online. US and Australian officials have either criticized or expressed surprise over the move. Can you confirm when and where this incident took place? Do you have a response to comments circulating about the photo?","I noted relevant reports and comments and worked to verify the reports. I believe what really deserves attention is the comments by the people of Kiribati. At the invitation of the council and MPs of Marakei Island in Kiribati, Chinese Ambassador to Kiribati Tang Songgen paid a visit to the island. This is the first visit by a Chinese ambassador after the two countries resumed diplomatic relations in September 2019. The local government and people received the ambassador with a warm welcome. Out of respect for the local culture and customs, Ambassador Tang eventually accepted and attended the traditional welcoming ceremony the gracious host insisted on. Many people on the Marakei Island expressed their firm support for the resumption of ties when interacting with Ambassador Tang. This illustrates the fact that resumption of relations is an irresistible trend with popular support.\nDifferent countries have different traditional customs. As Marakei Island MPs, Kiribati's minister for agriculture and others have explained, the pictured welcoming ritual with the most humble posture is a traditional way to pay the highest respect to distinguished visitors, which has been passed down from generation to generation on the island. It was the joint decision by the council of elders, the island council and the local church to welcome Ambassador Tang with this ceremony. Back in 1998, when the then Australian high commissioner to Kiribati visited the island, local people welcomed him with the same ceremony. The Kiribati side is infuriated that some Australians smeared China and deliberately omitted their knowledge of the unique customs on each island of Kiribati. As for the reports you mentioned, among those releasing the photo is Drew Pavlou, who has been pursuing an anti-China agenda out of political motivations.\nChina always believes that all countries are equal regardless of size. In exchanges with Pacific Island countries, China fully respects their local culture and customs and practices the saying of \"a guest should suit the convenience of the host.\" I'm sure you've noticed that many in Kiribati and other Pacific Island countries have spoken up on social media to appreciate the Chinese ambassador's respect for the local customs and condemn the few people who deliberately misrepresent local culture and attempt to sow discord between China and Kiribati. Some netizens criticized certain few people for having taken money from Taiwan and posting pictures and comments online with ulterior motives to drive a wedge between China and Kiribati. When confronted by facts, malicious smears on China's policy towards island countries and attempts to sabotage their relations are bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1807885.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202008/t20200820_5419255.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-21","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","During the US Democratic National Convention which was closed on Thursday night, the Democratic shared their 2020 Party Platform for the upcoming US election. In a change from their 2016 Party Platform, they did not include endorsement for the one-China principle. Given the Republican administration has also taken a hard line on China and Taiwan, is China concerned that this could represent a toughest stance on…","China has repeatedly made clear our position on the US presidential elections. On the matter you mentioned, China's position on Taiwan remains consistent and clear. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue between China and the US. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and a common consensus of the international community. We urge relevant side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.\nChina hopes that the Democratic and Republican parties in the US can view China and China-US relations in an objective way, and work with China to advance China-US relations featuring coordination, cooperation and stability, which serves the common interests of people in China, the US and the whole world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1808069.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1808053.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: It is reported that the DPP authorities will further strictly review and restrict mainland capital investment in Taiwan, and will also prohibit Taiwan operators from acting as agents or distributors for mainland OTT and related commercial services. What comments do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 21 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 21st, pointing out that for some time, the DPP authorities have, through various pretexts and means, deliberately manipulated “anti-China” populism and have increasingly undermined cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. Now they are following Western anti-China forces in further obstructing mainland capital investment in Taiwan and prohibiting Taiwan businesses from cooperating with relevant mainland enterprises, creating cross-Strait “decoupling.” This again exposes their true face of undermining cross-Strait relations and harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nHe also pointed out that cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation is a lifeline benefiting compatriots on both sides, bringing tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, the mainland has been the first to resume work and production, effectively driving cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and becoming a key factor in Taiwan's economic development. From January to July this year, cross-Strait trade totaled US$134.94 billion, a year-on-year increase of 8.7%, and Taiwan's trade surplus exceeded US$70 billion. Mainland enterprises employ nearly 25,000 workers in Taiwan and pay more than NT$1.2 billion in taxes each year. The conduct of the DPP authorities cannot change the broad trend of integrated economic and social development across the Taiwan Strait; it will only compress Taiwan's development space, cut off its development opportunities, and damage the interests and well-being of the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200821_12291497.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-24","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Brent Christensen, the head of the American Institute in Taiwan and the de-facto US representative to the island, took part in a commemoration of the anniversary of the 1958 \"Taiwan Strait crisis\" on Sunday and talked about the history of security cooperation between the US and Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this?","China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. The so-called history of security cooperation between the US and the Taiwan region is nothing but an infamous track record of interfering in China's internal affairs and obstructing China's reunification. The 1.4 billion Chinese people knows that record all too well.\nWe urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and three China-US joint communiques, stop pulling petty tricks to change the substance of its relationship with Taiwan, stop thin-ice skating on the Taiwan question, and stop sending out misleading signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. It is the China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait that are at high stakes here.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1808713.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1808692.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The Taipei office of the “American Institute in Taiwan” took part in the commemorative activities for the “823” Artillery Battle in Kinmen organized by the Taiwan side, describing security cooperation as an important part of the US-Taiwan partnership. Tsai Ing-wen claimed that “peace relies on solid defense” and that she will not retreat in defending “sovereignty.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 24 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 24th in response to questions: Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question absolutely does not allow external forces to interfere. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers and escalating provocations by depending on external forces, will only harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides, endanger the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and place Taiwan in an even more dangerous position. We demand that the U.S. abide by the One China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop repeatedly sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200824_12291955.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-26","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","It is reported that Taiwan authorities plan to open a new representative office in Aix-en-Provence in Southern France, which they say is aimed at fostering cooperation between Taiwan and France and other European countries in culture, tourism, business, innovation, and education. What is China's comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. China firmly opposes any country having diplomatic ties with China making any form of official contact and exchanges with Taiwan, including the establishment of official institutions in each other's places. France should abide by the one-China principle and prudently and properly handle issues related to Taiwan. The attempts of the DPP authorities to carry out separatist activities in the international arena will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1809457.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1809439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-27","Zhao Lijian","NHK","Speaker of the upper house of the Czech Parliament will visit Taiwan soon and meet with President Tsai Ing-wen. Do you have any comment?","First I need to correct you on one point. We only recognize the person you mentioned as the leader of the Taiwan region.\nChina firmly opposes any form of official exchanges between countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. Despite China's solemn representation and Czech's mainstream public opinion and official stance on the one-China policy, this politician, in pursuit of self-interest, insisted on making this so-called \"visit\" to the Taiwan region, which constitutes a deliberate sabotage of the political basis for bilateral relations. China condemns such despicable behavior and urges the Czech side to abide by the one-China principle and correctly and prudently handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1809870.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1809844.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-08-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US and the Taiwan authorities have been interacting frequently this month. The US Secretary of Health and Human Services arrived in Taiwan for certain activities, the USS Mustin (DDG 89) passed through the Taiwan Strait, and US military aircraft increased the frequency of provocative activities in waters around. What's your comment, please?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. China resolutely opposes any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist actions and any form of official exchanges and military ties between the US and the Taiwan region. This position is clear.\nRecently, the PLA Eastern Theater Command has deployed troops from multiple military services and arms and organized real-combat exercises along the Taiwan Strait, targeting external interference and a small group of \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist forces and their separatist activities. China will take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-08/28/content_4870290.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-08-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media in Taiwan reported that the US Department of Defense recently announced a 10-year military sales order with a total value of US $62 billion, possibly including a sale deal of 66 F-16V Viper fighter jets to Taiwan. What's your comment?","China firmly opposes the US arms sale to Taiwan. The arms sale has been a major issue harming the relations between the two countries and militaries, and undermining regional peace and stability.\nOn this issue, China's position is clear. After the US announced the sale of 66 F-16V Viper fighter jets to Taiwan last year, China immediately stated its firm opposition. If the US insists on executing the new round of arms sales to Taiwan, China will take all necessary measures to resolutely counteract.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-08/28/content_4870290.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-08-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 27 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 27th, introduced that on August 15, the centralized events of the 8th Straits Youth Festival, co-hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the All-China Youth Federation and the Fujian Provincial Government, were officially launched in Fuzhou. This is the largest cross-Strait youth exchange activity since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic. It built a platform for cross-Strait youth exchange, interaction, heart-to-heart communication and integration, and continued to demonstrate the appeal and strong brand effect of the Straits Youth Festival.\nMa Xiaoguang summarized three main features of the 8th Straits Youth Festival:\nFirst, the format of the activities was innovative. This year’s festival took “Happiness · Home · Dreams” as its theme, and explored an innovative “online + offline” model. Using the internet as a medium, it carefully designed 14 activities, with a focus on four online exchange events: the “Cloud Summit,” “Cloud Cheer,” “Cloud Live Stream” and “Cloud Tour of the Strait.” The “Cloud Summit” had its main venue in Fuzhou and sub-venues in Wuhan, Kunshan, Xiamen, Pingtan and Taipei. The activities made extensive use of video links, Douyin interaction, live-stream sharing and other methods to carry out broad-coverage, real-time, interactive and sustainable cross-Strait youth exchanges.\nSecond, the practical results were more prominent. This year’s festival provided job matching and quality services for Taiwan youth coming to Fujian for employment and entrepreneurship. During the event, the first Fujian-Taiwan Talent Cooperation Forum released 2,349 positions for Taiwan youth. Trendy new economic formats such as live-stream sales were incorporated into the activities for the first time. Using a combined “online + offline” format, the activities overcame the limits of time and space imposed by the pandemic and deepened cross-Strait youth exchanges. An epidemic prevention plan was formulated, and a three-party joint epidemic prevention and control mechanism involving the “event organizers,” “venues” and “hotels” was established to ensure the activities were safe and orderly.\nThird, the topics of exchange drew strong attention. This year’s festival drew attention from more than 60 million people. The “Cloud Summit” reached over 72.68 million views across the internet, the “Cloud Cheer” coastal live-stream session was watched by 3.2 million people on both sides of the Strait, and the “Cloud Tour of the Strait” recorded a total of 22.65 million reads. Some 230 journalists from more than 40 media outlets in the Straits, across both sides of the Strait and Hong Kong, reported on the Straits Youth Festival across all platforms, including Toutiao, Douyin, Facebook, Twitter and various media news apps. The “Media Trip to Fuzhou” activity launched a special series of reports titled “Straits Youth Stories,” encouraging and supporting more Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to develop. As of August 25, the total number of reads of festival news reached 37 million, and video views exceeded 73 million.\nRelated activities of this year’s festival are still ongoing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200827_12292606.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-28","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The American Institute in Taiwan today released a photo of a Taiwanese fighter jet refueling midair from an American Air Force tanker. I wonder if you have any comment?","I haven't read reports on that. Our position is consistent and clear: we firmly oppose military ties and cooperation between the US and the Taiwan region. We urge the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, strictly observe the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, properly handle Taiwan-related matters and stop sending erroneous signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatists.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1810182.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1810179.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 28: Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office stated in response to questions on the 28th that the DPP authorities, disregarding public opposition, insisted on opening the import of problematic US agricultural and livestock products for political purposes. This harms the health and well-being of the island's residents, and uses this to trade for external forces' support for “Taiwan independence” forces. It will inevitably meet with resolute opposition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200828_12292782.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","US National Security Adviser O'Brien criticized China on issues related to China's political system, Taiwan, Hong Kong and the South China Sea during an online event at the Atlantic Council on August 28, and advocated using the US alliance system to deal with \"challenges\" from China and Russia. What is China's response?","For some time, some US politicians, out of a zero-sum mentality, the Cold-War mindset and selfish political interests, have been viciously attacking China's political system, smearing China, and sowing discord between other countries and China. China is firmly opposed to this.\nThe Chinese people know the best and have the best say on whether socialism with Chinese characteristics is good or not. It is not up to US politicians to judge. As to whether China's development is an opportunity or a threat to the world, the answer is self-evident in the fact that China is the largest trading partner of more than 130 countries and regions and China has active exchanges and cooperation with others. When we look at the United States, it has been doing the opposite, arbitrarily withdrawing from international agreements and organizations and cherry-picking on international law, which has seriously undermined international fairness and justice as well as global peace, stability and development. In fact, the international community will not follow suit as they are well aware of the practices of US politicians to spread rumors on China, hype up the \"China threat\" and attempt to hijack other countries onto its \"anti-Communist and anti-China chariot\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202008/t20200831_693359.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1810690.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","A delegation from the Czech Republic led by the Senate speaker Milos Vystrcil is visiting Taiwan. In response to that, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said the Chinese government and people, instead of sitting idly by, will make them pay a heavy price for the short-sighted behaviors and political speculation. I wonder what measures China will take as a response?","We express strong condemnation and grave concerns over the egregious practices of anti-China forces in the Czech Republic who deliberately violate China's sovereignty and blatantly interfere in China's internal affairs. Like you said, as State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi explicitly stated yesterday in Germany, Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory, and those who challenge the one-China principle on the Taiwan question are walking away from international commitments and making themselves enemies of the 1.4 billion Chinese people. Facing provocations from the Czech Senate speaker and the anti-China forces behind him, the Chinese government and people won't sit idly by; they shall pay a heavy price for their short-sighted behaviors and political opportunism.\nWe urge the relevant authorities of the Czech Republic to immediately take measures to eliminate the negative impact of this erroneous practice, so as to avoid damaging the big picture of bilateral relations. We also solemnly inform the Taiwan authorities and the anti-China forces behind Vystrcil: your acts cannot alter the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and your attempts of political manipulation and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202008/t20200831_693359.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1810690.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-08-31","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 31 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 31st in response to a question: In less than two weeks, Shanghai has successively recorded three confirmed COVID-19 cases imported from Taiwan. The frequency has drawn high attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait and raised concerns among people on both sides about Taiwan's epidemic prevention and control. How large the loopholes in Taiwan's COVID-19 prevention and control still are, how many actual infections there are, and how much risk compatriots on the island face: these issues, which concern the health and life safety of compatriots on the island, cannot be ignored.\nMa said: Epidemic prevention and control concerns the lives and health of the people, and any negligence or falsehood will cost the public dearly. We earnestly urge the DPP authorities to genuinely take responsibility, handle epidemic prevention and control with a professional attitude, and cut off the chain of virus transmission. The health and lives of people on the island are no child's play, and they must not become sacrificial victims of political window-dressing.\nAccording to reports, on the 30th the Shanghai Municipal Health Commission reported one confirmed COVID-19 case imported from Taiwan, the third such case reported since the cases on August 19 and August 24.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202008/t20200831_12293244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-09-01","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News","Czech Senate speaker who is on a visit to Taiwan delivered a speech at the \"parliament\", in which he claimed visiting Taiwan is a correct decision. What's your comment?","China's position on the visit by the President of the Czech Senate is very clear. Vice Foreign Minister Qin Gang summoned the Czech Republic Ambassador to China and lodged stern representations over Czech Senate President Milos Vystrcil's visit to Taiwan.\nTempted by the Taiwan authority, instigated by anti-China forces and driven by selfish gains, Vystrcil insists on visiting the Taiwan region regardless of China's firm opposition and solemn representations. This is open support for \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities and has severely infringed upon China's sovereignty and flagrantly interfered in China's domestic affairs. China strongly condemns the move.\nThere is only one China in the world, and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing the whole of China, which is recognized by the international community. The one-China principle is the Czech Republic's foreign policy and the political basis for China-Czech ties. Vystrcil, as one of the country's leaders, has openly broken international consensus and breached the one-China principle which the Czech government has promised to uphold, severely violating international law and basic norms of international relations. China shall take necessary actions to safeguard its legitimate interests.\nWe urge those who openly challenge China's sovereignty out of selfish interest to heed China's solemn position and grave concerns, and not to underestimate the firm resolve of the 1.4 billion Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and security. We also call on the Czech people to jointly prevent further harm to China-Czech relations caused by Vystrcil's malicious and shortsighted behavior.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1811140.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-01","Hua Chunying","CCTV","US Assistant Secretary of State David R. Stilwell told a virtual forum hosted by the Heritage Foundation that for nearly four decades, US has been guided by the Taiwan Relations Act of 1979, the three joint communiqués between Washington and Beijing, and the Six Assurances provided by President Reagan to Taipei in 1982. The US has declassified the Reagan-era Six Assurances to Taiwan and they endure today. The…","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is the political foundation and fundamental premise for the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and the US. The so-called Taiwan Relations Act unilaterally promulgated by the US and its so-called Six Assurances to Taiwan severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously breach the basic norms governing international relations and grossly interfere in China's internal affairs. They are completely wrong, illegal, null and void, and the Chinese government is firmly opposed to them right from the start. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, rather than the Taiwan Relations Act or the Six Assurances.\nI want to stress that the Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and China's core interests. No one should underestimate China's firm determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués between China and the US, make no attempts to change the nature of its relationship with Taiwan, stop conducting any official exchange with Taiwan, and refrain from moving further down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1811140.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The “American Institute in Taiwan” released “declassified telegrams” mentioning the so-called “Six Assurances,” and the DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 1 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 1st in response to questions that the so-called “Six Assurances” put forward by the U.S. side seriously violate the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués and the U.S. side's commitment to the one-China principle, and are illegal and null and void. We firmly oppose this. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing to assert themselves and on the U.S. to seek “independence,” are no different from drinking poison to quench thirst, and will inevitably reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200901_12293414.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-09-02","Hua Chunying","NHK","Taiwan media report that the Taiwan authorities will have the \"Taiwan\" and \"Taiwan passport\" printed bigger on the new \"passport\" cover. Does China have any comment?","No matter what tricks the DPP authorities play, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346873.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1811463.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-03","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News","First question, according to Japanese media reports, a Japanese press photographer was recently arrested in Hong Kong. It is said the photographer is a Hong Kong resident, and the Japanese government acknowledged this. Can you confirm it and give us more details? Second question, Taiwan \"president\" Tsai Ing-wen met with the Czech senate president today in Taipei. Do you have any comment?","On your first question, I'm not aware of that.\nOn your second question regarding the Czech senate president's visit to Taiwan, we have made clear China's position in the past few days. The Czech senate president, in disregard of opposition from China and the Czech government, insistently visited China's Taiwan region and outrageously supported the \"Taiwan independence\" forces, which is an open provocation. The one-China policy is an important political basis of the establishment and development of China-Czech diplomatic ties. We noticed that the Czech government also drew a line between them and the senate president, noting that what he has done doesn't represent the government's policy. We hope the Czech side can have a clear understanding of the damage he has caused to bilateral relations, and immediately take measures to eliminate the negative impact.\nWe solemnly inform the Taiwan authorities and the anti-China forces behind Vystrcil: your acts cannot alter the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and your attempts of political manipulation and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities will never succeed.\nI also want to correct you that when you mention Tsai Ing-wen in the future, please don't refer to her as the Taiwan \"president\". She's merely a leader in China's Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1812001.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1811894.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-07","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","President Milos Zeman of the Czech Republic said in an interview on September 6 that the supreme constitutional leaders' foreign policy meeting voted against the visit to Taiwan by Vystrčil, President of the Senate. However, Vystrčil insisted on going, which was a \"boyish provocation\" that might harm practical cooperation with China. President Zeman said he himself attaches importance to relations with China and…","China appreciates President Zeman's dedication to advancing friendship and cooperation between the Czech Republic and China and his firm position on major and sensitive issues relating to China. The sound development of bilateral relations serves the common interests of both countries and peoples. We hope to work together with the Czech Republic on the basis of mutual respect and equality to rise above disturbances and move relations forward. As to President Zeman's expressed hope of attending the China-CEEC Summit, we would like to extend our welcome.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1812840.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1812810.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA News Agency, Beijing, September 8 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 8th that the 12th Straits Forum will open in Fujian Province on September 19. Continuing the theme of \"expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,\" this edition will carry out exchanges through a combination of online and offline methods, with the main venue set in Xiamen, and relevant prefecture-level cities in Fujian Province and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone holding related events.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the forum will arrange more than 30 events in four major sections—the forum conference and youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges—providing a stage for cross-Strait youth to exchange and showcase their talents in forms such as \"cloud debates,\" \"online knowledge competitions,\" and \"cloud creativity PK.\" Through approaches such as \"cloud recruitment\" and \"live-streamed product sales,\" it will help serve Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in employment and entrepreneurship and in resuming work and production; using means such as \"cloud ancestor worship,\" \"cloud evening performances\" and \"cloud exhibitions,\" it will inject new vitality into traditional cultural exchanges, and combined with offline activity formats such as epidemic-themed scripted dramas, environmental runway shows, and \"city spokesperson\" study tours, it will allow more people on the island, especially young people, to participate online through internet links. We warmly welcome compatriots in Taiwan to take part in Straits Forum-related activities in various ways.\nMa Xiaoguang said that despite the influence of factors such as the epidemic, this edition of the forum still attracts wide attention from all sectors on both sides of the Strait. Wang Chin-ping, former vice chairman of the Kuomintang of China, Lee Chien-lung, its secretary-general, as well as representatives of the New Party, the People First Party and other relevant Taiwan parties, groups and sectors, will come to Fujian to attend forum activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200908_12294513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-09-09","Zhao Lijian","South China Morning Post","Editor in Chief Hu Xijin of the Global Times tweeted on his account that China will sanction senior US officials that visit Taiwan and related US companies. Can you confirm that?","Usually we make no specific responses to media reports and comments.\nI can tell you that the Taiwan issue bears on the core interests of China. China's position on this issue is consistent and clear. No one shall underestimate the steadfast determination and resolve of the Chinese government and people in safeguarding national interests. We urge the US to adhere to the one China principle and the three joint communiques between the two sides, stop any form of official exchanges with Taiwan, and cautiously and properly handle the Taiwan issue so as to avoid any serious damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Straits.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1813551.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1813460.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-11","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan's defense authorities said yesterday that China's air and naval drills off its coast were a serious provocation and a threat to international air traffic. Do you have any comment on this?","It is not a diplomatic matter. I would refer you to competent authority.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1814379.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1814243.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 11 — In response to media questions about former Chinese Nationalist Party Vice Chairman Wang Jin-pyng leading a Kuomintang delegation to attend the 12th Straits Forum, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 11th that the 12th Straits Forum will open on September 19 in Fujian Province. Around the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,” people from all walks of life across the Strait will carry out diverse exchange activities to promote practical exchange and cooperation in economic, cultural, grassroots, youth, epidemic prevention and control, public health, film and television, and other fields through concrete actions, and to deepen integrated development across the Strait. We welcome Mr. Wang Jin-pyng to lead the delegation of the Kuomintang to attend the forum.\nMa Xiaoguang said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are members of one family, and should jointly promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. People from all walks of life on both sides should do more things that help enhance understanding and build trust and dispel doubts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200911_12295261.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-09-13","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On September 2, Beijing time, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2020 “Military and Security Developments Involving the People's Republic of China” report, which arbitrarily distorts the relationship between the Communist Party of China and the Chinese military, misinterprets China's national defense policy and military strategy, hypes the so-called “China military threat,” comments irresponsibly on China's national defense and military modernization, and makes groundless accusations on issues such as defense spending, nuclear policy and Taiwan. This is yet another example of the U.S. side smearing and slandering China and the Chinese military. The U.S. has released such reports for 20 consecutive years, which is a blatant act of hegemony and provocation, seriously damaging the relations between China and the United States and between the two militaries. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this, and has lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army is a people's army under the leadership of the Communist Party of China. The Constitution of the People's Republic of China clearly stipulates: “The leadership of the Communist Party of China is the most essential feature of socialism with Chinese characteristics.” The armed forces of the People's Republic of China belong to the people. Upholding the Party's absolute leadership over the army is the eternal soul of the people's army. As armed forces founded and led by the Communist Party of China, the founding purpose of the Chinese People's Liberation Army has always been to wholeheartedly serve the people, to make tremendous sacrifices for achieving national independence and people's liberation, and to make outstanding contributions in economic construction, in responding to major natural disasters, and in protecting the lives and property of the people.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development and firmly follows a defensive national defense policy and an active defense military strategy. China's military development is entirely driven by the need to safeguard its national sovereignty, security and development interests, is not directed at any country, and will not pose a threat to any country. The development and construction of China's weapons and equipment have always adhered to the principles of independence, self-reliance and independent innovation, relying mainly on its own strength for research and production. The Chinese military's going out into the world brings security rather than threats to the world, and opportunities rather than challenges. The Chinese military has always been a steadfast force for maintaining world peace, and in recent years has increasingly carried out overseas military missions such as peacekeeping, escort and disaster relief. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, the Chinese military has actively promoted international military cooperation through exchanging letters, phone calls, video exchanges on experiences in epidemic response, and medical supply assistance, fulfilling the responsibilities of a major country and its international obligations through practical actions.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The fundamental cause of the current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities seek to rely on foreign backing for leverage and to resist reunification by force, and that external anti-China forces attempt to “use Taiwan to contain China” and split China. We must sternly point out that pursuing “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. If anyone dares to try to separate Taiwan from China, the People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to resolutely defeat any plot or act that interferes in China's internal affairs and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nIn the past 20 years, the U.S. has illegally launched wars and military operations against Iraq, Syria, Libya and other countries, causing more than 800,000 deaths and displacing tens of millions of people. Years of facts have proven that the U.S. side is the instigator of regional turmoil, the violator of international order, and the disruptor of world peace. The international community has long reached a consensus on this. Instead of reflecting on itself, the U.S. side has issued a so-called report that makes unwarranted comments on China's normal national defense and military development, and makes remarks about China's justified actions to safeguard its sovereignty and security interests. We demand that the U.S. side view China's national defense and military development objectively and rationally, stop issuing erroneous statements and relevant reports, and, through practical actions, safeguard the healthy development of relations between the two countries and the two militaries.\nThe Chinese military will faithfully practice the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind, firmly uphold the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, actively carry out regional security cooperation, promptly provide international public security goods, and always be a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a maintainer of international order.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-09/13/content_4871125.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2020-09-14","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US Under Secretary of State Keith Krach could lead a delegation to visit Taiwan for talks later this month, according to Taiwan media reports. What is the ministry’s comment on this proposed trip by the under secretary?","China firmly opposes official exchanges between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. I would like to stress once again that the Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China's core interests. It is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and to stop all forms of official ties between the US and Taiwan so as to avoid serious damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1814845.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1814788.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-16","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","First, Japanese Prime Minister Suga has picked Abe's younger brother Nobuo Kishi as the new defense minister. Mr. Nobuo Kishi is known for his close ties with Taiwan. He visited there as recently as last month. Does the Ministry have a stance on the appointment of Nobuo Kishi as defense minister? Second, according to a report by cyber security firm Red Delta, hackers alleged to be backed by China have renewed…","We congratulate Mr. Nobuo Kishi on his appointment as Japanese Defense Minister. We hope that the defense departments of the two countries will strengthen dialogue and exchanges, continuously enhance security mutual trust, promote the building of constructive bilateral security relations and jointly safeguard regional and international peace and stability. We also hope the Japanese side will abide by the one-China principle and refrain from any form of official exchanges with the Taiwan region.\nOn your second question, China firmly opposes and combats all forms of cyber attacks and cyber crimes. This position is consistent and clear. Hacker attacks are a common threat to all countries. We need to investigate, collect evidence about and combat such problems through bilateral dialogue, judicial assistance, etc., and the issue of cyber security should not be politicized.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1815499.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1815427.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-16","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan's Chinese Wild Bird Federation was recently removed from BirdLife International, a bird conservation partnership. Taiwan's authorities said that this is a direct result of the Chinese government's pressure and interference. Do you have a comment on this claim?","I'm not aware of the situation. But I want to stress that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Taiwan's participation in the activities of international organizations must follow the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1815499.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1815427.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends! Welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Because of the COVID-19 epidemic and the needs of epidemic prevention work, we suspended in-person press conferences starting in February of this year. During the more than seven months of suspension, we continued to respond to hot cross-Strait issues of concern through news releases and spokesperson written Q&A, and media friends also reported on them extensively. Here, I thank everyone for supporting the work of the Taiwan Affairs Office during this extraordinary period. Starting this month, we are resuming our regular press conferences. Today’s press conference is hosted by me. Now I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Could you introduce the main situation regarding cross-Strait personnel exchanges and economic and trade exchanges since the epidemic began this year?","This year, the COVID-19 epidemic has had a certain impact on cross-strait exchanges and personnel travel. At the same time, the DPP authorities have escalated their obstruction and restrictions on cross-strait exchanges. They unreasonably obstruct Taiwan compatriots and their relatives who are stranded on the mainland from returning to Taiwan, still fully ban mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, forcibly implement the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act,” create a “green terror,” and frequently threaten and intimidate Taiwan residents and civic groups that take part in normal cross-strait exchange activities.\nCross-strait exchanges conform to the shared wishes and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, and no person or force can prohibit or block them. In January and February this year, the most severe months of the epidemic, more than 100,000 Taiwan compatriots still came to the mainland. Since the outbreak, compatriots on both sides have overcome temporary difficulties and, combining online and offline formats through the internet, have successfully held a series of exchange activities on different themes in the fields and sectors of economy, culture, health care, education, youth, grassroots, folk beliefs, and others, continuing the momentum of cross-strait exchanges.\nCross-strait trade and Taiwan business investment on the mainland have continued to grow. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, from January to August this year, cross-strait trade totaled US$158.928 billion, up 10% year on year. Of this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$37.733 billion, up 8.11%, and mainland imports from Taiwan were US$121.195 billion, up 10.6%. In August this year, the share of Taiwan's exports to the mainland (including Hong Kong) in Taiwan's total exports was 46.39%, a record high. Many large Taiwan-funded projects have started construction and production or have increased capital and expanded on the mainland, involving electronics and information, petrochemicals, cement, and many other industries, showing new features of large investment amounts and high technology content. Relevant statistics published on the island also show that from January to July this year, Taiwan business investment in the mainland grew by more than 50% year on year.\nI want to emphasize that the two sides across the Taiwan Strait were cut off for 38 years, yet the artificial barriers that blocked exchanges between compatriots were ultimately broken. Now, more than 30 years after cross-strait exchanges were opened, the internal drive and deep foundation accumulated in exchanges and cooperation across all fields have formed an irreversible historical trend, which cannot be shaken by immediate difficulties and obstacles.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296409.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Taiwan media reported that PLA aircraft entered Taiwan's southwestern airspace on the 9th, 10th and 13th of this month consecutively. In response, Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities and military each held press conferences expressing opposition and claimed that “threat information has been communicated to relevant countries.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Taiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of Chinese territory. The relevant combat training activities of the PLA are necessary actions taken in response to the current security situation across the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty.\nAt present, cross-Strait relations have become more complicated and grim, and the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces are the instigators. They rely on foreign powers to elevate themselves, willingly serving as pawns for Western anti-China forces who play the “Taiwan card” to contain China’s development. They constantly incite cross-Strait confrontation and opposition, vigorously agitate for and accelerate a series of “independence” activities, and seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Their constant provocations make them the makers of threats and troubles.\nWe are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort. The actions of the PLA are aimed at external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and are by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. If anyone feels threatened, that can only show that they are attempting to collude with external forces to pursue separatism. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. “Taiwan independence” elements, who harm the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides and of the Chinese nation, are the common enemy of compatriots on both sides, and they will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan’s 23 million people. “Taiwan independence” elements who twist black and white and run to foreign powers to complain, attempting to hold Taiwan society hostage, only further expose their evil nature.\nWe are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We have the resolve and the capability to defeat all “Taiwan independence” activities, to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to resolutely safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296408.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The DPP authorities plan to hold a “US-Taiwan Economic and Commercial Dialogue” with the US side, and US Deputy Secretary of State Krach is about to visit Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and external forces are not allowed to interfere. We demand that the United States side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop conducting any form of official exchanges with the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opposition, insisted on opening imports of problematic US agricultural and livestock products for political purposes, harming the health and well-being of the island's people. Now, using this as a pledge of loyalty, they are developing official relations with the US under the pretext of “economic and commercial” matters. This will only further subject themselves to US manipulation, impact the island's market, and harm the economic livelihood interests of Taiwan compatriots. Others hold the knife and the chopping board, while the DPP authorities are willing to be the fish on the cutting board. Taiwan compatriots must be on guard.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296407.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Mainland universities have gradually begun the new academic year. Please introduce the situation this year regarding mainland universities enrolling Taiwan students and Taiwan students returning to school. What conveniences do mainland universities provide for the study and daily life of Taiwan students? Also, what is the current situation of mainland students studying in Taiwan?","The COVID-19 epidemic that broke out at the beginning of this year has disrupted the work, study and daily lives of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and has also affected Taiwan students applying to mainland universities. At the same time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ obstruction and restriction of cross-Strait exchanges and their threats and intimidation of the Taiwan public have grown even more severe. Under these circumstances, many Taiwan students have insisted on their choice to apply to mainland universities, and relevant mainland universities have worked hard to create favorable conditions for Taiwan students’ applications. It is understood that a total of nearly 6,800 Taiwan student applications to mainland universities were made this year, and admissions work has not yet been fully completed. Here, we welcome them to come to the mainland to pursue their academic goals and life dreams.\nAt the start of the new semester, the Ministry of Education has already made comprehensive arrangements for autumn and winter COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control work in universities, primary and secondary schools, and preschool institutions nationwide, and has recently made specific arrangements for the resumption of classes by students and teachers from Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan. Localities and universities, based on their own actual circumstances, have arranged for students to return to campus in batches, by category, in a reasonable and orderly manner. After completing epidemic prevention, quarantine and monitoring under the regulations of the locality where their school is located, Taiwan students will resume classes together with mainland students. Universities will carry out full-process health management for all students, striving to ensure “zero infection.” If some Taiwan students temporarily cannot return to school for various reasons, schools will adopt measures such as online learning and online tutoring to safeguard their studies, and online and offline courses will be consistent to ensure teaching quality. Universities in various localities are also proactively maintaining contact and communication with Taiwan students newly admitted this year through personalized means such as holding online freshman training camps, holding freshman meet-ups on the island, and sending professional textbooks in advance, and are trying to provide convenient and thoughtful services for new students to enroll. Here, I would like to extend congratulations to the Taiwan students admitted by mainland universities, and wish them smooth starts to their new studies and success in their academic pursuits.\nEveryone will remember that since the beginning of this year, mainland students going to Taiwan to study have encountered many difficulties, which include both the impact of the epidemic and many man-made obstacles from the Taiwan side. At the very beginning of the epidemic outbreak, mainland students were among the first groups banned from going to Taiwan by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. Even after the epidemic eased and students outside the Taiwan region gradually returned to school, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities still prevented thousands of mainland students from returning to school. Mainland students repeatedly called on the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to change their unreasonable policies, but they ignored these appeals, and only in early August, after all degree-seeking students were allowed to return to school, did they permit mainland students to return. Many mainland students also reported that during the epidemic, the Taiwan universities where they study did not make proper arrangements for adjustments to teaching, which greatly affected their studies. From this, it can be seen that mainland students going to Taiwan to study face difficult and complex circumstances, which is also an important reason why the Ministry of Education decided to suspend this year’s applications for further study in Taiwan by graduates of all levels and types of programs from all parts of the mainland. For mainland students who applied in the past and are still studying in Taiwan, we will continue to support them in safeguarding their own legitimate rights and interests through appropriate means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Public opinion holds that in the new session of Taiwan’s legislature, the DPP authorities will use lowering the voting age and abolishing the “Examination Yuan” and “Control Yuan” as breakthroughs to pave the way for so-called “Taiwan independence through constitutional amendment.” What is your comment on this?","We are paying close attention to the relevant developments. We firmly oppose any attempt by forces on the island to pursue “independence” through so-called “constitutional amendments and legal revisions.” “Taiwan independence” is a reverse current of history and a dead end, and it will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will remain highly vigilant and, through concrete actions, oppose “Taiwan independence” and safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296406.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","In response to questions from public opinion on the island as to why the mainland can refuse US pork containing ractopamine but the DPP authorities cannot, Chen Shih-chung, head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention authority, argued in an interview that they are “worried that mainland residents will eat dead pork.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","For the sake of party self-interest and undisclosed purposes, the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces and disregarding the food safety and health of the people of Taiwan, have insisted on opening imports of problematic foreign pork and beef products, causing great concern and strong indignation among the island’s residents. The person you mentioned has tried hard to argue this, but has never been able to make his story consistent. He diverts attention by baselessly attacking the mainland, which fully exposes his dark mentality and a personality without moral bottom line. His political countenance is clear to compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The 12th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian on September 19. May I ask what features, characteristics and highlights this forum has? The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council has imposed so-called “three bans” to restrict and obstruct the forum; what is your comment?","This year's Straits Forum has the following features and highlights. First, under the normalized epidemic prevention and control situation, and especially under the obstruction and interference of the DPP authorities, the Forum was able to proceed smoothly, which shows that strengthening cross-Strait exchange and cooperation is the mainstream public sentiment of compatriots on both sides. Relevant parties, groups, and people from all walks of life in Taiwan came to take part in this event, demonstrating the responsibility, commitment, and courage to advance cross-Strait relations.\nSecond, this Forum includes 46 events covering economic, cultural, grassroots, youth, and other exchange sections across the Strait. The arrangements are more refined, and exchange and cooperation will be deeper. In particular, exchanges and cooperation in the fields of epidemic prevention and control and public health have been newly added, which better matches the issues of greatest concern to compatriots on both sides at present.\nThird, by leveraging internet technology, exchanges are conducted through a combination of online and offline formats. Various “cloud-based” activities bring vivid experiences to everyone, and through online links, more people across the Strait, especially young people, can participate interactively online.\nThe DPP authorities' intimidation and obstruction of Taiwan compatriots attending the Straits Forum, and their attempt to completely ban cross-Strait exchanges, can only further expose their “Taiwan independence” nature. Such actions run counter to the wishes of compatriots on both sides for exchange and cooperation, and will only result in “all for nothing, like drawing water with a bamboo basket.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296404.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The KMT recently decided to cancel its delegation to this year's Straits Forum, and Wang Jin-pyng also said he would not attend in a personal capacity. What is your comment? Will this affect the effectiveness of this year's forum?","Since its founding, the Straits Forum has adhered to the principle that across the Taiwan Strait we are one family, and has maintained its positioning as “civil, grassroots, and broadly inclusive.” It has fully played its role in expanding and deepening civil exchanges across the Strait, jointly promoting Chinese culture, boosting the integration of economic and social development across the Strait, and promoting emotional connection among people on both sides. It has become the largest and most widely participated civil exchange event across the Strait, and is an important platform for uniting compatriots on both sides and building shared public opinion in support of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Last month, poll results released by institutions on the island showed that nearly six in ten Taiwan compatriots, and in particular more than seven in ten young people, support strengthening cross-Strait exchanges at present. Continuing to hold the Straits Forum well meets the shared wish of compatriots on both sides for more exchanges and for closer contact. We believe that, through the broad participation and joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, the Straits Forum will certainly achieve its intended results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296403.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Reports say that, under the coordination of the Taiwan Affairs Office, a Mainland host recently submitted a “draft apology statement” to the KMT, but later did not apologize according to the draft statement, which the KMT could not accept. Could you explain the specific situation?","There is absolutely no such situation as described in the quoted report. The so-called “apology statement” reported by some Taiwan media is completely inconsistent with the facts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Public opinion holds that the DPP authorities are trying to \"decouple\" cross-Strait economies, while the mainland was the first to bring the epidemic under control, and economic recovery will provide more development opportunities for Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland. What views and comments does the spokesperson have?","The mainland was the first to overcome the adverse impact of the epidemic and achieve the full resumption of work and production, and its economy has steadily recovered. The second-quarter economic growth rate was 3.2%, making it the only major economy in the world to achieve positive growth. The mainland's institutional advantages are significant, its governance capacity is superior, its material foundation is solid, its human resources are abundant, its market space is broad, its development resilience is strong, and social stability overall is maintained. The economy has multiple advantages and conditions for long-term positive prospects, and we are accelerating the formation of a new development pattern in which the domestic great cycle is the main body and domestic and international dual circulations promote each other. This will provide more opportunities and greater space for cross-Strait economic cooperation, especially for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises developing on the mainland. We are confident that broad Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, by seizing the opportunities, will certainly achieve greater development success on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200916_12296405.htm"],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","May I ask the spokesperson: the KMT has decided to cancel sending personnel to attend the Straits Forum. How will the mainland strengthen cross-Strait exchanges? How will it strengthen exchanges with other parties on the island? What is the spokesperson’s evaluation and view of the KMT’s “new cross-Strait narrative”?","I will answer your second question first. We note that at the 6 September National Congress, the Kuomintang presented a report on its cross-Strait policy for the current stage. Since 2005, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the Communist Party and the Kuomintang have strengthened exchange and cooperation, promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides, achieving abundant results. Facts have repeatedly proven that if this foundation is upheld and protected, cross-Strait relations can develop peacefully and stably. If this foundation is changed or even abandoned, cross-Strait relations will inevitably stagnate or even regress.\nOn your first question, while resolutely containing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, the mainland actively promotes exchange and cooperation between compatriots on both sides in all fields, maintains the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and safeguards peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Straits Forum is a civil forum and a platform for exchange and dialogue among people from all sectors and relevant groups on both sides of the Strait. As I said earlier, as long as compatriots on both sides participate together, the momentum of exchange and cooperation will continue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The KMT chairperson believes that, because mutual trust between the two sides' peoples is weak, the KMT canceled its participation in the Straits Forum this time. Is there now a problem in exchanges between the mainland and the KMT? If even the KMT feels that mutual trust across the Strait is somewhat weak, will there be adjustments?","As many of you may have noticed, many Taiwan media outlets have published commentary arguing that the key reason for this outcome is the treacherous political situation and the poor political ecology within Taiwan. I want to stress again: adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the political foundation for exchanges and dialogue between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China. As long as this foundation exists, we are willing to further strengthen communication, seek common ground while setting aside differences, build trust and dispel doubts, accept differences while seeking common ground, and jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","The KMT decided to cancel sending a delegation to the Straits Forum. Then how will exchanges between the KMT and the CPC, or between the Mainland and other political parties on the island, be carried out? Which Taiwan parties and individuals will attend this Straits Forum? Will Chairman Wang Yang attend?","First, regarding the specific arrangements for the Straits Forum, its organizing committee will hold a press conference in Xiamen on the afternoon of September 18 to provide details. Everyone is welcome to follow it.\nSince 2008, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides have built comprehensive platforms for exchange and cooperation. However, because the DPP authorities deny the “1992 Consensus,” refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle, and rampantly promote a series of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, cross-Strait relations are now complex and grim, and even tense and turbulent. This is the fundamental reason. Under these circumstances, our policy of carrying out exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan’s parties and groups on the political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” remains unchanged, and the door remains open. I believe that as long as everyone considers the common interests of compatriots on both sides, such exchanges and cooperation will not be fundamentally blocked.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Some people believe that the KMT's decision to cancel its participation in this year's Straits Forum was prompted by the view that remarks made by a mainland host had damaged the KMT's image. Why has this host not apologized as the KMT requested? After the incident, the Taiwan Affairs Office issued a press release welcoming 王金平 to lead a delegation to visit the mainland, yet relevant media still have not arranged…","First, I must formally clarify that there is no situation of “multiple cooks” or “hawkish” dominance in the mainland's Taiwan work. On the major policy guidelines for Taiwan, the attitude from the top to the bottom on the mainland is consistent. We are sincere and well-intentioned, but we also act on principle. You are also a news media professional, and you too have “offended” or “defied” the DPP authorities by expressing some personal views. I do not know whether you have been subjected to pressure from public power and required to apologize? We are all journalists, and we can put ourselves in each other's shoes. Do not magnify a host's personal remarks without limit or elevate them to matters of principle; this is not the attitude to take in handling problems.\nIn fact, everyone has also noticed that since this incident occurred, some on the island have sown discord, some have seized on the matter to make a point, some have taken pleasure in others' misfortune, and some have fanned the flames. Who among them has apologized? Everyone may also examine whether these actions are harming the feelings between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","ET-Today新闻云记者","The ECFA has reached its ten-year expiration, and there are rumors that the mainland may terminate it. What is your comment on this? In addition, some scholars on both sides have pointed out that cross-Strait relations are currently more severe and complicated, and there is a possibility of an accidental exchange of fire. How do you comment?","On the first question: the entry into force and implementation of ECFA has brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities have repeatedly and increasingly undermined cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and restricted cross-Strait trade and investment, seriously harming the vital interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Only by safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can cross-Strait agreements be implemented smoothly.\nOn the second question: the current situation in the Taiwan Strait is becoming more complex and grave, and the originators are the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces. We have confidence and capability to firmly hold the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations. Where cross-Strait relations go next depends critically on the thinking of the DPP authorities. The “Taiwan independence” forces who think that relying on foreign powers, pledging allegiance to them, and colluding with external forces will allow them to confront and seek separation have completely misjudged the situation and are blinded by profit. Colluding with external forces to pursue “Taiwan independence” is walking a dangerous single-log bridge with an abyss beneath; the ladder is in someone else’s hands, and they could be smashed to pieces at any time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, two months ago, five Hong Kong people, after being implicated in a case in Hong Kong, illegally crossed over to Taiwan and have been detained by the Taiwan authorities until now; the Hong Kong SAR Government says it has not received any relevant information. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office view this? Second, following the visit to Taiwan by the US Secretary of Health, the US Deputy…","On the second question: we firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic ties with us and the Chinese Taiwan region. This conduct interferes in China's internal affairs, hurts the feelings of the Chinese people, and also violates internationally recognized norms of international relations, and we firmly oppose it. We have also repeatedly warned the DPP authorities that attempting to rely on foreign backing to throw their weight around and to seek confrontation and “Taiwan independence” separatism is a dead end.\nOn the first question: I do not have the specific information. What I want to emphasize is that the DPP authorities' interference in Hong Kong affairs aims to create chaos in Hong Kong and seek political private gain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央广记者","On the 20th of this month, the old-style paper Taiwan Compatriot Permit will exit the historical stage. Please introduce the application of the card-style electronic Taiwan Compatriot Permit.","The Taiwan Compatriot Permit is the travel document for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland. Since it was first issued in May 1992, the Taiwan Compatriot Permit has gone through three upgrades. As of 2019, more than 11.6 million Taiwan compatriots have been issued over 23 million permits in total. To facilitate travel across the Strait for Taiwan compatriots, the mainland side fully abolished the Taiwan compatriot visa endorsement policy starting July 1, 2015, and fully implemented the card-type electronic Taiwan Compatriot Permit starting September 21 of that year, ceasing to accept applications for the booklet-type Taiwan Compatriot Permit. It is understood that the last batch of booklet-type Taiwan Compatriot Permits will expire on September 20, and Taiwan residents holding booklet-type permits may exchange them for card-type permits or apply for a one-time-valid Taiwan Compatriot Permit to come to the mainland. The new electronic Taiwan Compatriot Permit is designed and produced with mature technology and uses information-based means to provide Taiwan compatriots with more convenient and efficient entry and exit services. Since its trial implementation in 2015, it has been widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","日本NHK记者","Reports say that after the President of the Czech Senate visited Taiwan, mainland clients canceled orders from a well-known Czech piano manufacturer. Some European and American countries believe this is China’s “retaliation.” What comment do you have on this?","Some Czech political figures colluded with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and, incited by external forces, recently visited Taiwan. This violated the commitment to adhere to the One-China Principle and the basic norms of international relations, interfered in China’s internal affairs, and hurt the feelings of the Chinese people. We firmly oppose this. As for the specific matters you mentioned, I am not aware of the situation; please direct your inquiry to the relevant authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Because iQiyi and Taobao can no longer be listed in Taiwan, the Taiwan General Chamber of Commerce said there are reports that an atmosphere of boycotting “Taiwan goods” is emerging on the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s response and explanation?","For some time now, the DPP authorities, out of self-interest, have used all kinds of pretexts and means to deliberately manipulate “anti-China” populism, escalating their sabotage of cross-Strait exchanges, obstructing and restricting cross-Strait economic cooperation, and attempting to bring about “decoupling” across the Strait. They have crudely and unreasonably targeted some mainland enterprises in Taiwan, once again exposing the essence of their undermining of cross-Strait relations. In the end, the ones actually harmed are still the interests of Taiwan's consumers. Our policies on strengthening cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation have not changed. It is understandable that some mainland netizens have voiced countermeasures, given that the DPP authorities have repeatedly stirred up cross-Strait confrontational sentiment.\nToday's press conference ends here. Welcome, everyone. Over the past more than seven months, many reporters, especially Taiwan-based correspondents, have overcome the inconveniences caused by the epidemic and traveled back and forth across the Strait, and their work and lives have been affected to some extent. The Taiwan Affairs Office, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, and the China Association for Journalists have done their best to provide services to everyone. Once again, thank you all for your hard work. We will see you at our next press conference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200916_12296400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-09-17","Wang Wenbin","NHK","US Under Secretary of State Keith Krach is going to visit Taiwan for commemorations of Lee Teng-hui and the US-Taiwan economic and commercial dialogue. What's your comment?","China firmly opposes any forms of official ties between the US and Taiwan. Our position is consistent and clear. The US insisting on Under Secretary of State Keith Krach's visit to Taiwan severely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, bolsters \"Taiwan independence\" separatists, and undermines China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes it and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nWe urge the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, strictly observe the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop official exchange with Taiwan, make no attempts to change the nature of its relationship with Taiwan, and properly handle Taiwan-related matters. China will make necessary reaction in light of the development of the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1815853.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1815722.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-18","Wang Wenbin","El Pais","Is the military exercise the Chinese defense ministry announced today in the Taiwan Strait has something to do with the visit of US Under Secretary Krach?","I have already elaborated on China's position on US Under Secretary Krach's visit to Taiwan.\nThe Spokesperson of the Chinese Ministry of National Defense also responded to the relevant military exercise this morning. The exercise is a justifiable and necessary action taken in response to the current situation across the Taiwan Strait and to safeguard China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair which allows no foreign interference. Any attempt to contain China with the Taiwan question or solicit foreign support will lead nowhere. China has the firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to foil any interference by external forces and the secessionist acts of \"Taiwan independence\" forces and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1816244.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1816207.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-21","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","According to reports, during US Under Secretary of State Krach's visit to Taiwan from September 17 to 19, he met with the region's leadership including Tsai Ing-wen, and attended a memorial service of Lee Teng-hui. This is another visit to Taiwan by a senior US official following HHS Secretary Azar in August. What's China's comment on this?","China firmly opposes any kind of official ties between the US and the Taiwan region. By insistently sending HHS Secretary Azar and Under Secretary Krach to visit the region, the US has seriously violated the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. It is a political provocation that emboldens \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and undermines China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns it. We will take countermeasures, including against relevant individuals. The US acts will have further negative consequences on China-US coordination and cooperation on major regional and international issues, for which it bears full responsibility.\nChina is determined to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity, oppose external interference, and realize the reunification across the Taiwan Strait. We solemnly inform the US side that \"Taiwan independence\" only leads to a dead end, and efforts to condone and support \"Taiwan independence\" are doomed to fail. Any attempt to hurt China's core interests and interfere in China's internal affairs will be met with strong reactions. The historical trend of China's reunification won't be stopped by any force. China urges the US to correct its mistakes, fulfill its commitments in the three joint communiqués, stop its official exchange and military ties with Taiwan, and stop its interference in China's internal affairs as well as words and deeds that undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202009/t20200921_693391.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1816686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-21","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Taiwan newspaper reported that PLA pilots flew across the so-called median line on September 17. What's China's position on the \"median line\" issue?","The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. The so-called \"median line\" is non-existent.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202009/t20200921_693391.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1816686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-09-22","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","China and the Vatican extended the agreement on the appointment of bishops. What significance does this have on relations between the two sides? With the Vatican having \"diplomatic ties\" with \"the Republic of China\" now, what effect will this extension have on the possible establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Vatican?","First I need to stress that the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. Please remember to use its proper name \"China's Taiwan region\" in the future.\nThe China-Vatican provisional agreement on appointment of bishops has been working smoothly since it was reached two years ago, thanks to the concerted efforts, and Catholicism in China has witnessed sound development. The two sides will maintain close communication and consultation to continuously improve bilateral relations. There is good communication between the two sides. China holds a sincere and positive attitude towards advancing relations with the Vatican side. We welcome exchanges between the two sides with an open attitude.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1817104.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1817075.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 22 — In response to the visit to Taiwan by US Deputy Secretary of State Krach, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 22nd in response to a question: The US has recently sent senior officials to Taiwan one after another, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing and colluding with the US, will ultimately harm the interests of compatriots on both sides. We advise the DPP authorities not to underestimate our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and not to go further and further down the road of seeking “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200922_12297749.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-09-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reported that PLA aircraft have recently conducted exercises one after another in the airspace near Taiwan, and the Taiwan leader responded that the mainland should remain restrained. What comment do you have?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. The People's Liberation Army's live-troop exercises in the Taiwan Strait area demonstrate our determination and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and are aimed at external forces' interference and a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their secessionist activities. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities in Taiwan have disregarded the safety and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots, constantly stirred up cross-Strait confrontation, and carried out provocations of \"seeking independence,\" endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This scheme is doomed to fail. If \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist forces dare, under any name or by any means, to split Taiwan from China, we will not spare any cost and will resolutely crush them.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/jzhzt/2020-09/24/content_4871798.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2020-09-25","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","According to some reports, this year's APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting will be held virtually for the first time. Taiwan authorities have said they would strive for Tsai Ing-wen's participation. I wonder if you have a comment?","Chinese Taipei participates in APEC in the capacity of regional economy under the one-China principle. No matter what form the APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting may take, Chinese Taipei's participation must comply with relevant APEC MOU and well-established practice. This is a key political precondition for the region's participation in APEC. Our position on this issue is clear and firm. No one shall harbor any illusions. It is completely futile for Taiwan authorities to attempt to take advantage of the occasion to maneuver a \"breakthrough\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1818610.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1818536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Welcome to the press conference. Now, I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently published a series of question-and-answer pieces on the “1992 Consensus” through media platforms, which attracted attention on the island. In response, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said, “We have never accepted any imposed political proposition or framework, and the ‘1992 Consensus’ has turned a page in cross-strait history.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Thank you, media friends, for your attention to the TAO's new media graphic products. The historical background and concrete process of the “1992 Consensus” are very clear. In the Consensus, both sides expressed their adherence to the one-China principle and their pursuit of national reunification. Its essence is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and both sides jointly strive to seek national reunification. As for the political meaning of one China, both sides set the dispute aside, seeking common ground while reserving differences. The “1992 Consensus” was reached through equal communication and consultation between the two sides, applying political wisdom. It was not imposed by one side on the other. The DPP authorities' refusal to recognize the “1992 Consensus” exposes their essence: stubbornly adhering to the separatist position of “one side, one country,” attempting to undermine the fact that “both sides of the Strait belong to one China,” and pursuing “Taiwan independence.” I must emphasize: heaven does not change, and neither does the Way (天不变、道亦不变). As the common political foundation for promoting the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations, the “1992 Consensus” cannot be overturned by anyone or any force. In the past, present and future, this is so.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299553.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Reportedly, the Taiwan authorities' legislature will launch the so-called “constitutional revision project” in its new session, and DPP members including Tsai I-yu and Chen Ting-fei will put forward pro-“independence” proposals that include “revising the inherent territory” and “giving priority to joining international organizations and participating in international activities under the name of Taiwan.” What is…","This is blatant conduct aimed at plotting “independence.” Recently the forces of “Taiwan independence” have been stirring again, and we are highly attentive to this. We solemnly warn a small handful of “Taiwan independence” diehards not to underestimate our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and not to go further and further down the evil path of “amending the constitution to seek independence.” You must pull back from the brink, otherwise you will be playing with fire and burning yourselves. “Amending the constitution to seek independence” will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will maintain high vigilance. Only by opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions can we safeguard the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299550.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 12th Straits Forum was recently held in Xiamen, Fujian. Please introduce what outcomes this forum achieved.","Despite obstruction by the DPP authorities and the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic, the 12th Straits Forum was still held successfully, and a large number of Taiwan compatriots enthusiastically took part in various activities. As Chairman Wang Yang pointed out in his video address, the sincere and strong desire of people on both sides of the Strait for exchanges cannot be blocked by any force. In summary, the main outcomes of this forum are reflected in the following aspects:\nFirst, the forum brought together compatriots on both sides of the Strait to join in a great endeavor, becoming the largest-scale grassroots exchange \"big stage\" under special circumstances. According to incomplete statistics, about 2,000 Taiwan compatriots took part in the forum's various activities, and 90,000 Taiwan residents watched the forum's main session online. This became the largest cross-Strait exchange activity since the outbreak of the epidemic this year, with the greatest number of participants from Taiwan.\nSecond, the forum innovated an exchange model combining online and offline activities, entering the \"cloud era\" of cross-Strait exchanges. This forum widely used new media and new technology, overcoming the unfavorable factors caused by the epidemic and artificial obstruction. Among the 46 series of activities, 34 combined online and offline formats. Young people on both sides of the Strait exchanged ideas through \"cloud debates,\" \"online knowledge competitions,\" and \"cloud creative PK\"; cultural activities such as \"cloud ancestor worship,\" \"cloud evening performances,\" and \"cloud exhibitions\" were rich and colorful; and people from all walks of life across the Strait moved from \"face-to-face\" to \"screen-to-screen,\" with \"cloud signings,\" \"cloud recruitment,\" and \"live-streamed product sales\" sparking enthusiasm for cooperation and development.\nThird, the forum promoted spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides and jointly rode the \"cloud express\" of integrated development. Around topics such as economic cooperation, cultural exchange, youth exchange, and grassroots exchange, people from all walks of life across the Strait jointly recalled the fight against the epidemic, jointly promoted Chinese culture, jointly advanced \"all-round connectivity\" (应通尽通), and jointly pursued integrated development, achieving valuable results. \"Cloud recruitment\" provided more than 1,300 job opportunities for young people from Taiwan; \"cloud signings\" facilitated the matching of more than 80 economic and trade projects, with total investment exceeding 3 billion yuan; and offline signed projects totaled nearly 11 billion yuan.\nFourth, the forum drew wide attention, and its influence further increased. Within a few days, videos of related activities were viewed more than 400 million times, Taiwan's online and social media carried more than 3,000 reports, and there were more than 131,000 comments.\nHere, the organizers have entrusted me to take the opportunity of today's press conference to convey sincere thanks to all friends from all walks of life across the Strait who care about and support the work of the forum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299552.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Regarding New Party Chairman Wu Cheng-tien's call at the Straits Forum to jointly promote the “one country, two systems” Taiwan proposal, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan declared that it will launch a so-called “administrative investigation.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The New Party has consistently pursued national unification and national rejuvenation, and advocates peaceful reunification of both sides of the Taiwan Strait. As early as the party’s anniversary celebration last August, the New Party announced eight proposals on a Taiwan plan under “one country, two systems.” During the forum, Chairman Wu Cheng-tien reiterated the New Party’s consistent position and put forward the rational proposition of hoping for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and pursuing peaceful reunification. This is a righteous act. While manipulating and tolerating all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist words and deeds, the DPP authorities fabricate “groundless” charges, strive to suppress voices in Taiwan that advocate unification, interfere with and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, extensively create a “green terror” and a “chilling effect,” and deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation. Such crude political manipulation does not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299546.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台记者","Entertainers such as Ouyang Nana and Angela Zhang will take part in the “October 1” gala and sing songs such as 《My Motherland》. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan threatened that it “will closely monitor and investigate according to regulations.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Whenever major festivals of the Chinese people arrive, we celebrate together with compatriots from Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macau, and overseas Chinese. When Taiwanese entertainers come to the mainland to develop their careers, take part in cross-Strait film and television exchange activities, or perform on stage with mainland singers, audiences enjoy them, and we actively support this as well. For the DPP authorities to repeatedly threaten and intimidate Taiwan residents who engage with the mainland can only be described as “if one wants to charge someone with a crime, one will never lack an excuse.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The Straits Forum has just been successfully held, and recently the Shandong-Taiwan (Lu-Tai), Tianjin-Taiwan (Jin-Tai) and Jiangxi-Taiwan (Gan-Tai) cross-Strait economic and trade exchange events have also been held in Shandong Province, Tianjin Municipality and Jiangxi Province, attracting wide attention and discussion. Please introduce the relevant situation.","In September, we successively held cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities such as the Lu-Taiwan Conference, the Jin-Taiwan Conference, and the Gan-Taiwan Conference.\nFrom September 1 to 4, the 26th Lu-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference, held in Weifang, Shandong, organized activities including the Cross-Strait Agricultural Forum. More than 3,000 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait attended online, and more than 100 Taiwanese businesspeople attended offline. During the period, the Cross-Strait Expo, held “on the cloud” for the first time, had 1,750 enterprises participating, 2.2 times the number of exhibiting enterprises last year. Of these, 436 were Taiwan-invested enterprises, 1.4 times last year's number.\nThe 13th Jin-Taiwan Investment and Cooperation Negotiation Conference and the 2020 Tianjin Taiwan Commodities Expo, held September 20 to 23, were conducted with online and offline activities advancing simultaneously. A cloud exhibition hall was set up, with 6 Taiwan county and city commodity zones (New Taipei City, Hsinchu County, Taitung County, Yilan County, Kinmen County, and Lienchiang County) and 3 industry association commodity zones. During the event, the “920 (Love You) Cross-Strait E-Commerce Festival” was held, achieving sales of RMB 100 million through five e-commerce platforms: JD, Alibaba, Pinduoduo, Yunji, and Kuaishou.\nThe 17th Gan-Taiwan Economic, Trade, Cultural Cooperation and Exchange Conference, held in Ji'an, Jiangxi, September 23 to 25, had more than 620 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait in attendance, about 400 of whom were Taiwanese guests. During the period, a plaque-granting ceremony for the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone was held, along with industry matchmaking activities for cross-Strait leisure agriculture, smart mobile terminals, automobile manufacturing, and other industries. A total of 63 projects were signed, with total investment of US$3.963 billion, mainly involving electronic information, equipment manufacturing, new energy, new materials, and other fields.\nIn the near future, the TAO will also work with relevant provinces and cities to hold the Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, the Chongqing?Taiwan Week, the Zhejiang?Taiwan Cooperation Week, the Ji-Taiwan Conference, and other economic and trade activities, continuing to advance cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and deepen cross-Strait integrated development. We will introduce the relevant details to you at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Affected by the epidemic, this year's APEC meeting will be held by video. Taiwan's external exchange department claims it will actively strive for Tsai Ing-wen to participate in the leaders' summit by video. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Regarding Chinese Taipei sending relevant personnel to participate in APEC-related activities as an economy, the APEC organization itself has long-standing established practices. Our position is very clear: it must conform to the One-China principle and to the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding. Any tricks and schemes that take the opportunity to pursue “independence” will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台国广记者","Taiwan media reported that PLA aircraft recently flew over the so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait” several times during combat-oriented drills near the Taiwan Strait, and an MFA spokesperson said there is no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” Please explain the relevant position.","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and Taiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of China. There is no such thing as a so-called line between the two sides of the Strait. The relevant combat training activities of the PLA are necessary actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299549.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Reportedly, the news center of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently replaced its backboard. The original map of the mainland has disappeared, leaving only Taiwan, and its slogan has been changed from “Peace and Goodwill, People First” to “Peace, Reciprocity, Democracy, Dialogue.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Such petty moves are not worth commenting on in themselves. Still, I want to make two points here. First, no matter how it is changed, it cannot alter the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and that Taiwan is part of China. Second, even the pretext of “peaceful goodwill, people first” has been abandoned. I do not know what the Mainland Affairs Council intends to do.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, Yang Pin-hua, a young person of the Amis ethnic group from Hualien, said in a speech at the Straits Forum, “I am Chinese.” Subsequently, Taiwan’s Council of Indigenous Peoples said, “Taiwan’s Indigenous peoples are not descendants of the Yan and Huang emperors.” What is the spokesperson’s view?","The so-called \"Council of Indigenous Peoples\" is a subordinate body of the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities have been frantically obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchanges and inciting cross-Strait confrontation, so it is not surprising that the head of this body would say such things. But speaking on behalf of the DPP authorities does not represent ethnic minority compatriots, including the Amis people. The Chinese nation is a community of shared destiny composed of multiple ethnic groups, and members of every ethnic group are upright and proud Chinese. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should take pride in belonging to the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","There is news on the island that, once a chairperson of the Straits Exchange Foundation acceptable to both sides is found, cross-Strait contact will take place after the U.S. presidential election. Is this what the spokesperson is saying?","Do not be misled by the remarks of such so-called experts. What I want to stress is that the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations, and the basis for contact and interaction between ARATS and SEF. With this foundation, the two organizations can resume consultations; without this foundation, it is futile no matter who serves as chairman.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央视记者","The Taiwan transportation authorities recently studied adding six mainland cargo routes but cancelled them due to obstruction by the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council. What is your comment?","Since February 10, Taiwan's relevant authorities have unilaterally suspended cross-Strait passenger flights other than those to and from Beijing, Shanghai (Pudong and Hongqiao), Xiamen, and Chengdu. At present, the mainland has achieved major strategic results in its fight against the epidemic, and the demand for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and economic and trade interaction has greatly increased. The DPP authorities should stop political manipulation and respond to the needs of businesses and the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾ETToday新闻云记者","First question: Many people in Taiwan now feel like “sandwich biscuits,” caught in the middle. The DPP authorities' “anti-China” policies make Taiwan residents feel considerable pressure in developing on the mainland. For Taiwan residents who are already on the mainland or who wish to develop there, will the mainland side provide more psychological or policy support? Second question: Although the mainland has…","I will answer the first question first. On cross-strait policy, we have consistently adhered to the development philosophy that puts the people first. We are willing to provide equal treatment to the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan, including Taiwan’s young people, for development on the mainland, so that they can more conveniently share the fruits of mainland development. Forty years of cross-strait exchanges have proven that the more compatriots on both sides interact, the more it helps eliminate estrangement, increase communication, and enhance mutual identity. This is a good thing. Who is placing obstacles in the way of compatriots in Taiwan? Who readily turns normal cross-strait exchanges into political issues and pins “red hats” on them? Who manipulates the online troops they raise, carries out campaigns of public denunciation and malicious attacks, and even resorts to judicial measures to punish people? Everyone can see this clearly. Whoever deliberately creates a “sandwiched” situation for the people of Taiwan is the chief culprit.\nWhat I want to emphasize is that no matter what difficulties we encounter, we will continue to implement the “31 measures,” “26 measures,” and a series of other policy measures that promote cross-strait integrated development, expand cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and provide equal treatment to compatriots in Taiwan. This will not change.\nOn the second question, first of all, people must clearly distinguish right from wrong: the chief culprits behind the current complex and severe, and even tense and turbulent, situation in the Taiwan Strait are the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their “Taiwan independence” activities. As I mentioned just now, recently some people on the island have dared to use means such as “constitutional amendment” to put forward separatist propositions of so-called “altering the existing territory,” which amount to “de jure Taiwan independence.” It is precisely these provocative activities that have prompted solemn responses from the mainland. The relevant measures we have taken are aimed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, and at foreign forces interfering, not at the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan. If these activities can be stopped and the two sides return to the common political position of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the Taiwan Strait can return to peace and stability.\nSecond, we have repeatedly declared that we are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form. Do not doubt our resolve, will and capability on this point.\nFinally, we call on the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan to clearly distinguish right from wrong and to join us in opposing and containing “Taiwan independence.” Only in this way can cross-strait relations return to the correct path of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Ouyang Nana and Zhang Shaohan will take the CCTV stage tonight and sing songs such as *My Motherland*. Are you familiar with them, and what is your evaluation? In addition, do the “31 Measures” set certain preconditions for activities of Taiwan performing artists on the mainland?","First, among the “31 measures,” three items provide policy support for people in Taiwan’s film and television industry to develop in the mainland (the “three broadcasting and TV measures”), which everyone is familiar with. We have, as far as possible, provided policy convenience and created a good environment for cross-Strait film and television cooperation and for Taiwan performing artists to develop in the mainland.\nRegarding the evaluation of artists and programs: after this incident, I specifically watched some performances by two young Taiwan artists. Personally, I think their bright images and artistic styles are each beautiful in their own way, and together they are even more beautiful. I believe not only young people on both sides of the Strait but also audiences of other age groups will like them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广电总台央广记者","Could you please tell us what progress has been made in deepening integration between Fujian and Taiwan in various fields?","As everyone knows, the Straits Forum was held in Fujian not long ago. I would like to introduce some of the work Fujian has done in recent years to promote high-quality economic development and to deepen integrated development between Fujian and Taiwan in all fields, for your reference.\nSince the 18th Party Congress, Fujian’s economic development has continually reached new heights. From 2014 to 2019, its economy grew at an average annual rate of 8.5%. In 2019, its total economic output exceeded 4 trillion yuan.\nFujian and Taiwan are close geographically and tied by kinship, and exchanges between them in all fields are frequent. In recent years, the Fujian Provincial Party Committee and Provincial Government have actively issued a series of supporting measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, fully leveraged the roles of platforms such as the Fujian Pilot Free Trade Zone and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, and successively introduced a series of pioneering and trial policy measures to explore a new path for cross-Strait integrated development. Taiwan compatriots investing, working, starting businesses, living and studying in Fujian enjoy more and more support policies and more convenient services.\nIn the economic and trade field, Fujian-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation has grown against the trend despite the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic. From January to July this year, contracted Taiwan investment in Fujian reached 16.42 billion yuan, up 73.7% year on year; total Fujian-Taiwan import and export trade reached 45.41 billion yuan.\nIn terms of “connecting everything that can be connected,” Fujian has made phased progress with Kinmen and Matsu in water supply, electricity, gas and bridge connections. As of the end of August 2020, Fujian had supplied a cumulative 8.65 million tons of safe water to Kinmen. The ship-based water supply project from Fujian to Matsu has also recently been put into operation. Relevant cross-Strait enterprises, industry associations, experts and scholars have on multiple occasions engaged and discussed the issues of electricity, gas and bridge connections with Kinmen and Matsu, and relevant mainland authorities have preliminarily completed the relevant technical plans.\nIn humanities, social exchange and integrated development between Fujian and Taiwan, more than 3.87 million Taiwan compatriot visits to Fujian were recorded in 2019. More than 200 activities centered on cultural exchange between Fujian and Taiwan are held each year. Fujian has established the Fujian-Taiwan Historical and Cultural Research Institute, the Cross-Strait Austronesian Archaeology Teaching and Practice Base, and 16 cross-Strait exchange bases. It has cultivated 75 Taiwan youth internship, training, employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites, introduced more than 700 Taiwan teachers, and more than 70 Taiwan compatriots have won honors such as provincial and municipal model workers, “Three-Eight Red Banner Bearers” and “Youth May Fourth Medals.” To date, more than 36,000 Taiwan youth have been attracted to come to Fujian to study, work and start businesses. Fujian has directly recognized 52 Taiwan professional titles and 14 occupational qualifications.\nIn addition, Fujian has further improved its “one-stop” services, set up a dedicated window for Taiwan-related services under the “12345” hotline, and advanced the construction of the digital “First Home” integrated service platform for Taiwan affairs. Through measures such as setting up Taiwan compatriot service centers, opening a “green channel” for the children of Taiwan talent to enroll in school, designating hospitals to provide medical services, and opening public rental housing, Fujian has preliminarily formed a policy framework system whose main content is equal treatment, which promotes economic and cultural exchange and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan, deepens Fujian-Taiwan integrated development, and safeguards the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202009/t20200930_12299548.htm"],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The Ouyang Nana incident has aroused concern from the DPP authorities and netizens, and it ultimately comes down to the issue of “identity.” Question for the spokesperson: How will the mainland deal with the inherent political differences across the Strait? Second question: If the mainland is willing to adopt a pragmatic attitude toward the inherent political differences across the Strait, in a way that could…","Regarding some developments concerning Taiwanese youth and Taiwanese entertainers developing careers on the mainland, the crux of the problem is not what you call “identity,” but whether the DPP authorities are willing to engage in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This is a fundamental question. There is a political barrier between the two sides, but it does not prevent compatriots on both sides from taking pride in being Chinese people, descendants of Yan and Huang, and children of the Chinese nation. In recent years, who has created divisions between Taiwan and the mainland, and between Taiwan and the Chinese nation, and misled Taiwan's public? The facts are very clear. The responsibility for these problems lies with certain political forces on the island with ulterior motives, not with the mainland.\nI want to emphasize that since 1949, the facts and legal principles of cross-Strait relations have proven that there is only one China in the world, that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have not been divided. This is reflected not only in mainland law but also in your own regulations. Now, some “Taiwan independence” forces in Taiwan are doing things that are “in violation of regulations and laws,” which has already gone beyond the scope of political differences across the Strait. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and a reversal of history, and Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should jointly denounce and condemn it.\nRegarding the political differences that have long existed between the two sides, we have repeatedly advocated that, in the process of jointly pursuing national reunification, and in a responsible attitude toward the nation and future generations, we should seek solutions through equal consultation on the basis of the one-China principle. General Secretary Xi Jinping has also repeatedly pointed out that the political differences long existing between the two sides are the fundamental root affecting the stable and long-term development of cross-Strait relations, and they cannot be passed down from generation to generation. We call on all sectors in Taiwan to respond positively to our proposal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Chen Shih-chung, Taiwan’s head of health authorities, recently said he “will not buy mainland vaccines,” which has caused controversy. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","This person's remarks once again prove that the DPP authorities, apart from exploiting the epidemic to incite confrontation, carrying out political manipulation, and scheming for their own private gain, have never kept the health and life safety of the Taiwan people in mind.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中天电视台记者","Recently, PLA aircraft have frequently entered the Taiwan Strait. On the other hand, the mainland has actively invited Taiwan political parties and civil groups to participate in cross-Strait exchanges, which makes Taiwan residents feel like they are in a “sauna,” alternately cold and hot. The Mainland Affairs Council claimed this is the mainland's “one hand pulling, one hand striking” tactic, a means of dividing…","Everyone is clear that the relevant necessary measures taken by the mainland are aimed at the provocations and reckless adventures of “Taiwan independence,” and are by no means aimed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Our policy toward Taiwan is to implement the development philosophy centered on the people. We regard Taiwan compatriots as our own flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters, and we are willing to unite with them and work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly pursue the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-09-30","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","Continuing the previous question: in fact, many people in Taiwan are quite worried about the possibility of cross-strait war. May I ask the spokesperson: if we rate the scale from peace to war on a scale of 1 to 10, which number would you say cross-strait relations are at now?","I will not make an assessment of the figures. However, I would like to reiterate some positions and views.\nThe current situation in the Taiwan Strait is tense, which has caused panic among some Taiwan residents. Who is the instigator and who is the provocateur, everyone can see clearly. As long as such activities stop, cross-Strait relations can stabilize. This is first.\nSecond, we are willing to provide various possibilities for peaceful reunification, but we will absolutely not tolerate any “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and we will leave them no room. I solemnly declare here: do not doubt or underestimate us, and above all do not lightly test our resolve, confidence, and capability.\nThird, I once again call on broad Taiwan compatriots to join hands with us. Only by opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” can cross-Strait relations return to the track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202009/t20200930_12299544.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, October 6 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated on the 6th that the Third Straits Forum on Cross-Strait Youth Development will be held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, on October 13. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang and Chairperson of the Chinese Youth Peace Education Foundation, will be invited to attend the forum. Guests from relevant sides across the Strait and youth representatives from all sectors will take part in the forum’s related activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201006_12300014.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 6th, the KMT caucus in Taiwan’s legislature proposed so-called resolutions on “requesting the United States to assist in resisting the mainland” and “restoring Taiwan-US ‘diplomatic relations.’” What comment do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 6 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 6th that the root cause of the current complex, grave and tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities collude with external forces and continually take “Taiwan independence” separatist and provocative actions. Thoughtful people and responsible parties on the island should clearly recognize this, remain highly vigilant, and firmly oppose it. Any words or deeds that violate the one-China principle and harm the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation will be firmly opposed by all Chinese people. Relevant members of the Kuomintang should distinguish right from wrong and not do anything that harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China, and that both sides of the Strait belonging to one China is an immutable historical and legal fact. We firmly oppose any separatist acts that create so-called “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas,” or “one China, one Taiwan.” Cross-Strait affairs are family matters for compatriots on both sides, and any external interference is absolutely not permitted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201006_12300135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 10: In response to remarks made on the 10th by the leader of the DPP authorities and the head of the island's public opinion bodies concerning cross-Strait relations, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded: these remarks continue confrontational thinking and hostile awareness, advocate “Taiwan independence” statements, clamor to collude with external forces, and mislead public opinion in Taiwan. They once again expose the essence of the DPP authorities' pursuit of “independence.”\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the root cause of the tension in cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle; that they interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation; that they push a series of acts to pursue “independence”; and that they collude with external forces to provoke. The responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, confrontation has no way out, and relying on foreign powers to inflate one's own standing will only bring self-inflicted consequences. We urge the DPP authorities to stop all provocative words and deeds aimed at “independence,” and not to go further and further down the wrong path. If they return to the correct track of the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait dialogue and consultation can resume, cross-Strait relations can improve, and peace and stability can prevail in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201010_12300708.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-10-13","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Sources said that the US State Department had approved three arms sales to Taiwan. What is China's comment on this?","The United States seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 communiqué, by selling arms to Taiwan, seriously interferes in China's internal affairs and seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests. China firmly opposes this.\nChina urges the US side to fully recognize the very damaging nature of its arms sales to Taiwan, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately cancel all arms sales plans to Taiwan, and stop arms sales to Taiwan and military ties between the United States and Taiwan. China will make a legitimate and necessary reaction in the light of the development of the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1823606.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1823581.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-14","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The White House is moving forward with plans of sales of sophisticated weaponry to Taiwan. It told Congress on Tuesday that it will seek to sell drones and other coastal defense equipment to the island. What's the ministry's comment?","China consistently opposes US arms sales to Taiwan. I already reiterated China's position on this yesterday.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1823951.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202010/t20201014_5419415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Good morning, friends. Welcome to today's Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Questions now begin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","On October 13, the 3rd Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was held in Zhejiang Province. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, attended by invitation. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant details?","The Third Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was held on October 13 in Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province, with more than 200 guests from both sides of the Strait attending. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, and Yuan Jiajun, Secretary of the Zhejiang Provincial Party Committee, attended the forum. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang (KMT) and Chairperson of the Chinese Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, attended at the invitation of the organizers. The forum focused on cross-Strait youth exchange and cooperation, took “Building a Beautiful Home Together” as its theme, and young people from both sides conducted extensive exchanges on topics including jointly fighting the epidemic, developing the digital economy, and supporting youth entrepreneurship, achieving positive results. At the opening ceremony, Zhejiang Province announced eight measures to support Taiwan youth in developing in Zhejiang, covering training and internships, entrepreneurship and employment, e-commerce, financial assistance and other areas.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301279.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Taiwan Industrial Association recently released a survey on the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic on Taiwanese businesses’ investment on the mainland, stating that more than 80% of Taiwanese enterprises on the mainland have been affected in operations, more than 50% of Taiwanese enterprises have not recovered to over 70% of their production capacity, and nearly 10% of operators are still suspended. Is this…","The COVID-19 epidemic is the most serious infectious disease pandemic in a century. It has caused global investment and trade to shrink and the global economy to fall into recession. This impact is global and widespread, and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland naturally cannot stand aside. As everyone can see, over the past nine-plus months, all regions and departments on the mainland have thought about what Taiwan businesspeople think and worried about what they worry about. They have adopted a series of relief measures, including the “11 Measures” to help Taiwan-funded enterprises, and have vigorously assisted Taiwan-funded enterprises in doing a good job of epidemic prevention and resuming work and production. The situation has maintained a steady recovery, and positive changes are increasing.\nLet us take a look at Kunshan, Jiangsu, where Taiwan capital on the mainland is most concentrated. Kunshan now has more than 3,700 Taiwan-funded enterprises, all of which have resumed production, and no Taiwan enterprise remains shut down due to the epidemic. Local authorities have actively helped relevant Taiwan enterprises solve difficulties in labor employment, industrial supporting, epidemic prevention supplies, and other areas, and have provided maximum convenience for Taiwan businesspeople to return to the mainland. Local Taiwan enterprises have also accelerated the resumption of work and production. In particular, orders for relevant Taiwan enterprises engaged in the manufacturing of electronic products such as laptops, tablets, and servers have continued to increase, and their performance has grown against the trend. According to statistics, from January to August, Kunshan approved 118 new Taiwan-funded projects, up 5.4% year on year, and 47 capital increase projects, up 27%, fully demonstrating the confidence of Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in the mainland and in putting down roots there. Facing an unfavorable external environment, many Taiwan enterprises have also actively sought to expand the domestic market, participate in the construction of new infrastructure on the mainland, and form joint ventures and cooperation with mainland enterprises, achieving considerable development.\nLet us look at cross-Strait trade again. According to data published by the General Administration of Customs yesterday, from January to September this year, cross-Strait trade totaled US$185.38 billion, up 12.4% year on year. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$43.05 billion, up 8.2% year on year, and mainland imports from Taiwan were US$142.33 billion, up 13.7% year on year. Looking at September alone, Taiwan's exports to the mainland accounted for 46.24% of Taiwan's total exports, the second-highest single-month record in history. Many Taiwan-funded projects have started operations or expanded production on the mainland, showing features of large investment amounts and high technology content.\nIt must be emphasized that we are accelerating the construction of a new development pattern in which the domestic big cycle is the main body and the domestic and international dual cycles promote each other. We are expanding opening up to the outside world, continuously optimizing the business environment, and fully promoting high-quality development. In the first half of this year, overall tax and fee reductions exceeded 1.5 trillion yuan, and more enterprises have benefited. Various measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople are bringing more benefits to them. The trend of the mainland's economy being stable and improving and sound in the long term has been further consolidated, and it remains the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises to invest and do business, and the greatest opportunity for their future development.\nIn fact, Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises see this very clearly. From recent events such as the Shandong-Taiwan Business Meeting, the Tianjin-Taiwan Business Meeting, and the Jiangxi-Taiwan Business Meeting, as well as the Beijing-Taiwan Technology Forum and the Chongqing?Taiwan Week and Zhejiang?Taiwan Cooperation Week that will be held soon, we can see that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople are throwing themselves into the wave of mainland development, and they will surely achieve greater development of their own.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301275.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Lin Wei-chou, convener of the KMT caucus, posted on Facebook that it is possible to discuss whether to remove the two characters “China” (中国) from the name “Kuomintang of China” (中国国民党). What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Recent moves by certain members of the Kuomintang have raised many doubts in island public opinion and across society. We are following this closely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","DPP-affiliated legislator Wang Ting-yu and others have proposed amending the “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area,” which would stipulate that if any Taiwan school at any level makes any commitment or statement to cooperate with so-called “united front” work, the Taiwan education authorities would order it to stop enrollment. In addition, Su Tseng-chang has also…","For some time, some DPP politicians have used so-called “legislative amendments” and other means to forcibly obstruct and restrict private cross-Strait exchanges and to create a “green terror.” Now they have further escalated, reaching out to Taiwan's colleges and universities and to cross-Strait academic exchanges. Such perverse actions run counter to the shared wishes and practical needs of people on both sides of the Strait for greater exchanges, and do not win public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301273.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, a Taiwan media survey showed that the island's public assessment of cross-Strait relations has turned for the worse, and the proportion leaning toward “independence” has risen. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The culprits threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and undermining cross-Strait relations are the DPP authorities and the 'Taiwan independence' forces. They hold the Taiwan people hostage, willingly act as 'pawns' of Western anti-China forces, and seriously harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nWe must point out that 'Taiwan independence' is a countercurrent of history and a dead end that cannot be traversed. It can only bring unbearable risks to Taiwan and profound disaster to the 23 million Taiwan people. Only by containing 'Taiwan independence' can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully and stably, and only then can the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides be safeguarded and enhanced. We believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots will see this clearly as the facts unfold.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","In response to Hung Hsiu-chu attending the Third Straits Forum on Youth Development, Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council claimed that if violations are involved, it will take action, and threatened that Taiwan youth should not take part in such activities, lest they become tools of so-called “united front” propaganda. What is your comment on this?","The Straits Forum for Youth Development is a platform for exchanges between young people across the Strait. We have consistently and actively supported and encouraged young people across the Strait to strengthen exchanges, enhance mutual understanding, and jointly seek development. Out of narrow party interest, the DPP authorities deliberately obstruct and sabotage civilian exchange activities across the Strait, and mount threats and suppression against people on the island who are committed to improving cross-Strait relations, creating a “chilling effect” and harming the legitimate rights, interests, and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Who is thinking of Taiwan’s young people, and who is harming their interests and well-being, is crystal clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301278.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Taiwan legislature recently established a so-called “Constitutional Amendment Committee” and launched a so-called “constitutional amendment project.” Some reports say this round of “constitutional amendment” will not involve the issue of unification or “independence.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We are highly attentive to the relevant developments. We firmly oppose any force in Taiwan that seeks to “amend the constitution to seek independence,” including opening convenient doors for seeking “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301280.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently there was news that the US State Department has approved the sale of three sets of weapons and equipment to Taiwan, and has proposed leasing or selling advanced weapons such as the F-35 to Taiwan to counter the mainland. What is the comment?","The Foreign Ministry already stated its position yesterday. We firmly oppose the United States selling arms to the Taiwan region of China and oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to “use arms to seek independence,” are nothing more than a mantis trying to stop a chariot; they will only bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","October 25 of this year marks the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. Will there be related commemorative activities?","Taiwan has been Chinese territory since ancient times. After the end of World War II, Taiwan, which had been under Japanese colonial rule for 50 years, was recovered on October 25, 1945, and returned to the embrace of the motherland. This was an important achievement of all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, in the joint war of resistance. On the 75th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, compatriots on both sides of the Strait have commemorated the recovery of Taiwan in various ways. This is of great significance for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and for promoting the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland: remembering the historical merits of the martyrs, reviewing the heroic struggle of jointly resisting external aggression, and carrying forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301274.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that the mainland side will closely monitor the KMT’s recent proposals and motions, including its moves to change the party name. Some people within the KMT believe that the purpose of these proposals is to highlight that the DPP authorities’ policies are unworkable, and that they are merely deceiving the public. May I ask the spokesperson whether the mainland side agrees with this…","We have seen this interpretation, and we have also seen another view that says this is a test of the DPP's bottom line. I want to stress that on major issues of right and wrong, testing is not tolerated. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and the fact that the two sides belong to one China is an unchangeable historical and legal fact. We firmly oppose any separatist act that creates so-called “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas,” or “one China, one Taiwan.” Cross-strait affairs are a family matter for compatriots on both sides, and no external interference will be tolerated.\nEveryone should be clear on one point: the fundamental cause of the current tense, complex, and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities collude with external forces and continually take separatist, provocative “Taiwan independence” actions. People of insight and responsible political parties on the island should recognize this clearly, remain highly vigilant, and resolutely oppose it. Any words or deeds that violate the one-China principle and harm the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation will be firmly opposed by all Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Taiwan's relevant authorities have said that they withdrew from the travel fair of the Asia-Pacific Travel Association because the association changed the exhibitor name. Our understanding is that in past years, Taiwan participated in the association's related exhibitions under the name “Taiwan Travel Association.” This year, however, they intended to register under an official name, so the Asia-Pacific Travel…","As everyone is well aware, our basic principle is that Taiwan's participation in the activities of international organizations must be handled under the one-China principle. It is our understanding that the Pacific Asia Travel Association (PATA) is a non-governmental tourism organization among the world's three major tourism organizations. The claims made by relevant parties in Taiwan regarding Taiwan's participation in this association, and the reasons for its failure to attend this year's travel fair, are pure nonsense. The DPP authorities' attempts to challenge the one-China principle in the international community and to seek \"Taiwan independence\" under this pretext will ultimately fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Mainland media recently reported four Taiwan espionage cases, which has drawn public attention. Why were such cases made public at this time, and what considerations lie behind this?","We are following the relevant situation very closely. According to information from the relevant departments, recently the state security organs have organized the special operation “Lightning-2020” (迅雷-2020) to crack down, in accordance with the law, on intelligence infiltration and sabotage activities against the mainland by the DPP authorities and their espionage and intelligence agencies. In recent times, the DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing to elevate their standing, have intensified collusion with external anti-China forces, repeatedly stirred up incidents, and vigorously pursued “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, seriously endangering peace across the Strait and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously endangering national sovereignty, security, and development interests. Relevant parties in Taiwan should conform to the historical trend of a strong country, national rejuvenation, and cross-Strait reunification, and not do anything that harms the overall interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201014_12301277.htm"],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","Reports say the mainland has uncovered hundreds of cases of Taiwan spy espionage. Can the family members of the Taiwan personnel involved who have been arrested apply to visit them, and can Taiwan media go there to interview them?","Taiwan's espionage and intelligence agencies have long targeted the mainland, engaging in large-scale intelligence theft and infiltration and sabotage activities. Relevant mainland judicial organs investigate, prosecute, and try the related cases strictly in accordance with law, and protect the litigation rights of criminal suspects and defendants in accordance with law.\nAs for the question you raised, it is my understanding that the investigative authorities have, as required, notified the families of the persons involved of their detention locations and other circumstances, and have retained lawyers for the persons involved. According to the provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law, cases involving state secrets are not tried in public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾ETtoday东森新闻云记者","The first question: Recently, cross-Strait flights have introduced a new rule requiring a nucleic acid test certificate taken within three days before boarding. A nucleic acid test in Taiwan costs roughly 1,800 yuan RMB. This may impose a certain financial burden on some students or Taiwan youth who want to develop their careers on the mainland. May I ask the spokesperson whether adjustments will be made for…","First, let me explain the regulation you mentioned. Based on the current COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control situation, the relevant competent authorities have decided that, starting from 0:00 on October 12, persons on cross-Strait two-way flights, including those traveling from Taiwan to the mainland and from the mainland to Taiwan, must each present, when boarding, a personal nucleic acid test negative certificate issued by a cross-Strait testing institution within 3 days (72 hours). This is a risk prevention measure taken with high regard and a high sense of responsibility for the life safety and health and well-being of passengers, flight crew, and the broad masses of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the relevant persons traveling across the Strait and the airlines concerned will understand and cooperate, so that we can jointly do well in epidemic prevention and control.\nAs for the two groups you mentioned just now, one is the young student group and the other is the Taiwan business group. We have always warmly welcomed Taiwan youths and firmly supported them in coming to the mainland to share opportunities, seek development, and realize their dreams. However, under the current circumstances in which the global COVID-19 epidemic has not yet been effectively brought under control, in order to ensure the life safety of people on both sides of the Strait, we have adopted relevant epidemic prevention measures, and we still hope to have the understanding and cooperation of our young friends. This is both for their own safety and health and a highly responsible approach to the life safety of people on both sides of the Strait.\nAs for the broad Taiwan business community, at present, in order to ensure the life safety of people on both sides of the Strait, we have adopted some scientific and necessary entry prevention and control measures. Everyone has also noticed that since mid-to-late August, the mainland has detected 4 imported COVID-19 confirmed cases from Taiwan, reflecting that there are loopholes in epidemic prevention and control on the island. At present, how many actual infected persons remain on the island is unclear, which should draw the attention of the people on the island to prevent a rebound of the epidemic. The DPP authorities should adopt responsible epidemic prevention and control measures, cut off the chain of virus transmission, and genuinely safeguard the life safety and health and well-being of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan’s defense authorities plan that starting in 2021, reserve force education week convening will change from the original two sessions of training every eight years to one session of training per year, and the training period will be extended to 14 days. It is also understood that voices calling for the restoration of conscription have emerged on the island. What is the spokesperson’s response?","I think this question may be related to the combat training activities of the People's Liberation Army that have drawn attention recently. First, Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. The relevant combat training activities of the PLA are necessary actions taken to meet the security situation in the Taiwan Strait and to safeguard national sovereignty. They are aimed at the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their separatist acts, and at interference by external forces. They are by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots.\nAs I have already pointed out, the root cause of the complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have colluded with external forces and repeatedly taken \"Taiwan independence\" separatist and provocative actions, seriously harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. For the sake of their party's narrow interests, the DPP authorities have stirred up confrontation across the Strait, attempting to tie Taiwan compatriots to the chariot of \"Taiwan independence\" and drag them into a deep disaster, which fully exposes their vicious political nature. More and more Taiwan compatriots see this very clearly and do not wish to be dragged into the abyss of \"Taiwan independence.\"\nWe have stressed many times that we are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for \"Taiwan independence\" activities in any form. The \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are stirring up trouble and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Compatriots on both sides are bound to oppose them together and resolutely contain them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","广东深圳卫视记者","There are growing signs that the United States is trying to draw Taiwan into its so-called “Asia-Pacific Strategy,” and the DPP authorities are eager to cooperate. What is your view on this?","We emphasize two points. First, both sides of the Strait belong to one China, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and cross-Strait affairs are family matters of compatriots on both sides, and no external interference will be permitted. This is the inherent meaning of the One China principle universally upheld by the international community. Second, the DPP authorities, with intentions of seeking “independence,” are relying on foreign powers to enhance their own standing and depending on external forces to escalate provocations. This will only harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides, harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and place Taiwan in an even more dangerous position.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Some mainland media interpreted Cai Yingwen’s remarks of October 10 as the “softest” she has made since taking office. However, officials and scholars on the mainland have criticized the Cai authorities for still not acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and not acknowledging that both sides belong to one China. As a result, the two sides still lack the political mutual trust needed as a basis, and dialogue cannot…","Regarding the second half of your question, I have already responded to it in answering a question from a reporter of Shenzhen Satellite TV just now. As for the first half of your question, we have already stated our position on the remarks made by the leader of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the head of the island's popular representative body on that day. So-called \"softened tone\" and \"eased language\" are merely carefully designed political language; in substance, they continue the confrontational mindset and hostile consciousness and amount to advocating \"independence.\" It must be emphasized that only by returning to the correct track of the \"1992 Consensus\" political foundation can the two sides resume dialogue and consultation, cross-Strait relations improve, and the Taiwan Strait remain peaceful and stable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","The espionage case the mainland announced this time involves some Taiwan scholars, from both the Blue and the Green camps. In addition, the DPP also wants to amend the “Regulations on Cross-Strait People’s Relations” to tightly control and screen cross-Strait academic exchanges. This has made scholars fearful. Will cross-Strait academic exchanges be made even harder as a result? What is the spokesperson’s view?","On this issue, we must treat it differently. On the one hand, cracking down on criminal acts that endanger national security according to law is to safeguard national security, to maintain normal order in cross-Strait exchanges, and to protect the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. The Taiwan espionage case announced this time is clear in its facts and conclusive in its evidence. On the other hand, for the overwhelming majority of Taiwan compatriots, and for Taiwan compatriots who take part in normal cross-Strait exchange activities, we regard them as our own flesh and blood, and we always work to do practical things for them, do good deeds and resolve difficulties, firmly safeguarding and continually enhancing the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots, hoping to achieve greater and better development together. The DPP authorities, by obstructing and restricting exchanges between compatriots on both sides, are standing against the broad masses of compatriots on both sides and doing the opposite of what we are doing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-14","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","On the 13th, Taiwan's epidemic prevention authorities said that one new imported case from the mainland had been recorded. The confirmed patient returned to Taiwan from Jiangsu on October 11 and was confirmed on the 13th. Please provide an explanation.","We noted the situation yesterday and inquired with the relevant departments. As you mentioned, regarding the confirmed case of this Taiwan resident after returning to Taiwan on the 11th, which was announced by the relevant Taiwan authorities, Jiangsu and other relevant localities are carrying out verification and other necessary work in accordance with the relevant prevention and control plans. The latest information just received is that yesterday, sampling and testing were conducted overnight on more than a thousand employees at the enterprise where the case was located, and no positive cases have been found so far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201014_12301271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 16 — After mainland media reported the Taiwan espionage case, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has repeatedly spread untrue remarks in recent days, baselessly accusing the mainland. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 16th, saying: Regarding the Taiwan espionage case involving the “Xunlei-2020” special operation, the criminal facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive and sufficient. State security organs and relevant judicial organs have handled the case strictly according to law and have protected the criminal suspects' and defendants' lawful rights according to law. The Mainland Affairs Council knows this full well; its claim of “framing Taiwan residents” completely distorts the facts, and it has a guilty conscience.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that, as is well known, because the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and have undermined the common political foundation across the Strait, the communication and liaison mechanisms between the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Mainland Affairs Council, and between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, have been stalled to this day. The Mainland Affairs Council fabricated the lie of “making demands through existing cross-Strait liaison mechanisms,” which completely disregards the facts and openly deceives Taiwan residents.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Mainland Affairs Council's claim that “149 Taiwan compatriots have gone missing on the mainland” seriously deviates from the facts and is malicious hype. In fact, with the assistance of relevant mainland authorities, many so-called “missing Taiwan compatriots” have already contacted their families or returned to Taiwan. On the one hand, the DPP authorities carry out large-scale intelligence theft and infiltration and sabotage activities against the mainland; on the other hand, they muddy the waters and deliberately package a small number of involved persons as people engaged in cross-Strait exchanges, trying to shift blame onto and frame the mainland. Their intentions are malicious.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that facts outweigh sophistry. The DPP authorities should stop political manipulation and stop intelligence infiltration and sabotage activities against the mainland, and not go further and further down the wrong path.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201016_12301642.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-10-19","Zhao Lijian","AFP","According to reports, two Chinese diplomats went to a reception organized by the Taiwanese authorities in Fiji. These was a physical clash between one Chinese diplomat and a Taiwanese official. According to the Taiwanese authorities, the Taiwanese official was beaten up. Can you tell us what exactly happened during this incident?","First of all, there are no \"Taiwanese diplomats\" in Fiji. Fiji has long been committed to the correct position of the one-China principle, and in 2019 asked Taiwan's trade office in Fiji to not use the self-styled name or pursue the \"one China, one Taiwan\" or \"two Chinas\" approach in Fiji. China applauds Fiji for that.\nThe report you cited is totally untrue, and Taiwan was like a thief calling \"stop the thief\". The Taiwanese institution in Fiji blatantly displayed the self-styled flag, and its cake was also decorated with a self-styled flag. The Chinese Embassy to Fiji already published a statement on this matter. China also asked Fiji to have a thorough investigation on it. Fiji said it attached high importance to China's concerns and would stick to the one-China principle and properly settle it.\nI'd like to stress that there's only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. The attempt to sow discord between China and Pacific island countries under the pretext of the Taiwan question is doomed to fail.\nI also want to cite the statement by the Chinese embassy in Fiji. The truth is, the Taipei Trade Office in Fiji publicly held the so-called \"National Day\" event on the evening of October 8, which severely violated the one-China principle and the Fijian government's regulations regarding Taiwan. Taiwan's intention was to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" on the international stage. On that very evening, the staff of the Taipei Trade Office in Fiji spoke and acted provocatively against the Chinese Embassy staff who were carrying out their official duties in the public area of the same hotel where the \"event\" was held. One Chinese diplomat was injured with the belongings also damaged. We have expressed our serious concerns to the Fijian side about the above incidents, requesting the country to carry out thorough investigation into the incident and hold the perpetrators of the Taiwan region accountable according to law. We believe Fiji will settle this issue in a just and proper manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202010/t20201019_693423.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202010/t20201019_5419430.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-20","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Support is growing within Indian government to formally start talks on a trade deal with Taiwan. This is according to a Bloomberg reported. What's the Foreign Ministry's comment on this push to formally start trade talks with Taiwan?","There is only one China and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community, including India, and also serves as the political foundation for China to develop relations with any other country. China is firmly opposed to any official exchanges of any form and the signing of any agreement of official nature between Taiwan and any country having diplomatic relations with China. The Indian side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and handle the Taiwan question prudently and properly.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1825401.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1825370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-20","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","After the incident in Fuji, Taiwanese officials said that China's diplomats are acting like hooligans with barbaric actions. What is your comment?","They're just making false accusations to shift blame and talking nonsense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1825401.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1825370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-22","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The Pentagon said on Wednesday that the United States has approved the potential sales of three weapons systems to Taiwan that could have a total value of 1.8 billion dollars. What is your comment on this potential sales?","The United States seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, by selling arms to the Taiwan region. It seriously interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests, sends out gravely wrong signals to Taiwan independence forces and severely undermines China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes it.\nChina urges the US side to fully recognize the very damaging nature of arms sales to Taiwan, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military ties with the Taiwan region, cancel its arms sales plans to avoid further harming China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability. China will make a legitimate and necessary reaction in the light of the development of the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1825949.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1825922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-22","Zhao Lijian","FSN","About US arms sales to Taiwan. Taiwan said it does not want to engage in arms race with China. It just wants to build credible capabilities for defense. Do you have any response?","If they truly don’t want to engage in an arms race, then they should match their words with actions, instead of saying one thing and doing the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1825949.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1825922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-10-22","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency stated on October 21 that the U.S. State Department had approved arms sales to Taiwan totaling more than US$1.8 billion. What is your comment on this?","The US sale of weapons to Taiwan seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué. It seriously interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously undermines China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously damages China-US and military-to-military relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and is vital to China's core interests. China strongly urges the US to immediately cancel its arms sales plan to Taiwan, halt US-Taiwan military ties, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, so as to avoid serious consequences for China-US military-to-military relations and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If the US side ignores the basic norms of international relations, goes back on its word, and insists on acting recklessly, China will certainly respond with resolute countermeasures.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/15935983.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278499.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2020-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 22 (dispatch): In response to the U.S. government's just-announced approval of a plan to sell weapons to Taiwan worth about 1.8 billion U.S. dollars, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 22nd, saying that we have consistently and firmly opposed U.S. arms sales to the Chinese Taiwan region. The U.S. side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the \"August 17\" Communiqué, and stop all arms sales to Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities' attempt to purchase arms from the United States in order to \"resist reunification by force\" and to provoke \"independence\" will only seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to stop all forms of collusion with the United States and not to go further and further down the road of \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201022_12302540.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 23 — The DPP authorities once said their cross-Strait policy would be “non-provocative,” but Taiwan’s defense department recently boasted that the US had approved three arms sales plans for Taiwan, “two of which missiles and rockets can hit the coast of the mainland.” Asked about this on the 23rd, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said this claim fully confirms that “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are a real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities’ so-called “non-provocation” lie has once again been exposed. They openly carry out naked military provocations and threats against the mainland, overestimating themselves and courting their own destruction.\nZhu Fenglian said we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities’ constant escalation of provocations in pursuit of “independence” will ultimately lead only to a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201023_12302860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-10-26","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency released a statement on October 21, saying that the Department of State has approved arms sales worth of about $1.8 billion to Taiwan. The Chinese foreign ministry spokesperson said on October 22 that China will make legitimate, necessary response according to how the situation develops. Has China taken any step yet?","As China pointed out on multiple occasions, the U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and seriously undermine China's sovereignty and security interests. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns it.\nTo uphold national interests, China decides to take necessary measures to sanction U.S. companies involved in the arms sales to Taiwan including Lockheed Martin, Boeing Defense, Space & Security (BDS) and Raytheon, as well as the U.S. individuals and entities who played an egregious role in the process.\nOnce again we urge the United States to strictly fulfill its commitment to the one-China principle and observe the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop selling weapons to Taiwan or having any military ties with it. We will continue taking necessary measures to safeguard national sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202010/t20201026_693454.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1826627.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-10-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 26 — As the mainland solemnly commemorates the 70th anniversary of the Chinese People's Volunteers' going abroad to fight in the War to Resist U.S. Aggression and Aid Korea, Su Zhenchang claimed “do not use war to threaten the Taiwan people.” TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to this on the 26th, saying that Su Zhenchang is accustomed to turning black into white, deliberately stirring up cross-Strait confrontation and intimidating Taiwan residents, with sinister intent.\nZhu said that the greatest current threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities colluding ever more closely with external forces and continuously provoking with “Taiwan independence.” Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood kin, and “Taiwan independence” is the greatest scourge for Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are attempting to kidnap Taiwan compatriots onto the “Taiwan independence” war chariot and drag them into deep disaster. Broad Taiwan compatriots will not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201026_12303368.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-10-27","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The United States on Monday said it approved a $2.4 billion sale of 100 Harpoon Coastal Defense Systems to Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, seriously undermine China's sovereignty and security interests, send out wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and gravely undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes them.\nChina urges the United States to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military ties with the Taiwan region, and cancel its arms sale plan to avoid further damaging China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability. China will take legitimate and necessary actions to firmly safeguard its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1827017.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1826997.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-10-27","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","U.S. Ambassador to the United Nations Kelly Craft attacked China's cooperation with the UN in an article published by New York Post. She also wrote that the United States, with all its actions, is not retreating from multilateralism, but preserving the multilateral system. What's China's comment?","The article by U.S. Ambassador to the UN Kelly Craft once again shows the ignorance and bias of some American politicians. As a permanent member of the UN Security Council and the second largest contributor to the UN regular budget and peacekeeping budget, China firmly upholds multilateralism, supports the work of the UN, and defends the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. While attending the series of high-level meetings to mark the 75th anniversary of the UN, President Xi Jinping announced a range of new major initiatives and measures, demonstrating China's support for multilateralism and sense of responsibility towards world peace and development. The United States, however, has not only been following unilateralism itself, but also criticizing other countries' cooperation with the UN by wantonly distorting facts. With regard to the erroneous allegations by Craft, I would like to stress the following three points:\nFirst, international staff members from various countries are all part and parcel of the UN team. They fulfill their duties according to the collective will of member states and are subject to the supervision of member states. With widely-recognized capability and professionalism, they make important contributions to the UN cause and deserve to be respected. Craft's groundless allegation is an insult to all of them. The spokesperson of the UN secretary-general has responded, saying Secretary-General António Guterres has good cooperation with the heads of the International Civil Aviation Organization and the International Telecommunications Union and does not doubt that they work to serve the interests of the UN. The UN system currently has 2,531 staff members from the United States, including 19 under-secretary-generals and assistant-secretary-generals, more than any other member state. Can their integrity stand Craft's scrutiny?\nSecond, some U.S. politicians such as Craft chose to provoke confrontation among great powers and interfere in the internal affairs of other countries at the UN, which is deeply unpopular. At the third Committee of the UN General Assembly, representatives of a small number of countries, including Craft, maliciously discredited China during their deliberations on human rights issues. China sternly refuted this with facts and truth and won the support of more than 70 countries. This fully proves that more and more countries, after learning the true face of the United States-a troublemaker, acted to oppose hegemony and political confrontation. I would like to know just how much longer can Craft persist in ignoring the voices of most countries?\nThird, Craft seems quite complacent about her behavior of interfering in China's internal affairs through issues relating to Xinjiang, Hong Kong, and Taiwan. She can tell lies with such pretense and no scruples at all, not knowing that she has already violated international law and the basic norms of international relations. The first order of business for Craft is to understand the territorial space of the United States and its own responsibilities, instead of preaching nonsense and using lies as a weapon. Problems facing the United States will not be solved and the it will not be made great again by this.\nWe are in the 21st century and no one can and should return to the old path of Cold War confrontation of the 20th century. As mankind fights against COVID-19 and faces more and more global challenges, we have no other choice but to hold consultation as equals and strengthen cooperation to uphold multilateralism and safeguard the UN-centered international system. We hope Craft and other American politicians will mend their misguided ways and truly do their job.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1827017.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1826997.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-10-27","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. State Department has decided to approve the sale to Taiwan of the “Harpoon” missile system and related equipment, with an estimated total value of US$2.37 billion. Just a few days ago, the U.S. administration approved three other arms sales plans to Taiwan totaling more than US$1.8 billion. What is your comment on this?","Recently, the U.S. government again approved arms sales to Taiwan, seriously violating the One-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously interfering in China's internal affairs, seriously harming China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously undermining China-U.S. relations, relations between the two militaries, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and is a core interest of China. It brooks absolutely no foreign interference. Some in the United States and in the Taiwan region who seek to use Taiwan to contain China and refuse unification by force will not succeed; in the end, they will surely meet a dead end. China strongly urges the United States to immediately cancel its arms sales plan to Taiwan, halt military contacts between the United States and Taiwan and the sale of weapons to Taiwan, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, so as to avoid causing serious consequences for China-U.S. relations, relations between the two militaries, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese People's Liberation Army has firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to thwart any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes. It will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and continue to advance the process of national unification.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/qwfb/4873330.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2020-10-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 27 dispatch: In response to the US government's announcement on October 27 that it had approved the sale to Taiwan of arms worth approximately 2.37 billion US dollars, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said the same day in response to a question: The US government has time and again violated the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, particularly the provisions of the \"August 17\" Communiqué, by selling arms to the Taiwan region of China and sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces. We firmly oppose this. The DPP authorities, stubbornly \"seeking independence through arms,\" will only further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and bring greater calamity to the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201027_12303533.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO press conference. We will now begin the question session.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","央视海峡两岸记者","Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation of the mainland’s solemn commemoration of the 75th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, and what is the significance of holding these commemorative activities under the current situation in cross-Strait relations?","This year marks the 75th anniversary of victory in the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. On October 22, relevant departments on the mainland held an academic symposium commemorating the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, which was attended by Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, who delivered an important speech. More than 100 compatriots from both sides of the Strait attended the symposium, which conducted in-depth discussions around the theme of “commemorating the restoration of Taiwan and advancing the reunification of the motherland.” On October 25, the “Golden Bowl Intact — Thematic Exhibition Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration” opened at the National Museum of China.\nThe holding of these commemorative activities is of great significance for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly remember history, learn from the past and understand the present, carry forward the great national spirit, share the national responsibility, jointly promote the reunification of the motherland, and jointly realize the great dream of national rejuvenation. The restoration of Taiwan was an important achievement of the victory in the War of Resistance, a great victory forged through the successive, blood-soaked struggles of all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots. The history of Taiwan's restoration irrefutably proves that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are a community of shared destiny, sharing weal and woe.\nAt present, cross-Strait relations are complex and severe. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have intensified their collusion with external forces and continuously engaged in provocations seeking “independence,” seriously endangering the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the interests and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots. We hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the trend of the times and the situation, recognize benefit and harm, distinguish truth from falsehood, follow the historical trend, share historical responsibility, and join hands with mainland compatriots to firmly hold the fate of the nation in their own hands.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303689.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","We understand that a thematic exhibition marking the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration was recently held in Beijing. Could you introduce the considerations behind holding this exhibition and the situation of the exhibits?","The theme exhibition “Golden Bowl Intact: Theme Exhibition Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan’s Restoration” opened on October 25 at the National Museum of China. The exhibition displays a total of more than 160 sets of cultural relics from the National Museum’s collection and more than 50 sets of copies of important documents and archives since the Qing dynasty. These include, for the first time on display, Qing-era official documents of the 宏字练军 (Hong Zi Lian Jun) troops, the “Outline of the Taiwan Takeover Plan” drafted on the eve of Taiwan’s restoration, and the writing brush used by the Chinese government representative at the Taiwan Province surrender ceremony of the China Theater of War. These historical documents and precious cultural relics systematically reproduce the course of Taiwan compatriots’ heroic resistance to Japanese colonial rule, the bloody struggle of all Chinese people, and the restoration of Taiwan to the motherland. They powerfully prove that Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and powerfully reveal that national rejuvenation and national reunification are the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people.\nThe purpose of holding this theme exhibition is to commemorate the major historical event of Taiwan’s restoration, review the heroic struggle of Taiwan compatriots against Japanese invasion and colonial rule and the victory won by compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly defending against foreign aggression, carry forward the great national spirit, highlight that the mainland and Taiwan are an inseparable community of shared destiny, and inspire compatriots on both sides to remember history, honor the martyrs, jointly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, share the righteous cause of the nation, jointly promote national reunification, and jointly realize the great dream of national rejuvenation.\nThe theme exhibition is expected to run for two months, after which the National Museum will continue to display it online. Compatriots on both sides are welcome to visit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303688.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","At the academic symposium commemorating the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, the cross-Strait guests in attendance put forward several proposals, including sharing historical materials across the Strait, jointly writing the history of the War of Resistance, and jointly condemning the DPP authorities for promoting the “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines and glorifying Japan's colonial rule and…","The cross-Strait guests attending the meeting put forward many suggestions, which we believe are very positive.\nWe support encouraging historians on both sides of the Strait to actively play a role in setting the record straight, and to strengthen research on the history of the War of Resistance against Japan and the history of Taiwan’s restoration. Through sharing historical sources, co-writing histories, and co-compiling textbooks, we should critique, on scholarly grounds, the various “Taiwan independence” historical views, and enhance Taiwan compatriots’ identification with the nation, the state, and Chinese culture.\nThe DPP authorities are vigorously pursuing “de-Sinicization” and promoting the “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines. They deliberately distort Chinese history, attempting to sever cultural ties across the Strait and to deceive the Taiwan public with this. This has caused confusion in the historical memory of Taiwan’s younger generation and distortion of their national identity, which requires a high degree of vigilance. We note that many teachers and parents in Taiwan strongly oppose the middle-school history textbooks compiled according to the “new curriculum guidelines” fabricated by the DPP authorities. As a parent, I feel great sympathy for Taiwan’s children. In their textbooks, there is “no Records of the Grand Historian, no Book of Han, no knowledge of the Three Kingdoms or the Northern and Southern Dynasties, and no knowing what the restoration of Taiwan means.” In the future, they will not know why temples worship Guan Di, the Sage Lord, or how the artifacts of the National Palace Museum in Taipei came to be, and they will be unable to “know the rise and fall of dynasties and understand their gains and losses.”\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides belong to the same Chinese nation. No one can deprive Taiwan compatriots of their rights as sons and daughters of China. Any act of “de-Sinicization” cannot sever the historical ties across the Strait, and cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities, acting recklessly and forgetting their ancestors, will certainly meet strong opposition from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303687.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, a “Taiwan Strait Security” public opinion poll jointly conducted by the Taiwan International Strategic Studies Association and the International Studies Association shows that 94% of respondents hope the two sides can live in peace, more than 80% of the public support cross-strait exchanges, and only 2.6% support confrontation. How does the spokesperson view this figure?","Support for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has always been the mainstream public opinion of compatriots on both sides. Despite deliberate obstruction by the DPP authorities and the impact of the epidemic, from January to September this year, exchange activities in all areas across the Taiwan Strait have continued in various forms, and cross-Strait trade volume and Taiwanese investment in the mainland have continued to grow. Compatriots on both sides want to exchange, cooperate, and develop; this is the will of the people and the trend of the times, and no person or force can stop it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, DPP members Chen Ting-fei and Chen Po-wei of the Radical Progressive Party took the lead in putting forward so-called “constitutional amendment” proposals with a clear “Taiwan independence” color. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","A small handful of “Taiwan independence” elements have repeatedly manipulated “constitutional revision to pursue independence,” provoking trouble and seeking to gain personal political advantage. Responsible political parties and figures on the island should not tolerate or indulge such provocations, which disregard the interests of the public and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303686.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Some Taiwan media outlets with particular positions have continued to hype up claims that the mainland is spreading false information through “collaborators” on the island in order to build a so-called “pro-China ruling alliance” and carry out “infiltration and division” of Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","These claims are entirely fabricated out of thin air, with ulterior motives.\nDue to historical and realistic reasons, indeed many Taiwan compatriots still lack understanding and knowledge of the mainland. Between people, what matters is sincerity. We actively promote exchanges in all fields across the Strait precisely so that compatriots on both sides can learn from each other, engage in dialogue with tolerance, deepen mutual understanding, and enhance mutual trust and recognition.\nThe DPP authorities and some irresponsible media on the island have long habitually smeared and vilified the mainland in various ways, using every means to obstruct and restrict civilian exchanges across the Strait, and on a large scale suppressing people engaged in cross-Strait exchanges and media that objectively report on the mainland. They seek to fool the island's public and deprive them of their right to “know.” Such retrograde actions are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303681.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the U.S. Center for Strategic and International Studies published a report on Taiwan advocating the strengthening of “U.S.-Taiwan relations,” and stated that relevant Taiwan institutions provided support for the release of this report. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We firmly oppose the United States developing official relations with Taiwan region of China. Sectors of American society, including think tanks, should urge the U.S. government to abide by the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, properly handle the Taiwan question, and not send wrong signals to the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" forces. It is futile for the DPP authorities to use the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents to buy off think tanks and to concoct and spread \"pro-Taiwan\" arguments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303685.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","According to reports, on October 23, more than 20 mainland fishing boats, having encountered winds of force 7 to 10, sought to enter islands near Penghu to take shelter from the wind, but were forcibly driven away by Taiwan's coast guard. What comment do you have?","For many years, the mainland has set up Taiwan fishermen reception stations and reception points at many places along the coast to provide shelter, resupply, emergency rescue, and other assistance to Taiwan fishing boats and fishermen. By comparison, the inhumane practice of Taiwan’s relevant side brutally driving away mainland fishing boats seeking shelter from the wind is very outrageous.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","It is understood that the online promotion and matching event for “Taiwan-invested enterprises expanding into the domestic market,” a special session for Guangdong, is about to be held, and some other provinces and municipalities are also preparing cross-Strait economic and trade activities. Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the specific details.","To implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on promoting the integrated development of cross-Strait relations, to carry out the central government's overall deployment for epidemic prevention and control and economic and social development, and to help Taiwan-funded enterprises integrate into the new development pattern of domestic great circulation as the main body, with domestic and international circulations reinforcing each other, the Ministry of Commerce and the Taiwan Affairs Office jointly guided relevant localities in holding a series of online promotion and matchmaking events on \"Taiwan-funded enterprises expanding domestic sales.\"\nThe first matchmaking event was held in Fujian on July 3, with a hundred Taiwan enterprises and more than 200 mainland enterprises participating. It produced more than 1,000 effective matches and letters of intent for signing amounting to nearly 1 billion yuan. The second matchmaking event was held in Shandong on September 15, attracting 102 Taiwan enterprises and 115 mainland enterprises, and producing letters of intent for signing amounting to nearly 400 million yuan. The event you mentioned is the third matchmaking event, which will be held in Guangdong tomorrow. More than 200 Taiwan-funded enterprises and mainland enterprises will carry out promotion and matchmaking combining online and offline formats. We welcome enterprises and the public on both sides of the Strait to follow the official website of the Guangdong Provincial Department of Commerce (http://guangdong.mofcom.gov.cn) and the website of the Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange Association (http://aetats.mofcom.gov.cn) for relevant information.\nEntering November, cross-Strait economic and trade activities will also be lively. On November 11, the 2020 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit Innovation and Development Seminar will be held in Nanjing, Jiangsu. Cross-Strait entrepreneurs will explore how to help Taiwan-funded enterprises grasp the pulse of mainland economic development, deepen cooperation with mainland enterprises, and seek common development. Hainan, Zhejiang, Fujian, Guangxi and other places will successively hold economic and trade events such as the Sanya Taiwan Businessmen Summit, the Zhejiang-Taiwan Cooperation Week, the Cross-Strait Machinery Industry Expo, and the Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum, continuing to promote cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and to facilitate integrated development across the Strait. We welcome people from all walks of life on both sides to participate actively, and we welcome media friends to follow and report on these events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303683.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, in the past week the United States has made two arms sales to Taiwan, including some offensive weapons. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond? Second, Singapore’s Changi Experience Studio labeled Taiwan as “Chinese Taiwan,” and relevant parties in Taiwan sent a letter demanding that the organizer correct it. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond?","First, the US government has repeatedly and again and again violated the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, in particular the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué, by selling arms to the Taiwan region of China, sending a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces. We firmly oppose this. Everyone has seen the statements made by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Taiwan Affairs Office the day before yesterday and yesterday. The DPP authorities are openly making naked military threats and provocations against the mainland, overestimating themselves and attempting to collude with external forces to “seek independence by force,” intensifying tensions across the Taiwan Strait. This will only seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, bring profound disaster to the Taiwan people, and will ultimately lead to a dead end.\nSecond, the international community generally adheres to the one-China principle. Singapore acts in accordance with the one-China principle, which is a matter of course.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Starting October 15, “Taobao Taiwan” suspended functions such as user orders, merchant onboarding, and product listings. Following the removal of iQIYI and Tencent Video, the DPP authorities have again forced out “Taobao Taiwan.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","I recall that a year ago, “Taobao Taiwan” went online in Taiwan, serving Taiwan residents and businesses locally and bringing them real convenience and benefits. Less than a year later, “Taobao Taiwan” was forced to exit the Taiwan market. The DPP authorities have engaged in political manipulation, obstructing and restricting cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and attempting to create a cross-Strait “decoupling.” What is directly harmed can only be the well-being and interests of Taiwan's people and businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Since the epidemic began this year, various localities and departments on the mainland have introduced a series of measures to assist Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. Please introduce the implementation of these beneficial policies and measures.","Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, we have thoroughly implemented the deployment by the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council to coordinate the work of epidemic prevention and control and economic and social development, and have actively assisted Taiwan businesses and enterprises in carrying out epidemic prevention and control and resuming work and production. On May 15, the National Development and Reform Commission, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and 8 other departments, a total of 10 departments, jointly issued the “Notice on Responding to the Epidemic, Coordinating the Development of Taiwan-Funded Enterprises and Promoting Work Related to Taiwan-Funded Projects,” which proposed 11 specific measures, including continuing to help Taiwan-funded enterprises resume work and production, coordinating and advancing major Taiwan-funded projects, actively supporting Taiwan-funded enterprises in expanding capital and capacity, and promoting Taiwan-funded enterprises’ participation in new and traditional infrastructure construction. The “11 measures” are in direct continuity with the “31 measures” and the “26 measures.” All of them are aimed at providing development opportunities and equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises, and at offering precise and effective support to enterprises in response to new problems caused by the epidemic.\nRelevant departments and localities have actively implemented policies and measures to help Taiwan businesses and enterprises enjoy on an equal footing the mainland’s relief and enterprise-support policies, so as to overcome the adverse effects of the epidemic as soon as possible. The Ministry of Commerce and the Taiwan Affairs Office jointly guided relevant localities to hold three online promotion and matching series events for “Taiwan-invested enterprises expanding domestic sales” from July to October. Beijing, Shanghai and other localities have helped Taiwan enterprises enjoy relief policies such as employee training subsidies on an equal footing. Zhejiang, Guangdong and other localities have helped Taiwan businesspeople and their relatives use “livestream e-commerce” and “short videos” to expand the domestic market. In Kunshan, Jiangsu, the policy of not temporarily collecting withholding income tax on profits distributed by foreign investors for direct reinvestment was implemented, and deferred tax preference for reinvestment amounting to 47.8 million yuan was granted to 7 Taiwan enterprises.\nAt present, the overall production and operations of Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland are stable, and many enterprises have achieved significant growth. Facing complex factors such as the impact of the epidemic and the countercurrent of economic globalization, the advantages of the mainland’s vast market space and strong development resilience have become even more evident. GDP grew by 3.2 percent in the second quarter and by 4.9 percent in the third quarter, showing a stable growth trend. Total imports and exports in the first three quarters reached 23.12 trillion yuan, a record high for the same period in history. The International Monetary Fund recently forecast that the global economy will contract by 4.4 percent this year, but the mainland economy will grow by 1.9 percent, becoming the only major economy to achieve positive growth. Recently, the “Implementation Plan for Comprehensive Reform Pilots in Shenzhen Building a Pioneering Demonstration Zone of Socialism with Chinese Characteristics (2020–2025)” was released, and the “Outline Plan for Building the Chengdu-Chongqing Twin-City Economic Circle” was deliberated. These are new opportunities and benefits for Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises. Against the backdrop of increasing instability and uncertainty in the external environment, Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises who seize the development opportunities on the mainland and move forward with the momentum will certainly achieve greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201028_12303684.htm"],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","A UNI Air charter flight recently was ordered to turn back by the Hong Kong Flight Information Region Control Centre while en route to Pratas Island (Dongsha). This shows that the mainland can cut off the links between Taiwan and Pratas Island at any time, making it difficult for the island to be garrisoned or resupplied. The mainland has said that, regarding the inherent territory in the South China Sea, both…","Your inference is baseless. Regarding the return of the Uni Air charter flight, the Hong Kong Civil Aviation Department has already issued an explanation. I suggest you read it carefully.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央广记者","According to island media reports, a Czech arms company briefed on artillery and other weapons in Taiwan in October, but its headquarters then received a warning from the Chinese Embassy in the Czech Republic. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any country selling arms to the Taiwan region of China or conducting any form of military contact with Taiwan. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “resist unification by force” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, some scholars on the island listed “eight pieces of evidence” and claimed that cross-Strait relations have entered a “quasi-state of war.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. The DPP authorities colluding with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces, and intensifying provocations to seek “independence,” is the root cause of the current complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait. I will only reiterate one point: our will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock, and we will leave no space whatsoever for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan media reported that a Hong Kong resident surnamed Li, who violated the purpose of his residence, illegally followed and filmed Hong Kong “student movement” figures in Taiwan during his stay, in violation of the “Hong Kong and Macao Regulations” and other provisions, and was forcibly expelled. May I ask for your comment on this?","We firmly oppose the DPP authorities interfering in Hong Kong affairs in any way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾ETToday东森新闻云记者","Recently, reports have emerged of large numbers of mainland sand dredgers appearing near Nangan in Matsu, and residents feel it is like a “siege of the island.” Some voices in Taiwan suggest that this may be the PLA rehearsing the requisition of civilian vessels. May I ask the spokesperson for an evaluation?","I am not aware of the specific situation you mention. Isn't it precisely because the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have continually engaged in provocations aimed at seeking “independence” that the people of Taiwan have all sorts of associations or worries, and that tensions in the Taiwan Strait have been created?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","The 7th of next month marks the fifth anniversary of the meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Strait. Cross-Strait relations have changed greatly over these five years. May I ask the spokesperson whether the leaders on both sides may in the future create opportunities to meet and hold talks, and what the preconditions for this would be?","As everyone knows, in November 2015, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the two sides achieved a historic meeting between their leaders. Do you think the current atmosphere and conditions across the Strait are in place?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-10-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","I would like to follow up once more on the question of Dongsha Island. Recently, the PLA conducted exercises in Fujian and Guangdong, and then the UNI Air charter flight turned back. Connecting these clues, may I ask the spokesperson: does the PLA plan to seize Dongsha Island?","The clues you mentioned are numerous, but the inference you draw is a hypothetical question. I may decline to answer, but I would like to reiterate our basic position. We have the determination and capability to defeat any “Taiwan independence” provocation, to resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202010/t20201028_12303699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-10-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Some media recently reported that the PLA had taken new moves to deter the “Taiwan independence”. J-20 stealth fighters have been spotted at the Quzhou Airport in Zhejiang Province, which is only 500 kilometers away from Taiwan, and the Dongfeng-17 hypersonic missiles have been deployed along the southeast coast. Can you confirm and comment on that?","The specific location of weapons and equipment is a matter of military secret. What I can tell you is that the PLA has the capability and determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and defeat any form of separatist attempts for “Taiwan independence”. Here, I want to warn those “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that there is no way out for confrontation, and the use of force to seek “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Overrating themselves and attempting something impossible can only hasten their own destruction.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-11/01/content_4873600.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2020-10-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, Canada’s Minister of National Defense Harjit Sajjan said this month that NATO needs to “monitor” China’s activities as the actions that it has been “demonstrating in the South China Sea are obviously concerning”. Taiwan media also reported that a guided-missile frigate of the Royal Canadian Navy had sailed across the Taiwan Strait during China’s National Day holiday. What’s your…","Canada is located thousands of miles away from the South China Sea. As an outside country, Canada has made irresponsible remarks and groundless accusations against China. Its move is indeed worrying. We want to remind the Canadian side to take a closer look at itself before clamoring to monitor other countries.\nRegarding the high-profile sailing of the Canadian warship through the Taiwan Strait and its provocative actions in the process, we think this is an expression of unfriendliness. China has lodged solemn representations with Canada. Undoubtedly, this makes the already poor bilateral ties and mil-to-mil relationship even worse. China asks the Canadian side to take a responsible attitude and be cautious in its words and actions, so as not to undermine the common interests of both countries and regional peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2020-11/01/content_4873600.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2020-10-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 29 (Electronic dispatch): On the 28th, a Taiwan epidemic prevention agency confirmed that a Taiwan businessman who had previously been announced as a confirmed case after returning to Taiwan from Jiangsu was in fact not infected, and that the test result was the result of a specimen mix-up. The medical record has now been removed. Public opinion holds that this amounts to giving the mainland's disease control authorities a measure of justice. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 29th, saying that this is not the first time that the relevant Taiwan authorities have made a problem in confirming cases. Since the outbreak of the epidemic, we have repeatedly stressed that people's lives and health are not a game, that case confirmation must be scientific and rigorous, must not be mixed with political factors, and must not become a tool for political manipulation.\nZhu Fenglian said that on February 3 this year, a Taiwan compatriot returning from Wuhan to Taiwan was announced by a Taiwan epidemic prevention agency as a confirmed case, which triggered hype, fueled rumors and attacks on the mainland's epidemic prevention and control work on the island, and also became a pretext used by the DPP authorities at the time to obstruct Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei from returning home. Yet this Taiwan compatriot was not informed of the confirmation at the first opportunity, nor was he arranged to receive any treatment. Based on the actual situation it knew, the Wuhan Taiwan Affairs Office immediately questioned Taiwan's confirmation determination, and, out of the needs of epidemic prevention and control and concern for the health of Taiwan compatriots, raised seven questions from a professional standpoint, demanding that the Taiwan epidemic prevention agency promptly provide specific and accurate, truthful explanations. Yet the Taiwan side has consistently evaded the matter up to now and remained silent.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Taiwan compatriot who returned to Taiwan from Kunshan, Jiangsu, was wrongly confirmed by the Taiwan side, which has both caused distress and harm to this compatriot and caused Kunshan City to expend a great deal of manpower and material resources, conducting 2,000 nucleic acid tests and environmental disinfection overnight. After Kunshan authorities announced that the nucleic acid test results for all relevant persons were negative, nearly another half month passed before the Taiwan epidemic prevention agency finally acknowledged that this Taiwan compatriot had been wrongly confirmed. We hope the relevant parties in Taiwan will take this as a lesson, and that the proper approach to epidemic prevention and control is to uphold a rigorous scientific attitude and professional spirit. They should also sincerely say \"sorry\" to this Taiwan compatriot.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202010/t20201029_12303921.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-04","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The U.S. State Department on Tuesday approved the proposed sale of MQ-9B drones from General Atomics in a $600 million deal. The sale is the first one approved since the Trump administration eased export restrictions on armed drones in July. We're wondering if the foreign ministry has any comment on this?","China's position on the U.S. arms sales to Taiwan is consistent and clear. I'd like to stress again that the U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, constitute blatant interference in China's internal affairs, seriously undermine China's sovereignty and security interests, send out wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and gravely undercut China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes such acts.\nChina urges the United States to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military ties with the Taiwan region, and immediately cancel its arms sale plan to avoid further damaging China-US relations and cross-strait peace and stability. China will take legitimate and necessary reactions to firmly safeguard national sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1829367.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1829336.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-11-04","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, on November 3 the U.S. approved the sale of four MQ-9 drones to Taiwan, with a total value of about US$600 million. What is your comment on this?","The US arms sales to Taiwan seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. They seriously endanger China's sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity, seriously challenge China's core interests, and seriously damage China-US relations between the two militaries and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this and strongly condemns it.\nThe Taiwan question involves China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China's core interests. No foreign interference will be tolerated. ‘Using Taiwan to contain China’ and ‘using force to resist reunification’ will ultimately only be a praying mantis trying to block a chariot, a dead end. We demand that the US fully recognize the grave harm of its arms sales to Taiwan, immediately cancel any arms sales plan to Taiwan, stop arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military ties, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, so as not to cause immeasurable and serious consequences for China-US relations between the two militaries and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Those who play with fire will burn themselves. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will never allow anyone or any force to split the sacred territory of the motherland. If anyone insists on going their own way, we will certainly deliver a head-on blow.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/15939080.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278500.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2020-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 4 — In response to the announcement by the U.S. government on November 4 that it had approved the sale to Taiwan of 4 MQ-9B unmanned aerial vehicles and other weapons worth about 600 million U.S. dollars, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to questions the same day: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China. We demand that the U.S. side abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the \"August 17\" Communiqué, and stop its wrongful practice of selling arms to Taiwan. U.S. arms sales to Taiwan will only cause serious harm to peace in the Taiwan Strait and send wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, who seek \"independence\" through force, will only push the Taiwan people into disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201104_12304933.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 9 — On November 9, the resumed session of the 73rd World Health Assembly was held by video. The meeting again decided not to place Taiwan-related proposals on the agenda. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions the same day, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Our position on the issue of Taiwan regional participation in WHO activities is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The resumed 73rd World Health Assembly’s decision once again not to place Taiwan-related proposals on the agenda fully demonstrates that the one-China principle is a common consensus and international norm of the international community. “Two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” in the international arena is unpopular and is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201110_12305882.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-11","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan's deputy minister of economic affairs is set to lead a delegation to the United States for the Taiwan-U.S. Economic Prosperity Partnership Dialogue with U.S. Undersecretary of State Keith Krach on November 20. Do you have any comment on this visit?","China consistently opposes official exchanges between the US and the Taiwan region. We urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiques, stop all forms of official exchanges and contacts with Taiwan, stop elevating its relationship with the Taiwan region in any substantive way, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and send no misleading signals to the Taiwan separatist forces, so as to avoid serious damage to China-U.S. relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Enlisting support from external forces will not help build up their unjust cause, and no one and no attempt will succeed in sabotaging the relations between the mainland and the Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202011/t20201111_693480.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1831504.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Welcome everyone to the press conference. We will now begin the questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The “Recommendations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Formulating the Proposals for the Fourteenth Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development and the Long-Range Objectives Through the Year 2035” sets out plans and arrangements for “promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland.” May I ask the spokesperson for his…","The Recommendations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Formulating the 14th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development and the Long-Range Objectives Through the Year 2035, adopted at the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, lists “promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification” as an important component of the 14th Five-Year Plan and the long-range objectives through 2035. It sets out the goals and tasks for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification in the new journey of building a modern socialist country in all respects, reflecting the strategic position of Taiwan work in the process of national rejuvenation. We will thoroughly study and understand the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee, fully implement General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important exposition on Taiwan work, make vigorous and proactive efforts to do Taiwan work well in the new era, solidly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and resolutely advance the process of national reunification.\nThe 14th Five-Year Plan period is the first five years after China has completed the building of a moderately prosperous society in all respects and achieved the first centenary goal, when China, seizing the momentum, embarks on the new journey of building a modern socialist country in all respects and marches toward the second centenary goal. The high-quality development of the mainland economy, and the accelerated construction of a new development paradigm with the domestic circulation as the mainstay and with domestic and international circulations mutually reinforcing each other, will provide more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises to develop on the mainland.\nWe will adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, continue to promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, deepen integrated development across the Strait, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. We will uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” continue to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises on a broader scale and in wider fields. We will continue to implement and refine the policies and measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, and continuously improve the relevant institutional arrangements and policy measures. We will actively promote higher quality and greater efficiency in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, helping Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan’s young people, pursue their dreams on the mainland.\nAt present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause is that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have repeatedly engaged in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” seriously harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We will uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and firmly oppose and deter any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nWe hope that Taiwan compatriots will fully understand the grand blueprint for the country’s future development drawn up in the Recommendations and the enormous development space it unlocks, seize opportunities, actively promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and devote themselves to the just cause of jointly pursuing national reunification and jointly promoting national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306172.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","On November 6, the \"Symposium Marking the 5th Anniversary of the Historic Meeting Between the Leaders on Both Sides of the Strait\" was held in Beijing. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, what is the important significance of holding this symposium?","On November 7, 2015, the leaders of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait met for the first time since 1949. This was a landmark event in the history of cross-Strait relations. It pioneered direct dialogue and communication between the leaders of both sides, elevated cross-Strait exchanges and interactions to a new height, opened a new chapter in the development of cross-Strait relations, and created new space.\nTo illuminate the present and inspire the future, the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a “Symposium Marking the 5th Anniversary of the Historic Meeting of the Leaders of the Two Sides of the Taiwan Strait” in Beijing on November 6, attended by more than 60 guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait. Under the current complex and severe cross-Strait situation, holding this symposium is of particularly important significance. Guests and compatriots on both sides of the Strait gained a deeper understanding that they must firmly grasp the correct direction of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, unwaveringly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and resolutely oppose and contain “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces. This helps us better grasp and lead the trend of cross-Strait relations, unite and rally Taiwan compatriots to solidly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, firmly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and strive together to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306171.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Leaders of the DPP authorities have repeatedly claimed that they are “willing to promote meaningful dialogue between the two sides of the Strait.” May I ask the spokesperson: if the DPP authorities, on the one hand, insist on not recognizing the “1992 Consensus” while, on the other hand, seeking to promote cross-Strait dialogue, is there any chance of success?","Without the “foundation” of the “1992 Consensus,” how can there be a “building” of cross-Strait dialogue? Any attempt to bypass the “1992 Consensus” renders any exchange or dialogue impossible.\nWe advise the DPP authorities to stop playing word games and deceiving the island's public. Only by truly proceeding from the well-being of the Taiwan people, acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” ceasing to collude with external forces and engage in provocations seeking “independence,” and improving cross-Strait relations through concrete actions is the right path.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306170.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The DPP authorities have recently tried, through various means, to “decouple” cross-Strait economic ties. However, statistics on the island show that cross-Strait trade has grown against the trend, playing a vital role in Taiwan’s economic development. What is your comment on this?","As the Mainland's economy stabilizes, recovers and actively builds a new development pattern, the Mainland's pull on the recovery and growth of the global economy has become increasingly apparent. Cross-strait trade, especially Taiwan's exports to the Mainland, has grown against the trend. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, from January to October this year, cross-strait trade reached US$209.555 billion, up 13% year on year. Of this, the Mainland's exports to Taiwan were US$48.212 billion, up 7.3% year on year, and its imports from Taiwan were US$161.343 billion, up 14.8% year on year. According to Taiwan's statistics, from January to October this year, the share of Taiwan's exports to the Mainland (including Hong Kong) in its total exports was 43.6%, and in October it reached 44%.\nThis set of trade data fully demonstrates that cross-strait economic and trade cooperation conforms to the laws of the market economy and has strong resilience against interference. It cannot be broken by some people or forces seeking to “decouple” or to obstruct it. As a market of 1.4 billion people, with 400 million middle-income people, and the most promising large market in the world, the Mainland's door to opening up will continue to widen, and opportunities for cooperation will keep multiplying. The economic and trade dividends across the Strait have tangibly benefited broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots. That Taiwan's development prospects lie on the Mainland, and that the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to cross-strait relations, will be repeatedly proven by facts. The DPP authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests and disregarding the well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, are moving against the tide and acting against public opinion. They will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306165.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","According to reports, DPP members Tsai Yi-yu and Yu Tian recently proposed a so-called “partial amendment to the Constitution,” which demands the deletion of provisions involving Mongolia and Tibet. What is your comment?","A small handful of “Taiwan independence” diehards keep changing their tactics and manipulating schemes for “independence,” attempting to split the country and undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Compatriots in Taiwan should remain highly vigilant and firmly oppose this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306168.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","After Biden is expected to become U.S. president, Tsai Ing-wen, who has been closely aligned with the Trump administration, did not anticipate this and is now making every effort to take various remedial and corrective measures. How does the spokesperson view this?","Taiwan is part of China. We have always handled Taiwan's external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose official exchanges between the Taiwan region and relevant countries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Some public opinion on the island holds that after the U.S. presidential election, cross-Strait relations have an opportunity to seek reconciliation and return to the right track. Spokesperson, do you think the outcome of the U.S. presidential election will affect cross-Strait relations?","We have repeatedly pointed out that the root cause of the current tension in cross-Strait relations is the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle; their interference with and obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation; their pushing of a series of separatist acts; and their collusion with external forces to provoke. Only when the DPP authorities return to the correct track of the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and stop separatist provocations can cross-Strait relations improve and develop.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The motherland must be reunified, and it will inevitably be reunified. This is the historical verdict on the development of cross-Strait relations. Development and progress on the mainland are the key factors determining the development of cross-Strait relations and leading the rejuvenation of the nation. At present, the mainland has achieved decisive results in winning the battle to build a moderately prosperous society in all respects, and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has taken a new big step forward. This has laid a firmer foundation and provided stronger support for advancing national reunification. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the historical trend and work with us toward the bright prospect of national rejuvenation and reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Today is “Double Eleven,” which has become the largest e-commerce shopping festival in the mainland. What opportunities will it bring to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses? In addition, please introduce what progress Taiwan-invested enterprises have made in expanding domestic market sales.","November is the hottest online shopping season on the mainland, and this year the “Double Eleven” was launched early, on November 1. It is projected that this year's “Double Eleven” will attract more than 800 million consumers from within and outside the mainland, with 250,000 brands and 5 million merchants taking part, making it the edition with the broadest coverage and highest level of participation. The State Post Bureau projects that during “Double Eleven” the average daily express delivery volume will reach 490 million parcels, twice the normal volume. Last year, the Taiwan region had the largest increase in shopping spending during “Double Eleven.” We believe that Taiwan residents will continue to participate enthusiastically this year.\nThe mainland has a population of 1.4 billion, of whom more than 400 million are middle-income earners, making it the world's largest and most promising consumer market. As of June this year, the mainland had 749 million online shopping users, of whom 309 million were e-commerce livestreaming users. The thriving mainland e-commerce market not only provides convenient services for Taiwan compatriots, but also offers a strong platform for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to deepen their presence in the mainland market and expand domestic sales, creating enormous business opportunities. To further help Taiwan-funded enterprises expand into the mainland's domestic market, this year mainland departments and local governments have taken many concrete measures, including guiding the holding of multiple online promotion and matchmaking events on “Taiwan-funded enterprises expanding domestic sales,” helping Taiwan businesspeople and young Taiwanese use “livestream selling” and “short videos” to expand markets, and helping Taiwan businesses and enterprises take part in the China International Import Expo, among other things. Many Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises have ridden the express train of the mainland's internet economy, kept pace with the development of the mainland's e-commerce sector, and gained tangible benefits. During the just-concluded Zhejiang–Taiwan Cooperation Week, cross-Strait enterprises achieved more connections in industries such as the digital economy and finance, signing 38 new Taiwan-funded projects with total investment of US$4.83 billion. At the just-concluded third China International Import Expo, the first purchase intention order worth US$500 million was also signed by a Taiwanese enterprise.\nDuring the “14th Five-Year Plan” period, the mainland will enter a stage of high-quality development, accelerate the building of a new development pattern with the domestic circulation as the mainstay and with domestic and international circulations mutually reinforcing each other, and form a new system of open economy at a higher level. This contains enormous opportunities for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and integrated cross-Strait development, and will certainly offer broad room for development to Taiwan compatriots. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots to actively join in the new era of great development and great achievements of the Chinese nation, to jointly pursue a good life and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306167.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The Seventh National Population Census is under way. This census will randomly select 10% of households to fill out the long-form census questionnaire, which investigates more detailed information. May I ask the spokesperson: does this include Taiwan compatriots? Will this census leak the personal privacy of Taiwan compatriots?","The Seventh National Population Census will conduct household registration from November 1 to December 10 of this year. According to the Regulations on the National Population Census, the objects of this census include Taiwan residents living on the mainland. All information provided by census subjects will be kept confidential in accordance with law.\nAccording to the requirements of the national census plan, the census long form is completed only by mainland residents selected through sampling; Taiwan residents do not need to fill out the long form. In addition, the census charges no fees and involves no income investigation.\nThe census is a matter of national importance, providing solid population data for compiling major national strategic plans and scientifically formulating policies in related fields. We hope that Taiwan compatriots living on the mainland will actively support and cooperate with the census work. Taiwan Affairs Offices at all levels will, in accordance with work arrangements, assist local census agencies in providing relevant consultation services to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","US Secretary of State Pompeo announced yesterday that Under Secretary of State Krach will hold an economic dialogue with Taiwan on the 20th of this month, conducted both in person and by video. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between Taiwan and the United States. Regarding the topic you mentioned, which may involve the issue of pork and beef imports into Taiwan in this dialogue, Taiwan people are clear about it. The DPP authorities collude with external forces, disregard opposition from public opinion, and insist on opening imports of relevant products, and the public on the island has great concern and indignation. I want to emphasize that the DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers to inflate themselves and using the pretext of “economic and commercial” matters to develop official relations with the US, will only fall into a situation of being further dominated by the US side, and will only damage the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","Recently Taiwan’s military claimed that U.S. Marines arrived in Taiwan to teach combat courses to Taiwan’s military, drawing public attention. What is your assessment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and Taiwan. This position is very clear to everyone. The conduct of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, colluding with the United States and using force to seek “independence,” is extremely dangerous. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop all forms of risky collusion with the United States, not to go further and further down the road of “Taiwan independence,” and not to push the Taiwan people into disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306169.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","Yesterday morning, a PLA Y-8 anti-submarine aircraft entered Taiwan’s southwest Air Defense Identification Zone, and in the afternoon it appeared for the first time at an altitude of 1,500 meters. May I ask the spokesperson whether the PLA aircraft’s move is intended to maintain or intensify tensions in the Taiwan Strait?","The relevant actions of the PLA are necessary measures taken in response to the current security situation in the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty. They are a stern response to the provocative “Taiwan independence” conduct of the DPP authorities. In fact, today, besides the shopping festival, everyone should also pay attention to the fact that today is the 71st anniversary of the founding of the People's Air Force. We wish the People's Air Force a happy birthday.\nWe must emphasize one point: refusing to acknowledge oneself as Chinese, vigorously pursuing “Taiwan independence,” and still expecting external forces to protect you will only create historic blunders and catastrophic consequences. Regarding our resolve, will, and capability in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces must not underestimate them, must not provoke, and must not take risks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台中国新闻记者","According to Taiwan media reports, because many internet users on the island posted large volumes of comments attacking Biden before the US election, on the 6th Facebook shut down a large number of social media accounts on the island, as well as the so-called “Little Ying Fan Club” page with 147,000 followers, on the grounds of “violating community standards.” In addition, the Apple Daily previously claimed to…","We have noted the relevant reports. In order to advance “independence,” the DPP authorities and certain forces on the island have stopped at nothing, and have even taken sides in the U.S. election. This is their long-standing trick for seeking political private gain, and it will only end up lifting a rock to drop it on their own feet.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Public opinion holds that, compared with the China policy of current US President Trump, Biden's related positions would be relatively moderate. What is the spokesperson's assessment of how the mainland side views cross-Strait relations after Biden takes office? Will they get worse, or will there be an opportunity to move in a more moderate direction?","You have raised questions about cross-Strait relations, which I have already answered. I can answer your question from another angle.\nIt must be emphasized that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. We hope the U.S. government will fully recognize the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question, adhere to the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with caution and appropriateness.\nOur policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification, and resolutely contain “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The third China International Import Expo has just closed. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan enterprises.","Since the China International Import Expo was first held in 2018, Taiwan enterprises have actively recognized it, and registrations to exhibit have continued to be brisk. Over the past three years, a cumulative total of more than 300 Taiwan enterprises have exhibited. This year, 103 Taiwan enterprises are exhibiting, with a net exhibition area of 3,075 square meters. Taiwan enterprises' participation this year has two main characteristics. First, broad coverage: the exhibition scope spans five major exhibition areas, namely food and agricultural products, technology and equipment, consumer goods, medical devices and healthcare, and services trade.\nSecond, many enterprises are returning exhibitors. More than 40% of Taiwan enterprises are consecutive exhibitors. Taiwan enterprises such as Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Factory and Guanjie Technology, which exhibited at the Expo, generally report that the trip was worthwhile, and they have come to recognize even more the importance of the mainland market, strengthening their determination to deepen their roots there. The role of the Expo in opening business opportunities and boosting domestic sales has been highly recognized by the industry.\nRegistration for the commercial exhibition of the fourth CIIE next year has already begun, and many booths are “selling out fast”; quite a few Taiwan enterprises have already reserved booths. We welcome more Taiwan enterprises to open up the mainland market and diversified overseas markets through participation in the Expo, and to obtain more business opportunities and greater returns.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201111_12306166.htm"],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","Both Beijing and Taipei held events marking the fifth anniversary of the cross-Strait leaders' meeting. Mainland Affairs Council Chairman Chen Ming-tong said, “this has already been treated as a historical event.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The historic meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Strait is a milestone event in the history of cross-Strait relations. It set a precedent for direct dialogue and communication between the leaders of both sides and raised cross-Strait exchanges and interactions to a new height. History cannot be denied.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Given that the DPP authorities are colluding with external forces and their \"independence\" conduct has grown increasingly extreme, we have heard voices suggesting \"use war to promote peace, use force to promote reunification.\" How does the spokesperson view this?","Our major policy on Taiwan affairs is consistent and clear. The peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the mainstream public opinion on both sides, and national reunification is an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We are willing to make the utmost sincere efforts and do our utmost to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, since achieving reunification peacefully is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and to the whole nation. At the same time, our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering; we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. Not a single bit may be missing from the map of China, and not an inch of China's territory will be lost.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","The mainland's COVID-19 vaccine development is progressing smoothly and has advanced to the third phase of research. I would like to ask: for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland who want to receive the COVID-19 vaccine, what channels or approaches are available?","Taiwan compatriots are our flesh and blood, and no one cares more about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots than we do. We will continue to follow up on the issues you raised and make appropriate arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201111_12306163.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-12","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Further to your answer about Australia. You said that Australia should do more to improve relations with China and the relationship should be based on mutual respect. What are the actions you are looking for from Australia that are necessary to improve relations?","China's position on developing China-Australia relations is consistent and clear. The reason why China-Australia relations are in a difficult situation is very obvious. Over a period of time, the Australian side has repeatedly spoken and acted out of turn on issues concerning China's core interests like Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Taiwan and grossly interfered in China's internal affairs in blatant violation of the basic norms governing international relations, In the absence of any evidence, some people in Australia slandered and accused China of engaging in so-called \"intervention and infiltration activities\" in Australia, and they sought to politicize, stigmatize and create barriers for normal exchanges and cooperation between China and Australia. These practices have seriously damaged the mutual trust between the two countries, poisoned the atmosphere of bilateral relations, and clipped the developing momentum of China-Australia relations.\nAs the saying goes, \"the one who tied the knot should be the one to undo it.\" In order to get out of the predicament, the key lies in Australia facing squarely the crux of the current setback, looking at China and China's development objectively and rationally, handling bilateral relations in accordance with the principles of mutual respect and equal treatment, and doing more things conducive to enhancing mutual trust and promoting practical cooperation between the two countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1831861.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1831796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-11-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 11th, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council made provocative remarks about the four Hong Kong Legislative Council members losing their seats. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 12 (reporter): Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to a question on the 12th: The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, driven by their “Taiwan independence” political agenda, have frantically attacked and slandered the relevant decisions of the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, and have blatantly interfered in Hong Kong affairs. This once again exposes their despicable intent to manipulate politics and undermine Hong Kong while pursuing “independence.” Their efforts are futile and ineffective.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, in accordance with the Constitution, the Basic Law of Hong Kong, and the relevant provisions of the National Security Law for Hong Kong, made a decision on the qualifications of members of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Legislative Council. This is an inevitable requirement for upholding and improving the “one country, two systems” institutional framework and implementing the Basic Law of Hong Kong and the National Security Law for Hong Kong. It is a necessary step to safeguard the rule of law in Hong Kong and the constitutional order of the Special Region. It is reasonable, sound, constitutional, and lawful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201112_12306380.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-13","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","US Secretary of State Pompeo said in an interview on November 12 that Taiwan has not been a part of China. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Central People's Government of the PRC is the sole legitimate government representing China. This is an objective fact and a basic norm governing international relations. Taiwan was once occupied by Japan, but the 1943 Cairo Declaration and the 1945 Potsdam Declaration clearly stipulate that the Chinese territory occupied by Japan, like Taiwan, shall be returned to China. Resolution 2758 adopted by the UN General Assembly in 1971 also reaffirmed the one-China principle. It is based on the one-China principle that China has formally established diplomatic ties with 180 countries worldwide.\nThe one-China principle is the political underpinning of China-US relations. As per the 1979 Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the People's Republic of China and the United States of America, the United States recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. This serves as the basis for China and the US to recognize each other and to establish diplomatic relations. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\nFor Pompeo, compared with his own political interests, the fundamental interests of the Chinese and American people are just nothing. He is only interested in making up one lie after another to confound right and wrong, confuse the public, torpedo China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. His ugly and malicious intentions have been laid bare for all to despise.\nPompeo should know that China will resolutely fight back against all attempts that undermine China's core interests and interfere in China's internal affairs. Nothing will stop the historical trend of China's reunification. We urge the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop any form of official contacts and military links with Taiwan, stop doing or saying anything detrimental to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations, and promptly halt its steps down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1832285.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1832213.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 13 (Electric). In response to US Secretary of State Pompeo's erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question on the 12th, and the DPP authorities' expression of 'thanks,' Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 13th in response to questions: Pompeo has repeatedly made erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question, seriously violating the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. These remarks contradict the facts, contradict the basic norms of the international community, and contradict the commitments the US government has made to China. Taiwan is part of China, and this is something no one or force can change. The DPP authorities stubbornly rely on the US to resist the mainland and to seek 'independence,' and have no way out. Engaging in provocations to seek 'independence' will only be like lifting a rock to smash one's own foot.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201113_12306574.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-16","Zhao Lijian","The Global Times","Regarding US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo's statements last week that \"Taiwan has not been a part of China\", the US State Department spokesman said on Wednesday that the US has followed the One-China policy guided by the Taiwan Relations Act, the three joint communiques between the US and China, and the \"Six Assurances\" to Taiwan over the past four decades. What is China's comment?","Last week, we already made clear our solemn position on Pompeo's erroneous remarks. I would like to stress once again that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Central People's Government of the PRC is the sole legitimate government representing China. This is an objective fact and a basic norm governing international relations. The one-China principle is the political underpinning of China-US relations. As per the 1979 Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the People's Republic of China and the United States of America, the United States recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. This serves as the basis for China and the US to recognize each other and to establish diplomatic relations. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\nThe so-called \"Taiwan Relations Act\" unilaterally formulated by the US side and the \"Six Assurances\" it made to Taiwan severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and basic norms of international relations and constitute gross interference in China's internal affairs, which is completely wrong, illegal, null and void. The Chinese government is firmly opposed to them right from the start. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, rather than concocting something unilaterally.\nWe once again warn the US that any act that undermines China's core interests or interferes in China's internal affairs will be resolutely countered by the Chinese side and cannot stop the historical trend of China's reunification. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan in any form, and stop words and deeds that undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations, and refrain from going further down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202011/t20201116_693487.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1832660.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-16","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","Taiwan's Representative to the US tweeted on November 15 that she spoke to Biden's policy adviser Blinken to convey congratulations to the President-elect, and hoped to continue close cooperation with the US in coming years. What is your comment?","China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. The one-China principle cannot be violated, and those who seek external interference to sabotage cross-Strait relations will end up hurting their own interests and suffering shameful failure. We urge the US side to stick to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid seriously hurting China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202011/t20201116_693487.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1832660.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-17","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council accused China of attempting to damage cross-strait peace with the reported plan to compile a list of Taiwanese who support independence, according to the Central News Agency. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","I want to tell you that China is firmly determined to uphold its national unity and territorial integrity. Any separatist act to seek Taiwan independence, no matter in any form, is an dead end and will lead no where.\nAs for the specific question you mentioned, I suggest you refer it to the competent Chinese authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1833054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1833003.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-17","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","China has recently taken some restrictive measures against a variety of imports from Australia. In response, Australian Trade Minister Simon Birmingham said that the ball is very much in China's court to come to the table for dialogue. Some Australian media say Australia should not give up its values and its own national interests. What is China's comment on this?","Looking back over the past few years' China-Australia relations, it is clear that some people in Australia, with their Cold War mentality and ideological prejudice, tend to regard China's development as a threat, and have subsequently taken a series of wrong moves related to China, which is at the root cause of China-Australia relations taking a sharp downturn and stuck in the current difficult situation. I can give you more details in three aspects.\nFirst, the Australian side, in blatant violation of the basic norms of international relations, has time and again made mistakes on issues concerning China's core interests like Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Taiwan. It also exploited platforms like the Human Rights Council to initiate or participate in joint actions against China on Xinjiang-related issues, meddled in the national security legislation of Hong Kong in a high-profile way, and endorsed Taiwan's attempt to force its way into the World Health Assembly. These practices have grossly interfered in China's internal affairs and seriously hurt the feelings of the Chinese people.\nSecond, in the absence of any evidence, some people in Australia slandered and accused China of engaging in so-called \"intervention and infiltration\" activities in Australia, and there was no justification for the politicization and stigmatization of normal exchanges and cooperation between China and Australia. Australia was the first in banning Chinese company from participating in its 5G network construction, repeatedly prevented Chinese enterprises from investing in Australia under the guise of \"national security\", and conducted arbitrary searches of Chinese media reporters in Australia. These acts have seriously damaged mutual trust between the two countries, poisoned the atmosphere of bilateral relations, and curtailed the original good momentum of practical cooperation between China and Australia.\nThird, Australia has also engaged in political manipulation on the pandemic by promoting the so-called \"independent international inquiry\", which seriously interfered with international cooperation on pandemic prevention and control. What happened to China-Australia relations, as I just recounted, is very clear. There are even many clear-eyed people in Australia calling on the Australian government to take a rational and impartial stand in dealing with its relations with China. The Australian side should reflect on this seriously, rather than shirking the blame and deflecting responsibility.\nChina has always adhered to the five principles of peaceful coexistence, including \"non-interference in internal affairs\", to develop relations with other countries. We unswervingly follow the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics and respect the development paths chosen by other countries in accordance with their own national conditions. We never deny that China and Australia have different historical traditions and social systems and we are at different development stages. It is perfectly normal for the two sides to have contradictions and differences. What matters is to properly manage them in a constructive manner, rather than imposing one's own ideas and wills on others under the pretext of safeguarding national interests and values.\nI would like to stress that the serious difficulties facing China-Australia relations are nothing China wishes to see, and the responsibility for causing this situation doesn't lie with China at all. We hope that the Australian side will own up to the real reason for the setback in bilateral relations, look at China and China's development objectively and rationally, earnestly handle bilateral relations based on mutual respect and equal treatment, and do more things conducive to enhancing mutual trust and promoting pragmatic cooperation between the two countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1833054.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1833003.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-18","Zhao Lijian","The Global Times","US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo and Polish Foreign Minister Zbigniew Rau co-chaired the third Ministerial to Advance Religious Freedom on November 16. At the meeting, Pompeo criticized China's religious policies. The Taiwan region's Joseph Wu also delivered a video address. What is China's comment?","The spokesperson of the Chinese Embassy in Poland has issued a statement which seriously refutes the erroneous remarks made by certain US politicians including Pompeo. Pompeo has been habitually criticizing, slandering and smearing other countries on the so-called \"religious freedom\" issue. The Chinese side has stated its position on this on many occasions. We are firmly opposed to relevant country ganging up with the US to interfere in other countries' internal affairs.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China. We urge relevant countries to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, respect China's sovereignty, refrain from providing a stage for \"Taiwan independence\" secessionists, and making any form of official contact with the Taiwan authorities. Any attempt or act that violates the one-China principle and seek external interference to sabotage cross-strait relations is doomed to fail.\nI must point out that compared with the situation in China, the religious situation of the United States is truly worrisome. There is a long-term and systematic problem of racial discrimination in the United States. According to poll results released by Gallup and Pew Research Center, 75% of American Muslims believe that their community is seriously discriminated against in the country. We urge politicians from individual countries, such as the United States, to look in the mirror and examine themselves and stop using religious issues to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries. We also advise the countries concerned not to be exploited by the United States and used as its chess pieces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1833362.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1833328.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-18","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News Agency","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council indicated that the mainland is working on a list of diehard elements seeking \"Taiwan independence\". Will this list include people of foreign nationality?","As you said, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council is in charge of this matter. I think you'll have to ask them.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1833362.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1833328.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-11-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to reports, relevant mainland authorities are studying the formulation of a list of “diehard Taiwan independence” elements to precisely strike at “Taiwan independence” forces both on and off the island. Can the Taiwan Affairs Office confirm this? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 18. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, in response to a question on the 18th, said: “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and the greatest obstacle to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The acts of a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements who openly challenge China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are absolutely intolerable. They and their major backers, including their financial backers, will be punished in accordance with the law, with the aim of safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. The lawful rights and interests of the broad Taiwan compatriots will be fully protected.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that leads nowhere and will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots. Cross-Strait reunification is an irresistible trend. All “Taiwan independence” elements who persist in their delusions and resist to the end will surely be condemned by the people and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201118_12307169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-11-20","Zhao Lijian","Tass","Andrew Wheeler, the head of the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, is to visit Taiwan in December to discuss cooperation on marine environment protection issues. What is the Foreign Ministry's comment?","China firmly opposes all forms of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the U.S. side to fully grasp the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question, stick to the one China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately halt their official ties and interactions with Taiwan in any form, and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues so as to avoid any serious harm to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US cooperation in relevant key areas. China will make legitimate and necessary reactions in light of the development of the situation on the ground.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1834154.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1834134.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-11-23","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","On the evening of November 22, a U.S. charter plane landed at Songshan airport, Taiwan, China. Neither the United States nor Taiwan gave any details about the flight. According to some media in Taiwan, it was a visit by high-level U.S. intelligence officials to Taiwan. I wonder if you have any comment on this and if the mainland is going to take some measures in response to the frequent visits to Taiwan by the…","As for your first question, China firmly opposes any form of official exchange and military contact between the U.S. and the Taiwan region. This stance is clear and consistent. We urge the U.S. to fully grasp the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiques, immediately halt official exchanges and contacts in any form and handle Taiwan-related issues in a prudent and proper manner. China will make legitimate and necessary responses in light of the developments.\nAs to your second question, China consistently opposes official exchanges between the U.S. and the Taiwan region and have lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side. We urge the United States to earnestly adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiques, stop official exchanges and contacts with the Taiwan region and stop elevating its relationship with the Taiwan region in substance so as to avoid serious damage to China-U.S. relations and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1834673.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1834656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","This year is the final year of the poverty alleviation campaign. As of November 23, all 832 impoverished counties identified by the State Council Poverty Alleviation Office have been removed from the poverty list. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises in the mainland’s poverty alleviation campaign.","On November 23, Guizhou announced that all of its poor counties had been removed from the poverty list, marking the complete “clearing” of the 832 poor counties designated by the State Council Poverty Alleviation Office. This achievement has drawn worldwide attention. In this process, compatriots from Taiwan and Taiwan-invested enterprises practiced the concept that “cross-Strait families are one family,” actively giving back to society. Through direct investment, technology introduction, employment assistance and other means, they took part in poverty-alleviation efforts in various localities and made positive contributions to raising incomes and improving people’s livelihoods.\nWe have seen that they built 500 “Tongxin water cisterns” in the mountainous areas of Guangxi to solve the drinking water problems of poor residents; they established a broccoli planting base of more than a thousand mu in Zhangwu, Liaoning, whose products are sold to Southeast Asia; and they even introduced dragon fruit cultivation in the desert area of Gulang, Gansu, leading local residents to get rich together… There are many such examples. Of particular note, among the 832 counties that have exited poverty, Guanghe County in Gansu Province, which is located in the “three regions and three prefectures” of deep poverty, achieved poverty alleviation and graduation in February this year. The All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, the Taiwan associations in various localities, and Taiwan compatriots and enterprises actively took part. More than 160 poverty-alleviation projects were implemented in industry, employment, education, health care and other areas, with investment and donations exceeding 60 million yuan. The infrastructure of 42 primary schools, middle schools and kindergartens was repaired or newly built, greatly improving local teaching conditions. More than 10 Taiwan-invested enterprises signed long-term employment agreements with Guanghe County, transferring more than 8,000 laborers and generating nearly 150 million yuan in income, making positive contributions to Guanghe County’s successful poverty graduation.\nIn our contacts, some Taiwan businesspeople have said, “I am also a true farmer. I came from the countryside in Taiwan, and once I got here, we are all one family. It is not right for me to make money alone; I must get rich together with everyone and with the local villagers.” Other Taiwan businesspeople have said, “Cross-Strait families are one family. When cross-Strait relations are good, the people on both sides will be well. Taiwan businesspeople are beneficiaries of reform and opening up, so of course we should step forward and give back to society.”\nFrom these Taiwan businesspeople, we see that people on the mainland and people in Taiwan are one family, deliberating together and striving together (in Hokkien). They have worked hard together with local villagers for a better life, fully reflecting the sentiment and sense of responsibility to enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We applaud them, and we hope that more Taiwan businesspeople will take part.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308215.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan has failed to join the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP). Industry and public opinion on the island generally worry that Taiwan's traditional industries will be severely impacted and that Taiwan will fall into a state of foreign trade and economic isolation. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) is a modern, free, high-quality, mutually beneficial large-scale regional free trade agreement. Its signing marks the official launch of what is now the world's most populous free trade area, with the largest economic and trade scale and the greatest development potential. It means that members will achieve high-level liberalization and facilitation in trade, investment and other areas, and will certainly inject strong momentum into the recovery and growth of the regional and global economy.\nWe note that at present, people from all sectors on the island are worried about the future development of Taiwan's economy, especially the impact that traditional industries may suffer as a result. We reaffirm that we welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to invest and start businesses on the mainland, to take part in and integrate into the mainland's economic development, and to share the strategic opportunities of mainland development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308211.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Many Taiwan-invested enterprises have expressed hope to learn more about the mainland listing policy provisions and related practical issues. To our understanding, a policy briefing on mainland listing for Taiwan-invested enterprises was recently held in Wuhan. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","The Recommendations of the CPC Central Committee on Formulating the 14th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development and the Long-Range Objectives Through the Year 2035, deliberated and adopted at the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee, clearly proposed \"supporting Taiwan-invested enterprises that meet the conditions to list in the Mainland.\" On November 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) co-hosted a policy briefing on the listing of Taiwan-invested enterprises in the Mainland, a concrete measure to implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session. Relevant CSRC departments and officials from the Shanghai Stock Exchange and the Shenzhen Stock Exchange interpreted the policies for representatives of more than 100 Taiwan-invested listed companies and companies preparing to list in provinces and municipalities across the Mainland, and engaged in exchanges and interactive discussion.\nListing in the Mainland allows Taiwan-invested enterprises to raise the funds needed for development, and also to enhance their brand image and better integrate into the Mainland's economic development process. More and more Taiwan-invested enterprises have chosen to list in the Mainland.\nWe want to stress that there are no policy obstacles to Taiwan-invested enterprises listing in the Mainland; they enjoy exactly the same treatment as Mainland enterprises. We will earnestly implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee, take effective measures to create a more favorable environment for Taiwan-invested enterprises to develop in the Mainland, support them in using the Mainland's capital market to grow bigger, better and stronger, and help them better share in the development opportunities of the Mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently public opinion has paid close attention to the Mainland's research into formulating a list of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements. What plans does the Taiwan Affairs Office have for formulating the list of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements? What considerations are there at present regarding implementation steps?","The conduct of a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements who openly challenge national sovereignty and territorial integrity is intolerable. We will continue to take precise crackdown measures and punish diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their principal backers and major supporters in accordance with law. Those diehard “Taiwan independence” elements who are arrogant in their “independence” rhetoric and vile in their “independence” conduct, including the ringleaders who organize, plan, and carry out activities to split the country both on and off the island, along with their principal backers and major supporters, will surely be subject to the judgment of the people in accordance with law and the punishment of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308214.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The relevant Taiwan authorities rejected the license “renewal” case of CTi News, which has triggered strong criticism and questioning from all sectors of the island. What is your comment on this? In addition, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently also declared that mainland media stationed in Taiwan are prohibited from renting and using studios in Taiwan to record and produce talk-format programs, and…","We have noted that the review by relevant Taiwan authorities of the \"license renewal\" case of CTi News has aroused widespread questioning and strong criticism from all sectors of Taiwan society. As Taiwan public opinion has pointed out, this move by the DPP authorities is using political means to suppress dissenters, and the relevant departments are performing strictly according to a script to complete so-called \"political tasks\".\nOn the second issue, cross-Strait media are a bridge and link for enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides. Under the current impact of the COVID-19 epidemic, it is even more necessary for media to play a role in communication across the Strait. We have consistently supported news exchange and cooperation between cross-Strait media, and, in light of the normalized needs of epidemic prevention and control, we have earnestly safeguarded the rights and interests of Taiwan media and reporters reporting in the Mainland and provided corresponding services and guarantees. The DPP authorities look for excuses and apply double standards, and have continuously obstructed the rotation of Mainland media reporters stationed in Taiwan. Most Mainland resident reporters in Taiwan have now been working continuously for nearly a year, causing serious distress to the relevant media, to the reporters themselves, and to their families. Such practices are extremely irresponsible and extremely inhumane. Now the DPP authorities are even threatening to punish Mainland resident media, and we strongly condemn this.\nThe DPP authorities should stop unreasonably making things difficult for Mainland resident media and reporters in Taiwan, restore the normal rotation of Mainland resident reporters in Taiwan as soon as possible, and safeguard their legitimate rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308210.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","According to China Review News, US Navy Asia-Pacific intelligence commander Shi Daman (史达曼) led a delegation to Taipei on the 22nd and will stay in Taiwan for three days. This visit is intended to strengthen US-Taiwan intelligence exchange and deployment. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between Taiwan and the United States.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, some people in Taiwan have again advocated enacting a so-called “agent law” and amending the so-called “anti-infiltration law” while increasing penalties. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","A small handful of “Taiwan independence” diehards, unwilling to accept their isolation and failure, have repeatedly used so-called “law amendment and legislation” and other means to intimidate Taiwan people and groups participating in cross-Strait exchanges, attempting to further restrict and suppress normal cross-Strait interaction and exchanges. This harms the interests and well-being of people on both sides and undermines the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations. Their sinister intentions will not succeed. It is the will of the people on both sides to exchange, cooperate, and develop, and it is the trend of the times. We solemnly warn these “Taiwan independence” diehards that those who commit evil will bring about their own demise, and in the end they will not escape the judgment of justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308212.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","On the 22nd, Taiwan held an “autumn struggle” rally, and multiple civic groups on the island sharply criticized the DPP authorities for disregarding the people. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted the relevant situation. The DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest and completely disregarding the interests and welfare of the Taiwan people, have aroused public outrage. Justice lies in the hearts of the people; those who act righteously gain abundant support, while those who act unrighteously gain little.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan and the United States recently held a so-called “Economic Prosperity Partnership Dialogue” and signed a so-called “memorandum of economic cooperation,” establishing that “economic dialogues” will be held every year. What is your comment?","We oppose the United States developing official exchanges with the Taiwan region on the pretext of economic and trade matters. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rely on the United States and seek “independence” under the pretext of “economic dialogue” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan has been excluded from RCEP. Some scholars on the island suggest that deepening ECFA is the key, and hope to further reach follow-up agreements on ECFA-related goods trade and other matters. Regarding the prospects for future ECFA negotiations, what suggestions does the spokesperson have?","Ten years ago, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides of the Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA), which brought enormous benefits to enterprises and people on both sides. The Democratic Progressive Party, in pursuit of political self-interest, has used various means to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, claiming it wants to “decouple” from the mainland economy. They deliberately obstructed the entry into force of the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement, causing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises to lose the development opportunities they should have enjoyed, and seriously harming the development interests of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.\nWe reiterate that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the basis and prerequisite for signing and implementing cross-Strait agreements. If the Democratic Progressive Party authorities remain obstinate and act recklessly, they will only create more obstacles to Taiwan’s economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","We note that Taiwan's economic authorities recently released statistics showing that in October this year, approved investment in the mainland fell 31% from the previous year, but the investment amount reached US$490 million, up 29% over the same period last year. Another set of figures: from January to October this year, Taiwan's investment in the mainland reached US$4.71 billion, up 47% year on year. How does…","Since the beginning of this year, against the backdrop of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control, cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation has grown against the trend. This shows that cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation meets the interests of compatriots on both sides and brings tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. No force can stop this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","央视海峡两岸记者","Some public opinion is concerned that the mainland’s compilation of a list of “Taiwan independence” diehards will affect the sense of security of Taiwan residents coming to the mainland for exchanges, and further restrict cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. What is your comment?","Drawing up a list of stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements targets only a very small number of stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements and their main backers, such as their financial backers, and is definitely not aimed at the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. Only by resolutely cracking down on “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully, and only then can the interests and well-being of cross-Strait compatriots, including Taiwan compatriots, be safeguarded and enhanced.\nAs for cross-Strait exchanges, we have always kept the door to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation open, and as always welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various forms and share in the development opportunities of the mainland. All localities and departments will not only effectively safeguard the lawful rights and interests of broad Taiwan compatriots, but will also continue to introduce policy measures conducive to Taiwan residents coming to the mainland to exchange, work and study, promoting mutual understanding and emotional integration between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202011/t20201125_12308213.htm"],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","All sectors in Taiwan have expressed concern and worry over Taiwan's failure to join RCEP, yet the DPP authorities declared that the reason Taiwan has not joined RCEP is that the mainland set up an obstacle by requiring Taiwan to accept “one country, two systems.” What is the spokesperson's evaluation of this?","The one-China principle is the premise for Taiwan’s participation in regional economic cooperation. Only by returning to the correct path of adhering to the one-China principle can the two sides share development and prosperity, and Taiwan can share the dignity and glory of the great motherland internationally.\nOn the question of Taiwan’s participation in regional economic cooperation: in the past, on the basis of both sides adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the two sides had engaged on this matter, and Taiwan had its opportunities. But as everyone can see, after the DPP authorities took office they refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and single-handedly undermined this situation. When the one-China principle cannot be upheld, cross-Strait political mutual trust no longer exists, and the consequences of the DPP authorities undermining cross-Strait relations and harming Taiwan’s economy will become apparent step by step.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","After a Taiwanese Air Force F-16 fighter jet took off on November 17 and lost contact, while Taiwan was making every effort to search and rescue, a rumor appeared on the mainland internet claiming that the missing pilot had \"defected\" to the mainland and landed at Xiamen Airport. May I ask the spokesperson for your comment on this?","I want to make two points. First, the mainland's internet is open, and it is also managed according to law. Second, the DPP authorities and certain forces on the island have taken the opportunity to stir up trouble and maliciously hype the issue, attempting to divert attention and, under this pretext, incite hostility and confrontation across the Strait. Their intentions are clearly not innocent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","When will the list of “Taiwan independence” diehards be published? Recently, some media named Su Tseng-chang on the list. Su said his reputation will rise the more it is attacked, while some people who are not on the list instead expressed anger. What is the purpose of the mainland in compiling this list? Did it anticipate other consequences?","A very small number of hardened \"Taiwan independence\" diehards have long incited cross-Strait confrontation, undermined cross-Strait relations, and endangered peace in the Taiwan Strait. Everyone sees this clearly. This account will certainly be settled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","According to today's news, the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Administrator had originally planned to visit Taiwan in December, but due to domestic pressure and excessively high charter flight costs, the trip has tentatively been postponed. What is the spokesperson's view on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We demand that the United States abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","日本广播协会记者","Recently Taiwan's “self-built submarine” project officially began construction. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The DPP authorities are attempting armed confrontation; using force to seek “independence” is doomed to fail. The more they stir up trouble, the closer they come to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","If, after next year's Lunar New Year, mainland-stationed Taiwan media reporters return to the mainland to spend the holiday and are unable to return to Taiwan, and mainland media are therefore unable to dispatch reporters to be stationed in Taiwan, will the Taiwan Affairs Office consider taking the same countermeasures against Taiwan media stationed in the mainland?","Media on both sides of the Strait are bridges and links that enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides. Under the current situation of cross-Strait relations and the background of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control, it is even more necessary for the media to play a role in communication between compatriots on both sides. We will not do anything that “tears down bridges” or “destroys roads.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","美国彭博新闻社","The mainland is studying the formulation of a list of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements, targeting an extremely small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements. May I ask whether there is a specific figure for this extremely small number? Who are they? Will “Taiwan independence” elements outside the Taiwan region be included on the list?","Those diehard “Taiwan independence” elements who are arrogant in their “independence”-related rhetoric and whose “independence”-seeking conduct is egregious—including the ringleaders who organize, plan, and carry out secessionist actions on and off the island, as well as their principal backers and major supporters—will all be sanctioned in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Once the mainland publishes a list of stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements, if the Taiwan side also begins publishing so-called lists of personnel who support the mainland, would the mutual establishment of “lists” further affect civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait?","Regarding concerns about civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, I have already explained them just now. Resolutely cracking down on a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and stopping “Taiwan independence” separatist acts are the proper meaning and necessary condition for safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. As people often say, justice in trials is never absent; this is what that means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中天电视台记者","After the US election, the situation across the Taiwan Strait has seen some subtle changes. For example, the intelligence commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command visited Taiwan quietly, and the head of the US Environmental Protection Agency just cancelled a visit to Taiwan. Can it be considered that US-China relations and the situation across the Taiwan Strait have eased? What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated. We demand that the US government abide by the One-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with prudence and appropriateness. This position has been consistent. We advise the DPP authorities to stop relying on foreign powers to bolster themselves and to stop serving as “pawns” for external anti-China forces, as this will only bring disaster to the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-11-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Last week, a mainland fishing boat rescued four Taiwan marine survey personnel who had fallen into the water in the Penghu sea area. Could the spokesperson introduce the specific process and details?","I have seen the relevant reports in the media. We applaud these rescuers. As for the details of the incident you mentioned, I do not have information on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202011/t20201125_12308209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2020-11-26","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed that Taiwan would keep trying to seek the US's support and deepen their so-called \"partnership\". What's your comment?","China firmly opposes any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the US and Taiwan. The rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and reunification of the country is an unstoppable trend and a just cause supported by all Chinese people. Those who follow this trend will prosper, and those who go against it are doomed to failure. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP)'s attempt to borrow strength from foreign forces and seek \"Taiwan independence\" by military means is nothing but a suicidal attempt like a mantis trying to stop a chariot. We will not allow anyone or any force to infringe upon and secede the sacred territory of our motherland. Once such a serious situation occurs, the Chinese PLA will surely deal a head-on blow and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.chinamil.com.cn/view/2020-11/29/content_9944372.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-11/26/content_4876300.htm",0,1,1,""],[0,"2020-11-30","Hua Chunying","Beijing Daily","Brent Christensen, head of the American Institute in Taiwan, said Taiwan has record-breaking military expenditure this year. The U.S. government will still sell arms to Taiwan next year. What's your comment?","The first thing I'd like to stress is that China firmly opposes U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. Our position is consistent and clear.\nI read reports that Taiwan has spent $11.8 billion, or NT$342.2 billion in purchasing American weapons this year, equaling the per capita spending of NT$14,500. I don't know how our Taiwan compatriots feel when they know their wealth gained through hard work is spent on buying second-hand American weapons and used like it came from an automated teller machine for interest groups in the United States.\nWe once again send this stern message to the U.S. side: China will resolutely fight back against all attempts that undermine China's core interests and interfere in China's internal affairs. We urge the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop selling arms to Taiwan or having military links with Taiwan, deal with Taiwan-related issues properly and with caution, and promptly halt its steps down the wrong and dangerous path. We also once again give the stern message to the Taiwan authorities that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end. Attempts and actions to seek external interference and use weaponry to deny reunification are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202011/t20201130_693509.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202011/t20201130_5419580.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-01","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","The Australian Prime Minister said yesterday that a spokesperson of China's Foreign Ministry posted a \"falsified photo\" on his Twitter account. The official Weibo account of the Australian Embassy in China also updated a post, saying that the photo was falsified. What is your comment?","A falsified photo? Australia accuses China of using a falsified or fake photo, and even of spreading false information, but such an accusation is in itself a false one. What's going viral online is not a \"photo\", but a graphic created with computer techniques by a young Chinese artist. Computer-generated graphics and falsified pictures are two different things. The graphic depicts a fact because its creation is based on the inquiry report issued by the Australian Defense Department.\nChinese netizens had some heated discussions about Australia's reaction yesterday. The artist of this graphic was also interviewed by media. According to media reports, he called out to Mr. Morrison, telling him that what some of his soldiers did was crueler than his artwork depicts.\nBefore coming here, I asked my colleague to print out some photos and the inquiry report by the Australian Defense Department. These are all what really happened. These are all released by the Australian side. Some of you may have the same question mark as I do: why does the Australian side react so strongly on this? The Australian side has made such a scene with this graphic because it wants to divert attention, avoid the real issue and relieve some pressure off its shoulder. It is under immense criticism and condemnation from the international community for the ruthless killing of Afghan innocents by some of its soldiers, but the Australian side wants to turn that into a tough-on-China position. Everyone sees that very clearly.\nI also read an article on WeChat that I want to share with you. It's titled \"How Come It's 'I Can, But You Cannot'?\". I believe this article speaks for a lot of Chinese people. It is a fact that China is treated with this \"I can, but you cannot\" approach. For example, I can have 5G technologies, but you cannot; I can have a bigger economy than yours, but you cannot; I can make accusations against you while siding with \"Tibet independence\" forces, \"Taiwan independence\" forces, Xinjiang separatist forces, and the opposition and violent criminals in Hong Kong, but you cannot. This \"I can, but you cannot\" approach reflects the attitude of those unbelievably arrogant hypocrites. Their real motive is to deprive China of the right to tell facts and truth. They are afraid to hear that loud and clear voice-\"Look, the emperor has no clothes on!\"\nWhen it comes to \"false information\", I hope that these people will calm down and do some level-headed thinking. They need to view China and China's development with soberness and reason and work in constructive ways. They need to face up to the issues and work with China to properly address them and uphold the sound development of bilateral relations on the basis of equality and mutual respect. This is what the people hope to see and what truly serves the fundamental and long-term interests of their countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1837026.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1836913.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-12-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 3: In response to the DPP authorities’ comments on the conviction and imprisonment of three “Hong Kong independence” elements, including Wong Chi-fung, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 3rd in response to questions: We firmly support the Hong Kong SAR government in upholding the rule of law in Hong Kong. The DPP authorities’ finger-pointing at Hong Kong affairs once again exposes their true face of sowing chaos in Hong Kong and plotting “independence,” their hypocrisy in clamoring for “aid to Hong Kong,” and their false benevolence under the banner of “democracy.” We once again warn the DPP authorities to immediately withdraw the black hand they have stuck into Hong Kong affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201203_12309361.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","Reuters","The United States this week announced a new arms sale package to Taiwan worth US$280 million, which would be the 6th sale this year. Do you have any comment on that?","China's position on the U.S. arms sales to Taiwan is consistent and clear. I'd like to stress again that the U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region severely violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, constitute blatant interference in China's internal affairs, seriously undermine China's sovereignty and security interests, send out wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and gravely undercut China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes such acts.\nChina urges the United States to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military contacts with the Taiwan region, and immediately cancel its arms sale plans to avoid further damaging China-U.S. relations and cross-Strait peace and stability. China will take legitimate and necessary reactions to firmly safeguard national sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","The Taiwan side thanked the US for emphasizing the importance of helping the island strengthen its self-defense capabilities. This is according to a statement from the \"presidential office spokesman\". Taiwan will continue to deepen its ties with the US and other like-minded nations with solid defense capabilities, the statement said. What's the foreign ministry's comment on this statement from Taiwan?","First of all, I want to say that Taiwan is not a country. Second, the Taiwan authorities now thank the U.S. side for selling it arms and strengthening military ties. I hope they will first of all figure it out whether the U.S. side is helping them or hurting them?\nI would like to reiterate that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity as well as China's core interests. China firmly opposes US arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan, and this position is clear and consistent. No one should underestimate China's firm determination and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Taiwan authorities also need to be absolutely clear on the fact that seeking \"Taiwan independence\" is heading towards a dead end. They want to resist the unstoppable trend of reunification by inviting in external parties and by resorting to force, but they do not stand even the slightest chance of success in that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","China Daily","The Stockholm International Peace Research Institute released a report on December 7, putting the United States and China on the top 2 in arms sales, with 12 American arms companies in the global top 25. I wonder if you have any comment?","I noticed the report. I'm not sure about its data source or statistical criteria. One thing we have noticed is that according to the report, the United States remains the world's top arms exporter, with 12 American companies taking up 61 percent of all sales of the top 25 arms traders, to which, as is well known, Taiwan authorities contributed significantly.\nLike other countries, China enhances national defense and conducts normal arms trade cooperation with other countries. The Chinese government enforces strict management of export of military articles with a highly responsible and prudent attitude based on domestic policies, laws and regulations as well as international obligations. We are committed to the three principles for arms export: it should be conducive to the legitimate self-defense capability of the recipient country; it should not undermine peace, security and stability of the region concerned and the world as a whole; and it should not be used to interfere in the internal affairs of the recipient country. In particular, China does not sell weapons to non-state actors, which marks a substantive difference from the practices of the Untied States and a few others.\nChina joined the Arms Trade Treaty in July this year whereas the United States unsigned the same treaty in April last year. As a state party to the treaty, China stands ready to enhance cooperation with others to contribute more to regulating global arms trade.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","","本周，美国宣布向台湾出售2.8亿美元武器设备，这是今年的第六次。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","","台湾方面“总统府发言人”在一份声明中，对美国重视协助台湾增强防卫能力表达感谢，并称台湾将进一步深化同拥有强大防卫能力的美国和其他观点相近国家的关系。外交部对台湾方面表态有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2020-12-08","Hua Chunying","","据报道，7日，瑞典斯德哥尔摩国际和平研究所（SIPRI）发布报告称，美国和中国分列2019年全球军火销售总额一二名。在全球前25名军火商中，美国占12家排名第一。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1838677.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1838639.shtml",0,3,0,""],[1,"2020-12-08","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reported that on December 7 local time, the US State Department approved the sale to Taiwan of military communication equipment worth about US$280 million. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The United States' arms sales to Taiwan seriously violate international law and the basic norms of international relations, seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué, grossly interfere in China's internal affairs, seriously endanger China's sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity, and seriously undermine the relations between the two countries' armed forces and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China, and the Taiwan question concerns China's core interests. Foreign interference of any kind is absolutely not allowed. Any US attempt to use Taiwan to contain China is futile. We strongly urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately revoke the relevant arms sales projects to Taiwan, and stop selling weapons to Taiwan and military contacts between the US and Taiwan, so as to avoid further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to China-US military relations. The Chinese People's Liberation Army has the confidence and capability to resolutely defeat any plot to split the motherland, and it firmly defends the sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity of the country.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2020-12/08/content_4875161.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2020-12-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 8 (electronic dispatch). In response to the US State Department’s recent approval of the sale to Taiwan of military communications equipment worth about 280 million US dollars, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 8th: We firmly oppose US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué, and to stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nShe also pointed out that the DPP authorities keep spending money that could have been used to improve people’s livelihoods on purchasing weapons from the US in an attempt to resist reunification by force, a effort that is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201208_12310068.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-12-16","Wang Wenbin","Hubei TV","The Ministry of Commerce released data yesterday that paid-in foreign investment in China has increased for the eighth consecutive month. Many foreign media and agencies believe China's growth trend is good for the world economic recovery. Do you have any comment on this?","Authoritative international economic agencies have been projecting that China will be the only major economy to achieve a positive growth rate this year. You just mentioned that foreign capital keeps flowing into China, I believe it demonstrates the confidence in China's economic prospect and the outcomes of fostering a new development paradigm and expanding opening up. Since the beginning of this year, China has been comprehensively implementing the Foreign Investment Law and its implementation regulations. The negative lists for pilot free trade zones have been shortened from 190 items in 2013 to 30 now, financial market access has been steadily eased, and a master plan has been drawn up for the development of the Hainan Free Trade Port, which will open up broad space for China's economic development and inject strong impetus into global economic recovery. China has become the biggest trading partner for ASEAN, the EU and the United States. In the first three quarters of this year, China's non-financial outbound direct investment to countries along the BRI routes recorded a year-on-year increase of 29.7 percent. The third China International Import Expo records higher intended deals of $72.62 billion. The OECD Economic Outlook estimated that China will account for over one-third of world economic growth in 2021.\nAs China opens its door wider to the world, it will create more opportunities for mutually beneficial cooperation with other countries and make greater contributions to the stability and prosperity of a post-COVID world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1840675.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1840586.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to today’s press conference. Questions now begin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 2020 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting was recently held via video link in Taipei and Xiamen. Please have the spokesperson introduce the situation of this year's annual meeting and the results achieved.","On December 9, the 2020 Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit was held simultaneously in Xiamen and Taipei via video link. The theme of this annual meeting was “Facing New Circumstances, Creating New Opportunities Again,” and more than 700 business people from both sides of the Strait attended. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, sent a congratulatory letter to the Council of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, extending warm congratulations on behalf of the CPC Central Committee and General Secretary Xi Jinping. In his letter, Chairman Wang Yang fully affirmed the important role of cross-Strait economic cooperation in the development of cross-Strait relations and the interests of compatriots on both sides, and highly praised the positive contributions made by enterprises on both sides to cross-Strait economic cooperation and the development of cross-Strait relations. He also pointed out profoundly that the development of the mainland during the “14th Five-Year Plan” period will bring major opportunities and long-term benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. He earnestly hoped that the Summit would unite and lead cross-Strait entrepreneurs in hand-in-hand advancement of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and join hands in striving for the great cause of national rejuvenation.\nThe outcomes of this annual meeting reached many consensus points for the Summit’s work next year. It was distinctive, substantive in content, and remarkable in effect. Once again it played an irreplaceable platform role for cross-Strait industrial cooperation and enterprise exchanges, and again proved that integrated development across the Strait is the trend of the times and the aspiration of the people. Enterprises are the main body of cross-Strait economic cooperation and are also meritorious contributors to the development of cross-Strait relations. The TAO will, as always, strongly support the Summit in uniting and leading cross-Strait entrepreneurs to survey the trends, plan the overall picture, and seek greater benefits, enhance exchanges and cooperation, make the interest “cake” bigger, jointly benefit compatriots on both sides, and make new contributions to creating a beautiful future of national rejuvenation together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312356.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Some public opinion on the island holds that cross-strait epidemic control has been very effective, and that a “travel bubble” should be negotiated first, gradually relaxing restrictions on cross-strait tourists so that exchanges can be restored as soon as possible. May I ask the spokesperson for your comment?","This is a question of great concern to compatriots on both sides of the Strait recently. Since February this year, cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel have been in a very abnormal state. This is affected by the epidemic, but it is more the result of artificial factors. Under the pretext of epidemic prevention and control, the DPP authorities have fully suspended travel to Taiwan by mainland residents, unilaterally closed the “Mini Three Links” between Kinmen and Matsu and Fujian, and extensively canceled cross-Strait direct flight points, so that at present only 4 mainland points have direct flights to Taiwan. This situation has now lasted 10 months and seriously affects cross-Strait personnel exchanges and travel. Compatriots in Taiwan hope that cross-Strait exchanges can be resumed as soon as possible; this reflects the will of the people.\nRecently, the two biggest problems we have heard from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses on the mainland are: first, the cost of nucleic acid testing on the island is too high; second, travel back and forth across the Strait is too hard and too roundabout, consuming too much time and money. The Taiwanese journalists present have firsthand experience of this. The mainland's fight against the COVID-19 epidemic has achieved major strategic results, which is plain for all to see. We hope the problems troubling Taiwan compatriots can be properly resolved as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, both sides of the Strait released trade data for the first 11 months of this year. According to statistics from the Taiwan side, from January to November this year, Taiwan's total trade with the mainland (including Hong Kong) was US$195.15 billion, up 12.9% over the same period last year, of which exports were US$136.74 billion, accounting for 43.8% of total exports. Regarding this data, the Taiwan…","On the question you raised, I want to emphasize three points.\nFirst, the numbers speak for themselves. According to the General Administration of Customs, from January to November this year, total cross-Strait import and export trade was US$235.69 billion, accounting for 5.4% of the mainland’s total import and export trade. Of this, the mainland imported US$181.71 billion from Taiwan, accounting for 9.8% of the mainland’s total imports over the same period. Taiwan’s trade surplus from the mainland was US$127.73 billion. You just mentioned Taiwan-side statistics, and we have also seen the relevant figures. The mainland imported US$181.71 billion from Taiwan, accounting for 9.8% of the mainland’s total imports. According to Taiwan-side statistics, its exports to the mainland accounted for 43.8% of its total exports. Who depends on whom? Looking at this chart should make it fairly clear. The mainland is Taiwan’s largest export market and its largest source of trade surplus. This is a fact. Without the mainland, Taiwan’s foreign trade would face a huge deficit, and its economy would find it difficult to maintain positive growth this year. That is the first point.\nSecond, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises operating on the mainland actively take part in cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation. In cross-Strait integrated development, they benefit Taiwan compatriots and have made a contribution to Taiwan’s economic growth that cannot be smeared.\nThird, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation accords with the common interests of people on both sides and benefits the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312353.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, Taiwan's culture authorities, on the grounds of violating the “Regulations Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Two Sides,” demanded that the mainland's children's picture book themed on COVID-19 response, 《等爸爸回家》 (Waiting for Dad to Come Home), not be distributed in Taiwan, and libraries at all levels and online platforms in Taiwan have taken the book off their shelves. What is the…","Is this the picture book you mean? After seeing the reports, I made a special trip to buy one, and I brought it today to show everyone, to see what exactly about this small picture book caused such a big commotion of attention in Taiwan.\nThis picture book has only 20 thin pages. Through the perspective of a child and a family, it depicts scenes of life during the Wuhan epidemic, telling the story of a child’s concern for and longing for his father, who is a doctor, and a story related to responsibility, commitment, support, and vigil. The origin of this picture book is that during the epidemic, 540,000 medical personnel in Hubei Province and Wuhan City fought the virus face to face, 346 national medical teams and more than 40,000 medical personnel rushed to the front lines, interpreting the benevolence of doctors and the boundless love with their sincere devotion to the people and reverence for life. The mother in the picture book says, “This is a battle against the virus; as long as everyone does their own job well, everyone is a glorious soldier.” Is it not very wrong for such a picture book, which can sow the seeds of love and courage in children’s hearts and help children understand the reading material of mutual care and assistance in human society, to be exploited by people on the island with ulterior motives?\nThe DPP authorities and some politicians on the island only ask about positions, not right and wrong; they only look at colors, not facts. As long as matters are related to the mainland, they politicize and stigmatize them, desperately inciting “anti-China” and “hostility toward China” sentiments. What are they afraid of? What they fear is that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will grow closer and become more intimate, that people in Taiwan will understand the real situation on the mainland, and even more that the lies they have painstakingly built will be exposed. Such an operation that violates conscience is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312350.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","There have been reports that the leader of the Taiwan authorities, in a video dialogue with a US think tank, said on the one hand that he looks forward to “constructive dialogue across the Strait,” while on the other hand continuing to attack the mainland using issues such as Hong Kong, the South China Sea, and Xinjiang. The Mainland Affairs Council recently also said it “hopes both sides can communicate…","We have repeatedly pointed out that the root cause of the current tension in cross-Strait relations lies in the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermining the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. Our policy toward Taiwan is clear and consistent. Denying the “1992 Consensus” and deviating from the one-China principle makes any dialogue or exchange unthinkable.\nIn recent times, the DPP authorities, while talking about cross-Strait “reconciliation” and “dialogue,” have actually intensified collusion with external forces to provoke the mainland. They disregard facts and spout nonsense on issues such as Hong Kong and Xinjiang, maliciously attack the mainland, and create cross-Strait antagonism. Such conduct is completely contrary to the so-called “reconciliation” and “dialogue.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312357.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","At the recent Global Times annual conference, several experts believed that the possibility of peaceful unification across the Taiwan Strait is declining. The mainland should adopt the approach of “promoting unification by force” and “promoting peace by force,” that is, strive for peaceful unification by applying pressure of “forceful unification” on Taiwan. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","We have also seen the relevant reports.\nFor a long time, we have made unremitting efforts to resolve the Taiwan question and promote the peaceful reunification of the motherland. “Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is the best way to achieve national reunification and best serves the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. This policy fully takes into account Taiwan's actual circumstances, fully respects the objective differences across the Strait, and fully safeguards the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Upholding peaceful reunification embodies the great righteousness of the nation and profound feelings that cherish the value of peace, treasure the well-being of compatriots, and take responsibility for the nation and future generations. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification across the Strait with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. As long as there is even a slight possibility of a peaceful solution, we will make a hundredfold effort.\nAt the same time, “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their actions openly challenge the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, seriously damage the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and seriously endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We will never leave any space for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We will always maintain full preparedness to deal with external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, with the aim of fundamentally safeguarding the prospects for peaceful reunification of the motherland and advancing the process of peaceful reunification. If the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces persist in their course or even take desperate risks, we will take all necessary measures to resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312355.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Polls on the island show that more than 80% of Taiwan residents oppose opening imports of U.S. pork and beef containing ractopamine. Some public opinion on the island has pointed out that the mainland can refuse to import “ractopamine pork,” but Taiwan cannot. What is your comment?","In order to seek personal political gain, the DPP authorities have colluded with external forces and insisted on harming the health and well-being of the people of Taiwan, which has aroused worry and righteous indignation among the people on the island. In accordance with provisions such as the Food Safety Law, the mainland does not permit the import of pork and beef and their products containing ractopamine. We will take effective measures to prevent meat products that do not meet mainland requirements from flowing in.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312352.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","We noted that on December 4, National Constitution Day, the Taiwan Affairs Office’s account published a publicity poster reading “National Constitution Day: Let’s take a look together at the Constitution’s provisions on national unification.” May I ask whether, under the current cross-Strait situation, publishing this kind of propaganda content means the mainland may introduce a “National Unification Law”?","The Constitution is the fundamental law of the state, possessing the highest legal status, legal authority and legal effect. The Constitution’s provisions on national unification are clear, and we will resolutely implement them. We will take all necessary measures to firmly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","According to reports, Chen Yung-fu, a DPP member of the New Taipei City Council, recently incited the destruction of nuclear power plants on the mainland's coast, which Taiwan netizens condemned as “drunken suicidal remarks.” What is the spokesperson's view on this?","Some DPP politicians, in defiance of universal condemnation, have clamored to attack nuclear power plants, and the DPP authorities have even tacitly allowed such crazy remarks, fully exposing the evil nature of a very small number of people who have abandoned human conscience and trampled on the bottom line of civilization. Any “Taiwan independence” separatist and provocative act will certainly be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312351.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan’s external affairs department said that Taiwan has been striving to join the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), and informal consultations with the 11 member states are still ongoing. Please comment.","On the question of Taiwan’s participation in regional economic cooperation, we have emphasized many times that it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","December 10 is World Human Rights Day. At its regular press conference held that day, the Mainland Affairs Council slandered the mainland on issues related to Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Tibet. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment?","The DPP authorities, under the pretext of so-called “human rights,” groundlessly accuse the mainland and spread claims that contradict basic facts and common sense. These claims are full of prejudice and hostility and do not win popular support. We advise the DPP authorities to stop making irresponsible remarks on these issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201216_12312354.htm"],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Some people in the DPP recently accused several Taiwan internet celebrities and some groups of producing and disseminating videos with “united front” implications, cooperating with the mainland in “united front” propaganda. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Are you referring to the video on Bilibili titled “Taiwan Girl PK” by one of the influencers you mentioned? After I saw the reports, I deliberately watched some of the videos she posted. One of them describes her experience seeking medical treatment in Shanghai, where she felt that mainland medical insurance is fairer and more reasonable than Taiwan's National Health Insurance. An ordinary young woman who lives on the mainland wants to share her story of life here. What is wrong with that? Why do DPP politicians so readily elevate such matters to questions of principle and call for punishment and violence? What is their intention?\nTaiwan compatriots living on the mainland have a first-hand feel for the progress of the mainland's development. We have seen that during the 13th Five-Year Plan period, the world's largest higher education system was completed, with a gross enrollment rate in higher education reaching 51.6%. The world's largest social security system has also been completed: basic medical insurance covers more than 1.3 billion people and basic pension insurance covers nearly 1 billion people. The largest and most intensive poverty alleviation campaign in human history has been completed, lifting nearly 100 million people out of poverty. We open our doors and welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to live, work and study, to share the opportunities of mainland development and achieve better development for themselves.\nWe must point out that the DPP authorities and some politicians have repeatedly and again and again abused public power to suppress and bully certain people from Taiwan and to incite hostility, hatred and confrontation between the two sides. In fact, this will only further tear Taiwan society apart. Using the stock response of diverting attention, shifting contradictions and suppressing dissenters as a panacea for deceiving the Taiwan public is truly absurd and laughable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the joint reporting event “Second Cross-Strait Online New Media Mainland Tour” concluded successfully. I would like you to introduce the relevant situation.","From December 4 to 11, the “Second Cross-Strait Online New Media Mainland Tour” joint reporting event was held in Guangdong. Under the theme “Cross-Strait Concentric Circles, Dreaming in the Greater Bay Area,” more than 50 new media journalists and self-media personalities from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong and Macau conducted joint interviews in Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Zhuhai and Shantou. They made full use of online new media platforms to present, from multiple angles, the development prospects of the economy, society and culture of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, told stories of Taiwan compatriots’ employment and entrepreneurship on the mainland, and showcased the historic opportunities for economic and social integration and development across the Taiwan Strait. The joint reporting drew wide attention on both sides of the Strait. The topic “两岸e眼” (Cross-Strait e-Eye) was read more than 200 million times, and the series of posts “仪封家书” (Yifeng Family Letters) was read more than 3.3 million times across both sides.\nWe have said many times that media on both sides are bridges and links that enhance mutual understanding among compatriots across the Strait. Under the current impact of the COVID-19 epidemic, it is even more necessary for media to play a role in connecting both sides. We actively support cross-Strait news exchange and cooperation, and hope more young friends can make good use of various media to enhance mutual understanding and play a positive role in promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","A Taiwanese manager surnamed Cai of the Taiwan-invested company Kerui Technology is suspected of major economic crimes. Taizhou police in Jiangsu issued a wanted notice on the evening of November 28. Could the spokesperson introduce the current progress of the investigation in this case?","We have always done practical things, good things, and solved difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, and we safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in accordance with law. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises have deep experience of this. If disputes or other situations arise, they will be properly handled in accordance with law and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","At the end of the year, many compatriots from Taiwan working on the mainland are following information about returning home for the Spring Festival. Recently, the DPP authorities introduced the so-called “autumn-winter epidemic prevention special project,” which has added obstacles to the journey home for compatriots from Taiwan. At the same time, there is no news about charter flights for next year's Spring…","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and it is the same for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. For many years, relevant mainland authorities, guided by the purpose of serving cross-Strait exchanges and facilitating the return home of Taiwan compatriots for the New Year, have actively made arrangements for cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights. This year we will coordinate epidemic prevention and control with the needs of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots returning home, and make our utmost efforts to guarantee that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots can go home for the New Year. We also hope the DPP authorities will not, out of political calculation, deliberately make it harder for Taiwan residents to go home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","The controversy over opening Japan’s nuclear food imports is fermenting in Taiwan. Some commentators have pointed out that since only importing “Lai pork” (莱猪) can secure the Taiwan–U.S. trade agreement, naturally only by opening to nuclear food would Japan support Taiwan’s accession to the CPTPP. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any foreign country signing with Taiwan any agreement that has sovereignty implications or an official nature. As for the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), I have already answered this question: Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities, using “economic and trade” as a pretext and seeking political private gain at the cost of the food safety and health and well-being of the Taiwan people, will certainly fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","Two questions. First question: According to statistics, PLA aircraft conducted 300 sorties of exercises and training around Taiwan this year. Some foreign media interpret this as the mainland conducting so-called “gray zone tactics” to deplete Taiwan’s military strength and economy. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: At this year’s annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, some…","Let me answer the first question first. You just mentioned a foreign media article, which should be the Reuters report of December 10. Some of the so-called experts quoted in that report have no factual basis for their remarks. As I just pointed out, the root cause of the current complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities collude with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces, and continuously change tactics to provoke and pursue “independence,” undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seriously harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and gravely undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe PLA's organization of realistic combat drills in the Taiwan Strait area is a necessary action taken in response to the current security situation in the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty, and it is a stern response to interference by external forces and provocations by “Taiwan independence” forces. We will never allow anyone, any organization, any political party, at any time, in any form, to split any piece of Chinese territory away from China.\nSecond, you mentioned that there is a cognitive gap between Taiwan businesses and Taiwan residents on the mainland regarding cross-Strait economic development. The formation of this cognitive gap is both a result of the DPP authorities' political manipulation and a factor in the insufficient understanding of mainland conditions among Taiwan residents. At present, the mainland has achieved major strategic results in epidemic prevention and control, and the economy is stable and improving. In the first three quarters, mainland GDP grew by 0.7%, actual use of foreign capital grew by 5.2%, and foreign trade grew by 2.4% over the first 11 months, making it the only major economy in the world to achieve positive growth this year. Whether judged from the development trend or from the policy environment, resilience to pressure, market potential, and the quality of the workforce, the mainland is the best choice and greatest opportunity for Taiwan businesses to invest and establish themselves now and for some time to come.\nThe major opportunities and long-term benefits described for Taiwan in the Recommendations for the 14th Five-Year Plan create a broader space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses to develop on the mainland. The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) will also bring major benefits for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses seeking to establish their future layout on the mainland. “Both sides of the Strait are one family, and when relatives are close, both are well.” The mainland market is naturally the one that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses can reach first, being close to the water and so getting the moon first. If Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses can actively seize new opportunities for mainland development, fully participate in and deeply integrate into the new development pattern of the “major cycle” and “dual circulation,” they will surely achieve greater development and gains.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the “National Palace Museum” in Taipei may be downgraded and placed under the cultural authority. Some commentators believe this move has political considerations behind it and is related to ideology. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We note that rumors about the “renaming and downgrading” of the “National Palace Museum in Taipei” have aroused widespread questioning and strong criticism from all sectors of Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","On December 13, the 7th Cross-Strait Think Tank Academic Forum was held in Beijing. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","On December 13, the 7th Cross-Strait Think Tank Academic Forum was held in Beijing via video link, co-hosted by the Taiwan Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, the National Association for Taiwan Studies, the Taiwan Research Institute of Xiamen University, the Taiwan 21st Century Foundation, and the Institute of Social Sciences of Chinese Culture University in Taiwan.\nThe theme of this forum was “Safeguarding Peace and Stability, Deepening Integrated Development.” Under the current circumstances in which cross-Strait relations face severe challenges, how to overcome difficulties, remove obstacles, and push cross-Strait relations out from under the gloom and reopen a bright path that conforms to the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation is a matter of general concern to far-sighted people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait and to compatriots on both sides. The theme of the forum responds in a timely way to the general concerns of compatriots on both sides and fully matches their common expectations, and it has important practical significance. More than 60 experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait conducted in-depth discussions at the meeting on promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and built broad consensus.\nThe Cross-Strait Think Tank Academic Forum is an important platform for cross-Strait think tank exchanges. Since its founding in 2014, it has brought together think tank heads, experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait to conduct in-depth discussions and exchanges on key, difficult and hot issues in cross-Strait relations, has achieved positive results, and has drawn high attention from academic circles at home and abroad. We support the forum and hope it will become better and better, offering suggestions for promoting the forward development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","US President-elect Biden's staff recently called for cross-Strait dialogue. But Tsai Ing-wen still does not acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” Does the Mainland still insist that both sides return to the “1992 Consensus” before dialogue can be opened?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. The two sides of the Strait are one family, and matters across the Strait are family affairs. Chinese on both sides of the Strait have the wisdom and ability to resolve their own problems well.\nIf one denies the “1992 Consensus” and departs from the one-China principle, exchanges and dialogue are out of the question. Only when the DPP authorities return to the correct track of the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and stop scheming for “independence” and provocations can cross-Strait relations improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201216_12312348.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-12-22","Wang Wenbin","NHK","The U.S. Congress passed a funding bill for fiscal year 2021 and a COVID-19 relief bill containing content on Tibet's human rights and religious freedom. Do you have any comment on this?","China noticed reports on this. We resolutely oppose the U.S. Congress adoption of bills containing such ill contents on China. Issues related to Tibet, Taiwan and Hong Kong concern China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. They are China's internal affairs that allow no foreign interference. The Chinese government is determined in safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests. We urge the United States to stop meddling in our domestic affairs under those pretexts, refrain from signing the bills or implementing the negative contents and items in them that target China and undercut China's interests, so as to avoid further damaging overall China-U.S. cooperation and bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1841988.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1841959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-25","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Japan's deputy defense minister Yasuhide Nakayama told Reuters in an interview that he urged US President-elect Biden to clarify his position and policy on Taiwan. He also expressed worries that China would be more aggressive towards Taiwan. What's your comment?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. We are firmly against any country and anyone interfering in China's domestic affairs in any way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1842734.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1842731.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-28","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Besides the Tibetan Policy and Support Act, the U.S. leader also signed into law the Taiwan Assurance Act. What's your comment on this act?","I have just talked about China's position on the U.S. signing into law of the Tibet-related Act. What I said also applies to this Taiwan-related Act. China firmly opposes this.\nTaiwan-related issues, as part of China's internal affairs, bear on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and allow no interference by any external forces. The U.S. side should stop exploiting relevant issues to interfere in China's internal affairs, and take no actions to implement articles in the Act that target China and hurt China's interests, so as to avoid undermining China-U.S. relations and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1843027.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1842983.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2020-12-28","Zhao Lijian","","除了“西藏政策与支持法案”，美国领导人还签署了“台湾保证法案”。中方有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1843027.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1842983.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first reviewed and summarized the progress of cross-strait relations in 2020, looked ahead to the development of cross-strait relations in 2021, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-strait relations.","Welcome, everyone, to today's press conference.\nToday is the second-to-last day of 2020, and in one more day we will welcome the new year. The end of the year is a time to summarize, look back, and plan ahead. Today, we will first report on a summary of cross-Strait relations progress in 2020, and look ahead to the development of cross-Strait relations in 2021.\n2020 was an extraordinarily unusual year for Taiwan affairs work. The COVID-19 epidemic spread across the globe, the international situation changed profoundly, the situation across the Taiwan Strait was complex and grave, and cross-Strait relations faced severe challenges. We thoroughly implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan affairs work and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee, and under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we adapted, adjusted, and pushed forward through difficulties, achieving positive results in our Taiwan work.\nIn response to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities on the island and some external forces that have aggressively played the \"Taiwan card,\" we adopted a series of effective measures, dared to struggle, and were skilled at struggle. We severely dealt a blow to the arrogance of the \"Taiwan independence\" forces, curbed external interference, effectively safeguarded the overall stability of the situation across the Taiwan Strait, and served the overall cause of the Party and the state.\nWe upheld the principle of putting the people first and life first, shared weal and woe with Taiwan compatriots, and jointly fought the COVID-19 epidemic. We attached great importance to and safeguarded the lives and vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, took a series of measures to help Taiwan compatriots and enterprises with epidemic prevention and control, and assisted Taiwan-funded enterprises in resuming work and production. Taiwan compatriots and enterprises contributed love in various ways and conveyed warmth, and many moving stories emerged, demonstrating that the blood ties between the people on both sides of the Strait run deep.\nWe insisted on deepening cross-Strait integrated development and worked to relieve the concerns and difficulties of compatriots on both sides and to bring them benefits. Building on continued and thorough implementation of the \"31 Measures\" and the \"26 Measures,\" we also introduced the \"11 Measures\" to help Taiwan-funded enterprises resume work and production, and held a policy briefing for Taiwan businesses on participating in new infrastructure and a series of \"Taiwan-funded enterprises expand domestic sales\" activities. We issued measures on the hiring and management of Taiwan teachers, creating favorable conditions for Taiwan teachers to teach on the mainland. We actively promoted the connection of everything that can be connected and the integrated development of Fujian, as well as the \"small four connections\" work between the coastal areas of Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu. We actively carried out work to protect the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. These policies and measures are concrete expressions of the development philosophy centered on the people and vivid depictions of close relatives looking out for each other and family helping family.\nWorking hand in hand and with one heart with Taiwan compatriots, we pushed forward through difficulties and maintained momentum in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Although affected by the epidemic and by artificial obstruction and restrictions on the island, cross-Strait trade and economic exchanges continued to grow, the production and operations of mainland Taiwan-funded enterprises were generally stable, and some enterprises posted significant growth in performance. Taiwan businesses continue to see opportunities in mainland development and are confident in the mainland market's prospects and in putting down roots on the mainland. From January to November 2020, cross-Strait trade reached US$235.69 billion, up 13.8% year on year. We innovated in form and, combining online and offline methods, held more than 500 exchange activities, including the 12th Straits Forum, the 2020 annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum, and the 3rd Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, which Taiwan compatriots enthusiastically took part in. The trend of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation is unstoppable.\n2021 is the first year of the new journey to comprehensively build a modern socialist country and the opening year of the \"14th Five-Year Plan.\" We will continue to thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan affairs work and the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, actively promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, strive to create greater space and more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to take part in the process of national rejuvenation, and unite compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly advance the process of national reunification.\nNow, I invite everyone to ask questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314487.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","You just mentioned that, despite the impact of the epidemic and the artificial interference of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, cross-strait economic and trade exchanges continued to grow this year. Could you please introduce the progress made in cross-strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2020, and your outlook for 2021?","In 2020, facing the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and profound changes in the international situation, we insisted on deepening cross-Strait integrated development, sharing the burdens and solving the difficulties of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and bringing benefits to them. We actively helped Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises fully enjoy the policies to help enterprises tide over difficulties issued by regions and departments, issued the “11 Measures,” and implemented in detail the measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, while doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control and in resuming work and production. We actively helped Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises expand the mainland's domestic market, held a series of online promotion and matchmaking activities for “Taiwan-funded enterprises expanding domestic sales,” assisted Taiwan enterprises in participating in the Third China International Import Expo, and made good use of platforms such as “Taiwan businesses going e-commerce” and cross-border e-commerce. We actively paved the way for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to participate in the Belt and Road construction and the national regional coordinated development strategies, guiding more than ten provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, including Shandong and Beijing, to hold cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities combining offline and online formats. We provided more investment opportunities for Taiwan businesses and enterprises, strengthened the construction of cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones, and newly established a cross-Strait industrial cooperation zone in Jiangxi. We actively assisted Taiwan youth in internships, employment, and entrepreneurship on the mainland, guided regions and departments to hold a series of Taiwan youth employment and entrepreneurship activities, and strengthened the construction of cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites.\nThanks to the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges this year have generally been stable and making progress. From January to November, cross-Strait trade totaled US$235.69 billion, up 13.8% year on year. Of this, the mainland's exports to Taiwan were US$53.98 billion, up 8.4% year on year, and its imports from Taiwan were US$181.71 billion, up 15.6% year on year. Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland have generally maintained stable production and operations, and some Taiwan-funded enterprises have continued to increase capital and expand production; eight Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland successfully listed on the A-share market. Taiwan investment has shown the positive changes of more large projects and higher technological content, and cross-Strait industrial and supply chains have continued to stabilize.\nThe above situation fully illustrates two points. First, cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation meets the interests and needs of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, possesses strong endogenous momentum, and cannot be blocked by accidental events or human interference. Second, Taiwan's economy has maintained growth this year, which is inseparable from the contributions of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland and from the ties of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. Facts prove that Taiwan's economic development cannot do without the mainland; the development opportunities on the mainland and the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland have powerfully driven the economic development of the island and enhanced the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Only when compatriots on both sides of the Strait strengthen cooperation can Taiwan's economy have better prospects and Taiwan compatriots benefit more.\nIn 2021, we will thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on work concerning Taiwan and the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, follow the deployment of the 14th Five-Year Plan, take the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as our guiding principle, and continuously expand cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation. We will base ourselves on the new development stage, implement the new development philosophy, and build a new development pattern, helping Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises seize new opportunities and achieve new accomplishments. We will support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in expanding the domestic market and participating in the Belt and Road construction and the national regional coordinated development strategies, and help them seize the opportunities brought by the signing of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP). We will support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in integrating into the mainland's high-quality development, accelerating transformation and upgrading, deepening cooperation with mainland enterprises, complementing each other's strengths, and growing together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314486.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Cross-Strait Entrepreneurship Incubator Summit Forum was recently held in Nanjing. This year's establishment of the Entrepreneurship Incubator Alliance has injected new momentum into cross-strait youth entrepreneurship. May I ask the spokesperson what benefits there will be next year for Taiwan youth coming to the mainland to start businesses?","On December 17, the Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Incubator Summit was held in Nanjing. During the event, the Nanjing-Taiwan Service Industry Cooperation Promotion Center and the Nanjing Inno Light Dream Base jointly initiated the establishment of the Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Incubator Alliance, aiming to build a cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship incubator exchange and cooperation platform and to explore new paths and models for cooperative development.\nTaiwan's young people hope to gain more development opportunities on the mainland, and relevant mainland authorities have actively responded by providing policy support, creating a good environment, and working to resolve the practical difficulties and problems they face. The \"14th Five-Year Plan\" period is the opening and starting phase of our comprehensive building of a modern socialist country, and also an important period of opportunity for deepening cross-Strait integrated development. The mainland, based on the new development stage, implementing the new development philosophy, building a new development pattern, and promoting high-quality development, will provide more opportunities for Taiwan's young people to develop on the mainland. The signing and implementation of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) will also create greater space for Taiwan's young people to develop on the mainland. We hope that young friends will actively seize opportunities and achieve more and better development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314484.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","According to Taiwan statistics, in 2019, 395,000 people went to the mainland for work. Please introduce the relevant achievements of Taiwan youth in studying and working in the mainland, and what new opportunities will be available for Taiwan youth to develop in the mainland in 2021?","In recent years, we have successively introduced a series of policy measures, including the “31 Measures,” the “26 Measures” and the “11 Measures.” We have established 75 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases, launched 76 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases and demonstration sites, and encouraged 363 institutions of higher education to enroll Taiwan students, providing more favorable conditions for Taiwan youth to exchange, study, intern, find employment and start businesses on the mainland.\nIn 2020, affected by the adverse impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and the deliberate obstruction of the DPP authorities, Taiwan youth faced some difficulties in studying and working on the mainland, but this could not stop the steps of young people on both sides of the Strait toward closer contact and friendship. Taiwan youth actively took part in the battle against the COVID-19 epidemic and in the development of the mainland's economy and society, and demonstrated their talents and aspirations in many fields, including higher education, urban and rural grassroots governance, poverty alleviation, rural revitalization, technology services and cultural undertakings. Through their actions, they have proven that the Taiwan youth generation is not a “strawberry generation” but a “generation of hustlers.”\nAs we can see, during the fight against the epidemic, Taiwan youth and mainland youth fought side by side. Some rushed to the front lines of treating patients, some went down to the forefront of community epidemic prevention, and some created songs such as “Together with You,” “Mazu” and “Add Oil, Wuhan!”, fully demonstrating the responsibility and sentiment of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, whose blood is thicker than water and whose destinies are bound together.\nIn Fujian, 66 Taiwanese architect teams and more than 200 Taiwan youth have participated in local rural construction and rural innovation endeavors, serving 112 beautiful village projects across 30 counties. 97 Taiwan compatriots have been hired as science and technology commissioners, covering fields such as machinery, biotechnology, agriculture, environmental engineering and cultural tourism, and have carried out entrepreneurship and technical services in more than a hundred townships and villages.\nIn Guangdong, relying on the “1+2+3+11+n” social operation and management model, resources have been integrated, interconnected and coordinated, providing one-stop, all-round services for Taiwan youth for innovation and entrepreneurship, internships and employment, and living in Guangzhou. Many Taiwan youth have entered the live-streaming e-commerce industry, connecting Taiwan-invested enterprises with MCN agencies and livestreamers and providing new retail solutions, which have been welcomed by Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises.\nA Taiwan youth who has worked for many years in the machinery industry in Zhangzhou said, “The mainland's domestic market is strong enough, and it develops and improves greatly every year. As long as you are willing to work hard, there are plenty of opportunities.” His words reflect the voice of Taiwan youth on the mainland. We hope that more Taiwan youth will not be blinded by the hatred and discrimination deliberately stirred up by people with ulterior motives on the island, and will not miss great opportunities. Instead, they should see the situation clearly, seize opportunities, come to the mainland to pursue their dreams, and gain greater and better development in the great tide of cross-Strait integration and development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","We know that 2020 was an especially unusual year for cross-Strait exchanges. Could you introduce how cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields have gone this year? What plans are there for cross-Strait exchanges in 2021?","As you mentioned, in 2020, cross-Strait exchanges faced unprecedented impact. We firmly implemented the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” earnestly implemented the requirements for Taiwan work set out by the 19th National Congress and the Fourth and Fifth Plenary Sessions of the 19th Central Committee, and, together with relevant departments and localities, continued to implement in detail the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures,” continuously improved the policy of according Taiwan compatriots equal treatment, and at the same time innovated work methods, holding more than 500 “cloud exchange” events in the form of video links and a combination of online and offline activities. We guided Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities in doing the Taiwan-related work of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control; five Taiwan compatriots diagnosed in the mainland received timely treatment, and not a single Taiwan student studying on the mainland was infected. We carefully prepared a series of major Taiwan-related events such as the 12th Straits Forum, the 4th Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum, the academic symposium commemorating the 75th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, and thematic exhibitions. Through the joint efforts of various localities and relevant parties, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have continued, with highlights emerging continuously. Taiwan compatriots who study, work and live on the mainland have become the main participants in offline exchanges, and social media and entertainment apps have been more widely used among young people on both sides of the Strait; compared with traditional forms of exchange, some online exchange events have wider reach and greater awareness.\nIt should be pointed out that although we have overcome great difficulties, exchanges and personnel travel between the two sides of the Strait remain in a highly abnormal state. Artificially created obstacles have a greater impact than the COVID-19 epidemic. Since February, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have unilaterally suspended mainland residents' travel to Taiwan, closed the “small three links” between Kinmen, Matsu and Fujian, and extensively cancelled direct cross-Strait flight routes, seriously affecting personnel exchanges across the Strait and exchanges in all fields, and also adding many difficulties and obstacles for Taiwan compatriots traveling between the two sides.\nIn 2021, we will strive to eliminate interference, implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan work, improve measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepen cross-Strait integration and development. We will jointly promote Chinese culture, and strengthen exchanges at the grassroots level and among young people across the Strait. We will actively promote the forward development of exchanges and cooperation in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314485.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently Taiwan's legislature revised and passed certain provisions of the so-called Civil Code, lowering the age of civil majority to 18. Yu Si-kun claimed this opens the curtain on the so-called “constitutional amendment project.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We firmly oppose any force in Taiwan “amending the constitution to seek independence,” including opening the door to “independence” through “amending laws.” We hope that Taiwan compatriots will remain highly vigilant and oppose and curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities through concrete actions, so as to effectively prevent the occurrence of catastrophic consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314482.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Some Green camp politicians and media in Taiwan recently claimed that the “Kinmen Times” subscribed to by the Army in Taiwan stationed in Kinmen quoted reports from mainland media such as China Taiwan Network and China Youth Online, and that this would become a breach for alleged mainland “infiltration,” “helping the mainland carry out major external propaganda.” What is your comment on this?","Certain “Taiwan independence” politicians on the island and media holding specific positions have repeatedly slandered the mainland for so-called “united front” work and “infiltration,” creating topics and stirring up hostility and confrontation between the two sides. This kind of attention-grabbing operation for private gain has crossed the moral bottom line.\nChina Taiwan Net is a website based on letting the Taiwan public understand the mainland and letting the mainland public understand Taiwan. China Youth Net is currently the largest website on the mainland serving young people, reflecting youthful warmth and youthful appeal. We hope the broad Taiwan public can, through these two websites and more mainland media, more widely and deeply understand the economic and social development of the mainland, and understand the lives of mainland compatriots from more angles and at deeper levels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the DPP held an “Economic Security Symposium,” at which it was mentioned that adjusting Taiwan's industrial dependence on the mainland has become a focus of attention. What is your comment on this?","Over 40 years of practice of reform and opening up fully demonstrate that Taiwan’s economic development cannot do without the mainland. Cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation helps give play to complementary advantages and achieve mutual benefit and win-win outcomes, and it also helps stimulate Taiwan’s domestic economic development and enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities, looking at the issue through “tinted glasses,” obstruct and restrict cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. This way of thinking and acting, which excludes oneself from the world’s most potential large market, is like trying to lift oneself off the ground by pulling one’s own hair. It is extremely ridiculous and futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan's legislature recently, disregarding public opposition, forcibly passed nine executive orders, including those permitting the import of U.S. pork containing ractopamine and U.S. beef from cattle over 30 months of age. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We see that most people on the island have opposed, from the very beginning, opening imports of US pork and beef containing ractopamine, and cannot accept importing agricultural and livestock products with problematic hidden dangers at the cost of health. As Taiwan public opinion has pointed out, before taking office, the DPP strongly opposed importing 'ractopamine beef,' but after taking office it arbitrarily opened imports of 'ractopamine pork.' This is a typical 'hairpin bend.' It shows that the DPP cares only about the private interests of its own party and does not truly care about the immediate interests of the Taiwan people.\nAccording to the Food Safety Law and other provisions, the mainland does not permit imports of pork, beef, and their products containing ractopamine. We will take effective measures to prevent non-compliant meat products from flowing in.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314481.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Continuing the topic of US-Taiwan relations: US President Trump recently signed the “Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021,” which contains Taiwan-related content. What is the spokesperson's view?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and the United States has no right to interfere. We firmly oppose the U.S. side's adoption of legislation containing Taiwan-related content. The DPP authorities are willing to serve as a pawn, attempting to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence,” and are destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202012/t20201230_12314483.htm"],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Mainland airlines require that nucleic acid test reports carried by passengers entering the mainland from Taiwan must not contain the words “Wuhan pneumonia,” otherwise they will be deemed invalid. What is your comment on the DPP authorities’ continued use of this stigmatizing name to this day?","As early as February this year, the World Health Organization officially announced that the pneumonia caused by the novel coronavirus would be named COVID-19. The name of a virus must not contain the name of a region, animal, individual, or any group. The DPP authorities have disregarded the WHO's official naming and the naming norms for diseases and viruses, and deliberately used stigmatizing labels, with base intentions. We have consistently and firmly opposed this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","We note that the possibility of the mainland formulating a “National Unification Law” has recently drawn attention from the media on both sides of the Strait. What comment does the spokesperson have?","National reunification is the trend of the times and will inevitably be realized. We will resolutely curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","《海峡之声》广播电台记者","We know that Kunshan is one of the earliest and most concentrated areas for Taiwanese investment in the mainland. Kunshan, Jiangsu recently held a symposium marking the 30th anniversary of Kunshan–Taiwan integrated development, and the 《Kunshan Regulations on Deepening Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone》 will take effect on January 1 next year. May I ask the spokesperson: after the promulgation of the…","Since the first Taiwan-funded enterprise settled in Kunshan in October 1990, Kunshan has approved more than 5,300 Taiwan-funded projects in total, and nearly 100,000 Taiwanese businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots live and work in peace and contentment in Kunshan. Taiwanese enterprises contribute more than 30% of Kunshan's gross domestic product, 50% of its gross industrial output value, 60% of its utilization of foreign capital, and over 70% of its import and export volume. Kunshan has become one of the regions on the mainland with the densest Taiwanese investment and the most active cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges. In February 2013, the State Council approved the establishment of the Kunshan Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone. Recently, the State Council approved expanding the scope of the Kunshan Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone to the entire city of Kunshan.\nOn December 25, a symposium marking the 30th anniversary of Kunshan–Taiwan integrated development was held in Kunshan City, Jiangsu Province. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Ning Jizhe, Vice Chairman of the National Development and Reform Commission, Luo Qinjian, Party Secretary of Jiangsu Province, and other relevant people from both sides of the Strait attended. In his speech at the symposium, Director Liu Jieyi pointed out that Kunshan and Taiwanese businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots worked together to forge a path of Kunshan–Taiwan integration with Kunshan's own characteristics, which has become a microcosm of compatriots on both sides of the Strait working together to broaden and deepen the path of cross-Strait integrated development. This successful practice demonstrates that economic cooperation is the solid foundation for deepening cross-Strait integrated development, that the will of the people is the inexhaustible driving force for deepening cross-Strait integrated development, that institutional arrangements are an important guarantee for deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and that building together and sharing together is the fundamental pursuit of deepening cross-Strait integrated development.\nThe 《Regulations on the Kunshan Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone》, reviewed and adopted by the Standing Committee of the Jiangsu Provincial People's Congress, will take effect on January 1 next year. The Regulations will provide stronger legal support for the Kunshan Pilot Zone to carry out reform and opening up over a wider scope, in more fields and at deeper levels, and to create a first-class business environment. We will, as always, support the Kunshan Pilot Zone, carry out more beneficial explorations in deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and make greater contributions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","With Spring Festival approaching, is there any latest news on charter flight arrangements for Taiwan businesspeople returning to Taiwan?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots all hope to return home smoothly to celebrate the holiday and be reunited with their families. We feel deeply for their wishes and attach great importance to them. We will coordinate the consideration of epidemic prevention and control with the needs of Taiwan compatriots to return home, and do our utmost to provide positive assurance for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots to return home for the New Year. But solving this problem also requires cooperation from the Taiwan side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The results of Taiwan's 2020 Character of the Year were announced recently in Taipei. The character “epidemic” (疫) was elected as Taiwan's 2020 Character of the Year with one-third of the votes. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted this situation. Looking back: from “bitter” in 2016, “lost” in 2017, “turn” in 2018, “chaos” in 2019, to “epidemic” in 2020, for five consecutive years, characters expressing negative emotions have been selected as Taiwan's character of the year. What does this indicate? To a certain extent, does it reflect the dissatisfaction of Taiwan's people with the status quo on the island and their concern about the prospects of cross-Strait relations? We have seen many interpretations in the island's media, and we also hope the DPP authorities will reflect seriously.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Taiwan's cultural authorities recently stated that they will strengthen the review of publications from the mainland. What is your comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. The measures you mentioned, once implemented, would most affect Taiwan’s publishing industry and its people.\nCross-Strait publishing exchange was one of the earliest and most notably successful areas of cross-Strait cultural exchange. In recent years, through the joint efforts of publishing circles and relevant parties on both sides, cross-Strait publishing exchange has progressed from indirect to direct, from one-way to two-way, and from general exchange to substantive cooperation, and from copyright trade and joint publishing to resource integration and complementary advantages. It has made positive progress and allowed people on both sides to enjoy a richer cultural feast. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, instead of following public sentiment and doing more good things that benefit exchanges between people on both sides, have gone against the trend, constantly erecting political obstacles, which will only further harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","We know that the mainland has recently begun administering COVID-19 vaccines to key groups, including people working in imported cold chain, aviation, fresh food markets, and medical and disease control, who face relatively high infection risks. Are Taiwan compatriots working in related industries on the mainland eligible to be vaccinated?","At present, in arranging COVID-19 vaccination, priority is given to groups with higher infection risk, such as those in imported cold-chain logistics, ports, and international and domestic transportation. These priority groups include Taiwan compatriots. After COVID-19 vaccines are launched, proper arrangements will also be made for preventive vaccination of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. Here I would also like to remind everyone: when going out, please continue to take good personal protection, wear masks, wash hands frequently, and keep a safe distance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Continuing on the vaccine issue: Previously, the MAC reminded the public to carefully consider the necessity of getting mainland vaccines in order to protect their own safety rights. What is your comment?","Since the COVID-19 outbreak, the mainland has from the outset laid out five technical routes for vaccines: inactivated vaccines, recombinant protein vaccines, adenovirus vector vaccines, attenuated influenza virus vector vaccines, and nucleic acid vaccines, and has conducted research and development in a standardized and orderly manner. I believe everyone has also learned from the joint prevention and control mechanism press conference of the State Council that five vaccines are currently undergoing Phase III clinical trials in several countries, including the UAE, Brazil, Pakistan and Peru. At the same time, multiple vaccines are accelerating Phase I and II clinical trials. These Phase I, II and III clinical trials of COVID-19 vaccines, as well as the emergency vaccination of nearly one million person-times already carried out on the premise of voluntariness, informed consent, and in accordance with laws and regulations, fully demonstrate that the mainland's COVID-19 vaccines are very safe. The DPP authorities do not understand these vaccines and groundlessly spread doubts. This is unethical and entirely politically motivated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the Fuping Railway, the mainland railway closest to Taiwan, officially opened for operation. What new conveniences does this bring to mainland Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises?","The Fu-Ping Railway officially opened for operation on December 26. Running from Fuzhou to Pingtan, it is 88 kilometers long, and the trip takes as little as 35 minutes. It brings greater convenience to Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots living in Fujian, especially Pingtan.\nPingtan is located in eastern Fujian Province, facing Taiwan across the strait. It is only 68 nautical miles from Hsinchu, Taiwan, making it the point on the Chinese mainland closest to Taiwan Island. The Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone is a national-level comprehensive experimental zone \"established because of Taiwan and distinguished by Taiwan.\" Here, land and sea shake hands and the two sides of the Strait are connected. The Fu-Ping Railway, which crosses the Haitan Strait, has formed a \"half-hour living circle\" with Fuzhou, the provincial capital of Fujian, and other places, further optimizing and improving the Fujian railway network. As a main channel for cross-Strait exchanges, Pingtan has already opened cargo and passenger direct flight routes to Taipei, Taichung, and Kaohsiung. Combined with the Fu-Ping Railway and the Lan-Tai direct flight route, Pingtan will build a \"golden corridor\" that benefits compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Through this \"sea-rail intermodal transport,\" realizing cross-Strait interconnection creates comparative advantages of low cost, high speed, and fast customs clearance, which can continue to help Fujian explore new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that in 2020, the Taiwan side set up many man-made obstacles to personnel exchanges across the Strait, such as canceling the “small three links” and canceling most flight routes, etc. We hope that in 2021, man-made interference can be eliminated as much as possible. Since August 2019, the mainland has suspended individual free-travel tours for residents to Taiwan. May I ask the…","When this situation arose, we clearly stated that it was due to cross-Strait relations. To solve this problem, we still have to return to cross-Strait relations. We have repeatedly stressed that the root cause of the tension in cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and unilaterally undermine the common political foundation of cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, causing cross-Strait dialogue and consultation to stall, and also seriously undermining the basis and conditions for the pilot program of individual travel by mainland residents to Taiwan. In recent times, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and on the other hand, constantly engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” causing many matters between the two sides to be unable to proceed normally. Only by returning to the right track of the “1992 Consensus” can the relevant issues be resolved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2020-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Recently, the US think tank “National Committee on American Foreign Policy” proposed that both sides of the Taiwan Strait establish an “effective signaling mechanism” to promote stability in the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's view?","In fact, the door to dialogue between our two sides of the Strait has always been open. On the basis of the One-China Principle, there are no obstacles to exchanges between us and any Taiwan political party, group, or individual. As I have just said, the root cause of the tension in cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and unilaterally deny the common political basis for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. If the “1992 Consensus” is denied and the One-China Principle is abandoned, there can be no talk of any exchange or dialogue.\nI want to stress once again that, on the political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to conduct dialogue and consultation in diverse forms and on a wide range of topics with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals on political issues across the Taiwan Strait and on matters related to advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, seeking common ground while setting aside differences and accumulating consensus.\nTomorrow we will bid farewell to 2020. This year we have gone through an extremely extraordinary journey. Everyone has worked together with one heart, and after arduous efforts, we have pulled through. As we face the coming 2021, let us wish compatriots on both sides of the Strait good health, success in their careers, and happy families. Good cross-Strait relations are good for Taiwan. Cross-Strait affairs are a family affair (in Hokkien). I hope that in the new year, compatriots on both sides will visit each other more, exchange more, make big money together, and stay safe together (in Hakka).\nI also want to express my sincere thanks to the media friends present here. Over the past year, the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office has received strong support from journalists and media outlets, and I am very grateful! You have worked hard!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202012/t20201230_12314479.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2020-12-31","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Two US destroyers passed through the Taiwan Strait early this morning. The US said this operation shows its commitment to the freedom of navigation in the relevant waters in line with international law. We noticed that since the beginning of this year, the US military activities in the relevant waters have increased significantly compared with previous years. What is your comment?","The spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense already made a response. The Chinese side was closely following and fully aware of the US military vessels' passage through the Taiwan Strait. The US warships have repeatedly flaunted their prowess in the Taiwan Strait, provoked and stirred up trouble, sent wrong signals to the Taiwan-independence forces, and seriously jeopardized peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We express our firm opposition to this.\nChina will continue to be on high alert, ready to respond to all threats and provocations at any time, and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US side to play a constructive role for regional peace and stability rather than doing the contrary.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1843871.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202012/t20201231_5419694.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2020-12-31","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","In 2020, the COVID-19 pandemic wreaked havoc around the world and there have been profound changes in the international security environment. Nevertheless, the Chinese military has risen to the challenge and achieved fruitful outcomes in international military cooperation through innovative methods. The PLA Daily published an article on December 31, which reviewed and interpreted the highlights of China’s…","The year 2020 is an unusual year both for China and the world. The review of China’s international military cooperation and its highlights published by the PLA Daily is a faithful portrayal of how we have overcome difficulties and made progress in international military cooperation. In the face of the sweeping outbreak of COVID-19 and complicated international security environment in 2020, the Chinese military, guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, has strictly implemented the decisions made by the CPC Central Committee, CMC and President Xi on international military cooperation. Keeping in mind and focusing on the overall political and diplomatic interests of the Party and the country, the military has endeavored to foster opportunities out of crises and open a new horizon amid changes, making new a contribution to defending national interests, preserving world peace, and building a community with a shared future for mankind.\nFirst, the military has been actively engaged in international cooperation with foreign counterparts in fighting the COVID-19 pandemic. Leaders of the CMC have sent letters to the defense and military leaders of 28 countries and held phone talks with defense leaders of 12 countries, expressing sympathies to their pandemic situation and gratitude for their assistance to China. The PLA has provided anti-epidemic supplies to the militaries of 50 countries, sent experts to the militaries of four countries, held video conferences to share epidemic prevention and control experience with the militaries of 18 countries (international organizations), and offered assistance to foreign military personnel in China, making great contributions to building a community of common health for mankind.\nSecond, the Chinese military has fostered favorable strategic posture. The Chinese and Russian militaries have continuously deepened exchanges and cooperation in high-level exchanges, epidemic prevention and control, joint exercises and other fields, intensified strategic coordination and mutual support and maintained the high-level development of mil-to-mil relationship.\nThe Chinese and the US militaries have strengthened strategic communication, and managed and controlled risks and divergences to keep their relations generally stable.\nChina and Europe have steadily advanced defense and security cooperation and carried out institutional dialogues and exchanges. With neighboring countries, China has had active high-level exchanges to deepen practical defense cooperation and advance the construction of a neighborhood community with a shared future.\nChina has also kept close military relations with developing countries in Africa and Latin America.\nBesides, China participated in the China-ASEAN defense ministers’ informal meetings and ASEAN Defense Ministers’ Meeting-Plus (ADMM-Plus), and hosted workshops underthe Beijing Xiangshan Forum, doing its active part to respond to regional and global challenges. China has also engaged deeply in the international arms control cooperation and the global security governance, and consistently provided public security products in forms of peacekeeping operations and naval escort missions to safeguard global strategic stability.\nThird, the Chinese military have focused on military preparedness and combat readiness. In implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Strengthening the Military and the military strategic guideline for a new era, the military, while strictly carrying out anti-pandemic measures, has strengthened practical exchanges and cooperation with foreign counterparts on military training.\nIt organized the second China-Russia joint aerial strategic patrol, and participated in a list of international military events, including the “Military World Games 2020”, “Kavkaz-2020” strategic exercise hosted by the Russian military, China-Pakistan “Sea Guardians 2020” joint maritime exercise and “Shaheen (Eagle) – IX” joint air force training, China-Cambodia “Dragon Golden 2020” joint training, and “Cobra Gold-2020” multilateral military exercise.\nThese joint exercises and training have enhanced the mutual trust and exchanges between the Chinese military and its foreign counterparts, and improved realistic training of Chinese troops.\nFourth, the Chinese militaryhas defended national interests and dignity. Whenever foreign forces tried to pressure and provoke China on the Taiwan question and the South China Sea issue, the Chinese military has always made its stance known and firmly fought back.\nThe Chinese military has staunchly safeguarded national sovereignty and territorial integrity and strongly responded to the US arms sales to Taiwan, its military vessels’ trespassing into Chinese territorial waters off islands and reefs in the South China Sea, and its defense leaders’ groundless accusations against China.\nAdhering to military and diplomatic channels, including border defense exchange, Chinese side has communicated and consulted with the Indian side, urging it to maintain peace and tranquility in the border area. Furthermore, the military has been committed to expose all kinds of disinformation, lies and slanders about the military, clarifying facts and truths.\nFinally, the Chinese military has been sharing its vision with the world. The Chinese military has released a white paper titled China’s Armed Forces: 30 Years of UN Peacekeeping Operations, which expounds on the original aspiration, policies, practices, visions and initiatives of China's participation in the UN peacekeeping operations.\nIn combination with the anti-epidemic aid to foreign counterparts, the Chinese military, taking into consideration of the recipients’ cultural features, has designed 50 bilingual posters that embody the essence of the Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and sent them along with the anti-epidemic supplies, in a bid to pass confidence and strength to the peoples afflicted by COVID-19 .\nThe year 2021 marks the 100th anniversary of the founding of the CPC and the beginning of China’s 14th Five-year Plan. No matter how the international situation changes, the Chinese military, under the guidance of the Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, will continue to uphold the concept of building a community with a shared future for mankind, advance international military cooperation of the new era, and contribute to creating a beautiful world of lasting peace and universal security.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-01/02/content_4876356.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2021-01-04","Hua Chunying","N/A — opening announcement (no press Q)","","Welcome to the year 2021's first regular press conference. The year 2020 has been an extraordinary year for China and the world, giving me all the more reasons to thank friends from the press for being with us every step of the way, documenting and bearing witness to how we in the foreign service have forged ahead and tackled the challenges head on.\nThe year 2021 will be of historic significance to China as we will celebrate the CPC's centenary. In the 1930s and 1940s, when the then Kuomintang government sealed off Yan'an and spared no efforts to \"demonize\" the CPC, foreign journalists like Americans Edgar Snow, Anna Louise Strong and Agnes Smedley, curious about who and what the CPC is, chose to blend in with the CPC members in Yan'an after going through various difficulties to get there, where they wrote many objective reports as well as works like the famous Red Star over China, giving the world its first glimpse of the CPC and its endeavor in uniting and leading the Chinese people in pursuing national independence and people's liberation. They were indeed a window for the world to understand the CPC and China. They will always be remembered by the Chinese people as our good and true friends.\nWe will celebrate the CPC's centenary and realize the first \"centenary goal\" in the year 2021, the first chapter of the Party's great cause and embark on the second \"centenary goal\" to build a new journey of fully building a modern socialist country. We sincerely hope that all of the foreign journalists will employ their pens and cameras to faithfully and objectively report on the CPC's state governance, the Chinese people's pursuit of their dreams and China's commitment to peaceful development. In promoting mutual understanding and cooperation, you will serve as the indispensable bridge and bond between China and the rest of the world.\nThe Information Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs will continue to provide all necessary convenience and assistance for your work and life in China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1844368.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210104_5419697.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-01-04","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, on January 1 local time, the US approved the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2021,” which contains multiple China-related provisions. The act calls for developing a “whole-of-government strategy toward China” and implementing the “Pacific Deterrence Initiative” to respond to China's military development, supports continued arms sales to Taiwan, and maintains its…","The China-related content of the above bill clings to Cold War mentality, hypes the so-called “China military threat,” fuels U.S.-China strategic competition, flagrantly departs from the basic norms of international relations, crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously undermines the development of China-U.S. and military-to-military relations, and seriously damages China's sovereignty, security, and development interests. China firmly opposes this and has lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side.\nChina has always adhered to the path of peaceful development, upholds a common, comprehensive, cooperative, and sustainable security concept, firmly pursues a defensive national defense policy and a military strategy of active defense, and insists on being a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a defender of the international order. In recent years, the Chinese military has provided an increasing number of public security goods in areas such as international peacekeeping, far-seas escort, and humanitarian rescue and disaster relief. In particular, since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic, the Chinese military has actively carried out international anti-epidemic cooperation, contributing to building a global community of health for all. Facts fully prove that the development of the Chinese military brings the peoples of the world not threats and challenges but security and hope. The Chinese military is always a firm force for safeguarding world peace.\nThe U.S. side, out of its own selfish interests, advocates implementing the “Pacific Deterrence Initiative,” continuously strengthens its military presence in the Asia-Pacific region, hypes military competition, and promotes military confrontation. This exposes its consistent hegemonic nature. It will only intensify regional tensions and endanger world peace, and it will ultimately harm the interests of the United States itself.\nTaiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, and other issues concern China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and are purely China's internal affairs, which brook no interference from any external force. China's resolve to safeguard its national sovereignty, security, and development interests is unwavering. It must be emphasized that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the sacred territory of the motherland. Whatever way the United States uses to “use Taiwan to contain China” is doomed to be a fool's dream. We firmly oppose any country conducting any form of official exchange or military contact with Taiwan. We will never allow anyone, any organization, or any political party to split any piece of Chinese territory from China at any time, in any form. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe urge the U.S. side to follow the trend of the times toward peace and development, discard Cold War thinking and zero-sum game notions, view China and the development of the Chinese military objectively, immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, and not implement the China-related provisions of the bill. We also look forward to the U.S. side meeting China halfway to jointly safeguard the overall situation of China-U.S. and military-to-military relations and world peace and stability.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278503.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-01-06","Hua Chunying","The Paper","U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo told an interview that \"The China-EU investment deal was a weak deal. It didn't protect the European workers from the predation of the Chinese Communist Party.\" Do you have any comment?","Isn't that sour grapes? If the China-EU investment deal can't protect European workers, can the U.S. additional tariffs protect them?\nChina and the European side have concluded a balanced, high-level and mutually beneficial investment agreement after seven years of joint efforts, which not only demonstrates China's determination and confidence in promoting high-level opening-up, but also provides greater market access, a better business environment, stronger institutional guarantee and brighter prospects for China-EU mutual investment. It has been highly commended by people from in China and Europe as well as the international community. The conclusion of the negotiations is widely regarded as a milestone in China-EU economic and trade cooperation and a victory for multilateralism. In a grim situation where the pandemic hit the global economy hard, the conclusion of the China-EU investment agreement will help promote the recovery of the world economy, uphold multilateralism and safeguard an rules-based, open world economy.\nJust as an ancient Chinese poem said, \"Despite the incessant cry of apes from the banks, the swift boat has already sailed through thousands of hills\". China is ready to work with all parties, including the EU, to make the pie of shared interests bigger and achieve higher levels of mutual benefit and win-win results.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1844806.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1844754.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-06","Hua Chunying","China Daily","According to media reports, the U.S. Assistant Secretary of State for Political-Military Affairs R. Clarke Cooper will attend and address the virtual US-Taiwan Political Military Dialogue on the evening of January 6 EST. Do you have a comment?","We note relevant reports. The U.S. act is in serious violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. We reject and condemn it.\nThe Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations as it bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop any form of official exchange and military ties with Taiwan to avoid causing further damage to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations. China will take necessary actions in response to the developments to firmly defend its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1844806.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1844754.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","(Xinhua) Beijing, January 6 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fengl ian responded on the 6th to the planned so-called “political-military dialogue” between Taiwan and the US, pointing out that we have consistently and firmly opposed any form of official exchanges and military contacts between Taiwan and the US. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces. The DPP authorities, “relying on the US to seek independence” and willing to be pawns, will only bring deep disaster to the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210106_12315446.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-07","Hua Chunying","Global Times","U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo said in a statement that more than 50 people arrested by the Hong Kong police should be released immediately and unconditionally. He also said that the United States will consider sanctions and other restrictions on any and all individuals and entities involved in executing this assault on the Hong Kong people, explore restrictions against the Hong Kong Economic and Trade Office in…","Pompeo's statement gravely runs counter to basic norms of international relations, interferes in China's domestic affairs and judicial sovereignty, and violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. China rejects and condemns it.\nThere is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Central People's Government of the PRC is the sole legal government representing China. This is a fact recognized by the international community. The United States made an explicit commitment on this in the 1979 Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, China firmly opposes any forms of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear.\nHong Kong is a society with rule of law where all is equal before the law and no extrajudicial privilege exists. Laws must be complied with and offences must be prosecuted. This is the basic connotation of rule of law. We firmly support relevant authorities of the Hong Kong SAR in cracking down on criminal offenses according to law. We stand firmly against interference in Hong Kong affairs and disruption of Hong Kong's rule of law by any country, organization or individual in any means.\nFor some time, a handful of anti-China politicians within the Trump administration have been staging a show of madness as their days at the rein are numbered, stopping at nothing to deliberately sabotage China-US relations for selfish political interests. Such ploys go against the trend of history and the friendly sentiment of both peoples and are bound to be punished by history.\nWe urge the United States to immediately stop meddling in China's internal affairs, harming Chinese interests and undermining bilateral relations. China will take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and security interests. The U.S. side shall pay a heavy price for its erroneous actions.\nI also noticed that Pompeo called what happened at Congress unacceptable. Did he find the violent storming of Hong Kong's Legislative Council acceptable? He said he wanted to free the people of Hong Kong from the CPC's oppression. I hope he will open his eyes and see how the people in Hong Kong and the rest of China are leading perfectly happy lives. From Pompeo we did have learned a lot and we are actually grateful for that. Thanks to him, we Chinese people cherish our life and love our motherland more, and are more convinced in the decisions we've made and path we've taken.\nI've also noticed American media's coverage of an opinion piece that says \"There is not enough space in this newspaper to chronicle all of Pompeo's falsehoods.\" There is a post circulating on Chinese social media that jests \"If the United States saw what the United States is doing in the United States, the United States would invade the United States to liberate the United States from the tyranny of the United States.\" In that vein, shouldn't Mr. Pompeo consider applying some sanctions on himself?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845062.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1844973.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-07","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News Agency","According to Taiwanese media reports, the United States and Taiwan held a political military dialogue today. Do you have any comment on this?","I responded to a similar question yesterday. China's position on the exchange between China and the Taiwan region is clear and consistent. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and refrain from further undercutting China-U.S. mutual trust and causing more damages to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations. The Chinese side has lodged stern representations to the U.S. side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845062.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1844973.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-01-07","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that on January 7, the U.S. and the Taiwan authorities held a so-called “political-military dialogue” via video. What is the Chinese Ministry of National Defense’s comment on this?","We strongly condemn this serious act by the US side, which violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and we have lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair. It concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, involves China's core interests, and brooks no foreign interference. We demand that the US immediately stop any form of official exchanges and military contact with Taiwan. The PLA will, with firm resolve and strong capabilities, thwart any form of external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278504.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-01-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","People's Daily Online, Beijing, January 7. Recently, the DPP authorities and some of their prominent figures have made remarks about the Hong Kong police's lawful arrest of persons suspected of violating the Hong Kong National Security Law. In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 7th when asked that it is only natural for the Hong Kong SAR government to sanction lawbreakers in accordance with the law. The DPP authorities' big talk once again exposes their overestimation of themselves and their evil nature of disrupting Hong Kong and seeking “independence.” They must stop such despicable acts of political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs and attempts to encourage illegal activities. Accumulating crimes by stubbornly seeking “independence” will inevitably bring retribution upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210107_12315762.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 7 (dateline). In response to the so-called “political-military dialogue” held between Taiwan and the United States, the DPP authorities took the opportunity to once again promote “Taiwan independence” rhetoric. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 7th, saying that the “Taiwan independence” forces’ scheme of seeking “independence” while groveling before external forces is entirely futile and cannot change the fact that Taiwan is a part of China.\nZhu Fenglian said that we solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop all forms of official exchanges and military contacts with the United States, not to go further and further down the wrong path of “relying on the US to seek independence,” and not to push the people of Taiwan into disaster; otherwise, they will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210107_12315774.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 7 — In response to Pompeo's statement on the U.S. State Department website on January 7, which viciously attacked China, and his announcement that the U.S. Ambassador to the United Nations would visit Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to questions on the same day: We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose the United States' serious and wrongful actions on the Taiwan question in violation of the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués.\nZhu Fenglian further pointed out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have sold out the interests of the nation and the Taiwan people, obstinately \"relied on the U.S. to seek independence,\" and gone down a dead-end road; they will surely reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210107_12315776.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-08","Hua Chunying","RIA Novosti","The U.S. Mission to the United Nations announced last night that U.S. ambassador to the United Nations Kelly Craft will visit Taiwan from January 13 to 15. Do you have any response?","We stated China's principled position yesterday. China's position on the issue of U.S.-Taiwan exchanges is clear and consistent. The actions of the U.S. side seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. China firmly opposes it.\nThere is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. This is a fact recognized by the international community. The United States made a clear commitment on this in the Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between China and the United States. China firmly opposes any form of official ties between the United States and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear. We have noticed that for a period of time, a few anti-China politicians in the Trump administration, or Pompeo and his like if you will, have put on stage their \"final madness\", unscrupulously using the remaining days in office to sabotage China-U.S. relations and serve their personal political gains. This trick goes against the tide of history and runs counter to the desire of the Chinese and American peoples for friendship and peace, which will definitely get punished by history.\nWe also urge the U.S. side to return to reason and stop any words and deeds that undermine bilateral relations. China will take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard its own sovereign and security interests. If the U.S. side insists on going its way, it will pay a heavy price for its wrong words and deeds.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845310.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1845277.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-11","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","U.S. Secretary of State Pompeo announced the lifting of \"self-imposed restrictions on the U.S.-Taiwan relationship\". An official with Biden's transition team also said that once inaugurated, Biden will continue to support a peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question in keeping with the wishes and best interests of the Taiwanese people. What's China's response?","China rejects and condemns the U.S. move.\nThere is but one China in the world. The People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a fact recognized by the international community and a basic norm of international relations.\nThe U.S. government made a solemn commitment to the Chinese side on the question of Taiwan. The China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, released on December 16, 1978, clearly stipulates that \"The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\" The United States should honor its commitment and not misinterpret or deviate from it under any pretext.\nThe so-called \"Taiwan Relations Act\" severely violates the one-China principle, the three China-US joint communiqués and basic norms of international relations. The Chinese government is firmly opposed to it right from the start. It is the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués that the United States should abide by when it comes to issues relating to Taiwan, not the unilaterally-concocted \"Taiwan Relations Act\".\nThe Chinese people is firmly determined to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will never allow anyone or any force to stand in the way of national reunification or to meddle in China's domestic affairs with Taiwan as a pretext. Actions that harm China's core interests are futile and will be met with resolute responses.\nThe Taiwan question remains the most important and sensitive issue at the core of China-U.S. relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of bilateral relations and the precondition for establishing and developing diplomatic relations. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop elevating relations and military ties with Taiwan. We advise Mr. Pompeo and his likes to recognize the historical trend, stop manipulating Taiwan-related issues, stop retrogressive acts and stop going further down the wrong and dangerous path, otherwise they will be harshly punished by history.\nAs to the remarks you mentioned by an official with Mr. Biden's transition team, we urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official exchanges and military ties with Taiwan, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845634.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1845585.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 11 — On January 9, Pompeo issued a statement lifting restrictions on official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. The DPP authorities expressed gratitude. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 11th: We will take firm and forceful measures to counter any collusion between Taiwan and the United States.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that we have repeatedly reiterated our firm opposition to official exchanges between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. The one-China principle is the political foundation and fundamental premise for the establishment of China-US diplomatic relations. Adhering to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués is a commitment made by the US government. Any practice that violates this commitment seriously contravenes the basic norms of international relations and is illegal and void. The DPP authorities, acting as pawns for external forces and “relying on the US to seek independence,” will only bring serious disaster to the people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/wyly/202101/t20210111_12316309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-12","Zhao Lijian","Reuters/Bloomberg","Taiwan's representative to the Netherlands recently met with the U.S. Ambassador at the U.S. Embassy there after Secretary of State Pompeo lifted restrictions on U.S.-Taiwan interactions. The U.S. Assistant Secretary of State Cooper met with Taiwan's Representative to the United States Bi-khim Hsiao on January 11. Does the foreign ministry have any response?","I already stated China's solemn position on Taiwan-related issues yesterday.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation and fundamental precondition for the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the United States. The China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations clearly stipulates that \"The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\" It is the solemn pledge of the U.S. side not to have official interactions with the Taiwan region. It should honor its commitment and not misinterpret or deviate from it under any pretext.\nWe urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop manipulating Taiwan-related issues and stop going further down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845846.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1845835.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-12","Zhao Lijian","","1月10日，吉尔吉斯斯坦举行总统选举。根据吉中央选举委员会11日公布的初步结果，卡德尔·扎帕罗夫高票胜选。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1845846.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1845835.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2021-01-13","Zhao Lijian","South China Morning Post","The U.S. State Department confirmed that the U.S. Ambassador to the UN Kelly Craft's visit to Taiwan is canceled. What's your comment?","My colleagues and I have repeatedly stated China's position on the U.S. ambassador Craft's plan to visit Taiwan. I'd like to stress once again that China has a clear and consistent position on opposing any kind of official relations between the United States and Taiwan. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, cut all official and military ties with Taiwan, and refrain from walking further down the wrong and dangerous path. China will continue taking all necessary measures to uphold sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346965.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210113_5419734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-13","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","The U.S. government reportedly declassified 30 years earlier than normal an Indo-Pacific strategy, which contains elements including defending Taiwan, accelerating India's rise as a counterbalance to China and maintain U.S. dominance in the region. Do you have any comment?","Some U.S. politicians want to leave behind a \"legacy\" by declassifying the document, but its content only serves to expose the malign intention of the United States to use its Indo-Pacific strategy to suppress and contain China and undermine regional peace and stability. In essence, this is a strategy of hegemony. I can point out at least three major mistakes in it.\nFirst, it highlights the Cold War mentality and military confrontation, which goes against the mutually-beneficial spirit of regional cooperation, runs counter to regional people's aspiration for peace, stability and development, and threatens regional prospects of peace and development. As such, it should rightly be thrown into the dustbin of history. The U.S. side is obsessed with ganging up, forming small cliques and resorting to despicable means such as wedge-driving, which fully exposed its true face as a trouble-maker undermining regional peace, stability, solidarity and cooperation. We believe countries in the region are clear-headed and vigilant enough not to be hijacked onto the U.S. chariot or be used as a tool to maintain U.S. hegemony.\nSecond, it is a serious breach of the U.S. government's solemn commitment on Taiwan to China. There is but one China in the world, and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. China has the determination, confidence and capability to foil any foreign interference and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist plots. We will resolutely defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. All U.S. attempts to contain China with Taiwan are futile. We urge the United States to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, strictly observe the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related matters, not to send wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and not to go further down the dangerous and wrong path to avoid seriously undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-U.S. relations.\nThird, it maliciously distorts China's neighborhood diplomacy and hypes up the so-called \"China threat\". However, lies will always be lies and justice will prevail. China is committed to the path of peaceful development and a defense policy that is defensive in nature. We are a builder of world peace, contributor to global development and guardian of international order. As a responsible member of the Asia-Pacific, China actively practices a neighborhood diplomacy of amity, sincerity, mutual benefit and inclusiveness, making important contributions to regional peace, stability and prosperity. Regional countries all bear witness to this.\nI must point out that the Asia-Pacific is a region where Chinese and American interests are most tightly entwined and interact most frequently. We hope the U.S. side will discard the Cold War zero sum mentality, earnestly respect China's core interests and major concerns, strengthen communication and dialogue with China, properly manage differences and help make the Asia-Pacific a stage for mutually-beneficial cooperation instead of an arena for major power rivalry.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346965.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210113_5419734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first introduced the establishment of four new cross-strait exchange bases and the situation of exchange activities carried out by previous bases, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Before we take your questions, I would like to brief you on our approval of new Cross-Strait Exchange Bases.\nAs you know, exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait in all fields are an important driving force for the development of cross-Strait relations. Since 2009, the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office have approved the establishment of 79 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 24 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian. These exchange bases have given compatriots on both sides more opportunities to exchange and cooperate, to look back on history, appreciate culture, share kinship, and develop together. Since the epidemic last year, these exchange bases have also become important platforms for \"cloud exchanges\" across the Strait. For example, from February to March last year, the Fujian Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple and relevant Mazu temples and organizations in Taiwan jointly held the event \"Heaven Protects China, Praying for Wuhan — Cross-Strait Mazu Temples Join Hands in Online Prayer Against the Epidemic.\" More than 120 Mazu temples and over 3,000 believers in Taiwan took part on site, and 200,000 people watched the online live broadcast. The Xiamen Haicang Qingjiao Cishan Temple and relevant Baosheng Dadi temples in Taiwan jointly held the 13th Cross-Strait (Xiamen Haicang) Baosheng Cishan Culture Festival, themed \"Promoting Baosheng Cishan, the Whole Nation United Against the Epidemic,\" and short films were simultaneously broadcast to millions of people on both sides. Also, starting last October, the Zhang Family Marshal's Mansion Museum in Liaoning and the Former Residence of Zhang Xueliang in Taiwan have cooperated to hold a live linked broadcast once a month, enabling audiences in Shenyang and Hsinchu to \"visit\" and \"gather\" online, which strengthens shared historical memory and inspires new experiences and emotions.\nThe four newly approved Cross-Strait Exchange Bases are: Changting Tingzhou Hakka Capital in Longyan, Fujian, Anxi Qingshui Rock in Quanzhou, Fujian, the Grand Canal Cultural Belt in Huai'an, Jiangsu, and the Wenchang Ancestral Temple in Zitong, Mianyang, Sichuan. Each of these four exchange bases has its own distinctive character: some carry the shared historical and cultural memories of compatriots on both sides, some showcase the close kinship ties between them, and some are important venues for exchange and interaction among grassroots people on both sides.\nThe establishment of these exchange bases reflects our firm implementation of the policy toward Taiwan, our active expansion of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, our continued deepening of cross-Strait integration and development, and our ongoing efforts to promote heartfelt connection between compatriots on both sides. We welcome more and more Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange at these bases, and we hope relevant localities will build and develop these bases well so that they play a positive role in promoting cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nNow we begin the questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316801.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The newly revised Regulations on the Work of the Chinese Communist Party's United Front were recently issued. Its Taiwan-related section adds content such as “widely unite Taiwan compatriots at home and abroad, develop and strengthen Taiwan's patriotic unification forces, and oppose ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist activities.” Please have the spokesperson interpret this. In addition, the Mainland Affairs Council…","Many Taiwan compatriots may not be very familiar with the concept of the “united front.” The united front led by the Communist Party of China is, in essence, about gathering hearts and minds and pooling strength: uniting all forces that can be united, and mobilizing all positive factors that can be mobilized, to jointly strive for national prosperity, national rejuvenation, and the happiness of the people.\nThe main content and basic spirit of the united front work on Taiwan in the Regulations on United Front Work of the Communist Party of China are consistent before and after the revision. This reflects our consistent central policy on Taiwan. The important task of united front work on Taiwan in the new era is to widely unite Taiwan compatriots at home and abroad, jointly oppose separatist “Taiwan independence” activities, continuously advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and ultimately accomplish the great cause of reunification of the motherland. This is also the common wish of all Chinese people.\nThe DPP authorities have long been accustomed to smearing and slandering the mainland's united front work, attempting to incite opposition between people on both sides of the Strait. Such attempts will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316799.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Some public opinion holds that the deepening of cross-Strait integrated development is entering an accelerated period, and Taiwan businesses and enterprises should use their own advantages to participate deeply in the development of the mainland's new economy and promote the integrated development of cross-Strait industries. May I ask the spokesperson what new opportunities Taiwan businesses and enterprises have…","The economies on both sides of the Strait belong to the economy of the Chinese nation, and there is no reason why they should not join hands for development and common development. The Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, held in October 2020, drew up a magnificent blueprint for cross-Strait relations over the next five years and even fifteen years, which is a shared bright future and historic opportunity for compatriots on both sides. The signing of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement and the timely completion of the China-EU Comprehensive Agreement on Investment negotiations will also greatly enhance the level of trade and investment liberalization and facilitation between the mainland and relevant economies.\nThese major opportunities and long-term benefits will certainly promote the integrated development of cross-Strait industries and make the road to peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations broader and broader. We will further improve the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland; we will further expand the space for Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises to participate in the \"Belt and Road\" initiative and national regional development strategies; and we will further give play to the advantages and strengths of Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises in intelligent manufacturing, information technology, and the transformation of scientific and technological achievements, and to their unique role in strengthening the cross-Strait industrial and supply chain linkage.\nFor example, the industrial internet, as an important support for promoting technological progress and industrial upgrading, has attracted great attention from cross-Strait industry circles. At the end of last year, relevant cross-Strait enterprises and industry associations initiated the establishment of the Cross-Strait Industrial Internet Industry Promotion Alliance, which will play a positive role in promoting cooperation and achieving mutual benefit among relevant cross-Strait enterprises. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises should fully grasp the development trend and major opportunities on the mainland, actively adapt to the new stage and new requirements of mainland development, fully participate in and deeply integrate into the mainland's \"major cycle\" and \"dual cycle\" development pattern, and they will certainly obtain greater and better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316797.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The “Jinou Wuque — Theme Exhibition Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration” has been on display at the National Museum of China for more than two months. May I ask which part of the exhibition is most popular with visitors? We have also heard that this exhibition will be displayed online. When will the online exhibition hall open, approximately?","The theme exhibition “Golden Bowl Without Flaw — Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration” has attracted wide attention since its opening on October 25, 2020, and visitors have been very enthusiastic. The exhibition consists of six parts: “Treasure Island Taiwan,” “Nine Continents Share Grief,” “Resisting Wokou and Defending the Territory,” “Singing Long with a Sword,” “Swinging the Spear to Recover the Frontier,” and “Cross-Strait Dream Realized.” It objectively reproduces the course of Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland, and the irresistible trend of the times in the forward development of cross-Strait relations. The parts most followed by visitors are the fifth part, “Swinging the Spear to Recover the Frontier,” and the sixth part, “Cross-Strait Dream Realized.”\nMany visitors left messages in the exhibition's guestbook and online after viewing. A visitor signed as “Third-Grade Elementary Student” drew three small hearts and wrote a sentence: “I hope Taiwan returns home soon.” A visitor wrote a poem: “Once separated by a mere arm's length, now distant as sea and sky. Now we vie for every moment; may the cross-Strait dream be realized soon. Seventy-five years since restoration, let us together contribute to a lasting great cause. The mountains and rivers remain intact, and the bonds of kinship run deep.” Another visitor wrote: “Unification cannot wait forever. Our generation must see the day of unification and must not leave the problem to the next generation.” All the messages strongly expressed the urgent desire to see the motherland reunified as soon as possible.\nAt the request of the broad audience, the National Museum decided to extend the exhibition until the end of March this year. Meanwhile, to make it convenient for more people on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, to view the exhibition, the show will launch an online exhibition hall. Preparations are progressing smoothly, and it is expected to go online within this month.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316800.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","After the US announced the lifting of so-called “restrictions on official US-Taiwan interaction,” Taiwan's representative office staff in the US met with a US Assistant Secretary of State, and the US Ambassador to the Netherlands also met with Taiwan's representative office staff in the Netherlands. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Regarding the US claim of “lifting restrictions on official US-Taiwan exchanges,” we already stated our solemn position on January 11. The US government should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués; this is a commitment made by the US. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the US and the Taiwan region of China, and demand that the US immediately stop its erroneous practices. The DPP authorities, stubbornly “relying on the US to seek independence,” are going further and further down the wrong path and will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316798.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan's epidemic prevention hotels are in short supply. Some Taiwan businesspeople have reported being told that if they cannot book a hotel, they will not be able to board a flight back to Taiwan. This year, the road for Taiwan businesspeople to return to Taiwan for the Spring Festival is full of difficulties. What comment does the spokesperson have?","At our last press conference we already said that we will take into overall consideration epidemic prevention and control and the needs of Taiwan compatriots to return home, and make our utmost effort to provide positive assistance to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople returning home for the Spring Festival. We hope the Taiwan side will put itself in the shoes of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland and provide relevant conveniences for their return home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The Spring Festival is approaching. Affected by the epidemic, more Taiwan compatriots will spend the New Year on the mainland this year than in previous years. Do the local Taiwan Affairs Offices have specific arrangements to help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises during the spring travel rush and in responding to the epidemic over the holiday?","The Spring Festival is the most solemn traditional festival of the Chinese nation. For Chinese on both sides of the Strait, it is also a time for family reunions and welcoming the new spring. Affected by the epidemic, quite a few Taiwan compatriots will spend the Spring Festival on the mainland this year. On the eve of the Spring Festival, Taiwan Affairs Offices in all localities will, in accordance with epidemic prevention and control requirements, help local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises make arrangements and implement epidemic prevention measures. At the same time, local Taiwan Affairs Offices will also visit and extend greetings to local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in various forms, learn in depth about their specific needs, help solve their practical problems, and make every effort to ensure that Taiwan compatriots on the mainland have a peaceful and harmonious good year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316795.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Fujian Province recently published a list of 225 measures granting equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Fujian. Please introduce the relevant details. We note that the Mainland Affairs Council has claimed that “Taiwan compatriots may not hold party, government or military posts on the mainland,” and that “Taiwan investors should not overlook long-term risks due to the incentives…","\"Promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland\" is an important component of the 14th Five-Year Plan and the 2035 long-range objectives, one item of which is to support Fujian in exploring a new path toward integrated development across the Taiwan Strait. To thoroughly implement Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee, actively explore a new path toward integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, and accelerate the building of the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to land on the Mainland, the Taiwan Affairs, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the Fujian Provincial People's Government released to society on January 2 the first batch of 225 equal-treatment lists. This list covers four fields—economy, society, culture and education, and facilitation—and involves many aspects including cultural and creative tourism, land use needs, industry market access, medical and health care, food, clothing, housing and transportation, employment and entrepreneurship, and cultural and educational exchanges. This is an important measure by which Fujian continues to implement the central government's policies toward Taiwan and advances pioneering trial implementation, and it further facilitates Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in systematically understanding and grasping the policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots in Fujian.\nThis list shows that Fujian will continue to take the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and will provide more equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises in Fujian, jointly building the first home. This is a positive measure that benefits Taiwan compatriots and is a good thing welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities have arbitrarily obstructed Taiwan people's participation in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation; whether by reversing right and wrong and sensationalizing, or by threats and intimidation, they attempt to deprive Taiwan people of the opportunities and rights to pursue a better life. This is not popular and will not succeed, and it harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","On the 12th, a spokesperson for the US State Department announced that the department had cancelled all overseas travel this week, including the planned visit to Taiwan by US Ambassador to the United Nations Craft. What is your comment?","I have already stated our basic position: we firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The Taiwan authorities recently introduced a new version of the “passport,” which reduces the “China” lettering and enlarges the word “Taiwan.” Taiwan public opinion holds that it is now more recognizable, and that Taiwan is seen by more people internationally. What comments does the spokesperson have?","We have already stated our position on this matter. No petty schemes by the DPP authorities to pursue “independence” in the international arena will succeed, and none can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","We know that the US Congress was recently subjected to a violent assault. Tsai Ing-wen has remained silent on this, in stark contrast to her repeated “expressions of support” for protesters on the Hong Kong issue. What comment does the spokesperson have?","This fully exposes the essence of the DPP authorities: disregarding right and wrong, politically manipulating Hong Kong affairs, and disrupting and harming Hong Kong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","I would like to follow up: regarding the cancellation of the U.S. ambassador to the UN's visit to Taiwan, does the spokesperson believe this removes the possibility of further tension in cross-Strait relations?","Our position is very clear: under any circumstances, the US government should abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués; this is a commitment made by the US side. The DPP authorities should immediately stop “relying on the US to seek independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Regarding mainland Taiwan compatriots receiving COVID-19 vaccines: The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council claims that information such as the efficacy and protection level of the COVID-19 vaccines approved for marketing on the mainland has not yet been made public, and that Taiwan compatriots on the mainland should carefully consider the necessity of vaccination. What is your comment on this? In addition, some…","I emphasize once again that in the process of vaccine research, development and production, we have always placed vaccine safety and effectiveness first. In December 2020, the National Medical Products Administration formally granted conditional approval for the marketing application of the inactivated COVID-19 vaccine developed by China National Biotec Group's Beijing Institute of Biological Products. Existing data show that its protective efficacy meets the standards required by the WHO and the National Medical Products Administration. As of January 9, more than 9 million doses of COVID-19 vaccine had been administered in total. Vaccination is carried out entirely on the premise of voluntary application and informed consent, and Taiwan compatriots have the right to choose whether to be vaccinated.\nWhether relevant epidemic prevention policies and measures should change because of vaccination is a professional question. WHO experts have reminded that there is currently no evidence that vaccinated people no longer carry a risk of transmitting the virus, and vaccinated people also need to take the same prevention and control measures. Therefore, I want to remind everyone again: whether or not you have been vaccinated, everyone should take personal protective measures, such as wearing masks, washing hands frequently, ventilating rooms frequently, and keeping safe distances.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210113_12316796.htm"],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","A DPP spokesperson recently said that in 2020 Taiwan's exports to the mainland reached a record high, proving that “the mainland needs Taiwan,” rather than that Taiwan's dependence on the mainland has deepened. What is the spokesperson's comment?","In 2020, Taiwan's exports to the mainland, both in value and as a share of Taiwan's total exports, reached record highs in history. This is inseparable from the mainland being the first to bring the epidemic under control, the first to resume work and production, and the first major economy to turn global economic growth from negative to positive. This fully demonstrates two points. First, Taiwan's economy cannot do without the mainland, and the mainland's continued development and progress is a major opportunity for Taiwan's economic development and a major benefit for Taiwan compatriots. Second, cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation conforms to the interests of compatriots on both sides, and as it continues to expand and deepen, Taiwan compatriots will benefit more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","US “lean hog” pork (ractopamine-fed pork) has begun to be exported to Taiwan. Will Taiwan's lean hog products flow into the mainland market? Have relevant mainland authorities taken any measures to prevent such products from entering?","Regarding mainland regulations, as we introduced before, under the Food Safety Law and other provisions, the mainland does not permit the import of pork and beef and their products containing ractopamine. We will also continue to take effective measures to prevent non-compliant meat products from flowing in.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Reportedly, the DPP authorities' opening of imports of “ractopamine pork” not only failed to secure a so-called “bilateral trade agreement” with the United States, but the U.S. Department of Commerce also ruled to impose anti-dumping duties on Taiwan products such as tires. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Facts have already proven that the DPP authorities, relying on a foreign power and using the pretext of “economic and commercial affairs,” have developed relations with the United States. This will only further subject Taiwan to US manipulation and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots. Colluding with external forces and stubbornly pressing ahead while disregarding the interests, health, and safety of the people will only cause greater worry and indignation among the public, and ultimately the DPP will be abandoned by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报人民政协网记者","Recently there has been talk in mainland academic circles of “smart unification” of Taiwan. What are the spokesperson's views?","Recently, mainland academia has held many Taiwan-related seminars. Among them, on December 29, 2020, the National Taiwan Studies Association held the seminar “2020 Review and Prospects of Taiwan's Political Situation and Cross-Strait Relations” in Beijing, where more than 40 experts and scholars discussed and exchanged views on hot issues in cross-strait relations. We support relevant research institutions in holding Taiwan-related seminars in diverse forms with rich content, to offer suggestions for advancing Taiwan affairs work, promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and achieving the reunification of the motherland.\nWe adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” This is the best way to achieve national reunification, and it reflects our care, concern, and consideration for compatriots in Taiwan. We are willing to make the utmost sincere effort and do our best to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification of the two sides. At the same time, our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering. We will never allow anyone or any force to infringe upon or split the sacred territory of the country.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The mainland’s inactivated COVID-19 vaccine has been approved for conditional market launch, and the National Health Commission has stated that the vaccine will be provided free of charge to the entire population. May Taiwan compatriots on the mainland receive the COVID-19 vaccine free of charge? What is the current vaccination situation for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland?","Under a unified work arrangement, Xiamen City launched the COVID-19 vaccination program for key groups on December 14. The first phase vaccinated nine categories of people at higher risk of infection first, including medical and health workers and frontline customs inspection and quarantine personnel at ports handling imported cold-chain goods. The Xiamen Taiwan-Invested Enterprises Association and other organizations serving Taiwan compatriots in Xiamen registered and tallied Taiwan compatriots from these nine categories who voluntarily chose to get vaccinated and arranged their vaccinations. At present, COVID-19 vaccination work across various localities is proceeding in orderly phases, and appropriate arrangements will be made for eligible people, including mainland Taiwan compatriots.\nYou mentioned the question of cost. At present, some Taiwan compatriots in Guangxi, Xiamen, and other places who have been vaccinated do not have to pay personally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Newly elected US President Biden will take office on January 20. Hu Xijin, editor-in-chief of the Global Times, wrote on his personal Weibo that the period before January 20 is a rare window for mainland China to give “Taiwan independence” forces a “painful lesson.” Mainland netizens commented: “Is this the rhythm of ‘armed reunification’?” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our position is very clear: we firmly oppose any form of Taiwan-US collusion and will take resolute and forceful countermeasures. The DPP authorities acting as “pawns” of external forces and “relying on the US to seek independence” will only bring disaster to the people of the island.\nFinally, I would like to say a few words. In recent days, several cold waves have swept in, causing considerable inconvenience to compatriots on both sides. Taiwan's aquaculture operators are also facing very severe challenges. We extend our sympathies to them and hope they can get through these difficulties smoothly and soon. Next week, many students will sit for exams in severe cold. In particular, over a hundred thousand senior high school students in Taiwan will take the General Scholastic Ability Test. We hope they will keep warm, take good personal epidemic prevention measures, work hard, achieve good results, and get into their ideal schools.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210113_12316793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-14","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, the U.S. ambassador to the United Nations Kelly Craft had a video call with leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen on January 14 after a planned visit was canceled. After the call, Craft tweeted that \"Taiwan is unable to share those successes in UN venues, including the World Health Assembly, as a result of PRC obstruction\", referring to its success in fighting COVID-19. Do you have any…","China is firmly opposed to official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. Craft's words and deeds constitute grave interference in China's domestic affairs in serious violation of the one-China principle, the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and the political commitment made by the U.S. side on Taiwan. China is firmly opposed to them.\nThere is but one China in the world. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a fact recognized by the international community and a basic norm of international relations.\nThe United Nations consists of sovereign states. Taiwan's participation in the activities of international organizations including WHO must follow the one-China principle. This is an important principle affirmed by the UNGA Resolution 2758 and Resolution 25.1 of the World Health Assembly.\nThe Chinese Central Government always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, we have been updating the Taiwan region in a timely manner of the latest information. We've made proper arrangement for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region. So channels of information flow are unimpeded.\nThe U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop meddling in China's domestic affairs or undermining China-U.S. relations. We will continue to take all necessary measures to safeguard sovereignty and security interests. Certain U.S. politicians will pay a heavy price for their mistakes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202101/t20210114_693580.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210114_5419739.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-14","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","U.S. Under Secretary of State Keith Krach tweeted on January 13 that Secretary Pompeo orders lifting of self-imposed restrictions with Taiwan by US Govt giving it Free Country status\". Do you have any comment?","Krach's remarks are a grave breach of basic norms of international relations, the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and the political commitment made by the U.S. side on Taiwan. China rejects and condemns them.\nWe urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop the political manipulation of the Taiwan question, stop official exchange with Taiwan, and stop elevating relations with it in essence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202101/t20210114_693580.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210114_5419739.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 14 — In response to the video call between US Permanent Representative to the United Nations Craft and Tsai Ing-wen on January 14, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated that day in response to questions: We firmly oppose the Taiwan-US scheme to use official exchanges to challenge the one-China principle. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop all forms of collusion with the United States. “Relying on the US to seek independence” will only bring humiliation upon oneself and will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210114_12317573.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-18","Hua Chunying","Beijing Youth Daily","The United States also took measures on relaxing restrictions on U.S.-Taiwan relations. China said it would take all necessary measures to safeguard sovereignty and security interests and the United States would pay a heavy price for its erroneous behaviors. Is there any update on the measures that China is going to take?","In light of the U.S. erroneous behaviors, China has decided to impose sanctions on the U.S. officials who bear major responsibilities and acted egregiously with regard to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346968.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210118_5419749.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-18","Hua Chunying","Global Times","On January 14, the Permanent Mission of the United States to the United Nations released on its official website a video of remarks to students in Taiwan by the U.S. Ambassador to the UN Kelly Craft. Speaking from the UN General Assembly Hall, Craft said: \"It is here, and in other UN venues, where the United States makes clear its support for a role for Taiwan on the global stage.\" What is your comment?","Spokesperson of the Permanent Mission of China to the UN already made comments on the wrong words and deeds on the Taiwan Question by the US Permanent Representative to the UN. There is but one China in the world. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. As facts have proven and will continue to prove, attempting to challenge the one-China principle and separating China will not get the support from the vast majority of the UN membership and is doomed to fail.\nIt is worth noting that as verified by the United Nations, no meeting was held in the General Assembly Hall on January 14, and the UN Secretariat gave no approval to any country to hold any event in the Hall on the same day. Clearly, the video was made as Craft sneaked into the Hall and posed for the camera, abusing her right as the US Permanent Representative to the UN.\nIn China we say \"the things one person is capable of are beyond your wildest imagination\". This farce staged and acted out by Craft is equally preposterous and contemptible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346968.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210118_5419749.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-18","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Just a clarification. You talked about sanctions on U.S. officials with regard to Taiwan. Are they new sanctions? Has China imposed sanctions on American officials for Taiwan-related causes before?","In light of the U.S. erroneous behaviors, China has decided to impose sanctions on the U.S. officials who bear major responsibilities and acted egregiously with regard to Taiwan and Hong Kong.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346968.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210118_5419749.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-20","Hua Chunying","NHK","US Secretary of State nominee Antony Blinken said at the hearing that a tough stance should be taken on China's human rights issue and military development. What is your comment?","You mentioned some comments on China made by Secretary of State nominee Antony Blinken at a senate hearing. I'd like to make three points.\nFirst, China's domestic and foreign policies and strategic intent are open and transparent. China is committed to pursuing the path of peaceful development, upholding world peace, promoting global development, and safeguarding international order.\nSecond, China's positions on China-US relations and Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are consistent and clear. China is committed to developing a relationship with the United States featuring non-conflict, non-confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation. At the same time, China will firmly safeguard its own sovereignty, security and development interests. We firmly oppose the U.S. side using relevant issues to interfere in China's internal affairs, damage China's interests and tarnish China's image.\nThird, we hope that the U.S. side will adopt a right perspective in viewing China and China-U.S. relations, work with China to manage differences through cooperation and bring China-U.S. relations back to the right track. This serves the common interests of the two countries and is also the shared aspiration of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346970.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210120_5419759.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-21","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Was the Chinese ambassador invited to President Biden's inauguration ceremony? \"Taiwan's representative to the United States\" attended the ceremony. I wonder what's your comment?","The Chinese embassy has received invitation to attend President Biden's inauguration ceremony. The Chinese side has extended congratulations to President Biden.\nChina's position is very clear and consistent. We are firmly against official interactions between the United States and the Taiwan region. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, prudently and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan and avoid undermining bilateral relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346971.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210121_5419764.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-21","Hua Chunying","Reuters","That was a very positive summary of China-U.S. relationship, though it's impossible to ignore that on Biden's first day in office, his administration did several things that are potential warnings in the relationship. You've mentioned Taiwanese attendance at his inauguration as well as condemnation of the sanctions. Is there anything that the Chinese side is concerned about in the upcoming administration?","The importance of China-U.S. relations is self-evident. In the past few years, as you witnessed, some extremely anti-China and anti-Communist politicians of the Trump administration, represented by Pompeo, caused severe difficulties in China-U.S. relations by meddling in China's internal affairs and undermining China's sovereignty, security and development interests. It doesn't serve the interests and or meet the aspirations of Chinese and American people at all. In fact, many countries don't want to see that either. They hope China and the United States, the two largest economies and UNSC permanent members, can cooperate and contribute to world peace and development, which will be great news for many. I think this point is shared by all.\nChina's position on China-U.S. relations is consistent and clear. We have been stressing that China would like to strengthen dialogue and cooperation and properly manage differences following the spirit of non-conflict, non-confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation. China hopes the United States will meet us halfway. There's boundless potential in China-U.S. relations as long as we both demonstrate good faith and wisdom, truly hear what each other says, respect facts, and manage differences properly. That said, it is also our clear position that China will take firm reactions to all moves undermining our sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346971.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202101/t20210121_5419764.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: over the past few years, the DPP authorities have colluded with Pompeo and others and done many bad things on the Taiwan question, including official exchanges, military contacts, and arms sales to Taiwan. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in response to the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 21: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 21st in response to a question: We firmly support sanctions against relevant US personnel who have behaved egregiously on the Taiwan issue. The DPP authorities are frantically colluding with anti-China forces in the United States such as Pompeo to plot “independence” and provoke, willingly serving as pawns of anti-China forces and selling out the national interest. They will certainly face historical judgment and severe punishment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210121_12319944.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","(January 21, 2021)\nIt is reported that Hsiao Bi-khim, the so-called “representative to the U.S.” of Taiwan, attended Biden's inauguration ceremony. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the One-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question properly. No scheme or pretext of the DPP authorities can conceal the nature of its “Taiwan independence.” The DPP authorities, going down the road of “Taiwan independence” to the bitter end, will inevitably reap the bitter fruit they have sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210121_12326462.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 22 — Regarding the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council's baseless criticism of the mainland's sanctions on Pompeo and others, Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to questions on the 22nd, saying: The DPP authorities are colluding with Pompeo, undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council has shown no remorse and has spouted nonsense, which precisely proves that the DPP authorities still tie themselves to Pompeo and his kind.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that facts have long proven that, for the sake of narrow party interests, the DPP authorities have been determined to cling to anti-China politicians of the former US government. After \"betting on the wrong horse\" in the US presidential election, they have resorted to all kinds of tactics, attempting to consolidate the \"achievements\" of Taiwan-US collusion with Pompeo and his kind. They have even gone so far as to open imports of American pork containing ractopamine, damaging the life and health of Taiwan's people and provoking strong indignation among the Taiwan public.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the sanctions on Pompeo and others were entirely self-inflicted. The DPP authorities' alignment with them shows only that they are birds of a feather, and they will certainly face the judgment and severe punishment of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210123_12326952.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-01-25","Zhao Lijian","Macao Monthly","According to reports, the USS Theodore Roosevelt aircraft carrier entered the South China Sea via the Bashi Channel. U.S. reconnaissance aircraft and early warning aircraft also flew near the Taiwan region. What's your response?","It does no good to regional peace and stability for the United States to frequently send military vessels and aircraft to the South China Sea to show off muscles.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1848316.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1848292.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-01-25","Zhao Lijian","NHK","Firstly, the U.S. State Department issued a statement on January 23, urging China to stop pressuring Taiwan and to engage in meaningful dialogue with Taiwan. What is your comment? Secondly, Taiwan media reported that there were more than ten sorties of PLA military aircraft operating in the airspace near Taiwan on January 23 and 24. Taiwan experts said the PLA's move was ostensibly a military exercise, but above…","On your first question, China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. There is but one China in the world, and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. China is determined in safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and interference by external forces.\nThe root cause of the current tension and disturbance in cross-Straits relations lies in the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refusing to recognize the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle, strengthening contacts with external forces and making provocations in pursuit of \"Taiwan independence\". On the political basis of adhering to the 1992 Consensus and opposing \"Taiwan independence\", we stand ready to conduct dialogue and consultation with all political parties, groups and personages in the Taiwan region, so that we can resolve differences and build up consensus on political issues across the Strait and on issues related to promoting the peaceful reunification of China.\nWe urge the U.S. side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from sending any wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces so as to avoid damaging China-U.S. relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, I'll leave it to the Ministry of National Defense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1848316.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1848292.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 27, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first introduced the main situation of the 2021 Cross-Strait Work Conference, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Strait.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office’s regular press conference. Before taking questions, I would first like to brief you on the situation of this year’s Taiwan work conference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","From January 17 to 18, the 2021 Taiwan Work Conference was held in Beijing. Wang Yang, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, attended the conference and delivered a speech. The conference held that in 2020, all regions and departments thoroughly studied and implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on Taiwan work, coordinated Taiwan-related work amid epidemic prevention and control and economic and social development, effectively responded to complex situations, and consolidated the trend of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and promoting reunification, as well as the international community's one-China pattern.\nAt present and for a considerable period ahead, the situation across the Taiwan Strait remains complex and grave, and both the opportunities and challenges facing Taiwan work have undergone new changes. In line with the arrangements of this conference, we will, guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" resolutely curb \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and interference by external forces, support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in actively participating in the implementation of the \"14th Five-Year Plan\" and the national regional coordinated development strategy, support Fujian in exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development, continuously improve institutional arrangements and policy measures that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and realize equal treatment, unite compatriots on both sides of the Strait to actively promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification.\nNow, let us begin the question-and-answer session.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328122.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","We note that the “Jin Ou Wu Que — Theme Exhibition Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration” has gone online. Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation.","We previously introduced some aspects of the theme exhibition. The online exhibition hall of the “Jinou Wuque: Theme Exhibition Commemorating the 75th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration,” carefully prepared by the National Museum of China, went online on January 26 on the museum's official website. You can log in to the museum's official website homepage on your mobile phone or computer and visit it online.\nThe online exhibition hall makes full use of virtual reality, web-based 3D and other technologies, highly integrating digital media innovation and creativity. Through text, images, sound, video, 3D scenes and other forms of display, it forms several sections including online guided tours, mini exhibition features and interactive games, enriching the exhibition's display effects and enhancing the participation, interactivity, entertainment value and communicative reach of the online exhibition hall.\nTo give everyone a more intuitive understanding of the online exhibition hall, we specially asked the National Museum to provide a display screen so that we can demonstrate it on site:\nThis is the homepage of the online exhibition hall. Clicking in immediately shows the look of the exhibition hall, giving a strong sense of being there. We click into “3D Scenes” and look at the fifth section, “Raising the Spear to Restore the Territory,” which is the one most viewers care about and resonate with most. The exhibit is a writing brush. Clicking on it plays the explanation: “The writing brush once used by Chen Yi, the Chinese theater officer in charge of receiving Japanese surrender in Taiwan Province, at the surrender ceremony.” After viewing the exhibition, if you are interested or wish to bring children to visit, you can click “Exhibition Extension,” where you can take part in “Interactive Quiz,” and also look at “Visitor Messages,” “Selected Poetry” and more. We believe you will gain a great deal.\nWe welcome people on both sides of the Strait, especially the Taiwan public, to log in to the online exhibition hall of the National Museum of China to view the theme exhibition, look back at history together, and draw inspiration for the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328121.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","I have two questions. First, according to reports, the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Association has begun organizing Taiwanese businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots in Beijing to receive COVID-19 vaccines. Please introduce the current progress of vaccination for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. Second, in response to Taiwan compatriots on the mainland receiving vaccines one after another, the DPP authorities and…","At present, COVID-19 vaccination work across the mainland is being carried out in an orderly manner, and appropriate arrangements will be made for eligible people, including Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. Several Taiwan compatriots interviewed said they have confidence in mainland vaccines and are willing to get vaccinated as early as possible. Beijing began the COVID-19 vaccination of key groups on January 1, and has completed the first dose for more than 1.9 million people in key groups. For Taiwan-funded enterprise employees and Taiwan compatriots in Beijing who voluntarily get vaccinated and meet the requirements, vaccination arrangements are coordinated by the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office with the Beijing Taiwan-Funded Enterprises Association. It must be stressed that vaccination on the mainland is carried out entirely on the premise of voluntary application and informed consent. The claims by some politicians and media on the island of \"semi-coerced\" vaccination are pure malicious rumors.\n(On-site display) Everyone can take a look: vaccination requires signing a vaccination informed consent form, and every Taiwan compatriot who gets vaccinated fills out the informed consent form to express their personal wishes.\nSince the mainland officially launched COVID-19 vaccination of key groups on December 15 last year, as of January 20 this year, a cumulative total of 15 million vaccine doses have been administered. More than 40 countries have requested to import mainland COVID-19 vaccines, and some have already approved their use. All of this fully demonstrates the good safety of mainland COVID-19 vaccines. Vaccination work on the mainland is advancing in an orderly way, with vaccination provided free of charge to all, so that eligible people can all get vaccinated as soon as possible, gradually building an immunity barrier and cutting off the transmission of the novel coronavirus.\nThe facts speak louder than words. The DPP authorities and certain media on the island have slandered and smeared mainland vaccination, with despicable intentions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328084.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","We know that since last year, the Taiwan Affairs Office has guided relevant localities in holding multiple online promotion and matchmaking events for “Taiwan-funded enterprises expanding domestic sales.” Recently, the “Taiwan Enterprises Expanding Domestic Sales: Cross-Strait Together” Sichuan session was held in succession. What are the characteristics of this event? Looking ahead to 2021, what opportunities…","To help Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises cope with the epidemic and effectively expand sales in the Mainland's domestic market, since July 2020 the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Ministry of Commerce have guided relevant parties to hold four online promotion and matchmaking events for \"Taiwan-invested enterprises expanding domestic sales\" in Fujian, Shandong, Guangdong and Sichuan respectively. The most recent one was held in Chengdu, Sichuan on January 14, and nearly 300 cross-Strait enterprises participated in online one-on-one negotiations. This event also specially built a \"cloud exhibition hall\" to continuously promote the products of the relevant Taiwan-invested enterprises until the end of this month, providing more cooperation opportunities for cross-Strait enterprises.\nAt present, the Mainland has entered a new stage of development; its institutional advantages are remarkable, governance effectiveness has improved, the economy is on a long-term upward trend, its material foundation is solid, its human resources are abundant, its market space is broad, its development resilience is strong, and social stability is overall sound; continued development has many advantages and conditions. In 2020, the Mainland's gross domestic product exceeded 100 trillion yuan for the first time, growing 2.3% against the trend, and residents' income doubled compared with 2010. The Mainland has nearly 1.4 billion people, more than 400 million middle-income group members, more than 100 million market entities, and the world's most complete and largest-scale industrial system; domestic demand potential continues to be released and the vitality of the great circulation is increasingly strong. This provides very broad space and rare development opportunities for Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises to develop in the Mainland.\nWe will continue to implement in detail and in depth the various measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, help Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises share in the Mainland's development opportunities, and fully participate in and deeply integrate into the new development pattern of the \"great circulation\" and \"dual circulation.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328119.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Starting January 1 this year, Taiwan has officially opened imports of US pork containing ractopamine and US beef from cattle over 30 months of age. Some mainland netizens are worried that US pork and beef containing ractopamine, and related products, may flow into the mainland market through Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's response to this? What preventive measures has the mainland already taken?","We note that the recent concerns among some netizens are because some irresponsible online users on the island have put forward some malicious ideas.\nTo protect consumer health, the mainland has long prohibited the use of ractopamine in animal breeding and strictly bans the import of meat products containing ractopamine. Meanwhile, because Taiwan has highly pathogenic avian influenza and other epidemics, to prevent the risk of epidemic introduction, the mainland strictly prohibits the import of meat products produced in Taiwan or transshipped through Taiwan.\nTo prevent such meat products from flowing from Taiwan into the mainland market, relevant mainland authorities have recently stepped up inspections. Customs have already seized some meat and meat products, meat-containing foods, and meat-containing seasonings from parcels mailed to the mainland and from the luggage of travelers entering the mainland from Taiwan, such as pork floss and pork jerky. These have been handled in accordance with relevant regulations. If consumers find meat products from Taiwan on the market, they may report them to local regulatory authorities. We also ask the broad masses of consumers to purchase imported meat products through legitimate channels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328097.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","We note that the cluster infection epidemic at Taoyuan Hospital in Taiwan has continued to ferment, causing public panic. Against this background, the DPP authorities still engage in “political epidemic prevention.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have noted reports that this hospital cluster infection in Taiwan has caused public panic. What I want to say is that in the face of the epidemic, “political epidemic prevention” is of no help. Only by seeking truth from facts and, from a scientific and professional standpoint, sincerely safeguarding the health and well-being of the people of Taiwan is the solution. We also once again urge the DPP authorities not to treat the lives and health of the people of Taiwan as a child's game, and not to treat the people of Taiwan as tools for political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","We have seen reports that the Taiwan Constitution Foundation recently initiated the establishment of a so-called “Taiwan New Constitution United Front,” claiming to make “new constitution” a normalized and organized movement. May I ask the spokesperson for your comment?","A small handful of stubborn “Taiwan independence” diehards keep stirring up and manipulating the so-called “constitutional reform” issue, undermining cross-Strait relations, tearing Taiwan society apart, and harming the immediate interests of Taiwan compatriots. We hope all sectors of Taiwan society and the broad masses will stay vigilant and firmly oppose and resist this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328120.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The Green Party of Taiwan recently declared that it will push a so-called “constitutional amendment referendum” and demanded the deletion of the expression “national unification.” What is your comment?","A few diehard “Taiwan independence” elements, unrepentant, have repeatedly played the trick of “referendum for independence,” which is another form of “Taiwan independence” movement. We hope that all sectors of Taiwan society and the broad masses of the public can recognize the harm and will not tolerate or condone any such provocative acts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, a series of cross-Strait fishing boat rescue incidents have occurred. For example, on January 13, a Taiwan fishing boat rescued 22 crew members of a mainland cargo ship in distress, and on the 21st, relevant authorities in Fujian rescued 4 crew members of a Taiwan fishing boat in distress. Could you please introduce the relevant situation?","Two recent cases of cross-Strait fishing vessels rescuing each other have been reported by the media. We have looked into them in depth, and here we would like to share some details.\nIn the distress incident involving the mainland vessel “Yongfeng,” after the China Maritime Search and Rescue Center received a distress signal, it immediately activated its emergency response, notified the maritime search and rescue agencies of the Philippines and Japan as well as the Taiwan maritime search and rescue authority, and urgently coordinated passing vessels to proceed to the rescue. After receiving the signal, the Taiwan fishing vessel “Minfa Yu” abandoned its fishing operations and, overcoming its own difficulties of a small vessel, high waves, and harsh sea conditions, rushed to the scene with all its strength to rescue. At that time, the vessel was carrying supplies for five crew members, but it still generously provided food to the 22 crew members it rescued, and declined the remuneration and thank-you payment offered by the owner of the “Yongfeng.”\nIn the distress incident involving the Taiwan fishing vessel “Shunying,” after relevant parties in Pingtan, Fujian received the report, they immediately activated the joint emergency mechanism. Overcoming difficulties such as the failure of the distressed vessel's positioning system, they urgently contacted the Pingtan fishing vessel “Minping Yu 61618,” which was operating near the incident sea area, to take part in the rescue. The vessel was successfully rescued, and the four crew members were properly accommodated. The four crew members will return to Taiwan after their vessel is repaired.\nThese two emergency maritime rescues fully reflect the brotherly bond of mutual support between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. They are acts of great love that place the value of life above all, and they make this winter a little less cold.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently the U.S. State Department issued a statement on Taiwan-related issues. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment?","Taiwan is part of China. Adhering to the One-China Principle is the political foundation for the development of cross-strait relations. In the more than four years since the DPP authorities took office, they have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle, have interfered with and obstructed cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and have colluded with external forces to carry out “Taiwan independence” provocations. This is the root cause of the current complex and severe state of cross-strait relations.\nThe key to communication and dialogue between the two sides from 2008 to 2016, and to promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, was that both sides adhered to the “1992 Consensus” and opposed “Taiwan independence.” Only if the DPP authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and stop their “Taiwan independence” provocations can cross-strait relations improve and develop, and can there be peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. There is no other way.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests and the national feelings of the Chinese people, and it is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-U.S. relations. We hope the U.S. government will abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question prudently and properly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328082.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报、人民政协网记者","Looking back over the past few months, during the U.S. presidential election, the DPP authorities tolerated green-camp politicians and media in Taiwan openly making pro-Trump remarks and smearing Biden. They condoned pro-Trump forces in Taiwan buying billboards on Florida highways labeled “Taiwanese support Trump,” and some even took part in the violent storming of the U.S. Congress on January 6. What is the…","You have just listed the various acts by which the DPP authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests, cling to the anti-China forces within the former US government. That is indeed the case.\nOver the past period, the DPP authorities have colluded with anti-China forces such as Pompeo, going to every extreme to “rely on the US to seek independence.” Their methods are despicable and have earned universal scorn. Still unwilling to accept that they “bet on the wrong horse” in the US presidential election, they have resorted to various schemes, attempting to entrench the Taiwan-US collusion “achievements” they forged with Pompeo's clique. They have even gone so far as to harm the life, health, and well-being of Taiwan residents by opening imports of US pork containing ractopamine. These retrograde actions have already aroused strong dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents.\nThe DPP authorities' alignment with Pompeo and his ilk only shows that they are birds of a feather. They will surely be subject to historical judgment and severe punishment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210127_12328083.htm"],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","In response to Taiwan residents’ questions that the cost of self-paid COVID-19 testing on the island is 19 times higher than on the mainland, Chen Shih-chung, head of Taiwan’s epidemic prevention department, said, “This is because Taiwan’s testing is more accurate, while the mainland’s batch testing is less accurate.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","I think everyone does not believe this claim. Someone has even used this reasoning to justify the high nucleic acid testing fees in Taiwan, which is utterly absurd and laughable. Either he is genuinely ignorant of the professional matter, or he is deliberately confusing concepts in an attempt to muddle and deceive the Taiwan public.\nCOVID-19 nucleic acid testing is divided into dedicated testing targeted at individuals and dilution-pooled testing suited to large-scale population samples—that is, “single testing” and “pooled testing.” These two testing techniques and methods, each with its own purpose, are widely used on the mainland, and both have high accuracy. The role of “pooled testing” is screening, and its results are not used as the basis for the final diagnosis of any individual. On the mainland, large-scale “pooled testing” generally does not require personal payment. As for “single testing,” anyone on the mainland can make an appointment for nucleic acid testing at any time according to personal needs—“test whoever wishes to be tested,” which is very convenient. Everyone present has probably undergone both “single testing” and “pooled testing” because of work; I personally, because of my work, have also taken nucleic acid tests many times, including both “pooled” and “single” tests. As for the cost of “single testing,” I personally experienced 80 yuan in Beijing and also 120 yuan. By comparison, the nucleic acid testing cost in Taiwan is not just 19 times but more than 21 times. This is a pain point that has aroused resentment among the Taiwan public.\nI advise this gentleman to honestly explain to the Taiwan public the real reasons why nucleic acid testing in Taiwan costs so much. Playing clever tricks, deliberately swapping concepts, and even smearing the mainland in an attempt to hide the truth and deceive the Taiwan public will not work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Last week, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced sanctions against 28 U.S. officials including Pompeo. The Taiwan Affairs Office expressed support and mentioned that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and people like Pompeo are birds of a feather. My question is: when will the Taiwan Affairs Office announce sanctions against those “Taiwan independence” diehards who have behaved badly?","Resolutely cracking down on diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and stopping “Taiwan independence” separatist acts are the necessary meaning and essential conditions for safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We will closely monitor the moves of a small handful of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements at home and abroad, and will impose strict punishment and crackdown in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Mainland military aircraft have recently appeared frequently in Taiwan's southwestern Air Defense Identification Zone. The U.S. State Department has called on the mainland to stop exerting pressure on Taiwan and has expressed the hope of conducting meaningful dialogue with Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","As for the latter half of the question you just raised, I have already answered it. Let me explain the first half of the question to everyone.\nRegarding the PLA's live-fire drills in the Taiwan Strait, we have previously stated our position multiple times. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Since the Taiwan question arose from the civil war in the late 1940s, our will and determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity have been firm and have never changed. To effectively respond to interference by external forces and to a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their separatist acts, we do not commit to renouncing the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This will not change at any time.\nFor some time, the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces have continually changed tactics to engage in provocations seeking \"independence,\" attempting to split the country, undermine cross-Strait relations and peaceful development, seriously harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe PLA's organization of combat-oriented drills in the Taiwan Strait area is precisely to resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, to sternly warn external forces to stop interfering, and to sternly warn \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to stop provoking. Only in this way can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area be maintained, the common interests of compatriots on both sides be safeguarded, and the prospect of peaceful reunification of both sides be preserved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The DPP authorities previously sent letters requiring public agencies at all levels to replace mainland-brand communication products by the end of this year. Recently, a school in Taiwan investigated the mobile phone brands used by teachers. What is your comment?","The reason Taiwan consumers like smartphones from mainland brands is that mainland phones have advanced performance, superior quality and high cost-effectiveness. In fact, mainland phones enjoy a good reputation not only on the island but around the world. The DPP authorities have contracted a “fear-of-the-mainland disease” and are carrying out “green terror,” seeing enemies everywhere. Now they even manage which phones the public uses, which is truly baffling.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","As the Spring Festival approaches, reports say that only some 20,000-plus Taiwan compatriots are expected to return to Taiwan from the mainland for the New Year this year, less than one-third of the usual figure. For Taiwan compatriots spending the New Year on the mainland, what preparations have TAO offices in various localities made for them?","Today is the 15th day of the twelfth lunar month, and in less than half a month it will be the Spring Festival of the Year of the Ox. Family reunion is the shared wish of all Chinese. Many Taiwan compatriots in the mainland have not been able to return home and reunite with their families for a long time because of the COVID-19 epidemic, and they are longing for home. We understand their feelings deeply, and we are willing to make every effort to provide convenience and necessary assistance for their return home.\nFor Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople who remain in the mainland for the New Year, we and the Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities will provide service work, such as visiting Taiwan-funded enterprises, comforting Taiwan compatriots in difficulty, and distributing warm mobile packages and New Year gift packs, to help them spend a joyful and peaceful Spring Festival holiday in the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Many Taiwan residents are concerned: Is it possible for the mainland to donate vaccines to Taiwan through civil organizations such as the Red Cross?","As the mainland’s COVID-19 vaccines accelerate production and begin large-scale vaccination, in the recent period we have indeed received many reports from Taiwan compatriots hoping to be able to receive mainland vaccines in Taiwan. However, as everyone knows, the head of Taiwan’s epidemic prevention authority has repeatedly stated, “we will not use mainland vaccines.” So on this issue there are indeed obstacles, mainly political obstacles.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","First question: Last year, Taiwanese investment in the mainland grew by 41.5% year on year. Some Taiwanese media say this shows that Taiwanese businesses remain optimistic about the mainland market despite the pandemic and China-U.S. trade frictions. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: According to statistics from the Taiwan side, cross-border marriage registrations in Taiwan in 2020 decreased by…","On the first question: in fact, in 2020 not only did Taiwan businesses’ investment in the mainland reach a new high, but cross-Strait trade also reached a historic high. The facts fully prove that the mainland has a market and Taiwan businesses have opportunities. Taiwan’s economic development cannot do without the mainland. The development opportunities on the mainland, and the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland, have powerfully promoted economic development on the island and enhanced the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The development of the motherland’s mainland is a major benefit for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Only when compatriots on both sides strengthen cooperation can Taiwan’s economy have a better outlook and Taiwan compatriots gain more benefits and advantages. Strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation is an irresistible trend. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “decouple” the cross-Strait economies has no way out and does not win popular support.\nOn the second question: in recent years, the number of new marriage registrations for cross-Strait couples forming families has been roughly six to seven thousand pairs per year. Cross-Strait marriages and families are a fine achievement of integrated cross-Strait development and a vivid expression of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family.” We extend our heartfelt best wishes to them.\nYou mentioned the sharp drop in new cross-Strait marriage registrations in Taiwan last year. This is clearly abnormal. The causes include the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, and even more the artificial obstruction by the DPP authorities. Since the outbreak of the epidemic, the DPP authorities have used epidemic prevention and control to engage in extensive political manipulation. Starting in February last year, they unilaterally announced a ban on mainland residents traveling to Taiwan and substantially cancelled cross-Strait direct flight routes, seriously disrupting normal personnel exchanges across the Strait. This has prevented many cross-Strait couples from registering their marriages in Taiwan, and has also kept many cross-Strait married couples and their children from reuniting normally in Taiwan. Cross-Strait married persons on the island have repeatedly appealed and protested to the relevant Taiwan authorities, demanding that unreasonable policies be changed. We hope the DPP authorities will heed mainstream public opinion on both sides, allow people on both sides of the Strait to exchange and travel normally, and refrain from doing things that are inhumane and undermine the happiness of cross-Strait marriages and families.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Chen Shih-chung, head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention authority, responded to whether Taiwan would use mainland vaccines by saying, “It is not a question of whether to use mainland vaccines, but that regulations do not allow it, because their manufacturing process has not been verified.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","I once again emphasize that on the mainland, relevant institutions and enterprises have always placed the safety and effectiveness of vaccines first in the research, development and production process. The inactivated COVID-19 vaccine produced by China National Pharmaceutical Group’s China National Biotec Group has been formally approved by the National Medical Products Administration for conditional marketing, and its protective efficacy meets the relevant standards required by the World Health Organization and the National Medical Products Administration. As a global public good, mainland vaccines have also been used in many countries around the world.\nSome people in Taiwan who refuse mainland vaccines always invent various excuses and lies, merely harming the lives and health of the people of Taiwan for their own political self-interest.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","We note that Taiwanese media personality Huang Chih-hsien recently shared the entire process of his vaccination on the mainland, but this move was met with sarcasm and ridicule from some people on the island. What is your comment?","My earlier answer was already very clear. First, mainland vaccines are very safe. Second, many Taiwan compatriots have said in interviews that they have confidence in mainland vaccines and are willing to be vaccinated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Taiwan recently adopted relevant regulations guaranteeing the legal validity of same-sex marriages for Taiwan residents and foreign nationals. However, same-sex partners across the Strait still cannot marry. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The mainland practices freedom of marriage, monogamy, and gender equality in its marriage system. I suggest you carefully read through the content on marriage and family in Book Five of the “Civil Code.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-01-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","PLA military aircraft are conducting intensive live-combat training in the Taiwan Strait. Although this warns the “Taiwan independence” forces, would it also raise tensions in the Taiwan Strait? Could accidental conflict occur?","This depends on the extent to which the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" forces engage in provocations to pursue independence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202101/t20210127_12328077.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-01-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Taiwan's Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities recently stated that they would deepen ties between the US and Taiwan. At the same time, Taiwan's defense agency keeps mentioning the so-called entry of mainland military aircraft into Taiwan's “southwest air defense identification zone”. What's your comment, please?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which allows no foreign interference. The military activities carried out by the PLA in the Taiwan Strait are necessary actions in response to the current security situation across the Taiwan Strait and the need to maintain national sovereignty and security. It is also a solemn response to the interference of external forces and the provocations by the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.\nThe rejuvenation and reunification of the Chinese nation is an unstoppable trend. It is where the greater national interest lies, and what the people desire. In the long history of the Chinese nation, the actions taken by a small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists for “independence” are just like a bubble, which will not make any wave. We seriously warn those \"Taiwan independence\" forces that those who play with fire will set themselves on fire. \"Taiwan independence\" means war. The PLA will take all necessary measures to resolutely defeat any attempt by the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2021-02/01/content_4878336.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2021-01-29","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Bloomberg has just reported that the Biden administration is planning to have a meeting next week with Taiwan authorities and industry officials including the Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co (TSMC) and they're expected to talk about resolving a crunch in auto-chips, chips for automakers. Does China have any comment on this meeting?","I'm not aware of the meeting you mentioned. China's position on the Taiwan question has been consistent and clear. We firmly oppose any official ties between the United States and the Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202101/t20210129_693602.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1849552.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-01-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 29: In response to the so-called “representative to the United States” of the DPP authorities, who on social media insinuated that the mainland is “bullying the weak” toward Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 29th in response to a question: Taiwan is part of China. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. The DPP authorities, with the aim of seeking “independence,” have consistently taken things out of context and deliberately distorted them, and continue to confront the mainland. In the end, they will only reap what they sow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202101/t20210129_12328808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-02-04","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan has opened a representative office in Guyana. Do you have any comment on that?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community. We hope relevant party will abide by the one-China principle, refrain from any form of official exchanges and establishment of official institutions with Taiwan, take concrete actions to correct the error and eliminate the negative effects. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any attempt to solicit foreign support and engage in separatist activities in the international arena will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346981.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202102/t20210204_5419818.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-02-04","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The U.S. warship McCain transited the Taiwan Strait on February 4th, according to the US Navy, marking the first time since President Biden was inaugurated that this has happened. Does the foreign ministry have any comments?","China paid close attention to and monitored from start to end the passage of the US military vessel through the Taiwan Strait.\nChina will continue to stay on high alert and is ready to respond to all threats and provocations at any time, and will resolutely safeguard its national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope the US side will play a constructive role for regional peace and stability, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11346981.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202102/t20210204_5419818.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-02-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 4 (electronic dispatch): In response to Taiwan media reports that the DPP authorities have set up a so-called \"Taiwan Office\" in Guyana and described it as a \"diplomatic\" breakthrough, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang stated on the 4th in response to questions: We firmly oppose Taiwan region of China developing any form of official relations with countries that have diplomatic ties with China, or establishing any official institutions. We require Guyana to abide by the one-China principle and properly handle matters relating to Taiwan. The DPP authorities' various tricks cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210204_12330177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-02-05","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","According to media reports, the government of Guyana issued a statement on February 4, local time, saying that it will continue to follow the one-China principle and maintain committed to diplomatic ties with the People's Republic of China. The government of Guyana has not established any \"diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan and has terminated the agreement for Taiwan to set up an office in Guyana. What is China's…","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. China firmly opposes any official exchanges in any form between Taiwan and a country having diplomatic relations with China. Correctly adhering to the one-China principle, the Guyanese government announced the termination of the relevant \"agreement\" for Taiwan to set up office in Guyana and reiterated it values developing friendly relations with China and will not establish so-called official relations with Taiwan. The timely correction of mistakes by the Guyanese side is conducive to the overall interests of bilateral relations. The authorities of Taiwan's Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) deliberately seek \"Taiwan independence\" and expand \"international space\" under the pretext of carrying out unofficial economic and cultural activities, in an attempt to hide the truth and deceive the world. Facts have once again proved that the one-China principle is a widely recognized norm for international relations and universal consensus of the international community. The Taiwan authorities' secessionist behavior and clumsy performance are unpopular, and their ugly face has been fully exposed, making themselves a laughing stock.\nRelevant US officials have made seriously wrong remarks in breach of the principle of international law and norms governing international relations, to which China is firmly opposed. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is purely China's internal affair and allows no interference by any external forces. We urge the US side to correct its mistakes, take concrete actions to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and act in a prudent manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202102/t20210206_693611.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202102/t20210205_5419823.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-02-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 5 — Regarding the announcement by the Government of Guyana that it has terminated the establishment of the so-called “Taiwan Office” hyped up by the DPP authorities, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 5th in response to questions: We have consistently opposed the Taiwan region of China developing official relations with countries that have diplomatic relations with China. The so-called “diplomatic breakthrough” trumpeted by the DPP authorities will only bring humiliation upon themselves and end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210205_12330398.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The Government of Guyana reiterated its adherence to the One-China Principle and announced the termination of the establishment of the so-called “Taiwan Office.” The DPP authorities, however, have not repented and instead slandered and attacked the mainland. What comment do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 5 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 5th in response to questions: Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a generally recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The relevant countries that uphold justice and the basic norms of international relations reflect the common consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities cling to the erroneous “Taiwan independence” position, are accustomed to reversing black and white and misleading public opinion, and their conduct is egregious in nature. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop any “independence” activities; otherwise, they will only face failure time after time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210205_12330402.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, February 9 — In response to the claim made by the leader of Taiwan's regional authorities in his Spring Festival remarks that the key to peace across the Taiwan Strait lies in the hands of the mainland, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 9th, saying that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are attempting to lean on foreign powers to bolster their own standing and to spread the “two-state theory,” seeking to deceive and anesthetize the island's public by distorting facts and confusing the public, and their true nature has once again been fully exposed.\nMa Xiaoguang said that from 2008 to 2016, before the DPP authorities took office, the two sides of the Strait, on the common political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence” and adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opened up a new situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and compatriots on both sides shared a peaceful and stable environment and the fruits of cooperative development. The current grave situation in cross-Strait relations is entirely the result of the DPP authorities' doing. They refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” previously reached by both sides, which embodies the one-China principle, obstruct and hinder cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, collude with external forces, and constantly plot “independence” and provoke, creating tension and confrontation across the Strait and seriously harming the immediate interests of compatriots on both sides.\nMa Xiaoguang said that if the DPP authorities have even the slightest sincerity, they should immediately abandon the “Taiwan independence” stance, stop their independence-seeking activities, and return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210209_12331519.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-02-18","Hua Chunying","AFP","The US announced it would be renewing its quad alliance with Australia, India and Japan. Do you have any comment on this? Secondly, the head of Taiwan's health department Chen Shih-chung said in a radio interview that a deal to acquire five million doses of the Pfizer-BioNTech vaccine failed at the last minute due to what he believed was political pressure. Do you have any comment?","On your first question, peace and development is the mainstream of our era. It is our hope that cooperation between relevant countries will be open, inclusive and win-win, benefit the world and regional peace and stability and act as a force for good, instead of being used to target any specific country. Only this will receive support.\nOn your second question, the central government of China always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. We are always ready to provide necessary assistance to their fight against the virus. The DPP authorities should stop using the pandemic as an excuse to serve their political manipulation and hyping purposes, and do something real to promote the health and well-being of the people in the Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202102/t20210218_9721147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202102/t20210218_9604765.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-02-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to Taiwan media reports, the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention department claimed that 5 million doses of COVID-19 vaccine originally planned to be purchased from the German company BNT could not be contracted because of mainland obstruction, and that he was criticized externally for a lack of transparency and was in a “position of having difficulty expressing himself.” What is your comment on this?…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 18 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 18th that the claim that mainland factors are obstructing the sale of the BNT-Pfizer vaccine to Taiwan is pure fabrication and baseless, and once again exposes the amoral, bottomless political nature of certain DPP politicians.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Shanghai Fosun Group signed with Germany's BNT company as early as March 2020, participating in BNT's vaccine development and holding exclusive agency rights in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. Under these circumstances, why did relevant Taiwan institutions bypass Shanghai Fosun Group to buy vaccines from BNT? Why did they deliberately conceal the fact that Shanghai Fosun Group took part in vaccine development? What are their unspeakable difficulties? What is the real reason the contract was not signed? They should explain this clearly to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan media have long reported that a Taiwan company sought to negotiate with Fosun Group for this vaccine in the second half of 2020, but was blocked by relevant Taiwan authorities. What hidden circumstances lie behind this? Relevant personnel of the DPP authorities know this very well. So-called “unspeakable difficulties” are in fact self-contradiction and an inability to make a coherent account, caused by their political manipulation of “opposing the mainland and resisting the mainland.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that to date, the Taiwan region has been unable to obtain COVID-19 vaccines in a timely manner, and the people who truly suffer are the broad masses who eagerly await vaccination at the earliest opportunity. The way out is clearly right there, yet DPP authority politicians are playing conspiracies at the cost of the people's welfare, a nature that is extremely egregious. On this issue, concealing the truth and turning black into white will not get them past the test. We advise the DPP authority politicians: slander and defamation cannot shirk responsibility; only by removing the demons in their hearts can the people's suffering be relieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210218_12332879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. The Spring Festival has just passed, and the Lantern Festival is coming soon. As the saying goes, “Until the fifteenth day has passed, it is still the New Year.” Here, on behalf of the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, I offer you belated New Year greetings and wish you a prosperous Year of the Ox, with good fortune and all your wishes fulfilled!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the situation of visits and condolences to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises across various localities during the Spring Festival, and the assistance given to help them implement epidemic prevention measures so they can spend the New Year on the mainland.","Affected by the COVID-19 epidemic, and especially by the epidemic prevention policies of the DPP authorities, significantly more Taiwan compatriots stayed on the mainland for the Spring Festival this year than in previous years. Before the Spring Festival, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council sent letters of greeting to the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and to Taiwan associations in various localities, extending sincere regards and festive wishes to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople. It also required local Taiwan Affairs Offices to actively help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople enjoy a joyful and peaceful Spring Festival holiday. Localities put into practice the concept of “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family,” conducting visits and condolence activities with rich content and diverse forms in communities, factories and schools. They delivered blessings, talked about family ties, listened to their voices, showed concern for their well-being, and coordinated the resolution of issues that Taiwan compatriots care about.\nLeading officials of more than ten provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Beijing, Tianjin, Guangdong, Fujian, Shandong, Anhui, Henan, Jiangxi, Sichuan and Chongqing, visited Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople, extended New Year greetings, learned about their production and living conditions, and encouraged them to seize opportunities for development on the mainland to achieve greater and better development. Guangdong Province organized nearly 200 visiting and condolence teams, which conducted condolence activities at nearly a hundred schools and colleges, about a thousand Taiwanese enterprises, and more than 10,000 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople, and also extended condolences online to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople abroad and in other parts of the mainland. Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office used 18 days to visit all 13 prefecture-level cities in the province, calling on 51 Taiwanese enterprises and extending condolences to 184 representatives of Taiwanese businesspeople and compatriots.\nDuring the Spring Festival, localities adapted to local conditions, highlighted distinctive features, and arranged a series of cultural activities that greatly enriched the material and cultural life of Taiwan compatriots. Guangzhou, Fuzhou, Changsha, Xiamen, Zhangzhou and other places delivered Spring Festival couplets and New Year gift packages to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople, and held activities full of New Year atmosphere, such as small fireside vigil banquets, New Year's Eve dinners, and cross-Strait live-link New Year greetings. Zhejiang Province arranged for calligraphers to visit universities to carry out the “Ink Welcomes Spring” activity with Taiwanese teachers and students, and arranged for Taiwan compatriots staying in Zhejiang to visit rural communities, urban commercial districts and characteristic streets to fully experience local Spring Festival customs. Tianjin, Wuhan, Foshan and other places held cross-Strait photography and micro-video competitions, and Jinan held the “Cross-Strait Family, Praying for Blessings and Welcoming Spring in Quanzhou” event. Guangdong, Hebei and other places also combined Spring Festival visits and condolences with stepped-up services for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises, carrying out special operations to comprehensively screen and coordinate Taiwan-related issues, and fully supporting the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises locally.\nTaiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople widely felt the care of family members and the warmth of kinship, and many said “a local place is also a hometown.” This Spring Festival was joyful and fulfilling, and unforgettable. This also fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same blood, are connected in spirit, and are united in emotion, which is precisely the internal driving force behind the continued advancement of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334029.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce the situation in 2021 of mainland universities recruiting Taiwan high school graduates based on “Xuece” (General Scholastic Ability Test) scores.","At the start of the new year, mainland China's recruitment of Taiwanese students by universities officially began. The Ministry of Education recently issued the 《Notice on Recruiting Taiwanese High School Graduates by Ordinary Institutions of Higher Education on the Mainland Based on Scores of the Taiwan Academic Ability Test in 2021》. Under the notice, 384 mainland universities with recruitment qualifications will publish their admission brochures in late February or early March, simultaneously on their official websites, on the Cross-Strait Admissions Service Center website, and on the Admissions Information Website for Mainland Higher Education Institutions Recruiting Students from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. Fudan University has recently published relevant admission information on its website. Any Taiwanese high school graduate who holds a Taiwan Residence Permit or Taiwan Compatriot Permit, or valid proof of identity residing in Taiwan, and who achieves at least the “均标级” (uniform standard level) in any one of the Chinese, mathematics or English subjects of the 2021 “学测” (Scholastic Ability Test) is eligible to apply. We ask Taiwanese students to pay close attention to the above websites and promptly obtain the information needed to apply to mainland universities.\nTo avoid, as far as possible, affecting Taiwanese students because of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control factors, mainland universities will, while ensuring the health and safety of candidates, arrange online and offline examinations reasonably, to ensure that the admissions work proceeds steadily.\nApart from applying to mainland universities based on “学测” scores, Taiwanese students who choose to apply to mainland universities through the mainland college entrance examination, the examinations for applicants from Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and overseas Chinese, and university independent admission examinations will see no change in these arrangements.\nIn recent years, the quality of education and the level of internationalization of mainland universities have continued to rise, and the prospects for economic and social development on the mainland remain bright, bringing rare development opportunities to Taiwanese students. Although cross-Strait relations currently face some obstacles, no matter how the situation across the Taiwan Strait changes, relevant parties on the mainland will, as always, provide convenience and services for Taiwanese students who come to the mainland to study and pursue advanced degrees. We sincerely hope that Taiwanese students will overcome difficulties, strengthen their confidence, seize opportunities, and win the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334024.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to reports, Taiwan's legislature will launch a so-called “constitutional amendment project.” The DPP caucus said that if sensitive issues are involved, the DPP will not take “extreme positions.” What response does the spokesperson have?","We are highly attentive to relevant developments and firmly oppose any “constitutional amendment to seek independence” by Taiwan, including any move that opens the door to seeking “independence.” This position is consistent and clear.\n“Taiwan independence” separatist activities seriously undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and seriously harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We will take all necessary measures to firmly counter them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334026.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Some Taiwan compatriots are worried that applying for residence permits on the mainland may lead to double taxation. Will the spokesperson say whether such a situation will occur?","I can answer you definitively: No.\nWhen the Taiwan Residence Permit was introduced, we also addressed this issue. Here, I would like to state again to the public: The Taiwan Residence Permit is an identity document that helps Taiwan compatriots study, work, and live more conveniently on the mainland and enjoy equal treatment. The tax status and obligations of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are determined by mainland tax authorities in accordance with laws and regulations such as the “Individual Income Tax Law” and its “Implementing Regulations,” and have nothing to do with whether one holds a residence permit. Taiwan compatriots will not change their tax residency status or tax obligations on the mainland merely by applying for a residence permit, nor will they bear worldwide tax obligations on the mainland merely by receiving a residence permit. This must be clarified.\nIt also needs to be explained that on August 25, 2015, ARATS and the SEF signed the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Avoidance of Double Taxation and Strengthening of Tax Cooperation,” aimed at reducing the tax burden on enterprises and individuals in cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges. Regrettably, due to obstruction by the DPP, this agreement has not taken effect to date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334022.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Please introduce what explorations the Fujian Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone has undertaken to promote cross-Strait integrated development, and what results it has achieved.","The Fujian Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone is earnestly implementing the important speech General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the \"Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan\" and during the deliberations of the Fujian delegation at the 2019 National \"Two Sessions.\" It is striving to explore new paths for cross-Strait integrated development and to fully build Pingtan into the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises that come to the mainland.\nFirst, it is thoroughly implementing equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Adhering to the spirit of \"serving Taiwan compatriots as we serve mainland residents,\" it continuously improves the public service system relating to Taiwan affairs and keeps refining \"full-chain\" service functions, both online and offline. It actively provides policy support and guarantees, focuses on pioneering and experimenting first, and has issued more than 50 policy measures in areas including industrial cooperation, finance and taxation, and social security, effectively strengthening Taiwan compatriots' sense of gain and belonging. It is vigorously building a number of innovation and entrepreneurship platforms for Taiwan youth, including the Taiwan Entrepreneurship Park, Taiwan Town, cultural and creative villages, and popular homestays. It was the first to issue \"financial credit certificates\" to Taiwan compatriots to resolve their financing difficulties. It has built offline service windows and set up \"Taiwan Compatriot and Taiwan Enterprise Service Centers,\" which integrate 164 administrative approval and public service items across 8 major categories, so that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises can \"enter one door and handle all matters.\" It has built an online service platform to make life and work more convenient for Taiwan compatriots in the experimental zone. To date, cumulative sea-direct passenger transport between Pingtan and Taiwan has exceeded 1 million passenger trips, nearly 1,300 Taiwan-funded enterprises have registered and settled in the zone, and the number of Taiwan compatriots residing there has increased 3.5 times compared with 2017.\nSecond, it is actively promoting the \"new four connections\" across the Taiwan Strait. In promoting the connection of economic and trade cooperation, it was the first to achieve full coverage of sea-direct cargo and passenger routes to northern, central and southern Taiwan. With the opening to traffic of the Beijing-Taipei high-speed railway's Fujian Pingtan section in October 2020, the corridor's role has become even more prominent. Cross-Strait trade in agricultural and fishery products, sea express delivery, cross-border e-commerce and other activities along the \"Pingtan–Taipei\" and \"Pingtan–Kaohsiung\" channels have maintained rapid growth of 40%–60% in recent years. In promoting the connection of infrastructure, it is participating in planning the \"Taiwan Strait Channel\" construction and exploring the operation of China-Europe and China-Central Asia international freight trains departing from Pingtan or connecting to Zhengzhou. In exploring the mutual recognition of industry standards, it was the first to build an equivalent certification and supervision system covering recognition of Taiwan's professional qualifications, enterprise qualifications, industry standards and commodity inspection, directly recognizing 95 Taiwan professional qualifications. More than 20 of the recognized skill items have been promoted across the province and were further replicated and promoted by the State Council as reform pilot experience. In promoting the connection of energy and resources, it is leveraging the port and shipping advantages of the experimental zone to actively explore new energy supply routes for Taiwan and to promote the establishment of a Strait shipping replenishment base.\nThird, it is striving to explore new paths for the integration of cross-Strait grassroots governance. It creatively carries out cross-Strait grassroots integration pilot work, promotes two-way grassroots exchanges between the two sides, introduces Taiwan community builders, actively participates in and helps advance rural industrial revitalization, innovates management models, and promotes the complementary integration of grassroots governance strengths on both sides of the Strait.\nFourth, it is deeply carrying out cross-Strait exchanges in distinctive culture. Drawing on the shared resources of the Lan-Taiwan two places, including prehistoric culture, coastal defense culture, clan surnames and ancestral ties, and folk customs, it holds various forms of exchange activities such as the Common Home Forum and the Cross-Strait Village Chief Exchange Meeting, to strengthen kinship between the compatriots on both sides. It carries out cross-Strait academic exchanges and joint research projects in archaeology to jointly trace the common roots of both sides, strengthen compatriots' identification with their shared roots, builds a cross-Strait Chinese studies center, and regularly holds Chinese cultural exchange and study activities, providing a high-level platform for the study, inheritance and dissemination of Chinese studies and for carrying forward and promoting traditional Chinese culture.\nLooking ahead, the Pingtan Experimental Zone Party Working Committee and Management Committee will further \"cultivate the experimental field and serve as the ferryman,\" playing their advantageous role in deepening cross-Strait integrated development and making special contributions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334021.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","It is my understanding that the Supreme People's Court recently issued rules allowing litigants in Taiwan to file cases online. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,3,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视记者","Recent Taiwan data show that Taiwan-funded investment in the Mainland grew 41.5% last year over the previous year, and some public opinion on the island says this shows the failure of the DPP authorities' “New Southbound Policy.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","2020 was an extraordinary year for the mainland's development. The sharp increase in Taiwan businesses' investment in the mainland had three main causes:\nFirst, despite adverse factors such as the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic, the mainland took the lead in controlling the epidemic, resuming work and production, and its economic growth was the first among major economies to turn from negative to positive. Full-year GDP surpassed 100 trillion yuan for the first time, with growth of 2.3%, and its share of global GDP rose to 17%. It became the only major economy in the world to achieve positive growth.\nSecond, against the backdrop of a global economic recession, we resolutely advanced cross-Strait economic cooperation, continuously implemented and refined the “31 measures” and the “26 measures,” provided equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, and created a better development environment. We introduced the “11 measures” to help Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland orderly resume work, production and full capacity, generally achieving stable operation and healthy development. Many Taiwan enterprises achieved substantial growth, some large enterprises continued to invest and add capital, and Taiwan enterprises listing on the mainland formed a wave.\nThird, the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China drew the development blueprint for the mainland for the next five and even fifteen years. The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) was formally signed, and the China-EU investment agreement negotiations were completed as scheduled. These major opportunities and long-term benefits have created broader space for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to develop on the mainland. They fully prove that Taiwan's economic development cannot be separated from the mainland, and that when compatriots on both sides strengthen cooperation, Taiwan's economy can have better prospects and Taiwan compatriots can benefit more.\nAs for the DPP authorities' so-called “New Southbound Policy,” it serves political purposes, violates economic laws, and will only cause damage to Taiwan's economy and to Taiwan enterprises and businesspeople.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334025.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Chiu Tai-san took office as Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council on the 23rd, and said cross-Strait exchanges are bound to resume, expressing the hope that cross-Strait relations can enjoy “spring is warm and flowers are in bloom” in the future. Some figures in the Green camp have also said they hope Chiu's taking office will open an opportunity for cross-Strait dialogue. What is the spokesperson's response?","Cross-Strait relations once saw spring warmth and blossoming flowers. Warmth in spring needs the east wind, and blossoms need rain and dew. The east wind and the rain and dew are the “1992 Consensus.” If the gentlemen in Taiwan hold such expectations and are willing to comply with the wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, they should return to the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Recently, the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention department has repeatedly slandered the mainland for interfering with Taiwan's purchase of vaccines. Domestic media have pointed out the underlying purposes: first, to stir up hostility toward the mainland among Taiwan residents; second, to pursue his personal political aims. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","We have made clear that in March 2020, Shanghai Fosun Group signed a contract with Germany's BioNTech, participating in BioNTech's vaccine development and holding exclusive agency rights in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan. Previously, when we answered written questions, we raised several doubts. Why did relevant Taiwan agencies bypass Shanghai Fosun Group to buy vaccines from BioNTech? Why were the facts of Shanghai Fosun Group's participation in vaccine development deliberately concealed? What was the real reason the contract was not signed? Some people in the DPP authorities still have not clearly responded to these questions, and they have not given the broad public on the island a responsible account.\nI reiterate that the claim that mainland factors are blocking the sale of BioNTech vaccines to Taiwan is pure fabrication. On the vaccine issue, some people in the DPP authorities are obsessed with political manipulation and are “staging” this drama. Their aim is nothing more than to cover up their own inability to obtain vaccines in time, and to direct the resentment of Taiwan people, who still have no vaccines available, toward the mainland. The DPP authorities' practice of bypassing agents to obtain vaccines in defiance of commercial rules is political manipulation that completely disregards the health and well-being of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding mainland vaccines, Chen Shih-chung said the technical data were incomplete, so they were not included in consideration. Later he said that if mainland vaccines are particularly good and trusted by Taiwan's people, there is no need to necessarily exclude them. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond to Chen Shih-chung's statements?","Relevant mainland institutions and enterprises, in the process of vaccine research, development, and production, have always put vaccine safety and efficacy first. Vaccines produced on the mainland, since being launched in December 2020, have achieved protective efficacy that meets the standards required by the WHO and the National Medical Products Administration. As of February 9, the mainland had reported a cumulative 40.52 million doses administered, with an adverse reaction rate no higher than that of influenza vaccines. As a global public good, mainland vaccines have been used in many countries around the world. To date, we have provided vaccine aid to 53 countries and are exporting vaccines to 27 countries. At the request of the World Health Organization, we have also provided 10 million doses of vaccine to the “COVID-19 Vaccine Implementation Plan” (COVAX). All of this fully demonstrates the good safety of mainland COVID-19 vaccines.\nFacts speak louder than words. Some people in the DPP authorities disregard the health and well-being of Taiwan’s people, and fabricate all kinds of absurd excuses to refuse mainland vaccines. This is entirely the product of political obsession.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210224_12334023.htm"],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, starting from February 22, the DPP authorities successively held multiple military exercises in the Bashi Channel, the eastern offshore waters, Dongsha Island in the South China Sea, Taiping Island, and other locations. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The reasons behind the grave and complex situation across the Taiwan Strait are well known. The DPP authorities refuse to repent and instead seek to intensify confrontation. This approach is neither wise nor a reflection of realistic self-assessment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Minister Wang Yi recently called on the US side to stop condoning “Taiwan independence.” Mainland Affairs Council Chairman Chiu Tai-san said he is not quite clear what the mainland's definition of “Taiwan independence” is and will look into it further. May the spokesperson please answer?","Over the past more than four years, the DPP authorities have unilaterally overturned the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, interfered with and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, colluded with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation, and created tension and confrontation in cross-Strait relations, seriously harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. Every instance of this is so numerous that it could not be recounted even with bamboo slips exhausted. Everyone can see this clearly. Can they really not see it?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Chiu Tai-san said that, regarding the future of cross-Strait relations, he hopes for spring warmth and blossoming. He also said that after the mainland added new annotations to the “1992 Consensus,” the Taiwan public has been unable to accept it. What is the spokesperson’s view?","As for spring blossoming, as I already pointed out, it is not enough merely to hope that spring will bloom. We must consider why there was spring blossoming in the past. Why was the situation of spring blossoming once destroyed by the DPP authorities, turning into autumn winds and desolation?\nOn the question of the “1992 Consensus,” I would like to explain the basic facts again here. In 1992, the Straits Exchange Foundation of the Mainland (ARATS) and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) reached a consensus through talks in Hong Kong and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, under which each side orally expressed that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” The SEF's formulation was: “In the process of both sides of the Strait jointly working to seek national unification, although both sides adhere to the one-China principle, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.” ARATS's formulation was: “Both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive to seek national unification. However, in cross-strait consultations on matters of a functional nature, the political meaning of one China is not involved.” In the consensus, both sides expressed their adherence to the one-China principle and their pursuit of national unification. The essence is “both sides of the Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national unification.”\nWe have said many times that whether one accepts the “1992 Consensus” concerns the fundamental nature of cross-strait relations and is the touchstone for testing the so-called “good faith” of the DPP authorities. As long as one acknowledges the historical fact of the “1992 Consensus” and endorses its core meaning, there will be no obstacles to contact and exchanges between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Recently, the “New Power Party” requested that the Taiwan Ministry of the Interior evaluate changing the so-called “national emblem,” and the proposal was passed with the support of all DPP people’s representatives. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Recently, the New Power Party and relevant political forces on the island have colluded and exploited each other, with provocative moves appearing frequently and farcical performances repeatedly staged. In pursuit of their own political gain, disregarding the well-being of the public, they have not hesitated to aggravate the division and confrontation in Taiwan society, and public opinion on the island has widely criticized them. We believe that all sectors of Taiwan society and the broad public will see through this clumsy performance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Many people on the island have expressed an open and welcoming attitude toward mainland vaccines. Is cooperation on vaccines across the Strait possible in the future? Will the mainland provide vaccines to the Taiwan region?","We attach great importance to and care deeply about the health rights and interests of Taiwan residents. As everyone can see, we have made many efforts in this regard.\nFirst, Taiwan compatriots who live, work, or study on the mainland may, like mainland residents, voluntarily receive mainland vaccines. In addition, we have provided 10 million doses of vaccine to the World Health Organization's “COVID-19 Vaccines Global Access” plan, and the scope of this plan includes the Taiwan region.\nSecond, our overseas embassies and consulates are also assisting Chinese citizens abroad, including overseas Taiwan compatriots, in getting vaccinated locally. It can be said that our efforts and care are comprehensive. At present, whether mainland vaccines can be used on the island of Taiwan is not an obstacle or bottleneck on the mainland's side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Li Du-jong, professor in the Department of Chemical Engineering at National Taiwan University, was found by Taiwan's education authorities to have violated relevant regulations and was fined for leading related mainland research projects. The Mainland Affairs Council said it will continue to work with relevant agencies to investigate similar situations. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Strengthening cross-Strait science and technology exchange and cooperation is conducive to mutual benefit and win-win outcomes for both sides, and this has long been a consensus in cross-Strait science and technology circles. For political purposes, the DPP authorities restrict such exchange at every turn and even use legal means to punish Taiwan science researchers who participate in cross-Strait science and technology exchange projects. Professor Li's penalty this time is yet another manifestation of the DPP authorities' “excessive politicization” operations. The DPP authorities have escalated their interference with and sabotage of normal exchange and cooperation in cross-Strait science and technology circles, which will only make more and more Taiwan science and technology personnel feel disheartened.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The spokesperson just mentioned that whether cross-Strait relations can flourish depends on the “1992 Consensus,” and that the obstacle does not lie on the mainland side. However, Chiu Tai-san has added new annotations to the mainland's position on the “1992 Consensus.” It is understood that Chiu Tai-san is referring to the Taiwan plan of “one country, two systems,” and that compared with the mainland's one-China…","The gentleman you mentioned deliberately conflates the “1992 Consensus” with “One Country, Two Systems.” He is not unaware of this; he deliberately distorts and confuses the two and maliciously grafts them together. As everyone knows, “One Country, Two Systems” is a scientific concept proposed by the mainland for resolving the Taiwan question. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations at present. Splicing these two together and conflating them is a new trick by the DPP authorities to negate the “1992 Consensus” and negate the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Chiu Tai-san said in an interview that in the future he will strive to restart dialogue in cross-Strait relations, which have been frozen for a long time. May I ask the spokesperson: if relations do not return to the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” will Mr. Chiu's wish have no chance of being realized?","Since a so-called “wish” has been raised, you should know where the path and conditions for fulfilling it lie. The causes of the current complex and grave situation in cross-Strait relations and the tense, confrontational state are well known. Only the one who tied the bell can untie it. Those who look forward to spring must adopt the pragmatic attitude and practical actions of sowing the seeds of spring.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-02-24","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","民进党当局认为，邱太三等人事安排是对大陆方面释出的善意。岛内舆论也认为邱立场态度比较温和。请问大陆如何看待？另外，有关两岸疫苗合作，台前“卫生署长”杨志良说，两岸曾签署《两岸医药卫生合作协议》。请问发言人，这个协议现在是否还有效？如果台打算使用大陆疫苗，是否可以通过这份协议进口？","On the first question: We have no comment on the personnel changes within Taiwan. We believe the key is to look at policies and actions. As the saying goes, changing the soup is not as good as changing the medicine. If it is merely changing the soup without changing the medicine, this illness probably still cannot be cured. The key is what kind of cross-Strait policy the DPP authorities will put forward, and whether it can return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.”\nOn the second question: The Cross-Strait Medical and Health Cooperation Agreement is still being implemented. As I mentioned just now, the crux of the problem regarding the use of mainland vaccines lies in the DPP authorities' political manipulation. If they can get rid of the political obsession of “opposing and resisting the mainland,” there will be no problem for the people on the island of Taiwan to use mainland vaccines.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202102/t20210224_12334012.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-02-26","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","On February 25, the UN Human Rights Council held an Interactive Dialogue on the country-specific resolution on Sri Lanka by the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights. Some western countries used this Dialogue to criticize Sri Lanka's human rights situation, demand Sri Lanka carry out thorough investigation in to human rights violations during its period of internal conflicts and pursue accountability, and ask the…","As a friendly neighbor, China sincerely hopes that Sri Lanka will maintain political stability, national solidarity and unity, and that it will make greater achievements in national development. China commends the efforts taken by the Sri Lankan government to promote and protect human rights, advance sustainable socioeconomic development, improve people's livelihood, guarantee the rights of vulnerable groups, and continue to promote national reconciliation and combat terrorism.\nChina consistently opposes politicizing and applying double standard on human rights and using so-called human rights issues to interfere in other countries' internal affairs. All countries should adhere to the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, respect other countries' sovereignty, political independence and efforts to promote and protect human rights, and reject moves that interfere in others' internal affairs and exert political pressure. All countries should address differences in the human rights sector through constructive dialogue and cooperation, thus jointly promoting the sound development of the international human rights cause.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1857036.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1857003.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-02-26","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 26: In response to the General Administration of Customs’ notice published on its website on the 26th suspending imports of pineapples from Taiwan, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in reply to inquiries: Since 2020, mainland customs have on several occasions intercepted quarantine pests in pineapples shipped from Taiwan into the mainland. Once introduced, these pests would seriously threaten mainland agricultural production and ecological security. To prevent plant pest risks at the source, the General Administration of Customs decided to suspend imports of pineapples from Taiwan into the mainland starting March 1, 2021. This is a normal biosecurity measure, scientific and reasonable, and in line with relevant mainland laws, regulations and standards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202102/t20210226_12334538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-01","Wang Wenbin","NHK","First question, now one month has passed since the \"military coup\" took place in Myanmar. Several people have been shot to death recently by the Myanmar military. Myanmar's military stressed that they've been treating the protests cautiously. What's the comment of the Chinese side? The second question is that the EU floated the idea of holding talks that would include all of the remaining participants in the…","On your first question, as a friendly neighbor of Myanmar, China is following the current situation in Myanmar and hopes that each party will bear in mind the big picture of national development and stability, exercise restraint, properly handle differences under the constitutional and legal framework, and maintain political and social stability. At the informal meeting on the Myanmar issue held recently by the UN General Assembly, the Permanent Representative of China to the United Nations expounded China's position on the relevant issue. What I want to emphasize here is that cooling down the situation in Myanmar is a top priority and also a consensus of the international community. The international community should respect Myanmar's sovereignty, political independence, territorial integrity and national unity, and help all relevant parties in Myanmar engage in dialogue and reconciliation in accordance with the wishes and interests of the Myanmar people, properly handle differences, maintain political and social stability, resolve outstanding issues in a peaceful manner, and continue to promote domestic democratic transformation process in an orderly manner. Any action by the international community should contribute to Myanmar's political and social stability and peaceful reconciliation, avoid escalating conflicts and further complicating the situation. China is willing to continue to play a constructive role to ease up the situation on the ground in Myanmar.\nRegarding the second question, the Iranian nuclear issue is at a critical juncture. The top priority is for the United States to take specific measures to lift sanctions against Iran while Iran resumes compliance reciprocally in order to jointly push the JCPOA back on track. It is for this reason that China proposes to hold an international conference participated by all remaining JCPOA parties plus the United States, and supports the specific ideas put forward by the EU. We call on the United States and Europe to refrain from taking confrontational actions at the International Atomic Energy Agency so that the aforementioned meeting will be materialized as soon as possible. China will continue to maintain contact with relevant parties and make joint efforts to this end.\nRegarding the third question you mentioned, China is following the implementation of the US and Taliban peace agreement and the progress of the intra-Afghan negotiations. We have noticed that relevant parties and the international community have expressed concerns about the current direction of the evolving situation in Afghanistan. The security situation in Afghanistan is still complicated and severe. The intra-Afghan negotiations are moving towards substantive ones. We maintain that all parties and the international community should jointly and firmly advance the political settlement of the Afghan issue in a responsible and constructive way, thus helping Afghanistan realize peace, unity and development at an early date.\nChina firmly supports the \"Afghan-led, Afghan-owned\" process of peace and reconciliation that is extensive and inclusive. On the basis of respecting the wishes of all parties, China will act as a constructive party in upholding a fair and objective position and continuing to be a supporter, mediator and facilitator of the Afghan peace and reconciliation process.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202103/t20210301_9721183.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1857566.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, March 1 — After the General Administration of Customs announced the suspension of pineapple imports from the Taiwan region into the mainland, the DPP authorities accused the mainland of political oppression. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 1st in response to questions: The General Administration of Customs' decision to suspend pineapple imports from the Taiwan region into the mainland starting March 1, 2021, is a normal biosecurity precautionary measure, and is entirely reasonable and necessary.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that customs inspection and quarantine of imported agricultural products in accordance with the law is a requirement for implementing relevant laws, regulations, and standards, and is also necessary to prevent plant pest risks and safeguard people's rights and interests. The DPP authorities, however, deliberately distorted this, maliciously interpreting a technical issue and using it to attack and smear the mainland. This fully exposes their consistent practice: whenever cross-Strait affairs are involved, they engage in malicious manipulation. This shows that they have neither the will nor the ability to solve practical problems, and can only evade their own responsibility by slandering the mainland.\nZhu Fenglian also said that the safety of agricultural products is closely related to agricultural production, ecological security, food safety, and the rights and interests of the people. We have always attached great importance to this and will continue to adopt strict measures to control it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210301_12335172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The DPP authorities have made remarks disparaging the Hong Kong police's lawful prosecution of persons suspected of engaging in activities to subvert the state's political power. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","XINHUA, Beijing, March 2 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 2nd in response to questions: It is entirely justified and not subject to interference for the Hong Kong SAR government to pursue the legal responsibility of law violators in accordance with the law. The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities once again expose their true face of plotting chaos in Hong Kong and seeking “independence,” and their hypocrisy of using human rights and freedoms as a pretext. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs and not to keep sliding further down the wrong path.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210302_12335311.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to reporters' questions about Kuomintang Chairman Jiang Qichen's remark in an exclusive interview with Reuters that “the mainland is the main threat facing Taiwan,” which attracted attention, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd: The current situation in cross-Strait relations remains complex and grave. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are deliberately…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 3 —\nZhu Fenglian said: Only by resolutely curbing the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence” can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded. Relevant parties and individuals on the island should distinguish right from wrong, should not fall into the irrational confrontational mindset of populism on the island, should adhere to a positive mainland policy position, and should do more of what promotes peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhances the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and safeguards peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210303_12335669.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-04","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Lithuania said it will open a trade representation office in Taiwan. The country also said that the 17+1 economic initiative didn't bring expected results. Do you have any comment on this?","On your first question, there is but one China in the world and the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We are firmly against the mutual establishment of official agencies and official exchanges in all forms between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic relations with China including Lithuania. We urge the Lithuanian side to stay true to the one-China principle, abide by the commitments it made upon establishing diplomatic ties with China, refuse to be taken advantage of by \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and avoid doing anything detrimental to bilateral political mutual trust.\nOn your second question, we've taken note of the news. It should be pointed out that China-CEEC cooperation is a cross-regional cooperation mechanism established at the joint initiative of China and countries in central and eastern Europe. It embodies our shared aspiration for development. The mechanism is not dominated by China. Instead, the principle of freewill-based consultation, joint contribution, openness and inclusiveness is always upheld in advancing cooperation. Every party's opinion is respected and everything is handled upon consultation and every outcome is shared by all. This is for mutual benefit. China-CEEC cooperation, nine years since its launch, has yielded fruitful results and delivered tangible benefits to the people of participating countries. It has become a useful supplement to China-Europe relations. We have every confidence in its prospects and stand ready to work with like-minded friends for more fruitful China-CEEC cooperation, which will also boost and invigorate bilateral cooperation between China and relevant countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1858537.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1858527.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Taiwan's security authorities said the Mainland, by holding cross-Strait live-streaming competitions and training Taiwanese youth as broadcasters, is conducting so-called “cognitive warfare” against Taiwan to win the recognition of Taiwan residents. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 4 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 4th, in response to questions, that the DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest, fear that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will grow closer and better, fear that Taiwan residents will understand the real situation on the mainland, and, based on their “Taiwan independence” nature, carry out malicious manipulation to deliberately obstruct and sabotage exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, harming the legitimate rights, interests and well-being of Taiwan's young people in obtaining more and better development opportunities. This does not win popular support. Who is thinking for Taiwan's young people, and who is undermining their development prospects, is plain to see.\nShe said that we have always actively supported and encouraged exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, especially young people, to enhance mutual understanding and develop together.\nZhu Fenglian said that in 2020, the online live-streaming industry, represented by e-commerce live streaming, flourished and became an effective way to drive the domestic economic circulation. As of December 2020, the number of online live-streaming users on the mainland reached 617 million, of which e-commerce live-streaming users numbered 388 million. Cross-Strait online live-streaming exchange activities have provided very good opportunities for Taiwan youth who aspire to start businesses or find employment in the e-commerce live-streaming industry. They have built a stage for them to realize their dreams and shared development opportunities with them, which has been warmly welcomed by Taiwan youth. Some Taiwan youth frankly said, “In the new media industry, the mainland has mature short-video platforms and a relatively complete industrial chain. I hope to use such exchange activities to better enter this industry and develop my own career.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210304_12335780.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to the agenda, the Fourth Session of the 13th National People's Congress will deliberate the “Decision of the National People's Congress on Improving the Electoral System of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (Draft).” The DPP authorities have been making unwarranted remarks about this. What is the spokesperson's comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in answering…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 5 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 5th: Improving Hong Kong's electoral system is to provide a sound institutional guarantee for thoroughly and accurately implementing the “one country, two systems” policy and fully implementing the principle of “patriots administering Hong Kong.” The DPP authorities are accustomed to maliciously manipulating Hong Kong affairs, creating chaos in Hong Kong and seeking “independence.” Their sinister intentions will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210305_12336179.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-09","Zhao Lijian","NHK","First question, the White House spokesman said on March 8 that the United States would continue to assist Taiwan in maintaining a sufficient self-defense capability. What's China's comment on this? Second question, Japan's Defense Minister voiced concern over China's Coast Guard Law, which Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said was fully in line with international law, saying that it was vague…","On your first question, China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China remains resolutely determined to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and opposes Taiwan independence and external interference.\nThe root cause of the current tension and turbulence in cross-strait relations is that the DPP authorities refuse to recognize the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle, collude with external forces, and constantly seek independence. We are willing to carry out dialogue and consultation with all parties, groups and personages in Taiwan on cross-strait political issues and issues related to promoting the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland on the political basis of adhering to the 1992 Consensus and opposing Taiwan independence, so as to build up consensus and resolve differences.\nWe urge the U.S. side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiques, stop official interactions with and arms sales to Taiwan, handle Taiwan related issues prudently and properly, and avoid sending any erroneous signals to the Taiwan independence forces, lest it should damage China-U.S. relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, State Councilor Wang Yi has clarified China's position on this issue. The Coast Guard Law is just a routine piece of domestic legislation. It is not targeted at any specific country. And it is totally in line with international law and international practice. In fact, many countries, including Japan, have enacted similar laws and regulations long before China. Settling maritime disputes through friendly consultation and without the use or threat of force is the consistent position of the Chinese government. It is also a long-established common understanding between China and its neighbors. It is hoped that the Japanese side will abide by the spirit of four-point principled consensus between China and Japan, move in the same direction, and avoid words and deeds that could complicate the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347000.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1859626.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-10","Zhao Lijian","AFP","I have two questions. First of all, U.S. President Biden will hold Quad alliance talks with Australia, India, and Japan on Friday. What's China response to this? Secondly, the top U.S. Admiral Philip Davidson said that he fears China could invade Taiwan in the next six years. And China's Ministry of Defense in January said that Taiwan formally declaring independence means war. What's your response to Admiral…","Regarding your first question, regional cooperation arrangements should all conform to the trend of the times which is peaceful development and win-win cooperation. We hope that the relevant countries will act in line with the common interests of regional countries, uphold the principle of openness, inclusiveness and win-win outcomes, and do more things that are conducive to regional peace, stability and development, not the other way around.\nOn your second question, China has stated its position on the Taiwan question many times. By exploiting the Taiwan question to exaggerate China's military threat, some people in the United States are actually looking for excuses to justify the increase of the U.S. military expenditure, expansion of its military power, and interfere in regional affairs. The United States should abandon the Cold War zero-sum mentality, view China's development and national defense development objectively and rationally, and do more things that are conducive to mutual trust between China and the United States and regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202103/t20210310_9721218.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1859958.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 11 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 11th, said that the DPP authorities made baseless comments on the NPC decision concerning Hong Kong, deceived public opinion under the banner of so-called ‘democracy’ and ‘freedom,’ and maliciously attacked it. This once again exposes their sinister intent and evil nature of manipulating Hong Kong affairs politically and seeking ‘independence’ by disrupting Hong Kong. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: seeking ‘independence’ has no way out, the attempt to disrupt Hong Kong will not succeed, and accumulated crimes will surely be severely punished.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the Fourth Session of the 13th National People’s Congress voted to adopt the ‘Decision of the National People’s Congress on Improving the Electoral System of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.’ It embodies the comprehensive implementation of the principle of ‘patriots administering Hong Kong.’ It is a necessary measure to safeguard the country’s sovereignty, security, and development interests and the long-term prosperity and stability of Hong Kong, and it will powerfully guarantee that the practice of ‘one country, two systems’ advances steadily and far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210311_12337800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-17","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","The United States and Japan issued a joint press statement after holding their \"2+2\" Security Consultative Committee on March 16 saying that China's behavior, where inconsistent with the existing international order, presents challenges to the international community. They also expressed concerns over issues relating to Taiwan, the South China Sea and Xinjiang. I wonder if you would like to comment on this?","The US-Japan joint statement maliciously attacks China's foreign policy, flagrantly interferes in China's domestic affairs, and attempts to harm China's interests. We deplore and reject it and have lodged stern representations with both countries. I would like to stress the following:\nFirst, there is only one system in the world, and it is the UN-centered international order; there is only one set of rules, and it is the basic norms governing international relations with the UN Charter as its cornerstone. The US and Japan are not entitled to define what the international order is, still less to impose their standard on others.\nSecond, China is always an important force to safeguard world peace and promote common development. We have established partnerships with 112 countries and international organizations, joined more than 100 inter-governmental organizations and signed over 500 multilateral treaties. China now stands as the largest contributor of peacekeepers in all the permanent members of the Security Council. The US is accustomed to upholding double standards and cherry-picking with international law and international rules. During its nearly 250 years of history, there were only 16 years when it was not at war. It also runs hundreds of military bases all over the world. The international community has its fair judgement as to who poses the top threat to world peace and security.\nThird, China's position on issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, the South China Sea and the Diaoyu Island is consistent and clear. Our resolution and will to defend national sovereignty, security and development interests is rock solid. China's sovereignty over islands in the South China Sea and the adjacent waters, the Diaoyu Island and its affiliated islands is indisputable. The South China Sea is more than 8,300 miles away from the continental United States. Despite the distance, the U.S. side has repeatedly sent warships and military aircraft to the South China Sea for military drills and close-in reconnaissance, without a break all year round. It is the United States that has been flexing muscles and practicing coercion and intimidation. Issues concerning Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are China's domestic affairs that brook no foreign interference. The US-Japan joint statement shows a disregard for historical merits of the issues, as well as facts and truth. It is but further evidence of the two countries colluding to meddle in China's internal affairs and malign China.\nFourth, the United States and Japan, stuck in the Cold-War mentality, deliberately seek bloc confrontation and attempt to form an anti-China circle. This runs counter to the trend of our times and the aspiration for peace, development and cooperation shared by the region and the vast majority of countries in the world. It will only bring chaos or even conflict to the region and further expose the US-Japan alliance's true face of undermining regional peace and stability.\nFifth, Japan, driven by the selfish aim to check China's revitalization, willingly stoops to acting as a strategic vassal of the United States, going so far as to break faith, harm relations with China, invite the wolf into the house, and betray the collective interests of the whole region. Such despicable behavior is deeply unpopular.\nSixth, we urge the United States and Japan to immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop forming the anti-China clique, and stop undermining regional peace and stability. China will take all measures necessary to resolutely defend sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1861993.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1861952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-17","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","You said just now that issues with regard to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are China's domestic affairs. Does that mean that China is not willing to discuss such topics at the upcoming talks or will all topics that the US is willing to talk about be on the table?","I'd like to stress that this high-level strategic dialogue is proposed by the US side and the \"2+2\" format is also its idea. We hope that, through this dialogue, the two sides can follow through on the consensus reached between President Xi Jinping and President Joe Biden in their phone call, focus on cooperation, manage differences and bring China-US relations back to the right track. We didn't say that Taiwan, Hong Kong- and Xinjiang-related issues cannot be discussed during the dialogue. We will brief the US side on the relevant situation and express our solemn position. But the US moves to sway public opinion /poison the atmosphere in the run-up to the dialogue in an attempt to pressure China is futile and doomed to fail. China will always firmly uphold its sovereignty, security and development interests. We ask the US side to abide by norms governing international relations and refrain from doing things that undermine China's core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1861993.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1861952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-17","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan's newly appointed \"defense minister\" said today that the United States has approved the export of sensitive technology to equip Taiwan's new submarine fleet. How does the Chinese side feel about these developments?","I am unaware of the situation you mentioned. I can assure you that our positions on the Taiwan question and relations between the US and the Taiwan region are consistent and clear. We also urge the US side to fully recognize that the Taiwan question is a highly sensitive issue and that it should strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and handle Taiwan-related issues cautiously and prudently.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1861993.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1861952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on March 17, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian presided, and together with Jiang Jianping, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Agricultural Affairs Office of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, and Hu Yuanhui, Deputy Director of the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Forestry and Grassland…","Dear journalists, good morning! Welcome to the press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Today, eleven departments, including the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, and the State Forestry and Grassland Administration, have jointly issued the “Several Measures on Supporting Taiwan Compatriots and Taiwan-Funded Enterprises in Developing Agriculture and Forestry on the Mainland” (referred to as the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures”). To help you better understand the Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures, we have specially invited Deputy Director Jiang Jianping of the Taiwan Agriculture Affairs Office of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, and Deputy Director Hu Yuanhui of the Office of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the State Forestry and Grassland Administration, to give detailed explanations. Now we will begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","In recent years, the mainland has successively introduced policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, such as the “31 Measures,” the “26 Measures,” and the “11 Measures.” May I ask what considerations led to the introduction of the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” now? What are the characteristics of the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry”?","I will explain this question to everyone. The issuance of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” is an important step to fully implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee and the speech delivered at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of General Secretary Xi Jinping's “Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan,” taking the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nThe Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee made deployments for promoting peaceful development, integrated development, and priority development of cross-Strait relations, and for prioritizing the development of agriculture and rural areas and comprehensively advancing rural revitalization. The Outline of the Fourteenth Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development and Long-Range Objectives for 2035, released not long ago, proposes to improve institutions and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and enjoy equal treatment on the mainland, continuously introduce and implement policy measures that benefit Taiwan and its people, and let Taiwan compatriots share development opportunities and take part in the process of the mainland's economic and social development. To help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises participate in the high-quality development of agriculture and forestry and rural revitalization on the mainland, the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” put forward measures addressing the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in the agriculture and forestry sectors, including the use of farmland and forest land, financing convenience and funding support, investment and operation, research and innovation, and opening up the domestic market.\nAfter reading the full text of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” carefully, everyone can sense that the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” continue the same line as the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures,” further providing equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises participating in the high-quality development of agriculture and forestry and rural revitalization on the mainland. These measures both look to the new requirements of agriculture and forestry development on the mainland during the 14th Five-Year Plan period and respond to the main demands of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. In brief, they have three major features.\nFirst, they are grounded in the new development stage. As the mainland accelerates the implementation of the strategy for high-quality development of agriculture and forestry and rural revitalization, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have brighter prospects and more opportunities for development in agriculture and forestry on the mainland. The “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” are grounded in the new development stage and encourage Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to seize opportunities and upgrade their development. For example, Articles 10, 11, and 12 support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in developing rural characteristic agriculture and forest-grass ecological industries, participating in the integrated development of primary, secondary, and tertiary industries in rural areas, and taking part in research, innovation, achievement transformation, and technical services in areas such as smart agriculture and green agricultural inputs.\nSecond, they meet the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. The “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” are close to the needs of grassroots Taiwan compatriots and focus on common issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. For example, Articles 1 and 2 address the operating rights of rural land and forest land, Articles 4, 5, and 6 address financing issues, and Article 22 proposes targeted solutions for opening up the domestic market.\nThird, they have broad coverage and strong support. The “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the construction and production and operation in many fields, including urban and rural cold-chain logistics infrastructure and livestock and aquaculture. They encourage Taiwan-funded enterprises to take part in drafting national standards for agricultural and forestry products and support Taiwan compatriots in participating in rural construction. They largely cover all aspects of Taiwan compatriots' and Taiwan-funded enterprises' development in agriculture and forestry. In addition, they propose specific measures on applications for fiscal subsidies related to agriculture and forestry, deepening cooperation between Taiwan-funded enterprises and state-owned agricultural reclamation enterprises, and strengthening the construction of Taiwan farmers' entrepreneurship parks, providing strong support for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nGoing forward, the Taiwan Affairs Office, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the State Forestry and Grassland Administration, and other departments will implement each measure thoroughly and in detail, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and enhance the affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339184.htm"],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","农视网记者","The 14th Five-Year Plan proposes to give priority to developing agriculture and rural areas and to comprehensively advance rural revitalization. What new opportunities will this bring for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop on the mainland?","This question will be answered for everyone by Deputy Director Jiang Jianping.\nJiang Jianping: Hello everyone, I am very glad to answer your questions. The Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee made strategic arrangements to give priority to the development of agriculture and rural areas and to comprehensively promote rural revitalization. This year's No. 1 Central Document, centered on comprehensively promoting rural revitalization and accelerating the modernization of agriculture and rural areas, further clarified work ideas and key measures. At the “Two Sessions” that just concluded, General Secretary Xi Jinping participated in the deliberations of relevant delegations and gave a series of important instructions on rural revitalization, proposing many new judgments and new requirements. Premier Li Keqiang devoted a separate chapter of the Government Work Report to deployments and arrangements. All of these bring new opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to develop on the mainland, and Taiwan compatriots and enterprises can accomplish much in mainland rural revitalization.\nDuring my research in Fujian, I learned that starting in 2018, they successively introduced 66 Taiwan architect teams and more than 200 rural construction and creative talents, who have participated in the construction of 112 villages in 30 counties across the province. They have created a batch of internet-famous spots, rural tourism villages and industrial bases, which have not only injected new vitality into rural revitalization but also brought new development achievements for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. There are many other examples in other provinces, which I will not list one by one here. As long as Taiwan compatriots and enterprises seize the opportunities, they will certainly achieve better and faster development in comprehensively promoting rural revitalization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央电视台记者","In recent years the mainland has achieved many successes in forestry development. In this process, where are the opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises?","We have Deputy Director Hu Yuanhui answer this question for everyone.\nHu Yuanhui: Hello, everyone. I am very glad to exchange views with media friends on forestry work. Forestry is a green industry, and developing forestry is of very important and practical significance for improving the ecological environment and responding to climate change. During the 13th Five-Year Plan period, the mainland's forestry development achieved gratifying results, and forest coverage has now reached 23.04%, with forest stock volume of 17.56 billion cubic meters. During the 14th Five-Year Plan period, forestry efforts will be further intensified, concentrating strength to implement 13 major ecological projects, including the Qinghai-Tibet, Yellow River, Yangtze River and Three-North projects. The implementation of these projects will drive the development of industries such as tree seedlings and project afforestation, and will also provide more investment opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nIn addition, in 2020 the total output value of the mainland's forestry industry exceeded 7.5 trillion yuan, and three fields each had output value exceeding 1 trillion yuan. They are economic forest product planting and collection, wood processing and wood-bamboo product manufacturing, and forest tourism and leisure services. Many provinces on the mainland have proposed characteristic industries for priority development and support; for example, Yunnan promotes the development of the nut industry, and Jiangxi vigorously advances the under-forest economy. These are all fields with promising prospects, and they also bring new opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nThird, we continuously optimize forestry management, for example in the review and issuance of forest felling permits. To simplify procedures, we have basically completed the development of a mobile app system, and a new version of the felling management system will soon be launched, gradually building a felling management government service system that integrates application, acceptance, inquiry and licensing. These convenience measures will also provide a better investment environment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Article 17 of the \"22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry\" mentions supporting eligible Taiwanese farmer entrepreneurship parks in establishing national modern agricultural industrial parks. Please introduce the situation in this regard.","The 17th measure involves the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs. Please allow Vice Minister Jiang Jianping to answer everyone's questions.\nJiang Jianping: Since 2017, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and the Ministry of Finance have vigorously promoted the construction of modern agricultural industrial parks. At present, a cumulative total of more than 9 billion yuan in central financial subsidies has been arranged, supporting the establishment of 151 national modern agricultural industrial parks, and a construction pattern of progressive advancement at the national, provincial, municipal and county levels has been formed. Looking at the results of construction: first, we have strengthened leading industries and promoted industrial revitalization; second, we have innovated closely-knit mechanisms of benefit-sharing with and support for farmers, increasing farmers' incomes. In 2019, the per capita disposable income of farmers in industrial parks was 21,000 yuan, 31% higher than the average level; third, we have cultivated growth momentum and strengthened the county economy; fourth, we have promoted industrial integration and driven rural construction.\nThe application and establishment of industrial parks are organized by each province; after review and approval by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and the Ministry of Finance, the central government will, depending on the circumstances, arrange some subsidy funds. At present, four Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Parks, namely Cixi in Zhejiang, Qixia in Shandong, Xishan in Jiangsu and Hexian in Anhui, have been successfully included in the list of national modern agricultural industrial park construction. Regarding the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” we will continue to support the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Parks and actively apply to establish national modern agricultural industrial parks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Article 14 of the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” proposes that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises may, in accordance with the law, engage equally in the cultivation of superior forest tree varieties and the production and operation of forestry and grass seedlings. Could you introduce this measure in detail?","The “14 measures” involve the State Forestry and Grassland Administration. We have invited Deputy Director Hu Yuanhui to answer everyone’s questions.\nHu Yuanhui: The breeding of forest seedlings, including the breeding of grass seed, falls within the scope of franchised operation. In this field, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises enjoy the same rights to business operations as mainland residents and enterprises. As long as they meet the requirements of the Seed Law and the Administrative Measures for Forest Seed Production and Business Licenses, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises may fully engage in the cultivation and operation of forest seedlings.\nAt present, Taiwan-funded enterprises that hold a Forest Seed Production and Business License issued by the competent forestry and grassland authorities and engage in the production and operation of forestry and grassland seedlings are mainly concentrated in coastal areas. These enterprises mainly engage in the production and operation of landscaping seedlings and flowers, which has played a certain role in helping local farmers increase their incomes and employment and has also played a positive role in developing the local economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","We all know that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople have been participating in agricultural development on the mainland for more than 30 years. Please introduce the current state of cross-Strait agricultural exchanges and cooperation, and what major achievements have been made?","I would like Deputy Director Jiang Jianping to introduce the situation in this area for everyone.\nJiang Jianping: Overall, after more than thirty years of development, cross-Strait agricultural exchange and cooperation has formed a development pattern that is comprehensive, wide-ranging and multi-level. It is mainly reflected in three aspects:\nFirst, cooperation has become closer. Exchanges of personnel, exhibitions and information are increasingly frequent; every year, the agricultural products fairs and economic and trade negotiation meetings attract high-quality agricultural products from both sides to “shine” and “compete on the same stage,” entering ordinary households.\nSecond, platforms are steadily expanding. We have approved the establishment of 15 Straits Agricultural Cooperation Experimental Zones and 28 Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Parks. After years of development, they have become the preferred destination for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises investing in agriculture on the Mainland, and a bridge and link for the integration of agriculture across the Strait.\nThird, development is increasingly diverse. Beyond traditional planting and breeding, more and more Taiwan compatriots and enterprises are using approaches such as “agriculture+,” “tourism+,” and “internet+” to enter fields such as rural tourism, deep processing of agricultural products, and rural e-commerce, developing new industries and new business forms, becoming increasingly diversified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Article 21 of the “22 Agriculture and Forestry Measures” involves the floriculture industry. May I ask how to strengthen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in floriculture and promote common development?","I think this should be a measure that many Taiwanese businesses and enterprises are paying particular attention to. Please ask Deputy Director Hu Yuanhui to interpret it for everyone.\nHu Yuanhui: The flower industry is a rather beautiful undertaking, and also an industry that adds luster to everyone's life. Flowers are an important area of cross-Strait cooperation. The Mainland's flower market has developed rapidly in recent years and has become an important flower consumption area and import-export trading place. In 2019, the total import and export value of flowers in the Mainland was 620 million US dollars, of which imports were 262 million US dollars and exports were 358 million US dollars.\nCross-Strait cooperation in the flower field has already explored some good models. For example, Guangxi held the Guangxi-Taiwan Flower Industry Cooperation Seminar, and a batch of flower cooperation projects took root locally; the Nanning Taiwan Flower Industry Park, the Liuzhou Qingmao Flower Base and others have become models of Guangxi-Taiwan cooperation. According to statistics from Guangxi forestry authorities, as of the end of 2019, the flower area in Guangxi reached 66,700 hectares, realizing flower output value of 15.07 billion yuan.\nWe welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to invest in the Mainland's flower industry, encourage relevant parties on the Mainland to actively invite Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to participate in flower expositions, flower arrangement competitions and other activities held on the Mainland, and also welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to actively take part in drafting and applying for national standards for flower products, promoting the interconnection of cross-Strait flower industry standards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Regarding the issue of land management rights: we note that Article 1 of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” proposes that rural land management rights obtained by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises through transfer are protected by law. When the land management rights expire, they may be given priority to continue leasing under equal conditions. Please interpret this.","Please allow Deputy Director Jiang Jianping to answer this question for everyone.\nJiang Jianping: The issue of land management rights is a matter of common concern. To guide the orderly transfer of land management rights and protect the lawful rights and interests of the parties to a transfer, since 2014 the mainland has successively issued the \"Opinions on Guiding the Orderly Transfer of Rural Land Management Rights and Developing Moderate-Scale Agricultural Operations\" and the \"Opinions on Improving the Separation of Rural Land Ownership, Contracting Rights, and Management Rights.\" In 2018, the \"Rural Land Contracting Law\" was revised, further clarifying the connotation of rural land management rights and making explicit provisions on the lawful protection of the various rights of transferees.\nTaiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, as business entities, have always had their management rights protected, just like those of other entities. Since March 1 of this year, the newly revised \"Measures for the Administration of Rural Land Management Right Transfers\" have formally taken effect, further emphasizing that, on the premise of lawfully protecting collective ownership and rural households' contracting rights, the land management rights acquired by management entities through transfer contracts are equally protected, ensuring they have stable business expectations. The management entities here naturally also include Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Article 2 of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” involves forestland management rights of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. It proposes that the forestland management rights of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises may be registered in accordance with law, and that ownership certificates may be issued and the rights transferred. May the spokesperson please explain this?","This question will first be answered by Deputy Director Hu Yuanhui.\nHu Yuanhui: Forest land management rights are a matter of great concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. According to the relevant provisions of the Rural Land Contract Law, revised in 2018, and the Forest Law, revised in 2019, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises may, in accordance with law, obtain collective forest land management rights, as well as ownership and use rights of trees on forest land, through transfer from forestry operators such as village collective economic organizations, contracting households and forestry enterprises, and may operate forestry accordingly. They may also, in accordance with law and regulations, carry out forest-right mortgage loans or transfer and disposal. In the specific process, Taiwan compatriots and enterprises should note that when obtaining forest land management rights, they need to pass the qualification review and project examination for the transfer of collective forest land management rights by the local people's government, and operation of forest land must comply with the forest resource management system.\nBecause this measure also involves other departments, I will add a supplementary explanation. To adapt to the needs of forestry reform and development and to meet the registration needs of rights holders, relevant mainland departments issued the “Notice on Further Standardizing Registration of Forest-Right Real Estate and Well Connecting Forest Rights Registration with Forestry Management.” It clarifies that where forest land management rights are transferred or re-transferred in accordance with law for a term of 5 years or more, applications may be made, per the contract, to register forest land management rights/forest tree ownership or forest land management rights/forest tree use rights. It also emphasizes that, apart from cases where acceptance is legally prohibited, real estate registration authorities may not refuse to accept such applications.\nTaiwan compatriots and enterprises can lawfully obtain collective forest land management rights and the ownership and use rights of trees on forest land. Taiwan compatriots and enterprises may register forest land management rights in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Rural Land Contract Law, and may also re-transfer them in accordance with the regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The National People's Congress and the National Committee of the CPPCC reviewed and approved the 14th Five-Year Plan and the Outline of Long-Range Objectives for 2035, which has attracted much attention. Please interpret the content relating to cross-strait relations. What important significance does it have? How will it be implemented?","The “14th Five-Year Plan” Outline clearly sets out the goal and tasks of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland in the new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country, reflecting the strategic positioning of work on Taiwan in the process of national rejuvenation. Based on the new development stage, we apply the new development philosophy and build a new development pattern, implement the Taiwan-related arrangements of the Outline in a thorough and detailed manner, promote high-quality development of work on Taiwan, and firmly advance peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and the process of reunifying the motherland.\nWe adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, take the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as our guide, continue to improve institutional arrangements and policy measures that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and deepen cross-Strait integrated development. We actively promote higher quality and efficiency in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, unite compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly inherit and carry forward the excellent traditional Chinese culture, and strengthen national identity and emotional connection through exchange and cooperation.\nWe adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and resolutely oppose and curb any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nWe hope that a broad range of Taiwan compatriots will fully understand the magnificent blueprint for the country's future development drawn up in the Outline and the enormous development space it contains, seize opportunities, ride the momentum to achieve better and greater development for themselves, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339183.htm"],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","After the mainland suspended imports of pineapples from Taiwan, the head of Taiwan's agriculture department said: why did the mainland find Taiwan pineapples unqualified in inspections last year, and only now announce a ban on imports? Please explain the relevant situation.","We have also seen the relevant reports, and it is necessary to explain the situation to everyone. In 2020, relevant mainland authorities notified the Taiwan side of 28 batches of non-compliant pineapples from the Taiwan region, reminding the Taiwan side to strengthen management at the source. Regrettably, the non-compliance has never improved, and the Taiwan side has given no response.\nAfter risk assessment, the risk of plant pests and diseases being carried by pineapples from the Taiwan region is very high. To prevent the introduction of plant pests and protect the mainland’s agricultural production and ecological security, in accordance with relevant laws and regulations, the relevant authorities have suspended the import of pineapples from the Taiwan region. This is a normal biosecurity measure, scientific and reasonable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Regarding the mainland's suspension of imports of Taiwan pineapples, some in the DPP have claimed that this is the mainland “bullying Taiwan's farmers.” Other opinion on the island holds that Taiwan's farmers are “taking the blame” for the DPP authorities. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","For many years, the mainland has attached great importance to the interests and well-being of Taiwan farmers, and has actively taken measures to address their difficulties and help them expand the mainland market. When agricultural products on the island are unsold, the mainland promptly extends a helping hand to help Taiwan farmers tide over difficulties, so that they receive tangible benefits.\nThe mainland's temporary suspension of pineapple imports from the Taiwan region is a normal precautionary measure taken to safeguard agricultural production and ecological security, and is entirely reasonable and necessary. The DPP authorities have over-politicized a technical issue and maliciously smeared the mainland, closing the door to solving the problem themselves. Resolving the safety of agricultural products at the source is not difficult; the key is that the DPP authorities have no willingness at all to consider the interests of Taiwan farmers. Making a surface show of eating pineapples is merely a way to muddle through.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339174.htm"],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The head of Taiwan's agriculture authorities said that the pineapple pest situation reported by the mainland actually also exists in more than two places on the mainland, and that the risk can be eliminated through fumigation treatment. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","On this issue, after seeing the reports, I also looked into it specifically and consulted the relevant professional departments. Regarding the two pests that some people in Taiwan have mentioned, which also exist on the Mainland, namely the Oceanic buttock-streak mealybug and the new pineapple gray mealybug, they are sporadically distributed in certain places on the Mainland, but are under effective quarantine control.\nAs for the risk of eradication through fumigation treatment, everyone should pay special attention to the fact that fumigation easily causes pineapples to turn black and reduces their quality. The methyl bromide fumigant used in fumigation is a harmful agent; large-scale use would endanger the health of operators and also damage the atmospheric ozone layer. Therefore, the Mainland side has consistently required that source control be strengthened during pineapple planting and processing to eliminate plant epidemic risks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","First question: since the mainland has said it is “suspending” imports of Taiwan pineapples, that means there is still a chance of resumption in the future. Is the mainland willing to consult with the Taiwan side on jointly preventing and controlling agricultural biological pests and diseases, or to handle this under the current counterpart mechanism between cross-Strait agricultural agencies? Second question:…","Let me answer the first question first. As I just stated, in 2020 the mainland side repeatedly notified the Taiwan region of substandard pineapples and reminded the Taiwan side to strengthen control at the source. However, this substandard situation has not improved, and we have not received any reply from the Taiwan side. The safety of agricultural products concerns people's vital interests. We hope relevant Taiwan authorities will pay attention, fulfill their regulatory responsibilities, strengthen source control, and avoid causing losses to businesses and the public. The DPP authorities, on the one hand, use this to create hostility, while on the other hand they claim they want to “sit down and talk.” Don't they find this pointless?\nThe second question: will other Taiwan agricultural products be included on the suspension-of-import list? Whether to suspend imports of Taiwan pineapple products or other agricultural products into the mainland will be decided by the competent authorities based on relevant mainland regulations and standards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The first question: Regarding the mainland's suspension of imports of Taiwan pineapples, the Taiwan side calls it “political oppression” that pressures ordinary farmers, and has now issued the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” which benefit Taiwan agricultural practitioners. Are you worried that the Taiwan side views this as pulling the firewood from under the cauldron or as a “carrot and stick”…","For the first question, let me summarize our position once again. Regarding the suspension of pineapple imports from Taiwan by the mainland, this is a normal biosecurity precaution taken to protect the mainland's agricultural production, ecological security, and the vital interests of the public. It is scientific and reasonable.\nThe \"22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry\" are concrete steps to implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee and to advance the implementation of the 14th Five-Year Plan. They are an important component of promoting cross-Strait exchange, cooperation, and integrated development, and will further deepen agricultural and forestry cooperation across the Strait and enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nWhether it is the suspension of pineapple imports from Taiwan or the issuance of the \"22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,\" they share one commonality: both are concrete manifestations of the mainland's implementation of the people-centered development philosophy in its work on Taiwan. What the people need, we do. The people need safe agricultural products and a healthy ecological environment, so we must guard the gate and fulfill our responsibility. The people need high-quality development to meet their aspirations for a better life, so we create a better business environment and, in promoting integrated development across the Strait, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nFor the second question, we have already made our position clear. The DPP authorities have turned a technical issue into a political one and shut the door on resolving the problem themselves. This is of no help in solving anything.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国电视公司记者","First question: The US and Japan held “2+2” talks, and US Secretary of State Blinken mentioned that if the mainland side undermines Taiwan's democracy by coercive means, the US will definitely respond. May I ask for the spokesperson's response? Second question: Reports say the mainland is negotiating with several countries to introduce a “vaccine passport.” Can the two sides handle this in the same way? If the…","On the first question, our position is very clear. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no external interference. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.\nOn the question of vaccines: as to whether there will be “mutual recognition of vaccines” across the Strait, after more than a year of the epidemic's impact, the feelings of people on both sides are the same. We hope that, under normalized epidemic prevention and control and as vaccination proceeds steadily, personnel exchanges across the Strait can gradually return to normal. To date, the Taiwan side has not resumed opening to mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, which is the greatest obstacle to normal personnel exchanges across the Strait.\nAs for your question about whether epidemic prevention measures could be adjusted so that vaccinated Taiwan compatriots can travel to and from the mainland, the relevant authorities will comprehensively consider various factors in studying and handling it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen said, while meeting with representatives of Taiwan's small and medium enterprises, that Taiwan's economic growth rate this year has a chance to exceed 4%. In your view, what is the main driver of Taiwan's current economic growth?","In 2020, cross-Strait trade totaled US$260.81 billion, of which Taiwan's exports to the mainland reached US$200.66 billion. According to Taiwan's own statistics, Taiwan's exports to the mainland and Hong Kong accounted for as much as 43.9% of its total exports. Taiwan's economic development cannot be separated from the mainland. The mainland, based on the new development stage, implementing the new development philosophy, building a new development pattern, and promoting high-quality development, is bringing major opportunities for Taiwan's economic development, which is a major benefit for Taiwan compatriots. We hope that compatriots on both sides will strengthen economic and trade cooperation, so that Taiwan's economy can have a better outlook and Taiwan compatriots can gain more benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视中国新闻记者","Recently, the mainland has been orderly carrying out COVID-19 vaccinations. I would like to ask about the progress of vaccinations for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland and what the next steps are.","As of March 14, the mainland had administered a cumulative 64.98 million (6498万) doses of COVID-19 vaccine. As of March 9, we had carried out vaccine cooperation with more than 90 countries through means including providing vaccines as aid, exporting vaccines, carrying out vaccine research, development, and production cooperation, and licensed use.\nThe mainland attaches great importance to and cares about the health rights of Taiwan residents, and actively and orderly arranges for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland to receive vaccination. Since late December 2020, in accordance with the unified deployment for emergency use of vaccines, Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities, under the overall coordination of local governments, have treated Taiwan compatriots in nine key groups, including those engaged in imported cold chain and port quarantine, equally, and included them in local free vaccination arrangements, following the principles of territorial management, voluntary application, and informed consent.\nRelevant departments are studying and formulating vaccination policies for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland outside the above key groups, in order to properly arrange vaccination for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","On the 10th of this month, the US destroyer USS Fitzgerald sailed through the Taiwan Strait and publicized it openly. This is also the third time a US warship has transited the Taiwan Strait since US President Biden took office. What is your comment?","The passage of US warships through the Taiwan Strait sends a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, deliberately interferes with and undermines the regional situation, and damages peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We resolutely oppose this. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence. The PLA will always remain highly vigilant and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","According to reports, the International Olympic Committee will purchase COVID-19 vaccines from mainland China to provide to athletes participating in the Tokyo Olympics. Regarding whether Taiwanese athletes may use mainland vaccines, Chen Shih-chung, head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention authority, said that mainland vaccines cannot be ruled out. May I ask the spokesperson for your comment on this?","We believe the International Olympic Committee will make appropriate arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that under the 2021 policies for mainland universities enrolling Taiwan students that have been announced so far, Taiwan students who score “均标级” (average-standard level) or above in any subject of the General Scholastic Ability Test (學測) may apply to mainland universities, but some mainland universities have raised their admission thresholds. Is this actually the case?","The relevant claims are not true. According to the Ministry of Education's relevant enrollment policies, the conditions for mainland universities' enrollment of students from Taiwan this year are basically the same as in previous years. Some universities set requirements for “Xuece” (学测) scores based on their own enrollment situations. This is entirely normal and reasonable.\nIn recent years, mainland universities have accelerated the construction of first-class universities and first-class disciplines, and their educational quality has continuously improved. More and more Taiwan students see this and voluntarily choose to study on the mainland. In 2020, even though affected by the COVID-19 epidemic, many Taiwan students' enthusiasm for applying to mainland universities did not diminish. At present, the number of Taiwan students studying at mainland universities has reached 12,000. A Taiwan student studying at Wuhan University said in an exchange, “Crossing the Strait and traveling a thousand miles to study at Wuhan University is the most correct investment I have made for myself.”\nWe sincerely welcome Taiwan students to study and develop on the mainland. We suggest that students obtain application information through authoritative channels, such as school official websites, the Cross-Strait Admissions Service Center website, and the admissions information website for mainland universities enrolling students from Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Recently, Yao Chia-wen (姚嘉文), convener of the DPP’s so-called “Constitutional Revision Group,” vowed to pursue “Taiwan independence constitution-making,” and DPP legislator Chen Ting-fei (陈亭妃) again put forward a proposal to substantially lower the threshold for so-called “constitutional amendment.” What response does the spokesperson have?","We are closely following the relevant developments. A small handful of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements on the island have not given up their “independence” ambitions and keep changing tactics to scheme for “independence” and create trouble. These reckless acts will only continuously tear Taiwan’s society apart, aggravate the turbulence in cross-Strait relations, push Taiwan into a dangerous situation, and bring profound disaster to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will remain highly vigilant and resolutely oppose and curb the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence” through concrete action. To safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, we will never sit idly by in the face of any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and we will take all necessary measures to counter them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339175.htm"],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Fourth Session of the Thirteenth National People’s Congress voted to adopt the 《Decision of the National People’s Congress on Improving the Electoral System of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region》. The DPP and its authorities have made groundless accusations and maliciously attacked it. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The NPC’s decision to improve the electoral system of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region provides institutional guarantees for comprehensively implementing “patriots administering Hong Kong.” It is an urgent need to eliminate social chaos in Hong Kong and consolidate the situation of moving from chaos to order, and it is also a fundamental solution for achieving long-term stability and prosperity in Hong Kong and ensuring that “one country, two systems” advances steadily and far. This helps Hong Kong raise the quality of its democracy, develop high-quality democracy, improve the governing efficiency of the Special Administrative Region, and achieve good governance. It serves the vital interests of the broad masses of citizens and ensures Hong Kong’s long-term prosperity and stability.\nThe reason the DPP and its authorities are panicked about this, and repeatedly jump out to distort facts and make baseless accusations, is that it will cut off the black hand of “Taiwan independence” and “Hong Kong independence” colluding to disrupt Hong Kong and divide the country, and it will shatter their delusional fantasy of pursuing “independence” through disorder in Hong Kong. For a long time, the DPP, its authorities, and “Taiwan independence” forces, fearing that Hong Kong would not be in turmoil, have vigorously undermined Hong Kong’s stability. They have done so by colluding with “Hong Kong independence” forces, providing funds and equipment, training personnel, and sheltering violent rioters who disrupt Hong Kong, and they have slandered and attacked “one country, two systems.” They serve their political aim of splitting the country by sacrificing the interests of the broad masses of Hong Kong citizens. Such incidents are too numerous to recount.\nWe urge the DPP and its authorities: democracy and freedom are not a fig leaf for disrupting Hong Kong and plotting “independence.” If you are harming Hong Kong, do not pose as a weasel paying New Year’s greetings to a chicken. We solemnly warn the DPP and its authorities: any attempt by any person or force to harm national sovereignty, security, and development interests, or to undermine Hong Kong’s prosperity and stability, is futile and will surely bring retribution upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339176.htm"],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","First question: The Xiamen Taiwan Business Association recently said that it has separately written letters to the relevant departments on both sides, hoping to communicate and resume the “small three links.” What is the mainland's attitude toward resuming civil economic and trade exchanges across the Strait? Second question: regarding the National People's Congress's passage of the relevant decision on Hong…","On the first question: the “small three links” have always been the most important and convenient channel for exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, especially between the people of Fujian and Taiwan. Since last year, there has not been a single confirmed COVID-19 case in Kinmen and Matsu, and Fujian has gone more than 390 days without a locally confirmed case. Residents of both areas hope to restore the “small three links” as soon as possible. We hope the DPP authorities will do more things that benefit cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than trying every means to obstruct and restrict them and engage in political manipulation.\nOn the second question: I have just explained the relevant situation regarding the decision of the National People's Congress to improve the electoral system of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. We hope that relevant Taiwan parties and figures can view the relevant measures for improving the electoral system of the Hong Kong SAR objectively and pragmatically, set aside prejudice, and distinguish right from wrong.\nThat concludes today's press conference. Tomorrow we will release article-by-article interpretation materials on the “22 measures for agriculture and forestry” to help everyone further understand these measures. We also hope everyone will continue to follow the implementation of the relevant measures and work together to enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210317_12339172.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 17 — On March 16, a serious traffic accident occurred on the Suhua Highway in Yilan, Taiwan, when a tour bus carrying 45 people crashed into a mountain wall, killing 6 people and injuring 39. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said: We are deeply saddened by this accident. We mourn the Taiwan compatriots who died in the tragedy and extend our sincere condolences to the families of the victims and to the injured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210317_12339202.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 19 — Qiu Guozheng, head of Taiwan's defense department, recently boasted, “The mainland can fight as long as it wants, and we will accompany it for as long as it fights,” which drew mockery from Taiwan netizens. In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 19th, when asked by reporters, that some people in the DPP authorities have spoken wildly, once again exposing the boundless provocations of the “Taiwan independence” forces. They think that colluding with external forces allows them to “seek independence by force,” but this runs against the fundamental interests and overall interests of the Chinese nation; it is entirely a case of being blinded by self-interest. Such words and deeds, relying on foreign powers to bolster oneself and whistling to embolden oneself, are no different from quenching thirst with poison.\nShe said that Taiwan is part of China. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is a common obligation of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. In response to interference by external forces and a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. Doing so is by no means directed at Taiwan compatriots; rather, it safeguards the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that history has long proven that “Taiwan independence” is a dead-end road that cannot be traveled. If the DPP authorities dare to take desperate risks, wagering the well-being of compatriots on both sides and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait, they will surely face devastating failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210319_12339683.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","BEIJING, March 19 (Xinhua) — After the mainland introduced the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” several departments of the DPP authorities made outrageous remarks and maliciously attacked them. In response, Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 19th that the DPP authorities' attempt to block the path by which Taiwan compatriots seek development and well-being is bound to fail. They cannot block the opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to achieve better and greater development in the vast expanse of the mainland, nor can they block the room for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to seize mainland development opportunities and enhance their interests and well-being, and they certainly cannot block the historical trend of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer to each other.\nZhu Fenglian said that the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” are a concrete step to implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee and advance the implementation of the “14th Five-Year Plan.” They further provide equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to take part in high-quality development of agriculture and forestry on the mainland and in rural revitalization, which will deepen cross-Strait agricultural and forestry cooperation and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The measures have received a warm response from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that it is not surprising that the DPP authorities attack and smear the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry.” Their consistent logic is that whenever the mainland introduces something beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, they oppose it across the board, and whatever benefits the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they set out to oppose. The reason they do this is that they fear that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will obtain tangible benefits from the development opportunities of the mainland, and thereby see through their political nature and deceptive tactics, and further resist their schemes to create cross-Strait confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210319_12339684.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Chiu Tai-san, Chair of the Mainland Affairs Council, said on the 18th that he calls on the mainland to “abandon the political framework and confrontational measures imposed on Taiwan,” to respect each other, and to resolve problems through pragmatic dialogue. He also said that the “1992 Consensus” has already caused controversy in Taiwan, and that the mainland's continued insistence on this political precondition…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 20: TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 20th: Compatriots on both sides of the Strait see very clearly that the DPP authorities, on the one hand, adopting a conciliatory posture, and on the other hand, continuing to confront the mainland, simply will not work. Only by taking practical actions, stopping the creation of hostility and slander, stopping any provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” and returning to the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully and stably.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” was reached through negotiations authorized by the relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, and its process and content have clear documents and written records. On the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides of the Strait launched consultations and negotiations and opened the road of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Facts have proven that the “1992 Consensus,” confirmed by both sides of the Strait and enjoying broad public support, is the “Divine Needle that Steadies the Sea” for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nZhu Fenglian said that after the DPP came to power in 2016, it unilaterally negated the “1992 Consensus” and refused to acknowledge its core meaning, deliberately stirring up controversy on the island. Its purpose is to attempt to change the legal and factual reality that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and to change the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in cross-Strait relations. The importance of the “1992 Consensus” lies in the fact that it embodies the one-China principle, clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations, and lays the foundation for equal consultations between the two sides. Since 1992, the contacts and exchanges between the two sides of the Strait have all been conducted on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” fully reflecting the spirit of equal consultation. How could there be “unfairness” or “injustice”? If one were to deny that both sides of the Strait belong to one China through so-called “constructive ambiguity,” that would only prove that the DPP authorities still intend to obscure the focus and confuse the public through word games and double-dealing. They have no sincerity at all in improving cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210320_12339798.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-22","Hua Chunying","CCTV","The high-level strategic dialogue between China and the United States concluded last weekend. How do you evaluate the outcome of the dialogue? Do you believe the dialogue has achieved desired goals?","China's attendance at the high-level strategic dialogue at the invitation of the U.S. side in Anchorage is an important step to implement the consensus reached by the two heads of state in their telephone conversation, and the dialogue was decided by the two presidents personally. The Chinese side already issued readouts on that. After the talks concluded, Director Yang Jiechi and State Councilor Wang Yi gave an interview to the press.\nDuring the dialogue, the two sides conducted candid, in-depth, long and constructive communication on domestic and foreign policies, China-U.S. relations and major international and regional issues of common concern. The dialogue is timely, helpful and deepens mutual understanding.\nFirst, the two sides agreed to follow the spirit of the telephone conversation between the two presidents to maintain dialogue and communication, conduct mutually beneficial cooperation, avoid misunderstanding and misjudgment, forestall conflict and confrontation, and promote sound and steady development of China-U.S. relations. Both sides expressed readiness to continue such high-level strategic communication.\nSecond, China has made clear its firm position on issues concerning its sovereignty, security and development interests, which we believe the U.S. side understands more clearly. The Chinese side has unequivocally stated that sovereignty and territorial integrity are major issues of principle. The United States should never underestimate China's resolve to defend its sovereignty, security and development interests and the Chinese people's determination to uphold national dignity and legitimate rights and interests. We hope that the U.S. side will work with China toward the same direction, and we need to respect and accommodate each other's core interests and major concerns in particular. The United States reiterated its adherence to the one-China policy on the Taiwan question.\nBesides, the two sides had discussions on cooperation and other issues in specific areas and reached consensuses including stepping up dialogue and cooperation on climate change by establishing a joint working group on climate change. The two sides discussed making reciprocal arrangements for the COVID-19 vaccination of each side's diplomats and consular officials, agreed to hold talks on facilitating activities of each other's diplomatic and consular missions and personnel, as well as on issues related to media reporters, in the spirit of reciprocity and mutual benefit. The two sides also agreed to maintain and enhance communication and coordination on other topics, including economy and trade, military, law enforcement, culture, health, cyber security, climate change, the Iranian nuclear issue, Afghanistan, the Korean Peninsula and Myanmar, etc.\nI want to stress that China's attitude toward China-U.S. relations remains clear and consistent. China is committed to achieving non-conflict, non-confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation with the United States. At the same time, we are firm in safeguarding our sovereignty, security and development interests. We hope that the United States will work with us toward the same direction, and it's particularly important for us to respect and accommodate each other's core interests and major concerns. On this basis, China's door is always open for continued dialogue with the U.S. side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347008.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210322_9171231.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","After the US-China high-level strategic dialogue, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council claimed that “Taiwan has never belonged to the People's Republic of China; only the people of Taiwan have the right to decide its future and development.” What comment do you have? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","XINHUA, Beijing, March 22 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 22nd, saying: Although the Taiwan Strait has not yet been reunified, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and are not to be divided. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people, and matters involving China's sovereignty and territorial integrity must be decided by all Chinese people. The DPP authorities' attempt to swap concepts and engage in provocations seeking “independence” is very dangerous. If they do not repent, they will surely reap what they have sown.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Adhering to the One-China principle is a common consensus of the international community. This historical fact and legal basis cannot be changed by anyone or any force.\nZhu Fenglian said that the motherland must be and will certainly be reunified; this is an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan's compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. We will continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots in advancing peaceful development, integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210322_12340124.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, Chiu Tai-san (邱太三), head of the Mainland Affairs Council, put forward “three appeals” on “the greatest common denominator for maintaining ‘peace, stability and development’ across the Taiwan Strait at this stage.” What comments do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian (朱凤莲) made the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 23 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 23rd, said that if the DPP authorities truly respect the “existing facts and political foundation,” they should return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” If, on the one hand, they glibly talk about “mutual ‘respect’ and ‘pragmatic’ dialogue to solve problems,” while on the other hand they continue to deliberately evade the “1992 Consensus,” distort the “1992 Consensus” as a “political framework imposed on Taiwan,” and thereby deny that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, this is nothing but a two-faced maneuver to divert attention, mislead public opinion and deceive the world.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” embodies the historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations. Since 1992, the dialogues and negotiations conducted by both sides on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” have fully reflected the spirit of equal consultation, pragmatically resolved specific problems in cross-Strait exchanges, enhanced the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and safeguarded the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations.\nZhu Fenglian said that differences in systems across the two sides are not an excuse for separatism. In recent years, the DPP authorities have colluded with external forces and continuously engaged in provocations to seek “Taiwan independence.” Some politicians have recklessly attacked and smeared the mainland, created hostility, and published “Taiwan independence” remarks, escalating cross-Strait confrontation. This is the root cause of the current turbulence in cross-Strait relations. The necessary measures we take to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity are not directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. They are entirely aimed at curbing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and at safeguarding the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The DPP authorities, using “differences in cross-Strait systems and values” as a pretext, rely on foreign powers to bolster their own position and provoke confrontation. Regardless of the cost to the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and at the expense of the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, they will inevitably be condemned by the entire Chinese people.\nZhu Fenglian said that since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic, the DPP authorities have unilaterally suspended mainland residents’ travel to Taiwan, closed the “mini three links” between Kinmen and Matsu and Fujian, and extensively canceled cross-Strait direct flight routes. This has seriously affected personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields across the Strait, and has seriously harmed the legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. The series of discriminatory and political restrictive measures adopted by the DPP authorities are fundamentally different in nature from the epidemic prevention measures taken by the mainland to protect the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. At present, compatriots on both sides of the Strait look forward to restoring personnel exchanges across the Strait and expanding and deepening economic and cultural exchanges. What the DPP authorities should do is stop using the epidemic and other issues for political manipulation, and remove restrictive measures that obstruct the travel of compatriots across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210323_12340470.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-24","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","There's an official statement from Paraguay that said that some people offered the government there access to Chinese-made vaccines in exchange for Paraguay agreeing to shift its diplomatic recognition from Taiwan to the PRC. The statement said that it's unclear if those people were acting on behalf of the PRC government. Can you confirm that? And do you have any other comments on this?","I don't know where you got this information. I would like to point out that vaccines bring hope for saving lives. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, China has remained committed to building a community with a shared future for mankind and a global community of health for all. China is among the first to pledge that vaccines will be made a global public good and to act on that, and has worked hard to make vaccines accessible and affordable in developing countries. At the request of some countries, China has provided help to them on vaccines. Relevant cooperation has been open and aboveboard.\nAs for what you mentioned about Paraguay, it is a typical example of malicious disinformation. I understand that some people in Taiwan have made some petty moves behind the scenes. I would like to take this opportunity to stress that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. This is not only a historical and legal fact, but also a consensus of the international community. We urge those in Taiwan to stop political manipulation or slander in any form, as all these attempts are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202103/t20210324_9170712.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210324_9171233.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A U.S. Department of Defense website recently published an article containing the phrase “Taiwan is not part of China.” The DPP authorities have also echoed this. May I ask for comment? Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the relevant U.S. remarks are completely wrong, and at the same time made the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 24 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 24th: Taiwan is part of China. The Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all of China. This is the common understanding of the international community. We urge the US government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question with prudence. The DPP authorities challenge the one-China principle; they overestimate themselves, and their attempt will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210324_12340647.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 24 (Electric). In response to the DPP authorities' slander that the mainland used vaccine issues to pressure Paraguay into severing 'diplomatic ties' with Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 24th in response to questions that the one-China principle is the broad consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities' conduct of promoting 'two Chinas,' 'one China, one Taiwan,' and 'Taiwan independence' internationally has no way out.\nZhu said that on vaccine issues, we have consistently advocated making vaccines a public good that people in all countries can use and afford, and we have provided vaccines or carried out vaccine cooperation with many countries in need through practical actions. We oppose politicizing vaccine issues. The DPP authorities are a thief crying 'stop the thief,' which will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210324_12340658.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-03-25","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","This year marks the 100th anniversary of the founding of the CPC. President Xi Jinping attended a recent launch meeting of the campaign on Party history learning and education, and delivered an important speech. A few days ago, the CMC issued the Circular on Launching a Campaign of Party History Learning and Education in the Military. What are your arrangements for this campaign?","In the recent Circular on Launching a Campaign of Party Learning and Education in the Military, the CMC rolls out the overall arrangements for launching a Party learning and education campaign in the military. The Circular highlights the devotion to the Party, the nation, and socialism, emphasizes the Party’s absolute leadership over the people’s military, focuses on the military’s centenary goal, and aims to strengthen the conviction of our officers and soldiers to obey the Party’s order and follow the Party’s lead under the banner of the Party.\nFirst, we will strengthen theoretical studies. The campaign will involve all officers and soldiers. It will be organized by military units at and above regiment level through events such as learning sessions of the theoretical study groups of the Party committees and officer theoretical workshops. And military universities and colleges will highlight relevant contents in their curriculums.\nSecond, we will offer courses and guidance. The CPC and the Communist Youth League organizations at all levels will hold themed sessions of their semimonthly institutional events on Party history learning and education, put on lectures in the period around July 1, the CPC Founding Day, present microlectures and MOOCs online, and carry out publicity and cultural activities including ceremonies and study tours.\nThird, we will deliver thematic briefings. Expert teams will be sent on lecture tours across the military to offer targeted and face-to-face guidance.\nFourth, we will connect learning and education with practice. We will translate the results of the campaign into greater efforts to accomplish our fundamental purpose of serving the people wholeheartedly, effectively fulfill the missions and tasks of the armed forces in the new era, and approach key and tough issues in promoting capabilities and readiness. Measures will be adopted to address the realistic concerns of our service members such as their promotion and career development, family members’ employment, and children’s education. And we will continue to provide active support for economic and social development, consolidate and expand the achievements in poverty alleviation, and brave urgent, difficult, hazardous, and arduous tasks including emergency rescue and disaster relief.\nFifth, we will hold themed discussions. Formal themed discussions in various forms will be held by Party organizations at all levels in their quarterly or semiannual institutional events with a view to encouraging greater dedication to the Party through history learning, experience sharing and honest criticism.\nThe Circular stressed that units at all levels should view the campaign as a major political task and secure tangible results through effective organization and leadership.\nThe history of the CPC is the most vivid and convincing textbook. In the modern history of China, there used to be various political parties and organizations. Most of them were wiped out by the tide of history. Why is the CPC the only one capable of undertaking the important task of wining independence and rejuvenation of the Chinese nation? In its early days, the CPC was once short in experience and did not recognize the importance of having its own armed force. In 1927 when the Kuomintang reactionaries betrayed the revolution, a large number of unarmed Party members and revolutionary public were brutally murdered. The CPC learned a hard lesson that it could not defeat the armed reactionaries or lead the revolution in China unless it had an armed force loyal to the revolution. On August 1, 1927, the CPC fired the first shot against the Kuomintang reactionaries in Nanchang. The Nanchang Uprising marked the beginning of the Party’s independent leadership of the revolutionary war, the founding of the people’s military, and the drive to seize state power with military force. Six days after the uprising, the CPC Central Committee held an emergency meeting in Hankou, Hubei province, known as the August 7th Meeting, and identified the Agrarian Revolution and armed resistance to the Kuomintang reactionaries as the overarching policy. This was the right conclusion that the Party reached at the cost of blood. After the meeting, the CPC led a series of armed uprisings such as the Autumn Harvest Uprising and the Guangzhou Uprising, and gradually embarked on the revolutionary path of using rural areas to encircle the cities and seizing state power with military force. The spark of the Chinese revolution spread across the entire country like wildfire. In 1949, 22 years after the Nanchang Uprising, the People’s Republic of China was founded. History has fully proved that there would not be a new China without the CPC. Upholding the Party’s absolute leadership over the people’s military is a distinctive feature of socialism with Chinese characteristics, an important political advantage of the Party and the country, and the foundation for building a strong military. This is a principle not to be altered and a tradition not to be discarded.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-03/28/content_4882173.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-03-25","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that US Navy Adm. Philip Davidson claimed that the Chinese mainland could settle the Taiwan question within six years and supplant the US’s leadership by 2050. Adm. John Aquilino, nominated to become commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, said the biggest concern in the Indo-Pacific region was a military takeover of Taiwan by the Chinese mainland. What’s your comment on that?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, which brooks no outside interference. The great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and complete reunification of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are inevitable. Any attempt by external forces to “contain China with the Taiwan question” or by “Taiwan independence” forces to seek “independence by force” will be a dead end.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation for China-US relations. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and properly handle the Taiwan question. We resolutely oppose the US side hyping the so-called “military threats from China”. The US side should abandon its zero-sum mindset, view China’s national and defense development in an objective and rational way, and do more to promote mutual trust between the two countries and contribute to regional peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-03/28/content_4882173.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-03-25","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The website of US Department of Defense recently published an article on the situation in the Indo-Pacific region, in which the expression of so-called “Taiwan was never part of China” appeared. Please comment on that.","The expression by the US side seriously breached the one-China principle and sent a wrong message to the “Taiwan independence” separatists. Such expression is egregious. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to that.\nThe historical and legal facts that Taiwan is a part of China and both sides across the Taiwan Strait belong to one China can never be altered by anyone or any force. The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China. It bears on China’s core interests and brooks no outside forces’ interference in any form. The PLA is determined to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests.\nThe Chinese side urges the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US Joint Communiqués, and prudently and properly handle the Taiwan question, so as to avoid severe damage to the relations between the two countries and militaries and further jeopardizing the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-03/28/content_4882173.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2021-03-26","Hua Chunying","The Paper","On March 25, the US House Foreign Affairs Committee adopted a bill to direct the Secretary of State to develop a strategy to regain observer status for Taiwan in the World Health Organization, asking the Secretary of State to give an account of the changes and improvements made to the United States plan to endorse and obtain observer status for Taiwan at the World Health Assembly. I wonder if you have a comment?","The US bill is a serious breach of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques. It runs counter to international law and basic norms governing international relations. China rejects it. According to UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1, the participation of China's Taiwan region in WHO events must be handled following the one-China principle. Based on this principle, the Central Government of China has made proper arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and the core content of the three China-US joint communiques. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, comply with international law and basic norms governing international relations, stop reviewing and pushing the negative Taiwan-related bill, not to send out wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces and not to help the Taiwan region to expand its so-called \"international space\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347012.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210326_9171235.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-26","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","The US and Taiwan have reached an agreement for their coast guards to cooperate. They signed a memorandum of understanding yesterday. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","China's position on US-Taiwan interactions is clear and consistent. We ask the US to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three Sino-US communiques, stop official exchanges and military interactions with Taiwan and be prudent on Taiwan-related issues. We also ask Taiwan not to try to add to its importance by soliciting US support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347012.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210326_9171235.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-26","Hua Chunying","","据报道，3月25日，美国会众院外委会审议通过了“要求美国国务卿制定战略使台湾重获世界卫生组织观察员地位”议案。该案要求美国务卿就其调整改进旨在支持台获得世卫大会观察员地位的方案作出说明。请问中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347012.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210326_9171235.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2021-03-26","Hua Chunying","","周四，法国总统马克龙在欧盟视频峰会上称，欧洲在疫苗领域正面临一场新“世界战争”，造成这种情况的原因有很多，其中就包括中国、俄罗斯利用疫苗扩大全球影响力。中方对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347012.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210326_9171235.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2021-03-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Recently, a former head of the DPP authorities’ defense department claimed at a video seminar that “Taiwan is a country.” Ip Lai-yuk-yee (Regina Ip), a Hong Kong SAR Legislative Council member who attended, immediately issued a stern rebuttal, and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan commented on it. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 26: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 26th, pointed out that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory. This is an iron-clad fact and a common consensus of the international community, and it brooks no challenge. Zhu Fenglian said that Regina Ip, a member of the Legislative Council of the Hong Kong SAR, immediately offered a forceful rebuttal on the spot, voicing the sound of justice. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. The DPP authorities, stubbornly refusing to wake up, disregarding facts and deceiving the Taiwan people, will ultimately face utter failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210326_12341068.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 26 — In response to the so-called “memorandum on establishing a coast guard working group” signed on the 26th by the American Institute in Taiwan and the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions the same day, said: We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between Taiwan and the United States, or the signing of any agreement with sovereignty implications.\nZhu Fenglian said that on the question of national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, it must be pointed out that safeguarding the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation is a shared responsibility of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ “relying on the United States to seek independence” and selling out national interests will only drive Taiwan toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210326_12341108.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-29","Zhao Lijian","NHK","First, over 100 protesters were killed in Myanmar the day before yesterday. The UN Special Rapporteur for Myanmar called on Myanmar's military to stop killing civilians. Do you have any comment? Second, Palau's President arrived in Taiwan for a visit yesterday and he is supposed to meet with Tsai Ing-wen. What's your response?","On your first question, we are concerned about the situation in Myanmar. As we have said on many occasions, we hope all parties in Myanmar can keep calm, exercise restraint, and take actions with a constructive attitude to deescalate and cool down the situation. Violence and bloodshed serve no one's interests, and it is the people of Myanmar who suffer. We hope that all parties will bear in mind the fundamental interests of the people of Myanmar, continue to exert efforts to ease tensions through dialogue and consultation, address disputes and differences within the constitutional and legal framework, and continue to push forward the process of democratic transition in the country.\nOn your second question, we noticed that US Ambassador to Palau is also among the delegation members. I want to stress that the one-China principle is a universally recognized norm for international relations and a common consensus recognized, accepted and practiced by the vast majority of countries in the world. Following the one-China principle is the overriding trend with popular support. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. China firmly opposes any form of official interactions between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the US side to fully recognize that the Taiwan question is highly sensitive, and that it should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. It must stop any official interaction with Taiwan, refrain from sending any wrong signals to Taiwan independent forces, stop any attempt to cross the bottom line, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, lest it should damage China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347013.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202103/t20210329_9171236.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","In response to the mainland consumer boycott triggered by H&M’s groundless refusal to use Xinjiang cotton, several DPP figures and their authorities have made comments, falsely claiming that “the mainland has long suppressed the thoughts, beliefs and freedoms of the Uyghur people in Xinjiang, will closely watch the human rights situation on the mainland, will refer to the practices of the international community,…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 29: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 29th, saying that the DPP authorities, relying on lies and false information fabricated by external anti-China forces, are following the crowd in smearing and slandering the mainland. This is extremely malicious, and we firmly oppose it.\nZhu Fenglian said that over the past 60-plus years, the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region has comprehensively implemented the Party's ethnic policies, resolutely implemented the system of regional ethnic autonomy, and worked hard to promote the unity, joint struggle, and common prosperity and development of all ethnic groups. According to statistics, from 2010 to 2018, Xinjiang's permanent resident population rose from 21.8158 million to 24.8676 million, an increase of 13.99%. Among them, the Uyghur population rose from 10.1715 million to 12.7184 million, an increase of 25.04%, clearly higher than the population growth rate of Xinjiang as a whole. In 2020, Xinjiang's gross regional product was RMB 1,379.758 billion, growing 3.4% year on year, 1.1 percentage points higher than the national figure. Cotton output was 5.162 million tonnes, accounting for 87.3% of the national total, and the comprehensive level of mechanization exceeded 80%. Laborers of all ethnic groups in Xinjiang freely choose their occupations on an equal and voluntary basis, and their rights to labor remuneration, rest and leave, labor safety and health protection, and social insurance and welfare are protected in accordance with the law. Their rights and interests in religious belief, ethnic culture, and language and script are likewise respected and safeguarded in accordance with the law.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that external anti-China forces have concocted the rumors of “forced labor” and “genocide” in order to smear the image of the mainland, undermine Xinjiang's security and stability, and obstruct the mainland's development. They bring up cotton as a pretext, but their true intentions lie elsewhere. This is a smear with no bottom line. They selectively forget the dirty and sinful history of profiting from the brutal exploitation of laboring people, including American slaves, to obtain bloody cotton profits, and they selectively ignore the serious racial discrimination in their own society today, yet they solemnly fabricate lies to smear others. This is utterly absurd.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities are doing their utmost to cooperate with anti-China forces in a clumsy performance with ulterior motives. This is no surprise and once again fully exposes their long-standing tricks: whenever matters involving the mainland arise, they maliciously manipulate and attack and smear. We advise the DPP authorities: rather than going to great lengths to follow the crowd and hype, or even threatening Taiwan people who speak out for justice, they would do better to pay attention to the livelihood hardships of the island's people, such as water shortages and drought and the long wait for vaccines, and to reflect on their own reckless conduct of raising a cyber army, controlling public opinion, and attacking dissenters. Fabricating lies cannot solve problems, nor can it divert attention. Stoking hostility to please external anti-China forces is a completely misguided calculation.\nZhu Fenglian said that we believe Taiwan compatriots who respect facts and have a sense of justice will see through the schemes of external anti-China forces, and will see Xinjiang's geographic advantages in jointly building the “Belt and Road” and the development opportunities it offers to Taiwan compatriots. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to visit Xinjiang for tourism, and to invest and start businesses, and to experience the real Xinjiang of prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210329_12341656.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-03-30","Hua Chunying","Reuters","According to a report from the Financial Times, the US is preparing to issue guidelines that would make it easier for US diplomats to meet Taiwanese officials. Do you have any comment on this?","With regard to US-Taiwan interactions, China's position is clear and consistent. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the US and China's Taiwan region. We hope the US side will attach high importance to China's concerns and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues to avoid further harming China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347014.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1865482.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-03-31","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","I have two questions. First, WHO's Director General has said the virus probe didn't adequately analyze the possibility of a lab accident before deciding that it's most likely the pathogen spread from bats to humans via another animal. In a briefing to member countries yesterday he said he is ready to deploy additional missions involving specialist experts. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this? My…","On your first question, the Chinese side has mad clear its position on the origin-tracing study report released by WHO. China has taken note of the report released by WHO. We commend the Chinese and international experts who have taken part in this joint study for their commitment to science, tireless industry and professionalism.\nChina has always been a supporter for global scientific research on the source of the virus and its transmission routes. We co-sponsored the WHA resolution on COVID-19 and support WHO-led cooperation on zoonotic source research among member states. Despite the daunting task of domestic prevention and control, China twice invited WHO experts in for study of origins. The Chinese side offered necessary facilitation for the team's work, fully demonstrating its openness, transparency and responsible attitude.\nStudy of origins is a matter of science, which should be jointly conducted by scientists all over the world. To politicize this issue will only severely hinder global cooperation in study of origins, jeopardize anti-pandemic cooperation, and cost more lives. It would run counter to the international community's aspiration for solidarity against the virus.\nStudy of origins is also a global mission that should be conducted in multiple countries and localities. We believe the joint WHO-China study will effectively stimulate global cooperation in origin-tracing.\nAs to your remarks that Director-General Tedros said the possibility of lab leak cannot be completely ruled out and they need further study, I want to say that in the China-WHO COVID-19 origin-tracing joint study, experts of the joint mission made field trips to institutions including the Hubei Provincial Center for Disease Control, the Wuhan Center for Disease Control and the Wuhan Institute of Virology, and visited biosafety laboratories and had in-depth and candid exchanges with experts there. Through these field trips and in-depth visits, members of the mission unanimously agreed that the allegation of lab leaking is extremely unlikely, and this is an important scientific conclusion made clear in the joint study report released this time.\nI want to stress that China is conducting joint scientific research on origin-tracing with the WHO at the request of the latter. All parties should respect science and the opinion and conclusion of scientists. The WHO, in particular, should set a good example in this regard.\nAs for the question of further research, I think you may also note that in the video press conference of the WHO mission, the experts said that there has always been speculation about lab leak, but after earnest study in China, no suspicious signs have been found. They took a detailed look at the management of the laboratory, its working practices and recent virus research, and concluded that a \"lab leak\" was \"extremely unlikely\". They added that work could be done with laboratories around the world if there is further evidence that the hypothesis needs to be reassessed.\nAs I said yesterday, there is always a question mark over lab leak. The expert team had an in-depth study in Wuhan, and we also know there are many reports of early outbreaks various in many places around the world. In addition to Fort Detrick, certain country has more than 200 biological bases around the world. So I think, if necessary, scientists should be allowed to work in a scientific spirit with relevant laboratories around the world. We hope that other relevant countries will cooperate closely with WHO experts in a scientific, open, transparent and responsible manner, as China has done. We believe this serves the interest of the world. Because everyone wants answers so that we can better respond to similar public health crises in the future.\nAs to your second question, are you referring to BBC correspondent John Sudworth who has left China's mainland?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347015.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1865908.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 31, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Please begin your questions.\nChina Huayi Broadcasting Corporation: General Secretary Xi Jinping recently stated during an inspection in Fujian, “We must highlight promoting integration through exchanges, promoting integration through benefits, and promoting integration through emotional connection, and boldly explore new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.” How will this be implemented?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Deepening cross-Strait integrated development is a major policy proposition regarding Taiwan put forward by General Secretary Xi Jinping. It points the way for us to advance national reunification from the new era and on the great journey of national rejuvenation. We conscientiously implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on work regarding Taiwan, adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, treat Taiwan compatriots equally, serve Taiwan compatriots in the same way we serve mainland residents, vigorously promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, support Fujian in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development, and have achieved positive progress.\nWe will thoroughly implement the important speech spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping during his inspection in Fujian, actively promote the integrated development of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait through connectivity, benefits, and emotional bonds, and continuously deepen peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations:\nIn promoting integration through connectivity, we will continuously enhance cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, infrastructure connectivity, energy and resource interconnection, and common industry standards, promote water, electricity, gas, and bridge connections between Kinmen and Matsu and the coastal areas of Fujian, and actively advance the connection of everything that can be connected across the Strait.\nIn promoting integration through benefits, we will continuously implement and carry out the \"31 Measures,\" \"26 Measures,\" \"11 Measures,\" \"Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures\" and other policy measures that benefit Taiwan and its people, improve the system and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland, and support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the \"14th Five-Year Plan\" and integrating into the new development pattern, so that Taiwan compatriots can share more new development opportunities.\nIn promoting integration through emotional bonds, we will continuously expand cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, jointly inherit and develop the outstanding traditional Chinese culture, strengthen exchanges between grassroots communities and young people across the Strait, and promote heart-to-heart connection among compatriots.\nWe support Fujian in fully leveraging its unique advantages in cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, taking the lead in pilot reforms, continuously exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development, and building the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises coming to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342243.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","MAC Chairperson Chiu Tai-san said recently that the MAC would evaluate phased resumption of cross-Strait personnel and transport exchanges, including humanitarian visits by mainland residents to relatives in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's response?","Regarding the Mainland Affairs Council’s claim that it will assess resuming cross-Strait personnel and transport exchanges, including humanitarian family visits by mainland residents, we should listen to what it says, but even more so watch what it does.\nSince the COVID-19 outbreak, cross-Strait personnel exchanges have suffered unprecedented impact. From February 2020 to the present, the DPP authorities have unilaterally banned mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, closed the “mini three links” between Kinmen, Matsu and Fujian, and extensively cancelled cross-Strait direct flight points. Many children of cross-Strait marriage families and mainland spouses have been treated unfairly.\nThe various blocking measures adopted by the DPP authorities have seriously affected cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields, and have also created many difficulties and obstacles for Taiwan compatriots traveling back and forth across the Strait. This is the direct and main cause of the obstruction of normal cross-Strait personnel exchanges. Judging from the remarks and conduct of the DPP authorities regarding people since the epidemic, the motives behind these obstructive measures are plain to see. Their most urgent task is to immediately correct course.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Chiu Tai-san, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, said a few days ago that both sides of the Strait should actively implement existing agreements and, through agreement mechanisms, communicate and handle matters that affect public health and safety, such as epidemic prevention, health, and agricultural product quarantine and inspection. May I ask what attitude the mainland side takes on this?","Our position has always been very clear. We have consistently worked to strengthen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, establish a stable cross-Strait economic cooperation mechanism, and safeguard the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nFrom 2008 to 2016, the two sides signed 23 agreements on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" After the DPP authorities came to power in May 2016, they refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" and unilaterally undermined the common political foundation across the Strait, causing the cross-Strait liaison and communication mechanisms to stall and affecting the implementation of cross-Strait agreements, which is something compatriots on both sides do not wish to see. In recent times, although the DPP authorities have repeatedly claimed that they hope for \"reconciliation\" and \"dialogue\" across the Strait, in reality they have tried every means to pursue \"Taiwan independence,\" intensified collusion with external forces to \"rely on foreign powers to seek independence,\" and made extravagant remarks on issues involving Hong Kong and Xinjiang, maliciously attacking and provoking the mainland and creating confrontation across the Strait. Is this \"reconciliation\"?\nWe adhere to the people-centered development philosophy. We attach great importance to and act responsibly on important matters concerning the health and safety of the people on both sides of the Strait, respond and handle them promptly and properly, and do our utmost to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. If the DPP authorities truly cared about the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, they should take concrete actions, return to the political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" and stop shooting off empty cannons, which cannot solve any problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342234.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","We note that Taiwan’s agricultural authorities claimed that, regarding the nonconformity of Taiwan’s pineapples, they received only 13 notifications, not the 28 the mainland mentioned. As for the pests found on the pineapples, the mainland has also not provided scientific evidence. What is your response?","We are also continuously following the issue of the mainland's suspension of pineapple imports from Taiwan. In 2020, the mainland authorities notified the Taiwan side in writing of 28 batches of pineapples that were found non-compliant. Of these, 14 batches were found to contain Diaspidiotus (Aspidiotus) cistudiphagus-type scale insects; we specially obtained some images from the relevant departments, which we can show everyone. This is the pest found on pineapples, and this is the Diaspidiotus scale insect magnified 50 times. In addition, 8 batches were Pseudococcus (Dysmicoccus) pests, which is this kind of pest (image shown), and 6 batches were Pseudococcus neopinearum pests (image shown). The Taiwan side has never provided any reply, and the non-compliance has not been improved. Among the Taiwan pineapples declared to mainland customs at the beginning of this year, another 5 batches were found to contain Diaspidiotus scale insects. These are the notification letters and inspection reports for the 28 batches provided by the relevant departments (shown), every single one of which is well documented.\nThe DPP authorities should genuinely take on their regulatory responsibility, resolve the relevant problems at the source, and stop engaging in political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342235.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","NASA recently launched a “Mars Ticket” campaign online, and its official website listed “Taiwan” separately as a “country,” provoking a boycott by mainland netizens. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","I believe many netizens are following this matter. Our position is very clear: Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The relevant practice of the U.S. National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, violates the general consensus of the international community, and also hurts the feelings of the Chinese people. We hope that NASA, as an agency of the U.S. federal government, will respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and correct the relevant mistakes as soon as possible.\nWe also believe that Chinese people at home and abroad will have a correct understanding of this matter.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342230.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Recently, a U.S. senator proposed the so-called “Taiwan Relations Reinforcement” bill, which requires that the head of the American Institute in Taiwan be upgraded to “ambassador” level. In addition, a U.S. lawmaker has proposed advocating for including Taiwan as a member of the so-called “NATO+.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US Joint Communiqués, and to properly handle the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities have for a long time, by all means, tried to win over some US lawmakers to fabricate various Taiwan-related bills in service of their “Taiwan independence” schemes. Such trickery will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Some in the KMT have proposed that the “1992 Consensus” needs to keep pace with the times. KMT Chairman Jiang Qichen said that keeping pace with the times at this stage means the “1992 Consensus” based on the “Constitution of the Republic of China.” May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","The core essence of the \"1992 Consensus\" is \"both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and jointly strive to seek national reunification.\" This must not be blurred or changed at any time.\nOver the years, the reason the \"1992 Consensus\" has been able to play an important positive role in cross-Strait relations lies in both sides abiding by it. Any practice that highlights differences is not conducive to upholding the consensus or allowing it to play its positive role, and will not be recognized by compatriots on both sides. Taking a long-term view, recognizing the trend of the times, and adhering to the correct direction and policies is the responsible course for oneself, for cross-Strait relations, and for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342233.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's head of the executive authority, Su Tseng-chang, recently said that the mainland's “22 measures for agriculture and forestry,” “in name benefit Taiwan, in fact benefit China,” and have “political purposes.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The purpose of issuing the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” is to further provide equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises participating in high-quality development of agriculture and forestry and rural revitalization on the mainland, deepen cross-Strait agricultural and forestry cooperation, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Since the measures were released, relevant departments and localities are working to quickly arrange the implementation of specific tasks, and are also publicizing the relevant measures to local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises through forums, visits and other means. We will strengthen overall coordination and guidance, and push all regions and departments to implement the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” thoroughly and in detail, so that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises genuinely benefit and profit. We also hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will seize the opportunities to achieve better and greater development of their own.\nIt is not surprising at all that the DPP authorities have consistently smeared and attacked the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” and have nothing good to say about them. Their consistent logic is that whenever the mainland introduces something beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, they oppose it across the board; whatever is good for the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they set themselves against. They do this mainly out of fear that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will obtain tangible benefits from development opportunities on the mainland, will see through their political nature and deceptive tactics, and will thereby resist their schemes to create cross-Strait confrontation.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to block the path by which Taiwan compatriots seek development and well-being cannot succeed. They cannot block the opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to achieve better and greater development in the vast expanse of the mainland, nor can they block the room for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to seize mainland development opportunities and raise their interests and well-being. Still less can they block the historical trend of compatriots on both sides drawing closer together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, some Taiwan students took part in the “First Cross-Strait Youth Essay Contest on Good Family Customs and Family Precepts” held in Pingtan and won awards, and their schools commended them. The Mainland Affairs Council said in response that violations of relevant regulations or provisions will be investigated and punished. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Family style and family precepts are an important part of China’s excellent traditional culture and a common spiritual wealth of all Chinese descendants. The essay-writing activity on family style and family precepts held in Pingtan, Fujian, provides a good platform for young people across the Strait to tell stories of family style and family precepts and to demonstrate their literary and moral cultivation. It has been warmly welcomed and enthusiastically joined by young people on both sides. We congratulate the children from both sides who won awards, and we will continue to encourage and support young people across the Strait in carrying out various forms of exchange activities, upholding righteousness, following the right path, and growing up healthily in mutual friendship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Regarding the recent Xinjiang cotton controversy, Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen claimed that “human rights are universal values” and called on the Mainland to stop “oppression” in order to resolve “international doubts and confrontation and conflict.” What is the comment?","We have already stated our position on this before, and today I would like to take a moment to emphasize it again. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, relying on lies and false information fabricated by external anti-China forces, are following suit in smearing and slandering the mainland. This is extremely malicious, and we firmly oppose it.\nSome of the journalist friends present took part in the 2015 \"Belt and Road\" Xinjiang Trip, a cross-Strait joint journalist reporting activity, and have seen and experienced the situation in Xinjiang firsthand. Over the past more than 60 years, the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region has fully implemented the Party's ethnic policies, firmly implemented the system of regional ethnic autonomy, and worked hard to promote solidarity, common struggle, and shared prosperity and development among all ethnic groups. According to statistics, from 2010 to 2018, Xinjiang's permanent resident population rose from 21.8158 million to 24.8676 million, an increase of 13.99%. Among them, the Uyghur population rose from 10.1715 million to 12.7184 million, an increase of 25.04%, clearly higher than the growth rate of the population of Xinjiang as a whole. In 2020, Xinjiang's gross regional product was 1,379.758 billion yuan, growing 3.4% year on year, 1.1 percentage points higher than the national rate. Cotton output was 5.162 million tons, accounting for 87.3% of the national total, and the level of comprehensive mechanization exceeded 80%. Laborers of all ethnic groups in Xinjiang freely choose their occupations on an equal and voluntary basis, and their rights to labor remuneration, rest and leave, labor safety and health protection, and social insurance and welfare are all protected in accordance with the law. Their rights and interests in religious belief, ethnic culture, language, and script are likewise respected and safeguarded in accordance with the law.\nThe rumors about so-called \"forced labor\" and \"genocide\" fabricated by external anti-China forces aim to smear the image of the mainland, disrupt Xinjiang's security and stability, and hold back China's development. They use cotton as a pretext, and their real intention lies elsewhere; this is slander without any bottom line. They selectively forget the shameful history of profiting from the bloody cotton trade by brutally exploiting working people, including Black slaves in the United States, and they selectively ignore the serious racial discrimination in their own society today, yet they solemnly fabricate lies to smear others. This is utterly absurd.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have made crude, scheming attempts to cooperate with anti-China forces. This is hardly surprising, and it once again fully exposes their long-standing tactics: whenever something involves the mainland, they maliciously manipulate and attack it. I advise the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that, rather than taking great pains to follow suit and hype the issue, or even recklessly threatening Taiwanese people who speak up for justice, they should pay more attention to the people's hardships on the island, such as water shortages, drought, and the long wait for vaccines, and should reflect more on their own reckless conduct of keeping an online army, controlling public opinion, and attacking dissenters. Fabricating lies cannot solve problems, nor can it divert attention. Winning favor with external anti-China forces by creating hostility is a serious miscalculation.\nWe believe that compatriots in Taiwan who respect facts and have a sense of justice will see through the schemes of external anti-China forces, and will see Xinjiang's geographic advantages in the joint construction of the \"Belt and Road\" and the development opportunities it offers to Taiwan compatriots. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises to visit Xinjiang as tourists and to invest and start businesses, and to experience the real Xinjiang of prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Taiwan is currently evaluating whether the quarantine period for travelers who have been vaccinated can be reduced from 14 days to 7 days, plus a nucleic acid test. Will the mainland relax its epidemic prevention quarantine measures for Taiwan businesspeople traveling back and forth across the Strait?","We do hope that, under normalized epidemic prevention and control and as vaccination advances, cross-Strait personnel exchanges can gradually return to normal. Epidemic prevention and control can only be pragmatic and wise if it returns to science and professionalism. Regarding the convenience of cross-border travel for people who have been vaccinated, I believe the relevant authorities will study the matter and make unified arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The President of Palau visited Taiwan accompanied by the U.S. Ambassador to Palau. Taiwan says that trilateral relations will become even closer. Foreign media further reported that the U.S. may relax restrictions on official exchanges between U.S. diplomats and Taiwan. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have?","On this issue, our position is consistent and clear: we firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan. We demand that the U.S. side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and properly handle the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities’ stubborn attempt to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” will ultimately fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Recently, the two sides of the Strait have offered different explanations of the “common political foundation.” The mainland emphasizes that the “1992 Consensus” is the sea-anchoring divine needle (定海神针), and that both sides belong to one China, but it has not clearly specified what “China” the “one China” refers to. Internationally, the mainland stresses that “the People's Republic of China is the sole legal…","“One China” means that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will not be allowed to be divided.\nThe “1992 Consensus” embodies the historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and it is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations. Political differences across the Strait must be resolved through dialogue and consultation between the two sides on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","The 27th meeting of the Standing Committee of the 13th National People's Congress deliberated and adopted amendments to Annexes I and II of the Hong Kong Basic Law, and the DPP authorities have offered their opinions on it. What is the comment?","The 27th session of the Standing Committee of the 13th National People's Congress deliberated and adopted the amendments to Annex I and Annex II of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. This provides a solid institutional guarantee for comprehensively and accurately implementing the principle of “one country, two systems” and “patriots administering Hong Kong,” and for ensuring Hong Kong's long-term prosperity and stability.\nOut of sinister “Taiwan independence” intentions, the DPP authorities have consistently twisted right and wrong on Hong Kong issues and maliciously smeared them, aiming to attack “one country, two systems” and attempting to seek “independence” and create chaos in Hong Kong. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop their political manipulation of Hong Kong affairs and withdraw their black hands. Those who seek “independence” and create chaos in Hong Kong will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342231.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Chen Shih-chung recently relented and said he accepts mainland vaccines. For mainland students studying on the island who want to receive mainland vaccines, can the mainland provide assistance?","Regarding vaccination for mainland residents, the free vaccination program for the entire population has now been fully rolled out. Under the relevant community and village arrangements, people can take part in vaccination through WeChat appointments or telephone appointments. Regarding vaccination for Taiwan compatriots in the mainland, it has been included in the unified deployment of the free vaccination program for the entire population, and the relevant policies and specific arrangements will be announced as soon as possible. The question you raised about vaccination for mainland students in Taiwan can be handled through the two approaches above.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","At the press conference on “Xinjiang-related” issues jointly held recently by the Foreign Ministry and the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region government, the mainland side said that Xinjiang is an open region and welcomes foreign media interviews. The spokesperson just also said that Taiwan compatriots and businesses are welcome to travel and sightsee in Xinjiang. Is Taiwan media also welcome to conduct free…","We welcome Taiwan media to report in Xinjiang so that more Taiwan compatriots can objectively and in depth understand Xinjiang. In fact, as early as 2015 we organized media from both sides of the Strait to visit Xinjiang, and three reporters present here took part. In 2019, the China Taiwan Network also organized cross-Strait youths to carry out exchange activities in Xinjiang. If any reporters present have such needs, you may contact us to arrange them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Reports say that on the 26th of this month, 20 sorties of PLA aircraft entered Taiwan's “southwest airspace,” the largest scale in recent times. Some commentary on the island interprets this as targeting the Taiwan-US memorandum on establishing a “Maritime Affairs Working Group.” The US State Department has said it “urges Beijing to stop exerting military, diplomatic, and economic pressure on Taiwan.” What…","Taiwan is part of China’s territory. It is entirely justified for the PLA to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to carry out relevant exercises and drills.\nAmid the still complex and grim situation in the Taiwan Strait, the US side continues to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces with sinister intentions. This both fuels “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and brings more burdens and disasters to the people on the island. In the end, the party that suffers the greatest loss will be Taiwan. We urge the US government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question properly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202103/t20210331_12342232.htm"],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The cross-strait Olympic committees held a sports exchange symposium to exchange views on the 2022 Winter Olympics. It is rumored that the mainland hopes Taiwan will continue to participate under the “Chinese Taipei” name and not join the Western “boycott” camp. What is your comment?","The event you mentioned should refer to the cross-Strait Olympic committees' sports exchange symposium held online yesterday (March 30). As far as we know, this symposium did not discuss the Beijing Winter Olympics.\nI can give you an introduction to this symposium. Since 1997, the Olympic committees on both sides of the Strait have held a cross-Strait sports exchange symposium every year, a practice that has been maintained for many years. The one held online yesterday was the 23rd Cross-Strait Sports Exchange Symposium, attended by the heads of the Olympic committees of both sides and others. At the symposium, the Olympic committees of both sides jointly reviewed the state of cross-Strait sports exchange and cooperation in 2019 and 2020, planned cross-Strait sports exchange activities for 2021, and exchanged views in depth on issues of common concern, such as continuing to maintain the good situation of cross-Strait sports exchange and cooperation. Both sides agreed that in the face of new situations and new challenges, sports circles on both sides of the Strait must strengthen communication and coordination, enhance mutual understanding and trust, improve exchange mechanisms, share development opportunities, and promote steady and far-reaching cross-Strait sports exchange.\nAs for the Winter Olympics issue you mentioned, the two sides did not discuss it at the symposium.\nOn the question of Taiwan's participation in the Winter Olympics, I would like to stress three points. First, we sincerely welcome the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee to send a delegation to the Beijing Winter Olympics, the Hangzhou Asian Games and other series of competitions. Second, within the scope permitted by the rules, we are willing to provide convenience for athletes from the Taiwan region to compete and conduct training outside their home area. Third, regarding the vaccination arrangements for Taiwan athletes, the Chinese Olympic Committee is cooperating with the International Olympic Committee to provide vaccines for participants in the Tokyo Olympics and the Beijing Winter Olympics. This plan includes Taiwan-region athletes participating in the Olympics. We are willing to do our utmost to provide relevant assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","The Taiwan side has proposed that it will gradually resume mainland residents' visits to Taiwan to visit relatives, and that it may recognize mainland vaccines, among other measures. You just said we must “listen to what they say and watch what they do.” Will the mainland regard these measures proposed by Taiwan as positive signals?","As I have just pointed out, the fact that people on both sides of the Strait cannot travel normally is due to the restrictive measures unilaterally introduced by the Taiwan side on the pretext of the epidemic. These unscientific and unreasonable restrictive measures should be adjusted, and inhumane practices should be cancelled.\nI would also like to mention that this spring, Taiwan region has encountered the most severe water shortage problem in decades; several reservoirs are in dire straits, and even Sun Moon Lake has rarely reached its bottom; irrigation for crops and industrial water use have been restricted, and the people's domestic water use has also been greatly affected. We express concern and sympathy to the Taiwan public, hope that the drought will be alleviated as soon as possible, and hope that the relevant parties will take practical measures to combat drought and provide disaster relief to safeguard the production and daily life of the Taiwan public.\nKinmen, which is separated from Fujian only by a strip of water, is also facing the same drought, but thanks to the cross-Strait water supply project completed in August 2018, the living water needs of Kinmen residents have been fully guaranteed. From August 5, 2018 to March 28, 2021, Fujian has provided Kinmen with continuous, stable and high-quality water supply totaling 12.1912 million tons. Since the beginning of this year, in response to the continued drought on the island and in the Kinmen-Matsu area, and to the request from Kinmen's water plant for increased supply in the spring, Fujian raised its average daily water supply to Kinmen from 14,000 tons to 17,100 tons, with a cumulative supply of 1.489 million tons. Kinmen residents no longer suffer distress from difficulties in obtaining water.\nGood cross-Strait relations mean a better Taiwan, and the well-being of the Taiwan public will be even better. We hope that compatriots on both sides will work together, remove obstacles, and continuously enhance common interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202103/t20210331_12342228.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-01","Hua Chunying","The Paper","BBC said on Twitter yesterday that John Sudworth has relocated to Taiwan and he remains their China correspondent. Sudworth also took an interview with BBC. The FCCC criticized China's \"worsening working conditions\" in a statement. Do you have any response?","After the abnormal departure of John Sudworth from China's mainland, some people came together to put on a farce, a textbook example of how to shift the blame to the innocent party by distortion of facts and fallacy of composition.\nFirst, John Sudworth left unceremoniously without notifying the competent Chinese officials or fulfilling any departure procedures required of foreign resident journalists in China. If he was worried about being sued by people in Xinjiang, he should have stayed to face the litigation if he knew for sure he hadn't produced any fake news or rumors. In China, a place with rule of law, no innocent people will be wronged. If he was concerned about his safety, he could have called the police. Relevant Chinese departments protect the safety of foreigners in China. People with a clear conscience have nothing to fear at night. But he chose to run. Why? Why did he leave in such a hurry? What's he worried about? What's he afraid of? There is only one explanation: a guilty conscience.\nAlthough Mr. Sudworth departed without fulfilling the required procedures, we could have left it there. But then he tried to deflect the blame. And he's not doing it alone by posing as a victim, but has also rallied the BBC and the so-called FCCC to issue statements. All this is utterly unacceptable. We must point out that China is the victim when it comes to BBC's disinformation targeting China. In recent years, BBC has fabricated a large amount of immoral fake news and disinformation, especially on COVID-19 and Xinjiang, which has not only caused direct damages to the interests of some people in Xinjiang, but has also cast a severe negative influence on China's national image. China lodged solemn representations over this repeatedly with the BBC, asking it to correct its mistakes and uphold press ethnics to cover China in an objective and just manner. However, John Sudworth, instead of mending his ways and changing course, went from bad to worse. Now they are trying to extort and threaten China with the abrupt departure of Sudworth. Nothing could be more absurd. This only serves to show the character of Mr. Sudworth and how pathetic the time-honored BBC is.\nBesides, according to Article 13 of the Regulations of the People's Republic of China on News Coverage by Permanent Offices of Foreign Media Organizations and Foreign Journalists (Decree of the State Council No. 537) and Section G, Part 1 of the Handbook for Foreign Journalists in China, resident journalists should go through relevant procedures before terminating their posts in China. Mr. Sudworth didn't notify the relevant department or fulfill any due procedure. His Press Card has now expired and he no longer retains the status of a resident journalist.\nSecond, the FCCC statement is a perfect example of giving a one-sided story that distorts facts and blames the innocent party for what one is guilty of.\nFirst of all, the FCCC is an illegal organization, which China has never acknowledged.\nSecond, fewer than half of all foreign correspondents in China are members of the FCCC, which has basically become a small circle of Western correspondents from the US and Europe. And even within this small circle, so far as I know, FCCC statements are always crafted by several board members, while other journalists are kept in the dark.\nThird, the FCCC says nothing about the large amount of assistance and support that China provides to foreign journalists working and reporting in China, but makes complaints from time to time, claiming that the reporting environment in China is deteriorating. Instead of advising against the many false reports by BBC correspondent John Sudworth, FCCC endorses his erroneous acts. It has no sense of right and wrong, and follows no principles.\nFourth, the FCCC statement said that John Sudworth had endured a long period of uncertainty about his ability to raise his family in Beijing, after spending the past two years being kept on a series of short visas valid for only a few months, which the organization claims to reflect the deteriorating environment for foreign journalists. But the fact is that the majority (over 98%) of nearly 500 foreign journalists in China, including the FCCC board members, are granted press cards with one-year duration. Many foreign journalists have been working in China for more than 10 or even 30 years. According to the FCCC statement, John Sudworth and his family had been in China for nine years. His wife, who is also a journalist, also has a press card valid for one year. How is that possible for the family to have stayed in China for nine years if he was under threat? Besides, do they know that all Chinese journalists in the US have their visa limited to a maximum 90-day stay, which means they have to apply for visa renewal every three months and pay an extra $455 for each application? By contrast, foreign journalists in China should feel lucky. The FCCC is well aware of this. It just doesn't want to admit it.\nFifth, the statement mentioned the \"departure of Sudworth...on top of at least 18 correspondents last year\". The merits of the issue concerning journalists between China and the US are very clear. The US side, out of political oppression of China, the US denied or delayed visa issuance for more than 20 Chinese journalists and expelled over 60 with no good reason. China is forced to make justifiable and necessary reactions. As correspondents, members of the FCCC are fully aware of that, aren't they? The statement on the one hand said Sudworth left China's mainland on his won will, but on the other hand mentioned it in the same breath with the expulsion of those US journalists last year. What a shoddy lie!\nSixth, the statement claimed the attacks against Sudworth and the BBC escalated after Britain's broadcasting regulator Ofcom revoked the license of CGTN in accordance with law. I must point out that as an international, professional media agency, CGTN has been making objective and honest reports following ethics of journalism. It has played an active role in enhancing communication and understanding between China and the UK but suffered political oppression from the British side. China reserves the right to make necessary, legitimate reactions.\nSeventh, the FCCC statement said the departure of Sudworth is a loss for anyone committed to understanding China. This is far from the truth. Without his malicious rumor-mongering and disinformation, the outside world will get to know China in a more objective, true and unbiased manner.\nFinally, I want to emphasize that the life of journalism lies in truth. You may not like China, but you are not allowed to spread rumors and engage in smearing campaign in China. If some Western media continue to put ideology above truth, it will only lead to shattered credibility. China has always been and will continue to be committed to facilitating and helping foreign journalists in their reporting work in China. However, we are firmly opposed to strong ideological bias against China, acts that violate the professional ethics and morality. We also firmly reject manufacturing fake news and disinformation to malign and attack China in the name of so-called freedom of the press.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347016.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1866238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-01","Hua Chunying","","昨天BBC官方推特声明称沙磊转移到了台湾，同时表示沙磊仍将是BBC驻华记者。沙磊本人也接受BBC采访。外国驻华记者协会也发表声明指责中方环境恶化。你对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347016.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1866238.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2021-04-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 1 — The US State Department released its so-called “2020 Country Reports on Human Rights Practices,” alleging that the mainland is attempting to “manipulate Taiwan’s media through commercial pressure.” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 1st in response to a question that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs spokesperson has already refuted this so-called “human rights report,” which is full of lies. The so-called “remarks that the mainland manipulates Taiwan media through commercial pressure” are malicious fabrications that completely disregard the facts.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, for the sake of their own party interests, have long manipulated the media, raised cyber armies, persecuted dissenters, and muzzled public opinion, fabricating lies to deceive the public. The US side, for the purpose of exploiting the DPP authorities, has turned a blind eye and deaf ear to the widespread questioning and strong condemnation of these vile acts of the DPP authorities by all sectors of Taiwan society; instead, it has reversed black and white and slandered China, fully exposing the crudeness of the US side’s methods and the malice of its intentions, and fully exposing the dirty political deals behind US-Taiwan collusion. What the US side should do is open its eyes and look at the extremely serious human rights problems in its own country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210401_12342577.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-02","Hua Chunying","Global Times","US Department of State spokesperson Price said yesterday that \"we are committed to deepening ties with Taiwan...it is a critical economic and security partner of the United States, and that's why we will continue to engage Taiwan consistent with the longstanding \"one China\" policy. We will consider, just as we have, opportunities for visits to Washington and Taipei by senior-level authorities that advance our…","We noticed that recently, there have been unusual interactions between the US and Taiwan, and the latest ploy even entails the US ambassador's joining of the delegation of Palau. Does the US really care about the people in Taiwan? Or is it using Taiwan as a pawn in its plot to contain China? I think we all see through its real intention.\nBut I want stress that China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. There is but one China in the world. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a fact recognized by the international community. The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue between China and the US. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and a red line that cannot be crossed. We urge the US side to fully understand the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, stop the dangerous practice of challenging the bottom line and playing with fire as the previous administration did and stop official exchange with Taiwan in any form. It should prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, refrain from sending any wrong signals to the Taiwan independence forces in order to avoid serious damage to China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202104/t20210402_9170719.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1866593.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-04-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Chang An-lo, Chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Unification Promotion Party, gave an exclusive media interview in January this year and was threatened and intimidated by the DPP authorities. What comment do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 2 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 2nd in response to questions that the DPP authorities have fabricated various pretexts and frenziedly cracked down on parties and individuals on the island that support reunification and oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" creating a \"green terror,\" deliberately escalating cross-Strait antagonism, and once again exposing their true nature of plotting \"independence.\"\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that advocating and pursuing national reunification is a great righteousness of the nation and should be affirmed and supported by the entire nation. We hope all Taiwan compatriots will take part in the righteous cause of advancing reunification. Reunification is the future of Taiwan and is bound up with the well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and promoting reunification is the common will of Chinese sons and daughters at home and abroad. Those who go against the tide and stubbornly persist in plotting \"independence\" and division will surely reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210402_12342757.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 2 dispatch: On the morning of April 2, Taiwan Railway's “Taroko Express” train No. 408 derailed. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that day that relevant parties on the mainland are highly concerned about and following the progress of the subsequent rescue, and expressed condolences and sympathy to the casualties caused by the accident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210402_12342861.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","（2021年4月2日）\nRecently, relevant courts in Hong Kong ruled that Jimmy Lai and others were guilty of charges including “unlawful assembly.” The DPP authorities have made remarks on this. What comment do you have?","The Hong Kong SAR Government's handling of law-breakers in accordance with the law is a matter of course and brooks no interference. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces ignore the rule of law, confuse right and wrong, and maliciously attack. This once again exposes their nature of meddling in Hong Kong affairs and attempting to pursue “independence” and create chaos in Hong Kong. The DPP authorities attack dissenters on the island and suppress public opinion, stopping at nothing. What qualifications do they have to talk about human rights and democracy? We warn the DPP not to keep piling up wrongdoing on the Hong Kong issue, or they will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210403_12342984.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-07","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The president of the Pacific island nation of Palau recently said in an interview that Palau would stick to diplomatic recognition of Taiwan over the PRC no matter what since Taiwan is a democracy. What's your comment?","We firmly oppose the remarks you mentioned. As we know, the one-China principle is a basic norms of international relations followed by the overwhelming majority of countries.\n*******************\nThe Foreign Ministry Special Promotion Event for Hubei Province will be held online and offline at 16:45 on Monday, April 12, 2021, at Lanting, South Building of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China. With the theme of \"Heroic Hubei: Reborn for New Glories\", the event is co-organized by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the People's Government of Hubei Province. Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Foreign Minister, will be present and address the audience. Mr. Yingyong, Secretary of Hubei Provincial Committee of the Communist Party, Mr. Wang Xiaodong, Governor of Hubei Province and Mr. Wang Zhonglin, Secretary of Wuhan Municipal Party Committee, will make presentations of Hubei Province and its capital Wuhan city. Representatives from the Diplomatic Corps and international friends who contributed to fighting against Covid-19 in Wuhan will make remarks. This will be the first special promotion event the foreign ministry holds since the epidemic was brought under control.\nIn 2020, faced with a ferocious disease, Chinese people of all ethnic groups and on all fronts, united as one under the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, fought hard against the epidemic, and won the battle of defending Wuhan and Hubei, and achieved major strategic outcomes. The heroic people in Wuhan and Hubei, bearing in mind the greater good, made enormous sacrifice for a national victory over COVID-19 and contributed significantly to the global COVID-19 response. In addition to demonstrating the anti-epidemic achievements of Wuhan and Hubei, this promotion event will also present a new look of all-round economic and social development in Wuhan and Hubei now that the difficult situation is behind us. It will elaborate on the new opening-up measures taken in pursuit of new development philosophy for high-quality development in Wuhan and Hubei. The event offers a good opportunity for countries around the world to strengthen exchanges and cooperation with Hubei. We look forward to your attendance at and coverage of this event. For more details, please follow the notice to be posted by the Information Department of Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347019.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1867361.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-08","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","According to reports, US State Department spokesperson Ned Price said on April 7 that the US has \"taken note with great concern the pattern of ongoing PRC efforts and attempts to intimidate in the region, including in the context of Taiwan\", adding that \"The United States maintains the capacity to resist any resort to force or other forms of coercion that would jeopardize the security ... of the people on…","The US side falsely accuses China of intimidation and coercion, which have nothing to do with China.\nFirst, on the Taiwan question, who's actually guilty of intimidation and coercion? There is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Government of the PRC is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a basic fact recognized by the international community. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations, an explicit commitment made by the US to China in the three China-US joint communiques, and a red line that cannot be crossed. Lately US warships have frequently sailed to the Taiwan Strait to flex muscles, provoke and stir up trouble, sending gravely wrong signals to \"Taiwan-independence\" forces and threatening peace and stability across the region. I'd like to ask, have Chinese warships gone to the Gulf of Mexico to flex muscles?\nSecond, who is truly guilty of intimidation and coercion across the globe? When has the US stopped at mere intimidation and coercion? It has fought no war for only 16 of its nearly 250 years of history. It runs over 800 overseas military bases all over the world. Its military expenditure has ranked top in the world for many years in a roll, accounting for 40 percent of the global total. A report shows that the US has launched 228 military interventions and wars during the three decades since the Cold War ended, which equates to 7.6 each year on average. Citing a tube of laundry powder and a staged video as evidence, it struck Iraq and Syria, both sovereign nations, causing massive civilian casualties and wrecking numerous homes. The US also wantonly wields sanctions as a big stick and arbitrarily imposes illegal unilateral sanctions on other sovereign states. A US senior official once said, \"we make mistakes... but we confront challenges... not trying to ignore them\". So what the US should do first is apologize to the people of Iraq and Syria and shoulder relevant responsibilities. I'd like to ask, if it fails in doing this, how can the US claim that it always confronts challenges instead of trying to ignore them?\nLet me stress once again, China has no intention to intimidate or coerce anyone, but we have no fear for intimidation or coercion, wherever it may come from. China won't be found lacking in either will or capacity to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US should fully recognize that the Taiwan question is highly sensitive, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, avoid the dangerous path of challenging the bottom line and playing with fire, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues and refrain from sending any wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces to prevent serious damage to its own interests and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1867692.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210408_9171243.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-08","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","We also have a question about Taiwan's announcement that India is providing vaccines to Paraguay. I wonder if the foreign ministry have any comment on that?","It is customary practice for the Taiwan authorities to measure other people's corn by their own bushel.\nThe virus can spread across borders, but mankind's love also transcends borders. At the request of some countries, China has offered them help with vaccination. This is part of our active efforts contributing to international anti-epidemic cooperation. It is completely above-board. There is a huge difference between this and the despicable trick of Taiwan authorities attempting to buy so-called \"international space\" with money.\nA solemn reminder to the Taiwan authorities: Vaccines should be used to fight the pandemic and save lives, not as a tool for political manipulation. Attempts to take advantage of COVID-19 to seek independence or to pursue \"cash diplomacy\" are both doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1867692.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210408_9171243.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-09","Zhao Lijian","AFP","US Senators recently presented a bill that proposes tougher action on alleged Chinese intellectual property theft and the bill says the US should use \"the same nomenclature and protocol\" for dealing with Taiwan as with foreign governments. What's China's comment on this?","China's position on China-US relations, intellectual property rights and Taiwan-related issues is clear. The relevant US lawmakers should look at China and bilateral relations in an objective and rational light, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, reject Cold-War and zero-sum mentality, stop pushing negative bills that interfere in China's domestic affairs and harm Chinese interests, and act in ways beneficial to the sound and steady development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347021.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210409_9171244.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-09","Zhao Lijian","RIA Novosti","Two members of the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee yesterday introduced a bill, laying out the principles and proposing some initiatives for the United States' strategic competition with China. The bill also accuses China of leveraging its political, diplomatic, economic, military, and ideological power to become a strategic competitor of the United States. The Committee is expected to consider this bill on…","China is firmly opposed to the bill introduced by relevant members of Congress. Our position on China-US relations and issues relating to trade, Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Taiwan are clear and consistent. I reiterate that China is committed to developing a relationship with the US featuring non-conflict, non-confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation. At the same time we will continue to firmly safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests. Relevant individuals on the US side should view China and China-US relations in an objective and rational light and stop pushing the negative bill concerning China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347021.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210409_9171244.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-13","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","US State Department spokesperson said in a statement on April 9 that following a review as set forth in the Taiwan Assurance Act, the State Department has issued new guidelines to liberalize guidance on contacts with Taiwan and encourage U.S. government engagement with Taiwan that reflects its deepening unofficial relationship. Do you have any response?","The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. As the China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations clearly stipulates, \"The people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\" This is the premise for China and the US to develop bilateral relations over the past four decades or so. The so-called guidelines for U.S. government interaction with Taiwan counterparts blatantly encourages U.S. government engagement with Taiwan, which severely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and runs counter to the serious political commitment the US has made to China on the Taiwan question.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. There is zero room for compromise and not an inch to give. We urge the U.S. side to grasp the situation, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, refrain from playing with fire, immediately stop official contact with Taiwan in any form, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid sending any wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces, lest it should shake the foundation of China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1868644.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210413_9171245.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 13 (dateline). Recently, the U.S. State Department released the so-called new version of the “Guidelines on Interactions with Taiwan,” relaxing restrictions on U.S.-Taiwan interactions. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 13th, saying that we firmly oppose the United States developing any form of official relations with the Taiwan region of China.\nHe pointed out that adhering to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués is a solemn commitment the U.S. government has made to China. We urge the U.S. side to keep its commitments through concrete action, not to send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces, and to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete action. The DPP authorities’ “relying on the US to seek independence” will surely end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210413_12345104.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-14","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","First, US climate envoy John Kerry will visit China this week, I believe he arrives today, to discuss curbing carbon emissions. Could you provide us with any details, as to who he will meet? The second question is, a US delegation will meet Taiwanese \"President\" Tsai Ing-wen during its trip to Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on the US former officials' meeting with Tsai?","On your first question, the Ministry of Ecology and Environment has released information on the matter. At China's invitation, US Special Presidential Envoy for Climate John Kerry visits China from April 14 to 17. During his visit, China's special envoy on climate change Xie Zhenhua will have talks with him in Shanghai. The two will have exchanges on China-US climate cooperation and COP26 of the UNFCCC.\nOn your second question, I need to point out that Tsai Ing-wen is only head of a Chinese region. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between the US and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear. The Chinese side has lodged solemn representations with the US over the high-level government decision to send personnel to visit the Taiwan region. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop immediately all official interactions with the Taiwan region, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from sending any wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to avoid further grave damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347023.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210414_9171246.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. I will host today's press conference. Now I am willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Have the specific policies and arrangements for vaccination of mainland Taiwan compatriots been determined? Could the spokesperson please introduce them in detail?","We attach great importance to, and deeply care about, the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. For the vaccination of Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland, following the principles of local management and equal treatment, we apply the same policies and standards as those for mainland residents in their area of residence, namely: on the premise of being informed, consenting and voluntary, they may register for vaccination at their place of residence with a Taiwan resident residence permit or a mainland medical insurance enrollment certificate. Taiwan compatriots without a Taiwan resident residence permit or mainland medical insurance enrollment certificate may apply to the Taiwan Affairs Office at or above the county level where they reside, and the Taiwan Affairs Office at or above the county level will organize unified vaccination at designated vaccination units. Vaccination of Taiwan teachers and students in mainland schools of all levels and types will be included in the local unified vaccination arrangements, and they will be treated equally with mainland teachers and students at their schools. In terms of cost-bearing for applicable groups, treatment and compensation for abnormal reactions, they will follow the same requirements and standards as mainland residents in the locality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345447.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","After the serious Taiwan Railway accident, the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed condolences at the first opportunity. Reports say one mainland student was slightly injured in the accident. Please introduce the specific situation.","After the Taiwan Railway train accident, General Secretary Xi Jinping expressed deep concern over the major casualty accident caused by the train derailment and expressed profound mourning for the compatriots who died. The Taiwan Affairs Office, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, the Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots also expressed condolences and sympathy to the injured and deceased Taiwan compatriots and their families.\nWe were deeply concerned and quickly learned whether this accident involved mainland residents studying, working, or living in Taiwan. It is understood that one mainland student studying at National Taiwan University was lightly injured in the accident, and after hospital examination, it was confirmed there is no serious harm. This mainland student is from Zhuhai, Guangdong, and the local Taiwan Affairs Office expressed care and sympathy to him and his family. I also wish to remind mainland students studying in Taiwan to be mindful of risk prevention and ensure personal safety.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345446.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Wu Chao-hsieh, head of Taiwan's foreign contact department, recently told foreign media that the US believes the likelihood of the mainland using force against Taiwan is high, and that if war breaks out, “Taiwan will fight to the end.” A US State Department spokesperson subsequently reiterated the so-called “Taiwan commitment” and accused the mainland of so-called “military coercion” against Taiwan. What comments…","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no interference from any external force. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will never leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form. We do not promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is aimed at external interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, and is by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots. Where is the so-called “coercion by force” claim coming from?\nThe root cause of the current complex and grave situation across the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities collude with external forces and continuously provoke by pursuing “independence.” The United States has reversed right and wrong, promoting the so-called “China military threat” narrative and continuously sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, with malicious intent. This not only fans the flames of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities but also brings more burdens and disasters to the people on the island, and in the end the Taiwan people will suffer the greatest losses. We urge the US government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to properly handle the Taiwan question. Some politicians of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism, rely on foreign backing to advance their own interests, frequently speak recklessly, and overestimate themselves, and they will not escape the punishment of history. Whether external forces “use Taiwan to contain China” or “Taiwan independence” forces “use force to seek independence,” both are doomed to fail in the face of the firm resolve and powerful capability of the 1.4 billion Chinese people to deter “Taiwan independence” and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345445.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","KMT Chairman Chiang Chi-chen recently made remarks at an online forum on the so-called “how to respond to the influence of the CPC.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on the content related to cross-Strait relations?","We have noted the relevant reports. The Taiwan question concerns national reunification and national rejuvenation, and it concerns the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Differences in systems between the two sides of the Strait are not an obstacle to unification, much less a pretext for confrontation and division. Facts have repeatedly shown that the DPP and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, in seeking “independence” and provoking confrontation, are the root cause of the threat to Taiwan Strait peace and stability. We hope that all sectors on the island will have a clear understanding of this, voice rational views, not mistake cause for effect, and certainly not confuse right and wrong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345443.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","A Taiwan magazine, citing staff of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said that many Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan cadres who failed in business or lost their jobs are stranded on the mainland. In recent years, the number of these elderly, impoverished stranded persons returning to Taiwan has continued to rise, creating a burden for Taiwan society. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The relevant reports do not accord with the facts. For many years, guided by the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we have done everything we can to resolve problems arising from exchanges between compatriots on both sides and to safeguard the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides. For a small number of Taiwan compatriots who have been stranded on the mainland for reasons such as illness, documentation, or other personal circumstances, relevant mainland authorities and localities have always shown great concern and have actively provided medical assistance and living care. Individual Taiwan compatriots choosing to return to Taiwan according to their own wishes and actual circumstances is their right. Relevant mainland authorities have also made active efforts in helping contact family members or placement institutions on the island and in arranging their return, and we hope that they will be properly cared for after returning to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345436.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the first African swine fever-positive drifting pig was recently found on the main island of Taiwan. Taiwan’s agricultural authorities said they have ruled out that it was caused by the disposal of dead pigs from pig farms on the island, and speculated that it drifted over from the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The mainland attaches great importance to the prevention and control of African swine fever. Since February this year, coastal provinces including Zhejiang, Fujian, and Guangdong have not reported any African swine fever outbreaks, so the DPP authorities’ so-called speculation has no factual basis. At present, African swine fever occurs frequently and is widely distributed around the world, and gene sequencing alone cannot determine the direct source of the virus. We hope the DPP authorities will strengthen their own epidemic surveillance, precisely carry out outbreak tracing, earnestly implement prevention and control measures, and enhance epidemic prevention and control capabilities, rather than habitually passing the buck to divert the public’s attention and obscure the focus of the problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345442.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","In response to the so-called outflow of Taiwan's agricultural plant varieties to the mainland, Taiwan's agricultural authorities claim they will draft amendments to the “Plant Variety and Seedling Act” to hold relevant conduct accountable. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Deepening cross-Strait agricultural exchanges and cooperation is conducive to promoting the development of the island's agricultural industry and enhancing the interests and well-being of island farmers and fishermen. This is obvious. In order to seek political self-interest, the DPP authorities attempt to intimidate Taiwan residents with so-called “law amendments” and to restrict cross-Strait agricultural exchanges and cooperation. This is not strange at all. Whenever the mainland introduces measures beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, they oppose them across the board; whatever is beneficial to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they go against. The DPP authorities' attempt to block the path for Taiwan compatriots to seek development and well-being is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345441.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, the US aircraft carrier Roosevelt entered the South China Sea, and the destroyer Mustin even closely tracked and surveilled the Liaoning carrier. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is worrying, and some have described it as a possible “Balkan powder keg.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","First, the current cross-Strait situation is complex and severe. The root cause is that the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, in collusion with external forces, have continuously engaged in provocations seeking “independence,” undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond, we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and make our utmost efforts, but we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. The PLA's combat-oriented drills in the Taiwan Strait area are necessary actions taken in response to the current security situation in the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty. They are a solemn response to external interference and “Taiwan independence” provocations.\nThird, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose the US side's promotion of the so-called “China military threat” narrative, and firmly oppose the US side playing the “Taiwan card” and continuously sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question prudently and properly.\nFourth, “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. We warn the DPP authorities that relying on foreign backing, “seeking independence by relying on the US,” and even arrogantly fantasizing about “seeking independence by force” is like drinking poison to quench thirst. It will only lead Taiwan toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The vaccines Taiwan has currently obtained have expiration dates at the end of May and in mid-June, yet the DPP authorities still refuse mainland vaccines for political self-interest. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","To date, the mainland has administered more than 160 million doses of COVID-19 vaccine cumulatively and has made arrangements for vaccinating Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. By contrast, the broad masses of Taiwan's people continue to suffer from vaccine shortages. The cause of this situation is entirely the political manipulation of the DPP authorities. As the saying goes: “Political confrontation is placed in the middle, while the people's suffering and grievances are placed on the sides.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, Hsiao Mei-chin, the Taiwan “representative to the United States,” met with Pompeo, and the island has hyped this extensively. What is your comment? In addition, Hsiao Mei-chin also said that the United States is very concerned about the Taiwan “ractopamine pork referendum,” and that if it passes, it may affect Taiwan-U.S. economic and trade relations. Internet users on the island are very dissatisfied…","First question: Everyone is very clear about who Pompeo is. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have courted and flattered certain American politicians, and even meddled heavily during the U.S. presidential election, picking sides. Everyone can see this clearly, and so can the American people. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, relying on foreign powers to elevate themselves and using any means necessary, grab at everything indiscriminately, which is chilling to behold.\nSecond question: From the remarks you mentioned, one gets the sense that this person is a spokesman for American interests, willing to harm the interests of the Taiwan people for the sake of the United States. This shows that, in order to “rely on the United States to seek independence,” the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are fully prepared to sacrifice the lives, health, and well-being of Taiwan’s people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The U.S. State Department recently published the so-called new “Taiwan Travel Guidelines,” which relax restrictions on U.S.-Taiwan contacts. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We firmly oppose the United States developing any form of official relations with Taiwan. Adhering to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués is a solemn commitment the US government made to the Chinese side. We urge the US side to honor its commitments through concrete actions, not to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions. The DPP authorities' “relying on the US to seek independence” will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210414_12345444.htm"],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","According to Taiwan’s side, since April 3, the PLA has entered the so-called “southwest air defense identification zone” of Taiwan for ten consecutive days, with 25 sorties entering on the 12th, a single-day record high. Some analysts believe the mainland judges the current situation in the Taiwan Strait to be rather tense, with a possibility of further escalation. May I ask how you view these comments?","I have just explained this, and I would like to add one point. The relevant military exercises and drills of the PLA send a signal: our determination to contain “Taiwan independence” and to contain provocations by Taiwan-US collusion to seek “independence” is not just talk.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","At the request of U.S. President Biden, former U.S. Senator Dodd will lead a delegation to visit Taiwan and meet with Tsai Ing-wen. Some people believe this is a personal signal from Biden of his commitment to Taiwan's democracy. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The US side must first clarify right and wrong. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and its root cause and responsibility lie with the DPP authorities. This is the first point.\nSecond, we oppose any form of official exchange between Taiwan and the United States. The United States has made commitments to China on the Taiwan question. We hope it will seriously and earnestly fulfill those commitments and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Regarding cross-Strait relations, the new edition of “A Brief History of the Communist Party of China” speaks more, in its description of the Taiwan-related situation after the DPP authorities took office in 2016, of the Party's position and actions in opposing “Taiwan independence.” However, if cross-Strait exchanges and interactions are to resume in the future, both sides will need to make joint efforts. My…","It seems you have also studied the history of the Communist Party of China seriously. The part you mentioned, Section 5 of Chapter 10 of “A Brief History of the Communist Party of China,” titled “Adhering to ‘One Country, Two Systems’ and Advancing the Reunification of the Motherland,” introduces the basic situation of cross-Strait relations and Taiwan work since the 18th National Congress. In 2016, when the DPP came to power, the momentum of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations was seriously impacted. This is a basic fact.\nSecond, to safeguard the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation, we have taken a series of important measures to oppose and contain “Taiwan independence,” drawing clear bottom lines for the “Taiwan independence” forces and creating a strong deterrent. This is also entirely necessary.\nThird, our overall policy toward Taiwan is clear. For cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, consultation and dialogue between the two sides must of course be conducted on the basis of the one-China principle, and built on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus.” We have also stated many times that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and its core meaning is recognized, dialogue and exchanges across the Strait are not a problem.\nFourth, we have always actively encouraged compatriots on both sides to expand exchanges and cooperation. To this end, we have implemented many policies and substantive measures that people can feel. From the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures,” to the “11 Measures” supporting Taiwan enterprises, and then to the newly promulgated and implemented “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” we are doing everything we can to provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises coming to the mainland to develop, so that they can take the lead in sharing the opportunities of mainland development. We believe that as exchanges among compatriots on both sides deepen and cross-Strait integrated development goes further, compatriots on both sides will certainly be able to grow closer, come nearer, and get along better, working together toward the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台《台海之声》记者","In recent years, Taiwan businesses' investment in Fujian's service sector has grown markedly. Statistics show that in the first eight months of 2020, Taiwan businesses' investment in Fujian's service sector amounted to nearly US$400 million, an increase of 128.5% over the same period in 2019. What is the spokesperson's comment?","These data fully show that in recent years Fujian has made great progress in economic and social development and has become a fertile ground for Taiwan compatriots choosing to invest on the mainland. They also show that the various policy measures Fujian has vigorously introduced in recent years to promote Fujian-Taiwan exchanges and cooperation and to build the first home for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland have achieved remarkable results. This is an important reason why Taiwanese businesses, including those in the service sector, invest in Fujian.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","彭博社记者","You just mentioned that the mainland opposes any form of official exchanges between Taiwan and the United States. Both Taiwan and the U.S. have said that former U.S. Senator Dodd's visit to Taiwan is an unofficial visit, and that he may meet with Tsai Ing-wen during it. What comment do you have on this?","So-called official and unofficial claims are merely a pretext for their deception. We firmly oppose any official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, in any form and under any pretext. No contact between Taiwan and the United States can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, a Taiwan youth donated bone marrow to a mainland youth, and an allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant was successfully completed. This is the first case of cryopreserved hematopoietic stem cells donated to the mainland from the Tzu Chi Bone Marrow Bank in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","On April 7, with the joint efforts and assistance of Nanjing Medical University Affiliated Mingji Hospital, the China Marrow Donor Program, the Tzu Chi Bone Marrow Bank, the team of Chinese Academy of Engineering academician Lu Daopei, and the team of Chinese-American scientist Li Zhengdao, the hematopoietic stem cells of a Taiwan young man were successfully transplanted into a young male patient in Jiangsu. This matched bone marrow transplant succeeded despite the adverse impact of the epidemic, demonstrating the great love of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and fully showing that compatriots on both sides are one family with blood ties. We express our deep respect to the above institutions and to the Taiwan donor.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","You just mentioned that the arrangements for vaccination costs and medical insurance for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are the same as for mainland residents. I would like to confirm: does simply holding a Taiwan residence permit allow one to be vaccinated for free?","It is free of charge. Let me reiterate the relevant policies and specific arrangements. The first category: Taiwan compatriots holding a Taiwan Residence Permit or a mainland medical insurance enrollment certificate may register for vaccination at their place of residence. The second category: Taiwan compatriots without a Taiwan Residence Permit or a mainland medical insurance enrollment certificate may also apply for registration with the Taiwan Affairs Office at the county level or above in their place of residence, and vaccination will be organized uniformly. There is also a category of Taiwan teachers and students studying and working at mainland universities, who are treated equally with mainland teachers and students at their schools and may also be vaccinated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","The annual meeting of the Boao Forum for Asia will be held in Hainan next week. In the past, Taiwan would usually have the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation lead a delegation to attend, and hold cross-Strait entrepreneurs’ roundtable meetings, among other activities. Due to the epidemic this year, the agenda has no related arrangements. I would like to ask the spokesperson: will there be a cross-Strait…","Regarding the preparations for the 2021 Annual Conference of the Boao Forum for Asia, the forum secretariat already held a press conference on March 30 and gave a detailed explanation, which I believe everyone has noted. This year's annual conference will be held in a combination of online and offline formats. Affected by the epidemic and other factors, fewer Taiwan representatives will attend than in the past, but this does not prevent cross-Strait business and industry circles from obtaining information and conducting exchanges through this platform. From the topics currently announced for the annual conference, there is both continuity and innovation, including dual circulation, financial opening, carbon neutrality, the digital economy, and sustainable development, among other hot topics of common concern. This will provide many opportunities and room for deepening cross-Strait economic development and for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to develop on the mainland.\nThere are many channels and ways for cross-Strait economic cooperation and development, and it will not be affected solely because this forum has no Taiwan delegation. I believe that as the mainland promotes high-quality development and exchanges and interactions among compatriots on both sides continue to deepen, economic cooperation across the Strait will also go deeper, more solidly, and better.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Hong Kong media recently reported that some historical textbooks in Hong Kong have changed the previous phrase “the Republic of China government’s relocation to Taiwan” to “the Kuomintang’s relocation to Taiwan.” Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council responded that this practice is “hiding the bell while covering the ears.” How does the spokesperson view this, and how do you comment?","In 1949, the KMT regime was defeated in the civil war it launched against the people, retreated to Taiwan Island, and from then on lost its status as the legal government representing all of China. This is an indisputable historical fact.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","彭博社记者","A follow-up question regarding the possibility that a former U.S. official visiting Taiwan may meet with Tsai Ing-wen. What comment does the TAO have on the validity of this meeting?","We oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan, and no matter what pretext is used to disguise it, we firmly oppose it. Such meetings do not help improve cross-Strait relations, do not help stabilize the situation in the Taiwan Strait, and will only exacerbate tensions. Such meetings also cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Taiwan is facing its worst water shortage in 56 years. Some scholars point out that the DPP authorities have channeled large amounts of funds and resources into arms procurement, weakening economic construction and infrastructure such as water conservancy. What comment do you have on this?","I think the comment you mentioned is very correct. Right and wrong, and good and bad, Taiwan compatriots will gradually come to feel them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","We have noted that over the past year, the mainland's military exercises and training activities near Taiwan have continued without interruption. The Kuomintang has also shown some changes in its discourse on cross-Strait relations, and the people of Taiwan harbor doubts about these military activities. May I ask whether the mainland is concerned that this will affect the views of the people of Taiwan toward the…","Your question tangles several issues together. First, as I have already made clear, the apparent increase in mainland military exercises is in fact caused by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities colluding with external forces and by escalating “Taiwan independence” provocations aimed at independence. Which is cause and which is effect is clear to everyone; do not mistake the effect for the cause or reverse black and white. We have repeatedly stated that the relevant PLA exercises and drills are not aimed at Taiwan’s people, and Taiwan compatriots need not harbor any concerns. If there are any concerns, then compatriots on both sides of the Strait should unite to jointly curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait, to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and to the common interests of compatriots on both sides. As the saying goes, “If Qingfu is not dead, the troubles of Lu will not end.” Resolutely curbing “Taiwan independence” means there is no need for any concern at all.\nSecond, cross-Strait relations have had ups and downs, but the facts prove that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop; conversely, they will fall into confrontation and even into tension and turmoil. Let us look back: why did peaceful development open up in cross-Strait relations from 2008 to 2016? Because both sides established basic political mutual trust on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” It was the DPP authorities who single-handedly destroyed this situation. Whatever party or faction one belongs to, everyone should be able to clearly see this distinction between right and wrong.\nThird, improving cross-Strait relations is not difficult. As long as the DPP authorities abandon the “Taiwan independence” stance, stop “Taiwan independence” activities, and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations will enjoy spring warmth.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-14","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社","Reportedly, Wu Chao-hsieh recently said that Taiwan is determined to improve its own military capabilities, increase military spending and enhance its defensive capabilities. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Taiwan compatriots should not fall for this. According to his account, Taiwan compatriots will not only face a heavier tax burden and fiscal burden, but the existing standard of living will also be affected. Doing so would push Taiwan into a bottomless abyss.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210414_12345433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-15","Zhao Lijian","The Globe and Mail","The Canadian Parliament has declared Tsai Ing-wen an ideal candidate for the John McCain Prize for Leadership in Public Service. Does the Chinese government believe that Ms. Tsai is an ideal candidate for this prize?","China deplores and rejects the wrong motion related to Taiwan passed by the Canadian House of Commons. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-Canada relations and a solemn commitment by the Canadian government. Canada should recognize that the Taiwan question is highly sensitive, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues and avoid further undermining bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347024.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1869182.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-15","Zhao Lijian","NHK","When meeting with an unofficial US delegation in Taiwan today, Tsai Ing-wen thanked the Biden administration for the emphasis it places on peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have a comment?","I already stated China's solemn position on the visit to Taiwan by the US delegation yesterday.\nThe Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and core interests. We are firmly determined to safeguard sovereignty, security and development interests. The US should fully grasp the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from sending any wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to avoid serious damage to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as China-US coordination and cooperation in key areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347024.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1869182.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-16","Zhao Lijian","NTV","According to reports, Japanese and American leaders will have talks on April 16 local time. The two countries are expected to mention the importance of maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait in a document to be released afterwards. Do you have any comment?","We have noticed relevant reports. China has expressed grave concern to the US and Japan over their negative moves including collusion against China following the Japanese leader's visit to the US. I'd like to point out China-US and China-Japan relations both stand at an important juncture. The world is watching closely what signals the visit will send. China has got nothing against the development of normal bilateral ties between the US and Japan, but this relationship should be conducive to enhancing mutual understanding and trust among regional countries and peace and stability in the Asia Pacific, and should not target any third party or undermine third party interests.\nChina's position on Taiwan, Hong Kong, the South China Sea and Diaoyu Dao is consistent and clear. Our determination and resolve to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests are rock solid. The US and Japan should take China's concerns and demands seriously, avoid moves that interfere in China's internal affairs and undermine China's interests, and refrain from forming a clique targeting China. China will make necessary reactions as the situation evolves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1869451.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1869432.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-19","Wang Wenbin","Nippon TV","Also on the joint statement of Japan and the US. It refers to the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. We ask the US and Japan to take seriously China's concerns, abide by the one-China principle, immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs and harming China's interests. China will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1869850.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210419_9171249.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-04-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 19 — Jimmy Lai and others were recently found guilty of charges including “organizing an unauthorized assembly,” and the DPP authorities have attacked and smeared this. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response on the 19th that it is only natural that the Hong Kong SAR government handles lawbreakers in accordance with the law, and no interference will be tolerated.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities, under the banner of democracy and human rights, hypocritically shout about “public opinion” and “dialogue,” while engaging in the shady practice of seeking votes and plotting to create chaos in Hong Kong and seek “independence.” These base tricks are plain for all to see. We warn the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation, or they will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210419_12346474.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 20 — In response to the recent joint statement by the United States and Japan expressing “concern” over the situation in the Taiwan Strait, which the DPP authorities have thanked them for, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 20th, responding to questions: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and it brooks no foreign interference.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We urge the United States and Japan to abide by the one-China principle, handle the Taiwan question properly, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign powers and bolstering themselves with them, willingly serve as pawns of anti-China forces, which will only place Taiwan in an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210420_12346817.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The DPP authorities have played down the Japanese government's decision to dispose of Fukushima nuclear wastewater by ocean discharge. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","(Xinhua) Beijing, April 20 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 20th, saying that regarding the Japanese government's decision to dispose of the Fukushima nuclear power plant's nuclear wastewater by ocean discharge, relevant departments have repeatedly stated their position. The DPP authorities have been evasive on Japan's discharge of nuclear wastewater into the sea, and some people have even stepped forward to defend Japan's erroneous practices. This fully exposes how the DPP authorities, for political self-interest, disregard the livelihood and well-being of the people on the island, which has already aroused strong dissatisfaction among the island's populace.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210420_12346818.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 21 — In response to remarks by Chiu Tai-san, Chairman of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, concerning cross-Strait relations in an interview on April 20, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to questions on April 21 that the DPP authorities' latest remarks continue to distort and deny the “1992 Consensus,” which fully exposes the DPP authorities' stance of pursuing “Taiwan independence” and their lack of sincerity in improving cross-Strait relations. They are attempting to shirk responsibility for undermining cross-Strait relations, confuse public perception, and deceive people on the island and the international community.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the “1992 Consensus” embodies the historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations. In the consensus, both sides expressed adherence to the one-China principle and the pursuit of national reunification. As to the political meaning of one China, both sides chose to set the matter aside. The “1992 Consensus” was reached by both sides through equal consultation and political wisdom; its core essence is that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and jointly seek unification, a fact reflected in both sides' written words that cannot be denied. It was the 1992 consensus, that is, the “1992 Consensus,” that made the “Wang-Koo Talks” possible and led to the signing of the 23 cross-Strait agreements. The DPP authorities, in the name of the consensus, negate the substance of the consensus, which is typical sophistry. History has repeatedly proven that whether one acknowledges the “1992 Consensus” is the “touchstone” for testing all understanding and goodwill. The DPP and its authorities regard the “1992 Consensus” as a thorn in their side that restrains their pursuit of “Taiwan independence”; on the one hand they negate the “1992 Consensus,” and on the other hand they fabricate so-called goodwill. This will not work.\nHe pointed out that the root of the current tense and turbulent state of cross-Strait relations is the provocations of the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces in pursuit of “Taiwan independence.” We oppose and curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, targeting the provocations of the “Taiwan independence” forces and the interference of external forces, and we safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The DPP authorities' attempts to distort black and white and deceive the world will not work.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we have consistently adhered to the concepts of “one family across the Strait” and a people-centered development philosophy, sincerely doing practical things, good things and things that solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, serving Taiwan compatriots as we would serve mainland residents, continuously improving the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure their equal treatment on the mainland, and actively promoting cross-Strait integration through connectivity, benefits and emotional bonds, continuously deepening the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Taiwan compatriots see this clearly and feel it deeply. The DPP authorities' attempts to sow discord will not succeed.\nHe said that we will continue to advance cross-Strait consultations and negotiations on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” and our position of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has not changed in any way. Only if the DPP authorities genuinely show sincerity, take practical actions, stop provocations for “Taiwan independence,” and return to the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully and stably.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210421_12347136.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 22 (electronic dispatch). In response to the recent move by the DPP authorities, in collusion with some anti-China US lawmakers, to float the so-called “Taiwan International Solidarity” bill and to question and challenge UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to questions on the 22nd: The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, have repeatedly made an issue of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, attempting to overturn the iron-clad fact that Taiwan is part of China and to challenge the authority and legitimacy of the UN resolution, in an attempt to lend endorsement to their “Taiwan independence” fallacies. This is ultimately wishful thinking and will end in failure.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that in 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, recognizing the People’s Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. This thoroughly resolved the question of China’s representation in the United Nations politically, legally, and procedurally, and fully reflects the one-China principle upheld by the UN. International organizations, including the World Health Organization, must abide by the UN General Assembly resolution and handle Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210422_12347280.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-04-23","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","At a meeting of Liberal Democratic Party lawmakers on the evening of April 22, speaking of China's activities around the Diaoyu Islands, Japanese Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi said that \"China is invading in a subtle way step by step.\" He also talked about the Taiwan question. What is China's comment?","These remarks are completely reckless and highly irresponsible. With such person misleading the public opinion, how can the Japanese people view China's development in an objective and rational way and build up confidence in China-Japan relations? I want to stress some points as follows.\nFirst, China always adheres to the path of peaceful development and firmly pursues a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. In his speech at the opening ceremony of the Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference 2021, President Xi reiterated that China will continue to be a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of the international order. However strong it may grow, China will never seek hegemony, expansion, or a sphere of influence. Nor will China ever engage in an arms race. And I tell the Japanese side now, stop talking nonsense about China's development and misleading the public.\nSecond, the Diaoyu Island and its affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. China's patrol and law enforcement in waters off the Diaoyu Island is an exercise of its inherent rights. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. China will never allow any country to interfere in any way. Some Japanese people's erroneous words related to Taiwan fully expose their sinister thinking that they do not want to see China's peaceful reunification and will do everything possible to obstruct that great cause. China must and will be reunified. The Japanese side should never harbor any illusion with ulterior motives.\nThird, in more recent history, Japan's act of aggression and expansion in Asia has brought untold suffering to the people of the victimized countries, including China. To this day, however, Japan is still reluctant to honestly face up to and repent its history of aggression, but has staged political farces, one after another, to deny and whitewash this part of history. Certain Japanese politicians wantonly smear China while turning a blind eye to its deplorable records of aggression. The world should be on high alert as to their real intention. We urge Japan to reflect on itself, immediately stop slinging mud at China and refrain from going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1871098.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210423_9171253.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-04-26","Wang Wenbin","","澳大利亚国防部长达顿称，在台湾问题上，不应忽视与中国发生冲突的可能性，中方统一的意志很明确。但同时，澳希望继续成为该地区的友好邻居。中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210426_9171254.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2021-04-28","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","Amid growing tensions between China and the US over Taiwan, Australian Home Affairs Department Secretary Mike Pezzullo highlighted the \"protection afforded to Australia\" by its military alliance with the US and New Zealand. He said, \"Today, as free nations again hear the beating drums... let us continue to search unceasingly for the chance for peace while bracing again, yet again, for the curse of war\". Australia…","Some individual politicians in Australia, out of their selfish interests, are keen to make statements that incite confrontation and hype up threat of war, which is extremely irresponsible and will find no audience. These people are the real troublemakers. I have noticed that many people in Australia have expressed disapproval on social media, saying that such inflammatory language are outrageous and extremely crazy.\nChina has been a promoter of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of international order. China's development means opportunities for the world. As a country long benefited from cooperation with China, Australia is being untruthful and immoral with its false allegation of \"China threat theory\". This will only end up hurting its own interests. We urge certain individuals in Australia to shake off the Cold War mentality, stop making irresponsible remarks and act in ways that are conducive to regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347033.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202104/t20210428_9171256.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends. Today’s press conference is hosted by me. I am now willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","At the previous press conference, the spokesperson introduced the arrangements and policies for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland to receive COVID-19 vaccinations. I would like to ask the spokesperson what the situation of vaccination among Taiwan compatriots on the mainland is so far.","After the vaccination program for Taiwan compatriots residing in the mainland was launched, Taiwan compatriots in various localities responded actively and enthusiastically registered. Vaccination was carried out on the basis of voluntary participation and equal treatment. According to preliminary understanding and incomplete statistics, in just the first two days, the number of Taiwan compatriots in Guangzhou and Shenzhen who voluntarily registered for vaccination exceeded 350 and 130, respectively. As of the 25th, Fujian Province had vaccinated 1,807 Taiwan compatriot visits. As of the 26th, Jiangsu Province had vaccinated 4,906 Taiwan compatriot visits. As of the 27th, Beijing and Zhejiang Province had vaccinated 1,836 and 1,072 Taiwan compatriot visits, respectively, and Shanghai had administered 3,385 doses to Taiwan compatriots. As vaccination coverage expands and the work deepens in various localities, more Taiwan compatriots will voluntarily get vaccinated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council has repeatedly stated that the two sides need goodwill and mutual understanding, and that restoring healthy and orderly exchanges is the primary task. The mainland keeps placing blame on Taiwan, which will only misjudge the situation and add to confrontation. What comment does the spokesperson have?","For some time, although the DPP authorities have verbally claimed that goodwill and mutual understanding are needed across the Strait and that exchanges should resume, in practice they have continuously used various pretexts and methods to obstruct and restrict personnel exchanges across the Strait, intimidated and penalized Taiwan compatriots who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, and sought to cut off Taiwan compatriots' and young people's access to the Mainland's development opportunities and their path to better development. Is this goodwill? Since the outbreak of the epidemic, the DPP authorities have unilaterally banned Mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, closed the \"mini three links\" at Kinmen, Matsu and Fujian, broadly canceled cross-Strait direct flight routes, subjected many children of cross-Strait marriages and Mainland spouses to discriminatory treatment, and still do not allow the rotation of Mainland agency and enterprise personnel stationed in Taiwan. Is this goodwill? The DPP authorities should stop using the epidemic for political manipulation and promptly and fully lift the restrictive measures that hinder exchanges between people on both sides.\nThe crux and the solution of cross-Strait relations are very clear. The DPP authorities should first honestly face the \"1992 Consensus,\" the \"touchstone\" that embodies the one-China principle. This is a matter of great principle in cross-Strait relations and cannot be bypassed. The DPP authorities keep creating cross-Strait confrontation, colluding with external forces to seek \"independence\" and provoke, and attempt to fabricate so-called \"goodwill\" to deceive the public, shift blame and evade responsibility. This will not work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","At an event recently held by “Taiwan independence” groups, Yao Chia-wen, one of the co-convenors of the DPP's so-called “constitutional” group, claimed that the basic position of “constitutional amendment” is to “rectify the name” to “Republic of Taiwan.” May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","We are highly concerned about these developments. A handful of “Taiwan independence” diehards, for their own selfish ends, disregard the interests and well-being of the people of Taiwan and keep engaging in reckless “Taiwan independence” adventurism and provocations. This only intensifies turmoil in cross-Strait relations, pushes Taiwan toward danger, and brings profound suffering to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP claims it will not go to extremes, yet it lets such people repeatedly spread “extreme independence” fallacies. What exactly does it intend? We firmly oppose any form of “constitutional amendment to pursue independence” separatist behavior on the island, and we will take all necessary measures to counter it. Do not say we did not warn you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Su Tseng-chang recently said that the investment-in-Taiwan plan proposed during the China-US trade conflict has produced results, with investment returning to Taiwan exceeding NT$1.2 trillion, and Taiwan's investment in the mainland as a share of total outbound investment having dropped significantly. What is the spokesperson's comment?","As for the so-called \"data\" claimed by certain DPP politicians, which carry special political motives and \"domestic propaganda\" considerations, people may simply listen to them and take them with a grain of salt. In fact, Taiwanese businesses and enterprises' investment and development on the Mainland maintain a steady growth momentum. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, in the first quarter of this year, the Mainland newly established 1,195 Taiwan-invested enterprises, a year-on-year increase of 33.4%; actual use of Taiwan capital was 330 million US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 29.9%. Including reinvestment made through third places, the Mainland newly established 1,214 Taiwan-invested enterprises, a year-on-year increase of 32.4%; actual use of Taiwan capital was 910 million US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 80.7%.\nThe Mainland has a solid material foundation, a huge market scale, abundant human resources, and the world's largest, most complete-category, and best-supported industrial system. The \"14th Five-Year Plan\" brings new opportunities and broader development space for Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to integrate into the Mainland's new development pattern, participate in the construction of the \"Belt and Road\", and the national regional coordinated development strategies. We continue to welcome and support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to develop on the Mainland, and will continue to improve systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the Mainland, creating a better development environment for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. The Mainland was, is, and will continue to be the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to invest and start businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声电台记者","After the mainland suspended imports of Taiwanese pineapples, some U.S. politicians clamored to establish a so-called “Economic NATO” and push for imports of sanctioned goods. The head of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said that if the “Economic NATO” is established, Taiwan could seek to join it, and claimed it would “guard against China” economically. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation is mutually beneficial and has brought real benefits to the broad Taiwan compatriots. Facts have proven that Taiwan's economic development cannot do without the mainland. Peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations are the broad avenue that benefits compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. Starting from normal biosecurity precautions, the mainland has suspended imports of pineapples from Taiwan. The DPP authorities have disregarded the interests of the people and engaged in slanderous and smearing political manipulation. By sacrificing the development opportunities and vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, their conduct is aimed at seeking political self-interest.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The Haidian District People's Court in Beijing recently sentenced 46 Taiwanese suspects in telecom fraud who were extradited from Spain. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","On April 16 this year, the Haidian District People’s Court of Beijing separately held public sentencing hearings for 46 Taiwan residents in telecommunications fraud cases. The defendants voluntarily confessed and accepted punishment. During the trial, the People’s Court fully guaranteed the defendants’ procedural rights in accordance with the law. Information on the trial of these cases can be checked on the official website of the Haidian District People’s Court of Beijing or on the WeChat official account of the Beijing Higher People’s Court, “京法网事.”\nTelecommunications network fraud causes serious harm to society. People on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have suffered from it and deeply loathe it. From 2016 to 2019, Chinese and Spanish police carried out “Operation Great Wall,” a three-year joint campaign to combat cross-border telecommunications network fraud. Spain extradited 225 criminal suspects to China in batches, 218 of whom were Taiwan suspects. This criminal gang carried out frenzied frauds against mainland residents, involving a total of 120 million yuan. Many people’s money for medical care, retirement, and children’s schooling was swept away by the fraudsters, and a teacher in Gansu was driven to suicide after being defrauded.\nWe will continue to put the people first. On the principles of being conducive to combating crime, safeguarding judicial fairness, and protecting the rights and interests of victims, we will strictly crack down on telecommunications fraud in accordance with the law, and effectively safeguard the property security and lawful rights and interests of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Taiwan’s so-called “representative to Japan” Xie Changting recently openly made excuses for Japan’s decision to discharge nuclear-contaminated water into the ocean. He conflated the Fukushima nuclear-contaminated water with the wastewater produced by the normal operation of nuclear power plants, and claimed that Taiwan’s nuclear power plants also discharge wastewater. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The contaminated wastewater from the Fukushima nuclear accident in Japan is fundamentally different from the cooling water normally discharged by nuclear power plants during normal operation. The former is wastewater generated after core meltdown, which directly contacts nuclear fuel and undergoes arbitrary reactions, and it is vastly different from the latter.\nSome people in the DPP authorities have deliberately conflated the two, calling a deer a horse, defending Japan's handling of the Fukushima contaminated wastewater, and recklessly deceiving Taiwan residents, treating the life safety and health of Taiwan compatriots as a plaything. This raises the question of whose interests such people represent and what their true intentions are.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The WHA will be held in Europe in late May. Taiwan media reported that in responding to Taiwan media, the EU Council claimed that the EU supports Taiwan's participation in the meeting. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Taiwan is part of China. Any matter concerning the participation of the Taiwan region of China in international organizations, including activities of the World Health Organization (WHO), must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that their schemes to hype the Taiwan-related issue at the World Health Assembly in order to seek “independence” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202104/t20210428_12349062.htm"],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The cross-strait “Small Three Links” has been suspended for more than a year. Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that the resumption of the “Small Three Links” must take into account not only cross-strait interactions but also the reactions and needs of local residents. We have also noted that the Kinmen County Magistrate and others have repeatedly called for opening the “Small Three Links.”…","As we all know, the “mini three links” were unilaterally cut off by the DPP authorities. We hope they will listen to the appeals of the people of Kinmen. If they truly have sincerity and goodwill, they should take practical measures to resume the “mini three links.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","On April 16, after U.S. President Biden and Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihide Suga held talks, the U.S.-Japan joint statement mentioned the Taiwan issue. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. We urge the United States and Japan to abide by the one-China principle, properly handle the Taiwan question, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs. The DPP authorities, relying on a foreign power and willing to serve as pawns of anti-China forces, will only place Taiwan in a more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","Ko Wen-je stated in a video posted on social media that there are many roads in Taipei named after mainland provinces and cities, raising the topic of “renaming” Taipei's streets. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","The historical and cultural ties between the two sides of the Strait are the bonds that sustain the emotional connection between compatriots on both sides, and they should be respected. We hope that political figures on the island will pay more attention to the livelihood and well-being of the island’s people and spend less time and breath on unnecessary issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, three main types of PLA Navy vessels were commissioned in Hainan. Taiwan's security authorities said the PLA's deployment in the South China Sea has caused tension in surrounding areas. Taiwan's military's ongoing “Han Kuang Exercise” also incorporates these vessels into the exercise scenario. What is your response?","As for the handover and commissioning of People's Liberation Army Navy vessels, please inquire with the Ministry of National Defense. As for the current situation across the Taiwan Strait, the root cause of the tension and turmoil lies in the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to pursue \"Taiwan independence\" and provoke, creating cross-Strait confrontation. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest possible effort, but we will not leave any space for \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities in any form. Our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering, and our capability is beyond doubt.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, some US lawmakers proposed the so-called \"Taiwan International Solidarity Act,\" which questions UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and advocates so-called \"international participation of Taiwan.\" What is your evaluation?","I want to reiterate that Taiwan is part of China, a fact that no person or force can change. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted by the 26th session of the UN General Assembly in 1971, recognized the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government representing all of China. This thoroughly resolved the question of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally, and procedurally, and fully embodies the one-China principle upheld by the United Nations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Taiwan’s Ministry of Health and Welfare said that a small-scale trial of a “vaccine passport” will begin as early as mid-May, and vaccines administered on the mainland are also within its scope. Does the mainland consider relaxing medical observation requirements for Taiwan businesspeople traveling back and forth across the Strait?","We hope that, under the normalization of epidemic prevention and control and as vaccination continues to advance, including vaccination of Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland, cross-Strait personnel exchanges can gradually return to normal. I want to emphasize that since the outbreak of the epidemic, the scientific and necessary entry prevention measures the mainland has taken to ensure the health and well-being of people on both sides of the Strait are fundamentally different from the series of discriminatory restrictions the DPP authorities have imposed, including banning mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan. We believe the DPP authorities should lift unreasonable restrictions as soon as possible so that cross-Strait personnel exchanges can gradually return to normal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company recently announced plans to expand its 28-nanometer chip global production capacity in Nanjing. Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation previously also announced plans to expand 28-nanometer chip production in cooperation in Shenzhen. In this regard, some mainland experts have said that TSMC's expansion may produce a crowding-out competitive effect on SMIC.…","Regarding Taiwan-funded enterprises and Taiwan businesses investing on the mainland, there is a complete system of laws, regulations and management mechanisms. For specific cases, the relevant departments will conduct scientific assessments and handle them in accordance with law and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The Beijing-Taiwan Domestic Waste Management Exchange Symposium was recently held in Beijing and Kaohsiung. Some participants from the Taiwan side said that they have doubts about cross-strait exchange activities and cross-strait video interactions, worrying that they will be labeled and treated in an over-politicized way on the island. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","These normal cross-Strait exchange activities have been obstructed, leaving Taiwan participants feeling doubtful. This is clearly caused by the DPP authorities' unscrupulous suppression and obstruction in recent years, and even the enactment of the so-called “anti-infiltration law,” an evil law. We firmly oppose this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","On the 27th, the Exit and Entry Administration of the Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau set up a service station for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises at the Xiamen Taiwan Businessmen Association. I believe such a mechanism has also been approved by the central government. Could the spokesperson introduce what functions this service station performs? Will it be promoted in other provinces and…","Thank you very much for following this information. It is understood that on April 27, the Taiwan Compatriot and Taiwan Enterprise Service Station of the Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau Exit-Entry Administration was officially unveiled at the Xiamen Taiwanese Businessmen Association. It will handle, in a centralized manner, five-year Taiwan Resident Travel Permits to the Mainland for Taiwan compatriots, guide Taiwan residents in Xiamen through temporary residence registration and residence permit procedures, and handle the relevant procedures for settling permanently on the mainland. It will also regularly station staff on site to provide policy consultation services to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. This measure will provide good service guarantees for the broad Taiwan compatriots who come to Xiamen to invest, start businesses, and live, and it reflects how relevant Xiamen authorities implement equal treatment and pioneer trials to build Xiamen into the first home for Taiwan compatriots to settle on the mainland, which will strongly promote the integrated development of Xiamen and Taiwan. Simply put, there are central-level policies encouraging such practices. Xiamen, Fujian, is pioneering trials and willing to experiment. We are glad to see more localities take further measures to provide more convenient services to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Now people on both sides of the Strait are getting vaccinated. Will the mainland recognize vaccines administered to Taiwan residents in Taiwan? Do you think this requires cross-Strait communication and cooperation?","We hope that under normalized epidemic prevention and control, as vaccination advances, personnel exchanges across the Strait can gradually return to normal. This is a scientific matter that requires scientific assessment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","A recent poll on the island showed that nearly 40% of Taiwan residents agreed with the statement that “if cross-strait political disputes that have accumulated over a long time are to be resolved, a military war will inevitably occur,” while 54% disagreed. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on this?","We do not comment on specific Taiwan opinion polls, because the various polls in Taiwan differ in design, and their results are not entirely consistent.\nI want to stress two points.\nFirst, the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. It is precisely on the basis of this legal and factual reality that the two sides reached the “1992 Consensus,” jointly expressing the position and attitude that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive to seek national reunification,” thereby laying the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. As for the inherent political differences between the two sides, the “1992 Consensus” reflects the two sides' use of political wisdom to set the disputes aside. In the future, the two sides can fully seek solutions through equal consultation on the basis of the one-China principle.\nSecond, the root cause of the current tension and turmoil in cross-Strait relations lies in the provocations of the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, who are seeking “independence.” “Taiwan independence” splits national sovereignty and territory, harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides, and harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The contest between “Taiwan independence” and opposition to “Taiwan independence” is no longer the so-called traditional “political dispute” across the two sides. We believe the broad masses of the Taiwan public are able to distinguish between two contradictions of different natures and recognize the harm and danger of “Taiwan independence.” Compatriots on both sides are all Chinese. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence,” and we will never allow the tragedy of national division to recur. If “Taiwan independence” forces think they can rely on foreign backing to take reckless risks, they will inevitably suffer a heavy blow and push Taiwan into the abyss.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中央社记者","I would like to follow up on the question of cross-Strait personnel exchanges. You just mentioned that since the epidemic began, the DPP authorities have imposed many restrictions. The Taiwan side is now also interested in relaxing some of these exchange restrictions. Which of these does the mainland consider the most important and urgent to resolve? In addition, is it possible for the two sides to communicate…","Since the outbreak of the epidemic, we have not adopted any restrictive measures on Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. We have only adopted some scientifically necessary epidemic prevention and control measures out of a need to protect the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots and others. Who is responsible for interrupting personnel exchanges across the Strait? Everyone understands that it is the DPP authorities. Only the one who tied the bell can untie it. If the DPP authorities are sincere, they should lift these restrictive measures as soon as possible. To this day, mainland residents still cannot travel to Taiwan, and mainland institutions and corporate personnel stationed in Taiwan cannot rotate normally; some personnel stationed in Taiwan have been there for more than a year and cannot return, because once they return, no one can be sent to replace them. And there are the cross-Strait marriage and family issues and the well-known “Xiao Ming” issues — have they all been thoroughly resolved? This is the key to the problem. The DPP authorities’ various so-called “bubbles” are not a cure at the root. Our position is very clear: whoever closed the door should be the one to open it.\nFinally, I wish everyone a happy May Day holiday.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202104/t20210428_12349058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-04-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","April 23 marked the 72nd anniversary of the founding of the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Navy, and the PLA Navy (PLAN) held a series of celebrations for its 72nd birthday. Could you give us more details on that?","President Xi Jinping, also general secretary of the Communist Party of China (CPC) Central Committee and chairman of the Central Military Commission (CMC), attended the commissioning ceremony of three main battle warships of the PLA Navy and boarded the three vessels for inspection on April 23, 2021. PLA officers and soldiers were greatly inspired and invigorated. Besides, the PLAN organized a series of celebrating activities including the launch of a theme video titled \"The PLAN’s Report to the CPC Flag\", which fully reflects the new achievements and fresh look of the navy in its development in the new era. PLAN units carried out various celebrating activities such as flag-raising ceremonies, theme lectures, quiz on naval knowledge, visits to military history museums, reviewing the CPC membership oath, holding theatrical performances, and having full dress on warships, celebrating the Navy’s founding anniversary in the sailors’ ways. The PLAN cooperated with the Military Museum of the Chinese People’s Revolution to offer theme education and publicity activities. Pilots of carrier-based aircraft were invited by the museum to give lectures to middle school students in Beijing.\nAt this point, I can't help thinking of the extraordinary years when the navy was founded. In more than 100 years from 1840 to 1949, China had suffered foreign invasion from sea for more than 470 times. How to defend the coastal areas of the fledgling People’s Republic and safeguard China’s sea frontiers? The Chinese Communists led by Comrade Mao Zedong made arduous explorations into the reinforcement of coastal defenses and development of a naval force. In January 1949, the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee proposed to establish a navy capable of \"defending the country's coastal and riverine areas.\" On April 23, the CPC Central Committee and the CMC telegraphed an order (to the Third Field Army of the PLA) to establish the navy of the PLA East China Military Command and appoint Zhang Aiping as commander and political commissar of the naval force. April 23 later became the founding day of the PLAN. On the afternoon of April 23, 1949, amidst the rumbling fire of cannons in the Crossing-the-Yangtze-River Campaign, and with only several old warships rebelled from the Kuomintang, the establishment of the navy of the PLA East China Military Command was announced at the Baima Temple in a small village in Taizhou, east China’s Jiangsu Province, where the commanding post of the Third Field Army for the Crossing-the-Yangtze-River Campaign was located.\nWith only 13 people at that time, the navy of the PLA East China Military Command seemed to be the smallest naval force in the world. However, they held the firm conviction that, with the 13 persons as the vanguards, a naval force consisting of 130,000 troops would surely be built. In August of the same year, Chairman Mao wrote an inscription for the navy of the East China Military Command: \"We must build a navy capable of safeguarding our coastlines and effectively defending us against potential imperialist invasions.\" Since then, the PLAN embarked on the road of development amid great difficulties and grew up through battles. Cutting through waves and experiencing storms and wind to move forward, it has developed from scratch to possessing all the five arms with both nuclear and conventional weapons. From coastal waters to high seas, from defending sovereignty of China’s territorial waters to safeguarding world peace, the PLAN has made great accomplishments. History has proven and will continue to prove that the PLA Navy has always been an iron Great Wall at sea that defends national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and has always been a staunch force serving the building of the maritime community with a shared future.\n(The Baima Temple, Taizhou, Jiangsu)","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-04/29/content_4884413.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-04-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, US military ships and aircraft have been frequently operating in the seas and airspace around China. In April, the guided-missile destroyer USS John S. McCain sailed through the Taiwan Strait and the Theodore Roosevelt Carrier Strike Group was operating in the South China Sea. The website of US Navy recently published photos of the commander of guided-missile destroyer USS Mustin observing the PLAN…","Recently, during a regular training of the PLAN aircraft carrier Liaoning formation in relevant sea areas, the US guided-missile destroyer Mustin kept having close reconnaissance of the Chinese naval formation, which seriously obstructed regular training of the Chinese side and threatened the safety of ships and personnel of both sides. It’s of an egregious nature. The Chinese naval ships on site warned the US ship to leave. The Ministry of National Defense has lodged a solemn representation with the US side in this regard.\nSince the current US administration took office, the number of activities conducted by US warships and surveillance aircraft in the sea areas around China has increased by more than 20% and 40% respectively over the same period last year. The US frequently sends ships and aircraft to conduct activities in waters and airspace around China, escalating regional militarization and threatening regional peace and stability. China is firmly opposed to that. We urge the US side to strictly restrain its troops on the ground, abide by the \"Rules of Behaviour for Safety of Air and Maritime Encounters between China and the US\" and \"International Maritime Collision Prevention Regulations\", so as to prevent the recurrence of similar dangerous incidents.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-04/29/content_4884413.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-04-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media reports, targeting Chinese mainland's military aircraft, the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities have recently set up the so-called surveillance, warning and destruction zones in the \"airspace over Taiwan Strait\", and set a \"red line\" for reaction when Chinese mainland's military aircraft approach areas 30 nautical miles from Taiwan Island. Meanwhile, according to the…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The PLA’s exercises and training near Taiwan are aimed at the provocation by the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces seeking \"independence\" and the interference of external forces, rather than at Taiwan compatriots. All the zones or lines set by the DPP authorities across the Taiwan Strait are totally invalid and will not shake our resolve and will to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities’ strategy of \"seeking independence by force\" is but like a mantis trying to stop a chariot and will only lead to its own destruction.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-04/29/content_4884413.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-04-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to official media reports, the Liaoning aircraft carrier formation has been conducting training in waters around Taiwan recently. Could you please brief us on the training? Will such training activities be organized regularly for the aircraft carrier formation in the future?","The PLAN Liaoning aircraft carrier formation recently conducted routine drills and training in waters around Taiwan and related waters in the South China Sea, aiming to test the performance of weapons and equipment, and improve the troops’ capability to perform missions and tasks. As for the second question, I want to say that the aircraft carrier is not a \"homebody\", and it will be the norm for the aircraft carriers to sail far away.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-04/29/content_4884413.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-04-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On April 23, a Type 075 amphibious assault ship was commissioned to the PLA Navy. Some media commented that the commissioning of this type of warship is to make substantive preparation for \"military unification\" of Taiwan. What is your comment?","It is a common aspiration of all Chinese people to solve the Taiwan question and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland. Our position on Taiwan is consistent and clear. We adhere to the major principles and policies on works related to Taiwan, uphold the one-China principle and the 1992 Consensus, promote the peaceful development of cross-Straits relations and the reunification of the motherland, and also remain highly vigilant against and resolutely contain the separatist activities for \"Taiwan independence\". We will strive for the prospects of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and greatest efforts.\nThe \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their actions have openly challenged the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, gravely harmed the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and seriously jeopardized the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We will never leave any room for any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, and will always be fully prepared to deal with external interference and separatist activities for \"Taiwan independence\". The purpose is to promote peaceful reunification of the motherland. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces act willfully and even make reckless moves, we will take all necessary measures to resolutely crush their attempt for \"Taiwan independence\" and safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-04/29/content_4884413.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2021-04-30","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US Director of National Intelligence said that she sees views in Taiwan hardening in favor of independence. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","The root cause of the tension across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are making provocations by seeking independence. I want to stress that China is firmly resolved in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and has every confidence and capability to frustrate all forms of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. The US should fully recognize that \"Taiwan independence\" is harmful and dangerous, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, be prudent with its words and actions, avoid sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces, and refrain from undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1872887.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1872880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-04-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Japanese government recently released the “Diplomatic Bluebook”, claiming that China’s military rise shows clear momentum, that its military spending has grown substantially, and that China’s strengthening military power and its activities in the East China Sea and South China Sea have caused strong concern in the international community, including Japan. In addition, the Bluebook positions Taiwan as an…","The Japanese government recently published a diplomatic white paper that hypes up the so-called “China military threat,” maliciously attacks and smears China, and rudely interferes in China's internal affairs. This is extremely wrong and irresponsible. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues a defensive national defense policy. Its military expenditure and military development have always been open and transparent. China adheres to the policy of coordinated development of national defense and economic construction and reasonably determines the scale of defense spending. For nearly 30 years, defense spending has accounted for less than 2% of GDP each year, which is not only lower than that of major countries in the world but also lower than the world average of 2.6%.\nThe development of China's national defense forces is needed both to safeguard its own sovereignty, security and development interests and to maintain international and regional peace and stability. The Chinese military practices the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind and provides public security goods such as peacekeeping, escort, humanitarian rescue and disaster relief, and anti-epidemic cooperation to the international community, continuously injecting positive energy into maintaining world peace and stability.\nChina's position on maritime issues has been consistent and clear. The Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands are an inseparable part of China's territory. China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands and their adjacent waters. The determination and will of the Chinese government and military to defend national sovereignty, security and development interests are as firm as a rock, and at the same time China is committed to resolving relevant disputes through dialogue and consultation. As long as a country has no intention of infringing on China's interests, it will not feel threatened.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs. China will never allow any country to interfere in the Taiwan question in any way. China must and will be reunified. Japan should not stretch its hand too far, and it should certainly not harbor any unrealistic illusions, which would be very dangerous.\nSince modern times, Japanese militarism launched wars of aggression abroad, bringing profound disasters to regional countries, including China. Some Japanese politicians, disregarding their own notorious record, have gone to great lengths to smear and slander China. What they really intend to do is worthy of high vigilance. We urge the Japanese side to draw lessons from history, stop fabricating rumors and smearing China, view China and the Chinese military objectively and rationally, and make constructive efforts to promote the healthy and stable development of China-Japan relations.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrth/16112910.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-05-06","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","On May 5, the G7 foreign ministers' meeting issued a communiqué, expressing concern over issues concerning Xinjiang, Tibet and Hong Kong as well as the situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea, and voicing support for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly. Does China have any comment?","The G7 foreign ministers' meeting launched groundless accusations against China, blatantly interfered in China's internal affairs and engaged in anachronistic bloc politics. This is gross interference in China's sovereignty, flagrant trampling on norms of international relations and violation of the trend for peace, development and win-win cooperation of our times. China strongly condemns it.\nIssues concerning Xinjiang, Tibet and Hong Kong are all China's domestic affairs. China's sovereignty, rights and interests over the Diaoyu Dao, its affiliated islands, islands in the South China Sea and their adjacent waters are rooted in ample factual and legal basis. The participation of China's Taiwan region in activities of international organizations, including the WHO, which consists of sovereign nations, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is an important principle established by UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nThe G7, as a grouping of developed nations, should take more concrete actions to boost world economic recovery and help accelerate developing countries' growth, rather than stoking confrontation and difference and disrupting global economic recovery.\nIn the context of COVID-19, G7 finds within its membership the worst-stricken and the most medically-advanced nations. As such, it is naturally expected to focus on international cooperation in fighting the virus and promoting the equitable distribution of vaccines, instead of hoarding vaccines at home while offering merely superficial lip service when it comes to helping other countries in need. Still less should it blame others or meddle in their efforts in a condescending manner to undermine the top international priority of jointly fighting the pandemic.\nThe G7 claims to be a grouping of democracies, but as a latest poll suggests respondents in 53 countries and regions see the US as the top threat to global democracy, we haven't seen any comment or action from the G7.\nWe urge relevant countries to take a hard look at their own problems, redress their self-serving approach in fighting COVID-19 and stop the wrong practice of stretching national security concept. Attempts to concoct all sorts of excuses to meddle in China's internal affairs, harm Chinese sovereignty and tarnish China's image in disregard of basic norms of international relations are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1873782.shtml","",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-10","Hua Chunying","Reuters","There are reports that China asked UN member states not to attend a virtual Xinjiang event planned by Germany, the US and the UK on Wednesday. Do you have any comment?","The US, rallying a handful of countries like the UK and Germany, plans to hold the so-called virtual meeting on Xinjiang and falsely calls it a sideline event of the UN. This reminds me of the farce back in January this year when US Permanent Representative to the UN Kelly Craft, abusing her capacity, sneaked into the UN General Assembly Hall to make a video of virtual interaction with students in Taiwan. The US and the few countries it has assembled are abusing the resources and platform of the UN to smear and attack China to serve selfish political interests. This is a shameful travesty of the UN. I must point out that a handful of Western countries such as the US, the UK and Germany can by no means represent the UN, even less the international community.\nThe US claims that it cares about the human rights of Muslims, but it is the US that killed more Muslims than any other country in the world. Putting aside the long-standing systemic racial discrimination in the US, we know the US has waged wars and carried out military operations in the name of \"counterterrorism\" in 80-plus countries around the world. More than 800,000 people have died from direct war violence, most of whom were civilians, and tens of millions of people have been displaced. Today, over 20 million people in Afghanistan, Iraq, Syria and other countries are still living in extreme conditions. Nearly 600,000 Americans have died from COVID-19, and I noted that a study by the University of Washington estimates the real number may far exceed that. How hypocritical it is for the US to watch callously as tens of thousands of Muslims in Afghanistan, Iraq and Syria died at its hand, and as more than 600,000 Americans died from COVID-19, and then to go all out and fabricate the so-called human rights issues in Xinjiang!\nIf there were a real human rights problem in Xinjiang, wouldn't the Organization of Islamic Cooperation and its over 50 member states be more concerned than the US? The OIC sent a delegation to visit Xinjiang upon invitation, during which it fully recognized the importance the Chinese government attaches to protecting the rights of Muslim believers and spoke highly of China's preventive counterterrorism and de-radicalization efforts. At the 46th session of the UN Human Rights Council, more than 80 countries, including Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates and other Muslim countries, voiced their support for China's position on Xinjiang-related issues in different ways. For the United States, a country that has killed nearly a million Muslims and infringed upon the human rights of tens of millions more, to profess concern over the human rights of Uyghurs in Xinjiang is just like the weasel paying respect to the hen without the best of intentions.\nAs is pointed out in a recent article titled \"Things to Know about All the Lies on Xinjiang: How Have They Come About?\" on Chinese media, the anti-China forces in the US and the West seem to have developed a routine for manufacturing and peddling lies and rumors to attack China. First, rumors are packaged as information leaked by \"scholars\" and \"victims\", which are then hyped up by media, and followed by official intervention. With this routine, \"witness accounts\" and \"reports\" emerge one after another, \"directors\" and \"actors\" come on stage in various disguises. In response, China has issued 12 white papers on Xinjiang and \"Fact Check: Lies on Xinjiang-related issues versus the truth\". The Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region has also held more than 40 special press conferences to share the real situation in Xinjiang. I believe you all have a very clear idea of what the issue is truly about. As we all noted, Lawrence Wilkerson, chief of staff to former Secretary of State Colin Powell and Sibel Edmonds, former FBI translator, admitted that they never care about people or any ethnic minority in Xinjiang. They only want to use them to foment unrest and destabilize China from internal places rather than external in order to realize their conspiracy of disrupting Xinjiang and containing China. There are many media reports about this. US independent news website The Greyzone published an article exposing how anti-China \"scholar\" Adrian Zenz has fabricated the centenary lie of \"genocide\" in Xinjiang through data abuse, information distortion and false witness account. The Hong Kong-based South China Morning Post, the Australian Citizens Party's weekly publication The Australian Alert Service, and Brazil's Estado de Minas and many other media ran reports and articles to show the effective counter-terrorism work in Xinjiang and expose the double standard on fighting terrorism held by Western countries including the US and their geopolitical conspiracy to use Xinjiang to contain China. The Singapore-based Lianhe Zaobao, the website Project Syndicate, the Sweden-based Transnational Foundation for Peace and Future Research and the US independent website Counterpunch published articles or released reports to point out that the US claim of \"forced labor\" and \"genocide\" in Xinjiang is totally groundless. A recently-released feature report by former mayor of Frogn municipality in Norway, \"The Xinjiang Genocide Determination As Agenda\", laid bare the lack of objectivity, verity and integrity of a report alleging genocide in Xinjiang by US think tanks. Another example, French author Maxime Vivas in his book \"Uyghurs: To Put an End to Fake News\" proved that all sorts of lies and rumors on Xinjiang are baseless with his own two trips there.\nSome in the US have repeatedly hyped up the so-called \"human rights issue\" in Xinjiang on nothing but the words of merely about 20 false witnesses and scholars. By contrast, there are so many Xinjiang residents who told their own stories in the press conferences on Xinjiang held by China and so many people from the international community like those who disclosed the true intention of Xinjiang-related lies and rumors fabricated by the US and the West as I just cited. They have far exceeded the false witnesses and scholars treasured by the US in terms of number and representation. Isn't the US a democracy? Even from a democratic perspective, certain individuals on the US side choose to buy the \"account\" of 20-plus false witnesses and actors but refuse to listen to the voice of people whose number is several times, ten times, one hundred times, one thousand times, even ten thousand times greater than the former, refuse to heed the call of the 1.4 billion Chinese people, including more than 25 million people of all ethnic groups in Xinjiang. Is it in line with their self-styled democratic values? In the final analysis, they are too cowardly to face the truth and are afraid of the truth.\nBut no matter how deep they bury their heads into the sand or how hard they try to cover their ears, the facts and truth about Xinjiang are there for all to see. These politicians in the US and other Western countries have been fabricating lies and rumors without any scruples out of the vicious intention of suppressing and containing China, but this farce is being seen through by more and more people. The cheap shot will only accelerate the erosion of the credibility of the US itself. So they should know better than keeping up the play.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347038.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1874625.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-10","Hua Chunying","Beijing Youth Daily","On May 7, US Secretary of State Blinken released a statement calling on the WHO Director-General to invite Taiwan to participate as an observer at the WHA. The statement reads that \"excluding the interests of 24 million people at the WHA serves only to imperil, not advance, our shared global health objectives\" and would be detrimental to collective international efforts to prevent future health crises. The G7…","China has stated its solemn position on the content concerning Taiwan in the communiqué of the G7 foreign ministers' meeting. The statement by US Secretary of State Blinken gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and interferes in China's domestic affairs. We deplore and reject it.\nThere is only one China in the world. The participation of China's Taiwan region in activities of international organizations, including the WHO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a key principle established by UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1, which has received broad support from the international community. It is the DPP authority's entrenched \"Taiwan-independence\" separatist position that has depleted the political foundation for the region's participation in the WHA. The DPP authority knows only too well that it bears full responsibility for this.\nDriven by political agenda, the US is pushing the narrative that excluding Taiwan from the WHA will imperil shared global health objectives and would be detrimental to efforts to prevent future health crises. This is nothing but a political lie. As a matter of fact, no one cares more about the health and welfare of our compatriots in Taiwan than us. After COVID-19 broke out, the Central Government of China invited health experts from the Taiwan region, before inviting anyone else outside the mainland, to visit Wuhan, Hubei Province to see the situation on the ground. We shared 52 epidemic-prevention documents with Taiwan in 13 batches and updated it on the latest information for multiple times, including information on Taiwan residents infected in the mainland. We also notified it in particular of the information that the mainland shared the genome sequencing and routes to obtain relevant genome sequencing. By May 5, the Central Government had given the Taiwan region 258 updates about the COVID-19 outbreak. In March this year, a cross-strait virtual seminar on prevention policies and experience-sharing was held to share technical experience.\nBased on the one-China principle, the Central Government of China has made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. According to incomplete statistics, since 2020, health experts in Taiwan have participated in 16 WHO technical activities, including important meetings like the fourth Global Vaccine and Immunization Research Forum and WHO Strategic Advisory Group of Experts on Immunization meetings. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region. Taiwan also has an account to log onto the WHO event information website and has timely access to WHO information on public health emergencies through the website and the daily updates. It can also report incidents to the WHO in a timely manner. With the approval of China's Central Government, the WHO Secretariat notified health experts in Taiwan three times of information about COVID-19. Taiwan has also joined COVAX. Experts in the region attended multiple times WHO Strategic Advisory Group of Experts on Immunization meetings and got timely and full access to COVID-related information.\nI want to draw your attention to one point. Isn't it self-contradictory for the Taiwan authority to tout itself as a model for epidemic prevention and for the US to pile praise on Taiwan's anti-epidemic outcomes while sensationalizing the narrative of imperiling global heath objectives? This exposes fully that the US claim that excluding the 24 million Taiwan people at the WHA would be detrimental to collective international efforts to prevent future health crises is purely political manipulation to justify Taiwan's participation in the WHA.\nI would like to stress again that the Taiwan question bears on China's core interests, where there is not a single inch for compromise. As COVID-19 continues to rage, this WHA's primary task is to focus on global anti-pandemic cooperation. We urge the US to stop hyping up Taiwan-related issues, which will not help with the global anti-virus cooperation and will be firmly rejected by the vast majority of members of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347038.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1874625.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-11","Hua Chunying","Xinhua News Agency","Chas W Freeman Jr, former US assistant secretary of defense and a veteran diplomat, published an article on the website of East Asia Forum titled \"Washington is playing a losing game with China\". He wrote in the article that the US tried to cripple and contain China with an escalating campaign of \"maximum pressure\". There are US aircraft and ships aggressively patrolling China's borders, but no Chinese aircraft…","Many people have noted this article by Mr. Chas Freeman. He aptly laid out some basic facts, facts that we know for certain but some in the US deliberately ignore or disregard. In short, China is not a threat to the United States. Instead, the threat is within the United States itself. The US, for quite some time, especially since the previous administration, has been doing everything it can to resort to the threat of force, political isolation, economic sanctions and technological blockade against China, interferes in China's internal affairs on issues related to Hong Kong, Taiwan and Xinjiang and intimidates and beguiles other countries into forming an anti-China clique. Such practice is illegal and immoral, and will not succeed. It will only harm the interests of the US and its people in the end.\nThe US now begins every conversation with competition and eyes China as a major strategic competitor. As a leading sporting nation and a major Olympic player, the US should have a deep understanding of the Olympic spirit of \"faster, higher and stronger\". The pursuit of athletes is to constantly improve themselves, outperform themselves and achieve better results, rather than to undercut or maliciously disrupt others, otherwise they will only be sent off for breaking the rules.\nChina's strategic intent has been open and transparent. We never aim to overtake the US. Instead, our goal is to constantly improve and go beyond ourselves, make sure that Chinese people can live a better life, and that China will contribute more to world peace and development through its own development.\nAs the world's largest economies, China and the US have highly intertwined interests, and we stand for mutually beneficial and win-win cooperation. Such cooperation calls for mutual accommodation to achieve reciprocal benefit, where there is no room for one to unilaterally impose a list of conditions or requests on another. China will not shy away from competition. However, the competition should be fair and just, and market rules should be followed, instead of depriving other countries of their normal and legitimate right to development by backstabbing or force.\nI think Mr. Freeman put it very well. The US should focus on improving its own competitiveness, which can only be achieved through cooperation. We hope that the US government will listen to the just views of visionary people at home and from the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210511_9170741.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210511_9171262.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-11","Hua Chunying","The Paper","At the Copenhagen Democracy Summit 2021 held from May 10 to 11, Danish foreign minister denounced as \"deplorable\" recent sanctions imposed by China against the EU. The event also invited those supporting independence for Taiwan and Hong Kong. Does China have a comment?","The so-called Copenhagen Democracy Summit is nothing short of a political farce filled with ideological bias. Its organizer, the Alliance for Democracies Foundation, was sanctioned by China for gravely undermining China's sovereignty and interests through its longtime efforts to spread malicious lies and disinformation. Relevant measures taken by China is necessitated by the need to uphold its interests and come as a necessary, legitimate and just response to unilateral sanctions imposed by the European side against relevant Chinese individuals and entities.\nThe Taiwan question and matters concerning Hong Kong are purely China's domestic affairs where no foreign government, organization or individual has any right to meddle. We urge relevant countries, organizations and politicians to earnestly respect China's sovereignty and refrain from sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan-independence\" and \"Hong Kong independence\" forces.\nSince the event is called a \"democracy summit\", I would like to spend some time talking about democracy. Democracy is a common value of humanity. There are various ways to realize democracy. True democracy must be rooted in the realities of a country and serve its people. The socialist democracy practiced by China is a whole-process democracy and the most representative democracy. It embodies the will of the people, fits the country's realities and is thus endorsed by the people.\nThe Chinese government puts people front and center. In the face of the sudden onslaught of COVID-19, it put people's life and health first, took the most rigorous control measures and first brought the epidemic under control, making it possible for people to carry on with their life and work as normal. I saw media reports that after going through the epidemic, the Chinese people's trust in the government increased to 98 percent. This is true democracy.\nChina works to ensure that development outcomes benefit all the people in a more equitable manner. The CPC and the Chinese government serve the Chinese people heart and soul and take people's happiness and satisfaction as their pursuit and the yardstick to measure their work. After over seven decades of relentless efforts, the 1.4 billion Chinese people all shirked off poverty, with no one left behind. All have access to means of subsistence, housing, education and health care. People are able to lead fulfilling lives free from the sufferings of war, conflict, poverty and hunger. This is true democracy.\nThe Chinese government always solicits people's needs, relies on their wisdom, and enables them to be their own masters. When drafting the 14th five-year plan, the Chinese government, taking into full consideration the role of the Internet today, collected a large number of comments and recommendations from online channels, allowing people to voice their will and appeals. People's affairs are handled by themselves through consultation. This is true democracy.\nDemocracy is not about throwing a summit and putting forward some slogans, still less should it be used as a political tool to suppress other countries. We hope a handful of European politicians can honor the spirit of democracy and do something real for their people's safety and welfare.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210511_9170741.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210511_9171262.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-11","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","As WHA registration closed yesterday, Taiwan said it didn't get an invitation and claimed that suppression by the mainland led to the result. Taiwan's foreign affairs authority called the mainland's position on proper arrangement for Taiwan's participation in WHO a lie and accused the mainland of misquoting UNSCR 2758 and relevant WHO resolution. Does the foreign ministry have any comment? My second question is,…","On your first question regarding Taiwan not receiving an invitation to the 74th session of the WHA. There is only one China in the world. The participation of China's Taiwan region in activities of international organizations, including the WHO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a key principle established by UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. The DPP authority, since coming to power in 2016, has been insisting on the \"Taiwan-independence\" separatist position and refusing to acknowledge that the mainland and Taiwan belong to the same China, which has depleted the political foundation for the region's participation in the WHA. The DPP authority knows only too well that it caused the current situation where Taiwan couldn't attend the WHA.\nTaiwan compatriots are our siblings. The Central Government of China takes all necessary measures to guarantee the health and welfare of our compatriots in Taiwan. After COVID-19 broke out, the Central Government of China invited health experts from the Taiwan region, before inviting anyone else outside the mainland, to visit Wuhan, Hubei Province to see the situation on the ground. We shared 52 epidemic-prevention documents with Taiwan in 13 batches and updated it on the latest information for multiple times, including information on Taiwan residents infected in the mainland. We also notified it in particular of the information of the genome sequencing and routes to obtain relevant genome sequencing that the mainland shared with WHO. By May 10, the Central Government had given the Taiwan region 259 updates about the COVID-19 outbreak. In March this year, a cross-strait virtual seminar on prevention policies and experience-sharing was held to share technical experience.\nBased on the one-China principle, the Central Government of China has made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. According to incomplete statistics, since 2020, health experts in Taiwan have participated in 16 WHO technical activities. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region. Taiwan also has an account to log onto the WHO event information website and has timely access to WHO information on public health emergencies through the website and the daily updates. It can also report incidents to the WHO in a timely manner. With the approval of China's Central Government, the WHO Secretariat notified health experts in Taiwan three times of information about COVID-19. Taiwan has also joined COVAX. Experts in the region attended multiple times WHO Strategic Advisory Group of Experts on Immunization meetings and got timely and full access to COVID-related information.\nThe DPP authority hypes up the so-called WHA participation issue with the true intention of seeking independence by taking advantage of the epidemic. We firmly reject it. As has been proven time and again, the one-China principle is the overwhelming trend of the international community with broad support. The DPP authority's attempts will never succeed. We advise it to stop using the pandemic to engage in political manipulation and stop further humiliating itself.\nAs to the \"misquotation\" of UNGA Resolution 2758, how could it be? UNGA Resolution 2758 recognizes the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations. There is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is part of China. China's representation at the UN certainly covers the Taiwan region.\nNow, coming to your second question. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, China has upheld the vision of building a global community of health for all, and done its best to provide help, support and vaccines to developing countries including El Salvador. The anti-epidemic cooperation between China and El Salvador serves as a model in the region, demonstrating that the one-China principle conforms to international justice and trend of our times. On the basis of the one-China principle, China will continue to conduct practical cooperation across the board with El Salvador and other Central American countries. We are glad to see our vaccines help relevant countries fight the epidemic and protect the life and health of local people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210511_9170741.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210511_9171262.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-12","Hua Chunying","CRI","It is reported that Honduras President Hernandez recently stated that Honduras would purchase vaccines from China's mainland though El Salvador, which would help Honduras to break geopolitical blockade. He also mentioned the intention to set up a business office in China for further purchase. Do you have any comment?","Vaccine is the hope for saving lives. Since the outbreak of Covid-19, China has been adhering to the vision of building a community of shared future for mankind and a global community of health for all, and making significant contribution to reducing the vaccination divide and promoting the accessibility and affordability of vaccines in developing countries. Relevant cooperation is totally aboveboard, and highly appreciated by the international community, including central American countries, which serves as a good demonstration.\nI'm not sure what the statement of so-called \"geopolitical blockade\" made by some people in Honduras is driving at. I want to reiterate that there is only one China in the world, and that Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China, which is a fact based on history and jurisprudence. The correct path is to make the right choice that is in line with the trend and people's aspiration.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347040.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210512_9171263.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","I am hosting today's regular Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. It's been a while; welcome, everyone. Questions now begin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","On April 29, Fujian Province issued an announcement on the pilot work of a “fast track” for quarantine entry of Taiwan compatriots coming to Fujian, but on May 8 it announced a suspension of implementation. Could the spokesperson introduce the background to the launch of this pilot “fast track” and the relevant situation regarding the suspension?","The launch of the pilot “convenience channel” for quarantine of Taiwan compatriots entering Fujian is aimed, under the normalized epidemic prevention and control situation and based on the actual needs of Fujian-Taiwan exchanges, at facilitating urgently needed work and business exchanges for Taiwan compatriots coming to Fujian, promoting personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan, and serving the normal production and daily life of Taiwan compatriots in Fujian. The relevant work plan was carefully studied and scientifically assessed by all relevant parties, and was judged necessary and feasible.\nThe reason for suspending the pilot work has been explained by the relevant parties in Fujian Province. According to the dynamic management requirements of the pilot work plan for the “convenience channel,” if more than 10 locally confirmed cases occur on the island within 14 consecutive days, the “convenience channel” measures for the entire Taiwan region will be suspended. After the Fujian Provincial authorities issued the announcement on the quarantine “convenience channel” for Taiwan compatriots entering Fujian on April 29, several locally confirmed cases appeared in the Taiwan region, with more than a dozen new cases added between April 30 and May 7. On May 8, the relevant parties in Fujian Province, in accordance with the dynamic management requirements, issued an announcement deciding to adjust the arrangements for the pilot work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, the Taiwan Affairs Office has repeatedly named Wu Chao-hsu's “Taiwan independence” remarks. Public opinion speculates that the mainland has listed Wu Chao-hsu as one of the “diehard Taiwan independence” elements. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","Resolutely cracking down on diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and stopping “Taiwan independence” separatist acts is the inherent meaning and necessary condition for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Wu Zhaoxie has repeatedly and arrogantly carried out “Taiwan independence” provocations, maliciously defamed the mainland, incited cross-strait confrontation, seriously endangered peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harmed the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Against such diehard “Taiwan independence” elements, we will take all necessary measures to punish them severely and hold them accountable for life in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210512_12351725.htm"],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Given the shortage of vaccines on the island, some Taiwan compatriots hope the mainland can donate COVID-19 vaccines and testing reagents to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We attach great importance to the life, health and safety of Taiwan compatriots. For Taiwan compatriots residing permanently on the mainland, we treat them equally and without discrimination in vaccination arrangements, whether during the emergency use phase of mainland COVID-19 vaccines or after conditional market approval.\nOn May 7, the inactivated novel coronavirus vaccine researched and produced by the Beijing Institute of Biological Products of China National Pharmaceutical Group received emergency use authorization from the World Health Organization and was included in the global “Emergency Use List.” It is a safe, effective, high-quality vaccine certified by the WHO. As of May 10, the mainland had cumulatively reported 332.96 million COVID-19 vaccine doses administered. On the issue of importing mainland COVID-19 vaccines and test reagents into Taiwan, the DPP authorities have disregarded the health and well-being of the Taiwan public, fabricated all kinds of absurd excuses, and refused at every turn. This is entirely the result of political demons at work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Ma Ying-jeou called on Tsai Ing-wen to return to the “original, unadulterated ‘1992 Consensus’.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” embodies the historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and it is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations. From 2008 to 2016, the reason cross-Strait relations were able to present a situation of peaceful development is that both sides established basic political mutual trust on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Since 2016, the reason cross-Strait relations have encountered setbacks and even turmoil is rooted in the refusal of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which unilaterally undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe crux of the cross-Strait problem and its solution are very clear. We have repeatedly stated that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and its core meaning is recognized, there is no problem with dialogue and exchanges across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","After the “22 measures for agriculture and forestry” were issued, they drew much attention from Taiwan compatriots. What progress has been made in implementation in various localities?","On March 17, the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” were issued, attracting attention from all sectors on both sides and wide praise from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. At present, localities and relevant departments are comprehensively advancing implementation, with positive progress.\nOn March 25, Sichuan Province convened a symposium with 11 provincial-level departments to implement the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” guiding the upgrading of Taiwan-related agricultural parks and continuing to deepen agricultural exchanges and cooperation between Sichuan and Taiwan.\nFujian Province has advanced the implementation of the vast majority of the measures in the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry.” On March 31, Fujian Province issued the Notice on Several Measures for Deepening the Integrated Development of Rural Construction and Rural Innovation between Fujian and Taiwan, further exploring new paths for integrated rural construction and rural innovation across the Taiwan Strait. It supports rural revitalization in four areas: expanding fields of Fujian-Taiwan cooperation, increasing financial support, improving guidance and matchmaking services, and strengthening organizational work systems.\nOn April 8, Zhejiang Province held a special matchmaking and promotion meeting to implement the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” and the “Eight Measures Benefiting Taiwan Youth,” launching 22 rural construction and homestay projects and becoming the first to share development opportunities in agriculture and forestry in Zhejiang with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth.\nOn April 26, Shandong Province held the 10th Cross-Strait Leisure and Sightseeing Agriculture Exchange Conference, promoting integrated development of cross-Strait leisure and sightseeing agriculture. Weifang City issued implementation rules for the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” specifying responsible units, contact persons, contact phone numbers, and service locations for each measure, providing concrete operational guidance for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises to obtain policy support.\nThe Guizhou Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, together with relevant departments, repeatedly visited and conducted research on Taiwan-invested enterprises, Taiwan industrial parks, and Taiwan-related research institutions in the province, publicized the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” distributed the Guide to Investment, Work, and Life Services for Taiwan Compatriots in Guizhou, and advanced related implementation work.\nWe will continue to work with relevant departments to strengthen overall guidance and press forward with implementing the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry” thoroughly and in detail, so that more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises benefit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, some scholars and media on the island have hyped the illegal and invalid “Treaty of San Francisco,” attempting to challenge the one-China principle. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The historical and legal fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China cannot be changed by anyone or any force. In 1945, the Chinese people, together with the peoples of other countries around the world, achieved the great victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and Taiwan was thereby restored and returned to the embrace of the motherland. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, have clearly and unmistakably confirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan.\nThe so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty” is a product fabricated by a very small number of Western countries during the Cold War. It wantonly tramples on international law and interferes in other countries' internal affairs, and it is entirely illegal and void. We made our solemn position of never recognizing it clear from the very beginning. This position is long-standing and consistent, and has never changed in the slightest. The DPP authorities hype up this illegal and void historical scrap of paper, attempting to confuse the public, mislead public opinion, and challenge the one-China principle universally recognized by the international community. In the end, this will be in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 74th World Health Assembly will convene on May 24, and Taiwan has not received an invitation for the fifth consecutive year. We note that recently some foreign forces have successively claimed to support Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly, and the DPP authorities said they will continue to seek assistance from relevant countries. What is the spokesperson's comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. The participation of the Taiwan region in international organizations, including the activities of the World Health Organization, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is the fundamental principle affirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1.\nFrom 2009 to 2016, the Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei.” This was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” under which both sides adhered to the one-China principle. It does not constitute a precedent. Since the Democratic Progressive Party authorities took office in May 2016, they have obstinately insisted on a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” They have unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations, which directly led to the Taiwan region being unable to participate in the World Health Assembly. The responsibility lies entirely with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities keep hyping up the Taiwan-related issue at the World Health Assembly and fabricating the political lie of a so-called “gap in the international epidemic prevention system.” They are using the epidemic to engage in extensive political manipulation, and their real aim is to “use the epidemic to seek independence” (“以疫谋独”), rather than to genuinely care about the health and well-being of the people on the island.\nCompatriots in Taiwan are our flesh-and-blood kin. After the COVID-19 epidemic broke out last year, we were the first to invite Taiwanese health experts to visit Wuhan, Hubei, to conduct on-site inspections, and we repeatedly notified the Taiwan region of the latest information on epidemic prevention and control. We also made a special notification to share with the World Health Organization the virus gene sequences and information on how to obtain the relevant gene sequences. Since 2020, medical and technical experts from the Taiwan region of China have participated in 16 technical activities of the World Health Organization, including important conferences such as the 4th Global Forum on Vaccines and Immunization Research.\nI want to emphasize that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no interference from outside. We hope the relevant parties will abide by the one-China principle through concrete actions. Playing the “Taiwan card” to make trouble for China will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210512_12351720.htm"],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","It is reported that Taiwan’s labor authorities recently issued a letter requiring that job postings recruiting personnel to work on the mainland not be published, with heavy fines for violators. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan compatriots’ choice to work on the mainland is their personal freedom and legitimate right. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have gone to great lengths to obstruct it, undermining Taiwan residents’ right to access employment information and development opportunities and harming the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. This will surely lose public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","“Taiwan independence” figures such as Ku Kuan-min recently again advocated “Taiwan's status is undetermined” and clamored for “constitutional revision to rectify the name.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","There is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. No matter how “Taiwan independence” separatist forces distort historical facts or package their “Taiwan independence” schemes, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China. We solemnly warn a small handful of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements: the trend of reunification is irresistible; those who comply will prosper and those who defy will perish. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and anyone who defies the law will certainly be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently claimed that the mainland has recently pre-drawn “red lines” to prevent Taiwan from further participating in “international cooperation,” while continuously carrying out “united front” work against Taiwan, forcing Taiwan to accept the cross-strait pattern set by the mainland. This is also the main root of the current instability in the Taiwan Strait. What is the…","The root of the current tense and volatile cross-strait relations lies in the DPP authorities' denial of the “1992 Consensus,” their continual creation of cross-strait opposition and confrontation, their collusion with external forces, and their “independence-seeking” provocations. Recently, in order to cope with public dissatisfaction on the island and divert public attention, they deliberately raised the pitch of “Taiwan independence,” intensified attacks and provocations against the mainland, and willingly served as the vanguard of Western anti-China forces. They obstruct cross-strait exchanges, sharpen cross-strait antagonism, and damage the interests and well-being of the broad public, and have thoroughly torn off the mask of their so-called “easing cross-strait relations” and “encouraging cross-strait exchanges.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, the British magazine The Economist described Taiwan as “the most dangerous place on earth.” In response, the DPP authorities said the mainland is threatening Taiwan. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment?","At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait remains complex and grave, and cross-Strait relations are tense and confrontational. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces are the instigators. They rely on foreign backing and willingly act as “pawns” of external forces, continuously create hostility across the Strait, intensify provocations seeking “independence,” seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. If they remain obstinate, continue to collude with external forces, and escalate provocations seeking “independence,” they will only intensify tension and turmoil in the Strait and push Taiwan compatriots into a dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","In response to Ma Ying-jeou's call for the DPP authorities to return to the “1992 Consensus,” the DPP authorities responded that the “1992 Consensus” is “one country, two systems,” does not conform to Taiwan public opinion, and cannot resolve current cross-Strait problems. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities deliberately distort the ‘1992 Consensus,’ attempting to deceive and mislead Taiwan compatriots, with sinister intent. The ‘1992 Consensus’ is the common political basis for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is a political consensus reached by both sides through authorized agencies. ‘One country, two systems’ is an institutional arrangement for achieving national reunification. Its specific form of realization in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan’s actual situation, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nAt present, adhering to the ‘1992 Consensus’ and opposing ‘Taiwan independence’ is the political basis for our exchanges with Taiwan’s authorities and political parties. The history of cross-Strait relations shows that as long as the ‘1992 Consensus’ is upheld, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop. Otherwise, they will encounter setbacks and even turmoil.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Honduras recently announced that it will purchase mainland vaccines through El Salvador and will set up an office in the mainland if necessary. What is the spokesperson's view?","Your question involves two aspects. On the vaccine issue, the Mainland is committed to building a community with a shared future for mankind in health. We were the first to propose, and have consistently upheld, the commitment to vaccines as a global public good, and we strive to improve the accessibility and affordability of vaccines in developing countries. To date, we have provided vaccine assistance to more than 80 countries and 3 international organizations, exported vaccines to more than 50 countries, carried out vaccine research, development, production and cooperation with more than 10 countries, and actively participated in the WHO's “COVID-19 Vaccines Global Access (COVAX) Facility.” On May 7, the novel coronavirus inactivated vaccine researched and produced by the Beijing Institute of Biological Products of Sinopharm China National Biotec Group received World Health Organization Emergency Use Listing, was included in the global “Emergency Use List,” and is a safe, effective, high-quality vaccine certified by the WHO.\nAs for the second question you raised, the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a general consensus of the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle is the wish of the people and the trend of the times. We hope that relevant countries will properly handle Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: regarding Taiwan's inability to attend the World Health Assembly, the DPP authorities claim that UN Resolution 2758 and relevant WHO rules do not cover the handling of the Taiwan issue. What is your comment on this? Second question: Tsai Ing-wen recently repeated “Taiwan independence” remarks at the “Copenhagen Democracy Summit,” and some people on the island have recently stepped up accusations…","On the first question: this year marks the 50th anniversary of the adoption of UN Resolution 2758. Over these fifty years, in accordance with Resolution 2758, the international community has continuously consolidated the pattern of one China. Adhering to the One-China Principle is a norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and no one and no force can shake it.\nRegarding the second question you raised, we already responded in writing yesterday. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are accustomed to swindling and deceiving internationally under the guise of so-called “democracy,” but at home they persistently persecute dissenters and muzzle speech, weaving lies and deceiving the public. Their so-called “democracy” has long since degenerated and mutated; what qualifies them to talk about “democracy”! In collusion with external forces and anti-China institutions, they have staged many political farces, which fully exposes that their only aim is to seek “Taiwan independence.” None of these actions can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. We also urge the relevant countries to abide by the One-China Principle and not provide convenience or a stage for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to seek “independence” internationally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Taiwan has not been invited to the World Health Assembly for five consecutive years. A person from the Kuomintang said that Taiwan should actively communicate with the mainland; some representatives from the Blue camp said that it should actively seek help from the US side. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. The World Health Organization, as a specialized agency of the United Nations, handles Taiwan-related issues in accordance with UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1. All WHO members should abide by the relevant resolutions of the UN General Assembly and the WHO. As for the relevant suggestions you mentioned from the Kuomintang, as I already pointed out, the reason the Taiwan region cannot participate in the World Health Assembly is that the DPP authorities do not recognize the “1992 Consensus” and unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait consultation and dialogue. The solution is very clear: the DPP authorities should abandon the “Taiwan independence” position, stop “Taiwan independence” activities, and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Only then can cross-Strait relations improve and develop, and cross-Strait dialogue and consultation resume.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","On April 30, several Taiwan civic groups went to the Mainland Affairs Council to express their demands, asking the DPP authorities to restore the cross-strait “mini three links” as soon as possible to facilitate travel between people on both sides. May I ask how the spokesperson views these voices in Taiwan society?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait want exchanges, cooperation and development; this is the mainstream public opinion. We hope that, as epidemic prevention and control becomes routine and vaccination continues to advance, cross-Strait personnel exchanges can gradually return to normal.\nSince February 10 last year, relevant authorities in Taiwan have unilaterally suspended the entry of Mainland residents into Taiwan, closed the \"Small Three Links\" at Kinmen, Matsu and Fujian, and cancelled a large number of cross-Strait direct flight routes. This has caused great difficulties and inconvenience for cross-Strait people-to-people exchanges and exchanges in all fields. We hope the Taiwan side will do more things conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, lift restrictions on Mainland residents traveling to Taiwan as soon as possible, and restore the \"Small Three Links\" and cross-Strait direct flight routes as soon as possible, providing the necessary conditions and a good environment for normal exchanges between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","This year, July 1 coincides with the centenary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, and the Straits Forum may be held in June. Recently, it has been reported that the mainland side intends to invite the KMT to participate in related activities. Chiang Chi-chen said he had not yet received any relevant information. Please introduce the relevant circumstances of these two activities. Does the mainland…","This year marks the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China (CPC). Over these 100 years, the CPC has always upheld its founding aspiration and mission of working for the well-being of the people and the rejuvenation of the nation. It has led the Chinese people in tenacious struggle and sustained effort, achieving a great leap from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, and has earned world-renowned great achievements.\nCelebrating the 100th anniversary of the founding of the CPC is a major event in the political life of the CPC and the people of all ethnic groups in China, and it is closely followed across the Taiwan Strait and at home and abroad. On March 23, the CPC Central Committee held its first press conference, introducing arrangements for the centenary celebration activities. Currently, various activities are being actively prepared and carried out in an orderly manner.\nThat compatriots on both sides of the Strait want exchanges, cooperation, and development is the will of the people and the trend of the times. We hope that, while carrying out epidemic prevention and control, cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields can be gradually restored. The DPP authorities once claimed: “Once the epidemic is under control, we look forward to the peoples across the Strait gradually restoring normal and orderly exchanges.” We hope they will keep their word and not renege.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Has the mainland ever considered how to keep war away from the Taiwan Strait?","The best way to avoid war is for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to abandon their \"Taiwan independence\" position, stop their provocations aimed at \"independence,\" and return to the common political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" so that cross-Strait relations can be improved and developed. They should not push the people of Taiwan into danger in pursuit of \"independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Two questions. First, regarding Ma Ying-jeou's call to return to the “original-flavor ‘1992 Consensus’,” the Mainland Affairs Council responded that Taiwan has turned a page on the history of the “1992 Consensus.” What is your view of the MAC's statement? Second, MAC Minister Chiu Tai-san once proposed that cross-Strait exchanges resume and that cross-Strait relations enjoy “spring warmth and flowers in bloom” in…","Whether to adhere to the “1992 Consensus” concerns the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations and is the touchstone for testing the so-called “goodwill” and “sincerity” of the DPP authorities. This is a major question of principle in cross-Strait relations that cannot be avoided or gotten around.\nThe development of cross-Strait relations proves that upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” allow cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, and allow Taiwan compatriots to benefit. Denying the “1992 Consensus” and departing from the one-China principle will lead to tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations and harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nRegarding your second question, as we have said before, spring warmth needs the east wind. The east wind is the “1992 Consensus.” The facts of the past period prove that without the east wind, “spring warmth and flowers in bloom” is merely a politically calculated pretext of the DPP authorities. They once released a smokescreen of so-called “easing tensions in cross-Strait relations” to shift responsibility for damaging cross-Strait relations and to deceive the public, but soon tore off the mask of their so-called “easing tensions in cross-Strait relations” and “encouraging cross-Strait exchanges.” To cope with public dissatisfaction on the island and divert the public's attention, they deliberately raised the pitch of “Taiwan independence,” intensified attacks on and provocations against the mainland, willingly served as the vanguard of Western anti-China forces, obstructed and restricted cross-Strait personal exchanges, intimidated and punished Taiwan compatriots participating in cross-Strait exchanges, and brutally cut off Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth from sharing in the mainland's development opportunities and pursuing greater and better development. Do these actions look in any way like wanting “spring warmth and flowers in bloom”?\nI want to stress once again that the crux and the remedy of cross-Strait relations are very clear: as long as the DPP authorities abandon the “Taiwan independence” position, stop “Taiwan independence” activities, and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations can improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","Yesterday the National Bureau of Statistics published the results of the Seventh National Population Census, in which 157,886 Taiwan residents registered for the census, about 12,000 fewer than in the Sixth National Population Census ten years ago. How do you interpret the change in the number of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland over these ten years?","The reference time point for the Seventh National Population Census was 0:00 on November 1, 2020, and the main data on Taiwan compatriots covers those who live in the mainland and were registered. Affected by the COVID-19 epidemic, many Taiwan compatriots who returned to Taiwan have not yet come back to the mainland.\nToday is the 13th anniversary of the Wenchuan earthquake. Thirteen years ago, Taiwan compatriots expressed deep concern and generous assistance to the people in the disaster areas, and we once again express our thanks here. Thirteen years have passed, and the earthquake-stricken areas have been reborn from the ashes, creating miracles that have amazed the world. We welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses to return to Sichuan and Wenchuan to see the current scene there, where agritourism, rural revitalization, and thriving industries come together.\nToday is also the 110th International Nurses Day. We extend holiday greetings to nurses on both sides of the Strait, express our respect for their professional dedication in fighting the epidemic, and for their devotion to protecting lives with their own lives. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210512_12351715.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-13","Hua Chunying","China Review News","The United States, Britain, Germany and NGOs including Human Rights Watch and Amnesty International hosted a virtual event on Xinjiang's human rights situation in New York on May 12, keeping up the shameless hype-up on the so-called \"genocide\" issue in Xinjiang and also calling on China to allow unfettered access to Xinjiang by the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights. Does China have any comment?","The United States, Britain and Germany ganged up with some NGOs to host a virtual conference on Xinjiang's human rights situation based on lies and political prejudice falsely in the name of the UN. China deplores and rejects it. The conference was awash with outrageous lies and disinformation. It was another despicable shoddy show and sheer political farces put together by a handful of countries including the US. In fact, it was firmly rejected by the vast UN membership.\nI must point out that these countries that are always trying to lecture others on human rights issues actually have a deplorable record on human rights and have committed piles of crimes. The false allegations they launch against China mirror their own historical crimes and sinister mentality.\nUS history has recorded the horrific systemic ethnic cleansing and slaughter of Native Indians, which constitute genocide and crimes against humanity. Between the 19th century and the 1970s, the US government sent a large number of Indian children to boarding schools, which can be called the progenitor of concentration camps. An American historian at the University of Hawaii points out that the US warfare against the Native American population was the largest genocide in history. Pulitzer Prize winner John Toland wrote in his book Adolf Hitler: The Definitive Biography that Hitler attributed his idea of concentration camps and his practice of genocide to his study of British and American history. In the US today, racism is still a systemic and persistent existence penetrating every aspect of life. Former President Obama said, \"the legacy of discrimination in almost every institution of our lives - you know, that casts a long shadow. And that's still part of our DNA that's passed on\". \"Defined broadly enough, one could say that there's systemic racism across every institution in America,\" said former Homeland Security Secretary Jeh Johnson. The US claims loudly enough that it is concerned about the human rights of Muslims. However, it is exactly the US and its accomplices that have killed the most Muslims. The US waged wars and military operations in Iraq, Libya, Syria, Afghanistan and other countries in the name of \"fighting terrorism\", taking the lives of over a million Muslims and displacing tens of millions. Where is the US concern for human rights?\nBritain committed countless horrifying crimes all over the world during hundreds of years of colonial rule. The world's first concentration camp in South Africa carries with it the disgraceful brand of the British Empire. British forces killed innocent people and committed torture in places like Iraq and Afghanistan, but the culprits are sheltered by the government and remain beyond the law. Where is the UK concern for human rights?\nIn the beginning of the 20th century, German colonists slaughtered over 100,000 indigenous Namibian tribespeople. United Nations Economic and Social Council Commission on Human Rights said in a report that this is the first genocide in the 20th century. During WWII, Nazi Germany slaughtered almost six million Jews. Where is Germany's concern for human rights?\nInstead of reflecting deeply on their poor human rights records and crimes in the past and at present, the countries above crossed every line to smear and denigrate China. This only exposes their sanctimonious hypocrisy. If they truly care about human rights, why didn't they invite residents from Xinjiang to attend the event? If they truly care about human rights, why don't they reflect upon and redress serious racial discriminatory polices and behavior at home? If they truly care about human rights, why are they so callous as millions die of COVID-19 at home? If they truly care about human rights, they should take effective measures immediately to make sure all ethnic minorities can breathe freely, stop killing innocent civilians in overseas military operations, hold the culprits accountable and apologize to the affected countries and victims, and take prompt measures to ensure equitable distribution of vaccines globally.\nInstitutions and individuals attending this meeting are all anti-China in nature. Non-governmental organizations like the Human Rights Watch and Amnesty International have always been biased, confusing right with wrong and spreading rumors around. The so-called \"World Uyghur Congress\" (WUC) is an out-and-out anti-China separatist organization. Its president Dolqun Isa, one participant to the meeting, is a terrorist identified by the Chinese government. He has all along been fabricating rumors and lies on Xinjiang, spreading religious extremism, and instigating violent terrorism and separatism. The US is mechanically repeating those lies and rumors fabricated by a handful of fake \"witnesses\" and \"scholars\".\nThose Western countries would rather believe the lies concocted by a few people than heed the voice of the 25 million people of all ethnic groups in Xinjiang and the 1.4 billion Chinese. They would rather play along with the clumsy show of a handful of anti-China forces than acknowledge the development and progress in Xinjiang. This further exposed the hypocritical nature of their so-called democracy and human rights, and laid bare their intention to make an issue out of the human rights situation in Xinjiang to disrupt and contain China, and to divert people's attention from their own past and on-going human rights crimes and incompetency in domestic governance and COVID-19 response.\nSome people said,\"If you have nothing to hide, why don't you grant unimpeded access to the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights?\" My question is, if someone makes a false accusation against you and arbitrarily asks you to open the door unconditionally so that they can rummage through your chests and cupboards, will you allow it? This is not about facts, but sovereignty and dignity! We welcome all unbiased people to visit Xinjiang. That said, we firmly reject so-called investigation with presumption of guilt by citing lies and rumors, firmly reject interference in China's domestic affairs under the pretext of human rights, and firmly reject playing up the so-called Xinjiang-related issues to undermine China's stability and contain China's development.\nA Chinese poem reads that amid monkeys' howl along the riverbanks, my skiff has travelled a thousand miles. China's growth and Xinjiang's stability and development will never be shaken by the clumsy show of these countries and individuals. We hope and believe that the international community will see their real nature and avoid being misled by people with ill intentions. This political farce started by a few countries ganging up with some anti-China organizations and individuals will only end up in a disgraceful self-defeat.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347041.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210513_9171264.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-14","Hua Chunying","China Review News","It is reported that on May 13, a US State Department spokesman said that \"we condemn the cynical use of potentially life-saving medical assistance to advance the narrow political agendas of certain donors.\" \"Taiwan's relationships with countries in the region, including Honduras, reinforce the hemisphere's democratic values and support sustainable development,\" the spokesman said, adding that the US \"stands with…","The US diplomacy is quite consistent, with sanctimonious hypocrisy running through issues related to both human rights and vaccines. The US has been repeatedly touting its commitment to strengthening global democratic values, voicing its solidarity with one country today and another tomorrow. But can the US tell us how many doses it has exported to other countries including its allies? The US has 330 million people, only 4% of the world's population. However, it has purchased 2.6 billion vaccine doses, or a quarter of the world's total. While countries are trying every means to get urgently-needed vaccines, hundreds of millions of doses are sitting in US warehouses. US officials keep stressing that the US should stick to the approach of \"America First\" or domestic priority on vaccine distribution. The US also restricts the export of raw materials of vaccines. Such moves remind me of a line by Chinese poet Du Fu: \"while meat and wine go to waste behind the vermilion gates of the rich, the poor is frozen to death on an empty stomach by the roadside.\"\nOn epidemic response and vaccines, the US has been hiding the truth of its botched response from its own citizens at home while trying to divert attention by blame-shifting and political manipulation on the international stage. At critical junctures in the global fight against the virus, the US either sits idly by and makes things worse for those already in difficulty, or pays lip service only. A while ago, it even jumps the lip service part by emphasizing \"America First\". More recently, the US made some gestures without taking any concrete actions yet, but it is already posing as a \"savior\" of the world. If the US really cares about life and health of people in other countries, if it really stands with them, if it really believes in democracy and human rights as it claims to, it should honor words with deeds.\nChina is the first to initiate and act on the pledge to make vaccines a global public good. Despite its own huge population and supply shortage, China has to date provided anti-epidemic supplies to over 160 countries and international organizations, and is offering direly needed vaccines to over 100 countries and international organizations in various forms. We are also working with more than 10 developing countries including Egypt and the UAE on technological transfer and cooperative production. After the Sinopharm vaccine is listed for emergency use by the WHO, we are working actively to advance providing vaccines to COVAX. China will continue to contribute to greater accessibility and affordability of vaccines in developing countries. We hope the US can stop political manipulation on vaccines, and take more concrete actions to contribute to the global cooperation in fighting COVID-19.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210514_9170744.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1875845.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-14","Hua Chunying","Global Times","According to media reports on May 13, Japan's defense white paper 2021 will include for the first time content that stability across the Taiwan Strait is very important to the security of Japan and the stability of the international community. It will also claim that China's military moves were causing concern. The white paper will also falsely claim that Chinese Coast Guard vessels' activities around the Diaoyu…","It is extremely wrong and irresponsible for the Japanese side to keep creating issues concerning China for some time, grossly interfere in China's internal affairs, unjustifiably criticize China's normal national defense endeavor and military activities, make wanton comments about China's legitimate maritime activities and hype up the so-called \"China threat\". China deplores and rejects this and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nI must stress that Taiwan is China's territory and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. China will never allow any country to interfere in the Taiwan question in any form. China must and will be reunified.\nThe Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands and reefs are an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. China's patrol and law enforcement activities in waters off the Diaoyu Dao are legitimate and lawful exercise of its inherent right. We hope the Japanese side will adjust its mindset properly and show respect for China's sovereignty and sincerity in safeguarding regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210514_9170744.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1875845.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-18","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The spokesperson of the Hong Kong SAR government said early today that Hong Kong had temporarily suspended operations at its representative office in the Taiwan region. Do you have any insight or comment on this?","This is not a diplomatic question. I would like to refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210518_9170746.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1876601.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-18","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","It is reported that Australian Industry Group chief executive Innes Willox warned the nation was facing a long-feared \"day of reckoning\" between its security and economic relationships. He urged the government to calm tensions with China through \"negotiation, common sense and diplomacy\" and called for an end to inflammatory language. He believed that the industrial and business community should work to avoid an…","I noted relevant reports. For quite some time, the Australian government has repeatedly made provocative and confrontational moves on such issues of China's core interests and major concerns as those related to Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Taiwan. This has severely undermined the political trust and cooperation foundation between the two sides.\nWe noticed that more and more visionary people in Australia expressed their concern over this, calling on the Australian government to reflect on its China policy and putting forward very valuable suggestions. We hope the Australian government will face squarely the crux of the setbacks of the bilateral relations, take China's concerns seriously and heed rational voices. Australia should set aside the cold war mentality and ideological bias, and do more things that are conducive to mutual trust and cooperation and are in line with the China-Australia comprehensive strategic partnership.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210518_9170746.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1876601.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, Taiwan social groups including the New Party have called on the DPP authorities to open imports of mainland COVID-19 vaccines as soon as possible, saying they are willing to play a bridging role and help bring in mainland vaccines to respond to the recent spread of COVID-19 on the island. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks when answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 17 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 17th, said that while the virus is merciless, people are compassionate. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all descendants of the Chinese nation, and Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood kin. People from all walks of life on the mainland have always been concerned for the life, health, and safety of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and we are willing to do our utmost to help the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic as quickly as possible.\nShe said that recently the COVID-19 epidemic on the island has become increasingly severe, and the epidemic prevention pressure faced by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots continues to grow. We are deeply worried about this and hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots can bring the epidemic under effective control as soon as possible, ensure life, health, and safety, and return to normal life.\nZhu Fenglian also pointed out that epidemic prevention is paramount, and life comes first. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots urgently hope to use mainland vaccines. The most pressing task is to remove the artificial political obstacles on the island, so that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots have vaccines available and their life, health, and well-being are necessarily protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210518_12353016.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-19","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Do you have any comment on the US military vessel that sailed through the Taiwan Strait today?","The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command already made remarks on the issue. The Chinese side was closely following and fully aware of the US military vessel's passage through the Taiwan Strait. The US warships have repeatedly flaunted their prowess in the Taiwan Strait, provoking and stirring up trouble. This is by no means commitment to freedom and openness, but rather deliberate disruption and sabotage of regional peace and stability. The international community sees this crystal clear. China is firmly resolved in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US to play a constructive role in regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210519_9170747.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1876874.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-05-20","Tan Kefei","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On May 18, the US destroyer “Wilbur” transited the Taiwan Strait. On May 20, without approval from the Chinese government, the ship illegally entered China's Xisha territorial waters. The relevant PLA theater organized sea and air forces, and in accordance with law and regulations, tracked and surveilled the US warship and carried out warning and expulsion. The US warships transiting the Taiwan Strait and illegally entering China's Xisha territorial waters in a few consecutive days constitute a serious provocation of very bad nature. We firmly oppose and strongly condemn this.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. It concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. US warships frequently transiting the Taiwan Strait, flaunting military might and creating crises, send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. This is an extremely irresponsible and dangerous act, tantamount to “playing with fire.”\nThe Xisha Islands are China's inherent territory. According to the Law of the People's Republic of China on the Territorial Sea and the Contiguous Zone, the Chinese government published the baselines of the territorial sea of the Xisha Islands in 1996. The intrusion of the US warship into China's Xisha territorial waters seriously violates China's sovereignty and security, violates Chinese law and relevant international law, and undermines peace, security and good order in the waters concerned.\nWe demand that the US side recognize the situation, stop its provocations, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, do more things conducive to regional peace and stability, and stop creating obstacles and troubles for China-US relations and military-to-military relations. The Chinese military will take all necessary measures to respond to all threats and provocations and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/TopStories/4885765.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/qwfb/16119559.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: At present, the epidemic situation in Taiwan is severe, yet relevant figures of the DPP authorities claim that the mainland has once again launched “cognitive warfare against Taiwan,” spreading false information to undermine the authority of the DPP authorities and delay the slowing of the epidemic, and that it will be investigated and dealt with. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian responded…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 20th, said that what compatriots in Taiwan look forward to is scientific and effective epidemic prevention and control measures and relevant support. The DPP authorities should devote more attention to how to prevent and control the epidemic with a scientific and professional attitude, stop playing political games, take practical and effective measures to bring the epidemic under control as soon as possible, and effectively safeguard the lives, health, interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nShe pointed out that these statements once again confirm the DPP authorities' habitual tricks of fabricating falsehoods, deliberately making things up, shifting focus, and shifting blame onto others.\nZhu Fenglian also said that epidemic prevention is paramount and life comes first. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family linked by blood. We deeply empathize with the severe epidemic facing the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and we are willing to make our greatest efforts to help them get through this difficult time as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210520_12353554.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-21","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","The 74th World Health Assembly will take place from May 24 to June 1. It is learned that the Taiwan authorities didn't receive an invitation from the WHO. Recently, many countries wrote to the WHO to support the Chinese government's decision of not agreeing to the Taiwan region's participation in this year's WHA and express the hope not to discuss Taiwan-related issues at the WHA74. Do you have any comment?","There is but one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The one-China principle is a recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The Taiwan region's participation in the activities of international organizations including WHO must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a fundamental principle affirmed by the Resolution 2758 of the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) and Resolution 25.1 of the World Health Assembly (WHA).\nBefore 2016, China made special arrangements for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA on the basis of the fact that both sides across the Taiwan Strait uphold the one-China principle. Since the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) came to power, it has placed its political agenda over the wellbeing of the people in the Taiwan region, obstinately adhered to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence\", and refused to admit the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA has ceased to exist.\nThe Chinese Central Government always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. Under this precondition of abiding by the one-China principle, we have made appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs. Since the early stages of COVID-19, the Chinese Central Government has given the Taiwan region 260 updates about the situation, and approved participation by health experts from the Taiwan region in 16 WHO technical activities. The Taiwan region received multiple notifications of information about COVID-19 from the WHO Secretariat. The claim of a \"gap\" in global anti-epidemic efforts is groundless. The DPP authorities, turning a blind eye to the common aspiration of the international community to focus on anti-epidemic cooperation and the life and safety of the people in the Taiwan region, are pursuing political maneuvering under the pretext of the pandemic. They violated the UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1 and are bent on initiating proposals relating to the Taiwan region at the cost of disrupt the WHA proceedings and international cooperation. Their true intention is to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\".\nIn order to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and uphold the solemnity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China cannot agree with the Taiwan region's participation in this year's WHA. This decision by China received broad-based support and understanding from the international community. By yesterday, over 150 countries voiced their support for our decision through diplomatic channels. Nearly 80 WHO members sent letters to the WHO to express their commitment to the one-China principle and opposition to Taiwan's participation in the WHA. This once again shows that the one-China principle is the common aspiration and the overriding trend and the fact that the overwhelming majority of countries hold a just and right position on the relevant issue. People around the world are always sharp-eyed. The US and a handful of other countries have been emboldening the DPP and clamoring for Taiwan's participation in the WHA with all kinds of petty tricks. Their attempt has no chance of success!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210521_9170749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210521_9171270.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-21","Zhao Lijian","South China Morning Post","It is reported that the Japanese Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi said that considering China's increased capabilities, Japan must speed up the efforts to increase its defense capabilities. The report believes that the statement signals Japan's readiness to do away with its long-standing 1% GDP ceiling for annual defense spending. Do you have any comment?","I have taken note of relevant reports. I also noticed that the relevant Japanese official cited China's increased capabilities as the most important reason for Japan's decision to increase defense budget and alleged that the situation in Taiwan should be taken as Japan's own problems and that Japan will discuss with the US relevant revisions of the Guidelines for Japan-US Defense Cooperation.\nThe Japanese side made these irresponsible remarks to blatantly advocate arms race, play up regional tensions, provoke military confrontation, and even attempt to interfere in the Taiwan question and China's internal affairs. Such actions are extremely vile in nature. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to that. I would like to stress the following points.\nFirst, China follows the path of peaceful development and is committed to a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. The development of China's national defense forces is necessitated by the need to safeguard its own sovereignty, security and development interests, and to uphold international and regional peace and stability. China will continue to be a promoter of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of the international order. No matter how strong China grows, it will never seek hegemony, expansion or sphere of influence. China has no interest in engaging in an arms race with anyone.\nSecond, the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs that brook no foreign interference in any form. China must and will be reunified. A small group of people in Japan have always been obsessed with the obsolete illusion of reviving militarism, showing no repent and harboring wild ambitions. They want to get their hands on Taiwan even till this day. We once again warn the Japanese side that the determination and will of the Chinese government and military to safeguard national sovereignty, security and unity is rock-solid. Japan should not overstretch itself.\nThird, aggression and expansion launched by Japanese militarism in modern times have inflicted untold sufferings on the people in Asia, including China. Japan is a defeated country in World War II. Its belligerent moves are aimed at shaking off the post-war shackles and return to the old path of military expansion. As an ally of the US whose military spending accounts for nearly 40% of the world's total, Japan has been flexing muscles everywhere while criticizing other countries' normal military development. This is extremely unjustified. I urge the Japanese side to reflect on itself, stop undermining regional peace and stability, and stop slandering China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210521_9170749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210521_9171270.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-21","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan's health minister said that he spoke to the US health minister to ask for help in obtaining COVID-19 vaccines. Would China like to comment?","First of all, I would like to correct you on the term \"health minister\" because we do not recognize the so-called \"minister\" of Taiwan. It is pointless for the Taiwan region to seek independence and engage in political manipulation under the pretext of COVID-19.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210521_9170749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210521_9171270.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-24","Zhao Lijian","JoongAng Ilbo","The leaders of the United States and South Korea pledged to strengthen US-ROK alliance after they met in Washington on May 21. What is China's position on this? When will China have face-to-face summit with other countries? Do you have any plan for that?","We noted the relevant content of the joint statement of the US and the ROK and are concerned about that. We believe that the development of US-ROK relations should be conducive to promoting regional peace, stability, development and prosperity, rather than the opposite, still less harmful to the interests of third parties including China.\nThe joint statement mentioned issues related to Taiwan and the South China Sea. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. It bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and allows no interference by external forces. We urge relevant countries to speak and act prudentially on the Taiwan question and refrain from playing with fire. With regard to the South China Sea issue, all countries enjoy the freedom of navigation and overflight in the South China Sea in accordance with international law, and there is no problem with it. Relevant countries know these very clearly.\nAs to international order, I want to stress that there is only one system in the world, and it is the UN-centered international order; there is only one set of rules, and it is the basic norms governing international relations with the UN Charter as its cornerstone. Neither one nor several countries are entitled to define what the international order is, still less to impose their standard on others. China always opposes relevant countries in creating small cliques targeting other countries including the \"Quad\" and \"Indo-Pacific strategy\". Such unpopular practice will not succeed and will only lead to a dead end.\nOn your second question, I have no information to offer at this moment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210524_9170750.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1878152.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-24","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","There have been media reports over the weekend that three researchers from the Wuhan Institute of Virology became sick enough that in November 2019 they sought medical care. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this report? Does it have anything to add to China's previous comments about the origins of the coronavirus? My second question, Taiwan \"foreign minister\" Joseph Wu and \"health minister\" said the…","Regarding your first question, the Wuhan Institute of Virology of the Chinese Academy of sciences has issued a statement on March 23. According to the statement, the Wuhan Institute of Virology had not been exposed to COVID-19 before December 30, 2019, and a \"zero-infection\" record is kept among its staff and graduate students so far.\nThis January, the China-WHO joint mission made field trips to institutions including the Hubei Provincial Center for Disease Control, the Wuhan Center for Disease Control and the Wuhan Institute of Virology, and visited biosafety laboratories and had in-depth and candid exchanges with experts there. Through these field trips and in-depth visits, members of the mission unanimously agreed that the hypothesis of lab leaking is extremely unlikely. Member of the joint mission Peter Daszak said during an interview with American media that they were able to have in-depth exchanges with authoritative experts in the Wuhan Institute of Virology with a level of openness even he hadn't anticipated, when the claim of lab leaking was politicized on a global scale. The experts went to every place they asked to see, and met everyone they wanted to meet. The visit has been a great success.\nMeanwhile, I also want to point out that there are increasingly more reports on the virus and COVID-19 pandemic being spotted in various places around the world in the second half of 2019, and that the international community is highly concerned about the questions around the biological lab at Fort Detrick and the real intentions of the US' establishment of 200-plus overseas bio-labs. What is the real purpose for the US to continue to play up the so-called \"lab leak theory\"? Does it really care about the origin-tracing of the virus or just want to divert attention? We hope that the relevant departments in the US will make a clarification and explain that to the world as soon as possible. We hope that relevant parties will follow China's example, take a scientific and cooperative attitude, work with the WHO on origin-tracing, and make positive contribution to the humanity's early victory over the pandemic and better capabilities in dealing with public health emergencies in the future.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan region's participation in the activities of international organizations including WHO must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a fundamental principle affirmed by the Resolution 2758 of the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) and Resolution 25.1 of the World Health Assembly (WHA). Since the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) came to power, it has placed its political agenda over the wellbeing of the people in the Taiwan region, obstinately adhered to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence\", and refused to admit the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA has ceased to exist.\nIn order to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and uphold the solemnity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China cannot agree to the Taiwan region's participation in this year's WHA. This decision by China received broad-based support and understanding from the international community. By yesterday, over 150 countries voiced their support for our decision through diplomatic channels. Over 80 WHO members sent letters to the WHO to express their commitment to the one-China principle and opposition to Taiwan's participation in the WHA. This once again shows that the one-China principle is the common aspiration and the fact that the overwhelming majority of countries hold a just and right position on the relevant issue.\nThe DPP authority hypes up the so-called WHA participation issue with the true intention of seeking \"Taiwan independence\" by making capital of the epidemic. We firmly reject it. As has been proven time and again, the one-China principle is the overwhelming trend of the international community. The DPP authority's attempts will never succeed. We advise it to stop using the pandemic to engage in political manipulation and stop inviting humiliation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210524_9170750.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1878152.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-24","Zhao Lijian","CRI","Mikiko Matsuyama, a renowned ballet dancer who was the first in Japan to play the part of Xi'er in \"The White-Haired Girl\", passed away in Tokyo at the age of 98 on May 22. Would you like to offer a comment?","Ms. Mikiko Matsuyama is the Chinese people's old friend. Dedicated to deepening China-Japan friendship, she made important contributions to friendly exchanges between our two countries. We are saddened by her passing and extend our deep condolences.\nMs. Matsuyama, founder of the Matsuyama Ballet, is a renowned Japanese ballet performance artist. Even before the normalization of relations between China and Japan, Ms. Matsuyama and her husband the late Mr. Masao Shimizu used to lead the Matsuyama Ballet to China for friendly exchanges. During those trips, they forged a deep bond of friendship with the Chinese people. In 1955, the Matsuyama Ballet adapted the Chinese story \"The White-Haired Girl\" into a ballet with Ms. Matsuyama as the heroin Xi'er. The ballet was staged many times in China and Japan and and was applauded by the audience in both countries. Last year, when China was going all out to fight COVID-19, the Matsuyama Ballet recorded a heart-warming video message expressing support for us. Ms. Matsuyama's contribution to China-Japan friendship will be remembered forever by both peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210524_9170750.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1878152.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently the epidemic in Taiwan has become increasingly serious, and shortages of vaccines and other issues have drawn public concern. Some people on the island had previously repeatedly advocated obtaining COVID-19 vaccines from the mainland. On May 17, a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said, “We are willing to do our utmost to help compatriots in Taiwan overcome the epidemic as soon…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 24 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 24th, in response to questions, that in the face of the increasingly severe epidemic on the island and the constant epidemic prevention pressure borne by Taiwan compatriots, some groups and individuals on the island have repeatedly called for the purchase of mainland vaccines. Our position is very clear: we are willing to make arrangements quickly so that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots can have mainland vaccines available as soon as possible. If needed, we are also willing to actively consider sending epidemic prevention and control experts to Taiwan to share anti-epidemic experience with Taiwan's medical and health personnel and provide epidemic prevention consultation.\nZhu Fenglian said that life comes first, and anti-epidemic work is a priority. We are very concerned about, and deeply empathize with, the rampant epidemic in Taiwan, which endangers the life and health safety of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We have said many times that we are willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots strengthen epidemic prevention and control and overcome the epidemic as soon as possible.\nShe also pointed out that the virus is merciless, but people have love. At this moment, when the epidemic in Taiwan is increasingly severe, the life safety and health well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots must come first. We must do our utmost to help them get through this difficulty as soon as possible and return to normal life. The DPP authorities using political manipulation to divert attention is an extremely irresponsible approach toward Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities must immediately stop all slander and smearing of mainland assistance to Taiwan compatriots in anti-epidemic efforts, take concrete action to remove man-made obstacles, and ensure that the life, health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots are protected as early as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210524_12354449.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-26","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","In a recent interview with Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, Taiwan's \"foreign minister\" Joseph Wu talked about the mainland's military activities in the East China Sea, the Taiwan Strait and the South China Sea and its attempt to expand its influence. He hopes fellow \"states\" could pay attention to and support Taiwan. He also said that Hong Kong no longer enjoys the same economic and political freedom as it did…","First of all, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory and there is no so-called \"foreign minister\" of Taiwan. Under the guise of so-called democracy and freedom, the Taiwan authorities have repeatedly taken advantage of Hong Kong affairs to maliciously slander and denigrate the mainland. It's real purpose is to disrupt Hong Kong and seek \"Taiwan independence\". Its clumsy political manipulation for grandstanding will not succeed, and will only invite humiliation on itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210526_9170752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210526_9171273.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-26","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Recently, the actor John Cena apologized for referring to Taiwan as a country. And then his apology was criticized by some in the US including Republicans and conservative media. They sort of slammed him for bowing to China. Tom Cotton, a Republican Senator, described Cena's as apology as pathetic. Does the foreign ministry have a response to Cotton's remarks?","The criticism of the people you mentioned is groundless. Everyone knows what kind of person Cotton is. His words are nothing but like what's written on a piece of waste paper.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210526_9170752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210526_9171273.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-26","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan's \"president\" Tsai Ing-wen said today that the government has not been able to sign a deal with Germany's BioNTech for vaccines because of China's intervention. Do you have any comment on this?","First of all, I must correct you on one point. We don't recognize this so-called \"president\". She is only the leader of a region of China. I'm not aware of what you mentioned, but I can tell you that Taiwan's access to vaccines from the mainland is open. Taiwan's attempt to seek independence under the pretext of COVID-19 will only lead to a dead end.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210526_9170752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210526_9171273.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-26","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The Ensuring American Global Leadership and Engagement Act was introduced to the United States House of Representatives on Tuesday. This bill is calling for the US to coordinate with allies to compete with China. Do you have any comment on that?","The relevant bill of the US Congress defames China's development path and domestic and foreign policies in disregard of facts. It interferes in China's internal affairs and undermines China's interests on issues concerning China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. China is firmly opposed to this and will firmly defend its own interests.\nThe Taiwan question is the political foundation of China-US relations. It is a red line that cannot be crossed and allows no interference by any outside forces. Hong Kong is part of China's territory. Only after Hong Kong's return did Hong Kong compatriots truly begin to exercise their democratic rights as masters of the city. The so-called \"genocide\" of the Uyghurs in Xinjiang is a blatant lie conspired by a few Western anti-China forces, which has been proved false by numerous facts. The US has abused the concept of national security to suppress Chinese companies and curb China's development. Such actions harm others and do no good to the US itself. China pursues an independent foreign policy of peace and a win-win strategy of opening-up, and promotes the building of a new type of international relations and a community with a shared future for mankind. The US has been ganging up around the world, forcing other countries to take sides and forming a \"clique\" against China, which is unpopular. We also noted that the relevant bill includes the content of supporting closer cooperation between China and the US in addressing climate change and other global challenges. At the same time, it must be pointed out that cooperation must and can only be carried out on the basis of mutual respect.\nChina urges relevant members of US Congress to abandon the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop making use of false information to engage in political manipulation on China-related issues, stop saying or doing anything to undermine China's interests under the guise of so-called \"democracy and human rights\", stop deliberating and pushing forward the relevant negative China-related bill, and remove the China-related negative content. The US side should do more to promote China-US relations, mutual trust and cooperation and create favorable conditions for our cooperation in climate change and other fields.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210526_9170752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202105/t20210526_9171273.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's TAO press conference. Now we open the floor for questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, the epidemic situation on the island has been severe, and some groups and individuals on the island have repeatedly expressed hope to obtain mainland vaccines. Could the spokesperson introduce whether the mainland has already helped relevant Taiwan institutions obtain mainland vaccines through civilian channels, and what related assistance has been provided?","Yesterday, the heads of the Shanghai Municipal Medical and Health Development Foundation and the Jiangsu Provincial Cross-Strait Cultural Exchange Promotion Association each indicated that they are willing to donate a batch of COVID-19 vaccines to Taiwan compatriots, to help relieve their urgent needs and assist them in strengthening epidemic prevention. We support this, will actively assist, and also hope that the relevant parties on Taiwan will quickly clear the obstacles to shipping this batch of vaccines to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, an official of the DPP authorities said that the mainland is using vaccines to carry out “united front divide-and-conquer” against Taiwan, and is “manipulating public opinion” by declaring that it has never offered vaccines to Taiwan through existing cross-Strait agreement mechanisms and has never made any application. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Over the past year, people have seen enough of the various sophistries and deceptive political rhetoric of certain people on the island. Faced with the urgent calls of Taiwan compatriots for mainland vaccines, and the sincere desire of the mainland side to do its utmost to help Taiwan compatriots fight the epidemic, the answer need only be stated clearly: For mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO, will they be used or not? Is the wish of the broad Taiwan compatriots to use mainland vaccines as soon as possible being heeded or ignored?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355052.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, a writer for a Taiwan green-camp media outlet was caught posing as a mainland netizen in online communities and spreading rumors. In coordination with green-camp politicians such as Wang Dingyu, who staged a performance of their own, they slandered the mainland as having launched so-called “cognitive warfare against Taiwan.” After these acts were exposed, they argued that it was “a parody they found…","Toward this kind of conduct that has no conscience and no bottom line, netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should jointly condemn it and jointly boycott it.\nRecently, the COVID-19 epidemic has been raging in Taiwan, seriously threatening the life, health and safety of the broad Taiwan compatriots. Relevant institutions and figures on the island urgently hope that the DPP authorities will promptly take measures to close loopholes in epidemic prevention, and have repeatedly called for universal screening, rapid screening, and purchasing vaccines, yet the DPP authorities have attached political labels to them. Not only that, the DPP authorities have also resorted to old tricks, inciting internet troops to stage a farce of the so-called “cognitive warfare” that shifts blame and smears the mainland, attempting to divert attention and deceive the island's public. Such self-staged frame-up scripts by the DPP authorities have been repeatedly staged, from imported pork containing ractopamine to exported pineapples, from algae reef protection to the Taiwan Railways accident. Whenever they face public doubt, they instigate their raised “internet army” to steer opinion. Passing the buck, shifting responsibility, and diverting focus have become their most practiced routine. They have always been this way, and will continue to be. Only in the face of the epidemic, the more this routine is used, the more their tricks will be seen through.\nAs one family with blood ties, we are willing to do our utmost to help the broad Taiwan compatriots strengthen epidemic prevention and control as soon as possible. Manipulating politics on epidemic prevention and control, which concerns the life, health and safety of the broad Taiwan compatriots, is extremely immoral and extremely irresponsible toward the broad Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355051.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广《台海之声》记者","The 74th World Health Assembly was recently held. The international community has expressed support from multiple quarters for China's position on the Taiwan-related issue at the WHA. Meanwhile, the foreign ministers of the Group of Seven recently issued a so-called joint statement inviting Taiwan to participate in the WHA, which foreign media interpreted as “by no means sincere, but treating Taiwan as a tool of…","Regarding the Taiwan-related issue at the 74th World Health Assembly, we have already stated our position earlier. I reiterate here that the relevant decisions of this session of the World Health Assembly once again demonstrate that “Taiwan independence” leads nowhere, and that hyping Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly is unpopular. The one-China principle is a consensus of the international community, reflecting the wishes of the people and the trend of the times. It should be pointed out that the mainland side has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We not only promote exchange and cooperation in the health sector between the two sides of the Strait, but also adhere to the one-China principle in international affairs, and have taken a number of measures to make appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs. The channels for Taiwan to obtain various epidemic prevention and control information and support are smooth and effective.\nSince the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, we have notified Taiwan's region of the epidemic situation 260 times, and agreed to let Taiwan's region's health experts take part in 16 WHO technical activities. The political lie that Taiwan has been spreading about a so-called “international epidemic prevention gap” is nothing more than a pretext for the DPP authorities to use the epidemic to pursue “independence.”\nThe DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, causing the political foundation for the Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly to no longer exist.\nWe advise the DPP authorities not to go further and further down the wrong path. Any act that challenges the one-China principle will inevitably end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","With the summer vacation approaching, some localities and enterprises on the mainland have recently rolled out internship and employment programs for Taiwan's young people. Could the spokesperson introduce the specific details?","Internships and employment are matters that young people in Taiwan give great weight to in their personal development, and they are very eager to receive help with them. We attach great importance to this and actively create conditions to help Taiwanese youth study, live and develop on the mainland, and we hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriot youth will seize the opportunities on the mainland and achieve greater development. Relevant departments and localities, overcoming the difficulties brought by the epidemic and on the basis of doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, have actively provided services for Taiwanese youth seeking internships, employment and entrepreneurship, and have held activities themed on internships, employment and entrepreneurship for cross-Strait youth, providing more platforms for them to pursue, nurture and realize their dreams. Some specific developments are introduced below.\nIn January this year, Xiamen issued the \"Several Measures on Further Encouraging and Supporting Taiwanese Youth to Come to Xiamen for Internships, Employment and Entrepreneurship,\" providing policy support and safeguards for Taiwanese youth coming to Xiamen for internships and employment.\nSince March, Guangdong has continued to carry out the \"Guangdong Taiwan Youth Employment Station\" activities, with various enterprises and institutions providing more than 600 internship and job positions for Taiwanese youth. Recently, various localities in Guangdong have been planning to hold multiple internship and employment activities, such as the \"Taiwan Youth Elite Internship Program with Famous Enterprises,\" to help Taiwanese youth put down roots and develop.\nOn May 11, the \"2021 Shanghai Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Competition\" was officially launched. The host invited a mentor group of experts from many fields to build a \"stage for realizing dreams\" for cross-Strait youth, especially Taiwanese youth entrepreneurs, and to provide on-the-ground support.\nOn May 14, Hunan held the \"Building the Future, Embracing the Xiang River\" recruitment fair for Taiwanese youth and a policy-sharing session on studying, working and starting businesses in Hunan for Taiwanese youth, building platforms and creating conditions for Taiwanese youth to study, work and start businesses in Hunan. More than 60 Taiwanese and mainland enterprises in Hunan and more than 130 Taiwanese students and youth took part in the event. A Taiwanese youth shared on site his experience of starting a business in Changsha, saying: \"From the various procedures required to establish a company to the support and condolences that relevant units gave during the epidemic, it makes Taiwanese enterprises here more confident to keep working toward sustainable development.\"\nOn May 15, Wenzhou, Zhejiang held the \"Building Dreams in Wenzhou, Entrepreneurship and Innovation\" matchmaking event for Taiwanese youth internships and employment, where 52 enterprises and institutions offered 1,500 job positions and more than 300 internship positions, providing a platform for exchange and momentum for development for Taiwanese youth in Wenzhou. This summer, Zhejiang will also hold special recruitment events for Taiwanese youth internships and employment, offering 1,000 internship and job positions to help Taiwanese youth develop in Zhejiang.\nJiangsu will hold the 2021 Taiwan university student internship and employment intensive training during the summer vacation. A batch of well-known Jiangsu enterprises representing \"high-end, cutting-edge\" standards in relevant fields will offer more than 1,200 quality internship positions to Taiwanese youth. The intensive training camp will also organize exchange activities such as city visits, cultural experiences and science and technology interactions.\nIn addition, the first Yangtze River Delta Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition will be held in Changzhou, Jiangsu at the end of June. Taking full advantage of the strategic opportunity of the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta region, it will invite well-known experts and entrepreneurs in technology, venture capital and finance to take part, building an exchange platform for cross-Strait youth innovation and entrepreneurship, and providing comprehensive, in-depth entrepreneurship support including policy support, financing loans, technology transfer and coaching and training. Cross-Strait youth entrepreneurs are welcome to register for this competition through the China Taiwan Network.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355050.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The TAO has twice expressed its willingness to do its utmost to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic, and the Mainland Affairs Council successively responded by saying “Don’t feign good intentions” and “united front divisive manipulation.” Mainland netizens have reacted strongly. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","In the face of the epidemic, life comes first. Guided by the development philosophy of putting people first and the value of placing life above all, we have repeatedly stated our willingness to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic. However, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, starting from their own political self-interest, not only turn a blind eye to the goodwill of the mainland, but even maliciously slander it and brutally cut off possibilities that would help Taiwan residents strengthen epidemic prevention.\nThe actions of the DPP authorities on cross-Strait epidemic issues since last year are visible to Taiwan residents, and they are also visible to people on the mainland.\nAs the epidemic spreads on the island, what the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots expect is scientific and effective epidemic prevention and control policies and related guarantees. The DPP authorities should devote more thought to how to control the epidemic with a scientific and professional attitude, stop playing political games, and adopt practical and effective measures to bring the epidemic under control as soon as possible, and genuinely protect the life, health, and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355054.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Company's expressed willingness to provide vaccines to Taiwan, Chen Shih-chung said, “all sectors keep making statements, but we have not received any application.” Regarding Foxconn Group and other pharmaceutical companies asking whether they could import the BNT vaccine distributed by Fosun, Chen Shih-chung said, “If you want it, formally contact us.” As for foreign…","Everyone can see clearly that, amid the spread of the epidemic on the island, the DPP authorities still ignore the serious shortage of vaccines on the island and disregard the urgent expectations of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. They not only use various pretexts to prevent Taiwan residents from receiving mainland vaccines, but also do not allow vaccines distributed by mainland companies to enter Taiwan. Every additional day they do this wastes another day of precious epidemic prevention time, and Taiwan residents will be forced to pay a greater cost in lives and health.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","On the day of “5·20”, some domestic commentary reviewed the performance of the DPP authorities in cross-Strait relations over the past five years, arguing that “cross-Strait confrontation has grown more severe, and cross-Strait relations appear to have no way back.” May I ask the spokesperson for a response?","The fact that such public opinion exists on the island shows that all sectors of the island are very worried about the current state of cross-Strait relations. Since May 2016, the DPP authorities have denied the “1992 Consensus,” colluded with external forces, provoked independence, created cross-Strait confrontation, obstructed and undermined cross-Strait exchanges, and caused the current tense and turbulent state of cross-Strait relations. Their conduct undermines the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and harms the broad interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and will only push Taiwan into a very dangerous situation.\nOur position of promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations has not changed, and the solution for easing the tension in cross-Strait relations is also very clear. As long as the DPP authorities abandon the “Taiwan independence” stance, stop independence-seeking activities, and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations can improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355055.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Hung Hsiu-chu recently said she was willing to help obtain vaccines from the mainland. Some in Taiwan's epidemic prevention authorities, however, said that Taiwan has already purchased vaccines from different manufacturers through various channels, and that as for mainland vaccines, “Taiwan residents' confidence is probably insufficient.” What is your comment on this?","Mainland vaccines are safe, effective, and high-quality vaccines. On May 7, the World Health Organization approved the inactivated COVID-19 vaccine developed and produced by the Beijing Institute of Biological Products of China National Biotec Group (Sinopharm) for inclusion in the Emergency Use Listing. As of May 24, the mainland had reported a cumulative total of more than 527 million doses of COVID-19 vaccines administered.\nWhile the epidemic is raging in Taiwan, vaccines are in serious shortage, and the Taiwanese public is eagerly awaiting vaccination, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities still obstruct mainland vaccines from being brought to Taiwan in every possible way, which is entirely the result of political paranoia. Recently, many counties, cities, and civil organizations on the island have called for letting the Taiwanese public use mainland vaccines as soon as possible, and surveys have shown that nearly half of the Taiwanese public is willing to be vaccinated immediately with qualified vaccines. All of this fully reflects the confidence of the Taiwanese public in mainland vaccines. The DPP authorities have turned a deaf ear to this, fabricated falsehoods, and smeared mainland vaccines. In essence, this is a disregard for the life and health of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355053.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","June 1 this year marks the tenth anniversary of the joint exhibition in Taipei of the famous painter Huang Gongwang's \"Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains.\" Will any related activities be held on that occasion?","\"Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains\" (《富春山居图》), painted by the Yuan dynasty artist Huang Gongwang, is one of China's ten most celebrated classical paintings. After the end of the Ming dynasty, the famous painting was separated into two sections for various reasons. After 1949, the two sections were held separately by the Zhejiang Provincial Museum and the National Palace Museum in Taipei.\nOn June 1, 2011, under the joint promotion of farsighted people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the \"Remaining Mountains\" (剩山图) and the \"Scroll of the Useless Master\" (无用师卷), which had been separated for several centuries, were reunited and exhibited together in Taipei. This became a fine tale in the history of Chinese art and a cultural event of important significance in cross-Strait exchanges. This year marks the tenth anniversary of the reunion of \"Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains.\" Relevant authorities in Zhejiang Province will hold a commemorative meeting for the tenth anniversary of the reunion of \"Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains\" and related supporting activities in Hangzhou on June 1. More than 350 young people from both sides of the Strait and personalities from all sectors of society are expected to attend.\nChinese culture is the common root and soul of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and the spiritual bond that holds them together. We hope that through the commemorative activities marking the tenth anniversary of the reunion of \"Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains,\" compatriots on both sides, especially young people on both sides, will be able to remember history, gain insight from history, and together shoulder the mission of the era to inherit, innovate, and promote Chinese culture. We also hope that more Taiwan compatriots will actively take part in the new development pattern on the mainland, and join hands to paint the most beautiful picture of national rejuvenation in the new era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","The 23rd Straits Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Fair, recently held in Fuzhou, featured 14 distinctive exhibition zones. The role of cross-strait integration platforms and the elements of cross-strait integration were more prominent than before, and all parties reacted enthusiastically. Could the spokesperson introduce similar cross-strait economic and trade activities?","In the first year of the “14th Five-Year Plan,” we are actively taking measures to help Taiwan businesses and enterprises share the development opportunities of the mainland's “14th Five-Year Plan,” integrate into the mainland's new development pattern, participate in the mainland's high-quality development, and achieve greater development for themselves. Various localities have held or are planning cross-Strait economic and trade activities of diverse forms and distinctive features to deepen cross-Strait integrated development.\nIt is understood that five cross-Strait economic and trade activities involving Taiwan will take place one after another this month. On May 11, the “Shaanxi-Taiwan Economic and Trade Cooperation Project Promotion Conference” was held in Xi'an, Shaanxi. On May 17, the “New Opportunities, New Pattern, New Breakthroughs — Promotion Conference for Deepening Shandong-Taiwan Cooperation” was held in Jinan, Shandong. From May 18 to 22, the 4th 21st Century Maritime Silk Road Expo and the 23rd Straits Economic and Trade Fair were held in Fuzhou, Fujian. From May 24 to 28, the “Taiwan Enterprises Go West” activities were held in Chongqing and Sichuan. On May 30 and 31, the Yangtze River Delta Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zhuhu Forum will be held in Taizhou, Jiangsu. Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland are actively participating in these activities, and we also hope media friends will pay more attention to and report on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","The mainland has expressed willingness to help Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic as soon as possible, and noted that the DPP authorities should remove “man-made barriers” through concrete action. What do “man-made barriers” refer to? Second question: Taiwan's Central Epidemic Command Center said that if Shanghai Fosun wishes to sell vaccines to Taiwan, it should apply to Taiwan for a drug license. What is…","First question. In facing epidemic prevention and control, everyone now shares a consensus that universal vaccination can greatly reduce the severity and fatality rate of COVID-19 and significantly lower the harm of the disease. As of May 24, the mainland had cumulatively reported 527 million doses of COVID-19 vaccine administered. Nearly half of Taiwan's residents are willing to receive qualified vaccines, including mainland vaccines. However, the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention department has used various pretexts to prevent Taiwan compatriots from obtaining mainland vaccines. This is the greatest political obstacle to the export of mainland vaccines to Taiwan, and an even greater political obstacle to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots getting out of the epidemic's troubles as soon as possible; the victims are the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question: Fosun Pharma Group has already indicated its willingness to make the mRNA COVID-19 vaccine of Germany's BioNTech, which it represents, available to Taiwan compatriots, and has stated that since last year it has been actively pursuing the provision of this vaccine to Taiwan through multiple channels. We are pleased that Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group is willing to make vaccines available to Taiwan compatriots, and we are also willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic. For specific technical and procedural matters, we suggest you inquire directly with the Fosun Group.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报海外版记者","Recently, COVID-19 has continued to spread on the island, and large-scale blackouts and water outages have frequently occurred, as well as problems such as the Taiwan Railway accident. Public opinion on the island has criticized the DPP authorities for incompetent governance. Yet the DPP authorities, on the one hand, refuse assistance from the mainland, and on the other hand, use various excuses to provoke…","In recent days, compatriots in Taiwan have faced both water and electricity shortages and been severely afflicted by the rampant epidemic, with normal production and daily life, and even life, health and safety, affected and harmed. We are deeply concerned. The people of Taiwan know best what the root causes of these problems are. Faced with public criticism and appeals from the island's people, the DPP authorities have neither offered nor been able to produce any concrete, feasible and effective solutions to the problems. Instead, they keep creating estrangement and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait and engaging in political manipulation. It is no surprise that they behave this way: shirking responsibility and passing the blame to the mainland is their habitual routine. It is foreseeable that the DPP authorities will continue to use the mainland as an excuse, keep fabricating new lies and diverting attention, and in the end will only harm the people of Taiwan even more.\nAs the epidemic in Taiwan grows increasingly severe, we reaffirm once again that we are willing to do our utmost to help compatriots in Taiwan overcome the epidemic as soon as possible and to enable them to receive mainland vaccines quickly. Mainland epidemic-prevention experts are also willing to share anti-epidemic experience with their counterparts on the island and provide epidemic-prevention consultation.\nEach person's life is lived only once, and cherishing every person's life is the most basic social conscience. The DPP authorities must truly put the life and health of the people of Taiwan first, stop playing political games, remove artificial obstacles as soon as possible, and ensure that the people's life, health and safety are effectively protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355056.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: after the World Health Assembly rejected the Taiwan-related proposal, Wu Zhaoxie, Chen Shizhong, and other politicians, along with some Taiwanese media, responded forcefully. In addition, Wu Zhaoxie has recently accepted interviews with foreign media several times and made improper remarks on Hong Kong-related issues. What comment do you have on this? Second question: Taiwan's “representative to…","On the first question, regarding the Taiwan-related issue at the 74th World Health Assembly, I have just stated our position. Compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh and blood, and we are willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots bring the epidemic under control. What matters most right now is to do a good job of epidemic prevention and control on the island, effectively contain the outbreak, and ensure the life, health, and safety of the Taiwanese public, rather than using it as an opportunity to hype the issue, shift focus, confuse the public, and shirk responsibility for inadequate epidemic prevention. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities fabricate various lies and excuses and lash out in all directions, and their real aim is to “use the epidemic to seek independence.” This conduct, which places one party’s private interests above the health and well-being of the people, will surely be rejected by the public.\nOn the second question, we firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan, China, and this position is consistent and clear. We demand that the U.S. side abide by the One-China Principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and handle the Taiwan question appropriately. Any attempt by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to play tricks and “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","According to Taiwan media reports, at dawn on the 25th, four Taiwan military F-16 fighters flew to the United States to carry out replacement training missions. Some Taiwan media interpreted this as the first time Taiwan pilots have flown from Taiwan to the United States, and a so-called new breakthrough in US-Taiwan military cooperation. Spokesperson, how do you view these petty moves in US-Taiwan military affairs?","The motherland must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces do not accept the One-China Principle and insist on military confrontation, seeking “independence” through armed force. This has no way out and will only bring disaster to the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","A Shanghai institution has expressed willingness to donate vaccines to Taiwan, and specifically stressed concern for the epidemic situation in Taipei. I would like to ask: Could Shanghai donate vaccines to Taipei through the Twin Cities Forum platform? In addition, would the donated vaccines be mainland-made vaccines?","Civil organizations in Shanghai and Jiangsu have already said they are willing to donate a batch of vaccines to Taiwan compatriots, and now it depends on whether the relevant parties in Taiwan accept. As for which vaccines to donate, I think the wishes of the recipient should be taken into account. The immediate priority is to promptly remove artificial political obstacles; if there are no artificial political obstacles, donations will not be a problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The DPP authorities recently colluded with a US scholar to hype the illegal and invalid \"San Francisco Peace Treaty,\" using it to agitate for the so-called \"undetermined status of Taiwan.\" What is the spokesperson's comment?","On this question, I have responded before, and today I can elaborate on it in more detail.\nThe so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty” is an illegal and null document that the United States fabricated in 1951 by gathering a very small number of countries for a separate peace with Japan. This “treaty” violates the provisions of the 1942 Declaration by United Nations, namely that “the governments signatory to this Declaration will not make a separate armistice or separate peace with the enemies,” and does not conform to international law practice or to the provisions of the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties that “a treaty does not create either obligations or rights for a third State without its consent.” The so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty” has no authority to dispose of Taiwan's sovereignty status or any other sovereign rights and territory involving China as a non-signatory state, and has no effect under international law. This is the stern position that the Chinese government solemnly declared from the outset: it will never recognize it.\nIt must be pointed out that the Cairo Declaration expressly stipulates that territories Japan “has stolen from China, such as the Northeast Four Provinces, Taiwan, the Pescadores Islands, etc.” shall be returned to China. The Potsdam Proclamation reaffirmed that “the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” Japan's Instrument of Surrender expressly states that “Japan undertakes to faithfully fulfill the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation.” The factual and legal basis for Taiwan being part of China is not open to challenge. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. Any scheme by the DPP authorities to distort the facts or challenge the one-China principle is futile, and it is even less capable of blocking the historical trend of cross-Strait reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210526_12355049.htm"],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中央社记者","First question: Taiwan residents have some doubts about vaccines from various manufacturers, including AZ. The mainland has expressed willingness to provide mainland vaccines to Taiwan. Would you be willing to provide the relevant clinical trial data for the vaccines, so that Taiwan residents can obtain more complete information? Second question: Regarding the mainland's willingness to provide vaccines to Taiwan,…","First question: It is understood that Sinopharm Beijing, Beijing Sinovac, CanSino, and Sinopharm Wuhan have all publicly released the main results of the clinical trials of their developed vaccines. Sinopharm published the instructions for its COVID-19 inactivated vaccine on its website, including the main data from the interim analysis of the Phase III clinical trials. Taiwan compatriots who need information about mainland vaccines can look up specific information on these companies' websites.\nSecond question: The reason mainland netizens have reacted so strongly is directly related to the slander of the mainland by Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council. In the face of the epidemic, life comes first. Guided by our people-centered development philosophy and our pursuit of the value of life above all, we have repeatedly stated our willingness to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic. The DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, not only turn a blind eye to the mainland's goodwill but even maliciously slander it, and rudely block the possibility of benefiting the Taiwan people by strengthening epidemic prevention. The DPP authorities' conduct on cross-Strait epidemic issues since last year has been seen by the Taiwan people, and seen by mainland people too.\nRight now Taiwan compatriots are facing ever-growing epidemic pressure and harm. The latest public opinion poll shows that as many as 85% of Taiwan residents are worried that their family members will be infected with COVID-19, and nearly half are willing to be vaccinated immediately with any qualified vaccine. The DPP authorities should put the lives, health, and safety of Taiwan compatriots first, immediately stop political manipulation targeting the mainland, and remove artificial political obstacles, so that broad Taiwan compatriots can have mainland vaccines available as soon as possible and get through this difficult time early.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广台海之声记者","Taiwan’s economic affairs authority recently released statistics showing that in April this year, orders from Taiwan enterprises to the mainland grew by more than 40% year on year, while mainland investment in Taiwan fell by more than 50% year on year. In your view, what new characteristics does cross-Strait economic and trade exchange show?","Cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges help leverage complementary advantages and promote the common economic development of both sides. They are a good thing that is mutually beneficial. The DPP authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, have arbitrarily restricted cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, subjecting cross-Strait trade to numerous artificial interferences. Ultimately, what they harm are the vital interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and this does not win popular support. We will, as always, promote cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges, deepen exchange and cooperation in all fields, and seek greater well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, in addition to the worsening epidemic, Taiwan has also experienced repeated island-wide regional power outages. Some Taiwanese economic experts have pointed out that the renewable energy generation targets planned by the DPP authorities are far from expectations, while nuclear power, which accounts for a large share, will be completely shut down, so power shortages on the island are probably…","Recently, Taiwan has experienced frequent power outages, which have indeed caused much inconvenience to Taiwan compatriots and businesses and affected their vital interests. The main causes of the outages are well known to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. As for how to deal with this situation going forward, this is something Taiwan compatriots and the industry should reflect on even more deeply.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","彭博社记者","John Cena, male lead of “Fast & Furious,” recently posted a video on Weibo apologizing for his earlier improper remarks involving Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Taiwan is part of China, which is well known in the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Recently, after a meeting between US President Joe Biden and South Korean President Moon Jae-in, a US-ROK joint statement was issued that includes content on the so-called peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's response?","The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and is China's internal affair, admitting no external interference. It is precisely the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces who collude with external forces, continuously engage in provocations seeking “independence,” seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and bring disaster to ordinary Taiwan people. We hope relevant countries will abide by the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Reports say this round of the epidemic in Taiwan may not peak until June 15. In just 10 days, new cases have exceeded four thousand. May I ask the spokesperson: if the epidemic on the island continues to rage, will the mainland consider suspending cross-Strait flights and prohibiting cross-Strait cargo business?","Recently, the COVID-19 epidemic on the island has become increasingly severe, and the epidemic prevention pressure faced by Taiwan compatriots continues to increase. We feel this deeply and hope that Taiwan compatriots can overcome the epidemic and get through this difficult time as soon as possible.\nEpidemic prevention is paramount, and life comes first. We will strengthen control and strictly implement the measures to “prevent imported cases from outside.” Doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202105/t20210526_12355044.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-27","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwanese leader Tsai Ing-wen said yesterday that China intervened to stop a deal that would provide Germany's BioNtech vaccine to the island. Can the foreign ministry confirm and give any explanation why it made this decision?","I took this question at this podium yesterday and you may refer to my reply in case you were not here then.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210527_9170753.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1879058.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-05-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Japanese Defense White Paper 2021 will include for the first time the content that “a stable Taiwan situation is of great importance to Japan’s security and world stability”. It claimed that China’s military actions have raised some concerns. The Japanese white paper also accused the activities of China Coast Guard’s vessels around the Diaoyu Islands\" violating international law\". Please…","Recently, the Japanese side, in disregard of the basic norms governing international relations, has grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs, deliberately played up the so-called “China military threat”, and groundlessly criticized China’s legitimate maritime activities. China firmly opposes that and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. On this issue, what the Japanese side should do is to bear in mind the dire miseries its aggression against China has brought to the Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. Japan should correctly review and deeply reflect on the history of aggression by Japanese militarists. China urges the Japanese side to follow the principle of learning from history and looking into the future, be cautious with its words and deeds and do not overstretch its arms on issues concerning China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and work with China to push bilateral relations along the right track.\nThe Diaoyu Island and its affiliated islands are inherent territory of China. This is a fact solidly backed by historical records and legal documents. The Diaoyu Islands were illegally occupied by the Japanese imperialist in 1895 during the Sino-Japanese War of 1894-1895. After the end of WWII in 1945, sovereignty over the Diaoyu Islands was returned to China in accordance with the international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration in 1943 and the Potsdam Proclamation in 1945. Therefore, the China Coast Guard’s vessels have full right to carry out patrol and law enforcement in waters off the Diaoyu Islands as a legitimate way of exercising national sovereignty.\nInternational law is a just instrument that serves the whole world. It will not be tilted or distorted by any single country’s reckless and irresponsible talks for self-interests. Japan’s false accusation of China’s activities as violating the international law exactly reveals its blatant contempt for the law. Those holding this view should go to read the Cairo Declaration and Potsdam Proclamation. China will continue to resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly defend the outcome of the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War and the international order based on international law.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-05/31/content_4886488.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-05-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Defense Security Cooperation Agencyof the US Department of Defense plans to announce the sale of the M109A6 self-propelled howitzer and other offensive weapons to Taiwan. It will be the first arms sale to Taiwan after the Biden administration took office. According to other reports, Taiwan air force recently test-fired the AIM-120 medium-range air-to-air missile in southeast Taiwan, which…","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affairs. We firmly oppose any country selling weapons to Taiwan or having military interactions in any form with Taiwan. The US arms sale to Taiwan seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the US side to abide by the principle of non-interference in other countries' internal affairs, a basic norm of international relations clearly set out in the Charter of the United Nations and the Declaration on Principles of International Law concerning Friendly Relations and Co-operation among States, honor its solemn commitments to China on the Taiwan question, handle Taiwan-related issues carefully and properly, cease official exchanges and military contacts in any form with the island and stop arms sales to Taiwan.\nTaiwan's Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities colluded with and catered to external force and harmed the interests of the Chinese nation.Theyeven attempted to “seek independence by force\", which will only lead Taiwan compatriots into the abyss of disaster. We sternly warn the DPP authorities that any attempt or act of courting foreign supportfor separatist purposes is doomed to be futile and bound to fail. The PLA will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart any separatist attempt for \"Taiwan independence\" and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-05/31/content_4886488.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-05-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Australian defense minister recently said that the possibility for a conflict in the Taiwan Strait should not be underestimated. The Secretary of Australia’s Department of Home Affairs warned of an increasing drumbeat to war and argued that Australia must be ready for that. What's your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an integral part of China. The one-China principle is a common understanding of the international community. Recently, the Australian side has taken a series of provocative actions, and some people have even incited confrontation and exaggerated the threat of war on Taiwan-related issues. Such actions are incredibly irresponsible. We express strong dissatisfaction and resolute opposition to that.\nCurrently, China-Australia relations face serious difficulties. The responsibility lies squarely with the Australian side. We have noted some rational voices in Australia calling on the Australian side to remain calm and prudent on the Taiwan question. For example, former Australian Prime Minister Kevin Rudd criticized the speculation about war with China as \"pouring fuel on the fire unnecessarily\". John Hewson, a former leader of Australia’s Liberal Party, wrote that the situation across the Taiwan Strait has nothing to do with Australia's national interests. We hope the Australian side will not go further down the wrong path and can do more things conducive to the relations between the two countries and the two militaries.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-05/31/content_4886488.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2021-05-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: DPP authority leader Tsai Ing-wen claimed that, because of mainland interference, Taiwan has been unable to sign a contract with the original manufacturer of the German vaccine BNT (BioNTech) to purchase vaccines. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.","BEIJING, May 27 (Xinhua) — Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 27th in response to a question that the claim that the mainland is blocking the sale of BNT vaccines to Taiwan is pure fabrication. This lie by the leader of the DPP authorities once again exposes their consistent political tactics of shifting blame to the mainland and evading responsibility, and their habitual tricks of diverting attention and covering up problems.\nShe said that, as everyone knows, as early as March 2020, Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group signed an agreement with Germany's BNT company to participate in the development of the BNT vaccine and to hold exclusive commercial rights in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. The DPP authorities are fully aware of this, yet they did not follow the proper path. They insisted on violating commercial rules and the principle of good faith by bypassing Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group to purchase vaccines directly from Germany's BNT company. Knowing that this could not be done and yet doing it shows that they were not considering how to meet the actual needs of Taiwan residents, but were merely putting on a show to deceive the island's public and to gain political advantage for themselves.\nZhu Fenglian said that people can see very clearly that on the vaccine issue, it is the DPP authorities who have been putting up obstacles. To this day, the epidemic is spreading on the island, and the public is desperately waiting for vaccines, yet the DPP authorities still cling to political manipulation, throwing out various excuses and staging various scenes, and continue to trample the life, health, and sanitary well-being of the island's residents under their own political interests. Every extra day this charade continues, a precious window for epidemic prevention is lost by one more day, and the island's residents will pay with their lives and health for one more day.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210527_12355405.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-28","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","The US Senate has taken a step toward passing a bill to bolster US economic competitiveness and confront China's rise. It would devote spending in R&D and domestic semiconductor manufacturing. The bill also includes measures directly targeting China on human rights and its influence in the US. Similarly, US Secretary of Commerce Gina Raimondo said the Biden administration's jobs plan is \"all about competing with…","On your first question, recently China has repeatedly stated its solemn position on continued US Congress action regarding legislation with negative content on China. The legislation disregards facts, hypes up the so-called \"China threat\" and \"malign influence\", calls for all-out strategic competition with China, and even lobbies for a decoupling and confrontation between China and the US. Such unpopular moves run counter to the aspiration for bilateral exchange and cooperation shared by people in both countries and beyond. China firmly rejects them.\nChina's objective is never about overtaking, replacing or outcompeting the US, but about constant self-improvement to become a better version of China and enable the Chinese people to lead better lives. As the world's top two economies, China and the US have highly intertwined interests. Our cooperation in such areas as economy, trade, science and technology and education is mutually beneficial in nature. Both China and the US stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. Working together, we can achieve great things in the benefit of both countries and the world while confrontation spells disaster for both countries and the world.\nI'd like to reiterate that China is committed to forging a relationship with the US featuring no conflict, no confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation. At the same time, we will continue to firmly safeguard our sovereignty, security and development interests. We urge the US to adjust its mindset, look at China and China's development in a rational light, respect the Chinese people's legitimate right to development and stop pushing negative legislation on China to avoid undermining China-US relations and cooperation in important areas.\nOn your second question, I stated China's position on the Taiwan region's access to vaccines yesterday. The channel for China's Taiwan region to obtain vaccines from the mainland is unfettered. The Taiwan authorities' attempt to seek independence by exploiting the issue of vaccines won't succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210528_9170754.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1879392.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-28","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","Japan and the EU held a summit yesterday and released a joint statement, which explicitly stressed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and called for peaceful settlement of the Taiwan question. Do you have a comment?","The above-mentioned remarks by Japan and Europe have completely gone beyond the scope of normal development of bilateral relations, and are harmful to international peace and stability, mutual understanding and trust among regional countries, and the interests of a third party. This obviously runs counter to their stated goal of \"building a more secure, democratic and stable world\". China deplores and rejects relevant remarks in the joint statement of the Japan-EU summit, and will continue to firmly defend its national sovereignty, security and development interests.\nFor quite a while, driven by selfish intention of containing China and in total disregard of the basic norms governing international relations, the Japanese government has made an issue out of China on various occasions, portraying China as a threat, ganging up with a few others to pursue geopolitical confrontation, throwing mud at China based on lies and false information, and grossly interfering in China's internal affairs. Japan's wrong approach goes against the trend of the times of win-win cooperation and have brought adverse effects on bilateral relations and regional stability.\nI'd like to emphasize once again that the affairs of Hong Kong and Xinjiang are purely China's internal affairs. There are no human rights issues whatsoever, and no foreign government, organization or individual has the right to interfere. Taiwan constitutes part of China's territory. China will never allow any country to interfere in Taiwan-related issues in any way. China must and will be reunified. As far as the situation across the Taiwan Strait is concerned, reunification is the best solution to maintaining regional and world peace and stability. The Japanese side is advised not to stretch its arm too long, still less stir up trouble everywhere.\nRegarding maritime issues, with the concerted efforts of relevant regional countries, the situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable. China resolutely safeguards national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and at the same time, stands ready to properly settle maritime disputes with countries concerned through consultation and negotiation, to jointly safeguard regional peace and tranquility. As for the handling of nuclear contaminated water from Fukushima, since the Japanese side attaches such great importance to maritime issues, why does Japan ignore its due international responsibilities and obligations? Why turning a blind eye to lives and well-being of mankind, and global maritime cleanness and safety? And why not revoke its release decision immediately? The Japanese side keeps talking about freedom and openness. Does it mean freedom of release?\nI would like to stress that on dealing with China, megaphone diplomacy is not the right approach, attacks and smears will backfire, ganging up won't help, and coercion and confrontation is a dead end. We hope Japan will know better than to go further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210528_9170754.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1879392.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, May 28. The heads of the Fuzhou and Xiamen Red Cross societies said on May 27 that they were willing to donate COVID-19 vaccines to Kinmen and Matsu. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council rejected the offers, saying the mainland had never provided any vaccine information through existing cross-Strait channels, that Taiwan's relevant authorities had received no formal document or application, and emphasizing that vaccines for Taiwan should be provided through the formal vaccine import procedures. On May 28, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions by saying that the Mainland Affairs Council's remarks are still fabricated pretexts to block Taiwan compatriots from using mainland vaccines and to ease the epidemic as soon as possible.\nShe said that in fact, on the issue of importing mainland vaccines into Taiwan, facing the good intentions of the mainland, which hopes to do its utmost to help Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic, and facing the good deeds of some civil organizations willing to donate vaccines, the DPP authorities have consistently used all kinds of excuses to block and reject them, and even openly slandered and smeared mainland vaccines. By refusing mainland vaccines regardless of the safety of Taiwan compatriots' lives, they have shown cold-blooded disregard for the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian said that the question is simple: whether the DPP authorities can clearly answer whether the life and health of Taiwan compatriots matter, whether their need for vaccines must be met, and whether the mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO should be used. The so-called procedures are deliberate obstruction. We advise the DPP authorities that the epidemic on the island is worsening, epidemic prevention pressure is growing, and the death toll is rising. The urgent task is to let the island's public receive mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO as soon as possible, and not to play with words, play political games, or miss the opportunity to build an immunity barrier for the island's public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210528_12355644.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-05-31","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","According to media reports, the Japanese government said the other day that it would study the possibility of providing vaccines to Taiwan, to which the Taiwan authorities expressed thanks. Earlier heads of the Red Cross Society branches in Chinese cities Fuzhou and Xiamen expressed readiness to donate vaccines to Jinmen and Mazu in the Taiwan region, but the Mainland Affairs Council declined the offer. Do you…","Recently many counties, cities and groups in the Taiwan region have been calling for early access to vaccines from the mainland and some institutions have announced that they will receive donations from the mainland. All this demonstrates the Taiwan people's confidence in mainland vaccines. We expressed on many occasions the readiness to do our best to help Taiwan compatriots fight the virus.However, the DPP authorities, proceeding from selfish political calculations, turned a blind eye to the goodwill of the mainland, and even resorted to malicious smears and various other means to thwart the shipment of vaccines from the mainland to the island. This is running roughshod over the life and health of our compatriots in Taiwan.\nChina always supports international cooperation in combating COVID-19 and has been taking active efforts in this regard. That being said, we are firmly against those who exploit the pandemic to put on political shows or even meddle in China's internal affairs. I've noticed that Japan can barely ensure adequate supply of vaccines at home. Under such circumstances, the Japanese government's announcement of considering providing vaccines to China's Taiwan region has drawn doubts from media and the public including in Taiwan. I would like to stress that vaccine assistance should be restored to its origin purpose, which is to save lives, and should not be reduced to a tool for selfish political gains.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210531_9170755.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1880107.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-05-31","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan's DPP said today that China prevented Taiwan from getting vaccines. Do you have any comment on that?","The State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson has already responded to the relevant question, which you can refer to. As we have said many times, we stand ready to do our very best to help our Taiwan compatriots bring the epidemic under control and defeat the virus at an early date. The DPP authorities are extremely irresponsible to our Taiwan compatriots by using political manipulation to divert attention. They should immediately stop all kinds of slanders and smears on the mainland helping Taiwan compatriots in their fight against the epidemic, and take practical actions to remove man-made obstacles, so as to ensure the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202105/t20210531_9170755.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1880107.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: recently, voices across the island have urgently called for mainland vaccines to be supplied to Taiwan, but the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan continues its old game of political manipulation, slandering the mainland for “political operations,” intending to obstruct possible assistance to Taiwan from third parties. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering questions.","XINHUA, Beijing, May 31 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian (朱凤莲), responding to questions on the 31st, said that epidemic prevention is paramount and life comes first. What the broad Taiwan compatriots expect are scientific and effective epidemic prevention and control measures and related support. The DPP authorities should quickly remove their political demons and stop harming the life and health of the people on the island.\nShe said that the COVID-19 epidemic in Taiwan is becoming increasingly grave, the shortage of vaccines is prominent, the epidemic prevention pressure faced by the broad Taiwan compatriots continues to grow, and their life and health safety faces serious threats. Some political parties, groups, personages and some counties and cities on the island have repeatedly called on the DPP authorities to quickly remove the political obstacles to the delivery of mainland vaccines to Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that we attach great importance to this and are willing to make our greatest efforts to help the broad Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic, including promptly making arrangements to provide mainland vaccines to Taiwan compatriots and supporting relevant civil organizations in Shanghai, Jiangsu and Fujian in donating vaccines to Taiwan compatriots, so that the broad Taiwan compatriots can have mainland vaccines available as soon as possible.\nShe said that, in contrast, at this critical juncture of epidemic prevention, the DPP authorities let political demons run amok, turn a deaf ear to the appeals of the Taiwan public, disregard the safety of the people's lives and health, and keep playing political tricks, attempting to shift blame onto the mainland, smear it, divert attention and blur the focus. Every additional day they continue this way is a further delay in the precious window for epidemic prevention, and the Taiwan public will be forced to pay an even higher price in lives and health.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202105/t20210531_12356084.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-01","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","According to media reports, as the US marks the National Memorial Day, many US soldiers stationed in the ROK were granted leave and held mass gatherings without wearing masks in violation of epidemic prevention rules on the Haeundae Beach of Busan, causing an uproar among the local residents. Do you have a comment?","We noted relevant reports. If my memory serves me right, this is not the first time that US troops in the ROK have violated local epidemic prevention rules.\nWe hope the US can earnestly assume its responsibility, discipline its forces stationed overseas and honor its pledge to support international anti-virus efforts with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1880521.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1880495.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-01","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Taiwan's epidemic continues to spread, vaccines are in severe shortage, and calls from all sectors on the island to import vaccines from the mainland are growing louder. However, the DPP authorities continue to obstruct and restrict this under pretexts such as “questionable safety,” while at the same time announcing the signing of contracts to purchase self-developed vaccines that have not…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 1 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 1st in response to questions that the DPP authorities should earnestly listen to the calls of all sectors of the island for safe vaccines, put the life, health, safety, well-being and interests of the broad Taiwan compatriots first, quickly change the practice of political manipulation on vaccine issues, and remove artificial obstacles to the import of mainland vaccines to Taiwan as early as possible.\nMa Xiaoguang said, \"We have noted these reports. As to whether there is any suspicion of economic arbitrage or stock speculation, we are not in a position to comment.\"\nMa Xiaoguang said that the epidemic on the island continues to spread, and the epidemic prevention pressure faced by Taiwan residents is growing. Recently, some political parties, counties and cities, groups and individuals on the island have successively called for opening the import of mainland vaccines or the purchase of BioNTech (BNT) vaccines. Public opinion polls on the island show that more than 90 percent of respondents said that as long as there are qualified vaccines to get, they are willing to take them, including mainland vaccines.\nHe pointed out that we deeply care about the life, health and well-being of Taiwan residents, and are willing to do our utmost to provide assistance. Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group holds the exclusive commercial rights to BioNTech's mRNA COVID-19 vaccine in the mainland and in Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. The pharmaceutical group previously said it was willing to make the BNT vaccines it represents available to Taiwan residents. We are actively assisting relevant parties in Taiwan in contacting Fosun. At the same time, Sinopharm's relevant vaccines have been included by the World Health Organization in its global \"Emergency Use Listing,\" and they are convenient to transport and highly safe, which is very conducive to universal vaccination. As of May 31, the mainland had reported a cumulative total of more than 661 million doses of COVID-19 vaccines administered, and we are willing to make arrangements as quickly as possible so that broad Taiwan compatriots have mainland vaccines available.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210601_12356328.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: a spokesperson for Taiwan’s external affairs department cited false reports from foreign media and again fabricated that Taiwan failed to purchase vaccines from the original manufacturer, Germany’s BioNTech (BNT), because of mainland interference, and falsely accused the mainland of interfering in Taiwan’s vaccine procurement process. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 2: TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 2nd, said: While the epidemic in Taiwan continues to rage and Taiwan compatriots are longing for vaccines, the DPP authorities have once again resorted to their usual tactics, using false foreign media reports as a pretext and fabricating lies to shift blame onto the mainland, attempting to make the mainland a scapegoat to cover up their incompetence and evade responsibility. This is a completely baseless blame-shifting trick.\nHe pointed out that we have stated many times that we are willing to do our utmost to help broad Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic as soon as possible and to let Taiwan compatriots quickly receive mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO. We have also repeatedly explained to the outside world that the DPP authorities themselves set up obstacles and did not procure BNT vaccines through the normal agency channels. The general agent for the BNT vaccine in Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan is Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group, and purchasing BNT vaccines must go through Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group. This is a basic commercial rule. The DPP authorities know this full well, yet they knowingly do what cannot be done and act against the proper course. What is consumed is precious time for epidemic prevention, and what is lost is precious lives of the people. This is the DPP authorities placing political self-interest above human life. Perhaps in the eyes of the DPP authorities, the lives of the people are merely a number.\nMa Xiaoguang said that time passes day by day, and the number of infections and deaths on the island increases day by day. Every day the DPP authorities continue their political manipulation is another day of precious epidemic prevention opportunity lost. The earlier the island’s people receive vaccines, the earlier their lives and health will be protected. People cannot help but ask: in the calculations of the DPP authorities, are the lives and health of the broad population of the island really so inconsequential?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210602_12356578.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-04","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Today Japan will deliver to Taiwan 1.24 million doses of AstraZeneca coronavirus vaccine for free, more than doubling their current stores, what's China's comment on this? Japan has indicated it's a friendly gesture, does China also see it this way?","I noted relevant reports. China's position on this was already articulated. The mainland and Taiwan are one family. Our hearts are with our Taiwan compatriots who are faced with the grave situation. We have always made clear the readiness to do our utmost to help our compatriots in Taiwan overcome the difficulties at an early date.\nHowever, despite the goodwill of the mainland and the eagerness of the majority of Taiwan compatriots to use vaccines from the mainland, the DPP authorities tried every means to obstruct the shipping of vaccines from the mainland to Taiwan, and even falsely claimed that the mainland was obstructing its vaccine procurement. For their own selfish political gains, the DPP authorities constantly seek political manipulation over anti-epidemic cooperation, showing disregard of the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots and violating the basic humanitarian spirit.\nEpidemic prevention and control is the most important task and people's lives should be given top priority. I would like to advise the Taiwan authorities to focus on scientific epidemic prevention and control, remove man-made political obstacles, and ensure that the lives, health, interests and well-being of our Taiwan compatriots are effectively protected.\nChina always supports anti-epidemic cooperation and has made positive contributions to this end. We hope that relevant parties will earnestly follow through on the original aspiration of providing vaccines to save lives, rather than be obsessed with political posturing.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1881482.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1881464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-04","Wang Wenbin","","日本将于今天向台湾免费提供124万剂阿斯利康新冠疫苗，是台湾目前库存的两倍多。中方对此有何评论？日方暗示此举展现了友好姿态，中方对此是否认同？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1881482.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1881464.shtml",0,3,0,""],[2,"2021-06-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to Taiwan media reports, Japan will provide Taiwan with a batch of AstraZeneca COVID-19 vaccines, and the DPP authorities have expressed gratitude. What comment do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 4 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 4th, saying that people in Taiwan all understand that at present only mainland vaccines that are safe, efficient and sufficient in quantity can effectively protect against the virus. But the DPP authorities still place political manipulation above the health and safety of the people. The spread of the epidemic in Taiwan is entering a new peak, and the lives and health of the people will suffer serious harm. Is the political life of the DPP authorities more important than the lives of the Taiwan people? Is it more important to build an immunity barrier among the people on the island sooner, or to keep playing the game of cross-Strait political confrontation? The DPP authorities must give an answer to the broad masses of Taiwan people.\nMa Xiaoguang said that since the outbreak of the epidemic in Taiwan, we have repeatedly said we are willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic as soon as possible, and are willing to provide Taiwan compatriots with mainland vaccines that the World Health Organization has included in its “Emergency Use List.” Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group has also said it is willing to make the mRNA COVID-19 vaccine of BNT (BioNTech), which it participated in developing and agency-distributing, available to people in Taiwan. More than half a month has passed, and the DPP authorities have fabricated all kinds of excuses and obstructed the entry of mainland vaccines into Taiwan, causing the numbers of infections and deaths on the island to climb steadily.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210604_12357018.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: What is the TAO's attitude toward this incident?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 4 (electronic dispatch). According to reports, on May 31, a passenger holding a positive screening test certificate boarded Taiwan’s UNI Air flight B7-511 from Taipei to Xiamen and arrived in Xiamen. In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on June 4 that this incident exposed a series of loopholes at all links of epidemic prevention on the island. We demand that relevant parties in Taiwan face these problems squarely, not create epidemic prevention breaches that endanger the life and health safety of people on both sides of the Strait, and truly shoulder their responsibilities.\nAsked whether control measures would be further strengthened given the increasingly severe epidemic situation in Taiwan, Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in response.\nHe said that since the outbreak of the epidemic, all parts of the mainland have strictly implemented measures to prevent imported cases, applied strict quarantine measures to all persons entering the country, and built a solid quarantine line at ports. According to epidemic prevention requirements, all passengers boarding cross-Strait flights must present a negative nucleic acid test certificate issued within 3 days.\nMa Xiaoguang said that, regarding the airline’s violation of mainland epidemic prevention regulations by allowing a person holding a positive nucleic acid test certificate to board a flight to Xiamen, relevant mainland departments have summoned the airline for talks, ordered it to rectify, plugged the loopholes, and required that similar situations must not happen again. Regarding a Taiwan resident surnamed Chen, who violated mainland epidemic prevention regulations by boarding an aircraft and filled in false health information, relevant parties will handle the matter seriously in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210604_12357054.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-07","Wang Wenbin","New York Times","What is the reaction of China to the visit by the three US Senators to Taiwan and particularly the use of an air force jet for that trip?","The visit by relevant US senators and their meeting with the leader of the Taiwan region gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. China strongly opposes this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side. We urge the US to faithfully implement its one-China policy, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately discontinue all forms of official interactions with Taiwan and handle issues relating to Taiwan in a prudent manner. It should avoid sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and causing further damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347058.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1881907.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-07","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Just like to have a quick follow-up on an earlier question, and then I have a separate question, so bear with me, please. On the Taiwan visit by the US senators, there was a question around the type of aircraft that was used, a C-17 military aircraft. Does this constitute the crossing of a line on Taiwan matters by the US? That's my first follow-up question on the Taiwan issue. Separately, I'd like to ask about a…","On your first question, I already stated China's solemn position. We urge the US to faithfully implement its one-China policy, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately discontinue all forms of official interactions with Taiwan and handle issues relating to Taiwan in a prudent manner. It should avoid sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and causing further damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, I'm not aware of what you mentioned.\nI'd like to stress that economic globalization is the objective reality and historical trend. The politicization and weaponization of science, technology and economic and trade issues based on ideology and the formation of exclusive small groups run counter to the principles of market economy and fair competition. They will only artificially divide the world, undermine international trade rules, threaten the security of global industrial and supply chains, and ultimately do harm to others and oneself.\nWe hope relevant countries will abandon the zero-sum thinking, go with the trend of the times, contribute more to normal science and technology exchange and trade in the world, and foster an open, fair and non-discriminatory environment for innovation to flourish. All should work together to build an open world economy to achieve common development and prosperity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347058.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1881907.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 7 (Electric). In response to the recent visit to Taiwan by three US federal senators, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 7th in response to questions: We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately, and stop all forms of official exchanges and military contacts with the Taiwan region of China.\nMa said that at present, the epidemic on the island continues to worsen. The DPP authorities disregard the life and health safety of the broad Taiwan compatriots, deliberately provoke cross-Strait relations and create incidents. This once again exposes the DPP authorities' 'independence'-seeking nature, which treats people's lives as worthless grass, disregards the health and well-being of the Taiwan people, engages in political manipulation, and their ugly face.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210607_12357590.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 7: In response to green media in Taiwan falsely claiming that the mainland had obstructed Japan from providing vaccines to Taiwan, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 7th: Fabricating lies cannot ease the increasingly intense anxiety of the island's people over the epidemic, and it cannot escape the responsibility for neglecting the lives and health of the people.\nHe said that since mid-May this year, the epidemic on the island has spread and intensified, the number of infected people has continued to rise, and the number of deaths has kept climbing. As of June 7, a cumulative total of 286 deaths had been recorded, and the fatality rate exceeds the global average. We are deeply worried about the lives and health of the island's people.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that since this round of the epidemic outbreak on the island, we have, from the very beginning, stated that we are willing to do our utmost to help the broad Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic, and we have repeatedly said that we want the broad Taiwan compatriots to have vaccines available as soon as possible and are willing to provide Taiwan compatriots with safe and effective vaccines. The DPP authorities, on the one hand, loudly spread the so-called lie that the mainland is blocking Taiwan from obtaining vaccines, and on the other hand, go to great lengths to prevent the broad Taiwan compatriots from obtaining vaccines from the mainland. They have even returned kindness with enmity, loudly slandering and defaming the mainland for its efforts to help Taiwan compatriots.\nHe said that, as everyone knows, widespread vaccination is a necessary measure for epidemic prevention and control. The DPP authorities' loud and malicious hype cannot conceal the truth of the severe vaccine shortage on the island; relying on fabricated lies cannot gloss over the loopholes in epidemic prevention and control; relying on the spread of rumors cannot fool the island's people; and relying on confrontation and hostility toward the mainland cannot ease the epidemic on the island.\nMa Xiaoguang said that lies and the epidemic are equally deadly. The DPP authorities still need to honestly face the grim epidemic situation on the island and genuinely take the lives of ordinary people seriously. The sooner the mainland's vaccines are opened up, the sooner the lives and health of the island's people will be protected. Stop placing political self-interest above the lives of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210607_12357599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-08","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The US has said that it will soon start discussing a trade deal with Taiwan. How will this affect the Chinese mainland's trade negotiations and diplomatic ties with Washington? And if there is such a trade deal with Taiwan, how would Beijing react?","China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We oppose any agreement with implications of sovereignty and of official nature between countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region. We urge the US to act on its commitment to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, discontinue all forms of official interactions with the Taiwan region, prudently handle Taiwan-related issues and refrain from sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347059.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1882167.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-09","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","US Senate passed a sweeping bill intended to boost the country's ability to compete with Chinese technology. The bill authorizes $190 billion to strengthen US technology and $54 billion to strengthen US production of semiconductors and telecommunications equipment. It also bans TikTok from being downloaded on government devices and blocks the purchases of Chinese drones. Do you have any comment on this?","The content on China in the bill just passed by the US Senate distorts facts, denigrates China's development path and domestic and foreign policies, hypes up \"China threat\", advocating strategic competition with China, and gravely interferes in China's domestic affairs on issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Tibet. Filled with Cold War zero-sum mentality, it runs counter to the aspiration for more exchange and cooperation shared by people from all walks of life in both countries. China firmly rejects it.\nHow the US intends to develop and strengthen its competitiveness is its own business, but we are firmly against the US making an issue out of China and perceiving it as an imaginary enemy. The US is the greatest threat to itself. Getting its own house in order trumps all else.\nChina is committed to the path of peaceful development. The objective of our development is to constantly improve ourselves and to enable the Chinese people to lead happier lives. Nobody can deprive the Chinese people of their legitimate right to development.\nChina is committed to developing a relationship with the US featuring no conflict, no confrontation, mutual respect and win-win cooperation. That being said, we will continue to resolutely defend our sovereignty, security and development interests. We urge the US to adjust its mindset, look at China's development and China-US relations in a rational light, stop pushing the relevant bill and stop meddling in China's internal affairs to avoid undermining overall bilateral relations and cooperation in important areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1882549.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1882538.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 9 — In response to a recent interview in which the head of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei office told Taiwanese media that “the deterioration of cross-Strait relations was not caused by Taiwan,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 9th: It is well known that the root cause of the tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations is the DPP authorities’ stubborn insistence on the “Taiwan independence” position and refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Out of political self-interest, they have continually incited “anti-China and China-hatred” sentiment on the island, stirred up cross-Strait confrontation, and obstructed and undermined normal cross-Strait exchanges. The responsibility for cross-Strait relations reaching their current state lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nHe said that the epidemic on the island is currently worsening. The DPP authorities, disregarding the life and health and safety of the island’s people, have placed their pursuit of “independence” for private gain above the lives and well-being of the people. They have slandered and smeared the mainland’s efforts to help Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic, further exposing their true nature of seeking “independence.”\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that we have always upheld promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, have always adhered to the people-centered development philosophy, and have done practical things, good things, and things that resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. In the course of fighting the COVID-19 epidemic, we have made our utmost efforts to provide assistance to the broad Taiwan compatriots. But we will never allow the DPP authorities to treat our goodwill as an opportunity to seek “independence,” and we will never allow anyone to split Taiwan from China in any way.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we urge the US government and certain people to act in practice in accordance with the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to distinguish right from wrong on the Taiwan question, to be prudent in their words and deeds, not to send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and to play a constructive role in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210609_12358201.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-10","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","On June 9, Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihide Suga listed Australia, New Zealand, and Taiwan as \"nations\" that had adopted strong restrictions on private rights in a debate with opposition party leader at the National Diet. Do you have any comment?","I noted relevant reports. Japanese leaders flagrantly refer to Taiwan as a \"country\" on multiple occasions, severely violating principles set out in the four political documents including the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement and its solemn and repeated commitment of not seeing Taiwan as a country. China is strongly dissatisfied with Japan's wrong remarks and has lodged solemn representations to the Japanese side. We ask Japan to make prompt clarification, remove the severe damage and ensure that such things won't happen again.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations, the basic trust and good faith between the two countries and the international rule of law and justice. We seriously urge the Japanese side to earnestly honor its commitment, be prudent in words and actions, avoid undermining China's sovereignty in any form and refrain from sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1882905.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1882887.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-11","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Yesterday, the US Trade Representative and her Taiwanese counterpart had a meeting in which they agreed to resume the discussions on the trade and investment framework agreement between the two parties. Do you have any comment on this and on those contacts? And also, do you have any comment to make about Taiwan's expressed interest in joining the CPTPP?","On your first question, China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We firmly oppose all forms of official interactions between the US and Taiwan and reject any agreement with implications of sovereignty and of official nature between countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region.\nChina urges the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, discontinue all forms of official interactions with the Taiwan region, avoid sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" forces to avoid undermining China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, as we have repeatedly said, the Taiwan region's participation in regional economic cooperation must be handled on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1883214.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1883188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to Taiwan media reports, due to a severe vaccine shortage on the island, many Taiwan compatriots have recently hoped to travel to the mainland for vaccination. What attitude does the mainland take toward this? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 11. TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to questions on the 11th, said: We fully understand the eager desire of Taiwan compatriots to be vaccinated with mainland vaccines as soon as possible in order to protect their own life and health and safety, and we are willing to do our utmost to provide assistance. For Taiwan compatriots who travel to the mainland on civil aviation passenger flights, as long as they meet the vaccination conditions, they may be vaccinated on the mainland under relevant policies, on the premise of strictly complying with entry epidemic prevention regulations (including before boarding and after arrival), and on a voluntary basis with informed consent. According to incomplete statistics, as of May 31, 62,000 Taiwan compatriots had been vaccinated on the mainland.\nHe said: We attach great importance to the life and health and safety of the broad Taiwan compatriots. Since the COVID-19 outbreak, in epidemic prevention and control, vaccination, and other areas, we have treated Taiwan compatriots on the mainland equally, without discrimination. After the outbreak in Taiwan in early May, we stated from the very beginning that we are willing to do our utmost to help the broad Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic and to make vaccines available to them as soon as possible.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out: As is well known, vaccines are the guarantee for overcoming the epidemic. As of June 8, more than 800 million doses of COVID-19 vaccines had been administered on the mainland. The World Health Organization has included China's Sinopharm and Sinovac vaccines in its Emergency Use Listing. Mainland vaccines have been approved for marketing or emergency use in more than 90 countries and regions, and more than 350 million doses have been supplied to the world, fully demonstrating that mainland vaccines have good safety and protective effectiveness. The epidemic on the island continues to spread, and the life, health, and well-being of Taiwan residents are increasingly threatened. Getting vaccinated as soon as possible is an effective way for the broad Taiwan compatriots to end the suffering of the epidemic's rampant spread at an early date. More than 80% of residents on the island are willing to be vaccinated with mainland vaccines and also hope that mainland vaccines can be imported as soon as possible. However, the DPP authorities disregard public opinion, ignore the life and health and safety of Taiwan compatriots, have persistently politicized the vaccine issue, and fabricate all kinds of excuses to obstruct Taiwan compatriots from using mainland vaccines. This has lost popular support.\nHe said: We urge the DPP authorities to earnestly listen to the calls of all walks of life and ordinary people on the island, to promptly remove the artificial obstacles to importing mainland vaccines into Taiwan, so that the broad Taiwan compatriots can get safe and effective mainland vaccines locally at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210611_12358743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 11. In response to the repeated public references by several Japanese government officials in recent days to Taiwan as a “country,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 11th in response to a question that Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose the erroneous statements by some Japanese officials regarding the Taiwan region of China, and we are shocked by the Japanese side's repeated wrongful actions on the Taiwan question. We urge the Japanese side to immediately correct its mistakes, act in practice in accordance with the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, exercise prudence on the Taiwan question, and not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that their attempts to collude with external forces to carry out acts violating the one-China principle cannot in the slightest alter the iron fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210611_12358830.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-15","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","On June 13, the G7 summit concluded and issued a communiqué, which made groundless accusations on China with regard to Xinjiang, Hong Kong and other issues. What is your comment?","We have noted that the G7 summit communiqué mentions China-related issues, deliberately slandering China on issues related to Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Taiwan as well as maritime issues, and interfering in China's internal affairs. Such moves seriously contravenes the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and the trend of the times for peace, development and win-win cooperation. It reveals the bad intentions of the US and a few other countries to create confrontation and estrangement and widen differences and disagreements. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to this.\nIssues related to Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Taiwan are purely China's internal affairs that brook no foreign interference. China is firmly resolved in safeguarding its sovereignty, security and development interests.\nI want to emphasize that multipolarization and democratic international relations are irresistible trend of the times. The era of one country or a bloc of countries dictating world affairs is over. Under the current situation, the international community need to strengthen solidarity and cooperation and practice true multilateralism more than ever. Countries should not seek bloc politics on the basis of the interests of small cliques, suppress different development models by holding ideology as the yardstick, and still less confuse right with wrong and shift blames onto others. The US is ill, very ill indeed. We'd like to advise the G7 to take its pulse and come up with a prescription for the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210615_9170765.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1883951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-15","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","In NBC News' exclusive interview, Russia's President Vladimir Putin said that \"we have developed a strategic partnership relationship- between Russia and China that previously had not been achieved in the history of our nations, a high level of trust and cooperation in all areas: in politics, in the economy, in the area of technology...\" He expressed support to China on issues related to Xinjiang and Taiwan and…","We highly appreciate President Putin's positive remarks on China-Russia relations. Indeed, China and Russia are united like a mountain, and our friendship is unbreakable. Under the strategic guidance of President Xi Jinping and President Putin, bilateral relations have withstood the test of the changing international landscape, setting an example of a new type of major-country relationship. The two countries have firmly supported each other on issues concerning each other's core interests, and the political mutual trust and strategic coordination between the two has been continuously consolidated and enhanced. In the first five months of this year, bilateral economic and trade volume surged by 23.6 percent, injecting strong impetus and confidence into the world economy, which is struggling to recover. Together, we have resisted political viruses, safeguarded the outcome of the victory of World War II and international equity and justice, and firmly defended genuine multilateralism and international equity and justice. Together, we have become an important force for stability in a turbulent world. It is fair to say that the China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for the new era is all-dimensional and all-weather. The sky is the limit for down-to-earth China-Russia cooperation, and we are full of confidence in the development of bilateral relations.\nIn one month's time, we will mark the 20th anniversary of the signing of the Treaty of Good-Neighborliness, Friendship and Cooperation between China and Russia, which is of special significance to bilateral relations. With this as the focus, the two sides will fully implement the consensus reached by the heads of state of the two countries, revisit the original aspiration of signing the treaty for enduring friendship and win-win cooperation, advance China-Russia cooperation at a higher starting point, in a broader scope and at a deeper level, and inject impetus into global strategic stability and world economic recovery.\nAs a Chinese proverb says, \"True gold doesn't fear the test of fire.\" We have to tell those who try every means to drive a wedge between China and Russia that any attempt to undermine China-Russia relations is doomed to fail. We hope they will not go further down the path of zero-sum game and political confrontation of blocs, but return to the right path of building a community with a shared future for mankind and play a constructive role in safeguarding world peace, stability and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210615_9170765.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1883951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-15","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","It is reported that Franz Gayl, a retired US Marine major who is now working at the Pentagon, is under a counterintelligence investigation by the Marine Corps for his two articles published in the Global Times that criticized open confrontation with China by the US regarding Taiwan. Reports say he could face an early exit from the civil service. What is China's comment on this?","I think many people would want to ask: Isn't the US a self-proclaimed champion of the freedom of speech and justice? Franz Gayl is under investigation just because he wrote two articles expressing different position from the US government. Why can't the US allow two articles clearly marked to represent the author's personal opinion?\nAs a matter of fact, similar cases abound in the US. Since the COVID-19 outbreak, many people in the US have spoken out. Dr. Helen Y. Chu, a whistle-blower, sounded the alarm on the epidemic in the US; Dr. McCarthy entreated US health authorities to test suspected cases; Captain Brett Crozier of the aircraft carrier USS Theodore Roosevelt wrote a letter to Navy leaders asking that most of the crew be taken ashore. These people have been either muzzled, investigated or dismissed from their posts just because they told the truth that the government doesn't like. Is this the way the US champions the freedom of speech? When clamoring for freedom of speech, the US side should really look at itself in the mirror rather than look at others through a magnifying glass.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210615_9170765.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1883951.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-16","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","The US-EU summit took place in Brussels on June 15. The statement of the summit mentioned China-related issues including Xinjiang, Tibet, Hong Kong, Taiwan, the East China Sea and the South China Sea, and accused China of economic coercion and disinformation campaigns. According to the statement, the US and the EU intend to closely consult and cooperate in the framework of their respective similar multi-faceted…","The content in the US-EU summit statement has gone far beyond the scope of normal development of bilateral relations. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to such moves to groundlessly interfere in China's domestic affairs, and create and spread disinformation. The US and the EU should reflect on their own serious problems and they are in no position to lecture others.\nWe oppose imposing one's own interest and requirement on other countries, forming small cliques and bloc politics targeting a third party, and dividing the world with ideology as the yardstick.\nThe US and the EU should follow the trend of the times for peace, development and win-win cooperation, abide by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, practice true multilateralism, and make their due contribution to the international community's efforts to fight the epidemic together and meet global challenges.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210616_9170766.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1884257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-16","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg News","A question about the Chinese air force sending aircraft close to Taiwan in recent days. Can you confirm this?","This is not a diplomatic issue. Please refer to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210616_9170766.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1884257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. I will host today's press conference and am willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","At last month's press conference, the spokesperson introduced the implementation of the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” in some localities. What new progress has been made recently?","Since the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” were issued, they have drawn attention from all sectors on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and wide praise from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. Localities and relevant departments have actively pushed for implementation in detail. At our earlier press conference, we introduced the implementation in Sichuan, Fujian, Zhejiang, Shandong and Guizhou provinces. Here we would like to introduce the progress Guangdong Province has made.\nTo implement the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” the Guangdong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, the Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the Forestry Bureau and 18 other departments, on the basis of in-depth research and extensive solicitation of opinions, issued and implemented the “Several Measures to Support Taiwan Compatriots and Taiwan-Invested Enterprises in Developing Agriculture and Forestry in Guangdong” on May 28. Focused on high-quality development of local agriculture and forestry, these measures further specify equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises and propose 34 support measures with Guangdong characteristics. For example, Taiwan-invested business entities engaged in agricultural production and operations in Guangdong may apply for support policies under the same conditions as local business entities for projects such as the agricultural comprehensive production capacity improvement project and the quality-driven agriculture project. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises participating in projects such as developing Guangdong's advantageous and distinctive agricultural products and rural living environment improvement may, if they meet the project application guidelines, apply for support policies under the same conditions as local residents and enterprises. The issuance and implementation of these measures will create a better environment and better conditions for the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in the agricultural and forestry sectors in Guangdong.\nWe will continue to work with relevant departments to strengthen overall coordination and guidance, and push for more solid progress in implementing the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” so as to achieve mutual benefit and win-win results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359727.htm"],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The epidemic on the island continues to spread, with a fatality rate among confirmed patients exceeding 3%, higher than the global average. Calls from all sectors on the island to relax restrictions on counties and cities and to allow private purchase of vaccines are very strong, yet the DPP authorities have imposed many restrictive conditions on private and business sector vaccine procurement and insist on…","We attach great importance to the life, health and safety of the vast majority of Taiwan compatriots. Since the outbreak of the epidemic on the island, we have from the very beginning said we are willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic as soon as possible, and have repeatedly said we want Taiwan compatriots to have vaccines available as soon as possible, and are willing to provide safe and effective vaccines to Taiwan compatriots.\nOver the past month, some political parties, counties and cities, groups and individuals on the island have repeatedly called for opening up the introduction of mainland vaccines, or purchasing the mRNA COVID-19 vaccine of BioNTech (BNT) from Germany, which Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group participated in developing and acts as agent for. The DPP authorities continue to refuse to introduce mainland vaccines. For private imports of vaccines to Taiwan, they also keep artificially setting obstacles, layering barriers through cumbersome procedures and harsh requirements. This “delay tactic” has left some counties and cities, the private sector, and business circles facing great difficulties in vaccine procurement, and the vast majority of Taiwan compatriots still cannot get vaccines when they need them most.\nIn stark contrast, as of June 14, the mainland had administered more than 900 million vaccine doses. The Sinopharm and Sinovac vaccines, both recognized by the WHO, have been approved for marketing or emergency use in more than 90 countries and regions, and have supplied over 350 million doses globally, fully demonstrating that mainland vaccines have good safety and protective effectiveness. People cannot help but ask: why is it that vaccines that people of all races and skin colors around the world can use, yet Taiwan compatriots, who are connected by blood, are deprived of the right to use them? Is manipulating cross-Strait confrontation and seeking one-party private gain really more important than the life, health and safety of Taiwan compatriots? In the face of stark reality, more and more Taiwan compatriots have come to realize that in critical moments, the foreign forces that the DPP authorities rely on do not take the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people seriously. The earlier the DPP authorities remove the artificial obstacles to importing mainland vaccines to Taiwan, the earlier the life and health safety of people on the island will be guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359728.htm"],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Two questions. First question: during the just-past Dragon Boat Festival holiday, Taiwan compatriots on the mainland showed especially strong willingness to receive COVID-19 vaccinations, and we have also heard feedback from some Taiwan compatriots that this is the best “health gift” the mainland has given to broad Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the situation of COVID-19 vaccinations among Taiwan…","First question. Since mid-April this year, in accordance with the principle of equal treatment, various localities have successively launched vaccination work for Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland. According to incomplete statistics, as of May 31, a total of 62,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated under relevant policies, on a voluntary basis and with informed consent. Their active registration for vaccination fully demonstrates the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots' trust in the safety and efficacy of mainland vaccines.\nSecond question: since the outbreak of the epidemic in Taiwan, we have seen the epidemic spreading on the island, vaccines in short supply, and residents dying from infection every day. We immediately expressed our willingness to swiftly make arrangements to provide mainland vaccines to Taiwan compatriots and to support civil organizations in donating vaccines to Taiwan compatriots. However, the DPP authorities have used various pretexts to obstruct and refuse, and have even openly smeared and slandered mainland vaccines. As for the desire of many people on the island to come to the mainland to get vaccinated, we fully understand and are willing to do our utmost to provide help. For Taiwan compatriots who come to the mainland on civil aviation passenger flights, as long as they meet the vaccination conditions, they may be vaccinated on the mainland under relevant policies, on a voluntary basis and with informed consent, while strictly observing entry epidemic prevention rules (including before and after boarding).","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The head of Taiwan’s epidemic prevention authority said that companies on the island need an “original manufacturer’s authorization letter” to purchase the German BNT vaccine. Can Taiwan-side entities, including civilian bodies and companies, obtain an “original manufacturer’s authorization letter” when purchasing the BNT vaccine from Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group?","After the outbreak on the island, Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group said it was willing to supply the BNT vaccine it participates in developing and distributes to Taiwan residents. It is understood that if groups or enterprises on the island purchase the BNT vaccine distributed by Fosun, and consensus is reached through consultation, Fosun Pharmaceutical Group will, on the basis of commercial agreements, fulfill its responsibilities and obligations.\nAt present, the epidemic on the island continues to spread and deaths keep increasing. Only by getting safe, highly effective and sufficient quantities of vaccines as early as possible can an immunity barrier be built for residents of the island as soon as possible. The latest poll on the island shows that 63% of Taiwan residents support procuring the BNT vaccine through Mainland agents. Is the life of Taiwan compatriots more important, or political calculation? This lies in one decision of the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","According to reports, a responsible person of Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group stated at a shareholders' meeting that the company is willing and will actively provide vaccines to Taiwan, and that whether Taiwan's civil or official sectors procure the German BNT vaccine, it must go through Shanghai Fosun. Chen Shizhong, head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention authority, said, “Fosun does indeed have agency rights,…","A responsible person of Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group has already publicly stated that the company is willing to make vaccines available to Taiwan compatriots, and has introduced the company's relevant commercial rights. Taiwan media have also widely reported this. It is understood that recently some counties, cities, and enterprises on the island have been negotiating with Fosun over vaccine purchases. We are glad to see Taiwan compatriots able to use Fosun-distributed vaccines as early as possible. The DPP authorities should create favorable conditions for this. The responsible persons of relevant Taiwan agencies continue to make groundless accusations and abusive remarks against Fosun, which in fact constitutes an obstruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","More and more Taiwan compatriots hope that when they come to the mainland for vaccination, there can be more flexible supporting measures, such as setting up vaccination zones at Shanghai and Xiamen airports, where they do not need to undergo quarantine after entering and can return immediately after vaccination. Another example is chartering flights or organizing groups to bring Taiwan compatriots to the…","Epidemic outbreaks on the island continue to spread, deaths keep rising, and the mortality rate keeps climbing, yet the DPP authorities still stubbornly refuse mainland vaccines. Under these circumstances, some Taiwan compatriots have made these suggestions, and we can understand their feelings.\nConsidering the needs of Taiwan compatriots, on June 11 we issued a written press release stating that we are willing to make appropriate arrangements for Taiwan compatriots who take civil aviation passenger flights to the mainland to get vaccinated. As long as they meet the vaccination requirements, they may receive vaccines on the mainland under the relevant policies, provided that the entry epidemic prevention regulations are strictly enforced (including before boarding and after arrival), and that the vaccination is voluntary and based on informed consent.\nAt present, nucleic acid testing and quarantine are the basic prevention and control strategies commonly used by all countries and regions, aimed at screening out infected cases and cutting off the transmission of the virus. According to regulations, all inbound travelers from abroad must undergo nucleic acid testing and be quarantined after arriving on the mainland. This is a responsible approach toward crew members and passengers, and also a responsible approach toward the life and health and safety of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nIf we follow the suggestions you mentioned, it will be hard to avoid infected cases, which would lead to the quarantine of everyone on the same aircraft. If even one infected case and close contact is missed, it would create a breach in epidemic prevention on both sides, which does not serve the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Therefore, we should still handle this in accordance with the relevant mainland policies. Although this may add some time and cost, we will get the good done well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","The Japanese House of Councillors recently passed a resolution on Taiwan-related matters supporting Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Regarding the issue of Taiwan in the World Health Organization, we have stated our position many times: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities deny the “1992 Consensus” and refuse to accept the one-China principle, thereby excluding themselves from the World Health Assembly. They have brought this on themselves.\nTaiwan is part of China. Japanese militarism once illegally occupied Taiwan for fifty years and launched wars of aggression against China, bringing profound disasters to the Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. What Japan should most do is correctly face and reflect on its inglorious history of aggression, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four Sino-Japanese political documents, and stop pointing fingers and making comments on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359723.htm"],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Office of the United States Trade Representative recently issued a press release stating that the United States and Taiwan will resume negotiations under the \"Trade and Investment Framework Agreement (TIFA) between the United States and Taiwan.\" Some media report that Taiwan will propose signing a \"bilateral trade agreement (BTA)\" with the United States. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We firmly oppose the United States negotiating and concluding with Taiwan any agreement with sovereignty implications. The DPP authorities “rely on the U.S. to seek independence,” do not hesitate to import “ractopamine pork,” and repeatedly sell out the interests of the island’s residents. It can be foreseen that the DPP authorities, for the private interests of their party, will only continue to harm the interests and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359724.htm"],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","Japanese Prime Minister Suga Yoshihide recently mistakenly referred to Taiwan as a “country” during a party leaders' debate in the Diet. Japanese Chief Cabinet Secretary Katsunobu Kato subsequently clarified that Japan's positioning of Taiwan is still that of a region, that there has been no change in Japan's basic position on the Taiwan question, and that its relationship with Taiwan remains a non-governmental…","Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose some Japanese officials' erroneous statements regarding the Taiwan region of China. We urge the Japanese side to abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, to be cautious in word and deed on the Taiwan issue, and not to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The G7 summit recently issued a joint communiqué containing Taiwan-related content. What is the spokesperson's comment on it?","Here I want to ask the G7: The DPP authorities keep provoking ‘independence’ and undermining the status quo in which both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Is this maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait? The Chinese government and people adhere to the one-China principle, curb ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist conduct, and safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Is this not maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait?\nTaiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. The United States has repeatedly taken erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question that violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and it also seeks to win over some countries to play the ‘Taiwan card’ together. We urge the relevant countries to honor in practice their solemn commitments to China, handle the Taiwan question properly, not send wrong signals to the ‘Taiwan independence’ forces, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359725.htm"],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Many Taiwan entertainers are now getting vaccinated on the mainland and posting online praise for mainland vaccines and vaccination arrangements. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Since the outbreak of the epidemic in Taiwan, the mainland has expressed its willingness to help Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic as quickly as possible through various means, and to enable Taiwan compatriots to receive mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO as soon as possible. The feelings and sentiments expressed by Taiwan personnel after being vaccinated on the mainland reflect the cross-Strait kinship of blood being thicker than water.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻云记者","After the joint communiqué of the G7 summit mentioned peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, on the 15th more than 20 sorties of PLA military aircraft entered Taiwan's “southwest airspace.” May I ask the spokesperson whether this move reveals any message?","As everyone knows, the root cause of the tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Out of political self-interest, they constantly incite “anti-China and China-hatred” sentiment on the island, stir up cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and obstruct and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges. Even as the epidemic on the island continues to worsen, they still disregard the life, health and safety of the island's people, placing their private interest in pursuing “independence” above the well-being of the people. The current state of cross-Strait relations is entirely the responsibility of the DPP authorities. We have consistently upheld promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and have consistently adhered to the development philosophy centered on the people. We have done practical things, good things and things that resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, and in the fight against the epidemic we are willing to do our utmost to provide assistance to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. But we will never allow the DPP authorities to treat our goodwill as an opportunity to pursue “independence,” and we will never allow anyone, in any way, to separate Taiwan from China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","The DPP authorities expressed thanks for vaccine donations from the United States and Japan, calling them “a timely rain.” Recently, reports emerged in Taiwan of the first suspected death following an AstraZeneca vaccine injection. There are also reports that Tainan decided to let Japanese nationals residing in Taiwan be vaccinated first. The mainland's Sinopharm and Sinovac vaccines have obtained WHO…","We have also noted reports in Taiwan media about this batch of AstraZeneca vaccines from Japan: these are vaccines that Japanese people did not take and that are close to expiration. Moreover, Taiwan media have also reported that some Taiwan residents suffered serious adverse reactions after being vaccinated.\nThe Dragon Boat Festival that has just passed is a festival in which Chinese people on both sides of the Strait pray for peace and health. But in Taiwan, some people have lamented, “Dragon Boat, life and death both in vain.” The DPP authorities have put their own political self-interest above people’s lives, refused mainland vaccines right in front of them, and kept drawing pies to satisfy hunger for Taiwan residents. They have turned their own crimes into punishment for Taiwan residents, causing resentment across the island, and it is no wonder that there is “Zongzi longing, family apart.” Faced with lives that keep slipping away, as I have said before: the sooner mainland vaccines are opened to Taiwan, the sooner the health and safety of island residents will be protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","Taiwan media reported that many Taiwan residents are willing to go to the mainland to get vaccinated, and there have even been “groups going to the mainland for vaccination.” Some Taiwan media also reported that the mainland has opened a dedicated “green channel” for Taiwan compatriots to get vaccinated. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","For Taiwan compatriots who travel to the mainland by civil aviation passenger flights to receive vaccination, as long as they meet the vaccination conditions, we are willing to make appropriate arrangements in accordance with relevant mainland policies and epidemic prevention regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","May I ask whether the activities marking the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China will invite Taiwan parties, groups or individuals to participate?","We have already introduced the relevant situation. The Central Committee of the Communist Party of China held its first press conference on the matter and has already introduced the arrangements for the centenary celebrations of the Party’s founding. Currently, all activities are being actively prepared and carried out in an orderly manner. If there is further news, we will provide it promptly, and we hope everyone will pay attention to the relevant information released by the organizers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Two questions. First, recently several Taiwan youths who live on the mainland recorded videos calling on the DPP authorities to prevent the epidemic scientifically and not to treat the mainland's epidemic-prevention experience and vaccines through an ideological lens. How does the spokesperson view these voices? Second, regarding the Taiwan-related content in the G7 summit joint communiqué, the DPP authorities…","On the first question: facts have proven that the mainland's series of epidemic prevention measures and practices have been effective, scientific, professional and rigorous, and have also been recognized by the international community. Mainland vaccines are safe and effective. As of June 14, we had administered more than 900 million doses. The DPP authorities cannot turn a blind eye to these or refuse to use them merely because they want to operate on a “oppose anything from China” line. This is by no means beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, nor is it a blessing for them.\nOn the second question: the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, a matter for Chinese on both sides of the Strait themselves. Cross-Strait relations have seen a situation of peaceful development on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” At present, as long as the DPP authorities change course in their cross-Strait policy, it is entirely possible for both sides to continue promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” As for the DPP authorities insisting on drawing the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait into others' so-called “Indo-Pacific Strategy,” this “appealing to foreign powers” approach precisely exposes their political nature of relying on external forces to confront the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Taiwan is in the midst of an epidemic, and the Mainland Affairs Council said that if the mainland truly cares about the health and safety of Taiwan residents, it would not stop “military aircraft harassment” and “international suppression” during this period. Regarding the PLA military aircraft, has the mainland considered making adjustments?","I want to emphasize that during the epidemic, the DPP authorities have not for a single day stopped colluding with external forces to provoke the mainland, challenge cross-Strait relations, and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Containing “Taiwan independence” is entirely necessary. This is consistent with our sincere willingness to help Taiwan compatriots overcome the epidemic, and both aim to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Taiwan has begun administering imported vaccines. In the future, will the mainland side recognize the efficacy of these vaccines? In addition, Taiwan's Medigen vaccine was recently unblinded, and vaccination may be opened after late July. Will the mainland also recognize it in the future?","Regarding whether vaccination changes the relevant epidemic prevention measures, this is a professional question. WHO experts have reminded that there is currently no evidence showing that vaccinated people no longer carry the risk of transmitting the virus, and vaccinated people also need to take the same protective measures. Professional questions should be assessed by professionals in the future.\nAs for the Taiwan-produced vaccine you mentioned, according to reports from Taiwanese media, currently 65% of Taiwan residents say they are unwilling to receive the Taiwan-produced vaccine. More media and professionals have pointed out that the Taiwan-produced vaccine is being prepared for administration without having completed Phase III clinical trials, and its safety and efficacy have been questioned, as has whether it will be recognized by the WHO and the international community. Under these circumstances, the question you just asked seems to have no practical significance for discussion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","日本NHK记者","I have two questions. First, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities said yesterday that 28 sorties of PLA military aircraft entered Taiwan's “southwest airspace” on that day, the largest scale ever. What is the mainland's intention? Second, the joint communiqué of the G7 summit mentioned peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?","I have already answered both of these questions just now. I wish to reiterate that responsibility for the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait lies entirely with the DPP authorities. Our policy has not changed; we still insist on advancing peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. But we will also absolutely not tolerate acts of seeking “independence,” and absolutely not tolerate external forces arbitrarily interfering in the Taiwan question. We need to make a strong response to these collusive acts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Tso Cheng-tung, Director of the KMT Department of Mainland Affairs, expressed concern over the Hubei gas explosion accident, and also expressed thanks to Taiwan businesses and enterprises both at home and abroad, especially on the mainland, who generously donated to support Taiwan's epidemic prevention efforts. May I ask the spokesperson for your response?","I believe that people on the island who oppose “Taiwan independence,” support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and hold no prejudice can fully appreciate the goodwill the mainland has expressed—out of the conviction that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family—in its willingness to support Taiwan compatriots in fighting the epidemic.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Amid the epidemic, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities continue to manipulate cross-strait “decoupling,” but this cannot stop Taiwan businesses from accelerating their westward expansion. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, in the first quarter of this year, the mainland newly established 1,195 Taiwan-funded enterprises, a year-on-year increase of 33.4%. What is the spokesperson's…","This fully demonstrates that the mainland, as the first major economy in the world to recover from the COVID-19 pandemic, is a case of “this side of the landscape being uniquely beautiful.” This is also the basis on which we attract Taiwan and foreign investment to keep investing and doing business on the mainland. At the same time, it fully demonstrates that after more than 40 years of economic exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, cross-Strait industrial and supply chains have become deeply interlocked and deeply compatible. Anyone who violates economic laws and, for political purposes, tries to weaken or sever them is simply deluded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202106/t20210616_12359721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: It is reported that Taiwan compatriots on the mainland are actively registering for COVID-19 vaccination. Please introduce the situation.","At the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office on June 16, spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions: Since mid-April this year, in accordance with the principle of equal treatment, various localities have successively begun vaccination work for Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland. According to incomplete statistics, as of May 31, 62,000 (6.2万) Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated under relevant policies, on a voluntary basis and with informed consent. The active registration for vaccination fully demonstrates that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots trust the safety and effectiveness of mainland vaccines.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210616_12359726.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 17 — Regarding the death of Zhou Qingjun, a well-known pro-unification figure in Taiwan and chairman of the Chinese Patriotic Concord Party, who died in Taipei on June 16 after contracting COVID-19, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a media inquiry on June 17, saying: We express our deep condolences on the passing of Mr. Zhou Qingjun. Mr. Zhou was a well-known pro-unification figure in Taiwan who always kept the great righteousness of the nation in his heart and unwaveringly devoted himself to the reunification of the motherland, firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism. We deeply admire his patriotic sentiment.\nAccording to Taiwanese media reports, Zhou Qingjun died at noon on June 16 at Chung Hsing Hospital in Taipei City after contracting COVID-19. He was 78 years old.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210617_12359952.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 17 dispatch: The Macao SAR Government issued a communiqué on June 16 announcing that the Macao Economic and Cultural Office in Taiwan will temporarily cease operations starting June 19. In response to the DPP authorities' rash comments, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 17th in response to a question: We support the Macao SAR Government in handling Taiwan-related affairs in accordance with the Basic Law and the central government's basic principles and policies on handling Macao's Taiwan-related affairs. The SAR Government has already explained the reasons for the temporary suspension of the Macao office in Taiwan. The DPP authorities know this full well, and any distortion or rationalization is pale and powerless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210617_12359976.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The US Ambassador to the United Nations falsely claimed that the mainland is using vaccines to pressure Taiwan's so-called “diplomatic allies,” and the DPP authorities expressed thanks. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 18th in response to a question that the DPP authorities take pride in serving as a “pawn” for US anti-China forces and feel no shame in sacrificing national interests in pursuit of “independence,” pushing Taiwan’s people toward disaster. Ignoring the ongoing epidemic on the island and the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots, they are single-mindedly colluding with external forces to pursue “Taiwan independence,” and their political scheme will inevitably fail.\nHe stressed that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. For some time, certain people in the US government have repeatedly made erroneous remarks on Taiwan-related issues that violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. This both goes against the serious commitments the US government has made to China and contravenes the facts and the basic norms of international relations. We urge the US government to abandon its scheme of “using Taiwan to contain China,” and to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions, not to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and not to add negative impacts to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210618_12360178.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18: According to Taiwan media reports, the DPP authorities said they agreed to authorize TSMC and the Yonglin Foundation to purchase BNT vaccines, and put forward four “practices.” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 18th: At the very beginning of the outbreak on the island, we made clear that we would do our utmost to help compatriots in Taiwan cope with the epidemic as quickly as possible. We repeatedly stated that we were willing to provide safe and effective vaccines to compatriots in Taiwan so that they could have vaccines available as soon as possible. For more than a month, the epidemic on the island has not been effectively controlled, the number of deaths from infection has continued to rise, and the vaccine shortage has never eased. Some political parties, counties and cities, groups and individuals have actively sought to purchase vaccines, and have repeatedly called on the DPP authorities to open up the import of mainland vaccines or to purchase the mRNA COVID-19 vaccine from BioNTech (BNT), a German company whose distribution in China is handled by Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group. But the DPP authorities have disregarded the urgent need of the Taiwan people for vaccinations. They have not only refused to import mainland vaccines, but have also placed numerous obstacles in the way of some counties, cities, and private institutions and enterprises in Taiwan that seek to purchase vaccines. Their cold-blooded obstruction has delayed access to vaccines, causing many Taiwan residents to die of infection.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that it is well known that Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group participated in the development of the BNT vaccine and holds the exclusive commercial rights to it in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. The company has long made clear that it is willing to serve compatriots in Taiwan with this vaccine, and has been actively working to supply this vaccine to the Taiwan region. We hope that counties, cities and private parties on the island will reach a vaccine purchase agreement with Fosun in accordance with normal commercial rules at an early date, so that Taiwan residents can receive the vaccines they urgently need as soon as possible. The press release issued by the DPP authorities deliberately avoids these facts and even falsely claims a so-called “international procurement contract,” and so on. What do they intend? At a time when Taiwan residents are eagerly awaiting vaccines, the DPP authorities are still making political capital, confusing the public, and trying to distort the commercial purchases of mainland companies by Taiwan counties, cities, enterprises and institutions. What is their purpose? Will the DPP authorities continue to engage in political manipulation and place obstacles in the way on the vaccine issue? We advise them to stop using the life and health of the Taiwan people as a bargaining chip for political manipulation, to abandon political obsessions, and to stop all immoral conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210618_12360186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, June 20 (Xinhua) — In response to the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council's reckless attack on the Hong Kong SAR government for suspending the Hong Kong offices in Taiwan, Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 20th, in response to a question, that the relevant remarks of the DPP authorities show that their nature of meddling in Hong Kong and pursuing “independence” has not changed, that they have shown no reflection on their sinful conduct of interfering in Hong Kong affairs and supporting and sheltering violent black forces, and that instead they are shouting “stop the thief” and recklessly accusing the Hong Kong SAR government of its legitimate actions.\nHe said that regarding the Hong Kong SAR government's suspension of the operation of offices in Taiwan, the SAR government has already stated its solemn position. Exchanges between the Hong Kong SAR of China and the Taiwan region of China must of course be conducted on the political basis of the one-China principle, and Taiwan's offices in Hong Kong must of course abide by the Basic Law of the Hong Kong SAR and relevant laws, and must not engage in any words or deeds that violate the one-China principle.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we firmly support the Hong Kong SAR government in handling Taiwan-related affairs in accordance with the Basic Law and the central government's basic principles and policies on handling Taiwan-related matters in Hong Kong, and firmly support its legitimate actions to curb “Taiwan independence” and counter the DPP authorities' meddling in Hong Kong affairs.\nHe pointed out that, especially against the backdrop of the current epidemic prevention efforts, the DPP authorities, for their own private political interests and disregarding the life and health of people on the island, continue to suppress dissidents, stifle speech, and engage in political manipulation. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately withdraw the black hand that undermines Hong Kong's prosperity and stability and interferes in Hong Kong affairs, or they will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210620_12360451.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-21","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US shipped 2.5 million doses of coronavirus vaccine to Taiwan yesterday. Do you see this as a provocative move? Do you have any comments on this?","The mainland and Taiwan are one family. Our hearts are with our Taiwan compatriots who are faced with the grave situation. We have always made clear the readiness to do our utmost to help our compatriots in Taiwan overcome the difficulties at an early date. However, despite the goodwill of the mainland and the eagerness of the majority of Taiwan compatriots to use vaccines from the mainland, the DPP authorities tried every means to obstruct the shipping of vaccines from the mainland to Taiwan, and even falsely claimed that the mainland was obstructing its vaccine procurement. For their own selfish political gains, the DPP authorities constantly seek political manipulation over anti-epidemic cooperation, showing disregard of the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots and violating the basic humanitarian spirit.\nChina always supports anti-epidemic cooperation and has made proactive efforts to this end. We urge the US side not to use vaccine aid for political maneuver or interference in China's internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210621_9170769.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1885422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-21","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","A question on the recalling by Taiwan of seven official representatives from Hong Kong. They cited unreasonable political preconditions for the personnel to operate in Hong Kong. Does the foreign ministry have any comment about the recalling of seven Taiwan representatives from Hong Kong?","This is not a diplomatic question. Please refer it to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210621_9170769.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1885422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","(June 21, 2021)\nThe United States recently provided a batch of COVID-19 vaccines to Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The current outbreak in Taiwan has raged for more than a month, seriously endangering the life, health and safety of the broad mass of compatriots in Taiwan. As of June 21, Taiwan had a cumulative total of 14,080 confirmed COVID-19 cases and 569 deaths, with a fatality rate exceeding 4%, while the island's vaccination rate is currently only about 6%. We are deeply concerned about the current epidemic in Taiwan and the life, health and safety of the broad mass of compatriots in Taiwan. We have repeatedly stated our willingness to do our utmost to assist compatriots in Taiwan in overcoming the epidemic and to enable them to have vaccines available as soon as possible. We are willing to provide mainland vaccines that the World Health Organization has included in its global \"Emergency Use Listing,\" or the German BNT vaccine that Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group has participated in developing and distributing. Civil organizations in Shanghai, Jiangsu and Fujian have also announced that they will donate a batch of vaccines to the island.\nWe hope to see, and are willing to actively assist, compatriots in Taiwan in overcoming the epidemic as soon as possible. Regrettably, the DPP authorities have engaged in a \"politicized epidemic prevention,\" ignoring the life and health of the island's people and disregarding the mainland's goodwill. They have imbued vaccines with political color and persistently engaged in political manipulation, continuing to create political spectacles of confrontation across the Strait. Compatriots in Taiwan still cannot obtain safe, effective and sufficient vaccines from the mainland, and precious time for effective epidemic prevention on the island continues to be lost. Using vaccines for political purposes is an extremely irresponsible and gratuitous harm to the life and health of the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210621_12360800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-06-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 21 — On the 21st, the Mainland Affairs Council once again attacked the Hong Kong SAR government’s suspension of Hong Kong offices in Taiwan, and used the banner of “democracy and freedom” to defend the Hong Kong disorder and “independence” agenda. In response, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, on the same day, pointed out in answer to questions: The DPP authorities suppress dissenters on the island, muzzle speech, deceive the public, and manipulate public opinion. For political purposes, they resort to despicable means of various political manipulations. What qualifications and face do they have to talk about democracy and freedom, and what courage do they have to label themselves “defenders of democracy”?\nMa Xiaoguang said that we have already stated our solemn position on the DPP authorities’ reckless attacks on the Hong Kong SAR government’s suspension of the operation of offices in Taiwan. We must point out once again that Taiwan’s offices in Hong Kong must, as a matter of course, conduct their activities on the political basis of the One-China principle, and must, as a matter of course, abide by the Basic Law of the Hong Kong SAR and relevant laws. The words and deeds of Taiwan’s offices in Hong Kong in events such as the “extradition bill controversy” and their promotion of disorder in Hong Kong cannot be concealed. The DPP authorities’ renewed attacks and smears against “one country, two systems” only expose the political intentions behind the conduct of their Hong Kong offices!\nHe also warned the DPP authorities to abandon the illusion of colluding with external forces to pursue “independence,” and to immediately stop their various fake “support for Hong Kong” that in reality create disorder in Hong Kong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210621_12360802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-23","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","On June 22, guided-missile destroyer USS Curtis Wilbur sailed through the Taiwan Strait. This is the sixth transit through the Taiwan Strait since the start of the Biden administration. Do you have any comment?","The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command already made remarks on the issue. The Chinese side was closely following and fully aware of the US military vessel's passage through the Taiwan Strait from start to end. The US warships have repeatedly flaunted their prowess in the Taiwan Strait, provoking and stirring up trouble. This is by no means commitment to freedom and openness, but rather \"freedom of trespassing\", and deliberate disruption and sabotage of regional peace and stability. The international community sees this crystal clear.\nChina is firmly resolved in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US to play a constructive role in regional peace and stability, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210623_9170771.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1886125.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-06-23","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Lithuania said they will donate 20,000 vaccine shots to Taiwan, and open a representative office in Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this?","Recently, my colleagues and I have responded to this question on many occasions. Here I would like to reiterate that our hearts are with our Taiwan compatriots who are faced with the grave situation. We have always made clear the readiness to do our utmost to help our compatriots in Taiwan overcome the difficulties at an early date. I would like to advise the Taiwan authorities to focus on scientific epidemic prevention and control, remove man-made political obstacles, and ensure that the lives, health, interests and well-being of our Taiwan compatriots are effectively protected, rather than seek political manipulation on anti-epidemic cooperation for selfish interests. This disregard for the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots goes against the basic humanitarian spirit.\nChina firmly opposes any official exchanges and the mutual establishment of so-called \"representative offices\" between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic relations with China. We urge the Lithuanian side to adhere to the one-China principle and honor its commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties. Also a word of advice to the Taiwan authorities: \"Taiwan independence\" leads to a dead end and any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210623_9170771.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1886125.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-06-24","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Some media reported that the US and Taiwan have taken small actions to strengthen their collusion, and there are some military exchanges between them. Meanwhile, the PLA recently dispatched more than 20 sorties of military aircraft to Taiwan's \"southwestern airspace\", setting a record for the number of aircraft in a single day since Taiwan's \"defense department\" released relevant data. What's your comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. China is firmly opposed to any form of official exchanges or military contacts between the US and Taiwan , firmly opposed to attempts by the US to use Taiwan to contain China, and firmly opposed to efforts of Taiwan to solicit US support and seek \"Taiwan independence\" with force.\nThe complete reunification of China is a historical trend. The great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable. Peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is a common aspiration of all. \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead-end. To China, \"Taiwan independence\" means war. The US should fully realize that China's development cannot be stopped by anyone or any force. It should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop any form of military contacts with Taiwan. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities in Taiwan should realize that the future of Taiwan lies in national reunification and the wellbeing of the Taiwan compatriots hinges on the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Any attempt to \"seek independence by relying on the United States\" is doomed to failure.\nIn recent days, the PLA dispatched multiple types of aircraft to conduct exercises around the Taiwan Strait, which is a necessary action in response to the current security situation across the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty. The PLA will resolutely perform the sacred mission of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and ensuring national security.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-06/28/content_4888346.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-06-24","Ren Guoqiang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","In mid-June, the China-ASEAN Defense Ministers' Informal Meeting and the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting Plus (ADMM-Plus) were held successively. State Councilor and Defense Minister General Wei Fenghe attended the meetings. Could you please give us more information?","On June 15 and 16, the 12th China-ASEAN Defense Ministers' Informal Meeting (10+1) and the 8th ADMM-Plus(10+8) were held successively via video link. State Councilor and Defense Minister General Wei Fenghe attended and addressed the events.\nAt the \"10+1\" meeting, General Wei reviewed the fruitful cooperation achieved in the past 30 years since the establishment of the China-ASEAN strategic partnership. He said China will continue to connect the \"Belt and Road\" initiative with the development strategy of ASEAN and jointly promote the building of a China-ASEAN community with a shared future.\nGeneral Wei also stated that defense and security cooperation has played an important role in supporting the China-ASEAN strategic partnership. China is willing to strengthen cooperation with ASEAN countries in defense and military areas and continue to provide vaccines and other medical supplies. He said all parties should work together to build consensus, manage differences, promote cooperation and safeguard peace and tranquility in the South China Sea.\nAt the \"10+8\" meeting, General Wei expounded China's views on the current international strategic landscape and regional security situation and called on all countries to join hands in building a community with a shared future for mankind. He stated that the growth of China's military strength will contribute to the force for peace in the world. China values security cooperation with other countries and fully understands and respects the legitimate concerns of others. Meanwhile, China’s national interests must also be fully respected and maintained. China has an unwavering determination to safeguard its core national interests with regard to the Taiwan question and issues related to Xinjiang, Hong Kong and the South China Sea.\nBesides, General Wei pointed out that there are both development challenges and opportunities for the Asia-Pacific region. All parties should adhere to the global security concept of common, comprehensive, cooperative, and sustainable security, jointly build and utilize the ADMM-Plus mechanism and create a security pattern built and shared by all.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-06/28/content_4888346.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2021-06-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 24 — The Hong Kong SAR government recently took legal action against personnel and entities related to Apple Daily, a publication under Next Digital. The DPP authorities have maliciously attacked this. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 24th in response to a question: The Hong Kong SAR government has taken legal action in accordance with the law against conduct suspected of violating the Hong Kong National Security Law. This is a due measure to safeguard Hong Kong's prosperity and stability, and no one has the right to interfere. We firmly support it.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities and some “Taiwan independence” leading figures have colluded with Jimmy Lai and the Apple Daily he founded to disrupt Hong Kong and plot “independence,” as the whole world knows. Now they have once again trotted out the usual so-called “democracy and freedom” tricks, posing as “defenders of freedom,” deceiving public opinion, turning black into white, disregarding the judiciary, defending illegal acts aimed at disrupting Hong Kong and plotting “independence,” and providing cover for the sinister acts of seeking political gain by interfering in Hong Kong affairs.\nHe also stated: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately withdraw their black hands from interfering in Hong Kong affairs. Those who break the law will be prosecuted, and all evil deeds will be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210624_12361609.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-25","Zhao Lijian","Macao Monthly","It is reported that on June 24, Raymond Greene, deputy head of the American Institute in Taiwan, said in a speech in Taipei that there is a fundamental change in the US-Taiwan relationship, that the US is the most important international backer of Taiwan. What is China's comment?","We firmly reject the erroneous remarks by the US side. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a fact based on history and jurisprudence that no one or any force can change. China has all along opposed any US attempt to elevate relations in essence or engage in official interactions with Taiwan in any form.\nThe Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue between China and the US. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, immediately stop using the Taiwan question as a pretext for political manipulation, discontinue official interactions and forsake its attempt to elevate substantive relations with Taiwan, lest it should further damage China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202106/t20210625_9170773.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1886930.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-06-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 25 — Wu Zhaoxie, head of Taiwan's external exchanges department, recently accepted an interview with foreign media and made provocative remarks promoting “Taiwan independence.” He falsely claimed that the mainland's “military intimidation” toward Taiwan continues to escalate, and that Taiwan “needs to prepare for possible military conflict.” TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 25th: We warn Wu Zhaoxie and his ilk that if you stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and dare to take risks, gambling with the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides and with the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait, and fantasize about “seeking independence through force,” you will certainly suffer a devastating defeat.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the root cause of the currently complex and grim situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have intensified their collusion with external forces and continuously engaged in provocations to seek “independence.” The various measures we have taken are powerful responses to the above provocations. They are legitimate actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and protect the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nMa Xiaoguang said that Wu Zhaoxie confuses right and wrong and puts the cart before the horse. He defends the DPP authorities' vile provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” and tries to deceive the people of the island and mislead the international community by fabricating lies and shifting blame onto the mainland. This is entirely shameless “Goebbels-style” rhetoric. Out of his stubborn “Taiwan independence” nature, Wu Zhaoxie and his ilk disregard the interests of the Chinese nation and the well-being of the Taiwan people. They are willing to serve as “pawns” for foreign powers, place their bets on external forces, rely on foreign backing to bolster their own standing, advocate war, and attempt to drag the lives of the broad Taiwan compatriots into the abyss created by “Taiwan independence.” Not only will they fail, they will ultimately be unable to escape the judgment of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202106/t20210625_12361743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-06-29","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Japan's deputy defense minister on Monday spoke of the growing threat posed by Chinese and Russian collaboration and said it was necessary to \"wake up\" to Beijing's pressure on Taiwan and protect the island \"as a democratic country.\" What's the ministry's comment on this?","China deplores the erroneous remarks by the senior Japanese government official, and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nSome Japanese politicians, in disregard of the fact of China's peaceful development, unjustifiably point fingers at China's socioeconomic development and normal national defense building, portray China as a threat, and openly stoke big-power confrontation with the sinister motive to find excuses to break free from the military restrictions imposed on Japan over crimes of aggression committed by Japanese militarism in history. This is extremely irresponsible and dangerous.\nThe politician in question flagrantly refers to Taiwan as a \"country\" on multiple occasions, severely violating principles set out in the four political documents including the China-Japan Joint Statement and its solemn and repeated commitment of not seeing Taiwan as a country. We ask Japan to make crystal clarification, and ensure that such things won't happen again.\nThere is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's sacred territory. The Taiwan question bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations, the basic trust and good faith between the two countries and the international rule of law and justice. We seriously urge the Japanese side to earnestly honor its commitment, be prudent in words and actions, avoid undermining China's sovereignty in any form and refrain from sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces. I would like to stress that China's will and determination to safeguard national sovereignty, security and unity is unshakable. China must and will be reunified. This is an unstoppable historical trend.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1887945.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1887936.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-07-01","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg News","The Financial Times report said US and Japan have been conducting war games and joint military exercises to prepare for any potential conflict with China over Taiwan. The planning began in the final year of the Trump administration. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","We note relevant reports. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Chinese government and people's firm resolve and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not waver in the face of any external pressure. We hope relevant sides will stop hyping up the \"China threat\" theory and instead do more things in the interest of regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1888806.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1888785.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","(July 2, 2021)\nAround “July 1,” the DPP and its authorities made wild remarks and viciously attacked the mainland. What comment does the spokesperson have?","For one hundred years, the Communist Party of China has always taken striving for the well-being of the Chinese people and national rejuvenation of the Chinese nation as its original aspiration and mission. Uniting the people of all ethnic groups across the country, it has forged the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics, ushered in the great leap of the Chinese nation from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, comprehensively built a moderately prosperous society, and achieved great accomplishments that satisfy the people, attract worldwide attention, and are worthy of being recorded in history, writing the most magnificent epic in the Chinese nation's several thousand years of history. The DPP and its authorities have spoken recklessly, disregarding the great achievements the Communist Party of China has made in leading the Chinese people in united struggle, maliciously vilifying the social system and development path chosen by the Chinese people, and deliberately distorting the independent and peaceful foreign policy of the mainland. Once again, this exposes their despicable nature: willingly serving as pawns of Western anti-China forces, being enemies of the 1.4 billion Chinese people, and seeking “Taiwan independence” separatism.\nSince taking office, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermined the common political foundation across the Taiwan Strait, relied on external forces, incited cross-Strait confrontation, manipulated “anti-China and hatred of China,” and pursued “Taiwan independence” separatism. This has led to tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations and has seriously harmed the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, as well as the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The DPP authorities are incompetent in governance, skilled at fabrication, suppress dissent, muzzle speech, deceive the public, and manipulate public opinion. They have even obstructed the entry of mainland vaccines to the island and the procurement of vaccines by private entities. As a result, today's Taiwan is marked by spreading epidemics, floods and droughts compounding each other, energy shortages, pervasive air pollution, “Lai pork” imports into Taiwan, gangsters interfering in politics, trading of power for money, man-made disasters without end, and public grievances. Green terror runs rampant, the people dare not speak openly and can only exchange glances on the road, and this has aroused the anger of heaven and the resentment of the people. What face do they have to keep indulging in talk of “democracy and freedom” to deceive the world? This fig leaf should have been thrown into the Taiwan Strait long ago.\nResolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the country is the unwavering historical mission of the Communist Party of China and the shared aspiration of all Chinese descendants. Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country. The Chinese people will never allow Taiwan to be separated from China. We will firmly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” schemes. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that in today's increasingly strong mainland, pursuing confrontation and seeking separation is nothing but a fantasy and can only lead to a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210702_12363400.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","According to Taiwan media reports, on July 2, Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (TSMC) and the Yonglin Foundation signed documents with Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group regarding the procurement of BNT vaccines. What comment do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian stated the above when answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 5 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 5th in response to inquiries that counties, cities, civil organizations and enterprises on the island that have the willingness may purchase vaccines from Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group in accordance with normal commercial rules. We hope Taiwan compatriots will soon receive the vaccines they urgently need.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group signed with Germany's BNT company as early as March 2020, participating in the development of the BNT vaccine and holding exclusive commercial rights in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. As the sole purchaser of BNT vaccines in Taiwan, a responsible person at Shanghai Fosun has already publicly stated willingness to make the vaccines available to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210705_12363862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-06","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Japan's Deputy Prime Minister Taro Aso said that Japan and the US would have to defend Taiwan together in the event of a major problem. He said an invasion of Taiwan by China could be seen as an existential threat, allowing Japan the right to collective self-defense. This is according to a report from Kyodo News. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","Those remarks are extremely wrong and dangerous as they severely violate principles set out in the four political documents between China and Japan and undermine the political foundation of China-Japan relations. China deplores and rejects this and has lodged solemn representations with Japan.\nJapanese militarism once committed innumerous crimes in the aggression against China. However, some politicians are still coveting Taiwan till this day. This fully shows that they haven't learned the lesson from history.\nToday's China is no longer what it was back then. We will never allow anyone to meddle in the Taiwan question in any way. No one should underestimate the resolve, the will, and the ability of the Chinese people to defend their national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210706_9170779.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1890096.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: recently some Taiwan compatriots described their experience of receiving Sinovac vaccines at the Chinese Embassy in Thailand. Could you introduce what assistance overseas Taiwan compatriots have received from overseas embassies and consulates in responding to the epidemic? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua, Beijing, July 6 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 6th, saying: Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood kin, and the people on both sides of the Strait are one family, bound by ties thicker than water. Wherever Taiwan compatriots are and whatever difficulties they encounter, the motherland is their firm backing, and we are willing to provide assistance to the greatest extent possible. Especially now that the COVID-19 pandemic is raging around the world, we are willing to do everything possible to help them.\nZhu Fenglian said that in March this year we launched the “Spring Seedling Action” overseas to assist Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots, in getting COVID-19 vaccines locally. According to incomplete statistics, as of now we have helped more than 1.7 million overseas Chinese citizens get COVID-19 vaccines in more than 160 countries, including thousands of Taiwan compatriots. For example, Taiwan compatriots in need in Thailand, Myanmar, Vietnam, Bolivia, Brunei, Madagascar, Georgia and other countries have received domestic or foreign vaccines. The Chinese embassy in Thailand carefully organized two dedicated vaccination sessions for Taiwan compatriots in Thailand, helping more than a thousand of them receive domestic vaccines; the Chinese embassy in Georgia pushed the local government to make special arrangements to vaccinate Taiwan compatriots stranded there by the epidemic with domestic vaccines; and the Chinese embassy in Myanmar, overcoming local political turmoil, included more than a hundred Taiwan compatriots in the vaccination scope and helped them smoothly receive domestic vaccines. Overseas Taiwan compatriots in need may contact the Chinese embassies and consulates abroad as soon as possible to obtain assistance. Contact information has been published on the websites of the overseas embassies and consulates.\nShe said that in addition to assisting with vaccinations, we have also provided all-round anti-epidemic assistance to overseas Taiwan compatriots through various channels, including providing information and services such as safety reminders, scientific epidemic prevention and psychological counseling; precisely distributing anti-epidemic supplies such as “health packages” and “Spring Festival packages”; and actively responding to the needs of overseas Taiwan compatriots and arranging temporary return flights in a steady manner.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that we will continue to uphold the people-centered development philosophy and the concept of “Cross-Strait people are one family,” do real things, good things and resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, protect the lives, health and safety of overseas Taiwan compatriots, and do our utmost to provide anti-epidemic assistance to them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210706_12363986.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, Japanese Deputy Prime Minister and Finance Minister Taro Aso declared that “the United States and Japan should jointly defend Taiwan,” which is no different from the wrong remarks about Taiwan made recently by several Japanese government officials. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 6 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 6th in response to a question: We urge Japan to deeply reflect on history, immediately correct its mistakes, act in practice in accordance with the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, exercise caution on the Taiwan question, and stop all wrong words and deeds concerning Taiwan. The DPP authorities' delusion of colluding with Japan and some other external forces to provoke in pursuit of “independence” is a misjudgment of the situation and a miscalculation.\nShe pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Some Japanese politicians have successively made erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question, openly violating the political commitments Japan made to China on the Taiwan question, violating the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and violating international law and the norms governing international relations. We firmly oppose this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210706_12364135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-07","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","Recently Eswatini has seen a spate of protests and riots and the situation is still developing. How do you comment on that?","China is highly concerned about the situation in Eswatini and hope the country will realize economic development and improvement of people's livelihood. As COVID-19 continues to spread in Africa, Eswatini still faces a daunting task of fighting the virus and reinvigorating the economy. China stands ready to provide humanitarian assistance to Eswatini including vaccines to help its people tide over the difficulties.\nWe also noted that the US, UK and the EU got Taiwan authorities to join them in a statement on the situation in Eswatini. The Taiwan region is part of China's territory and the one-China principle is a universally recognized international norm of international relations. We urge relevant countries and organization to abide by their commitment and stop attempts to create \"two Chinas\" and \"one China, one Taiwan\" in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210707_9170780.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1890370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-07-07","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","White House Indo-Pacific coordinator Kurt Campbell said at a forum that it's possible for China and United States to coexist in peace; the US does not support Taiwan's independence, but will respond if China takes steps \"antithetical to the maintenance of peace and stability\". He also said that Beijing is becoming increasingly assertive. Do you have a response?","I think you raised two questions, one on China-US relations and another on China's foreign policy.\nOn China-US relations, I'd like to say that China's development and progress isn't the result of other's gift or charity, but comes from the hard work of the Chinese people. We hope the US side will adopt a rational and practical China policy, focus on cooperation, manage difference and bring bilateral relations back onto the track of sound and stable development.\nChina's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. There is but one China in the world, and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. We urge the U.S. side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, tread carefully on Taiwan-related issues, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to avoid damaging China-U.S. relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn China's foreign policy, General Secretary Xi Jinping just elaborated on it at the ceremony marking the centenary of the CPC. We hope relevant people in the US will find time to read the transcript carefully. Here I would like to stress a few points.\nFirst, as China grows, the strength for peace in the world also grows. The Chinese nation does not carry aggressive or hegemonic traits in its genes. China remains committed to the ideas of peace, concord, and harmony, an independent foreign policy of peace and a path of peaceful development. We offer Chinese solutions and contribute to political settlement of hotspot issues to safeguard regional and global peace and stability. We always safeguard world peace.\nSecond, China's development drives global growth. China's development cannot be achieved isolated from the world and global prosperity cannot be realized without China. We adopt a basic national policy of reform and opening-up, uphold an opening-up strategy of win-win cooperation, pursue an ecological-friendly, green and low-carbon development path and work for high quality BRI cooperation. With China's fresh development we offer new opportunities for the world. We always contribute to global development.\nThird, what China pursues is the common progress of humanity. China works for the cause of human progress, and stands ready to join hands with all progressive forces to carry forward the shared human values of peace, development, equity, justice, democracy, and freedom. We will continue to champion cooperation over confrontation, to open up rather than close our doors, and to focus on mutual benefits instead of zero-sum games. We will oppose hegemony and power politics, and safeguard the international order.\nFourth, China defends international fairness and justice. Chinese people uphold justice and are not intimidated by foreign power. We welcome helpful suggestions and constructive criticism. We will not, however, accept condescending preaching from those who feel they have the right to lecture us. We will remain committed to the path that we have chosen for ourselves. China will not infringe upon other countries' sovereignty or interfere in other countries' internal affairs. Neither will we allow other countries to do that to us. This is not only to protect China's legitimate rights and interests, but also to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of the vast developing world and the basic norms governing international relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210707_9170780.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1890370.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 7 dispatch: Recently, Kurt Campbell, Indo-Pacific Coordinator at the White House National Security Council, said that “the United States does not support ‘Taiwan independence.’” TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 7th, said: We have noted the relevant reports. It must be stressed that “Taiwan independence” is a counter-current of history and a dead end. The motherland must be and will inevitably be reunified. We urge the US government to act in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, clearly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and play a constructive role in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210707_12364364.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The MAC recently issued a so-called report on Hong Kong affairs, making false comments on Hong Kong affairs and attacking \"one country, two systems.\" What is the comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in responding to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 8 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 8th, said: We firmly support the Hong Kong SAR government in administering in accordance with the law. We resolutely cut off the black hand that the DPP authorities have extended into Hong Kong, firmly thwart the scheme of “Taiwan independence” forces to throw Hong Kong into chaos in pursuit of “independence,” and continue to push forward the process of national reunification.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that for some time, the DPP authorities have constantly manipulated Hong Kong affairs, supported “black violence” forces, clamored for “aid Hong Kong” operations, attacked “one country, two systems,” and tried to make Hong Kong ever more chaotic, in order to achieve their political aim of seeking “independence” and rejecting unification. Their vicious conduct is plain for the world to see, and their sinister intentions are obvious.\nShe stressed that the DPP authorities' conduct on Hong Kong issues has nothing to do with “democracy and freedom.” Instead, it throws Hong Kong into chaos, harms Hong Kong, damages Hong Kong's interests, and provokes the strong indignation of the broad masses of Hong Kong people!\nZhu Fenglian said that since the Hong Kong national security law took effect, the rule of law in the Hong Kong SAR has been protected, order has been maintained, society has been stable, and the economy has prospered. National sovereignty, security, and development interests have been safeguarded. This situation best serves Hong Kong's interests and enjoys wide support and welcome from the people of Hong Kong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210708_12364612.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-09","Wang Wenbin","AFP","I have two questions. The first one, the European Parliament passed a resolution yesterday calling for EU officials to boycott the Beijing Winter Olympics over human rights concerns in Hong Kong and Xinjiang. What's the foreign ministry's response to this? The second question, what's China response to the situation surrounding the assassination of Haiti's President, including the announcement by Taiwan that 11…","On your first question, what you mentioned is not worth any attention.\nOn your second question, we noted relevant reports. I want to stress that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China.\nWith regard to the situation in Haiti, we hope Haiti can restore social stability at an early date, achieve sound economic development and safeguard people's wellbeing.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210709_9170782.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1891046.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently issued a so-called “report” falsely accusing the mainland of exploiting the epidemic to carry out “united front” operations, putting Taiwan under the dual pressure of a “political epidemic” and a “virus epidemic.” What comments do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 9: TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 9th: “Heaven-made calamities can still be avoided; self-made calamities cannot be survived.” We advise the DPP authorities: lying cannot conceal your lack of virtue and incompetence, and shifting blame onto the mainland cannot deceive the people on the island. You had better honestly face up to the various despicable acts you have committed, which have harmed people's lives and health, and apologize to the broad Taiwan public.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the remarks of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council completely disregard facts and reverse black and white.\nShe introduced that since the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, we have treated Taiwan compatriots on the mainland equally in epidemic prevention and control, vaccination, and other aspects. After the epidemic outbreak in Taiwan in May, we immediately expressed our willingness to do our utmost to help the broad Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic, including providing Taiwan compatriots with mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO, and supporting the BNT vaccine that Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group participated in developing and is the exclusive agent for, to serve the people of Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian said that by contrast, since the epidemic broke out on the island, the DPP authorities, proceeding from the interests of their own party, have ignored the health and well-being of the people of Taiwan and stubbornly maintained their “anti-China” “political epidemic prevention” stance. They have slandered and smeared the goodwill of the mainland in every way and used various excuses to block the import of mainland vaccines, and they have set up numerous political obstacles to certain counties and cities, civil organizations, and enterprises on the island purchasing vaccines from Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group in accordance with commercial rules. They reject all epidemic prevention measures related to the mainland, including vaccines, and completely ignore the lives and health of the people. Facts prove that it is the DPP authorities who have plunged Taiwan into a “vaccine shortage,” it is the DPP authorities who have used the “virus epidemic” to manipulate a “political epidemic,” and it is the DPP authorities who are the true culprits behind the nearly 14,000 people infected and more than 700 people who have died to date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210709_12364844.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-12","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The tech companies Foxconn and TSMC are buying 5 million Pfizer-BioNTech vaccine doses each from China's Fosun Pharma. This comes after Taiwan had trouble in securing a direct deal with Fosun. What's the foreign ministry's view on this arrangement?","This is not a question concerning foreign affairs. I would like to refer you to the competent authorities and relevant companies. I want to stress that we truly care about the welfare of our Taiwan compatriots and hope they can have early access to the direly-needed vaccine.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210712_9170783.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1891432.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 12 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said in an interview on the 12th that, in order to create more platforms for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and to give compatriots on both sides more opportunities to look back on history, savor culture, share family bonds and develop together, the Central Taiwan Work Leading Group Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have approved the establishment of two new Cross-Strait Exchange Bases: one at the Xiandu Scenic Area in Jinyun, Lishui, Zhejiang, and one at the Leizu Mausoleum Park in Yanting, Mianyang, Sichuan. These two exchange bases rely respectively on Yellow Emperor culture and Leizu culture, and they centrally showcase the excellent traditional Chinese culture of honoring ancestors and passing down traditions from generation to generation. They are important places where Taiwan compatriots can commemorate the ancestors of the Chinese nation and remember the glory of Yan and Huang. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange at these two exchange bases, and we hope the relevant localities will build and develop the exchange bases well, strengthen attention and overall planning, and play a greater role in expanding and deepening cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nZhu Fenglian said that exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides in all fields are an important driving force for advancing cross-Strait relations. Since 2009, the Central Taiwan Work Leading Group Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have successively approved the establishment of 81 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases across 24 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian. The establishment of these two new exchange bases reflects our unwavering implementation of established policies, our resolve to actively expand cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, our efforts to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and our determination to continuously promote heart-to-heart connection among compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210712_12365224.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-13","Zhao Lijian","SCMP","Japan released Defense of Japan 2021 white paper on Tuesday, which referred to the importance of stability around Taiwan for the first time. What is China's response?","Recently, the Japanese side has been making issues out of China, grossly interfering in China's internal affairs, making groundless accusation of China's normal national defense and military activities, pointing fingers at China's legitimate maritime activities and playing up the so-called \"China threat\". This is extremely wrong and irresponsible. China deplores and rejects this.\nI must stress that, Taiwan is part of China and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. China never allows interference in the Taiwan question in any form by any country. China must and will be reunified. A complete reunification of China is most beneficial to regional peace and stability.\nDiaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. By conducting patrol and law enforcement activities in waters off Diaoyu Dao, China is exercising the inherent right of China as prescribed by law. The Coast Guard Law is just a routine piece of domestic legislation. It is not targeted at any specific country. And it is totally in line with international law and international practice. In fact, many countries, including Japan, have enacted similar laws and regulations long before China. Enough with Japan's \"lying diplomacy\" and double standard!\nThe \"Indo-Pacific Strategy\" aims to stoke bloc confrontation and create cliques for geopolitical game. It marks the comeback of Cold War mentality and retrogression and should be tossed into the dustbin of history. Will Japan first solve the problem of its flagrant discharge of nuclear contaminated water into the Pacific Ocean before touting the idea of \"free and open Pacific\"?\nWe once again urge Japan to approach the relevant issues with the right mentality, and show its respect for China's sovereignty and sincerity in upholding regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210713_9170784.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1891716.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, the U.S. “2049 Project Institute” published absurd remarks spreading “China's armed invasion of Taiwan.” Some Taiwan media have also used this to advocate that the United States provide Taiwan with a so-called “wartime ally reserve.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 13 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 13th, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities have for a long time spent large sums to bribe so-called “think tanks” in the United States, with the aim of inflaming tensions in the Taiwan Strait and attempting to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” and “resist reunification by force.” Their scheme will not succeed. The various fallacies hyped by some Taiwan media about “U.S. defense of Taiwan” will only bring disaster to the people of Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the “2049 Research Institute” has, since the day it was founded, made clear its mission of supporting Taiwan against China and advocating that the U.S. help Taiwan “resist reunification by force.” The publication of relevant remarks reflects its consistent nature of disregarding facts, distorting right and wrong, promoting the “China threat theory,” and helping Taiwan plot “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210713_12365587.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: According to reports, Japan recently released its Defense White Paper, which for the first time mentions that “the situation in Taiwan is very important to Japan's security and international stability.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above remarks.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 14 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 14th that for some time, Japan has successively taken erroneous words and actions on Taiwan-related issues, stubbornly heading in the wrong direction. This seriously violates the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, seriously contravenes the one-China principle, sends a grave erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and brings serious negative effects to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We express our strong dissatisfaction.\nZhu Fenglian said that the “Defense White Paper” that Japan has just released contains a series of errors on Taiwan, which is yet another irresponsible and erroneous display. We warn Japan that Japan has historical debts on the Taiwan issue. We demand that Japan seriously heed China’s solemn position, deeply reflect on history, immediately correct its errors, and take concrete measures to eliminate the bad influence. We warn the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatists that clamoring to collude with external forces, and seeking “independence” by force or “resisting reunification” by force, is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210714_12365811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: after Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical signed a BNT vaccine sales agreement with TSMC, Foxconn, and the Yongling Foundation, someone in the office of the Taiwan leader said the agreement was reached through “joint efforts of the German government and two Taiwanese companies,” and that “whether Chinese political power interfered is self-evident,” and that under the pressure of the US and Japan…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 14 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 14th in response to a question that in recent period, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have continuously fabricated lies to shift the blame for their failures and misconduct in epidemic prevention. On the vaccine issue, they have smeared and framed the mainland, once again exposing their ugly political nature.\nShe said that we highly care about and attach great importance to the life, health and safety of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Since the outbreak of the epidemic on the island in May this year, we have, from the very beginning, stated that we are willing to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic, and have repeatedly expressed the hope that Taiwan compatriots can have access to vaccines as soon as possible. We are willing to provide Taiwan compatriots with mainland vaccines recognized by the World Health Organization, and we support Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical in participating in the development and agency of the BNT vaccine to serve the people of Taiwan. As the only purchasing party for the BNT vaccine in the Taiwan region, a responsible person of Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical has long publicly stated that it is willing to make the vaccine available to Taiwan compatriots and to play a positive role in epidemic prevention and control on the island.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the facts show that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities bear the greatest responsibility for the outbreak of the epidemic on the island. Their cold-blooded political calculations and vicious political manipulation on epidemic prevention are the root cause of the shortage of vaccines on the island and the continuous loss of innocent lives. Out of their “anti-China” political purpose, they have not only tried every means to vilify and smear the mainland’s goodwill and, under various pretexts, refused to accept mainland vaccines, but have also blocked some counties, cities, enterprises and private institutions on the island from purchasing BNT vaccines from mainland enterprises. It was not until late June, when the epidemic on the island kept worsening, the vaccine shortage could not be eased and public resentment kept rising, that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, under pressure, reluctantly agreed for two Taiwan companies to negotiate with Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical. As Taiwan public opinion has pointed out, had the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not repeatedly obstructed the process, an agreement on the purchase of BNT vaccines could have been reached long ago through normal commercial rules. To this day, when some counties and cities in Taiwan have requested to negotiate with Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical for vaccine purchases, they are still refused by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. All sectors in Taiwan see this very clearly, and no matter how the Democratic Progressive Party authorities slander and deny, this fact cannot be changed.\nShe said that we are willing to do our utmost to help the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots get through this difficult time as soon as possible, and our sincerity is constant. The difficulty Taiwan people face in getting vaccinated lies in the fact that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have completely ignored the urgent needs of the public for epidemic prevention and have only cared about their own party interests. We urge the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not to place their political self-interest above the life, health and safety of the people of Taiwan. Fabrication and slander cannot change the facts, and smearing and framing cannot shirk responsibility; they will only make innocent people in Taiwan pay an even higher price in lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210714_12365889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-15","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Two questions from AFP. South China Morning Post has reported that authorities in Yunnan have put up border walls and fences to prevent illegal entry from neighboring countries including Myanmar. Can you confirm this and provide any details of China's border enforcement in Yunnan? My second question is whether you have any response to reports that a US military plane landed in Taiwan this week?","On your first question, I'm not aware of the situation. I can assure you that China and Myanmar regulate borders in accordance with law.\nOn your second question, the Ministry of National Defense has made a response. I'd refer you to the competent authorities if you have more specific questions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210715_9170786.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1892338.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-07-15","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On July 15, some media reported that a US military transport aircraft landed in Taiwan. We express serious concern. Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory. Any foreign military aircraft landing on our territory must obtain permission from the Government of the People's Republic of China, and any foreign vessel or aircraft that illegally intrudes into our airspace will trigger serious consequences. We solemnly warn the US not to play with fire, to immediately stop its risky and provocative acts, not to send wrong signals to ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces, and to avoid aggravating the creation of dangerous and tense situations in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe warn the DPP authorities not to misjudge the situation, not to invite wolves into the house, not to take desperate risks, and not to collude with external forces to plot ‘independence’ and provocations. This will only lead Taiwan into a dangerous situation. China must be unified, and it will certainly be unified. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's resolve, firm will, and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese People's Liberation Army maintains a high state of alert and will take all necessary measures to firmly crush any ‘Taiwan independence’ scheme.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/TopStories/4889511.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278439.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 15 — According to reports, on the 15th a US military transport aircraft landed in Taiwan. In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said that day in response to a question: We have noted the relevant reports. We firmly oppose any form of US-Taiwan military collusion and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and security. We urge the US side to abide by the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués on the Taiwan question and stop all provocations. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and reject unification, are leading the people of Taiwan toward disaster, and their scheme will inevitably fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210715_12366076.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-19","Zhao Lijian","HRTN","Could you offer more information about State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s official visit to Egypt on July 18?","During his visit to Egypt, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with the Egyptian President Abdel Fattah El-Sisi and held talks with Foreign Minister Sameh Shoukry. The two foreign ministers signed an agreement on establishing the China-Egypt inter-governmental cooperation committee and attended an online ceremony marking the joint production of one million doses of COVID-19 vaccine.\nState Councilor Wang Yi stated China’s firm support for Egypt’s continued exploration for a development path in keeping with its national realities as well as China’s readiness to further dovetail the BRI with Egypt Vision 2030. China will support Egypt’s local vaccine production, seek greater synergy between the two sides’ development strategies and expand cooperation in the fields of industrial capacity, infrastructure, new energy, space and aviation, and cutting-edge technology to break new ground in our mutually beneficial cooperation. China looks forward to working together with Egypt to act on the important consensus reached by our heads of state, build on the momentum of the 65th anniversary of diplomatic ties to elevate relations to a new height, strive to forge a China-Egypt community with a shared future, and build this relationship into a prototype of China-Arab and China-Africa community with a shared future.\nThe Egyptian side said it firmly opposes foreign interference in China’s internal affairs under the pretext of issues relating to Hong Kong, Xinjiang, Taiwan and Tibet, appreciate China’s help in producing vaccines, support China on the origins study, and is ready to enhance cooperation and exchanges with China in such areas as economy and trade, industries, science and technology, and people-to-people and cultural ties under the Belt and Road framework.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi also had in-depth exchanges with Foreign Minister Shoukry on the Palestinian question.\nState Councilor Wang Yi put forward three proposals for the implementation of the two-state solution. First, the authority of the Palestinian National Authority should be enhanced, and it should be authorized to exercise sovereign functions in security, finance and other areas, so as to gain effective control over the autonomous and occupied territories. Second, the Palestinian factions should be supported for greater unity, whereby they can achieve internal reconciliation through consultation and dialogue, and come to a unified position on talks for the settlement of the Palestinian question. Third, Palestine and Israel should be encouraged to resume peace talks based on the two-state solution. China calls for the holding of an international peace conference led by the UN with the participation of the permanent members of the UN Security Council and all stakeholders in the Middle East peace process.\nEgypt agrees with the proposals put forward by China. China and Egypt agreed to work together to offer 500,000 doses of vaccine to the Palestinian people in the Gaza Strip to address the urgent needs of the local people.\nDuring his visit to Egypt, State Councilor Wang Yi also met with Secretary-General of the League of Arab States Ahmed Aboul Gheit and had an in-depth exchange of views with him on China-Arab states relations as well as regional and international issues. The two sides issued a joint statement, stressing that they will strengthen China-Arab states long-term cooperation, prepare for the first China-Arab states summit and strive to build a China-Arab community with a shared future. In the joint statement, the two sides also stressed the need to adhere to the principle of non-interference in other countries' internal affairs, uphold multilateralism, oppose politicizing human rights issues, oppose unilateralism, and promote the building of a new type of international relations. They stressed the importance of a just, comprehensive and durable solution to the Palestinian question on the basis of the two-state solution, supported all efforts aimed at preventing the proliferation of nuclear and other weapons of mass destruction, and advocated more robust counter-terrorism efforts and the eradication of the root causes of terrorism.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1893359.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1893300.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-07-20","Zhao Lijian","RIA Novosti","Taiwan's \"foreign ministry\" today announced that it is going to establish its representative office in Lithuania. I wonder if you have any comment on this and has the foreign ministry made any representations to Lithuania?","China firmly opposes any official exchanges and the mutual establishment of so-called \"representative offices\" between Taiwan and countries with diplomatic relations with China. We urge the Lithuanian side to adhere to the one-China principle and honor its commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties. Also a word of advice to the Taiwan authorities: \"Taiwan independence\" leads to a dead end and any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210720_9170789.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1893709.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-07-20","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On July 13, Japan released the 2021 edition of its “Defense White Paper,” falsely claiming that China's military development “lacks transparency,” that China is “changing the status quo by force” in the East China Sea and South China Sea, and included statements such as “the situation in Taiwan is very important to Japan's security and international stability.” In addition, senior Japanese defense officials have…","On July 13, the Japanese side released its 2021 Defense White Paper. It groundlessly accuses China's normal national defense and military development, maliciously speculates about China's defense policy, deliberately hypes the so-called “China threat,” and crudely interferes in China's internal affairs on the Taiwan question. The Chinese military expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition, and has lodged stern representations with the Japanese side.\nThere is only one China, and Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory. The Japanese side's use of the Defense White Paper to dictate on the Taiwan question seriously violates UN Resolution 2758 and the international community's consensus on one China. It undermines the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan and the solemn commitments the Japanese side made to China on the Taiwan question, and damages the political foundation of China-Japan relations. This is entirely wrong and irresponsible. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external force may interfere. The Chinese military will take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nIt must be emphasized that China has always firmly pursued the path of peaceful development and steadfastly adheres to a defensive national defense policy. China's national defense development always aims to meet its own legitimate security needs, and the growth of China's military strength is entirely an expansion of the forces for world peace. Japan should view China and the Chinese military's development objectively and rationally, and stop hyping the so-called “Chinese military threat.” The Chinese military has the resolve, confidence, and capability to safeguard the people's happy lives and to firmly uphold national sovereignty, security, and development interests.\nRecently, Japanese senior defense officials have frequently made negative remarks about China, undermining the foundation of China-Japan defense relations and poisoning the atmosphere of bilateral relations. We remind the Japanese side to always keep the lessons of history in mind, abide by the peace constitution and the exclusively defense-oriented policy, stop making erroneous remarks on related issues, and move in the same direction as China to push China-Japan defense relations forward on the right track.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2021-07/20/content_4889768.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-07-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 20 — In response to the DPP authorities' announcement that they will set up a “representative office” in Lithuania, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 20th in response to questions: Taiwan is part of China. We oppose our diplomatic partner developing official relations with the Chinese Taiwan region. We urge Lithuania to adhere to the one-China principle and not send the wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces. The farce of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces in setting up an “office” aims to pursue “independence.” No matter how they carry on, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the one-China international landscape.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210720_12367042.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-21","Zhao Lijian","","美国国务院东亚局发推特称，美欢迎台湾拓展国际伙伴关系及应对疫情、投资审查、供应链韧性等共同挑战所作努力。美对台设立“驻立陶宛台湾代表处”表示赞赏。外交部对此有何回应？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1894085.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2021-07-21","Zhao Lijian","","我有两个问题。第一个问题是关于舍曼的亚洲之行。据媒体报道，她已与韩国、日本的外交官共同表示，要一起维护台海稳定局势的重要性。请问中方对此有何评论？第二个问题是，英国和日本的防长发出联合声明，指出英国将在亚洲水域永久部署两艘军舰。请问中方对此有何评论？","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1894085.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2021-07-22","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","On July 20, Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Japan issued a press release on the bilateral meeting between Japanese Vice Foreign Minister Takeo Mori and US Deputy Secretary of State Wendy Sherman. They criticized China on issues relating the East China Sea and the South China Sea, reaffirmed the importance of maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and expressed grave concern over the situation in…","China has lodged solemn representations here in Beijing and in the other side's capital to deplore and reject the negative moves by Japan and the US against China. I want to stress that issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are China's internal affairs that allow no foreign interference. No one should underestimate the resolve, the will, and the ability of the Chinese people to defend their national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWith regard to maritime issues, China is firmly resolved in safeguarding national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. In the meantime, we are ready to properly settle maritime disputes with countries concerned through consultation and negotiation. Attempts to meddle in the the East China Sea and the South China Sea under all kinds of pretexts will only bring unnecessary disruptions to the peace and tranquility in the region, and run counter to the interests of regional countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1894390.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1894384.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 22. Recently, Henan has continued to suffer rare torrential rain, and serious waterlogging has occurred in places including Zhengzhou, causing casualties and property losses. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 22nd that relevant parties in Taiwan and people from all sectors have expressed concern and sympathy for the disaster-stricken areas through various means, and that some Taiwan-invested enterprises have donated money and goods. We express our gratitude for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210722_12367573.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-23","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","On July 20, a group of US lawmakers proposed the Taiwan Partnership Act, urging the US National Guard to establish a partnership programme with the Taiwan military to ensure a well-integrated defense force capable of fast deployment during a crisis. Separately, the US Senate Armed Services Committee passed the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2022 (NDAA), saying that the US should \"maintain the…","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a historical and legal fact that cannot be altered by anyone or any force in any way. The US should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, act prudently on Taiwan question, stop advancing the Taiwan-related bill, delete the articles concerning Taiwan, stop clamoring for military interactions between the US and Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210723_9170792.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1894631.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Starting October 1, Taiwan compatriots holding Taiwan residence permits may participate in Beijing's urban and rural residents' basic old-age insurance. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed that the residence permit is a “united front” measure by the mainland to weaken Taiwan's so-called “sovereignty.” What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in answering…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 23 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 23rd in response to questions that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have consistently harbored dark intentions toward the mainland's care for Taiwan compatriots. They oppose anything that benefits Taiwan compatriots, routinely launch attacks and smears, deliberately mislead, and even threaten and intimidate the people of Taiwan. Whether a policy is good is for Taiwan compatriots to judge most authoritatively. Mainland regions and departments will, as always, implement the policy of equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots well, and concretely put care and support for Taiwan compatriots into practice.\nShe said that the policy issued by the Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau is a good thing and a practical matter that further refines and implements equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that, as is well known, the Taiwan Residence Permit is an identity document issued by the motherland's mainland to facilitate Taiwan compatriots working and living on the mainland in enjoying basic public services. According to the Interim Measures on Social Insurance Participation by Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Residents in the Mainland, issued in November 2019 by the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security and the National Healthcare Security Administration, to guarantee that Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal social insurance rights in the mainland according to law, both employed and unemployed Taiwan compatriots may participate in local urban and rural residents' basic old-age insurance with a residence permit. After participating in insurance, if a Taiwan compatriot leaves the mainland before reaching the prescribed conditions for receiving pension benefits, they may choose to keep their account so they can continue making contributions when they return to work or reside on the mainland again. They may also choose to submit a written application to terminate their social insurance relationship and withdraw the balance of their personal social insurance account in a lump sum. Taiwan compatriots who have already insured themselves in Taiwan may also choose, according to their own circumstances, not to participate in mainland old-age insurance and unemployment insurance.\nShe said that these flexible and pragmatic arrangements were made by the competent mainland authorities after earnestly listening to and actively studying the opinions of Taiwan compatriots. They fully reflect the continued improvement of relevant mainland departments' policy measures to safeguard the welfare of Taiwan compatriots, and their wholehearted commitment to doing practical things, doing good things, and solving difficult problems for Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210723_12367860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, some anti-China members of the U.S. Congress concocted the so-called “Taiwan Partnership Act,” and the Senate Armed Services Committee passed the “FY2022 National Defense Authorization Act,” which contains anti-China content related to Taiwan, and even clamored to promote military collusion between the U.S. National Guard and Taiwan. The DPP authorities have expressed gratitude. What…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 23 (Electric). Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 23rd in response to questions: We urge certain members of the US Congress to stop concocting negative bills related to Taiwan, to stop wrong words and deeds that violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and not to send wrong signals to 'Taiwan independence' forces.\nShe also said that 'Taiwan independence' is a dead end, and 'resisting unification by force' only accelerates pushing the Taiwan people further along that dead end toward disaster. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The 'Taiwan independence' forces regard collusion with external forces as a lifesaving straw for protecting 'Taiwan independence,' but the result will only be to be firmly crushed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210723_12367890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-26","Zhao Lijian","SCMP","First, US Deputy Secretary of State Sherman is visiting the Chinese city of Tianjin. How does China assess the progress of the talks with the US? The US side said prior to the visit that it hoped Sherman's visit would help set up \"guardrails\" to see to it that the bilateral relationship won't become worse. Could I have China's view on that? Second, according to media reports, US forces recently intensified…","On your first question, China has already released readouts on US Deputy Secretary of State Sherman's visit, which is still underway.\nDuring the talks, the Chinese side faced the existing problems in bilateral relations squarely, expounded on China's attitude and position on developing relations with the US in a candid manner, expressed its unequivocal opposition to the US side's practice of interfering in China's internal affairs and harming China's interests, and made it clear that the US side must change course and correct its mistakes. The two sides also had in-depth exchange of views on a wide range of issues of their respective and mutual interest. The US side sought China's cooperation and support on climate change, Iran and the Korean nuclear issue among others. In fact, China has been playing a responsible and constructive role on all these issues. It needs to be emphasized that cooperation should be based on mutual trust, mutual benefit and a sound atmosphere for bilateral relations. The US should adopt a correct view of cooperation. It simply won't work when the US seeks cooperation with China while harming China's interests.\nApart from expounding on its principle position on China-US relations, and requiring the US side to change its extremely wrong perception and dangerous policy toward China, China once again expressed strong dissatisfaction with the US side over its wrong words and deeds on issues relating to COVID-19 origin-tracing, Taiwan, Xinjiang, Hong Kong and the South China Sea, urging the US side to immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop damaging the interests of China, stop crossing the red lines and playing with fire, and stop seeking bloc confrontation under the guise of values. We urge the US to never underestimate the strong resolution, determination and capability of the 1.4 billion Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests.\nOn the whole, the talks have been profound, candid and helpful for the two sides to gain a better understanding of each other's position and seek healthy development of China-US relations going forward.\nOn your second question, the situation in Afghanistan has come to a critical crossroads with severe challenges. War or peace, chaos or order, much is at stake. China always believes that political negotiation is the only correct way to resolve the Afghan issue.\nIt needs to be stressed that the recent sudden announcement by the US of full withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan is the root cause of the acute deterioration of the security situation there. It puts Afghanistan's peace and stability as well the security interests of regional countries under grave threat. As the culprit that started the Afghan issue, the US must assume its due responsibility and take concrete actions to ensure a steady transition and prevent terrorist forces from swooping in and strengthening their hold, so as to safeguard the peace and reconciliation process in Afghanistan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202107/t20210726_9170793.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1895085.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 26 — On the eve of the opening of the Tokyo Olympics, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities said, “No matter what great challenges we encounter, Taiwan will not be prevented from becoming a member of the world,” and thanked “Japan for making everything possible.” In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 26th: Questions of principle allow no challenge. Playing petty tricks to seek “independence” in sporting events has no way out and will only bring about self-inflicted consequences.\nShe said that regarding the participation of “Chinese Taipei” in the Olympic Games, in keeping with the One-China Principle, the International Olympic Committee adopted the “Nagoya Resolution” in 1979 and, in accordance with past practice, clearly specified the team name and emblem of “Chinese Taipei” for participation in the Tokyo Olympics. Its essence is to resolve the participation of “Chinese Taipei” under the One-China Principle. The “Olympic model” is a principle jointly followed by international sports organizations and sports circles on both sides of the Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said that Taiwan is part of China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. We wish the athletes of both sides of the Strait success in achieving excellent results together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210726_12368458.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: recently, some people in the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have hyped the “Taiwan representative office in Lithuania” as a “major diplomatic breakthrough,” claiming that the English name of the “representative office” includes “Taiwanese,” representing a “country.” What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in response to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 26 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 26th in response to a question: The DPP authorities keep deceiving on the island, and keep infiltrating and courting external forces, scheming in every way to pursue “independence.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that all attempts at “independence” are futile and cannot escape the outcome of failure. She said: We have repeatedly reiterated that we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have established diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region. We urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210726_12368460.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-27","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","US Deputy Secretary of State Sherman concluded her visit to China yesterday. How does China see her trip to Tianjin? Has China achieved its expected outcomes from the meeting and talks?","The trip to Tianjin by Deputy Secretary Sherman is another important diplomatic interaction between China and the US after the dialogue in Anchorage. During her brief 24-hour stay, Ms. Sherman spent altogether six hours in the meeting with State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and talks with Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng. We can say that the two sides had deep and thorough conversations and enhanced mutual understanding.\nChina made clear its views on the current China-US relations in the meeting and talks. China-US relations face severe difficulties and challenges. There is a big question mark on whether bilateral ties will head to conflict and confrontation or improvement and development. The US needs to think carefully and make the right choice.\nChina made clear its attitude to the China policy of the new US administration. It pointed out that this administration has in general inherited its predecessor's erroneous China policy, constantly challenged China's bottom line, and stepped up containment and suppression on China. China firmly opposes such practices and has made resolute responses.\nThe Chinese side pointed out that the erroneous China policy comes down to the US side's misguided perception about China, its view of China as an \"imaginary enemy\", the primary rival, and increasingly an adversary. It is this perception that drives the US to hype up the competitive, collaborative and adversarial rhetoric, the notion of \"a position of strength\" and the so-called \"rules-based international order\". This perception can also be found behind erroneous words and acts that interfere in China's internal affairs, slander and smear China, and undermine China's interests. China urges the US side to come to an objective and correct understanding of China, change course by redressing mistakes, work with China on the basis of mutual respect, seek fair competition and peaceful co-existence, and return to a rational and pragmatic China policy. China always believes that a sound and stable China-US relationship not only serves the interests of both parties, but is also the common aspiration of the international community.\nThe US talked about \"responsible management\" of bilateral relations during this visit. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi underlined three basic demands as bottom lines on how to effectively manage differences and prevent China-US relations from getting out of control. The first is that the US must not challenge, slander or even attempt to subvert the path and system of socialism with Chinese characteristics. The second is that the US must not attempt to obstruct or interrupt China's development process. The third is that the US must not infringe upon China's state sovereignty, or even damage China's territorial integrity.\nThe US also talked about setting \"guardrails\" for bilateral relations. The Chinese side stressed that any norm of behavior in China-US relations must be discussed and agreed on by both sides. It must be based on equality and mutual benefit and guided by safeguarding the interests of both sides. It must be binding on both parties and cannot be barriers set by the US unilaterally for China.\nDuring the meeting and talks, the Chinese side solemnly elaborated on China's position on issues relating to study of origins of SARS-CoV-2, Taiwan, Xinjiang, Hong Kong, the South China Sea and cybersecurity, sternly rebuking US fallacies and putting forward clear demands. China also gave the US two lists, as I said yesterday, one consisting of 16 items detailing erroneous US policies, words and actions that should be redressed, another containing 10 key individual cases of particular concern.\nThe two sides also exchanged views on some international and regional issues including climate change, the Iranian nuclear issue, the Korean Peninsula, Afghanistan and Myanmar. On these issues, China and the US have sound cooperation and there is broad space for both to work together. That being said, China also pointed out explicitly that cooperation must be based on mutual trust and premised on mutual benefit. The US needs to show sincerity and create conditions for cooperation. It cannot expect to harm China's interests on one hand while hoping for unconditional cooperation from China on the other.\nDifferences and somewhat tense encounters are commonplace in diplomacy. Both sides believe that the meeting and talks are candid, in-depth and constructive. Both agree on the utmost importance of maintaining communication between China and the US and the need for more frank and sincere dialogues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1895361.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1895350.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-07-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: After US Executive Deputy Secretary of State Sherman visited China, the Chinese side released relevant information. When State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Sherman, the US side stated that it adheres to the One-China policy and does not support Taiwan “independence.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for the recent visit of US officials to China that mentioned the Taiwan…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 28 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated on the 28th in response to questions: We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle through concrete actions. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an iron fact that no person or force can change. If the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to provoke, they will face only complete failure.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that no one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210728_12368917.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Yu Hsi-kun, head of Taiwan's legislative body, recently once again made “Taiwan independence” remarks, advocating so-called “normalization of the Taiwan state,” and claiming that “if Taiwan-US ‘diplomatic relations’ succeed, goals such as ‘Taiwan name rectification,’ ‘constitution-making,’ and ‘joining the UN’ will follow naturally.” What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian made the above…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 28 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 28th in response to a question: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces not to misjudge the situation; persisting stubbornly on the dead-end road of “Taiwan independence” will only end with bloodied heads. The motherland must be and will inevitably be reunified. Any provocation by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will be firmly defeated. We will closely monitor the movements of the handful of “Taiwan independence” diehards on the island and will impose stern punishment and crackdowns in accordance with the law.\nShe pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The historical and legal facts that both sides of the Strait belong to one China cannot be changed by anyone or any force.\nZhu Fenglian said that recently, Su Tseng-chang and his ilk have openly spread “Taiwan independence” remarks. Knowing full well that “Taiwan independence” cannot be done, dares not be done, and must not be done, they stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, and are determined to impose “Taiwan independence” propositions on the broad masses of Taiwan people, attempting to deceive and fool the island’s public with fabrications and mislead the international community. It is both absurd and pitiful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210728_12368985.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-07-29","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","According to reports, the former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe expressed concern about increasing Chinese military pressure on Taiwan. This was at the first strategic dialogue between lawmakers from Japan, the US and Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have a comment?","The so-called \"dialogue\" you mentioned has no influence whatsoever. It is negative and wrong in both form and content. In fact, it plays the same old tune that no one cares to listen.\nI want to stress that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. China's national reunification and rejuvenation are an unstoppable trend. No one should underestimate the strong resolution, determination and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" will be like trying to hold back the tide with a broom, and is doomed to fail.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the political foundation of China-US relations and China-Japan relations. Both the US and Japan have the responsibility and obligation to abide by the principles set in relevant bilateral political documents with China and the solemn commitments they have made to China on the Taiwan question, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347097.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1896050.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-07-29","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","There are reports that the US Senate Committee on Foreign Relations passed a bill on 28 July to direct the State Department to develop a strategy to assist Taiwan in obtaining observer status at the World Health Assembly. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of bilateral relations and the consensus of the international community.\nThe US bill is a serious breach of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and a violation of the fundamental principle affirmed by UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. We firmly reject it. The Chinese Central Government always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. Under the precondition of abiding by the one-China principle, we have made appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs.\nThe US should fully recognize that the Taiwan question is a highly sensitive issue. It should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques and comply with international law and basic norms governing international relations. The US should stop reviewing and pushing the negative Taiwan-related bill, not to send out wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces and not to help the Taiwan region to expand its so-called \"international space\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347097.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1896050.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-07-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, the US has frequently colluded with Taiwan recently, as shown by the US congress promoting Taiwan-related legislation, the false statements repeatedly made by the US officials about Taiwan, and the landing of a US military transport plane in Taiwan on July 15. At the same time, the PLA has continuously increased the intensity of military operations in the Taiwan Strait. What’s your…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and the One-China Principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The US has violated international law and the basic norms of international relations through irresponsible remarks and deeds, gravely interfered in China’s internal affairs, seriously harmed China’s territorial sovereignty and security interests, and severely threathened the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, to which China is strongly opposed. China has solemnly informed the US that those who play with fire would set themselves on fire and the “salami-slicing” approach taken by the US on the Taiwan question would sure cut itself. China urged the US to abide by the One-China Principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, stop all provocative acts, and send no wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Otherwise, the US will have to bear all serious consequences caused. Furthermore, China warned Taiwan’s Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities not to misjudge the situation, borrow strength from foreign forces and invite the wolf into the house as a result. “Relying on the US to seek independence” will only lead to a dead end, harming both the Taiwan people and the DPP itself.\nChina must and will get reunified. No one should underestimate the Chinese people’s determination and strong ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese PLA has always been on high alert and will take all necessary measures to resolutely smash any separatist plots or actions for “Taiwan independence”.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-08/02/content_4890889.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2021-07-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: U.S. Defense Secretary Austin recently made negative remarks involving Taiwan, and the DPP authorities expressed gratitude for them. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in response to questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 29 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 29th in response to a question: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the US and the Taiwan region of China.\nZhu Fenglian said: We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities, attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “use force to resist unification,” will only push the people of Taiwan into disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210729_12369199.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 29 — Some media have reported that the DPP authorities, colluding with Japanese and US lawmakers, are staging a so-called “strategic dialogue,” advocating “sharing democratic values and confronting the mainland.” In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated on the 29th in response to questions: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to once again stage a “Taiwan independence” farce will only bring humiliation upon themselves.\nShe said that, at the same time, she urges relevant countries to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and not to send any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. China must be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified. This is something no person or force can stop!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210729_12369235.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Wu Chao-hsieh recently played up the so-called “mainland military threat to Taiwan” in an interview with foreign media, spread “Taiwan independence” remarks, and sought to expand so-called “international space.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in response to the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 30. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 30th in response to questions: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Wu Zhaoxie and his ilk openly spread “Taiwan independence” remarks, attempting to deceive and mislead the people on the island and mislead the international community. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and Wu Zhaoxie and his ilk: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Any scheme to collude with external forces to pursue “independence” and reject unification is nothing but wishful thinking and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210730_12369361.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-07-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 30 — Some media reported that the U.S. House of Representatives recently passed an appropriations bill containing Taiwan-related content, clamoring not to use Chinese maps that include the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities expressed thanks. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 30th when asked: All the facts and legal evidence concerning Taiwan prove that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan-related content fully exposes the ignorance and sinister intentions of certain members of the U.S. Congress.\nZhu Fenglian said that we urge the U.S. side to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to stop interfering in China's internal affairs. We warn the DPP authorities: willing to serve as pawns and “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202107/t20210730_12369490.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-08-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 5 (Electric). The US Defense Security Cooperation Agency announced on August 4 that it had approved a weapons sale to Taiwan worth approximately 750 million US dollars. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 5th in response to questions: We firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the 'August 17 Communiqué,' to stop all arms sales to Taiwan, not send wrong signals to 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces, not endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and not harm the well-being of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities' attempts to 'rely on the US to seek independence' and 'resist reunification by force' will only push the Taiwan people toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210805_12370660.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-08-06","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Department of Defense’s Defense Security Cooperation Agency issued a press release on August 4 stating that the U.S. State Department has approved the sale to Taiwan of a self-propelled howitzer system and related equipment worth approximately US$750 million. What is your comment on this?","This US move disregards international law and the basic norms of international relations. It seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, damages China's sovereignty and security interests, sends a wrong signal to ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces, and endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's core interests. China strongly demands that the US honor its commitments, strictly abide by the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the ‘August 17 Communiqué’, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, and stop arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military ties, so as not to further damage China-US relations between the two militaries and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army has the resolve, will, and capability to resolutely thwart any form of external interference and ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist schemes. It will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/15994627.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278457.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-08-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: on the afternoon of August 10, the Foreign Ministry spokesperson issued a statement on China's decision to recall its ambassador to Lithuania, which has attracted great attention from all sectors. What comment do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response when answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 10 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 10th in response to questions: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that colluding with external forces to provoke “independence” schemes will only reap its own bitter fruit. No one should underestimate our firm determination, strong will and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that our relevant departments have already stated our stern position. I must reiterate: there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The one-China principle is a generally recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The historical trend toward reunification of the two sides of the Strait cannot be blocked by anyone or any force!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210810_12371663.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-08-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 11 — In response to Tsai Ing-wen's recent interview with Japanese media, in which she spread “Taiwan independence” remarks and played up the mainland's military threat to Taiwan, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 11th: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. This is a fact that no person or force can change. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: attempting to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation is a miscalculation, and it is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210811_12371759.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-08-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: some media reported that Mo Jian, Chairman of the “American Institute in Taiwan,” recently said that uncertainty in the Taiwan Strait has increased and that the United States needs to strengthen regional deterrence. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above statement when answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 11 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 11th in response to a question that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The US side has fabricated various pretexts to sell weapons to Taiwan, attempting to maintain so-called “deterrence in the Taiwan Strait.” This will only bring greater threats to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and greater harm to the interests and well-being of the people on both sides. We resolutely oppose the US side playing the “Taiwan card,” and urge it to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with prudence and appropriateness, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence.”\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and the root cause is that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, in collusion with external forces, have continuously engaged in provocations to seek “independence,” undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is a core interest of the country and a common responsibility of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. If “Taiwan independence” dares to provoke and takes desperate risks, we have the right to take all necessary measures to stop it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210811_12371872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-08-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 11. Taiwan media reported that Taiwan and the US held a joint coast guard drill in the waters east of Taiwan, but relevant Taiwan authorities said this is not the case. In this regard, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 11th in response to questions: We have noted the relevant reports. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the US and the region of Taiwan, China. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces and provoking and playing with fire, will surely reap what they have sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210811_12371873.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-08-13","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reports say that before the August 15 anniversary of Japan's surrender, Japanese Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi visited the Yasukuni Shrine on the afternoon of the 13th. This is the second time the current Japanese Defense Minister has visited Yasukuni Shrine. What comment do you have?","China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to the visit by Japan's Minister of Defense to the Yasukuni Shrine, and has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nAs everyone knows, the Yasukuni Shrine is a spiritual tool and symbol of Japanese militarism's external wars of aggression. It enshrines 14 Class-A war criminals who bear grave responsibility for that war of aggression. The Japanese Minister of Defense's visit to the Yasukuni Shrine once again reflects the Japanese side's wrong attitude toward its history of aggression and its sinister intent to challenge the post-war international order. Those who cannot face history will have no future. We demand that the Japanese side earnestly reflect on its history of aggression, always keep the lessons of history in mind, take measures to correct its mistakes, and win the trust of Asian neighbors and the international community through concrete actions.\nRecently, Japan's defense departments have repeatedly taken negative actions on China-related issues: colluding with countries outside the region to smear China's national defense policy and military development, carrying out targeted military exercises on a large scale, crudely interfering in the Taiwan question, which is purely China's internal affair, and carrying out provocative actions in the South China Sea. These actions have seriously disrupted the development of China-Japan defense relations. We urge the Japanese side to discard Cold War mentality and, in accordance with the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, move in the same direction as China on the basis of mutual respect and non-interference in each other's internal affairs, and promote China-Japan defense relations along the correct track.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/info/2021-08/13/content_4891861.htm","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-08-13","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: Recently, Aquilino, commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, made negative remarks on several China-related issues at the Aspen Security Forum. When asked whether the US military is capable of assisting Taiwan in an emergency, Aquilino said the United States has the world's most advanced and most powerful military and can respond to any contingency. He also gave negative assessments of China's…","Tan Kefei: We have noted the relevant remarks by the US side. Recently, US military personnel have repeatedly made irresponsible and erroneous remarks on China-related issues, interfered in China's internal affairs, and hyped up China-US confrontation. We firmly oppose this. The issues of Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are purely China's internal affairs, and no foreign country has the right to interfere. US officials' arbitrary interference in other countries' internal affairs is a contempt for and trampling of international law and the basic norms of international relations. On the South China Sea issue, the United States, as an extra-regional country, often uses the pretext of “freedom of navigation” to show off its military force in the South China Sea, provoke, and stir up trouble, undermining the efforts of regional countries to jointly maintain peace and stability in the South China Sea. Facts have long proven that the United States is the “troublemaker” in the South China Sea and the greatest threat to regional peace and stability.\nAt present, China-US and China-US military relations are at a critical juncture, and which way they go is of close concern to both peoples and the international community. Developing healthy and stable military relations between the two militaries serves the common interests of both sides and is the general expectation of the international community. China's position on developing China-US military relations is one of principle. We urge the US side to earnestly respect China's core interests and major concerns, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, speak and act with prudence, and do more things that are conducive to the development of China-US and military relations.\nOne must first correct oneself before correcting others, and one must reflect before speaking. As is well known, after World War II the US military continued to frequently launch wars and military operations around the world. Since 2001 alone, the wars in Iraq, Libya, Syria and other places have caused the deaths of more than 800,000 people and the displacement of tens of millions. In stark contrast, the Chinese military has always held high the banner of win-win cooperation. It has repeatedly participated in international peacekeeping, maritime escort, humanitarian rescue and disaster relief operations, actively promoted reform of the global security governance system, and firmly upheld justice and fairness and promoted peaceful development. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, the Chinese military has also actively carried out anti-epidemic international cooperation with the militaries of relevant countries. The Chinese military will, as always, firmly defend national sovereignty, security and development interests, and make new and greater contributions to serving the building of a community with a shared future for mankind.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278458.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-08-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 13 (dateline). Some media reported that, recently, under the coast guard cooperation memorandum signed between Taiwan and the United States in March this year, the two sides held their first working group meeting. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 13th, saying that we firmly oppose the U.S. side signing any agreement or conducting any activities with the Taiwan region of China that carry sovereignty implications. We urge the U.S. side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués on the Taiwan question, and to stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, pursuing “independence” and rejecting unification, will only push Taiwan toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210813_12372246.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-08-17","Hua Chunying","CCTV","Today marks the 39th anniversary of the publication of the August 17 Communiqué between China and the US. Do you have any comment?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. It was on the basis of the one-China principle that China and the US established diplomatic ties 42 years ago. Thirty-nine years ago today, China and the US jointly published the August 17 Communiqué. The US side pledged that it does not seek to carry out a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan, that its arms sales to Taiwan will not exceed, either in qualitative or in quantitative terms, the level of those supplied in recent years since the establishment of diplomatic relations between the United States and China, and that it intends gradually to reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution. The August 17 Communiqué, the Shanghai Communiqué and the China-US Joint Communiqué constitute the political foundation of China-US relations, and their core essence is the one-China principle, which the US side should strictly abide by.\nBut what we see is the fact that the US side has kept breaching its own commitment. It has engaged in official exchanges with the Taiwan region, sold arms to Taiwan and helped it to expand the so-called international space. Let's take US arms sales to Taiwan as an example. Over the past 39 years, the total amount of arms sales to Taiwan by successive US administrations has hit as high as nearly $70 billion. The Trump administration alone has sold arms to Taiwan 11 times in four years, totaling $18.3 billion. Not long ago, the Biden administration announced its first arms sale deal to Taiwan, approving a $750 million weapons sale to Taiwan. In response to all this wrong moves on the US side, the Chinese side has made strong and resolute reactions to firmly safeguard its sovereignty and security interests.\nTo solve the Taiwan question and realize the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all the Chinese people. We are ready to make every effort with the utmost sincerity to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. At the same time, we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures in response to the interference of external forces and the very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their activities. No one should mistakenly underestimate the strong determination, firm will and strong capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No matter how many weapons the US provides to Taiwan, it cannot change the overriding trend of cross-Straits relations, still less to stop the process of China's reunification.\nA person without faith can not establish himself or herself; a country without credibility will decline. China urges the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature and serious harm of its arms sales to Taiwan, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official contacts and military ties with and arms sales to Taiwan, oppose the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities, so as to avoid causing further serious damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1900083.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1900050.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-08-17","Hua Chunying","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, President of Lithuania Gitanas Nauseda said recently that the country is committed to defend its democratic principles and values. He said, \"as a sovereign and independent country, Lithuania is free to decide which countries or territories it develops economic and cultural relations with\". What is China's comment?","I have read relevant reports. The Lithuanian President said it would defend its own values and interests. If Lithuania can do that, China certainly should and can defend its own interests more firmly, especially the core interests concerning territory and sovereignty. It must be pointed out that the Lithuanian side tries to distort concepts and disguise its challenge against the one-China principle as the so-called defence of \"principles and values\" to quibble for its development of relations in essence with Taiwan authorities. Such attempt can only fool themselves. The meaning of the one-China principle is clear and brooks no distortion and misrepresentation. Supporting the one-China policy means strict compliance with the one-China principle, including severing official exchanges in both flagrant and secret ways with Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1900083.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1900050.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-08-19","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","The Japanese Liberal Democratic Party plans to have a “2+2” high-level dialogue with the Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan through the inter-party communication channel, instead of an inter-governmental dialogue. Do you have any comment?","I noted relevant reports. Taiwan is part of China. The Chinese side firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations. On the Taiwan question, the Japanese side bears historical crimes and responsibilities to the Chinese people. We seriously urge Japan to review the relevant matter, avoid interfering in China’s domestic affairs in any form, and refrain from sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1900554.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1900508.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-08-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Yu Shyi-kun, head of Taiwan's legislature, recently accepted an interview with the Voice of America and again advocated “US-Taiwan diplomatic relations,” and said that Tsai Ing-wen's use of “Republic of China, Taiwan” is in principle “Taiwan independence,” and that the DPP authorities are gradually making “Taiwan move toward normal statehood” through means such as “amending laws” and “amending…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 19 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 19th: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a historical and legal fact that no person or force can change. We warn the DPP authorities and Su Tseng-chang and his kind: the more rampant their provocations to seek “independence,” the faster they will accelerate their own destruction. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm determination, resolute will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Su Tseng-chang's remarks fully expose his nature of willingly serving as a “pawn” of external forces and obstinately promoting “Taiwan independence.” “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, blinded by profit, attempt to bet on external forces, and act against the fundamental interests of all Chinese sons and daughters and the Chinese nation. They will certainly reap what they sow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210819_12373463.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-08-20","Hua Chunying","China Review News","US leader said in an interview on August 19 that there's a fundamental difference between Taiwan, South Korea, NATO and Afghanistan. The US side made a commitment to Article Five that if in fact anyone were to invade or take action against its NATO allies, the US would respond. Same with Japan, same with South Korea, same with Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","I noticed that some media have suggested that this may have been a slip of the tongue. There is indeed a fundamental difference between Taiwan and Afghanistan. Afghanistan is a sovereign state, while Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a red and bottom line that cannot be crossed. China must and will be reunified. No one should underestimate the strong determination, firm will and strong capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202108/t20210820_9170802.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202108/t20210820_9171324.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-08-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 20 — According to reports, Japan's Liberal Democratic Party plans to hold a so-called “security dialogue” with the DPP authorities in Taiwan. In response to this, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang stated on the 20th in response to questions: Over a period of time, the Japanese government and relevant individuals have made a series of erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question, and we firmly oppose them. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect on history, immediately correct its mistakes, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents through concrete actions, act with caution on the Taiwan question, and stop all erroneous words and deeds involving Taiwan. The DPP authorities' attempt to collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210820_12373664.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-08-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 20 dispatch: The DPP authorities expressed thanks for the recent remarks by US leaders on Taiwan-related issues. In response, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 20th, responding to questions, that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed a solemn position on this. It should be pointed out that the DPP authorities keep carrying out provocations to seek “independence,” and vainly hope to rely on external forces to embolden their “Taiwan independence” conduct. The only result will be pushing the Taiwan people into disaster. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop all manner of “independence”-seeking conduct, or they will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202108/t20210820_12373665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-08-25","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The ruling parties of Japan and Taiwan will hold their first security talks this week. The bilateral concerns about increasing Chinese military strength will likely to be atop the agenda. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment?","I noted relevant reports. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations. On the Taiwan question, the Japanese side bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people for its past crimes and should especially be prudent with its words and actions. We seriously urge Japan to review its considerations, avoid interfering in China's domestic affairs in any form, and refrain from sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347107.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1901762.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-08-26","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Jaushieh Joseph Wu, head of the Taiwan authorities’ foreign relations department, has stated on many occasions that Taiwan is at the very forefront of the threat of mainland’s military expansion, hence, Taiwan should improve its self-defense capabilities and keep strengthening cooperation with “like-minded countries”. Besides, it’s also reported that in order to ensure the accomplishment of the…","The one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community, and adherence to the one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities blatantly made “Taiwan independence” remarks, arrogantly clamored for provocations. They are just biting off more than they could chew.\nWe warn the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that any attempt to solicit foreign support is doomed to be a pipe dream, and seeking “independence” by military means leads to a dead end. China must and will be reunified. No one should underestimate the strong determination, firm will and strong capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army (PLA) has maintained a state of high alert at all times and stood ready to smash any “Taiwan independence” separatist plot.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/focus/2021-08/30/content_4893498.htm","",0,1,1,""],[0,"2021-08-27","Zhao Lijian","NHK","Today, the Japanese Liberal Democratic Party and the Taiwanese Democratic Progressive Party held an online \"2+2\" meeting. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The Chinese side has lodged solemn representation to the Japanese side.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations. On the Taiwan question, the Japanese side bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people for its past crimes and should especially be prudent with its words and actions. We seriously ask Japan to stop interfering in China's domestic affairs, and refrain from sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1902496.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202108/t20210827_9171329.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-08-27","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Taiwan officials said yesterday that they will tighten economic espionage laws in order to protect trade secrets from being leaked to Chinese companies. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","This is not a diplomatic issue. Please refer to the competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1902496.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202108/t20210827_9171329.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-08-28","Tan Kefei","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","On August 27, the US Navy guided-missile destroyer ‘Kidd’ and the Coast Guard gunboat ‘Munro’ transited the Taiwan Strait and publicly hyped it. The Eastern Theater Command of the PLA organized forces to shadow and monitor the US ships throughout. The US has repeatedly carried out similar provocations. Their nature is very egregious, which fully demonstrates that the US is the greatest disruptor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest creator of security risks there. We firmly oppose and strongly condemn this.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, admitting no foreign interference. We demand that the US recognize the situation, stop provocations, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not create obstacles to China-US relations or to relations between the two militaries, and not undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. The Chinese military maintains a high state of alert at all times and resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278440.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-09-02","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","First, the South China Morning Post reported that John Kerry will meet with Yang Jiechi today. Could you comment on that, and if possible, tell us what their agenda might be? Second question, the European Parliament's Foreign Affairs Committee on Wednesday adopted a report that urged the EU to begin work on a bilateral investment agreement with Taiwan. It also suggested that the bloc rename its trade office in…","On your first question, please stay tuned. We'll release information in due course.\nWith regard to your second question, the Chinese Mission to the EU has released a statement. The so-called \"EU-Taiwan Political Relations and Cooperation\" report concocted by the European Parliament's Committee on Foreign Affairs gravely violates the basic norms governing international relations, the one-China principle and the commitment on the Taiwan question made openly by the EU upon establishment of diplomatic relations with China. We strongly condemn and firmly reject it.\nWe urge the relevant committee and members of the European Parliament to immediately correct their wrong words and actions concerning Taiwan to avoid further damage to China-EU mutual trust and cooperation. The EU side is advised not to underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, unwavering will and strong capability to defend their sovereignty and territorial integrity and immediately cease all provocations and confrontational moves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1904112.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1904097.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The DPP authorities recently gathered personnel from the United States, Japan and other countries to hold a so-called security dialogue and made sweeping remarks about the situation in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above response in answering questions.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 2 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, stressed on the 2nd: Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!\nZhu Fenglian also said that the DPP authorities continue to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” and, hoping to rely on external forces to resist unification by force, they pose a serious threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, drive Taiwan's people toward disaster, and will only bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210902_12376021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 2 (electronic dispatch). Some media reported that the Foreign Affairs Committee of the European Parliament recently passed a report related to Taiwan that advocates for the EU to upgrade its relations with Taiwan. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 2nd: Our relevant departments have already expressed a stern position on this. The one-China principle is a recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The relevant committees and members of the European Parliament should abide by the one-China principle and correct the relevant erroneous words and deeds.\nShe also stated: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any attempt to win over or cling to external forces to pursue “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210902_12376022.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-03","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","This morning, just before Prime Minister Suga resigned in Japan, former Foreign Minister Kishida said \"Taiwan is at the frontline of the standoff between the US and China. Looking at the situation with Hong Kong and the Uyghurs, I have a strong feeling that the Taiwan Strait will be the next big problem\". Kishida is now the only candidate for the prime ministership in Japan. Do you have any comment on his remarks…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations. On the Taiwan question, the Japanese side bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people for its past crimes and should especially be prudent with its words and actions. We seriously urge relevant individual in Japan to refrain from interfering in China's internal affairs in any form and to refrain from sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1904576.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1904453.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, some opinion on the island holds that Tsai Ing-wen's statement that “Taiwan is willing to bear the responsibility of defending regional stability and hopes to coexist with neighboring countries on the principles of peace, stability and mutual benefit” refers to the mainland as a “neighboring country,” and in effect advocates the “two-state theory.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 3 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd in response to questions: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations. This is a fact that no one or force can change. The DPP authorities have floated remarks that smuggle in the “two-state theory” and have continuously engaged in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” This will only further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and bring profound disaster to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nShe also said: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that reckless provocations and evil conduct will surely invite the actions of justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210903_12376252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-07","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, Honduran presidential candidate for the left-wing Liberty and Refoundation Party Xiomara Castro said on September 6 that she would open diplomatic relations with China if she wins elections in November. Relevant Taiwan authorities in charge of foreign affairs issued a statement to warn Honduras against \"flashy and false\" promises by the mainland, adding that it is a usual trick to undermine…","There is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community. Following the one-China principle is the overriding trend with popular support. China welcomes all moves that endorse and support the one-China principle.\nWe solemnly warn the Taiwan authorities that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, “dollar diplomacy” is rejected by all, and attempts to reverse the historical trend by soliciting foreign support is bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1905278.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202109/t20210907_9604837.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-07","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","It is reported that think tanks in Taiwan said that the region should prioritize joining CPTPP, because if the mainland joins the trade pact first, it would obstruct Taiwan’s accession and its participation in regional trade integration. Do you have any comment?","The Taiwan region's participation in regional economic cooperation must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. We oppose the discussion and signing of agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature between any country and the Taiwan region. China’s position on this issue is clear and resolute.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1905278.shtml","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202109/t20210907_9604837.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 7 — Some media reported that a candidate for president of Honduras said that if elected, he would establish diplomatic relations with China, and the DPP authorities are using this to smear and attack the mainland. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response on the 7th: Our relevant departments have already stated our solemn position. The one-China principle is a generally recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. We hope relevant countries will handle the Taiwan question in accordance with the one-China principle.\nShe said that the DPP authorities, based on the political nature of “Taiwan independence,” distort right and wrong and deceive themselves and others, and their attempt to sow discord internationally is even more foolish and overreaching.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210907_12376919.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 8 — According to media reports, a Taiwan think tank has said that Taiwan should make joining the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) a priority. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 8th, in reply to a question, that relevant departments have already stated a solemn position on this. Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. We firmly oppose any agreement with sovereign implications and official nature between countries that have established diplomatic relations with China and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210908_12377111.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-09","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","It is reported that Japan's Deputy Defense Minister Yasuhide Nakayama said on September 8 that the distance between Taiwan and Japan is very close, like that between one's tip of nose and mouth. That's why Japan takes as its own business peace and stability in Taiwan and it's impossible to regard it as others' affairs, he said. Do you have any comment?","The remarks on Taiwan by the Japanese politician you mentioned are ludicrous. China strongly deplores and firmly rejects that and has lodged solemn representation with the Japanese side.\nJapan's militarists once used geographical proximity as the main excuse to wage wars of aggression. It is a very dangerous development that some in Japan are still touting this logic in the 21st century. We need to stay on high alert about this. On the Taiwan question, the Japanese side bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people for its past crimes and should especially be prudent with its words and actions. Japan should stop interfering in China's domestic affairs, avoid undermining China's sovereignty in any form and refrain from sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces in any form.\nI want to stress once again that the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. No one should underestimate the strong resolution, determination and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347118.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1905828.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-09","Zhao Lijian","NHK","First question, a new warship was commissioned by Taiwan today to strengthen \"defence\" against mainland forces. What is the foreign ministry's comment? Second question, the DPRK held a military parade today. What is your comment?","On your first question, I want to stress that the attempt of Taiwan separatist forces to confront the mainland militarily can lead nowhere.\nOn your second question, China and the DPRK are friendly close neighbors. China congratulates the DPRK on the 73rd anniversary of its founding, and wishes it new progress in all its endeavors.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347118.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1905828.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: regarding the Taiwanese entertainer Chang Chun-ning, who was recently questioned by netizens for “Taiwan independence,” Tsai Ing-wen said, “Banning someone and depriving them of their right to work because their remarks do not suit one’s own wishes is not only an infringement on individual rights, but also further highlights the difference between the two sides of the Strait in the values of…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 9 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 9th in response to a question: Some political forces and unscrupulous media on the island, with ulterior motives, have deliberately created incidents, attempting to obstruct the development of Taiwan entertainers on the mainland, undermine the atmosphere of cross-Strait cultural exchange, sow discord between compatriots on both sides, and worsen cross-Strait relations. We hope compatriots on both sides will open their eyes and more precisely recognize and oppose vicious conduct that drives a wedge between the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said that the relevant remarks by the DPP authorities are pure malicious slander and a diversion of attention. We have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation, and warmly welcome Taiwan performers to develop on the mainland. More and more Taiwan entertainers have already been and are participating in cross-Strait film and television production and variety shows, bringing many works and programs welcomed by audiences on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210909_12377317.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 9 — Regarding the captions on pictures for the “Double Ten” events released by the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities on the 8th, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated in response to questions on the 9th: The DPP authorities have recently staged repeated political farces that smuggle in “one China, one Taiwan” contraband, and are going further and further down the road of seeking “independence” and provoking confrontation. Playing such furtive political maneuvers cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. It will only endanger peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nShe also said that the motherland must be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified. No “Taiwan independence” scheme can succeed; any such scheme will only be thoroughly crushed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210909_12377327.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-10","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","The head of Taiwan's so-called foreign affairs department Joseph Wu wrote that China's mainland has pressured the UN and its agencies to exclude Taiwan by misusing and misinterpreting the Resolution 2758 (XXVI) adopted by the UN General Assembly in 1971 as a legal basis. He added that only Taiwan's democratically elected government can represent its people on the international stage. Do you have any response to that?","What Joseph Wu said is purely \"Taiwan independence\" remarks. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China's representation at the UN certainly includes Taiwan. On the issue of the Taiwan region's participation in activities of international organizations, China's position is consistent and clear. It must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is an important principle established by UNGA Resolution 2758. This Resolution has already recognized the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations in political, legal and procedural sense, so there is no such issue of \"misusing and misinterpreting\" whatsoever. We urge the DPP authorities to stop pushing for de jure independence and political manipulation, otherwise they are just inviting further humiliation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347119.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1906157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-10","Zhao Lijian","SCMP","President Biden said that the US side has no intention to change the one-China policy. Do you have any comment on this statement? Are you satisfied with it?","The Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. As President Xi stressed during the call, on the basis of respecting each other's core concerns and properly managing differences, China and the US should continue engagement and dialogue to advance coordination and cooperation to inject more positive dynamics into the relationship. President Biden said during the phone call that the US side has no intention to change the one-China policy.\n******\nToday is Teacher's Day in China. Respecting teachers and valuing education is a fine tradition of the Chinese nation. Students will always be grateful to their teachers and keep with them the guidance wherever they go. To all teachers: Happy Teacher's Day!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347119.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1906157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-13","Zhao Lijian","Pheonix TV","First, North Korea announced on September 13 that it carried out tests of long-range cruise missile over the weekend. The United States said the missile tests posed “threats” to the country’s neighbours and beyond. Do you have any comment? Second, US media reports said the Biden administration is \"seriously considering\" to allow Taiwan to change the name of the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office…","On your first question, China remains committed to maintaining peace and stability on the Peninsula and holds that the issue should be settled through dialogue and negotiation. We call on relevant parties to exercise restraint, meet each other half way, actively conduct dialogue and engagement, and follow the “dual-track” approach and take phased and synchronized actions to continuously advance the political settlement of the Korean Peninsula issue.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue at the core of China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of bilateral relations. In the China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, the US unequivocally that “the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan”. In his phone call with President Xi Jinping, President Biden said that the US has no intention to change the one-China policy. China has lodged solemn representation with the US side in terms of the above-mentioned issue reported by the media. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor its commitments with concrete actions, stop all forms of official exchanges with Taiwan, and stop elevating substantive relations with Taiwan. This should include refrain from renaming the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the US as “Taiwan Representative Office”, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The US side should handle the Taiwan question in a prudent manner, lest it should seriously undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1906650.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1906645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 13 (electronic dispatch): Some media have reported that the United States is considering allowing the DPP authorities to rename their institutions in the United States. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 13th, saying that our relevant departments have already expressed our position and attitude on this matter. Taiwan is part of China, and we firmly oppose Taiwan region of China developing any form of official relations or establishing reciprocal official institutions with countries that have diplomatic ties with China.\nShe also said that no matter what tricks the DPP authorities play in pursuing \"Taiwan independence,\" they are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210913_12378056.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on September 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first introduced cross-Strait civil exchanges during the summer vacation, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Affected by multiple factors, cross-Strait personnel exchanges have not yet returned to normal. During the summer vacation that just passed, I believe you journalist friends were very busy, because you witnessed a kind of enthusiasm and a kind of perseverance. Whether it is the COVID-19 pandemic or man-made obstruction on the island, none has been able to stop cross-Strait civil exchanges from continuing to advance. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait overcame all kinds of difficulties, and while doing good epidemic prevention and control, held a series of exchange activities rich in content and diverse in form through methods combining online and offline, presenting new characteristics very different from previous years.\nFirst characteristic: cross-Strait youth became the main body of summer exchange activities. During the summer vacation, large numbers of Taiwan students and young people studying and working on the mainland enthusiastically took part in cross-Strait exchange activities held in various places. The 4th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum held in Zhejiang in July had more than 350 participants. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee Political Bureau and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, sent a congratulatory letter encouraging cross-Strait youth to have more contact, more frequent exchanges, and deeper interaction, and hoping that Taiwan youth will see the trend of history clearly, shoulder the mission of the era, and contribute to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. On the occasion of the Qixi Festival, the All-China Youth Federation took the lead in holding the “Strait Youth Qiqiao Folk Festival” activity, with online participation exceeding 5.5 million person-times. The 18th Thousand-Person Summer Camp for Taiwan Compatriot Youth, held by the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, was held in more than 20 provinces, with more than 500 Taiwan youth participating. The Cross-Strait Youth Exchange and Cooperation Summit held in Beijing covered 35 series of activities, and the number of online viewers of the opening ceremony exceeded 10 million person-times.\nSecond characteristic: cross-Strait cultural exchange activities are colorful and varied. Carrying out cross-Strait exchange activities themed on inheriting and promoting excellent traditional Chinese culture was a major feature of this year's summer exchanges. Sichuan held the “Cross-Strait Bashu Culture and Art Season,” including the Cross-Strait Public Art Graduation Works Exhibition, the Cross-Strait University Original Art Seminar, and other activities. A ceremony commemorating Great Yu's birthday and a public sacrifice to Fuxi were held in Beichuan in connection with Taiwan, to deepen spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides. The “5th Cross-Strait Yue Fei Culture Summer Camp” held in Chongqing and other places attracted more than 1,300 teachers and students from 15 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, and 217 teachers and students from Taiwan and its region, who together inherited the Yue Fei story and carried forward the national spirit. The “Taiwan Youth Students Hui Culture Summer Camp” held in Anhui had cross-Strait youth together visit the former residence of Liu Mingchuan, to feel the inseparable historical kinship across the Strait. The 12th Cross-Strait Film Festival was held simultaneously in Beijing and Taipei; five Taiwan films including 《秋决》 were screened in Beijing, and five mainland films including 《东北虎》 were screened in Taipei.\nThird characteristic: exchange activities cover a wide range of themes and feature innovative methods. Various localities organized exchange activities such as study-tour experiences, sports exchanges, and physical construction competitions in a way that combines online and offline. Sichuan held “We Came from the Yangtze River — the 11th Taiwan Students Tianfu Summer Camp and Yangtze River Ecology Study Camp,” which, through study-tour experiences, site visits, and interactive exchanges, deepened Taiwan students' understanding of the results of ecological governance, protection and development in the Yangtze River basin. The Fujian Provincial Federation of Trade Unions and the Fujian Provincial Committee of the Zhi Gong Party held the “First Home — Province-Wide Fujian-Taiwan Workers' Sports Exchange Competition,” with 24 workers' teams and nearly 240 athletes competing, of whom nearly 100 were Taiwan workers' athletes. Fujian also held the 8th Cross-Strait University Student Physical Construction Competition, which for the first time adopted a roadshow format of “main venue + live studio + remote video connection,” and teams from 9 mainland universities and 3 Taiwan universities entered the final.\nFourth characteristic: summer internships and social practice activities help Taiwan students grow. Many localities combined the theme practice of the Party history study and education campaign, “I Do Practical Things for the Masses,” to organize Taiwan students at mainland universities in summer internships and social practice activities. Jiangsu carried out the “I Help Taiwan Students Find Jobs” and “I Do Public Welfare with Taiwan Students” activities, arranging more than 500 Taiwan students to intern for over a month at well-known enterprises in technology, finance, media and other industries. Guangzhou held the “Building Dreams on the Pearl River, Spreading Wings to Fly — Taiwan University Student Internship Experience Activity,” in which 58 Taiwan university students from 8 universities carried out 60 days of internship training at 42 enterprises and public institutions. Shenzhen also organized nearly 70 Taiwan young people to intern at 38 enterprises. Sichuan held the Cross-Strait University Summer Youth Startup Workshop, and a food-street design proposal submitted by a team of Taiwan students was adopted by the local government. Shanghai, Fujian, Zhejiang, Jiangxi and other places also held summer social practice activities for Taiwan students in various forms.\nFifth characteristic: going to the grassroots and staying close to everyday life. In organizing cross-Strait exchange activities, many localities and units placed greater emphasis on going deep into the grassroots and on in-depth experience. Huaqiao University in Fujian organized Taiwan students to travel to Qianxinan Prefecture in Guizhou for study activities on the results of the poverty alleviation campaign. The Taiwan Affairs Office in Tibet invited Taiwan students from Tsinghua University and Peking University to go into grassroots communities and frontline Tibetan areas to understand the state's ethnic policies and the results of the poverty alleviation campaign. The Taiwan students said these activities gave them the opportunity to “measure the great mountains and rivers of the motherland with their own feet, and discover the nation's development achievements with their own eyes.”\nIt is worth mentioning that many Taiwan youth actively took part in various public welfare activities in local areas during the summer vacation. More than 70 Taiwan students from Nanjing University's School of Medicine and other universities participated in nucleic acid sampling work in local communities, with a cumulative total of nearly 800,000 sampling operations, making a positive contribution to epidemic prevention and control. More than 20 Taiwan youths took part in voluntary blood donation activities in Fuzhou City. Some Taiwan youth took the initiative to join flood relief and rescue work for the extraordinarily severe flood in Henan in late July.\nEntering September, some cross-Strait exchange activities are underway or about to begin. Chongqing is holding the “Commemorating the 110th Anniversary of the 1911 Revolution and Cross-Strait Youth Art Exhibition Activity” under the theme “Remember Xinhai, Paint Rivers and Mountains Together,” as well as the first “‘Chiyou Cup’ Cross-Strait Culture and Arts Festival.” The 2021 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival, under the theme “Blossoming Together, Lanterns Illuminating Both Sides of the Strait,” will be held from September 16 to October 15. Kunshan will also hold the Kunshan leg of the Cross-Strait All-People Baseball and Softball League in late October. The 8th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour will be held in 21 prefecture-level cities in Guangdong, with an opening ceremony in Guangzhou on September 24. In addition, submissions are currently being collected for the 4th Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Drone Aerial Photography Creative Competition, the Cross-Strait Youth Bashu Cultural and Creative Design Competition, and the 13th Cross-Strait Children's Art Exhibition, and young people from both sides are welcome to participate actively.\nComrade General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed, “Among people, what is valued is understanding each other's hearts,” and “No matter how many disturbances and obstacles are encountered, exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait must not stop, must not break, and must not diminish.” The internal driving force for cross-Strait relations to move forward comes from civil society and the grassroots. We encourage all sectors on both sides of the Strait to keep expanding and deepening exchanges, will actively create favorable conditions for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, promote deeper understanding and greater mutual trust among compatriots on both sides, unite hearts and efforts, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378625.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","On cross-Strait trade, Tsai Ing-wen said that the future goal is to break away from heavy dependence on mainland products and to make Taiwan’s trade partners and investment more diversified. What is your comment on this? Recently, what new characteristics have cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges shown, and what new progress can be expected in the future?","Since the beginning of this year, cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange cooperation has maintained a good momentum of development. Cross-Strait trade and investment have grown substantially, financial cooperation has continued to deepen, and enthusiasm for economic and trade exchanges has not waned. In summary, there has been progress in four areas:\nFirst, cross-Strait trade has grown substantially. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, from January to August this year, cross-Strait trade totaled US$208.82 billion, up 31.8% year on year. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$50.32 billion, up 33.4% year on year; mainland imports from Taiwan were US$158.5 billion, up 31.3% year on year. Since the beginning of this year, the growth rates of cross-Strait trade volume, mainland exports to Taiwan, and mainland imports from Taiwan have all exceeded 30%, showing that the momentum of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation continues to strengthen.\nSecond, Taiwanese investment in the mainland continues to grow. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from January to July this year, the mainland newly approved 3,552 Taiwan-funded projects, up 47% year on year; actual utilized Taiwan capital was US$640 million, up 9.6% year on year. Since the beginning of this year, the number of newly approved Taiwan-funded projects and the amount of Taiwan capital attracted have continued to grow substantially, fully demonstrating that Taiwanese businesses remain confident in the mainland's huge domestic market, complete industrial system, strong manufacturing capacity and broad development prospects.\nThird, cross-Strait financial cooperation continues to deepen. Changchun Yingli, Nanqiao Food, Huali Group and Dongya Machinery, four Taiwan-invested companies, listed on the A-share market this year, bringing the number of Taiwan-invested companies listed on the mainland A-share market to 42. Applications for listing by Zhongfu Circuit and Juxin Technology have been approved, and Shanghai Guanlong, Hefu Medical and others are actively applying for listing. Taipei Fubon Bank, Taichung Bank Securities Investment Trust, Kgi International (Hong Kong) and other Taiwan-funded financial institutions are also actively applying for Qualified Foreign Institutional Investor (QFII) status to participate in mainland securities market investment.\nFourth, enthusiasm for economic and trade exchanges among compatriots on both sides of the Strait has not waned. While ensuring normalized epidemic prevention and control, relevant provinces and cities have successively held the “Deepening Shandong-Taiwan Cooperation Promotion Meeting,” the Sichuan-Chongqing “Taiwan Enterprises Western Tour,” the “Yangtze River Delta Regional Project Promotion Conference and ‘Taiwan Businesspeople and Youth Come to Shanxi’,” the “2021 Haikou Taiwan Business Summit,” the “Taiwan Businesspeople and Enterprises Jilin Tour” and other activities, promoting the matching and implementation of a batch of projects that conform to the mainland's industrial development direction. Relevant mainland authorities have established the Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone in Hunan, building a platform for Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop in central China. Focusing on implementing the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” Sichuan, Jiangsu, Heilongjiang and other places have held policy promotion and experience-exchange activities to help Taiwan agricultural and forestry enterprises develop, supporting Taiwan farmers and enterprises in participating in the rural revitalization strategy and deepening agricultural and forestry exchange and cooperation with Taiwan.\nThe facts fully prove that the mainland has always been the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest and do business. Strengthening economic and trade cooperation across the Strait is the only way for Taiwan's economy to develop better and for Taiwan compatriots to benefit more. It is unwise and unworkable for the DPP authorities to repeatedly interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378620.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","On August 22, the New Party held its 28th anniversary celebration and firmly advocated peaceful reunification of the two sides. What is the spokesperson's comment?","In the 28 years since its founding, the New Party has firmly advocated peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait, resolutely opposed “Taiwan independence,” and supported “one country, two systems,” making positive contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. We are willing to work in solidarity and move forward together with all Taiwan political parties, groups, and individuals, including the New Party, that uphold the One China principle, support the reunification of the motherland, and oppose “Taiwan independence.” We will resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” schemes, firmly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly create a bright future for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378619.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau recently announced that, starting October 1, Taiwan compatriots holding Taiwan residence permits may participate in Beijing's urban and rural residents' basic old-age insurance. Some Taiwan compatriots said this policy resolves issues they have long cared about, such as double enrollment; the policy is flexible and thoughtful and will enhance the…","This policy issued by the Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau is a good and practical measure that refines and implements equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots. The Taiwan Residence Permit is an identity document issued to facilitate access to basic public services for Taiwan compatriots who work and live on the mainland. Relevant measures formulated in 2019 by the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security and the National Healthcare Security Administration provide that, to safeguard the equal social insurance rights that Taiwan compatriots enjoy on the mainland in accordance with law, both employed and unemployed Taiwan compatriots may hold a residence permit to participate in the local urban and rural residents' basic old-age insurance. After a Taiwan compatriot enrolls in insurance, if they leave the mainland before meeting the prescribed conditions for receiving a pension, they may either keep their account so they can continue making contributions when they next come to the mainland to work or live, or they may apply in writing to terminate their social insurance relationship and withdraw the balance of their personal social insurance account in a lump sum. Taiwan compatriots who are already insured in Taiwan may also, depending on their own circumstances, choose not to participate in the mainland's old-age and unemployment insurance. These flexible and pragmatic arrangements were all made by the competent mainland authorities on the basis of carefully listening to and actively studying the views of Taiwan compatriots. They fully reflect the mainland's relevant departments' continuous efforts to improve policy measures safeguarding the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, wholeheartedly doing practical things, good things and solving difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities have consistently harbored sinister motives toward the mainland's concern for and care of Taiwan compatriots. They readily attack and smear policies that benefit Taiwan and its people, and deliberately mislead and even threaten and intimidate the Taiwan public. This is in fact a very serious harm to the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said, “hope to coexist with neighboring countries under the principles of peace, stability, and mutual coexistence.” Some analysts or commentators believe the “neighboring country” Tsai refers to is the mainland. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment?","You may also have noticed that, on the one hand, they are making all sorts of petty moves, and on the other hand, the Mainland Affairs Council says it wants to promote positive interaction across the Strait. These words and deeds contradict each other.\nFirst, I must emphasize that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China, and the relationship between the two sides is not a relationship between two countries. This is a fact that no one or force can change. The DPP authorities put forward remarks laced with the “two-state theory” and continually engage in “independence”-seeking provocations. This will only further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and bring profound disaster to compatriots in Taiwan. Reckless provocations and evil conduct will surely invite righteous action.\nPromoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations is the mainstream public opinion on both sides. The key lies in both sides upholding the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle and is the political foundation of cross-strait relations. Only when the DPP authorities abandon their separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-strait relations return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council recently approved the establishment of a cross-Strait exchange base at the September 18 Historical Museum in Shenyang, Liaoning. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant details?","This year marks the 90th anniversary of the “September 18” Incident. Ninety years ago, Japanese imperialism launched the “September 18” Incident, which marked the beginning of its war of aggression against China. This period of national humiliation is a national wound that all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, should remember forever. Of the 82 cross-Strait exchange bases established so far, 12 have the history and culture of the War of Resistance as their theme, including the “September 18” History Museum, the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japan Memorial Hall, the Memorial Hall for Compatriots Killed in the Nanjing Massacre by Japanese Invaders, the Chongqing War of Resistance Relics Museum, Taierzhuang, the Kunming Southwest Associated University Museum, the Zhang Zizhong Memorial Hall, the Kunlun Pass Battle Site, Liyang Ancient Town, the Tengchong Martyrs' Cemetery, the Songshan War of Resistance Site, and Zhijiang County. Together they preliminarily cover relics or related memorial facilities for important events of the Chinese nation's War of Resistance against Japan from 1931 to 1945, a span of 14 years. These places record the heroic history of Chinese people's valiant resistance and carry the great spirit of the Chinese nation's War of Resistance. We hope compatriots on both sides, especially young friends, will visit these places to exchange, study and investigate, remember history, commemorate heroes, draw spiritual strength, and devote themselves to the great cause of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national rejuvenation.\nThe China Society for the History of the Anti-Japanese War and the Taiwan Chinese Nation Anti-Japanese War Memorial Association will hold the “Remembering History, Inheriting Aspirations: Cross-Strait Calligraphy and Painting Exhibition Commemorating the 90th Anniversary of the September 18 Incident” at the “September 18” History Museum from September 23 to October 23. The exhibition will display about 130 calligraphy and painting works on related themes created by well-known figures and calligraphers from both sides of the Strait. Relevant people from all sectors across the Strait will attend the opening ceremony of the exhibition and related events. Media friends are welcome to follow and report on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378624.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The Mainland Affairs Council announced its regular opinion poll on the 9th, claiming that 87.5% of Taiwan residents oppose “one country, two systems,” and more than 80% support defending so-called “national sovereignty” and “Taiwan democracy.” The Mainland Affairs Council claimed: “Most Taiwan public opinion opposes the mainland's political and military ‘pressure’ on Taiwan and endorses the Taiwan authorities'…","The DPP authorities have always been adept at fabricating so-called public opinion poll data in an attempt to deceive Taiwan society, and such data has absolutely no credibility. “Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. Peaceful reunification is the best way, and “one country, two systems” is the best plan. It fully embodies respect, understanding and care for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and conforms to the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and, for political self-interest, deliberately distort and vilify “one country, two systems,” with extremely sinister intentions, and such attempts will not succeed either. We believe the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will break through the veil of illusion and discern right from wrong.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, while the United States has reaffirmed that it has no intention of changing its One-China policy, it has repeatedly played the “Taiwan card.” It is brewing a plan to rename the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office” the “Taiwan Representative Office,” and it is encouraging Japan, Australia and some European countries to stir up trouble using the Taiwan question. At the same time, the DPP…","We firmly oppose the scheming “renaming” plot. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The One-China Principle is a broad consensus of the international community, a recognized basic norm of international relations, and the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. When China and the United States established diplomatic relations, the U.S. side made serious political commitments to China on the Taiwan question, and the U.S. side and Taiwan maintain only cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations. Engaging in Cold War mentality and zero-sum games, and using the Taiwan question to try to “use Taiwan to contain China” and curb China's development, are all in vain. Since the U.S. side has repeatedly stated that it has never intended to change its One-China policy, it should abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, fulfill its relevant commitments to the Chinese side through concrete actions, and stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces.\nThe DPP authorities, out of their “Taiwan independence” nature, disregard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the well-being of the Taiwan people, willingly serve as pawns of external forces, and keep playing “independence”-seeking tricks and provoking trouble internationally. This only severely damages peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and pushes the Taiwan people toward disaster. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how they collude with external forces or stage performances, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot stop the historical process of the inevitable reunification of the motherland. “Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history, and it is a dead end. No one should underestimate the firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378622.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","We see that Comirnaty (Pfizer-BioNTech) vaccines have arrived in Taiwan one after another, and soon people on the island will be able to get vaccinated smoothly. At the same time, many Taiwan compatriots who are already on the mainland have been vaccinated, and overseas Taiwan compatriots have also been vaccinated with the assistance of embassies and consulates. I would like you to introduce the situation and…","As of September 13, the mainland has administered more than 2.152 billion doses of COVID-19 vaccines. As of August 31, more than 156,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated, with more than 290,000 doses administered in total. Some localities, in accordance with the unified arrangements for local vaccination, have begun vaccinating Taiwan students on the mainland aged 12 to 17. On the mainland, no one will worry about not being able to get a vaccine; even compatriots overseas, including Taiwan compatriots, can receive priority access to domestically produced vaccines, with all who should be vaccinated being vaccinated, and all who are willing being vaccinated. At present, the \"Spring Seedling Action\" has helped thousands of overseas Taiwan compatriots get vaccinated with domestic or foreign vaccines in dozens of countries, including Thailand, Vietnam, Georgia, and Mauritius.\nWe also note that, even now, vaccines remain hard to obtain on the island of Taiwan. We have stated many times that we are willing to do our utmost to assist broad Taiwan compatriots in coping with the epidemic and to ensure that Taiwan compatriots have access to vaccines; this remains our greatest concern at present. We hope the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will no longer let politics override science, and will take practical action to protect the lives, health, and well-being of the Taiwan public, putting the interests of the Taiwan public first.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378623.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Japanese Deputy Minister of Defense Nakayama Yasuhide recently said that the Japan-China Treaty of Peace and Friendship is no longer suited to the times, and Japanese Diet member Sato Masahisa claimed that intelligence sharing between Taiwan and Japan in the Bashi Channel and the Miyako Strait is very important. What is the spokesperson’s comment on the increasing number of improper remarks about Taiwan emerging…","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no interference from any external force. Some Japanese politicians have successively made erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question, which we firmly oppose. Japan has historical debts to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question and especially needs to be prudent in its words and deeds. We urge the Japanese side to reflect deeply on history, immediately correct its mistakes, act in accordance with the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and stop all erroneous words and deeds concerning Taiwan. The DPP authorities’ attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","According to reports, the new session of Taiwan's legislature will continue to push so-called “constitutional amendment,” and the DPP's version of the draft amendment may also involve issues such as “lowering the threshold for constitutional amendment.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","We are following relevant developments closely and firmly oppose any form of “amending the constitution to seek independence,” and we will take resolute countermeasures. For some time, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, seeking to divert attention and pursue narrow political gain, have disregarded the expectations of the broad Taiwan compatriots for epidemic prevention and control, improving people's livelihood and well-being, and stabilizing and developing cross-Strait relations. They have persistently manipulated the so-called “constitutional amendment” issue, clamored “Taiwan independence” fallacies, and stirred up social antagonism. All responsible parties and individuals on the island should see clearly the political calculations and sinister intentions of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, refrain from following along or echoing them, and safeguard Taiwan Strait peace and stability and the well-being of Taiwan residents through concrete action. Broad Taiwan compatriots must also remain highly vigilant and oppose and resist all forms of “amending the constitution to seek independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378621.htm"],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声看台海新媒体记者","On September 14, the 76th session of the UN General Assembly convened at UN headquarters in New York, and the DPP authorities attempted to obtain support for joining the United Nations through their so-called “diplomatic allies.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is part of China and has absolutely no qualification to participate. The DPP authorities are hyping this opportunistically, aiming to pursue “Taiwan independence.” This is pure wishful thinking and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the so-called “Transitional Justice Commission” in Taiwan has planned to convert Taipei's Chiang Kai-shek Memorial Hall into a “Park for Reflecting on Authoritarian History” and remove the statue of 蒋介石, which has prompted questions from all sectors on the island. Some have proposed that the office of the Taiwan region's leader and the Taipei Guest House, which symbolize the authority of Japanese…","Everyone should note that many people on the island question the political intentions behind these actions. Any scheme that promotes “de-Sinicization” to serve “Taiwan independence,” or that misleads Taiwan residents with the “imperial subject” (皇民) historical view or the “Taiwan independence” historical view, will inevitably be jointly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","First question: The Kuomintang recently proposed the possibility of Ma Ying-jeou visiting the mainland, and Chiang Chi-chen said Ma Ying-jeou is currently the most suitable candidate to serve as “cross-Strait envoy.” What is the mainland side’s attitude toward this? Second question: As the BNT vaccine arrives in Taiwan, more and more people on the island will get vaccinated with it. In the future, can the…","I will answer the first question first. Since 2005, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang have worked together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the common well-being of compatriots on both sides, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, earning broad recognition and support from compatriots on both sides and from the international community. Faced with the great changes unseen in a century and the complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait, and in keeping with the irreversible historical tide of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, the two parties should, on the basis of the existing common political foundation, maintain positive interaction, strengthen exchange and cooperation at all levels and in all fields, jointly seek peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, jointly benefit compatriots on both sides, and jointly create a bright future for national rejuvenation.\nOn the second question: we have heard some Taiwan compatriots say that, as the epidemic prevention situation changes, it may be possible to adjust measures for Taiwan compatriots who have been vaccinated and are coming to the mainland, such as shortening the quarantine period, and whether a third dose of vaccine is required. Epidemic prevention and control is still at a critical stage, and vigilance must not be relaxed in the slightest. On facilitating cross-border travel for vaccinated people and on the question of a third dose, decisions will be made according to the development of the epidemic and will abide by the unified deployment and arrangements for epidemic prevention and control work.\nOn the third question, this is indeed a new phenomenon. Using simplified characters, listening to mainland songs, watching mainland TV dramas and films, and speaking mainland slang have indeed become a trend among Taiwan youth. This fully shows that promoting exchanges among cross-Strait youth, whether online or offline, is an effective way for cross-Strait youth to increase mutual understanding. Although cross-Strait youth have grown up in different environments and do not all see the world in the same way, our roots are the same and our culture at heart is the same. As long as we show sufficient respect and tolerance, listen attentively, look attentively, and participate attentively, we will certainly be able to dispel unfamiliarity, move from knowing to understanding, and together shoulder the responsibilities of being young Chinese. We will, as always, create favorable conditions and support and promote exchanges for cross-Strait youth in all fields and at all levels, and we hope more Taiwan youth will view mainland development and progress objectively and gain a correct understanding of cross-Strait relations. At the same time, we also see that the various “de-Sinicization” manipulations by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have indeed misled some Taiwan youth's understanding of cross-Strait history and reality, and we hope compatriots on both sides can resolutely oppose and resist “de-Sinicization” and other “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","From the “Little S incident” to the Taiwanese entertainer “Chang Chun-ning incident,” some public opinion holds that Taiwan entertainers cannot work diligently and happily on the mainland. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s view? Who exactly should judge whether this entertainer is “Taiwan independence”? We note that in similar incidents, some Weibo bloggers have played a bad role. How will the mainland side…","The claim that “Taiwanese entertainers cannot work happily on the mainland” is completely untenable. We have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait cooperation and exchanges in the cultural field, and we warmly welcome Taiwanese performing artists to develop on the mainland, share opportunities, and realize their dreams. More and more Taiwanese entertainers have been and are participating in cross-Strait film and television production and variety shows, producing many works and programs popular with audiences on both sides. The potential and room for development are enormous.\nRecently, a series of online hype campaigns targeting Taiwanese entertainers developing normally on the mainland have occurred. Compatriots on both sides strongly suspect that certain political forces on the island deliberately stirred up trouble, in an attempt to disrupt and obstruct the normal development of Taiwanese performing artists on the mainland, undermine the atmosphere of cross-Strait people-to-people exchanges, sow discord between compatriots on both sides, and worsen cross-Strait relations. We hope and call on compatriots on both sides to remain highly vigilant, keep their eyes open, discern accurately, and not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","We understand that Taiwan's defense department recently submitted the “2022 Defense Budget,” NT$471.7 billion, a record high. In the so-called “2021 China Military Power Report,” the DPP authorities played up the mainland's “military threat,” claiming there are seven possible timings for the mainland to “attack Taiwan.” What comments does the spokesperson have?","Recently, the DPP authorities have been quite active in this regard. I want to emphasize two points. First, Taiwan is part of China, and all actions recently taken by the PLA are to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. They target external forces and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and are by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots. Second, the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces are colluding with external forces and continuously provoking “Taiwan independence,” which is the root cause of the current tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait area. People on both sides of the Strait are very clear about this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视记者","The Kuomintang chairperson election is about to take place. Among the candidates, is there anyone whose policies are more in line with the mainland’s positions?","The Kuomintang (KMT) has adhered to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposed \"Taiwan independence,\" and has played a positive role in advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. We hope that the KMT leadership will learn from history and take a broader, farsighted view. Starting from safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, we hope they will work with us to consolidate and deepen the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" maintain positive interaction, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, and jointly advance the development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait—pursuing peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for our compatriots, and national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Just now you introduced the many rich cross-Strait exchange activities over the summer. But we also see that internationally, Lithuania has been clamoring to set up a “Taiwan representative office,” and the United States is considering renaming its “representative office.” In addition, on the mainland internet there have been debates over whether some Taiwan entertainers are suspected of “Taiwan independence,”…","What you describe is indeed a reflection of the current complex and grave situation across the Taiwan Strait. We have repeatedly pointed out that the root cause of the complex and grave situation across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces continuously collude with external forces to engage in “independence” provocations, undermining the atmosphere and climate of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait feel this keenly and are deeply worried. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together: on the one hand, to resolutely oppose and curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and on the other hand, to continue promoting all forms of cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Reports indicate that some factories have halted production due to the current outbreak in Putian, Fujian. Fujian is one of the gathering places for Taiwan businesses. Have any Taiwan businesses or factories been affected?","We have been continuously in contact with the relevant departments and localities to understand the situation. As of September 15, we have not received any report of a confirmed case among Taiwan compatriots in Fujian. Screening for the related outbreak is still being intensified. We will continue to follow and understand the situation. We also hope everyone will cooperate with local epidemic prevention requirements and overcome this round of the epidemic as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻记者","The Taiwan-side council of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit recently completed a high-level re-election. What is the spokesperson's view?","The Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit is one of the most important civilian exchange and cooperation platforms across the Taiwan Strait. It has played a positive role in promoting economic exchange and cooperation and industrial integration and development across the Taiwan Strait. Economic integration and development across the Taiwan Strait is the general trend and the will of the people. We hope that under the leadership of Chairman Liu Zhaoxuan, the Taiwan side of the Summit will maintain the Summit's tradition of pragmatic cooperation, work in harmony and solidarity with the mainland side of the Summit, and lead cross-Strait entrepreneurs to uphold our national interests and grasp the trend of development, so as to make the pie of cross-Strait economic cooperation bigger and bigger, and enable compatriots on both sides of the Strait to enjoy ever better benefits and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Earlier, DPP legislators called for seizing the international “Taiwan-friendly wave” to promote renaming Taiwan’s overseas representative offices as “Taiwan.” We note that the international credit rating agencies Fitch and Moody’s recently used the designation “Chinese Taiwan” for Taiwan in their statements. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Taiwan is part of China, and we firmly oppose Taiwan region from developing any form of official relations or establishing official institutions with countries that have diplomatic ties with China. No matter what tricks the DPP authorities play or how they provoke with \"Taiwan independence,\" they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. In fact, more and more countries and institutions have recognized the sensitivity of the Taiwan issue and have adopted practices that respect the one-China principle and seek truth from facts, and we appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","日本NHK记者","In the “Han Kuang Exercise,” the DPP authorities imagined an “attack” from the mainland and conducted airborne landing training on a highway. What is the spokesperson's view?","Any act by the DPP authorities to pursue \"independence\" through force is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland has recently proposed common prosperity and third distribution, and has introduced measures in the entertainment and education-and-training industries. Many Taiwan businesspeople worry whether this will bring back the “big pot of rice” (egalitarianism). What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Common prosperity is an essential requirement of socialism, an important feature of Chinese-style modernization, and also the common expectation of the people. We encourage prosperity through diligent labor and innovation, and encourage prosperity leaders who work hard, operate legally, and dare to start businesses. We allow some people to get rich first, and let those who get rich first lead and help those who are behind. Realizing common prosperity requires building a basic institutional arrangement in which primary distribution, redistribution, and third distribution are coordinated and complementary. Third distribution is voluntary, not compulsory, and is absolutely not “robbing the rich to help the poor.” The state's tax policy will give appropriate incentives, playing a supplementary role in improving the distribution structure through charitable donations and other means.\nFor many years, many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises have invested and started businesses on the mainland, and while growing and developing, they have fulfilled their social responsibilities, enthusiastically participated in various public welfare undertakings on the mainland. This embodies the traditional virtues of the Chinese people of mutual help and kindness, and we give them full encouragement and affirmation.\nThe Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. Here, on behalf of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, I extend holiday greetings to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, wishing compatriots on both sides a happy festival, a bright moon and a reunited family, with everything going well. We also send special greetings to compatriots who, due to the epidemic and other factors, are living separately across the Strait and unable to reunite, and we hope that through everyone's joint efforts, families can be reunited and both sides of the Strait can be united in heart as soon as possible. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210915_12378616.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210915_12378618.htm"],[0,"2021-09-16","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","First question. Slovenian Prime Minister, whose country holds the EU presidency, criticized China for expelling the Lithuanian ambassador in a letter to fellow EU leaders. He wrote that these measures have hurt China-EU ties and called for unity among countries to oppose the threat from China on any member state. Do you have any comment? Second question, Indian media reported that the country is set to…","On your first question. The ins and outs of the Taiwan-related issues on the part of Lithuania are very clear. The responsibility rests solely with the Lithuanian side. China urges Slovenia and the EU to take correct and objective positions on Taiwan-related issues and not to make excuses to create new troubles in China-EU relations. The Slovenian side should be keenly aware of the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle, handle Taiwan-related issues cautiously and prudently and avoid creating unnecessary disturbances to China-Slovenia relations.\nOn your second question. Maintaining peace, security and stability in South Asia meets the common interests of all, where China hopes that all parities would make constructive efforts. As for whether India can develop ballistic missiles capable of delivering nuclear weapons, the UNSCR 1172 already has clear stipulations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202109/t20210916_9721334.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1907464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-16","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Two questions. First, according to a German foreign ministry spokesperson, China denied a German warship entry into a local harbor. I was wondering if you have any comment on this? Second, Taiwan on Thursday proposed extra defense spending of nearly $9 billion over the next five years, warning that China was a severe threat. Do you have any comment on that?","On your first question, thanks to the joint efforts of China and ASEAN countries, the situation in the South China Sea has remained generally stable. However, in recent years, in the name of safeguarding freedom of navigation, certain major country has frequently sent military vessels and aircraft to the South China Sea to flex muscles and stir up trouble, deliberately creating disputes on maritime issues. China is firmly resolved to safeguarding its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. We will continue to properly address differences with relevant countries through consultation and negotiation. We also hope that countries outside the region can respect the efforts of regional countries to safeguard peace and stability in the South China Sea and play a constructive role toward this end.\nChina attaches importance to its all-round comprehensive strategic partnership with Germany, including military-to-military cooperation. China is ready to conduct friendly exchanges on the basis of mutual respect and mutual trust and hopes relevant party can create a favorable condition for this.\nOn your second question, this is not a diplomatic issue. I want to stress that Taiwan is part of China. China must and will be reunified. This is the historical trend that can be held back by no one and no force. A word for the Taiwan authorities: Any attempt to seek independence and resist reunification with force is overestimating itself and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202109/t20210916_9721334.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1907464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-17","Zhao Lijian","NHK","I have two questions. The LDP presidential election in Japan kicked off today. The result would have a major impact on the candidate for the new Prime Minister of Japan. What is China's comment on this? The EU released the EU Strategy for Cooperation in the Indo-Pacific, which said it would strengthen economic relations with Taiwan, and enhance naval presence by EU Member States in the Indo-Pacific. What is…","Your first question is about Japan's internal affairs which China would not comment on.\nOn your second question. The Taiwan region's participation in regional economic cooperation must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. We firmly oppose the discussion and signing of agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature between any country and the Taiwan region. China's position on this issue is clear and resolute. As to the issue of non-regional countries sending vessels to the Asia-Pacific, China hopes that countries outside the region will respect the aspiration of countries in the region to maintain peace and stability and promote cooperation for development, and refrain from taking actions that could complicate the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1907901.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1907872.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-09-17","Zhao Lijian","TASS","I have a question about the joint statement of Australia-US ministerial consultations. It contains some remarks against China on issues related to the South China Sea, Xinjiang, Hong Kong, Taiwan, and other China-related issues. Does China have any comment on that?","China's position on the issues including the South China Sea, Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang is consistent and clear. The United States and Australia are complicit in deliberately smearing China, interfering in China's internal affairs and driving a wedge between regional countries for their own geopolitical gains. China deplores and firmly opposes this.\nFacts have proved that China is not only the main engine driving economic growth in the Asia-Pacific region, but also a staunch supporter of regional peace and stability. China's development is a growing force for world peace and good news for regional prosperity and development. China always believes that cooperation between countries should conform to the trend of peace and development of the times and help enhance mutual trust and cooperation among countries. It should not target any third party or harm its interests.\nThe US and Australia should follow the trend of the times, respect the common aspirations of countries in the region, discard the outdated Cold War zero-sum mentality and narrow-minded geopolitical perception, view China's development in a correct way, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs and making waves in the Asia-Pacific region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/t1907901.shtml","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/t1907872.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: according to reports, Slovenian Prime Minister recently wrote to the leaders of EU member states, making negative remarks about Taiwan. The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 17 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 17th in response to questions that Slovenia should earnestly fulfill the solemn commitments it made on the Taiwan question when establishing diplomatic relations with China, adhere to the one-China principle, and handle Taiwan-related matters prudently. The DPP authorities' attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.\nShe said that the relevant departments on our side have already made our solemn position clear. I want to stress again that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a generally recognized norm of international relations and a broad international consensus.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210917_12379232.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 17 — Recently, Wu Chao-hsieh took part via video in an event held in the United States by the \"Global Taiwan Research Center\" and spread \"Taiwan independence\" remarks. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to questions on the 17th: The \"Global Taiwan Research Center\" is a so-called \"think tank\" funded and in practice controlled by \"Taiwan independence\" forces, which has long peddled \"Taiwan independence\" positions under the guise of academic research. Wu Chao-hsieh and his kind are accustomed to swindling and posturing internationally, boasting of the so-called \"democratic achievements\" of Taiwan in order to deceive public opinion and collude with external anti-China forces. The \"Taiwan independence\" words and deeds of Wu Chao-hsieh and his kind keep piling up and will inevitably be settled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210917_12379233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, the United States, the United Kingdom, and Australia announced the establishment of a trilateral security partnership, emphasizing Taiwan's role in the Indo-Pacific. The United States and Australia issued a joint statement containing negative content related to Taiwan, and the DPP authorities expressed their thanks. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian responded as above in answering the…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 17 — In response to a question on the 17th, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that including China's Taiwan region in the so-called \"Indo-Pacific Strategy\" of the United States, Britain and Australia seriously interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, and damages peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nShe said that the announcement by the United States, Britain and Australia of the establishment of a military partnership and the deal to provide Australia with nuclear-powered submarine technology undermines regional peace and stability and runs counter to commitments made by the countries concerned within international mechanisms. This practice of exclusive, closed \"small circles\" that form military cliques and create confrontation is essentially a product of Cold War zero-sum thinking and geopolitical concepts; it goes against the trend of the times and is unpopular.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the remarks by the United States and Australia concerning Taiwan once again expose their long-standing wrong understanding of the Taiwan question and their insidious scheme of \"using Taiwan to contain China.\" There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affairs. Any words or deeds that use so-called \"democracy\" or \"meaningful participation in international affairs\" as a pretext to support Taiwan are serious interference in China's internal affairs. We urge the countries concerned to abide by the one-China principle and their solemn commitments to China in practice, and to be cautious in their words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues.\nZhu Fenglian stated that it must be pointed out that \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities are the greatest source of turmoil undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Crushing the \"Taiwan independence\" scheme is a necessary and just act to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Any external force that backs up and emboldens \"Taiwan independence\" forces is extremely dangerous. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop all \"Taiwan independence\" conduct and stop colluding with external forces. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm determination, strong will, and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity! Provoking trouble to seek independence will only lead to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210917_12379252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 18 — The European Parliament recently adopted the “New EU-China Strategy Report,” which contains negative content concerning Taiwan, and the DPP authorities have expressed gratitude for it. In response, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 18th, responding to questions, that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated.\nShe said that the reports recently adopted by the European Parliament and its relevant committees, insofar as they contain Taiwan-related content, violate the one-China principle commonly recognized by the international community and the solemn commitments the EU side made on the Taiwan question when China and the EU established diplomatic relations. They brutally interfere in China’s internal affairs, and we firmly oppose them. We urge the European Parliament and its relevant committees to be prudent in words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues and to stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.\nZhu Fenglian further pointed out that the DPP authorities should not misjudge the situation or miscalculate. Their attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210918_12379422.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: After the General Administration of Customs announced the suspension of imports of sugar apples and wax apples from Taiwan into the mainland, the DPP authorities accused the mainland of “political repression” and of harming the interests of Taiwan farmers. What comments do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above remarks in answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 22 (Electronic dispatch). Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 22nd, saying that this year, mainland customs have repeatedly intercepted the quarantine pest Dayang hip-striped mealybug in custard apples and wax apples imported from Taiwan, and in all cases took return or destruction measures in accordance with the law and promptly notified the Taiwan side. This pest endangers a variety of fruit and grain crops, and once introduced, would seriously threaten mainland agricultural and forestry production and ecological security. To prevent plant pest risks at the source, based on relevant mainland laws, regulations, and standards, the General Administration of Customs has decided to suspend imports of custard apples and wax apples from Taiwan starting September 20, 2021.\nShe said that since 2020, the mainland has repeatedly notified relevant Taiwan authorities of non-compliant fruit imports and reminded them to strengthen source control, but such situations have not improved. The temporary suspension of imports of custard apples and wax apples from Taiwan is to protect agricultural production, ecological security, and the vital interests of the people. It is scientific, reasonable, and entirely legitimate. The General Administration of Customs has notified the Taiwan side accordingly through the contact channel of the Cross-Strait Agricultural Products Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities have politicized the necessary suspension measures concerning agricultural production, ecological security, and the vital interests of the people, and have taken the opportunity to maliciously smear the mainland and incite cross-Strait antagonism. This is entirely with ulterior motives. It shows that they simply do not want to solve the problem and have no intention of considering Taiwan's farmers, and will only further harm the vital interests of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210922_12379985.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-23","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","Yesterday, the Taiwan authorities submitted application to join the CPTPP. Considering that China's mainland and the Taiwan region both acceded to the WTO, what is China's comment on the position of the Taiwan authorities?","There is only one China in the world, and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community. China firmly opposes all official interactions between Taiwan and any country, firmly rejects Taiwan's accession to any agreement or organization of official nature. China's position on this issue is clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202109/t20210923_9580315.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1909160.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: according to Taiwan media reports, the DPP authorities announced that they have formally submitted an application to join the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), and made absurd remarks about the mainland’s application to join the CPTPP. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above response when answering the question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 23 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian stated on the 23rd in response to questions: Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. We oppose the DPP authorities using economic and trade matters as a pretext to expand so-called “international space” and carry out activities aimed at “independence.” We hope that relevant countries will properly handle Taiwan-related matters and will not provide any convenience or platform for “Taiwan independence” conduct.\nShe said that our joining the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) is conducive to promoting the process of regional economic integration in the Asia-Pacific, and conducive to promoting the post-pandemic economic recovery, trade development and investment growth around the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210923_12380191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-27","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Can I clarify that China's position is that the release of Meng and the release of Kovrig and Spavor is entirely coincidental? And secondly, a British warship passed through the Taiwan Straits today. Do you have any comment on that?","We have stated many times that the Meng Wanzhou incident is completely different in essence from the cases of Michael Kovrig and Michael Spavor. Many media outlets, including those in Canada, pointed out that the Canadian side should not have done the dirty work for the US and should draw lessons. The groundless detention of Meng Wanzhou is a serious mistake made by the US and Canada, which they should have corrected long ago.\nAs to your second question, China's position is very clear. We hope some country can do more that helps to build mutual trust and truly safeguards regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347130.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1910167.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The results of the Kuomintang chairperson election were announced recently, and Chu Li-luan was elected. What is the spokesperson's comment on the election result? Second, what are the mainland side's plans for the next steps of exchanges between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party? Third, will the new Kuomintang chairperson be invited to visit, or will there be a high-level meeting between the two parties?","After Eric Chu was elected chairman of the Kuomintang (KMT), General Secretary Xi Jinping sent him a congratulatory message, and Eric Chu replied with thanks. Both sides reached positive consensus on increasing mutual trust, strengthening exchanges and cooperation, and promoting the development of cross-Strait relations on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” in order to benefit compatriots on both sides.\nWe noted that during this KMT chairman election, Eric Chu and the other three candidates, Chiang Chi-chen, Chang Ya-chung and Cho Po-yuan, all made positive statements on adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” and developing relations between the two parties and across the Strait. They stated that compatriots on both sides belong to the Chinese nation, that we must defend the Chinese historical view and oppose the “Taiwan independence” historical view, and that cross-Strait dialogue must be restarted quickly on the basis of cross-Strait consensus, with cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation resumed and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait maintained. We appreciate this.\nAt present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and all Chinese people must unite and move forward together. We hope the Kuomintang will work with us to uphold the common political foundation, adhere to national righteousness, cooperate with determination, seek well-being for compatriots, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek reunification for the country, and seek rejuvenation for the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381862.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently the General Administration of Customs issued a notice stating that quarantine pests were repeatedly detected in sugar apples and wax apples imported into the mainland from Taiwan, and announced the suspension of imports of sugar apples and wax apples from Taiwan. The DPP authorities accused the mainland of “political suppression” and of “harming the interests of Taiwan farmers.” What is your comment on this?","Since the beginning of this year, mainland customs has on multiple occasions intercepted the quarantine pest dayang buttock-striped mealybug (大洋臀纹粉蚧) in custard apples and wax apples imported from the Taiwan region, and in each case has taken return or destruction measures in accordance with law and promptly notified the Taiwan side. This pest endangers many fruit and grain crops and poses a serious threat to agricultural and forestry production and ecological security. According to customs, besides the dayang buttock-striped mealybug, pests including cacao flower gall pathogen (可可花瘿病菌) and the new pineapple grey mealybug (新菠萝灰粉蚧) were also detected in custard apples and wax apples imported from Taiwan. To prevent plant epidemic risks at their source, and in accordance with relevant mainland laws, regulations and standards, the General Administration of Customs has decided to suspend imports of custard apples and wax apples from the Taiwan region into the mainland, effective September 20, 2021.\nSince 2020, the mainland side has repeatedly notified the relevant Taiwan side of non-compliant imported fruit and urged it to strengthen control at the source, but such situations have never improved. To protect agricultural production, ecological security and the vital interests of the public, the suspension of imports of custard apples and wax apples from the Taiwan region is scientific, reasonable and entirely legitimate. The General Administration of Customs has notified the Taiwan side accordingly through the liaison channel of the Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement. The DPP authorities politicize a necessary suspension measure that concerns agricultural production, ecological security and the vital interests of the public, and take the opportunity to maliciously smear the mainland and incite cross-Strait confrontation. This is entirely with ulterior motives and shows that they have no real intention of solving the problem and no willingness at all to consider Taiwan farmers. They will only further harm the vital interests of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381861.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities claimed that the mainland's suspension of imports of Taiwan's sugar apples and wax apples is \"undermining international trade rules,\" and threatened to file a complaint with the WTO. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and affairs across the Taiwan Strait are internal affairs handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities are precisely their long-standing political manipulation aimed at seeking “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381860.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","In response to outside questions about New Zealand also banning imports of Taiwan lychees and mangoes, why does Taiwan not file a complaint with the WTO? Taiwan's Council of Agriculture said that after the problems arose in New Zealand, it has continued to consult with Taiwan, but the mainland has never responded to Taiwan's requests and has demanded that the mainland resolve the quarantine issue. What is the…","As I said just now, since 2020 the mainland side has repeatedly notified the relevant Taiwan authorities of non-compliant fruit imports and reminded them to strengthen source control, but such problems have persisted without improvement. The General Administration of Customs has notified the Taiwan side through the contact channel under the Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement. Regarding custard apples (番荔枝), the mainland notified Taiwan in writing of 13 batches of non-compliant custard apples: 11 batches had Pacific mealybug (大洋臀纹粉蚧), 1 batch had Pacific mealybug and cacao flower-gall pathogen (可可花瘿病菌), and 1 batch had gray pineapple mealybug (新菠萝灰粉蚧). (The spokesperson displayed pictures of the detected pests on the on-site large screen.) The Taiwan side provided feedback on these problems but did not effectively rectify them, so the risk of pest introduction cannot be effectively reduced. Regarding wax apples (莲雾), the mainland notified Taiwan in writing of 6 batches of non-compliant wax apples: 5 batches had Pacific mealybug and 1 batch had gray pineapple mealybug. The Taiwan side has not provided any feedback on these problems. The facts show that the DPP authorities should earnestly fulfill their regulatory responsibility, resolve the problems at their source, and stop engaging in political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381857.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","After the mainland announced its application to join the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), the DPP authorities also submitted an application on the 22nd of this month. Some analysts believe that in order to join the CPTPP, the DPP authorities, ignoring opposition from the Taiwan public, may lift restrictions on imports of food from Fukushima Prefecture, the site of the…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Chinese Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. We oppose Taiwan's participation in any free trade arrangement of an official nature or the signing of any free trade agreement of an official nature.\nWe also note that most Taiwan residents are unwilling and unable to accept imports of food with problematic hazards at the cost of their health. The DPP authorities, in pursuit of partisan political interests, have repeatedly sold out the health interests of Taiwan residents, which will inevitably cause them to lose popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","Foreign media reported that the U.S. House of Representatives passed the “FY2022 National Defense Authorization Act,” which proposes inviting Taiwan to participate in the 2022 U.S. “RIMPAC” exercise, and also calls for strengthening cooperation between the U.S. National Guard and Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We firmly oppose the US Congress promoting and deliberating bills containing content related to Taiwan. Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair; the US government and the US Congress have no right to interfere. The DPP authorities must not misjudge the situation. Any attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” will end in failure. Our determination to curb “Taiwan independence” and to curb collusion between Taiwan and the United States is not just empty talk.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381859.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 13th \"Chongqing·Taiwan Week\" was recently held in Chongqing. Could you please introduce the relevant situation?","On September 27, the 13th “Chongqing·Taiwan Week” opened in Chongqing. Under the theme “Sharing New Opportunities, Integrating into the New Development Pattern,” this year’s event focuses on deepening grassroots engagement, economic and trade cooperation, and people-to-people exchange. Guo Jinlong, mainland chairman of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, Tang Liangzhi, Mayor of Chongqing, and relevant officials of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises attended the opening ceremony and delivered speeches. Liu Zhaoxuan, newly elected Taiwan-side chairman of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, delivered a video address. More than 800 guests from both sides of the Strait participated online and in person. The event fully reflected the positive willingness of Taiwan businesses and enterprises to be optimistic about the mainland’s development prospects and actively integrate into the new development pattern, especially participation in the construction of the Chengdu-Chongqing dual-city economic circle, and will further deepen economic, cultural, and cooperative exchanges and integrated development between Chongqing and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","In order to help more Taiwan compatriots start businesses and find jobs better on the mainland, the mainland has successively introduced a series of policy measures in recent years. Recently, Fujian issued the “Notice on Directly Recognizing Social Worker Certificates Issued in the Taiwan Region,” and I would like the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation.","Since the “31 Measures” were issued more than two years ago, 5,661 Taiwan compatriots have obtained professional qualifications for skilled personnel in Fujian. Fujian Province's introduction of a policy to directly recognize the social worker certificates issued in Taiwan is a concrete measure to thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech during his inspection of Fujian and to actively promote cross-Strait integration through exchanges, benefits and shared feelings. Social work is highly specialized and wide in scope, involving many groups such as the elderly, women, children, young people and persons with disabilities, and many fields such as social assistance, poverty alleviation and relief, medical and health care, staff assistance, drug prevention and education, and judicial rehabilitation. Following the principles of “similar structural framework, comparable examination requirements, similar professional management requirements, and urgent need for industrial development,” Fujian Province has standardized the direct recognition of Taiwan social worker certificates. This provides convenience for Taiwan social workers to work in Fujian and has a positive effect on deepening cross-Strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","A follow-up on the mainland’s suspension of imports of sugar apples and wax apples from the Taiwan region. Some commentary says that the DPP authorities have not engaged in self-reflection, and their first reaction was to “pass the buck” to the mainland, claiming that “the mainland is bullying Taiwan’s farmers.” At the same time, we have also noted that public opinion on the island questions whether the DPP…","For many years, the mainland has attached great importance to the interests and well-being of Taiwan farmers and has actively taken measures to address their concerns and help them expand into the mainland market. On March 17 this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with ten departments including the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and the National Forestry and Grassland Administration, issued the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” to further provide equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises participating in high-quality development of agriculture and forestry and rural revitalization on the mainland, and to create more development opportunities.\nThe mainland's temporary suspension of imports of sugar apples and wax apples from the Taiwan region is intended to protect agricultural production, ecological security and the vital interests of the public. It is scientific, reasonable and entirely justified. The DPP authorities have politicized a necessary suspension measure and maliciously smeared the mainland, showing no consideration at all for Taiwan's farmers. Their intention is to incite emotions among compatriots on the island and create cross-Strait confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Lithuania recently announced that it will donate AstraZeneca vaccines to Taiwan for a second time, and the DPP authorities expressed thanks. Some media reported that Lithuania’s health minister said the country is not very welcoming of this vaccine, so it can be donated away. Taiwan residents remarked, “You discard it, I pick it up, Taiwan can help.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","In fighting the COVID-19 epidemic, we have always adhered to the development philosophy centered on the people, and have taken safeguarding the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as our guiding principle. We treat Taiwan compatriots equally and are willing to share the mainland's epidemic-fighting achievements and vaccines with Taiwan compatriots. We have also broadly carried out the \"Spring Seedling Action\" overseas, so that as many overseas compatriots as possible, including Taiwan compatriots, can have access to vaccines.\nThe demand of the broad Taiwan compatriots for safe, reliable and sufficient vaccines is entirely a reasonable demand concerning health and well-being. The DPP authorities' various practices on the vaccine issue are entirely political manipulation for the sake of partisan self-interest.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381858.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Xie Zhiwei, the Taiwan authorities' so-called “representative to Germany,” recently claimed falsely that one of the most noteworthy focal points of Germany's new government is its “China policy,” which is closely tied to the “Taiwan issue.” He asserted that the world should have long ago abandoned the “one-China policy” and replaced it with a “China policy,” paired with a “Taiwan policy.” What is the…","Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose anyone creating “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” in any way. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces keep playing with “Taiwan independence” rhetoric and engaging in various schemes to seek “independence,” but they cannot shake the one-China principle or the international community's one-China framework.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《台海之声》和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the Hong Kong SAR Government reminded citizens not to use so-called “Double Ten” activities to split the country. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said, “We hope Hong Kong will face the historical facts of the 1911 Revolution.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We firmly support the HKSAR government in administering in accordance with the law, and we resolutely thwart the “Taiwan independence” forces' schemes to create chaos in Hong Kong and seek “independence.” The DPP authorities have long meddled in Hong Kong affairs, creating chaos and seeking “independence.” Their crimes have accumulated, and they will inevitably be held to account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The British Navy posted on Twitter on the 27th, hyping that the frigate HMS Richmond transited the Taiwan Strait and conducted sea and air drills. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this?","The Eastern Theater Command has already expressed a stern position on this. The PLA Eastern Theater Command has organized sea and air forces to conduct full-process shadowing and vigilance. Relevant countries should properly handle Taiwan-related issues and not do anything that is detrimental to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","According to media reports, a French Senate delegation plans to slip into Taiwan in October, and the DPP authorities' foreign affairs department has said it welcomes this. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' collusion with external forces to seek “Taiwan independence” will not succeed, and they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","After the epidemic broke out in Fujian this month, many Taiwan compatriots have been active on the front lines of epidemic prevention and control, fighting the epidemic side by side with mainland compatriots. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","After the outbreak of the epidemic in Fujian in early September, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Fujian participated in epidemic response work in various ways, contributing love and strength, demonstrating the blood-is-thicker-than-water kinship and mutual support between compatriots on both sides. This can be summarized in three aspects:\nFirst, Taiwan-funded enterprise associations in Fujian acted swiftly. Eleven Taiwan-invested enterprise associations, including those in all prefecture-level cities of the province and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, jointly issued a \"Letter to Taiwan Compatriots and Taiwan Enterprises in Fujian,\" calling on all Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in Fujian to overcome difficulties together and win the battle of epidemic prevention and control hand in hand. Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in Xiamen have cumulatively donated more than RMB 12 million in money and goods, and those in Putian have donated more than RMB 3.2 million.\nSecond, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises were active on the front line of the fight against the epidemic, guarding their homes together with local residents. In Xiamen, many Taiwan compatriots took part as volunteers in community nucleic acid testing registration, personnel guidance and other work, including Taiwanese \"couple teams,\" whole families mobilized together, and Taiwan youths and students. In Putian, after Edinburgh Friendship Hospital was designated as a centralized medical observation site, four Taiwan medical staff at the hospital quickly set up a medical team and established care workflows. Taiwan businesspeople on Meizhou Island delivered hot \"love meals\" to medical staff, police officers and volunteers on the front line of epidemic prevention. In Quanzhou, the Taiwan medical team at Yihe Hospital took the initiative to take on the important task of nucleic acid testing. Entrepreneurial Taiwan youths in Nan'an teamed up with public welfare organizations to donate 1,000 cartons of herbal cooling drinks to support front-line epidemic prevention personnel. In Fuzhou, Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople put on volunteer \"red vests\" and went into communities to carry out epidemic prevention publicity. In Zhangzhou, the Taiwan Businesspeople Association organized Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to donate money and goods, distributed comfort items to children at centralized quarantine sites in the area, and provided medical workers taking part in epidemic prevention with sleeping bags, daily necessities and other supplies.\nThird, Taiwan musicians created songs against the epidemic, using music to convey the power of warmth. Taiwan musicians wrote lyrics and composed the song \"Xiamen Is Our Home\"; Taiwan compatriot teachers and students at Minnan Normal University co-created \"Light of the City\"; Taiwan compatriots and youths in Xiamen created \"Let Love Form a Circle\"; and Taiwan compatriots in Putian created the song \"Mazu\" and other anti-epidemic songs. These songs record the vivid moments of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youths joining hands with mainland compatriots to fight the epidemic, convey positive energy through music, and show the brotherly bond and heartfelt connection between compatriots on both sides.\nAs the song created by Taiwan compatriots against the epidemic sings, \"With your and my shared perseverance, everything will surely pass (Hokkien).\" We believe that with everyone's concerted cooperation, the epidemic will certainly recede as soon as possible, and we will meet in Fujian and jointly promote a new path of cross-Strait integration and development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210929_12381856.htm"],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","After Chu Li-lun was elected Chairman of the Kuomintang, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent him a congratulatory telegram, and Mr. Chu Li-lun replied by telegram to express thanks. The Mainland Affairs Council criticized Chu Li-lun for “catering to the CCP's position, ignoring the facts, and going against Taiwan public opinion.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment?","The “1992 Consensus” was reached through negotiations conducted by authorized representatives of relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, and it is the common political foundation for cross-Strait negotiations and consultations. Advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” accords with the common aspirations and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, and it is the mainstream public opinion across the Strait. In the five years since the DPP came to power, it has distorted and denied the “1992 Consensus” and engaged in all sorts of “independence”-seeking activities, seriously violating the mainstream wishes of Taiwan residents and gravely harming their interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","First question: Recently, several places on the mainland have implemented power rationing, which has had a considerable impact on Taiwan businesses engaged in manufacturing in Guangdong, Jiangsu, Zhejiang and other places. How will local Taiwan Affairs Offices help these Taiwan businesses? Second question: After Zhu Lilun was elected chairman of the Kuomintang, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent him a…","On the first question, the State Grid Corporation of China and other major power companies have stated that they will go all out to win the battle to secure electricity supply and avoid power rationing to the greatest extent possible.\nOn the second question, Mr. Chu Li-luan was elected Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang. General Secretary Xi Jinping sent him a congratulatory message, and Mr. Chu Li-luan replied subsequently. The two sides reached a positive consensus to enhance mutual trust, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, promote the development of cross-Strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides on the common political basis of adhering to the ‘1992 Consensus’ and opposing ‘Taiwan independence.’\nRegarding the differences across the Strait, including long-standing political differences, we are willing to engage in equal consultation and dialogue, and seek solutions, with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals, including the Chinese Kuomintang, on the common political basis of adhering to the one-China principle and the ‘1992 Consensus’ and opposing ‘Taiwan independence.’","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","On the mainland's suspension of imports of certain Taiwan fruits. The Taiwan side hopes to consult with the mainland but has not been agreed to. Is the mainland considering seeking a solution through existing consultation mechanisms? An online joke once circulated saying that the spokesperson's name is the “code” for cross-Strait exchanges, especially in agriculture. Taiwan farmers are very worried and also want…","On the first question, I have already provided an explanation. Since last year, the mainland side has repeatedly notified the Taiwan region of the unqualified situations of various fruits imported from Taiwan into the mainland, and has reminded the Taiwan side to strengthen control at the source, but such situations have never been improved. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, on the one hand, claim to be willing to \"sit down and talk,\" while on the other hand, not only fail to take timely corrective measures, but instead politicize necessary measures concerning agricultural production, ecological security, and the immediate interests of the people, using them as opportunities to maliciously smear the mainland and incite cross-Strait antagonism. This is entirely with ulterior motives, and shows that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities simply do not want to solve the problem and have not the slightest intention of considering the interests of Taiwan farmers, and will only further harm the immediate interests of Taiwan people.\nRegarding the internet jokes you mentioned, I have also seen some of them. In fact, I hope my name can become a byword for praise of Taiwan's agricultural products, rather than, as it is now, a byword for criticism of Taiwan's agricultural products. We understand the concerns of Taiwan farmers. In fact, mainland consumers are also quite worried: what insects might come with fruits imported from Taiwan next? The crux of the problem lies in the fact that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have not effectively fulfilled their regulatory responsibilities and have not effectively reduced the risk of plant pests and diseases at the source, and are not considering the interests of Taiwan farmers and cross-Strait consumers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","First question: if the KMT intends to refer to and promote the “cross-Strait peace agreement” proposed by Ma Ying-jeou, how does the mainland view this? Second question: Taiwan farmers are now very worried that other fruits may be banned. Do you know whether the mainland customs has sent notices to the Taiwan side reminding it about other Taiwan fruits?","On the first question: The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces, colluding with external forces, continue to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” This is the root cause of undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and it is also the crux of what truly causes anxiety among Taiwan's people. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the essence and harm of “Taiwan independence,” and, starting from safeguarding their own security and well-being, join us in firmly crushing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to maintain positive interaction with the Kuomintang, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, and communicate and dialogue on issues concerning the security, interests, and well-being of Taiwan's people. Together we will promote the development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question, whether to temporarily suspend the import of other Taiwanese agricultural products into the mainland will be decided by the competent authorities in accordance with relevant mainland laws, regulations, and standards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Regarding Taiwan’s application to join the CPTPP: Taiwan is already a member of the WTO, APEC and other international economic and trade organizations. From the perspective of fair trade and mutually beneficial cooperation, could both sides of the Strait together contribute to the inclusive development of the Asia-Pacific regional economy? What is the spokesperson’s comment?","As I have already said, Chinese Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. It is precisely under the premise of the one-China principle that Chinese Taiwan was able to join the World Trade Organization in an appropriate name and capacity. Taiwan's accession to the WTO as a separate customs territory does not constitute a precedent for Taiwan joining regional free trade arrangements or negotiating bilateral free trade agreements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-09-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","First question: please introduce the relevant situation of the mainland's meeting this year marking the 110th anniversary of the 1911 Revolution. Second question: after the newsroom of the Taiwan Affairs Office was renovated, the backdrop was replaced with a world map. Outside observers speculate whether this means the mainland is gradually handling cross-strait relations within a larger framework that considers…","First question: The 1911 Revolution opened up the modern national democratic revolution in the full sense in China and explored a path for the development and progress of the Chinese nation. The aspiration of Dr. Sun Yat-sen and the pioneers of the 1911 Revolution to revitalize China should become a common pursuit of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hold commemorative activities for the 1911 Revolution every year and invite Taiwan compatriots to participate.\nSecond question: Our press briefing hall has been in use for many years. This time, during the summer recess, we carried out some renovation, with the greatest aim being to provide a better environment and service for reporters' questions and for live broadcasting by television, the internet and text transcripts. Thank you all for your attention, and we also welcome your comments and suggestions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202109/t20210929_12381853.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-09-30","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","French Senator Alain Richard will lead a French delegation visiting Taiwan soon. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this visit?","The one-China principle is the political foundation for China to develop friendly and cooperative relations with other countries, including France. China firmly opposes all forms of official contact and exchanges between certain French congressmen and the Taiwan authorities. We urge relevant individuals to abide by the one-China principle and safeguard the favorable environment for normal development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347134.html","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/t1911631.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-09-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Japan's Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi recently said that “Chinese military trends, including the rapid strengthening, increasing activity and expansion of its operational capabilities, combined with the lack of transparency regarding its defense policy and military capabilities, have become a strong security concern for Japan, the region and the international community”. He claimed that the Diaoyu Islands are…","Senior Japanese defense officials have repeatedly hyped up the so-called “China military threat”, grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs, and damaged China’s sovereignty. China deplores and firmly opposes that.\nChina is committed to the coordinated development of national defense and the economy. China’s defense expenditure is open and transparent, and its spending is reasonable and appropriate. For the past three decades, China’s defense expenditure as a percentage of GDP has remained below 2%, which is lower than that of other major countries and the world average of 2.6%. China's per capita military spending only accounts for one fifth of Japan’s. In contrast, Japan, instead of sincerely reflecting on its aggressive history, has kept increasing its defense budget to new records. It has also reinforced military forces on its southwestern islands and developed emerging combat forces such as the cyber force and space force, which far exceeds the needs of “exclusively defense-oriented strategy”. The Asian neighbors and the international community should be highly vigilant about what Japan is up to.\nThe Diaoyu Island and its affiliated islands are an inherent territory of China. This is a basic fact that cannot be changed no matter how Japan clamors. Japan should stop its provocations against China on the Diaoyu Islands issue, and stop confounding right and wrong and putting the blame on China.\nAt last, I want to emphasize that the Taiwan question is fully and completely an internal affair of China. It has nothing to do with Japan. The so-called “geographical proximity” is just an excuse used by Japanese politicians to meddle in Taiwan affairs. It is a gross interference in China’s internal affairs, which reminds us of Japan’s history of waging aggressive wars and colonizing other Asian countries. The Chinese side has a solemn message for the Japanese side that China today is not what it used to be. We will not allow any country to meddle in the Taiwan question by any means.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-10/09/content_4896379.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2021-09-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US House of Representatives recently passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2022”, which called China and Russia America’s primary threats. It also claimed that the Chinese mainland's \"threat of military force against Taiwan\" is contrary to the expectation of the peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question, and the US should continue to provide support to \"enhance…","The relevant US Act clings to the Cold War mentality, makes groundless hype about the so-called “China threat”, and grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs. China is firmly opposed to it. We’ve noticed that whenever budget and appropriation come into question, some American politicians will make a big fuss over China and exaggerate the non-existent “China threat”. This is an extremely irresponsible and dangerous move. In fact, it is exactly these self-serving politicians that pose threat to the US.\nThe US Act also encourages develop military ties between the US and Taiwan, which is a very dangerous move. The Taiwan question belongs to China’s internal affairs. It concerns China’s core interests and brooks no foreign interference. Chinese people will cherish China’s sovereign and territorial integrity like they cherish their eyes, and they will allow no sand in the eyes. If anyone dares to challenge China’s bottom line on the Taiwan question, the PLA will never agree with it and will resolutely defend China's sovereign and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/news/2021-10/09/content_4896379.htm","",0,1,1,""],[2,"2021-09-30","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 30 — On September 30, a spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council issued a statement on Wu Chao-hsu’s frenzied pursuit of “independence.” The full text of the statement is as follows:\nFor some time, stubborn “Taiwan independence” diehard Wu Chao-hsu has, on various occasions and in various ways, frantically spread “Taiwan independence” remarks, disregarding the fact and legal basis that Taiwan is part of China, and peddling internationally the lie that Taiwan is a “sovereign state.” He has ignored the basic norms of international relations, distorted and attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and openly challenged the one-China principle upheld by the international community. Under the banner of economic and trade cooperation, academic exchanges and other pretexts, he has collided with efforts to join the United Nations and other international organizations, their activities, and regional economic cooperation mechanisms. He has concealed the fact that “Taiwan independence” is the root cause of stirring up cross-Strait opposition and creating tension in the Taiwan Strait, fabricated so-called mainland “coercion,” and attempted to evade responsibility. Using so-called “democracy and freedom” as a pretext, he has deceived public opinion, colluded with international anti-China forces, and provided cover for separatist “independence” acts. Wu Chao-hsu’s above-mentioned “Taiwan independence” separatist acts are futile and will only add to his crimes.\nIt must be pointed out that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and has never been a country. No matter how Wu Chao-hsu and his ilk distort the facts and turn black into white, they cannot change the historical fact and legal basis that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China.\nThe one-China principle is a universally recognized consensus and a basic norm of international relations in the international community. This year marks the 50th anniversary of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. Resolution 2758, adopted by the 26th UN General Assembly on October 25, 1971, restored the lawful rights of the government of the People’s Republic of China at the United Nations and all its rights, and the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all of China. This resolution embodies the UN Charter and its purposes, and clearly, justly and thoroughly resolves the question of China’s representation at the UN politically, legally and procedurally. It marks the confirmation of the one-China principle in the most important and most universal intergovernmental international organization, the UN. At present, 180 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with the People’s Republic of China; they all recognize the one-China principle and have committed to handling Taiwan-related matters within the framework of one China.\nWu Chao-hsu and his ilk’s hopping around and clamoring for Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly (WHA), for accession to the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), and the like, are openly challenging the international community’s one-China principle. Taiwan region’s external exchanges and its participation in international organizations and regional economic cooperation mechanisms must be premised on the one-China principle. We firmly oppose Taiwan region developing any form of official relations with countries that have diplomatic ties with China, firmly oppose Taiwan region joining any agreement or organization of an official nature, and firmly oppose the DPP authorities’ use of economic and trade as a pretext for pursuing “independence” activities. We understand the thoughts and feelings of Taiwan compatriots about participating in international activities; as long as the one-China principle is upheld, proper arrangements can be made. But the attempt by a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists to pursue “independence” through “participation in international activities” is absolutely impossible.\nThe current tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations is entirely caused by the DPP authorities’ provocations in pursuit of “independence.” We continue to advance the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and we wholeheartedly do practical things, good deeds and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, because realizing unification by peaceful means is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and to the entire nation. But toward all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, we will certainly show no leniency. So-called mainland “coercion” is pure nonsense.\nWu Chao-hsu and his ilk constantly speak of so-called “democracy and freedom,” but the fact is that “Taiwan independence” forces are carrying out a “green terror” on the island, engaging in the suppression of dissidents and the muzzling of speech. Whether it is so-called “common values” or “shared ideals,” these are merely tricks of the “Taiwan independence” forces, which attempt to collude with external forces, serve as their pawns, willingly act as cannon fodder, and even tie the welfare of the broad compatriots on the island to the war chariot.\nEverything Wu Chao-hsu says and does revolves around one word, “independence,” and all his tricks come down to one word, “deception.” We solemnly warn Wu Chao-hsu and his ilk: unification is the right path, and “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Facing the historical trend of national rejuvenation and national reunification and the great righteousness of the nation, the various “Taiwan independence” forces are like grasshoppers after the autumn frost, and all their “Taiwan independence” remarks are no more than flies buzzing, “a few shrill cries, a few sobs.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202109/t20210930_12382313.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-08","Zhao Lijian","CRI","How does China see the recent meeting between Director Yang Jiechi and US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan? How do you envision China-US relations after the meeting?","This high-level meeting was constructive, and conducive to enhancing mutual understanding.\nDirector Yang Jiechi pointed out that whether China and the United States can handle their relations well bears on the fundamental interests of the two countries and two peoples, as well as the future of the world. When China and the United States cooperate, the two countries and the world will benefit; when China and the United States are in confrontation, the two countries and the world will suffer severely. The US side needs to have a deep understanding of the mutually beneficial nature of China-US relations and correctly understand China's domestic and foreign policies and strategic intentions. China opposes defining China-US relations as \"competitive\".\nChina attaches importance to the positive remarks on China-US relations made recently by US President Joe Biden, and has noticed that the US side said it has no intention of containing China's development, and does not seek a \"new Cold War\". China hopes the US side could adopt a rational and pragmatic China policy, and, together with China, respect each other's core interests and major concerns, and follow a path of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation.\nDirector Yang Jiechi expounded China's solemn position on issues related to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, Xizang and human rights as well as maritime issues, urging the US side to truly respect China's sovereignty, security and development interests, and stop using the above issues to interfere in China's internal affairs.\nThe two sides agreed to take action, following the spirit of the phone call between Chinese and US heads of state on September 10, strengthen strategic communication, properly manage differences, avoid conflict and confrontation, seek mutual benefits and win-win results, and work together to bring China-US relations back on the right track of sound and steady development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347135.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211008_9584076.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-08","Zhao Lijian","AFP","I have two questions. A Pentagon official has said that US Special Operations forces have been quietly training troops in Taiwan for months. How does Beijing react to this? The CIA has announced a new China-focused unit to counter alleged security threats from Beijing. How do you react to this?","On your first question, the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. China and the US established diplomatic relations on the premise of the three principles, namely, the US should sever \"diplomatic relations\" and abrogate the \"mutual defense treaty\" with the Taiwan authorities and withdraw US military forces from Taiwan. The US explicitly pledges in the China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations that it will \"maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan\". The US should fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of Taiwan-related issues and the gravely detrimental nature of relevant issues, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan to avoid seriously damaging China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China will take all necessary measures to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nOn your second question, this is a typical symptom of the Cold War mentality. Relevant US agency should view China's development and China-US relations in an objective and rational light and stop doing things detrimental to mutual trust and cooperation between China and the US and China's sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347135.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211008_9584076.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-08","Zhao Lijian","AFP","A French senator visiting Taipei has referred to Taiwan as a \"country\". How does Beijing view the visit by the French delegation to Taiwan?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Referring to Taiwan as a \"country\" is a flagrant violation of the consensus of the international community, France included. People like Alain Richard either lack basic respect for and knowledge of norms governing international relations, or attempt to hijack state-to-state relations out of selfish agenda. China expresses strong condemnation and firm opposition to this. We hope France can earnestly abide by the one-China principle and avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347135.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211008_9584076.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-08","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","US President Joe Biden said that he has spoken to Chinese President Xi Jinping about Taiwan and they agreed to abide by relevant agreement concerning the Taiwan question. Can you confirm that this was part of the conversation between the two sides?","China's position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. On the Taiwan question, the United States has made clear commitments to China. In his phone call with President Xi Jinping, President Biden made it clear that the United States has no intention to change the one-China policy. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, translate relevant commitments into concrete action, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, lest it should seriously damage China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nDuring his meeting with US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan in Zurich, Switzerland on October 6, Director Yang Jiechi once again expounded China's solemn position on issues related to Taiwan, urging the US side to truly respect China's sovereignty, security and development interests, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop using Taiwan-related issues to interfere in China's internal affairs. The US side expressed its adherence to the one-China policy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347135.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211008_9584076.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-08","Zhao Lijian","NHK","First question, on October 10 the Tsai Ing-wen authorities will hold a military drill. Do you have any comment? Second question, a large number of Chinese military aircraft entered the Taiwan authorities' so-called \"air defense identification zone\" this month. What's the purpose of this?","Neither of your questions is about foreign affairs. I would refer you to the competent departments.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347135.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211008_9584076.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 9 dispatch. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to a question on the 9th, said that the DPP authorities, scheming for “Taiwan independence” separatism, refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” collude with external forces to carry out provocations seeking “independence,” undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation,…","Ma Xiaoguang said: The “1992 Consensus” was reached through authorized negotiations between relevant parties on both sides of the Strait. It reflects the spirit of seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and of equal consultation on the basis of the one-China principle, and it is the common political foundation for cross-Strait negotiations. Advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” conforms to the common aspirations and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and is the mainstream public opinion across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211009_12383390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 9 dispatch. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the TAO, said in response to a question on the 9th that the DPP authorities have repeatedly made an issue of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, going to any lengths to pursue “independence.” This not only exposes their ignorance but also reflects their arrogance in attempting to challenge the basic norms of international relations,…","Ma Xiaoguang said there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, have clearly and unmistakably confirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. In 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly, by an overwhelming majority, adopted Resolution 2758, restoring the lawful rights of the government of the People’s Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. It thoroughly resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the question of China’s representation in the United Nations, including Taiwan.\nHe also stated that the United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states, and Taiwan is part of China and simply has no qualification to join. The question of Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211009_12383391.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 9 dispatch. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the TAO, said in response to a question on the 9th that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, colluding with external forces to frantically engage in provocations to seek “independence.” Their conduct harms the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, endangers their safety, and sells out the interests…","Ma Xiaoguang said that this year marks the 110th anniversary of the 1911 Revolution. Commemorating the historic achievements of Dr. Sun Yat-sen and other revolutionary pioneers and carrying forward their lofty spirit of unwavering devotion to revitalizing China is of great significance for rallying the powerful strength of Chinese people at home and abroad and for uniting in struggle to achieve the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the 1911 Revolution made a great and arduous exploration toward achieving national independence and liberation of the people, and is a milestone standing tall on the path of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The Communist Party of China is the most steadfast supporter, most loyal collaborator, and most faithful successor of Dr. Sun Yat-sen’s revolutionary cause. We have carried out Dr. Sun Yat-sen’s last wishes, realized and developed the great aspirations of the pioneers of the 1911 Revolution, completed the historic tasks of national independence and liberation of the people, and opened a new historical era of development and progress for the Chinese nation. The Chinese nation has ushered in the great leap from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong, and the process of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has entered an irreversible historical course. This earth-shaking, enormous historic achievement has made Chinese people at home and abroad immensely proud and has been unanimously recognized by peoples of all countries around the world.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that realizing national unification and the revitalization of China is the ardent expectation of Dr. Sun Yat-sen and the pioneers of the 1911 Revolution and their unfinished wish. Taiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of China; Taiwan’s future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. In the process of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared will of all Chinese people. This is an iron law of history and, even more, the justice of history.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities’ plotting of “independence” and provocations are the root cause of the current tense and turbulent cross-Strait relations and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and a counter-current, and has not the slightest connection with so-called “democracy and freedom.” History has already proven and will continue to prove that those who forget their ancestors, betray the motherland, and divide the country have never come to a good end, and will certainly be rejected by the people and judged by history.\nMa Xiaoguang concluded by saying that resolving the Taiwan question peacefully best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. On the basis of adhering to the One China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the mainstream public opinion of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We will continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots in upholding the great righteousness of the nation, stand on the right side of history, and jointly accomplish the historic mission of the complete reunification of the motherland. The Taiwan question arose because of national weakness and turmoil, and it will inevitably be resolved with national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211009_12383412.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 10 — In response to a question about the content concerning cross-strait relations in the so-called “speech” delivered by the leader of the DPP authorities on October 10, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that this “speech” advocates “Taiwan independence” and incites confrontation, fragments history and distorts facts, and, under the pretext of so-called “consensus and unity,” seeks to hijack Taiwan public opinion, colludes with external forces, and lends support to its provocations aimed at pursuing “independence.”\nHe said that Taiwan is part of China. Since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has never changed and cannot change; China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and division will never be permitted. The DPP authorities collude with external forces, rely on foreign backing to boost their own standing, recklessly seek “independence” and provoke, and constantly create incidents; their so-called “maintaining the status quo” is nothing more than an attempt to pull the wool over people's eyes and deceive the world. At present, the DPP authorities' pursuit of “independence” and provocations are the root cause of the tension and turmoil in cross-strait relations and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. Our efforts to strike at and contain “Taiwan independence” are directed at the reckless actions of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, and are by no means directed at the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities sow discord and confuse the public; they cannot deceive the people on the island or the international community.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that we advocate peaceful reunification; realizing the reunification of the motherland through peaceful means best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. We are willing to resolve differences across the Taiwan Strait on the basis of the one-China principle, promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation of cross-strait relations. The DPP authorities deny the “1992 Consensus,” undermining the basis for dialogue; by pursuing “independence” and division, they have closed the door to cross-strait dialogue. Isn't this changing the status quo! If this is called “goodwill,” then what would be called “malice”? If this is not “rash advance,” then what is “rash advance”?\nHe said that since coming to power, the DPP authorities have been incompetent in governance and the people's livelihoods have been a source of resentment, yet they indulge in creating ethnic conflict, dividing Taiwan society, vigorously carrying out a “green terror,” and frantically suppressing dissenters. Promoting “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence,” forcibly severing the flesh-and-blood ties between Taiwan compatriots and Chinese culture and the Chinese nation, has greatly harmed the fundamental interests of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. If such “Taiwan independence” populism is packaged as so-called “democracy and freedom,” and the so-called “Taiwan getting better and better” is boasted about, this greatly underestimates the intelligence of Taiwan's people.\nMa Xiaoguang said that realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of Chinese descendants at home and abroad, and the common will of the Chinese nation. Taiwan is the treasured island of the motherland; it is Taiwan of all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots, and its future is jointly determined by all Chinese people. The DPP authorities, begging for favor, colluding with external forces, stirring confrontation, rejecting reunification, scheming for “Taiwan independence,” and heading down a dead end, are nothing more than scheming for the narrow interests of one party. They cannot coerce the wishes of the 23 million people of Taiwan, and they cannot stop the great trend of historical development. The motherland must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. We are willing to work together with the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots in harmony and unity, moving forward together, to crush any “Taiwan independence” scheme and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211010_12383506.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-11","Zhao Lijian","Maucau Monthly","Former Australian Prime Minister Tony Abbott made inappropriate remarks about China on several occasions during his recent visit to Taiwan. What is China's response?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations. It is also the prerequisite and political foundation for the development of friendly relations between China and other countries. Relevant actions of certain Australian politician seriously violate the one-China principle and send a seriously wrong signal to the outside world. China is firmly opposed to this and has lodged solemn representations with the Australian side.\nThe remarks of certain Australian politician are completely confusing black and white and extremely absurd. Such remarks that incite confrontation, drum up the \"China threat theory\", grossly interfere in China's internal affairs and wantonly slander and smear China out of selfish political gain are immoral, irresponsible and find no support.\nWe urge relevant individuals in Australia to abandon the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, respect basic facts, view China and its development in an objective and rational way, and stop making irresponsible remarks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347136.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211011_9546532.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 11 dispatch — Recently, the U.S. Wall Street Journal and the UK's The Economist reported that the U.S. military has been secretly stationed in Taiwan for over a year, which island media have hyped. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to questions on the 11th, saying: We firmly oppose any form of military contact between Taiwan and the United States. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to properly handle the Taiwan question.\nHe also stated: We warn the DPP authorities that their attempts to collude with external forces to seek 'independence' and to 'resist unification by force' are a miscalculation, and they will not escape a failed end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211011_12383758.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-12","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","Recently, certain politician in Taiwan has made statements to foreign media to deliberately distort UNGA Resolution 2758, saying it doesn't decide the representation of Taiwan and doesn't even mention Taiwan. He even falsely claimed that invoking this resolution to block Taiwan from joining the United Nations is inappropriate, and Taiwan's participation in the international body is a shared aspiration of all its…","The remarks of the politician in Taiwan are just nonsense. China has made clear its position on the Taiwan-related issues concerning the UN General Assembly on multiple occasions. I would like to reiterate the following points:\nFirst, there is only one China in the world and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a basic fact recognized by the international community. Our position of adhering to the one-China principle will remain unchanged; our attitude of rejecting \"two Chinas\", \"one China, one Taiwan\" and \"Taiwan independence\" is not to be challenged, and our resolve of upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unswerving.\nSecond, the United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Resolution 2758 adopted by the General Assembly in 1971 has solved once and for all the issue of China's representation in the UN in political, legal and procedural terms. The system, agencies and the Secretariat of the UN should abide by the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758 when dealing with Taiwan-related affairs. As a province of China, Taiwan is not qualified to join the UN at all. Practice over the years fully shows that the UN and the vast number of its member states recognize that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and they fully respect China's exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan.\nThird, the UNGA Resolution 2758 embodies the legal facts recognized by the international community. It is there in black and white and allows no denial or distortion by the Taiwan authorities or anyone. \"Taiwan independence\" in all forms are doomed to fail. The moves of hyping up this issue by certain individual in Taiwan constitute a flagrant challenge and serious provocation of the one-China principle, and a blatant violation of the UNGA Resolution 2758. We firmly reject such typical \"Taiwan independence\" rhetoric which will garner no support in the world.\nWe believe that the just cause of the Chinese government and Chinese people to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity, oppose secession and achieve reunification will continue to win understanding and support of the UN and its member states.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347137.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211012_9546533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-13","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov said on October 12 that \"Russia, like the overwhelming majority of other countries, considers Taiwan to be part of the People's Republic of China. We have proceeded and will proceed from this premise in our foreign policy.\" Do you have any comment?","We highly appreciate Foreign Minister Lavrov's remarks on Taiwan.\nI would like to reiterate that there is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a basic fact recognized by the international community.\nWe believe that China's just cause of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposing secession and realizing national reunification will continue to win the understanding and support of the international community including Russia. We stand ready to abide by the consensus on firm support to each other in four respects together with Russia. China firmly supports Russia's efforts to safeguard sovereignty and regime security and oppose external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347138.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211013_9546784.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on October 13, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporter friends, good morning! The briefing now begins.\nOn October 9, the conference marking the 110th anniversary of the Revolution of 1911 was solemnly held in Beijing. General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the conference, highly appraising the historical achievements and great significance of the Revolution of 1911, reviewing and summarizing the glorious course by which the Communist Party of China inherited the revolutionary cause of Dr. Sun Yat-sen and united and led the people in unremitting struggle, and profoundly explaining the historical lessons of the 110 years since the Revolution of 1911.\nStarting from the strategic height and historical perspective of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, the speech pointed out that the Taiwan question arose from the weakness and turmoil of the nation and will inevitably be resolved along with the rejuvenation of the nation. It profoundly revealed the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified. It solemnly reaffirmed the Party Central Committee’s major policy of advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland, and solemnly declared the firm resolve and steadfast will to adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, oppose any external interference, and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to stand on the right side of history and jointly create the glorious cause of the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech is inspiring and spurs people forward, and it points the way for doing Taiwan-related work in the new era. We will study and understand it in depth, implement it conscientiously, continue to unite all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, jointly devote ourselves to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, work together to advance the process of the complete reunification of the motherland, and jointly realize the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384231.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","In response to recent PLA aircraft exercises in the Taiwan Strait, the DPP authorities have blatantly played up military threats and incited opposition and confrontation. What comments do you have on this? Is the mainland sending a signal?","The DPP authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" forces have misjudged the situation, colluded with external forces, and continued to carry out \"independence-seeking\" provocations, which is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait.\n\"Taiwan independence\" will only bring disaster to Taiwan compatriots. Resolutely stopping \"independence-seeking\" acts is the only way to safeguard the security and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The PLA's exercises and training activities are necessary actions taken to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. They are aimed at \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and interference by external forces, and their purpose is to fundamentally safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384229.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The head of Taiwan’s defense department recently said that the current situation in the Taiwan Strait is the most severe in 40 years, and that the PLA will have the full capability to “attack Taiwan” by 2025. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must clearly recognize that the current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and that the tension and confrontation in cross-Strait relations stem from the DPP authorities colluding with external forces and stepping up provocations for “independence.” Their conduct seriously harms the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and also seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nAs I said earlier, the PLA's exercises and training activities are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces. Their purpose is to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides. They are entirely just actions. The DPP authorities' hyping of a so-called mainland “military threat” completely reverses right and wrong and shifts the blame. Such lies cannot deceive compatriots on both sides or the international community. If the DPP authorities remain obstinate and fail to rein in at the brink, they will only drive Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Could the spokesperson introduce recent progress in localities implementing the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry”? What tangible results have been achieved?","Localities and departments continue to thoroughly implement the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” promptly coordinating and resolving issues of concern to Taiwan-funded agriculture and forestry enterprises, and achieving tangible results in fund subsidies, loan financing, land use, and opening up the domestic market. Here, I will introduce some specific examples to everyone.\nIn terms of fund subsidies and financing, the Zhejiang Provincial Rural Credit Cooperatives Union specially launched the “Taiwan Financing Card,” a product exclusively for Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople, with credit lines of up to 1 million yuan. So far, more than 2,200 cards have been issued, with a total credit amount exceeding 60 million yuan. Sichuan Province implemented policy funds of more than 60 million yuan for agriculture and forestry. The Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region helped Taiwan-funded enterprises obtain loans of 6 million yuan through the government-backed financing guarantee system. Fujian Province arranges interest subsidies of 8 million yuan each year for Taiwan-funded agricultural enterprises established in the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park and the Fujian-Taiwan Agricultural Integration Development Industrial Park.\nIn terms of land use, Yingtan City in Jiangxi Province helped Taiwan-funded enterprises lease more than 800 mu of land as an oil-tea camellia base, and processed a 30-year forest rights certificate. Shanghai supported Taiwanese businesspeople in obtaining 200 mu of land in Chongming District through land transfer.\nIn terms of opening up the domestic market, Tianjin fully leveraged the platform of the “920 Cross-Strait E-Commerce Festival” to support Taiwan compatriots and enterprises in participating in online agricultural product exhibition and sales events. Shanghai actively helped Taiwan-funded enterprises participate in the China International Import Expo and the cross-Strait Taiwan enterprise product exhibition. Anhui Province organized Taiwanese businesspeople to exhibit at the 14th Anhui Tea Industry Expo in 2021.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384227.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","We note that cross-Strait civil exchange activities have continued to flourish recently, and have not been affected by epidemic prevention and control or by well-known factors on the island. Please introduce these activities, and which activities will be held in the near future.","At the last press conference, we introduced cross-Strait exchanges during the summer vacation. Since September, cross-Strait exchanges have continued to be active, mainly focusing on youth exchanges and cultural exchanges. The activities have distinctive features and are rich and varied.\nFirst, cross-Strait youth exchange activities continued to advance. From September 22 to 26, the 5th “Taiwan Youth Visit Wuhan: Charming River City Snapshots” activity was held in Wuhan. More than 20 Taiwan students and Taiwan youth entrepreneurs from 8 universities including Nanjing University experienced and presented Wuhan's development achievements from multiple angles on online platforms through short video shooting and other forms.\nOn September 24, the 8th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour was launched in Guangzhou and will last nearly 3 months, with more than 2,000 cross-Strait youth expected to participate. The activity launched 9 featured routes, including the exploration of Sun Yat-sen's historical and cultural heritage, science experiences in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, Guangdong beautiful countryside experiences, and exploration of the Maritime Silk Road culture. It designed a series of characteristic exchange projects that suit youth interests, allowing cross-Strait youth to feel the historical imprints of Lingnan culture, experience the charm of Lingnan humanities, and promote integrated development between Guangdong and Taiwan.\nOn September 25, the award ceremony of the 5th We Love· Cross-Strait Youth Short Film Competition was held simultaneously in Shanghai and Taipei via video link. A total of 1,258 works were entered, and cross-Strait young filmmakers learned from one another and made progress together.\nMore provinces and cities also held cross-Strait youth exchange activities. Hebei held the 5th Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Taiwan Middle School Students' Education Development Forum, Anhui held a Cross-Strait Youth Students' Cultural Exchange Week, and Hunan will launch a series of activities titled “Taiwan Youth Culture and Technology Hunan Tour and Red Tour.”\nSecond, cross-Strait cultural exchange activities continued to heat up. On September 22, the “Wenlan Restored to Glory” cloud donation ceremony of the facsimile edition of the 《Wenlan Pavilion Siku Quanshu》 was held via live link in Hangzhou and Taipei. The 《Siku Quanshu》 is a treasured compendium of Chinese cultural and academic achievements that survived after many twists and hardships. Donating this book to relevant Taiwan parties is a major event in cross-Strait humanities exchange. Well-known Taiwan cultural figures including Ching Fu, Hsu Cho-yun and Chu Yun-han attended the event.\nDuring the Mid-Autumn Festival, Kunshan, Jiangsu, held the 2021 Straits Cross-Strait Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival, where guests from both sides of the Strait enjoyed the finest cultural elements together and shared the bonds of compatriots. During the lantern festival, cultural and sports activities were also held, including the “Kunshan Mazu Cup” Straits Cross-Strait Youth Lantern Design Competition and a Cross-Strait folk culture exchange performance. In Jinan, Shandong, the event “Deep Ji-Taiwan Bonds: Family Moon-Viewing Reunion in Quan” was held, where compatriots from both sides made mooncakes, viewed the moon, and visited and experienced intangible cultural heritage traditions together. Anhui held the 2021 “Luzhou Moon · Straits Affection” Hefei Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering, interacting online with Taiwan townsfolk through a Mid-Autumn poetry competition, the theme performance “Enjoying Bao Gong Opera Together,” and “Copying Bao Gong's Family Precepts Together.”\nThe China Media Group invited Taiwan youth actors, writers, gourmets and photographers to participate in the “Seeking Rhythm: Classical Poetry of the Yangtze River” activity. From August 4 to September 15, it launched the integrated media series program 《People Coming and Going on the River: Seeking Rhythm in Classical Yangtze Poetry》, introducing ancient Chinese poets and poems and the natural scenery and humanistic heritage along the Yangtze River to cross-Strait youth, exploring new forms for promoting outstanding Chinese culture across the Strait.\nIn addition, Yuncheng, Shanxi held the “32nd Guan Gong Cultural Tourism Festival,” and Tianjin held the 2021 “Cross-Strait Mazu Bond” cultural exchange activity.\nThird, several important cross-Strait exchange activities will be held in various places in the near future, with rich content that merits anticipation. In October, Zhejiang will hold the 2nd Cross-Strait Image Culture Week and the award ceremony of the 4th Chinese Design Award, among other important activities. Taking the Chinese Design Award as an example, students from more than 450 universities across the Strait, Hong Kong, Macao and abroad, along with more than 230 design companies, participated in this year's competition, submitting 12,141 works, including 1,339 works from Taiwan, an increase of 28% over last year. Its influence in cross-Strait cultural and creative circles continues to expand. Jiangsu will hold the first Cross-Strait National Baseball and Softball League Kunshan leg and the 2nd Wuxi Inter-city Taiwan Youth Basketball Invitational Tournament. Peking University will hold the 7th Chinese Culture Forum.\nIn addition, Suzhou will hold the 2021 Straits Cross-Strait (Suzhou) Youth Culture Month from October 26 to late November. Themed “Continuing One Lineage, Blending Both Sides of the Strait,” it will enhance cross-Strait youth cultural exchange and emotional identity through cultural salons, cultural tourism experiences and other forms. The main venue opening activities will be held on October 26 and 27, inviting more than 300 cross-Strait youth from the Yangtze River Delta region to participate. Branch venues will be set up across Suzhou, holding 16 cross-Strait youth cultural exchange activities, including the Huang Gongwang Cross-Strait University Cultural and Creative Forum and the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Lantern Design Competition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","During the National Day holiday, a study tour to Beijing by students from Guanghe County, Gansu Province took place, and we have seen many video and picture reports. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","During the National Day holiday, the theme event “Both Sides of the Strait in One Frame, Dreams Set Sail” was held in Beijing, jointly organized by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Association, and the county Party committee and county government of Guanghe County. Twenty-three students from Guanghe County, Linxia Hui Autonomous Prefecture, Gansu Province, came to Beijing to take part in this study tour. Eight young people from Taiwan interacted and exchanged views with these students, many of whom were leaving the mountains for the first time. The students truly experienced places they had previously seen only in textbooks and had long dreamed of, such as Tiananmen, the Forbidden City, the Peking University Red Building, and the China Science and Technology Museum. Through the study tour they broadened their horizons, increased their knowledge, clarified their aspirations, strengthened their confidence, and forged friendships with Taiwanese youth. Media and Taiwanese youth also produced emotionally moving, warm short videos to bring compatriots on both sides of the Strait together to experience the past and present transformation of Guanghe, the results of poverty alleviation, and the fresh image of Guanghe’s young students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The Xin-chou (2021) Xiandu ceremony honoring the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan will be held. Please introduce the relevant details.","The ceremony for worshipping Emperor Xuanyuan (the Yellow Emperor) at China Xiandu in Jinyun County, Zhejiang Province, will be held on October 14 of the Xinchou year (2021). Themed “Four Seas United in Ancestor Worship, Common Prosperity Opens a Glorious Chapter,” the event will be held both online and offline. It aims to promote deeper and broader exchanges among all sectors across the Taiwan Strait, strengthen the national identity and cultural identity of the descendants of Yan and Huang, and help build a shared spiritual home for the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are welcome to take part in interactive activities such as offering flowers online and praying for blessings through the China Xiandu Yellow Emperor Worship Online Platform at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","During the National Day holiday, several Taiwan entertainers extended their blessings to the motherland, but they were attacked and threatened by green media on the island. China Media Group published a post refuting this vile suppression of entertainers and stated that it will continue to support Taiwan performers participating in related events. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. During this year's National Day holiday, many Taiwanese performing artists celebrated the birthday of the motherland in various ways, expressing their patriotic sentiments and sincere blessings, which we affirm. We will, as always, support and encourage cross-strait cultural exchanges and cooperation, and welcome Taiwanese performing artists to develop on the mainland. We hope that more Taiwanese performing artists will share opportunities in the course of the development of the mainland's cultural undertakings and play a positive role. The green media on the island and people with ulterior motives always seize the opportunity to create trouble, obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people, which runs counter to popular will.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384224.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, Tsai Ing-wen and Wu Zhaoxie have frequently spoken out in international media, hoping the United States and its allies will strengthen their commitments to Taiwan to deter the mainland. Wu also claimed that “Taiwan will fight to the end.” What comments do you have on these remarks?","We have repeatedly pointed out that the DPP authorities' collusion with external forces and provocations to seek “independence” are the root cause of tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations, and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. Instead of reflecting on themselves, they twist right and wrong on various occasions and exaggerate the so-called “military threat” from the mainland. These practices cannot deceive the broad masses of Taiwan's people or the international community. We warn the DPP authorities: if they attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence,” and even arrogantly attempt to seek “independence” by force, they have miscalculated, and they will not escape failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","It is understood that the 2021 Tianjin·Taiwan Commodities Expo was successfully held recently. Please have the spokesperson introduce what positive results this expo achieved.","Since 2010, the \"Tianjin·Taiwan Commodities Expo\" has been successfully held for 12 consecutive sessions, helping a number of high-quality Taiwan-invested enterprises and projects settle in Tianjin. This year's Tianjin Taiwan Expo was held from September 20 to 26. Under the theme \"Integrated Development, Shared Results,\" the event aimed to further help Taiwan-invested enterprises upgrade their industries and achieve high-quality development, better integrate into the mainland's new development pattern, and explore new pathways for promoting entrepreneurship and employment among cross-Strait youth. It achieved positive results in three areas:\nFirst, it fully demonstrated the results of economic integration and development between Tianjin and Taiwan. It focused on promoting Taiwan-invested enterprises in Tianjin's five distinctive industrial chains: electronic information, food processing, finance, automobile manufacturing, and e-commerce and logistics. It showcased the agglomeration effect of Taiwan-invested enterprises' integrated development on the mainland, reflecting how these enterprises actively participate in Tianjin's high-quality development and deeply integrate into the new development pattern.\nSecond, it helped cross-Strait youth work together to start businesses. More than 30 cross-Strait young people and internet influencers livestreamed recommendations of products from over a hundred Taiwan-invested enterprises, reaching a fan audience of 29 million. It opened a platform for cross-Strait youth entrepreneurship and employment, increasing opportunities for cross-Strait young people to understand and cooperate with each other.\nThird, it achieved new results through innovative expo formats. Working together with the \"920 (Love You) Cross-Strait E-Commerce Shopping Festival,\" it used new formats such as livestream sales and \"cloud exhibition halls\" to achieve sales exceeding RMB 40 million, with cumulative readership of related online topics surpassing 100 million times. This built a broader sales platform for Taiwan-invested enterprises and brought a new shopping experience to mainland consumers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Recently, some Taiwan educators have pointed out that the history subject of the “new curriculum guidelines” launched in 2019 has been “de-Sinicized” and cut apart by the DPP authorities, leaving its content fragmented. Recently, Taiwanese scholars have also pointed out that 60 years ago, the content on the Xinhai Revolution in Taiwan's secondary school history textbooks totaled more than 6,000 Chinese…","The so-called new curriculum guidelines for secondary school history introduced by the DPP authorities are filled with a large amount of content promoting “de-Sinicization” and advocating “Taiwan independence.” They poison the younger generation in Taiwan and have met with strong opposition from all sectors of Taiwan society.\nThe mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait both belong to the Chinese nation. No one can deprive Taiwan compatriots, as descendants of the Chinese people, of their right to receive education in Chinese culture and to understand the history of the nation. Any act of “de-Sinicization” cannot sever the historical ties between the two sides of the Strait or the blood ties between compatriots on both sides, and it certainly cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.\nAs for your mention of their distorting history and downplaying or even erasing the great achievements of Mr. Sun Yat-sen and the 1911 Revolution, this is precisely part of their efforts to implement “de-Sinicization” and pursue gradual “Taiwan independence.” The harmful consequences are obvious.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384226.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","First question: In her \"Double Ten\" speech, Tsai Ing-wen mentioned for the first time that the two sides of the Strait are \"not subordinate to each other.\" Taiwan scholars worry that the mainland side may interpret this sentence as the \"two-state theory,\" which would make the already extremely severe cross-Strait relations even worse. What is the mainland's view? Second question: The Taiwan Affairs Office…","First question. On October 10, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded comprehensively and systematically in writing to the so-called \"speech\" by the leader of the DPP authorities. This \"speech\" advocates \"Taiwan independence,\" incites confrontation, severs history and distorts facts, uses the pretext of so-called \"consensus and unity\" to attempt to kidnap Taiwan public opinion, colludes with external forces, and gives backing to its provocations seeking \"independence.\"\nSince 1949, although cross-Strait relations have not been fully unified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has never changed and cannot change; China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China; cross-Strait relations are by no means \"state-to-state\" relations, and the so-called \"mutually not subordinate\" is nothing but a blatant peddling of the \"two-state theory.\" No matter how \"Taiwan independence\" separatist propositions are packaged, they cannot conceal their evil intent of splitting the country. This further shows that it is the DPP authorities' provocations seeking \"independence\" that have caused the current tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations and threatened peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. Our efforts to combat and contain \"Taiwan independence\" are entirely necessary and righteous.\nSecond question. Recently, the statements and relevant actions of the Taiwan Affairs Office and related departments have demonstrated our solemn stance and attitude and sent a clear signal. We will not tolerate any \"Taiwan independence\" conduct, and we will not allow Taiwan to break away from China. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, strong will, and powerful capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. If the DPP authorities remain obstinate and fail to pull back from the brink, they will only push Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384230.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Two questions. First, Ko Wen-je recently said that the content of Tsai Ing-wen's “Double Ten” speech “conforms to the greatest common denominator of the Taiwan people.” What comment do you have on this? Second, will the recent power rationing measures and power supply problems in some mainland provinces and cities increase the risks for Taiwan businesses investing on the mainland?","First question. I also noted that Mayor Ko Wen-je strongly condemned the DPP authorities' leader for creating “anti-China” hostility and dividing Taiwan society. This “speech” by the DPP authorities' leader cannot represent the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan's 23 million compatriots. Opposing “Taiwan independence” and hoping for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the common public opinion of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question: The State Council has further deployed measures to ensure the supply of electricity and coal this winter and next spring, to safeguard people's basic livelihoods and the stable operation of the economy. The State Grid Corporation of China and other power enterprises have taken a series of measures to ensure power supply. The mainland remains the most reliable and broadest investment hotspot for Taiwan compatriots. Some people on the island do not understand the actual situation and exaggerate, but they cannot shake the confidence of Taiwan businesses and enterprises in putting down roots and developing on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently wrote an op-ed in foreign media claiming that she is “willing to continue engaging in dialogue with the mainland with an open attitude, on the principle of parity and without political preconditions.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Our position is clear and consistent. The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and also the common political foundation for cross-Strait consultation and dialogue. Upholding the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, means dialogue and communication are not a problem; denying the “1992 Consensus” and deviating from the one-China principle means no dialogue or exchange is possible. Since 2016, it is the DPP authorities who have denied the “1992 Consensus,” undermined the basis for dialogue, and closed the door to cross-Strait consultation and dialogue. The DPP authorities claim on the one hand that they are willing to “dialogue,” while on the other hand they intensify their collusion with external forces and carry out provocations to seek “independence.” This despicable two-faced tactic is a deception both of compatriots on the island and of international public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211013_12384228.htm"],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The DPP authorities are going further and further down the road of “Taiwan independence.” What containment measures will the mainland take?","If you care about cross-strait relations and follow the situation in the Taiwan Strait, you will notice that we not only have a resolute attitude of containing “Taiwan independence,” but also demonstrate our firm determination through concrete actions. This struggle will certainly end in the failure of the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. The first: Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida said on the 11th that Japan will further deepen cooperation and exchanges between Japan and Taiwan. Some analysts believe this represents Japan's intention to strengthen its relations with Taiwan. What is your comment? The second: the United States announced six vaccines recognized for entry, which do not include Taiwan's self-developed high-end…","First question: Taiwan is part of China. We have consistently and firmly opposed any official relations in any form between countries with which we have diplomatic ties and the Taiwan region of China. We hope the new Japanese government will abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents and the one-China principle, and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.\nSecond question: Compatriots in Taiwan need safe, reliable, and efficient vaccines. A series of political manipulations by the DPP authorities on epidemic prevention and control and vaccine issues have ultimately made the people of Taiwan bear the bitter fruit. It is the DPP authorities who have turned their own 'crime' into a 'punishment' for the broad masses of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","It is understood that the DPP authorities and Somaliland have established so-called “representative offices” in each other’s territory, and have long provided huge bribes to relevant Somaliland politicians and their families. They have long relied on despicable methods to infiltrate, buy over and win over politicians of relevant countries and regions, providing convenience for peddling “Taiwan independence”…","From Lee Teng-hui to Chen Shui-bian, and up to the present DPP authorities, none of them has ever stopped practicing “dollar diplomacy.” In recent times, in order to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, they have become even more extreme, adopting all kinds of despicable tactics that cannot see the light of day. This is well known to everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","A responsible person of a Taiwan people’s representative institution recently said in an interview: “China-US trade friction has caused China-US relations to decline, while Taipei-Washington relations have warmed, and the goal of Taiwan-US ‘diplomatic ties’ can be achieved before 2028.” Some netizens on the island mocked, “Daydreaming again” and “deceiving the people.” What is the comment on this?","That is a daydream. He cannot realize it even if he takes this dream to his grave.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, the Russian website Today Russia published an article arguing that “if the United States publicly supports defending Taiwan, it is playing a dangerous game, and the U.S. has zero capability to implement this policy.” What comments do you have on this?","As for reports from foreign media, we will not comment. Here, I would like to stress our position and attitude.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair and is also the most core and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The United States has made commitments to China on the Taiwan question. The US should earnestly abide by this commitment, not send erroneous signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces, and even less give the “Taiwan independence” forces backing and encouragement, so as not to further damage China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","彭博社记者","The director of Harvard University’s Chinese language program recently said that, starting in 2022, the summer Chinese course that was originally taught at Beijing Language and Culture University will instead be run in cooperation with Taiwan University. Is the Taiwan Affairs Office worried that Beijing’s influence and soft power in international educational exchange activities will weaken?","I am not aware of the specific situation you mention. This is just an ordinary inter-university exchange program. US universities, including Harvard University, have numerous cooperative programs with mainland universities. Whether or not a single cooperative program can continue, and whatever the real reason may be, there is nothing to make a fuss about and nothing to hype up. Some politicians on the island hype everything, which is merely a sign of a guilty conscience.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland side emphasizes that the Communist Party of China inherits the revolutionary cause of Mr. Sun Yat-sen and unites and leads the people in unremitting struggle. The Mainland Affairs Council, however, claims that Taiwan is the legitimate successor of Sun Yat-sen. Spokesperson, in your view, what is the significance of the two sides’ dispute on this point? How should public recognition be won?","Who has inherited Mr. Sun Yat-sen's legacy has already been settled by history. During his lifetime, Mr. Sun Yat-sen unwaveringly pursued national reunification, but today the DPP authorities are bent on “independence.” During his lifetime, Mr. Sun Yat-sen unwaveringly pursued the revitalization of China, but today the DPP authorities collude with external forces and sell out the national interests. Who is the true inheritor and who is “hanging a sheep's head to sell dog meat” is clear to all and needs no debate.\nWe commemorate the 110th anniversary of the 1911 Revolution. Its important significance lies in our willingness to unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to carry forward the lofty spirit of Mr. Sun Yat-sen, who unwaveringly strove to revitalize China, to uphold national righteousness, oppose “Taiwan independence,” safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, stand on the right side of history, and unite and work hand in hand to achieve national rejuvenation and continuously strive for the complete reunification of the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","In his speech on taking office as Chairman of the Kuomintang, Eric Chu said that the KMT needs to connect the two sides of the Strait with the world and restart cross-Strait exchange platforms. What is your comment?","On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with the Kuomintang to consolidate and enhance mutual trust, strengthen exchanges and cooperation at all levels and in all fields, jointly promote the development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nThank you all for coming, and see you next time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211013_12384220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-14","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","Pentagon Press Secretary John F. Kirby told journalists on Tuesday that \"the PRC has stepped up efforts to intimidate and pressure Taiwan and other allies and partners; including increasing their military activities, conducted in the vicinity of Taiwan, the East China Sea and the South China Sea; which we believe are destabilizing and only increase the risk of miscalculation.\" What is China's comment?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. The US is in no position to make irresponsible remarks. Relevant steps taken by China are legitimate and reasonable measures to safeguard its sovereignty, security, territorial integrity and rights and interests. With joint efforts of China and other neighbouring countries around the South China Sea, the situation in the South China Sea is generally stable at present. The remarks on the US side are in grave violation of the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques. The US' deliberate attempt to drive a wedge between China and regional countries with the relevant issues has sent out an extremely erroneous and irresponsible message. China deplores and firmly opposes this.\nFor some time, the US has been making negative moves by selling arms to Taiwan and strengthening its official and military ties with Taiwan, including the launch of a $750 million arms sale plan to Taiwan, the landing of US military aircraft in Taiwan and frequent sailing of US warships across the Taiwan Strait. The US has been stirring up trouble, flexing muscles in the South China Sea and China's neighboring areas and stoking geopolitical confrontation. This has fully revealed that the US is a troublemaker, a saboteur of regional peace and stability, and a spoiler of solidarity and cooperation.\nThe US side should take China's position and concerns seriously, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, and stop making irresponsible remarks on Taiwan and maritime issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347139.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211014_9552504.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 14 — US Deputy Secretary of State Fernandez and Assistant Secretary for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Kanda met with the head of the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office,” and the DPP authorities expressed thanks. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 14th: We urge the US government to act in deeds in abiding by the One-China principle and the solemn commitments it has made to China on the Taiwan question, not to have any form of official interaction with Taiwan, not to send any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and not to create new troubles for the situation in the Taiwan Strait.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that attempting to provoke by colluding with external forces to seek “independence” will only bring disaster to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211014_12384502.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-14","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 14 — On October 14, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council issued a statement regarding the DPP authorities' continuous distortion and attacks on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. The full text of the statement is as follows:\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding the facts and legal principles that Taiwan is part of China and ignoring the basic norms of international relations, have repeatedly distorted and attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 on various occasions and in various ways, openly challenging the international community's one-China principle, spreading the fallacy that Taiwan is a \"sovereign state,\" and weaving lies to pursue the so-called \"Taiwan independence\"; this is a very dangerous provocation for \"independence.\"\nThe DPP authorities' distortion and attack on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 is essentially an attempt to deny that Taiwan is part of China. Taiwan is China's Taiwan; its history and legal principles are very clear. The DPP authorities stubbornly hold the \"Taiwan independence\" position, have long spread the \"Taiwan independence\" view of history, deceived island residents and international public opinion, and openly challenged the facts and legal principles recognized by the international community; but they cannot change the iron fact that Taiwan is part of China.\nThe DPP authorities' distortion and attack on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, using \"representation\" as a pretext, reveals their ignorance of and contempt for international law. In 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, clearly and thoroughly resolving the question of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally, and procedurally. Years of practice have fully demonstrated that the United Nations and the vast majority of member states recognize that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and fully respect China's sovereignty over Taiwan. China's representation in the United Nations is, of course, the representation of all of China, including Taiwan. Taiwan is part of China, and there is fundamentally no so-called \"representation\" issue for it in the United Nations. The DPP authorities' hype about Taiwan's \"representation,\" flagrantly disregarding the basic norms of international relations and scheming to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan,\" is a blatant provocation for \"independence.\"\nThe DPP authorities' distortion and attack on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, claiming to seek \"international space\" for Taiwan, aim to create political incidents. On the question of Chinese Taiwan region's participation in international organizations and their activities, our position and the international consensus are very clear: it must be resolved on the basis of the one-China principle. From 2009 to 2016, the Chinese Taiwan region was able to participate in the World Health Assembly under the name \"Chinese Taipei\" as an observer, which was resolved through cross-Strait consultations on the premise of the one-China principle. Since 2016, the DPP authorities have stubbornly insisted on a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" and unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations, directly leading to the Chinese Taiwan region being unable to participate in the World Health Assembly. The responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nTaiwan compatriots are Chinese. We attach great importance to the aspirations and concerns of Taiwan compatriots to participate in international activities. Whether in economic, social, cultural, or sports activities, or in health, epidemic prevention, and response, we make our utmost efforts on the premise of the one-China principle to make proper arrangements for Taiwan compatriots. We are glad to see Taiwan compatriots showcasing the spirit of the Chinese people on the world stage. Our overseas \"Spring Seedling Action,\" which broadly carries out COVID-19 vaccination, benefits all Chinese citizens including Taiwan compatriots, ensuring everyone has access to vaccines. When Taiwan compatriots encounter disasters or wars overseas, our consular protection provides them shelter. Facts prove that only on the premise of the one-China principle can the well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots be effectively safeguarded internationally, and only then can they stand tall. Taiwan compatriots, as Chinese, share with all the people of the motherland the dignity and glory of the motherland internationally. It is precisely the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces that have harmed the immediate interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe cause of China's unification is a just cause and enjoys broad support from the international community. This is the most distinctive feature of the times of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 in the current situation. This resolution embodies the authority of international law and must not be distorted or challenged.\n\"Taiwan independence\" separatism is the greatest obstacle to the unification of the motherland and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. The wheel of history toward the complete reunification of the motherland rolls forward and cannot be stopped. \"Taiwan independence\" separatists will surely be brought to account. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any schemes for \"independence\" are futile; the higher they jump, the harder they will fall!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211014_12384505.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2021-10-15","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","The 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China was recently successfully concluded. Please introduce the situation regarding the study and implementation of the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress by officers and soldiers across the armed forces.","The 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China was a very important congress convened at a critical moment when the whole Party and all ethnic groups across the country were embarking on a new journey of building China into a modern socialist country in all respects and marching toward the second centenary goal. Comrade Xi Jinping's report gave the whole Party, the whole military, and the people of all ethnic groups across the country strong inspiration in their convictions, clear direction, and spiritual encouragement. It is a political declaration by which the Party unites and leads the people to forge ahead on the new journey and achieve new victories. The Congress elected the new Central Committee and the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, and adopted the resolution on the report of the 19th Central Committee, the resolution on the work report of the 19th Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, and the resolution on the Constitution of the Communist Party of China (Amendment). The First Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee elected the new central leadership, which the officers and soldiers of the entire military resolutely endorse and support.\nIn accordance with the deployment requirements of the Party Central Committee and the Central Military Commission, the officers and soldiers of the entire military earnestly organized the viewing and listening of the Congress proceedings and widely carried out study and discussion. Military media outlets opened special columns to showcase vivid scenes and practical actions of military units at all levels studying and implementing the spirit of the 20th Party Congress through various forms. The upsurge in studying and implementing the Congress spirit is vigorously rising across the armed forces. Over the past 10 years of the new era, we established the goal of strengthening the military for the Party in the new era, implemented Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military, implemented the military strategic guidelines of the new era, upheld the Party's absolute leadership over the people's military, coordinated the military struggle in all directions and domains, boldly and resolutely deepened national defense and military reform, and gave the People's Military a new system, new structure, new pattern, and new look. The great changes of the new era's 10 years fundamentally stem from the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, and from the scientific guidance of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era. The report of the 20th Party Congress proposed “achieving the centenary goal of army building as scheduled,” enriching and expanding the era connotation of the Party's goal of strengthening the military in the new era, and clearly setting the central task of our army's development for the next five years. This is the historic responsibility the People's Military must shoulder and the historic answer it must deliver.\nStudying, publicizing, and implementing the spirit of the 20th Party Congress is the top political task for the whole Party and the whole military now and for a considerable period to come. Chairman Xi Jinping gave important instructions, the Central Military Commission made special arrangements, and units carefully planned and solidly organized the study, publicity, and implementation of the Congress spirit. Next, the Whole Military Study and Implementation of the 20th Party Congress Spirit Propaganda Group will hold its first report session and organize circuit propaganda tours. Some delegates to the 20th Party Congress and outstanding political instructors of the whole military will go deep into grassroots units to provide theoretical propaganda services. A special seminar for senior cadres of the whole military on studying and implementing the spirit of the 20th Party Congress will be held at the National Defense University, and military theorists will be organized to conduct research and interpretation of the Congress spirit. The officers and soldiers of the entire military resolutely implement the decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee, the Central Military Commission, and Chairman Xi Jinping. They comprehensively implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military. They profoundly grasp the decisive significance of the “Two Establishes,” strengthen the “Four Consciousnesses,” firmly establish the “Four Confidences,” and achieve the “Two Upholds.” They implement the Chairman Responsibility System of the Central Military Commission and resolutely obey the command of the Party Central Committee, the Central Military Commission, and Chairman Xi Jinping, contributing strength to achieving the centenary goal of army building as scheduled and accelerating the building of the People's Military into a world-class military.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/10-15/9587570.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-10-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 15: Regarding the matter of a mainland spouse who died in the Kaohsiung fire, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on October 15: We express deep condolences to the mainland spouse who died, are working urgently to understand the situation, and will actively assist the family in handling all post-incident arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211015_12384760.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-18","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","The missile destroyer USS Dewey and the Canadian frigate HMCS Winnipeg sailed through the Taiwan Strait on October 15. Do you have any response?","The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command already made remarks on the issue. The Chinese side was closely following and monitoring, and on the alert against the US and the Canadian military vessels’ passage through the Taiwan Strait from start to end. US warships have repeatedly flaunted their prowess in the Taiwan Strait, provoking and stirring up trouble, and even gone further to collude with its allies to provoke, disrupt and mess around. The vile acts of the US are by no means commitment to freedom and openness, but rather deliberate disruption and sabotage of regional peace and stability. The international community sees this crystal clear.\nI want to reiterate that China is unswervingly determined to safeguard its national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese military is always on high alert and will resolutely respond to all threats and provocations. The US side should change course and redress mistakes. The Canadian side should proceed from its own interests and overall situation of China-Canadian relations, and reject acting as a cat’s paw of others.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347141.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211018_9578871.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-19","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Ten Chinese and Russian warships on Monday passed through the Tsugaru Strait between Japan's Honshu and Hokkaido for the first time. Could you please explain the purpose of the transit? Secondly, the Taiwan Strait and the Tsugaru Strait are both legally international waters, meaning that warships are allowed to sail through them. Yet China argues that the Taiwan transits earlier this week are vile. So I was…","Regarding your first question, please refer it to the Ministry of National Defense.\nOn your second question, the international community sees clearly who are flexing muscle, provoking and stirring up trouble, and who, under the disguise of freedom of navigation, are conducting military deterrence and undermining regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347142.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211019_9604337.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-10-19","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to Japan's Kyodo News, the Japanese government is considering stating in its National Security Strategy, to be revised at the end of the year, that it “does not recognize unilateral changes to the status quo by force” with regard to the situation in the Taiwan Strait. The policy content may also reflect the “Free and Open Indo-Pacific” vision and the Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (Quad) mechanism…","We have noted the relevant reports. For some time, the Japanese side has deliberately hyped up Taiwan-related and other China-related issues, brutally interfered in China's internal affairs, and played up the so-called \"China military threat.\" This is with ulterior motives and is irresponsible.\nThe two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Fifty years ago, the Japanese side solemnly committed in the Joint Communiqué of the Government of Japan and the Government of the People's Republic of China to recognize the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China. Regarding the Chinese government's reiteration that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People's Republic of China, the Japanese government fully understands and respects this position, and it adheres to the position of Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation. Japan should abide by the basic norms of international relations, fulfill its solemn political commitments to China, and not interfere in the Taiwan question. It must be pointed out that in recent years, Japan has been enthusiastic about closely following other countries in their policies to contain China, and has formed exclusive \"small circles\" under the banner of a \"free and open\" Indo-Pacific. This runs counter to the shared expectations of regional countries for peace, development, and cooperation.\nThis year marks the 50th anniversary of the normalization of diplomatic relations between China and Japan. Japan should revisit its original aspirations, move in the same direction as China, and put into practice the important consensus that \"the two countries are cooperative partners and do not pose threats to each other,\" pushing bilateral relations to keep advancing along the right track. We urge the Japanese side to learn from history, be cautious in words and deeds in the field of military security, not interfere in China's internal affairs or harm China's security interests, and not undermine regional security and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/10-19/9590184.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-10-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 19 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 19th: Taiwan region of China’s participation in international organizations and their activities must adhere to the One-China principle. The arrangements regarding Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Organization have long been settled. The remarks of the World Medical…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities use various tricks to win over certain organizations to seek “independence” and create the illusion of international “support for Taiwan.” This is nothing but self-deception, and their scheme will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211019_12385412.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-21","Wang Wenbin","SCMP","At a hearing on October 20 local time, US ambassador to China nominee Nicholas Burns called on the government to remain committed to the “one-China” policy while increasing security assistance to Taiwan. He also criticized China over its policies on Xinjiang and Tibet and the origins study of the coronavirus. Do you have any comment? My second question is about the statement of the meeting of the Moscow Format…","On your first question, the remarks of Mr. Burns smack of Cold War zero-sum mentality and run counter to facts. China firmly rejects them.\nChina is committed to the path of peaceful development. We will always be the advocate of world peace, contributor to global development, defender of international order and a provider of public good. We oppose defining China-US ties as competitive. Even when there is competition between the two sides in such pragmatic areas as economy and trade, it is healthy competition with each other for excellence. Issues related to Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are purely China’s internal affairs that brook no foreign interference. The accusation of the so-called “genocide” in Xinjiang is an outrageous lie fabricated by a few anti-China scholars in Western countries and US politicians, with the true intention of oppressing and containing China’s development. The one-China principle is a political foundation of China-US relations and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The US made the pledge of stopping arms sale to Taiwan in explicit terms in the August 17 Communique. It should honor its commitment. Since the start of COVID-19, China has acted in an open, transparent and responsible manner in providing timely updates to the WHO and the international community. Origins-tracing is a scientific issue, but a handful of US politicians are obsessed with politically-motivated studies. Their malicious intention of denigrating and stigmatizing China is evident to all.\nWe advise Mr. Burns to be keenly aware of the overall trend of world development and people’s aspiration, learn the real situations of China objectively, view China and China-US ties in an rational manner and avoid underestimating the strong resolve, determination and capability of the Chinese people to defend their rights. We hope he will speak and act in a more constructive manner, and play a constructive part in promoting China-US relations and the friendship between the two peoples.\nTo answer your second question, Mr. Yue Xiaoyong, China’s Special Envoy for Afghan Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs attended upon invitation the meeting on Afghanistan alongside with special envoys of Russia and Pakistan, and the third meeting of the Moscow Format Consultations on Afghanistan on October 19 and 20 in Moscow. All parties had an in-depth exchange of views and reached broad consensus on such issues as the current situation in Afghanistan, counter-terrorism and anti-narcotics security and humanitarian assistance to Afghanistan. They stressed the importance of respecting Afghanistan’s independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity and upholding the “Afghan-owned and Afghan-led” principle, called on the country to establish a broad-based and inclusive political structure, implement moderate and prudent domestic and foreign policies, respect the basic rights of ethnic minorities, women and children, take concrete measures to fight all forms of terrorist forces and adopt friendly policies toward its neighbors. All parties called on the international community to provide urgently-needed humanitarian, livelihood and economic assistance to Afghanistan, work for a smooth transition in the country for it to achieve lasting peace and stability, development and prosperity at an early date.\nDuring the meeting, Special Envoy Yue Xiaoyong elaborated on China’s policy and position. He said that as Afghanistan is at the critical stage of moving from chaos to stability, China is ready to work with regional countries to advance the political settlement of the Afghan issue, help Afghanistan to tackle the humanitarian crisis, work for all multilateral mechanisms on the issue to form synergy, and create an enabling external environment for Afghanistan to achieve peace, reconstruction and sustained development.\nChina, Russia, Pakistan and parties at the meeting also had dialogue and communication through various means with representatives of the Afghan interim government attending the meeting.\nAs for whether China recognizes the interim government, I would like to tell you that the new Afghan regime is still in the process of formation and the international community is watching and coordinating on the issue. China is in close communication with relevant countries and all parties agree on the need for dialogue and engagement with Afghanistan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347143.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211022_9606113.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-21","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","On October 21, the plenary session of the European Parliament adopted the report on EU-Taiwan political relations and cooperation. Do you have any comment?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally-recognized norm of international relations and consensus of the international community. It is also the political foundation of China-EU relations. The European Parliament’s adoption of the above-mentioned report gravely violates the basic norm governing international relations, the one-China principle and the EU’s public commitment on the Taiwan question. It is vile in nature and has an egregious impact. China strongly condemns and rejects this move.\nThe European Parliament should immediately stop rhetoric and behavior that undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and stop seeking provocation and confrontation. A word for the relevant side: do not underestimate the Chinese people’s determination, will and capacity to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347143.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211022_9606113.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-21","Wang Wenbin","NHK","The chief of Taiwan's foreign affairs department will visit the Czech Republic and Slovakia. These are countries having diplomatic relations with China. Do you have any comment?","First, I want to reiterate that there is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. This is an indisputable fact and a basic norm governing international relations. We deplore and firmly oppose relevant countries' connivance at these visits, and urge them not to risk universal condemnation, maliciously challenge the one-China principle and undermine the political foundation of bilateral relations and the atmosphere of cooperation. We would also admonish the Taiwan authorities that any attempt to solicit foreign support and seek political manipulation is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347143.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211022_9606113.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 21 — The European Parliament has adopted a report related to Taiwan, advocating that the European Union upgrade its relations with Taiwan. The DPP authorities expressed their gratitude. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 21st when asked that the DPP authorities, in collusion with lawmakers from certain countries, have concocted various Taiwan-related motions in an attempt to attach themselves to external forces for \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, which are bound to fail.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the European Parliament's adoption of the relevant report seriously violates the one-China principle and the public commitments the European side made on the Taiwan question when China and Europe established diplomatic relations. It sends a seriously wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firmly oppose this.\nHe also said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We urge the relevant EU institutions to act in practice in adhering to the one-China principle, correct their mistake, and handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211021_12385885.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-22","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","US leader said when asked if the US would come to the defense of Taiwan that the US has a commitment to do so. The White House later said there is no change in US policy on Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs that allow no foreign interference. On issues that bear on China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and other core interests, no one shall expect China to make any compromise or trade-offs. No one should underestimate the resolve, the will and the ability of the Chinese people to defend their national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Do not stand on the opposite side of the 1.4 billion people. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiques, be prudent with its words and actions on the Taiwan question, and avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, lest it should seriously damage China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347144.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211023_9729494.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-22","Wang Wenbin","CNR","It is reported that the spokesperson of the Taiwan region’s foreign affairs department said that the head of the agency Joseph Wu will visit the Czech Republic and Slovakia. Previously, China took countermeasures on Lithuania’s announcement of allowing the Taiwan authorities to set up a “representative office” in the country under the name of Taiwan. Will China take countermeasures on the Czech Republic and Slovakia?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China is firmly resolved in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe firmly oppose all forms of official interactions between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We are watching closely the visit of the relevant personnel in the Taiwan region and will take legitimate and necessary measures to firmly uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No one should be under any illusion about this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347144.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211023_9729494.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 22: The so-called “Constitutional Reform Group” of the DPP recently set six directions for “constitutional reform,” involving lowering the threshold for “amending the constitution,” abolishing the examination and supervision bodies, and so on. The relevant amendment draft will be submitted to the Legislative Yuan in Taiwan for deliberation. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 22nd in response to a question: We are highly attentive to these developments and firmly oppose any form of “constitutional amendment to seek independence,” including lowering the threshold to open the door for seeking “independence” and smuggling in issues aimed at seeking “independence.” The ringleaders will certainly be severely punished by law.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, disregarding the livelihood and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots and their expectations for peace and stability in cross-Strait relations, have persistently manipulated the “constitutional amendment” issue, and their political calculations and sinister intentions are plain to see. All responsible parties and insightful people on the island should see through the DPP authorities' schemes and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the well-being of the Taiwan public through concrete actions. Taiwan compatriots must also remain highly vigilant and consciously oppose and resist all forms of “constitutional amendment to seek independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211022_12386131.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 22 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 22nd in response to a question: The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no external interference. The U.S. side has repeatedly stated clearly that it has no intention of changing its one-China policy. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that the historical task of complete reunification of the motherland must be accomplished, and it certainly can be accomplished. The DPP authorities' attempts to sell out the interests of the Chinese nation and the well-being of the people on the island, and to collude with external forces to seek “Taiwan independence,” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211022_12386132.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-25","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The State Department said that on October 22, the American Institute in Taiwan and the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office convened high-level representatives for a virtual forum on the theme of expanding Taiwan’s ability to participate meaningfully at the UN in such areas as global public health, environment and climate change, etc. What's the foreign ministry's comment on this virtual meeting?","The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Resolution 2758 adopted by the General Assembly in 1971 has solved once and for all the issue of the PRC's representation in the UN in political, legal and procedural terms. The system, agencies and the Secretariat of the UN should abide by the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758 when dealing with Taiwan-related affairs. The vast number of UN member states, including the US, recognize that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The participation of the Taiwan region in activities of international organizations must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The Taiwan authorities’ attempt to expand the so-called “international” space by brownnosing foreign forces is in essence trying to expand the room for “Taiwan independence” and separatism and will only prove a failure.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, observe UNGA Resolution 2758, stop official contact with Taiwan, stop making irresponsible remarks, refrain from sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces in any form, avoid emboldening or supporting the Taiwan authorities in expanding the room for “Taiwan independence”, and stop doing things that undermine China-US relations and damage peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347145.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211025_9982422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-26","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","KCNA recently reported that DPRK Deputy Foreign Minister Pak Myong Ho said the US clamor for Taiwan independence is escalating military tensions and may increase the tensions on the Korean Peninsula. He also said the DPRK supports China’s position of reunification. What is your comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which allows no interference by external forces. China will firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, oppose any country’s interference in the Taiwan question, and acts that undermine regional peace and stability. As a close and friendly neighbor, China will strengthen communication and cooperation with the DPRK, safeguard peace and stability of the Korean Peninsula and the whole region and defend shared interests of the two countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347146.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211026_10080158.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-26","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, Joseph Wu will visit Slovakia and the Czech Republic soon. What is your comment?","Joseph Wu is a typical “Taiwan independence” separatist, who makes such visits with the real purpose of advocating “Taiwan independence” and separatism, creating the illusion of \"one China, one Taiwan\", and pitting China and countries it has with diplomatic ties with against each other and hurting their relations. China expresses its firm opposition to certain countries’ connivance of “Taiwan independence” separatists, and asks the countries to abide by the one-China principle and not to create platforms for any activities by “Taiwan independence” separatists. We also warn the Taiwan authorities that any attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” by soliciting foreign support is bound to fail. China has firm resolve to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will take all necessary measures to resolutely crush all attempts at \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347146.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211026_10080158.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-27","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","On October 26, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken issued a statement, which read “Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system is not a political issue, but a pragmatic one” and the US encourages “all UN Member States to join us in supporting Taiwan’s robust, meaningful participation throughout the UN system and in the international community, consistent with our ‘one China’ policy, which is guided by the…","The US statement seriously violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, violates the promise it has made, violates the basic norms governing international relations, and has sent a seriously wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this, and has made clear its solemn position to and lodged stern representations with the US. I want to stress the four-point basic position.\nFirst, there is only one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. A total of 180 countries, including the US, have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of commitment to the one-China principle. The one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community and a widely recognized norm of international relations, which does not allow unilateral challenge or distortion by the US. In the three China-US joint communiqués, the US unequivocally recognizes the government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China. Within this context, the people of the US will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.\nSecond, the Taiwan region’s participation in activities of international organizations must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Resolution 2758 adopted by the UN General Assembly has solved once and for all the issue of the China’s representation in the UN in political, legal and procedural terms. The system, agencies and the Secretariat of the UN should abide by the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758 when dealing with Taiwan-related affairs. By touting and whitewashing of Taiwan’s so-called democracy and contribution and endorsing Taiwan, the US is trying to distort concepts and mislead others. But the US motive and intention are seen clearly by the international community. Fifty years ago, the US attempted to create “one China, one Taiwan” or “two Chinas” in the UN, only to confront setbacks. If the US still backpedals in history today, it is pitting itself against the 1.4 billion Chinese people and the vast majority of countries in the world, and will only face another failure.\nThird, the Taiwan authorities recalcitrantly stick to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refuse to recognize the 1992 consensus and go all out to expand its so-called “international space”, going further down the path of “Taiwan independence” separatism. This is the greatest realistic threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the crux for the repeated frustration Taiwan has experienced in participating in activities of multilateral institutions such as the ICAO and WHO in recent years. As a matter of fact, the Taiwan region has unfettered access to information from the ICAO. It is linked to many cities in the world with convenient flights. On the premise of observing the one-China principle, medical and health experts in the Taiwan region can attend WHO technical meetings. Taiwan has unfettered access to public health information including with regard to COVID-19. Now the US is making an issue out of Taiwan’s participation in the ICAO and WHO to angle for sympathy. This attempt is miscalculated and futile.\nFourth, the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués constitute the political foundation of China-US relations. The so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and “Six Assurances” unilaterally concocted by the US gravely violate international law, basic norms governing international relations and the one-China principle. China has made clear its firm rejection to them from the very beginning. For a while, the US has been keeping up erroneous words and acts on the Taiwan question. The Chinese side has made resolute and necessary reactions every step of the way. Should the US side choose to continue playing the “Taiwan card”, it would inevitably pose seismic risks to China-US relations, seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and gravely harm the interests of the US itself.\nWe urge the US to abide by its commitment, the one-China principle, the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués and UNGA Resolution 2758, stop making irresponsible erroneous remarks, stop assisting Taiwan in expanding the so-called “international space”, avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and safeguard the political foundation for China-US relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211027_10282710.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-27","Zhao Lijian","Associated Press of Pakistan","Yesterday, President Xi and Prime Minister Imran Khan held a telephonic conversation. Can you share some details of it?","President Xi Jinping had a phone conversation with Pakistani Prime Minister Imran Khan yesterday. The Chinese side has released a readout about it. I can add several points.\nPresident Xi Jinping pointed out, during the past 70 years since the establishment of China-Pakistan diplomatic ties, no matter how the international situation may change, the two sides have always stood side by side in weal and woe. History has fully proved that the two countries are the most reliable iron-clad brothers for each other. Under the new circumstances, the two countries should stand together even more firmly and push forward the all-weather strategic cooperative partnership, and build a closer China-Pakistan community with a shared future in the new era. President Xi stressed that China supports Pakistan in exploring a development path suited to its own national conditions and is willing to share China's new high-quality development opportunities with Pakistan. China will continue to support Pakistan in its fight against COVID-19, jointly pursue high quality CPEC cooperation and continue to unleash the positive effects of CPEC in promoting growth and improving people's wellbeing. The two sides should strengthen counter-terrorism and security cooperation. China is ready to work with Pakistan to enhance multilateral coordination, practice true multilateralism and promote international fairness and justice, so as to safeguard the shared interests of the two countries and maintain world peace and stability.\nPrime Minister Imran Khan said that the world is faced with many major issues that require Pakistan and China to communicate and work together more closely. Pakistan-China relations have withstood all tests and the two countries always support each other in both good and bad times. China has supported Pakistan in its fight against COVID-19, and protected the life and safety of the Pakistani people, setting an example for global cooperation against the pandemic. Pakistan staunchly pursues the one-China policy, firmly supports China's stance on issues concerning China's core interests such as the issues related to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, Tibet and human rights, and firmly supports the Global Development Initiative proposed by President Xi Jinping. Pakistan stands ready to work with China to promote the building of CPEC and practical cooperation in various areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211027_10282710.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-27","Zhao Lijian","AFP","According to the South China Morning Post, a delegation from the European Parliament will travel to Taiwan next week. Do you have any comment on this?","The Chinese Mission to the EU already released a statement on this. I’d like to stress that the one-China principle is a universally-recognized norm governing international relations and a consensus of the international community. It is a solemn commitment made by the EU side upon establishing diplomatic relations with China. The European Parliament is an important official organ of the EU. It follows naturally that its members should stay true to the commitment made by the EU, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues and keep the political foundation for China-EU relations intact. I stress once again that the Chinese people are firmly resolved to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211027_10282710.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-27","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","According to reports, the Senate of the Parliament of the Czech Republic has invited Joseph Wu, head of the foreign affairs department of the Taiwan authorities, to visit the Czech Republic. Does the Chinese side have any comment?","China strongly deplores and firmly rejects the malicious provocative act by the Senate of the Parliament of the Czech Republic and the individuals concerned. We have lodged solemn representations with the Czech side and will make legitimate and necessary reactions.\nThere is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. This is an ironclad fact, a basic norm in international relations and a consensus of the international community. The despicable maneuvers by a few individuals in the Czech Republic are doomed to fail. We urge them to promptly change course, otherwise they will end up swallowing the bitter fruit themselves. The Taiwan authorities should bear in mind that seeking “Taiwan independence” by soliciting external support is a dead end. China’s resolution and will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is steadfast. We will take all necessary measures to crush any “Taiwan independence” plot.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211027_10282710.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-27","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","I have a question on comedian John Oliver’s television segments. He aired the segment on Taiwan, which has gained attention from China’s state media, as well as Taiwanese officials. I am wondering if the foreign ministry has any comment.","I have never heard of the program or the comedian you mentioned. Neither do I have time to watch it. I want to stress that the historical merits of the Taiwan question is very clear and China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear-cut.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211027_10282710.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on October 27, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. The press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","US State Department official Hua Ziqiang recently claimed at an online meeting hosted by the German Marshall Fund that China “misused” UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, “excluding Taiwan from international organizations such as ICAO and WHO.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","This year marks the 50th anniversary of the restoration of the lawful seat of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations. General Secretary Xi Jinping attended the commemorative meeting on October 25 and delivered an important speech. Fifty years ago, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all the rights of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing that the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China are the sole legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 clearly and thoroughly resolved the issue of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally, and procedurally. The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is not a country; it is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and China's representation in the United Nations is naturally the representation of all of China, including Taiwan.\nBefore the establishment of China-US diplomatic relations, the United States attempted to create “two Chinas” at the United Nations, a dishonorable record that ended in failure. The day Resolution 2758 was adopted was also the day the so-called “dual representation resolution draft” proposed by the United States and others was rejected. The mistake of some people in the United States is that they disregard historical and legal facts, deny the authority of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and attempt to overturn the UN's decision, thereby going against the majority of the international community.\nTaiwan is part of China. Chinese Taiwan region's participation in international organizations and their activities must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The mistake of some people in the United States is that they disregard the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, and even contradict the US government's repeatedly reiterated position of “not supporting Taiwan's accession to any international organization that must be joined by sovereign states.” The so-called “exclusion of Taiwan from the United Nations, the International Civil Aviation Organization, and the World Health Organization” is pure nonsense.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities have long clamored about “Taiwan's representation,” “Taiwan's international space,” and other fallacies, aiming to split Taiwan from China. Their essence is “Taiwan independence.” The mistake of some people in the United States is that they facilitate the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” actions, violating the long-standing position of the US government of not supporting “Taiwan independence.”\nWe urge relevant US government officials to act in practice to uphold the US government's position of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to be prudent in their words and deeds on the Taiwan question, and not to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387227.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","U.S. Secretary of State Blinken again touted on October 26 the so-called “meaningful participation of Taiwan in the United Nations and other international organizations.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Just now I solemnly stated that the United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states, that Taiwan is part of China, and that the People’s Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing all of China. Taiwan has no right to join the United Nations. On the question of the Taiwan region of China’s participation in international organizations and their activities, the international community has a settled conclusion and established practice: the one-China principle must be upheld. For some time, the U.S. side has come up with various formulations, including so-called “meaningful participation in international organizations” and even “meaningful participation in the United Nations.” These seriously violate relevant UN resolutions, seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and send a serious wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces.\nWe understand the thoughts and feelings of Taiwan compatriots about participating in international activities. On the basis of upholding the one-China principle, appropriate arrangements have been made in the past and can be made in the future. But the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces are deceiving the island’s public with various specious lies and misleading international public opinion, and they are fantasizing about promoting the Taiwan region of China to “join the United Nations” and to seek “independence” through participation in international activities. This is absolutely impossible. We advise the DPP authorities to immediately abandon the illusion of “seeking independence by relying on the United States” and “seeking independence by relying on outside forces.” Every act aimed at undermining the one-China principle and splitting the country can only end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Wu Zhaoxie, head of the Taiwan region’s external affairs department, recently made an intrusive visit to Slovakia and the Czech Republic, blatantly peddling “Taiwan independence” positions and spreading “Taiwan independence” remarks. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Wu Chao-hsieh is a diehard “Taiwan independence” element who has gone further and further down the path of criminal “independence” activities. For some time, under various pretexts and in various forms, Wu Chao-hsieh has internationally clamored that “Taiwan is a sovereign state,” peddled “Taiwan independence” propositions, and gone to great lengths to serve as a pawn of external anti-China forces, continuously provoking “independence.” Acts of “Taiwan independence” by people like Wu Chao-hsieh cannot change the iron fact that Taiwan is part of China, and cannot shake the international pattern of one China. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: unification is the right path, and “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Any conduct of colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and resist unification will ultimately be settled.\nWe oppose any form of official exchanges between Taiwan, China, and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the relevant countries to match their words with their deeds, abide by the one-China principle through concrete actions, handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately, not provide a stage and convenience for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387220.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","In her National Day speech, Tsai Ing-wen claimed that the so-called “four insistences” she put forward are not the personal or DPP party-line positions, but conform to Taiwan’s mainstream public opinion and current needs. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities' so-called “four adherences” openly deny that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and are a blatant peddling of the “two-state theory.” No matter how they package or polish it, they cannot conceal their evil intention of seeking “independence,” provoking, and splitting the country. This reckless conduct is an extremely dangerous act of playing with fire, will inevitably heighten tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait, and push Taiwan compatriots into peril. Anyone or any force that attempts to split the country will come to no good end and will inevitably end in complete failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387226.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","In response to the PLA's recent exercises and training activities in the Taiwan Strait, MAC head Qiu Taisan said the situation “has reached a quasi-wartime deployment,” which was criticized as manipulating “fear of China” and raised questions. Qiu Taisan, Su Chang-chih, Chen Ming-tong and others then said, “No one wants war” and “if there are no unexpected incidents, there will be no war during Tsai Ing-wen's…","These remarks precisely expose the DPP authorities’ hypocritical nature: on one hand, they stoke “anti-China, fear-China” populism and create confrontation between the two sides, while on the other hand they pretend to “maintain the status quo and hope for peace.” They further expose their true intention to distort right and wrong, play up the mainland’s “military threat,” coerce Taiwan public opinion, deceive international public opinion, and constantly pursue “independence” provocations.\nThe DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces collude with external forces, continuously carry out “independence” provocations, and openly peddle the “two-state theory.” This is the root cause of the current tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. The PLA’s exercises and training are necessary actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. They target “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, including peddling the “two-state theory,” and external interference, with the aim of fundamentally safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. Only by containing “Taiwan independence” can peace in the Taiwan Strait be guaranteed and cross-Strait relations return to the right track.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387225.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The DPP recently claimed that “constitutional amendment” is a response to changes in Taiwan's situation and “some necessary reforms concerning Taiwan's future,” that it is “entirely Taiwan's internal affair,” and that it “does not need the other side of the strait to point fingers.” What comments do you have on this?","After Chen Shui-bian took office in 2000, the DPP authorities plotted to split Taiwan from China through a so-called \"constitutional revision\" approach, and once pushed cross-Strait relations to the dangerous brink. Their reckless conduct is plain for all to see.\nAt present, the DPP authorities stubbornly maintain their \"Taiwan independence\" position, frantically carry out provocations seeking \"independence,\" and persistently manipulate the \"constitutional amendment\" issue, harboring sinister intentions such as lowering the threshold to open the door for seeking \"independence\" and smuggling in the agenda of seeking \"independence.\" Their claim that \"'constitutional amendment' concerns Taiwan's future\" precisely reveals their true aim. Taiwan is a treasured island of the motherland, and Taiwan's future is absolutely not a \"matter of Taiwan's internal affairs\"; rather, it concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and can and must only be decided jointly by all Chinese people. The complete reunification of the motherland is where Taiwan's future lies. This is a settled conclusion.\nWe firmly oppose any form of \"constitutional amendment for independence\" or any other act aimed at splitting the country, and those who seek \"independence\" will surely be severely punished. All responsible political parties and far-sighted people on the island should see through the DPP authorities' schemes and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the well-being of the Taiwan public through concrete action. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots should also remain highly vigilant and consciously oppose and resist all forms of \"constitutional amendment for independence\" conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387224.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","It is reported that relevant departments may soon enact special legislation to punish “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","“Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to national reunification and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. Resolutely cracking down on die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements is a necessary part of safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and also a necessary measure to ensure the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. “The net of the law is vast; though its meshes are sparse, nothing escapes” (法网恢恢，疏而不漏). Any die-hard “Taiwan independence” element who organizes, plans, or carries out acts to split the country or undermine national unification will be severely punished. This includes the ringleaders who manipulate “constitutional amendment to seek independence” and who open doors of convenience for those seeking “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387221.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","After measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, such as the “31 Measures” and the “26 Measures,” were issued, all localities actively promoted their implementation. What results have been achieved so far in helping Taiwan compatriots obtain professional and technical occupational qualifications?","Since the “31 Measures” and “26 Measures” were introduced, the competent authorities have actively guided localities in promoting the implementation of measures enabling Taiwan compatriots to take professional and technical personnel and skilled personnel occupational qualification examinations, and phased results have been achieved.\nFirst, regarding occupational qualification examinations for professional and technical personnel. The “31 Measures” explicitly stipulate that Taiwan compatriots may register to take examinations for 53 occupational qualifications for professional and technical personnel. Since 2008, a total of 1,351 Taiwan compatriots have registered to take occupational qualification examinations for professional and technical personnel, including 237 in Guangdong, 213 in Fujian, and more than 100 each in Shanghai and Jiangsu. These mainly involve occupational qualifications such as licensed pharmacist, first-class constructor, social worker occupational qualification, registered safety engineer, and translation professional qualification. A total of 111 people passed.\nSecond, regarding skills evaluation for skilled personnel. Relevant evaluation work includes three methods: occupational skills appraisal, occupational skill level certification, and direct recognition of occupational skill qualifications from Taiwan.\n(1) Occupational skills appraisal. In July 2020, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security clarified that occupational qualifications for skilled personnel at the level-evaluation category would no longer be certified and issued by the government or units authorized by it, but would instead be converted to socialized level certification. Taiwan compatriots may, in accordance with regulations, take occupational skills appraisals and obtain occupational qualification certificates. To date, a cumulative total of 4,650 Taiwan examinees in Fujian Province have taken occupational skills appraisals for 26 occupations (types of work) such as beauty care, hairdressing, and psychological counselor, and 4,224 people have obtained occupational qualification certificates at various levels.\n(2) Occupational skill level certification. At the end of 2018, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security stipulated that the main body for occupational skill level evaluation work would change from the government to market entities such as employers and social training and evaluation organizations. Taiwan compatriots may, in accordance with regulations, take occupational skill level certification and obtain occupational skill level certificates. In May 2020, the Fujian Talent Development Center (China Strait Talent Market) organized and implemented the first occupational skill level certification examination for Taiwan compatriots, marking the official launch of the pilot work of market entities certifying occupational skill levels for Taiwan compatriots. To date, Fujian has successively conducted occupational skill level certification for eight batches of Taiwan compatriots, and a total of 82 Taiwan compatriots have obtained occupational skill level certificates.\n(3) Direct recognition of Taiwan occupational skill qualifications. This approach is currently carried out only in Fujian. In 2018, Fujian announced direct recognition of five Taiwan occupational skill qualifications, including Chinese-style cook, Western-style cook, beautician, hairdresser, and auto repair worker. From 2019 to 2021, the scope of recognized qualifications was expanded to 20 Taiwan occupational skill qualifications, including eyeglass lens making, lathe operator, and milling machine operator. To date, a total of 1,437 Taiwan compatriots have obtained corresponding occupational qualification certificates through the above methods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387217.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","The DPP authorities have continually manipulated the situation, attempting to “decouple” cross-strait economic and trade relations. However, we note that against the backdrop of the COVID-19 pandemic, cross-strait economic and trade exchanges have not stopped. Please introduce recent cross-strait economic and trade exchanges, and which activities are expected to be held next?","At previous press conferences, we introduced exchanges in various cross-strait fields, including culture. Now, I will further introduce recent cross-strait economic and trade exchange activities.\nRecently, relevant departments and localities, while doing a good job of epidemic prevention and control, held a series of cross-strait economic and trade exchange activities that were rich in content, diverse in form, and fruitful. The main ones include: the 15th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Cooperation and Development Forum held in Xiamen on September 8; the 2021 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference cross-strait modern agriculture and rural revitalization special project matchmaking event held in Zhumadian, Henan, from September 25 to 28; the 13th Chongqing·Taiwan Week held in Chongqing from September 26 to 30; the promotion meeting for the construction of the Cross-Strait New and Old Kinetic Energy Conversion Industrial Cooperation Zone and the license-granting ceremony and the 2021 Cross-Strait Agriculture Forum held in Weifang, Shandong, on October 11; the 15th Hunan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Conference and the first Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Yuelu Mountain Forum held in Changsha, Hunan, from October 20 to 22; and the 2021 Cross-Strait (Sichuan-Chongqing) Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference held in Chengdu, Sichuan, from October 21 to 24. Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan enterprises have eagerly participated in the above activities, fully demonstrating their optimism about the development prospects of the mainland and their positive attitude toward cross-strait exchanges and cooperation.\nBefore the end of this year, a number of cross-strait economic and trade exchange activities are also being planned intensively, such as the 2021 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference cross-strait smart kitchenware industry special matchmaking event, the 12th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo, the 24th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, the 27th Shandong-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference, the 14th Tianjin-Taiwan Investment and Cooperation Negotiation Conference, the 17th Guilin-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum, the 17th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week, and the 2021 Zhejiang·Taiwan Cooperation Week. Relevant departments and localities will, in light of the epidemic trend and on the premise of meeting prevention and control requirements, hold the above activities as circumstances permit. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan enterprises to participate at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211027_12387219.htm"],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The concentrated activities of the 9th Straits Youth Festival will soon take place. Please Spokesperson introduce the relevant information.","To further explore a new path for cross-Strait integrated development and promote youth exchanges across the Strait, the 9th Cross-Strait Youth Festival concentrated activities, co-hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the All-China Youth Federation and the People's Government of Fujian Province, will be held in Fuzhou, Fujian, from October 28 to November 1. The theme is “Cooperation · Development · Future,” centered on the main line of “promoting integration through connectivity, through benefits and through emotion,” and adopts a combination of online and offline formats with linked events in multiple locations. This year, a total of 24 activities will be held throughout the year, covering many fields including Fujian at sea, the digital economy, rural revitalization, community building, intangible cultural heritage, entrepreneurship and innovation, meteorology and environmental protection, culture and arts, and sports and education. Youth from both sides of the Strait are widely invited to take part in activity design, and the forms are more diverse and the content more creative. At that time, more than 1,200 quality job positions for Taiwan youth will also be released, providing opportunities and a platform for Taiwan youth to pursue their dreams on the mainland. More than 2,000 Taiwan youth are expected to take part in the activities.\nSince 2013, the Cross-Strait Youth Festival has been successfully held eight times, creating distinctive programs such as the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the Cross-Strait College Students' Leadership Camp and the Cross-Strait College Students' Physical Construction Competition. It has attracted a total of 30,000 youth from both sides of the Strait and become a “golden brand” for exchanges, interaction, heart-to-heart communication and integration among cross-Strait youth. We welcome youth from both sides of the Strait to register for Youth Festival activities, and we also welcome journalists from media on both sides of the Strait to cover them, provided epidemic prevention and control is well managed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan patriot Chu Kao-cheng, who supports reunification, has passed away. How does the spokesperson assess Chu Kao-cheng's role in the development of cross-Strait relations?","Mr. Chu Kao-cheng resolutely opposed “Taiwan independence,” supported national reunification, enthusiastically promoted Chinese culture, and actively carried out cross-Strait exchanges. We express deep mourning at his passing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","A fire at the “City of Cities” building in Kaohsiung, Taiwan, caused 46 deaths, including 3 mainland spouses. Please introduce the relevant situation of the mainland's assistance to the relatives of the deceased mainland spouses.","Upon learning that three mainland spouses died in the fire at the “Cheng Zhong Cheng” building in Kaohsiung, relevant mainland authorities promptly contacted their relatives on the mainland, expressed concern and condolences, and actively assisted relatives planning to travel to Taiwan in handling the relevant procedures; all of them successfully travelled to Taiwan last week. After entering Taiwan, some local civil groups also extended condolences to and assisted the mainland spouses’ relatives, and we express our thanks here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Recently, US-Taiwan collusion has not let up. Taiwan media reported that the Biden administration is discussing with the DPP authorities the possibility of delivering F-16V fighter jets early. At the same time, the Taiwan Army is planning to “reorganize five infantry brigades to strengthen beach and shore defense capabilities.” May I ask how the spokesperson views the Taiwan military’s intention to buy fighter…","Behind the recent intensified collusion and provocation between the United States and Taiwan lies the malicious intent of “using Taiwan to contain China” and the scheme of “relying on the United States to seek independence.” No matter how they collude and stir things up, it will be in vain. I want to emphasize four points here:\nFirst, the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait at present is the intensified collusion between the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and external forces, and their continued “Taiwan independence” provocations, including the blatant peddling of the “two-state theory.” This is the root cause of undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and raising the risks of the situation there.\nSecond, the United States constantly wants to make trouble over the Taiwan question and repeatedly challenges China's core interests, but this is a futile effort. Today's China fears no suppression from any country. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” and to stop all arms sales to Taiwan.\nThird, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, going deep into debt to buy arms, can only “blow the whistle to boost their courage”; they will never grow “muscles” and cannot bring about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They use the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people to buy weapons from the United States at exorbitant prices. Who profits from these losing deals, who lines their own pockets, and whose interests are harmed is self-evident.\nFourth, we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence,” and we will never allow Taiwan to split away from China. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and powerful capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity! If the Democratic Progressive Authorities continue to indulge in the illusion of “relying on the United States to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force,” and dare to take desperate risks, they will surely meet with utter destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海记者","October 25 marks the 76th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. What is the significance of commemorating the restoration of Taiwan today? In recent years, the DPP authorities have blindly pursued “de-Sinicization” and distorted history. What impact has this had on young people on the island?","Seventy-six years ago, Taiwan returned to the motherland. This was the result of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, winning the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan, and it should be remembered and commemorated by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We note that many anti-“Taiwan independence” political parties and unification groups on the island held various commemorative activities. On October 25, the China Memorial Hall of the Victims of the Japanese Aggression also held an academic symposium marking the 76th anniversary of Taiwan’s Restoration.\nFor some time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have blatantly manipulated “de-Sinicization” and gradual “Taiwan independence,” promoting and instilling the “Taiwan independence view of history,” attempting to sever the flesh-and-blood ties between Taiwan compatriots and the Chinese nation and to distort the national and ethnic identity of Taiwan residents, especially the younger generation. The poison spreads and harms future generations. Commemorating Taiwan’s Restoration has important practical significance for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to remember history together, learn from the past to understand the future, carry forward the great national spirit, shoulder the great righteousness of the nation together, oppose and contain “Taiwan independence,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","TSMC is the backbone of Taiwan's semiconductor industry. It is reported that TSMC has decided to submit commercial data by November 8 as requested by the US government. Public opinion on the island has criticized the DPP authorities for allowing the United States to exert pressure in this matter. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have seen the relevant reports and will continue to follow developments. We also note that public opinion on the island holds that this U.S. move will cause serious impact on Taiwan's industrial chain. Public opinion on the island also comments that, compared with the mainland's firm support for Huawei, the DPP authorities have “silenced” themselves, and their response is full of absurd “Ah Q”-style logic. Public opinion is also asking: is this the fate of those who beg for pity from external forces?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","A poll in Taiwan shows that, regarding the performance of the DPP authorities in handling cross-strait relations, 48% of respondents are dissatisfied and 40% are satisfied. Compared with last year, when nearly half of respondents were satisfied, this represents a significant change. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted the relevant public opinion polls, and we have also noted that opinion on the island holds that this is a backlash and resistance from the broad masses of Taiwan residents against the DPP authorities’ behavior of creating “anti-China and hatred of China,” undermining cross-Strait relations, and carrying out provocations to seek “independence.”\nFor some time, Taiwan residents’ perception of the military tensions across the Taiwan Strait and the rising risks to the Taiwan Strait situation has continued to grow. The fundamental cause is that the DPP authorities have intensified their collusion with external forces and constantly carried out “Taiwan independence” provocations, including brazenly peddling the “two-state theory,” increasingly pushing Taiwan toward danger. We hope that more Taiwan compatriots will see through their political self-interest and sinister intentions, reject their seduction and coercion through concrete actions, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence,” and safeguard their own interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","A World Trade Organization official recently said that Taiwan's so-called “specific trade concerns” regarding the mainland's temporary suspension of imports of custard apples and wax apples have been placed on the agenda of the WTO Committee on Sanitary and Phytosanitary Measures' November regular meeting. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Affairs across the Taiwan Strait are internal affairs handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The fundamental way to resolve this problem is for the DPP authorities to genuinely fulfill their regulatory responsibility, solve the relevant problems at their source, and stop continuing to politicize and manipulate the issue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾ETToday新闻云记者","Russian President Vladimir Putin recently said, “The mainland does not need to use force. Relying on economic strength alone, it can achieve the goal of unification.” In view of the severe situation across the Taiwan Strait, the people of Taiwan are also very worried: in what way will the Taiwan question be resolved in the future? Second question: An American talk show recently discussed the Taiwan Strait issue,…","On the first question: China's historic mission of complete reunification must be realized, and it certainly can be realized! We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts, because achieving reunification by peaceful means best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. We do not promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures; this is directed at foreign interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. China's just cause of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and advancing national reunification has won broad understanding and support from the international community, including Russia.\nOn the second question: we do not comment on a foreign TV program. We have always believed that opposing “Taiwan independence” and hoping for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. We also always adhere to the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” implement the development philosophy centered on the people, unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and work together for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","After the Taiwan film 《时光机》 (Time Machine), which was adapted from a mainland work, was exposed as receiving subsidies from Taiwan’s official bodies and its director had previously made inappropriate remarks, the film’s lead actor Chen Linong requested to terminate his contract. Is it now necessary for Taiwan entertainers who want to develop on the mainland to first declare their support for unification and…","It is understood that the situation you describe does not exist. For a long time, we have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait cultural and entertainment exchanges, welcomed Taiwan entertainers to develop in the mainland, and supported more Taiwan performers in sharing opportunities and realizing their dreams in the development of the mainland’s cultural industry. We hope that Taiwan performers, while developing their careers in the mainland, will shoulder due social responsibility, abide by relevant regulations, exert positive influence as public figures, and play an active role in enhancing the emotional bonds and spiritual affinity between compatriots on both sides. Some Taiwan performers have, through practical actions, expressed a clear stance in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and supporting national reunification, which deserves full affirmation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","Taiwan's economic affairs authority recently released data showing that mainland investment in Taiwan in the first three quarters of this year decreased by 70% compared with the same period, and some Taiwanese experts believe this is the result of obstacles deliberately created by the DPP authorities. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","That statement is entirely correct. In recent years, in order to seek political private gain and in coordination with external forces, the DPP authorities have continually concocted bad laws and unscrupulously restricted and obstructed mainland enterprises from investing in Taiwan. In the end, this harms the vital interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","Chen Tsung-yen, deputy commander of Taiwan's “Epidemic Command Center,” recently responded to media questions by asking, “What country is the mainland?”, which caused an uproar. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I want to ask him first: who exactly is he? What are his ancestors like? Where does his family come from? Whose blood runs in his veins? Someone who betrays his ancestry and his clan is truly not worth commenting on. This is nothing more than a farce he staged to beg for a petty official post.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, some KMT members are preparing to propose at the KMT National Congress the establishment of an anti-“Taiwan independence” working group, arguing that opposing “Taiwan independence” is a historic responsibility the Kuomintang should bear. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation for exchanges between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party, and also the common political foundation for cross-Strait relations. At present, the situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. We are willing to work with the Kuomintang to adhere to the common political foundation, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, join hands to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the common well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","It is reported that the British Defence Secretary recently claimed that “mainland incursions into Taiwan's air defense identification zone are dangerous and could possibly trigger conflict.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","First, Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no interference from external forces. We hope that certain British officials will abide by the commitments the British side made to China when the two countries established diplomatic relations, and not cause damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond, I would like to remind them to recognize right from wrong. The root cause of the current tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities' “seeking independence” and provocative activities in collusion with external forces, not the just act of the Chinese People's Liberation Army in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","The song “Glass Heart,” sung by a Malaysian singer and an Australian singer of Chinese descent, recently ranked third on a certain Asian pop chart, and some mainland netizens have expressed dissatisfaction with the song. How does the spokesperson view this matter?","I hear the implication in your question, and I will respond here.\nSince 2016, the DPP authorities have undermined cross-Strait relations, continuously carried out provocations to seek “independence,” and created “anti-China” populist sentiment. Those who sow melons reap melons, and those who sow beans reap beans. Their reckless actions have aroused the anger and counterattacks of the vast number of netizens, which is entirely natural. It is not difficult to see that since 2008 and before 2016, no such situation existed. Who is the root cause of the current situation and who is the chief culprit goes without saying. Eliminating this situation is not difficult; as long as everyone firmly opposes “Taiwan independence,” and especially as long as the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots maintain awareness and vigilance. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and will ultimately move toward heart-to-heart harmony.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","According to reports, the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention agency recently said that the DPP authorities are planning digital certificates for vaccination. In principle, all vaccines approved by the WHO may be included, and only if evidence is found proving insufficient efficacy might the two mainland vaccines be excluded. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have discussed this matter on many occasions. The Sinopharm and Sinovac COVID-19 vaccines received WHO Emergency Use Listing on May 7, 2021 and June 1, respectively, making them two COVID-19 vaccines that have passed WHO verification for safety, efficacy and quality. As of October 25, the mainland had reported a cumulative total of 2.249 billion doses of COVID-19 vaccine administered. According to incomplete statistics, as of October 15, about 165,000 compatriots from Taiwan had been vaccinated on the mainland, with a cumulative total of about 315,000 doses administered. All of this fully demonstrates that mainland vaccines are safe, reliable and effective. We have stated many times that we are willing to provide compatriots in Taiwan with mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO. The sooner the DPP authorities agree to allow mainland vaccines into Taiwan and recognize their efficacy, the more it will help safeguard the health and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Chen Ting-fei, a “Taiwan independence” public representative, recently said that the mainland may stop the ECFA agreement starting New Year’s Day next year, and that the mainland will fully resume tariffs on Taiwan. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","The Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait has brought real benefits to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. The fundamental reason why people in Taiwan worry about the fate of ECFA is that the DPP authorities have undermined cross-Strait economic and cultural cooperation and harmed the vital interests of Taiwan's businesses and people. As long as the DPP authorities do not stop their provocative “seeking independence” and do not stop harming the interests of the people, the people's worries will persist.\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all for attending. Goodbye!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202110/t20211027_12387213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-28","Wang Wenbin","MASTV","The leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen confirmed in a recent interview that US troops are present on the island to help with training. She claimed that the threat from Beijing is growing \"every day\". What is your comment on this?","The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. On the Taiwan question, the US should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, rather than something unilaterally concocted by itself. We firmly oppose official and military ties in any form between the US and the Taiwan region, and oppose the US interference in China’s internal affairs. The US vessels have repeatedly flexed its muscles to make provocations and stir up troubles in the Taiwan Strait in recent times, sending gravely wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces and threatening cross-Strait peace and stability. The international community is clear-eyed about who is engaging in “coercion” on the Taiwan question.\nThe cross-Strait reunification is an overriding historical trend and the right course, while “Taiwan independence” is a retrogression leading to a dead end. The DPP authorities’ acts of seeking “Taiwan independence” can not change the iron-clad fact that Taiwan is a part of China, neither will it shake the international community’s universal and firm commitment to the one-China principle. Those who forget their heritage, betray their motherland, and seek to split the country will come to no good end.\nSeeking “Taiwan independence” leads to a dead end. So does supporting “Taiwan independence”. No country and no one should underestimate the resolve, the will, and the ability of the Chinese people to defend their national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Otherwise, they will suffer another defeat.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347148.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211028_10349005.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-28","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","At the East Asia Summit (EAS) on October 27, the Japanese leader interfered in China’s internal affairs including Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang, accused China of activities that violate Japan's sovereignty in the East China Sea and violate UNCLOS in the South China Sea and expressed opposition to economic coercion in the region. Do you have any comment?","On a multilateral occasion, the Japanese leader, in total disregard of facts, has engaged in “smearing diplomacy” and grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs. Such acts are not constructive to the healthy and steady development of China-Japan relations and regional peace and stability. The Chinese side has lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347148.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211028_10349005.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-28","Wang Wenbin","AFP","A quick follow-up. Taiwan’s Tsai Ing-wen has confirmed a small number of US troops are present in Taiwan to help with training, adding that she has faith that the American military will defend the island in the event of a military maneuver by Beijing. How does Beijing view these comments? Also adding to that, President Biden on Wednesday criticized Beijing’s coercive actions across the Taiwan Strait while…","I just took a similar question. I want to stress that seeking “Taiwan independence” leads to a dead end. So does supporting “Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347148.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211028_10349005.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-28","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","The US Secretary of State Antony Blinken recently issued a statement that encourages all UN Member States to join the US in supporting Taiwan’s robust, meaningful participation throughout the UN system and in the international community, and highlighted Taiwan’s participation in ICAO and the WHO. What is your comment?","The US statement seriously violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, violates the promise it has made, violates the basic norms governing international relations, and has sent seriously wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. China deplores and firmly opposes this, and has made clear its solemn position to and lodged stern representations with the US.\nOn the issue of the Taiwan region’s participation in the UN and other international organizations, China has made its position clear many times. There is only one China in the world. The government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory, which is a fact based on history and jurisprudence that no one and no force can change. The participation of the Taiwan region in activities of international organizations, including the WHO and ICAO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Fifty years ago, Resolution 2758 adopted by the General Assembly restored the lawful seat of the PRC in the UN, and has solved once and for all the issue of the China’s representation in the UN in political, legal and procedural terms. The system, agencies and the Secretariat of the UN should abide by the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758 when dealing with Taiwan-related affairs. The WHO, ICAO and other relevant international agencies all affirmed this fundamental principle in resolution or in other legal forms.\nThe Taiwan authorities recalcitrantly stick to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to recognize the 1992 consensus. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the activities of the WHO and ICAO has ceased to exist. The responsibility fully rests with the Taiwan authorities. In fact, on the premise of the one-China principle, the Central Government of China has made proper arrangement for the Taiwan region’s participation in international cooperation in various areas. In the health sector, there is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in Taiwan. Taiwan enjoys unimpeded channel and sound mechanism for information exchanges with the WHO and countries in the world. Medical and health experts in the Taiwan region also regularly attend WHO technical meetings and activities. In the civil aviation sector, the Taiwan region is linked to many cities in the world with convenient flights and has unfettered access to standards, suggested measures and other information from ICAO. The US statement exalts Taiwan’s “contributions” in the science and health sectors and endeavors to solicit support for its participation in activities of the UN and other international organizations under such pretexts as a “gap” in the defense against COVID-19 and aviation safety. It is attempting to achieve political goals by fabricating lies to angle for sympathy. The international community has long seen through this sort of political trick. In recent years, when certain countries hyped up Taiwan-related issues on the platforms of the World Health Assembly and the International Civil Aviation Conference, they were opposed unanimously by all countries upholding justice and their attempts were foiled time and again. This fully demonstrates that the one-China principle is the overriding trend with strong popular support in the international community and shall not be defied.\nWe urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, comply with UNGA Resolution 2758, stop issuing irresponsible erroneous remarks, stop assisting Taiwan in expanding its so-called “international space”, refrain from sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and uphold the political foundation for China-US relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347148.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211028_10349005.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-10-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped up recently that the mainland's military drills around Taiwan are “irresponsible” “provocations.” According to Taiwanese media, the Taiwan military recently carried out heavy artillery firing training and test-firing of the “Wuxian Gao” missile, and conducted anti-landing drills. What is your comment on this?","The white paper “The Taiwan Question and the Cause of China's Reunification in the New Era,” published recently, comprehensively and systematically sets out Taiwan's historical record and legal facts of belonging to China since ancient times, as well as the positions, principles and policies for advancing national reunification in the new era. The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, for their own selfish interests, have not hesitated to abandon the great righteousness of the nation, colluding with external forces to engage in provocations for “independence.” This is the root cause of the escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The series of military operations we recently organized is a deterrent and punishment against “Taiwan independence” separatists and interference by external forces. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” will only plunge Taiwan into an abyss of disaster and bring profound harm to compatriots in Taiwan. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces: if they remain obsessed with relying on foreign powers to raise their own standing and persist in provocations for “independence” without repentance or stopping, we will continue to let our actions speak and resolutely take countermeasures.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/10-28/9597107.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-10-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, recently, the US State Department has intensified its “support for Taiwan” by approving arms sales projects for Taiwan; US and Canadian warships have transited the Taiwan Strait; and the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee passed the “Taiwan Policy Act of 2022,” which includes provisions such as providing military financing to Taiwan and accelerating the processing of Taiwan’s arms…","The relevant conduct of the U.S. side seriously violates China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and seriously impacts the military-to-military relations between China and the United States. We are highly concerned about this, firmly oppose it, and have lodged stern representations with the U.S. side. For some time, some people on the U.S. side have violated international law and basic norms of international relations, violated the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, reneged on solemn political commitments made to China on the Taiwan question, obstinately clung to the strategy of “using Taiwan to contain China,” continuously hollowed out and emptied the one-China principle, strengthened U.S.-Taiwan military collusion, and encouraged and supported the DPP authorities in intensifying cross-Strait confrontation. This series of provocative acts is very dangerous and extremely harmful. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and concerns China’s core interests. Regarding the U.S. side’s erroneous conduct on Taiwan, we will firmly counter it. We advise the U.S. side to stop military collusion with the DPP authorities of Taiwan; otherwise it will bear the serious consequences arising therefrom.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/10-28/9597107.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-10-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. White House recently released its National Security Strategy report, claiming that China is the only competitor with both the intention and the capability to reshape the international order, and that it poses the most serious geopolitical challenge to the United States. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","This U.S. report is full of Cold War mentality and zero-sum game thinking. It deliberately exaggerates China's \"challenge,\" geopolitical conflicts, and great-power competition, draws ideological lines to maliciously create bloc confrontation, and questions China's normal military development. This is a misjudgment of China-U.S. relations and a misreading of China's development, and it runs counter to the theme of the times of peaceful development and the common expectations of the international community.\nAs a founding member of the United Nations and a permanent member of the Security Council, China firmly follows the path of peaceful development, actively participates in reform and construction of the global governance system, and has always been a firm defender of the international system centered on the United Nations and the international order based on international law. This has long been a consensus in the international community and an established fact, and it cannot be turned upside down by a report issued by any one country. By contrast, this U.S. report still follows the playbook of creating enemies, forming cliques, and expanding military forces. It militarily pursues \"integrated deterrence,\" accelerates the construction of the \"triad\" nuclear forces, creates pretexts for seeking and consolidating hegemony and power politics, and places its own interests above international justice. This is the real major threat and severe challenge to the international system and international order.\nWhen China and the United States cooperate, both benefit; when they confront each other, both suffer. We urge the U.S. side to view the development of China and the Chinese military objectively and rationally, to put into practice President Biden's statement of \"four noes and one non-intention,\" to move in the same direction as China, and to push China-U.S. relations back onto the track of healthy and stable development.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/10-28/9597107.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-10-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 28 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a question on the 28th, saying that Tsai Ing-wen and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have stubbornly pushed “Taiwan independence,” spreading “Taiwan independence” remarks internationally on various occasions, packaging “Taiwan independence” propositions under the guise…","Ma Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities keep provoking “Taiwan independence.” This is the root cause of undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and raising the risk of the Taiwan Strait situation. The DPP authorities “resist reunification by force” and “seek independence by relying on the United States,” and use the hard-earned money of the people of Taiwan to buy weapons, which will only harm the interests of the people of Taiwan and bring the calamity of war to the island. We have zero tolerance for “Taiwan independence.” We will spare no cost in combating “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, strong will, and powerful capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!\nMa Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the People’s Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing all of China. Taiwan has no right to join the United Nations, an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. We understand the thoughts and feelings of Taiwan compatriots about participating in international activities, and on the basis of upholding the one-China principle, appropriate arrangements have been made in the past and can be made in the future. It is absolutely impossible for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to seek “independence” through “participation in international activities.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that we urge the governments and media of relevant countries to recognize the essence of the DPP authorities’ pursuit of “independence,” abide by the one-China principle, not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and not provide any platform for “Taiwan independence” remarks, so as to avoid further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211028_12387558.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-10-29","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","In recent days, the spokesperson of the foreign ministry has made elaborate and comprehensive responses to US Secretary of State Antony Blinken’s Taiwan-related statement. I want to follow up on a specific part. Blinken particularly stressed that Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system is not a political issue, but a pragmatic one. US officials also claimed that China “abused” UNGA Resolution 2758. Do…","The relevant remarks by the US side are a distortion of historical facts. Here, I’d like to shed some light on the truth.\nFifty years ago, before the UNGA reviewed the draft resolution submitted by Albania and Algeria, known as Resolution 2758, the US and some other few countries put forward the so-called reverse-IQ draft resolution and the \"dual representation\" draft resolution in order to retain the Taiwan authorities’ seat. The former required that any proposal to deprive Taiwan of representation at the UN would require a two-thirds supermajority for approval, and the latter required accepting the representatives of the PRC while retaining the representation of Taiwan. The reverse-IQ draft resolution failed to pass. With the adoption of Resolution 2758, the PRC has fully restored its lawful seat at the UN. The “dual representation” proposal by the few countries including the US immediately became null and void.\nThe historical facts have clearly shown that the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan region is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The system, agencies and the Secretariat of the UN should abide by the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758 when dealing with Taiwan-related affairs. These principles have been universally recognized by the international community since half a century ago.\nThe one-China principle brooks no challenge and Resolution 2758 cannot be distorted. Fifty years ago, the attempt by a few countries to reject the one-China principle and obstruct the passing of Resolution 2758 was foiled. Fifty years later, anyone that tries to challenge the one-China principle and Resolution 2758 will suffer a greater defeat.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347149.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211029_10403693.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-10-29","Wang Wenbin","","《北京青年报》记者：近日，外交部发言人针对美国务卿布林肯此前发表的涉台声明作了详细且全面的回应。我想就一个细节问题提问。布林肯特别强调，台湾有意义地“参与”联合国体系是务实问题而非政治问题。美方官员还声称中国“滥用”联大第2758号决议。请问你对此有何回应？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202110/t20211029_10403693.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[2,"2021-10-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 29 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 29th, saying that since 2016, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have denied the “1992 Consensus,” undermined the basis for cross-Strait dialogue, and shut the door on cross-Strait consultation and dialogue. The root cause of the current complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, together with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, have intensified collusion with external forces, openly peddled the “two-state theory,” and constantly engaged in provocations to pursue “independence.” This is a deliberate act by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, and it is a fact clearly understood by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. There is no such thing as “misunderstanding, miscalculation or misjudgment.”\nA reporter asked: Recently, in an interview with CNN, Tsai Ing-wen said that Taiwan has repeatedly stated its willingness to engage in dialogue with the mainland, which is the best way to avoid misunderstanding, miscalculation and misjudgment in handling cross-Strait relations. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in response.\nHe pointed out that adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” is a fundamental and critical issue in cross-Strait relations, and a touchstone for testing whether there is genuine sincerity for dialogue and whether cross-Strait relations, peaceful development, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots are truly upheld. On the one hand, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities fawn on external anti-China forces, eagerly seek to ingratiate themselves with them, and cooperate with external forces’ scheme to “use Taiwan to contain China,” sacrificing the interests of Taiwan compatriots and the Chinese nation. On the other hand, they put on a hypocritical show, fabricating the appearance of willingness to engage in dialogue, shirking responsibility for their provocations to pursue “independence,” attempting to mislead Taiwan’s public and deceive the international community. This trick is extremely crude and should be abandoned!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211029_12387707.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-10-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 29 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 29th by saying that the remarks of Chiu Tai-san, chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, continue to peddle the \"two-state theory,\" continue to confuse right and wrong and reverse black and white, seek to deceive the people on the island, mislead the international community,…","Ma Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities maliciously attack the mainland and play up the so-called \"threat\" from the mainland. This is a shameless lie that reverses black and white. It is a \"pledge of allegiance\" submitted to external anti-China forces, and a begging for external forces to cheer them on in provocation, confrontation, and national division. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Our necessary actions to strike at and contain \"Taiwan independence\" have never been aimed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots; they are aimed at the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their separatist activities. It is the DPP authorities who are plotting \"independence\" and provoking conflict, colluding with external forces to undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait. This is what constitutes coercion of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and damage to the fundamental interests of the entire Chinese people.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that on the major questions of cross-Strait relations, there are only \"two adherences\": adhering to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and adhering to opposition to \"Taiwan independence.\" The so-called \"four adherences\" are a blatant insistence on peddling the \"two-state theory.\" The so-called \"unchanged commitment\" is that the commitment to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces has not changed, which will inevitably cause tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait situation, will inevitably seriously harm the security interests and livelihood and well-being of the Taiwan compatriots, will inevitably be repudiated by compatriots on both sides of the Strait and all descendants of the Chinese nation, and will also inevitably end in complete failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202110/t20211029_12387769.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-04","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News Agency","It is reported that the leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen met with members of a European Parliament delegation today. Do you have any comment?","China strongly deplores and firmly opposes the visit to Taiwan by certain members of the European Parliament and has lodged solemn representation to the European side. As a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community, the one-China principle is the political foundation for the establishment of China-EU diplomatic relations and development of ties. No official interaction with the Taiwan authorities in any form is an inherent requirement of the one-China principle. The European Parliament is an important official organ of the EU. It follows naturally that its members should fully recognize the complex and sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, stay true to the commitment made by the EU, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues and keep the political foundation for China-EU relations intact. China urges the European side to redress its mistake and avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, lest it should cause a serious impact on China-Europe relations.\nI would also like to point out that the DPP authorities in Taiwan tend to whitewash their “Taiwan independence” separatist acts under the disguise of democracy and human rights. But however hard they try to cover it, their true agenda of seeking independence is laid bare. Nor will they make a dent in the indisputable fact that Taiwan is part of China. The clumsy show of a few people won’t shake in the slightest the international community's universal and firm commitment to the one-China principle or the inevitable trend of reunification of China. Their plot is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347153.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211104_10442611.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-04","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The US Joint Chiefs Chairman Mark Milley said yesterday that the United States military absolutely has the ability to defend Taiwan from a potential attack from China. Do you have any response to this comment?","For some time, the US has been acting with negative and erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan, which has emboldened the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and heightened tensions across the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China's core interests. No one should underestimate China's firm determination and will to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will never allow anyone or any force to separate Taiwan from the motherland in any way.\nThe US should pursue a real one-China policy, instead of a fake one; fulfill its commitments to China faithfully rather than treacherously; truly implement the one-China policy and put it into action, instead of saying one thing and doing the opposite. We urge the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and avoid sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan-independence” separatist forces to prevent seriously hurting China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347153.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211104_10442611.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-11-05","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q) [per digest]","Recently, China made a statement at the Review Conference of the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, firmly opposing nuclear-powered submarine cooperation between the US, UK and Australia, and warning Japan and related countries not to replicate “nuclear sharing” in the Asia-Pacific region. Please further introduce China's position on these issues.","China has repeatedly emphasized that the nuclear submarine cooperation between the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia constitutes a serious risk of nuclear proliferation. It impacts the international nuclear non-proliferation regime, intensifies arms races, and undermines regional peace and stability. As nuclear-weapon states and parties to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, the United States and the United Kingdom transferring naval nuclear propulsion reactors and weapons-grade highly enriched uranium to non-nuclear-weapon states is a flagrant violation of the object and purpose of the Treaty. We urge the countries concerned to earnestly fulfill their non-proliferation obligations, rescind the decision to carry out nuclear submarine cooperation, and call on the international community to jointly uphold the international nuclear non-proliferation regime, which is founded on the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, and to safeguard international peace and security.\nWe have noted that some voices in countries such as Japan have recently called for seeking \"nuclear sharing\" with the United States. China believes that the countries concerned should earnestly fulfill their obligations under the Treaty and their own commitments, and stop clamoring for \"nuclear sharing\" or any other form of nuclear deterrence arrangements. Any attempt to replicate the \"nuclear sharing\" model in the Asia-Pacific region will seriously undermine the regional strategic balance and stability, and will inevitably be firmly opposed and countered by countries in the region.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-05/9603247.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2021-11-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 5 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to a question on the 5th that over a period of time, Su Tseng-chang, Yu Hsi-kun, Wu Chao-hsieh and a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards have gone to great lengths to incite cross-Strait confrontation, maliciously attacked and slandered the mainland, engaged in despicable acts in pursuit of “independence,” colluded with external forces to split the country, seriously undermined cross-Strait relations, seriously endangered peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harmed the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The mainland has, in accordance with law, imposed sanctions on the above-listed “Taiwan independence” diehards on the list, prohibiting them and their family members from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, restricting cooperation between their affiliated institutions and relevant mainland organizations and individuals, absolutely not allowing their affiliated enterprises and backers to profit on the mainland, and taking other necessary sanctions.\nA reporter asked whether it is true, as some media have reported, that the mainland is studying sanctions against “Taiwan independence” diehards. Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in response.\nShe pointed out: We solemnly warn such “Taiwan independence” diehards that those who forget their roots, betray the motherland, and split the country have never come to a good end. They will certainly be spurned by the people and face judgment by history. The mainland will, in accordance with law, pursue criminal liability against “Taiwan independence” diehards, and this will be valid for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211105_12389168.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 5: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 5th, stating that the United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is part of China and is not a sovereign state. It naturally cannot become a member of the United Nations, nor can it become a member of specialized agencies under…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that 50 years ago, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, which also rejected the so-called 'dual representation' proposal put forward at the time by the United States and others. The US is now rehashing old accounts and reviving the wrong proposition, clearly challenging the international consensus and placing itself in opposition to the majority of UN members.\nShe said that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 has clearly and thoroughly resolved the question of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally and procedurally. The Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all of China, and Taiwan is part of China. There is simply no so-called issue of 'Taiwan's participation in the United Nations.' Any matter involving Taiwan region of China within the UN system, its specialized agencies, the UN Secretariat and other bodies shall adhere to the One-China principle and UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. The World Health Organization, the International Civil Aviation Organization and other relevant international institutions have also confirmed this fundamental principle through legal instruments such as resolutions. At its root, it is the One-China principle.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the US government has stated many times that it 'does not support Taiwan's participation in international organizations that are limited to sovereign states.' The recent remarks by the US side seriously violate the basic norms of international relations, seriously contravene the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and also seriously violate the US side's consistent commitments. They not only send a seriously wrong signal to 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces, but are also yet another manifestation of the US's repeated breaches of trust on the international stage.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that we urge the US government to stop any form of support for and encouragement of 'Taiwan independence' remarks, and to abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions. Attempts to attack UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and to hype the so-called issue of 'Taiwan's participation in the UN system' will only expose the ugly side of some people in the US who ignore international justice and national credibility and will stop at nothing in playing the 'Taiwan card.'\nShe said that we advise the DPP authorities to abandon their illusions of 'relying on the US to seek independence' and 'relying on outsiders to seek independence.' Any act aimed at undermining the One-China principle and splitting the country will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211105_12389169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-08","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","It is reported that an official of the Taiwan region’s foreign affairs department said recently that Taiwan is following closely the presidential elections in Honduras and will strengthen communication with the ruling and opposition parties in Honduras to prevent the mainland from undermining their relationship through all means. Do you have any comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm of international relations and universal consensus of the international community. Upholding the one-China principle is the overriding trend with strong popular support. We want to admonish the Taiwan authorities that “Taiwan independence” leads to a dead end, “dollar diplomacy” is rejected by all, and all attempts to reverse the historical trend by soliciting foreign support are bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347155.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211108_10445594.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-11-09","Tan Kefei","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","It is reported that the air forces of China and Thailand recently held a joint air force training exercise in Thailand, codenamed “Eagle Strike-2022.” Please further introduce the relevant situation.","On the morning of August 24, the closing ceremony of the “Eagle Strike-2022” China-Thailand air force joint training exercise was held at the Udon Thani base of the Royal Thai Air Force. Members of the command groups of both sides, personnel from the Chinese Embassy in Thailand, and representatives of participating officers and soldiers attended.\nThis joint training marked the fifth time the air forces of China and Thailand have conducted joint training. The training highlighted diversity in composition, practical combat orientation in training, and integration of command; force scale has gradually expanded, subject content has come closer to actual combat, and the intensity of confrontation has continuously increased. The two sides jointly dispatched 17 aircraft of 7 types, including fighters and early-warning aircraft, to take part in the training, and conducted seminars and exchanges on mission planning, command coordination, tactical application, and comprehensive support, successfully completing training subjects including close air support, ground strike, and small- and large-scale force employment. This joint training deepened practical cooperation between the two militaries, enhanced the tactical and technical levels of both sides, and helps jointly maintain regional security and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2021/11-09/9605697.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-11-10","Wang Wenbin","RIA Novosti","Taiwanese media reported yesterday that several members of the US Congress have visited Taiwan yesterday on a military plane. Do you have any comment on this?","The visit of the relevant members of the US Congress gravely violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques. China firmly opposes this and has lodged solemn representation with the US side. We ask the US side to immediately stop all forms of official interactions with Taiwan and avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, lest it should seriously undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The one-China principle is an unshakable norm governing international relations. China's reunification is an unstoppable trend of history. On both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our compatriots in Taiwan, share the overwhelming aspiration for national reunification. The clumsy show of a handful of \"Taiwan independence\" elements and foreign politicians cannot change the unbreakable landscape where 180 countries in the world are committed to the one-China principle.\nWe urge the relevant US lawmakers to get a clear understanding of the situation: it is a dangerous game to collude with \"Taiwan independence\" forces, and joining the \"Taiwan independence\" forces in playing with fire will only get oneself burnt. All adventurist and provocative moves to confront the trend of China's reunification is like an ant trying to topple a giant tree and will end up in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347157.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211110_10446600.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-10","Wang Wenbin","TBS","Yesterday the PLA conducted a patrol in the Taiwan Strait. Does it have anything to do with the fact that US lawmakers visited Taiwan?","As for this combat readiness patrol of the PLA military aircraft, I would refer you to competent authorities. As for the US congressmen's visit to Taiwan, I have just answered the question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347157.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211110_10446600.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on November 10, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","For some time, the US has continually taken negative actions regarding arms sales to Taiwan and strengthening US-Taiwan military ties, which has heightened tensions in the Taiwan Strait. In response, the Chinese side has said the US should take China's position and concerns seriously and stop improper words and deeds. But just last night, US Senator Kenien and others flew to Taiwan on a military aircraft and will…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge some members of the U.S. Congress to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and not to send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. Otherwise, this will only cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe DPP authorities' “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390155.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The mainland recently named Su Tseng-chang, Yu Shyi-kun and Wu Chao-hsieh, and stated that it will punish the above “Taiwan independence” diehards listed in the list in accordance with the law. What specific measures may be taken?","We will not tolerate in any way conduct that openly challenges national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and we will impose sanctions on diehard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with law. This is an inherent requirement for safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests, and also a necessary measure to ensure the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Anyone who dares to break the law will be punished in accordance with law. This includes banning diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their family members from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, restricting cooperation between their affiliated institutions and relevant mainland organizations and individuals, absolutely not allowing their affiliated enterprises and backers to profit on the mainland, and other necessary sanctions. At the same time, criminal responsibility will be pursued against diehard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with law, and this will be effective for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390160.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“海峡两岸”记者","In response to the mainland's announcement that it will punish diehard “Taiwan independence” elements such as Su Tseng-chang in accordance with law, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said it will study taking necessary countermeasures at an appropriate time. What is your comment?","Punishing a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards in accordance with the law is an inevitable requirement for safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests. It helps combat and curb “Taiwan independence” separatism, maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and protect the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. The mainland side will closely monitor relevant developments and firmly crack down on any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390159.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The measures the Taiwan Affairs Office announced to punish die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements include “absolutely not allowing their affiliated companies and backers to profit on the mainland.” May I ask the spokesperson whether this will affect Taiwanese business investment and normal cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges?","Cracking down in accordance with the law on “Taiwan independence” diehards and their main supporters, including financial backers, is precisely aimed at curbing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Fundamentally, this will help promote normal cross-strait economic and trade exchanges and help safeguard the lawful rights and interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390153.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","A responsible official of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said, “After reunification, the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be fully improved, and Taiwan's fiscal revenue can be fully used to improve people's livelihoods.” The Mainland Affairs Council of the Taiwan authorities claimed in response that the mainland “has not grasped the current state of cross-Strait relations.” What is your…","The status quo across the Taiwan Strait is clear: there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed.\nIt must be pointed out that the DPP authorities, out of political self-interest in obstinately pursuing “independence,” have gone further in using the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people to buy arms, extensively using “financial aid” to seek so-called “solidifying the alliance,” and occupying more public social resources that should have been used for the people’s livelihood and welfare in Taiwan. If the wealth created by the hard work of Taiwan’s people were not used to buy weapons or squandered on useless things such as “checkbook diplomacy,” but instead used to develop the economy and improve people’s livelihood, Taiwan’s people would not be so dissatisfied with their living conditions. Looking ahead, after cross-Strait reunification, the wealth created by Taiwan’s people can be fully used to improve livelihood, and people’s well-being will be fully enhanced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390152.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Spokespersons of the US State Department and Department of Defense recently said that the US one-China policy differs from the one-China principle of China. What comments does the spokesperson have on the US consistently inserting the “Taiwan Relations Act” and the so-called “Six Assurances” into its one-China policy?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Taiwan’s international activities, including its exchanges with countries that have diplomatic relations with China and its participation in international organizations and their activities, must all be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The three China-US joint communiqués clearly stipulate: “The United States recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan,” and “The United States acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” The so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and “Six Assurances” put forward by the US side violate the three China-US joint communiqués and crudely interfere in China’s internal affairs. They are completely wrong, illegal and null and void, and China has firmly opposed them from the very beginning. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately, and not cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390156.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 9th Strait Youth Festival Strait Youth Summit was successfully held on October 29 in Fuzhou, Fujian. According to statistics, the total online dissemination volume of the summit exceeded 130 million, the total number of online live-stream clicks was nearly 42 million, the topic dissemination volume exceeded 50 million, and cumulative coverage on overseas platforms reached 20.98 million person-times. What is…","From October 28 to November 1, the 9th Straits Youth Festival was held in more than 20 cities, including Beijing, Shanghai, Chengdu, Taipei and Taichung, through a combination of online and offline activities and linked events across multiple locations. Themed “Cooperation, Development, Future,” this year's Youth Festival saw 22 Taiwan youth associations and civil groups, 53 Taiwan universities, and 31 mainland universities participate in related exchange activities. The festival released 1,232 job positions for Taiwan youth with an average annual salary of 150,000 yuan, launched more than 1,000 sets of public rental housing, and also released 10 rural construction and rural entrepreneurship projects. Many Taiwan youth who could not attend in person due to the epidemic learned about the event and participated in interactions through media reports and online platforms. As of November 5, cross-Strait media had published more than 4,600 related reports and articles. The online dissemination of the Straits Youth Summit alone exceeded 130 million, including nearly 42 million views of online livestreams, more than 38 million views of short videos, and 20.98 million person-times of coverage on overseas platforms.\nThe successful holding of the Youth Festival fully reflects the urgent desire of cross-Strait youth to strengthen exchanges and interactions, and demonstrates the youthful energy of cross-Strait integrated development. A Taiwan youth said, “I want to build a future that is not as dull as plain boiled water.” This represents the voice of a broad number of cross-Strait youth. We will, as always, build bridges for cross-Strait young friends to exchange and interact, and provide opportunities and a stage for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams, so that more cross-Strait youth can work hand in hand, achieve their life ideals, and together realize the Chinese Dream of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","Please Spokesperson Introduce the Participation of Taiwan Businesses and Enterprises in the 4th China International Import Expo.","Since the first China International Import Expo was held in 2018, we have actively responded to the appeals of Taiwanese enterprises and provided assistance and convenience for their participation in the exhibition. This CIIE has 35 enterprises from the Taiwan region exhibiting, with a net exhibition area of 1,595 square meters. Through participation in the exhibition, enterprises will further open up the mainland market and diversified overseas markets, and will gain more business opportunities and greater returns.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan’s defense department recently claimed that since the beginning of this year, PLA aircraft entering Taiwan’s “southwest airspace” have exceeded 700 sorties, that the cross-Strait military standoff is hard to ease, and that Taiwan will face greater military pressure in the future. What comments do you have on this?","We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will absolutely not leave any space for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form. The root cause of the current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces blatantly peddle the “two-state theory” and collude with external forces to continuously engage in “independence” provocations.\nThe PLA’s holding of relevant drills and training activities is to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, to effectively respond to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, and to fundamentally safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. As long as “Taiwan independence” provocations continue, the tension in the Taiwan Strait will hardly ease.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390158.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","It is reported that Taiwan's defense authorities expect to complete the production of a “civilian survival and evacuation handbook for wartime” by next March, which has prompted speculation among Taiwan's people about “armed unification.” May I ask the spokesperson to respond to the various speculations among the public and the current atmosphere in the Taiwan Strait?","People on both sides of the Strait are very clear that \"Taiwan independence\" means the loss of peace and the arrival of disaster. For their own private interests, the DPP authorities stubbornly carry out \"independence-seeking\" provocations and do not hesitate to tie the people of Taiwan to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot. This reckless coercion of public opinion, which goes against the trend, will greatly harm the welfare of Taiwan compatriots and will inevitably meet with opposition and resistance from Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will open their eyes and not become sacrificial victims of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and jointly safeguard the vital interests of our compatriots and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","TSMC founder Morris Chang will represent Taiwan at this year's APEC informal leaders' meeting. Chang said that during the meeting he will present Taiwan's strength in applying to join the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) and strive for support. What comment do you have on this?","Personnel from the Chinese Taiwan region sent to participate in APEC-related activities must comply with the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.\nThe question of the Taiwan region’s participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. We firmly oppose the Taiwan region’s participation in any free trade arrangement of an official nature, or its signing of any free trade agreement of an official nature.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","The 20th China (Suzhou) Electronic Information Expo is about to be held. How is this year's expo going?","From November 18 to 20, the 20th China (Suzhou) Electronic Information Expo will be held in Suzhou. The expo is hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the People's Government of Jiangsu Province, supported by the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, and organized by the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, the Jiangsu Provincial Department of Industry and Information Technology, the Jiangsu Provincial Department of Commerce, and the People's Government of Suzhou Municipality. Its theme is “Digital Manufacturing, Smart Future.” The exhibition hall covers an area of over 20,000 square meters and features five major specialized exhibition zones: electronic intelligent manufacturing, optoelectronics, semiconductor and printed circuit board equipment, new-generation information technology applications, electric vehicle supply chains, and smart security. It also creates four themed special exhibition zones: “Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait,” “Shanghai-Jiangsu Same City,” “Intelligent Transformation and Digital Transformation,” and “Intelligent Driving.” At present, more than 300 enterprises have registered to exhibit, of which over 50% are Taiwan-funded enterprises. During the expo, a series of activities will be held, including an opening ceremony, keynote forums, and specialized forums, with enterprises from both sides of the Strait interacting and exchanging views at the same venue, to further promote the integrated development of the electronic information industries across the Taiwan Strait. On November 18, the opening day of the expo, the third Jiangsu Zifeng Award presentation ceremony will also be held, to honor 30 Taiwan-funded enterprises that have made positive contributions to the high-quality economic development of Jiangsu, and the government big-data application platform “Su-Tai Connect,” the first in Suzhou to serve Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan-funded enterprises, and Taiwan compatriots, will be officially launched.\nSince 2002, the expo has been successfully held 19 times and has become one of the well-known exhibitions in the cross-Strait IT industry, with the largest scale, the most exhibiting enterprises, and the most complete industrial support. It has served more than 12,000 enterprises in total. The holding of the expo has also promoted the development of Taiwan-funded electronic information industries on the mainland, especially in Suzhou, and Suzhou has become the mainland's most concentrated manufacturing base for the electronic information industry. We welcome media reporters to follow and report on the expo.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中国新闻社、中国新闻网记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je said “cross-Strait exchanges are better than a complete halt” and said this year's “Twin City Forum” will be held online. What is your comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. In recent years, good-faith exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait have been disrupted and undermined. The root cause lies in the vicious conduct of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, who incite cross-strait confrontation, collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, and harm the interests of compatriots on both sides. We hope that responsible political parties and enlightened people on the island can join hands with us in exchanges and cooperation, jointly resist all vicious conduct that undermines cross-strait relations, and together promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Taiwan polls show that young people aged 25 to 34 on the island do not believe the DPP authorities are fully prepared to deal with armed conflict across the Taiwan Strait. Some public opinion on the island holds that the DPP authorities, on the one hand, manipulate “anti-China” sentiment, and on the other hand try to downplay the cross-Strait crisis and advocate for external forces to provide defense. What…","We have noted the relevant public opinion polls, and we have also noted the commentary in island public opinion.\nFor some time now, Taiwan residents have clearly felt rising cross-Strait military tensions and increasing risks in the Taiwan Strait situation. They increasingly see clearly the harm and danger of the DPP authorities' blatant peddling of the “two-state theory” and their intensifying collusion with external forces to repeatedly carry out “Taiwan independence” provocations. We hope more Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities' political selfishness and, through concrete actions, oppose being coerced by “Taiwan independence” and safeguard their own interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211110_12390157.htm"],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Two questions. First, the list of “Taiwan independence” diehards announced by the mainland does not include Tsai Ing-wen, Lai Ching-te, or others. Some public opinion in Taiwan holds that this means the mainland still retains some room for maneuver, preserving the possibility of future contact between the two sides. Will there be a second or third follow-up list? Second, Taiwan has had no locally transmitted…","First question: The net of justice is vast, and nothing escapes it. “Taiwan independence” diehards who persist in their delusions and resist to the end, including the chief criminals who organize, plan, and carry out acts to split the country and undermine national reunification, who collude with external forces to seek “independence,” and who seek “de jure independence” through means such as “constitutional amendment,” as well as their financial backers, will all certainly be severely punished in accordance with the law.\nSecond question: Recently, the global epidemic has fluctuated and remained high, and the epidemic prevention and control situation this winter and next spring is complex and grave. We will continue to implement strict epidemic prevention and control measures and firmly build a solid barrier of “preventing imported cases from abroad and guarding against rebounds at home.” Regarding the convenience of cross-border travel for vaccinated people, we will act in accordance with the development of the epidemic situation and obey the unified deployment and arrangements for epidemic prevention and control work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Continuing the issue of the list of “Taiwan independence” diehards, KMT Chairman Eric Chu said, “The law of the other side has nothing to do with Taiwan.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s view? Second question: Chiu Tai-san, Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, pointed out that the “sand theft” by mainland sand-dredging vessels in the waters of Kinmen, Matsu and Penghu seriously damages marine resources.…","First question: Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. Resolutely combating die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with the law is an inherent requirement for safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and is also an appropriate measure to ensure the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The state has full legal basis for taking disciplinary measures against die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements.\nSecond question: The Taiwan side, under the pretext of “prohibited waters” and “restricted waters,” has seized mainland vessels and even adopted dangerous and brutal methods against mainland crew members. This is entirely aimed at creating incidents. It is an irresponsible and dangerous act, and we firmly oppose it. In fact, we attach great importance to the issue of illegal extraction of sea sand. Relevant departments have also been actively taking a series of measures, including strengthening coastline patrols and carrying out special rectification campaigns, to prevent, rectify, and investigate it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云记者","First question: Ma Ying-jeou recently said that Taiwan is now regarded as the most dangerous place in the world and called on both sides of the Strait to “seek peace and avoid war.” What is the TAO’s view? Second question: A Taiwanese scholar has said that once the sanctions list of “Taiwan independence” diehards was released, many Taiwanese companies with business dealings on the mainland no longer dare to…","On the first question. On November 7, 2015, the leaders of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait held a meeting for the first time since 1949. This was a milestone event in the history of cross-Strait relations. It pioneered direct dialogue and communication between the leaders of the two sides, raised cross-Strait exchanges and interactions to a new height, opened a new chapter in the development of cross-Strait relations, and created new space.\nAdhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist line, refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” incite and aggravate cross-Strait confrontation, arbitrarily collude with external forces, and constantly engage in provocations for “independence.” These are the root causes of the current setbacks in cross-Strait relations and the tense and volatile situation in the Taiwan Strait. Only by returning to the “1992 Consensus” and restoring the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation can peace in the Taiwan Strait be guaranteed and cross-Strait relations return to the right track and continue to move forward.\nOn the second question. In fact, there is no so-called “one-size-fits-all” approach as you put it. We have stated very clearly that the purpose of punishing, in accordance with the law, the obstinate “Taiwan independence” elements and their principal backers and supporters is to curb “Taiwan independence” separatism, to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to protect the rights and interests of people on both sides of the Strait. Only institutions and enterprises that have direct or indirect ties with obstinate “Taiwan independence” elements, as well as those who provide support for the “independence” activities of obstinate “Taiwan independence” elements, are subject to restrictions. Therefore, fundamentally speaking, this will be conducive to promoting normal economic and trade exchanges across the Strait and to safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the third question, what you just mentioned is a new song, I suppose. I have heard an online song before, “Taking the High-Speed Rail to Taipei,” and these two songs should have something in common. I think this actually reflects the good wishes of people on both sides of the Strait for the long-term plan of a Beijing-Taipei high-speed rail, from Fujian to Taipei. We hope that both sides of the Strait will achieve full connectivity, so that compatriots on both sides can travel and exchange more conveniently, see more of the beautiful scenery and taste more of the delicacies across the Strait. I believe this wish will certainly be realized.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, there has been a great deal of discussion about “armed reunification” in cross-Strait and international media. How does the spokesperson view the current highly tense situation across the Taiwan Strait? Recently, a responsible official of the Taiwan Affairs Office, in a speech, mentioned some arrangements after reunification. What message is this sending to the outside world?","We have repeatedly pointed out that the root cause of the current tense cross-Strait relations and rising risks to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' disregard for the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. They have blatantly peddled the “two-state theory” and, in collusion with external forces, have continuously carried out “Taiwan independence” provocations. The people on both sides of the Strait are highly concerned and worried about the harmfulness and danger of the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” provocations.\n“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the basic policy toward Taiwan that we have always adhered to, and it is also the best way to achieve national reunification. It best serves the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. At the same time, our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering. We will never allow anyone or any force to infringe upon or divide the sacred territory of the motherland. Compatriots in Taiwan should join hands with compatriots on the mainland to eliminate the root of “Taiwan independence” and work together for national righteousness, Taiwan's future, and a bright future of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","A deputy director of the TAO said that “after unification, Taiwan’s fiscal revenue can be used to improve people’s livelihoods,” which set off a flood of speculation among mainland netizens. Are some of the netizens’ remarks beneficial to promoting the process of unification?","The complete reunification of the motherland is an inevitable historical trend, it is where Taiwan's future lies, and it bears on the interests of Taiwan compatriots. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the best way to achieve national reunification. It fully takes into account the actual situation in Taiwan and is conducive to Taiwan's long-term stability and security after reunification. The specific form of implementing “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account the actual situation in Taiwan, will fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and will fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the premise of safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, after peaceful reunification, the social system and way of life of Taiwan compatriots will be fully respected, and their private property, religious beliefs, and lawful rights and interests will be fully protected. Taiwan will remain forever at peace, its people will live and work in contentment, and they will share in the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. With a strong motherland to rely on, the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be better, their room for development will be greater, they will stand taller and more confidently in the international arena, and they will be safer and have more dignity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视记者","Su Tseng-chang, Wu Zhaoxie and Yu Hsi-kun said that being on the sanctions list makes them feel honored, and that they will continue to fight for “freedom and democracy.” What is your comment?","These “Taiwan independence” diehards incite cross-strait confrontation, undermine cross-strait relations, plot to split the country, and endanger peace in the Taiwan Strait, and everyone can see this clearly. This account is well documented and cannot be denied. The higher they jump, the harder they fall. Those who persist in their delusions and resist to the end will surely be severely punished by the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Spokesperson, can this list of punishments really serve as a warning? Another question: Spokesperson, how do you view the desire of some people on the mainland for the government to take action to “reunify Taiwan by force”? Would such thinking affect the mainland's position on peaceful reunification?","First question: Cracking down on the “Taiwan independence” diehards and their principal backers, including their financial patrons, in accordance with the law, aims to curb the separatist acts of “Taiwan independence” and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This accords with the common interests of people on both sides of the Strait. No one wishes to see the stable, peaceful environment disrupted. The higher the “Taiwan independence” diehards jump, the harder they will fall.\nSecond question: We must point out that reunification is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters and lies at the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We adhere to making the utmost sincere effort and doing our best to strive for prospects of peaceful reunification. However, if anyone misjudges the situation and insists on pushing “Taiwan independence” separatism, attempting to tear down the prospects for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peaceful reunification of the motherland, I believe that all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, will not accept it, and the entire Chinese nation will absolutely not accept it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","According to Taiwan media, before November 8, TSMC had responded to the U.S. Department of Commerce’s request and submitted commercial data. The DPP said it would not interfere, which has caused strong doubts on the island. What comments does the spokesperson have?","We have noted the relevant reports and will continue to closely follow the developments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","A recent US military report stated that in 2027 the Chinese mainland will have more reliable military options in the event of a sudden incident in the Taiwan Strait. It also said the mainland may believe the window of opportunity for “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” has closed. What is the spokesperson's comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The so-called \"report\" released by the US side seriously violates the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three joint communiqués, stop any form of military contact with the Taiwan region of China, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.\n\"Using force to resist reunification\" will only push Taiwan toward disaster. Any act by the DPP authorities that colludes with external forces to provoke through \"independence-seeking\" is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","Taiwan’s retired general Xia Yingzhou recently said that PLA aircraft appearing in the “southwest airspace” of Taiwan island are over their own territory, and that they have every right to patrol. His remarks have caused concern on the island. The head of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said it does not agree with such a view and that it will handle the matter according to regulations. What is the…","Taiwan is part of China. It is entirely justified for the People's Liberation Army to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity and carry out relevant military operations.\nTomorrow is the 72nd anniversary of the founding of the People's Air Force. I saw a sentence yesterday that moved me, and I would like to share it with everyone. “As a pilot, how do you express your love for the motherland? By completing the tasks entrusted by the motherland well, and by safeguarding the motherland's airspace well.” We are the same: we must safeguard the motherland's sovereignty and territory well, and protect and take good care of the interests and well-being of the people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The Tsinghua University Alumni Association, the Xiamen Municipal Government and Beijing's Tsinghua University jointly established the “Tsinghua Cross-Strait Research Institute” and the “Tsinghua Cross-Strait Research Institute Hsinchu Office” on the Tsinghua University campus in Hsinchu, engaging in technology R&D, talent recruitment and investment. This has drawn questions from relevant Taiwan authorities, who…","It is understood that the Tsinghua Cross-Strait Research Institute is a scientific research institution operated in a corporate manner. Since its establishment in 2015, it has played a positive role in promoting cross-Strait science and technology exchange and innovation, and promoting integrated development across the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities are accustomed to using all kinds of excuses to set up obstacles to normal exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and keep interfering and sabotaging. The relevant situation you just mentioned is yet another bad example of the DPP authorities obstructing and restricting normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and this reckless conduct is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Continuing on the epidemic prevention issue: if Taiwan residents have received two doses of WHO-certified vaccines, will they be recognized as fully vaccinated when coming to the mainland? At the end of this year and early next year, many Taiwan journalists will rotate in to station and report, and most of those coming have received AZ, Comirnaty or Moderna vaccines. Does this meet the epidemic prevention…","Taiwanese reporters stationed on the mainland who take part in important events will be arranged according to the epidemic prevention and control situation and the epidemic prevention requirements of important events. Many of your colleagues have previously attended some important events, so you may communicate with them.\nThis press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211110_12390149.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-11","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Firstly, China and the US announced a surprise climate agreement at COP26. Does this suggest some degree of improvement in China-US ties? Secondly, the US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said in an interview that \"we have commitments... to make sure that Taiwan has the ability to defend itself\". He added that there are many countries that would take action if they see any unilateral action to use force to…","On your first question, on November 10, London time, China and the US reached and issued the Joint Glasgow Declaration on Enhancing Climate Action in the 2020s on the sidelines of the Glasgow Climate Change Conference.\nBuilding on the China-US Joint Statement Addressing the Climate Crisis released in Shanghai in April and the talks in Tianjin in September, this joint declaration further puts forward specific measures for China and the US to carry out their respective domestic actions, promote bilateral cooperation and advance multilateral processes. The two sides appreciate the work done so far and pledge to continue the combined efforts and work with all parties to strengthen the implementation of the Paris Agreement. The two sides will take enhanced climate actions to effectively address the climate crisis in accordance with common but differentiated responsibilities and respective capabilities, and in the light of different national circumstances. The two sides agreed to establish a \"Working Group on Enhancing Climate Action in the 2020s\" to advance bilateral climate cooperation and the multilateral processes. The joint declaration has been released online for your reference. The Glasgow Climate Change Conference is concluding soon. I believe that the joint declaration will enhance the confidence of all countries in jointly tackling climate change and contribute to the success of the conference.\nSince the beginning of this year, China and the US have held intensive dialogues and consultations on climate change in accordance with the spirit and instructions of the telephone conversation between the two heads of state. The joint declaration is the product of candid exchanges, mutual understanding, mutual respect and active efforts to expand consensus between the two sides. This shows once again that China and the US can work together on major international issues, and accomplish many great things that benefit the people of both countries and the world through cooperation, and inject positive energy into the multilateral processes.\nOn your second question, I want to stress that relevant remarks by the US side disregard facts and violate international law. The one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques are the foundation for the establishment of diplomatic ties and the sound development of China-US relations. The Taiwan Relations Act unilaterally formulated by the US is illegal, null and void, as it goes against the commitment the US made in the three joint communiques and puts its domestic laws above international obligations. China never allows the US to wantonly violate China's sovereignty and interfere in China's internal affairs citing any reasons or with any excuses. The US should take real actions to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, speak and act prudently and stop sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" forces.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. This is not only a historical and legal fact that cannot be changed, but also a status quo that cannot be challenged. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations and the consensus of the international community. Resolution 2758 of the United Nations General Assembly recognized \"the representatives of the Government of the People's Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations\", and decided to \"expel the representatives of Chiang Kai-shek from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations\". When Resolution 2758 was under consultation, the \"dual representation\" draft resolution proposed by the US and a few other countries to create \"two Chinas\" failed to pass, which fundamentally denied the representation of Taiwan in the UN. Relevant UN documents pointed out explicitly that \"the United Nations considers 'Taiwan' as a province of China with no separate status\", and the \"authorities in Taipei are not considered to ... enjoy any form of governmental status\".\nThe one-China principle is recognized and supported by 180 countries in the world. The landscape of the international community upholding the one-China principle is becoming ever more solid and China's reunification has become an unstoppable trend of history. The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the Taiwan authorities and a handful of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces try to negate and challenge the one-China principle and expand the space of \"Taiwan independence\" activities, which has been firmly rejected by the Chinese government and the international community. All acts to challenge the one-China principle and resist the trend of reunification will be resolutely foiled. All attempts to support the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts and go against the trend of history will end in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347158.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211111_10447072.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 11 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 11th that recently, some people in the United States have repeatedly and again and again spread erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question. It must be pointed out that the U.S. government has made solemn commitments to the Chinese side on the Taiwan question. The three China-U.S. joint communiqués are principles that the U.S. government must abide by through concrete actions. We urge the U.S. side to stop its erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and not cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nA reporter asked: Recently, when asked about the Taiwan question by U.S. media, U.S. Secretary of State Blinken said that the United States has committed to “ensuring Taiwan has the capability to defend itself,” and that regarding so-called “unilateral use of force to undermine the status quo,” Blinken said “many countries will take action.” Taiwan media reported on this. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.\nShe said that we warn the DPP authorities that any act of colluding with external forces to advance “Taiwan independence” and provoke confrontation will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211111_12390382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-15","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","Last week, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said in a interview that the US has commitments under the Taiwan Relations Act to make sure that Taiwan has the ability to defend itself. We noticed that in a tweet on November 14, Blinken emphasized US interest in peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment?","We are firmly opposed to the wrong words and actions of the US side. I would like to emphasize a few points:\nFirst, over the past 40 years or so, the US statements on the Taiwan question have lost shape, turned sour and retrogressed, running counter to the consensus reached between the US and China upon the establishment of diplomatic relations. What the US should abide by is the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, which are important political consensus between China and the US and the political foundation for the bilateral ties. Both the so-called \"Taiwan Relations Act\" and the \"Six Assurances\", concocted by some forces in the US, contravene the three China-US joint communiques. In essence, they place US domestic law above international obligations and are illegal and invalid.\nSecond, for some time now, the DPP authorities in Taiwan and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces have been pursuing \"de-sinicization\", trying to create \"one China, one Taiwan\" or \"two Chinas\", and engaging in provocative activities to seek independence in collusion with external forces. This is the biggest threat to peace and stability and the root cause of the current tension across the Taiwan Strait.\nI want to stress that China's reunification is an unstoppable historical trend and upholding the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community. All acts supporting and emboldening \"Taiwan independence\" constitute interference in China's internal affairs and are in no way conducive to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The US should commit itself to the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiques, and prudently and properly handle the Taiwan-related issues, lest it should undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347160.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211115_10448526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-15","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","The US and Taiwan will hold political military discussions and an annual defense review later this week. This is according to the United Daily News reports. The talks will be participated by Jessica Lewis, the Assistant Secretary of State and another official, the Assistant Secretary of Defense for the Indo-Pacific. So my question pertains to these meetings later in the week between the US and Taiwan. Does the…","The Taiwan question bears on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China's core interests. It is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and immediately stop official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan in any form. We also need to warn the Taiwan authorities that Taiwan independence is a dead end. Any attempt or act to solicit foreign support and resist reunification with force is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347160.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211115_10448526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-15","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","According to reports, on November 13, visiting Honduran President Juan Orlando Hernandez met with Tsai Ing-wen. \"At this very moment amid tensions in the region, Honduras is here to demonstrate that we are real friends\", he said. Tsai called Hernandez's visit significant and said she hoped the two sides would continue to help each other on the international stage. Do you have any comment?","The one-China principle is a universally-recognized norm governing international relations and a shared consensus of the international community. Adherence to the one-China principle is an overriding trend that represents international justice and enjoys popular support. The DPP authorities in Taiwan are apt to create the false illusion of international support to bolster its \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts, which is nothing but a trick to deceive themselves and others. It cannot alter the iron-clad fact that Taiwan is part of China and can by no means thwart the invincible trend of China's reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347160.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211115_10448526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-15","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","The Biden administration has spurned a plan by Intel to increase production in China citing security concerns. Intel had proposed using a factory in Chengdu to manufacture silicon wafers. But this plan has been strongly discouraged by the Biden administration. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on the Biden administration's reaction to this plan by Intel?","Economic globalization is an objective reality and historical trend. The US has repeatedly overstretched the concept of national security and abused state power to politicize and weaponize science, technology and economic and trade issues based on ideology, and intentionally put in place trade and investment barriers against specific countries. Recently, it has forced the Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co (TSMC), Samsung and other companies to provide chip supply chain data to the US, calling the submission \"voluntary\". Such actions not only undermine international trade rules and divide the global market, but also end up hurting others and the US itself. We urge the US to adopt a correct attitude, follow the trend of the times, discard the zero-sum mentality, earnestly uphold a fair, just and non-discriminatory market environment, and take concrete actions to build an open world economy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347160.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211115_10448526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-15","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","According to Reuters report, China's embassy has been lobbying US executives, companies and business groups in recent weeks to fight against certain China-related bills in congress. Do you have any comment on this report?","The China-related content in relevant legislation in the US Congress distorts facts, denigrates China's development path and domestic and foreign policies, hypes up the \"China threat\" theory, clamors for strategic competition with China, gravely interferes with China's domestic affairs on issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Tibet, politicizes economic and trade issues, and brims with Cold-War zero-sum mentality. If the legislation were to become law, it would doubtlessly hijack bilateral relations and severely disrupt normal exchange and cooperation, which serves neither side's interests. China is consistently and firmly opposed to it.\nRelevant US lawmakers should adjust their attitude, view China's development and China-US relations in a rational light, stop reviewing and pushing negative legislation concerning China, delete negative clauses concerning China, and stop meddling in China's internal affairs, so as to prevent undermining overall bilateral relations and cooperation in important areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347160.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211115_10448526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-16","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","The Chinese and US heads of state just held their virtual meeting this morning. How does China see the outcomes of the meeting? Were the expected goals reached? What specific measures will be adopted to implement the two heads of state’s consensus?","President Xi Jinping held a virtual meeting with President Joe Biden this morning. Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng briefed journalists on the meeting in an interview afterwards. It is the first head-of-state meeting in the virtual format in the history of China-US relations. It is of great significance to China-US relations and international relations. The meeting started at 8:45 Beijing time and lasted for three and a half hours, ending at 12:25, later than scheduled. The two sides had exchanges on a broad range of issues, including those of strategic, overarching and fundamental importance shaping the development of China-US relations, respective development agenda, domestic and foreign policies and regional and international issues of mutual interest.\nThe key points of the meeting can be summarized as one important question President Xi elaborated on, two principled consensuses reached between the two Presidents, three principles and four priorities put forward by President Xi on developing China-US relations.\nOne important question is the Taiwan question, which remains the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations and a topic always on the agenda whenever our heads of state meet. President Xi pointed out unequivocally in this meeting that the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués are the political foundation of China-US relations. Achieving China’s complete reunification is an aspiration shared by all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. That said, should the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence” provoke us, force our hands or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures. On this question bearing on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, there is no room for compromise. President Biden reiterated in the meeting that the US is committed to the one-China policy and does not support “Taiwan independence”.\nOne of the two principled consensuses is the importance of China-US relations. President Xi said that a sound and stable China-US relationship is required for advancing the two countries’ respective development and for safeguarding a peaceful and stable international environment. The two sides should increase communication and cooperation, each run their domestic affairs well and, at the same time, shoulder their share of international responsibilities, take active steps to move China-US relations forward in a positive direction, and work together to advance the noble cause of world peace and development. Doing so will advance the interests of the two peoples and meet the expectation of the international community. President Biden said that how our bilateral relationship evolves will have a profound impact not only on our countries but also the rest of the world. We have a responsibility to the world, as well as to our people. He agrees that we cannot afford to mess up our relationship. He reiterated that the US does not seek to change China’s system and is willing to work with China on the basis of mutual respect and peaceful coexistence. The most pressing task at hand is to engage in candid dialogue on a broad range of substantive issues in bilateral relations to make sure that competition is healthy and does not veer into conflict.\nThe second consensus is rejection of a “new Cold War”. China consistently opposes a “new Cold War” in any form. President Biden has also explicitly stated that the US does not seek a “new Cold War”. Actually, no country, not even US allies, wants to see another Cold War or choose sides between China and the US. President Xi stressed during the meeting that drawing ideological lines or dividing the world into different camps or rival groups will only make the world suffer. The Chinese side called on the US side to meet its word of not seeking a “new Cold War” with concrete actions. It is hoped that the US will play a constructive role in the Asia-Pacific that is conducive to enhancing solidarity.\nPresident Xi pointed out three principles for China and the US to get along in the new era. First, mutual respect. The two countries need to respect each other’s social systems and development paths, respect each other’s core interests and major concerns, and respect each other’s right to development. They need to treat each other as equals, keep differences under control, and seek common ground while reserving differences. Second, peaceful coexistence. No conflict and no confrontation is a line that both sides must hold. Third, win-win cooperation. The two sides’ interests are deeply intertwined. The world is big enough for the two countries to develop individually and collectively. The right thing to do is to choose mutual benefit over zero-sum game or the I-win-you-lose approach.\nWith regard to the four priority areas, President Xi identified four areas where China and the US should focus their efforts on. First, shouldering responsibilities of major countries and leading global response to outstanding challenges, such as climate change, global public health, energy, and industrial and supply chain security. China-US cooperation may not solve all problems, but few problems can be solved without China-US cooperation. The global initiatives China has proposed are all open to the US. We hope the reverse is also true. Second, acting in the spirit of equality and mutual benefit to move forward exchanges at all levels and in all areas and generate more positive energy for China-US relations. The two heads of state can stay in touch with each other through multiple means to set the direction and inject more momentum into bilateral relations. The two countries, with broad common interests in a wide range of areas including economy, energy, mil-to-mil, law-enforcement, education, science and technology, cyber, environmental protection and sub-national interactions, should complement each other to make the cake bigger for China-US cooperation. The two sides could fully harness the dialogue channels and mechanisms between their diplomatic and security, economic and financial, and climate change teams, in an effort to advance practical cooperation and resolve specific issues. Third, managing differences and sensitive issues in a constructive way to prevent China-US relations from getting derailed or out of control. It is only natural for the two countries to have differences. The key is to manage them constructively so that they don’t magnify or exacerbate. China is firmly determined to defend its sovereignty, security and development interests, and it is important that the US properly handle the relevant issues with prudence. Fourth, strengthening coordination and cooperation on major international and regional hotspot issues to provide more public goods to the world. The world is not tranquil. China and the US need to work together with the rest of the international community to defend world peace, promote global development, and safeguard a fair and equitable international order.\nThe two Presidents agreed that their meeting is candid, constructive, substantive and productive. It helps increase mutual understanding, adds to the positive expectation of the international community for this relationship, and sends a powerful message to the two countries and the world. The two sides agreed to maintain close communication in different forms and steer China-US relations back on the right track of sound and steady development, for the good of the people in both countries and around the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347161.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211116_10448926.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-16","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","After the virtual meeting this morning, can you give us any details on further meetings which may be planned either at the head-of-state level or lower levels? Do you expect this virtual meeting to help reduce tensions over the Taiwan Strait?","The virtual summit today is another example of the two heads of state steering and guiding China-US relations at a critical moment. It is of great, far-reaching significance to the development of China-US relations in the next stage. President Xi Jinping and President Joe Biden agreed to stay in touch through various forms. We are open to all forms of communication between the two heads of state, including face-to-face interactions. We should let things take their course. They will happen when conditions are ripe. The key is for the two sides to work in the same direction, create an enabling atmosphere with actions and ensure positive outcomes from the summit.\nIf we cannot bring China-US relations back to where they were, then we should be forward-looking. China holds no illusions, but it is confident and will continue to stay focused. China is open to all options that are conducive to the development of China-US relations. In the meantime, we uphold principles, which can be summed up as the three principles President Xi Jinping talked about today: mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation.\nChina-US relations have now come to a crucial crossroads. We hope the US side will work with us in the same direction, follow through on the spirit of the meeting between the two Presidents with concrete actions, maintain dialogue and communication, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, manage differences responsibly and bring China-US relations back to the track of sound and steady development.\nAs for the impact of the China-US virtual summit on the situation across the Taiwan Strait, President Xi has fully stated China's principled position on the Taiwan question during the meeting. The US should abide by the formal bilateral agreements reached between China and the US and the formal resolutions adopted at the UN General Assembly with an overwhelming majority, face up to the fact and will of the overwhelming majority of countries to adhere to the one-China principle, and win the trust of the Chinese people and the international community with actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347161.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211116_10448926.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-17","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","On Tuesday, Biden told reporters that Taiwan makes its own decisions and is independent. He later said that “we are not encouraging independence, but that we're not going to change our policy at all. We're encouraging them to do exactly what the Taiwan Act requires. That's what we're doing. Let them make up their mind. Period.” Does China have any comment on these comments?","Regarding the two Presidents’ discussion about the Taiwan question in their virtual meeting, I already briefed you on the situation yesterday. China also released a readout on the meeting.\nI want to stress that what the US should abide by is the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, which are important political consensus between China and the US and the political foundation of Chine-US ties. Both the so-called \"Taiwan Relations Act\" and the \"Six Assurances\", concocted by some forces in the US, contravene the three China-US Joint Communiqués. In essence, they place US domestic law above international obligations and are illegal and invalid.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347163.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211117_10449472.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 16 -- Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responding to a question on the 16th, said: The DPP authorities stubbornly cling to the “Taiwan independence” stance, obstinately challenge the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and scheme to change the status quo in which both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Their “Taiwan independence” actions…","Zhu Fenglian said: We warn the DPP authorities that for all acts attempting to split the country, all provocations and coercion, and even actions that cross red lines, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211117_12391235.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 17 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 17th when asked that we are highly attentive to recent moves by the DPP caucus. We firmly oppose any form of \"amending the constitution to seek independence.\" The DPP, in pursuit of private interests, has stubbornly pressed ahead regardless of the firm opposition and solemn warnings from all sides, and will surely reap the consequences.\nA reporter asked: Recently, the DPP caucus submitted the party's draft \"constitutional amendment\" to Taiwan's legislature, including lowering the threshold for \"constitutional amendment\" and abolishing the examination and oversight bodies. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering the question.\nShe pointed out that all responsible political parties and enlightened people on the island should expose the DPP's conspiratorial calculations and, through concrete actions, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the well-being of the people of Taiwan. Compatriots in Taiwan must remain highly vigilant, consciously oppose and resist all forms of \"amending the constitution to seek independence,\" and not be step by step tied to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot by the DPP.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211117_12391327.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 17 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 17th when asked that we are very clear about the situation concerning the Taiwan-related content of the video meeting between the leaders of China and the United States. The US position of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\" is one that the US government has repeatedly reaffirmed over a long period. We warn the DPP authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" forces that attempts to seek independence by relying on external forces are impossible to succeed. We will take resolute measures against all provocations, coercion, and even actions that cross red lines.\nA reporter asked: The DPP authorities have made remarks criticizing mainland media's reports on the meeting between the leaders of China and the United States, defending their \"Taiwan independence\" statements and actions. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in answering the question.\nShe pointed out that we urge the US government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question properly, not send any erroneous signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and not cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211117_12391364.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-18","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","Anne Neuberger, Deputy Assistant to the US President and Deputy National Security Advisor for Cyber and Emerging Technology on the National Security Council, who is in Japan for a visit, said on November 17 that “under the Taiwan Relations Act, we ensure that Taiwan can maintain sufficient self-defense, including in cyber”. She also expressed concerns over the cyber attack launched by China’s mainland and others…","The so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” cited by the US side gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués and essentially places domestic law above international obligations. It is illegal, null and void. On the Taiwan question, the US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, rather than something it unilaterally concocted. What truly undermines cross-Strait relations is “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference. China consistently opposes and cracks down on all forms of cyber attacks. As is well-known, the US is the notorious “empire of hacking”. The US should stop playing the trick of the thief crying “stop the thief”, and stop instigating cross-Strait confrontation, to avoid severely harming China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347164.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211118_10449941.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-18","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","A report from the US-China Economic and Security Review Commission said that the US should bolster its ability to deter a Chinese attack against Taiwan and strengthen oversight of Chinese companies. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on the report? In addition, White House officials said the US is seeking ways to discuss issues of strategic stability with China as concerns in Washington mount over…","On your first question, this commission you mentioned concocts the so-called report on China year after year, which interferes in China’s domestic affairs and undermines China-US relations. The report, awash with disinformation and malicious slander, mirrors the commission’s persistent ignorance and entrenched bias against China.\nThe relevant US institution should reject the Cold-War zero-sum mentality and ideological bias, follow the trend of the times and the aspiration of people of the world, plant more flowers and fewer thorns, do more things conducive to promoting mutual trust and cooperation between our two countries instead of the opposite.\nOn your second question, I noted the clarification made by the US side on this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347164.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211118_10449941.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-18","Zhao Lijian","NHK","Taiwan held a ceremony this morning to commission the first squadron of F-16V fighters. The ceremony was chaired by Tsai Ing-wen and attended by the Director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT). Do you have any comment?","China's position on the Taiwan question and US-Taiwan relations is consistent and clear-cut. China opposes any official contact between the US and Taiwan. We hope that the US side will earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of three China-US Joint Communiqués, speak and act with prudence on the Taiwan question and refrain from sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The crux of the tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces spare no effort to split the motherland and collude with external forces. What they do is just like an egg knocking itself against a stone and an ant trying to shake a huge tree, which is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347164.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211118_10449941.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-19","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","The Lithuanian government has approved the establishment of the so-called \"Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania\" by the Taiwan authorities. We took note of the statement made by the foreign ministry spokesperson last night to express strong protest. What measures will China take in response?","The Lithuanian government, in disregard of the Chinese side’s strong objection and repeated dissuasion, has approved the establishment of the so-called “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania” by the Taiwan authorities. This act creates the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world, flagrantly violates the one-China principle, and renounces the political commitment made by Lithuania in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China. It undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs. The Chinese government expresses strong protest over and firm objection to this extremely egregious act, and will take all necessary measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Lithuanian side shall be responsible for all the ensuing consequences.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We demand that the Lithuanian side immediately correct its wrong decision. We also have this stern warning for the Taiwan authorities: Seeking \"Taiwan independence\" by soliciting foreign support is a totally misguided attempt that is doomed to fail.\nAs to what necessary measures China will take, you may wait and see. The Lithuanian side shall reap what it sows.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347165.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211119_10450526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-19","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Daily","An international seminar on the significance of UNGA Resolution 2758 was held yesterday. Could you share more information on that?","Chinese and foreign experts at the seminar agree that UNGA Resolution 2758 affirmed that the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing the whole of China including Taiwan in the world. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations affirmed in this resolution that is widely recognized by the international community and shall not be challenged.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is not only supported by a solid factual and jurisprudential basis, but also affirmed in a series of legal instruments including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. UNGA Resolution 2758 resolved the issue of representation of the whole of China, making it clear that the PRC Government is the only legitimate government representing the whole of China including Taiwan in the UN. The resolution stated explicitly that it decided to “restore all its rights to the People's Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations, and to expel forthwith the representatives of Chiang Kai-shek” claiming representing the whole of China including Taiwan “from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations and in all the organizations related to it”.\nIf we look at the history of the adoption process of Resolution 2758, we can see that the so-called international representation of the Taiwan authorities has long been denied outright. A handful of countries including the US proposed the \"dual representation\" draft resolution in an attempt to create “two Chinas” in the UN, only to end in failure.\nLately, the US and Taiwan authorities have maliciously distorted UNGA Resolution 2758, spread false argument on the issue of Taiwan’s so-called representation at the UN, and intentionally brought up an issue that has long been settled by the international community. Such acts have no legal basis and violate international consensus. The historical and legal facts which prove that Taiwan is part of China and that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China shall never be altered by anyone or any force. The political manipulation and malicious intention of certain forces is bound to end in failure and disgrace again in front of the overwhelming recognition of and support for the one-China principle by 180 countries and the invincible trend of China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347165.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211119_10450526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 19: In response to the Taiwan representative office in Lithuania beginning official operations under its signboard, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 19th in response to questions that the DPP authorities, driven by their intent to seek “independence,” are carrying out activities under various banners on the international stage that undermine the one-China principle and split the country. Their tactics include establishing relevant institutions, changing relevant names, courting and infiltrating politicians of relevant countries, fabricating lies, and spreading “Taiwan independence” rhetoric. We firmly oppose all such activities seeking “independence” and will resolutely combat them.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that we firmly oppose any form of official relations between countries that have diplomatic ties with us and Taiwan region of China. We urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently, and not go further down the wrong path of supporting and tolerating “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211119_12391756.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-22","Zhao Lijian","Radio Television Hong Kong","The Lithuanian Foreign Ministry issued a statement that said it regrets China's decision to downgrade the diplomatic relations with Lithuania to the chargé d'affaires level. The Vice Foreign Minister noted in an interview that the \"Representative Office\" in Lithuania established by Taiwan does not have diplomatic status and that Lithuania hopes to normalize relations with China. What is your comment?","Lithuania, in disregard of China's strong protest and repeated representations, allowed the Taiwan authorities to set up a \"Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania\". This act openly creates the false impression of \"one China, one Taiwan\" in the world, creating an egregious precedent. Lithuania blatantly renounces the political commitment made by Lithuania in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China, which is an erroneous act in bad faith. Given the fact that the political foundation for an ambassadorial-level diplomatic relationship has been damaged by Lithuania, the Chinese government, out of the need to safeguard national sovereignty and basic norms governing international relations, has no choice but to downgrade its diplomatic relations with Lithuania to the chargé d'affaires level. The Lithuanian government must bear all the ensuing consequences.\nThe quibble that the representative office does not have diplomatic status by the Lithuanian side is purely cover-up. The Taiwan authorities claimed that the establishment of \"Taiwanese Representative Office\" in Lithuania is Taiwan's so-called \"major diplomatic breakthrough\" and so-called \"major diplomatic outcome\". This is a confession of the Taiwan authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and a solid evidence for their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts.\nThe Lithuanian side should immediately put right its mistake. It should not underestimate the Chinese people's strong resolve to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We also have this stern warning for the Taiwan authorities that no matter how \"Taiwan independence\" forces try to misrepresent facts and confound black and white, the historical fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China cannot be changed. Attempts to seek foreign support for political manipulation will prove a dead end.\nFinally, I want to stress that Lithuania has got to where it is today obviously at the instigation of certain major country, but what has been hurt is Lithuania's own interests. We call on other countries to act in light of their own fundamental interests and international justice, and refrain from being a pawn in senseless confrontation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347167.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211122_10451497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-22","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","A European Commission spokesperson said on November 21 that the EU does not regard the opening of a representative office from Taiwan in Lithuania as a breach of the EU's one-China policy. \"We have made clear in contacts with China and in public statements that this is predominantly a bilateral matter between China and Lithuania, but also since the summer, the EU has stood by Lithuania in the face of sustained…","The merits of the Taiwan-related issue concerning Lithuania are plain and clear. Lithuania, in disregard of the Chinese government's solemn position, the broader interests of bilateral ties and the basic norms governing international relations, has allowed the establishment in Lithuania of the \"Representative Office\" bearing the name of Taiwan. This act openly creates the false impression of \"one China, one Taiwan\" in the world and renounces the political commitment made by Lithuania in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China. This act in bad faith has created an egregious precedent internationally. The Lithuanian government must bear all the ensuing consequences.\nThe remarks by the EU side disregard facts and obviously run counter to the commitment it made to the People's Republic of China upon establishing diplomatic relations in 1975. Sir Christopher Soames, then vice-president of the Commission of the European Economic Community (EEC), visited China in 1975. It was during this visit that China and the EEC agreed to establish official relations. On the Taiwan question, Sir Soames stated that \"all the Member States of the Community recognized the government of China and had taken positions with regard to the Taiwan question acceptable to the People's Republic\". He also confirmed that \"the Community does not entertain any official relations with Taiwan or have any agreements with it\". The EU side should honor its word instead of breaking faith.\nWe urge Lithuania and the EU to truly abide by the one-China principle and fulfill their political commitment on Taiwan-related matters with actions in good faith. Those who think they can use Taiwan as a handy card to undermine China's interests have completely miscalculated. Such acts can never change the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China. They will only further strengthen the Chinese people's resolve to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity and realize the complete reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347167.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211122_10451497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-22","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","In response to the Chinese Embassy to Australia's remarks regarding Australia's nuclear-powered submarine deal, Australian Defence Minister Peter Dutton on November 19 called Chinese official's remarks provocative, silly and funny. Do you have any comment on that?","Mr. Dutton's remarks are extremely absurd and irresponsible. As a senior official of the Australian government, he is obsessed with the Cold War mentality and ideological prejudices. Driven by selfish political gains, he has repeatedly made provocations, sensational and astonishing statements on China-related issues. He wouldn't scruple to hijack Australia onto the chariot in confrontation with China. His real intention has been exposed to all.\nFor a while, some Australian politicians have been hyping up \"China threat\", wantonly criticizing and attacking China, provoking tension and inciting confrontation and making all sorts of trouble. On issues relating to Taiwan, they grossly interfere in China's domestic affairs and bolster and embolden \"Taiwan independence\" forces. Its nuclear submarine cooperation with the US and the UK undermines international nuclear non-proliferation efforts, aggravates arms race, and has caused grave concern among regional countries. Such acts run counter to the trend for peace, development and cooperation in today's world and is detrimental to Australia's own interests and its international image.\nCertain Australian politicians should discard the Cold War mentality and ideological bias and not to erect any \"imaginary enemy\" when it's completely uncalled for. If they attempt to pocket selfish political gains by singing the anti-China tune, they will end up shooting themselves in the foot and becoming a laughing stock in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347167.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211122_10451497.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 22 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 22nd by pointing out that we welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises who support investment and development on the mainland, and we will continue to protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in accordance with the law.…","Zhu Fenglian said that the words and deeds of the “Taiwan independence” diehards in pursuing “independence” are vile, seriously undermine cross-Strait relations, seriously endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Those diehards, their affiliated enterprises and their financial backers must be punished in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211122_12392201.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-23","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","A US warship sailed through the Taiwan Strait today as part of what the US called routine activity. Does China have any comment on this?","The spokesperson of the People's Liberation Army (PLA) Eastern Theater Command already responded to the issue. The Chinese side was closely following and fully aware of the US military vessel's passage through the Taiwan Strait. The US warships have repeatedly flexed muscles, made provocations and stirred up trouble in the Taiwan Strait in the name of “freedom of navigation”. This is by no means commitment to freedom and openness, but rather deliberate disruption and sabotage of regional peace and stability. The international community sees this plainly.\nChina is firmly resolved in upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US side should immediately correct its mistakes, stop making provocations, challenging the bottom line and playing with fire, and play a more constructive role in regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347168.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211123_10452063.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-23","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","It is reported that the US State Department spokesperson said the establishment of the “representative office” by the Taiwan authorities in Lithuania is an important step to expand Taiwan’s international space. “We reaffirm our support for Lithuania,” he said. Does China have any comment?","The one-China principle is a widely recognized norm governing international relations, an overwhelming consensus of the international community and the political foundation for China and countries it has diplomatic ties with to develop bilateral relations. In response to acts undermining China’s national sovereignty and security interests, the Chinese side took reasonable and lawful countermeasures to defend its own legitimate rights and interests, and international fairness and justice.\nThe relevant remarks of the US side are an unwitting confession which only serves to prove that Lithuania’s approval of the establishment of the \"Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania\" blatantly creates the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world and that Lithuania is colluding with the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The remarks also make us see clearly who is behind all this.\nThe US should abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US Joint Communiqués, adhere to its solemn political commitments made upon the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China, stop instigating disputes and confrontation, and avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We would also like to admonish the Lithuanian side that being a cat’s paw for some major country will only end up getting itself burnt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347168.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211123_10452063.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-24","Zhao Lijian","Radio Television Hong Kong","As the participant list published on the US State Department website shows, US President Biden has invited about 110 countries and regions to attend the \"Summit for Democracy\", the Taiwan authorities included. What is the foreign ministry's response?","China firmly opposes the invitation by the US to the Taiwan authorities to the so-called \"Summit for Democracy\". There is but one China in the world, the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the one-China principle is a widely recognized norm governing international relations. Taiwan has no other status in international law than being part of China. We solemnly urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués, stop providing \"Taiwan independence\" forces with any platform, and stop bolstering and emboldening them. Those offering platform to \"Taiwan independence\" forces will find themselves in an awkward place. Those playing with fire with \"Taiwan independence\" forces will end up getting burned.\nAs to the \"Summit for Democracy\", we have repeatedly stated our position. Democracy is a common value of all humanity, not the patent of a few countries. What the US has done shows exactly that it is only using democracy as a cover and tool to advance its geostrategic goals, suppress other countries, divide the world, and serve its selfish agenda of maintaining hegemony. Its acts of practicing bloc politics and inciting confrontation under the guise of democracy are reincarnation of the Cold War mentality and have been widely questioned and rejected by visionary people of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347169.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211124_10452621.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-24","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","First question. According to the website of US State Department, US Under Secretary Jose Fernandez attended the second US-Taiwan Economic Prosperity Partnership Dialogue online on November 22. The two sides welcomed the dialogue as an opportunity to deepen cooperation. The American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) said the two sides plan to convene the Digital Economy Forum and the first in-person Science and Technology…","On your first question. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions in any name or form between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The US should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués, immediately stop elevating relations with Taiwan in essence, stop any form of official interaction and contact with Taiwan and stop sending any wrong signal to \"Taiwan independence\" forces. We also have this stern warning to the Taiwan authorities that any attempt and act to solicit US and other foreign support and sabotage cross-Strait relations is doomed to fail.\nOn your second question. It is China's consistent and clear-cut position that we oppose politicization of business projects and oppose unilateral and illegal sanctions.\nOut of its own geopolitical and economic interests and following the \"America first\" mantra, the US has been putting its domestic law above normal international relations, imposing unwarranted sanctions on normal cooperation between sovereign countries, and willfully slapping \"long-arm jurisdiction\" on other countries. Such flagrant bullying and hegemonic mentality tramples on international law and basic norms governing international relations and undermines other countries' legitimate rights and interests. This wins no support and will ultimately face opposition from the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347169.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211124_10452621.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-24","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","J.P.Morgan CEO Jamie Dimon said on Tuesday that \"the Communist Party is celebrating its 100th year -- so is J.P.Morgan. I'd make a bet we last longer.\" He also made some comments on the Taiwan question. Do you have any comment about these remarks?","Isn't Bloomberg a serious media outlet? Why the publicity stunt with some grandstanding remarks?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347169.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211124_10452621.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-24","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","China has announced its decision to downgrade China-Lithuania diplomatic relations. Will China take relevant punitive measures in other areas such as economy and trade?","China has reiterated on many occasions that it will take all necessary measures to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity and safeguard its core interests. Lithuania has acted in bad faith and knowingly made a mistake. It openly creates the false impression of \"one China, one Taiwan\", and sets an egregious precedent in the world. It must pay for the mistake it has made.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347169.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211124_10452621.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on November 24, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Regarding the mainland's publication of the “Resolution of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on the Major Achievements and Historical Experience of the Party over the Past Century,” the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed it would handle cross-Strait issues with an attitude of “not capitulating and not rashly advancing,” and called on the mainland to “respect reality and Taiwan public…","The DPP authorities distorted and slandered the relevant content of the “CPC Central Committee Resolution on Major Achievements and Historical Experience of the Party's Century-Long Struggle,” exposing the political essence of their obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. In over five years, the DPP authorities have constantly undermined the peace and stability of cross-Strait relations and engaged in provocations to seek “independence.” They deny the “1992 Consensus” and deny that both sides belong to one China. Isn't this “recklessness”? They clamor for so-called “mutual non-subordination” and peddle the “two-state theory.” Isn't this “recklessness”? They collude with external forces to create cross-Strait confrontation and attempt to coerce compatriots in Taiwan onto the evil path of “anti-China and seeking independence.” Isn't this “recklessness”?\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided. Advancing cross-Strait relations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” for peaceful development accords with the shared aspirations and fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides and is the mainstream public opinion across the Strait. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, have repeatedly engaged in reckless provocations to seek “independence,” causing tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait, undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and running counter to the mainstream public opinion on both sides.\nThe inevitability of national reunification and the doom of “Taiwan independence” are determined by the trend of cross-Strait relations and the historical process of national rejuvenation. They are an irreversible historical current. We hope that the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan will see clearly the trend of history, follow the currents of the times, join hands and share hearts with compatriots on the mainland, resolutely oppose and contain “Taiwan independence,” and strive together for national righteousness, Taiwan's future, and a bright future of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392631.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China reviewed and adopted the “Resolution of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on the Major Achievements and Historical Experience of the Party over the Past Century,” and the wording of its Taiwan-related content has drawn attention on both sides of the Strait. How should the Taiwan-related content of the…","The Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee was an important meeting of landmark significance, convened at an important moment marking the Party's centenary and at a key juncture where the two centenary goals converge. The Resolution of the CPC Central Committee on the Major Achievements and Historical Experience of the Party's Century of Struggle, adopted by the plenary session, scientifically summarizes the Party's glorious historical experience over its century of struggle. It is an action guide for the Party to learn from history and create the future, and to unite and lead the people onto a new journey toward realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe historical process in which the CPC has striven to resolve the Taiwan question and promote national reunification is an important component of the CPC's century-long history of struggle. The Resolution systematically summarizes how the CPC has always firmly held the leadership and initiative in cross-Strait relations and gathered the mighty strength of all Chinese people, including broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, effectively promoting major achievements in cross-Strait relations. It demonstrates the CPC's unwavering historical responsibility, sets out the task requirements of firmly advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland in the process of national rejuvenation, and points the way for us to further do Taiwan work in the new era.\nWe must earnestly study, publicize, and implement the spirit of the Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee, effectively turn the spirit of the plenary session into a powerful force for advancing Taiwan work, draw wisdom and strength from the major achievements and historical experience of the Party's century of struggle, resolutely implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, unswervingly uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct and interference by external forces, and unite broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to shoulder the great righteousness of the nation and jointly devote themselves to national rejuvenation and the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392632.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","When President Xi Jinping held a video meeting with the U.S. President, he stressed that the real status quo of the Taiwan question and the core content of the one-China principle are: there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. Some public opinion on the island holds that the mainland's…","President Xi Jinping, in the China-U.S. heads-of-state video meeting, expounded in depth to the U.S. side on China's position on the Taiwan question, clearly pointing out that the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. Successive U.S. administrations have made clear commitments to this. Whether it is UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 or the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, both clearly explain the true status quo of the Taiwan question and the core content of one China, namely that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China.\nOur policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. As far as cross-Strait relations are concerned, upholding the one-China principle means upholding that there is only one China in the world, that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are not to be divided. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. At the same time, our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering, and we will never allow anyone or any force to split the sacred territory of the motherland. Compatriots in Taiwan should, together with compatriots on the mainland, stand on the right side of history and jointly create the glorious undertaking of the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392629.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","When President Xi Jinping touched on the Taiwan question at the China-U.S. leaders' video meeting, he said that achieving complete reunification of China is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. We are patient and willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort; but if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and coerce, or even…","Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters, and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, the historical task of complete reunification of the motherland must be accomplished, and it certainly can be accomplished.\nAchieving national reunification by peaceful means best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. We have patience and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort. We adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” take the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as our guide, and promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, working for peace in the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation.\n“Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to national reunification and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. The root cause of the current tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities stubbornly cling to the “Taiwan independence” stance, “rely on the US to seek independence,” and “amend the Constitution to seek independence,” going further and further down the wrong path of “Taiwan independence” separatism. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke or coerce, or even cross red lines, we will have to take resolute measures to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to protect the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will recognize that the DPP authorities seek “independence” out of political self-interest, recognize the harmfulness and danger of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and act in practice to oppose being coerced by “Taiwan independence” and to safeguard their own interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392628.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, the mainland side published a list of “Taiwan independence” diehards, on which Su Zhenchang, Yu Xikun and Wu Zhaoxie are named. Some public opinion analysis holds that this is only the first batch, and other “Taiwan independence” diehards may be announced successively afterward. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","Su Zhenchang, You Xikun, Wu Zhaoxie and a very small number of other obstinate “Taiwan independence” diehards have stirred up cross-Strait confrontation, undermined cross-Strait relations, plotted to split the country, and endangered peace in the Taiwan Strait, and we will impose punishment on them in accordance with the law. It is clear that the list of obstinate “Taiwan independence” diehards does not stop at these three people. We also note that recently a few “Taiwan independence” elements have been jumping rather high, and some even claimed to feel “regret” at not being included on the list of obstinate “Taiwan independence” diehards. Don't be in a hurry, there will be a time when they truly have cause for regret.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392627.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Please Spokesperson Introduce the Latest Situation of Vaccination for Taiwan Compatriots on the Mainland.","As of November 15, about 172,000 Taiwan compatriots had been vaccinated on the mainland, with a cumulative total of about 330,000 doses administered.\nWe have noted that some Taiwan compatriots wish to learn how to obtain vaccination certificates, so allow me to introduce this here. The relevant departments on the mainland have clear regulations on the registration and reporting of information for COVID-19 vaccination recipients. Vaccination units should promptly record vaccination-related information and provide a preventive vaccination certificate to the recipient after vaccination is completed. Taiwan compatriots who have completed vaccination on the mainland may obtain a preventive vaccination certificate from the vaccination unit, or may check their personal electronic vaccination information through channels such as the Health Code mini-program. Please take a look: this is the reference format for the preventive vaccination certificate issued by the Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism of the State Council; this is a preventive vaccination certificate issued by a vaccination unit in Guangdong; and these are electronic preventive vaccination certificates issued by the Shanghai Health Cloud software and the Beijing Health Treasure mini-program.\nTaiwan compatriots who have been vaccinated on the mainland and need certificates may obtain vaccination certificates in the above manner in their respective localities. If they encounter difficulties, the Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities can provide assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan's Far Eastern Group has been punished in accordance with law for violations of laws and regulations in environmental protection and land use by its chemical fiber, textile, and cement enterprises in Shanghai, Jiangsu, and three other provinces and municipalities. Can the spokesperson introduce the specific situation? Previously, the TAO said it would not allow diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and…","First question: Recently, law enforcement authorities in Shanghai, Jiangsu, Jiangxi, Hubei, Sichuan and other provinces and municipalities conducted law enforcement inspections and found that the chemical fiber, textile and cement enterprises invested in by Taiwan's Far Eastern Group have committed a series of violations of laws and regulations in environmental protection, land use, occupational health of employees, work safety and fire protection, taxation, product quality and other areas. The relevant law enforcement authorities adhered to facts as the basis and law as the criterion, and imposed penalties on the enterprises involved in accordance with relevant national laws, regulations and procedures.\nAccording to preliminary information, fines and recovered taxes totaling about 474 million yuan have been imposed so far, and idle construction land of one of the enterprises has been reclaimed. Investigation and handling are still ongoing. The illegal and irregular conduct of the enterprises concerned and the legal basis for the penalties have been published on the websites of the relevant law enforcement authorities in accordance with legal procedures, and everyone can look them up.\nSecond question: Punishing “Taiwan independence” die-hards and their affiliated enterprises and financial backers in accordance with the law is fundamentally aimed at safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. We encourage and support normal economic and trade exchanges across the Strait and protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in accordance with the law. However, we will absolutely not allow any individual or enterprise to earn money on the mainland while acting as a financial backer and providing financial support to “Taiwan independence” die-hards. We will take necessary measures in accordance with the law to severely punish the affiliated enterprises and financial backers of “Taiwan independence” die-hards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Compatriots from Taiwan are still very concerned about the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry,” and hope to learn about the specific implementation methods in various localities through more channels. What work has been done by various localities to help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises understand their participation in the implementation of relevant policies and measures?","Since the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” were introduced, various localities have used multiple means to help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises gain a deeper understanding of the policies and make good use of them. Preliminary statistics show that Jiangsu, Fujian, Shandong, Henan, Hubei, Guangdong, Sichuan, Shaanxi and other provinces, as well as Weifang in Shandong and Guangzhou in Guangdong, have issued relevant implementation opinions, operation guides or policy interpretations based on local conditions. These introduce the specific application and handling procedures, policy basis, consultation windows and other details of each matter, making the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” concrete and easy to implement.\nZhejiang, Anhui, Hubei, Guangdong and 13 other provinces have set up special columns through WeChat official accounts, websites and other channels, and Beijing, Zhejiang, Jiangxi and 8 other provinces and municipalities have done so through newspapers, magazines, television and radio stations, broadcasting the full text of the policies, policy interpretation articles, service guides and other materials. For example, the WeChat official account of the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “E-Tai Home” (鄂台e家), has recently released a series of service guides for Taiwan compatriots applying for agricultural machinery purchase subsidies, start-up guaranteed loans with interest subsidies, and agricultural insurance premium subsidies. These guides are very specific and practical.\nBeijing, Hebei, Inner Mongolia, Anhui, Guangdong, Qinghai and other provinces (autonomous regions and municipalities), as well as the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps, have repeatedly visited and investigated Taiwan-invested agriculture and forestry enterprises to understand their situation, solicit opinions and carry out face-to-face promotion and explanation.\nZhejiang, Hubei, Guangdong, Guangxi, Sichuan, Yunnan, Shaanxi and other provinces and regions have held more than 40 events, including publicity and explanation meetings, seminars and training sessions, and have printed and distributed promotional brochures. Beijing, Shanghai, Yunnan, Hubei and other provinces and municipalities have organized nearly 30 promotion meetings, matchmaking events and other activities to interpret policies and promote matching of agriculture and forestry projects.\nWe will continue to work with relevant departments and localities to thoroughly implement the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry.” We also hope that broad Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises will make good use of the various measures, participate deeply in and share the greater development opportunities brought by the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” and achieve greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392624.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The Ministry of Natural Resources recently said that it will, together with relevant departments and Fujian Province, study how to “include major transportation and other infrastructure for cross-Strait integrated development in relevant national plans.” The Implementation Opinions on Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development, previously issued by Fujian Province, also mention advancing the…","Promoting the full connectivity of cross-Strait transportation, including infrastructure connectivity, is a major proposal put forward by General Secretary Xi Jinping. It meets the needs of deepening cross-Strait integrated development and serves the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides. The mainland is planning and promoting work related to cross-Strait transportation infrastructure construction. The Pingtan section of the Pingtan Strait Road-Rail Dual-Purpose Bridge has achieved full connection of both highway and railway; relevant departments of Fujian Province have completed a preliminary technical plan for bridges linking Kinmen and Matsu; and the “Outline of the National Comprehensive Three-Dimensional Transportation Network Plan,” issued by the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, has planned the construction of a Fuzhou-to-Taipei branch line. Building a more convenient and unobstructed transportation network between the two sides as soon as possible will provide better transportation resources and services for compatriots on both sides and benefit them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","China recently decided to downgrade its diplomatic relations with Lithuania to the level of chargé d'affaires. A Taiwan scholar believes that Lithuania dares to challenge the one-China principle mainly because it was incited and instigated by the United States and colluded with by the DPP authorities. What comments does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this?","Regarding the downgrading of China-Lithuania diplomatic relations to chargé d’affaires level, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position. It must be pointed out that the relevant conduct of the DPP authorities once again shows that their dealings internationally, whether under the banner of “democracy” or under the cover of trade cooperation, are in essence peddling “Taiwan independence” positions such as the “two-state theory,” attempting to split the country. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and force the issue, or even cross red lines, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.\nWe also advise any anti-China forces in the international community that are pro-Taiwan: using Taiwan to contain China is very dangerous. It is playing with fire, and those who play with fire will burn themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the so-called “constitutional amendment” draft proposed by the DPP passed the first reading in Taiwan's legislature. Its contents include lowering the threshold for “constitutional amendment,” among others. What is your comment?","We are paying close attention to the relevant developments. We firmly oppose any form of “amending the constitution to seek independence,” including lowering the threshold to open the door for seeking independence and slipping the issue of seeking independence in through the back door. The DPP, in pursuit of its own interests and disregarding the firm opposition and solemn warnings of all parties, is bent on going its own way, and will surely reap the consequences. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait in Taiwan must stay highly alert, consciously oppose and resist all forms of “amending the constitution to seek independence,” and not be bound step by step by the DPP onto the “independence” chariot.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211124_12392626.htm"],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","On the 22nd, the economic authority of the DPP authorities released statistics showing that approved mainland investment in Taiwan (including additional investment) in the first ten months of this year totaled US$41.3 million, a decrease of 66.68% from the same period last year. Some media on the island pointed out that the DPP authorities have continued to tighten policies on mainland investment in Taiwan for…","Investment by mainland enterprises in Taiwan is conducive to complementary advantages between enterprises on both sides of the Strait and to jointly enhancing competitiveness. It is also conducive to increasing employment on the island and promoting economic development. It is a good thing that benefits both sides. However, since the DPP authorities came to power, out of political considerations aimed at seeking “independence,” they have strictly guarded against and restricted mainland capital investing in Taiwan. These excessively politicized practices have clearly worsened the island's business environment and seriously affected the willingness of mainland capital to invest in Taiwan. In the end, they will only limit Taiwan's own economic development space and harm the vital interests of the island's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","Could the spokesperson introduce the current preparations for this year's Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit? When will it be held?","Following consultations between both sides of the summit, the 2021 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit is planned to be held in Nanjing, Jiangsu, on December 7. This year’s summit is hosted by the mainland side, adopting a combination of online and offline formats, with main venues set up in Nanjing and Taipei respectively. Members of the Cross-Strait Summit Council, summit members, entrepreneurs, and representative scholars from relevant fields will attend. Centered on the theme “Grasping the New Landscape, Sharing New Opportunities,” the summit will explore in depth how cross-Strait entrepreneurs can seize the new opportunities of the mainland’s high-quality development, further strengthen exchanges and cooperation, and achieve greater development for themselves. At present, both sides of the summit are orderly carrying out preparatory work for the annual meeting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the United States and Taiwan successively held the so-called “political and economic dialogue,” “defense seminar” and “economic dialogue.” The Taiwan authorities claimed that U.S.-Taiwan relations are stable. What is your comment?","We resolutely oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the “Taiwan region of China,” and urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities’ “relying on the US to seek independence” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","Reports say that the gunman in the New Taipei shooting case fled to Xiamen on the 23rd and is currently in quarantine at an epidemic prevention hotel, and that Taiwan police have requested mainland assistance in arresting him. Does the spokesperson have any latest information?","We have noted the relevant reports, and the situation is being further verified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Regarding the mainland's punishment of Taiwan's Far Eastern Group in accordance with law, some in Taiwan worry that it may cause Taiwanese businesses that support cross-Strait relations development or support the mainland to return to Taiwan for investment. What is the spokesperson's view? The MAC claims this is intimidation of Taiwanese businesses and says it will propose so-called “countermeasures.” Is the…","First question: Our position of welcoming and supporting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises investing and developing on the mainland, and of safeguarding their legitimate rights and interests in accordance with law, has not changed. We are willing to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, provide them with more equal treatment, continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and bring greater benefits to compatriots on both sides. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will distinguish right from wrong, take a firm stand, draw a clear line with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and use concrete actions to safeguard and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nSecond question: We are closely following relevant developments. The mainland side has, in accordance with law, imposed punishment on a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards; our attitude is clear and our position firm. If some forces on the island openly prop up and champion “Taiwan independence” figures, they will inevitably face the appropriate countermeasures. No person or force should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Beijing Stock Exchange recently officially opened for trading. What impact will this have on Taiwan-invested enterprises listed on the mainland and on their future development?","The Beijing Stock Exchange is a specialized platform serving the innovative development of small and medium-sized enterprises. It mainly focuses on 'specialized, refined, distinctive, and innovative' industries such as manufacturing, information technology, materials, and healthcare, bringing major benefits to high-quality SMEs with strong specialization and distinctive advantages in a particular field, by facilitating their listing and accelerating their connection with the capital market. The relevant policies apply equally to Taiwan-funded enterprises. This means that Taiwan-funded enterprises have greater room and better opportunities to participate in the mainland's multi-tiered capital market system. We welcome Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to seize the opportunities and actively participate by giving full play to their own strengths, so as to achieve better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The 2021 “Shanghai–Taipei City Forum” will be held next month. Please introduce the current preparations.","Following consultations between relevant parties in Shanghai and Taipei, the 2021 “Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” will be held via videoconference on December 1, with venues set up in Shanghai and Taipei respectively.\nThe theme of this forum is “New Economy, New Development.” Through exchanges and discussions, it will promote experience-sharing and interaction between the two cities on “readable architecture” and “digital transformation of cities under normalized epidemic prevention and control.” Over the years, Shanghai and Taipei have, through the city forum, deeply explored and exchanged urban development experiences and consolidated and expanded cooperation in various fields, achieving positive results. To date, 36 exchange and cooperation memoranda have been signed. We welcome further deepening of exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields. We believe such exchanges and cooperation are conducive to strengthening the family ties and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, promoting the common development of cities across the Strait, and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","The US State Department recently announced the “Summit for Democracy” to be held in December and listed “Taiwan” on its official website, while the mainland was not on the list. What is your response?","First of all, it must be pointed out that the Taiwan-related titles listed on the US website are wrong. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and China’s Taiwan region; this position is consistent and clear. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","During the video meeting between Chinese and US heads of state, US President Biden clearly stated that the United States does not support “Taiwan independence.” However, the US Congress’s subordinate body, the U.S.-China Economic and Security Review Commission, recently released a report that urges strengthening Taiwan’s so-called “defense capabilities” and reinforcing its so-called “military threat” to the…","The “committee” you mentioned has long published reports that are inconsistent with the facts and full of prejudice. The Taiwan-related content of such reports seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously interferes in China's internal affairs, and we firmly oppose it.\nSome people on the island use this so-called “report” to lend endorsement to “Taiwan independence,” which is extremely ridiculous. No matter how much the “Taiwan independence” forces make trouble, their attempt to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体记者","Nearly 80% of Taiwan's top 500 companies have business on the mainland, and they donate to both the blue and green camps during elections; the difference lies in the proportion. The mainland's investigation of Taiwan's Far Eastern Group in accordance with the law has caused a certain chilling effect among Taiwan businesspeople. Everyone wants to know whether the financial backers on the sanctions list have been…","First question: We will absolutely not allow affiliated enterprises and financial backers of diehard “Taiwan independence” figures to profit on the mainland, and we will not allow Taiwan enterprises to earn money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” on the island and undermining cross-Strait relations, which would be destroying the rice bowl that feeds them. This position is clear and consistent. Taiwan enterprises with investments on the mainland understand this well, and we believe the responsible persons of these enterprises have a clear understanding of whether they should donate to diehard “Taiwan independence” figures.\nSecond question: Whether to adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and whether to oppose or support “Taiwan independence” separatism, are major issues of right and wrong in cross-Strait relations. They concern peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and the safety and well-being of every Taiwan resident, and there is simply no room for ambiguity. We sincerely hope that all Taiwan compatriots will cherish peace as they cherish their own eyes, pursue unification as they pursue the happiness of life, and actively join the righteous cause of promoting the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视记者","Some commentators in Taiwan believe the mainland is using the investigation of “green financial backers” to manipulate Taiwan's elections. What is your view?","We never interfere in Taiwan's regional elections. Cracking down on “Taiwan independence” diehards and their affiliated enterprises and backers in accordance with the law is to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, to safeguard the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, and to strike at and contain “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Some public opinion holds that the mainland's punishment of Taiwan's Far Eastern Group according to law targets not only the DPP but also the KMT. May I ask whether the identification of “backers of Taiwan independence” will be based solely on the list of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, or whether it may also cover Taiwanese businesspeople who support the KMT?","I would like to reiterate once again that we will never allow the affiliated enterprises and financial backers of “Taiwan independence” diehards to profit on the mainland, and we will never allow Taiwanese companies to make money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” on the island and undermining cross-Strait relations. This position is clear and consistent. Regarding “Taiwan independence” diehards and their affiliated enterprises and financial backers, we will, based on facts and in accordance with the law, carry out precise crackdowns.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The political commissar of the Eastern Theater Command said in an earlier interview that it resolutely contains “Taiwan independence” conduct and effectively responds to any provocation from the sea. The Eastern Theater Command also recently explicitly defined the military activities it organizes as “combat-readiness patrols.” Some analysts point out that this represents round-the-clock combat-readiness duty with…","The Eastern Theater Command organized forces to conduct combat-readiness patrols and joint sea-air exercises in the Taiwan Strait. These are necessary measures to respond to the provocations of “Taiwan independence” forces seeking independence. We resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and we will thwart any person or force from planning or carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","When President Xi Jinping touched on the Taiwan question at the China-U.S. leaders' video meeting, he said that achieving complete reunification of China is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. We are patient and willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort; but if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and coerce, or even…","“Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, the greatest obstacle to national reunification, and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. In response to external interference and to a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. The 《Anti-Secession Law》 clearly stipulates several circumstances under which the state may adopt non-peaceful means and other necessary measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, clarifying the legal bottom line and red line. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope more Taiwan compatriots will recognize the harm and danger of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and that for the sake of national righteousness, Taiwan's future, and their own interests and well-being, they will stand up and, together with mainland compatriots, eliminate the root of “Taiwan independence” and jointly thwart “Taiwan independence” schemes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities recently claimed that they would accelerate the work of completing accession to the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), declaring that this is an important so-called “strategic goal of Taiwan's current foreign economic and trade policy.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The question of Taiwan's participation in regional economic cooperation must be premised on the one-China principle. We firmly oppose Taiwan's participation in any free trade arrangement or signing of any free trade agreement of an official nature.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202111/t20211124_12392621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, the Social Democratic Party, the Greens and the Free Democratic Party of Germany held a joint press conference on November 24. They announced the completion of government coalition negotiations and officially released the coalition agreement, which involves such China-related issues as Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong. What is China’s comment? Can you share your view on the bilateral relations…","China attaches importance to the China-Germany comprehensive strategic partnership. We believe that developing the bilateral relations well meets the common interests of the two countries and the two peoples, and benefits China-Europe exchange and cooperation. Next year will mark the 50th anniversary of the establishment of China-Germany diplomatic relations. We hope the new German government can carry on China policies that are practical, work with China in the same direction, develop bilateral relations based on mutual respect, equality and mutual benefits, and focus on advancing practical cooperation between China and Germany in various areas.\nI want to stress that issues related to Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are all China’s internal affairs, bearing on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Successive German governments all followed the one-China policy. We hope the new German government would continue to follow the policy, respect China’s core interests and safeguard the political foundation for the bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","CRI","According to media reports, Lithuania’s Minister of the Economy and Innovation disclosed that Lithuania will sign a US$600 million export credit agreement with the US, after China vowed to take all necessary measures in response to Lithuania’s decision to allow the Taiwan authorities to set up the so-called “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania”. Media reports are saying that Lithuania is likely to get US…","The reports you mentioned are further proof that behind Lithuania’s provocative move, there is a puppeteer master running the entire show with premeditation. The international community can see this clearly.\nI want to stress the following points. Lithuania chose to pave its way to the loans by harming China’s sovereignty. It is an immoral and dangerous deal. In disregard of China’s solemn representations and international justice, Lithuania acted in bad faith as a cat’s paw for a major country. Eventually it shall pay for this.\nThe US went so far as to coerce or cajole other countries into serving as fodder for its political agenda. No responsible country would ever act in this way. At the end of the day, such behavior will hurt others as well as itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","Macau Monthly","It is reported that Lithuanian Foreign Minister Gabrielius Landsbergis who was visiting the US said on November 24 that he had discussions with senior US officials about making the country less dependent on China. “I think that the biggest lesson out of Lithuania is that economic coercion does not necessarily mean that the country needs to step away from independent foreign policy decisions,” he said, adding that…","Lithuania ignored China’s stern position, disregarded the bigger picture of China-Lithuania relations and basic norms governing international relations, and openly created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world, thus creating an egregious precedent. China always makes resolute and necessary responses to all provocative moves undermining China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Those acting in bad faith and going further down the wrong path will only reap what they sow.\nIf the Lithuanian government is still making independent foreign policy decisions like the Lithuanian Foreign Minister said, how will he explain what he is doing in the US?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","US Under Secretary of State Jose W. Fernandez talked about the outcomes of the second US-Taiwan Economic Prosperity Partnership Dialogue (EPPD) in an interview, saying, “We are going to start creating private-sector engagement between the two private sectors” to deepen economic ties. He said the US told Taiwan the measures it can take to counter China’s economic coercion. The US believes very strongly that…","I already stated China’s position on this yesterday. China firmly opposes official interaction between the US side and the Taiwan authorities in any form. We have lodged solemn representations with the US side. Certain US officials should immediately stop making irresponsible remarks and sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nWe also noted the latest cliche from certain US officials. I must stress that the US stretches the national security concept, abuses state power, and even resorted to such means as fabricating lies to wantonly suppress foreign businesses. With myriads of tricks up its sleeve, the US is a peerless master of coercion, juggling economic, military, hostage and other sorts of coercion. China has nothing to do with the word coercion. A stern warning to certain US officials: forming small cliques in the world and attempting to smear China by distorting facts will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","Hubei Media Group","On November 24, a State Department official said in a telephone briefing on condition of anonymity that Brian Nichols, the US Assistant Secretary of State for Western Hemisphere Affairs, led a delegation to Honduras, where they explained to two Presidential candidates why the Honduras-Taiwan relationship is important and said they would like to see that continue. The US also warned Central American nations of…","It is not China’s approach that the Latin American people should be wary of, but the US’ long-standing hegemonic approach of regarding Central American countries as US “backyard”. With the acts in Honduras, the US blatantly violates the one-China principle, and points fingers at and grossly interferes in others’ internal affairs. Is this “rules-based order” long preached by the US? Is this “democracy” championed by the US? What the US has done shows its so-called “rules-based order” is nothing but “the strong bullying the weak”, and the so-called “democracy” is nothing but “pitting one group against the other”.\nSince the Monroe Doctrine was enunciated in 1823, Monroeism has been haunting Latin America. The US infiltration and oppression in Latin America can be found anytime, anywhere. There are no stones left unturned: military intervention, political subversion, bribery, and the list goes on. All this has severely impeded Latin America’s political and economic development and brought deep sufferings to Latin American people. Even to this day, the US, holding to the old dream two centuries ago, still sees Latin America as its sphere of influence and “backyard”. Such power politics and hegemonic practices by the US are abhorred by the Latin American people and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-25","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The United States has made it clear to both leading Presidential candidates in Honduras’ election that Washington wants the country to maintain its longstanding diplomatic relations with Taiwan. Would you comment on it?","I just elaborated on China’s position on the relevant issue. The US moves blatantly violate the one-China principle and constitute flagrant and gross interference in other countries’ internal affairs. Such acts of power politics and hegemony will garner no support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347170.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211125_10453188.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","At the regular press conference of the Ministry of National Defense of China on July 28, spokesperson Wu Qian pointed out that China values China-US military relations, but China's development of military relations is governed by principles: China's sovereignty, dignity and core interests are not to be infringed upon. He also emphasized that China demands that the US stop its infringing and provocative actions, strictly restrain its frontline forces, and prevent accidents from occurring.\nA reporter asked: Recently, Li Zuocheng, member of the Central Military Commission and Chief of the Joint Staff Department of the CMC, held a video call with Milley, Chairman of the US Joint Chiefs of Staff. According to US Department of Defense officials, Milley requested that the US military collect all China-US military interactions over the past five years to assess the overall situation of the continuously increasing interactions between the two sides in the South China Sea and other regions. Please the spokesperson further introduce the relevant situation and comment.\nWu Qian introduced that not long ago, Li Zuocheng, member of the Central Military Commission and Chief of the Joint Staff Department of the CMC, held a video call with Milley, Chairman of the US Joint Chiefs of Staff. The two sides exchanged in-depth views on the international and regional situation, China-US relations and military relations between the two countries, Taiwan, maritime and air military security issues, and other matters, and reached an important consensus on maintaining the stable development of military relations and avoiding conflict and confrontation. This was a frank, in-depth and constructive strategic communication.\nWu Qian said that China-US military relations are an important component of the relationship between the two countries. China values military relations, but China's development of military relations is governed by principles: China's sovereignty, dignity and core interests are not to be infringed upon. Regarding some statements by the US side, China listens to what they say but will watch what they do more closely. Some people in the US who cling to erroneous perceptions of China and insist on comprehensive containment and suppression of China will not be tolerated by China, which will naturally take resolute countermeasures.\nWu Qian pointed out that regarding the maritime and air military security issues raised by the reporter, their root cause lies in the US's infringing and provocative actions, such as long-term, large-scale, high-intensity close-in reconnaissance and harassment in China's sea and air space facing it, as well as highly targeted military exercises and training. China firmly opposes this and has taken reasonable, forceful, secure and professional measures to respond resolutely. 'We demand that the US stop its infringing and provocative actions, strictly restrain its frontline forces, and prevent accidents from occurring.'","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9615962.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","At the regular press conference of the Chinese Ministry of National Defense on the 28th, spokesperson Wu Qian said that the People's Liberation Army will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatist acts or external interference, and will firmly counter them. Actions speak louder than words.\nA reporter asked: The Taiwan defense authorities recently claimed that PLA aircraft have repeatedly crossed the so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait,” seriously undermining regional peace and stability, and hyped up a PLA warship that recently appeared off the coast of Hualien. A Taiwan source said that in view of the visit to Taiwan by U.S. Senator Scott, the PLA “clearly sent out a provocative message.” What is your comment on this?\nWu Qian pointed out that Taiwan is part of China, and there is absolutely no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait” between the two sides. At present, the root cause of the tension and volatility in the Taiwan Strait is the collusion and mischief of “Taiwan independence” forces and external forces. It is precisely the DPP authorities, which continue to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation, and the external forces attempting to “use Taiwan to contain China,” that are undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nWu Qian said that the People's Liberation Army will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatist acts or external interference, and will firmly counter them. Actions speak louder than words. Relevant parties need to learn to adapt, learn to reflect, and, more importantly, learn to pull back from the brink.\nAnother reporter asked: The U.S. House of Representatives recently passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” which reaffirmed so-called “U.S. support for Taiwan's defense,” stating that the U.S. military has the right to conduct joint exercises with Taiwan and invite Taiwan to participate in the “RIMPAC” exercises. The U.S. government also recently approved a new round of arms sales to Taiwan. What is the Chinese side's comment on this?\nWu Qian pointed out that Taiwan is Taiwan of China, the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and it brooks no interference from the United States. For some time, the United States has said one thing and done another: on the one hand, it claims to adhere to the One China policy and not support “Taiwan independence,” while on the other hand, it strengthens military and political collusion with the so-called Taiwan region of China and rolls out arms sales plans to Taiwan. This playing with fire is extremely dangerous. It will seriously impact China-U.S. and military-to-military relations, seriously endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and seriously raise the risk of military confrontation between China and the United States.\n“Reunifying the motherland and preventing separation is the sacred mission of the Chinese People's Liberation Army. We will, as always, have zero tolerance for ‘Taiwan independence,’ show no leniency in combating ‘Taiwan independence,’ and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity,” the spokesperson said.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2021/11-25/9616013.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","According to the official Weibo account of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense, Ministry of National Defense spokesperson Wu Qian made a statement on Pelosi's intrusive visit to Taiwan. Wu Qian said that on August 2, Speaker of the U.S. House of Representatives Pelosi intruded into the Taiwan region of China. The Chinese side strongly condemns this and firmly opposes it.\nThe Chinese side has repeatedly made clear the serious consequences of such a visit to Taiwan, but Pelosi knowingly and deliberately went ahead, maliciously provoked and created a crisis. This seriously violates the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously undermines the political foundation of China-U.S. relations, and seriously damages the relations between the two militaries of China and the United States. The U.S. move sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and further exacerbates the escalation of tensions across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing to advance their own interests, colluded with external forces to create chaos, and insisted on inviting Pelosi to visit Taiwan. Their conduct is extremely dangerous and is bound to lead to serious consequences. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is on high alert and will carry out a series of targeted military actions in response, resolutely defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely thwarting external interference and the “Taiwan independence” separatist plot.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616033.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","On August 2, U.S. House Speaker Pelosi made an intrusive visit to China's Taiwan region. This move runs counter to the U.S. side's commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" constitutes a serious political provocation against China, a serious damage to China-U.S. and China-U.S. military-to-military relations, and a huge shock and threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China strongly indignant and strongly opposes this. The Chinese military means what it says. The Eastern Theater Command of the People's Liberation Army organized targeted drills around the waters and airspace of Taiwan Island involving multiple services and multiple科目 such as joint maritime assault, land strikes, and air superiority operations, and organized live-fire shooting with precision-guided weapons, which constitutes a stern deterrent aimed at the collusion between the United States and Taiwan.\nWe solemnly warn the U.S. side and the DPP authorities: \"Using Taiwan to contain China\" is doomed to fail, and \"relying on foreign powers to enhance one's own position\" has no way out. The collusion and provocation between the U.S. and Taiwan will only push Taiwan toward the abyss of disaster and will only bring profound harm to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Firmly safeguarding China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the resolute will of 1.4 billion Chinese people, and the complete reunification of China is an unstoppable historical trend. The will of the people cannot be defied, and those who play with fire will burn themselves. We will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will leave absolutely no room for any form of \"Taiwan independence\" acts or external interference.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616039.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Recently, in response to Pelosi's “visit” to Taiwan, China announced eight countermeasures, including the cancellation of three measures for China-US military exchanges. US media reported that senior US military officials had called Chinese military leaders several times recently, but were rejected by the Chinese side. What is your comment on this?","The current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait was entirely caused by the United States' proactive provocation and unilateral creation. The U.S. side must bear full responsibility and the serious consequences. China has repeatedly stated its solemn position on China-U.S. military-to-military relations, the Taiwan question, and related issues, and has made multiple stern representations in particular regarding the intrusive visit of U.S. House Speaker Pelosi. Yet the U.S. side says one thing and does another, condoning and supporting Pelosi's visit and deliberately creating tension in the Taiwan Strait.\nIn response to the U.S.'s egregious provocative conduct, China has announced eight countermeasures, including canceling the arranged video call between the theater commanders of the two militaries, canceling the China-U.S. defense departments' working meeting, and canceling the meeting of the China-U.S. Maritime Military Security Consultation Mechanism. These Chinese countermeasures are necessary warnings against the U.S.-Taiwan provocations and a legitimate defense of national sovereignty and security, entirely reasonable, appropriate, and proportionate.\nThe bottom line cannot be crossed, and communication requires sincerity. The U.S. side creates crises on one hand while claiming it wants to manage them on the other, seeking excuses and cover for its wrong words and provocative actions, and even hyping and confusing the public externally and shifting blame. We firmly oppose this. We urge the U.S. side to genuinely respect China's core interests and major concerns, abandon the illusion of \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" and not go further and further down the wrong path.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616042.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to Taiwan media reports, after US House Speaker Pelosi visited Taiwan, the PLA organized high-intensity live-fire exercises in the sea and airspace around Taiwan island in a “Taiwan encirclement” style, with several missiles flying over Taiwan island. This may only be the beginning, and Taiwan’s shrinking strategic space cannot be restored. What is the comment on this?","The series of countermeasure operations that the Chinese People’s Liberation Army has recently carried out in the sea and airspace around the island of Taiwan are a solemn deterrent against the collusion and provocations between “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces. They are a legitimate and necessary step to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and the relevant exercises and training are open, transparent, and professional, in line with domestic law, international law, and international practice. U.S. House Speaker Pelosi stubbornly insisted on visiting the Taiwan region of China, brazenly challenging and undermining China’s core interests and seriously damaging peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing to advance themselves and provoking “independence,” disregard the safety of the people of Taiwan, push Taiwan into the abyss of disaster, and will ultimately be nailed to the pillar of historical shame!\nThe historical process of cross-Strait reunification is unstoppable, and the timing and momentum for resolving the Taiwan question have always been on the side of the forces advancing national reunification. For the welfare of the people of Taiwan, we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but the Chinese People’s Liberation Army will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts or interference by external forces. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, for the sake of party interests and personal gain, disregard national righteousness, go against the tide of the times, and are destined to walk the road of self-destruction with no return. At present, cross-Strait relations once again face a choice between two futures, and the Taiwan authorities must make the correct choice about where to go.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616064.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","According to the website of the Ministry of National Defense, Ministry of National Defense spokesperson Wu Qian, commenting on the visit to Taiwan by members of the U.S. Congress, said that the People's Liberation Army of China continues to train and prepare for combat, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely crushes any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist or foreign interference schemes.\nWu Qian said that on August 14, U.S. Senator Markey and others made a provocative visit to the Taiwan region of China. This blatantly violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, infringes on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, sends a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and fully exposes the true face of the United States as a disruptor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Eastern Theater Command of the PLA has organized joint multi-service combat readiness patrols and live-fire drills in the sea and airspace around Taiwan Island, which is a resolute response to and a stern deterrent against the collusion and provocation between the U.S. and Taiwan.\nHe pointed out that Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. We solemnly warn the U.S. side and the DPP authorities: “using Taiwan to contain China” is doomed to fail, and “relying on the U.S. to seek independence” will lead to self-destruction. Any scheme or act that goes against the tide of history, defies the will of the Chinese people as a whole, or obstructs the process of China's reunification is bound to end in failure. The People's Liberation Army of China continues to train and prepare for combat, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely crushes any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist or foreign interference schemes.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616078.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-11-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Officials from the US, Japan and other countries have repeatedly made statements recently, unjustifiably criticizing military exercises and training conducted by the Chinese military near Taiwan Island. What is your comment?","The remarks of the relevant country are completely a reversal of black and white and a shifting of blame. China has repeatedly stated its firm opposition. The causes and effects of the current situation in the Taiwan Strait are clear, and right and wrong are plain to see. The series of military training activities the Chinese People's Liberation Army has recently conducted around Taiwan Island is open, transparent, professional and proportionate. It is a warning and counterattack against provocateurs and disruptors, and a proper and righteous act of firmly defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The United States, as the instigator of this crisis, should and must bear full responsibility for it. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and immediately take measures to correct its mistakes, rather than further aggravating tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nRecently, Japan has echoed the US side's negative words and deeds on Taiwan, hyping the so-called “Chinese military threat,” which is extremely irresponsible. For some time, Japan has continued to increase its defense budget and strengthen its military deployments, which has already caused high vigilance among regional countries and the international community. We urge Japan to profoundly reflect on its own history of aggression, stop slandering and smearing China, and do more things that help enhance mutual trust with its neighbors and help maintain regional peace and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2021/11-25/9616096.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-11-26","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","It is reported that a bipartisan delegation of five members of the US House of Representatives visited Taiwan. The “foreign affairs department” of the Taiwan authorities issued a statement saying that they will exchange views on issues including Taiwan-US relations, and that the visits of delegation from the US Congress demonstrate the firm bipartisan and bicameral support to the bilateral relations. We noted…","The visit to Taiwan by certain US lawmakers gravely violates the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués and sends a seriously wrong signal of supporting the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly deplores and firmly rejects this and has lodged solemn representation with the US side.\nThe one-China principle is an unshakable norm governing international relations. The moves of certain US politicians to wantonly challenge the one-China principle and embolden the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have caused strong indignation among the 1.4 billion Chinese people. Taiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of China’s territory, not a card in international relations. We advise some in the US against playing the “Taiwan card”, because it will be an ill-conceived attempt that is doomed to fail. If they insist on playing this card, they will reap what they sow. China’s reunification is an unstoppable trend of history. The clumsy show put up by certain US politicians and the Taiwan authorities is only to be overwhelmed by China’s reunification process and can never change the unbreakable landscape where 180 countries in the world are committed to the one-China principle. All erroneous acts that run counter to the trend of China’s reunification are like ant trying to topple a giant tree and will end up in failure.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and bears on China’s core interests. The one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués constitute the political foundation of China-US relations. The US should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, immediately stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and clear the landmines and barriers in bilateral relations. A stern warning to the Taiwan authorities: Attempting to solicit foreign support and rely on the US to seek independence will prove a dead end.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347171.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211126_10453959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-26","Zhao Lijian","Hubei Media Group","Nathan Law said on his social media account that he met with Lithuania’s foreign minister and vice foreign minister, among others, and expressed thanks to their support for Taiwan and Hong Kong. Do you have any comment?","This individual you mentioned is opposed to China and attempts to destabilize Hong Kong, and is wanted by Hong Kong police. The Lithuanian side is now emboldening the anti-China, destabilizing forces like Nathan Law, immediately after it flagrantly created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”. What it did has further laid bare its collusion with those anti-China, separatist elements.\nWhoever plays with fire will get burnt. We hope certain individuals in Lithuania will heed this word of admonition and behave with ration and a clear head.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347171.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211126_10453959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-26","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","We noticed that the Chinese diplomatic representation in Lithuania is renamed the Office of the Chargé d’Affaires of the People’s Republic of China in the Republic of Lithuania. Can you share more information?","On November 18, the Lithuanian government, in disregard of China’s solemn representations, allowed the Taiwan authorities to set up the “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania”. The act openly creates the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world and sets an egregious precedent. To safeguard national sovereignty and basic norms governing international relations, the Chinese government has announced the downgrading of China-Lithuania diplomatic relations to the chargé d’affaires level. On November 26, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of China informed the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Lithuania via diplomatic note of its decision to rename China’s diplomatic representation in Lithuania the Office of the Chargé d’Affaires of the People’s Republic of China in the Republic of Lithuania as well as its demand that the Lithuanian side change the name of its diplomatic representation in China accordingly.\nI would like to point out that the step China has taken is a legitimate countermeasure to Lithuania’s decision that harms China’s sovereignty. The responsibility lies solely with the Lithuanian side. The Chinese people shall not be insulted and China’s sovereignty shall not be infringed upon. The Chinese government’s determination to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests is unwavering. No acts that challenge China’s core interests will succeed. We advise the Lithuanian side to abide by widely recognized norms governing international relations, immediately correct its mistakes and return to the right path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347171.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211126_10453959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-26","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","According to reports, Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare of Solomon Islands accused certain politicians of inciting riot in his remarks, saying he will not surrender to rioters and will never resign under pressure. He also said that the riot was encouraged by forces that wanted to thwart the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Solomon Islands. There are also comments saying that many of the…","China is closely monitoring the latest developments in Solomon Islands. We condemn the violence that has caused serious damage and property loss and support the Solomon Islands government’s efforts to end the violence and chaos. We are confident that under the leadership of Prime Minister Sogavare, the Solomon Islands government has the capability to restore social order at an early date and stabilize the domestic situation. China is taking all necessary measures to safeguard the safety and lawful rights and interests of Chinese citizens and institutions in Solomon Islands.\nIt is universal knowledge that the one-China principle is a norm governing international relations and an invincible trend with overwhelming popular support. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Solomon Islands is a correct choice in keeping with the trend of the times that can stand the test of history. Since the establishment of diplomatic ties, bilateral relations have come a long way with fruitful outcomes in practical cooperation in various sectors, receiving Solomon Islands people’s sincere support and endorsement. As facts have proven, the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Solomon Islands serves the fundamental and long-term interests of Solomon Islands. All attempts to disrupt the normal development of relations between our two sides are nothing but futile.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347171.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211126_10453959.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-11-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 26 dispatch. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a question on the 26th, said: The DPP authorities are engaging in political manipulation over the case of enterprises involved in the Far Eastern Group in Taiwan being investigated and punished in accordance with law, staging the old routine of inciting confrontation and creating hostility. This…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the violations of laws and regulations by some enterprises under Taiwan's Far Eastern Group in areas such as environmental protection, land use, occupational health of employees, work safety and fire protection, taxation, and product quality are clear in fact and conclusive in evidence, and have been publicly announced. The penalties imposed by the relevant law enforcement departments have sufficient factual and legal basis and were carried out strictly in accordance with statutory procedures. The enterprises involved have all admitted to the facts of their violations of laws and regulations, and have paid or are paying fines and taxes according to procedures. As the party concerned, the Far Eastern Group has remained silent since the incident, while some politicians on the island have ignored the above illegal facts and deliberately made irresponsible remarks. Does this have anything to do with you? I want to emphasize that we uphold the rule of law: there must be laws to follow, laws must be obeyed, law enforcement must be strict, and violations must be punished.\nShe said that what truly harms and undermines cross-strait economic and trade relations and cross-strait relations are the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities have escalated their collusion with external forces, carried out provocations to seek “independence,” raised tensions in the Taiwan Strait region, and seriously undermined the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. They have violated market rules, drastically restricted cross-strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and set many obstacles to normal cross-strait economic and trade interactions. They have repeatedly intimidated Taiwan residents and groups that participate in cross-strait exchanges, carried out a “green terror” on the island, and created a “chilling effect,” seriously affecting the normal interactions of compatriots on both sides of the strait. These aspects are truly appalling and outrageous.\nZhu Fenglian said that I must reiterate that our position of strengthening cross-strait economic exchanges and cooperation and deepening cross-strait integrated development has never changed, and our actions will never stop. Our welcome and support for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises coming to the mainland to invest, develop, and engage in exchanges and cooperation has not changed, and we will continue to protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in accordance with the law. But we will never allow affiliated companies and financial backers of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements to profit on the mainland, and we will never allow Taiwan enterprises to make money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” on the island and undermining cross-strait relations, engaging in the act of smashing their own rice bowls.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211126_12393050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, November 26 — From November 25 to 26, five U.S. federal House members flew to Taiwan aboard a U.S. military executive aircraft. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a query on the 26th, said: We firmly oppose the United States engaging in any form of official exchange or military contact with the Taiwan region of China. The visit to Taiwan by some U.S. congressmen seriously violates the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and sends a serious erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” forces. We urge some in the U.S. Congress to handle the Taiwan question prudently, to stop encouraging and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and to stop playing the “Taiwan card” and fanning the flames, otherwise they will only cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that any DPP authority scheme to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence,” or to carry out so-called “parliamentary diplomacy” to build ties and infiltrate, will not end well and is destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211126_12393087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-11-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 26 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 26th in response to a question: We warn certain members of the U.S. Congress to stop challenging the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop playing the “Taiwan card,” and stop making trouble and playing with fire on the Taiwan question. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Any act that undermines China's sovereignty and territorial integrity will be resolutely countered.\nA reporter asked: Among the U.S. federal House members who have just made a provocative visit to the Taiwan region of China, one named Meeks falsely claimed a “Republic of Taiwan.” The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have hyped this extensively. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.\nShe pointed out that the scheme of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces to collude with external forces to seek “independence” will not succeed. The higher they jump, the harder they fall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202111/t20211126_12393088.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-11-29","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","We’re wondering if there’s any more information on the timing of the opening ceremony for the Forum on China-Africa Cooperation? The second question is that Xiomara Castro has claimed victory in the Honduran presidential election after preliminary result showed her on track for a landslide win. Castro has floated the idea of switching having full official diplomatic relations with Taiwan to Beijing. Does the…","On your first question, China has released the information that President Xi Jinping is to attend the opening ceremony of the eighth Ministerial Conference of the Forum on China-Africa Cooperation (FOCAC) and deliver a keynote speech via video link. Please stay tuned.\nOn your second question, the one-China principle is a widely recognized norm governing international relations and an overwhelming consensus of the international community. Opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and adhering to the one-China principle is an overriding trend with strong popular support. The attempt to create the false impression of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” leads nowhere. We are ready to grow friendly and cooperative relations with all countries on the basis of upholding the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347172.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211129_10458501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-29","Wang Wenbin","NHK","A group of lawmakers from the three Baltic countries visited Taiwan and held talks with Tsai Ing-wen today. What is the foreign ministry’s response?","China firmly opposes any form of official and political interaction with Taiwan by any country having diplomatic ties with China. This position is consistent and clear-cut. We urge relevant parties to exercise prudence and stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. We have this stern warning to the Taiwan authorities: Attempts to engage in provocative activities to seek independence in collusion with external forces are ill-conceived and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347172.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211129_10458501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-11-29","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Taiwan announced last Friday that it will set up an office in Washington next year to handle veterans affairs. On Sunday, 27 Chinese aircraft entered Taiwan’s “Air Defense Identification Zone”, according to the “Ministry of National Defense” in Taipei. And today Tsai Ing-wen said that Lithuania is expected to open a representative office in Taiwan early next year. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on…","On your first question, the Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and bears on China’s core interests. China’s resolve to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity is rock-solid and the historical trend for China to achieve reunification is unstoppable. We advise some in the US not to play the “Taiwan card” and not to play with fire. Otherwise, they will get burnt and reap what they sow. We also have this stern warning to the Taiwan authorities that trying to solicit foreign support, relying on the US to seek independence and resisting reunification with force will prove a dead end.\nYour second question is not a diplomatic question. I would like to refer you to competent authorities.\nOn your third question, China has taken legitimate and strong countermeasures over Lithuania’s erroneous act to create the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”. China’s sovereignty shall not be infringed upon. Those who undermine China’s sovereignty will pay the price. No one should harbor any illusion about this. We once again urge the Lithuanian side to correct its mistakes with concrete actions and earnestly fulfill its political commitment on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347172.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202111/t20211129_10458501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-01","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Rights groups say Beijing has pressured foreign governments to deport Taiwanese criminal suspects to the mainland, despite a 2009 agreement that police from both sides would return overseas suspects to their respective territories. What is the reason for deporting Taiwanese fugitives to the mainland? And how will they be dealt with?","What you mentioned is completely unfounded.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347174.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211201_10460717.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-01","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","Speaking virtually at a Taiwanese think tank today, former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe said, “A Taiwan emergency is a Japanese emergency, and therefore an emergency for the Japan-US alliance.” Do you have any comment?","In total disregard of the basic norms governing international relations and the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan, former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe blatantly babbled utter nonsense and wantonly leveled criticism on the Taiwan question, and made presumptuous remarks about China’s internal affairs. China deplores and rejects this and has lodged stern representations with the Japanese side through diplomatic channels.\nTaiwan is China’s sacred territory, where no external interference shall be tolerated. During its colonial rule over Taiwan for half a century, Japan committed innumerable crimes, over which it has grave historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. No one should underestimate the strong resolve, determination and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Those who dare to pursue the old path of militarism and challenge our bottom line will find themselves on a collision course with the Chinese people!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347174.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211201_10460717.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 1 (electronic dispatch). Regarding the visit to Taiwan by a delegation of lawmakers from the three Baltic states, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 1st in response to a question: The spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated our solemn position. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region of China under any pretext. We urge the countries concerned to abide by the one-China principle and to handle the Taiwan question with prudence and properly. The DPP authorities' attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence” will not succeed, no matter what tricks they play or what schemes they resort to.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211202_12393867.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 2 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 2nd by saying that Shinzo Abe's disregard for facts and reversal of black and white, and his attempt to challenge the outcome of the world anti-fascist war and the international order established after World War II, are shocking. His rhetoric on the Taiwan question, advocating…","Ma Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, by going against the interests of the Chinese nation and the well-being of the island's people, and by colluding with external forces to pursue “independence,” are extremely dangerous. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: do not misjudge the situation. Provocations that attempt to rely on external forces to split the country and seek political gain are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211202_12394026.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-03","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","A follow-up on the US-EU Dialogue on China. The joint press release also reaffirmed the importance of diversifying supply chains and “addressing economic coercion”, and expressed strong concern over China’s “unilateral actions in the South and East China Seas and the Taiwan Strait”. Do you have any comment?","How the US and the EU develop their economic and trade relations is their own business, but they should not make an issue out of China. I would like to ask those who wantonly accuse China of economic coercion: What’s the basis for such allegations? China doesn’t bully or wantonly sanction others, wield long-arm jurisdiction or suppress foreign businesses. How can anyone accuse it of coercion? It is well known that coercion is the strong suit and distinct feature of the US. With its policies and actions, the US has provided some textbook examples of economic coercion for the world. It has long wielded the big stick of sanctions over Cuba, the DPRK, Iran and Venezuela. It wantonly starts trade wars with other countries and also suppresses foreign high-tech companies in the name of national security. I believe the European side still has vivid memories of US coercion in the cases of the French company Alstom and the Australian nuclear submarine project. China stands ready to work together with all parties to safeguard the steady and smooth operation of global industrial and supply chains.\nAs to the concern expressed by the US and the EU on the so-called “unilateral actions in the South and East China Seas and the Taiwan Strait” by China, I would like to point out that the provocative moves by the DPP authorities to seek independence by colluding with external forces are the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the root cause of the current tensions. China’s resolute response to Taiwan-independence separatist activities and external interference is absolutely necessary. The US and the EU should abide by the one-China policy, act prudently and stop sending wrong signals to Taiwan-independence forces. As to the issue concerning the East China Sea and Diaoyu Dao, it is essentially about Japan illegally coveting China’s territory and constantly provoking China on the matter of sovereignty. As to issues concerning the South China Sea, they are essentially about relevant countries’ illegal occupation of Chinese islands and reefs and external forces’ disruption. Everything China does is to safeguard its rights and is completely legitimate and lawful.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347176.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211203_10462100.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 3 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd that the 13th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian on December 10, with the main venue set in Xiamen. The forum conference will be held on the 11th, and relevant prefecture-level cities and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone will hold related activities. At present, preparations are basically complete. The forum organizing committee has invited representatives of relevant Taiwan political parties, representatives of Taiwan host organizations, and guests from all sectors, including Taiwan industry elites, heads of social organizations, representatives of the Youth League, Workers’ Federation and Women’s Federation, township and village neighborhood officials, agricultural, fishery and water conservancy sectors, and folk belief groups, to attend forum-related activities in various ways.\nMa Xiaoguang said that this forum continues the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development.” It adopts a hybrid format combining online and offline, centralized and decentralized events, and arranges 41 events across four major sections: the forum conference and youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges. In addition, 15 events will be held concurrently. Since June, more than 20 events have been successfully held, with more than 1,500 Taiwan compatriots participating, more than 100,000 Taiwan compatriots taking part in online interaction and exchanges, and related topics on the internet exceeding 20 million reads. This forum offers 1,603 positions to Taiwan youth, and multiple agreements will be signed in areas such as rural construction and creative industries, talent cultivation, entrepreneurship for Taiwan youth, and industry cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211203_12394230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-06","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","It is reported that US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said if China’s mainland “invades” Taiwan, it would be a potentially disastrous decision. In the last couple of years, China has been trying to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait by engaging in provocative military maneuvers and by trying to isolate Taiwan in the international community. The US is resolutely committed to “making sure Taiwan has…","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. The remarks by relevant officials in the US flagrantly challenge the one-China principle, violate the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués and US commitment, and send a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this.\nThe real status quo on the Taiwan question is: there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The root cause of the tensions across the Taiwan Strait is the attempts by the “Taiwan independence” forces to look for US and other foreign support to seek independence. The crux of the escalated tensions is the moves of some Americans to use Taiwan to contain China by condoning and supporting the DPP authorities in changing the status quo. The collusion of these people in the US and Taiwan in making provocations and playing with fire is extremely dangerous.\nThe US must understand that the historical and legal fact of one-China is not to be challenged, the fact that both sides on the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China is not to be changed, and the process of the 1.4 billion Chinese people to advance China’s peaceful reunification is not to be held back. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. That said, should the separatist forces for Taiwan independence provoke us, force our hands or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures. Efforts to support and embolden the “Taiwan independence” forces and challenge the one-China principle will turn out to be like trying to hold back the tide with a broom. They will not stop the progress of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347177.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211206_10463052.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-06","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","According to reports, on December 3 China lodged solemn representations with Japan over former Prime Minister Shinzo Abe’s remarks that “A Taiwan emergency is a Japanese emergency”. Abe said in response that he felt honored to gain China’s attention in the capacity of a lawmaker. On the same day, Japan’s Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi said it is necessary for China to understand such thinking in Japan. What is…","Certain Japanese politicians’ taking pride in instead of feeling ashamed for their erroneous deeds and words once again reveals their problematic sense of right and wrong.\nI want to point out that there is indeed much thinking going on in Japan. To name a few, some people want to deny and even whitewash the history of aggression and colonial rule. Some try to discharge the nuclear contaminated water into the sea in disregard of the safety of global marine environment and humanity’s life and health while shirking responsibilities. Some even try to interfere in China’s internal affairs on the Taiwan question. Some thinking does exist, but that doesn’t mean it is right. The wrong perceptions are merely wishful thinking of some individuals in Japan, which will never be recognized by the Asian neighbors and the international community.\nI would like to stress that the Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests, the political foundation of China-Japan relations and the fundamental trust and faith between the two countries. The Japanese side should honor its commitments, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop provoking the one-China principle and stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347177.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211206_10463052.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 6 — U.S. Secretary of State Blinken and Secretary of Defense Austin recently made erroneous remarks on Taiwan, including openly calling the Taiwan region of China a “country” and claiming that the United States has committed to “ensuring Taiwan has the capability to defend itself.” In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, pointed out on the 6th that some people in the U.S. government have recently made erroneous remarks on Taiwan again and again, revealing that the U.S. government stubbornly holds to wrong positions on the Taiwan question and continues to play the “Taiwan card.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is entirely China's own affair and does not tolerate any external interference. Playing with fire on the Taiwan question is very dangerous. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and not cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces that any act of colluding with external forces to advance “Taiwan independence” and provoke confrontation will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211206_12394580.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-07","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","Japan staged a surprise attack on Pearl Harbour 80 years ago today, which triggered the Pacific War. Do you have anything to say on this occasion?","Today is a commemorative day of the surprise Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor during WWII and the outbreak of the Pacific War. The war of aggression launched by Japanese militarism has inflicted untold sufferings on the people of regional countries, especially the victimized countries in Asia, and left them with indelible painful memories. Over the past decades, the international community has been watching whether Japan will show a sincere and correct understanding of that history. Several decades on, Japan still owes an explicit explanation to its Asian neighbors, including China. Several decades on, some in Japan are still denying and even beautifying the history of aggression and colonial rule. Recently, certain Japanese politician went so far as to claim that “a Taiwan emergency is a Japanese emergency”. Today, nearly a hundred Japanese lawmakers paid a high-profile visit to the Yasukuni Shrine, where convicted WWII Class-A war criminals are honored. Rather than learning historical lessons, they only seek to revive the specter of militarism.\nHistory cannot be denied and travesty of justice cannot be tolerated. China firmly opposes any wrong act to backpedal, defends international fairness and justice, safeguards world peace and stability, and upholds the UN-centered international system and the international order based on international law. The Japanese side should adopt a right attitude, deeply reflect upon the Japanese militarism’ Fascist atrocities and crimes against humanity and win trust from people around the world with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347178.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211207_10463549.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-07","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","On December 6, the parliament of Solomon Islands rejected a no-confidence motion on Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare with 32 votes to 15. Do you have any comment?","China noted the relevant situation. We believe that under the leadership of Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare, the situation in the nation’s capital city will become stable at an early date. We also noticed that Prime Minister Sogavare said in a parliament speech that as stated in the UNGA Resolution 2758, the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing the whole of China and Taiwan has no status as a country. The establishment of diplomatic relations with China in 2019 is a right decision made by the government of Solomon Islands on behalf of its people and Solomon Islands is very proud to be the 179th country to have diplomatic ties with China. He reaffirmed the government’s firm commitment to the one-China principle, which is a position that no one can change. He said the establishment of diplomatic ties with China is based on Solomon Islands’ national interest and development needs and China will bring important opportunities for Solomon Islands’ development. China appreciates this.\nFacts have proven once again that the one-China principle is an overriding trend of the times with popular support, a widely recognized norm governing international relations and the common consensus of the international community. Any attempt to violate the one-China principle and undermine China-Solomon Islands relations will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347178.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211207_10463549.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-07","Zhao Lijian","AFP","I have a question on Taiwan. The deputy economic minister of Slovakia is visiting Taiwan with a delegation. He said that his country supports Taiwan and he is ready to enhance closer economic and trade relations with the island. Do you have any comment?","Slovakia insisted on sending officials to visit Taiwan, which has obviously violated the one-China principle, emboldened the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and seriously undermined the political trust between China and Slovakia. China firmly opposes and deplores this. Slovakia should abide by its commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People’s Republic of China, stop all forms of official interactions with the Taiwan authorities, stop endorsing the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and avoid further hurting China-Slovakia relations. We also have this stern warning for the Taiwan authorities: All attempts to seek independence under any pretext and in any form are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347178.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211207_10463549.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 7: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on December 7, stating that on November 23, 2021, Taiwan media reported that a man surnamed Huang had shot and killed someone with a gun, then boarded Xiamen Airlines flight MF888 on the 22nd and arrived in Xiamen, where he underwent epidemic prevention centralized quarantine. After learning of this, the Xiamen public security authorities immediately launched an investigation. After interrogation, the suspect surnamed Huang confessed to having shot and killed a man surnamed He in New Taipei City. To combat violent crime, protect the lives and property of people on both sides of the Strait, and maintain order in cross-Strait exchanges, the Xiamen public security authorities decided to repatriate the suspect surnamed Huang to Taiwan.\nA reporter asked that on November 22, a Taiwan shooting suspect fled to Xiamen and was about to be released from epidemic prevention quarantine, and asked how the mainland side would handle it. Ma Xiaoguang made the above statement in response to the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211207_12394669.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, December 7 (Xinhua). Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 7th by saying: Expanding exchanges and cooperation and deepening integrated development is what compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait desire, and it is the broad road for the development of cross-Strait relations. We advise the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that, in the face of the historical trend of strengthened exchanges and cooperation among all sectors on both sides of the Strait, their “green terror,” which is outwardly fierce but inwardly timid, should come to an end!\nA reporter asked: The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has twice recently made statements prohibiting relevant personnel in Taiwan from participating in the Straits Forum and intimidating Taiwan compatriots from taking part. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in answering the question.\nHe pointed out that it is not the first time that the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has openly issued threats and intimidation against all sectors of Taiwan's participation in the Straits Forum. It is also nothing new for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to interfere with and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges for political purposes. In recent days, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, on the one hand, have claimed they will evaluate resuming cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, while on the other hand they have continuously made statements obstructing Taiwan residents from participating in the Straits Forum, further exposing their true face of undermining cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and restricting the freedom of Taiwan residents. Facts have proven that intimidation and suppression are futile. Since its founding in 2009, the Straits Forum has been warmly welcomed by people on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, and more than 100,000 Taiwan compatriots have participated in total.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211207_12394787.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-08","Wang Wenbin","Sputnik","US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said after the meeting between President Putin and President Biden on December 7 that the US is going to take every action to make sure that Taiwan is not reunified by force and to deter the invasion into Ukraine by Russia. What is your comment on this? And what is your comment on the Russia-US summit?","As for the Russia-US summit, we believe that as permanent members of the UN Security Council and major countries with important international influence, both Russia and the US shoulder important responsibilities for international peace and security. China is glad to see them engage in communication and dialogue to improve their relations, which is conducive to world peace and development and the international community’s joint efforts to address common challenges.\nAs to the Taiwan-related remarks by Mr. Sullivan you mentioned, the US statement once again proved the allegation that the Indo-Pacific strategy does not target any third party is nothing but a disguise. On the Taiwan question, the US has been saying and doing wrong things and emboldening the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China is firmly opposed to this.\nThe root cause of the current tension in cross-Strait relations lies in the DPP authorities’ repeated attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence”. This also has to do with some people in the US, who seek to use Taiwan to contain China. We are ready to make every effort with the utmost sincerity to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. But it is absolutely necessary for China to resolutely respond to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, and safeguard its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. No one should entertain any illusion about this. The sequence and causal relations here are crystal clear, and the US should not distort facts. We urge the US side to fully recognize the highly-sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, and strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués. It should handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop all official and military ties with Taiwan, refrain from sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and avoid seriously undermining China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. I need to stress that China’s reunification is an unstoppable historical trend that will not be changed by anyone, any force or any country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347179.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211208_10464195.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 8 dateline: Recently, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit closed in Nanjing. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan falsely claimed that the mainland created obstacles to normal cross-Strait exchange activities, and distorted the mainland's measures to punish diehard “Taiwan independence” elements as interfering with Taiwanese businesses' operations and creating a “chilling effect.” In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 8th in response to a question that the DPP authorities' attempts to sow discord are doomed to be a waste of effort.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the 2021 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit was held simultaneously via video link in Nanjing and Taipei on the 7th. More than 500 business figures from both sides of the Strait attended the forum and discussed the overall picture of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. At a time when the development of cross-Strait relations is under impact, and under the DPP authorities' relentless obstruction and intimidation, business people from both sides have demonstrated through their actions that strengthening economic cooperation is the will of the people and the trend of the times, and an inevitable choice for mutual benefit and win-win results across the Strait.\nHe pointed out that “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and the greatest obstacle to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Cracking down on diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their affiliated enterprises and financial backers according to law aims precisely to curb “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Fundamentally, this will help promote normal cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and help safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Only by firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism can Taiwanese businesses investing and setting up operations in the mainland have a secure and stable environment, and only then can cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation have the guarantee of peace and stability. The DPP authorities have long obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and arbitrarily suppressed groups and individuals who oppose “Taiwan independence” and advocate reunification. They have deliberately engaged in political manipulation and stirred up a “green terror,” as the whole world knows. No matter how the DPP authorities distort facts and reverse black and white, they cannot conceal their true colors of colluding with the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the mainland has always been a fertile ground for Taiwanese businesses to invest and set up operations, and a reliance for development and progress. We welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises to invest and develop in the mainland, and we will continue to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises in accordance with law. Our consistently upheld concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family” will not change. The policy of taking the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots will not change. The measures to do practical good deeds for Taiwanese businesses will not change. The DPP authorities' attempts to sow discord are doomed to be a waste of effort. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwanese businesses will discern right from wrong, stand firm in their position, draw clear lines with the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and participate in cross-Strait economic cooperation through practical action, advancing the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211208_12395032.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-09","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Reuters reported that China has told companies to cut ties with Lithuania or face being shut out of its market. Lithuania’s Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs said China has been sending messages to multinationals that if they use parts and supplies from Lithuania they won’t be allowed to sell in its market. A Lithuanian industry body also confirmed this to Reuters. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","I am not aware of the specific situation you mentioned. I want to stress that China always acts in a way that conforms to WTO rules. Lithuania acted in bad faith, renounced the political commitment it has made to China upon the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People’s Republic of China, and openly created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. Such egregious act seriously undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and created a vile precedent in the world. We will resolutely uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity and defend our core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347180.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211209_10465049.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 9 (Dispatch). U.S. National Security Advisor Sullivan, when answering reporters' questions on December 7, said that the United States will take action to ensure that a situation of forcibly unifying Taiwan does not happen. The DPP authorities expressed gratitude to the diplomatic departments. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 9th when asked: We urge the U.S. side to act in practice in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We warn certain people: do not play with fire, for those who play with fire will burn themselves.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Taiwan is part of China. Achieving the complete unification of China is the common wish of all Chinese descendants. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and force the issue, or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.\nHe said that at present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait continues to be tense and turbulent. The fundamental cause is that the DPP authorities have repeatedly attempted to “seek independence by relying on the U.S.,” while some people in the U.S. deliberately pursue “using Taiwan to contain China.” Some people in the U.S., disregarding facts and reversing right and wrong, have repeatedly made erroneous remarks and taken erroneous actions on the Taiwan question. Fundamentally, they intend to play the “Taiwan card,” treating Taiwan as a pawn, and obstructing the process of China's unification and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The Taiwan question is entirely China's own affair, and it tolerates no external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211209_12395271.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-10","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","This morning, China and Nicaragua resumed diplomatic relations. What is the significance of the resumption of diplomatic ties under the current circumstances?","This morning, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi held a virtual meeting with Nicaragua’s Foreign Minister Denis Moncada and met with a government delegation of Nicaragua visiting China via video link. The two sides officially confirmed all the contents in the Joint Communiqué on the resumption of diplomatic relations between China and Nicaragua. China welcomes the Nicaraguan government’s political decision to sever “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan and resume diplomatic ties with the People’s Republic of China. Nicaragua has thus become the 181st country to have normal diplomatic relations with China.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang stressed that the one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community and a universally-agreed norm governing international relations. Nicaragua has made an important decision to resume and develop normal relations with China, thus choosing to stand on the right side of history with the overwhelming majority of countries in the world. The resumption of diplomatic ties is fully in keeping with the fundamental and long-term interests of the two countries and is sure to be welcomed and supported by the two peoples. China and Nicaragua shall cement the one-China principle, the political foundation of bilateral relations, work together to chart the course of development of bilateral ties, and steadily advance exchanges and cooperation in various fields that will bring benefits to both countries and peoples.\nThe Nicaraguan side noted that exchanges between the two countries date back a long time. The two governing parties and two countries share revolutionary friendship and brotherly bonds. The resumption of diplomatic ties is supported by the entire Nicaraguan population. With profound sincerity in resuming diplomatic relations, Nicaragua will fully honor its commitments, firmly uphold the one-China principle, and support all the endeavors and actions of China for its complete reunification.\nBefore the meeting, Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu held talks with Laureano Ortega, the representative of the Nicaraguan government. They signed the Joint Communiqué on the Resumption of Diplomatic Relations Between the People’s Republic of China and the Republic of Nicaragua.\nNicaragua has resumed diplomatic ties with China without preconditions and stands on the right side of history. We highly appreciate that. Nicaragua is an important country in Central America. The resumption of diplomatic ties between China and Nicaragua opens a new chapter of friendly cooperation between the two countries in various fields on the basis of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit. We believe the development of bilateral relations will surely benefit the two countries and two peoples. China will continue to develop friendly relations and cooperation with other countries on the basis of the one-China principle.\nThe resumption of diplomatic ties between China and Nicaragua once again indicates that the one-China principle is a universally-agreed norm governing international relations and the general consensus of the international community. Upholding the one-China principle is in line with global justice. No force can stand in the way of the shared aspiration of the people and the general trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347181.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211210_10466651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-10","Wang Wenbin","RTHK","Some countries still remain the so-called “diplomatic allies” of Taiwan. How do you comment on that?","I just made clear China’s position on the resumption of diplomatic ties with Nicaragua. I want to stress one more point. Taiwan is a part of China. This is a clear and simple fact that can be easily understood. There are still a few countries in the world that maintain “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan. The reason behind this is that the Taiwan authorities engaged in “dollar diplomacy” in negligence of the well-being of the people in Taiwan. It is also due to various sorts of pressure imposed by the US on these countries. Sooner or later, these countries will establish or resume normal diplomatic relations with China in accordance with the spirit of Resolution 2758 adopted by the United Nations General Assembly 50 years ago. It is just a matter of time because this is an unstoppable trend of the times.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347181.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211210_10466651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-10","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The Biden administration aims to sign what it describes as a very powerful economic framework agreement with Asian nations next year, according to Commerce Secretary Gina Raimondo. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this economic deal?","The formation and development of global industrial and supply chains is the result of market rules and choices of businesses. As an economy with the greatest dynamism and potential, China has been actively maintaining the stability of global industrial and supply chains, and unswervingly building an open world economy.\nThe US repeatedly abuses state power to politicize and instrumentalize science and technology and economic and trade issues based on ideology. It has also intentionally put in place trade and investment barriers against specific countries. Such moves have undermined international trade rules and divided the global market.\nThe US forced the Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co (TSMC), Samsung and other companies to provide chip supply chain data to the US. Is this also part of the framework you mentioned? In a world where the global economy is deeply integrated, the US moves to undermine the stability of global industrial and supply chains are against the trend. They are unpopular and will inevitably end up harming the US itself. We urge the US to adopt a correct attitude, follow the trend of the times, discard the zero-sum mentality, earnestly safeguard a fair, just and non-discriminatory market environment, and stop doing things that undermine world economic recovery and growth.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347181.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211210_10466651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 10 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 10th that the so-called \"democracy\" of the United States is widely questioned both in the international community and within the United States. The United States holding the so-called \"Summit for Democracy\" is in fact a political manipulation to safeguard US interests and…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out: We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and Taiwan, China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. Any scheme by the DPP authorities to “rely on the US to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211210_12395436.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 10 dispatch. On December 10, China and Nicaragua restored ambassador-level diplomatic relations. TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said in response to a question that Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. We appreciate the relevant countries for following the trend and supporting China’s cause of unification, and we welcome the few remaining so-called “diplomatic allies” of Taiwan to recognize the trend and stand on the right side of history as soon as possible.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that history and reality have once again shown that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and no person or force can stop the historical trend of the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211210_12395467.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-13","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","On December 12, Elizabeth Truss, the UK’s Secretary of State for Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Affairs, issued a statement in her capacity as Chair of the G7 Foreign and Development Ministers’ Meeting. The Chair’s Statement said that on China, they “discussed a range of issues and challenges, such as the situations in Hong Kong and Xinjiang, in the East and South China Seas and the importance of peace and…","China’s positions on issues relating to Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Taiwan as well as maritime issues are consistent and clear. We firmly oppose the G7’s attempt to interfere in China’s domestic affairs, smear China’s image, and harm China’s interests.\nThe US and the UK are the world’s most advanced economies with cutting-edge medical technology. And yet, with a combined population accounting for 5% of the world’s total, they registered 23% of all COVID-19 cases and 18% of fatalities. We urge them to strive to protect their people’s right to life and health and prevent further loss of lives to the pandemic instead of selling hollow rhetoric about democracy and human rights around the world.\nWe urge the US, the UK and others to stop adopting coercive means such as arbitrary detention of foreign citizens, wanton suppression of certain companies, and flagrant illegal unilateral sanctions, work to foster an open, inclusive, transparent and non-discriminatory international trade and investment environment, and respect other countries’ legitimate development rights and interests.\nWe urge the US, the UK and others to discard the Cold War mentality, stop drawing ideological lines, practice true multilateralism, and contribute to safeguarding international solidarity and jointly addressing global challenges instead of dividing the world and setting up barriers to thwart concerted efforts to confront problems faced by humankind.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347182.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211213_10467487.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-15","Zhao Lijian","China Review News","According to reports, French lawmakers including François de Rugy, the head of the Taiwan Friendship group in the National Assembly, the lower house of France’s parliament, arrived in Taiwan for a “visit” on December 15. Do you have any comment?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We firmly oppose any form of official or political interaction between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic relations with China. The relevant side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and safeguard the sound and steady development of bilateral relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347184.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211215_10470135.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-15","Zhao Lijian","Radio Television Hong Kong","The head of Taiwan’s so-called foreign affairs department Joseph Wu said that China’s mainland approached Nicaragua, a country that had “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan, when the US was busy hosting the “Summit for Democracy”. Do you have any comment?","I noted the ridiculous remarks by the certain “Taiwan independence” individual. He said so to cover up the failure in separatist activities. The DPP authorities’ participation in the “Summit for Democracy” cannot cover up the true intention of seeking independence by using democracy as a pretext.\nFollowing the one-China principle is an unstoppable and overriding trend with popular support. Attempts by the DPP authorities to deny the one-China principle are self-deceiving and rejecting the one-China principle leads no where.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347184.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211215_10470135.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on December 15, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Welcome to the TAO press conference.\nIn less than two months, the Olympic flame will be lit again in Beijing, the city that has hosted both the Summer and Winter Olympics, drawing worldwide attention and anticipation. As you have noticed, we just played on a loop in the briefing hall “Together Toward the Future,” the promotional song for the theme slogan of the 2022 Winter Olympics and Winter Paralympics. What is different is that this version was recorded by Taiwan compatriots in Beijing, organized by the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office. They used this special way to express their anticipation of the Beijing Winter Olympics and their beautiful vision of moving toward the future together. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to take part in activities related to the Beijing Winter Olympics, and we hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will meet in Beijing and share the passion and joy of the Winter Olympics. Now, I will take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Director Wang Yang attended the 13th Straits Forum in Xiamen on the 11th and delivered a speech, which has drawn attention from all sectors on the island. Please interpret the meaning of the speech.","On December 11, Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the 13th Straits Forum in Xiamen and delivered a speech. Chairman Wang Yang's speech expressed our firm confidence in advancing the reunification of the motherland, our resolute determination to oppose “Taiwan independence” and external interference, and our unchanging original aspiration to bring well-being to compatriots.\nFirst, resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is a historic task to which the Communist Party of China is unwaveringly committed, and we are confident of success. Our confidence comes from the power of justice, the power of the people, and the power of culture. The Chinese people inwardly support reunification, earnestly look forward to it, and firmly defend it. This is our greatest source of strength.\nSecond, the Chinese nation is a peace-loving nation, but its will to defend the country and oppose separatism is as firm as a rock. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will never leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. No one should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThird, peace, development, and a good life are the common aspirations of Taiwan compatriots. We are capable of enabling Taiwan compatriots to live better lives. We will fully implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, improve the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland, and encourage Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams.\nChairman Wang Yang's speech has drawn wide attention and positive appraisal, and has had a major impact on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will seize the moment and the trend, recognize what is beneficial and what is harmful, distinguish right from wrong, firmly stand on the right side of history, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely draw a clear line with the forces of “Taiwan independence,” and be upright and proud Chinese. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should unite in common cause, work together, and strive together for the lofty cause of completing the reunification of the motherland and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396448.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Reports say that the 13th Straits Forum adopted a combination of online and offline formats and is the largest cross-Strait civil exchange activity this year. Please introduce the achievements of this forum.","The activities of the 13th Straits Forum were successfully held on December 11. According to incomplete statistics, more than 9,600 people took part online and offline, including about 4,600 guests from Taiwan. The main achievements are reflected in the following aspects.\nFirst, the forum demonstrated the strong public support for cross-Strait exchanges. Despite the adverse impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and man-made obstruction on the island, the forum was still grandly held, and compatriots from Taiwan in all walks of life actively participated in various forms. Chinese Kuomintang Chairman Eric Chu delivered a video speech at the main forum session, and Vice Chairman Xia Liyan delivered a speech via live link at the Straits Youth Forum. New Party Chairman Wu Cheng-tien and more than 100 other Taiwan guests traveled specially from the island to attend the main forum. The enthusiastic participation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait in this forum once again eloquently demonstrates that the trend of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is irresistible, and compatriots' wish to draw closer to and visit one another cannot be denied.\nSecond, the forum promoted fruitful civil cooperation. During the forum, a batch of cross-Strait investment, trade, industry cooperation and grassroots exchange agreements were signed. For example, at the “Straits Financial Forum · Taiwanese Enterprise Development Summit,” the All-China Federation of Taiwanese Enterprises signed a strategic cooperation agreement with Jinyuan Group. The Mazu Culture Week innovatively integrated economic and trade cooperation topics, signing 15 projects with a planned investment of 3.73 billion yuan. The Straits Science and Technology Expert Forum shared more than 400 technical papers and facilitated 9 project collaborations with a total value of more than 30 million yuan. The Straits Women's Forum facilitated paired signings between female science and technology commissioners and representatives from Taiwan's science and technology sector, and conferred the title for the establishment of the Cross-Strait Women's Human Resources Service Industrial Park. The Cross-Strait Characteristic Towns Exchange and Matchmaking cum Rural Industry Integration Development Forum facilitated 10 pairs of Fujian-Taiwan agricultural enterprises signing cooperation and exchange agreements. Cross-Strait community exchange activities reached 6 project cooperation agreements.\nThird, practical measures helped Cross-Strait youth grow and develop. This forum focused on youth needs and served youth development, actively responding to the strong desire of Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to participate in exchanges and pursue careers. Xiamen will introduce new policy measures to deepen Xiamen-Taiwan youth exchange and integration. Fuzhou City launched the first batch of 550 public rental housing units for Taiwan compatriots who are employed or starting businesses locally. The “Taiwan Talent Southwest Fujian (Xiamen) Matchmaking Meeting” offered 1,603 job positions for Taiwan youth. The Straits Youth Forum selected 10 outstanding Taiwan youth entrepreneurship projects and included them in Fujian's “101 Taiwan Youth Entrepreneurship Support Program.” The Straits Women's Forum awarded gold prizes to 10 outstanding projects from the Cross-Strait College Students' Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition. The 3rd Creative Graffiti Awards selected 5 works from nearly 100 original design submissions to be painted on the wall, and held the unveiling ceremony of a Taiwan youth live-streaming base at the same time. The Common Home Forum held the first Taiwan Goods Shopping Festival, providing a platform for cross-Strait youth e-commerce entrepreneurship. The Straits Film and Television Season announced the results of the selection of film and television works most popular among cross-Strait youth and officially launched them for online streaming.\nFourth, cross-Strait “cloud” exchanges were advanced in depth.新媒体 was widely used to move a series of forum activities from offline to the “cloud,” breaking through pandemic barriers and allowing more compatriots on both sides of the Strait to participate in exchanges and interaction. Performances of cross-Strait traditional crafts (intangible cultural heritage projects) were connected live with Kinmen via the “cloud” to discuss the inheritance and development of outstanding traditional Chinese culture. The Cross-Strait Good Trend Set and the “Cross-Strait Families Are One: Hearts Connected from Childhood” study camp attracted 100,000 Taiwan compatriots to participate online. The “Mazu Cup” Straits Cross-Strait Online Marathon attracted more than 22,800 Taiwan compatriots to sign up to compete. The Straits Cross-Strait Industry and Commerce Cooperation Forum attracted 12,100 people to attend online. More than 1,500 cross-Strait nursing experts and representatives gathered online at the “Straits Nursing Summit Forum” to explore mechanisms for coordinated development of nursing across the Strait. The Straits Science and Technology Expert Forum attracted more than 300 experts, scholars and business representatives from both sides of the Strait to discuss the integration of science and technology across the Strait online. The Straits Cross-Strait Shipbuilding Culture Seminar simultaneously launched the “Chuanzheng in the Cloud” big data resource database for shipbuilding research.\nThis forum has been widely covered by media on both sides of the Strait. Taking the mainland as an example alone, according to incomplete statistics, as of now, there have been more than 2,700 reports from central media outlets. In terms of online media, the topic of the Straits Forum on Toutiao has been read 190 million times, on Douyin 320 million times, and on Sina Weibo 270 million times. Public attention is still rising steadily.\nThe activities of this Straits Forum have now concluded successfully. Here, on behalf of the 84 host units of this forum, we extend our heartfelt thanks to all sectors of society and media friends on both sides of the Strait for their strong support. We hope everyone will continue to support civil exchanges across the Strait, so that the path of integrated development across the Strait becomes broader and wider.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396447.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The so-called “four referendums” are about to be held on the island. The DPP authorities and Tsai Ing-wen and others claimed, “If the import of American pork does not pass, Taiwan’s economy will return to the predicament of being locked in by China,” and said that the so-called “four disagrees” means “disagreeing with China annexing Taiwan.” What is the comment on this?","These politicians are once again switching concepts. Pork from pigs containing ractopamine is not the same as all American pork. The former is harmful to human health, which is why the mainland does not import it. Why would Taiwan import it? Taiwan has always been part of China. How can there be talk of “annexation”? By manipulating facts in this way, they insult the intelligence of the Taiwan public. How shameless!\nRecently, the DPP authorities, for their own private interests, have once again used their customary tricks to politically manipulate the “four referendums.” On the one hand, they collude with pro-Taiwan politicians from the United States, Japan, and other countries to intimidate the Taiwan public. On the other hand, they deliberately provoke the mainland, using this to stir up “anti-China” populism and conceal their essence: damaging the interests of the Taiwan public and willingly allowing foreign forces to take whatever they want. Compatriots in Taiwan should keep their eyes open and not be deceived by this political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Tang Feng, the representative sent by the DPP authorities, recently peddled Taiwan's so-called “democratic achievements” at the so-called “Summit for Democracy” in the United States. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Here we must ask the DPP authorities: for the sake of their own party's interests, they suppress dissidents on the island, manipulate ethnic antagonism, and divide Taiwan's society. What kind of democracy is this? During elections they use fancy words and make empty promises, and after the election they cast aside their commitments to the people on the island. What kind of democracy is this? They engage heavily in power-for-money deals and black-gold politics, accept illegal political donations, carry out illegal lobbying, and pursue personal and party self-interest. What kind of democracy is this? They muzzle public opinion, create a “chilling effect,” and disregard public outrage by shutting down the CTi channel. What kind of democracy is this? They abuse administrative and judicial resources, engage in “green terror,” and suppress political parties, groups and individuals who advocate cross-Strait exchanges and support reunification, depriving Taiwan residents of their legitimate right to engage in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. What kind of democracy is this? To collude with and cling to hostile anti-China forces abroad in pursuit of “independence,” they are willing to harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots, even at the cost of the health and well-being of people on the island, “exhausting Taiwan's resources to win the favor of foreign countries.” What kind of democracy is this? Disregarding the interests of Taiwan enterprises and the economic future of Taiwan, they are willing to kowtow to external anti-China forces on supply chain issues, harming enterprise interests. What kind of democracy is this? Like Goebbels, they treat lies as truth, constantly spread false information that attacks and smears the mainland, manipulate populism, stage a self-written and self-directed “cognitive warfare” farce, and incite confrontation between the two sides of the Strait. What kind of democracy is this? They hype up the so-called “military threat” from the mainland, use the hard-earned money of the people to buy weapons from foreign masters, and do not hesitate to tie the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and push them toward disaster. What kind of democracy is this? Openly and covertly meddling in Hong Kong affairs by every means, peddling the so-called “Hong Kong Support Plan” and posing as “defenders of democracy,” even the island's own media say that the DPP authorities are feasting on Hong Kong's “mantou dipped in human blood” to win votes. What kind of democracy is this?\nThe DPP authorities sending people to attend this event is itself a great joke, once again exposing the essence of their false “democracy” and real pursuit of “independence,” and merely adding a bit of comic relief to the so-called “Summit for Democracy” cobbled together for the United States.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396446.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, the Taiwan military and certain individuals on the island have repeatedly played up the so-called “mainland threat,” and have also aggressively hyped the so-called steps of the mainland “attacking Taiwan.” What is your comment?","As is well known, the root cause of the current tension in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces colluding with external forces to continuously pursue “independence” and provoke. Recently, the DPP authorities and some people on the island have joined foreign anti-China forces in deliberately spreading so-called “attack on Taiwan” rhetoric about the mainland and hyping a so-called “military threat” from the mainland to Taiwan, with sinister intent. First, they attempt to distort right and wrong and whitewash the image of the “troublemaker,” continuing provocations to pursue “independence.” Second, they attempt to divert attention, incite island populism, coerce island public opinion, create “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, and reap political self-interest. Third, they attempt to rely on foreigners to enhance their own standing, creating a pretext for foreign forces to interfere in the situation in the Taiwan Strait. Compatriots in Taiwan should remain highly vigilant against this.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: relying on fabricating rumors to create trouble cannot conceal that it is they who are the real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If they misjudge the situation and dare to take a desperate gamble, they will surely face a catastrophe that will be their undoing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396444.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Some U.S. lawmakers recently introduced the so-called “Taiwan Preclearance Act,” advocating the establishment of “preclearance” checkpoints at airports on the island, where U.S. law enforcement officers would go to carry out enforcement. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, out of political self-interest, have simply not taken the rights and dignity of the Taiwan people into account. As long as they can curry favor with and cling to external forces to help them seek “independence,” they are capable of doing anything. We believe more and more Taiwan compatriots will see through this. As for certain members of the U.S. Congress drafting relevant bills to push this matter, this further proves that those anti-China lawmakers’ aims and schemes serve U.S. interests, not Taiwan’s interests. We urge certain people on the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop playing the “Taiwan card” and “using Taiwan to contain China,” and stop playing with fire on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396443.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Hsu Hsu-tung, chairman of Taiwan's Far Eastern Group, recently wrote in a Taiwan newspaper, expressing opposition to “Taiwan independence,” support for the “1992 Consensus,” and support for the one-China principle. This is the first statement from the Far Eastern Group since its mainland-subsidiary enterprises were investigated and penalized in accordance with the law. What comments do you have on this?","We have noted relevant reports. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. It will only bring disaster to Taiwan and seriously harm the fundamental interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, including the business community. It will never succeed. We hope that relevant Taiwan enterprises and their responsible persons will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” stand on the right side of history, draw a clear line with “Taiwan independence” forces through practical actions, and do more to maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nI wish to reiterate that our attitude of welcoming and supporting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest, develop, and engage in exchanges and cooperation on the mainland has not changed. We are willing to share mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises first, provide them with more equal treatment, continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and benefit compatriots on both sides more. At the same time, we will absolutely not allow affiliated enterprises and financial backers of diehard “Taiwan independence” figures to profit on the mainland, and we will not allow Taiwan enterprises to earn money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” on the island and undermining cross-Strait relations, which would be destroying the rice bowl that feeds them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211215_12396445.htm"],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Slovak Deputy Minister of Economy Galek, Director-General of the Economic Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs Kiss and others recently intruded into Taiwan. Slovakia and Taiwan signed nine cooperation documents, including the “Declaration on the Outcomes of the Economic Cooperation Consultation Meeting,” covering economy and trade, education, outer space and other areas. It is reported that Slovakia and…","Certain Slovak government officials slipped into Taiwan and conducted official contact with the DPP authorities. This seriously violates the one-China principle, sends a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces, and runs counter to the 1.4 billion Chinese people’s cause of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity and advancing the process of national reunification. No pretext can conceal the essence of the Slovak government’s above conduct, which encourages the arrogance of “Taiwan independence.” We urge the relevant national governments to stop erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues and return to the right path of adhering to the one-China principle and properly handling Taiwan-related issues. The DPP authorities’ scheme to collude with external forces to seek “independence” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声电台记者","Taiwan media reported that Wang Chin-chuan, a Taiwanese businessman, claimed that his factory in Xinjiang was demolished without warning by the local government. The Mainland Affairs Council said that if cross-Strait agreements are involved, it will assist Taiwanese businesses through the agreement liaison channels. May I ask whether the spokesperson is aware of the relevant situation?","The mainland has always attached great importance to protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in accordance with law and regulations. After verification, the situation described by Wang Jinquan does not match the facts. First, in March 1998, mainland resident Shang Xiaomei used the land she applied for in Karamay, Xinjiang, not for planting or breeding as agreed, but in violation of regulations for leasing and operating construction sites, which posed serious safety and fire hazards. Second, the required lawful land approval procedures were not completed. Third, in September 2018, after Shang Xiaomei registered her marriage with Taiwan resident Wang Jinquan, she continued to use the land in violation of regulations. In order to eliminate safety and fire hazards, the competent authorities, after multiple unsuccessful attempts to communicate with Shang, demolished the illegal structures in accordance with law and regulations. We hope the parties concerned will actively cooperate with local governments to properly handle all follow-up matters in accordance with law and regulations, and jointly safeguard the lawful rights and interests of all parties involved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","On December 14, the Supreme People's Court released “Ten Typical Cases of People's Courts Protecting the Rights and Interests of Taiwan Compatriots.” Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","On December 14, the Supreme People's Court released the \"Ten Typical Cases of People's Courts Protecting the Rights and Interests of Taiwan Compatriots.\" The cases were selected from representative examples in recent years of measures taken by people's courts at all levels to implement in detail and carry out judicial services for deepening cross-Strait integrated development and to effectively protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, providing concrete guidance for people's courts handling Taiwan-related cases. These cases reflect three characteristics of how people's courts handle Taiwan-related cases.\nFirst, strengthening comprehensive and equal protection. Courts in Zhejiang, Anhui, Fujian, Henan, Guangxi, Sichuan, and other places have promptly issued specific work opinions or implementing rules to protect the equal litigation rights of Taiwan compatriots, and promptly provide judicial relief for disputes that arise when Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal treatment with mainland residents in various policy preferences, subsidies, awards, incentives, and market access on the mainland. Second, making efforts to optimize the business environment. Courts in Liaoning, Heilongjiang, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Fujian, Shandong, Guangdong, Guangxi, and other places with many Taiwan-related cases have all set up specialized Taiwan-related adjudication bodies to lawfully protect the security of Taiwan compatriots' investments and property on the mainland. Third, adhering to providing high-quality litigation services. Eighteen local courts in Beijing, Tianjin, Fujian, and other places have established mechanisms with local Taiwan Affairs Offices for the coordinated resolution of Taiwan-related disputes, fully leveraging the role of non-litigation dispute resolution mechanisms such as mediation. Seven local courts in Liaoning, Jiangsu, Fujian, and other places have explored having Taiwan compatriots serve as people's assessors, specially invited mediators, and consultant experts to participate in the adjudication of Taiwan-related cases, conveying judicial warmth. The Supreme People's Court has issued judicial documents providing cross-border online case-filing services and online litigation guidance for litigants, including Taiwan compatriots, so that Taiwan compatriots can enjoy convenient and efficient smart judicial services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The spokesperson just introduced the People's Courts handling cases involving Taiwan and protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Please briefly introduce the work of the procuratorial organs related to Taiwan.","The procuratorates, as judicial organs and legal supervisory organs, have played an important role in safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises according to law and creating a good rule-of-law business environment. This includes: giving full play to procuratorial functions and unique advantages, and refining and implementing preferential institutional arrangements and service measures for Taiwan; further strengthening supervision over criminal, civil and administrative litigation involving Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises, and improving the effectiveness of supervision; accurately grasping the boundaries of laws and policies, applying lenient arrest, prosecution and detention in accordance with law, and focusing on ensuring the compliant operation of Taiwan-invested enterprises while punishing crimes according to law; establishing regular mechanisms such as Taiwan-related procuratorial liaison offices, liaison points and liaison hotlines in Fujian, Jiangsu, Zhejiang and other places, and hiring Taiwan compatriots as liaison officers, to genuinely help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises solve their problems and difficulties.\nRecently, the book “Clean and Close” Procuratorial Blue -- Handbook of Procuratorial Organs Serving Taiwan Compatriots and Taiwan-Invested Enterprises, compiled under the organization of the Supreme People's Procuratorate, was officially published. Starting from the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises who live, work, and start businesses on the mainland, the book sorts out and answers more than 60 legal questions of great concern to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises from four aspects: national institutional policies, procuratorial duties and functions, Taiwan-related service measures, and Taiwan-related case handling practice. It cites more than 30 real cases close to the lives of Taiwan compatriots, and thoroughly explains major Taiwan-related laws and regulations as well as the judicial policies and institutional measures by which procuratorial organs protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises according to law, providing a detailed, vivid and practical legal reference for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, after Nicaragua severed “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan, the head of the DPP authorities' department in charge of foreign affairs said that mainland China, disregarding the feelings of the Taiwanese people, took away its “diplomatic ally.” What is your response? Second, on the 14th, Taiwan held the so-called “Taiwan-U.S.-Japan-India Indo-Pacific Security Dialogue,” where it claimed that “no…","On the first question: Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. We appreciate the countries concerned for following the trend of the times and supporting China's cause of reunification. We welcome the handful of so-called \"diplomatic allies\" of Taiwan to recognize the trend of history and join the right side of history at an early date. History and reality have once again shown that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end. No person or force can stop the historical trend of China's complete reunification and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe DPP authorities, in provoking for independence and relying on foreign powers to boost their own position, have continually colluded with external forces to create incidents. They are willing to serve as pawns for \"using Taiwan to contain China\" and are selling out the national interests. Such conduct must be met with a decisive counterblow.\nOn the second question: we have repeatedly pointed out that the root causes of the current tense and turbulent situation across the Taiwan Strait are, first, the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to provoke for independence, and second, some Western anti-China politicians playing the \"Taiwan card\" in an attempt to \"use Taiwan to contain China.\" This trend is extremely dangerous and amounts to playing with fire. We solemnly warn them to stop these schemes, or they will only burn themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","First question: Recently, the mainland repatriated the suspect in the Taiwan shooting case back to Taiwan. Does this mean that the cross-Strait agreement on jointly combating crime remains valid and continues to be implemented? Second question: This year, the Straits Forum newly established the “Cross-Strait New Media Forum.” May I ask how the spokesperson evaluates the role new media plays in promoting cultural…","The first question: cracking down on violent crime, protecting the life and property safety of people on both sides of the Strait, and safeguarding the peaceful and secure living environment of compatriots on both sides and the order of cross-Strait exchanges are our consistent practice. For cases that affect the life, health and safety of people on both sides of the Strait, the mainland side attaches great importance, handles them responsibly, and promptly and properly resolves them in accordance with the law, making every effort to safeguard the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.\nThe second question: We highly affirm the role of new media on both sides of the Strait as a bridge and a link in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nFirst, it helps the dissemination of information across the Strait. In particular, when the Democratic Progressive Party authorities strictly block the entry of mainland media information into Taiwan, the internet and new media have provided a new platform and channel for compatriots on both sides to understand each other. We also note that in recent times, many excellent mainland films, TV dramas, variety shows and documentaries have been broadcast widely in Taiwan, and some have been extremely popular. The internet deserves credit for this.\nSecond, as technology changes the way people interact, especially under the current epidemic prevention and control situation, the internet provides convenient ways for compatriots on both sides to continue exchanges through a combination of online and offline methods. Some mainland internet companies also fulfill their social responsibilities by carrying out good deeds such as searching for relatives across the Strait and providing services to compatriots on both sides, and by offering convenient measures such as employment and education information, which greatly facilitates exchanges between compatriots on both sides.\nThird, science and technology are neutral; whether they are good or bad depends on the people who master them. Over these years, everyone has deeply felt that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have gone to every extreme on the island to strengthen their control over the internet and new media, and have raised all kinds of \"cyber troops\" to attack, slander, spread rumors about, smear the mainland, sow discord and undermine cross-Strait relations. The many cases exposed on the island fully illustrate this.\nTo mainland netizens, we hope you will raise your vigilance, grasp the policy boundaries, never be fooled, and never be led astray by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the Green camp's cyber troops. While we firmly rebut those who incite hostility and confrontation between compatriots on both sides and promote \"Taiwan independence,\" we must also pay attention to unity and win over the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We must oppose \"Taiwan independence\" and not oppose Taiwan. To netizens in Taiwan, we also hope you will break through the barriers created by collusion between the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and external forces, not fear suppression, and not fear having your accounts deleted, and bravely voice rational support for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Do not let the internet in Taiwan become a \"battlefield\" where the \"demons and monsters\" such as \"1450\" and \"Ta Lu Ban (塔绿班)\" that the Democratic Progressive Party raises run rampant.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","According to British media reports, companies in seven countries including the United States and the United Kingdom have secretly helped Taiwan build submarines, and the relevant countries have provided export licenses for selling key components to Taiwan. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any country selling arms to the Taiwan region of China or conducting military contacts with it, and we oppose any words or deeds that encourage “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to “seek independence by force.” We urge all countries to fully recognize the high sensitivity of Taiwan-related issues and the serious harm of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, so as not to harm peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. No one should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces and attempting to “seek independence by force,” will only aggravate tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait and will certainly suffer complete failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","First question: Chairman Wang Yang reiterated at the Straits Forum the peaceful and integrated development of cross-strait relations, and especially emphasized exchanges and integration between cross-strait youth. He also made a special visit to an entrepreneurship and employment base for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan youth. What specific measures does the TAO have to further strengthen cross-strait youth…","On the first question: earlier, when I comprehensively introduced the outcomes of this year's Straits Forum, I already gave a fairly detailed account of our measures and achievements in helping cross-Strait youth grow and succeed and encouraging Taiwan youth to start businesses and find employment, which reflects the results of implementing our relevant policies. Going forward, we will further implement each measure benefiting Taiwan in concrete and meticulous ways, so that it produces greater policy effect.\nYou may also have noticed that at this year's Straits Forum conference, three Taiwan youths shared their stories of studying, starting businesses, and working on the mainland. As they put it: \"Unlimited opportunities on the mainland + the courage of Taiwan youth to strive = dreams can come true.\" We are glad to see that tens of thousands of Taiwan youths, like these three Taiwan compatriots, are diligently studying at mainland universities and working hard in their respective fields. They have not only achieved success in their studies and careers, but also deeply participated in the development of mainland social undertakings such as poverty alleviation, rural revitalization, teaching support and medical assistance, public welfare and charity, and environmental protection, contributing their strength to the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. We believe that the mainland is a solid arm that Taiwan youth can rely on, and we welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to participate more in the process of cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development.\nOn the second question: before the press conference, we played the song \"Towards the Future Together,\" the promotional song for the Beijing Winter Olympics' theme slogan, which was recorded with participation from some Taiwan compatriots living in Beijing. Taiwan youths and compatriots have actively participated in Winter Olympics volunteer services, which shows that the policies and measures we have adopted in recent years to support Taiwan youths and compatriots in developing on the mainland have achieved results. It also shows that as long as one breaks through the information barriers created by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and comes to the mainland to see, hear, learn, and work for oneself, compatriots on both sides of the Strait can draw closer. It further shows that compatriots on both sides carry the same blood, share the good virtues of the Chinese nation, and are willing to contribute love to the cause of humanity. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots to participate in Winter Olympics activities in various forms, to contribute to the grand event together and share the glory together.\nAccording to our understanding, since the global online recruitment was launched on December 5, 2019, and in accordance with the work arrangements for the preparation of the Beijing Winter Olympics, the Beijing Winter Olympics has begun recruiting Taiwan students from Beijing universities as event volunteers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","A Taiwan businessman reported that, due to epidemic prevention and control, the Dalang area of Dongguan has also implemented district-wide traffic control. May I ask whether you are aware of how Taiwan businesses and factories have been affected?","First, I want to emphasize that epidemic prevention and control involves the physical health and life safety of every person. It must be taken very seriously. Every individual and every enterprise, including Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-invested enterprises, has the obligation and responsibility to do epidemic prevention and control work well in accordance with the requirements of the joint prevention and control mechanism. We believe that Taiwan businesses and enterprises will fully understand this.\nSecond, we believe that relevant localities will coordinate epidemic prevention and control work with local economic and social development, and will provide good services to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in accordance with the \"11 measures\" we issued last year to help Taiwan enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: Taiwan is about to hold “four referendums,” most of whose topics relate to the daily lives of Taiwan residents. What is the mainland’s view on the topics of the “four referendums”? Second question: Some pan-green camp members have already begun to push the “resist China, protect Taiwan” theme, hoping to block the passage of the “four referendums.” What is your comment on this?","Regarding this, when I answered another reporter's question just now, I clearly pointed out and reminded everyone, especially Taiwan compatriots, to remain highly vigilant. The DPP authorities are engaging in political manipulation over the “four referendums.” One of the tricks they habitually use is to promote whether or not to vote, and what kind of ballot to cast, as “resisting China and protecting Taiwan.” This is entirely a fraud. As you said, the “four referendums” involve the island's economy, people's livelihood, and some public policies. On this, we have no particular views.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Taiwan media reported that Yang Ming Marine Transport Corporation of Taiwan proactively invited bids from two mainland companies closely associated with the PLA. Although the tenders were open and transparent, outside parties still question it as a “red supply chain” and an “intrusion” risk. What is your response? Second question: a recent Bloomberg report listed the Taiwan Strait crisis as one of…","On the first question: it is not at all surprising that Taiwan's Yang Ming Marine Transport Corporation has been obstructed from signing contracts with mainland enterprises. The DPP authorities have consistently obstructed cross-Strait economic cooperation, fabricating all kinds of pretexts and hyping so-called \"red industrial chains\" and \"infiltration\" of Taiwan. This is a lie fabricated entirely for the sake of pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" and provocative political manipulation. Economic cooperation should conform to economic laws. The DPP authorities should not artificially engage in political manipulation, let alone use this to create a \"green terror,\" recklessly label people as \"red hats,\" divide the two sides of the Strait, and intimidate the Taiwan public.\nOn the second question: we do not comment on the personal views of media outlets and scholars. It must be pointed out that the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation across the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities colluding with external forces and continually engaging in provocations to pursue \"Taiwan independence.\" Only by curbing these provocations for \"Taiwan independence\" can the crisis be resolved. Our position is clear: we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces provoke and force us, or even cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe yesterday again made erroneous remarks concerning China, threatening that Japan, the United States and other countries should allow Taiwan to join international organizations. Taiwan's foreign affairs department expressed thanks for this. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, not part of Japan. We warn these Japanese right-wing politicians that if they still dream of inheriting the mantle of militarism to undermine China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and indulge the “Taiwan independence” forces, they have miscalculated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Data released recently by the DPP authorities' finance department show that from January to November this year, Taiwan's exports to the mainland, including Hong Kong, rose 25.7% year on year to US$171.81 billion, the highest for the same period in history. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have expressed our views on the relevant topics several times at previous press conferences, so I will not repeat them here. Cross-Strait investment and trade have grown against the trend, which fully shows that the mainland's economic development is “a scenery that is uniquely beautiful on this side,” and fully shows that the mainland was, is, and will continue to be a fertile ground for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest and develop. Behind the trade surplus, what we see is the enthusiasm of Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest in the mainland, and the advanced technology, equipment and raw materials they bring. We have seen them vote with their feet, traveling far and wide.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The 2021 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year was announced in Taipei recently, with “difficult” (難) selected. What is your comment?","The choice of the character “difficult” (难) as the 2021 Cross-Strait Character of the Year can be understood from three aspects:\nFirst, the normal work, study and life of compatriots on both sides of the Strait have been affected to varying degrees by the COVID-19 pandemic. In particular, Taiwan compatriots also face vaccine shortages and vaccine safety issues artificially created by the DPP authorities, which makes things even more difficult.\nSecond, there is concern that the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, continue to engage in provocations to seek “independence,” leading to the current complex and grave state of cross-Strait relations and the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait.\nThird, there is indignation and anger at the DPP authorities' obstruction and sabotage of exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait under various pretexts and by various means, and their creation of confrontation and opposition between the two sides. The DPP authorities' perverse actions not only undermine the situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, but also seriously harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nIn contrast, the mainland side resolutely opposes “Taiwan independence,” adheres to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” upholds the development philosophy centered on the people, continuously removes interference, unites broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to overcome difficulties and move forward, continuously implements and refines a series of measures, steadily improves policies for equal treatment of Taiwan compatriots, and carefully organizes a series of cross-Strait exchange activities, promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and safeguarding the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nFinally, I would like to stress that “difficult” means both hardship and opportunity. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will work together with us to kick aside the stumbling block of “Taiwan independence,” so that cross-Strait relations regain a bright future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","What is the spokesperson's view on the matter in which, at the so-called “Summit for Democracy” organized by the United States, the Taiwan region's representative tried to play “Taiwan independence” tricks, but the video was cut off by the US side?","This is a case of trying to steal a chicken and losing the rice as well: a complete embarrassment that brings humiliation upon themselves.\nToday's press conference is now concluded. Thank you all for coming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211215_12396440.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-16","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Lithuania’s diplomatic delegation to China seems to have left the country yesterday amid worsening relations between the two countries. Do you have any comment on this?","In response to Lithuania’s erroneous acts of violating the political commitment it made in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China and openly creating the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world, the Chinese side has announced the downgrading of bilateral diplomatic relations to the chargé d’affaires level and informed the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Lithuania via diplomatic note of its decision to rename China’s diplomatic representation in Lithuania the Office of the Chargé d’Affaires of the People’s Republic of China in the Republic of Lithuania as well as its demand that the Lithuanian side change the name of its diplomatic representation in China accordingly.\nIt needs to be pointed out that the so-called allegations that Lithuanian personnel based in China were concerned about their safety and that the Chinese government has prohibited the employment of Chinese citizens by the office of the chargé d’affaires of Lithuania are purely groundless. The Chinese side always attaches high importance to protecting the safety of foreign diplomatic missions’ premises and personnel in China and to ensuring that all foreign diplomatic missions in China including the Lithuanian side can conduct their work normally. The Lithuanian side never mentioned to the Chinese side any issue with regard to its safety.\nThe ins and outs of the damaged relations between China and Lithuania are very clear. If the Lithuanian side refuses to face up to reality, does not reflect on itself and redress the mistake, and tries to shift its own responsibility, it will only produce a greater impact on bilateral relations, further hurt the two peoples’ feelings, and eventually harm itself. We urge the Lithuanian side to earnestly abide by basic norms governing international relations, conscientiously fulfill its commitment, and redress its erroneous acts that undermine China’s sovereignty and core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347185.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211216_10470530.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-16","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 16 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 16th that the DPP authorities' bad deeds in colluding with external forces to advance “Taiwan independence” keep piling up, and they will eventually be held to account.\nA reporter asked: Deluji, Chair of the “Taiwan Friendship Group” of the French National Assembly, and other French parliamentarians recently visited Taiwan and met with Tsai Ing-wen, Su Tseng-chang, and others. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above statement when answering the question.\nHe pointed out that the DPP authorities stubbornly collude with external forces to pursue “Taiwan independence,” and by any means court anti-China foreign lawmakers, attempting to create the illusion that their “Taiwan independence” conduct has the support of the international community and to mislead the people of the island and sway public opinion. Some anti-China forces in certain countries, for the purpose of “using Taiwan to contain China,” treat Taiwan as a pawn, attempting to manipulate Taiwan-related issues and obstruct China's reunification and national rejuvenation. We warn certain lawmakers in the relevant countries to immediately stop providing any form of support to “Taiwan independence” forces, and we urge the governments of the relevant countries to abide by the One-China principle and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211216_12396646.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-17","Wang Wenbin","MASTV","Lithuania’s Foreign Minister Gabrielius Landsbergis told the press that Chinese authorities had informed diplomats that their identification cards would soon no longer be valid. He said, “We asked for a longer period, simply because it would be complicated to arrange that return so quickly. We did not get any answer to the request, and people returned as fast as possible.” Unilateral changes to the status of a…","In response to the Lithuanian government’s erroneous move to allow the Taiwan authorities to set up the “Taiwan Representative Office” in Lithuania and flagrantly create the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world, the Chinese side has announced the downgrading of bilateral diplomatic relations to the chargé d’affaires level and informed the Lithuanian side via diplomatic note of its decision to rename China’s diplomatic representation in Lithuania the Office of the Chargé d’Affaires of the People’s Republic of China in the Republic of Lithuania as well as its demand that the Lithuanian side change the name of its diplomatic representation in China accordingly. This is consistent with the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations, genera international law and relevant international practices, and in line with the principle of diplomatic reciprocity.\nWith the downgraded relations to the chargé d’affaires level, China asked Lithuania’s diplomatic representation in China to reapply for the identification cards for diplomats. This is a normal procedure of China’s support and management of foreign missions in China, which complies with international law and common international practice. It does not affect the normal fulfillment of duties and life of Lithuanian diplomats in China. At the same time, China protects the security and legitimate rights of all diplomatic missions in China and their normal operation, including Lithuania’s diplomatic representation, in accordance with the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations.\nThe Lithuanian side has never applied for the extension of identification cards for its diplomats. The claim that it “did not get any answer to the request”from the Chinese side is purely made out of thin air. The fact is, without prior notification to the Chinese side, the Lithuanian side suddenly decided to pull out all its diplomats from China, thus putting on a self-directed farce.\nInstead of facing up to and addressing its wrong acts, the Lithuanian side spreads disinformation to shirk responsibilities. China deplores and rejects this. The attempt to create the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” and undermine China’s sovereignty will never succeed. The attempt to shift the blame and blackmail China politically is also miscalculated.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347186.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211217_10471141.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 17 — During a recent visit to Indonesia, US Secretary of State Blinken delivered a speech saying that there are \"concerns about Beijing's aggressive behavior\" in the Indo-Pacific region, and that the United States is determined to ensure \"peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\" In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 17th that some people in the United States, out of consideration of \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" have been stirring up trouble everywhere, blaming mainland China for tensions in the Taiwan Strait while disregarding the facts, and linking the Taiwan Strait and the South China Sea together, attempting to rally certain forces to jointly obstruct China's reunification and national rejuvenation.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, stubbornly \"relying on the United States to seek independence,\" fantasize about splitting the country with the help of external forces, which has led to the current tense and turbulent state of cross-Strait relations. Any provocation aimed at \"independence\" will certainly be resolutely defeated. No person and no force should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will, and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211217_12396879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 17 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 17th in response to an inquiry: We demand that the US Congress stop its erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues, stop bolstering and emboldening “Taiwan independence” forces, and stop further damaging peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the US government and relevant…","Ma Xiaoguang said: we warn the DPP authorities that colluding with external forces to “resist unification by force” will only push Taiwan toward disaster. If they provoke and coerce, or even cross the red line, we will have to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211217_12396880.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-20","Zhao Lijian","Hubei Media Group","According to reports, on December 17, an official of Lithuania’s Ministry of Agriculture said that the trade dispute with China may cause Lithuania huge losses. What happened to Lithuania is a warning for other European countries that if they stand by their interests and values and refuse to follow the Chinese government’s rules, similar consequences will follow. Lithuanian manufacturers will attend the Food…","Lithuania openly created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world, renounced the political commitment it made in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Lithuania, and violated the one-China principle, a basic norm governing international relations and consensus of the international community. The move is bound to be disdained and rejected. Speaking of rules, it is right and just that national sovereignty and territorial integrity shall be inviolable. Lithuania broke faith and stood on the opposite side of what is right and just. Nothing good will come out of this. If certain people or forces in Lithuania insist on colluding with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and going further down the dark path, they will eventually end up in the trashcan of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347187.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211220_10471943.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-20","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","In response to a question on December 17, US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said that the US position on Taiwan is clear because it is a position that the US has sustained to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait for decades. It is rooted in the one-China policy, the Taiwan Relations Act, the three communiqués. The whole purpose of American policy toward Taiwan and toward cross-Strait…","We have noted relevant reports. China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear-cut. Here I would like to stress the following three points.\nFirst, there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. This is not only a historical and legal fact that cannot be changed, but also a status quo that cannot be challenged. The DPP authorities refuse to recognize the 1992 Consensus that embodies the one-China principle, constantly provoke confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and solicit US support for the purpose of seeking Taiwan independence. This is what changes the status quo and is also the source of tensions across the Taiwan Strait. Some forces in the US have obstinately manipulated the Taiwan question to contain China. They have emboldened the Taiwan independence forces and increased tensions across the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond, the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués are the political foundation for the establishment of diplomatic ties and the steady development of bilateral relations between China and the US. The Taiwan Relations Act unilaterally fabricated by the US runs counter to its commitments made in the three joint communiqués, violates basic norms governing international relations, and places US domestic law above international obligations. It is illegal, null and void. What the US should earnestly abide by is the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, rather than something cooked up unilaterally by itself.\nThird, China’s complete reunification is unstoppable. The historical trend will not be changed by anyone, any force or any country. We urge the US side to take seriously China’s position and concerns, be cautious in words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues, stop military contacts with Taiwan, stop developing ties with Taiwan in essence, and stop sending any wrong signal to the Taiwan independence forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347187.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211220_10471943.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, December 21 — Responding to remarks by Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council on the 7th Legislative Council election in Hong Kong, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 21st that the 7th Legislative Council election in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, which has just concluded, was a successful practice in implementing the new electoral system of the HKSAR, fully demonstrating the new electoral system's broad representativeness, political inclusiveness, balanced participation and fair competitiveness. The DPP authorities jumped out to make irresponsible remarks, distorting and slandering, which once again exposes the evil political nature of their scheme to throw Hong Kong into chaos and pursue \"Taiwan independence.\"\nHe said this is a fair, just and open election, unlike the elections the DPP authorities manipulate, which involve large-scale power-for-money deals, black gold politics, illegal campaign donations and illegal vote-buying, with constant schemes and frequent dirty tricks. This is a healthy competition and a rational, pragmatic election, unlike the elections the DPP authorities manipulate, which care only about blue versus green and not about right and wrong, mobilize with hate-based organizations, and are full of lies and populism. This is an election free from interference by external forces, independent and self-determined, unlike the elections the DPP authorities manipulate, which watch the eyes of external forces, cater to their likes and dislikes, and safeguard their interests. This is an election that selects the worthy and the capable, unlike the DPP politicians who only trade barbs, chase attention, make empty promises to deceive the public, and attack and smear opponents without any bottom line.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the smooth holding of the 7th Legislative Council election of the HKSAR fully embodies the principle of \"patriots administering Hong Kong\" and fully demonstrates the strong vitality of \"One Country, Two Systems.\" The reason the DPP authorities jumped out to viciously attack is that the successful practice of \"One Country, Two Systems\" in Hong Kong has laid bare their true face of using democracy as a cover to deceive the island's public for a long time, and has rendered their deceptive tactic of profiting by smearing the HKSAR self-defeating. A lie repeated ten thousand times is still a lie. In the face of the historic trend of Hong Kong moving from chaos to order and from governance to prosperity, the DPP authorities' tricks of using Hong Kong as a pretext should come to an end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211221_12397493.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-23","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","On December 22, Spokesperson for the US Department of State said that Secretary Antony Blinken spoke with EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy Josep Borrell. They highlighted shared concerns about escalating political pressure and economic coercion by China against Lithuania, which are impacting both US and European companies. They underscored continuing solidarity with Lithuania and…","Lithuania has made grave mistakes on Taiwan-related issues. Instead of admitting and addressing its mistakes, it has been making up lies to shirk responsibilities and distort facts. The US and the EU know this too well. What they should do is to urge Lithuania to immediately admit and address its mistakes, rather than disregard facts and screen the faults. Accusing China of the issue groundlessly further mixes right with wrong, transgresses justice and hurts the images of the US and the EU.\nFacts have proven many times that the US is the master of unilateral sanctions and coercive diplomacy in all their forms. Examples abound in terms of unwarranted unilateral sanctions, long-arm jurisdiction and the abuse of state power to suppress foreign institutions, companies and individuals in accordance with US domestic law, which have drawn wide opposition from the international community. If the EU wants to uphold an international order that is equitable and fair, it should tell right from wrong, stay objective and unbiased, and take real actions to safeguard the steady and sound development of China-EU relations. It should not dance to the US’ tune, and stand on the wrong side of justice.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347190.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211223_10474830.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-24","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","We’ve noted that Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Hirokazu Matsuno said on December 24 that Japan’s Olympic Committee President Yasuhiro Yamashita, Paralympic Committee President Kazuyuki Mori and Tokyo Olympic Organizing Committee President Seiko Hashimoto will attend the Beijing Winter Olympics and Paralympics. Do you have any comment on this?","China welcomes representatives of Japan’s Olympic Committee and other organizations as well as Japanese athletes to the Beijing Winter Olympics and Paralympics. We have every confidence that working together with all sides under the Olympic motto of “together”, China will deliver a streamlined, safe and splendid Olympic event to the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347191.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211224_10475509.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-24","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Yesterday Kyodo News reported that Japan and the US have made a draft joint operation plan in case of a Taiwan emergency. And the two nations are likely start working to formalize the operation plan when their foreign ministers and defense ministers meet in January. What is your response?","There have been quite some reports like this recently. China is following them closely.\nI want to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. China never allows any country to meddle in the Taiwan question and interfere in China’s internal affairs under any pretext or in any form. No one should underestimate the strong resolution, determination and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347191.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211224_10475509.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-28","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","The Economist published an article saying that China unilaterally announced its decision to downgrade diplomatic relations with Lithuania to the chargé d’affaires level and asked Lithuanian diplomats to hand in their Chinese identity cards to have them changed to reflect their mission’s status, thus chasing them from Beijing. Being unable to ensure the diplomatic status of the embassy personnel, and not accepting…","China “chased” Lithuanian diplomats from Beijing? The allegation is pure defamation. Acting in bad faith, Lithuania openly creates the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. This gravely undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and damages the political foundation for an ambassadorial-level diplomatic relationship. The Chinese side, out of the need to safeguard its core interests and the one-China principle, a basic norm governing international relations, has downgraded its diplomatic relations with Lithuania to the chargé d’affaires level. This is entirely legitimate and reasonable. With relations downgraded to the chargé d’affaires level, China asked Lithuania’s diplomatic representation in China to reapply for identification cards for its diplomats and administrative and technical personnel. This is a normal procedure of China’s support for and management of foreign missions in China, which complies with international law and common practice. It does not affect the normal fulfillment of duties and life of Lithuanian diplomats in China. At the same time, China protects the security and lawful rights of all diplomatic missions in China and their normal operation, including Lithuania’s diplomatic representation, in accordance with the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations.\nWithout prior notification to the Chinese side, the Lithuanian government abruptly decided to pull out all its diplomats from China and spread false information afterwards to shift the blame. China firmly opposes this. Lithuania cannot cover up its repeated erroneous acts even if it resorts to distorting facts and confusing right with wrong. We believe that the international community will adopt an objective and just position and refuse to buy Lithuania’s one-sided story.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347193.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211228_10476420.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-28","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” said it strongly condemns that Nicaragua has “embezzled” Taiwan’s assets including its former “embassy” on December 27 and handed them over to Beijing. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","First I need to point out that there is no “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” in Taiwan, only provincial authorities in charge of foreign affairs. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Ever since its founding, the Government of the People’s Republic of China has been the sole legal government representing the whole of China, Taiwan included. This is an unshakable historical and legal fact. According to basic principles of international law including respect for national sovereignty and territorial integrity, all state assets of China, whether in China or overseas, are property of the PRC Government. This has been widely recognized throughout many years of diplomatic practice.\nChina highly appreciates Nicaragua’s act of justice showing respect for China’s sovereignty and commitment to the one-China principle. The Taiwan authorities attempt to achieve its sinister agenda by playing the trick of giving away China’s state assets, which is illegal, null and void and will never work.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347193.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211228_10476420.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 23 — In response to a recent proposal by a Kuomintang (KMT) Tainan City councilor to “change the national title of the Republic of China to Republic of Taiwan,” which was passed by the city council, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 23rd: We note that the Kuomintang has stated that it does not endorse such words and deeds and opposes “Taiwan independence.” Individuals engaging in political manipulation on major issues of right and wrong is a very dangerous act. We firmly oppose this and severely condemn it.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” are the basic political positions of the Kuomintang and the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. “Taiwan independence” separatist acts seriously endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harm the well-being of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. They should be condemned in one voice by compatriots on both sides of the Strait and firmly opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211228_12398583.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-29","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to media reports, in a recent letter to the President of the European Commission Ursula von der Leyen and the President of the European Council Charles Michel, co-chairs and members of the Formosa Club in 25 European countries urged the two EU bodies to take concrete actions to support Lithuania as soon as possible. Do you have any comment?","The ins and outs of what happened regarding Lithuania on the Taiwan question is clear. Lithuania blatantly violates the one-China principle and stands against basic norms governing international relations and the universal consensus of the international community. Its scheme is doomed to fail.\nOnly by correcting its mistakes and returning to the right path of adhering to the one-China principle can Lithuania get out of the current predicament.\n“Formosa” is a word with strong colonial undertones. The platform of a club with “Formosa” in its name can be easily imagined. Its malicious hype-up is not even worth commenting on.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347194.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211229_10476917.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on December 29, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends. Welcome to this year's final regular press conference of the TAO. I will host today; please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Please summarize cross-strait relations in 2021 and look ahead to cross-strait relations in 2022.","In 2021, cross-strait relations were complex and grim, and the Taiwan Strait faced a new round of tension. We firmly grasped the initiative and leadership in the development of cross-strait relations, and united Taiwan compatriots in working together to push cross-strait relations forward despite difficulties, with steady progress. Several outstanding features have emerged:\nFirst, we held the right direction and shaped the trend toward unification. General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches at the Grand Gathering Celebrating the 100th Anniversary of the Founding of the Communist Party of China and at the Grand Gathering Commemorating the 110th Anniversary of the 1911 Revolution, as well as the resolution adopted by the Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, set forth the Party Central Committee's major policies on Taiwan, guiding and propelling the ship of cross-strait relations to always move in the right direction. Chinese people at home and abroad have repeatedly sounded the era's powerful call that \"if the country is strong, I am there; if unification is achieved, I am there,\" gathering the mighty strength to realize national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nSecond, we decisively deterred provocations seeking \"Taiwan independence\" and firmly resisted external interference. All Chinese people have firmly stood on the right side of history, adhered to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and with strong determination, firm resolve and great capability, have resolutely crushed the provocations of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities seeking \"Taiwan independence,\" firmly curbed the schemes of external forces to \"use Taiwan to contain China,\" and firmly defended national sovereignty and territorial integrity, effectively safeguarding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThird, we deepened integrated development and shared development opportunities. We adhere to the development philosophy of \"putting the people first,\" and continue to provide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises with development opportunities and equal treatment, and further improve policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have actively integrated into the new development pattern of the mainland and taken part in high-quality development, personally witnessed the achievements of China's modernization drive, obtained tangible benefits, and written a vivid chapter of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer together and developing in integration.\nFourth, we maintained exchanges and cooperation and deepened heart-to-heart understanding. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait, overcoming the impact of the pandemic and artificial interference on the island, actively carried out cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and held nearly 800 civil exchange activities such as the 13th Straits Forum and the 2021 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zijin Mountain Summit, which demonstrated the shared voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait who oppose \"Taiwan independence\" moving against the tide and who look forward to peaceful cross-strait development.\nIn 2022, we will thoroughly understand and fully implement the overall strategy of the new era for resolving the Taiwan question and the decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work. We will take more forceful measures, resolutely crush the schemes of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, firmly oppose interference by external forces, continue to promote peaceful development of cross-strait relations, bravely explore new paths for integrated development across the Strait, continue to take the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and promote heart-to-heart understanding among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end. Colluding with external forces to split the country and standing against the Chinese nation is an abyss of no return, and they must rein in their horses at the edge of the cliff. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should work together in harmony and unity to jointly promote peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advance the process of national reunification, join hands to accomplish this historic undertaking, and share in the glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398853.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the state of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2021. What were the main characteristics? What are your expectations for cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2022?","In 2021, we emphasized “using exchanges to promote integration, using benefits to promote integration, and using affection to promote integration,” and firmly advanced cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation.\nFirst, Taiwanese businesses’ investment in the mainland has grown steadily, and cross-Strait trade has reached a record high. From January to November, total cross-Strait trade reached US$298.28 billion, up 27.3% year on year. Of this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$70.77 billion, up 31.2% year on year, and imports from Taiwan were US$227.51 billion, up 26.2% year on year. The mainland newly established 5,923 Taiwan-funded enterprises, an increase of 34.7% year on year. Cross-Strait industrial cooperation has deepened continuously, the industrial and supply chains have remained stable, the production and operations of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland have generally been stable, and Taiwanese investment has shown positive changes, with more large projects and higher technological content.\nSecond, we have helped Taiwanese businesses and enterprises reach a new level of development on the mainland. We have actively guided and supported Taiwanese businesses and enterprises in participating in the implementation of the 14th Five-Year Plan. Taiwanese enterprises have made significant progress in integrating into the new development pattern, participating in high-quality development, the Belt and Road Initiative, and national regional coordinated development strategies. We encourage and guide more Taiwanese businesses and enterprises to increase capital, expand production, and take root and develop. We have supported a number of high-quality Taiwanese enterprises in listing on the mainland. In 2021, a total of 6 Taiwanese enterprises were listed on the mainland A-share market, and as of now the total number has exceeded 40.\nThird, we have made new progress in continuously deepening cross-Strait integration and development. We have implemented a series of measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, issued and carried out in detail the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” and supported Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises in participating in the mainland’s rural revitalization strategy and high-quality development of agriculture and forestry. We have strongly supported Fujian in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integration and development, and have preliminarily formed a policy system under which Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises in Fujian enjoy equal treatment.\nFourth, the construction of platforms for cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation has achieved new results. We have established the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone in Hunan and the Cross-Strait Cooperation Zone for New and Old Growth Drivers Transition in Shandong, and newly approved the establishment of two Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases. We have actively assisted Taiwanese youth in internships, employment, and entrepreneurship on the mainland. We helped Taiwanese businesses and enterprises participate in the 4th China International Import Expo, made good use of various e-commerce platforms, and expanded the mainland’s domestic market. More than 10 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities held Taiwan-related economic and trade exchange activities combining offline and online formats, effectively promoting economic and trade cooperation between localities and Taiwan.\nIn the new year, our philosophy that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family” will not change, our policy of sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first will not change, and our measures to do practical good deeds for Taiwan compatriots will not change. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises will stand on the right side of history, draw a clear line with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and play a positive role in promoting cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integration and development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398851.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Please briefly introduce cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2021. What are the main characteristics?","Although affected by the COVID-19 pandemic and by obstacles deliberately set up by the DPP authorities, cross-strait personnel exchanges still cannot return to normal this year, our efforts to promote cross-strait exchanges and deepen integrated development have not stopped, the earnest desire of compatriots on both sides to draw closer has not diminished, and exchanges and cooperation across all civil fields between the two sides have not ceased. Some new characteristics have emerged:\nFirst, the new era and new journey have brought a new atmosphere of spiritual affinity between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This year marks the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China. Many Taiwan compatriots attended major events such as the celebration of the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China and the commemoration of the 110th anniversary of the 1911 Revolution, and took part in related theme-based exchange and visit activities. They gained a deeper understanding of the original aspiration and mission, the struggle, and the glorious achievements of the Communist Party of China, and are full of confidence in realizing national reunification and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Many Taiwan compatriots studying and working in the mainland actively took part in volunteer services such as helping with rural revitalization, teaching in remote schools, offering free clinics and medical services, and aiding people affected by disasters. Numerous Taiwan artists spoke out enthusiastically, paying tribute to border-guarding heroes, standing firmly behind Xinjiang cotton, and donating to flood relief in Henan, and during the National Day holiday they extended blessings for the prosperity of the motherland, expressing the voices of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond, policies on equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots have been implemented with new results, and more Taiwan compatriots are coming to the mainland to pursue and realize their dreams. This year, 20 Taiwan literary and art figures and writers attended the national congresses of the China Writers Association and the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles for the first time as formal delegates. Thirteen Taiwan compatriots became new members of the relevant art associations under the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles. Eight Taiwan compatriots residing in Fujian were named representative inheritors of Fujian Provincial intangible cultural heritage. Baseball player Li Xuanze became the first Taiwan athlete to obtain a mainland athlete technical grade certificate. In addition, many Taiwan professionals have come to the mainland to work in science and technology, education, rural entrepreneurship and rural construction, among other fields. More than 2,000 Taiwan teachers are now teaching at mainland universities. Increasing numbers of Taiwan compatriots have found stages for their own development on the mainland and have joined the process of realizing integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.\nThird, cross-strait exchange activities remain colorful and diverse, and new media dissemination has had notable effects. A large number of cross-strait signature exchange activities, such as the Straits Forum, continued to be held, and the enthusiasm of compatriots on both sides to take part has not waned. “Cloud meetings” on various themes, Film and Video Culture Week, study camps, online competitions, live-streamed events and other activities overcame the barriers imposed by the pandemic, and the number of people from all sectors in Taiwan who actually took part and who could access them online greatly exceeded that of traditional exchange models. Tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots, especially young people and students, who had never been to the mainland before, took part in cross-strait exchange activities online for the first time and left a favorable impression.\nFourth, Taiwan compatriots working, studying and living on the mainland have gradually become the main body of offline cross-strait exchanges, and young people have increasingly become the main force in integrated cross-strait development. Over the past year, more and more Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life have actively taken part in exchanges across all cross-strait fields, shared their own experiences and successful practices, told the wonderful stories of coming to the mainland to chase and realize their dreams, and called on compatriots on both sides to work together in harmony and pursue common development. A group of Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland received provincial- and municipal-level May Day Labor Medals, Youth May Fourth Medals, and the title of “Three-Eight Red Banner Bearer.” At the 13th Straits Forum recently held in Xiamen, three Taiwan youths shared their stories of striving and growing up on the mainland and their inner journeys. Their accounts were vivid, authentic, inspiring, and drew close attention from people on both sides of the Strait and strong resonance among young friends.\nIn the new year, we will continue to promote cross-strait exchanges and interactions, deepen integrated cross-strait development, and unite compatriots on both sides to create a bright future together. It should be noted that the Taiwan side has prohibited mainland residents from visiting Taiwan for nearly two years. This is long out of step with the times and should be lifted as soon as possible. The DPP authorities should face the trend of the times and the mainstream public opinion that wants exchange, cooperation and development, and stop interfering with and obstructing civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398850.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Fujian Province recently issued the “Opinions on Supporting Xiamen in Building a Demonstration Zone for High-Quality Development,” which involves promoting the integrated development of Xiamen and Kinmen ahead of others. What progress has Xiamen made in further promoting integrated development across the Taiwan Strait? What other measures will be taken?","On December 19 this year, the Fujian Provincial Party Committee and the Provincial People's Government issued the “Opinions on Supporting Xiamen in Building a High-Quality Development Leading Demonstration Zone.” This is an important measure by Fujian Province to fully implement the important speeches and instructions of General Secretary Xi Jinping on Fujian's work, and to carry out General Secretary Xi Jinping's major policy propositions on deepening cross-Strait integrated development. The relevant opinions propose to “build a pilot demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development. Promote the pioneering integrated development of Xiamen and Kinmen, advance projects such as the Xiamen-Kinmen bridge, power, and gas connections, support the implementation of more convenient cross-strait personnel exchange and customs clearance arrangements between Xiamen and Kinmen, develop and strengthen tourism to Kinmen, deepen financial cooperation with Taiwan, innovate the methods of talent exchange and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan, and continue to hold well important events such as the Straits Forum. Support the establishment of a cross-Strait industry standards cooperation information base, and promote the interoperability of information standards for logistics, electronic ports, and other areas.” At present, policies on equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian are being comprehensively and continuously advanced, and more and more Kinmen residents are starting businesses, buying property, and living in Xiamen. Exchanges and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan in various fields continue to deepen. Fujian's water supply to Kinmen has cumulatively exceeded 16 million tons, and the preliminary technical preparations for power, gas, and bridge connections between Kinmen and Matsu have been essentially completed.\nRecently, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a letter congratulating Xiamen on the 40th anniversary of its establishment as a Special Economic Zone, hoping that Xiamen will comprehensively deepen reform and opening up, promote high-quality development, and advance cross-Strait integrated development. We deeply study and implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's letter, vigorously support Fujian in exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development, and continue to support the pioneering integrated development of Xiamen and Kinmen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic, how to do a good job in epidemic prevention has been a matter of constant concern. Please introduce the situation of the mainland's assistance to Taiwan compatriots in responding to the epidemic, including how many Comirnaty vaccines have been provided to Taiwan so far?","We attach great importance to the life, health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Since the epidemic broke out on the island, the mainland side has promptly activated the cross-Strait public health emergency notification mechanism. From January 3, 2020 to date, through the contact channels under the cross-Strait Agreement on Medicine and Health Cooperation, the mainland has notified Taiwan’s disease control authorities of mainland epidemic information a total of 324 times, shared COVID-19 prevention and treatment technical materials 16 times (55 documents), and agreed to let Taiwan health experts attend more than 20 World Health Organization technical meetings. At the same time, we made orderly arrangements for vaccination of Taiwan compatriots residing on the mainland. According to incomplete statistics, as of December 15 this year, 177,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated, with a cumulative total of about 350,000 doses administered.\nIn May this year, after a new round of COVID-19 outbreaks in Taiwan, we repeatedly expressed our willingness to do our utmost to help Taiwan compatriots cope with the epidemic and actively promoted providing vaccines to people on the island. This included providing Taiwan compatriots with mainland vaccines recognized by the WHO, and supporting the BNT vaccine, which Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group participated in developing and for which it holds exclusive agency rights, to serve Taiwan residents. Relevant civil organizations in Shanghai and Jiangsu also expressed willingness to donate a batch of vaccines to Taiwan compatriots. We also actively considered sending epidemic prevention and control experts to the island, sharing anti-epidemic experience and providing epidemic prevention consultation, among other things. However, the DPP authorities, for the sake of political self-interest, not only turned a blind eye to the goodwill of the mainland but even maliciously slandered mainland vaccines and crudely blocked mainland vaccines from entering the island for use by Taiwan compatriots.\nWhile the epidemic was raging in Taiwan, vaccines were in severe shortage, and Taiwan residents were eagerly awaiting vaccination, we made proper arrangements for Taiwan compatriots who came to the mainland on civil aviation passenger flights to be vaccinated on the mainland in accordance with relevant policies. After many efforts, the first batch of Comirnaty vaccines supplied to Taiwan by Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group arrived in Taiwan smoothly in September this year, and on September 22, Comirnaty vaccination officially began in Taiwan. To date, a total of 14 batches, totaling about 12.4 million doses, have arrived. The 15th batch, of 930,000 doses, will arrive in Taiwan at the end of December, and by then a total of 13.33 million doses will have been delivered to the island this year.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are bound by blood ties. We will continue to uphold the spirit of “serving Taiwan compatriots as we serve the people on the mainland,” help the people on the island cope with the epidemic, and effectively safeguard the life and health of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398847.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","The Central Economic Work Conference held recently has drawn much attention. How will the spirit of this conference be implemented to advance economic work regarding Taiwan and deepen cross-Strait integrated development?","The Central Economic Work Conference held this month pointed out that the fundamental economic resilience and long-term positive trend of the mainland will not change. Economic work in 2022 must adhere to the overall principle of seeking progress while maintaining stability, fully, accurately and comprehensively implement the new development philosophy, accelerate the building of a new development paradigm, comprehensively deepen reform and opening up, adhere to innovation-driven development, and promote high-quality development.\nWe will thoroughly implement the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference, continue to expand cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and actively support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in participating in the implementation of the 14th Five-Year Plan, so that they can share more development opportunities, enjoy more equal treatment, and receive better service and guarantees. As the 14th Five-Year Plan and the Outline of the Long-Range Objectives Through the Year 2035 are advanced and implemented, the mainland's economic environment will become more stable and healthy, and its business environment will become fairer and better optimized, providing Taiwan businesses and enterprises with more opportunities and better services. Taiwan businesses and enterprises, with firm confidence and rooted development, will surely achieve greater development, and more Taiwan compatriots will also benefit from cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and integrated development, living better and more comfortable lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398848.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Some public opinion on the island holds that the DPP authorities will open imports of Japanese Fukushima food. What comments do you have on this? What regulations does the mainland have on food imports from areas of Japan affected by nuclear contamination?","After the Fukushima nuclear power plant leak in March 2011, to guard against the import into the mainland of Japanese food contaminated with radioactive substances, the relevant departments of the mainland adopted strengthened supervision measures for food imported from Japan. First, they prohibited the import of food, edible agricultural products, and feed from 10 prefectures, including Fukushima. Second, when importing food, edible agricultural products, and feed produced in other regions of Japan, they required the provision of certificates of origin and radioactive substance testing qualification certificates issued by the Japanese government, and continued to assess the radioactive contamination risks of Japanese food. On the premise of ensuring safety, they dynamically adjusted the strengthened supervision measures to prevent the entry of products that do not meet the requirements.\nFood safety is closely related to people's vital interests. We have always attached great importance to it and actively taken effective measures, because we adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people and genuinely protect the lives and health and safety of the people. As for the DPP authorities' conduct on issues concerning the life and health safety of Taiwan compatriots, we believe that the eyes of the broad Taiwan compatriots are sharp and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Relevant parties in Taiwan recently said that a hearing is necessary regarding the “referendum proposal” to apply for participation in international sports events, including the Paris Olympics, under the full name “Taiwan.” What comments do you have on this?","The participation of Taiwan region teams and athletes in international sports events has long been subject to clear rules and standards. A very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island, supported and tolerated by the DPP authorities, have repeatedly attempted to participate in international sports events under the name of “Chinese Taipei” in order to make political capital out of sports events. This is entirely a political manipulation aimed at grandstanding. In 2018, they staged a farce of this kind, which ultimately ended in failure. The lesson is not far off. No person or force has the right to deprive Taiwan athletes of the right to participate in international competitions. The political manipulation of the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces ultimately harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, sacrifices the competitive opportunities of Taiwan's sports athletes, and challenges the rules of international sports organizations. It will inevitably be opposed by the international community and compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202112/t20211229_12398846.htm"],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","It is learned that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Supreme People’s Court jointly promoted the online litigation-mediation connection mechanism for Taiwan-related disputes established through the “People’s Court Mediation Platform,” which has recently been put into operation. Please introduce the relevant information.","To implement the Party Central Committee’s decisions and arrangements on comprehensively governing the country according to law and on Taiwan work, to actively practice the development philosophy centered on the people and the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and to effectively safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has, adhering to placing non-litigation dispute resolution mechanisms in the forefront and giving full play to the important role of mediation in resolving Taiwan-related disputes, closely cooperated with the Supreme People’s Court to establish an online mechanism for linking litigation and mediation for Taiwan-related disputes on the “People’s Court Mediation Platform.” The platform provides compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, with high-quality, one-stop, full-process online dispute resolution services, including diversified mediation, judicial confirmation and case registration, and resolves Taiwan-related disputes promptly and efficiently in accordance with law. Going forward, for civil and commercial disputes accepted by the people’s courts in which one or more parties are Taiwan compatriots or Taiwan-invested enterprises, and for other Taiwan-related disputes suitable for mediation, the parties may actively apply through the platform to use the online mechanism for linking litigation and mediation to resolve them.\nOn December 28, the mechanism was officially launched. More than 180 mediation organizations and more than 540 mediators have registered on the platform, including more than 80 Taiwan compatriots serving as mediators. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises can conveniently use this mechanism through the “People’s Court Mediation Platform” website, mobile app, WeChat mini-program, and the “Diversified Mediation Express” WeChat official account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","The new Cross-Strait Exchange Base column on China Taiwan Net officially went online today. Please introduce the relevant details.","Since 2009, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office have successively approved the establishment of 82 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 24 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei, and Fujian. To further comprehensively showcase to compatriots on both sides of the Strait the construction, development, and Taiwan-related exchanges and cooperation of each base, promote mutual learning and reference among the bases, and better play their platform role in cross-Strait exchanges, China Taiwan Network has launched the “Cross-Strait Exchange Bases” special column, which officially went online today (29th) (http://www.taiwan.cn/xwzx/zxzt/zhuanti111/jljdxl/). The special column can be accessed by clicking from the homepage of China Taiwan Network on mobile or PC. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to learn about the exchange bases and related cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation through this platform. We hope relevant localities will fully use the platform role of this special column to build, develop, and promote the bases well, and play a greater role in deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and promoting heart-to-heart connection among compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和《看台海》新媒体记者","We note that a Taiwan survey shows that in 2021, 76.3% of surveyed enterprises on the island confirmed they would pay year-end bonuses, down 10% from last year, and the average payout base is only 1.13 months, a new 11-year low. What does the spokesperson think is the reason for this phenomenon?","I have seen the relevant reports. There is a huge gap between the economic data released by the DPP authorities and the actual feelings and actual incomes of the Taiwan people. As to what causes this, Taiwan compatriots will think about it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The “four referendums” in Taiwan recently all failed. Is the mainland worried that the Blue camp on the island is being marginalized?","You mentioned this matter, and there have been many comments on the island. On issues involving the island's economy, people's livelihood and certain public policies, the DPP authorities are maliciously engaging in political manipulation for their own private interests, and what is ultimately harmed are the welfare of Taiwan residents and the development prospects of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The DPP and Japan's LDP held the so-called “2+2” meeting for the second time on the 24th. The LDP side said it welcomes Taiwan joining the CPTPP. What is your comment?","The Japanese government and relevant figures have for some time made a series of erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question, and we firmly oppose them. We urge Japan to deeply reflect on history, immediately correct its mistakes, and, through practical action, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents. Japan should be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question and stop all erroneous words and deeds concerning Taiwan. The DPP authorities’ attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke is doomed to fail.\nRegarding the participation of Taiwan region of China in regional economic cooperation, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities’ attempt to seek “independence” under the banner of economic and trade matters will not succeed. Relevant foreign politicians should adhere to the one-China principle and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","On the 27th, US President Biden signed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2022,” which contains negative Taiwan-related provisions, including helping Taiwan develop asymmetric “defense capabilities,” strengthening cooperation between the US National Guard and Taiwan, and Congress’s recommendation to invite Taiwan to participate in the RIMPAC exercises. The DPP authorities said they welcome…","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and the US has no right to interfere. We firmly oppose the US passing bills that contain Taiwan-related content. No person or force can stop us from defeating provocations to seek independence and from the just action of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities are willing to serve as pawns and attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence,” and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Recently media disclosed that Taiwan businessman Lin Ruiyang is suspected of illegal activity. Is this also a warning to Taiwan enterprises and businesspeople on the mainland? Second question: Reuters reported, claiming that mainland spies have infiltrated the Taiwan military, aiming to weaken the Taiwan military's will and the trust of Taiwan residents in the military. What comment do you have on…","First question: The specific situation still needs further understanding. Judging from the announcement issued by the relevant department, this is entirely a commercial matter and has nothing to do with cross-Strait relations. What I want to emphasize is that anyone who does business or starts a business in the mainland must, first and foremost, comply with the law and regulations.\nSecond question: The DPP authorities are using this routine of turning external propaganda into internal propaganda to exaggerate the so-called \"mainland threat,\" attempting to mislead the public on the island, serve the political purpose of inciting \"anti-China and anti-Chinese sentiment,\" and seek private gain. This set of tricks and schemes is utterly devoid of novelty, and the people of Taiwan should have seen quite enough of it by now.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","Kuomintang Chairman Eric Chu plans to visit the United States as early as after the Spring Festival, and will discuss Taiwan-U.S. relations, military security, economic and trade exchanges, technology and other issues. What is the spokesperson's comment?","I hope the countries with which I have diplomatic relations will uphold the One-China Principle and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","First question: Because airports such as Pudong on the mainland have recently strengthened disinfection, Taiwan's Songshan and Xiaogang airports' flights to the mainland can only 'depart empty and return with passengers,' causing crew consumption and economic losses for airlines. With the Spring Festival homecoming crowds greatly increasing, what is the spokesperson's view? Second question: The mainland requires…","I will answer the second question first. Firstly, the mainland governs the country according to law, and taking up employment in accordance with professional qualifications is also a rule that applies across the Taiwan Strait. Working without a license is not permitted anywhere; this is the basic premise for ensuring industry standards.\nSecondly, I have looked into this. The qualification certification for performance agents began in 2006. Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland may voluntarily apply for it and enjoy the same treatment as mainland personnel. This policy reflects our sincere willingness to share the mainland's development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots.\nThe purpose of the newly revised “Administrative Measures for Performance Agency Personnel” is to strengthen the building and management of the performance agent workforce and to regulate performance agency conduct. The door to the occupational qualification certification examination remains open to Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan compatriots who meet the application requirements are welcome to take the performance agent qualification certification examination.\nWhat I cannot understand is: since they came to the mainland to develop their careers, why do they not abide by mainland laws? If the DPP authorities use this as a pretext for political manipulation and make things difficult for these Taiwan compatriots who came to the mainland to develop, then the responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nRegarding the first question, doing a good job of epidemic prevention and control concerns the health and life safety of compatriots on both sides. Recently, the overseas epidemic situation has been complex and severe. To further strengthen epidemic prevention and control and protect the health and life safety of passengers, Shanghai Pudong Airport has adopted new on-board disinfection and epidemic prevention measures for all international routes and for flights on routes involving Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. At present, a Taiwan airline has adjusted some cross-Strait flight arrangements, but overall, the air transport support for Taiwan compatriots returning to Taiwan for the New Year is not affected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the DPP authorities' economic affairs competent authority recently said that for Taiwanese enterprises investing in the mainland that have been approved by the key technology review group, if they plan to sell equity in their mainland business in the future and it involves technology transfer, they must apply in advance for a technology cooperation license. Voices in Taiwan's…","Regarding Taiwan businesses investing in the mainland, the DPP authorities have used all kinds of means to obstruct and restrict them. The move you mentioned is yet another new action by them to make things difficult for Taiwan businesses. Their practices that harm the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses are seen and remembered by Taiwan businesspeople and industrial and commercial circles.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","Taiwan entertainer Wang Leehom recently said he would temporarily step away from the entertainment industry. Will the mainland impose any penalty on him? Will he be placed on the list of disgraced artists?","Our policy of supporting cross-strait cultural exchanges has not changed. For commercial performance activities conducted on the mainland, the relevant departments have consistently managed them in accordance with law and regulations, in order to guide more culturally healthy and uplifting products into the market. At the same time, we encourage and support performers to consciously uphold professional conduct and ethics, continuously improve their ideological and moral cultivation, professional ethics, and humanistic and artistic refinement, establish a good public image, and become cultural workers who are both virtuous and talented.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland's “Measures for the Administration of Performance Brokers” apply to residents of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. However, for Taiwan residents, if they are harassed by the DPP authorities for supporting the mainland's Constitution or complying with relevant regulations, it will cause trouble. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Both our Constitution and Taiwan's relevant regulations uphold one China. What is the conflict? As for the political differences across the Taiwan Strait, we can fully seek common ground while setting aside differences, so as to achieve commonality and reduce divergence. The key issue is that the DPP authorities should not do things that make things difficult for Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Reports say that the Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Factory's applications to the General Administration of Customs of the mainland for a new import registration number were rejected twice. A Taiwan public representative believes the failure to pass the application may be due to political factors or incomplete information. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","To implement the Food Safety Law and its implementing regulations, among other provisions, the General Administration of Customs organized the revision of the original rules on registration management of overseas manufacturers of imported food. In April this year it issued the Provisions on the Registration Management of Overseas Manufacturers of Imported Food (General Administration of Customs Order No. 248), which took effect on January 1, 2022. These registration provisions optimize the registration procedures, implement categorized management for different types of overseas manufacturers, clarify the primary responsibility of enterprises and the regulatory responsibility of the competent authorities at their locations, and refine the applicable scenarios of the provisions. The General Administration of Customs has notified this in accordance with relevant WTO rules, and has notified the Taiwan side of relevant matters and requirements through the contact channel of the Cross-Strait Agreement on Cooperation on Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection.\nIt is understood that alcohol products are registered by their manufacturers by submitting application documents directly to the General Administration of Customs. The relevant manufacturers have promptly corrected and supplemented their application materials in accordance with the rules, and the relevant business departments will handle them in accordance with law and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","We note that Taiwan entertainer Fang Fang recorded a video stating that she has already obtained a Taiwan residence permit on the mainland, and wished the motherland peace, which drew likes from mainland netizens. This is another well-known Taiwan entertainer, after Qian Baihui, to publicly state that she has obtained a Taiwan residence permit. How does the spokesperson view this phenomenon?","Since its launch, the Taiwan residence permit has been widely welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots. It provides equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots living and working on the mainland and enjoying basic public services. As our policies are implemented and the document's validity continues to be strengthened, more and more Taiwan compatriots have applied for residence permits. We are deeply gratified by this phenomenon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","We noted that Taiwan media recently reported that the mainland officially announced it would continue to implement ECFA from January 1, 2022. Please confirm.","Since the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait was signed and implemented, it has brought real and tangible benefits to enterprises and people on both sides. By the end of 2020, Taiwan enterprises had enjoyed cumulative tariff reductions of about 7 billion U.S. dollars. I would like to stress again that we are willing to make the greatest efforts to benefit compatriots on both sides. However, whether the well-being and interests of Taiwan compatriots can be guaranteed and enhanced depends critically on compatriots on both sides uniting, firmly opposing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and jointly safeguarding the peaceful and stable development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","According to reports, after the Wang Leehom incident, he was accused of involvement in marketing, screen control and manipulation of public opinion, and online commentary on the mainland pointed out that “Wang Leehom’s luxurious presence on the mainland has basically ended.” Is this also the official attitude?","One should not take individuals’ statements online as official positions. We have always supported and encouraged cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation. Regarding individual incidents and circumstances involving certain individuals, we hope that performing artists who come to the mainland to develop will all achieve both moral integrity and artistic excellence (德艺双馨). We place greater importance on public morality than on some other statements online.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The spokesperson just called on the DPP authorities to stop interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. In 2019, the mainland suspended the pilot program for individual tourist travel to Taiwan by residents of 47 cities. When will it be lifted?","The answer to who is obstructing cross-Strait exchanges is very clear, and we have explained the reasons many times.\nBefore 2016, cross-Strait relations had a situation of peaceful development, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait enjoyed the benefits of peaceful development across a very wide range. After the DPP came to power, it refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China principle, unilaterally undermined the political foundation of mutual trust and interaction across the Strait, and in recent times has continuously engaged in “Taiwan independence” provocations, seriously worsening the situation in cross-Strait relations. Under these circumstances, the willingness of mainland residents to travel to Taiwan has decreased, which is entirely understandable.\nI must point out that since the outbreak of the 2020 epidemic, the DPP authorities have unilaterally suspended normal exchanges by mainland residents to Taiwan. For example, some personnel of mainland enterprises cannot rotate normally, and mainland journalists who have colleagues in Taiwan and mainland reporters stationed in Taiwan still cannot fully rotate normally. This is clearly caused by artificial political manipulation by the DPP authorities. We once again call on the DPP authorities to lift these unreasonable restrictions, and they must do so.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","彭博社记者","Data released by Taiwan shows that in 2021, nearly 950 sorties of PLA military aircraft entered Taiwan's “defense identification zone” for exercises and drills, far exceeding the 380 sorties in 2020. What does the spokesperson predict for exercises and drills in the Taiwan Strait area next year?","Next year, the situation in the Taiwan Strait will become even more complex and severe, and it cannot be ruled out that our struggle against the DPP authorities' provocative pursuit of “independence” and external forces' interference may become even sharper and more intense. We firmly believe that we always hold the dominant position and initiative. Our policy is very clear: we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts. But if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke, force us, or even cross the red line, we will have to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2021-12-29","Ma Xiaoguang","东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je recently said that he can cooperate with everyone, but if one does not take the right stance, one will be labeled a “fellow traveler of the CCP.” Indeed, “opposing whatever China says” has now become the “main theme” of the DPP authorities. Faced with this situation, how will the mainland strengthen cross-strait exchanges and mutual trust?","The actions of the DPP authorities across the Taiwan Strait have turned what Mr. Ko Wen-je once called “building walls” into arbitrary incitement of “confrontation.” They everywhere manufacture “anti-China and China-hatred” and “oppose anything Chinese” political populism, fabricate various false information to attack and smear the mainland, readily label people on the island with “red hats,” indiscriminately wield the power of “green terror,” and create a chilling effect of “those who comply prosper, those who oppose perish,” all in service of their provocations to seek “independence.” They think they have succeeded, but the vast majority of Taiwan's people are not “A-Dou,” and one day they will erupt in silence. As exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait expand and integrated development deepens, the political theatrics manipulated by the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces will inevitably turn to ash.\nDear media friends, “Heavenly seasons and human affairs press on day by day; with the Winter Solstice, yang returns and spring comes again.” In just two days it will be the New Year's Day of 2022. Here, on behalf of the Information Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, I sincerely thank you all for your support of our work over the past year, and I earnestly wish all of you good fortune and prosperity in the new year. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202112/t20211229_12398843.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2021-12-30","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, the Japanese and Australian governments are in consultations on revising the Japan-Australia Joint Declaration on Security Cooperation signed in 2007 to strengthen joint efforts to deal with China, including responding to a so-called Chinese attack against Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","Hmm, interesting. A slew of reports have emerged about this bilateral declaration that is allegedly under discussion and has yet to be published. I wonder, is this the result of poor management of confidential information by government departments of relevant countries, or is the information deliberately released to “set the tempo”?\nWe believe that no bilateral arrangement should target any third party, and we firmly oppose any collusion that undermines China’s interests and regional peace and stability.\nWhat we need in the Pacific is the joint efforts of countries in the region to uphold peace, not attempts to drum up the so-called “threat” theories or stir up trouble. All moves against the tide are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347195.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211230_10477521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，中共中央总书记、国家主席、中央军委主席习近平在出席中央军委人才工作会议时强调，聚焦实现建军一百年奋斗目标，深入实施新时代人才强军战略。请发言人进一步介绍有关情况。","At a regular press conference of China’s Ministry of National Defense on June 30, spokesperson Tan Kefei stated that China solemnly warns the US that any attempt to “use Taiwan to contain China” or to help Taiwan “use force to resist reunification” is doomed to fail.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the US and Taiwan recently held the so-called annual “national security dialogue” and the military security conference “Monterey Talks,” discussing US arms and other military support for Taiwan, helping Taiwan enhance its “asymmetric warfare” capabilities, and plans to strengthen cooperation with Taiwan through the US National Guard’s “State Partnership Program.” What is your comment on this?\nTan Kefei pointed out that the Taiwan question has always been the most important and sensitive core issue in China-US relations, and mishandling it will have a subversive impact on China-US relations. President Biden clearly made a commitment to China that the US “does not support ‘Taiwan independence,’” but the US’s actions run counter to this statement. This is support for and indulgence of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, is of a vile nature, and has an extremely bad impact.\nTan Kefei said that China solemnly warns the US that any attempt to “use Taiwan to contain China” or to help Taiwan “use force to resist reunification” is doomed to fail. China urges the US side to abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military collusion, and stop all forms of official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan. China will continue to take resolute and forceful measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nAnother reporter asked: Some media speculate that the Japanese government may soon dispatch active-duty civilian officials of the Ministry of Defense to be stationed permanently in Taiwan. What is China’s comment on this?\n“China firmly opposes Japan conducting any form of official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan under any pretext. We have expressed serious concern to the Japanese side on this matter and demanded that Japan provide a responsible clarification,” Tan Kefei said.\nTan Kefei pointed out that the Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty, territorial integrity, and core interests, and is a major principled issue that bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations. Japan has clearly stated in the four China-Japan political documents that it recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, fully understands and respects the Chinese government’s position that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China,” and maintains only unofficial and regional exchanges with Taiwan.\nThis spokesperson also said that if Japan insists on stirring up trouble, attempts to make a breakthrough in its relations with Taiwan, or even meddles in the highly sensitive field of military security, it will cause serious consequences. China urges Japan not to send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces in any form, not to interfere in China’s internal affairs in any form, and to do more things that help promote China-Japan political mutual trust and regional peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","美国当地时间12月27日，美总统签署“2022年国防授权法案”，其中包括多项涉华内容，请问发言人对此有何评论？","According to the Ministry of National Defense website, Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters' questions on the 8th about a US congressional visit to Taiwan, saying the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Reunification of the motherland must be realized, and interference by external forces will never succeed.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, US Republican Senator Scott of Florida recently visited Taiwan. What is your comment?\nWu Qian said that this move by the US seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously undermines the political foundation of China-US relations, seriously damages China-US military-to-military relations, and aggravates tensions and escalation in the Taiwan Strait region. China firmly opposes it. In response to the vicious acts of US-Taiwan collusion and provocation, the Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People's Liberation Army recently organized multi-service joint combat readiness patrols and actual-combat drills in the sea and airspace around Taiwan island.\nWu Qian pointed out that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Reunification of the motherland must be realized, and interference by external forces will never succeed. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is on full-time standby, ready to fight at any time. It will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","今年以来，全球新冠肺炎疫情持续蔓延，百年未有之大变局深入演进，面对复杂多变的国际局势，中国军队积极开展国际军事合作，取得丰硕成果。《解放军报》12月23日刊文回顾了本年度中国军队国际军事合作亮点活动。请发言人进一步介绍有关情况。","Tan Kefei, spokesperson of the Chinese Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters' questions on the evening of the 18th regarding U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. He said that China firmly opposes them and demands that the United States immediately revoke the above arms sales plan and halt all arms sales to Taiwan and all U.S.-Taiwan military contacts. Otherwise, the responsibility for undermining China-U.S. relations between the two militaries and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will rest entirely with the United States.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the Defense Security Cooperation Agency of the U.S. Department of Defense recently announced that the U.S. State Department has approved the sale to Taiwan of military technical assistance worth about US$108 million, to strengthen so-called U.S.-Taiwan military cooperation and enhance Taiwan's capacity to respond to “threats.” What is your comment?\nTan Kefei pointed out that the U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region of China seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué; they crudely interfere in China's internal affairs, seriously harm China's sovereignty and security interests, and gravely undermine China-U.S. relations between the two militaries. China firmly opposes this.\nTan Kefei said that the Taiwan question concerns China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity and involves China's core interests. Recently, the U.S. side has repeatedly made “four noes and one no intention” commitments to China, clearly stating that it does not support “Taiwan independence,” but on the issue of arms sales to Taiwan, its words and deeds are inconsistent and it is utterly lacking in credibility. China demands that the United States immediately revoke the above arms sales plan and halt all arms sales to Taiwan and all U.S.-Taiwan military contacts. Otherwise, the responsibility for undermining China-U.S. relations between the two militaries and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will rest entirely with the United States.\n“It must be emphasized that the future of Taiwan and the security, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots cannot be bought. The DPP authorities and the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces, who seek to rely on the United States to bolster themselves and ‘use force to seek independence,’ are only quenching thirst with poison,” the spokesperson said. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely thwart any form of interference by external forces and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","美军印太总部近日发表声明称，印太总部、太平洋舰队及太平洋空军代表近日同中国人民解放军海、空军代表以视频方式举行美中海上军事安全磋商机制（MMCA）工作组和海军将领年度会议。美国防部发言人认为，美中之间的军事接触对于降低误判风险十分重要。请发言人进一步介绍此次会议有关情况。","According to a message released on the official WeChat account of the Ministry of National Defense, Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters’ questions on the 26th about the 2022 edition of the Defense White Paper adopted by the Japanese government. He said that the content of the 2022 edition of the Japanese Defense White Paper concerning China disregards facts and is full of prejudice. He demanded that Japan face up to and reflect on its history of aggression and stop disguising itself as a victim to confuse international public opinion.\nA reporter asked: On July 22, the Japanese government adopted the 2022 edition of the Defense White Paper, which says that China’s national defense policy and military buildup “lack transparency,” and that China is attempting to unilaterally change the status quo in the East China Sea and South China Sea. The white paper also significantly increases content concerning Taiwan. What is your comment on this?\nWu Qian pointed out that the content of the 2022 edition of the Japanese Defense White Paper concerning China disregards facts and is full of prejudice. It makes baseless remarks about China’s national defense and military buildup and normal military activities, deliberately exaggerates the so-called “China military threat,” grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, and creates tension in the regional situation. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this, and has made solemn representations to Japan.\nWu Qian stressed that China unswervingly follows the path of peaceful development and pursues a defensive national defense policy and an active defense military strategy. China strengthens its national defense and military buildup in order to defend its national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and to better provide public security goods to the international community. History has proven and will continue to prove that the Chinese military has always been a firm force for safeguarding world peace. By contrast, Japan not only fails to reflect on and learn from its history, but instead keeps using China as an excuse. It deliberately plans to revise the pacifist constitution, sharply increases defense spending, develops offensive combat capabilities, and attempts to break through the postwar international order. This has aroused serious concern and high vigilance in the international community, including China.\nWu Qian said that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will not forget that Japan once forcibly seized Taiwan by means of aggressive war, and its colonial crimes are too numerous to recount, leaving it with an inescapable historical responsibility to the Chinese people. Japan’s use of the Defense White Paper to meddle in the Taiwan question seriously violates the basic norms of international relations, betrays Japan’s solemn commitments to China on the Taiwan question, undermines the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and intensifies tensions in the Taiwan Strait area. This is entirely wrong and very dangerous. The Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands are China’s inherent territory. China’s patrols and law enforcement in the waters of the Diaoyu Islands are justified and lawful, and Japan has no right to make irresponsible remarks. China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands and the waters adjacent to them, and has consistently respected and upheld the freedom of navigation and overflight that countries enjoy in the South China Sea under international law. Japan is not a party to the South China Sea issue. Its sowing discord, dancing to the tune of the United States, and stirring up trouble on the South China Sea issue are driven by ulterior motives and are irresponsible. The Chinese military has the determination, capability, and confidence to defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity, to safeguard national maritime rights and interests, and to maintain regional peace and stability.\n“We demand that Japan face up to and reflect on its history of aggression, stop disguising itself as a victim to confuse international public opinion, stop its wrong words and deeds on relevant issues, and earnestly win the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community with a responsible attitude and practical actions,” Wu Qian said.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，中越“和平救援-2021”卫勤联合演习近期在越南广宁省芒街市顺利举行。请发言人进一步介绍此次演习的有关情况和主要特点。","According to a report on the website of the Ministry of National Defense, Tan Kefei, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters’ questions on the 26th regarding the planned visit to Taiwan by U.S. House Speaker Pelosi, saying that the Chinese side requires the U.S. side to fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, and not to arrange a visit to Taiwan by Pelosi. If the U.S. side insists on going its own way, the Chinese military will certainly not stand idly by.\nA reporter asked: In response to U.S. House Speaker Pelosi’s plan to visit Taiwan, some media have said that China may take military action in response. What comments does the Chinese military have on this?\nTan Kefei responded: Regarding the planned visit to Taiwan by U.S. House Speaker Pelosi, the Chinese side has repeatedly stated its firm opposition. As the “third-ranking figure” in the U.S. government, if Speaker Pelosi visits Taiwan, it would seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously endanger China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, seriously undermine the political foundation of China-U.S. relations, inevitably cause extremely serious damage to China-U.S. and military-to-military relations, and lead to further escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nTan Kefei pointed out that the Chinese side requires the U.S. side to fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, and not to arrange a visit to Taiwan by Pelosi. If the U.S. side insists on going its own way, the Chinese military will certainly not stand idly by, and will surely take strong measures to thwart any interference by external forces and any schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2021-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，民进党当局近期频繁炒作所谓“大陆威胁”，宣称今年以来大陆军机940余架次进入台湾“空域”，是2019、2020年度总和的两倍。另外，美国防部官员称，中国大陆在台湾周边海空域的行动增加了印太地区武装部队之间误判的可能性，加强台湾“自卫”是一项紧迫任务。请问发言人对此有何评论？","According to the website of the Ministry of National Defense, on the afternoon of July 28, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference. Wu Qian, Senior Colonel, Director of the News Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and its spokesperson, answered reporters' questions, saying: \"The people support the military, and the military cherishes the people.\" The broad masses of officers and soldiers have always cherished the honor bestowed upon them by the Party and the people. On the battlefield, in disaster areas, and on the borders, in the places where the motherland and the people most need us, we will likewise take the lead and charge to the front.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, as of the end of June this year, all transport airports nationwide had opened lawful priority passages for military personnel. Please further introduce the relevant situation and next steps.\nWu Qian said that the report of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China pointed out that military personnel should become an occupation respected by all of society. Opening lawful priority passages for military personnel at civil aviation airports is an important part of implementing the instructions of Chairman Xi on building the honor system for military personnel; it is a good thing for military-civilian cooperation to improve the quality of services for the military, and also a practical measure by the civil aviation system to support national defense construction and sincerely serve the troops and officers and soldiers.\nWu Qian introduced that since 2017, military and civilian transport and delivery departments have fully advanced the work of lawful priority for military personnel, from pilot implementation at Chengdu Shuangliu Airport first, to comprehensive rollout at 81 key airports, and then to full coverage of all transport airports nationwide. Work procedures have been consolidated and optimized, cooperation models have been improved and perfected, and service quality has continuously increased. This has provided maximum convenience for officers and soldiers and their families when traveling, fully reflecting the concern and care of Chairman Xi and the Central Military Commission for the troops, and comprehensively enhancing military personnel's sense of mission, honor, and gain. It has become a warm-hearted project that benefits the military and encourages soldiers, and a demonstration project for civil aviation's support of the military. Going forward, relevant functional departments of the military and civilian sectors will continue to advance the upgraded version of lawful priority for military personnel, innovate and improve work content and support models, and push priority and quality service to expand toward preferential treatment and benefits, so that military personnel and accompanying family members enjoy more convenient, considerate, and warm services. At the same time, we will educate the broad masses of officers and soldiers to support, understand, and make good use of policies, and to maintain the good image of military personnel.\nWu Qian said: The people support the military, and the military cherishes the people. The broad masses of officers and soldiers have always cherished the honor bestowed upon them by the Party and the people. On the battlefield, in disaster areas, and on the borders, in the places where the motherland and the people most need us, we will likewise take the lead and charge to the front.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10119551.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2021-12-31","Zhao Lijian","Macau Monthly","Lithuanian Prime Minister Ingrida Šimonytė recently said that China imposed inappropriate pressure on Lithuania after the establishment of the “Taiwanese Representative Office” in Lithuania, which doesn’t deserve such a reaction. Do you have any comment?","The Lithuanian government blatantly violated the one-China principle and renounced the political commitment made by the Lithuanian side in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations with China. Of all countries having diplomatic relations with China, Lithuania is the only one to allow the Taiwan authorities to set up a “representative office” bearing the name of Taiwan, which creates the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. This erroneous act severely infringed upon China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and gravely hurt China’s core interests. China has every right to make legitimate and reasonable responses. If such things were to happen to other sovereign and independent countries, they would surely take resolute and decisive measures, too. The Lithuanian side was in the wrong. However, instead of reflecting on itself and showing remorse, it resorted to spreading rumor and making trouble. Such publicity stunts of glossing over the real issue to deflect attention elsewhere are just pathetic.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211231_10478030.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-31","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","Taiwan’s authorities in charge of foreign affairs said Nicaragua seized Taiwan’s “diplomatic property” and Taiwan will pursue international legal proceedings. The authorities also criticized the mainland for illegally snatching property in a rude manner together with Nicaragua. Do you have any comment?","I stated China’s position on relevant issues earlier. You may refer to that. I want to stress that the Taiwan authorities attempt to give away China’s state assets to others for ulterior purposes. This trick is illegal, null and void. The so-called “international proceedings” they clamor for has no legal basis and is flat-out fraud that is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211231_10478030.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2021-12-31","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","The “foreign affairs department” of the Taiwan region on December 30 praised the foreign ministers of the US, the UK, France and Germany for speaking out in support of Lithuania and called on democratic partners around the world to stand in solidarity with Lithuania against China’s diplomatic and economic threats. What is the foreign ministry’s comment on this?","Lithuania openly challenged the one-China principle and created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”. It is Lithuania that made serious mistakes in its relations with China first. China has been compelled to take legitimate and reasonable countermeasures. That the US and relevant countries know very well. If they really care for Lithuania, they should urge it to admit and correct its mistakes as soon as possible, instead of using it as a tool to contain China, emboldening it to go further down the wrong path and inflicting greater losses on Lithuania and its people.\nAt the same time, we must warn the Taiwan authorities that “Taiwan independence” leads to a dead end. Attempts to solicit foreign support in seeking “Taiwan independence” and make provocations will never succeed.\n**************************\nIn observance of the 2022 New Year’s Day holiday, our press conference will be in recess on Monday, January 3 and resumed on Tuesday, January 4. During the recess, you may still reach the MFA Spokesperson’s Office via email, fax and WeChat.\nIn 2021, we have witnessed the accelerated evolution of the pandemic and changes unseen in a century. We celebrated the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China (CPC), completed the building of a moderately prosperous society in all respects, historically eliminated absolute poverty, and embarked on a journey toward realizing the second centenary goal of building China into a great modern socialist country in all respects. We have written a splendid chapter in China’s diplomacy, from head-of-state diplomacy to anti-COVID-19 diplomacy, from the Belt and Road Initiative to the Global Development Initiative, and from the return of Meng Wanzhou to the resumption of diplomatic relations between China and Nicaragua.\nIn this year of 2021, the foreign ministry has held 230 regular press conferences and took more than 3,000 questions from the press in total. Official accounts of the foreign ministry have been opened in 17 new media platforms at home and abroad, garnering more than 73 million followers. We launched the “100 CPC Stories in 100 Days” series, which has been read by over one billion people. It’s probably fair to say that 2021 witnessed the steady increase of China’s voice in the world.\nIn the upcoming year of 2022, China will host the Beijing Winter Olympic Games and hold the 20th National Congress of the CPC. We will continue to tell the stories of China, the CPC and the Chinese people, play our part to ensure a successful Beijing Winter Olympics and foster a secure and stable external environment for the 20th National Congress of the CPC. In a nutshell, we will expect more exciting moments in China’s diplomacy in the year to come.\nMy colleagues and I, together with friends from the press, have been part of and witnessed the historic moments of China’s diplomacy in 2021. We’re pleased to see that with your pen and camera, you have reported on China in a more objective and multi-dimensional manner. On behalf of the Information Department of the Foreign Ministry and my colleagues, I would like to take this opportunity to extend my heartfelt thanks to you all for your hard work over the past year, and we are looking forward to more and better stories of China from you. I would also like to thank all friends who have been caring for China’s diplomacy, especially the followers of the MFA Spokesperson’s Office for your “likes” and support.\nI would like to wish you and your family in advance good health, success, happiness and good luck in the upcoming year! As we bid farewell to 2021, let me say this once again: thank you for your hard work. See you next year!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202112/t20211231_10478030.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, January 1 (Xinhua). In response to the New Year's Day address by the leader of the Taiwan region and the remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said: The current tense and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait stems from the refusal of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” their reckless provocations to seek independence, their collusion with external forces to confront the mainland, and their attempt to change the fact that the two sides belong to one China. They repeatedly claim “no provocation,” but in fact, in pursuit of political self-interest, they keep fabricating lies, escalating hostility, and peddling hatred. The so-called “Four Insistences” harbor sinister intentions to split the country. The road of “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and will only push Taiwan into the abyss and bring profound disaster to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian said that realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common wish of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces continue to provoke and coerce, or even cross red lines, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures. The successful practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong cannot be sabotaged by any force through rumors, and the evil conduct of disrupting Hong Kong and seeking independence will never succeed. We sincerely hope that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will work together in harmony, join hands and move forward, jointly oppose the adventurism of “Taiwan independence” and the manipulation by external forces, jointly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and jointly promote the complete reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220101_12399372.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-04","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The South China Morning Post has reported that a Taiwanese company bought a shipment of Lithuanian rum that China would not allow to be imported. This is meant as a way of showing support to the Baltic nation. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this story about the Lithuanian rum?","I’m not aware of the situation you mentioned. I would like to tell you that the Taiwan authorities’ attempt to maintain “the room for Taiwan independence activities” through dollar diplomacy will prove to be all in vain.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347197.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220104_10478763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-04","Wang Wenbin","Macau Monthly","On January 3, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken spoke with foreign ministers of the Bucharest Nine (B9) group over the phone. They highlighted their solidarity with Lithuania in the face of escalating political pressure and economic coercion by China. Do you have any comment?","The ins and outs of the Taiwan-related issues on the part of Lithuania are very clear. Acting in bad faith, Lithuania created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” and undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is the crux of the difficulties in China-Lithuania relations.\nThe US side not only defends Lithuania’s erroneous act of creating the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”, but also attempts to put together a small clique condoning the “Taiwan independence” forces under the pretext of supporting Lithuania. This will only lead the international community to question the US’ sincerity in upholding its one-China policy and its true intention on the Taiwan question. This act of the US will not erode China’s firm determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, but will only send a wrong message to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nWe urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués. We also hope relevant sides can tell right from wrong, uphold an objective and fair position and avoid being misled and misguided by the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347197.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220104_10478763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 4 — The DPP authorities and some of their prominent figures have made wild remarks about the recent law enforcement actions by the HKSAR government and police against Stand News, attacking and smearing “one country, two systems.” Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded on the 4th in response to an inquiry: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that the black hand interfering in Hong Kong affairs will be cut off, and the crimes of disrupting Hong Kong and seeking “independence” will surely be settled.\nShe also said: The HKSAR government handles relevant cases in accordance with law, and we firmly support it. No one has the right to interfere.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out: For the purpose of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities have continuously meddled in Hong Kong affairs. At present, the situation in Hong Kong has turned from chaos to order and is back on track, and “one country, two systems” is showing strong vitality and a bright future. The DPP authorities are eager to jump out and make a fuss, for fear that Taiwan residents will see through the truth of their plot to disrupt Hong Kong and seek “independence.” They smear “one country, two systems,” peddle a false “democracy,” pose as “guardians of democracy,” distort right and wrong, disregard the judiciary, defend illegal acts, and even clamor about a so-called “Hong Kong aid plan.” More and more people on the island see through them: they merely seek personal political gain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220104_12399767.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-05","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Lithuanian President said on January 4 that the government’s decision to allow Taiwan to open a representative office under the name of Taiwan was a mistake. The Taiwan authorities said Lithuania is facing comprehensive pressure from China and Taiwan strongly condemns that and firmly supports Lithuania. Do you have any comment?","Recognizing one’s mistake is a step in the right direction, but it is more important to take actions to redress the erroneous act of creating the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” and come back onto the track of upholding the one-China principle.\nI also want to point out that the ins and outs of how China-Lithuania relations encountered setbacks are very clear. Looking for excuses for one’s erroneous act does not help to solve the problem or improve China-Lithuania relations.\nWe also have this stern warning for the Taiwan authorities that seeking “Taiwan independence” and secession is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347198.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220105_10479124.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-06","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US and Lithuania have agreed to cooperate on ways to counter what they call China’s “economic coercion.” In addition, Taiwan pledged to establish a $200 million fund to invest in Lithuania and open up its markets to the nation. Does the foreign ministry have any comment? Just to follow up on Kazakhstan, does China support the CSTO’s effort and is Beijing considering its own contribution to this effort?","You just mentioned “coercion”. The first thing I want to tell you is that the US fabricates lies and makes trouble with Xinjiang-related issues and pressures multinational companies to take sides. This is nothing if not coercive diplomacy. The ins and outs of the Taiwan-related issues on the part of Lithuania are very clear. The US has repeatedly defended Lithuania’s wrong words and deeds to create the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”, and tried to cobble together a clique that emboldens the “Taiwan independence” forces. These moves further expose the US’ scheme to use Taiwan to contain China, which will only tarnish its international image and be self-defeating.\nWe urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués. We also have this stern warning for the Taiwan authorities. “Dollar diplomacy” cannot change the trend that “Taiwan independence” forces are doomed to collapse and soliciting foreign support for“Taiwan independence”will prove a dead end.\nOn your second question, much has been said about China’s position. We hope the situation can be stabilized soon and public order restored.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347199.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220106_10479459.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-07","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The defense and foreign ministers of the US and Japan met today and expressed concern about actions by China. They said they are resolved to work together to respond to “destabilizing” activities by China. Does the foreign ministry have a comment?","We have noticed that the US, Japan and Australia pointed fingers at China’s internal affairs during their relevant talks and consultations yesterday and today. I want to stress that China’s position on the Taiwan question and issues related to the South and East China Sea, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are clear and consistent. We deplore and reject the US, Japan and Australia’s gross interference in China’s internal affairs, fabrication of lies to smear China and sabotage of solidarity and mutual trust among regional countries, and have lodged solemn representations with relevant countries.\nTo defend peace, stability and development in East Asia and the Asia-Pacific, we need to uphold true multilateralism, respect the open and inclusive framework of regional cooperation that was formed over the years, and embark on the path of solidarity, dialogue and cooperation. While professing “free, open, and inclusive”, the US, Japan and Australia are ganging up to form a clique targeting other countries in practice and flexing muscles for military intimidation. This runs counter to the trend of peace and development in the region, and contradicts their self-claimed “opposition to pressure and coercion”. The international community sees this very clearly.\nThe current priority for the US, Japan and Australia should be earnestly fulfilling their due international responsibilities. We urge countries concerned to stop the AUKUS nuclear submarine cooperation plan, stop advancing the discharge of the Fukushima nuclear contaminated water into the Pacific, stop denying and whitewashing the history of militarist aggression and seeking the status of a military power by hyping up the situation of the neighborhood, and stop stoking division and confrontation between regional countries. They should be contributors to regional peace, stability and development, rather than troublemakers that spread lies and create obstacles.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347201.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220107_10479922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-07","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","China fined 7-Eleven Beijing for identifying Taiwan as an “independent state” on its website. Do you have a comment on this?","I am not aware of the situation you mentioned. I want to tell you that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the one-China principle is a widely-recognized norm governing international relations and the broad consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347201.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220107_10479922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 7 — The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently released a so-called “situation analysis” report on Macau, making irresponsible remarks on Macau affairs and maliciously attacking “one country, two systems.” In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 7th when asked: We warn the DPP authorities that we will never allow anyone to interfere in Macau affairs or to plot “independence,” we will never allow political manipulation of Macau affairs, and any act of plotting “independence” will be severely punished according to law.\nZhu Fenglian said that since Macau’s return to the motherland 22 years ago, “one country, two systems” has been successfully implemented in Macau, with clean politics, social stability, economic development and improved livelihoods, which the whole world can see. The DPP authorities, driven by their intention to pursue “independence,” are afraid precisely of the success of “one country, two systems” in Macau; they are afraid that more and more Taiwan compatriots will see the strong vitality of “one country, two systems” and its positive role in advancing national reunification; they are afraid that the “Taiwan independence” lie will completely collapse in the face of facts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220107_12400453.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-10","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","On January 7, US Trade Representative Katherine Tai spoke with European Commission Executive Vice President Valdis Dombrovskis over the phone and expressed the US’ strong support for the EU and for Lithuania in the face of economic coercion from China. Do you have any response?","Speaking of coercion, we should look at what the US did: The US government forced the military government of Haiti to step down in 1994, and referred to that as “a textbook example of coercive diplomacy”; in 2003, it explicitly characterized the $30.3 billion additional military expenses for “coercive diplomacy” as incurred expenses; it spared no effort to crack down on its competitors like Alstom and Toshiba and coerced the TSMC, Samsung and other companies to provide to the US chip supply chain data. This is flat-out “blackmail diplomacy”. Its attempt to misrepresent China’s legitimate measures to uphold national sovereignty as “coercion” only serves to reveal how hypocritical and deceptive the US’ “discourse bullying” is.\nLithuania violated its political commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties with the People’s Republic of China and created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. These facts are indisputable. Visionary people in Lithuania criticized these acts. The US instigated the Lithuanian authorities to undermine the one-China principle from the outset and then supported, aided and abetted them. The US tries to seek political calculation aimed at using Taiwan to contain China at the expense of Lithuania’s interests.\nWe urge the Lithuanian side to correct the mistake and not to be a pawn for anti-China forces. We also warn the US side that playing the Taiwan card is counterproductive and will get itself burnt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347202.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220110_10480649.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-11","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Taiwan and Canada held exploratory discussions about ways to boost trade ties, which is Taipei’s latest move to reduce economic reliance on China’s mainland. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","China opposes official contact and agreement of official nature between countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region. This position is clear and consistent. The Canadian government should abide by the one-China principle, and prudently and properly handle relevant issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347203.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220111_10481018.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-11","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","According to reports, Lithuania’s shadow cabinet issued a statement that said it hopes Lithuania-China relations can be normalized, and recognizes Taiwan as an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. It expects the Lithuanian government to redress its mistakes and rename the “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania” to “Taipei Representative Office”. What is your comment?","I have noted relevant reports. The ins and outs of the problems in China-Lithuania relations are very clear. The Lithuanian government acted in bad faith, and disregarded the overall interests of the bilateral ties and the interests of the country and the people, thus inviting wide suspicion and opposition at home and abroad. We urge the Lithuanian government to correct the mistakes, stop acting as a pawn for the “Taiwan independence” forces and anti-China forces, make choices in line with its own interests and basic norms governing international relations, and return to the right track of adhering to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347203.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220111_10481018.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-12","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Taiwan plans to open a $1 billion fund for joint projects between Lithuania and Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","The one-China principle is an invincible trend with strong popular support. The Taiwan authorities’ attempts to expand space for “Taiwan independence” activities with “dollar diplomacy” are futile and bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347204.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220112_10481425.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on January 12, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome, everyone, to the first press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office in 2022. There is a lot to do in the new year. We hope to work together with all of you to help people on both sides of the Strait gain a deeper understanding of the central government’s policies toward Taiwan, and a more comprehensive understanding of the efforts and work of all regions and departments to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and to advance the process of national reunification. Now, please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed in his 2022 New Year’s message that realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In his speech at the New Year tea reception of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, he stressed that we adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” strengthen the…","On the eve of the New Year, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a New Year's message and an important speech at the New Year tea party of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference. In these remarks, he reviewed the achievements of the work on Taiwan over the past year, set out the goals and tasks for resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland, and expressed his earnest hope that all Chinese people will join hands and move forward together to create a better future for the Chinese nation. He pointed out the direction for cross-Strait relations in the new year.\nWe will, in accordance with the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech, fully implement the overall strategy of the Party for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, firmly curb interference by external forces, continuously promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, bravely explore new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, actively guide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to integrate into the new development paradigm, continuously improve policy measures that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they receive equal treatment on the mainland, and work hard to promote heartfelt connection between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation. The aspirations of Taiwan compatriots for a better life can only, and will surely, become reality in the national rejuvenation. Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait must work together in harmony, unite and move forward, and strive for the lofty cause of completing the reunification of the motherland and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401173.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","In his New Year message, Director Liu Jieyi revealed the broad prospects for Taiwan after unification, stating that Taiwan society will no longer be disturbed by “unification” and “independence” disputes and can focus on people's livelihood and well-being, doing more good deeds, solving more problems, and doing more practical things for the people. How should this be understood?","At the end of last year, Taiwan residents chose \"homebound\" (宅) and \"difficult\" (难) as the representative Chinese characters of 2021, expressing their dissatisfaction with the status quo in Taiwan and their worries about the future. As 2022 arrived, many Taiwan residents were interviewed on the streets and expressed their expectations and wishes for the new year. Some hoped that prices would stop rising, so that ordinary people's life burdens would be lighter and their days would be easier. Some hoped that the epidemic would ease, that mainland tourists would return, and that cross-Strait tourism would develop well. Some worried about employment and were considering going to the mainland, where there are more opportunities, to look for work. Still others hoped that 2022 would bring favorable weather, that there would be no more water shortages, and that there would be no more power outages or brownouts. We deeply empathize with the New Year wishes of Taiwan residents.\nDirector Liu Jieyi issued a New Year message on January 2 on behalf of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. He extended New Year greetings and sincere regards to the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan, explained that national reunification is an irresistible historical trend, that Taiwan's future and the well-being of its compatriots are tied to national reunification, exposed the serious harm of \"Taiwan independence,\" and called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to work together in harmony and unity, jointly contribute to the great cause of national reunification, and share in the glory of national rejuvenation.\nIn the New Year message, Director Liu Jieyi revealed to compatriots in Taiwan the bright prospects of Taiwan after reunification, pointing out that after reunification Taiwan will have a powerful motherland to rely on and will truly enjoy lasting peace, with a more developed economy, a more prosperous culture, a more harmonious society, better improved livelihoods, and greater security and dignity internationally. He emphasized that \"after reunification, Taiwan's society will no longer be disturbed by the 'Taiwan independence' issue and can focus on the well-being of the people, doing more good deeds, solving more difficult problems, and doing more practical things for ordinary people.\" This stands in sharp contrast to the current Democratic Progressive Party authorities, who are engaging in reckless actions that create chaos on the island. \"Taiwan independence\" is the root of the political and social chaos on the island and the greatest threat to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Only by eradicating the root of \"Taiwan independence\" can Taiwan compatriots truly live a good life.\nPeace, development, and a good life are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and the common voice of Taiwan compatriots. The original aspiration and mission of the Communist Party of China is to seek happiness for the Chinese people and rejuvenation for the Chinese nation, so that all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, can live a good life. Under the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China, the Chinese nation has made the great leap from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong. We now have better conditions, greater capability and more confidence to complete the great cause of national reunification and to let compatriots on both sides of the Strait live better lives. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should join hands and move toward the beautiful future of realizing national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401172.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) formally took effect on January 1. What benefits will this bring to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland?","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) Agreement officially took effect on January 1 this year. It is a modern, free, high-quality, and mutually beneficial large-scale regional free trade agreement. It marks the official launch of the free trade area with the largest population, the greatest economic and trade scale, and the greatest development potential in the world. Trade, investment, and other areas among member states will achieve a high level of liberalization and facilitation, injecting strong momentum into the recovery and growth of the regional and global economies. After RCEP takes effect, more than 90% of goods trade within the region will gradually reach zero tariffs, and trade costs and commodity prices will fall substantially. The effects will be especially pronounced in key sectors such as petrochemicals, machinery, textiles, and agriculture.\nTaiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland can fully enjoy the tariff and rules-of-origin preferences of RCEP member states and open up broader markets. At the same time, the combined benefits of various regional development plans on the mainland, policy measures supporting enterprises in integrating into high-quality development, and accelerated reform and opening up will bring greater development space and more opportunities to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. We will, as always, vigorously support Taiwan businesses and enterprises in achieving stable and sound development on the mainland. We welcome more Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest and start businesses on the mainland, and we welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to pursue and realize their dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401170.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The General Administration of Customs recently issued a notice suspending customs clearance for live fish from two aquaculture farms in the Taiwan region. Is this measure targeted at Taiwan's fish farmers?","Xiamen Customs recently detected the banned drugs leucomalachite green and crystal violet in two batches of grouper imported from Taiwan. These two substances can persist in fish bodies and the environment for a long time, posing risks of mutagenicity, teratogenicity and carcinogenicity, and their use is prohibited in aquaculture on both the mainland and in Taiwan. In addition, the two batches of grouper were also found to exceed the limit for the restricted drug oxytetracycline.\nRelevant mainland authorities have suspended, in accordance with law, the import of live fish from two Taiwan aquaculture farms. The purpose is to protect the health and safety of mainland consumers, and it is not targeted at any aquaculture operator. We hope relevant parties in Taiwan will strengthen supervision of the aquaculture process, strengthen guidance for aquaculture operators, and ensure the safety of agricultural and fishery products imported into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401165.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Data released by the DPP authorities' finance department show that in 2021, Taiwan's exports to the mainland amounted to US$188.91 billion, accounting for 42.3%. The mainland has continued to rank as Taiwan's largest export market and largest source of trade surplus, and Taiwan's industrial development and trade prospects increasingly rely on the mainland. However, the DPP authorities are “leaning on foreign…","These data once again prove that Taiwan’s economic growth depends on cross-strait economic and trade cooperation. Only by strengthening cross-strait economic and trade cooperation can Taiwan’s economy develop and Taiwan compatriots benefit more from it. Any practice that interferes with or obstructs cross-strait economic and trade cooperation for political self-interest is unwise and also futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","厦门卫视记者","The DPP authorities recently said that the mainland’s extensive establishment of cross-strait exchange bases is mainly aimed at strengthening Taiwan residents’ cultural and national identification with the mainland. In the post-pandemic era, they may combine online and offline exchange methods to increase “united front propaganda and divisive infiltration” against Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Since 2009, the Taiwan Affairs Office has established 82 cross-Strait exchange bases in 24 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, carrying out exchange activities of diverse forms and rich content to enhance the emotional bonds, kinship, and interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, which have been welcomed by people from all walks of life on both sides. Carrying out exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Taiwan Strait and strengthening compatriots' identity with Chinese culture and the Chinese nation is a natural and righteous good thing; why should the DPP authorities be afraid? The 'Taiwan independence' activities they promote on the island to 'de-Sinicize' and negate Chinese culture, and to stir up ethnic antagonism, are nothing less than 'dividing' Taiwan's society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401171.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The Beijing Winter Olympics is about to open. Could the spokesperson introduce the situation of Taiwan compatriots' participation in the Winter Olympics?","The Beijing Winter Olympics is a grand gathering of global winter sports, a platform where compatriots on both sides of the Strait can join together in the celebration and share the glory, and an important opportunity for compatriots on both sides to move forward together into the future. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to take part in the Beijing Winter Olympics and share in the excitement, glory and joy of the Winter Games.\nRegarding athlete participation, it is understood that Taiwan athletes are expected to compete in speed skating, luge and alpine skiing. We wish them the courage to strive hard and to achieve outstanding results.\nRegarding media coverage, in accordance with the epidemic prevention requirements for this Winter Olympics, 8 reporters from 5 Taiwan media outlets currently stationed in Beijing have registered to take part in the non-accredited reporter coverage of the Winter Olympics. We will cooperate with the Beijing Organizing Committee to provide assistance and convenience to Taiwan reporters covering the Winter Olympics, and we hope that through their reporting, the reporters will bring a splendid sporting feast to compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nRegarding volunteer service, since the global online recruitment of volunteers for the Beijing 2022 Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games was launched on December 5, 2019, Taiwan compatriots on the mainland have actively signed up. More than 30 Taiwan students studying at universities in Beijing have so far been successfully selected as event volunteers, and will take part in service work for the Games in venues such as the Olympic Public Zone, the Main Press Center and the National Stadium, including event services, media operations, sports and transportation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401167.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","东南卫视记者","As the Spring Festival approaches, we note that some localities have begun visiting and extending condolences to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation in detail?","For many years, governments at all levels on the Chinese mainland have shown great concern for and attention to Taiwan compatriots working, studying, and living on the mainland. Every year-end and New Year, they send New Year greetings and Spring Festival blessings to Taiwan compatriots in various ways. Affected by the epidemic, a considerable number of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople will stay on the mainland for the Spring Festival this year. As 2022 approaches, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council sent letters of condolence to the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises and provincial Taiwan associations, extending sincere condolences and holiday wishes to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople. In recent days, localities have put into practice the concept of \"compatriots across the Strait are one family,\" carrying out rich and varied visits and condolence activities into enterprises, factories, and schools, holding discussions and exchanges with Taiwan businesspeople and students, earnestly listening to their opinions and suggestions, and promptly resolving the issues they care about.\nYin Li, Secretary of the CPC Fujian Provincial Committee, conducted an inspection tour in Xiamen and Zhangzhou. During this period, he visited Minnan Normal University to see Taiwan teachers and students studying and working there, encouraging them to integrate their own development into the school and the local community, to \"be masters, not guests,\" and to use their own experiences and feelings to inspire more Taiwan youth to come and pursue and realize their dreams.\nRelevant responsible persons from the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the CPC Beijing Municipal Committee visited Peking University and Xicheng District to call on and extend condolences to Taiwan youth and students, encouraging them to integrate into Beijing's development, to release their youthful dreams in the vivid practice of realizing the Chinese Dream, and to not waste their youth or the times.\nRelevant responsible persons from the Guangdong Provincial Committee visited and extended condolences to Taiwan compatriots in Guangzhou, encouraging Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople to actively devote themselves to the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area and to realize their personal ideals.\nThe Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office held a Spring Festival tea gathering for Sichuan-Taiwan teachers and students at Sichuan Agricultural University, extending New Year's greetings to Taiwan teachers and students in Sichuan and encouraging them to serve as bridges for deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to play a greater role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges.\nShanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, and other places arranged visits and condolence activities for Taiwan compatriots and their relatives. Through activities such as \"Staying at School for the New Year, School Sends Blessings,\" they ensured that Taiwan students staying at school for the New Year would enjoy undiminished happiness and festive atmosphere. For those unable to visit in person due to the epidemic, condolence letters and gifts were mailed instead to deliver care and concern to Taiwan compatriots. Many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople said they felt care like that of family and warmth like that of kin.\nAt present, related visit and condolence activities are still ongoing. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in various places can enjoy a joyous and peaceful Spring Festival holiday.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401169.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The DPP authorities recently launched a so-called “special fund” for investment in Lithuania, and said, “We believe that deepening cooperation between Taiwan and Lithuania will certainly produce many success stories.” What comments does the spokesperson have?","There is only one China in the world, and adhering to the one-China principle is a recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The Lithuanian government should fully recognize its error and take concrete action to promptly correct its wrongful act of creating “one China, one Taiwan,” stop supporting and condoning the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, and return to the track of one China. The DPP authorities' attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The DPP authorities recently held, in a high-profile manner, a so-called simulated street fighting exercise targeting the PLA, and subsequently the United States and Japan announced they had reached a so-called major defense cooperation agreement on “protecting Taiwan.” Public opinion holds that Taiwan’s collusion with the United States and Japan will not affect the general trend toward China’s reunification and…","The DPP authorities are accustomed to using political manipulation to create and reinforce on the island the illusion that “if there is trouble in the Taiwan Strait, the US will surely help.” In fact, people on the island are well aware that what the US truly cares about is only meeting US needs and serving US interests, and that the US will never take Taiwan's interests or the Taiwan people seriously. The doom of “Taiwan independence” is an irreversible historical trend. The DPP authorities' attempt to collude with external forces to “seek independence by force” will absolutely not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401163.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the DPP authorities added “Taiwan” in parentheses after the English name of their so-called “Constitutional Court,” and later revised and deleted it. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, have repeatedly played vile tricks and “small maneuvers,” which has provoked widespread dissatisfaction and criticism in Taiwan society. Recently, they again high-handedly manipulated the so-called “constitutional amendment” issue during the interim session of the Legislative Yuan, attempting to lower the threshold for “constitutional amendment” to open a convenient door for “independence.” We firmly oppose this. We hope responsible political parties and groups on the island and the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will remain highly vigilant, will not be dragged step by step onto the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and will not allow the very few parties on the island seeking political self-interest to push Taiwan into a dangerous abyss. Join us in jointly opposing any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401164.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's legislature passed a draft amendment to some provisions of the “Organic Act of the National Communications Commission.” Some public opinion on the island holds that the DPP authorities pushed this through in order to provide convenience for the “East Court” and the cyber army. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities have long manipulated the media, kept internet armies, attacked dissenters, and woven lies to deceive the public, and now they are going further by amending bad laws in an attempt to further muzzle public opinion. Public opinion on the island is already highly doubtful. Does this mean that from now on, Taiwan can only have one voice?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The U.S.-Japan “2+2” meeting of foreign and defense ministers maliciously played up the “China threat theory” and blatantly hyped Taiwan Strait issues. Some experts believe the United States and Japan are moving their Taiwan Strait policy toward operational implementation. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, brooks no foreign interference, no external forces' finger-pointing, and no country taking any action that undermines China's sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related matters, and stop sending any erroneous signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities' attempts to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Sun Yafu, Vice Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said in a recent interview that the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China may put forward some new propositions and arrangements, which would have a positive impact on promoting work toward Taiwan and the situation in the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","This year is an important year as we embark on a new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country and marching toward the second centenary goal. The Communist Party of China will convene its 20th National Congress, a major event in the political life of the Party and the state. We will thoroughly implement the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Central Committee on Taiwan-related work. We will firmly crush “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, firmly oppose interference by external forces, continue to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, steadily advance the process of national reunification, and strive to create a favorable environment in the Taiwan Strait for comprehensively building a modern socialist country and realizing the second centenary goal, so as to welcome the successful convening of the 20th National Congress of the Party with outstanding achievements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The General Administration of Customs recently issued a notice suspending customs declarations for live fish from two aquaculture farms in Taiwan region. Has the TAO received clarification materials from the two Taiwan operators? Has the Taiwan side provided assistance with the follow-up investigation? Second question: We note that when the mainland issued a warning notice regarding South Korean…","The first question concerns the suspension of customs declarations for live fish from two Taiwanese aquaculture farms. Under the Cross-Strait Agreement on Cooperation in Inspection and Quarantine of Agricultural Products, the General Administration of Customs has already notified the Taiwan side through liaison channels and made its requests.\nThe second question: there is absolutely no meaning of “killing the chicken to scare the monkey.” The mainland side's issuance of a warning notice on strengthening inspection and quarantine of live fish exported from Taiwan to the mainland is a reasonable and legitimate measure. It aims to protect consumer health and safety, and also to ensure the normal conduct of cross-Strait agricultural product trade.\nThe third question: the music video “We Sing the Same Song” was produced and released by Taihai Voice and Kan Taihai. I have listened to it several times and strongly agree with a comment from a Taiwanese netizen that it is “a New Year's gift” from musicians on both sides of the Strait to everyone. The song is set against the backdrop of three siblings from Taiwan who used half a genealogy record to search for their ancestral home in Fujian. Musicians on both sides of the Strait created and performed it with care and feeling, fully displaying the longing of Taiwan compatriots for their homeland and reunion, and the blood ties of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. “On the road to find our roots, you and I in dialogue, crossing the Strait, the two sides have always been one family.” Through this song, we hope compatriots across the Taiwan Strait will not only sing together, but also seek their roots together and strive together.\nAs for the song being attacked in Taiwan by some “green media” and “cyber army” accounts, we believe that for the kinship between the two sides and the connection between them, any fabrication, lies, malicious incitement, or sowing of discord is hollow. Taiwan compatriots openly and upright expressing their affection for the motherland and their longing to return to their ancestral roots is something no one can drive a wedge into or suppress.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","First question. Some mainland media have analyzed data showing that at the Taiwan Affairs Office's 2021 press conferences, half involved opposing “Taiwan independence,” and four in ten mentioned promoting cross-Strait integration. Although cross-Strait relations were severe last year, the trend toward peace has not changed. Will the spokesperson say whether Taiwan policy in 2022 will move in a direction of easing…","We will, in accordance with the important speeches of General Secretary Xi Jinping, fully implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. We will uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, firmly curb interference by external forces, continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, boldly explore new paths for cross-Strait integrated development, actively guide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to integrate into the new development pattern, continuously improve policies and measures that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland, and strive to promote spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nAt our last press conference, we introduced the overall situation of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in 2021, which compatriots on both sides carried out despite the impact of the epidemic and man-made interference from within the island. With the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, we successfully held the 13th Straits Forum, the 2021 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit (Zijin Mountain Summit), and nearly 800 other civil exchange activities. This demonstrated the shared will of compatriots on both sides against the reckless actions of “Taiwan independence” and their hope for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, as well as their strong resolve. In the new year, cross-Strait exchanges and interactions will certainly be more numerous and richer than in 2021. We will continue to create conditions to promote cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and unite compatriots on both sides to work together and jointly create a better future. The DPP authorities should face up to the trend of the times and the mainstream public opinion that wants exchange, cooperation and development, and promptly lift restrictions that prohibit mainland residents from visiting Taiwan for exchanges, and stop interfering with and obstructing civil exchanges across the Strait.\nRegarding the second question, I have not heard of this information. The relevant policies shall be subject to those issued by the Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism of the State Council.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The Taiwan Air Force recently organized F-16V fighters at Chiayi Air Base for enhanced combat readiness training, simulating the PLA's “attack on Taiwan” during the Spring Festival. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities, overestimating their own capabilities, are trying to “seek independence by force.” This not only seriously harms the well-being of Taiwan's people, but also intensifies cross-Strait tensions and turbulence, pushing Taiwan's people into a dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声记者","Former Kuomintang legislator Pang Chien-kuo fell to his death on the 11th. Before his death, he posted “unjust and unfair Taiwan,” which sparked discussion among netizens. What is your comment?","At noon yesterday, we learned that Mr. Pang Chien-kuo had unfortunately passed away, and we are deeply saddened and express our heartfelt condolences. Mr. Pang Chien-kuo adhered to the one-China principle, was committed to the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, actively promoted cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and consistently fought against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, which is admirable. Before Mr. Pang Chien-kuo's death, Mr. Pang Chien-kuo repeatedly posted articles condemning the “unjust and unrighteous Taiwan” under DPP rule, expressing this resistance in such a tragic manner, which is worth reflection by a broad range of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220112_12401162.htm"],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","Reports say that the Taiwan side recently repatriated 21 mainland personnel who had illegally crossed the Strait back to the mainland by charter flight. Some public opinion on the island holds that this represents goodwill from the DPP authorities toward the mainland. What comments does the spokesperson have?","This is the repatriation operation carried out by the cross-strait Red Cross organizations in accordance with the “Kinmen Agreement.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","First question: The mainland has suspended customs declarations for live fish from two aquaculture farms in the Taiwan region. Does this forewarn that new bans on Taiwan agricultural products may be imposed in the future? Second question: Mainland media have noted that the KMT has recently suffered “three straight defeats” in “referendums” and recalls, and some public opinion analysis holds that the KMT may…","First question: We will take effective measures in accordance with relevant regulations and standards to guard and perform our duties, and protect the vital interests of mainland consumers.\nSecond question: We firmly believe that voices on the island opposing “Taiwan independence,” supporting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and hoping for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will only grow louder and stronger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Regarding the currently sluggish cross-Strait relations, Professor Pang Chien-kuo has chosen a tragic way to resist, voicing the sentiments of many people, who feel that cross-Strait relations seem to be walking through a tunnel with no visible end, in endless night, with no sign of dawn. May I ask whether the spokesperson has positive expectations for cross-Strait relations in the new year?","We note that Mr. Pang Jianguo has expressed his resistance to the DPP's reckless actions in a tragic manner, which should prompt reflection among the people on the island. Indeed, the situation on the island has entered a dark period due to the DPP's manipulation, but the timing and momentum of cross-Strait relations are in the hands of those who advocate developing cross-Strait relations and peaceful reunification, so there is no reason to be pessimistic. As long as compatriots on both sides of the Strait join hands, oppose “Taiwan independence,” strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and deepen integrated development, we will certainly be able to build a bright future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The 4th “Cross-Strait Sister Lakes Industrial Cooperation Annual Conference,” guided by the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, was recently held in Changchun. The DPP authorities criticized the Nantou County Magistrate who attended for cooperating with the mainland's united front work toward Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities are doing this because they fear that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will grow closer. Closer ties between compatriots on both sides will only benefit Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation regarding the mainland side's supply of the BioNTech BNT vaccine to Taiwan, including the time and quantity of the arrival of 15 batches of vaccines in Taiwan. Did the mainland side play an important role in Hon Hai, TSMC and Tzu Chi purchasing the BNT vaccine from the German original manufacturer?","We have repeatedly stressed that the mainland attaches great importance to the life and health welfare of Taiwan compatriots, and has always adhered to the spirit of “serving Taiwan compatriots as we serve the people of the mainland,” helping residents on the island cope with the epidemic. We have consistently supported providing to the Taiwan public the BNT vaccine, namely the Comirnaty vaccine, which was developed with the participation of Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group, and for which the group is the exclusive agent, so as to effectively safeguard the life and health welfare of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In 2021, Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group supplied and delivered to Taiwan a total of 15 batches, 13.33 million doses, of Comirnaty vaccine. The specific times and quantities of these 15 batches’ arrival in Taiwan have been reported by relevant media, and everyone can look them up online.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","As the Spring Festival approaches, what convenience measures has the mainland taken this year to facilitate Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year?","The Spring Festival is the most grand traditional holiday for Chinese on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, a time for family reunion and welcoming the new spring. Taking into account both epidemic prevention and control and the needs of Taiwan compatriots to return home, we are doing our utmost to actively assist Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots in returning home for the New Year. First, local Taiwan Affairs Offices, in accordance with epidemic prevention and control requirements, are helping local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises make arrangements and implement epidemic prevention measures, especially in vaccination, where they are ensuring that everyone who should be vaccinated is vaccinated (“应接尽接”). According to incomplete statistics, as of January 2 this year, 180,000 Taiwan compatriots in the mainland had been vaccinated, with a cumulative total of about 370,000 doses. Second, local Taiwan Affairs Offices are visiting and extending greetings to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in various forms, gaining an in-depth understanding of their specific needs and helping them solve practical problems, so that Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople who wish to return to Taiwan can do so with peace of mind, and those who do not return can spend the New Year in the mainland with peace of mind.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","A video recently circulated online showing the PLA using Hakka and Hokkien in training to shout: “Surrender quickly, we will treat prisoners well.” It has sparked heated discussion on the island, where some believe Taiwanese people are being treated as “enemies.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","I want to emphasize two points. First, the Chinese People's Liberation Army is a mighty, civilized and peaceful army; it is the defender of the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation, and it is the \"great nemesis\" of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. The PLA's relevant exercises and training activities are aimed at a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their separatist activities, as well as external interference, and are by no means aimed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Second, Taiwan compatriots are our family, bound by blood as thick as water, and we will never regard Taiwan compatriots as \"enemies.\"\nIn fact, recently another video circulated online: a young Taiwanese man randomly interviewed passersby on the streets of Beijing about their impressions of Taiwan and what they want to say to Taiwanese people. Most of them said, in one voice, things like \"We are one family, Happy New Year, come back.\" Many Taiwanese netizens also responded to this video with goodwill. The facts prove that the kinship and identification across the Strait will not be diluted or lost because of the agitation of hatred and division by a few Taiwan politicians; instead, they will be expressed in a broader and more lasting way.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220112_12401159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-13","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, Vince Cable, former UK Secretary of State for Business, Innovation and Skills, said on January 10 that the UK government’s decision to ban Huawei 5G equipment and services “had nothing to do with national security,” and was because of American pressure. He said it was “because the Americans told us we should do it”. He added that during his tenure as the secretary, the intelligence and…","This is further evidence that “national security” and the so-called “risk posed by 5G technology” is just a pretext the US uses to suppress China’s hi-tech companies. The US “Clean Network” is synonymous with its coercive diplomacy.\nFrom Toshiba to Alstom, Huawei, Samsung and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co., victims of the US’ coercive diplomacy can be found all across the globe. The US bullying practice will be met with more boycott and opposition from the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347206.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220113_10495224.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-14","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","Recently State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi has held talks and met with several GCC member states’ foreign ministers and the GCC Secretary General, who are visiting China concurrently. Could you share more information, for example, the outcomes achieved? And how do you see China’s relations with these countries at present and in the future?","From January 10 to 14, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi held talks with visiting Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Saudi Arabia, Dr. Abdullatif bin Rashid Al-Zayani, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Bahrain, Sheikh Dr. Ahmed Nasser Al-Mohammed Al-Ahmed Al-Sabah, Foreign Minister and Minister of State for Cabinet Affairs of Kuwait, and Mr. Sayyid Badr Albusaidi, Foreign Minister of Oman, Dr. Nayef Falah M. Al-Hajraf, Secretary General of the Cooperation Council for the Arab States of the Gulf (GCC), and had a telephone conversation with Sheikh Abdullah bin Zayed Al Nahyan, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the United Arab Emirates. They held in-depth exchange of views on bilateral relations, practical cooperation and international and regional issues of mutual concern, reaching broad consensus.\nThey agreed to further elevate bilateral relations and stressed that China and GCC countries enjoy mutual trust and support, always treat each other as equals, and seek shared development. Bilateral relations have sustained a sound, steady and robust momentum of growth, setting a good example of peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation. They stand ready to implement the important consensus reached between President Xi Jinping and the GCC countries’ heads of state to elevate and deepen relations between China and GCC countries. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and GCC Secretary General Nayef Falah M. Al-Hajraf agreed to establish the China-GCC strategic partnership, complete the negotiations on a China-GCC Free Trade Agreement, and sign the 2022-2025 action plan of China-GCC Strategic Dialogue at an early date so as to elevate bilateral relations to a new high.\nThey also reiterated firm support for each other’s efforts to safeguard core national interests. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said that China firmly supports GCC countries in safeguarding national independence, security and stability, and will continue to oppose any country’s interference in the internal affairs of GCC countries under the pretext of “human rights”. The GCC countries’ foreign ministers and the GCC Secretary General all stated their resolute support for the one-China principle and China’s just position on issues relating to Taiwan, Xinjiang and human rights as well as their firm opposition to interference in China’s internal affairs and politicization of human rights. GCC countries also expressed firm opposition to politicization of sports and reiterated their support for China in hosting the Beijing Winter Olympics. They believe that the Games will be a complete success.\nThe two sides agreed to actively enhance solidarity against the pandemic and practical cooperation in various fields. We will strengthen synergy between Belt and Road Initiative and Saudi Arabia’s “Saudi Vision 2030”, Kuwait’s “2035 National Vision”, Oman’s “Oman Vision 2040” and Bahrain’s “Economic Vision 2030”, and deepen cooperation in oil and gas resources, clean energy, 5G communications, e-commerce and digital economy, and jointly address global challenges.\nThe two sides said they will firmly advocate and practice multilateralism and work for greater democracy in international relations. We should uphold the international system with the UN at its core, and abide by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and basic norms governing international relations. We should jointly reject unilateralism, protectionism, the law of the jungle and bullying practice to safeguard international fairness and justice and uphold the collective interests of developing countries.\nThe two sides also exchanged views on the regional situation and agreed to work for political settlement of regional hotspot issues such as Palestine, Yemen, Iraq and Syria. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said that China propose the establishment of a multilateral dialogue platform for the Gulf region to explore ways for countries in the Middle East to resolve conflicts and disputes in the Middle East way while countries outside the region play a constructive role in the process. GCC countries appreciate China’s contribution to promoting peace talks and regional security and stability, and believe that this demonstrates China’s positive role as a responsible major country.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347207.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220114_10495743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-14","Wang Wenbin","CRI","On January 13, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Diplomatic Advisor to the President of France Emmanuel Bonne co-chaired the 22nd China-France Strategic Dialogue. Could you give us more details? What consensus did the two sides reach?","Yesterday, Diplomatic Advisor to the President of France Emmanuel Bonne paid a visit to China. Vice President Wang Qishan and Vice Premier Liu He met with Bonne via video conference respectively. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi co-chaired the 22nd China-France Strategic Dialogue with Bonne in Wuxi, Jiangsu Province. The two sides agreed that China and France share the same or similar views on a series of major issues and have common expectations for strengthening bilateral relations. They expressed their readiness to further leverage the strategic role of the heads-of-state diplomacy in steering the relations, highlight the role of practical cooperation in underpinning the bilateral ties and let China-France relations play the role of serving as a model in China-Europe relations. We should take France’s rotating presidency of the EU as an opportunity to promote the sound and steady development of China-France and China-Europe relations.\nThe Chinese side said that as permanent members of the UN Security Council and major global countries, China and France shoulder important international responsibilities. The two sides should follow the important consensus reached by the two heads of state, give top priority to serving the heads-of-state diplomacy, adhere to the tradition of independent diplomacy, enhance mutual trust through dialogue and consultation, and deepen cooperation in the spirit of mutual benefit, so as to kick off China-France and China-Europe relations to a good start. Bonne said that France and China are permanent members of the UN Security Council and both play a vital role in promoting peace and security. The French side cherishes the friendship between the two heads of state and attaches great importance to strategic communication with China. France looks forward to jointly implementing the consensus reached and ambitious goals set by the two heads of state to achieve mutual benefit and win-win results. France stands for upholding the Olympic spirit and opposing the politicization of sports. French athletes look forward to participating in the Beijing Winter Olympics. The two sides agreed to continue to advance cooperation in such areas as aviation, aerospace, agro-food products, nuclear energy, third market, green development and digital economy and explore cooperation in emerging fields like big data and cloud computing.\nThe two sides exchanged views on China-Europe relations. The Chinese side stressed that harmony without uniformity is a successful lesson in EU’s development and a steady relationship meets Europe’s fundamental and long-term interests. Europe as an independent force is an integral part of the multi-polar world. China supports Europe’s integration, the EU’s development and its greater role in the international community. This policy will not change whether China-EU relations are in smooth progress or encounter setbacks. We hope the European side can continue to follow an active and practical China policy. Bonne said Europe will continue to uphold strategic autonomy. Europe and China should not stand in opposition, still less confrontation, but should further strengthen mutual trust and promote cooperation, and stay as high-level partners. The French side understands the importance and sensitivity of the Taiwan question, and will abide by the one-China principle.\nThe two sides exchanged views on fighting the pandemic and improving global governance. Bonne thanked China for its support for France against the pandemic, and appreciates China’s active role in the global fight against COVID-19. The two sides expressed readiness to stand together to combat the virus and promote equitable vaccine distribution across the world. Both sides agreed that multilateralism should be upheld, and cooperation on climate change and biodiversity protection strengthened. The two sides also had a thorough discussion on issues including the Iranian nuclear issue, Afghanistan and Myanmar, and coordinated respective positions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347207.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220114_10495743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-18","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, a recent informal EU foreign ministers’ meeting criticized China’s “coercive” behavior against Lithuania. I wonder if you have any comment?","I noted relevant reports. The spokesperson of the Chinese Mission to the EU has responded to this. I would reiterate that China firmly opposes all forms of political and diplomatic coercion and never uses economic coercion against any country. If the relevant side truly stands in solidarity with Lithuania, then it should remind Lithuania that there is only one solution to the problem, namely, returning to the right path of adhering to the one-China principle.\nThe ins and outs of the strained China-Lithuania relations are crystal clear with no room for misrepresentation or smearing. The Lithuanian side obstinately endorsed the establishment of the “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania”, blatantly listing “Taiwan” alongside “China” and creating the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan”. This constitutes a grave violation of the one-China principle. Now the Lithuanian side, out of selfish calculation, attempts to hold China-EU relations hostage with its own mistakes. This is irresponsible and highly dangerous. The European side should be highly vigilant. It is hoped that the EU could tell right from wrong, abide by the one-China principle and the solemn commitment it made upon the establishment of China-EU diplomatic relations, uphold an objective and just position, and safeguard the sound and steady development of China-EU relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347209.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220118_10629910.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 18 — Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan again clamored that the two sides are “not subordinate to each other,” claiming that the Hong Kong National Security Law does not apply to Taiwan, which it described as “democratic.” In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 18th in response to an inquiry: Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country. The DPP authorities' continued hyping of “mutual non-subordination between the two sides” is peddling the “two-state theory.” In the face of the trend toward reunification of the motherland, any form of “Taiwan independence” provocation is doomed to fail.\nZhu Fenglian said that since the implementation of the Hong Kong National Security Law, the situation in Hong Kong has continuously consolidated from chaos to order, the rule of law has been protected, order has been maintained, society is stable, the economy is prosperous, and national sovereignty, security and development interests have been safeguarded, receiving widespread support and welcome from Hong Kong residents. Faced with the fact of the successful practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong, the DPP authorities' plot to deceive the public has been further exposed. The Hong Kong National Security Law is the Sea-Anchoring Divine Needle that safeguards Hong Kong's prosperity and stability and protects the lawful rights and interests of Hong Kong residents. The scope of application and the specific provisions of this law are crystal clear. Anyone or any force that dares to break the law will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220118_12402272.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 18 (electronic dispatch). According to reports, on January 17, the Taipei District Court in Taiwan sentenced Taiwan businessman Lin Huai to 3 years and 10 months in prison, and the other four involved persons to 1 year and 8 months each, on the so-called grounds that in 2019 Lin Huai and others received funds from the mainland to assist a Kuomintang candidate in an election campaign. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 18th: We note the relevant reports. The DPP authorities are accustomed to fabricating all kinds of pretexts to attack Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan groups and individuals who participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, creating “green terror,” manipulating politics to create hostility and confrontation across the Strait, undermining cross-Strait relations, and harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots. We strongly condemn the DPP authorities for framing and persecuting the Taiwan compatriots concerned. We warn the DPP authorities that those who commit many injustices will bring about their own downfall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220118_12402290.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-19","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Slovenia’s Prime Minister has announced that the country is preparing for an exchange of representatives with Taiwan. How does Beijing view this?","The Chinese side is shocked by and strongly opposes the dangerous remarks by the Slovenian leader who flagrantly challenged the one-China principle and voiced support for “Taiwan independence”. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The PRC government is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a universally-recognized norm governing international relations and common consensus of the international community. It is also the political foundation of China-Slovenia and China-EU relations. China must be and will be reunified. Nobody should underestimate the Chinese people’s strong resolution, will and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347210.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220119_10630363.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 19 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 19th that we urge the Slovenian government to act on its solemn commitments on Taiwan-related issues and handle Taiwan-related matters prudently and appropriately. The DPP authorities are using various tricks to win over and infiltrate politicians of relevant countries, attempting to rely on external forces to pursue “independence,” and are bound to fail.\nA reporter asked: Recently, the Slovenian Prime Minister made erroneous remarks on Taiwan-related issues, calling the Taiwan region of China a “democratic country,” lobbying for Taiwan’s accession to the World Health Organization, and stating support for Lithuania’s approach to Taiwan-related matters. Slovenia is also reportedly advancing “mutual establishment of representative offices” with Taiwan. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in response.\nShe said: The remarks of certain Slovenian politicians disregard facts and confuse the public. They should be clear about what the one-China principle is, and should carefully read the original text of the Joint Communiqué between the People’s Republic of China and the Republic of Slovenia. In it, the Slovenian side reaffirmed that it will continue to adhere to the one-China principle, recognizes that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and that the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all Chinese people. Slovenia’s position of not having any official exchanges with Taiwan and not establishing any official relations with it remains unchanged.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220119_12402500.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-20","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","According to reports, Taiwan will send Lai Ching-te to Honduras to attend the inauguration ceremony of the Honduran president. He plans to engage with the US side during his transit in the country, and may find an opportunity to directly interact with US Vice President Kamala Harris, who will also attend the ceremony. Do you have any comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations, and a wide consensus that has been recognized, accepted and practiced by the overwhelming majority of countries in the world. Adherence to the one-China principle is an overriding trend that represents international justice and enjoys popular support. Any attempt to create the false impression of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” will be rejected by all Chinese people. We hope relevant country will grasp the overriding international trend and make a resolute decision in line with the trend of the times at an early date.\nRegarding the so-called “transit” of leaders of the Taiwan region and “engagement” between the US and Taiwan, China has made clear its consistent position on various occasions. We firmly oppose the arrangement of such “transit” by the US or any other country that has diplomatic ties with China as well as any form of official exchange between the US and Taiwan. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, take seriously China’s position and concern, refrain from conducting official engagement with Taiwan in any form and sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347211.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220120_10631036.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, January 20 — Lai Ching-te will soon use his trip to Honduras to “transit” through the United States, during which he may interact with U.S. officials. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 20th: The DPP authorities' attempt to use the so-called “transit” through the United States to plot official U.S.-Taiwan contact and seize opportunities to manipulate for “independence” is their consistent trick of “relying on the U.S. to seek independence.” No matter under what pretext or with what tricks, it cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China.\nZhu Fenglian said: We firmly oppose the United States engaging in any form of official exchange with the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and not send erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. Supporting Taiwan in seeking independence will only further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and will only bring about the consequence of playing with fire and burning oneself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220120_12402647.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-21","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Daily","According to reports, Lithuanian President Gitanas Nauseda said at a press conference on January 19 that “the fraught relations with Beijing have incurred business losses” and they need to “implement a de-escalation plan”. The Lithuanian Foreign Minister has presented the plan. “We have passed over some ideas through European institutions and directly by ourselves, but as I said during the meeting de-escalation…","The root cause of the fraught relations between China and Lithuania is that the Lithuanian authorities have obstinately taken erroneous steps on issues concerning Taiwan, which harm China’s core interests and undermine basic norms governing international relations. The international community has its fair judgement as to who is culpable for the souring China-Lithuania ties and the ensuing escalation. On China’s part, the door to communication with Lithuania remains open. If the Lithuanian side truly hopes to mend fences, it should show its sincerity with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347212.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220121_10631768.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-24","Zhao Lijian","AFP","I have two questions. First, Taiwanese media reported that yesterday China’s PLA sent 39 warplanes into Taiwan’s \"Air Defense Identification Zone\". I wonder if you have any comment on this? Second, US President Joe Biden and Japanese Prime Minister Kishida on Friday agreed to push back against China in their virtual meeting. They expressed concern over what they called China “intimidating” its neighbor. This is…","On your first question, this is not a diplomatic issue. I would like to refer you to competent authorities.\nOn your second question, the US and Japanese leaders’ meeting has struck up the same old tune on China-related issues. They’ve once again wantonly discredited and attacked China and grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs, seriously violating international law and basic norms governing international relations. China deplores and rejects this, and has lodged solemn diplomatic representation with the two countries.\nThe affairs of Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are purely China’s internal affairs. They brook no interference from any country or external force. No one is allowed to slander China on the basis of lies and prejudice. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have been China’s inherent territory since ancient times. No matter what the US and Japan say or do, it will not change the objective fact that Diaoyu Dao belongs to China. No one should underestimate the strong resolve, determination and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. On maritime issues, the US and Japan should stop making trouble and sowing discord.\nI want to stress that the US and Japan have clung to the Cold War mentality, incited ideological antagonism and confrontation between countries, manipulated the internal affairs of other countries in the name of democracy and freedom, and bullied and coerced other countries under the pretext of rules. This runs counter to the trend of seeking peace, cooperation and development in the region and beyond. The international community sees this clearly. China once again urges the US and Japan to follow the trend of the times, abandon the narrow-minded policy of zero-sum game and beggar-thy-neighbor, and return to the constructive track of dialogue and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347213.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220124_10632711.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on January 26, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Happy New Year. Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Now let's begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 2022 Taiwan Work Conference was held in Beijing yesterday (the 25th). Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant details of the conference. What will the mainland do next to promote the development of cross-Strait relations?","On January 25, the 2022 Work Conference on Taiwan Affairs was held in Beijing. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the conference and delivered a speech. The conference held that in 2021, under the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, work on Taiwan maintained strategic resolve and historical patience while also boldly tackling difficult problems and forging ahead through hardship. It effectively shaped the trend toward reunification, firmly carried out struggle against Taiwan-related separatist activities, continuously promoted the integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and achieved positive results.\nAt present, risks, challenges, and uncertainties and instability in the Taiwan Strait have increased. We will, in accordance with the arrangements of the conference, be guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, fully implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and the successive plenary sessions of the 19th Central Committee, thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the CPC Central Committee on Taiwan work, strengthen historical confidence, firmly establish bottom-line thinking, uphold the spirit of struggle, strengthen precise policy implementation, resolutely crush “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, resolutely curb interference by external forces, improve policies for sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and ensuring equal treatment, provide more convenience for grassroots people and young people in Taiwan to take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, support Fujian in exploring new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and in building a demonstration zone for integrated development across the Strait, and steadily promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of reunifying the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403709.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, in 2021, both imports from Taiwan and exports to Taiwan by the mainland grew substantially, and the mainland firmly remained Taiwan's largest export market and largest source of trade surplus. What is your view on Taiwan's exports to the mainland rising against the trend? In addition, according to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, in…","In 2021, despite unfavorable factors such as the COVID-19 pandemic, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation overcame difficulties and moved forward, and cross-Strait trade and investment generally maintained growth. The data from the past decade of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation make the following very clear:\nFirst, cross-Strait trade has grown substantially. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, cross-Strait trade in 2011 was US$160.03 billion, and in 2021 it grew to US$328.34 billion. Over these 10 years, cross-Strait trade doubled. The share of cross-Strait trade in the mainland’s foreign trade rose from 4.4% in 2011 to 5.4% in 2021, an increase of 1 percentage point. According to statistics from the Taiwan side, the share of cross-Strait trade in Taiwan’s foreign trade rose from 28.6% in 2011 to 33% in 2021, an increase of 4.4 percentage points. The mainland has consistently remained Taiwan’s largest export market and largest source of trade surplus.\nSecond, Taiwan businesses’ investment in the mainland has grown steadily. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, in 2011 a total of 2,639 mainland projects invested in by Taiwan businesses were approved, and in 2021 there were 6,595. As of the end of 2021, Taiwan businesses had invested in a total of 123,781 projects on the mainland, with actual investment amounting to US$71.34 billion. Over the past 10 years, the number of newly approved Taiwan-invested projects and the amount of Taiwan capital attracted have continued to increase, fully demonstrating that Taiwan businesses remain optimistic about the mainland’s huge domestic market, complete industrial system, strong manufacturing capacity and broad development prospects. By comparison, because the DPP authorities have continually set new obstacles to mainland enterprises investing in Taiwan, as of the end of 2021, mainland capital invested in Taiwan had increased only slightly, with a total of just US$3.71 billion.\nThe facts fully show that whether it is the artificial restrictions imposed by the DPP authorities for political self-interest, or unexpected events and accidental factors such as the epidemic, none of them can change the solid foundation, objective needs and inexhaustible momentum of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, nor can they erase the enormous benefits and well-being this brings to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. Expanding cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integration and development is what the hearts of people on both sides desire and the trend of the times. It cannot be blocked by anyone or any force. The DPP authorities should promptly remove unreasonable restrictions that interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, create a good environment for cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges, and create a better future for the interests and well-being of the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403708.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The Spring Festival is approaching, and reports say that many Taiwan performing artists will take part in Spring Festival arts performance activities on the mainland. Please introduce the relevant situation. How does the spokesperson view the growing number of Taiwan performers taking part in performance activities on the mainland?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait celebrating the festive season together, feeling the blood-thicker-than-water kinship of compatriots on both sides and the warmth of the big family of the Chinese nation in a harmonious and festive atmosphere, is a vivid manifestation of the two sides being one family. Taiwan performers and mainland cultural workers jointly participating in holiday performance activities have been warmly received and eagerly anticipated by audiences on both sides. During the Spring Festival, various regions of the mainland will hold rich and colorful Spring Festival arts performance activities. We welcome Taiwan performers to take part in the performances and look forward to their outstanding performances.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","With the Spring Festival approaching, many Taiwan compatriots have chosen to spend the New Year where they are due to the epidemic. Could the spokesperson introduce the visits, condolences and arrangements carried out across the mainland?","As the Spring Festival approaches, Taiwan compatriots on the mainland increasingly feel that spending the New Year on the mainland is both warm and reassuring. Localities are putting the concept of “Cross-Strait families are one family” into practice and continuously carrying out visits, condolences, and celebratory gatherings, mainly in three areas.\nFirst, visits and condolences that express family affection. Hebei, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Hunan, Hubei, Qinghai and other places have organized Taiwan Affairs Offices across their provinces to carry out visits and condolence activities in various forms for Taiwan businesses, Taiwan compatriots and their relatives, and to coordinate the resolution of issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Zhang Ximing, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Anhui Provincial Committee and Minister of the United Front Work Department, Huang Ningsheng, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Guangdong Provincial Committee and Minister of the United Front Work Department, and Liu Rui, Deputy Minister of the United Front Work Department of the CPC Guizhou Provincial Committee and Director of the Guizhou Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, visited and condoled with local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises and extended New Year greetings. The Liaoning Taiwan Affairs Office visited and condoled with 105 Taiwan-funded enterprises. The Henan Taiwan Affairs Office visited and condoled with 18 Taiwan students spending the New Year in Zhengzhou, one by one. The Chongqing Taiwan Affairs Office visited and condoled with more than 80 Taiwan-funded enterprises and more than 600 Taiwan compatriots and their relatives in Chongqing in batches, produced Year of the Tiger New Year greeting videos, and greeted the Spring Festival together with Taiwan compatriots in the cloud. The Shenzhen Taiwan Affairs Office also visited and condoled with more than 300 Taiwan teachers and students at local universities and more than 100 Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots in Shenzhen through various means.\nSecond, cultural exchanges that deliver blessings. The Confucius Museum in Qufu, Shandong, held a cross-Strait Kong clan kinship New Year dialogue with the Chinese Art Museum in Taipei via video link. More than 300 fellow natives from Jilong and Taipei gathered in the “cloud” through the “Cross-Strait Shandong Fellow Natives Welcome Spring and Send Blessings Activity.” Jinan carried out the “Jinan-Taiwan Deep Affection, Happy Family” series of activities, in which Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan students in Jinan exchanged blessings online with fellow Shandong natives in Taiwan, making dumplings and celebrating family reunion. Sichuan Province held the “Crossing the Strait, One Family Across Cross-Strait” 2022 Spring Festival Hearth Gathering, where cross-Strait marriage families, Taiwan youth in Sichuan, and cross-Strait media professionals gathered together. In Xuzhou, Jiangsu, the 2022 “Xuzhou-Taiwan One Family” fellow-native New Year gathering was held, in which more than 50 Taiwan relatives and Taiwan businesspeople in Xuzhou connected online with more than 50 Taiwan compatriots from the Taipei Xuzhou Fellow Natives Association to welcome the New Year together.\nThird, gathering together to welcome the New Year. During the Spring Festival, Guangdong Province will hold the “Four Cities of the Bay Area, Hearts Connected” series of Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao-Taiwan Youth Spring Festival events. The main event is the launch ceremony of the “Tigers Full of Vigor Toward the Future” Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao-Taiwan Youth Spring Festival Gala and New Year Carnival, which uses a virtual scene plus AR recording method, integrates various performance forms such as street dance, rap and gesture dance, tells the story of Bay Area integration, and conveys patriotic feeling. In addition, six featured activities will be held, including the “Innovating in the Bay Area, Inspiring Youth” Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Youth Creative Market, and the “Healthy Bay Area, Romantic Haizhu” Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Youth Lakeside Run, allowing Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan youth who stay in Guangdong for the New Year to enjoy a Spring Festival with the feel of home, the flavor of Guangdong, the spirit of the New Year, and the vitality of youth. Fuzhou held a series of “Beautiful Homeland, New Year Blessings” activities, and more than 60 Taiwan youth staying in Fuzhou for the New Year gathered together. Changsha also held a New Year event for Taiwan university students, conveying holiday wishes to the Taiwan students.\nWe believe that with the care and concern from all localities and the warm human bonds of fellow compatriots nearby, Taiwan compatriots will certainly be able to spend the New Year on the mainland in peace and contentment, and welcome the Spring Festival joyfully and festively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403705.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Beijing Winter Olympics and Winter Paralympics are approaching, and the atmosphere of welcoming and taking part in the Winter Olympics is growing stronger. Please introduce the relevant situation of Taiwan compatriots participating in the Beijing Winter Olympics.","It is understood that a 17-member delegation from Chinese Taipei has registered to take part in the Beijing Winter Olympics. Among them, four athletes have obtained eligibility to compete in the speed skating, alpine skiing, and luge events, and one other athlete has obtained a reserve eligibility. We hope that athletes from both sides of the Strait will carry forward the Olympic spirit, fight tenaciously, and together achieve excellent results.\nThe Beijing Winter Olympics torch relay will be held from February 2 to 4. At that time, five Taiwan compatriots will take part in the torch relay and share the solemn and wonderful moments of the Olympic flame's relay. In terms of volunteer service, more than 30 Taiwanese students studying at universities in Beijing have already joined the Games as volunteers and are engaged in Olympic service work.\nIt is worth mentioning that, apart from directly taking part in the Winter Olympics in Beijing, Taiwan compatriots have also expressed their joy in welcoming the Winter Olympics and their enthusiasm for participating in them in various forms across the country. First, musicians from both sides of the Strait have jointly created songs welcoming the Winter Olympics. Guided by the Cross-Strait Civil Exchange Promotion Association of Taiwan Compatriots, the Straits Two-Shore Magazine Press, Hualiu Music Group and others jointly sponsored the “Welcome the Winter Olympics, Shape the Future” Chinese-pop music album solicitation campaign across the Strait, soliciting original works from young musicians on both sides, which has received an enthusiastic response. Works created with the participation of well-known musicians Fang Wenshan and Huang Qishan—the campaign's first song, “I'm Waiting for You in Beijing”—was officially released yesterday, fully showing the spirit of compatriots on both sides of the Strait welcoming the Beijing Winter Olympics. The solicitation campaign will continue until March 13, and a release ceremony and award ceremony for the “Winter Olympics” commemorative vinyl album will be held, with outstanding works selected and compiled into a commemorative album that gathers the classic chapters of young musicians from both sides of the Strait working hand in hand to chase their dreams.\nSecond, Taiwan youth and students across various regions are actively participating in activities welcoming the Winter Olympics. The 28th Taiwan Compatriot Youth Winter Camp of the All-China Taiwan Affairs Federation opened in Beijing on January 24. Branch camps were set up in 25 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities on the mainland as well as in Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macao, and more than a thousand Taiwan youth will take part online and offline, experiencing the Beijing Winter Olympics and feeling the pulse of mainland development. Peking University held a series of 2022 Cross-Strait University Students' “Ice and Snow Carnival” activities, where nearly 50 Taiwanese students from eight universities in Beijing joyfully experienced skiing, ice kart racing, outdoor curling, and other ice sports. The Taiwan Affairs Office of Hubei Province held a series of “Taiwan Youth and Students Welcome the Winter Olympics, Tiger Spirit Greets the New Year” activities, in which more than 40 Taiwan students and youth spending the Chinese New Year in Hubei played ice hockey, cut paper window decorations, wrote Spring Festival couplets, and took part in ecological farm New Year's Eve dinners, family reunions around the hearth, and visits to Jingchu culture. The Taiwan Affairs Office of Guangdong Province held the “Guangdong-Taiwan Students, Chinese Bonds” cultural exchange activity welcoming the Winter Olympics, which was also a campus ice and snow sports event, spreading knowledge about the Winter Olympics, passing on Olympic ideals, and helping compatriots on both sides of the Strait share a simple, safe, and splendid Winter Olympics. Taiwanese students who took part in the activities were very excited, saying that they rarely have access to ice and snow sports in Taiwan, and they hope to share the grandeur of the Beijing Winter Olympics and their experiences of cross-Strait sports exchanges with more people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403707.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities have recently staged a series of political shows under the banner of “commemorating Chiang Ching-kuo,” claiming that “Chiang Ching-kuo's firm position of defending Taiwan is also the greatest consensus of the people of Taiwan today.” What is your comment on this? How does the mainland evaluate Chiang Ching-kuo?","Mr. Chiang Ching-kuo upheld one China, opposed 'Taiwan independence,' advocated national reunification, and once said during his lifetime, 'I am a Taiwanese, and also an upright Chinese,' making positive efforts to ease cross-strait relations. Some DPP politicians, while deepening their collusion with external anti-China forces to seek 'independence' and provoke, and inciting hostility and enmity among people on both sides, also distort historical facts in commemorating Mr. Chiang Ching-kuo, engage in political manipulation, and incite so-called 'resisting China and protecting Taiwan.' The essence of this is to mislead Taiwan's people and to seek the private interests of one party and its individuals. We hope all sectors of the island will open their eyes, distinguish right from wrong, and see through the DPP's sinister intentions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Taiwan actress Fang Fang recently gave an interview to mainland media, expressing views in support of reunification, and said that Taiwan performing artists who come to the mainland to perform and develop should abide by relevant regulations. Taiwan's MAC said in response that public figures should not cooperate with the mainland's “united front” propaganda, and threatened that if there are “violations,” they…","We have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait cultural exchanges, welcomed Taiwan performers to develop in the mainland, and supported them in sharing opportunities and realizing their dreams in the development of the mainland’s cultural industry. More and more Taiwan performers are developing their careers in the mainland and have also taken the initiative to shoulder due social responsibility, speaking out to enhance the emotional bonds and spiritual affinity between compatriots on both sides and openly expressing a clear stance of supporting national reunification. Their voices carry weight and have won the praise of people on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities smear normal exchanges between people on both sides as “united front” work and loudly intimidate; this fully illustrates that the closer and more intimate the people on both sides of the Strait become, the more uneasy and fearful the DPP authorities are.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403703.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","The DPP authorities recently used “crossing the boundary” as a pretext to forcibly board a mainland fishing vessel and detain 14 crew members. What is your comment on this? We note that since 2021, the DPP authorities have continuously strengthened so-called “coast guard forces” and held so-called “coast guard joint exercises” in collusion with the United States. May I ask whether this is connected with Taiwan’s…","First question: Relevant parties in Taiwan should respect the fact that fishermen on both sides of the Strait have long operated in traditional fishing grounds. They should immediately stop treating mainland fishermen in rough and dangerous ways, stop detaining mainland fishing boats, ensure the safety of the lives and property of the personnel involved, and release the people and boats as soon as possible.\nSecond question: The DPP authorities, in collusion with external forces, keep carrying out \"independence-seeking\" provocations, which is the root cause of the current tense and grim situation in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that Taiwan-US coast guard collusion directly affects peace and stability on the Taiwan Strait. If they dare to create incidents, they will surely reap the bitter consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403704.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, in order to cooperate with the DPP authorities’ push to lift the ban on food imports from Fukushima and surrounding areas in Japan, some pan-green politicians have proposed renaming “核食” (nuclear food) as “福食” (fortune food). What is the spokesperson’s comment on this? In addition, some people on the island claim that in order to win Japan’s support for joining the CPTPP, the mainland will open its…","On the first question: the DPP authorities are accustomed to switching concepts and substituting one thing for another. Food safety concerns the vital interests of the people, and the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots should be effectively guaranteed. Anyone or any force that, in pursuit of political self-interest, disregards the life, health, and well-being of the people will certainly be abandoned by public opinion.\nOn the second question: the relevant claims are pure rumor. After the Fukushima nuclear power plant leak accident in March 2011, to prevent radioactively contaminated Japanese food from being exported to the mainland, relevant mainland departments adopted enhanced supervision measures on food imports from Japan, prohibiting the import of food, edible agricultural products, and feed from Fukushima and nine other prefectures in Japan; for imports of food, edible agricultural products, and feed produced in other regions of Japan, they require certificates of origin issued by the Japanese government, certificates of qualified radioactive material testing, and similar documents, to prevent the import of products that do not meet the requirements.\nFood safety is closely tied to the vital interests of the people. We have consistently attached high importance to it and have actively taken effective measures, because we adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people and genuinely protect the life and health and safety of the people. As for the DPP authorities' conduct on matters concerning the life and health and safety of Taiwan compatriots, we believe the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots see it with clear eyes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","In 2021, the DPP authorities passed the so-called “Act for the Development of National Languages,” which, starting from the 2022 school year, will include “local languages” such as Southern Min, Hakka and Taiwan's indigenous languages in the compulsory curriculum for primary and secondary school students. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities deliberately divide the dialects, minority languages and Mandarin used by Taiwan residents into so-called “local” and “foreign” categories, harboring the sinister intent of “de-Sinicization” that they have long schemed for.\nIn fact, Minnan and Hakka in Taiwan are both Chinese dialects, regional branches or variants of Chinese formed over a long history, brought to Taiwan by early settlers from Fujian and Guangdong. I am a Hakka from Meizhou, Guangdong. The Hakka I speak can be understood by Hakka people in Taoyuan, Hsinchu, Miaoli, Pingtung and Kaohsiung in Taiwan. (Hakka) So I hope to have the opportunity to visit Taiwan and communicate face to face with Hakka kinsfolk in Taoyuan, Hsinchu, Miaoli, Pingtung and Meinong, especially to communicate in Hakka. Family members should speak their own family language.\nAs for minority languages, China is a country with multiple ethnic groups, multiple languages and multiple scripts. Taiwan's indigenous peoples, like many ethnic minorities in many parts of the mainland, have their own languages. This is a very normal phenomenon.\nAnyone who attempts to use language as a tool to change the Chinese cultural identity and Chinese national identity deeply rooted in Taiwan society will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","According to Taiwanese media, the DPP authorities intend to use the so-called “transit” through the United States to seek official contact between the US and Taiwan. What impact will this have on the situation in the Taiwan Strait? It is understood that in addition to Lai Ching-te's planned “transit” through the United States, Chu Li-luan and Ko Wen-je also intend to travel to the US. What is your comment on this?","First of all, it must be stressed that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and affairs across the Strait are family matters for compatriots on both sides. We believe that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait are fully wise and capable of solving their own problems well.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to use the so-called “transit” through the United States to seek official contact between the U.S. and Taiwan, and to look for opportunities to manipulate “independence,” is their long-standing ploy of “relying on the U.S. to seek independence.” Regardless of what name they use or what tricks they play, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. We resolutely oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and not send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. Backing Taiwan to seek “independence” will only further undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and will only bring about the consequence of playing with fire and immolating oneself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Mr. Wu Cheng-tien was re-elected as chairman of the New Party. Did the mainland express congratulations? What are your expectations for future exchanges with the New Party?","After Mr. Wu Cheng-tien was elected chairman of the New Party in its new term, Liu Jieyi, director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, sent a letter expressing congratulations, and Chairman Wu Cheng-tien replied with a letter of thanks. The New Party has clearly supported national reunification, supported \"one country, two systems,\" and firmly opposed \"Taiwan independence,\" and has made positive contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. The situation in the Taiwan Strait is becoming more complex and grim. We look forward to the New Party, under the leadership of Chairman Wu Cheng-tien, continuing to adhere to correct principles, actively taking part in cross-Strait exchanges, and jointly contributing to the great cause of national reunification and sharing in the glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报海外版记者","Under the strong dominance of the DPP, the so-called “Constitutional Amendment Committee” of Taiwan's legislature passed the “18-year-old citizenship rights proposal,” and is promoting sending to the February legislative session a plan to hold a so-called “referendum” jointly with the island's local elections at the end of the year. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose the DPP authorities manipulating “constitutional revision to seek independence” in any form, or opening the door for “seeking independence” in any way. In order to pursue their own private interests, the DPP authorities do not hesitate to incite severe social antagonism and arbitrarily manipulate the so-called “constitutional revision” issue. Compatriots in Taiwan must remain highly vigilant, see through the DPP authorities’ political calculations, and resist their customary tricks through practical actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403706.htm"],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The U.S. and Japanese leaders mentioned the Taiwan Strait issue in their video summit, and the U.S.-Japan “2+2” joint statement included content on both sides increasing military capabilities and paying attention to the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's comment on the repeated meddling by the U.S. and Japan in the Taiwan Strait issue?","There has been quite a lot of news of this kind recently, and we are following it closely. I want to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. We will never allow any country to interfere in the Taiwan question or in China's internal affairs under any pretext or in any way, and we will also never allow anyone to “seek independence by force” in any way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Lin Huai, former chairman of the Changsha Taiwan Association, was recently sentenced to prison for allegedly violating the 《Public Officials Election and Recall Act》. This has caused great concern among mainland Taiwan business groups, and some people say it is not conducive to cross-Strait exchanges. What is your comment?\nSecond question: Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Le Yucheng recently said…","On the first question, we are closely following relevant developments. The DPP authorities indulge in political manipulation, fabricate all kinds of pretexts to crack down on Taiwan groups and individuals who participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, create a “green terror,” manufacture hostility and confrontation across the Strait, undermine cross-Strait relations and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots. We strongly condemn the DPP authorities for framing and persecuting relevant Taiwan compatriots. We warn the DPP authorities that those who do evil will eventually bring about their own downfall.\nOn the second question, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a generally recognized norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. No person or force can stop the trend of national reunification. The DPP authorities, scheming for “independence” and provoking confrontation, are going against the tide of history and selling out the interests of the Chinese nation and harming the interests of the people of Taiwan. Their complete failure is only a matter of time. We believe that the few remaining so-called “diplomatic allies” of Taiwan will eventually recognize the trend and stand on the right side of history.\nOn the third question, first of all, I must point out that this media outlet’s initiation of a vote on the so-called “most unacceptable words” is ill-intentioned and highly misleading. Due to differences in living environments and popular culture, people on both sides of the Strait have differences in some customary expressions, which is a very natural phenomenon. For example, “土豆” is also called “马铃薯” or “洋芋” (potato) in many places on the mainland, while in Taiwan it refers to “peanut.” Another example is the word “窝心”: on the mainland it means being wronged or feeling hurt, while in Taiwan it means feeling warm-hearted and very comfortable. “湾湾” is an affectionate nickname many mainland people use for Taiwan people, conveying a cute feeling. Regrettably, in Taiwan it has been deliberately stigmatized by some people.\nAs cross-Strait exchanges grow increasingly close, we believe that artificially created barriers will gradually be removed, and people on both sides will increasingly understand each other’s language habits and the stories behind different expressions. Together they will spark new ideas and new cultural content, promoting the prosperity, diversity and innovation of cross-Strait cultural exchanges. We hope that exchanges at the grassroots and among the people will provide more intrinsic momentum for the advancement of cross-Strait relations, and we will, as always, create favorable conditions for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, encourage people on both sides to expand exchanges, deepen understanding, enhance mutual identity, and together promote the power of goodness and the power of justice. We also hope that people on both sides of the Strait will stay alert and not be led astray in rhythm or direction by the DPP authorities, the Green camp’s online armies and specific media, which would only deepen misunderstanding and prejudice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","We note that within Lithuania there has been much dispute over setting up the so-called “Taiwan Representative Office,” and that Slovenia recently made erroneous remarks on related Taiwan-related issues. What comments do you have on this?","First of all, it must be pointed out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, in order to seek political gain, spend huge sums of money, play the “sucker” (凯子), and seek “independence” internationally. This is nothing new. The money they spend is the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people. It is outright “money diplomacy” and “sucker diplomacy,” which not only adds to the ridicule but also harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people.\nAdhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. We believe that the countries concerned will fully recognize this and properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The 2022 Taiwan Work Conference mentioned preparing ideologically and operationally to respond to various risks and challenges. Public opinion in Taiwan has sniffed a “smell of gunpowder” in this, feeling that cross-Strait relations are only one step away from armed confrontation. What comment does the spokesperson have on this? The conference also stressed resolutely containing “Taiwan independence” provocations…","First question: Where does the “smell of gunpowder” come from? The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” stance and collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke. This is the root cause of the threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and of the tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations, and it is also a scourge that seriously harms the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should share peace, jointly safeguard peace and jointly seek peace. In response to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, we must take all necessary actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond question: In the new year, we will closely watch “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist activities, and strike them down whenever they show their heads.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Foreign media reported that Lithuania’s Foreign Minister recently proposed changing the Chinese name of the so-called “Taiwan Representative Office” to “Taiwan People’s Representative Office,” while the English and Lithuanian names would remain unchanged. What comments do you have?","We firmly oppose any act that undermines the one-China principle. We hope the relevant parties in Lithuania will take concrete action and correct their previous mistakes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Regarding PLA aircraft flying around the island for two consecutive days, the people of Taiwan do not feel it is very friendly. A Taipei city councilor has proposed freezing the budget for this year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum and has even demanded that it be cancelled. How does the spokesperson view this matter?","First of all, it must be emphasized that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are by no means equivalent to the people of Taiwan. The aim of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities is to split Taiwan from China, endangering national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The PLA’s training and exercises are precisely to oppose “Taiwan independence” and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. If “Taiwan independence” provocations do not stop or lessen, the PLA’s training and exercises will only increase, not decrease.\nOn the other hand, strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides and is in line with the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Over the years, the cities of Shanghai and Taipei have, through the city forum, deeply explored and exchanged urban development experiences, consolidated and expanded cooperation in various fields, and signed 39 cooperation memoranda, bringing many tangible benefits to residents of both cities. Such good things should be cherished and protected, rather than obstructed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that cross-Strait sides have never communicated about connecting the power grids of Kinmen and Matsu with Fujian, that Taiwan has no plans for such a connection, and claimed that Kinmen and Matsu's power infrastructure can ensure electricity supply for 10 years without problems, and that there is no necessity or urgency for Kinmen and Matsu to be connected with…","Upholding the concept that “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family,” and starting from enhancing the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and helping Kinmen resolve practical livelihood difficulties, we continue to advance work on water, electricity, gas, and bridge links between coastal areas of Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu. On water supply: on August 5, 2018, the Fujian-to-Kinmen water supply project overcame numerous difficulties and officially began supplying water. As of December 31, 2021, Fujian had safely supplied water to Kinmen for 1,245 days, with a total supply of 17.03 million tons, accounting for 73% of Kinmen’s domestic and industrial water demand. On electricity: relevant enterprises, industry associations, and experts and scholars from both sides have held multiple rounds of coordination and exchanges on the electricity issue; relevant departments on the mainland have completed the relevant technical plan, and the related power transmission project on the Fujian side has commenced construction.\nElectricity connection between Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas is conducive to enhancing the well-being of compatriots in Kinmen and Matsu and the long-term development of both areas. The DPP authorities’ wanton obstruction does not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Recently, many members of the Fujian Provincial CPPCC have proposed advancing economic cooperation between Xiamen and Kinmen, suggesting the establishment of a 'Xiamen-Kinmen Cross-Border Free Trade Zone' and implementing free trade port policies of 'zero tariffs, zero barriers, and zero subsidies' to promote the pioneering integration of the Xiamen-Kinmen area. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? In…","Fujian and Taiwan are geographically close and share close kinship ties. Over the years, a good trend has formed in which economic and trade cooperation has continuously expanded, industrial cooperation has steadily deepened, social interactions have gradually become more frequent, and bonds of hometown and kinship have increasingly grown. Policies providing Taiwan compatriots in Fujian with equal treatment have been comprehensively and continuously advanced, and exchanges and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan in all fields have continuously deepened. In particular, Xiamen and Kinmen, the closest points across the Taiwan Strait, have seen especially lively civil exchanges.\nIn March last year, General Secretary Xi Jinping, during an inspection in Fujian, further pointed out that Fujian should “take greater steps in exploring a new path for the integrated development of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait” and “emphasize promoting integration through connectivity, promoting integration through benefits, and promoting integration through emotional bonds, and boldly explore a new path for the integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.” The Fujian Provincial Party Committee and Provincial Government attached great importance to this and did much work. Among these, at the end of last year they issued the “Opinions on Supporting Xiamen in Building a High-Quality Development Leading Demonstration Zone,” which, with the aim of “building a pilot demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development,” proposes a series of policy goals, and these are being steadily implemented.\nWe will, as always, support Fujian in deepening the integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan in all fields, and will also support Fujian in actively exploring effective paths for promoting economic and trade cooperation between Xiamen and Kinmen. We welcome more residents and businesses of Kinmen to seize the opportunity presented by Xiamen's push for high-quality development and to start businesses, find employment, invest, and develop in Xiamen.\nYesterday and today, the fellow townspeople of the north and south respectively celebrated Little New Year. The Year of the Tiger is approaching, and I wish you all great fortune in the new spring. On behalf of the Information Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office, I extend New Year's greetings to everyone in advance. (In Hokkien) I wish fellow townspeople on both sides of the Strait great good fortune, family reunions, and a joyful New Year. (In Hakka) I hope that wherever you spend the New Year and whatever way you choose, you can say to your family: Happy New Year, and let's all work hard together in the new year!\nThank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202201/t20220126_12403701.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-01-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 26 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 26th in response to a question: Since taking power, the DPP authorities have suppressed speech, deceived the public, persecuted dissidents, manipulated populism, created ethnic antagonism, divided Taiwan society, incited cross-Strait confrontation, treated democracy as a private tool, and, in the name of…","Zhu Fenglian said that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. We firmly oppose official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic ties with China and the DPP authorities. Any US-Taiwan contact conducted under the guise of “transit,” meetings, chance encounters and the like cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities are accustomed to using so-called “parliamentary diplomacy” to win over and infiltrate foreign legislators, creating the illusion of external support for their independence-seeking activities. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We advise certain US politicians to stop the practice of “using Taiwan to contain China.” Playing with fire on the Taiwan question is very dangerous, and those who play with fire will burn themselves.\nShe said that Lai Ching-te's remarks have once again exposed his independence-seeking nature. No matter how they lie and whatever titles they concoct, Taiwan is not a country. The process of national reunification is unstoppable, and apart from realizing unification with the mainland, Taiwan has no other future option.\nZhu Fenglian said that we solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and no one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220126_12403725.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-01-27","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","The EU has launched a WTO case against China over its “discriminatory trade practices” against Lithuania. Does the foreign ministry have any comment and will this action impact plans for the China-EU summit in March?","I would refer you to competent authorities for specific questions about trade. What I can tell you is that China has been following WTO rules. I want to stress that the ins and outs of the fraught China-Lithuania relations are very clear. The so-called China’s “coercion” of Lithuania is groundless and distorts facts.\nThe problem between China and Lithuania is a political not an economic one. They were caused by Lithuania's acts in bad faith that hurt China’s interests, not China’s pressure on Lithuania. They are issues between China and Lithuania, not China and the EU. We urge the Lithuanian side to immediately mend its ways, avoid willingly act as a pawn for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and anti-China forces, and return to the right track of adhering to the one-China principle. We would also remind the EU to tell right from wrong, stay wary of Lithuania’s attempts to take China-EU relations hostage and advise Lithuania to follow other EU members in fulfilling the political commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties with the PRC.\nAs for your question about whether the EU’s moves will impact plans for the China-EU summit, I would like to tell you that the two sides are in communication on high-level exchanges. We will release information in a timely manner if there's any.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347216.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220127_10635286.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson opening announcement (no press Q)","According to reports in Taiwanese media, a PLA WZ-10 attack helicopter recently entered the so-called “southwest air defense identification zone” of Taiwan. It not only crossed the “median line of the Taiwan Strait,” but also penetrated 900 meters into the other side, drawing attention from the island's media. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. Where does this “median line of the Taiwan Strait” come from? The Chinese People's Liberation Army bears the sacred mission of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Relevant combat training activities are necessary actions taken entirely in response to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Since the beginning of this year, several members of the US Congress have made illicit visits to Taiwan. Among them, Senator Graham, when meeting with Tsai Ing-wen, threatened to “make the Chinese mainland pay a price.” Taiwanese media also reported that several US House members jointly sent a letter calling on President Biden to visit Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing all of China; this is the common consensus of the international community and the recognized norm of international relations. The visit to Taiwan by U.S. lawmakers and their provocative remarks are purely a 'political show' for show-off purposes, and China firmly opposes them. Those who clamor to 'make mainland China pay the price' should first prepare to pay the price themselves. On the issue of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the Chinese People's Liberation Army has always dared to act decisively and, when it fights, is sure to win.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","近日，美日外长、防长举行“2+2”线上会议并发表联合声明，恶意渲染所谓“中国威胁”，声称中国正破坏基于规则的国际秩序，给地区和世界带来挑战。此外，美日还大肆炒作台海议题，有专家认为，美日正把台海政策向实操化推进。请问中方对此有何评论？","According to a report on the website of the Ministry of National Defense on the 7th, Defense Ministry spokesperson Tan Kefei, answering questions regarding the incident in which Australia hyped up “interference” by Chinese military aircraft against Australian military aircraft, said: Australia has reversed right and wrong, repeatedly spread false information, and advocated creating confrontation and opposition. China firmly opposes this. We solemnly warn Australia to immediately stop similar dangerous provocative acts, strictly restrain the actions of its sea and air forces, or else bear all the serious consequences arising therefrom.\nA reporter asked: The Australian Department of Defence recently issued a statement saying that on May 26, while an Australian military aircraft was conducting a reconnaissance mission in airspace over the South China Sea, it was intercepted by a Chinese military aircraft, and the safety of the Australian aircraft and personnel was threatened. What is China's comment on this?\nTan Kefei said: On May 26, an Australian P-8A anti-submarine patrol aircraft entered the airspace near China's Xisha Islands and conducted close reconnaissance. Disregarding China's repeated warnings, it continuously approached China's Xisha territorial airspace. The Southern Theater Command of the PLA organized sea and air forces to identify and verify the Australian military aircraft, and issued a warning and drove it away. The Australian military aircraft seriously threatened China's sovereignty and security. The countermeasures taken by the Chinese military were professional, safe, reasonable, and lawful. Australia has reversed right and wrong, repeatedly spread false information, and advocated creating confrontation and opposition. China firmly opposes this. We solemnly warn Australia to immediately stop similar dangerous provocative acts, strictly restrain the actions of its sea and air forces, or else bear all the serious consequences arising therefrom.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, on June 8 the U.S. government announced approval of a new arms sales plan for Taiwan, intending to provide Taiwan with spare parts for naval vessels and related technical support valued at 120 million U.S. dollars. What comments do you have on this?","The United States’ sale of weapons and provision of military technical support to Taiwan, China, seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué. It crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs, seriously damages China’s sovereignty and security interests, and seriously endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposes this.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. China must be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified. China urges the US side to immediately cancel the above-mentioned arms sales plans to Taiwan, stop selling weapons to Taiwan and military contacts between the US and Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, so as to avoid further damage to China-US relations and military-to-military relations.\nWe solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and certain external forces: “Relying on foreign powers to seek independence” has no way out, and “using Taiwan to contain China” is doomed to fail. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will take forceful measures to resolutely defeat any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","中印第十四轮军长级会谈后，有印度媒体评论，此次会谈虽然未能取得实质进展但具有建设性。另据美国媒体报道，白宫发言人表示，美方正密切关注中印边境局势，对中国“胁迫”印度等邻国的企图予以关注。请问中方对此有何评论？","On the afternoon of June 10, local time, Wu Qian, spokesperson of the Chinese Ministry of National Defense, held a briefing for Chinese and foreign media at the Shangri-La Dialogue in Singapore on the China-U.S. defense ministers' talks.\nWu Qian said that Chinese Defense Minister Wei Fenghe reaffirmed China's firm position on the Taiwan question during the meeting. Wei Fenghe said that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's sacred territory, and that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. Attempts to “use Taiwan to contain China” are doomed to fail.\nWei Fenghe pointed out that the U.S. side recently announced again arms sales to Taiwan, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously undermines China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously damages China-U.S. relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this.\nWei Fenghe stressed that if anyone dares to split Taiwan from China, the Chinese military will certainly fight at any cost and resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-01-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Zhang Youxia, Vice Chairman of the Central Military Commission of China, recently met with Pakistani Army Chief of Staff Bajwa in Qingdao. Please further introduce the state of China-Pakistan military relations.","Amid a complex and ever-changing international and regional situation, the Chinese and Pakistani militaries and nations have consistently maintained healthy and stable exchanges and cooperation, and their “all-weather” friendship is unbreakable. Military-to-military relations are the linchpin of China-Pakistan friendship. The Chinese and Pakistani militaries have carried out all-round, broad-field, multi-level exchanges, and cooperation between the two sides in areas such as defense and security consultations, troop training, personnel training, academy exchanges and non-traditional security continues to deepen, playing a positive role in safeguarding each country’s sovereignty, security and development interests. The Chinese military is willing to further strengthen strategic communication with the Pakistani side, consolidate the foundation for cooperation, help China-Pakistan relations advance further, and accelerate the building of an even closer China-Pakistan community with a shared future in the new era.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10126917.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-01-28","Zhao Lijian","Dragon TV","According to reports, Lithuanian President Gitanas Nausėda has called on the country’s officials to fix the name of the so-called “Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania”, noting that the office’s name in Chinese “was a key factor” in the conflict with China. What is China’s comment?","China has articulated on the nature of the Taiwan-related issue concerning Lithuania on many occasions. Lithuania is clear about crux of the issue. If the Lithuanian side truly wants to ease tensions with China, then it should demonstrate sincerity, correct mistakes with concrete actions, and return to the right track of adhering to the one-China principle. Muddling through the issue by playing with words simply does not work.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347217.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220128_10636086.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-01-28","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Yesterday US Vice President Kamala Harris said that she spoke with her Taiwanese counterpart in Honduras where the two traveled to attend the inauguration ceremony of the newly-elected President of Honduras. Harris said they talked about common interests in Central America, not about China’s mainland. I wonder if you have any comment on this and how do you view these discussions?","There is no Taiwanese “vice president” since Taiwan is a province of China. China always opposes all forms of official exchanges between the US and Taiwan. Lai Ching-te claims that his approach toward “Taiwan independence” is pragmatic. He made “Taiwan independence” comments on many occasions and obstinately insists on a “Taiwan independence” platform. The US should abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiques, take China’s position and concerns seriously, stop all forms of official interactions with Taiwan and avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347217.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202201/t20220128_10636086.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-01-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 28 dispatch — Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to questions on the 28th, saying: The DPP authorities are colluding with external forces and continuously engaging in provocations to seek 'independence.' By treating their role as a pawn of the United States in containing and opposing China as a so-called 'diplomatic breakthrough,' they have placed…","Zhu Fenglian said: We urge the U.S. government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, to fulfill its solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, and to stop playing with fire on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202201/t20220128_12404250.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-01-31","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest does not say whether this was a question or an a","According to reports, the US State Department website recently updated its “US-Taiwan Relations Fact Sheet,” deleting statements such as “Taiwan is part of China” and “the US does not support Taiwan independence.” A US State Department spokesperson later explained that US policy toward Taiwan has not changed, that the US still adheres to the one-China policy, and that it does not support “Taiwan independence.”…","The U.S. State Department's statements on Taiwan policy are self-contradictory, exposing a scheme that is plain to all: Sima Zhao's intent is obvious, known to every passerby. For some time, the U.S. side has continuously hollowed out and emptied the one-China principle, attempting to use a 'salami-slicing' approach to achieve its scheme of 'using Taiwan to contain China,' which is utterly wishful thinking. We warn some people on the U.S. side: if you slice salami on the Taiwan question, you will surely cut your own hand. The Chinese People's Liberation Army stands at the ready and will take all necessary measures to crush any form of 'Taiwan independence' separatist scheme and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/01-31/9666379.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-02-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 3 – TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 3rd that on February 2, Ms. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairwoman of the Kuomintang (KMT), arrived in Beijing and will attend the opening ceremony of the Beijing Winter Olympics at the invitation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220203_12405260.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-02-07","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, the US House of Representatives passed the America COMPETES Act of 2022 on February 5. Do you have any comment?","We noted that the US House of Representatives passed the so-called America COMPETES Act of 2022. The China-related content in this Act is steeped in Cold War mentality and zero-sum game. It denigrates China’s development path and domestic as well as foreign policy, clamors for strategic competition with China, and makes wanton remarks on issues relating to Taiwan, Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Tibet. China firmly opposes it.\nAs we have said repeatedly, how the US develops itself and enhances its competitiveness is its own business, but it shouldn’t make an issue out of China, still less use it as a pretext to meddle in China’s domestic affairs and harm China’s interests. This Act once again exposes the hegemonic and bullying practice of the US, which in a fundamental sense runs counter to the trend of our times and people’s shared aspiration for peace, development and cooperation. Eventually it will only hurt the US’ interests.\nThe US should discard the Cold War mentality and zero-sum game, view China’s development and China-US relations in an objective and rational light, delete the negative content regarding China in the bill, stop reviewing and pushing the Act, and stop undermining China-US relations and cooperation in important areas.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347218.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220207_10639812.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-08","Zhao Lijian","NHK","A question on the import restrictions on Japanese food following the Fukushima nuclear accident. The Taiwan region announced today that it would lift import restrictions after countries including Singapore and the US removed restriction policies last year. Can you share with us the position of China’s mainland on the import restrictions on Japanese food? How do you see the Taiwan region’s lifting of the restrictions?","After the nuclear leak accident happened in the Fukushima nuclear power plant in March 2011, to prevent radioactively contaminated Japanese food from entering China’s mainland, China has strengthened regulatory and supervision measures on food imports from Japan, and consistently conducted risk assessment on radioactive contamination of Japanese food to prevent importing food that fail to meet requirements so as to ensure people’s life, health and safety.\nWe believe our Taiwan compatriots are clear-eyed about what the DPP authorities have done on issues related to the life, health and safety of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347219.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220208_10640207.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-08","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, Lithuania’s Foreign Minister Gabrielius Landsbergis is visiting Australia. He said in an interview before the visit that this trip is about how Lithuania and Australia can help each other in response to China’s coercion and trade sanctions. Landsbergis is also slated to make a speech on “The Rules-based World Order Under Attack: The Cases of Ukraine and Taiwan” at the Australian Strategic…","The ins and outs of the fraught China-Lithuania relations are very clear. China has responded properly in defense of its legitimate rights and interests and international justice, which is completely legitimate and lawful. China always follows WTO rules. The so-called “coercion” of China against Lithuania is purely made out of thin air. China urges Lithuania to face up to the objective facts, mend its ways, and come back to the right track of adhering to the one-China principle. It should stop confounding right with wrong and maliciously hyping things up, let alone trying to rope other countries into ganging up on China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347219.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220208_10640207.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-08","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US has approved a possible $100 million arms sale to Taiwan. What’s China’s comment?","The US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this and strongly condemns this.\nChina urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately revoke the arms sales plan, and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan. China will take legitimate and strong measures to resolutely defend its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347219.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220208_10640207.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-02-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 8 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 8th that the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to provoke “Taiwan independence” and using the hard-earned money of the people of Taiwan to buy weapons cannot save “Taiwan independence” from its inevitable demise. It will only aggravate tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait and push Taiwan step by step toward disaster.\nA reporter asked: On February 7, a U.S. government department decided to sell to the Taiwan region of China the “Patriot Missile Engineering Services” (IESP) and “Battlefield Surveillance” (FSP) program plans, valued at about 100 million U.S. dollars. The DPP authorities immediately made a statement expressing thanks, saying it was “U.S. support for Taiwan.” What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above statement when answering the question.\nMa Xiaoguang also pointed out that we urge the U.S. side to stop playing with fire on Taiwan-related issues, correct its wrong action of selling arms to Taiwan, stop using “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to harm China's interests, and return to the correct path of abiding by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220208_12406213.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-02-09","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","First, Somaliland’s officials visited Taiwan today and the two sides had high-level interactions. Do you have any comment? Second, February 21 this year marks the 50th anniversary of former US President Nixon’s visit to China. Does China have any plan for commemorative activities?","On your first question, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a widely recognized norm governing international relations and the common consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities are not only seeking secession, but also fanning the flames to undermine the independence and unification of other countries, harming others without benefiting themselves. They will only end up shooting themselves in the foot.\nOn your second question, I am not aware of the specifics yet. I will keep you informed when I get more information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347220.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220209_10640532.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-02-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to Japanese media reports, a draft of Japan's 2022 Defense White Paper was recently exposed. The draft states that stability in the Taiwan Strait is crucial to Japan's security, and that Japan will continue to pay close attention to the situation in the Taiwan Strait. Another report says that a delegation of the Youth Bureau of Japan's Liberal Democratic Party recently visited Taiwan, and a lawmaker…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and Japan has no right to meddle or interfere. As everyone knows, Japan once seized Taiwan through aggression and expansion, and colonially ruled Taiwan for 50 years, committing crimes too numerous to recount. Japan has absolutely no qualification to comment on the Taiwan question.\nFor historical and practical reasons, Japan's military and security moves have long drawn close attention from the international community. We demand that Japan deeply learn the lessons of history, genuinely reflect on its own responsibility for its crimes, and win the trust of its Asian neighbors through concrete actions.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/02-09/9671883.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-02-11","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","Two questions that both have something to do with Japan. First, Taiwan confirmed that Tsai Ing-wen and former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe had a phone conversation in January, during which she thanked Abe and the Japanese government for their support to Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment? Second, the ROK President expressed regret over Japan’s bid to have a group of gold mines on Sado Island…","On your first question, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes official interaction in any form between countries having diplomatic ties with China and Taiwan. We solemnly urge certain Japanese politicians not to harm China’s sovereignty in any way and not to send wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces in any way. We also have this solemn warning to Taiwan authorities: all attempts to advance its agenda by soliciting foreign support are doomed to fail.\nOn your second question, we responded to related questions on other occasions. Forced recruitment and enslavement of laborers is a grave crime committed by the Japanese militarism during its overseas aggression and colonial rule. In a similar bid previously, Japan admitted that there was forced labor at some of these sites involving workers from China, the Korean Peninsula and other Asian countries, and promised to set up an information center to honor the victims, but it never fulfilled the promise. Now ignoring the painful memories of its neighbors, Japan is trying to make a similar new bid, which will only trigger stronger indignation and opposition. Japan should face up to history, adopt an honest and responsible attitude and take concrete actions to properly handle issues left over from history and win the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347222.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220211_10641427.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-11","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Daily","According to reports, US Secretary of State Blinken said in an interview with Australian media outlets that China’s trade sanctions on Australia have backfired and b y standing up to Beijing, Australia “set an incredibly powerful example” for the world . “I think China has lost more than Australia has in its efforts to squeeze Australia economically,” he said, adding that Beijing would be “thinking twice about…","With regard to “coercion”, no one has a better claim to the title of “master of coercion” than the US. Speaking of “coercion”, the US government forced the military government of Haiti to step down in 1994, and referred to that as “a textbook example of coercive diplomacy”. In 2003, it explicitly characterized $30.3 billion additional military expenses for “coercive diplomacy” as incurred expenses. The US government went all out to hobble competitors like Huawei of China, Alstom of France and Toshiba of Japan and used coercion to force the Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co (TSMC), Samsung and other companies to provide chip supply chain data. These are textbook examples of economic coercion.\nI would like to reiterate that China always proceeds from the lawful rights and interests of domestic industries and the safety of consumers and adopts appropriate measures on imported products in strict compliance with Chinese laws and regulations as well as WTO rules. This is fully justified, lawful and beyond reproach. The label of “economic coercion” cannot be pinned on China. All attempts to gang up with others to misrepresent facts and resort to malicious hype-up are bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347222.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220211_10641427.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-02-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On February 11, the US government released the so-called “Indo-Pacific Strategy Report,” which contains negative content concerning Taiwan. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 14 (electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang responded to questions on the 14th, pointing out that Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China’s territory, and Taiwan’s future can and must be decided jointly by all Chinese people. National reunification is where Taiwan’s future lies and where its interests are tied. The US “Indo-Pacific Strategy” seriously interferes in China’s internal affairs on the Taiwan question, violates the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, and causes harm to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose it.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that we urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and not to play with fire on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, serving as pawns to oppose and contain China, will inevitably end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220214_12407305.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 15 -- Recently, the Ministry of Education made arrangements for matters concerning the 2022 admission of Taiwan students to master's and bachelor's programs at mainland universities, and related enrollment work has begun. At a briefing on the 15th in response to a question, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, introduced that for bachelor's program…","Ma Xiaoguang said that through the new admissions system, the registration and admission process for Taiwanese students will be further optimized, specifically in the following ways:\nFirst, registration is more convenient for applicants. Under past admissions arrangements, although applicants could receive admission offers from multiple schools, because the admissions progress of each school differed, the waiting time was long. This year, while the system retains the ability for applicants to \"apply to multiple schools within one tier\" and receive provisional admission eligibility from several schools, it also enables applicants to view admission results all at once with one click and select the one university they most desire. At the same time, the system will also provide convenience for applicants' future student registration.\nSecond, applicants have more opportunities to choose. The system innovatively designs a two-round admissions function of \"first-round registration and admission plus solicitation of preferences.\" Applicants who were not admitted in the first round, or who newly register, may take part in the solicitation of preferences, giving applicants more chances of admission. Applicants should pay close attention to the release time of provisional admission results and promptly log in to the system to confirm their admission results. Applicants who do not confirm by the deadline will be deemed to have given up their eligibility and may not take part in the solicitation of preferences registration. After applicants confirm, universities with insufficient sources of students, universities that have not completed their enrollment plans, or universities that increase their admission quotas may enroll additional students through the solicitation of preferences.\nThird, admissions services are more detailed. The system has created a registration and login interface for applicants, supporting an \"automatic screening\" function. After applicants enter their \"Xuece\" (learning test) scores, they can see the corresponding schools, majors, admissions brochure links and other information that meets the application requirements. To prevent applicants from missing the admission result confirmation step, the system will also send reminders by \"mobile text message plus email\" at that time, and provide a concise handbook and consultation service hotline to guide Taiwanese students in registering online.\nMa Xiaoguang also introduced that for the 2022 cross-strait master's degree admissions arrangements, due to the pandemic, registration will run from February 10 to 25, online confirmation must be completed before March 11, and admission tickets will be printed from March 21 to 31. Master's degree entrance examinations, both the preliminary and retest stages, are organized by each university on its own. The examination time, location, format and requirements are determined by each university and announced to the public. Applicants are requested to pay close attention to the specific notices from each university in a timely manner.\nMa Xiaoguang said that Taiwanese applicants and their parents are requested to pay timely attention to admissions information from mainland universities. The \"Admissions Information Network for Mainland (Chinese Mainland) Universities Enrolling Students from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan\" (website:\nhttps://www.gatzs.com.cn\n), the official website under the Ministry of Education that is specifically responsible for admissions matters concerning Taiwan, publishes authoritative information first.\nMa Xiaoguang said that since 2020, although the COVID-19 pandemic has raged across the globe, localities and universities on the mainland have strictly implemented epidemic prevention and control measures, and not one of the more than 10,000 Taiwanese students studying at mainland universities has been infected, and vaccines have been administered to everyone who should receive them. In 2021, the number of Taiwanese students applying to study at mainland universities continued to increase.\nHe said that relevant departments on the mainland will, as always, provide convenience and services for Taiwanese students coming to the mainland to study and pursue further education, and help Taiwanese young people realize their life dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220215_12407574.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-02-21","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","After the US announced a plan to sell $100 million worth of arms to Taiwan on February 7, China’s Foreign Ministry Spokesperson said in response that China will take legitimate and strong measures to resolutely defend its sovereignty and security interests and people may wait and see what measures China will take. Do you have more information to offer at the moment?","The US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this.\nTo safeguard China’s sovereignty and security interests, the Chinese government has decided to take countermeasures in accordance with relevant stipulations in China’s Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law on the infringing acts of Raytheon Technologies Corporation and Lockheed Martin Corporation, both of which are military industrial enterprises that have long participated in the US’ arms sales to China’s Taiwan region.\nChina once again urges the US government and relevant sides to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan. China will continue to take all necessary measures to resolutely uphold its sovereignty and security interests in light of the situation’s development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347228.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220221_10644054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-21","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Media reports in Taiwan say that former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo will visit Taiwan on March 3 and meet with Tsai Ing-wen. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","Mike Pompeo has long been sanctioned by China for his anti-China remarks and actions. The DPP authorities in Taiwan, in seeking independence by soliciting US support, is playing with fire and will end up being consumed by it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347228.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220221_10644054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-22","Wang Wenbin","The New York Times","Does China see any parallels between Russia’s assertion that Ukraine is not a separate state and Beijing’s assertion that Taiwan is a part of China?","I just made clear China’s position on the Ukraine issue.\nSince you mentioned the Taiwan question, I would like to stress that there is but one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact. The one-China principle is a universally-recognized norm governing international relations. The Chinese people have the strong resolve, determination and capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347229.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220222_10644486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-23","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","Spokesperson of the Taiwan region’s leader and the head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department compared the Ukraine issue to the Taiwan question, and expressed the hope that the international community will continue to provide Taiwan with weapons so that China’s mainland dare not “invade” Taiwan by force. Some people also said that we should not make Ukraine’s today Taiwan’s tomorrow. Do you have any comment?","It is unwise of certain people of the Taiwan authorities to latch on to and exploit the Ukraine issue to their advantage.\nTaiwan for sure is not Ukraine. Taiwan has always been an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm governing international relations. The Taiwan region’s peace hinges on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, rather than fawning on foreign forces for arms sales and military support. “Taiwan independence” only leads to a dead end. No one shall have any illusion or make any miscalculation on this issue.\nSince the Ukraine crisis broke out, Taiwan has been frequently mentioned by some people. Some of their remarks fully reveal their lack of knowledge of the history of the Taiwan question. I’d like to take this occasion to share some basic facts with you.\nIt is common knowledge that the Taiwan question was caused by a civil war, and there is political confrontation between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait due to that civil war. However, China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided and cannot be divided. This is the status quo of the Taiwan question.\nThis year marks the 50th anniversary of President Nixon’s visit to China. During that visit in February 1972, the two sides issued the China-US Joint Communiqué in Shanghai, marking the normalization of China-US relations. There are very important lines on the Taiwan question in the Shanghai Communiqué. The U.S. side stated: There are essential differences between China and the United States in their social systems and foreign policies. However, the two sides agreed that countries, regardless of their social systems, should conduct their relations on the principles of respect for the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all states, nonaggression against other states, noninterference in the internal affairs of other states, equality and mutual benefit, and peaceful coexistence. The U.S. side also declared: The United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position. It reaffirms its interest in a peaceful settlement of the Taiwan question by the Chinese themselves. With this prospect in mind, it affirms the ultimate objective of the withdrawal of all U.S. forces and military installations from Taiwan. In the meantime, it will progressively reduce its forces and military installations on Taiwan.\nIn the August 17 Communiqué issued by the Chinese and US governments in 1982, the US government stated that it attaches great importance to its relations with China, and reiterates that it has no intention of infringing on Chinese sovereignty and territorial integrity, or interfering in China’s internal affairs, or pursuing a policy of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” The United States Government states that it does not seek to carry out a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan, that its arms sales to Taiwan will not exceed, either in qualitative or in quantitative terms, the level of those supplied in recent years since the establishment of diplomatic relations between the United States and China, and that it intends gradually to reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution.\nThese are some historical facts that I’d like to take this opportunity to share with you about Taiwan and the relationship between the US and Taiwan, so you may have some idea as to whether the US honors its commitment or not. In the context of what’s happening now in the world, I believe this will help you to better understand the Taiwan question. On this issue, we would also like to advise certain people, including some on the Taiwan island, not to have any illusion or make any miscalculation on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347230.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220223_10644870.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on February 23, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. Let me first extend New Year greetings to everyone. I will host today's press conference. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","During this year’s Spring Festival, compatriots on both sides of the Strait exchanged New Year greetings through various forms, and many Taiwanese entertainers took part in mainland arts performances, which were well received. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. During the Spring Festival of the Year of the Renyin Tiger, compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait exchanged New Year greetings in various forms and celebrated the festival together. People from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait posted New Year greeting videos in diverse styles, using internet platforms to send New Year wishes to relatives and friends across the Strait. A wave of \"cloud New Year greetings\" swept across the civilian sphere on both sides, and the topic \"New Year blessings across the Strait\" kept trending online. Fang Hanqi, 96, a leading authority on journalism on the mainland, and Li Zhan, 98, a leading authority on journalism in Taiwan, Bai Xianyong, a Taiwanese writer, and Yu Jiulin, a Kunqu opera performer from the mainland, Gao Binghan, a Taiwanese veteran, and his younger brother Gao Bingtao, who lives on the mainland, as well as students from Guanghe, Gansu, and Taiwanese youth they met through exchanges, exchanged New Year greetings in videos that were widely circulated online. Many netizens who reposted these videos left comments saying they were \"warmed.\" In the warm New Year greetings that touched hearts, everyone felt the close bond of \"Cross-Strait Families Are One Family\" and the joy of the big family of the Chinese nation.\nMany Taiwan businesspeople, young Taiwanese and Taiwanese entertainers who spent the New Year on the mainland also posted New Year greeting videos on social media, sharing their experiences of local customs, expressing their longing for and concern about family and friends on the island, and their good wishes for compatriots on both sides, full of sincere warmth and deep affection. They invested and started businesses, studied and found jobs, or developed their careers in the performing arts on the mainland. They integrated into this place, met warm-hearted people, and gained their own small happiness and a bright future.\nDuring the Spring Festival, more than 20 Taiwanese performers also appeared in the CCTV Spring Festival Gala and Spring Festival art performances across the mainland, presenting wonderful performances and holiday greetings to audiences alongside mainland artists. They truly showed warm moments of Chinese people celebrating the festival together and sharing reunion, drawing attention and affection from people on both sides of the Strait.\nThe heartfelt New Year interactions between compatriots on both sides once again demonstrate that the natural bond of compatriots on both sides, who share the same language, culture and blood, cannot be severed by any force, and that the major trend of civilian exchanges across the Taiwan Strait cannot be blocked by any force.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409299.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","What is the spokesperson's assessment of Taiwan athletes' participation in the Beijing Winter Olympics and of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises participating in the Olympics in various forms?","The Beijing Winter Olympics was successfully held. Under the challenge of the still-raging global pandemic, it presented the world with a simple, safe and splendid Olympic event, earning high recognition and praise from compatriots on both sides of the Strait and from the international community. This is an important opportunity for compatriots on both sides to move toward the future hand in hand. Chairman Wang Yang met with Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang, and Wu Chengdian, chairman of the New Party, who were invited to attend the opening and closing ceremonies of the Winter Olympics respectively, and conveyed General Secretary Xi Jinping's New Year greetings to the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan. Compatriots in Taiwan participated in the Beijing Winter Olympics in various ways, jointly contributing to the grand event and sharing its glory. This is a vivid interpretation of the Olympic spirit and a true reflection of \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.\"\nAthletes from the ice and snow sports of both sides of the Strait gathered in Beijing and together displayed the sporting spirit of Chinese athletes. The Chinese Taipei team had a total of 4 athletes participating in the Beijing Winter Olympics, including speed skater Huang Yuting, luge athlete Lin Xinrong, and skiers Li Wenyi and He Bingrui. They fought hard on the field, and compatriots on the mainland cheered them on. In the women's giant slalom event in alpine skiing, 19-year-old skier Li Wenyi persevered in the face of setbacks and completed her run successfully amid the encouragement of the spectators on site, which was moving. When speed skater Huang Yuting took the field, the spectators on site gave her warm applause and cheers.\nThe broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan and Taiwan-funded enterprises have added to the Beijing Winter Olympics with concrete actions. Five Taiwan compatriots participated in the Olympic torch relay, and eight Taiwan journalists took part in the reporting work of the Winter Olympics. More than 30 Taiwan students studying at universities in Beijing served as volunteers for the event and devoted themselves to Olympic service work. Taiwan youth in Beijing established a Winter Olympics city volunteer service team to carry out volunteer service and held the \"Cross-Strait Creative Theme Activities for the Winter Olympics.\" More than a thousand Taiwan youth and students across the mainland eagerly participated in various activities to welcome the Winter Olympics. Musicians from both sides of the Strait jointly created songs such as \"I'm Waiting for You in Beijing\" to welcome the Winter Olympics, and more than 10 Taiwan entertainers participated in recording and singing the theme song of the Winter Olympics, \"Together Toward the Future.\" Some Taiwan enterprises participated in services such as clothing production, equipment manufacturing and pipeline network construction for the Beijing Winter Olympics. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait participated in and followed the Beijing Winter Olympics in various ways, bringing their hearts closer and holding hands more tightly.\nWe believe that on the new journey in which the Chinese nation is marching confidently toward the second centenary goal and realizing the great rejuvenation, compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will certainly not be absent. They will surely become important participants and beneficiaries, and they will also become contributors to and witnesses of the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Let us move toward the future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409298.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","In recent years, many places on the mainland have established cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites. Please introduce the development of these bases and demonstration sites, and the situation of the bases newly established in 2021.","To help Taiwan’s young people come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams, we have actively built platforms. Since 2015, the Taiwan Affairs Office has licensed the establishment of 78 cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites, of which 59 are bases and 19 are demonstration sites, covering all kinds of platforms such as industrial parks, schools, business incubators, enterprises and social organizations. These bases and demonstration sites hold various exchange activities, provide internship and employment positions and coaching and training for Taiwan youth, and help Taiwan youth intern, find employment, start businesses and innovate on the mainland. According to statistics, as of the end of 2021, the bases and demonstration sites had served and hosted more than 4,500 Taiwan-invested enterprises and entrepreneurial teams, more than 20,000 Taiwan youth had interned, found jobs or started businesses in total, and nearly 200,000 person-times had participated in various exchange activities.\nIn 2021, the Taiwan Affairs Office newly established two cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases, namely the Sichuan Chengdu (Xingdian) Cross-Strait New Economy Entrepreneurship Park and the Changsha Furong District Cross-Strait Youth Cultural Industry Incubation Base in Hunan. Through models focused on serving start-up enterprises and hiring professional teams to operate them, these bases provide Taiwan youth and entrepreneurial teams with services such as business incubation, business consulting, and capital and market matching.\nGoing forward, we will work with relevant parties in various localities to continue supporting these bases and demonstration sites in growing bigger and stronger, creating a better environment and providing better services for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland. We also welcome more Taiwan young people to intern, find employment and start businesses at these bases and demonstration sites, so as to achieve greater development for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Ku Kuan-min recently claimed, “If ‘constitution-making’ cannot be resolved through a referendum, perhaps only revolution remains.” Relevant figures on the island have criticized him for inciting a so-called “revolution” and have called on Tsai Ing-wen to respond promptly and state her position. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, including seeking “de jure Taiwan independence” through so-called “drafting a new constitution and amending the constitution.” A handful of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements on the island, in order to serve their own private interests, arbitrarily manipulate the so-called “constitutional referendum” and clamor for a so-called “revolution.” They disregard the safety of Taiwan's people and will push Taiwan into an abyss of no return. If the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces miscalculate the situation, take desperate risks, and touch the red line, we will take resolute measures to crush them decisively. Let it not be said that we did not give warning.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409296.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Some mainland scholars recently said that the mainland should formulate a “Unification Law,” with the core being to jointly formulate with Taiwan compatriots a “one country, two systems” plan for Taiwan. Other mainland scholars believe that the above proposals do not mention the Anti-Secession Law, but instead propose setting up another “Unification Law” and set three preconditions for resolving the Taiwan…","In recent times, quite a few scholars on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have offered views on how to achieve the reunification of the country, reflecting their deliberation on how to advance the reunification process. We will not comment on specific views. I would like to stress three points:\nFirst, resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. With the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, the historical task of completely reunifying the motherland must be accomplished, and it certainly can be accomplished. Reunification is a settled conclusion; it is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. The timing and momentum for resolving the Taiwan question have always been on the side of the forces advancing national reunification.\nSecond, \"peaceful reunification, one country, two systems\" is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification. It fully takes into account the actual situation in Taiwan and is conducive to Taiwan's long-term stability and security after reunification. Adhering to peaceful reunification demonstrates the righteousness of the nation and a cherishing of the value of peace and the well-being of compatriots, reflecting a deep sense of responsibility to the nation and to future generations. Achieving national reunification by peaceful means best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including compatriots in Taiwan. Peaceful reunification means equal consultation and joint deliberation on reunification. On the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to hold dialogue and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and individuals on cross-Strait political issues and matters related to advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, broadly exchange views, seek social consensus, and advance political negotiations.\nThird, national laws such as the Constitution and the Anti-Secession Law already contain clear provisions for resolving the Taiwan question and promoting national reunification, and they provide solid legal safeguards for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing national reunification. The Constitution stipulates that Taiwan is a sacred part of the territory of the People's Republic of China, and that completing the great cause of reunifying the motherland is the sacred duty of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan. The Anti-Secession Law is based on the Constitution. It is an important component of the institutional system for upholding \"one country, two systems\" and promoting the peaceful reunification of the motherland, and it is an important guide for fulfilling the political responsibility and mission of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and promoting reunification. In the 17 years since the Anti-Secession Law was implemented, it has already played, and will continue to play, a unique and important role in deterring \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of national reunification. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces continue to provoke and coerce, or even cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409297.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, an article published by a mainland media outlet named two representatives of the people from the KMT as being “covert Taiwan independence” supporters. Both have denied it. KMT Chairman Eric Chu reiterated the KMT's position on this matter. What is your comment on this?","I must point out that although the two sides of the Strait have not been fully unified, China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. Regarding the long-standing political differences between the two sides, compatriots on both sides should, on the basis of the one-China principle, pool wisdom through dialogue and communication, seek common ground while setting aside differences, and seek a way to resolve them. The DPP authorities colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke is the root cause of cross-Strait tensions and turmoil and the disruption of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We hope that responsible political parties and figures on the island will join us in jointly opposing and containing “Taiwan independence,” eliminating the root of “Taiwan independence,” advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, consolidating the foundation for peaceful reunification, and upholding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409295.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, the DPP authorities, in coordination with public opinion in the United States and Western countries, have hyped up Taiwan and Ukraine as comparable, claiming “we deeply empathize with the situation in Ukraine.” What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “empathize” is entirely self-indulgent. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Recently, the DPP authorities, in coordination with U.S. and Western public opinion, have maliciously hyped the so-called mainland “military threat” using the Ukraine issue. This harbors the sinister intent of internationalizing the Taiwan question and inciting “anti-China” and “resist-China” populism on the island. It is entirely political manipulation for the narrow interests of one party. It must be pointed out that the root cause of the current tension in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, in collusion with external forces, have continuously engaged in provocations to seek “independence.” All necessary actions we take to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, with the aim of fundamentally safeguarding the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220223_12409294.htm"],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, when a Taiwan publishing house printed and distributed the book “Spicy China” by a mainland author, it replaced every instance of “mainland” (大陆) in the book with “China” (中国), resulting in absurd sentences such as “Columbus discovered New China.” What comments do you have on this?","This farce that has gone haywire is yet another bitter fruit and another freak born of the DPP authorities' push for “de-Sinicization.” The DPP authorities have schemed to incite confrontation across the Strait and have forcibly severed Taiwan's flesh-and-blood ties with Chinese culture and the Chinese nation. They have gone so off-key and anti-intellectual that it is both the greatest joke under heaven and an endless harm to Taiwan's society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","The DPP authorities recently passed draft amendments to parts of the so-called “Security Act” and the “Regulations on Relations between the Peoples of the Two Sides,” adding content such as an “economic espionage crime” targeting the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","Cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation have brought tangible benefits to people on both sides of the Strait, especially to Taiwan businesses and residents. This is a well-known fact that no one can deny. For some time now, the DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, have used various pretexts and, through so-called \"law amendments\" and \"regulation revisions,\" ruthlessly and increasingly obstructed and restricted normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They have even stigmatized this normal exchange and cooperation, which is shameful. These reckless actions by the DPP authorities will only harm the interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台《台海之声》和看台海新媒体记者","The 2022 Taiwan graduate student admission examinations of mainland universities are imminent. Under the current complex and severe situation in the Taiwan Strait and the impact of the epidemic, the number of Taiwan students coming to the mainland to study continues to rise. How do you view the phenomenon of Taiwan students eagerly “coming to the mainland to study”?","In recent years, mainland universities have accelerated the construction of world-class universities and world-class disciplines, and their educational quality has continuously improved, with more and more Taiwan students voluntarily choosing to study on the mainland. Since 2020, although the COVID-19 epidemic has ravaged the world, localities and universities on the mainland have strictly implemented epidemic prevention and control measures. Not one of the tens of thousands of Taiwan students studying at mainland universities has been infected, and they have also achieved full vaccination wherever vaccines were recommended. In 2021, the number of Taiwan students applying to study at mainland universities continued to increase. Recently, the Ministry of Education made arrangements for matters concerning the enrollment of Taiwan students in master's and undergraduate programs at mainland universities in 2022, and related enrollment work has been launched. We issued a press release on the 15th of this month introducing in detail some new changes to the 2022 enrollment policy for Taiwan. After adjustment, the registration and admission procedures for Taiwan students will be further optimized, making registration more convenient for candidates, offering more choice opportunities, and making enrollment services more meticulous. We believe that with the continued rapid and comprehensive development of the mainland's economy and society, broad development opportunities have been and will continue to be provided to Taiwan students. We sincerely hope that broad Taiwan students will seize opportunities and win the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","The head of Taiwan’s external affairs department claimed that the mainland is attempting to “economically isolate” Taiwan, not just “diplomatically isolate” it, and called on the United States to negotiate a so-called “bilateral free trade agreement” with Taiwan. What is your response?","Our position is clear and consistent. We firmly oppose any agreement with sovereignty implications and an official nature, or any official exchanges, between a country with which we have diplomatic relations and the Taiwan region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: some people on the island now believe that the Ukraine issue and the Taiwan Strait issue are extremely similar. What is the spokesperson's comment? Second question: some Taiwan residents believe the mainland may “use force” against Taiwan in the same way as the Ukraine crisis. What is your comment? Third question: Taiwanese Winter Olympics athlete Huang Yu-ting wore a mainland team uniform before…","Regarding the first two questions, I have already answered them. I would like to reiterate that Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. The root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to provoke for independence. Only by resolutely containing “Taiwan independence” can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be ensured, so that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots need not live in fear.\nThird question: Exchanges and interactions between athletes from both sides of the Strait are normal, correct, and a matter of course. Some politicians and media on the island have been denouncing them both verbally and in print and making unreasonable scenes, and the DPP authorities even plan to impose penalties. This fully exposes their true nature: they cannot bear to see compatriots on both sides of the Strait visit each other and grow closer, and they scheme to create cross-Strait antagonism through various pretexts in pursuit of political self-interest.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to reports, former US Secretary of State Pompeo will make an unwelcome visit to Taiwan next month and will also meet with Tsai Ing-wen during the visit. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Everyone is clear about who Pompeo is. The DPP authorities are colluding with anti-China politicians, attempting to use external forces to build momentum for seeking “independence.” It is nothing but a farce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Recently, outside observers have believed that the future of US-Taiwan relations may no longer be limited by US-China relations, highlighting the situation of the Taiwan issue becoming “regionalized” and “internationalized,” which the mainland side will inevitably need to handle properly. What is your comment on this? Second question: Recently, Lü Xiulian proposed using “One Zhonghua” to replace…","The first question. As I said just now, Pompeo's visit to Taiwan was nothing but a farce. At present, the Taiwan Strait situation continues to be tense and turbulent. The fundamental cause is that the DPP authorities have repeatedly attempted to “rely on the United States to seek independence,” while some people in the United States deliberately pursue “using Taiwan to contain China.” Some people in the United States keep making erroneous remarks and taking wrong actions on the Taiwan question; fundamentally, they seek to play the “Taiwan card,” treating Taiwan as a pawn to obstruct the process of China's reunification and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. No matter how the DPP authorities and foreign forces collude and perform, they cannot change the iron-clad fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they stop the historical trend of national strengthening, national rejuvenation, and cross-Strait reunification.\nThe second question, I have also seen related reports. She criticized the DPP authorities for relying on the United States, pointed out that “resisting China” cannot “protect Taiwan,” and warned Taiwan's young people that they will certainly face the mainland's handling of the Taiwan question “in their lifetime.” Her remarks above expose the smokescreen of “anti-China and resisting China” that the DPP authorities have long manufactured. They show that the DPP authorities' policy of deceiving the people by colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation has, to a considerable extent, including within the DPP itself, aroused strong dissatisfaction and doubt.\nThe Taiwan question is a problem left over from China's civil war. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided, nor shall they be. Peaceful reunification best serves the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, jointly promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Some mainland media recently named two KMT representatives as “covert independence” advocates. Does this represent the mainland official attitude toward the KMT?","On September 26, 2021, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory message to Chu Li-luan on being elected chairman of the Kuomintang of China, pointing out that the positive interaction between the two parties over the past period, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” has promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and benefited compatriots on both sides, with results that are plain to see. In fact, upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” remain the basis for exchanges, cooperation and dialogue between the KMT and the CPC.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Some mainland netizens interpreted the “straggling little pigeon” in the “Snowflake” segment of the Winter Olympics opening ceremony being brought back by its companions as symbolizing “Taiwan's return and the reunification of the motherland.” Green media on the island said the children's performance had become a “united front prop.” What comments do you have on this?","The opening ceremony of the Beijing Winter Olympics attracted global attention. It was splendid and successful, and it received high praise and affirmation at home and abroad. The “Lost Little Pigeon” (掉队的小鸽子) segment in the program “Snowflake” (《雪花》) showed children's romance, innocence, and friendship, and was intended to promote the Olympic spirit of unity, friendship, and moving toward the future together. Some netizens believe this symbolizes “Taiwan's return and the reunification of the motherland,” and that “not one pigeon (鸽) can be missing” (一个（鸽）不能少), reflecting their longing for the realization of national reunification. Pan-Green figures and media on the island have distorted and hyped this, which only exposes their hysteria, born of mistaking a bow's reflection in a cup for a snake.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently a COVID-19 outbreak occurred in Suzhou, Jiangsu, involving Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","It is understood that as of February 21, this round of the epidemic in Suzhou involved 18 employees of 2 Taiwan-invested enterprises, including 4 Taiwan compatriots, 2 of whom were confirmed cases and 2 of whom were asymptomatic. Suzhou has more than 150,000 permanently resident Taiwan compatriots and more than 12,600 Taiwan-invested enterprises. Apart from the two enterprises above, which have been placed under lockdown in accordance with regulations, the situation of other Taiwan compatriots and enterprises is generally stable, and production and daily life are normal.\nSince the outbreak of the epidemic, the local Taiwan Affairs Office and Taiwan business associations have been on 24-hour duty, carrying out service and guarantee work to ensure the personal safety of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots and the normal production of Taiwan-invested enterprises. They have coordinated quarantine hotels and provided protective supplies and personal daily necessities. Taiwan compatriots and enterprises in Suzhou have actively participated in epidemic prevention and control and volunteer services. The Taiwan-invested BenQ Hospital and Tsung-Jen Ching Memorial Hospital have cumulatively dispatched 1,700 person-times of medical staff, responsible for work at 532 nucleic acid sampling sites. Taiwan-invested enterprises such as Nangang Rubber dispatched more than 100 employees to participate in volunteer services, and the sampling site in the factory area also took samples from more than 2,000 person-times of external employees. Taiwan-invested enterprises such as Uni-President Group, Thermos, Giant, Aiwei'er Food and Xinhuaxi, along with a number of Taiwan compatriots and their relatives, actively donated epidemic prevention supplies and expressed condolences to frontline epidemic prevention personnel.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The Kinmen-Xiamen “small three links” have been suspended for more than two years due to the epidemic, and when they will resume has drawn attention. Kinmen County Magistrate Yang Zhenwu recently said that preparations for a “Qingming special case” have been made, and he hopes that, based on the principles of “humanitarian considerations” and “limited exchanges,” it can play an icebreaking role for “small…","Everyone knows that since the outbreak of the epidemic in 2020, the DPP authorities have unilaterally cut off the \"mini three links,\" and at the same time stopped mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan and stopped exchanges. This is completely different from our approach of safeguarding the rights of cross-Strait compatriots to normal exchanges while doing a good job of epidemic prevention and control. The \"mini three links\" are indeed the most important and most convenient channel for exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, especially between residents of Fujian and Taiwan, and residents on both sides hope to resume the \"mini three links\" as soon as possible. We hope the DPP authorities will heed reason and stop delaying and obstructing this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-02-23","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Recently, a poll on the island showed that the KMT had the lowest favorability rating, while the DPP had the highest. Has the Taiwan Affairs Office noticed this change in public opinion? Will the mainland's future Taiwan strategy no longer place as much emphasis on winning Taiwan public opinion as it did before?","Taiwan’s island is full of various public opinion polls, which differ in their design orientation, and whose results are not consistent. We will not comment on specifics. It should be pointed out that our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan are clear and consistent, including resolutely containing and opposing “Taiwan independence,” adhering to the one-China principle while improving and developing cross-Strait relations, and of course also including our adherence to placing hope in the Taiwan people. No matter how much interference and obstruction we encounter, we will regard winning the hearts and minds of the Taiwan people as an important part of our work to oppose “independence” and promote reunification. We will continue to do so.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all for coming. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202202/t20220223_12409292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-02-24","Hua Chunying","CCTV","Speaking on the Ukraine issue, US State Department spokesperson Ned Price said that China should respect the principle of state sovereignty and territorial integrity and that China has an obligation to urge Russia to “back down”. He also said the growing relationship between China and Russia is concerning. The two sides’ joint statement shows that China is trying to use its influence on Russia to create a world…","I noted the remarks by the US State Department spokesperson.\nFirst, when it comes to respect for state sovereignty and territorial integrity, I’m afraid the US is in no position to tell China off. The Chinese people have deep understanding and strong feelings about state sovereignty and territorial integrity through first-hand experience. Recent history saw China invaded by the Eight-Power Allied Forces and other colonialist powers, which left behind indelible poignant memories of national humiliation. Just a little more than 20 years ago, the Chinese embassy in the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia was hit by NATO bombing, which killed three Chinese journalists and injured many more. NATO still owes the Chinese people a debt of blood. Even today, China still faces a realistic threat from the US flanked by its several allies as they wantonly and grossly meddle in China’s domestic affairs and undermine China’s sovereignty and security on issues including Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Taiwan. China remains the only permanent member of the Security Council that has yet to realize complete national reunification. It is because of all these that China consistently and firmly uphold the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and basic norms governing international relations, firmly safeguard its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity, and firmly defend international equity and justice.\nIf we look at the US, during its nearly 250 years of history, there were only 20 years when it was not conducting military operations overseas. The pretexts it used can be democracy or human rights or simply a test tube of laundry powder or even fake news. Such a country’s understanding of respect for state sovereignty and territorial integrity is definitely different from ours. The international community can see this very clearly.\nThe US side suggests that Russia acted with complicit support from China. I don’t believe Russia would be too pleased to hear that. Russia is a permanent member of the UN Security Council and an independent major power. It is fully capable of formulating and implementing its diplomatic strategy independently based on its judgement and national interests.\nI must also stress that China-Russia relations are based on the foundation of non-alliance, non-confrontation and non-targeting of any third party. This differs fundamentally and essentially from the practice of the US, which is, ganging up to form small cliques and pursuing bloc politics to create confrontation and division based on ideology. China has no interest in the friend-or-foe dichotomous Cold War thinking and the patchwork of so-called allies and small cliques and has no intention to follow such a path.\nAs to the China-Russia joint statement, I suggest the US side give it some further study. China and Russia aim to strengthen strategic communication and coordination, firmly uphold the international system with the UN’s central coordinating role in international affairs, and firmly safeguard the international order based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and international law. This shows exactly that China and Russia are acting responsibly and positively maintaining international strategic security and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347231.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220224_10645295.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-02-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，向汤加运送救援物资的中国海军舰艇编队近日抵达汤加首都努库阿洛法。请进一步介绍有关情况。","According to the website of the Ministry of National Defense, Defense Ministry spokesperson Tan Kefei, when answering a reporter's question on the 25th, said that the PLA Eastern Theater Command has organized multi-service joint combat readiness patrols and combat-oriented drills in the sea and air space around Taiwan island. This is a necessary action taken in response to US-Taiwan collusion and in accordance with the need to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese People's Liberation Army stands ready at all times and will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart interference by external forces and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the PLA Eastern Theater Command recently organized joint combat readiness patrols and combat-oriented drills in the sea and air space around Taiwan island. Some analysts believe this is a stern warning against recent US-Taiwan collusion. What is your comment on this?\nTan Kefei said: We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. Pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and supporting \"Taiwan independence\" is a road of no return. The US has repeatedly and explicitly stated that it adheres to the one-China policy and does not support \"Taiwan independence.\" But for some time now, the US has escalated its playing of the \"Taiwan card,\" attempting to \"use Taiwan to contain China,\" which is bound to lead the situation into a dangerous place.\nTan Kefei stressed that Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. The PLA Eastern Theater Command's organization of multi-service joint combat readiness patrols and combat-oriented drills in the sea and air space around Taiwan island is a necessary action taken in response to US-Taiwan collusion and in accordance with the need to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese People's Liberation Army stands ready at all times and will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart interference by external forces and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10135068.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-02-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","美方近日发布《美国的印太战略》报告称，中国持续整合经济、外交、军事和科技力量，在印太地区寻求构建“势力范围”，导致印太地区面临重大挑战，美将进一步密切与盟友、伙伴合作，以应对挑战、展开竞争，同时声称支持台湾提升防御能力。请问中方对此有何评论？","First, I will take the initiative to release two pieces of news.\nFirst news.\nTo practice the Global Security Initiative and the concept of a Maritime Community with a Shared Future proposed by Chairman Xi, build a closer China-Africa community with a shared future, and strengthen maritime security cooperation with militaries of countries around the Gulf of Guinea, the Chinese military held a video seminar on the security situation in the Gulf of Guinea on May 24.\nThe theme of this meeting was “Maritime Security in the Gulf of Guinea from the Perspective of a Maritime Community with a Shared Future.” Dong Jun, Commander of the Navy, attended the meeting and delivered a keynote speech. Leaders of navies and coast guards of countries around the Gulf of Guinea and leaders of relevant regional organizations attended. Participants held in-depth discussions and exchanges around topics including “Maritime Security and Sustainable Economic Development in the Gulf of Guinea,” “Maintaining Secure Development in the Gulf of Guinea: The Role and Action of Maritime Forces,” and “New Vision for China-Africa Maritime Security Cooperation.” Second news.\nSecond news.\nOn May 24, the Chinese and French militaries held a video conference on military health service exchange. About 20 leaders from both sides' health departments and experts in the field of COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control attended. The exchange took “Main Practices and Experiences of Militaries in Fighting COVID-19” as its theme. Both sides introduced the overall situation and experiences of their militaries participating in national epidemic prevention and control, focusing on topics such as military support for local anti-epidemic actions, epidemic prevention and control in overseas military operations, and progress in prevention and treatment technology, and agreed to hold a second video conference on health service issues.\nThe Chinese military is willing to work with the French side to continue deepening strategic mutual trust between the two militaries, strengthen practical cooperation in all fields, push Sino-French military relations to a new level, and join hands to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10135068.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-02-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that US Defense Secretary Austin, at a Senate hearing recently, said that the focus of US military force deployment is to counter China’s “aggressive bullying.” US Joint Chiefs of Staff Chairman Milley said the United States faces two major powers, China and Russia, both of which have strong military forces and intend to fundamentally undermine the rules-based international order. What is China’s…","The US statements are as usual, reflecting a strong Cold War mentality, a hegemonic mindset, and anxiety in the face of China's peaceful rise. Whether the US uses the words “bullying behavior” or “undermining international rules and order,” I find that every word describes the United States itself.\nSpeaking of “bullying behavior” in international relations, the United States is the undisputed originator and the greatest practitioner. In Iraq, the United States, relying on a vial of some unknown white powder, brazenly invaded a sovereign state, causing large numbers of civilian casualties and displacing many families. In Syria, the United States used the “White Helmets” organization to fabricate videos and militarily intervened in Syria's internal affairs, causing a tragic humanitarian disaster. The Chinese people will not forget that in May, 23 years ago, NATO, led by the United States, bombed the Chinese Embassy in Yugoslavia, once again incurring a debt of blood to the Chinese people. This is not only bullying, but also a crime.\nSpeaking of the rules-based international order, the United States is globally recognized as a breaker of rules. As everyone knows, the United States loves to talk about “rules” the most, yet the country that takes rules least seriously is precisely the United States. The US uses international law and international rules when convenient and discards them when inconvenient. In recent years it has successively withdrawn from the Comprehensive Agreement on the Iranian Nuclear Issue, the Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty, the Treaty on Open Skies, and others, fully displaying its selfish and hypocritical face. On this issue, the United States is the least qualified to blame other countries.\nWe demand that the United States stop packaging “family rules and gang rules” as international rules and stop promoting the erroneous practice of an American-style “hegemonic order,” and objectively and rationally accept China's peaceful development. This is beneficial to China-US relations and to world peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10135068.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-02-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japanese Defense Minister Kishi Nobuo said that the Chinese Navy’s aircraft carrier Liaoning carrier group has recently been active in areas near Japan’s southwestern islands and Taiwan, with Chinese carrier-based aircraft taking off and landing more than several hundred times. Japan is closely monitoring this. Japan’s Ministry of Defense announced that it dispatched the Izumo helicopter…","We have noted the relevant hype from the Japanese side. Many Chinese internet users have referred to the Japanese ships and aircraft as the “official photographers” of the Liaoning carrier. We believe this “photographer” is better off not being around. The training activities of the Liaoning are entirely reasonable, lawful, and beyond reproach. The Japanese side's close attention has some ulterior motives. It is likely trying to gain attention by hyping the actions of the Chinese military and to create a pretext for its own military expansion. We firmly oppose this.\nI must point out that the close-range tracking and interference activities by the Japanese side are extremely dangerous and can easily lead to misunderstandings, miscalculations, and maritime or air accidents. The actions of the Japanese side are not conducive to mutual trust between the two sides and also pose a serious threat to the safety of ships, aircraft, and personnel on both sides. China demands that the Japanese side stop all meaningless interference activities and safeguard bilateral relations and regional peace and stability through concrete actions.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10135068.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-02-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","May 29 this year is the 20th International Day of UN Peacekeepers. Please introduce the relevant situation of the Chinese military's participation in United Nations peacekeeping operations in recent years.","In April 1990, China sent five military observers to the United Nations Truce Supervision Organization, opening the glorious journey of the Chinese military's participation in UN peacekeeping operations. Over the more than 30 years since, the number and types of peacekeepers dispatched by the Chinese military have developed comprehensively, from the initial military observers to engineering detachments, medical detachments, transport detachments, helicopter detachments, guard detachments, infantry battalions and other organized units, as well as professional military peacekeeping personnel such as staff officers, military observers, and contracted officers. Chinese peacekeepers have left their footprints in more than 20 countries and regions, including Cambodia, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Liberia, Sudan, Lebanon, Cyprus, South Sudan, Mali, and the Central African Republic. They have made important contributions to advancing the peaceful settlement of disputes, safeguarding regional security and stability, and promoting economic and social development in host countries.\nThe Chinese military's participation in UN peacekeeping operations stems from the Chinese nation's peaceful genes, the Chinese people's sense of all-under-heaven responsibility, the fundamental purpose of the people's military, and China's responsibility as a major country. Over more than 30 years, the Chinese military has successively participated in 25 UN peacekeeping operations and dispatched nearly 50,000 officers and soldiers in total, and 16 officers and soldiers have given their precious lives. At present, a total of 2,240 of our officers and soldiers are performing missions in seven peacekeeping mission areas and at UN headquarters. In UN peacekeeping operations, the Chinese military has always kept in mind its original aspiration and mission of fulfilling its responsibilities as a major country, safeguarding world peace, and serving the building of a community with a shared future for mankind. It has marched bravely and forged ahead for world peace, and Chinese “Blue Helmets” have become a key force for the United Nations in maintaining peace.\nBy taking concrete actions to safeguard world peace, China has become the largest troop contributor among the permanent members of the UN Security Council. In the second half of this year, the Chinese military plans to hold the “Shared Vision” International Peacekeeping Forum, inviting representatives from the United Nations and relevant countries, as well as peacekeeping experts and scholars, to offer suggestions, share experiences and practices, and contribute wisdom to the innovative development of UN peacekeeping operations. The “Shared Vision” International Peacekeeping Forum, together with the “Shared Destiny” International Peacekeeping Live-Troop Exercise and the “Shared Mission” Peacekeeping Mission Headquarters Tabletop Exercise previously held by our military, form the “Shared” series of international peacekeeping brand events regularly hosted by the Chinese military. We welcome all countries of the world to participate actively.\nThe International Day of UN Peacekeepers is three days away. In December 2002, the UN General Assembly adopted a resolution designating May 29 of each year as the International Day of UN Peacekeepers, to commemorate and honor peacekeepers who have sacrificed their lives for UN peacekeeping and to praise the role and contributions of peacekeepers from all countries. This year marks the 20th International Day of UN Peacekeepers. Here I extend my highest respect to all personnel participating in UN peacekeeping operations, including Chinese peacekeepers! I also hope that you will pay close attention to safety while completing your missions. The motherland and your loved ones are waiting for you to come home!","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10135068.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-02-25","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","What is China’s response to Taiwan deciding to sanction Russia?","The Taiwan authorities won’t let go of any opportunity to chase the clout and assert themselves in a grandstanding manner. Such attempts are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347232.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220225_10645686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-02-25","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Recently, the US said it would work closely with the EU, Australia, Japan, Canada, the UK, New Zealand and Taiwan, China to implement export controls against Russia. The DPP authorities subsequently said that they “will participate in the international community's economic sanctions against Russia.” What is your comment on this? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 25 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 25th in response to questions: The DPP authorities have repeatedly exploited the situation in Ukraine to hype up hot topics and ride on them, once again exposing their stubborn “relying on external forces to seek independence.” They have tried every means to cling to and collude with the US and the West, attempting to cover up the fact that Taiwan is part of China and to achieve their goal of “independence.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and no matter how much they kick up, they cannot stop the process of complete reunification of the motherland.\nMa Xiaoguang also said: We advise some countries to abide by the One-China principle and stop playing the “Taiwan card.” No one should underestimate the Chinese people’s firm resolve, strong will and great ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202202/t20220225_12409889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-02-28","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","According to reports, former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe said in an interview that given the Russia-Ukraine situation, Japan should start discussing issues related to nuclear sharing with the US, and that the US should give up strategic ambiguity on the Taiwan question. What is your comment on this?","Recently, certain Japanese politicians have been making wild talks repeatedly on the Taiwan question and irresponsible remarks about China’s internal affairs. China is firmly opposed to this.\nJapan committed countless crimes during its aggression against China and the colonial rule in Taiwan for half a century, and thus bears grave historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. During the second World War, Japan was defeated and Taiwan returned to the motherland. But some forces in Japan still covet Taiwan. They fail to face up to and reflect upon Japan’s track record of belligerence, unhinged aggression and expansion, and brutal colonialism and enslavement. Worse still, they attempt to exploit and hype up the situation in the neighborhood for a military breakthrough. Japanese politicians recently made absurd remarks about Taiwan, and even wild comments that openly violate its own Three Non-Nuclear Principles and the obligations of a party to the Nuclear Non-proliferation Treaty (NPT). Besides, by raising nuclear sharing with the US, Japan has fully exposed the dangerous tendency of lingering militarism in the country.\nTaiwan is China’s internal affair, and has nothing to do with Japan. We strongly urge the Japanese side to have a deep reflection on history, earnestly abide by the principles stipulated in the four political documents between China and Japan and its commitments made so far, act prudently on the Taiwan question and stop making provocations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347233.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220228_10646369.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-02-28","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","Today, the Chinese People’s Association for Friendship with Foreign Countries (CPAFFC) held the Meeting in Commemoration of the 50th Anniversary of the Shanghai Communiqué. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended and addressed the meeting. Do you have more information on that?","This morning, the Meeting in Commemoration of the 50th Anniversary of the Shanghai Communiqué was successfully held in Shanghai. Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Secretary of the CPC Shanghai Municipal Committee Li Qiang attended and addressed the meeting. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi delivered a video address. Representatives from the political, business and academic sectors participated in the meeting. In his remarks, State Councilor Wang Yi, together with people from both countries, walked through again that ice-breaking journey, drew experience from history, and sought inspirations for the road ahead.\nState Councilor Wang Yi pointed out that to get a correct understanding of the Communiqué’s spirit will help us see more clearly why the ice in the relationship thawed and barriers were removed, and know how the relationship can forge ahead. History tells us that by following the trend of the times, we can make the right strategic choice; by seeking common ground while reserving differences, we can attain peaceful co-existence between countries with different social systems; and by following the basic norms of international relations, we can build real guardrails for China-US relations.\nState Councilor Wang Yi expounded on the ins and outs of the Taiwan question. He pointed out that facts on the Taiwan question are crystal clear, and that the historic dynamics of the one-China principle are self-evident. History brooks no falsification, and what is right or wrong should not be distorted. The US should return to the original and true meaning of the one-China principle, honor its political commitments to China, and fulfill its due international obligations. It should stop draining the one-China principle of its essence, and hollowing it out. It should stop encouraging and supporting “Taiwan independence” moves, stop attempting to use the Taiwan question to contain China, and stop saying or doing things that interfere in China’s internal affairs. Only in doing so can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait be truly maintained and the larger interests of China-US relations be upheld.\nState Councilor Wang Yi made four proposals on following through on the common understandings between the two presidents and putting China-US relations back on track at an early date. First, we must uphold the one-China principle and consolidate the political foundation of China-US relations. Second, we must respect each other and ensure the right direction for China-US relations. Cooperation represents the mainstream of China-US relations. To define the relationship as competition is oversimplification. Third, we must pursue win-win cooperation and promote the development and prosperity of both countries. Fourth, we must shoulder responsibilities as major countries and provide the world with more public goods. Neither should seek hegemony in the Asia-Pacific region.\nAs noted by State Councilor Wang Yi, since the door of China-US relations has been opened, it should not be closed again. Since the world has emerged from the Cold War, it should not see the descending of another iron curtain. We hope the US can work with China to draw wisdom from the Shanghai Communiqué, follow the guidance of the important common understandings between the two presidents, and find the right way for China-US relations under the new circumstances on the basis of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, so as to deliver benefits to both countries and the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347233.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202202/t20220228_10646369.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-01","Wang Wenbin","Macao Monthly","According to reports, US President Biden today decided to send a bipartisan delegation led by Mike Mullen, chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, to visit Taiwan. Tsai Ing-wen is set to receive the delegation in Taipei on the morning of March 2. Do you have any comment?","The Chinese people are firmly determined and resolved to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The attempt by the US to show support to Taiwan will be in vain, no matter who the US sends. China urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, stop all forms of official interactions with Taiwan, and handle Taiwan-related issues in a prudent manner, lest it should further undermine the larger interests of China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220301_10646842.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-01","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","The US guided-missile destroyer USS Ralph Johnson recently sailed through the Taiwan Strait and hyped it up. What is your comment on this?","I noticed that spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has released a written statement on this.\nWhat is the true intention of the US hyping of the USS’ passage through the Taiwan Strait?\nIf the US wants to embolden the “Taiwan independence” forces in this way, then we have this to say to the US: such move will only accelerate the demise of the “Taiwan independence” forces. The US will also pay a heavy price for its adventurist act.\nIf the US tries to intimidate and pressure China in this way, then we have this stern warning: the so-called military deterrence will be reduced to scrap iron when facing the steely great wall of the 1.4 billion Chinese people.\nThe trick of sending vessels to sail through the Taiwan Strait should be better saved to entertain those obsessed with hegemony.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220301_10646842.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-01","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan has sent relief supplies to Ukraine. Is China prepared to provide humanitarian assistance to the country?","China is ready to play a constructive role in easing the situation in Ukraine. We will release relevant information in due course.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220301_10646842.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 1 — In response to the visit to Taiwan on March 1 by former Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Mike Mullen and others, and the DPP authorities’ welcoming of it, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 1st in response to questions that colluding with external forces cannot bring security, cannot bring well-being to Taiwan’s people, and will only further turn Taiwan into a pawn of external forces in their anti-China and China-containment efforts. The DPP authorities, resorting to external forces to prop up their provocations to pursue “independence,” keep going down the same road to the bitter end, which will only accelerate their demise.\nZhu Fenglian said we firmly oppose any official exchanges of any form between the United States and the Taiwan region under any pretext. Any so-called “support for Taiwan” does not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can it stop China’s unification process and national rejuvenation. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220301_12410768.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-03-02","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","It is reported that former Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff in the US had talks with the leader of the Taiwan region. Do you have any comment?","I would like to refer you to my answer to a relevant question yesterday. I want to stress again that the Chinese people are firmly determined and resolved to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The attempt by the US to show support to Taiwan will be in vain, no matter who the US sends.\n*************************\nTo better meet the needs of foreign service and build a more authoritative and convenient platform for information release and interaction with the public, the social media accounts of “Diplochat” on Weibo and WeChat have been renamed “The Ministry of Foreign Affairs”. You are most welcome to follow and support China’s diplomacy through these accounts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347235.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220302_10647272.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 50th anniversary of the “Shanghai Communiqué,” the DPP authorities once again jumped out to attack UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and challenge the one-China principle. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 2 (Reporter) — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 2nd, solemnly warning the DPP authorities that any scheme for “Taiwan independence” is futile, and the higher they jump, the harder they will fall! The schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatists colluding with external forces to challenge the one-China principle will certainly be crushed by the historical wheel of national reunification pushed forward by the Chinese people.\nShe said that the DPP authorities disregard international law and the basic norms of international relations, continuously distort and attack UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and challenge the one-China principle. Their purpose is to try every means to deny the fact that Taiwan is part of China, deceive the people on the island and the international community, and find excuses for their “Taiwan independence” position.\nZhu Fenglian said that as is well known, in 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly, by an overwhelming majority, adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore all the lawful rights of the People’s Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing that the representatives of the government of the People’s Republic of China are the only legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. This clearly and thoroughly resolved the question of China’s representation in the United Nations politically, legally and procedurally. Years of practice have fully proven that the United Nations and the vast majority of member states recognize that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and fully respect China’s sovereignty over Taiwan.\nShe said that although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully unified, China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities hype “mutual non-subordination” in order to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan,” which is a blatant provocation to pursue “independence.” The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and openly challenge the legal principles and facts recognized by the international community, yet they cannot change the iron fact that Taiwan is part of China.\nZhu Fenglian said that the cause of China’s reunification is a just cause, widely supported and endorsed by the international community. This is the most distinctive feature of the era for UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 under the current circumstances. “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to national reunification, a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation, and the root cause of undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. No one should underestimate the Chinese people’s firm resolve, steadfast will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220302_12410892.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-03-03","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","According to Taiwan media reports, former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo met with Tsai Ing-wen in Taipei today. Do you have any comment?","This act of Mike Pompeo is simply shameless and futile.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347236.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220303_10647693.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-04","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said in a speech in Taipei Friday that the US should take immediate steps to offer Taiwan diplomatic recognition. What’s the foreign ministry’s comment on former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo’s remarks?","Mike Pompeo is former politician with bankrupt credibility. His lunatic remarks will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347237.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220304_10648105.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On March 4, Pompeo posted erroneous remarks about Taiwan on his personal Facebook account, falsely claiming that “the US government should immediately grant Taiwan diplomatic recognition, recognizing it as a free and sovereign state.” Taiwanese media have hyped this extensively. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","XINHUA News Agency, Beijing, March 4 (electronic dispatch) — In response to erroneous remarks about Taiwan made by Pompeo on his personal Facebook account, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the TAO, stated on the 4th in response to a query: The set of fallacies put forth by Pompeo is a stale cliché that the DPP authorities have consistently hyped, and is complete nonsense. It is not surprising that someone who publicly boasts of being good at “lying, deceiving, and stealing,” and takes pride in it, would say such things; it only further exposes Pompeo's true nature and sinister intentions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220304_12416483.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-03-10","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Reportedly, certain senior U.S. officials recently declared loudly that they will firmly fulfill the commitment to defend Taiwan, “assisting Taiwan just as they assisted Ukraine,” and will continue to enhance Taiwan's self-defense capability. In addition, Taiwan's “Ministry of National Defense” revealed that, to respond to threats from the mainland, the Taiwan military adopted a “combining training with combat…","The Taiwan question is fundamentally different from the Ukraine question. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Recently, certain US officials have repeatedly made erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan, and members of Congress have made provocative visits to Taiwan in an attempt to bolster and embolden “Taiwan independence” elements. This seriously contradicts the US side's commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” is utterly lacking in good faith, and China firmly opposes it.\nThe DPP authorities, for their own selfish political interests, disregard the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and attempt to collude with external forces to split the country. This is a complete miscalculation. More and more Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities' scheme of “relying on the US to seek independence,” recognize their true face of forgetting their ancestors and betraying the motherland, and will not become sacrificial pawns of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces' “seeking independence through armed force.”\nRecently, in response to the US side's provocative visit, the Chinese People's Liberation Army organized relevant military operations in the sea and airspace around the Taiwan Strait. Going forward, we will show no leniency toward the DPP authorities' provocations aimed at “independence” and toward external interference schemes, and we will continue to demonstrate through decisive action our firm resolve to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/tw/2022/03-10/9698457.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-10","","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The government work report submitted to the Fifth Session of the 13th National People's Congress for deliberation states that we firmly oppose the separatist acts of “Taiwan independence” and firmly oppose interference by external forces. According to reports, the DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped mainland military aircraft flying around Taiwan. The United States has again sold weapons to Taiwan, US lawmakers…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share a common destiny, and are brothers and sisters of one blood, one family bound by ties thicker than water. We have consistently adhered to the policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” and we are willing to strive, with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, for the prospect of peaceful reunification across the Strait. However, we absolutely will not tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatists splitting the country. The PLA's relevant exercises and training activities are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and are by no means directed at Taiwan compatriots.\nSince the DPP authorities came to power, they have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” intensified “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and at the same time colluded with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” Such conduct seriously harms the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and is the root cause of the current tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait region. History proves that those who commit wrongdoing will eventually destroy themselves. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” is like a mantis trying to shake a tree, and it can only end in self-destruction.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and tolerates no external interference. The attempts by the US and Japan to achieve their political scheme of “containing China with Taiwan” by playing the “Taiwan card” are doomed to remain a fantasy. The more the US and Japan make noise on the Taiwan question, the more resolutely we will act to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It must be pointed out that the Chinese People's Liberation Army will show absolutely no tolerance toward “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, and will strike whenever they show their heads.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/ztjzh/4906559.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-03-14","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, Taiwan has signed an arms sale contract with the US recently to purchase a Field Information Communications System (FICS) at a total of NT$6.99 billion. This is follow-up implementation of a US arms sale plan to Taiwan from December 2020. Do you have any comment?","The Chinese side firmly opposes US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region, which severely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, interferes in China’s internal affairs, and harms China-US relations as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe US should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347241.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220314_10651532.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-14","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","According to reports, the US Congress passed the Consolidated Appropriations Act of 2022, which includes a section that bans the US government from using funds made available by the Act to create, procure, or display any map that \"inaccurately\" depicts Taiwan and the islands or island groups administered by Taiwan authorities. What is China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a historical and legal fact and an international consensus. Any accurate map should be based on these facts.\nThe US’ move grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, pursues political manipulation with the map of the Taiwan region, and attempts to create the false impression of “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan”. China deplores and rejects this.\nA stern warning to the US side: playing the “Taiwan card” is like playing with fire. It will not only push Taiwan to a precarious situation, but also bring unbearable consequences for the US. The US should stop hollowing out the one-China principle and stop condoning or abetting “Taiwan independence” moves. It should return to the original and true meaning of the one-China principle, honor its political commitments to the Chinese side, earnestly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the overall China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347241.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220314_10651532.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-14","Zhao Lijian","Yomiuri Shimban","Russia recently released a list of unfriendly countries and regions, which includes Taiwan. What is China’s comment? If Russia takes actions against Taiwan, what would China do?","As to why Taiwan is on the list, the answer is clear to all. If Taiwan is sanctioned, it has only itself to blame.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347241.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220314_10651532.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-15","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","According to reports, a US official said at a briefing on the meeting between Director Yang Jiechi and National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan that Sullivan “reiterated our One China policy based on the Taiwan Relations Act, Three Communiqués, and Six Assurances. And he underscored concerns about Beijing’s courses and provocative actions across the Taiwan Strait”. What is China’s comment?","Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Yang Jiechi met with US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan in Rome, Italy on March 14 local time. The two sides had candid, in-depth and constructive exchange on China-US relations and international and regional issues of common concern. They agreed to jointly follow through on the consensus of the two heads of state, enhance understanding, manage differences, expand consensus, strengthen cooperation and create more conditions to bring China-US relations back to the right track of sound and steady development.\nDirector Yang stressed that the Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In the three China-US Joint Communiqués, the US clearly recognized that there is only one China. The one-China principle is the prerequisite for the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the US and the political foundation for China-US relations. The current US administration has made a commitment on the Taiwan question to adhering to the one-China policy and not supporting “Taiwan independence”, but its recent actions are obviously not consistent with its statements. China is gravely concerned about and firmly opposed to the US’ recent erroneous acts and words on the Taiwan question. Any attempt to connive at or support the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and to play the “Taiwan card” to “use Taiwan to contain China” will get nowhere. China urges the US to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, strictly abide by the one-China principle, the provisions of the three China-US Joint Communiqués and the commitments made by the US, and not to go further down the road of great danger.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347242.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220315_10651924.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 16, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first announced the status of the policy measures for Taiwan residents to apply to set up individual businesses in pilot areas for innovative development of trade in services, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Welcome, everyone, to the Taiwan Affairs Office's regular press conference. Before taking your questions, I will first announce a newly issued policy measure that benefits Taiwan compatriots.\nOn March 16, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Ministry of Commerce, and the State Administration for Market Regulation jointly issued the \"Notice on Doing a Good Job in Handling Applications by Taiwan Residents to Establish Individual Industrial and Commercial Households in Pilot Regions for Innovative Development of Trade in Services\" (hereinafter the \"Notice\"), which takes effect immediately.\nThe Notice implements the State Council's \"Overall Plan for Comprehensively Deepening the Innovative Development Pilot of Trade in Services,\" and further provides support for Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people and young people, to work and start businesses on the mainland. Previously, relevant departments issued three documents in 2007, 2011, and 2015 on Taiwan residents establishing individual industrial and commercial households on the mainland. Compared with those, this new policy measure has two features:\nFirst, the number of open industries has increased substantially, from 24 items such as retail, catering, wholesale of textiles, apparel and household goods, and wholesale of stationery to 122 items, covering the \"National Economic Industry Classification.\"\nSecond, the open regions have been further expanded to include 27 pilot regions for innovative development of trade in services. Starting March 16, in addition to implementing the three earlier policy documents, relevant provinces and municipalities (districts) may apply the new opening policy to Taiwan residents applying to establish individual industrial and commercial households within their local pilot areas for comprehensively deepening innovative trade in services.\nIssuing the Notice is an important step by the relevant departments to further improve the institutional policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland. It fully demonstrates that our concept of \"both sides of the Strait are one family\" will not change, that our policy of sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first will not change, and that our measures to do practical good deeds for Taiwan compatriots will not change. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to seize opportunities and come to the mainland to achieve greater and better development for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419752.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","Premier Li Keqiang stressed in the Report on the Work of the Government: “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should work together in harmony and mutual support to create the glorious cause of national rejuvenation.” Several delegates from the Taiwan Provincial Delegation to the National People’s Congress also said that the Taiwan-related content in the Report on the Work of the Government reflects the…","This year is an important year as we enter a new journey toward building a comprehensively modern socialist country and advancing toward the second centenary goal. The Taiwan-related content of the Government Work Report sets out in concentrated form the major policies, principled positions, and goals and tasks for current Taiwan affairs work, and has very important guiding significance for doing Taiwan affairs work well this year.\nAt present, the overall cross-Strait situation is tense, and the root cause lies in the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces colluding with external forces to continuously seek “independence” and provoke. However, the historical process of national strength, national rejuvenation, and cross-Strait reunification cannot be stopped, and the trend is becoming clearer. We will thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan affairs work. We will firmly uphold the one-China principle and the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” continue to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, boldly explore new paths for cross-Strait integrated development, continuously improve policies that share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises and implement equal treatment, promote exchanges and cooperation and heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and gather strong positive energy for the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation. We will firmly hold the bottom line, carry forward the spirit of struggle, resolutely overcome risks and challenges on the road ahead, resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, firmly oppose all interference by external forces, and steadily advance the process of national reunification.\nWe hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the trends of the times and the situation, recognize what is beneficial and what is harmful, distinguish the genuine from the false, firmly stand on the right side of history, work in harmony with mainland compatriots to move forward united, jointly create the glorious cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation, and share the dignity and glory of being Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419751.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Please introduce the current situation of Taiwan residents establishing individual businesses on the mainland. We note that previously, the geographic scope for Taiwan residents to establish businesses was limited to provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the central government. Why is this time different?","To encourage and support compatriots in Taiwan, especially grassroots people and young people, to find employment and start businesses on the mainland, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, together with relevant departments, successively issued policy documents including the \"Several Opinions on the Application for Registration and Management of Individual Industrial and Commercial Households by Taiwan Farmers in the Cross-Strait Agricultural Cooperation Experimental Zone and the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park\" in November 2007, the \"Notice on Opening Up Applications by Taiwan Residents to Establish Individual Industrial and Commercial Households\" in December 2011, the \"Notice on Expanding the Opening Up of Applications by Taiwan Residents on the Mainland to Establish Individual Industrial and Commercial Households\" in December 2015, and supplementary notices, continuously expanding the opening of applications by Taiwan residents to establish individual industrial and commercial households on the mainland. These three policy documents remain in effect. Taiwan farmers may apply to establish individual industrial and commercial households in the Cross-Strait Agricultural Cooperation Experimental Zone and the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park, and Taiwan residents may apply to establish individual industrial and commercial households in 24 industries in 26 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the central government on the mainland, including retail, catering, wholesale of textiles, apparel and household goods, and wholesale of stationery. According to statistics from market regulatory departments, as of the end of 2021, 359 individual industrial and commercial households of Taiwan farmers and 9,926 individual industrial and commercial households of Taiwan residents had been registered.\nThe introduction of these new opening measures takes into account that the pilot zones for innovative development of trade in services have excellent business environments and great potential for the development of commerce and service industries. Taiwan residents who establish individual industrial and commercial households in these areas can share the better employment and entrepreneurship opportunities created by the overlay of policies, which is more conducive to their achieving better personal development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419747.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","This year's Government Work Report proposed that efforts be made to stabilize market entities and secure employment, and to step up the implementation of macroeconomic policies. Is the recent introduction of policies to expand the application for individual businesses by Taiwan residents aimed at implementing this requirement? What development opportunities will this bring to Taiwan compatriots?","The new measures recently introduced to allow Taiwan residents to set up individually owned businesses on the mainland are an important step in implementing, in the field of Taiwan work, the State Council's Overall Plan for Comprehensively Deepening Pilot Programs for Innovative Development of Trade in Services. Undoubtedly, this is also in line with the macro policy orientation set out in the Report on the Work of the Government. After the new measures take effect, the business scope for individually owned businesses set up by Taiwan residents in the pilot areas for innovative development of trade in services will expand substantially from 24 items to 122 industry sectors, covering the National Economic Industry Classification of the mainland. These include many industries in which Taiwan has development advantages and in which compatriots from Taiwan are highly willing to operate. Examples include the cultivation of vegetables, fruits, edible fungi and horticultural crops; the manufacture of baked goods, candy, chocolate and preserved fruit; the manufacture of tea beverages and other beverages; pet services; cultural and entertainment agents; and other indoor recreational activities centered on leisure and entertainment, such as hands-on crafts (pottery, sewing, painting, etc.). This will provide more opportunities and options for employment, entrepreneurship and realizing dreams for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people and young people.\nAs for how to apply, since the Regulations on the Administration of Registration of Market Entities took effect on March 1, 2022, the registration of all types of market entities has become more convenient. To apply for registration as an individually owned business, a Taiwan resident need only go to the registration authority where the business premises are located and complete the relevant registration procedures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","March 14 marks the 17th anniversary of the implementation of the Anti-Secession Law. A member of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference recently said in an interview, “If there is only ‘anti-secession’ and no ‘promoting unification,’ then the peaceful development of the country and cross-Strait relations cannot truly be promoted,” and said he will submit a proposal for…","We earnestly listen to and study all opinions and suggestions from National People’s Congress deputies and Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference members that are conducive to promoting national reunification. For a long time, we have united compatriots on both sides of the Strait, promoted the easing and improvement of the Taiwan Strait situation from tension and confrontation to peaceful development, and led cross-Strait relations steadily forward toward unification. Unification is a historical conclusion, the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. With the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, the historic task of complete reunification of the motherland must be accomplished, and it will certainly be accomplished.\nIn March 2005, the Third Session of the Tenth National People’s Congress deliberated and adopted the “Anti-Secession Law.” Its first article clearly states: “In order to oppose and curb ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces and their attempts to split the country, to promote the peaceful reunification of the motherland, to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area, to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, this Law is enacted in accordance with the Constitution.” In the 17 years since the Anti-Secession Law was implemented, it has played and will continue to play a unique and important role in deterring “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of national reunification. We will, in light of changes in the situation, strengthen the use of the rule of law and legal means to combat “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Tomorrow (March 17) marks the first anniversary of the release and implementation of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry.” Please have the spokesperson introduce, with concrete examples, what results have been achieved over the past year.","Since the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” were issued and put into effect one year ago, all regions and departments have actively worked to implement them, coordinated the resolution of issues of common concern to Taiwan-funded agriculture and forestry enterprises, and achieved more concrete results in capital subsidies, financing and loans, participation in rural revitalization, development of the domestic market, and R&D and innovation. Here, I would like to share some specific examples with everyone.\nFirst, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have gained more capital support and financing convenience. Last year, Taiwan-funded enterprises in various localities received subsidies, allowances, and interest subsidies totaling over RMB 100 million, and credit lines and financing from financial institutions also exceeded RMB 100 million. Taiwan-funded agricultural enterprises in the Taiwan-related agricultural parks of Fujian Province received interest subsidy support, and after the subsidies, loan interest rates were reduced to about 1% on average. The Zhejiang Provincial Rural Credit Cooperatives specially launched the “Taiwan Financing Card,” a product exclusively for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, with credit limits of up to RMB 1 million. More than 2,300 cards have been issued so far, with total credit lines exceeding RMB 60 million. Guangxi, through its government-backed financing guarantee system, helped a local Taiwan-funded fish products company obtain a RMB 6 million loan and helped a breeding pig research company obtain a RMB 7 million loan. A Taiwan businessperson said that the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” provided convenience for Taiwan enterprises to expand their scale and business operations through financing, and increased their confidence in developing agriculture on the mainland.\nSecond, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have made new progress in participating in the mainland’s rural revitalization strategy. Taiwan businesspeople in Beijing, taking advantage of the favorable policies of the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures,” joined the fast track of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei coordinated development and established a project in Fuping, Hebei, combining aquaculture with feed planting. In 2021, its sales revenue grew significantly, it created jobs for more than 300 rural laborers, and it effectively promoted economic and social development in a poverty-stricken area. A Taiwan businessperson in Shanghai obtained 200 mu of land through land transfer and invested in establishing a “Happy Farm,” which became a local internet-famous homestay and helped the construction of rural revitalization. Taiwan businesspeople in Ganzhou, Jiangxi, leased and transferred more than 300 mu of forest land and obtained forest ownership certificates.\nThird, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have made new progress in developing the domestic demand market. Various localities support Taiwan enterprises in making good use of e-commerce platforms and participating in various exhibitions and sales events, such as the Taiwan Expo and the Tea Expo, continuously widening their product sales channels. Jiangsu held docking events for the alliance of the agriculture and food processing industries, helping local Taiwan enterprises successfully list products in 55 supermarkets and open new sales outlets in major cities such as Beijing and Shanghai.\nFourth, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have received more support in R&D and innovation. The technology (products) of a Shanghai Taiwan-funded enterprise was successfully included in the key promotion and guidance catalogue of advanced practical water conservancy technologies. Fujian launched a pilot program of low-temperature index characteristic agricultural insurance for tea planting, provided subsidies to self-developed varieties that obtained “plant variety rights,” and provided special credit support to Taiwan enterprises in Taiwan innovation parks and industrial parks, as well as to Taiwan agriculture projects.\nThis year’s No. 1 Central Document made arrangements for the key work of comprehensively advancing rural revitalization, and clearly put forward requirements such as accelerating the development of facility agriculture, continuously promoting the integrated development of primary, secondary and tertiary industries in rural areas, and strengthening the building of rural revitalization talent teams. This points the way for doing “three rural issues” work well this year. We will continue to implement the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” thoroughly and in detail, and create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in mainland rural revitalization and the high-quality development of agriculture and forestry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419748.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The DPP authorities have already opened up imports of food from Japan's five Fukushima prefectures to Taiwan, and the quality inspection situation has been questioned by Taiwan residents. What comments do you have on this? In addition, after Taiwan opens up Fukushima food, will it affect food safety on the mainland?","Food safety concerns the vital interests of the people, and the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots should be effectively protected. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their party's narrow interests, have not hesitated to harm the health and well-being of Taiwan's people, and many people in Taiwan strongly question this.\nThe mainland has a complete food safety regulatory system and is fully capable of preventing problematic products from flowing in. The relevant competent authorities on the mainland will further strengthen supervision, strictly prevent related products from entering the mainland market via Taiwan, and safeguard food safety on the mainland and the health of consumers.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","According to reports, Taiwan and the US recently formally signed a military sales case for a “Field Information and Communication System” worth NT$6.99 billion, expected to be completed in September 2025. Some netizens on the island sarcastically said, “It's time to pay protection money again.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We firmly oppose the United States selling arms to China’s Taiwan region, and oppose any form of official exchanges such as military contacts between the United States and Taiwan. The DPP authorities have repeatedly used the hard-earned money of Taiwan taxpayers to buy American weapons, attempting to “seek independence through military means.” This will not succeed; it will only damage peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","After the outbreak of the Russia-Ukraine conflict, the US government stated that it “will not send troops to Ukraine under any circumstances.” Voices such as “Taiwan’s security cannot rely on the United States” emerged on the island, and polls showed that more than half of Taiwan residents recognize that the US will not send troops to aid Ukraine. Ma Yingjiu stated that if a cross-Strait conflict broke out, the…","First of all, it must be pointed out that the Taiwan question and the Ukraine question are fundamentally different. The most fundamental difference is that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is entirely China's internal affair, admitting no foreign interference.\nThe DPP authorities “rely on the US to seek independence,” fantasizing about relying on external forces to split the country. This is a complete miscalculation. From the “Kabul moment” to the “Ukraine situation,” more and more Taiwan compatriots have clearly recognized that the United States, for its own interests, on the one hand pours oil on the fire and fears no chaos, and on the other hand watches the fire from across the water to avoid getting burned itself. They have recognized that the US always puts American interests first, and its commitments to others cannot be relied upon at critical moments. They have recognized that the so-called “assurances” the DPP authorities obtained by paying high “protection fees” for “seeking independence” are nothing but poison that quenches thirst the way drinking poison does. They have recognized that external forces manipulating Taiwan-related issues are playing the “use Taiwan to contain China” game, sacrificing the interests of the Taiwan people, and that the “chess piece” will ultimately be “discarded.” They have recognized that the DPP authorities' blind “resistance to China” not only cannot “protect Taiwan” but will only “harm Taiwan,” pushing Taiwan further toward the abyss of no return.\nThe future of Taiwan, the security guarantee of Taiwan compatriots, and their interests and welfare lie in the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and national reunification, not in hoping for the “empty checks” of any external forces. Broad Taiwan compatriots should see clearly through the “relying on the US to seek independence” scam woven by the DPP authorities, break the spell of their manipulation of “anti-China and resistance to China,” and join us in pushing cross-strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, resolve the political confrontation at an early date, achieve lasting peace across the Taiwan Strait, realize the vision of national reunification, and allow future generations to live and grow up in a common homeland that is peaceful, tranquil, prosperous, and dignified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419750.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","After the outbreak of the Russia-Ukraine conflict, some foreign politicians have hyped and exaggerated the mainland's “military threat” to Taiwan. They not only “express support” for Taiwan but even clamor that they will provide weapons to Taiwan to assist its “resistance.” The DPP authorities have expressed gratitude for this. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs. It is a matter of course for China to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it brooks no foreign interference. For some time, some anti-China foreign forces, indulging in Cold War mentality, have played the “Taiwan card,” clamoring to turn Taiwan into a so-called “porcupine” and stirring up trouble to undermine cross-Strait relations. The DPP authorities, for the sake of party interests, willingly serve as chess pieces for external forces to “use Taiwan to contain China,” constantly provoke “independence,” and pay no attention at all to the safety of the 23 million Taiwan compatriots. They do not hesitate to kidnap the people of Taiwan as profitable “cannon fodder.” This is fundamentally harming Taiwan and will only push Taiwan further into the abyss of disaster.\nThe broad masses of Taiwan compatriots must fully recognize that peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait depend on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, not on external forces. If the DPP authorities are allowed to “seek independence by relying on foreign powers” and “seek independence by force,” willingly serving as pawns to be manipulated, Taiwan society will ultimately pay a heavier price. Today, as the Chinese mainland grows increasingly strong, “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” has no way out, and “using Taiwan to contain China” is doomed to fail. We are willing to work with Taiwan compatriots to resolutely crush the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism, firmly curb interference by external forces, steadily promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419745.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","The Russia-Ukraine conflict has caused Taiwan residents to worry that “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow.” The DPP authorities have called on the island to bolster its courage and incited “resisting China and defending Taiwan.” Tsai Ing-wen claimed that Taiwan has “the natural barrier of the Taiwan Strait, its geostrategic position, and the continuously rising defense will and combat capability of the Taiwan…","Recently, the DPP authorities have repeatedly ridden the Ukraine situation for attention, going around provoking incidents, playing up the so-called mainland “threat,” and deliberately escalating cross-Strait confrontation and “independence”-seeking rhetoric, and have even arrogantly advocated war. This not only exposes their guilty conscience, cowardice, and fierce posturing with no substance, but also completely tears off the hypocritical mask of their so-called “non-provocation.”\nWe are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. National sovereignty and territorial integrity are above all. If the DPP authorities continue to indulge in the delusion of “relying on external forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force,” and dare to take a reckless gamble, the various lies they have fabricated and hyped will vanish in an instant. We hope compatriots in Taiwan will recognize where their interests lie, refuse to be coerced and deceived by the DPP authorities, and resolutely draw a clear line with the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419749.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Since the outbreak of the Russia-Ukraine conflict, the DPP authorities have frequently used the Ukraine issue to ride the wave of popularity. For example, they previously announced joining the sanctions against Russia, and recently announced a donation of NT$100 million to Ukraine. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's view of this series of actions by the DPP?","The DPP authorities are using the Ukraine issue to raise their profile and ride the hot topic. This is entirely an attempt to muddy the waters and seek “independence.” Their schemes to stir up confrontation and create hostility through political manipulation will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The first question: This year’s Report on the Work of the Government added content to its Taiwan-related section, namely “implementing the overall strategy of the Party for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era” and “firmly opposing interference by external forces.” Can this be interpreted as meaning that, apart from continuing past Taiwan policy guidelines, the mainland may make tougher adjustments in the…","In answer to the first question, our policy guidelines toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. As everyone knows, the DPP authorities have increasingly colluded with external forces, engaged in provocations seeking \"independence,\" and attempted to change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. This is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation across the Taiwan Strait. We will firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. All necessary actions we take are directed against \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and interference by external forces, with the aim of fundamentally safeguarding the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.\nWe will adhere to the policy guidelines for work on Taiwan, implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan issue in the new era, uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" resolutely crush the schemes of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists, firmly curb interference by external forces, solidly promote peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of reunifying the motherland.\nIn answer to the second question, we have pointed out many times that the current cross-Strait relations are tense and grave, and the risk to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait has increased. The root cause lies in the DPP authorities colluding with external forces and continuously engaging in provocations seeking \"independence,\" and in certain countries manipulating Taiwan-related issues for the purpose of \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" obstructing China's reunification and national rejuvenation.\nRealizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. We have patience and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort. At the same time, our determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering, and we will never allow anyone or any force to infringe upon or split the sacred territory of the motherland. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces provoke and coerce, or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.\nIn answer to the third question, responding in this manner to how to handle the Taiwan blackout problem only shows that such DPP political figures are masters at calling a deer a horse, and their indifference to the interests of the people is fully exposed. I advise him not to shift the focus, and even less to boast about himself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities claimed that the mainland is using the Ukraine issue to carry out so-called “cognitive warfare” against Taiwan, affecting the morale of the Taiwanese public. Moreover, according to media reports and netizen reports, after the Russia-Ukraine conflict broke out, “Taiwan independence” forces spread large numbers of rumors online to incite hostility across the Strait. What is the spokesperson’s…","The DPP authorities have a long record of spreading “fake news” and are repeat offenders of so-called “cognitive warfare.” Those who commit many injustices will bring about their own downfall. The internet has memory, and the eyes of the people are sharp. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have meddled in the situation in Ukraine, stirring up trouble on mainland social media platforms. On the island, they selectively “cite” some mainland self-media content to exaggerate the so-called mainland “threat” and mislead residents of the island. In support of their clamor for “resisting China and defending Taiwan” and their rejection of unification in pursuit of “independence,” they fabricate public opinion and manipulate public sentiment. The DPP authorities’ maneuvers this time seriously underestimate the intelligence of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait must keep their eyes open and discern accurately, see through the sinister intent of “Taiwan independence” forces in inciting the people on both sides to confront each other, and see through the DPP authorities’ deception.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220316_12419746.htm"],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The national two sessions have just concluded. We have noted that more and more Taiwan youth are paying attention to the two sessions and to the whole-process people's democracy on the mainland. During the two sessions, Xinhua News Agency launched a short video report, “Taiwan Youth Watch the Two Sessions,” in which several Taiwan youth working and living on the mainland shared their many points of focus…","The annual National People’s Congress and Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference (the “Two Sessions”) is an important window through which Taiwan compatriots understand China’s socialist democratic political system with Chinese characteristics. Taiwan youth working and living on the mainland are paying increasing attention to the Two Sessions, understanding the country’s economic and social development and the mainland’s democratic political system, and seeking and gaining development opportunities for themselves in the course of the mainland’s development. In recent years, many Taiwan compatriots have expressed views and offered suggestions and proposals through various channels, effectively promoting the thorough implementation of policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots. Xinhua’s short video series “Taiwan Youth Watch the Two Sessions” and the China Taiwan Network’s column “Watching the Two Sessions Together” provide platforms for Taiwan youth to express their views, which is a very good thing.\nMany Taiwan youth have shared, through various means, their firsthand observations and experiences on the mainland, believing that democracy that reflects the will of the people is true democracy, and that democracy that brings benefits to the common people is true democracy. We will create better conditions and provide more opportunities for Taiwan youth to observe, experience and participate in the whole-process people’s democracy, and continue to deepen cross-Strait integration and development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Online registration for the mainland’s undergraduate and master’s graduate student recruitment for Taiwan students has gradually closed. Please introduce the relevant situation of this year’s registration for the mainland’s recruitment of Taiwan students. It is also understood that spring recruitment for fresh graduates at mainland universities is under way. What measures will the mainland introduce this year to…","The registration for undergraduate and master’s graduate admissions for Taiwan students at relevant mainland universities has ended. Information on registrations by Taiwanese students can be obtained from the education authorities after some time.\nFor Taiwanese fresh graduates studying at mainland universities who seek employment or entrepreneurship, all relevant universities will incorporate them into fresh graduate work and make unified arrangements. To actively do well in employment and internship work for Taiwanese students this year, since the second half of 2021 the All-China Federation of Industry and Commerce and the Central Committee of the China Democratic National Construction Association have raised nearly 1,500 job positions, and the relevant position information was recently published on the official website and official WeChat account of the China Vocational Education Society. These positions are mainly distributed in central and eastern regions such as Beijing, Tianjin, Shanghai, Jiangsu, Shandong, Guangdong, and Fujian, with some in western regions such as Shaanxi and Sichuan. Taiwanese fresh graduates from mainland universities and graduates from universities in Taiwan are welcome to apply.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: Senior officials of China and the United States recently held a meeting in Rome, Italy, with the Taiwan question a key focus. Can the spokesperson introduce the specific content? Second question: The recent epidemic in Shenzhen has also affected Taiwanese businesses there, and there are rumors that Foxconn has suspended work for several days. Please confirm this. For Taiwanese businesses and…","First, on March 14, Yang Jiechi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Foreign Affairs Commission, met in Rome, Italy, with Sullivan, Assistant to the President of the United States for National Security Affairs. Director Yang Jiechi reiterated China's position and stance on the Taiwan question, stressing that the Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. Any scheme that condones or supports the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, or attempts to play the “Taiwan card” and “use Taiwan to contain China,” will never succeed. He demanded that the US side recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle, the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and the commitments the US side has made, and not go further and further down a very dangerous road. Any so-called “US backing for Taiwan” or “US commitment to Taiwan is as solid as a rock” hype by the DPP authorities is nothing more than whistling to bolster courage and deceiving the people. “Relying on the US to seek independence” cannot escape a failing outcome.\nSecond, recently there have been local COVID-19 outbreaks in many places, making epidemic prevention and control more difficult, and the prevention and control situation is severe and complex. Based on the needs of epidemic prevention and control, Shenzhen has comprehensively upgraded its prevention and control measures and decided to conduct three rounds of whole-population nucleic acid testing from March 14 to 20, further implementing the prevention and control strategy of “using space to gain time,” so as to cut off the chain of social transmission of the new round of the outbreak as soon as possible and safeguard the lives and health of citizens.\nWhat I want to say is that epidemic prevention and control concerns the physical health and life safety of every person and must be taken very seriously. Every person and every enterprise, including Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises, has the obligation and responsibility to cooperate with local governments' epidemic prevention and control work and adopt the relevant anti-epidemic measures. We believe that Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises can fully understand this. We believe that the relevant localities will coordinate epidemic prevention and control with local economic and social development and provide good services to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","First question: When Su Tseng-chang was questioned at Taiwan's legislature, he quoted a poem from the mainland TV drama “Walking Toward the Republic.” How do you view the fact that Su Tseng-chang, whom the mainland has listed as a “Taiwan independence” diehard, is actually fond of watching mainland mainstream TV dramas? Second question: The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that the mainland's most…","First question: According to media reports, Su Tseng-chang has mentioned several mainland TV dramas, including “Story of Yanxi Palace” and “Advance to the Republic.” I can recommend a few more, such as “Awakening Age,” “Like a Flowing River,” “Under the Sign of Zhengyang Gate” and “Mountains and Seas Bring Love,” all of which are quite good and are excellent sources of education and inspiration. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same blood and culture; this is engraved in our genes and cannot be erased. Some people loudly shout “de-Sinicization” while privately and quite honestly pursuing the nourishment of traditional Chinese culture. Isn’t that a bit of a split personality? This also fully shows that “Taiwan independence” simply cannot work.\nSecond question: As everyone knows, the root cause of the current tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have escalated their collusion with external forces and engaged in provocations to pursue “independence,” attempting to change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and recklessly undermining the prospects for peaceful reunification. It is the Democratic Progressive Party authorities who are deliberately inciting confrontation across the Strait and escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe will adhere to the major policies for Taiwan-related work, implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely crush the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence,” firmly curb interference by external forces, steadily promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort. But if the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces continue to provoke and force the issue, or even cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Among the 300 “2021 National Three-Eight Red Banner Bearer” titles recently awarded by the All-China Women's Federation, two Taiwan compatriots were included. What is the spokesperson's view?","Granting honorary titles to representatives of Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland is a concrete measure to implement the “31 Measures” and realize equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots, and is also an inherent requirement for deepening integrated development across the Strait. Since 2019, the All-China Federation of Trade Unions, the All-China Women’s Federation, and the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League of China have issued measures encouraging localities to include Taiwan compatriots working on the mainland in the scope of commendation and honor selections within local trade union, youth, and women’s federation systems, and positive results have been achieved. According to statistics, a total of about 300 Taiwan compatriots (Taiwan compatriot families and Taiwan compatriot groups) have received honors at or above the prefecture-level city level on the mainland, such as May Day Labor Medals, Model Workers, Youth May Fourth Medals, and March 8th Red Banner Bearers. This is a high affirmation of the long-standing contributions that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots have made to economic and social development on the mainland.\nThe two Taiwan compatriots who received the honor of “2021 National March 8th Red Banner Bearers” this time are Lin Jiayan, chairperson of Hangzhou Aierbao Education Consulting Co., Ltd., and Wang Mengyun, a teacher at the School of Political Science and Public Administration of Guangxi Normal University. They have devoted themselves to early childhood education and higher education on the mainland, achieved outstanding results in their respective posts, and made positive contributions to promoting cross-Strait exchanges and integration. We hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots will join the great cause of promoting national reunification and national rejuvenation, and that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will move forward hand in hand, gather mighty strength, and create a brighter future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","The U.S. Congress recently passed the federal government's “Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2022,” which includes a provision prohibiting executive departments from producing or purchasing maps that “incorrectly label Taiwan's ‘territory.’” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, brooking no foreign interference. China firmly opposes the passage by the US Congress of bills containing negative content regarding Taiwan. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question. Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have stepped up collusion with the US, willingly serving as a tool for the US to play the “Taiwan card.” This is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","We have noted that the DPP authorities have recently gone all out on the island to carry out the so-called “strongest military training recall in history,” and at the same time declared that they will mass-produce the “Hsiung Sheng missile” to expand their so-called “counter-operations” capabilities, hyping up war and attempting to “seek independence through force.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The question you raised is very moving. Looking back at 2008 to 2016, the mainstream topic on the island was the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and compatriots on both sides shared a peaceful and stable environment and the fruits of exchange and cooperation. Now the island hypes topics such as “street battles” and “reservist call-ups” every day, with an atmosphere of war pervading everywhere and people in panic. Who is the instigator? It is entirely because the DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, willingly serve as pawns of external forces, constantly seeking “independence” and provoking, escalating cross-Strait confrontation, and going so far as to tie Taiwan’s people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and push them into the abyss of disaster. Continuing like this is extremely dangerous.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220316_12419743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-03-18","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","China sailed its aircraft carrier, the Shandong, through the sensitive Taiwan Strait on Friday shadowed by a US destroyer, a source with direct knowledge of the matter told Reuters. This took place just hours before the Chinese and US presidents were due to talk. Was the timing of this a coincidence?","This doesn’t fall within the purview of the foreign ministry, does it? You yourself wondered if it is a coincidence.\nI’m not aware of the specific situation about the Shandong aircraft carrier you just mentioned. But I’m sure the aircraft carrier has routine training arrangement. One shouldn’t link this with the communication between the Chinese and US heads of state. I think you may be too sensitive. Perhaps what is sensitive is you, not the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347245.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220318_10653084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-23","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Just a question on a virtual call between former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and Taiwan President Tsai Ing-wen on Tuesday evening where they discussed various topics, including COVID, Ukraine, the CPTPP and peace in the Indo-Pacific region. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this virtual meeting?","First of all, I must correct you on one point. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and there is no “president” whatsoever of the Taiwan region. China firmly opposes any official interaction between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region’s accession to any agreement or organization of official nature. This is our consistent and clear-cut position.\nDuring its colonial rule over Taiwan for half a century, Japan committed innumerable crimes, over which it bears grave historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. Some political forces in Japan openly colluded with “Taiwan independence” forces and made wanton remarks on the Taiwan question. China rejects and deplores such moves and has lodged solemn representation with the Japanese side.\nThe Taiwan question and the Ukraine issue are different in nature and are not comparable at all. The Taiwan question is purely China’s own affair and none of Japan’s business. It is dangerous and futile for some people in Japan to mention Taiwan and Ukraine in the same breath and incite “breakthroughs” in the relations with Taiwan. We seriously urge the Japanese side and certain politicians to make deep reflection on history, earnestly abide by the principles stipulated in the four political documents between China and Japan and Japan's commitments, avoid any official interaction with the Taiwan authorities, refrain from emboldening “Taiwan independence” elements, speak and act prudently on the Taiwan question and stop making provocations.\nWe have also noted that since the outbreak of the Ukraine crisis, the DPP authorities have manipulated the issue to sway public opinion and embolden “Taiwan independence” propositions. Such moves are futile. No matter what trick the DPP authorities play, the fact that Taiwan is part of China can never be changed, the overriding trend of Taiwan being reunited with the motherland can never be held back, and the defeat of “Taiwan independence” forces can never be reversed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347248.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220323_10654579.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 23 dispatch. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said in response to a question on the 23rd that some people in Japan have made erroneous remarks on Taiwan-related issues, and their nature is extremely vile. We urge these people in Japan to profoundly reflect on the lessons of history, not to keep making mistakes on Taiwan-related issues, to immediately correct their errors, and to return to the right path of adhering to the one-China principle. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.\nA reporter asked: On March 22, former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe had a video call with Tsai Ing-wen, and Abe again falsely claimed that “a contingency in the Taiwan Strait is a contingency for Japan.” What comment do you have? Zhu Fenglian made the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220323_12421244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-03-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Japanese Defense Minister, when discussing the defense budget for fiscal year 2023, said that China's arms buildup and military activities have caused “strong concern in the international community,” and hinted at including “counterstrike capability against enemy bases” within the scope of budget consideration. In addition, Japan's Liberal Democratic Party has proposed that in the new…","Recently, in order to expand its military strength and increase its defense budget, Japan has been seeking the so-called 'counterstrike capability against enemy bases,' constantly fabricating various pretexts and spreading irresponsible remarks. This dangerous trend of attempting to break through the 'exclusively defense-oriented policy' is what the international community should be highly vigilant about and strongly concerned about. Japanese militarism once launched wars of foreign aggression on the pretext of external threats, bringing profound disasters to the peoples of regional countries, including China. We urge the Japanese side to learn from history, restrain its words and deeds, and do more things that are conducive to maintaining regional peace and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-24/9710953.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Australian Prime Minister Morrison recently said that the security cooperation agreement signed by China has alerted Australia and that Australia's national security faces continuing threats. Other Australian media have speculated that China may use the leased land to build a Chinese naval base. What comments do you have on this?","The reports that the Chinese side will build a naval base in the Solomon Islands are pure fake news. Recently, Australian officials and media have repeatedly hyped the China-Solomon Islands security cooperation agreement, deliberately distorting facts and creating tension, which is extremely irresponsible, and the Chinese side firmly opposes this.\nChina and the Solomon Islands, as two sovereign and independent countries, carry out cooperation on the basis of equality and mutual benefit in areas such as maintaining social order, protecting the lives and property of the people, humanitarian assistance, and natural disaster response. This is conducive to promoting social stability and long-term peace and security in the Solomon Islands, and also accords with the common interests of the South Pacific region. We urge the relevant parties to stop hyping and exaggerating the “China military threat theory” and to do more practical things that benefit peace, stability, and prosperity in the South Pacific region.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/03-25/9711027.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-03-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 24 — In response to remarks made on the 23rd by the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 24th in response to an inquiry: These remarks continue to confuse right and wrong and reverse black and white, smuggle in the “two-state theory,” and further expose the nature of the DPP authorities, who shirk…","Zhu Fenglian said that the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the foundation for maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and for promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and healthy interaction between the two sides. The DPP authorities have single-handedly undermined this hard-won situation. They deliberately incite confrontation between the two sides, have increasingly colluded with external forces in provocations for “independence,” and caused the current tense and turbulent situation across the Taiwan Strait. This is known to the whole world and cannot be denied. Recently, the DPP authorities have repeatedly ridden on the Ukraine situation to chase hot topics, gone about “picking fights” and fabricated lies, defied the mainstream public opinion on the island that people want peace and development, and fantasized about continuing to “rely on foreign forces to seek independence” and “seek independence by force.” They are doomed to fail.\nZhu Fenglian said that we solemnly warn the DPP authorities: the attempt to deceive with the “two-state theory,” and to pursue “independence” under the guise of releasing “goodwill,” is pure wishful thinking. The attempt to coerce Taiwan compatriots onto the evil path of “opposing China to seek independence,” and to make them serve as “cannon fodder” for the realization of one party's private interests, will surely be held accountable. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides belong to one China can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development. There is no other way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220324_12421390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-03-28","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","US Indo-Pacific Command Admiral John C. Aquilino reportedly said in an interview that the Ukraine issue has underscored the serious threat that China poses to Taiwan, and that Asian allies must take seriously the possibility. What is your comment on this?","We have stated on multiple occasions that the Taiwan question is essentially different from the Ukraine issue. The two are uncomparable. Some people in the US repeatedly link up the two unrelated things with the real agenda to smear and attack China. Such an act is ill-intentioned.\nAs a Chinese proverb puts it, it takes more than one cold day for the river to freeze three feet deep. The current Ukraine issue is an outbreak of tension that has built up for years with Europe’s security as the root cause. NATO’s unchecked eastward expansion warrants reflection. Facing the current situation in Ukraine, the US did nothing to reflect on the responsibility it should assume, or make efforts to cool down the situation and promote talks for peace. Instead, it has been adding fuel to the flame. When European countries are paying the price for refugees and economic volatility due to the conflict, US arms dealers and oil and gas industry have made a fortune.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This makes it fundamentally different from a sovereign country like Ukraine. Those in the US who deliberately compare the Taiwan question with the Ukraine issue harbor a vile intention rather than lack common sense. Their real agenda is to create a new crisis across the Taiwan Strait to serve US geopolitical and economic interests at the expense of the wellbeing of people across the Strait and regional peace and stability.\nBut Taiwan is not Ukraine. The Chinese people’s resolve and determination to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity is invincible. Those who play with and fan up the fire on the Taiwan question will only wind up burning themselves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347251.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220329_10656950.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-29","Wang Wenbin","TASS","The Pentagon delivered the classified National Defense Strategy to Congress on Monday. According to a Department of Defense fact sheet about the National Defense Strategy, China is described as the “most consequential strategic competitor” and Russia as an “acute threat”. I wonder if you have any comments on this report?","The above-mentioned US national defense strategy report is full of Cold War and bloc confrontation mentality. China and Russia are two major countries. The US attempt to contain and suppress them will not succeed. The US should reflect on its due responsibilities in the Ukraine crisis, show repentance for and correct the practice of establishing imaginary enemies, ignoring other countries’ legitimate security concerns and stoking bloc confrontation. We urge the US to earnestly implement its leadership’s statements that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; that it does not aim to change China’s system; that the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; that it does not support “Taiwan independence”; and that it has no intention to seek a conflict with China. The US should work with China to find the right way to get along with each other under the new circumstances featuring mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347252.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220329_10657226.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-29","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","It is reported that the Taiwanese side said that Damon Wilson, President of the National Endowment for Democracy, is leading a delegation to visit Taiwan from March 27 to 30. The two sides announced that this year’s Global Assembly of the World Movement for Democracy will be held in Taipei in October. Do you have any comment?","The National Endowment for Democracy (NED) is believed to be a “second CIA”. This self-proclaimed “non-governmental” and “non-profit” organization actually has long been receiving funds from the US Congress and the White House. Under the pretext of so-called “democracy”, the NED is engaged in such shady activities as the infiltration of values, subversion and sabotage of other countries’ regimes, and instigation of anti-government movements around the world. The NED is behind color revolutions, upheavals and violent incidents in many parts of the world, including the “Orange Revolution”, the “Jasmine Revolution”, disturbance over proposed legislative amendments in Hong Kong and the anti-government demonstration in Thailand that happened in recent years. The organization has long colluded with anti-government entities in many countries. It is used by the US as a tool to interfere in other countries’ internal affairs and serve its selfish interests.\nThe NED has long been in league with “East Turkistan”, “Hong Kong independence” and “Tibet independence” forces. It funded and manipulated various anti-China demonstrations and protests, and is a main source and spreader of many China-related lies and rumors. In 2020 alone, the NED provided more than $10 million to nearly 70 China-related projects to promote activities that threatened China’s political and social stability, according to data published on the organization’s website. From 2004 to 2020, the NED provided $8.7583 million in funds to various “East Turkistan” organizations. It is dedicated to inciting and sponsoring anti-China separatist activities.\nNow the head of this organization is on a trip to Taiwan under the pretext of democracy. They are not bringing good recipe for democracy to the Taiwan region, but have the poison of separatism up their sleeves. A stern warning to the US side: the attempt to contain China by emboldening the “Taiwan independence” forces in the name of upholding democracy has never succeeded over the years, and will not succeed in the future. The so-called Summit for Democracy hosted by the US last year ended with little support. If the US again tries to seek political manipulation in support of “Taiwan independence” under the pretext of democracy, it will only encounter greater failure.\nAlso a stern warning to the DPP authorities in Taiwan: democracy is not a shield for “Taiwan independence” propositions or elements. True democracy meets the aspiration for the reunification of the nation of the 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities’ political manipulation of seeking “Taiwan independence” in the name of democracy will only push the people in Taiwan to the abyss of disasters and they will have to face the reckoning of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347252.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220329_10657226.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-30","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","On March 29, the Taiwan region’s leader Tsai Ing-wen met with Damon Wilson, President of the US National Endowment for Democracy (NED). Tsai said that she looks forward to sharing experience with the NED and jointly strengthen the resilience of democracy. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities are apt at using democracy as a pretext to mask its true face of “Taiwan independence”. But no matter how they try to gloss it over, their nature of seeking Taiwan independence by refusing to recognize the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle or pursuing “de-sinicization” or seeking “de jure independence” is laid bare.\nLast year, the DPP authorities tried to expand the space for their secessionist activities with the so-called Summit for Democracy, only to court a rebuff. This year, their attempts to put on a farce where the “Taiwan independence” forces hijack democracy in cahoot with the NED, or the “second CIA”, will only invite humiliation once again.\nNo matter how the DPP authorities try to cover things up, the international community cannot be fooled, and the ugly face of “Taiwan independence” will only be more nasty.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347253.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220330_10657653.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on March 30, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's regular TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","We note that on March 16, after the new policy for Taiwan compatriots applying to set up individual businesses was introduced, Taiwan compatriots in various places responded enthusiastically. On the 18th, the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office issued the first business license to a Taiwan resident individual business in a newly opened sector. Please introduce the reactions of Taiwan compatriots on the…","On March 16, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Ministry of Commerce, and the State Administration for Market Regulation jointly issued and implemented the \"Notice on Doing a Good Job in Handling Applications by Taiwan Residents to Establish Individual Industrial and Commercial Households in Pilot Regions for Innovative Development of Trade in Services.\" The response from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth on the mainland has been enthusiastic. The National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, local Taiwan associations, and Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople forwarded the full text of the Notice and related reports on websites, WeChat groups, and Moments.\nSeveral Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople interviewed said that the opening policy introduced this time fully demonstrates the concept of \"both sides of the Strait are one family.\" It suits Taiwan residents, mainly Taiwan youth, who want to start small-scale businesses on the mainland, meets the needs of Taiwan's young people and grassroots Taiwan businesspeople, and helps lower the threshold for Taiwan compatriots to start businesses on the mainland. Compared with setting up a company, applying for an individual industrial and commercial household requires only one person, has no registered capital requirement, and involves a smaller tax burden. This \"light cavalry,\" \"step-by-step\" model of entrepreneurship is well suited to Taiwan youth starting out, allowing them to gradually adapt to the market and environment and grow from small to large. The newly opened fields involve cultural and creative industries, rural revitalization, the service sector, and other industries, many of which are Taiwan's strong sectors. They offer Taiwan youth who wish to come to the mainland to run small businesses and start out a new option for employment, entrepreneurship, and realizing their dreams.\nAs the main beneficiaries, Taiwan youth fully recognize and actively respond to this policy. Taiwan youth in Jiangsu, Beijing, Shanghai, Guangdong, Fujian, Zhejiang, Chongqing, Hubei, Liaoning, and other provinces and municipalities have each consulted local competent authorities about establishing individual industrial and commercial households. On March 18, two days after the Notice was issued, a Taiwan youth in Kunshan, Jiangsu became the first to obtain a business license for an individual industrial and commercial household in a newly opened industry. Yesterday (March 29), a Taiwan youth in Wuhan, Hubei also obtained a business license for an individual industrial and commercial household in a newly opened industry. We believe that more and more Taiwan youth and Taiwan compatriots will benefit from this, take new steps in entrepreneurship and employment, and achieve better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422935.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","We note that recently, the Nongshi Network's program “Three Agriculture, Three People Talk” launched a series of short video programs marking the first anniversary of the “22 agriculture and forestry measures,” inviting responsible officials from relevant departments to answer, in a targeted way, questions of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses. After the videos were broadcast, many media outlets…","On March 17, 2021, eleven departments, including the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, and the State Forestry and Grassland Administration, jointly issued the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry.” Over the past year, many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have benefited, but some questions and difficulties have also arisen. To further help Taiwan compatriots and enterprises resolve doubts and clear up confusion, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs directed the “Sannong Sanren Tan” (Three Rural Issues, Three People Discuss) program of Nongshi TV to solicit questions from Taiwan compatriots and enterprises and provide answers. Based on the results of the question collection, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople are most concerned about two areas. The first is agricultural finance: How do I apply for a loan? What are the requirements for a loan? How can I get a loan without collateral? What are the standards for agricultural insurance subsidies and claims? The second is rural land transfer: How do I obtain land management rights? How do I renew the lease when it expires? How is the transfer price determined?\nIn response to these questions, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs invited relevant government officials and Taiwanese businesspeople's representatives to give video interviews introducing Taiwan compatriots in detail to agricultural loans, agricultural credit guarantees, the application process for agricultural insurance premium subsidies, land management rights, land transfer contracts, lease renewal for land transfers, and the prevention of land transfer risks, and offered specific operational recommendations. Mr. Yang Yong'an, a Taiwan compatriot representative from the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park in Zhangping, Fujian, and Mr. Zhuang Jiuyi, a Taiwan compatriot chili grower representative in Guangxi, each shared their experiences of obtaining a 3 million yuan loan and management rights to over 5,000 mu of land, providing examples that other Taiwan compatriots and enterprises can learn from and refer to.\nTaiwan compatriots and enterprises with needs may continue to follow the official websites of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and other departments, as well as related Nongshi TV programs, to gain a deeper understanding of mainland policies that benefit farmers. For further service consultations and case references, they may follow the official websites and WeChat public accounts of local Taiwan Affairs Offices, such as “Jingcai Taiwan” of the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, “Hutai Tong” of the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, “Jiangsu and Taiwan” of the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “Zhetai Weixun” of the Zhejiang Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “Etai Yijia” of the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “Xiangtai Xuan” of the Hunan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “Yinxiang Yuetai” of the Guangdong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, “Chuanyue Haixia” of the Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, and “Qianjin Baodao” of the Guizhou Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office. There they can learn about detailed local policy measures and implementation progress, as well as the many stories of Taiwan compatriots pursuing and realizing their dreams locally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The latest survey on employment of those born in the 1980s published on the island shows that 56% want to leave Taiwan to work, and 33% of young people list the mainland as their first choice. Recently, the phenomena of talent outflow and talent gaps in Taiwan have become increasingly prominent, and reports also show that 40% of young people will choose to become the “lying-flat” tribe in the future. What is your…","We welcome young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to work and live. The mainland has a strong material foundation, a huge market, abundant human resources, and the world’s largest and most complete industrial system with the most comprehensive categories and supporting facilities, providing sufficiently broad space and sufficiently diverse opportunities for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland. Since 2015, the Taiwan Affairs Office has granted the title to 78 Cross-Strait Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Bases and Demonstration Sites, covering various platforms such as industrial parks, schools, business incubators, enterprises and social organizations, providing internship and employment positions, coaching and training for Taiwan youth, and helping them intern, find jobs and start businesses on the mainland.\nThere are 8.71 million young people aged 20 to 45 in Taiwan. Many of them face pressures such as high housing prices, difficulty finding jobs and low salaries, to the point that some no longer believe that “hard work pays off.” You mentioned that nearly half of young students tend to become “lying flat” tribe members. We understand their pressures, and we want to say to them: while “small but refined” small joys are indeed a kind of happiness, “big and comprehensive” great innovations are even more stirring. To pursue life ideals and achieve better development, you may consider coming to the mainland to take a look. The opportunities the mainland can offer exceed what many people imagine. If you love traditional culture, you can work on the inheritance of intangible cultural heritage on the mainland, where there are the most intangible cultural heritage projects in the world. If you like taking unconventional paths, you can find the most interesting music, dance and painting on the mainland, and there are no shortage of like-minded people. For example, the nine members of the Taike rock band have already found their place in Chengdu. If you want to outshine all rivals, you can find the coolest skill-forging arena on the mainland and strive toward becoming one of the world’s most formidable skill masters or the most advanced scientists and engineers. If you love delicious food, you can bring Taiwan’s distinctive dishes to mainland dining tables and share the delicacies……\nYouth with dreams and drive, who see the situation clearly, seize opportunities, make good use of policies and work hard, will certainly succeed in the great tide of cross-Strait relations development. We will continue to create better conditions, benefit Taiwan compatriots just as we serve mainland people, and enable more aspiring Taiwan youth to have the opportunity to devote themselves to the great cause of national rejuvenation and write their own stories of striving on the vast land of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","American scholars Ge Laiyi and Zhuang Wanhua recently published a report attacking UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. It claims that the resolution did not resolve the so-called status issue of Taiwan, questions the one-China principle, and advocates that the international community should allow Taiwan to participate in international organizations. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","First, I must point out that this report is explicitly sponsored by the DPP authorities. The entire report is a collection of clichés from the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” rhetoric, and when discussing the one-China principle, it does not even mention the Cairo Declaration or the Potsdam Proclamation. We question whether the relevant US scholars have basic common sense.\nRegarding UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, we have systematically stated our position on many occasions. Resolution 2758 resolved the issue of China's representation in the United Nations politically, legally, and procedurally, and its premise is one China, with Taiwan being part of China. The relevant historical facts and legal basis are very clear. Anyone who distorts Resolution 2758 dares not mention the Cairo Declaration or the Potsdam Proclamation, and dares not face the real status quo of the Taiwan question or the core content of one China, which is that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China.\nThe relevant US report repeatedly says that Resolution 2758 expelled “Chiang Kai-shek's representatives,” without referring to “Taiwan” or the so-called “Republic of China.” In fact, after the founding of the People's Republic of China in 1949, the sole legal government representing China was the government of the People's Republic of China, which completed the succession of government under international law. Distorting Resolution 2758 and attacking the one-China principle is either ignorance or ulterior motives. The relevant US report does not mention at all the real reason the DPP authorities cannot participate in relevant international organizations and their activities after taking office, and it does not dare to face the reality that the DPP authorities are desperately pursuing “independence” and provoking and undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. This reflects that some people in the United States say they do not support “Taiwan independence” but in reality keep engaging in acts that tacitly approve of or even condone “Taiwan independence.”\nThe DPP authorities, in collusion with external forces, are seeking so-called “legal grounds” for their own pursuit of “independence,” but apart from evading historical facts, swapping concepts, and deceiving public opinion, they have no other means. “Taiwan independence” elements and their “court scholars” keep repeating so-called “Taiwan is Taiwan, China is China” and “Resolution 2758 did not resolve the issue of Taiwan's representation,” aiming to use such plausible-sounding concepts to evade the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China. We warn the DPP authorities: relying on such base tactics to distort international law and attack the one-China principle leads nowhere and will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422938.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The epidemic prevention and control situation on the mainland is currently severe and complex, and all localities are strictly and practically carrying out epidemic prevention and control work. Have recent cross-strait exchange activities, personnel travel, and Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises been affected? How will cross-strait economic and trade and exchange activities in various fields be…","Over the past two years since the outbreak of the epidemic, we have overcome the impact of epidemic factors and the obstacles artificially set up by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. Our efforts to promote cross-Strait exchanges and deepen integration and development have not stopped, the eager desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer and visit one another has not diminished, and cross-Strait civil exchanges and cooperation in all fields have not been interrupted.\nRecently, the epidemic in some localities has inevitably had a certain impact on cross-Strait exchange activities held locally. But we believe that, as various localities strictly and rigorously implement epidemic prevention and control work and strive to achieve dynamic zero-case status across society as soon as possible, exchanges in all fields across the Strait will certainly continue to maintain their momentum of development. We will overcome the adverse impact of the epidemic and continue to expand and deepen cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation. On the one hand, while ensuring epidemic prevention safety, we will adopt forms combining online and offline activities to support localities in holding more small-scale, specialized economic and trade activities related to Taiwan, based on local resources, industrial support, and other conditions, to promote pragmatic cooperation and mutual benefit between enterprises across the Strait.\nOn the other hand, we will make good use of the series of measures proposed in this year's Government Work Report, including the implementation of new combined tax and fee support policies, to provide timely help to enterprises and revive their vitality. Eligible Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland may all enjoy these benefits equally. In 2021, the mainland implemented tax and fee reductions exceeding 1 trillion yuan, and many Taiwan enterprises derived real, tangible benefits from them. We believe that as the new and stronger policy measures this year are implemented, Taiwan-funded enterprises, especially those engaged in manufacturing, will benefit more.\nMany journalist friends are also very concerned about the impact of the recent Shanghai epidemic on relevant Taiwan enterprises, so let me briefly introduce this here. According to our understanding, the overall production and operation of Taiwan-funded enterprises in Shanghai is currently stable. For some Taiwan enterprises where temporary logistics disruptions have occurred, local Taiwan Affairs Offices have specifically coordinated with relevant departments to issue enterprise certificates, passes, and other documents to help Taiwan enterprises minimize the impact of the epidemic to the greatest extent possible. The Shanghai Municipal Government recently issued the \"Several Policy Measures of Shanghai on Fully Fighting the Epidemic, Helping Enterprises, and Promoting Development,\" which includes 21 specific measures in 6 areas, to fully support the development of enterprises in Shanghai, including Taiwan enterprises. We believe that with the implementation of a series of measures coordinating epidemic prevention and control with economic and social development in the localities, Taiwan enterprises affected by the epidemic will soon return to normal production and operation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422933.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Chiu Tai-san, head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently claimed that the so-called cross-Strait formula of “mutual non-recognition of sovereignty and mutual non-denial of jurisdiction” advocated by Ma Ying-jeou is no longer sufficient, and that the two sides should “mutually recognize sovereignty.” What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided.\nSome DPP politicians, out of their political nature and narrow party self-interest, arbitrarily reverse right and wrong and confuse truth and falsehood, attempting to further escalate the “two-state theory.” This is blatant provocation and reckless advance. The reckless actions of the DPP authorities are a political scheme harboring malicious intent that is extremely dangerous and seriously endangers the security and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: do not misjudge the situation or miscalculate, and do not underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422937.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Some polls on the island show that if war breaks out across the Strait, more than half of Taiwan residents would be unwilling to go to the battlefield, and among those aged 20 to 29, as many as 70% are unwilling to go. There is also a lot of public opinion holding that the DPP authorities should not provoke and confront the mainland, and should create a peaceful and stable cross-Strait atmosphere through…","Taiwan is part of China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, one family with blood ties tighter than water. Promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the common wish of compatriots on both sides. Realizing peaceful reunification of the motherland is a shared vision of mutual benefit and win-win results for compatriots on both sides. But the wind does not stop when the tree wishes to be still. The DPP authorities collude with external forces, incite “anti-China and hatred of China” populism, escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and resort to any means to provoke “Taiwan independence,” attempting to change the fact that both sides belong to one China. This seriously undermines the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nFor a long time, the DPP authorities have relied on weaving lies to deceive the island’s public. They think they have succeeded, but lies remain lies and cannot deceive the broad masses of Taiwan people, including Taiwan’s youth. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to deeply recognize that “Taiwan independence” means war, and that “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Being coerced into serving as cannon fodder for the DPP authorities’ pursuit of “independence,” doing what pleases enemies and grieves kin, runs counter to the common aspiration of Taiwan compatriots for peace, development, and a good life. We advise the DPP authorities not to turn back the wheel of history. Only by returning to the correct track of the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and stopping provocations for “independence” can cross-Strait relations improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422932.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: Recently, Qiu Taisan, Hsiao Bi-khim and other officials of the DPP authorities have hyped the \"two-state theory,\" and Tsao Hsing-cheng, former \"honorary chairman\" of UMC in Taiwan, has also claimed that \"what truly brings long-term peace to Taiwan is the 'two-state theory.'\" What comment do you have on this? Second question: The DPP authorities claim that the mainland is exploiting the situation…","First, Taiwan is part of China, and both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Those who advocate the \"two-state theory\" only prove that they are forgetful of their ancestors and clowns who have abandoned their roots.\nSecond, we have always supported and encouraged compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially young people, to strengthen exchanges, deepen mutual understanding, and develop together. Online exchanges have built a platform for young people on both sides of the Strait to showcase themselves in diverse ways, provided greater room for self-development, and created more opportunities for mutual understanding and positive interaction among young people across the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities, out of narrow partisan interests, have deliberately obstructed and undermined civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. At bottom, they fear that compatriots on both sides will draw closer and get along well, and that the people of Taiwan will come to understand the real situation on the mainland. They use so-called \"cognitive warfare\" to deceive the people of Taiwan, create an \"information cocoon,\" and use it as a \"fig leaf\" to incite hostility, hatred, and antagonism. In the end, what is harmed is the development space and interests of the people of Taiwan, especially Taiwan's young people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","On March 25, the Taiwan legislature passed the so-called “constitutional amendment” lowering the voting and candidacy age to 18. What is your comment?","Our position has always been consistent and clear: we firmly oppose any form of “amending the Constitution to seek independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422936.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","The DPP authorities recently organized a so-called expert group to visit Japan to learn about the Japanese government’s situation regarding the discharge of nuclear-contaminated water, which has caused dissatisfaction in public opinion on the island. Many Taiwan residents believe they are going on a “publicly funded trip” and “whitewashing” Japan, attempting to mislead the public into believing that the Fukushima…","No matter how nuclear-contaminated water is packaged, it is still nuclear-contaminated water, and its threat to the marine ecological environment and to people's lives and health is obvious. The so-called “inspection” is merely a tactic by the DPP authorities to try to deceive Taiwan's residents. I believe Taiwan compatriots can see this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202203/t20220330_12422926.htm"],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","On March 18, President Xi Jinping held a video call with US President Biden at the latter’s request. The US side reiterated the “four noes and one no intention,” stressed that it does not support “Taiwan independence,” and adheres to the one-China policy. The DPP claimed that “the mainland distorted the content of the conversation.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","On the evening of March 18, President Xi Jinping held a video call with US President Biden at the latter’s request. The two heads of state candidly and in-depth exchanged views on China-US relations, the situation in Ukraine, and other issues of common concern.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests and the national sentiment of the Chinese people, and it is the most important and most sensitive core issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. During the call, the US government reiterated its “four noes and one non-intention,” clearly stating that it does not support “Taiwan independence” and adheres to the one-China policy. However, the DPP authorities are accustomed to deceiving the island’s public with lies and are obsessed with dragging external forces in to cheer on and back up their provocations to seek “independence.” Their intentions are sinister and their methods despicable, and they will only push Taiwan step by step toward danger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","At present, the COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control situation is severe in many places. Chen Baiyuan, a Taiwanese student at Huaqiao University, created several rap songs on the theme of fighting the epidemic, calling on everyone to cooperate with epidemic prevention in a mix of Mandarin and the Minnan dialect and conveying the positive energy of compatriots on both sides of the Strait joining hands to fight…","Since the outbreak of the epidemic, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in various places have participated in epidemic response work in different ways, contributing love and strength and reflecting the bond of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, where blood is thicker than water and they look out for one another. Many Taiwan youth have created epidemic-response songs and short videos recording the stories of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth on the mainland working hand in hand with mainland compatriots to fight the epidemic, using music to convey positive energy and showing the fraternal bond of compatriots on both sides of the Strait joining hands to weather the difficulties together. We believe that with everyone's concerted cooperation, the epidemic will soon ease. Everyone, keep it up!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","Chen Ming-tong, head of Taiwan's security department, said that, inspired by the Russia-Ukraine conflict, if the mainland were to launch a war against Taiwan, “if it does not move, then that is that; if it moves, it will absolutely be all-out.” A former head of Taiwan's defense department also said that if the two sides go to war, “the first battle is the last battle,” and the PLA could completely end the…","We have stressed time and again that we have patience and are willing, with the utmost sincerity and the greatest efforts, to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. At the same time, we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence.” If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to provoke and coerce, or even cross the red line, we will take resolute measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海记者","Lithuania's Minister of Economic Innovation recently said in an interview with Taiwan media that Lithuania is fully prepared to establish a so-called “economic and trade office” in Taiwan. The DPP authorities confirmed that they have received relevant applications from the Lithuanian government. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We urge the Lithuanian government to correct its mistakes on Taiwan-related issues as soon as possible and not to go further down the wrong path. The DPP authorities are infiltrating and courting some anti-China forces internationally, attempting to rely on external forces to seek “independence.” This will only end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","This year marks the 360th anniversary of the national hero Koxinga's defeat of the Dutch colonists and recovery of Taiwan. Recently, several pro-unification groups in Taiwan jointly held a symposium in Taipei titled “The Epochal Significance of Koxinga's Recovery of Taiwan.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Zheng Chenggong is a national hero revered by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. 360 years ago, he led his troops to drive out the Dutch colonialists and recover the sacred island of Taiwan; his historical merits will always be worth commemorating by compatriots on both sides.\nTaiwan's pro-unification groups held a symposium in Taiwan marking the 360th anniversary of Zheng Chenggong's recovery of Taiwan, discussing the historical value and contemporary significance of that recovery and voicing the call for compatriots on both sides to work together and jointly realize national reunification, which is very meaningful.\nIt is understood that relevant parties on both sides of the Strait will hold related commemorative activities at an appropriate time this year in Quanzhou, Fujian, Zheng Chenggong's ancestral home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","National Endowment for Democracy (NED) President Wilson led a delegation on a provocative visit to Taiwan from the 27th to the 30th. During this period, it will announce cooperation with the “Taiwan Foundation for Democracy” and hold the so-called “World Movement for Democracy” global conference in Taipei in October. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","This foundation, under the banner of “democracy,” is engaged in infiltration and subversion, and has been placed on the sanctions list by relevant authorities. The DPP authorities collude with this anti-China organization, act in concert with it, use the name of democracy to pursue the substance of “seeking independence,” engage in political manipulation and deceive the public. They will only end in a crushing defeat and will surely be punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","A Taiwanese youth recently brought Yellow River water back to Taiwan and held a “drop-of-water kinship test” at the Zhuoshui River in Yunlin County. A DPP people's representative called this act a mainland “cognitive warfare,” and the DPP authorities threatened to investigate and deal with it. What is your comment on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family. We support compatriots on both sides expressing, in any way, their promotion of exchanges and their enhanced mutual understanding and comprehension. Some DPP politicians readily wield the big stick of so-called “cognitive warfare” to suppress and threaten Taiwan compatriots who take part in cross-Strait exchanges. This only shows that their minds are beset by demons and they have gone astray.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan and the US recently formally signed the arms sale of the “Field Information Communication System.” Some commentators believe this system can “change the entire battlefield” and is preparation in communications and command for future joint combat operations by the US military in Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose the United States selling arms to the Taiwan region of China, and oppose any form of official exchanges such as military contacts between the United States and Taiwan. The DPP authorities' attempt to collude with external forces to “seek independence by force” will only push Taiwan toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","Since taking office, the DPP authorities have continuously expanded their so-called “defense spending.” Apart from having already allocated a NT$500 billion “special budget” for fighter jet procurement and so-called “combat power enhancement,” they will also allocate a special budget for “domestically built submarines.” Will this increase cross-Strait confrontation? In addition, there are rumors that the DPP…","Several recent polls on the island have shown that nearly 80 percent of Taiwan residents believe cross-Strait relations should maintain peaceful exchanges. Peace, development, and good living are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan compatriots and the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities, going against public opinion, have repeatedly raised topics such as the so-called \"strongest military training call-up,\" \"extension of military service,\" and \"expanded budget,\" inciting \"resisting China and defending Taiwan.\" This is entirely a political manipulation seeking the private interests of one party. On the surface they claim to protect the people of Taiwan, but in reality they are pushing the people of Taiwan into the flames of war, which is extremely sinister.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Recently, a DPP public representative claimed that Taiwan’s civil service examinations should “abolish classical Chinese,” saying “young people should not waste their youth on classical Chinese,” which was questioned as “de-Sinicization.” What comments do you have on this?","Public opinion in Taiwan has raised many criticisms and doubts about this blatant “de-Sinicization” conduct. Certain DPP politicians have deliberately and carefully sought to sever the ties between Taiwan and Chinese culture and the Chinese nation, incite cross-Strait confrontation, and have gone so far off-key and into anti-intellectualism that the harm will be endless.\nFacts have already proven, and will continue to prove, that no “de-Sinicization” conduct can change the Chinese cultural identity and Chinese national identity deeply rooted in Taiwan's society, nor can it sever the historical connections across the Strait or the blood ties between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","DPP people’s representative Lin Chuyin recently said that the mainland uses social apps such as Douyin, Xiaohongshu and Xigua Video to “infiltrate Taiwanese youth” in a down-to-earth way, carrying out “cognitive warfare.” Afterward, Taiwanese netizens found an account named “Lin Chuyin” on Douyin. What is the comment on this?","Many young people in Taiwan like to use some social media apps from the mainland, such as Xiaohongshu, Douyin, and iQIYI. The most direct reasons are that they are convenient, easy to understand, and fun. These apps provide many guides to life and learning: food, scenery, health, and exercise; beauty, outfits, films, TV, and anime; education, parent-child activities, gardening, and pets; writing, photography, painting, and dance; large and small courses, every kind of course... Any question you can think of about life can be answered on these apps. In a sense, making good use of these apps is a way for young people in Taiwan to improve their quality of life and enhance their sense of happiness. DPP politicians have been making outrageous claims about this, which only shows that they treat everything as political manipulation. They have long been detached from the lives of the Taiwan people and have long abandoned the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","中评社记者","First question: Chiu Tai-san (邱太三), head of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, said several days ago that there should be a flexible adjustment mechanism for deciding when the “Small Three Links” will be restarted, so as to avoid sudden interruptions that cause unnecessary misunderstandings. What is your comment on this?\nSecond question: CTi TV in Taiwan recently applied for a channel license for CTi Asia,…","First question: Since the outbreak of the epidemic, we have not imposed any restrictive measures on Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. We have only adopted some scientifically necessary epidemic prevention and control measures to protect the health and safety of Taiwan compatriots and other personnel. Who exactly caused the interruption of cross-Strait personal exchanges? Everyone understands that it is the DPP authorities. The “Small Three Links” is the most important and convenient channel for exchanges between the two sides, especially between Fujian and Taiwan. Residents on both sides hope to restore the “Small Three Links” as soon as possible. We hope the DPP authorities will do more to benefit cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than trying every means to obstruct and restrict them and engaging in political manipulation.\nSecond question: We have noted that public opinion on the island has commented on this a great deal. If one wants to frame someone, there is never a shortage of pretexts. The relevant practices of the DPP authorities have once again exposed their political face of “fake democracy, real suppression,” and their despicable conduct of brutally suppressing media with different positions in order to control public opinion and create a “chilling effect.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question. Recently, Chen Ming-tong, head of Taiwan's security agency, claimed when questioned by the legislature that during Tsai Ing-wen's term, “there was no problem in cross-Strait relations.” He also said that the US and Taiwan have the “Taiwan Relations Act,” and that if conflict broke out across the Strait, US intervention would be deeper. What comment do you have on this? Second question: a recent…","First question. Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have repeatedly made wild statements about the Ukraine situation in order to draw attention to themselves. In fact, more and more Taiwan compatriots have seen through the timid and empty bluster of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, who keep consoling themselves with lies, and have seen the truth that external forces are unreliable and untrustworthy.\nThe Taiwan question and the Ukraine question are fundamentally different. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is entirely China's internal affair, leaving no room for external forces to interfere. Taiwan's future lies in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and in achieving national reunification, not in relying on any external forces' “empty promises.” We warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that “seeking independence by relying on foreigners” has no way out, and betting on external forces is doomed to fail. If they continue to misjudge the situation, persist in their delusions, and take desperate risks on the road of “Taiwan independence,” they will surely be met with head-on blows.\nSecond question. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to recognize that external forces manipulating Taiwan-related issues are playing the scheme of “using Taiwan to contain China,” at the cost of the interests of the Taiwan people. The deception laboriously concocted by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, namely “if something happens in Taiwan, America will come to help,” has long since gone bankrupt.\nThe future of Taiwan, the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will work with us to push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, resolve the political confrontation across the Strait, achieve lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait, and realize the vision of national reunification.\nThat concludes this press conference. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202203/t20220330_12422915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-03-31","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","China’s diplomatic and military pressure on Taiwan represents a threat to all democracies and the US is committed to helping the island defend itself. Those were comments from a US official at the AIT. What’s China’s comment?","The relevant remarks are purely smears and denigration. They represent interference in China’s internal affairs. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiques, and handle issues related to Taiwan in a prudent and proper manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347254.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220331_10658157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-03-31","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, the US Department of Defense submitted the classified Nuclear Posture Review to Congress on March 28, which shows that the Biden administration will maintain the established nuclear deterrence policies and fails to fulfill the campaign pledge of no first use of nuclear weapons. Japan’s Chief of Cabinet Secretary Matsuno Hirokazu commented on the other day that as a US ally, Japan strongly…","We cannot make a comprehensive assessment on the US Nuclear Posture Review which has not gone public yet. Based on the limited information the US has released, we regret to note that the Biden administration has not fulfilled its campaign pledge to give up the policy of first use of nuclear weapons, a commitment expected by the outside world. This will have a negative impact on global strategic stability and the process of international nuclear disarmament.\nJapan, the only country that has ever lived through a nuclear strike, advocates building a world free of nuclear weapons while “strongly supporting” the US in adopting a nuclear deterrence policy based on the first use of nuclear weapons. This fully reveals the hypocritical nature and double standard of Japan’s policies. I would also like to point out that regional countries and the international community are gravely concerned about the irresponsible remarks made by some Japanese politicians recently on the so-called “nuclear sharing” between the US and Japan. Japan should earnestly fulfill its obligations under the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons (NPT), its three non-nuclear principles, and avoid doing things that will undermine global and regional security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347254.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202203/t20220331_10658157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","According to a message from the WeChat official account \"Ministry of National Defense Releases,\" on the 15th, Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, made a statement regarding the visit to Taiwan by U.S. congressional members.\nWu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense.\nWu Qian said that recently, U.S. congressional members, disregarding the strong opposition of the Chinese side, deliberately provoked and visited Taiwan. This U.S. conduct seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously undermines the political foundation of China-U.S. relations, and has led to further tension and escalation in the Taiwan Strait situation. On the one hand the U.S. has made a commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" and on the other hand it has sent serious wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces; this is extremely hypocritical and utterly lacking in good faith. The Chinese side firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nTaiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of Chinese territory. The Taiwan question brooks no external interference. The Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People's Liberation Army recently organized a multi-service joint combat readiness patrol in the sea and airspace around Taiwan Island and conducted multi-subject targeted exercises. This is a necessary action taken in accordance with the current security situation in the Taiwan Strait and the need to safeguard national sovereignty. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is ready for battle and will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart the schemes of external interference and \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716230.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","This year marks the 73rd anniversary of the founding of the People’s Navy. Born for the sea and striving for strength through the sea, the Navy has become an important force in defending national sovereignty, security and development interests, and in maintaining world peace, stability and prosperity. Please spokesperson further introduce the development of the People’s Navy since the 18th National Congress of…","As you said, this year marks the 73rd anniversary of the founding of the People's Navy. On this occasion, I extend holiday greetings to my comrades in the Navy! Since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, the People's Navy has resolutely implemented the decisions and instructions of the Party Central Committee, the Central Military Commission, and Chairman Xi, deeply studied and implemented Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military, and achieved historic changes and historic accomplishments in all areas of development. First, political and ideological building has become stronger. Navy units at all levels have persistently used the Party's innovative theories to shape the soul and cultivate people, deeply carried out major educational activities such as theme-based education and Party history learning and education, vigorously promoted and celebrated advanced models in the Navy in the new era, and continued to inherit the glorious tradition and red genes of the People's Navy, greatly gathering a powerful force of will, with loyalty to mission, courage in battle, and achievement at sea. Second, combat readiness has become more capable. Navy units have made practical combat-oriented training a priority, built and improved a new military training system, comprehensively raised the level of combat-oriented training, and steadily advanced the transition from a near-sea defensive force to a far-sea defensive force, with steady improvements in strategic deterrence and counterstrike, maritime maneuver operations, joint maritime operations, comprehensive defensive operations, and comprehensive support capabilities. Third, transformative development has continuously achieved breakthroughs. The building of new-quality combat forces has improved in quality and accelerated in speed. A new contingent of talent, represented by carrier-based aircraft pilots and aircraft carrier command personnel, has risen and grown. A modern equipment system led by fourth-generation equipment and built mainly on third-generation equipment is taking shape. The comprehensive support chain, relying on overseas support bases and maritime medical rescue, has become more efficient, achieving leapfrog development. Fourth, military exchanges with foreign countries have become closer. The Navy is committed to building a community with a shared future for mankind and a community with a shared future for the oceans. Its “circle of friends” is growing larger, its voyages are reaching farther, and high-level exchanges, professional communication, and technical cooperation continue to deepen. It provides more and more international public security goods. Bilateral and multilateral maritime exercises such as those with Russia, Pakistan, Thailand, and China-ASEAN countries, along with international military competitions and other joint exercises, training, and competitions, are being held on a regular basis. Escort missions in the Gulf of Aden and the “Harmonious Mission” medical services have won praise, and assisting in rescuing and salvaging the sunken Indonesian submarine and delivering relief supplies to Tonga have earned full recognition from countries in the region. The increasingly strong People's Navy will surely continue to make new contributions to world peace, stability, and prosperity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716231.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to reports, State Councilor and Minister of National Defence Wei Fenghe recently held a phone call with U.S. Secretary of Defense Austin, the first phone call between the defense ministers of China and the United States since the Biden administration took office. Please further introduce the relevant situation and comment.","On April 20, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe held a call at the invitation of U.S. Secretary of Defense Austin. This was a concrete step to implement the important consensus reached by President Xi Jinping and President Biden. The two sides exchanged views on the relationship between the two countries' militaries and on issues of mutual concern. It was a candid, in-depth, and constructive strategic communication. During the call, both sides agreed that China and U.S. militaries should keep communication channels open, manage risks, and advance the development of crisis communication mechanisms.\nAs the world's two most important major countries, China and the United States benefit when they cooperate and suffer when they confront each other. Neither can defeat the other, and neither can change the other. Both sides have a thousand reasons to make China-U.S. relations work well, and not a single reason to make them worse. A stable relationship between the two militaries serves the common interests of both countries and the shared expectations of the international community. We demand that the U.S. side truly implement President Biden's \"four no's and one no-intention\" statement.\nIt must be stressed that China's development of military relations with the United States is guided by principles. In response to recent U.S. military provocations against China, smearing and framing, and threats and pressure on issues such as Taiwan, maritime and air security, and Ukraine, we have resolutely and forcefully countered them, firmly defending our national interests and dignity. We solemnly warn the U.S. side never to underestimate China's resolve and capabilities. We hope the U.S. side will abandon Cold War zero-sum thinking, view China's development objectively and rationally, and, together with China, seriously implement the important consensus reached by the leaders of the two countries, enhance military mutual trust, strengthen dialogue and exchanges, manage risks and crises, carry out pragmatic cooperation, and ensure the normal and stable development of relations between the two militaries.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716277.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","It is reported that on April 19, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe held a video call with Mozambican Minister of National Defense Su Mei. Please further introduce the details of this call, and what are China's expectations for the development of military relations between China and Mozambique?","State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe recently held a video call with Mozambican Minister of National Defence Su Mei. The two sides had friendly exchanges and in-depth discussions on military relations, anti-epidemic cooperation, and the international and regional situation, and reached many points of consensus.\nChina and Mozambique are good brothers and good partners who share weal and woe through thick and thin. In recent years, guided by the strategic leadership of the heads of state of the two countries, bilateral military relations have continuously deepened, with remarkable results in cooperation in personnel training, equipment and technology, military medicine, force building, and other areas. Standing at a new historical starting point, the Chinese military is willing to further consolidate the special friendship of “comrades and brothers” with the Mozambican side, further deepen practical cooperation in all fields, and jointly promote the forward development of military relations between the two sides.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716314.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","The US Department of Defense recently released its Freedom of Navigation Operations report for fiscal year 2021, claiming that from October 2020 to September 2021, the US challenged 37 “excessive maritime claims” by 26 countries and regions, the most of which were related to China, involving the Chinese mainland five times and the Taiwan region once. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have noted this report. For years, the United States, under the pretext of so-called “freedom of navigation,” has disregarded other countries’ maritime rights and security concerns, and has frequently dispatched military vessels and aircraft that infringe on other countries’ sovereignty and security and undermine regional peace and tranquility. China firmly opposes this and calls on relevant countries to jointly resist this kind of maritime bullying.\n“Navigation” is not running amok, and “freedom” is not wanton conduct. Everything must be based on international law and the basic norms of international relations, with the sovereignty and security of coastal states as the boundary. This is a self-evident truth. The United States has still not even joined the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, yet it has repeatedly relied on gunboats to carry out brutal “law enforcement” around the world. In essence, it is challenging the international order based on international law, continuously threatening the safety of maritime navigation, and aggravating regional tensions. Such acts are not worth issuing any report to boast about. Instead, it should deeply reflect on how many collision incidents and how many casualties its obstinate and self-righteous conduct has caused.\nWe urge the United States to shoulder the responsibility expected of a major country, stop so-called “freedom of navigation operations,” stop issuing such irresponsible reports, genuinely respect other countries’ sovereignty, security and maritime rights, and do more things that are conducive to regional peace and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716316.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-03-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Not long ago, at a UN Security Council meeting on biosecurity issues, Russia released documents on US military biological activities in Ukraine and globally, accusing the US of violating the Biological Weapons Convention. In response to Russia's accusations, the US has not only consistently failed to respond directly, but has also, in its published “2022 Arms Control Compliance Report,” questioned China, Russia,…","Biological weapons are weapons of mass destruction. Recently, reports that the United States has violated the Biological Weapons Convention and engaged in biological military activities have continued to surface, causing sustained attention and concern in the international community, including China. China believes that on this major security issue, the United States needs to explain clearly.\nFirst, the United States is the true creator of biochemical crises. There is solid evidence showing that in the 1950s, the US military used bacteriological weapons on the Korean Peninsula, including in the China-North Korea border region, a fact that even American historians have publicly acknowledged. During the Vietnam War, the “Agent Orange” used by the US military caused irreversible harm to the Vietnamese people and the local ecological environment. It can be said that the United States is the only country in the world to have used all weapons of mass destruction, including nuclear weapons, chemical weapons, and biological weapons, against other countries.\nSecond, a growing number of practical questions cannot be avoided. According to information published by the United States itself, the US has established 336 laboratories in 30 countries. According to statements by the US Deputy Secretary of State herself, there are biological research facilities in Ukraine involving US participation, and there is concern to prevent research materials from falling into the hands of Russian forces. Therefore, the peoples of the world have every right to question the US: what exactly is the relationship between the US Department of Defense and the US overseas biological laboratories? If the US laboratories in Ukraine were merely for scientific research, why did the US Department of Defense deeply participate in them? Why do rare epidemics often break out in the locations of US military overseas biological laboratories? The United States must give a clear and unambiguous account of these questions; it cannot evade them by hiding.\nThird, we have consistently and strictly abided by the relevant provisions of the Biological Weapons Convention, and advocate the comprehensive prohibition and thorough destruction of all weapons of mass destruction, including biological weapons, and firmly oppose any country researching, possessing, or using biological weapons under any circumstances. The so-called “Arms Control Compliance Report” fabricated by the United States adopts the posture of a schoolmaster, pointing fingers at other countries' compliance with treaties; it is baseless and utterly absurd. On the contrary, the United States alone opposes establishing a verification mechanism for the Biological Weapons Convention, and it sets up biological laboratories around the world and carries out biological military activities. Why does the United States apply double standards on this issue? What exactly is it trying to hide? Such an irresponsible attitude has greatly heightened the concern of the international community on this issue.\nFourth, biological military activities concern international peace and security and the security interests of all countries. As a former victim of biological weapons, China solemnly demands that the United States adopt a responsible attitude, earnestly face the concerns and doubts of the international community, make comprehensive and concrete clarifications about its biological military activities, and accept multilateral verification.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/03-31/9716321.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-04-06","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Daily","The US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said in a press release on April 5 that the State Department has approved a sale of up to $95 million worth of military technical support and related equipment to the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States”. It mainly consists of training, planning, deployment, operation, maintenance, and sustainment of the Patriot Air Defense System and…","US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, especially the August 17 Communique, gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China rejects and deplores this.\nThe US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, cancel the above-mentioned arms sale plan, stop arms sales to and military contacts with Taiwan. China will take firm and robust measures to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347257.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220406_10664971.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Taiwan's foreign affairs chief Wu Zhaoxie recently made fallacious remarks about cross-Strait relations in an interview, using the situation in Ukraine to attack and smear the mainland. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 6 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 6th that recently, the DPP authorities have deliberately exploited the situation in Ukraine to jump around, misleading the people of Taiwan and international public opinion. On one hand, they incite “anti-China and resist China” sentiment, fawn and beg for pity, and profess their “value” as a strategic pawn of external forces, seeking so-called “protection” and “support.” On the other hand, they hype up the so-called “military threat” from the mainland, bark loudly but are timid inside, shout “war theory,” and continue to coerce and hold hostage the people of Taiwan. Their fundamental purpose is to attempt to “internationalize” the Taiwan question and to provide cover for their “Taiwan independence” provocations. Remarks by Wu Chao-hsieh and his ilk are clumsy performances of the above scheme.\nMa Xiaoguang said that Taiwan is part of China, China will inevitably be reunified, and “Taiwan independence” separatism has no way out. No matter how Wu Chao-hsieh and his ilk use “democracy” and “freedom” as a fig leaf to dress themselves up, they cannot conceal their face of splitting the country and selling out national interests, and they cannot escape the fate that “Taiwan independence” is bound to perish.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220406_12424510.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 6 dispatch. In response to the decision by relevant US government departments on the 5th to sell to the Taiwan region a “Patriot” missile technical assistance project worth approximately US$95 million, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to a question on the 6th, said: The US selling arms to the Taiwan region seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué. The US side should immediately correct its erroneous conduct of arms sales to Taiwan and stop playing with fire on Taiwan-related issues.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, attempting to “resist reunification by force,” and spending the hard-earned money of Taiwan compatriots to buy weapons in pursuit of political self-interest, will only push Taiwan compatriots step by step into the fire pit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220406_12424511.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-07","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen said on April 6 that the US has the ability and resolve to use sanctions against China as it has against Russia following Moscow’s invasion of Ukraine if Beijing “invades” Taiwan. US Deputy Secretary of State Wendy Sherman said on the same day that Beijing should take away the right lessons from the coordinated Western response over Ukraine that any moves by China to take Taiwan…","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is an issue left over from the civil war in China. The means of its resolution is China’s internal affair, where no foreign country has any right to interfere. The Chinese people’s resolve and will to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. That being said, we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures in response to the interference of foreign forces and the secessionist activities of a handful of “Taiwan independence” separatists.\nCurrently there is a new wave of tension across the Taiwan Strait. The root cause is that the authorities in Taiwan keep pushing for the independence agenda by soliciting US support and that some in the US attempt to use Taiwan to contain China. The two sides have been colluding with each other. A few people even deliberately draw an analogy between Taiwan and Ukraine despite their completely different nature in an attempt to confuse public opinion and profit from the chaos. This is playing with fire. Those who play with fire are bound to get burned themselves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347258.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220407_10665432.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-07","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi apparently plans to visit Taiwan on Sunday after her trip to Japan. This will be the first visit to Taiwan by a holder of the Speaker’s office in 25 years. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","China resolutely opposes all forms of official contact between the US and Taiwan. Congress is a branch of the US government and should stringently abide by the one-China policy that the US upholds. If Speaker Pelosi visits Taiwan, this would gravely violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US Joint Communiqués, seriously undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, severely impact the political foundation of China-US relations and send a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nThe US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, immediately cancel Speaker Pelosi’s plan to visit Taiwan, stop official contact with Taiwan, and fulfill its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” with real actions. If the US insists on having its own way, China will take firm and strong measures to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. All possible consequences that arise from this will completely be borne by the US side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347258.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220407_10665432.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-07","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","You just said that if US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi visits Taiwan, China will respond with strong measures. What kind of strong measures will China respond with?","I just made my point very clear. If this visit is made, China will take firm and strong measures in response. The ensuing consequences will be completely borne by the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347258.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220407_10665432.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-04-07","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","","According to the official WeChat account of the News Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense, Tan Kefei, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, responded to a question on US arms sales to Taiwan, emphasizing that China urges the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to immediately cancel the arms sales plan to Taiwan and stop US-Taiwan military ties, so as to avoid further damage to the relations between the two countries' militaries.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, on April 5, the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency announced that the US had approved the sale to Taiwan of military technology and related equipment worth a total of 95 million US dollars, and personnel and technical assistance for Taiwan's “Patriot” air defense missile system. What is your comment on this?\nTan Kefei said that the US sale of weapons to Taiwan region of China seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously undermines China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously damages China-US relations and military-to-military relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this and has lodged serious representations with the US side.\nTan Kefei stressed that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question concerns China's core interests, and any external interference is absolutely not permitted. China urges the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to immediately cancel the above arms sales plan to Taiwan and stop US-Taiwan military ties, so as to avoid further damage to the relations between the two countries' militaries. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take strong measures to resolutely thwart any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-07/9722224.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-04-07","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 7 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 7th in response to a question: We will not tolerate at all “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct or the erroneous words and deeds of the United States that undermine our core interests. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop any attempt to collude with external forces to seek…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities are stubbornly pushing the erroneous line of “Taiwan independence” and colluding with U.S. anti-China forces to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence.” Some people in the U.S. government and Congress continuously provoke, undermine the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, repeatedly violate the solemn commitments the U.S. has made on the Taiwan question, and play the “Taiwan card” to “use Taiwan to contain China.” Taiwan and the U.S. have stepped up collusion to carry out separatist activities, further aggravating tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220407_12424720.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-08","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","So it appears Nancy Pelosi isn’t going to make a trip to Taiwan after all, because she has COVID. Do you have a comment about this?","China has recently made its position clear on Speaker Pelosi’s planned visit to Taiwan and Chinese officials have also lodged solemn representations with the US side. We extend sympathy to Speaker Pelosi for contracting COVID-19 and wish her a speedy recovery. What she should do is not postpone the visit, but cancel it immediately.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347259.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220408_10665796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-08","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 8 (electronic dispatch). Regarding the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council's remarks on April 7 about the election of the Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 8th in response to a question: For the purpose of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities are accustomed to manipulating Hong Kong affairs, making irresponsible remarks, and maliciously smearing. They attempt to use channels of exchange between Hong Kong and Taiwan to keep extending their black hands. They have repeatedly failed and will not succeed in the future either. The DPP authorities' record of disrupting Hong Kong is replete with disgraceful acts, each one of which is on record. For the conduct of relevant DPP personnel, we will punish them in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220408_12424994.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-11","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Just wanted to follow up one more time on the Serbia question. You just now said it was a bilateral arrangement between China and Serbia and wasn’t targeting a third party. But is China not worried in some way that completing arms transfers like this threatens what is at the moment a very fragile peace in that part of Europe?","What do you mean by that question? Did you ever care whether regional peace and stability is threatened when the US sold arms to Europe and Taiwan? Why do you think it’s so when China sells some conventional military items to Serbia?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347260.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220411_10666674.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-13","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","The Seventh Our Ocean Conference will be co-hosted by the US and Palau on April 13 and 14. According to spokesperson for Taiwan’s foreign affairs department, Chang Tzi-chin, “special envoy of Taiwan’s President”, will attend the conference in the official capacity of Taiwan Environmental Protection Administration Minister. What is your comment?","To start, I must stress that China does not recognize the so-called “special envoy of Taiwan’s President”. The US and Palau try to create the false impression of “two Chinas” by allowing officials of the Taiwan authorities to attend the meeting. China deplores and firmly opposes this.\nThere is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a historical and legal fact that cannot be changed by any individuals. The US and Palau should abide by the one-China principle and not provide any platform for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We also have this stern warning to the DPP authorities: any attempt to seek “breakthroughs” in the international community is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220413_10667402.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on April 13, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear media friends, good morning. I will host today's press conference. I am now willing to take your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","We note that, to implement the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference and help enterprises cope with the epidemic and promote development, various localities have successively issued policies and measures to help enterprise development recently, and Taiwan-funded enterprises are equally benefiting. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, localities have been working to implement the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference and the deployments and requirements put forward in the 2022 Government Work Report, and have successively introduced policies and measures to support enterprise development. Relevant parties have actively assisted Taiwan-funded enterprises in enjoying the same benefits, and have provided support and convenience for Taiwan-funded enterprises in fighting the epidemic and stabilizing production.\nAfter Shanghai issued the “Several Policy Measures for Fully Fighting the Epidemic, Helping Enterprises and Promoting Development,” the local Taiwan Affairs Office assisted Taiwan-funded enterprises in applying to enjoy relevant policies, actively helping enterprises ease difficulties and stabilize jobs. This included assisting Taiwan-funded enterprises in applying for epidemic prevention expenditure subsidies and rent reductions, implementing differentiated epidemic prevention measures of “one policy per enterprise” and “one plan per factory,” supporting key enterprises and supporting enterprises to resume production, and coordinating with relevant commercial banks to provide financial relief plans for Taiwan-funded enterprises during the epidemic, etc.\nJiangsu Province published and implemented the “Several Policy Measures on Further Helping Market Entities Relieve Difficulties and Solve Problems and Focusing on Stabilizing Economic Growth,” which includes 40 specific measures in 8 areas, to fully help enterprises in Jiangsu, including Taiwan-funded enterprises, boost confidence and stabilize expectations. At present, Nanjing, Suzhou, Huai’an, Taizhou, Changzhou, Lianyungang, Yangzhou, Yancheng and 8 other prefecture-level cities in Jiangsu have also successively introduced and vigorously promoted the implementation of help-enterprise and benefit-enterprise relief measures with local characteristics.\nHubei Province implemented the “Several Policies on Promoting the Recovery and Development of Difficult Industries in the Service Sector” issued by the National Development and Reform Commission and other departments, proposing 42 relief measures and 3 safeguard measures. These mainly include universal measures for the service sector, relief and support measures for the catering, retail, culture, tourism, sports and transportation industries, and precise implementation of epidemic prevention and control measures. Taiwan-funded enterprises in Hubei that meet the conditions can all enjoy them equally.\nHunan Province issued the “Several Policies on Promoting Steady Growth of the Industrial Economy” and the “Several Policies on Promoting the Recovery and Development of Some Difficult Industries in the Service Sector.” Shandong, Guizhou, Shenyang and other places have also successively launched policy measures to help enterprises ease difficulties.\nWe treat Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises equally. Since the beginning of this year, the policy measures to support enterprise development introduced by the State Council, relevant departments and localities can all be applied uniformly by Taiwan businesspeople who meet the conditions. We hope that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will actively learn about and master them and enjoy what they are entitled to. Local Taiwan Affairs Offices will, as always, provide proactive services to help Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises understand and make good use of the relevant policy measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426347.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","The Standing Committee of the Jiangsu Provincial People's Congress recently deliberated the “Jiangsu Province Regulations on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation with Taiwan (Draft),” which has drawn public attention. What is your evaluation?","Recently, the 《Jiangsu Province Regulations on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation with Taiwan (Draft)》, reviewed by the Standing Committee of the Jiangsu Provincial People's Congress, takes as its main thread providing equal treatment to Taiwan businesses and compatriots and promoting comprehensive economic and cultural exchange and cooperation between Jiangsu and Taiwan. It actively responds to the reasonable demands of Taiwan compatriots in entrepreneurship, employment, study, and daily life, and explores ways to consolidate and raise the level and quality of Jiangsu-Taiwan economic and cultural exchange and cooperation through the rule of law. It is a beneficial exploration for promoting high-quality development of Taiwan work in the new era and has a positive role in deepening cross-Strait integrated development.\nWe encourage and support all regions and departments in using rule-of-law thinking and methods to provide more equal treatment and development opportunities to Taiwan businesses and compatriots, and in continuously improving institutional arrangements and policy measures that promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426338.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2022 Government Work Report clearly implemented new combined tax and fee support policies, with tax reductions and tax refunds carried out together. Relevant competent authorities said that留抵退税 (refunds of retained input tax credits) amount to about 1.5 trillion yuan, with processing starting on April 1. Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland are equally eligible for the relevant policies. Please ask the…","The 2022 Government Work Report proposed adopting both tax cuts and tax refunds, with an expected total of about RMB 2.5 trillion in tax refunds and reductions for the year, including about RMB 1.5 trillion in excess-credit tax refunds (留抵退税). All refund funds will go directly to enterprises. Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland are equally eligible for this policy. To give a few examples: a Taiwan-funded small and micro enterprise in Huai'an City, Jiangsu Province, which uses rice husks to produce environmentally friendly lunch boxes, went to the tax authority to inquire on April 1, the first day the new policy took effect, and successfully applied for a tax refund of RMB 337,600. The company's chairman said this tax refund is “real money” in hand. As of April 7, seven Taiwan-funded enterprises in Shandong Province had applied for excess-credit tax refunds, with a cumulative amount of RMB 3,431,100. We hope that eligible Taiwan-funded enterprises will actively apply for excess-credit tax refunds, enjoy all that they are entitled to, and benefit from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Some media reported that the DPP authorities have recently been summoning mainland enterprises operating in Taiwan on a large scale to investigate so-called “illegal activities of poaching Taiwan's high-tech talent,” creating momentum for the introduction of an “Economic Espionage Act.” May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","We are highly attentive to these developments. For some time, the DPP authorities have increasingly obstructed and undermined cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Recently, they have also scheming to smear and intimidate mainland enterprises operating in Taiwan, further escalating cross-Strait confrontation and provoking trouble. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: this political manipulation cannot halt the trend of exchanges and cooperation among compatriots across the Strait, and will only harm the vital interests of Taiwan’s business community and compatriots on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","In response to suggestions from Taiwan businesspeople to restore cross-Strait cargo and passenger air routes to cities such as Nanjing and Wuxi, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said Nanjing is already one of the 10 cross-Strait air cargo points, and that cross-Strait airlines can submit flight applications to the cross-Strait aviation authorities. What is the mainland side's attitude on this?","It should be pointed out that from February 10, 2020 to the present, the DPP authorities have unilaterally suspended cross-Strait air passenger flights other than round-trip flights to and from the four cities of Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen and Chengdu. On the operation of cargo routes, there is no obstacle on the mainland side. If Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises and cross-Strait shipping companies have demand, we will actively support them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities claim that the mainland's epidemic prevention and control measures have limited effect, and that the island will implement the so-called “New Taiwan Model” for epidemic prevention. What is the spokesperson's comment?","More than two years since the epidemic began, we have always adhered to the principles of putting the people first and life first. We have placed the lives and health of the people in first place, implemented the general policy of “dynamic zero-COVID” for epidemic prevention and control, and adopted practical and effective measures to combat the COVID-19 epidemic, achieving epidemic-fighting accomplishments that have attracted worldwide attention. We are one of the countries with the lowest COVID-19 infection and mortality rates in the world, and we were the first to turn economic growth from negative to positive. Last year, economic growth was 8.1%.\nOur epidemic prevention and control practice has proven that, through scientific and effective measures and the active cooperation of the broad masses, it is possible to coordinate epidemic prevention and control with economic and social development, and to achieve the goals of precise prevention and control and dynamic zero-COVID. The lives and health of the people can be effectively safeguarded.\nAs for the epidemic prevention and control policies on the island, all sectors of the island have their own comments.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, relevant mainland localities held a ceremony commemorating Xuanyuan Huangdi (the Yellow Emperor) during the Qingming Festival, with compatriots on both sides of the Strait participating online. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland “uses specific Taiwanese figures for political manipulation and ‘united front’ propaganda, which cannot change the fact that the two sides are ‘not…","Cherishing the dead and honoring ancestors is the common cultural heritage of Chinese people, and it is also the powerful spiritual driving force that has enabled the Chinese nation to endure and continue unceasingly to this day. Each year, worshipping Xuanyuan Huangdi, the human ancestor of the Chinese nation, has become an important traditional ritual in the spiritual life of Chinese people at home and abroad. Around this year’s Qingming Festival, relevant worship activities were held in Shaanxi, Henan, Zhejiang and other places, and Taiwan compatriots on the mainland and on the island actively participated both offline and online. This reflects that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and share a common cultural root and spiritual home, which no one can separate or sever by any obstruction.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have deliberately peddled the “two-state theory,” attempting to cut off the Chinese national roots of Taiwan compatriots, sever the blood ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, smear and attack the mainland in various ways, and stir up antagonism between compatriots on both sides, in order to carry out their goal of “independence.” Now they even slander and frame the joint worship of Huangdi by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This is pure ingratitude toward their ancestors, and is truly despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426345.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Several members of the U.S. House of Representatives recently jointly called on the Biden administration to invite Taiwan to participate in the so-called “Indo-Pacific Economic Framework.” The DPP authorities said they would seek U.S. support on this. What comments do you have?","No matter what economic framework the Taiwan region of China wishes to join, the premise must in every case conform to the one-China principle. We oppose the Taiwan region participating in any economic or trade arrangements of an official nature or signing any economic or trade agreements of an official nature.\nAs for the US government constantly hyping the concept of the “Indo-Pacific” and promoting the so-called “Indo-Pacific Strategy,” its essence is an attempt to set up small cliques to contain China. The DPP authorities' attempt to squeeze into such small cliques fully exposes their nature of “relying on the US to seek independence” and provoking the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426334.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Senior U.S. officials have recently repeatedly used the situation in Ukraine to hype up the so-called “military threat” from the mainland to Taiwan, claiming that if the mainland were to “use force against Taiwan,” the United States and the international community would intervene and impose sanctions on China. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. We advise relevant US government officials to first clarify the basic facts that the Taiwan question involves China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, clarify the serious commitment that the US government does not support “Taiwan independence,” and clarify the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. Some people on the US side who attempt to play the “Taiwan card” and “use Taiwan to contain China” have miscalculated. If they keep playing with fire, they will surely “burn themselves.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426343.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan media hyped that on the 8th, U.S. Deputy Secretary of State McKeown mentioned to WHO Director-General Tedros that the U.S. supports Taiwan becoming a WHO observer. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The World Health Organization is a UN specialized agency that only sovereign states may join, and the Taiwan region, as part of China, has no right to join. Any question concerning the participation of the Taiwan region of China in international organization activities must be resolved under the one-China principle. The US government has repeatedly expressed its opposition to the Taiwan region of China participating in international organizations that only sovereign states may join. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to be prudent in words and deeds on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426330.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Since taking office, the DPP authorities have constantly distorted and denied the “1992 Consensus,” attempting to create the illusion on the island that the “1992 Consensus” is a “political framework unilaterally set by the mainland.” The Mainland Affairs Council recently claimed that the island’s people do not agree that “the ‘1992 Consensus’ is the stabilizing anchor of cross-strait relations.” What is the…","The reaching of the “1992 Consensus” reflects the common position of both sides of the Taiwan Strait in upholding the one-China principle. It defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the cornerstone of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. At the same time, the “1992 Consensus” was reached through negotiations authorized by the relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, and the Mainland Affairs Council of the Taiwan authorities is one of the bodies authorized to reach the “Consensus.” Since the DPP came to power, the Mainland Affairs Council has flip-flopped, saying one thing yesterday and another today, and has been working hard to distort and slander the “1992 Consensus” on behalf of the DPP authorities, calling it a “unilaterally set political framework.” I do not know whether they are blushing or feeling guilty.\nThe facts prove that upholding the “1992 Consensus” allows cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, while denying the “1992 Consensus” plunges cross-Strait relations into tension and turmoil. From 2008 to 2016, both sides of the Strait built mutual trust on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” jointly opened a new chapter in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. In the more than five years since the DPP authorities took office, they have distorted and denied the “1992 Consensus” and engaged in all kinds of separatist activities, seriously running counter to the mainstream aspirations of the Taiwan people and seriously harming their interests and well-being. We advise the DPP authorities to change their ways and stop using political rhetoric to deceive the people on the island. Only by genuinely starting from the well-being of the Taiwan people, acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” and improving cross-Strait relations through concrete actions will they be on the right path.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220413_12426341.htm"],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报海外版记者","KMT Chairman Eric Chu recently appointed Huang Chieh-cheng as the party's “representative in the United States.” Huang said in an interview that he will propose a so-called “new narrative” based on maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","Adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" are the common political foundation for our interaction with the Chinese Kuomintang, and are the key to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is rooted in the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus\" and their large-scale collusion with external forces to carry out \"independence-seeking\" provocations, inciting cross-Strait opposition and confrontation and disrupting cross-Strait relations. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and affairs across the Strait are internal family matters of compatriots on both sides. We believe that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have full wisdom and ability to resolve their own affairs well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: the Taiwan defense authorities recently issued a so-called “whole-of-society defense handbook” that promotes and hypes “wartime evacuation,” causing anxiety among the people on the island. Will this action escalate cross-Strait tensions and civilian antagonism? Second question: U.S. House Speaker Pelosi was originally scheduled to visit Taiwan on the 10th but postponed the trip after being…","First question. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are very clear that \"Taiwan independence\" means the loss of peace and the coming of disaster. For their own selfish interests, the DPP authorities stubbornly carry out provocative activities seeking \"independence,\" and they do not hesitate to tie the Taiwan people to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot, which will only push the Taiwan people into an abyss of disaster. Especially recently, they have not been content to remain idle and have exploited the situation in Ukraine to jump around. On the one hand, they follow Western anti-China forces in loudly hyping the so-called \"military threat\" from the mainland, continuously stirring up cross-Strait confrontation and intensifying cross-Strait tensions. On the other hand, this move is not for the interests of the Russian and Ukrainian peoples, but for their own political self-interest, attempting to take the opportunity to \"internationalize\" the Taiwan question. These schemes are plain to all. We call on compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, to open their eyes and not become sacrificial pawns of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. Only when compatriots on both sides of the Strait work together to contain \"Taiwan independence\" can we truly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and truly safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question. Regarding this matter, we have already stated our solemn position. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, fulfill the solemn commitments the US made to China on the Taiwan question, stop playing the \"Taiwan card,\" and stop \"using Taiwan to contain China.\" We will firmly strike back against acts that seriously undermine China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. What Speaker Pelosi should do is immediately cancel, not postpone, the relevant visit. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop colluding with external forces and provoking \"Taiwan independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Wu Chao-hsieh said in an interview with foreign media that the current situation in Hong Kong runs counter to the publicized “one country, two systems,” and that the greatest consensus on the island of Taiwan is not to accept “authoritarian rule.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's response?","This person consistently distorts facts and confuses right and wrong. In fact, under the policy of “one country, two systems,” Hong Kong has moved from chaos to order and from order to prosperity, and continues to maintain a good situation of stable development. The success of the practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong is something the DPP authorities do not want to see. Driven by their nature of seeking “independence,” they constantly interfere in Hong Kong affairs and smear and vilify the practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong.\nIt must be emphasized that the cross-Strait issue is not a dispute over systems, nor is it a matter of “democracy and freedom” versus “authoritarian rule.” It is a matter of division and anti-division. Since the DPP authorities came to power, they have acted recklessly. What “democracy and freedom” do they have? Their so-called “democracy and freedom” means allowing only “Taiwan independence” to set fires, and not allowing those who hold different opinions to light lamps.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","A DPP people’s representative recently proposed draft amendments to the “Cross-Strait People’s Relations Act,” demanding that “retired generals who accept interviews with mainland media will have their pensions revoked if their remarks impair ‘Taiwan’s dignity’ or affect ‘Taiwan’s security.’” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","What a striking irony that someone is punished for speech, in such stark contrast to the “democracy and freedom” they proclaim! As the saying goes, “Officials may set fires, but common people may not even light a lamp.” This is the “democracy and freedom” manipulated by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","First question: The epidemic in Shanghai is severe. Recently, some Taiwan compatriots have reported that the lockdown has affected their daily lives; for example, a Taiwan entertainer mentioned eating only one meal a day. Does the TAO know about the impact of the epidemic on Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai, and what assistance will it provide to help resolve their difficulties? Second question: In response to the…","On the first question, regarding the epidemic prevention and control situation for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Shanghai, we gave a brief introduction at our last press conference. As we understand it, first, on the enterprise side, Taiwan-funded enterprises in Shanghai are generally stable in their production and operations at present. For some Taiwan enterprises that have temporarily encountered problems such as logistics disruptions, the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office specifically coordinated with relevant departments to issue enterprise certificates, passes and other documents to help Taiwan enterprises minimize the impact of the epidemic as much as possible. The Shanghai Municipal Government issued a number of policy measures to fight the epidemic and help enterprises develop, and the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office actively coordinated with relevant parties to ensure these policies and measures are fully implemented among Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises. Second, regarding the impact on the daily lives of Taiwan compatriots as individuals caused by epidemic prevention and control, the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office actively assisted in resolving urgent and difficult matters, including coordinating donations and distribution of supplies. As for the Taiwanese entertainer you mentioned, the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office called him specifically to ask about his daily needs. He said that his residents' committee had organized group purchases, that he was able to buy the items he needed, and that he had also received the emergency supply vegetables distributed uniformly by the city. His basic living needs are not a problem.\nI want to stress that epidemic prevention and control involves the health and life safety of everyone, and we believe that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will fully understand and cooperate with local epidemic prevention measures. As we understand it, many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises in Shanghai have eagerly donated supplies to jointly fight the epidemic. Localities will coordinate epidemic prevention and control work with local economic and social development, and will continue to provide good services to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.\nOn the second question, we have repeatedly made clear that we have full legal grounds to take punitive measures. Anyone who endangers the national sovereignty, security or development interests will not escape the sanctions of national law. Let's wait and see.\nOn the third question, the DPP authorities, out of political calculation, demanded that certain airlines change their names and logos, which is itself a farce. Facts have proven that putting political manipulation above economic livelihood does not work, and that using \"Taiwan independence\" ideology to carry out so-called \"renaming\" activities hurts Taiwan enterprises and the public the most.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","We note that following the recent new round of U.S. arms sales to Taiwan, U.S. Senator Hawley proposed the so-called “Taiwan Arms Export Act” to accelerate the transport and sale of key weapons to Taiwan. What comments does the spokesperson have?","We have repeatedly reiterated that we firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to China's Taiwan region. We urge the U.S. side to genuinely abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” and to stop all arms sales to Taiwan. U.S. arms sales to Taiwan are no different from strapping a bomb onto every Taiwan compatriot, while the DPP authorities are using the hard-earned money of the people to walk onto bombs, which will only push the Taiwan people toward disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","According to statistics from relevant Taiwan authorities, in the first quarter Taiwan’s trade surplus with the mainland was US$27.63 billion. Although since the DPP authorities took office they have vigorously promoted the so-called “New Southbound Policy,” attempting to weaken cross-strait economic and trade ties, cross-strait economic and trade relations have not declined but have increased. What is the…","This set of data once again proves that Taiwan's economic development and the well-being of the people of Taiwan cannot do without cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. The DPP authorities' attempt to “decouple and break supply chains” is merely wishful thinking, and will only harm the interests of the people of Taiwan.\nTaiwan","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中国时报记者","First question: Lee Ming-che is about to be released from prison after completing his sentence. Could you explain Lee Ming-che's current status in serving his sentence and the specific date of his release? Has the mainland side arranged for Lee Ming-che's family members to come to the mainland to visit him, and are there any relevant arrangements to assist his return to Taiwan? Second question: It is reported…","First question: The Lee Ming-che case was given a first-instance verdict in November 2017. The legal documents of the criminal judgment were duly served on the defendant and his defense counsel in accordance with the law, and Lee did not file an appeal. Since Lee Ming-che began serving his sentence, the prison authorities have strictly protected his health, communications and other rights in accordance with laws and regulations, and his physical condition has been stable. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic in 2020, in accordance with epidemic prevention and control needs, and in light of actual working conditions, the prison authorities have suspended all in-person visits by relatives of prisoners during the epidemic. According to the effective criminal judgment, Lee Ming-che will soon complete his five-year fixed-term sentence, and he will be released in accordance with the law. The relevant parties will arrange for Lee Ming-che to return to Taiwan in the near future.\nSecond question: Since its establishment in 2001, the Phoenix Television Taiwan Station has played an important role in helping global Chinese better understand Taiwan and in promoting mutual understanding and harmonious kinship between Taiwan and compatriots on the mainland and in Hong Kong and Macau. The DPP authorities' move is yet another evil act of suppressing cross-Strait exchanges, and it will be put on record. The DPP authorities should stop harming the legitimate rights and interests of media from the mainland, Hong Kong and Macau, and stop high-handedly suppressing the normal news reporting activities of mainland, Hong Kong and Macau media institutions and journalists stationed in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","According to reports, the DPP authorities have forced elementary and secondary schools on the island to add so-called “local language courses” as compulsory subjects starting from August of this year. The “local languages” available for selection include Minnan, Hakka, the Eastern Min language spoken by locals in Matsu, and 49 others in total. A Taiwanese teacher said that the DPP’s so-called “local language…","This move by the DPP authorities actually harms Taiwan and harms Taiwan’s younger generation, depriving them of development opportunities. Where does this so-called “Taiwanese language” come from? It all came from Minnan and Hakka, and it is part of the Chinese language and part of Chinese culture. The DPP authorities deliberately divided the Minnan and Hakka dialects, the languages of indigenous peoples, and Mandarin used by Taiwan residents into “native” and “foreign,” harboring their scheming intent of “de-Sinicization.” Attempting to use language as a tool to change the Chinese cultural identity and Chinese national identity deeply rooted in Taiwan society is bound to fail. From their enthusiasm for watching mainland dramas and using mainland apps, one can see that they are a bunch of hypocrites and pseudo-moralists who say one thing and mean another.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that a conflict occurred on the 9th when the Dajia Jenn Lann Temple Mazu patrol procession passed through Changhua in Taiwan's Taichung. The DPP authorities threatened to investigate whether any so-called “red forces” were involved in this conflict. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities are talking complete nonsense. Mazu is a faith shared by believers on both sides of the Strait. The Mazu circumambulation of Taiwan held by the Dajia Zhenlan Temple in Taichung has its own origins, and parties, groups, and people from all walks of life on the island have taken part in it. On what grounds is the right to participate being stripped from people who favor unification? This fully exposes the DPP authorities' political manipulation with its essential nature of scheming for “independence,” and its vicious habit of deliberately suppressing pro-unification figures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-13","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","In a recent interview, Wu Zhaoxie said that an important principle of Taiwan-US relations is that Taiwan needs to show some consideration for the United States: when the US is busy, Taiwan should not cause trouble or give it too many surprises. He has been criticized by public opinion on the island as a pitiful “watchdog” of the Americans. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Your question reminds me of a line of Tang poetry: “Having finished my makeup, I softly ask my husband, ‘Is the depth of my eyebrow-painting in fashion?’” Wu Chao-hsieh's remarks give themselves away, and vividly reveal the slavish, servile face of the DPP authorities before external forces: bowing and scraping, depending on others' breath, and wagging their tails to beg for pity.\nThank you all for coming. The press conference is concluded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220413_12426310.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-14","Zhao Lijian","Macau Monthly","It is reported that Democrat Senator Bob Menendez, Chairman of the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee, and Republican Senator Lindsey Graham are leading a delegation to Taiwan on April 14 and will meet with Tsai Ing-wen. Do you have any comment?","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region. Members of the US Congress should act in consistence with the US government’s one-China policy. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official exchanges with Taiwan and avoid going further down the dangerous path. The Chinese side will continue to take strong measures to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347263.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220414_10668000.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-15","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Republican US Senator Lindsey Graham said today in his meeting with Taiwan’s Tsai Ing-wen that the US will start to make China pay “a greater price for what they are doing all over the world”, including what he described as never-ending cyber attacks on the Taiwanese people and its economy. What is Chinese response to these remarks?","I stated China’s solemn position on US lawmakers’ visit to Taiwan yesterday. China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region. Members of the US Congress should act in consistence with the US government’s one-China policy. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official exchanges with Taiwan and avoid making irresponsible remarks. The Chinese side will continue to take strong measures to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. I believe you have all noticed the statement released by the PLA Eastern Theater Command. The relevant moves by the Chinese army are a countermeasure to the US negative actions recently, including the lawmakers’ visit to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347264.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220415_10668513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-15","Zhao Lijian","TASS","First question. Alexander Sergeev, President of the Russian Academy of Sciences, said the other day the Chinese Academy of Sciences put their cooperation with their Russian counterpart “on hold”. Can you confirm this? How do you comment on the people-to-people exchanges between China and Russia on these areas? My second question is about Taiwan. US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said yesterday that “if…","On your first question, to our knowledge, China and Russia are continuing cooperation and exchange activities in science and technology as scheduled. Guided by the vision of everlasting friendship and win-win cooperation, the two sides will advance relevant cooperation in a practical manner.\nCooperation in science and technology, as an important part of China-Russia practical cooperation, has been gaining momentum in recent years. The China-Russia Year of Scientific and Technological Innovation was successfully held from 2020 to 2021, during which over 1,000 innovative cooperation and exchange activities were held, delivering fruitful results. This has opened new ground for future cooperation and testified to the immense potential and broad prospects of bilateral scientific and technological cooperation.\nOn your second question, there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The current situation across the Taiwan Strait faces a new round of tension. The root cause is that the Taiwan authorities have repeatedly tried to seek “Taiwan independence” by soliciting US support, while some in the US intend to contain China with the Taiwan question. The US and Taiwan have colluded with each other, and certain individual deliberately draws parallel between Taiwan and Ukraine despite they are two fundamentally different issues. Their aim is to mislead the public and profit from that. It is such move of playing with fire that would change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Taiwan question is a legacy of the Chinese civil war. China must and will be reunified. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. That being said, we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures in response to the interference of foreign forces and the secessionist activities of a handful of “Taiwan independence” separatists.\nThe so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” unilaterally concocted by the US side runs counter to the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués and basic norms governing international relations. China has been firmly opposed to it since the very beginning. The US has no right to put its domestic law above international law, still less use it as a pretext to meddle in China’s internal affairs. On the Taiwan question, the US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, not the so-called “Taiwan Relations Act”.\nThe US should abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, cut off official interactions and military ties with Taiwan, stop arms sales to Taiwan and take concrete actions to fulfill its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”.\nAs for the visit to Taiwan by the US Senate delegation, I answered this question earlier. This is obviously in violation of the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347264.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220415_10668513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-15","Zhao Lijian","The Paper","It is reported that former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe recently published an op-ed on an American newspaper, in which he mentioned Ukraine and Taiwan in the same breath and said the time has come for the US to make clear that it will defend Taiwan. Does China have any comment?","Certain Japanese politician repeatedly makes wild talks on the Taiwan question and irresponsible remarks about China’s internal affairs, in a vicious attempt to instigate confrontation between major countries. China firmly rejects this.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. The Taiwan question and the Ukraine issue are different in nature and are not comparable at all. During its colonial rule over Taiwan for half a century, Japan committed innumerable crimes, over which it bears grave historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. The Japanese politician should speak and act with extra prudence on the Taiwan question and avoid sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347264.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220415_10668513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-04-15","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q) [per digest]","","According to the official WeChat message of “Ministry of National Defense Release,” on the afternoon of March 31, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, at which Senior Colonel Wu Qian, Director of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and Ministry of National Defense spokesperson, announced: On March 31, Liu Zhenli, Commander of the Army of the People’s Liberation Army of China, held a video call with Hong Mannai, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Royal Cambodian Army. The two sides exchanged in-depth views on bilateral cooperation and signed the “Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the Army of the People’s Liberation Army of China and the Army of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.”\nWu Qian said China and Cambodia are close neighbors and iron-clad friends. In recent years, practical cooperation between the two militaries in areas such as strategic communication, joint training and exercises, academic exchanges, and personnel training has continued to deepen. The Chinese side is willing to work with the Cambodian side to earnestly implement the important consensus reached by the two countries’ leaders, promote deeper development of China-Cambodia bilateral and military relations, and continue to build a China-Cambodia community with a shared future of strategic significance.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/04-15/9729835.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-04-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 15 dispatch. In response to the visit to the Taiwan region on the 14th by US Federal Senator Graham and others, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, responding to a question on the 15th, said: For some time, the US government and Congress have repeatedly engaged in provocations on the Taiwan question, increasingly playing the “Taiwan card,” attempting to “contain China through Taiwan” and obstruct the process of China’s complete reunification and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We urge the US government to fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” with concrete actions, rather than saying one thing and doing another.\nHe pointed out that Graham and others’ visit to Taiwan, and the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces fawning over and flattering them, cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and cannot stop the process of the complete reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220415_12427004.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 18 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 18th in response to questions: Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people, and its future shall be decided jointly by all Chinese people. The Chinese people have the overwhelming courage and ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No matter how the DPP authorities beg, collude with…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that the relevant remarks by the DPP authorities distort facts, reverse right and wrong, and deliberately exploit the situation in Ukraine to mislead Taiwan residents and international public opinion. First, they distort the facts that Taiwan is part of China and that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, peddling the fallacy of the “two-state theory.” Second, they cover up the fact that the DPP authorities’ provocations for independence have brought the current Taiwan Strait situation into tension and turmoil, shifting blame and deceiving the world. Third, they follow external anti-China forces and serve as strategic pawns for “using Taiwan to contain China” and containing the development of the Chinese nation. They misjudge the situation, are blinded by self-interest, and are obsessed with relying on external forces to seek independence and provoke, emboldening themselves. At the same time, this exposes their lack of confidence. They keep administering themselves “bewitching soup” and taking “reassurance pills,” revealing that they are bold in appearance but timid inside.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220418_12427986.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-22","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","A question about Ukraine. US Deputy Secretary of State Wendy Sherman said China wasn’t helping the situation in Ukraine by doing things like amplifying Russian disinformation campaigns. And she also said that she hoped Beijing learned the right lessons, also her words, “from Russia’s war, including that it can’t separate the US from its allies.” Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","I noted the remarks by the US side. China believes that these remarks, especially the accusations against China, are entirely clichés and an old trick to smear and slander China. China has repeatedly made clear its position on the so-called “competition-cooperation-confrontation” trichotomy. This is in essence a cover-up for US containment and suppression of China, which boils down to the US’ problematic perception of China. We urge the US to view China and China-US relations in an objective light, earnestly implement its leadership’s statements that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; that it does not aim to change China’s system; that it does not seek to target China by revitalizing its alliances; that it does not support “Taiwan independence”; and that it has no intention to seek a conflict with China. The US should work with China to find the right way to get along with each other featuring mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation under the new circumstances.\nFacts have proven that China is a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of international order. China always attaches great importance to the protection of intellectual property right. Our efforts and achievements in this regard are there for all to see. The Chinese government follows a people-centered approach in human rights protection, earnestly implements the constitutional principle of respecting and protecting human rights and has made historic achievements. China’s position on the Ukraine issue is aboveboard, just, objective and beyond reproach. On the contrary, it is the US side that has a poor track record on relevant issues. We advise the US side to look in the mirror and properly manage its own affairs before pointing fingers at others.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347269.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220422_10672257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-24","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 23rd, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” organizations on the island held a so-called seminar hyping the illegal and invalid “San Francisco Peace Treaty,” agitating the “theory of undetermined status of Taiwan,” and spreading the claim that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other.” What is your comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 24. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 24th in response to a question that the DPP authorities, out of their political nature and partisan self-interest, have arbitrarily reversed black and white and confused right and wrong, hyping up illegal and invalid historical waste paper and deliberately peddling the “two-state theory,” attempting to challenge the internationally recognized One China principle. All of this will ultimately be futile and can never stop the historical trend of cross-Strait reunification.\nHe said the so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty” was an illegal and invalid document issued after World War II by the United States, which gathered some countries to conclude a separate peace with Japan while excluding the People's Republic of China and the Soviet Union. The “treaty” violated the “Declaration by United Nations” signed in 1942 by 26 countries including China, the United States, Britain, and the Soviet Union; violated the Charter of the United Nations and basic principles of international law; and any disposition involving Chinese territory and sovereign rights as a non-signatory, including the question of sovereignty over Taiwan, is also illegal and invalid. The Chinese government solemnly declared from the very beginning that because the People's Republic of China did not participate in the preparation, drafting, or signing of the “San Francisco Peace Treaty,” the Chinese government considers it illegal and invalid and will never recognize it. The Soviet Union, Poland, Czechoslovakia, North Korea, Mongolia, Vietnam, and other countries also refused to recognize the effect of the “treaty.”\nMa Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unequivocally confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220424_12429970.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-25","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Recently, during the third meeting of the US-EU Dialogue on China, the US and the EU expressed “concern” about issues relating to Taiwan, Xinjiang and China’s “disinformation program”, and said they will continue to maintain the centrality of the UN Charter. Do you have any comment?","China firmly rejects the US and the EU’s groundless interference in China’s internal affairs and unwarranted denigration and smearing against China. We have lodged solemn representation with the two sides and made clear our stern position.\nThe US purports to maintain the centrality of the UN Charter, but it is clear to anyone that the US is doing quite the opposite. When the UN Security Council refused to authorize the US’ use of force in the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, Iraq, Syria and other places, the US and NATO brushed the UN aside and waged wars on sovereign states in wanton interference.\nThe US claims to respect human rights, but the wars of aggression launched by the US and its allies in countries including Afghanistan and Iraq killed over 300,000 civilians and made over 26 million people refugees. Yet, no one is held accountable for war crimes and crimes against humanity. The US even announced sanctions on the International Criminal Court who would investigate the war crimes of the US military.\nThe US asserts opposition to economic coercion, but it is also the US that invented “coercive diplomacy” and excels at coercing countries whether they are big or small, faraway or nearby, friend or foe. The embargo and sanctions imposed on Cuba have lasted half a century and the sanctions slapped on Iran have been there for 40 years. When it comes to stabbing its allies such as the EU and Japan in the back, the US has never hesitated, as we have seen repeatedly.\nFacts have proven that the US is the biggest spreader of disinformation, culprit of coercive diplomacy and saboteur of world peace and stability. From the US-EU dialogue to the AUKUS trilateral security partnership, the Quad and the Five Eyes Alliance, the US is using democracy, human rights, rules and order as a pretext to cover up its shady activities of creating division, stoking confrontation and reaping benefits at the expense of others. As a result, not only small and weak countries are hurt, US allies including Europe are also paying a heavy price for the US’ selfish acts. It is hoped that the EU can see the truth and stop holding the candle to the devil.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347270.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220425_10673513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-27","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Yesterday, a US guided-missile destroyer made a transit through the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment?","You may have read the statement on this made by the spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command. We hope the US can abide by the one-China principle and stop such dangerous provocations in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347272.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220427_10674571.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-04-27","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","According to reports, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said at a congressional hearing on April 26 that the administration is determined to make sure that Taiwan has all necessary means to defend itself against any potential aggression and that it is focused on strengthening Taiwan’s asymmetric capabilities. What is your comment on this?","I have noted those remarks of the US side. We deplore and reject Secretary Blinken’s statement. Since China and the US established diplomatic ties in 1979, US administrations, including the current one, have all clearly stated that they would adhere to the one-China policy. The China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations and the August 17 Communiqué clearly noted that the United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and it acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China. In the Shanghai Communiqué, the U.S. side also declared that “The United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” The US admits that Taiwan is part of China, but keeps talking about the mainland’s potential “aggression” of Taiwan. Isn’t this self-contradictory since a country can not “invade” part of its own territory?\nThe US leadership has stated on multiple occasions that the US does not support “Taiwan independence”. However, the US side has not stopped selling arms to and having official contact with Taiwan, which have sent wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We have this stern warning for the US side: The historical trend of China’s reunification cannot be held back, and the one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The US side shall not underestimate the strong resolve, determination and capability of the 1.4 billion Chinese people in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Reneging on the commitment will push Taiwan to dangerous waters and bring unbearable cost to the US itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347272.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220427_10674571.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on April 27, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Today's press conference will be hosted by me. I am willing to take questions; please raise your hands.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the epidemic situation in Shanghai, Suzhou, Kunshan and other places, and its impact on Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises there, have drawn attention. Shanghai recently released a list of key enterprises resuming work, which includes Taiwan-funded enterprises. Please introduce how relevant localities are helping Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises with relief and with…","Party committees and governments in Shanghai, Suzhou, Kunshan and other places, including Taiwan Affairs Offices at all levels, have, under the premise of meeting epidemic prevention and control requirements, taken a series of measures to actively assist Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises in overcoming difficulties and stabilizing production.\nFirst, strengthen the promotion and explanation of policies to help enterprises overcome difficulties, and promote the implementation of relevant policies and measures. Taiwan Affairs Offices in Shanghai, Suzhou and other places promptly released policy measures to help enterprises develop through online platforms and other means, making them easy to access, and carried out promotion, explanation and implementation work. They also promoted in their localities the experience of some Taiwan-invested enterprises in achieving efficient and precise epidemic prevention, to help more enterprises obtain 'epidemic-free enterprise' status and provide assistance for resuming work and production.\nSecond, promptly understand and respond to the demands of Taiwan businesspeople and help resolve their practical difficulties. Taiwan Affairs Offices and Taiwan associations in Shanghai, Suzhou, Kunshan and other places improved their working mechanisms in a timely manner, established special working groups to help Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots overcome difficulties, and organized special work meetings and online exchanges to understand the demands of enterprises, discuss work plans and provide targeted services. The Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office actively coordinated with local relevant departments to issue enterprise certificates, passes and other documents to address the urgent needs of Taiwan-invested enterprises. It actively helped Taiwan-invested enterprises connect with financial institutions, set up dedicated service windows to address their financing needs, and promoted faster approval processes. The Kunshan Taiwan Affairs Office coordinated and helped Taiwan-invested enterprises resolve freight transport and other problems.\nIt is understood that recently, Shanghai released its first batch of 'white lists' for resuming work and production, which includes 11 Taiwan-invested enterprises that have arranged closed-loop production or are gradually resuming production. Kunshan City released its first batch of 60 'epidemic-free enterprises,' including 22 Taiwan-invested enterprises, which may apply to resume work and production on the premise of closed-loop management and other conditions.\nIt should be pointed out that the broad masses of Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises have actively done epidemic prevention and control work and eagerly participated in the fight against the epidemic. Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises in Shanghai have enthusiastically donated money and materials. As of April 20, the total donations of materials and cash amounted to 10.977 million yuan. Many Taiwan compatriots have actively joined epidemic prevention work by volunteering as community volunteers and in other ways. Everyone has united to fight the epidemic and overcome difficulties together.\nNext, we will continue to work with relevant departments and localities to actively assist Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises in overcoming the impact of the epidemic, restore normal production and business operations as soon as possible, and work together for better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431208.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","We note that since the policy measures on expanding the opening to Taiwan residents for applying to set up individual businesses were introduced on March 16, various localities have publicized them in various ways, and Taiwan compatriots have responded actively. Please introduce the current state of policy implementation.","Since the policy implementation more than a month ago allowing Taiwan residents to apply to set up individual industrial and commercial households in the pilot areas for innovative development of trade in services, Taiwan Affairs Offices and market regulation departments in various localities have actively conducted policy publicity and ensured policy implementation, providing services and convenience for Taiwan compatriots applying to set up individual industrial and commercial households.\nTo cite just a few examples: Wuhan, Hubei Province, formulated a “one-day, one-visit” registration service guide for Taiwan residents applying to set up individual industrial and commercial households, optimizing procedures and shortening processing time limits. It held the 2022 “Entrepreneurship in Wuhan · Taiwan Youth Talk” policy promotion meeting in a format combining online connection with live streaming, with more than 3,000 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth from many places on both sides of the Strait participating online. The Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office carried out policy promotion and consultation services through new media platforms and a hotline for Taiwan compatriots. The head of the Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office led visits to Taiwan compatriots, proactively understood their needs, explained in detail specific questions of concern to Taiwan compatriots, and worked with relevant departments to connect policy implementation. Liaoning, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Fujian, Shandong, Hubei, Hainan, Sichuan, Guizhou and other places also promptly answered questions of concern to Taiwan youth and compatriots through various means, including registration conditions for individual industrial and commercial households, applicable industries, tax amounts, and how to apply quickly.\nBroad numbers of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth have responded actively, regarding the “new policy” as exciting good news that provides new opportunities and new space for Taiwan compatriots to work, start businesses, and live and settle on the mainland. They have each made corresponding development plans and put them into action by applying to local competent authorities to set up individual industrial and commercial households.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431207.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Media reported that Taiwan's defense authorities recently proposed “four no's” regarding U.S. arms sales to Taiwan for the first time, including not wanting retired U.S. military warships, among others. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities’ scheme to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and “seek independence by force” has not changed. They lavishly squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwan public on buying weapons, create cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and do not hesitate to tie Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and make them cannon fodder. This completely harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan residents and pushes Taiwan step by step toward the disaster of war.\nThe future of Taiwan, the security guarantee for Taiwan compatriots, and their interests and well-being lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize where their true interests lie, reject the coercion and deception of the DPP authorities, and join us in jointly promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and building a peaceful home where compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live in tranquility.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431204.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that the Taiwan military has obtained “US consent” to extend the runway at the Taiping Island base in the South China Sea so that all existing fighter jets can take off and land on Taiping Island. What is your comment?","The Nansha Islands, including Itu Aba (Taiping Island), are inherent Chinese territory, and China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands and their adjacent waters. The name of Taiping Island originates from the Chinese Navy frigate 'Taiping,' which, after World War II, was responsible for taking over the South China Sea islands and reefs occupied by Japan. Naming by ship, remembering history, and declaring sovereignty. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and should jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintain the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Any act attempting to collude with external forces and sell out the interests of the Chinese nation is playing with fire, and will surely be spurned by the people on both sides and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431203.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Some Taiwan media reported that, due to the impact of the epidemic in Shanghai, Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai have been unable to return to Taiwan. The Mainland Affairs Council said that for Taiwan residents who cannot obtain a nucleic acid test report before boarding, it will help them complete the test after arriving in Taiwan. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","There is no such situation as the one claimed by Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, in which a nucleic acid test report could not be obtained before boarding in Shanghai and would only be processed after arrival in Taiwan.\nAccording to epidemic prevention and control requirements, all persons boarding cross-Strait two-way flights must present a negative nucleic acid test certificate before boarding. To curb the spread of the epidemic and protect the lives and health of the people, starting from 00:00 on April 2, persons leaving Shanghai must hold a negative nucleic acid test certificate issued within 48 hours and must also provide a negative antigen test certificate issued within 24 hours. Without the relevant negative test certificates, one cannot leave Shanghai. Since April, relevant authorities in Shanghai have provided testing, transportation and other services to more than 30 Taiwan compatriots arriving in and leaving Shanghai, addressing their urgent needs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe reiterated China’s solemn position on the Taiwan issue in a phone call with US Defense Secretary Austin. The DPP authorities claimed that the mainland “deliberately highlights discussion of the Taiwan Strait issue, misleading and distorting the US side’s stated position.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe, at the invitation, held a phone call on the 20th with U.S. Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin, and emphasized that if the Taiwan question is not handled properly, it will have a subversive impact on China-U.S. relations. Austin said that the United States adheres to the one-China policy. The content of the call concerning Taiwan is very clear.\nThe DPP authorities deliberately distorted the facts, which precisely exposes their nature of provoking “independence” while being strong in appearance but weak within. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and the DPP authorities' attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Deputy Secretary of State Sherman recently linked the Taiwan question with the Ukraine issue, claiming that she “opposes any actions that undermine the status quo.” What is your comment?","First, it must be pointed out that the Taiwan question and the Ukraine question are fundamentally different. The most fundamental difference is that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, the Taiwan question is entirely China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated.\nAt present, what threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities' provocative acts aimed at seeking “independence.” They undermine the status quo that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and seek to separate Taiwan from China. The US side, proceeding from its own geopolitical interests, not only turns a blind eye to this, but also constantly distorts facts and plays the “Taiwan card” to pursue “using Taiwan to contain China.” We advise relevant US government officials to first clarify the basic facts that the Taiwan question involves China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, honor the political commitments made to China, stop hollowing out and emptying the one-China principle, stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” acts, stop plotting the “using Taiwan to contain China” scheme, stop any words and deeds that interfere in China's internal affairs, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the overall situation of China-US relations. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence” and collude with external forces to split the country is wishful thinking, and it will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431202.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","It is reported that Xie Changting recently claimed at a forum in Tokyo that the so-called “first island chain,” including Taiwan, being attacked would be equivalent to “a shared threat to the US and Japan,” and that if Taiwan were lost it would mean “the failure of the democratic camp.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","This person’s remarks echo those of Japanese far-right politicians, exposing the DPP authorities’ political nature of attempting to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and their face of betraying the interests of the Chinese nation. Taiwan is China’s treasured island, not a so-called “island chain” that anyone else presumptuously wants to use to “contain China through Taiwan.” The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and tolerates no external interference. The future of Taiwan, the security guarantee for Taiwan compatriots, and their interests and well-being lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. Groveling and begging for pity everywhere cannot bring peace and stability to the Taiwan Strait. Attempting to introduce external forces to carry out provocations to seek “independence” is no different from Shi Jingtang and Wang Jingwei! The Chinese people are not afraid of ghosts and do not believe in evil; we have an overwhelming resolve and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431201.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","The pro-green island media outlet CTS recently broadcast a news flash in the subtitles of its TV programming, stating that “New Taipei City has been attacked by PLA missiles, a warship exploded at Taipei Port, and facilities and vessels were damaged,” among other things, which caused panic on the island. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","This “flash news” and the panic it has caused on the island fully demonstrate that the DPP authorities' provocative pursuit of “independence” is the greatest threat to Taiwan's security, causing enormous psychological shadows for Taiwan residents. Recently, the DPP authorities have constantly exploited the Russia-Ukraine situation to hype up the mainland's “military threat,” clamor for war, and kidnap Taiwan compatriots into “anti-China and resisting China,” placing Taiwan residents in a state of being unable to be free from fear. This farcical incident was entirely self-inflicted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431200.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have successively published fallacies about the “Treaty of San Francisco,” claiming that the so-called “international legal status of Taiwan has long been established,” and spreading remarks that the two sides are “not subordinate to each other.” What comments do you have on this?","We have previously issued a stern written refutation of this fallacy. Here, I am willing to reiterate our position once again and expose the absurdity, illegality and invalidity of this fallacy.\nThe so-called “Treaty of San Francisco” is an illegal and invalid document issued after World War II, when the US gathered some countries to conclude a separate peace with Japan, excluding the People's Republic of China and the Soviet Union. This “treaty” violates the 1942 Declaration by United Nations, signed by 26 countries including China, the US, Britain and the Soviet Union, and violates the UN Charter and the basic principles of international law. Any disposition involving China's territory and sovereign rights, including the question of sovereignty over Taiwan, made without China as a participant is also illegal and invalid. The Chinese government solemnly declared from the outset that, because the PRC did not take part in preparing, drafting or signing the Treaty of San Francisco, the Chinese government considers it illegal and invalid and will never recognize it. The Soviet Union, Poland, Czechoslovakia, North Korea, Mongolia, Vietnam and other countries also refused to recognize the effect of the “treaty.”\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unmistakably confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided. The DPP authorities, out of their political nature and narrow party interests, have arbitrarily turned black into white and confused right and wrong, hyping up illegal and invalid historical waste paper. They have distorted the special state of political confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, a legacy of the prolonged civil war, into a “two-state theory” and “one side, one country,” attempting to challenge the one-China principle recognized by the international community. The DPP authorities' schemes and perverse conduct will ultimately come to nothing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220427_12431206.htm"],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","First question: The DPP authorities opened up to foreign relatives visiting Taiwan on April 12, but the Mainland Affairs Council says that people from the mainland are still not admitted. Does the spokesperson think this is playing a “double standard”? Second question: The Mainland Affairs Council plans to relax employment and residence rules for Hong Kong residents in Taiwan in May, which coincides with the…","In answer to the first question, I completely agree with the view you cited in your question. The DPP authorities' related actions are a blatant political \"double standard.\" Since the epidemic began, the DPP authorities have unreasonably suspended travel by mainland personnel to Taiwan, made things difficult for the normal rotation of mainland institutions' staff in Taiwan, and coldly obstructed family reunions of cross-Strait marriages. They have fabricated all kinds of excuses to take discriminatory measures against mainland enterprises, mainland students, mainland spouses, and their family members. This exposes their political nature of \"opposing China and seeking independence,\" and can only further arouse the hatred of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities use a so-called high-sounding reason, saying that \"the epidemic on the mainland is spreading in multiple locations,\" and do not allow mainland compatriots to visit relatives in Taiwan. I want to say: do not always use the mainland as a scapegoat. We must ask: Is the number of infections abroad smaller than on the mainland? Is the death toll lower than on the mainland? Is the severity of the epidemic lighter than on the mainland? Or, is the purpose of the DPP authorities' measure not epidemic prevention, but rather to guard against a specific group of people? Liars should beware of their tongues being struck by lightning.\nIn answer to the second question, the DPP authorities' continued manipulation of Hong Kong affairs is entirely driven by political self-interest in destabilizing Hong Kong and seeking \"independence,\" but in essence it is feeding on the \"human blood buns\" of Hong Kong's people, a point everyone can see clearly. I solemnly warn the DPP authorities that all the crimes of destabilizing Hong Kong will be punished according to law.\nIn answer to the third question, \"Taiwan independence\" is the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and it is a delusion that can never be realized. As long as it is \"Taiwan independence,\" no matter how it is packaged, its essence is to split the country and harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for all forms of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. If someone on the island insists on provocative acts seeking \"independence\" and even tries to take external forces as a backer, they will ultimately only end up with bloodied heads.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","The mainland has adopted “dynamic zero-COVID” epidemic prevention measures. Taiwan has recently chosen a model of “coexisting with the virus,” which has caused confirmed cases to soar. How does the spokesperson view Taiwan’s current epidemic prevention approach?","I briefly answered this question at the last press conference. For more than two years since the epidemic broke out, we have consistently upheld the concept of putting the people first and life first, placing the safety and health of the people in the first place, and implemented the overall anti-epidemic policy of “dynamic zero-COVID.” We have effectively and resolutely stopped the COVID-19 epidemic. We are among the countries with the lowest COVID-19 infection and mortality rates in the world, and we were the first to turn economic growth from negative to positive, with economic growth of 8.1% last year. In the first quarter of this year, gross domestic product was 270,178 hundred million yuan, up 4.8% year on year. This fully shows that the mainland’s overall anti-epidemic policy can coordinate epidemic prevention and control with economic and social development, can achieve the goals of precise prevention and control and “dynamic zero-COVID,” and can most effectively protect the lives and health of the people.\nAs for the epidemic prevention and control policies on the island, all sectors on the island have their own views. We have also noted that the COVID-19 epidemic has recently spread on the island, with confirmed cases increasing rapidly. The day before yesterday, there were more than 5,000 new local cases in a single day, and yesterday there were more than 6,000. Some commentary on the island suggests that by the end of the year, about 4 million to 7 million people in Taiwan may be confirmed to have the disease. Under the DPP authorities’ so-called “new anti-epidemic model,” and referring to the current global average COVID-19 mortality rate, everyone can calculate how many lives will be lost. This is something that compatriots on both sides of the Strait do not want to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","The two sides of the Strait have adopted different approaches to epidemic prevention measures. Some Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, in order to avoid the mainland's lockdown measures, want to return to Taiwan or postpone to a later date on the mainland. May I ask whether the spokesperson believes that epidemic response is yet another cross-Strait “system contest”?","First, I must emphasize that cross-Strait relations are, in essence, a struggle between unification and “Taiwan independence” separatism, not a so-called “contest of systems.” Second, regarding cross-Strait epidemic prevention, I have just introduced the mainland's relevant practices. I recall that before this, many compatriots from Taiwan went to the mainland, feeling that the mainland was the safest. As for the individual phenomena you mentioned, please do not be impatient; we can observe for a while longer.\nIn answering the previous question, I already said that under the so-called “new epidemic prevention model” currently in Taiwan, and given the probability that by year-end the island may see 4 to 7 million infections, one can calculate how many compatriots in Taiwan will lose their lives. If among those who die are your family members, especially the elderly and children, then what mind and confidence do you have to talk to the mainland about the so-called “contest of systems” in epidemic prevention?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, a relevant person in charge of the Taiwan Army and some representatives of public opinion formed a delegation to inspect the defense of Kinmen, calling Kinmen and Matsu the “cross-Strait front line” that must “safeguard Taiwan’s security.” The Kinmen County Magistrate, however, said that the people of Kinmen long for peace, do not want war across the Strait, and that both sides should resolve their…","That slap from the Kinmen County authorities was well deserved. Everyone understands that “Taiwan independence” means war. The “Taiwan independence” separatist forces disregard the lives, property, and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. They engage in “Taiwan independence” provocations for their own private interests, and even rely on external forces and even military force. This is completely a case of greed clouding judgment. Kinmen was once the so-called frontline of “anti-communism and protecting Taiwan.” The people of Kinmen suffered greatly from the military confrontation across the Strait in those years. They finally prospered and developed into the frontier of cross-Strait exchanges. Some people try to make them go back the old way, enduring bitterness twice over and suffering twice. The people of Kinmen certainly will not agree. Not only the people of Kinmen, but also the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will certainly not be coerced and deceived by the DPP authorities. The desire for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and opposition to “Taiwan independence” has always been the mainstream wish of people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海媒体记者","Liu Genghong, a Taiwan entertainer living in Shanghai, has recently sparked a fitness craze among mainland and Taiwan audiences through new media. How does the spokesperson view this phenomenon? Green media have taken the opportunity to frantically smear and suppress Taiwan entertainers. How do you view this?","Under the current epidemic prevention and control situation, the internet and new media have provided convenient avenues and new platforms for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to understand each other and carry out exchanges. The phenomenon you mentioned is the best illustration of this. Exchanges are based on the kinship of blood ties and also accord with the common interests of compatriots on both sides, and more and more Taiwan compatriots are gaining tangible benefits through cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. You may also have noticed that whatever compatriots on both sides cheer in unison is necessarily what the DPP authorities “curse,” what the “Taiwan independence” forces “smear,” and what the green media “sneer at.” This is not surprising. On the contrary, this can only show that compatriots on both sides drawing closer together is the will of the people and the trend of the times, which no one can stop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: A US congressional delegation recently visited Taiwan. Recently, due to the situation in Ukraine, US arms sales to Taiwan have increased. What is the TAO's response? Second question: The US missile destroyer “Sampson” transited the Taiwan Strait on the 26th, and the US claimed that this demonstrates its commitment to a free and open Indo-Pacific. What is the TAO's response?","I have already answered the first question. We firmly oppose the US selling arms to Taiwan and oppose the development of any form of military ties between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. The US move violates the solemn commitments made to China on the Taiwan question. We urge the US side to act in line with its words and return to the position of the One-China principle.\nOn the second question, the Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests. We firmly oppose, and will never allow, any external interference. The US side should abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness, and stop doing things that undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and escalate tensions in the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","You just mentioned that the epidemic on the island has been quite serious recently and that by year-end as many as 4 million people may be infected. Does this mean that the entry epidemic prevention measures from Taiwan to the mainland will not be relaxed this year?","Since the outbreak of the epidemic, the two sides across the Strait have adopted markedly different measures toward exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides, reflecting different positions. The DPP authorities have tried every means to restrict and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges: they suspended mainland residents’ travel to Taiwan, suspended the normal rotation of mainland institutions and personnel stationed in Taiwan, even prevented cross-Strait marriages and family reunions, did not allow “Xiaoming” to visit relatives, and created various inconveniences for mainland students studying in Taiwan. These are well known to everyone. The mainland has always adhered to the position of promoting cross-Strait exchanges. We have repeatedly stressed that exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides must not stop, be cut off, or be reduced under any difficult circumstances. The epidemic prevention measures we have taken are not aimed at restricting Taiwan compatriots from coming, but are necessary for epidemic prevention and control, to protect the life safety and health of Taiwan compatriots and others. As for the situation you mentioned, we will abide by the relevant “prevent imported cases” epidemic prevention regulations and will not impose any special restrictions targeting Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视记者","According to Taiwanese media, on the 26th Taiwan's defense authorities announced the timing and content of this year's “Han Kuang 38” exercise. It is based on the so-called possible mainland “invasion of Taiwan” operations, and refers to lessons from the Russia-Ukraine war to discuss various combat readiness issues. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The nature of the DPP authorities is to seek “independence,” and seeking “independence” inevitably entails provocation. One manifestation of provocation is attempting to use external forces to embolden themselves. But facts have proven that external forces are utterly unreliable. Another manifestation is fantasizing about “seeking independence through force.” This is entirely a move blinded by self-interest. If they carry on like this, it can only be a dead end. It would not matter much if the DPP authorities were seeking their own dead end, but they even want to take the 23 million people of Taiwan hostage and make them cannon fodder. We also appeal to Taiwan compatriots not to be deceived. Only by returning to the correct track of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can compatriots on both sides share peace, share prosperity, share development, and together live a good life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Taiwan media reported that the cumulative value of U.S. arms sales to Taiwan that have not yet been delivered has reached 14.2 billion U.S. dollars. Some netizens on the island bluntly accused the DPP authorities of being “played by the Americans.” What comments does the spokesperson have?","We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China and firmly oppose any form of military contact between Taiwan and the United States. This position is clear and consistent. In order to carry out \"independence-seeking\" provocations, the DPP authorities, borrowing from Peter to pay Paul, keep using money that could have been used to improve people's livelihoods to purchase weapons from the United States. They are squandering the hard-earned money of the people of Taiwan, which has already placed a heavy burden on the people of Taiwan. Being a \"pawn\" of external forces not only makes them the fall guys, forcing the people of Taiwan to become \"ATMs,\" but will also lead them step by step into an abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have floated the idea of using so-called “law amendments” to counter the so-called “mainland false information attacks.” Some commentators have pointed out that the DPP authorities are disguising themselves as victims and crying wolf first. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities are thieves crying “stop thief.” For a long time, they have controlled green media, raised online troops, and wantonly fabricated and spread all kinds of rumors, attacking dissenters on the island and creating confrontation across the Strait. They are the habitual offenders of “cognitive warfare.” Isn't the recent farcical incident at Huashi the best illustration of this? We advise the DPP authorities that trying to fool the people and mislead public opinion by fabricating false information is underestimating the intelligence of Taiwan's people. In the end, they will only end up hitting their own feet with the rock they lifted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中国新闻社记者","The DPP Authorities Say They Will Sign a Contract with Shanghai Fosun to Purchase Vaccines. Please Introduce the Relevant Situation.","In view of the recent spread of COVID-19 across the island and the rapid increase in confirmed cases, we are highly concerned about and attach great importance to the life and health safety of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and we are pleased to see vaccines produced or represented by mainland enterprises serve Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Recently, Taiwan reports indicated that Li Meng-chu, a township government adviser of Fangliao Township, Pingtung County, who was arrested in 2019, was released from prison last year after completing his sentence, but still cannot return to Taiwan because he is serving the supplementary penalty of deprivation of political rights. Please introduce his current situation.","We learned from relevant departments that Li Mengju’s criminal facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive and sufficient. Relevant departments have strictly handled the case in accordance with the law. He has now completed his prison term and is serving his supplementary penalty. During the handling of the case, including during his imprisonment, his various lawful rights have been protected in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-27","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The “Implementation Rules” of the “Several Measures of Xiamen City for Building the First Home and First Stop for Taiwan Compatriots and Taiwan-funded Enterprises to Land,” jointly formulated by 26 functional departments of Xiamen City, have been officially issued. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Xiamen has actively and thoroughly implemented equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots, promoted cross-Strait integrated development, emphasized promoting integration through connectivity, through benefits and through emotional bonds, and increased policy innovation. It has introduced eight targeted, high-value, broadly beneficial specific measures in areas including helping Taiwan compatriots and enterprises obtain financing, directly recognizing the professional qualifications of some Taiwan personnel, facilitating employment and entrepreneurship for Taiwan youth, replicating the pilot policies for Taiwan under the free trade zone, and supporting Xiamen-Taiwan agricultural cooperation. The “Implementation Rules” specify the concrete provisions, application conditions, required materials, and procedures for each measure, as well as the contact persons and phone numbers of the responsible units, to make it convenient for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to look up information and handle related business, providing support for their development in Xiamen. We support this.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all for coming. Thank you for your hard work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202204/t20220427_12431191.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-28","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","According to some media in Taiwan, Republican US Senator Lindsey Graham openly asked the Taiwan authorities to purchase 24 Boeing 787 airplanes manufactured in his constituency the state of South Carolina, with a total value of $8 billion, during his visit to Taiwan this month. He wrote to press the Taiwan authorities to make a decision after he returned to the US. What is your comment?","As for putting the bite on the Taiwan authorities, Mr. Graham is not alone. According to reports, US politicians like former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo pocketed $150,000 during his visit to Taiwan for a couple of days.\nWhy would the US politicians bother to travel afar if not for the huge profits? While professing values like defending democracy, those visiting Taiwan are thinking about nothing but self-interests. And the DPP authorities are fooling no one but themselves when boasting about the US’ support. But it is our Taiwan compatriots that suffer, as they are tied to the chariot of “Taiwan independence” traveling toward the abyss with their hard-earned money spent on pleasing others.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347273.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220428_10675132.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media reports, during the Spring Festival holiday, the “Taiwan military” carried out various training and combat readiness tasks; the “Army” conducted combat readiness patrols and various readiness drills; “Navy” ships closely monitored the maritime situation; and the “Air Force” dispatched contingency forces to take off in response to PLA aircraft continuously entering Taiwan's “southwest air…","The DPP authorities, relying on foreign backing to boost their own standing, engage in provocations seeking 'independence' in various forms and continually escalate cross-strait confrontation. This is the source of the threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and also a grave scourge seriously endangering the well-being of Taiwan's compatriots. The PLA's organization of multi-service forces and multiple batches of ships and aircraft to carry out routine patrols and alert patrols in the sea and airspace around Taiwan is precisely to resolutely strike down the arrogance and 'independence'-seeking conduct of 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces. Guarding the frontier and defending the land is our unshirkable duty. As long as 'Taiwan independence' provocations continue, the PLA's actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity cannot and will not stop for a moment.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，针对网民陈某在微博平台发表关于卫国戍边烈士的不当评论一事，近期杭州检方已提起民事公益诉讼，依法追究陈某的法律责任。请问发言人有何评论？","According to the website of the Ministry of National Defense, Tan Kefei, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, said on the 10th: We demand that certain senior Australian military and political officials stop exaggerating and hyping the “China threat,” handle Taiwan-related issues prudently, do more things conducive to enhancing mutual trust between the two sides, and not go down a dead-end road.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, Australian Defence Minister Dutton recently said in an interview, regarding whether Australia would arm Taiwan, that Australia will do everything it can to deter the Chinese side's “aggression” in the region. Earlier, in response to the so-called “laser illumination” incident involving Chinese warships that Australia alleged, Dutton said Australia must expose China's bullying. The Australian Department of Defence has also repeatedly issued statements defending the close reconnaissance flights of Australian military aircraft. What is the spokesperson's comment?\n“We have noted the relevant reports. The remarks by Australia's defense leaders grossly interfere in China's internal affairs and arbitrarily distort China's actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. This fully exposes their Cold War mentality and ideological bias, and seriously damages China-Australia and China-Australia military-to-military relations. China expresses strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this,” Tan Kefei said.\nTan Kefei stressed that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs and brooks no foreign interference; it is not for Australia to make irresponsible remarks. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving complete national reunification is a historical trend that no person or force can stop. Those who stir up trouble on the Taiwan question will only fall harder the higher they jump. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is on high alert and resolutely will thwart any interference by external forces and any “Taiwan independence” secessionist schemes.\nRegarding the encounter between Chinese and Australian ships and aircraft, Tan Kefei pointed out that the Chinese side has already explained the full course and merits of the incident. I must emphasize again that throughout the entire encounter with Australian military aircraft, Chinese naval vessels consistently maintained safe, standard, and professional operations, in line with relevant international law and international practice. “As can be seen from the video shot by our ships, the Australian aircraft conducted close-range reconnaissance of our vessel, which was malicious in intent and highly unprofessional in operation, threatening the safety of both sides' ships, aircraft, and personnel. Instead of reflecting on itself, Australia has repeatedly spread false information and made untrue accusations against China, constantly promoting confrontation and opposition, and has become a ‘troublemaker’ for regional peace and stability.”\n“For some time, Australian senior military and political officials, for their own political gain, have frequently made negative remarks about China, promoting so-called ‘Chinese military expansion,’ clamoring for opposing China in the South China Sea, and advocating alliances to confront China. We note that many far-sighted people in Australia have also criticized these erroneous remarks,” Tan Kefei said. We demand that certain senior Australian military and political officials stop exaggerating and hyping the “China threat,” handle Taiwan-related issues prudently, do more things conducive to enhancing mutual trust between the two sides, and not go down a dead-end road.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, since the Ukraine crisis broke out, the DPP authorities have attempted to link the Ukraine issue with the Taiwan issue, hyping up the possibility that the mainland might exploit the Ukraine situation to strengthen so-called “military pressure” on Taiwan, inciting “resisting China and defending Taiwan,” and stepping up combat preparation training to enhance their armaments and defense…","First of all, it must be pointed out that Taiwan is not Ukraine, and the Taiwan question is fundamentally different from the Ukraine question. The root of the matter is that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. The two sides must and will be reunified. This is the trend of history, and it is something no person or force can stop.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have escalated their collusion with external forces and their provocations to seek independence, attempting to change the fact that the two sides belong to one China. This is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. Recently, they have taken advantage of the situation in Ukraine to “ride the hype” and “gain attention,” deliberately exaggerating the so-called “threat” from the mainland, raising the pitch of cross-Strait confrontation and of seeking independence, and even recklessly advocating war. This conduct, which attempts to “rely on foreigners to seek independence” and “seek independence through force,” is harming Taiwan and will only push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster.\nChina's defense of its own sovereignty and territorial integrity is entirely justified, and no external interference is permitted. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and certain external forces: “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” has no way out, and “containing China with Taiwan” is doomed to fail. The People's Liberation Army of China stands ready and will take all necessary measures to resolutely strike back at any provocation that endangers China's core interests and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据了解，国务委员兼国防部长魏凤和近期出席中越边境国防友好交流活动，并访问哈萨克斯坦、土库曼斯坦、伊朗和阿曼，能否进一步介绍有关情况？","Wu Qian, Senior Colonel, Director of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters' questions on the situation in Ukraine on the 24th. He said that the United States has repeatedly spread rumors targeting China on the Ukraine issue recently, which is malicious and despicable. We hope all parties will continue to commit to dialogue, consultation and negotiation, strive to ease the situation as soon as possible, and continue to play a constructive role in seeking peace and realizing peace.\nThe so-called claims that China had prior knowledge, “acquiesced” or “condoned” are completely false information\nWu Qian said that on the issue of “Russia preparing to attack Ukraine,” “the so-called claims that China had prior knowledge, ‘acquiesced’ or ‘condoned’ are completely false information, intended to shirk responsibility and smear China. China expresses strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this.”\nWu Qian said that the Ukraine issue has complex historical background and realities, and its evolution to date is the result of multiple factors acting together. But who is the biggest instigator of the crisis? Everyone knows. China has always adopted an objective and impartial attitude, made independent judgments based on the rights and wrongs of the matter itself, and stated its position. China believes that to resolve the current crisis, it is necessary to adhere to the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and respect and safeguard the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all countries; it is necessary to adhere to the principle of indivisible security and take into account the legitimate security concerns of the parties concerned; it is necessary to adhere to resolving disputes peacefully through dialogue and negotiation; and it is necessary to focus on long-term stability in the region and build a balanced, effective and sustainable European security mechanism.\nHe stressed that China's approach stands in sharp contrast to the approach of the United States, which creates crises, shifts crises onto others, and profits from crises. We hope all parties will continue to commit to dialogue, consultation and negotiation, strive to ease the situation as soon as possible, and continue to play a constructive role in seeking peace and realizing peace.\nOn biological military activities, the United States owes the world a clear and definite account\nA reporter asked: According to reports, during the current Russia-Ukraine conflict, Russia discovered that the United States has multiple biological laboratories in Ukraine. The Russian Ministry of Defense recently released related documents stating that the US has conducted biological weapons research in laboratories in Ukraine. US Deputy Secretary of State Nuland acknowledged that Ukraine has “biological research facilities,” and that the United States is working with Ukraine to prevent related “research materials” from falling into Russian hands. A former official of Ukraine's security service disclosed that biological laboratories operated by the US within Ukraine are developing biological weapons. What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian said that we have noted these reports. Biological weapons are weapons of mass destruction, and biological military activities are major issues concerning international peace and security and the security interests of all countries. Any information or clues about biological military activities should arouse high concern in the international community.\nWu Qian said that as the country that engages in the most biological military activities in the world, the United States has 336 biological laboratories in 30 countries around the world, and it has also carried out a large number of biological military activities at Fort Detrick within its own territory. According to publicly disclosed information, dozens of biological laboratories in Ukraine were operated under orders from the US Department of Defense. The above-mentioned activities by the US are seriously lacking in transparency and pose security risks that cannot be ignored. Previously, rare epidemics broke out in the locations of several overseas US military biological laboratories, triggering protests and doubts from multiple countries. This is also an important reason why the US biological laboratories in Ukraine have aroused widespread concern in the international community.\n“We cannot help but ask, what exactly is the real intention behind these US projects? Why has the US not made the detailed information of these projects public? What is the relationship between US overseas biological laboratories and the US Department of Defense? If the US laboratories in Ukraine are only engaged in scientific research and disease surveillance, why is the US Department of Defense deeply involved? Why has the US, for 20 years, been the sole country opposing the establishment of a multilateral verification mechanism under the Biological Weapons Convention?” Wu Qian said that on these five questions, the United States owes the world a clear and definite account. These major matters of principle cannot be brushed aside with a flippant “false information.”\nHe stressed that China was once a victim of biological weapons, and has consistently advocated the comprehensive prohibition and complete destruction of all weapons of mass destruction, including biological weapons, and firmly opposes any country developing, possessing or using biological weapons under any circumstances. China has consistently held that the purposes and objectives of the Biological Weapons Convention must be strictly observed. We urge the US to respond seriously to the concerns of the international community in an open, transparent and responsible manner, faithfully fulfill its obligations under the Convention, provide a comprehensive explanation of its biological military activities both inside and outside its borders, and accept multilateral verification.\nThe so-called “China providing military assistance to Russia” is completely false information\nWhen answering questions regarding the so-called “China providing military assistance to Russia,” Wu Qian said that this is completely false information, and both China and Russia have already made clarifications. The United States has repeatedly spread rumors targeting China on the Ukraine issue recently, which is malicious and despicable, and has also allowed the international community to see the true face of the US, which is accustomed to fabricating rumors and stirring up trouble.\n“It must be emphasized that China's position on the Ukraine issue is consistent and clear,” Wu Qian said. “We have all along played a constructive role in promoting peace and facilitating negotiations. What is most urgent is for all parties to exercise restraint, to cool down and ease tensions rather than add fuel to the fire, and to promote a diplomatic resolution rather than further escalating the situation. We demand that the US immediately stop this despicable behavior of fabricating rumors, slandering and making trouble, deeply reflect on the inglorious role it has played in the development and evolution of the Ukraine crisis, and genuinely do some concrete work to promote the easing of the situation in Ukraine.”\nThose who clamor to give China a “lesson” must first learn to accept a lesson themselves\nIn response to remarks by the Commander of US Pacific Air Forces that he “hopes China will draw three lessons from the Russia-Ukraine conflict,” Wu Qian responded: Those who clamor to give China a “lesson” must first learn to accept a lesson themselves. When it comes to provoking other countries and launching wars, if the United States is second in the world, then no country dares to be first.\nWu Qian stressed that it is well known that China has always pursued a defensive national defense policy and an active defense military strategy, upholds the diplomatic philosophy of amity, sincerity, mutual benefit and inclusiveness toward neighboring countries, adheres to good-neighborliness and partnership with neighbors, and is committed to building a community of shared future with its neighbors. Since the founding of New China, we have never invaded other countries, never engaged in proxy wars, never sought spheres of influence, and never participated in military bloc confrontation. For a long time, the Chinese military has carried out in-depth, pragmatic cooperation with the militaries of neighboring countries in all fields, actively provided public security goods, and properly handled hot-button and sensitive issues, playing an important role in maintaining regional peace and stability.\nWu Qian said that on issues of peace and security, the United States itself has a long record of misdeeds. Since its founding, it has frequently initiated wars overseas, exported turmoil globally, and caused serious humanitarian disasters. It has become the greatest source of chaos in the world and has no qualifications whatsoever to play the role of “schoolmaster” to other countries.\n“Colluding with foreign powers for independence has no way out; using Taiwan to contain China is doomed to fail”\nA reporter asked questions regarding the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' attempt to link the Ukraine issue with the Taiwan issue, and some Western politicians' exploitation of the opportunity to hype up the so-called mainland “military threat” against Taiwan.\nWu Qian said that, first of all, it must be pointed out that Taiwan is not Ukraine, and the Taiwan question is fundamentally different from the Ukraine question. The crux is that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. Cross-Strait reunification must and will happen; it is the trend of history, and no person or force can stop it.\nHe pointed out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have increasingly colluded with external forces, engaged in provocations to seek “independence,” and sought to change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. This is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. Recently, they have been “riding the wave” of the Ukraine situation and “seeking attention” by deliberately hyping the so-called mainland “threat,” raising the level of Cross-Strait confrontation and their rhetoric for “independence,” and even arrogantly advocating war. This behavior, which seeks to “rely on foreign powers for independence” and “use force for independence,” harms Taiwan and will only push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster.\nWu Qian stressed that it is entirely justified for China to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it brooks no foreign interference. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and certain external forces that “colluding with foreign powers for independence” has no way out, and “using Taiwan to contain China” is doomed to fail. The Chinese People's Liberation Army stands ready and will take all necessary measures to resolutely counter any provocations that endanger China's core interests or undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","美国防部前不久发布“航行自由行动”2021财政年度报告，声称自2020年10月至2021年9月，美方挑战了26个国家及地区的37项“过度海洋主张”，其中与中国相关的最多，涉及中国大陆5次、台湾地区1次。请问发言人有何评论？","According to a message from the WeChat public account “MND Release” (国防部发布), on the afternoon of March 31, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, at which Wu Qian, spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense, answered reporters' questions and emphasized that the big hat of “militarization of the South China Sea” cannot be placed on China; the United States is its rightful owner. Facts prove that the United States is the biggest driver of militarization of the South China Sea, and the greatest disruptor of regional peace and stability and troublemaker.\nAt the meeting, a reporter asked: According to reports, the US Department of Defense recently submitted a national defense strategy report to Congress that views China as the most important strategic competitor of the United States. Admiral Aquilino, commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, recently flew on a P-8A patrol aircraft to the South China Sea and said that China's construction on relevant reefs in the South China Sea undermines regional stability and poses a threat to nearby countries. Washington's primary goal in disputed areas is to prevent war through deterrence, and if deterrence fails, the second mission is to be prepared to fight and win. Also, according to reports, the US Navy expeditionary base ship “Miguel Keith” recently entered the South China Sea for activities. What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian responded: On March 18, President Xi Jinping had a video call with US President Biden at the latter's request. The US side again pledged: it does not seek a “new Cold War” with China, does not seek to change China's system, does not seek to oppose China by strengthening alliances, does not support “Taiwan independence,” and has no intention of clashing with China. China believes that the relevant US actions are seriously inconsistent with President Biden's statement of “four noes and one no intention,” and we firmly oppose them.\nHe stressed that China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands and their adjacent waters. China's deployment of necessary territorial defense facilities is both the legitimate right of a sovereign state and a necessary measure in response to US provocations, and fully conforms to relevant international law and international practice. The big hat of “militarization of the South China Sea” cannot be placed on China; the United States is its rightful owner. What General Aquilino saw during his flight should not have been only the scattered reefs, but probably also many US military ships and aircraft flaunting their power. They came all the way to the South China Sea to stir up trouble, and what they intend to do is clear to the regional countries. Facts prove that the United States is the biggest driver of militarization of the South China Sea, and the greatest disruptor of regional peace and stability and troublemaker.\nWu Qian said: This year marks the 50th anniversary of the Shanghai Communiqué. China and the United States, as two major countries, benefit when they cooperate and suffer when they fight. Standing at a new historical starting point, China hopes the United States will move toward China, draw on historical experience and wisdom, and push China-US and two-militaries relations back onto a healthy and stable track as soon as possible, making greater contributions to world peace and tranquility.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","澳大利亚总理莫里森近日表示，中所签署安全合作协议令澳警醒，澳国家安全面临持续威胁。另有澳媒猜测中方可能在所租赁土地用于建设中国海军基地。请问对此有何评论？","According to a WeChat post from the \"National Defense Ministry Release\" account, on the afternoon of March 31, the Ministry of National Defense held a regular press conference. Senior Colonel Wu Qian, Director of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and its spokesperson, answering a reporter's question, said: Taiwan is China's own affair and has nothing to do with Japan. Japan should not stretch its hand too far.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida recently said that Russia's invasion of Ukraine is an act that undermines the foundations of the international order, and that such use of force to change the status quo must never be allowed to happen in East Asia. Peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are very important for Japan's security and the stability of the international community. In view of the situation in Ukraine, Japan is considering comprehensively strengthening its defense capabilities by revising its National Security Strategy. Kishida also said that the Japanese government has no intention of discussing the \"nuclear sharing\" policy of deploying and jointly operating U.S. nuclear weapons on Japanese territory, but there is no problem with political parties and even the public discussing it. What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian said: Taiwan is China's own affair and has nothing to do with Japan. Japan should not stretch its hand too far. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and is fundamentally different from the Ukraine issue.\nFor some time, certain political forces within Japan have sought various ways to create pretexts for breaking through the postwar international order and engaging in military expansion, and recently they have made dangerous statements that run counter to Japan's own “three non-nuclear principles.” Asian neighbors and the international community are highly vigilant about this. Japan, as a party to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, should earnestly fulfill its non-proliferation obligations. China has consistently opposed nuclear-weapon states deploying nuclear weapons on the territory of other countries. We urge Japan to deeply reflect on history, respect the security concerns of its Asian neighbors, and adhere to the path of peaceful development, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，美方个别官员近期高调表示将坚决履行协防台湾承诺，“像协助乌克兰一样协助台湾”，持续提升台湾自卫能力。另据台“国防部”披露，台军为应对大陆威胁，采取“训练战备结合”模式验证作战计划与战场建设，并开展“联翔操演”模拟解放军攻台。请问发言人对此有何评论？","According to the website of the Ministry of National Defense, on the afternoon of March 31, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference. Wu Qian, Director of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense, answering questions from reporters, said: Recently, some Australian politicians, for their own selfish interests, have intensively hyped issues related to China and repeatedly made erroneous remarks on bilateral relations, Taiwan-related issues, and other matters. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this. We warn Australia: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. If Australia insists on going its own way, it must be prepared to pay a painful price for interfering in China's internal affairs.\nAt the meeting, a reporter asked: Before the election, Australian Prime Minister Morrison said that Australia plans, with the assistance of the United States and the United Kingdom, to build a nuclear-powered submarine fleet and construct a nuclear submarine base on Australia's east coast; Australia will spend 38 billion Australian dollars on expanding its military. Australian media commentary said that China's military buildup is one of the main reasons for Australia's increased defense spending. Australia's assistant defense minister said that Australia must prepare for the PLA's “potential operations in Taiwan and elsewhere.” What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian said that recently some Australian politicians, for their own selfish interests, have intensively hyped issues related to China and repeatedly made erroneous remarks on bilateral relations, Taiwan-related issues, and other matters. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this.\nWu Qian pointed out that the cooperation among the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia on nuclear-powered submarines violates the purpose and principles of the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, undermines the international nuclear non-proliferation system, and disrupts regional peace and stability, and it has met with widespread opposition from the international community. Australia, disregarding the facts, has deliberately stirred up the so-called “China military threat theory” to greatly expand its armed forces and substantially increase its military budget. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this.\nWu Qian stressed that Australia's erroneous remarks on the Taiwan question are extremely dangerous. We warn Australia: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. If Australia insists on going its own way, it must be prepared to pay a painful price for interfering in China's internal affairs.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9742006.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-04-28","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest does not say whether this was a question or an a","","According to the WeChat public account “National Defense Ministry Release,” on the afternoon of March 31, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, at which Senior Colonel Wu Qian, Director of the Information Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and its spokesperson, answered reporters' questions. He said that Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the welfare of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. On the question of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, you can always trust the Chinese People's Liberation Army.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, a poll in Taiwan shows that only 35% of respondents believe the US would send troops to help defend Taiwan if conflict broke out across the Taiwan Strait, a sharp drop of 30.5% from last October. A former head of Taiwan's defense department said that if the two sides went to war, the PLA could end the fighting completely within one or two days. Also according to reports, Taiwan recently signed an arms procurement contract with the US to purchase the “Field Information Communication System” from the US. Wu Zhaoxie, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, said the US will provide Taiwan with weapons with defensive capability in accordance with the “Taiwan Relations Act,” and that further arms sales will be announced. What is your comment on this?\nWu Qian said: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and admits no foreign interference. We firmly oppose the US selling weapons to the Chinese Taiwan region, and we oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the US and Taiwan.\nTaiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the welfare of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Those “empty checks” from external forces will ultimately prove unreliable. Those who are willing to be “chess pieces” for others will in the end face the fate of being “discarded.” From Kabul to Ukraine, what others cannot obtain from foreign countries, how could Taiwan obtain? “Leaning on foreign powers to elevate oneself” has no way out, and “resisting reunification by force” is a dead end. On the question of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, you can always trust the Chinese People's Liberation Army.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/04-28/9741874.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 28: In response to a question on the 28th, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that Mr. Wu Shupei, former president of the Mutual Aid Association of Political Victims in Taiwan, passed away on April 24, 2022, after his illness could not be cured. The Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office extend deep condolences.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that Wu Shupei was a loyal patriot. He unswervingly promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, firmly opposed “Taiwan independence,” firmly opposed foreign interference in China's internal affairs, actively pursued social progress, fairness, and justice, and devoted his whole life to the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation. His patriotic sentiments and noble conduct stand in sharp contrast to those “Taiwan independence” elements who have forgotten their ancestors and their roots.\nMa Xiaoguang said that although this person is gone, his aspirations live on. The historical trend toward national reunification and national rejuvenation cannot be stopped by anyone or any force. All patriotic and reunification forces will be inscribed on the historical monument of national reunification, and all “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will certainly be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220428_12431413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-04-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On the 28th, Lai Ching-te and Yu Hsi-kun again hyped the so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty,” spread the “two-state theory,” and falsely claimed that the mainland is “invading” Taiwan. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 28 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on the 28th that recently the DPP authorities have been repeatedly hyping an illegal and invalid historical scrap of paper and spreading the “two-state theory,” attempting to confuse people and mislead public opinion, which fundamentally exposes their political nature of challenging the one-China principle and stubbornly engaging in provocations to seek “independence.”\nMa Xiaoguang said history cannot be tampered with and facts cannot be distorted, and this must be rectified. It is well known that Taiwan has been an inseparable part of Chinese territory since ancient times and has never become a separate country. In 1945, the Chinese people, together with the peoples of other countries around the world, won the great victory of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and Taiwan was subsequently restored and returned to the embrace of the motherland. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unambiguously confirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was established, replacing the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legal government of all China and the sole legal representative of China internationally, fully enjoying and exercising China's sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. In 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore all the rights of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the government representatives of the People's Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China at the United Nations. The relevant historical facts and law make very clear that Taiwan has no international legal status other than being part of China. The so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty,” which the DPP authorities cling to desperately, is merely a product concocted by a handful of Western countries during the Cold War; it arbitrarily tramples on international law and interferes in other countries' internal affairs, and is entirely illegal and invalid.\nHe pointed out that the Taiwan question is a leftover issue of China's civil war and is fundamentally different from the Ukraine issue. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter of China's internal affairs. Achieving complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people. All necessary measures taken in response to provocations and coercion by “Taiwan independence” forces are just acts to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to thwart secessionist schemes; how can they be called “aggression”?\nMa Xiaoguang said that we adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never allow Taiwan to be separated from China. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that if they continue to misjudge the situation, stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, indulge in the illusion of “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” and “seeking independence by force,” and take risks on the road of “Taiwan independence,” crossing the red line, we will certainly take resolute measures to firmly crush them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220428_12431626.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-04-29","Zhao Lijian","CNR","The Foreign Ministers’ Meeting among China and Caribbean Countries Having Diplomatic Relations with China was held today. Can you share more information?","The Foreign Ministers’ Meeting among China and Caribbean Countries Having Diplomatic Relations with China was held this morning via videoconference. The meeting was co-chaired by State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Acting Prime Minister Reginald Austrie of Dominica, and attended by all nine Caribbean countries having diplomatic relations with China. All attendees took stock of the experience over the past five decades of diplomatic relations between China and Caribbean countries, had an in-depth exchange of views on building a closer China-Caribbean countries community with a shared future, and shared their full confidence in the future of the relations between China and Caribbean countries.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi stressed at the meeting that all parities believe that over the past 50 years, especially since President Xi’s visit to the Caribbean in 2013, the comprehensive cooperative partnership between China and Caribbean countries have been deepening, with fruitful outcomes of cooperation in various areas. The two sides have set an example in mutual respect, equality, mutual benefits and common development between countries. All sides agreed to take the 50th anniversary of the diplomatic ties as an opportunity to bring China-Caribbean countries relations to new levels. State Councilor Wang Yi put forward four suggestions on building China-Caribbean countries relations at a higher level, namely jointly promoting peace and development, jointly chart a blueprint for the development of China-Caribbean countries relations, jointly deepen mutually beneficial cooperation and jointly carry on the friendship between the peoples.\nThe parties at the conference have reached six-point consensus. First, enhancing political mutual trust, rendering each other support on issues concerning core interests as always, and upholding and practicing true multilateralism. Second, jointly promoting post-COVID economic recovery and solid Belt and Road cooperation, implementing the Global Development Initiative, working to upgrade practical cooperation including on Juncao. Third, strengthening COVID-19 response and cooperation on health, improving public health governance and building a community of health between China and Caribbean countries. China will continue to provide anti-pandemic supplies and vaccines to Caribbean countries. Fourth, forging a dynamic and interactive architecture of people-to-people exchange, with more scholarship opportunities provided by the Chinese government to Caribbean countries. Fifth, responding together to the challenge of climate change. China has decided to set up a fund for disaster prevention and mitigation between China and Caribbean countries. Sixth, having closer policy communication between China and Caribbean countries.\nThe Caribbean countries attending the conference welcomed and endorsed the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative put forward by President Xi Jinping. They expressed gratitude to China for its selfless and longstanding help for Caribbean countries’ socioeconomic development, and said that China has become a reliable and important partner of Caribbean countries. The Caribbean side firmly supports the one-China principle, China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and the great cause of the reunification of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347274.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202204/t20220429_10680663.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-04-29","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Ma Ying-jeou recently wrote on Facebook that the “theory of undetermined status of Taiwan” is an “absurd argument,” and that the claims that “the Cairo Declaration has no international legal effect and the Treaty of San Francisco does not govern Taiwan's sovereignty” do not hold up. What comments do you have on this?","XINHUA News Agency, Beijing, April 29 (electronic dispatch) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the TAO, responding to a query on the 29th, pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. A series of international legal documents, such as the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, have already clearly established China's sovereignty over Taiwan. No matter how the DPP authorities distort historical facts or package “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202204/t20220429_12431900.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-05","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","During the consultations between the US and the UK on the Indo-Pacific in early March, the two countries had talks on how they can cooperate to reduce the chances of war over Taiwan and to explore conflict contingency plans for the first time. What is China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is a historical and legal fact, and a consensus of the international community. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no interference by any foreign country. The root cause of the new round of tensions across the Taiwan Strait lies in the Taiwan authorities’ attempt to solicit the US support for “Taiwan independence” and some US individuals’ intention to contain China with the Taiwan question. For some time, the US has been playing the “Taiwan card” more often and hyping up Taiwan-related issues with certain countries in an effort to make the Taiwan question an international issue. Their relevant actions endanger the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and represent a step further down a very dangerous road. The US and relevant countries should stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, abide by the one-China principle, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347275.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220505_10681886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-05","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US Secretary of State has postponed his announcement of the US’ China strategy after he contracted COVID-19. What’s the Chinese government’s comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. We wish Secretary Blinken a speedy recovery. We have no comment on a speech that has not yet been delivered.\nI want to stress that sound and steady relations between China and the US, permanent members of the UN Security Council and the world’s largest economies, serve the fundamental interests of the two countries and meet the shared expectation of the international community. History and reality show that China and the US both stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation.\nNot long ago, President Xi Jinping had a virtual meeting with President Biden. The two sides agree that China and the US should respect each other, co-exist in peace and avoid confrontation. President Biden reiterated that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; that it does not aim to change China’s system; that the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; that it does not support “Taiwan independence”; and that it has no intention to seek a conflict with China.\nThe China-US relationship is now at a critical crossroads. We hope the US side will act on President Biden’s positive remarks and abandon the obsolete Cold War mentality and zero-sum game. The US should work with China to earnestly implement the common understanding reached by the two leaders to enhance communication, manage differences and focus on cooperation, so as to bring the bilateral relations back to the track of sound and steady development at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347275.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220505_10681886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, May 5 (Xinhua) — According to Taiwan media reports, an article in the US magazine *The Diplomat* claims that the CPC's position on Taiwan is inconsistent and incoherent, and that the CPC's position during its founding period regarded the people of Taiwan as a distinct nation and once expressed support for Taiwan's struggle for “independence.” In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 5th in response to a question that the relevant report by the US magazine deliberately takes things out of context and distorts facts, attempting to mislead Taiwan's public and international opinion, and its intentions are evil.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that Taiwan is part of China, and this is an unchangeable fact. In 1895, Japanese imperialism used a war of aggression to forcibly seize Taiwan and the Penghu Islands, subjecting Taiwan compatriots to 50 years of miserable life under Japanese colonial rule. Since its founding on July 1, 1921, the Communist Party of China has persistently striven to achieve national liberation and national reunification. In the 1920s, it actively supported the struggle of Taiwan compatriots to rise up against Japanese colonial rule. After the September 18 Incident, it further put forward the view that Taiwan's destiny is closely tied to the destiny of the Chinese revolution. In 1936, having just arrived in northern Shaanxi after the Long March, it took the lead in proposing to “immediately convene a National Congress of Representatives for Resisting Japan and Saving the Nation,” to discuss and decide policies including severing diplomatic relations with Japan and declaring war on it, recovering lost territory, and publicly declaring all unequal treaties between China and Japan completely null and void. This clearly and unmistakably shows the CPC's position and stance of advocating the abrogation of the Treaty of Shimonoseki and the recovery of Taiwan. On May 15, 1937, when Mao Zedong met with American journalist Nym Wales, he said: “China's War of Resistance aims to win the final victory, and the scope of this victory is not limited to Shanhaiguan, nor to the Northeast, but also includes the liberation of Taiwan.” On June 17, 1943, the *Xinhua Daily* published an editorial titled “Taiwan, Return to the Motherland!”, which comprehensively and systematically expounded the CPC's political position on Taiwan's return to the motherland, solemnly pointed out that “Taiwan is part of China,” and stated that “only by strengthening unity and actively participating in the motherland's War of Resistance, and winning a complete victory, can the Japanese invaders be driven out of Taiwan and Taiwan return to the embrace of the motherland.” In August 1945, the Chinese people, together with the people of all countries in the world, won the great victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, Taiwan was thereupon recovered and returned to the embrace of the motherland. Subsequently, due to the continuation of the Chinese civil war and interference from external forces, the two sides of the Taiwan Strait fell into a special state of long-term political confrontation. Since 1949, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided. The CPC has always regarded resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland as an unwavering historic mission, and has promoted continuous breakthroughs in cross-Strait relations and advanced the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nZhu Fenglian said that we will unswervingly adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” scheme. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces that, in today's increasingly strong mainland, to pursue confrontation and plot separation is nothing but a fanciful delusion, and can only lead to a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220505_12433424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-06","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","We notice that Japan has been very active on the international stage lately, with many political figures visiting countries in Asia, Europe and America. On May 5, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida said during his visit to the UK that Japan is deeply concerned over unilateral attempts to change the status quo in the East China Sea and the South China Sea, rapid but obscure military building activities and…","State-to-state cooperation should contribute to regional peace, stability and prosperity. It should not target any third parties or undermine their interests. The Japanese side has kept slipping its own agenda in diplomatic activities, played up regional tensions by making an issue out of China and hyped up the so-called China threat. By doing so, Japan aims to find excuses for beefing up its military capabilities and undermine mutual trust and cooperation among regional countries. This is not conducive to regional peace and stability and will win no support. China firmly rejects relevant words and deeds of the Japanese side.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which can never be mentioned in the same breath with the Ukraine situation. Japan bears grave historical responsibilities to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question and should thus exercise greater prudence in its words and actions. It has no right to spout off on this issue. On maritime issues, China firmly defends its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. We also stand ready to properly resolve differences with countries concerned through negotiations and consultations to maintain regional peace and tranquility.\nIf the Japanese side is sincere about maintaining peace and stability in East Asia, then it should immediately stop provoking major-country confrontation, and do more things that will promote mutual trust between regional countries and peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347276.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220506_10682440.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, May 7 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a query on the 7th, said that since April, the COVID-19 epidemic in Taiwan has spread rapidly, with more than 30,000 new confirmed cases per day recently, and rapid antigen test kits urgently needed by compatriots in Taiwan are in severe shortage, which we are very concerned about. It is crucial for compatriots in Taiwan to obtain rapid antigen test kits as soon as possible for epidemic prevention, control and treatment. Relevant Taiwan enterprises and institutions need to contact relevant mainland manufacturers to negotiate procurement, and relevant mainland authorities are willing to provide assistance.\nA reporter asked: Recently the epidemic has broken out on the island, infections are rising rapidly, and rapid test kits are in severe shortage, and public opinion hopes the mainland will provide assistance. What is your consideration on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said: We are deeply concerned about the lives and health of compatriots on the island, and we hope the epidemic will end soon and life will return to normal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220507_12434086.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-09","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","We noticed that the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs released the Fact Sheet on the National Endowment for Democracy on its website over the weekend. Could you offer more on that?","On May 7, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs released the Fact Sheet on the National Endowment for Democracy on its website. The fact sheet, with about 12,000 words in six sections, lays bare the true face of the National Endowment for Democracy (NED) through hundreds of specific examples gathered from public reports.\nThe US has long used democracy as a tool and a weapon to undermine democracy in the name of democracy, to incite division and confrontation, and to meddle in other countries’ internal affairs, causing catastrophic consequences. NED, as one of the US government’s main “foot soldiers” and “white gloves”, has subverted lawful governments and cultivated pro-US puppet forces under the pretext of promoting democracy. NED was seen behind color revolutions instigated and orchestrated by the US, including the disintegration of the Soviet Union, the Rose Revolution in Georgia, the Orange Revolution in Ukraine and the Arab Spring. NED has been stirring up protests and demonstrations in Thailand, inciting the opposition parties in Nicaragua to seize power by force, funding anti-Cuba forces to manipulate public sentiment against the government, and long interfering in Venezuela’s internal affairs through various means. Hellbent on disrupting the world, NED has not brought social stability and development or contented lives and good work to other countries. On the contrary, it has caused a host of issues including withered livelihood, languishing economy and social confrontation. NED also extends its evil hand to China and invests heavily in anti-China programs every year to incite “Xinjiang independence”, “Hong Kong independence”, and “Tibet independence” activities by various means. It also colludes with “Taiwan independence” forces and attempts to incite division and disrupt stability across the Taiwan Strait, which has been met with indignation and opposition from the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.\nNED is actually the “second CIA” of the US. It is by no means an NGO that provides support for democracy abroad. Instead, it takes orders directly from the US government and manipulates NGOs through the provision of funding to conduct subversion, infiltration and sabotage to serve US strategic interests. We believe the international community will see its true face more and more clearly, and more countries will expose its heinous deeds in various forms. In today’s world, peace and development remains the theme of our times. NED's meddling in other countries’ domestic affairs is doomed to fail no matter what disguise it uses.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347277.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220509_10683545.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-09","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","Suzuki Norikazu, acting head of the LDP delegation of Japan’s House of Representatives, told the press on May 6 in Taipei that stability across the Taiwan Strait is crucial to the Asia-Pacific. Japan has a sense of crisis over the sorties of mainland’s military aircraft’s frequent entry into Taiwan’s so-called “Air Defense Identification Zone”, and hopes to strengthen practical cooperation with Taiwan. What is…","China firmly opposes official interaction in any form between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, which has nothing to do with Japan. It is totally unnecessary for certain individuals of Japan to grandstand on the matter.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347277.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220509_10683545.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-09","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Taiwan official Joseph Wu said on Monday that it would be very difficult for Taiwan to be invited the World Health Assembly (WHA) meeting this month, although he said efforts to obtain an invitation are still ongoing. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","The participation of China’s Taiwan region in activities of international organizations, including the WHO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a fundamental principle confirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. Since the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) came to power, it has placed its political agenda over the well-being of the people in the Taiwan region, obstinately adhered to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence”, and refused to admit the 1992 Consensus embodying the one-China principle. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA has ceased to exist.\nIn order to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and uphold the solemnity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China cannot agree with the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA. We advise the DPP authorities to stop exploiting the COVID-19 pandemic to engage in political manipulation. Otherwise, it will only invite humiliation to itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347277.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220509_10683545.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on May 9 that the Fifth Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum will be held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, on May 11. Hong Xiuzhu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang and chairperson of the Qingyan Peace Education Foundation of China, has been invited to attend the forum. About 450 guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, youth representatives from all sectors, and others will take part in forum-related activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220509_12434387.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 9 — The election of the sixth Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region was held smoothly. In response to the remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 9th in response to a question: The election of the sixth Chief Executive of the Hong Kong SAR fully embodies the principle of “patriots administering Hong Kong,” fully demonstrates the strong vitality of “one country, two systems,” and is another successful practice of developing Hong Kong's characteristic democracy. In the face of the historical trend of Hong Kong moving from chaos to order and from governance to prosperity, the DPP authorities' tricks of using Hong Kong as a pretext should come to an end!\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the reason the DPP authorities jumped out to point fingers and make irresponsible remarks is that the successful practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong has fully exposed their long-standing deceptive face of deceiving the island's public, and their deceptive tactic of smearing the Hong Kong SAR to seek private gain has collapsed of its own accord.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220509_12434554.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-10","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Numerous reports have noted that the US State Department’s website has recently updated its page on US-Taiwan relations, removing expressions such as “Taiwan is part of China” and “The United States does not support Taiwan independence”. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The PRC government is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a universally-recognized norm governing international relations and common consensus of the international community. History brooks no falsification, facts cannot be denied, and right and wrong should not be distorted. The US has made solemn commitments on the Taiwan question and the one-China principle in the three China-US joint communiqués. The US’ latest modification of the fact sheet is a trick to obscure and hollow out the one-China principle. Such political manipulation of the Taiwan question and the attempt to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait will hurt the US itself.\nThe US should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three joint communiqués, follow through on the political commitments on the Taiwan question it made to China, and fulfill President Biden’s statement that the US does not support “Taiwan independence” with real actions. It should stop engaging in political manipulation of Taiwan-related issues and containing China with the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347278.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220510_10684000.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on May 11, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Now let's begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Taiwanese entertainer Liu Genghong, through new media, has led a fitness craze among people on both sides of the Strait, which has made many Taiwan compatriots realize that as long as they have a special skill, they can develop their careers by coming to the mainland. We have also noted that many Taiwan youth who come to the mainland to develop not only achieve success in their studies and careers in their…","In recent days, the live-streamed home fitness exercises led by coach Liu Genghong have indeed drawn wide attention. Millions of netizens have exercised side by side to familiar music such as “Herbal Compendium” and “Dragon Fist,” gaining health and joy and feeling a wealth of positive energy. Related topics have also sparked much discussion on the island. Many Taiwan compatriots have truly felt that the mainland is a fertile land of hope, offering boundless possibilities for the growth, success and career development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth. In recent years, various localities and departments have rolled out a series of policies and measures that benefit Taiwan and its people. Many Taiwan youths have seized opportunities in a timely manner, actively integrated into life on the mainland, and continuously expanded the stage for pursuing and realizing their dreams, achieving personal value, and winning the affection and recognition of mainland compatriots. Today we present an overview.\nIn the field of internships and employment, we actively create conditions to provide positions, helping Taiwan youth use internships to promote employment and employment to spur entrepreneurship. We have granted plaques to establish 78 cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship bases and demonstration sites, and through providing employment and entrepreneurship guidance, legal consultation, and investment and financing support, help Taiwan youth take the first step in developing on the mainland. For example, the Nanjing Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Academy base designs distinctive courses and invites cross-Strait experts, scholars and well-known Taiwanese businesspeople to teach, providing guidance and training to Taiwan youth. The Shanghai (Jinshan) Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Base held the “Shanghai Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurship Competition,” providing a showcase platform for Taiwan youth. The Taiwan High-Tech Park base at Songshan Lake in Dongguan connects with resources such as the Dongguan Incubation Association to provide financing support for Taiwan youth projects that move in.\nIn the cultural field, we implement the equal-treatment measures in detail, welcoming and encouraging Taiwan youth cultural workers to come to the mainland to take part in performing arts, film and television, cultural and creative industries, and other endeavors. Many Taiwan youth have joined cultural institutions and social organizations such as the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles and its national literary and artistic associations, displaying their talents on cultural performance platforms at all levels. Each year, more than a thousand Taiwan performing artists participate in producing radio and film/television programs, and they continually deliver outstanding performances in major arts performances, popular film and television dramas, and variety shows. A large number of Taiwan youth performers have won tens of millions of fans through their professional accomplishments and excellent works. Commendably, they proactively take on social responsibility, pay attention to current affairs, are enthusiastic about public welfare, actively spread positive energy, eagerly speak out to pay tribute to heroes, take part in the struggle against the epidemic, donate money for disaster relief, and extend blessings on the centenary of the Party's founding and on the National Day of the motherland……\nIn the field of education, we continuously create convenient conditions for Taiwan youth to study and teach on the mainland. Each year, several thousand Taiwan students attend universities on the mainland, and nearly 3,000 Taiwan students at mainland universities have received scholarships. Participating in various social practice, social research, and volunteer service activities has also become an important platform for Taiwan students at universities to devote their love, showcase their talents, and understand national conditions. For example, the “Cross-Strait Spring” camp of East China Normal University went to Ludian, Yunnan, to investigate local poverty alleviation work; Taiwan students from Beijing University of Chinese Medicine participated in the “Traditional Chinese Medicine Youth Cross-Strait Bond · Healthy China Rural Tour” social practice, carrying out free clinic services and popular science outreach in rural communities, among other activities.\nWe have issued relevant policies, encouraging and supporting Taiwan teachers to enjoy all kinds of commendations and awards on an equal basis, and to apply for national and all-level plans, research projects, and fund projects under equal conditions. A group of universities such as Minnan Normal University in Fujian, Zhaoqing University in Guangdong, Baise University in Guangxi, and Hubei University of Economics have actively recruited outstanding Taiwan education talent. At present, more than 2,000 Taiwan youth scholars teach at universities across the country, teaching and educating people and conducting research; for example, Teacher Wang Mengyun of Guangxi Normal University, who received the title of National Three-Eight Red Banner Bearer and actively devotes herself to local service, and Teacher Lai Yanjun of Zhongnan University of Economics and Law, who received the Hubei Provincial May Fourth Youth Medal and enthusiastically takes part in public legal education.\nIn the field of rural revitalization, Taiwan youth bring their expertise into in-depth participation in agricultural modernization, building beautiful villages, and flourishing rural culture. In Fujian, 97 Taiwan compatriot science and technology commissioners carry out entrepreneurship and technical services in more than a hundred townships and villages, covering machinery, biotechnology, agriculture, environmental engineering, and cultural tourism. Taiwan youth Fanjiang Feng, working hand in hand with mainland youth, built the Qida Entrepreneurship Cross-Strait Mass Entrepreneurship and Innovation Base, helping more than 2,000 people obtain professional qualification certificates through offline rural industry talent training. In Guangdong, relevant parties have explored establishing a Cross-Strait Rural Integrated Development Pilot Zone and launched the Cross-Strait Rural “Cloud Lecture Hall,” providing strong policy support for pilot zone project construction and for Taiwan-invested enterprises to obtain land and financing loans, attracting Taiwan agricultural youth talent to start businesses and develop in Guangdong. In Sichuan, Taiwan youth Dr. Lin Shuren has deeply cultivated the Daliang Mountains, building a 30,000-mu high-standard olive oil industry base with annual oil output reaching 160 tons, driving more than 6,200 rural households in surrounding areas out of poverty toward a moderately prosperous life.\nIn the field of grassroots governance, Taiwan youth, through vivid practices of innovative services and refined management, are exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development at the grassroots level. After policies such as the “31 Measures” and “26 Measures” and the pilot program for Taiwan compatriots to take jobs in public institutions were announced, the areas in which Taiwan youth participate in grassroots services have continued to expand. Xiamen, Fujian, has recruited dozens of Taiwan compatriots to serve as community director assistants and community development workers, participating in grassroots community governance, and has gradually built a new service model of “advisory team + execution team + project-based operation.” Jian Minan, a young woman born in the 1990s who became a street social worker through the community worker recruitment examination, speaks fluent Shanghainese every day and has become a “good girl” in the mouths of community residents, providing thoughtful and meticulous community services to residents.\nIn the field of medicine and health, Taiwan doctors continue to write new chapters of benevolent medicine and saving the wounded and rescuing the dying in various places. Zeng Renhong, director of the Rehabilitation Department of Fuzhou No. 6 Hospital, spent a year and a half participating in Xinjiang aid work, actively relieving the suffering of local residents and gaining abundant friendship, native-place affection, and kinship. On the front lines of epidemic prevention, where conditions are the harshest and tasks the heaviest, Taiwan compatriot “white-suit” workers have always been seen busily at work. Fifteen Taiwan youth students at Nanjing University of Chinese Medicine formed a “Anti-Epidemic Vanguard Team” to carry out nucleic acid testing for residents. Teacher Cui Liyou of Shanghai University of Medicine & Health Sciences has provided continuous volunteer service for more than 40 days, recording heartwarming interactions with local residents in his “Anti-Epidemic Volunteer Diary.” Dr. Huang Xinyi of Tianjin Third Central Hospital actively volunteered to join the front line of epidemic prevention and control and was awarded the title of “National Three-Eight Red Banner Bearer for the Fight Against COVID-19.”\nBeyond this, in fields such as science and technology, sports, and public welfare services, large numbers of Taiwan youth are also working diligently and steadily, pursuing their life ideals.\nYesterday (May 10), the grand meeting celebrating the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Youth League of China was solemnly held. Over the past 100 years, the Communist Party of China, focusing on the future of the country and nation, has always cared about the growth of youth and supported youth development. Looking ahead, we are willing to create better conditions for cross-Strait youth to get to know and understand each other and to grow and succeed, build more platforms, and look forward to more Taiwan youth bravely shouldering the responsibility of this generation, joining hands with mainland youth to merge into the torrent of the times, take part in great endeavors, and become active participants and capable builders on the great journey of the new era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435173.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体平台记者","The 5th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was held today (11th) in Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province. Please introduce the basic information of the forum. Under the current circumstances, what is the significance of insisting on holding this session of the forum?","On the morning of May 11, the 5th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum opened in Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province. Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the CPPCC National Committee, sent a congratulatory letter to the forum, extending congratulations on behalf of the CPC Central Committee and General Secretary Xi Jinping, and urging young people across the Strait to keep pace with the times and share the destiny of the nation, to boldly pursue a better life, and to make greater contributions to promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and the great cause of national reunification and the great rejuvenation of the nation. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the forum by video. Yue Jianjun, Secretary of the Zhejiang Provincial Party Committee, attended in person. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China and Chairperson of the Chinese Ching Yen Peace Education Foundation, was invited to attend the forum. Guests from relevant sides across the Strait, youth representatives from all sectors, and about 450 people engaged in extensive exchanges and communication around the theme \"Working Together to Create a Better Life,\" building development consensus.\nAt present, the world is undergoing accelerated changes unseen in a century, and the situation in the Taiwan Strait has become increasingly uncertain and unstable. Cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation have been severely hindered by the pandemic and by artificial interference from the island. Since 2018, with the joint efforts of the organizers and cross-Strait youth friends who have enthusiastically participated, the Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum has overcome various difficulties and been held for five consecutive sessions. It has become an important platform for cross-Strait youth to interact, exchange, and open their hearts to each other, and has played a positive role in helping cross-Strait youth exchange ideas, enhance understanding, seek common development, and create a shared future. This fully demonstrates that the will of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer to each other cannot be suppressed by anyone, and that the momentum of peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations cannot be blocked by anyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435174.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Beijing has recently seen multiple sporadic COVID-19 outbreaks. What services and guarantees have relevant mainland authorities provided to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in Beijing?","Recently, the COVID-19 prevention and control situation in Beijing has been severe and complex. Beijing's Taiwan Affairs Office and other relevant departments have earnestly implemented the requirements for epidemic prevention and control in areas involving Taiwan, and actively provided services and support to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Beijing. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Beijing have responded to the call, understood and cooperated with epidemic prevention and control arrangements, and actively participated in epidemic prevention and control work.\nTaiwan compatriots in Beijing can learn about Beijing's epidemic prevention and control policies, raise questions for consultation, and resolve matters such as nucleic acid testing and vaccination through platforms including the Beijing Taiwan compatriot service hotline and the online consultation function on the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office's government affairs website. At the same time, Beijing has continued to do a good job in vaccinating Taiwan compatriots in Beijing. As of May 6, 2022, 8,000 Taiwan compatriots in Beijing had received COVID-19 vaccines, totaling more than 19,000 doses. We would like to remind everyone that vaccination remains the most effective method of preventing and controlling the epidemic, and also the most effective personal protective measure. As of April 30, about 193,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated, with a cumulative total of 448,000 doses. We hope that Taiwan compatriots who meet the vaccination requirements will complete their vaccinations promptly and in accordance with the procedures.\nTo minimize the impact of the epidemic, Beijing issued the “Several Measures on Further Increasing Support for Small, Medium and Micro Enterprises and Accelerating the Recovery and Development of Struggling Enterprises,” which proposes support measures of “three reductions, three subsidies and two guarantees.” The total scale of funds is about 130 billion yuan, benefiting more than 1.6 million small, medium and micro enterprises, including Taiwan-funded enterprises in Beijing. To keep the transportation of key epidemic prevention medical resources, essential living goods for residents, and important industrial production materials unobstructed, Beijing officially began using the nationally unified “Key Materials Transport Vehicle Pass.” This has ensured smooth transportation of materials for many Taiwan-funded enterprises and steady progress in enterprise production and operations as well as epidemic prevention and control work. To stimulate the enthusiasm and innovation of market entities and optimize the consumer experience, Beijing launched the “2022 Beijing Consumption Season” campaign, providing financial support to urban commercial complexes and offline retail and catering enterprises that actively participate and achieve significant results. Taiwan-funded enterprises have already signed up to participate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","First question: The US State Department website recently updated its Taiwan-related content, and in the “US-Taiwan Relations Fact Sheet” it deleted content such as “the United States does not support Taiwan independence.” What is your comment? Second question: At present, the epidemic on the island is relatively severe, with confirmed cases repeatedly reaching new highs, yet the DPP authorities continue to refuse…","First question: some people on the island have hyped the revision of Taiwan-related content on the US State Department website, attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence.” This cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. We urge the US government to stop any act that hollows out and empties the one-China principle, and to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions.\nSecond question: compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family linked by blood. Defeating the epidemic as soon as possible and restoring normal life is the common wish of compatriots on both sides. The mainland has always cared about the life, health and safety of Taiwan compatriots and is willing to do its utmost to help Taiwan compatriots through difficult times. When masks, vaccines and rapid test reagents are in short supply on the island, the mainland has shared the urgent concerns of Taiwan compatriots and promptly expressed its willingness to actively provide donations and assistance, demonstrating sincerity, goodwill and fraternal affection.\nRegarding the mainland's willingness to provide Taiwan residents with epidemic-prevention supplies and vaccines and test reagents that are urgently needed, the DPP authorities have consistently blocked and rejected them. They always place their own narrow political interests above the lives and health of the people. Their “opposing everything from the mainland” has gone to extremes, and will only further endanger the life safety of Taiwan residents and cause serious consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435164.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435171.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Recently a mainland social media platform launched a function showing users' IP location. The Weibo influencer “Di Ba Official Weibo” had its IP location displayed as “Taiwan,” which drew public attention. The DPP authorities said that they will continue to monitor such controversial information platforms, and if illegal activity is involved, cases will be filed and investigated. What comment does the…","According to information from relevant departments, the relevant website platforms have earnestly fulfilled their primary responsibility by displaying the IP address attribution information of user accounts on relevant pages. This measure serves two purposes: first, to effectively govern online rumors, false information, and cyber violence; second, to help netizens effectively discern the authenticity of online information.\nPreviously, some people on the island with ulterior motives deliberately created trouble on relevant website platforms, undermining the atmosphere of cross-strait exchanges and inciting antagonism between compatriots on both sides. This measure can help compatriots on both sides of the Strait open their eyes and more accurately identify and oppose vicious acts that sow discord in the emotional ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, the DPP authorities said that this year a group led by a deputy head of the epidemic prevention department will participate in World Health Assembly-related activities. Please ask the spokesperson: for what political calculation is the DPP authorities frequently hyping up the WHA issue?","The World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations that is open only to sovereign states, and the Taiwan region, as part of China, has no right to join.\nOur position on the participation of the Taiwan region in WHO activities is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. From 2009 to 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides of the Strait adhered to as embodying the one-China principle, the Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly for eight consecutive years under the name “Chinese Taipei” in the capacity of an observer, through cross-Strait consultations. This was a special arrangement made under the premise of adhering to the one-China principle and against the backdrop of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations at that time.\nSince the DPP authorities came to power in May 2016, they have stubbornly adhered to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, distorted and negated the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations, and caused the political basis for the Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. This situation was entirely caused by the DPP authorities. Any attempt to hype the Taiwan-related issue at the World Health Assembly, or to deceive and swindle internationally, create momentum and provoke, will be futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435163.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, some figures in Japan’s political circles have repeatedly claimed to “continue to pay close attention to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait” and “not allow the status quo to be changed by force,” and so on. What comments does the spokesperson have on these Taiwan-related remarks by Japanese politicians?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have been in a special state of long-term political confrontation due to the continuation of the civil war in the last century, China’s state sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided, and never can be divided. This is the true status quo of the Taiwan question. The current tensions in the Taiwan Strait situation are rooted in the Democratic Progressive Party authorities colluding with external forces to attempt to change the status quo in which both sides of the Strait belong to one China.\nIn 1895, Japanese imperialism used aggressive war to forcibly seize Taiwan and the Penghu Islands, and colonially ruled Taiwan for 50 years. The crimes it committed are too numerous to recount, and they brought profound disasters to Taiwan compatriots. Japan bears historical responsibility to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question, and should be all the more prudent in its words and deeds, in particular deeply reflect on history, earnestly abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, stop supporting “Taiwan independence” elements, and stop provocations and troublemaking. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ collusion with external forces, which betrays the national interests, will surely be severely punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435168.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Some public opinion on the island holds that if the mainland uses force against Taiwan, the Cairo Declaration will make it difficult for the international community to intervene. The MAC of Taiwan claims that the mainland “attempts to use force against Taiwan and constantly creates regional security risks, violating the UN Charter's principle of peace and international order,” and states, “Taiwan has never been…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. This has an indisputable historical fact and legal basis and is generally recognized by the international community. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unequivocally confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided. The relevant claims of the DPP authorities are completely a distortion of right and wrong and a confusion of the public's perception.\nIt must be pointed out that the DPP authorities openly challenge the one-China principle universally recognized by the international community, stubbornly engage in provocations seeking \"Taiwan independence,\" incite confrontation and antagonism across the Strait, are the creators of tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations, and are the destroyers of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We adhere to the basic policy of \"peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,\" and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will absolutely not allow Taiwan to split away from China. The necessary measures we take in response to the provocations and coercion of the \"Taiwan independence\" forces are a just act to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to thwart the schemes of splitting the country, and no external force is permitted to interfere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435172.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Rapid test kits are now in very short supply in Taiwan. The mainland has already said it is willing to help the island purchase rapid test kits as soon as possible, but the DPP authorities have obstructed this, saying “it would be better to take good care of the people under the lockdown measures.” How does the Taiwan Affairs Office comment on this? Second question: after returning to Taiwan, Lee Ming-che held a…","First question: We expressed our willingness to actively assist relevant Taiwan enterprises and institutions in connecting with relevant mainland production enterprises to negotiate the procurement of rapid test reagents. It depends on whether the DPP authorities are willing to think of the people’s interests and address their urgent needs.\nSecond question: In a society governed by the rule of law, anyone who violates the law will be held accountable according to law. Lee Ming-che was sentenced according to law by mainland judicial authorities for the crime of subversion of state power, which has ample factual and legal basis, and he himself has confessed. During Lee Ming-che’s imprisonment, relevant parties have protected his lawful rights and interests in accordance with the law, including the rights to meet with visitors, to communicate, and to life and health. Lee’s untrue statements are not worth commenting on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The DPP authorities have continuously spread the “theory of Taiwan’s undetermined status,” which has sparked great controversy. Hsieh Chang-ting claimed that “the United States has never recognized Taiwan as belonging to China,” that Japan in practice takes the approach of respecting the Cairo Declaration, and that “Taiwanese living in Japan have suffered great grievances because they are often classified as…","Mainland China and Taiwan belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. Hsieh Chang-ting colludes with external forces to twist black into white, harms the feelings between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and sells out the interests of the Chinese nation, which is despicable.\nTaiwan's status is very clear: it is an inseparable part of China's territory. Relevant historical and legal facts fully prove this. Any deliberate distortion of facts and hyping of the so-called “undetermined status of Taiwan” theory are bound to fail.\nIt must be pointed out that the basis on which the United States and Japan handle the Taiwan question is very clear. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and an important premise for the normalization of China-Japan diplomatic relations. In the 1978 “Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the United States and China,” the US government clearly stated, “The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China. Within this framework, the American people will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan,” and “The United States acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” In the 1972 “Joint Communiqué of the Government of the People's Republic of China and the Government of Japan,” the Japanese government clearly stated, “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China,” and “The Chinese side reiterates: Taiwan is an inseparable part of the territory of the People's Republic of China. The Japanese side fully understands and respects this stance of the Chinese side, and adheres to the stance of Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” These are solemn commitments made by the governments of the United States and Japan to the Chinese side on the Taiwan question.\nHere we advise Hsieh Chang-ting not to jump too high, and it would be better for him to show some restraint.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220511_12435170.htm"],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The epidemic on the island continues to spread, with new cases exceeding 40,000 for several consecutive days. Does the TAO know about the situation of mainland students on the island? Has the DPP authorities paid attention to their epidemic prevention and health?","Recently, the COVID-19 epidemic in Taiwan has spread rapidly, and we are highly concerned about the health and safety of mainland students studying on the island. We have learned that several mainland students have been diagnosed, and we are deeply concerned. We hope they can receive timely treatment and recover as soon as possible. Relevant parties in Taiwan should take effective measures in this regard.\nIt should be pointed out that regarding mainland students studying at universities in Taiwan, the DPP authorities have never provided them with fair treatment or guarantees of related rights and interests, and the outbreak of the epidemic on the island has made this issue even more prominent. We call on the DPP authorities to face up to and improve the protection of the rights and interests of mainland students, and to stop shirking responsibility and being perfunctory.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: After Lee Ming-che returned to Taiwan, he held a press conference on the 10th, claiming that \"I was kidnapped by the mainland side.\" \"In prison, only specific individuals could talk to me, and I was mentally abused.\" How does the spokesperson view his claim? Second question: Lee Meng-chu cannot return to Taiwan after being released from prison because he is serving an additional penalty. Although…","First question: As we have already pointed out, in a society governed by the rule of law, anyone who violates the law will be held accountable according to law. Lee Ming-che was sentenced by mainland judicial authorities in accordance with law for the crime of subversion of state power, and this has ample factual and legal basis. During the interrogation by the investigating authorities, Lee admitted his criminal facts without concealment, wrote handwritten confessions and letters of repentance 23 times, described the course of his crimes in detail, and repeatedly expressed admission of guilt and repentance. During Lee's term of imprisonment, relevant parties protected his various lawful rights and interests in accordance with law.\nSecond question: Lee Ming-che's return to Taiwan after serving his sentence was a decision made by relevant mainland departments in accordance with legal provisions and in light of the circumstances of this case. After returning to Taiwan, Lee must still strictly abide by relevant requirements.\nRegarding the enforcement of the supplementary penalty of deprivation of political rights against Taiwan residents on the mainland, relevant departments have strictly followed legal provisions and made decisions based on the circumstances of each individual case.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","At present, the two sides of the Strait adopt different epidemic prevention measures. Taiwan is basically in a state of “lying flat” (躺平), while the mainland side still adheres to “dynamic zero-COVID.” The Mainland Affairs Council is making use of this, claiming that the mainland’s strict epidemic prevention and control affects Taiwan compatriots locally, and calling on the public to think carefully about the…","The statement you mentioned from the Mainland Affairs Council is aimed at the Shanghai epidemic. This claim is pure fabrication and slander, intended to obstruct Taiwan residents from participating in cross-Strait exchanges. Here, I can briefly introduce some of the situation regarding Shanghai's efforts to respond to the epidemic and assist Taiwan compatriots.\nIn fact, since March, the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office has consistently and responsibly carried out urgent-need services for Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai in an orderly manner. First, it has continuously optimized the workflow of urgent-need services for Taiwan compatriots during the epidemic. Through the WeChat official account “Shanghai-Taiwan Connect,” it promptly released operating guides for the “Health Cloud” and the “nucleic acid code,” ensuring that Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai smoothly completed multiple rounds of nucleic acid testing and that the emergency service hotline for Taiwan compatriots remained open. From March 19 to May 9, the 24-hour comprehensive service platform of the Shanghai Taiwan Compatriot Service Center received a total of 2,103 requests for help from Taiwan compatriots. Of these, 1,907 were general consultation requests, all of which have been resolved, and 196 were urgent-need requests, of which 176 have been resolved and 20 are being handled. Second, it has focused on resolving urgent difficulties such as the daily life and medical care needs of Taiwan compatriots. As of May 9, it had resolved shortages of living supplies for 165 Taiwan compatriots and provided medical treatment and medication-procurement assistance to 52 Taiwan compatriots. It has also gone through the situation of each Taiwan student one by one and further improved the work related to Taiwan students enrolled at school and those living off campus. Third, it has provided assistance to Taiwan compatriots who needed to return to Taiwan urgently. As of May 9, the Municipal Taiwan Compatriot Service Center had received 43 requests from Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai who needed to return to Taiwan urgently; 26 have been properly handled and 17 are being handled.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding the unprecedentedly severe situation of the epidemic on the island, and not focusing their attention on the safety and lives of Taiwan residents, are still scheming to use the epidemic to engage in political manipulation of cross-Strait relations. This once again exposes their ugly face of “using the epidemic to seek independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Recently, some Taiwanese media reported that Taiwan residents encountered setbacks in developing agriculture on the mainland, such as “the mainland side terminating cooperation after obtaining the relevant technology.” How does the spokesperson view this? Could you introduce the current implementation of the “22 measures for agriculture and forestry”?","More than a year since the release and implementation of the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry,” relevant localities and departments have actively implemented them, promptly coordinating and resolving issues of concern to broad Taiwan-funded agriculture and forestry enterprises. Many Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have gained tangible benefits and well-being. Some have obtained more capital support and financing convenience; some have transferred many mu of forest land and handled forest tenure certificates; some have expanded product sales channels through various exhibition and sales events; some have received more support in research, development and innovation; and some have achieved rapid development by participating in rural revitalization. We have fully introduced the specific benefits gained by Taiwan compatriots and enterprises in various localities at the press conference.\nAdhering to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” we have actively provided equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in high-quality development of agriculture and forestry on the mainland and in rural revitalization, sharing development opportunities. This has drawn enthusiastic responses from Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. The DPP authorities, blinded by a single leaf, spout wild remarks and launch attacks and slander at every turn. They can only repeatedly show that whatever is beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, the mainland does, and they oppose it across the board. Whatever benefits and profits Taiwan compatriots gain on the mainland, they go out of their way to smear. This is the nature of the DPP authorities, who will stop at nothing to seek political gain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","Residents of Hualien and their mainland spouses, who run Facebook groups such as “Diba Central Group Army” (帝吧中央集团军) in Taiwan, were indicted by prosecutors on the grounds of “spreading epidemic rumors” and punished. Some politicians on the island have questioned whether this couple “has private financial dealings with mainland official agencies.” We note that using social networks and training online influencers…","The relevant speculation is purely a case of “if one wants to frame someone, there is never a shortage of pretexts.”\nWe have always supported and encouraged exchanges between young people across the Taiwan Strait, and have actively created conditions to promote such exchanges. With the development of converged media, young people have gradually become the main force in online cross-Strait exchanges. Through online social platforms, they share their own experiences and successful practices, express opinions, interact and communicate, and understand and help each other succeed. The “Liu Genghong phenomenon” that reporters just asked about is a concrete example. Many young Taiwanese internet celebrities have seized opportunities, stood out, found stages to showcase themselves, and won the love and recognition of netizens on both sides of the Strait. Young internet personalities who enhance mutual understanding and emotional integration between compatriots on both sides should be supported and encouraged, not intimidated and suppressed. The DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest, are using a so-called “rule of law” as a pretext for political manipulation, and ultimately what is harmed is the legitimate rights, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nThat concludes today’s press conference. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202205/t20220511_12435155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-12","Zhao Lijian","Hubei Media Group","Kurt Campbell, Coordinator for Indo-Pacific Affairs in the US National Security Council, said at the United States Institute of Peace on May 11 that issues including China will be discussed at the upcoming US-ASEAN Summit. He also said that there is a deep sense in the US that other challenges cannot distract it from the Indo-Pacific region and that the US will increase investment in and engagement with ASEAN…","I have taken note of relevant reports. On the Taiwan question, I would like to stress again that the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community and an established basic norm governing international relations. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor its political commitment to China on the Taiwan question, earnestly act on President Biden’s statement that the US does not support “Taiwan independence”, and stop exploiting Taiwan-related issues to engage in political manipulation in an attempt to contain China.\nAs to the US-ASEAN Summit, it is China’s view that the US, as a non-regional country, should play a positive and constructive role in promoting peace and development in the region. It should not undermine regional peace, stability, solidarity and cooperation, still less use cooperation as a cover to force others to pick sides, or play with fire on issues concerning China’s core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347280.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220512_10685100.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-13","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","On May 12 local time, the US co-hosted the second virtual Global COVID-19 Summit alongside a few countries. Do you have any comment? Why didn’t China participate in the meeting?","China welcomes all efforts that help members of the international community fight COVID-19 together in a science-based manner and opposes political manipulation of anti-epidemic efforts by any country. Since the US insists on inviting Taiwan to the meeting in disregard of China’s stern position and in defiance of the international community’s consensus on the one-China principle, China could not attend the second virtual Global COVID-19 Summit.\nIn the wake of COVID-19, China proposed the vision of a global community of health for all, fully leveraged its strengths, ensured stability of global anti-epidemic supply chains and actively advanced international cooperation in vaccines to contribute to the global fight against the coronavirus. Here are some numbers. By early May, China has provided 4.6 billion protective gears, 18 billion testing kits and over 430 billion facial masks to 153 countries and 15 international organizations. China was the first country that has announced to make vaccines a global public good, supported waiving intellectual property rights on COVID-19 vaccines, and conducted joint production of vaccines with developing countries. China has supplied more than 2.2 billion doses of vaccines to more than 120 countries and international organizations. China also actively participated in the WHO’s COVAX plan and Access to COVID-19 Tools (ACT) Accelerator initiative. We have donated $100 million to COVAX and joined the Vaccine Manufacturing Working Group of the ACT Accelerator initiative. At the end of last year, President Xi Jinping announced that China will donate another 600 million and 150 million doses of vaccines to Africa and ASEAN countries respectively. The relevant work is well underway. With these efforts, China is making important contributions to promoting the accessibility and affordability of vaccines in developing countries. Besides, China sent 37 medical expert teams to 34 countries, and shared anti-epidemic experience with more than 180 countries and international organizations.\nThe coronavirus raging across the globe requires joint response of all countries. China will continue to work with the rest of the international community to take concrete actions to make contributions to bridging the immunization gap, building a line of defense and eliminating the virus at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347281.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220513_10685849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-13","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","It is reported that on May 12, leaders of Japan and the EU held a summit and released a joint statement in which they expressed concerns over the situation in Diaoyu Dao, the East China Sea, the South China Sea, Taiwan, Hong Kong and human rights in Xinjiang. President Von der Leyen of the European Commission said that Russia is today the most direct threat to the world order with the war against Ukraine and its…","Japan and the EU hyped up China-related issues at the meeting to smear and denigrate China, interfere in China’s internal affairs and stoke regional confrontation. China firmly rejects this and has lodged solemn representation with parties concerned.\nDiaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China’s inherent territory since the ancient times. No matter what others say or do, the fact that Diaoyu Dao is part of China can never be changed. On maritime issues, China resolutely upholds territorial integrity and maritime rights and interests. In the meantime, China is ready to properly settle disputes through negotiations and consultations with relevant countries, and safeguard regional peace and tranquility. Issues relating to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang are all China’s internal affairs that brook no foreign interference. We urge relevant countries to focus on getting their own house in order and take their mind off China’s internal affairs.\nI want to stress that China is always a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a champion of international order. China’s development is an important opportunity for the world. In recent years, China has contributed about 30% to the world's economic growth and achieved strategic outcome in COVID-19 prevention and control, making important contribution to the global fight against the virus and maintaining the stability of global supply chains. China put forth a series of proposals including the community with a shared future for mankind, the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative, which won widespread praise and warm response across the world. The Belt and Road Initiative is delivering benefits to more than 180 countries and organizations. All these facts have debunked the “China threat” theory which now enjoys no popularity.\nAt a time when the world faces multiple challenges presented by the resurgence of COVID-19 and sluggish economic recovery, we need solidarity, cooperation and a joint response to the challenges more than ever. We hope Japan and the EU can avoid drawing ideological lines, and stop seeking bloc politics and zero-sum game. They need to respond to the international community’s common aspiration for peace, cooperation and development, practice true multilateralism, and inject more positive energy into the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347281.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220513_10685849.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 13 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 13th: Yu Hsi-kun, that infamous “Taiwan independence” element, wildly advocates “one side, one country” across the Strait, forgets his roots, betrays the Chinese nation, and deliberately seeks to sever the ties between Taiwan and Chinese culture and the Chinese nation. His “Taiwan…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, Taiwan has never been a country, and it will never be possible to split it from China. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origin, the same language and the same race, and Chinese culture is the spiritual root, belonging, and shared precious spiritual wealth of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are nourished by Chinese culture. The profound and extensive Chinese culture has long flourished in Taiwan and has been fused into the living habits, ways of thinking, values, and emotions of Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan's regional culture is rooted in Chinese culture and also enriches its content.\nShe said that facts have proven and will continue to prove that no act of “de-Sinicization” can change the identification with Chinese culture and the Chinese nation deeply rooted in Taiwanese society, sever the historical ties and blood connections between the two sides of the Strait, or change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China and both sides belong to one China. Hsieh Jih-kun, this die-hard “Taiwan independence” element, will surely be cast off by history and severely punished by the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220513_12435761.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-16","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","The G7 released a Foreign Ministers’ Communiqué on May 14, which contains various items relating to China including Hong Kong, Xinjiang, human rights, maritime issues, the situation in Ukraine, peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, among others. Do you have any comment?","China’s position on Hong Kong, Xinjiang, Taiwan and maritime issues is consistent and clear. We have expressed our firm opposition to the G7 presidency. The lengthy G7 communiqué is filled with preposterous allegations not even worth refuting. In total disregard of China’s solemn position and objective facts, it grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, maliciously slanders and smears China, and once again exerts pressure on China using such pretexts as the Russia-Ukraine conflict.\nWe urge the G7 to uphold the international system with the United Nations at its core, the international order based on international law, and the basic norms governing international relations underpinned by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. We urge the G7 to respect China’s sovereignty, stop maligning China or meddling in China’s domestic affairs in any form, and stop bullying other countries with the rules of their own clique.\nWe urge the G7 to act in the interest of world peace and development, stop applying double or multiple standards, stop sending military aircraft and warships to other countries’ doorsteps to flex muscles at every turn, stop wantonly instigating color revolutions in other countries, stop arbitrarily resorting to illegal sanctions or long-arm jurisdiction, and stop fabricating and spreading lies and rumors about China.\nWe urge the G7 to assume its responsibility, fulfill its due international obligation, safeguard true multilateralism, focus on global governance, strengthen cooperation with the UN, G20 and other multilateral mechanisms, and play a positive role in addressing global challenges and promoting world economic recovery, instead of clinging to the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, pursuing “small clique” group politics, creating confrontation and division, and bringing chaos to the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347282.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220516_10686612.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-16","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","On May 13, US President Biden signed a bill to direct the Secretary of State to develop a strategy to regain observer status for Taiwan in the World Health Organization. What’s China’s comment?","The bill gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, severely contravenes international law and basic norms governing international relations, and grossly interferes in China’s domestic affairs. China rejects and deplores that the US should insist on signing it into law.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s domestic affair. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations. According to relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, the participation of China’s Taiwan region in WHO activities must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Attaching high importance to our Taiwan compatriots’ health welfare, the Chinese central government has made proper arrangements for the region’s participation in global health affairs under the precondition of following the one-China principle.\nWe urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, comply with international law and basic norms governing international relations, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and not to use this bill to help Taiwan expand its so-called “international space”. Otherwise it will cause further damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347282.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220516_10686612.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-17","Wang Wenbin","AFP","US investigators said on Monday that a man who padlocked a church and opened fire on his Taiwanese American congregation was motivated by political hatred, and he was upset about the political tensions between the Chinese mainland and Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","We have noted the report you mentioned. Reports also said that this man emigrated from China’s Taiwan to the US. We hope the US government will take earnest and effective measures to solve the worsening gun violence problem at home.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347283.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220517_10687165.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A shooting incident recently occurred in California, USA, and some green media on the island disregarded the facts and used it for political hype. What is your comment?","We note that some Taiwan media have reported that both the gunman and the victims emigrated from Taiwan, China to the United States. Some green media in Taiwan have seized the opportunity to hype the matter, attempting to fabricate rumors from this unfortunate shooting and make political capital out of it. Their intentions are vicious and utterly inhumane.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220517_12436685.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-18","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US’ top naval officer Admiral Michael Gilday said that Taiwan must protect itself against potential Chinese aggression through military deterrence that includes acquiring the right weapons and proper training. Does the foreign ministry have any comments about his remarks?","The relevant remarks of the US side fly in the face of US commitment to China on the Taiwan question and constitute an interference in China’s internal affairs. China is firmly opposed to them.\nThe China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations and the August 17 Communiqué clearly noted that the United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and it acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China. In the Shanghai Communiqué, the US side also declared that, “The United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” The US admits that Taiwan is part of China, but keeps talking about the mainland’s potential “aggression” of Taiwan. It says it doesn’t support the independence of Taiwan, but removed such expressions as “Taiwan is part of China” and “The United States does not support Taiwan independence” from the State Department’s website. Such self-contradictory moves only lead people to question the seriousness and efficacy of the US claim that it adheres to the one-China policy.\nThose who break faith not only tarnish their own reputation, but will also pay the price for doing so. Breaking commitments on the Taiwan question will incur historical punishment. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and earnestly act on its statement of not supporting “Taiwan-independence”, to prevent severe damage to China-US ties and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347284.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220518_10688414.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-18","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The first one, and it’s a repeat from yesterday’s questions. Is China planning on sending a representative to the World Health Assembly next week? And if so, could you tell us who it is? Second question, the US State Department said on Tuesday that Taiwan should be allowed to attend this assembly, arguing that the island’s exclusion at China’s behest was unwarranted. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","On your first question, I have nothing to add to my response yesterday.\nTo answer your second question, there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. On the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, China’s position is consistent and clear, that is, it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. UNGA Resolution 2758 explicitly recognizes the representatives of the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations. WHA Resolution 25.1 explicitly recognizes the representatives of the People’s Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the World Health Organization. The one-China principle affirmed in these two resolutions has received universal support from the international community and represents an unstoppable trend with overwhelming public support.\nThe Chinese Central Government attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region, and has made proper arrangement for Taiwan’s participation in global health affairs on the precondition of following the one-China principle. By April 28, the Central Government had given the Taiwan region 386 updates about the COVID-19 situation, and over the past year, it approved the participation of 47 public health experts in 44 groups from the Taiwan region in WHO technical activities. The channels for Taiwan to obtain information and participate in the international COVID-19 response are unimpeded. The so-called serious health concern of the US is untenable. We advise the US to stop exploiting the WHA to play up Taiwan-related issues. Any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China will be firmly rejected by the overwhelming majority of members of the international community and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347284.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220518_10688414.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-18","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Japanese and Chinese foreign ministers had a video meeting, according to information from the Chinese foreign ministry. Can you share more details on that?","As you said, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi held a virtual meeting with Japanese Foreign Minister Yoshimasa Hayashi today.\nState Councilor Wang Yi said that this year marks the 50th anniversary of the normalization of China-Japan diplomatic ties, which is an important milestone in the development of bilateral relations. Last year the leaders of the two countries reached important common understanding on building a China-Japan relationship in keeping with the times. The two sides should be guided by this consensus and take the 50th anniversary of the normalization of ties as an opportunity to cement the political foundation for bilateral relations, and safeguard, consolidate and deepen the hard-won friendship cultivated by our predecessors and the people of both countries.\nState Councilor Wang Yi pointed out that the pressing task now is to do three things well. First, we need to steer bilateral relations in the right direction. The four political documents between China and Japan set the general direction of peace, friendship and cooperation and laid down a series of important principled consensus including the one that the two countries are cooperative partners and do not pose a threat to each other. They underpin the steady and sound development of China-Japan relations. The more complicated and challenging our relations become, the more we need to stay true to our original aspiration and unswervingly adhere to the principles and spirit enshrined in the four political documents. We should have a correct understanding of each other, actively engage in positive interactions, make good plans for the commemoration of the 50th anniversary of the normalization of diplomatic ties, strengthen exchanges and cooperation at all levels and in various fields, and foster a positive public opinion and social atmosphere. Second, we need to strengthen the impetus driving the bilateral relations forward. Economic and trade cooperation is the ballast and propeller of bilateral relations. China’s accelerated efforts to foster a new development paradigm with domestic circulation as the mainstay and domestic and international circulations reinforcing each other will provide more opportunities for Japan and the world at large. The two sides should tap the potential of cooperation, strengthen coordination and cooperation in digital economy, green and low-carbon development and climate change governance, in order to achieve win-win results at a higher level. Third, we need to remove disturbances in a timely manner. Recently, Japan’s negative moves on Taiwan and other issues concerning China’s core interests and major concerns have become increasingly visible. Some political forces have wantonly smeared and attacked China, severely undermining mutual trust and shaking the foundation of bilateral relations. The lessons of history should never be forgotten. The Japanese side should honor the commitments it has made, keep faith with China, prevent forces trying to undermine China-Japan relations from gaining ground, and work with China to maintain the achievements made over the past 50 years since the normalization of diplomatic ties.\nForeign Minister Hayashi said that Japan and China share extensive common interests and enjoy huge potential and broad prospects for cooperation. This year marks the 50th anniversary of the normalization of diplomatic relations between Japan and China. The two sides should develop constructive and stable bilateral relations in accordance with the important consensus reached by the leaders of the two countries. Japan is ready to work with China to remain true to the original aspiration of normalizing the diplomatic relationship, keep up candid communication, reduce misunderstanding and miscalculation, properly handle sensitive issues and enhance political mutual trust.\nThe two sides also exchanged views on regional and international issues of mutual interest and agreed to maintain communication.\nDuring the meeting, State Councilor Wang Yi also made clear China’s position on the negative moves targeting China by Japan and the US. On the QUAD summit to be held by Japan, he pointed out that what is concerning and alarming is that even though the US leader has yet to travel to Japan, the argument that Japan and the US should join hands in confronting China has already been widely circulated, creating pandemonium. Japan and the US are allies. China and Japan have signed a treaty of peace and friendship. When pursuing bilateral cooperation, Japan and the US should not provoke bloc confrontation, still less undermine China’s sovereignty, security and development interests. We hope that the Japanese side will learn from history, bear in mind regional peace and stability, act with prudence, refrain from acting as a cat’s paw, and avoid adopting the ill-conceived beggar-thy-neighbor approach.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347284.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220518_10688414.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-19","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","On May 18, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said in a statement that the US strongly advocates for the WHO to invite Taiwan to participate as an observer at the 75th World Health Assembly (WHA) this May. What’s China’s comment?","We firmly oppose the US statement. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. UNGA Resolution 2758 explicitly recognizes the representatives of the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations. WHA Resolution 25.1 explicitly recognizes the representatives of the People’s Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the World Health Organization. The one-China principle affirmed in these two resolutions has received universal support from the international community and represents an undeniable and unstoppable trend with overwhelming public support.\nThe Chinese Central Government attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region, and has made proper arrangement for Taiwan’s participation in global health affairs on the precondition of following the one-China principle. The channels for Taiwan to obtain information and participate in the international COVID-19 response are unimpeded.\nThe US should adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, abide by international law and basic norms governing international relations, and stop exploiting the WHA to play up Taiwan-related issues. Any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China will be firmly rejected by the overwhelming majority of members of the international community and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347285.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220519_10689450.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-19","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Director Yang Jiechi said in a phone call with US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan that if the US kept supporting Taiwan, it would lead to “a dangerous situation”. Can the foreign ministry elaborate on exactly what Yang meant by “a dangerous situation”?","I can tell you that over some time, the US has tried to play “the Taiwan card” time and again, reneged on its promise on the Taiwan question and sent wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. Such moves have harmed the China-US relations and undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nI want to stress that the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-US relations. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués as well as its political commitment to China on the Taiwan question. It should also act on President Biden’s statement that the US doesn’t support “Taiwan independence” and stop seeking political manipulation with Taiwan-related issues to contain China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347285.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220519_10689450.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th when asked: “Taiwan independence” diehard forces “exhaust Taiwan’s resources to curry favor with foreign countries,” attempt to tie all Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, turn them into victims of “independence by force,” and push them into the abyss of disaster. They are thoroughly…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that Wu Chao-hsu's remarks thoroughly expose the deliberate intention of the stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" forces to split the country and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They collude with external forces to pursue \"Taiwan independence,\" undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and attempt, under the so-called \"whole-of-society mobilization,\" to make the people of Taiwan hostages to their pursuit of \"independence,\" which is utterly inhumane. They \"exhaust Taiwan's resources to curry favor with foreign countries,\" seeking to bind all Taiwan residents to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot and turn them into victims of \"seeking independence through force,\" pushing them into an abyss of disaster. They are thoroughly traitors to the nation.\nShe said that some people in the United States have threatened to \"blow up TSMC\" and \"destroy Taiwan's infrastructure,\" fully revealing the cold-blooded indifference of treating the people of Taiwan as pawns and cannon fodder, and the evil intention to use every means to \"use Taiwan to contain China.\" This is the devastating consequence for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces selling themselves to foreign powers. How can the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots bear this!\nZhu Fenglian stated that we once again emphasize that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, the Taiwan question is entirely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. If the \"Taiwan independence\" forces misjudge the situation and collude with external forces to take reckless risks, we will certainly take resolute measures to crush them firmly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220519_12437200.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On May 18, U.S. Secretary of State Antony Blinken issued a statement saying that the United States “strongly advocates” that the WHO invite Taiwan to attend the 75th World Health Assembly as an observer. Taiwan's foreign affairs department expressed thanks. What is your comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 20th, pointing out that Taiwan is part of China and has no right to participate in international organizations that are open only to sovereign states. The US side knows this well; it has repeatedly stated that it does not support “Taiwan independence” and opposes Taiwan's participation in international organizations open only to sovereign states. The relevant US commitments should be reflected in the issue of Taiwan's participation in the World Health Organization.\nShe pointed out that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. Regarding Taiwan's participation in World Health Organization activities, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is also the fundamental principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1.\nZhu Fenglian said that the US side's use of “observer” status has ulterior motives. It must be pointed out that from 2009 to 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhered to in embodying the one-China principle, Taiwan participated in the World Health Assembly for eight consecutive years under the name “Chinese Taipei” in the capacity of an observer through cross-Strait consultations. This was a special arrangement made under the premise of adhering to the one-China principle and against the background of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations at that time. It does not constitute a precedent. The reason the Democratic Progressive Party authorities cannot attend the meeting lies entirely in their obstinate insistence on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence.”\nShe pointed out that Taiwan compatriots are our flesh and blood, and no one cares more about their health and well-being than we do. Under the premise of the one-China principle, we have made proper arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. Any epidemic information that the WHO notifies to the world is timely received by Taiwan, and the WHO has also repeatedly and publicly and in detail notified the exchanges on epidemic situations with Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian said that we urge the US side to respect facts, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, fulfill the solemn commitments the US side has made to China on the Taiwan question, stop playing the “Taiwan card” and stop pursuing “using Taiwan to contain China.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220520_12437550.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","AFP","President Biden has said that the United States would defend Taiwan militarily if Beijing invaded or forcibly tried to take control of Taiwan. He has said, we agreed with the one China policy, we signed on it, but the idea that Taiwan can be taken by force is just not appropriate. How does the foreign ministry view this US position? And how will this affect China-US ties going forward?","China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to the remarks by the US side. There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a consensus of the international community and a political commitment made by the US to China. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. On issues concerning China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and other core interests, China has no room for compromise or concession. No one should underestimate the strong resolve, determination and capability of the Chinese people in safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No one should stand in opposition to the 1.4 billion Chinese people.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, honor its important commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, speak and act with prudence on the Taiwan question, and avoid sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, lest it should seriously undermine peace across the Taiwan Strait and China-US relations. China will take firm actions to safeguard its sovereignty and security interests. We mean what we say.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","NHK","In their meeting, the US President and Japanese Prime Minister opposed China’s attempts to change the status quo in the East China Sea and South China Sea and reiterated the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment?","China’s position on Taiwan, Diaoyu Dao and maritime issues is consistent and clear-cut. We firmly oppose attempts by the US and Japan to hype up relevant issues to damage China’s reputation and interfere in China’s internal affairs. The biggest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities’ separatist activities and the moves of certain countries, including the US, to aid and abet such efforts. Japan bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. It should speak and act with extra prudence, earnestly learn lessons from history and avoid repeating past mistakes.\nI must stress that the US’ so-called “deterrence” and “containment” policy has already disrupted Europe. It should stop trying to destabilize the Asia-Pacific region. The Asia-Pacific should become the pacesetter of peace and development, not the arena of geopolitics. The US and Japan hold onto the Cold War mentality, gang up to build military alliances and small cliques featuring economic decoupling, and stoke division and confrontation. Their scheme is unpopular in the Asia-Pacific and will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","PTI","In his press conference today, Mr. Biden said that any action by the mainland on Taiwan will not only dislocate the entire region, and it would be another action similar to what happened in Ukraine. What’s your response?","It is absurd to compare the Taiwan question to the Ukraine issue as the two are of completely different nature. We once again urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and not to underestimate the Chinese people’s strong resolve, will and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Taiwan media reported yesterday that former Japanese prime minister Shinzo Abe might visit Taiwan at the end of July. Does China oppose the potential visit by Abe, who is not the incumbent prime minister?","As I said just now, on the Taiwan question, Japan bears historical responsibilities toward the Chinese people for the crimes it committed in the past. Therefore, it should be even more prudent with its words and deeds. We urge the Japanese side to adhere to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","Yonhap News Agency","On May 21, the ROK and the US held a leaders’ summit and released a joint statement, which stressed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Does China have any comment?","The Chinese side has lodged solemn representations with relevant sides. Taiwan is part of the Chinese territory and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs. We will never allow any country to meddle in China’s domestic affairs in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","On May 21, US State Department Spokesperson Ned Price said on social media platform that China continues to misrepresent US policy. “The United States does not subscribe to the PRC’s ‘one China principle’ – we remain committed to our longstanding, bipartisan one China policy, guided by the Taiwan Relations Act, Three Joint Communiques, and Six Assurances,” he said. Do you have any comment?","The relevant remarks of the US side misrepresent history and distort facts.\nThe Taiwan question is the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The core of the Taiwan question is “one China”. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is the core concept of the one-China principle and has become a consensus of the international community and basic norm governing international relations. In October 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, which “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations, and to expel forthwith the representatives of Chiang Kai-shek from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations and in all the organizations related to it.” A total of 181 countries, the US included, have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of recognizing the one-China principle.\nIn history, the Taiwan question was once the biggest obstacle in the normalization of China-US relations. That’s because China firmly adheres to the one-China principle and makes no compromise or concession on the Taiwan question. In 1971, the US affirmed to China the new principles it would follow with regard to the Taiwan question. They include: the US would acknowledge that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is a part of China; the US would not repeat the phrase that the status of Taiwan is undetermined; the US had not supported, and would not support movements for “Taiwan independence”. President Nixon reaffirmed these principles to Premier Zhou Enlai during his visit to China in 1972. That was how the Shanghai Communiqué came into being.\nThe US side explicitly declared in the Shanghai Communiqué released in 1972 that “the United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” The above-mentioned commitments made by the US started the process toward normalization of China-US relations. China decided to establish diplomatic relations with the US only when three preconditions had been met, namely, the US severed “diplomatic relations” and abrogated the “mutual defense treaty” with the Taiwan authorities and withdrew US military forces from Taiwan. In the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the United States of America and the People’s Republic of China released in 1978, the US “recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China” and “acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China”.\nIn the August 17 Communiqué released in 1982, the US explicitly stated, “In the Joint communique on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations on January 1, 1979, issued by the Government of the People’s Republic of China and the Government of the United States of America, the United States of America recognized the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China, and it acknowledged the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” It also “reiterates that it has no intention of infringing on Chinese sovereignty and territorial integrity, or interfering in China’s internal affairs, or pursuing a policy of ‘two Chinas’ or ‘one China, one Taiwan’.” These commitments are there for all to see. They are crystal clear and inked in the documents. Such historical facts cannot be wiped off or denied.\nHowever, the US has not been faithfully implementing the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués over the past 40 years or so. There are more than enough examples in this regard. The US has significantly eased constraints on official exchanges with Taiwan, and the level and frequency of bilateral exchanges have greatly increased. This is a breach of its commitment to maintaining unofficial relations with Taiwan only. There have been more frequent open military interactions between the US and Taiwan, and the size and performance of arms sold by the US to Taiwan have kept increasing, with a total worth of over $70 billion. This is a breach of its commitment to gradually reducing its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution. The US has helped Taiwan to expand its so-called “international space”, even jumping into the front stage to help Taiwan consolidate its so-called diplomatic ties. This is a breach of its commitment that it has no intention of pursuing a policy of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”.\nIn recent years, the US has doubled down on efforts to mislead the public in order to hollow out the one-China principle. For example, the US is using more descriptions to modify its one-China policy, including its unilaterally-concocted Taiwan Relations Act and Six Assurances which have never been recognized and are firmly opposed by China from the very beginning. The China-US relationship, as that between two states, can only be guided by political consensus between the two countries, rather than be established on policy unilaterally formulated by the US side. The US has spread the fallacy in the international community that UNGA Resolution 2758 has not resolved the status of Taiwan, claiming that its one-China policy is different from China’s one-China principle and that each country has the right to define its own one-China policy framework. It is not hard to tell from the facts that China is not misrepresenting the US policy. It is the US who has been constantly reneging on its own commitments, bilateral consensus and its original position. Such moves are aimed at historical backpedaling, obstructing China’s peaceful reunification by using the Taiwan question, undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and building Taiwan into “an unsinkable aircraft carrier” to contain China with the Taiwan question.\nIt must be pointed out that be it the one-China principle or the one-China policy, their essence is both about “one China”. This is a political consensus reached between China and the US. Without this consensus, China and the US couldn’t have engaged with each other and established diplomatic ties and the bilateral relationship couldn’t have achieved development.\nWe must also stress that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and realizing China’s complete reunification is the shared aspiration of all the Chinese people. China is firmly resolved in defending its sovereignty and security interests. There is zero room for compromise and not an inch to give on the Taiwan question.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, return to the original and true meaning of “one-China”, follow through on President Biden’s remarks of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop hollowing out the one-China principle, stop seeking to contain China with Taiwan-related issues, stop emboldening “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and avoid causing further severe damage to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","AFP","US National Security Adviser Jake Sullivan has said that the United States is looking to deepen economic partnerships with Taiwan, including on high technology issues, including on semiconductors and supply chains. Now, this was said during the launch of the Indo-Pacific Economic Framework for Prosperity. How does Beijing view US attempts to deepen trade ties with Taiwan?","I would like to reiterate that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. This is a widely-held consensus of the international community. Recent US moves on Taiwan challenge the one-China principle and escalate tensions across the Taiwan Strait. This is no different from playing with fire, which is very dangerous. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and immediately stop meddling in China’s internal affairs, lest it should undermine China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-23","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","We just learned that the 75th World Health Assembly (WHA) has explicitly refused to include a proposal on Taiwan’s participation as an observer in its agenda. Do you have any comment?","The General Committee and the Plenary Session of the 75th World Health Assembly (WHA) have respectively decided to reject the so-called proposal of “inviting Taiwan to participate in the WHA as an observer” submitted by certain countries. This fully demonstrates the shared international commitment to the one-China principle, an overriding trend that cannot be challenged.\nIn disregard of the aspiration of all parties and the well-being of our Taiwan compatriots, the DPP authorities obstinately instigated countries having what it calls “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan to make Taiwan-related proposals. A handful of countries have encouraged and emboldened this move overtly or covertly, which goes against the trend of history and is egregious in nature. The relevant proposal has been rejected by countries taking a just stand. By the time the assembly commenced, nearly 90 countries sent letters to the WHO to express their commitment to the one-China principle and opposition to Taiwan’s participation in the WHA.\nThe Chinese Central Government always attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region. Under the precondition of abiding by the one-China principle, we have made appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region’s participation in global health affairs. The Central Government has given the Taiwan region about 400 updates about the pandemic situation since the start of COVID-19, and approved 47 visits by public health experts from the Taiwan region to 44 WHO technical activities over the past year. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region for it to promptly access and report information related to health emergencies. The claim of a “gap” in global anti-epidemic efforts is groundless.\nThe DPP authorities should know that the attempt to seek the independence of Taiwan by taking advantage of the pandemic will lead nowhere. We also urge certain countries to stop politicizing the health issue and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs by exploiting Taiwan-related issues. Otherwise, they are doomed to fail just like a man who lifts a rock only to drop it on his own feet.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347287.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220523_10691438.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 23 (Electronic dispatch). Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated in response to questions on the 23rd that on May 22 and 23, the General Committee and the plenary session of the 75th World Health Assembly respectively decided to clearly refuse to place a Taiwan-related proposal submitted by certain countries on the Assembly's agenda. Facts have repeatedly proven that 'Taiwan independence' has no way out, and that hyping Taiwan-related issues at the World Health Assembly is unpopular and will not succeed. The One-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community. It reflects popular sentiment and the trend of the times, and it is not subject to any challenge.\nZhu Fenglian said that it must be pointed out that the mainland has always attached great importance to the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, we were the first to invite Taiwan health experts to inspect Wuhan, Hubei, sharing more than 50 technical documents, and made special trips to notify them about the mainland sharing the virus gene sequence with the WHO and information on ways to obtain the relevant gene sequences. To date, we have notified the Taiwan region of COVID-19 epidemic information about 400 times, including information on Taiwan residents diagnosed on the mainland. According to incomplete statistics, over the past year, Taiwan, China, technical experts participated in 44 batches of WHO technical activities, totaling 47 person-times. The channels for the Taiwan region to obtain various epidemic prevention and control information and support are completely smooth and effective. The so-called 'gap in the international epidemic prevention system' is a political lie and merely a pretext for the DPP authorities to 'use the epidemic to seek independence.'\nShe said that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist 'Taiwan independence' stance, distort and deny the '1992 Consensus' which embodies the One-China principle, undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait consultations, and have caused the political foundation for the Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. This situation was entirely created by the DPP authorities.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, have repeatedly made trouble and provoked on the WHO Assembly issue. Relevant countries play the 'Taiwan card' and, on occasions such as the World Health Assembly, support Taiwan in expanding so-called 'international space,' attempting to shake the international consensus that Taiwan is part of China. Facts once again show that any act aimed at undermining the One-China principle and splitting the country will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220523_12438040.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-05-23","Zhu Fenglian","美国总统拜登访日期间在被记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 23 (electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 23rd: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. We urge the US side to stop any words or deeds that…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, stubbornly engage in provocations to seek “independence,” causing the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop any act of splitting the country, and immediately stop “relying on the US to seek independence,” or they will come to no good end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220523_12438066.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-24","Wang Wenbin","NHK","I have two questions. First, it is reported that the Quad Joint Leaders’ Statement said that the US, Japan, India and Australia should champion adherence to international law to respond to China’s intensifying maritime activities and to meet challenges to the maritime rules-based order presented by China. Do you have any comment? Second, when taking a question from the press, US President Biden said that US…","As to your first question, China actively upholds the UN-centered international system and the international order underpinned by international law. As a party to UNCLOS and other important maritime conventions, China actively fulfills its obligations to relevant international law. We hope certain countries would not see China through tinted glasses and make unwarranted accusations. Building small cliques and stoking bloc confrontation is the real threat to a peaceful, stable and cooperative maritime order.\nOn your second question, the US has been racking its brains to play with words when it comes to the one-China principle. I want to remind the US side that no forces, the US included, can hold back the Chinese people’s endeavor to reunify the nation. Also, no forces, the US included, can change the fate of the “Taiwan independence” forces who are doomed to fail.\nReneging on its promise on the Taiwan question, the US has obscured and hollowed out the one-China principle, and publicly or stealthily incited and endorsed “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. If the US continues to go down the wrong path, there will be irretrievable consequences for the China-US relations and the US will have to pay an unbearable price.\nOur stern message to the US: There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China’s territory and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a consensus of the international community and a commitment made by the US to China. The one-China principle is unshakable, China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity cannot be violated and the red line of avoiding creating “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” must not be crossed.\nChina has full confidence and capability and is fully prepared to firmly stem the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, foil all external interference and resolutely uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity. I’d like to advise the US to listen to a well-known Chinese song with these lyrics: “For our friends, we have fine wine. For jackals or wolves, we welcome with shotguns.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347288.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220524_10691994.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-24","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","On May 23, Japanese and US leaders had a meeting and released a joint statement in which they manipulated China-related issues and criticized China on several issues. They also clamor for advancing a “free and open Indo-Pacific” and extending military deterrence in the region. Do you have any comment?","In disregard of the grave concerns of China and other countries in the region, Japan and the US insisted on manipulating China-related issues to attack and smear China and grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs. Such moves violate international law and basic norms governing international relations and undermine China’s sovereignty, security and development interests. China deplores and rejects this and has lodged solemn representations. I wish to emphasize the following points:\nFirst, China’s resolve and will to safeguard its sovereignty, security and development interests are as firm as rock. The Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and concerns China’s core interests. China will respond firmly and forcefully to any attempt by any country or force to play the Taiwan card and use Taiwan-related issues to contain China. Hong Kong and Xinjiang affairs are China’s internal affairs that allow no interference from any country. China has indisputable sovereignty over Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands. Our activities in relevant waters are completely legitimate and lawful. China is firmly committed to upholding territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. In the meantime, China is committed to advancing COC consultations with ASEAN countries and jointly upholding peace and stability in the South China Sea. Japan and the US have misrepresented facts and truth, ignored the history of relevant issues, seriously undermined China’s territorial sovereignty and gravely violated international law and basic norms governing international relations. Such acts are the real threats to regional peace and stability.\nSecond, the people of Asia-Pacific countries cherish the hard-won environment for peace and development and will never allow turmoil and war to recur in this region, or confrontation between military blocs and camps to be introduced into the Asia-Pacific region. In the name of freedom and openness, the US concocted the “Indo-Pacific Strategy” and created political and military confrontation by ganging up with some countries. In essence, this is like reversing the course of history. It will only undermine regional peace and stability and is doomed to fail. The international community has its fair judgement on this. To quote some lines of a poem: “In a world that is not so big, / a few flies bumped into the wall, / buzzing and sobbing in misery”. The mainstream appeal for harmonious coexistence and win-win cooperation among Asia-Pacific countries will remain unchanged, and the trend of the times for advancing regional integration and the building of an Asia-Pacific community with a shared future will remain unchanged.\nThird, due to the aggression and colonization by Japan’s militarism in modern history, Japan’s moves in the military and security fields have always been followed closely by its Asian neighbors and the international community. Japan has increased its defense budget for a decade in a row and has often made an issue out of its neighbors to justify its military build-up. Japan keeps in long-term storage a large amount of sensitive nuclear materials exceeding its actual needs. To enjoy the benefits of the US’ nuclear umbrella, Japan spares no effort to thwart the adoption of a no-first-use policy by the US. Recently, there have been repeated dangerous calls in Japan that contravene its three non-nuclear principles, which makes its Asian neighbors and the international community seriously question Japan’s security policy. The Japanese side should stick to the path of peaceful development and continue to speak and act with prudence in the military and security field. This is the right path to take and the only way to avoid repeating past mistakes.\nAt last, I want to stress that China is always a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a champion of international order. We are ready to work with all peace-loving and development-seeking countries to strengthen solidarity and cooperation, jointly respond to challenges, promote the implementation of the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative and build a community with a shared future for mankind. At the same time, China never allows any country to interfere in China’s internal affairs, undermine China’s interests or tarnish China’s image. We will defend our sovereignty, security and development interests, and stay committed to safeguarding peace, stability and lasting prosperity in the Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347288.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220524_10691994.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-25","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","China’s military says it conducted military exercises around Taiwan in recent days. What’s the Chinese government’s comment on this? And is it related in any way to the US president’s recent comments regarding Taiwan?","As to the relevant military exercises you mentioned, the spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has released relevant information. You can check it out. We have repeated many times China’s position on the US recent erroneous actions on Taiwan-related issues. I would like to stress again that the US attempts to hollow out the one-China principle, and overt and covert instigation and support for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities will not only cause irreversible consequences for China-US relations, but also make the US pay an unbearable price.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347289.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220525_10692555.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-05-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to reports, Japanese Defense Minister Nobuo Kishi, during a meeting with the US Ambassador to Japan, touched on issues such as China's “attempts to unilaterally change the status quo,” the Korean Peninsula, and the Russia-Ukraine conflict, saying the regional security situation is not optimistic and that “the two countries must resolutely safeguard universal values such as democracy and the rule of…","We have noted relevant reports. China has consistently held that exchanges and cooperation between relevant countries should help safeguard regional peace and stability, and should not target or harm the interests of third parties. Maliciously speculating and taking sides along partisan lines will only create more trust deficits, tension and confrontation.\nOn the Taiwan question, for some time now, Japan and the United States have disregarded the basic norms of international relations, brutally interfered in China’s internal affairs, and deliberately hyped and manipulated Taiwan-related issues on various occasions. These vicious words and deeds not only send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces and pose a serious threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but also allow the international community to see more clearly which countries and individuals are undermining international rules, infringing on other countries’ sovereignty, and creating regional turmoil. It must be pointed out that this in no way shakes the determination and will of the Chinese People’s Liberation Army to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We are unafraid of storms and are fully prepared, and we will firmly thwart any form of external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/05-25/9763067.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","In an interview with Australian media in February, Australian Defence Minister Peter Dutton said that because the United States and its allies have acquiesced to China's “militarization” conduct, China has already established 20 “military strongholds” in the South China Sea. This is obviously not conducive to regional stability. He said, “If this continues, we will lose the next decade,” and that Australia must…","The Nansha Islands [South China Sea islands] are China's inherent territory. It is only natural and entirely justified for China to carry out infrastructure construction on its own territory and deploy necessary defensive forces, and no one, including Australia, has any right to make irresponsible remarks about it. I would like to stress that if the officials of a country's defense department are obsessed with confrontation and deliberately stir up trouble and unrest in the South China Sea, that country will lose not only the next decade, but also its international credibility and its opportunities for cooperation with the countries of the region.\nWe have repeatedly expressed our grave concern and firm opposition to nuclear-powered submarine cooperation between the United States, Britain and Australia under the framework of the trilateral security partnership. The three countries forming a small circle highlights a Cold War zero-sum mentality, has a strong military security character, runs counter to the trend of the times, goes against the wishes of the countries of the region, and is destined to lead nowhere. The project involves nuclear-weapon states transferring large quantities of weapons-grade nuclear material to non-nuclear-weapon states, violating relevant provisions of the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons and the South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty. It carries serious risks of nuclear proliferation, will intensify the regional arms race, and will also have far-reaching effects on the resolution of other nuclear hotspot issues in other regions. China urges the U.S., UK and Australian small clique to abandon Cold War thinking and zero-sum game concepts, to respond to the concerns of the international community in a responsible manner, to mind their own business and spend more time on self-reflection, to revoke their erroneous decision as soon as possible, and to fulfill their non-proliferation obligations through concrete actions.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/05-25/9763447.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，日防卫大臣岸信夫称，中国海军辽宁舰航母编队近期在接近日西南诸岛和台湾附近区域活动，中方舰载机起降次数超过数百余次，日方对此保持密切关注。日防卫省通报，日出动“出云”号直升机航母跟踪监视，日战机升空应对中方舰载机活动。请问中方对此有何评论？","According to a message from the WeChat public account “National Defense Ministry Release,” on the 9th, Wu Qian, spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense, responded to a question on US arms sales to Taiwan, saying that China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nA question was raised: According to reports, on February 7, the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency announced that the US had approved the sale to Taiwan of Patriot missile defense system equipment and services worth about 100 million US dollars. What is your comment?\nWu Qian pointed out that the US sale of weapons to Taiwan, China's Taiwan region, seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. It crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, harms China's sovereignty and security interests, undermines the relationship between the two countries and the two militaries of China and the United States, and endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. China strongly demands that the US side immediately cancel the above arms sales plan to Taiwan, stop military contacts between the US and Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, so as to avoid causing serious consequences for the relationship between the two countries and their militaries and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nWu Qian said that the future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and Taiwan's security depends on the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait under the one-China principle, not on US arms sales to Taiwan. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely thwart any form of external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, and continue to advance the process of national reunification.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10158481.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the CPC Central Committee, the State Council and the Central Military Commission recently issued the “Regulations on Military Merit and Honor Commendations” and a notice requiring all regions and departments to conscientiously implement them. Please spokesperson introduce the innovations and highlights of the “Regulations”? What provisions are there for foreign-related military merit and honor…","After the \"Regulations on Honors and Awards for the Armed Forces\" were promulgated and took effect, society at large paid close attention, and officers and soldiers across the armed forces were greatly encouraged. The atmosphere of venerating heroes, learning from heroes, and striving to become heroes has grown even stronger throughout the units. The main innovations of the Regulations include: first, they were issued jointly by the CPC Central Committee, the State Council, and the Central Military Commission, which is unprecedented in the history of our military; second, they specify that the honors and awards of the armed forces include medals, honorary titles, awards, commendations, and commemorative medals; third, they extend the circumstances in which military honors and awards are implemented to wartime, peacetime, and major non-war military operations; fourth, they systematically standardize the items, conditions, authority, procedures, honor insignia, treatment, publicity, and management and supervision of honors and awards; fifth, they standardize foreign-related military honors and awards; sixth, they uniformly standardize the treatment of recipients of military honors and awards; seventh, in their system design, the medals, badges, and commemorative medals focus on winning battles and strengthening the military.\nThe promulgation and implementation of the Regulations are of great significance for improving the system of honors and awards of the Party and the state, enhancing the attractiveness of the military profession and servicemembers' sense of mission and honor, educating and guiding officers and soldiers to carry forward the fearless heroic spirit and tenacious fighting style of our military, and inspiring the entire armed forces to work hard to achieve the goal of the centenary of the founding of the military.\nRegarding foreign-related military honors and awards, the Regulations specify matters concerning our military's conferral of honors and awards on foreign personnel and our military personnel's acceptance of foreign honors and awards. They specify that foreign-related military medals, badges, and commemorative medals include the \"Peace Medal,\" the Peace Badge, and the Peace Commemorative Medal, which are mainly composed of elements such as the military emblem, the dove of peace, and the olive branch.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10158481.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Chinese naval fleet delivering relief supplies to Tonga recently arrived in Nuku'alofa, the capital of Tonga. Please further introduce the relevant situation.","At the request of the Kingdom of Tonga for assistance with volcanic disaster relief, the Chinese military dispatched the Wuzhishan ship and the Chagan Lake ship to form a maritime transport formation to Tonga to carry out the mission of transporting disaster relief supplies. The formation departed from Guangzhou on January 31, the Lunar New Year's Eve, and arrived at Nuku'alofa Port in Tonga on February 15, the Lantern Festival. After continuously sailing more than 5,200 nautical miles, it transported a total of more than 1,400 tons of disaster relief supplies, including large items such as mobile sheds, tractors, and generators, as well as emergency supplies such as drinking water, food, and medical and epidemic prevention equipment. The formation properly handled complex meteorological conditions and sea conditions such as high winds, heavy waves, and volcanic pumice, strictly implemented epidemic prevention and disinfection protocols, ensured the safety of navigation and supply transport, and, in accordance with changes in the disaster situation and epidemic prevention situation in Tonga, closely coordinated with the Tongan side to safely and smoothly complete the handover of supplies. The Tongan prime minister, foreign minister, and other senior officials went to the port to greet the formation, expressed sincere gratitude to the Chinese side, and highly praised the friendship between Tonga and China.\nAll within the four seas are brothers, and all under the same sky share the same sunrise. The China-Tonga disaster relief cooperation vividly embodies the concepts of a community with a shared future for mankind and a community with a shared future for the oceans, and has deepened the comprehensive strategic partnership between China and Tonga. The Chinese side will, according to Tonga's needs, continue to provide assistance within its capacity for Tonga's post-disaster reconstruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10158481.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The United States recently released the report “The Indo-Pacific Strategy of the United States,” claiming that China continues to integrate its economic, diplomatic, military, and technological strength, seeks to build a “sphere of influence” in the Indo-Pacific, and has caused major challenges for the region. The US will further closely cooperate with allies and partners to respond to these challenges and engage…","This U.S. report uses the pretext of hyping threats from other countries and the means of building closed and exclusive small circles and cliques, while claiming to aim at promoting a free, open, prosperous, and secure region. Its logic is confused and its reasoning does not hold. Promises and visions painted with such an outdated Cold War mentality and confrontational concept cannot be convincing either, because once this veneer is stripped away, its true face is nothing other than containing the development of other countries and maintaining its own hegemony.\nDiversity and inclusiveness are the foundation for the prosperity and development of the Asia-Pacific region. The peoples of the Asia-Pacific expect openness and inclusiveness, not narrowness and closure. To try to forcibly shape and change the Asia-Pacific region based on one’s own selfish interests and strength is itself a high-handed and ignorant idea. We urge the countries concerned to follow the trend of the times toward peaceful development and win-win cooperation, shoulder the historic responsibility of promoting regional peace, stability, and prosperity, and make the Asia-Pacific a driving force for mutually beneficial cooperation, not an arena for zero-sum games.\nThe negative content concerning Taiwan in the U.S. report seriously interferes in China’s internal affairs and seriously violates the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations. We firmly oppose this. The Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests and brooks no foreign interference. We urge the U.S. side to recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10158481.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-05-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the US Navy recently acknowledged that the video circulating in the media of a US Navy F-35C fighter jet falling into the sea in late January is authentic. Also, a US Department of Defense spokesperson confirmed that the Navy is “doing everything possible” to carry out a recovery operation for the F-35C in relevant waters of the South China Sea. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We have noted the relevant reports. Freedom of navigation and overflight in the South China Sea has never been an issue. For a long time, the U.S. side, under the banner of “freedom of navigation and overflight,” has frequently sent military ships and aircraft to the South China Sea to provoke, infringe upon rights, and flaunt its military strength, heightening regional tensions. “Showing off muscle too often inevitably leads to muscle strain.” As is well known, since last year the U.S. military has bumped into submarines underwater and lost aircraft at sea in the South China Sea region. In previous years, its ships and aircraft also suffered multiple collisions in different sea areas, causing serious casualties. This series of incidents shows that the U.S. side has not only failed to be a defender of freedom of navigation and overflight, but has instead become a “troublemaker” and an “accident maker.”\nWe believe that the South China Sea should be a sea of peace, a sea of friendship, and a sea of cooperation, not a “Wild West” where certain countries act recklessly and seek to win by force. The U.S. side should immediately stop its large-scale, high-frequency military activities that it has carried out for a long time. Otherwise, what will be damaged is not only the efforts of regional countries to maintain peace and stability in the South China Sea, but also its own credibility and the safety of its personnel.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10158481.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-05-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 26 dispatch — Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office pointed out on the 26th in response to questions that Wu Chao-hsi and his ilk attempt to collude with external forces, seeking political self-interest at the expense of the welfare and interests of Taiwan's people. They are thoroughly diehard 'Taiwan independence' elements. Their 'Taiwan independence' words and deeds have once again exposed their essence of seeking 'independence'; every one of their disgraceful acts is on record and they will surely be severely punished.\nA reporter asked: Wu Chao-hsi recently accepted an interview with the U.S. National Public Radio (NPR), spreading 'Taiwan independence' remarks to attack the mainland and advocating collusion between the United States and Taiwan. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220526_12438906.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-27","Wang Wenbin","AFP","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken called yesterday for vigorous competition with China to preserve the existing global order. He said that Beijing posed the most serious long-term challenge to the international order. I wonder if you have any comment on this?","In his verbose speech, Secretary Blinken went to great length to spread disinformation, play up the so-called “China threat”, interfere in China’s internal affairs and smear China’s domestic and foreign policy. The sole purpose is to contain and suppress China’s development and maintain the US hegemony. China deplores and rejects this. I’d like to stress the following:\nFirst, humanity is now living in a new era of connectivity, where all countries share a common future and their interests are closely intertwined. The pursuit of peace, development and win-win results is an unstoppable trend of the times. In the face of changes unseen in a century, we must stick together and promote solidarity and cooperation if we want to uphold world peace and stability, meet the challenge of COVID-19 and revitalize the global economy. The US sensationalization of the so-called “China threat” cannot solve its own problems, and will only lead the world to a dangerous abyss.\nSecond, the US side is completely confusing right and wrong when calling China “the most serious long-term challenge to the international order”. China was, is and will remain a defender of the international order. We uphold the UN-centered international system, the international order based on international law and the basic norms governing international relations underpinned by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. People with discerning eyes can easily see that the so-called “rules-based international order” claimed by the US is nothing but a set of “house rules” established by the US and a handful of other countries to maintain the so-called “order” led by the US. The US always puts its domestic law above international law, and cherry-picks international rules as it sees fit in a pragmatic way. This is the biggest source of instability in the international order.\nThird, peace, development, equity, justice, democracy and freedom are the common values of humanity. Democracy and human rights have historical, specific and practical contexts. Countries can only explore suitable paths in light of national realities and people’s needs. There is no one-size-fits-all model. No country has the right to monopolize the definition of democracy and human rights, to lecture others on those issues, or to meddle in other countries’ internal affairs under the pretext of human rights. The US is running a huge deficit in democracy and human rights with its deplorable track record. Is it in a position to posture as a guardian of democracy and human rights and criticize other countries on these issues?\nFourth, China advocates the principle of extensive consultation, joint contribution and shared benefits, and holds that the future of the world should be decided by all countries together. Countries should build partnerships featuring equal treatment, consultation and mutual understanding. Major countries should take the lead in charting a new course of international engagement of dialogue and partnership rather than confrontation and alliance. Creating “small cliques” is reversing the course of history. Forging “small groups” is against the trend of history. The US creates the so-called “Indo-Pacific strategy” to rope in regional countries to encircle and contain China, and claims to “shape the strategic environment around Beijing”. This move to gang up on China will get no support and is doomed to fail.\nFifth, China’s diplomacy champions and practices the five principles of peaceful coexistence, stays committed to establishing and developing friendly and cooperative relations with all countries, calls for equality of all countries regardless of size, and opposes imposing one’s own will on others. The label of “coercive diplomacy” can by no means be pinned on China. The US is the inventor of and the synonym to “coercive diplomacy”. Those being coerced by the US could be big or small, close or distant, and friend or foe. The US obsession with bullying has brought deep sufferings to the international community. It is high time that the US worked on this bad habit.\nSixth, issues relating to Taiwan, Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Tibet are purely China’s internal affairs. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving complete national reunification is the shared aspiration and firm will of all the Chinese people. There is no room for any compromise. The US said that it does not support “Taiwan independence”, but it is not practicing what it says. The US has violated the political commitment it made to China time and again, trying to hollow out the one-China principle and embolden the “Taiwan independence” forces. It is such moves that attempt to change the status quo and constitute severe threats to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Xinjiang-related issues are essentially about fighting violent terrorism, extremism and separatism. The accusations of “genocide” and “forced labor” have long been proven lies of the century. The US is risking its own credibility by insisting on spreading those lies. Hong Kong is part of China. When implementing the policy of “people of Hong Kong administering Hong Kong”, the guiding document can only be China’s Constitution and the Basic Law of Hong Kong, not the Sino-British Joint Declaration. We urge the US to abide by basic norms governing international relations, stop using the above-mentioned issues to interfere in China’s internal affairs, and stop spreading lies and disinformation. We solemnly warn the US side not to underestimate the strong resolution, will and capability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nSeventh, while talking about competition with China, the US is actually overstretching the concept of national security to impose illegal unilateral sanctions, exercise long-arm jurisdiction and seek decoupling and industrial chain breakage, which have gravely undermined the legitimate rights and interests of Chinese enterprises and deprived other countries of the right to development. This is by no means “responsible competition”, but rather unscrupulous suppression and containment. The key for the China-US relationship to walk out of the predicament is for the US side to abandon its mania for zero-sum games, give up its obsession with encircling and containing China and stop undermining China-US relations.\nThe China-US relationship is now at an important crossroads. Antagonism and confrontation or dialogue and cooperation? Mutual benefit and win-win cooperation or zero-sum game? The US side should make the right choices bearing in mind the common interests of people in both countries and the world. It needs to act on President Biden’s remarks that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; it does not aim to change China’s system; the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; the US does not support “Taiwan independence”; and it has no intention to seek a conflict with China. We have noted that Secretary Blinken said in his speech that the US is not looking for conflict or a new Cold War with China; it doesn’t seek to block China from its role as a major power, nor to stop China from growing its economy; and it wants to coexist peacefully with China. We are watching what the US will do.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347291.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220527_10693630.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-27","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Just on the speech by Antony Blinken. You mentioned that Blinken was spreading disinformation. I wonder if you could elaborate a little bit about that in terms of specific examples or what exactly you were referring to when you mentioned spreading disinformation. And also secondly, you said that China is watching what the US will do. Could you give some specific examples in terms of Taiwan, for example? What will…","Let me start with your first question. You asked me to give you an example of what Secretary Blinken said was disinformation. Here is a typical example. Secretary Blinken said that China poses “the most serious long-term challenge to the international order”. This is a classic piece of disinformation.\nInternational rules and order have been clearly defined. China has always maintained that all countries should firmly uphold the international system with the UN at its core, international order underpinned by international law, and basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. China has always been a staunch defender of the international order. Secretary Blinken said that China poses “the most serious long-term challenge to the international order”. What will you call it if not disinformation?\nWe urge the US side to follow China’s example and make a clear statement that it firmly upholds the international system with the UN at its core, international order underpinned by international law, and basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, instead of smearing and attacking others.\nAs to your second question, I made clear China’s position just now. We urge the US to bear in mind the common interests of people in both countries and the world. It should act on President Biden’s remarks that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; it does not aim to change China’s system; the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; the US does not support “Taiwan independence”; and it has no intention to seek a conflict with China. The US should work with China to find a way for our two major countries to get along with peaceful coexistence, mutual respect and win-win cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347291.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220527_10693630.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","(Xinhua News Agency) Beijing, May 27 — U.S. Secretary of State Blinken delivered a speech on China policy on the 26th, spreading erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 27th, pointing out that the relevant speech by the U.S. Secretary of State is full of untrue claims, hypes the “China threat,” spreads erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan, and once again exposes the U.S. nature of “backing Taiwan to contain China” and attempting to prevent the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nZhu Fenglian said that as far as the Taiwan question is concerned, it must be pointed out that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. The U.S. side made solemn commitments on the Taiwan question in the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, but in fact has repeatedly violated its commitments and said one thing while doing another. The U.S. side has frequently colluded with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, sold arms to Taiwan, helped Taiwan expand its so-called “international space,” and so on, and it has attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and hyped the “theory of undetermined status of Taiwan,” attempting to play the “Taiwan card.” We firmly oppose this.\nShe pointed out that the U.S. side's so-called “coercion of Taiwan” and “changing the status quo” remarks are completely black-and-white reversals. Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question does not allow any interference from external forces. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts, while at the same time we will never renounce the use of force and reserve the option of taking all necessary measures, which is directed at external interference and at an extremely small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities.\nZhu Fenglian said that the true status quo of the Taiwan question and the core content of the one-China principle are: there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China. “Taiwan independence” forces keep seeking “independence” and provoking, and the United States is egging them on and backing them up, which is the root cause of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait region. “Taiwan independence” separatists and external anti-China forces must immediately stop their provocations. No one should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220527_12439232.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-05-30","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","According to media reports, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Sen, commenting on some negative remarks by the US side on Taiwan, stressed that Taiwan is a Chinese province and an inalienable part of China’s territory and that pushing Taiwan to declare independence is a dangerous adventure. He called on all sides to respect China’s sovereignty and avoid adding fuel to the flame. Do you have any comment?","China highly appreciates Prime Minister Hun Sen’s remarks on Taiwan. There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a consensus of the international community. The Taiwan question is purely China’s domestic affair and brooks no foreign interference. The Chinese side’s just cause of safeguarding sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposing secession, and realizing national reunification has received and will surely continue to receive understanding and support from Cambodia and the rest of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347292.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220530_10694611.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-31","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","In a meeting with Taiwanese “President” Tsai Ing-wen today, US Senator Tammy Duckworth said she wanted to emphasize support for Taiwan, not only about military, but also to ensure that Taiwan will not stand alone and the US will stand with Taiwan. Do you have any comment? Given the clear signal of supports to Taiwan sent by the US recently, does China believe that the US has given up its policy of strategic…","Taiwan is a province of China, what president does it have to speak of? Relevant US congresswoman’s visit to Taiwan seriously violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiques. China deplores and rejects this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nWe urge relevant US politicians to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, and immediately stop official exchanges with Taiwan in any form and refrain from sending any wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. China will continue to take forceful measures to resolutely safeguard China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We noted that the US government has recently sent out a series of wrong signals on the Taiwan question. What the US government should do is to follow through on President Biden’s remarks that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; it does not aim to change China’s system; the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; the US does not support “Taiwan independence”; and it has no intention to seek a conflict with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347293.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220531_10696664.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-05-31","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","According to reports, in response to Japan’s submission to the Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf on the extension of its continental shelf to the south of the Okinodori Reef, there have been many dissertations in China refuting the claim recently. Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Matsuno Hirokazu said at a press conference on May 30 that the Japanese government noted those science papers but would…","We have noted relevant reports. As is well known, Okinodori is a reef, not an island. It is submerged underwater except for less than ten square meters above water at high tide. However, Japan, in pursuit of self-interest, has illegally staked claim to nearly 700,000 square kilometers of jurisdictional waters based on the tiny reef. This encroaches upon the high seas and international seabed areas and undermines the overall interests of the international community. According to UNCLOS, Okinodori is a reef, not an island. As such, it is not entitled to an EEZ or continental shelf. Japan’s claim of an EEZ and continental shelf based on it violates international law.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347293.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202205/t20220531_10696664.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 31: US Senator Duckworth recently visited Taiwan. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 31st, saying: We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military collusion between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. Some members of the US Congress have repeatedly taken wrong actions on the Taiwan question that seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, tolerating and supporting \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. This is very dangerous! The DPP authorities' attempt to win over external anti-China forces to provoke with \"independence\" is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202205/t20220531_12440111.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-01","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","We noted yesterday that President Biden met with Prime Minister Jacinda Ardern of New Zealand and they issued a joint statement. They said “We are concerned with growing strategic competition in the Pacific region...we note with concern the security agreement between the People’s Republic of China and Solomon Islands. In particular, the United States and New Zealand share a concern that the establishment of a…","We noted the relevant contents of the joint statement, which distorts and smears China’s normal cooperation with Pacific Island countries (PICs), deliberately hypes up the South China Sea issue, makes irresponsible remarks on and grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs including issues related to Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong. China is firmly opposed to this.\nI would like to take some time to make a detailed response. China has repeatedly expounded its position on China-Solomon Islands security cooperation, stressing that such cooperation is conducive to peace, stability and development of Solomon Islands and the South Pacific and proceeds in parallel with existing regional arrangements. The security cooperation does not target any third party, nor does it intend to establish a military base. The hype-up of relevant issues in the joint statement by the US and New Zealand is out of ulterior motives to create disinformation and attack and discredit China. The US has military bases all over the world, yet it expresses concerns about normal security cooperation with other countries. Such act is hypocritical and reflects the US' deep-rooted hegemonic mentality. The real security threat is that the US has cobbled together military blocs in the region, stimulated an arms race and brought nuclear proliferation risks to the South Pacific.\nI want to stress that State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi recently visited South Pacific Island countries and co-chaired the second China-Pacific Island Countries Foreign Ministers’ Meeting with the Prime Minister and Foreign Minister of Fiji. State Councilor Wang put forward four principles on developing China’s relations with PICs, namely, equality, mutual respect, win-win cooperation, and openness and inclusiveness, which have been widely welcomed and recognized by PICs. This visit has achieved the expected goals of strengthening communication, enhancing mutual trust, building consensus, deepening friendship and expanding cooperation, and achieved positive results. PICs leaders spoke highly of China’s positive role in supporting their economic development, improving people’s livelihood and fighting the epidemic, and expressed high expectations for the future of China’s cooperation with PICs. China and PICs will continue to support and help each other, firmly uphold each other’s core interests and major concerns, constantly consolidate and develop their comprehensive strategic partnership, pursue common development and prosperity, and work together to build an even closer community with a shared future for China and PICs.\nI also want to stress that the issues relating to Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are purely China’s internal affairs, which brook no interference from any country or external force. There has never been any problem with the freedom of navigation in the South China Sea, and there should not be such problem in the future. China is firmly committed to safeguarding its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, as well as the international system with the UN at its core and the international order based on international law. We always maintain that the development of bilateral relations between countries should be conducive to world peace and stability and should not target or undermine the interests of any third party. At the same time, we are firmly opposed to drawing the ideological line and interfering in other countries’ internal affairs with erroneous words and deeds on issues concerning the sovereignty and security of a third country.\nChina urges the US to abandon its Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs and stop slandering and discrediting China. We hope New Zealand will adhere to its independent foreign policy and do more to enhance security and mutual trust among regional countries and safeguard regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347294.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220601_10697547.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-01","Zhao Lijian","TASS","You responded to US Congresswoman Duckworth’s visit to Taiwan at yesterday’s press conference. Will this issue threaten China’s security? If US officials keep sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and cross the red line, will conflicts be triggered across the Taiwan Strait?","I expounded on China’s solemn position on the US congresswoman’s visit to Taiwan yesterday. I want to stress that the fundamental reason for the current tension across the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities’ attempt to seek Taiwan’s independence by soliciting US support and some US individuals’ scheme to contain China with the Taiwan question. The US has recently made frequent moves on the Taiwan question in contradiction to its own statements. It encourages and supports \"Taiwan independence\" forces covertly or overtly. This will not only push Taiwan into a dangerous situation, but also cause grave consequences to the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347294.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220601_10697547.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-01","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","US Secretary of State Blinken characterized the Biden administration’s China strategy as “invest, align and compete” in his recent speech. Do you have any comment on this latest statement?","China believes that it’s a shared responsibility and obligation for China and the US to build a world of connectivity, diversity, inclusiveness, security and shared benefits. Whether China and the US can properly handle the relationship is a question of the century to which the two countries must provide a good answer. State Councilor Wang Yi and Foreign Ministry Spokespersons have responded to Secretary of State Blinken’s speech repeatedly. In response to the US’ three-point strategy to China, I’d like to stress the following points:\nFirst, we are glad to see the US achieve development through legitimate investment, but the US shouldn’t try to revitalize its sense of purpose as a nation by making China an imaginary enemy. How to improve the capability for innovation and competitiveness is the US’ own business. It’s ill-advised to make China an issue, still less use this as excuse to suppress and contain China, interfere in China’s internal affairs and harm China’s interests. China will undoubtedly rejects such things once they happen. Take the proposed bipartisan innovation legislation that is still under review as an example, it professes to increase the US’ competitiveness, but is aimed to make China an imaginary enemy, with the word “China” mentioned as many as more than 800 times and full of articles and provisions detrimental to China’s interests. China would firmly reject this.\nSecond, we do not interfere in the normal coordination and cooperation between the US and its allies, but such relations should not target or harm the interests of any third party, neither should they violate basic norms governing international relations. The US has put together an “anti-China” alliance. Be it the \"Indo-Pacific Strategy\", the Quad or AUKUS, these exclusive and closed cliques are products of the Cold War mentality and the tool of zero-sum game. This is historical back-peddling, which will escalate tensions and undermine solidarity and cooperation in the region. This runs counter to the shared aspiration of countries in the region to seek common development and regional integration through dialogue and cooperation. It garners no support and is doomed to fail.\nThird, we do not deny that there is competition between China and the US in the field of economy and trade. However, our relations cannot be defined by competition, nor should we pursue vicious zero-sum competition or engage in major power confrontation under the cover of competition. While talking about competition, the US has actually been stretching the national security concept and flagrantly resorting to illegal unilateral sanctions, long-arm jurisdiction, decoupling, and breakage of supply and industrial chains, which severely undermines Chinese companies’ legitimate rights and interests and wantonly deprives other countries of their right to development. This is not responsible competition, but rather unscrupulous suppression and containment. If the US insists on defining China-US relations by major power competition and pursuing “I-win-you-lose” policy objectives, it will only push the two countries to confrontation and conflict and lead the world to division and turmoil.\nThe US side’s recent China policy speech is just \"old wine in a new bottle\". The three-point strategy is merely a rehash of its previous “trichotomy” of competition, confrontation and cooperation. Essentially, it is about using all the internal and external resources of the US to encircle, suppress and contain China. As China-US relations stand at an important crossroads, the US must make the right choice. Instead of playing word-games, it should focus its efforts on the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, act on President Biden’s remarks that the US does not seek a new Cold War with China; it does not aim to change China’s system; the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China; the US does not support “Taiwan independence”; and it has no intention to seek a conflict with China. The US need to work with China toward the same direction to find the right way of interaction between the two major countries in the new era and deliver more benefits to the people in both countries and the rest of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347294.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220601_10697547.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-02","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The US and Taiwan launched talks aimed at deepening trade relations yesterday. Do you have any comment?","China firmly opposes all forms of official interaction with the Taiwan region by countries having diplomatic ties with China, including negotiating or concluding agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature. Lately the US has made frequent moves and kept devising schemes on Taiwan. They are nothing but attempts to breach the one-China principle, bolster “Taiwan independence” separatists and disrupt peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a consensus of the international community and a solemn commitment made by the US in the three China-US joint communiqués. If the US insists on playing the Taiwan card, it will only lead China-US relations to a dangerous situation. The US must abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop negotiating agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature, and refrain from sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We would also like to make it clear to the DPP authorities that they need to give up at once on the idea that they could seek independence with US support, because the more ambitious they are, the bitterer their failure will be.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347295.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220602_10698108.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-02","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","US Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin said in an interview with Japanese media before his upcoming trip to Asia that the US’ concern over the Ukraine crisis “won’t distract us from facing the challenges to a free, stable and secure Indo-Pacific region”. He also indicated that Washington is willing to expand arms aid and military training for Taiwan. Does China have any response?","We have always firmly opposed US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region, which gravely infringes on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and interferes in China’s domestic affairs. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués and stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan.\nIf the US truly wants “a free, stable and secure Indo-Pacific region”, then it should stop the erroneous practice of ganging up and stoking political antagonism and military confrontation in the region, and play a constructive role in enhancing mutual trust and cooperation among regional countries.\n***\nIn observance of the Dragon Boat Festival, the MFA regular press conference will be adjourned on June 3 (Friday), and resumed on June 6 (Monday). During the recess, you can reach the Spokesperson’s Office by fax, email or WeChat.\nOn Dragon Boat Festivals, we Chinese people eat Zongzi (sticky rice dumpling wrapped in bamboo leaves) and race dragon boats. We also hang calamus and mugwort on doors to deter insects, drive away evil spirits and diseases, and bring good health. In a sense, the Dragon Boat Festival is the oldest health and epidemic awareness day in China. Tomorrow will be this special day. I hope the festival will bring you happiness and auspiciousness. Have a good Dragon Boat Festival!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347295.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220602_10698108.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-06-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 2 dispatch. In response to the DPP authorities’ announcement on the 1st that they would jointly launch with the United States the so-called “U.S.-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative,” Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office (TAO), said in response to a question on the 2nd that the DPP authorities, in pursuit of their own political self-interest for “independence,” are willing to sacrifice the interests of enterprises and people on the island by colluding with external forces. We firmly oppose the United States concluding with Taiwan region of China any agreement that has sovereign implications or official nature. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués in practice. Attempting to play the “Taiwan card” to block China’s reunification and national rejuvenation will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220602_12440822.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-06","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","The US State Department again updated the US-Taiwan Relations Fact Sheet on its website on May 28, putting back the statement that “we do not support Taiwan independence”, which was deleted previously. Do you have any comment? My second question is, it is reported that Sheila Carey, Consul and Head of the Economic / Political Section of the US Consulate General in Guangzhou and Andrew Chira, told guests at a…","On your first question, we have noted that the US State Department has once again updated the US-Taiwan Relations Fact Sheet on its website and put back the statement that “we do not support Taiwan independence”. Facts are not to be denied. History shall not be falsified. Truth must not be distorted. There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The PRC government is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a shared consensus of the international community and an established norm of international relations. It is also a solemn commitment made by the US to China in the three China-US joint communiqués. The US needs to abide by the one-China principle, the provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués, and its political commitment to China on the Taiwan question, and act on President Biden’s statement that the US does not support “Taiwan independence”. It needs to stop using Taiwan-related issues to engage in political manipulation or to contain China. Otherwise, it could cause further damage to China-US relations and to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nI suggest you raise the second question to the US side too and ask them for an explanation. But I won’t be surprised if what you mentioned is true, because this is not the first time US officials spoke their true mind. Back in 2018, former senior US official Lawrence Wilkerson was quite frank about it when he said the US “would want to destabilize China” and “the best way to do so” would be to “foment unrest and to join with those Uyghurs in pushing the Han Chinese in Beijing from internal places rather than external”. Sibel Edmonds, a former FBI translator, revealed in 2015 that the US never cared about people in Xinjiang and the US claimed that minorities in Xinjiang were gunned down and tortured only to get the US’ objective of destabilizing Xinjiang.\nMike Pompeo once said, “We lied, we cheated, we stole ... It reminds you of the glory of the American experiment.” “Genocide in Xinjiang” is the lie of the century concocted by US politicians and a classic work of US “lying diplomacy”.\nThe ethnic unity, social stability and economic prosperity that Xinjiang enjoys is the best rebuttal of the US lies. The US attempt to undermine harmony and stability in Xinjiang and contain China’s development will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347296.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220606_10699238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-06","Zhao Lijian","TASS","According to foreign media reports, Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov was forced to cancel a visit to Serbia on June 6 and 7 after Bulgaria, North Macedonia and Montenegro prevented his plane from passing through their airspace. What is the foreign ministry’s comment on this? Lately the Taiwan region announced a ban on exporting semiconductors to Russia, which took corresponding measures to ban exports of…","On your first question, we have also noted relevant reports. China supports Russia and Ukraine in continuing to engage in negotiation and consultation to properly resolve relevant issues. We believe that all efforts that are conducive to the peaceful settlement of the crisis should be supported and that the international community should create favorable conditions for negotiations between Russia and Ukraine.\nOn your second question, since the start of the Ukraine crisis, the DPP authorities have been exploiting and latching onto the issue at every chance possible for grandstanding. They are hyping tensions with the hidden agenda of seeking “independence” and provocation in collusion with external forces. Their despicable tricks will only prove futile.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347296.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220606_10699238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-06-07","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Reportedly, the militaries of China and the United Kingdom, and China and France, recently held defense strategic consultations by video, exchanging views in depth on military relations and issues of common concern. Please further introduce the outcomes of these China-UK and China-France defense strategic consultations, and what expectations China has for the development of China-Europe defense and security…","The Chinese and British militaries, and the Chinese and French militaries, held defense strategy consultations by video on January 12 and 13, respectively. These consultations are important institutional exchange programs between the Chinese military and the militaries of the United Kingdom and France. During these consultations, the Chinese side and representatives of the defense departments of the United Kingdom and France conducted in-depth exchanges of views on issues of common concern, including military exchanges and cooperation, the regional security situation, and national defense and military development. All sides agreed that the Chinese and British militaries, as well as the Chinese and French militaries, should strengthen strategic communication and institutional exchanges, carry out cooperation in multiple fields, enhance mutual understanding, deepen trust, and appropriately handle differences, making a positive contribution to the healthy and stable development of military-to-military relations between the two countries. At the same time, the Chinese side set out its position and expressed concerns on issues such as Taiwan and the South China Sea, calling on all parties to abide by the one-China principle, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness, and respect and support the efforts of regional countries to maintain peace and stability in the South China Sea.\nRegarding China-EU military relations, China has always attached importance to military exchanges and cooperation with European countries, and hopes that the defense departments of China and the EU will continually strengthen communication and coordination in all fields, jointly uphold genuine multilateralism, and jointly safeguard regional peace and stability.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/06-07/9773617.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-06-09","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","Firstly, Taiwan today awarded a medal to a French lawmaker. Do you have any comment? Secondly, the US has announced a new round of arms sales to Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","Let me start with your first question. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes all forms of official and political interactions with the Taiwan region by countries having diplomatic ties with China. We urge relevant sides to abide by the one-China principle, avoid sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and take concrete actions to maintain the sound and steady development of bilateral relations.\nOn your second question, US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this.\nThe US should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, revoke the arms sales plan, and stop arms sales to and military ties with Taiwan. China will continue to take resolute and strong measures to firmly defend its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347299.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220609_10700965.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-06-09","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the U.S. Navy recently announced with fanfare that a strategic nuclear submarine had docked at Guam, and several carrier strike groups have gathered around China's periphery and conducted exercises. There are signs that the United States may continue to hold military exercises with its allies around China's periphery before, around, or during the Beijing Winter Olympics. Also, according to U.S. media…","The Beijing Winter Olympics is a sporting event of the international community. When friends come, there is good wine. The Chinese side will serve well as host and, together with all parties, strive to hold a simple, safe, and splendid Winter Olympics. But it must be pointed out that the Chinese military is fully prepared for external provocations and emergencies.\nRegarding the US side’s admission that the “Mustin” conducted close-in reconnaissance deliberately, the Chinese side is not surprised, as this is simply the fact. As early as last April, the Chinese military, on the basis of on-site handling, had already issued strong refutation and serious representations on this matter. But shockingly, the US side not only feels no shame about this military provocation, but even takes pride in it. This hegemonic syndrome and cognitive disorder have indeed reached the point where they need to be seriously treated.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/06-09/9776181.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-06-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 9 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 9th that the “1992 Consensus” must not be arbitrarily distorted. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and cross-Strait relations are becoming increasingly tense. We hope that any political party, group, or individual on the island committed to developing…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that the Communist Party of China is a party whose original aspiration and mission is to work for the well-being of the Chinese people and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Having traveled a glorious path of one hundred years, it has achieved great accomplishments that are recorded in history and universally recognized. The Chinese nation has ushered in a great leap from standing up, to becoming prosperous, to becoming strong, and is marching with high spirits toward the second centenary goal of building a modern socialist country in all respects. The people and history have already made a correct judgment.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the “1992 Consensus” refers to the consensus reached in 1992 by the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan through the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, in which each side orally expressed that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” The exchanges of letters and telegrams between the two sides clearly expressed the position and attitude of upholding the one-China principle and pursuing national reunification. It is black and white, clear as day. On the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides across the Strait launched consultations and negotiations, opened the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang also carried out exchanges and cooperation, making contributions to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220609_12442606.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 9 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 9th that we firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China. The U.S. arms sales seriously violate the One-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the August 17 Communiqué. They are an indulgence and support of “Taiwan independence” forces and a serious violation of the U.S. commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.” We urge the U.S. side to put its “four noes and one no intention” position into practice, immediately correct its mistake, cancel the plan to sell arms to Taiwan, and stop playing with fire on Taiwan-related issues.\nA reporter asked: On June 8, a U.S. government department decided to sell to the Taiwan region of China a warship spare parts project valued at about 120 million U.S. dollars. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above statement when answering the question.\nHe pointed out that the DPP authorities' attempt to buy weapons to “use arms to resist reunification” will only further harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots and push them into a fire pit. We warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop their conduct of colluding with external forces to advance “Taiwan independence” and provoke confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220609_12442768.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-06-10","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest does not say whether this was a question or an a","Recently, the “Reform Moment” column program aired on the National Defense and Military Channel of China Media Group. The program focuses on reform of military policies and systems and vividly showcases the new changes, new atmosphere and new look of the People’s Liberation Army after its reform and restructuring. Please further introduce the progress of reform in military policies and systems.","Since the military policy and institutional reform and deployment was implemented, under the centralized and unified leadership of the Party Central Committee and the Central Military Commission, and under the overall guidance of the Central Military Commission's Leading Group for Deepening Reform of National Defense and the Armed Forces, relevant departments of the Central Military Commission's organs have fully demonstrated, concentrated their efforts on key problems, and successively issued a series of policies and regulations, providing strong legal safeguards for the modernization of national defense and the armed forces.\nAt present, the Regulations on Party Building in the Armed Forces have been promulgated and implemented, and the Regulations on Political Work, the Regulations on the Work of Discipline Inspection Commissions, and the Regulations on Political and Legal Work in the Armed Forces have been formulated, with supporting systems issued. The system for Party building in the armed forces has become more systematic and complete. The National Defense Law, the Military Service Law, the Law on the Protection of Military Facilities, and the People's Armed Police Law have been revised and implemented, and the Law on the Status and Rights and Interests of Servicemen and the Coast Guard Law have been formulated and issued, providing a firmer legal foundation for military activities. Focusing on preparing for combat, policies and regulations in areas such as joint operations, combat readiness, military training, logistics and equipment, military scientific research, and national defense mobilization have been improved, effectively promoting the generation and release of combat capability in the troops. The policy system for active-duty officer management has been implemented as a package, and the military merit and honor commendation system has been successively issued, along with reform measures that officers and soldiers have long anticipated, such as preferential treatment for children's education, medical care and recuperation, and employment for military family members who accompany servicemembers. The sense of professional honor and gain among servicemembers has been further enhanced.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/06-10/9777154.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-06-13","Wang Wenbin","TASS","According to reports, US Secretary of Defense said in Singapore last Saturday that the US will abide by the one-China policy and the US does not support Taiwan independence. Do these remarks signal positive changes on the Taiwan question lately? Or does China think the US still falls short of real actions?","We noticed that the US Secretary of Defense Lloyd J. Austin said in his remarks at the Shangri-La Dialogue that China has adopted a more coercive and aggressive approach to its territorial claims in the East China Sea and the South China Sea, and the stakes are especially stark in the Taiwan Strait. He also said that the US remains committed to its one-China policy. The Chinese delegation attending the event has responded to Secretary Austin’s remarks. I would like to stress that by repeatedly spreading disinformation and painting an ugly picture of China, the US could only further expose its ill intention to sow discord and the true nature of its hegemonic practices and exercise of power politics.\nThe biggest threat to the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait does not come from elsewhere but the obdurate separatist activities of the “Taiwan independence” forces and the US’s connivance and endorsement of such activities. It is the US that has sought to obscure and hollow out the one-Chine principle and kept backpedaling on its commitments. It is the US that is relaxing restrictions on official interactions between the US and Taiwan and increasing the sales of weapons to Taiwan both in qualitative and quantitative terms. It is still the US that has been helping Taiwan expand the so-called international space and even acting openly to support Taiwan in “strengthening” its so-called “diplomatic relationships”. What could possibly be the US’s aim for these actions other than to send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces and undermine cross-Strait peace and stability?\nThe US is also the biggest factor fueling militarization in the Asia-Pacific. The US has deployed many military aircraft and warships in the South China Sea on a regular basis and its reconnaissance aircraft have electronically impersonated the civil aircraft of other countries there many times. Not long ago, a US nuclear-powered submarine even hit an “uncharted seamount” in the South China Sea. According to statistics from institutions with professional knowledge, the number of the US’s close-in military reconnaissance missions against China has more than doubled compared with a decade ago. Since the beginning of this year, the US naval ships have transited the Taiwan Strait once a month on average. US military aircraft have engaged in large-scope, frequent and provocative close-in reconnaissance to deter and pressure China. Apparently, “militarization” and “endangering freedom of navigation” are more accurate when used to describe the behavior of the US.\nThe international community will not be deceived by the US’s remarks to smear China. What the US has said will only chip away at the US’s credibility. We urge the US to match its words with action, including not seeking confrontation or conflict, not seeking a new Cold War, and not seeking an Asian NATO or a region split into hostile blocs. We also urge the US to stop saying or doing things that could create division and confrontation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347301.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220613_10702387.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-13","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","We reported that Chinese military officials have repeatedly asserted that the Taiwan Strait is not international waters in recent months during meetings with US counterparts. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan Strait ranges in width from about 70 nautical miles at its narrowest and 220 nautical miles at its widest. According to UNCLOS and Chinese laws, the waters of the Taiwan Strait, extending from both shores toward the middle of the Strait, are divided into several zones including internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone, and the Exclusive Economic Zone. China has sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. At the same time, it respects the lawful rights of other countries in relevant waters.\nThere is no legal basis of “international waters” in the international law of the sea. It is a false claim when certain countries call the Taiwan Strait “international waters” in order to find a pretext for manipulating issues related to Taiwan and threatening China’s sovereignty and security. China is firmly against this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347301.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220613_10702387.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-13","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","It is reported that Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelenskyy attended the Shangri-La Dialogue via video link on June 11. When asked how Taiwan should respond if China seeks to take it, by force if necessary, Zelenskyy said that today’s example of Ukraine is an example for the whole world; no one benefits from war; if there is a way out diplomatically, we need to use the diplomatic way, but it must be a pre-emptive…","We have noted that President Zelenskyy didn’t mention the Taiwan question when answering the question. As some media pointed out, some people are simply raising the question about Taiwan in order to try to put words in President Zelenskyy’s mouth. The Taiwan question and the Ukraine issue are fundamentally different in nature. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. We will take strong measures to respond to all “Taiwan independence” attempts aimed at splitting China in order to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347301.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220613_10702387.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-13","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","The Japanese Defense Minister had talks with State Councilor and Defense Minister Wei Fenghe yesterday in Singapore. The Japanese side expressed concerns over China’s military activities surrounding Japan. What is China’s comment?","I would also refer you to the Chinese Ministry of National Defense for the meeting between Chinese and Japanese defense ministers.\nI want to stress that China’s position on the Taiwan question and the issue of Diaoyu Dao is consistent and clear. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliating islands have been part of China’s territory since ancient times. Whatever the Japanese side says or does cannot change the fact that Diaoyu Dao is part of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Japan bears historical guilt to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. Japan needs to act and speak with extra prudence, refrain from meddling in the cross-Strait situation in any way, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces in any form. The Japanese side needs to do more things that would enhance mutual trust among regional countries and promote regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347301.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220613_10702387.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-15","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Officials in Taiwan have complained to organizers of the 2022 Qatar World Cup about the fact that football fans for the World Cup currently have to select an option saying that they are part of Taiwan as a province of China. And there’s no option for Taiwan being a separate option when they buy their tickets. And they have asked the Qatar World Cup organizers to rectify this. Does the Chinese foreign ministry…","I am not aware of what you mentioned. I would like to reiterate that Taiwan is part of China and adhering to the one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and shared consensus of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347303.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220615_10703737.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on June 15, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, media friends. I am glad to take questions from you now.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Under the current complex and severe cross-strait situation, it is even more valuable for Taiwan compatriots to publicly support the reunification of the motherland. The second “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” was recently held in Beijing. Please introduce the outcomes of this event.","With strong support from the Beijing Municipal Party Committee and Municipal Government, the second “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams” event, despite the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic, was successfully held in Beijing from June 7 to 8. On June 9, Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, met with representatives of Taiwan guests attending the event. On behalf of the CPC Central Committee and General Secretary Xi Jinping, he congratulated the successful holding of the event. He stressed that national reunification is the historical trend, that no force can stop the resolute advance of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and he hoped that Taiwan compatriots will always stand on the right side of history, clearly oppose “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces, and work together for the historic cause of advancing national reunification and realizing national rejuvenation.\nMore than 120 people attended the event, either in person or online, including Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang and chairperson of the China Youth Peace Education Foundation; leaders and representatives of 27 Taiwan political parties and groups; Taiwan compatriot and Taiwan youth representatives; and personnel from relevant mainland circles. Centered on the theme “Historical Juncture and the Great Rejuvenation of the Chinese Nation,” they held exchanges and discussions on three sub-topics: “The New Era and National Reunification,” “The New Journey and Cross-Strait Integration,” and “The New Vision and Youth Pursuing Dreams.” They reached eight points of consensus, including “Hand in hand to realize the great dream of national rejuvenation, cherish and defend the ‘1992 Consensus,’ resolutely oppose ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist acts, resolutely oppose interference by external forces, deepen the practice of cross-Strait integrated development, strengthen the shared historical memory across the Strait, explore ways of governing Taiwan after reunification, and shoulder the youth's responsibility for national rejuvenation.”\nThis event profoundly grasped the historical juncture of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, thoroughly explored the proposition of national reunification in the new era, demonstrated the strong will of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to oppose “independence” and promote reunification, put forward insightful views on advancing cross-Strait relations toward closer, more friendly and better ties, envisioned a bright future for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and expressed the strong desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly realize the Chinese Dream. It achieved positive results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444612.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Commemorative events marking the 360th anniversary of Zheng Chenggong's recovery of Taiwan were held in Fujian yesterday (June 14). Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant details?","Zheng Chenggong is a great national hero revered by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Three hundred and sixty years ago, he led his troops to drive out the Dutch colonialists and recover the treasured island of Taiwan, making major contributions to upholding the dignity and interests of the Chinese nation, defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and developing and building Taiwan. To commemorate Zheng Chenggong's historic merit in restoring the territory and establishing Taiwan, and to carry forward the spirit of patriotism, the Conference Commemorating the 360th Anniversary of Zheng Chenggong's Recovery of Taiwan was grandly held on the morning of June 14 in Nan'an City, Quanzhou, Fujian, the hometown of Zheng Chenggong. More than 500 representatives from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait attended, either offline at the main venue in Nan'an City or online at the branch venue in Chiayi County, Taiwan. The commemorative conference was co-hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the People's Government of Fujian Province, with relevant civil organizations on the island and 14 units, including Zheng Chenggong temples and Zheng clan associations, participating as co-organizers. Liu Jieyi, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Yin Li, Party Secretary of Fujian Province; Zeng Yongquan, former Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang; Wu Rongyuan, Chairman of the Taiwan Labor Party; and Zheng clan representatives from both sides, experts and scholars, and representatives of the temples enshrining Zheng Chenggong delivered speeches and remarks at the conference.\nAfter the conference, a civilian visit to the Zheng Chenggong Mausoleum, jointly organized by 26 civil institutions from both sides of the Strait, was held simultaneously in Nan'an City and Chiayi County. Long Mingbiao, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Luo Dongchuan, Deputy Secretary of the Fujian Provincial Party Committee; and about 600 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait attended.\nThrough commemorating the historic feat of Zheng Chenggong's recovery of Taiwan, this event fully demonstrated the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to carry forward patriotism, oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" and work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the epidemic in multiple mainland localities has had some impact on Taiwan businesses and enterprises. The State Council recently launched a package of policy measures to firmly stabilize the economy and required all localities and departments to promote their implementation quickly. What measures have been mainly adopted recently to stabilize Taiwan businesses and enterprises and help them develop?…","Recently, the State Council issued the 'Package of Policy Measures to Solidly Stabilize the Economy,' which introduces 33 measures in six areas: finance, monetary and financial affairs, stabilizing investment and boosting consumption, ensuring food and energy security, ensuring the stability of industrial and supply chains, and safeguarding basic livelihoods. Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises that meet the conditions are equally eligible and will benefit. Beijing, Tianjin, Heilongjiang, Shanghai, Zhejiang, Anhui, Fujian, Hunan, Guangdong, Guizhou and other provinces and municipalities promptly issued implementation plans, formulating supporting detailed rules and specific operating measures in light of local conditions. In addition, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises recently compiled and distributed the 'Major Enterprise-Support Policies Issued by the State Council and Relevant Departments in Recent Years' to its members and local Taiwan business associations, to help Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises know and enjoy all policies and measures for supporting enterprises and relieving difficulties.\nWe introduced at the press conference some specific examples of how certain provinces and municipalities helped Taiwan-invested enterprises with VAT credit refunds and other matters to relieve their difficulties and stabilize production. Here I would like to give some more examples of local assistance for the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises. The Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office optimized services for enterprises, provided precise matching on a one-enterprise-one-policy basis, worked with relevant departments to resolve new problems that Taiwan-invested enterprises encountered in resuming work and production, and provided diversified financial support in a timely manner. Since June, the rate of resumption of work and production by Taiwan-invested industrial enterprises in Shanghai has exceeded 90%, and that of commercial enterprises has exceeded 70%. The Anhui Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office actively coordinated with relevant parties to build a bank-enterprise cooperation platform to provide financial services to Taiwan-invested enterprises and help them overcome difficulties. At present, it has coordinated with financial institutions such as the Hefei branch of the Industrial Bank to provide financial loans totaling about 2.6 billion yuan to 43 Taiwan-invested enterprises. After the epidemic eased, Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province quickly pushed for all 644 above-scale Taiwan-invested industrial enterprises in the city to resume work, giving a 'boost' to the resumption of work and production by local Taiwan-invested enterprises. At present, production capacity has returned to normal levels.\nDoing practical things, doing good deeds, and solving difficult problems for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises is our consistent policy. We will thoroughly implement the relevant decisions and arrangements of the State Council, guide Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities to work with relevant parties to provide greater support and better services to Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises, help them overcome difficulties, and develop steadily, advancing steadily and going far.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444607.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","An important path for Taiwan youth to study and pursue development on the mainland is to take part in the national unified entrance examination for Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and overseas Chinese, and the separate admission examinations of Jinan University and Huaqiao University. This year, due to the epidemic, the route for Taiwan examinees in many places to travel to take the exams has been affected to some…","The 2022 Joint Entrance Examination for Students from Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan and Overseas Chinese, along with the autonomous enrollment examinations of Jinan University and Huaqiao University, were successfully concluded in mid-to-late May. This year, more than 1,000 Taiwanese students took the joint entrance examination. Under the epidemic situation, the examinations were able to proceed as scheduled and candidates were able to complete them smoothly, which required tremendous efforts from relevant parties, and many heartwarming examples emerged. I can give everyone a brief introduction here.\nBecause of the epidemic in the Shanghai area, out of responsibility for the health and safety of candidates, the education authorities decided in April to make appropriate adjustments to the examination arrangements at the Shanghai examination site for the joint entrance examination. Shanghai candidates continued to take the examination locally, while non-local candidates who had chosen the Shanghai examination site had to choose another examination site in a different city. This adjustment involved more than 200 Taiwanese candidates, most of whom were from Jiangsu, and they were sent to Guangzhou, Fuzhou, and other places to take the examination. To fully ensure that Taiwanese candidates could take the examination, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council promptly coordinated with the relevant localities to take swift action and make proper arrangements. The Taiwan Affairs Offices of Shanghai, Jiangsu, Guangdong, Fujian, and other provinces and municipalities, together with local epidemic prevention and control, airport, hotel, examination venue, and other relevant departments and key points, separately refined work procedures and strengthened work coordination, providing assistance and convenience to Taiwanese students to the greatest extent possible. The Taiwan Affairs Offices of Shenzhen and Guangzhou set up special working groups for this purpose, providing convenient services in flight rescheduling, on-arrival nucleic acid testing, dedicated car transfers, and epidemic prevention guidance, distributing warm gift packages, and establishing a closed-loop transfer across the entire chain to help candidates prepare for the exam safely and with peace of mind. Xiamen and Fuzhou actively carried out coordination work. Jimei District in Xiamen, where Huaqiao University is located, specially formulated an epidemic prevention and control plan for Taiwanese students from Kunshan coming to Xiamen to take the exam, ensuring that the 28 Taiwanese students were connected smoothly at every stage after arriving in Xiamen.\nAfter the Taiwanese candidates successfully took the examination, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises and the Kunshan Taiwan Association sent letters of thanks. Many Taiwanese students, parents, and teachers expressed deep gratitude to the relevant departments for opening a “green channel” and providing relay-style escort support. One Taiwanese student's parent said, “The changes to the examination venue and the difficulties in travel caused by the epidemic left us very anxious, but we were treated so thoughtfully along the way, and we were deeply moved. Not only did they help our child, but they also warmed the hearts of us parents.”\nHere, we wish all Taiwanese students success in getting into their desired universities and realizing their life goals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444605.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We note that recently some Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan compatriot groups and Taiwan compatriot families have been awarded honorary titles such as the Provincial May Fourth Youth Medal and the National Five-Good Family, becoming highlights of Taiwan compatriots developing on the mainland. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Around this year's May Fourth Youth Day, various localities commended a group of outstanding young individuals and collectives. We are pleased to see that nine Taiwan youths, including Lin Shuren, deputy general manager of Sichuan Liangshan Prefecture's Mianning Yuansheng Agricultural Technology Co., Ltd. (one of whom received a nomination award), were awarded the Provincial Youth May Fourth Medal, and five teams led by Taiwan youths, including the Xiamen Haicang District Strait Urban-Rural Development Foundation, received the collective honorary title of Provincial Youth May Fourth Medal. These Taiwan youths and teams are in various roles: some are at the forefront of economic and technological development, some devote themselves to the front lines of epidemic prevention and control, some take root at the grassroots to help rural revitalization, some cultivate the teaching podium, and some dedicate themselves to public welfare. They have made outstanding contributions in their respective posts across different industries, and the commendations are well deserved.\nOn May 15, the All-China Women's Federation commended the 13th National Five-Good Families and Family Work Advanced Collectives and Individuals, and announced the 2022 National Most Beautiful Families. Five Taiwan compatriot families won the National Five-Good Family honor, from Shanghai, Guangxi, Yunnan, Shaanxi and Gansu respectively. The common characteristics of these families are loving the country and the family, caring for one another, and striving upward and toward goodness, and they have set an example in passing down fine family traditions and promoting new civilized customs. This is the second national honor for Taiwan compatriot families, following the national Women's Day Red Banner title awarded to two Taiwan compatriots in March this year, which fully shows that the spiritual outlook and social contributions of Taiwan compatriot women on the mainland have been fully recognized by all sectors of society.\nIn recent years, more and more Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, have broken through obstacles and overcome various difficulties to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams, painting a beautiful picture of cross-strait integrated development. The good image of the commended Taiwan compatriots is a highlight among them. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to come to the mainland to develop their careers and create achievements, to become participants in and promoters of the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations, and to jointly plan development, share glory, and create the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444604.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Remarks by Chu Li-luan, Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, during his recent visit to the United States, which touched on Taiwan-US relations and cross-Strait relations, have been interpreted in different ways on the island. What is the spokesperson's overall comment on his remarks? Will this affect future exchanges and cooperation between the mainland side and the KMT?","TAO spokesperson already stated our position on the 9th regarding the relevant issue. Our stance is clear and consistent: on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” there are no obstacles to exchanges between us and any political party or group in Taiwan. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The DPP authorities are intensifying their scheming for “independence” and provocations, and external forces are increasing efforts to play the “Taiwan card,” seriously threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harming the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that all parties, groups and individuals on the island who are committed to developing cross-Strait relations and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will always stand on the right side of history, join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and defend the national interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444606.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Wei Fenghe, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense, recently emphasized at the Shangri-La Dialogue that if anyone dares to split Taiwan away, we will “spare no cost in fighting, spare no price, and will certainly fight to the end.” The head of Taiwan's MAC claimed this is “a declaration of war that disdains the principle of peace in international relations.” What comment do you have on this?","The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities distort the nature of the Taiwan question, smear the mainland's policy toward Taiwan, and once again expose their vicious intention to hype the so-called mainland “military threat” and to attempt to “internationalize” the Taiwan question. Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and the Taiwan question is a problem left over from China's civil war. The way the Taiwan question is resolved is an internal Chinese affair. Achieving the complete reunification of the country is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. All necessary measures taken in response to the provocations and coercion by “Taiwan independence” forces are just actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to thwart separatist schemes. Where does the so-called “declaration of war” come from?\nAs everyone knows, since the DPP authorities came to power, they have denied the “1992 Consensus,” manipulated the “two-state theory,” and attempted to change the status quo in which both sides belong to one China, and single-handedly closed the door to cross-Strait negotiations. The tension and severity of current cross-Strait relations are rooted in the DPP authorities' constant provocations to seek “independence” in collusion with external forces, and in some countries' attempts to “use Taiwan to contain China” and obstruct China's development and reunification. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never allow Taiwan to be split away from China. Minister of National Defense and State Councilor Wei Fenghe has already expressed our solemn position on the Taiwan question at the 19th Shangri-La Dialogue; his words were forceful and the signal clear. If the DPP authorities continue to misjudge the situation, stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, indulge in the illusion of “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” and “seeking independence by force,” and take risks on the road of “Taiwan independence,” crossing the red line, we will certainly take resolute measures to crush it decisively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444608.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","The General Administration of Customs announced that from June 13 it will suspend exports of Taiwan grouper to the mainland, which has drawn high attention on the island. Please explain the relevant situation.","Since last year, mainland customs have repeatedly detected oxytetracycline exceeding the standard in grouper imported from Taiwan, and have also detected the banned drugs malachite green and crystal violet in two batches of grouper. Malachite green and crystal violet are drugs banned on both sides of the Strait; they can persist in fish and the environment for a long time and pose risks of mutagenicity, teratogenicity, and carcinogenicity to humans. Oxytetracycline residues exceeding the standard in fish also harm the health of consumers. Recently, mainland customs have continued to detect the banned drug crystal violet in grouper imported from Taiwan into the mainland, indicating that the drug safety management system for grouper aquaculture in Taiwan has serious problems.\nFood safety concerns the health and lives of the broad masses, and the mainland has always attached great importance to it. To guard against risks and protect the health and safety of mainland consumers, in accordance with relevant laws, regulations and standards, the General Administration of Customs has decided to suspend the export of Taiwan grouper to the mainland starting June 13. This is a normal safety precaution, scientifically reasonable and entirely justified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444610.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","The DPP authorities accused the mainland of suspending imports of Taiwan grouper as “suppression” of Taiwan, claimed it “has political purposes” and “unilaterally harms cross-strait relations,” and called on the mainland to respond to the evidence provided by Taiwan and resolve the issue through cross-strait consultations. What comments do you have on this?","Since last year, the mainland side has repeatedly notified relevant Taiwan authorities of multiple batches of grouper containing drugs that did not meet standards, and has demanded that they improve their aquatic animal safety management system. The Taiwan side has never provided any so-called evidence of rectification, and recently, there have been successive cases of banned drugs being detected in groupers exported to the mainland. In order to protect consumers’ health and safety, the mainland side has had no choice but to suspend imports of Taiwan grouper.\nThis is a normal issue of aquatic animal safety and hygiene management, but the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not consider the vital interests of fishermen on the island, do not genuinely fulfill their regulatory responsibilities, and do not reflect on their own problems. Instead, they once again use this as an opportunity for political manipulation, politicize necessary safety precautions, complicate a purely technical problem, maliciously smear the mainland, create antagonism across the Strait, and attempt to extend the malicious political hype on the island to the World Trade Organization. We must ask in return: Is selling agricultural and fishery products containing banned drugs and drugs in excessive amounts to the mainland what they call “normal trade”? When problems arise, instead of trying to solve them, they keep politically smearing and blaming the mainland, misleading the public, sowing discord, and escalating antagonism. Does this not count as “one-sidedly harming cross-Strait relations”?\nThe actions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities create obstacles to the normal resolution of the problem and undermine the proper channels for solving it. This precisely shows that they have no real intention of solving the problem. Once again, they have put their own political self-interest above the interests of fishermen on the island, showing not the slightest intention to consider the interests of Taiwan’s fishermen.\nChina Media Group","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444609.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, the General Administration of Customs announced publicly that, because SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid positives were detected in the outer packaging samples of chilled aquatic products imported into the mainland from the Taiwan region, emergency precautionary measures were taken against the producing enterprises. Please explain the relevant situation.","Because the outer packaging samples of chilled aquatic products imported into the mainland from Taiwan tested positive for COVID-19 viral nucleic acid, in accordance with the provisions of General Administration of Customs Announcement No. 103 of 2020, customs suspended acceptance of import declarations from the relevant enterprises for one week starting June 10. Customs will increase nucleic acid testing for COVID-19 on cold-chain products imported from Taiwan and their outer packaging, strictly guard against the risk of importing COVID-19, and effectively protect public health and safety.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","First question: Yu Xikun, head of Taiwan's legislature, recently claimed that the “Yunfeng missile” developed in Taiwan can hit Beijing. What is your comment on this? Second question: The mainland recently stated that the Taiwan Strait is not “international waters.” The DPP authorities denied this, saying, “the Taiwan Strait is international waters.” What is your comment on this?","First question: There is an old Chinese saying: “When Heaven intends to destroy someone, it first drives them mad.” The wild talk of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements such as Yu Xikun (游锡堃) once again exposes the essence of their depravity. If they dare to “strike a stone with an egg,” they will surely hasten their own destruction.\nSecond question: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed our position on behalf of the Central People's Government of China. The DPP authorities' cooperation with external forces to hype this issue is entirely based on the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. It harms the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and sells out the interests of the Chinese nation, which is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","As Taiwan is expected to relax its border epidemic prevention measures, outsiders are concerned about whether cross-Strait air routes and passenger flight points can be resumed at that time. The Mainland Affairs Council stated that it attaches great importance to this issue and is currently conducting a “comprehensive assessment.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities have repeatedly said they will 'evaluate,' but 'they only hear footsteps on the stairs and never see anyone come down.' Since cross-strait direct flights were implemented, the mainland has consistently taken active measures to safeguard and facilitate direct travel between compatriots on both sides. It should be pointed out that from February 2020 to the present, the DPP authorities, using epidemic prevention as a pretext, have unilaterally suspended cross-strait air passenger flights other than those to and from the four cities of Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, and Chengdu. This is detrimental to cross-strait personnel exchanges and to economic, trade, and cooperation. As for resuming flights to the other points, the mainland side has no obstacles. The DPP authorities should readily accept good advice and respond to the needs of enterprises and the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: Taiwan scholar Zhang Yazhong and Lü Xiulian have both recently proposed replacing “cross-Strait unification” with “cross-Strait integration.” How does the spokesperson view this claim? Second question: Starting from the 15th of this month, the Taiwan region has implemented the new “3+4” regulation on home quarantine upon entry, shortening the quarantine period after arrival. Will the mainland also…","The first question: Developing cross-Strait relations and achieving national reunification must be based on the legal principles and realities of cross-Strait relations. This legal principle and reality is that although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and must not be divided. Peaceful reunification best serves the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together, resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of the motherland's reunification.\nThe second question: We do not comment on the island's epidemic prevention policies. We have noted that since April this year, the COVID-19 epidemic in the Taiwan region has spread rapidly, the number of newly confirmed cases has increased rapidly, the daily number of new cases once exceeded 90,000, and the daily number of deaths reached 213. Recently, figures from all walks of life on the island have also been \"infected\" one after another. It can be said that the Taiwan public has indeed paid a painful price.\nWe have always upheld the philosophy of putting the people and life first, implemented the overall policy of \"dynamic zero-COVID\" for epidemic prevention, adhered to \"preventing imported cases from abroad and preventing rebound at home,\" further coordinated epidemic prevention and control with economic and social development, and focused on doing our own work well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","According to Taiwan's statistics, in 2021 almost 100% of the grouper produced on the island was sold to the mainland. After the mainland suspended imports of Taiwan grouper, fishermen on the island called on the DPP authorities to negotiate with the mainland as soon as possible. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We fully understand the appeals of Taiwanese fishermen. First, the most urgent task is for the DPP authorities to conduct a serious and thorough inspection and rectification of the drug safety management system for grouper aquaculture in the Taiwan region. They must not shirk responsibility or delay, and should genuinely consider the interests and well-being of Taiwanese fishermen. Second, the DPP authorities should stop all political manipulation of this issue and all smears and attacks against the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","We have seen that the U.S. has been very active on the Taiwan question recently, including changes in the wording about Taiwan on the U.S. State Department website; U.S. President Biden's remarks on “defending Taiwan” made in Japan; U.S. legislators' visits to Taiwan; and the “Indo-Pacific Economic Framework” launched by the U.S., which, although it does not include Taiwan, was followed by the U.S. launching the…","Recently, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe has already expressed our solemn position on the Taiwan question at the 19th Shangri-La Dialogue. His words were powerful and his signal was clear. On June 13, Yang Jiechi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and director of the Office of the Central Foreign Affairs Commission, held a meeting in Luxembourg with Jake Sullivan, Assistant to the President of the United States for National Security Affairs. On how to properly handle the Taiwan question in China-US relations, he stated our position, made clear our bottom line, and also put forward a solution. I will not elaborate further here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","First question: this year marks the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus” reached across the Strait. The “1992 Consensus” has played an important role in the development of cross-Strait relations, but over these 30 years cross-Strait relations and the international situation have both changed. Will the mainland consider seeking, together with the Taiwan side, a new “consensus” that is more suitable for…","I'll answer the second question first. I would like to express my sympathy. If they are short of rapid antigen test kits, they only need to say so and we can mail them. I hope they will receive them.\nRegarding the first question: regardless of how the international situation changes or how cross-Strait relations develop and evolve, the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China cannot be changed and will not change; the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations has not changed and must not change. I was an eyewitness to the 1992 Consensus reaching, and here I would like to briefly review it with everyone.\nThe “1992 Consensus” refers to the consensus reached in 1992 through the Hong Kong talks between the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the subsequent exchange of letters and telegrams, in which each side orally expressed that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” In the exchanges of letters and telegrams between the two sides, the position and attitude of adhering to the one-China principle and pursuing national reunification were clearly stated; it is black and white and crystal clear.\nThe Taiwan SEF's formulation is: “In the process of both sides of the Strait jointly working toward national reunification, although both sides adhere to the one-China principle, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.” The ARATS formulation is: “Both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive for national reunification. However, in consultations on affairs across the Taiwan Strait, the political meaning of one China is not involved.” It can be seen that the common ground of both sides is to express the attitude of adhering to the one-China principle and to express the attitude of pursuing cross-Strait reunification. The difference is that regarding the political meaning of one China, the Taiwan SEF stated that they “have different understandings,” while ARATS stated that it is “not involved in consultations on affairs.” This was handled by seeking common ground while setting aside differences. This is the basic fact of the “1992 Consensus.” The “1992 Consensus” is not a mere noun or symbol, much less a word game. It was reached through authorized consultations between the relevant parties on both sides; it embodies the historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and it is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations, and it brooks no arbitrary distortion.\nFacts have proven that upholding the “1992 Consensus” enables cross-Strait relations to improve and develop; denying the “1992 Consensus” causes cross-Strait relations to fall into tension and turmoil. From 2008 to 2016, cross-Strait relations were able to present a peaceful development situation precisely because the two sides established basic political mutual trust on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Since 2016, the continued deterioration of cross-Strait relations is rooted in the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which unilaterally undermined the political foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The crux of the cross-Strait problem and the solution are both very clear. We have stated many times that as long as they stop seeking “independence” and provocations and uphold the “1992 Consensus” and recognize its core meaning, the cross-Strait deadlock can be readily resolved, and dialogue and exchanges between the two sides will not be a problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220615_12444611.htm"],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体记者","After the mainland suspended imports of Taiwan grouper, there is concern on the island that the next product to be banned could be wuzai fish, which is highly dependent on the mainland market. Has the mainland sent letters to remind Taiwan about other aquatic product issues?","I do not know what the source of the speculation is. I want to emphasize that the cultivation of agricultural and fishery products involves the food safety of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan residents all attach great importance to the safety of what is on their own dining tables, and ordinary people on the mainland attach equal importance to it. Selling agricultural and fishery products that contain banned drugs or have drug residues exceeding the limits to the mainland is, under any circumstances, unacceptable. We urge the DPP authorities to strictly fulfill their regulatory responsibilities and to earnestly and responsibly correct the problem at its source.\nWe are strengthening supervision in order to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to safeguard the rights and interests of Taiwan's fishermen, and to ensure the smooth conduct of cross-Strait trade. In fact, it is not difficult for the DPP authorities to solve the problem. Everyone has also seen some reports. For some time, when agricultural products that Taiwan exported to Japan, Singapore, and New Zealand encountered problems, how did the DPP authorities handle them? They expressed “respect,” apologized, and offered compensation. Why, when the mainland detected the same problems in agricultural products imported from Taiwan, have they changed to a different face? No matter what reasons they fabricate, they cannot be justified. If the DPP authorities truly had the interests of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen at heart, they should respond to the mainland's demands.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-15","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体记者","Taiwanese blogger Jin Tangli, who grew up in Shanghai, returned to live in Taiwan for two years and then posted a video expressing her different feelings about living in the two places, including that in Taiwan one must carry a wallet when going out and ordering takeout is inconvenient. She was then subjected to a “campaign” by island netizens, and some even told her to “get back to Shanghai.” What comment does…","Exchanges between young people across the Strait, whether online or offline, should all start from goodwill and show more tolerance. Chinese culture has always been diverse yet unified. The lack of “Taiwan independence” education promoted by the DPP authorities stems from emphasizing only differences and failing to see tolerance.\nWhat is “diverse yet unified”? The shared values of Chinese culture are the same, but life in Beijing and Shanghai is different. This is difference. Exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait should be tolerant. If everything is politicized, that is very bad.\nThe phenomenon of such “vicious language” has its root in the DPP authorities manipulating online armies and controlling public opinion. Those who advocate developing cross-Strait relations, or who say even a few kind words about the mainland, are readily “sent into battle” against. This is the DPP’s sin and the tragedy of Taiwan’s young people. I hope this situation can be stopped immediately.\nThank you all for coming. Today’s press conference is concluded here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220615_12444598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-16","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","A question about the football World Cup in Qatar. The organizers have now changed once again the website for people wanting to buy tickets. What’s the Chinese foreign ministry’s comment to that change by the World Cup organizers?","I am not aware of what you mentioned. We have stated China’s position. Taiwan is part of China. Adhering to the one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and shared consensus of the international community. We believe the parties concerned will follow the one-China principle and handle the matter in accordance with established practice in international sports events.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347304.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220616_10704461.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-17","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, Taiwan’s foreign affairs office admitted in a statement that it had long been the island’s practice to employ public relations companies in the US to help consolidate Taiwan-US ties. The DPP authorities have paid $140,000 in service fees to political lobbying agents for pulling strings to get former US leader to receive Tsai Ing-wen’s phone call. They also paid lobbyists to organize the…","We’ve noticed that the Taiwan authorities only admitted to this and disclosed the figures after being probed by the press. In fact, this is just the tip of the iceberg when it comes to the big bucks paid to the US. According to media reports, US politicians like former Secretary of State Mike Pompeo pocketed $150,000 for a four-day visit to Taiwan. Republican Senator Lindsey Graham openly asked the Taiwan authorities to buy Boeing airplanes worth $8 billion while visiting Taiwan.\nHow much of Taiwan people’s hard-earned money have the DPP authorities squandered for such activities? The DPP authorities wouldn’t even dare disclose a complete list of payments. The US says others are engaged in political infiltration against the US. What then is the US’s attitude over these activities? Will it take punitive action against them?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347305.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220617_10705605.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-06-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 18: Lien Chan, former chairman of the Kuomintang of China, was recently hospitalized for treatment due to illness. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the TAO, told the media on the 18th in response to questions: The mainland side is very concerned about Mr. Lien Chan's health, has sent greetings to Mr. Lien and expressed condolences, and wishes him a speedy recovery and that everything goes smoothly and safely!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220618_12445331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-20","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","We reported that the Biden administration officials are increasingly worried that the vague new assertion by China on the Taiwan Strait could result in more frequent challenges at sea for Taiwan. So does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","We’ve previously made it clear that China has sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction in the Taiwan Strait. China has always respected the navigational rights that countries are entitled to in accordance with international law. However, we firmly reject any country’s provocation and threat against China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347306.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220620_10706553.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-20","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","We have learned that the organizer of the Qatar World Cup has changed “Taiwan” to “Chinese Taipei” in its application system. What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and shared consensus of the international community. China appreciates Qatari government’s commitment to the one-China principle and its handling of the issue in line with the established practice of international sports events.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347306.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220620_10706553.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-21","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","It is reported that the Five Eyes alliance is collecting and forging evidence to fabricate rumors that China is conducting “political infiltration” into Western countries, with the aim of tarnishing China’s image in the world. Do you have any comment?","We have noted the reports. Countries concerned must give an explanation for this.\n“Political infiltration” is a signature act of countries like the US and the UK. In the name of freedom and democracy, the US instigated color revolutions and created turbulence in Eastern Europe, Central Asia, Middle East, Latin America, etc. to serve its own geopolitical agenda. As American writer William Blum noted in his book America’s Deadliest Export: Democracy, since the end of World War II, the US has made attempts to overthrow more than 50 foreign governments and grossly interfered in elections in at least 30 countries. Politicians in the US, the UK and other countries frequently colluded with anti-China rioters in Hong Kong. The US co-opted with other Five Eyes countries to lecture China on Hong Kong affairs by issuing joint statements. The National Endowment for Democracy acted as the “henchman” and “white glove” of the US government and meddled repeatedly in Hong Kong’s political agenda to make Hong Kong a “bridgehead” for subversion and infiltration against the mainland. These plain facts are for all to see.\nOn top of all their infiltration and interference activities in China, countries like the US and the UK have sought to deflect the blame on China. This reveals their deeply held Cold War mentality and ideological bias. In the name of preventing “infiltration”, certain countries have politically persecuted individuals having normal exchanges and cooperation with China, creating a chilling effect and reviving McCarthyism. Such moves not only gravely undermined bilateral relations with China but also fed racial discrimination and hate speech and act domestically. The “China Initiative” launched by the US and the “China Research Group” set up by anti-China lawmakers in the UK are typical cases in point. As disclosed by media reports, the Tsai Ing-wen authorities paid big bucks for phone calls with US leaders and interactions with senior US officials. I wonder what the Five Eyes make of this?\nWe urge relevant countries to stop political infiltration, stop spreading disinformation on China and stop relentlessly containing and suppressing China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347307.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220621_10707146.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-06-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 21 dispatch — In response to Taiwanese media reports that 'Taiwan independence' diehard Yu Hsi-kun might visit the Czech Republic, Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to questions on the 21st, saying: Yu Hsi-kun is a 'Taiwan independence' diehard on the list, and his visit to relevant countries to engage in so-called 'parliamentary diplomacy' aims to win over external anti-China forces to pursue 'Taiwan independence.'\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that we urge governments and parliamentarians of relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle, stop sending wrong signals to the 'Taiwan independence' forces, and stop providing a stage and support for the 'Taiwan independence' forces' acts of splitting the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220621_12445942.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-22","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","I have two more questions. The first one is China's mainland made its third largest incursion into Taiwan’s ADIZ on Tuesday, sending 29 aircraft near the island. What prompted this? And is Beijing aware that Taiwanese officials are in Washington this week to discuss a potential arms deal?","Your first question does not concern China’s foreign relations. I would like to refer you to the competent authorities.\nOn your second question, we always firmly oppose official interactions and military ties between the US and Taiwan and US arms sales to Taiwan. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the norms established in the three China-US joint communiqués, stop all forms of official interactions and military ties with Taiwan, stop arms sales to Taiwan, and stop emboldening “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We would also like to make it clear to the DPP authorities that soliciting foreign support to seek “Taiwan independence” will get them nowhere. Anyone who throw themselves on the mercy of others will only end up being tossed aside like used chess pieces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347308.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220622_10707875.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-24","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Again on Afghanistan. So just on the point about Taiwan vowing to donate money to Afghanistan. We’ve seen that there, rather like with Ukraine, Taiwan has been quite speedy in its announcements of pledges of support. Is the Chinese government supportive about this?","I’m not aware of what you mentioned.\nLet me stress again that Taiwan is part of China and the one-China principle is a widely-recognized basic norm as far as international relations are concerned. The Taiwan authorities’ political motive to expand “international space” in the name of providing “assistance” or under any other pretext will not materialize.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347310.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220624_10709637.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-27","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The foreign minister of Tuvalu has decided to pull out of a United Nations oceans conference in Portugal after three Taiwanese participants on the pacific islands’ delegation had their accreditation blocked. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and shared consensus of the international community. It is also a fundamental principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758. The Taiwan authorities are accustomed to resorting to such gambits in the context of international affairs. Stooping to joining the entourage of a foreign country in order to tag along and wedge into the United Nations Ocean Conference can only bring disgrace. China follows true multilateralism and supports parties in participating in the UN Ocean Conference in line with relevant laws and rules.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347311.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220627_10710612.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-28","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","The Hudson Institute established a “China Center” in May this year, with former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo as the chair of the Center’s advisory board. What is your comment?","The Hudson Institute is a conservative think tank in the US. In recent years, it has provided a platform for US politicians including then Vice President Mike Pence and Secretary of State Mike Pompeo to speak against China. The institute also received long-term funding from the Taiwan authorities and assisted the latter to spread “Taiwan independence” rhetoric.\nAcademic institutions should be bridges of communication and mutual learning between countries, rather than build deep trenches or high walls. They should become bridges of understanding and cooperation, rather than a source of disinformation about China. I believe people will stay vigilant to the real purpose and the potential moves of the China Center, and will not pull chestnut from fire for certain anti-China elements.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347312.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220628_10711216.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-28","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said on his way to the NATO Summit that the Chinese government should learn the lessons from Russia’s “strategic failure” in Ukraine. In an apparent reference to any attempt to seize Taiwan by force, Albanese said that the war “had shown attempts to impose change by force on a sovereign country meet resistance”. How does the foreign ministry view Mr. Albanese’s remarks?","We have elaborated on China’s position on the Ukraine crisis on multiple occasions. We have also stressed many times that Taiwan is not Ukraine. A parallel cannot be drawn between them. Taiwan is not a sovereign country. We hope relevant politicians will stop making irresponsible remarks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347312.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220628_10711216.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-28","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","The US and Taiwan held a meeting of the US-Taiwan Initiative on 21st-Century Trade recently. The two sides discussed the development of a roadmap for negotiations with a view to reaching agreements with high-standard commitments and economically meaningful outcomes. Do you have any comment?","China firmly opposes all forms of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China, including negotiating or concluding agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués with concrete actions, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop negotiating agreements with implications of sovereignty and of official nature with the Taiwan authorities, and refrain from sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities need to give up on the idea that they could seek independence with US support, otherwise the higher they jump, the harder they will fall.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347312.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220628_10711216.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-29","Zhao Lijian","CCTV","The 48th G7 Summit released a Leaders’ Communiqué on June 28. The word “China” appears 14 times in the text, which is largely critical of China on matters concerning Hong Kong, Xinjiang, human rights, the East China Sea, the South China Sea, peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, etc. What’s China’s comment?","Despite China’s solemn position and firm opposition, the G7 used the Leaders’ Communiqué to peddle the “democracy versus authoritarianism” narrative, interfere in China’s internal affairs, attack and smear China, and incite confrontational sentiments. This shows that the G7 has no intention of having dialogue and cooperation on the basis of equality and mutual respect, that the G7 remains entrenched in its Cold War mentality and ideological bias, and that the G7 prefers bloc politics that serves the group’s own interests.\nHong Kong affairs are purely China’s internal affairs. Today, 25 years after Hong Kong’s return to the motherland, the democratic rights and freedoms of Hong Kong residents guaranteed by law are fully protected. The Chinese government governs Hong Kong in accordance with the Constitution of the People’s Republic of China and the Basic Law of the Hong Kong SAR. On human rights, the G7 countries, with their own record being far from perfect, have no authority to lecture others or use human rights issues as a political tool to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries. By attacking and smearing China on topics such as Xinjiang and Tibet, they are simply showing the world their hegemonic nature and hypocrisy. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan authorities are pushing the “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda, and the US and a few other Western countries are using Taiwan to contain China. This is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China has the right to take all necessary measures to resolutely safeguard our sovereignty and security. China has been firmly committed to the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and a staunch defender of world peace and development and regional security and stability. This stands in sharp contrast with the US, a warmonger and wielder of illegal unilateral sanctions.\nThe G7 members have benefited the most from globalization. As such, they have a special responsibility to promote globalization, boost world economic growth and tackle global economic and financial challenges. However, at a critical juncture in the global pandemic response and economic recovery, the G7, rather than committing to solidarity and cooperation, is preoccupied with stoking division and confrontation and has shown absolutely no sense of responsibility or moral authority. I must also point out that for a group which accounts for about one tenth only of the world’s population, the G7 has no authority to speak for the whole world, still less to present its own values and standards as universal values and standards.\nWe urge the G7 to earnestly step up to its responsibility and due international obligations, uphold true multilateralism, and stop applying double or even multiple standards, stop causing confrontation and division, stop discrediting and slandering China, and stop all forms of meddling in China’s domestic affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347313.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220629_10712009.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-29","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","We have learned that the Taiwan authorities failed to sneak into the UN Ocean Conference by trying to become part of the Tuvalu delegation. What is your comment?","We have stated our position on the issue yesterday. I would like to reiterate that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and the shared understanding of the international community. It is also a fundamental principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758. Certain country ignored the one-China principle and the overriding trend in the world. It facilitated the personnel of the Taiwan authorities to wedge into the conference, and deliberately hyped up this matter. China is firmly opposed to this. China practices true multilateralism and supports parties in attending the UN Ocean Conference in accordance with relevant laws and rules. We welcome the steps taken by the party concerned to correct the mistake and return to the conference. It is important that the conference focuses on the sustainable development of the ocean.\nI also want to say that the Taiwan authorities will only bring disgrace to itself when it stoops to joining a foreign entourage in order to tag along and wedge into international conferences.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347313.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220629_10712009.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","We note that Taiwanese youth who took part in the “Taiwan Youth Yellow River Travelogue” have recently produced and released many new media works, which have drawn attention and praise. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant details of the event.","It is understood that the “Taiwan Youth Yellow River Travelogue” is a civil cross-Strait exchange activity led by the School of Tourism of Beijing Union University. It was launched on June 8 in Dongying, Shandong. More than ten Taiwan youths traveled upstream from the Yellow River estuary to the Yellow River source in Qinghai, visiting and filming Yellow River households across 36 prefecture-level cities in nine provinces and autonomous regions along the way. Together with local youth, they experienced firsthand the magnificent scenery, excellent traditional culture, folk culture and ecological protection of the Yellow River basin, and witnessed the development, progress and profound changes of the Yellow River basin over the past 30 years. So far the activity has visited Shandong, Henan and Shaanxi provinces and produced and released many excellent new media products. Media including Straits Flying Rainbow, CCTV.com, Straits TV, Xiamen TV, Straits Herald and the China Agricultural Film Center have followed up with reports, producing a positive impact on both sides of the Strait.\nWe support and encourage compatriots on both sides, especially young people, to carry out rich and colorful exchange activities to enhance mutual understanding. We hope that the Taiwan youths participating in this activity can provide more Taiwan young people with a new perspective for understanding the Yellow River, the mainland, and the history and reality of the Chinese nation. We thank the Taiwan Affairs Offices, culture and tourism departments, and agriculture and rural affairs departments of the local governments of the nine provinces and autonomous regions for their strong support of the activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Ke Wenzhe recently publicly advocated building the Kinmen-Xiamen Bridge, arguing that it could solve Kinmen's water, electricity and transportation problems, which has sparked heated discussion on the island. The Mainland Affairs Council says building the bridge carries so-called “security risks,” and some politicians in the Green camp have accused Ke Wenzhe of “selling out Taiwan.” The Speaker of the Kinmen…","The Xiamen–Kinmen bridge is a good thing that responds to the livelihood demands of people on both sides of the Strait; it is conducive to the common development of Jinmen and Xiamen and benefits compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities and certain Green camp politicians \"oppose everything from the mainland\" and always take the opportunity to incite cross-Strait antagonism and undermine cross-Strait relations. This mindset and practice are not popular. We believe that Taiwan compatriots, including the fellow villagers of Kinmen, all hope that Kinmen will become a frontier of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and oppose its being turned into a tool for the DPP authorities to incite cross-Strait confrontation.\nAs for the Mainland Affairs Council using so-called \"security risks\" as a pretext, I want to say that the DPP authorities are accustomed to intimidating and deceiving the Taiwan public with lies. When cross-Strait direct \"Three Links\" were being promoted years ago, the DPP widely spread absurd and ridiculous claims such as the mainland \"Trojan horse will destroy cities\" and \"civil aircraft hide military aircraft.\" Facts have proven that these were outright political lies. Today, faced with the call for the Kinmen–Xiamen bridge, they have once again resorted to the same old tricks. This once again shows that whatever benefits the Taiwan public, and whatever is conducive to improving and developing cross-Strait relations, they oppose. This is their political nature.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448397.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","In a recent interview, Wu Zhaoxie claimed that “China has never ruled Taiwan,” continued to spread the remark that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other,” and also said that the US and other countries sending warships through the Taiwan Strait is an exercise of so-called “freedom of navigation,” demonstrating their emphasis on “regional peace and stability.” What is your comment on this?","The fallacies put forward by Wu Chao-hsu, in addition to once again exposing his separatist nature of peddling the “two-state theory” and colluding with external forces to provoke “Taiwan independence,” are untenable both in law and in fact, and cannot lead to the absurd conclusions of “mutual non-subordination between the two sides of the Strait” or the “two-state theory.” I would like to emphasize four points:\nFirst, national sovereignty is indivisible. Territory is the space in which a state exercises sovereignty. Within the territory of a state, there can be only one central government that exercises sovereignty on behalf of the state. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China replaced the government of the Republic of China and became the sole legal government of all of China and the sole legal representative of China internationally. This was a new regime replacing an old one while the same subject of international law remained unchanged. China's sovereignty and inherent territorial boundaries did not change as a result. The government of the People's Republic of China naturally fully enjoys and exercises China's sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan.\nSecond, although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, Taiwan's status as part of China's territory has never changed and will not be allowed to change, and China's sovereignty over Taiwan has never changed and cannot change. The long-standing existence of the state of civil war across the Taiwan Strait has not granted Taiwan a status or rights under international law, nor can it change Taiwan's legal status as part of China.\nThird, the international community recognizes that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government of China. Under this principle, Taiwan has no right to participate in the United Nations or other international organizations that only sovereign states can join, and countries that have established diplomatic relations with China may not develop official relations with Taiwan, sell weapons to Taiwan, or form any kind of military alliance with Taiwan. The Chinese government treats Taiwan's external exchanges under the one-China principle and safeguards all legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. This is the concrete manifestation of our exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan.\nFourth, China enjoys sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. At the same time, we respect the navigation rights enjoyed by other countries under international law, but we firmly oppose any country using freedom of navigation as a pretext to engage in provocations that threaten China's sovereignty and security. Wu Chao-hsu and his ilk, by cooperating with external forces to hype up the issue, are entirely based on the separatist scheme of “Taiwan independence,” harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and betraying the overall interests of the Chinese nation. The 1.4 billion Chinese people will never accept this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448404.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Zhu Lilun, speaking recently about the results of his visit to the United States, said the KMT “loves America and cherishes Taiwan” and “defends Taiwan through defense,” and hopes that both sides can avoid conflict and war through dialogue and exchanges. In addition, a KMT think tank published a poll stating that 37% of respondents believe “dialogue should not be conducted with the mainland on the basis of the…","The “1992 Consensus” refers to the consensus reached in 1992 through authorized oral communication between the Chinese mainland’s Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and Taiwan’s Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), with each side expressing that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” It defines the nature of cross-Strait relations as both the mainland and Taiwan belonging to one China. It is the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations, and it must not be distorted, let alone discarded.\nUpholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the common political foundation for our interaction with the Chinese Nationalist Party (Kuomintang), the anchor for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and the key to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is rooted in the DPP authorities’ refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and their collusion with external forces to continuously carry out provocations aimed at pursuing “independence.” This includes squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people on large-scale purchases of weapons from abroad. The result will not only fail to protect Taiwan, but will also push Taiwan step by step into danger, seriously harming the safety and well-being of the broad mass of Taiwan people.\nWe hope that all political parties, groups and individuals on the island who are committed to developing cross-Strait relations and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will recognize the trend, distinguish right from wrong, and take a firm stand. We hope they will uphold national righteousness, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and work with us to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and defend the national interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448405.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the problems of “parasitic unregistered operations” and “license borrowing” in the export of farmed grouper on the island are serious, and the DPP authorities are letting violators off, while fish farmers are taking the blame for exporters. The head of the Taiwan agricultural authority claimed that cross-Strait agricultural trade has not been conducted under “normal regulatory…","The grouper farmers who export to the mainland were all approved by the Taiwan competent authorities after being certified as qualified under the rules and standards on the island, and each batch of groupers exported to the mainland comes with a certificate issued by the Taiwan competent authorities, certifying the legality and safety of the goods. Where the \"borrowed license\" problem has occurred, the Taiwan competent authorities, as the certificate administrator and issuer, should bear full responsibility. The so-called chaos on the island, such as \"parasitic unregistered households\" and \"borrowed licenses,\" is entirely due to the DPP authorities' lax supervision and disorderly management.\nFaced with the major loopholes in its own management, the DPP authorities not only show no willingness to improve but instead seize the opportunity to shift blame to the mainland. After issues were exposed by Taiwan society and they had no valid reply, they forcibly attributed the problem to the cross-Strait agricultural trade mechanism. This clumsy trick of politicizing everything is utterly laughable. We must ask in response: from the \"Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement\" to the \"Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement across the Taiwan Strait,\" which clause permits \"borrowed licenses\"? Which clause permits \"parasitic unregistered households\"? Which clause permits passing off inferior goods as good, or bad money driving out good? Clearly, to this day the DPP authorities still take an irresponsible attitude. This again proves that they simply do not want to solve the problem and have not given the least thought to the fishermen on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448402.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","After the mainland suspended imports of Taiwan grouper, Taiwan’s agricultural authority claimed that it has completed inspections of 11 grouper farms, “none of which used banned drugs,” and hopes the mainland will resume imports as soon as possible. What comments do you have on this?","At the end of last year, after the mainland notified relevant Taiwan authorities of the non-compliance of grouper drugs, the Taiwan side replied that “no banned drugs were detected.” However, recently the mainland again detected the banned drug crystal violet in two batches of Taiwan grouper. This shows that the relevant problems have not been fundamentally resolved. We have also noted that industry insiders on the island have reported that there is a phenomenon of “unregistered farms hiding behind licensed boats” in grouper exports, and only after media exposure did the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have to acknowledge that “borrowed licenses” indeed exist. This shows that the regulatory loopholes of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are riddled with problems. We cannot help but ask: under such circumstances, how can their claimed “no banned drugs” test results be convincing? Have the problems in Taiwan’s grouper aquaculture and food safety and hygiene management system been investigated? Have they been fundamentally resolved? And who can guarantee that the problems occurring in grouper exported to the mainland will not appear elsewhere? If the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not face up to their own problems and resolve them at the source, they will be unable to protect the vital interests of fishermen on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448401.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Some Taiwan media recently exposed contents of US Department of Justice documents showing that the so-called “diplomatic achievements with the US” that the DPP authorities heavily hyped were mostly achieved by throwing money at US political public relations firms. Taiwan's foreign affairs department said this is a long-standing, consistent practice, and claimed the mainland is using this matter for “cognitive…","These scandals and dirty secrets once again show that the DPP authorities, driven by their nature of seeking “independence,” colluding with external anti-China forces, will stop at nothing and have no bottom line. They keep using the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people to bribe certain US politicians, serve anti-China forces, fabricate so-called “diplomatic achievements,” deceive public opinion and the people on the island, and can truly be called repeat offenders of “cognitive warfare.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. We believe more and more Taiwan compatriots will see through their essence of seeking “independence” and selling out Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448396.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Media reports state that the University of Copernicus in Poland, together with relevant institutions in the Taiwan region, established a so-called “Taiwan Polar Research Station” and displayed a “fake flag.” What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any act that provides a stage and convenience for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities. We urge the countries concerned to abide by the one-China principle and immediately correct their wrong actions. The DPP authorities' various tricks cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","浙江卫视记者","The so-called “US-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative” meeting was recently held. The DPP authorities said its goal is to sign a so-called “trade agreement” with the United States. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any agreement between the United States and Taiwan region that has sovereign implications or official nature. For political gain, the DPP authorities are accustomed to sacrificing the interests of businesses and people on the island and colluding with external forces to seek “independence.” We advise the DPP authorities to stop harming the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, not to go further and further down the wrong path of “relying on the US to seek independence,” and not to become accomplices of external forces that arbitrarily carve up the interests of Taiwan's people and extract the fruits of Taiwan's economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448399.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡卫视记者","It is reported that the United States and the Taiwan region recently held the so-called “Monterey Talks,” discussing military security issues including U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities continue to strengthen their military and quasi-military collusion with external forces, causing tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Their behavior of purchasing weapons from foreign countries is even more a matter of spending the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people, and they are willing to push the people of Taiwan into the flames of war. “Relying on the US to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” will inevitably end in failure. We urge the US government to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop military and quasi-military collusion with the Taiwan region of China, and stop selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202206/t20220629_12448398.htm"],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声广播电台记者","Everyone is very interested in when the 14th Straits Forum will be held. Could the spokesperson introduce the current preparations for the forum?","It is understood that the 14th Straits Forum is expected to be held in Xiamen in mid-July. Guided by the concept that “cross-strait compatriots are one family,” this forum will adhere to its positioning of being “civil, grassroots, and broad-based,” continue its theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and continue to play an active role in deepening civil exchanges across the Strait, promoting integrated development across the Strait, and fostering spiritual affinity among people on both sides. Specific arrangements will be announced to everyone in a timely manner once they are determined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国电视记者","First question: The General Administration of Customs recently announced that novel coronavirus nucleic acid tested positive in the outer packaging samples of two batches of aquatic products imported into the mainland from the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities claimed that no problems were found after spot checks, and said the mainland “should do a good job in food safety management.” What comment do you have?…","First question: Because two batches of aquatic product outer packaging samples imported into the mainland from Taiwan tested positive for COVID-19 nucleic acid, in accordance with the provisions of Announcement No. 103 of 2020 of the General Administration of Customs, the mainland took emergency precautionary measures suspending acceptance of product declarations for one week each for the relevant production enterprises. The Taiwan side was notified before these measures were implemented. As of now, the Taiwan side has not provided any feedback on the relevant situation. Since the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, the epidemic in some regions has been linked to contaminated imported cold-chain food and packaging. Guided by the principle that life comes first, and aiming to effectively safeguard people's health, we have taken relevant monitoring measures for imported food. This is entirely necessary, reasonable and legitimate.\nSecond question: Amid the severe epidemic on the island and the shortage of antigen test kits, the DPP authorities, disregarding the health and safety of Taiwan residents, have made baseless insinuations and played politics on the antigen kit issue. Their aim is to tear apart the emotional bonds between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and undermine cross-Strait relations. Since the outbreak of the epidemic, the DPP authorities have continuously manipulated “using the epidemic to oppose China,” inciting confrontation across the Strait. This kind of political manipulation has not been the first time, and in the end it always harms the health and well-being of Taiwan residents.\nThird question: Since taking office, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” colluded with external forces, and constantly plotted “Taiwan independence” and provoked trouble, undermining cross-Strait relations. This is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. The intrusive visits and small maneuvers you mentioned are the best proof. Adhering to the one-China principle is the universal consensus of the international community. We hope that relevant countries will properly handle Taiwan-related issues on the basis of the one-China principle, not do anything that harms their relations with China, and not do anything that hurts the feelings of the Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: The joint statement issued after the Group of Seven (G7) summit again emphasized the so-called “importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait” and encouraged the peaceful resolution of cross-Strait issues. At the same time, it claimed it would launch a financing plan to counter the mainland’s “Belt and Road” initiative, and the DPP authorities said they would seek opportunities to…","The first question: Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely an internal Chinese affair and brooks no foreign interference. The United States and Western countries are rallying allies to play the “Taiwan card,” attempting to contain China's development and reunification, which is extremely dangerous. To achieve their goal, they turn a blind eye to the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces' provocations to seek independence, and instead accuse the mainland of being a so-called “disruptor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.” This completely distorts the facts and reverses black and white. I advise them to immediately stop sending erroneous signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, for those who play with fire will burn themselves.\nThe second question: The various public opinion polls on the island are a mix of truth and fiction, with different orientations and different designs, and we will not comment on them specifically.\nEveryone has noticed that in recent years, the atmosphere and heat of discussions on the island about cross-Strait tensions have been rising, and even discussions about so-called “military unification” or war have emerged. This phenomenon reflects the deep-seated concern of the Taiwan public and Taiwan society about the danger and harm posed by the DPP authorities' provocations to seek independence.\nI want to emphasize that our policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” has not changed. Compatriots on both sides are all Chinese, and compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. No one is more willing than we are to achieve the complete reunification of the country by peaceful means. But we will never stand idly by in the face of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts that dare to split the country's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan will discern right from wrong and understand where their interests lie, resolutely oppose and contain “Taiwan independence,” and join us in continuing along the path of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Peaceful reunification and national rejuvenation will surely be achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体记者","On the 24th, Taiwan recorded its first confirmed imported case of mpox from abroad. The related news topped mainland internet trending searches and caused concern among mainland netizens. Will the mainland adjust its relevant entry regulations for Taiwan travelers in the future?","The first confirmed case of monkeypox in Taiwan has sparked heated online discussion among people on both sides of the Strait, which is only natural. I want to stress that we attach great importance to the safety of people's lives and health. For specific professional and technical questions, please consult the competent health authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The cross-strait risk index and cross-strait risk barometer recently released by the US Goldman Sachs Group show that cross-strait tensions have risen to their highest level in nearly a decade. The latest report from the China Strait Research Institute in Hong Kong also points out that the cross-strait risk index has reached a historic high. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","First, everyone should reflect on the reasons behind this phenomenon: it is because the DPP authorities are colluding with external forces to seek 'independence' and provoke, causing tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait and arousing deep-seated, widespread concern in Taiwan's society. Second, if the DPP authorities did not engage in provocation and confrontation, or in 'Taiwan independence' separatism, there would be no 'rising risks' in cross-strait relations. Finally, our policy of 'peaceful reunification and one country, two systems' has not changed. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will never allow Taiwan to split away from China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","The Mainland Affairs Council said it has provided the grouper inspection results and data to the mainland side through the relevant agreement platform, but the mainland has not responded. It said it hopes that technical issues in future inspection and quarantine matters can be resolved through direct communication between relevant departments on both sides of the Strait. What is the response to this?","The fundamental cause of this situation is problems with Taiwan’s grouper aquaculture and its health and safety management system. The DPP authorities providing only a few sets of test data cannot solve the problems of “borrowed licenses” and “parasitic unregistered operations.” The risks in the island’s grouper aquaculture and health and safety management system remain. The DPP authorities must face their own problems, earnestly fulfill their regulatory responsibilities, and resolve at the source the serious problems in the island’s grouper aquaculture and food safety and hygiene management system. To date, the DPP authorities and some politicians are still taking advantage of this to sow discord, incite confrontation between the two sides of the Strait, and attack and smear the mainland. They must immediately stop this behavior and use concrete actions to eliminate the adverse impact caused thereby.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Taiwan compatriots in Shanghai have reported that, due to airlines’ epidemic prevention policies, return tickets to Taiwan have been hard to buy recently. Is the mainland considering adding flights from Shanghai to Taiwan, or relaxing the epidemic prevention rules for Taiwan businesspeople traveling across the Strait?","Due to the recent epidemic prevention and control situation in Shanghai, and because the global epidemic continues to rebound, especially as the epidemic on the island remains at a high level, in order to guard against imported cases and prevent spillover, the relevant authorities have dynamically adjusted all outbound international flights from Shanghai Airport, including cross-Strait routes. Doing so is fundamentally for the sake of safeguarding the lives and physical health of the people.\nWe are very mindful of the demands of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to travel between the two sides of the Strait. The relevant departments will actively study this and continue to adjust flights dynamically, based on developments in the epidemic prevention and control situation and the requirements for precise and scientific prevention and control. Starting July 1, the passenger load factor for civil aviation aircraft flying cross-Strait routes from Shanghai Airport was raised from 50% to 75%, which helps increase passenger capacity and facilitates travel for Taiwan compatriots to the mainland as much as possible.\nEveryone has noticed that yesterday (June 28), the Comprehensive Group of the State Council's Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism for the COVID-19 Pneumonia Epidemic revised and formulated the \"COVID-19 Pneumonia Prevention and Control Plan (Ninth Edition),\" adjusting the quarantine and control period for inbound personnel from \"14+7\" to \"7 days of centralized quarantine medical observation + 3 days of home health monitoring.\" This likewise applies to Taiwan compatriots and likewise facilitates travel for Taiwan compatriots between the two sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","After Ko Wen-je proposed building a Kinmen-Xiamen Bridge, he was criticized by the DPP authorities. The Mainland Affairs Council issued a statement denying that Tsai Ing-wen had ever proposed a similar idea. Later, Kuomintang legislators cited a media report from Kinmen from years ago, which “directly slapped them in the face.” Some people in Taiwan also believe that rather than discussing the Kinmen-Xiamen…","Regardless of whether Tsai Ing-wen ever put forward a similar proposal, the construction of the Kinmen-Xiamen Bridge meets the actual needs of the people. The DPP authorities should not forcibly obstruct it on various pretexts. Of course, judging by the DPP authorities' consistent behavior, they always fabricate lies, and now they have come up with a so-called “security risk” to deceive and intimidate the people of Taiwan. Their purpose in doing so is to obstruct exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to obstruct the improvement of the well-being of compatriots in Kinmen and Xiamen.\nIn addition, I do not think that opening the Kinmen-Xiamen Bridge is a meaningless matter. In a sense, its significance is much greater than the “Mini Three Links.” Once the bridge is open, people can travel directly back and forth, and goods can circulate directly. What could be more convenient and smooth than this? As for the resumption of the “Mini Three Links,” as the old saying goes, the one who tied the knot must untie it. The suspension of the “Mini Three Links” was unilaterally decided by the DPP authorities at the outbreak of the 2020 epidemic. If they want to resume the “Mini Three Links,” they must take concrete action.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-06-29","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中央社记者","Why did this year's cross-Strait journalists' joint interview choose Xinjiang? Could the spokesperson introduce the highlights of this itinerary?","The Cross-Strait Journalists' Joint Reporting Tour is a cross-strait news exchange activity co-hosted by the News Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Department of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Affairs of the China Journalists Association. Since 2000, it has been held once a year, organizing cross-strait journalists to conduct in-depth reporting tours in various localities to appreciate the magnificent rivers and mountains of the motherland, understand Chinese history and culture, experience the pulse of economic and social development, and feel the achievements of cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. It has played a positive role in promoting media exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and enhancing mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, and it has earned a good reputation among journalists on both sides of the strait, including those in Taiwan, becoming a beautiful brand of cross-strait news exchange.\nThe choice of Xinjiang for this year's Cross-Strait Journalists' Joint Reporting Tour came in response to the strong request of cross-strait journalists, especially Taiwan journalists stationed on the mainland. We all know that Xinjiang is a wonderful place. In 2015, cross-strait journalists conducted a joint reporting tour in Xinjiang and left a deep and beautiful impression of Xinjiang. Seven years have passed, and everyone very much wants to go back and take another look. Many Taiwan journalists who took part in the 2015 reporting tour have sent me messages expressing regret at being unable to join this time. With the strong support and careful arrangements of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region Taiwan Affairs Office and relevant departments, from July 3 to 11, cross-strait journalists will once again enter Xinjiang and go to Urumqi, Ili, Kashgar and other places for in-depth reporting, to experience firsthand the changes and great achievements of Xinjiang in economic development, ethnic unity, social harmony, ecological protection, rural revitalization, and the inheritance and development of the cultures of all ethnic groups.\nWe believe that Xinjiang, full of magical charm, will certainly not disappoint everyone's expectations, and will once again amaze you. We also believe that whether they are new friends or old friends, everyone will gain a completely new understanding of Xinjiang through this trip. We warmly welcome cross-strait journalist friends to join actively and, through your cameras, words, and voices, show both sides of the strait a real and beautiful Xinjiang.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all for coming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202206/t20220629_12448394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-06-30","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, British Foreign Secretary Liz Truss said on June 29 that NATO must make clear to China that “invading Taiwan” would be “a catastrophic miscalculation”. What’s your comment?","Recently a certain British senior official has repeatedly hyped up issues relating to Taiwan. The Chinese side has lodged solemn representations over this. I would like to stress once again that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair where no foreign force has any right to interfere. This is a basic norm in international relations. China is committed to the policy of peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems and will make every possible effort to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. That being said, we will not sit idly by and do nothing about “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. It was quite surprising that a senior UK official would make such remarks, which lacked basic common sense and sounded rather presumptuous.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347314.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220630_10713013.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-06-30","Zhao Lijian","BBC","British Foreign Secretary said at the NATO Summit that it’s so important that the free world, as she put it, works together to help ensure that Taiwan is able to defend itself. What is China’s response?","I have made China’s position amply clear just now. The Chinese side has lodged solemn representations to the British side over this. It was a surprise to hear her remarks, which lack basic common sense and sound rather presumptuous. We hope she will make no more such irresponsible remarks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347314.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202206/t20220630_10713013.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-06-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","At the start of the new year, Chairman Xi signed Central Military Commission Order No. 1 of 2022 and issued the training-launch mobilization order to the entire armed forces. Please introduce the specific measures the entire military is taking to implement Chairman Xi's training-launch mobilization order, and what is your outlook for military training work in the new year?","On January 4, Chairman Xi signed the order of the Central Military Commission mobilizing the 2022 training year, requiring all levels of the entire military to comprehensively advance the transformation and upgrading of military training and to forge elite forces capable of fighting and winning battles. This is the fifth consecutive year that Chairman Xi has issued a training-year mobilization order, establishing a clear orientation toward placing great emphasis on military training and sounding the era's call to train and prepare for combat. Units across the military have responded to the order and acted in accordance with it, organizing training activities such as combat command research and practice, confrontation exercises, theoretical concentrated training, skills competitions, and combat readiness drills, and have promptly launched a new year's upsurge in actual-combat military training.\nBe vigorous and diligent in refining martial skills, and steadfast and unremitting in training. This year, the People's Liberation Army will mark its 95th anniversary. The military training of the entire armed forces will take the spirit of the Central Military Commission's military training conference as its main thread, strengthen the tackling of key tasks in the “14th Five-Year Plan” for military training, and comprehensively advance the transformation and upgrading of military training. First, vigorously promote the deep integration of combat and training, emphasize testing according to scenarios, strengthen training against the enemy on the front line of military struggle, strengthen training under extreme and harsh conditions, maintain constant readiness to fight and the ability to fight at any time, and accelerate the integration of training and actual combat. Second, vigorously promote systematic training, innovate the organization and training of typical combat operations, increase training in joint operational command and adaptability, and comprehensively enhance joint operational capabilities and all-domain operational capabilities based on the networked information system. Third, vigorously promote technology-driven training, accelerate the integration and conversion of advanced technology into combat capability, strengthen the integration of theory and technology and innovation, vigorously develop simulation training and network training, make concerted efforts to improve the technological literacy of officers and soldiers, and continuously innovate asymmetric tactics for winning. All officers and soldiers across the armed forces will adhere to diligent training, scientific training, and safe training, strengthen their combat skills and combat style, and welcome the successful convening of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with a more vigorous spirit and first-class training results.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/06-30/9792579.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-06-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","Recently, the foreign ministers and defense ministers of the United States and Japan held a “2+2” online meeting and issued a joint statement, maliciously hyping the so-called “China threat” and claiming that China is undermining the rules-based international order and posing challenges to the region and the world. In addition, the United States and Japan have extensively hyped the Taiwan Strait issue. Some…","The US and Japan are brazenly interfering in China's internal affairs and fabricating false information to maliciously smear China. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this, and has lodged serious representations with the relevant countries.\nSpeaking of a rules-based international order: there is only one set of rules in the world, namely the basic norms of international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, not so-called rules based on the interests of a “small circle.” There is only one order in the world, namely the international order based on international law, not the egoistic order advocated by a few countries. On the issues of rules and order, the US and Japan have no qualification whatsoever to accuse China.\nAs for the so-called “China threat,” this is a lie repeated a thousand times that should have long been swept into the dustbin of history. In contrast, the US and Japan have continuously strengthened their military deployments in the East China Sea and South China Sea and carried out highly targeted military provocations, and the Cold War confrontation mindset reflected behind this deserves high vigilance from the international community.\nIt must be pointed out that Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no external interference. The root cause of the current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces colluding with external forces and continuously plotting “independence” and provoking trouble. The US and Japan, by playing up the so-called “China threat” and hyping the Taiwan Strait issue, are fueling the DPP authorities' “independence” ambitions and sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. This is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe US and Japan's attempt to meddle in the Taiwan question is a dangerous trend. On this issue, the deeper the US and Japan sink in, the more painfully they will suffer in the future. In defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the determination and will of the Chinese People's Liberation Army are as solid as a rock, and its capabilities and means are constantly growing; this is by no means just talk.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/06-30/9792639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-07-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, July 1 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a query on the 1st, said: We firmly oppose the erroneous remarks by NATO leaders on Taiwan-related issues. Taiwan is part of China, and compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. Our resolute punishment of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and countermeasures against interference by external forces in accordance with law are just actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Spreading the so-called “China threatens Taiwan” fallacy aims to use the Taiwan issue to interfere in China's internal affairs.\nA reporter asked: At the NATO summit press conference, NATO Secretary General Stoltenberg said, “China threatens Taiwan.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe pointed out that the relevant organizations and individuals must correct their mistakes, must abide by the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, and stop sending erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220701_12449000.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 1 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 1st, pointing out that on the 25th anniversary of Hong Kong’s return to the motherland, “Taiwan independence” diehards Su Tseng-chang and Yu Shyi-kun and their ilk jumped out to vilify the successful practice of “one country, two systems,” fully exposing the essence of…","Zhu Fenglian said that in the face of the overall trend of Hong Kong's development from chaos to order and from order to prosperity, any malicious attacks and smears by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements against “one country, two systems” in order to seek political gain are futile and will certainly be rejected by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220701_12449058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-04","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","A representative of Palau said at the closing ceremony of the UN Ocean Conference on July 1 that “Taiwan representatives were not allowed to be part of our delegation simply because they hold Taiwanese passports”, adding that Palau views this as a violation of its sovereign rights and the UN shouldn’t have excluded the 23 million people of Taiwan from the conversation. Representative of the US said that no…","This is the third time that I have answered this question. The Taiwan authorities have tried several times to make an issue out of this. Is it because they are proud of the way they tried to wedge into the conference?\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and an established international consensus. Based on the one-China principle, Taiwan has no right to attend as a delegation the activities of the UN and its special agencies and those of intergovernmental international organizations limited to sovereign countries. These principles and consensus will not change just because certain countries have endorsed and emboldened the Taiwan authorities. The failure of the Taiwan authorities to get into the conference was inevitable. Such a disgraceful act only exposes themselves to international ridicule.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347316.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220704_10715102.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-05","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","Michael Rubin, a senior fellow at the American Enterprise Institute (AEI), recently wrote in an op-ed that “the one-China policy is a lie” and “Taiwan was never part of China”. He wrote, the 1951 Treaty of San Francisco after the Second World War read that “Japan renounces all right, title and claim to Formosa and the Pescadores ... however, the Treaty did not transfer sovereignty to any other state.” What is…","Let me first say that to tell a lie, it often requires some sort of camouflage. The AEI op-ed has told a lie under an academic camouflage. The article is written in the name of a research fellow from a research institute, yet its content is clearly inconsistent with historical and legal facts, and deliberately misinforms and misleads its readers. The article has a clear motive: to grab attention, hollow out and obscure the one-China principle, echo anti-China forces’ attempt to use the Taiwan question to contain China, and embolden “Taiwan-independence” forces to solicit US support.\nThe Treaty of San Francisco is an illegal and invalid document issued by the US and a number of other countries after World War II to reach post-war settlement with Japan, a process that excluded China and the Soviet Union. The document violates the provisions of the Declaration by United Nations signed by 26 countries including China, the US, the UK and the Soviet Union in 1942. It also deviates from the UN Charter and the basic principles of international law. The way the document handles the sovereignty over Taiwan and the territory and sovereign rights of China, which is not a signatory to the document, was also illegal and invalid. The Chinese government made it clear from the very beginning that the Chinese government considers the Treaty of San Francisco illegal and invalid and does not recognize it, because the People’s Republic of China was never part of the preparation, drafting or signing of the document. Countries including the Soviet Union, Poland, Czechoslovakia, the DPRK, Mongolia, Vietnam refused to recognize the validity of the so-called treaty as well.\nThere is only one China in the world. Taiwan has been an inalienable part of China since ancient times. A number of international legal instruments including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation have affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan in clear-cut terms. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have yet to be reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one and same China has never changed and the sovereignty and territory of China has never been split.\nThe facts about the Taiwan question and the history of the one-China principle are crystal clear. History cannot be tampered with, and truth cannot be distorted. Any attempt to challenge the one-China principle which is recognized internationally will prove futile. China’s efforts to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity brook no foreign intervention.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347317.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220705_10715682.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-06","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","I would like to follow up on the upcoming meeting between Chinese and US foreign ministers you just mentioned. Will the Taiwan question and Xinjiang-related issues be covered during the meeting?","The Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests. It has always been the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-US relations. Previous US administrations have all made clear commitments to this, and President Biden also stated that the US does not support “Taiwan independence” in his statements which include five assurances (i.e. the US does not seek a new Cold War with China, that it does not aim to change China’s system, that the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China, that it does not support “Taiwan independence”, and that it has no intention to seek a conflict with China). The US needs to abide by the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop turning back the wheel of history, stop hollowing out the one-China principle, stop encouraging and supporting “Taiwan independence”, and take concrete actions to safeguard the political foundation of China-US relations.\nXinjiang-related issues are of major concern to China. The so-called forced labor in Xinjiang is an outrageous lie from the US side to smear and contain China. The US’s Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act is an extension of this lie and designed to amplify its approach of using Xinjiang to contain China. The international community knows what is truly going on. China is not engaged in “forced labor”, but it is facing forced unemployment caused by the US. By accusing China, the US is depriving hundreds of thousands of workers in Xinjiang of their most basic right to work in various sectors. China is not engaged in “suppression of human rights”, but it is facing a forced return to poverty caused by the US. What the US has done is taking away the livelihoods of people from all ethnic backgrounds in Xinjiang who have worked really hard to have lifted themselves out of poverty. The US is even going after Xinjiang’s poverty alleviation projects. China is not violating international rules, but it is facing forced decoupling and cutting off of international industrial and supply chains caused by the US. It is the US that is destroying international economic and trade rules and destabilizing international industrial and supply chains.\nWe urge the US side to stop propagating lies about forced labor and implementing the Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act, and take concrete actions to create favorable conditions for bilateral cooperation in various fields instead of creating new obstacles.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347318.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220706_10716331.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Taiwan's Liberty Times reported that Chang Hsiu-yeh, head of the Chinese Patriotic Harmony Party, and others were wanted by the DPP authorities on the pretext of so-called “violation of the national security law,” and some of the content also involves relevant mainland departments. What is your comment on this?","The relevant reports are pure fabrication and malicious rumors. They are yet another vicious political manipulation by the DPP authorities, who, driven by their essence of seeking “Taiwan independence” and their own political interests, have concocted charges to suppress forces on the island that support unification and oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220706_12450162.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on July 7 that the 14th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian from July 12, with the main venue in Xiamen, and the forum conference will be held on the 13th. At present, preparations are basically in place. The forum organizing committee has invited representatives of relevant Taiwan political parties, representatives of host units, and guests from all walks of life, including industry elites, heads of social groups, the Youth, Workers and Women's federations, township and village communities, agriculture, fisheries and water conservancy sectors, and folk belief, to attend forum-related activities in various ways.\nZhu Fenglian said that this session of the forum continues the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,” adopting a combination of online and offline, and centralized and decentralized formats. It arranges 43 events in four major sections (the forum conference and youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges) and 12 events in prefecture-level cities and districts. Approximately 2,000 Taiwan guests will attend the forum in person. This session of the forum will continue to focus on and serve grassroots people and young people, work hand in hand with Taiwan compatriots to carry forward traditional Chinese culture, take the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and help promote integrated economic and social development across the Strait. We warmly welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to participate in Straits Forum-related activities in various ways.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220707_12450253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-08","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The PLA recently conducted drills near Taiwan. Taiwan said that the PLA planes flew across “the middle line” of the Taiwan Strait, an act which they described as provocative. Do you have any comment?","China’s position on the so-called “middle line” in the Taiwan Strait is clear and consistent. The Taiwan authorities’ political manipulation on this issue will not succeed.\nThe Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People’s Liberation Army (PLA) recently organized multi-unit joint combat readiness patrols and real-combat drills in the sea and airspace around the Taiwan island. The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command has put out relevant press release. The exercises are a response to foreign interference and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will resolutely safeguard its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity and foil any attempts for “Taiwan independence”.\nThe following question was raised after the press conference:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347320.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220708_10717686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-07-08","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to reports, the DPP authorities have recently and frequently hyped the so-called “mainland threat,” claiming that since the beginning of this year, mainland military aircraft have entered Taiwan's “airspace” more than 940 sorties, twice the total for 2019 and 2020 combined. In addition, a US Department of Defense official said that mainland China's activities in the sea and airspace around Taiwan have…","The root of the current escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces' provocations aimed at \"independence,\" and in the schemes of external forces to \"use Taiwan to contain China.\" The People's Liberation Army of China is duty-bound to defend national sovereignty and security and to curb \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts. Since the beginning of this year, the PLA has routinely organized bombers, reconnaissance aircraft, fighter jets, and other forces to conduct patrols around the island of Taiwan, routinely conducted joint combat readiness patrols by multiple services close to the waters around the island, and routinely organized combat-oriented drills such as joint anti-ship strikes, joint land strikes, and joint air defense operations in the sea and airspace near the island. The actual number of aircraft sorties will only increase, not decrease, compared with the figures hyped by the DPP authorities. The objective is clear: to respond with decisive action to the vicious acts of forces both within and outside the island repeatedly colluding and challenging the one-China principle, to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to effectively safeguard the common well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/07-08/9798599.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-07-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 8: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 8th, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Some members of the US Congress have interfered in China's internal affairs with their wrong words and actions and tolerated and supported \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, which is very dangerous. The DPP authorities' attempt to win over external anti-China forces to provoke with \"independence\" is doomed to fail.\nA reporter asked: US Senator Scott visited Taiwan on July 7 and advocated strengthening cooperation with Taiwan. What comment do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220708_12450729.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, July 11 (Xinhua). Recently, after the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government and the Macao Special Administrative Region Government detected positive results for SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid on the outer packaging samples of mangoes from Taiwan, they adopted measures such as suspending sales, removing products from shelves, and suspending import applications. This drew extensive attacks from the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and figures like Wu Zhaoxie. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on July 11 by saying: The actions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities show that they have no desire to solve the problem at all, and that they place their own narrow political interests above the interests of the people and business operators on the island.\nZhu Fenglian said that regarding the detection of positive SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid in mangoes imported from Taiwan, China, into the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, the Hong Kong SAR Government and the Macao SAR Government have issued announcements explaining the relevant policies and circumstances. The practices of the SAR governments conform to the regulations and common practices of trade inspection and quarantine, meet the epidemic prevention requirements for responding to the COVID-19 pandemic, and are necessary to protect the health and safety of residents of the SARs. We support these measures.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have also conducted nucleic acid testing on imported goods, but when it involves the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, they have unreasonably engaged in political manipulation, politicized necessary epidemic prevention measures, and used so-called “international norms” and “economic coercion,” which do not exist, to maliciously smear and mislead the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220711_12451223.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-12","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","On July 11, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi delivered a speech at the ASEAN Secretariat, calling for upholding peace, independence, development and inclusiveness, and resolutely practicing open regionalism. Can you share some details on that?","Yesterday, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi visited the ASEAN Secretariat and delivered a speech on China’s propositions and suggestions on deepening China-ASEAN relations and promoting regional peace and prosperity, which was warmly received by officials of the ASEAN Secretariat and participants of the event.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi reviewed the extraordinary development path traversed by China and ASEAN since the establishment of dialogue relations 30 years ago, especially the most encouraging, touching, heartening and gratifying cooperation outcomes and highlights in China-ASEAN relations over the past 10 years thanks to the strategic guidance and personal commitment of President Xi Jinping and leaders of ASEAN countries. Between China and ASEAN, relations have stayed ahead in many areas. China and ASEAN have been standing together in solidarity to fight COVID-19. The economic cooperation and trade has thrived. Security cooperation has been making steady progress. Wang Yi noted that with this year being the first year for building the China-ASEAN comprehensive strategic partnership, China will continue to support ASEAN Centrality, call for settling differences in the Asian way, pursue firmly its open strategy for development, resolutely advance cooperation in science, technology and innovation and carry forward Asian values, so as to write a new chapter of regional cooperation and Asian vitalization.\nWang Yi stressed that there are two completely different trends concerning the future of Asia. One advocates open regionalism, true multilateralism, a development-first approach and mutually beneficial cooperation; it aims to help countries in the region emerge from the pandemic and achieve all-round development as soon as possible. The other pursues a relapse into the obsolete Cold War mentality and closed group politics, and classifies countries in the region based on their values; it attempts to divide the regional economy into different blocs and even apply the NATO approach to Asia-Pacific security. China’s choice is to join hands with ASEAN members and other regional countries to adhere to the vision of peace, development, independence and inclusiveness, firmly uphold open regionalism and, by drawing experience and wisdom from Asian civilizations and practices, constantly add new dimensions to open regionalism. We need to always uphold the concept of peaceful coexistence, the goal of development and rejuvenation, the principle of independence and the spirit of openness and inclusiveness. Together, we will build a common homeland that enjoys peace, tranquility, prosperity, beautiful environment and friendship.\nWhile answering questions from the press after the speech, State Councilor Wang Yi stressed that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. Although the two sides have been politically against each other for a long time, China’s state sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been split. This is the real status quo of the Taiwan question. Stability across the Taiwan Strait is underpinned by the one-China principle, which constitutes part of the post-WWII world order. The more unequivocal we are about upholding the one-China principle and the more forceful our measures are to contain and prevent separation, the more likely it is to ensure peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and peace and prosperity in the region.","","https://web.archive.org/web/2022id_/https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202207/t20220712_10718946.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220712_10718935.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-12","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","A question regarding William Lai, the Taiwan “Vice President”, who has visited Japan to attend the funeral of former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe. This represents the highest-level official to visit Japan from Taiwan in decades. Does the Chinese foreign ministry have a comment on this visit?","I need to correct you first. Taiwan is part of China. There is no so-called “Taiwan Vice President”. After the sudden and unfortunate passing of former Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, the Taiwan authorities have sought to engage in political manipulation and benefit politically by taking advantage of the incident. Their political calculations will not succeed. The Chinese side has lodged stern representations to the Japanese side both in Beijing and Tokyo and has made our position absolutely clear.","","https://web.archive.org/web/2022id_/https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202207/t20220712_10718946.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220712_10718935.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-12","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The Japanese foreign minister said William Lai was participating in relevant activities in a private capacity and that Japan’s basic policy toward Taiwan remains unchanged. What’s China’s comment?","I have made clear China’s position.","","https://web.archive.org/web/2022id_/https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/xwfw_665399/s2510_665401/2511_665403/202207/t20220712_10718946.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220712_10718935.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 13 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 13th when asked: The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory, and there is no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” The “Haixun 06,” as a large integrated law enforcement vessel, is mainly used for offshore patrol and rescue, investigation and handling of maritime traffic accidents, and ship pollution monitoring. It is of great significance for maintaining navigation order in the coastal waters of Fujian and ensuring water transport safety. We advise the DPP authorities to stop exploiting this issue, engaging in political manipulation and confusing public perception.\nA reporter asked: The mainland’s “Haixun 06” has been formally commissioned and has become the first large patrol and rescue vessel in the Taiwan Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has claimed that “‘the median line of the Taiwan Strait’ is a concrete practice of the two sides’ ‘mutual non-aggression and non-crossing’” and that “the mainland must not use the excuse of performing official duties to undermine the status quo in the Taiwan Strait or challenge international order.” What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220713_12452043.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 14 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 14th when asked that just as compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait eagerly expressed at the 14th Straits Forum their strong desire to strengthen exchanges and cooperation and jointly promote integrated development, the DPP authorities jumped out to peddle the \"two-state theory\" and smear and…","Zhu Fenglian said that Taiwan is a sacred part of Chinese territory; its historical context is clear, and its legal facts are plain. Thirty years ago, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan reached the “1992 Consensus,” in which each side orally expressed that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” This clearly indicates the position and attitude of adhering to the one-China principle and pursuing national reunification. It is black and white, crystal clear.\nShe said that the one-China principle is the political foundation of cross-Strait relations, and the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the key to ensuring the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We firmly oppose any words or deeds that distort, deny, or slander the “1992 Consensus” and its core essence.\nZhu Fenglian said that at present, the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait is that “Taiwan independence” forces collude with external forces to make trouble. It is precisely the DPP authorities, who constantly seek “independence” and provoke, and external forces attempting to “use Taiwan to contain China,” that undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. No one should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220714_12452458.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office responded to questions on July 16, saying: As agreed upon by relevant parties in Shanghai and Taipei, the '2022 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum' will be held via video conference on the 19th. Over the years, as an important institutionalized exchange platform between Shanghai and Taipei, the forum has played a positive role in promoting exchanges and cooperation in various fields between the two cities and in enhancing the people's livelihood and well-being of residents of both places; its achievements are plain for all to see. Strengthening cross-strait exchanges and cooperation is the will of the people and the trend of the times. We support extensive and in-depth exchanges between cities on both sides of the Strait, sharing the dividends of cooperation and benefiting compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220716_12452915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-18","Wang Wenbin","The following question was raised after the press conference","According to reports, the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said in a statement on July 15 that the US State Department has approved the potential sale of military technical assistance to the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the US” worth an estimated $108 million. Do you have any comment?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The sales gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this. We have made serious demarches to the US side over this.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, revoke the above-mentioned arms sales plan, stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan and stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will continue to take resolute and strong measures to firmly defend its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347326.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220718_10722922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-07-18","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to reports, U.S. Defense Secretary Austin recently said that the Chinese military's vigorous development of its military strength has made it a rival of equal strength to the U.S. military in Asia and even globally, representing a 'challenge of steadily mounting pressure' from the United States. Admiral Aquilino, commander of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command, further said that China has rapidly modernized…","For some time now, senior officials of the US defense establishment and military have clung to prejudice and distorted facts. In order to compete for military budgets at home and \"set the tone\" abroad, they have pinned labels on China and groundlessly hyped up the development of China's military strength. China firmly opposes this and has lodged serious representations with the US side.\nFor many years, in order to maintain its global hegemony, the US has continuously and substantially increased its defense spending. Despite possessing the world's most advanced weapons and equipment and the largest network of overseas military bases, it has shown no restraint and has recklessly expanded. From Yugoslavia to Libya, from Syria to Afghanistan, wherever the American war machine has gone, smoke of war has risen everywhere and devastation has been left behind, directly driving the lives of innocent people in war-torn areas into desperation. After the US has lost its credibility and its image has collapsed, it instead accuses others of being “challenges that press forward step by step,” which is utterly absurd.\nRegarding trilateral nuclear submarine cooperation among the US, UK and Australia, we believe this constitutes a serious risk of nuclear proliferation, contrary to the purpose and objectives of the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, and has caused increasing vigilance and opposition among more and more countries. However, the US, UK and Australia ignore international community concerns and insist on advancing nuclear submarine cooperation. This once again highlights their double standards on non-proliferation issues, which apply “cooperation when convenient, abandonment when not.” The world belongs to all people, not to be the exclusive domain or private property of any power or group. The Asia-Pacific region is the common home of the peoples of Asia-Pacific countries, and it cannot be tolerated for a few countries banded together to spread fog and smoke of conflict, shift their problems onto neighbors, and treat others as enemies. China will firmly pursue a defensive national defense policy, will actively promote building regional security cooperation frameworks and new security partnerships in the Asia-Pacific region, and will continue to play a constructive role in promoting security dialogue and mutual trust and cooperation in the Asia-Pacific region.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-19/9806463.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-07-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 18 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 18th, pointing out that the US has time and again sold weapons to Taiwan, China, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué. This indulges and supports “Taiwan independence” forces and seriously violates the US commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.” The US’s actions fully expose its sinister intention to arm Taiwan and “use Taiwan to contain China.” We urge the US side to abandon its scheme of playing the “Taiwan card,” and to stop further playing with fire on the Taiwan question.\nA reporter asked: On July 15, a US government department decided to sell to Taiwan, China, items such as tank and armored vehicle parts worth about 108 million US dollars. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.\nShe pointed out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are using the hard-earned money of Taiwan compatriots to buy weapons, attempting to “resist reunification by force.” This will only further harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots and push Taiwan compatriots into the fire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220718_12453408.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-19","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Financial Times reported that US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi plans to visit Taiwan next month. How do you comment about this?","The Chinese side has repeatedly stated its stern position on this. We firmly oppose any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region. The US Congress is part of the US government and supposed to strictly adhere to the US’s one-China policy. If Speaker Pelosi visits Taiwan, it would seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués and harm China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It will have a severe negative impact on the political foundation of China-US relations, and send a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes such a visit.\nWe urge the US side to adhere to the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués. The US must not arrange for Speaker Pelosi to visit the Taiwan region and must stop official interactions with Taiwan, stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and follow through on the US’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”. Should the US side insist on doing otherwise, China will take strong and resolute measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US must assume full responsibility for any ensuing consequences.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347327.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220719_10723410.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-19","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","It is reported that US State Department spokesperson Ned Price said during his briefing that the US has “obligations under the Taiwan Relations Act” to “make available to Taiwan defense articles and services necessary to enable Taiwan to maintain a sufficient self-defense capability”, adding that this is “entirely consistent with our ‘one China’ policy”. Do you have any comment?","Yesterday, we made clear China’s stern position on the US’s latest proposed arms sale to Taiwan. I must reiterate that China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this. We have made serious demarchés to the US side over this.\nThe so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” is a domestic legislation unilaterally adopted by the US. It seriously breaches widely recognized international laws and basic norms in international relations and runs counter to the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués. China has never recognized the Act and has always rejected it. A domestic law like this is no justification or rationale for the US to brazenly interfere in China’s internal affairs and sell arms to Taiwan.\nBe it the one-China principle or the one-China policy, both terms have “one China” at their core. Acknowledging that Taiwan is part of China is a solemn commitment made by the US in the three China-US joint communiqués. US arms sales to Taiwan gravely violate the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués, embolden the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and escalate tensions across the Taiwan Strait. The US side needs to immediately stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and follow through on the US government statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347327.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220719_10723410.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-19","Zhao Lijian","NHK","Former US Defense Secretary paid a visit to Taiwan and met with Tsai Ing-wen. He said that Washington’s one-China policy has “outlived its usefulness” and it is time for the Biden administration to review the “strategic ambiguity” on issues relating to security across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment?","The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and an established international consensus. China firmly opposes the attempt by any force or individual to play the “Taiwan card”, interfere in China’s internal affairs and undermine China’s core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347327.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220719_10723410.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-19","Zhao Lijian","AFP","The European Parliament Vice President Nicola Beer is visiting Taiwan this week. She said today that Europe must stand firm with Taiwan and avoid turning a blind eye to the mainland’s threats to Taiwan. Do you have any response to these comments?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a widely recognized basic norm in international relations and the political foundation of China-Europe relations. The European Parliament is an official institution of the European Union. Hence its members and senior officials are expected to abide by the one-China principle.\nOver the past two years, the European Parliament has promulgated multiple Taiwan-related resolutions to support and embolden “Taiwan independence” forces. Such moves have gravely violated the one-China principle and poisoned the atmosphere of China-Europe relations. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between the EU side and the Taiwan region. We urge the EU side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, speak and act with prudence on issues related to Taiwan, and prevent any serious disruption in China-Europe relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347327.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220719_10723410.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","A media outlet asked: It is understood that the 2022 Cross-Strait Youth Summit will soon be held in Beijing. Please introduce the relevant situation.\nTaiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on July 19, said that the series of activities of the 2022 Cross-Strait Youth Summit will be held in Beijing from mid-July to the end of September. The opening ceremony, main forum and special seminars of the summit will take place from July 21 to 22, and before the end of September, 25 supporting series activities and practical benefit projects will be carried out successively. Since 2018, Beijing has successfully held four sessions of the Beijing Summit on Cross-Strait Youth Exchange and Cooperation, with good results and positive impact. This year, the summit's scale has been further raised and it has been officially named the “Cross-Strait Youth Summit.” Its content is richer and its participants more extensive, fully reflecting the strong desire of cross-strait youth to strengthen exchange and cooperation.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping recently sent a reply letter to Taiwan youth attending the Straits Forum, fully reflecting his care and concern for Taiwan youth and his earnest expectations for cross-strait youth. Cross-strait youth are deeply moved and encouraged. The 2022 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, with the theme “Joining Hands to Paint Youth, Striving Forward in the New Era,” is co-hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Ministry of Education, the All-China Youth Federation and the Beijing Municipal People's Government. More than 120 representatives, including heads of Taiwan youth organizations, outstanding Taiwan youth and representatives of the Beijing Youth Federation, will attend the summit. The summit has invited Lin Yifu, member of the Standing Committee of the National Committee of the CPPCC and Dean of the Institute of New Structural Economics at Peking University, and Ye Cong, Vice Chairman of the All-China Youth Federation, chief pilot of the “Jiaolong” manned deep-sea submersible and chief designer of the “Fendouzhe” (Striver), to deliver keynote speeches. Five special seminars will be held, on “Growth and Talent,” “Entrepreneurship and Employment,” “Era and Fashion,” “Marriage, Love and Life,” and “Integration and Development,” along with 25 supporting activities and practical benefit projects, including the “Rejuvenation Needs Me” cross-strait youth running relay.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220719_12453741.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 19: In response to a question on the 19th, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, pointed out that regarding Pelosi's plan to visit Taiwan, China has repeatedly stated its solemn position. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, and firmly oppose Pelosi's visit to Taiwan. For some time, certain members of the U.S.…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities rely on colluding with external anti-China forces to seek “independence.” Regardless of the name or form they adopt, their only fate will be failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220719_12453780.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 19 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, responding to questions on the 19th, said that Yu Hsi-kun obstinately adheres to the “Taiwan independence” position and, by any means, carries out provocations to pursue “independence,” attempting to win over anti-China forces in some countries to pursue “independence by relying on foreign powers.” But no matter how they act, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and cannot change that they will ultimately face legal reckoning.\nA reporter asked: “Taiwan independence” diehard Yu Hsi-kun made a sneaky visit to the Czech Republic, and the Czech Senate hung a “fake flag.” Reportedly, Yu will also visit other European countries. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian responded with the above remarks.\nShe said we urge the relevant countries to recognize the grave harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, abide by the one-China principle and the commitments made on the Taiwan question, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220719_12453781.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-07-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Vice President of the European Parliament Bell is making a visit to the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities said this visit demonstrates the European Parliament's “strong support” for Taiwan. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 19: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian responded to questions on the 19th, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Some members of the European Parliament visited the Taiwan region of China, which seriously violates the one-China principle and constitutes a serious interference in China's internal affairs. We urge the relevant persons of the European Parliament to abide by the one-China principle and stop their wrong conduct on the Taiwan question.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities, in collusion with external anti-China forces, have staged one farce after another of \"independence-seeking\" provocation, but this cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220719_12453803.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-20","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","The European Parliament Vice President said when meeting the leader of the Taiwan region in Taipei that the EU urges China to “refrain from its threatening gestures” against the Taiwan region, and expressed support for Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a widely recognized basic norm in international relations and the political foundation of China-Europe relations. The European Parliament is an official institution of the European Union. Hence its members and senior officials are expected to abide by the one-China principle.\nOver the past two years, the European Parliament has adopted multiple Taiwan-related resolutions to support and embolden “Taiwan independence” forces. Such moves have gravely violated the one-China principle and poisoned the atmosphere of China-Europe relations. China firmly opposes all forms of official interactions between the EU side and the Taiwan region. We urge the EU side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, speak and act with prudence on issues related to Taiwan, and prevent any serious disruption in China-Europe relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347328.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220720_10725171.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-21","Wang Wenbin","MASTV","On US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s possible trip to Taiwan, White House Press Secretary said Pelosi’s visit has not been locked in. Do you have any comment?","The Chinese side has repeatedly stated its stern position on firmly opposing US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan. The US Congress is part of the US government and supposed to strictly adhere to the US’s commitment on the Taiwan question. If Speaker Pelosi visits Taiwan, it would seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations in the three China-US joint communiqués and harm China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It will have a severe negative impact on the political foundation of China-US relations, and send a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Should the US side insist on making the visit, China will act strongly to resolutely respond to it and take countermeasures. We mean what we say.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347329.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220721_10725546.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-21","Wang Wenbin","AFP","CIA’s chief William Burns said at a security forum yesterday that Sri Lanka’s decision to take on debt-heavy Chinese investment was a factor in its economic troubles. He also said that Russia’s experience in Ukraine is making China rethink when and how to resolve the Taiwan question. Do you have any response to his remarks?","China and Sri Lanka are close neighbors with traditional friendship. We have always respected, trusted and supported each other, established the strategic cooperative partnership based on sincere mutual assistance and ever-lasting friendship, and conducted comprehensive, mutually beneficial cooperation in various areas. China will as always follow a friendly policy toward Sri Lanka. We stand ready to support and help the efforts of the Sri Lankan government and people in stabilizing the situation and revitalizing the economy to the best of our capacity, and bring bilateral relations to new heights.\nThe US official’s groundless accusation against China cannot hide the truth from people in Sri Lanka and elsewhere in the world, nor can it hold back the deepening of China-Sri Lanka friendly cooperation.\nOn Ukraine, we urge the US side to face up to its due responsibilities as the one that created the crisis, and work actively toward resolving the issue through dialogue and ending bloc confrontation, instead of fanning the flames. The Ukraine issue and the Taiwan question are fundamentally different. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and not to interfere in China’s internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347329.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220721_10725546.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-22","Wang Wenbin","NHK","The Japanese government released the Defense of Japan 2022 white paper, which says that China has become a grave security concern to the region and the international community. What is China’s comment?","The new Defense of Japan white paper contains groundless accusations against China’s defense policy, normal defense development and legitimate maritime activities, deliberately plays up the so-called “China threat”, and grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs on the Taiwan question. China strongly deplores and firmly rejects this. We have made stern demarchés to the Japanese side.\nChina is committed to the path of peaceful development, and follows a defense policy that is defensive in nature. China’s defense building is aimed at upholding our sovereignty, security and development interests. It is legitimate, reasonable and beyond reproach. Military cooperation including joint naval patrol between China and relevant countries is consistent with international law and established international practice. It does not target any particular country. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliating islands have always been part of China’s territory. The Chinese side’s maritime activities in the waters of Diaoyu Dao are legitimate exercise of sovereign rights. Taiwan is an inviolable and inalienable part of China’s sovereignty. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference.\nI would like to stress that due to the recent history of overseas aggression waged by Japanese militarism, Japan’s moves in the military and security fields have always been closely followed by its Asian neighbors including China and the international community. In this latest white paper, Japan has openly added content about revising relevant defense documents by the end of this year, further increasing its defense budget, and developing so-called counter-strike capabilities. All these give rise to the concern that Japan is deviating further from the path of pacifist and exclusively defense-oriented strategy. We urge the Japanese side to immediately stop the erroneous practice of arbitrarily hyping up security threats in the neighborhood to justify its military build-up, heed the voice of the international community, deeply reflect on the history of aggression, stay committed to the path of peaceful development, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347330.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220722_10726447.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","XINHUA, Beijing, July 22 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a query on the 22nd, said: In the six years since the DPP authorities came to power, they have engaged in large-scale political manipulation for the narrow interests of their party, desperately colluded with external forces, and continuously engaged in provocations for “independence,” creating cross-Strait confrontation and pushing Taiwan…","Zhu Fenglian said: The DPP authorities distort and smear, refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" and seek to change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, unilaterally undermining the common political foundation across the Strait. They clamor for so-called \"mutual non-subordination,\" constantly churn out separatist fallacies full of the \"two-state theory,\" manipulate \"anti-China and hatred of China,\" and even openly advocate war. They openly tamper with history, castrate and distort the historical connection between the mainland and Taiwan, promote \"de-Sinicization,\" and forcibly sever the flesh-and-blood ties between the people of Taiwan and Chinese culture and the Chinese nation. They do not hesitate to serve as \"vanguards\" for external forces seeking to contain China's development, repeatedly provoking trouble and selling out the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. They ignore the wishes of the Taiwan public to improve the economy and livelihoods and to share the dividends of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and they do everything possible to restrict and obstruct cross-Strait civil exchanges and cooperation. To call these perverse actions \"goodwill\" is entirely self-deception.\n\"These sophistries of the DPP authorities, which distort facts and use glib words, cannot deceive the people on the island,\" she said.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220722_12454829.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-25","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","According to the Financial Times, China has heightened its warnings to the US over the possible US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan. These warnings or threats have been perceived to be stronger than in the past. According to the sources of the Financial Times, they may include a possible military response. Is it accurate? And if there may be a possible military response, what kind of response is…","The Chinese side has repeatedly made clear to the US side our serious concern over Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan and our firm opposition to the visit. We are fully prepared for any eventuality. If the US side insists on making the visit, the Chinese side will take firm and strong measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US must assume full responsibility for any serious consequence arising thereof.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347331.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220725_10727711.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-25","Zhao Lijian","Xinhua News Agency","It is reported that German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock said in an interview on July 22 that China no longer accepts One Country, Two Systems, Germany should take China’s declaration on “attacking Taiwan” seriously just like the US and this is why Germany and the US worked out the strategy of NATO. Baerbock also said that Germany will work with partners to reduce economic dependency on China. Do you have…","The remarks of the German official you mentioned reflect some typical biased views on China. I would like to stress four points.\nFirst, China always stands for respecting the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all countries and is committed to the path of peaceful development. Among the major countries, China has the best peace and security record. We have never started a war or occupied one inch of foreign land. China does not pose a threat to any country.\nSecond, the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. China is committed to the policy of peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems. No one should underestimate the strong resolve, will and ability of the Chinese people to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. Anyone who dares to challenge China’s red line will find themselves on a collision course with the Chinese people.\nThird, the last thing the security and stability in the Asia-Pacific needs is disruption from NATO. The 21st century is characterized by multi-polarity. Gone is the era in which a few Western countries called the shots on everything.\nFourth, economic globalization and trade liberalization are the trend of the times. China is the largest trading partner of over 120 countries and regions. This is the result of the combined force of the market and the choices of businesses. Not even so-called “democracy” or “values” can replace the economic principles of the free market.\nI would like to remind certain Western politicians that sticking to the outdated Cold War mentality and bloc confrontation is not going to work. Anyone doing so will only fall into the trap they dig for themselves. Only by upholding norms in international relations, drawing lessons from history and reality, and adopting the right perception on China based on facts, can we set the right tone for the bilateral relationship which should be win-win in nature, and together safeguard the peace and security of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347331.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220725_10727711.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-25","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","A moment ago, you said that China is getting seriously prepared for any visit by Pelosi to Taiwan. Could you offer any details about it? Is that a military response that China is preparing, or is it a diplomatic response or some other?","I’ve just made our position very clear. If the US side insists on making the visit, the Chinese side will act strongly to resolutely respond to it and take countermeasures.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347331.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220725_10727711.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 25 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a question on the 25th, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. The Japanese government's Defense White Paper has no right to make irresponsible…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that attempting to collude with external forces to seek “Taiwan independence” by relying on outsiders, or to seek “Taiwan independence” by force, is a dead end. Those who betray national interests will surely be severely punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220725_12455412.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-07-26","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Today Taiwan President Tsai Ing-wen boarded a naval warship for only the second time in her six years in office, during which she lauded the military’s determination to defend the island whilst overseeing the annual naval and air exercises. What’s the Chinese foreign ministry’s comment?","I need to make it clear first that there is no so-called “President” in Taiwan. Please pay attention to the term you use. I also want to take this opportunity to make it clear to the Taiwan authorities that the path of “Taiwan independence” will lead to a dead end. If Taiwan wants to confront the mainland militarily, it will only find it futile and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347332.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220726_10728257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-26","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","Today marks the 77th anniversary of the release of the Potsdam Proclamation. How does China see the positive role of this document?","On July 26, 1945, China, the US and the UK issued the Potsdam Proclamation. This document, together with the Cairo Declaration released by the three countries in 1943 and other documents on international law, constitute the legal cornerstone of the post-war international order and played an important role in consolidating the outcomes of the victory of the world anti-fascist war and in safeguarding world peace.\nThe Cairo Declaration stipulates clearly that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan and the Penghu Islands, shall be restored to China. The Potsdam Proclamation states that these terms shall be carried out. In 1945, Japan signed the Instrument of Surrender, which explicitly states that the Japanese side accepts the provisions set forth in the Potsdam Proclamation.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a fundamental principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758. It is the premise on which the PRC established diplomatic relations with 181 countries. It is an established international consensus and a widely recognized basic norm in international relations. However, certain individuals are openly challenging the legal force of the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. They even openly broke commitments and keep challenging China’s red line on the Taiwan question. This is an act of trampling on historical facts and justice, challenging the post-war international order and undermining international rule of law. This is an affront to the outcomes of the victory of the world anti-fascist war.\nThe one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. When the one-China principle is fully recognized and earnestly followed, the Taiwan Strait would remain calm and tranquil. Otherwise, there would be dark clouds or even violent storms across the Taiwan Strait. To remember the history of the issuance of the Potsdam Proclamation can remind the world that to forget history means to betray it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347332.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220726_10728257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-26","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","According to reports, former US Secretary of State Dr. Kissinger said in a recent interview that the US and its allies must maintain their strength, while also respecting China as a participant in the international order. A “cooling” of rhetoric by the US and China over Taiwan would ease tension, reduce the potential for conflict, and improve relations, he said. What’s China’s comment?","We appreciate Mr. Kissinger’s remarks. As the world’s top two economies and permanent members of the UN Security Council, China and the US must make the relationship work and not mess it up. We urge the US side to view China and China-US relations objectively, follow through on the five assurances reiterated by President Biden and the positive statements by Secretary of State Blinken, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués in particular, properly and prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, and work with China to find the right way forward for the two countries to get along under the new circumstances by following the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347332.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220726_10728257.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-07-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","The US Indo-Pacific Command recently issued a statement saying that representatives of the Indo-Pacific Command, the Pacific Fleet, and the Pacific Air Force recently held, by video, the working group meeting of the US-China Military Maritime Consultative Agreement (MMCA) and the annual admirals' meeting with representatives of the Navy and Air Force of the People's Liberation Army of China. A spokesperson for…","From December 15 to 17, the Chinese and U.S. militaries held this year's Maritime Military Security Consultative Agreement (MMCA) working meeting via video conference. Both sides exchanged views on the current maritime and air security situation between China and the United States, evaluated the implementation of the “Rules of Behavior for the Safety of Air and Maritime Encounters between China and the United States,” discussed measures to improve China-U.S. maritime military security, and preliminarily exchanged views on matters related to the 2022 working meeting.\nThe Chinese side clearly pointed out to the U.S. side that the safety of ships and aircraft is inseparable from national security. The prolonged, high-intensity close-in reconnaissance, surveying and highly targeted exercises by U.S. military ships and aircraft in the sea and airspace directly facing China, and their frequent infringing and provocative actions, are the root cause of China-U.S. maritime and air military security problems. Only if the U.S. side stops its hostile maritime and air force operations can China-U.S. maritime and air military security problems be fundamentally resolved.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-26/9812299.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-07-26","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","According to reports, the China-Vietnam medical joint exercise “Peace Rescue-2021” was successfully held recently in Mong Cai City, Quang Ninh Province, Vietnam. Please further introduce the relevant details and main features of this exercise.","In accordance with the annual plan for military exchange and cooperation between the Chinese and Vietnamese armed forces, the two militaries organized and carried out the “Peaceful Rescue-2021” joint military medical support exercise in Mong Cai City, Quang Ninh Province, Vietnam, from December 6 to 12, with more than 600 participants from both sides. This exercise has the following three main features:\nFirst, the exercise theme was clear. Closely adhering to the lofty mission of military medical support to “save the dying and heal the wounded,” and in deep alignment with the joint exercise theme of “Peaceful Rescue,” the exercise centered on two main threads, disaster relief and epidemic response. Organization and command, casualty treatment, epidemic prevention and control, and support and assurance were carried out to combat-realistic standards, honing the two militaries' ability to coordinate action and handle emergencies in military medical support.\nSecond, the exercise insisted on deep joint operations. In training subjects such as joint medical support command, joint on-site rescue, mass casualty handling, and joint epidemic prevention and control, both sides learned from each other and explored a joint rescue model characterized by “coordinated command, real-time information sharing, unified allocation of forces, and overall use of materials,” providing a useful reference for carrying out international humanitarian medical rescue missions.\nThird, the exercise employed innovative methods. The exercise incorporated the latest military medical concepts, emphasized the use of advanced equipment, and used real-time visual new technologies to test and enhance the supporting capacity of the military medical systems of both militaries.\nThis exercise was the first live-troop military medical exercise organized by the two militaries, and it was also the first time since the COVID-19 outbreak that our military medical forces were deployed overseas as a complete unit for a joint military medical exercise abroad. The exercise was safe and smooth throughout, all participating officers and soldiers remained “free of infection,” and the comradely friendship and mutual trust in cooperation between the two militaries were deepened.\nVideo: Liu Mingjiu, Bi Yunwei, Teng Huaijin","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-26/9812592.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-07-27","Zhao Lijian","AFP","A US official said that if Pelosi goes to Taiwan, the military would increase its movement of forces in the Asia-Pacific, including fighter jets. What is your comment?","Perhaps you missed our briefings in the past few days. We have repeatedly made clear our our firm opposition to Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan. If the US side insists on making the visit and challenges China’s red line, it will be met with resolute countermeasures. The US must bear all consequences arising thereof.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347333.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220727_10728801.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-28","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","Newt Gingrich, who visited Taiwan when he was the US House Speaker, said on July 25 that Nancy Pelosi absolutely has to go to Taiwan so that China understand the US is not a “paper tiger”. “We had a lot of tension in 1996, 97, and President Clinton and I collaborated in trying to send very strong signals, including putting American aircraft carriers in the Taiwan Strait,” he said. Do you have any comment?","Newt Gingrich has a serious track record on issues related to Taiwan. There is no merit in his extremely irresponsible remarks. This only proves once again how some US politicians would stoke tensions in China-US relations, turmoil across the Taiwan Strait and instability in the world only to benefit themselves.\nOver the past few days, the Chinese side has repeatedly made clear to the US side its firm opposition to the potential visit of Speaker Pelosi to Taiwan. Apart from the foreign ministry spokesperson, China’s Ministry of National Defense and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council also made statements on the issue. The Defense Ministry Spokesperson said that if the US side insists on making the visit, the Chinese military will never sit idly by, and will certainly take strong and resolute measures to thwart any interference by external forces and secessionist attempts for “Taiwan independence”. We Chinese mean what we say.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347334.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220728_10729417.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-07-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","It is reported that the 21-style combat uniforms and work uniforms recently reissued across the armed forces have drawn great attention from all sectors of society. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation regarding the reissuance of the 21-style military uniforms.","With the approval of the Central Military Commission, starting this winter, all troops across the military will gradually be issued the Type 21 combat training uniforms and work uniforms. This uniform change implements Xi Jinping Thought on Strengthening the Military and the new era military strategic guidelines, focuses on preparing for war and fighting battles, lets requirements guide the approach, designs by function, and promotes continued optimization of the varieties, style structures, and materials and craftsmanship of our military uniforms.\nThe Type 21 combat training uniforms and work uniforms are an important component of building a new-era military uniform system with Chinese military characteristics. The Type 21 combat training uniforms mainly include camouflage combat training uniforms, special duty combat training uniforms, and combat boots, to be worn for combat, training, combat readiness, duty, and the performance of non-war military operations. Camouflage combat training uniforms are differentiated by colors such as jungle and desert; special duty combat training uniforms include combat training uniforms for warships, aviation, and ground crew, to meet the needs of personnel in special posts; combat boots (shoes) are divided into general-purpose and special-purpose. The Type 21 work uniforms are a new series in the adjustment and optimization of our military uniforms, featuring a jacket style design, divided into spring/autumn and winter work uniforms, using new service colors, and matched with varieties such as large (rolled) brim caps and work uniform leather shoes, to be worn for office work and other general daily activities.\nThe main considerations for this uniform change are: First, highlight preparing for war and fighting battles. Following the steps of prioritizing combat readiness and issuing urgently needed items first, the camouflage combat training uniforms and the combat training uniforms for warships, aviation, and ground crew were made the first batch of varieties to be issued, reflecting a clear orientation toward preparing for war and fighting battles and prioritizing the urgent needs of troops' combat training. Second, adhere to frugal uniform changes. Expenses are arranged scientifically and reasonably; on the basis of making full use of existing military clothing, new varieties are gradually introduced, the replacement cycle is extended, and old items are replaced with new ones as they wear out. This both saves budget expenditure and makes full use of inventory, maximizing the efficiency of resource use. Third, emphasize steady and orderly progress. Taking into account the necessity and feasibility, research and finalization, and progress and effectiveness, we adhere to steady advancement, introducing one variety once it matures, issuing them step by step and in an orderly sequence, and gradually raising the standard of dress for officers and soldiers.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-28/9814511.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-07-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","On December 27, U.S. local time, the U.S. President signed the “2022 National Defense Authorization Act,” which includes multiple provisions concerning China. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The United States recently enacted the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2022,” which contains a number of negative clauses targeting China. The Act is full of Cold War mentality and ideological prejudice, hypes the “China threat theory,” viciously smears China’s national defense policy and military development, makes groundless accusations against China on issues such as Taiwan and Xinjiang, incites stronger containment of China in regions such as the Asia-Pacific and Latin America, instigates economic, trade and technological competition with China, and slanders China’s normal exchanges and cooperation with relevant countries. The Act seriously interferes in China’s internal affairs, seriously harms China’s national sovereignty, security and development interests, seriously damages mutual trust between China and the United States, and seriously poisons China-U.S. relations between the two countries’ militaries. China expresses strong dissatisfaction with and firmly opposes this.\nChina has consistently adhered to the path of peaceful development and a defensive national defense policy, and has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, a maintainer of international order and a provider of public goods. By contrast, the United States has for many years frequently launched wars against other countries, causing large numbers of civilian casualties and displacement, and is the greatest threat to regional and world peace and stability. The United States’ rough interference in China’s internal affairs, its hyping of the China threat, its smearing of China’s development and its emphasis on competition with China are in fact bringing relations between the two countries and their militaries into a dangerous situation.\nChina urges the United States to abandon the zero-sum game mentality, view China’s national defense and military development objectively and rationally, stop enacting hostile policies toward China, stop casting China as an opponent or even an enemy of the United States, and do more things that benefit the healthy and stable development of relations between the two countries and their militaries.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-28/9814617.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-07-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (digest; reported as answer to a reporter question)","This year, the COVID-19 pandemic has continued to spread worldwide, and the great changes unseen in a century are deepening. Faced with a complex and changing international situation, the Chinese military has actively carried out international military cooperation and achieved fruitful results. The PLA Daily published an article on December 23 reviewing the highlights of the Chinese military's international…","2021 was a milestone year in the history of the Party and the state. This year, the international military cooperation work of the Chinese military thoroughly implemented Xi Jinping Thought on Strengthening the Military and the responsibility system under the Chairman of the Central Military Commission. Keeping in view the once-in-a-century great changes unfolding in the world and the overall strategy of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, it strengthened strategic planning, actively pursued innovation and progress, and made new and important contributions to safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests, to maintaining world peace and stability, and to serving the building of a community with a shared future for mankind. Its main features are as follows:\nFirst, it closely centered on the theme of the Party's centenary. Through high-level exchanges, professional exchanges, multilateral meetings and other international military cooperation activities, it vigorously promoted the great achievements of the Party's first hundred years, and organized visits by military attachés from nearly 70 countries stationed in China to the exhibition “Never Forget Original Aspiration, Keep Mission in Mind” on the history of the Communist Party of China. At the same time, defense departments and military leaders of Russia, Cambodia, Vietnam, Laos, Namibia, Syria, Belarus, Fiji, Cuba and other countries expressed good wishes to the Chinese side through letters, phone calls, and articles.\nSecond, it effectively maintained overall strategic stability. China-Russia military relations maintained high-level operation, and strategic coordination achieved new breakthroughs; China-US military relations remained generally stable amid ups and downs; China and European defense departments and militaries maintained strategic communication; exchanges and cooperation with neighboring countries deepened continuously, and the concept of building a community of shared future with neighboring countries took deeper root; military exchanges and cooperation with the broad mass of developing countries were strengthened; and true multilateralism was upheld and practiced, promoting international cooperation on arms control compliance.\nThird, it served the core duties of preparing for and fighting wars. Under the conditions of normalized COVID-19 prevention and control, it actively organized and took part in joint exercises, training and competitions with foreign militaries, such as “Western·Joint-2021,” “Common Destiny-2021,” and “International Military Competition-2021.” While deepening military mutual trust with the militaries of relevant countries, these activities raised the level of combat-oriented training of the troops.\nFourth, it practiced the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind. It implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping's important announcement that China's COVID-19 vaccines would be treated as a global public good, and actively carried out international anti-epidemic cooperation. Building on last year's provision of material assistance to the armed forces of more than 50 countries, this year it provided vaccines and material assistance to the armed forces of more than 30 countries. It continuously provided international public security goods to the international community and actively took part in international peacekeeping, far-sea escort, humanitarian rescue and other operations.\nFifth, it safeguarded national sovereignty, dignity and core interests. In response to interference and provocations by some countries on issues such as Taiwan and the South China Sea, it resolutely carried out military countermeasures, organized targeted exercises and training, and at the same time made solemn representations, promptly refuted these claims, and stated its position.\nSixth, it emphasized improving strategic management capacity. The Regulations on International Military Cooperation Work, issued and implemented at the beginning of the year, clarified the main tasks and fields of cooperation in international military cooperation work, and established systems for planning, risk control, work support, and inspection and assessment. They provide a legal guarantee for further improving the overall benefits of international military cooperation in the new era and promoting innovative development of international military cooperation work.\nFor the cause of peace, we advance with firm resolve. Looking ahead to the new year, the Chinese military will resolutely fulfill its mission and tasks in the new era, faithfully practice the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind, comprehensively advance international military cooperation, provide strong strategic support for realizing the Chinese Dream of national rejuvenation, and make new and greater contributions to safeguarding world peace and promoting common development.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/07-28/9814619.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","Macau Monthly","A delegation of Japanese lawmakers, led by former Defense Minister Shigeru Ishiba, recently visited Taiwan and met with the leader of the Taiwan region. What is China’s response?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. China firmly opposes all forms of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We seriously urge the Japanese side to earnestly abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and its solemn commitment on the Taiwan question, prudently and properly handle relevant issues and not to send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rope in external forces to engage in political manipulation and benefit politically will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","PTI","We have seen the elaborate statements from both sides after yesterday’s talks between President Biden and President Xi Jinping. From China’s point of view, what exactly is the outcome, especially on the issue related to Taiwan?","With regard to the telephone conversation between the heads of state between China and the US, the Chinese side has issued a press release at the earliest time possible.\nAs for the Taiwan question, President Xi elaborated on China’s principled position on the Taiwan question. China’s opposition to official exchanges between the US and Taiwan is clear and consistent. Recently, China has made its position and attitude clear on multiple occasions. As President Xi stressed, the three Sino-US joint communiqués embody the political commitments made by the two sides, and the one-China principle is the political foundation for China-US relations. China firmly opposes separatist moves toward “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces, and never allows any room for “Taiwan independence” forces in whatever form. The position of the Chinese government and people on the Taiwan question is consistent, and resolutely safeguarding China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the firm will of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. The public opinion cannot be defied. Those who play with fire will perish by it. It is hoped that the US will be clear-eyed about this. The US should honor the one-China principle and implement the three joint communiqués both in word and in deed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","During the call between the two Presidents, the Chinese side made clear its position on the Taiwan question. The two sides also agreed to stay in touch. But if Speaker Pelosi would visit Taiwan, does China believe that the atmosphere to keep the China-US high-level dialogue going will no longer exist?","In their phone conversation yesterday, Chinese and US Presidents had a candid, in-depth communication and exchange on China-US relations and issues of interest. The Chinese side has repeatedly made clear to the US side our serious concern over Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan and our firm opposition to the visit. If the US side challenges China’s red line, it will be met with resolute countermeasures. The US must bear all consequences arising thereof.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","China Daily","Former Australian Prime Minister Paul Keating openly criticized US House Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan in a recent statement, saying it would be “foolish, dangerous and unnecessary to any cause”. “If the situation is misjudged or mishandled, the outcome for the security, prosperity and order of the region and the world and above all for Taiwan would be catastrophic”, he added. Do you have any comment?","About Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan, people with insight both within and outside the US have spoken out on this. We believe former Prime Minister Paul Keating’s statement is one such example. We hope the US side will see what they see and hear their voice of reason.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Can you confirm whether the specific question of Nancy Pelosi’s possible visit to Taiwan came up on the call?","I think I have covered the related points.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-07-29","Zhao Lijian","PTI","Are there any other issues besides Taiwan discussed by the two leaders, especially the issues related to the Indo-Pacific? Can you just give us an idea of any outcome related to that?","It was late at night when the phone call between the two Presidents concluded. The Chinese side released a readout immediately afterwards.\nDuring the call, the two Presidents had a candid communication and exchange on China-US relations and issues of interest. President Xi elaborated on China’s principled position on the Taiwan question. He stressed that the two sides need to maintain communication at all levels and make good use of existing channels to promote bilateral cooperation. The two Presidents also exchanged views on the global economic situation. The two sides believe that China and the US need to maintain communication on such important issues as coordinating macroeconomic policies, keeping global industrial and supply chains stable, and protecting global energy and food security. President Xi also stressed that attempts at decoupling or severing supply chains in defiance of underlying laws would not help boost the US economy. They would only make the world economy more vulnerable. The two sides need to work for deescalation of regional hotspots, help rid the world of COVID-19 as early as possible, reduce the risk of stagflation and recession, and uphold the international system centering on the UN and the international order underpinned by international law. The two Presidents exchanged views on issues including the Ukraine crisis.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202207/t20220729_10730439.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-07-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Japanese Diet member and former government official Ishiba Shigeru and others visited Taiwan on the 27th. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 29 dispatch. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to a question on the 29th, pointed out that some Japanese lawmakers and politicians have, for some time, frequently taken wrong actions on Taiwan-related issues and spread erroneous remarks, jumping very high, which is very dangerous. We urge certain people on the Japanese side to fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, recognize the facts that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, and in particular draw lessons from history, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and be cautious in words and deeds on the Taiwan question.\nZhu Fenglian said that we solemnly warn the DPP authorities not to misjudge the situation: “relying on external forces to seek independence” and serving as pawns for external anti-China forces will only end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202207/t20220729_12456655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-01","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi is scheduled to visit Southeast Asia and East Asia this week and Taiwan is not mentioned in her itinerary. What’s China’s comment?","Recently, the Chinese side has repeatedly made clear to the US side our serious concern over Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan and our firm opposition to the visit. We have been stressing that such a visit would lead to serious consequences. As President Xi Jinping stressed to US President Joe Biden in their phone call, the position of the Chinese government and people on the Taiwan question is consistent, and resolutely safeguarding China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the firm will of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. The public opinion cannot be defied. Those who play with fire will perish by it. We believe that the US side is fully aware of China’s strong and clear message.\nWe are closely following the itinerary of Speaker Pelosi. A visit to Taiwan by her would constitute a gross interference in China’s internal affairs, seriously undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, wantonly trample on the one-China principle, greatly threaten peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, severely undermine China-US relations and lead to a very serious situation and grave consequences.\nWe want to once again make it clear to the US side that the Chinese side is fully prepared for any eventuality and that the People’s Liberation Army of China will never sit idly by, and we will make resolute response and take strong countermeasures to uphold China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, What the US should do is to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three Sino-US joint communiqués, fulfill President Biden’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” and not arrange for a visit by Speaker Pelosi to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347336.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220801_10731604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-01","Zhao Lijian","NPR","Two questions about Nancy Pelosi’s visit to Asia. The first is that in her official schedule, she said she’s going to Singapore, Malaysia, South Korea and Japan. There was obviously no mention of Taiwan. What’s China’s take on that? Is that cause for optimism? The second question is, you said the military would not sit by idly. Can you elaborate on that? What are we likely to see if she were to visit Taiwan?","On your first question, we’ve seen the press release issued by Speaker Pelosi’s office, her own tweets and the press reports. I have made the Chinese government’s position very clear just now.\nOn your second question, Pelosi is the third highest-ranking official in the US government, which means it would be highly sensitive for her to visit Taiwan no matter what. Whatever the timing or way she chooses to go to Taiwan, it will seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three Sino-US joint communiqués and seriously undermine China-US relations. It will undoubtedly create an egregious political impact. If Pelosi visits Taiwan, the Chinese side will respond resolutely and take strong countermeasures to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. As for what those measures will be, let’s see what happens if she actually goes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347336.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220801_10731604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-01","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","John Kirby, National Security Council Coordinator for Strategic Communications at the White House, said that the US has seen no evidence of looming Chinese military activity against Taiwan. “If such a visit occurred, it would signal no change in US policy”, he said, adding that there is no reason for the US and China to “come to blows” or to “come to increased physical tension”. Do you have any response?","The Chinese side has repeatedly made clear our serious concern over Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan and our firm opposition to the visit. We will take firm and strong measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity. I would like to stress that the one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It is the US side that has kept distorting and hollowing out the one-China policy, making irresponsible remarks and creating factors of tension on the Taiwan question. The US has recently begun to emphasize the importance of upholding all countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope the US will honor those words first and foremost on the Taiwan question and refrain from applying double standards.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347336.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220801_10731604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-01","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","Japanese Foreign Minister Yoshimasa Hayashi said in his remarks at a US-based think tank on July 29 that it’s essential to maintain high-level and candid communication with China and to cooperate with China on matters such as climate change and the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue. He also expressed so-called concerns over China-Russia relations and the issues related to the South China Sea, the East China Sea and…","Japan has been mischaracterizing China’s normal military and maritime activities, which constitutes interference in China’s internal affairs and stokes division and confrontation in the region. This is by no means constructive.\nI want to stress that China is committed to the path of peaceful development and firmly pursues a nuclear strategy of self-defense. China-Russia military cooperation is consistent with international law and international practice and does not target any specific country. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no interference from external forces. What has Japan done? On the East China Sea, Japan has connived at the trouble-making right-wing forces and invited non-regional countries to interfere in the issue. On the South China Sea, Japan has been flexing its muscles along with the US in the area. This is what truly poses a threat to regional peace and stability. For a long time, Japan has characterized itself as a victim of nuclear weapons and sat comfortably under the US’s nuclear umbrella, yet Japan has been against and hindering the US’s renouncing of the first use of nuclear weapons, and even suggested the possibility of nuclear sharing with the US. Japan’s position on those issues is full of hypocrisy and contradictions.\nChina and Japan are close neighbors and both important countries in the region. To maintain and develop friendly and cooperative relations between China and Japan serves the fundamental interests of the two countries and peoples. We urge the Japanese side to be objective and rational about China’s development, abide by the principles set out in the four political documents between China and Japan, and stop stirring up trouble and hyping up disputes in the Asia-Pacific region for its own selfish interests. Japan needs to take concrete actions to keep the China-Japan relationship on the right track and work for its sound and steady development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347336.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220801_10731604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-02","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","Since yesterday’s press conference, there has been more information coming out about the trip by the House Speaker Nancy Pelosi to Asia. And at this point it looks increasingly likely that she will visit Taiwan, arriving possibly tonight and holding talks with the Taiwan leaders potentially. So my question to the Chinese foreign ministry is, is Nancy Pelosi is still on time to cancel her trip? Is this something…","All eyes are on Speaker Pelosi’s trip to Asia. Your question would be more suited for the US side or the Speaker herself to answer. China has, on many occasions, made its principled position clear and made multiple serious démarches to the US side. We are closely following the itinerary of Speaker Pelosi. And if the US continues down the wrong path, we will take strong and resolute measures to protect our sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347337.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220802_10732122.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-02","Hua Chunying","The Wall Street Journal","Has there been any communication with the US side over the past 24 hours about the planed visit to ensure that there’s no misunderstandings or miscalculations from either side?","China and the US have maintained close communication in Beijing and in Washington at different levels and through different channels. And we have repeatedly and unmistakably expressed to the US side our firm opposition to Speaker Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan. And we hope that the US officials are clear about the importance and sensitivity of this issue and the potential danger in the event of this visit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347337.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220802_10732122.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-02","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said on the margins of the NPT Review Conference yesterday that “Congress is an independent, coequal branch of government...this is very much precedent in the sense that previous speakers visited Taiwan...And so if the Speaker does decide to visit, and China tries to create some kind of crisis or otherwise escalate tensions, that [responsibility] would be entirely on Beijing.”…","I think the world has seen very clearly that it is the US’s provocations that have led to the escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The US should and must take full responsibility for it. Secretary Blinken’s words confound black with white and have once again revealed the hegemonic mindset and extortionist logic of some people in the US. The US is essentially saying to us that “I can make provocations against you as I please, but you cannot reject them or act in self-defense.”\nOver the past few days, China has made clear its stern opposition through various channels and at different levels both in Beijing and Washington to the potential visit to Taiwan by Speaker Pelosi. Let me just reiterate certain points.\nFirst, any US government institution, executive, legislative and judicial alike, must act on the foreign policy recognized and committed to by the US government. In 1979, the US government made a clear commitment in the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations that “the United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China. Within that context, the people of the US will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.” The US Congress is part of the US government, and it should strictly abide by the foreign policy recognized and committed to by the US government. When the House Speaker, being the third-highest ranking figure in the US government, flies on US military aircraft and makes a provocative visit to the Taiwan region, it is by no means an unofficial action.\nSecond, the wrongful actions of certain US politicians in the past do not constitute a precedent and still less should they become an excuse for the US to repeat its mistake on the Taiwan question.\nAnd third, the one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and a common understanding of the international community. It is on the basis of the one-China principle that China has established diplomatic ties with the US and 180 other countries. This is a solemn commitment the US has made on the one-China principle to China in the three Sino-US Joint Communiqués.\nIn recent years, the US has claimed that it is committed to the one-China policy, but action-wise, it has been backtracking, and even blurring and hollowing out the one-China principle. It has inserted into its characterization of the one-China policy the so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and the “Six assurances”, which were unilaterally concocted and have never been recognized and have been firmly opposed to by China. The US has also gone against its commitment of maintaining unofficial ties with the Taiwan region. It has upgraded its level of contact with Taiwan and has steadily increased arms sales to Taiwan.\nMany people with insight both within and outside the US have seen this very clearly. They have repeatedly pointed out the danger of US actions. According to former US Secretary of State Henry Kissinger, who said at this year’s World Economic Forum, “my understanding of the agreement has been that the US would uphold the principle of one China”, “I think it’s essential that these principles be maintained”, and “the US should not by subterfuge or a gradual process develop something of a two-China solution”. After news came out about Pelosi’s potential visit to Taiwan, many people, including those from mainstream media and think tanks in the US and former political leaders of some US allies, have publicly said that whatever reason Pelosi uses to visit Taiwan, it would be foolish, dangerous, and unnecessary; that it would be a dangerous gamble; that it would be hard to imagine anything more reckless and provocative than this; and that if the US side misjudges or mishandles the cross-Strait situation, it will lead to disastrous consequences for the Taiwan region and even the security, prosperity and order of the entire world.\nFourth, the US has been following a strategy of using Taiwan to contain China. And based on this strategy, the US has supported and connived at Taiwan-independence separatist forces and has made deliberate provocations against China on the Taiwan question. It has been pushing the envelope on China’s red lines. The US and Taiwan have made provocations together first, whereas China has been compelled to act in self-defense. Any countermeasure to be taken by China would be a justified and necessary response to the US oblivion to China’s repeated démarches and the US’s unscrupulous behavior. And China is only exercising its right as any independent sovereign country would, not to mention that China is a country of more than 1.4 billion people with over 5,000 years of history. We hope that the US is clear-eyed about that.\nAnd fifth, the historical ins and outs of the Taiwan question are crystal clear, so are the facts and status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. China firmly opposes separatist moves toward “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces, and never allows any room for “Taiwan independence” forces in whatever form. The position of the Chinese government and people on the Taiwan question is consistent. Resolutely safeguarding China’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity is the firm will of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. Achieving full reunification of the motherland is a shared aspiration of all Chinese people. And the US should give up any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” and strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three Joint Communiqués both in words and deeds and to the letter. If the US insists on pursuing the wrong course of action, it will assume full responsibility for all serious consequences arising therefrom.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347337.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220802_10732122.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-08-02","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q) [per digest]","","Wu Qian, Senior Colonel and spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense, said at the regular press conference on the 25th: At present, espionage agencies abroad and various hostile forces are intensifying their infiltration and secret-stealing activities against us. We hope everyone will strengthen national security awareness and strictly guard military secrets.\nA reporter asked: According to media reports, a certain marine public-interest organization, having received funding from foreign non-governmental organizations in recent years, has set up nearly one hundred monitoring points in areas near China's coastline under the name of “marine litter monitoring,” 22 of which are adjacent to important military targets and naval vessel routes, directly threatening our military security. The organization was recently dealt with by national security authorities in accordance with the law. What is your comment on this?\nWu Qian said: At present, espionage agencies abroad and various hostile forces are intensifying their infiltration and secret-stealing activities against us, posing a serious threat to our national security, including military security.\nWu Qian pointed out: National security is not far from us; it is even right beside us. Each of us is a line of defense for national security. We hope everyone will strengthen national security awareness and strictly guard military secrets. Acts that harm national security and leak military secrets will surely be severely punished by law.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/mil/2022/08-02/9818385.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","CGTN","US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi said in a statement on the night of August 2 that “Our congressional delegation’s visit to Taiwan honors America’s unwavering commitment to supporting Taiwan’s vibrant democracy. America’s solidarity with the 23 million people of Taiwan is more important today than ever, as the world faces a choice between autocracy and democracy.” Do you have any comment?","The issue of her visit is not about democracy, but China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. What she has done is definitely not about upholding or defending democracy, but a provocation and infringement on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nMany people have hit the nail in their comments about the visit. They pointed out that Pelosi’s dangerous provocation is all about making personal political gains. It is a sheer ugly political farce. In this ugly stunt, democracy has been reduced to nothing more than a cheap tool and a pretext constantly used by the US. While Pelosi is the one staging this grandstanding act, it is the China-US relationship and the peace and stability in the region that are taking the toll.\nThe kind of democracy Pelosi refers to is like nothing but an ornate robe with lice crawling all over it. It might look magnificent from a distance, but couldn’t stand up to close scrutiny. From the Capitol riot, the death of George Floyd, the Robb Elementary School shooting and America’s over a million COVID deaths, we see the hypocrisy and cold-bloodedness of the kind of democracy Pelosi refers to. We see the empty pledge and so-called strength of this type of democracy from what the US military has done in Iraq and Syria and from its retreat from Kabul.\nBeing the number three figure in the US government, Pelosi has been spending taxpayer money and flying to Taiwan on US military aircraft to pull a political stunt, while problems with US democracy keep piling up. Her behavior of violating the international law and basic norm in international relations and jeopardizing other countries’ internal affairs, sovereignty and territorial integrity would only open up people’s eyes about the hypocrisy and ugliness of the US and further bankrupt the US’s credibility as a country. As US Republican Congresswoman Majorie Greene has tweeted, Pelosi is “not staying in America and solving problems afflicting our people” and she is “obsessed with her own power she’s held for decades while our entire country crumbles ... enough with this fake ‘courage’ defending democracy.”\nI would also like to remind Pelosi that she is pitting herself against a nation with one-fifth of the world’s population and making a provocation to the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. People will not be fooled. Public opinion cannot be defied. Will Pelosi go down in history with a favorable or foul reputation for her stunt? I’m sure history will give a fair answer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","AFP","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said today that China will punish those who provoke China. Can you tell us what further punishment is planned?","China will do everything necessary to firmly uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity. All consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We mean what we say. I would like to kindly ask you for some additional patience and confidence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","Global Times","On Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, US officials now try to justify it and even to shift blame. For example, White House National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said that “China tries to turn what is in the historical norm into a crisis” and is the one “who’d be escalating”. National Security Council Coordinator for Strategic Communications at the White House John Kirby said that this visit doesn’t violate the US’s…","I think you summed it up quite well. The US officials are simply trying to say anything to explain the visit away. They have even put the blame on us like a thief crying “Stop thief!” This reflects the lack of credibility, knowledge about history and self-reflection on the part of the US government. As an old Chinese saying goes, “A man’s troubles lie in reading too little about history.” It is high time that the US officials caught up on the history of the Taiwan question.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the entire China. This is at the heart of the one-China principle and also a universal consensus of the international community and a basic norm in international relations. In October 1971, the 26th Session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, which “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations, and to expel forthwith the representatives of Chiang Kai-shek from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations and in all the organizations related to it.” A total of 181 countries, including the US, have established diplomatic ties with China on the basis of the one-China principle.\nHistorically, the Taiwan question once represented the main roadblock to the normalization of China-US relations. China stood firm on the one-China principle and would not make any compromise or concession on that issue. In 1971, the US affirmed to China the new principles that it would follow with regard to the Taiwan question. They include, the US would acknowledge that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is a part of China; the US would not repeat the phrase that the status of Taiwan is undetermined; the US had not supported, and would not support movements for “Taiwan independence”. When President Nixon visited China in 1972, he reaffirmed those principles to Premier Zhou Enlai, and hence the Shanghai Communiqué.\nAnd in that Communiqué, the US made it very clear that “the United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” These US commitments led to the start of the process toward normalization of China-US relations. According to the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the United States of America and the People’s Republic of China released in 1978, the US “recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China” and “acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China”. And in the August 17 Joint Communiqué of 1982, the US side made it clear that “the United States of America recognized the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China, and it acknowledged the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” Also in that communiqué, the US “reiterates that it has no intention of infringing on Chinese sovereignty and territorial integrity, or interfering in China’s internal affairs, or pursuing a policy of ‘two Chinas’ or ‘one China, one Taiwan’.” It is based on those three Joint Communiqués that our ties with the US have generally achieved stable development in the past 40-plus years.\nHowever, in recent years, the US has not matched its words with deeds. It has been distorting, altering, obscuring, and hollowing out the one-China principle and trying to cross red lines and pushing the boundaries. It has used all means to play the “Taiwan card”and mischaracterized the one-China policy by claiming that the unilaterally concocted “Taiwan Relations Act” and “Six Assurances”are also part of what guides the policy. The US has even at one point dropped key formulations such as “Taiwan is part of China” from the website of the State Department. The US has also brazenly sought to upgrade US-Taiwan exchanges, intensify arms sales to Taiwan and embolden the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nThe US government was supposed to rein in the attempt to visit Taiwan by its third highest-ranking member. However, the US government has connived at her provocation. This is the root cause and truth behind the tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe historical ins and outs of the Taiwan question are crystal-clear, so are the facts and status quo that the two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. The international community knows it too. Over the past few days, many leaders around the world and people from different walks of life have voiced their opposition to the visit. The spokesperson of the UN Secretary-General has just said that the policy of the UN on this issue is guided by General Assembly Resolution 2758 from 1971 on one China. Clearly, people with a sense of justice can easily tell right from wrong.\nThe position of the Chinese government and Chinese people on the Taiwan question is consistent. Resolutely safeguarding China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity is the firm will of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. To achieve China’s full reunification is the shared aspiration and sacred duty of all Chinese people. Public opinion will not be defied, and the trend of the times cannot be reversed. No country, force or individual shall misestimate the firm resolve, strong will and great capability of the Chinese Government and people to defend state sovereignty and territorial integrity and to achieve national reunification and rejuvenation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","Just to follow up on the possible countermeasures that you mentioned. Can you elaborate a little bit on whether there will be sanctions directly on Taiwan? Will there be sanctions on Nancy Pelosi as an individual and on other US officials?","In disregard of China’s strong opposition and serious representations, Speaker Pelosi visited China’s Taiwan region. This is a serious violation of the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US Joint Communiqués. It has a severe impact on the political foundation of China-US relations, and seriously infringes upon China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It gravely undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and sends a seriously wrong signal to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence”. Last night, China’s Foreign Ministry, the National People’s Congress, the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Ministry of National Defense immediately issued statements or remarks to condemn the visit. Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng summoned US Ambassador to China Nicholas Burns at once. Chinese Ambassador to the US Qin Gang immediately made serious representations to the White House National Security Council and also the State Department. This morning, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi issued remarks on this.\nChina will do everything necessary to firmly defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. All consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US side and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We mean what we say. As for the specific countermeasures that you are interested to know, what I can say is that what needs to be done will be done and these measures will be resolute, strong and effective. They will be continuously felt by the US side and “Taiwan independence” forces.\nAnd also, I wish to stress that if we look back at each provocation the US has made against China, we can see that they have invariably disgraced and backfired on the US itself. The most recent example is when Pelosi and some others incited riots and violence in Hong Kong, calling them a “beautiful sight to behold”. That, however, gave more reason to expeditiously end chaos, and restore order and prosperity in Hong Kong. The city, known as the Pearl of the Orient, regained its vigor and charm. This visit by Pelosi to Taiwan is no exception. For people like Pelosi, their futile attempt to collude with the “Taiwan independence” forces and use the Taiwan question to contain China and undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity will not stop, but only accelerate the historic process of China’s reunification.\nAs State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi has said, the US has reneged on its commitments on the Taiwan question, openly played with fire and pitted itself against the 1.4 billion Chinese people. None of this will end well.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","CCTV","In response to a question concerning US House Speaker Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, Stéphane Dujarric, Spokesman for the UN Secretary-General, said that “the policy of the United Nations on this issue is that we are guided by General Assembly Resolution 2758 from 1971 on one China”. At the same time, we also see that many countries and fair-minded people in the US have voiced support for China, including the renowned…","Following the visit by Speaker Pelosi to the Taiwan region, within less than a day, people of different ranks and backgrounds from more than 100 countries and international organizations have spoken up in various ways to condemn her wrong, foolish and insane decision and express their support for the one-China principle and for China’s legitimate efforts to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Their voice for justice has truly touched us.\nLet me just give you a few examples. The Press Secretary of the President of Russia, the Spokesperson for the Russian Foreign Ministry, the Russian Foreign Ministry, Deputy Chairman of Russia’s Security Council, and Deputy Chairman for the Federal Assembly of Russia have stated that Russia firmly adheres to the one-China principle, opposes any form of “Taiwan independence”, supports China’s right to do everything necessary to defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity on the Taiwan question. The statement of the Foreign Ministry of Belarus said that Speaker Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is an obdurate and irresponsible act of the US; that Belarus fully understands China’s concerns about the US’s interference in China’s internal affairs and the escalated tensions across the Taiwan Strait as a result of it; and that Belarus supports China’s measures to realize national reunification. The Spokesperson for the DPRK Foreign Ministry said that the US’s interference in others’ internal affairs is contemptible, and constitutes deliberate political and military provocations and the root cause for the disruption to peace and security in the region; that the DPRK strongly condemns any foreign interference in the Taiwan question, which is China’s internal affair; that the DPRK fully supports the just position of the Chinese government to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity; and that the US’s attempt to hold back China’s development and reunification will surely be resolutely thwarted. Iran’s Foreign Ministry Spokesperson said in a statement that the US is interfering in China’s internal affairs and undermining China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity; and that the visit is another example of the US’s policy of interfering in other countries’ internal affairs and the way the US conducts its foreign policy, which will only further undermine regional peace and stability. The Syrian Foreign Ministry’s statement said that Syria condemns in the strongest language the US’s unprecedented ratcheted-up actions and provocation policy against China; that Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is against international law; and that this irresponsible behavior reflects the US’s “commitment” to disrupting peace and stability of the region and the world and serious harm to world peace and security. The Palestinian Presidency released a statement calling for halting any actions that run contrary to the one-China principle while affirming China’s right to defend its sovereign, security and development interests. Nicaragua’s President Daniel Ortega has issued a statement saying that when Speaker Pelosi flies on a military aircraft into the Taiwan region, it constitutes an invasion; and that such provocations will only make China stronger. Nicaragua’s Foreign Ministry also released a statement saying that Nicaragua supports China’s efforts to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity and the government of Nicaragua urges the US to stop provocations. The Foreign Minister of Trinidad and Tobago openly reaffirmed commitment to the one-China principle. The Foreign Ministry of the Laos issued a statement that said it reaffirms its support for the one-China principle, opposition to any intention aiming at creating a situation for “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and support for China’s reunification by peaceful means. The royal family of Cambodia said on social media that there is only one China and Taiwan is a province of China. The Spokesperson of the UN Secretary-General reiterated the UN’s commitment to the one-China principle, which was laid down in Resolution 2758 adopted by the 26th General Assembly in 1971. The office of the leading Assistant Secretary-General of the League of Arab States (LAS) put out a statement on the official LAS website stressing that the one-China principle should be complied with, that it opposes actions that violate relevant UN resolutions and undermine regional peace and stability, and that the Arab League supports China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and firmly upholds the one-China principle. Main political parties in Tunisia said on social media platforms that no country has the right to interfere in China’s internal affairs and Pelosi’s visit will only further damage the image of the US. It also believes that the US has made its fortune by plundering other countries. When it cannot win through fair competition, it would play disgraceful gambits like this. This is nothing surprising.\nIn addition to that, we have seen statements from government officials including former political leaders and people from all walks of life in many countries. For instance, Max Baucus, who used to be the US Ambassador to China, said that “We are playing with fire when we get pretty close to the line, and Pelosi is pushing us much, much closer to recognizing Taiwan as an independent country. And once we get there, we’re going to pay a price.” People from Egypt, South Africa, Madagascar, and All-Africa China Association for Peaceful Reunification of China have also spoken up on this. And also Süddeutsche Zeitung from Germany, Neue Zürcher Zeitung from Switzerland, Al Arabiya in Saudi Arabia, Prensa Latina, and other news agencies from many countries including the Bahamas have said that Speaker Pelosi’s visit will trigger regional instability; the US’s claim of not changing the status-quo across the Taiwan Strait is not convincing at all. The US’s provocative activities are intended to create tension at China’s doorstep and hinder China’s development. This will only worsen the turbulent international situation, which is already suffering from the Ukraine crisis and the COVID pandemic. Also, вести, a news outlet in Uzbekistan noted in a commentary that the visit by Speaker Pelosi is about provoking China against the backdrop of a downward economy in the US, which is very unwise. A survey conducted by the online newspaper udn.com in Taiwan found more than two thirds of the people in Taiwan not supportive of Speaker Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, saying that it will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe fact that so many have spoken up for justice is a clear indication that people in the international community are clear-eyed about the nature and intention of the visit. The visit is an ugly political stunt. It will not change the historical and legal reality that Taiwan belongs to China. It will not stop the reunification course of China and will not change the fact that 181 countries in the world recognize and support the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Chinese military said it will carry out targeted military operations in a few areas around Taiwan. Some of these areas encroached into the “internal waters” of Taiwan, which according to UNCLOS is not allowed. Taiwan said that this endangers their “national security ” and hinders the freedom of navigation protected under international law. What’s your comment on this?","On the actions taken by the Chinese military, I’m sure you have seen the statements made by the spokespersons of the Ministry of National Defense and the PLA Eastern Theater Command. The actions are aimed at deterring the “Taiwan independence” forces, so they are legitimate and necessary.\nWe have never seen any problems with the freedom of navigation in relevant waters. I think what truly needs our attention is how the US military vessels and aircraft would fly thousands of miles all the way from their homeland just to flex muscles at the doorstep of China. And also for the US side, maybe it is better not to mention UNCLOS. If the US wants to mention it, please join UNCLOS now first. Taiwan, being a part of China, has no right to claim “internal waters”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","The Wall Street Journal","Earlier today Speaker Pelosi met with Tsai Chi-chang, who is the “Vice President of Taiwan’s legislature”. She spoke about how the US could learn from Taiwan on COVID response. There she said “how you address the COVID crisis, how we advance respect for all of the people in our countries as we go forward”, appearing to refer to Taiwan as a country. Does China have any response on that?","I think you knew full well what the answer would be. Taiwan has never been a country. Both historically and legally, Taiwan has always been a province of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","AFP","Another question on China’s military exercises around Taiwan. Japan has said that some of the military drills are taking place in the Japanese exclusive economic zone (EEZ). In holding these exercises so close to Taiwan, including to the east of Taiwan, is China prepared for the situation to escalate if there’s a misfiring or a close encounter with other vessels or aircraft?","The Chinese military drills in the waters off China’s Taiwan island are necessary and legitimate both as a response to the major provocation of the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and as a step to firmly uphold China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The relevant Chinese authorities issued safety alerts and navigation warnings before the start of the drills. Since China and Japan have not yet carried out maritime delimitation in relevant waters, China does not accept the notion of so-called “Japanese EEZ”. The Chinese side urges Japan to uphold the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries and be prudent on the Taiwan question.\nJust now, some of you just mentioned the actions taken by China’s military, and we’ve also noted the remarks of the US side on these drills. I’d like to say a bit more about this.\nOver the past few days, through multiple channels and at various levels, China has been making clear time and again our firm opposition to Pelosi’s visit to the US side, but apparently the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have not taken the message to heart. In that case, the Chinese side is left with one option only, which is to “speak” to them in a way that they can understand.\nThe important thing is, while expressing our serious opposition to Pelosi’s visit, we need to be absolutely clear that it is the US who is the provocateur, and China the victim. The US side colluded with those in Taiwan and made provocations first, whereas China has been compelled to act in self-defense. The root cause of the tensions in the Taiwan Strait is that the Taiwan authorities have been soliciting US support to seek “Taiwan independence”, and certain individuals in the US intend to use the Taiwan question to contain China. History and reality have proved time and again that the one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. When the one-China principle is fully recognized and earnestly followed, the Taiwan Strait would remain calm and tranquil. However, when the one-China principle is willfully challenged or even sabotaged, there would be dark clouds or even violent storms across the Taiwan Strait.\nIf people truly care about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, particularly friends from the press, it would be critical for you to send a clear message to the US officials and to “Taiwan independence” forces about the need to strictly abide by the one-China principle in both words and deeds. That is how we can truly see the peace and stability that people want in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Many Chinese people were disappointed when China did not and could not take more concrete actions to prevent Pelosi from making this visit to Taiwan. On hindsight, should China have done more to guide the public to understand more rationally what is best for the development of US-China relations?","The Chinese side has made its serious position clear through statements and actions. Once again, people have seen that certain US politicians would pull self-serving political stunts at the expense of regional peace and stability and the overall interest of China-US relations, whereas China’s behavior shows its commitment to regional peace and stability as well as its resoluteness in upholding its sovereignty and security interests.\nThe Chinese side has unwavering resolve and will to uphold China’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. There should be no questions about our strong capability to do so. Our countermeasures will be strong, effective and resolute, which will be felt steadily and continuously by the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatists.\nThe Chinese people are rational patriots. We have full confidence in the ability of our country and our government to firmly defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. I recommend that you take some time to learn about the century-long history of the Communist Party of China. We have been through all kinds of challenges, haven’t we? And look how far we have come. We are fully confident in the future ahead of us.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","O Globo","You just mentioned that the one-China principle is at the very basis of US-China relations. Now that you see this visit of Ms. Pelosi to Taiwan as a serious violation of this principle, do you see the need of seeking fundamental changes in this relation between the US and China?","The one-China principle is the most important political prerequisite and foundation for establishing and developing diplomatic relations with all countries, including the US. The one-China principle is what has underpinned the overall stable development of the relationship between China and US over the past 40-plus years. And I think that the overwhelming majority of people in the US and elsewhere hope to see a sound and stable China-US relationship. Any responsible government would be willing to follow the trend of history and to listen to the will of the people.\nWhat the US needs to do is stop trying to hollow out and obscure the one-China principle and not continue down the wrong path.\nChina always follows the principles of mutual respect and win-win cooperation in developing friendly relations with the US and other countries. Nevertheless, on the one-China principle and issues about sovereignty and territorial integrity, which are China’s core interests, there is no room for us to concede or compromise. We hope the US side would clearly get that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","AFP","China’s Customs Administration said today that it would suspend certain imports from Taiwan over health and safety issues. A number of other Taiwan imports were also blocked earlier this week despite having the required documentation. Can you clarify if these suspensions are intended also to punish Taiwan for Pelosi’s visit?","I would like to refer you to the competent authorities about your specific questions. But one thing is for sure: the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces must take the responsibility and pay the price for their wrong actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-03","Hua Chunying","TASS","Germany’s Foreign Minister reportedly said at a UN meeting that if the mainland invades Taiwan, Germany will give support to Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","I assume you are referring to the remarks made by the German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock at the Review Conference of the NPT. Her indication that China broke international law and attacked its smaller neighbor lacks basic knowledge of history and does not square with facts.\nThe historical ins and outs and legal facts about the Taiwan question are crystal clear. No individual or force can deny or distort them. I do not have to go far back into history to find an example. Around the end of the Second World War, the Cairo Declaration of 1943 and the Potsdam Proclamation of 1945 were very clear about China’s rights over Taiwan. “All the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, including Taiwan and Penghu Islands, shall be restored” to China. The UNGA Resolution 2758 of 1971 decided to restore all these rights to the PRC and reaffirmed the one-China principle.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Some people compare Ukraine to Taiwan in order to twist the logic and mislead public perceptions. This constitutes interference in China’s domestic affair and we will definitely not accept that.\nThe one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and the political foundation and fundamental prerequisite for China’s relations with other countries. Violating that principle will undermine bilateral relations. We hope Germany will have an objective and accurate understanding of the Taiwan question and be careful with getting swayed by the US. We hope Germany will keep its commitment to the one-China policy with concrete action and act prudently on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220803_10733353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (Dispatch): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on August 3 that, in accordance with relevant import and export regulations, as well as food safety requirements and standards, relevant authorities have, effective today, suspended imports of citrus fruits such as grapefruit, lemons, and oranges from the Taiwan region to the mainland, as well as chilled hairtail and frozen horse mackerel. At the same time, it has been decided to suspend exports of natural sand to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12457716.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on August 3: The “Taiwan Democracy Foundation” and the “International Cooperation and Development Foundation,” institutions linked to diehard “Taiwan independence” figures, are using the guise of “democracy” and “cooperative development” to engage extensively in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally. They are desperately colluding with and clinging to external anti-China forces, attacking and smearing the mainland, and using money and other inducements to expand what Taiwan calls its “international space,” attempting to undermine the international community’s one-China framework. The mainland has decided to take punitive measures against these foundations: prohibiting their cooperation with mainland organizations, enterprises and individuals; punishing according to law any organizations, enterprises and individuals that provide funding or services to these foundations; and taking other necessary measures. Mainland organizations, enterprises and individuals are prohibited from conducting any transactions or cooperation with enterprises that have donated to the above foundations, including Xuande Energy, Lingwang Technology, Tianliang Medical and Tianyan Satellite Technology, and the principal responsible persons of these enterprises are prohibited from entering the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12457720.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (dateline): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on August 3 that Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities have for a long time obstinately insisted on the position of “Taiwan independence,” refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” openly promoted the “two-state theory,” wantonly attacked the “one country, two systems” framework, carried out “de-Sinicization” across the island in all areas, and manipulated “de jure Taiwan independence.” They have deliberately created confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, held the people of Taiwan hostage, incited social populism, and vigorously suppressed the righteous forces and rational voices on the island that advocate peaceful development and peaceful reunification of cross-Strait relations. They have colluded with external anti-China forces and engaged in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities internationally, disregarding peace in the Taiwan Strait and the safety of the Taiwan people, and insisted on promoting Pelosi's visit to Taiwan, relying on foreign backing to provoke the mainland and assert their own importance. They are standing on the opposite side of the Chinese nation, seriously undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seriously endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nWe solemnly warn Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities: colluding with external forces to seek independence and provoke confrontation for the sake of selfish personal or partisan gain will only accelerate their own downfall and push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster. History has proven, and will continue to prove, that “Taiwan independence” separatism can never succeed, and that selling out the interests of the country and nation will certainly end in complete failure. No one and no force should underestimate the Chinese people's firm resolve, strong will and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12457820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","During Pelosi's intrusive visit to Taiwan, Tsai Ing-wen presented her with the so-called “Special Grand Cordon of the Cloud Banner Medal.” What is your comment?","Pelosi's intrusion into Taiwan this time is a further development of her consistent, stubborn pro-Taiwan and anti-China words and deeds, and its nature is extremely vile. We strongly condemn and firmly protest, and have announced a series of resolute and forceful countermeasures. The DPP authorities, on the separatist path of “relying on the US to seek independence,” have gone down a dead-end road, leaving a series of servile and disgraceful records. They will inevitably pay an increasingly unbearable price and can only end in failure. As for the so-called “medal,” everyone knows that Pompeo, a man of vile character who takes pride in “lying, deceiving, and stealing,” accepted such “medals.” One can imagine what a political farce the DPP authorities’ “bestowal of a medal” on Pelosi is.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12457953.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, August 3 (Xinhua) — On the 3rd, Tsai Ing-wen met with Pelosi and once again played up the so-called \"military threat\" from the mainland, advocated \"strengthening our self-defense capabilities,\" and declared \"defending the democratic front line.\" In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 3rd in response to a question that Tsai Ing-wen's remarks package \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes as so-called \"defending democracy,\" and distort our just act of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity into a so-called \"military threat.\" This is a complete distortion of right and wrong and a confusion of the public's perception.\nMa Xiaoguang said that currently, the root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is the collusion and conspiring together of the \"Taiwan independence\" forces and external forces. The DPP authorities rely on foreign powers for self-importance, willingly serve as pawns, and intensify provocations seeking \"independence\"; the U.S. escalates its playing of the \"Taiwan card\" and constantly fans the flames, scheming to \"use Taiwan to contain China.\" No matter how they argue or gloss over this, they cannot whitewash the fact that they are the creators of cross-Strait conflict, the destroyers of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the harmers of the interests of the Taiwan public.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We solemnly warn Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, that relying on outsiders is unreliable, that attempting to \"rely on the U.S. to seek independence\" is bound to fail, and that fantasizing about \"using force to seek independence\" is a case of being blinded by profit and will only accelerate their demise.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12458038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, answering reporters’ questions on the 3rd, said: We note that in recent days, political parties, groups, and individuals on the island who oppose “Taiwan independence” and advocate unification have voiced protests against Pelosi’s brazen visit to Taiwan. They have exposed the despicable tricks by which Pelosi stirred up tensions in the Taiwan Strait for personal political gain, fooled Taiwan residents, and harmed Taiwan. They have also condemned the vile conduct of Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities, who collude with external forces, deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and continuously provoke for independence. This is a righteous act that embodies a sense of national righteousness. It reflects the broad public will of Taiwan residents, who reject manipulation by external forces, refuse to be coerced by the DPP authorities, and want peace, development, and good lives. We express our sincere appreciation and full affirmation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12458039.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","It is reported that on the 3rd, Pelosi made a provocative visit to Taiwan's “Jingmei Human Rights Cultural Park” and met with so-called “human rights and democracy” activists. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 -- In response to Pelosi's meeting with so-called “human rights and pro-democracy” figures during her incursion into Taiwan, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 3rd, saying: We warn Pelosi and her ilk that treating “democracy and human rights” as “private goods” will only earn scorn. We warn the DPP authorities that using the banner of “democracy and human rights” to draw in anti-China forces, incite cross-Strait confrontation and engage in acts to split the country will not succeed.\nMa Xiaoguang said that this is yet another farce staged by Pelosi, based on her consistently anti-China, anti-communist stance and ideological prejudice, in collusion with the DPP authorities.\nMa Xiaoguang said: As is well known, American anti-China politicians, including Pelosi, ignore human rights abuses within the US, have long politicized and instrumentalized so-called “democracy and human rights,” arbitrarily interfered in the internal affairs of other countries, created contradictions and conflicts everywhere, and seriously undermined the cause of human rights progress worldwide. With the US midterm elections approaching and scandals continuing to surface in Pelosi's family, her waving the banner of so-called “democracy and human rights” on the Taiwan question is merely for personal gain. Some of the people she has cheered on are anti-China elements, some are forces disrupting Hong Kong, and some are ex-convicts released after serving sentences for the crime of subverting state power. They were tools and puppets serving US anti-China forces to begin with. And the so-called “democracy and human rights” invoked by the DPP authorities is nothing more than a “fig leaf” for its incitement of “anti-China, resist-China” sentiment, its scheming for “independence,” and its provocations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12458045.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-03","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3 (electronic dispatch). It was reported that on August 3, one “Taiwan independence” element was placed under review by national security organs in accordance with the law. In response, Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in answer to a reporter's question: On August 3, the spokesperson of the CPC Central Committee's Taiwan Affairs Office, having been authorized to do so, issued a statement on punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with the law. The national security organs took measures in accordance with the law against “Taiwan independence” elements suspected of crimes endangering national security. This fully demonstrates that die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements who break the law cannot escape the strict punishment of national law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220803_12458047.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","CCTV","On August 3, the G7 foreign ministers and the High Representative of the EU released a statement saying they are concerned by China’s “announced threatening actions” which “risk unnecessary escalation”, and alleging “There’s no justification” to use Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan as pretext for aggressive military activity or coercion. They claimed its “normal” for legislators to travel internationally and “There is no…","Reading this statement is like being transported back in time. The foreign ministers of these countries clearly believe that they still live in the days of the Eight-Power Allied Forces over 120 years ago. We no longer live in a world where the imperialist powers could run roughshod over Chinese people on Chinese soil. Today’s China is not the old China humiliated and bullied over 100 years ago. It is time for these people to wake up from their imperial dream.\nLet me stress the following points.\nFirst, China has the right to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity. The tensions in the Taiwan Strait is fundamentally caused by the US connivance at the third highest-ranking official of the US government to take a military aircraft to visit China’s Taiwan region in disregard of China’s strong opposition and serious representations. This is a major incident that seeks to upgrade the substantive exchanges between the United States and Taiwan. It causes serious harm to the one-China principle and to China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China has repeatedly made clear its stern opposition to the incident and stressed its firm opposition to separatism aimed at “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. China will allow no room for any form of “Taiwan independence” forces. If the US continues down the wrong path, then all consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US. And do not say that we have not told them so in advance. The US made a malicious provocation first, and China has been compelled to act in self-defense. In the event of such a blatant provocation that violates China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, it is only legitimate and necessary that we are taking countermeasures in response, and these measures are sure to be strong and resolute. The world sees this very clearly. Over 100 countries spoke up soon after the visit took place, stressing the importance of upholding the one-China principle and expressing support for China’s efforts to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity. If the G7 countries truly care about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they should have urged the US early on not to make such a dangerous, reckless and irresponsible provocation against China. Before Pelosi’s visit, those countries played dumb and did not say a word. Now, however, they suddenly became vocal and made irresponsible accusations against China’s justified response. This says everything about their hypocrisy and ugliness.\nSecond, the one-China principle is an important political foundation for establishing diplomatic ties between the G7 countries and China. We have consistently and firmly opposed any form of official exchanges between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The leaders of the legislatures of the G7 countries should abide by the foreign policies recognized and committed to by their governments. If a country’s legislature acts against the country’s foreign policy and the government does nothing about it, it will only prove the government’s political incompetence, poor governance and lack of credibility internationally. On this serious question, playing games with words or trying to redefine commitments means nothing and achieves nothing.\nThird, there is only one version and one connotation of the one-China principle, i.e. there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The government of the PRC is the sole legal government representing the entire China. This is written down clearly in Resolution 2758 adopted at the 26th Session of the UN General Assembly in 1971. It is the basic norm in international relations and the political foundation on which China established and has developed diplomatic relations with 181 countries, including the G7 countries. Nothing should be unilaterally inserted into the principle. And there should be no misinterpretation or distortion of the principle.\nFourth, either today or historically, members of the US-led G7 personify aggression and coercion. If anyone should be accused of aggression and coercion, the G7 countries deserve it more than anyone else.\nThe G7 must not forget that they are in no position to represent the global community. Their views only represent a tiny fraction of the world of nations. As Singaporean scholar Kishore Mahbubani wrote recently, “the G7 is dictatorial globally”. The latest statement is a case in point.\nI need to remind the G7 foreign ministers again that we all live in the third decade of the 21st century now. There would be a problem if someone follows the mindset of over a century ago.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","China often complains that too many in the West subscribe to what it calls the “China threat” narrative. But what would you say to those that will cite the military drills today, these missiles and weapons, as evidence of the threat that is posed by China?","Your question is a typical example of how certain people think in the West. This is an issue about fundamental facts and principles because it involves China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nChina has made it clear many times that we are firmly opposed to Pelosi’s visit. And we made it clear that once the visit is made, it would be a serious violation of the one-China principle and grave infringement on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China will definitely take strong and resolute measures in response and all consequences shall be borne by the US side. So do not say that we have not said in advance about the implications of this incident.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Chinese military drills in the waters off the Taiwan Island are a necessary and legitimate measure to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity and a necessary and legitimate countermeasure against the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and foreign interference. China’s competent authorities have issued safety alerts and travel warnings in advance. So what we have done is consistent with international law and international practices. Anyone who try to use that to prove China to be a so-called threat will only prove themselves to be rather dark inside, because they choose to view the incident selectively, ignoring the basic fact that things have ended up like this all because Pelosi went ahead with a wrong decision in disregard of China’s repeated serious representations and the repeated dissuasion from various parties.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said this morning on the sidelines of the ASEAN-plus foreign ministers’ meetings in Phnom Penh to outline China’s position on the US’s provocation in violation of China’s sovereignty.\nState Councilor Wang Yi said that Pelosi’s stunt is another bankruptcy of US politics, diplomacy and credibility. It proves the US to be the biggest saboteur of peace in the Taiwan Strait and the biggest troublemaker to regional stability. It proves the US’s Indo-Pacific strategy to be highly confrontational and harmful. It also proves the hypocrisy and double standards of the US regarding international rules. If China does not firmly resist the US’s recklessness, irresponsibility and extreme irrationality, then the principle of respecting sovereignty and territorial integrity in international relations will just become words on paper and separatists and extremists will only become more reckless and the hard-won peace and stability in this region will be seriously undermined.\nState Councilor Wang Yi also stressed that this incident is single-handedly orchestrated and provoked by the US and the cause, consequences and merits of the incident are crystal clear. China has done everything that is diplomatically possible to prevent this crisis which has been imposed on China. But we will not tolerate any act that harms our core interests and national rejuvenation. We will not sit by and watch the US play the “Taiwan card” to serve the US’s domestic politics and the selfish interests of some politicians. We will not tolerate moves to incite tensions, confrontation and separatism in this region. The host of measures China is taking and will take are necessary, timely countermeasures that are defensive in nature which have gone through serious consideration and careful assessment, and they’re aimed at protecting our nation’s sovereignty and security. They are consistent with international law and domestic laws. They are a warning to the provocateurs and also aimed at protecting regional stability and peace in the Taiwan Strait. All parties need to clearly recognize the cause and nature of the current crisis, jointly oppose the recklessness and the provocation of the US, continue to support China’s just position and measures and jointly protect regional and cross-Strait peace.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","CGTN","Nancy Pelosi said in a statement on August 3 that the Congressional delegation’s visit to Taiwan should be seen as a strong statement that America stands with Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","We often hear US politicians say that they are standing together with so and so, but history and facts have repeatedly shown that whomever the US politicians claim they are standing together with would become the targets of chaos and disaster. Just look at Iraq, Syria, Libya, and Afghanistan, and also look at the people responsible for what Pelosi called “a beautiful sight to behold” in Hong Kong and the “Hong Kong independence” separatists. See what has become of them?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News","We just heard that the previously scheduled meeting between State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Japanese Foreign Minister today has been canceled. Can you confirm this? If so, is it China’s decision or is it caused by the Japanese side? If it’s the former, does it have anything to do with the G7 statement that you just responded to?","I’ll answer your three questions altogether. China has made it clear that it will no longer schedule a meeting between Chinese and Japanese foreign ministers in Phnom Penh. Japan joined other members of G7 and the EU in issuing a joint statement which contains groundless accusations against China, confounds black and white and tries to justify the US’s infringement on China’s sovereignty. This has caused a public outcry among the Chinese people. We thus decided not to go ahead with the meeting between the two foreign ministers in Phnom Penh.\nJapan is historically responsible for its wrongdoing on the Taiwan question. Japan is in no position to make unwarranted remarks on issues related to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","AFP","ASEAN foreign ministers expressed their concerns in a statement today against provocative action in the Taiwan Strait. They said the current situation could lead to miscalculation and serious confrontation. Is China concerned about such potential miscalculations or confrontations resulting from military exercises this week?","The root cause of the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait is the joint provocation of the US side and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, which seriously violates the one China principle and infringes upon our sovereignty and territorial integrity. In the face of such flagrant provocation, we are compelled to take justified, necessary countermeasures to uphold our sovereignty and territorial integrity. All our measures are targeted against the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Anyone who is concerned about regional tensions should be asking the US to immediately and credibly follow the one-China principle, stop violating China’s sovereignty and take real actions to uphold regional peace and stability. It is very clear here who is responsible for the incident and who is the provocateur. China is only being compelled to act in self-defense. I hope that you could see that fact.\nI’m sure you know that in the statement, ASEAN says it is opposed to provocations. And Pelosi’s visit itself is a serious provocation. ASEAN countries hope to see peace and stability in this region and oppose any serious provocation like Pelosi’s visit. They are concerned that such reckless provocations could put regional peace and stability into a precarious situation.\nAs I said yesterday, many countries spoke up immediately in various ways to express opposition to the visit, a serious and dangerous provocation, and reiterated the commitment to the one-China principle.\nThe Spokesperson of the UN Secretary-General said that the UN is guided by the one-China policy. UN Secretary-General António Guterres then reiterated that the UN abides by the one-China policy and UNGA resolution 2758. The League of Arab States expressed support to China yesterday. The Shanghai Cooperation Organization just made a statement saying that the SCO adheres to the one-China principle, firmly opposes interference in the internal affairs of its member states by any external force, supports all member states in safeguarding national unity and defending their own sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will continue to promote further cooperation among member states in this regard to ensure peace, security and stability in the region. Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov said again that he did not see any reason to create such an irritant literally out of nowhere. Pakistan’s Foreign Ministry reaffirms in a statement Pakistan’s strong commitment to the one-China principle and firm support for China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Cuba’s Foreign Ministry issued a statement condemning interference in China’s internal affairs, stating its firm rejection to the actions aimed at harming China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and emphasizing its concern over the increasing tensions as a direct result of the aggressive policy and high military presence of the US and its allies in the Taiwan Strait. Cuban Foreign Minister said on social media that Cuba rejects actions aimed at harming the territorial integrity and sovereignty of the People’s Republic of China, and condemns interference in its internal affairs. Iranian Foreign Minister said that his country’s support of one-China principle is indubitable. US provocative actions have turned into a source of threat to international peace and stability and the international community must stop it. Myanmar’s Foreign Ministry issued a statement saying that Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is causing escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait. Myanmar opposes any provocative actions causing instabilities in the region and attempts that aim to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries and Myanmar fully supports the one-China principle. Spokesperson of the Indonesian Foreign Ministry said that Indonesia continues to respect the one-China policy. Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan may escalate confrontation between China and the US. If not managed well, it may lead to open conflict and disrupt peace and stability, including in the Taiwan Strait. The Thai Foreign Ministry said that Thailand stands by the one-China principle and it is important to abide by principles of respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity. Spokesperson of Vietnam’s Foreign Ministry reiterated that the country adheres to the one-China policy. The Ethiopian Foreign Ministry said that the country firmly supports the one-China principle, which is also supported by the UN and the African Union. The Sudanese Foreign Minister said in a statement that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and Sudan supports China’s efforts to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Republic of the Congo’s Foreign Minister said that upholding the one-China principle is his country’s unwavering policy and the Republic of the Congo firmly supports China’s actions to defend its national sovereignty and territorial integrity. South Sudan’s Foreign Ministry said it supports the one-China principle and opposes interference in China’s internal affairs. Chairperson of South African Parliament said that the US moves are a gross interference in China’s internal affairs, which will ruin the efforts over the years to uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and inevitably endanger regional peace and stability. Greek Foreign Minister expressed support for the one-China policy when it comes to upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity during a meeting with State Councilor Wang Yi on the sidelines of the ASEAN ministerial meetings. Serbian Prime Minister said when meeting with the Chinese Ambassador that Serbia supports the one-China policy and considers Taiwan as an integral part of China. The Nicaraguan Vice President openly expressed support for China in its effort to uphold national sovereignty and condemned the imperialist intervention of the US. Nicaragua’s Foreign Minister, in a statement, strongly condemned Pelosi’s visit and said Nicaragua fully supports China’s position on the Taiwan question, supports China in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and urges the US side to immediately stop its contemptible provocation against China. The Venezuelan foreign ministry said that Pelosi’s visit is a direct provocation and serious threat to China’s independence and territorial integrity and Venezuela firmly supports the one-China principle and urges the US to respect China’s sovereignty.\nGeneral Secretary of People’s Vanguard Party (PVP) of Costa Rica said that the PVP firmly supports China in defending sovereignty and territorial integrity. In Brazil, President of the Communist Party and Secretary of International Relations issued a statement titled Taiwan: Imperialism Provokes China and Further Threatens World Peace to condemn Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan. The Communist Party of Argentina released a declaration condemning the US for violating UNGA resolution 2758 and its commitment in the Joint Communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the US, and pointing out that Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is a strong provocation and imperialist aggression, and calling on governments and people across the world to speak up against what the US has done.\nIn addition, press from Russia, Thailand, Cuba, South Africa, Zimbabwe and Angola have published commentaries to stress that Taiwan is a part of China and how Pelosi’s visit seriously violates the one-China principle, constitutes a serious provocation, seriously infringes on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Well-known British scholar Martin Jacques wrote in an article that Pelosi’s provocation over Taiwan leads the US and the world into an age of disorder and instability. The tension in the Taiwan Strait is caused by the US’s encroachment on the understanding it reached with China.\nAll this shows that the one-China principle is a universal consensus and what is a just cause can receive the support of many around the world. So I hope what I have shared with you will help you understand who is the provocateur and should be responsible for the tensions in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","China Daily","A US State Department official said that China should not use Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan as a pretext to continue seeking to change the status quo with regard to Taiwan. And if any escalation or crisis were to somehow follow her visit, it would be on Beijing. Do you have any comment on these remarks?","This is the US’s typical way of confounding right and wrong and acting like a thief crying “stop thief”. It shows how domineering, arbitrary and unscrupulous the US always is. I would like the US to answer four questions.\nFirst, what is the status quo on the Taiwan question? The facts are crystal clear, i.e. both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China and Taiwan is part of China’s territory. Despite being politically against each other for a long time, China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been split. This is the real status quo of the situation in the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond, who is creating the crisis in the Taiwan Strait? The collusion between the US and “Taiwan independence” forces and their provocation is the fundamental factor in causing the tension in the Taiwan Strait. In recent years, the DPP authorities have refused to recognize the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle, and tried to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence”. The US side has been distorting, obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle to serve its strategic goal of disrupting and containing China’s development. The US has sought to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China. It has been upgrading its contact with Taiwan and increased arms sales to Taiwan. Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan in disregard of global backlash gravely upgrades the substantive exchanges between the US and Taiwan. It seriously violates the US government’s commitment to the Chinese government on the Taiwan question and the basic norm in international relations and gravely infringes on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThird, who should be responsible for the tensions in the Taiwan Strait? China has repeatedly told the US the grave nature and harm of the visit and made it clear that all consequences arising therefrom should be borne by the US side. So do not say that we have not told the US all this in advance. But the US government and Speaker Pelosi staged a double act and insisted on pursuing the wrong path. The US made the provocation first, and China has been compelled to act in self-defense. The Chinese government has the right to do whatever necessary and justified to resolutely uphold our sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nFourth, who is changing the status quo in the Taiwan Strait? The US cited its wrongful action 25 years ago to justify the visit. But we have made it very clear that past mistakes do not serve as justification for repeating that mistake. China always learns from past experience. We will not allow the US to continue to use salami tactics to encroach upon, obscure and hollow out the one-China principle. We will not allow the US to use any pretext or excuse to gradually change the status quo.\nLet me emphasize once again that at present any tension emerging in the Taiwan Strait is caused single-handedly by the US. Fundamentally, it is because Speaker Pelosi insisted on visiting Taiwan out of selfish interest and serious violated the one-China principle. We would not be dealing with this had Pelosi not made that provocative visit to Taiwan. Many countries and media outlets across the world also share a clear, objective and correct understanding of that and have warned the US in various ways. So if the US truly cares about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, then the most important and crucial thing for it to do is make sure at once that it would strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-US Joint Communiqués in both words and deeds.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Has China’s deepening tensions with the US over Taiwan now extended to the rest of the G7 nations?","China always hopes to have friendly and cooperative relations on the basis of mutual respect, equality and win-win cooperation with the G7 countries and all other countries in the world. I believe this is the shared aspiration of people in all countries and serves countries’ common interests. Meanwhile, on issues concerning sovereignty and territorial integrity, there is no room for China to compromise or concede. All countries having diplomatic relations with China must abide by the one-China principle.\nAnd as for the impact of the tension emerging from the Taiwan question between China and the US on China’s relations with other G7 members, I think it’s up to those G7 nations -- what they think and do about this. If they decide to follow the US and admit that they do not have an independent foreign policy or if they do not care about the interests of their own countries and peoples and are willing to tie their own countries to the US and be the US’s sidekicks, then I very much doubt whether the people of their respective countries would say yes to that.\nIf they are truly independent nations, then they should make decisions based on the interests of their own countries and peoples and follow the one-China principle, because it is the most important political prerequisite and foundation for their diplomatic relations with China. Relevant countries should be able to understand that because any responsible government would act in the long-term and fundamental interest of their own countries and the aspiration of their peoples and make independent decisions that best serve their interests.\nThis statement will not win the G7 any dignity or respect. The G7 only represents a tiny minority. Even if every person in the G7 countries support this statement, they only account for less than 10% of the world’s population. They do not represent the international community. Not to mention the fact that 85% of Americans do not approve of US policies and believe things in the US are headed in the wrong direction. How many people can this G7 foreign ministers’ statement really represent? What significance can it possibly have?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","You just told us that China has canceled a meeting with the Japanese foreign minister because of this statement or following this statement. Does that mean that China does not want to hold any foreign minister meetings with any G7 member nations for the moment due to this statement? And when will that change?","I have been very clear that since Japan has joined the other G7 countries and the EU in issuing this statement, which makes groundless accusations against China, confounds right and wrong and tries to justify the US’s violation of China’s sovereignty. The Chinese people deplore this move. Japan is historically responsible for its wrongdoing on the Taiwan question and is in no position to make unwarranted remarks on Taiwan-related issues.\nAs for the other G7 countries, unless they change their wrong practice on the Taiwan question, we may have to reconsider the meaning of having meetings and dialogue with them, which are supposed to boost trust and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Does China believe that these drills are conducive with winning the hearts and minds of the people in Taiwan?","Did you ask the Taiwan authorities, when they insisted on inviting Speaker Pelosi to Taiwan, had they asked the Taiwan people about their hearts and wills? I know that after Pelosi arrived in Taiwan, quite many people in Taiwan actually protested to that. Do Taiwan authorities put the expectations, wills and the welfare and interests of the Taiwan people close to its heart?\nAs I have said, the measures we have taken are justified, necessary and resolute. The aim is to protect our sovereignty and territorial integrity and send a message of warning to the provocateurs. These measures are directed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and interference of foreign forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Bloomberg","Just to clarify on the Japan issue. So on the G7, are you saying that it’s only Japan that has been singled out for this treatment or will that extend to other countries?","I think I have been clear enough. Japan, along with the other G7 countries, issued this so-called statement that accuses China, confounds black and white and does not distinguish right from wrong, not to mention that Japan is historically responsible for its wrongdoing on the Taiwan question. That’s why the Chinese people have been extremely unhappy about it. Under those circumstances, we no longer plan to schedule the meeting between the Chinese and Japanese foreign ministers in Phnom Penh.\nIn today’s world, global challenges like the COVID pandemic, the Ukraine crisis, and economic, energy and food issues, and regional hotspot issues all call for better cooperation between China and the G7 countries. However, if the G7 decides not to respect, and even hurt China’s core interests on issues concerning its sovereignty and territorial integrity, then there is no way that such wrongdoing would not impact the G7’s relations with China and cooperation on key issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News","First, given the meeting in Phnom Penh will still be going on tomorrow, is there any possibility for a meeting between Chinese and Japanese foreign ministers? Or what kind of atmosphere will it need for such a meeting to take place? Also you said yesterday, and I quote, “Since China and Japan have not yet carried out maritime delimitation in relevant waters, China does not accept the notion of so-called ‘Japanese…","On your first question, the reason is quite clear as to why China will no longer schedule the two foreign ministers’ meeting in Phnom Penh. To solve the problem, the most realistic way is for Japan to recognize its serious mistake and redress it through real action. Japan is historically responsible for its wrongdoing on the Taiwan question and is in no position to make unwarranted remarks, still less should it blindly follow the US’s steps and violate our sovereignty and territorial integrity. This would not be in the interest of the Japanese people, either.\nAs for your second question, China and Japan have not carried out maritime delimitation in relevant waters, so there is no such thing as China’s military actions being held in or entering Japan’s EEZ. Competent authorities in China have put out a notice. The military operations are fully in line with international law and international practices.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","You sort of suggested that if the G7 nations don’t respect China’s core interest on issues concerning China’s sovereignty, then this could affect relations. How might China’s relations with the seven countries be affected and for how long?","It would be very unwise for the G7 to say or do something improper on issues concerning China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Such things could easily remind the Chinese people of the days more than 100 years ago, in which China was invaded by the Eight-Power Allied Forces, a painful memory shared by all Chinese people.\nAs I said just now, we no longer live in a world in which imperialist powers could ride roughshod over Chinese people on Chinese soil. Today’s China is no longer the old China bullied and abused more than 100 years ago. The countries that historically invaded China and launched wars against China should develop a greater sensitivity and consciousness when it comes to issues concerning China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. They should respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and not offend the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people on those issues.\nIt might be useful for the G7 countries to think about how the US managed to keep the country unified whatever the costs during the Civil War. The UK has the issue of Scotland, while Canada has the issue of Quebec. Some states are seeking independence from the US. So on issues concerning sovereignty and territorial integrity, I hope these countries are fully aware of their own stakes and act prudently.\nAs to how these countries’ wrongful actions on the Taiwan question could affect their relations with China, and how long would it take before relations could become normal again, that’s entirely up to them, what they would do, whether they could quickly recognize the mistakes and whether they could take real actions to correct their mistakes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","PTI","You took a question earlier on the status quo prevailing over Taiwan. There is a big report today in the Global Times, which says Pelosi’s visit changes the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. There is some kind of peace prevailing in the Taiwan Strait for a long time. So perhaps the status quo also means that. So the drills, the military exercises, is it going to be a new normal of what we’re going to witness…","About the status quo in the Taiwan Strait, I have said in detail what exactly the status quo is. The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. That is the real status quo of the Taiwan Strait. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been split. For some time, the US and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces have colluded with each other, substantively upgraded the exchanges between the US and Taiwan, intensified armed sales to Taiwan and violated the one-China principle and the commitments made to the Chinese government. In particular, Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan despite opposition from across the world is a grave provocation that substantively upgrades US-Taiwan exchanges.\nWe have issued warnings many times. It is based on the experience and lessons we have learned from the past that we know we cannot let the US use this type of salami tactics to keep pushing the envelope on China’s red lines. So in the face of such a provocation that seriously undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, we are left with no choice but to take resolute measures to demonstrate our resolve and capability to uphold our sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nAnd will this become a new normal? It hinges on the action of the US side and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. Unless they stop trying to split China, China will never stop taking resolute actions to uphold our sovereignty and territorial integrity, not even for a day. And we will not stop demonstrating our resolve, will and capability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Taiwan’s Digital Minister Audrey Tang said the volume of cyberattacks on Taiwan government units on Tuesday was over 15,000 gigabits, 23 times higher than the previous daily record. What’s China’s comment? And is the Chinese government sponsoring these attacks?","I’m not aware of what you mentioned.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","AFP","Seeing as Nancy Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is already over, what does China feel needs to be done either by Taiwan or the US in order to make amends for its move?","Pelosi’s stunt ended very fast, but the grave damage and negative impact will not disappear any time soon. I believe the US and the Taiwan authorities know very well that the only way forward is to strictly abide by the one-China principle both in words and in deeds, and do nothing that will harm China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-04","Hua Chunying","Reuters","The Taiwan authorities is saying that there have been such a large number of cyber attacks on them in recent days, is that a matter of concern for China and what does China make of suggestions that it may have been behind these attacks?","This is not a foreign policy question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347339.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220804_10734474.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-08-04","Tan Kefei","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","A reporter asked: According to reports, Taiwan's defense authorities recently released their annual \"National Defense Report,\" hyping the mainland's military preparations against Taiwan and claiming they will build \"solid and resilient\" defensive combat capability to achieve the goal of holding firm. The head of Taiwan's defense authorities also clamored that they have the capability to counter the mainland and incited Taiwan's military officers and soldiers to fight to the death. What is the spokesperson's comment?\nWu Qian said: \"Taiwan is part of China; where does this 'National Defense Report' come from!\" For some time, the DPP authorities, seeking political self-interest, have incited cross-Strait confrontation, arbitrarily colluded with external forces, and stubbornly engaged in provocations for independence. These perverse actions seriously harm the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and they will inevitably be rejected by the people and subjected to historical judgment.\nWu Qian emphasized: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: confrontation leads nowhere, and \"using force to seek independence\" is a dead end. National reunification is unstoppable; a mantis trying to stop a chariot is overestimating itself. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is on full-time standby, ready to fight at any time, and will swiftly and decisively thwart any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist scheme, and will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16188390.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-08-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 4 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on August 4 that Hsiao Bi-khim frequently spread pro-independence remarks, zealously instigated US political figures to visit Taiwan, vigorously promoted arms purchases from the US, incited the drafting of negative bills related to Taiwan, and recently strongly pushed for Pelosi’s intrusion into Taiwan, openly challenging the One-China principle, seriously undermining cross-Strait relations and further exacerbating the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. In order to seek political gain, Hsiao has not hesitated to serve as a pawn of external anti-China forces, harming the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and pushing Taiwan compatriots into the abyss of danger. Anyone who sells out national interests and engages in “Taiwan independence” separatism will have no good end and will inevitably be subject to historical reckoning.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220804_12458074.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-04","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","On August 3, the foreign ministers of the Group of Seven and the High Representative of the European Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy issued a statement saying that China's response to Pelosi's visit to Taiwan would heighten tensions and cause regional instability. Earlier, US officials also claimed that China's response should not lead to a crisis. What is your comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 4 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered questions on August 4, saying: Regarding Pelosi's sneaking visit to Taiwan, the facts are very clear and the nature is very serious. It was not a defense or safeguarding of any so-called \"democracy and freedom\"; rather, it was a provocation against and an infringement upon China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Taiwan question is not a \"regional\" issue; it is China's internal affair. Our taking necessary countermeasures is the proper and justified course of action to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity. Our punishment of diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements and external interfering forces is a measure taken to safeguard sovereignty, security and development interests in accordance with international law and the basic norms of international relations, as any sovereign state would do. It is reasonable, lawful and justified.\nHe said that we urge the relevant organizations and individuals to stop confusing right and wrong and reversing black and white, to stop making excuses for the \"Taiwan independence\" forces and anyone who interferes in other countries' internal affairs, to act on the solemn commitments made on the Taiwan question through concrete actions, to adhere to the one-China principle, and to cease all conduct that interferes in China's internal affairs and provokes China's sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220804_12458406.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","CGTN","US officials like the NSC Coordinator for Strategic Communications said that “China has chosen to overreact and use the Speaker’s visit as a pretext to increase provocative military activity in and around the Taiwan Strait”. NATO Secretary-General also shared his view. Do you have any comment?","The current situation is entirely caused by Speaker Pelosi and other US politicians. Hearing this type of rhetoric from the US officials reminds people of the story of the Emperor’s New Clothes. It is time for the US to get rid of its arrogance, selfishness, and hypocrisy and bullying practices.\nThe context and the events that led to the tensions in the Taiwan Strait are crystal-clear. The US is the unprovoked provocateur and creator of the crisis.\nThe Taiwan question is not about democracy. It is a major issue of principle about China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US needs to put itself in others’ shoes. If an American state were to secede from the US and declare independence, and then some other nation provided weapons and political support for that state, would the US government — or the American people — allow this to happen?\nThe visit of Pelosi to Taiwan is a grave provocation that upgraded substantive exchanges between the US and Taiwan. It is a serious violation of the one-China principle. It seriously tramples on basic norms in international relations. It also seriously undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China has done everything diplomatically possible. We had repeatedly warned the US through various channels of the grave nature and severe harm of this visit. We made it clear that China will not sit by and watch; we will not allow any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces; and all consequences arising therefrom must be borne by the US. The international community had been warning the US of the potential consequences as well. Many openly pointed out that the visit was a completely unnecessary, egregious provocation and could trigger a serious crisis. Sadly, however, the US turned a deaf ear to all of those and just let the visit happen.\nChina has acted in legitimate self-defense only after the US made this egregious provocation. Our countermeasures are necessary as a warning to the provocateurs and as a step to uphold our sovereignty and security. Now the US and its sidekicks have spoken up accusing China of “overreacting”. But if they truly care about regional peace and stability, why hadn’t they stood up and tried to dissuade Pelosi early on? Couldn’t they have seen this coming and prevented it? On such an issue concerning China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, China’s countermeasures are justified, necessary and proportionate, and there is nothing excessive about them. The US, as the provocateur and the one that caused the crisis, should and must assume the entire responsibility for it.\nChina’s measures are also about staunchly safeguarding regional peace and stability and international law and basic norms in international relations. As we have seen over the past decades, the US and the US-led NATO countries have selectively applied international law. They made up various pretexts such as so-called possession of weapons of mass destruction to picture other countries as threats - and sometimes even without any valid reason - to blatantly launch military strikes and even unleash wars on sovereign countries. How many humanitarian tragedies have they created in the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, Iraq, Libya, Syria and Afghanistan? How many innocent civilians have been wounded and killed? How many families have been torn apart and lost? Have the US and other NATO countries involved done any soul-searching on these tragedies? Have they felt even a tinge of guilt for the serious ramifications and catastrophes they caused? Have they ever made an apology to the victims in those countries? And have they ever given them any compensation?\nWe are living in the 21st century. The world must never allow the US to see itself as a “world policeman” or an “international judge” and continue to treat other sovereign nations like George Floyd as if the US can just bully and strangle them at will. If China does nothing about the US’s relentless interference in our internal affairs and violation of our sovereignty or does not firmly resist the US’s reckless and irresponsible behavior, respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity and other purposes of the UN Charter and basic norms in international relations will become nothing but words on paper. And the vast developing world which account for over 80% of the world’s population could well become the next target anytime. For this exact reason, already more than 160 countries have made their voice of justice heard. They reiterated their commitment to the one-China policy and expressed support for China’s efforts to firmly uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is a fight against hegemony, against interference and against secession.\nChina had historically been a victim of foreign aggression. Today, the US and several of its sidekicks still grossly interfere in our internal affairs and undermine our sovereignty and security from time to time. But China is not the China 120 years ago, and we refuse to be treated like Iraq, Syria, or Afghanistan. The Chinese people will never allow any foreign force to bully, oppress, or subjugate us. Anyone who would attempt to do so will find themselves on a collision course with a great wall of steel forged by over 1.4 billion Chinese people. The position of the Chinese government and people on the Taiwan question is consistent. To uphold the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China is the firm will of the 1.4 billion Chinese people. We hope that the US and its sidekicks who style themselves as democracies will be very clear about that. They need to take seriously and respect the core interests and the firm will of the Chinese people, who account for one fifth of the world’s population.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","Shenzhen TV","As we understand, the Chinese, the US and the Japanese foreign ministers had a war of words on the Taiwan question at the East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting on August 5. Do you have more to say on that?","At the East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting on August 5, some countries made unwarranted accusations against China’s legitimate measures to uphold its rights. But the majority of countries present did not agree with those accusations and showed understanding for China’s position.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi made a full and strong rebuttal to each of the pieces of disinformation and false accusations uttered by certain countries. He made clear what the facts are, defended China’s sovereignty and upheld justice.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","Phoenix TV","The US has decided to reschedule its long-planned Minuteman III ICBM test because it is demonstrating the behavior of a responsible country by reducing security risks. How do you respond to that?","Somehow the word “responsible” sounds a bit awkward when the US uses it to describe itself.\nIf the US is indeed a responsible country, it should have stopped Speaker Pelosi from visiting Taiwan early on to prevent this type of major provocation from happening. And the US should have removed the many military vessels and aircraft it has deployed in the Asia-Pacific and right at China’s doorstep.\nIf the US is indeed a responsible country, it should immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs on whatever grounds or under whatever pretexts, immediately stop using salami tactics to encroach upon and hollow out the one-China principle, immediately stop upgrading the substantive exchanges between the US and Taiwan, and immediately stop arms sales to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Japan said yesterday five ballistic missiles were fired by China and landed in Japan’s EEZ. Is this true and does the foreign ministry have any comment on?","For the Chinese military’s drills in the waters off the Taiwan Island, the Chinese competent authorities have issued safety alerts and navigation warnings in advance. The practices of the Chinese side were consistent with international law and practices.\nAs for “Japan’s EEZ” that you mentioned, China and Japan have not carried out maritime delimitation in relevant waters, so there is no such thing as what you called “Japan’s EEZ”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","CCTV","Over the past few days, we noticed many countries have voiced support for China over US House Speaker Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, and you shared quite some examples with us. Could you give us more updates today?","Indeed, in the wake of Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, over 160 countries have spoken up for justice, condemned the visit as a serious, reckless and irresponsible provocation and expressed their commitment to the one-China principle and support for China’s efforts to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity. Apart from what I shared with you over the past couple of days, I have some further updates for you today.\nSri Lankan President Ranil Wickremesinghe reiterated on social media Sri Lanka’s firm commitment to the one-China policy as well as to the UN Charter principles of sovereignty and territorial integrity of nations.\nSingaporean Foreign Minister Vivian Balakrishnan said in talks with State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi during the East Asia cooperation foreign ministers’ meetings that Singapore has a clear and consistent one-China policy and is opposed to Taiwan independence and any unilateral moves to change the status quo.\nThailand’s Foreign Ministry spokesperson expressed respect for China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Laos released a statement reiterating its support for the policy of China on national reunification by peaceful means and reaffirming its consistent policy that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China as well as its opposition to any intention aimed at creating a situation for “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”. Lao Foreign Minister Saleumxay Kommasith said while meeting with State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi that the US’s recent provocation on the Taiwan question goes against its own commitment and undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Laos is strongly against any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and supports China’s efforts to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Malaysian Prime Minister’s Special Envoy to China released a statement urging Western nations against practicing double standards by trying to compare Taiwan with Ukraine or trying to encircle Russia and call for respect for Ukraine’s sovereignty and territorial integrity on one hand while meddling in China’s internal affairs and intending to use Taiwan to divide China on the other. This would be using democracy as a pretext to interfere in and infringe upon China’s sovereignty in violation of basic principles of international law.\nThe UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation issued a statement, reaffirming its support for China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity as well as the importance of respecting the one-China principle, while calling for adherence to relevant UN resolutions. The UAE indicated its concern over the impact of any provocative visits on stability and international peace.\nKyrgyz Foreign Ministry said in a statement that the Kyrgyz Republic confirms its firm support for the one-China principle. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Kyrgyzstan opposes “Taiwan independence” and any attempt to create the false impression of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”.\nThe spokesperson of Kazakhstan’s Foreign Ministry reaffirms its adherence to the one-China principle and the UN General Assembly resolution 2758 on the Taiwan question.\nUzbekistan’s Foreign Ministry reiterated in a statement that Uzbekistan supports the one-China principle and the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China in accordance with the generally recognized principles of international law.\nTajikistan’s Foreign Ministry expressed in a statement its support to China’s territorial integrity and reiterated its commitment to the one-China principle.\nThe spokesperson of the Afghan Interim Government’s Foreign Ministry stressed adherence to the one-China principle and urged all countries to refrain from decisions that are considered a violation of national sovereignty of states and lay the groundwork for provocative actions.\nThe spokesperson of Egypt’s Foreign Ministry affirmed Egypt’s commitment to the one-China principle and all relevant UN resolutions.\nEritrea’s Foreign Ministry said in a statement that at a time when the flaws and follies of its global policy have become more apparent, and in an attempt to ramp up its policy of containment of China, Washington has concocted the provocative visit of House Speaker Pelosi to Taiwan with all its perilous ramifications. The latest act is but a continuation of reckless policies that the US administration has pursued in the past years in Asia to advance this singular objective, which is deplorable.\nZimbabwean Minister of Information, Publicity and Broadcast Services and government spokesperson said that Zimbabwe stands fully behind the People’s Republic of China in the face of the intrusive and provocative visit by Nancy Pelosi, which seriously violates the one-China principle.\nBurundi’s Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs said the government of Burundi firmly follows the one-China policy and China’s effort to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Foreign Ministry of the Commonwealth of Dominica said in a statement that many sides and the international community have expressed serious concerns over Pelosi’s visit to China’s Taiwan region and this visit constitutes serious violation of China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Vice President of the Senate of Mexico published an article, saying that the illegal visit of Pelosi to Taiwan is an interventionist action that seriously violates other country’s sovereignty and undermines regional peace and stability.\nVanuatu’s Minister for Climate Change in a statement expressed support to China’s upholding of sovereignty and territorial integrity and opposition to undermining stability in any form.\nLuxembourg’s Foreign Minister said that Pelosi’s visit is a useless provocation and that with this trip, there will be no more trust between the US and China. He also reiterated Luxembourg’s support to the one-China policy.\nCyprus’ Government Spokesperson said that Cyprus is committed to the one-China policy and fully respects international law, sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nIn addition, political parties and political dignitaries in many countries have added their voice to the chorus of condemnation of Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan. They say this is an act of hegemony and support China in upholding sovereignty and territorial integrity. For example, the Communist Party of Nepal (Marxist–Leninist), the Nepal Workers’ and Peasants’ Party (NWPP) and Rastriya Prajatantra Party (RPP) have spoken out through various means, pointing out that Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is extremely erroneous, foolish and irresponsible act of hegemony. They said that the Nepali side firmly supports all of China’s effort to uphold its sovereignty and dignity.\nMongolia’s third largest party Civil Will-Green Party stressed in a statement that countries need to abide by the one-China principle stipulated in UNGA resolution 2758 and support China’s position on the Taiwan question and other issues.\nThe General Secretary of the All India Forward Bloc issued a statement strongly condemning Pelosi’s visit to the Taiwan region and saying that the visit and Pelosi’s remarks violate UNGA resolution 2758.\nThe Communist Party of Tajikistan released a statement saying that the visit by Pelosi is a flagrant provocation, which is consistent with the US’s all-round containment and aggression on China. China has the right to take necessary measures on the Taiwan question to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Chairman of the Kenya-China Parliamentary Friendship Group of Kenya released a statement supporting China in its efforts for achieving the full reunification, and supporting the Chinese government’s measures to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Socialist Party of Zambia said in a statement that the US has neither the ability to solve domestic issues like COVID-19 and human rights violations nor the ability to address global challenges like poverty and hunger. Yet, it tries to start wars and ruin peace to sustain its hegemony. Such imperialist practices will be condemned by all peace-loving people.\nThe Communist Party of Chile, a member of Chile’s ruling coalition, condemned the US government’s provocation against China in a statement.\nPresident of the Workers’ Party of Brazil pointed out Pelosi’s visit is a move that threatens peace and incites armed conflict. It not only emboldens the “Taiwan independence” forces, but also generates instability and insecurity in the region.\nThe Chairman of Kiribati’s ruling party released a statement, expressing extreme disappointment at Pelosi’s visit, saying that the US government is fully responsible for this and the US should offer an official apology.\nThe Communist Party of Bolivia issued a statement saying that the US’s provocation is repudiating. Bolivia will be in solidarity with China, and support China in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It will stand with political, civil and social organizations to denounce the US imperialism undermining international security and stability.\nThe Party of Socialists of Moldova said in its statement that it is committed to unconditional respect and support for China’s efforts in upholding sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nJapanese former Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama criticized the US on social media saying that what it has done is unwise without drawing lessons from the past.\nIn addition, foreign ministers of ASEAN countries called for upholding the UN Charter, and reiterated the Member States’ support for the one-China policy.\nThese countries, with their population accounting for 80% to 90% of the world’s total, are standing with the Chinese people. Our shared belief is that countries should be committed to the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and the basic norms in international relations. We are all firmly against the attempts to interfere in other countries’ domestic affairs and undermine other countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity. We have the backing from over 160 countries. We are standing on the right side of history and on the side of peace and justice.\nI hope that the US and its handful of “buddies” will realize that if they do respect the principle of democracy, then they should hear and respect the voice of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, and also the voice of the people from the countries accounting for close to 90% of the world’s population in non-Western countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","Kyodo News","According to reports, Foreign Minister Wang Yi and his Russian counterpart walked out of a speech by Japan’s foreign minister at today’s East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting. Can you give us more information? How do you comment on that?","I am not aware of what you described, but I wish to use this opportunity to remind the Japanese side that the Japanese leadership has acted egregiously on Taiwan. The Chinese people are very unhappy about that.\nAs we have said, Japan is historically responsible for its serious wrongdoing on the Taiwan question. Japan is in no position to make unwarranted remarks on the Taiwan question. Today, when meeting with Speaker Pelosi, the Japanese Prime Minister made groundless accusations against China. During the ASEAN-plus foreign ministers’ meetings, the Japanese foreign minister joined US State Secretary in spreading disinformation on China and made unwarranted accusations against China. China firmly opposes this.\nWe have repeatedly made clear our principled position on the Taiwan question. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is caused by Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan in disregard of China’s opposition and dissuasion of other countries. Japan selectively ignores the US’s violation of China’s sovereignty, and yet loudly criticizes the one protecting its rights and tries to justify the other side’s violations. This is confounding right with wrong and confusing white with black. Those trying to make provocations and create troubles on the Taiwan question in an attempt to delay China’s development, undermine China’s peaceful reunification and rise will only end in vain.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-05","Hua Chunying","Reuters","Japan reported that China fired four missiles over Taipei during its drills. Is that true? If so, what’s China’s comment on that?","The Chinese side has released information on the military exercise. The visit by Speaker Pelosi triggered the current tensions and all China’s countermeasures are justified, necessary, and proportionate. We hope the Japanese side will have the correct understanding on this.\n***\nIf there are no further questions, I would like to recommend an article to you, especially media outlets from Europe and the US including Reuters and Bloomberg. In response to US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s op-ed titled Why I’m leading a congressional delegation to Taiwan published on August 2, the Chinese Ambassador to the US Mr. Qin Gang published an article titled Why China objects to Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan on The Washington Post on August 4. Ambassador Qin Gang’s article is very well written. It provides a very clear and succinct outline of the historical context of the Taiwan question. I’m sure this will help you gain a deeper understanding of the Taiwan question and a deeper and accurate understanding of why China is opposed to Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220805_10735734.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-05","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Regarding the fact that “Taiwan independence” element Yang Chih-yuan is being investigated by the national security authorities in accordance with law, the DPP authorities expressed so-called “protest” and called on Taiwan residents to exercise caution when traveling to the mainland. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 4 (Xinhua) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on the 4th that on August 3, state security organs, in accordance with the law, placed Yang Chih-yuan, a suspect who has long engaged in \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and is suspected of endangering national security, under criminal detention review. This is the first case in which relevant state departments have pursued criminal liability in accordance with the law against a \"Taiwan independence\" element on the island on suspicion of the crimes of splitting the country and inciting to split the country. The case is currently being handled, and the handling authorities are protecting all of the suspect's lawful rights in accordance with the law.\nHe said that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and safeguarding national sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity is a legal obligation of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan. Any individual or organization that fails to fulfill this statutory obligation or engages in activities that endanger national security shall be held legally accountable in accordance with the law. \"Taiwan independence\" diehards who openly advocate \"independence\" and engage in egregious acts to pursue \"independence\" will not escape the severe punishment of the nation's laws.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that punishing a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" diehards in accordance with the law aims to resolutely oppose and curb the separatist schemes and acts of \"Taiwan independence,\" maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. We have consistently and warmly welcomed and supported the broad mass of compatriots in Taiwan to come to the mainland for development, and we have consistently and effectively enhanced and protected the various lawful rights and interests of compatriots in Taiwan. The so-called \"protests\" by the DPP authorities can neither save the \"Taiwan independence\" elements from being punished in accordance with the law, nor stop the general trend of compatriots on both sides of the Strait engaging in exchanges, cooperation, and drawing closer together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220805_12458634.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-06","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Tsao Hsing-cheng used Pelosi’s incursion into Taiwan to attack and smear the mainland and Taiwan’s unification-supporting forces, and claimed that donations would be used to help strengthen so-called “Taiwan security.” What comments do you have? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 5 (dateline): In response to Tsao Hsing-cheng's attacks and smears against the mainland and the pro-unification forces in Taiwan, using Pelosi's visit to Taiwan as a pretext, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said in answering a reporter's question on the 5th that Tsao Hsing-cheng's words and deeds distort basic facts, wildly attack and smear the mainland, and serve as a cover for “Taiwan independence” forces and external forces. They do not represent Taiwan's business community, let alone the broad masses of Taiwan's people, and are doomed to be wasted effort. We believe that the vast majority of people in Taiwan's business community and Taiwan compatriots are able to distinguish right from wrong, recognize that “Taiwan independence” will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan, recognize the sinister intention of the U.S. to “use Taiwan to contain China,” and, through concrete actions, maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nMa Xiaoguang said that it is well known that the DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to seek independence and provoke confrontation is the root cause of the current tense and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait. Pelosi's visit to Taiwan seriously infringed on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and seriously endangered peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and the interests of compatriots on both sides. In the face of malicious provocation, the countermeasures we have taken are entirely just and justified.\nMa Xiaoguang said that it should be emphasized that all the necessary actions we have taken to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and are by no means directed at Taiwan compatriots. The purpose is to fundamentally safeguard the vital interests of compatriots on both sides and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220806_12458791.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi just wrapped up attending the ASEAN-plus foreign ministers’ meetings. What’s your comment on the outcomes of these meetings?","From August 4 to August 5, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the ASEAN-China Ministerial Meeting, the ASEAN Plus Three (APT) Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, the East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, and the ASEAN Regional Forum Foreign Ministers’ Meeting. This is the first time that the ASEAN-plus foreign ministers’ meetings are held physically since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic. At the meetings, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi elaborated on China’s propositions on China-ASEAN cooperation, East Asian cooperation and regional security cooperation and held in-depth exchange of views with other participating countries on strengthening solidarity and cooperation, maintaining security in Asia and promoting recovery and development.\nFirst, the need to uphold ASEAN centrality and practice open regionalism. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi pointed out the importance to keep East Asian cooperation in the right direction, uphold the spirit of openness and inclusiveness, adhere to the Asian way, consolidate the ASEAN-centered regional cooperation architecture, strengthen the ASEAN-centered cooperation platform, reject drawing ideological lines, oppose the introduction of bloc confrontation, prevent small exclusive groupings from impacting the regional architecture. The Chinese side also distributed documents such as the Position Paper of the People’s Republic of China on Supporting ASEAN Centrality in the Evolving Regional Architecture and a list of cooperation initiatives and projects in four priority areas of the ASEAN Outlook on the Indo-Pacific. Foreign ministers attending the meetings expressed appreciation for China’s long-standing support for ASEAN centrality.\nSecond, the need to deepen post-COVID recovery cooperation. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi proposed that in pursuing regional cooperation, countries should continue to give priority to development and people’s livelihood, and increase input in poverty alleviation and other fields, to better solve the development issue and achieve common development. China supports ASEAN in setting up regional vaccine production and distribution centers and strengthening capacity building in public health. We call for efforts to implement the cooperation initiative on global food security, jointly promote energy security and availability, and ensure a stable energy supply. We call for efforts to support the liberalization and facilitation of trade and investment, keep the functioning of industrial and supply chains stable and smooth, and build a Free Trade Area of the Asia-Pacific (FTAAP) and an Asia-Pacific Economic Community. China is willing to arrange a special allocation for RCEP economic and technical cooperation within the framework of the ASEAN-China Cooperation Fund. China supports the building of the APT Reserve of Medical Supplies for Public Health Emergencies. China will increase financial support for the ASEAN Plus Three Emergency Rice Reserve. It is important to expand exchanges and cooperation in digital infrastructure, e-commerce, digital logistics, smart cities and other fields. Countries need to work for the establishment of an APT low-carbon cooperative partnership.\nAll parties agreed to accelerate regional economic integration, fully implement RCEP, deepen cooperation in public health, digital economy, green development and other fields to achieve low-carbon and sustainable development and better benefit the people of all countries.\nThird, the need to uphold regional peace and stability. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said that countries should promote common security, attach importance to and show respect for other countries’ legitimate security concerns, and jointly safeguard regional peace and stability. All countries should earnestly abide by the UN Charter and international law, jointly maintain the international system with the United Nations at its core, and uphold the international order underpinned by international law, instead of imposing the so-called \"rules\" of an individual country or a bloc of countries on other states and coercing them into taking sides. China opposes the action of certain major countries to wantonly advance unilateralism, still less will China accept illegal sanctions and acts of suppression.\nChina has played a constructive role in further promoting the sound and solid development of East Asian cooperation and demonstrated its sense of responsibility as a major country.\nDuring the meetings, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi further elaborated on China’s stern position on the US’s provocation that infringed upon China’s sovereignty. He stressed that the one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The true “guardrails” for peaceful coexistence between China and the US are the three China-US joint communiqués. Seeking independence by soliciting US support is a dead end and attempts to use Taiwan to contain China are doomed to fail. The US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi insisted on visiting China’s Taiwan region in disregard of China’s grave concern and firm opposition. The Chinese side absolutely needed to respond resolutely to it. China’s position is justified, reasonable and lawful; our measures are firm, strong and proportionate; and China’s military exercises are open, transparent and professional. They are consistent with domestic and international laws, as well as international practices. China is not only firmly safeguarding its sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also upholding the international law and the basic norms governing international relations, particularly non-interference in countries’ internal affairs, which is the most important international norm enshrined in the UN Charter. That is why more than 100 countries have openly reiterated their firm commitment to the one-China policy and said that they understand and support China’s legitimate position.\nMany foreign ministers at the meeting said that they adhere to the one-China policy and understand and support the necessary measures China has taken to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity. The ASEAN foreign ministers released a statement on the cross-Strait development reiterating ASEAN Member States’ support for the one-China policy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","Japan’s Prime Minister Fumio Kishida said recently that Japan strongly condemned China’s firing of missiles during military drills after they landed in Japan’s exclusive economic zone (EEZ), adding that they’ve noted China doesn’t agree to this. He also called it a “problem that impacts our national security and the safety of our citizens” and has “a serious impact on the peace and stability of ... the…","We are firmly against Japan’s erroneous remarks and groundless accusations. Either legally, politically or morally, Japan is in no position, and has no right to make such remarks on the Taiwan question.\nRecently, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi has seriously refuted the Japanese side’s remarks at the East Asia cooperation foreign ministers’ meetings. Japan once illegally invaded and occupied Taiwan and kept the island under its colonial rule for as long as five decades. It has killed more than 600,000 of our Taiwan compatriots, plundered local resources there, and forcibly recruited laborers from countries in East Asia and elsewhere, many of whom were tortured to death. The Cairo Declaration jointly issued by China, the US and the UK in 1943 stipulates clearly that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan and the Penghu Islands, shall be restored to China. Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation published in 1945 stipulates that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. Later Japan accepted the Potsdam Proclamation and announced unconditional surrender. The China-Japan joint statement signed in 1972 when the two countries normalized their diplomatic relations clearly stipulates that “The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation”. Japan must never forget that part of history and there is a need for Japan to reflect on it from time to time.\nJapan has adopted such an assertive tone on the Taiwan question lately. Does it mean Japan has forgotten the commitments it made when signing the China-Japan joint statement? Does it mean Japan intends to subvert the political foundation of China-Japan relations? Does it mean that Japan has the ambition of laying its hands on China’s Taiwan region again? Does it mean that Japan is ready to use this as a pretext to expand military buildup, forsake its pacifist constitution and stop following the path of peaceful development? The Japanese side needs to give the international community a responsible explanation to all these questions.\nAs to Japan’s claim that China’s military drills have infringed on Japan’s so-called EEZ, since China and Japan have yet to carry out maritime delimitation in relevant waters, how could areas there be called “Japan’s EEZ”? Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China has conducted normal military drills in waters off its own territory. This move is open, transparent, professional and in line with China’s domestic law, international law and established international practices. This is both a warning we send to the provocateurs and a legitimate step to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nChina urges the Japanese side to earnestly reflect upon its history of aggression, fully understand the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, abide by the principles of the four China-Japan political documents and the commitments it has made, stop echoing the US’s negative rhetoric and act, stop following the US’s erroneous behavior of containing China using the Taiwan question, and avoid further causing serious harm to bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Can you help us understand if the drills in the immediate area of Taiwan have ceased as scheduled? Last week you announced some drills in the area. My question is, have they ceased as scheduled or are there ongoing military drills that you can share more details with us?","The Chinese military has issued a notice on that. Let me refer you to that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","AFP","As you mentioned, the Chinese military said today that it will continue to carry out joint exercises around Taiwan. What is the reason for this? Is this part of the countermeasures against Pelosi’s Taiwan visit? And if so, why were the exercises last week not considered sufficient?","In total disregard of the firm opposition and repeated representations of the Chinese side and with the connivance and arrangement of the US government, Speaker of the US House of Representatives Nancy Pelosi went ahead with the visit to China’s Taiwan region. This reckless move seriously undermined China’s sovereignty, seriously interfered in China’s internal affairs, seriously violated the commitments made by the US side, and seriously jeopardized peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. As State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi pointed out, China’s position is justified, reasonable and lawful; our measures are firm, strong and proportionate; and our military exercises are open, transparent and professional. They are consistent with domestic and international laws, as well as international practices. They are aimed at sending a warning to the perpetrator and punishing the “Taiwan independence” forces. We will firmly safeguard China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely stop the US’s attempt to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China, and shatter the Taiwan authorities’ wishful thinking to pursue “Taiwan independence” by soliciting the support of the US. By doing so, China is also upholding the international law and the basic norms governing international relations, particularly non-interference in countries’ internal affairs, which is the most important international norm enshrined in the UN Charter.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Anadolu Agency","The drills are mentioned in previous questions. But the Notice to Airmen, NOTAM, which was published for those activities, expired yesterday on August 7, at noon. To continue the exercises seems like a move which is not very consistent with the internationally customary practices. So will NOTAM for those new exercises be declared? Will there be any warning for civilian shipping or air traffic?","Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s normal military exercises are open, transparent and professional. Relevant authorities have issued notices in a timely manner. They are consistent with domestic and international laws, as well as established international practices. This serves as a message of warning to the provocateurs and is also a legitimate move to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","On August 5, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken, Australian Foreign Minister Penny Wong, and Japanese Foreign Minister Hayashi Yoshimasa released a joint statement after holding a trilateral strategic dialogue. “There is no change in the respective one China policies, where applicable, and basic positions on Taiwan of Australia, Japan, or the United States”, they said in the statement. Similar wording was found…","The one-China principle is an established international consensus and widely accepted basic norm in international relations. It constitutes part of the post-WWII world order and is affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758. It is the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and countries in the world. The UN Secretariat stressed in legal opinions that “the United Nations considers ‘Taiwan’ as a province of China with no separate status”. Certain countries have unilaterally added preconditions and provisos to the one-China policy in an attempt to distort, fudge and hollow out their one-China commitment. This is illegal, null and void. China is firmly against this.\nThe definition of the one-China principle is crystal clear, i.e., there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The applicability of this principle is universal, unconditional and indisputable. All countries having diplomatic relations with China and all Member States of the UN should unconditionally adhere to the one-China principle and follow the guidance of UNGA Resolution 2758. What some individual countries have done is essentially an attempt to misrepresent and distort the one-China principle. This is in effect challenging the basic principles of international law and basic norms governing international relations. This is also a challenge to the post-WWII world order.\nA person without credibility has no place in society; and a country that loses its credibility would falter. We urge certain countries to make sure that they read about the history, abide by the commitments they seriously made in black and white and recognize how dangerous and detrimental it is to act in bad faith and to justify the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Attempts to challenge the one-China principle, international rule of law and the international order are bound to be rejected by the international community and get nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","About the joint statement on the situation across the Taiwan Strait and the Taiwan question released by the Australian Foreign Minister together with the US Secretary of State and the Japanese Foreign Minister after their trilateral strategic dialogue, how does China see this move by Australia against the background of the current atmosphere of China-Australia relations?","I just stated China’s position on the statement by the US, Australia and Japan. The Australian side, in disregard of facts, has wantonly criticized China’s legitimate, justified and lawful measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Australia’s act violates the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, and undermines regional peace and stability. China firmly opposes it.\nIn the past few years, China-Australia relations have experienced serious difficulties for reasons caused by the Australian side. The merits of the issues involved are quite clear. China’s position on developing relations with Australia is consistent and clear. The sound and steady development of China-Australia relations serves the fundamental interests and shared aspirations of the two peoples. We urge the Australian side to develop a clear understanding of the situation, pursue the right course, respect China’s core interests and major concerns, abide by the one-China principle, observe basic norms governing international relations, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop saying or doing the things that undermine regional peace and stability, refrain from echoing or assisting certain countries’ misguided strategy of using the Taiwan question to contain China, and avoid creating new obstacles for China-Australia ties.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","I just want to clarify, did the ASEAN group support China on the recent Taiwan actions? I’m asking because Antony Blinken is also citing ASEAN supporting the US position. I wonder if you could clarify a little bit about the ASEAN response specifically on recent Taiwan actions by China?","I am happy to share with you some details in this regard.\nThe ASEAN foreign ministers released a statement on the cross-Strait development reiterating their commitment to the one-China policy.\nThe Spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Laos released a statement saying the following: The Lao PDR reaffirms its consistent policy of supporting “One China Policy” and that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and opposes any intention aiming at creating a situation for “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”. The Lao PDR reiterates its support for the policy of the Government of the People’s Republic of China on the national reunification by peaceful means.\nCambodian Foreign Minister Prak Sokhonn said the US has recently violated China’s sovereignty, reneged on its own promise and heightened the tension across the Taiwan Strait, which exposed Washington’s failure to match its words with actions as well as its hegemonic nature. Cambodia supports China’s effort to safeguard its legitimate rights and interests, and respond firmly to the provocative moves of the US.\nSingaporean Foreign Minister Vivian Balakrishnan said during talks with State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi on the sidelines of the East Asia cooperation foreign ministers’ meetings that Singapore has a clear and consistent “One China” policy and is opposed to “Taiwan independence” and any unilateral moves to change the status quo.\nThe Malaysian Prime Minister’s Special Envoy to China Tiong King Sing released a statement urging Western nations against practicing double standards, trying to compare Taiwan with Ukraine. “On the one hand, they condemn Russia’s aggression against Ukraine ... but, on the other hand, they intend to interfere in the internal affairs of the Taiwan Strait region”, he said. These acts are typical examples of using democracy as a pretext to interfere in and infringe upon other countries’ sovereignty in violation of basic principles of international law.\nIn fact, not just ASEAN countries, more than 170 countries in the international community have voiced staunch support for China on the Taiwan question through various means. They form an overwhelming majority versus the US and its few followers.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The Prime Minister of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines said today in Taipei that the Chinese military drills won’t prevent him from visiting friends. What’s China’s comment?","Just now I made it clear that China’s military exercises are open, transparent and professional. They are consistent with domestic and international laws, as well as international practices. They are aimed at sending a warning to the perpetrator and punishing the “Taiwan independence” forces. The vast majority of countries in the world have expressed their understanding and support.\nAs to the remarks you mentioned, I want to stress that there’s only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. No one can change this fact no matter what pretext or gambit they use. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. We believe relevant countries will eventually recognize this trend and make a decision that is consistent with where the trend is leading at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","On Friday, there was an announcement whereby China listed many different areas where communication between it and the US would either be curtailed or stopped completely. I wonder if you could tell us about what areas will continue to be open for discussion, where lines of communication will remain open between China and the US?","For any dialogue and communication to happen, there needs to be sincerity in the first place. China will continue to make démarches to the US side over Pelosi’s visit to the Taiwan region. We urge the US to earnestly reflect on and immediately correct its mistakes, stop its connivance at and support for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop playing the “Taiwan card” to contain China. At present, it is particularly important for the US to stop confounding right with wrong and deflecting blame, and stop escalating the situation and aggravating the crisis. The US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués with real actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-08","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","According to reports, a White House spokesperson said on August 6 that China’s activities in and around the Taiwan Strait are a significant escalation in its efforts to change the status quo and they are provocative and irresponsible. Do you have any comment?","The US’s mischaracterization of those events does not cover up one obvious fact: it is the US that is seeking to change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and causing the situation to escalate; it is the US that has made wanton provocations; and it is the US that has acted irresponsibly.\nSince four months ago, China has time and again made clear to the US through multiple channels and at various levels our stern position on Pelosi’s visit to the Taiwan region. We have been stressing that such a visit would seriously violate the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiqués and constitute a major escalation of US provocations. We have also made clear that the Chinese side would not sit idly by in the event of such a visit; that the US side must not harbor any illusion or miscalculate on this; and that all consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US side. China has tried every means and done everything possible to warn about the consequences of such a visit. However, the US has chosen to pursue the wrong course of action in disregard of China’s dissuasion and warnings. Just as State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said, what has happened is single-handedly orchestrated and provoked by the US and the context, cause and course of events are crystal clear. China has taken legitimate countermeasures only after the US made the provocation. Our countermeasures are aimed to uphold China’s sovereignty and security and consistent with international law and China’s domestic law. The US has been going down a wrong path which deviates from its commitment to the one-China principle, and yet it accuses China of escalating the situation. This is gangster logic.\nI have to point out that China’s resolute countermeasures against Pelosi’s visit is not only a necessary step to uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also a legitimate move to safeguard the basic norms governing international relations and the international order established after WWII. The one-China principle has been recognized by the UN and the overwhelming majority of countries in the world, and it has become a widely accepted basic norm in international relations and constitutes an important part of the post-WWII world order. To resolutely uphold the one-China principle and firmly reject attempts to fudge and hollow out the one-China policy is to unequivocally uphold the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs and the principle in international law of respecting countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity. For quite some time, in the name of democracy and human rights, the US has wantonly interfered in the internal affairs of developing countries and launched military interventions and aggression against them. That poses the biggest threat to regional and international security. By firmly opposing the US’s provocations on the Taiwan question, we are saying no to the US’s bullying and highhandedness, protecting cross-Strait peace and regional stability, and upholding international fairness and justice.\nChina’s legitimate measures have won broad support from the international community. More than 170 countries in the world have voiced their strong support for China to uphold its sovereignty and the one-China principle. They overwhelmingly outnumber the US and its few supporters. If the US acts wantonly and arbitrarily on the Taiwan question, neither the Chinese people, nor people elsewhere in the world will say yes to this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347341.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220808_10737382.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-08-08","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","近日，中方针对佩洛西窜台宣布八项反制措施，其中包括取消中美军事交往三项措施。有美国媒体报道，美军高层近日曾多次给中国军队领导打电话，但被中方拒绝。请问对此有何评论？","In response to Indian officials' groundless hyping of the so-called \"Chinese military threat,\" Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense and Senior Colonel, said at the regular press conference on the 25th that this seriously violates the strategic guidance from the leaders of both countries that China and India \"do not pose a threat to each other,\" incites geopolitical confrontation, is irresponsible, and is also dangerous. China firmly opposes this and has lodged solemn representations with the Indian side.\nA reporter asked: Recently, Indian Chief of Defence Staff Rawat said that India's greatest current security threat is China, and that there is a lack of \"trust\" between India and China in resolving the boundary dispute, with growing \"suspicion.\" What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian said that Indian officials' groundless hyping of the so-called \"Chinese military threat\" seriously violates the strategic guidance from the leaders of both countries that China and India \"do not pose a threat to each other,\" incites geopolitical confrontation, is irresponsible, and is also dangerous. China firmly opposes this and has lodged solemn representations with the Indian side.\nWu Qian stressed that China's position on the China-India boundary question is clear and definite. The determination and will of the Chinese border forces to safeguard national sovereignty and security are unwavering, while they are also committed to maintaining peace and tranquility in border areas and have made tremendous efforts to promote easing and de-escalation of the situation.\n\"China has an old saying: 'Use bronze as a mirror to correct your appearance; use history as a mirror to understand rise and fall; use people as a mirror to understand gains and losses,\"' Wu Qian said. \"As neighbors, we hope the Indian side will move in the same direction as China, jointly maintain peace and tranquility in border areas, and jointly maintain the healthy development of bilateral relations.\"","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16191696.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-08-09","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","On August 8, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi paid a visit to Mongolia upon invitation. Could you share more information on the visit?","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi just wrapped up a successful visit to Mongolia. During the visit, he met respectively with Mongolian President Ukhnaagiin Khurelsuh, Prime Minister Luvsannamsrai Oyun-Erdene, and Chairman of the State Great Khural of Mongolia Gombojav Zandanshatar, and held talks with Foreign Minister Battsetseg Batmunkh. The two sides held strategic communication on bilateral relations, practical cooperation and international and regional issues of mutual interest and reached extensive common understandings.\nBoth agreed that in the face of the complicated and fluid international and regional landscape, China and Mongolia share a closely-intertwined future. Both sides expressed readiness to seek greater synergy between the Belt and Road Initiative and Mongolia’s Steppe Road Program, between the Global Development Initiative and Mongolia’s New Revival Policy, between China’s “two-stage” development strategy and Mongolia’s long-term development vision, so as to foster three engines driving the development of bilateral relations. Both sides reiterated respect for each other’s independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity, and that they will continue to firmly support each other on issues concerning each other’s core interests. China supports Mongolia in upholding stability, focusing on development and exploring a development path suited to its national reality. China appreciates Mongolia’s reiteration of firm adherence to the one-China principle and opposition to interference in China’s internal affairs on issues related to Taiwan, Tibet, Xinjiang and Hong Kong. Both sides agreed to strengthen border cooperation, open up ports and connect railways and highways wherever possible so as to keep the industrial and supply chains stable and unimpeded. The two sides signed the Memorandum of Understanding on the cross-border railway connection program at the Gants Mod port, which will play an important role in helping Mongolia to expand its opening-up and achieve strong growth. Both sides agreed to promote cooperation in such fields as economy and trade, investment, mining and energy, science and technology, agriculture and animal husbandry, forge major demonstration projects in areas including infrastructure and energy, and strive to achieve coordinated development and common prosperity between the two countries. The two sides agreed to promote the Erdeneburen hydropower plant project in a coordinated manner, and speed up solving the electricity supply problem for people in western Mongolia. The two sides will support the implementation of livelihood projects such as shanty-town renovation, sewage treatment plant and meat processing plant as soon as possible to better benefit the Mongolian people. The two sides will enhance cooperation in afforestation and counter-desertification. China commends Mongolia’s plan to plant one billion trees, and China has proposed to plant 70 billion trees in the next ten years. We are ready to have mutual support in efforts to make the world greener and preserve a green natural environment and blue skies. The two sides agreed to continue working together to end the pandemic and protect people’s lives and safety. The two sides agreed to increase direct flights between the two countries to facilitate personnel exchanges. China supports the early returning of Mongolian students to China to resume their study. The two sides also agreed to strengthen youth exchanges and sub-national cooperation to consolidate people’s support for the China-Mongolia friendship. The two sides agreed to step up coordination in international and regional affairs, uphold true multilateralism and open regionalism, advance implementation of the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative, safeguard the common interests of developing countries, jointly promote development and prosperity in Asia, and build a community with a shared future for mankind.\nChina and Mongolia are good neighbors with ties more precious than gold, and good brothers and good partners sharing weal and woe. China stands ready to build on the momentum of the visit to work together with the Mongolian side to implement the important common understandings reached by the two heads of state, advance mutually-beneficial and friendly cooperation and better realize shared development and prosperity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347342.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220809_10738238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-09","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","First of all, Taiwan’s Joseph Wu said that China has used the visit by Nancy Pelosi as an excuse to practice “war invasions”. I’d like to ask the Foreign Ministry’s comment on Joseph Wu’s remarks. And also, I would like to ask that the Chinese military announced more drills around Taiwan again today. My questions would be how long will these extended drills last for? And the second point of that would be are…","The countermeasures taken by China in response to Pelosi’s provocative visit to Taiwan are justified, reasonable and lawful. They are aimed at sending a warning to the provocateurs and punishing the “Taiwan independence” forces.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the entire China. This is the real fact and status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities and the obdurate “Taiwan independence” elements have tried to mislead the public by misrepresenting events and facts, which again exposes their nature of seeking independence and separatism.\nI want to stress that to achieve the full reunification of China is the shared will of all Chinese and an unstoppable historical trend. Be it the “US card” or anything else that the DDP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces seek to play, they cannot save the “Taiwan independence” forces from failure. Their provocations and lies are futile and will only accelerate their own demise.\nRegarding the military drills you mentioned, I responded to similar questions yesterday. I would like to reiterate that China has conducted normal military drills in waters off its own territory, which are open, transparent and professional. Relevant authorities have issued notices in a timely manner. This move is in line with China’s domestic law, the international law and established international practices. This is both a warning we send to the provocateurs and a legitimate step to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity. As for your question on whether this will be a new normal, I’d like to refer you to the competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347342.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220809_10738238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-09","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Firstly, Taiwan is holding artillery drills today and on Thursday. Does China plan to have any additional countermeasures in response to this? The second question is, does China feel that the Iran nuclear talks in Vienna might lead to a breakthrough soon?","The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have been colluding with foreign forces to seek independence and make provocations. They refuse to recognize the one-China principle and attempt to change the status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. We want to make it clear to the Taiwan authorities that any attempt to go against the trend of history or to use military force to resist reunification is bound to be rejected by all Chinese people and become futile. Such attempts are doomed to fail.\nOn your second question, with the concerted efforts of parties, the negotiations on resuming compliance with the Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action (JCPOA) nuclear deal have resumed recently in Vienna. Although no breakthrough is achieved, parties have explicitly expressed their readiness to reach an agreement, which is of important significance for keeping the Iranian nuclear issue on the right track of dialogue and negotiations. China appreciates the EU’s effort to advance the talks and encourage it to continue diplomatic mediation efforts.\nAt this point, parties have reached consensus on the overwhelming majority of the arrangement concerning the resumption of compliance, and only a few issues are left to be ironed out. We call on the parties concerned to stay committed to the approach of dialogue and negotiation and step up diplomatic efforts to actively seek solutions to outstanding issues. The US, as the one who started the Iranian nuclear crisis, needs to get a clear sense of where things are headed, make the political decision sooner rather than later, respond positively to Iran’s reasonable concerns and enable the negotiations to produce results at an early date. All parties concerned should speak and act prudently and create a favorable atmosphere for the negotiations.\nChina will be actively involved in future negotiations and contribute to bringing the JCPOA back on track. We will at the same time resolutely uphold our own lawful rights and interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347342.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220809_10738238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-09","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said to the press on August 6 that the current situation is “not something that’s happened overnight or in a vacuum. What we’ve seen over the last few years is China engaging in increasingly destabilizing and potentially dangerous actions with regard to Taiwan, and this follows from that. And that’s why we say that the change to the status quo that’s prevailed with regard to…","What is the status quo across the Taiwan Strait? The answer is crystal-clear, i.e., both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China and Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been split. In other words, the one-China principle clearly defines the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. To violate and challenge this principle is to change the status quo.\nHere are the facts: the US has gone back on its commitments in the three Sino-US joint communiqués and going further down the path of fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China policy. The US clearly pledged in the Sino-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations that it will maintain unofficial relations with Taiwan. In recent years, however, the US greenlighted and connived at visits to Taiwan by senior officials including the House Speaker, who is considered a US leader. The US pledged in the August 17 Communiqué released in 1982 that “it intends gradually to reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution”. However, the US has actually kept increasing arms sales to Taiwan in both qualitative and quantitative terms, with the total volume to date exceeding US$70 billion, including over US$1.1 billion of arms sales conducted by the current US administration. The US also reiterated in the August 17 Communiqué that “it has no intention of pursuing a policy of ‘two Chinas’ or ‘one China, one Taiwan’.” However, it has been assisting Taiwan in expanding its so-called “international space” and even openly helped Taiwan consolidate its so-called “diplomatic relations”. In recent years, the US’s moves to fudge, hollow out and distort its one-China commitment have become even more blatant. It has inserted more preconditions and provisos into its one-China policy such as the “Taiwan Relations Act” and the “Six Assurances”, which were unilaterally concocted and have never been recognized and have been firmly opposed to by China from the very beginning. The US has also been colluding more with the Taiwan authorities and flexing muscles around the Taiwan Strait to bolster “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nAll these facts show that it is the US and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that are undermining the one-China principle and changing the status quo in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Anyone who renounces the one-China principle would be responsible for causing fierce storms in the Taiwan Strait. We Chinese people have the guts not to yield to bullying or intimidation, the resolve to unite as one and face any challenge together, and very importantly the ability to resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and dignity. We will continue to stand with the international community to resolutely uphold the one-China principle, defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, deter and push back any attempt to contain China by using the Taiwan question, and shatter the Taiwan authorities’ wishful thinking of seeking “Taiwan independence” through soliciting US support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347342.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220809_10738238.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Wu Chao-hsieh once again spouted nonsense, falsely claiming that the mainland has unreasonably “provoked” and is “militarily threatening” Taiwan to change the status quo, and calling on countries that love “democracy and freedom” to support Taiwan and maintain the status quo in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 9 dateline: Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 9th in response to a reporter's question that Wu Zhaoxie is a diehard “Taiwan independence” element. His remarks distort right and wrong and confuse the public, once again exposing his stubborn nature of seeking “independence.”\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed, and China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided. This is the law and reality of cross-Strait relations. Countless facts fully prove that the DPP authorities are the destroyers of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Since the DPP came to power, it has refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, and has openly spread fallacies of the “two-state theory” such as “Republic of China Taiwan” and “the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are not subordinate to each other.” If this is not an attempt to change the status quo, what is it?\nMa Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities seek to realize their political ambitions by selling out national interests and relying on external anti-China forces, especially “relying on the US to seek independence.” The farce of Pelosi's incursion into Taiwan fully shows that the DPP authorities are unmistakable provocateurs. The DPP authorities constantly incite confrontation and opposition between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, promote “Taiwan independence” activities, and collude with external forces to openly challenge national sovereignty and territorial integrity. This seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. If this is not provocation, what is?\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that under our series of firm and powerful countermeasures, the DPP authorities have shown no remorse. Instead, they openly distort facts, package themselves as “victims” and “lodge complaints with foreign powers,” fabricate a narrative of “authoritarianism” versus “democracy,” and cover up the essence and conduct of their scheme of independence and provocation. As is well known, the so-called “democracy” in the mouths of Western anti-China forces is merely a pretext for interfering in other countries' internal affairs, while the so-called “democracy” in the mouths of the DPP authorities is even more a “fig leaf” for inciting “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment and scheming for independence and provocation.\nMa Xiaoguang said that our struggle to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity has received broad support from the international community. The vast majority of countries in the world have a clear understanding of the one-China principle, a just judgment of right and wrong, and full vigilance against the harm of the DPP authorities' independence scheme. The DPP authorities' sophistry cannot deceive Taiwan's people or the international community.\nMa Xiaoguang said that we warn the DPP authorities: if they do not mend their ways on the evil path of relying on foreign powers to assert themselves and provoke through independence, they will surely face even harsher blows.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220809_12459702.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-10","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Recently, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken and Special Presidential Envoy for Climate John Kerry both said that China’s decision to suspend bilateral climate talks with the US doesn’t punish the US — it punishes the world. What’s China’s comment?","We have taken note of the relevant remarks of the US side. I would like to stress the following points:\nFirst, the measure taken by the Chinese side is part of our legitimate and reasonable countermeasures against Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan. For quite some time, we have repeatedly stressed to the US side that the one-China principle is the political foundation on which China develops bilateral relations with other countries. In disregard of China’s strong opposition, Speaker Pelosi went ahead with the provocative visit to China’s Taiwan region, which seriously violated China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. This visit took place with the US government’s connivance and support. The visit has undermined the political foundation of the China-US relations and will inevitably cause major disruption to the exchanges and cooperation between the two sides. China had made those points perfectly clear long beforehand. We said it and we mean it. The US has no reason to feel surprised.\nSecond, due to the egregious impact of Pelosi’s visit to China’s Taiwan region, China has suspended its climate talks with the US. All consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US. As a responsible major country, China will continue to actively participate in international and multilateral cooperation on climate change. China is a country committed to real action on global climate governance. We have made a solemn pledge to strive to peak carbon dioxide emissions before 2030 and achieve carbon neutrality before 2060. We are endeavoring to formulate and implement a “1+N” policy framework for low-carbon development and green transition. China will staunchly pursue its carbon peak and carbon neutrality targets, actively participate in main-channel negotiations on climate change, provide other developing countries with support and help as our ability permits, and make our own contributions to tackling the global climate challenge.\nThird, the US side should earnestly shoulder its historical responsibilities and obligations on climate change. It is our consistent belief that to address climate change, it is not enough to just chant slogans without doing one’s part. Not long ago, the US Supreme Court decided that it would limit the US Environmental Protection Agency’s powers to curb greenhouse gas emissions. Besides, the US has been sanctioning and suppressing China’s solar companies citing the so-called Xinjiang-related issues as a pretext, which has dealt a direct blow to the atmosphere of our cooperation and the climate response of China and other countries. These self-contradictory moves make the world question the US’s capability and seriousness on addressing climate change. The US should earnestly deliver on its historical responsibilities and due obligations on climate change and stop looking around for excuses for its inaction.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347343.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220810_10739931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-10","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","About China’s military drills around the island of Taiwan, are they ongoing or have they already ended?","As we have made clear, China’s military drills in the waters surrounding our own territory are justified, legitimate and lawful. They are a warning to the provocateurs, and a punishment for the “Taiwan independence” forces. I would refer you to the Chinese military for the specific question you raised.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347343.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220810_10739931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-10","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","According to reports, US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi questioned in an interview why her trip to Taiwan has received so much attention, while the visit of a group of US lawmakers to Taiwan several months earlier had no impact. She also said, “We cannot allow the Chinese government to isolate Taiwan”. What’s China’s comment?","We have always opposed visits to Taiwan by members of the US Congress. Nancy Pelosi is the third highest-ranking political figure in the US. She travelled to Taiwan on a US military aircraft. While she was there, she repeatedly mentioned herself being there on behalf of the US and described the trip as an official visit. The DPP authorities touted the visit as a major breakthrough in Taiwan-US relations. All these show that Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan is a major political provocation that upgrades US-Taiwan exchanges. This goes against the US’s commitment of only maintaining unofficial relations with Taiwan in the Sino-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations. This goes against the one-China principle, which is widely accepted by the international community and has been affirmed by UNGA Resolution 2758. This goes against the principle in international law of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, which is enshrined in the UN Charter.\nSince four months ago, China has time and again made clear to the US through multiple channels and at various levels our stern position of firmly opposing Pelosi’s visit to the Taiwan region. However, the US has chosen to pursue the wrong course of action in disregard of China’s dissuasion and warnings. It is the US that has gone back on its commitment, not China. It is the US that has infringed on China’s sovereignty, not the other way round. It is the US that connives at and supports “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, instead of China conniving at and supporting separatist activities in the US. The US made the provocation first, and China has been compelled to take legitimate countermeasures, which are justified, lawful, necessary and proportionate.\nThe US has been going further down the path of fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China principle, and yet it accused China of changing the status quo. The US conducts up to one hundred military drills in waters around China on an annual basis, and yet it accused China of overreacting. This is gangster logic. China does not accept it, nor will the international community recognize it.\nChina will not hesitate to fight back each time the US makes a serious provocation that violates China’s sovereignty and interferes in China’s internal affairs. We will never allow our sovereignty and territorial integrity to be trampled and sabotaged.\nIf the US truly hopes to adhere to international law and uphold all countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity as it claims to, it should play no games but return to the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiqués. The US must not act recklessly, and stop going further down on the doomed path. The US should give up the attempt to use Taiwan to contain China and do right things and take concrete steps to facilitate peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347343.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220810_10739931.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-08-10","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据台媒报道，美国会众议院议长佩洛西访台后，解放军在台湾岛附近海空域组织“锁台”式高强度实弹演训，数枚导弹飞越台岛，这可能只是个开端，台湾被压缩的战略空间回不去了。请问对此有何评论？","In response to rumors related to the military that have circulated on certain internet platforms, Wu Qian, Senior Colonel and spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense, responded at the regular press conference on the 25th: “Military affairs are a matter of vital importance to the state.” The internet is not a lawless zone. Certain internet platforms that fabricate military-related rumors to “ride the wave of popularity,” make “baseless associations,” and engage in “reckless interpretations” are extremely irresponsible and also illegal.\nA reporter asked: For some time, public opinion related to cross-Strait issues has been very heated. We have noted that a text message about retired veterans being “recalled to fight” has circulated on certain internet platforms, and authoritative military media have debunked it. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?\nWu Qian said that after the above rumor appeared, relevant military media debunked it immediately. He further emphasized two points: First, wise people stop rumors. We hope everyone will not believe or spread rumors and will obtain military information through formal channels. Second, “Military affairs are a matter of vital importance to the state.” The internet is not a lawless zone. Certain internet platforms that fabricate such military-related rumors to “ride the wave of popularity,” make “baseless associations,” and engage in “reckless interpretations” are extremely irresponsible and also illegal.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16193223.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-08-10","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 10: In response to the DPP authorities’ attempts to obstruct and smear the visit of Chinese Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Liyan and his delegation, Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 10th in response to a question: It is entirely normal for Chinese Kuomintang figures to visit and exchange views on the mainland, and it is absurd to maliciously hype it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220810_12460159.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-11","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Agnė Vaiciukevičiūtė, Deputy Minister of Transport and Communications of Lithuania, led a delegation to Taiwan on August 7 for a five-day visit. Do you have any comment?","We strongly condemn the act of Lithuania’s anti-China forces to deliberately infringe on China’s sovereignty and grossly interfere in China’s domestic affairs. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and the political foundation on which China develops bilateral relations with all other countries including Lithuania. The Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the People’s Republic of China and the Republic of Lithuania clearly stipulates that the Government of the Republic of Lithuania recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China and Taiwan as an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Government of the Republic of Lithuania undertakes the obligation not to establish official relations or engage in official contacts with Taiwan. However, Lithuania has time and again reneged on its commitment and apparently been acting in bad faith.\nChina will act resolutely in response to the egregious provocation of certain individuals in Lithuania to challenge the one-China principle and undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge certain people in Lithuania to stop being the pawn of the “Taiwan independence” and anti-China forces and stop moving even further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347344.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220811_10741518.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-11","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the State Council Information Office published a white paper titled “The Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era” yesterday morning. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on it?","Yesterday morning, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the State Council Information Office jointly published a white paper titled “The Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era”. The white paper systematically outlined in detail the position and policies of the CPC and the Chinese government of realizing national reunification in the new era, and fully demonstrates the firm resolve of the CPC and the Chinese people and their commitment to national reunification. We believe the white paper will help people from various walks of life in and outside China to fully and accurately understand the Chinese government’s position on the Taiwan question. Here I would like to stress a few points.\nFirst, Taiwan is part of China - this is an indisputable fact. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times. In 1895, Japan forced the Qing government to cede Taiwan after Japan’s war of aggression against China. In 1943, the Cairo Declaration clearly stipulated that all the territories Japan had stolen from China, including Taiwan, should be restored to China. The Potsdam Proclamation of 1945 reiterated that “The terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” On October 25, 1945, the Chinese government announced that it was resuming the exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan and China had recovered Taiwan de jure and de facto. In 1949, the People’s Republic of China (PRC) was founded, becoming the successor to the Republic of China, and the Central People’s Government became the sole legal government of the whole of China. The new government replaced the previous KMT regime in a situation where China, as a subject of international law, did not change and China’s sovereignty and territory did not change. The two sides of the Taiwan Strait have fallen into a state of protracted political confrontation. But the sovereignty and territory of China have never been divided and will never be divided, and Taiwan's status as part of China’s territory has never changed and will never be allowed to change. This effectively refutes the false argument that the status of Taiwan has yet to be determined, and makes a powerful case against various kinds of wrong perceptions of history and lies that seek to justify “Taiwan independence”.\nSecond, the CPC and the Chinese government have always been committed to realizing complete national reunification. Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing complete national reunification is the shared aspiration of all the Chinese people and a commitment and a historical mission of the CPC. Peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems are our fundamental guidelines for resolving the Taiwan question. National reunification by peaceful means is the first choice of the CPC and the Chinese government in resolving the Taiwan question, as it best serves the interests of the Chinese nation as a whole, including our compatriots in Taiwan. We are ready to create vast space for peaceful reunification; but we will leave no room for separatist activities in any form. We will work with the greatest sincerity and exert our utmost efforts to achieve peaceful reunification. If separatist elements or external forces make provocation or even cross our red lines, we will be forced to take resolute measures. This clearly answers the question in the international community about what China’s fundamental guidelines are on the Taiwan question, and shatters the wishful thinking of “Taiwan independence” forces and foreign interfering forces to split China.\nThird, the one-China principle brooks no distortion or challenge. The connotation of the one-China principle is crystal-clear, i.e. there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The Government of the PRC is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and widely accepted basic norm in international relations. It is affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758. It is the political foundation for interactions between China and all countries in the world. To date, 181 countries have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. This fully shows that standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. In response to US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s recent visit to the Taiwan region, more than 170 countries and many international organizations have reiterated their one-China commitment. The international community has once again spoken out for justice.\nFourth, China’s complete reunification is a process that cannot be halted. National reunification is an essential step towards national rejuvenation. Peaceful cross-Strait reunification is of benefit not only to the Chinese nation, but to all peoples and the international community as a whole. We call on the international community to have a right understanding of the Taiwan question, support China’s reunification, enhance commitment to the one-China principle and unequivocally reject “Taiwan independence”. The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have been attempting to solicit US’s support to seek independence and some forces in the US have been seeking to use the Taiwan question to contain China. This is a very dangerous move that is comparable to playing with fire. And those playing with fire will perish by it. We urge relevant countries to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop double dealing, and take real actions to honor their commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”. Seeking independence with foreign support will go nowhere, and using the Taiwan question to contain China is doomed to fail. Any individual or force attempting to interfere in China’s internal affairs and obstruct China’s reunification will find themselves on a collision course with a great wall of steel forged by over 1.4 billion Chinese people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347344.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220811_10741518.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-11","Wang Wenbin","AFP","I have a follow-up question on the Taiwan white paper. Taiwan authorities said today in response to the white paper that China is simply trying to create a new normal to intimidate the Taiwanese people. In addition to this, the Taiwan military also held another live-fire drill today. What’s your response to both of these actions?","Tsai Ing-wen and the DPP authorities have confounded black and white in an attempt to mislead the public. This once again exposes their separatist nature and real agenda of seeking “independence”. I would like to stress that realizing complete national reunification is the shared aspiration of all the Chinese people and an unstoppable historical trend. We are ready to create vast space for peaceful reunification; but we will leave no room for separatist activities of any form.\nWe would like to make it clear to the DPP authorities that colluding with external forces to make provocations and seek independence will only accelerate their own demise and push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster. Their “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda will get nowhere. Betraying the interests of one’s country and nation will surely result in utter failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347344.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220811_10741518.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-11","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","About the comments made recently by the US commerce chief Gina Raimondo. In an interview with Bloomberg TV, Ms. Raimondo said that President Biden is very cautious about actions he will take on the Trump-era tariffs on Chinese imports. She added that he was weighing his options and mentioned that this was happening in an environment that has been complicated in the wake of the visit by Nancy Pelosi to Taiwan.…","As we have repeatedly pointed out, there is no winner in a trade war. The US’s unilateral imposition of additional tariffs does not serve the interests of the US, China or the world. To remove all additional tariffs imposed on China as soon as possible is good for the US, China and the world.\nThe context and the events that led to the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait are crystal-clear. The US is the unprovoked provocateur and creator of the crisis. The US needs to be fully aware of the egregious nature of Pelosi’s visit to the Taiwan region, earnestly reflect on the serious consequences of the visit, and immediately rectify its mistake. The US should not expect China to trade away its core interests. The US should play no games but return to the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347344.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220811_10741518.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-11","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","British Foreign Secretary Liz Truss said on August 10 that, “The UK and partners have condemned in the strongest terms China’s escalation in the region around Taiwan, as seen through our recent G7 statement.\" Behaviour and rhetoric from Beijing threaten peace and stability in the region. The United Kingdom urges China to resolve any differences by peaceful means, without the threat or use of force or coercion.”…","The UK has mischaracterized the facts and made irresponsible remarks on China’s justified, necessary and lawful move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. China deplores and is firmly against this, and has lodged solemn démarches with the UK side.\nEverything happens for a reason. The US is the one who made the provocation first and started the crisis. The DPP authorities have been seeking “Taiwan independence” through soliciting US support. It is only legitimate, lawful and justified for China to uphold its territorial integrity and oppose secession. The UK turned a blind eye to the US’s provocation and violation while groundlessly criticizing the countermeasures China has taken for the sake of defending justice. This is typical double standard. It fully exposes the UK’s hypocrisy stemming from its imperialist past. If the UK truly cares about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should condemn the US and the “Taiwan independence” forces and stop them from being provocative and playing with fire. If Scotland were to collude with external forces and split itself from the UK, would the UK remain calm, show restraint, sit by and watch the situation deteriorate?\nEvery issue has its own merits. Justice must prevail and be upheld. If facts and truth mean nothing to the UK, in what way could it possibly think it deserves a “Global Britain”? The UK follows the US’s lead and does the US’s bidding along with a handful of other countries. The UK’s reputation as an independent country has long gone bankrupt, and its so-called “diplomatic ambition” is based on empty premises. More than 170 countries and many international organizations have openly voiced support for the justified measures China has taken to uphold its rights. Their voice has drowned out the noise of the joint statement by the UK and other G7 members.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. The reunification of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait is a historical trend that will surely be realized in the course of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. No force can stand in the way of the reunification of China. Any words and deeds endorsing the “Taiwan independence” forces are doomed to be swept into the dustbin of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347344.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220811_10741518.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 11 — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 11th, in answering reporters' questions, that as the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has entered an irreversible historical process, and the cause of national reunification is at a new historical juncture in the new era, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the State Council Information…","Ma Xiaoguang pointed out that Taiwan is the Taiwan of all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan's future is tied to national reunification and can and must be decided jointly by all Chinese people. National reunification is the trend of history and will not be shifted by the will of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. The DPP authorities, under the pretext of \"democracy,\" practice \"green terror,\" and seek \"independence\" while rejecting reunification. This runs counter to historical trends and the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and is \"self-deception\" that cannot represent or coerce the public opinion of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nHe said that in firmly upholding the one-China principle, combating \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and interference by external forces, promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, we have always worked for the well-being of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and have always been committed to realizing the aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for a better life. \"Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems\" reflects our cherishing and safeguarding of the great righteousness of the nation, the well-being of compatriots, and peace across the Strait. It fully takes into account the differences in social systems and ideologies between the mainland and Taiwan, and we are willing to continue uniting Taiwan compatriots, actively explore the Taiwan plan of \"two systems,\" and enrich the practice of peaceful reunification. The DPP authorities' attempts to distort, smear, and spread rumors cannot deny that \"one country, two systems\" is a peaceful, democratic, well-intentioned, and win-win plan. We believe that, over time, \"one country, two systems\" will be re-recognized, understood, and accepted by the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. In the process of compatriots on both sides of the Strait working together to achieve peaceful reunification, the scope and substance of the Taiwan plan of \"two systems\" will be fully demonstrated.\nMa Xiaoguang stressed that the key factor determining the direction of cross-Strait relations and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the development and progress of the mainland. The DPP authorities' reckless actions are merely a mantis trying to stop a chariot, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220811_12460412.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-12","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","According to reports, protests occurred in places including Hargeisa, the capital of the Somaliland region in northern Somalia on August 11. The protesters were calling for elections for the region’s leadership to be held as scheduled. Clashes with security forces led to the death of several protesters. What’s China’s comment?","Somaliland is an inalienable part of Somalia. What happens in Somaliland is Somalia’s internal affairs. China always follows the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs. We firmly support the Federal Government of Somalia’s efforts to safeguard national unity, security and stability. Continued stability and tranquility in Somaliland serves the interests of all the people of Somalia. At the same time, we ask the authorities of Somaliland to earnestly protect the safety and property of Chinese enterprises and nationals there.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347345.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220812_10742450.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-12","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi said at a recent press conference with the Congressional delegation to Asia that Taiwan is one of the freest “countries” in the world and their visit is to salute this democracy. She also noted that the visit signals no departure from the US government’s one-China policy and they are not trying to upset the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. What’s your comment?","Pelosi’s remarks are further proof that her visit to China’s Taiwan region shows connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. She openly referred to Taiwan as a “country”. This is a serious political provocation that violates the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiqués. The DPP authorities have redoubled efforts within the island to remove the Chinese identity of Taiwan and push for “incremental independence”, and sought every means to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” in the international arena. Against such a background, Pelosi chose to visit Taiwan and claimed in a high-profile fashion that she was there on behalf of the US. The visit was clearly official in nature and aimed to provoke cross-Strait confrontation and interfere in China’s internal affairs. This is an extremely egregious move. To defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity, to uphold the basic norm in international relations of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, and to truly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, China has every right to take resolute countermeasures in response to the US’s provocations. Such measures are absolutely necessary under those circumstances.\nPelosi will achieve nothing by using democracy as a pretext for her visit. Her visit has nothing to do with democracy. It was a political stunt that went against the will of the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our compatriots in Taiwan, and challenged the one-China principle widely accepted by the international community. Her visit tramples on democracy and shows how the US puts its selfish interests above international justice. If Pelosi truly cares about democracy and human rights, she should visit Afghanistan, Iraq, Syria and Libya instead, where she could express repentance over the hundreds of thousands of innocent civilians killed by the US military and vow to prevent such atrocities caused by US violation of UN Charter and norms in international relations from happening again.\nChina will stand together with friends in all countries who love peace and uphold principles to firmly oppose anything said or done that interferes in other countries’ domestic affairs, firmly resist all reckless moves that undermine regional peace, jointly defend the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, and safeguard regional stability and world peace.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347345.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220812_10742450.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-12","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Rahul Gupta, Director of National Drug Control Policy at the White House, tweeted on China’s countermeasures in response to Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan that “it’s unacceptable” that China is suspending counternarcotics cooperation with the US “in light of an overdose epidemic ... that has claimed more than 100,000 lives in America last year”. What’s your comment?","In disregard of China’s stern warnings and repeated representations, Nancy Pelosi visited China’s Taiwan region. This has dealt a heavy blow to the political foundation of China-US relations. The Chinese side announced eight countermeasures including suspending China-US counternarcotics cooperation. This is a firm and strong response to the US and “Taiwan independence” separatists’ provocation. It is completely justified, appropriate and proportionate. On the fentanyl abuse issue in the US, I would like to stress the following:\nFirst, the root cause of the fentanyl abuse crisis in the US lies in the US itself. The international community, China included, has been strengthening control of fentanyl-related substances, while in the US, abuse of synthetic opioids including fentanyl has been deteriorating. There have been more deaths from overdose. The US should seriously reflect on the underlying reason. According to data from the International Narcotics Control Board, the US is the world’s largest producer and consumer of fentanyl-related substances. With five percent of the world’s population, the US consumes 80 percent of opioids in the world. The US government has lost effective control over the management of prescription drugs. There aren’t enough public awareness campaigns about the harm of narcotics, and measures to reduce demand and ban narcotics have not worked well. The US must look squarely at its own problem instead of deflecting blame.\nSecond, China has made tremendous efforts to help the US solve its fentanyl issue. There is no immediate hazard or large-scale fentanyl abuse in China. China has always acted in a humanitarian and responsible way in helping the US solve the fentanyl abuse crisis and working with other countries to address new challenges in counternarcotics. The UN Conventions on drug control scheduled 27 categories of fentanyl substances. China was the first in the world to have scheduled fentanyl as a class, covering more categories than what are scheduled by the UN Conventions. In contrast, while the US has the most acute fentanyl challenge in the world, it has yet to officially schedule fentanyl-related substances as a class. China has shown utmost goodwill and sincerity and gone out of our way to work together with the US in this area, which is unprecedented in our drug control practice. This has not only played an important role in preventing the illicit manufacturing, trafficking and abuse of fentanyl-related substances, but also set a fine example for international counternarcotics cooperation and has been fully recognized by the international community.\nThird, the responsibility for undermining China-US counternarcotics cooperation is entirely on the US. It has been over two years since the US put the Institution of Forensic Science of the Ministry of Public Security and the National Narcotics Laboratory of China, which are responsible for testing and controlling fentanyl-related substances, on the US’s “entity list” in the name of so-called human rights issues in Xinjiang. They still have not been removed from the list. The US has been publicly making irresponsible remarks and repeatedly rehashing old cases. The US has sanctioned Chinese companies in the name of controlling fentanyl-related substances and offered high reward for the arrest of certain Chinese citizens. The US has done this to mislead the public, deflect the blame, and shift away the responsibility for the botched response to narcotics abuse in the US. China has made démarches with the US side over this multiple times, but has received no response. All the consequences arising therefrom, including the damage caused to bilateral relations and China-US counternarcotics cooperation must be borne by the US side.\nChina takes a firm stance on counternarcotics. China has achieved notable results in counternarcotics governance despite the global spread of narcotics. As a responsible major country, China will as always actively participate in international and multilateral counternarcotics cooperation and contribute China’s expertise and effort to global counternarcotics efforts. We also sincerely hope that the US can find an effective solution to the fentanyl abuse in the country at an early date so that the American people can rid themselves of the scourge of narcotics sooner rather than later.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347345.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220812_10742450.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-14","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Recently, the New Party held a celebration marking its 29th founding anniversary. What is your comment on this?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 14 dispatch — Spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answering reporters' questions on the 14th, said: In the 29 years since its founding, the New Party has unequivocally advocated peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait, firmly upheld one China, and resolutely opposed 'Taiwan independence,' making positive contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. We believe the New Party will certainly continue to play an important role in future cross-strait relations. We are willing, on the basis of the one-China principle, to continue working together with enlightened people from all walks of life on the island, including the New Party, to jointly create the historic cause of national reunification and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220814_12461112.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-15","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Today marks the 77th anniversary of Japan’s defeat in World War II. August 15 also marks a special day in China-Japan relations. Also today, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida sent a ritual offering to the Yasukuni Shrine. Certain member of Japan’s Cabinet also visited this place the other day. Do you have any comment on this?","The Yasukuni Shrine, where World War II Class-A war criminals are honored, is a spiritual tool and symbol of the wars of aggression launched by Japanese militarists. The negative move of Japanese political leaders on the issue of the Yasukuni Shrine once again shows the Japanese side’s erroneous attitude toward historical issues. The Chinese side has lodged solemn démarches to the Japanese side.\nToday marks the 77th anniversary of Japan’s defeat and unconditional surrender. Seventy-seven years ago, the Chinese people, together with the people of the world, defeated the Japanese militarist aggressors and fascism. It was a decisive battle between justice and evil, between light and darkness, and between progress and reaction. This great victory will forever be remembered in the history of the Chinese nation and the pursuit of justice for all humanity.\nFacing up to and deeply reflecting on history is an essential prerequisite for Japan to restore and develop normal relations with its Asian neighbors after World War II. For quite some time, some Japanese politicians have kept using various means to distort and glorify its history of aggression and openly acted against important legal instruments including the Cairo Declaration of 1943, which clearly stipulates that Taiwan shall be restored to China. This constitutes serious defiance to the outcomes of the victory of the World Anti-fascist War and the post-war international order. This is unacceptable to anyone who loves peace and stands for justice. Those who try to turn back the wheel of history are bound to find themselves on the wrong path again. Only by sticking to the path of peaceful development can Japan find the right direction. We urge the Japanese side to draw lessons from history, make a clean break with militarism and avoid further losing the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347346.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220815_10743513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-15","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Does the Chinese foreign ministry have any comment on the visit to Taiwan by the US lawmakers group led by US Senator Ed Markey that arrived in Taipei on Sunday?","The delegation led by US Senator Ed Markey, in disregard of China’s serious démarches and firm opposition, insisted on visiting the Taiwan region of China. It is a blatant violation of the one-China principle and the stipulations of three Sino-US joint communiqués. It also infringes on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community and a basic norm in international relations. It is also the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic ties between China and the US. China’s national reunification is an unstoppable historical trend and the formidable common will of the Chinese people.\nChina once again urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues and stop fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China principle to prevent further damaging China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China will take resolute and strong measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Associating themselves with the separatists in Taiwan and attempting to challenge the one-China principle is a misjudgment and will get these small number of US politicians nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347346.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220815_10743513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-08-15","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q) [per digest]","","Senior Colonel Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, said at the regular press conference on the 25th that the root cause of the collision incident involving the U.S. nuclear-powered submarine “Connecticut” lies in the large-scale, high-frequency close-in reconnaissance, interference and provocation, and displays of military strength and other military activities that U.S. warships have carried out in the Asia-Pacific region, and in the United States' large-scale militarization of the South China Sea and its hegemony over navigation. China demands that the United States immediately stop such activities and not persist even after hitting a wall.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the U.S. military has taken accountability measures over the collision incident involving the nuclear-powered submarine “Connecticut” and has removed the submarine's commander, executive officer, and others from their posts. What is China's comment on this?\nWu Qian said that since the incident occurred, the U.S. side's evasive and secretive attitude cannot but cause the international community to harbor doubts. Three questions about this incident must be made clear: first, what exactly was the U.S. submarine's navigational intent; second, where exactly did the incident take place; and third, was there any nuclear leakage or marine environmental pollution at all?\nChina believes that the root cause of this incident lies in the large-scale, high-frequency close-in reconnaissance, interference and provocation, and displays of military strength and other military activities that U.S. warships have carried out in the Asia-Pacific region, and in the United States' large-scale militarization of the South China Sea and its hegemony over navigation. China demands that the United States immediately stop such activities and not persist even after hitting a wall.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/08-15/9827592.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-08-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","US Senator Markey recently made an unwelcome visit to Taiwan, China. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in response to a question.","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 15 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 15th when answering reporters' questions that the visit to Taiwan's region by certain US politicians and members of Congress is yet another example of violating the solemn commitments the US side has made on the Taiwan question and deliberately undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. This erroneous act seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose it.\nMa Xiaoguang said that certain people in the United States have failed to learn the lesson from the grave consequences of Pelosi's visit to Taiwan, and the DPP authorities have repeatedly colluded with external anti-China forces to engage in provocations aimed at \"independence.\" This fully exposes the sinister intentions of the US in \"using Taiwan to contain China\" and of the DPP authorities in \"relying on the United States to seek independence.\"\nMa Xiaoguang said that our struggle to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity enjoys broad support from the international community. We warn the DPP authorities that if they do not rein in their behavior on the path of relying on foreign powers for self-protection and provoking \"independence,\" they will surely face harsher blows.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220815_12462459.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-16","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","An official from Taiwan’s air force said on Monday that a video released by China’s Eastern Theater Command manipulated footage to make it seem like Chinese military planes were close to the area around Penghu Islands. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","I would like to refer you to the Ministry of National Defense for your specific question. Let me just say that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces can certainly feel the Chinese side’s resolute measures to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347347.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220816_10744204.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-16","Wang Wenbin","People’s Daily","According to reports, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi had a virtual meeting on August 15 with Geneva-based envoys from developing countries in Asia and Africa who are visiting China. Can you share more with us?","Upon China’s invitation, the delegation of Geneva-based envoys from Asian and African developing countries including Sierra Leone, Lesotho, Eritrea, Côte d’Ivoire, Zimbabwe, Iraq, The Gambia, Somalia, Cameroon and the Laos arrived in China recently and will visit Guangdong and Xinjiang. Yesterday, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi had a virtual meeting with these envoys.\nState Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang recalled President Xi Jinping’s visit to the UN Office at Geneva in 2017 and his historic speech there, in which the president fully outlined the objectives and the substance of building a community with a shared future for mankind, and pointed the way forward for common efforts to achieve progress of human civilization and world peace and development. China will uphold the vision of a community with a shared future for mankind, and work in solidarity and coordination with fellow developing countries for common development and shared prosperity.\nWang Yi shared the achievements of human rights development in China. He said that on the basis of equality and mutual respect, China is ready to stay open-minded and conduct exchange and cooperation on human rights for mutual learning and common progress. Wang Yi put forward four suggestions on strengthening global human rights governance and improving the work of multilateral human rights institutions. First, countries need to uphold mutual respect and oppose imposition of one’s own will onto others. Given countries’ different national conditions, histories and cultures, it is important that all countries are allowed to explore their own paths for human rights development that best serve the interest of their respective peoples based on their unique national conditions. No country should force its own will or standards on others. Second, countries need to advance human rights development in a systemic way rather than selectively. For the people in developing countries, ensuring their right to subsistence and development is what matters most. Multilateral human rights institutions need to take the legitimate concerns of developing countries seriously, and channel more attention and input to their economic, social and cultural rights and right to development. Third, countries need to stand for openness and inclusiveness, and against interference in others’ internal affairs. The claim that “human rights is above sovereignty” is nothing but a false pretext for interfering in others’ internal affairs. The idea of so-called values-based diplomacy is nothing but a cover for forcing other countries to pick a side in the name of human rights. Forced democratic transformation has achieved nothing but turmoil, conflict and humanitarian disaster. Multilateral human rights institutions are supposed to be platforms for constructive exchange and cooperation, not a battlefield for fierce political confrontation. Fourth, countries need to uphold fairness and justice and oppose double standards. Some Western countries see themselves as the judge on human rights, criticizing others while being oblivious to the human rights problems of themselves and their allies, like holding a “flashlight” only to check out on the behavior of others and not themselves. Countries need to jointly say no to such double standards and to such selective oblivion.\nDuring the virtual meeting, State Councilor Wang Yi mentioned the historical ins and outs of the Taiwan question and China’s stern position. He stressed that each time the US made a blatant provocation, it was met with a necessary and legitimate response from China. This is China exercising its legitimate right to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguarding the principle of non-interference in each other’s internal affairs, which is both the golden rule in state-to-state interactions and what underpins the survival of any developing country.\nThe envoys from Asian and African developing countries said that the one-China principle reaffirmed by UNGA Resolution 2758 is an international consensus and a political foundation for countries to develop bilateral ties with China. Taiwan and Xinjiang are part of China. China’s internal affairs brook no interference, and human rights issues should not be politicized. The legitimate measures China has taken should be firmly supported by the international community. The envoys fully recognized China’s achievement and the leading role China has played, and said they look forward to broad communication with Chinese departments. They are ready to continue to advance friendly relations with China, strengthen multilateral coordination and improve humanity’s wellbeing.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347347.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220816_10744204.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-17","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","Japanese media speculated that in the upcoming dialogue, Japan will raise the Taiwan question and exchange views with China on building a constructive and stable China-Japan relationship. What is China’s comment?","Like I just said, there is a high-level political dialogue mechanism between China and Japan, and I have no further information to offer at this moment. I want to stress that Taiwan is part of China’s territory, the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and no foreign country has the right to interfere in it. Japan should abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan, truly act upon its statement of valuing China-Japan relations and work constructively to improve and grow bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347348.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220817_10744880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-17","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","On August 16, Russian President Putin said in his address to 10th Moscow Conference on International Security that Pelosi’s “escapade towards Taiwan is not just a voyage by an irresponsible politician”, but “a thoroughly planned provocation”. It is part of the “deliberate US strategy designed to destabilize the situation and sow chaos in the region and the world. It is a brazen demonstration of disrespect for…","China highly appreciates the remarks by President Putin. Since US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi visited Taiwan, more than 170 countries have spoken up for justice. They reiterated their one-China commitment and support for China’s efforts to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The latest remarks by President Putin demonstrate the high-level strategic coordination between China and Russia, and the firm support the two countries have rendered each other on issues concerning their respective core interests. China is ready to continue to work with the international community to jointly defend the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and safeguard regional and international peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347348.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220817_10744880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-17","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","White House National Security Council Indo-Pacific Coordinator Kurt Campbell said during a press call that “China has overreacted” to Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan and used it to try to change the status quo, and the goal is to intimidate and coerce Taiwan. He said that the US will continue to “support Taiwan in line with our longstanding policy”, and that includes conducting standard air and maritime transits through…","What the senior US official said is sheer misrepresentation of facts and distortion of principles. It is clear that the US is trying to defend the indefensible by applying a gangster logic and acting like a bully. I would like to make the following clear:\nFirst, this incident is single-handedly orchestrated and provoked by the US, and the context, cause and course of events are crystal-clear. The US made an unwarranted provocation first, and China has been compelled to act in defense of its own rights. With the connivance and arrangement of the US government, Pelosi went on a high-profile visit to China’s Taiwan region. This reckless move seriously undermined China’s sovereignty, interfered in China’s internal affairs and jeopardized peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese side absolutely needed to make a firm response. China’s position is justified, reasonable and lawful; our measures are firm, strong and proportionate. They are aimed at sending a warning to the perpetrator and punishing the “Taiwan independence” forces. More than 170 countries have voiced their commitment to the one-China principle and opposition to the US’s provocation, including 20 heads of state, seven deputy or vice heads of state, nine heads of government, about 60 foreign ministers and ten-plus international organizations such as the UN. They form an overwhelming majority. If China did not firmly resist the US’s recklessness, irresponsibility and extreme irrationality, then the principle of respecting sovereignty and territorial integrity in international relations would just become words on paper, separatists and extremists would only become more reckless and the hard-won peace and stability in this region would be seriously undermined.\nSecond, it is the US, not China, that has undermined cross-Strait peace and stability. Taiwan is not and never was a sovereign country. There is only one China and both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. This has been the status quo of Taiwan since ancient times. The Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the United States of America and the People’s Republic of China released in 1978 clearly stresses that the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal Government of China and Taiwan is part of China. This is the status quo across the Taiwan Strait that has been there for decades. But this status quo has now been sabotaged, not by China, but the US and the separatist forces in Taiwan. In 2000, the US unilaterally adopted the so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and put it before the three China-US joint communiqués in its policy statement. In recent years, the US has openly inserted the secretly formulated “Six Assurances” into its characterization of the one-China policy. After it took power, the DPP authorities have advanced “incremental independence” and gone all out to remove the Chinese identity of Taiwan, and tried to create the false impression of “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” at various occasions. It is those actions of the US that are truly changing the status quo.\nThird, the Taiwan Relations Act and the Six Assurances run counter to the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués and the basic norms governing international relations. China has been firmly against that from the very beginning. The US has been changing the status quo, encroaching on China’s core interests, going further down the path of fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China principle, and trying to cross China’s red lines and pushing the boundaries. But the attempt to contain China with the Taiwan question is pure wishful thinking. The stunt orchestrated by Pelosi will not in any way change the prevailing international consensus on the one-China principle, nor can they change the irreversible historical trend of Taiwan’s return to the motherland, still less halt the historical process of national rejuvenation. We the Chinese people have the guts not to yield to bullying or intimidation, and we are firm in defending our country’s core interests. The US should heed China’s serious warning: the US must not act recklessly or create bigger crises. Those who play with fire will not come to a good end. Those who provoke China will surely be punished.\nFourth, China had repeatedly warned the US that the Pelosi visit would create a crisis and would seriously obstruct and sabotage bilateral exchange and cooperation. The US, however, turned a deaf ear to this and went ahead with the wrong move. Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan seriously undermined China’s core interests, and China has every reason to respond resolutely. All the consequences arising therefrom shall be borne by the US. China had made those points perfectly clear long beforehand. We said it and we mean it. The US has no reason to feel surprised.\nDue to the egregious impact of Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, China had to suspend bilateral climate talks with the US. Let me be clear, the US does not represent the entire world. China will remain actively involved in international and multilateral cooperation on climate change, continue to work hard to meet its carbon peak and carbon neutrality targets, actively participate in main-channel negotiations on climate change, provide other developing countries with support and help as our ability permits, and make our own contributions to tackling the global climate challenge. For the US, instead of making unwarranted criticisms or viciously smearing other countries, what it needs to do is to take its responsibilities seriously and honor its own commitments. It must stop confounding right with wrong and deflecting attention.\nChina once again urges the US to abide by the basic norms in international relations including respecting other countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity, and non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, return to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop undermining China’s core interests and create necessary conditions for China-US cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347348.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220817_10744880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-17","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","Today 40 years ago, the August 17 Communiqué between China and the US was published. How can this history inspire current China-US relations?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Forty-three years ago, it was on the basis of the one-China principle that China and the US established diplomatic relations. And today 40 years ago, China and the US jointly released the August 17 Communiqué. The US Government states in the joint communiqué that “it does not seek to carry out a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan, that its arms sales to Taiwan will not exceed, either in qualitative or in quantitative terms, the level of those supplied in recent years since the establishment of diplomatic relations between the United States and China, and that it intends gradually to reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution.”\nThe August 17 Communiqué, the Shanghai Communiqué and the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between China and the US constitute the political foundation for China-US relations and are all based on the one-China principle. The US recognized that the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government of China. It also recognized China’s position that there is only one China and Taiwan is part of China. And on this basis, the US met the three preconditions put forward by China, namely severing so-called “diplomatic relations” and abrogating the “mutual defense treaty” with the Taiwan authorities and withdrawing US military forces from Taiwan. This made it possible for China and the US, countries with different social systems and ideologies and at different development stages, to have dialogue and cooperation, and achieve important outcomes that have benefited both sides and the world at large.\nThe US has backpedaled on the one-China principle. It substantially relaxed restrictions on official interactions with Taiwan. It increased frequent military contact with Taiwan and arms sales to Taiwan in both qualitative and quantitative terms. Not long ago, US House Speaker Pelosi made a provocative visit to Taiwan in disregard of China’s opposition, blatantly violated its commitment of maintaining only unofficial relations with Taiwan. The US also keeps fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation for resuming interaction and developing relations between China and the US. The US has violated its commitment and moved further down the path that deviates from the one-China principle. This will surely take a huge toll on the mutual trust between the two countries.\nThe one-China principle also underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The US reneges on the one-China principle, colludes with the “Taiwan independence” forces, connives at and supports separatist activities, keeps changing the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, and shall bear all the responsibilities for the tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe one-China principle is reaffirmed by UNGA Resolution 2758. It is an integral part of the post-war international order, an established international consensus and a widely-accepted basic norm in international relations. By breaching the one-China principle, the US is also challenging the post-war international order, which will surely be met with wide opposition from the international community.\nFacts have shown that when the one-China principle is honored, China-US relations can grow smoothly and cross-Strait peace can be effectively maintained. When the one-China principle is undermined, China-US relations would suffer turbulence and regression, and the cross-Strait situation could face severe challenges.\nThe China-US relationship is now at a critical juncture. Undermining the one-China principle is risky and irresponsible. Just as Dr. Kissinger who was part of the drafting of the three China-US joint communiqués pointed out, it’s essential that the one-China principle be maintained and “the US should not by subterfuge or a gradual process develop something of a two-China solution”. We hope the US side can draw lessons from history, return to the provisions of the three joint communiqués, strictly abide by the one-China principle, and stop going further down the wrong path of distorting, manipulating, fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347348.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220817_10744880.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to questions on August 17: To implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's reply letter to Taiwan youths attending the Straits Youth Forum, and to build a platform for young people on both sides to join hands in experiencing Chinese culture and achieving spiritual connection, the 2nd Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month will be held in Jiangsu from mid-August to the end of September.\nThe Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month is guided by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and co-hosted by the Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office and the Suzhou Municipal People's Government. Under the theme “Same Heart, Same Path, Power of Youth,” on August 19 to 20 the main venue in Suzhou will host an opening ceremony, cultural exhibitions, cultural salons, cultural and tourism experiences and other activities. Young people from both sides of the Strait are invited to attend, including more than 100 Taiwan youth representatives who are interning or working in the Yangtze River Delta. During the Culture Month, more than 30 online and offline cross-Strait cultural exchange activities will be held in Suzhou, Nanjing, Taizhou, Xuzhou, Yancheng and other places. They cover esports, creative culture, lantern festivals, Peking opera, poetry, calligraphy and seal carving, and other fields, and include cultural salons, cultural and tourism experiences, online competitions, cloud sharing and other content, further providing more resources for young people across the Strait to learn from and draw on each other and move forward together with one heart.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220817_12463117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-17","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 17 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered questions on August 17, saying: Taiwan is part of China. The state has full legal basis for taking punitive measures against diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements. Anyone who endangers national sovereignty, security and development interests will not escape the sanctions of national law.\nMa Xiaoguang pointed out that the DPP authorities and a small handful of diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements have recklessly undermined cross-Strait relations, repeatedly pushed for Pelosi and U.S. congressional members to visit Taiwan, colluded with external forces to provoke for independence, and are the chief culprits in undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Resolutely cracking down on diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements in accordance with the law and stopping \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts is a just action to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, a necessary requirement for maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and an inevitable requirement for maintaining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It is entirely legitimate, reasonable and lawful.\nMa Xiaoguang said: If the DPP authorities continue to defy the trend of the times and righteousness, and condone and support diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements in provocations or even in defying to the end, we will take further necessary measures to resolutely thwart any scheme to split the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220817_12463118.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-18","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","This is a question about missing Hong Kongers and Taiwanese held captive in Myanmar. According to a report from media outlet TVBS, there are over 6,000 Taiwanese that have fallen for a scam in Myanmar. Over 2,000 of these are still being held captive. The Hong Kong SAR government has recently said that five Hong Kongers who also fell for a similar scam in Myanmar are also still missing. Does the foreign ministry…","The Chinese government attaches great importance to consular protection and is fully committed to protecting the safety and lawful rights and interests of overseas Chinese citizens, including our compatriots in Hong Kong and Taiwan. The Chinese embassy and consulate in the country concerned are in close communication with its government in the ongoing search and rescue efforts.\nWe once again remind our fellow citizens to be vigilant against fake overseas job postings on the Internet, strictly abide by laws and regulations, protect themselves, and promptly report any information related to fraud and gambling. In case of an emergency outside China, please contact the local police immediately and get into touch with the Chinese embassy or consulate there.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347349.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220818_10745415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-18","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US and Taiwan will start formal talks on a trade and economic initiative. The first round of these talks is expected to take place early this fall. That’s according to the USTR in a statement. Does the foreign ministry have any comment about this trade and economic initiative between the US and Taiwan?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is the prerequisite for China’s Taiwan region to participate in external economic cooperation. China is always against any country negotiating economic and trade agreements of sovereign implication or official nature with China’s Taiwan region. We ask the US to follow the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués with concrete actions, and stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan. The US must not negotiate agreements with sovereign implication or official nature with China’s Taiwan region or send any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in the name of trade and economic interactions. We urge the US not to repeat its wrongdoing. China will act resolutely to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US not to miscalculate on this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347349.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220818_10745415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-18","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, during the ninth China-Japan high-level political dialogue held yesterday, the Japanese side stated its position on the situation in the Taiwan Strait, said that China’s military exercises involve Japan’s EEZ and stressed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question concerns China’s core interest and is purely China’s internal affair. The historical ins and outs of the Taiwan question are crystal clear, so are the facts and status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. The history of and China’s policy and position on the Taiwan question is fully outlined in the white paper titled “The Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era” released by the Chinese government. It demonstrates the firm will and determination of the CPC and the Chinese people to achieve national reunification.\nOver the past few months, there have been a string of frequent negative moves concerning the Taiwan question from Japan. Some people in Japan claim that “Any contingency for Taiwan is a contingency for Japan”. This is a wrong perception which has undoubtedly sent a very dangerous and wrong message to the “Taiwan independence” forces. Following Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, more than 170 countries and many international organizations have spoken up for justice, reaffirming their one-China commitment and expressing their support for China’s efforts to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity. Japan, however,chose to confound right with wrong by supporting the US’s erroneous action and making groundless accusations against China. This is a gross interference in China’s internal affairs. China has made clear its stern position to the Japanese side on multiple occasions.\nThe Taiwan question bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and the basic trust between our two countries. There should be no ambivalence or vacillation about the attitude on the Taiwan question, still less any attempt to provoke or cross the red line on this. The Japanese side has made serious political commitments to China on this quite a few times. If the bedrock is shaken, whatever built upon it could rapidly collapse. Japan knows how sensitive the Taiwan question is and should be quite clear about the danger and harm in emboldening “Taiwan independence” forces. We urge Japan to draw the lessons from history, abide by the principles of the four China-Japan political documents and the commitments it has made.\nSince China and Japan have not yet carried out maritime delimitation in waters east of Taiwan, China does not accept the notion of so-called “Japanese EEZ”. The Chinese military drills in the waters off China’s Taiwan island are necessary and legitimate both as a response to the major provocation of the US side and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and as a step to firmly uphold China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The relevant Chinese authorities had issued safety alerts and navigation warnings before the start of the drills. Our practice is fully in line with international law and established international practices. We hope the Japanese side will truly and strictly abide by the one-China principle both in words and in deeds and actually do something that would contribute to cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347349.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220818_10745415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-18","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 18 (Dispatch): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, answering reporters’ questions on the 18th, said: We firmly oppose any agreement of a sovereign implication or official nature that the United States negotiates with the Chinese Taiwan region.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the United States and Taiwan will launch negotiations on the so-called “US-Taiwan…","Ma Xiaoguang said: We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through practical actions. Attempting to play the “Taiwan card” to block China’s reunification and national rejuvenation will not succeed.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that the vicious conduct of using economic and trade cooperation as a pretext, colluding with external forces, selling out the interests of the people on the island, and seeking political private gain will surely be held to account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220818_12463450.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-19","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","We have noted that the Coordinators’ Meeting on the Implementation of the Follow-up Actions of the 8th Ministerial Conference of the Forum on China-Africa Cooperation (FOCAC) was successfully held yesterday via video link. Can you share with us the details and outcomes of the meeting?","Yesterday State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi chaired the Coordinators’ Meeting on the Implementation of the Follow-up Actions of the 8th Ministerial Conference of FOCAC in Beijing via video link. Foreign Minister Aïssata Tall Sall of Senegal, the African co-chair of FOCAC, representatives of previous African co-chairs of FOCAC, sub-regional representatives of Africa, and representatives of the AU Commission, and African Diplomatic Envoys in China attended the meeting. The meeting was held amid evolving international situation and rising global challenge. Following the 8th FOCAC Ministerial Conference held last November, the meeting sends a strong message of China and Africa joining hands to cement solidarity and cooperation, focus on win-win cooperation and uphold fairness and justice.\nThe meeting was warm, effective and results-oriented. The two sides had a thorough exchange of views on comprehensively implementing the follow-up actions of the 8th FOCAC Ministerial Conference, and promoting China-Africa friendship and cooperation, and reached important common understandings. State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi put forward five suggestions on how China and Africa need to stand even closer with each other to truly build a China-Africa community with a shared future in the new era. First, we need to uphold sincerity, real results, amity and good faith and enhance solidarity and mutual support. Second, we need to take concrete actions to promote common development. Third, we need to uphold independence and jointly promote peace in the region. Fourth, we need to deepen our friendship and forge a stronger bond between the peoples. Fifth, we need to uphold openness and win-win results and promote the sound development of international cooperation with Africa. Representatives from Africa at the meeting and African Diplomatic Envoys in China spoke highly of China’s strong efforts for the implementation of the follow-up actions of the ministerial meeting and the important progress in this regard. Senegalese Foreign Minister Aïssata Tall Sall, Angolan Foreign Minister Tete António, DRC Industry Minister Julien Paluku Kahongya, Egyptian Foreign Minister Sameh Shoukry, Ethiopian Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Demeke Mekonnen Hassen, Libyan Undersecretary for International Cooperation and Organizations Affairs Omar Katti, South African Deputy Foreign Minister of International Relations and Cooperation Candith Mashego-Dlamini and Deputy Chairperson for the African Union Commission Monique Nsanzabaganwa, among others, highly commended President Xi Jinping’s proposal of building a China-Africa community with a shared future in the new era and the nine programs. The African side appreciated China’s important role in helping African countries in their response to food and energy crises and COVID-19. They hoped to work with China to continue to enhance mechanism building for FOCAC, form greater synergy between development strategies of African countries and the Belt and Road Initiative, and improve and upgrade Africa-China cooperation.\nThe joint statement adopted at the meeting encapsulates China and Africa’s common understandings on adhering to the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, opposing external interference, unilateral sanctions and racial discrimination and standing together in response to COVID-19. It demonstrates the firm support both sides have rendered each other on issues of our respective concerns and core interests, and testifies to our firm determination to jointly build a China-Africa community with a shared future in the new era. The African side reaffirms its commitment to the one-China principle, and its support for China’s national reunification and China’s efforts to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity. China highly commends that.\nGoing forward, the two sides will focus on the important common understandings reached at the meeting to step up strategic coordination and solidarity and continue to make solid steps to advance the nine programs. We will remain committed to accelerating the effort to build a China-Africa community with a shared future in the new era, enhancing solidarity and cooperation among developing countries, and building the shining example of FOCAC. By doing so, we will be able to make relentless effort for the in-depth development of China-Africa comprehensive strategic partnership and make greater contributions to world peace and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347350.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220819_10746168.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-19","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","US Assistant Secretary of State for the Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel J. Kritenbrink said that China overreacted to Pelosi’s visit and used coercive and provocative actions to increase pressure against Taiwan. He added that the US will act responsibly and resolutely. Do you have any comment?","The context, cause and course of events on US House Speaker Pelosi’s provocative visit to Taiwan are crystal clear. It is the US that has breached its one-China commitment and undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, not the other way round. It is the US leader who traveled to China’s Taiwan region to support the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. No one from China has gone to Alaska or elsewhere in the US to support separatist movement there.\nChina’s response to US provocation is legitimate, lawful and justified and has received extensive understanding and support from the international community. If the US wants to make things right, the only right way is to return to the three China-US joint communiqués and the one-China principle, rather than shift blame, still less act recklessly and create an even bigger crisis. China will not waver in defending its sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US must not miscalculate.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347350.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220819_10746168.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-19","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","In response to China’s sanctions on Lithuania’s Deputy Transport and Communications Minister, Lithuania’s Foreign Ministry said in a statement that it issued a formal protest to China, calling for the restrictions to be rescinded. Do you have any comment?","Senior Lithuanian officials made a provocative visit to China’s Taiwan region. This clearly violates Lithuania’s political commitment to upholding the one-China principle, the common understanding of the international community and basic norms in international relations. China has made a necessary response to Lithuania’s erroneous acts, which is totally legitimate, reasonable and lawful. We urge the Lithuanian side to tell right from wrong, immediately redress its mistakes and stop chipping away the political foundation of China-Lithuania relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347350.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220819_10746168.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-19","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Taiwan media reported that recently there have been frequent incidents of Taiwan residents being lured to work in Cambodia, then imprisoned and beaten, which has caused dissatisfaction among the island's people toward the DPP authorities, and some on the island have tried to shift the blame to the mainland. What comment do you have on this? Island residents hope the mainland can assist in the rescue. Will the…","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 19 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 19th when answering reporters' questions that compatriots from Taiwan are citizens of China, and safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots is our duty. For a long time, we have always attached great importance to protecting the safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. From providing consular document services, to assisting in handling civil disputes, economic cases, and criminal cases involving Taiwan in foreign countries, to evacuating citizens during major emergencies, the motherland has been their strong backing and has helped them overcome difficulties. Whatever difficulties Taiwan compatriots encounter overseas, they can promptly contact Chinese embassies and consulates abroad for assistance.\nMa Xiaoguang said that the DPP authorities have been passive toward the calls of the people of Taiwan to protect their legitimate rights and interests, and have even attempted to fabricate lies and shift blame onto the mainland. This fully exposes their long-standing tactics of disregarding the safety and well-being of the people of Taiwan, turning everything into political maneuvering, inciting confrontation, and deceiving the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220819_12463712.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-22","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 22 dispatch. Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, answering a reporter’s question on the 22nd, said: The visit to the mainland by a delegation led by the Vice Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, and the exchanges between the Central Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, relevant departments, and localities with the visiting delegation, are a matter of…","Ma Xiaoguang said that over the years, the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have maintained mutual trust and strengthened exchanges and cooperation, and have played an important positive role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220822_12464312.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-08-23","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","XINHUA News Agency, Beijing, August 23 (electronic dispatch) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 23rd that certain Japanese politicians and lawmakers are following the trend in making visits to the Taiwan region of China, seeking to gain political self-interest, and that China firmly opposes this.\nA reporter asked: Recently, Tsai Ing-wen, in an interview…","Ma Xiaoguang said, we urge these people on the Japanese side to learn from historical lessons, fully recognize the sensitivity of the Taiwan question, recognize the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents through concrete actions, and be cautious in their words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues.\nHe pointed out that we warn the DPP authorities: colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoking trouble is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220823_12464595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-08-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say the DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped up US-Taiwan military ties recently. Meanwhile, Taiwan's so-called “Army Commander” led a delegation to the United States, where it attended the annual meeting of the Association of the United States Army and met with US defense departments and military personnel. What comments do you have on this?","We have noted relevant reports. We have expressed serious concern to the United States and made solemn representations, demanding that the United States provide clarification to China on this matter. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. China firmly opposes any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and Taiwan's region. For some time, some people in the United States have violated the political commitment to one China, repeatedly played the \"Taiwan card,\" sent extremely wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and brought serious negative impacts to China-U.S. relations, military-to-military relations between the two countries, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. If the United States continues to obstinately cling to the illusion of \"using Taiwan to contain China\" and attempts to substantively upgrade U.S.-Taiwan military ties through a \"salami-slicing\" approach, China will resolutely take countermeasures and retaliate.\nThe historical mission of complete reunification of the motherland must be accomplished, and it will certainly be accomplished. Any scheme that depends on others, relies on foreign powers to boost its own position, and obstructs national reunification and national rejuvenation will ultimately fail. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to thwart the interference of external forces and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts, and will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16194729.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-08-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，中央军委副主席许其亮近日在广州会见柬埔寨副首相兼国防大臣迪班。请进一步介绍有关情况，并评价当前中柬两军关系。","Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Chinese Ministry of National Defense, made a statement on the 5th regarding the US's release of the 2021 \"Military and Security Developments Involving the People's Republic of China\" report. He pointed out that China must solemnly warn the US that any attempt or act to interfere in China's internal affairs or bully China will be met with a head-on blow against the Great Wall of steel that is the Chinese People's Liberation Army.\nWu Qian said that at 11/4 Beijing time, the US Department of Defense released the 2021 \"Military and Security Developments Involving the People's Republic of China\" report. The report disregards facts and is full of prejudice, makes baseless comments on China's national defense policy and military strategy, fabricates the so-called \"China military threat,\" groundlessly accuses China of its nuclear capability development, and interferes in China's internal affairs on issues such as Taiwan. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged serious representations with the US.\nWu Qian pointed out that China firmly pursues a defensive national defense policy and an active defense military strategy. China's military development is entirely for the purpose of safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, for crushing any schemes that endanger regional peace, stability, and prosperity. It is not directed at any country and does not pose a threat to any country. In recent years, the Chinese military has actively served the building of a community with a shared future for mankind, and has actively provided international society with public security products such as peacekeeping, escort, epidemic response, and humanitarian rescue, demonstrating the responsibility of a major power's military and injecting strong positive energy into world peace and regional stability. \"History and reality both prove that the development of the Chinese military brings security rather than threats to the world, and opportunities rather than challenges.\"\nWu Qian pointed out that however large a country is, if it loves war, it will perish. In recent years, the US has accelerated the development of military capabilities in areas such as nuclear, space, cyber warfare, and hypersonic technology, has recklessly withdrawn from the INF Treaty and the ABM Treaty, established a trilateral security partnership with the UK and Australia, and carried out nuclear submarine cooperation, artificially creating serious risks of nuclear proliferation and causing enormous shocks to the international nuclear non-proliferation system. As is well known, the US possesses the world's largest nuclear arsenal, yet continues to upgrade its nuclear forces and lower the nuclear threshold; the US is truly the greatest creator of global nuclear threat.\nWu Qian said that, moreover, for many years the US has single-handedly obstructed negotiations on a verification protocol for the Biological Weapons Convention, has deployed more than 200 biological laboratories overseas, and to date has not completed the destruction of its stockpile of chemical weapons; these US actions pose a major threat to world peace and security. \"In particular, it must be pointed out that on the issue of the underwater collision accident involving US nuclear submarines, the US still owes the international community a clear and unambiguous explanation.\"\nWu Qian pointed out that on the issues of territorial sovereignty and maritime rights disputes, China's position is clear and explicit: the Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands are an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and China has indisputable sovereignty over the islands and reefs of the South China Sea and their adjacent waters. China has consistently advocated resolving disputes peacefully through negotiation and consultation, but firmly opposes interference and intervention by extraregional countries.\n\"There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan has been an inalienable part of China's sacred territory since ancient times,\" Wu Qian said. Over a period of time, the DPP authorities, under the indulgence of external forces, have continuously pursued \"independence\" and provoked confrontation; this is the fundamental reason for undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and raising the risk of the situation there. We firmly oppose the US playing the \"Taiwan card\" to pursue \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" firmly oppose any external forces interfering in Taiwan affairs, and firmly oppose the DPP authorities' \"relying on the US for self-reliance\" to pursue \"using force to resist unification.\" The Chinese nation has a glorious tradition of opposing division and safeguarding unity. Against any secessionist acts by the Taiwan authorities, and against any external forces that stir up tensions in the Taiwan Strait or deliberately create regional crises, the Chinese People's Liberation Army will strike back head-on with firm resolve, unwavering will, and powerful capability.\nThis spokesperson pointed out that for more than 20 years, the US has stubbornly insisted on year after year deliberately fabricating the so-called \"China Military and Security Developments Report,\" which is a blatant act of hegemony. \"Here, we must solemnly warn the US that any attempt or act to interfere in China's internal affairs or bully China will be met with a head-on blow against the Great Wall of steel that is the Chinese People's Liberation Army.\"","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16194735.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-08-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，2022年全国下半年征兵工作日前全面展开。请进一步介绍征兵工作有关情况，这次征兵工作有哪些新特点新政策？","On November 9, members of the US Congress flew on military aircraft to visit Taiwan, and we firmly oppose and strongly condemn this. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s sacred territory. The United States’ brazen actions interfere in China’s internal affairs, seriously harm China’s territorial sovereignty, and seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We solemnly warn the United States to immediately stop its provocative acts and immediately cease all destructive actions that escalate tension in the Taiwan Strait, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We warn the DPP authorities not to misjudge the situation or take reckless risks, or they will only plunge Taiwan into deep disaster.\nChina must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. No one should underestimate the Chinese people’s firm determination, steadfast will and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will always maintain a high state of alert and take all necessary measures to resolutely crush any interference by external forces and any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16194738.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-08-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，中泰两国空军近期在泰国举行代号为“鹰击-2022”的空军联合训练。请进一步介绍有关情况。","According to an official WeChat message from the News Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense, Wu Qian, Director of the News Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense and spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, Senior Colonel, said on the 25th that the Chinese side's approach to developing China-US military relations is based on principles, namely that China's sovereignty, dignity, and core interests must not be violated. On the Taiwan question in particular, China has no room for compromise, and the US side should harbor no illusions.\nAt a regular press conference held by the Ministry of National Defense on the 25th, a reporter asked: On November 16, President Xi Jinping and US President Joe Biden held a video meeting, conducting an in-depth exchange of views on China-US relations and issues of common concern, and reached important consensus. President Xi pointed out that China and the United States have broad common interests in many areas, including between their militaries, and should share what they have and learn from each other's strengths to make the “pie” of China-US cooperation bigger. Against this backdrop, what are China's expectations for developing China-US military relations?\nIn response, Senior Colonel Wu Qian said that on November 16, President Xi Jinping held a video meeting with US President Biden. This was a major event in China-US relations and international relations. At a critical moment, the heads of state of the two countries once again steered China-US relations and charted the course, pointing the way forward and injecting new momentum into the future development of bilateral and military relations between the two countries.\nChina-US military relations are an important component of bilateral relations. Maintaining the healthy and stable development of military relations between the two countries is in the common interests of both countries and in line with the common expectations of the international community. China values the development of military relations and is willing to maintain exchanges and cooperation with the US side. However, for some time, the US side has made many irresponsible remarks and carried out many provocative acts on issues such as Taiwan, the South China Sea, and close-in reconnaissance by ships and aircraft. In response, China has naturally waged resolute struggle in a tit-for-tat manner. We have stated many times that China's approach to developing military relations is based on principles, namely that China's sovereignty, dignity, and core interests must not be violated. On the Taiwan question in particular, China has no room for compromise, and the US side should harbor no illusions.\nPresident Xi profoundly pointed out that in the next 50 years, the most important matter in international relations is for China and the United States to find the right way to get along. The Chinese military is willing to work together with the US side to implement the spirit of the meeting between the two heads of state through concrete actions, adhere to the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence, and win-win cooperation, take a long-term view while focusing on the present, strengthen communication, manage differences, carry out cooperation, and promote the healthy and stable development of China-US military relations forward, benefiting the peoples of China, the United States, and the rest of the world.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16194743.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-08-25","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","民进党当局近期多次炒作，大陆在台湾周边军演是“不负责任”的“挑衅”行为。另据台媒报道，台军近日开展重炮射击训练和“无限高”导弹试射，并进行反登陆操演。请问对此有何评论？","At its regular press conference on the 25th, Senior Colonel Wu Qian, spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, said that China-Russia military relations have no “best,” only “better”; China-Russia military cooperation has no “full stop,” only a “march.”\nA reporter asked at the meeting: On November 23, State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe held a video call with Russian Defense Minister Shoigu. How do you assess the current state of China-Russia military relations?\nWu Qian said that in recent years, under the strategic guidance of President Xi Jinping and President Putin, the comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for a new era between China and Russia has continued to move forward. Exchanges and cooperation between the two militaries in all fields have deepened day by day, strategic communication has reached a new level, practical cooperation has achieved new breakthroughs, and mechanism building has made new progress, continuously enriching the strategic content of bilateral relations.\nFirst, strategic communication has been close. Since the beginning of this year, the leaders of the two militaries have maintained close strategic communication. State Councilor and Minister of National Defense Wei Fenghe participated in the 9th Moscow International Security Conference by recording a video address, and met with Russian Defense Minister Shoigu twice, in Dushanbe, Tajikistan, and in Ningxia, China. Li Zuocheng, member of the Central Military Commission and Chief of Staff of the Joint Staff Department of the Central Military Commission, went to Russia to observe the “Peace Mission-2021” joint counterterrorism military exercise of Shanghai Cooperation Organisation member states and held talks with the Russian Chief of the General Staff. On November 23, Minister Wei Fenghe and Minister Shoigu held a video call to review the year's cooperation and exchange views on the next steps of cooperation, with naval and air force leaders of both sides participating. In addition, the leaders of the two militaries have promptly exchanged views on important issues of military cooperation through letters.\nSecond, practical cooperation in the field of exercises and training has deepened. Since the beginning of this year, the two militaries have successfully organized a series of joint exercises and training activities under the normalized epidemic prevention and control context. The Russian military came to China for the first time to take part in the Chinese-hosted “West·Joint-2021” exercise. The two sides jointly held the “Joint Sea-2021” exercise and the first joint naval patrol, and carried out the third joint air strategic patrol. They jointly took part in the SCO “Peace Mission-2021” joint counterterrorism military exercise and continued to deepen relevant cooperation within the framework of the “International Army Games-2021,” further enhancing the joint operational capabilities of the two militaries.\nThird, the military cooperation mechanism has continued to improve. Since the beginning of the year, the two sides have continued to advance the construction of the military cooperation mechanism, formulated cooperation development plans, and the two militaries have further strengthened coordination and cooperation within multilateral frameworks such as the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation.\nWu Qian said that China-Russia military relations have no “best,” only “better”; China-Russia military cooperation has no “full stop,” only a “march.” This year marks the 20th anniversary of the signing of the Treaty of Good-Neighborliness and Friendly Cooperation between China and Russia, which is of special and important significance to the two countries. The Chinese military is willing to work with the Russian side to closely coordinate strategically, deepen exchanges and cooperation, bring more well-being to the two countries and their peoples, and play a greater role in safeguarding world peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16194749.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-08-29","Zhao Lijian","China News Service","We noted recent revelations about people from Taiwan who are held captive and subject to beating in Cambodia after being lured to the country by job scams. This has received much attention from many social sectors. Is the Chinese embassy in Cambodia offering any consular protection to the compatriots from Taiwan? What is it doing exactly?","The Chinese government attaches great importance to and is fully committed to protecting the safety and lawful rights and interests of overseas Chinese nationals, including our compatriots from Taiwan. The Chinese embassy in Cambodia is in close communication with the Cambodian government in the ongoing search and rescue efforts. The Chinese embassy has so far received help requests from over 20 compatriots who came from Taiwan and has assisted the Cambodian side in successfully rescuing some of them. We will continue to closely follow the handling of relevant cases. Compatriots from Taiwan and their families in need can contact the Chinese embassy in Cambodia promptly to seek help.\nWe once again remind our fellow citizens to be vigilant against fake overseas job postings on the Internet, strictly abide by laws and regulations, protect themselves, and promptly report any information related to fraud and gambling. In case of an emergency outside China, please contact the local police immediately and get in touch with the Chinese embassies or consulates there.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347351.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220829_10757191.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-29","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","On Sunday, two US warships passed through international waters in the Taiwan Strait, a move that a White House official described in the same day as very consistent with the US’s one-China policy and its policy of seeking a free and open Indo-Pacific. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","Spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has responded to this. The Eastern Theater Command conducted security tracking and monitoring of the US warships’ passage in the whole course, and had all movements of the US warships under control.\nUS warships frequently flex muscles in the name of exercising freedom of navigation. This is not about keeping the region free and open. This is provocation aimed at “freedom of trespassing” and it constitutes deliberate sabotage of regional peace and stability.\nChina once again urges the US side to stop fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China principle, observe basic norms in international relations including respecting other countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in their internal affairs, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop being a trouble maker for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347351.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220829_10757191.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-29","Zhao Lijian","AFP","In addition to reports on people from Taiwan trapped in Cambodia and other Southeast Asian countries and forced to operate phone scams, we've also seen reports that there are people from Hong Kong as well as the mainland. I just wanted to ask the foreign ministry if you had received any request for help from people from Hong Kong and the mainland, and if you could share more details on what concrete steps are…","","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347351.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220829_10757191.shtml",0,3,0,""],[0,"2022-08-29","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","The EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy Josep Borrell had reportedly said that “Taiwan is a small country”, but later the EU spokesperson’s office said it was a mistranslation that didn’t reflect the High Representative’s view. Do you have any comment?","We have noted relevant reports.\nLet me stress that the definition of the one-China principle is crystal clear, i.e., there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. There is no room for ambivalence on this major matter of principle.\nWe hope the EU side will continue to follow the one-China principle, respect China’s core interests and major concerns, and reflect its commitment in concrete actions on Taiwan-related issues to avoid affecting China-EU relations and mutual trust.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347351.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220829_10757191.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-29","Zhao Lijian","TBS","Recently on the internet, there are many videos of private drones flying from the mainland to the Kinmen island to take pictures. Do you have any comment on this?","I have seen the videos too. Chinese drones flying over China’s territory — what’s there to be surprised at?","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347351.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220829_10757191.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-30","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","US White House official John Kirby said that China is trying to introduce a “new normal” in the Taiwan Strait with military activities to escalate the situation, and that the US will not accept this. We also noticed that the White House Press Secretary said that in response to Chinese provocative moves, the US will conduct military exercises in the future with a view toward guiding the situation in western…","It is the US and Taiwan separatist forces, not China, that seeks to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The “Taiwan independence” forces’ attempt to solicit foreign support including from the US to advance their agenda is the source of the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe US, under the pretext of stability in the West Pacific, blatantly tries to use Taiwan contain China. How is this not about China or China-US relations? If the US truly wants to guide the situation toward greater stability, it should immediately return to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and avoid sending any more wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347352.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220830_10757747.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-30","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Guatemalan Foreign Minister Mario Bucaro said today that “Guatemala will always support Taiwan because we firmly believe in the principles of peace, sovereignty and territorial integrity.” This is said in Taipei when Mario Bucaro was meeting with Tsai Ing-wen. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this statement?","The one-China principle is a widely accepted norm in international relations and a common understanding of the international community. The DPP authorities are seeking political manipulation by using certain countries having what they call “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan. This deceptive gambit will not work. Nor will it hold back the inevitability of China’s reunification. In the meantime, we urge Guatemala to refrain from emboldening the DPP authorities, get a clear understanding of the overwhelming trend in the international community as soon as possible and make a decision that is in keeping with the historic trend at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347352.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220830_10757747.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-08-30","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Recently, the mainland side has been actively assisting in rescuing Taiwan compatriots who were lured to Cambodia and trapped there, yet the DPP authorities have attacked this effort. What is your comment?","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 30 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 30th in response to reporters' questions: Taiwan compatriots are citizens of China. When they are trapped in danger overseas and their lives and property are threatened, we share their feelings and will naturally do our utmost to help. Our embassy and consulates in Cambodia are in close communication with the Cambodian side, actively searching for and rescuing trapped Taiwan compatriots. We have so far received dozens of requests for help from Taiwan compatriots, and have assisted some of them in escaping danger and returning home safely.\nMa Xiaoguang said that for many years, we have been making every effort to provide consular protection and services to overseas Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots. The mainland of the motherland will always be the strong backing of the broad Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities' political manipulation of issues concerning the safety of Taiwan compatriots can only once again expose their vile nature of disregarding the life and death of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202208/t20220830_12466280.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Phoenix TV","Principal deputy spokesperson of the US State Department said when answering a question related to the situation across the Taiwan Strait that China has overreacted and has made provocations, whereas the United States’ response has been “ measured and responsible ” . Do you have any response to this?","The context, cause and course of events that led to the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait are crystal clear. The US made the provocation first, and China was compelled to take legitimate countermeasures, which are justified, lawful, necessary and proportionate. It is the US that breached its one-China commitment and undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, yet it accused China of overreacting. It is the US that has frequently sent warships to flex muscles in waters off China’s coast in the name of freedom of navigation, yet it accused China of making provocations. This is confounding right with wrong. China will not accept it, nor will the international community endorse it.\nWhat the US needs to do is to stop fudging, hollowing out and distorting the one-China principle, abide by the basic norms in international relations including respecting other countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in their internal affairs, and return to the three China-US joint communiqués and the one-China principle, instead of shifting responsibilities, blaming the innocent party and attempting to create an even bigger crisis.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347353.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220831_10758360.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Beijing Youth Daily","According to reports, Republican Arizona Governor Doug Ducey has arrived in Taiwan, and will meet Tsai Ing-wen and Joseph Wu, participate in activities of the business community and meet with representatives of the semiconductor sector in Taiwan. What is your comment on that?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly rejects any official interaction between the US and Taiwan in any form and in any name. We urge relevant parties in the US to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop all forms of official contact with Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. China will take strong measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347353.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220831_10758360.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","The Taiwan Army Chief of Staff has said that the Javelin anti-tank missiles that Taiwan has ordered from the US are now in the production and delivery stage. My first question would be, do you have any comment on this update on the status of the anti-tank missiles? And separately, the Taiwan military has said that it plans to increase an order of the HIMARS rocket system, increasing the number from 11 to 29.…","I noted relevant reports. Let me just say that the Taiwan authorities’ attempt to seek independence by soliciting US support will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347353.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220831_10758360.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-31","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","In April, US Republican Senator Lindsey Graham openly asked the Taiwan authorities to buy $8 billion worth of Boeing 787 planes during his visit to Taiwan. Recently, news agencies in Taiwan reported that Taiwan’s China Airlines will buy Boeing airplanes which means that the Taiwan authorities lapped up the deal peddled by Graham . Do you have any comment?","Certain US politicians use Taiwan visits as a money generator and make an exorbitant ask to the Taiwan authorities. This is hardly news. The DPP authorities have been squandering the hard-earned money of the people in Taiwan and have been reduced to an ATM for US politicians to seek selfish gains.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347353.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220831_10758360.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-08-31","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","A Taiwanese defense official told reporters at a news briefing that for aircraft and ships that enter Taiwan sea and air territory, the national army, referring to Taiwan national army, will exercise right to self-defense to counterattack without exception. The same defense official said the same right to counterattack Chinese drones would apply. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","Let me start by saying that Taiwan is a province of China and it does not have a “defense ministry”. The act of the Taiwan authorities to heighten tensions does not mean anything.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347353.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202208/t20220831_10758360.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-01","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Russian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said yesterday that the passage of US Navy ships through the waters of the Taiwan Strait is a provocation that makes the situation more complex and unpredictable. “We consider the settlement of the situation in the Taiwan Strait as purely China’s domestic affair with it having the right to take measures to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity”, she…","We appreciate the remarks by the Russian side. More than 170 countries in the world have made it clear that they are committed to the one-China principle, and support China in safeguarding its sovereignty and territorial integrity. This reflects the prevailing voice of the international community. The US’s acts of provocation will not have people’s support and will only end in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347354.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220901_10759230.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-01","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","It is reported that on August 31, Japan ’s Ministry of Defense claimed in its annual defense budget request that China continues to threaten to unilaterally change the status quo with force and exert pressure by conducting military exercises around Taiwan. Japan is seeking budget to develop and mass produce cruise missiles, high-velocity ballistic missiles and hypersonic missile warheads. The report also said…","The Chinese side has elaborated its position on this issue several times.\nRecently, Japan has been hyping up the so-called “China threat” and talking about missile development plans and the so-called “counterstrike capabilities” with the purpose of creating excuses for developing offensive military capability. It reveals Japan’s ambition to breach its commitment to the pacifist constitution and embark on its old path of military expansionism again. This sends a dangerous signal to the world that Japan is seeking to subvert the post-WWII international order. This calls for international vigilance.\nAs a country responsible for its historical crimes to the Asian neighbors, Japan needs to earnestly reflect on its history of aggression, respect the security concerns of Asian neighbors and immediately stop the erroneous practice of hyping up so-called security threats in the neighborhood to find pretext for its military build-up.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347354.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220901_10759230.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-01","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","According to reports, the Arizona Governor had a meeting with Tsai Ing-wen this morning, where the two sides agreed to have semiconductor cooperation. What is China’s comment?","The global industrial and supply chains come into shape as a result of both the law of the market and the choices of businesses. The “Taiwan independence” forces thought they could raise their profile by promoting the so-called notion of “democracy chips”. And they seek to politicize economic and trade issues. Such a design to use democracy as a false pretext to seek independence will not lead anywhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347354.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220901_10759230.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-02","Zhao Lijian","CRI","Based on information released by the DPRK, the DPRK side concluded that balloons floated over the border from the ROK is a route of the coronavirus inroads into the country and said it will take measures in response. An official of the DPRK’s research institute for national unification said yesterday that the US-ROK Ulchi Freedom Shield military exercise is an extremely provocative and dangerous nuclear war game…","China noted relevant reports and is closely following the recent developments on the Korean Peninsula.\nIn 2018, the DPRK and the ROK reached common ground on a number of important measures such as the proper handling of balloons and joint military exercises. After that, the situation on the Peninsula took a major turn for the better, which was widely welcomed by countries in the region and the international community. Regrettably, the situation on the Peninsula later reached an impasse. China believes that dialogue and consultation is the only right and effective way to resolve the Peninsula issue. Improving and developing relations and promoting reconciliation and cooperation between North and South has an irreplaceable role in easing tensions on the Peninsula and pushing forward the process of political settlement of the Peninsula issue. The DPRK’s concerns over the balloons and military exercises should be taken seriously. China calls on all parties to show goodwill, meet each other halfway, jointly prevent escalation of the situation and make positive efforts for an early resumption of dialogue and peace talks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347355.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220902_10760376.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-05","Mao Ning","NHK","The US government has approved a new arms sale to Taiwan. What is China’s comment?","US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region are a blatant violation of the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. The arms sales gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and send a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns them. We will take resolute and strong measures to firmly defend our own sovereignty and security interests.\nFor some time, the US has repeatedly trampled on international law and basic norms in international relations and breached the US leader’s political commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”. The US side keeps distorting, fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, deliberately makes provocations on the Taiwan question, and supports and connives at “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The US has an unshirkable responsibility for causing tensions to rise in the Taiwan Strait. China urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to Taiwan and military contact with Taiwan, stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait, stop seeking political manipulation with Taiwan-related issues, stop using Taiwan to contain China, and avoid going further down the wrong and dangerous path.\nI want to once again make it clear to the US side that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. The Taiwan question brooks no external interference. No individual or force can halt the historic process of China’s complete reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347356.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220905_10762291.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on September 5, said that from September 7 to 8, Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province will hold three cross-Strait exchange and cooperation events: the 2022 Cross-Strait Industrial Internet Integrated Development Seminar; the launch of the 10th Cross-Strait (Kunshan-Taiwan) Cultural Exchange Month and the opening of the “Baodao Yicun” cultural, tourism and commercial street at Kunshan Huiju Square; and the lighting of the 2022 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival.\nThe 2022 Cross-Strait Industrial Internet Integrated Development Seminar, to be held on September 8, is co-hosted by the China Industrial Internet Research Institute and the Taiwan Electrical and Electronic Manufacturers' Association. Enterprise representatives from both sides of the Strait and relevant industry experts will engage in in-depth exchanges on “digital transformation of small and medium-sized enterprises,” injecting new vitality and momentum into the integrated development of the industrial internet across the Strait.\nThe launch of the 10th Cross-Strait (Kunshan-Taiwan) Cultural Exchange Month and the opening of the “Baodao Yicun” cultural, tourism and commercial street at Kunshan Huiju Square will take place on September 7. The commercial street will deeply integrate the characteristics of Taiwan night markets with Jiangnan culture, aiming to build the most influential Taiwan-featured cultural district in the Yangtze River Delta, the most attractive showcase of Kunshan's urban night economy, and a new retail experience zone in the digital economy.\nThe 2022 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival, themed “Blossoms on One Stem, Lanterns Shining Across the Strait,” will be lit on the evenings of September 7 and 8 at the Kunshan Development Zone's Huiju Square and the Tourism Resort (Zhouzhuang Ancient Town), and will continue until October 7. This festival fully blends the charm of Jiangnan with Taiwanese customs and features 13 concurrent cross-Strait cultural exchange, lantern carnival, thematic publicity and cultural tourism consumption events.\nIn recent years, Kunshan in Jiangsu has continued to build itself into the best platform for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. In 2022, Kunshan plans to hold 59 series events to deepen economic, social and cultural exchange and practical cooperation between Kunshan and Taiwan, covering economy, technology, education, healthcare, culture and many other fields, playing a positive role in promoting exchanges between the two places and deepening practical cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220905_12467621.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-09-06","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. Department of Defense announced that the U.S. State Department has approved arms sales to Taiwan worth approximately US$1.1 billion in total, including missile and surveillance radar projects. What is your comment on this?","The United States' sale of weapons to Taiwan, China seriously violates the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the “8·17” Communiqué. It crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, harms China's sovereignty and security interests, and escalates tensions across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this.\nRecently, the United States has repeatedly gone back on its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” intensified its military collusion with the DPP authorities, stoked tensions, and been inconsistent in word and deed on arms sales to Taiwan, showing no credibility, and sending a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We demand that the United States immediately cancel the above-mentioned arms sales plan and immediately halt military contacts between the United States and Taiwan.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. No one and no force can block the historical trend of the complete reunification of the motherland. The “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, who try to rely on buying “foreign weapons” to “seek independence by force,” are overestimating themselves and are doomed to fail. The will of the people cannot be defied, and those who play with fire will get burned. The Chinese People's Liberation Army continues to train and prepare for combat, and will resolutely thwart any form of external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278475.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-09-07","Mao Ning","The Paper","Deputy Spokesperson of the US State Department Vedant Patel said during a press briefing on September 6 that the US’s latest arms sales to Taiwan are for defensive purposes and there is no reason for China to react. Do you have any comment on this?","China has always been unequivocally against the US’s military contact with Taiwan and arms sales to Taiwan. Taiwan is a province of China. There is no such thing as “defense for Taiwan”. US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region violate the US’s political commitment in the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. By selling arms to Taiwan, the US is supporting and conniving at “Taiwan independence” and creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The US side needs to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués and stop using Taiwan against China. China will act resolutely in response to acts that undermine China’s sovereignty and security and interfere in China’s internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347358.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220907_10763395.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-08","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan said on Thursday that it would send a representative to former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe’s state funeral. What is the foreign ministry’s response to this? Can the foreign ministry announce if a representative from China is attending the funeral and if so, who it is?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and the basic trust between our two countries. The Japanese side has made serious political commitments on this to China for multiple times. The Japanese side should abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and handle relevant issues in strict accordance with the one-China principle. Japan must not provide any platform for “Taiwan independence” forces to find opportunities for political manipulation.\nThe Taiwan authorities seek to use the event to engage in political manipulation and benefit politically. Their political calculations will not succeed.\nRegarding your question on whether someone will represent China at the funeral, I gave an answer yesterday and have nothing to share.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347359.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220908_10764065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-08","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","A bipartisan group of eight US lawmakers arrived in Taiwan on Wednesday, led by Stephanie Murphy, a Representative from Florida. Today, some of the representatives met with Taiwan’s Tsai Ing-wen. Does the Chinese foreign ministry have a comment on this visit by the US lawmakers to Taiwan?","The US lawmakers’ visit to China’s Taiwan region seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués and goes against the US’s commitment of maintaining only unofficial ties with the Taiwan region. The Chinese side deplores and firmly rejects this.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We will not waver in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference. We urge the relevant US politicians to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop all forms of official interactions with Taiwan, and immediately stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will continue to take strong measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347359.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220908_10764065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 8 (electronic dispatch): TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said in response to questions on the 8th that on September 5, a magnitude 6.8 earthquake struck Luding County, Garze Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan, causing major casualties. After the disaster, people from all walks of life in Taiwan expressed concern and sympathy for the disaster area through various forms, and Taiwanese businesses enthusiastically donated money and goods. We express our thanks for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220908_12468805.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-09-09","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","The 158th meeting of the Council of Foreign Ministers of the League of Arab States (LAS) on September 6 and 7 adopted a resolution on Arab-China relations which reiterated the Arab states’ support for the one-China principle, their readiness to strengthen cooperation with China in various fields under the Belt and Road Initiative, and their appreciation of China’s diplomatic effort in supporting the Arab cause,…","China highly appreciates the annual adoption of the resolution on strengthening relations with China by the Council of Foreign Ministers of the League of Arab States (LAS) for years running. This fully demonstrates the firm determination of Arab states to develop relations with China and reflects the profound traditional friendship and solid strategic partnership between China and Arab states.\nChina and Arab states are future-oriented strategic partners of comprehensive cooperation and common development. We have always firmly supported each other on issues concerning each other’s core interests and major concerns. After US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi made the provocative visit to China’s Taiwan region in August, the LAS Secretariat immediately issued a statement stressing its firm commitment to the one-China principle. Our two sides enjoy fruitful cooperation under the Belt and Road Initiative. China has been the largest trading partner of Arab states for many years. Our practical cooperation in various fields has continued to deepen and become a fine example of South-South cooperation. The two sides have maintained close coordination on hotspot issues in the Middle East and jointly contributed to regional peace and development.\nChina will continue to firmly support Arab states in addressing regional security issues through solidarity and coordination, and support people in Arab states in independently exploring their development paths. We will continue to strengthen solidarity and cooperation with Arab states, actively conduct Belt and Road cooperation, implement the Global Development Initiative and Global Security Initiative, and jointly build a community with a shared future for China and Arab states in the new era.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347360.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220909_10764638.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-14","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","A Taiwan-based outlet reported that Chinese Ambassador to the US Qin Gang told US Deputy Secretary of State Wendy Sherman last month that China-US ties would “face disintegration” if the Taiwan Policy Act is passed. My question is, does that accurately characterize Ambassador Qin’s remarks?","I have no knowledge of what Ambassador Qin specifically said, but I believe he was stressing the importance of upholding the one-China principle to China-US relations. The Chinese side has repeatedly expressed its firm opposition to the Taiwan Policy Act of 2022. The one-China principle constitutes the political foundation of China-US relations. This principle is at the heart of the three China-US joint communiqués. The US side needs to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués and stop advancing the relevant Taiwan-related Act. Only by handling Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly can further damage be prevented to China-US relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347362.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220914_10766027.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-14","Mao Ning","Reuters","I’d like to ask a question about a Reuters report that came out yesterday. So the United States is considering options for a sanctions package against China in order to deter it. And the European Union has come under diplomatic pressure from Taipei to do the same. This is according to sources familiar with these discussions. These are a response to fears which have grown as military tensions escalate in the…","The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the one-China principle has been challenged and the DPP authorities keep pursuing the “Taiwan-independence” separatist agenda. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. No foreign country has the right to interfere in it. Let me stress that no country or individual should underestimate the Chinese government and people’s strong resolve and firm will to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity and to realize national reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347362.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220914_10766027.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-14","Mao Ning","Reuters","This is another question regarding a Reuters report that also came out yesterday. Taiwan’s representative in Washington on Tuesday hosted international lawmakers in Washington who back sanctions on China if it continues to proceed with military drills around Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","The one-China principle is the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and other countries. China firmly opposes any form of official exchanges between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. Recently more than 170 countries and many international organizations have made their voice of justice heard. They reiterated their commitment to the one-China principle and expressed support for China’s efforts to firmly uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity. This once again shows that the one-China principle is a shared consensus of the international community.\nChina opposes all foreign interference and never accepts any threat. The DPP authorities’ attempt to collude with external forces in pursuit of the “Taiwan-independence” separatist agenda will only lead to a dead end. Only by returning to the one-China principle and the 1992 Consensus can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait be effectively ensured.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347362.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220914_10766027.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on September 14, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Now please begin asking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the mainland side held a symposium and an academic seminar marking the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus.” Under the current situation of cross-Strait relations, what is the significance of holding activities marking the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus”? What signals are being sent?","This year marks the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus,” and the mainland has held a series of commemorative events. As Wang Yang, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, pointed out, we held the symposium on the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus” to review and explain the historical context and major significance of the “1992 Consensus,” to consolidate the ideological foundation for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and, under the guidance of the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, to unite compatriots on both sides of the Strait in working together to advance the peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nThe core essence of the “1992 Consensus” is “both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national reunification.” The historic significance of the “1992 Consensus” lies in having laid the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. The “1992 Consensus” is important because it clarifies the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations: the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and the two sides are neither a relationship between two countries nor “one China, one Taiwan.”\nThe course of cross-Strait relations has repeatedly proven that the “1992 Consensus” has played an irreplaceable and important role in establishing basic mutual trust between the two sides, carrying out dialogue and consultation, and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. No matter how the situation in the Taiwan Strait changes, the “1992 Consensus” has always been the divine needle that steadies the sea in improving and developing cross-Strait relations. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will cherish and uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose and resist “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and join hands with compatriots on the mainland to build a bright future for national rejuvenation together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470172.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","We note that among the five chapters of the white paper “The Taiwan Question and China’s Cause of Reunification in the New Era,” one chapter specifically elaborates the benefits to Taiwan and the Taiwan people after peaceful reunification. What signal is this sending?","Pursuing the well-being of all Chinese people, including the vast number of Taiwan compatriots, is our unwavering original aspiration. National reunification is the future of Taiwan and the welfare of Taiwan compatriots depend on it. Achieving peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait under “one country, two systems” will bring tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. After reunification, the economic cooperation mechanisms and institutions across the Strait will be further improved, supply chains and industrial chains will be more stable and smooth, and many problems that have long troubled Taiwan’s economic development and people’s livelihoods can be solved through integrated development across the Strait, offering enormous opportunities to Taiwan compatriots. The cultural creativity of Taiwan compatriots will be fully brought into play. The social systems and ways of life of Taiwan compatriots will be fully respected, and their private property, religious beliefs, and lawful rights and interests will be fully protected. Taiwan compatriots will have greater room to develop internationally, and will be safer and more dignified.\nThe DPP authorities deliberately attack and smear “one country, two systems,” and incite so-called “fear of China and resistance to unification” and “resisting China to protect Taiwan,” purely for political self-interest. If they obstinately persist in seeking “independence” and provoking confrontation, they will push the people of Taiwan into the abyss of disaster. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots have come to understand this more and more clearly. We hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots, out of national righteousness, the future of Taiwan, and their own interests and welfare, will actively join the just cause of advancing peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470174.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Qiu Taisan, head of the MAC, recently said that “cross-Strait relations themselves are peaceful and equal, and sovereignty and democracy cannot be infringed,” that political differences should be resolved peacefully, and that “we do not accept any so-called political strategy or institutional arrangement to ‘resolve Taiwan.’” He also put forward four opinions on the grounds of easing the current situation in the…","Qiu Taisan's remarks go to great lengths to conceal the fact that the DPP authorities' “relying on the United States to pursue independence” and “resisting China to protect Taiwan” have caused tension in the Taiwan Strait. He attempts to reverse black and white, confuse right and wrong, and adopt a conciliatory posture to shift blame to the mainland and deceive the world, but this cannot hide the political nature of the DPP authorities' stubborn pursuit of “independence.” I would like to emphasize four points here.\nFirst, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. It has never been a country, so where does this so-called “sovereignty” come from? The essence of the Taiwan question is China's internal affairs, and the essence of cross-Strait relations is that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, not a relationship between two countries. This is a historical and legal fact that no person or force can change. The DPP authorities use the so-called “democracy” as a cover to package “Taiwan independence” separatist propositions, which is utterly untenable.\nSecond, we have consistently advocated achieving peaceful reunification through equal consultation. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One China principle, is the political foundation for mutual respect and equal consultation across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities deny the “1992 Consensus” and, by themselves, close the door to equal cross-Strait consultation, which shows they have no sincerity in easing the current tension in the Taiwan Strait or resolving political differences through peaceful means.\nThird, achieving reunification of the motherland through peaceful means best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. “One country, two systems” is the most inclusive solution proposed to resolve the differences in social systems and ideologies between the two sides of the Strait. It is a peaceful solution, a democratic solution, a well-intentioned solution, and a win-win solution. The specific form of implementing “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nFinally, we must point out that the DPP authorities' continued pursuit of “independence” and provocations, and external forces' intensified “using Taiwan to contain China,” are the root cause of the current tense and volatile situation in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Strait. I solemnly warn the DPP authorities that pursuing “independence” and provoking confrontation is a dead end, and “relying on foreign powers to bolster oneself” is self-destruction. Only by returning to the One China principle and the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations improve and develop, and can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470173.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Cross-Strait civil exchange activities have been colorful recently. Could the spokesperson introduce the important exchange activities and highlights?","Due to factors such as the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic and interference and obstruction by the DPP authorities, cross-Strait personal exchanges have not yet returned to normal. However, civilian exchanges across the Taiwan Strait that combine online and offline formats have strong intrinsic momentum. Since the summer vacation, departments in various localities have held a series of exchange activities with rich content, diverse forms and good experiences. Some new features and highlights have emerged.\nFirst, major cross-Strait exchange events continue to play a brand-building and leading role. On July 12, the 14th Straits Forum was successfully held in Fujian. The forum continued the theme of “expanding civilian exchanges and deepening integrated development” and arranged 43 exchange activities in four sections: the forum plenary and the youth, grassroots, culture and economy sections. About 20,000 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait participated online and offline, including more than 2,000 Taiwan compatriots who took part in Fujian. On the eve of the forum, General Secretary Xi Jinping replied to the Taiwan youth attending the Straits Youth Forum. This fully reflects the Party Central Committee's warm care for Taiwan youth and gives special significance to this Straits Forum.\nSecond, cross-Strait youth have become the main force of summer exchange activities. General Secretary Xi Jinping's reply to Taiwan youth further encouraged cross-Strait youth to actively take part in various exchanges, learn from and draw on each other, and move forward together with one heart. On July 21, the 2022 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, themed “Joining Hands to Paint Youth, Striving Forward in the New Era,” was held in Beijing. The summit showcased the youthful vitality of Taiwan youth integrating into the mainland in recent years and issued the “Revival Depends on Me” initiative to cross-Strait youth friends.\nFrom late August to late September, the 2nd Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, themed “Moving Forward Together with One Heart, Youth Power,” was held in Suzhou, Nanjing, Xuzhou, Taizhou, Yancheng and other places. More than 30 events covered many fields, including cultural and creative industries, e-sports, Peking opera, poetry, calligraphy and seal carving.\nThe Guangdong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office carefully designed multiple routes for the 9th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour, including the 2nd Cross-Strait Youth Honey-Hunting Romance Tour, the Mei (Zhou) Taiwan Youth Summer Camp themed on Hakka culture study, and the “Continuing One Lineage · Gathering in Leizhou” Cross-Strait Youth Cultural Exchange Week.\nYang Minzhong, chairman of the Taiwan Bicycle Angels Association, led cross-Strait youth riders in cycling in Xiamen, Fujian and Ya'an, Sichuan. Over 10 years they cycled 12,000 kilometers, carrying the spirit of volunteerism across both sides of the Strait and witnessing the development and progress of 55 cities.\nThird, cross-Strait cultural exchange activities are rich and colorful. Localities have successively launched cross-Strait exchange activities with the theme of inheriting and promoting outstanding traditional Chinese culture, combined with local characteristics. From July 25 to 30, the “Feelings for the Three Rivers Source · Beautiful Qinghai” Cross-Strait Culture and Tourism Friendship Tour was successfully held in Qinghai. More than 150 guests from the cultural, tourism, media and art sectors on both sides of the Strait took part and discussed “poetry and distant places” together.\nFrom July 3 to 11, a photography field trip by Taiwan teachers and students along the Ancient Tea Horse Road was held in Diqing Prefecture, Yunnan Province. They used cameras to record the historical appearance and magnificent landscapes of the Ancient Tea Horse Road. From July 31 to August 7, a documentary photography exhibition of the Ancient Tea Horse Road was held in Taipei, allowing more Taiwan compatriots to learn about Yunnan, Shangri-La and the Ancient Tea Horse Road.\nIn addition, the 10th Cross-Strait Tourism and Sightseeing Seminar and Homestay Tourism Development Summit in Beijing, the 6th Cross-Strait Yue Fei Culture Summer Camp in Chongqing, the “Joining Hands, Writing Together” Cross-Strait Huzhou Brush Culture Exchange in Zhejiang, and the study camp on intangible cultural heritage for Taiwan-origin teachers and students in Guizhou all demonstrated the profound foundation of Chinese traditional culture and distinctive local characteristics, and achieved good results.\nFourth, summer internships and social practice are highly popular with Taiwan students. The Taiwan College Students' Jiangsu Internship and Employment Intensive Training Camp continued this year. 206 enterprises and institutions in 13 prefecture-level cities of Jiangsu Province and Kunshan City offered 739 internship positions covering science and technology, finance, medical services, news and media, and other fields.\nGuangdong Province held the “Dreaming on the Pearl River, Spreading Wings to Fly: 2022 Taiwan College Students Guangzhou Internship Experience Activity.” More than 150 Taiwan college students from over 30 universities in the two sides of the Strait and Macao took part. They carried out two-month internship training at nearly 50 enterprises, institutions and research institutes in industries such as financial securities, artificial intelligence, biotechnology and the internet.\nThe Higher People's Court of Hubei Province received Taiwan students from universities in Wuhan, Zhengzhou and other places this year for a two-month summer internship. Henan, Fujian, Zhejiang, Jiangxi and other places also held summer social practice activities for Taiwan students in various forms.\nIn addition, during the Mid-Autumn Festival, localities also held colorful activities. Kunshan held the 2022 Straits Cross-Strait Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival. The 2022 Beijing-Kaohsiung Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering was held simultaneously in Beijing and Kaohsiung, with more than 200 people from both sides of the Strait gathering in the cloud to recite and sing poetry together. The 4th “Colorful Yunnan, Meet in Taiwan” theme day and 2022 Mid-Autumn Tea Gathering, themed “Cross-Strait Is One Family, Yun-Tai Is One Family,” was held in Kunming, Yunnan. The 2022 Suzhou-Taiwan Youth Dating and Friendship Gathering, “Full Moon Across the Strait, Love Settled in Suzhou,” was held in Suzhou, where more than 100 single cross-Strait youths and members of cross-Strait marriage families gathered by Lake Tai to enjoy the full moon together.\nThe intrinsic driving force for the development of cross-Strait relations comes from civil society and the grassroots. We will continue to create favorable conditions for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, encourage and support all sectors of cross-Strait society in expanding and deepening exchanges, help compatriots on both sides of the Strait deepen mutual understanding and enhance mutual trust and identity, and jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation with one heart.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470169.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges have continued to be lively recently. Could the spokesperson introduce the important exchange activities and hot topics?","Under the premise of doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, relevant departments and localities have held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities that are rich in content, diverse in form, and effective, to help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises integrate into the new development pattern on the mainland and participate in the mainland's high-quality development. The main activities include: the 9th “Taiwan Businesspeople Visit Gansu” event held in Lanzhou from July 6 to 10; the promotion meeting on intelligent transformation and digital transformation of Taiwan-funded enterprises in Jiangsu, held in Kunshan on July 15; the 2022 Zhejiang-Taiwan Week held in Hangzhou on July 20; the “Policy Promotion Meeting on Supporting the Development of Taiwan Businesses and Deepening Cross-Strait Integration” and the online promotion event for the 5th China International Import Expo, held in Beijing on July 21; the 2022 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference held in Luoyang on August 26; the 13th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo held in Dongguan from September 1 to 4; the Shandong-Taiwan Economic and Trade Cooperation and Cross-Strait Empowerment for Ecological Protection and High-Quality Development in the Yellow River Basin Forum held in Weifang on September 1; and the 16th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Cooperation and Development Forum held in Xiamen on September 8. Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises eagerly took part in the activities, fully demonstrating their optimism about the mainland's development prospects and their active attitude toward participating in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nTwo large-scale cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities are also being intensively prepared this month. The 18th Jiangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation and Exchange Conference will be held in Shangrao, Jiangxi, from September 16 to 18. The 25th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum will be held simultaneously in Beijing and Taipei on September 19 and 20 in a combination of online and offline formats. Under the theme “Exploring New Paths, Integrating into New Development, and Sharing New Achievements,” the forum will focus on industries such as technological innovation, the carbon-neutral economy, financial services, and biomedicine and health, promote the implementation of cross-Strait cooperation projects, and further deepen economic cooperation between Beijing and Taiwan.\nRelevant departments and localities will do the related preparatory work under the premise of doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises to actively participate, and we also welcome media friends to follow and report on these events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470170.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The “Ten-Year Symposium on Taiwan-funded Enterprises in the Mainland” was held in Beijing on September 5. Please introduce the relevant situation. How do you evaluate the role Taiwan businesses have played over the past ten years in promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations?","The “Ten Years of Taiwan Enterprises on the Mainland” symposium, sponsored by the National Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises, was held in Beijing on September 5. Li Zhenghong, President of the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, and about 30 Taiwan business representatives from various localities attended the symposium. The symposium reviewed the brilliant achievements the mainland has made over the past decade and exchanged views on the development of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland.\nThe Taiwan business representatives at the meeting believed that over the past decade, cross-Strait relations have experienced ups and downs. From 2012 to May 2016, the Taiwan Strait was calm, and cross-Strait relations reached a new level of peaceful development. After the Democratic Progressive Party authorities took office in May 2016, the Taiwan Strait became turbulent, and the situation in cross-Strait relations became complex and grave. Taiwan business people who work hard on the mainland and travel between the two sides have reaped results and made contributions, and they especially hope that cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation can have a peaceful and stable environment. At the symposium “Ten Years of Taiwan Enterprises on the Mainland,” Li Zhenghong said: “When the mainland is good and cross-Strait relations are good, Taiwan businesses and enterprises can truly do well.”\nOver the past decade, Taiwan business people and enterprises have actively upheld and promoted the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, actively promoted cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, and are beneficiaries of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, as well as firm supporters and vigorous promoters of it. Looking ahead, the process of building a modern socialist country in all respects will bring more opportunities to Taiwan compatriots. We hope that Taiwan business people will uphold the righteousness of the nation, firmly stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, and actively devote themselves to advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the just cause of the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220914_12470171.htm"],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声记者","The “Jiangsu Province Regulations on Economic and Cultural Exchanges and Cooperation with Taiwan” were promulgated and took effect on September 1. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","Jiangsu Province has consistently attached great importance to legislation related to Taiwan. In 2012, it formulated the \"Jiangsu Province Regulations on Protecting and Promoting Investment by Taiwan Compatriots,\" and in 2020 it formulated the \"Kunshan Regulations on Deepening Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone.\" The \"Jiangsu Province Regulations on Promoting Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation with Taiwan,\" promulgated and implemented this time, is a pioneering local legislation in the national work on Taiwan affairs. Its relevant provisions make specific stipulations on promoting economic, cultural, and youth exchange and cooperation between Jiangsu and Taiwan, and on attracting Taiwan youth to develop in Jiangsu. By means of regulations, it guarantees that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Jiangsu enjoy equal treatment and share development opportunities. This is conducive to raising the level of economic and cultural exchange and cooperation between Jiangsu and Taiwan, and benefits the people of both places.\nWe encourage and support all regions and departments in actively exploring new paths for the integrated development of both sides of the Taiwan Strait, providing Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises with more equal treatment and development opportunities, and creating better conditions for them to invest, start businesses, and live and work in peace and contentment on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, many Taiwan entertainers appeared at Mid-Autumn Festival galas across the mainland, and many Taiwan residents interacted through social media while watching, expressing that “Both sides of the Strait share the same bright moon” (两岸共婵娟). What comments does the spokesperson have?","Affected by the epidemic, online exchanges have become the main form of interaction between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Thanks to the efforts of relevant parties, people on both sides have more opportunities and channels to achieve direct two-way exchanges on the same screen. This summer, we saw many people in Taiwan enjoy many online concerts by performers from both sides of the Strait on platforms such as CCTV Video, WeChat Video and Douyin, and there has been much positive interaction. We will continue to make more efforts and create more favorable conditions to further promote exchanges and cooperation between the people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","First question: Both on and off the island, people continue to pay attention to consular protection work for Taiwan compatriots involved in telecom fraud and online gambling in Cambodia. Please introduce the relevant situation. Second question: Recently, Ke Wenzhe said, “The Taiwan question should be discussed within the framework of China-US relations. Cross-Strait relations are not ‘across the Taiwan Strait’…","On the first question: since Taiwan media exposed the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ disregard for the incident in which Taiwan residents were lured to Cambodia and imprisoned and beaten, the mainland side has stepped up consular protection for Taiwan compatriots in Cambodia. Relevant units have wholeheartedly rendered assistance, maintained close communication with relevant Cambodian departments, and spared no effort to protect the safety and lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in Cambodia. It is understood that this work is ongoing, and the relevant cases are still being further investigated.\nHere we once again remind people on both sides of the Strait not to lightly believe the false “high salaries” of online gambling fraud syndicates, and not to illegally cross the border into Cambodia. If one is unfortunately trapped, the victim, family members, or informed persons should try to report to the Chinese and Cambodian police as soon as possible, or report directly to the Chinese Embassy or Consulate General in Cambodia. As we always say, compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family; if something happens abroad, call the consular protection hotline 12308.\nOn the second question: the Taiwan question is a leftover of the Chinese Civil War and an internal affair of one country, which needs to be resolved through consultation among Chinese on both sides of the Strait, and brooks no interference from external forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Please introduce the current progress of the investigation into the Yang Chih-yuan case and the relevant situation. Can he contact his family? Has the mainland notified relevant Taiwan authorities? In addition, please introduce the trial status of the cases of Li Meng-chu and others on the mainland.","It is understood that on August 3, the National Security Bureau of Wenzhou City, Zhejiang Province, in accordance with the law, placed under criminal summons review Taiwan region criminal suspect Yang Zhiyuan, who has long engaged in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and is suspected of the crimes of splitting the state and inciting to split the state. On August 4, the case-handling department changed the criminal coercive measure against him in accordance with the law, from summons to residential surveillance at a designated location. On August 5, his family was notified in accordance with the law. The National Security Bureau of Wenzhou City, Zhejiang Province, is conducting investigation in accordance with relevant national laws. The case is currently being further handled, and the case-handling department is ensuring all of the criminal suspect's lawful rights in accordance with the law.\nThe illegal facts committed by Li Mengju and others are clear, and the evidence is conclusive and sufficient. The relevant departments have strictly handled the case in accordance with the law, including ensuring all of Li Mengju and others' lawful rights during the handling of the case.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, Taipei Mayor Ko Wen-je raised the notion of “cross-Strait families are one family” again and said that people on both sides of the Strait should not hate each other. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than hostility and antagonism, are the mainstream public opinion on the island and serve the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, incite populism on the island, and stir up cross-strait confrontation. This is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","During Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Liyan's visit to the mainland at the end of August, his remarks and actions were attacked by the Green camp. How does the mainland view Xia Liyan's visit to the mainland?","The Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang maintain exchanges, enhance mutual trust, and advance cooperation on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” This has positive significance for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhancing the well-being of people on both sides of the Strait, and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It reflects the wishes and demands of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwanese businesspeople on the mainland, for peace, stability, exchanges, and development.\nAt present, the DPP authorities constantly plot “independence” and provoke confrontation, and external forces are intensifying efforts to “use Taiwan to contain China,” pushing the situation in the Taiwan Strait into tension and turmoil. We will continue to work together with all political parties, groups, and individuals on the island who care about the well-being of compatriots and are committed to developing cross-Strait relations, to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and defend the interests of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体记者","First question: Taiwan businesses are very concerned about when the “mini three links” will resume navigation, and the Kinmen County Government has been making active efforts and communication all along. Is there any new progress now? Second question: Recently the mainland suspended imports from more than 100 Taiwan food companies. When can the relevant Taiwan enterprises resume imports after rectification?","On the first question: the \"Mini Three Links\" are the most important and most convenient channel for exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, especially between Fujian and Taiwan. Residents on both sides hope the \"Mini Three Links\" will be restored as soon as possible. We hope the DPP authorities will do more things that benefit cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than going to great lengths to obstruct, restrict, and engage in political manipulation.\nOn the second question, regarding food imports: to implement the Food Safety Law and its implementing regulations and other provisions, the General Administration of Customs organized the revision of the original rules on registration management for overseas food production enterprises importing food. In April 2021 it issued the \"Provisions on Registration Management of Overseas Food Production Enterprises for Import\" (General Administration of Customs Order No. 248), which took effect on January 1, 2022. These registration management provisions optimize the registration procedures, implement classified management for different categories of overseas production enterprises, clarify the primary responsibility of enterprises and the supervisory responsibility of the competent authorities at their locations, and refine the circumstances in which the clauses apply. The relevant competent authorities have already notified the Taiwan side of relevant matters and requirements through the contact channels under the \"Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement.\" The relevant competent authorities will continue to handle matters related to the registration of Taiwan food production enterprises exporting to the mainland in accordance with the relevant provisions on registration management of overseas food production enterprises for import.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Taiwanese entertainer Yang Chenglin made remarks about her personal experiences on a mainland variety show, which led some netizens on the island to “launch a campaign” against her, and some Green camp politicians and media successively published articles attacking Yang Chenglin. We have noted that in recent years, many Taiwanese entertainers who have developed their careers on the mainland have become…","Recalling past hardships and savoring present sweetness is a sentiment that people on both sides of the Strait often feel when reflecting on their life experiences. Some DPP politicians rushed to jump on the bandwagon, using the matter to make sarcastic remarks and sensational claims, yet they have remained tight-lipped about livelihood issues that Taiwan residents care about. This shows that they can only divert attention and incite antagonism through empty talk.\nIt must be emphasized that we are thoroughly implementing measures for equal treatment and welcome and encourage Taiwan artists to come to the mainland to take part in performing arts, film and television, and cultural and creative industries. Many Taiwan performers have participated in the production of radio and television programs and have shone in major art performances, popular TV dramas and variety shows, gaining tens of millions of fans on the mainland. At the same time, they have actively assumed social responsibility, paid attention to current affairs, been enthusiastic about public welfare, and spread positive energy, which everyone fully affirms. Recently, after the earthquake disaster in Luding, Sichuan, we also saw dozens of Taiwan performers post on social media to cheer on the rescue, which are very positive phenomena.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The 59th Golden Horse Awards are expected to be held in Taipei on November 19. Taiwan media reported that the Hong Kong Film Industry Association recently sent a letter calling on its members not to register for participation. What is your comment?","We have consistently and actively supported exchange activities that promote mutual understanding and mutual recognition between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. However, activities that are given political coloring are a different matter.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","彭博社记者","The island has recently been hyping the shooting down of a mainland civilian drone. What is the spokesperson's comment?","On this issue I want to emphasize two points. First, any unit or individual taking off and landing civil small aircraft or releasing free-floating balloons in the relevant administrative areas must do so in accordance with law and regulations. Second, some people in the DPP authorities are making a mountain out of a molehill, hyping the issue to create a tense atmosphere and escalate confrontation between the two sides. It is utterly pointless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The DPP authorities' 2023 annual general budget includes so-called defense spending that is 12.9% higher than the previous year. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities, overestimating their own capabilities and attempting to seek “independence” by force, not only seriously harm the well-being of the people on the island, but also intensify cross-Strait tensions and turbulence, pushing Taiwan's people into an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","The KMT has repeatedly criticized Chen Shih-chung for having blocked the purchase of BNT vaccines. The DPP countered that the KMT is “rehashing old stories,” and said that “it was the mainland that blocked the Comirnaty vaccine from entering Taiwan.” What is your response?","On this matter, people on both sides of the Strait see it very clearly: compatriots on both sides are one family connected by blood, and we have always cared about the life, health and safety of Taiwan compatriots. Since the outbreak of the COVID-19 pandemic in January 2020, we have always made every effort to help Taiwan compatriots respond to the epidemic. Nearly 200,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland have received vaccinations, and Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises in various places have resumed production, kept production stable and reached full capacity. For masks, vaccines and rapid test reagents urgently needed by compatriots on the island, we have also promptly expressed our willingness to actively provide donations and assistance. These goodwill and sentiments have never changed.\nIn contrast, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not only place their own political and private interests above the health and safety of the people, but also, whenever matters involving the mainland are concerned, engage in political manipulation regardless of everything on the basis of their \"Taiwan independence\" nature. From blocking Taiwanese residents stranded in Hubei from returning to Taiwan, to drastically cancelling cross-strait flight routes, to banning the export of masks and medical supplies to the mainland, and then to banning the mainland from providing vaccines and antigen testing reagents to Taiwan residents and blocking relevant institutions on the island from purchasing vaccines from mainland companies, they \"oppose everything that comes from the mainland\" and are cold-blooded and heartless. They disregard basic humanitarian principles, wantonly damage the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and completely disregard the health, safety and epidemic prevention needs of Taiwan residents.\nThe relevant situations reported by Taiwanese media in the past two days are firsthand experiences of the people involved. What can be told to everyone here is that last year, when the epidemic on the island was most severe and the demand for vaccines was most urgent, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not only used all kinds of pretexts to block mainland vaccines from being shipped to Taiwan, but also set up all kinds of obstacles to certain counties and cities in Taiwan, private institutions, and related enterprises that were purchasing vaccines from Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group in accordance with commercial rules. They kept fabricating rumors, creating problems and making trouble, which caused Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Group's supply of Comirnaty vaccines to Taiwan to be delayed for several months. As for the Democratic Progressive Party's conduct, I believe the broad masses of Taiwan residents will have their own verdict.\nFinally, I would also like to say a few words about the Luding earthquake in Sichuan. At 9 September 5, a 6.8-magnitude earthquake struck Luding County, Garze Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan, causing major casualties. After the disaster occurred, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office immediately activated emergency plans related to Taiwan, promptly surveyed the disaster situation affecting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and assisted in earthquake relief work. Sectors of Taiwan society also expressed concern and condolences to the disaster area through various forms. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises eagerly donated money and goods to the disaster area, totaling nearly 9 million yuan. Many Taiwan compatriots also posted messages on social media cheering for and blessing the disaster area, and many Taiwanese young people took part in volunteer service in the disaster area. Small contributions gather into great love across the Strait, and here we express our most sincere thanks.\nOne moment was especially touching: a Taiwanese girl went from being a disaster-stricken tourist to a rescue volunteer within a single day. After escaping danger safely, she immediately and voluntarily took part in distributing supplies, logistical disinfection, cleaning and other rescue services. She said, \"How is it that such a handsome man has come in to save us?\" Here I would like to say to her, \"Thank you, such a beautiful young woman, for staying to help everyone.\"\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220914_12470167.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-09-15","Mao Ning","CCTV","President Xi Jinping made a state visit to Kazakhstan yesterday. Can you share more information on the visit?","At the invitation of President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev of the Republic of Kazakhstan, President Xi Jinping made a state visit to Kazakhstan on September 14. President Tokayev received President Xi at the airport and held a warm welcome ceremony for him. The two Presidents toured an art exhibition titled “Kazakhstan-China: A Dialogue Across Millennium”. President Xi held formal talks with President Tokayev, attended the welcoming banquet, and received the Order of the Golden Eagle, the highest order of Kazakhstan, awarded by President Tokayev.\nPresident Xi’s visit is highly productive and fruitful. The two heads of state signed and issued the Joint Statement Between the People’s Republic of China and the Republic of Kazakhstan on the 30th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, and announced that China and Kazakhstan will work for the goal and vision of building a community with a shared future defined by lasting friendship, a high degree of mutual trust and sharing weal and woe. Relevant departments of the two sides signed bilateral cooperation documents in such areas as economy and trade, connectivity, finance, water conservancy and the media. The two sides also decided to set up consulates general in Xi’an and Aktobe respectively.\nGoing forward, the two sides will continue to support each other on issues concerning each other’s core interests such as sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. The Kazakh side said it will continue to firmly support the one-China principle and oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence”.\nThe two sides will fully leverage the important role of head-of-state diplomacy in providing strategic guidance and have regular strategic communication on major issues of common interest.\nThe two sides will advance high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, and seek synergy between the Belt and Road Initiative and Kazakhstan’s new economic policy of the “Bright Road”Initiative.\nThe two sides will actively follow the new vision of common, comprehensive, cooperative and sustainable security, jointly combat terrorism, separatism and extremism, and uphold political security and the security of political authority.\nThe two sides will firmly abide by the UN Charter and principles of international law, practice true multilateralism, expand cooperation under such multilateral frameworks as the UN and the SCO, implement the Global Development Initiative and Global Security Initiative, jointly build a community with a shared future for mankind, and make our share of contribution to fostering a more equitable and reasonable global governance system.\nChina is ready to work with Kazakhstan to follow the guidance of the important common understanding reached by the two Presidents during this visit, follow the spirit of mutual respect, good neighborliness, friendship, mutual assistance, mutual benefit and win-win outcomes, and move the China-Kazakhstan relationship into the next 30 golden years.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347364.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220915_10766466.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-15","Mao Ning","The Paper","It is reported that on September 14 local time, the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee approved the Taiwan Policy Act of 2022, which now heads to the Senate floor. Do you have any comment?","The bill seriously breaches the US’s commitment to China on the Taiwan question, and violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. It constitutes an interference in China’s internal affairs, violates international law and basic norms in international relations, and sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China is firmly opposed to this and has lodged serious démarches with the US side.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China will unswervingly advance the complete reunification of the country. No country, no force and no individual should ever misestimate the firm resolve, strong will and great capability of the Chinese Government and people to defend state sovereignty and territorial integrity and to achieve national reunification and rejuvenation.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and is at the core of the three China-US joint communiqués. If the bill continues to be deliberated, pushed forward or even become law, it will greatly shake the political foundation of China-US relations and cause extremely serious consequences to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nWe strongly urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly act on the commitment made by the US leadership of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop playing the “Taiwan card” and using Taiwan to contain China, and stop advancing the deliberation of the relevant bill. China will take all necessary measures in light of the bill’s process and final outcome to firmly safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347364.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220915_10766466.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-16","Mao Ning","MASTV","Spokesperson of the Taiwan authorities said on September 15 that Taiwan will send three persons to attend the state funeral of former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe. Do you have any comment? Is China still going to send someone to attend Abe’s state funeral?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a widely accepted norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community. China urges Japan to abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and the serious political commitments it previously made, handle relevant matters in strict accordance with the one-China principle, and refrain from providing any platform or opportunity for “Taiwan independence” elements to take advantage of the occasion for political manipulation.\nAs for Japan’s invitation to China for the state funeral of former Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, China and Japan are in communication over this. I do not have any information to offer at the moment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347365.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220916_10767035.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-16","Mao Ning","Global Times","After the US announced a planned arms sale worth $1.106 billion to Taiwan on September 2, the Spokesperson for the Chinese Foreign Ministry said that China will “firmly defend our own sovereignty and security interests”. Do you have any updates about that?","US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The arms sales gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and severely harm China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns the sales.\nTo defend China’s sovereignty and security interests, the Chinese government has decided to sanction Gregory J. Hayes, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Raytheon Technologies Corporation, and Theodore Colbert III, President and Chief Executive Officer of Boeing Defense, Space & Security, who were involved in the latest arms sale.\nChina once again urges the US government and relevant parties to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to Taiwan and military contact with Taiwan, and stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will continue to take all necessary measures in light of the situation to firmly defend its own sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347365.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220916_10767035.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-16","Mao Ning","RIA Novosti","A delegation from the Czech Republic will visit Taiwan on Sunday. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. It concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and bears on China’s core interests. We firmly oppose all forms of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We firmly oppose external forces’ attempt to use the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs. The Chinese government and people have unwavering resolve and commitment to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the Czech politicians to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, refrain from sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and avoid inflicting further damage to the political foundation of the development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347365.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220916_10767035.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","The U.S. Senate Foreign Relations Committee passed the “Taiwan Policy Act” on September 14, Eastern Time, and Taiwan's media hyped it extensively. The bill will next be submitted to the full Senate for consideration, and if it passes the Senate, it will then be sent to the House of Representatives for consideration. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and tolerates no external interference. Some members of the U.S. Congress are promoting the review of the “Taiwan Policy Act.” This seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, seriously contravenes the solemn commitments of the U.S. side, and is a blatant provocation against China's sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nFrom the information that has been published, the so-called “Taiwan Policy Act” is filled with false information and provocative content. It encompasses a series of erroneous propositions put forward over a period of time by anti-China forces in the U.S. that “support Taiwan and contain China.” It attempts to “use Taiwan to contain China,” to create fundamentally destructive effects on the Taiwan question, to subvert the political foundation of China-U.S. relations, and to obstruct China's reunification and national rejuvenation.\nThe content of this bill is absurd and full of loopholes. For example, it maliciously attacks UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, advocates that the U.S. negotiate and sign a free trade agreement with the Taiwan region of China, invites Taiwan to join the “Indo-Pacific Economic Framework,” grants Taiwan “sovereign status,” and demands that Taiwan be “armed” and “jointly defended.” It is, from beginning to end, a thoroughly evil bill.\nWe advise certain members of the U.S. Congress to immediately stop erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues, abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, fulfill the U.S. government's solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately abandon the fantasy of “seeking independence by relying on the U.S.” and “seeking independence by relying on external forces.” All “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220916_12470785.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 18: Since the night of September 17, Taitung County and Hualien County in Taiwan have successively experienced magnitude 6.5 and magnitude 6.9 earthquakes and multiple aftershocks, causing property losses and casualties. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 18th that the relevant mainland authorities are highly concerned about this, expressed condolences to the families of those who died, expressed sympathy to the injured, and hope that disaster-affected residents can soon restore normal production and daily life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220918_12471121.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-09-19","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Taiwanese representative to the UK has been given a special invitation to sign the condolence book for the Queen. Is the Chinese foreign ministry OK with this?","It is rather contemptible for the DPP authorities to use the condolence arrangement for political hype and political gains. Such a move cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China and that such political schemes of the DPP authorities will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347366.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220919_10767860.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-20","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","According to reports, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi had an exchange with representatives of the National Committee on US-China Relations, the US-China Business Council and the US Chamber of Commerce, and met with former US Secretary of State Dr. Kissinger in New York on September 19 local time. Can you share more information?","On September 19 local time, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi had an exchange with representatives of the National Committee on US-China Relations, the US-China Business Council and the US Chamber of Commerce in New York.\nWang Yi pointed out that this year marks the 50th anniversary of President Richard Nixon’s visit to China and the Shanghai Communiqué. It is an important year to take stock of the past and carry on from a new starting point. But one may find less certainty and more uncertainty in the prospects of China-US relations. In that context, Wang Yi talked about the five certainties China can provide.\nFirst, China’s development prospects are certain. The upcoming 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China will lay out the blueprint and the objectives of China’s future development. A modernized China with more than 1.4 billion people approaching common prosperity will create bigger markets and development opportunities for the US and other countries.\nSecond, China’s resolve to further advance reform and opening-up is certain. China will continue to deepen reform and open up even wider, foster a new system of opening-up of higher standards, build an open world economy and continue to advance economic globalization.\nThird, China’s policy toward the US is certain. President Xi Jinping put forward the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation in developing China-US relations. President Joe Biden has reiterated the “five noes” commitment (i.e. the US does not seek a new Cold War with China, it does not aim to change China’s system, the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China, it does not support “Taiwan independence”, and it has no intention to seek a conflict with China) on many occasions. The most critical thing now is for the US to adopt a rational and practical policy toward China sooner rather than later.\nFourth, China’s commitment to closer bilateral trade and economic cooperation is certain. China welcomes US business operations in China and will continue to provide a market-oriented, world-class business environment governed by a sound legal framework. We need to have more, not less, economic and trade interactions between China and the US. We need to “join hands” with each other instead of “letting go” of each other’s hands. We need to remove barriers, not build up walls. We need dialogue and consultation, not confrontation or coercion, when it comes to each other’s concerns.\nFifth, China’s readiness to engage in multilateral consultation with the US is certain. History has proven and will continue to prove that when China and the US cooperate, the two sides can accomplish many big things that are good for the two countries and for the world. For that to happen, it is vital to protect the political foundation for China-US relations and in particular, uphold the one-China principle.\nWang Yi stressed that China-US relations bear on the future of the two countries and the peace and stability of the world. The two sides need to work together to find a way for the two major countries with different social systems, histories and cultures to get along.\nWhen meeting with former US Secretary of State Dr. Henry Kissinger, Wang Yi said that this year marks the 50th anniversary of President Richard Nixon’s visit to China and the issuance of the Shanghai Communiqué. China and the US should earnestly take stock of the useful experience in the 50 years of exchanges. China’s policy toward the US remains consistent and stable. The US, out of a wrong perception of China, insists on viewing China as its primary rival and a long-term challenge. Some people even described stories of the success of China-US exchanges as failures. This is a lack of respect for both history and these people themselves. The US needs to adopt a rational and practical policy toward China, return to the right track of the three China-US joint communiqués, and safeguard the political foundation of China-US relations.\nWang Yi stressed that the pressing task is to properly manage the Taiwan question; otherwise, it would have a disruptive impact on China-US relations. A Chinese saying goes to the effect that “To defend even an inch of land, a country will not hesitate to sacrifice thousands of troops.” The saying reflects the will and resolve of the Chinese people. If the Anti-Secession Law is violated, China will surely take firm action in accordance with the law to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Wang Yi stressed that to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, the US must return to the true meaning of the one-China principle, and unequivocally oppose and curb “Taiwan independence” activities.\nThe US participants said that as the world’s two largest economies that are interdependent, if China and the US can manage their bilateral relations well, reduce impediments and negative factors and jointly respond to climate change, public health and food and energy security challenges, people of both countries and the world at large will enjoy more benefits. The two sides need to work in a cooperative spirit and in the right direction and keep having constructive and productive dialogues at various levels. Small steps can build into major progress. The level of trust will also grow. This will contribute to world peace, stability and prosperity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347367.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220920_10768479.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-21","Wang Wenbin","Associated Press","The United States has promised greater engagement with the South Pacific, in particular, after China and Solomon Islands had signed a bilateral security treaty earlier this year. This also includes a comment by US Vice President Kamala Harris that they would open new embassies in Tonga and Kiribati. I’d like to first ask for your comments on such increased engagement in the region by the US and also Australia,…","On your first question, let me first say that Pacific Islands Countries (PICs) are independent sovereign countries and they have the right and freedom to develop friendly cooperation with other countries which should not be constrained or denied.\nSecondly, China never attaches any political strings to its friendly and cooperative ties with the PICs. Growing relations with the PICs is not about seeking a “sphere of influence” and does not target any third party. As noted by State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi during his meeting with Foreign Minister of Solomon Islands Jeremiah Manele in New York yesterday, developing countries have the right to development as much as anyone else, and their people are entitled to a happy life. China’s cooperation with the PICs is about promoting common development and improving people’s wellbeing. It is warmly welcomed by the local people.\nOn your second question, the spokesperson for the Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese PLA has issued a statement on that. According to the spokesperson, the Chinese troops tracked and monitored the US and Canadian warships the entire time and stayed on high alert at all times to resolutely counter any threat or provocation and safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and sensitive. Recently, US warships have repeatedly flexed muscles and made provocations in the Taiwan Strait under the pretext of “freedom of navigation”. The US has also been ganging up with other countries and resorting to pressure and intimidation. This is worsening the tensions and hurting the peace and stability in the region.\nWe urge the US side to clean up its act, rectify its erroneous practice and stop being a troublemaker for regional peace and stability. We also urge other countries to act prudently and not to seek to pull chestnut out of the fire.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347368.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220921_10769226.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-21","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Wenjun, Director-General of the Bureau of External Propaganda of the Publicity Department of the CPC Central Committee and Spokesperson:\nLadies and gentlemen, good morning! Welcome to the press conference of the Publicity Department of the CPC Central Committee. Today we are holding the 35th session of the press conference series “China in the Past Decade.” We have invited Mr. Chen Yuanfeng, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, to introduce the work on Taiwan and the development of cross-Strait relations since the 18th National Congress of the CPC and to answer your questions. Joining Director Chen at the press conference are: Mr. Ma Xiaoguang, Director of the Publicity Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office and its spokesperson; Mr. Qiu Kaiming, Director of the Research Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office; and Ms. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office.\nNow, we first invite Mr. Chen Yuanfeng to introduce the situation.\nChen Yuanfeng, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee:\nDear reporters, first of all, I welcome you all to this press conference on Taiwan work. On this occasion, I also thank the news media, on behalf of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, for their long-standing concern, attention and support for Taiwan work. Below, I will briefly introduce the main achievements of Taiwan work over the past decade and the important lessons they have given us.\nSince the 18th National Congress of the CPC, the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core has, taking into overall consideration the grand strategy of realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the once-in-a-century changes unfolding in the world, accurately grasped the development and changes of the situation at home and abroad, comprehensively advanced theoretical and practical innovation in Taiwan work, firmly held the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations, effectively safeguarded peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and steadily promoted the process of national reunification. General Secretary Xi Jinping has put forward a series of new concepts, new thoughts, new strategies and major policy propositions on Taiwan work, delivered a series of important expositions, and issued a series of important instructions and directives. These have formed the overall strategy of the Party for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and provided the fundamental guidelines and plan of action for doing Taiwan work well in the new era.\nOver the past ten years, cross-Strait political exchanges have achieved historic breakthroughs. We promoted the first meeting and direct dialogue between the leaders of the two sides of the Strait since 1949, raising cross-Strait exchanges and interactions to a new height and making it a new milestone in the development of cross-Strait relations. The authorities in charge of cross-Strait affairs on both sides established regular communication mechanisms on the basis of their common political foundation, and the heads of the two departments conducted mutual visits and opened a hotline.\nOver the past ten years, cross-Strait dialogue and consultation have entered a new phase. We adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” promoted inter-party exchanges between political parties on both sides of the Strait, conducted dialogue and consultation with Taiwan-related political parties, groups and individuals on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, reached multiple points of consensus and issued joint initiatives, and worked together with all sectors of Taiwan society to explore a “two systems” plan for Taiwan.\nOver the past ten years, Taiwan compatriots on the mainland have gradually enjoyed equal treatment and development opportunities. We adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, practice the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” take the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as our guiding principle, and promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. We have improved institutional arrangements and policy measures that promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We have implemented the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit, realized water supply from Fujian to Kinmen, issued Taiwan residence permits, and gradually provided Taiwan compatriots with equal treatment in studying, starting businesses, finding employment and living on the mainland, and we have continued to take the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots.\nOver the past ten years, cross-Strait trade and Taiwan business investment in the mainland have grown significantly. Cross-Strait trade volume was 160.03 billion US dollars in 2011 and increased to 328.34 billion US dollars in 2021, doubling in ten years. As of 2011, the cumulative number of Taiwan-invested projects in the mainland was 85,772; by the end of 2021, the cumulative number had reached 124,142, an increase of 44.7% over ten years. The mainland has consistently remained Taiwan’s largest export market, its largest source of trade surplus, and the largest destination of Taiwan’s overseas investment.\nOver the past ten years, personnel exchanges and exchanges across all sectors between the two sides have continued to expand. We have united the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, eliminated the interference and obstruction of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and promoted exchanges, cooperation and personnel travel between the two sides in all fields in greater depth. We have held a series of cross-Strait exchange activities such as the Straits Forum, the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum and the Straits Youth Forum, sustaining the development momentum of exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides. In 2011, there were 7.1 million cross-Strait personnel exchanges, of which 5.26 million were Taiwan compatriots visiting the mainland; in 2019, there were about 9 million cross-Strait personnel exchanges, of which more than 6 million were Taiwan compatriots visiting the mainland. Over the past three years, affected by the COVID-19 epidemic, online exchanges have become the main form of interaction between compatriots on both sides, and the number of actual participants and online reach across Taiwan’s sectors has repeatedly reached new highs.\nOver the past ten years, the trend of opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification has continued to strengthen. We firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, and effectively safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We have punished die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with the law and effectively deterred “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We have properly handled Taiwan’s external relations and consolidated and developed a международного pattern in which the international community adheres to the one-China principle.\nThe important achievements of Taiwan work over the past decade were made under the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, and by conscientiously implementing General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important expositions on Taiwan work. They are an important part of the historic achievements and historic transformations of the Party and the country’s cause. This process fully demonstrates that: Taiwan work must uphold the leadership of the Party and resolutely achieve the “Two Upholds”; it must adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus”; it must firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and never allow anyone or any force to split Taiwan from the motherland; it must firmly oppose external interference and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity; it must plan the resolution of the Taiwan question together with the realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and steadily advance the process of national reunification; it must seek well-being for all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and always strive to realize the cross-Strait compatriots’ aspiration for a good life; it must emancipate the mind, seek truth from facts, and actively promote theoretical and practical innovation in Taiwan work; it must have the courage and skill to struggle, and resolutely struggle against all forces that undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and seek to obstruct national reunification; and it must uphold great unity and broad alliances, widely mobilize all positive factors conducive to opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification, and jointly accomplish the historic mission of national reunification.\nAt present, against the backdrop of profound and complex changes in both the domestic and international situations, the advancement of complete national reunification faces new circumstances. The realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has entered an irreversible historical process. The timing, momentum and righteousness of reunification always lie on the side of the mainland. In the new era, our strength to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference is greater, and our will and determination to realize national reunification are firmer. No obstruction or sabotage by any force can change the historical trend of national reunification. We will thoroughly implement the overall strategy of the Communist Party of China for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the CPC Central Committee on Taiwan work, resolutely crush the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, steadily promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, firmly advance the process of national reunification, and unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to jointly create the glorious cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nI will stop here, and my colleagues and I are very willing to answer your questions. Thank you.\nChen Wenjun:\nThank you, Deputy Director Chen Yuanfeng. Now we welcome your questions. Before asking, please identify your news organization.\nCCTV reporter, China Media Group:\nIn the white paper “Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era” released in August this year, the implementation of “one country, two systems” in Taiwan was mentioned. May I ask, what benefits will the realization of national reunification in the manner of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” bring to Taiwan? In addition, what well-being and interests will it bring to Taiwan compatriots?\nMa Xiaoguang, Director of the Publicity Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office and spokesperson:\nI will answer your question. “Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and also the best way to realize national reunification. It embodies the Chinese wisdom of embracing diversity and tolerating differences. After peaceful reunification, the specific form of “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. “One country, two systems” is the most inclusive plan proposed to resolve the differences in social systems and ideologies between the two sides of the Strait. It is a peaceful plan, a democratic plan, a goodwill plan and a win-win plan. Achieving peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait in accordance with “one country, two systems” will bring tangible benefits to Taiwan’s economic and social development and to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nAfter cross-Strait reunification, Taiwan may practice a social system different from that of the mainland. Taiwan compatriots can live and work in a peaceful and secure state. The mainland will be in a better position to take care of Taiwan compatriots. On the premise of ensuring national sovereignty, security and development interests, the social systems and ways of life of Taiwan compatriots will be fully respected, and the private property, religious beliefs and lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots will be fully protected. All Taiwan compatriots who support the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation will truly be masters of their own affairs in Taiwan, participate in the construction of the motherland, and fully share the dividends of development.\nAfter cross-Strait reunification, economic cooperation between the two sides will be institutionalized and more fully regulated. With the mainland market as a vast hinterland, Taiwan’s economy will have greater room for development, stronger competitiveness, and more stable and smooth industrial and supply chains, and its innovative vitality will be more vibrant. Many long-standing difficulties hindering Taiwan’s development and the improvement of people’s livelihoods can be solved through integrated development and full connectivity across the two sides of the Strait. Taiwan’s fiscal revenue can be used to the greatest extent to improve people’s livelihoods, so that more practical, beneficial and problem-solving work is done for ordinary people.\nAfter cross-Strait reunification, Taiwan’s cultural creativity will be fully developed. Compatriots on both sides will jointly inherit Chinese culture, carry forward the national spirit, and learn from each other to nurture future generations. Taiwan’s regional culture will flourish and shine more brightly, nourished by the roots of Chinese culture.\nAfter cross-Strait reunification, Taiwan compatriots will have greater room for development, will stand taller and with more confidence internationally, will be safer and more dignified, and will share the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nIt must be emphasized that China’s reunification will not harm the legitimate interests of any country, including its economic interests in Taiwan. It will only bring more development opportunities to all countries, inject more positive energy into the prosperity and stability of the Asia-Pacific region and the world, and make greater contributions to building a community with a shared future for mankind and to the cause of world peace, development and human progress. Thank you.\nChina Daily reporter:\nRecently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have vigorously promoted the fallacy of “mutual non-subordination between the two sides of the Strait,” and the United States has continuously hollowed out and undermined the one-China principle. Under the current circumstances in cross-Strait relations, how should we understand the nature of the Taiwan question and the connotation and significance of the one-China principle? Thank you.\nQiu Kaiming, Director of the Research Bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office:\nGood morning, dear reporters. I will answer this question. The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is grave and complex. The reason is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, collude with external forces, and continuously carry out provocations aimed at seeking independence. Some forces in the United States, driven by a hegemonic mentality and Cold War thinking, have escalated their use of “Taiwan to contain China.” For this reason, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have vigorously promoted the fallacy of “mutual non-subordination between the two sides of the Strait,” and the United States has continuously hollowed out and undermined the one-China principle, in order to achieve their political aims. We must thoroughly expose them, set the record straight and restore the original face of the issue. Whether it is the fallacy of “mutual non-subordination” or the U.S. side’s hollowing out of the one-China principle, both attempt to distort the nature and status quo of the Taiwan question and to negate the one-China principle.\nThe historical and legal facts that Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times are clear. A large number of historical books and documents record the early development of Taiwan by the Chinese people, and also record that since the mid-12th century, successive Chinese central governments began to establish administration over Penghu and Taiwan and exercise administrative jurisdiction.\nThe emergence and evolution of the Taiwan question are closely linked to the destiny of the Chinese nation since modern times. After the Opium War of 1840, Western powers invaded, and China fell into a miserable state of internal turmoil and external threat, with its territory broken. Taiwan was even occupied by a foreign power for half a century. In 1943, the governments of China, the United States and the United Kingdom issued the Cairo Declaration, which clearly stipulated that Japan must return to China the Chinese territories it had stolen, including Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. In 1945, the Potsdam Proclamation reaffirmed that the terms of the Cairo Declaration would be carried out. Also in 1945, after bloody struggle, all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, achieved the great victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and Taiwan was subsequently restored and returned to the embrace of the motherland.\nOn October 1, 1949, the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the government of the Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. This was a change of regime while the subject of international law, China, remained unchanged. China’s sovereignty and inherent territory did not change, and the government of the People’s Republic of China fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. Due to the continuation of the civil war and interference by external forces, the two sides of the Taiwan Strait fell into a special state of long-term political confrontation.\nIn October 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore the lawful seat of the People’s Republic of China in the United Nations. This resolution not only thoroughly resolved the question of representation of all of China in the United Nations politically, legally and procedurally, but also clarified that China has only one seat in the United Nations and that there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” The United Nations and its specialized agencies follow the one-China principle when dealing with matters involving Taiwan. On the basis of the one-China principle, China has established diplomatic relations with 181 countries. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations generally recognized and accepted by the international community.\nRelevant historical facts, legal foundations and international realities fully prove that Taiwan is part of China, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has never changed and can never change. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China’s national sovereignty and territory have never been divided. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, out of “Taiwan independence” nature and political self-interest, disseminate and hype up fallacies such as “mutual non-subordination between the two sides of the Strait” and “the status of Taiwan is undetermined,” negate and challenge the one-China principle. This is distorting the facts and confusing the public.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference. The establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the United States was premised on the proper handling and resolution of the Taiwan question, and the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. The three China-U.S. joint communiqués clearly set forth the commitments made by the United States on the Taiwan question. In the 1972 Shanghai Communiqué, the U.S. government clearly stated that “the United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” In the 1978 Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, it clearly committed that “the United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China,” that “the American people will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan,” and that “the United States acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” However, in recent years, the United States has continuously hollowed out and undermined the one-China principle, openly violating its commitments on the one-China principle made in the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and turning back the wheel of history. We firmly oppose this. We urge the United States to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question with prudence and properness.\nAs pointed out in the white paper, the historical facts and legal facts that there is only one China and that Taiwan is part of China are indisputable, and the status of Taiwan as part of China, and never as a country, is not subject to change. Any act that distorts the facts, negates or challenges the one-China principle will end in failure. Thank you.\nPeople’s Daily reporter:\nEarlier, when Director Ma Xiaoguang introduced the white paper “Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era” released in August this year, he mentioned that “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” will bring tangible benefits to Taiwan’s economic and social development and to Taiwan compatriots. I have two questions. First, what considerations were behind the release of the white paper at this time? Second, what new formulations does the white paper contain in its policies and positions on advancing the realization of national reunification in the new era? Thank you.\nChen Yuanfeng:\nI will answer this question. Director Ma Xiaoguang has just explained the benefits that “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” can bring to Taiwan, and the white paper also elaborates on this question in some detail. After “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is realized, the “two systems” plan under which “one country, two systems” is implemented in Taiwan can be further discussed in depth with all sectors of Taiwan society.\nOn August 10, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Information Office jointly issued the white paper “Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era.” On the same day, a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee issued a statement on the white paper under authorization. Here, I would like to briefly introduce the relevant issues further.\nFirst, the release of the white paper is timely and of great significance. The Chinese government issued the white papers “The Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification” in August 1993 and “The One-China Principle and the Taiwan Issue” in February 2000, respectively, which comprehensively and systematically set out the basic policies and relevant measures for resolving the Taiwan question. Over the past more than 20 years, especially since the 18th National Congress of the CPC, the theory of national reunification and the policies on Taiwan have continuously been enriched and developed. General Secretary Xi Jinping has put forward a series of important concepts and major policy propositions on Taiwan work, forming the overall strategy of the Communist Party of China for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, which provides fundamental guidelines and a plan of action for Taiwan work. The realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation has entered an irreversible historical process, and we are better placed, more confident and more capable of completing the great cause of national reunification. However, for some time, the Taiwan authorities of the Democratic Progressive Party have intensified “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and some external forces have vigorously pursued “using Taiwan to contain China,” attempting to obstruct China from achieving complete reunification and the Chinese nation from advancing toward great rejuvenation. Faced with the new situation, it is necessary to release a new white paper on national reunification to further reaffirm the fact and status quo that Taiwan is part of China, to demonstrate the firm will and strong determination of the Communist Party of China and the Chinese people to pursue national reunification, and to elaborate on the positions and policies of the Communist Party of China and the Chinese government on advancing the realization of national reunification in the new era.\nSecond, the white paper’s content is comprehensive and systematic, with prominent highlights. Based on the overall strategy of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the once-in-a-century changes unfolding in the world, the white paper fully explains the historical context of the Taiwan question, comprehensively summarizes the struggle, major achievements and valuable experience of the Communist Party of China in advancing the complete reunification of the motherland, deeply exposes and criticizes the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ intensified provocations for “independence” and the United States’ vigorous playing of the “Taiwan card” as well as their fallacies, systematically sets out the major guidelines, policies and propositions of the Communist Party of China and the Chinese government on advancing national reunification in the new era, clearly explains the bright prospects after peaceful reunification in accordance with “one country, two systems,” and fully demonstrates our unwavering confidence in achieving complete national reunification, our firm determination to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and our unchanging original aspiration to seek well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThird, the white paper has strong practical significance for opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification. Under the complex international situation and the grave situation in the Taiwan Strait, the release of this white paper helps expose and criticize the vicious words and deeds of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces who collude and provoke, attempting to harm China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and to obstruct and sabotage the process of China’s reunification. It helps demonstrate the position and attitude of the Communist Party of China and the Chinese government of continuing to strive for peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. It helps boost the spirit and determination of the whole Party and all ethnic groups in China to pursue national reunification with resolve, and strengthens the confidence and courage of forces at home and overseas that oppose “Taiwan independence” and promote reunification, gathering the mighty power to support and promote the reunification of the motherland.\nFourth, the white paper helps unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, compatriots from Hong Kong and Macao, and overseas Chinese to jointly devote themselves to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great cause of peaceful reunification of the motherland. Achieving peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait is a blessing not only for the Chinese nation and the Chinese people, but also for the international community and the people of the world. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will firmly stand on the right side of history, think carefully about Taiwan’s position and role in the rejuvenation of the nation, and actively participate in the just cause of promoting the peaceful reunification of the motherland. We hope that compatriots in Hong Kong, compatriots in Macao and overseas Chinese will again make new contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the realization of peaceful reunification of the motherland. We hope that the international community will abide by the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and understand and support the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving to complete national reunification. Thank you.\nETtoday reporter, Eastern Multimedia, Taiwan:\nMay I ask, what progress has been made in exchanges and cooperation in various civil fields and in personnel exchanges across the two sides of the Strait in recent years? And how can the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic on cross-Strait exchanges be alleviated? In addition, we have also noticed that more and more young people from Taiwan are going to the mainland to study and work. What work has been done to attract young people from Taiwan to develop on the mainland? Thank you.\nZhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee:\nThank you for your attention to grassroots people and young people on both sides of the Strait. Indeed, the internal driving force for the development of cross-Strait relations comes from civil society and young people. Since the 18th National Congress of the CPC, we, together with localities and departments, have earnestly implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important instructions and the decisions and arrangements of the CPC Central Committee, continuously expanded exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, enhanced the family ties and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and added powerful internal impetus to the development of cross-Strait relations. We have summarized it, and it is mainly reflected in four aspects:\nFirst, the concept that compatriots on both sides should exchange, cooperate and develop together has taken root deeply in people’s hearts, and the broad pattern of large-scale cross-Strait exchanges is solid and stable. Cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields have continued to expand, forming an all-round, multi-level pattern of exchange. In 2015, the policy of visa-free travel for Taiwan compatriots to the mainland was implemented, and the card-format Taiwan compatriot permit was fully introduced, further facilitating travel for Taiwan compatriots between the two sides, and reaching a peak of 9.85 million person-times that year. Since 2020, affected by the COVID-19 epidemic and by political obstacles set up by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, online exchanges have become the main form of interaction between compatriots on both sides, and all sectors on both sides have carried out nearly a thousand exchange activities each year through a combination of online and offline methods.\nSecond, the policies of equal treatment have been continuously deepened and refined, helping more Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams. We, together with localities and departments, have successively introduced a series of policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots, providing Taiwan compatriots with development opportunities on the mainland and implementing equal treatment, including issuing Taiwan residence permits, abolishing the Taiwan residents’ employment permit, expanding pilot programs for Taiwan compatriots to work in public institutions, expanding enrollment for Taiwan students, safeguarding Taiwan compatriots’ participation in professional qualification examinations and social insurance on the mainland, and providing free COVID-19 vaccination for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland.\nMore and more Taiwan compatriots are now finding stages for development on the mainland. We have established a total of 78 cross-Strait youth employme","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220921_12471899.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-09-22","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","During a hearing before the US House Financial Services Committee on Wednesday, Republican congressman Blaine Luetkemeyer pressed US banking chief executives on how they would respond in the hypothetical event of a Chinese invasion of Taiwan. The chief executives all said they would follow US government guidance suggesting a reduced or even removal of their bank’s presence in the Chinese market. Does the foreign…","The Taiwan question has always been the most central and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The US side needs to abide by the one-China principle and provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly follow through on the US leader’s statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, and stop manipulating Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347369.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220922_10769846.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-22","Zhao Lijian","AFP","President Joe Biden in his speech at the UN General Assembly yesterday said he does not wish to seek a Cold War, nor does he wish to seek a conflict with China and he also mentioned China several other times, including in relation to the UN Xinjiang report. What’s China’s response?","China’s policy on the US has shown continuity and certainty. President Xi Jinping proposed that China and the US follow the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation. They not only embody the experience that China-US relations have gained over the past 50 years, but also constitute the basic principle that both sides need to follow in order to keep bilateral ties on the right course. President Biden has made the “five-noes” commitment on many occasions. We hope that the US side will act on the statements made by the US leader, view China and China-US relations from the right perspective, return to the three China-US joint communiqués, which are of fundamental importance to the bilateral relationship, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, and uphold the political foundation of China-US relations.\nWe hope that the US will work with China to find a way for the two major countries with different social systems, histories and cultures to get along and cooperate for win-win results. This will not only benefit the people of the two countries, but also contribute to world peace, stability and development.\nOn your second question about Xinjiang, the so-called assessment of the human rights condition in Xinjiang released by the OHCHR is orchestrated and produced by the US and some Western forces and is completely illegal, null and void. It is a patchwork of disinformation that serves as a political tool for the US and some Western forces to strategically use Xinjiang to contain China.\nIn recent years, nearly 100 countries, including Muslim countries, have spoken out at the Human Rights Council, the Third Committee of the UN General Assembly and on other public occasions to support China’s justified position on issues including Xinjiang and oppose interference in China’s internal affairs in the name of so-called Xinjiang-related issues. They are the mainstream of the international community. The US and some Western forces seek to destabilize Xinjiang and use it to contain China. Their unjust, pernicious political agenda will not have people’s support and will only fail.\nThe US side should face up to and address its own human rights issues such as racial discrimination, gun violence, violations of the Indigenous people’s rights, violations of immigrants’ rights, human trafficking, disinformation campaign, and indiscriminate unilateral sanctions. It should deliver a responsible account to the international community and the victims.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347369.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220922_10769846.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-22","Zhao Lijian","Kyodo News","Tsai Ing-wen today met with a delegation of Czech Senators, and the two sides agreed to deepen their relations. What is China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. It concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and bears on China’s core interests. We firmly oppose all forms of official interactions between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We firmly oppose external forces’ attempt to use the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs. The Chinese government and people have the unwavering resolve and conviction to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the relevant Czech politicians to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, refrain from sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and avoid inflicting further damage on the political foundation of the development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347369.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220922_10769846.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-23","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","According to reports, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi delivered a speech at the headquarters of Asia Society in New York on September 22. Can you share some information?","On September 22 local time, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi delivered a speech at the headquarters of Asia Society in New York. State Councilor Wang Yi pointed out that, the past few years have seen China-US relations at a low ebb since the establishment of diplomatic ties. This is bringing tremendous uncertainty to the future of our peoples and to countries across the world. It boils down to how the United States perceives China, the world and itself. Be it full confrontation or strategic competition, both have deviated from the right course of China-US relations. Regarding the right way for China and the US to get on with each other, President Xi Jinping has given a clear answer. That is mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation. These three principles are an important conclusion informed by the evolution of China-US relations over the past 50-odd years. They are also the right way for major countries to live with each other in this era.\nState Councilor Wang Yi said, that China and the US need to respect each other is an important lesson drawn from past exchanges between our two countries, and also a basic prerequisite for the bilateral ties to return to the right track. China respects the development path chosen by the American people. We welcome an open and confident United States that enjoys growth and progress. The US should also respect the Chinese people’s choice of development path, i.e., socialism with Chinese characteristics. China will unswervingly follow its chosen path and direction, and will forge ahead steadily along this path toward greater success. China will continue to draw upon the valuable experience of other countries and achievements of all civilizations, embrace the world with open arms and open its door even wider.\nPartner or rival? Cooperation or confrontation? These are questions of fundamental importance in China-US relations, and no catastrophic mistakes could be made, State Councilor Wang Yi noted. China chooses peace and commits to peaceful development. Our most basic expectation for China-US relations is for the two countries to live with each other in peace. Expansion, coercion and hegemony are never in the veins of the Chinese people. Today’s China is built on the heritage of ancient China. The CPC, China’s governing party, has incorporated peaceful development into its constitution, and China is the only major country that has codified peaceful development in the Constitution. Some in the US try to take China down by repeating the containment tactic used on the former Soviet Union, and hope to encircle China through geopolitical maneuvering like the Indo-Pacific strategy. Such attempts will only prove futile.\nState Councilor Wang Yi said, win-win cooperation is not only possible, but also a must. This is the true narrative of China-US relations in the past half a century, and it should remain the goal we both pursue. As the world’s largest developing and developed countries, China and the United States have a lot to offer each other. We enjoy broad room for cooperation in a wide range of areas covering economy and trade, energy, science and technology, education, and people-to-people and cultural exchanges. We shoulder important responsibilities in addressing global issues like COVID-19, economic recovery, climate change, terrorism, proliferation and regional hotspots. An unfailing truth in China-US interactions is that we both stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. Cooperation is our best choice. Undeniably, China and the US have competition in areas like economy and trade, and China does not fear such competition. However, we do not agree that China-US relations should be simply defined by competition, because this is not the entirety or the mainstream of this relationship. At the same time, competition should have boundaries and, more importantly, be fair play. We need healthy competition that brings out the best in each other, not vicious competition that aims at each other’s demise.\nState Councilor Wang Yi stressed that the one-China principle is the cornerstone of the political foundation for China-US relations; the three China-US joint communiqués are the most crucial “guardrails” for our relations. As things stand, the Taiwan question is growing into the biggest risk in China-US relations. Should it be mishandled, it is most likely to devastate our bilateral ties. Just as the US will not allow Hawaii to be split away, China has the right to uphold the unification of the country as Taiwan is part of China. Since the Government of the People’s Republic of China is recognized as the sole legal government representing the whole of China, Taiwan should not be allowed to join any international organization with sovereign implications. If one recognizes the one-China principle, one should not engage in any official interactions with Taiwan. The logic here cannot be simpler. The Taiwan question arose as a result of weakness and chaos in the nation, and it will be resolved as national rejuvenation becomes a reality. Reunification is the trend of history and the aspiration of the people. The US should choose to stand on the right side of history.\nIt is our hope that China and the US will draw on past experience to find inspiration for the present, and gain strength for going forward. Together, let us explore a way to a China-US relationship for the new era and create a better future for both of our countries!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347370.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220923_10770565.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-23","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock said in a statement released on September 22 that in their meeting, the G7 Foreign Ministers and the High Representative of the European Union said that they opposed unilateral changes to the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and that there is no change in the basic positions of G7 members on Taiwan, including stated one China policies. Do you have any comment?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s state sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been split. This is the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and one China is at the heart of this status quo. The one who is trying to change the status quo is not China, but rather the DPP authorities and the external meddling forces who have been emboldening “Taiwan independence” separatist elements. The one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The clearer and stronger the commitment of the international community is to the one-China principle, the more likely peace across the Taiwan Strait will be ensured. We hope Germany and other G7 members will not only unequivocally commit to the one-China principle, but also follow the principle with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347370.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220923_10770565.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-26","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi delivered a statement at the General Debate of the 77th Session of the United Nations General Assembly on September 24. Could you share more information on that?","On September 24 local time, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended and addressed the General Debate of the 77th Session of the United Nations General Assembly at the UN headquarters in New York. He put forward a series of propositions on the current international landscape and joint efforts to build a community with a shared future for mankind, which can be summarized as the following “six dos and six don’ts”:\nFirst, we must uphold peace and oppose war and turbulence. We should remain committed to addressing differences through peaceful means and resolving disputes through dialogue and consultation.\nSecond, we must pursue development and eliminate poverty. We should place development at the center of the international agenda and see that everyone in every country benefits more from the fruits of development in a more equitable way.\nThird, we must remain open and oppose exclusion. We should stay true to openness and inclusiveness, uphold the multilateral trading system with the WTO at its core and endeavor to build an open world economy.\nFourth, we must stay engaged in cooperation and oppose confrontation. We should engage in dialogue, consultation and win-win cooperation, and reject conflict, coercion and zero-sum game. We should jointly oppose group politics and bloc confrontation.\nFifth, we must strengthen solidarity and oppose division. We should stand against drawing lines on ideological grounds and work together to expand common ground and convergence of interests to promote world peace and development.\nSixth, we must uphold equity and oppose bullying. We should promote and practice true multilateralism, promote equality of all countries in terms of rights, rules and opportunities, and build a new type of international relations featuring mutual respect, equity and justice, and win-win cooperation.\nState Councilor Wang Yi said that in response to various challenges, President Xi Jinping proposed the Global Development Initiative, which is a rallying call to refocus attention on development and build a global community of development. President Xi Jinping also proposed the Global Security Initiative, contributing China’s vision to reducing the peace deficit and providing China’s input to meeting global security challenges.\nState Councilor Wang Yi stressed that the one-China principle has become a basic norm in international relations and a general consensus of the international community. China will continue to endeavor to achieve peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and greatest efforts. To realize this goal, we must combat “Taiwan independence” separatist activities with the firmest resolve and take the most forceful steps to repulse interference by external groups. Only by resolutely forestalling in accordance with the law separatist activities can we forge a true foundation for peaceful reunification. Only when China is completely reunified can there be enduring peace across the Taiwan Strait. Any scheme to interfere in China’s internal affairs is bound to meet the strong opposition of all us Chinese, and any move to obstruct China’s cause of reunification is bound to be crushed by the wheels of history.\nState Councilor Wang Yi pointed out that as China has one-fifth of the global population, its march toward modernization has important, far-reaching significance for the world. The upcoming 20th National Congress of the CPC will, in response to the expectation of all the Chinese people, set well-conceived goals and tasks for China’s development in the next five years and beyond, and it will draw an overarching plan for China’s future development. Having reached a new historical starting point, China will follow the Chinese path to modernization to achieve the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. China will work with other countries to make every effort for peace and development, shoulder the responsibility for solidarity and progress, build a community with a shared future for mankind, and embrace an even better world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220926_10771881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-26","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","In an address at the General Debate of the 77th Session of the UN General Assembly on September 23, Solomon Islands Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare said that Solomon Islands has been subjected to a barrage of unwarranted and misplaced criticisms in the media since formalizing diplomatic relations with the People’s Republic of China. He also called on all countries not to inflame tensions in the Taiwan Strait and…","Prime Minister Sogavare’s compelling statement is a firm rejection of the groundless criticisms and accusations against the relations between China and Solomon Islands. He defended the two countries’ legitimate right to normal exchanges and cooperation and spoke out for justice regarding the situation in the Taiwan Strait and the situation in the region and around the world. China highly commends his statement.\nDuring the General Debate of the 77th Session of the UN General Assembly, many countries reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle. This once again shows that the one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a basic norm in international relations.\nChina is committed to growing friendly cooperative ties with Solomon Islands in line with the principles of mutual respect, equality, win-win results and openness and inclusiveness. We will always remain a good friend and partner whom Solomon Islands can trust and support the country as always in pursuing an independent development path that suits its national reality.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220926_10771881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-26","Wang Wenbin","ANZA","Italy just held its general elections last weekend. The center - right coalition is going to get a solid majority. The leader of Brothers of Italy Giorgia Meloni, who is expected to be the next Italian Prime Minister, criticized China a few days ago on some kind of policies, for example, the ones related to Taiwan. What are the Chinese expectations about bilateral relations?","We have noted what came of Italy’s parliamentary election. China and Italy are comprehensive strategic partners. A sound and steady development of bilateral relations meets the shared interest of both sides. We hope the new Italian government will continue to follow a positive and practical China policy, work with China, uphold the spirit of mutual respect, mutual trust and mutual benefit and keep deepening bilateral cooperation and people-to-people exchange in various areas for the benefit of the two countries and the two peoples.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. The one-China principle is an established international consensus and a basic norm of international relations. It is the political prerequisite and foundation for Italy and other countries to establish and develop diplomatic relations with China. China urges certain individuals in Italy to fully recognize the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle, and avoid sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220926_10771881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-27","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","US Vice President Kamala Harris met with Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Tokyo. They discussed China’s recent aggressive and irresponsible provocations in the Taiwan Strait, and reaffirmed the importance of preserving peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any comment on this?","The US House Speaker, in disregard of China’s four-month-long dissuasion, made a provocative visit to China’s Taiwan region and referred to Taiwan as a “country”. What the US side has done seriously violates China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, hurts China-US relations and undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. As a response, China took countermeasures that are legitimate, lawful, proportionate and necessary.\nWhat constitute the biggest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait at the moment are the DPP authorities’ provocations aimed at “Taiwan independence” and the connivance and support they have received from external forces. The one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The clearer and stronger the commitment of the international community is to the one-China principle, the more likely peace across the Taiwan Strait will be ensured. We urge the US side to return to the three China-US Joint Communiqués and the one-China principle in their true and original form, reaffirm its commitment to the one-China policy in the simple and straightforward way, and state its opposition to all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities with absolute clarity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347372.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220927_10772591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-27","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Former US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo is in Taiwan today. Do you have a comment on this?","You mentioned a former politician of diminished credibility who staged these stunts for personal political gains. His calculations will not materialize.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347372.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220927_10772591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-27","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","The state funeral for Japan’s former Prime Minister Shinzo Abe was held today in Japan. Besides the representative of the Chinese side, the representative of the Taiwan region was also invited to lay flowers at the funeral. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a widely accepted norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community. Japan needs to observe the principles set out in the four China-Japan political documents and the solemn commitments it has made, handle the relevant matters in strict accordance with the one-Chine principle and refrain from providing any platform or opportunity for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to engage in political manipulation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347372.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220927_10772591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-28","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","US Vice President Kamala Harris said in a speech today that Washington will continue to deepen its unofficial ties with Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","I noted that Vice President Kamala Harris also said in Japan that China is undermining the international rules-based order.\nLet me stress first that the US House Speaker, in disregard of China’s four-month-long dissuasion, made a provocative visit to China’s Taiwan region and referred to Taiwan as a “country”. This has seriously violated China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, hampered China-US relations and undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community and a basic norm in international relations. It is also the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic ties between China and the US. In the Shanghai Communiqué of 1972, the China-US Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations of 1978 and the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, the US made clear that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China and that the US recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The US also stated clearly that it has no intention of infringing on Chinese sovereignty and territorial integrity, or interfering in China’s internal affairs, or pursuing a policy of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”.\nSpeaking of rules, keeping one’s commitment is the most basic rule. If the US cannot even keep its own word, in what position is it to talk about rules and order? A country like that could only become a disruptor of international rules. We urge the US to faithfully honor its commitments and return to the three China-US Joint Communiqués and the one-China principle in their true and original form, reaffirm its commitment to the one-China policy in the simple and straightforward way, and state its opposition to all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities with absolute clarity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347373.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220928_10773313.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-09-28","Wang Wenbin","AFP","China told the United Nations Security Council on Tuesday that Ukraine’s territorial integrity should be respected, stopping short of explicitly condemning Russia. Why? Will this send a wrong signal to separatists in other parts of the world, especially in the Taiwan region?","Let me first reiterate China’s consistent and clear position on the Ukraine issue. We believe that the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all countries must be respected, that the purposes and principles of the UN Charter must be observed, that the legitimate security concerns of all countries must be taken seriously, and that all efforts conducive to peaceful settlement of the crisis must be supported. As a responsible major country, China has all along been committed to promoting peace talks. We are never a bystander, and we would never add fuel to the fire, still less exploit the crisis. We will always stand on the side of peace and will continue to play a constructive part in deescalating the situation.\nTurning to your question, I need to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. The Taiwan question and the Ukraine issue are different in nature and are not comparable at all. The future of Taiwan can only be jointly decided by all Chinese people including our compatriots in Taiwan.\nAnyone who seeks to insinuate relevance of the Ukraine issue to the Taiwan question is invariably driven by political calculations. Such insinuation would constitute a violation of the principle of respecting a country’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and serious interference in China’s internal affairs. Anyone hoping to exploit the Ukraine issue and find a pretext for “Taiwan independence” will only end up nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347373.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202209/t20220928_10773313.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on September 28, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's Taiwan Affairs Office regular press conference. Now let's begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The book “The Communist Party of China and the Reunification of the Motherland” was recently officially published. What considerations led the Central Taiwan Affairs Office to organize its compilation?","Recently, the book \"The Communist Party of China and the Reunification of the Motherland,\" compiled under the organization of the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee, was published and distributed by People's Publishing House and Jiuzhou Press. The book fully displays the glorious course, major achievements, and valuable experience of the Communist Party of China's unremitting struggle over the past century to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve the reunification of the motherland. It shows the core leading role played by the Communist Party of China in pursuing national reunification in various periods, highlights the sincere sentiment of the Communist Party of China wholeheartedly seeking well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and reveals the historical law and bright prospects that the motherland must and will be reunified.\nReading this book can help compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait systematically and deeply understand the Taiwan question and the development of cross-Strait relations. It also helps cadres and the masses comprehensively and accurately understand and implement the Party Central Committee's policies on Taiwan, and contribute to promoting cross-Strait relations of peaceful development and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, while working diligently to do well in Taiwan affairs work in the new era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473878.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, earthquakes of magnitude 6.5 and 6.9 occurred successively in Taitung and Hualien, Taiwan, and the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed condolences. Earlier, when an earthquake struck Luding, Sichuan, various sectors in Taiwan also promptly expressed condolences and provided assistance. May I ask how the spokesperson views this situation in which compatriots on both sides of the Strait…","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are blood-related brothers and sisters, a community with a shared destiny. In the face of major natural disasters and emergency accidents, compatriots on both sides stand together in adversity, look out for one another, and lend each other a helping hand.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping has paid close attention to major natural disasters and emergency accidents on the island and has been deeply concerned about the life and property safety of compatriots on both sides. After the TransAsia Airways crash in Taiwan in July 2014, the gas explosion in Kaohsiung in August 2014, the magnitude 6.7 earthquake in southern Taiwan in February 2016, and the derailment of the \"Taroko Express\" train of Taiwan Railways in April 2021, General Secretary Xi Jinping immediately expressed condolences to the compatriots who died and sincere sympathy to their families and to the injured compatriots. Relevant departments on the mainland actively organized donations of money and goods. When major natural disasters have occurred on the mainland, compatriots in Taiwan have also actively lent a helping hand. After strong earthquakes struck Lushan County in Sichuan Province in April 2013 and Luding County in Sichuan Province in August 2022, all sectors of Taiwan society continued to pay close attention, generously opening their wallets and donating money and goods.\nWhen vessels on both sides of the Taiwan Strait or in its surrounding waters encountered danger during operations, passing vessels from both sides and maritime search and rescue agencies actively took part in rescue efforts and made every effort to search and rescue.\nWe have also consistently attached great importance to, and actively acted on, the safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. From providing consular document services, to assisting in handling civil disputes, economic cases and criminal cases involving Taiwan in foreign countries, to evacuating citizens during major emergencies, we have provided timely assistance. Whenever Taiwan compatriots overseas encounter any difficulties, they can promptly contact Chinese embassies and consulates abroad for help.\nIn the nearly three years since the outbreak of COVID-19, we have practiced the concept that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,\" earnestly safeguarded the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and made every effort to do well in epidemic prevention and control involving Taiwan. We have continuously notified Taiwan's disease control authorities of epidemic information and shared technical materials, and we have helped more than a thousand Taiwan compatriots stranded in Hubei return home as soon as possible. We have actively and orderly arranged free vaccinations for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. As of August 31, 198,000 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland had been vaccinated, with a cumulative total of 470,000 doses administered. We have introduced a series of policy measures to help Taiwan-funded enterprises in various places resume work and production. When vaccines and antigen test kits were in severe shortage on the island, relevant parties and social sectors on the mainland expressed concern at the first opportunity and actively provided assistance. Mainland enterprises and civil organizations have donated and provided large quantities of vaccines, test kits and urgently needed medical equipment to compatriots in Taiwan.\nThe facts prove that the deeper the friendship of \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family\" is, the more it can bring hope and comfort to compatriots on both sides in times of difficulty and crisis, and the more courage and strength it brings for overcoming hardship together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473875.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwanese girl Lai Lai recently said on social media that, with help from netizens and clansmen, she found her ancestral home in Pinghe County, Zhangzhou, Fujian. This wondrous roots-seeking journey has drawn attention and support from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. What comment does the spokesperson have on the growing number of Taiwan compatriots seeking their roots on the mainland?","We have also noticed the relevant news. First, congratulations to Lai Lai on successfully finding the roots of his family. A thread that had been broken for more than three hundred years was reconnected in an instant, and this feeling is indeed very wonderful. On behalf of the fellow villagers of Xintian Village, Banzai Town, Pinghe County, Zhangzhou City, Fujian Province, we welcome Lai Lai's family members and clansmen in Taiwan to return to their ancestral home to worship their ancestors and seek their roots when convenient. We also greatly appreciate the enthusiastic assistance and hospitality that netizens and the fellow villagers of Xintian Village have extended to Lai Lai, which together have created a moving story of 'compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, reunited at the Mid-Autumn Festival.'\nHonoring one's ancestors with care and remembering the past, and promoting harmony among clans and kin, are fine traditions of the Chinese nation. Since the long-term isolation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait was broken at the end of 1987, compatriots from Taiwan have returned to the mainland in various ways to seek their roots and visit relatives, and in recent years many young people from Taiwan have been willing to return to their ancestral homelands to trace their origins. The song 'We Sing the Same Song,' which spread widely online at the beginning of this year, was inspired by the story of three Taiwanese siblings studying at Peking University who, last summer, relied on 'half a genealogy' to return to Putian, Fujian, to seek their roots. Over the years, Taiwan Affairs Offices and relevant departments across the mainland have actively created conditions and provided various forms of assistance for Taiwan compatriots returning to their hometowns to seek roots and relatives. In recent years, with the help of internet technology, it has become more convenient and faster for Taiwan compatriots to return home and search for relatives. For example, the Toutiao 'Cross-Strait Relative Search' project, jointly with media and public welfare organizations from both sides of the Strait, has helped Taiwan compatriots realize their wishes to find relatives and roots. Over the past four and a half years, it has witnessed the reunion of 377 cross-Strait families. Among them, the oldest veteran was 100 years old and had lost contact with his relatives in his hometown for 85 years; the fastest case saw a family successfully located just 15 minutes after the information was published.\nThe root-seeking efforts of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots demonstrate a most basic fact: compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture, and are one family connected by blood. Our shared national and cultural identity is an innate gene that withstands the trials of time, and no person or force can change it. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to return to their ancestral homelands to take a look and see, and, like Lai Lai, to embark on a wonderful journey to seek their roots, to understand their family history and feel a sense of spiritual roots and belonging.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473873.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The MAC commissioned island scholars to prepare a report on the mainland's “overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era under the leadership of the Party,” which states: “In the future, the CCP will focus its Taiwan policy on ‘military intimidation’ and integrated development, deter the international community from getting involved, intensify anti-‘independence’ legal warfare, public opinion…","Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is an unwavering historic mission of the Communist Party of China. Our Party has long engaged in unremitting struggle for this goal, formulating and implementing policies toward Taiwan in keeping with the times, which has effectively promoted the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and advanced the process of national reunification. Since 2016, the DPP authorities have intensified \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, and some external forces have vigorously pursued \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" attempting to block China from achieving complete reunification and the Chinese nation from advancing toward great rejuvenation. To defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, we have taken resolute and forceful measures to oppose and curb \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct and external interference. This is entirely a just and legitimate act.\nThe DPP authorities distort facts and confuse public perception, smearing and slandering the mainland's policies toward Taiwan, but this cannot conceal their evil intention of plotting \"independence,\" provoking confrontation, and splitting the country.\nWe will thoroughly implement the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work. We will resolutely crush the schemes of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, solidly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, steadfastly advance the process of national reunification, and unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to jointly create the glorious cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473876.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The ceremony for worshipping Xuanyuan Huangdi at Zhongguo Xiandu is about to be held in the Year of Renyin, and Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province has also successively held three cross-Strait exchange and cooperation events. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly worship Huangdi, the Yellow Emperor, the human ancestor of the Chinese nation, and jointly inherit and promote Yellow Emperor culture. This helps enhance the cultural, ethnic and national identity of Taiwan compatriots and gathers the spiritual momentum for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. The Renyin Year Ceremony of Worshipping Xuanyuan Huangdi at Zhongguo Xiandu in Zhejiang will be held in Jinyun County, Lishui, Zhejiang, on October 4, 2022 (Double Ninth Festival). Jinyun's worship of the Yellow Emperor began in the Eastern Jin Dynasty, flourished in the Tang and Song dynasties, and has continued to the present. This year's Jinyun Ceremony of Worshipping Xuanyuan Huangdi takes the theme “Compatriots from Four Seas United in Honoring the Ancestor, ‘Two Pioneering Roles’ Opening a New Chapter.” More than 300 representatives from compatriots on both sides of the Strait, overseas Chinese and all sectors of society will attend, including nearly 100 Taiwan compatriots. During the event, eight sub-events will also be held, including the Fifth Yellow Emperor Culture Seminar, cross-Strait cultural exchange activities, the joint worship of Xuanyuan Huangdi by compatriots at home and abroad, and a series of Yellow Emperor culture performances. We warmly welcome compatriots both on and off the island to take part in related activities in various forms.\nRecently, Kunshan City in Jiangsu Province has also successively held three cross-Strait exchange events: the launch of the 10th Cross-Strait (Kunshan-Taiwan) Cultural Exchange Month and the opening of the “Baodao Yicun” cultural, tourism and commercial street at Kunshan Huiju Square; the 2022 Cross-Strait Industrial Internet Integrated Development Seminar; and the 2022 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival themed “Blossoms on One Stem, Lanterns Shining Across the Strait.” Efforts are being made to build an influential Taiwan-featured cultural district in the Yangtze River Delta, a landmark of Kunshan's urban night economy, and a new retail experience zone in the digital economy. The city released the 2022 “Cross-Strait Industrial Internet Innovative Development Case Collection,” and displayed scenes combining traditional lanterns with digital technology in four lantern areas: Huiju Square, Zhouzhuang, Dianshan Lake and Jinxi. These reflect the traditional cultural concept that has been passed down across both sides of the Strait and showcase the achievements of the integrated development of the Kunshan Tourism Resort and the Jin-Dian-Zhou region. Some events will continue into early October, and cross-Strait residents are welcome to take part actively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","The Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office recently released the handbook “Hundred Questions for Taiwan Compatriots” and organized a series of activities to serve Taiwan compatriots. The Guangdong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office also recently issued the “2022 Guide to Procedures for Guangdong Province's Policy Measures Benefiting Taiwan.” Please introduce the relevant situation.","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,3,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473874.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","On the 22nd, Taiwan’s “Executive Yuan” announced that its “0+7” epidemic prevention measures, under which entrants are not subject to home quarantine and self-manage their epidemic prevention for 7 days, are expected to be officially implemented starting October 13. Penghu, Kinmen and Lienchiang counties recently reached a consensus, demanding that the DPP authorities not practice differential treatment and…","We have consistently held that, on the premise of doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, personnel exchanges and interactions across the Taiwan Strait should return to normal, which is the common expectation of people on both sides of the Strait. In the adjusted entry control measures recently announced by Taiwan, many restrictions are still imposed on personnel from the mainland and Hong Kong and Macao. This is obviously a double standard, and it continues to obstruct mainland residents from visiting Taiwan.\n“Small Three Links” is the most important and convenient channel for exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, especially for the people of Fujian and Taiwan. Residents on both sides hope to restore the “Small Three Links” as soon as possible. We hope the DPP authorities will do more things that are beneficial to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than trying every means to obstruct and restrict, and engaging in political manipulation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","Recently, the giant panda “Tuan Tuan,” gifted from the mainland to Taiwan, was suspected of having an epileptic seizure, drawing attention from netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The Taipei Zoo’s conservation team said it has maintained professional communication channels with the Sichuan Giant Panda Base, and the expert team also said it does not rule out inviting mainland experts to Taiwan for a…","On September 22, the Taipei Zoo informed the mainland’s Giant Panda Protection and Research Center of the recent physical condition of giant panda “Tuantuan.” Experts on the mainland are deeply concerned and have expressed willingness to provide technical support and assistance within their professional field.\nSince “Tuantuan” and “Yuanyuan” settled at the Taipei Zoo in 2008, they have been deeply loved by Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan’s children. Through the joint efforts of experts from both sides of the Strait, “Tuantuan” and “Yuanyuan” successfully gave birth to cubs “Yuanzai” in 2013 and “Yuanbao” in 2020 respectively, forming a happy little family. Like everyone, we hope that “Tuantuan” recovers soon and continues to accompany the friends in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473870.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Is it possible for the mainland to arrange professionals from the Giant Panda Protection and Research Center to come to Taiwan to assist in the treatment of “Tuan Tuan”? Second question: The Kinmen County Magistrate has been actively striving with the MAC for the “mini three links” to resume navigation by the winter solstice this year. Is the mainland side optimistic about this timing?","First question: As we have just stated, experts on the mainland are very concerned about the condition of “Tuantuan” and are willing to provide technical support and assistance within their professional field. We are also willing to provide relevant assistance.\nSecond question: Compatriots on both sides hope that the “small three links” will be restored as soon as possible, and hope the DPP authorities will do more work in this direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding Wang Yi, State Councilor and Foreign Minister, emphasizing sovereignty over Taiwan at the UN General Assembly, the DPP authorities said, “The mainland deliberately misinterprets UN General Assembly Resolution 2758,” “the resolution does not involve the question of Taiwan's representation in the UN system,” and “does not accept the unilaterally set political preconditions and ‘final outcome’ of…","The historical context and legal facts of the Taiwan question are clear. Taiwan is part of China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This fact has never changed and cannot change. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully unified, China's national sovereignty and territory have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided. In October 1971, the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, which thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all of China, including Taiwan, in the United Nations. China's seat in the United Nations is only one, and there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” The United Nations and its specialized agencies all adhere to the one-China principle when dealing with matters involving Taiwan. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations, universally shared and recognized by the international community.\nTaiwan belongs to all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan's future can only, and must, be decided jointly by all Chinese people. Reunification of the motherland is the trend of history. In order to satisfy narrow political interests, the DPP authorities disregard facts, reverse right and wrong, refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle, scorn the basic norms of international relations, and spread and hype so-called fallacies such as “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other.” They distort UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and have created the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait, harming the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Their conduct runs counter to the trend of history and the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides, and it is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202209/t20220928_12473877.htm"],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The 41st International Civil Aviation Assembly was held in Canada on the 27th. The DPP authorities recently claimed they regret not receiving an invitation. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","ICAO is a specialized agency of the United Nations, and only sovereign states are qualified to participate. Taiwan, as part of China, has no right to participate.\nThe DPP authorities, colluding with external forces and fabricating various pretexts to demand participation in ICAO assemblies and other activities, have the real aim of pursuing “independence” and creating division, and they will surely be resolutely defeated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The white paper 《The Taiwan Question and China’s Cause of Reunification in the New Era》 addresses Taiwan’s status after reunification, including its military and foreign relations. This is more restricted than the “one country, two systems” the mainland has spoken of in the past, and it has not been discussed with the Taiwan side. Both the DPP and the KMT have expressed opposition. What is the mainland’s view of…","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question, and also the best way to achieve national reunification. We hold that after peaceful reunification, Taiwan may adopt a social system different from that of the mainland and exercise a high degree of autonomy in accordance with law, and the two social systems will coexist and develop together over the long term. The specific form in which “one country, two systems” is realized in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan's actual circumstances, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully accommodate the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\n“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” reflects our cherishing and safeguarding of the great righteousness of the nation, the well-being of compatriots and peace across the Strait. Fully considering the differences in social systems and ideologies between the mainland and Taiwan, it is a peaceful, democratic, well-intentioned, win-win proposal. We are willing to continue uniting Taiwan compatriots, actively explore the “two systems” Taiwan plan, and enrich the practice of peaceful reunification. We believe that with the passage of time, “one country, two systems” will be clearly understood by broad Taiwan compatriots; in the process of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly working toward peaceful reunification, the scope and connotation of the “two systems” Taiwan plan will be fully demonstrated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","According to a recent announcement from the Ministry of Education, in the 2021 academic year mainland universities had a total of 38,200 students from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan enrolled, and more and more Taiwan students are choosing to study at mainland universities. Please ask the spokesperson to introduce the current situation of Taiwan students studying at mainland universities. How many Taiwan students…","We welcome Taiwan students to study at mainland universities. In recent years, the number of Taiwan students coming to the mainland for study has remained generally stable, and at present there are about 12,000 Taiwan students studying at mainland universities. This year's enrollment of students from Taiwan has two new features:\nFirst, the procedure for admitting Taiwan students based on \"General Scholastic Ability Test\" scores has been optimized and adjusted. This year, a nationally unified admissions platform was piloted for the first time, with 207 universities including Peking University and Tsinghua University participating in the first batch of the new system pilot. Judging from the pilot results, the new platform is convenient to use, gives candidates more options, and has been well received by the broad masses of Taiwan students. This year, the number of Taiwan students admitted based on \"General Scholastic Ability Test\" scores increased by more than 20% over last year.\nSecond, a new pathway has been provided for Taiwan students to study on the mainland. This year, enrollment of students from Taiwan was conducted for the first time based on \"Unified Test\" scores. Preliminary pilot work has been launched at 13 undergraduate institutions including Minnan Normal University and 6 vocational colleges including Fujian Information Vocational and Technical College.\nIn addition, other channels for enrolling students from Taiwan, including the joint examination for Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, and overseas Chinese, the Fujian universities' special enrollment for Taiwan students, and the \"joint enrollment of two schools\" by Jinan University and Huaqiao University, are also proceeding smoothly. We welcome more Taiwan students to study on the mainland, and we will create better conditions for Taiwan students to grow and succeed on the mainland and realize their life ambitions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","First question: Recently, the list of more than 2,000 delegates to the 20th CPC National Congress was published, and we noted the names of party delegates originally from Taiwan Province, such as Lu Li'an. Can the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation and the significance of these people becoming delegates to the 20th Congress? Second question: What effective assistance can the Taiwan Affairs Office…","First question: Compatriots of Taiwan origin who participate in the Communist Party of China and the various democratic parties and groups on the mainland, and who actively take part in political consultation, deliberation and governance, contribute to building socialism with Chinese characteristics and advancing the cause of national reunification. This reflects the care, concern, trust and respect of the Party and government for the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan. The 2,296 delegates to the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China have been elected, including delegates of Taiwan origin. They will attend the 20th Congress representing more than 96 million Party members and more than 4.9 million grassroots Party organizations nationwide, faithfully fulfill their duties as delegates, and fully play their representative role.\nSecond question: At present, there are relatively mature and comprehensive supporting measures for Taiwan compatriots entering the mainland. You can fully understand the various information before coming to the mainland, and if you need help, you may seek it nearby. The relevant local Taiwan Affairs Offices will, as always, provide assistance and services to you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Former US Secretary of State Pompeo recently made an unwelcome visit to Taiwan, claiming that “Taiwan is an independent country.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated its position on this matter. Everyone knows what kind of person Pompeo is. The DPP authorities have repeatedly incited him to make a provocative visit to Taiwan to put on a show and deceive people. How much of the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people has been wasted on this? The DPP authorities owe the people of Taiwan an explanation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Chu Li-lun, Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, said that the so-called “international support” sought by the DPP would put Taiwan in peril, and that supporting peace in the Taiwan Strait requires dialogue and communication, a position the Kuomintang has consistently upheld. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Our position is very clear. We are willing to make the utmost sincerity and the greatest efforts to create room for peaceful reunification across the Taiwan Strait, including cross-Strait dialogue and communication. The basis for cross-Strait dialogue and communication lies in the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Only by returning to the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations get back on the right track.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi clearly stated China's solemn position on the Taiwan question during the 77th session of the United Nations General Assembly, likening “Taiwan independence” to a “gray rhino” that must be resolutely prevented. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities, in collusion with external forces, keep carrying out \"independence-seeking\" provocations, undermining the hard-won situation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, attempting to change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and harming China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities pose a serious threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait and to peaceful reunification, and cause grave harm to the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Only by resolutely containing \"Taiwan independence\" can we ensure the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, ensure peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and ensure peaceful reunification across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","The travel itineraries of Chen Ming-tong, head of Taiwan’s security department, and others have been exposed one after another. Some so-called intelligence personnel on the island claimed that “this is a new form of the mainland’s intelligence war against Taiwan, used to suppress the morale of Taiwan’s military intelligence, and it will become the new normal of cross-strait intelligence warfare.” What is the…","The DPP authorities are accustomed to exaggerating the so-called “mainland threat” to divert attention and mislead the island's public, attempting to seek political gain by inciting “anti-China and hatred of China.” This trick is nothing new and cannot fool the broad masses of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Wu Zhaoxie, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department, recently accepted interviews with several foreign media outlets, claiming that the root of tensions in the Taiwan Strait is the mainland’s “external expansion.” What comments does the TAO have on this?","This person's statement completely disregards the facts and reverses right and wrong. We promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations in accordance with the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” Opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and advancing the just cause of realizing the complete reunification of the country have won full understanding and support from the international community. At present, the root of the tense situation across the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, their eagerness to cater to external forces, their pursuit of “using Taiwan to contain China,” and their continuous provocations to seek “independence,” which harm the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视记者","A US State Department spokesperson recently said that the US “one China policy” has not changed, and that the United States does not take a position on Taiwan’s “sovereignty.” Recently, the United States has frequently reiterated its “one China policy” while seldom mentioning the one-China principle, and has stated that the “one China policy” the United States has long adhered to differs from the mainland’s…","First, Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference.\nSecond, the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The three China-US joint communiqués clearly set out the commitments the United States made on the Taiwan question. In the 1972 Shanghai Communiqué, the US government clearly stated: “The United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.” In the 1978 Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, it clearly committed: “The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan,” and “The United States acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.” We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-09-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The Taiwan region reported more than 45,000 new COVID-19 cases yesterday. At present, more than 6 million Taiwan residents have been infected with COVID-19 and more than 10,000 have died. Yet the DPP authorities, with no real intention of fighting the epidemic and only concerned with elections, do not take the lives of the people seriously at all. What is the spokesperson's evaluation of the DPP authorities'…","In the nearly three years since the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, the DPP authorities have put political self-interest first, ignored the urgent needs of the public for epidemic prevention, and engaged in extensive political manipulation and political calculation, seriously harming the life, health, safety, and well-being of the people on the island.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202209/t20220928_12473868.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-09-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that on October 10, a leader of the DPP authorities delivered a so-called “speech” claiming that the two sides “are not subordinate to each other,” that Taiwan will continue to expand its military strength to demonstrate its determination to defend itself, and that it will fully prevent any unilateral change to the status quo. Does the spokesperson have any comment?","President Xi delivered an important speech at the conference commemorating the 110th anniversary of the 1911 Revolution, solemnly declaring the firm resolve and steadfast determination to uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” to resolutely curb “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The speech revealed the historical trend of national reunification and national rejuvenation, and pointed out the direction for the future of cross-Strait relations.\nThe DPP authorities, true to their “independence” nature, disregard the interests of the Chinese nation and the well-being of Taiwan's people. They incite confrontation and clamor for opposition, attempt to use a so-called “consensus” as a pretext to kidnap Taiwan public opinion, and frequently collude with external forces, intensifying their provocations for “independence.” Their despicable conduct of forgetting their ancestors, betraying the country, and splitting the nation once again proves that “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to national reunification and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation.\nThe Chinese nation has a glorious tradition of opposing division and upholding unity. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the country is the fundamental interest of the Chinese nation and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Resolutely defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly defeating all external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, is the sacred mission of the People's Liberation Army. The trend is irresistible and righteousness lies in it. The PLA will be steady as a mountain and move like thunder. The PLA will strengthen its sense of mission and responsibility, maintain a high state of combat readiness, and ensure that when the Party and the people need it, it can answer the call immediately, arrive ready to fight, and win every battle.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2022/09-29/9863668.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-10-08","Mao Ning","Reuters","Tesla founder Elon Musk in an interview with Financial Times suggested that a reasonably palatable solution to cross-Strait tensions would be for China to make Taiwan into a special administrative zone. How do you comment about this?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. China’s position on resolving the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We remain committed to the basic principle of peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems and aim to work with the greatest sincerity and effort to achieve peaceful reunification. At the same time, we will resolutely defeat attempts to pursue the “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda, push back interference by external forces, and safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347376.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221008_10779681.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-09","Mao Ning","CCTV","Tesla’s founder Elon Musk drew wide attention yesterday with his remarks on Taiwan. You also shared China’s position as the spokesperson. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said Musk’s comments are unacceptable. Do you have any further comment?","Yesterday I shared China’s principled position on the Taiwan question. The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have been acting with external forces to make provocations and seek independence. Only by resolutely deterring “Taiwan independence” separatism and opposing external interference can peace and stability be ensured in the Taiwan Strait.\nI want to stress that peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems is the basic principle for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to realize national reunification. Provided that national sovereignty, security and development interests are ensured, Taiwan can adopt a high degree of autonomy as a special administrative region, Taiwan’s social system and its way of life will be fully respected and the lawful rights and interests of our Taiwan compatriots will be fully protected. China’s reunification will not undermine any country’s legitimate interests. Instead, it will only bring more development opportunities to other countries and inject more positive energy into the prosperity of the Asia-Pacific region and the world at large. We welcome and hope to see understanding and support from more and more people for China’s peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems.\nThe remarks you mentioned from the DPP authorities have no merit. Whatever the DPP authorities say, they cannot change the basic fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347377.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221009_10779962.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-18","Wang Wenbin","AFP","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said that China is determined to take over Taiwan on a much faster timeline than previously considered. What’s the foreign ministry’s response?","I have noted Secretary Blinken’s remarks. The US has made clear commitments on “one-China”, acknowledging that there is but one China in the world and that Taiwan is a part of China and recognizing the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government representing China. These commitments are reflected explicitly in the three China-US Joint Communiqués. However, the US has time and again broken its word.\nThe US pledged to maintain only non-official ties with Taiwan, but in recent years it has substantially relaxed restrictions on official interactions with the region. The US House Speaker even visited the Taiwan region despite China’s strong opposition.\nThe US promised to gradually reduce its sale of arms to Taiwan, leading, over a period of time, to a final resolution, but in fact, since the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and the US, US arms sales to Taiwan have been increasing in both quantitative and qualitative terms, exceeding $70 billion to date.\nIn his remarks, Secretary Blinken also linked the US’s one-China policy to China’s commitment to a peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question, saying the latter is at the heart of the former. I need to stress that this is not a reiteration but an alteration of the US’s commitments.\nNational reunification by peaceful means is the first choice of the CPC and the Chinese government in resolving the Taiwan question, as it best serves the interests of the Chinese nation as a whole, including our Taiwan compatriots, and it works best for the long-term stability and development of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, a matter that must be resolved by the Chinese. We are ready to create vast space for peaceful reunification; but we will leave no room for separatist activities in any form. Division of the country for “Taiwan independence” and a peaceful solution are incompatible with each other. The more rampant “Taiwan independence” forces are, the less likely it is for a peaceful solution to the Taiwan question. To truly safeguard peace across the Taiwan Strait, there needs to be unequivocal opposition to all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and such acts must be stopped.\nThe US needs to honor its commitments, return to the original meaning of “one China” and reflect its statements of not supporting “Taiwan independence” in concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347384.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221018_10785260.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-21","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The US Chief of Naval Operations said that the US military must be ready to respond to a potential invasion of Taiwan as soon as this year. Do you have any comment on this?","The US needs to be fully aware of the extreme importance and highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, credibly act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, and refrain from sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no interference from any external force. We firmly oppose US moves of manipulating Taiwan-related issues to stoke confrontation in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347387.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221021_10790127.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-25","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Fifty-one years ago today, the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, which recognized the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government representing the whole of China, including the Taiwan region. For some time, some forces in the US have falsely claimed that UNGA Resolution 2758 doesn’t decide Taiwan’s status in an attempt to help Taiwan expand the so-called “international…","On October 25, 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 with an overwhelming majority, which “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations”, and to expel forthwith the representatives of the Taiwan authorities from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations and in all the organizations related to it. With the adoption of Resolution 2758, the “dual representation” proposal put forward by the US and some other few countries in order to retain Taiwan’s seat became a piece of waste paper. Once and for all, Resolution 2758 resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the UN and international institutions. It has also made it clear that there can only be one seat representing China in the UN. The one-China principle has become a prevailing consensus of the international community and a widely-held basic norm of international relations, thus fully eliminating any room for anyone, any country or any force to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”. The Taiwan region has no basis, ground or right whatsoever to participate in the UN or any other international organizations that can only be joined by sovereign countries.\nOver the past 51 years, on the basis of abiding by the one-China principle, the number of countries having established diplomatic relations with China has risen from over 60 to 181. This fully shows that the one-China principle has the overwhelming support and recognition of the international community and represents the irreversible trend of the world.\nIn recent years, some forces in the US have deliberately distorted UNGA Resolution 2758 and falsely claimed that the resolution does not decide Taiwan’s status, and called for Taiwan’s participation in the UN system. In doing so, they have attempted to fudge and hollow out the one-China principle and connive at and support the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, which has seriously harmed peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Attempts like these to turn back the wheel of history will only meet the opposition of the international community and fail completely in front of the strong resolution, will and capability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe history of the past half century shows that UNGA Resolution 2758 must not be challenged and the one-China principle is unshakable. The wheels of history are rolling on toward China’s reunification and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Complete reunification of our country can, without doubt, be realized!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347389.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221025_10791753.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-25","Wang Wenbin","NHK","Tsai Ing-wen, leader of the Taiwan region, said in a speech today that Taiwan is facing increasing military threat and economic coercion from the mainland. Do you have any comment?","The DPP authorities have confounded black and white in an attempt to mislead the public. This once again exposes their separatist nature and real agenda of seeking “independence”. Let me stress that there is no other right way forward for Taiwan than to reunify with the mainland. Advancing the “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda will only spell failure for the DPP authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347389.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221025_10791753.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-10-26","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","It is reported that a Taiwan university’s research vessel New Ocean Researcher 1 was interfered with and demanded to leave by a patrol ship of the Japan Coast Guard when operating in waters east of Taiwan. The patrol ship claimed that the research vessel should not conduct research activities in what it called Japan’s Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ) without Japan’s consent. Do you have any comment?","The incident you mentioned occurred in waters only 60-plus nautical miles off the coast of the island of Taiwan. Chinese research institutions, including those from Taiwan, have the right to carry out scientific research activities in those waters free from foreign interference. China and Japan have not yet carried out maritime delimitation in waters east of Taiwan. China does not accept the notion of the so-called “Japanese EEZ” and the so-called exercise of jurisdiction. The Chinese side has made démarches to the Japanese side and asked Japan not to interfere with the research activities of Chinese vessels, including the vessels from the Taiwan region, in those waters.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347390.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221026_10792317.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","The 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, which recently concluded, has been the focus of attention and discussion. The Taiwan-related content of the report to the 20th Congress has aroused great attention. May I ask how to interpret the Taiwan-related content of the report to the 20th Congress, and how it will be implemented?","On October 22, the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China successfully concluded. The Taiwan-related content of the report of the 20th Congress fully affirms the major achievements in work on Taiwan over the past five years and the ten years of the new era. It systematically expounds the CPC's policy positions on resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland. Based on the new historical position of advancing national reunification, it accurately grasps the new changes and characteristics of the situation across the Taiwan Strait, and, coordinating the overall strategic situation of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation with the once-in-a-century great changes in the world, makes an overall deployment and arrangement for work on Taiwan for the current and future period. It emphasizes implementing the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, puts forward the goals and requirements for advancing the process of national reunification on the new journey, and sets out the basic principles, positions, and important measures for work on Taiwan. It draws red lines and bottom lines, and demonstrates the firm determination to oppose foreign interference and “Taiwan independence” separatism, the victorious confidence in advancing national reunification, and the unchanging original aspiration to bring well-being to Taiwan compatriots. It points the way for us to firmly grasp leadership and initiative in the development of cross-Strait relations and to resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification. It is the fundamental guideline and action plan for doing work on Taiwan on the new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country.\nOn the new journey, we will fully implement the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, thoroughly implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and deployments of the CPC Central Committee on work on Taiwan, firmly grasp leadership and initiative in cross-Strait relations, and adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems.” We will firmly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” adhere to the people-centered development philosophy, steadily promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, resolutely defeat the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and firmly advance the process of national reunification. We will work hand in hand with the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to strive together for a beautiful future of reunifying the motherland and rejuvenating the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482047.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The report to the 20th Party Congress emphasizes adhering to and implementing the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. Please have the spokesperson interpret this.","Since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, General Secretary Xi Jinping, taking into account the overall strategic situation of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the great changes unseen in a century in the world, grasping historical trends and changes of the times, has delivered a series of important expositions on Taiwan work, issued a series of important instructions and directives, and put forward a series of new concepts, new ideas, and new strategies. This has formed the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, guiding Taiwan work to forge ahead through difficulties and composing a new chapter of the great changes of the past decade in Taiwan work in the new era.\nThe overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era profoundly answers major theoretical and practical questions on advancing national reunification in the new era and on the new journey, including the fundamental guarantee, historical position, strategic thinking, major policies, political foundation, practical approaches, fundamental driving forces, inevitable requirements, external conditions, and strategic support. It is an important component of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, the most important theoretical achievement in Taiwan work since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China that upholds correct principles while innovating, the inheritance, development, and culmination of the Party's major policies toward Taiwan, and the crystallization of wisdom from the Party's century-long struggle for the motherland's reunification. It is a scientific guide and action program for advancing the great cause of national reunification in the new era and on the new journey. It marks the maturing and further consolidation of the Party's theory of national reunification, which must be upheld over the long term and fully implemented.\nFully implementing the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era requires us to uphold the centralized and unified leadership of the Party Central Committee over Taiwan work; advance national reunification in the process of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation; resolve the Taiwan question on the basis of the development and progress of the mainland; adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems”; adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus”; promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations; unite Taiwan compatriots and win the hearts and minds of the Taiwan people; crush the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence”; oppose interference by external forces; and maintain the firm commitment not to renounce the use of force.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482046.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","The 20th CPC National Congress adopted amendments to the Party Constitution, adding content such as opposing “Taiwan independence,” which has drawn high attention from all sides, especially Taiwan public opinion. What is your comment?","Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is a historic task to which the Communist Party of China is unwavering in its commitment. Our Party has made long-term, unremitting efforts toward this goal, formulating and implementing policies toward Taiwan in keeping with the times, effectively promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of reunifying the motherland. “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to the reunification of the motherland and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. The 20th National Congress of the Party added content to the Party Constitution, including “resolutely oppose and contain ‘Taiwan independence,’” which is an inevitable requirement of the situation and tasks of work on Taiwan, reflecting the will of the entire Party and the wishes of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482044.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The report to the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China pointed out that 'we always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to commit ourselves to promoting economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, and deepen integrated development in all areas of cross-Strait relations,' which has drawn attention and recognition from Taiwan compatriots. What…","Deepening integrated development across the Taiwan Strait is a major policy proposition put forward by General Secretary Xi Jinping. We will earnestly implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, continue to work to promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, deepen integrated development in all fields across the Strait, uphold the development philosophy centered on the people, serve Taiwan compatriots as we serve mainland residents, continuously improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, continue to take the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, encourage more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to study, work and start businesses, and provide more platforms and better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to integrate into the mainland's new development pattern and participate in high-quality development. Whatever is conducive to deepening integrated development across the Strait, and whatever helps enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, we will persistently pursue, so that good things are done in practice and real things are done well.\nWe will emphasize promoting integration through exchange, benefits and emotional bonds. We will study and introduce more policies that give Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises equal treatment. We will actively support Fujian in exploring new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and accelerate the construction of the Demonstration Zone for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait. We will support other areas with concentrations of Taiwan businesses in pioneering and experimenting with Taiwan-related policies, and guide enterprises on both sides to strengthen cooperation in funds, technology, management, standards, brands, channels and other areas. We will help Taiwan businesses and enterprises expand the mainland's domestic market. We will further encourage and support regions, industries and sectors to broadly engage with all walks of life in Taiwan, and continuously expand and deepen civil exchange and cooperation in all fields across the Strait. We will promote the joint inheritance and promotion of China's fine traditional culture by compatriots on both sides, strengthen exchanges at the grassroots level and among young people across the Strait, promote heart-to-heart connection among compatriots, and rally strength for national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nOur long-held concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family” will not change. The policies of providing equal treatment and development opportunities to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will not change. Our efforts to do practical good for Taiwan compatriots will not stop. We are willing to work with Taiwan compatriots to advance integrated development across the Strait in greater depth and substance, benefit more compatriots on both sides, and create a bright future for cross-Strait relations and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482045.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","On the occasion of the 20th CPC National Congress, relevant political parties, groups, and individuals in Taiwan have expressed congratulations in various forms. Please introduce the relevant situation.","As the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China convened, political parties, groups and individuals in Taiwan expressed congratulations in various forms.\nThe Central Committee of the Kuomintang of China sent a congratulatory telegram to the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on the 16th, stating that, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence,” cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation have yielded fruitful results. It hopes that the two parties will maintain communication, cooperate sincerely, deepen mutual trust, seek common ground while setting aside differences, jointly enhance the rights and well-being of the people on both sides of the Strait, strive to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and open up a prosperous and developing future for cross-Strait relations.\nLien Chan, former Chairman of the Kuomintang; Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang; Soong Chu-yu, Chairman of the People First Party; Wu Cheng-tien, Chairman of the New Party; as well as political parties, groups and individuals on the island such as the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union, the Labor Party, the Unification Alliance Party, the Chinese Patriotic Heart Party, the Taiwan People’s Communist Party and the Chinese Women’s Party also sent congratulatory telegrams or letters.\nPeople from all walks of life in Taiwan published articles and accepted interviews, congratulating the convening of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China in various forms. They praised the great achievements of the Communist Party of China in leading the people of all ethnic groups across the country in socialist modernization construction. They expressed their expectations for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and jointly working toward national rejuvenation. They stated that compatriots on both sides are one family with blood ties, and that the two sides of the Strait are a community of shared destiny. At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is becoming increasingly complex and grave, and they hope that compatriots on both sides will unite in harmony and work together, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, join hands to promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, strive to advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly create a bright future of national rejuvenation and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","We have noted that the report of the 20th Party Congress has triggered enthusiastic responses among Taiwan compatriots on the Mainland. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The successful convening of the 20th CPC National Congress and the development blueprint for the country over the next five years and longer, drawn up in the report of the 20th Congress, have triggered enthusiastic response and positive reactions among the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. In recent days, news media have reported extensively on this, and the reactions of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople have focused on three aspects.\nFirst, they feel it firsthand. Many Taiwan businesspeople said that over the years they have personally witnessed the rapidly changing development on the mainland, and that the Party and the state keep their word and treat Taiwan compatriots equally, providing equal treatment and sharing development opportunities, which has further strengthened their determination to develop on the mainland.\nSecond, the future is promising. Many Taiwan compatriots said that after listening to the report of the 20th Congress on the country's plans for the next five years, they were deeply encouraged and believe more favorable policies will be introduced, so they are even more confident about developing on the mainland in the future. Some Taiwan businesspeople also said that, facing the development opportunities of the new era, they should more actively integrate, work together, and strive shoulder to shoulder.\nThird, a sense of mission and responsibility. Many Taiwan youth have closely linked personal growth with national development, saying they will be strivers with ideals and bridges of communication between compatriots on both sides, so that more young people in Taiwan can see the vast development space on the mainland and actively join the just cause of promoting the peaceful reunification of the two sides and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe strength of the country and the rejuvenation of the nation are closely tied to the future and destiny of Taiwan compatriots. For many years, Taiwan compatriots who have studied, started businesses, and developed on the mainland have personally felt the tremendous achievements of national development, and the broad space and stage it has provided for their academic and career development. This has led them to be optimistic about the mainland's development prospects and willing to more actively integrate into the overall development of the country, pursuing their dreams and writing wonderful lives as they deepen cross-Strait integrated development and advance the course of national reunification. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will grasp the trend, seize opportunities, seek development together, share prosperity, and create the future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482043.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","At the opening session of the 20th CPC National Congress, when General Secretary Xi Jinping said that “complete reunification of the motherland must be realized, and it will certainly be realized,” the venue erupted in long and sustained applause, and the topic of reunification quickly heated up on both sides of the Strait. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the historic mission the Communist Party of China has unswervingly pursued, the shared aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters, and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The solemn declaration in the report to the 20th Party Congress that \"complete reunification of the motherland must be achieved and certainly will be achieved\" once again fully demonstrates our confidence in winning the battle for reunification, our firm resolve to oppose external interference and \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and our unchanging original aspiration to bring well-being to compatriots. It has voiced the common voice of over 1.4 billion compatriots on the mainland and Chinese descendants at home and abroad, and has won strong resonance and wide acclaim. The applause in the venue of the opening session of the 20th Party Congress and outside the big and small screens resonated across the land of China, prompting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to discuss and long for reunification, jointly advancing the great cause of national reunification.\nThe complete reunification of the motherland is determined by the history and culture of the Chinese nation, and it is also determined by the timing and momentum of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We are closer than at any time in history, and more confident and more capable, of realizing the goal of great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and we are also closer to, and more confident and more capable of, realizing the goal of complete reunification of the motherland. All Chinese sons and daughters sincerely support reunification, eagerly anticipate reunification, and firmly defend reunification; this is the greatest source of our confidence. We will continue to thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Central Committee on Taiwan work. We will resolutely thwart any external interference and any acts of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, firmly advance the process of national reunification, and unite compatriots in Taiwan to create the glorious undertaking of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the DPP authorities, disregarding the actual epidemic situation and the appeals of Taiwan compatriots, have removed the household registrations of Taiwan compatriots who have not returned to Taiwan for two years. This harms the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, including their voting rights in the year-end “nine-in-one” elections. Public opinion on the island points…","The relevant practices of the DPP authorities directly harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, including those investing, studying and living on the mainland. In order to serve the narrow interests of one party, the DPP authorities have engaged in political manipulation on issues concerning the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and have arbitrarily harmed their interests. Their sinister intentions are known to all passersby, and they will surely be punished by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482041.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","In recent times, senior officials of the DPP authorities have loudly promoted the so-called “constitutional amendment on civil rights at age 18” as a key step in Taiwan’s so-called “constitutional reform.” They say that after the “referendum on the constitutional amendment for 18-year-olds” passes at the end of this year, they will continue to push “constitutional reform” to lead Taiwan toward a so-called “normal…","These remarks fully expose the DPP authorities' 'independence-seeking' nature. Disregarding the strong desire of Taiwan's ordinary people for peace, stability, and a good life, they strive to fabricate and clamor for so-called 'constitutional amendment referendums.' The fundamental purpose is to pave the way and build momentum for continued manipulation of 'amending the constitution to seek independence.' We hope all sectors of Taiwan society and the broad Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities' sinister intentions, remain highly vigilant against the serious harm this brings, and take practical action to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221026_12482042.htm"],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","The 90th INTERPOL General Assembly was recently held. The DPP authorities repeatedly hyped and manipulated the issue of attending the meeting. INTERPOL recently made clear that Taiwan is part of China, and once again refused Taiwan's attendance. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","INTERPOL is an intergovernmental international organization. Taiwan is part of China, and it has no basis, reason, or right to participate in the UN system or other international organizations that only sovereign states may join. The Chinese National Central Bureau allows police agencies in the Taiwan region of China to exchange data and coordinate case investigations with the central bureaus of member countries through the INTERPOL General Secretariat. Over the years, information sharing and case cooperation between the national central bureaus and the police agencies of the Taiwan region of China, carried out through the existing mechanism, have covered all fields and received effective responses. This is documented. The channels for the Taiwan region to participate in global anti-crime cooperation have always been open. The DPP authorities' repeated hyping and manipulation of the so-called issue of Taiwan's participation in international organizations is, in essence, an attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and to engineer “Taiwan independence” separatism. Its scheme will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","We note that, under the premise of implementing epidemic prevention policies, various localities have recently held a number of relatively large-scale and influential cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation. What other economic and trade exchange activities are expected to be held?","Recently, relevant departments and localities held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities that were rich in content, diverse in form, and productive. They mainly included the 18th Jiangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation and Exchange Conference, held in Shangrao, Jiangxi from September 16 to 18; the 25th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, held in Beijing on September 19 and 20; the Tianjin·Taiwan Commodity Expo, held in Tianjin on September 20; and the special promotion sessions “Taiwan Businesspeople and Taiwan Youth Come to Shanxi,” held in Linfen and Taiyuan, Shanxi, on September 22 and 24. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises eagerly took part in these activities, fully demonstrating their optimism about the prospects for economic development on the mainland and their enthusiasm for participating in cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation.\nA number of other cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities are now being intensively prepared and are expected to be held before the end of the year. For example, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will hold the Forum on Digital and Low-Carbon Development of the Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone in Changsha, Hunan. The Promotion Meeting on the Construction of the Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone and the Quancheng Forum on Cooperation in the Big Health Industry will be held in Jinan, Shandong. The Jiangsu-Taiwan New Energy Vehicle and Parts Industry Matchmaking Meeting and the 2022 Yangtze River Delta Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Zhenhu Forum will be held in Jiangsu. Yunnan will hold the theme-day activities of the 10th Yuntai Conference, the Yuntai Green Food Industry Cooperation Matchmaking Meeting, the Yuntai Cultural Tourism Industry Cooperation Matchmaking Meeting and other events. The 14th Chongqing·Taiwan Week, the 17th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week and the 18th Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum will also be held soon. The relevant departments and localities will carry out the related preparatory work while doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, and they welcome Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises to actively participate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, cross-Strait civil exchange activities have continued to be lively. Please introduce the relevant situation. What other important exchange activities are expected to be held?","Although the summer vacation has ended, exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have remained active recently. On the premise of doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, localities and departments have continued to carry out a series of cross-Strait exchange activities that are rich in content, diverse in form, and fruitful in results.\nIn jointly inheriting the excellent traditional Chinese culture, in late September the 4th Cross-Strait Youth Forum on the Inheritance and Innovation of Traditional Chinese Medicine was held in Fuzhou. A total of 250 TCM experts and practitioners from both sides attended the in-person conference, and more than 3,300 people joined online simultaneously. They conducted in-depth exchanges and discussions on themes including the inheritance and innovation of TCM across the Strait, talent cultivation, authentic medicinal materials, and serving grassroots communities. On October 4, the Double Ninth Festival, compatriots from both sides jointly attended the ceremony offering sacrifices to the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan in Jinyun County, Lishui, Zhejiang, commemorating the ancestor of human civilization and consolidating the national spirit. On the same day, the board of directors of the Langgong Temple in Dagang Township, Taiwan, and Xiamen Haixia Tonggen Art and Culture Development Co., Ltd. jointly produced the original Southern Min song “Hanging Incense” to promote Mazu culture together. In September and October, the “8th Cross-Strait Intangible Cultural Heritage Month — Guarding Our Spiritual Homeland” and the Beautiful China Travel Promotion event were held at the Buddha’s Memorial Hall of Fo Guang Shan in Kaohsiung, Taiwan. They showcased the colorful intangible cultural heritage of Guangxi, and compatriots from both sides experienced the endless charm of excellent traditional Chinese culture. The 12th Cross-Strait Chinese Character Culture and Art Festival was held in Taipei, exhibiting 200 pieces (sets) of calligraphy and seal carving works by famous artists from both sides. In the “Taking the Same Intangible Cultural Heritage Class” online cross-Strait intangible cultural heritage teaching activity, more than 620 residents of Beijing and Kaohsiung took part in the teaching and hands-on experience of intangible cultural heritage items including kite-making, dough sculpture, Beijing clay-sculpture painted facial masks, round fans, shadow puppetry, and Hanfu origami.\nEsports activities that young people on both sides of the Strait like are also in full swing. On September 19, “Huihaishang · 2022 Cross-Strait Esports Culture Festival” was launched online. This year, building on the three major sections of “esports exchange,” “humanities exchange,” and “cultural and creative exchange,” it integrates innovative elements such as the metaverse, the online economy, and youth cultural creativity. On September 28, the 1st Cross-Strait and Hong Kong, Macao Esports League was launched in Shenzhen. The league has four competition zones—Shenzhen, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan—and its offline grand finals and other activities will be held in December. Yesterday (October 25), the academic symposium “Commemorating the 77th Anniversary of Taiwan’s Restoration” was held in Beijing, where experts and scholars from both sides held discussions and exchanges on the theme “Adhere to the ‘1992 Consensus’ and Promote Peaceful Development.”\nBefore the end of the year, localities will also hold a number of important cross-Strait exchange activities. Three highlights deserve attention. First, this year marks the 35th anniversary of the start of civil exchanges across the Strait. Fujian, Sichuan, Hebei, Shandong, Guangdong and other places will hold a series of commemorative exchange activities to review and summarize the fruitful achievements of exchanges in all fields across the Strait over the past 35 years, and to actively explore ideas and measures for resuming offline cross-Strait exchanges in the post-epidemic era and continuing to deepen cross-Strait integration and development. Second, cultural and artistic exchange activities across the Strait continue to advance. The China Federation of Literary and Art Circles, China Film Association, China Drama Association, China Television Artists Association, and China Cultural Relics Exchange Association will hold a series of cultural exchange activities. Beijing, Zhejiang, Jiangsu, and Jiangxi will also hold calligraphy, painting, and photography exhibitions and cultural and creative design competitions. Fujian will hold the 14th Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Expo and Trade Fair, the 18th Cross-Strait Book Fair, and the “IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival” activities. Guangxi will hold the 2022 Guangxi-Taiwan “Sharing New Opportunities” event and Guangxi-Taiwan ethnic minority cultural exchange activities, among others. Third, youth exchange activities across the Strait have distinctive features. Fujian will hold the 10th Cross-Strait Youth Festival, which is expected to invite 3,000 Taiwan youths to participate. Hubei will hold a series of activities of the 5th Cross-Strait Youth Donghu Forum; Guangdong will hold the 8th Guangzhou-Taiwan Youth Forum and the 1st Guangzhou Taiwan Youth Lingnan Culture Commentator Competition; and Kunshan, Jiangsu will host the grand final of the 2022 Cross-Strait National Baseball and Softball League. Compatriots from both sides are welcome to take part actively in the above exchange activities, each of which has its own distinctive features.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","We note that some politicians in the United States and Taiwan have recently been in unison beating the drums of 'Taiwan Strait war.' US Secretary of State Blinken has frequently stated that 'Beijing intends to accelerate cross-Strait unification,' and Chen Ming-tong, head of Taiwan's security agency, has also said that 'the mainland may use war to force talks in 2023.' What is your comment?","We have also noted that recently, rhetoric advocating so-called \"cross-Strait war\" has been rampant, and those behind it have different motives and purposes. People on the island who oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" recognize the \"1992 Consensus,\" and advocate peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, are concerned about the Taiwan Strait crisis caused by the reckless actions of the DPP authorities, and call on the DPP authorities to change course and return to the correct path of the \"1992 Consensus,\" consultation and dialogue, and peaceful cross-Strait development. They have expressed their deep concern that \"Taiwan independence\" could trigger war. The DPP and Green camp politicians, however, are using the war topic to hitch themselves to and cooperate with external forces in hyping up the so-called \"mainland threat.\" This is to find excuses to keep \"anti-China and resist-China\" going, to find excuses to keep colluding with external forces to pursue \"independence\" and provoke confrontation, and even to find excuses for \"seeking independence through force,\" so that they can keep relying on external forces to coerce and deceive Taiwan's people, prolong their own political lives, and serve the narrow interests of one party. Everyone must remain highly vigilant and discern carefully.\nAs for some people on the U.S. side, I would like to stress that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and brooks no interference from external forces. They should recognize that the root cause of the current tension and volatility in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities' obstinate insistence on the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" their collusion with external forces to pursue \"independence\" and provocation, and external forces playing the \"Taiwan card\" to \"contain China through Taiwan.\" Our major policy principles toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, to translate its political commitment of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\" into concrete action, and to stop sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Will the mainland side set up a “strategic guardrail” to reduce the risks and harms to the Taiwan Strait, or choose another path? Second question: The 20th CPC National Congress amended the Party Constitution to add content such as “resolutely oppose and contain ‘Taiwan independence.’” Does this indicate that, in addition to the Anti-Secession Law and the list of “diehard ‘Taiwan independence’…","On the first question: “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest risk and harm threatening peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Only by containing “Taiwan independence” can the risk be stopped and the harm eliminated. There is no other choice.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. The US side should earnestly adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question properly, and put into practice its political commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.”\nOn the second question: Actively using legal weapons to strike at and contain “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities is an important measure to safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. We will continue to strengthen the use of rule-of-law approaches and rule-of-law means to strike at “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and advance the process of national reunification. In light of developments and changes in the situation, we will further introduce new rule-of-law measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","First question: What is your comment on the concerns of all parties on the island about a 'cross-Strait war'? Second question: The report to the 20th Party Congress mentioned adhering to the greatest sincerity and making the greatest efforts to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. Mr. Spokesperson, can we see the dawn of peaceful reunification now?","First, as is well known, the root cause of the current tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” colluding with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation, while external forces play the “Taiwan card” and “use Taiwan to contain China.” Only by firmly opposing external interference and containing “Taiwan independence” separatism can the Taiwan Strait maintain a peaceful and stable development.\nSecond, our major policies toward Taiwan are consistent and clear. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort. We do not promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is aimed at external interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, and is by no means aimed at Taiwan compatriots. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should discern right from wrong and recognize where their interests lie, jointly oppose and resist “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and must not allow the “gray rhino” of “Taiwan independence” separatism to disrupt peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Together, we should promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nRegarding the second question, compatriots on both sides are all Chinese, and Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood brothers and sisters. No one wishes more earnestly and sincerely than we do to see peaceful reunification across the Strait. However, “the tree wants to be still, but the wind will not subside.” At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is tense and turbulent, and where things go from here rests on a single decision by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","At least four major Taiwan industry and commerce groups have stated that they plan to visit the mainland after the 20th Party Congress. What is your comment?","Major Taiwan business groups have independently arrived at the same position, each stating that they will organize delegations to visit and exchange on the mainland. This fully expresses the common voice of the island’s business community, which hopes for exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides and yearns for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it reflects the deep concern of all sectors on the island over the complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait. This shows that the DPP authorities’ schemes and practices of intensifying cross-Strait hostility and confrontation and aggravating tension in the Taiwan Strait are unpopular.\nThe report to the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China emphasized that we always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to commit ourselves to promoting economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, and to deepening integrated development in all fields across the Strait. We warmly welcome major Taiwan business groups to visit the mainland in delegations, and we warmly welcome the broad Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to take a look around, talk about family bonds, deepen cooperation, and work together for development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-10-26","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed at the so-called 'World Democracy Movement Congress' that 'the Taiwan people will not be shaken by threats from the mainland.' What is the spokesperson's comment? Second question: After the 20th Party Congress, some people on the island speculated that the mainland would accelerate 'armed unification.' What is your comment on this?","I will answer the second question first. Socialism with Chinese characteristics has entered a new era and a new journey, and the cause of advancing national reunification is at a new historical juncture. We will more firmly oppose “independence” and promote reunification, firmly commit to the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and firmly advance the cause of national reunification.\nAs for the first question, the so-called “conference” you just mentioned is nothing but a farce. The DPP authorities are carrying out a “green terror” on the island, persecuting and oppressing dissenters, and deceiving and swindling public opinion internationally. What qualifications and face do they have to talk extravagantly about “democracy”? The DPP authorities, under the banner of “democracy,” court some anti-China forces to seek “independence,” incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and engage in actions to split the country. They are doomed to fail.\nThe press conference is over. Thank you all for coming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202210/t20221026_12482038.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-10-27","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said Beijing was trying to “speed up” its seizure of Taiwan during an interview with Bloomberg. He said, “What’s changed is this -- a decision by the government in Beijing that that status quo was no longer acceptable, that they wanted to speed up the process by which they would pursue reunification.” Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","First of all, the status quo in the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China and Taiwan is part of China. It is not China that is trying to change the status quo, but the DPP authorities’ “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and US moves to distort and fudge the one-China principle.\nThe one-China principle is the most important political prerequisite and bedrock of the establishment and advancement of diplomatic relations with the US. It is a basic common understanding between China and the US on the Taiwan question. How to resolve the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. We are ready to create vast space for peaceful reunification; but we will leave no room for separatist activities in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347391.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221027_10792929.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-10-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据报道，军委办公厅近日印发新修订的《军人休假工作暂行规定》。请问修订这部法规有什么重要意义？修订后的法规有哪些创新点和亮点？","According to a message from the WeChat account “National Defense Ministry Release,” in response to recent negative remarks about Taiwan by the US Department of Defense, Defense Ministry spokesperson Tan Kefei stated on the 15th that the US statements twist black and white and confuse right and wrong, and China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, a US Department of Defense spokesperson recently said that China (mainland) has intensified “intimidation” and pressure against Taiwan and other allies and partners, strengthened military activities in the Taiwan Strait and other areas, undermined regional peace and stability, and increased the risk of miscalculation. The US side also said that it has long adhered to the “One China policy,” but this differs from the One China principle of China (mainland), and that it will continue to help Taiwan maintain sufficient defense capabilities. What is your comment on this?\nTan Kefei said that the US statements twist black and white and confuse right and wrong, and China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition. There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all of China. This is a basic fact recognized by the international community. The One China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and the core content of the three China-US joint communiqués.\nTan Kefei pointed out that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated. For some time, the US side has obstinately clung to the strategy of “using Taiwan to contain China,” and its negative words and deeds on the Taiwan issue have continued: it has upgraded official exchanges with Taiwan’s authorities, increased military collusion with Taiwan, announced plans to sell weapons to Taiwan, sent US warships through the Taiwan Strait multiple times, and had military aircraft arrive and land on Taiwan island. These provocative acts by the US seriously damage China-US and military-to-military relations and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the One China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately correct its mistakes, stop all forms of official US-Taiwan exchanges and military contacts, handle the Taiwan question prudently and properly, stop backing and cheering on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and, through concrete actions, uphold China-US relations, military-to-military relations, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nTan Kefei stressed that “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest obstacle to the reunification of the motherland and a serious hidden danger to national rejuvenation. The DPP authorities have continuously colluded with external forces and plotted “independence” and provocations, which is the root cause of the current tense and volatile situation in the Taiwan Strait. The historic task of complete reunification of the motherland must and will be accomplished. The People’s Liberation Army of China will maintain a high state of alert, ready to fight at all times, resolutely defeat all external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10195249.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-10-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","据日本共同社报道，日政府拟考虑在年底修订的《国家安全保障战略》中，针对台海局势写明“不承认凭实力单方面改变现状”，并可能体现“自由开放印太构想”、日美澳印“四边安全对话”机制等政策内容。请问中方对此有何评论？","First, I will issue an announcement.\nFrom November 9 to 11, the PLA Army Engineering University will hold the 8th International Army Cadet Week in Nanjing. Themed “Capabilities and Qualities of Army Officers in Joint Operations and Their Cultivation,” this year's event plans to include keynote reports, guest forums, thematic seminars, a simulated United Nations peacekeeping tabletop exercise, and an introduction to traditional Chinese culture. The event will adopt a “combination of online and offline” format, inviting cadets from army academies in many countries, including the United States, the United Kingdom, Japan, Pakistan, Australia, Brazil, and South Africa, to attend online, while cadets from 12 Chinese army academies will attend at the main venue in Nanjing. The purpose of holding this event is to build an international exchange platform for young army officer cadets and promote mutual learning among cadets from various countries.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10195251.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-10-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the FY2023 “National Defense Authorization Act” being discussed by the U.S. Senate may include some content from the “Taiwan Policy Act of 2022” passed by the Senate Foreign Relations Committee in September. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The US side has recently repeatedly concocted Taiwan-related policies and bills that undermine China's sovereignty. It has escalated its “using Taiwan to contain China” approach, and in particular, some provisions aim to strengthen US-Taiwan military ties and support so-called Taiwan “self-defense.” These actions seriously interfere in China's internal affairs, seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and seriously breach the solemn political commitments the US side has made to China on the Taiwan question. A country that knows well that “a divided house cannot stand,” and that once used armed force to safeguard national unity, has repeatedly broken its word and acted recklessly on matters involving the sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity of another country. This is a typical case of “double standards.” We firmly oppose this and have lodged serious representations with the US side.\nTaiwan is Taiwan of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is China's own internal affair, to be decided by the Chinese people. We urge the US side to stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question. The Chinese People's Liberation Army has always been a steadfast force in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and any scheme to obstruct China's complete reunification is bound to fail.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10195255.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-10-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media reports, the 21st “U.S.-Taiwan Defense Industry Conference” recently concluded. A Taiwan source revealed that the United States may announce several arms sales projects to Taiwan before the end of the year. What comments do you have on this?","For some time now, the United States has repeatedly violated its political commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" has repeatedly played the \"Taiwan card\" to interfere in China's internal affairs, and has even sent erroneous signals of supporting Taiwan in \"resisting reunification by force.\" These despicable actions by the United States seriously undermine China's national sovereignty and security, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, pose major strategic risks to China-U.S. relations and to military-to-military relations between the two countries' armed forces, and send a serious erroneous signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. China expresses serious concern and firmly opposes this.\nThis year marks the 40th anniversary of the \"August 17\" Communiqué between China and the United States. In that communiqué, the United States explicitly acknowledged that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is part of China, and that the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government of China; it explicitly committed not to pursue a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan and to gradually reduce arms sales to Taiwan until the issue is ultimately resolved. It is written in black and white and is perfectly clear. Yet in practice, the United States has repeatedly reneged on its commitments. In particular, in recent years, the United States has hollowed out and gutted the one-China principle, continuously instigated arms sales to Taiwan, and created obstacles to China's achievement of peaceful reunification.\nTaiwan's security ultimately depends on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The U.S. arms sales to Taiwan will only push up tensions in the Taiwan Strait and the risk of conflict and confrontation. We urge the United States to stop selling weapons to Taiwan and to halt U.S.-Taiwan military contacts, and not to make one mistake after another on the Taiwan question. The People's Liberation Army of China is closely monitoring the situation in the Taiwan Strait and will continue to take resolute measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and security interests.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10195258.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-10-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On October 10, Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen delivered a so-called “speech” saying that she would accelerate the building of Taiwan's own military strength and build asymmetric combat capabilities. It is also reported that Taiwan's defense department will soon submit a 2023 budget proposal report that significantly increases defense spending. What comments does the spokesperson have?","We have noted the relevant reports. The DPP authorities have always sought to deceive the people on the island and mislead international audiences, and to seek political self-interest, by fabricating false narratives such as defending “democracy and freedom” and responding to the “mainland threat.” They have always been most “generous” when wagering the safety of Taiwan compatriots. In essence, this is about seeking “independence” through force and splitting the country. This scheme and conduct, which deviate from the trend of history and betray the national interest, will not succeed. They will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots, and they are an obstacle that must be removed in the process of striving for peaceful reunification. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; reunification is the right path. The Chinese People's Liberation Army maintains a high state of vigilance at all times and resolutely fulfills its sacred mission of defending national sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity through concrete actions.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10195266.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-10-28","Wang Wenbin","RIA Novosti","Yesterday, Russian President Putin said it is wrong for the US to undermine its relations with China on the Taiwan question. Putin also said that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. What’s the foreign ministry’s comment?","We deeply appreciate President Putin’s statement. I would like to stress that the one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community and a widely recognized basic norm in international relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347392.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221028_10793563.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-10-28","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 28 — The giant panda “Tuan Tuan,” gifted by the mainland to Taiwan, is suspected of suffering from a malignant brain tumor. The Taipei Zoo recently stated that it has submitted an application for permission and hopes to invite experts from the mainland to Taiwan to assist with diagnosis and treatment. Zhu Mingguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, introduced the situation when answering reporters' questions on the 28th: The Giant Panda Protection and Research Center plans to dispatch two diagnosis and nursing experts to Taiwan to participate in the treatment and nursing of “Tuan Tuan.” Procedures for travel to Taiwan are currently being handled with the assistance of relevant parties on the mainland.\nZhu Mingguang said that the Giant Panda Protection and Research Center set up an expert team in late September, which has maintained close contact with the Taipei Zoo, continuously followed “Tuan Tuan's” treatment, and provided relevant technical support. After the center received the Taipei Zoo's invitation letter requesting assistance on the afternoon of October 27, it planned to dispatch two experts to Taiwan to participate in the treatment and nursing of “Tuan Tuan.” He said he hopes that, with the joint care and support of all parties on both sides of the Strait, “Tuan Tuan” will receive better treatment and care and get through this difficulty.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202210/t20221028_12482849.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-10-31","Zhao Lijian","Global Times","According to reports, US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said in an interview that regarding China, “It is a worry to us because it’s been a few years. We’re seeing...more aggression on the outside, including on Taiwan...So if there’s a crisis, it will be bad for the entire world, so we need to maintain security. We need to resolve issues in a peaceful way”. Do you have any comment?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, a matter that must be resolved by the Chinese. We will continue to strive for peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all measures necessary. This is directed solely at interference by outside forces and the few separatists seeking “Taiwan independence” and their separatist activities.\nThe real root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have been soliciting the US’s support for “independence” and some people in the US have been using Taiwan to contain China. The remarks confound right with wrong. Its characterization of Taiwan as part of China’s “outside” and of China as being “aggressive towards Taiwan” is not only inconsistent with the basic fact that Taiwan is part of China, but also seriously contrary to the US’s own political commitments made to China on the Taiwan question. China is firmly against this. If the US truly does not want to see a crisis in the Taiwan Strait, it needs to act on its statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, put an immediate end to irresponsible rhetoric and action, and reject and curb “Taiwan independence” with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347393.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202210/t20221031_10794475.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-02","Zhao Lijian","CGTN","Prime Minister Muhammad Shehbaz Sharif of Pakistan has started his official visit to China. Can you share more about his visit?","On the morning of 2 November, President Xi Jinping met with Prime Minister Muhammad Shehbaz Sharif of Pakistan on his official visit to China at the Great Hall of the People.\nPresident Xi welcomed Prime Minister Sharif and thanked him for his congratulatory letter right after the opening of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC). President Xi noted that China and Pakistan are good friends, good partners and good brothers. Amid global changes and uncertainties in recent years, the two countries have supported each other and forged ahead, demonstrating an iron-clad friendship. China views its relations with Pakistan from a strategic and long-term perspective, and Pakistan has always been a high priority in China’s neighborhood diplomacy. China is ready to work with Pakistan to elevate the level of all-round strategic cooperation, speed up efforts to build a closer China-Pakistan community with a shared future in the new era, and inject new impetus into their all-weather strategic cooperative partnership.\nPresident Xi stressed that China commends Pakistan’s firm commitment to advancing friendship and cooperation with China, and expressed appreciation for Pakistan’s support on issues vital to China’s core and major concerns. China will continue to firmly support Pakistan in safeguarding its sovereignty, territorial integrity, development interests and dignity, and in achieving unity, stability, development and prosperity. China expressed deep sympathies to the Pakistani people over the devastating floods that have hit the country, and will provide additional emergency relief to help with post-flood reconstruction. China supports Pakistan’s efforts to revive agricultural production, and will strengthen cooperation with Pakistan on disaster prevention and relief and climate change.\nAfter presenting the key outcomes of the 20th CPC National Congress, President Xi underscored that China will continue its fundamental policy of opening-up and provide new opportunities to Pakistan and the rest of the world through continuous development. China will further deepen synergy between its development strategies and those of Pakistan. The two sides will make full use of the Joint Cooperation Committee of the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor (CPEC), advance CPEC with greater efficiency, and make CPEC an exemplar of high-quality Belt and Road cooperation. It is important to accelerate the construction of auxiliary infrastructure for Gwadar Port to unleash its role in driving interconnected development in the region. The two sides will work together to create conditions for the early implementation of the upgradation of ML-1 and the Karachi Circular Railway project. Pakistan is welcome to export more quality agri-products to China. China will work with Pakistan to expand cooperation in digital economy, e-commerce, photovoltaic and other new-energy technologies, and take solid steps to advance cooperation concerning agriculture, science, technology and people’s livelihood. China will continue to do its best to support Pakistan in stabilizing its financial situation. China supports its provinces with a strong industry in pairing up with Pakistani partners to advance industrial cooperation, and hopes the Pakistani side will provide a sound business environment. President Xi said the safety of Chinese nationals in Pakistan is close to his heart, and conveyed his hope that Pakistan will provide a reliable and safe environment for Chinese institutions and personnel working on cooperation projects there.\nPresident Xi pointed out that the world, our times and history are changing in ways like never before. Facing a highly uncertain world, both sides should stand on the right side of history, keep up their strong cooperation in multilateral mechanisms, and work closely on major international and regional issues so as to uphold true multilateralism, international fairness and justice and the shared interests of developing countries, and inject certainty and positives into the world. China will work with Pakistan to advance the operationalization of the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative, make the global economic governance system more fair, equitable, inclusive and beneficial to all, and build a community with a shared future for mankind. These collaborative efforts will provide a strong underpinning for the development of the two countries, and contribute more to global peace, stability and prosperity.\nPrime Minister Sharif noted that it is a great honor for him to be among the first foreign leaders to visit China after the successful 20th CPC National Congress, which marked a new milestone. The visit is a testament to the profound, iron-clad friendship between Pakistan and China. On behalf of the Pakistani government and people, Prime Minister Sharif once again expressed hearty congratulations to President Xi on his re-election as General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee. He said that over the past decade, under the dynamic leadership of President Xi, China has created a miracle of great development achievements. China has upheld multilateralism, promoted global solidarity and cooperation, and made important contributions to safeguarding world peace and development. In doing so, China has lived up to its responsibility as a major country. The world cannot operate without China, and China’s development cannot be isolated or contained by any force. Prime Minister Sharif expressed his confidence that President Xi, with his extraordinary vision, will continue to lead China toward even more remarkable achievements and create an even brighter future for the world.\nPrime Minister Sharif stressed that deepening Pakistan’s all-weather strategic cooperative partnership with China is a cornerstone of Pakistan’s foreign policy and the national consensus of Pakistan. He expressed heartfelt appreciation to the Chinese government and people for the valuable anti-COVID support, and for the generous assistance in the wake of the devastating floods. No country has ever helped Pakistan or other developing countries with such wholehearted sincerity, he said. He reiterated Pakistan’s firm commitment to the one-China policy and its firm support for China’s position on issues concerning China’s core interests including Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong. Even as Pakistan learns from China’s successful experience and tries to rely on its own efforts, Pakistan will deepen all-round cooperation with China to better develop itself. This is the only way forward for Pakistan. CPEC has had a profound impact on Pakistan’s economic and social development. Pakistan is ready to work with China to continue promoting high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, and hopes to have China’s strong support in the upgradation of ML-1, the Karachi Circular Railway and other important infrastructure projects. Pakistan will further step up security measures and do all it can to protect the safety of Chinese institutions and personnel. Pakistan fully supports the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative put forth by President Xi. It will strengthen communication and collaboration with China in international and regional affairs to make a positive contribution to world peace and development. The Pakistan-China friendship is unbreakable. Pakistan will always stand firmly with China.\nAfter the meeting, President Xi held a welcoming banquet for Prime Minister Sharif at the Golden Hall of the Great Hall of the People.\nWang Yi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, State Councilor and Foreign Minister, and He Lifeng, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Development and Reform Commission, were present at the events.\nPrime Minister Sharif will also meet with other Chinese leaders later today. We will release updates in due course.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347395.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221102_10797427.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-03","Zhao Lijian","Nos Television","I have a question on a visit that is going on in Taipei. At this point of time, several members of parliaments of European countries, including a representative of the Dutch coalition party D66, are meeting today with Tsai Ing-wen. And this MP, Sjoerdsma, has also called for sanctions in case China would take Taiwan by force. What do you make of this?","The legislators you mentioned have often deliberately hyped up issues and spread falsehoods and rumors against China. They have little credibility to speak of and are not worth taking up your attention. The farcical political stunt of these few MPs will lead nowhere but only invite disgrace. A word of advice to the DPP authorities: to collude with external forces and seek “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347396.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221103_10799876.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-11-04","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the U.S. Department of Defense recently released the “2022 National Defense Strategy,” which contains a large amount of content concerning China. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The China-related content in the U.S. 2022 National Defense Strategy continues the erroneous “threat-driven” narrative of its National Security Strategy Report. Disregarding the facts, it exaggerates so-called Chinese “challenges” and great power competition, and uses the planning of U.S. defense strategy to smear China's normal military development. This is an old tune of Cold War mentality and zero-sum thinking. We firmly oppose this and have lodged serious representations with the U.S. side.\nChina firmly follows the path of peaceful development and firmly upholds the international system with the United Nations at its core. China has always worked through practical actions to safeguard peace in the Asia-Pacific, promote development in the Asia-Pacific, participate in Asia-Pacific cooperation, and is committed to building a community with a shared future in the Asia-Pacific. A strong Chinese military is not only the strategic support for defending national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity, but also a firm force for maintaining peace and stability in the world and the region. This is plain to see for the international community. The countries that obstinately put their own interests first and form cliques in the Asia-Pacific to pursue “integrated deterrence” are the true “relentlessly pressing challenges” to the international system and the Asia-Pacific region.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. At present, the U.S. side is continually hollowing out and emptying out the one-China principle, and is increasingly pursuing “using Taiwan to contain China.” These egregious acts seriously infringe on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and gravely endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. The Chinese People's Liberation Army continues to train and prepare for combat, and resolutely counters “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form and interference by external forces.\nChina firmly adheres to a nuclear strategy of self-defensive nature, and abides by a nuclear policy of never being the first to use nuclear weapons at any time and under any circumstances, keeping its nuclear forces at the minimum level required for national security. China actively participates in international arms control, disarmament, and nonproliferation processes, and has signed or acceded to more than 20 multilateral arms control, disarmament, and nonproliferation treaties, including the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons. On the contrary, the U.S. has torn up treaties and withdrawn from agreements in the fields of arms control and nonproliferation, accelerated the upgrading and replacement of nuclear weapons and their delivery systems, lowered the threshold for nuclear weapons use, carried out nuclear submarine cooperation with the United Kingdom and Australia, and aggravated the risk of nuclear proliferation in the region.\nWe urge the U.S. side to abandon Cold War zero-sum thinking, remove its tinted glasses, correct its wrong perceptions of China, view the development of China and the Chinese military rationally, adopt an objective and pragmatic attitude, and do more things that help safeguard world and regional peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16195179.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-11-07","Zhao Lijian","TASS","The G7 foreign ministers’ statement following their meeting at Münster, Germany said that the G7 members “aim for constructive cooperation with China, where possible and in our interest”. The G7 foreign ministers also reminded China of the need to uphold the principles of the UN Charter on peaceful settlement of disputes and to abstain from threats or the use of force. The statement also mentioned China’s…","China’s position on issued related to Hong Kong, Xinjiang, Taiwan is consistent and clear-cut. The G7 foreign ministers’ statement grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs and maliciously smears China in disregard of our solemn position and the plain facts. We deplore and firmly reject it.\nChina has been exemplary in implementing the UN Charter and practicing true multilateralism. We are committed to promoting joint international response to global challenges and to building a human community with a shared future. We urge the G7 to discard the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop meddling in other countries’ internal affairs, stop peddling lies and falsehoods, stop stoking regional tensions and bloc confrontation, and work instead to create enabling conditions for global cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347398.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221107_10801513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-07","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Britain’s Department for International Trade said on Monday that the Minister of State for Trade Greg Hands would visit Taiwan and meet Tsai Ing-wen. The two will co-host the 25th annual UK-Taiwan trade talks. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","We have reiterated China’s principled position on the Taiwan question on multiple occasions. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We firmly oppose any form of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The one-China principle is the political foundation of the development of diplomatic ties between China and the UK. We urge the UK to earnestly respect China’s sovereignty, adhere to the one-China principle, stop having any form of official interaction with Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The Taiwan authorities should also beware that any attempt to seek independence by colluding with external forces is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347398.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221107_10801513.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-08","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Does the foreign ministry have any comments on Lithuania opening a trade office in Taiwan on Monday?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China, any action that violates China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and any practice that runs counter to the prevailing consensus of the international community and the basic norm of international relations. We urge the Lithuanian side to strictly abide by the one-China principle, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently, and take credible steps to safeguard the political foundation of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221108_10823564.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-08","Zhao Lijian","Bloomberg","Just to follow up on Taiwan. China’s air force has also stepped up its incursion into sensitive areas near Taiwan to the highest level since US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi visited three months ago. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on the warplane incursion over Taiwan?","This is not a question about diplomacy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221108_10823564.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-08","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Just on this question of Taiwan announcing yesterday that it’s going to invest ten million euros towards chip production in Lithuania. A Taiwanese official, the one who made the announcement, also said yesterday that Taiwan would like to work with Lithuania together to strengthen the resilience of the “democratic supply chain” in the face of coercion. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on these remarks?","The root cause of the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities, refusing to recognize the one-China principle, have been making provocations in collusion with external forces in an attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” and to change the status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. We want to make it clear to the Taiwan authorities once again that any move against the trend of history is bound to be rejected by all Chinese people, and any attempt to collude with external forces is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221108_10823564.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-10","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","The US side said on Wednesday that the US and Chinese leaders would discuss American “red lines” during an expected meeting next week, and that the US side is not willing to make any fundamental concessions. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","The heads of state of China and the US have maintained regular contact through various means. The Chinese side takes seriously the US proposal for a meeting between the two presidents in Bali. The teams on both sides are in communication on this.\nChina’s US policy is consistent and clear. We are committed to mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation with the US. At the same time, we will firmly defend our sovereignty, security and development interests.\nThe Taiwan question is at the heart of China’s core interests; the one-China principle is the bedrock of the political foundation for China-US relations; the three China-US Joint Communiqués are the most crucial “guardrails” for our relations. What the US needs to do is stop fudging, distorting and hollowing out the one-China principle, strictly abide by the basic norms of international relations including respect for other countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity and non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, and return to the three China-US joint communiqués and the one-China principle. The economic and trade relations between China and the US are mutually beneficial and win-win in nature. The US should stop using economic and trade issues as a political tool or making them an ideological matter. Instead, the US needs to take concrete actions to uphold the rules of the market economy and the international trading system. The development of state-to-state relations is not a zero-sum game. China always stands for inclusive partnerships that do not target any third party and rejects coercing countries into choosing sides.\nChina views and grows its relations with the US in accordance with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping and calls for establishing the right way forward for our relations in the new era. It is important that the US work together with China to properly manage differences, advance mutually beneficial cooperation, avoid misunderstanding and miscalculation, and bring China-US relations back to the right track of sound and steady development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347401.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221110_10960383.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-10","Zhao Lijian","Shenzhen TV","On November 7 local time, a Salvadoran court upheld a suspension of El Salvador’s free trade agreement with Taiwan. Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele and the Chinese side jointly announced that both sides will begin free trade talks and finalize a treaty as soon as possible. Do you have any comment?","On the evening of November 7 local time, the Constitutional Chamber of the Supreme Court of Justice in El Salvador ordered the cessation of the effects of the protective measure for the so-called “free trade agreement” with Taiwan, which marks the complete abolition of the deal. In doing so, El Salvador has chosen to stand on the right side of history and made a decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of both countries. China highly appreciates that. This again shows that upholding the one-China principle is an overriding trend that represents the overwhelming consensus of the world and enjoys popular support. This is a trend that no force can hold back.\nToday, China and El Salvador jointly announced that the two sides are ready to launch the bilateral free trade negotiation process as soon as possible and will make joint efforts for an early conclusion of the deal. This speaks volumes about the shared desire of the two sides to deepen bilateral ties and upgrade economic and trade cooperation. In recent years, acting upon the common understanding reached between the two heads of state, China and El Salvador have broken new ground in the development of bilateral relations, delivered new outcomes in practical cooperation, and further deepened friendship. China stands ready to work with El Salvador to strengthen the momentum of growth in bilateral ties, fully tap into our potential, and foster new highlights in cooperation, to create a better future for China-El Salvador relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347401.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221110_10960383.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-10","Zhao Lijian","Reuters","Canadian Foreign Minister Mélanie Joly said on Wednesday that China is an “increasingly disruptive global power”. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","These remarks by the Canadian side run counter to facts, smack of ideological bias, and blatantly interfere in China’s internal affairs. We firmly reject them and have made solemn démarches to the Canadian side. I would like to emphasize the following points:\nFirst, China is committed to peaceful development, openness, inclusiveness and win-win cooperation. We have always been a force for world peace, a contributor to global development, and a defender of the international order, a fact that has been widely recognized in the international community. China’s development brings opportunities to the world and strengthens the world’s forces for peace. No matter what stage of development we reach, we will never seek hegemony or engage in expansionism.\nSecond, peace, development and win-win cooperation are the trend of our times and the shared aspiration of countries in the Asia-Pacific. The formulation of an “Indo-Pacific strategy” is Canada’s own affair, but no matter what kind of regional strategy Canada comes up with, it should be guided by the vision of mutual benefit rather than zero-sum game. Those who cling to the Cold War zero-sum mentality, practice group politics and stoke bloc confrontation will find no support and get nowhere.\nThird, relations between countries can only be built on the basis of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit. China-Canada relations are no exception. Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong affairs are purely China’s internal affairs and brook no meddling from any country. The China-Canada relationship is at a crossroads now. Its future course hinges on whether Canada can return to the rational and practical trajectory and view China in an objective and unbiased light.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347401.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221110_10960383.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-11-11","Zhao Lijian","MASTV","US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said that the US will have the opportunity to brief Taiwan on the results of the meeting between the Chinese and US leaders. He said he is confident that Taiwan will feel “secure and comfortable” in the US’s position when it comes to US support for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the US’s commitment to the Taiwan Relations Act, which “does commit the…","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The root cause of the tensions in the Taiwan Strait is that the Taiwan authorities have been soliciting US support to seek “Taiwan independence”, and that some people in the US intend to use the Taiwan question to contain China. It is moves like this that are undermining the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe official interaction between the US and Taiwan goes against the US’s commitment of maintaining only unofficial ties with the Taiwan region. What the US said about briefing Taiwan on the meeting between the Chinese and the US heads of state gravely violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués. This is truly egregious, and China firmly rejects this.\nThe so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” unilaterally concocted by the US runs counter to the principles of the three China-US joint communiqués and the basic norms governing international relations. China has been firmly against it from the very beginning. The US has no right to place its domestic law above international law, still less use it to interfere in China’s internal affairs. When it comes to the Taiwan question, what the US should abide by is the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, not the so-called “Taiwan Relations Act”.\nChina urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official interactions and military ties with Taiwan, stop arms sales to Taiwan, follow through on the commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” with real actions, and avoid dragging China-US relations into a dangerous situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347402.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221111_10972853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-11-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answers reporters' questions\n(November 11, 2022)\nQuestion: Recently, the DPP authorities hyped the so-called “U.S.-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative” meeting as having “fruitful results.” What is your comment?\nAnswer:\nThe DPP authorities, in pursuit of their political self-interest in “independence,” have increased economic and trade collusion with the United States, selling out the interests of the people on the island in exchange for external support. Their performance on issues such as “U.S. beef” and “nuclear-contaminated food” has already let everyone see their true face. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués through practical action, and to properly handle Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221111_12486739.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-11-14","Mao Ning","Yonhap News Agency","On November 13, leaders of the ROK, the US and Japan held a meeting and released the Phnom Penh Statement on Trilateral Partnership for the Indo-Pacific. The leaders “oppose any unilateral attempts to change the status quo in waters of the Indo-Pacific”, and “reiterate the importance of maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait”. What is China’s comment?","State-to-state exchange and cooperation needs to be conducive to mutual understanding and trust between regional countries, and to peace and stability of the region and the wider world, instead of targeting any third party or their interests. If the countries concerned truly hope to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, what they need to do is to follow the one-China principle, and join China in unequivocally opposing “Taiwan independence”.\nThe Asia-Pacific is a promising land for cooperation and development, not a chessboard for major-power rivalry. The countries concerned need to follow the trend of the times, abandon the Cold War mentality, stop piecing together exclusionary circles, and refrain from affecting peace and stability in the Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347403.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221114_10974396.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","The leaders of China and the US recently held a meeting in Bali. The DPP authorities once again invoked the so-called “four insistences,” said that “peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the common expectation of the international community,” and claimed they will work with like-minded countries to counter the so-called “coercion of authoritarian systems.” What is your comment?","We have consistently worked to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and to advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. This includes maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. From 2008 to 2016, the two sides built mutual trust on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” jointly created a new situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. Since the DPP authorities came to power, they have unilaterally denied the “1992 Consensus” that both sides have long upheld, manipulated the “two-state theory,” attempted to change the status quo that both sides belong to one China, and colluded with external forces to continuously engage in provocations seeking “independence.” This is the root of the current tense and severe state of cross-Strait relations and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. What we most hope to see, and what we have always worked to maintain, is peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but “Taiwan independence” separatism and peace and stability in the Strait are irreconcilable. Only by resolutely opposing and containing “Taiwan independence” separatism can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be safeguarded.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and outsiders cannot be relied upon. Stop using the so-called banner of “democracy” to cover up for “Taiwan independence,” confusing right and wrong and deceiving the world. Persistently misjudging the situation and scheming to rely on external forces to bolster your “independence” provocations will only plunge you into an abyss of no return.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488022.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the DPP authorities and the UK held the so-called 25th “Trade Dialogue,” attended by UK International Trade Minister Hands, who traveled to Taiwan. The DPP authorities have hyped it extensively. May I ask what comment the spokesperson has?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have established diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the UK side to abide by the one-China principle and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Facts prove that the DPP authorities are accustomed to using pretexts such as economic and trade cooperation, colluding with external forces to seek political gains, “exhausting Taiwan's resources to win the favor of foreign countries,” and continuously selling out Taiwan's economic interests and the well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan residents. This trick is being seen through by more and more of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","深圳卫视直新闻记者","This year marks the 30th anniversary of the reaching of the “1992 Consensus.” The mainland has organized a series of activities. Please introduce the relevant situation. Under the current cross-Strait situation, what is the important significance of holding related activities?","This year marks the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus.” Thirty years ago, after the two sides' cross-Strait institutions were authorized by their respective sides, through negotiations in Hong Kong and a series of subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, they reached a consensus that each side would orally express that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” The consensus consists of two passages of text that were negotiated and mutually acknowledged. In these two passages, both sides expressed the stance of “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle” and “striving to seek national reunification.” Regarding the political meaning of one China, the Straits Exchange Foundation stated that both sides “have different understandings,” and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits stated that it “does not touch upon this in matters-oriented consultations,” thus setting the dispute aside for the time being. The achievement of the “1992 Consensus” reflects the political wisdom of seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and proves that as long as both sides across the Strait put national interests first and uphold the greater righteousness of the nation, they are fully capable of handling cross-Strait relations wisely.\nThe “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the anchor that steadies the course of advancing peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Facts from the past 30 years of cross-Strait relations have repeatedly proven that only by upholding the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully and stably, can compatriots on both sides benefit, and can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be guaranteed. On July 26 this year, a symposium on the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus” was held in Beijing. Wang Yang, Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended and delivered a speech, systematically reviewing and explaining the historical course, core meaning, and great significance of the “1992 Consensus.” Since the second half of the year, academic circles and civil groups on both sides of the Strait have respectively held academic seminars and round-table forums on the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus,” and compatriots from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, from Hong Kong and Macao, and overseas Chinese have also held various activities around the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus.” This fully demonstrates that upholding the “1992 Consensus” embodies the aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and that it reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times.\nWe will carry out the comprehensive strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question, implement the deployment of Taiwan work set out at the 20th National Congress of the Party, unwaveringly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and on this basis promote dialogue and consultation with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals, unite broad Taiwan compatriots to firmly defeat the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence,” firmly oppose interference by external forces, promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488021.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","The “Striving in the New Era” achievement exhibition recently opened at the Beijing Exhibition Center, and its Taiwan-related section has attracted great attention from compatriots on both sides. Please introduce the relevant information.","Since its opening on September 27, the achievement exhibition “Forging Ahead in the New Era” has drawn wide attention from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The Taiwan-related part of Unit 10, “Adhering to ‘One Country, Two Systems’ to Advance National Reunification,” in the central exhibition area presents to everyone the latest achievements in Taiwan work since the 18th National Congress.\nThe exhibition, with 56 photos, 49 physical objects, 2 videos, and a picture slideshow, vividly shows how the CPC grasped the changing times in cross-Strait relations, enriched and developed national reunification theory and Taiwan policies, proposed the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, and led cross-Strait relations in the correct direction. We uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and continuously improve the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland. We strengthen the shaping of the trend toward opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification, and resolutely curb “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, fully demonstrating our firm determination and strong capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and proclaiming: “Complete reunification of the motherland must be realized, and it certainly can be realized!” In the exhibition, the white paper “The Taiwan Question and China’s Cause of National Reunification in the New Era,” the large physical exhibit “Horizontal Electric Flanged Butterfly Valve for the South-to-North Water Diversion” designed and produced by Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland, the commemorative baseball bat “Cross-Strait Baseball Is One Family,” the painted wall “Cross-Strait Is One Family,” as well as images and objects on punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and the PLA’s targeted military exercises regarding Taiwan, have drawn great attention.\nOn October 29 and November 11, 57 outstanding Taiwan youth representatives visited the exhibition respectively. Some Taiwan youths saw photos of themselves serving as volunteers for the Beijing Winter Olympics in the exhibition and happily took group photos to commemorate the moment. Others wrote “Cross-Strait Is One Family” in the guestbook to express their feelings. The Taiwan youths said one after another that through their visit they deepened their understanding of the mainland’s development achievements and enhanced their recognition of “Cross-Strait Is One Family.” Many journalists present also visited the exhibition and reported on its content actively and objectively.\nStarting October 31, the exhibition opened to the public for reservations. We welcome more compatriots on both sides to visit the exhibition, learn the stories behind it, enhance their recognition of the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and contribute to advancing the national reunification process.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488020.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","The Comprehensive Group of the State Council Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism recently announced twenty measures to further optimize COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control. Will there be any adjustments to the prevention and control measures involving Taiwan compatriots?","On November 11, the Comprehensive Group of the Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism of the State Council issued the “Notice on Further Optimizing COVID-19 Prevention and Control Measures and Doing Prevention and Control Work Scientifically and Precisely,” announcing twenty measures to further optimize prevention and control work. The relevant competent authorities decided that, starting from 0:00 on November 18, personnel boarding cross-Strait passenger flights will be adjusted from presenting a negative nucleic acid test certificate from two tests within 48 hours before boarding to presenting a negative nucleic acid test certificate from one test within 48 hours before boarding. The test report must indicate a nucleic acid test CT value of ≥35. At the same time, the current regulations will continue to be enforced: passengers transferring through Taiwan from other countries or regions may not be carried into the mainland. Quarantine and medical observation requirements for persons entering from the Taiwan region will be adjusted in step with the latest epidemic prevention and control measures at the destination. We hope that people traveling across the Strait and relevant airlines will fully cooperate to do a good job in epidemic prevention and control together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488018.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The “Regulations on Promoting the Development of Individual Industrial and Commercial Households” were recently issued and implemented, including the provision that Taiwan residents may apply to register as individual industrial and commercial households in accordance with relevant regulations. Please introduce the relevant situation. How is this related to the policy on expanding Taiwan residents' applications…","Recently, the mainland issued and implemented the “Regulations on Promoting the Development of Individual Industrial and Commercial Households.” Formulated on the basis of the original “Regulations on Individual Industrial and Commercial Households,” and taking into account the overall development situation, problems, difficulties, and interest demands of individual industrial and commercial households, the regulations are conducive to better promoting their long-term healthy development. Article 37 stipulates that “residents of Taiwan may apply to register as individual industrial and commercial households in accordance with relevant national regulations.” In March this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Commerce, and the State Administration for Market Regulation jointly issued the “Notice on Doing a Good Job in Handling Applications by Taiwan Residents to Establish Individual Industrial and Commercial Households in Pilot Areas for Innovative Development of Service Trade,” further providing support for Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people and young people, to seek employment and start businesses on the mainland. For Taiwan compatriots, these two provisions apply equally and are consistent in spirit. Based on their own conditions and development aspirations, Taiwan compatriots may apply to establish individual industrial and commercial households in pilot areas for innovative development of service trade on the mainland or in other regions. We welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to seize the opportunity and come to the mainland to achieve greater and better development for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488019.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","The health condition of the giant panda “Tuan Tuan,” a gift from the mainland to Taiwan, concerns compatriots on both sides. Please introduce the situation of mainland experts going to Taiwan to assist in diagnosing and treating “Tuan Tuan.”","At the invitation of the Taipei Zoo, two mainland experts travelled to Taiwan from November 1 to 7 to take part in the treatment and care of the giant panda \"Tuan Tuan.\" During their stay in Taiwan, based on the earlier examination results of \"Tuan Tuan\" as well as observed physical condition and medication responses, the two experts, after discussion with the mainland expert team, proposed targeted treatment and care plan recommendations and held in-depth, detailed exchanges with the Taipei expert team. It is gratifying that \"Tuan Tuan\"'s feeding, mental state, and gait have all improved, and the duration of continuous normal walking has been steadily increasing.\nAccording to the mainland experts who went to Taiwan, the cause of \"Tuan Tuan\"'s illness still needs to be accurately determined. In view of the fact that \"Tuan Tuan\"'s physical condition is not yet suitable for anesthesia or invasive examination, and since its condition is gradually improving, the experts on both sides have reached a consensus to continue with gentle treatment methods for some time to come. At the same time, the treatment plan will be adjusted in a timely manner according to the condition, and efforts will be made to trace the cause of the illness in order to achieve better treatment results. The mainland experts will continue to maintain close communication with the Taipei expert team and provide advice and assistance in real time. If mainland experts are needed to travel to Taiwan again to assist with treatment and care later on, we will continue to provide support and assistance as we always have.\nThe giant pandas \"Tuan Tuan\" and \"Yuan Yuan\" have been settled in Taiwan from Sichuan for 14 years, and in Taiwan they have produced a pair of adorable panda cubs, \"Yuan Zai\" and \"Yuan Bao,\" and this family is deeply loved by Taiwan compatriots. Since \"Tuan Tuan\" fell ill this time, compatriots on both sides of the Strait have expressed their care and blessings in various ways, and everyone is deeply concerned, hoping that \"Tuan Tuan\" can overcome the illness and recover soon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488016.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Chiu Tai-san, head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that preparations for resuming “mini three links” flights have been completed and that Taiwan will actively coordinate with the mainland to resume them as soon as possible. What is your response?","In February 2020, the DPP authorities, citing epidemic prevention and control, unilaterally suspended direct exchanges between coastal Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas, seriously affecting the travel and exchanges of people across the Strait, especially residents of Fujian and Taiwan. We hope the DPP authorities will quickly remove the relevant restrictions and no longer harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially compatriots in Kinmen and Matsu. The mainland side has no obstacles to restoring direct exchanges between coastal Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","Taiwan’s fiscal authorities recently announced that Taiwan’s exports to the mainland and Hong Kong have recorded negative year-on-year growth for three consecutive months, and their share of total exports fell to 38.8% in the first 10 months, the lowest for the same period in nearly 18 years. Some voices on the island claim this reflects “a weakening mainland economy” and “reduced reliance of Taiwan’s economy on…","This year, facing a complex and severe domestic and international situation and shocks from unexpected factors, the Chinese mainland has efficiently coordinated epidemic prevention and control with economic and social development, accelerated the implementation of the package of policies to stabilize the economy and follow-up policy measures, and the national economy has continued to recover, with overall operation within a reasonable range. In the first three quarters, the mainland's gross domestic product exceeded 87 trillion yuan, up 3% year on year. Among them, GDP grew 3.9% year on year in the third quarter, with the economy recovering steadily and picking up noticeably.\nCross-Strait economic and trade cooperation continued to develop. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, cross-Strait trade in the first 10 months of this year reached US$271.044 billion, up 2.4% year on year. Taiwan's exports to the mainland were US$201.759 billion, and its imports from the mainland were US$69.285 billion. Cross-Strait trade volume, Taiwan's exports to the mainland, and Taiwan's imports from the mainland all hit record highs for the same period.\nThis shows that the mainland economy has demonstrated strong resilience and great potential, and cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation remains the driving force and opportunity for Taiwan's economic development, in line with the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Any words or deeds that attempt to talk down the mainland economy or seek to “decouple and break supply chains” are futile. The Chinese mainland fully, accurately and comprehensively implements the new development philosophy, accelerates the building of a new development dispensation, and focuses on promoting high-quality development. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested businesses coming to the mainland to develop will find more opportunities, broader space and better prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","On November 6, the Ningbo fishing vessel “Yongfa 1” successfully rescued 48 crew members of a Taiwan fishing vessel in distress in the North Pacific. Please introduce the relevant situation.","At around noon on November 6, the fishing vessel “Yongfa 1,” belonging to Zhejiang Ningbo Yongfa Overseas Fishery Co., Ltd., was operating in the North Pacific Ocean (153°36′ E, 42°39′ N) when it found that a fishing vessel nearby was in distress and calling for help. The vessel immediately approached the scene and found that the hull of Taiwan's fishing vessel “Xiangqing” was on fire, and its crew had been transferred to two life rafts. “Yongfa 1” quickly and safely transferred the 48 crew members on the two life rafts, and conducted a search and rescue for one missing crew member from that vessel, but regrettably, he was not found. On the afternoon of November 6, the 48 rescued crew members were safely transferred to another Taiwan fishing vessel.\nWhen vessels on either side of the Taiwan Strait or in other sea areas encounter danger during production operations, passing vessels and maritime search and rescue agencies on both sides actively participate in rescue operations and make every effort to search. This is both an act of great love that puts life first, and a demonstration of the brotherly bond between compatriots on both sides who look out for one another.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488015.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","Regarding the restoration of the cross-Strait 'mini three links,' Su Tseng-chang said that 'government-to-government consultation across the Strait must be insisted upon.' But a Xiamen shipping company said that the service can resume as long as private enterprises coordinate well. What is your comment on this? Is it true that resuming the 'mini three links' only requires businesses on both sides to reach…","Yesterday (November 15), some Taiwan compatriots residing in Fujian and reporters stationed in Fujian went together to Xiamen Wutong Wharf and to shipping companies to learn about the relevant situation firsthand and listen to the views and concerns of these operators. As I said earlier, the saying goes that only the one who tied the bell can untie it. The suspension in 2020 of direct exchanges between coastal Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas was a unilateral action by the DPP authorities, yet their restoration now requires both sides to hold “official communication.” If this is not political manipulation, what is it? If it is not an excuse to delay restoration and shift blame to the mainland, what is it?\nI would like to emphasize once again that the mainland side has no obstacles to restoring direct exchanges between coastal Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas, and I believe the relevant cross-Strait operators have none either. A mature set of norms and practices that has proven effective is already in place. As long as the DPP authorities remove the barriers they have set up, cross-Strait operators can handle specific matters such as flights according to the actual needs of people on both sides, and flights between Kinmen and Xiamen can resume normally. If the DPP authorities truly care for the people on the island, they should promptly take action to remove artificial restrictions and stop harming the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially those in Kinmen and Matsu.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221116_12488017.htm"],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Two questions. First question: It is reported that the 2022 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting is expected to be held in Xiamen from December 19 to 20. Taiwan’s representative Liu Chao-hsuan plans to lead a delegation to Beijing at the end of the month. Please provide information on this. Second question: The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently opened applications for mainland trainees to enter…","On the first question: It is understood that the two sides are communicating about holding this year's annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit. If there is definite news, it will be released in a timely manner. Our position has been consistent: we support, encourage, and welcome more exchanges and cooperation among cross-Strait economic and trade figures, and jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn the second question: We have always advocated strengthening exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In February 2020, the DPP authorities, using the epidemic as a pretext, comprehensively banned mainland personnel from traveling to Taiwan, obstructing cross-Strait personnel exchanges. To date, we have never imposed restrictions on cross-Strait personnel exchanges, including trainees and exchange students. There were none in the past, there are none now, and there will be none in the future. As for the decline in the number of mainland students recruited by Taiwan that you mentioned, the reasons are well known, and you may ask the DPP authorities to answer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","I have two questions. First, the Chinese and US heads of state held a meeting a few days ago, and at this meeting President Xi Jinping clearly pointed out that the Taiwan question is the core of the core of China’s core interests, and that he hopes to see and always strive to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. How does the spokesperson view the message conveyed therein? Second, Taiwan’s cultural…","On the first question: after the meeting between the leaders of China and the United States in Bali, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi gave a detailed briefing to the media, which were widely reported. I want to stress two points here. First, the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves to decide, and no external force is allowed to interfere.\nSecond, the connotation of the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question is clear. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” and we are committed, on the basis of upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and improving and developing cross-Strait relations. We ardently hope for, and will make every effort to pursue, national reunification by peaceful means. However, “The tree wants stillness, but the wind will not cease.” We do not promise to renounce the use of force. This is directed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist activities, as well as interference by external forces, and is by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. As we have said before, the future of cross-Strait relations lies in the hands of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nOn the second question: whether it is Hokkien or Hakka, both are local dialects of China and part of Chinese culture. Just as many Taiwan youth who went to Xiamen, Zhangzhou and Quanzhou for the first time found that the local people speak the same way they do, this fully shows that both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ so-called “rectification of names” is merely another farce in their deliberate push for “de-Sinicization,” and it cannot change the Chinese cultural identity and Chinese national identity deeply rooted in Taiwan’s society. As a Taiwan netizen put it, “Even if you change the name, can you erase the Chinese imprint engraved in your DNA?”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: You just mentioned that the mainland side has further optimized COVID-19 epidemic prevention and control measures. However, there are currently only four flight destinations across the Taiwan Strait, and the number of flights is quite limited. As Taiwan opens its border controls, more people will travel across the Strait. Will the mainland side consider gradually restoring flight destinations and…","On the first question: as is well known, since February 2020, without any communication with the mainland side, the DPP authorities not only suspended the “mini three links” but also unilaterally suspended all cross-Strait passenger flights other than those to and from the four locations of Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, and Chengdu. Over the past year or more, the DPP authorities have repeatedly said they would gradually restore cross-Strait personnel exchanges and talked about doing this and that, and everyone has heard this countless times, yet it has always been “all we hear is footsteps on the stairs, but no one comes down.” We have consistently encouraged personnel exchanges across the Strait. As long as each side does a good job in epidemic prevention and control, there is no problem with personnel exchanges across the Strait. As soon as the DPP authorities remove the barriers they have set up, we are glad to see cross-Strait routes and destinations gradually restored and expanded.\nOn the second question: I recall that a similar scene occurred during the drone show at the New Year's Eve gala in Kaohsiung last year. The dramatic reversal from “pride of Taiwan” to “thorough investigation and ban” cannot but be seen as a kind of irony. The mainland's drone industry leads the world, and it is entirely normal for all sectors of Taiwan to purchase mainland drones. The DPP authorities, however, always view things through tinted glasses and readily impose “bans,” which shows that they have a guilty conscience and sick minds.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The 5th China International Import Expo Recently Concluded. Please have the spokesperson introduce the participation of Taiwan businesses and enterprises in the exhibition.","This session of the China International Import Expo (CIIE) has more than 20 Taiwanese companies exhibiting, covering a wide range of fields with a high degree of scale and good product quality. According to statistics from relevant units, the exhibiting Taiwanese companies have an expected transaction volume of US$535 million. The heads of the exhibiting Taiwanese companies also said that through the CIIE platform they expanded brand influence and tapped into the mainland's huge domestic market, and they will continue to participate in the CIIE, actively seize development opportunities on the mainland, and achieve mutual benefit and win-win outcomes while developing themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Taiwan's defense authorities recently announced that Taiwan and the US signed, this month, the third-phase follow-on maintenance case of the “Long-Range Early Warning Radar System,” worth NT$15.76 billion, under which the US will provide five years of logistics and support services. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","If these NT$15.7 billion were used to improve people's livelihoods on the island and develop the economy, wouldn't that be better than giving it away to Americans for nothing? The DPP authorities should be clear that seeking “independence” through provocation has no way out, and that trying to rely on external forces to “seek independence by force” can only further hasten their own destruction. If one wants to ease cross-Strait relations and stabilize the situation in the Taiwan Strait, then return to the common basis of the “1992 Consensus.” There is no other way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中国时报记者","The National Palace Museum in Taipei recently suffered damage to three cultural relics due to negligence by its staff. CCTV once released a documentary, “I Repair Cultural Relics in the Palace Museum,” which gave all walks of life a glimpse of the superb skills of mainland cultural relic restorers. May I ask the spokesperson whether the Palace Museums on both sides of the Strait have a chance to exchange with…","We have noted reports of damage to artifacts at the National Palace Museum in Taipei, and we deeply regret this. The Palace Museums on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and are an integrated whole connected by blood. The artifacts they hold are treasures of the Chinese nation and testimony to and inheritance of China's long history and brilliant culture. They carry the inseparable cultural lineage and historical bonds between the two sides and embody the shared humanistic feelings of Chinese people. Ensuring the safety of artifacts is a fundamental responsibility of the relevant parties in Taiwan.\nWe have always been committed to promoting cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and deepening integrated development between the two sides. The Palace Museums on both sides have a solid foundation for cooperation, and in the future they can continue to engage in in-depth exchanges, jointly carry forward excellent traditional Chinese culture, and jointly safeguard the precious cultural heritage of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-16","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾中视记者","As Taiwan's county and city magistrate local elections approach, Tsai Ing-wen has once again played the card of 'resisting China and defending Taiwan' to win votes. However, we note that at the ASEAN Summit and the G20 Summit, Southeast Asian countries, the United States and other nations have shifted toward cooperative talks with the mainland. What is your comment on the DPP's insistence on playing the…","The DPP authorities are accustomed to exaggerating the so-called \"mainland threat,\" attempting to seek political self-interest by stirring up \"anti-China and hatred of China\" populism. This routine is unoriginal; Taiwan's people have long seen through it and grown tired of it, and it cannot fool anyone. With the mainland's development and progress, and as China's international cooperation expands in scope and its influence grows, this routine of the DPP authorities will find less and less market on the island. In fact, more and more Taiwan people have come to realize that \"opposing China\" not only cannot \"protect Taiwan,\" but instead will only \"harm Taiwan,\" only pushing Taiwan further toward the abyss of disaster.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all for attending.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202211/t20221116_12488010.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-18","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲18日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 18 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters' questions on the 18th, reiterated: Regarding the resumption of cross-Strait “small three links,” there is no obstacle on the mainland side. Relevant parties have made full preparations and can begin operations at any time. We advise the DPP authorities not to continue harming the vital interests of compatriots on both…","Zhu Fenglian said that since 2020, the DPP authorities, using epidemic prevention as a pretext, have unilaterally cut off direct exchanges between the coastal areas of Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas, seriously affecting cross-Strait personnel exchanges, especially exchanges between people in Fujian and Taiwan. Over the past three years, in the face of persistent calls and strong demands from the broad Taiwan public, especially fellow townspeople in Kinmen and Matsu, the DPP authorities have, on the one hand, feigned willingness to resume exchanges, while on the other hand creating various pretexts to drag things out. This fully exposes their hypocrisy.\nZhu Fenglian said that, as is well known, the “mini three links” between the coastal areas of Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu have been in operation for many years. The routes, ports of call, participating shipping companies, and the customs clearance, entry and quarantine inspection arrangements have formed a mature and effective set of norms and practices. As long as the DPP authorities remove the obstacles they deliberately set, relevant cross-Strait industry players can, based on the actual needs of people on both sides, communicate under the existing model to handle specific matters such as flights, and the direct flights between Kinmen and Xiamen can return to normal.\nZhu Fenglian said that in the face of facts, the DPP authorities have repeatedly insisted that resumption must go through so-called “inter-governmental consultations” or “official-level communication.” This shows that their claimed resumption of the “mini three links” is false, while keeping it closed is real; that restoring cross-Strait exchanges is false, while continuing to block them is real; and that caring about people's well-being is false, while seeking personal political gain is real. We believe Taiwan compatriots see this with perfect clarity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221118_12488668.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲19日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 19: Regarding the unfortunate death of the giant panda “Tuan Tuan,” gifted by the mainland to Taiwan, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters’ questions on the 19th, said: The mainland’s Giant Panda Protection and Research Center received notice today from Taipei Zoo that the giant panda “Tuan Tuan” stopped beating at 1:48 p.m. We are heartbroken and deeply regret…","Zhu Fenglian said that after the giant panda ‘Tuan Tuan’ fell ill, compatriots on both sides have been deeply concerned. The Giant Panda Protection and Research Center set up an expert group, maintained continuous online communication with Taipei Zoo, and at the invitation sent two experts to Taiwan to assist with diagnosis, treatment, and nursing care. We thank the professional teams on both sides, Taipei Zoo, and all relevant parties for their efforts to save ‘Tuan Tuan,’ and we hope relevant parties across the Strait will continue to do well in exchange and cooperation on giant panda protection.\nZhu Fenglian said that 14 years ago, the giant pandas ‘Tuan Tuan’ and ‘Yuan Yuan’ went to Taiwan to make their home, which was an important symbol of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Over the years, they have brought countless joy and fond memories to Taiwan compatriots. Today, many people on both sides have expressed their mourning and remembrance of ‘Tuan Tuan’ in various ways. As ‘national treasures,’ giant pandas deserve to be cherished by compatriots on both sides. The mutual understanding and positive interaction between the hearts of the people on both sides should be jointly cherished and safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221119_12488910.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-11-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The head of Taiwan's defense department recently said that if cross-strait war breaks out, they will absolutely fight to the end and absolutely have a chance of winning. It is also reported that a video of the PLA Xiamen ship and the Taiwan military's Magong ship has attracted attention online. In the video, the Taiwan Magong ship unreasonably shouts at the Xiamen ship, and the Xiamen ship responds forcefully:…","Regarding the response of the Xiamen ship, I would like to give them a thumbs-up. The lines unilaterally drawn by Taiwan, one after another, are all illegal and invalid. They cannot change the fact that Taiwan belongs to China, and they cannot stop the PLA’s advance in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nAs for the clamor of some people in the DPP authorities, which is like an ant trying to shake a tree, I want to warn them: if anyone dares to split Taiwan from China, the PLA will certainly act resolutely and deliver a head-on blow.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10201226.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-11-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the “U.S.-China Economic and Security Review Commission” under the U.S. Congress recently released its annual report, recommending that ways to strengthen Taiwan's defense be assessed and that the U.S. capacity to deny a mainland attack on Taiwan be enhanced. What comments do you have on this?","China firmly opposes US-Taiwan military ties and US arms sales to Taiwan. On November 14, when the heads of state of China and the United States met, US President Biden reaffirmed that the US does not support “Taiwan independence,” nor “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan,” and has no intention of coming into conflict with China. We hope the US side can genuinely implement this policy position and abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, so as not to further harm the common interests of China and the United States.\nIt must be emphasized that Taiwan is part of China, a sacred and inalienable part of China's territory. Any practice that strengthens US-Taiwan military ties is an erroneous act that interferes in China's internal affairs and violates US commitments. Any attempt to arm Taiwan to contain mainland China is nothing but a pipe dream, and is doomed to crash and bleed against the steel Great Wall of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10201229.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-11-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 26 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the evening of the 26th regarding the results of Taiwan’s “nine-in-one” elections, saying: We have noted the results of this election. The results reflect the mainstream public opinion on the island that “seeks peace, seeks stability, and wants to live well.” We will continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots to jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221127_12490685.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-11-28","Zhao Lijian","AFP","Firstly, the Vatican said that the recent appointment of a bishop in Jiangxi province violates the Sino-Vatican agreement. What’s China’s response? Second, Canada recently released its diplomatic strategy for the Asia-Pacific region designed to mitigate risks posed by China. The Canadian Foreign Minister also said that China does not respect international norms in a newspaper interview. What’s China’s comment?","On your first question, I’m not aware of what you mentioned. I need to point out that in recent years, China and the Vatican have maintained engagement and reached a host of important common understandings. The sustained improvement of ties between China and the Vatican has also contributed to the harmonious development of Catholicism in China. China stands ready to work with the Vatican to continue to expand common understandings on friendly ties and jointly uphold the spirit of the provisional agreement.\nOn your second question, the content on China in the strategy released by Canada is dominated by ideological bias. It hypes up the so-called “China threat” and makes unwarranted accusations against China. The Chinese side is gravely concerned and strongly opposes this, and we have made solemn démarches to the Canadian side.\nChina has all along been committed to peaceful development, advocated openness and inclusiveness and engaged in win-win cooperation. China has been a defender of world peace, a contributor to global development and an upholder of international order. China’s development creates opportunities for the world and strengthens the force for world peace. No matter what level of development China achieves, it will never seek hegemony or expansion. Who is safeguarding world peace and promoting common development and who is fanning up the Cold War mentality and hyping up bloc confrontation? The international community knows all too well.\nThe principle of non-interference in each other’s internal affairs is a “golden rule” governing state-to-state exchanges. Affairs related to Taiwan, Xinjiang and Hong Kong are purely China’s internal affairs, and we accept no finger-pointing from external forces. The Chinese side will not waver in its resolve to safeguard the nation’s sovereignty, security and development interests. The Canadian side has said on many occasions that it attaches importance to its relations with China and would like to improve and grow the relations with eyes set on the future. The Canadian side needs to honor its words, show sincerity and goodwill, seek common ground while reserving differences, adopt reasonable and practical policies towards China, and deliver its commitments with concrete efforts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347413.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202211/t20221128_10981777.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-11-30","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","To implement the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and General Secretary Xi Jinping's reply letter to Taiwan youth attending the Straits Forum, and to further promote mutual learning among cross-Strait youth and foster spiritual resonance among compatriots on both sides, the centralized events of the 10th Straits Youth Festival, jointly hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the All-China Youth Federation, and the People's Government of Fujian Province, will be held in Fuzhou, Fujian, from December 1 to 5. This is the first large-scale cross-Strait youth exchange event since the 20th CPC National Congress. During the event, a series of activities will be held, including the Straits Youth Festival Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Cultural Exchange Week, “Entering the CPPCC: Taiwan Youth Speak,” the Straits Weather Youth Gathering, the Fujian-Taiwan Talent Cooperation Forum, and the Straits Rural Revitalization Life Festival.\nThe 10th Straits Youth Festival takes “Integrated Development, Cultural Inheritance” as its theme and “10 Years of Straits Youth, 10 Brands, 10 Stories” as its main thread. It is expected that in 2022, 36 events will be held throughout the year in a combination of online and offline formats, covering a wide range of fields including Chinese traditional culture, Digital China, the Fuzhou-Matsu Shared Home, rural construction and rural entrepreneurship, and talent work. At the same time, 1,756 job positions from 155 units will be released to Taiwan youth, helping to establish a number of characteristic Taiwan youth entrepreneurship and employment bases in areas such as sports and music, and providing more convenience for Taiwan youth to study, work, start businesses, and live on the mainland. So far, 20 events have been successfully held, with nearly 2,000 Taiwan youth directly participating both online and offline.\nSince the first event was held in 2013, the Straits Youth Festival, combining centralized events with series events, has cumulatively held 265 cross-Strait youth exchange events and attracted 30,000 cross-Strait youth participants. It has become the “golden brand” of cross-Strait youth exchanges and an important platform for Taiwan youth to pursue, build, and realize their dreams on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202211/t20221130_12491555.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-12-05","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","The Financial Times reported that Canada plans to sail more warships through the Taiwan Strait to affirm the waters claimed by Beijing are international. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","We have made it clear on multiple occasions that China has sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction in the Taiwan Strait. China always respects the navigational rights that countries are entitled to in accordance with international law. However, we firmly reject any country’s provocation and threat against China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347418.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221205_10985354.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-06","Mao Ning","AFP","A group of Australian lawmakers have arrived in Taiwan for a five-day visit. What’s China’s response?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and the prerequisite and political foundation for the development of friendly relations between China and other countries. The Australian side should earnestly adhere to the one-China principle, stop all forms of official interaction with the Taiwan region and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan-independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347419.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221206_10985881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-12-06","Tan Kefei","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","Recently, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2022 “China Military and Security Development Report,” which distorts China's national defense policy and military strategy, baselessly speculates about the development of China's military power, and crudely interferes in China's internal affairs on the Taiwan question. This is its customary trick of hyping the so-called “China military threat.” China expresses strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this, and has lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues a defensive national defense policy. It has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a defender of the international order. China develops its military power to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. No matter how far it develops, it will never seek hegemony and never engage in expansion. By contrast, in the nearly 250 years since its founding, the United States has been at peace for only 16 of them. It stirs up trouble everywhere for its own selfish interests, creates division and confrontation in the world, and wherever it goes it brings mostly turmoil and disaster. Facts have repeatedly proven that the United States is the greatest troublemaker and the greatest disruptor of world peace and stability.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is China's own affair, to be decided by the Chinese people. At present, some people on the U.S. side cling to the illusion of “using Taiwan to contain China,” and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities seek to “rely on the United States to seek independence.” This is the root cause of the tension in the Taiwan Strait. We are committed to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. The Chinese military has the confidence and capability to defeat any external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and to achieve the complete reunification of the country.\nThe U.S. report points fingers at and makes baseless speculations about the modernization of China's nuclear forces, when in fact it is the United States that most needs to deeply reflect on its own nuclear policy. The United States possesses the world's largest nuclear arsenal, continuously upgrades its “triad” nuclear forces, vigorously develops and seeks forward deployment of tactical nuclear weapons, lowers the threshold for the use of nuclear weapons, and spreads nuclear weapons through the trilateral security partnership among the United States, the United Kingdom, and Australia. It has increasingly become a source of nuclear conflict. It must be emphasized that China firmly pursues a nuclear strategy of self-defense. It always adheres to a policy of no first use of nuclear weapons at any time and under any circumstances, and it keeps its nuclear forces at the minimum level required by national security.\nWe urge the U.S. side to discard Cold War thinking, correct its erroneous perceptions of China, view China's national defense and military development objectively and rationally, stop issuing erroneous remarks and relevant reports, and genuinely take concrete actions to put China-U.S. and military-to-military relations back on a path of healthy and stable development.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/4927969.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278448.html",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-12-08","Mao Ning","China Daily","According to reports, the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said in a press release on December 6 that the State Department had approved sales of aircraft parts and equipment to Taiwan. Taiwan’s defence department has said the sales will help its air force operations. What’s your comment?","US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region are a blatant violation of the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The arms sales undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, harm peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and send a wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and rejects them. We will act firmly to defend our own sovereignty and security interests.\nWe urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués and earnestly act on the commitment made by the US leadership of not supporting “Taiwan independence”. It should stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait, stop using Taiwan to contain China and stop moving even further down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347421.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221208_10987179.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-12-08","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. recently announced that it will sell Taiwan military aircraft components and related equipment worth a total of US$428 million. What is your comment on this?","The US side's move openly disregards China's solemn position, once again brazenly interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously endangers China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously damages China-US relations, China-US military-to-military relations, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China is strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly opposes it, and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nIn recent years, on the Taiwan question, the US side has made solemn commitments to China on the one hand, while on the other hand it has hollowed out and emptied the one-China principle. It has continued arms sales to Taiwan, pushed through negative Taiwan-related bills, and sent senior officials to visit Taiwan, further aggravating tension across the Taiwan Strait. The US side's words are still ringing in our ears, yet it has gone back on its word. This self-contradictory conduct fully exposes its hypocritical face of saying one thing and doing another, and seriously damages its political credibility and international reputation.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the foundation of the political basis of China-US relations, and it is the first red line that China-US relations must not cross. “Taiwan independence” and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Resolving the Taiwan question is the Chinese people's own affair and China's internal affair. We urge the US side to genuinely respect China's core interests and major concerns. If it repeatedly breaks its word and persists in recklessness, condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence,” it will inevitably aggravate tension across the Taiwan Strait and will ultimately bring disaster upon itself. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will resolutely thwart any form of external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/4928236.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278478.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-12-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 8 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters’ questions on the 8th, said: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan, China. The U.S. arms sales seriously violate the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China–U.S. joint communiqués. They condone and support “Taiwan independence” forces and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the United States to genuinely abide by the One-China Principle, immediately stop arms sales to Taiwan and military contacts between the United States and Taiwan, and turn its political commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” into concrete action.\nA reporter asked: On December 6, relevant U.S. government departments announced two arms sales plans for Taiwan. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. “Resisting unification by force,” colluding with external forces, and provoking and seeking “independence” will only push compatriots in Taiwan into a fire pit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221208_12493730.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-12-09","Mao Ning","AFP","The US House of Representatives just passed a defense spending bill that includes up to $10 billion in military grant assistance for Taiwan over the next five years. Do you have any reaction to that?","We firmly reject inserting negative content about China into the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA).\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. The US side needs to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, remove the negative content about China from the bill, stop playing the Taiwan card and using Taiwan to contain China, stop military contact with Taiwan, and refrain from further undermining China-US relations. China will take all necessary measures to resolutely uphold its sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347422.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221209_10988033.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-12-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 9: In response to the recent agreement reached by the U.S. House and Senate on the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” which contains negative content related to Taiwan, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 9th, saying: Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated. The relevant U.S. bill that inserts content related to Taiwan seriously violates the basic norms of international relations, seriously interferes in China's internal affairs, and seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. We firmly oppose this. We urge the U.S. side to immediately stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question and not to engage in any form of military contact with the Taiwan region of China.\nA reporter asked: The U.S. House and Senate recently reached consensus on the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” which includes negative Taiwan-related content such as “providing Taiwan with US$10 billion in military financing over the next five years” and “accelerating arms sales to Taiwan.” The DPP authorities have been hyping this heavily. What comments do you have on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said that the DPP authorities' “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221210_12494170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2022-12-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 9 (Reporter) — Recently, media on the island reported that the mainland had banned imports of Taiwan’s Wuzai fish, Pacific saury and other aquatic products without warning, and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed it would lodge a stern protest. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on the 9th and said that reports of the mainland’s so-called suspension of imports of Taiwan’s Wuzai fish, Pacific saury, squid and other aquatic products are inconsistent with the facts, and the so-called “stern protest” is even more unreasonable.\nZhu Fenglian stated that, in order to implement the Food Safety Law and its implementing regulations and other provisions, the General Administration of Customs issued the Administrative Provisions on the Registration of Overseas Manufacturers of Imported Food (General Administration of Customs Order No. 248) in April 2021, which took effect on January 1, 2022. These provisions optimized the registration procedures, implemented categorized management of different types of overseas manufacturers, clarified the主体 responsibility of enterprises and the supervisory responsibility of the competent authorities at their location, and also help safeguard food safety for consumers. The competent authorities concerned have already notified the Taiwan side of relevant matters and requirements through existing channels of contact, and have handled the registration of Taiwan food manufacturers exporting to the mainland in accordance with relevant provisions. Enterprises that have updated their registration information as required and passed review have continued to export to the mainland normally.\nShe said that the so-called “ban on imports without warning” is purely deliberate hype. It is understood that the registration information of some Taiwan food enterprises exporting to the mainland is incomplete and does not meet the mainland’s requirements, so the competent authorities have temporarily not granted registration to these enterprises. This is a normal food safety regulatory measure. We hope Taiwan food enterprises will promptly provide registration information that meets the requirements to the competent authorities. At the same time, we warn the relevant departments on the island to immediately stop any political manipulation and not do anything foolish that harms the island’s operators.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221210_12494171.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-12-12","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US will send a delegation to China in the coming days. This follows up on Joe Biden’s meeting with President Xi at the G20 in Indonesia. Does the foreign ministry have any information about this delegation’s visit and what issues would be discussed?","On December 11 and 12, Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng held talks with visiting US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel Kritenbrink and National Security Council Senior Director for China Laura Rosenberger in Langfang, Hebei.\nThe two sides had in-depth communication on following through on the common understandings between the two heads of state in Bali, advancing consultations on the principles guiding China-US relations, properly handling important and sensitive issues in bilateral relations including the Taiwan question and strengthening interactions at all levels and cooperation in relevant areas. The two sides also had a broad exchange of views on international and regional issues of mutual interest.\nThe two sides agreed that the meeting and talks are candid, in-depth, and constructive, and agreed to maintain communication.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347423.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221212_10989293.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-12","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Just to go back to the meeting. I think you said it was in Langfang. Can you talk about what the Chinese and US officials talked about? And did the US officials have the quarantine?","As I just shared with you, on December 11 and 12, Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng held talks with visiting US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel Kritenbrink and National Security Council Senior Director for China Laura Rosenberger in Langfang, Hebei. The two sides had in-depth communication on following through on the common understandings between the two heads of state in Bali, advancing consultations on the principles guiding China-US relations, properly handling important and sensitive issues in bilateral relations including the Taiwan question and strengthening interactions at all levels and cooperation in relevant areas. The two sides also had a broad exchange of views on international and regional issues of mutual interest. The two sides agreed that the meeting and talks are candid, in-depth, and constructive, and agreed to maintain communication.\nAs for the arrangements related to COVID control you just mentioned, arrangements are made according to the current COVID policies.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347423.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221212_10989293.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-13","Wang Wenbin","CNR","Yesterday China announced that Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng held talks with visiting US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel Kritenbrink and National Security Council Senior Director for China Laura Rosenberger in Langfang, Hebei, which has received a lot of attention. Can you share more details? Was the Taiwan question discussed during the talks?","Yesterday I briefed you on the talks. On December 11 and 12, Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng held talks with visiting US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel Kritenbrink and National Security Council Senior Director for China Laura Rosenberger in Langfang, Hebei. The two sides had in-depth communication on following through on the common understandings between the two heads of state in Bali, advancing consultations on the principles guiding China-US relations, properly handling important and sensitive issues in bilateral relations including the Taiwan question and strengthening interactions at all levels and cooperation in relevant areas. The two sides also had a broad exchange of views on international and regional issues of mutual interest.\nThe Chinese side noted during the talks that implementing the two leaders’ important common understandings reached in Bali should be front and center for both sides in stabilizing and growing China-US relations. Both sides need to firmly adhere to the strategic guidance of head-of-state diplomacy, follow through on the two presidents’ common understandings to the letter, spare no effort in the whole-process management of bilateral relations, and send an unequivocal positive message to the wider world. Both sides need to act with a great sense of responsibility to our two countries, the world and history, strengthen communication and dialogue, carry out mutually beneficial cooperation, properly manage differences and bring China-US relations back onto the track of sound and steady development. The zero-sum Cold War mentality must be abandoned, ideological antagonism and bloc confrontation must be rejected, and decoupling, supply disruption and sci-tech suppression must be stopped.\nThe Chinese side stressed that it has remained committed to the constructive approach of growing relations with the US on the basis of the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, and that China will not waver in its resolve to uphold its sovereignty, security and development interests. The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests, the bedrock of the political foundation of China-U.S. relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. The Chinese side reiterated its solemn position on the US side’s erroneous acts such as high-level exchanges with Taiwan, arms sales to Taiwan and Taiwan-related legislation, and urged the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués with concrete actions.\nThe Chinese side noted that China does not shy away or flinch from competition. However, the Chinese side is against defining the entire China-US relations by competition and seeking containment and suppression in the name of competition. The US and China have their respective sets of values. What the two sides should do is respect each other, instead of imposing its values on others, still less interfering in other countries’ internal affairs. China is committed to upholding the UN-centered international system, the international order underpinned by international law, and the basic norms governing international relations built on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. We do not accept the so-called “rules” defined by individual countries or a small group of them. China handles individual cases in accordance with the law, and the US should respect facts and the rule of law in China.\nOn matters such as the Ukraine issue and the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue, Vice Foreign Minister Xie Feng reiterated China’s clear and consistent position.\nThe two sides agreed that the talks were candid, in-depth, and constructive, and agreed to maintain communication and follow through on the important common understandings between the two heads of state.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347424.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221213_10989848.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-16","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Japan will describe China as an unprecedented strategic challenge in a new national security policy. This is obviously done because Japan feels that China is a greater threat than in the past. How does the foreign ministry respond to this?","China is always committed to maintaining peace and stability in the Asia-Pacific and the world. China is a partner and an opportunity for the development of all countries. Japan’s new defense policy ignores facts, deviates from its commitment to China-Japan relations and the common understandings between the two countries, and groundlessly discredits China’s defense building and normal military activities. China resolutely opposes this and has made serious démarches to the Japanese side through diplomatic channels.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no interference by any external forces. The Japanese side in particular needs to be prudent on the Taiwan question, honor its commitments and refrain from sending wrong signals. China’s position on maritime issues is consistent and clear. The Japanese side has been allowing right-wing forces to cause trouble in the East China Sea, and has colluded with certain countries to hype up and even create tensions in the South China Sea. Such moves pose the biggest challenge to the peace and stability in the region. The Japanese side should stop making provocations and stirring up trouble on maritime issues for selfish geopolitical interests.\nChina and Japan are close neighbors and important countries in the region. Maintaining and developing friendly and cooperative relations between China and Japan is in the fundamental interests of the two countries and peoples. We once again urge the Japanese side to adhere to the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan, effectively reflect in its policies and act upon the political consensus that the two countries are cooperative partners and do not pose a threat to each other. Hyping up the “China threat” to find an excuse for its military build-up is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347428.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221216_10991336.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-12-19","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Question: Recently, the DPP authorities have frequently claimed that the mainland is creating trade barriers and unfairly discriminating against the registration of Taiwan food enterprises. What is your comment?\nAnswer: The DPP authorities continue to maliciously distort the facts. This is purely deliberate defamation and an obvious political manipulation to cover up their wrongdoing.\nIn April 2021, the mainland issued the “Administrative Provisions on Registration of Overseas Manufacturers of Imported Food” (General Administration of Customs Decree No. 248), which took effect on January 1, 2022. These provisions apply to the registration and management of food producers, processors, and storage enterprises of all countries and regions exporting food to the mainland. The relevant regulations have legal basis, are open and transparent, conform to international rules and common practice, and fully take into account the principle of trade facilitation. The competent authorities notified the WTO in accordance with relevant WTO rules, and in October 2021 notified the Taiwan side of the relevant matters and requirements.\nUnder the requirements of General Administration of Customs Decree No. 248, the competent mainland authorities promptly review registration applications submitted by Taiwan food enterprises. Applications that meet the requirements are promptly registered, and for applications that do not meet the requirements, the specific reasons are notified one by one. The deadline for enterprises to supplement their registration information was extended from June 30, 2022 to August 31. Enterprises that have updated their registration information as required and passed review have continued to export normally to the mainland.\nFrom April 2021 to August 2022, there was ample time to properly handle the registration matters of Taiwan food enterprises, and the problem of incomplete or non-standard registration information for some Taiwan food enterprises is not difficult to solve. Rather than taking effective measures to assist the relevant enterprises, the DPP authorities have slandered the mainland's normal food safety regulatory measures as “trade barriers” and “discriminatory treatment.” This fully exposes their essence of disregarding the interests of businesses on the island and pursuing the political self-interest of one party.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221219_12495801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-12-20","Mao Ning","TASS","The newly-appointed Guatemalan “Ambassador” to Taipei announced on Monday that Guatemala plans to host a summit for ‘Taiwan-friendly’ countries next March and hopes that the leader of Taiwan will attend. Do you have any response to this?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a widely accepted norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities will not succeed in political manipulation by using countries having so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan. The relevant countries need to see where the world trend is moving and come to decisions that are in keeping with the trend.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347430.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221220_10992544.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-20","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","It is reported that the leader of Taiwan met with some visiting members of the European Parliament earlier today. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and the political foundation for China-EU relations. As an official institution of the EU, the European Parliament must abide by the one-China principle.\nChina firmly opposes official exchanges of any form between the EU and Taiwan. We urge the EU to earnestly observe the one-China principle and act prudently, so as to avoid disrupting the overall China-EU relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347430.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221220_10992544.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2022-12-23","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲23日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 23 -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fengling, answering reporters' questions on the 23rd, said that there are no obstacles on the mainland's side to restoring direct exchanges between coastal Fujian and the Kinmen and Matsu areas. We hope the DPP authorities will keep the well-being of compatriots in mind, thoroughly remove the obstacles they have unilaterally set…","Zhu Fenglian said that with the Spring Festival approaching, the demand of Taiwan compatriots for travel across the Strait is increasing. We are willing to adopt optimization measures and will do our utmost to meet the demand for exchanges between compatriots on both sides through various means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221223_12496721.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2022-12-24","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","At 24 December, Beijing time, the U.S. president signed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” which includes a number of provisions concerning China. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The U.S. side has issued the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” which contains multiple negative provisions targeting China. Disregarding the facts, it hypes up the “China threat,” arbitrarily interferes in China's internal affairs, and seeks excuses for increasing military spending and maintaining hegemony. It attempts to place a domestic bill full of conjecture and prejudice above the basic norms of international relations. This not only harms China's national sovereignty, security, and development interests, but also poisons China-U.S. and China-U.S. military relations. China expresses strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this and has lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nChina steadfastly follows the path of peaceful development, consistently implements a defensive national defense policy, always takes concrete actions to safeguard world peace and promote common development, and promotes the building of a community with a shared future for mankind. The growth and advancement of the Chinese military into the world has always been a firm force for maintaining world peace and stability. This is clearly seen by the international community and cannot be defamed. In sharp contrast, the United States stubbornly pursues the priority of its own national interests, arbitrarily launches wars and creates conflicts against other countries for its own selfish interests, causing large numbers of innocent civilian casualties and displacement. Facts have repeatedly proven that the United States is the direct threat to the international order and the mastermind behind regional turmoil.\nResolving the Taiwan question is China's own affair and an internal matter of China, which brooks no foreign interference, and the U.S. side has no right to pass judgment. For some time, the U.S. side has continuously hollowed out, emptied, and distorted the one-China principle, frequently sold arms to Taiwan, strengthened military collusion between the U.S. and Taiwan, and fabricated Taiwan-related bills and documents that undermine China's sovereignty. This will only seriously endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region and raise the risk of China-U.S. military confrontation. The People's Liberation Army of China will, as always, stand ready and resolutely defend the reunification of the motherland and its territorial integrity.\nChina urges the U.S. side to abandon its obsession with zero-sum games, view China's national defense and military development objectively and rationally, genuinely respect China's core interests and major concerns, and work with China to implement and carry out well the consensus reached by the heads of state of the two countries. Only in this way will it be possible for China-U.S. military relations to return to the right track.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10207459.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-12-24","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲24日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 24 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 24th, stating: Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs. The US “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023,” as a domestic US law, openly interferes in the Taiwan question, and even includes content on providing “military…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that for some time, some people on the U.S. side have escalated their wrong words and deeds on the Taiwan question. The U.S. \"National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023\" includes provisions for the U.S. government to provide Taiwan with \"military assistance\" of 10 billion U.S. dollars and \"military loans\" of 2 billion U.S. dollars within five years, and to accelerate arms sales to Taiwan. This further shows that a faction within the United States that supports Taiwan and seeks to contain China has not given up its evil intent, attempting to militarily arm the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, to \"hand them knives\" and \"send them guns and cannons,\" to incite confrontation across the Strait, fan the flames in the Taiwan Strait, push the Strait to the brink of war, and drive the people of Taiwan into a situation of widespread death and suffering. The DPP authorities, for the political purpose of \"Taiwan independence,\" obstinately pursue \"relying on the U.S. to resist the mainland\" and \"relying on the U.S. to seek independence,\" are willing to sacrifice the lives and well-being of the people of the island, willingly serve as pawns of external anti-China forces, and are going down a road to nowhere.\n\"We solemnly warn some people on the U.S. side that resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves and must be decided by the Chinese people. Some people on the U.S. side should immediately correct their wrong words and deeds on the Taiwan question and return to the correct path of adhering to the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that 'Taiwan independence' has no way out, and 'seeking independence by relying on the U.S.' is a dead end. No one should underestimate the firm resolve, strong will, and great capability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity,\" Zhu Fenglian said.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221224_12496901.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2022-12-28","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Hiroshige Seko, a Liberal Democratic Party lawmaker of Japan, held talks with Tsai Ing-wen in Taiwan today. During the talks, Tsai Ing-wen welcomed Japan’s three defense documents. What is China’s comment?","Certain Japanese politicians, in order to seek selfish political gains, have repeatedly put on political stunts and made provocative visits to China’s Taiwan region to bolster and embolden “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes this and has made serious démarches to the Japanese side.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Japan once kept Taiwan under its colonial rule for half a century. Japan is historically responsible for its serious wrongdoing to the Chinese people and has all the more reason to be prudent in its words and deeds. We urge Japan to uphold the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries, stop all forms of official contact with the Taiwan region, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We also have this serious message to the DPP authorities: any attempt to go against the trend of history and solicit foreign support in seeking “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347436.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221228_10997351.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2022-12-28","Wang Wenbin","AFP","One more question about Taiwan. Taiwan will extend mandatory military service from four months to one year over what authorities there called “China threat”. What’s your comment on this?","Achieving complete reunification is the shared will of the Chinese people and a historic trend that no one can stop. National reunification is one of the noblest causes a person can dedicate his or her life to, whereas to serve the “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda is to give one’s life away to an unworthy cause. We believe the vast majority of our Taiwan compatriots are fully conscious about what is right for the nation and will not be used as cannon fodder by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347436.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221228_10997351.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-12-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to the PLA Daily, since the beginning of this year, the Chinese military has faithfully practiced the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind, persistently fulfilled the international responsibilities of a major-country military, actively carried out international military cooperation, and achieved fruitful results. Please further introduce the relevant situation.","2022 holds great significance in the history of the Party and the country. The successful convening of the 20th Party Congress marked solid steps on the new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country. Over the past year, the work of international military cooperation of the Chinese military has been guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era. It has thoroughly implemented Xi Jinping's thought on strengthening the military and Xi Jinping's diplomatic thought, deeply grasped the decisive significance of the “Two Establishes,” and upheld the Chairman Responsibility System of the Central Military Commission. Closely centered on the Party's goal of strengthening the military in the new era, it has focused on preparing for war and fighting, boldly pursued innovation, and made positive contributions to safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, to maintaining world peace and stability, and to serving the building of a community with a shared future for mankind.\nFirst, serve the overall political and diplomatic situation.\nSince the beginning of this year, under the strategic guidance of Chairman Xi Jinping's head-of-state diplomacy, leaders of the Central Military Commission have held meetings, talks, or video calls with defense departments and military leaders of Russia, the United States, Cambodia, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, and other countries, promoting the implementation and effectiveness of head-of-state diplomatic outcomes in the field of international military cooperation. They hosted the reception marking the 95th anniversary of the founding of the army, the Ministerial Meeting of the Second China-Africa Peace and Security Forum, the Fifth China-Latin America High-Level Defense Forum, and other events. At these events, the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and major concepts proposed by Chairman Xi Jinping, such as the Global Security Initiative and the community with a shared future for mankind, were actively promoted, enhancing foreign parties' understanding and endorsement of China's policy positions.\nSecond, defend national sovereignty, dignity, and core interests.\nIn response to provocative words and actions by the United States and certain other countries on issues involving China's core interests and major concerns, such as Taiwan and the South China Sea, military operations were resolutely conducted to defend national sovereignty and security, while solemn representations were lodged, countermeasures and punishments were implemented, and statements were promptly issued to refute these actions and clarify China's position.\nThird, focus on the primary responsibilities and core business of preparing for war and fighting.\nThe Chinese military actively organized and took part in joint exercises, joint training, joint competitions, and joint patrols with foreign militaries, such as “Vostok-2022,” the China-Russia Joint Air Strategic Patrol, “Joint Sea-2022,” “Eagle Strike-2022,” and “International Military Games-2022.” These activities deepened mutual trust and cooperation with the armed forces of relevant countries and played a positive role in raising the level of combat-oriented training.\nFourth, effectively maintain the stability of the overall strategic situation.\nOver the past year, the Chinese military faithfully practiced the Global Security Initiative, continuously deepened pragmatic exchanges and cooperation between the Chinese and Russian militaries, and maintained high-level operation of strategic coordination between the two militaries. It maintained overall stability in China-U.S. military relations, encouraged the United States to meet China halfway in implementing the consensus of heads of state, unblocking communication channels, appropriately handling differences, and strengthening crisis management. It maintained strategic communication between China's defense departments and militaries and those of Europe. It continuously deepened pragmatic cooperation with neighboring countries in all fields, playing a positive role in promoting the building of a community with a shared future with neighboring countries. It strengthened defense and security cooperation with the broad developing countries of Africa, Latin America, and the South Pacific. It actively carried out international arms control compliance cooperation, resolutely safeguarded national strategic interests, and maintained global strategic stability.\nFifth, deeply participate in global security governance.\nThe Chinese military actively participated in institutional meetings such as the SCO Defence Ministers' Meeting, the ASEAN Defence Ministers' Meeting-Plus, and the China-ASEAN Informal Defence Ministers' Meeting. It sent a senior military delegation to attend the Shangri-La Dialogue and participated in multilateral dialogue and cooperation mechanisms such as the Moscow Conference on International Security. It hosted the first “Shared Vision” International Peacekeeping Forum, the Beijing Xiangshan Forum expert video conference, and other events, continuously enhancing our military's international discourse power and influence.\nSixth, serve the building of a community with a shared future for mankind.\nThe Navy's hospital ship “Peace Ark” went to Indonesia to carry out the “Harmonious Mission-2022” mission, providing medical services to local residents. Air Force Y-20 transport aircraft successively went to Tonga, Afghanistan, Pakistan, and other countries to carry out humanitarian relief missions. The Chinese military actively participated in peacekeeping, escort, and other operations, continuously providing public security goods to the international community.\nIn the cause of peace, the Chinese military goes out to the world. Facing the changes in the world, changes in the times, and changes in history, the Chinese military will continue to be guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era. It will focus on achieving the centenary goal of army building as scheduled, expand and deepen foreign military relations, strengthen pragmatic exchanges and cooperation, and make new and greater contributions to safeguarding world peace and promoting common development.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10208341.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-12-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that during the Sino-U.S. defense ministers' talks, the U.S. Secretary of Defense recently spoke about the importance of restoring the military dialogue mechanism between the two militaries. A U.S. Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense recently said at a U.S. think tank seminar that China's suspension of the Sino-U.S. military dialogue mechanism because of Pelosi's provocative visit to Taiwan is…","We have noted the relevant reports. Right and wrong must not be confused. China's cancellation of three exchange activities between the Chinese and US militaries was a necessary countermeasure against the US side's deliberate creation of a major crisis that seriously damages China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. The cause and effect are crystal clear, and the US side knows this full well. Recently, the US has successively issued multiple negative policy documents and bills concerning China, vigorously agitated for great-power competition, hyped up the so-called “China threat,” brazenly interfered in China's internal affairs, and further undermined the foundation and atmosphere for communication and exchanges between the two militaries.\nIt should be pointed out that China values the development of China-US military relations, and communication between the two militaries at the working level has not been interrupted. But the US cannot both seek a comprehensive resumption of dialogue and exchanges with China while constantly harming China's interests, and it cannot turn the facts upside down by shifting onto China the responsibility for canceling some military exchanges. There is no such logic under heaven. If the US side truly wants to conduct positive and constructive dialogue and exchanges with China, it must show sincerity and action, earnestly respect China's core interests and major concerns, and actively create conditions and an atmosphere for returning China-US military relations to the right track.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10208347.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-12-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reports say Japan recently revised its security documents, including the National Security Strategy, the National Defense Strategy and the Defense Buildup Program, positioning China as the “greatest strategic challenge to date.” These documents also include content such as Japan’s “counterstrike capability” to strike enemy missile launch bases, an expansion of defense spending, and the Taiwan question. Some…","The Japanese side's relevant documents, which involve China, distort facts and are full of prejudice. They deliberately hype up the so-called “China threat,” smear China's national defense and military development as well as its normal military activities, brutally interfere in China's internal affairs, and create regional tensions. China firmly opposes this.\nFacts have proven that China is a partner and opportunity for the development of all countries in the world, and the Chinese military is a firm force for safeguarding world peace. It has never challenged anyone, let alone threatened anyone. On the contrary, it is Japan that in recent years has seriously violated its pacifist constitution and its “exclusively defense-oriented” policy. Using the so-called “external threat” as a pretext, it has sharply increased defense spending, strengthened military technology research and development in fields such as space, missile defense, and hypersonic weapons, deepened U.S.-Japan military cooperation, sought to develop the so-called “counterstrike capability,” clamored with the United States about “nuclear sharing,” and followed behind other countries to form targeted “small cliques.” It has already become a real “challenge” to regional peace, security, and stability.\nTaiwan is Taiwan of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Japan launched wars of aggression against China in the past, bringing deep disasters to the Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and the painful memories remain to this day. In the four political documents between China and Japan, Japan clearly stated that it recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and fully understands and respects the Chinese government's position that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People's Republic of China.” There is no room for Japan to meddle in the Taiwan question. What Japan should do is keep history in mind, reflect on its war guilt, keep its promises, and be prudent in its words and deeds.\nNext year marks the 45th anniversary of the conclusion of the Treaty of Peace and Friendship between China and Japan. Looking back on history, only when Japan adheres to peaceful development and genuinely respects the security concerns of other countries can it earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community. We urge the Japanese side to earnestly draw lessons from history, not to stir up trouble or seek private gains on the Taiwan question, not to repeat the old path of beggaring its neighbors and being hostile to them, and to do more things that are conducive to maintaining regional peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10208365.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2022-12-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department recently said that the “military threat” from mainland China has reached an “unprecedented level of severity,” that since 2020 the number of times mainland military aircraft have “intruded” into Taiwan's “Air Defense Identification Zone” has increased fivefold, and that the mainland will again find an excuse to stage exercises simulating attacks…","The military operations of the Chinese People's Liberation Army are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, with the purpose of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Wherever there is conduct that forgets one's roots and splits the country, there will be PLA military operations. Rather than painstakingly tallying the frequency of PLA military aircraft sorties, the DPP authorities should face history and reality squarely, see clearly the trend toward reunification and the sentiment of the people, and earnestly reflect on their erroneous words and deeds: relying on foreign backing to bolster their own standing, seeking “independence” through force, constantly stirring up cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, and undermining cross-Strait relations.\nDefending national sovereignty and containing “Taiwan independence” separatism has always been the sacred duty of the Chinese People's Liberation Army. The PLA always keeps its mission in mind, continuously trains and prepares for combat, and resolutely crushes any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and external interference schemes, firmly defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/10208366.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2022-12-30","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","It is reported that the US State Department approved the sale of Volcano anti-tank mine-laying systems to Taiwan for an estimated $180 million. Do you have any comment on this?","We have all along firmly opposed US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region.\nChina urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, and earnestly act on the commitment made by the US leaders of not supporting “Taiwan independence”. It should stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will act firmly to defend our sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347438.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202212/t20221230_10998876.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2022-12-30","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Department of Defense recently said that the U.S. State Department has approved the sale to Taiwan of anti-tank mine systems worth approximately US$180 million. What comments do you have on this?","We have always firmly opposed US arms sales to China's Taiwan region. This move by the US seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué,” harms China's sovereignty and security interests, emboldens the arrogance of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China is strongly dissatisfied with this and will resolutely counter it.\nThe US side's attempt to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China's development and obstruct China's reunification is sheer wishful thinking. We urge the US side to stop arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military ties, stop creating new factors of tension in the Taiwan Strait, and stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Otherwise, it will ultimately bring fire upon itself, and the US side will bear the serious consequences that result.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/10208751.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2022-12-30","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲30日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 30 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 30th, saying: We firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. The U.S. arms sales conduct seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, particularly the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué. It is a condoning and…","Zhu Fenglian said: We urge the U.S. side to abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China–U.S. joint communiqués, to put its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” into practice, to stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop U.S.–Taiwan military ties, and to handle the Taiwan issue with prudence. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that scheming to “use force to resist reunification,” and colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202212/t20221230_12498417.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-01-04","Mao Ning","AFP","Former NATO chief Anders Rasmussen met with Taiwan’s Tsai Ing-wen today and said that democracies must join together to resist autocracies. Does China have any response to these remarks?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is not about democracy, but about China’s territorial integrity and reunification. Let me stress that any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” in the world is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347440.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230104_11000666.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-09","Wang Wenbin","AFP","A high-level delegation of German lawmakers arrived in Taipei today for a visit to the island. Will China take countermeasures against them?","The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. The one-China principle is the political foundation of the development of bilateral relations between China and countries having diplomatic relations with it, including Germany. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We urge the German politicians to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and immediately stop colluding and interacting with or sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We will take necessary measures to resolutely defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe need to point out that the root cause of the Taiwan question is that the law of the jungle, hegemonism, colonialism and militarism were wreaking havoc across the world back then, which inflicted deep suffering on China. Germany has learned a hard and poignant lesson in this regard. Over the past one century and a half or so since then, the Chinese people have been committed to fighting imperialism, hegemonism and colonialism and upholding our sovereignty, territorial integrity and national dignity. We will never allow any forces to turn the Asia-Pacific into an arena of geopolitical games once again to maintain their dominance.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347443.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230109_11004570.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-09","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The Chinese military conducted fresh drills around Taiwan yesterday. Is this aimed at sending some signals to the US?","The spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has made a statement on this. The drills are aimed at testing the joint combat capability of the troops and resolutely countering the provocative acts of external forces and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in collusion.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347443.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230109_11004570.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-09","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","It is reported that Paraguay would cut so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and establish relations with China if the opposition wins the election in April, said its presidential candidate Efrain Alegre recently. What is China’s comment?","Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. We believe relevant countries will eventually recognize this trend and make the right decision that is consistent with where the trend is leading.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347443.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230109_11004570.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-11","Wang Wenbin","Tokyo News","A group of Lithuanian lawmakers are on a visit to Taiwan and will meet with Tsai Ing-wen. What’s your comment?","We have pointed out repeatedly that Lithuania violated its commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties with China and blatantly created the false impression of “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. This contravenes the basic norm governing international relations. We urge Lithuania to abide by its commitment made upon the establishment of diplomatic ties with China and return to the one-China principle as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347445.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230111_11005831.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear media friends, good morning. You have all worked hard during this period. I will be hosting today's press conference.\nOn the eve of the New Year, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a New Year's address, expressing deep affection for Taiwan compatriots and hoping that compatriots on both sides of the Strait would join hands to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, which drew wide attention and enthusiastic responses on Taiwan. As the traditional Chinese festival of the Spring Festival approaches, the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have actively implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches, taking a series of measures to care for and extend greetings to Taiwan compatriots and to promote the resumption of normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.\nOn January 2, Song Tao, Director of the Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, published a New Year message titled “Working Hand in Hand to Create a Great Cause,” extending New Year blessings and sincere greetings to Taiwan compatriots, comprehensively expounding the central government's policies and positions on Taiwan and major cross-Strait issues, and calling on compatriots on both sides to act in harmony and unity, act together, uphold national righteousness, shoulder historical responsibility, jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, share in the glory of a prosperous motherland, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. On January 10, Director Song Tao visited Taiwanese youth representatives in Beijing and held a discussion, listening to their experiences of studying, working, living, and starting businesses on the mainland, their feelings about actively participating in cross-Strait exchanges, and their opinions and suggestions on deepening integrated development across the Strait. He conveyed our side's policies and concepts for advancing cross-Strait relations in the new year and gathered the shared expectations of compatriots on both sides for a fresh outlook in the new year. The Taiwanese youth were deeply encouraged and felt warmth in their hearts. On January 7, Deputy Director Long Mingbiao of the Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council went to the Xiamen Wutong Passenger Terminal to welcome Kinmen County Magistrate Chen Fu-hai and his delegation, who arrived on the first passenger ferry to Xiamen, and to see off Kinmen fellow townspeople returning home for the New Year. The Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council recently issued a notice requiring Taiwan affairs offices in all localities to do a good job of extending greetings and visits to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople during the 2023 Spring Festival. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council also sent Spring Festival greeting letters to the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and to Taiwan business associations in various localities, extending greetings and best wishes to Taiwan businesspeople and their families.\nNext, we will, guided by the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” take a series of measures to encourage and inspire the confidence of compatriots on both sides, oppose “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces, respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, promote the resumption of personnel exchanges across the Strait and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, continuously deepen integrated development, and jointly create a bright future for cross-Strait relations.\nThank you all. Now I will take questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501444.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","Today is the Taiwan Affairs Office's first press conference of 2023. The spokesperson is asked to review and summarize cross-Strait relations in 2022 and look ahead to cross-Strait relations development in 2023.","In 2022, cross-Strait relations were complex and grim. Under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we firmly grasped the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations, united compatriots on both sides to advance cross-Strait relations forward, and achieved new progress in our work on Taiwan.\nWe effectively guided the correct development direction of cross-Strait relations. The 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China solemnly announced the major policies and strategic deployment on Taiwan work for the new era and new journey, providing fundamental guidelines and an action plan for our Taiwan work, with far-reaching significance for advancing cross-Strait relations and the process of national reunification. We issued the white paper “The Taiwan Question and China’s Reunification in the New Era,” and held a series of activities including the symposium marking the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus” and the second “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams” theme event. We continued to explain to Taiwan compatriots and the international community the historical background of the Taiwan question and the major policies on Taiwan work, so that the Party’s policies on Taiwan are more deeply rooted in people’s hearts.\nWe actively promoted peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Practicing the development philosophy centered on the people, we consistently respected, cared for, and benefited Taiwan compatriots, and continuously improved the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We supported Fujian and other places in exploring new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, continuously optimized the business environment related to Taiwan, and helped Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development. Cross-Strait trade and Taiwan business investment in the mainland remained generally stable throughout the year. We actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, encouraged compatriots on both sides to jointly carry forward excellent traditional Chinese culture, and successfully held the 10th Straits Forum, the 2022 Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, and more than 600 key cross-Strait exchange projects. Many Taiwan compatriots pursued, built, and realized their dreams on the mainland, and the atmosphere of “cross-Strait families are one family” became even stronger.\nWe resolutely carried out major struggles against secession and against interference. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces are the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait, seriously endangering the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the immediate interests of Taiwan compatriots. We took a series of forceful measures to resolutely defeat all forms of “Taiwan independence” provocations and external interference schemes, further gained strategic initiative in realizing the complete reunification of the motherland, and further consolidated the international community’s adherence to the one-China pattern. “Seeking independence by relying on outside forces” and “using Taiwan to contain China” are unpopular and destined to fail. The mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that seeks peace, stability, and development has become more prominent.\nIn the new year, we will fully implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, persist in uniting the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of national reunification, and work hand in hand to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501445.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","Please introduce the cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2022. In addition, what is your outlook for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchange and cooperation in 2023?","In 2022, due to the impact of the COVID-19 epidemic and obstruction by the DPP authorities, personnel exchanges and in-person exchanges across the Taiwan Strait were blocked. However, cross-Strait exchanges carried out through methods combining online and offline activities never stopped, and the eager desire of compatriots on both sides to get closer to one another never diminished. Over the past year, cross-Strait exchanges and integration have overcome difficulties and moved forward, achieving new progress and new results, and showing some new characteristics:\nFirst, the new era and the new journey have added powerful momentum to strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepening integrated development. The 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China formulated major guidelines and policies for the development of all mainland undertakings over the coming period and drew a grand blueprint, bringing new vision and new impetus to cross-Strait exchanges and integration, and deeply inspiring and greatly boosting the confidence of compatriots on both sides. On the eve of the 14th Straits Forum, General Secretary Xi Jinping replied to Taiwan youth attending the Straits Youth Forum, encouraging cross-Strait youth to march together and work hand in hand to realize the Chinese Dream of national rejuvenation, further motivating young people and compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges, expand cooperation and unite in striving forward.\nSecond, exchanges across all sectors on both sides of the Strait continued to maintain their momentum of development. From early 2022 to the end of the year, various exchange activities were continuously held in fields including culture, education, science and technology, health, sports, grassroots communities, youth, ethnic minorities, religion and folk belief, among others. The total for the year exceeded 1,000 sessions. These exchange activities displayed characteristics of multiple themes, multiple levels and multiple forms, fully reflecting the strong internal demand and broad development space for exchanges in all fields across the Strait. People from all sectors on both sides expressed hopes in these exchange activities that cross-Strait exchanges would soon return to normal.\nThird, the positive influence and cohesive role of cross-Strait exchange activities have further expanded. Major exchange activities such as the 14th Straits Forum and the series of activities commemorating the 360th anniversary of Zheng Chenggong's recovery of Taiwan played a demonstrative and leading role in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation under epidemic conditions. Taiwan compatriots working, studying and living on the mainland have become the main body of in-person exchanges. Guangdong, Sichuan, Shandong and other places held activities related to the 35th anniversary of the start of cross-Strait exchanges, reviewing and summarizing the fruitful results and experiences gained from strengthening exchanges and cooperation and deepening integrated development across all fields, further strengthening the confidence of compatriots on both sides to advance together.\nFourth, youth have demonstrated vigorous and dynamic strength in the process of cross-Strait exchanges and integrated development. A series of cross-Strait youth exchange activities, including the 2022 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the 10th Straits Youth Festival, the Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour, the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, the Taiwan Youth Border Tour, and the Taiwan Youth Yellow River Travelogue, have inspired cross-Strait youth to strive with courage and determination. Many Taiwan youths vividly described, through media and social media, their struggles and growth on the mainland and stories of cross-Strait youth moving forward together, generating broad and positive influence. Relevant parties actively supported Taiwan youth in internships, employment and entrepreneurship on the mainland, providing thousands of internship and job positions. Interest among Taiwan students in applying to mainland universities remains strong. In 2022, the mainland for the first time piloted a unified platform for admitting Taiwan students based on their “General Scholastic Ability Test” (“学测”) scores, and 207 universities, including Peking University and Tsinghua University, participated in the first batch of the pilot, achieving a 22% increase in admissions compared with 2021. Also in 2022, Taiwan students could for the first time apply to 13 mainland undergraduate universities and six higher vocational colleges using their “Comprehensive Scholastic Ability Test” (“统测”) scores, opening a new channel for studying on the mainland.\nFifth, integrated development across the Strait continues to write a new chapter. An increasing number of Taiwan compatriots have found stages for career development on the mainland and have participated in the process of Chinese-style modernization, making positive contributions. In 2022, a total of 37 Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, Taiwan compatriot families and Taiwan compatriot groups were honored with prefecture-level or higher honorary titles from the Youth League, Women's Federation and trade union systems. Among them, two people were named National “March 8” Red Banner Bearers, 21 Taiwan compatriot families were recognized as National Model Families and “Most Beautiful Families” of relevant provinces (municipalities), and 14 Taiwan youths (individuals and groups) received honors such as the provincial-level Youth (Group) May Fourth Medal. The China Federation of Literary and Art Circles' national literary and art associations newly admitted 13 Taiwan literary and art figures as members, and several Taiwan artists were nominated for important awards such as the China Opera Peony Award, the China Photography Golden Statue Award and the Golden Rooster Awards for Chinese films.\nWanting exchanges and wanting cooperation is the shared voice of compatriots on both sides. In the new year, we will continue to work toward promoting exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, continuously deepening integrated development across the Strait, and bringing benefits to compatriots on both sides. Under the new circumstances of adjusting and optimizing mainland epidemic prevention and control measures, restoring normal personnel exchanges across the Strait as soon as possible and making exchange and cooperation in all fields across the Strait routine is the common expectation of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities should follow the will of the people and remove, as soon as possible, the obstacles they have set up to personnel exchanges and exchanges across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501440.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the economic exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait in 2022. What were the main characteristics? What are your expectations for cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2023?","In 2022, we overcame adverse effects such as the COVID-19 pandemic and restrictions and obstruction by the DPP authorities, emphasized “promoting integration through exchanges, promoting integration through benefits, and promoting integration through emotional connection,” and steadily advanced economic exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait.\nFirst, with the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges have persevered through difficulties and remained generally stable. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, from January to November 2022, total cross-Strait trade was US$294.39 billion, roughly flat compared with the same period in 2021. Of this, the mainland's exports to Taiwan were US$75.32 billion, up 6.6% year on year, and its imports from Taiwan were US$219.07 billion, down 2.9% year on year. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from January to November 2022, the mainland newly approved 5,470 Taiwan-funded projects (including investments made through third places), and actually utilized US$1.92 billion in Taiwan capital. Cross-Strait industrial cooperation continued to deepen, and industrial and supply chains remained fundamentally stable.\nSecond, we actively helped Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland overcome the impact of the pandemic and kept their production and operations generally stable. All localities continuously optimized the business environment related to Taiwan, fully implemented equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, delivered policies and services to their doorsteps, and devoted every effort to doing practical things, good things, and resolving difficulties for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises. Policies were introduced to expand the eligibility to apply for setting up individual industrial and commercial businesses, which greatly lowered the entry threshold for Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots residents and young people, to start businesses on the mainland, and was warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots and youth. Taiwan-funded enterprises participated for the first time in the selection of China's Industrial Awards, and 8 Taiwan-funded enterprises and projects, including TPV Electronics, won the 7th China Industrial Awards, Commendation Awards, and Nomination Awards, significantly enhancing the sense of gain and honor of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland.\nThird, we supported Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in rural revitalization and high-quality agricultural development. We further implemented the “22 Measures for Agriculture and Forestry” in detail, supported Zhangping Taiwan Entrepreneurship Park in Fujian in successfully becoming a national modern agricultural industrial park, supported Sanming in Fujian in establishing a cross-Strait rural integrated development pilot zone, and advanced the establishment of cross-Strait rural revitalization cooperation bases. At present, the cumulative number of Taiwan-funded enterprises investing in the agricultural and food industries on the mainland has exceeded 10,000.\nFourth, we vigorously supported Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in participating in national development strategies, and the investment structure of Taiwan businesspeople became more optimized. Relevant provinces and municipalities and the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit and other innovative approaches held diverse Taiwan-related economic and trade activities, built platforms for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to participate in major national regional strategies and regional coordinated development strategies, and provided business opportunities. We actively supported Fujian in exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development, and guided and supported Taiwan-funded enterprises in orderly relocating to central and western regions and participating in the Belt and Road Initiative. We supported Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in using the China International Import Expo, various trade fairs, e-commerce platforms, and other channels to expand the domestic market. We supported high-quality Taiwan enterprises in going public and deepened cross-Strait financial cooperation. In 2022, a total of 10 Taiwan enterprises were listed on the mainland A-share market, bringing the number of Taiwan enterprises listed on the mainland to 57.\nIn the new year, we will continue to work for promoting cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and improving systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, so that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will have a greater sense of gain and pride in participating in national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501439.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the situation of exchanges and dialogues between the Mainland and Taiwan's political parties, groups and representative figures in 2022.","In 2022, on the basis of upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we held exchanges and dialogues in diverse forms and with rich content with relevant Taiwan political parties, groups, and representative figures, continuously building consensus and achieving positive results.\nFirst, in the golden autumn of October, the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China was successfully convened. Political parties and figures in Taiwan expressed congratulations in various forms. The Central Committee of the Kuomintang sent a congratulatory telegram to the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China. Lien Chan and Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairpersons of the KMT, James Soong, chairman of the People First Party, Wu Cheng-tien, chairman of the New Party, Lin Bing-kun, chairman of the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union, as well as the Labor Party, the Unification Alliance Party, the Chinese Patriotic Loyalty Party, the Communist Party of Taiwan, and other political parties, groups, and figures on the island also sent congratulatory telegrams or letters.\nSecond, Taiwan political parties, groups, and representative figures actively supported and participated in cross-Strait exchange activities in various forms. At the opening ceremony of the Beijing Winter Olympics, the 5th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the 2nd “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams: Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” activity, the 14th Straits Forum, the Cross-Strait Relations Seminar, the academic seminar marking the 30th anniversary of the “1992 Consensus,” the seminar marking the 35th anniversary of cross-Strait exchanges in Guangdong, and other events, people from both sides communicated, sought common ground while setting aside differences, and voiced positive messages: adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference, promoting cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and striving for national reunification and national rejuvenation. In August, Xia Liyan, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, led a delegation to visit the mainland. Responsible persons of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits met with them respectively, and both sides agreed that on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” they were willing to strengthen party-to-party exchanges, consolidate and enhance mutual trust, deepen exchange and cooperation, and jointly work to advance relations between the two parties and across the Strait.\nThird, exchanges between cities across the Strait remained active. Relevant cities and counties on both sides strengthened exchange and cooperation through a combination of online and offline methods and achieved positive results. In July, Shanghai and Taipei successfully held the “2022 Shanghai–Taipei City Forum” via video, which played a positive role in promoting exchange and cooperation in all fields between the two cities and enhancing the livelihood and well-being of residents in both places.\nIn the new year, we will continue, on the basis of the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” to conduct extensive and in-depth consultations with far-sighted people from all sectors in Taiwan on cross-Strait relations and national unification, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501436.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","In 2022, the DPP authorities extensively colluded with external forces to carry out provocations seeking “independence,” and external forces have continued to play the “Taiwan card.” What are your expectations for the development of the situation? How will the mainland continue to effectively contain this?","In 2022, the situation across the Taiwan Strait remained tense and turbulent. The root cause lies in the DPP authorities' obstinate adherence to the “Taiwan independence” position and their collusion with external forces to continuously carry out provocations to “seek independence.” Some anti-China forces in certain countries, out of their own interests, have condoned and supported “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in taking risky provocations, constantly hollowing out and emptying the one-China principle. Their aim is to use the Taiwan question to contain China's development and progress and to obstruct the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is China's own affair, and any scheme to split Taiwan from China will never succeed. “Taiwan independence” separatism is doomed to fail, and “relying on external forces to seek independence” will surely be held to account. We urge the countries concerned to genuinely abide by the one-China principle, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question.\nIn the new year, we will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces' provocations to “seek independence” and their schemes of external interference, and firmly safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501433.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","The “Small Three Links” (mini three links), suspended for three years, partially resumed on January 7. Residents of the island call on the DPP authorities to completely lift the restrictions and fully restore the links. What comment do you have on this? In addition, the mainland has optimized and adjusted its epidemic prevention and control policies, and the Spring Festival is approaching. Besides the “Small…","On January 7, partial resumption of the cross-Strait “Small Three Links” sea passenger routes, which had been suspended for nearly three years, took place. But there is still a large gap from what Taiwan compatriots hope for. Not only are Taiwan businesspeople, students and officials excluded, but mainland residents also cannot travel to Taiwan through this channel because of restrictions imposed by the DPP authorities, which falls far short of the expectations of compatriots on both sides.\nStarting January 8, the mainland implemented “Category B management” for novel coronavirus infection. With the Spring Festival approaching, to facilitate Taiwan compatriots returning home to celebrate the New Year, relevant authorities on the mainland have actively supported cross-Strait airlines in substantially increasing cross-Strait routes and flights. Relevant airlines will gradually increase capacity and adjust cross-Strait transport arrangements, and cross-Strait flights will increase noticeably. Take Shanghai Pudong International Airport, which everyone is concerned about, as an example: from January 8 to 31, the number of two-way passenger flights to and from Taiwan is expected to reach an average of 8 per day. Besides adding flights, expanding destinations is also a necessary measure to provide convenience and assurance for Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year. The mainland originally had 61 cross-Strait air passenger destinations. Since the epidemic, the DPP authorities have unilaterally closed most of them, and at present only 4 mainland destinations remain. We hope to increase capacity by expanding destinations, so as to provide assurance for Taiwan compatriots returning home for the New Year.\nWe urge the DPP authorities to heed public opinion, remove the various unreasonable obstacles they have set up over the past three years, promote the full resumption of the “Small Three Links” as early as possible, promptly restore the original cross-Strait passenger destinations, and restore normal personnel exchanges and regular exchanges between the peoples on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501432.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te and other political figures on the island have repeatedly proposed replacing “resisting China to defend Taiwan” with “peacefully defending Taiwan,” which outside observers regard as the DPP’s deliberate adjustment of its cross-Strait narrative. What comment do you have?","Seeking peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation is the common voice of compatriots on both sides and is in their common interest. “Taiwan independence” and peace are irreconcilable like fire and water. If some politicians on the island truly want peace across the Taiwan Strait, they should abandon the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, return to the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” and stop acting as pawns of external anti-China forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501430.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Recently, the DPP authorities extended the compulsory military service period on the island to one year, which has caused controversy on the island. What is your comment?","Seeking peace, seeking stability, and seeking development is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. Returning to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” would allow cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, and would ensure peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait in a practical way. The DPP authorities are manipulating the “using force to seek independence and resisting reunification” approach, and in coordination with external forces are pushing Taiwan’s young people onto the battlefield as “cannon fodder.” This will only increase tension and turbulence in the cross-Strait situation, and will only harm the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan. It is bound to end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230111_12501428.htm"],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The first question: Recently, PLA aircraft training and exercises have been frequent. The DPP authorities have made large-scale arms purchases from the United States and restored the one-year military service system. What is your comment? The second question: The latest tabletop wargame results from the U.S. think tank Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) say that if the PLA attacked Taiwan in…","First question. Everything has causes and consequences. Recently, the DPP authorities have accelerated military collusion with the United States. The PLA's drills are a stern warning against the escalation of Taiwan-US collusion and provocation, which undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and it brooks no interference from outsiders. Any scheme to separate Taiwan from China is doomed to fail. No person and no force should underestimate our resolve and capability to contain \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and oppose external interference. As I mentioned just now, we look forward to cross-Strait relations improving and developing in the new year, to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to the swift resumption of normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This is our sincere hope and also the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides should unite to stop the escalation of Taiwan-US collusion and provocation, so that our good wishes and kind intentions can be realized.\nSecond question, regarding so-called public opinion polls and research reports, we will not comment on them. I would like to point out that in recent times, some U.S. think tanks have repeatedly released so-called reports on the Taiwan question and the situation across the Strait. Under the guise of academic research, they are engaged in carefully calculated schemes. They lavishly promote and peddle the \"China threat theory,\" profit the domestic military-industrial complex, seize opportunities to sow discord in the emotional ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and serve the strategy of \"using Taiwan to contain China\" for their allies. Their motives and purposes are obvious. Regarding such reports, we believe that compatriots in Taiwan have the reason to make their own judgments, not be deluded, and not be coerced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Last year, many major events occurred in cross-Strait relations. The online selection event for the “Top Ten Cross-Strait Relations News of 2022” officially launched on January 10. Please introduce the relevant information.","To record major events in cross-Strait relations, the online selection of the “Top Ten Cross-Strait News of 2022,” hosted by China Taiwan Network, was officially launched on January 10, and voting will close at 5 p.m. on January 17. Since its launch in 2005, the annual online selection of the Top Ten Cross-Strait News has been successfully held for 17 consecutive editions, attracting the attention of netizens on both sides and exerting broad influence across the Strait. This year's selection will combine netizen voting with expert opinions, and the results will be officially announced on January 18. We welcome netizens on both sides to vote and interact through the China Taiwan Network website and its official Weibo, WeChat public account, Facebook and other new media platforms, and to select the “Top Ten Cross-Strait News of 2022” of their choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视《台海时刻》新媒体记者","At the turn of the year, Taiwan Strait Moment interviewed several cross-strait experts, scholars, Taiwan youth, and Taiwan businesspeople, asking them to use a few keywords to review and look ahead to cross-strait relations. We found that the words “He” (和, harmony), “Tong” (通, connection), and “Rong” (融, integration) received high recommendation rates, showing that compatriots on both sides share a common hope…","Over the past year, despite the complex and severe situation in the Taiwan Strait, compatriots on both sides are bound by blood ties. The desire for peace and development, and for exchanges and cooperation, is both the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and the common voice of compatriots on both sides, accords with the shared interests of compatriots on both sides. I think this is also why words such as “He” (harmony), “Tong” (connection), and “Rong” (integration) have taken deep root in people’s hearts.\nAt the same time, I am also reminded that the character “思” (si, meaning “think” or “longing”) was selected as the 2022 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year. The character “思” reflects the longing of compatriots on both sides for one another amid pandemic-related separation, and also embodies deep reflection on the future and destiny of cross-strait relations. We hope that compatriots on both sides will think before they act, and in the new year, work together to pursue the realm of exchange and cooperation of “He,” “Tong,” and “Rong,” join hands with one heart, and create a bright future for the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The PLA has frequently conducted exercises and drills around the Taiwan Strait. Some Taiwan scholars analyze that this is meant to obstruct the US from implementing the Taiwan-related provisions of the 2023 National Defense Authorization Act. How do you comment?","As I have already pointed out, the PLA's series of exercises and drills are a response to the escalation of Taiwan-US collusion and provocations. As for the United States' enactment of the so-called \"Annual National Defense Authorization Act,\" we have already expressed our basic position. Here I want to say that Taiwan compatriots should give serious thought to this: the US move is by no means good for Taiwan. It merely wants to sell to Taiwan the weapons it sold to Ukraine, turning Taiwan into a battlefield and making Taiwan's young people \"cannon fodder.\" We are curbing the escalation of Taiwan-US military collusion and provocations in order to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to safeguard the peaceful and secure lives of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","海峡之声电台记者","The relevant authorities on the island recently announced that the 2022 consumer price index rose 2.95% year on year, a 14-year high, with egg prices up 26.39%. Persistent inflation is keenly felt by Taiwan residents, who criticize the DPP authorities for holding office without doing their jobs. What is your comment?","The 'egg shortage' farce on the island has played out more than once and shows a tendency to grow more severe. This is not a superficial problem. Do not underestimate the matter of 'one egg,' and do not ignore these figures; it directly concerns the daily lives of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots compatriots. What causes the partial shortages of supplies and the inflation on the island? What is the reason? Compatriots in Taiwan know better than we do. What to do in the future? Compatriots in Taiwan should also have a better answer than we do.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Deputy Head of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that due to epidemic-prevention controls on the mainland side, the four current cross-Strait air routes have only been approved for 29 flight rotations. If the mainland side expands the routes in the future, airlines will be able to increase capacity. Please confirm. In addition, apart from the Lunar New Year, cross-Strait flights also face a…","First, as I have already said, in addition to adding flights, we also call for restoring routes as soon as possible. The mainland’s epidemic prevention and control is now transitioning in a stable and orderly manner, and both sides have better conditions to open more routes as soon as possible to meet the needs of cross-strait personnel exchanges. As I understand it, the mainland side has consistently hoped to add routes and has already proposed this to the Taiwan side.\nSecond, capacity and passenger volume are mutually causal. In the past, affected by the epidemic, compatriots on both sides could not travel normally, so passenger volume inevitably declined, and airlines naturally reduced flights. Now we hope this issue can become a virtuous cycle. Adding flights is one aspect; restoring normal cross-strait personnel exchanges as soon as possible is the more important aspect. As compatriots on both sides resume normal, more frequent and convenient travel, cross-strait routes, capacity and passenger volume will also increase accordingly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","中国日报记者","On January 7, local time, McCarthy was elected Speaker of the US House of Representatives. He had previously stated that if elected, he would make a provocative visit to Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The United States, as part of the U.S. government, should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.”\nBloomberg:\nFirst question: The United States and Taiwan will begin face-to-face negotiations on the “21st Century Trade Initiative” this Saturday. What is your comment on this? Second question: The DPP authorities require people traveling from the mainland to Taiwan via Hong Kong and Macao to submit nucleic acid test certificates. Will the mainland impose similar travel restrictions on Taiwan?\nOn the first question, we firmly oppose the United States negotiating with the Taiwan region of China on any agreement with sovereign implications or official nature. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués in practice. Attempts to play the “Taiwan card” to block China's reunification and national rejuvenation will not succeed. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that the despicable conduct of using economic and trade cooperation as a pretext, colluding with external forces, selling out the interests of the people on the island, and seeking personal political gain will surely be held to account.\nOn the second question, the COVID-19 strains currently circulating on the mainland have already spread to other parts of the world, and new strains may emerge anywhere. At present, the mainland's epidemic prevention and control measures have been optimized and adjusted, and the situation is under control. The DPP authorities' singling out of mainland travelers to Taiwan for nucleic acid testing is clearly unrelated to scientific epidemic prevention.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: In his New Year's message, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, stated that this year the mainland will \"conduct extensive and in-depth consultations with knowledgeable people from all sectors of Taiwan on cross-Strait relations and national reunification.\" May I ask the spokesperson, how do you define who counts as \"knowledgeable people,\" how does the mainland decide on consultation…","On the first question, “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. Whether promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations or advancing the process of achieving peaceful reunification of the motherland, both are inseparable from consultation and dialogue. Our position is very clear: on the basis of the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we are willing to promote extensive and in-depth consultations with Taiwan's political parties, sectors, and people from all walks of life on cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We will hold consultations and dialogue with whoever recognizes the “1992 Consensus,” sincerely upholds the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and maintains peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nOn the second question, over the three years since the epidemic broke out, compatriots on both sides of the Strait have cared for each other and helped each other through hardship, reflecting the sincere kinship of blood ties. We have not forgotten that when the epidemic in Wuhan was critical, many Taiwan enterprises, groups, and individuals broke through numerous obstacles to provide epidemic prevention supplies to the mainland. Compatriots in Taiwan should also not forget that at critical moments when Taiwan faced shortages of test reagents and a vaccine shortage, mainland supporting enterprises and civil organizations donated to and provided large quantities of vaccines, test reagents, and urgently needed medical equipment to Taiwan compatriots. After the mainland's epidemic prevention and control transitioned to a new stage, many people from all walks of life in Taiwan still expressed sincere greetings, goodwill, and blessings to us, and we express our thanks here.\nAt the same time, everyone has seen that since the outbreak of the epidemic, some politicians on the island have exploited the epidemic for political manipulation: either “using the epidemic to seek independence,” or attacking and slandering the mainland, or inciting “anti-China and resistance to China.” These misdeeds will be recorded in the history of cross-Strait relations.\nAt present, the mainland's epidemic prevention and control measures have been optimized and adjusted, the situation is under control, and the supply of medicines and medical supplies is generally adequate. We will continue to optimize and adjust prevention and control measures in response to the epidemic situation, to better protect people's lives and health. As for the remarks you mentioned by the head of Taiwan's epidemic prevention authority, to my understanding, the mainland's counterpart unit for the cross-Strait medical and health cooperation agreement has not received any relevant information.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: The last batch of mainland students studying in Taiwan are now in their senior year of university. After they graduate this summer, the number will be “reset to zero,” and Taiwan will have no mainland undergraduate students, nor graduate students pursuing master's or doctoral studies. In the post-epidemic era, is the mainland willing to reopen the admission of mainland students to Taiwan? Second…","On the first question: our policy signal in promoting the resumption of normal exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is clear, and our position is firm. Mainland students pursuing degrees in Taiwan are a product of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Since the DPP came to power, it has nearly destroyed the achievements of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. \"Taiwan independence\" poisonous waves have pervaded Taiwan's campuses, causing mainland parents and students to shy away. If the island ends up with no mainland students, the responsibility is plain to see. The reasoning is clear: advancing the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus\" can continuously enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nOn the second question, I wish to reiterate: peace, development, exchange, cooperation, and living a good life are the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and they accord with the common interests of compatriots on both sides. But the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and external interference forces do not think so. The PLA's military drills targeting Taiwan are aimed at \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, not at Taiwan compatriots in general; their purpose is to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. As long as there is no \"Taiwan independence,\" there is nothing to worry about. Here, I also ask you to tell the girls of Alishan that the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are the \"terrifying lovers\" they should be worried about.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-01-11","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The first question: In 2024, regardless of which party comes to power in Taiwan, if it reaffirms the '1992 Consensus,' and public opinion in Taiwan also hopes to maintain the status quo and 'one China, each with its own interpretation,' can cross-Strait relations return to the peaceful and stable development of those years? The second question: Regarding the registration of Taiwan food enterprises, Taiwan's 'Food…","Regarding the first question, I will not answer hypothetical questions about the evolution of the political situation on the island. It should be pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the linchpin that keeps them on a peaceful course. No matter which party governs Taiwan, as long as the authorities on the island adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” cross-Strait relations can develop peacefully and steadily, compatriots on both sides will benefit, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will be guaranteed.\nRegarding the second question, since early December last year, our Office’s spokesperson has explained the situation three times through written press releases, clarifying the facts and refuting the DPP authorities’ political manipulation. In response to your question, I would like to make four further points.\nFirst, the mainland has issued the Provisions on the Registration Administration of Overseas Manufacturers of Imported Food (General Administration of Customs Order No. 248), which apply to the registration administration of food production, processing and storage enterprises in all countries and regions that export food to the mainland. The Provisions optimize the registration procedures, implement categorized management of different types of overseas manufacturers, and clarify the primary responsibility of enterprises and the regulatory responsibility of the competent authorities where they are located, with the aim of safeguarding the safety of imported food. In short, this is done to protect the safety of imported food and the health rights and interests of consumers. The Provisions have been notified in accordance with WTO rules, and Taiwan has also been notified. Under these Provisions, Taiwanese food production enterprises should supplement and improve their relevant registration information. This is not a ban on products from Taiwanese food enterprises, and it is certainly not a “trade barrier” or “discriminatory treatment” as the DPP claims.\nSecond, the registration information that Taiwanese food production enterprises must provide is the same as that required of other overseas enterprises. The information on raw materials and ingredients that must be reported as required is intended to safeguard the safety of imported food and the rights and interests of consumers. There is no so-called requirement to hand over “confidential formulas.” This information will not be made public and will not affect enterprises’ rights and interests. In fact, no such situation has occurred to date.\nThird, some Taiwanese enterprises have not yet obtained registration, mainly because the registration information they provided was incomplete and non-standard. Although the deadline we announced has passed, as long as enterprises complete their registration information as required, they can still export products to the mainland after review and approval.\nIt is my understanding that some Taiwanese food production enterprises have now supplemented their registration materials, and the relevant competent authorities are reviewing them. Those that meet the requirements will be registered.\nFourth, this is fundamentally a simple enterprise registration issue, and it is not difficult to resolve. Media on the island have already pointed out that someone has deliberately turned it into a “Rashomon.” What is puzzling is why, with ample time available, the DPP authorities have not actively helped enterprises handle the relevant matters properly. One cannot help but suspect that they are politicizing economic and trade issues and turning a simple matter into a complicated one.\nIn just a few days, we will celebrate the Spring Festival, the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and we will soon usher in the Guimao Year of the Rabbit. Reunion is the enduring theme of the Spring Festival, and reunion is the shared hope of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. As the poem goes, “The sea sends up the sun at the end of the night; the river welcomes spring as the old year passes.” Although cross-Strait relations still carry a chill and dark shadows, the new spring on the river and the sun rising from the sea will surely arrive. On behalf of all colleagues at the Information Bureau, I would like to extend early New Year greetings to media friends and audiences on both sides of the Strait. I wish everyone a happy Year of the Rabbit, with great prospects (“大展宏‘兔’”).\nThank you all. This concludes the press conference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202301/t20230111_12501424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-01-12","Wang Wenbin","AFP","A question on the US and Japan. The US and Japan yesterday announced a significant strengthening of their military relationship. So Japan approved US plans for new Marine force on Okinawa island, so very close to Taiwan island. What is China’s reaction to this strengthening of the US-Japan military relationship?","We have noted the reports. Military cooperation between the US and Japan must not harm the interests of third parties or undermine the peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230112_11006313.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-12","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, Papua New Guinea Foreign Minister Justin Tkatchenko announced lately that the “Papua New Guinea Trade Office in Taiwan” will be closed. Do you have any comment?","We appreciate and applaud the Papua New Guinea government’s announcement of closing the “Papua New Guinea Trade Office in Taiwan”. This is the latest example that the one-China principle has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230112_11006313.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-13","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The US and Japan released a joint statement following the Security Consultative Committee (“2+2”) on January 11, calling China “the greatest strategic challenge in the Indo-Pacific region and beyond” and criticized China on Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang and maritime issues. Do you have any comment?","The wording on China in this joint statement smacks heavily of a zero-sum Cold-War mentality and contains groundless smears and attacks on China. We are firmly against it.\nThe US and Japan claim to advance regional peace and security, but what they do is finding pretexts for military build-up and wilful use of force. They claim to champion a free and open Indo-Pacific region, but what they do is putting up various exclusionary blocs to create division and confrontation. They claim to uphold the rules-based international order, but what they do is trampling on international law and the basic norms governing international relations and grossly interfering in other countries’ internal affairs. What they have done poses a real challenge to regional peace, security and stability.\nThe Asia-Pacific is an anchor for peace and development, not a wrestling ground for geopolitical competition. Countries in the region are for justice and against hegemonism. They hope to engage in cooperation, not confrontation. They aspire for true multilateralism and reject small circles that incite bloc confrontation. We urge the US and Japan to abandon the Cold-War mentality and ideological bias, stop creating imaginary enemies and stop trying to sow the seeds of a new Cold War in the Asia-Pacific, and not to become disrupters of a stable Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347447.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230113_11006972.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-16","Wang Wenbin","Shenzhen TV","Foreign Minister Qin Gang also visited Egypt and the League of Arab States Headquarters during his trip to Africa. Could you share more on this?","Not long ago, President Xi Jinping attended the first China-Arab States Summit, which guided the China-Arab relations into a new era of all-round, deepened progress. On January 15, Foreign Minister Qin Gang visited Egypt and the League of Arab States Headquarters. This is an important action for delivering on the outcomes of the China-Arab States Summit. It demonstrates China’s strong determination to make every effort with the Arab world to build a China-Arab community with a shared future in the new era.\nDuring the visit, Egyptian President Abdel Fattah El-Sisi met with Foreign Minister Qin, and Foreign Minister Qin also held talks with Egyptian Foreign Minister Sameh Shoukry. The two sides had in-depth exchanges of views on following through on the important common understandings between the two heads of state, and reached extensive common understandings on bilateral relations and regional and international issues of common interest.\nThe two sides agreed that China and Egypt enjoy solid strategic mutual trust, and should continue to firmly support each other on issues that bear on each other’s core interests and major concerns. China appreciates Egypt’s valuable support on issues that bear on China’s core interests, including affairs related to Taiwan and Xinjiang. China firmly supports Egypt in following a development path that suits its own national conditions, and in safeguarding its sovereignty and security and realizing development and revitalization.\nThe two sides agreed that China-Egypt cooperation on the Belt and Road Initiative has been productive and full of potential. China stands ready to further synergize its development strategies with Egypt’s, work together to implement the Global Development Initiative, jointly advance the construction of major projects, import more quality products from Egypt, and encourage more Chinese companies to invest and do business in Egypt, so as to achieve mutually-beneficial results at a higher level.\nThe two sides agreed that China and Egypt, with profound civilizations, need to continue expanding cultural and people-to-people exchanges, actively encourage exchanges between the think-tanks, youth and media organizations of the two countries, and realize people-to-people connectivity at a deeper level. China appreciates Egypt’s decision to welcome Chinese tourists. We believe that in the near future, the number of Chinese tourists and flights to Egypt will return to or even surpass the pre-pandemic level.\nThe two sides agreed that China and Egypt, with similar views and positions on regional and international issues, need to coordinate and work more closely together to advance the political settlement of regional hotspot issues, uphold the basic norms in international relations, safeguard the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs and protect the common interests of developing countries.\nDuring his visit to Egypt, Foreign Minister Qin held talks with Secretary-General of the League of Arab States (LAS) Ahmed Aboul Gheit. The two sides agreed to deliver on the outcomes of the China-Arab States Summit and accelerate the implementation of the eight major cooperation initiatives, so as to bring more benefits to the peoples of both sides. Foreign Minister Qin noted that China firmly supports Arab states in working in solidarity to address security issues in the region, supports the Arab people in exploring their own development paths independently, and supports the LAS in playing a bigger role in promoting peace and stability in the Middle East.\nSecretary-General Gheit expressed appreciation to China for steadfastly upholding justice in the world, supporting the development of Arab states and the unity of the LAS, and providing invaluable help to Arab countries in the successful fight against COVID-19. He noted that he looks forward to deeper Arab-China cooperation in all areas and that more Chinese citizens are welcome to visit Egypt and other Arab countries for sightseeing or carrying out economic and trade cooperation.\nDuring the visit, Foreign Minister Qin pointed out that the Palestinian question is at the heart of the Middle East issue and matters to the region’s peace and stability. The heightening Israeli-Palestinian situation is fundamentally caused by the stagnation in Israel-Palestine peace talks and the protracted delay in the implementation of the two-state solution. The international community needs to act with a stronger sense of urgency, keep the Palestinian issue high on the international agenda, push for the resumption of peace talks between Palestine and Israel, and properly address Jerusalem’s final status and other issues, so as to bring about the just and lasting settlement of the Palestinian issue on the basis of the two-state solution at an early date. Major countries with influence need to step up to their responsibility on this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347448.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230116_11008984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-16","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","US President Joe Biden and Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida held talks in Washington D.C. on January 13 and released a joint statement, which claims that the Indo-Pacific faces growing challenges including from actions inconsistent with the rules-based international order by China. They also stressed the commitment to strengthening the US-Japan alliance and the US’s commitment to Japan’s defense and…","The ugly playbook jointly used by Japan and the US to tarnish China’s image, interfere in China’s internal affairs and suppress China’s development is packed with danger and hypocrisy. We firmly reject it and have conveyed strong démarches.\nJapan’s militarist past, marked by devastating wars of aggression and brutal crimes against humanity, brought untold suffering on this region and beyond. Instead of drawing serious lessons from its past, Japan has displayed a dangerous tendency of rearming itself, with sharp rises in its annual defense spending for the 11th year running and constant readjustment of its defense policy aimed at military breakthrough. To justify its aggressive military build-up, Japan has been falsely hyping up regional tensions. It is even seeking to bring NATO into the Asia-Pacific. All of this makes people wonder whether Japan is tearing itself away from post-war peaceful development and fear the growing danger of history repeating itself. Our message for Japan: anyone seeking to jeopardize and risk the security and stability in the Asia-Pacific will be rejected and pushed back by countries across the region.\nThe US preaches the so-called “rules-based order”, but is second to none when it comes to undermining the international rules and order. From unwarranted invasion of other countries to arbitrary unilateral sanctions, from owing large arrears to the UN’s regular budget to deliberately impeding the appointment of new judges to the WTO’s Appellate Body, from coercive diplomacy to piecing together exclusionary blocs, from muscle-flexing in the Asia-Pacific by deploying warships and military aircraft to opening Pandora’s box on nuclear proliferation, facts prove time and again that the US does not really care about rules or order. It cares about only one thing - the perpetuation of US hegemony. Any existing rule that stands in the way of US interests will be ignored, replaced or even thrown out of the window, even if it was proposed and written by the US itself.\nIt must be pointed out that China will stay firmly committed to the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics. No country or force can hold back China’s development. We will do what is necessary to resolutely defend our sovereignty, security and development interests.\nWe call on the US and Japan to step out of the Cold-War mentality, quit the obsession with containing and suppressing China, stop dangerously ramping up military build-up and propagating chaos in the world and return to the right path of peace, friendship and cooperation.\n**********************************\nThe 14th “Love Knows No Borders” international charity sale will open in a virtual format in Beijing on the afternoon of January 17 under the theme of “Showered with Love”. Foreign Minister Qin Gang, special guest Madame Qian Wei, wife of Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and State Councilor Wang Yi, among others, will attend the event. This year, there will again be online and livestreaming charity sales. You can access the special webpage for the online charity sale by searching for Alibaba digital county Tmall flagship store on Taobao APP. The webpage will be launched officially on January 17 and remain available till February 8. There will be a livestreaming sale in the evening around February 8.\nSince 2009, the “Love Knows No Borders” international charity sale has been successfully held for 13 consecutive years, and a host of poverty alleviation and assistance projects have been implemented, covering infrastructure, health, livelihood, medical care, child care and other fields. Over the past 13 years, the focus of the “Love Knows No Borders” international charity sale has been on poverty alleviation and rural revitalization. The love it gathers from both at home and abroad has yielded fruitful results.\nThis year’s charity sale will be held under the theme of “Showered with Love”. The donations will be used on the “projects of warmth”, installing and upgrading shower facilities for elementary and middle schools in Malipo and Jinping, two counties in Yunnan.\nYou will find an upcoming series of short videos on the official accounts of “Love Knows No Borders” on media platforms such as Wechat channel, Douyin, Kuaishou and Bilibili. Foreign diplomatic envoys and representatives of international organizations in China will share their experience and stories about being part of the charity sale and promote the culture and products of their countries. We hope you will follow the “Love Knows No Borders” international charity sale, join the activities and share your love.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347448.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230116_11008984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-01-29","Ma Xiaoguang","国台办发言人马晓光29日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 29: TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang answered reporters’ questions on the 29th, saying: We have always respected, cared for, and benefited Taiwan compatriots, and we continue to work to promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. Regarding the problem that the registration information of some Taiwan food companies is incomplete and irregular, we are…","Ma Xiaoguang said that we attach great importance to this and are handling it actively. After review by the relevant competent authorities, 63 enterprises that meet the requirements, including the Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Factory, have been registered or had their registration information updated. For those that do not meet the requirements and temporarily cannot be registered, we have also explained the specific reasons one by one.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202301/t20230129_12505897.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-01-30","Mao Ning","China Daily","The US State Department Spokesperson has repeatedly mentioned Secretary Blinken’s upcoming visit to China, saying that his team will discuss with China how to responsibly manage competition and step up cooperation on transnational challenges, and also raise concerns on issues related to Taiwan, fentanyl, Ukraine and the Korean Peninsula. Do you have any comment?","In growing relations with the US, China follows the three principles proposed by President Xi Jinping, namely mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, and at the same time remains committed to defending our sovereignty, security and development interests.\nChina does not shy away or flinch from competition, but we are against defining the entire China-US relations with competition alone and using competition as an excuse to contain and suppress others. We are ready to have both bilateral and multilateral communication and cooperation with the US on the basis of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit, but we need to remind the US that it cannot demand communication and cooperation from China while keeping interfering in China’s internal affairs and hurting China’s interests.\nThe Taiwan question is at the heart of China’s core interests. It is the bedrock of the political foundation of China-US relations, and the number one red line that must not be crossed between China and the US. At no time should the US ever seek to cross that red line.\nWith regard to international counternarcotics efforts, China is the first country in the world to have officially scheduled fentanyl-related substances as a class. China has taken an active part in international counternarcotics law enforcement cooperation under the framework of the UN conventions on drug control. China’s counternarcotics capacity has, however, been seriously hampered by US sanctions on relevant Chinese institutions. We are firmly against those sanctions and urge the US to reflect on its inadequate counternarcotics efforts instead of deflecting the blame.\nOn Ukraine and the Korean nuclear issue, China is committed to seeking a political settlement and bringing parties to the table. We are against any rhetoric or action that could fuel the tensions and make matters worse. Our policy and position can stand up to the test of history and facts.\nThe future of both our peoples — indeed, the future of the entire planet — depends on a healthy and stable China-US relationship. We hope the US will work with China and let China-US interactions be defined by dialogue and win-win cooperation, not confrontation and zero-sum competition, and deliver on the important common understandings reached by the two heads of state to bring bilateral relations back to the track of healthy and stable growth.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347453.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230130_11016413.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-30","Mao Ning","AFP","A US general has predicted a possible military conflict between the US and China probably over Taiwan in 2025. What’s your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese. The real cause of the new round of tensions across the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities’ continued act of soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence” and the agenda among some people in the US to use Taiwan to contain China. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, stop military contact with Taiwan and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347453.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230130_11016413.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-30","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Republican House Speaker Kevin McCarthy is reportedly expected to visit Taiwan in the spring, and the Pentagon is already planning his trip. How does the foreign ministry respond to this?","China opposes any form of official interaction between its Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We hope US lawmakers will abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and refrain from doing things detrimental to China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347453.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230130_11016413.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-01-31","Mao Ning","AFP","The Czech Republic’s president-elect Petr Pavel held a phone call with Tsai Ing-wen recently, during which he expressed hope to meet Tsai in person. Do you have any comment?","Despite China’s repeated dissuasion and démarches, the Czech Republic’s president-elect Petr Pavel went ahead with the call with Tsai Ing-wen, a move that constituted official contact with the Taiwan authorities and a serious interference in China’s internal affairs. This is a blatant violation of the Czech Republic’s political commitment to the one-China principle and sends a wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and strongly opposes this and we have made solemn démarche to the Czech side.\nThere is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is China’s core interest and the political foundation for China’s relations with countries that have diplomatic ties with China. We urge the Czech Republic to take immediate and effective measures to correct the wrongdoing, undo the negative impact of this incident and credibly abide by the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347454.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202301/t20230131_11017020.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-02-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 1 (dateline): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters' questions on February 1, stated that on February 1, the mainland's aviation authority had sent a letter via the contact channel under the Cross-Strait Air Transport Agreement to the Taiwan side, stating that at present, the epidemic situations on both sides of the Strait are stable, making this a favorable time to further restore the normal operation of cross-Strait air routes. It hopes that both sides will move toward each other to restore the normal operation of cross-Strait air routes, and that the Taiwan side can give priority to resuming the 16 cross-Strait direct flight destinations, such as Guangzhou, that Taiwan compatriots have frequently raised.\nZhu Fenglian said that we believe that at present, the epidemic on the mainland has been well controlled, and Taiwan compatriots can come to study, work, start businesses, and live with complete peace of mind. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a strong desire for normal exchanges and visits, and we attach great importance to this and have comprehensively made relevant preparations. We hope the Taiwan side will cherish the hard-won achievements of cross-Strait direct air links, take pragmatic measures, give priority to resuming the cross-Strait direct flight destinations that Taiwan compatriots have frequently raised, continue to promote the normal operation of cross-Strait air routes, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230201_12507017.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-02-02","Mao Ning","CGTN","NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg has concluded his visit to the ROK and Japan. During his visit, he mentioned China on several occasions, claiming that China is leading an “authoritarian pushback” against the rules-based, open and democratic international order; that China is developing military capabilities that could also reach NATO countries and is threatening Taiwan; that NATO must “remain united and…","We have stated our position on NATO several times this week. The NATO Secretary General went to the ROK and Japan, yet he kept referring to China and hyping up the so-called “China threat”, drawing ideological lines and sowing discord between countries in the region. The intention behind those moves is quite alarming.\nChina is committed to world peace and stability. We do not engage in geopolitical contests and have no intention to challenge or threaten any country. The peace, cooperation, stability and prosperity of the Asia-Pacific has been made possible thanks to the concerted efforts of countries in the region. The Asia-Pacific does not welcome Cold-War thinking and bloc confrontation. NATO needs to reflect on itself what kind of role it has played in European security. We have seen what NATO has done to Europe, and NATO must not seek to sow chaos here in the Asia-Pacific or elsewhere in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347456.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230202_11018699.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-02","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","Tsai Ing-wen met with former head of the US Indo-Pacific Command Phil Davidson in Taiwan today. What’s your comment?","We have time and again made our position clear on Taiwan. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese and must be decided by Chinese ourselves. The tensions across the Taiwan Strait are caused by the DPP authorities, which have kept soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence”, and some people in the US, who intend to use Taiwan to contain China. The US should credibly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop all forms of official interaction and military contact with Taiwan, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347456.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230202_11018699.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-02","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy said that China cannot tell him where he can go at any time or any place. He was responding to a question from reporters about the potential trip to Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on Speaker McCarthy’s words as to whether China can tell him where he cannot go?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. China urges relevant people in the US to credibly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, observe the basic norms in international relations, handle Taiwan-related issues in a prudent and proper manner, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and refrain from doing anything that could undermine China-US relations or peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China will continue to resolutely safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347456.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230202_11018699.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-02","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","The speaker of the Czech parliament has said that she will visit Taiwan in March. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on the potential visit to Taiwan in March of the Czech parliament speaker?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and concerns China’s core interest. China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between its Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We oppose any political manipulation using the Taiwan question.\nWe urge certain Czech politician to take China’s position seriously, respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, cancel the wrong decision, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347456.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230202_11018699.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-03","Mao Ning","CNN","The US military has also said that it is not the first time that high-altitude surveillance balloons from China have been discovered in the US airspace and they have expressed the hope several times to maintain communication with the Chinese side via multiple channels. But after Speaker Pelosi’s visit to Taiwan, the Chinese side has suspended mil-to-mil talks with the US. Does this incident highlight the…","China is a responsible country and we always act in accordance with international law. We have no intention to violate the territory or airspace of any sovereign country. As I said, we are gathering and verifying the facts. We hope both sides can handle the matter together in a cool-headed and prudent manner.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347457.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230203_11019334.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-03","Mao Ning","Reuters","US CIA Director William Burns said on Thursday that the Chinese leader’s ambitions towards Taiwan should not be underestimated despite him likely being sobered by the performance of Russia’s military in Ukraine. Do you have any comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. The Taiwan question and the Ukraine issue are different in nature and are not comparable at all. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese and must be decided by Chinese ourselves. The tensions across the Taiwan Strait are caused by the DPP authorities, which have kept soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence”, and some people in the US, who intend to use Taiwan to contain China. The US should credibly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop all forms of official interaction and military contact with Taiwan, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347457.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230203_11019334.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-02-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 6 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 6th that KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan will lead a delegation to visit from February 8 to 17 to attend relevant cross-Strait exchange activities and make visits.","Zhu Fenglian said: We welcome Vice Chairman Xia Liyan to lead a delegation on a visit. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges with the Kuomintang, consolidate and enhance mutual trust, deepen exchanges and cooperation in all fields, jointly promote the development of relations between the two parties and cross-strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and advance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230206_12508216.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 8, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first introduced the situation of the heads of the Central Taiwan Affairs Office, the Taiwan Affairs Office and the Straits Exchange Foundation (ARATS) visiting and extending Spring Festival greetings to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in the mainland, and…","Hello everyone, and welcome to the first press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office after the Spring Festival. Before answering questions, I would like to brief you on the situation during the Spring Festival and the Lantern Festival, when the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office thoroughly implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important New Year address and carried out a series of visits and condolence activities for Taiwan compatriots.\nOn January 28, Song Tao, Director of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, met with Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, in Xiamen, and conveyed General Secretary Xi Jinping’s Spring Festival greetings and regards to Hung Hsiu-chu. On January 29 and 30, Director Song Tao, in Xiamen, learned about the partial resumption of “mini three links” flights, visited and extended condolences to Taiwan compatriots traveling between Xiamen and Kinmen via the “mini three links,” visited the Xiamen Taiwan Association and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and held a discussion with Taiwan compatriot and Taiwan-invested enterprise representatives in Fujian to hear their opinions and suggestions. On February 5, the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held the 2023 Taiwan Businessperson Spring Festival Forum in Beijing, attended by more than 50 Taiwanese businessperson representatives, where Director Song Tao extended Spring Festival greetings to Taiwanese businesspeople. From January 16 to 18, Zhang Zhijun, President of the Straits Exchange Foundation, visited and extended condolences to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in Hefei, learning about enterprises’ production and operations and the study and living conditions of Taiwan compatriots, Taiwanese businesspeople and Taiwanese youth. On January 17, Long Mingbiao, Deputy Director of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, visited and extended condolences in Beijing to Taiwanese young entertainer Lu Chia-jung, who was injured in a traffic accident. On January 12 and 14, Li Wenhui, Vice President of the Straits Exchange Foundation, visited and extended condolences to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople in Shanghai.\nThrough this series of visits and condolence activities, we have strongly felt that cross-Strait exchanges accord with the will of the people on both sides and are the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides. We must work together to restore normal cross-Strait exchanges as early as possible. At present, the epidemic on the mainland has been well controlled, and using the epidemic as an excuse to block cross-Strait exchanges is untenable and unpopular. We will implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important expositions on work concerning Taiwan, and in advancing the process of national rejuvenation and national reunification, we will always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots. We will continue to uphold the concept of “Cross-Strait Compatriots Are One Family,” promote the restoration and expansion of personnel exchanges between the two sides and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and encourage and support compatriots on both sides to move toward each other and advance hand in hand, jointly creating a better future for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508983.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The Spring Festival has just passed. We note that during the Spring Festival, localities organized visits and condolences to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople and held a variety of Spring Festival friendship events. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During the Spring Festival and Lantern Festival, all localities fully implemented the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, respected, cared for, and benefited Taiwan compatriots, and actively carried out diverse forms of New Year visits and friendship events. I believe that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises who spent the New Year on the mainland strongly felt this.\nThis Spring Festival, Taiwan compatriots on the mainland fully witnessed the sincere care from all regions. Responsible officials of more than 10 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities, including Beijing, Liaoning, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Fujian, Jiangxi, Shandong, Henan, Guangdong, Guangxi, Chongqing, and Sichuan, went deep into factories, schools, and homes to care for and visit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, extended New Year greetings, and helped resolve difficulties they encountered in production, daily life, medical treatment, and other areas. After the Spring Festival, Xin Changxing, Secretary of the Jiangsu Provincial Party Committee, fulfilled a prior commitment by promptly visiting Taiwan-funded enterprises in Kunshan for research, encouraging local authorities to provide better public services to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises and to continue advancing the integrated economic development of Jiangsu and Taiwan. Luo Dongchuan, Deputy Secretary of the Fujian Provincial Party Committee, visited Taiwan youth spending the New Year in Fujian and took part in a New Year friendship event for Taiwan youth in Fujian. During the Spring Festival, departments in various parts of Jiangxi Province visited and extended greetings to more than 390 Taiwan compatriots and their relatives and more than 280 Taiwan-funded enterprises. Guangzhou visited and extended greetings to more than 300 Taiwan compatriots and their relatives and 75 Taiwan-funded enterprises. Chongqing visited and extended greetings to more than 800 Taiwan compatriots and their relatives and more than 50 Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nThis Spring Festival, compatriots on both sides of the Strait actively took part in rich and colorful New Year friendship events, both online and offline. Beijing, Shanghai, Tianjin, Sichuan, Chongqing, Hubei, Jiangsu, and other places held a series of activities, including New Year hotpot gatherings, symposiums and exchange meetings, cultural, sports, and friendship events, and traditional folk customs, deepening the friendship of “cross-Strait compatriots are one family.” “Cross-Strait compatriots wish each other a happy New Year” became a frequently used phrase in New Year greetings from netizens on both sides of the Strait, and related topics were exposed more than 800 million times. Taiwan political figures, media professionals, experts and scholars, entertainers, Taiwan businesspeople and youth, clan association representatives, as well as netizens from the mainland, Hong Kong, Macao, and overseas, posted New Year greeting videos on cross-Strait social platforms, expressing their earnest hope for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resumption of normal exchanges, and strengthened cooperation. The Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office organized a series of Beijing-Taiwan Spring Festival exchange activities via live video link titled “The Most Beautiful Cross-Strait Reunion,” in which more than 1,000 Taiwan grassroots residents reunited with Beijing residents “in the cloud.” Jinan, Qingdao, Weifang, Rizhao, and other cities in Shandong Province held online friendship events such as “Welcome Spring with Family and Friends, Send Blessings for a Happy Family,” and more than 270 compatriots from both sides of the Strait celebrated the holiday online together.\nThis Spring Festival, people on both sides of the Strait shared a cultural feast. Nearly 20 Taiwan performing artists took part in the Spring Festival Galas hosted by CCTV, local satellite TV stations, and the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles, and nearly 200 Taiwan youth performed in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao-Taiwan Youth Lantern Festival Gala. Together with mainland performers, they presented wonderful performances and festive blessings, expressing the sense of nation and family shared by people on both sides of the Strait whose blood ties are inseparable. High-quality films and TV series such as *The Wandering Earth 2* and *Shock Wave* set off a binge-watching craze on both sides of the Strait at the same time, and classic mainland TV dramas such as *The Legend of Zhen Huan* were broadcast on repeat around the clock on the island, fully demonstrating that people on both sides of the Strait share blood ties, cultural connections, and spiritual affinity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","What has been the effect of the partial resumption of the “mini three links” since it resumed? Yesterday (February 7), the Taiwan side normalized the “mini three links” special program, but there are still many restrictions. What comment do you have?","Since the partial resumption of the \"Mini Three Links\" on January 7, it has provided convenience for compatriots of Kinmen and Matsu to return home for the Lunar New Year and reunite with their families. As of February 6, vessels across the Strait had made 78 round trips in total, carrying 5,169 passengers. Among them, the Xiamen-Kinmen route had 62 voyages with 4,736 passengers; the Fuzhou-Matsu route had 16 voyages with 433 passengers.\nThe mainland side has continued to promote the full resumption of the \"Mini Three Links.\" On January 29, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, went to the Wutong Passenger Terminal in Xiamen to learn about the partial resumption of the \"Mini Three Links,\" and extended greetings to Taiwan compatriots who travel between Xiamen and Kinmen via the \"Mini Three Links.\" He said that the epidemic on the mainland is now well under control, that compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a strong desire to resume normal exchanges and travel, and that we attach great importance to this and have made full preparations. Using the epidemic as a pretext to block cross-Strait exchanges goes against the will of the people and does not win popular support; the full resumption of the \"Mini Three Links\" and normal exchanges and travel between the peoples of both sides should be realized as soon as possible.\nAlthough the DPP authorities have agreed to make the so-called \"Mini Three Links\" special program regular, they continue to exclude compatriots from areas outside Kinmen and Matsu, so the \"Mini Three Links\" cannot play its due role in cross-Strait exchanges. It is no wonder that the people of the island criticize them for disregarding the will of the people and for \"lacking sincerity.\" We hope the DPP authorities will put the well-being of the people first, and promptly lift all artificial restrictions so that the \"Mini Three Links\" can fully resume.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508979.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that the mainland’s aviation authority hopes the Taiwan side will give priority to restoring 16 cross-Strait direct flight routes. Which 16 routes exactly? How will the restoration of these routes be promoted going forward?","At present, the epidemic on the mainland has been well controlled, and compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the aviation industry eagerly look forward to the full resumption of direct cross-Strait flight routes. According to feedback from Taiwan compatriots and relevant groups on the island, on February 1 the mainland’s aviation authorities, through the channels of the Cross-Strait Air Transport Agreement, urged the Taiwan side to resume direct cross-Strait flight routes, giving priority to resuming 16 direct routes that Taiwan compatriots have most frequently raised: Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Nanjing, Wuxi, Hangzhou, Ningbo, Wuhan, Fuzhou, Hefei, Chongqing, Changsha, Zhengzhou, Haikou, Xi’an, Shenyang, and Harbin. Resuming these direct routes is the first step toward fully restoring cross-Strait passenger direct flights. Going forward, we will continue to promote the resumption of more cross-Strait direct routes according to the needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, to meet the needs of cross-Strait exchanges and interaction.\nIt must be emphasized that we have made all relevant preparations for resuming direct cross-Strait flight routes, with no restrictions or obstacles whatsoever. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public sentiment, take pragmatic measures, and stop using the epidemic as an excuse or stalling with so-called “assessments” and “considerations” that obstruct the resumption of direct cross-Strait flight routes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508974.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","It is understood that Fuzhou City, Fujian Province, took the lead in incorporating Taiwan compatriots who seek employment and start businesses into its housing security system, and has implemented it for more than a year, which has been welcomed by Taiwan compatriots there. Please introduce the situation of Taiwan compatriots renting public rental housing in Fuzhou and other relevant localities.","We uphold the concept that “cross-Strait families are one family” and respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots. To enable Taiwan compatriots to live and work in peace and contentment on the mainland, the Ministry of Housing and Urban-Rural Development and other departments and localities have continuously issued relevant policies to address the housing needs of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan compatriots holding the Taiwan Residence Permit may, in accordance with relevant policy provisions, purchase commercial housing or rent public rental housing on the mainland.\nFuzhou City is committed to exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development and building the pioneer city as the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to land on the mainland. In July 2021, it issued the “Implementation Plan for Housing Security Work for Taiwan Compatriots Employed and Starting Businesses in Fuzhou (Trial),” incorporating Taiwan compatriots who are employed or starting businesses into the housing security system and providing a total of 1,050 affordable housing units to Taiwan compatriots at one time. Three batches of applications have so far been accepted, and 304 Taiwan compatriots from 206 households have moved into Taiwan compatriot public rental housing. A “one-stop” policy system has been established from application to move-in, with a 30% rent reduction under market-based standards. Applicants who have no housing, hold a Taiwan Residence Permit, have signed a labor contract of more than one year with an enterprise or institution, or are enterprise legal persons engaged in self-initiated business are eligible to apply. After applying, applicants receive “one-stop” services from banks, gas, property management, and other departments at the housing selection site, achieving quick application and quick move-in. After moving in, a community-integrated service model for Taiwan compatriots is adopted. Fujian Province’s first Taiwan compatriot “building chief” was introduced, Taiwan compatriot community builders were appointed, and Taiwan compatriots are supported and encouraged to participate in cross-Strait community governance. Many Taiwan compatriots have reported that Taiwan compatriot public rental housing has complete supporting facilities and convenient living conditions, which helps young Taiwan people and Taiwan compatriots share employment and entrepreneurship information and integrate more quickly into local life, and it has been welcomed by Taiwan compatriots living in Fuzhou.\nBeyond Fuzhou, Beijing, Guangzhou, Xiamen, and other cities are also continuously creating conditions for Taiwan compatriots to live with peace of mind. Beijing launched the implementation of a rental housing allocation plan for Taiwan compatriots’ security housing in Beijing in July 2019. It has provided policy consultations to more than 200 Taiwan compatriots, and 53 Taiwan compatriots have applied for and moved into housing, and Taiwan compatriots are able to integrate, succeed, and stay in Beijing. Guangzhou has made 1,000 public rental housing units available for application by youth from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, and Taiwan compatriots have so far applied for and moved into nearly 100 units. The revised 2.0 version of the “Guangzhou 60 Measures Benefiting Taiwan Compatriots” issued in 2023 clearly states: support qualified Taiwan compatriots in applying to lease public rental housing as a whole for newly employed workers without housing; encourage qualified Taiwan compatriots to apply to rent talent apartments at all levels in urban districts or related rent subsidies, such as Nansha District providing youth apartments or a maximum annual accommodation subsidy of 20,000 yuan per person to qualified youth from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. Xiamen has a cumulative total of 115 person-times of Taiwan compatriots enjoying public rental housing policies, with 79 currently renting. In June 2022, Taiwan compatriots were included as eligible for purchasing subsidized commercial housing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508976.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","A spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that 63 Taiwan food enterprises that meet the requirements, including the Kinmen Kaoliang Liquor Factory, have been registered or had their registration information renewed. Can the list of these 63 enterprises be queried? For Taiwan food enterprises that do not meet the requirements and cannot currently be registered, what further assistance will the…","We attach great importance to and actively address the issue of registration for Taiwan food enterprises. Recently, 63 Taiwan food enterprises have completed registration or updated their registration information. Relevant information can be queried in the “Information Services” column of the website of the Import and Export Food Safety Bureau of the General Administration of Customs. At present, the competent mainland authorities are reviewing the registration materials submitted by other Taiwan food enterprises in accordance with regulations.\nWe are willing to continue working with relevant parties on the island to help resolve specific problems that Taiwan food enterprises encounter during the registration application process, and to facilitate the import of Taiwan food into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Since the partial resumption of the “Mini Three Links” flights, more and more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople have eagerly hoped for the full resumption of the “Mini Three Links” and the early realization of normal cross-Strait exchanges. May I ask what plans the mainland side has for promoting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in various fields?","Over the three years since the outbreak of the COVID-19 epidemic, the mainland has overcome the impact of epidemic factors and artificial obstacles set up by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. Our efforts to promote cross-Strait exchanges and deepen integrated development have not stopped, the eager desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer to each other has not diminished, and civil exchanges and cooperation across the Strait have not been interrupted. As the mainland's epidemic prevention and control enters a new stage, restoring offline cross-Strait exchanges as soon as possible and achieving normalized personnel movement across the Strait and regularized exchanges and cooperation in all areas is a shared expectation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nDuring the Spring Festival, many cross-Strait groups and institutions exchanged New Year greetings and festive wishes and discussed arrangements for cross-Strait exchanges this year. Relevant groups and institutions on the island are looking forward to visiting the mainland this year. Exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait have been carried out for more than 30 years, with a solid foundation and inherent momentum, and this is also the general trend. We believe that cross-Strait exchanges will soon welcome spring warmth. Various localities on the mainland will hold a series of cross-Strait exchange activities, and we welcome all sectors of Taiwan to take an active part and welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland more often and see it for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508982.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视新闻记者","It is reported that the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council recently approved another batch of cross-Strait exchange bases. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Exchange and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is an important driving force for the continued advancement of cross-Strait relations. In the new year, all sectors on both sides are eagerly looking forward to exchange and cooperation in all fields returning to normal as soon as possible. To create more platforms for cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and provide compatriots on both sides with more opportunities to look back on history, savor culture, share familial affection, and develop together, the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office have recently approved the establishment of nine Cross-Strait Exchange Bases, namely: the Zhaojun Museum in Hohhot, Inner Mongolia; the Guandi Temple in Dongshan, Zhangzhou, Fujian; the ancestral shrine of Kaizhang Sheng Wang in Yunxiao, Zhangzhou, Fujian; the Xianying Palace on Changdao Island, Yantai, Shandong; the Tianhou (Mazu) Museum in Nanshan, Shenzhen, Guangdong; the baseball fields including the Baseball Field in Zhongshan Park, Shenzhen, Guangdong; the Sanshan Guowang Ancestral Temple in Jieyang, Guangdong; the Guan Yue Temple in Chongqing; and the Taohuajiang Cultural Tourism Scenic Area in Guilin, Guangxi. Each of these nine exchange bases has its own distinctive features and unique resources for cross-Strait exchange. Among them are important venues that have hosted cross-Strait cultural and sports exchange activities in recent years. For example, the eight baseball fields including the Baseball Field in Zhongshan Park, Shenzhen, have successfully hosted the Grand Finals of the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League three times, with 116 student baseball teams from both sides and nearly 3,000 athletes, coaches and referees participating, making it a well-known cross-Strait student baseball event. There are also cultural and museum venues that carry the shared historical and cultural memories of compatriots on both sides, such as the Guandi Temple in Dongshan, Zhangzhou, which has continuously hosted the Cross-Strait (Dongshan, Fujian) Guandi Cultural Tourism Festival for 30 sessions since 1992, attracting an average of more than 50 temples and groups from the island each year and receiving nearly 60,000 Taiwan compatriot visits. It is one of the longest-running cross-Strait exchange activities. There is also the ancestral home of Kaizhang Sheng Wang culture in Yunxiao, Zhangzhou, Fujian, which has hosted eight sessions of the Cross-Strait Kaizhang Sheng Wang Culture Festival, involving about five million compatriots from both sides in related activities.\nSince 2009, the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office have successively approved the establishment of 91 Cross-Strait Exchange Bases in 24 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian, playing an important role in cross-Strait exchanges. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange at these exchange bases, and we hope relevant localities will build and develop the exchange bases well and effectively give play to their demonstrative and leading role in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508975.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","According to statistics, during the Spring Festival, domestic tourism on the mainland reached 308 million trips, and inbound and outbound travelers numbered 2.877 million person-times. However, because of the DPP authorities' political manipulation, Taiwan's tourism operators have been unable to share in the dividends of the mainland's tourism recovery. They have said they miss mainland tourists and that the DPP…","The situation of mainland tourism during the Spring Festival, which you mentioned, demonstrates a fact: as epidemic prevention and control work on the mainland has entered a new stage, economic and social life, including tourism, is fully returning to normal. Taiwan compatriots can come to the mainland to study, work, visit relatives and friends, travel, and engage in exchanges with peace of mind.\nAs for the target of Taiwan visitors claimed by the DPP authorities, do you think it is credible? Since last year, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan has repeatedly claimed it would gradually restore healthy and orderly cross-Strait personnel exchanges, but this is merely empty talk. In reality, the DPP authorities still restrict entry into Taiwan by people from the mainland and from Hong Kong and Macao. Where does the so-called 1 million mainland tourists come from?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's well-known political scholar Chu Yun-han has passed away. What is the TAO's evaluation?","Mr. Zhu Yunhan had deep national sentiment, devoted himself to promoting national rejuvenation, made many contributions to research on China’s modernization development model, and for a long time personally promoted cross-strait exchanges and cooperation and the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, contributing greatly. We deeply mourn Mr. Zhu Yunhan’s passing due to illness and extend our heartfelt condolences to his family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that, “under rationality, equality, and mutual respect,” she is willing to conduct dialogue with the mainland, “to jointly seek feasible paths acceptable to both sides that promote regional peace and stability.” What comment do you have?","Do you all believe these words? As everyone knows, the '1992 Consensus' is the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. This foundation fully embodies mutual respect and equal consultation between the two sides. Whether it is the consultations between the two sides' associations, or the liaison and communication mechanism previously established between the TAO and the Mainland Affairs Council, these are concrete and vivid examples. As long as the DPP authorities recognize the '1992 Consensus,' which embodies the one-China principle, and, through practical action, stop 'independence' provocations and collusion with external forces to confront the mainland, cross-Strait dialogue and consultation can resume.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508981.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Liyan will lead a delegation to visit from February 8 to 17. The mainland side welcomes this and is willing to strengthen exchanges on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” We note that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople are more concerned with issues such as restoring cross-Strait direct flight routes, customs…","To promote exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait and enhance the interests and welfare of people on both sides, during the visit of Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Liyan, relevant parties on both sides will jointly hold the following exchange activities.\nFirst, the Straits Institute for Cross-Strait Relations and the Kuomintang National Policy Research Foundation will jointly host a symposium titled “Cross-Strait Relations and Exchange and Cooperation in the Post-Epidemic Period,” to be held in Beijing on the morning of February 10.\nSecond, the All-China Youth Federation and the Kuomintang Youth Work Association serve as guiding units, and the Shanghai Municipal Youth Federation, the Shanghai Youth Entrepreneurs Association, the Youth Committee of the Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange Association, and the Young Entrepreneurs Committee of the “Three Three Society” jointly host the Cross-Strait Youth Entrepreneurs (Shanghai) Exchange Activity, to be held in Shanghai on the morning of February 13.\nVice Chairman Xia Liyan will attend the above activities and visit Nanjing, Wuhan, Chongqing, Chengdu and other places. We will release information about the specific arrangements in a timely manner, and we ask everyone to keep following our updates.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","It is reported that, under this year's enrollment policies and methods, starting March 1, Taiwan high school graduates may apply to mainland universities using their “General Scholastic Ability Test” (學測) scores. Please introduce the relevant policy.","Taiwan's 2023 academic year “Xuece” (General Scholastic Ability Test) concluded in mid-January. We warmly welcome eligible Taiwan students to apply for mainland universities, and we will provide all necessary support and services. High school graduates in Taiwan may apply to study at mainland universities through three channels:\nFirst channel: Starting March 1, Taiwan examinees who take the “Xuece” may register through the “System for Mainland General Higher Education Institutions to Recruit Taiwan High School Graduates Based on Taiwan Xuece Scores.” This year, all 412 mainland universities qualified to recruit students from Taiwan will use this system for admissions, and no application fee will be charged. Each examinee may apply to up to 6 universities, and each university may be applied to for up to 6 majors. From May 15 to 19, examinees may log into the system to check admission results and confirm; examinees who were not admitted may register supplementary applications during the “volunteer solicitation” session of the relevant universities in the system at the end of May.\nSecond channel: Taiwan examinees who take the “Tongce” (Unified Test) may apply to 13 undergraduate universities, including Minnan Normal University, and 6 higher vocational colleges, including Fujian Institute of Information Technology.\nThird channel: The policies for the Fujian-based eight universities' special enrollment for Taiwan students and the “joint enrollment by two universities” of Jinan University and Huaqiao University remain unchanged. Specific timing shall be subject to the announcements on the official websites of the universities.\nWe hope that all Taiwan students who wish to study on the mainland can realize their wishes. We will continue to provide convenience and services for Taiwan students to study and pursue further education on the mainland, helping more Taiwan students realize their life dreams on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508978.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: Regarding Kuomintang Vice Chairman Lin Hsia-yen's visit to the mainland, the DPP said he “may fall into the mainland's coercive political framework and endorse the ‘one country, two systems’ Taiwan plan.” What is your response to this? Second question: Wu Chao-hsieh, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, has recently been frequently interviewed by foreign media, claiming that “Taiwan will…","On the first question: The mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society is for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and sincerely work for the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and endangering their lives and property. They are step by step pushing Taiwan toward danger. This is coercion of the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and a threat to Taiwan's greatest interests.\nOn the second question: No matter how “Taiwan independence” forces and external forces collude, the international community's pattern of adhering to one China is unbreakable. We urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and the commitments they have made on the Taiwan question, and to handle the Taiwan question properly. The DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Hsing Yun, founding Master of Fo Guang Shan in Taiwan and founder of the International Buddhist Progress Society, passed away on February 5. Master Hsing Yun opposed “Taiwan independence” during his lifetime, advocated peace across the Taiwan Strait, and his greatest wish was to see cross-Strait reunification. What comment do you have?","Venerable Hsing Yun, founder of the Fo Guang Shan monastic lineage and founder of the International Buddhist Progress Society, passed away in Taiwan on February 5, and we are deeply saddened. The Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, and the Straits Exchange Foundation of the Chinese mainland expressed profound grief at Venerable Hsing Yun's passing.\nVenerable Hsing Yun devoted his life to promoting the Buddha's teachings, dedicated himself to public welfare and social well-being, edified people's hearts, and vigorously promoted Chinese culture. He enjoyed great renown across both sides of the Taiwan Strait and overseas. In particular, Venerable Hsing Yun consistently upheld national righteousness, firmly supported unification, resolutely opposed “Taiwan independence,” actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges, and worked to bring compatriots on both sides closer in spirit. His contributions were outstanding and he was deeply respected by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe lofty virtue and bearing of Venerable Hsing Yun will be remembered by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We should especially remember that Venerable Hsing Yun's long-held wish was for the Chinese nation to achieve great rejuvenation. We sincerely hope that Buddhist figures and the broad base of believers in Taiwan will uphold Venerable Hsing Yun's legacy, continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, help advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and work tirelessly toward the peaceful reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","Starting yesterday, the DPP authorities have made the “Small Three Links” special project permanent, but they continue to exclude Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople from areas other than Kinmen and Matsu. Recently, at the “2023 Mainland Taiwan Business Spring Festival Event” held in Taipei, a Taiwan businessperson told Tsai Ing-wen that they hoped cross-Strait exchanges would be fully restored, and Tsai…","From what you said, one can feel that the wishes of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople are very clear and strong: they hope that the \"Small Three Links\" can fully resume operations, and that personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides can be restored and expanded at an early date. However, the DPP authorities continue to exclude compatriots outside the Kinmen and Matsu areas, making it difficult for the \"Small Three Links\" to play its due role in cross-Strait exchanges. Ultimately, they are doing this out of political self-interest. We once again call on the DPP authorities to put the well-being of the people first, to promptly lift all artificial restrictions, and to fully restore the \"Small Three Links\" and normal exchanges between the people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","After assuming the chairmanship of the DPP, Lai Ching-te said that his “pragmatic” determination is that Taiwan is already a so-called “sovereign and independent country,” that there is no need to again declare “Taiwan independence,” and that in the future he will continue Tsai Ing-wen's cross-Strait line and the “4 insistences.” What is your comment?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China; the historical threads are clear, and the legal facts are evident. Taiwan has never been a country and will never become one. “Taiwan independence” separatism runs counter to the trend of historical development, defies the will of all Chinese descendants, and seriously harms the interests of compatriots on both sides. No matter what packaging or rhetoric is used, it cannot succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230208_12508980.htm"],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","Recently, news that a young Taiwan girl suffering from a rare disease went to the mainland for treatment because treatment costs on the island were too high has attracted great attention in Taiwan. The cost of the injection drug she needs for treatment is RMB 2.04 million on the island, but only RMB 130,000 on the mainland. What comment do you have on this? Please also introduce the situation regarding equal…","We are glad that this little Taiwanese girl received treatment services on the mainland at a relatively low price. The mainland has always attached great importance to reducing the medication burden on patients. In recent years, relying on the world's largest unified market by population, and leveraging our institutional, market, and management advantages, we have pooled the medication needs of 1.4 billion insured people for strategic procurement, and more and more “sky-high-priced drugs” have ultimately entered the national medical insurance catalog at “commoner prices,” benefiting a broad range of patients.\nThe nusinersen sodium injection that you mentioned this Taiwanese child used was a drug included in the national medical insurance negotiations in 2021. Through negotiation, the price of this drug dropped from a maximum of 700,000 yuan per injection at its initial launch to 33,000 yuan per injection, a reduction of 95.3%. The Taiwanese child used this drug for treatment on the mainland and enjoyed the price reduction together with mainland compatriots. If she enrolls in mainland medical insurance, she can enjoy an even lower price, only 11,000 yuan per injection. This year, another new SMA drug, risdiplam, also successfully entered the medical insurance catalog through negotiation. Its price dropped from a maximum of 63,800 yuan per bottle at its initial launch to 3,780 yuan per bottle, a reduction of 94.1%, and the burden on relevant patients will be further reduced.\nMedical insurance is a very important aspect of Taiwan residents being able to live and work in peace and contentment on the mainland. In November 2019, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security and the National Healthcare Security Administration jointly issued the Interim Measures on Participation of Residents of Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan in Social Insurance on the Mainland (Mainland China), which clearly stipulate that Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan residents who have stable employment relationships with employers on the mainland shall participate in basic employee medical insurance in accordance with the law, with employers and the individuals themselves paying contributions as prescribed and enjoying corresponding benefits. Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan residents who are not employed, who live on the mainland, and who have obtained Hong Kong, Macao, or Taiwan residence permits may participate in basic urban and rural resident medical insurance at their place of residence as prescribed, paying contributions at the same standard as urban and rural residents in their overall planning region and enjoying basic medical insurance benefits. Therefore, there are no policy obstacles for Taiwan residents who are employed and living on the mainland to participate in medical insurance; they may pay contributions as prescribed and enjoy corresponding benefits. As of the third quarter of 2022, the number of Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan residents insured on the mainland reached 310,000, of whom 127,000 participated in basic employee medical insurance and 183,000 participated in basic urban and rural resident medical insurance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视记者","Some public opinion holds that Tsai Ing-wen has said she is willing to engage in dialogue with the mainland and has 'allowed Chen Fu-hai and others to go to the mainland,' whereas after Lai Ching-te took over as chairman, the DPP accused Hung Hsiu-chu and Chen Yu-jen of going to the mainland as 'kowtowing to the Communists.' This is effectively contradicting Tsai Ing-wen, and Lai Ching-te's move is quite unusual.…","Everyone should have noticed that the DPP’s recent statements on cross-strait exchanges have been extremely vicious. This fully shows that the DPP authorities’ claim that they are “willing to dialogue with the mainland” is entirely false. Their actions run counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island, which seeks peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and they will surely be abandoned by the island’s residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","According to reports, on the 6th the Kinmen County Council established a “Cross-Party Governance Alliance” and an “Independent Alliance Political Group,” which jointly issued four major declarations, including advocating that Kinmen become a “permanent demilitarized zone.” They advocate peaceful development across the Strait and staying away from war, vigorously promote the early construction of the…","Pursuing peace and development, and seeking exchange and cooperation, is the shared voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and is in their common interest. The initiative jointly issued by relevant parties in Kinmen is a concrete embodiment of this public sentiment.\nWe have always attached great importance to and actively supported Kinmen's economic and social development, and we continuously take concrete measures to enhance the well-being of compatriots. We took the lead in realizing water supply to Kinmen in 2018, and preparatory technical work for electricity, gas and bridge connections with Kinmen has also been largely completed. We have heard the appeals of Kinmen fellow townspeople regarding Kinmen's construction and development and Xiamen–Kinmen cooperation, and we are willing to provide assistance wherever possible. We hope everyone will work together, pool strength and remove interference, so that the road of exchange and cooperation grows broader and the lives of compatriots on both sides grow better and better.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Members of the US House of Representatives “Select Committee on the CCP” recently threatened to travel to Taiwan to hold a hearing on arms sales to Taiwan. What is your comment?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. Congress to abide by the serious commitments the United States has made on the Taiwan question and to stop sending wrong signals to the DPP authorities and 'Taiwan independence' forces.\nMore and more Taiwan compatriots have clearly recognized that choosing 'Taiwan independence' means choosing war. The DPP authorities' attempt to 'seek independence by force' will only push Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Last August, Pelosi visited Taiwan, and the mainland took a series of countermeasures, including PLA exercises. Recently, reports have emerged that McCarthy, the new Speaker of the U.S. House of Representatives, plans to visit Taiwan this spring. Taiwan residents worry that if the visit takes place, it could trigger stronger countermeasures from the mainland and once again plunge the Taiwan Strait into a perilous…","We have repeatedly stated our firm opposition and solemn position. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.” The DPP authorities' “relying on the US to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Master Hsing Yun, founding patriarch of Fo Guang Shan and founder of the International Buddhist Progress Society, passed away on February 5. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the KMT, said that Master Hsing Yun hoped during his lifetime for peaceful development across the Taiwan Strait, that he has many followers and Buddhist friends on the mainland, and hoped the MAC could provide special assistance so they…","You will probably need to ask the relevant authorities in Taiwan about this question. People on both sides of the Strait hold Venerable Master Hsing Yun in high regard, remember his lofty virtue and exemplary demeanor, and will uphold his wishes and do what should be done.\nBloomberg News:\nAs the 2024 Taiwan leadership election gets underway, the mainland appears to be taking a moderate stance toward Taiwan. For example, Vice Chairman Xia Liyan of the Kuomintang visited, and the mainland resumed imports from more than 60 Taiwan food businesses. Why is the mainland doing this now? Does it mean that its Taiwan policy has changed?\nOur major policies toward Taiwan are consistent and clear, and they will not change because of the political situation on the island.\nWe adhere to Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era as our guide, fully implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, and fully implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. We uphold the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” and on the basis of the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we conduct extensive and in-depth consultations with far-sighted people from all walks of life in Taiwan on cross-Strait relations and national reunification, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nWe will continue working to benefit and bring well-being to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, promote exchanges and cooperation across industries and fields between the two sides, deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait relations, improve systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and encourage Taiwan compatriots, especially young people from Taiwan, to come to the mainland to pursue their dreams, build their dreams, and realize their dreams. We will promote the joint promotion of Chinese culture across the Strait, foster spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides, and help Taiwan compatriots participate in the process of national rejuvenation.\nWe firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, resolutely carry out major struggles against separatism and interference, and firmly safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nAt the start of the new year, everyone has seen our actions and sincerity in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together in harmony, walk the same path with one heart, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230208_12508972.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on February 11 that, due to obstruction by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, the mainland delegation to mourn Venerable Hsing Yun was unable to travel to Taiwan.\nVenerable Hsing Yun, founder of the Fo Guang Shan monastic lineage, passed away in Taiwan on February 5, and relevant mainland authorities attached great importance to this. At the invitation of Fo Guang Shan, the Taiwan Affairs Office, the State Administration for Religious Affairs, the Chinese Buddhist Association, and relevant parties in Jiangsu Province formed a mourning delegation, which had planned to travel to Taiwan from February 11 to 14 to pay respects. Over the past few days, the 38 members of the delegation, with the assistance of Fo Guang Shan, handled the formalities for travel to Taiwan in a uniform manner through the normal channels, and as planned, gathered at Capital Airport on the morning of the 11th to prepare for departure. Due to obstruction by the Taiwan side, the delegation was unable to go. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, disregarding basic humanitarian principles, brutally refused the mainland mourning delegation's travel to Taiwan, preventing Venerable Hsing Yun's funeral arrangements from being completed properly, seriously hurting the feelings of the broad base of Fo Guang Shan believers in Taiwan, and gaining no public support.\nRelevant mainland authorities will adjust the mourning itinerary and, on February 12, will travel to Dajue Temple in Yixing, Jiangsu, the ancestral home of Fo Guang Shan, to pay respects to Venerable Hsing Yun.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230211_12509637.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-12","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 12 — At a press briefing on the 12th, a spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council introduced in response to questions: At 3:00 p.m. on the 12th, the mainland condolence delegation paid respects to Venerable Master Hsing Yun at Dajue Temple in Yixing, Jiangsu, the ancestral temple of Fo Guang Shan. Long Mingbiao, leader of the condolence delegation and Deputy Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, along with officials from relevant bodies of the CPC Central United Front Work Department, Master Yanjue, President of the Buddhist Association of China, and representatives from all walks of life in Jiangsu Province, Hsing Yun's home province, attended the condolence ceremony.\nThe spokesperson said that during the ceremony, the condolence delegation held a video connection and dialogue with Fo Guang Shan's abbot, Venerable Xinbao, and others. Long Mingbiao said that the condolence delegation had originally planned to travel to Taiwan early yesterday morning to bid Venerable Master Hsing Yun a final farewell at Fo Guang Shan, but for reasons well known to all, the trip could not take place. Today, they came specially to Dajue Temple in Yixing to pay condolences, to express their remembrance of and reverence for Venerable Master Hsing Yun, and to honor his important contributions to the national rejuvenation and to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The mainland side extended condolences to the monastics of Fo Guang Shan. He sincerely hopes that everyone will carry on Venerable Master Hsing Yun's unfulfilled wishes, continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges, and devote their efforts to the reunification of the motherland, national rejuvenation, and the well-being of compatriots, so as to console Venerable Master Hsing Yun.\nVenerable Master Yanjue, on behalf of the Buddhist Association of China and the Buddhist community of mainland China, expressed endless grief and reverence for Elder Hsing Yun, and extended sincere condolences to the venerable masters and devout lay followers of Fo Guang Shan.\nVenerable Master Xinbao said that the mainland condolence delegation had originally planned to travel thousands of miles and overcome various difficulties to personally visit Fo Guang Shan in Taiwan to pay condolences. After many twists and turns, they were ultimately unable to travel to Taiwan, and decided instead to commemorate him at Dajue Temple, the ancestral temple of Fo Guang Shan. The disciples of Fo Guang Shan are endlessly grateful for this friendship. Our teacher had deep feelings for the nation and the people, upheld the great righteousness of the nation, and cherished the bonds of kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, which share the same language and culture. He devoted his life to promoting Chinese fine traditional culture and Humanistic Buddhism, and he always held deep affection for his hometown. The disciples of Fo Guang Shan will carry on our teacher's wishes and devote their wisdom and strength to promoting Buddhist exchanges across the Strait and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230212_12509803.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-02-13","Wang Wenbin","China News Service","Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Sen wrapped up his successful visit to China on February 11. How does China see this visit?","Prime Minister Hun Sen is an old friend familiar to the Chinese people and the first foreign leader received by China since the Spring Festival this year. His last visit to China was in early 2020 just after China was hit by COVID-19. Three years later, he visited China again on the occasion of the 65th anniversary of diplomatic ties and the “China-Cambodia Friendship Year”. Both sides attached high importance to this visit.\nOn February 10, President Xi Jinping had a warm meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Sen. They had a long, deep-going exchange, and drew a blueprint for the future course of China-Cambodia relations. Premier Li Keqiang and Chairman Li Zhanshu held talks and met with Prime Minister Hun Sen respectively. The two sides issued a productive joint statement, announced the launch of the “China-Cambodia Friendship Year”, held the China-Cambodia Economic Forum on Trade, Investment and Tourism, and signed 12 cooperation documents in the fields of foreign affairs, economic and trade cooperation, development cooperation, agricultural exports to China, infrastructure and so on.\nBoth sides agreed that no matter how the international situation changes, the two sides will unswervingly deepen their close ironclad friendship and jointly usher in a new era of building a high-quality, high-level and high-standard China-Cambodia Community with a Shared Future. The Chinese side reaffirmed resolute support for Cambodian people’s independent choice of development path that suits Cambodia’s national conditions, for Cambodia’s endeavors to safeguard her sovereignty and security, and for steady advancement of important Cambodian national political agenda and socioeconomic development while expressing firm opposition to any foreign interference in Cambodia’s internal affairs. The Cambodian side said that they hoped to convey a clear message that the Cambodian people have always stood firmly with the Chinese people. Cambodia opposes any attempt to interfere in China’s internal affairs or to block and contain China under the subterfuge of Taiwan and resolutely supports China’s every effort to achieve national reunification.\nThe two sides agreed to focus on the six areas including politics, production capacity, agriculture, energy, security and people-to-people exchange to build a “diamond hexagon” cooperation framework between China and Cambodia. The two sides agreed to uphold true multilateralism, jointly safeguard international fairness and justice, oppose hegemonism, power politics, and exclusive bloc politics which targets specific countries. The two countries call on relevant parties to carry forward the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea (DOC) fully and effectively, and reach an early conclusion on a substantive and effective Code of Conduct in the South China Sea (COC). Both sides stressed that any attempt to use the South China Sea issue to undermine regional peace and trust is counterproductive and should be avoided.\nIt is our belief that under the strategic guidance from the high level of both countries, the China-Cambodia relations will grow from strength to strength, and the ironclad friendship between the two countries will be even more unbreakable, bringing more benefits to the peoples of both countries and contributing more to the peace, stability and development in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347463.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230213_11024501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-02-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 13 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 13th that during this period, farmers and fishermen on the island have expressed their voices through the Kuomintang, relevant counties and cities, and groups, and are willing to improve product quality and ensure the safety of agricultural and fishery products exported to the mainland. They hope the mainland will resume imports as soon as possible. We are willing to work together with relevant parties on the island to help resume the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland.\nSince March 2021, quarantine pests, banned drugs and other contaminants have been detected in agricultural and fishery products imported from Taiwan. To safeguard agricultural production, ecological security and consumer health and safety, the mainland has suspended imports of relevant Taiwan agricultural and fishery products.\nZhu Fenglian said that the mainland has always placed great importance on the interests and welfare of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen. For many years, we have adhered to the concept of “two sides of the Strait are one family,” taking measures to ease the difficulties of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products with bumper harvests but unsold stock, and assisting in expanding the mainland market. Grassroots people in Taiwan have gained tangible benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230213_12510084.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 14 -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fengling, answering reporters' questions on the 14th, said that in the face of natural disasters, joining hands to save lives and looking out for one another is an embodiment of humanitarianism. But the DPP authorities, under the pretext of rescue, put on a show internationally, staging a series of \"rescue diplomacy\" political theatrics that have distorted the meaning of rescue and let people see clearly the essence of the DPP authorities' pursuit of \"independence.\"\nA reporter asked: Recently, the DPP authorities have made great use of the Turkey earthquake for hype, spreading false flags and false claims in the media, falsely asserting that a relevant United Nations body referred to Taiwan as a \"country,\" in order to opportunistically boost \"international presence.\" What comment do you have on this? Zhu Fengling gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230214_12510413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-02-17","Wang Wenbin","BBC","The UK’s former Prime Minister Liz Truss made a speech in Japan this afternoon, criticizing China’s human rights conditions and proposing closer cooperation between NATO and Pacific defense allies, as she called them. She called for the creation of an economic NATO in the region, and I suppose, use trade and things like that to counter China’s reach. Also, she said that regional countries should provide a package…","I haven’t gone through the speech you mentioned. But we are always opposed to the move to distort facts and smear China.\nWe would like to remind certain British politician a fact. According to a survey done by well-established international pollster , the approval rate of the Chinese government among the Chinese people is above 93 percent. This, I believe, is a clear rebuttal to the remarks you cited. We would also like to stress that China has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of world order. China’s development creates opportunities for the world and serves world peace, stability and common development. The notion that China threatens other countries’ security, and engages in economic coercion is utterly groundless. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. No country has the right to interfere under any pretext.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347467.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230217_11026614.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-17","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","There are reports that US Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense Michael Chase will visit Taiwan soon. Will China stage military drills near Taiwan if he goes there as it’s reported?","We are firmly opposed to official interaction and military contact between the US and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop all forms of official interaction and military contact with Taiwan, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347467.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230217_11026614.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-20","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","We noted the US observation that it was important that the US side and the Chinese side had the opportunity to meet during the Munich Security Conference. Could you offer more information on that?","At the request of the US side, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi had an informal contact with US Secretary of State Antony Blinken on the margins of the Munich Security Conference.\nWang Yi set forth China’s strong position on the so-called “balloon incident” and pointed out that what the US side has done was apparently an abuse of force and violation of customary international practice and the International Civil Aviation Covenant. China deplores it and strongly protests it. The US itself is the number one country in conducting surveillance worldwide, whose high-altitude balloons have illegally flown over China multiple times. The US is in no position to smear China. The US needs to demonstrate sincerity, and acknowledge and resolve the damage its abuse of force has done to China-US relations. If the US side continues to fuss over, dramatize and escalate the unintended and isolated incident, it should not expect the Chinese side to flinch. The US side should be prepared to bear all consequences arising from an escalation.\nWang Yi stressed that on the Ukraine issue, China stands by principles. China is committed to promoting peace talks and has played a constructive role. The China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination is built on the basis of non-alliance, non-confrontation and non-targeting of third countries, which is within the sovereign right of any two independent states. We do not accept the US’s finger-pointing or even coercion targeting China-Russia relations. The US, as a major country, has every reason to work for a political settlement of the crisis instead of fanning the flames or profiting from it.\nWang Yi pointed out that to preserve stability across the Taiwan Strait, one must firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” and uphold the one-China principle. On the Taiwan question, the US side should respect historical facts, honor its political commitments and follow through on its statement of “not supporting Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347468.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230220_11027645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-20","Wang Wenbin","CNR","We noted that on February 18 local time, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi attended the Munich Security Conference. Could you share any details?","On February 18, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi delivered a keynote speech titled “Making the World a Safer Place” at the Munich Security Conference in Germany.\nDirector Wang noted that humanity’s three-year fight against COVID tells us a simple truth: as President Xi Jinping repeatedly stressed, we are members of one global village, and we belong to one community with a shared future. Human society must not repeat the old path of antagonism, division and confrontation, and must not fall into the trap of zero-sum game, war and conflict.\nDirector Wang said that making the world a safer place is the strong desire of all people, the common responsibility of all countries, and more importantly, the right direction for the advance of our times. For a safer world, the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all countries must be respected. All countries should abide by the principle of sovereignty in both words and deeds, rather than apply it selectively, still less with double standards. For a safer world, disputes should be peacefully resolved through dialogue and consultation. However complex the issue is, dialogue and consultation should not be abandoned. However intense the dispute is, a political resolution should be pursued. However difficult the situation is, peace should be given a chance. For a safer world, the purposes and principles of the UN Charter should be upheld. It’s important for all to put the larger interest embodied in the purposes and principles of the UN Charter above one’s own lesser interest, and work together to oppose the Cold War mentality and bloc confrontation. For a safer world, the key role of development must be fully harnessed. We must firmly reject the attempts to politicize, weaponize and draw ideological lines in the cooperation on trade, science and technology. If security is to be firmly established and last, people in all countries should get to lead a better life.\nDirector Wang stressed that making the world a safer place is China’s abiding commitment. For China, keeping to peaceful development is a strategic choice informed by a deep grasp of the past, present and future. China will stay the course, and come together with more countries in the pursuit of peaceful development. Any increase in China’s strength is an increase in the hope for world peace. When all countries pursue peaceful development, the future of humanity will be full of promise.\nDirector Wang took questions about the Ukraine issue, China-US relations and the Taiwan question. He announced that China will put forth its proposition on the political settlement of the Ukraine crisis, and stay firm on the side of peace and dialogue. Director Wang also said that China will soon be launching a Global Security Initiative Concept Paper, to lay out a more systemic approach and more practical measures to address global security challenges, and we welcome the active participation of all countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347468.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230220_11027645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-20","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Reuters has reported that US Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense Michael Chase has arrived in Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","We are firmly opposed to official interaction and military contact between the US and the Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop all forms of official interaction and military contact with Taiwan, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347468.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230220_11027645.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-21","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Taiwan president Tsai Ing-wen noted that Taiwan will work more actively with the US in face of the so-called expansion of autocracy. What is your comment?","Let me point out once again the mistake of referring to the leader of the Taiwan region as “president” even though we have done it many times from this podium. Taiwan is part of China and there is no so-called “Taiwan president”. The person you mentioned is just a regional leader of China.\nLet me stress that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. China is strongly opposed to the US’s military ties with and arms sales to Taiwan. The “Taiwan independence” provocations of the DPP authorities will not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China or cause international support to falter over the one-China principle, and still less change the irreversible trend toward China’s reunification. Any separatist attempt or act of soliciting foreign support to undermine cross-Strait relations will only backfire and will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347469.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230221_11028718.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-22","Wang Wenbin","China News Service","There has been a lot of media coverage on China’s Global Security Initiative Concept Paper released by the foreign ministry. Foreign Minister Qin Gang said that the concept paper demonstrates China’s sense of responsibility for safeguarding world peace and firm resolve to defend global security. Could you share more on that?","Yesterday China held the Lanting Forum on the Global Security Initiative: China’s Proposal for Solving Security Challenges. Foreign Minister Qin Gang attended the opening session and delivered a keynote speech.\nForeign Minister Qin said that China’s Global Security Initiative Concept Paper expounds on the core ideas and principles of the Global Security Initiative (GSI), identifies the priorities, platforms and mechanisms of cooperation, and demonstrates China’s sense of responsibility for safeguarding world peace and firm resolve to defend global security. Security is a right for all countries. It is not a prerogative of some, still less should it be decided by any individual country. The GSI intends to serve the interests of all and protect tranquility for all. Its advances need the unity and cooperation of the international community.\nForeign Minister Qin noted that the GSI is rooted in the fine traditional Chinese culture that values peace above everything else, and is inspired by China’s independent foreign policy of peace and its practices. China is committed to the path of peaceful development. No matter how much it develops, China will never seek hegemony, expansion or sphere of influence, or engage in arms race, but remain a defender of world peace.\nForeign Minister Qin stressed that China is committed to following a Chinese approach to resolving hotspot issues. China believes in promoting peace through talks, emphasizes addressing both the symptoms and root causes, calls on the involved parties to meet each other halfway, and pursues fairness and justice. On the Iranian nuclear issue, China has actively promoted the resumption of the Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action (JCPOA), to uphold the legitimate rights and interests of relevant countries and the international nuclear non-proliferation regime. On the Korean Peninsula issue, China stands for pursuing in parallel the establishment of a peace mechanism and the denuclearization of the Peninsula, and addressing the legitimate concerns of all parties in a balanced manner, to safeguard peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula. On the Middle East, China welcomes and supports security dialogues among regional countries including Saudi Arabia and Iran, as well as regional efforts to build a Middle East security architecture that suits the realities of the region and accommodates the interests of all parties. On the Ukraine issue, China has taken an objective and impartial stance based on the merits of the issue, and has played a responsible and constructive role in easing the situation and deescalating the crisis. China will continue to promote peace talks, contribute its ideas for a political settlement of the crisis, and join the international community to promote dialogue and consultation, address the concerns of all parties and seek common security. In the meantime, we urge certain countries to immediately stop fueling the fire, stop shifting blame to China, and stop touting “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow”.\nForeign Minister Qin noted that the development of China cannot happen without a secure international environment. Likewise, world security would not be possible without the security of China. At present, external suppression and containment against China keep escalating, posing a serious threat to China’s sovereignty and security. We stand firmly against any form of hegemonism and power politics, against the Cold War mentality and bloc confrontation, and against any foreign interference in China’s internal affairs. We will resolutely safeguard China’s sovereignty, security and development interests, and international fairness and justice.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347470.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230222_11029632.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 22, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's TAO press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The mainland recently proposed giving priority to restoring 16 cross-Strait direct flight routes, but the relevant Taiwan authorities have not responded for a long time. What comment do you have on this? Please introduce the situation regarding promoting the restoration of cross-Strait direct flight routes.","We strongly support cross-Strait aviation enterprises in substantially increasing cross-Strait routes and flights, with airlines independently and dynamically optimizing flight arrangements. From February 13 to 19, a total of 214 passenger flights were operated on cross-Strait routes, a significant increase from fewer than 100 per week before January 8. However, compared with the maximum of 890 scheduled cross-Strait flights per week before 2020, current capacity cannot meet the needs of people on both sides. In particular, under the unilateral restrictions of the DPP authorities, the mainland currently has only four cross-Strait direct flight points: Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, and Chengdu. Overall, travel between the two sides remains quite inconvenient.\nAt present, the epidemic on the mainland is well under control, and compatriots on both sides and aviation enterprises are eagerly looking forward to the full resumption of cross-Strait direct flight points. On February 1, the mainland's aviation authorities, through the channels agreed upon by the two associations, urged the Taiwan side to give priority to resuming 16 cross-Strait direct flight points, including Guangzhou. No positive reply has been received to date. We hope the DPP authorities will take the well-being of compatriots on both sides as the guiding principle, remove artificial restrictions as soon as possible, and restore normal cross-Strait direct air passenger services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512543.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","February 28 of this year marks the 5th anniversary of the release and implementation of the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation.” What is the implementation status of the series of policy measures the mainland has introduced to give Taiwan compatriots equal treatment?","Since 2018, the Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, and other relevant departments, has successively issued the \"31 Measures\" and \"26 Measures\" to promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, the \"11 Measures\" to support Taiwan-invested enterprises during the epidemic, and the \"22 Agriculture and Forestry Measures\" to support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises in developing agriculture and forestry on the mainland, along with a series of other policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots. Over the past five years, localities and departments have continued to implement these measures thoroughly and in detail. Taiwan compatriots find it increasingly convenient to study, work, and live on the mainland, and the fields and scope in which they enjoy equal treatment continue to expand.\nFirst, in supporting the development of Taiwan-invested enterprises, the mainland actively supports Taiwan-invested enterprises in equally participating in intelligent manufacturing and green manufacturing project evaluations. Several Taiwan-invested enterprises, including Changchun Chemical, Lite-On Technology, Nan Ya Plastics, and Shuttle Electronics, were included in the 2022 green manufacturing list. Several Taiwan-invested enterprises, including Foxconn Industrial Internet, AUO Corporation, and Minghua Automotive Parts, were selected for the 2022 list of excellent intelligent manufacturing scenarios. Eight Taiwan-funded enterprises and projects, including Coretronic, won the 7th China Industrial Award, the Commendation Award, and the Nomination Award. Localities actively support Taiwan-invested enterprises in applying for high-tech enterprise status and equally enjoy preferential tax policies. Guangdong and Jiangsu provinces currently have a combined total of more than 1,400 Taiwan-invested high-tech enterprises. In 2022, Taiwan-invested enterprises investing more than 10 million US dollars in Guangdong enjoyed reductions and exemptions including value-added tax留抵 refunds totaling more than 4.7 billion yuan. In Jiangsu, 121 Taiwan-invested enterprises were recognized as provincial \"specialized, refined, distinctive, and innovative\" enterprises, 10 Taiwan-invested enterprises received special funds for transformation and upgrading support, 26 Taiwan-invested enterprises were recognized as provincial enterprise technology centers, and 848 Taiwan-invested enterprises were entered into the provincial list of science and technology-based small and medium-sized enterprises.\nSecond, in the field of agriculture and forestry, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises have achieved new progress in participating in the mainland's rural revitalization strategy. Sanming, Fujian, was approved to establish the Cross-Strait Rural Integration Development Pilot Zone, and the Zhangping Taiwan Innovation Park in Fujian was selected for the 2022 list of national modern agricultural industrial park construction. Chen Zhijian, a Taiwan businessman starting a business in Zhangping City, Fujian, successfully obtained the real estate certificate for forest-based economy covering 1,438 mu and received the first forest-based economy industry loan of 150,000 yuan. The certificate clarifies the property rights protection of land contract and management rights, effectively safeguarding the land contract rights and interests of operators. Sichuan Mianning Yuansheng Agricultural Technology Co., Ltd. was recognized by the National Forestry and Grassland Administration as one of the fifth batch of national key leading forestry enterprises. Xie Dongqing, chairman of Fujian Zhangping Taipin Tea Industry Co., Ltd. and chairman of the Minyuan Highland Tea Production and Marketing Professional Cooperative, was named one of the \"Three Rural Figures of 2022,\" becoming the first Taiwan compatriot to receive this honor in the 18 years since the activity began.\nThird, in finance, the mainland supports qualified Taiwan-invested enterprises in listing on the A-share market and provides Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople with more diverse and efficient financial services. In 2022, 10 Taiwan-invested enterprises listed on the A-share market, a record high for any year, and the cumulative total of Taiwan-invested enterprises listed on the A-share market now stands at 59. In March 2019, Fujian began a pilot program of \"Taiwan Business and Compatriot Financial Credit Certificates\" in Pingtan. It has now achieved full coverage across the province, providing certificate holders with efficient and convenient financial services such as higher credit limits, lower loan interest rates, and simplified procedures. As of January this year, certificates had been issued to 373 Taiwan compatriots and 233 Taiwan-invested enterprises, providing cumulative credit of 13.969 billion yuan. Zhejiang, together with local financial institutions, issued Taiwan-exclusive \"Tairong\" credit cards to Taiwan compatriots, with a total of 3,353 cards issued by the end of 2022 and a total credit amount of 55.62 million yuan. In 2022, Jiangsu Credit Guarantee provided financing credit enhancement of more than 3 billion yuan cumulatively to more than 30 Taiwan-invested enterprises.\nFourth, in key regions, support and empowerment for economic parks related to Taiwan affairs has been increased. The Taiwan Affairs Office, the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, and the Ministry of Commerce have approved the establishment of six cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones in Guangxi, Sichuan, Hubei, Jiangxi, Hunan, and Chongqing, and a cross-Strait industrial cooperation zone for new and old growth drivers transition in Shandong, as well as cross-Strait integrated circuit industrial cooperation pilot zones in Xiamen and Quanzhou, Fujian, and Hefei, Anhui. These measures help attract Taiwan-invested enterprises to cluster and develop, and help enterprises in need move to the central and western regions, integrate into the new development pattern, participate in high-quality development, and gain more business opportunities in expanding the domestic market.\nFifth, regarding Taiwan compatriots' participation in honorary awards and professional qualification examinations, Taiwan compatriots have gained a greater sense of participation, achievement, and integration. So far, 331 Taiwan compatriots (families and groups) have received honorary titles at prefecture-level or higher, such as the May Day Labor Medal, the Youth May Fourth Medal, the March 8th Red Banner Bearer, and the Five-Good Family, in 22 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the central government, and 6 Taiwan compatriots have been named National March 8th Red Banner Bearers. According to incomplete statistics, tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots have registered for various professional qualification examinations, among whom 578 passed the National Legal Professional Qualification Examination, more than 3,000 passed the medical practitioner qualification examination, and 156 passed the primary and secondary school teacher qualification examination.\nSixth, in the cultural field, Taiwan compatriots have actively joined various cultural groups on the mainland, applied for cultural awards, and participated in the project for inheriting and developing excellent traditional Chinese culture. The China Federation of Literary and Art Circles and its affiliated national associations of writers and artists have so far admitted 82 members from Taiwan. Seven Taiwan compatriots residing in Fujian have been named representative inheritors of intangible cultural heritage of Fujian Province. Taiwan artists have competed for important awards such as the China Quyi Peony Award, the China Photography Golden Statue Award, and the China Film Golden Rooster Award. Taiwan performing artists participate in producing mainland radio, film, television programs, and TV series, with nearly a thousand person-times each year. At overseas Chinese Cultural Centers in multiple locations, including Malta, Paris, Madrid, Sydney, Cairo, and Yangon, cultural and creative institutions and artists from both sides have held various cultural and art exhibitions to jointly carry forward excellent traditional Chinese culture.\nGoing forward, we will thoroughly implement the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, uphold the concept of \"One Family Across the Strait,\" continuously introduce and improve policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, and continuously deepen integrated development in all areas across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512540.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently said it will coordinate with relevant departments to resolve the issue of some Taiwan agricultural and fishery products being imported into the mainland, while the MAC said that trade and economic measures should not be used as a tool for “united front” work on Taiwan agriculture. What comment do you have?","For some time, farmers and fishermen on the island have expressed through various channels their willingness to take effective measures to improve product quality and ensure the safety of agricultural and fishery products exported to the mainland. Recently, during the visit to the mainland by a delegation led by Xia Liyan, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, and a delegation led by Huang Yi-cheng, Chairman of the Taiwan Cross-Strait Agricultural and Fishery Exchange and Development Investment Association, they both conveyed to us the strong desire of farmers and fishermen on the island for the resumption of imports of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland. Peace and development, and exchange and cooperation, are the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Supporting Taiwan's farmers and fishermen in sharing the development opportunities on the mainland is in the common interest of compatriots on both sides. We attach great importance to the appeals of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen to resume imports of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, and on the premise that inspection and quarantine standards are met, we will coordinate with relevant departments to actively resolve this issue.\nMore and more Taiwan compatriots have come to deeply recognize that restoring and expanding cross-Strait exchanges as soon as possible, and conducting face-to-face communication and dialogue, is conducive to enhancing their own interests and well-being. The DPP authorities have been delaying and passing the buck on restoring cross-Strait exchanges; they have neither the intention nor the ability to resolve issues that concern the vital interests of farmers and fishermen on the island. In pursuit of political self-interest, they have persistently engaged in political manipulation, smeared and slandered the mainland, and disregarded the interests of farmers and fishermen on the island, and are therefore destined to lose popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512544.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","In recent years, the Mainland has taken multiple measures to promote continuous progress in protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","We practice the development philosophy centered on the people, and we deeply empathize with the difficulties and problems faced by the broad Taiwan compatriots. We direct local Taiwan Affairs Offices to strengthen policy promotion, provide proactive service and guidance, focus on resolving the urgent difficulties and concerns of Taiwan compatriots, and earnestly safeguard the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. In 2022, Taiwan Affairs Offices at all levels across the country accepted a total of 4,060 cross-Strait dispute cases, concluded 3,951 of them, with a case closure rate of 97.3%, achieving good results.\nWe have adopted innovative measures to continuously improve institutional arrangements and policy measures that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. For example, at the end of 2021, we officially launched the “whole-to-whole” litigation-mediation linkage mechanism for cross-Strait disputes. Relying on the “People's Court Mediation Platform,” this mechanism provides high-quality, one-stop, end-to-end online dispute resolution services for compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots, including diversified mediation, judicial confirmation, and case registration. In 2022, through this mechanism, 1,628 cases were referred to pre-litigation mediation, 977 cases were concluded, and the mediation success rate was 68.2%, which fully demonstrates that the innovation of the platform mechanism has played an important role in protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nWe do our letters-and-visits work in accordance with the principles of understanding public sentiment, pooling public wisdom, safeguarding public interests, and uniting public sentiment. In 2022, the Letters and Visits Office of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council received 774 letters from compatriots on both sides of the Strait, of which 20% (more than 160) were letters from Taiwan compatriots. Many Taiwan compatriots on the island, in their letters, actively expressed opinions and suggestions on expanding cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepening the integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe will continue to uphold the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, open channels for Taiwan compatriots to express their demands, improve long-term mechanisms for resolving cross-Strait disputes, advance the application of the litigation-mediation linkage platform, promote the enhancement and protection of the well-being of Taiwan compatriots at the level of the rule of law, raise Taiwan compatriots' sense of gain, security, and happiness, and advance the high-quality development of work protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. If you have any opinions or suggestions regarding Taiwan affairs work, you are welcome to write to the Letters and Visits Office of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512535.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","At the February 8 press conference, the Taiwan Affairs Office introduced that 91 cross-Strait exchange bases have been approved in 24 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, including Shandong, Hubei and Fujian. We found that 20 of these exchange bases involve folk beliefs, accounting for 21.98%. What is the consideration behind this?","As is well known, Chinese traditional culture has deep roots in Taiwan, and numerous folk beliefs and customs remain abundant and active to this day, widely present in the daily lives of Taiwan compatriots. These folk beliefs all originated on the mainland. Most were brought to Taiwan as large numbers of people from Fujian and Guangdong crossed the sea to reclaim land and settle during the Ming and Qing dynasties, and over the course of several centuries they have consistently maintained devout reverence for the ancestral temples of their home regions.\nSince cross-Strait exchanges were opened in 1987, more than 100 million visits by Taiwan residents to the mainland for tourism, visits, and exchanges have taken place. Some folk beliefs' ancestral temples and important shrines on the mainland have become must-visit sites for large numbers of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland, serving as important venues and bonds that sustain the national identity, cultural identity, and emotional connections of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have approved the establishment of a group of cross-Strait exchange bases themed on folk beliefs, such as the Mazu Ancestral Temple in Meizhou Island, Putian, Fujian, which embodies Mazu culture, the Tianhou Temple in Tianjin, and the Guandi Temple in Xiezhou, Yuncheng, Shanxi and the Guandi Temple in Dongshan, Zhangzhou, Fujian, which embody Guandi culture. The purpose of establishing these exchange bases is to support and encourage these places to strengthen their development and play their roles, create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to visit and engage in cross-Strait exchanges, and promote spiritual connection among compatriots. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange at these exchange bases.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512536.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","What is your evaluation of the visit to the mainland by KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan and his delegation? What are your considerations for the next steps in exchanges between the KMT and the CPC?","Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Liyan led a delegation on a visit from February 8 to 17, successively visiting Beijing, Nanjing, Shanghai, Wuhan, Chongqing, Chengdu and other places, where they took part in relevant meetings, talks, exchange activities and visits. This was an important event in exchanges between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party this year, and a concrete practice of promoting the resumption and expansion of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation after epidemic prevention and control entered a new stage.\nWang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, and Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, respectively met with Vice Chairman Xia Liyan and his delegation. Both sides reaffirmed adherence to the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence,” the common political foundation for mutual trust and exchanges between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party. They held dialogue and exchanged views on the current situation in the Taiwan Strait and related issues concerning the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and achieved positive results.\nWe are willing, on the basis of the existing common political foundation, to strengthen high-level exchanges with the Kuomintang, consolidate and enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, respond to the wishes of compatriots on both sides, and deepen exchanges and cooperation at all levels and in all fields, including youth. Together we will promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and join hands in striving for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512545.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The report to the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China emphasized “promoting both sides of the Taiwan Strait to jointly carry forward Chinese culture and promote spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides.” Over the more than six years since the DPP authorities took office, they have carried out “de-Sinicization,” repeatedly staging farcical acts of “de-Sinicization,” such as the…","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots, the same origins, the same culture, and the same ethnicity. The long-standing Chinese culture is the spiritual root and sense of belonging of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and a precious common treasure and spiritual bond for them. General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed in an important speech at the commemorative meeting marking the 40th anniversary of the \"Letter to Compatriots in Taiwan\" that compatriots on both sides should jointly inherit the excellent traditional Chinese culture and promote its creative transformation and innovative development. The report of the 20th Party Congress emphasized promoting joint efforts by both sides to carry forward Chinese culture and fostering spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides. Over the years, despite the twists and turns in cross-Strait relations, compatriots on both sides have kept up uninterrupted people-to-people exchanges and cultural interaction. The mainland has actively built cross-Strait cultural exchange platforms in diverse forms and is committed to promoting compatriots on both sides working together to carry forward Chinese culture. These efforts have had broad and positive impact across the Strait and have played an important role in enhancing national identity and spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides and in deepening cross-Strait integrated development.\nFirst, the mainland supports cultural figures on both sides who take carrying forward Chinese culture as their mission in jointly holding various exchange activities to promote mutual exchange and learning. They carry out extensive and in-depth cooperation in literature, art, film and television, publishing, and cultural and creative industries, including ideological dialogue, academic research, joint creation, exhibitions and performances, and trading and venture investment, to jointly inherit the excellent traditional Chinese culture and to create high-quality cross-Strait exchange projects and industrial cooperation platforms. Brands such as \"Bonds with China——Cross-Strait Cultural and Tourism Friendship Tour,\" \"Cross-Strait Chinese Character Culture and Art Festival,\" \"Strait Film and Television Season,\" \"Cross-Strait Book Fair,\" and \"Cross-Strait Cultural Heritage and Creative Expo\" have been held continuously for many years, promoting industry players on both sides to discuss together the inheritance and innovation of Chinese culture and to jointly carry forward Chinese culture and the national spirit.\nSecond, the mainland encourages compatriots on both sides to conduct grassroots people-to-people exchanges and to strengthen the historical ties and emotional bonds across the Strait. Residents on both sides actively take part in exchanges on themes of Chinese culture such as traditional festivals, folk beliefs, and local distinctive cultures. The \"Joyful Spring Festival\" series of performances, the cross-Strait Lantern Festival and Mid-Autumn Festival lantern fairs, the Haipai Culture and Art Festival, and the Yue Fei Culture Summer Camp have been popular with residents on the island. The Qingming Ceremony for Sacrificing to the Yellow Emperor, the Grand Ceremony for Sacrificing to Fuxi, the ancestor of Chinese humanity, the Guan Gong Culture Tourism Festival, and the Mazu Culture Tourism Festival have attracted many Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to seek their roots and pay respects to their ancestors, carrying forward the root culture of the Chinese nation.\nThird, the mainland promotes joint protection and inheritance of excellent Chinese cultural heritage by compatriots on both sides, highlighting the kinship of common roots and blood ties across the Strait. It cooperates in holding intangible cultural heritage exhibitions and performances such as the \"Guarding Our Spiritual Home——Cross-Strait Intangible Cultural Heritage Month,\" supports Taiwan artists in participating in the protection and inheritance of intangible cultural heritage, and has named Taiwan artists as representative inheritors of intangible cultural heritage in Fujian Province. The \"Cross-Strait Cultural Heritage Protection Forum\" has been held continuously, and cultural relics and museum institutions on both sides actively carry out academic exchanges and professional cooperation, hold cultural relics exhibitions in Taiwan, and continuously deepen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in cultural relics.\nFourth, with the help of important platforms such as overseas Chinese Cultural Centers, the mainland supports cultural institutions and young artists on both sides in jointly telling China's stories well. For example, the \"Chinese Twelve Zodiac Cultural and Creative Exhibition\" was planned, designed, produced, and implemented jointly by artists from both sides of the Taiwan Strait. It was exhibited at overseas Chinese Cultural Centers during the Spring Festival and was well received by local residents. In 2022, the \"Cross-Strait Young Creative Design Exhibition,\" themed \"Culture Empowers Rural Revitalization,\" was launched. Through 200 outstanding works selected from nearly 10,000 students and young designers on both sides, it presented to the international community the contemporary Chinese story of how cross-Strait creative design empowers rural revitalization.\nFifth, the mainland implements measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots in the cultural field, encourages Taiwan compatriots to share in the prosperity of culture created together, and deepens cross-Strait integrated development. It actively implements the \"31 Measures\" and the \"26 Measures,\" encourages Taiwan compatriots to take part in the project for inheriting and developing excellent traditional Chinese culture, and to join various cultural groups and apply for cultural awards. The China Federation of Literary and Art Circles and its affiliated national associations of writers and artists have so far admitted 82 members from Taiwan. Taiwan artists have competed for important awards such as the China Quyi Peony Award, the China Photography Golden Statue Award, and the China Film Golden Rooster Award. An increasing number of Taiwan compatriots are taking part in the development of the mainland's cultural undertakings, and outstanding cultural and arts workers on both sides are working together, becoming promoters and contributors to inheriting and carrying forward Chinese culture.\nGoing forward, we will continue to respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and strengthen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation through various means, including jointly protecting cultural heritage, jointly promoting cultural and artistic creation, strengthening public cultural services, carrying out cultural industry cooperation, and jointly promoting Chinese culture to the world, to continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development and enhance spiritual affinity among compatriots. We hope more Taiwan compatriots will share the opportunities of the mainland's cultural development, resolutely oppose \"de-Sinicization\" and other \"Taiwan independence\" schemes, jointly promote the creative transformation and innovative development of excellent traditional Chinese culture, and together usher in a new era of glory for Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512538.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Since February 20, the DPP authorities have opened individual travel to Taiwan for residents of Hong Kong and Macau, but they still restrict mainland tourists from visiting Taiwan. The MAC said this is because the mainland’s “epidemic situation is not transparent,” and group and individual travel have not been opened. What comment do you have?","The mainland's epidemic prevention and control work has entered a new stage, and economic and social life, including tourism, is rapidly and fully returning to normal. This is a fact that is plain for all to see. Taiwan compatriots can come to the mainland with peace of mind to visit relatives and friends, make visits, exchange, study, and work. The DPP authorities still ban mainland residents from visiting or traveling to Taiwan for exchange and tourism, and the so-called mainland 'lack of epidemic transparency' is merely a pretext they fabricated. The DPP authorities' restriction and blockade of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions go against the wishes of compatriots on both sides and are unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512537.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","As the mainland's delegation to mourn Master Hsing Yun was unable to travel to Taiwan, the DPP authorities said it was because the mainland side “did not follow the previously established mechanism for application,” and claimed that the mainland was “deliberately conducting political manipulation” by using this matter. What is your comment?","The reason the mainland delegation commemorating Master Hsing Yun cannot travel to Taiwan is solely that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities disregarded humanitarian considerations and brutally blocked it. We have already introduced the relevant situation to the outside world through a press release issued on February 11.\nThe mainland delegation preparing to travel to Taiwan this time has a simple purpose, which is solely to pay respects to Master Hsing Yun. To this end, the 38-member condolence delegation, with the assistance of Fo Guang Shan, handled the entry formalities for Taiwan through normal channels, submitting the personnel list, itinerary, and relevant application forms. However, Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council (MAC) raised unnecessary complications, groundlessly proposing a so-called request that “the TAO first contact the MAC through the existing liaison mechanism,” deliberately creating obstacles. As everyone knows, because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not recognize the “1992 Consensus,” the TAO and the MAC have had no contact or exchanges in recent years, and the mainland condolence delegation’s trip to Taiwan does not involve any personnel exchanges between the TAO and the MAC at all. The MAC’s raising of the above request clearly has its political intentions and calculations. Its ulterior motive is obvious to all. The answer to who is “deliberately engaging in political manipulation” is very clear.\nIt must be pointed out that on February 11, just as the mainland condolence delegation was preparing to depart for Taiwan, Taiwan’s “Liberty Times” published a large-scale report that morning on the delegation being refused entry, and even publicly disclosed in detail the names and unit information of the 12 mainland public officials in the delegation. If not for the behind-the-scenes operations of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, how could this pan-green mouthpiece media have obtained such information? Such malicious manipulation is a typical case of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities “deliberately engaging in political manipulation.” The MAC later further argued that it did not know that the mainland side was traveling to Taiwan this time under the name of a “condolence delegation,” and did not know that the condolence delegation planned to “enter and leave as a group.” Such lies are not worth refuting.\nWe also need to point out that in order to find an excuse for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ brutal refusal of the mainland condolence delegation’s entry into Taiwan, the “Liberty Times” did not hesitate to fabricate rumors and frame others. A member of the condolence delegation from Master Hsing Yun’s hometown, the Vice Mayor of Yangzhou City, openly and truthfully reported her current position in her application for travel to Taiwan. The “Liberty Times” actually publicly fabricated rumors, accusing her of “fabricating her identity” and of applying under the name of a “Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office official.” Recently, some media have used authentic documents and materials to corroborate and expose this false report by the “Liberty Times,” pointing out that its fabrication and slander were “an attempt to cover up the lie with yet another lie for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.” Taken together with the situation described above, the duet performed by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and this “Taiwan independence” media outlet is nothing other than a thoroughgoing “deliberate political manipulation,” which fully exposes the true face of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ determination to brutally block the mainland condolence delegation from entering Taiwan.\nWe advise the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the “Taiwan independence” media on the island to stop doing these self-deceiving, guilty-conscience things and stop doing things that run counter to popular sentiment. Any tricks of “deliberate political manipulation” will eventually be exposed and are destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230222_12512541.htm"],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Li Dawei, newly appointed chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan, recently said that establishing the exchange mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation and ARATS is not easy, and he hopes the two sides can gradually begin mutual visits and that the SEF can travel to the mainland early. What comment do you have?","The establishment of the consultation and contact mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation (ARATS) and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) has indeed been difficult, and it should be all the more cherished. The mechanism has been interrupted and stalled for more than six years, and the reasons are well known. Our position is clear and consistent. As long as the SEF is authorized to confirm to ARATS that it upholds the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle as the common political foundation, the consultation and contact mechanism between the two associations can be restored.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The DPP authorities recently announced a ban and restrictions on the sale of mainland-produced snacks such as luosifen. After the ban was issued, some netizens on the island found that more and more stalls in Taiwan's night markets had begun selling luosifen, sour and spicy noodles and other mainland snacks and foods, and business is booming. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","Clearly, many tastes are the same for people on both sides of the Strait. I think mainland friends can recommend more mainland delicacies to Taiwan friends, and we also welcome Taiwan friends to come to the mainland to taste the specialty foods of various regions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","After visiting the mainland recently, Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Li-yen and his delegation said they felt a 'warm spring' in cross-Strait relations, but also noted that whether 'flowers will bloom' depends on joint efforts by both sides. Spokesperson, if we want the 'flowers to bloom,' what conditions does the mainland believe the two sides still need to create?","We are willing, on the basis of the One-China Principle and the “1992 Consensus,” to conduct exchanges and dialogue with far-sighted people from all sectors of Taiwan, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOur position is very clear: as long as the DPP authorities abandon their “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and return to the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait consultations and negotiations can resume. As long as the DPP authorities take the well-being of compatriots on both sides as the guiding principle and promptly cancel the various artificial restrictions that hinder cross-Strait personnel exchanges and travel, compatriots on both sides will be able to visit each other often and exchange more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, and Song Tao, Director of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, both emphasized recently when meeting Taiwan guests that civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait must be fully restored after the pandemic. What specific measures and arrangements does the…","Previously, due to the COVID-19 pandemic and the deliberate obstruction by the DPP authorities, cross-Strait exchanges were seriously hindered. Now that the epidemic situation on both sides of the Taiwan Strait has eased, the obstacles and interference to cross-Strait exchanges should be removed as soon as possible.\nAt the beginning of the new year, we sent New Year greeting letters to major Taiwan industry and commerce groups, inviting them to visit the mainland for visits and business negotiations, and received enthusiastic responses from all the groups. These industry and commerce groups have already planned to organize delegations to visit and exchange on the mainland. They have fully expressed the common voice of the Taiwan business community, which hopes that compatriots on both sides will strengthen exchanges and cooperation and looks forward to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and they reflect the deep concern of all sectors on the island over the current complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe welcome them to organize delegations to visit, and we will do our utmost to provide convenience for cross-Strait exchanges. We will make good reception arrangements, help arrange for the relevant visiting delegations to communicate and exchange with the relevant departments and localities, and actively assist their member enterprises in finding business opportunities on the mainland, negotiating cooperation, and investing in development. We also welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to see for themselves, and we hope that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots will work together with us to strive for the early realization of normalized cross-Strait exchanges and routine interaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Li Xiaodong, Deputy Director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office, led a delegation invited to visit Taiwan to attend the 'Taiwan Lantern Festival' and municipal exchanges. As the first official mainland exchange delegation to visit Taiwan since the pandemic, the trip has drawn attention on the island. However, the Mainland Affairs Council has imposed many restrictions on the itinerary of the visiting…","From February 18 to 20, Li Xiaodong, Deputy Director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office, led a delegation to Taiwan at the invitation of the Taipei City Government. They visited the relevant exhibition areas of the \"2023 Taiwan Lantern Festival in Taipei,\" held municipal exchanges with the Taipei City Government, and visited the Taipei Pop Music Center, the Taipei Performing Arts Center and others, promoting cross-Strait city exchanges and cooperation through concrete actions.\nPeace, development, exchanges and cooperation are what mainstream public opinion on the island wants, and they are an irresistible trend. We hope that relevant parties in Taiwan will heed public opinion, promptly lift the various unreasonable restrictions on personnel exchanges and interactions across the Strait, and restore normalcy to cross-Strait travel and normalize exchanges at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Reportedly, following the resumption of the Fuzhou–Langqi route in January on the Kinmen–Matsu “mini three links,” the Baisha–Huangqi route on the Matsu side was also officially resumed on February 19. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Huangqi (Lianjiang, Fuzhou) to Baisha (Matsu) “mini three links” passenger route opened on December 23, 2015. The route is 4.8 nautical miles long, and the sailing time is only 25 minutes. It has greatly facilitated exchanges between residents of Fuzhou and Matsu and has also contributed to the integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan. In February 2020, due to the epidemic, the Huangqi–Baisha route was forced to suspend service.\nOn February 19, the Huangqi–Baisha route resumed service, and 75 Matsu compatriots took the boat to travel back and forth between the two places that day. At present, the route operates two round-trip sailings per week, with cross-Strait passenger vessels operating in rotation, and each passenger ship carries 90 to 140 passengers. With this, the “mini three links” passenger routes of Xiamen–Kinmen, Quanzhou–Kinmen and Fuzhou–Matsu have all resumed service, but the number of round-trip sailings remains quite small, and compatriots outside Kinmen and Matsu are still excluded. We hope the DPP authorities will remove all artificial restrictions as soon as possible and fully restore the “mini three links” and normal exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Four U.S. congressmen recently wrote to Biden urging an increase in so-called “military financial assistance” to Taiwan in future budgets. U.S. Marine Corps Commandant Berger said they are considering expanding the use of attack suicide drones in the “Indo-Pacific” region, hinting that in a “Taiwan contingency” they would deploy this weapon to attack PLA naval vessels. What comment do you have on this?","“The tree wants stillness, but the wind will not stop.” The remarks of US politicians fully show that American anti-China forces, out of their own interests, are indulging and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatists in reckless provocations and stirring up tensions in the Taiwan Strait. Their aim is to use the Taiwan question to contain China’s development and progress, harm the interests of the Chinese nation, and obstruct the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. This also fully proves that the DPP authorities, who are attempting to “rely on the United States to seek independence,” will only bring disaster to Taiwan and calamity to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","The first question: On February 21, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, met with Singaporean Foreign Minister Vivian Balakrishnan in Beijing and rarely mentioned cross-strait relations. Some commentators believe this seems to indicate that the mainland hopes Singapore can play a “bridge” role between the two sides. What is your response?\nThe second…","The first question: If you have long followed the work of the Taiwan Affairs Office, you know that this situation is not uncommon. There is only one China in the world. Adhering to the one-China principle is a recognized basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. Explaining clearly to the international community the historical background and legal facts of the Taiwan question, and explaining the work and efforts we have made to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of national reunification, is one of the tasks of the Taiwan Affairs Office. The international community broadly understands and supports the just cause of the Chinese people in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and striving to complete national reunification. We appreciate this.\nThe second question: Restoring cross-Strait exchanges and normal personnel exchanges is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides and a need for the development of cross-Strait relations. We follow the will of the people, uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and actively promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait. We promote the joint promotion of Chinese culture by compatriots on both sides and foster heart-to-heart connection between them. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together, visit each other more often and stay in closer contact, enhance understanding and build consensus, so that more people on both sides of the Strait can share the dividends of peaceful development and exchange and cooperation.\nThe third question: The historical background and legal facts of the Taiwan question are clear. Taiwan is part of China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This fact has never changed and cannot change. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's national sovereignty and territory have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided. This is the legal and practical basis of cross-Strait relations.\nThe facts of the past six-plus years fully prove that the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities are the disruptors of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Since the DPP came to power, in pursuit of political self-interest, it has disregarded facts, reversed right and wrong, refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and spread and hyped fallacies such as the so-called “mutual non-subordination between the two sides” and other “two-state theory” fallacies. This has created the current tension across the Taiwan Strait and harmed the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Its conduct runs counter to the historical trend and the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides, and it is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan said that “One China, Each with Its Own Interpretation” is the basic spirit of the “1992 Consensus.” What is your comment?","In 1992, the Straits Exchange Foundation on the mainland and the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan reached a consensus that each would express orally that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle,” which is the “1992 Consensus.” Its core meaning is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national reunification.\nOver the years, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang have advanced the development of party-to-party relations, promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and achieved fruitful results. We are willing to work with the Kuomintang on this common political foundation to consolidate and enhance mutual trust, strengthen exchanges and communication, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","First question: US Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for China Affairs Chase visited Taiwan on the 17th. What is your comment? Second question: The Ministry of Commerce recently announced that Lockheed Martin and Raytheon Missiles & Defense, which take part in arms sales to Taiwan, have been placed on the Unreliable Entity List. What is your comment?","First question: There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military collusion between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the One-China Principle and stop the practice of “using Taiwan to contain China.” The DPP authorities’ collusion with external forces to seek “independence” will not succeed.\nRegarding the second question, the relevant departments have already stated their position. Punishing foreign entities that participate in arms sales to Taiwan in accordance with the law is reasonable, justified, and lawful. Any entity that undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","Recently, egg prices on the island have risen again, and many restaurant operators have said they will temporarily stop serving egg-related dishes, and adding an egg now requires an extra NT$15 to 20. However, Taiwan's agricultural authorities said, 'Each egg has only risen by NT$0.2, which is cheaper than in many places,' sparking dissatisfaction among the island's residents. What is your comment on this?","Adding NT$15 to 20 per egg may seem like nothing in the eyes of DPP officials, but for ordinary Taiwan residents it affects their daily livelihood and every meal of the day. We advise the DPP authorities to truly act from the well-being of the Taiwan people, keep the safety and welfare of the people always in mind, and promptly respond to people's livelihood concerns and demands.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","According to statistics from the National Film Administration, the box office for the 2023 Spring Festival film season was RMB 6.758 billion, with 129 million admissions, indicating a recovery of the mainland's film and television market. High-quality film and television works such as “The Wandering Earth 2” and “Furious” have simultaneously sparked binge-watching crazes on both sides of the Strait. Popular…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, roots and origins. Compatriots on both sides not only share a consistent taste in food, but also share common tastes in outstanding film and television works. Cross-Strait exchanges in film and television are an important channel for increasing mutual understanding among the peoples on both sides and jointly promoting outstanding traditional Chinese culture. Each year, more than a thousand person-times of Taiwan performing artists participate in mainland radio, television and audiovisual programs and film and television productions, and many outstanding mainland films and TV dramas are deeply loved by the Taiwan public, especially young people.\nWe actively support cross-Strait cultural exchanges. The “31 measures” and the “26 measures” include multiple measures involving the cultural field, providing greater space and better conditions for relevant Taiwan practitioners to develop on the mainland. In the performance market, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism recently issued an announcement that, starting February 16, local cultural and tourism administrative departments will resume accepting and approving commercial performances involving Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan. From February 6 to 10, the 11th Cross-Strait Television Arts Festival was successfully held in Fuzhou. During the event, the “Dream New Voice · 14th Cross-Strait TV Host Newcomers Contest” was held, with 54 contestants from both sides of the Strait competing on the same stage and showcasing their individual talents. Two of the three contestants who won “Best Newcomer” were from Taiwan, and as soon as the competition ended they received hosting invitations from the Fujian Radio and Film & Television Group.\nWe hope that cultural practitioners on both sides of the Strait will seize opportunities, share in the opportunities arising from the development of the mainland's cultural industry, further deepen cross-Strait cultural exchanges and cooperation, and jointly promote the prosperity and development of cultural undertakings.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202302/t20230222_12512525.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-02-23","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Director of the U.S. Central Intelligence Agency recently said that China has ordered the PLA to be ready to attack Taiwan by 2027. Meanwhile, the U.S. Assistant Secretary of Defense for Indo-Pacific Affairs stated at a congressional hearing that he is confident mainland China will not carry out a major “violation” against Taiwan before 2030. The U.S. Air Force Chief of Staff said he does not believe a…","We have noted that the US side frequently makes such self-contradictory remarks. I want to emphasize that Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and resolving the Taiwan question is China's own internal affair, to be decided by the Chinese people, and brooks no foreign interference. No matter what the US side says, it cannot change the course of China's reunification, and it cannot shake our determination and resolve to defend national unity and territorial integrity.\n“Of all people, none are like brothers.” Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort. However, if the Democratic Progressive Party authorities remain obstinate, colluding with external forces to continuously provoke “independence” and unilaterally escalate confrontation between the two sides, and even go so far as to put Taiwan compatriots in danger, the Chinese People's Liberation Army will let its actions speak, take necessary measures to resolutely thwart any “Taiwan independence” separatist act and external interference, and firmly safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16203972.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-02-24","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","US Radio Talkshow Host Garland Nixon tweeted last week that President Biden warned about a US “plan for the destruction of Taiwan”. Do you have any comment on that?","I’m also curious what the US “plan for the destruction of Taiwan” looks like. The US needs to offer a clear explanation.\nTaiwan is part of China. We will firmly defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347472.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230224_11031214.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-24","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Today marks the first anniversary of the outbreak of the Ukraine crisis. What’s your comment? Could you give us more details on China’s position on the Ukraine issue?","The Ukraine crisis happened in Europe, but its impact has spilled over the wider world. President Xi Jinping outlined the four principles, called for joint efforts in four areas and shared three observations on Ukraine. He noted perceptively that conflicts and wars produce no winner; there is no simple solution to a complex issue; and confrontation between major countries must be avoided. This points the right way forward for the deescalation of tensions and political settlement of the crisis. The Chinese side released China’s Position on the Political Settlement of the Ukraine Crisis today, which expounds on China’s basic position in a comprehensive and systematic manner.\nThis biggest crisis on Eurasia since WWII has taught us many lessons as follows:\nClinging to the Cold War mentality leads to antagonism and confrontation. The end of the Cold War more than three decades ago doesn’t mean the end to the zero-sum thinking and the Cold War mentality. The Berlin Wall was torn down, yet the fence of ideology and prejudices based on values still stand. If such Cold War mentality lingers on and goes unchecked, confrontation and crisis will be what the future holds in store for us all.\nStoking bloc confrontation leads to conflict and war. As a product of the Cold War, NATO continues to exist despite the end of the Cold War, and even constantly seeks to reach beyond its traditional defense zone and scope and stoke tensions and create troubles in the Asia-Pacific. NATO needs to reflect on itself. We have seen what NATO has done to Europe, and it must not seek to sow chaos here in the Asia-Pacific or elsewhere in the world.\nApplying double-standard will backfire. The US stresses the need to respect Ukraine’s sovereignty, yet it is exactly the US that has wantonly violated other countries’ sovereignty, grandstanded on the Taiwan question and blatantly interfered in China’s internal affairs. Such double standard has been rejected and opposed by most members of the international community.\nChina will stay firm on the side of peace, dialogue and the right side of history. We will stay committed to promoting peace talks, and work with the rest of the international community to play a constructive role in and make our own contribution to the political settlement of the Ukraine crisis.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347472.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230224_11031214.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-02-25","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲24日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 24 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters’ questions on the 24th, said: The “1992 Consensus” and “One Country, Two Systems” are two clearly distinct concepts. Some DPP politicians have repeatedly put the wrong labels on things, confusing the issue, attempting to deceive public opinion on the island and mislead the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, in order to…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” is the consensus reached in 1992 by the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits and the Straits Exchange Foundation under authorization, each stating orally that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the common political foundation for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nShe said that “one country, two systems” is an institutional arrangement after national reunification. The proposal of “one country, two systems” came much earlier than the “1992 Consensus.” Its specific form of realization in Taiwan will fully take into account the actual situation in Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230225_12513283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-02-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 25 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions on the 25th, saying: In January 2023, Taiwan residents Hong Zhengjun and Kong Xiangzhi were apprehended by public security authorities for illegally entering the mainland. To combat crime, safeguard the lives and property of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and maintain order in cross-Strait exchanges, the public security authorities handled Hong Zhengjun and Kong Xiangzhi appropriately in accordance with the law.\nA reporter asked: It is reported that the suspects in the Xuejia 88 shooting case in Tainan, Taiwan, Hong Zhengjun and Kong Xiangzhi, have been repatriated to Taiwan. Please confirm this. Zhu Fenglian responded as above.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202302/t20230225_12513322.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-02-27","Mao Ning","China News Service","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said China has been providing nonlethal assistance to Russia through its companies, and is now considering a provision of lethal aid. US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan warned that there would be “real costs” for China if the country went forward with providing lethal aid to Russia. Do you have any comment?","On the Ukraine issue, China has been actively promoting peace talks and the political settlement of the crisis. The US is in no position to point fingers at China-Russia relations. We do not accept coercion or pressure from the US.\nIn addition to pouring lethal weapons into the battlefield in Ukraine, the US has been selling sophisticated weapons to the Taiwan region in violation of the three China-US joint communiqués. What exactly is the US up to? The world deserves to know the answer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347473.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230227_11032123.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-27","Mao Ning","Dragon TV","It was reported that ROK Foreign Minister Park Jin mentioned Taiwan in an interview with CNN. Park said that peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is essential for peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula, and it’s indispensable for security and prosperity of the region as a whole, and that the ROK is opposed to unilateral change of status quo by force. So in that sense, the ROK will make sure that if…","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, we do not need to be told what should or should not be done. If the ROK needs to maintain peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula, it needs to respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, follow the one-China principle and be prudent on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347473.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230227_11032123.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-28","Mao Ning","The Paper","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said a few days ago that “one of the reasons that the world is so concerned about a crisis across the Taiwan Strait is because this is not an internal matter, as China would have it, based on its sovereignty. It’s a matter of concern to quite literally the entire world” and that “if there were a crisis in Taiwan as a result of China’s aggression in some fashion, that would…","Secretary Blinken’s remarks are absolutely irresponsible and absurd. China firmly opposes that. It seems that some history lessons are in order for the top US diplomat on the Taiwan question. Taiwan has been an inalienable part of China since ancient times. The one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and the important political prerequisite and foundation for China’s diplomatic relations with countries in the world.\nIn 1972, the US stated in the Shanghai Communiqué that “The United States acknowledges that all Chinese on either side of the Taiwan Strait maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan is a part of China. The United States Government does not challenge that position.”\nIn 1978, the US stated in the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the United States of America and the People’s Republic of China that “The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the United States of America acknowledges the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China.”\nIn 1982, the US stated in the August 17 Communiqué that “the United States of America recognized the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China, and it acknowledged the Chinese position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China. The United States Government...reiterates that it has no intention of infringing on Chinese sovereignty and territorial integrity, or interfering in China’s internal affairs, or pursuing a policy of ‘two Chinas’ or ‘one China, one Taiwan’.”\nThe US made those political commitments to China on the Taiwan question, which are written down in black and white.\nFor some time, the US has been deliberately ignoring and twisting the history and sending the wrong message on the Taiwan question. The US has significantly relaxed its restraint on official interactions and reinforced military contact with Taiwan and touted “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow”. It has even been revealed by the media that the US government has a plan for “the destruction of Taiwan”. We cannot help but ask, what exactly is the US trying to achieve?\nI need to stress again that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. It is at the very core of China’s core interests. It is the political foundation of China-US relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in this relationship. China will never allow any external force to interfere in our internal affairs. We have a clear message for the US: It is time to stop - stop walking on the edge, stop using the salami tactics, stop pushing the envelope, and stop sowing confusion and trying to mislead the world on Taiwan. If the US refuses to change course and goes down that wrong path, there will be real consequences and it will come at real costs to the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347474.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230228_11032791.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-02-28","Mao Ning","KBS","You said yesterday, “If the ROK needs to maintain peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula, it needs to respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, follow the one-China principle and be prudent on the Taiwan question.” Would you care to elaborate on that?","The one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and the premise on which China establishes and develops diplomatic relations with other countries. When it comes to the Taiwan question, the importance of respecting the one-China principle and China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity cannot be overemphasized.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347474.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202302/t20230228_11032791.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-02","Mao Ning","CCTV","US Secretary of State Blinken said on March 1 that if China was genuinely serious about the very first principle of sovereignty in the position paper it put out on the Ukraine issue, it would have been spending all of the last year working in support of the restoration of Ukraine’s full sovereignty. He said that China has been doing the opposite in terms of its own efforts to advance Russian propaganda, and now…","On the Ukraine issue, China’s position has all along been objective and fair. We are committed to promoting talks for peace and working for the political settlement of the crisis. We always stand on the side of peace and dialogue.\nThe US has been pouring lethal weapons into the battlefield in Ukraine, fanning up the flames and spreading disinformation. We are firmly against that.\nThe US keeps saying that territorial sovereignty must be respected, but on the Taiwan question, the US has been walking on the edge and pushing the envelope. The US has broken its own political commitments and been selling sophisticated weapons to China’s Taiwan region. The US says there’s desire for peace to prevail, yet it has waged wars and stoked confrontation around the world. The US says it’s important to respect and uphold the international order, yet it has slapped massive unilateral illegal sanctions and put its domestic laws above the international law. The US says competition must be fair, yet it has been cracking down on foreign companies by using all kinds of state apparatus and defying international trade rules.\nThe US needs to reflect on itself, stop sowing confusion, stop trying to mislead the world and stop making presumptions about others based on the US’s own behavior. The US needs to step up to its responsibility, help deescalate tensions and promote dialogue and stop pointing fingers and discrediting other countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347476.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230302_11034198.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-02","Mao Ning","AFP","The US State Department on Wednesday approved the sale of new weapons to Taiwan. And meanwhile, the Taiwan authorities announced that there has been another large-scale round of flights by the mainland military aircraft near the island. So how does Beijing intend to respond to rising tensions in the region?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. Such sales undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China firmly opposes this.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan and stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will continue to take resolute and strong measures to firmly safeguard its sovereignty and security interests.\nI need to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The DPP authorities’ separatist activities for “Taiwan independence” and the US’s calculus to use Taiwan to contain China are the root cause of the tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347476.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230302_11034198.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-02","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 2 — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to reporters' questions on the 2nd, saying: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China. The US arms sales seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué.” They are an indulgence and support of “Taiwan independence” forces and a sabotage of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nA reporter asked: According to media reports, relevant US government departments recently decided to sell the Taiwan region of China arms worth approximately US$619 million. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks in response.\nMa Xiaoguang said: We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop US-Taiwan military ties, to stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question, and to handle the Taiwan question prudently.\nHe said: We warn the DPP authorities that attempting to “resist reunification by force” and “rely on the US to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230302_12514636.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-03-03","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the U.S. State Department approved a new round of arms sales to Taiwan on March 1, including airborne missiles and related equipment for F-16 fighter jets, with a total value of US$619 million. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose US arms sales to China's Taiwan region. The US side's conduct crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests, and seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China is strongly dissatisfied with this and has lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nWe demand that the US side stop arms sales to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military ties, stop interfering in the Taiwan question, and stop aggravating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains at the ready and will at any time strike back at any provocation seeking “independence” and any interference by external forces, resolutely defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16205700.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-03-06","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan “defence minister” warned that the island has to be on alert for a “sudden entry” by the Chinese military into areas close to it amid the rising military tensions across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any response?","I need to first make clear that Taiwan is part of China and there is no such thing as a “defence minister” for Taiwan. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are China’s territory. China will firmly defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347478.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230306_11036323.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-08","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","Recent reports say that the leader of Taiwan Tsai Ing-wen will make a transit stop in the US in April, during which she will meet with US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy in California. Reports say that by persuading McCarthy to meet in California instead of Taiwan, Tsai Ing-wen is trying to avoid angering the Chinese mainland. What is your comment?","We are gravely concerned over this and have made serious démarches to the US side demanding clarification.\nAs Foreign Minister Qin Gang made clear at yesterday’s press conference held on the margins of the “two sessions”, Taiwan is part of the sacred territory of the People’s Republic of China. It is the inviolable duty of all Chinese people, including our compatriots in Taiwan, to accomplish the great task of reunifying the motherland. The Taiwan question is the core of the core interests of China, the bedrock of the political foundation of China-US relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. Separatism for Taiwan independence is as incompatible with peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait as fire with water. For peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, its real threat is the separatist forces for Taiwan independence, its solid anchor is the one-China principle, and its genuine guardrails are the three China-US joint communiqués.\nI need to stress that China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, firmly opposes any visit by “Taiwan independence” separatist leaders to the US in any name under whatever pretext, and firmly opposes the US having any form of contact with “Taiwan independence” separatist elements in violation of the one-China principle.\nWe urge the US to abide by the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle. No individual shall ever underestimate the firm resolve, staunch will and strong capability of the Chinese government and people to defend sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347479.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230308_11037694.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-09","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 9 dispatch: On the 9th, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said: We have noted that after the mainland side proposed on February 1 that priority be given to resuming direct flights at 16 cross-Strait points, including Guangzhou, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council announced on March 9 its “Plan for Resuming Cross-Strait Air Passenger Direct Flight Points,” which meets the needs for comprehensively resuming cross-Strait direct air passenger flights.\nA reporter asked: The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council and other relevant departments said on the 9th that some cross-Strait direct flight points would be resumed starting on the 10th. What is your comment? Ma Xiaoguang made the above remarks.\nMa Xiaoguang said: Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Resuming direct flights at cross-Strait points is conducive to personnel exchanges across the Strait and promotes exchanges and interaction. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion and promptly advance the full normalization of cross-Strait direct air and sea routes and the “mini three links,” to enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230309_12516887.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-03-10","Mao Ning","Reuters","The outgoing President David Panuelo of the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM) claims that he met with Taiwanese officials in February and asked for $50 million in exchange for the country recognizing Taiwan and that Taiwan agreed. Do you have any comment?","I have seen relevant reports. I would like to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and the political premise and foundation on which China establishes diplomatic relations with other countries including the FSM. China firmly opposes countries that have diplomatic ties with China engaging in any form of official interaction with the Taiwan region in violation of the one-China principle. On the basis of the one-China principle and in the spirit of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit, China stands ready to work with the FSM to enhance friendship and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347481.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230310_11039036.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-10","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","The Director of National Intelligence Avril Haines told the US House Intelligence Committee that the US intelligence community doesn’t think that China wants a military conflict over Taiwan. How does the foreign ministry respond to this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese and must be decided by Chinese ourselves. No one shall ever underestimate the firm resolve, staunch will and strong capability of the Chinese government and people to defend sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347481.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230310_11039036.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-15","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, March 15 (Xinhua) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang said on the 15th that the mainland has implemented “Class B management” for the novel coronavirus infection and canceled all measures targeting the novel coronavirus at import cold-chain food ports, including nucleic acid testing. To promote the healthy development of cross-Strait trade, the General Administration of Customs decided to resume imports of chilled white hairtail and frozen chub mackerel from the Taiwan region starting March 15.\nIn June 2022, mainland customs detected positive novel coronavirus nucleic acid samples in chilled white hairtail and frozen chub mackerel exported from the Taiwan region to the mainland. Based on considerations of biosecurity risk prevention, the General Administration of Customs suspended imports of chilled white hairtail and frozen chub mackerel from the Taiwan region starting August 3, 2022.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230315_12518533.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-03-16","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan’s “foreign ministry” warned Honduras that it should not be lured by China’s “poisonous” financial aid even though it faces a huge amount of debt. What’s your comment? A spokesperson for TikTok told Reuters that the Biden administration asked Byte Dance to sell its stakes, or face ban from the US. What’s your response?","To start, let me say that Taiwan has no foreign ministry, but a foreign affairs department. The one-China principle is the political foundation and prerequisite for the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and other countries. In recent years, Panama, El Salvador, the Dominican Republic and Nicaragua have established or resumed diplomatic relations with China. The practical cooperation between China and these countries have made rapid progress, which has effectively promoted the socioeconomic development of relevant countries and delivered tangible benefits to the people. China is ready to grow friendly cooperative relations with all countries including Honduras on the basis of the one-China principle. We believe that this will create more opportunities for socioeconomic development and efforts to improve people’s wellbeing in Honduras.\nAs to the remarks made by the DPP authorities, let me say that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The DPP authorities’ obsession with “Taiwan independence” and separatist agenda will lead nowhere.\nOn your second question, we have noted relevant reports. China always believes that data security should not be used as a tool to abuse the national security concept and state power to hobble foreign companies.\nThe US has yet to prove with evidence that TikTok threatens its national security. It should stop spreading disinformation about data security, stop suppressing relevant companies, and provide an open, fair, just and non-discriminatory environment for foreign businesses to invest and operate in the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347484.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230316_11043152.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-16","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Honduran foreign minister said that the country wants to sever diplomatic ties with Taiwan because Taiwan is reluctant to provide more financial aid to his country. What kind of aid policy will China take economically with regard to Honduras?","You may find the answer in my response to Reuters. We are ready to grow friendly cooperative relations with all countries including Honduras on the basis of the one-China principle. We believe this will create more opportunities for economic development and people’s well-being in Honduras.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347484.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230316_11043152.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-03-16","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that in recent period, U.S. congressmembers and Department of Defense officials have successively visited Taiwan to provoke, and the U.S. has approved a new round of arms sales to Taiwan, increased military training cooperation with Taiwan, and aggravated tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The head of Taiwan's defense department said that, given cross-strait tensions, Taiwan should be vigilant against…","Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people. At present, the situation across the Taiwan Strait remains tense, and its root cause is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities collude with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke, deliberately standing on the opposite side of the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same blood and are closely bound together. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form. In response to external interference and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, the People's Liberation Army carrying out relevant military operations is justified and entirely reasonable.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, it is the core of China's core interests, and it is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. China firmly opposes any form of official exchanges and military collusion between the US and Taiwan, and firmly opposes the US upgrading substantive US-Taiwan relations in any form. We urge the US to abandon its scheme of “using Taiwan to contain China” and stop “salami-slicing” and seeking breakthroughs on the Taiwan question.\nOpposing “independence” and promoting reunification, Taiwan should return to the motherland. Against any separatist act of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and any interference or provocation by external forces, the Chinese People's Liberation Army stands ready and will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16210239.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-03-20","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Ma Yingjiu, former leader of the Taiwan region, plans to visit central China from March 27 to April 7. His trip is mostly about student exchanges and tomb sweeping, but he is also open to meeting the leaders of the mainland. Would senior officials be open to meeting Ma?","I have noted that the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has made a statement. You may refer to that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347486.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230320_11044922.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Ma Ying-jeou will lead a delegation to the mainland on March 27 to pay respects to ancestors and engage in exchanges. Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the morning of the 20th that the mainland welcomes Mr. Ma Ying-jeou to come to the mainland to pay respects to ancestors and visit, and to bring Taiwan's young students for exchanges.","Ma Xiaoguang said, “Honoring ancestors and remembering the distant past is a Chinese tradition, and worshipping ancestors at Qingming Festival is a common custom of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Strengthening exchanges and interactions among young people across the Strait can add new strength and youthful vitality to the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. We are willing to provide necessary assistance for Mr. Ma Ying-jeou’s visit, and we wish him a smooth trip.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230320_12519505.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-03-21","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen will transit through New York and Los Angeles as part of a trip to Guatemala and Belize from March 29 to April 7. Sources say she may meet with US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy. How do you comment about this?","We strongly oppose any form of official interaction between the US and Taiwan, strongly oppose any US visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities regardless of the rationale or pretext, and strongly oppose all forms of US contact with the Taiwan authorities, which violates the one-China principle. China has made strong démarches to the US side on this matter. The reported trip is not so much a “transit”, but an attempt to seek breakthroughs and propagate “Taiwan independence”.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly deliver on its leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle. Our message to the Taiwan authorities is clear: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; any attempt to seek independence and make provocations together with external forces will fail. China will resolutely safeguard the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347487.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230321_11045971.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-21","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The German education minister is visiting Taiwan today and tomorrow. That’s the first trip to Taiwan at this level for German delegation in 26 years. Do you have any comment on this?","China firmly opposes the egregious act of the German official and has made serious démarches to the German side in Beijing and Berlin to express strong disapproval. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is the core of the core interests of China. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations, a prevailing consensus among the international community, and the political foundation of China-Germany relations.\nWe call on the German side to abide by the one-China principle, immediately stop interacting with and sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop using the Taiwan question as a pretext to interfere in China’s internal affairs. We will do what is necessary to resolutely defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347487.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230321_11045971.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-21","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","According to reports, Honduran Foreign Minister Enrique Reina said after meeting with US officials on March 20 local time that the US side said that it’s the sovereign decision of Honduras to establish diplomatic ties with China and they respect that. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. Every sovereign state has the right to independently choose to develop diplomatic relations with another sovereign country. We will welcome it if Honduras recognizes the trend of the world and makes the right decision that is consistent with where the trend is leading.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347487.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230321_11045971.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-22","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","President Xi Jinping’s state visit to Russia has drawn global attention. Could you offer some latest information?","On March 21, President Xi Jinping held small-group and large-group talks and jointly met the press with Russian President Vladimir Putin and met with Russian Prime Minister Mikhail Mishustin in Moscow. The two heads of state reached new, important common understandings in many fields. The two sides agreed to follow the principles of good-neighborliness, friendship and win-win cooperation in advancing exchanges and cooperation in various fields and deepening the comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for the new era.\nPresident Xi pointed out that China and Russia are each other’s biggest neighbor and consolidating and developing long-term good-neighborly relations with Russia is consistent with historical logic and a strategic choice of China. It will not be changed by any turn of events. China-Russia cooperation enjoys significant potential and space and is strategic, reliable and stable. No matter how the international landscape may change, China will stay committed to advancing China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for the new era. This state visit to Russia is a journey of friendship, cooperation and peace. China is ready to work with Russia to build on past achievements, enrich the comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for the new era, bring more benefits to the two peoples and make greater contribution to human progress.\nPresident Putin said that Russia-China relations are developing very well. Good progress has been made in all fields of bilateral cooperation. Russia firmly supports China in upholding its legitimate interests on questions related to Taiwan, Hong Kong and Xinjiang. Russia congratulates China on helping to successfully bring about historic outcomes from the talks between Saudi Arabia and Iran in Beijing. Russia appreciates China for consistently upholding an objective and impartial position on international affairs, supports the Global Security Initiative, the Global Development Initiative, and the Global Civilization Initiative China has put forward and stands ready to further enhance international coordination with China.\nPresident Xi and President Putin believe the exchange between the two sides during the visit is in-depth, rich and comprehensive and has injected new impetus into the development of China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination for the new era. The China-Russia relationship has gone far beyond the bilateral scope and acquired critical importance for the global landscape and the future of humanity. Under the new historical circumstances, the two sides will view and handle China-Russia relations with a broad vision and a long-term perspective, in a bid to make greater contribution to human progress.\nThe two heads of state agreed that the two sides need to strengthen overall design and top-level planning, boost trade in energy, resources, and electromechanical products, enhance the resilience of their industrial and supply chains, expand cooperation in such areas as information technology, the digital economy, agriculture and trade in services, promote greater complementarity and joint development of traditional trade and emerging areas of cooperation, and further facilitate cross-border logistics and transportation. The two sides should continue to cement the cornerstone of people-to-people exchanges. To be specific, efforts should be made to encourage more interactions between sister provinces/states and between sister cities, ensure the success of the Years of Sports Exchange, and facilitate the personnel movement between the two countries.\nThe two heads of state noted that as permanent members of the UN Security Council, China and Russia will continue to work with the international community to firmly uphold the basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. China and Russia will work more closely within multilateral frameworks including the Shanghai Cooperation Organization, BRICS and the G20, practice true multilateralism, and promote post-COVID economic recovery. The two sides will boost the constructive force for building a multi-polar world and improving the global governance system, contribute more to maintaining global food and energy security and keeping industrial and supply chains stable, and work together for a community with a shared future for mankind.\nThey agreed to stay in close touch through various means to jointly guide the sound and steady growth of China-Russia relations.\nAfter the talks, President Xi and President Putin jointly signed a Joint Statement of the People’s Republic of China and the Russian Federation on Deepening the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership of Coordination for the New Era and a Joint Statement of the President of the People’s Republic of China and the President of the Russian Federation on Pre-2030 Development Plan on Priorities in China-Russia Economic Cooperation , charting the course for future growth of bilateral relations and cooperation across the board.\nDuring the visit, the two sides also signed bilateral cooperation documents in such areas as agriculture, forestry, basic scientific and technological research, market regulation, and the media.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347488.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230322_11047173.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-22","Wang Wenbin","Macau Monthly","Former US National Security Advisor Robert O’Brien was awarded by Tsai Ing-wen in Taiwan on March 21. Tsai said he made contributions to Taiwan-US relations. What’s your comment?","If I remember correctly, this former White House senior official recently argued that the US should destroy Taiwan’s semiconductor factories including the TSMC rather than letting them fall into China's hands. Honoring such an individual shows that the DPP authorities do not mean it when they say they love Taiwan. The truth is they have been selling Taiwan away.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347488.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230322_11047173.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-23","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","On Honduras again. Separately, according to a person with knowledge of the situation, one day before the Honduran President announced on Twitter that she would seek to establish diplomatic ties with China, she privately asked Taiwan for $2.5 billion in aid. This person said that Taiwan suspects China was secretly behind Honduras’s request. What’s China’s response?","The remarks are preposterous and groundless. Honduran Foreign Minister Enrique Reina said in a recent interview that President Castro made the decision to grow relations with China in response to the trend of the world and in light of the realities of Honduras. The one-China principle represents the prevailing trend of the world and has the overwhelming support of the international community. China welcomes the Honduran government’s positive statements on growing relations with China, and stands ready to establish and grow bilateral relations with Honduras on the basis of equality and mutual respect.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347489.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230323_11048051.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-23","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwanese officials have said that a potential meeting between Taiwanese president Tsai Ing-wen and House Speaker Kevin McCarthy is still being arranged. What’s China’s response?","I need to correct you first. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and there is no such thing as “Taiwanese president”. As for your question, we have stated China’s position before. We would like to reiterate that we strongly oppose any form of official interaction between the US and Taiwan, strongly oppose any US visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities regardless of the rationale or pretext, and strongly oppose all forms of US contact with the Taiwan authorities, which violates the one-China principle. China has made strong démarches to the US side on this matter. The reported trip is not so much a “transit”, but an attempt to seek breakthroughs and propagate “Taiwan independence”. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly deliver on its leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347489.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230323_11048051.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-23","Wang Wenbin","NBC","Following up on that. Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen is in the US on the way to Latin America, while former Taiwan leader Ma Yingjiu is coming to China at the same time. Do you have any comment on this coincidence? What’s the significance?","I do not see any association between the two things you mentioned. We have stated our positions separately on these two matters. You may take another look at our answers if you are interested.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347489.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230323_11048051.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-23","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Separately, Blinken said China will have the ability to invade Taiwan by 2027. What is China’s response?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, a matter that must be resolved by the Chinese. We will continue to strive for peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort, but we will never pledge to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all measures necessary. This is directed solely at interference by outside forces, the few separatists seeking “Taiwan independence” and their separatist activities. The real root cause of the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities have been soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence” and some people in the US have been using Taiwan to contain China. If the US truly hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop meddling in the Taiwan question and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347489.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230323_11048051.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-24","Mao Ning","Reuters","Honduras is reportedly set to announce formal ties with China and end relations with Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","My colleague gave our answer to your question yesterday. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. China welcomes the positive statement by the Honduran government on developing relations with China, and stands ready to establish and grow bilateral relations on the basis of equality and mutual respect.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347490.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230324_11048747.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-27","Mao Ning","Reuters","China has established diplomatic relations with Honduras. So Honduras previously asked Taiwan for $2.5 billion in financial aid. Will China give Honduras this amount that it previously requested from Taiwan?","Establishing diplomatic ties with China is a political decision made by Honduras on the basis of the one-China principle and based on no preconditions. China highly appreciates the decision of Honduras. Diplomatic relations are not a bargaining chip. Over the past few years, when Panama, the Dominican Republic, El Salvador, and Nicaragua established or restored diplomatic relations with China, there were no preconditions whatsoever, neither were there any for Honduras.\nNow that we have established diplomatic ties with Honduras, China will, on the basis of the one-China principle, act in the spirit of mutual respect, equality, mutual benefit and common development, actively promote the mutually-beneficial cooperation in various fields with Honduras, and contribute to its economic and social development and the well-being of the local people.\nIt is widely known that the DPP authorities are an expert of using dollar diplomacy. We would like to make this clear to the DPP authorities that “Taiwan independence” and dollar diplomacy have no future and any attempt to go against the trend of history will end in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347491.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230327_11049724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-27","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","According to reports, Honduran Foreign Minister Eduardo Enrique Reina said that the Honduran government assured that they will not leave students who are studying in Taiwan with Taiwanese scholarships “helpless”, and a way to help them will be sought from China following the establishment of diplomatic ties. So will China allow these Honduran students to continue their study in the mainland?","China cares deeply about Honduran students in Taiwan. The mainland is ready to receive every one of them if they wish to come to study in the mainland, which will become their new home. The establishment of diplomatic relations will serve as our new starting point, as we set out to broaden cultural, people-to-people and educational exchanges and cooperation and bring our peoples closer to each other with Honduras.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347491.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230327_11049724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-27","Mao Ning","AFP","Former leader of the Taiwan region Ma Ying-jeou started a historic visit to the mainland today. Can the foreign ministry confirm that he will meet with senior officials? Do you have any comment on this visit?","This is not a question about diplomacy. I’d like to refer you to the competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347491.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230327_11049724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-27","Mao Ning","China Review News","The American Institute in Taiwan said that while Honduras’ severing of ties was a sovereign decision, China often makes promises in exchange for diplomatic recognition that ultimately remain unfulfilled. They added that “We strongly encourage all countries to expand engagement with Taiwan and to continue to stand on the side of democracy, good governance, transparency, and adherence to the rule of law.” Do you…","To quote a line from a Chinese poem, “Despite the incessant cry of apes from the banks, the swift boat has already sailed through thousands of hills.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347491.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230327_11049724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-27","Mao Ning","MASTV","On March 24, US President Biden released a joint statement with Prime Minister Trudeau while visiting Canada, in which they acknowledged the serious long-term challenge to the international order posed by China and stated that while they will cooperate with China in areas of mutual interest, such as on climate change, they remain committed to ensuring their ability to compete effectively with China on a level…","China is firmly against the unwarranted attacks and smears against China by the US and Canada.\nChina is committed to peace and development, advocates openness and inclusiveness and practices win-win cooperation. China has always been a force for world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of the international order. In contrast, the US and Canada cling to the Cold War mentality, advance group politics and stoke bloc confrontation. It is plainly visible to the international community who is right and who is wrong. The US and Canada should reflect on what they have done rather than misrepresent the facts and shift the blame onto China.\nWe often hear these countries talking about upholding the sovereignty and territorial integrity of a certain country, yet when it comes to issues concerning China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, these countries have openly applied double standards, which shows their hypocrisy. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US and Canada are in no position to point fingers.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347491.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230327_11049724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-28","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan officials announced today that Fiji has renamed Taiwan’s representative office as the Trade Mission of the Republic of China (Taiwan), upgrading it from the previous name of Taipei Trade Office. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on this recent decision by Fiji?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal Government representing the whole of China. This is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a universally recognized norm governing international relations. We oppose any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”. Such attempt will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347492.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230328_11050448.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-29","Mao Ning","AFP","A senior US official said today, there’s absolutely no reason for China to use Tsai’s visit to the US this week as a pretext to overreact. The same official also said Tsai’s trip is fully consistent with decades of practice. Does the Chinese side have any comment on this matter？","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region. We firmly oppose any visit by leader of the Taiwan authorities to the US in any name or under whatever pretext. And we firmly oppose the US’ having any form of contact with the Taiwan authorities, which violates the one-China principle. China has repeatedly protested to the US side on Tsai’s so-called stopover in the US. Past mistakes do not justify any new mistake. Repeating a mistake does not make it legitimate. The trip is not so much a “transit”, but an attempt to seek breakthroughs and propagate “Taiwan independence”. The issue is not about China overreacting, but the US egregiously conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatists.\nThe ones who are creating the problem and making provocations is not China, but the US and the “Taiwan independence” separatists. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly deliver on its leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, stop fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, and stop undermining the political foundation for bilateral relations while stressing the need to put “guardrails” on the relationship. China will closely monitor the developments and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347493.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230329_11051179.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 29, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please have the spokesperson interpret the Taiwan-related content in this year's Government Work Report.","This year is the opening year for comprehensively implementing the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, and an important year for laying the foundation for comprehensively building a modern socialist country. The Report on the Work of the Government reviewed the important achievements in Taiwan affairs work over the past five years and set out the major policies, principles and positions, and goals and tasks for Taiwan affairs work, providing clear direction for this year's Taiwan affairs work.\nWe will thoroughly implement the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question and the decisions and deployments of the Central Committee on Taiwan affairs. We will uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" adhere to the concept of \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,\" respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to introduce and improve policy measures that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation and enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, deepen integrated development across all fields between the two sides, promote spiritual connection among compatriots on both sides of the Strait, resolutely oppose the separatist acts of \"Taiwan independence\" and schemes of external interference, and solidly advance the development of peaceful cross-Strait relations and the process of advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nAt present, realizing normal exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait as soon as possible and restoring normal cooperation in all fields is the shared expectation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope the Taiwan side will heed the will of the people and remove all obstacles as early as possible. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will move toward us, walk together, and work hand in hand to contribute to the great cause of building a strong country and rejuvenating the nation, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522342.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","At the 2015 cross-Strait leaders' meeting, it was proposed that both sides jointly compile historical materials on the War of Resistance against Japan. What is the current progress in implementing this?","In November 2015, General Secretary Xi Jinping, at the leaders' meeting across the Taiwan Strait, proposed that “both sides of the Strait should support and encourage historians on both sides to join hands, share historical materials, co-author historical works, jointly carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, and jointly defend national dignity and honor.” Since 2016, historians on both sides of the Strait have worked together, using forms such as publishing books, special research projects, and academic conferences, to jointly study the history of the War of Resistance, achieving fruitful results.\nFirst, cross-Strait cooperation in compiling and publishing works on the history of the War of Resistance. In 2016, *The Great Wall and the War of Resistance*, co-edited by experts and scholars from both sides and jointly compiled by the Liaison Department of the Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang and the School of History of Nankai University, was published. In 2017, *A History of the War of Resistance in Fujian and Taiwan*, co-edited by experts from both sides from institutions including the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, Xiamen University, the Taiwan China Unification Alliance, the Taiwan Association for the Promotion of Relatives of Anti-Japanese (Patriotic) Fighters, and National Taiwan Ocean University, was published.\nSecond, scholars from both sides of the Strait jointly participate in special research projects. The National Social Science Fund's special project on research into the War of Resistance against Japan includes the topic “Jointly Compiling a History of China's War of Resistance Against Japan by Scholars from Both Sides of the Strait,” in which scholars from both sides jointly participate in special research, with the results presented in book form, divided into *Volume on War Mobilization and Social Construction* and *Volume on Wartime Diplomacy*. The *Volume on War Mobilization and Social Construction* plans to include 14 papers by scholars from both sides of the Strait, totaling more than 400,000 Chinese characters, and related work has now entered its final stage.\nThird, historians on both sides of the Strait have jointly held symposiums on the history of the War of Resistance. Since 2017, the Chinese Society for the History of the War of Resistance Against Japan and the Taiwan Chinese Nation Anti-Japanese War Memorial Association have successively co-hosted four sessions of the Symposium on the History of the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance Against Japan and the Inheritance of the Spirit of Resistance in Nanjing, Wuhan, Nanning, and Beijing, further deepening consensus among academic circles on both sides of the Strait on the study of the history of the War of Resistance. A total of more than 1,500 people, including retired military officers, experts and scholars, teachers, and young students from both sides of the Strait, have participated. From March 23 to 29, the Taiwan Chinese Nation Anti-Japanese War Memorial Association sent a delegation to visit Beijing and Yunnan, and, together with the Chinese Society for the History of the War of Resistance Against Japan, held a launch ceremony for the new book *Collected Papers on the Joint Study of the History of the War of Resistance Across the Taiwan Strait* at the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japan Memorial Hall.\nThe development and continued advancement of this work is of great significance in promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to remember the history of the War of Resistance, carry forward the spirit of resistance, jointly defend national dignity and honor, and unite their strength and will to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522331.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The first quarter of this year is nearly over, and various localities have held many cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation. What cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities are expected to be held next?","Since the beginning of the year, we have taken a series of measures to promote the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and the regularization of exchange and cooperation. These measures have been welcomed by compatriots on both sides, and cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges continue to be lively.\nFirst, major Taiwan industrial and commercial groups and agricultural and fishery sectors have successively organized delegations to visit and exchange on the mainland. From February 15 to 17, Huang Yicheng, chairman of the Taiwan Cross-Strait Agriculture and Fisheries Exchange and Development Investment Association, led Taiwan agricultural and fishery representatives to visit Beijing. This was the first agricultural and fishery group from the island to come to the mainland for exchanges in nearly three years. Song Tao, director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, met with the delegation. The delegation also visited the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the General Administration of Customs, the All-China Federation of Supply and Marketing Cooperatives and the China Fruit Circulation Association, toured the Jing-Shen Seafood Market, and conducted in-depth exchanges on issues of concern to Taiwan agricultural and fishery people, such as resuming the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland. On March 21, Hsu Shu-po, chairman of the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce, led an economic and trade exchange delegation to visit. Song Tao, director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, and Yin Yong, mayor of Beijing Municipality, successively met with the delegation. The delegation also held in-depth exchanges with the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism, the General Administration of Customs, the China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises on resolving issues such as food enterprise registration and the resumption of Taiwan agricultural and fishery product imports, as well as strengthening cross-Strait service industry cooperation. From March 22 to 24, Wang Zhi-hui, deputy county magistrate of Taitung County, Taiwan, and his party visited, and Pan Xianzhang, deputy director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, met with the exchange delegation. The delegation also held in-depth exchanges with the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the General Administration of Customs and other departments on issues of concern to Taiwan agricultural and fishery people.\nSecond, relevant departments and localities have organized a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities with rich content and diverse forms. On February 24, the Guizhou Province Characteristic and Advantageous Industry Investment Matchmaking Conference was held in Beijing, with more than 100 representatives of Taiwan-invested enterprises and leading agricultural enterprises from the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei region attending. On March 7, the Exchange Symposium of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Small and Medium-sized Enterprise Cooperation and Youth Entrepreneurship Promotion Group was held in Nanjing. From March 8 to 11, the unveiling of the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone (Chongqing) and investment inspection activities were held in Chongqing, with more than 100 guests from both sides of the Strait attending. On March 9, the Shanghai Taiwan Association held a “Taiwan Businessmen’s Lecture Hall” special session on tax-trade coordination, interpreting policies and answering questions for more than 50 representatives of Taiwan-invested export enterprises. On March 15, the 17th Cross-Strait Information Industry and Technology Standards Forum was held simultaneously in Beijing and Taipei via video link. It released seven common standards, one white paper and one case compilation, and reached 28 points of consensus in more than ten hot information industry fields such as semiconductor lighting, continuing to promote the common use of cross-Strait industry standards. On March 23 and 25, Guangzhou held Guangzhou-Taiwan High-Quality Development Promotion and Exchange Meetings in Hong Kong and Macao respectively, attended by Taiwan-invested enterprise institutions, Taiwan businesspeople representatives and Taiwan youth representatives in Hong Kong and Macao.\nNext, the Taiwan Industrial Association will lead a delegation to visit from April 17 to 21, and the Sansan Enterprise Exchange Meeting plans to jointly organize a delegation with the Chinese General Chamber of Commerce to visit in May. Some localities’ cross-Strait economic and trade activities are also being intensively prepared. For example, Qinghai Province will hold the second Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Forum on Jointly Seeking High-Quality Development in April or May this year; Fujian Province will hold the first Straits Cross-Strait Rural Revitalization and Common Prosperity Forum in April and the Straits Cross-Strait Commodity Exchange Fair in May; and Hubei Province will hold the 17th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week in June. We welcome Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots to participate actively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522311.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The mainland side continues to promote the restoration and expansion of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields. Please introduce the situation of cross-Strait civil exchange activities so far this year, and what activities are expected to be held next?","Since the beginning of the year, the mainland's economy and social life have rapidly and comprehensively returned to normal, and the enthusiasm of compatriots on both sides for mutual exchanges and interactions has risen sharply. More and more Taiwan compatriots are coming to the mainland to take part in in-person exchange activities. Several characteristics have emerged.\nFirst, cultural exchanges continue to be lively. On February 3, the \"2023 Kaohsiung-Beijing Special Week\" was held simultaneously via live link in Beijing and Kaohsiung, Taiwan. More than 600 Taiwan residents and over 200 Beijing community residents together experienced intangible cultural heritage and traditional snacks and took part in art gala performances and storytelling exchanges. From February 23 to March 14, a Taiwan ethnic minority delegation visited Guangxi and Yunnan respectively for ethnic cultural exchanges. On February 28, more than 700 compatriots from both sides gathered in Xiangyang, Hubei, to take part in the awards ceremony for the \"Hubei-Taiwan Anti-Japanese War Memory·Beautiful Life Today\" cultural and creative works competition. Themed \"Commemorating the Martyrs Together, Working Together for Rejuvenation,\" the competition received more than 1,000 entries from both sides. From March 20 to 27, the Cross-Strait Pop Music Joint Creation Camp was held in Beijing, where young musicians from both sides engaged in in-depth exchanges and jointly created outstanding musical works. On March 23 and 25, the drama \"Seeking Flavor,\" which traces the taste of cross-Strait family affection across 70 years and four generations, premiered in Beijing, as did the Kunqu opera \"People Among the Plants and Trees,\" which tells of the transplanting of Wuyi Mountain rock tea from Fujian to the Dongding Mountain of Taiwan more than a century ago. Both plays take cross-Strait exchanges as their subject, portraying the story of cross-Strait culture sharing the same roots and blood ties, and economic interests that rise and fall together. They have positive significance for promoting mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides.\nSecond, folk belief exchanges are rich in content. From February 17 to 21, a Taiwan Mazu Friendship Association delegation visited Tianjin for exchanges. Mazu temples on both sides jointly released the \"Tianjin Initiative of Cross-Strait Temples,\" reaching consensus on promoting exchanges between temples, strengthening Mazu culture research, carrying forward Chinese culture, and developing cultural and creative industries. From March 5 to 9, the Yan Yi Palace management committee, the General Ancestral Temple of the Kaizhang Holy King in Zhangzhou, Fujian, the former residence of Chen Yuanguang, together with the Taiwan Taoyuan-based Kaizhang Holy King Temple Development Association and others, jointly held in Yunxiao, Zhangzhou, and Taoyuan, Taiwan, the 1,366th anniversary celebration of the birth of the Kaizhang Holy King and a symposium titled \"The Kaizhang Holy King Belief Culture Across the Strait.\" Nearly 100 representatives of temples on the island, experts, scholars, and clan representatives attended. From March 12 to 14, the Fengshan Temple management committee in Nan'an City, Quanzhou, Fujian, together with the Yuqing Palace in Tainan and others, held a \"Series of Activities Commemorating the 1,100th Anniversary of the Birth of Guangze Venerable King\" in Nan'an, attended by more than 150 Taiwan compatriots.\nThird, youth exchanges take diverse forms. From January 30 to February 12, 18 students from both sides of the Strait from the Tsinghua University Rural Revitalization Work Station went to Liaocheng, Shandong, to carry out academic field research, cultural and creative product design, rural construction and appearance improvement, and live-streaming promotion of agricultural products. On February 21, a grassroots exchange delegation of 45 Taiwan youths conducted a seven-day exchange and visit in Wenzhou, Zhejiang, during which many Taiwan youths handled mainland bank cards on site and experienced mobile payment functions. On March 22, the 2023 Cross-Strait New Farmers Rural Construction and Rural Entrepreneurship Development Forum was held in Xiamen. Themed \"Telling Good Rural Stories and Helping Rural Revitalization,\" the forum used \"The Amazing Farming Innovators,\" created on Baidu's Baijiahao platform, as its exchange platform. It brought together more than 100 scholars, agricultural producers, and content creators from both sides, showcasing the efforts and achievements of cross-Strait new farmers in advancing rural revitalization. On March 27, Guizhou and Guangdong provinces jointly held the \"Guangdong and Guizhou Joining Hands, Gathering Strength——Taiwan Youth Lingnan Friendship Guizhou Tour\" event.\nFourth, sports and news exchanges are vibrant. On March 19, the Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Youth Cycling Event was held in Kunshan, Jiangsu, with more than 300 youth representatives from both sides eagerly taking part. From March 19 to 26, the 2023 \"Baodao Youyicun\" Slow-Pitch Softball Invitational Tournament was held in Kunshan, Jiangsu, with 18 teams from both sides and a total of more than 500 participants. From March 17 to 20, Tianjin held the \"Cross-Strait Media Jinggu Tour,\" in which more than 20 media professionals from nine media outlets on both sides learned about Tianjin's history and culture, business environment, rural revitalization, high-tech development, and the style of Taiwan-invested enterprises through interviews and exchanges.\nLooking ahead to the second quarter, as cross-Strait direct flight routes increase, travel for Taiwan compatriots to the mainland will become more convenient, and localities will hold more in-person cross-Strait exchange activities. In cross-Strait cultural exchanges, Guangxi will hold the 2023 \"Zhonghua Yijia Qin——Guangxi-Taiwan Ethnic Groups Celebrate the Zhuang Sanyue San\" activity, Sichuan will hold the Cross-Strait Bashu Culture and Arts Season, Chongqing will hold the Cross-Strait Yue Fei Culture Summer Camp, and Weifang, Shandong, will hold cross-Strait kite culture exchange activities. Youth exchange activities will increase noticeably: the 4th Cross-Strait Student Baseball League will kick off in Zhejiang, Shanghai will hold the \"We Love·7th Cross-Strait Youth Short Film Competition,\" Tianjin will hold the 4th \"Haihe Craftsman Cup\" skills competition—a series of Tianjin-Taiwan Youth Vocational Skills Competition activities, Hubei will hold the \"Striving Young Generation, Integrating New Journey——5th Cross-Strait Youth Donghu Forum series of activities,\" and Hunan will hold the Hunan-Taiwan Youth Culture Festival. In folk belief exchanges, Shaanxi will hold the Qingming Ceremony for Sacrificing to the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan, Henan will hold the Guimao Year Yellow Emperor Hometown Ancestor Worship Grand Ceremony, Shandong will hold the Mazu Spring Sacrifice Grand Ceremony, Shanxi will hold a series of Cross-Strait Shennong Yan Emperor Folk Ancestor Worship Ceremony activities, Hubei will hold the World Chinese Yan Emperor Hometown Root-Seeking Festival, and Gansu will hold the Grand Ceremony for Sacrificing to Fuxi, the ancestor of Chinese humanity. We welcome everyone to keep following and taking part in cross-Strait exchange activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522306.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Recently, reports have emerged of a US “plan to destroy Taiwan.” A former US official who had spread remarks about “destroying TSMC” encouraged “arming every Taiwanese citizen with AK-47 rifles” during his recent visit to Taiwan. The “suspicion of the US” theory on the island has reached its highest volume in recent years. A poll showed that 85% of Taiwanese internet users believe the US has a “plan to destroy…","The poll you mentioned reflects the widespread doubt among Taiwan compatriots about the United States playing the “Taiwan card” and their concern for their own future and destiny.\nFor a long time, anti-China forces in the United States, out of their own interests, have condoned and supported “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in taking reckless provocations and escalating cross-Strait tensions, with the aim of using the Taiwan question to contain China’s development and progress, damage the interests of the Chinese nation, and obstruct the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and are even willing to destroy Taiwan for this purpose. The fact that the United States stirs up trouble around the world, creates division and conflict, and abuses force in pursuit of its own interests is known to all. US military operations in Iraq, Afghanistan, Libya and other countries have caused countless humanitarian tragedies and seriously undermined international and regional security and stability, and the United States always withdraws and leaves the mess to others, making itself the “biggest winner” that profits from the situation. This is the so-called “America First.” Facts fully demonstrate that wherever the United States stokes the fire, the people there will suffer.\nRegarding the doubts and concerns of the people on the island, the more the DPP authorities argue and suppress, the more they expose their guilty conscience and cowardice, and expose their true face of selling out the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people in pursuit of political self-interest. Those who truly love Taiwan would not “award medals” to Americans who advocate the “destruction of Taiwan” theory, would not hand over Taiwan’s advantageous industries, would not lavishly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan people to buy weapons from the US at high prices to embolden “independence,” would not turn Taiwan into a “powder keg” in order to cling to the US, and even less would they bind Taiwan compatriots to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coerce young Taiwanese into becoming “cannon fodder.” Aren’t these exactly what the DPP authorities have done?\nWe believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots have clearly recognized that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders are unreliable. To the United States, Taiwan is purely a “chess piece” for containing China’s development; blindly “relying on the US” will only accelerate “harming Taiwan” and push Taiwan compatriots into the abyss of disaster. We hope that all sectors of Taiwan society and Taiwan compatriots will join us in jointly promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and building a peaceful home where compatriots on both sides can live in tranquility. Only this can bring real benefits and well-being to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522336.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","We have noted that some cross-Strait direct flight routes have recently resumed service. What is the current status of the restoration of cross-Strait direct flight destinations?","Compatriots and businesspeople in Taiwan eagerly hope that all cross-Strait direct-flight destinations will resume service as soon as possible, and cross-Strait airlines have also actively submitted resumption applications. On March 26, Shenzhen Airlines and Taiwan's China Airlines resumed the Shenzhen–Taipei route. On the 27th, China Airlines resumed the Guangzhou–Taipei route.\nAt present, the mainland civil aviation authority has approved the summer-autumn season flight plans of cross-Strait airlines. Cross-Strait airlines are arranging 794 passenger flights per week on cross-Strait routes, a year-on-year increase of 26.63%. We hope the Taiwan side will also take concrete action to implement its proposed “plan for restoring cross-Strait air passenger routes,” ensure that the relevant direct-flight destinations across the Strait resume service as soon as possible, do practical work for cross-Strait direct air links, and provide convenience for broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople traveling between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522327.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Reportedly, Tsai Ing-wen plans to make a “transit” and provocative visit to the United States, and plans to meet with US House Speaker McCarthy and others. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities, for their own political self-interest in pursuing “Taiwan independence,” have fabricated various pretexts and seized every opportunity to carry out “Taiwan independence” activities. The so-called “transit” of the Taiwan authorities’ leader is in essence a provocative act of “relying on the US to seek independence,” attempting to create incidents such as “one China, one Taiwan” and “two Chinas” that violate the One-China Principle. It seeks opportunities to peddle “Taiwan independence” internationally and to win the support of anti-China forces in the US. Tsai Ing-wen’s “transit” is not about staying quietly at an airport or hotel. Instead, under various pretexts, she seeks to meet with US government officials and members of Congress, conducts official US-Taiwan exchanges, and colludes with external anti-China forces. If she meets with US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy, it will be yet another serious provocation that violates the One-China Principle, damages China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose this and will certainly take measures to resolutely strike back.\nWe urge the US side to strictly abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not arrange for Tsai Ing-wen’s “transit” and visit, or even official contact with her, and to fulfill its solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522338.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, a joint protest action against “Taiwan independence” and against external interference, initiated by the Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum and composed of dozens of unification-leaning parties and groups, was held in Taipei. Nearly 300 representatives from all walks of life collectively expressed their strong demand to oppose “Taiwan independence” and oppose interference by external forces. They…","The rallies and protests by Taiwan's pro-unification forces concentrated reflect the true will of Taiwan society: opposition to the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to stir up cross-Strait tension and confrontation, and even scheming to seek 'independence' by force. They fully express the sincere wish of Taiwan compatriots for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and for cross-Strait relations to draw closer. We highly appreciate this. More and more Taiwan compatriots are taking action to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to actively promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, which is the only way to guarantee and enhance the interests and well-being of people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","As some cross-Strait direct flight routes and the 'mini three links' gradually resume, Taiwan compatriots hope that cross-Strait direct maritime passenger services can also resume as soon as possible. They especially hope that the direct maritime passenger routes between Pingtan and Taichung, Taipei and Kaohsiung will be restored early to facilitate direct travel between people on both sides. What is the attitude…","In November 2008, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan signed the Shipping Agreement across the Taiwan Strait, enabling direct shipping of passengers and cargo. The mainland-to-Taiwan island passenger shipping routes include five routes: Xiamen–Taichung, Xiamen–Keelung, Pingtan–Taipei, Pingtan–Taichung, and Damaishan in Zhejiang–Keelung. Over the years, cross-strait passenger shipping routes have become an important channel for cross-strait travel by residents on both sides. Since February 2020, cross-strait passenger shipping has been suspended due to the pandemic.\nAt present, compatriots in Taiwan earnestly hope to resume cross-strait passenger shipping direct routes. We attach great importance to this and have fully made relevant preparations. On the mainland side, there are no longer any obstacles to restoring normal cross-strait passenger shipping routes. We hope the DPP authorities will listen to the voice of the people, respond positively, and fully restore cross-strait passenger shipping routes as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522313.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","We note the reports on Liu Dewen, a Taiwan compatriot from Kaohsiung known as the 'soul ferryman' of Taiwanese veterans. Three years after the epidemic, Liu Dewen has resumed sending the ashes of veterans back to the mainland for burial. On the afternoon of the 27th, he flew to Beijing carrying the ashes of a veteran surnamed Tian. What is your view of Liu Dewen's action?","I have long heard of Mr. Liu Dewen's righteous deed. Mr. Liu Dewen is an ordinary citizen of Kaohsiung, Taiwan, who has done an extraordinary thing over the past 20 years. To help many mainland veterans who went to Taiwan fulfill their wish to return to their roots, since 2003 Mr. Liu Dewen, undaunted by hardship, has traveled back and forth across the Strait, visiting more than 20 mainland provinces, and has successively carried the ashes of more than 200 veterans back to their hometowns for burial. What he has done vividly illustrates that compatriots on both sides are one family, regardless of provincial origin or region. It is precisely this act of kinship that has soothed the veterans' pain of displacement and allowed them to return to their hometowns as they wished. We express our respect and gratitude to Mr. Liu Dewen, and we are also willing to actively support his good deeds and help more deceased veterans who went to Taiwan fulfill their final wishes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Song Tao, Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Affairs Office, recently held a discussion with Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwanese youth in Kunshan, Jiangsu. When responding to the question of what benefits unification would bring, he said that as long as it is under the one-China principle, whatever Taiwan compatriots want can be discussed. How should this be understood? Please further explain what benefits…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China; China’s national sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China has never changed. The one-China principle is the political foundation of cross-Strait relations. Achieving national reunification on the basis of the one-China principle is the trend of history and the right path. After reunification, Taiwan compatriots will enjoy tangible benefits.\nAfter reunification, Taiwan may adopt a social system different from the mainland’s. Under the premise of ensuring national sovereignty, security and development interests, the social system and way of life of Taiwan compatriots will be fully respected, and Taiwan compatriots’ private property, religious beliefs and lawful rights and interests will be fully protected.\nAfter reunification, the institutionalization and systematization of cross-Strait economic cooperation will be further improved. With the vast mainland market as its hinterland, Taiwan’s economy will have greater development space and stronger competitiveness, its industrial and supply chains will be more stable and smooth, and its innovation vitality will be more vibrant. Many long-standing problems that have plagued Taiwan’s development and the improvement of people’s livelihood, especially livelihood issues such as water and electricity shortages, can be solved through integrated development across the Strait and full connectivity. Taiwan’s fiscal revenue can be used to improve people’s livelihood, doing more practical, good and difficult things for ordinary people.\nAfter reunification, Taiwan’s cultural creativity will be fully promoted; compatriots on both sides will jointly inherit Chinese culture, carry forward the national spirit, exchange and learn from each other, and nurture future generations. Taiwan’s regional culture will flourish even more, nourished by the roots of Chinese culture.\nAfter reunification, Taiwan compatriots will have greater international development space, will stand taller and with more confidence internationally, will be safer and more dignified, and will share the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nWe hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize that adhering to the one-China principle allows cross-Strait relations to improve and develop and the prospect of peaceful reunification to be safeguarded; deviating from the one-China principle would make cross-Strait relations tense and turbulent and harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. For the sake of national righteousness, the future of the nation, and their own interests and well-being, compatriots on both sides should unite as one and actively participate in the just cause of advancing peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230329_12522340.htm"],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Reportedly, the US House of Representatives recently passed the so-called “Taiwan Assurance Implementation Act,” which requires the US Secretary of State to abolish restrictions related to US-Taiwan exchanges. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Taiwan-related bills promoted by certain people in the US Congress seriously violate the common consensus of the international community and the norms of international relations, and are a blatant provocation against China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US Congress to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to fulfill the US government's solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and to immediately stop deliberating the relevant bills.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","It is understood that a public ancestral worship ceremony will be held at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum in Shaanxi during Qingming Festival. Could you introduce the relevant information and which guests from Taiwan will attend?","Xuanyuan Huangdi is the human cultural ancestor of the Chinese nation. Offering a public sacrifice to Xuanyuan Huangdi at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum during Qingming is a traditional grand event for Chinese descendants to “trace the source, seek roots, unite hearts, and forge the soul.” The “Guimao Year (2023) Qingming Public Sacrifice Ceremony to Xuanyuan Huangdi” is co-hosted by the TAO of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese, and the People's Government of Shaanxi Province. It will be solemnly held on April 5, 2023 (Qingming Festival) at the Huangdi Mausoleum on Qiaoshan in Huangling County, Yan'an City, Shaanxi Province. On that occasion, Yu Muming, former chairman of the Taiwan New Party, representatives of the Taiwan Anti-Japanese (Patriot) Relatives Association, and heads of Taiwan business associations in some mainland provinces and cities, along with more than 50 Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life, will attend the public sacrifice ceremony and take part in tree-planting activities at the “Siyuan Forest” on Qiaoshan. We welcome Taiwan friends from all walks of life to attend this grand ceremony, to honor our ancestors and revere our forebears, to honor the departed with sincere respect, and to jointly inherit and promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","On the 25th of this month, Honduras severed so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. This is the ninth country to “cut ties” with Taiwan since the DPP came to power. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. Countries including Honduras establishing diplomatic relations with China is the correct choice in keeping with the trend of the times.\nIt must be emphasized that no person or force can stop the trend toward national reunification. The DPP authorities' 'independence' provocations go against the tide of history, sell out the interests of the Chinese nation, and harm the interests of the people of Taiwan. Their complete failure is only a matter of time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-03-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海记者","It is reported that Czech Chamber of Deputies Speaker Adamova recently visited Taiwan. What is your comment?","For the purpose of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have resorted to any means, including so-called “parliamentary diplomacy,” colluding with anti-China lawmakers from various countries and creating incidents that violate the one-China principle, staging farce after farce of seeking “independence.” None of these tricks can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. We urge the Czech side to immediately correct its erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question and return to the correct path of strictly abiding by the one-China principle.\nThis concludes today’s press conference. Thank you all!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202303/t20230329_12522289.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-03-30","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen has met with the Taiwanese diaspora and delivered remarks while transiting through the US. What’s your comment?","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region. We firmly oppose any visit by leader of the Taiwan region to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and we firmly oppose the US government having any form of official contact with the Taiwan region. In disregard of China’s strong démarches and repeated warnings, the US insisted on arranging the so-called “transit” for Tsai Ing-wen to go to the US. China strongly protests and condemns that.\nThe US and the Taiwan authorities made arrangements for Tsai to engage in political activities in the US and framed it as a “transit” to upgrade official exchanges and substantive relations with the Taiwan region. This seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, gravely undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and sends a seriously wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatists. This once again shows that the fundamental cause of the new round of tensions in the Taiwan Strait is the Taiwan authorities’ repeated attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence” and the fact that some in the US intend to use Taiwan to contain China.\nThe Taiwan question is the very core of China’s core interests, the bedrock of the political foundation of China-US relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in the relationship. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle. China will continue to closely follow the situation and resolutely safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347494.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230330_11051815.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-03-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 30 dispatch: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on the 30th that, after consulting the relevant competent authorities, starting April 1, the requirement for cross-Strait passenger flights in both directions will be adjusted from a negative nucleic acid test result within 48 hours before departure to a negative antigen test result within 24 hours. Cross-Strait passengers will fill in the health declaration card when passing through customs.\nA reporter asked: As cross-Strait direct flight points gradually resume, more and more Taiwan compatriots are traveling to the mainland. Will the mainland consider adjusting the rules on nucleic acid testing within 48 hours before departure for cross-Strait passengers to facilitate travel between compatriots on both sides? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nZhu Fenglian said that passengers from third places who enter the mainland via transit in Taiwan must still hold a negative nucleic acid test certificate issued within 48 hours at the place of origin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202303/t20230330_12522762.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-03-31","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen said yesterday that ties between Taiwan and the US are closer than ever. Taiwan will work together with its democratic partners, she added. What’s your response?","We have repeatedly made clear our position on Tsai Ing-wen’s trip to the US. We strongly oppose any form of official interaction between the US and Taiwan, strongly oppose any US visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities regardless of the rationale or pretext, and strongly oppose all forms of US contact with the Taiwan authorities, which violates the one-China principle. What has happened proves that this trip by the leader of the Taiwan authorities is not so much a “transit”, but an attempt to seek breakthroughs and propagate “Taiwan independence”. Let me stress that no matter what the Taiwan authorities say or do, it won’t change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. No one and no force can hold back China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347495.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230331_11052523.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-31","Mao Ning","CGTN","After Honduras established diplomatic relations with China, Guatemala is now the only country left in Central America without formal ties with China. Tsai Ing-wen is on her way to Guatemala. What’s your comment on that? We’ve also learned that Guatemala is sending a senior diplomat to China soon. Can you confirm that?","Honduras’ establishment of diplomatic ties with China brings the total number of countries having diplomatic ties with China to 182, which shows that the one-China principle is a universally recognized principle and represents the people’s aspiration and the trend of the world, and no force can block that trend. The separatist pursuit of “Taiwan independence” is against the will and interests of the Chinese nation and against the trend of history. It will not lead anywhere.\nWe hope Guatemala will see the trend of the world and make the right choice as early as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347495.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230331_11052523.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-03-31","Mao Ning","Reuters","The UK is about to join the CPTPP, a trade deal of 11 Asia-Pacific countries, like Australia, Canada and Japan. China and the Taiwan region have both applied for its membership. With the UK government currently describing China as a challenge, would China be concerned that the UK’s accession to the CPTPP would help Taiwan’s accession?","China is a staunch advocate for trade liberalization and facilitation and an important participant in regional cooperation and economic integration in the Asia-Pacific. The CPTPP is an important free trade agreement in the region. In September 2021, China officially applied to join the CPTPP. We are in contact, communication and consultation with all CPTPP members. Joining the CPTPP will help us further deepen reform in China and open up wider to the world. It will also give CPTPP members more access to the Chinese market and expand their economic and trade cooperation with China.\nAs to the Taiwan region’s accession to the CPTPP, our position is very clear. There is only one China in the world, and the Taiwan region is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. We firmly oppose any official interaction between countries and the Taiwan region and firmly oppose the Taiwan region’s accession to any agreement or organization of official nature.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347495.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202303/t20230331_11052523.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-03","Mao Ning","AFP","Last week, China said it would retaliate if House Speaker Kevin McCarthy meets with the Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen during a planned stop in the US. Can you tell us what kind of retaliation China would take? Will military drills be an option?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. As the Chinese side has repeatedly stressed, we strongly oppose any form of official interaction and contact between the US side and Taiwan authorities. Relevant US congressman needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, refrain from sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and avoid undermining the China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China will take resolute measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347496.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230403_11053644.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-03","Mao Ning","Reuters","Tsai Ing-wen has recently completed a tour of Guatemala and Belize. What does this say about the PRC’s relationships in Central America?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is affirmed in Resolution 2758 of the UN General Assembly adopted in 1971.\nHonduras’s establishment of diplomatic ties with China brings the total number of countries having diplomatic ties with China to 182, which shows that the one-China principle has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. No force can hold back this trend. The separatists’ pursuit of “Taiwan independence” is against the will and interests of Chinese nation and the trend of history. Their attempt is doomed to failure. We hope that Latin American and Caribbean (LAC) countries can see the trend clearly, handle issues related to Taiwan in a prudent manner and join the family of China-LAC friendly cooperation at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347496.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230403_11053644.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-04","Mao Ning","Reuters","US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy will meet with Tsai Ing-wen this Wednesday. Will China hold military drills again?","China firmly opposes the US’s arrangement for Tsai Ing-wen’s “transit” trip to the US and a meeting between her and House Speaker Kevin McCarthy, the third highest-ranking official of the US government, because it seriously contravenes the one-China principle and provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués and gravely undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués, not to allow Tsai Ing-wen’s “transit” trip to the US, and not to arrange for any meeting or contact between Tsai and US political figures and officials. The Chinese side will closely monitor the situation as it develops and resolutely defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347497.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230404_11054242.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-06","Mao Ning","AFP","Can you confirm that China’s Shandong aircraft carrier is currently carrying out exercises on Taiwan’s eastern coast? If so, is this the Shandong’s first time conducting exercises in the Pacific Ocean?","I would like to refer you to competent authorities of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347498.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230406_11055401.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-06","Mao Ning","AFP","Regardless of the Shandong aircraft carrier, can the foreign ministry offer any comments on any military exercises at all around the Taiwan region?","This is not a question about foreign affairs. Please refer to competent authorities of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347498.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230406_11055401.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-06","Mao Ning","China Daily","The Philippines’ Department of National Defense chief Carlito Galvez Jr. on April 5 said that the addition of four sites under the Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA) with the US will further boost the country’s capabilities to protect national interests and contribute to collective defense in the region, and also aims to protect the busy sea lanes of commerce in the South China Sea. Some have commented…","I already stated China’s position on this the day before yesterday. I would like to draw your attention to the long list of turmoil, division and devastation left behind by the US military around the world. Will increased US military deployment in one’s country or the region truly help protect sovereignty and security as well as regional peace and stability or rather cause grave irreparable consequences? Regional countries need to think carefully about this.\nAs to protecting sea lanes of commerce in the South China Sea, I believe the concern is really uncalled-for. There is never any issue with freedom of navigation and safety in the South China Sea. China and ASEAN countries are committed to the full and effective implementation of the DOC and steady progress in COC consultations. We have both the will and the capability to safeguard peace and stability in the South China Sea. There is no need for unwanted interference by forces outside the region.\nThe comments on the locations of the new military bases also speak to the concern shared by many insightful people in the Philippines, who worry that this may draw their country into the whirlpool of a potential conflict in the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and its resolution is a matter for the Chinese. It is not the Chinese side that is heightening cross-Strait tensions, but the “Taiwan independence” forces in the island and certain countries that support these forces. We hope regional countries could see clearly who is fueling tensions across the Taiwan Strait for what purpose and will not pull someone else’s chestnuts out of fire at their own expense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347498.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230406_11055401.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-06","Mao Ning","TV Tokyo","Regarding the meeting between Taiwan’s Tsai and McCarthy today, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that it would take resolute measures, but what specific measures will be taken?","The US acts with Taiwan to connive at “Taiwan independence” separatists’ political activities in the US, conduct official contact with Taiwan and upgrade the substantive relations with Taiwan, and frame it as a “transit”. This is a serious violation of the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. It seriously infringes upon China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and sends an egregiously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will take strong and resolute measures to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347498.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230406_11055401.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-04-06","MND spokesperson (unnamed)","N/A — spokesperson opening announcement (no press Q)","","The spokesperson pointed out that we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, firmly oppose any leader of the Taiwan region visiting the United States under any name or for any reason, firmly oppose the US side violating the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and firmly oppose any form of contact with the DPP authorities. We urge the US side to abide by the solemn political commitments it made to China on the Taiwan question, stop crudely interfering in China's internal affairs, stop official US-Taiwan exchanges and the upgrading of substantive US-Taiwan relations, and stop hollowing out and emptying the one-China principle. The Chinese People's Liberation Army keeps to its duties and mission, remains at a high level of vigilance at all times, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly upholds peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16215174.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-04-07","Mao Ning","AFP","According to Taiwan authorities, China sent warships and aircraft near the island today for the second day. This happened after the meeting between the Taiwan region leader with the US House Speaker. Can you confirm that and give us some details?","China will take resolute measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity. I would refer you to the Ministry of National Defence of China for your specific question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347499.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230407_11056146.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-07","Mao Ning","NBC","There is one argument prevailing in the US and other countries that it is not quite right for China to claim sovereignty over the “island democracy” of Taiwan, and that defending Taiwan is defending Taiwan’s democracy. How do you view this issue?","The Taiwan question is not about democracy, but about China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The sovereignty and territory of China have never been divided and shall never be divided. Some countries hype up the false narrative of “democracy versus autocracy”, connive at and support “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in the name of democracy, and use the Taiwan question to contain China. Such moves are highly dangerous and will get nowhere. The future of Taiwan lies in China’s reunification, and the wellbeing of the people in Taiwan hinges on the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The difference in systems across the Strait is not a barrier to reunification or an excuse for division. Peaceful reunification and One Country, Two Systems takes Taiwan’s realities into full account and helps Taiwan achieve longstanding peace and stability after reunification. It is the basic principle for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to realize national reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347499.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230407_11056146.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-04-07","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, April 7 (Xinhua) — Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on April 7 that the Taiwan-based “Prospect Foundation” and the “Asian Freedom and Democracy Alliance,” under the instruction of the DPP authorities, under the pretexts of “democracy,” “freedom,” and “cooperation,” and under the banner of “academic exchanges” and “seminars,” have aggressively peddled “Taiwan independence” positions internationally, sought to ally with and cling to anti-China forces, created incidents violating the one-China principle such as “one China, one Taiwan” and “two Chinas,” and expanded what the Taiwan authorities call “international space.” The mainland has decided to take disciplinary measures against these two institutions, prohibiting their principal responsible persons from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, and prohibiting relevant mainland organizations and individuals from cooperating with them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230407_12524480.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-07","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲7日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 7: TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on the 7th, saying: The complete reunification of the motherland must be realized, and it certainly can be realized! We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that we will not leave any room for any form of ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist activities, and we will certainly take resolute measures to thwart any external…","Zhu Fenglian said that for some time, the DPP authorities have persistently challenged the one-China principle. For political self-interest, they are willing to serve as the vanguard of the United States in containing and suppressing China, spreading 'Taiwan independence' theories such as 'one China, one Taiwan' internationally. They are going to great lengths to sell out the interests of Taiwan's people in order to cooperate with the United States in 'decoupling' and 'cutting supply chains' against China, intensifying efforts to court and infiltrate the U.S. Congress, and using the hard-earned money of people on the island to buy arms. This will ultimately only push Taiwan into a perilous situation of 'war being dire and battle dangerous,' bringing profound disaster to the broad Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230407_12524873.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","While displaying itself as a force for global peace, China is threatening Taiwan with military drills in the Taiwan Strait. How can China win the trust of the international community while conducting military drills?","I can’t see the logic in which you raised the question. I think your question makes no sense.\nThe spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command stated earlier that from April 8 to 10, the PLA Eastern Theater Command launched combat readiness security patrol encircling the Taiwan Island and carried out “Joint Sword” exercises. This is a stern warning to the provocative activities of “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces and their collusion with external forces, and a necessary move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. With regard to your question, I would like to tell you that the one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a universally recognized basic norm in international relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","NHK","Can you confirm if the PLA drills are meant to be a countermeasure in response to the meeting between Tsai Ing-wen and US House Speaker Kevin McCarthy?","The Foreign Ministry spokesperson has issued a statement on the “transit” by Tsai Ing-wen in the US, stressing that in response to the seriously wrong move taken jointly by the US and Taiwan, China will adopt strong and resolute measures to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity. As I said earlier, the spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command also stated earlier that the combat readiness security patrol encircling the Taiwan Island and the “Joint Sword” exercises is a stern warning to the provocative activities of “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces and their collusion with external forces, and a necessary move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. I think those statements have given a clear answer to your question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Two questions. The first one is another question about the ongoing PLA drills around Taiwan. Is China concerned about a possible escalation of the regional security situation during these drills? The second question is about the Philippines and the US. The two countries are about to hold their biggest-ever joint military exercises this week, starting tomorrow. How does China view this?","I have made abundantly clear China’s position on the military drills. Let me stress that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community and a basic norm in international relations. The greatest threat to cross-Strait peace is “Taiwan independence” forces and foreign connivance and support for their activities. We hope the world will see clearly the nature of the Taiwan question, follow the one-China principle and oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, one must reject all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nOn your second question, exchange and cooperation between relevant countries should not target any third party and should be conducive to regional peace and stability. The US-Philippines military cooperation must not interfere in South China Sea disputes, still less harm China’s territorial sovereignty, maritime rights and interests and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","AFP","French President Emmanuel Macron said in an interview yesterday that Europe should not be a follower of either the US or China on the Taiwan issue and that Europe should not become entangled in crises that do not concern it. Does China have any comment on the President’s remarks?","The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a basic norm in international relations. The biggest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait is the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and the US connivance at and support for them. We hope that all countries will see clearly what the Taiwan question is truly about, continue to abide by the one-China principle and firmly oppose all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","While conducting military drills near Taiwan, China is also holding high-level consultation on maritime affairs with Japan. Can you share the details about the consultation and the outcomes?","Information on this will be released in due course. Please check back for updates.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-10","Wang Wenbin","NBC","Some observers say that the intensity and scale of China’s military exercises around Taiwan is less than during or after Speaker Pelosi’s visit, but the Taiwanese authorities said today that the intensity is the same. Which one is more accurate in your view and has China paid more attention this time to the diplomatic and international impact of the Taiwan-related exercises?","I suggest that rather than follow the remarks by so and so from the US or the Taiwan authorities, perhaps you could give more attention to the statement from the spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command, which is more authoritative, accurate and helpful for your readers.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347500.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230410_11057054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-11","Wang Wenbin","AFP","French President Macron’s recent comment that Europe must not follow either Washington or Beijing on the Taiwan issue has sparked some criticism in Europe. The director of the Polish Institute of International Relations said that a brain death has occurred somewhere. What’s China’s view on the controversy？","We have stated China’s position on the issue. Let me reiterate that the Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community and a basic norm in international relations. The biggest threat facing peace in the Taiwan Strait is the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign forces’ connivance and support for those activities. We hope all parties will understand the true nature of the Taiwan question, continue to follow the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347501.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230411_11057544.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-11","Wang Wenbin","AFP","It’s about the recently-concluded PLA drills around Taiwan. Taiwan’s defense ministry says it has detected nine Chinese warships and 26 aircraft around the island today even after the drills had officially ended. Can you explain why the ships and aircraft are still there?","We have made clear China's position on this question. Let me stress again that China stands ready to take resolute measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Let me also add that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s defense ministry”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347501.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230411_11057544.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-12","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Can you confirm reports that China is planning to impose a no-fly zone north of Taiwan from April 16 to 18? The second question is, Taiwan has accused Chinese fishing crews of repeatedly cutting the island’s undersea cables. Does the foreign ministry have any response to this?","I am not aware of what you mentioned.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347502.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230412_11058062.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-12","Wang Wenbin","AFP","French President Macron has continued to receive criticism for saying that Europe should follow neither the US nor China when it comes to Taiwan. Former US President Trump yesterday accused Macron of pandering to China. You previously stated China’s stance on Taiwan, but would you be willing to comment specifically on Macron’s remarks and the controversy surrounding them?","As a journalist from AFP, you are particularly interested in President Macron’s visit to China, which I think is understandable. Not long ago, French President Emmanuel Macron paid a successful visit to China, during which the two sides reached important common understandings. The visit injected new impetus into China-France and China-EU cooperation.\nIt comes as no surprise that President Macron’s view that Europe should develop more strategic autonomy and avoid getting entangled in bloc confrontation has attracted some criticism, especially from the US. From our perspective, certain country is reluctant to see other countries being independent, and often seeks to coerce others into doing its bidding. But the truth is, strategic autonomy will bring more respect and friends, while coercion and pressure will only cause more resistance and opposition.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347502.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230412_11058062.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 12, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's TAO regular press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou visited the mainland from March 27 to April 7 for ancestral worship and exchanges. What is your evaluation of his visit to the mainland this time?","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation visited Nanjing, Wuhan, Changsha, Chongqing, Shanghai, and other places from March 27 to April 7. He fulfilled his long-held wish to return to his ancestral home to pay respects to his ancestors. He led Taiwan youth students in discussions and exchanges with students from Wuhan University, Hunan University, and Fudan University, visited important historical memorial sites, and experienced the high-quality economic and social development achievements of the mainland. Mr. Ma's visit has drawn great attention from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, and public opinion has generally given it positive evaluations. It is of positive significance for promoting exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides and for advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nMr. Ma Ying-jeou's visit fully reflects that compatriots on both sides are all Chinese and are members of one family, sharing the same bloodline, culture, history, and vision. It reflects the common voice of compatriots on both sides, who want peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. It once again proves that the “1992 Consensus” is the anchor of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations. We sincerely hope that compatriots on both sides will move toward each other and advance hand in hand on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526106.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, recently met Ma Ying-jeou in Wuhan and again pointed out: “Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese and one family. Matters at home can always be discussed in good faith, and should be discussed more. We are willing to widely listen to the opinions of Taiwan compatriots.” May the mainland next carry out broader dialogue with people from all…","Director Song Tao’s remarks mean that matters across the Taiwan Strait are matters for us, Chinese on both sides of the Strait, to handle ourselves. As long as we adhere to the One-China Principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we can find a solution through equal consultation and dialogue. These remarks are also directed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces colluding with external forces to undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and endanger peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. They are both a reminder and a warning.\nOur policy toward Taiwan is clear. We will fully implement the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the overall strategy of the new era for resolving the Taiwan question. On the basis of the One-China Principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we will extensively listen to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals, conduct dialogue and consultation in diverse forms, continuously build consensus, continuously improve policy measures that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and promote the restoration, expansion, and continuous deepening of exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Taiwan Strait. We will unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to firmly defeat the “Taiwan independence” separatist plots, resolutely oppose interference by external forces, and advance the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526107.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently returned to his ancestral home in Hunan with his family to worship his ancestors. While reading the memorial text, he choked up several times, which drew attention on the island. Many Taiwanese netizens said, 'A wanderer returning home and remembering one's roots and ancestors is authentic Chinese culture,' and 'Worshipping ancestors means not forgetting one's origins; I will also return…","Being prudent in the end and remembering one's origins, honoring ancestors and cherishing one's hometown, are the fine traditions of the Chinese nation. The core of the Chinese spirit has always included the longing to never forget one's homeland, to return to one's roots, and to be reunited with family. No person or force can sever this. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to find their ancestral homes and ancestral halls, look at their family genealogies, seek their roots, worship their ancestors, and return to their ancestral lineages.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led a group of Taiwan young students in a discussion and exchange with young students from three mainland universities. Ma said he hopes that meetings between students across the Taiwan Strait can become “routine,” and believes that for cross-strait youth, “more contact means more friendship,” and that “promoting exchanges among young people across the Taiwan Strait is an urgent task.” What…","As everyone has seen, many of the Taiwan youth who accompanied Mr. Ma Ying-jeou on his visit had come to the mainland for the first time. During the 12-day visit and exchange, they formed many views and had experiences different from before. For example, they said that mainland youth are “quite amiable, gentle, warm, and friendly in exchanges,” which is entirely free of the negative sentiment hyped up on the island. They saw that the mainland is developing rapidly and has achieved enormous accomplishments, and their understanding of historical sentiment and cross-Strait relations has risen to a new level.\nYouth are the future of cross-Strait relations. Stronger exchanges and interactions between young people on both sides can inject new strength and vitality into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Because of differences in their study, life experiences and environments, young people on both sides hold different views on some issues, and we fully understand this. For precisely this reason, young people across the Strait need to strengthen exchanges and enhance mutual understanding. We are glad to see and support stronger exchanges and interactions among young people across the Strait, and we are willing to create all necessary conditions for this. For example, on April 1, Xiamen University held the “Bonds of Affection Between Xiamen and Kinmen” 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Students Cultural Study Camp, at which 53 teachers and students from Taiwan gathered at Xiamen University and, together with Xiamen University teachers and students, took part in a five-day academic research and cultural visit. Young students from both sides engaged in in-depth exchanges and interactions, supported and encouraged one another, and grew together.\nIt should be pointed out that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities still strictly control and restrict exchanges between schools at all levels in Taiwan and schools on the mainland, and still prohibit mainland personnel from going to Taiwan for exchanges. This is the greatest obstacle to exchanges between young people and students across the Strait. Only when the Democratic Progressive Party authorities remove political barriers and cross-Strait exchanges return to normal can meetings between young people and students on both sides become “everyday occurrences.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526104.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Since the DPP authorities took office seven years ago, not only have the island’s problems of “shortages of water, electricity, land, workers, and talent” not improved, but “shortages of eggs and medicine” have been added, sparking public resentment on the island. What comment does the spokesperson have?","To serve its own political interests, the DPP authorities have focused solely on political infighting and disregarded people's livelihood needs. As a result, the island's infrastructure is lagging, industrial development is imbalanced, the wealth gap is widening, and shortages of essential goods and sharp price increases occur from time to time, causing the \"misery index\" to keep climbing. The facts show that the fruits of Taiwan's economic development have not benefited ordinary people.\nAmong the factors constraining Taiwan's economic development, in addition to the \"seven shortages\" you mentioned, there is a critical eighth shortage: the \"shortage of peace and security.\" The DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to seek \"independence\" and provoke confrontation is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Without a stable situation in the Taiwan Strait and cross-Strait relations of peaceful development, Taiwan cannot have a stable and favorable investment and business environment, which would directly affect the island's economic development and the immediate interests of the Taiwan people.\nAt present, the Chinese mainland is steadily advancing Chinese-style modernization, which will bring more business opportunities and dividends to the global economy. Sectors across the island have expressed through various channels their strong desire to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, achieve mutual benefit and win-win outcomes, and promote Taiwan's economic development. We hope the DPP authorities will heed the will of the people, abandon their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, promptly lift the various restrictions that hinder cross-Strait personnel exchanges, restore normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526102.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","As the mainland’s epidemic prevention and control work enters a new stage and normal economic and social life is being fully restored, some Taiwan students hope to intern on the mainland during this summer vacation. What plans are there in this regard?","We have always attached great importance to, and actively created conditions for, providing services to Taiwan youth who come to the mainland for internships, employment and entrepreneurship. We build platforms to help Taiwan youth take part in the process of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and share in the opportunities of high-quality development on the mainland. As epidemic prevention and control on the mainland has entered a new stage, and in response to the needs of Taiwan youth, we will encourage and support relevant localities and departments to offer internship positions for Taiwan youth this summer, and to hold exchange activities themed on cross-Strait youth internships, employment and entrepreneurship, to help Taiwan youth pursue, realize and fulfill their dreams on the mainland.\nWe hereby announce to everyone the 2023 “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” Taiwan Youth Internship Program in Shenzhen. This year, the program has collected 1,256 internship positions, with 359 enterprises participating. The enterprises offering internship positions have high name recognition and great influence, including Fortune Global 500 companies such as Ping An, Tencent and China Merchants Bank, as well as a number of industry-leading enterprises such as the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, Qianhai WeBank and Kingdee Software. The internship positions are diverse: technology accounts for 27%, finance for 18%, and culture and creativity and social services for 18%. Based on the needs of enterprises and the circumstances of interns, the organizers will also offer positions with flexible internship periods. For example, Great Wall Securities and others offer internship opportunities of one month to half a year, and 564 internship-to-employment positions will also be provided, offering a two-way selection platform for Taiwan youth who wish to intern and find employment in Shenzhen. Taiwan students with internship needs may follow the specific information released on April 13 by the organizer, the Shenzhen Taiwan Business Association.\nIn addition, Jiangsu Province will hold the “Hand in Hand, Heart to Heart, Create the Future — 2023 Taiwan College Students' Jiangsu Internship and Employment Intensive Training Camp” from July to August. This year's training camp will continue to offer nearly 1,000 internship positions to students from Taiwan universities and Taiwan students enrolled at universities within Jiangsu Province, covering news and media, healthcare services, legal affairs, information technology, finance and many other industries and fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","During Mr. Ma Ying-jeou’s visit to Hunan, he connected live to the Hunan Satellite TV program “Sheng Sheng Bu Xi · Baodao Season” and sang “The Moon Represents My Heart” together with everyone, which sparked heated discussion among netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. May the spokesperson introduce this program? In recent years, many musicians from the island have come to the mainland to develop their…","Hunan Television and Mango TV invited more than 30 singers and more than 40 music and cultural experts from both sides of the Strait to record “The Everlasting Sound: Treasure Island Season,” creating a platform for music and cultural exchange across the Strait. The program was recorded in Changsha and Taipei. Beginning in March this year, it has been simultaneously broadcast on Hunan Television, Mango TV, Taiwan's CTiTV Asia and CTiTV channels, Hong Kong's TVB, and its affiliated platforms. The cumulative view count for the four episodes released so far has exceeded 3 billion. Winning audiences with sincerity, the program awakened the shared cultural memories of several generations across the Strait, promoted mutual understanding and spiritual kinship between people on both sides, and guided viewers on both sides—especially young people—to remember their roots and find common ground. It showcased the positive, upward, and united spirit of people on both sides of the Strait, and it has generated strong repercussions both at home and abroad.\nThe development of Taiwan musicians on the mainland and large-scale music exchanges across the Strait can be traced back to the 1980s. We have consistently provided active support and welcome Taiwan musicians to come to the mainland to share development opportunities, realize their musical dreams, and jointly promote the prosperity and development of the music markets on both sides. Many Taiwan musicians have come to the mainland to develop, established regular cooperation with mainland performing arts organizations, and created many outstanding musical works loved by people on both sides, fostering emotional resonance and spiritual kinship among compatriots across the Strait.\nAs music exchanges across the Strait deepen, we have continuously increased policy support for Taiwan musicians developing on the mainland, implemented equal-treatment measures in detail, and provided policy consultation and assistance to Taiwan performing arts organizations with licensing, registration applications, and performance brokerage activities on the mainland. In concrete measures, we invite Taiwan musicians to take part in literary and artistic performance activities on major themes; we conduct cross-Strait music talent exchange, information sharing, and targeted training for Taiwan musicians, giving appropriate priority to selecting musical talent and outstanding works; and we welcome Taiwan musicians to join various cultural groups on the mainland. At present, several well-known Taiwan musicians have become members of the China Musicians Association, which is affiliated with the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles.\nStarting February 16 this year, relevant departments resumed accepting and approving commercial performances related to Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. According to available information, as of now, localities have approved a cumulative total of 75 batches comprising 431 performances involving Taiwan performers. Taiwan singers and bands are expected to hold nearly 100 large-scale concerts on the mainland this year and participate in dozens of large music festival projects.\nGoing forward, we will continue to pay attention to and support the development of Taiwan musicians on the mainland, deepen integrated development in the music field across the Strait, promote joint efforts by musicians on both sides to carry forward China's outstanding traditional culture, and jointly build a beautiful spiritual home for people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","TAO Director Song Tao and Mr. Ma Ying-jeou rode the high-speed train together from Wuhan to Changsha, and Ma Ying-jeou marveled that the mainland's high-speed trains are spacious and comfortable. Wang Yi-chuan, former Director of the Taichung City Transportation Bureau, claimed that Ma Ying-jeou had been deceived, saying “the mainland's high-speed trains have no backrests.” What is your comment?","The mainland's high-speed rail has attracted worldwide attention. At present, the mainland's high-speed rail operating mileage is 42,000 km, reaching 93% of cities with a population of over 500,000. By 2035, the operating mileage of high-speed rail will reach about 70,000 km, and all cities with a population of over 500,000 will be served by high-speed rail. Traveling by high-speed rail has long become the everyday norm for mainland residents, and many Taiwan compatriots also very much like riding high-speed rail on the mainland: it is very safe, very comfortable, and very convenient. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou and some Taiwanese young students in his delegation came to the mainland for the first time and took high-speed rail three times for inter-city travel, and they felt quite good about it. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come and see the mainland by high-speed rail, and to experience the feeling of “a thousand li in a day, with scenery that changes.” We also believe that once cross-Strait interconnection and intercommunication are realized, with everything that should be connected connected, people on both sides of the Strait will be able to travel conveniently back and forth across the Strait by high-speed rail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","What is the spokesperson's comment on Tsai Ing-wen's “transit” trip to the U.S.?","We have stated our position many times regarding Tsai Ing-wen’s “transit” through the United States. Her conduct during the “transit” has made clear to people that the so-called “transit” is merely a pretext; in reality, it is a provocation of “seeking independence by relying on the United States.”\nFor some time, the DPP authorities have continuously challenged the one-China principle. For political self-interest, they are willing to serve as the vanguard of US anti-China and China-containment efforts. They spread “One China, One Taiwan” and other “Taiwan independence” theories internationally, sell out the interests of the Taiwan people to cooperate with the US’s “decoupling” and “chain-breaking” against China, step up efforts to court and infiltrate the US Congress, and use the hard-earned money of people on the island to buy arms. In the end, this will only push Taiwan into the perilous situation of “war and danger,” bringing profound harm to the vast number of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe complete reunification of the motherland must be achieved, and it will be achieved! We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that we will leave no room whatsoever for all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and we will certainly take resolute measures to thwart any external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","After returning to Taiwan from a visit to the mainland, Ma Ying-jeou said the “1992 Consensus” has come back to life. The Mainland Affairs Council said the “1992 Consensus” is consistent with the “one country, two systems Taiwan plan,” while the DPP even argues that the “1992 Consensus” does not exist, so how could it be revived? What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities completely distort right and wrong, confuse the public, and deceive public opinion.\nThe “1992 Consensus” is the consensus reached in 1992 under authorization by the Straits Exchange Foundation on the mainland and the Straits Exchange Foundation in Taiwan, in which each side orally expresses that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the common political foundation for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\n“One country, two systems” is an institutional arrangement after national reunification. The concept of “one country, two systems” was proposed long before the “1992 Consensus.” The specific form of its realization in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and fully accommodate the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. We will unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to jointly explore a “two systems” plan for Taiwan, enrich the practice of peaceful reunification, and firmly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nThe “1992 Consensus” and “one country, two systems” are two clearly different concepts. The DPP authorities have repeatedly mixed them up, attempting to mislead the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and to find pretexts and excuses for denying the “1992 Consensus” and undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526103.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海之声和看台海记者","Ma Ying-jeou's visit to the mainland to pay respects to ancestors and exchange views was warmly welcomed by mainland compatriots. Tsai Ing-wen's “transit” sneaking into the US was not only “coldly handled” by the US side, but also met with protests from overseas compatriots and American anti-war activists. How does the spokesperson view this phenomenon?","I believe everyone has noticed the evaluations in Taiwan’s public opinion, which hold that “Ma Ying-jeou made efforts to strive for peace, while Tsai Ing-wen led Taiwan into peril,” that Ma Ying-jeou “proved through action the effectiveness of the ‘1992 Consensus’,” that it “helps promote cross-Strait exchanges and defuse hostility,” and that Tsai Ing-wen “has almost completely tilted toward the United States, pushing Taiwan into raging waves.”\nMr. Ma’s visit reflects the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait who want peace and development, and exchanges and cooperation, and it has positive significance for promoting exchanges and contacts between compatriots on both sides and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. The DPP authorities colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke has seriously undermined the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seriously harmed the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and seriously endangered peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Who is right and who is wrong is self-evident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526105.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","The mainland side is actively promoting the resumption of cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel. What measures has it introduced to facilitate cross-Strait personnel travel?","As the mainland's epidemic prevention and control work enters a new stage and the normal economic and social life is being fully restored, Taiwan compatriots can rest assured to come to the mainland to study, work, visit relatives and friends, travel, and engage in exchanges. While doing a good job in epidemic prevention and control, we have listened to the appeals of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and further optimized and adjusted the epidemic prevention and control measures related to Taiwan. Starting April 1, for cross-Strait passenger routes, the requirement for passengers in both directions has been adjusted from a negative nucleic acid test result within 48 hours before departure to a negative antigen test result within 24 hours. According to our understanding, a single nucleic acid test on the island currently costs about 3,000 to 4,500 New Taiwan dollars, equivalent to about 670 to 1,010 yuan in RMB; a single antigen test costs only 100 to 200 New Taiwan dollars, equivalent to about 22 to 44 yuan in RMB. These practical measures provide further convenience for normal exchanges between compatriots on both sides and reduce the economic burden on people traveling across the Strait.\nIn contrast, the DPP authorities, going against the wishes of compatriots on both sides, still set various restrictions and obstacles on mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, and have implemented policies of prohibition, restriction, and blockade on personnel exchanges and interaction across the Strait. Who is genuinely putting themselves in the shoes of compatriots on both sides and doing practical things, and who is scheming to obstruct exchanges between compatriots on both sides and only talking empty words, is clear to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Hsiao Bi-khim Has Become the First “Taiwan Independence” Stubborn Element to Be Named for Sanctions Twice. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Hsiao Bi-khim, acting as a pawn of external forces, is recklessly undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, even at the cost of pushing Taiwan compatriots toward a dangerous abyss. We solemnly warn Hsiao Bi-khim and other die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements that the mainland’s determination and resolve to crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces is firm and unwavering. Those who refuse to repent and act recklessly will surely be further severely punished by law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526101.htm"],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: During the PLA's exercises encircling Taiwan island, Tsai Ing-wen released a photo of herself listening to a security team briefing, saying “Let the people of Taiwan rest assured, the security of the Taiwan Strait is under control,” which outsiders questioned as a staged publicity stunt. What is your response? Second question: Terry Gou, founder of Hon Hai (Foxconn), said that he will strive to…","First question: To truly reassure the Taiwan people, the DPP authorities should immediately stop 'seeking independence through armed force,' stop 'buying weapons to resist unification,' and stop colluding with external forces to undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond question: Regarding the island's elections, we have always refrained from commenting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","On the first question: when Ma Ying-jeou visited the mainland, he said he hopes to expand exchanges among young students across the Strait, not only in schools, but also to bring them closer in heart and mind, and to revitalize the Chinese nation. Will the mainland allow mainland students to study in Taiwan and to live permanently with families in Taiwan? On the second question: the people of Taiwan all hope that…","On the first question: We actively advocate and promote the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and the routinization of exchanges in all areas across the Strait, which is also the shared wish of compatriots on both sides. However, as everyone can see, the DPP authorities have adopted various discriminatory and restrictive measures against mainland students, seriously harming the rights and interests of mainland students studying in Taiwan. Moreover, the DPP authorities still prohibit mainland residents from engaging in normal exchanges and business investigation visits to Taiwan. These are neither reasonable nor timely, and they should be removed as soon as possible. The obstruction of normalized cross-Strait personnel exchanges, and the failure to protect the legitimate rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan, are obstacles to mainland students studying in Taiwan.\nOn the second question: After the COVID-19 outbreak in January 2020, the DPP authorities banned mainland residents from visiting Taiwan and banned Taiwan travel agencies from operating group tours to the mainland, and this has not changed to date. The DPP authorities have implemented a policy of bans, restrictions and blockades on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions, which runs counter to the wishes of compatriots on both sides, runs against the trend of the times, and is not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","During Ma Ying-jeou’s visit to the mainland, he mentioned that both sides belong to one China. Tsai Ing-wen called this an “outdated discourse from the 1970s” and again mentioned so-called “mutual non-subordination” between the two sides. What comment do you have?","The historical background of the Taiwan question is clear, and the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China is beyond dispute. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China’s sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and will never be permitted to be divided. Taiwan’s status as part of China’s territory has never changed, and will never be allowed to change. In the face of the legal and practical realities of cross-Strait relations, fallacies such as “the two sides are not subordinate to each other” will only be swept into the dustbin of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, the Eastern Theater Command organized a three-day exercise encircling Taiwan island. Will this exercise cause adverse effects on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations?","The Chinese People's Liberation Army recently organized and carried out a series of countermeasure operations in the Taiwan Strait and in the surrounding sea and air areas. This is a serious warning against the collusion and provocations of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external anti-China forces, and a necessary action to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nAt present, the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are continuously pursuing “independence” and provoking confrontation, and external forces are intensifying their efforts to “use Taiwan to contain China.” This seriously undermines the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, seriously endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously undermines the prospects for peaceful reunification. All necessary actions we take to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity are aimed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign interference, and are by no means aimed at compatriots in Taiwan.\nAt the same time, the broad base of compatriots in Taiwan should further recognize the serious harm that “Taiwan independence” provocations pose to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They should recognize what is beneficial and what is harmful, distinguish right from wrong, stand on the right side of history, and join us in firmly opposing the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and foreign interference, and jointly safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The mainland-gifted giant pandas 'Tuan Tuan' and 'Yuan Yuan' have been beloved by Taiwan residents since 2008. Recently, reports emerged that the mainland intends to gift more giant pandas to Taiwan. Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an said on the 9th that this is a very good thing. Does the mainland have any plans in this regard?","We have noted this news. After inquiring with the relevant competent authorities, we found that the Taiwan media reports are untrue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Chairman of the US House Foreign Affairs Committee Michael McCaul mentioned that he will do everything possible to deliver arms sales to Taiwan as soon as possible and is also seeking the possibility of third-party arms sales to Taiwan. What comment do you have?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Some members of the U.S. Congress have repeatedly sent wrong signals to 'Taiwan independence' forces, which will only cause further damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to stop any form of official U.S.-Taiwan exchanges and military contacts.\nThe DPP authorities have bought off some anti-China U.S. lawmakers to champion 'Taiwan independence,' attempting to 'resist unification by force' and 'rely on the U.S. to seek independence.' This is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Guimao Year Yellow Emperor's Hometown Ancestral Worship Ceremony will be held on April 22 at the Yellow Emperor's Hometown in Xinlin, Zhengzhou City, Henan Province. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Yellow Emperor is the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation, and Yellow Emperor culture is the spiritual bond that unites Chinese people around the world. The Yellow Emperor Hometown Ancestral Worship Ceremony is jointly hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the People's Government of Henan Province, the CPPCC Henan Provincial Committee, the China Overseas Chinese Affairs Office, the All-China Taiwan Federation, and the China Yan-Huang Culture Research Association, and organized by the People's Government of Zhengzhou City and the CPPCC Zhengzhou Municipal Committee. The theme of this year's ceremony is “Same Roots, Same Ancestors, Same Origin, Peace, Harmony, and Concord,” and it will be held on April 22 (the third day of the third lunar month) at the Yellow Emperor Hometown in Xinzheng, Zhengzhou. Online ancestral worship and overseas ancestral worship will be held at the same time. On that occasion, responsible persons from relevant central units, some recipients of national honors, representatives of advanced workers from various industries, outstanding scientists, entrepreneurs, representatives of the new social strata, and mass representatives from all sectors of Zhengzhou City, about 2,500 people in total, will attend the ancestral worship ceremony. Representatives of relevant Taiwan authorities and civic groups will participate in on-site activities. We welcome journalist friends from both sides of the Strait to follow and report on the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","After the US House of Representatives passed a bill to fully ban TikTok, the DPP followed the US, using the pretext of “curbing election misinformation,” and also suggested a full ban on TikTok. What comment does the spokesperson have?","To pursue their own political interests, the DPP authorities and some politicians on the island are using various means to find excuses for creating an “information cocoon” for Taiwan residents. At bottom, they are afraid that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will draw closer and get along well, afraid that Taiwan residents will understand the real situation on the mainland, and afraid that the lies they have painstakingly built will be exposed. The DPP authorities want to shut Taiwan residents off by plugging their ears and covering their eyes, cutting off the channels through which Taiwan compatriots obtain the development information they need. What is harmed is Taiwan residents' rights, interests, and well-being in gaining more and better development opportunities.\nToday's press conference is now concluded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230412_12526099.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 12 dispatch: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering a reporter’s question on the 12th, said that the Taiwan authorities have for a long time adopted unilateral restrictive measures on the import of more than 2,400 mainland products into the Taiwan region, which has damaged the interests of related mainland industries and enterprises.\nA reporter asked: The Ministry of Commerce announced on the 12th that it will conduct a trade barrier investigation into the Taiwan region’s trade restrictive measures against the mainland. What comments do you have? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said that, at the request of the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Foodstuffs, Native Produce and Animal By-Products, the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Metals, Minerals and Chemicals, and the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Textiles, the Ministry of Commerce, in accordance with relevant regulations, has decided that starting April 12, 2023, it will conduct a trade barrier investigation into the Taiwan region’s trade restrictive measures against the mainland. The relevant investigation conclusions will be announced in due course.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230412_12526165.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-04-13","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan said China will set up a no-fly zone to the north of the Island of Taiwan on Sunday that will affect 33 flights. Has China notified neighboring countries and international airlines and vessels to avoid the area?","I’d refer you to competent authorities for this question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347503.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230413_11058793.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-13","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The Japanese government has demanded an explanation from China about the no-fly zone near Taiwan. What is China’s comment? And if there is a no-fly zone, how would you ensure the safety of civilian and commercial air and shipping traffic in the area?","I refer you to China’s competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347503.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230413_11058793.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-14","Wang Wenbin","TASS","German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock is on an official visit to China. She said in an interview earlier that China is Germany’s competitor, partner and systemic rival. What’s your comment? Will this affect China-Germany relations? On Taiwan, her position is very clear. Speaking after the PLA’s military drills around Taiwan between April 8 to 10, she said that Germany does not accept escalation in the…","China’s positions on China-Germany and China-EU relations and on the Taiwan question are consistent and clear. I would like to take this opportunity to update you on Foreign Minister Baerbock’s visit to China.\nEarly this morning, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang, returning from an overseas trip, went to Tianjin and visited a German business there together with Foreign Minister Baerbock. Afterwards they took a high-speed train to Beijing. This is Foreign Minister Baerbock’s first official visit to China. We believe her activities in Tianjin with State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang provide a first-hand impression of China’s development and China-Germany mutually beneficial cooperation.\nThis morning, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang and Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock co-chaired the 6th round of China-Germany Strategic Dialogue on Diplomacy and Security. They held candid, in-depth strategic communication on bilateral ties and international and regional hotspot issues. They agreed to conduct exchange across the board to enhance strategic mutual trust, avoid strategic miscalculation, and shape correct mutual understanding; to advance cooperation in various sectors for win-win results in a practical and open spirit; to stay committed to mutual respect, mutual trust, equality, seeking common ground while shelving differences, and respect for each other’s core interests; to step up communication and coordination in international affairs and jointly address common risks and challenges facing humanity. The Chinese side also elaborated on its position on the Taiwan question. On the Ukraine issue, China stressed that the only viable way out of the crisis lies in peace talks. We stand ready to work for peace. We also hope relevant parties will stay objective and calm and make joint efforts towards a negotiated resolution of the crisis.\nThis year will see robust exchange and cooperation between China and Germany. Both sides will take this visit as an opportunity to enhance dialogue and communication, deepen mutually-beneficial cooperation, work for the sound and steady growth of our all-round strategic partnership, and add stability and fresh impetus for world peace and development.\nWe’ll share more information about Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock’s visit. Please check back for updates.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347504.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230414_11059486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-14","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","China’s maritime authority has said it will ban vessels from an area north of Taiwan on Sunday due to potential falling rocket debris and a no-fly zone has also been put in place in that area. Can you clarify what this relates to?","China’s civil aviation authorities and relevant maritime authorities have both issued announcements. According to what we have learned from competent authorities, as is customary practice, civil aviation authorities notify the public in advance of the airspace that may be affected by space activities. This is aimed to alert relevant air traffic service departments and airspace users to possible impacts of such space activities. This is a responsible action to ensure aviation safety. The latest notices and announcements issued for the space activities identified the area that may be affected. I noted some earlier reports which said that China has set up a no-fly zone. This is not accurate. Relevant air traffic service departments have a responsibility to take measures accordingly to ensure flight safety.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347504.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230414_11059486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-04-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 14 -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fengling, answering reporters' questions on the 14th, said that relevant departments on the mainland, following established practice, issue advance notices and announcements of airspace affected by space activities. The purpose is to remind relevant air traffic service departments and airspace users to pay attention to the impact of the activities. This is a responsible routine practice to ensure flight safety.\nA reporter asked: Recently, the DPP authorities have hyped up the mainland's normal space activities as \"affecting the Taipei Flight Information Region.\" What comment do you have on this? Zhu Fengling gave the above response.\nZhu Fengling said: The DPP authorities, for their own selfish interests, distort facts and deceive public opinion, attempting to escalate cross-Strait confrontation. This political trick will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230414_12526988.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-04-17","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The United States Navy has said that one of its warships sailed through the Taiwan Strait yesterday citing freedom of navigation in accordance with international law. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on this US warship’s transit?","The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command has stated our position. The US sends a military vessel to the Taiwan Strait to flex muscles, which poses a threat to China’s sovereignty and security and undermines regional peace and stability. China urges the US to immediately end such moves of violation and provocation and stop causing troubles for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347505.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230417_11060477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-17","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","EU foreign policy chief Josep Borrell has said the EU-China relations depend on Beijing’s behavior. Do you have any comment on that?","China and the EU share a wide range of common interests, with more cooperation than competition and more consensus than differences. The China-EU relationship is not targeted at, dependent on or subject to any third parties. The EU needs to further uphold strategic autonomy, have a more independent and objective perception of China and work with the Chinese side based on the principles of independence, mutual respect and mutually beneficial cooperation, so that China-EU relations can have greater global influence and provide more stability and positive energy to the international community.\nI would also like to say that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests. I hope the EU will abide by the one-China principle and fulfill its solemn commitment of not maintaining official relations or concluding any agreement with Taiwan, which it made when establishing diplomatic relations with China, and truly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and international justice. I hope the EU will oppose the provocation of “Taiwan independence” elements and dissuade certain politicians from ganging up and playing the Taiwan card.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347505.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230417_11060477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-17","Wang Wenbin","China Daily","According to reports, German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock told an interview with German media that she warned China during her visit against the use of force over Taiwan. Citing Baerbock’s remarks, the German foreign ministry said on social media that destabilization in the Taiwan Strait will have serious consequences for every country and the global economy. “The shock wave of such a world economic crisis…","When meeting the press with German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang made clear China’s position on the Taiwan question. I want to stress again that Taiwan’s return to China is an important part of the post-war international order. The real status quo of the Taiwan question is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been split. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves. No foreign forces should try to interfere in the Taiwan question or expect China to make any concession on issues concerning its sovereignty and territorial integrity under external pressure.\nThe tensions in recent years in the Taiwan Strait are fundamentally caused by “Taiwan independence” separatists in Taiwan who are engaged in separatist activities with the support and connivance of foreign forces. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To keep the Taiwan Strait and the rest of the region peaceful and stable, it is essential to unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. We urge relevant parties to respect history and facts, and hope that certain German politicians will have a correct understanding of the nature of the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stop making irresponsible remarks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347505.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230417_11060477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-17","Wang Wenbin","NHK","The G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting opened in Japan. The ministers agreed they oppose China’s unilateral attempts to change the status quo by force and reaffirmed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Do you have any response?","There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. These are the core meaning of the one-China principle and the key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Relevant countries must recognize that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair which brooks no external interference. Though the mainland and Taiwan have yet to reunify, they belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided. This is the true status quo in the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan’s return to China is an important component of the post-war international order. To uphold the one-China principle is to defend the post-war international order.\nIf one truly cares about the situation in the Taiwan Strait, one must first have a clear understanding of the root cause for the tensions there. As facts have proven once and again, a separatist agenda advanced at all costs by “Taiwan independence” elements in Taiwan with the support and connivance of foreign actors — this is what’s changing the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and the root cause of cross-Strait tensions. To maintain a stable situation across the Strait and safeguard peace and tranquility in the region, one must unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nThose who say their one-China policy hasn’t changed, but wink at “Taiwan independence” separatists, overtly and covertly support them and even frame the opposition to such separatism as “changing the status quo” — they are not adhering to, but departing from the one-China policy and not defending, but endangering cross-Strait peace and stability. Their moves are irresponsible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347505.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230417_11060477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-18","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The G7 foreign ministers issued a communiqué after they held a meeting in Japan. They reaffirmed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and expressed concerns over the situation in the East and South China Seas and on issues related to Xinjiang and Tibet. They also urged China to ensure transparent, predictable, and fair business environments. Do you have any comment?","Regardless of China’s strong position and existing facts, the G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs and maliciously smeared and discredited China. The communiqué reflects the group’s arrogance, prejudice and deliberate desire to block and contain China. We deplore and reject this and have made a strong démarche to the host Japan.\nTaiwan is part of China’s sacred territory. The one-China principle is what underpins peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. To ensure real peace in the Taiwan Strait, it is absolutely essential to unequivocally oppose and stop any act for “Taiwan independence”. Matters related to Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Tibet are purely China’s internal affairs. No foreign forces may interfere in them in any way or under any pretext. The situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable. Relevant countries need to respect the efforts of regional countries to uphold peace and stability. They need to stop sowing discord and stop creating camp confrontation. As one of the most vibrant markets with the greatest potential, China is committed to providing a stable, fair, transparent and predictable investment and business environment for foreign investors. Certain G7 members have been oblivious to the principles of market economy and fair competition, overstretched and abused the concept of national security, and used every means possible to suppress foreign companies. They are in no position to jab fingers at China.\nAs a responsible major country, China firmly acts on the UN Charter and the basic principles of international law and is committed to building a community with a shared future for mankind. We once again urge G7 to reflect on their own problems and discard the Cold War mentality and ideological prejudices. They should stop running counter to the prevailing trend of today’s world, stop pointing fingers condescendingly, stop grossly interfering in other countries’ internal affairs and stop deliberately creating antagonism and division in the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347506.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230418_11061086.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-18","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Taiwan plans to buy as many as 400 US-made land-launched Harpoon missiles that are intended to repel any “Chinese invasion”. How does the foreign ministry respond to that?","US military contact with Taiwan and its arms sales to the region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. The move will harm China’s sovereignty and security interests and threaten peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We deplore and firmly oppose them. What has happened proves that the root cause of the new round of tensions in the Taiwan Strait is the Taiwan authorities’ repeated attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence”, the fact that some in the US intend to use Taiwan to contain China, and their joint attempt to change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait. This is an extremely dangerous trajectory no different from playing with fire. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop having military contact with and selling arms to Taiwan, stop creating factors that could cause tensions in the Taiwan Strait, stop seeking to change the status quo, and avoid going further down the wrong path of colluding with the Taiwan authorities. The Chinese side will take strong and resolute measures to firmly defend our sovereignty and security interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347506.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230418_11061086.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-19","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The President of Guatemala has announced that he will visit Taiwan this weekend. Does the ministry have a response to this announcement?","The fact that 182 countries have established diplomatic relations with China demonstrates that the one-China principle has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. The DPP authorities’ self-deceptive attempts to expand “international space” are leading them down a blind alley. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. “Taiwan independence” will not succeed. Any move that ignores the world trend and international justice and sticks to the wrong position is doomed to failure. We urge the Giammattei administration not to help those with malignant motives and not to go against the world trend and the aspiration of the Guatemalan people for selfish gains.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347507.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230419_11061802.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-19","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Early today, Liu Jinsong of your department on Asia called a senior Japanese diplomat to express concerns and unhappiness over the G7 foreign ministers’ statement. Can you speak to what specifically China is concerned about in this statement?","We stated China’s strong position yesterday on the negative developments at the G7 foreign ministers’ meeting hosted by Japan.\nI want to stress that the world has only one order, which is the international order underpinned by international law, and one set of norms, which is the basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter. If the G7 is truly against hegemonism and coercion, it needs to look inward and do some serious reflection, make sure that nothing like the invasion in Afghanistan, Iraq and Syria will happen again, reject long-arm jurisdiction and unilateral sanctions, and say no to any policy that puts a certain country first at the expense of others.\nIt is dangerous to seek the so-called solidarity of a few at the cost of a divided world. The world does not need a “G1” dictating the other countries, nor does the world need a “coalition of shared values” . What the world needs is mutual respect despite difference in ideology, values and development level, solidarity and joint efforts in line with the UN Charter and international law, and common endeavor to build a global community with a shared future.\nLet me also say that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been divided. This is the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. For those who say that they follow the one-China policy and yet frame China’s opposition to “Taiwan independence” as “changing the status quo”, they are in effect encouraging separatist provocation, hindering China’s reunification and making for a peaceful division. This is a total departure from the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347507.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230419_11061802.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-20","Wang Wenbin","Yonhap News Agency","ROK President Yoon Suk-yeol talked about the Taiwan question in a recent interview with Reuters. “We together with the international community absolutely oppose” the change of status quo by force, he said. How do you comment on this?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair at the core of China’s core interests. Its resolution is a matter for the Chinese, who do not need to be told what should or should not be done. The tensions in recent years in the Taiwan Strait are fundamentally caused by “Taiwan independence” separatists in Taiwan who are engaged in separatist activities with the support and connivance of foreign forces. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To keep the Taiwan Strait and the rest of the region peaceful and stable, it is essential to unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. The DPRK and the ROK are both sovereign countries with UN membership. The issue of the Korean Peninsula and the Taiwan question are completely different in nature, cause and history and cannot be mentioned in the same breath. This is a universally known fact. We hope the ROK side will follow the spirit of the China-ROK Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, stay committed to the one-China principle, and prudently handle matters related to the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347508.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230420_11062419.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-21","Wang Wenbin","Yonhap News Agency","The ROK side called in the Chinese Ambassador, made protests and pointed out the Chinese foreign ministry spokesperson’s remarks about the ROK yesterday amount to a “diplomatic discourtesy”. What’s your comment?","China has made serious démarches to the ROK side in Beijing and Seoul respectively regarding the ROK side’s wrong remarks on the Taiwan question. We fully outlined China’s position, stressed that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-ROK relations, and urged the ROK to act according to the spirit of the China-ROK Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations and be prudent about its words and actions when it comes to the Taiwan question. It is legitimate and justified for China to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Our commitment to that is unwavering. We hope the ROK will abide by the one-China principle and work together with China through concrete actions to maintain the sound and steady growth of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347509.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230421_11063331.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-21","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","Lately several countries have claimed that they oppose changing the status quo with force in the Taiwan Strait. What’s your comment?","The notion of “opposing the use of force to change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait”, uttered by certain individual countries, does not reflect the facts and reality on the Taiwan question. It is a narrative trap designed with a malign purpose.\nWhat is the status quo in the Taiwan Strait? It is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided.\nAnd who is trying to change this status quo? Certainly not the mainland, but the “Taiwan independence” separatists who have been promoting “incremental independence”, pushing for “de-sinicization”, and seeking to create the false impression of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, and the external forces who have been meddling in the Taiwan question by fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, selling arms to Taiwan, and peddling the narrative of “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow”. They are the ones responsible for disrupting the status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, it is essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. Those who talk about peace in the Taiwan Strait but refuse to oppose “Taiwan independence” are in effect conniving at and supporting separatist activities, which is bound to have a serious impact on cross-Strait peace and stability. China firmly opposes it. We will work together with the rest of the world to uphold the one-China principle, defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity, forestall any attempt to use the Taiwan question to contain China, and work for true peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347509.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230421_11063331.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-24","Mao Ning","AFP","The President of Guatemala arrived in Taiwan today to reinforce “diplomatic ties” with the island. What’s your position on this visit? And is there anything you want to say to the Guatemalan President?","We have taken note of what has been said by political figures in Guatemala in recent interviews. They said publicly that the overwhelming majority of countries recognize that Taiwan is part of China and that it is irrational for Guatemala not to have diplomatic ties with China. Their insightful words fully show that standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. China is the second largest source of imports and the fifth largest destination of exports for Guatemala. Recognizing the one-China principle and growing relations with China serves the fundamental interest of Guatemala and meets the aspiration of the Guatemalan people. Separatist activities for “Taiwan independence” go against the trend of history and are just DPP authorities’ self-deceptive attempts. They will not hinder the irreversible historical trend toward China’s reunification. Just as chair of the Guatemala-China friendship association Pedro Barnoya has said, China’s history has shown everyone that there is only one China in the world. History also shows that none of the attempts to split China will end well.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347510.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230424_11064751.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-24","Mao Ning","Global Times","According to reports, British Foreign Secretary James Cleverly said in a recent interview that he “fundamentally disagreed” that the Taiwan Strait was a domestic matter for China, insisting that it was in “everybody’s interests” to have a peaceful resolution to the situation. What’s your comment?","The British foreign secretary clearly needs to dust off his history books. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Taiwan’s return to China is an important component of the post-WWII international order, as is stated in black and white in the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community and a basic norm in international relations affirmed in Resolution 2758 of the 26th session of the UN General Assembly.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation and prerequisite for the establishment and development of China-UK diplomatic relations. More than 50 years ago, in the China-UK Joint Communiqué on an Exchange of Ambassadors, the UK acknowledged that Taiwan is a province of the People’s Republic of China and recognized the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China.\nLet me stress again that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair at the core of China’s core interests. Its resolution is a matter for the Chinese. No external force has any right to interfere. It is hoped that the UK side will approach this key matter of principle with a clear head and ample prudence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347510.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230424_11064751.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-25","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Guatemalan President today pledged his firm support for the “Republic of Taiwan”. Do you have any comment?","The fact that China has established diplomatic relations with 182 countries proves that standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. The DPP authorities’ self-deceptive attempt to seek wider “international space” is moving toward a dead end. The one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. “Taiwan independence” leads nowhere. Any move that goes against the trend of the world and international justice and clings to a wrong position is doomed to fail. We also urge the Giammattei administration to stop emboldening the DPP authorities in its wrongdoing and stop going against the overwhelming international trend and the aspiration of the people in Guatemala just to serve its selfish interest.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347511.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230425_11065451.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-26","Mao Ning","CNR","According to reports, UK Foreign Secretary James Cleverly said in his speech on foreign policy and the position on China on April 25 that it would be a betrayal of national interest to declare some kind of new Cold War or to isolate China. This Government will engage robustly and constructively with China, and at the same time, steadfastly defend the UK’s security and values. He said, China should fulfill its…","In today’s deeply interconnected world, the multiple challenges facing humanity require joint responses. Bloc politics and the Cold War mentality are against the trend of history and do not serve the interests of the UK or any other party in the world. China has grown its relations with the UK in the spirit of equality and mutual respect. However, the UK has not kept up with the times and has been repeating old lines from an outdated playbook, which will only keep the UK itself further and further away from the advancement of our times.\nRegarding the Hong Kong issue, all provisions concerning the UK under the Sino-British Joint Declaration have been fulfilled. The UK has no sovereignty, jurisdiction or right of “supervision” over Hong Kong and no so-called “rights” or “responsibilities” concerning Hong Kong. Xinjiang enjoys economic development, social stability, religious harmony and cultural prosperity and people there lead a happy life. These are facts for all to see, yet the UK side chooses to be oblivious to this and has deliberately smeared and slandered China. The status quo of the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China. The biggest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait comes from the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external connivance at and support for them. If the UK side wants sustained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it needs to strictly abide by the one-China principle and stand firmly against the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nI want to reiterate that the Taiwan question and issues concerning Hong Kong and Xinjiang are purely China’s internal affairs which brook no external interference. We urge the UK to be prudent in its words and actions, stop making groundless accusations against China and interfering in China’s internal affairs, and do more things that are conducive to the development of China-UK relations and world peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347512.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230426_11066591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-04-26","Mao Ning","The Paper","It was reported that the hospital in Chimaltenango, Guatemala built with support from the Taiwan authorities, was involved in a corruption case. The Vice Minister of Health and the director of the hospital were arrested for embezzling US$8.6 million. What’s China’s comment on this?","This is not Guatemala’s first Taiwan-related corruption case. In the name of enhancing so-called “diplomatic relations”, the DPP authorities have been spending Taiwan people’s hard-earned money to seek “dollar diplomacy” to advance the “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda. Such attempts not only undermine the real benefits of people in Taiwan but also breed corruption in relevant countries. We also urge the Giammattei administration not to selfishly succumb to the Taiwan authorities’ “dollar diplomacy”. The Guatemalan people are clear-eyed about who actually benefits from it. I would like to reiterate that recognizing the one-China principle is the right choice that echoes the trend of the world and advances national development and people’s interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347512.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230426_11066591.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 26, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Yesterday, a fire broke out at the Lianhua Food factory in Changhua, Taiwan, causing multiple casualties. We express deep condolences to the victims of the accident, and sincere sympathy to the injured compatriots and the families of the relevant personnel.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","In April 1993, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” Wang Daohan, Chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS), and Koo Chen-fu, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan, held the Wang-Koo Talks in Singapore. Over the past 30 years, the development of cross-Strait relations has had its ups and downs. Under the current complex and grim situation in the Taiwan…","The Wang-Koo Talks were the first high-level talks held by the two sides of the Strait in the name of authorized civil organizations since 1949, marking a historic and important step forward in the development of cross-Strait relations. The Wang-Koo Talks followed the historical trend of cross-Strait relations, opened the precedent of high-level cross-Strait contact, dialogue, and equal consultation, embodied the spirit of replacing confrontation with dialogue and promoting cooperation through consultation, demonstrated the important position of the \"1992 Consensus\" as the basis for cross-Strait consultation, and showed that Chinese on both sides of the Strait are fully capable and wise enough to solve their own problems. The Wang-Koo Talks and their outcomes have powerfully promoted the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe Wang-Koo Talks and the twisting and turning course of cross-Strait relations since then show that opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" are the key to maintaining the right direction and good momentum of peaceful cross-Strait development. Under the current circumstances of cross-Strait relations, drawing on the historical experience and useful lessons of the Wang-Koo Talks, firmly safeguarding the political foundation of the \"1992 Consensus,\" adhering to the correct direction of peaceful cross-Strait development, and striving to enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and jointly creating the future of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, is the best commemoration of the Wang-Koo Talks.\nOn April 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, and the Straits Exchange Foundation will hold a symposium in Beijing commemorating the 30th anniversary of the Wang-Koo Talks. We welcome everyone to follow and report on it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530260.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, junior high school biology textbooks on the island used “tudou” (potato) to refer to “malingshu” (potato), and Taiwan green-camp politicians said that “tudou” is mainland terminology that needs to be corrected. This has sparked online discussion. How does the spokesperson view this?","The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities are purely political maneuvering. Compatriots on both sides speak the same language and use the same characters, but because of differences in living environments and customary expressions, there are differences in how some items are called. For example, different places have different names for potatoes and 马铃薯 (ma lingshu), which is a natural phenomenon. As cross-Strait exchanges are gradually restored, expanded and deepened, people on both sides are increasingly able to understand each other’s language habits, and increasingly able to understand and comprehend one another, learning from and drawing on each other.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报海外版记者","Recently, the Ministry of Commerce announced a trade barrier investigation into the trade restriction measures that the Taiwan region has imposed on the mainland. Some public opinion on the island holds that the timing of the mainland's announcement of the investigation is 'sensitive.' The DPP authorities said the mainland's move is 'linking politics with trade' and that 'excessive politicization is not conducive…","It is an objective fact that the Taiwan authorities have long unilaterally imposed extensive restrictions on imports of mainland products. Based on the WTO non-discrimination principle and relevant mainland regulations, the Ministry of Commerce has launched a trade barrier investigation into Taiwan's trade restriction measures against the mainland, which is entirely justified and reasonable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530258.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The General Administration of Customs announced that in the first quarter of this year, total cross-Strait import and export trade fell 26.5% year on year. The latest data on the island show that Taiwan's exports in the first quarter fell 19.2% year on year. Analysts on the island believe that the US imposing a technology blockade on the mainland, and the DPP authorities cooperating with the US in the wrong…","We have noted the relevant data and the analysis and commentary from public opinion on the island.\nFacts have proven that, in order to safeguard its hegemony, the United States has hijacked normal international economic and trade cooperation, engaged in monopolistic suppression and technology blockades in high-tech fields, coerced some countries and regions into encircling and containing China's development, and artificially created “decoupling and supply chain severance.” This has seriously affected the stability of global industrial and supply chains, including cross-Strait trade. Yet the DPP authorities, out of their political nature of “relying on the US to seek independence,” and in pursuit of their own private interests, are willing to sacrifice Taiwan's economic prospects and smash the “rice bowls” of the Taiwan public. On the one hand, they restrict and suppress cross-Strait economic and trade relations and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, placing many obstacles to normal cross-Strait trade and personnel exchanges. On the other hand, they cling to and cooperate with U.S. and Western anti-China forces, handing over the island's core advantageous industries and causing a large outflow of Taiwan's technical talent and economic wealth. As a result, problems such as slow economic growth, declining exports, rising prices, and a widening wealth gap have become increasingly prominent on the island, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nIt should be pointed out that cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation is a driving force and opportunity for Taiwan's economic development. Facing an international economic environment full of uncertainty, only by resolutely opposing the decoupling of cross-Strait economies and the severing of industrial chains, and by further deepening cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, can Taiwan leverage the mainland's vast market, abundant resources, and complete industrial support to achieve better economic development, so that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses benefit more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530254.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","We noticed that the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee delegation recently visited the mainland for exchanges. How does this help promote cross-Strait sports exchanges?","In recent years, sports circles on both sides of the Strait have maintained close communication and coordinated cooperation, innovatively carrying out a series of rich and colorful exchange activities covering competitive sports, the sports industry, sports science, youth sports, and many other fields, promoting continuous new progress in cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation.\nAround major issues such as preparations for and participation in the Tokyo Olympic Games, the Beijing Winter Olympics, the Hangzhou Asian Games, and the Chengdu Universiade, the Olympic committees on both sides strengthened communication, coordinated positions, and mutually supported each other, jointly safeguarding the overall situation of cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation. At the request of the Taiwan sports community, we provided active support for Taiwan table tennis athletes to come to the mainland for training and competition and for preparations for the Tokyo Olympics, and provided maximum convenience for the Chinese Taipei delegation's preparations for the Beijing Winter Olympics, enabling compatriots on both sides to jointly participate in grand events and share the glory. Recently, at the invitation of the Chinese Olympic Committee, a delegation of 13 members from the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee came to Beijing to attend the 24th Cross-Strait Sports Exchange Symposium. Both sides reviewed cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation in 2021 and 2022, planned sports exchange activities for 2023, and conducted in-depth exchanges of views on current cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation and other issues of common concern. Both sides agreed that they would take the Hangzhou Asian Games as an opportunity to strengthen communication and cooperation and promote the normalization of cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation as soon as possible.\nThe 19th Asian Games, to be held in Hangzhou in September this year, is an important platform for sports circles on both sides of the Strait to share opportunities. At the request of the Taiwan sports community, relevant parties on the mainland successfully coordinated the inclusion of baseball as an official competition event at the Hangzhou Asian Games. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, recently met with a delegation led by Lin Hong-dao, President of the Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee, and said that the mainland, adhering to the concept of “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” will let Taiwan athletes experience the atmosphere of “a home court” at the Hangzhou Asian Games. He hoped that the delegations from both sides would strengthen communication, that athletes from both sides would unite and show mutual friendship, and strive for excellent results.\nIn this context, we would also like to further introduce the development of Taiwan sports personnel on the mainland.\nThe General Administration of Sport, together with relevant departments, has gradually provided equal treatment and convenient conditions for Taiwan sports personnel to work, study, and exchange on the mainland. In July 2021, the General Administration of Sport issued the Notice on Matters Related to Granting Athlete Technical Rank Titles to Athletes from the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions and Taiwan Region, formally including outstanding Taiwan athletes in the athlete development and support system. Five Taiwan athletes, including Lee Hsuan-tse, were awarded athlete technical rank titles, covering baseball, basketball, swimming, water polo, and other events. Taiwan basketball players such as Chen Ying-chun performed outstandingly in CBA games, setting a good example that encourages Taiwan youth to devote themselves to the mainland's sports undertakings and promotes the integrated development of sports across the Strait. In February this year, the General Administration of Sport issued a notice requiring relevant departments to add the Taiwan Compatriot Permit for Travel to the Mainland and the Taiwan Residence Permit to the document type options in the ticket reservation systems and organizing committee registration (sign-up) systems for various sports events and activities held on the mainland, providing convenience for Taiwan compatriots participating in sports activities on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, the State Forestry and Grassland Administration announced the first batch of 2023 plant variety rights grants, in which the new variety “Bixi (bì xì)” bred by a Taiwan resident was granted rights. Could the spokesperson please introduce the relevant situation?","April 20 to 26 is National Intellectual Property Publicity Week. Taking this opportunity, I would like to introduce the protection of intellectual property related to Taiwan. We have long attached great importance to protecting the intellectual property rights of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, including patents, trademarks, copyrights, and plant variety rights. We strictly crack down on infringement and piracy and support Taiwan compatriots in taking the qualification examination for patent attorneys and practicing the profession. Over the past decade, relevant authorities have accepted more than 180,000 patent applications and more than 160,000 trademark applications from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and granted 40 plant variety rights. The plant variety right for the Bougainvillea variety “Bixi,” which the National Forestry and Grassland Administration granted for the first time to a Taiwan resident and which you mentioned, is one of them. In addition, nearly 2,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots have registered for the patent attorney qualification examination, and 469 have passed. We will continue to protect the lawful rights and interests in intellectual property of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in accordance with the law, support cross-Strait economic, scientific, and technological exchanges and cooperation as well as the movement of professional and technical personnel, and provide better legal guarantees for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","We noticed that the Straits Forum Organizing Committee recently issued an announcement soliciting theme songs for the Straits Forum. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Since 2009, the Straits Forum has successfully held 14 sessions. It has consistently adhered to its positioning of being “civilian, grassroots, and broadly based,” focusing on promoting cross-Strait exchanges at the grassroots level. It has become the cross-Strait civil exchange platform with the largest number of participating institutions, the largest scale of activities, and the broadest scope of involvement. This year we will hold the 15th Straits Forum, and preparations are progressing in an orderly manner. At this important juncture of reviewing the past and opening a new chapter, the Straits Forum Organizing Committee, through public solicitation and commissioned creation, is soliciting theme songs for the Straits Forum from across the internet from April 18 to May 18. The submission requirements, application plan and other specific details have been published on the official website of the Straits Forum (http://www.taiwan.cn/hxlt/). We sincerely welcome and look forward to enthusiastic participation from people of all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, who are invited to contribute their talents, create and perform outstanding musical works, and stir emotional resonance among compatriots on both sides.\nMany Taiwan compatriots have expressed a strong wish to attend the 15th Straits Forum. In response to these expectations, this year the Forum's Organizing Committee will reopen online registration, so that a broad range of Taiwan compatriots will have the opportunity to visit the mainland, see for themselves, reconnect family ties, discuss cooperation, seek development, and talk about integration. For the specific timing and detailed information on online registration, please pay attention to the official website of the Straits Forum (http://www.taiwan.cn/hxlt/). We welcome broad participation from Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2023 “One Family of Chinese Nation” — Guangxi Cross-Strait Ethnic Groups Celebrate the “Zhuang Ethnic March Third” event was recently successfully held in Guangxi. Please introduce the relevant information.","The 2023 “Chinese One Family” Guangxi-Taiwan Ethnic Groups Celebrate the Zhuang “March Third” Festival activities were held in Guangxi from April 18 to 25. They were the first large-scale cross-Strait ethnic minority exchange event this year, and also the first large-scale in-person gathering of cross-Strait ethnic minority compatriots in three years, and were warmly welcomed by ethnic compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nMore than 100 Taiwan indigenous compatriots from 9 ethnic groups in 7 counties and cities, including Taitung and Hualien in Taiwan, came to Guangxi and celebrated the festival together with more than 40,000 local people of various ethnic groups in 5 prefecture-level cities. The song melody of “We Are All One Family” ran through the entire event, showcasing the moving scenes of cross-Strait compatriots of all ethnic groups celebrating the festival together and sharing family bonds.\nThe successful holding of this event fully demonstrates that peace and development, and exchanges and cooperation, are the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We will continue to support relevant localities in actively exploring new paths for exchanges between ethnic minority compatriots on both sides of the Strait, create better conditions and provide more support for Taiwan indigenous compatriots to share the development opportunities of the mainland and enjoy the achievements of the mainland’s development, and jointly promote the unity and prosperity of the big family of the Chinese nation and the development and progress of Taiwan indigenous compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The head of Taiwan’s economic authorities said that when the two sides joined the WTO, there were no consultations involving trade in related goods. Why has the mainland suddenly proposed a trade barrier investigation against Taiwan?","Both sides of the Strait are WTO members. Under WTO rules, after Taiwan joined the WTO in 2002 under the name “Separate Customs Territory of Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu,” it should have lifted relevant trade restrictions against the mainland. This has been mentioned in the Secretariat’s reports in each WTO trade policy review of Taiwan, and the mainland has expressed concern in its statements, urging Taiwan to fulfill its WTO commitments and amend non-compliant measures. However, the Taiwan authorities still unilaterally restrict more than 2,400 mainland products from being imported.\nRecently, the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Foodstuffs, Native Produce and Animal By-Products, the China Chamber of Commerce of Metals, Minerals & Chemicals Importers & Exporters, and the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Textiles submitted an investigation request to the Ministry of Commerce. In accordance with the WTO principle of non-discrimination and relevant mainland regulations, the Ministry of Commerce has decided to launch a trade barrier investigation into the trade restrictive measures that Taiwan imposes on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530256.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","After Lai Ching-te was nominated by the DPP to run in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election, he again declared that “Taiwan is in fact already a ‘sovereign independent state,’ and there is no need to separately declare ‘independence,’” that the two sides “are not subordinate to each other,” that “the vast majority of people oppose reunification,” that “Taiwan society does not have a unification-versus-independence…","Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and never will. Taiwan is not, and never will be, a “sovereign independent state.” Opposing “Taiwan independence” and supporting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the mainstream wish of the Taiwan people. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable, and “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and continue to collude with external forces to engage in provocations seeking “independence,” which is the root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. So-called “pragmatic ‘Taiwan independence’ workers,” continuing to disregard facts and distort right and wrong, covertly incite “hatred of China and resistance to China” and fool the Taiwan people. They will only push Taiwan into the perilous situation where war is grim and battle is dangerous.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530259.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","On April 25, the Supreme People's Procuratorate released the progress in handling the case of Yang Chih-yuan, a criminal suspect from the Taiwan region suspected of the crime of secession of the state. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On April 25, the Supreme People's Procuratorate released information that the case of Taiwan-region criminal suspect Yang Chih-yuan, suspected of the crime of secession of the state, had been concluded in investigation by the State Security Bureau of Wenzhou City and transferred to the Wenzhou City People's Procuratorate for review and prosecution. Recently, the Wenzhou City People's Procuratorate approved Yang Chih-yuan's arrest on suspicion of the crime of secession of the state. The case is still being further handled.\nState judicial organs have pursued criminal liability against “Taiwan independence” separatists in accordance with the law, further sounding the alarm for severely punishing “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Anyone who breaks the law will not escape the sanctions of national law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, Lai Ching-te has said, “The Taiwan Strait is wide enough to accommodate Taiwan and the mainland living and developing as ‘brother nations.’” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s response? Second, a Republican presidential candidate in the United States has claimed, “Let every family in Taiwan own a gun.” In addition, a so-called war game was conducted by a US House of Representatives…","On the first question: Both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Cross-Strait relations are absolutely not a relationship between countries, and of course not a relationship between “bang” (states). The nature of “Taiwan independence” has not changed. Merely playing word games and trying to dress oneself in the cloak of “goodwill” and “peace” will only cover up the truth. Persistently and stubbornly holding to the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance will only push Taiwan toward danger in the end and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the second question: Recently, the US side has constantly changed its tactics, hyping the “mainland threat theory.” The aim is to sow discord and confrontation across the Strait, sell arms to Taiwan, profit the US military-industrial complex, and prop up and cheer on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, while also pushing the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots into dangerous situations. Who is scheming to sacrifice Taiwan, profiting from it and gaining advantage, in order to ruin and harm Taiwan? We believe compatriots on both sides and the international community see this very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","The 76th World Health Assembly will be held in Geneva, Switzerland, in late May. The head of Taiwan’s health department said that he will lead a delegation there to expand exchanges with more neutral countries. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Regarding the issue of Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly, we have stated our position many times. The core is to adhere to the one-China principle. On the basis of the one-China principle, and against the backdrop of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, through cross-Strait consultations, from 2009 to 2016 the Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei.”\nAfter the DPP authorities took office, they stubbornly held to the “Taiwan independence” position and refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations and directly led to the disappearance of the political basis for the Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly. Now, on the eve of the World Health Assembly, they are seeking to free-ride on the meeting, which will only make them a laughingstock.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530253.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Taiwan media reported that at the recent G7 foreign ministers' meeting held in Japan, it falsely claimed “opposition to China's attempt to unilaterally change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait by force.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although cross-Strait reunification has not yet been fully achieved, the fact that both the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has not changed, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been and cannot be divided. This is the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, which is beyond dispute and must not be changed.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities openly promote the “two-state theory,” undermine the fact that both sides belong to one China, and collude with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the saboteurs of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The US and Western countries hype the issue of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and distort China's necessary actions to defend its national sovereignty and territorial integrity. In essence, this is an attempt to confuse public perception, interfere with China's advancement of the great cause of national reunification, and embolden the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. They are the instigators undermining the status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\nTo maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, we must firmly uphold the one-China principle. We will resolutely safeguard the one-China principle, solidly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and foreign interference, and unswervingly advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530252.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Wu Chao-hsieh, head of Taiwan's department for external affairs, recently accepted an interview with foreign media in which he played up the so-called 'military threat' from the mainland. He vowed that Taiwan will firmly commit to self-defense, strengthen its asymmetric strategy and seek international support, and that it will always be prepared to respond to possible attacks. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” stance, colluding with external forces to scheme for “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the destroyers of the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and the instigators of the tension and turmoil in the Strait. Now they put on a so-called “victim” pose and “complain to foreign powers.” Isn't that very ridiculous? We warn the DPP authorities: relying on foreign powers to enhance one's own standing harms Taiwan, and seeking “independence” by force will only hasten your own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","New Taipei City Mayor Hou Yu-ih recently spoke about cross-Strait relations, saying, “Both sides should reduce mutual misunderstanding and treat each other with dignity and equality. Only then can we move forward together.” What comment do you have?","Wanting peace and development, and wanting exchange and cooperation, is the mainstream public opinion on the island. The root of the current tension and turbulence in cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and continue to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. As long as both sides return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can be fundamentally safeguarded and promoted, and the Taiwan Strait can avoid falling into the perilous state of “war and danger.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","First question: This year marks the 30th anniversary of the Koo–Wang talks. Will the mainland continue to adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” to shelve disputes, seek equal consultation, promote mutual understanding and social integration? Second question: On the occasion of the 74th anniversary of the founding of the Navy, the mainland released the publicity film “Jiaolong Operation.” Does it carry a strong…","First question. The ‘1992 Consensus’ clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations. It is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the greatest common denominator for improving and developing cross-Strait relations. As we have just pointed out, the Wang-Koo talks and the tortuous development of cross-Strait relations since then show that opposing ‘Taiwan independence’ and upholding the ‘1992 Consensus’ are the key to maintaining the correct direction and good momentum of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations. Under the current situation in cross-Strait relations, we should draw on the historical experience and useful lessons of the Wang-Koo talks, firmly uphold the political foundation of the ‘1992 Consensus,’ adhere to the correct direction of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and strive to enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and guarding the country’s vast maritime frontier require a strong people’s navy. The DPP authorities and ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces, who attempt to collude with external forces to split the country, have no chance whatsoever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Taiwan media reported that about 25 US arms dealers will send representatives to Taiwan in early May to discuss cooperative production of drones and ammunition. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to Taiwan.\nU.S. arms dealers are accustomed to stirring up confrontation and conflict in order to profit from war, and the U.S. government is accustomed to providing protection for arms dealers. More than six years after the DPP authorities took office, they have colluded with the United States and squandered 22 billion U.S. dollars of Taiwan residents' hard-earned money on high-priced weapons from the United States, tying Taiwan compatriots to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coercing young people in Taiwan into serving as “cannon fodder.” This is by no means “protecting Taiwan”; it is “harming Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Fucha (Li Yanhe), editor-in-chief of Taiwan's “Eight Banners Culture” publishing house, has reportedly been arrested in Shanghai. What is the TAO's response?","It is understood that Li Yanhe, suspected of engaging in activities endangering national security, is under investigation by national security authorities. The relevant authorities will lawfully protect his various legitimate rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","The mainland recently announced a trade barrier investigation targeting Taiwan, which has put some pressure on Taiwanese enterprises and even raised concerns that ECFA could change. Recently, many Taiwanese civic groups have visited the mainland, expressing hope for peaceful cross-Strait exchanges and cooperative development. Is this contradictory? Does it raise concerns that it could 'accidentally harm' mutual…","First, it must be pointed out that you are raising two different matters; there is no so-called issue of “contradiction” or “collateral harm.”\nThe mainland side’s trade barrier investigation into the trade restrictive measures Taiwan imposes on the mainland is because the Taiwan authorities have for a long time unilaterally restricted the import of large quantities of mainland products, harming the interests of relevant mainland industries and enterprises, while also harming the interests of Taiwan consumers. Fair trade under the principle of non-discrimination between the two sides is more conducive to the healthy development of cross-strait trade, and to complementary advantages and common development of cross-strait industries and enterprises.\nAs for cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, the desire for peace and development, and for exchanges and cooperation, is the common voice of compatriots on both sides. We welcome and actively support industrial and commercial circles on both sides in strengthening exchanges and cooperation, and in playing a more active role in promoting cross-strait economic exchanges and cooperation and deepening cross-strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, Xiamen Port opened the first “Great Three Links” sea express route for cross-border e-commerce exports to Taiwan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To serve the rapidly growing demand for cross-border e-commerce exports to Taiwan, on April 19, Xiamen Port opened its first cross-border e-commerce Big Three Links sea express route. The inaugural sailing of this route carried 60 standard containers, 17,000 shipments, and cross-border e-commerce export goods worth 22.9 million yuan, departing from Xiamen Haitian Terminal and calling at Taipei Port on the morning of the 20th. Currently, this route operates 2 sailings per week.\nWith the opening of the first cross-border e-commerce Big Three Links sea express route from Xiamen Port for exports to Taiwan, quality mainland products purchased through e-commerce platforms can be delivered more quickly and conveniently to consumers in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","April 23 is World Book Day. A reporter recently visited bookstores in Taipei and found bookshelves filled with books from the mainland, many of which have become bestsellers. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share blood ties and a connected culture. Exchanging cultural products such as books and films is an important way to enhance mutual understanding and friendship. Through the joint efforts of publishing circles on both sides and relevant parties, cross-Strait publishing exchanges have progressed from indirect to direct, from one-way to two-way, and from copyright trade and co-publishing to resource integration and complementary advantages, achieving positive progress. Taiwan publishing and distribution institutions have carefully selected books from the mainland from the perspective of readers on the island to meet their reading needs. We support this and are willing to create more conditions and provide more assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Industry operators on the island worry that the mainland's trade barrier investigation against Taiwan will affect the early harvest list of the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA), and this has also raised doubts among all sectors about whether ECFA should be kept or abolished. May I ask whether the mainland will discontinue the implementation of ECFA?","In June 2010, building on the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait. ECFA has brought tangible benefits to relevant enterprises and the public on the island, including the vast number of small and medium-sized enterprises and fishermen and farmers. ECFA is a special arrangement reached to promote the normalization, institutionalization and liberalization of cross-Strait economic relations. However, for some time, the DPP authorities have not only failed to take practical measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but have increasingly escalated, using various pretexts and means to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This only shrinks the room for development of Taiwan's economy and directly harms the immediate interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202304/t20230426_12530255.htm"],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that the US will send 200 military personnel to Taiwan to train the Taiwan military and “reorganize and prepare for war.” What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will open their eyes wide and firmly oppose the conduct of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces colluding with external forces to ruin and harm Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-04-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Regarding the resumption of cross-Strait tourism, the mainland recently stated that the DPP still bans Taiwan tour groups from going to the mainland, while the Mainland Affairs Council said it is 'waiting for the mainland to open tourism to Taiwan.' Currently, the resumption of cross-Strait tourism seems to have reached a stalemate. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? Are there any relevant plans recently?","Over the past three years, the DPP authorities have adopted a series of restrictive measures, including prohibiting mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, unilaterally closing the “mini three links,” widely canceling cross-Strait direct flight points, and prohibiting Taiwan travel agencies from conducting tourism business to the mainland. These measures have blocked the path of cross-Strait tourism development. Since the beginning of this year, we have adopted a series of measures to promote convenient travel of people across the Strait, which have been affirmed and welcomed by compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities were forced to loosen their stance somewhat on the “mini three links” and on resuming some cross-Strait direct flight points, but this is still far from enough. Compatriots on both sides hope to normalize cross-Strait personnel exchanges as soon as possible and to make exchanges in all fields routine. The DPP authorities should follow the wishes of the public, completely remove artificial obstacles, and take concrete measures to restore two-way exchanges and normal travel across the Strait.\nThe press conference is over. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202304/t20230426_12530249.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-04-27","Mao Ning","Yonhap News Agency","The ROK and US leaders reiterated in a Joint Statement released after their talks “the importance of preserving peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait”. How does China comment on this?","We have noted what was said about Taiwan in the US-ROK Joint Statement and the ROK leader’s interview. I would like to stress that the Taiwan question is purely an internal affair at the core of China’s core interests. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese that brooks no interference from anyone. The real status quo of the Taiwan question is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been split. It is the “Taiwan independence” separatists seeking to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” and the external forces interfering in the situation by fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle who are responsible for undermining the status quo. We urge the US and the ROK to see the true nature of the Taiwan question, follow the one-China principle, be prudent when it comes to the Taiwan question, and avoid going further down the wrong and dangerous path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347513.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202304/t20230427_11067709.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-04-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, several U.S. defense companies will send a delegation to Taiwan in early May to discuss issues such as jointly producing drones and ammunition. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted the relevant reports and express serious concern. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The so-called “military-industrial complex” in the US has always been keen to peddle arms around the world, export war and chaos, and seek exorbitant profits. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' practice of inviting the wolf into the house is despicable and will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nIt must be emphasized that no person or force can shake our determination and will to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and none can block the historical process of China's inevitable reunification. We strongly urge the US side to fully recognize the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question and the complexity and severity of the current situation in the Taiwan Strait, to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately, to stop interfering in the Taiwan question, and to stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop US-Taiwan military ties. The Chinese People's Liberation Army always keeps a close watch on the situation in the Taiwan Strait and remains highly vigilant at all times. It will take necessary measures in accordance with law to resolutely counter any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.chinanews.com.cn/gn/2023/04-27/9998200.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-05-05","Mao Ning","CCTV","A delegation of US defense contractors attended the Taiwan-US Defense Industry Forum on May 3. Head of the delegation Steven Rudder, who was in charge of the US Marines operations in the Pacific, said in his speech that US defense contractors “want to be part of the self-defense capabilities of Taiwan” to increase its deterrence so that “we may never have to go to war”. What’s your comment?","US arms sales to the Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. China firmly opposes them.\nLately the US and the Taiwan authorities have been stepping up military collusion. A delegation of 25 US arms dealers swarmed to the island and held with the DPP authorities the “defense forum”. It is further proof that the US is turning Taiwan into a “powder keg”, which only spells trouble for our Taiwan compatriots. And they have made clear their position. As the “forum” was being held, people from all walks of life gathered nearby to protest the warmongers peddling conflict, oppose those soliciting US support for independence and opening the door to the devil, call on young people in Taiwan to refuse to be enlisted, and voice support for one China on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and cross-Strait peace. The DPP authorities need to hear these voices and immediately stop trading our Taiwan compatriots’ fundamental interests for selfish gains.\nWe once again urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, and stop creating factors that could cause tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese side will take strong and resolute measures to firmly defend our sovereignty and security interests. Any external forces that interfere in China’s internal affairs and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait shall bear the consequences and pay for their erroneous acts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347516.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230505_11070975.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-08","Wang Wenbin","China News Service","A recent report about Taiwan by the Swiss government noted that Switzerland follows the one-China policy but believes that Taiwan “has the characteristics of a state” and that “the recognition of Taiwan as a state is a decision that is left to the free discretion of each state.” The Swiss National Council has adopted a motion to tighten cooperation with Taiwan’s “legislature” and deepen economic and political…","China deplores and firmly opposes the wrongful words and actions of Switzerland.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests. There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a universally recognized norm governing international relations. It is a component of the post-war international order and shall not be distorted or misrepresented. Switzerland was one of the first countries to recognize and establish diplomatic ties with the PRC. The one-China principle is the most important political cornerstone for the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Switzerland and what has underpinned the smooth exchange and cooperation between the two countries over the past 70-plus years.\nWe urge the Swiss side to uphold its political commitment to the one-China policy, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, stop conniving at or supporting any “Taiwan independence” activities and work with China to maintain the sound momentum of growth of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347517.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230508_11073306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-08","Wang Wenbin","AFP","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang said in a meeting with US Ambassador Nicholas Burns this morning that a series of erroneous words and actions by the US side have undercut the hard-won positive momentum in bilateral relations. Could you elaborate on what specific words and actions he was referring to?","We have released a readout on State Councilor Qin Gang’s meeting with Ambassador Burns. You can find answers to your question in that readout. Let me go over that part for you.\nState Councilor Qin Gang said that the US needs to form a correct perception of China, return to rationality, get the basis right for China-US relations just like putting the first button on a shirt right, and succeed together. The US cannot talk about the need for communication on the one hand and yet keep suppressing and containing China on the other. The US cannot say one thing but do the opposite and needs to respect China’s red lines. The US needs to stop undermining China’s sovereignty, security and development interests, correctly handle the Taiwan question in particular, stop hollowing out the one-China principle, and stop supporting or conniving at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The US needs to handle unexpected and isolated incidents in bilateral relations in a calm, professional and pragmatic manner to avoid dealing more blows to China-US relations. The US needs to seek dialogue and cooperation on the basis of mutual respect, mutual benefit and reciprocity. We hope that Ambassador Burns will be able to see, listen, interact and think more here in China, and serve as a bridge between China and the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347517.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230508_11073306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-08","Wang Wenbin","Yonhap News Agency","Chinese experts have said through some Chinese media that if the ROK and Japan do not correct their wrong positions on the Taiwan question, it will be difficult to resume the ROK-China-Japan summit. What is China’s comment on this? Has China’s position on the resumption of the summit changed?","China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We hope all parties will abide by the one-China principle. As close neighbors, China, Japan and the ROK have every reason to work together to maintain the political foundation of bilateral relations and stay committed to the steady, sound and sustainable growth of trilateral cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347517.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230508_11073306.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-10","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Yesterday, Germany’s Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock urged Beijing to take a clear stance against Russian aggression in Ukraine. These comments were on the same day that an AFP journalist tragically lost his life during a rocket fire in Donetsk. Does the Chinese foreign ministry have any reaction?","You mentioned the remarks of the German Foreign Minister during State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang’s visit to Germany. I would like to take this opportunity to share some details about the visit.\nOn May 9 local time, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang held talks and jointly met the press with German Foreign Minister Annalena Baerbock in Berlin. The main purpose of this visit is to prepare for the upcoming seventh round of China-Germany intergovernmental consultation.\nState Councilor Qin noted that China and Germany are both major countries with global influence and need to step up dialogue and cooperation in a rapidly changing and turbulent world. The two sides need to make good preparations for the seventh round of China-Germany intergovernmental consultation and draw up a comprehensive plan for practical cooperation going forward. China and Germany need to follow the right path, stand together against a new Cold War, decoupling and severing of supply chains, and be a source of confidence and strength for world peace and prosperity. China is a key partner for Europe in the face of risks and challenges. We welcome Europe to share China’s market opportunities and development dividends and hope to see the mutual success of Chinese modernization and European integration.\nState Councilor Qin noted that while China appreciates Germany and the EU’s statements of not aiming for decoupling from China, China is, however, concerned about what the EU said about “de-risking”. What China brings to the world are opportunities, cooperation, stability and reassurance, not crises, confrontation, turmoil or risks. To shut out China in the name of “de-risking” is to throw away opportunities, cooperation, stability and development. It is essential that China, Germany and the EU all abide by international trade rules and honor the spirit of contract, stay open to each other, refrain from politicizing normal economic, trade and investment cooperation and do not interfere in market mechanisms.\nState Councilor Qin stressed that Taiwan’s return to China is an inherent component of the post-war international order. Anyone who truly hopes for cross-Strait peace and stability and upholds the international order needs to adhere to the one-China principle and oppose any act of “Taiwan independence”.\nChina and Germany agreed to lay a solid ground for the seventh round of China-Germany intergovernmental consultation and make a comprehensive plan for practical cooperation in various fields. The two sides agreed to step up coordination in multilateral fields and strengthen cooperation on COP28 and biodiversity.\nChina’s position on the Ukraine crisis is consistent and clear. As State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang made clear during his visit to Germany, the Ukraine issue is highly complex. An over simplified or emotionally driven approach clearly would not be the right way forward. The only viable approach is to stay calm and rational and create conditions for a political settlement. China is neither the one that created the conflict nor a party to it. We advocate peace and promote talks for peace. We hope that Germany will play a leading role and offer concrete proposals for building a balanced, effective and durable European security architecture.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347519.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230510_11074604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-10","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken issued a statement on May 9 saying that the US strongly encourages the WHO to invite Taiwan to participate as an observer at this year’s World Health Assembly (WHA) meeting. Taiwan has participated as an observer in previous WHA meetings. The US will continue to advocate for Taiwan’s return as an observer at the WHA and participation throughout the UN system. It is in line…","China firmly opposes the US statement.\nThere is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is an important principle affirmed in the UNGA Resolution 2758 and the WHA Resolution 25.1. With the DPP authorities refusing to recognize the 1992 Consensus that embodies the one-China principle and headstrong on “Taiwan independence”, the political foundation for cross-Strait consultation has been thrown into jeopardy, and the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. The US statement is misguided and misleading. It is intended to connive at and support separatist acts for “Taiwan independence”.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests. It is the number one red line that must not be crossed between China and the US. We once again urge the US to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, observe international law and the basic norms governing international relations, act on the US leader’s assurances of not supporting “Taiwan independence” and not supporting “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop hyping up issues related to Taiwan using the WHA. The one-China principle has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. This is not to be denied, nor can it be held back. Any attempt of playing the Taiwan card and using Taiwan to contain China will be rejected by the international community and not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347519.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230510_11074604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-11","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","We noted that State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang visited the site of the Potsdam Conference during his visit to Germany. What is the consideration behind this specific arrangement?","On May 10 local time, State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang visited the site of the Potsdam Conference in Berlin and delivered remarks.\nState Councilor Qin noted that the Potsdam Conference in 1945 played an important role in establishing the post-World War II international order and is of special historical significance to the Chinese people. The Potsdam Proclamation issued after the meeting reaffirmed the terms of the Cairo Declaration, which states that all the territories Japan has stolen from China, such as Taiwan, shall be restored to China. This is a major outcome of the World Anti-Fascist War that was won after 35 million Chinese soldiers and civilians were either killed or wounded during that war.\nToday, the US claims itself to be a champion of the “rules-based international order”, while ditching the Potsdam Proclamation it drafted, supporting and conniving at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, undermining the post-war international order and China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Chinese people will not accept this.\nIf there is any consideration for State Councilor Qin’s visit to the site, I would say that it is about reminding the world of the need to remember the lessons of history — that the post-war international order must be preserved and international fairness and justice must be upheld. To engage in “Taiwan independence” separatism, challenge international justice and order and try to reverse the trend of history will lead nowhere. China’s national reunification must and will be realized.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347520.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230511_11075423.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-12","Wang Wenbin","AFP","According to official reports, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi and US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan held talks for over eight hours earlier this week, but the two sides only issued two short readouts. I have two questions. First, does this mean that the two sides failed to reach any agreement on…","We’ve put out a readout on this. On May 10 and 11 local time, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi and US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan met in Vienna, Austria. The two sides held candid, in-depth, substantive and constructive discussions on ways to remove obstacles in China-US relations and stabilize the relationship from deterioration. Director Wang fully elaborated on China’s serious position on the Taiwan question. The two sides also exchanged views on the situation in the Asia-Pacific region, Ukraine and other international and regional issues of mutual interest. Both sides agreed to continue to make good use of this channel of strategic communication.\nXinhua News Agency: China announced the visit of Eritrean President Isaias Afwerki. Could you share with us the program and China’s expectations for the visit? How does China view the current China-Eritrea relations?\nEritrea is an important country in the Horn of Africa. China and Eritrea enjoy long-standing friendship. In 2022, President Xi Jinping and President Isaias Afwerki agreed to elevate our bilateral relations to a strategic partnership. This year marks the 30th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Eritrea. The two countries have deepened political mutual trust, achieved fruitful outcomes in practical cooperation and maintained close communication and coordination in international and regional affairs.\nDuring President Isaias Afwerki’s visit, President Xi Jinping will hold a welcome ceremony and banquet for him, and the two heads of state will hold talks. Premier Li Qiang will meet with President Isaias Afwerki. We believe that President Isaias Afwerki’s visit will give a new boost to the all-round, in-depth growth of China-Eritrea relations and further advance our friendly cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347521.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230512_11076477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-12","Wang Wenbin","","法新社记者：据官方报道，中共中央政治局委员、中央外事工作委员会办公室主任王毅与美国总统国家安全事务助理沙利文本周进行了8个多小时的会晤，但是双方只发表了两份简短声明。我有两个问题：第一，这是否表明双方未能就任何关键议题达成一致？第二，双方是否讨论过在即将举行的七国集团峰会期间举行更高级别会晤的可能性？","","","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230512_11076477.shtml","",0,3,0,""],[0,"2023-05-16","Wang Wenbin","CRI","According to reports, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida called out China and Russia in an interview on May 15, saying that unilateral changes to the status quo with might won’t be allowed and that the G7 Hiroshima Summit will send out a strong message on this to the international community. What’s your comment?","As the host of the upcoming G7 Summit, Japan has been stoking and creating bloc confrontation, which undermines the interests of the region. China firmly opposes it.\nWhat Japan has done – referring to the same narrative over and over again and trying to smear its neighbors – can only be explained by its need to deflect attention to its own and actual attempt to unilaterally change the status quo. In international legal instruments such as the Potsdam Proclamation and the Cairo Declaration which constitute the legal basis of the post-war international order, it is stated that Taiwan’s return to China is an important component of the post-WWII international order. However, some in Japan have been doing all they can to whitewash the history of aggression, honor the militarists and justify their crimes. They even claim that “Any contingency for Taiwan is a contingency for Japan”. Isn’t this the definition of “changing the status quo”?\nIf Japan is truly against “unilateral change to the status quo”, one thing it can do is to stop those within Japan trying to turn back the wheel of history, draw serious lessons from the history of Japan’s militarist aggression, recommit itself to the post-war international order and adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347523.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230516_11078417.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-05-16","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that, according to sources, the U.S. government plans to provide Taiwan with $500 million in weapons assistance through the “Presidential Drawdown Authority.” In addition, the U.S. recently sent more than 100 military personnel to Taiwan to help train Taiwan's military, to learn firsthand the strengths and weaknesses of Taiwan's military training model and to offer suggestions. What comments does…","For some time now, the US side has continuously strengthened its military collusion with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, enhanced military ties between the two sides, and upgraded substantive relations. This shakes the foundation of China-US relations and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is a very wrong and dangerous move. China is strongly dissatisfied, firmly opposes it, and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. The three principles of “severing diplomatic relations, abrogating treaties, and withdrawing troops” are the preconditions for the establishment of China-US diplomatic relations, and turning back the clock of history is absolutely not permitted. We solemnly warn the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to put into practice its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and to stop any form of US-Taiwan military collusion. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence” or “seek independence by force” is a dead end.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army continues to strengthen training and combat readiness, resolutely crushes any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and foreign interference, and resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16224888.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-05-17","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Former UK Prime Minister Liz Truss is visiting Taiwan today. She indicated before the trip that she would use it as an opportunity to urge the current Sunak government to treat China as a strategic threat. What is the foreign ministry’s comment on the visit?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. For a British political has-been, using Taiwan to grab attention is all about serving selfish political interests. I noticed that Truss’s trip drew fierce criticism across the UK, who say that this trip is “performative” and the serially irresponsible MP for South West Norfolk is doing her country another disservice. The DPP authorities are squandering Taiwan taxpayer money to ingratiate themselves with “the shortest-serving prime minister” in UK history. This is not an act of “love” for Taiwan. They are selling Taiwan away. Such attempts to pursue independence and make provocations with external forces will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347524.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230517_11078969.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The 2023 Taiwan Work Conference was recently held in Beijing. Please introduce the overall considerations the meeting set out regarding the situation and tasks facing Taiwan work, and how to promote the development of cross-Strait relations going forward.","The 2023 Cross-Strait Work Conference was held in Beijing on May 9 and 10. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the conference and delivered a speech. The conference fully affirmed the achievements made in cross-Strait work over the past decade of the new era, deeply analyzed the situation across the Taiwan Strait at present and for a period to come, and put forward clear requirements for doing a good job in cross-Strait work this year.\nThe conference stressed that the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era constitutes an important component of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era. It enriches and develops the theory of national reunification and the policies and principles on Taiwan, and answers the epochal question of how to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations in the new era and unite Taiwan compatriots in working together to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the reunification of the motherland. It is the fundamental guideline and action plan for doing Taiwan work in the new era. We must implement it completely, accurately and comprehensively, firmly grasp the leadership and initiative in cross-Strait relations, and unswervingly advance the process of national reunification.\nAt present, the situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, because “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external interference forces are stirring up trouble and provoking confrontation. In accordance with the arrangements and requirements of the conference, we will: take Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era as our guide; fully implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China; thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work; adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations; uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and continuously deepen integrated development across the Strait; gradually restore and expand cross-Strait exchanges, make friends with people from all walks of life in Taiwan, and promote heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides; resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity; strengthen the Party's comprehensive leadership over Taiwan work, conduct in-depth investigation and research, and promote high-quality development of Taiwan work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535084.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","新华社记者","As “5·20” approaches, may I ask what the spokesperson’s evaluation is of the DPP authorities’ performance on cross-Strait relations in the seven years since they took office, and what the spokesperson expects for the development of cross-Strait relations in the coming period?","Since May 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to accept the one-China principle, distorted and denied the ‘1992 Consensus,’ stubbornly maintained the separatist stance of ‘Taiwan independence,’ intensified collusion with external forces, and continuously carried out provocations to seek ‘independence.’ They have created cross-Strait confrontation and obstructed and undermined cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, causing cross-Strait relations to remain persistently in tension and turmoil. Their actions undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and are increasingly pushing Taiwan into an abyss of disaster.\nPeace and development, exchange and cooperation, are the common voice of compatriots on both sides and conform to their common interests. ‘Taiwan independence’ is as incompatible with peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as fire and water, and it runs counter to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides must join hands and work together, resolutely oppose ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist activities and external interference, and jointly promote the development of cross-Strait relations in the right direction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535083.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中新社记者","During the 2022 Taiwan “Nine-in-One” local elections, many Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots on the mainland were unable to return to Taiwan for two years due to the pandemic, and their household registrations in Taiwan were removed, depriving them of their voting rights. At present, cross-Strait exchanges are gradually being restored, but the DPP authorities still have many unreasonable restrictions…","We have noted reports in the Taiwan media and questions raised by all sectors of society on the island. In order to gain the narrow interests of their own party, the DPP authorities have not hesitated to politically manipulate related issues, directly harming the vital interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots who do business, study and live on the mainland. The DPP authorities should heed public opinion, resolve the relevant issues, remove all kinds of unreasonable obstacles, restore the original cross-Strait passenger routes as soon as possible, normalize personnel exchanges across the Strait, and provide Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots on the mainland with a convenient route home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535068.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","人民日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed that the biggest challenge facing Taiwan is the mainland's “military threat,” and that if one accepts the “1992 Consensus” and the one-China principle, it would be equivalent to abandoning “Taiwan sovereignty,” and the peace thus obtained would not be truly lasting. What is your comment?","Those remarks disregard facts and are logically confused, once again exposing the absurdity of the “Taiwan independence” narrative. Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country, so where does the notion of “sovereignty” come from? The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Denying this foundation and attempting to change the status quo in which the mainland and Taiwan belong to the same China will only undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait and plunge cross-Strait relations into turmoil. “Taiwan independence” provocations are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest threat to the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and will ultimately bring only profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535074.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","人民政协报记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed that Taiwan must raise its “self-defense capabilities” and cooperate with the “democratic world camp,” and seek to use so-called “war preparations to avoid war and achieve peace.” What comment do you have?","This further confirms that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their provocations in pursuit of “independence” are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Let me ask: if there were no provocation, why would there be a need to “prepare for war”? The best way to “avoid war” is to abandon the “Taiwan independence” position and take the path of peaceful development. Inviting external forces to embolden themselves, creating cross-Strait confrontation, and even serving as anti-China chess pieces for foreigners will only lead Taiwan step by step toward the risk of war and inflict profound disaster on the people of Taiwan. We advise them not to continue deceiving and misleading the Taiwan public, and not to overestimate themselves and court their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535069.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建东南卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that the mainland deliberately raised the “threat” to Taiwan through military exercises, affecting stability and peace in the “Indo-Pacific region.” What is your comment?","This is a complete reversal of black and white, and of cause and effect. It is precisely the DPP authorities who stubbornly adhere to the 'Taiwan independence' separatist position, who continuously collude with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at 'independence,' and who keep escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. They are the real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The military exercises and drills carried out by the People's Liberation Army are a legitimate and just response to provocations, undertaken to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535077.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中国台湾网记者","Terry Gou recently issued a 'Peace Declaration' in Kinmen, advocating that, on the basis of the principle of 'one China, each side with its own interpretation,' one should stand firm on one's position and re-launch negotiations with the mainland. The DPP authorities expressed skepticism and opposition, saying that launching a 'grand negotiation' is fundamentally a 'grand fantasy.' What is your comment on this?","The root cause of the current tense and volatile state of cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and continue to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. Peace, not war; development, not decline; exchange, not isolation; cooperation, not closure: this is the mainstream public opinion on the island. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. On this basis, we are willing to work together with people from all walks of life on the island and with Taiwan compatriots to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nResuming cross-Strait negotiations on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is not a fantasy; it is a feasible path in reality. It is the DPP authorities, who stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” position, keep provoking with schemes to seek “independence,” and even delude themselves into thinking they can succeed, that are living in a full-fledged fantasy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Hou Yu-ih recently said that he opposes “Taiwan independence” and does not agree with “one country, two systems.” What is your comment?","\"Taiwan independence\" harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. It is a dead end that cannot be traversed. Only by eliminating the root of \"Taiwan independence\" can there be peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and can Taiwan compatriots live and work in peace and contentment. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to unification, and even less an excuse for separation. We adhere to the basic policy of \"peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,\" precisely to take into account Taiwan's actual circumstances and to safeguard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. On the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to work together with people from all sectors on the island and with broad Taiwan compatriots to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, a U.S. congressman again threatened that if conflict breaks out across the Taiwan Strait, TSMC would be blown up. The DPP authorities, in coordination, have stirred up a “whole-of-society defense” atmosphere; in the “Han Kuang exercise,” they carried out so-called “hiding soldiers among the people” and, for the first time, drafted women to take part in reservist call-up training. These moves have…","Having heard these remarks, one wonders what those die-hard supporters of the \"Guardian Mountain\" would think, and how the Green camp politicians who lean on foreigners to gain weight would feel.\nFrom \"blowing up TSMC\" to \"destroying Taiwan's infrastructure,\" U.S. politicians have repeatedly made remarks about \"destroying Taiwan,\" fully exposing that U.S. anti-China forces, under the guise of \"supporting Taiwan,\" are actually engaged in the business of \"destroying Taiwan.\" Their evil intentions, which go to any lengths for their own interests, are plain to see. As netizens on the island have said, \"The one who most wants to destroy Taiwan is the United States.\" Facts prove that the United States is playing the \"Taiwan card\" and raising tensions across the Taiwan Strait for the purpose of \"containing China through Taiwan.\" Once Taiwan's utility has been squeezed dry, the \"chess piece\" will become a \"discarded piece.\"\nThe DPP authorities are making every effort to hitch themselves to and cooperate with external forces in hyping up the so-called \"mainland threat.\" This is to continue deceiving Taiwan's people for the sake of one party's interests and to manipulate \"anti-China and resist-China\" as a pretext, and to fantasize about colluding with external forces to \"seek independence through force\" as a pretext. If this is allowed to continue, it will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan and push Taiwan's people into the abyss of catastrophe.\nWe believe that more and more compatriots in Taiwan have clearly recognized that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end and that foreign forces cannot be relied upon. The DPP's so-called \"resisting China\" cannot \"protect Taiwan,\" \"relying on the U.S.\" will only accelerate \"harming Taiwan,\" and \"seeking independence through force\" has no way out at all. We hope that all sectors of Taiwan society and compatriots across Taiwan will join us in jointly promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and building a peaceful home where compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live in tranquility. Only this can bring real and tangible benefits and well-being to Taiwan's compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535066.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建海峡卫视记者","We noticed that around this year's May Fourth Youth Day, some Taiwan compatriots were again awarded the May Fourth Youth Medal. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Around this year's May Fourth Youth Day, Communist Youth League committees and youth federations at all levels commended a number of outstanding young individuals and collectives, among whom 25 Taiwan youths and 3 teams led mainly by Taiwan youths received the provincial- and municipal-level May Fourth Youth Medal and the honorary titles of Collective May Fourth Youth Medal (including nominee awards). We are very pleased to see that more and more Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youths, have found a stage on the mainland to realize their dreams. We will, as always, create good conditions for mutual learning between young people on both sides of the Strait and provide more convenience for Taiwan youths to study, find employment, start businesses and live on the mainland. We welcome more Taiwan youths to take part in the process of Chinese-style modernization, to pursue, build and realize their dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","US Secretary of State Blinken recently issued a statement saying the US “strongly encourages” the World Health Organization to invite Taiwan to attend this year’s World Health Assembly as an observer. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Regarding the participation of the Taiwan region of China in World Health Organization activities, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is the fundamental principle affirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This has caused the political foundation for Taiwan region's participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist, and this situation was entirely caused by the DPP authorities. Regarding the conduct of the US side, our relevant departments have lodged solemn representations with the US side, and we urge the US side to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535064.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","In 2020, CTi News was forced to shut down after the Taiwan regulator “NCC” refused to renew its license. Recently, the Taipei High Administrative Court ruled to revoke the original decision. The “NCC” said it will file another appeal. What comment do you have?","As the facts show, this matter was a political farce staged by the DPP authorities to suppress media outlets holding different positions, and from the very beginning it triggered widespread doubt and strong condemnation in Taiwan's public opinion. The DPP authorities, in defiance of universal condemnation, attack those who think differently, muzzle public opinion, and create “information cocoons,” precisely because they fear that the people of Taiwan will learn the truth. Such despicable conduct will surely bring its own consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently said in Greece that the “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation on which both sides of the Taiwan Strait seek common ground while setting aside differences, a guardrail for cross-strait peace, and he called on all parties to urge both sides of the Strait to hold war-avoidance dialogue to seek peace. The DPP authorities responded that “the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are not…","Upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the legal and factual reality that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and never will. The DPP authorities, with eyes wide open, tell lies: they repeatedly attack and smear the \"1992 Consensus\" and hype the fallacy of \"mutual non-subordination between the two sides,\" with the aim of changing the status quo in which both sides belong to one China and plotting to split the country. This is precisely the root cause of the tension in the Taiwan Strait. Can the DPP authorities' wishful subjective fantasies change objective facts? This is no different from a dream told by a madman.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230517_12535081.htm"],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港中评社记者","Some media on the island recently reported that one-third of Taiwanese businesses in Kunshan, Jiangsu have withdrawn, and most of the remaining factory capacity has also been moved out. Is this true?","It is understood that the relevant reports are seriously inconsistent with the facts. Suzhou in Jiangsu is one of the areas with the densest Taiwanese investment in the Chinese mainland. For a long time, Taiwan businesses have deeply cultivated Suzhou and put down roots in Suzhou, and they have become an important part of the city and a distinctive force for its development. In the first quarter of 2023, Suzhou newly established 98 Taiwan-invested enterprises and actually utilized US$612 million in Taiwan capital. Compared with the same period last year, the number of enterprises increased by 6.5%, and actually utilized Taiwan capital increased by 96%. Nine enterprises with new total investment exceeding US$10 million were added, with contracted Taiwan capital of US$640 million, and 38 capital increase projects with capital increase amounting to US$246 million. In 2022, capital increase projects by Taiwan-invested enterprises such as AUO, King Long Technology, and Chunqi Technology were successively implemented, further demonstrating the firm confidence and determination of Taiwan enterprises to continue to be optimistic about Suzhou and to put down roots there. As of March 2023, Suzhou had approved more than 13,000 Taiwan-invested enterprises in total, with actually received Taiwan capital exceeding US$36 billion.\nAs for the news reported by Taiwan media that Taiwan's Liuhe Group had withdrawn from Kunshan, Jiangsu, the relevant person in charge of the group's subsidiary, Liufeng Machinery Industry Co., Ltd., directly denied it. The actual situation is that in 2021, Liufeng Machinery had already launched a plan to build a new plant in Kunshan, and this project was also listed as a major industrial project of Kunshan City in 2022.\nNews can be fabricated, but figures speak for themselves. We hope that some media on the island will not violate their professional ethics, and will not become a “mouthpiece” for the Green camp.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾联合报记者","Could the spokesperson provide an update on the progress of the Li Yanhe case?","On March 21, 2023, the Shanghai National Security Bureau, in accordance with the law, took criminal coercive measures against Li Yanhe, a criminal suspect suspected of engaging in the crime of inciting secession of the country. The relevant case is currently being further processed. It is reported that the handling unit has arranged for Li Yanhe's wife to make phone calls and communicate with him in Shanghai, and will continue to lawfully protect Li Yanhe's various legitimate rights and interests.\nIt must be emphasized that Li Yanhe is suspected of engaging in activities to incite secession of the country; this is an individual case. As long as there is no such subjective malicious intent or conduct, broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots need have no doubts whatsoever about cross-Strait exchanges. We welcome and encourage Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for normal exchange activities, and we will continue to protect their legitimate rights and interests in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The newly revised Counter-Espionage Law of the People's Republic of China will take effect on July 1. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said this will significantly increase the risks for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland, and listed behaviors such as chatting with locals and using GPS maps as things that could potentially violate the crime of espionage. What is your comment on this?","The National People’s Congress Standing Committee’s revision of the Anti-Espionage Law is a necessity for implementing the overall national security concept and strengthening the struggle against espionage under the new circumstances. It is a powerful legal measure to advance the struggle against infiltration, subversion and theft of secrets and to ensure national security. It is also a necessary part of safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests, and it will provide an important legal guarantee for the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Our purpose in developing cross-Strait relations and expanding normal, healthy exchanges and interactions across the Strait is to deepen mutual understanding, strengthen our shared interests, and promote heartfelt connection between compatriots, not to steal intelligence from each other. We hope everyone will view the revision of this law from a positive perspective.\nAs for the remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council, they are entirely baseless. No article of the Anti-Espionage Law involves what they claim. They are deliberately blurring the line between normal conduct and espionage, with the aim of deceiving and misleading Taiwan’s public, intimidating and obstructing Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, and harming normal, healthy exchanges and interactions across the Strait. Everyone has basic common sense. For example, photographing the Sun Yat-sen Memorial Hall in Taipei is different in nature from photographing a certain military facility. How could a building that is permitted to be photographed on the mainland be treated as espionage and someone be arrested for it? In casual conversation with others, if the intent is good, no topic is off limits; even when cross-Strait differences are involved, we can communicate patiently, seek common ground while setting aside differences. But if a casual conversation is aimed at deliberately probing for intelligence, then it violates regulations and laws. We must remind Taiwan’s public not to be deceived by the Mainland Affairs Council’s sophistry. Administration according to law and openness of society can go hand in hand in any country or society governed by the rule of law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾东森新闻记者","Regarding the normalization of cross-Strait tourism, MAC Minister Chiu Tai-san has repeatedly said that it is not enough for Taiwan to lift the ban unilaterally, and that both sides should sit down and talk. Will mainland tourists be allowed to travel to Taiwan this year?","I advise the DPP authorities not to keep fabricating reasons as pretexts, and not to keep using non-reasons as justifications. Let me ask: Who is responsible for still not opening exchanges for mainland residents to visit Taiwan? Who is responsible for still obstructing mainland residents from going to Kinmen and Matsu, leaving the “mini three links” as a “half set”? Who is responsible for still not restoring the original direct cross-Strait flight points, keeping the gate half-closed? Who is responsible for still not allowing Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland in organized groups? Let them first answer these questions clearly, and then come up with those deceptive phrases.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Former British Prime Minister Liz Truss Visited Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Some Taiwan media have reported that this person was invited by Taiwan's \"Prospect Foundation.\" A series of recent outward-facing activities by the DPP authorities have been operated through this foundation. We have already taken punitive measures against Taiwan's \"Prospect Foundation,\" and if the reports are true, we will add another account to our ledger.\nEveryone can see that the DPP authorities are actually spending the tax money of Taiwan's ordinary people to buy off some anti-China politicians who have left office, to stage a series of farces of \"relying on outside forces to seek independence.\" No matter how much money is spent and no matter how much they stir things up, this cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can it shake the international pattern of one China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","中央广播电视总台央广记者","First question: Tsai Ing-wen was recently asked by a high school student on the island, “If cross-Strait relations go to war, does Taiwan have the strength to resist?” She replied that war is not an option, and that how to prevent conflict and war is extremely important, among other things. A series of remarks at the event provoked strong dissatisfaction in island public opinion. What is the spokesperson's…","On the first question: What this person said is nothing but a lie to deceive young people. Maintaining peace in the Taiwan Strait is the common wish of compatriots on both sides, but “Taiwan independence” and peace are as incompatible as fire and water. The DPP authorities talk about peace, but their actions undermine peace. Willingly serving as agents of external forces to “use Taiwan to contain China,” even to the point of pushing Taiwan into the abyss of disaster, is their “option.”\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair and a matter between the two sides of the Strait, and external forces are not allowed to interfere. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and taking the broad road of peaceful development, compatriots on both sides can fully negotiate and resolve their own problems. If anyone schemes to rely on external forces to egg on and embolden “seeking independence through peaceful means,” it is wishful thinking and will never succeed.\nOn the second question: Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any country that has diplomatic relations with China developing any form of official relations with the Taiwan region or establishing official institutions with each other. No matter how the DPP authorities collude with external forces and play tricks to “seek independence,” it will be futile. It cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","First question: Recently, news circulated among Taiwan businesspeople that the mainland side is willing to first open group tours from Taiwan to the mainland. Please confirm. Second question: The U.S. House Foreign Affairs Committee passed a related bill claiming that the mainland “distorts UN General Assembly Resolution 2758,” stating that “this resolution only addresses the question of China’s representation…","On the first question: everyone can wait for good news. As the COVID-19 epidemic has been effectively brought under control, the mainland's economy and social life are fully returning to normal. During the just-concluded May Day holiday, the mainland's tourism market rebounded strongly; tourism popularity brought market buoyancy, and consumer confidence in tourism has fully recovered. However, due to restrictions imposed by the DPP authorities, Taiwan's industry and the broad base of travelers have been unable to take part. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland for sightseeing, to tour its magnificent rivers and mountains, experience folk culture, and see the new developments in various places. We will create better conditions and provide better products and services for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland.\nOn the second question, the relevant U.S. proposal is entirely wrong and absurd. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unequivocally confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan, and the United States is a party to these documents. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 of 1971 thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the United Nations. Some American politicians have repeatedly made an issue of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758; they are either ignorant or have ulterior motives. Any attempt to distort or even deny the authority and validity of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾“中央社”记者","Some public opinion holds that the investigation of Li Yanhe is related to his publishing activities. Does this show a gap with the mainland's emphasis on respecting Taiwan's social system?","As I said just now, Li Yanhe is suspected of engaging in criminal activities to incite secession of the country. This involves national security and has nothing to do with whether one respects the system. We respect Taiwan's social system, and compatriots in Taiwan should also respect the mainland's social system. You only demand that I respect you, yet you engage in criminal activities inciting secession of the country. This is not mutual respect. It must be emphasized that the security of any sovereign state is not to be challenged, and no one may act willfully in the name of so-called 'freedom and democracy.'","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: Warren Buffett recently said at a shareholders’ meeting that TSMC is a good company but is located in a bad place, and he is worried about a crisis in the Taiwan Strait. In fact, many overseas enterprises have already reduced their investments in Taiwan. Commentators on the island have also said that the DPP’s so-called “resisting China and protecting Taiwan” cannot even keep TSMC safe. What is…","On the first question: Buffett's words are worth serious listening and reflection by Taiwan compatriots. I will not comment much.\nOn the second question, our position is clear. Whether they attempt to 'use Taiwan to contain China' or fantasize about 'relying on outside forces to seek independence,' they will not succeed. If they continue their provocations and coercion, or even cross the red line, we will have to take resolute measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No one should underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and powerful capabilities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","北京日报记者","Taiwan's police authorities recently issued a document requiring police stations across the island to mobilize the recruitment of young people aged 18 to 40 to join volunteer police or civil defense ranks in support of military-police missions. This has been questioned as the DPP authorities preparing for war. May I ask for the spokesperson's evaluation?","Your citation of the doubts on the island is very correct. I also noted that some Taiwanese media reported that over the past five years, about 20% of Taiwan military enlistees would rather pay money to be discharged. What does this show? It shows that they do not want to become cannon fodder for 'Taiwan independence' politicians, and that they have already seen through the essence of the DPP authorities' 'relying on outsiders to seek independence.'","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","福建厦门卫视记者","Since the partial resumption of “mini three links” passenger routes, they have been well received by people on both sides. Could the spokesperson introduce the specific situation since the resumption of cross-Strait “mini three links”?","Since the partial resumption of the “Small Three Links” on January 7, as of April 30, the “Small Three Links” routes have operated 830 sailings, carrying 75,825 passengers. Among them, the Xiamen–Kinmen route had 596 sailings and 69,211 passengers; the Fuzhou–Matsu route had 186 sailings and 5,102 passengers; and the Quanzhou–Kinmen route had 48 sailings and 1,512 passengers. The partial resumption of the “Small Three Links” has provided convenience for compatriots in Taiwan traveling across the Strait. At present, the COVID-19 epidemic has been effectively controlled, yet the DPP authorities still restrict mainland residents from engaging in exchange activities in the Kinmen and Matsu areas via the “Small Three Links.” We urge the DPP authorities to put the well-being of the peoples on both sides first, remove as soon as possible the artificial restrictions they have imposed, achieve full resumption of the “Small Three Links,” and adopt genuine, substantive measures of goodwill to expand cross-strait personnel exchanges and restore normal cross-strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","环球网记者","Former NBA player Howard recently co-filmed a promotional video with Lai Ching-te and referred to Taiwan as a “country,” which sparked controversy. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country. This is the common consensus and basic knowledge of the international community. Relevant persons should understand this common sense and catch up on their lessons. The DPP authorities, using all kinds of means, spare no effort in promoting and fabricating 'Taiwan independence,' but this is nothing more than a farce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-17","Ma Xiaoguang","台湾TVBS记者","The KMT is very likely to decide today to nominate Hou Yu-ih to run in 2024. Is the mainland relatively unfamiliar with him in terms of cross-Strait discourse and communication?","First, regarding the internal affairs of the Kuomintang, we will not comment. Second, regarding exchanges between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China, and jointly promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, our attitude and position are clear. Third, we also note that the Kuomintang leadership and all relevant parties have repeatedly stated that unity must be maintained and there must be no split. We continue to follow this closely.\nSee you next time, and thank you all for coming.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230517_12535058.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-05-18","Wang Wenbin","TASS","My second question is also about the interview with Dr. Kissinger. He said that “The two greatest dangers to peace right now are us two [America and China]. In the sense that we have the capacity to destroy humanity...We are on the path to great-power confrontation.” He also said that both sides need to reduce the rhetoric on Taiwan to ease tensions. The leaders of the US and China should meet regularly and…","China is committed to growing relations with the US in accordance with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping. We hope the US will form a correct perception of China, stop harming China’s sovereignty, security and development interests, and work together with China to bring bilateral ties back to the right track of sound and steady development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347525.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230518_11079549.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-18","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida said that Japan shares the position during the G7 summit that the issue of Taiwan should be resolved peacefully through dialogue and sent out the message. Japanese media stated that G7 members are coordinating on including such content as “the importance of peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait” into the summit joint statement. What’s your comment?","The real threat to cross-Strait peace and stability is the DPP authorities’ unwillingness to recognize the 1992 Consensus which embodies the one-China principle, separatist activities to seek “Taiwan” independence and attempts to change the status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. The US, Japan and certain countries have been fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, and echoing and collaborating with “Taiwan independence” forces in political, military and economic dimensions. It is quite clear they are also responsible for the tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nTo keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful, it is essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose risky and provocative moves by “Taiwan independence” forces and resolutely contain foreign connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” activities.\nThose who talk about peace in the Taiwan Strait without mentioning the need to oppose “Taiwan independence” forces will only embolden the separatists as they solicit foreign support for “Taiwan independence” and take reckless moves, which can only mean greater danger to the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThose who talk about peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question without mentioning the need to support China’s reunification are actually trying to impede China’s reunification and create a “peaceful division”. The Chinese people will firmly oppose it.\nNo one cherish cross-Strait peace more than us in China. We are committed to striving for peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort. But we will not accept any attempt by anyone or any force to curb our effort to stop separatism for “Taiwan independence”. And we will not allow anyone or any force to meddle in China’s own affairs under the disguise of seeking peace.\nWe urge the US, Japan and other G7 members to adhere to the political documents on their bilateral relations with China, follow the one-China principle, stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” forces, stop making provocations and playing with fire on the Taiwan question and never stand on the opposite side of over 1.4 billion Chinese people. Those playing with fire will get burnt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347525.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230518_11079549.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-19","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Registration for the 76th World Health Assembly will close this week. Taiwan has not received an invitation. What’s your comment?","There is only one China in the world. The PRC government is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, is consistent and clear. It must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a fundamental principle affirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nFor eight consecutive years from 2009 to 2016, the Taiwan region participated in the WHA as an observer in the name of “Chinese Taipei”. This is a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultation on the basis of adherence by both sides of the Taiwan Strait to the 1992 Consensus, which embodies the one-China principle. The one-China principle is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait ties and for the special arrangement for the Taiwan region’s participation in the WHA. After coming into power in 2016, the DPP has placed political calculations before the Taiwan people’s welfare and remained headstrong on “Taiwan independence”. As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. To uphold the one-China principle and the sanctity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China has decided not to agree to let the Taiwan region participate in this year’s WHA.\nThe Taiwan authorities claim that its absence from the WHA will cause a “gap” in global anti-epidemic efforts. That’s not true. They are just using this false assumption as a pretext to get into the WHA. The Chinese Central Government attaches great importance to the health and well-being of our compatriots in the Taiwan region, and has made proper arrangement for Taiwan’s participation in global health affairs on the condition that the one-China principle is upheld. According to the arrangement agreed on between China and WHO, Taiwan’s medical and health experts can participate in WHO technical meetings given that the one-China principle is upheld. Over the past year alone, medical and technical experts from China’s Taiwan region took part in WHO technical activities 24 times, which involved 26 participants. Taiwan has timely access to WHO information on global public health emergencies and reports to WHO in a timely manner the information of public health emergencies in Taiwan. Till now, the Chinese Central Government has updated the Taiwan region on COVID-19 over 500 times, including information about confirmed cases who are Taiwan residents staying in the mainland. These arrangements have ensured that Taiwan can promptly and effectively deal with any local or international public health emergency. The DPP authorities are hyping up Taiwan’s WHA participation not because this is necessary for epidemic response, but because they see it as a potential way to expand international space for “Taiwan independence”.\nChina’s decision of not agreeing to let the Taiwan region participate in this year’s WHA has received broad-based support and understanding from the international community. Recently, nearly 140 countries have communicated to China that they stand for the one-China principle and oppose Taiwan’s participation in the WHA. Nearly 100 countries wrote to the WHO Director-General or issued public statements to make that clear. This once again shows that the one-China principle has international support and represents the prevailing trend. It shows that the overwhelming majority of countries uphold the just and right position on Taiwan’s WHA participation. People around the world are sharp-eyed. Any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” to contain China will be firmly rejected by the overwhelming majority of members of the international community and will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347526.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230519_11080184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-19","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US and Taiwan agreed to boost trade ties, the first tangible results under an initiative announced last year. What’s the foreign ministry’s comment on this latest development?","China strongly opposes official interaction of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. That includes negotiating or signing any agreement that implies sovereignty and has an official nature. The US move gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and contravenes the US’s own commitment of maintaining only unofficial relations with Taiwan. China deplores and strongly opposes this move.\nThe US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués with concrete actions, stop official interaction of any form with Taiwan, refrain from negotiating or signing any agreement with implications of sovereignty and of official nature with China’s Taiwan region, and stop sending any wrong message to separatist forces seeking “Taiwan independence” in the name of economy and trade.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347526.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230519_11080184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-05-19","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Q: During this year’s May Day holiday, tourism markets across the mainland were booming, and both the number of tourist trips and tourism revenue exceeded those of the May Day holiday in 2019. Will the mainland side allow group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents?\nA:\nAfter consulting the relevant competent authorities, we have learned that, starting today, travel agencies are permitted to resume operating group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland for tourism and sightseeing, to enjoy its magnificent rivers and mountains, and to see the new developments in various localities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230519_12535699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-19","Ma Xiaoguang","国台办发言人马晓光19日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19 (Reporter) — Ma Xiaoguang, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on the 19th and said that the global epidemic situation remains far from optimistic, and the international community generally hopes to emerge from the shadow of the epidemic as soon as possible. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, sacrificing international public…","Ma Xiaoguang said that it must be pointed out that compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh-and-blood kin, and no one cares more about their health and well-being than we do. Since the outbreak of COVID-19, we were the first to invite Taiwan health experts to visit Wuhan, Hubei, sharing dozens of technical materials. We also specially notified the WHO of information on how the mainland shared the virus gene sequence and the means of obtaining relevant gene sequences. As of May 2023, we have notified the Taiwan region of COVID-19 epidemic information more than 500 times, including information on Taiwan residents diagnosed on the mainland. In the past year, Taiwan medical technology experts have participated in a total of 24 batches of WHO technical activities. The mainland side has also actively and orderly arranged free vaccinations for Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. As of February 2023, a cumulative total of 479,000 vaccine doses had been administered to Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. It can be said that the channels for Taiwan's participation in WHO technical communication and cooperation are fully open, and the channels for obtaining various epidemic prevention and control information and support are fully effective. The DPP authorities' political lie of a so-called “gap in the international epidemic prevention system” has collapsed on its own.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230519_12535852.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-20","Ma Xiaoguang","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19 -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, answering reporters' questions on the 19th, said that we firmly oppose the United States and Taiwan region of China concluding any agreement with sovereignty implications or official nature. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions. In order to seek political self-interest, the DPP authorities are willing to sell out the interests of Taiwan's enterprises and people. This shameful conduct of \"exhausting Taiwan's resources to win foreign favor\" is doomed to fail.\nA reporter asked: On May 19, the DPP authorities announced that they would sign the first batch of agreements under the \"US-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative\" with the United States. What comment do you have on this? Ma Xiaoguang gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230520_12535858.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-22","Ma Xiaoguang","国台办发言人马晓光22日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 22 (electronic dispatch): In response to the 76th World Health Assembly’s decision once again not to place Taiwan-related proposals on the agenda, TAO spokesperson Ma Xiaoguang, answering reporters’ questions on the 22nd, said: We advise the DPP authorities to immediately stop political manipulation of Taiwan-related issues at the WHO. Any conduct that challenges the One-China…","Ma Xiaoguang said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The relevant decisions of the 76th World Health Assembly once again show that adhering to the one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community, the will of the people, and the general trend, and it cannot be challenged by anyone. The DPP authorities neither recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, nor scheme to push so-called “Taiwan-related proposals.” This goes against the consensus of the international community and is bound to be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230522_12536362.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-05-25","Mao Ning","AFP","The outgoing president of Paraguay said yesterday that the country is open to trading with China, but would not switch diplomatic allegiance from Taiwan. Do you have any response to the statement?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. The fact that 182 countries have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle demonstrates that standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. Relevant countries need to see the prevailing trend of the world, choose the right side of history together with the overwhelming majority of countries and make the right decision soon that serves their fundamental and long-term interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347530.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230525_11083615.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-26","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","It was reported that a Taiwan defense official said on May 25 that the US government has started to deliver its plan to send weapons aid to Taiwan via presidential drawdown authority, with the first batch of Stinger anti-aircraft missiles already arrived in Taiwan on May 24. Do you have any comment on this?","The US provision of weapons to Taiwan gravely violates the three China-US Joint Communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, interferes in China’s internal affairs, harms China’s sovereignty and security interests, and undermines cross-Strait peace and stability. This is extremely wrong and dangerous. China strongly deplores and firmly rejects this and has made serious démarches to the US.\nFrom US politician’s clamoring for “destroying TSMC” to arming the island of Taiwan into a “porcupine”, it is all too obvious that the US would stop at nothing – even if it means destroying Taiwan – to contain China. The over 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our Taiwan compatriots, will not accept this.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop military contact with Taiwan and arming Taiwan, stop creating factors that heighten tensions across the Strait, and stop conniving at and supporting separatist forces’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” by force. We would like to, once again, make it clear to the DPP authorities that attempting to solicit foreign support for independence and reject reunification by force will only end in failure. China will closely follow the developments of the situation and resolutely safeguard our nation’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347531.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230526_11084394.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-05-30","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s vice president Lai Ching-te said that the Chinese leader is the head of state he would most like to have dinner with. He said and I quote, “If I had the opportunity to have dinner with him, I would urge him to chill out a little and not put everyone under so much pressure. People’s wellbeing is the most important thing and peace benefits everyone.” Do you have any comment about the comments from vice…","Taiwan is part of China and does not have the so-called “vice president”. This is not about foreign affairs and I have no comment. If the DPP authorities really care about peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, the key lies in upholding the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347533.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202305/t20230530_11085939.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 31, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Hello, everyone. Welcome to today's TAO regular press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","It is reported that the 15th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in June. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant information.","The 15th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian starting June 16, with the forum conference on June 17. The main venue is located in Xiamen, and relevant prefecture-level cities and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone will hold related activities. Preparations for all items are basically in place. The forum organizing committee has invited representatives of Taiwan political parties, representatives of host units, industry representatives, association heads, and guests from all walks of life, including the Communist Youth League, the Women's Federation, the All-China Federation of Trade Unions, and sectors in science and education, culture, health, agriculture, fisheries, water conservancy, and folk beliefs.\nThis forum is co-hosted by 84 institutions from both sides of the Strait. It adheres to the positioning of being “civilian, grassroots, and broadly based,” continues the theme of “expanding civilian exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and sets up four sections: grassroots exchanges, youth exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges. A series of 37 activities are arranged, with 14 activities in relevant prefecture-level cities, for a total of 51 activities. This forum will offer more than 1,200 employment positions and more than 1,000 internship and training positions for Taiwan youth, and will promote the signing of multiple cooperation agreements between relevant cross-Strait institutions and enterprises in the fields of rural revitalization, Taiwan youth entrepreneurship, technology, education, culture, and finance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538678.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","In response to the mainland's resumption of group tours for Taiwan residents to the mainland, the Mainland Affairs Council called on the mainland to simultaneously open tourism from the mainland to Taiwan. Taiwan's tourism authority said that the ban prohibiting travel operators from receiving and organizing groups to travel to the mainland can only be lifted after consultations through the tourism 'mini two…","On May 19, the relevant departments on the mainland announced the resumption of travel agencies' group tour business for Taiwan residents coming to the mainland, which was welcomed by Taiwan's travel industry and the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. We note that the DPP authorities have openly stated they will not lift the ban prohibiting travel agencies from organizing Taiwan residents' tour groups to the mainland, which has caused dissatisfaction across all sectors on the island. Comparing the two, it is clear at a glance who is considering the interests of Taiwan compatriots and the tourism industry, and who stands in opposition to those interests.\nThe Mainland Affairs Council claims that so-called “small two-association” consultations are needed for tourism, which is completely untenable. We have consistently advocated for convenient cross-Strait exchanges for Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan residents' group tours to the mainland gradually became routine 30 years ago, and there is no need at all for cross-Strait consultations. Taiwan's explicit ban on its residents' group tours to the mainland is unprecedented in more than 30 years. The DPP authorities' refusal to lift the ban will only harm the interests of Taiwan residents and the tourism industry, and it is not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538674.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Mobile payment has brought great convenience to people's daily life and travel, and has become a daily way of life for mainland compatriots. Many Taiwan compatriots hope to experience mobile payment as soon as they arrive in the mainland, but there are some inconveniences. May I ask whether the mainland side can provide assistance?","Using mobile payment on the mainland requires binding a bank card to payment platforms such as Alipay and WeChat Pay. At present, Taiwan compatriots can bind a card in two ways, and there is no obstacle in use. The first way is to bind an international bank card, such as a VISA or Mastercard, issued in Taiwan. The second way is to bind a debit card or credit card issued on the mainland.\nRegarding the specific binding procedures, Taiwan compatriots may download apps such as Alipay and WeChat to their phones and register with a Taiwan mobile number or a mainland mobile number. They complete identity verification using the Taiwan Compatriot Permit (i.e., the Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents) or the Taiwan Residence Permit, and then choose to bind an international bank card or a mainland bank card. After that, they can pay conveniently on the mainland.\nIt is understood that the inconvenience Taiwan compatriots have reported is mainly because some of them are not familiar with or do not understand the procedures for binding their bank cards to payment platforms. We are working with relevant parties to sort out the situation of Taiwan compatriots applying for mainland bank cards and binding payment platforms, and are producing “easy-to-understand packages,” short videos and leaflets, and strengthening publicity so that Taiwan compatriots can fully understand the various convenience services. We will also continue to optimize solutions to specific problems encountered in use.\nWe will, as always, provide more convenience for Taiwan compatriots to study, work, start businesses and live on the mainland, and we warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland and personally experience the security, convenience and efficiency of mainland mobile payment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538675.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The CSRC has implemented the “Trial Administrative Measures for Overseas Issuance and Listing of Securities by Domestic Enterprises” starting March 31, and overseas listing by domestic enterprises has formally shifted to a filing-based system. What impact will this new regulation have on Taiwanese enterprises on the mainland?","The Interim Measures for the Administration of Overseas Securities Offering and Listing by Domestic Companies, which took effect on March 31 this year, adhere to market-oriented and rule-of-law principles and create a more transparent and predictable institutional environment for domestic companies to list overseas. The relevant standards apply uniformly to all mainland domestic companies, including Taiwan-funded companies whose main business operations are in the mainland.\nOverseas listing by domestic companies is an important component of the two-way opening of the mainland's capital market and has positive significance for supporting companies in integrating into globalized development. The mainland respects the right of Taiwan-funded companies to independently choose their listing venue and supports qualified Taiwan-funded companies in listing overseas in accordance with law and regulation, making use of two markets and two types of resources to achieve standardized and healthy development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538676.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Pingtan, Guangzhou and other places have successively held sports and cultural exchange activities in novel formats. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From May 19 to 21, the 2023 7th Pingtan Cross-Strait Workers' Bicycle Race was held in the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, Fujian, with more than a thousand worker athletes from both sides of the Strait participating. Among them, more than 200 Taiwan worker riders from 16 counties and cities, including Taipei, Taichung and Yilan, crossed the sea to compete. Compared with previous editions, this year's event added a cross-Strait riding activity for athletes from both sides, which, while exchanging skills and competing, allowed participants to enjoy the island scenery together and share the magnificence of the land.\nOn May 26, the grand final of the first Guangzhou Taiwan Youth Lingnan Culture Interpreter Competition was held in Guangzhou. Themed “I Will Interpret Lingnan Culture,” the competition attracted nearly 4,000 Taiwan youths from 12 universities and primary and secondary schools in Guangzhou to take part in online training. Nearly 500 Taiwan youths visited 12 cross-Strait exchange bases and exchange points, and 185 Taiwan youths took part in the preliminary selection, with 20 contestants advancing to the final. During the competition, the contestants explored the beauty of Lingnan culture, experienced the imprint of history and culture, and presented the splendor of Lingnan culture. After the competition, the 185 preliminary contestants received letters of appointment and became volunteer interpreters at relevant venues, providing wonderful explanation services to visiting members of the public.\nWe will continue to support relevant localities in actively holding cross-Strait exchange activities that are innovative in form and diverse in target audiences, providing more platforms for people on both sides to exchange ideas, compete and deepen friendship, and promoting friendship and common progress among compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently called on political parties and politicians on the island not to peddle fear of war for electoral gain, and not to use fear to incite the Taiwan people, saying that “war is not an option for the whole world, nor is it an option for Taiwan.” What is your comment?","Who is peddling fear of war? Taiwan's people can see clearly. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, rely on external forces to provoke the mainland, and vigorously hype the so-called “mainland threat” to find pretexts for manipulating “anti-China” sentiment and deceiving votes. They recklessly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people and go abroad to buy large quantities of weapons, pushing Taiwan step by step toward danger and causing deep anxiety among people on the island that “Taiwan independence” will lead to war. The DPP authorities know full well that their obstinate pursuit of “Taiwan independence” means war, yet they do not allow ordinary people to worry about the disasters war would bring. The people's eyes are keen. If the DPP authorities do not abandon the “Taiwan independence” position, they have no qualification to talk lightly of “peace.” They are the originators of war fear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538672.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台海峡两岸记者","At her press conference marking the seventh anniversary of taking office, Tsai Ing-wen said that the Taiwan question should be resolved peacefully, that she adheres to the so-called “four insistences and maintaining the status quo,” that cross-Strait differences should be resolved through dialogue, and that taking “maintaining the status quo” as the greatest common denominator is the key to ensuring peace. What…","This speech, while empty talk about peace, openly peddles the “two-state theory” and pushes “Taiwan independence” positions; it claims to seek “peaceful dialogue” yet avoids mentioning the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” the political foundation for dialogue and consultation between the two sides. Lies cannot deceive the world, and attempts to pursue “peaceful separation” are impossible to achieve.\nThere is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and must not be divided. This is the true status quo of cross-Strait relations and the common consensus of the international community. Since the DPP authorities came to power in 2016, they have unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait relations, vigorously pursued “Taiwan independence” separatism, obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, openly promoted the “two-state theory,” undermined the fact that both sides belong to one China, and colluded with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the true destroyers of the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of turmoil threatening peace and stability in the Strait. This is a fact that no embellishment or sophistry can cover up.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end. We adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” and are willing to create broad room for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538673.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said, “The conditions for doing business on the mainland are much worse than before, and it is no longer the largest base for Taiwan enterprise investment,” and said he would help Taiwan companies lay out their global positioning. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Some people and forces on the island are habitual liars, accustomed to speaking nonsense with their eyes open. In fact, the mainland has long been the largest destination for Taiwanese investment. I have a set of figures to share with everyone. According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, from 2012 to 2022, the cumulative number of Taiwan-invested projects on the mainland increased from 88,000 to 129,700, the cumulative actual utilization of Taiwan capital increased from US$57.05 billion to US$72 billion, and 60 Taiwan-funded enterprises have successively listed and raised financing on the mainland capital market. Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan-funded enterprises have actively participated in cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development, and have achieved better development in the broad expanse of the mainland.\nIn the future, as the mainland accelerates the construction of a new development paradigm and promotes high-quality development, and as Chinese-style modernization advances across the board, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will have more opportunities, broader space, and a better future for development on the mainland. We will continue to improve the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and create a better environment for development and investment for Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan-funded enterprises. The mainland was in the past, is now, and will continue to be in the future the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to invest and start businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","On May 28, the domestically produced large passenger aircraft C919 successfully completed its first commercial passenger flight in the world, sparking heated discussion among compatriots on both sides. Some Taiwan compatriots said, “We look forward to the day when C919 opens cross-strait routes.” May I ask whether there is such a plan? In addition, yesterday the Shenzhou-16 manned spacecraft was successfully…","The C919 large passenger aircraft is the first jet-powered mainline airliner developed on the mainland that complies with internationally recognized airworthiness standards and has independent intellectual property rights. On May 28, China Eastern Airlines used the first C919 large passenger aircraft delivered globally by COMAC, taking off from Shanghai Hongqiao Airport and smoothly arriving at Beijing Capital Airport. The C919's first global commercial passenger flight marks the full integration of the C919's \"research and development, manufacturing, certification, and operation,\" and China's domestically produced large aircraft officially \"started out\" in commercial operation in civil aviation, and the \"in-flight experience\" of China's large aircraft has officially reached a broad base of consumers.\n\"When the great roc rides the same wind and rises, soaring nine myriad li.\" The domestically produced large aircraft taking flight on the wind is a shared source of pride for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. We fully feel the joy of Taiwan compatriots over the flight of China's domestically produced large aircraft and their keen anticipation of riding it. We also believe that people on both sides of the Strait will certainly be able to enjoy the experience of the C919 operating cross-Strait routes.\nYesterday was the seventh National Science and Technology Workers' Day, and on this day the Shenzhou-16 manned spacecraft successfully set out on its mission, and the two astronaut crews of Shenzhou-15 and Shenzhou-16 successfully \"rendezvoused\" in space. This has special significance, and we extend our warm congratulations.\nOn the path toward the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, Taiwan compatriots will, together with compatriots on the mainland, share the dignity and glory of one great country, and take pride and pleasure in being upright Chinese. The departure of Shenzhou-16, with engineers boarding the spacecraft, has inspired Taiwan compatriots, who sent many blessings. This is precisely the sharing of this dignity and glory, and the expression of this pride and pleasure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视新闻记者","First question: Taiwan's executive authority recently announced that it no longer recognizes mainland residents as “nationals,” and mainland residents will no longer enjoy the rights under Taiwan's relevant regulations. What is your comment on this? Second question: On the 25th, Taiwan's competent defense authority confirmed that the US government's US$500 million arms aid to Taiwan has been implemented, and the…","On the first question: We are closely following the relevant developments. It should be pointed out that the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, in pursuit of their own political interests, disregard the strong aspirations of Taiwan compatriots for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. They constantly change tactics to provoke “independence,” create cross-Strait confrontation, seriously harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are all Chinese. No matter how the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces keep changing their tactics and using whatever means, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.\nOn the second question: U.S. arms sales to Taiwan violate the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué,” and we firmly oppose them. The recent U.S. moves to adjust and accelerate arms sales to Taiwan once again prove that the United States is playing the “Taiwan card,” attempting to turn Taiwan into a “porcupine.” In essence, this is “destroying Taiwan” and “harming Taiwan,” making Taiwan compatriots serve as cannon fodder, and it is by no means for the good of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities' obstinate “relying on the United States to seek independence” will only push Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Taiwanese media reported that the DPP authorities said the mainland is carrying out “united front” work against Taiwan through the “police-overseas Chinese service stations” it has set up overseas, and has also launched hacking attacks against Taiwan's overseas institutions. They continue to accuse the mainland of spreading “false information that threatens democracy.” What is your comment?","The relevant departments have already refuted and clarified some media reports. The DPP authorities' claims are entirely a case of a thief crying “stop thief,” deliberately framing others.\nSince taking office seven years ago, the DPP authorities have fabricated and disseminated false information in all directions and across the entire chain. According to exposés by media outlets and individuals on the island, the DPP authorities are the “chain leader” of the false information industry, responsible for supplying the false information sources. Their kept cyber armies then steer public opinion, and Green-camp media follow suit and hype it, continuously producing false information to smear and attack the mainland. They are addicted to fabrication and persistently manufacture falsehoods to seek political gain, deliberately intensifying cross-Strait hostility and antagonism, harming the feelings of compatriots on both sides, and undermining the development of cross-Strait relations. To keep their lies from being exposed, they can only keep creating “information cocoons,” depriving ordinary people of their right to know, blocking compatriots on the island from channels to understand the real situation on the mainland, and misleading Taiwan society and the public's perception.\nWe advise the DPP authorities to stop lying and fabricating as soon as possible, or they will surely face retribution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538668.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently claimed that this year, 12 so-called “allies” and 13 countries spoke out in support of Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly, achieving a so-called “diplomatic breakthrough.” What comment do you have?","Regarding the issue of Taiwan's participation in World Health Organization activities, we have stated our position many times. The reason Taiwan cannot attend the World Health Assembly as an observer is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” stance, which has undermined the political basis for handling this issue.\nBy politicizing the Taiwan issue at the World Health Assembly, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have made it clearer to the international community two facts: first, Taiwan is part of China; second, what the Democratic Progressive Party authorities truly care about is not the health of the Taiwan public, but rather using the assembly as a platform to make political statements and seek so-called “international space.” For this reason, during this year's World Health Assembly, nearly 140 countries expressed their adherence to the one-China principle and their opposition to Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly. Nearly 100 countries sent letters to the WHO Director-General on this matter or issued public statements, clearly expressing their opposition to the political manipulation of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. The facts show that the more the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stir up trouble in international organization activities, the more they court humiliation and bring it upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538671.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海记者","It is reported that the US and Taiwan will sign the first batch of agreements under the so-called “21st Century Trade Initiative.” Some commentators believe that if the new trade rules and standards formulated in full accordance with this initiative are adopted, Taiwan will become an “economic colony” of the US. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any agreement with substantive sovereignty implications or official character being negotiated between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear.\nThe DPP authorities are vigorously promoting this so-called “agreement,” allowing the US to take whatever it wants. This is “exhausting Taiwan's resources to please foreigners,” a purely losing deal that is all show. This so-called “agreement” is an unequal agreement, a political transaction dressed up as an economic and trade deal, a case of the US grabbing and exploiting Taiwan, and the DPP authorities’ servile capitulation and selling out of Taiwan. The so-called “diplomatic achievements” the DPP authorities boast about come at the cost of selling out the interests of enterprises and the public on the island and weakening Taiwan's core industrial advantages and overall economic competitiveness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202305/t20230531_12538670.htm"],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","National People’s Congress deputy Ling Youshi was fined NT$500,000 by the Mainland Affairs Council for allegedly violating the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area,” and Ling said he refuses to pay the fine. The MAC claimed that “a few people cooperate with the CCP’s united front work and use distortion of the cross-strait act and improper linkage with the One-China…","Ms. Ling Youshi has already responded to the DPP authorities’ suppression. The actions of the DPP authorities once again expose their essence of undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and seeking “Taiwan independence” and separation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Taiwanese taekwondo athlete Lee Tung-hsien recently raised the five-star red flag in celebration after winning a medal at a sports event held in South Korea. The Green camp clamored for an investigation and punishment of him. The Mainland Affairs Council said, 'When developing or engaging in cross-Strait exchange activities on the mainland, one should not cooperate with the mainland's united front propaganda or…","Lee Tung-hsien is an outstanding taekwondo athlete. He participated in this sports competition in an individual capacity and achieved good results, and we extend our congratulations.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. After Lee Tung-hsien won a medal at the games, he expressed the honor and joy of being a proud and upright Chinese in his own way, which was supported by people on both sides of the Strait. The attacks, accusations, and even threats from Taiwan's Green camp media and the Mainland Affairs Council have exposed the extreme hypocrisy of their so-called “freedom and democracy,” and have once again shown that under the “green terror” created by the DPP, the island has only the freedom to advocate “Taiwan independence” and no freedom to identify with reunification.\nQuestion from Taiwan's CTV News: Lai Ching-te recently said that relations between the mainland and Hong Kong and Macao are “false peace,” and that if Taiwan wants to “avoid following in their footsteps,” it must “use preparation for war to avoid war.” What is your response?\nSince Hong Kong and Macao returned to the motherland, successful practices have been carried out in implementing “one country, two systems.” Hong Kong has now entered a new stage of moving from chaos to order and from order toward prosperity, and Macao has maintained a good trend of long-term stable development. Some people in Taiwan turn black into white and use Hong Kong and Macao as talking points; this only exposes their own shortcomings, shows that they still live in the old era, and that they still rely only on deceiving the people on the island to gain electoral benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","The children’s song “Wa Ya Wa” (Digging, Digging), which recently became a hit on the mainland, has also spread to the island. KMT spokesperson Li Mingxuan adapted the lyrics to mock the DPP authorities for their poor governance. What comment do you have?","The phenomenon in question illustrates two points:\nFirst, people on both sides of the Strait quickly share hot topics and communicate conveniently through the internet. Over the past month, the children's song \"Planting Flowers in the Garden\" spread from the mainland to Taiwan with its bright \"dig, dig, dig\" rhythm. Many people on the island adapted and sang it, and it has spread well. We encourage people on both sides of the Strait to communicate and exchange more through new internet media, to discover interesting things together and share more information and joy.\nSecond, during the seven years in which the DPP authorities have been in power, they have engaged in extensive political manipulation and reckless policies that disregard people's livelihoods, which has caused great resentment among the island's people, who have expressed it through multiple versions of \"dig, dig, dig.\" Ignoring public opinion and going against public will will ultimately lead to being abandoned by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Tesla founder Elon Musk said in an interview that achieving unification is China's official policy, and that this should not be read for implied meanings but should be taken seriously. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity are not divisible. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. China's reunification will not harm the legitimate interests of any country, but will only bring more development opportunities to all countries. We believe that more and more people of insight will understand and support the cause of China's reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","US scholar Ge Laiyi recently said that in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election, the mainland tends to support Ko Wen-je. Ko Wen-je has described himself as “a candidate that all parties can accept or tolerate.” May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have never interfered in the island's elections and have no comment on specific candidates.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that he hopes to tell the mainland side face to face that the people's well-being is the most important, and that peace benefits everyone. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Isn’t it quite strange for someone who calls himself a “pragmatic Taiwan independence worker” to say such things? The “Taiwan independence” nature has not changed; merely changing rhetoric and trying to dress oneself in the guise of “goodwill” and “peace” cannot deceive the world. Continuing to stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, disregarding the wishes and interests of the Taiwan public, will ultimately only push Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of deadly war and peril. Only by thoroughly abandoning the “Taiwan independence” position can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region be maintained, the interests and well-being of people on both sides be safeguarded, and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations be promoted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Mainland student Zhang Haichuan, who studied in Taiwan, has been accused of involvement in multiple bomb threat letter incidents in Taiwan. Will this increase resentment among Taiwan residents?","It is understood that Zhang himself has already clarified the matter with the relevant parties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Ko Wen-je recently reiterated his cross-Strait position, saying Taiwan must hold onto its “bottom line of autonomy and self-determination of its destiny,” and expressed that he does not want so-called “resisting China to defend Taiwan” to become a “Boxer Rebellion.” What comment do you have?","So-called “resisting China” can never “protect Taiwan.” The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are one family. People from all walks of life on both sides should move toward each other, advance hand in hand, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, resist any words or deeds that create cross-strait confrontation, jointly uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and keep the future and destiny of Taiwan firmly in the hands of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-05-31","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, many Taiwan singers and bands have held concerts in various parts of the mainland, with lively scenes that have triggered a wave of fond youthful memories among many fans. How does the spokesperson view this phenomenon?","At last month's press conference we said that, as of mid-April, various localities had cumulatively approved 75 batches totaling 431 performance events involving Taiwan performing artists. Taiwan singers and bands are expected to hold nearly 100 large-scale concerts on the mainland this year and to take part in dozens of large music festival projects. Now everyone has been gradually enjoying the wonderful performances of the relevant performing artists, online and in person. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are connected by blood and share the same cultural roots. Nourished by Chinese culture, both classical music and contemporary popular music can resonate emotionally with compatriots on both sides. We will continue to deepen the integrated development of the music sector across the Strait, promote exchanges and cooperation among musicians on both sides, and jointly promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202305/t20230531_12538665.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-06-01","Mao Ning","AFP","Relevant departments of Taiwan said that Taiwan will sign a trade agreement with the US on Thursday and it hopes that the two sides will reach a comprehensive free trade agreement in the future. Do you have any comment?","China strongly opposes official interaction of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. That includes negotiating or signing any agreement of sovereign implication or official nature. The US’s move gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and contravenes the US’s own commitment of maintaining only unofficial relations with Taiwan. China has made solemn démarches to the US many times.\nThe US needs to stop official interaction of any form with Taiwan, refrain from negotiating or signing any agreement of sovereign implication or official nature with China’s Taiwan region, and stop sending any wrong message to separatist forces seeking “Taiwan independence” in the name of economy and trade. The DPP authorities’ attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence” in the name of economic and trade cooperation is just futile.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347535.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230601_11088054.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-02","Mao Ning","CCTV","According to reports, the first agreement under the US-Taiwan Initiative on 21st Century Trade was signed in Washington D.C. on the evening of June 1. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","China strongly opposes official interactions of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. That includes negotiating or signing any agreement that implies sovereignty and has an official nature. The US government has deliberately pushed forward negotiations with the DPP authorities in Taiwan on the so-called “Initiative on 21st Century Trade” and signed the agreement. This gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and contravenes the US’s own commitment of maintaining only unofficial relations with Taiwan. China strongly deplores this and has made serious démarches to the US side.\nUnder the disguise of trade cooperation, the so-called “Initiative” is just a US tool to rip Taiwan off. The DPP authorities, driven by the selfish separatist agenda, have no scruples to betray Taiwan compatriots and businesses’ interests or sell Taiwan away. By signing the agreement, they are offering Taiwan to the US on a plate. This is the latest example of the US trying to fudge and hollow out the one-China principle. We once again urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately change course and stop official interactions of any form with Taiwan, stop pushing forward and revoke at once the so-called “Initiative” and agreement, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, otherwise all consequences shall be borne by the US side.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347536.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230602_11088743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-02","Mao Ning","Reuters","JPMorgan CEO Jamie Dimon is visiting staff and clients in Taiwan today. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","This is not a matter of foreign affairs. On the Taiwan question, China’s position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347536.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230602_11088743.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-06-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 2 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to reporters’ questions on the 2nd, saying: We firmly oppose any agreement between the United States and Taiwan region that carries sovereign implications or official nature. The DPP authorities, at the expense of Taiwan’s enterprises and the interests of its people, are cobbling together so-called “achievements” in US relations. This is unpopular and will only harm themselves and Taiwan.\nA reporter asked: On June 1, the DPP authorities signed the first batch of agreements under the “US-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative” with the United States. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian responded as above.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230602_12539361.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-06-05","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The US military has said that a Chinese navy ship maneuvered in an unsafe manner near an American military ship in the Taiwan Strait on Saturday, with the distance between the ships reportedly less than 140 meters. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this matter?","The spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has made a statement on this. You may refer to that.\nThe fact is the US side made provocations first and the Chinese side only responded by handling the incident in accordance with relevant laws and regulations. China respects the freedom of navigation and overflight all countries are entitled to under international law. The actions taken by the Chinese military are necessary steps in response to the provocations by the country concerned. These actions are completely justified, lawful, safe and professional. China resolutely opposes the country concerned stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait and is firmly determined to defend its sovereignty and security and regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347537.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230605_11089966.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-05","Wang Wenbin","NBC","Given the close encounter in the Taiwan Strait on the weekend and a recent encounter between US aircraft and Chinese aircraft in the South China Sea last week, should any foreign aircraft or maritime vessel expect the same sort of encounter with Chinese jets or ships when traversing these areas? From China’s perspective, is the message now “this is standard operating procedure or the new norm”?","I’ve shared China’s principled position just now. I would like to quote the response from the Chinese delegation at the Shangri-La Dialogue, who raised this question: why did all the so-called “unsafe” and “unprofessional” incidents – according to US officials – happen near the airspace and territorial waters of China, but not other countries? This deserves some serious thought.\nI also want to stress that China respects the right of navigation and overflight that all countries are entitled to under international law. The Chinese military responded to the situation in accordance with laws and regulations. These actions are completely professional, justified and lawful.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347537.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230605_11089966.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-05","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","We have a question related to the encounter in the Taiwan Strait. The US Navy has released a video showing the Chinese warship crossing in front of the US destroyer in the Taiwan Strait over the weekend. The US calls it an unsafe interaction. Could we have any more remarks on this?","As I said, the US made provocations first and China responded by handling the incident in accordance with relevant laws and regulations. The actions taken by the Chinese military are completely justified, lawful, safe and professional. It is the US that should reflect on and correct its wrongdoing.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347537.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230605_11089966.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-06","Wang Wenbin","AFP","US Republican Party presidential candidate Vivek Ramaswamy has suggested recently that every family in Taiwan should own and be trained to use AR-15 rifles to protect against what he sees as a potential invasion by Beijing. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on these remarks specifically, or more generally, how does it view the tough rhetoric towards China used by many US presidential candidates lately?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. We urge relevant US politicians to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. Taiwan people should not be treated as cannon fodder.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347538.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230606_11090598.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-06","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","On June 5, US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel J. Kritenbrink met with Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu, on which the foreign ministry has released a readout. Do you have more information to share?","China has released a readout on the talks and meeting between Chinese and US diplomatic officials in Beijing. Yesterday, US Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel J. Kritenbrink and White House National Security Council’s senior director for China affairs Sarah Beran visited China. Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Ma Zhaoxu met with them. Director-General of the Department of North American and Oceanian Affairs of China’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs Yang Tao held talks with them.\nThe two sides had candid, constructive and productive communication on improving bilateral relations and managing differences appropriately in accordance with the common understandings between the two presidents reached in Bali last November. China stated its serious position on Taiwan and other major issues of principle. The two sides agreed to maintain communication.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347538.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230606_11090598.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-07","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The European Union has agreed on a new tool that will enable it to place tariffs on countries it thinks are engaging in economic blackmail. This decision comes after China imposed trade restrictions on Lithuania, which has strengthened ties with Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on the EU’s decision?","First of all, China has made our position clear several times regarding Lithuania’s wrongdoing on the Taiwan question. We urge Lithuania to correct its mistake and return to the right path of adhering to the one-China principle at an early date.\nChina and the EU are both victims to US economic coercion. The US has openly coerced the EU and some countries into restricting export of semiconductor manufacturing equipment to China. Such acts of tech bullying severely hinder the development of the semiconductor sector. This not only hurts the interests of China and the EU, but also undermines multilateral trade rules and the global economic order. We hope the EU will stand together with the international community against US economic coercion.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347539.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230607_11091218.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-07","Wang Wenbin","CNR","US Indo-Pacific coordinator Kurt Campbell said on June 6 that episodes like what he called “dangerous” navigation by a Chinese destroyer in the Taiwan Strait showed the need “to prevent circumstances where unintended consequences can have terrible consequences.” US Democratic Senator Ben Cardin said that “what China is doing is against international law”, and “we’ve got to stand up to China’s bulliness; we cannot…","Speaking of bulliness and intimidation, the US knows them better than any other country in the world. It is reported that last year alone, large US reconnaissance aircraft conducted over 800 close-in flights to spy on China. Last year, the US also sent aircraft carrier strike groups to the South China Sea and areas nearby multiple times. Brandishing its military prowess, the US willfully flexes its muscles and infringes upon other countries’ sovereignty. This is what bulliness and intimidation at their best. This is the source of maritime and air security risks and dangers to regional peace and stability.\nFaced with US military provocations, China has responded in accordance with laws and regulations. These actions are completely justified and lawful, and have nothing to do with “bulliness”. When it comes to safeguarding China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, there is no room for China to concede or back down. This is absolutely not a case of “bulliness” or “intimidation”. This is about standing up for principles and China’s red line.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347539.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230607_11091218.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-08","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan activated its air defense system today after 37 Chinese military jets entered the air defense zone of the island. Why did China decide to do this on the same week as it staged the joint air patrol with Russia? Are the two events connected?","I am not aware of what you said. This is not a question about China’s foreign affairs. Taiwan is part of China. We never waver in our resolve and determination to uphold China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity. On the China-Russia joint strategic air patrol, I have stated China’s position just now.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347540.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230608_11093253.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-08","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The US, Taiwan and Japan will share real-time data from naval reconnaissance drones. This is according to the Financial Times citing four people familiar with the project. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this report that the US, Taiwan and Japan will share real-time data?","The one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations, a prevailing consensus among the international community, and the political foundation of China-US and China-Japan relations. The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and is at the core of China’s core interests. We are firmly opposed to any form of military contact between the Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. We urge relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and stop creating factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will firmly safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347540.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230608_11093253.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-09","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The Taiwan “foreign minister” will reportedly make a visit to Europe next week. The “minister” is expected to visit Brussels and also to appear with the Czech president at one event. What is the ministry’s comment on this trip?","Let me first point out that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. There is no so-called “Taiwan foreign minister” but the head of local foreign affairs department.\nThe one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations, a prevailing consensus among the international community and the prerequisite and political foundation for China to develop friendly ties with all countries around the world. We urge the EU to understand the real nature of the Taiwan question and follow through on the commitment it has made to China on the one-China principle. Do not support the Taiwan independence forces or have any official exchanges in any name with the Taiwan region. China never wavers in its resolve of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We also have a clear message for the Taiwan DPP authorities that any separatist moves and attempts to solicit foreign support are bound to fail.\nThe following questions were raised after the press conference:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347541.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230609_11094353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-09","Wang Wenbin","Q","According to reports, an official with the ROK’s Office of the President said on June 7 that recent reports about a Chinese foreign ministry official conveying the “four noes” position during a visit to the ROK are not true. The official also clarified that the reported dialogue between the two sides never happened. The ROK government can continue consultations with the Chinese side on issues concerning the DPRK.…","The current difficulties and challenges in the China-ROK relations are not caused by China. In the recent China-ROK diplomatic consultations at the director-general level, China has clearly and explicitly stated its position and concern. The ROK side is fully aware of this. It should have an in-depth understanding of the crux of the problem, take it seriously and work with China for the sound and steady growth of China-ROK relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347541.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230609_11094353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-09","Wang Wenbin","Q","It was reported that Chinese officials warned ROK officials that if Seoul crosses Beijing’s red line on the Taiwan question and engages in military coordination with Tokyo and Washington, China will suspend high-level diplomatic engagements and cancel cooperation on policies related to the DPRK. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. It is at the core of China’s core interests. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, a matter that must be resolved by the Chinese. The 1992 joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the ROK explicitly states that the Republic of Korea recognizes the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and respects China’s position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China. The ROK needs to act on the spirit of the joint communiqué, adhere to the one-China principle and handle Taiwan-related issues in a prudent way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347541.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230609_11094353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-12","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","It was reported that at an interview with the BBC a few days ago, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs office expressed thanks to the US for providing weapons and helping train military personnel in Taiwan. What is your comment?","For some time now, US politicians have openly said that every family in Taiwan should own AR-15 rifles and the US needs to send Stinger anti-aircraft missiles to arm the island into a “porcupine”. They have also clamored for “destroying TSMC” and making up a “plan for the destruction of Taiwan”. No matter how the US says it “supports” Taiwan, all it really thinks about is how to make use of or even sacrifice Taiwan to advance US interests.\nThe DPP authorities have awarded a US politician who openly advocated the “destruction of Taiwan.” They are willing to serve as pawns and cannon fodder for the US strategy of using Taiwan to contain China. This will only bring deep troubles to Taiwan and push the people of Taiwan to the abyss of disasters.\nWe believe that our Taiwan compatriots will see through the US’s malignant moves that would harm Taiwan and the fact that the DPP authorities are selling Taiwan away. And we believe that our Taiwan compatriots will stand on the side of what is most sacred for the Chinese nation and for historic justice. Taiwan is a dear and inalienable part of China’s territory. We will firmly safeguard our nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely push back at all moves that would harm Taiwan and sell Taiwan away.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347542.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230612_11095228.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-13","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","According to reports, multiple sources have told the US news website The Messenger that driven by concerns over escalation of cross-Strait tensions, the US government is drafting plans to evacuate Americans from Taiwan, which include routes and destinations. Considering that Taiwan is quite sensitive to this, the US hasn’t made it public. What’s your comment on this?","I am not aware of what you mentioned. But I do know that though the US says it supports Taiwan, it has been using Taiwan as a pawn and the Taiwan people as cannon fodder to serve the US strategy of using Taiwan to contain China. The US even has a “plan for the destruction of Taiwan”. I believe the Taiwan people are able to see clearly how the US is actually seeking to harm Taiwan’s interest and even destroy Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347543.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230613_11095920.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-14","Wang Wenbin","Anadolu Agency","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken spoke to Qin Gang on the phone this morning. Can you give any details about the exchange? The US media reported that Blinken will visit Beijing on June 18. Can you confirm that information? Is there any plan for the visit?","State Councilor and Foreign Minister Qin Gang had a telephone conversation with US Secretary of State Antony Blinken at US request this morning. State Councilor Qin pointed out that since early this year, the China-US relations have encountered new difficulties and challenges, and the responsibility for this situation is clear. China has viewed and handled this relationship under the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping.\nState Councilor Qin stated China’s strong position on its core concerns, including the Taiwan question. He stressed that the US needs to respect China’s concerns, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and stop undermining China’s sovereignty, security and development interests in the name of competition. It is hoped that the US will take concrete actions to deliver on the important common understandings between the two presidents in their meeting in Bali and the relevant commitments of the US, work with China to effectively manage differences, promote exchanges and cooperation, stabilize the relationship from further deterioration and bring it back to the track of healthy and stable development.\nAs for the visit you asked about, I have nothing to share at the moment. If we have anything, we will release it in a timely way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347544.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230614_11097381.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 14, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the TAO's regular press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The 15th Straits Forum is about to be held, the first large-scale in-person cross-Strait exchange event since the epidemic. Please introduce the preparation progress, including the Taiwan invited guests and the highlights of this forum.","The State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the Fujian Provincial People's Government, together with 82 cross-Strait entities, will hold the 15th Straits Forum in mid-June, and preparations are basically complete. The Forum's main session is scheduled for the morning of June 17 in Xiamen, Fujian. The Forum has invited representatives of Taiwanese political parties, including the Kuomintang, the New Party, the People First Party, the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union, and the Taiwan People's Party, as well as representatives of Taiwanese host organizations, and more than 5,000 guests from all walks of life, including Taiwanese industry representatives, heads of community organizations, youth, women's and labor groups, township and village representatives, farmers, fishermen, workers, business people, and folk-belief groups. KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan will lead a delegation to attend at the invitation of the Forum.\nThis Forum is the largest cross-Strait civil exchange event held since the COVID-19 epidemic was downgraded to “Category B management.” It continues the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development” and features 37 events in four sections: youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges. Another 14 events will be held concurrently, for a total of 51 events. We welcome media friends to take part in the Forum for interviews and reporting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542260.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation recently said it has invited 50 students from five mainland universities, including Peking University and Tsinghua University, to visit Taiwan in mid-July to hold exchanges with Taiwan university students, but the Mainland Affairs Council has reserved its attitude. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including young people, and they align with the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Strengthened exchanges and interactions among young people across the Strait can inject new vitality and youthful energy into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and this is a good thing. We welcome and support young people on both sides in strengthening exchanges and interactions, enhancing mutual understanding, deepening friendship, and working hand in hand to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly commit to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nWe hope the DPP authorities will face up to the aspirations and needs of young people on both sides, lift all kinds of unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, stop artificially creating obstacles, not be afraid of exchanges between young people across the Strait, and not let students be disappointed or disheartened.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542253.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The seminar “Prospects and Reflections on Cross-Strait Relations” was recently held in Beijing. Please introduce the relevant situation and the outcomes of this event.","On June 5, the Cross-Strait Relations Research Center and the Qingliu Cultural and Educational Association jointly held a seminar titled “Prospects and Reflections on Cross-Strait Relations” in Beijing. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the New Party delegation, and more than 70 guests and scholars from both sides attended. They engaged in exchanges and discussions on two topics, “The Path and Key Choices in Cross-Strait Relations” and “The Trend of Cross-Strait Relations and Working Together,” and achieved positive results.\nDirector Song Tao delivered a keynote speech, saying that we must take Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era as our guide, thoroughly implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, persist in uniting broad Taiwan compatriots, firmly support patriotic and unification forces on the island, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” and promote reunification, and unswervingly advance the great cause of national reunification. At present, cross-Strait relations once again face a choice of path and direction, and we must resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference. Cross-Strait affairs are family matters among Chinese on both sides of the Strait; they should be handled through consultation, and they can certainly be handled well through consultation. On the basis of the One China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we must promote extensive and in-depth consultation with people from all Taiwan parties, sectors, and strata on cross-Strait relations and national reunification, and enrich the practice of peaceful reunification.\nWu Chengdian, Chairman of the New Party, said in his keynote speech that in the process of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, Taiwan should not be absent, cannot be absent, and will not be absent. The New Party hopes that both sides of the Strait will join hands, adhere to the One China principle, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” safeguard peace in the Taiwan Strait, promote consultation on a “two systems” Taiwan plan, promote peaceful reunification, and realize national rejuvenation.\nThrough in-depth dialogue, participants from both sides further pooled their wisdom and reached consensus. Everyone believes that seeking peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the common voice of compatriots on both sides and serves their common interests. Facing the choice between two paths and their prospects, we must adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” which is the foundation for the stable development of cross-Strait relations, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, and seek peace for the Taiwan Strait and well-being for compatriots. We must actively take part in cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, contribute wisdom and strength to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful national reunification, and join hands to realize the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542264.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","It is understood that at the 15th Straits Forum conference, singers from both sides of the Strait will jointly perform the forum's theme song. Please introduce the relevant situation.","In April this year, the organizing committee of the 15th Straits Forum solicited theme songs from across the internet. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait enthusiastically participated, submitting a total of 142 original works. The creators come from 26 provinces, municipalities and regions on the mainland, as well as Taiwan and Hong Kong. They include old and new friends of the Straits Forum, as well as people from all walks of life who hope for peaceful cross-Strait development. There are mainland veteran artists aged 90 and Taiwan veterans aged 88, as well as cross-Strait youth of the “post-90s” and “post-00s” generations. Some cross-Strait married couples composed music together, and some cross-Strait musicians co-created outstanding works. These songs have composed a moving melody of “two sides of the Strait are one family,” and voiced the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides for exchange and integration, and for moving forward hand in hand toward the future.\nThe results of this solicitation and selection were announced on June 7. “We Believe,” with lyrics by Yu Fan and music by Jiang Zhou, was selected as the theme song of the Straits Forum. It will be performed jointly by Taiwan singer Chen Linong and mainland singer Shan Yichun at the 15th Straits Forum conference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, stated at the seminar “Outlook and Reflections on Cross-Strait Relations” that cross-Strait relations are once again facing a choice of road and direction. Please elaborate.","Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the correct path to maintaining peace across the Strait, promoting common development across the Strait, and benefiting compatriots on both sides. It best serves the immediate interests and shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides, and it best conforms to the trend of the times. The facts of the development of cross-Strait relations prove that adhering to the one-China principle and the ‘1992 Consensus’ is the key to ensuring peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Only by adhering to the ‘1992 Consensus’ can cross-Strait relations improve and develop; otherwise, they will fall into tension and turmoil.\nAt present, cross-Strait relations face a choice between two paths and two prospects: peace or war, prosperity or decline. Whether to indulge the forces and activities that deny the ‘1992 Consensus’ and deviate from the path of peaceful development, allowing them to push Taiwan increasingly toward danger, or to uphold national righteousness, adhere to the ‘1992 Consensus,’ and firmly take the path of peaceful development, the question of where to go is one that Taiwan compatriots should think about carefully and choose wisely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The New Party held a press conference on the 9th and released 10 cross-strait policy recommendations, including promoting a “cross-strait common market.” New Party Chairman Wu Cheng-tien said that after visiting the mainland, he felt that both sides should reduce hostility, that the “1992 Consensus” is an attitude, and that if even the “1992 Consensus” is opposed, that is fundamentally a tendency toward “Taiwan…","A delegation from the New Party recently came to Beijing, and Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, met with the delegation and fully affirmed the positive contributions the New Party has long made to promoting the development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland. The delegation engaged in extensive and in-depth exchanges with relevant parties on the mainland and achieved fruitful results.\nThe New Party clearly advocates peaceful reunification, adheres to the “1992 Consensus,” and opposes “Taiwan independence,” which we highly appreciate. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor that stabilizes the Taiwan Strait. Both sides should treasure it all the more, firmly uphold the foundational status of the “1992 Consensus,” jointly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","We have noted that many ancestor-worship exchange activities have recently been organized in various places. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Honoring ancestors and cherishing one’s hometown are fine traditions of the Chinese nation. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to find their ancestral homes and ancestral halls, read their family genealogies, seek their roots, worship their ancestors, and return to their ancestral lineage. On June 3, the Dongguan Taiwan Businessmen’s Children School organized over a hundred teachers and students to pay tribute to the founding ancestor, Emperor Yan Shennong, in Zhuzhou City, Hunan Province, for the 16th time, commemorating the merits of the founding ancestor and carrying forward Chinese civilization. On June 4, 47 members of the Sun clan of Yonghe, New Taipei City, Taiwan, went to the Sun ancestral hall in Gaolin West Village, Xiamen City, Fujian Province, to hold ancestor worship activities. This was the first time since the resumption of the “small three links” that the Taiwan Sun clan brought three generations of grandparents and grandchildren to seek their roots and pay respects to their ancestors. On June 5, more than 200 Taiwan compatriots, including representatives of five grassroots groups such as the Taiwan Youth Home in Guangzhou and ethnic minority representatives, took part in the cross-Strait compatriots’ public ceremony honoring Emperor Shun in Ningyuan County, Hunan Province. On June 13, more than 70 Taiwan compatriots took part in the World Chinese Yan Emperor Hometown Root-Seeking Festival held in Suizhou City, Hubei Province, in the Guimao Year.\nAs Taiwan compatriots have said, the most important meaning of cross-Strait clan exchanges is finding the “source” and the “root.” No matter how far the “sprouts” spread, the source of the descendants is on the mainland. We look forward to more Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to seek their roots and worship their ancestors.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 15th Straits Forum is about to be held in Fujian. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that it prohibits Taiwan civic groups from participating in the organization of the forum, imposes various restrictions and obstacles on Taiwan residents participating in cross-Strait exchanges, and threatens them with so-called “violation of the law.” What is your comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, connected by blood, and they should visit each other often and draw closer. Regarding the Straits Forum, a cross-Strait civil exchange event held for many years, what exactly are the DPP authorities afraid of, and what are they trying to block? On the one hand, they loudly claim they want to “let cross-Strait exchanges resume”; on the other hand, they openly threaten and intimidate Taiwan civic groups and Taiwan residents who participate in organizing and attending the Straits Forum. This is entirely saying one thing and doing another.\nThe DPP authorities are openly infringing upon the basic rights and freedoms of Taiwan residents in this way. How rampant the “green terror” is! We ask: what crime is there in Taiwan residents participating in cross-Strait exchanges? The Mainland Affairs Council alleges that the Straits Forum “opposes independence, promotes integration and promotes reunification.” Which of these three points is prohibited by current regulations in the Taiwan region? What reason does the Mainland Affairs Council have to oppose promoting the development of cross-Strait relations through democratic consultation among all sectors on both sides and resolving issues between the two sides through communication?\nPeace, development, exchange and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and are in their common interest. The holding of the 15th Straits Forum was enthusiastically supported by Taiwan civic groups and people from all walks of life, which fully demonstrates that this is a matter that accords with public opinion and wins popular support. The DPP authorities cannot obstruct or suppress it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542256.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Foreign media reported that, out of concern over escalating tensions across the Taiwan Strait, the US government is drafting a plan to evacuate US citizens in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We have seen the relevant reports, which show one thing: the DPP authorities loudly tout the \"best Taiwan-U.S. relations in history,\" yet the U.S. has long had its own calculations and stands ready to abandon Taiwan at any time.\nFor some time, some American politicians have said they hope for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, yet in fact they keep fanning the flames and pouring on oil: from continuously selling weapons to Taiwan, turning Taiwan into a \"landmine island\" and an \"ammunition depot,\" to formulating so-called \"evacuation\" plans, they have made people see clearly that Taiwan is merely a pawn in the U.S. strategy of \"using Taiwan to contain China,\" and it may become a \"discarded pawn\" at any moment.\nThe United States always follows \"America First.\" The fact that it stirs up trouble around the world, creates division and conflict, and abuses force to pursue its own interests is known to all. Whether in Iraq, Syria, or Afghanistan, the U.S. simply withdrew, reaping benefits for itself while leaving endless turmoil, division, and families ruined. Now the U.S. wants to replicate this approach in Taiwan. Once war breaks out in the Taiwan Strait because of \"Taiwan independence,\" Taiwan will become a battlefield, and Taiwan's ordinary people will only be coerced into becoming \"cannon fodder,\" while Americans in Taiwan will withdraw safely and slip away. Whether the U.S. is \"supporting Taiwan\" or \"harming Taiwan,\" and whether the DPP authorities are \"protecting Taiwan\" or \"endangering Taiwan,\" we believe that Taiwan compatriots will have a clear understanding and rational judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542252.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报记者","Regarding recent reports of Chinese and U.S. warships coming into close contact in the Taiwan Strait, some Taiwan netizens left messages saying, “The fundamental reason for the tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is clear: the United States is creating trouble and crisis,” and “The PLA has the ability to stop external forces from militarily interfering in Taiwan affairs. The DPP should think twice when it pushes…","The relevant departments have already expressed their solemn position on the issues raised in messages from Taiwan netizens. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. We have sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities, in order to “rely on the US to seek independence,” are willing to sell out the interests of the Chinese nation, cater to the US side's fallacious arguments, and cooperate with external forces in hyping the issue. Their “selling out Taiwan” has no bottom line, which is astonishing.\nThe messages from these Taiwan netizens reflect three points. First, Taiwan compatriots have fully felt our firm determination, resolve and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and they understand and support the People's Liberation Army's righteous actions to counter separatism and interference. Second, Taiwan compatriots recognize that US anti-China forces and the DPP authorities are the creators of cross-Strait conflict and the disruptors of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Third, the Taiwan public does not want to be used as “chess pieces,” does not want to be coerced into serving as “cannon fodder,” and only wants peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and a good life through exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Reportedly, the head of the International Air Transport Association (IATA) North Asia region recently said that the civil aviation industry hopes cross-Strait tourism can resume as soon as possible, saying, “Only with resumption will there be exchanges, especially in economic and trade matters.” What comment do you have?","We strongly support cross-Strait aviation operators in substantially increasing cross-Strait routes and flights, with airlines dynamically optimizing flight arrangements on their own. On February 1 this year, the mainland's aviation authority, through the liaison channels under the agreement between the two associations, urged the Taiwan side to give priority to restoring 16 direct cross-Strait destinations, including Guangzhou. On March 9, Taiwan's civil aviation authority stated that it would give priority to restoring 10 regular passenger flight destinations, including Guangzhou. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople eagerly look forward to this, and cross-Strait airlines have also actively submitted applications for resumption.\nIn the most recent week (June 4 to 10), 10 cities, including Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, Chengdu, Shenzhen, Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Nanjing, Chongqing, and Fuzhou, operated a total of 496 cross-Strait passenger flights, carrying 65,028 passenger trips. Although cross-Strait flights and passenger volume have increased significantly compared with during the epidemic, because of the limited number of destinations, overall travel between the two sides remains quite inconvenient. Resumption applications for four destinations, including Qingdao, Wuhan, Ningbo, and Zhengzhou, have still not been approved by the Taiwan side. We hope the Taiwan side will take concrete action, implement its own proposed “Plan for Restoring Cross-Strait Air Passenger Destinations,” and ensure that the relevant cross-Strait destinations resume service as soon as possible, providing convenience for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople traveling between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542250.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","A Taiwan transportation department official said that resuming cross-Strait tourism exchanges has no political considerations and is a matter of reciprocity, and expressed hope to negotiate through the “mini two associations” mechanism. What is your comment?","We have responded to this issue several times. On the question of cross-Strait tourism, there is no so-called “reciprocity” issue, and nothing needs to be negotiated. We have always kept our doors open to group tours and individual travel by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland. The Taiwan side, by contrast, only partially opened to mainland residents traveling to Taiwan in 2008. After the COVID-19 outbreak in early 2020, the DPP authorities unilaterally and comprehensively banned mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, and banned travel agencies on the island from operating group tours to the mainland. None of these measures were negotiated with the mainland side.\nThe mainland's tourism authority announced on May 19 this year that travel agencies would resume operating group tours for Taiwan residents to the mainland. However, the DPP authorities still refuse to lift the ban on island travel agencies operating group tours to the mainland. If cross-Strait tourism is at an impasse, the crux and the obstacle lie with the DPP authorities, and have nothing to do with the cross-Strait “mini two-organization” consultations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542251.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","It is reported that the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee recently passed the so-called “Taiwan Protection and National Resilience Act,” requiring US federal agencies such as the State Department, the Department of Defense and the Treasury Department to formulate a complete sanctions strategy against the so-called “mainland aggression against Taiwan.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and opposing external interference, and safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, is reasonable, lawful and entirely justified. How could this be called \"infringement\"!\nThe Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the foundation of the political basis of China-US relations, and it is the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. The Chinese people do not believe in evil, are not afraid of ghosts, and do not fear pressure. Some people in the US Congress have schemed to play the \"Taiwan card,\" attempting to stir up \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to take risky provocations by enacting some \"bills\" and clamoring for \"sanctions\" against China, in order to obstruct the historical process of China's reunification. This is pure wishful thinking.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230614_12542249.htm"],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that the mainland wants to create a war atmosphere in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election in order to “coerce” Taiwan residents into choosing the party the mainland wants, letting the mainland decide Taiwan's leader and cutting off the path of Taiwan's democracy. What is your comment?","We have never interfered in elections in the Taiwan region. Lai Ching-te's remarks are the DPP's usual routine. Every election, the DPP frames and smears the mainland, stirs up cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and seeks to deceive voters. Who knowingly pursues provocations for “independence” while understanding that “Taiwan independence” means war, and stubbornly insists on them even at the cost of plunging Taiwan residents into the danger of war? Who shouts about so-called “democracy” while running a “green dictatorship” on the island, intimidating and suppressing dissenters? The people of Taiwan know full well. The DPP's old trick of deceiving and fooling Taiwan residents is being seen through by more and more of them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Deng Zhenzhong recently said that although Taiwan's application to join the CPTPP has been opposed by the mainland, it has received support from many countries internationally. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Regarding the participation of the Taiwan region of China in regional economic cooperation mechanisms such as the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle and, under the guise of “economic and trade cooperation,” engage in provocations to seek “independence.” Their true face and their various lies will be increasingly recognized and seen through by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Rosenberger, Chair of the 'American Institute in Taiwan,' visited Taiwan and met with each of the candidates in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election. The island described her visit as an 'interview,' while the US side stated that it will not interfere in the island's elections and firmly supports communication between Taiwan and the mainland. What is your response?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Cross-Strait affairs are a family matter for compatriots on both sides, and of course they should be discussed by family members. On the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to communicate and dialogue with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals on cross-Strait political issues and matters related to advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. We believe that compatriots on both sides of the Strait have ample wisdom and capability to solve our own problems well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","Taiwan entertainer Di Ying recently said in an interview, when talking about cross-Strait relations, as a mother, that she does not want her children to go to war, and worries that if the two sides keep confronting each other, Taiwan will become Ukraine. How do you respond?","I have seen relevant reports, and I have also seen another report. Although the island’s military recruitment standards have recently been lowered, more and more young Taiwanese have said they are unwilling to fight a war for “Taiwan independence.” These are all expressions of public opinion. This fully shows that the people of Taiwan, especially young people, understand very clearly that “Taiwan independence” means the loss of peace and the coming of disaster. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “use force to seek independence” will only make Taiwan even more panicked, and will only meet with greater opposition and resistance from more Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","Lai Ching-te said that on the cross-Strait line, he himself, the DPP, and Tsai Ing-wen are consistent, and Tsai’s “four adherences” position is “very clear, with no room for ambiguity at all.” What comment do you have?","The so-called “Four Insistences” openly deny that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China and are a blatant peddling of the “two-state theory.” No matter how they are packaged or embellished, they cannot conceal the evil intent of seeking “independence” through provocation and splitting the country. Lai Ching-te's remarks further confirm his nature as a so-called “pragmatic Taiwan independence worker” and expose his true face: feigned goodwill, but real pursuit of “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Some DPP figures claim that among the 50 mainland university students invited by the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation for exchange visits to Taiwan, some were selected by mainland university Party secretaries and have a certain political purpose. How do you respond?","Young people are the future of cross-Strait relations. Stronger exchanges and interactions between young people on both sides can inject new strength and youthful vitality into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Some people in the DPP have stigmatized normal exchange activities, politicized the simple identity of students, and racked their brains to set obstacles to exchanges among young people across the Strait. This will only disappoint and chill young students, seriously harm the rights of young people on both sides to strengthen exchanges, and go against the wishes of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Recently, Taiwan media reported that the US military is developing low-cost, long-endurance drones for the Taiwan Strait to carry out strike or electronic warfare missions. What comment does the spokesperson have?","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between our diplomatic partners and the Taiwan region of China. We urge relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently. We warn the DPP authorities that their attempts to rely on external forces to seek 'independence' are doomed to fail, and that their illusion of 'seeking independence through armed force' is even more overestimated, like an egg hitting a stone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Ko Wen-je recently said that, if elected in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election, he would 'prioritize developing cyber troops' and, at an opportune time, 'paralyze the mainland's high-speed rail, ATM (cash machine) and other systems, so that the mainland knows we are capable.' This has sparked debate on the island. What is your comment?","We hope that relevant persons on the island will say more things that are conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and do more things that enhance mutual understanding and trust across the Taiwan Strait, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","First question: According to reports, the DPP authorities are working with the United States to build a so-called “common operational picture,” and Japan will also construct a so-called “new intelligence triangle.” What comment do you have on this? Second question: In recent days, a video of Tsai Ing-wen’s call with the Taiwan Air Force, which was allegedly interrupted by the PLA, has sparked widespread…","On the first question: we firmly oppose any form of military contact between China’s diplomatic partners and the Taiwan region of China. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rely on external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.\nOn the second question: safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and protecting the common interests of people on both sides of the Strait, is the sacred duty of the People’s Liberation Army. Containing “Taiwan independence” separatism and opposing external interference is not just talk; the PLA means it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","Since last year, some Taiwanese food companies have failed to obtain registration in the mainland. The chairman of Taiwan Tobacco and Liquor Corporation recently said that after supplementing documents in February this year, the mainland side returned the application on the grounds that “the wording on the application form does not meet the requirements,” and that the company will not supplement documents again…","We attach great importance to the issue of registration of Taiwan food companies and are handling it actively. Relevant competent departments on the mainland, in accordance with the relevant regulations on registration management of overseas production enterprises of imported food, review the registration materials submitted by Taiwan food companies, and register those that meet the requirements. We actively support cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. If Taiwan companies want to sell products in the mainland market, they must submit materials that meet the requirements in accordance with the regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中国时报记者","It is reported that Taiwan scholar Tsai Chin-shu, suspected of engaging in activities endangering national security, was released from prison last month but still cannot return to Taiwan. Please explain the situation.","Regarding the enforcement of criminal penalties against certain Taiwan residents on the Mainland, relevant departments have handled them in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 'Strait Combo' formed by Chinese tennis player Wang Xinyu and Chinese Taipei tennis player Hsieh Su-wei came from behind to win the women's doubles title at the 2023 French Open final. This is the first time in nine years that athletes from both sides of the Strait have joined hands again to win the women's doubles title at this top international tournament. What is your comment on this?","We extend our congratulations to cross-Strait players Wang Xinyu and Hsieh Su-wei, who together won the championship in the women's doubles final of the 2023 French Open tennis tournament. We also wish this good friend and good teammate pair an even better future. The 'Strait Pair' bringing glory to the nation in international competition is proof that cross-Strait sports exchanges and integration bring mutual benefit and win-win results, and it is a model of young people on both sides striving and sharing in glory. We believe that as cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation continue to expand and deepen, they will certainly bear more fruits of mutual benefit and win-win.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","On June 2, the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) formally entered into force for the Philippines. With this, RCEP has now fully entered into force for all 15 signatories. Since RCEP took effect for China on January 1, 2022, Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland have enjoyed the preferences granted to RCEP members, bringing tangible benefits to these businesses. Please introduce the relevant…","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) accounts for about 30% of the region's total population, GDP, and goods trade value worldwide. With the agreement now fully in effect for its 15 signatories, it marks the entry of the world's largest free trade area, in terms of population, economic and trade scale, and development potential, into a new stage of full implementation.\nRCEP has brought tangible dividends and benefits to a broad range of mainland enterprises. In 2022, mainland enterprises, including Taiwan-funded enterprises, exported goods worth 235.3 billion yuan in RMB under RCEP preferences, enjoying tariff reductions of 1.58 billion yuan in RMB. Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland fully enjoy the tariff and rules-of-origin preferences of RCEP member states and are opening up broader markets. For example, on January 1, 2022, the day RCEP officially took effect, Nanning Fugui Precision Industrial Co., Ltd. immediately applied to the Nanning Customs for export qualifications, and after review and approval, became the first mainland certified exporter to receive the corresponding tariff reduction and exemption benefits after RCEP took effect. We will, as always, strongly support Taiwan businesses and enterprises in achieving stable and good development on the mainland, welcome more Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest and do business on the mainland, and welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to pursue and realize their dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The so-called “U.S.-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative” has completed the signing of its first batch of agreements. Commentators on the island believe that the agreement “only talks about high standards but does not talk about tariff reductions,” and will lead to a sharp increase in imports from the US, which will be quite unfavorable to Taiwan's agriculture. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose the United States and the Taiwan region concluding any agreement with sovereign implications or an official nature.\nThe DPP authorities falsely claim that the agreement “represents a milestone in Taiwan's trade and economic system meeting international high standards,” but in essence it is merely an unfair trade agreement in which “Taiwan makes concessions and the United States benefits.” From beginning to end, the negotiations of this agreement have followed “America First,” guided by the agenda and content set by the United States, and have proceeded entirely according to a script directed by the United States. In exchange for U.S. support of its political self-interest, the DPP authorities have disregarded the interests of enterprises and the public on the island and are engaging in the scheme of “selling out Taiwan for personal glory,” cobbling together so-called “achievements” in relations with the United States. This is bound to be opposed and rejected by far-sighted people in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Reportedly, the US State Department has informed Congress that many weapons with delayed sales to Taiwan cannot be delivered faster. Taiwan’s defense department said it has “confidence in carrying out arms sales operations.” May I ask what comment the spokesperson has on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the US and the Taiwan region of China, and oppose US arms sales to Taiwan. This position is clear and consistent. The DPP authorities' “seeking independence through force” overestimates their own abilities and will only lead to their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Since Honduras established diplomatic relations with China, the results have been fruitful. It is reported that Honduras is seeking to join the New Development Bank of the BRICS countries, which will inject a strong tonic into its long-term healthy economic development. May I ask whether this will affect Taiwan's so-called “diplomatic allies”?","There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a norm governing international relations. Since Honduras established diplomatic relations with China more than two months ago, bilateral relations have started off rapidly and well, benefiting the peoples of both countries. We believe that more and more countries will fully recognize that adhering to the one-China principle is the general trend and the will of the people, and that it serves both the present and the long term.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Graduation season is approaching. Of the nearly 1.42 million college graduates on the island over the past five years, 4% chose to leave Taiwan for development, with the mainland being the most common destination. May the spokesperson introduce the policies and implementation results that ensure Taiwan youth enjoy equal treatment in employment and entrepreneurship on the mainland?","We welcome and encourage Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to develop on the mainland. We have introduced multiple policies and measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, taking the lead in sharing mainland development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots.\nIn terms of study, we provide convenience for Taiwan students who use “Learning Assessment” (xuece) scores to apply to mainland universities. Minnan Normal University and 12 other undergraduate institutions, along with 6 vocational colleges including Fujian Information Technology Vocational College, have piloted enrollment of Taiwan students based on “Unified Test” (tongce) scores, among other measures.\nIn terms of employment, various localities and departments actively support and help provide thousands of positions. For example, on May 26, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau, held the 2023 Beijing Taiwan Students Job Fair, where more than 90 employers, including central SOEs, state-owned enterprises, private enterprises, and foreign-invested enterprises, offered nearly 1,300 employment positions. During the 15th Straits Forum, more than 1,200 employment positions will also be offered to Taiwan youth.\nIn terms of internships, many internship activities for Taiwan students are being held this summer. Shenzhen held the 2023 “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” Taiwan Youth Internship Activity, collecting 1,256 internship positions, with 359 enterprises participating. Jiangsu Province will hold the “Hand in Hand, Heart to Heart, Create the Future — 2023 Taiwan College Students Jiangsu Internship and Employment Training Camp” activity, offering nearly 1,000 internship positions to Taiwan students, covering multiple industries and fields including news and media, healthcare services, legal affairs, information technology, and finance. During the Straits Forum, 1,000 internship and training positions will also be offered to Taiwan youth.\nThe 20th CPC National Congress has charted the grand blueprint for comprehensively building a modern socialist country and comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization. The mainland has vast development space and tremendous development opportunities. We warmly welcome Taiwan youth to actively participate in the building of Chinese-style modernization. As always, we will provide services for Taiwan youth and help them pursue, build, and realize their dreams on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Tsai Ing-wen’s phone conversation with Taiwanese pilots unexpectedly included shouts from the PLA Air Force, which sparked heated discussion. Some members of the public are worried that a military conflict will break out across the Strait. How do you respond?","The concern of Taiwan’s public arises because the risk of war triggered by “Taiwan independence” is rising day by day, and all of these risks stem from the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces colluding with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation. As long as they stop pursuing “independence” and provoking confrontation and return to the correct path of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait relations can return to the track of peaceful development.\nThe Dragon Boat Festival is only a few days away, and I wish everyone a safe and healthy Dragon Boat Festival! (In Hokkien: Go-jit-tsat, everyone stay safe and healthy! In Hakka: Ng-ngiet-tsiet, everyone stay safe and healthy!)\nDo you prefer savory or sweet zongzi? Every debate between the savory camp in the south and the sweet camp in the north is, in fact, a love letter to one’s hometown. We welcome our Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to celebrate the Dragon Boat Festival with our mainland friends and take part in exchange activities in various places. For example, from the 14th to the 26th, Yichang in Hubei will hold the “Cross-Strait Joyful Gathering for the Dragon Boat Festival, Discussing Qu Yuan, Praising the Ancestor of Poetry” Qu Yuan cultural exchange activities, inviting more than 50 descendants and fellow townspeople of the Qu clan from Changhua and Miaoli in Taiwan to Yichang to take part in joint sacrifices to Qu Yuan, dragon boat races, and the “Grabbing the Red” activity. From the 16th to the 22th, various places in Jiangsu will also plan and organize multiple activities to welcome the Dragon Boat Festival. Nanjing will hold the “Same Zongzi, Same Origin, Fragrance Across the Strait” 2023 Third Qixia District Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Youth Dragon Boat Festival Fun Sports Games; Changshu will hold the “Rich Zongzi Fragrance, Cross-Strait Family” zongzi-wrapping friendship event; and Nantong will hold the “Love in Nantong, Our Dragon Boat Festival” exchange activity. It is a very good thing for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to gather together, let traditional festivals continue in different ways, and become a shared memory of people on both sides of the Strait. We hope everyone will take part.\nThank you all. Today’s press conference is concluded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230614_12542234.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-06-16","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Former Secretary of State Henry Kissinger said that he believes military conflict between China and Taiwan is likely if tensions continue on their current course. He does say that he holds out hope for dialogue to de-escalate matters. How does China view Kissinger’s remarks? And is that de-escalation possible?","China-US relations are consequential for both countries and the world. China views and handles its relations with the US in accordance with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping. The US needs to respect China’s core concerns, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs and stop undermining China’s sovereignty, security and development interests in the name of competition. We hope that the US will take concrete actions to follow through the important common understandings reached by the Chinese and US presidents in Bali and the commitments the US has made, work together with China to effectively manage differences, boost exchanges and cooperation, stabilize the relationship from deterioration and bring it back to the right track of sound and steady growth.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347546.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230616_11098980.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-06-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 20 electronic dispatch: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 20th that, on the basis of a comprehensive assessment of the relevant rectification measures, the General Administration of Customs has decided to resume imports of custard apples from Taiwan region starting June 20, and custard apples exported to the mainland must…","Zhu Fenglian said that we adhere to the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” and always respect, care for, and bring benefits to Taiwan compatriots. We are willing to work together with relevant parties on the island to continue helping restore the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230620_12543977.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-06-26","Mao Ning","CCTV","According to reports, a statement from the Taiwan authorities said that the government of Fiji had recently decided to change their representative office in Fiji back to the name of “Taipei Trade Office in Fiji” and to halt its “diplomatic privileges”. What’s your comment?","The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community, a basic norm in international relations, and the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and other countries. The government of Fiji has honored the one-China principle by deciding to correct the name of Taiwan’s representative office in the country and to remove its so-called diplomatic privileges. We welcome this decision. It reflects the fact that there is unshakable, overwhelming support for the one-China principle among the international community. This is also evidence that attempts to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347550.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230626_11103877.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-28","Mao Ning","CRI","According to reports, Bernardo Arevalo, a presidential candidate in Guatemala, said in an interview on June 27 that Guatemala needs to formulate its foreign policy independently based on its national interest. If he wins the election, he will seek to develop friendly relations with China and the Taiwan region on the basis of mutual respect. What’s your comment?","There is only one China in the world. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. We are convinced that more countries will choose to stand on the right side of history and make the right decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of their countries and peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347552.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230628_11104988.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 28, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's regular TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The 15th Straits Forum is the largest cross-Strait civil exchange activity this year, and people on both sides are paying close attention to it. Please introduce what outcomes this Straits Forum has achieved.","The 15th Straits Forum is the largest cross-Strait civil exchange activity since 2020. More than 10,000 compatriots from both sides of the Strait participated in the main forum and 34 series of activities, including more than 5,200 people from all walks of life in Taiwan. The forum achieved fruitful results, which are mainly reflected in the following four aspects.\nFirst, General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter to the Straits Forum for the first time, fully affirming the important role of the Straits Forum in promoting extensive contacts among people from all walks of life across the Strait and promoting civil exchanges and cooperation between the two sides. The letter expounded the great truth that “when the country is good and the nation is good, compatriots on both sides of the Strait will be good,” and declared the policy position of continuing to promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, deepen integrated development in all fields across the Strait, and benefit compatriots in Taiwan, fully reflecting profound concern and care for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The letter has aroused enthusiastic response among attendees, encouraging people from all walks of life across the Strait to hold the Straits Forum even better at a new starting point, and injecting powerful momentum into promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nSecond, the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that “we want peace and development, we want exchanges and cooperation” was fully demonstrated. People from all walks of life in Taiwan, undeterred by the DPP authorities’ repression and intimidation, enthusiastically participated in the forum. The number of party delegations attending reached a record high of all past sessions. More than half of the Taiwan compatriots attending for the first time were “new faces,” more than one-third were Taiwan youth, and 300 Taiwan compatriots registered online to attend the forum. This fully reflects the strong desire of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots for accelerating the restoration and expansion of cross-Strait exchanges.\nThird, the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China introduced major strategic measures, pushing Fujian-Taiwan integrated development to take new steps forward. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, announced at the forum’s main session that the CPC Central Committee and the State Council had formulated the “Opinions on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” and the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone has become a focus of attention. During the forum, Fujian Province offered more than 2,200 internship and employment positions for Taiwan youth, established internship and training workstations for youth from Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macau, and two youth entrepreneurship bases signed cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship mutual assistance and cooperation agreements with the Taiwan association; 10 enterprises focused on the construction of the Pingtan Common Home and signed a strategic cooperation framework agreement; more than 10 pairs of Fujian-Taiwan rural revitalization cooperation projects were matched and signed; three cross-Strait academic society consortia were established in the fields of digital technology, marine affairs, and health, signing 7 science and technology cooperation projects and sharing more than 500 science and technology papers, and so on.\nFourth, a new upsurge in civil exchanges and cooperation across the Strait was set off. The forum activities were rich and colorful, with more than 30 sub-forum activities involving many sectors, including trade unions, youth, women, economy and finance, culture and film and television, health, rural revitalization, farmland water conservancy, village communities, clan and temple organizations, and cross-Strait marriages. Nearly 200 cross-Strait worker representatives, more than 200 representatives of cross-Strait marriage families and mainland spouse groups on the island, nearly 400 cross-Strait martial arts enthusiasts, as well as nearly 1,000 Taiwan township and village representatives and community workers gathered together to discuss cooperation. Twelve cross-Strait women’s organizations signed cooperation agreements. More than 1,000 believers from 100 Taiwan temples, who had not been able to “travel to the mainland” for three years, went to ancestral temples such as Mazu, Guandi, and Kaizhang Sheng Wang to worship. A hundred cross-Strait-themed film and television projects were showcased. The organizers held a call for entries for the forum theme song, and well-known young cross-Strait artists jointly performed the forum theme song “We Believe,” voicing the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to move forward together and create a better tomorrow.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are following the Straits Forum closely, and many friends who were not present joined the topic discussions online. As of June 20, there were 155,580 related domestic commentaries and reports and 6,068 overseas reports and commentaries, with a total online readership of 1.27 billion views. Among them, Toutiao had 400 million reads and 120,000 interactions; Douyin had 630 million plays and 150,000 interactions; and Weibo had 240 million reads. We look forward to the Straits Forum next year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546091.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","On June 17, Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, announced at the 15th Straits Forum that the CPC Central Committee and the State Council had formulated the “Opinions on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Cross-Strait Development and…","At the 15th Straits Forum, Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, announced that the CPC Central Committee and the State Council had formulated the Opinions on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.\nThe Opinions will fully leverage Fujian's unique advantages and pioneering demonstrative role in relation to Taiwan, focus on improving systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment, adhere to a problem-oriented approach, emphasize pilot and trial initiatives, promote more convenient personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan, smoother trade and investment, and the expansion of exchange and cooperation into broader and deeper areas, and build Fujian into a demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development. The Opinions will be published in the near future, so please stay tuned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","At the 15th Straits Forum, saying “long time no see” to each other has become a greeting between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Many Taiwan youth who are “first-time visitors” to the mainland hope to find development opportunities here. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? What cross-Strait youth exchange activities are there in the near future?","Strengthened exchanges between young people on both sides of the Strait can inject new strength and youthful vitality into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We welcome and support stronger exchanges and interactions among young people on both sides, enhancing mutual understanding and deepening friendship, so that more Taiwan youth who come to the mainland for the first time become regular visitors. We also actively provide more opportunities and platforms for Taiwan youth so that they can achieve great things on the mainland.\nNext, various localities will hold multiple exchange activities for Taiwan youth, so please pay attention. In mid-July, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Ministry of Education, the All-China Youth Federation and the Beijing Municipal Government will jointly host the 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Summit in Beijing. From July 12 to 13, the opening ceremony, main forum, and sub-forums on science and education, sports, and innovative talent will be held, with heads of 16 youth organizations in Taiwan and more than 220 youth representatives from various sectors attending on site. During the period, the Cross-Strait Youth Music Carnival Summer Evening Party, the Trendy Play Cultural Tourism Creative Market, the Scientific and Technological Achievements Vitality Exhibition, the Cross-Strait Youth Sports Exchange Camp, and the 2023 Beijing-Taiwan Youth Ride Around Beijing will be held simultaneously. From mid-July to late October, the summit will set up 25 series of activities in five chapters, such as “Building Nests to Attract Phoenixes” and “Integrated Development,” including the “Dancing Beijing-Taiwan, Youth Surpassing the Original” Beijing-Taiwan Youth Basketball Friendship Match and the 8th Beijing-Taiwan Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition. About 1,200 Taiwan youth are expected to participate in the various activities.\nIn late July, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the Jiangsu Provincial Government will jointly host the 2023 Straits Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month activities in Suzhou. This edition of the Youth Culture Month takes “Same Heart, Same Path, Youthful Strength” as its theme and “New Expressions of Traditional Culture” as its main thread, highlighting three “new”s: exchanging innovative development of Chinese culture, telling fresh stories of inheriting cultural lineage, and showing the trendy lifestyle of cross-Strait youth. The opening ceremony and main venue activities will invite more than 600 youth representatives from all sectors on both sides of the Strait to participate. From late July to mid-September, more than 20 activities will be held successively, including the Mei Lanfang Art and Culture Week “Plum Rhyme Through the Ages, Fragrance Flowing Across Both Sides,” the cross-Strait embroidery artisans dialogue meeting “Emotions Tied by a Single Thread,” the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition, and the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival, allowing cross-Strait youth to deeply experience the inheritance and evolution of China’s excellent traditional culture and jointly explore the “new” traditional culture in daily life such as clothing, food, housing and transportation.\nFrom July to August, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots will hold the 20th Taiwan Compatriot Youth Thousand-Person Summer Camp, themed “Inheriting the Dragon Lineage, Youthful China.” From July 3 to 7, the general camp visit and exchange activities will be held in Beijing with about 300 participants. Characteristic branch camp activities will be held successively across the country, covering 28 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities as well as Hong Kong, Macao and other places, with about 1,000 participants in total. The summer camp will focus on inviting Taiwan youth from the island to participate, helping Taiwan youth understand the humanities, history, economic and social development, and achievements in science, technology and culture on the mainland, and providing a broad stage for Taiwan youth to share development opportunities on the mainland and pursue their life dreams.\nWe welcome Taiwan youth friends to actively participate in cross-Strait youth exchange activities. We will continue to pay attention to the thoughts and hopes of Taiwan youth and provide good conditions for Taiwan youth to study, find employment and start businesses on the mainland, helping them chase, build and realize their dreams on the mainland. We also welcome media friends to interview and report on these activities so that they can get to know more Taiwan youth friends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546090.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","Regarding the fact that the Taiwan side has not approved resumption applications for some cross-Strait direct flight routes, the Mainland Affairs Council recently said that it has approved the resumption of the Qingdao route, that airlines have applied for the Wuhan and Ningbo routes, and that no airline has applied for the Zhengzhou route. May I ask whether this is the case?","On June 16, the Qingdao–Taipei air route resumed operations, currently operating 4 flights per week, with 8 round-trip sectors. Passenger flow on cross-Strait routes has steadily increased. In the most recent week (June 18 to 24), 11 cities — Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, Chengdu, Shenzhen, Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Nanjing, Chongqing, Fuzhou and Qingdao — operated a total of 510 cross-Strait passenger flights, carrying 82,636 passenger trips.\nTaiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople have high expectations and strong demand for the resumption of cross-Strait exchanges. Cross-Strait airlines have actively sought to restore cross-Strait routes and destinations, but the DPP authorities continue to obstruct the resumption of relevant destinations. Mainland airlines have repeatedly expressed to Taiwan's civil aviation authorities their willingness to resume destinations such as Wuhan, Ningbo and Zhengzhou and have submitted applications, but all were rejected or returned without processing. We hope the Taiwan side will remove as soon as possible the unreasonable restrictions it has unilaterally imposed, and leave cross-Strait routes and flights to airlines to adjust independently according to the market, so as to meet the travel needs of people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546087.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Regarding the mainland's resumption of imports of sugar apples from Taiwan, the DPP authorities smeared it as the 'Taitung model,' which has sparked public dissatisfaction. Some commentary holds that the DPP's attack reveals the Green camp's high level of anxiety before the election over the possibility of losing the votes of farmers and fishermen. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The DPP authorities neither have the ability to solve problems nor the willingness to consider Taiwan's farmers. They are only accustomed to smearing the mainland and inciting cross-Strait confrontation, and they do not win the people's hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council says that the mainland side's resumption of imports of sugar apples from the Taiwan region is using economic interests to carry out so-called “divide and united front” work against Taiwan. Taiwan's agricultural competent authority says that Taiwan's sugar apple industry has 1,009 supplying orchards and 50 packing plants, but currently only 25 orchards and 3 packing plants have…","We note that when Taiwan's guava imports to the mainland were resumed, farmers on the island were very happy and said one after another that \"a big stone has fallen from our hearts.\" But the DPP authorities are not happy, because they do not care about the interests of farmers on the island. Out of partisan self-interest, they fear that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will grow closer and get along well, so they smear the assistance the mainland provided for resuming imports of Taiwan's agricultural products, maliciously slander the mainland, and incite cross-Strait antagonism. Who is thinking of Taiwan's farmers and who is harming the well-being of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen? We believe Taiwan's farmers and fishermen friends have their own judgment in their hearts.\nWe are willing to work together with people from all sectors of Taiwan who have foresight to provide more assistance for the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546089.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that some Pan-Green politicians are hyping that the word “质量” (quality) appearing in a Taiwan military program is a mainland term. In response, residents of the island said the DPP’s argument is an old trick and very boring. Earlier, some people on the island used the different names for potatoes in the two sides of the Strait, “土豆” and “马铃薯,” to hype up “cultural united front” work by the…","I have seen many netizens on the island describe this matter as ‘boring’ and ‘disgusting.’ In the eyes of the DPP authorities and some Green camp politicians, anything that has even a slight connection to the mainland gets labeled and tagged. In fact, Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, now using mainland terms, eating mainland snacks, watching mainland TV dramas, and singing mainland songs has become a trend and a new way of life. Some DPP politicians cannot keep up with the pace of young people, so they recklessly pin labels on people and shout threats of violence. They will only be abandoned by young people.\nAs cross-Strait exchanges are restored and expanded and cross-Strait integrated development deepens, Taiwan compatriots will gain a better understanding of the real situation on the mainland and will be more willing to take part in cross-Strait exchanges. This is a trend that no one can stop. The more the DPP politicians deliberately scheme to incite cross-Strait confrontation, the more they will provoke greater disgust and opposition among the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","Recently, a US university conducted a public opinion poll on “how confident are you in the US defending Taiwan if conflict breaks out in the Taiwan Strait,” and the results showed that more than 60% of Taiwan residents have no confidence in “US defense of Taiwan.” How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","First, Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. We firmly oppose any words or deeds that interfere in China's internal affairs, and we firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Second, relevant opinion polls show that more and more Taiwan compatriots have seen through the sinister intent of the US side to treat Taiwan as “cannon fodder,” and through the deception that the DPP authorities have painstakingly concocted: “If something happens in Taiwan, the US will come to help.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","For some time, the US side has constantly clamored to enhance Taiwan’s so-called “defense capabilities and reserve forces.” Recently, the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024,” passed by the US Senate Armed Services Committee, proposed a “plan to establish training for Taiwan’s military.” Some foreign media have also reported that US military training of Taiwan’s forces has in recent years…","Recent developments once again show that American anti-China forces and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces are the instigators and behind-the-scenes promoters of the current tensions in the Taiwan Strait. Some American politicians say they hope for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but in reality they are accelerating the arming of Taiwan and intensifying tensions in the Strait. The DPP authorities claim that “war is not an option for Taiwan,” yet they are intensifying their reliance on external forces to pursue “seeking independence through force.” Who is raising tensions in the Taiwan Strait and who is peddling fear of war — we believe Taiwan's people can see this very clearly.\nSome media outlets have sorted out recent military collusion between the United States and Taiwan, which can help everyone see more clearly (image displayed). In July 2022, American politicians proposed that “Taiwan's military service must be extended by at least one year to have combat capability,” and by December the DPP authorities announced that the service period for conscripts would be extended to one year. In December 2022, the U.S. “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023” proposed “ensuring Taiwan's whole-of-society defense mobilization,” and by February 2023 the DPP authorities followed up with a plan to amend the “Total Defense Mobilization Preparedness Act.” In December 2022, the United States stated that it intended to establish a “regional emergency response reserve” for Taiwan, and by March 2023 the DPP authorities confirmed that they were negotiating with the United States to move the East Asia arms reserve to Taiwan. Are these coincidences? Obviously not. With the DPP authorities selling out Taiwan's future and the interests of its people and cooperating without bottom lines, the United States is increasing its arming of Taiwan and accelerating the transformation of Taiwan into a powder keg. Taiwan's young people are becoming sacrifices of the DPP authorities, who depend on and curry favor with the United States, and cannon fodder for “seeking independence through force.”\nThe United States always pursues “America First,” and Taiwan will not be an exception; a “chess piece” will ultimately become a “discarded piece.” We urge the U.S. side to stop military contacts with Taiwan and arms sales to Taiwan, and to stop its acts of “destroying Taiwan” and “harming Taiwan.” We warn the DPP authorities to abandon the illusion of relying on external forces to “seek independence through force,” and to stop their dealings of “selling out Taiwan” and “bringing disaster to Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546086.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","In response to the mainland's announcement that it will resume imports of Taiwan sugar apples (custard apples), Taiwan's agricultural authorities said they hope both sides will continue communicating on quarantine standards and lift the ban on other Taiwan agricultural products, such as pineapples and wax apples, as soon as possible. What is your response? What further arrangements does the mainland have for…","The DPP authorities ignore the problems with the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, and they have no sincerity in solving them. They only engage in political manipulation and smear the mainland, so some problems remain unresolved to this day.\nAgricultural and fishing people on the island have expressed their views through the Kuomintang, relevant counties and cities, and groups, and are willing to take effective rectification measures to ensure the safety of agricultural and fishery products exported to the mainland. We are willing to continue working with relevant parties on the island to help resume the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","During his recent visit to China, US Secretary of State Blinken repeatedly reaffirmed the United States' longstanding 'one-China policy' and stressed that the US does not support 'Taiwan independence.' The DPP authorities declined to comment. Does this US position have a positive effect in restraining the 'Taiwan independence' forces on the island from 'relying on the US to seek independence'?","The US government has made clear commitments on the Taiwan question. It has acknowledged that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is part of China, and that the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing all of China. These commitments are clearly reflected in the three China-US joint communiqués. US President Biden has also repeatedly said that the US does not support ‘Taiwan independence’ and has no intention of using Taiwan as a tool to seek a competitive advantage over China or to contain China. When the heads of state of China and the United States met in Bali last year, the US side reiterated that it does not support ‘Taiwan independence,’ does not support ‘two Chinas’ or ‘one China, one Taiwan.’ During the recent visit of US Secretary of State Blinken, the US side clearly stated that it abides by the commitments made by President Biden, reiterated that it does not support ‘Taiwan independence,’ and said it has no intention of clashing with China.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities that ‘Taiwan independence’ is a dead end. Provoking through collusion with external forces and fabricating the lie of so-called ‘international community support’ cannot deceive the public on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546084.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Recently, Hou Yu-ih, the Kuomintang's candidate in the 2024 Taiwan leadership election, said that the two sides of the Strait are like one family. Earlier, he also said he opposes “Taiwan independence,” and spoke of the two sides sharing the same writing system and the same ethnicity. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","For many years, the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” have enhanced political mutual trust between the two parties, promoted peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and achieved fruitful results. We hope that all sectors on the island will meet us halfway, uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, strengthen dialogue and exchanges, jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","First question: Ma Ying-jeou Foundation Executive Director Hsiao Hsu-tsen said that the Taiwan authorities’ demand that domestic universities submit so-called “security guarantees” for inviting mainland students to Taiwan is an extreme elevation of a security issue, and that the DPP authorities are deliberately obstructing the invitation of mainland students. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question:…","First question: Strengthening exchanges between young people across the Taiwan Strait and enhancing mutual understanding is a good thing and should be strongly supported. The DPP authorities say they value the rights and interests of young people and hope they will make many friends, yet at the same time they fabricate all kinds of pretexts and go to great lengths to obstruct exchanges between young people across the Strait, damaging their legitimate interests. This is completely inconsistent in word and deed, saying one thing while meaning another. Would visits to Taiwan by mainland students endanger Taiwan's security? This fully exposes the “Taiwan independence” nature of the DPP authorities, which deliberately confronts the mainland and intensifies cross-Strait antagonism.\nSecond question: We have noted the widespread dissatisfaction and backlash in Taiwan public opinion over this matter. The so-called “3+1 plan” clearly harms the rights and interests of Taiwan university students. It is obvious that three years of study at university is equivalent to receiving only a junior college education, which brings nothing but harm to Taiwan's students and to Taiwan's future economic and social development. The Taiwan public has every right to ask: Regardless of all else, the DPP authorities insist on extending military service and preparing Taiwan's young people to go to the battlefield. What is their game?\nIn recent years, the DPP authorities have colluded with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at “independence,” undermining the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and causing tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. This is the cause and root of the so-called extension of military service and the “3+1 plan,” and it is also the greatest threat to Taiwan's stability and the welfare of its people. This matter has once again made clear to the broad Taiwan public that without the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, there can be no peace across the Taiwan Strait, and not even the normal studies of Taiwan students can be guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《台海之声》和《看台海新媒体》记者","The June 2013 Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services was signed, but it has been delayed and has not taken effect. Recently, whether to restart cross-Strait services trade and goods trade negotiations has sparked discussion on the island. What comment do you have?","Ten years ago, the two cross-Strait associations, through good-faith communication and equal consultation, signed the 《Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services》. After ten years of trials, more and more people on the island, especially in the industry, have come to recognize that the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services is a mutually beneficial, win-win agreement. It helps strengthen cross-Strait service industry cooperation and create more employment opportunities, helps raise the level of cross-Strait service industries, helps jointly meet the challenges of economic globalization, and helps cross-Strait economies, especially Taiwan's economic development.\nThe Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services has long failed to take effect and be implemented, and the interests of Taiwan's industry and people have been seriously harmed. The reasons are well known.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230628_12546088.htm"],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","A street name in Wuhan, “Taipei Road” and “Taipei Police Station,” has recently drawn discussion on the island. Some netizens noticed that the end of Taipei Road is “Jiefang Avenue,” and some Taiwanese media said it “carries strong implications.” We note that many mainland cities have streets named after different counties and cities in Taiwan, and that cities in Taiwan, including Taipei, have streets and lanes…","Whether on the mainland or in Taiwan, probably the most common identically named roads across the Strait are Zhongshan Street or Zhongshan Road. The street and lane names of a city carry and bear witness to its local history and culture. In Taipei, people walk along Chengdu Road, Luoyang Street, and Xiamen Street; Wuhan has Taipei Road; Qingdao has Kaohsiung Road; Shanghai has Keelung Road; and Nanjing has Hualien Road. Moreover, over the past several hundred years, waves of early settlers crossed the Strait to settle in Taiwan, forming numerous villages with identical names on both sides of the Strait. For example, Taiwan has 9 places named Quanzhou, 4 named Anxi, and 6 named Haifeng, and 26 towns and villages in Chongqing share names with townships in Taiwan. As one netizen put it, “every road is a road home.” Each village with an identical name is a bond of common roots across the Strait. These roads and villages are the homesickness of Taiwan compatriots for the mainland, a historical and cultural link of shared roots and origins across the Strait, and a historical imprint shared by both sides. We look forward to netizens on both sides of the Strait sharing the stories behind these roads and villages together, and discovering Taiwan in the mainland and the mainland in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广网记者","Reportedly, business and industry figures in Taiwan have recently called one after another for restarting cross-Strait services trade and goods trade agreement negotiations, saying that if they can be reached, it would be a great boon to Taiwan’s economy. What comment do you have?","We have noted relevant reports. In June 2010, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” both sides of the Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA). As of the end of 2022, the mainland had cumulatively reduced tariffs on Taiwan products by US$8.52 billion, and 61 Taiwan financial enterprises and 2,065 non-financial enterprises had used the relevant preferential policies to provide services on the mainland. The benefits that ECFA has brought to relevant enterprises and people on the island, including the broad base of small and medium-sized enterprises, farmers, and fishermen, are real and tangible, and everyone can see this clearly.\nECFA merely established a framework for the normalization and liberalization of cross-Strait economic relations. The early harvest list only includes partial tariff reductions on some products and partial opening of some service sectors. Greater dividends are to be reflected in subsequent ECFA agreements on cross-Strait goods trade and services trade. For reasons that are well known, the subsequent ECFA services trade agreement, after being signed, has long failed to take effect, and negotiations on the goods trade agreement have been forced to halt, so ECFA has been unable to benefit more Taiwan compatriots. This is a very regrettable matter.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","Many political parties, groups, and Taiwan youths on the island participated in the 15th Straits Forum. Lai Ching-te said of this, “This is helping others count money.” What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te's remarks fully expose his arrogance toward the public and his disregard for public opinion. They also reveal his true face of feigned goodwill and genuine “scheming for independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Recently, nine provinces including Fujian have planned to participate in the Taipei Summer Travel Fair. Can this be interpreted as goodwill from the mainland in signaling the resumption of cross-Strait tourism?","We support the strengthening of exchanges and cooperation between tourism industries on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to travel and sightsee on the mainland. It is understood that tourism industry representatives from nine mainland provinces will be invited to attend the Taipei Summer Travel Fair in Taiwan on July 14. Through their participation in the exhibition, Taiwan compatriots will be able to see the new look of mainland tourism development under the new circumstances and learn about more new tourism products and routes. Relevant authorities in Taiwan should face squarely the wishes and expectations of the broad Taiwan public and the tourism industry, and lift as soon as possible the unreasonable restrictions on group tours to the mainland for Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Regarding resuming negotiations on the cross-Strait services trade agreement, Hou Yu-ih and Ko Wen-je have both recently mentioned it, and the MAC also proposed in April hoping to “take up the unfinished parts gradually.” Under what conditions can this be advanced further?","The authority of consultations authorized to the two associations and of the agreements they reach should be upheld, and the foundation of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations must not be undermined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","The Mainland Affairs Council has said that certain individuals on the island who took part in the cross-Strait joint ancestral worship of Fuxi violated the “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” and will investigate and punish them. What is your comment?","Fuxi is the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation, revered by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Since 2014, Gansu Province has held the joint sacrificial ceremony to Fuxi for ten consecutive years, with active participation from civil circles in Taiwan, demonstrating the shared national sentiment and national identity of Chinese descendants on both sides. On June 22, the 2023 (Guimao Year) cross-Strait joint sacrificial ceremony to the humanistic ancestor Fuxi was held simultaneously in Tianshui, Gansu and New Taipei City, Taiwan. About 500 people from all walks of life on the island attended the on-site event in New Taipei City. It must be pointed out that honoring the dead with care and remembering one's ancestors is a fine tradition of the Chinese nation. Yet the DPP authorities have even wantonly accused and suppressed Taiwan civil groups and individuals who took part in the Fuxi sacrificial ceremony, once again exposing their nature of pursuing “independence” and their ugly face of forgetting their ancestry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Regarding the resumption of negotiations on the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement, Lai Ching-te said that “we should not again accept the backward path toward the mainland.” Some people on the island worry that resuming negotiations on the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement will cause Taiwan to over-rely on the mainland market. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","The Cross-Strait Services Trade Agreement is one of the follow-up agreements to ECFA. It is a mutually beneficial and advantageous good agreement that helps raise the level of opening of cross-Strait service industries and promote their better development. It benefits cross-Strait operators to the greatest extent, especially Taiwan’s small and medium-sized enterprises and people, and brings greater development space and more opportunities to Taiwan operators. The DPP, to seek political self-interest, deliberately obstructed the entry into force of the Cross-Strait Services Trade Agreement. This directly deprived Taiwan compatriots and enterprises of the development opportunities they should have enjoyed and seriously damaged their development interests. For Taiwan, where the service industry accounts for a very high share of the economy, the promoting effect of the agreement on the economy is self-evident. The DPP authorities refuse to repent, stubbornly engage in political manipulation, and continue to slander and smear the Services Trade Agreement. No wonder their related remarks have been dismissed by island media as “fallacies.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The “Cross-Strait Agreement Oversight Act” has failed to pass Taiwan's legislature for many years. What is your comment on the DPP's long-standing technical obstruction of cross-Strait consultations?","Our position on cross-Strait consultations and negotiations has been consistent and clear. As long as the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” is upheld, there is no obstacle to exchanges with us for any political party or group in Taiwan. As long as the DPP authorities abandon the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait consultations and negotiations can resume.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202306/t20230628_12546080.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-06-29","Mao Ning","AFP","According to reports, the Taiwan authorities recently turned down applications by officials of nine provinces on China’s mainland to participate in a tourism fair in Taipei. Do you have a response to this?","This is not a question about China’s foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347553.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230629_11105673.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-29","Mao Ning","TASS","Vedant Patel, Principal Deputy Spokesperson of the US State Department, said on Wednesday that a visit by members of Congress to Taiwan does not mean a change in the US’s Taiwan policy. This is not Executive Branch travel, he said, adding that the US is not seeking to incite tensions or to change the status quo. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. We firmly oppose any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan authorities. All US government bodies, including the executive, legislative and judicial branches, should act on the foreign policy the US government has affirmed and committed itself to. The US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and refrain from sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347553.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230629_11105673.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-30","Mao Ning","Reuters","Two questions on New Zealand. Firstly, how would you characterize the China-New Zealand relationship? And second, New Zealand has on a number of occasions voiced its concerns about the treatment of Uyghurs in Xinjiang, democracy protests in Hong Kong and the situation in the Taiwan Strait. How do you feel about the country voicing those views?","China and New Zealand are each other’s important cooperative partners. The sound and steady growth of bilateral relations serves the interests of both countries and is conducive to regional peace, stability, development and prosperity.\nWe stand ready to engage in dialogue and exchanges with all parties on the basis of equality and mutual respect, but we oppose interference in internal affairs under the pretext of relevant issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347554.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230630_11106169.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-06-30","Mao Ning","Reuters","The US State Department has approved the potential sale of ammunition and logistics supply support to Taiwan in two separate deals valued at up to USD 440 million, according to the Pentagon. Do you have any comment on this?","China is firmly opposed to US’s military ties with and arms sales to Taiwan. This position is consistent and unequivocal. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop selling arms to Taiwan, stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait and stop posing risks to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347554.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202306/t20230630_11106169.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-06-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, June 30 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on June 30, saying that more and more Taiwan compatriots have clearly recognized that the US is turning Taiwan into a “powder keg” and “ammunition depot.” This is by no means “protecting Taiwan” or “defending Taiwan,” but rather “harming Taiwan” and “ruining Taiwan.” The DPP authorities are spending the hard-earned money of Taiwan compatriots to curry favor with the US, which will only push Taiwan compatriots into the abyss of war and danger. Facts have repeatedly proven that “Taiwan independence” has no way out, and “seeking independence by relying on the United States” is a dead end.\nA reporter asked: According to media reports, a relevant US government department recently decided to sell arms to the Taiwan region of China worth about US$440 million. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said, “We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose US arms sales to Taiwan. This position is clear and consistent. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop any form of US-Taiwan military contact, and not go further and further down the wrong and dangerous path.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202306/t20230630_12546820.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-07-03","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, on June 30, the US Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Mark Milley said at an event of the National Press Club that China wants “to be the regional hegemonic in Asia within the next 10 years” and “exceed global US military power by midcentury.” The People’s Liberation Army is developing its military capabilities with a plan of “unification with Taiwan by 2027.” The US should optimize such…","Some in the US with evil intentions misrepresent facts and has constantly hyped up the “China military threat” narrative. They are in fact creating excuses for their efforts of arms expansion, maintaining military hegemony and sabotaging regional peace and stability and finding ways to stoke tensions in the Taiwan Strait and use Taiwan to contain China.\nI want to point out that China has always pursued a national defense policy that is defensive in nature and stays committed to peaceful development. China’s military growth means a stronger force for world peace and is conducive to safeguarding peace and stability in the Asia Pacific and beyond. Realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of the Chinese people and we will strive for the prospects of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and efforts. Meanwhile, we will never allow anyone or any force to separate Taiwan from our motherland.\nWe urge the US to stop smearing China, stop dangerously ramping up military build-up, stop manipulating the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and safeguard regional peace and stability with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347555.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230703_11106909.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-04","Mao Ning","CCTV","Recently, surveys in China and the ROK show that people in Pacific Rim countries oppose the release of nuclear-contaminated water into the sea. People staged large-scale rallies in the ROK and protested in front of Japanese embassies and consulates in the Philippines, New York and Sydney, demanding that Japan stop pushing forward the ocean discharge plan. The Fukushima Prefectural Federation of Fisheries…","I noted relevant reports. The Japanese government’s pushing ahead with the ocean discharge plan has raised widespread concerns and worries from the international community. A Global Times survey conducted in 11 countries including China, the ROK, Japan, the Philippines and New Zealand indicates that of the 11,000 respondents, nearly 90 percent showed worries, fear and anger toward the plan, and more than 90 percent of them support their countries in taking measures to intervene in Japan’s ocean discharge plan.\nRegrettably however, the Japanese government has been stubbornly pushing through its ocean discharge plan and trying every means to give the false impression that the discharge is legitimate and justified. The IAEA will issue the review report later today. I would like to point out that the agency was invited by the Japanese side and its mandate is limited to evaluating the ocean discharge plan. The report cannot greenlight the discharge as it cannot prove that ocean discharge is the only option or the safest and most reliable option.\nChina once again urges Japan to, in a responsible attitude for the whole humanity and our future generations, stop pushing through the discharge plan, fully explore and evaluate the alternatives to ocean discharge to ensure that the nuclear-contaminated water is handled in a scientific, safe and transparent manner, and agree to rigorous international oversight.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347556.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230704_11107582.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-07-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 4 (electronic dispatch): Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 4th, saying that from 2008 to 2016, the two sides of the Strait established mutual trust on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” jointly created a situation of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, and brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides. We are willing to maintain positive interaction with political parties on the island, including the Kuomintang of China, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to consolidate and enhance mutual trust, strengthen exchanges and communication, promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nA reporter asked: On the 3rd, Hou Yu-ih, a candidate of the Kuomintang of China in the 2024 election for the leader of the Taiwan region, responded to a Taiwanese media interview by stating for the first time his position on the “1992 Consensus.” What is your response and comment? Chen Binhua made the above remarks.\nHe pointed out that the “1992 Consensus” was reached in 1992 through consultations between ARATS and the SEF of Taiwan, after authorization by each side. The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, which clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. It is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and a “divine needle” anchoring peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230704_12547741.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-07-05","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","It was reported that the first group of Honduran students left Taiwan and arrived in the Chinese mainland on July 4 for their new life of studying. What is your comment?","After China and Honduras established diplomatic relations, China pledged its readiness to accept all Honduran students in the Taiwan region. Over the past three months or so since then, the two sides have worked together with great efficiency to coordinate the matter. Yesterday, the first group of 26 Honduran students left Taiwan and arrived in Beijing, Tianjin, Xi’an and other mainland cities to continue their studies. We extend our warmest welcome to them. The Honduran students are looking eagerly forward to studying in the Chinese mainland, where they will make full use of the curriculum on campus, get steeped in the Chinese culture, and contribute to the development and progress of their home country as well as friendly exchanges between Honduras and China. We welcome more Honduran students to China’s mainland to pursue their education and stand ready to work together with the Honduran side to expand people-to-people exchange and cooperation and build a bridge of friendship to bring our two peoples closer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347557.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230705_11108739.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-07-05","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, on 29 June local time, the U.S. State Department approved the sale to Taiwan of ammunition and logistics support with a total value of US$440 million. What comments do you have on this?","China firmly opposes the US selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China, and has lodged stern representations with the US. The US has disregarded China's core concerns, brazenly interfered in China's internal affairs, and deliberately escalated tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is tantamount to accelerating the transformation of Taiwan into a “powder keg” and pushing Taiwan's people toward the abyss of disaster.\nWe demand that the US abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop arms sales to Taiwan, stop any form of US-Taiwan military collusion, and genuinely honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and not go further down the wrong and dangerous path. Whether it is the US “using Taiwan to contain China” or the DPP authorities “seeking independence through force,” both are delusional and doomed to fail. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains at a high state of vigilance, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly upholds peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2023/07/05/10485940.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-07-07","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","According to reports, Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Hirokazu Matsuno said yesterday that Chinese and ROK nuclear power plants had released into the sea liquid wastes with relatively high concentration of tritium. The standard Japan sets in this regard is much stricter than other countries including China and the ROK. Japan will explain its plan of releasing the Fukushima nuclear-contaminated water into the sea…","Japan deliberately compares the Fukushima nuclear-contaminated water with water released by nuclear power plants in normal operation across the world. With such disguised replacement of concept, it is seeking to mislead public opinion.\nIt doesn’t take an expert to see the fundamental difference between the nuclear-contaminated water that came into direct contact with the melted reactor cores in the Fukushima nuclear disaster and the water released by nuclear power plants in normal operation, the latter never having direct contact with reactor cores. No comparison can be drawn between the two as they come from different sources, contain different radionuclides and require different levels of sophistication to handle. In particular, the IAEA didn’t assess the efficacy and long-term reliability of Japan’s treatment facilities and therefore cannot guarantee that all nuclear-contaminated water will be up to standard after treatment in the next 30 years. Japan’s attempt to make an issue of normal water discharge from operating nuclear power plants is aimed at whitewashing its ocean discharge plan and misleading the international community under the disguise of science.\nWe have also noted that Japan has devised other tricks to sell the nuclear-contaminated water as something safe and harmless, for example, by launching a cute mascot representing radioactive tritium and coining the pseudo-scientific term “treated water.” Its sole purpose is to downplay the hazard of the nuclear-contaminated water. But no matter how Japan tries to dress up the ocean discharge plan, it’s impossible to get away with it under the sharp eye of the world. No matter what Japan says, the nuclear-contaminated water cannot be turned into normal water, nor can Japan walk away from the consequences and responsibility of dumping the water into the sea.\nOnce the water is released into the ocean, there is no way to take it back. It’s like opening Pandora’s box. We urge Japan to stop shifting responsibility, earnestly respond to the international community’s legitimate concerns, stop pushing forward the ocean discharge plan, and handle the nuclear-contaminated water in a truly science-based, safe and transparent manner after conducting thorough consultation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347559.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230707_11109960.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-10","Mao Ning","AFP","Paraguayan President-elect Santiago Pena plans to visit Taiwan this week to strengthen the country’s friendship with Taipei. Does China have any response to this planned visit?","There is only one China in the world and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It has the overwhelming support of the international community and represents the trend of the world. We believe relevant country will recognize the trend of the world sooner or later and make the right decision consistent with the trend of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347560.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230710_11110822.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-11","Wang Wenbin","TASS","Taiwanese island media published a report claiming the US has urged island military to construct a new Biosafety Level-4 laboratory to “secretly establish virus research and development capabilities.” Do you have any comments on that?","China has been clear and consistent about its opposition to US-Taiwan military engagement. If the report you cited is true, this is further evidence that the U.S. has malignant designs for Taiwan and the DPP authorities is simply selling Taiwan away.\nTaiwan is a sacred and inalienable part of China’s territory. We will firmly safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely push back all moves that would harm Taiwan’s interests and sell Taiwan away.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347561.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230711_11111465.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-07-11","Chen Binhua","国台办发言人陈斌华11日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 11 — TAO spokesperson Chen Binhua, answering reporters’ questions on the 11th, said: On April 12, 2023, at the request of relevant mainland chambers of commerce, the Ministry of Commerce launched, in accordance with law, a trade barrier investigation into the trade restrictive measures that Taiwan imposes on the mainland. The investigation is currently proceeding in an orderly…","Chen Binhua said: We welcome relevant Taiwan trade associations, chambers of commerce, and enterprises to participate in this survey, to reflect their views and positions and to safeguard enterprise interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230711_12549706.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-07-12","Chen Binhua","国台办发言人陈斌华11日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 11 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions on the 11th and introduced that, at the invitation of the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation, Hao Ping, Party Secretary of Peking University, plans to lead 36 teachers and students from five mainland universities, including Peking University, Tsinghua University, Fudan…","Chen Binhua said that this visit is the first group visit by mainland universities to Taiwan in more than three years, which is of positive significance for promoting the restoration of two-way cross-Strait exchanges. We hope the exchange visit by the mainland university faculty and student delegation in Taiwan goes smoothly. We support and encourage stronger exchanges between young people across the Strait, enhancing understanding through interaction, learning from each other, and joining hands to create a bright future.\nIn late March and early April this year, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led a delegation to the mainland to pay respects to ancestors and visit. During exchanges and seminars with faculty and students of Wuhan University, Hunan University, and Fudan University, which are 3 universities, he repeatedly expressed hope that mainland university faculty and students could also visit Taiwan for exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230712_12549733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-07-13","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","China carried out military drills around Taiwan the past couple of days, which coincide with the NATO summit in Lithuania. Is China sending a message to NATO not to interfere in the Taiwan issue?","I’d refer you to competent authorities on the specific question you asked.\nLet me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Chinese people will never waver in our resolve and determination to uphold China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347563.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230713_11112793.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-07-13","Chen Binhua","13日就目前对4家企业有无新的处理态度答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 13 — In August 2022, the mainland side decided to take punitive measures against the “Taiwan Democracy Foundation” and the “International Cooperation and Development Foundation,” institutions linked to hardline “Taiwan independence” elements. Mainland organizations, enterprises and individuals are prohibited from conducting any transactions or cooperation with enterprises that…","Chen Binhua said: We firmly oppose the affiliated enterprises and financial backers of “Taiwan independence” diehards profiting on the mainland. The disciplinary measures against the other three enterprises remain unchanged.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230713_12550405.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-07-17","Mao Ning","Reuters","William Lai from Taiwan is reportedly making a stopover in the US en route to Paraguay next month. Does the ministry have any comment on this?","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, firmly opposes any visit by “Taiwan independence” separatists to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and firmly opposes the US’s conniving with and supporting the “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities in any form. We have lodged serious representations with the US side.\nThe Taiwan question is the very core of China’s core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in the China-US relations. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitment including not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will closely follow the situation and take resolute and strong measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347565.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230717_11114255.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-17","Mao Ning","AFP","New Zealand’s prime minister said today that his country is concerned about a worsening strategic environment and rising tensions in the Indo-Pacific region, in particular, in places like the South China Sea and Taiwan strait. He said “we look to China to play its part to manage tensions.” Does the Chinese foreign ministry have any comment？","China is a member of the Asia-Pacific. We have always worked with other countries in the region to practice true multilateralism and safeguard peace and stability in the region. We would like to enhance dialogue and exchanges on the basis of mutual respect with New Zealand and other countries, and jointly play our part to uphold stability and prosperity in the region.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. To ensure peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, the most important and crucial thing is to uphold the one-China principle. The South China Sea has been generally stable. We hope relevant countries will respect regional countries’ effort to uphold peace and stability in the South China Sea.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347565.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230717_11114255.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-19","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan’s William Lai will transit the US in August. Does China plan to conduct military exercises or take similar measures in the Taiwan Strait in response to the “visit”?","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, firmly opposes any visit by “Taiwan independence” separatists to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and firmly opposes any form of US connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities.\nThe Taiwan question is the very core of China’s core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in the China-US relationship. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, and stop sending a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will continue to closely follow the situation and take resolute and strong measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347567.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230719_11115197.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-07-20","Chen Binhua","国台办发言人陈斌华19日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 19 (electronic dispatch): In response to the DPP authorities’ announcement that Lai Ching-te will “transit” through the United States in August, TAO spokesperson Chen Binhua, answering reporters’ questions on the 19th, said: We firmly oppose Lai Ching-te using the name of a “transit” to carry out a sneaky visit that is in reality “relying on the U.S. to seek independence,” and we…","Chen Binhua said that we firmly oppose any “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. We believe that compatriots in Taiwan will increasingly see clearly that the so-called “pragmatic ‘Taiwan independence’ workers” are the “troublemakers” of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230720_12552164.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-07-24","Mao Ning","Yonhap News Agency","Recently, many suspicious international packages have been found across the ROK. The Taiwan authorities claim that the packages were from China’s mainland and reached the ROK via Taiwan. The ROK foreign ministry said it has asked China for confirmation. Has China launched an investigation into this?","We have received the ROK’s request for assistance in the investigation. The matter is being looked into. We will stay in touch with the ROK.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347570.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230724_11117071.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-07-25","Mao Ning","China News Service","During a recent interview with a UK media organization, Japan’s State Minister of Defense Toshiro Ino claimed that if the Chinese mainland takes military action on Taiwan, Japan very possibly will provide Taiwan with some kind of support, not sure though whether it is going to be in the form of defence equipment or logistical support. Do you have any comment on this?","Taiwan is China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no interference by any external force. The remarks of the incumbent high-level official of Japan’s defence department constitute blatant interference in China’s internal affairs in disregard of the basic norms governing international relations and the principles set out in the four political documents between China and Japan and have a damaging effect on the political foundation of China-Japan relations. China strongly disapproves of and firmly opposes this and has made serious démarches to Japan.\nFor half a century, Japan exercised colonial rule over Taiwan and committed notorious crimes against the Chinese people. Given the grave historical responsibilities Japan bears for those crimes, it is all the more important for Japan to act prudently and draw lessons from the history. What makes Japan think it is in a position and has the confidence to make such unwarranted remarks on Taiwan? I want to stress that the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all the sons and daughters of the Chinese nation and an unstoppable historical trend. No one shall underestimate the strong resolve, will and capability of the Chinese people to defend the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge Japan to stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question. Those who play with fire will eventually get burnt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347571.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230725_11117587.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-07-27","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. House of Representatives recently passed the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024,” which includes measures such as accelerating the provision of asymmetric weapons to Taiwan and inviting Taiwan to participate in the RIMPAC exercise. In addition, the Monterey Talks between the U.S. and Taiwan in early July reached agreement on Taiwan's procurement of U.S.…","The United States explicitly acknowledged in the \"August 17 Communiqué\" that there is only one China in the world, that Taiwan is part of China, and that the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legal government representing China; it explicitly committed not to pursue a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan and to gradually reduce arms sales to Taiwan until the issue is ultimately resolved. However, the United States has repeatedly reneged on its commitments, has for a long time frequently carried out arms sales to Taiwan, and has strengthened military ties with the Taiwan region of China. These despicable actions seriously undermine China's national sovereignty and security, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and pose major strategic risks to China-U.S. relations and to military-to-military relations between the two countries' armed forces. China expresses serious concern and firmly opposes this.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no foreign interference whatsoever will be tolerated. Taiwan's security depends on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and \"Taiwan independence\" and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Any words or actions advocating strengthened U.S.-Taiwan military ties or arms sales to Taiwan will only push up the tensions in the Taiwan Strait and the risk of conflict and confrontation; in essence, they harm and ruin Taiwan. We urge the United States to stop selling weapons to Taiwan and to halt U.S.-Taiwan military contacts, and not to make one mistake after another on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities are attempting to \"rely on the United States to pursue independence\" and, by colluding with external forces, to turn Taiwan into a \"landmine island\" and an \"ammunition depot.\" Facts have proven that \"Taiwan independence\" and external interference are the greatest threats to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the greatest calamity to the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people. The People's Liberation Army of China is closely monitoring the situation in the Taiwan Strait and will continue to take decisive and forceful measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16246401.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-07-28","Mao Ning","CCTV","According to reports, the Japanese defense ministry released its Defense of Japan 2023 white paper on July 28. The white paper hypes up China’s military threat, raises concern over China’s build-up of defense capabilities and maritime and air military activities, and plans to further increase Japan’s defense budget to strengthen defense capabilities. The white paper also hypes up tensions across the Taiwan Strait…","The Defense of Japan 2023 white paper gravely interferes in China’s internal affairs, smears China’s normal defense development and maritime and air military activities, deliberately hypes up the “China threat” narrative, and creates tensions in the region. We deplore and reject this and has made serious démarches to Japan.\nChina is committed to the path of peaceful development and a defense policy that is defensive in nature. China’s defense development and military activities are legitimate and justified. Our military cooperation with relevant countries including joint patrols is consistent with international law and customary international practice. Taiwan is China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The so-called “military balance” across the Taiwan Strait is a groundless subject to begin with. On the Taiwan question, Japan bears grave responsibilities for the historical crimes committed against the Chinese people and should act all the more prudently and draw lessons from the history.\nI need to stress that given Japan’s history of militarist aggression during the last century, Japan’s military and security moves have been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. In recent years, Japan has been increasing defense spending, readjusting defense policy and seeking military breakthrough. It has triggered strong concerns over whether Japan will still stick to the path of peaceful development. We urge Japan to earnestly respect the security concerns of neighboring countries, deeply reflect on its history of aggression, stop hyping up so-called security threat in the region and finding pretexts for rearming itself, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the wider international community through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347574.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202307/t20230728_11119206.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-07-29","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Japanese government has adopted the 2023 Defense White Paper, which positions China as Japan’s “greatest strategic challenge ever faced,” says China has substantially increased its defense spending and accelerated military development, has “unilaterally changed the status quo” in the East China Sea and South China Sea, and that China and Russia have conducted joint operations in the sea and airspace around…","Japan's new edition of its *Defense White Paper* clings to a mistaken perception of China and deliberately hypes up the so-called “China military threat.” It smears and sensationalizes the normal development and military activities of the Chinese armed forces, brazenly interferes in China's internal affairs, and stirs up regional tensions. We firmly oppose this and have lodged stern representations with the Japanese side.\nThe Chinese armed forces have always been a firm force for safeguarding world peace and stability. They have never challenged anyone, let alone threatened anyone. On the contrary, in recent years Japan has repeatedly breached the constraints of its “Peace Constitution” and the principle of “exclusively defense-oriented defense,” substantially increased its defense expenditure, touted the development of so-called “counterstrike capabilities,” and gone further and further down the path of military expansion. It has followed certain major powers in forming targeted “small circles,” posing serious challenges to peace, security and stability in the region and the world.\nChina is a firm defender and builder of international maritime rule of law, and its position on maritime issues has been consistent and clear. At present, the situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea remains generally stable. Certain countries, for their own selfish interests, have frequently dispatched vessels and aircraft to relevant waters to flaunt their military might, seriously aggravating regional tensions. China-Russia defense cooperation is built on the basis of non-alignment, non-confrontation and not targeting any third party. It is committed to safeguarding regional and world peace and stability and poses no threat to any country.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. The one-China principle concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations and is an inviolable bottom line. On the Taiwan question, Japan bears grave historical responsibility toward the Chinese people. In recent years, instead of reflecting on itself, it has not only continuously interfered in China's internal affairs, violating the basic norms of international relations, but also contravened the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents and undermined the political foundation of China-Japan relations, further heightening tensions in the Taiwan Strait region. This is extremely wrong and dangerous.\nWe urge the Japanese side to deeply learn the lessons of history, stop irresponsible words and deeds, abandon the zero-sum confrontational mindset of beggar-thy-neighbor, establish a correct perception of China, keep its promises on major issues such as Taiwan, exercise prudence in the military and security field, and take concrete actions to bring bilateral relations back onto the right track.","","http://www.news.cn/world/2023-07/29/c_1129775227.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-07-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, July 29 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions on the 29th, saying that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, attempt to “seek independence by relying on the United States” and “seek independence by force,” constantly beg the United States to sell them weapons or provide military aid, and strengthen military collusion with the US military. Their conduct is turning Taiwan into a “powder keg” and “ammunition depot,” and aggravating the danger of war in the Taiwan Strait. If the DPP is allowed to go down a dead-end road, young people can only become cannon fodder.\nA reporter asked: According to media reports, the US government has decided to provide military assistance worth about US$345 million to the Taiwan region of China. What is your comment? Chen Binhua made the above remarks in answering. He said, “We firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. This position is clear and consistent.”\nChen Binhua said, “‘Taiwan independence’ is a dead end. No matter how much taxpayers’ money of Taiwan compatriots the DPP authorities and ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces spend, or how many American weapons they buy, they cannot shake our firm resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland, nor can they withstand our strong capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202307/t20230729_12554947.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-08-01","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the White House website recently announced that it will provide Taiwan with military assistance worth $345 million, including equipment and training. This is the first time the Biden administration has used the “Presidential Drawdown Authority” to provide assistance to Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","The United States has provided military assistance to Taiwan region of China, brutally interfered in China's internal affairs, seriously undermined China's sovereignty and security interests, and gravely threatened peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose this and have lodged serious representations with the US side.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's core interests and is an insurmountable red line in China-US relations. Some forces in the United States, driven by a hegemonic mindset and Cold War thinking, have continuously strengthened US-Taiwan military ties through vicious acts such as arms sales, military aid, and joint training, condoning and encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to make trouble and provoke confrontation, which has aggravated cross-Strait antagonism and tensions in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the US side to stop all forms of US-Taiwan military collusion and not to go further and further down the wrong and dangerous path. The wheel of history for China's unification rolls forward, and no person or force can stop it. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is closely monitoring the situation in the Taiwan Strait, remains on high alert at all times, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguards peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/2023-08/01/c_1129779812.htm","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-08-03","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲3日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 3. In response to the DPP authorities' announcement of Lai Ching-te's schedule for a “transit” sneak trip to the United States in mid-August, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 3rd, saying: We firmly oppose Lai Ching-te's sneak trips to the United States under any pretext and in any form, and we firmly oppose any form…","Zhu Fenglian said that Lai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and has openly declared himself a “pragmatic ‘Taiwan independence’ worker.” The purpose of his “transit” through the United States is to “rely on the United States to seek independence.” It is a fulfillment of his “Taiwan independence” pledge to “enter the White House,” and an effort to gain personal electoral advantage. In the end, it is the interests of the island’s people that will be harmed, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region that will be undermined. Facts will prove that Lai Ching-te is a “troublemaker” through and through.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230803_12556277.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 4 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on the 4th, introducing that to further promote closer exchanges among cross-Strait youth and to work together in unity and cooperation, the 11th Straits Youth Festival centralized activities, sponsored by the State Council TAO, the All-China Youth Federation, and the Fujian Provincial People’s Government, will be held in Fuzhou, Fujian, from August 5 to 13. During the centralized activities, events will include the Straits Youth Festival Summit, the 7th Cross-Strait College Student Leadership Camp, the Cross-Strait Youth Camp Gathering, the Straits Meteorological Youth Forum, the “Good Times · Gathering in Fuzhou” 2023 Fujian-Taiwan Youth Talent Study Camp, the 2023 Cross-Strait Breakdance Competition, and other activities.\nZhu said that this year’s Straits Youth Festival takes “Stand Up and Shoulder Responsibility, Co-create Well-being” as its theme, encouraging cross-Strait youth to live up to the times, advance hand in hand, and jointly create the long-lasting well-being of the Chinese nation. Throughout the year, 35 activities will be held, covering digital economy, rural revitalization, talent exchange, meteorology and environmental protection, intangible cultural heritage inheritance, internships and employment, innovation and entrepreneurship, and many other fields. The first event launched in May. So far, eight events have been held, with nearly 1,000 Taiwan youths participating. Throughout the year, more than 3,000 Taiwan youths are expected to take part in the Straits Youth Festival, and during the centralized activities, the number of participants expected to come to Fuzhou for the conference is 1,400.\nShe pointed out that this year’s Straits Youth Festival features higher participation and broader coverage, striving to become a vibrant cross-Strait youth carnival and a high-level event that is digital, platform-based, and standardized, showcasing the bright prospects of cross-Strait youth integrated development. It actively explores new development patterns and paths for cross-Strait youth to deeply integrate into development, and accelerates efforts to help Fujian build a “first home” for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises coming to the mainland and to build a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone.\nZhu said that since its founding in 2013, the Straits Youth Festival has always been rooted in, served, and benefited cross-Strait youth. It has played an important role in helping Fujian explore new paths for Straits integrated development and build a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone. Over the past ten years, 265 cross-Strait youth exchange activities have been held cumulatively, attracting more than 30,000 cross-Strait youths, including 17,000 Taiwan youths, of whom “first-time visitors” account for more than 50%. Through the Straits Youth Festival platform, cross-Strait youths have joined hands in common purpose, deepened their friendship, sought development together, discussed the future together, and jointly created a new pattern of cross-Strait youth integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230804_12556639.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","发言人朱凤莲13日就赖清德“过境”窜美答记者","Beijing, August 13 (Xinhua): Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on August 13 about Lai Ching-te's “transit” sneaking into the US.\nA reporter asked: Lai Ching-te arrived in New York today, sneaking into the US under the name of a “transit.” What is your comment?","Zhu Fenglian said that we have repeatedly stated our position regarding Lai Ching-te's “transit” slipping into the US. We firmly oppose Lai Ching-te's slipping into the US on any pretext and in any form, firmly oppose Lai Ching-te's “relying on the US to seek independence,” which harms Taiwan, and firmly oppose the US side indulging and supporting “Taiwan independence” elements and their separatist conduct in any form.\nZhu Fenglian said that Lai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and claims to be a “pragmatic ‘Taiwan independence’ worker.” For the purpose of deceiving votes, under the pretext of “transit,” he is engaging in going to the US to sell out Taiwan and seek personal gain. This harms the interests of the people on the island and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan region. He is a thoroughgoing “troublemaker.”\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are utterly incompatible. The conduct of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces runs counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island, which wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. In the end, it will only push Taiwan toward a perilous situation of war and danger, bringing profound disaster to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230813_12558748.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-14","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","A political scholar in Guatemala shared the analysis that the Seed Movement party candidate Bernardo Arevalo is very likely to win the second round of voting and he will recognize the one-China principle and establish diplomatic ties with China after being elected. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. The fact that China has diplomatic relations with 182 countries fully shows that establishing diplomatic ties with China is the right choice that accords with the trend of history and our times.\nChina is Guatemala’s second largest source of imports and fifth largest destination of exports. Recognizing the one-China principle and developing relations with China serves the fundamental interest of Guatemala. It is what its people want. We believe that Guatemala will choose the right side of history and make the right decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the country and its people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347575.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230814_11126620.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-14","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","I’d like to ask about the visit last week to Taiwan by three lawmakers from the Baltic states, one each from Estonia, Lithuania and Latvia. Does the foreign ministry have any comment about such a visit by the three lawmakers from the Baltic countries?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes all forms of official interaction between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We urge relevant parties to abide by the one-China principle, refrain from sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and take concrete actions to safeguard the sound and steady development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347575.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230814_11126620.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-15","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Does China plan to launch new war games or major military exercises, once William Lai returns to Taiwan on Friday?","Lai Ching-te clings stubbornly to the separatist position for “Taiwan independence”. He is a troublemaker through and through. The US and the Taiwan authorities arranged for Lai to engage in political activities in the US in the name of having a “stopover”. This seriously violates the one-China principle, and gravely undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The fact once again shows that the fundamental cause of the continued tensions in the Taiwan Strait is the Taiwan authorities’ attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence” and that the US is bent on using Taiwan to contain China.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of the core interests of China, the bedrock of the political foundation of China-US relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist activities and stop fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle. China is closely following the developments of the situation and will take resolute and strong measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347576.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230815_11127065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-15","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","According to a Japanese lawmaker who accompanied Taro Aso, Vice President of the Liberal Democratic Party and former Prime Minister of Japan, on his visit to Taiwan, Aso had discussed his remark in Taiwan about “a readiness to fight” and “deterrence” with the Japanese government beforehand, and the remark is in line with Japan’s official view. What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. China has made serious démarches to Japan over its certain politician’s visit to Taiwan and his irresponsible remarks.\nJapan illegally occupied Taiwan, exercised colonial rule over the region for half a century, and committed atrocious crimes. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the U.S. and the U.K. in 1943 made it clear that Taiwan and all the other territories Japan stole from China shall be restored to China. Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation in 1945 reaffirms this. The Instrument of Surrender signed by Japan in 1945 says explicitly that Japan accepts the Potsdam Proclamation. The China-Japan Joint Statement signed in 1972 when the two sides normalized diplomatic relations states that the Japanese government fully understands and respects the position of the Chinese government that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and declares the commitment to Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation. In 1978, the two countries concluded the Treaty of Peace and Friendship between China and Japan, which affirms the principles set out in the joint statement in legal form. The third and fourth political documents concluded in 1998 and 2008 respectively both reiterate Japan’s commitment to the position on the Taiwan question stipulated in the joint statement. Japan has more than once made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question, including not supporting “two Chinas”, “one China, one Taiwan” or “Taiwan independence”, and only maintaining people-to-people and region-to-region exchanges with Taiwan. Those are the historical context of the issue, and the principles and position that Japan must abide by.\nI wish to stress that the Taiwan question bears on China’s core interests, the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and basic trust and principles between the two countries. Japan needs to adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and take concrete action to honor its political commitment and related statements. China is ready to take all measures necessary to firmly safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347576.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230815_11127065.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-08-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 15 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 15th, saying that Lai Ching-te is incorrigible and this time used “transit” to travel to the United States and clamor for “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies. This again shows that Lai is a “‘Taiwan independence’ worker” in the full sense of the term, a “troublemaker” through and through, and that his so-called “peaceful” rhetoric is entirely a lie. Such a person can only bring war and danger to Taiwan.\nA reporter asked: Lai Ching-te accepted an interview with Bloomberg of the United States and spread “Taiwan independence” remarks. What is your comment on this? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230815_12559488.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 16: The Ministry of Commerce recently issued an announcement implementing provisional anti-dumping measures on polycarbonate imported from the Taiwan region. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 16th, saying that this is a normal anti-dumping investigation case. The competent authorities will adhere to the principles of fairness and justice, strictly follow laws and regulations, conduct further investigation, and make a final ruling. We hope the enterprises involved will actively cooperate and expand into the mainland market in a lawful and compliant manner.\nZhu Fenglian introduced that, as understood, on October 8, 2022, the Ministry of Commerce received an anti-dumping investigation application submitted by relevant mainland enterprises. In accordance with the provisions of the “Anti-Dumping Regulations of the People's Republic of China,” on November 30, the Ministry of Commerce issued Announcement No. 35 of 2022, initiating an anti-dumping investigation on polycarbonate originating in the Taiwan region. Based on the investigation results and relevant laws and regulations, the Ministry of Commerce issued a preliminary ruling announcement on August 14, 2023, determining that polycarbonate originating in the Taiwan region is being dumped, and decided to implement provisional anti-dumping measures on the above products in the form of a security deposit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230816_12559814.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-18","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","It was reported that during August 12 to 18, deputy leader of China’s Taiwan region Lai Ching-te “stopped over” in New York and San Francisco. What is your comment?","The US insisted on arranging two “stopovers” for Lai Ching-te. This has seriously violated the one-China principle and undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and sent a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns this.\nThe one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community and a basic norm governing international relations. It is also the prerequisite and basis for the establishment and development of diplomatic ties between China and the US. In the three China-US joint communiqués, the US made a clear commitment of maintaining only unofficial relations with Taiwan. As the deputy leader of the Taiwan region, Lai describes himself as a “pragmatic worker for Taiwanese independence”. What he said and did in the US over the past few days proved once again that he is a “Taiwan independence” separatist through and through. By allowing him to engage in political activities in the US, propagate separatist propositions for “Taiwan independence” and use it to upgrade official interaction and substantive relations with Taiwan, the US has once again exposed its calculations of saying one thing but doing another, following a strategy of using Taiwan to contain China, and fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of the core interests of China, the bedrock of the political foundation of China-US relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. The pursuit of “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere. Those who connive at and support “Taiwan independence” will eventually get burnt.\nChina again urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” or “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, stop all forms of official interaction with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive exchanges with the region, stop conniving at and supporting separatist forces seeking “Taiwan independence” and their separatist activities and stop obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle. China must be reunified, and will surely be reunified. Any attempt of holding back China’s reunification is doomed to fail. China will take strong measures to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347579.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230818_11128713.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-08-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 18 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on August 18, saying: According to the preliminary investigation results of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan, the Taiwan region's trade restrictive measures against the mainland do not conform to the ECFA's requirements to promote the normalization, institutionalization, and liberalization of cross-Strait economic relations, and violate the ECFA provisions on “gradually reducing or eliminating tariff and non-tariff barriers on substantially all trade in goods between the two sides.” We support the relevant competent authorities in studying and taking corresponding measures in accordance with relevant regulations, in light of the investigation of trade barriers.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Commerce recently announced the latest progress of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan, and stated that it would study, in accordance with relevant regulations, suspending or partially suspending the tariff preferences granted to Taiwan products under the ECFA. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe said that the preliminary investigation results of the Ministry of Commerce's investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan show that the DPP authorities have unilaterally restricted the import of large quantities of mainland products, which is suspected of violating WTO rules such as the “non-discrimination principle” and the “principle of general elimination of quantitative restrictions,” and has harmed the interests of relevant mainland industries and enterprises, and also harmed the interests of Taiwan consumers. Cross-Strait enterprises and trade associations participating in the investigation have called on the Taiwan region to promptly lift its trade restrictions against the mainland.\nZhu Fenglian said that in June 2010, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” both sides of the Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) across the Taiwan Strait. The ECFA is a special arrangement reached to promote the normalization, institutionalization, and liberalization of cross-Strait economic relations, and its entry into force and implementation has brought real benefits to enterprises and people on both sides of the Strait, especially in Taiwan. Since the DPP authorities took office, they have not only failed to take concrete measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but have continually escalated them. For example, when this investigation was initiated, it involved 2,455 products, and during the investigation this was adjusted to 2,509 products.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230818_12560257.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 19: The New Party held events on August 19 to celebrate its 30th founding anniversary. TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on the 19th, saying: We congratulate the New Party on its 30th anniversary. Over the past 30 years, the New Party has openly advocated the peaceful reunification of both sides of the Strait, firmly upheld the one-China principle and the ‘1992 Consensus,’ resolutely opposed ‘Taiwan independence,’ and made positive contributions to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nZhu Fenglian said that the situation across the Taiwan Strait is currently complex and grave, and Taiwan is facing a critical choice between two paths and two prospects: peace or war, prosperity or decline. We hope the New Party will continue to uphold national righteousness, adhere to the one-China principle, resolutely oppose ‘Taiwan independence’ separatism and external interference, actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, unite broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and jointly promote the peaceful reunification of the motherland, create lasting welfare for the Chinese nation, and share the glorious honor of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230819_12560513.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-21","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Japan, Korea and the US in a joint statement over the weekend criticized the “dangerous and aggressive behavior supporting unlawful maritime claims that we have recently witnessed by the People’s Republic of China (PRC) in the South China Sea.” They also affirmed the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as an indispensable element of security and prosperity in the international community.…","The trilateral summit of leaders of the US, Japan and the ROK at Camp David smeared and attacked China on Taiwan and maritime issues—an act of gross interference in China’s internal affairs, a deliberate attempt to sow discord between China and our neighbors and a serious violation of norms in international relations. China deplores and strongly opposes this and has made solemn démarches to relevant parties. We have also noted that the US says the trilateral partnership is not against anyone. We urge it to match its words with actions and act on its statement that the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China, stop smearing China’s image and harming China’s interests, and stop creating division and confrontation and undermining regional peace and stability.\nWe see two trajectories in the Asia-Pacific today. One features efforts to advance solidarity, cooperation and economic integration. The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) and the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) are two examples. The other features attempts to stoke division and confrontation and revive the Cold War mentality. Examples include exclusionary groupings such as AUKUS, the US-Japan-ROK partnership and Quad, to name just a few. Regrettably, the US has been missing in the former and all examples in the latter are centered around Washington DC.\nThe Asia-Pacific region is a promising land for peace and development. It should not be turned into a boxing ring for major power rivalry, still less a battlefield of a cold war or hot war. Attempts to stoke a new Cold War in the region will be met by firm rejection of regional countries and peoples. Those who seek to establish and maintain hegemony in the region are doomed to fail. We urge relevant countries not to go against the trend of the times, stop replicating the bloc confrontation elsewhere in this region, and stop pursuing selfish gains at the expense of other countries’ strategic and security interests and the wellbeing of people in Asia-Pacific.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving it is a matter for the Chinese. We strive for peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort, but we will never allow interference in China’s internal affairs using “peace” as a false pretext by anyone or any force. The greatest threat to cross-Strait peace is “Taiwan independence” forces and foreign connivance and support for their activities. If relevant countries do care about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they need to abide by the one-China principle, stop conniving at or supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, and protect regional peace and stability through concrete action. No one should underestimate the determination, resolve and capability of the Chinese people in safeguarding China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nChina has indisputable sovereignty over the Nanhai Zhudao (islands in the South China Sea) and the adjacent waters. China’s construction on its own territory and China Coast Guard’s action to protect China’s rights and enforce the laws in waters under China’s jurisdiction are legitimate, lawful and beyond reproach. As a state party to the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), China always abides by international law including UNCLOS and does not accept or recognize the illegal arbitral award on the South China Sea. In recent years, the US has gone to great lengths to interfere in the South China Sea issue. It has encouraged and supported certain countries’ violation of other countries’ maritime rights and sowed discord between countries in the region, which makes the US a disrupter and saboteur of the regional order. The US, together with its allies, frequently conducted military exercises and close-in reconnaissance in waters around China, including the South China Sea, to flex muscles and intensify tensions in the region. The US has become the biggest threat and challenge to regional peace and stability. China will continue to firmly defend its sovereignty and security interests, work with ASEAN countries to fully and effectively implement the DOC, promote steady progress in COC consultations, carry out practical maritime cooperation, and firmly uphold peace and stability and boost development in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347580.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230821_11129636.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-21","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Bloomberg aired an interview with Lai Ching-te a few days ago, in which Lai propagated “Taiwan independence” fallacies. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te’s propagation of “Taiwan independence” fallacies in a so-called “exclusive interview” at the time of his “stopovers” in the US reveals once again what kind of person he is—someone who has no qualms about betraying the interests of his nation to advance his selfish agenda and brazenly soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence”, and a stubborn, out-and-out “Taiwan independence” separatist and troublemaker.\nIn the interview, Lai claimed that “Taiwan is already a sovereign, independent country”, “it is not necessary to declare independence”, Taiwan is “not part of the People’s Republic of China”, and the two “are not subordinate to one another”. They are sheer lies and blatant provocations. Just recently, Lai openly claimed his ultimate goal is for the leader of Taiwan to “walk into the White House”, which says enough about the extremely dangerous nature of Lai as a “Taiwan independence” separatist. There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China—this has been so since ancient times. The historical context and legal facts to support that are crystal clear. Though the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are yet to be reunified, Taiwan’s status as part of China’s territory has never changed and must not change. China’s sovereignty over Taiwan has never changed and will not change. As of today, 182 countries in the world, including the US, have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. The US government has repeated time and again that it will not support “Taiwan independence”. How would Taiwan possibly have “sovereignty”? Taiwan has never been a country and will never be a country.\nLai claimed that he hopes democratic countries will support Taiwan for its participation in international affairs so that Taiwan can better contribute to the international community. This is a familiar gimmick of using “seeking participation in international affairs” as a pretext to engage in political manipulation. Taiwan, as part of China, has no basis, reason or rights whatsoever to join an international organization whose membership requires statehood. The Chinese government had, however, based on the prerequisite of upholding the one-China principle, made proper arrangements for the Taiwan region’s participation in the World Health Assembly (WHA) and the ICAO Assembly. Yet the DPP authorities have been bent on pursuing “Taiwan independence” and refusing to accept the 1992 Consensus, which means the political foundation for Taiwan to take part in the WHA and other international activities no longer exists, and the relevant arrangements cannot continue as a result. The DPP authorities’ repeated manipulation of health, Covid response, aviation safety and other issues is never about caring for the wellbeing of the people in Taiwan, but about trying to expand “international space” and make “diplomatic” breakthroughs. How would that possibly “contribute” to the international community? During this year’s WHA, nearly 140 countries publicly supported China’s position, and the proposals about Taiwan were once again rejected. This once again shows that the one-China principle has overwhelming international support and represents the trend of the world. The DPP’s attempts to gain sympathy by playing the underdog and use “democracy” as a cover for its separatist activities are nothing but wishful thinking, and will only end in failure.\nWhat Lai has been doing—accusing the mainland of posing “threats”, creating a false impression of “international support” in the name of “democracy”, and roping relevant countries in to support “Taiwan independence” propositions—these are all familiar pages from DPP’s old playbook of hyping up antagonism to manipulate elections. Lai claimed that Taiwan will work closely with the international community to deepen “democracy” and that the US Congress will continue to support Taiwan. This is essentially to trick the international community into cheering for his campaign, and to play up to external forces so that they would support his separatist agenda. This is all theatrics staged by Lai Ching-te again to hug the US close and solicit its support for “Taiwan independence”. It lays bare Lai’s true identity as a “practical worker for Taiwanese independence”. Lai thought he could use “pragmatism”, “democracy” and “peace” as a cover to stop others from questioning his pursuit of “Taiwan independence”, but he can never truly hide his separatist agenda. What he does will only bring grave harm to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It will only push Taiwan towards the danger of military conflict and lead our Taiwan compatriots to disaster.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Soliciting US support for “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere for “Taiwan independence” separatists. We will work with the international community to firmly uphold the one-China principle, firmly safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity and firmly oppose the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign connivance and support for such activities. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving complete national reunification is the shared aspiration of all the Chinese people and a historical trend that cannot be changed. China must and will be reunified.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347580.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230821_11129636.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-08-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 21 dispatch: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said on August 21 that, to prevent risks at the source, the General Administration of Customs has decided to suspend, starting August 21, 2023, the import of mangoes from the Taiwan region into the mainland. The mainland has notified the Taiwan side through the contact channel of the “Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Quarantine and Inspection Cooperation Agreement,” and has required the Taiwan side to further improve its plant quarantine management system. The above measures are normal biosecurity precautionary measures, scientific and reasonable, and in line with relevant mainland laws, regulations and standards.\nZhu Fenglian said that since the beginning of this year, mainland customs has intercepted the quarantine pest 大洋臀纹粉蚧 (Dayang tunwen fenjie) in mangoes imported into the mainland from the Taiwan region. Once this pest enters, it will pose a serious threat to the mainland’s agricultural production and ecological security.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230821_12560916.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-22","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The plenary meeting of the Central American Parliament on August 21 local time adopted the resolution of revoking the “permanent observer status” of the so-called “Legislative Yuan” of the Taiwan region and accepting the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. What’s China’s comment? Will China consider becoming a permanent observer of the Central American Parliament?","China welcomes and commends the resolution of the Central American Parliament to revoke the “permanent observer status” of the so-called “Legislative Yuan” of the Taiwan region and accept the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. This again shows that the one-China principle represents the unstoppable trend of the times and has the overwhelming support of the people. China stands ready to develop friendly cooperation with the Central American Parliament on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347581.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230822_11130236.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-08-22","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲22日答记者","BEIJING, August 22 (Xinhua) — The Central American Parliament recently passed a resolution to remove the so-called “permanent observer” status of the Taiwan region’s legislature and to admit the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer to the parliament. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on the 22nd, saying that “we appreciate…","Zhu Fenglian said: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community, and it reflects the will of the people and the general trend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230822_12561305.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-24","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","According to reports, the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said on August 23 that the US State Department has approved the possible USD 500 million sale to Taiwan of infrared search and track systems for F-16 fighter jets, as well as other equipment. What’s your comment?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. Such sales seriously violate international law and basic norms governing international relations, undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, harm peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and send gravely wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and firmly opposes them.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately cancel the planned arms sale to Taiwan, stop arms sales to and military contact with Taiwan, stop following the dangerous trajectory of arming Taiwan, and stop undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China will take resolute and strong measures to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347583.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230824_11132235.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-08-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 24 — TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters’ questions on the 24th, said: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan, China. The DPP authorities are trading the hard-earned money of Taiwan compatriots for weapons and engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities; this will not buy “security.”\nA reporter asked: According to media reports, the U.S. government recently decided to sell a military sales package worth approximately 500 million U.S. dollars to Taiwan, China. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above remarks in response.\nZhu Fenglian said: If the DPP authorities go all the way down the dead-end road of “relying on the United States to seek independence” and “using force to seek independence,” they will only bring the horrors of war to the Taiwan Strait and push the compatriots of Taiwan into a dangerous situation. The DPP authorities should immediately stop acts that harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots for political self-interest and endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230824_12562036.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-25","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲25日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 25 (Electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters' questions on the 25th, said: We have noted the so-called “plan” on cross-Strait tourism and exchanges recently issued by the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan. This “plan” has no clear implementation date. In name it is “restoration,” but in fact it refuses to lift restrictions; in name it is…","Zhu Fenglian said that in the field of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges, the mainland side has always encouraged and supported relevant cross-Strait industry sectors in carrying out exchanges and cooperation in various forms. Mainland enterprises, regardless of size or category, may invite Taiwan businesses for exchanges and business negotiations at any time, with no limits on the number of people or length of stay. The DPP authorities' “plan” specifies the exhibition booth area for Taiwan enterprises down to the square meter, limits the length of stay of mainland personnel in Taiwan down to the day, and, for Taiwan enterprises inviting mainland personnel to Taiwan for business study tours, divides enterprises into tiers according to annual turnover and sets graded invitation quotas. The strictness and meticulous detail of the restrictions on enterprises on the island and on mainland personnel traveling to Taiwan are astonishing. It is clearly “keeping people a thousand li away” — nominally “opening,” but in reality “blocking.” The DPP authorities have gone to great lengths and racked their brains to obstruct and restrict normal cross-Strait exchanges. It is absurd and goes against popular sentiment.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that “we want peace and development, we want exchanges and cooperation” is the common wish and voice of the broad masses of Taiwan people. The DPP authorities attempt to use a so-called “plan” to deceive the public and conceal their true face of obstructing exchanges between all sectors of Taiwan and the mainland. We believe Taiwan compatriots see this very clearly and will not be deceived or misled. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to steer cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, and truly realize the normalization and routinization of cross-Strait tourism and two-way exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230825_12562369.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-08-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 29 dispatch: TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, answering reporters' questions on the 29th, said that to further facilitate cross-Strait personnel exchanges, starting August 30, travelers who shuttle between the two sides of the Strait or third places and transit through Taiwan to enter the mainland will no longer be required to undergo antigen or nucleic acid testing before entry.\nA reporter asked: On August 28, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced adjustments to the entry quarantine measures for personnel coming to China. Are there new adjustments to the epidemic prevention and control measures for personnel traveling between the two sides? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response when answering the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202308/t20230829_12563209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-08-30","Wang Wenbin","TASS","A report by the UK’s House of Commons Foreign Affairs Committee says Taiwan is an “independent country”. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and the political foundation of China-UK relations. The relevant report of the British parliament blatantly referred to Taiwan as “an independent country”, which distorts the facts and is totally misleading. We urge the relevant committee of the British parliament to abide by the one-China principle, observe international law and the norms governing international relations, respect China’s core interests, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, take concrete actions to fulfill the UK’s political commitments on the Taiwan question and maintain the sound and steady growth of the China-UK relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347587.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230830_11135654.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-31","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The latest 2023 map released by China shows a 10-dash line in the South China Sea including two dashes east and southeast of Taiwan. In the map submitted by China to the UN in 2009, there were just 9 dashes. Malaysia, India as well as the Philippines have protested against this new map. Why is there a difference in the line on maps now currently released and the one in 2009?","China’s position on the South China Sea is consistent and clear. The competent authorities of China routinely publish standard maps of various types every year, which aims to make standard maps available to all sectors of society and raise public awareness of the standardized use of maps. We hope parties concerned can view it in an objective and rational light.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347588.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230831_11136284.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-31","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The Biden administration has for the first time approved a direct US military aid to Taiwan under an assistance program aimed at foreign governments. Do you have any comment on this?","The US decision to provide weapons to China’s Taiwan region under the so-called Foreign Military Financing used for sovereign states seriously violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. This move seriously violates international law and basic norms governing international relations, undermines China’s sovereignty and security interests, harms peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and sends gravely wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and firmly opposes them.\nThere is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop enhancing military contact with the Taiwan region or arming it by any means or under whatever pretext, stop creating factors that could heighten tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and stop conniving at and supporting the separatists’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” by force. No one should underestimate the determination, resolve and capability of the Chinese people in safeguarding our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347588.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230831_11136284.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-08-31","Wang Wenbin","Associated Press of Pakistan","According to media reports, on August 8, three former service chiefs of the Indian army, air force and navy visited Taiwan and attended a security dialogue organized by Taiwanese authorities. Do you have any comment on that?","China firmly opposes all forms of official interaction between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic relations with China. This is our consistent and clear position. We hope the country concerned will abide by the one-China principle, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and refrain from having any form of military and security cooperation with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347588.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202308/t20230831_11136284.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","During this year's Shangri-La Dialogue, the Chinese and US defense ministers did not hold a bilateral meeting. In addition, senior US military officials repeatedly requested calls, which were rejected. Public opinion generally holds that China-US military exchanges have been suspended, and this has caused great concern in the international community. May I ask whether China plans to resume exchanges with the US…","First, I must point out that military exchanges between China and the United States are not in a state of suspension; the two sides maintain candid and effective communication through military diplomatic channels. But it must also be acknowledged that the current state of military relations between the two countries does indeed face many difficulties and obstacles, and this situation is entirely caused by the United States. For some time now, the United States has clung to a mistaken perception of China, engaging in unreasonable containment and suppression of China; it has brutally interfered in China's internal affairs, sold and provided weapons to Taiwan, and developed military relations with Taiwan; and it has frequently deployed sea and air forces, strengthening military provocations and deterrent pressure around China's periphery. In addition, the United States also refuses to lift its unreasonable sanctions against leaders of the Central Military Commission. Under these circumstances, the Chinese military has every reason to take resolute countermeasures. We often say that communication cannot be without principle, and dialogue cannot be without bottom lines. For the United States to hope to damage China's national interests on one hand while carrying on exchanges with the Chinese military as if nothing had happened on the other is sheer wishful thinking. There is an old Chinese saying: \"Only the person who tied the bell can untie it.\" We demand that the United States demonstrate sincerity and take concrete actions in earnest, meet China halfway, and create conditions for returning China-U.S. military relations to the right track.\nOn your second question, I believe that whether it is weapons provided to Taiwan or weapons sold to Taiwan, we have consistently and firmly opposed them. It must be emphasized that Taiwan's security depends on the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait under the one-China principle, and certainly not on relying on U.S. arms provision and sales to Taiwan. U.S. military aid and arms sales to Taiwan only enrich the U.S. military-industrial complex, while harming the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. In response, the PLA will, as always, take all necessary measures to firmly counter it.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, overseas social media platforms have hyped reports that a Type 093 nuclear submarine of the PLA suffered a serious accident in waters near the Taiwan Strait. Please confirm this.","The relevant reports are pure rumors. We hope netizens will follow official, authoritative information and not be swayed by others' agendas.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, military exercises and training by the PLA in the sea and air areas near the Taiwan Strait have drawn attention. Relevant Taiwan authorities released photos of Taiwan military aircraft monitoring PLA aircraft, captioned with the four characters “Evil Neighbor, Begone.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","I will reply with four words: “Taiwan independence will surely perish.” The PLA's series of exercises and training activities all have reasonable force deployments and are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and interference from external forces. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities not to act like a mantis trying to stop a chariot; otherwise, they will be seeking their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Associated Press reported that the U.S. State Department recently notified Congress that the Biden administration has approved approximately $80 million in military aid to Taiwan through the Foreign Military Financing program. Taiwan authorities recently said they will spend an additional approximately $3 billion to purchase new weapons and enhance the combat capability of their F-16s. Some media reported…","Regarding U.S. military aid to Taiwan, I have already answered this question just now. The DPP authorities’ increase of the so-called “defense budget” in an attempt to “seek independence through force” is nothing more than an ant trying to shake a tree, an overestimation of their own strength. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army remains highly vigilant at all times and will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity, and resolutely crush any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After Lai Ching-te's so-called “transit” and “scurrying” to the United States, the Eastern Theater Command of the PLA conducted drills in sea and air areas near Taiwan. Many media outlets on the island believe this activity differs greatly from previous drills that were announced in advance. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The PLA recently organized joint live-fire sea and air exercises around Taiwan island. This is a warning and deterrent against the collusion and provocations of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces, and a necessary measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Do “Taiwan independence” elements not know in their own hearts what bad things they have done? Do they still need to be notified in advance when they are countered by the PLA?","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-08-31","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Taiwan side recently released a report claiming that the mainland side may push to resolve the Taiwan question in the coming years. How does the spokesperson respond to this?","Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, which can and must be decided jointly by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. China must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. Never underestimate the firm resolve, unwavering will and strong capability of the Chinese People's Liberation Army to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16249269.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-09-01","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","We noted that US media reports on China-US relations this year focus far more on competition than cooperation, with over 70 percent talking about competition. Meanwhile, there have been rational voices from the US political, business and academic sectors calling for closer cooperation with China. They expressed the hope that China and the US will promote development through reasonable competition, and strengthen,…","Currently, every time the US talks about its relations with China, it mentions competition, as if China-US relations are mainly about, or even, all about competition.\nChina’s attitude and position is clear. Competition should help promote each other’s progress and improvement and meet the common interests and aspirations of both sides and the wider world. It is not about using every means possible to trip up or thwart the other side. The US talks about competition at every turn. What the world has seen, however, is that in order to gain an edge, the US has resorted to state power under the pretext of competition to contain and suppress China by all government departments, on all fronts and in all areas, waging wars of tariffs, trade, science and technology, chips and rules. What the US does is nothing about competition, but about zero-sum and Cold-War mentality. It is in nature depriving the Chinese people of their rights to independently choose development path and pursue a better life, and China’s legitimate rights to development and national reunification. China firmly opposes moves to contain and suppress China in the name of competition. What the US does will only push the two countries to confrontation and conflict and bring the world a “new Cold War” with division and turmoil.\nWe never shy away from or fear competition, but competition should be fair and reasonable; it should be healthy and rule-based; there should be red lines and restricted zones; market economy rules and basic norms governing international relations should not be ignored; and issues bearing on core interests should not be used as tools for competition or means of provocation. As two major countries, China and the US should, from the height of the common interests of both countries and the future of mankind, compete on who can govern its country better and ensure a happy life for its people, who can provide greater impetus for global post-pandemic economic recovery, who can provide more public goods for climate response, who can come up with better solutions for regional hotspot issues, and who can make both countries and our planet that is home to eight billion people more secure, peaceful and prosperous.\nCompetition is not the sum total of China-US relations. We oppose using competition to define the whole of China-US ties. In fact, complementarity far outweighs competition in the economic relations between the two countries, and cooperation in this area is in nature mutually beneficial. Last year, China-US trade volume hit a record high of close to USD 760 billion. Given the size of economic ties, it is normal that differences and frictions may arise. The right way to resolve these is to find win-win solutions through equal-footed consultation. China and the US have different social systems, but this does not prevent the two sides from engaging in cooperation based on common interests, and doesn’t need to be the cause of confrontation and rivalry. Under the current circumstances, China and the US share more, not less, common interests. It is in our mutual and fundamental interest to prevent conflict and confrontation and achieve peaceful coexistence. The two economies are deeply integrated, and both face new tasks in development. It is in our mutual interest to benefit from each other’s development. It is also in our mutual interest to promote post-COVID global recovery, tackle climate change and resolve regional hotspot issues through China-US coordination and cooperation.\nPlaying up competition does all harm and no good, and seeking cooperation is a necessity not a choice. Facts prove once and again that China and the US stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. With cooperation, many big things can be accomplished that are good for both countries and the world, while confrontation spells disaster for both countries and the world. The two countries need to avoid the way of thinking focusing only on competition and confrontation, accommodate each other’s interests and concerns, seek the broadest areas of exchanges and cooperation, pursue the biggest common ground for win-win cooperation, and jointly contribute the wisdom and strength of two major countries to the development and common prosperity of the two countries as well as world peace and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347589.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230901_11136944.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-09-01","Chen Binhua","国台办发言人陈斌华1日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 1 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to reporters' questions on the 1st, saying: The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and keep spending the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people to buy weapons from the United States, attempting to “seek independence by force” and embolden their…","Chen Binhua said, 'It is like a mantis trying to stop a chariot, overestimating its own strength.' No matter how many weapons the DPP authorities buy from the United States, they cannot shake our firm resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification, nor can they withstand our powerful capability to crush the 'Taiwan independence' scheme and safeguard national sovereignty.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230901_12563964.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, said in response to a question on September 4 that the 5th Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum will be held in Zhongshan, Guangdong, from September 7 to 9.\nThe forum takes as its theme \"Carry forward Dr. Sun Yat-sen's spirit of struggle and work together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\" Its activities take the form of \"1+3+5\": on September 7, one opening ceremony (main forum) will be held simultaneously on both sides of the Strait, both online and offline; on September 8, three sub-forums will be held simultaneously in Guangzhou, Zhongshan, and Macao, namely \"Dr. Sun Yat-sen's Concept of Development and Chinese-Style Modernization,\" \"Deepening Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Cooperation to Pursue High-Quality Development,\" and \"Carrying Forward Dr. Sun Yat-sen's Patriotic Thought and Inheriting Excellent Traditional Chinese Culture.\" During the forum, five economic, trade, and cultural exchange activities will also be held: the Taiwan Investment High-Quality Development—Zhongshan Trip; the launch ceremony of the \"Greater Bay Area (Zhongshan) Taiwan High-Level Talent Recruitment and Scientific and Technological Achievement Transformation Platform\" together with the \"Hundred Taiwan PhDs Enter Enterprises\" event; the cross-Strait media reporting tour \"Visiting Zhongshan—Exploring the Hometown of a Great Man\"; the Historical and Cultural Exploration Camp of Sun Yat-sen, part of the 10th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour; and the \"Zhongshan Cup\" Cross-Strait Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament.\nWe warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to take part in the activities of the 5th Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum, and we also welcome cross-Strait media reporters to conduct interviews and reporting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230904_12564453.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","TAO spokesperson Chen Binhua stated in response to a question on September 4 that the 2023 \"Taiwan Businesses Come Together, Integrate into the Greater Bay Area\" theme event and the 14th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo will be held in Guangdong from September 6 to 10.\nThe event is co-hosted by the Economic Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Guangdong Provincial Government, the Guangdong Provincial Department of Commerce, the Dongguan Municipal Government, and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises. Its purpose is to support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in seizing the new opportunities of the construction of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, integrating into the new development pattern of \"dual circulation,\" building a common cross-Strait market, and jointly promoting cross-Strait integrated development. On the morning of September 7, the main venue event will be held in Dongguan; on the afternoon of September 7, guests from both sides of the Strait will be divided into three routes to visit and tour nine Greater Bay Area cities: Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Zhuhai, Foshan, Dongguan, Zhongshan, Jiangmen, Zhaoqing, and Huizhou; from September 7 to 10, the 2023 14th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo will be held at the Dongguan Guangdong Modern International Exhibition Center. The Strait Economic and Technological Cooperation Center, the China Chamber of Commerce for Import and Export of Machinery and Electronic Products, the Taiwan General Chamber of Commerce, the Taiwan Electrical and Electronic Manufacturers' Association, the Strait Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange Association, and other organizations, along with Taiwan business and industry guests, will participate in the related activities, with a total scale of about 4,500 people.\nThe Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area has fully leveraged its advantages of favorable transportation and location, high degree of internationalization, strong economic vitality, complete industrial system, and concentration of innovation factors, and has become a hot land for investment and a fertile ground for entrepreneurship, attracting attention from both sides of the Strait and overseas. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to actively take part in the related activities, to share opportunities, pursue common development, and achieve mutual benefit and win-win results in the construction of the Greater Bay Area. We also welcome cross-Strait media reporters to interview and report on the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230904_12564454.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-09-05","Mao Ning","The Paper","At a recent press briefing, the Taiwan authorities listed “four appeals” on Taiwan’s UN participation and claimed that they would invite “diplomatic allies” to submit a joint letter to the UN Secretary-General urging him to rectify the UN’s “ erroneous interpretation ” of UNGA Resolution 2758. What’s your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. Despite that fact and legal basis, the DPP authorities have been distorting UNGA Resolution 2758, openly challenging the internationally recognized one-China principle, and spinning lies to pursue “Taiwan independence”. These are extremely dangerous separatist provocations.\nOn October 25, 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 with an overwhelming majority, which “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations”, and to expel forthwith the representatives of the Taiwan authorities “from the place which they unlawfully occupy”. Henceforth, the “dual representation” proposal put forth by the US and a few other countries to keep Taiwan’s seat in the UN became a piece of waste paper. Once and for all, UNGA Resolution 2758 resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN. It also made it clear that there can only be one seat representing China at the UN. No issues exist about so-called “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”.\nSince the adoption of UNGA Resolution 2758, it has been observed by the UN and its specialized agencies and other international and regional organizations. On the basis of the one-China principle, 182 countries have established diplomatic relations with China. The one-China principle has long been a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. Any issue regarding the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations must be addressed under the framework of the one-China principle. Taiwan has no basis, reason or right to join the UN or other international organizations that require statehood.\nBoth sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. Although the two sides have been politically against each other for a long time, China’s state sovereignty and territorial integrity has never been split. This is the real status quo of the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities’ hype-up of Taiwan’s participation in the UN system is actually an attempt to create a false impression of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and challenge the UN-centered international order underpinned by international law. The DPP authorities have been promoting “incremental independence” and pushing for “de-sinicization”, while some external forces have been fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle and conniving at and supporting separatist acts for “Taiwan independence”. It is them, not anyone else, who are undermining the status quo and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. They are the ones responsible for disrupting the cross-Strait status quo.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and its resolution is a matter for the 1.4 billion Chinese on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities will not succeed in seeking external support to embolden its separatist acts. UNGA Resolution 2758 must not be challenged and the one-China principle is unshakable. The wheels of history will keep rolling on. The complete reunification of our country can, without doubt, be realized.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347592.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230905_11138658.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-06","Mao Ning","AFP","Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Hirokazu Matsuno has criticized the release of a Chinese government map that shows what Japan calls the Senkaku Islands and what China calls the Diaoyu Islands belonging to China. Matsuno said that Japan had complained to China through diplomatic channels and demanded the retraction of that map. What’s China’s response to that?","Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have all along been China’s territory. It is only natural that they are marked as Chinese territory on a map. China does not accept Japan’s protest.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347593.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230906_11139128.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-08","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Bloomberg has reported that India is studying possible responses to a potential war in Taiwan, according to senior Indian government officials. About six weeks ago, India’s top military commander commissioned a related study to examine the wider impact of any war in Taiwan and what action India could take in response, Bloomberg reported. The order came after the US raised the issue in several different forums,…","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese people and brooks no foreign interference.\nBy hyping up the Taiwan question on various occasions, the US has been creating tensions, provoking confrontation, and seeking to turn the Taiwan question into an international issue. This is highly dangerous. The most effective way to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is to adhere to the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347595.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230908_11140173.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-11","Mao Ning","Reuters","US President Biden said during his visit to Viet Nam that he does not think China will invade Taiwan given the economic challenges that may reduce China’s capacity. What is the ministry’s response to this? The US and Viet Nam have also upgraded their diplomatic ties and signed deals on semiconductors and minerals. How does the ministry respond to these developments?","To answer your first question, Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves. It shall be decided by the Chinese and brooks no foreign interference.\nAs to your second question, Viet Nam has stressed on multiple occasions that growing the China-Viet Nam comprehensive strategic cooperative partnership is its diplomatic priority and a top priority in the country’s foreign affairs. It is our view that the development of bilateral relations should not target any third party or harm regional peace, stability, development and prosperity.\nWe ask the US to respect regional countries’ shared aspiration for stability, cooperation and development, abide by basic norms governing international relations, discard the hegemonic and Cold War mentality when dealing with relations with Asian countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347596.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230911_11141117.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-13","Mao Ning","AFP","US and Canadian warships transited the Taiwan Strait last week. Recent reports say China staged large-scale military exercises around the Taiwan island. Could you offer more information?","On the US and Canadian warships’ transit through the Taiwan Strait, the PLA Eastern Theatre Command spokesperson already released a statement, which you may refer to.\nI want to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and China is unwaveringly determined to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. Relevant sides should immediately stop such provocative acts and stop being a trouble-maker disrupting peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347598.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230913_11142325.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. New spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporter friends, good day! Welcome to the press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Dear Taiwan compatriots, \"Xudai\" (meaning elders), brothers and sisters, good morning and good day! (In Hokkien.) I am Chen Binhua, currently Deputy Director of the News Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I will host today's press conference. Before working at the Taiwan Affairs Office, I had more than 20 years of media work experience, and I was stationed in Taiwan for interviews for many years, so some of the reporters present are old friends of mine. I hope that in my role as spokesperson, I can work together with everyone to enhance mutual understanding and comprehension between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe press conference now begins. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The 6th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum will be held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, in mid-November. I would like you to introduce the Taiwan guests invited and related details.","The 6th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum will be held from September 14 to 17 in Hangzhou, Huzhou and other places in Zhejiang Province, with the opening ceremony and main forum held in Hangzhou on September 15. Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang and Chairperson of the Chinese Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, has been invited to attend the forum. Guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait and youth representatives from various sectors, about 500 people in total, will take part in the forum’s related activities. Media reporters are welcome to attend and report on the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567301.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were released yesterday (September 12). Please explain the considerations behind launching this major strategy.","The \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development\" (hereinafter referred to as the \"Opinions\") is an important measure to implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on Taiwan work and Fujian work, and the Party's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work made at the 20th National Congress. Tomorrow (the 14th) morning, the State Council Information Office will hold a special press conference, at which our office's Deputy Director Pan Xianzhang, together with Cong Liang, Deputy Director of the National Development and Reform Commission, and Luo Dongchuan, Deputy Secretary of the Fujian Provincial Party Committee, will introduce the background, significance and main contents of the \"Opinions\" and answer reporters' questions. Please pay attention.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, US-Taiwan military collusion has continued: the US approved $500 million in arms sales to Taiwan and for the first time provided Taiwan with an $80 million military financing loan. The DPP authorities' 2024 defense budget reached a record high of NT$606.8 billion. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, recklessly squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwan public to buy weapons from the US at high prices, and attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” This seriously harms the vital interests of the Taiwan public and endangers peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nAccording to accounts calculated by relevant media, since the DPP came to power, Taiwan’s spending on purchasing weapons from the US and Taiwan’s defense budget have risen year after year. From 2020 to 2022, Taiwan was the largest weapons buyer of the US. In 2024, Taiwan’s defense budget was nearly double that of eight years earlier. Because of the “Taiwan independence” forces’ meddling, the more weapons are bought, the higher the debt mountain grows, yet the Taiwan compatriots feel increasingly uneasy. If the DPP authorities are allowed to keep going down the road of “selling out Taiwan,” “harming Taiwan,” and “destroying Taiwan” to the very end, they will only push Taiwan into a perilous situation of ominous war and bring profound disaster upon Taiwan compatriots.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: any act of “seeking independence through force” cannot shake our firm resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland, and cannot withstand our strong capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567297.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Song Tao, Director of the CPC Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office, recently visited the Guandi Temple in Yuncheng, Shanxi, together with Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Li-yen. Some public opinion on the island interprets this move as having a 'pointed meaning' toward Terry Gou, who worships Guan Yu. It is seen as a message across the air to Terry Gou to keep his word: 'be united in heart,…","Yuncheng in Shanxi is the hometown of Guan Yu. On August 30, Director Song Tao, after attending a cross-Strait exchange event in Taiyuan with KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan, made a special trip to Yuncheng to visit the Xiezhou Guandi Temple. Guan Yu culture is a common folk belief shared by both sides of the Strait. At present, cross-Strait relations are at a critical moment and face an important choice. Chinese people on both sides should jointly inherit and promote Guan Yu culture, emphasize loyalty and righteousness, value integrity, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, safeguard national unification, and oppose 'Taiwan independence' separatist acts and interference by external forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567299.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","As the spokesperson mentioned in the opening remarks, you moved from being a veteran of the news industry to the spokesperson's post, and you were stationed in Taiwan for many years. Your understanding of Taiwan's society, politics and economy is therefore more in-depth and comprehensive than that of ordinary mainland people. Now that you have taken office as spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, how will…","For 15 years, from 2001 to 2015, I reported on-site in Taiwan dozens of times, traveling throughout Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu. The dazzling New Year’s Eve fireworks at Taipei 101, the romantic sunset at Xizi Bay in Kaohsiung, the unique scenery of Lanyu in Taitung and the simplicity of the Tao people, the devotion of believers worshipping Mazu at the Tianhou Temple in Lukang, Changhua, and the figures of farmer friends working in the fields along the Zhuoshui River in Yunlin… scene after scene remains fresh in my memory. Treasure Island Taiwan has always been in my heart. Through contact and exchanges with people from all walks of life in Taiwan and fellow townspeople in various places, I have gained a fairly comprehensive understanding of their work, their lives, and their thoughts, and I have also developed a relatively in-depth observation of the Taiwan question. This will help me, in my position as spokesperson of the TAO, to better explain the mainland’s policies toward Taiwan in language that compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, want to hear and can understand, so that our fellow islanders can understand our sincerity and goodwill.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce the relevant situation of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities this summer.","This summer, relevant departments and localities held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities that were rich in content, diverse in form, and productive. A brief introduction follows.\nIn July, the 2nd Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Forum on Jointly Pursuing High-Quality Development, the 2023 Zhejiang·Taiwan Cooperation Week, and the 1st Jilin-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange Negotiation Conference were held in Qinghai, Zhejiang, and Jilin, respectively. In August, Tianjin, Henan, and Shanxi successively held the 14th Tianjin-Taiwan Investment Cooperation Negotiation Conference, the 2023 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference, and the 2023 “Taiwan Businesspeople and Youth Go to Shanxi” series of activities. In early September, Weifang, Shandong, held the 27th Shandong-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference; Suzhou, Jiangsu, held the 9th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Economic and Trade Forum; Xiamen, Fujian, held the 17th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Cooperation and Development Forum; Dongguan, Guangdong, held the 2023 “Taiwan Businesspeople Come Together, Integrate into the Greater Bay Area” theme activity and the 14th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo; and Chongqing held the 15th Chongqing·Taiwan Week. Broad Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises enthusiastically participated, fully demonstrating their optimism about the economic development prospects of the mainland and their enthusiasm for participating in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nRecently, some cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities are also being prepared intensively. From September 19 to 21, the 26th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, co-hosted by the State Council TAO and the Beijing Municipal Government and supported by the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, will be held in Beijing. The forum takes “Technology Empowers a Smart Future, Innovation Drives Integrated Development” as its theme. It features a forum summit and four parallel forums on finance, the digital economy, medical health, and the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains, as well as a series of sub-forums on smart low-carbon development, intellectual property protection, science and technology talent, women, and other topics. Invited participants include cross-Strait technology industry figures, representatives of industry and professional associations and entrepreneurs, and Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland. From mid-to-late September through October, the 17th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week, the 2023 Guizhou·Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Forum, the 16th Hunan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Conference, the 19th Hebei-Taiwan Economic Cooperation Negotiation Conference, the 4th Cross-Strait (Shaanxi) Economic, Trade and Technology Cooperation Conference, the 19th Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum, and other activities will also be held successively. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan enterprises to actively participate, seek development together, and create win-win outcomes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567293.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","When the spokesperson worked as a reporter, he was stationed in Taiwan for more than ten years and wrote three books. In \"Notes from the First Batch of Mainland Reporters Stationed in Taiwan — Stationed in Taiwan,\" in \"Chapter 10 Cross-Strait Relations: Where Is Spring?\", he recorded historical events such as the rejection of the \"1992 Consensus\" and the one-China principle during the Chen Shui-bian period. Now,…","All those who care about the future and destiny of Taiwan and support the peaceful development of cross-strait relations deeply deplore the fact that since the DPP authorities came to power, history has been turned back, causing cross-strait exchanges to seriously regress, and they are deeply worried about the increasingly complex and severe situation in the Taiwan Strait. The late Koo Chen-fu, former Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, often wrote a line of poetry during his lifetime: “Only knowing the spring stirring, who would know the heart that endures the winter’s cold?” I think this line of poetry very well reflects the state of mind of these people and of me personally at present.\nThere is no winter that cannot be crossed, and no spring that will not come. The foundation of cross-strait relations lies among the people, its driving force lies with the people, and its hope lies with the youth. We believe that as long as compatriots on both sides join hands with one heart and work together, we will certainly be able to push cross-strait relations forward through difficulties, return to the correct track of peaceful development, and usher in yet another spring of great exchanges, great cooperation and great development across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","After three years of the pandemic, cross-Strait exchanges have gradually heated up since the beginning of this year. Please introduce cross-Strait personnel travel and exchanges in various fields this summer.","This year, we have promptly optimized and adjusted epidemic prevention and control measures related to personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, promoted the resumption of the “Small Three Links” and direct cross-Strait flight routes, and announced the resumption of group tour business for Taiwan residents to the mainland. Cross-Strait exchanges in all fields have heated up rapidly, with good momentum. In the first half of the year, the number of Taiwan compatriots visiting the mainland increased sevenfold compared with the same period last year. Especially after the summer vacation, cross-Strait exchanges have become even more active, and the enthusiasm and initiative of Taiwan residents to take part in cross-Strait exchanges have soared. Overall, there are several main characteristics:\nFirst, youth have become the most active group in cross-Strait exchanges, and the content and forms of cross-Strait youth exchanges are rich and diverse. On July 12, the 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Summit opened in Beijing, and nearly 1,200 Taiwan youths took part in activities such as the music carnival summer evening party, the science and technology achievement exhibition, and the innovation and entrepreneurship competition. The 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month ran from late July to mid-September, with nearly 1,500 Taiwan youths participating in 21 thematic activities covering intangible cultural heritage, calligraphy and painting, traditional Chinese medicine, and more. On August 5, the 11th Cross-Strait Youth Festival opened in Fuzhou, Fujian, and more than 1,400 Taiwan youths participated in various activities. In addition, the first Cross-Strait Youth Grand Canal Village Cycling Event and the 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition also attracted large numbers of Taiwan youths.\nSecond, cross-Strait exchanges have broken through the numerous obstacles set up by the DPP authorities, achieving “two-way engagement.” As the return visit arrangement for Mr. Ma Ying-jeou’s trip to the mainland to pay respects to ancestors and engage in exchanges, from July 15 to 23, Hao Ping, Party Secretary of Peking University, led faculty and students from five universities, including Peking University, on an invited trip to Taiwan to enhance cross-Strait youth friendship and promote cross-Strait cultural and educational exchanges. In July and August, the “14th Cross-Strait Film Festival” Mainland Film Exhibition and Taiwan Film Exhibition were held in Taipei and Ya’an, Sichuan, respectively, screening 8 mainland films and 6 Taiwan films. On July 14, 62 mainland tourism industry professionals went to Taiwan to attend the Cross-Strait Taipei Summer Travel Fair, the largest number of mainland personnel to enter the island for exchange in recent years.\nThird, cross-Strait cultural exchanges are colorful and varied, and traditional Chinese culture and pop culture are increasingly loved by compatriots on both sides. The 7th Cross-Strait Yue Fei Culture Summer Camp, the 8th Chinese Cultural Heritage Study Camp, the 2023 Cross-Strait Archaeology Study Camp, the 12th Cross-Strait Cultural Heritage Protection Forum, and other activities have been held one after another. Nearly 50 writers from both sides gathered at the 2023 Cross-Strait Literature Exchange Meeting and travelled to Zhejiang and Fujian for field exchanges. The 2023 Cross-Strait Dragon and Lion Dance Competition was held in Zhangping, with more than 230 athletes from 13 teams across the Strait competing on the same stage. The 4th Cross-Strait Youth Online Literature Competition, the “Huihaishang · 2023 Cross-Strait Esports Culture Festival,” the Cross-Strait Youth Street Dance Arts Festival, and other pop culture activities have been warmly welcomed by compatriots on both sides.\nFourth, cross-Strait cultural industry cooperation has yielded rich results. The 14th Cross-Strait Cultural Industry Expo was held in Xiamen, with exhibition scale reaching a new high. Among them, there were 883 booths from Taiwan, an increase of 48% over the previous session. During the event, 77 culture and tourism investment projects were signed, with a total signed amount of 28.1 billion yuan, on-site transaction volume of 2.8 billion yuan, and 120,000 visits.\nIn mid to late September, a number of cross-Strait cultural exchange activities will also take place. The first Cross-Strait Animation Dubbing Competition is being held both online and offline. As of yesterday (September 12), it had received 2,852 entries, including 521 works from Taiwan. The 3rd IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival is being held in Pingtan, Fujian. It has collected 1,849 works from 331 schools at home and abroad, including 121 works submitted by 27 universities in the Taiwan region, and 15 of them have been shortlisted for awards. In addition, from September 18 to 28, the 2023 Cross-Strait Compatriots’ Escort of the Meizhou Mazu Golden Statue Patrol Activity will be held in Putian, Fujian; from September 21 to 23, the 2023 Cross-Strait Zhouyi Culture Forum will be held in Anyang, Henan; and from September 21 to 27, the 11th Central Plains (Gushi) Kinship Culture Festival will be held in Xinyang, Henan. We sincerely welcome compatriots on both sides to follow the relevant activities, take part in cross-Strait cultural exchanges, and jointly inherit and carry forward the excellent traditional Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567292.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Some public opinion on the island has pointed out that if Terry Guo insists on running as an independent candidate, he will become a “disruptor” and “spoiler” who lacks morality and credibility, and is even “handing Lai Ching-te the election.” What comment do you have?","We have noted the relevant comments from public opinion on the island. We respect the current social system of the Taiwan region, and we hope the election results can help maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The 19th Asian Games in Hangzhou will open on September 23. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan compatriots in this Asian Games.","The 19th Asian Games will open in Hangzhou on September 23, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are looking forward to this Asian Games event. Taiwan compatriots in Zhejiang are participating in Asian Games-related activities in various ways. Some Taiwan compatriots were selected as torchbearers for the torch relay, and some have become Asian Games staff and volunteers, joining mainland compatriots in contributing to this grand event. Regarding the registration of Taiwan athletes for the Hangzhou Asian Games, please follow the information released by the Organizing Committee.\nWe welcome Taiwan's sports athletes to come and compete, and we also welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit Zhejiang and experience the charm of Hangzhou, the Asian Games city.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567295.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently explained that 'pragmatic' means 'based on facts,' and 'worker' means 'guarding Taiwan.' He does not accept the label of 'Taiwan independence golden grandson.' Lai also said he is 'willing to engage in dialogue with the other side across the Strait on the basis of mutual benefit, dignity, equality and no preconditions, to create peace and shared prosperity.' What is your comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest hidden danger to Taiwan and the greatest threat to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. No matter how Lai Ching-te changes his rhetoric, he cannot erase his “Taiwan independence” words and deeds, nor can he conceal his “Taiwan independence” nature. On the basis of the one-China principle, there are no obstacles to exchanges between us and any political party or group in Taiwan. But if they insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, cross-Strait consultation and dialogue will be out of the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567298.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities recently released graphic designs for the 2023 “Double Ten” events, in which the Chinese label reads “Taiwan National Day” and the English reads “TAIWAN NATIONAL DAY ”. What is your comment?","This little trick is merely the DPP authorities deceiving themselves, and it will only let the world see more clearly their true 'Taiwan independence' face and their sham. Since taking office, the DPP authorities have stubbornly adhered to the 'Taiwan independence' separatist position, and from time to time use various occasions to manipulate the 'Taiwan independence' issue, making small moves they call 'name rectification.' No matter how they maneuver, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they stop the historical trend that the motherland must and will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The mainland announced that, in light of the trade barrier investigation against Taiwan, it will study suspending or partially suspending the tariff preferences granted to Taiwan products under ECFA, which has caused concern among industry and the public on the island. What comment do you have?","In June 2010, on the basis of the ‘1992 Consensus,’ both sides of the Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement between the Mainland and Taiwan (ECFA). Over the years, the mainland has consistently and earnestly fulfilled its commitments, promoting and ensuring the entry into force and implementation of the ECFA.\nBy contrast, since the DPP authorities came to power, they have not only failed to take concrete measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but have also continuously and increasingly amended rules and set up obstacles, maliciously obstructing and undermining normal economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. This has harmed the interests of relevant mainland industries and enterprises, and it has also harmed the interests of Taiwan consumers. This not only seriously hinders the implementation of the ECFA, but also seriously violates the non-discrimination principle of the World Trade Organization (WTO).\nWe express our support for the Ministry of Commerce’s plan to study, in light of the investigation into trade barriers targeting Taiwan and in accordance with relevant regulations, suspending or partially suspending the tariff preferences granted to Taiwan products under the ECFA.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","The State Council recently approved the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan.” Please introduce the relevant information.","The State Council's approval of the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan” is an important measure to thoroughly implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China. It fully reflects our sincere goodwill in respecting, caring for and benefiting Taiwan compatriots, and clearly sends a policy signal for deepening cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation.\nDongguan is one of the earliest and most densely invested areas for Taiwan businesses entering the mainland, and the number of Taiwan-invested enterprises and their investment amounts rank among the highest of all prefecture-level cities. The “Overall Plan” is based on Dongguan's foundation for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and the resource endowments of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area. It focuses on three key areas: industry, market and people's livelihood, and strives to build a new engine for cross-Strait industrial innovation and development, a new high ground for scientific and technological innovation cooperation, a new hub for social and cultural exchanges, and a new platform for exchanges and cooperation between the two sides of the Strait and the Hong Kong and Macao regions. This will further stimulate Dongguan's momentum for innovative development, build a demonstration platform for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses to integrate into the new development dispensation and participate in high-quality development, and help Taiwan enterprises transform, upgrade and expand the domestic market. It will also help Taiwan compatriots and businesses share more development opportunities and achievements on the mainland, and promote cross-Strait innovation cooperation, integrated development and heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides.\nOur office will, together with relevant departments and Guangdong Province, earnestly organize the implementation of the “Overall Plan,” continuously explore new paths for deepening cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation, build new platforms for cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and achieve more new results in cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567300.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","Public opinion has noted that the DPP authorities, on the one hand, call on ECFA not to stop, while on the other hand, they collude with external forces and clamor to “decouple and break chains” with the mainland’s economy. What comment do you have?","Since the ECFA took effect and began implementation, it has brought tangible benefits to both sides of the Strait, especially to relevant industries and the public in Taiwan. Hoping to ensure that the ECFA continues to take effect and be implemented is mainstream public opinion on the island, which also proves that the ECFA is a good agreement that benefits Taiwan compatriots.\nWhen the ECFA was being negotiated, the DPP, out of narrow partisan interest and ‘opposing for the sake of opposing,’ vigorously interfered and obstructed. As a result, the subsequent Services Trade Agreement under the ECFA was signed but did not take effect, and follow-up negotiations on the Goods Trade Agreement were forced to halt, affecting implementation of the agreements. Since the DPP authorities came to power, on the one hand, they have finally recognized that the ECFA is beneficial to Taiwan and have repeatedly said they do not wish to terminate it. On the other hand, they have colluded with external forces, attempting to ‘decouple and break chains’ with the mainland economically, and they have continuously obstructed and undermined normal economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. This two-faced approach shows that, in pursuit of ‘independence,’ they have lost basic reason.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","《中国日报》记者","The 78th UN General Assembly opened on September 5. The DPP authorities put forward the so-called “four appeals for participating in the UN,” and Wu Chao-hsieh, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, falsely claimed that he will urge the UN to correct the “wrong interpretation” of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. What is your comment?","Regarding UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, we have stated our position many times. The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan is part of China, not a state, and is not qualified to join the United Nations. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a consensus of the international community. These facts, and their historical and legal basis, are clear. The DPP authorities disregard the facts and keep smearing and attacking UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. I wish to state once again our position on this matter, to set the record straight.\nTaiwan is part of China. In 1894, Japan launched the First Sino-Japanese War, a war of aggression against China, and the following year forced the defeated Qing government to cede Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. The Cairo Declaration of 1943, the Potsdam Proclamation of 1945, the Japanese Instrument of Surrender of 1945, and declarations of the Chinese government all show that China recovered Taiwan both legally and in fact. After the founding of the People's Republic of China in 1949, it became the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This was a change of government while China's status as a subject of international law remained unchanged, and China's sovereignty and inherent territory did not change. The Government of the People's Republic of China naturally enjoys and exercises full sovereignty over China, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The status of Taiwan as part of China has never changed and will never be allowed to change.\nIn 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore all the lawful rights of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the representatives of the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. This clearly and thoroughly resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the question of China's representation in the United Nations. It also made clear that China has only one seat in the United Nations, and there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nThe DPP authorities' stubborn “Taiwan independence” separatist stance challenges the basic norms of international relations and the consensus of the international community year after year. In the end, it will only make the international community more clearly aware that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230913_12567296.htm"],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","《北京日报》记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that it was the mainland that unilaterally closed the “door” of cross-Strait communication, and that if he is elected, he will become an “opportunity” for cross-Strait exchanges. What is your comment?","Lai's remarks can be summed up in eight characters: “Distort right and wrong, dream like a fool!” As everyone knows, the reason the cross-Strait consultation and dialogue mechanism has stalled is that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” Lai Ching-te is an out-and-out “Taiwan independence worker” and a thoroughgoing “troublemaker.” His remarks are nothing more than an attempt to deceive people to win votes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The 2023 China International Fair for Trade in Services was recently held, and a Taiwan image exhibition with the theme “Integrated Development of Services, Sharing a National Future” made its debut. Many representatives of Taiwan-invested enterprises said they hope to further enhance cross-Strait exchanges. What is your comment?","From September 2 to 6, 2023, the China International Fair for Trade in Services (CIFTIS) was held in Beijing. During the event, a Taiwan image exhibition was held under the theme “Integrated Development of Services, Sharing a Common Future for the Nation.” It comprised four sections: “Colorful Taiwan,” “Taiwan Enterprise Style,” “Services for Taiwan Businesses” and “Interactive Interviews,” focusing on showcasing the distinctive style of Taiwan businesses and enterprises. A total of 28 Taiwan-invested enterprises exhibited, covering six major sectors: modern services, technology, finance, intelligent manufacturing, biomedicine and smart agriculture. The products and services on display were of high quality and high technological content, leaving a deep impression and a good experience for on-site audiences. We will, as always, support cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, help more Taiwan businesses and enterprises participate deeply in the fair, and gain more business opportunities by integrating into the new development pattern.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Taiwan regional leader Tsai Ing-wen recently made an intrusive visit to the African country Eswatini, and green media on the island hyped that Taiwan will build a so-called “strategic oil reserve tank” in Eswatini. What comment do you have?","The one-China principle is international consensus. The DPP authorities’ dealings with so-called “diplomatic allies” will not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. As for the relevant media reports, they further demonstrate the DPP’s incompetence in governance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","We note that since the beginning of this year, the island has been experiencing an 'egg shortage' crisis. Recently, it was exposed that a small company with registered capital of only NT$500,000 imported more than 80 million eggs and received a high subsidy of NT$175 million, which has triggered questions on the island. What is your comment on this?","Eggs are small, but they concern people’s daily lives and the three meals of ordinary families. Questions from all sectors on the island about the “miraculous operations” of the DPP authorities and the companies involved are reasonable and reflect Taiwan residents’ thirst for fairness and justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently released “plans” for resuming cross-Strait exchanges, but island tourism operators have found that this so-called “plan” has no clear implementation date, and the so-called “resumption and relaxation” is in name only. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","On August 25, we already responded to the relevant issues. The DPP authorities have attached a series of conditions to the resumption of cross-Strait tourism and exchanges, attempting to deceive: in name it is 'resumption,' but in fact they refuse to lift restrictions; in name it is 'relaxation,' but in fact they strengthen controls. The views of the operators and public opinion on the island that you mentioned show that more and more Taiwan compatriots have clearly seen that the DPP authorities are neither 'democratic' nor 'progressive.' They disregard public opinion, are autocratic and dictatorial, and are turning back the wheel of history in cross-Strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","Taiwanese media reported that recently, some Taiwan scholars were “questioned” when conducting exchange activities in the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council said that currently, exchanges in the religious and academic fields are “relatively dangerous,” and that people should not go to the mainland unless necessary. What is your comment?","The remarks by the Mainland Affairs Council are malicious hype, aimed at deceiving and misleading Taiwan's people and at intimidating and obstructing Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland for exchanges. Our position has always been consistent. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to walk around and take a look. We are pleased to see and support normal exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to deepen mutual understanding, enhance friendship, build consensus, strengthen common interests, and promote spiritual affinity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","This summer, various youth exchange activities were held across the mainland, attracting many Taiwan students and young people to come to the mainland to take part. On the Taiwan side, the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation for Education and Culture invited 37 teachers and students from five mainland universities to visit Taiwan. But in terms of numbers, Taiwan students going to the mainland far exceed mainland students…","We have responded to this before. The fundamental obstacle for mainland students studying in Taiwan is that normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges has been blocked, and the legitimate rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan cannot be guaranteed.\nWe actively advocate and promote the restoration of normalized cross-Strait personnel exchanges and the regularization of exchanges in all fields, which is also the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities still restrict normal cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel. This is both unreasonable and unpopular, and these artificial barriers should be removed as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-13","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","We noticed that foreign media reported that Japan's Ministry of Defense will dispatch a current civilian official to be stationed in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military ties between countries that have established diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. We urge Japan to learn from historical lessons, abide by the One-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and be prudent in words and deeds on the Taiwan issue.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all, and wishing everyone peace and good health!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230913_12567284.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-09-14","Tan Kefei","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reports say the DPP authorities will purchase 14 “Volcano” vehicle-mounted mine-laying systems from the United States. Some commentary on the island holds that Taiwan becoming a “mine island” is a foregone conclusion. In addition, reports say Taiwan recently took part in a military exercise led by the U.S. National Guard. Taiwan’s defense authorities’ 2024 budget proposal shows that the “TOW” and “Javelin”…","Tan Kefei said that we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the United States and Taiwan region of China, firmly oppose US arms sales to Taiwan, and urge the US side to abide by its solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” stop any form of US-Taiwan military contacts, and stop escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nTan Kefei noted that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, for their own selfish interests, do not hesitate to use the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people to curry favor with the United States, creating confrontation between the two sides of the Strait. Their conduct is turning Taiwan into a “landmine island” and an “ammunition depot,” seriously harming the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. US-Taiwan collusion is entirely about “harming Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan.” Stubbornly “relying on the US to seek independence” will only push Taiwan into a perilous situation of war. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains on high alert at all times, and will resolutely thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist act and external interference, and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/2023-09/14/c_1129863904.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-09-15","Mao Ning","China Daily","Lately the US has provided advanced weaponry to China’s Taiwan region through arms sales, military assistance and loans. China’s foreign ministry spokesperson said earlier that China would take strong measures to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity. I wonder if you have anything new on that?","In disregard of China’s firm opposition, the US government deliberately supplies weapons to China’s Taiwan region. This seriously violates the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, contravenes international law and basic norms governing international relations, and undermines China’s sovereignty and security interests. The US is going further down the wrong and dangerous path of arming Taiwan.\nLockheed Martin Corporation, St. Louis, MO directly participated in the US arms sale to Taiwan announced on August 24 as the principal contractor. Northrop Grumman participated in several US arms sales to Taiwan. In accordance with the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law of the People’s Republic of China, China decides to impose sanctions on these two above-mentioned US defense corporations.\nLet me stress, the Chinese government never wavers in its resolve of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We call on the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arms sales to Taiwan, stop military collusion with Taiwan, and stop arming Taiwan, otherwise it will be met with China’s resolute response.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347600.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230915_11143550.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-18","Mao Ning","China Daily","It was reported that President of the Central American Parliament Amado Cerrud will lead a delegation to China in the coming days. Can you confirm this?","At the invitation of Chairman of the National People’s Congress Standing Committee Zhao Leji, President of the Central American Parliament Amado Cerrud will lead a delegation to China from September 19 to 23. On August 22 this year, the Central American Parliament adopted the resolution to revoke the “permanent observer status” of the so-called “Legislative Yuan” of the Taiwan region and accept the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. China welcomes and commends the resolution. This again shows that the one-China principle represents the unstoppable trend of the times and has the overwhelming support of the people. China stands ready to develop friendly cooperation with the Central American Parliament on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347601.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230918_11144604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-18","Mao Ning","AFP","The Taiwan authorities claimed that they had detected the continued activity of 103 People’s Liberation Army warplanes near the island by 6 o’clock this morning, of which dozens crossed the “median line” in the Taiwan Strait. Can you further explain these military activities?","First of all, this is not a question about foreign affairs. I suggest you ask competent Chinese authorities for specifics. Let me say that Taiwan is part of China’s territory. There is no so-called “median line” in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347601.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230918_11144604.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-09-26","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","According to reports, on September 26, a plenary meeting of the Central American Parliament approved a special agreement on the accession of the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. What’s your comment?","On September 26, a plenary meeting of the Central American Parliament approved with strong support a special agreement on the accession of the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. The plenary meeting also approved with strong support the August plenary meeting minutes, which contains the resolution to revoke the “permanent observer status” of the so-called “Legislative Yuan” of the Taiwan region and accept the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer. We applaud that decision. It reflects the Central American Parliament’s firm resolve to develop relations with China and again shows that the one-China principle represents the prevailing consensus of the international community and the unstoppable trend of the times. China stands ready to further develop and consolidate friendly cooperative relations with the Central American Parliament and Central American countries on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347607.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230926_11150594.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 27, the TAO held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the TAO's regular press conference. Now we begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter on September 15 to the Sixth Straits Forum on Cross-Strait Youth Development, expressing earnest expectations for cross-Strait youth. What further steps will the mainland take to encourage cross-Strait youth to unite in heart and purpose and work hand in hand, contributing youthful energy to promoting peaceful development across the Taiwan Strait and…","General Secretary Xi Jinping’s congratulatory letter fully reflects his care and concern for young people across the Strait, especially Taiwan youth. The letter points out the historic opportunities and bright prospects for the development of young people across the Strait, and greatly encourages and inspires young people across the Strait to contribute to the realization of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nWe will earnestly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s congratulatory letter and his important instructions on youth work, and continue to create better conditions and provide more platforms for Taiwan youth coming to the mainland to study, find employment, start businesses and live, so that Taiwan youth are willing to come, can integrate well, and develop well. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring New Paths for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait,” announced not long ago, explicitly proposes specific measures, including supporting youth groups in all fields and industries in Fujian and Taiwan in establishing regular exchange channels, strengthening the construction of cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship platforms, and supporting exchanges between primary and secondary schools in Fujian and Taiwan. These measures will help more Taiwan youth come to the mainland to pursue, build and realize their dreams, so that young people across the Strait can get closer, get to know each other better and build good relations through exchange, and jointly contribute youthful strength to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570897.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After the release of the 'Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development of Cross-Strait Relations and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,' we noticed that reactions on the island show 'official cold, people hot.' The DPP authorities have deliberately downplayed the matter and smeared it, trying…","On September 12, Xinhua News Agency, authorized to publish the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” which drew high attention and wide discussion on the island. It is generally believed that the “Opinions” conform to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and benefit Taiwan compatriots. They fully demonstrate the goodwill and sincerity of the mainland toward the broad Taiwan compatriots, and will have a major and far-reaching impact on the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe DPP authorities slandered it as “poison wrapped in sugar-coated bullets.” This is exactly the same as the DPP’s reaction when the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) was being negotiated, once again proving that the DPP has consistently stood on the wrong side of history, on the opposite side of the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570895.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","On September 12, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” were released. On the same day, the DPP authorities published a defense report, claiming that they would prepare for “urban warfare.” These two documents, released by the two…","The ‘Opinions’ we issued are intended to provide Taiwan compatriots studying, working, and living in Fujian with the greatest possible convenience, the best possible conditions, and the strongest possible guarantees. They are full of sincerity and substance, fully demonstrating our goodwill toward benefiting cross-Strait compatriots and our sincerity in promoting peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and they have won wide acclaim from compatriots on both sides.\nThe DPP authorities’ ‘political demons’ have flared up. Driven by their nature of seeking ‘independence,’ they have concocted the so-called new version of the ‘Defense Report,’ touted ‘asymmetric warfare,’ clamored for ‘offensive defense,’ and threatened to prepare for ‘urban warfare.’ This exposes their vicious intent to drive up cross-Strait confrontation, to willingly serve as ‘pawns’ for external forces, and to disregard the safety of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nComparing the two, it is self-evident who is seeking development and greater welfare for Taiwan compatriots, and who is creating dangerous situations for them and stirring up conflict and chaos.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570896.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 19th Asian Games opened grandly in Hangzhou on the evening of the 23rd, attracting great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We noticed that shortly after the opening, the Chinese Taipei team won its first gold medal in men’s judo, and spectators on site cheered for the Taiwan athletes, creating a warm and lively scene. Please introduce the situation of Taiwan athletes and Taiwan…","We welcome the Chinese Taipei delegation of a large scale to the Hangzhou Asian Games, with 521 athletes competing in 33 events. Over these past few days, everyone has seen the athletes’ brilliant performances. We congratulate athletes such as Yang Yongwei and Lian Zhenling on their excellent results! We hear that tomorrow is Yongwei’s birthday—wishing Yongwei a happy birthday and continued outstanding achievements! We also wish other athletes success in realizing their dreams on the Asian Games stage!\nIt is worth noting that whether at the opening ceremony or at the venues of various competitions, members of the Chinese Taipei delegation have felt the warm support of mainland audiences and have responded with goodwill, which is very good. Outside the venues, many Taiwan compatriots in Zhejiang have also actively participated in the organization of the Asian Games, the torch relay, volunteer services and other related activities, jointly contributing to the event and sharing the glory.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently told an Australian legislative delegation that “intruded” into Taiwan that she hopes the Australian government and parliament will support Taiwan's accession to the CPTPP. What is your comment?","Regarding the issue of Chinese Taiwan’s participation in regional economic cooperation mechanisms, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities’ attempt to seek “independence” under the guise of economic and trade matters will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","On September 19, the Golden Body of Mazu from Meizhou, surrounded by tens of thousands of admirers, began a ten-day, nine-night tour of Putian in Fujian. Recently, Mazu temple groups in Taiwan jointly invited the Mazu deity statue from the Meizhou Mazu ancestral temple in Putian, Fujian, to tour Taiwan, and the Meizhou ancestral temple has also indicated its willingness to actively promote this. What is the…","It is understood that Taiwan Mazu Association and three other groups, along with hundreds of temples in Taiwan, recently jointly invited the Mazu statue of the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple in Putian, Fujian, to enter Taiwan for a tour of protection and blessing. The Meizhou Ancestral Temple quickly responded and plans to travel to Taiwan for the tour from November 3 to 13. At present, relevant temples on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are actively preparing for the event.\nMazu is a deity revered jointly by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The Mazu statue of the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple in Fujian has made several tours to Taiwan for protection and blessing, and has been warmly welcomed by believers on the island. We are pleased to see the Mazu statue of the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple travel to Taiwan for the tour of protection, to bestow blessings upon the broad Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570893.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","This year, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have continued to heat up, and the enthusiasm and initiative of Taiwan compatriots to take part in cross-Strait exchanges have continued to rise. What cross-Strait exchange activities have taken place recently?","Recently, exchanges in all areas across the Strait have continued to be lively. On September 21, the 2023 “Cross-Strait Ties, Li Village Visit” Straits Cross-Strait Cultural Exchange Activity was held in Lizhuang, Yibin, Sichuan. Under the theme “‘Yi’ Road Has ‘Li,’ Both Sides Win,” more than 240 representatives from cross-Strait economic, cultural, educational and other fields, as well as descendants of Lizhuang’s famous figures, took part. During the event, an investment promotion meeting, cross-Strait Nezha folk culture exchange activities, a cross-Strait specialty product fair, a cross-Strait calligraphy and painting exhibition and other activities were held.\nOn September 26, the first “Straits Cross-Strait Youth Arts Festival” opened in Xiamen. The series of festival activities will continue until January 2024. During this period, there will be the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Hokkien Dual-Song Competition, the “Hokkien Fireworks, Cross-Strait Love Letters” collection and broadcast of stories about the home and nation of Taiwan compatriots living in Xiamen, the “Seeing the Small to Know the Big” Straits Cross-Strait Youth Micro-Film Competition, the collection and selection of cross-Strait-themed souvenirs, and the screening of the cross-Strait-themed feature film “Three Days in Xiamen,” among other activities.\nIn addition, the first “Straits Cross-Strait Mobile Phone Photography Competition,” jointly planned and organized by the magazine “World of Photography” and the Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Center, began accepting submissions on September 13 and will close on November 30. The competition is collecting mobile phone photography works on themes such as “Happy Life,” “Green Mountains and Clear Waters,” “Cultural Confidence,” “Technology Empowerment,” “Both Sides of the Strait Are One Family” and “Chasing and Realizing Dreams,” reflecting and recording the lively scenes of exchanges in all areas across the Strait and spreading and interpreting vivid stories of cross-Strait exchanges. So far, nearly a thousand submissions have been received from compatriots on both sides. Interested friends may register by logging in to the official website of “World of Photography” or the “Mobile Phone Imaging Network” mini-program.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","This year, people on the island have experienced the 'longest egg shortage in history,' and recently imported eggs were exposed as 'containing poison.' The imported egg controversy continues to escalate, and the DPP authorities' practices of shielding, covering up and shifting responsibility on this matter have sparked strong dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Eggs are small, yet they concern the daily life of the public and the three meals a day of ordinary families. Since the DPP authorities took power, the island has not only failed to solve the “five shortages” of water, electricity, land, workers, and talent, but has also seen strange situations such as shortages of vaccines, eggs, and medicines. Scandals such as black-gold politics and collusion between officials and businesspeople have frequently surfaced. It can be said that the people of the island have “suffered from the DPP for a long time”! The root of these problems is that the DPP authorities are both corrupt and incompetent, and the longer they hold power, the more they reveal the arrogance of power and the greed of politicians. The people of Taiwan are increasingly seeing this clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570894.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The MAC recently said that from January to June this year, cross-Strait trade and mainland imports from Taiwan both decreased, showing that the mainland’s economic recovery is slow and cross-Strait trade activity continues to cool. What comment does the spokesperson have?","The mainland’s economy is resilient, has great potential, and is full of vitality. Its long-term positive fundamentals will not change, and it will always be the most solid support for Taiwan’s economic development and the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to invest and start businesses. In the first half of this year, although cross-Strait trade declined year on year, the amount remained at a substantial scale of US$123.63 billion, demonstrating that cross-Strait economic and trade relations have strong endogenous momentum. As the mainland’s economy recovers and improves, cross-Strait economic and trade relations have enormous room to expand into broader fields and rise to higher levels. We are highly confident in this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","During his recent visit to the US, Hou Yu-ih proposed a “3D” strategy, namely deterrence, dialogue and de-risking. He said that he will use a responsible attitude to keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, use strength to ensure peace, and use exchanges to enhance understanding. What is your comment?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Returning to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, will allow cross-Strait relations to return to the correct track of peaceful development, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will be effectively safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The PLA has recently conducted large-scale exercises and training activities around the Taiwan Strait. The head of Taiwan's defense authority said this has increased the risk of the situation getting out of control and triggering accidental conflict. According to Taiwanese media, a member of a Taiwan security advisory committee said at an internal briefing that in 2027 the mainland side will have the capability…","The PLA is conducting a series of exercises and training activities around the Taiwan Strait, aimed at resolutely striking down the arrogance of the separatist “Taiwan independence” forces and their independence-seeking conduct. As long as “Taiwan independence” provocations continue, the PLA's actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not stop for a moment. We hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will clearly discern right from wrong, cause from effect, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence,” and join us in jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","The “Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge Construction Promotion Association” of Kinmen County recently launched a referendum on “whether to agree to build the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge,” collecting 734 signatures in two weeks, reflecting that Kinmen fellow townsmen have high expectations for the construction of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have heard the call of Kinmen's fellow townspeople for the construction of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge. Over the years, we have continuously taken measures to enhance the interests and well-being of Kinmen's fellow townspeople. In 2018 we were the first to achieve water supply to Kinmen, and the preparatory technical work for connecting Kinmen with electricity, gas, and bridges has also been basically completed. The Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, published not long ago, clearly proposes to “explore models for Xiamen-Kinmen cooperation in jointly building infrastructure, and accelerate the progress of supplying electricity, gas and bridge connections with Kinmen.” We will work with all sectors in Kinmen, overcome interference, and strive to realize the beautiful vision of “Xiamen faces Kinmen head-on, Lu Island and Wu Island bridged together.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570892.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, former Singapore Foreign Minister George Yeo said that in the event of war across the Taiwan Strait, Taiwan would be a sacrificial pawn that the United States uses against mainland China. U.S. entrepreneur Elon Musk said that Taiwan is part of China and that the U.S. is “preventing reunification.” These views of international figures on the Taiwan issue have drawn public attention. What comment do you…","The One-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community. The Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and striving to complete national reunification is increasingly gaining broad understanding and support from the international community. The DPP authorities, willingly serving as pawns of the anti-China forces of the U.S. and the West, and the true face of the U.S. “using Taiwan to contain China” to interfere in China’s internal affairs, are increasingly being seen through by more discerning people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202309/t20230927_12570891.htm"],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","Recently, the mainland has cooperated with many Southeast Asian countries to combat telecom fraud. Myanmar, Laos, Indonesia and others have handed over a number of telecom fraud suspects to the mainland. May I ask whether there are Taiwanese suspects among them? Has the mainland notified or handed them over to the Taiwan side?","Cracking down on telecom and online fraud and other illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law, and actively safeguarding the life and property safety and legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, is our consistent stance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","It is reported that Taiwan's so-called first self-built submarine will hold a naming and launching ceremony at the CSBC Kaohsiung plant tomorrow. Taiwan military personnel said that the self-built submarine is intended to confine the PLA to the first island chain. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities are attempting to “seek independence by force.” Overestimating their own capabilities, they will only further intensify tensions and turmoil across the Taiwan Strait and push the Taiwan people into a dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The latest economic forecast published by the Asian Development Bank lowered Taiwan's economic growth rate for this year from 1.5% to 1.2%. Statistics published by the DPP authorities' economic competent authority also show that in August, Taiwan's industrial and manufacturing production indices both recorded 15 consecutive months of negative growth. Public opinion points out that cross-Strait economic and trade…","The mainland is thoroughly implementing the new development philosophy, accelerating the building of a new development pattern, promoting high-quality development, and establishing a modern economic system, and its development opportunities are very broad. Taiwan can fully rely on the mainland's extra-large-scale investment, consumption and production-factor markets to effectively withstand external risks and overcome problems such as insufficient resource endowment, and together with the mainland, it can jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nIt must be pointed out that any words or deeds that attempt to “talk down” the mainland economy or seek “decoupling and severing supply chains” are ulterior and futile. The mainland has always been the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and businesses. Broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots and businesses who actively take part in the mainland's high-quality development will surely gain more opportunities, broader space and a better future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, Hubei, Beijing, Guizhou, Hunan and other places have successively held rich cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange and cooperation have shown a vibrant atmosphere, and cross-Strait economic and trade activities held in Hubei, Beijing, Guizhou, Hunan, and other places have been highlights.\nFrom September 19 to 22, Hubei Province held the 17th Hubei–Wuhan Taiwan Week. Themed “Working Together to Build the Chinese Dream, Joining Hands to Build a Pioneer Zone,” this year's Taiwan Week featured 17 activities across four major sections—economic and trade cooperation, cultural exchange, grassroots exchange, and academic seminars—held in Wuhan, Yichang, Huangshi, Ezhou, and other places, with more than 900 cross-Strait guests in attendance. During the Taiwan Week, the Wuhan–Taipei air route resumed operation, and more than 60 projects in fields including electronic information, precision manufacturing, modern agriculture, biopharmaceuticals, and cultural and creative education were signed, with a total signed investment of 27.298 billion yuan. Multiple Wuhan enterprises signed letters of intent for cooperation with the Miaoli County Farmers' Association of Taiwan, and Hubei University of Economics and several other universities signed inter-school faculty and school-enterprise integrated development agreements with relevant Taiwan universities.\nFrom September 19 to 21, Beijing held the 26th Beijing–Taiwan Science and Technology Forum. Themed “Empowering a Smart Future with Technology, Innovating to Promote Integrated Development,” the forum hosted activities including a digital economy industry cooperation forum, a medical and health industry forum, a seminar on integrated development of industrial and supply chains, and a science and technology exchange and matchmaking meeting, with nearly 400 cross-Strait guests attending.\nOn September 19, Guizhou Province held the 2023 Guizhou–Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Symposium. Themed “Sharing New Opportunities, Integrating for Common Development,” the symposium included specialized industry matchmaking, featured industry tours, and Colorful Guizhou experiences. It focused on four promotion and matchmaking meetings on Guizhou–Taiwan agricultural industry, cultural tourism industry, forestry carbon sink economic development, and aromatic herbal and traditional Chinese medicine industries, promoting industrial matching and cooperation between Guizhou and Taiwan. More than 200 cross-Strait guests attended.\nOn September 22, Hunan Province held the 2023 Hunan–Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Conference. Themed “Seizing New Opportunities, Integrating into the New Pattern,” it hosted the 2nd Straits Yuelu Mountain Forum on Industrial Cooperation, a special matchmaking session for undertaking industrial transfer from the Guangdong–Hong Kong–Macao Greater Bay Area, and matchmaking sessions on tourism, health care, modern agriculture, and biopharmaceutical industries. Nearly 400 Taiwan guests attended, and 39 projects were signed with a total signed investment of 14.5 billion yuan.\nThe cross-Strait economic and trade activities held in Hubei, Beijing, Guizhou, Hunan, and other places have achieved remarkable results, fully demonstrating that the shared voice of compatriots on both sides is that they want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We will continue to hold various economic and trade exchange activities and provide more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses to develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Miaoli County Magistrate Chung Tung-chin recently said during a visit to Hubei that he had specifically communicated with the mainland side about lifting the ban on wendou pomelo. In June this year, Taitung County resumed exports of custard apples and other fruits to the mainland after improving their quality. Many Taiwan agricultural products are now also improving quality. Will individual products be able to…","The General Administration of Customs suspended imports of Taiwan citrus fruits, including pomelos, starting August 3, 2022, because pests and excessive pesticide residues were repeatedly detected in citrus fruits imported from Taiwan into the mainland. The relevant mainland authorities notified the Taiwan side, but the Democratic Progressive Party authorities turned a deaf ear and did not respond. After the mainland announced the suspension of imports, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities further seized the opportunity to engage in political manipulation and incite cross-Strait confrontation, completely disregarding the concerns and interests of fruit farmers on the island.\nRecently, Taitung County Government expressed a strong desire to resume the import of Taiwanese custard apples into the mainland and organized industry players to make rectifications to improve product quality and ensure the safety of custard apples exported to the mainland. We have therefore resumed the import of Taiwanese custard apples into the mainland in accordance with regulations. This provides a reference for Miaoli County in addressing related issues. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and we are willing to work with the Miaoli County Government and relevant industry players to jointly resolve the unsold agricultural products in the county, solve problems for Taiwan farmers, and increase their well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the opening ceremony of the Hangzhou Asian Games has become a hot topic on Taiwan's internet. Taiwan netizens, well-known commentators and people from all walks of life have expressed amazement at the use of advanced technology to showcase traditional Chinese culture in the ceremony. May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","It is a very good thing for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to take part together, share in the grand occasion, and enjoy the glory together. We look forward to the Hangzhou Asian Games bringing more positive energy to cross-Strait exchanges and to the spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Taiwan scholar Tsai Chin-shu was released from prison in May this year. What is Tsai Chin-shu’s recent situation? When can he return to Taiwan? Second question: The “Opinions” mention building an integrated living circle for Xiamen–Kinmen and Fuzhou–Matsu, which some Taiwan residents are concerned about. The “Opinions” encourage the purchase of property in Fujian. Are there corresponding measures now?","First question: Cai Jinshu was sentenced in accordance with law to four years' fixed-term imprisonment and four years' deprivation of political rights for the crime of espionage. The relevant departments have handled the execution of his sentence in accordance with law.\nSecond question: In recent years, the real estate market in Fujian Province has generally maintained a steady development trend, with market supply basically balanced, house prices basically stable, and housing quality continuously improving. Taiwan compatriots living in Fujian, according to their housing needs, voluntarily purchase homes in Fujian. To facilitate life for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian, various places in Fujian have actively taken measures to encourage Taiwan compatriots to buy and invest in property in Fujian.\nAt present, Taiwan compatriots are not restricted from buying homes in areas without purchase restrictions, and the online signing and registration procedures for home purchases are the same as for local residents. For purchases in cities that implement housing purchase restrictions, Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal treatment and equal opportunity with local hukou holders.\nRegarding loans, the People's Bank of China is vigorously promoting the exchange and sharing of cross-Strait credit information, and encourages financial institutions, within the bounds of law and compliance and under controllable risk, to provide individual home purchase loans to Taiwan compatriots. Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal treatment in loan conditions. In addition, Taiwan compatriots may pay into and use the housing provident fund in accordance with regulations, enjoying the same treatment as mainland employees.\nGoing forward, Fujian Province will earnestly implement the “Opinions,” put into practice the detailed measures for equal treatment of Taiwan compatriots in home purchases, continuously improve the mutual recognition mechanism for cross-Strait credit information, support Taiwan compatriots in applying for home purchase loans as needed, and facilitate their home purchases. At the same time, in accordance with law and regulations, Taiwan compatriots living in Fujian will be included in Fujian Province's housing security system, striving to ensure that Taiwan compatriots have housing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Keelung Mayor Hsieh Kuo-liang recently said in a media interview that he is considering referring to the Taipei–Shanghai Twin City Forum model to hold a Keelung–mainland city twin city forum focused on exchanges between port cities. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Seeking peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation is the common voice of compatriots on both sides. We will uphold the concept that “cross-strait compatriots are one family” and, on the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” work together with relevant political parties, counties and cities, groups, and people from all walks of life on the island to promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including exchanges between cities across the Taiwan Strait, to benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","The one-month preparation period for the “plan” on resuming cross-Strait tourism previously announced by the Mainland Affairs Council has passed. Does the mainland side plan to open individual travel and group tours for mainland residents to Taiwan?","Normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and making exchanges in all fields routine is the shared wish of compatriots on both sides and is in the common interest of compatriots on both sides. The mainland tourism authority announced on May 19 this year that travel agencies would be allowed to resume operating group tours for Taiwan residents to the mainland. However, the DPP authorities still refuse to lift the ban on travel agencies on the island operating group tours to the mainland, and they have attached a series of conditions to the resumption of cross-Strait tourism and exchanges. What is nominally “relaxation” is in fact tightened restriction and control, which is completely unpopular. Compatriots in Taiwan see this very clearly and will not be deceived or misled. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, and truly achieve normalization and routinization of cross-Strait tourism and two-way exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","First question: At the opening ceremony of the Hangzhou Asian Games, one scene left a deep impression: when the Chinese Taipei delegation entered the stadium, the spectators loudly chanted “Welcome home.” What is your comment on this? Second question: The Mid-Autumn Festival, a traditional Chinese festival, is coming soon. What activities have various places already held, or are about to hold, for compatriots on…","First question. In the Hangzhou Asian Games, the Chinese Taipei delegation will definitely feel the atmosphere of “home” and “home field” given by compatriots and spectators on the mainland from beginning to end.\nSecond question: In just 38 hours it will be the annual Mid-Autumn Festival, and on this occasion we wish our Taiwan compatriots a happy Mid-Autumn Festival and that all things go smoothly. (Hokkien) Worship the Moon Lady, eat mooncakes, and happily celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival. (Hakka) On the fifteenth day of the eighth month, welcome the moonlight, eat mooncakes, and the whole family reunites to celebrate the harvest. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to celebrate the festival, reunite with relatives and family on the mainland, admire the moon together, and gather with mainland friends for outings, to spend a different Mid-Autumn Festival.\nVarious colorful festive activities are being held or will soon be held in various places. For example, Liaoning hosted the “Full Moon over China, Ink Rhyme of Liaoning and Taiwan” Mid-Autumn calligraphy exhibition and the “Children Read Ancient Charm, Children Look to the Future” Shenyang–Hsinchu Youth Chinese Classics Culture Appreciation Event. Kunshan, Jiangsu hosted the “Twin Blossoms, Lanterns Shining on Both Sides, One Happy Family” Cross-Strait Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival. Zhangping, Fujian hosted the “Celebrating the Harvest · Promoting Harmony and Beauty” Cross-Strait Farmers’ Mid-Autumn Festival Gala. Jinan, Weifang, Qingdao, Yantai, Linyi and Liaocheng in Shandong, together with 11 cross-Strait cities including Taipei, Keelung, Taichung, Kaohsiung and Chiayi, simultaneously held online and offline Shandong–Taiwan Mid-Autumn get-togethers for compatriots on both sides. Anyang, Henan organized compatriots on both sides to celebrate the festival together through the Yijing (Book of Changes) culture, discussing and studying the Yi. Hubei hosted the “2023 Hubei–Taiwan Youth Sports Study Camp and Mid-Autumn Carnival” and the awards ceremony of the 2023 Hubei Taiwan Youth Mid-Autumn Gathering and “Youth Travel Diaries” VLOG Competition, among other events. Ningxia hosted the “Our Festival · Talking About Reunion” Mid-Autumn get-together with regional characteristics at the Goji Food Culture Museum.\nBy the way, I’d like to preview that on September 28, China Media Group launched the Mid-Autumn special program “Blessings Full, Moon Round, One Family” from its “Watching the Taiwan Strait” series of integrated media events, titled “Good Fortune Is Here! Integration Zone.” Filmed in Xiamen, Zhangzhou and Quanzhou in Fujian, and linked live with Taipei, Tainan and Kinmen in Taiwan, it focuses on the new picture of Fujian–Taiwan exchange and integrated development and tells the human stories of cross-Strait blood ties. Please pay attention.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-09-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Peking Opera performing artists Yu Kuizhi and Li Shengsu led a delegation of about 80 people from the National Peking Opera Company to Taiwan for an exchange visit, performing highly representative repertoire such as 'The Women Generals of the Yang Family' and 'Farewell My Concubine,' which was warmly welcomed by audiences on the island. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Cross-Strait relations share the same roots and origins, and the profound Chinese culture is increasingly recognized and loved by compatriots on both sides. We support exchange and cooperation between the two sides in the field of traditional culture and arts, and we also support relevant institutions and individuals on both sides in jointly promoting the excellent Chinese traditional culture.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202309/t20230927_12570889.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-09-28","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","On Taiwan’s submarine. The Taiwanese defense ministry staged the first sea trial of the diesel-electric vessel. The submarine named “Hai Kun” is one of eight new vessels being developed under a multi-billion dollar program to bolster Taiwan’s naval defenses. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on the submarine?","This is not a question about foreign affairs. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The reunification of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait must and will be realized. The DPP authorities have clung stubbornly to the separatist position for “Taiwan independence”, squandered hard-earned money of people in Taiwan and sought to create antagonism and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, which will only undermine cross-Strait peace and stability.\n**************************\nThe regular press conference of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs will be adjourned from September 29 (Friday) to October 6 (Friday) for the Mid-Autumn Festival and the National Day holiday and resumed on October 9 (Monday). During the adjournment, correspondents may reach the Spokesperson’s Office by fax, E-mail or WeChat.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347609.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202309/t20230928_11152824.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first is that the United States, Japan, Australia, Canada and other countries are interested in participating in joint patrols in the South China Sea, and the Philippine military is studying this proposal. In addition, reports say the United States and the Philippines have begun discussing expanding the U.S. military deployment on the Philippines’ east coast in response to China’s…","First, answering the first question. We have noted the relevant reports. It must be emphasized that defense and security cooperation between countries must not harm the interests of third parties, nor harm regional peace and stability. China firmly opposes extra-regional countries meddling in the South China Sea issue, and opposes their use of the pretext of “freedom of navigation” to stir up trouble and make waves, aggravating regional tensions. The Chinese military has always resolutely defended national sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and firmly upholds peace and stability in the South China Sea.\nOn the second question. The Taiwan defense authorities want to use this “whistling to boost courage” approach to prove that their information is accurate. As for whether it is accurate, we will wait and see. We warn the DPP authorities: attempting armed confrontation, “seeking independence through force,” and overestimating oneself will lead only to a dead end.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The PLA has recently conducted large-scale exercises and drills in the sea and airspace around Taiwan. According to Taiwan’s statistics, the number of mainland ships and aircraft has set a record. The head of Taiwan’s defense authorities said that PLA naval military activities around Taiwan are increasingly frequent, increasing the risk of accidental conflict. What comment do you have on this? In addition, we…","First, answering your first question: the joint live-troop drills that the Chinese People's Liberation Army recently organized in the sea and airspace around Taiwan are regular arrangements within the annual plan. They aim to test the joint training results of the troops and to improve multi-service joint operational capabilities. The PLA will regularly organize such drills, strengthen training on the front lines of military struggle, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nOn your second question, it is nothing but a mantis trying to stop a chariot; it will ultimately destroy itself. As for your mention of preventing the PLA from entering the Pacific, that is a pipe dream. No matter how many weapons the DPP authorities build or buy, they cannot block the trend toward national reunification, nor can they shake the PLA's firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Media reports say Taiwan’s defense authorities recently released the 2023 National Defense Report, which states that it will adhere to the military strategic concept of “defensive consolidation, layered deterrence.” The report states that the PLA Eastern and Southern Theater Commands have successively completed expansion of their coastal airports, that PLA military development poses a threat to Taiwan, and that…","Taiwan is part of China, so how can there be a “national defense” report? We have repeatedly pointed out that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and that outside forces are unreliable. In the face of the powerful PLA, so-called “defensive consolidation” cannot hold, and “deterrence” cannot bluff. As for “colluding with foreign powers to seek independence,” it is nothing but a pipe dream, like the Yellow Millet dream. Chinese people do not fight Chinese people, but if some people on the island do not want to be “Chinese,” we will not sit idly by.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Some foreign media have revealed that the United States plans to expand the scale of training for Taiwan's military. A source said this is an attempt by the U.S. side to strengthen deterrence against mainland China by deepening cooperation with Taipei. What comments do you have on this?","For some time, the DPP authorities have strengthened military collusion with the United States, expanded official exchanges and military ties between the two sides, and attempted to rely on external forces to pursue “seeking independence through military means,” seriously undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We will never sit idly by in the face of such conduct.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated. We solemnly warn the US side to immediately stop all forms of official exchanges and military ties between the United States and Taiwan. The Chinese People's Liberation Army, as always, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity and firmly upholds peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","U.S. entrepreneur Elon Musk recently stated that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China and that the United States is “preventing reunification.” What comments do you have on this?","The One-China principle is a common consensus of the international community. The true face of the DPP authorities’ “using force to resist reunification” and of the U.S.’s “using Taiwan to contain China” has been seen through by an increasing number of discerning people. Any act that distorts facts or denies and challenges the One-China principle will end in failure.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the Chairman of the U.S. Joint Chiefs of Staff said in an interview that the U.S. intelligence community assesses that the “balloons” from China earlier this year did not conduct intelligence collection activities and did not transmit any data back to China. What is your comment on this? The U.S. Assistant Secretary of Defense for Indo-Pacific Affairs said that if mainland China imposes a blockade on…","To answer the first question, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs has previously stated China's position many times. We ask the US side not to be like someone who mistakes a bow's reflection in a cup for a snake, or who sees enemy soldiers in every bush and blade of grass.\nAs for the second question, Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and resolving the Taiwan question is China's own internal affair, which can only be decided by the Chinese people themselves and brooks no foreign interference. China adheres to striving for the prospect of peaceful reunification across the Strait with the utmost sincerity and effort, but it will never accept anyone or any force interfering in China's internal affairs under the guise of “peace.” No one should underestimate the Chinese government's and people's firm determination, resolute will, and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe motherland must and will be reunified. The relevant remarks from the US side send a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and are extremely irresponsible and extremely dangerous. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is sharpening its weapons and feeding its horses, standing ready in battle formation, constantly strengthening training and combat preparedness, firmly defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Shandong carrier battle group recently conducted drills in waters near the Taiwan Strait. Some analysts say this is the closest drill to Taiwan so far. What comments do you have on this?","This is a training exercise within the annual plan, aimed at improving the army's combat readiness and warfighting capabilities.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the PLA sent more than 100 military aircraft to operate near the Taiwan Strait. Some experts analyze that the purpose is to exert more military pressure on Taiwan. What comments do you have on this? If the situation in the Taiwan Strait reaches a tense, critical point, is there a possibility of an accidental exchange of fire?","Just now I said that we are willing to show the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. But we will absolutely not allow the slightest room for “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. What truly harms the people of Taiwan are the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and interference by external forces. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will, as always, deter “Taiwan independence” and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-09-28","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson closing remarks (no press Q)","","Finally, I would like to say a few more words. Tomorrow is the Chinese traditional festival, the Mid-Autumn Festival. Chinese people often say, “The bright moon rises over the sea, and across the far corners of the earth we share this moment.” Here, I wish the Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait a happy festival and an early reunion. In two days, it will be the 74th anniversary of the founding of New China. All officers and soldiers of the armed forces will celebrate the birthday of our motherland at their posts, safeguarding the peace of countless households and protecting the rivers and mountains of ten thousand li. I wish our great motherland prosperity and flourishing, and the nation peace and prosperity!","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16255560.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-10-10","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Tsai Ing-wen said today that the island will be democratic for generations despite Chinese pressure and the Taiwanese people would remain free. Do you have any comment on this?","There’s only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory—this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities still cling to the separatist pursuit of “Taiwan independence” and seek foreign support in achieving that agenda and making provocative moves—this is the biggest threat facing peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. To ensure cross-Strait peace and stability, it is essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. Whatever the DPP authorities say or do, it does not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, still less the trend towards China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347611.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202310/t20231010_11158872.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear reporters, hello everyone. I will host today's press conference. First, I will announce information about a cross-Strait exchange event.\nTo implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Integrated Cross-Strait Development”, continuously raise the level of cross-Strait agricultural exchanges and cooperation, explore methods and pathways for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly participate in rural revitalization, and help build the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, the First Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Conference will be held in Zhangping City, Fujian Province, from October 23 to 27.\nThe event takes “Deepening Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchanges and Jointly Building Beautiful Villages” as its theme. It is co-hosted by cross-Strait civil organizations, including the Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Association, the Agriculture Committee of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, the Fujian Provincial Promotion Association for Rural Revitalization, the Taiwan Outstanding Farmers Association, the Taiwan Leisure Agriculture Development Association, and the Taiwan Fine Agriculture Development Association. Nearly 260 people are expected to attend, including experts and scholars in the agricultural field from both sides, Taiwan compatriots who are starting businesses at Taiwan Farmers Entrepreneurship Parks, farmers from Taiwan on the island, and representatives of relevant county, city and township farmers' associations. During the event, industry representatives from both sides will engage in in-depth exchanges on topics such as integrated development of the three industries in rural areas and the construction and development of Taiwan Farmers Entrepreneurship Parks. We warmly welcome Taiwan farmers to actively take part in related activities, and welcome media reporters from both sides of the Strait to cover the event. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","We have noted that in the annual cross-Strait relations survey recently released by Taiwan's United Daily News, the proportion of Taiwan residents worried about “Taiwan independence” and the DPP continuing to “govern” has risen. A spokesperson for the Kuomintang said that the DPP should quickly announce that it abandons “Taiwan independence” and not become a troublemaker for regional peace. What is the…","This poll result shows that more and more Taiwan residents have come to realize that “Taiwan independence” means war. The DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have become not only troublemakers for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, but also the greatest disruptors of the peaceful and secure lives of Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573403.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that the 2024 Taiwan regional election is absolutely not a choice between war and peace, but a choice between “democracy and authoritarian dictatorship.” He also said that other candidates who directly or indirectly accept the one-China principle do not represent mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","Both sides of the Strait belong to one China. The historical context is clear, the legal and factual basis is clear, and it is beyond doubt and cannot be changed. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatism runs against the common will of compatriots on both sides, seriously harms their interests, and will only push Taiwan into peril. “Taiwan independence golden grandsons” will only bring harm to Taiwan's descendants.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573405.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台央广网记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou was dissatisfied with the DPP authorities changing the English name of the “Double Ten” events to “TAIWAN NATIONAL DAY,” believing it is an attempt to smuggle in “Taiwan independence.” He refused to attend related events, and Chu Li-luan, Hou Yu-ih and others also did not attend. Could the spokesperson comment on this?","We appreciate Mr. Ma Ying-jeou and other figures from all walks of life on the island for their clear stance in opposing “Taiwan independence.” In recent years, the DPP authorities have repeatedly staged political farces that smuggle in “Taiwan independence” agendas. These only endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and only make the world see more clearly that their intention to seek “independence” has not died. No matter what the DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces do or what tricks they play, they cannot change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they stop the historical trend that the motherland must and will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573406.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","Recently, Kuomintang (KMT) Vice Chairperson Xia Liyan said on a program on the island that the KMT is neither a “pro-China” party nor a party that supports unification. May I ask the spokesperson for comment on this?","We express concern over the relevant remarks. Mainland residents have voiced their dissatisfaction with such remarks, which undermine mutual trust across the Strait and hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides. I want to emphasize that the two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the will of the people, the trend of the times, and a historical inevitability that no force can stop. We hope that Taiwan’s relevant political parties, groups, and individuals from all walks of life will join us, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” in upholding the great righteousness of the nation, firmly staying on the correct course, pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, safeguarding peace in the Taiwan Strait, promoting national reunification, and benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573404.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Taiwan residents have long been dissatisfied with the DPP authorities' opening of imports of “Lai pork.” Recently, it was exposed in Taoyuan that the origin of U.S. pork imported into Taiwan had been concealed and altered. Preliminary statistics show that 120,000 kilograms of such U.S. pork flowed into 15 counties and cities in Taiwan, confirming residents' earlier concerns about “washing origins.” What comments…","We have noted the relevant situation and are highly concerned about the health and well-being of the people of Taiwan.\nIn January 2021, the DPP authorities, against the wishes of the people of Taiwan, insisted on opening imports of American pork containing ractopamine. From the very beginning this triggered strong opposition from all sectors on the island and public outrage among the people of Taiwan. Over two years later, the whereabouts of the “ractopamine pork” remain a mystery. Now a controversy has erupted on the island over American pork being “origin-washed,” which precisely confirms the concerns the people of Taiwan had expressed earlier. In fact, over the years, from the opening to “ractopamine pork” to the “nuclear food,” and from importing “poisonous eggs” to whitewashing “American pork,” the people of the island have lacked due safety guarantees for their food. We hope the DPP authorities, keeping the food safety and health and well-being of the people in mind, will give the people a responsible account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573401.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","海峡之声电台记者","The mainland recently stated that it will study, in accordance with regulations, suspending or partially suspending the tariff preferences granted to Taiwanese products under the ECFA framework. Petrochemical, textile, and machinery industry operators on the island said they are very worried and hope the two sides can achieve peace and mutual benefit. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Since the ECFA took effect, it has brought tangible benefits to industries and residents on both sides of the Strait, especially to related industries and residents in Taiwan. The desire to ensure that the ECFA continues to take effect is mainstream public opinion on the island, which also proves that the ECFA is an agreement that benefits Taiwan compatriots. However, for some time, the DPP authorities have not only failed to take practical measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but have continually escalated them, using various pretexts and means to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This will only shrink the space for Taiwan’s economic development and directly harm the vital interests of broad Taiwan compatriots. To safeguard and advance the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots, the key lies in uniting compatriots on both sides of the Strait, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist actions, and jointly maintaining and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573402.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The Ministry of Finance and three other departments recently issued the “Announcement on Raising the Additional Deduction Ratio for R&D Expenses of Integrated Circuit and Industrial Machine Tool Enterprises,” which raises the additional deduction ratio for eligible R&D expenses by 20 percentage points. Does the spokesperson’s policy apply equally to Taiwan-invested enterprises?","This policy applies to all enterprises registered on the mainland, and of course that includes Taiwan-funded enterprises. Take a well-known Taiwan-funded enterprise in Shanghai as an example: in 2022, its R&D expenses were 42.92 million yuan. If the super deduction ratio is adjusted from 100% to 120%, this enterprise will save 1.29 million yuan in taxes. We will continue to improve policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, implement equal treatment, optimize the business environment, and help the broad masses of Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises develop better and faster on the mainland. We hope that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will make full use of the policies that benefit and assist enterprises, put down roots in mainland development, strengthen technological R&D to enhance product competitiveness, accelerate transformation and upgrading to build innovation-driven momentum, and better integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","The head of Taiwan’s security department recently claimed that after the mainland implemented the “Counter-Espionage Law,” the number of cases of Taiwan residents being questioned when going to the mainland has increased. Some people were “summoned for talks” after checking into hotels. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Revising and implementing the Counter-Espionage Law is a strong legal measure to prevent, stop, and punish various espionage-related illegal and criminal activities and to safeguard national security. It must be emphasized that we have consistently encouraged and supported normal, healthy cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in espionage or other illegal and criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland need have no concerns at all. They can come to the mainland happily and return to Taiwan safely. Come happily to 踢桃 (meaning “to stroll”), and return home safely 返去厝 (Min Nan).","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Singapore Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong recently said at the “Asia Forward Summit 2023” that the one-China issue should not be viewed as a confrontation between so-called “democracy and authoritarianism,” and that the parties involved in cross-Strait issues should not step by step approach danger, as this could lead to miscalculation or accidents. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The One-China principle is a common consensus of the international community. We appreciate the international community’s understanding and support for the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” and striving to complete national reunification.\nWhat qualifications do the DPP authorities have to talk about “democracy” when they vigorously carry out a “green terror” on the island, suppress and persecute dissenters, and deceive public opinion and swindle people internationally? Some people deliberately fabricate the false proposition of so-called “democracy versus autocracy,” aiming to cover up the fact that Taiwan faces a choice between peace and war, and to deceive votes. This old trick is already well known to all and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573400.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台国广记者","As “doubts about the United States” continue to rise on the island, the head of Taiwan’s security authorities declared that the United States has three reasons it cannot abandon Taiwan, including geostrategic, value-based and supply chain security cooperation. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The relevant remarks of the DPP authorities fully expose their guilty conscience and fear in plotting “independence,” and their attempt to borrow outside support to embolden themselves. Those who are willing to be pawns will inevitably become “discarded pieces”; this is a settled conclusion. From the “Saigon moment” to the “escape from Kabul,” and from Iraq and Afghanistan to Libya, the United States has stirred up trouble everywhere for its own selfish interests, and when the situation turns unfavorable, it withdraws and dumps the mess on others. I believe these examples will make more and more Taiwan compatriots recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders are unreliable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573399.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, there have been calls on the island to adjust “de-Sinicization” and the “curriculum guidelines,” which has also sparked discussion about how to pass on Chinese culture. How does the spokesperson evaluate this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and the same ancestry. Chinese culture is the root and belonging of the hearts of compatriots on both sides, and a precious common treasure and spiritual bond of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces, in order to seek “Taiwan independence” separatism, are deliberately and persistently pursuing “de-Sinicization.” This will only leave Taiwan compatriots spiritually and culturally like water without a source and a tree without roots, and it will also damage the feelings between compatriots on both sides and aggravate hostility and confrontation across the Strait. Such perverse conduct, which abandons ancestors and forgets one's origins, will certainly meet strong opposition and resolute boycott from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","I have two questions. First, according to reports, when DPP Taiwan leadership election candidate Lai Ching-te recently attended a symposium at National Sun Yat-sen University in Taiwan, a female student asked him about corruption-related issues in the DPP, but Lai countered by asking which specific incident she meant. We would like to ask the spokesperson for comments on this. The second question: during this…","First question: Since the DPP authorities took office, for the sake of party self-interest and heedless of people’s livelihoods, scandals and corruption cases such as “black gold” politics, graft, and fraud have emerged endlessly and grown ever more severe. It can be said that they have “fattened the DPP while bringing hardship to Taiwan’s people.” The people have their own scale in their hearts. The situation you mentioned fully shows what kind of goods the DPP is in the eyes of Taiwan’s people.\nSecond question: During the just-concluded Mid-Autumn Festival and National Day holidays, the mainland’s tourism industry showed strong momentum of recovery. Tourist popularity brought market prosperity, and tourism consumption confidence has been fully restored. Domestic trips and domestic tourism revenue both exceeded the same period in 2019, before the pandemic. The potential for cross-Strait tourism exchange and cooperation is enormous. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to travel and sightsee, to admire the beautiful landscapes of China, and to see the new face of development across the mainland. We will create better conditions for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland and provide better products and services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First question: We noted that in her “Double Ten” speech yesterday, Tsai Ing-wen said that peace is the only option for cross-Strait relations, and that she is willing to develop a basis for interaction acceptable to both sides and a way of peaceful coexistence with the mainland. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond? Second question: The Ministry of Commerce recently announced that the trade…","On the first question, the people of the island have their own views on the conduct of the DPP authorities. Since taking office in 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to recognize the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus.” They have stubbornly pursued “Taiwan independence” separatism and “relying on foreign powers to seek independence,” wantonly undermined the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, seriously harmed the vital interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and pushed Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war and peril.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the mainstream public opinion on the island. The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for cross-strait dialogue and consultation. While the DPP authorities talk empty words about peace and interactive dialogue, they stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to recognize the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus.” This two-faced approach cannot deceive the world, and the notion of “peaceful separation” is sheer wishful thinking.\nOn the second question, regarding the investigation of trade barriers against Taiwan, the DPP authorities’ claims do not conform to the facts and reverse right and wrong. For a long time, the DPP authorities have unilaterally and extensively restricted imports of mainland products, which is an objective fact. The Ministry of Commerce’s announcement of extending the time limit of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan was a decision made in accordance with relevant regulations and investigative needs, and it is a normal procedure. The DPP authorities are taking the opportunity to engage in political manipulation and incite cross-strait confrontation. This shows that they are solely interested in political self-interest and disregard the interests and well-being of operators and people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231011_12573407.htm"],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Spokesperson, in Tsai Ing-wen’s “Double Ten” speech this time, she pointed out that she is “willing” to offer, under four conditions such as “being based on the will of the Taiwan public and premised on equality and dignity,” the possibility of peaceful coexistence and development and interaction with the mainland. What comments does the Taiwan Affairs Office have on this? In addition, Tsai also said that peace…","On the first question you raised, I have already stated our position when answering Phoenix TV's question.\nOn the second question you mentioned, there is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and must not be divided. This is the true status quo of cross-Strait relations and the common understanding of the international community. Since the DPP authorities took office in 2016, they have denied the \"1992 Consensus,\" repeatedly colluded with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at \"independence,\" undermined the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They are the true disruptors of the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water, and \"Taiwan independence\" is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. Taiwan is \"the Taiwan of China.\" Any act attempting to change this status quo will only aggravate tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Only by returning to the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development, and only then will peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait have a practical guarantee.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: after Tsai Ing-wen's eight years in \"office,\" how does the Taiwan Affairs Office view the progress in cross-Strait relations? Second question: the DPP is one of Taiwan's two major parties, so is there a possibility of dialogue between the mainland and the DPP?","First question: Since May 2016, the DPP authorities have obstinately adhered to the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance, refused to acknowledge the one-China principle, distorted and denied the “1992 Consensus,” intensified their collusion with external forces, and continuously engaged in “independence” provocations, creating cross-Strait confrontation and obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development. This has caused cross-Strait relations to remain persistently in tension and turmoil. Their actions not only endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, but also harm the vital interests of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots.\nRegarding the second question you raised, any political party in Taiwan that acknowledges the one-China principle will face no obstacles in its dealings with us. As long as the DPP changes its “Taiwan independence” stance, the door to exchange and dialogue with it is open. But if it obstinately adheres to the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and refuses to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” then no exchange or dialogue is possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Spokesperson, when will the 2023 Guimao Year Xiandu Ceremony honoring the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan be held in China, and what Taiwan-related activities will take place during it?","The Guimao (2023) Chinese Xiandu Ceremony to Worship Emperor Xuanyuan (the Yellow Emperor), sponsored by the People's Government of Zhejiang Province, will be held on October 23 (Double Ninth Festival) in Jinyun County, Lishui City, Zhejiang Province. This year's Jinyun ceremony takes as its theme \"Hearts of the Four Seas Unite to Worship the Ancestor, 'Eight-Eight Strategy' Opens a New Chapter,\" and 500 representatives of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, overseas Chinese and various social sectors will attend. During the event, the 6th Yellow Emperor Culture Seminar, cross-Strait cultural exchange activities, economic and trade matchmaking meetings and other Taiwan-related sub-events will also be held.\nEmperor Xuanyuan is an important cultural symbol and spiritual emblem of the Chinese nation. The Jinyun worship of Emperor Xuanyuan began in the Eastern Jin dynasty and has a history of more than 1,600 years. Since Jinyun County resumed public worship in 1998, more than 3,800 Taiwan compatriots over the past 26 years have come to attend the ceremony, which has become an important cultural brand for cross-Strait exchanges. We warmly welcome compatriots on and off the island to take part in this grand ceremony in various forms, to honor ancestors and revere forebears, and to jointly inherit and promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","台湾“中国时报”记者","Recently, foreign media reported that four Taiwanese businesses are key companies assisting Huawei and may be placed on the US blacklist. Taiwan's “Ministry of Economic Affairs” also announced that it will launch an investigation, and that if the actual business operations of these companies on the mainland do not match the projects originally approved for investment, they will also be penalized on this basis.…","So-called “decoupling and breaking chains” and “small yard with a high fence” harm others without benefiting oneself, and they will not work. The four companies reported by the relevant media do not belong to the semiconductor industry chain, and they do not produce semiconductor-related materials, equipment, or products. The DPP authorities are jumping on the bandwagon to hype this, attempting to obstruct normal cooperation between enterprises across the Taiwan Strait and create obstacles to cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges. This is unpopular, and it will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-11","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","Taiwan’s self-built submarine has been mired in controversy recently. KMT legislator Ma Wen-chun revealed that GL, the winning design contractor for the self-built submarine, was established overseas only 48 days before it received a bid worth more than NT$600 million. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","The DPP authorities attempt to “seek independence through force,” which is overreaching and very dangerous, and will only push the people of Taiwan further into peril. The relevant issues you raised fully expose that the DPP authorities, for their own private interests, squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people; they are both corrupt and arrogant, and the people of Taiwan are increasingly seeing this clearly.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231011_12573384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-10-13","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, during the visit of Japan’s Minister of Defense to the United States, the US side said it looks forward to building a strong cooperative relationship with Japan and jointly advancing the US-Japan alliance. The two sides also reaffirmed the importance of maintaining peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific region and the Taiwan Strait. The US side said its defense commitment to Japan covers…","The Chinese side has consistently maintained that defense and security cooperation between relevant countries should not target third parties, much less undermine regional peace and stability. It must be stressed that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands have been China's inherent territory since ancient times. No matter what the US and Japan say or do, they cannot change this iron-clad fact, nor can they shake the Chinese side's firm resolve and steadfast will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nWe demand that the relevant countries respect history, face reality, stop hyping the so-called 'China threat,' stop stirring up confrontation, stop spreading false narratives and provocative remarks, and stop using bilateral alliance treaties to carry out military coercion against third countries. The Chinese military resolutely defends national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguards regional and world peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16258569.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-10-13","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, Japan plans to increase Self-Defense Forces deployments in Kyushu, and some analysts believe this is mainly to respond to the “military threat” posed by China that is growing in Okinawa and the Taiwan Strait. In addition, the FY2024 budget recently submitted by Japan’s Ministry of Defense set a record high, exceeding 7.7 trillion yen. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","In recent years, Japan has repeatedly broken through the constraints of the “Peace Constitution” and the principle of “exclusively defense-oriented defense policy.” Using the hype of regional threats, it has sharply increased defense spending, accelerated the development of new combat domains, and developed long-range strike capabilities, going further and further down the path of military expansion. This poses serious challenges to regional and world peace and stability and to the post-war international order, and has triggered widespread doubt and high vigilance at home and abroad.\nThe Chinese side urges Japan to deeply draw lessons from history, and to do more things that are conducive to maintaining regional peace and stability, rather than the opposite.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16258569.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-10-18","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that on October 16, Canadian military officials said that while a Canadian Armed Forces reconnaissance aircraft was conducting a mission in international airspace near China, it was intercepted by Chinese military aircraft, and the Canadian Defence Minister said the Chinese action was “unsafe and unprofessional”. What is China’s comment on this?","Wu Qian: Recently, a Canadian Air Force CP-140 aircraft repeatedly intruded into the airspace of China's Chiwei Yu and approached China's East China coast, entering the Taiwan Strait to conduct reconnaissance and harassment. China's air force, in accordance with Chinese law and relevant international rules, took control measures including verification and identification, tracking and surveillance, and warning and expulsion. The handling was entirely reasonable and lawful, and professional and standardized. The relevant hype by the Canadian side disregards facts and aims to confuse international audiences. The Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. The Canadian side's conduct seriously infringes China's sovereignty, threatens China's national security, and can easily cause misunderstanding and miscalculation. Its nature is egregious and very dangerous. China strongly condemns this and has lodged stern representations with the Canadian side.\nWe solemnly warn the Canadian side to be prudent in its words and deeds, strictly control the actions of its front-line forces, immediately cease any provocative acts, and earnestly avoid further escalation of the situation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/16260167.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278489.html",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-10-20","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the U.S. Department of Defense held a press conference on October 17, at which senior U.S. defense department and military officials said that since 2021, “coercive and risky actions” by Chinese military aircraft targeting the U.S. and its allies in airspace over the East China Sea and South China Sea have increased sharply. What is your comment on this?","The US side is shifting the blame. It is hyping up a “Chinese military threat” that does not exist. This is a premeditated attack and smear against China, with ulterior political motives. China firmly opposes this and has lodged stern representations with the US side.\nThe root of the China-US maritime and air military security issue lies in US warships and aircraft traveling thousands of miles to stir up trouble and provoke at China's doorstep, and in their long-term, large-scale, high-frequency reconnaissance harassment in the sea and airspace around China. Statistics show that since 2023, US reconnaissance aircraft have made more than 2,000 sorties of close-in approach. US warships have twice rushed into China's Xisha territorial waters, and five times transited the Taiwan Strait and publicized it, deliberately displaying strength and provoking China. This easily leads to dangerous encounters and pushes up regional tensions. Against foreign warships and aircraft that illegally intrude into China's jurisdictional sea and airspace or interfere with normal training activities, China has, in accordance with law and regulations, taken professional safety control measures, including verification and identification, tracking and surveillance, and warning and expulsion. For those that provoked first and showed hostile intent, China has been compelled to take necessary countermeasures. Any sovereign state would do the same. The facts speak louder than words: the US is the real provocateur, risk-taker and troublemaker.\nWe urge the US side to stop misleading international public opinion with false narratives, stop close-in reconnaissance of China, strictly control and restrain frontline force activities, stop all provocative actions, avoid causing misunderstanding and miscalculation, and prevent maritime and air accidents that would undermine regional peace and stability. The Chinese military remains on high alert and resolutely defends national sovereignty, security and maritime rights and interests.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278490.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-10-23","Mao Ning","AFP","Chinese media outlets reported yesterday that Chinese authorities have carried out investigation into the world’s biggest iPhone manufacturer Foxconn. Taiwan politician Zheng Wencan said that Taiwan companies should not be put under political review. Can you share the main reason behind the investigation?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347619.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202310/t20231023_11166298.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-10-24","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan “vice president” Lai has criticized the Chinese mainland over its tax probe into Foxconn. Lai said Beijing should cherish and treasure Taiwanese companies given their help to the mainland’s economic development and not put pressure on these companies during an election there. The Taiwan affairs office has not commented on Lai’s remarks. Would the foreign ministry comment on this?","There is no “vice president” in Taiwan and what you mentioned is not related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347620.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202310/t20231024_11167095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-10-25","Wu Qian","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","Recently, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2023 “Report on China's Military and Security Developments.” This report disregards facts and makes things up. It uses plausible-sounding rhetoric to distort the interpretation of China's national defense policy and military strategy, hypes a “China military threat” that does not exist, presumptuously speculates about China's military development in the nuclear, space and cyber domains, and points fingers and meddles in China's internal affairs on the Taiwan question. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this, and have already lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nChina adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues a defensive national defense policy. It never bullies the small or preys on the weak. In the more than 70 years since the founding of New China, China has never initiated a war and has never seized an inch of another country's land. The United States, by contrast, is addicted to war. In its more than 240 years as a nation, it has been at peace for only 16 years, and it has built more than 800 overseas military bases in over 80 countries and regions. From Afghanistan to Iraq, from Syria to Libya, wherever the U.S. war machine has rolled, the local people have been plunged into misery. The U.S. has sent depleted uranium munitions and cluster bombs to Ukraine, dispatched carrier strike groups to the Mediterranean, and delivered weapons and ammunition to Israel. Is this the “gospel” that the so-called “guardian of human rights” brings to the region? The U.S. has strengthened its military deployments in the Asia-Pacific, consolidated bilateral military alliances, cobbled together trilateral security partnerships, peddled the “Quad” mechanism, and strengthened the “Five Eyes” alliance. These manipulations intensify bloc confrontation and the arms race in the international community and cause serious shocks to the international security system and the global governance system. Facts prove that the United States is the “fundamental source of chaos” in the international order, the “behind-the-scenes manipulator” of world turmoil, and the “greatest disruptor” of regional peace and stability.\nFacing a severe and complex international security environment, China must build a strong military. The Chinese military will never stand idly by while national sovereignty, security and development interests are harmed, and it will never allow anyone or any force to infringe upon or split China. The development of the Chinese military aims to deter war threats, defend its own security and safeguard world peace. It is not directed at any specific country or target, and it is both legitimate and lawful and reasonable and appropriate. China has always kept its nuclear forces at the minimum level required by national security needs and has consistently worked to safeguard global strategic security. On the contrary, in recent years the U.S. has successively withdrawn from arms control treaties such as the Anti-Ballistic Missile Treaty and the Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty, upgraded its “triad” nuclear forces, and sought to deploy land-based intermediate-range missiles in Europe and the Asia-Pacific and to strengthen so-called “extended deterrence.” Nuclear submarine cooperation among the U.S., the UK and Australia constitutes a serious risk of nuclear proliferation and undermines regional peace and stability. The U.S. manipulates the “nuclear” issue and plays “nuclear double standards” merely as a pretext to expand its own nuclear arsenal and maintain its military hegemony.\nTaiwan's return to China is part of the international order after World War II, as clearly stated in the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, and the one-China principle affirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 has long become international consensus. The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and seek to “rely on the U.S. to pursue independence.” The U.S. government has upgraded official exchanges with Taiwan and continuously provided arms sales and military aid to Taiwan, seeking to “use Taiwan to contain China.” This is the root cause of changes to the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The U.S. and the DPP authorities are the “troublemakers” of tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China's taking of necessary measures to defend its national territory and sovereignty is justified, reasonable and lawful, and the U.S. has no qualification to pass judgment. We urge the U.S. to stop, under any pretext or by any means, strengthening U.S.-Taiwan military ties and illegally arming Taiwan, to stop creating factors that heighten tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and to stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in “seeking independence through armed force.” The Chinese People's Liberation Army has the confidence and capability to defeat any external interference and any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and to achieve the complete reunification of the motherland.\nMilitary-to-military relations are an important component of China-U.S. relations. We attach importance to them and maintain candid and effective communication with the U.S. through military diplomatic channels. The difficulties and obstacles currently facing military-to-military relations were entirely created by the U.S. side, and right and wrong are plain to see. The U.S. knowingly pretends ignorance: while doing things that harm China's security interests, it calls for crisis management and stronger communication. There is no such reasoning under heaven.\nFor more than twenty years, the U.S. has stubbornly clung to mistaken perceptions of China and has, year after year, published reports filled with falsehoods and clichés. It harms itself and misleads the world. We urge the U.S. to stop fabricating false narratives, correct its mistaken perceptions of China, and, with a sincere attitude and concrete actions, promote the healthy and stable development of relations between the two countries and their militaries.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278454.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's regular TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Please spokesperson introduce the 1st Straits Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Conference being held in Zhangping City, Fujian Province.","On October 24, the first Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Conference was held in Zhangping, Fujian, and related seminar and visit activities will continue until the 27th. This event is a concrete measure to implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” and it has the following three characteristics.\nFirst, it thoroughly implements the “Opinions” and pushes Fujian-Taiwan integrated development to take new steps. Experts and scholars were invited to interpret the content of the “Opinions” in depth, a new platform for cross-Strait agricultural exchange and cooperation was built, Taiwan compatriots were allowed to see the state of agricultural development on the mainland firsthand, and more Taiwan farmers were encouraged and supported to take root on the mainland. This fully reflects the strong atmosphere of integrated development in cross-Strait relations.\nSecond, it gathers mainstream public opinion in the cross-Strait agricultural sector. Nearly 500 people attended the conference, including experts and scholars in cross-Strait agriculture, Taiwan compatriot entrepreneurs from the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park, Taiwan farmers from the island, and representatives of relevant counties, townships, and farmers' associations. The overall scale greatly exceeded expectations, reflecting the strong desire of compatriots on both sides to accelerate the restoration and expansion of cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.\nThird, it brings together the wisdom of both sides' industries, with notable results. Under the theme “Deepen Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange, Jointly Create Beautiful Villages,” the conference conducted in-depth discussions on topics including the integration of the three rural industries (tea and tourism integration), the development and breeding of superior varieties, and the construction and development of the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park. Experts and scholars, entrepreneurs, and farmer representatives from both sides exchanged experiences on rural revitalization and industrial development, looked ahead to ways of future cross-Strait agricultural cooperation, and studied solutions to common problems. At the opening ceremony, 25 cross-Strait agricultural cooperation projects were signed, with notable results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Cross-Strait exchange activities continue to be vibrant recently. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","We hereby give advance notice of four economic, trade, and cultural exchange events that relevant departments and localities will hold in late October and early November.\nThe Sixth World Hakka Merchants Conference will be held in Meizhou, Guangdong, from November 2 to 4. The event is hosted by the People's Government of Guangdong Province, supported by the Central Office for Hong Kong and Macao Affairs, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese and Their Relatives, the All-China Federation of Industry and Commerce, and the China Council for the Promotion of International Trade, and organized by the People's Government of Meizhou City. The conference aims to promote connections, exchanges, and cooperation among overseas and domestic merchants and chambers of commerce, and to promote economic and cultural interaction and the shared prosperity of humanistic business paths. The conference has three main features. First, a clear theme: the conference takes 'Promoting the Hakka Merchant Spirit and Contributing to National Rejuvenation' as its theme, and will release the 'Global Hakka Merchants' Initiative for Supporting National Rejuvenation' and hold a launch ceremony for the global Hakka merchants' support for the 'High-Quality Development Project for Hundreds of Counties, Thousands of Towns, and Ten Thousand Villages.' Second, rich content: it covers the opening conference, economic and commercial activities, academic forums, sports events, and Hakka cultural performances, and will be a cultural feast with a strong Cantonese flavor and a rich Hakka character. Third, broad scope: more than 800 participants from over 100 countries and regions at home and abroad will attend. We welcome Hakka compatriots and merchant representatives from Taiwan to actively participate in the relevant activities, and we also welcome cross-Strait media reporters to conduct interviews and coverage.\nThe 2023 Sixth Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, Macao Drone Aerial Photography Creation Competition, themed 'Setting Sail,' was launched on May 31 with a brand-new competition schedule and format. It added a campus competition unit and an aerial photography track, and a total of 485 works from teams on both sides of the Strait were submitted. From October 28 to November 3, a series of award ceremony activities for the competition will be held in Shenzhen. The competition has fully leveraged Shenzhen's advantages in the drone industry and film and television creation bases, and has developed into one of the best-known competitions in cross-Strait drone aerial photography. To improve creative quality and enhance interaction and exchange, this year a creative camp for Taiwanese participants has also been added, and a drone performance will be held at the Dayun City in Longgang District on the evening of October 31.\nThe Fourth Golden Rooster Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao Youth Short Film Season will be held in Xiamen from October 30 to November 3. This year, a total of 1,232 short film works were collected, including 165 works from Taiwan and co-productions across the Strait. Six of them have made it into the top 20 and entered the final review stage. During the Short Film Season, youth director short film screenings, special screenings from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, creative exchange camps, and promotion ceremonies will be held. We welcome everyone to pay attention and participate.\nIn terms of economic and trade exchanges, the 21st China (Suzhou) Electronics Information Expo will be held at the Suzhou International Expo Center from November 9 to 11. Themed 'Digital Empowerment, Innovative Manufacturing,' this year's Expo includes an opening ceremony, five thematic forums, and one cross-Strait intelligent equipment industry matchmaking event. The Expo's exhibition area covers 20,000 square meters with 800 booths, and Taiwan-funded enterprises account for 52%. An online exhibition area is also provided, offering exhibitors online exhibitions, live streaming, and one-on-one online business negotiation services. More than 300 well-known cross-Strait enterprises have registered to exhibit so far. We welcome Taiwanese compatriot businesses and enterprises to actively participate in the relevant activities, and we welcome cross-Strait media reporters to conduct interviews and coverage.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Recently, cross-Strait Mazu cultural exchange activities were held in places such as Kunshan and Xiapu. Please introduce the relevant situation. In addition, has there been any new progress on the activity of the Mazu golden statue from the Mazu Ancestral Temple in Putian touring Taiwan for safety blessings mentioned at the previous press conference?","Mazu culture is an important part of China's excellent traditional culture and an important spiritual bond connecting compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Kunshan is one of the regions on the mainland where Taiwan investment is most active and Taiwanese-invested enterprises are most densely concentrated. In 2010, the Tianhou Palace of Huiju Temple in Kunshan received a divided incense spirit from a Mazu temple on the island, creating a spiritual home where Taiwan compatriots working in Jiangsu can find a sense of homeland. On October 16, the Kunshan Mazu Culture Exchange Association initiated and organized the activity “Passing on Incense and Destined Bonds, Hearts Linked Across the Strait—Kunshan Mazu Tour to Taiwan.” During the 7-day, 6-night tour to Taiwan, the group successively visited the Cihui Temple in Banqiao, New Taipei; the Zhenlan Temple in Dajia, Taichung; the Wanhe Temple in Nantun, Taichung; the Fengtian Temple in Xingang, Chiayi; the Qing’an Temple in Xigang, Tainan; the Tianhou Temple at Luermen in Tainan; and the Tianhou Temple in Qigang, Kaohsiung. There they paid respects with incense and established sister temple ties, fully demonstrating the blood kinship of compatriots on both sides who share the same language and culture and the same roots and origins, as well as their reverence for the “Goddess of Peace across the Strait.”\nOn October 20, the millennium celebration of the Songshan Mazu Palace across the Strait was held in Xiapu, Fujian. The event was jointly sponsored by the Songshan Mazu Culture Exchange Center of Xiapu, the Xiapu Mazu Association, the Taiwan Mazu Fellowship Association, and the Taiwan Chinese Excellent Traditional Culture Exchange Association, among other Mazu civil organizations on both sides. More than 80 temples on the mainland and nearly 40 Mazu temples and associations in 13 counties and cities in Taiwan responded and took part, and more than 1,000 guests from both sides paid homage to Mazu together, showing that both sides are one family and jointly praying for peace across the Strait.\nRegarding the matter of the Mazu golden statue from the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple in Putian, Fujian, touring Taiwan for a blessing, the relevant units are working hard to push it forward, and we are glad to see it take place smoothly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576961.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou recently gave a speech in the United States, pointing out that some people in the US intend to “use TSMC as a weapon,” “use Taiwan as a battlefield,” and “turn Taiwan into a second Ukraine,” completely without considering the safety and well-being of the Taiwan public. What comment do you have?","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou has exposed the true intentions of certain people in the United States who advocate interference in the Taiwan question, and has voiced the common aspirations of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Certain people in the United States have deliberately and persistently pursued a strategy of “using Taiwan to contain China,” attempting to suppress China's development and obstruct the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and are willing to sacrifice the lives and property of Taiwan compatriots for this purpose, with an extremely sinister intent. The DPP authorities, “relying on the United States to seek independence” and willing to serve as pawns of the United States, will inevitably become “discarded pieces.”\nOnly by resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively maintained, and only then can the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the future development of Taiwan be effectively safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576964.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","During his illicit visit to Taiwan, Rosenberger, Chairperson of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT), said, “The U.S. opposes unilateral changes to the status quo, including not supporting ‘Taiwan independence,’” and called for dialogue across the Taiwan Strait. Some media have pointed out that Lai Ching-te's remark about “pragmatic Taiwan independence workers” has worried the United States, and it is very…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a common consensus of the international community. Not supporting “Taiwan independence” is a solemn commitment made by the U.S. side. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable, and “Taiwan independence workers” are “troublemakers.” Stubbornly insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position and insisting on pursuing “independence” through provocation will only plunge Taiwan into danger and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","According to Taiwan media reports, a Taiwanese citizen stranded in Israel who had hoped to seek help from the DPP authorities was coldly told, \"Please book a flight online.\" What is your comment on this? What assistance will the mainland provide to Taiwan compatriots in the Palestinian-Israeli area, or those who wish to evacuate?","Taiwan compatriots are citizens of China and are our flesh and blood. A strong motherland is the solid backing of Taiwan compatriots. When Taiwan compatriots encounter difficulties overseas, or when their lives or property are threatened, please immediately call the Consular Protection and Service Emergency Hotline to seek assistance from Chinese embassies and consulates abroad (to call the hotline from overseas, dial +86-1012308, or you may dial the backup long-number +86-10-59913991). We will provide overseas consular protection to Taiwan compatriots in the same way as to mainland residents. The relevant departments will closely track developments in the Israel-Palestine conflict and will do their utmost to provide assistance to Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, a new round of large-scale conflict between Israel and Palestine has drawn intense attention on the island. Chu Li-lun said this has let everyone feel just how fearsome and perilous war is, and that peace across the Strait is what everyone most looks forward to. Some public opinion holds that when the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” thread becomes increasingly clear, talking about peace is…","The cruelty of war makes the preciousness of peace all the more evident. Wanting peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opinion on the island, persistently adhere to the “Taiwan independence” stance, continuously colluding with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at “independence,” escalating the risk of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait and step by step pushing Taiwan toward the brink of war and peril. This is extremely dangerous and profoundly irresponsible.\n“Taiwan independence” means war. We hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will cherish peace across the Taiwan Strait as they cherish their own eyes, and will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” and separatism just as they oppose war. Working together with compatriots on the mainland, let us promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576963.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Recently, the head of Taiwan's transportation authority said mainland tourists will not come this year, “we'll see next year,” effectively declaring that the promised “one million mainland visitors to Taiwan” this year has fallen through. What is your comment on this?","Cross-strait tourism should have broad room for development in a favorable overall environment of cross-strait relations; this is the common expectation of compatriots on both sides. In recent years, the reckless actions of the DPP authorities have seriously damaged cross-strait relations and seriously harmed the interests and well-being of cross-strait industries and compatriots, including the tourism industry on the island. Over the past three years, the DPP authorities have adopted a series of restrictive measures on cross-strait personnel exchanges and travel, blocking the path to the development of cross-strait tourism. Since this year, we have adopted a series of positive measures to promote the convenience of cross-strait personnel exchanges, and announced the resumption of travel agencies' group tourism business for Taiwan residents coming to the mainland. However, the DPP authorities still refuse to lift the ban prohibiting travel agencies on the island from operating group tours to the mainland. If cross-strait tourism is at an impasse, the crux and obstacle is the DPP authorities.\nRealizing the normalization and regularization of cross-strait exchanges, including tourism, is the common wish of compatriots on both sides and is in their common interest. We hope compatriots on both sides will work together to return cross-strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development as soon as possible, realize the healthy development of cross-strait tourism and two-way exchanges at an early date, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The “2023 Cross-Strait Peace Survey” by Taiwan's Global Views magazine shows that 74.4% of respondents believe that interaction across the Taiwan Strait should be increased. On how to maintain cross-Strait peace, the option most chosen by respondents was “voting to elect leaders who can handle cross-Strait relations and ensure peace.” What comment do you have?","We have noted the relevant public opinion polls. Peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. At present, cross-strait relations are at an important juncture, and Taiwan is facing a critical choice between two paths and two prospects: peace versus war, and prosperity versus decline. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, starting from safeguarding their own security and well-being, will firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” and make a rational choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Lai Qingde recently said that accepting the “1992 Consensus” is equivalent to giving up Taiwan's “sovereignty,” and that Taiwan must improve its defense capabilities to safeguard Taiwan's “sovereignty.” He also said that the cross-Strait issue is not a continuation of the Kuomintang–Communist Party civil war, but an “international issue,” and that if the mainland is willing to treat Taiwan equally and with…","Lai Ching-te is pursuing “Taiwan independence” while flying the banner of peace, which is the height of villainy. “Taiwan independence” means war; how could it bring peace! The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and is by no means an “international issue.”\nThe “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for cross-strait dialogue and negotiation. Lai Ching-te, on the one hand attempting to “seek independence through armed force” and “seek independence by relying on outside forces,” and on the other hand glibly talking about cross-strait dialogue and cooperation, is engaged in outright charlatanism. As commentators on the island have pointed out, Lai Ching-te is changing from a “Taiwan independence madman” into a “Taiwan independence swindler.” This comment hits the nail on the head and is fitting. We believe compatriots in Taiwan have a clear understanding of this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576965.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The third Belt and Road International Cooperation Summit Forum was held in Beijing, attracting wide attention from public opinion on the island. Some voices have called for both sides across the Strait to jointly promote economic and trade cooperation under the Belt and Road. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Since General Secretary Xi Jinping proposed the Belt and Road Initiative for jointly building the “Belt and Road” ten years ago, we have taken cross-Strait integrated development as the focus. We have thoroughly implemented the overall strategy of the Party for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech on “promoting integration through connectivity, promoting integration through benefits, and promoting integration through sentiment,” and have actively encouraged and supported Taiwan businesses and enterprises in key regions along the routes to participate in the construction of the Belt and Road.\nFirst, together with the National Development and Reform Commission and other departments and Fujian Province, we promoted the issuance of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,” providing policy and mechanism guarantees for Taiwan businesses and enterprises in Fujian to participate in the construction of the Belt and Road.\nSecond, we built platforms for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to participate in jointly building the Belt and Road. We guided Taiwan businesses and enterprises to actively participate in the concentrated development of cross-Strait industrial cooperation zones in Sichuan, Chongqing, Hunan, Hubei, Guangxi, Jiangxi, and other places, and encouraged them to conduct trade with Belt and Road co-building countries or regions through China-Europe Railway Express trains. We supported Taiwan businesses and enterprises in developing in cooperation parks that the Mainland has established in Belt and Road co-building countries or regions, and cross-Strait enterprises' cooperation in participating in infrastructure projects such as coal-fired power plants and combined-cycle power stations has made some progress. For example, from April 2018 to the end of September 2023, the Shaanxi Xianyang plant of Taiwan enterprise TPV Technology (冠捷科技) shipped a total of 5,168 containers via China-Europe Railway Express trains, with a total cargo value of about 716 million US dollars. Chongqing, through expanding international logistics channels such as the China-Europe Railway Express, the New International Land-Sea Trade Corridor, and the Yangtze River Golden Waterway, has helped the development of the Taiwan-invested electronics and information industry; in 2022, Chongqing's electronics and information industry import and export reached 4,951.2 billion yuan.\nThird, we strengthened publicity on Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots' participation in jointly building the Belt and Road. Since the beginning of this year, we have guided Jiangsu, Fujian, Zhejiang, Chongqing, Shaanxi, Qinghai, and other provinces and municipalities to receive multiple delegations of Taiwan industrial and commercial circles, fully publicizing the functional positioning, industrial characteristics, and cooperation advantages of major national strategies such as the Belt and Road co-building, and releasing positive signals of sharing high-quality development opportunities with Taiwan businesses and enterprises.\nNext, we will continue to work hard to build more platforms and provide more conveniences for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to participate in jointly building the Belt and Road and share development opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576966.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Before Taiwan's 2019 elections, Xiang Xin, chairman of China Innovation Investment Ltd. in Hong Kong, and his wife were baselessly accused by the DPP authorities of crimes such as “espionage” and “money laundering,” and their departure from the island was restricted. Recently, they were confirmed to be not guilty. After being trapped for 1,420 days, Xiang Xin and his wife finally returned to Hong Kong. What…","For a long time, the DPP authorities, in pursuit of political private gain, have deliberately fabricated charges and manufactured cases, vigorously carried out “green terror,” and staged one clumsy political farce after another, misleading and deceiving the public. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will open their eyes wide and stay highly alert to the DPP authorities repeating old tricks with new variations, and not be deceived by their “dirty tricks” and schemes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan's economic authorities recently said that in 2022 Taiwan exported US$185.9 billion worth of goods to the mainland, nearly half of which were integrated circuits. In recent years, the share of ECFA Early Harvest List products in Taiwan's exports has gradually declined, and the efforts of Taiwanese businesses to expand global markets and diversify risks have been clearly effective. What is your comment?","The mainland's economy has strong resilience, great potential, and ample vitality. In the first three quarters of this year, economic growth reached 5.2%, with continued recovery and improvement, steady growth in production and supply, continuous expansion of market demand, and steady improvement in development quality. From January to September, cross-Strait trade totaled US$195.06 billion, maintaining high-level operation. Cross-Strait economic and trade relations have strong endogenous momentum and enormous room to expand into broader fields and rise to higher levels, and we are very confident about this.\nIt must be pointed out that since the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) took effect, it has brought tangible benefits to both sides of the Strait, especially to Taiwan's related enterprises and people. Cross-Strait trade grew from US$145.37 billion in 2010 to US$319.68 billion in 2022, doubling. As of the end of June this year, in the area of trade in goods, the tariff preferences ECFA gave Taiwan reached as much as US$8.8 billion. ECFA has not only promoted the growth of cross-Strait trade, but has also steadily increased the market share of Taiwan products in the mainland market, deepened cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, and enhanced the international competitiveness of Taiwan enterprises.\nThe facts fully show that ECFA is a good agreement that benefits Taiwan compatriots. If the DPP authorities truly believed ECFA had little use, why have they repeatedly expressed the hope that the mainland will not abolish ECFA?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202310/t20231025_12576962.htm"],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Regarding the U.S. semiconductor equipment export control exemption, TSMC responded that the company has been permitted to continue operating its factory in Nanjing and is applying for an indefinite exemption for operations on the mainland. What is your comment on this?","Cross-Strait industrial cooperation is conducive to the development of enterprises on both sides and to improving the livelihoods and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and outsiders have no right to meddle. We will continue to improve policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises, continuously promote Taiwan enterprises’ equal enjoyment of mainland industrial promotion policies and development dividends, help Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern, and achieve high-quality development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The US Department of Defense released the so-called “2023 Report on Military and Security Developments Involving the People’s Republic of China,” which lists six scenarios that could lead the mainland to take military action against Taiwan. In response, some netizens on the island criticized that if the United States were not stirring things up, the Taiwan Strait would be very peaceful and stable. What is the…","The so-called “China Military Power Report” released by the United States is full of erroneous content, including its statements and arguments on the Taiwan question. It must be emphasized that Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and brooks no foreign interference. The root cause of tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait is “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference. As long as the DPP keeps seeking “independence” and provoking by colluding with external forces, the Taiwan Strait will not know peace.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Recently, the dance moves to the viral Douyin song from the Guangxi “Subject Three” driving test suddenly became a sensation online, and many young people in Taiwan have posted dance videos on social media platforms. What is your comment?","I have heard that among the top 10 most-requested songs on Taiwan's KTV charts, half are mainland songs, many of them internet-celebrity songs. It is indeed now often seen that a song, a dance move, or a food can quickly become a craze across both sides of the Strait through social media platforms, such as \"Lonely Warrior\" (《孤勇者》), \"Little Garden\" (《小小花园》), \"Begging Buddha\" (《求佛》), and Luosifen (螺蛳粉) that we have seen before. This is a unique way for young people across the Strait to exchange in the internet age, and it is also a new cultural exchange phenomenon in the process of integrated development across the Strait.\nThanks to the development of online social platforms, compatriots on both sides of the Strait can communicate more quickly and conveniently, and exchange more widely and diversely. People will find that compatriots on both sides are equally bold in daring to dream and striving, equally pursuing goals and holding dreams, and will find that compatriots on both sides share the cultural genes common to the Chinese people, and can fully reach historical consensus and cultural consensus through exchange. This emotional resonance and cultural consensus is a powerful endogenous driving force for promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We hope that more Taiwan compatriots will take part in such exchanges and jointly promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","凤凰卫视记者","First question: According to reports, mainland tax and natural resources authorities have launched an investigation into the tax and land use situation of some enterprises under the Taiwan company Foxconn. What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: Regarding the remarks Ma Ying-jeou recently made at a US think tank forum that touched on cross-Strait relations, Taiwan’s external affairs authorities…","On the first question: the relevant mainland authorities conducting compliance investigations into all enterprises equally, in accordance with law and regulations, is normal law enforcement.\nIt should be emphasized that our policy stance and our goodwill and sincerity in respecting, caring for, and benefiting Taiwan compatriots will not change. We will, as always, support Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises in investing and operating on the mainland, create a favorable development environment, continue to improve and implement policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, and provide opportunities and room for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to develop better and faster on the mainland.\nWhile Taiwan-invested enterprises share in growth dividends and achieve substantial development on the mainland, they should also bear corresponding social responsibilities and play a positive role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn the second question: the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community, and it is widely understood and supported by the international community. The DPP authorities must have a profound understanding of this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Reuters, citing sources, reported that US President Joe Biden may consider asking Congress to pass a supplemental appropriations act of about $100 billion, which would include so-called military assistance for Israel, Ukraine, and the Taiwan region. What comments do you have on this?","The U.S.’s relevant actions are not putting out a fire but pouring oil on it. The facts fully show that wherever the U.S. stokes the flames, the people there fall into war. We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the U.S. and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose the U.S. providing weapons to the Taiwan region of China in any way. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and attempt to “seek independence by force,” which will only turn Taiwan into a “powder keg,” intensify the peril of war across the Taiwan Strait, and push Taiwan compatriots into danger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently called again in the United States for the US and the international community to promote cross-Strait peace talks, saying that Taiwan’s people all want peace and that next year’s election of Taiwan’s leader will be a choice between peace and war. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","Taiwan is currently facing a choice between two paths and two prospects: peace versus war, and prosperity versus decline. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize where their interests lie, distinguish right from wrong, and firmly stand on the right side of history. They should resolutely oppose the separatism of “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference, and join hands with compatriots on the mainland to jointly steer cross-strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development and share the dividends of peaceful development in cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Taitung County Magistrate Rao Ching-ling recently led a delegation to visit Beijing and said she hopes to promote the resumption of sales of Taitung sugar apples to the mainland in December. Could you explain the current progress?","As long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and “Taiwan independence” is opposed, the two sides of the Strait are one family. Matters within one family are easy to discuss and resolve. Since this year, the Kuomintang, Taitung County and other parties have expressed the hope that the mainland side will resume importing custard apples from Taiwan. We attach great importance to this and have studied it carefully. On the basis of a comprehensive assessment, the competent authorities have announced the resumption of imports of custard apples from Taiwan into the mainland, which has brought benefits to grassroots Taiwan residents and generated positive responses. We are willing to communicate in depth with the Kuomintang, Taitung County and other parties on promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, expanding imports of custard apples from Taiwan, and make appropriate arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","日本广播协会记者","The mainland decided to resume imports of Taiwan sugar apples starting June 20, but only from packing plants and orchards that have obtained registration. Has this rule changed?","The relevant requirements of the General Administration of Customs and other departments are very clear. As I mentioned just now, we are willing to communicate in depth with the Chinese Kuomintang, Taitung County, and other parties on promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and on expanding imports of sugar apples (custard apples) from the Taiwan region. We will try to have relevant businesses meet the standards required by the relevant mainland departments after rectification, so that mainland residents can taste high-quality fruit from the Taiwan region.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202310/t20231025_12576959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-10-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that in its latest “China Military Power Report,” the US Department of Defense lists six so-called scenarios that might prompt mainland China to take military action against Taiwan, such as Taiwan formally declaring independence. What is the spokesperson's response?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest efforts. At the same time, we do not promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is directed at external interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. It is by no means directed at Taiwan compatriots. If the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces or external interfering forces provoke us, or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.\nAt present, some forces in the United States are scheming to “use Taiwan to contain China,” painstakingly playing the “Taiwan card” and inciting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to take reckless provocations. This damages China's sovereignty and security interests, endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and affects the healthy and stable development of China-U.S. relations. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle, stop saying one thing and doing another, and fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16262430.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-10-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have three questions. First, a report from the Budget Center of Taiwan's Legislative Yuan points out that the Taiwan military plans to procure five models of military-grade commercial drones next year, with a total requirement of 3,221 units and a total cost of over NT$5.68798 billion. It also plans to procure 26 drone countermeasure systems. What is your comment? Second, the head of Taiwan's external exchange…","On the first question: The Democratic Progressive Party authorities disregard the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, recklessly squander taxpayers' hard-earned money, and spend huge sums buying weapons at high prices to embolden their pursuit of \"independence,\" accelerating the push of Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and peril. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: \"Resisting reunification by force\" is a dead end, and \"relying on the United States to seek independence\" will inevitably fail. The Chinese People's Liberation Army continues to strengthen its training and combat readiness, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguards peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn the second question: I noted that in your question you already mentioned that the head of the Philippine defense department spoke of the possibility as being zero. I think this already makes the point. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. We firmly oppose any country conducting any form of official exchange or military contact with the Taiwan region of China, and this position is consistent and clear. China's resolve to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering.\nOn the third question: We often say that national defense is like sunlight and air: we benefit from it without noticing, but without it, survival is difficult. National defense is not the business of the military alone; it is the business of all Chinese people. The defense of tomorrow relies on young people, and students at universities across the country, including Tsinghua University, have a longstanding and glorious tradition of serving the country. Inviting you students to observe the Ministry of National Defense press conference is intended to help you feel, understand, care about, and love national defense. Today you are our guests; tomorrow, I hope you will become our comrades-in-arms.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16262430.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-10-26","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the U.S. government plans to request large-scale military assistance for Taiwan from Congress, and the DPP authorities recently used reserve funds to support joint training with the United States. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","For some time, the situation in the Taiwan Strait has been complex and grave. The root cause lies in the DPP authorities “relying on foreign backing to bolster themselves” and “relying on the US to seek independence,” and in the US playing the “Taiwan card,” attempting to “use Taiwan to contain China.” Whether it is military aid funds or reserve funds, they are playing with fire with the hard-earned money of the people, and will only push Taiwan into a grave and perilous state of war. On the issue of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the will of the Chinese People's Liberation Army is as firm as a rock, and its capabilities are growing stronger by the day.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16262430.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-10-30","Wang Wenbin","AFP","China’s Foreign Minister Wang Yi recently said that the preparation work for the meeting between President Xi Jinping and President Biden cannot be left to autopilot. What conditions need to be met to confirm the meeting?","Thank you for raising that question. To answer your question, let me briefly go over the visit to the US by Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi at US invitation. During the visit, Wang Yi met with US President Joe Biden and National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan respectively and held two rounds of talks with US Secretary of State Antony Blinken. Wang Yi also met with representatives of the US strategic and business communities.\nWang Yi said that the purpose of this visit is to communicate with the US to follow through on the important common understandings between the two heads of state. Noting the Bali meeting and the upcoming meeting in San Francisco, Wang Yi said the two sides should work to stabilize the China-US relationship from further deterioration, and bring it back to the track of sound and stable development at an early date. Wang Yi said that the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, the most important political foundation of the bilateral relationship, must be earnestly maintained with efforts to steer clear of disruptions. China attaches importance to the US side’s desire to stabilize and improve its relations with China. Wang Yi stressed the need to take on the responsibilities to the world, history and people to truly stabilize and improve China-US relations in line with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence, and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping. This not only serves the fundamental interests of both countries and their peoples, but also meets the common expectations of the international community.\nWang Yi said, looking back at the twits and turns in the course of China-US relations since the beginning of this year, the experience is worth summarizing and the lessons need to be drawn. The key is to follow the “five musts”. The two sides must follow the common understandings reached by the two heads of state; must stabilize bilateral relations; must keep communication channels open; must properly manage differences, disputes and frictions; and must promote mutually beneficial cooperation. Wang Yi stressed, to stabilize and improve China-US relations, the two sides should also have objective understandings of each other’s strategic intentions, correctly view the competitive factors in the exchanges between China and the US, and define the concept of national security.\nWang Yi stressed that the biggest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is “Taiwan independence”, which is also the biggest challenge facing China-US relations. Wang Yi said it must be resolutely opposed and such efforts must be reflected in specific policies and actions. Wang Yi also elaborated on China’s solemn position on the South China Sea issue. The two sides also had an exchange of views on the Palestinian-Israeli conflict, Ukraine and the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue, among others.\nThe US side noted that the US government values its relations with China. The US and China have maintained exchanges and interactions in recent months, and conducted candid and constructive communication, achieving positive results. The US side hopes that bilateral relations will be stable and sustainable, and is willing to strengthen communication with China to prevent miscalculation, explore cooperation in areas where cooperation is needed, make good preparations for the next phase of high-level exchanges between the US and China, and jointly address global challenges.\nDuring the visit, the two sides, in the spirit of equality and mutual respect, held in-depth, constructive and substantive strategic communication over various issues of mutual interest and jointly sent out a positive signal of stabilizing and improving China-US relations. Both agree that it is useful and necessary for our two major countries to keep up dialogue. Both hope to see the bilateral relationship stabilizing as soon as possible and moving towards improvement. The two sides agreed to work together for the meeting between the two heads of state in San Francisco. As for your question, I want to stress that it won’t be plain sailing to San Francisco, nor can we leave it to autopilot to get us there. Both sides need to earnestly return to what was agreed in Bali, act on the common understandings of the two Presidents, rise above disruptions, overcome obstacles, expand common understandings and accumulate outcomes.\nIn the coming days, the two sides will hold separately China-US consultations on maritime affairs, China-US consultations on arms control and non-proliferation, China-US consultations on foreign policies, and China-US Coordination Meeting on Disability Affairs and discuss the signing of a memorandum of understanding on cooperation in disability affairs. The two sides agreed to further increase direct passenger flights.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347624.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202310/t20231030_11170661.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-08","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","The Chinese Ambassador to Estonia told a member of the Estonian parliament that the ambassador may leave the country if Taiwan opens a representative office there. Can you confirm those comments that were told to the media by the Estonian parliamentarian? Do you have anything more to add to that?","There is only one China in the world. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We firmly oppose any form of official interaction between the Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China and oppose any action supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We call on Estonia to stay committed to its solemn commitment of adhering to the one-China principle, not to allow Taiwan to set up any organization of official nature, and earnestly safeguard the political foundation of its relations with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347631.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231108_11176036.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-11-08","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on November 8 that the 2023 Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will be held in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province, from November 14 to 15. At present, both sides of the Summit are carrying out preparations in an orderly manner.\nThis year’s annual meeting will center on the theme of “Integrated Development and High-Quality Development in the New Pattern.” It will explore in depth how cross-Strait entrepreneurs can seize the opportunities of the new development pattern, promote Taiwanese enterprises’ integration into the mainland’s domestic market, and deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. Approximately 800 people, including council members and members from both sides of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, cross-Strait entrepreneurs, and relevant experts and scholars, will participate in the annual meeting’s activities. This fully demonstrates the strong desire of the cross-Strait business community to strengthen exchanges and cooperation and to promote peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nIn the 10 years since its founding, the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit has held 10 annual meetings and has carried out activities in various forms, continuously promoting dialogue and close connections among the cross-Strait business community. It has played an important role in promoting economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231108_12580210.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-09","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","From November 11 to 12, 2023, the first Straits Port Cities Forum across the Taiwan Strait will be held in Shenzhen, establishing a new platform for urban exchanges across the Strait. Its purpose is to give full play to the characteristics and advantages of port cities on both sides of the Strait, promote exchanges and cooperation among cities, and foster the development of port cities. The inaugural forum is jointly initiated by Shenzhen City and Keelung City, with the theme “Port Cities Integrating, Working Together for Win-Win Results.” More than 160 people have been invited to attend, including government officials, business and industry representatives, and scholars from Taoyuan City, Hualien County, as well as Shantou City, Chaozhou City, Jieyang City, and Shanwei City. Centered on the topics of “port cities,” “maritime transport,” “marine education,” and “marine industry,” attending representatives will share experiences, exchange ideas and lessons, build consensus, deepen cooperation, and achieve mutual benefit and win-win results. We believe that the forum will further expand the scale of exchanges among port cities on both sides of the Strait, deepen exchanges and cooperation, jointly improve construction and development, and enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231109_12580460.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-11-10","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","On November 8, the G7 released a statement recognizing the importance of engaging candidly and expressing concerns directly to China. Do you have any comment?","The G7 foreign ministers said in the statement that they stand prepared to build constructive and stable relations with China and do not seek to thwart China’s economic progress and development. We hope they will reflect this in concrete actions and work in earnest with China for the sound growth of bilateral ties on the basis of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit.\nWe reject the G7’s unfounded allegations of China distorting the global economy and engaging in economic coercion. It is not China, but G7 members that have placed over 10,000 entities and individuals around the world on sanctions lists, abused state power to go all out after particular companies, politicized and weaponized economic and trade issues, and destabilized the international industrial and supply chains. The G7 needs to look within itself and reflect on its own behavior.\nWe firmly oppose the G7’s wrong actions that harm China’s sovereignty and interfere in China’s internal affairs.\nThe South China Sea arbitration case initiated by the Philippines concerns essentially territorial sovereignty and maritime delimitation, which is not subject to UNCLOS. The award is illegal, null and void, and completely invalid. The G7’s endorsement of the award and the antagonism and confrontation it could cause runs counter to regional countries’ desire for a peaceful and stable region.\nThe key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait lies in the one-China principle. The biggest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities’ refusal to change their “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and the external connivance and support they have received. The G7 countries all made a commitment to one-China and should therefore honor that commitment and fully put that into practice.\nIssues relating to Xinjiang, Xizang and Hong Kong are all China’s internal affairs that brook no external interference. The world knows what exactly the state of democracy and human rights looks like in each country, and the people of each country have the best say in that. We urge the G7 to abide by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and the basic norms of international relations. The G7 needs to look after its own affairs and stop interfering in other countries’ internal affairs under various pretexts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347633.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231110_11178377.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-13","Mao Ning","People’s Daily","China and the US have both announced an upcoming meeting between the two Presidents. Senior officials of the White House National Security Council said on the condition of anonymity on November 10 that through the meeting the US is looking toward “managing the competition, preventing the downside risk of conflict and ensuring channels of communication are open.” They also said that, “We know efforts to shape or…","China has announced President Xi Jinping’s trip to the US for a summit meeting at the US invitation. The two Presidents will have in-depth communication on issues of strategic, overarching and fundamental importance in shaping China-U.S. relations and major issues concerning world peace and development.\nChina views and handles its relations with the US in accordance with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping. Major-country competition runs counter to the trend of our times and provides no answer to the problems in the US or the challenges in our world. China does not fear competition, but we do not agree that China-US relations should be defined by competition. Speaking of concerns, the US needs to respect China’s concerns and legitimate right to development, rather than emphasizing its own concerns at the expense of China’s interests. To seek to remodel other countries in one’s own image is wishful thinking in the first place and typical hegemonism which is going nowhere. China doesn’t seek to change the US, nor should the US seek to shape or change China. We hope the US will act on its commitment of not seeking a new Cold War with China and having no intention to seek a conflict with China, and work with China to bring bilateral relations back to the track of sound and stable development.\nThe status quo in the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China. It is the DPP authorities and the external forces supporting and conniving at their separatist agenda that are changing the status quo. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and resolving it is a matter for the Chinese that brook no foreign interference. Successive US administrations have made clear commitments on the Taiwan question. During the summit meeting in Bali, the US said explicitly that the US government doesn’t support “Taiwan independence”. The US needs to honor its commitment to one China and oppose “Taiwan independence” with concrete actions.\nChina has made clear on multiple occasions the nature of the South China Sea issue and what our principled position is. China will neither take any inch of territory that is not ours, nor give up any inch of territory that belongs to us. China is committed to settling relevant disputes through negotiation and consultation with relevant countries and will not waver in our determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US needs to stop creating pretexts and interfering in the disputes between China and relevant countries over territorial and maritime rights and interests, still less contain and encircle China by exploiting those issues.\nThe ongoing Palestinian-Israeli conflict continues to grip the world’s attention. China stands on the side of equity and justice. We have been in close contact with relevant parties and committed to deescalation and protection of civilians. We hope that the US will follow an objective and just stance and play a constructive role in halting the conflict.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347634.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231113_11179210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-16","Mao Ning","Anadolu Agency","After talks in San Francisco, China and the US announced reestablishing military-to-military mechanisms which were canceled after Pelosi’s visit last year to Taiwan. I want to ask about what enabled this decision? Has China got any assurances about the Taiwan policy?","China has always attached importance to China-US military-to-military exchanges. In San Francisco, the two leaders agreed to promote and strengthen dialogue and cooperation between the two countries in various areas, including the resumption of high-level military-to-military communication, the China-US Defense Policy Coordination Talks, and the China-US Military Maritime Consultative Agreement meetings, and conducting telephone conversations between theater commanders on the basis of equality and respect.\nRegarding the Taiwan question, President Xi Jinping also set forth China’s solemn position. The Taiwan question has always been the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. The US side should follow through on its statement of “not supporting Taiwan independence”, stop arming Taiwan, and support China’s peaceful reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347637.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231116_11181657.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-11-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Japanese Ministry of Defense said that multiple Chinese Navy vessels, including the Shandong carrier, are sailing and conducting training in the Pacific Ocean, with large numbers of carrier-based fighter jets and helicopters taking off and landing frequently. Separately, Taiwan's defense authorities said that the Shandong recently transited the Taiwan Strait. Some analysts believe this is the first time the…","Recently, the PLA Navy organized the Shandong carrier formation to conduct training in relevant waters, aimed at honing the systematic combat capability of the carrier formation, improving the skills and tactics of officers and soldiers, and further enhancing the ability to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests. It should be pointed out that this is a routine arrangement made according to the annual training plan, in line with international law and international practice. The Chinese military will regularly organize similar exercises and drills.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16267213.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2023-11-17","Mao Ning","TASS","US National Security Council Coordinator for Strategic Communications John Kirby said at an online press conference that US President Biden made it clear that the US hopes to continue to provide self-defense capabilities to Taiwan. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","The Taiwan question remains the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. The US needs to deliver on its pledge of not supporting “Taiwan independence” with concrete actions, stop arming Taiwan, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and support China’s peaceful reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347638.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231117_11182492.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-17","Mao Ning","NHK","During the China-Japan summit talks today, Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida said that peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is very important to the international community, including Japan. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference. The most fundamental way to safeguard cross-Strait peace and stability is to uphold the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347638.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231117_11182492.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Yesterday (November 14), the 10th anniversary annual meeting of the 2023 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit opened in Nanjing. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On November 14, the 10th anniversary annual meeting of the 2023 Cross-Strait CEO Summit opened in Nanjing. This year marks the 10th anniversary of the Cross-Strait CEO Summit, and General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter to the annual meeting for the first time. The letter fully affirmed the important role the summit has played in promoting cross-strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-strait integrated development. It declared the continued commitment to promoting economic exchange and cooperation across the Strait, deepening integrated development in all fields across the Strait, improving systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, helping Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development, and it expressed high hopes that the summit would broadly unite business circles on both sides of the Strait and make new contributions to strengthening the economy of the Chinese nation, enhancing the well-being of compatriots, and advancing the cause of national reunification.\nWang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the opening ceremony of the annual meeting, read out General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory letter, and delivered a speech. Wang Huning said that the historic achievements in economic and social development on the mainland since the 18th National Congress of the CPC have created more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies to develop on the mainland. The mainland was in the past, is now, and will be in the future the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies to invest and start businesses. He hoped that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies would stay confident, seize the moment and the momentum, develop better and gain more in the process of comprehensively advancing Chinese-style modernization on the mainland, and contribute further to strengthening the economy of the Chinese nation. He hoped that compatriots on both sides of the Strait would get closer to each other, expand exchange and cooperation, deepen integrated development, promote understanding and integration through exchange, and continuously open up new prospects for cross-strait integrated development.\nThe theme of this annual meeting was “Integrated Development and High-Quality Development in the New Pattern,” and more than 800 members of both sides of the summit, cross-strait entrepreneurs, and scholars and experts attended the various activities of the annual meeting. The eight industry cooperation promotion groups conducted in-depth discussions around the theme of the annual meeting on issues such as how cross-strait enterprises and industries can grasp the new development pattern, promote the integration of Taiwan companies into the mainland's domestic market, and deepen the integrated development of industrial and supply chains. The theme of this annual meeting was clear and its content rich; guests enthusiastically participated, and the atmosphere of exchange was lively, fully demonstrating the strong desire of business circles on both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchange and cooperation and to promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations. We will implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory letter, support the summit in uniting cross-strait entrepreneurs, work together to advance peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations, and make new contributions to creating a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582193.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","On September 27, a special meeting was held in Fuzhou on the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.” What progress have localities and departments made in implementing these opinions?","After the release of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,” relevant departments took the initiative, put forward innovative measures, and strengthened policy support. Fujian Province strengthened its主体 responsibility, established a coordinated implementation mechanism, innovated working methods, and jointly promoted the implementation of the tasks and measures set out in the “Opinions.”\nRecently, the National Immigration Administration issued ten entry and exit policy measures supporting Fujian in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, effective from January 1, 2024, to further promote personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan, facilitate Taiwan compatriots' residence and daily life in Fujian, and deepen integrated development across all areas of cross-strait relations. Relevant departments are also studying policy measures to implement the “Opinions” and will introduce specific measures as soon as possible.\nFujian Province attaches great importance to implementing the “Opinions” and is currently working to formulate the first batch of policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, so that Taiwan compatriots can share in the benefits of building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. It is understood that Fujian Province plans to introduce a batch of policy measures in areas including facilitating the travel and daily life of Taiwan compatriots, deepening Fujian-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation, encouraging Taiwan compatriots to find employment and start businesses, and advancing rule of law related to Taiwan affairs. It will place particular emphasis on further providing convenience for Taiwan compatriots in obtaining entry and exit documents for their first homeland on the mainland, offering assistance for seeking relatives and paying respects to ancestors, and formulating detailed measures on allowing applications for “Fujian Time-Honored Brands,” expanding direct recognition of professional skill qualifications, and strengthening the protection of cultural relics related to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582192.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","We have noted that Guangdong, Sichuan and Jiangxi provinces have recently held rich and colorful cross-Strait cultural exchange activities. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","From late October to late November, the Straits Exchange Center and the Taiwan Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Foundation jointly hosted the Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month in Shenzhen, Guangdong. Themed “Integrating Across the Strait, Creating the Future Together,” the event focused on tapping into the shared cultural memories across the Taiwan Strait, targeted the employment and entrepreneurship development needs of Taiwan youth, promoted Shenzhen-Taiwan exchanges and cooperation as well as the integrated economic, social and cultural development of Guangdong and Taiwan, and strengthened the friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The event was divided into six sections: “Youth Integration,” “Grassroots Integration,” “Economic Integration,” “Cultural Integration,” “Sports Integration,” and “Media Integration,” and included more than 30 series of exchange activities, such as the grand final of the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League, the awards ceremony of the Cross-Strait and Hong Kong and Macao Drone Aerial Photography Creative Competition, the grand final of the esports league, sailing races, cycling races, the Taiwan Creative Lifestyle Festival, the Taiwan Campus Faculty and Student Carnival, the Taiwan Youth Maker Forum, the Taiwan Businesspeople Lecture Hall, legal knowledge lectures, cross-strait youth friendship gatherings, folk cultural exchanges among grassroots residents on both sides, and Taiwan specialty agricultural product fairs. More than 2,000 youth from the island, representatives of temple heads, business and industry circles, and media circles were invited, and more than 10,000 Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan youth in Shenzhen participated. It was the largest cross-strait exchange event held on the mainland before the end of the year.\nOn November 7 to 9, the 32nd World Hakka Conference was held in Longnan, Ganzhou, Jiangxi. Some 2,500 guests, including representatives of more than 200 Hakka associations (overseas Chinese groups) and Hakka individuals from around the world, as well as well-known entrepreneurs, attended the event, among them about 300 Taiwan compatriots from 11 Hakka associations on the island. During the conference, a series of activities was held, including an academic exchange on Hakka culture, the Hakka Youth Development Conference, and the first Hakka Folk Culture and Arts Festival, which deepened the feelings between Hakka kinsmen on both sides of the Strait and promoted exchange and cooperation in Hakka culture across the Strait.\nOn November 7, the 7th Cross-Strait Nezha Folk Culture Exchange was held in Jiangyou, Mianyang, Sichuan. More than 200 people attended, including representatives and believers from Nezha temples in Taiwan, Hong Kong, Macao and across the Strait, scholars and experts on Nezha folk culture, and figures from Taoist, business and other circles. Themed “Seeking the Roots of the Nezha Ancestral Shrine, Forging Cultural Bonds Across the Strait,” the event relied on cultural resources such as Li Bai's hometown in Jiangyou and the Nezha Ancestral Shrine to build a platform for economic, trade and cultural exchange and cooperation through folk culture activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Taiwan’s transportation authorities recently announced that they expect to open group tours from Taiwan to the mainland in March 2024. Zhan Zhihong (詹志宏), deputy head of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, subsequently denied this, saying it has not been determined that it will definitely open next year and that this is only a planning direction. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","The DPP authorities have prohibited travel agencies on the island from operating group tours to the mainland for more than three and a half years. In late August this year, the Mainland Affairs Council issued a so-called “plan” that claimed it would resume the operation of group tours to the mainland by Taiwan travel agencies, and said the tourism industry needed a one-month preparation period. More than two months have now passed, and the DPP authorities still have not lifted the ban. Some may say that the Mainland Affairs Council said the opening would be conditional. Then may we ask, have the so-called conditions changed? If they have not changed, why now say that opening could happen by March next year at the latest? If it can be opened, why must the island's tourism operators wait another five months? This shows that, whether it concerns the so-called “conditions” or the timing of opening, the DPP authorities are always engaged in political calculation and always disregard the voices and interests of the tourism industry and the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said in an interview that if he is elected, the probability of war between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait would be the lowest, because he is the most capable of safeguarding Taiwan's security. Cross-Strait experts and scholars have pointed out that Lai's statement is illogical and absurd, and that its purpose is to confuse public perception and deceive votes. What comment does the…","\"Taiwan independence\" means war. When a \"Taiwan independence worker\" says such things, can anyone believe them? \"Taiwan independence workers\" are war makers. Telling such lies that they themselves do not believe is typical of a scoundrel.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582189.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》栏目记者","The China International Import Expo was recently successfully held in Shanghai. What opportunities did the expo bring to Taiwan-invested enterprises? Please answer.","Since the first China International Import Expo (CIIE) was held in 2018, it has been held six times, and it is an important platform for buying from the world, selling to the world, and benefiting the world. We have actively responded to the demands of industrial and commercial circles on the island and provided assistance and convenience for their participation in exhibitions. Taiwan enterprises participating in this CIIE include both enterprises that have exhibited continuously and new exhibitors. The exhibition area is nearly 1,800 square meters, covering a wide range of fields, with a high degree of scale and good product quality. Taiwanese businesses participating in the exhibition said that industry circles on the island are very optimistic about the huge potential of the mainland’s domestic demand market, and hope to showcase their products, expand brand influence, and gain more business opportunities through platforms such as the CIIE, in order to achieve better development for their enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","It is understood that the 2023 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo · Cross-Strait Flower Expo will be held in Xiamen, Fujian. Please introduce the relevant preparations.","From November 30 to December 2, 2023, the 2023 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo · Cross-Strait Flower Expo will be held in Xiamen, Fujian Province, with the flower exhibition area located at the Southeast Flower Capital Flower Expo Park in Zhangzhou, Fujian. The expo is co-hosted by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the China Council for the Promotion of International Trade, and the China National Food Industry Association. Its purpose is to comprehensively showcase the achievements of cross-Strait agricultural and rural exchanges and cooperation, deeply exchange experiences in jointly advancing rural revitalization, promote and introduce high-quality characteristic agricultural products from both sides of the Strait, and expand channels of civil communication and dialogue across the Strait.\nThe expo takes “Agricultural Conditions Across the Strait, Integrated Development” as its theme and will invite more than 10,000 participants from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, including agriculture-related enterprises, social organizations, experts, and scholars. Activities during the period will include the Cross-Strait Agricultural Integrated Development Forum, a supply-demand matchmaking meeting for high-quality characteristic agricultural products, a Cross-Strait Farmers' Harvest Celebration and “Cross-Strait Flavors” Market, and a Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Meeting titled “Rural Creation and Construction, I Am Responsible for Revitalization.” We warmly welcome Taiwanese industry professionals and farmers to participate actively, and we welcome cross-Strait media reporters to pay attention to and cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the so-called “representative to the United States” of Taiwan, Hsiao Bi-khim, will return to Taiwan and serve as Lai Ching-te’s deputy. What comments do you have?","If the rumors are true and these two individuals form a “double-independence combination,” piling “independence” on top of “independence,” then I believe every Taiwan compatriot understands very clearly what this means for the situation in the Taiwan Strait, what it means for the lives and property of ordinary Taiwan people, and what it means for Taiwan’s future and destiny.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, news that the Chinese Department of Shih Hsin University in Taiwan plans to stop enrollment has drawn social attention. In addition, the DPP authorities have also significantly reduced the proportion of classical Chinese in textbooks, which has provoked wide criticism. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The DPP authorities have long promoted “de-Sinicization” education on the island, causing many harmful consequences. If the Department of Chinese at Shih Hsin University were to stop enrolling students, it would be another bad example of the DPP’s “de-Sinicization.” This would seriously affect young students’ studies and future development, with far-reaching harm.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Starting October 29, the direct passenger route from Wuhan to Kaohsiung officially resumed. Please spokesperson introduce the situation since the resumption of cross-Strait direct routes.","Recently, passenger flow on cross-strait routes has steadily increased. In the most recent week (November 5 to November 11), 14 cities, including Beijing, Shanghai, Xiamen, Chengdu, Shenzhen, Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Nanjing, Chongqing, Fuzhou, Qingdao, Wuhan, Ningbo, and Zhengzhou, operated a total of 580 passenger flights on cross-strait routes, carrying 84,528 passenger trips. It must be pointed out that although cross-strait flights and passenger volume have grown compared with the pandemic period, because the number of destinations is very limited, overall travel between the two sides remains quite inconvenient. Fully resuming cross-strait direct flight routes is conducive to people-to-people movement and promoting exchange. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion and, as soon as possible, fully restore cross-strait direct air links, direct sea links, and the “mini three links.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Cai Yingwen recently said that the top priority for Taiwan in safeguarding freedom and democracy is to strengthen its “self-defense capability.” The island's 2024 defense budget increased by 7.7% over this year, accounting for about 2.5% of Taiwan's gross domestic product. Taiwan media reported that the Taiwan military plans to build 15 new anti-ship missile sites across Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Under the banners of “freedom” and “democracy,” the DPP authorities squander the hard-earned money of ordinary people and stubbornly pursue “seeking independence through force,” even at the cost of turning Taiwan into an “arsenal” and an “explosives island,” pushing Taiwan into the perilous situation of war. This is not protecting Taiwan but “selling out,” “harming,” and “destroying” Taiwan. The more weapons they buy, the greater the disaster they bring to the people of Taiwan. Only by abandoning the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” and taking the path of peaceful development will Taiwan have a future, and will Taiwan compatriots be able to lead happy and secure lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","On the 8th of this month, the DPP authorities seized a mainland fishing vessel on the pretext of so-called “crossing the line,” dumped all of its catch into the sea, and took all 13 people on board back with them. What is your comment on this?","Relevant parties in Taiwan should respect the fact that fishermen from both sides of the Strait operate in traditional fishing grounds, respect the rights and interests of mainland fishermen engaged in normal production and operations, stop the practice of arbitrarily detaining mainland fishing boats, ensure the safety of the lives and property of the personnel involved, and release the people and boats as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","凤凰卫视记者","First question: The meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States is about to take place, and Taiwan media are hyping that the U.S. side will demand that the Mainland not “interfere” in Taiwan’s elections. Lai Ching-te said this is of great significance and that the United States wants to protect Taiwan’s democratic system. What is your response to this? Second question: We have noted that…","First, the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the most important and sensitive issue in China-US relations. We hope the US side will earnestly abide by the one-China principle, honor the solemn political commitments it has made to China, and implement the important consensus reached by the two heads of state.\nSecond, the Mainland Affairs Council has blatantly peddled the “two-state theory,” once again exposing the “Taiwan independence” nature of the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Last week saw the arrival of “Double Eleven,” the online shopping festival initiated by mainland e-commerce platforms, which as in previous years set off a shopping craze in Taiwan. Some netizens on the island commented that this year's shopping channels of mainland e-commerce platforms are more convenient for Taiwan consumers. Some mainland experts believe this shows that cross-Strait economic and trade…","The “Double Eleven” e-commerce shopping festival has sparked a shopping frenzy on both sides of the Strait, bringing affordable, high-quality mainland products to Taiwan. The shopping experience of “buying cross-border goods is as easy as buying local goods” has been fully recognized by Taiwan consumers. We are pleased to see that the vibrant mainland e-commerce market has built a convenient and affordable shopping channel for people in Taiwan, and has also provided greater room for deeper cooperation and innovative development in cross-Strait logistics and related industries. We welcome compatriots in Taiwan to share with compatriots on the mainland a safe, fast and convenient online shopping environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities in various localities have remained lively. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant information.","On November 8, the 12th Straits Machinery Industry Expo and the 14th China Longyan Investment Project Fair were held in Longyan, Fujian. The expo was approved by the Ministry of Commerce, guided by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Fujian Provincial Government, sponsored by the China Machinery Industry Federation, and undertaken by the Longyan Municipal Government. Under the theme of “Cross-Strait Integrated Development, Win-Win Investment in Longyan,” the expo set up seven major exhibition areas: industrial development, engineering and environmental protection machinery, special-purpose vehicles and emergency equipment, new energy and new materials, Taiwan machinery, intelligent manufacturing, and components. With an exhibition area of 30,000 square meters, nearly 500 enterprises and institutions from both sides of the Strait and abroad exhibited, and 25 industrial projects were signed on site, involving a total investment of 24.6 billion yuan. During the expo, the “Seeking Development, Promoting Integration—Well-Known Taiwan Enterprises Visit Longyan” activity was also held, helping Taiwan businesses and enterprises gain an in-depth understanding of investment opportunities in Longyan, facilitating precise matching of key projects, and deepening the integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan.\nOn November 11, the “Zhangzhou Chuangzhi New City · Taiwan Strait Model Home—Fujian-Taiwan Industry Promotion and Special Product Exhibition of the Zhangzhou Taiwan Businessmen Investment Zone” was held in Beijing. Through offline exhibitions and sales, online live streaming, and special exchange meetings, the event promoted Fujian-Taiwan industries and special products from the Taiwan Businessmen Investment Zone, including the food industry, electronics and home appliances, and daily chemical products, helping Taiwan-funded enterprises in the park expand domestic market demand and increase product sales.\nFrom November 14 to 16, the 17th Taiwan Businessmen Forum was held in Huai'an, Jiangsu. Under the theme of “Integrating into Domestic and International Dual Circulation, Jointly Building a Model Zone for Taiwan Investment,” the forum held an opening ceremony, a main forum, and sub-forums on the development of the new energy vehicle and parts industry, development trends of the circuit board industry, and “Domestic Market Expansion, Growing Together,” actively exploring models of cross-Strait industrial cooperation, helping Taiwan enterprises and businesses seize the opportunities of the integrated development of the Yangtze River Delta, expanding the domestic market with greater intensity, better integrating into the new development pattern, and further deepening the integrated economic development of both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Han Kuo-yu recently said that the business of a friend’s immigration company tripled this year, because many people are afraid of war. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and continuously collude with external forces to provoke “independence” moves. They are pushing Taiwan step by step into a dangerous situation of war, seriously harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and seriously endangering Taiwan's future and destiny. Many Taiwan compatriots are deeply worried about this and have made corresponding choices, which we fully understand.\nCross-Strait relations are currently at an important juncture. We hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will see the general trend clearly, recognize the stakes clearly, and resolutely oppose the separatist acts of “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces. We hope they will help push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and thereby better safeguard their own interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Recently, a leader of the Taiwan Affairs Office met with a Taiwan delegation including Su Ching-chuan and Huang Yi-cheng in Nanning, and said that under the premise of complying with relevant regulations, they would provide assistance for the import of Taiwan's grouper and other agricultural products into the mainland. What progress has been made?","Because banned drugs and excessive drug residues were detected, the General Administration of Customs suspended imports of Taiwan grouper starting June 13, 2022. For some time, grouper industry operators on the island have expressed through various channels their willingness to take effective measures to improve product quality and ensure the safety of grouper exported to the mainland. Su Chin-chuan, deputy executive director of the Policy Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang and chairman of the China Huaxia Agricultural Economics Association, and Huang Yi-cheng, chairman of the Taiwan Cross-Strait Agriculture and Fisheries Exchange and Development Investment Association, have actively guided island operators in rectification and led them to visit the mainland, expressing a strong desire for grouper imports to the mainland. We uphold the concept that 'compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,' attach great importance to the demands of island agriculture and fisheries operators, and, on the basis of their passing rectification, will provide more help for the import of Taiwan grouper and other agricultural and fishery products to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582183.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","First question: How does the Taiwan Affairs Office view the political parties on the island negotiating “Blue-White cooperation,” and what is the relationship between “Blue-White cooperation” and peace across the Taiwan Strait? Second question: Regarding the resumption of cross-Strait tourism, if the Taiwan side adjusts related measures, will the mainland also make corresponding adjustments? Have the competent…","On the first question, we have noted the relevant reports. I want to stress that peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should join hands, follow the trend of history, uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development.\nOn the second question, regarding mainland tourists visiting Taiwan, the boom in mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism will only return once cross-Strait relations are back on the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The DPP recently listed so-called mainland “election-interference tactics,” including the mainland issuing opinions on its Taiwan policy and introducing 10 entry-and-exit policies, and claimed that the Taiwan Enterprises Association is cooperating with the mainland in “united front” activities. Yesterday, the chairman of the Taiwan Enterprises Association responded that one should not, as soon as…","On the first question: I want to say that the DPP's tactics of reversing black and white and confusing right and wrong should come to an end. We would like to remind that as soon as election time comes, the DPP will step up all kinds of \"dirty tricks\" to seek electoral gain, and broad Taiwan compatriots see this very clearly.\nOn the second question: We uphold the concept that \"compatriots on both sides are one family,\" and we have always respected, cared for and brought benefits to Taiwan compatriots. On the political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to work together with relevant parties in Taiwan to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development, and enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.\nRegarding the import of custard apples from Taiwan to the mainland, we, together with relevant competent authorities, are maintaining communication with the Kuomintang of China, Taitung County and other parties, deeply understanding the appeals of relevant Taiwan people and enterprises. We are actively and orderly advancing the registration and review of custard apple packing plants and orchards to prepare for the import of custard apples into the mainland. This will both bring benefits to grassroots Taiwan people and operators, and allow mainland people to taste quality Taiwan fruit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582186.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Liu Chao-hsuan, Taiwan-side chairman of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, recently called on the mainland to grant Taiwanese businesses “domestic capital treatment,” to improve the effectiveness of measures benefiting Taiwan, and also expressed hope to consolidate the ECFA framework cooperation agreement and continue pursuing mutual benefit and win-win results. We also note that the mainland side previously…","We are continuously improving the systems and policies that enhance the well-being and interests of Taiwan compatriots, implementing equal treatment, optimizing the business environment, and helping broad Taiwanese businesspeople and enterprises develop better and faster on the mainland.\nRegarding ECFA, we have seen a lot of discussion on the island. For example, some people point out that if the Early Harvest list of ECFA were canceled, the petrochemical, machine tool, and steel industries on the island would be greatly impacted. It cannot be denied that since ECFA took effect, it has brought tangible benefits to relevant industries and people on both sides of the Strait, especially in Taiwan. Regrettably, since the DPP authorities took office, on the one hand, they have “generally accepted” the benefits of ECFA, saying they do not wish to terminate ECFA. On the other hand, they have colluded with external forces to continuously obstruct and undermine normal economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, seeking to “decouple and cut off chains” with the mainland economically. It is precisely this two-faced and double-standard approach that has made the implementation of ECFA face uncertainty, directly harming the vital interests of broad Taiwan compatriots.\nFor the well-being and interests of Taiwan compatriots to be guaranteed and enhanced, the key lies in Taiwan compatriots resolutely opposing the separatist conduct of “Taiwan independence” and promoting the return of cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231117_12582181.htm"],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","We note that the recently published list of the DPP’s “Top Ten Public Grievances” on the island ranks the “egg shortage and imported egg dispute” first. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Since the DPP came to power, “egg shortages” have occurred more than once, and there have even been farces such as imports of “poisonous eggs” and “origin laundering.” These problems fully demonstrate that the DPP authorities have never genuinely considered the well-being of the Taiwan public, and they are even less capable of properly resolving people’s livelihood issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The commemorative event marking the 25th anniversary of the “Taiwan Strait Passage Research” was recently held in Xiamen. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant information.","On November 10, the commemorative event marking the 25th anniversary of the study of the Taiwan Strait Tunnel was held in Xiamen. The event was co-hosted by cross-strait civil organizations, including the Fujian Provincial Cultural and Economic Exchange Center, the Fujian Provincial Exchange Association, the Fujian Provincial Geological Society, the Fujian-Taiwan Exchange Association, and relevant Taiwan associations. More than 140 people, including experts and scholars who have long engaged in research on the Taiwan Strait tunnel from both sides of the Strait, attended.\nAt the symposium, the guests discussed the progress and results of work on topics related to the preliminary planning of the Taiwan Strait tunnel. They exchanged views on comprehensive three-dimensional transportation planning, technological breakthroughs in bridge and tunnel engineering, and construction management and operation models. They reviewed and summarized important experience and achievements gained in 25 years of research on the Taiwan Strait tunnel, using research to promote integration and connectivity to promote integration, and further raising the level and standard of cross-strait academic exchanges. The guests also visited and inspected the construction of relevant projects on site.\nThe holding of this commemorative event is an important measure to earnestly implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” to respond to the livelihood demands of the people of Kinmen and Matsu, and to deepen the “same-city living circles” of Fuzhou-Matsu and Xiamen-Kinmen and the integrated economic and social development across the Taiwan Strait. It will certainly lay a firmer foundation for further promoting research on the Taiwan Strait tunnel and project construction, and for turning the grand vision of the Taiwan Strait tunnel into reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-17","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","According to foreign media reports, US President Joe Biden recently approved providing Taiwan with $80 million in military financing. Island media hyped this budget as the first time in nearly 40 years that the US has “used taxpayers' money to provide military aid to Taiwan.” In response, Li Dewei, a KMT-affiliated representative, said that what Taiwan wants is peace, not war. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office…","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan, China, and firmly oppose US provision of weapons to Taiwan. There is no free lunch in the world. Whether labeled as “military aid,” “financing,” or any other name, for the people of Taiwan these are “foreign debts” that bring war to Taiwan. The DPP authorities, who insist on colluding with external forces in an attempt to “seek independence through force,” will only push Taiwan into the ominous perils of war and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231117_12582175.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-11-20","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","ROK President Yoon Suk-yeol in an interview on November 20 said that China plays an important role in advancing freedom, peace and prosperity in East Asia. China’s seeking trilateral cooperation with the DPRK and Russia, who violate the UN Charter, Security Council resolutions and other international rules, does no good to its international reputation and status. The ROK always develops sound and mature ROK-China…","I noted the reports. I wish to stress that as a responsible major country, China has played an important, constructive role in international and regional affairs. China knows what its responsibilities and interests are. We don’t need to be told what to do or not to do. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affairs and brooks no foreign interference. On the South China Sea, China and ASEAN countries have the ability, confidence and wisdom to handle this issue well. The ROK is not a party to the South China Sea issue and there’s no point in getting involved.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347639.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231120_11183598.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-20","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan’s “presidential candidate” Lai Ching-te has announced Taiwan’s former “US envoy” Hsiao Bi-khim as his pick for “vice president”. How does the ministry respond to this? Does China plan to announce more sanctions on Hsiao if she becomes “vice president” of Taiwan?","It’s not a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347639.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231120_11183598.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-24","Mao Ning","Reuters","Australia confirmed today its warship named the Toowoomba transited the Taiwan Strait. Taiwanese officials said its military kept watch throughout but gave no further details. Does China have any comment on the passing of the Australian vessel?","China’s position is clear and consistent. We urge parties concerned not to make provocations or create trouble for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347643.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231124_11186665.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-24","Mao Ning","Global Times","According to reports, on November 22 local time, ROK President Yoon Suk Yeol and UK Prime Minister Rishi Sunak signed The Downing Street Accord, in which the two sides state that “We emphasise that our basic positions on Taiwan remain unchanged. Peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is an indispensable element in the security and prosperity of the international community. Given the serious nature of the…","I would like to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no interference by any external forces. As for issues related to the South and East China Seas, neither the ROK nor the UK is a party concerned, and there has never been any problem with regard to the “freedom of navigation and overflight”. China urges relevant parties to stop making irresponsible comment on issues bearing on China’s core and major concerns and be very prudent about what they say or do.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347643.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231124_11186665.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-11-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 24 (Electronic Dispatch): According to reports, on the 24th, Hou Yu-ih and Ko Wen-je registered as candidates on behalf of the Kuomintang and the Taiwan People's Party respectively, marking the collapse of the “Blue-White Cooperation.” In response, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 24th, saying: We have noted the relevant reports. We respect the existing social system in Taiwan and hope that the results of the elections in early next year in Taiwan will help maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan region and push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development.\nChen Binhua said that peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. At present, Taiwan faces a choice between two paths and two prospects: peace or war, prosperity or decline. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” make the right choice at a critical moment, and contribute to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231124_12583827.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office held a press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good day, and welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I will be hosting today's press conference. Please go ahead with your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","On November 15, the leaders of China and the United States met in San Francisco, USA. Public opinion on the island has paid close attention to the position on the Taiwan question expressed during the meeting, and has called for seizing the opportunity for peace across the Taiwan Strait brought by the meeting of the two leaders. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question has always been the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. At the San Francisco meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, President Xi Jinping explained to the US side in depth the Chinese government’s principled position on the Taiwan question, stressing that the US should translate its statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions, stop arming Taiwan, and support China’s peaceful reunification. US President Joe Biden reiterated the commitment the US made at the Bali meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, and clearly stated that the US does not support “Taiwan independence.”\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible like fire and water, and “Taiwan independence” is a source of turmoil for stability in the Asia-Pacific region. To return cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development and to ensure that peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait are effectively safeguarded, we must return to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584678.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that the 2024 election of Taiwan’s leader will decide “whether Taiwan takes the backward path of depending on China, or stands together with countries around the world,” and he hopes the public will unite to support him. What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te’s remarks are a manifestation of his “Taiwan independence” nature. Stubbornly insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position, creating confrontation and antagonism across the Taiwan Strait, and colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke will only lead to a tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait and threaten the security and well-being of broad Taiwan compatriots. It is a dead end, an evil path that cannot be taken. Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” will return cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development, and Taiwan compatriots can live and work in peace and contentment. This is the broad road leading to a bright future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently officially announced that Hsiao Bi-khim will serve as his running mate. Public opinion on the island holds that the Lai-Hsiao combination, forming a “double independence team,” will only push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster. What is your comment?","I have seen many netizens comment that the “Double Independence combination” is the “Double Poison combination,” where this “poison” is the “poison” of “poisonous drugs” and the “poison” of “poisoning harm.” “Taiwan independence” means war. The DPP’s introduction of such a dangerous “independence-independence pairing” will only poison the interests and well-being of compatriots on the island, poison peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and poison Taiwan’s future and destiny.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584677.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","According to US media reports, John Kirby, strategic communications coordinator of the White House National Security Council, disclosed that US President Biden said the US will continue to sell weapons to Taiwan to safeguard Taiwan’s “self-defense” capability. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","US arms sales to Taiwan violate the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” and we firmly oppose them. The relevant departments have repeatedly stated our principled position. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and fulfill its solemn political commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete action, and not to say one thing while doing another. Countless facts show that “seeking independence through force” is a dead end, and relying on foreigners to aggrandize oneself leads to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Hsiao Bi-khim recently said, “Fighting a war with the Mainland is not an option for Taiwan; communicating with the Mainland is the option for safeguarding peace.” What comments do you have?","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. As long as the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” is upheld, there is no obstacle to exchanges between us and any political party or group in Taiwan. Those who refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, while at the same time talking empty words about so-called cross-Strait communication, dialogue, and maintaining peace, are merely trying to conceal the nature and harm of “Taiwan independence” and to deceive voters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584676.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Taiwan's compulsory military service will be restored to one year starting next year. To support this policy, Taiwan's education authorities introduced the so-called “3+1 Study-and-Service Program,” which has drawn a lukewarm response at universities across the island, with only 46 applicants. What is your comment?","Students at Taiwan universities have not bought into the so-called “3+1 study-and-service program,” which is no surprise. More and more people in Taiwan, especially young people, have come to see that the DPP authorities' promise that “young people will not go to the battlefield” was merely a lie to win votes. From extending military service to rolling out a so-called supporting package, the DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to manipulate “seeking independence through force,” will only aggravate tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait, seriously harm the security and well-being of Taiwan residents, and sacrifice the studies and future of Taiwan students.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584674.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","海峡之声记者","According to reports, Taiwan is seeking to purchase littoral combat ships that the US military no longer wants, with negotiations having started as early as this summer. What comments do you have?","These reports make it clearer to everyone that the DPP authorities, for the sake of their party's interests, do not hesitate to lavishly squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people, willingly playing the role of a “sucker” and a “cash machine” for the United States. If the DPP authorities are allowed to stubbornly persist all the way down the evil path of “selling out Taiwan,” “harming Taiwan,” and “ruining Taiwan,” it will only push Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and peril, bringing profound disaster to compatriots in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视中国新闻记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently announced that from January to September this year, total cross-Strait trade (including Hong Kong) fell 21.8%, exports fell 21.9%, and imports fell 21.7%. Cross-Strait trade continues to decline, showing that the mainland's foreign trade continues to shrink and the shadow of deflation remains. What comment do you have?","This year, the mainland's national economy has continued to improve, production and supply have steadily increased, and market demand has continued to expand. It has always been the main driving force of world economic development. In the first three quarters, the mainland's gross domestic product (GDP) grew 5.2% year on year, total retail sales of consumer goods grew 6.8% year on year, value added of industry grew 4.0% year on year, value added of the service sector grew 6.0% year on year, and per capita disposable real income of residents grew 5.9% year on year. International capital and foreign capital are optimistic about the prospects of the mainland's economy and are continuously increasing their investment and layout. We have held many international economic and trade exchange events, including the Third Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation, the 134th China Import and Export Fair (Canton Fair), and the Sixth China International Import Expo, creating conditions for foreign businesses and foreign investors to come to the mainland to develop markets and seek opportunities. Relevant data show that the mainland's approach of “buying from the world, selling to the world, and benefiting the world” is welcomed around the globe, fully demonstrating that major economies around the world have cast a vote of confidence in the mainland's development.\nFrom January to September this year, the number of projects invested in the mainland by Taiwanese businesses increased 23.9% year on year, the actual amount of Taiwan capital utilized increased 7.5% year on year, and cross-Strait trade volume approached 200 billion US dollars, still maintaining a high level of operation. This shows that although the DPP authorities keep setting obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, Taiwan compatriots and young people, Taiwanese businesses and enterprises remain optimistic about the mainland and committed to deepening their roots there, and their confidence and willingness to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams have not changed. The bright prospects of cross-Strait economic exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development have not changed, and our policy stance of respecting, caring for, and benefiting Taiwan compatriots, sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots first, and protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises in accordance with the law has changed even less. As the mainland's opening-up steps grow larger and its business environment keeps improving, we are highly confident that cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation will expand into broader fields and rise to higher levels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584675.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","It is understood that applications by certain Taiwan organizations and temples to invite the Mazu golden statue from the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple in Fujian and the Guan Gong golden statue from the Guan Gong Temple in Dongshan, Zhangzhou, to tour the island for protection and blessings (巡安) were not approved by the Taiwan authorities. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan-based civil organizations invited the Mazu Ancestral Temple in Meizhou, Fujian, and the Guandi Temple in Dongshan to respectfully send the golden statues of Mazu and Guan Di to Taiwan for tours of inspection and blessings. This was obstructed and rudely blocked by the DPP authorities in every way, which aroused strong discontent among the broad masses of temple worshippers in Taiwan. Inviting the golden statues of Mazu and Guan Di to Taiwan for tours of inspection is an eager expectation of many temples and people in Taiwan. The DPP authorities have repeatedly demanded that the Taiwan-based civil inviting parties explain the so-called “necessity, urgency, and irreplaceability” of sending the golden statue of Mazu to Taiwan. They have even ignored the request for inviting the golden statue of Guan Di to Taiwan, completely disregarding the wishes of the broad masses of Taiwan people and showing not even basic respect for Mazu and Guan Di. We must ask: when a number of mainland personnel have recently visited Taiwan for exchanges, why does the DPP authorities insist on blocking the golden statues of Mazu and Guan Di from going to Taiwan? Why can the Mazu from the Huiju Tianhou Palace in Kunshan, Jiangsu, enter the island, while the DPP authorities deliberately and maliciously block the golden statue of Mazu from the Meizhou Ancestral Temple from going to Taiwan? A Hokkien proverb says it well: “People are doing it, and Heaven is watching.” The DPP authorities’ reckless actions are both unreasonable and impolite, and they are very unpopular in Taiwan. This matter once again shows that only when cross-strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development and artificial obstacles to cross-strait exchanges are removed can compatriots on both sides truly achieve free, smooth, and normal exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231129_12584673.htm"],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Hou Yu-ih recently declared to Taiwan's industrial and commercial circles that, as soon as he is elected, on the premises of equality, dignity, and friendliness, he will fully restart dialogue and exchanges with the mainland and rebuild cross-Strait mutual trust. Ko Wen-je has also stated that cross-Strait opening should proceed step by step. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on…","On the first question: On the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with relevant political parties, groups, and people from all sectors in Taiwan, including the Kuomintang, to consolidate and enhance mutual trust, strengthen exchange and cooperation, and jointly push cross-strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development. We aim to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question: The DPP authorities’ claim is pure fabrication. Every time there is an election, the DPP authorities solemnly and with great fanfare concoct all kinds of lies and rumors about mainland “interference in elections.” We believe that as voting approaches, the DPP authorities will fabricate even more rumors and tell even more lies. Taiwan’s people have long grown accustomed to this and will not easily be deceived.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Terry Gou recently announced his withdrawal from the race, saying “For Taiwan’s future, I choose to fulfill it.” What is your comment?","We have noted the relevant reports.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","Please, spokesperson, introduce recent cross-Strait cultural exchange activities in various localities.","Since November, cross-Strait cultural exchanges have continued to heat up. I will introduce two events held in Fujian recently.\nFrom November 16 to 18, the 15th Cross-Strait Tea Expo was held in Wuyishan City, Nanping, Fujian. Under the theme “Coordinated Development of the Three Teas, Integrated Development,” it was co-hosted by cross-Strait organizations including the China Tea Circulation Association, the Cross-Strait Tea Exchange Association, the Taiwan Farmers' Association, and the Taiwan Region Tea Manufacturing Industry Association. The exhibition covered 45,000 square meters with 1,900 booths, including 150 booths in the Taiwan Pavilion, and 14,300 exhibitors and buyers from both sides of the Strait attended. During the exhibition, cumulative visits to the pavilions exceeded 260,000 person-times, and the total transaction volume reached 8.436 billion yuan. During this Tea Expo, activities such as the 2023 Cross-Strait Marriage and Family Tea Culture Study Camp and the Min-Taiwan Tea Origins Inspection were also held. Relevant cross-Strait associations signed the “Framework Agreement on Strengthening Min-Taiwan Tea Industry Exchange and Cooperation.” These activities and achievements have effectively promoted exchanges and cooperation among tea merchants and tea people on both sides of the Strait, and promoted the integrated development of cross-Strait tea culture, the tea industry, and tea technology.\nFrom November 23 to 27, the “Bound by Xiamen and Kinmen” Cross-Strait Youth Students Cultural Study Camp and the first Xiamen University–Kinmen University Baseball Invitational Tournament were held at Xiamen University. Over five days, 50 students from both sides of the Strait gathered together, held two baseball invitational games, experienced the charm of traditional Chinese sports such as dragon boat racing and archery in depth, visited the Xiamen Special Economic Zone Memorial Hall, the Minnan red-brick historic settlements, and the former site of the Kinmen County Government, learned in depth about the development course and achievements of the Xiamen Special Economic Zone, and felt the historical connections between the two sides. Students from both sides exchanged ideas, interacted, opened their hearts to each other, and blended together during the activities, building deep friendships.\nCompatriots on both sides are one family, and the closer they go, the closer they become. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to visit and see for themselves. We are glad to see and support compatriots on both sides strengthening normal exchanges and contacts, cultivating shared interests, and promoting heart-to-heart understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Some public opinion holds that the DPP authorities have ignored Kinmen public opinion and deliberately delayed reviewing the “referendum case” on the “Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge,” so that the second-stage signature collection has not been carried out. What is your comment on this?","Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is the common call and urgent wish of the people of Kinmen. Over the years, we have continuously taken measures to enhance the interests and well-being of the people of Kinmen, benefiting Kinmen compatriots in the same way we serve compatriots on the mainland. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,” announced not long ago, explicitly calls to “explore the model of Xiamen-Kinmen cooperative infrastructure construction and accelerate the advancement of electricity, gas and bridge connections with Kinmen,” and outlines the appealing vision of “Xiamen and Kinmen facing each other across the water, Lu Island and Yu Island linked by bridge.” Like the people of Kinmen, we eagerly look forward to this vision becoming reality as soon as possible.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities, standing in opposition to the interests of the people of Kinmen and Matsu, deliberately restrict the development of Kinmen and Matsu. This mindset and these actions are not supported by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Question one: After the breakthrough in “blue-white cooperation,” the Taiwan Affairs Office responded that it respects Taiwan’s existing social system. Can it be interpreted that, regardless of the election results in Taiwan two months from now, the mainland side will respect the final choice of the Taiwan people?\nQuestion two: The mainland side has stated that it does not intervene in Taiwan’s regional…","On the first question, I want to emphasize two points. First, our position is very clear: we respect the social system of the Taiwan region. Second, at present, Taiwan faces a critical choice between two roads and two prospects: peace or war, prosperity or decline. We hope compatriots in Taiwan will recognize where their interests lie, distinguish right from wrong, firmly oppose 'Taiwan independence' separatism and external interference, and jointly promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development and share the dividends of peaceful cross-Strait development.\nOn the second question, many cases exposed in Taiwan have already proven that the DPP authorities are habitual offenders of so-called 'cognitive warfare.' Every election, the DPP authorities diligently and earnestly fabricate rumors and smear the mainland in order to cover up their poor governance and divert public criticism. It is foreseeable that as voting day approaches, they will fabricate even more rumors and tell even more lies to seek electoral gain. In this regard, the Taiwan public is already accustomed to it and will not easily be deceived.\nOn the third question, in order to conceal the essence of 'Taiwan independence,' deliberately fabricating rhetoric to win votes is an old trick that everyone knows. We advise the '独独配' ('Du-Du-Pei') to stop asking for humiliation.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","A media literacy survey on the island shows that 50.7% of Taiwanese youth most often use Douyin as their information platform. What is the spokesperson’s view on this phenomenon?","Both sides of the Strait share the same language and characters, the same ancestry, and the same customs. Mainland social apps such as Douyin, Xiaohongshu, Bilibili, Weibo, and WeChat are convenient and fun for young people in Taiwan to use, so they naturally win their love and recognition. We support whatever young people in Taiwan like, and we are pleased to see more young Taiwanese using the ways they enjoy to learn about the mainland and make friends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","台湾中视记者","Some foreign media reported that the island’s elections show a three-way standoff, the “blue-white” camp has failed to consolidate, and the pro-“independence” DPP may move toward a third “term,” which would again heighten tensions in the Taiwan Strait. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond?","This shows that the harm of “Taiwan independence” is known to all, and even foreign media increasingly see clearly that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities cause tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Right now, Taiwan faces a critical choice between two paths and two prospects: peace and war, prosperity and decline. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize that “Taiwan independence workers” are “troublemakers” and “war makers,” recognize that the “獨獨配” pairing is a “Taiwan-harming pairing,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","On the morning of the 23rd, the 10th batch of Chinese People’s Volunteers martyrs’ remains interred in the Republic of Korea was escorted back to Shenyang, Liaoning, by an air force special aircraft. The remains of 25 CPV heroes who died far from home now rest on their homeland after many years. This is the tenth year since the return and burial of CPV martyrs’ remains from the Republic of Korea, and it is the…","This year marks the 70th anniversary of the victory in the War to Resist U.S. Aggression and Aid Korea, and also the tenth year since the remains of Chinese People's Volunteers martyrs in Korea were returned home for burial. To remember history, commemorate the martyrs, fully demonstrate respect for and care for the CPV martyrs, and further unite national sentiment, from November 23 to 24, three Taiwanese primary and secondary school students studying in Shenyang were invited to participate in the burial activity for the tenth batch of CPV martyrs' remains returned from Korea.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新闻记者","Regarding Hou Yu-ih's recent statement that, if elected, he would open Taiwan to mainland students for study and employment, the DPP said this involves “national security” issues and would also impact Taiwan's job market. How does the spokesperson respond to this?","The development of exchanges and cooperation across the Strait in fields such as tourism and education depends on a healthy and favorable overall environment for cross-Strait relations. As long as cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development, cross-Strait tourism can fully resume normal operations, and exchanges in other fields are also expected to become normalized and routine. I believe this is a situation that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are pleased to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-11-29","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Hou Youyi recently publicly expressed opposition to 'Taiwan independence', saying 'Vote for the DPP, and your son goes to the battlefield'. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","“Taiwan independence” means war. The DPP authorities obstinately persist in the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, collude with external forces to plot “independence” and prepare for war, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the interests and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the grave harm of “Taiwan independence.” For their own safety and well-being, and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, we hope they will resolutely oppose and resist “Taiwan independence” and promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Wishing everyone health and safety. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202311/t20231129_12584670.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-11-30","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan “president” Tsai Ing-wen has told The New York Times in an interview that China’s leadership is too “overwhelmed” with its internal problems to consider an invasion of Taiwan. She said this was not a time to consider a major invasion largely because of China’s internal economic, financial and political challenges, and also because the international community has been clear that war is not an option. Would…","I need to correct you first. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and there is no such thing as “Taiwanese president”. This is not a question about foreign affairs.\nLet me stress that there is only one China in the world. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and standing up for the one-China principle is a prevailing consensus among the international community. To ensure cross-Strait peace and stability, it is essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference. The DPP authorities’ obsession with the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and provocations to pursue “Taiwan independence” will only end in a shameful failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347647.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231130_11190422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-11-30","Wang Wenbin","Antara","Based on a report, Taiwan’s health department today urged the elderly, the very young and those with poor immunity to avoid traveling to China due to the recent increase in respiratory illness in Chinese mainland. Does the ministry have any comment about it?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.\nChina’s National Health Commission (NHC) has held a press conference to share information on relevant matter. It is safe to travel, do business and study here in China and there’s no need to worry.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347647.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202311/t20231130_11190422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Flynn, Commander of the US Army Pacific, recently said that next year the US will deploy new intermediate-range land-based missiles in the Asia-Pacific region to deter the mainland from striking Taiwan. According to US media reports, these will include a small number of land-based “Tomahawk” cruise missiles and “Standard-6” missiles. What is the Ministry of National Defense’s comment?","The US push to deploy intermediate-range missiles in the Asia-Pacific region is a dangerous development that will seriously threaten the security of countries in the region and seriously undermine regional peace and stability. China firmly opposes this and will take firm countermeasures. It must be emphasized that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, brooks no foreign interference, and its resolution cannot be blocked by anyone or any force.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan plans to purchase six decommissioned U.S. littoral combat ships, and plans to build six shore-based “Harpoon\n” missile sites and nine shore-based “Hsiung Feng\n” missile sites, and will purchase 1,485 “micro drones” to strengthen the so-called “urban defense operations.” May I ask what the spokesperson's comment is on this?","The DPP authorities, \"relying on the US to seek independence,\" are turning Taiwan into an \"arsenal\" and a \"powder keg island.\" This is pushing Taiwan into an abyss of disaster and will surely bring enormous calamity to the people of Taiwan. Taiwan's security depends on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Relying on a few US-made weapons is fundamentally unreliable.\nThe People's Liberation Army of China is sharpening its weapons and readying its steeds, on high alert, resolutely defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Some reports say that China has no so-called “2027 or 2035 plan to attack Taiwan.” Does this mean that armed attack on Taiwan remains an option, but the timetable may be earlier? Some scholars even believe this is related to the outcome of Taiwan's election next year. I would like to ask the spokesperson for a response.","Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests. We adhere to striving for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. But if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke or coerce, or even cross red lines, we will be compelled to take resolute measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is the firm will of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people and the sacred mission of the Chinese People’s Liberation Army.\n“Relying on the US to seek independence” is doomed to be futile, and “seeking independence by force” is a dead end. No matter who attempts to separate Taiwan from China in any form, the Chinese People’s Liberation Army will absolutely not agree and will absolutely not show leniency.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have a similar question. Yesterday, Tsai Ing-wen said that mainland China is currently facing internal problems and is unlikely to attack Taiwan. What is your response to Tsai Ing-wen’s remarks?","China will eventually be reunified, and reunification is bound to happen. I just mentioned that “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail, and “seeking independence by force” is a dead end. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the U.S. 2023 National Defense Authorization Act provides gratis military aid to Taiwan, which has been implemented in succession recently. In the past half month, the latest wave of military aid included 80,000 sets of U.S. active-duty individual combat equipment and 1,000 M240B squad machine guns. The chairman of the U.S. House of Representatives “Select Committee on the CCP” and the…","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China, and demand that the United States match its words with actions, translate its statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions, stop arming Taiwan, and stop harming China’s core interests. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A Taiwan netizen said bluntly that if the PLA lands in Taiwan, Taiwan residents will “offer baskets of food and jugs of drink to welcome the royal army.” What comments do you have?","Taiwan will certainly return to the embrace of the motherland.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lai Ching-te and Hsiao Bi-khim, on the one hand, have vigorously hyped up the so-called mainland \"no plan to attack Taiwan\" in the coming years, claiming they hope to maintain the status quo of peace across the Taiwan Strait. On the other hand, they keep strengthening military entanglement with the U.S. military and clamor to \"strengthen our own capabilities.\" What is your comment on this?","I have already answered this question just now. Let me emphasize again: no matter who attempts to split Taiwan from China in any form, the Chinese People's Liberation Army will absolutely not allow it and will certainly not show leniency.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-11-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The spokesperson just mentioned that the premise for developing China-US military relations is equality and mutual respect. However, at today’s press conference, many questions involved US intervention in the Taiwan question and the South China Sea issue. Do you believe the US has broken the basis of equality and respect?","As I just said, equality and respect are the essential meaning of the correct way for China and the United States to get along, and also the basic premise for developing military-to-military relations. China has consistently adhered to the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence, and win-win cooperation in dealing with the United States. We hope the United States will move toward China, respect China's core interests and major concerns, show sincerity, and match its words with its actions, so as to create a favorable atmosphere and conditions for promoting the healthy and stable development of military-to-military relations.\nClosing remarks:\nIn the month of November that is about to end, there is an important date: the 74th anniversary of the founding of the PLA Air Force. We are able to “buy, buy, buy” freely on Singles' Day, and behind that is the strong protection of the People's Liberation Army, including the People's Air Force. Let us pay tribute to the Air Force and wish our air and space guardians to forge iron wings to reach first-class standing, and soar together with the times.\nThe comrades of the Air Force have asked us to present a small souvenir to all the reporter friends. It is a badge of the Air Force's main fighter aircraft, including the J-10C, J-20, J-16, Y-20, and H-6K. We hope you enjoy it. Thank you.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16270137.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-11-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 30 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 30th that the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan claimed the Mazu golden statue from the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple and the Guandi golden statue from the Dongshan Guandi Temple were “rejected” when they went to Taiwan. This is malicious false information. This claim is itself…","Chen Binhua pointed out that the DPP authorities’ obstruction of the Mazu golden body from the Meizhou Ancestral Temple and the Guandi golden body from the Dongshan Guandi Temple from going to Taiwan is a clear fact, and Taiwan’s temples and vast numbers of believers have seen it with their own eyes. The Taiwanese invitation unit wrote to the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple to explicitly inform it that the competent authority in Taiwan considers this trip to Taiwan to lack “necessity, urgency, and irreplaceability,” and therefore did not approve it. Relevant organizations on the island separately submitted written applications for the Guandi golden body to go to Taiwan in April, June, and September of this year, and relevant Taiwanese agencies ignored them throughout. It was not until October 25 that the Mainland Affairs Council telephoned the relevant organizations to inform them that the applications would not be approved before the end of the year, and requested that they stop submitting documents. Even more, Taiwanese individuals who helped apply for the Guandi golden body to go to Taiwan were summoned by Taiwan police, which shows how far the DPP authorities’ “green terror” has gone!\nChen Binhua said: Are these matters not “rejection” and obstruction? The Mainland Affairs Council clearly obstructs normal civil exchanges across the Strait, yet now denies it outright, which is futile. If they are not obstructing, then please let them proceed. As for “malice,” the DPP authorities’ crude obstruction of the Mazu and Guandi golden bodies from going to Taiwan for the patrol and blessing is the greatest malice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202311/t20231130_12584894.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-12-04","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The Philippine government said recently that it is deeply concerned about the over 130 Chinese boats around Niu’e Jiao. French Foreign Minister Catherine Colonna said recently that France is concerned by what the Chinese warship did to the Australian ship. She added that “stability must prevail in the Taiwan Strait, and certainly the world doesn’t need a new crisis.” What is your response to these?","On your first question, Niu’e Jiao is part of China’s Nansha Qundao. Relevant waters of the South China Sea, including Niu’e Jiao and its adjacent waters, have always been important operating areas and shelters for Chinese fishing boats. It is justified and lawful for Chinese fishing boats to operate or shelter from wind in the area, and the Philippines is in no position to make irresponsible remarks.\nOn your second question, you may refer to China’s previous response. I would like to stress that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and the solid anchor to cross-Strait peace and stability is the one-China principle. We hope relevant parties will adhere to the one-China principle, stand firmly with China against Taiwan independence, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347649.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231204_11194357.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-12-05","Wang Wenbin","Phoenix TV","Leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen recently said at a DPP campaign rally that “we don’t want Hong Kong-style peace, we want peace with dignity”, the 2024 general election is not a choice between peace and war, and it is the people of Taiwan who must choose peace with dignity. What is your comment?","This is not a question on foreign affairs. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The election in the Taiwan region is purely China’s internal affair.\nI would like to stress that “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with cross-Strait peace as fire with water. “Taiwan independence” means war and “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Whatever high-sounding rhetoric the DPP authorities try to use, it cannot cover up their malicious attempt to tie Taiwan residents to the war chariot of “Taiwan independence”; it cannot change the fact that “Taiwan independence” elements are doomed to failure; and it cannot stop the irreversible trend of reunification of China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347650.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231205_11195104.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-12-07","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","Japan’s National Institute for Defense Studies issued the China Security Report 2024 recently, which says that as China builds up its military strength, including nuclear power, and deepens strategic coordination with Russia, the US will have to face more intense rivalry from China and Russia in the future. The report also says that Japan must further strengthen the necessary defense capabilities to deter China’s…","China is committed to peaceful development and adheres to a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. China’s growth means a stronger force for world peace. Taiwan is part of China and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese and brooks no external interference. The report of the Japanese think tank pointed fingers at China’s internal affairs, modernization of China’s military and China’s relations with other countries. The comments are irresponsible and don’t hold water.\nFor historical reasons, Japan’s military and security moves have been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. In recent years, Japan has greatly increased its military expenditure and sought to develop offensive weapons, which has caused grave concern from its neighbors and the international community. We urge Japan to earnestly respect the security concerns of its neighbors, profoundly reflect on its history of aggression, stop hyping up the “China threat” narrative and using it as a pretext for its own military buildup, and take substantive steps to earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347652.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231207_11196724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-12-08","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan’s defense ministry said today that a Chinese weather balloon had crossed the Taiwan Strait median line on Thursday. Does the foreign ministry have anything to offer regarding the balloon’s location or purpose? And Taiwan’s foreign ministry today also said that China has failed to live up to the promises it made Latin American countries that ended ties with Taiwan in favor of China. Does the foreign…","First of all, I would like to correct you that Taiwan is part of China. There is no so-called “defense ministry” or “foreign ministry” of Taiwan. On your first question, I am not aware of the situation and this is not a question on foreign affairs. On your second question, let me say that the normal, friendly relations between China and Latin American countries are deepening and our mutually beneficial cooperation is making positive progress. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change such a sound momentum of growth.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347653.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231208_11198048.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-12-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 8 (electronic dispatch). Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on December 8 that a new batch of custard apple packing plants and orchards in Taitung County, Taiwan, have been registered with the General Administration of Customs, and that as the custard apple season arrives in Taiwan, this will create favorable conditions for importing…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that we have consistently upheld the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family.” On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we make every effort to do practical good deeds and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. Since this year, we have worked with the General Administration of Customs to actively respond to the wishes expressed by the Kuomintang, Taitung County and others to resume importing Taiwan custard apples into the mainland. On June 20, after comprehensive evaluation, the General Administration of Customs announced the resumption of imports of Taiwan custard apples into the mainland. We have maintained close communication with Taitung County and accelerated the registration and review of custard apple packing plants and orchards to prepare for imports into the mainland. After careful review by the General Administration of Customs, a new batch of Taitung County custard apple operators, including 34 packing plants and 1,263 orchards, obtained registration. As of now, a total of 37 packing plants and 1,288 orchards in Taitung County have obtained registration, and relevant operators may check the details on the General Administration of Customs website. Packing plants and orchards that have not yet passed the review may continue to rectify and apply in accordance with the rectification requirements.\nZhu Fenglian said that as long as they uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and comply with relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we are willing to discuss with relevant parties on the island matters regarding support for resuming imports of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland. We are willing to continue upholding the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” respecting, caring for and benefiting Taiwan compatriots, and working with relevant parties on the island to promote the resumption of imports of more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, benefiting Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231208_12586419.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2023 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo and Cross-Strait Flower Expo was recently held in Xiamen, Fujian. I would like the spokesperson to introduce the relevant details.","From November 30 to December 2, 2023, the 2023 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo · Cross-Strait Flower Expo was held in Xiamen and Zhangzhou, Fujian. Themed “Cross-Strait Agricultural Conditions, Integrated Development,” this session of the Cross-Strait Agriculture Expo comprehensively displayed the achievements of cross-strait agricultural and rural exchanges and cooperation, multidimensionally promoted high-quality, distinctive cross-strait agricultural products, matched preferential policies for Taiwan farmers and Taiwan businesspeople investing and starting businesses on the mainland, built bridges and links for cross-strait youth to increase exchanges, and promoted cross-strait economic, trade, personnel, cultural, and technological exchanges, creating a high-level, wide-ranging, multi-tiered cooperation and dialogue platform. There were three main highlights and achievements.\nFirst, it promoted the production, sales, and supply connections of cross-strait agricultural and fishery products. 142 agricultural enterprises from the island, 189 Taiwan-invested agricultural enterprises on the mainland, and more than 1,200 exhibitors from the mainland were invited. Face to face, they negotiated trade cooperation with more than 2,300 purchasers, including JD.com, Alibaba, Yonghui Superstores, and RT-Mart. The scale of the exhibition, the variety of products, and the breadth of exhibitors and buyers all set new records for cross-strait agricultural exhibitions. Over the three-day expo, more than 30,000 visitors came to view and shop, and more than 20 million people placed orders online through livestream platforms “touring the exhibition in the cloud.” By the close of the exhibition, the intended signed amount reached 12.56 billion yuan.\nSecond, it built a platform for cross-strait communication and dialogue. More than 500 people from political, business, agricultural, fishery, and academic circles on both sides of the Strait attended the events. At the opening ceremony, the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Forum, the Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Meeting, and other events, guests discussed and offered suggestions on the integrated development of cross-strait agriculture. Taiwan farmer and businessperson representatives shared stories of starting businesses on the mainland based on their own experiences, and cross-strait youth representatives talked together about their ideals of striving. Sincere exchanges, close communication, and two-way interaction were achieved. Representatives at the meeting said they would encourage more Taiwan farmers and compatriots to come to the mainland to chase, pursue, and realize their dreams.\nThird, it promoted the participation of Taiwan farmers and businesspeople in comprehensive rural revitalization. During this cross-strait agriculture expo, a policy matching event for Taiwan farmers and businesspeople to participate in rural revitalization was specially held. It explained the mainland's financial, land, and other policies supporting agriculture, introduced the preferential treatment for Taiwan compatriots developing agriculture in Fujian, and provided policy guidance addressing the concerns of Taiwan farmers and businesspeople. This further helped and supported Taiwan compatriots to share more of the mainland's development opportunities and market dividends, better integrate into work and life on the mainland, and put down roots to develop. On site, interaction was lively, attracting more and more “first-time visitors,” “second-generation Taiwanese,” and “third-generation Taiwanese” to devote themselves to comprehensive rural revitalization on the mainland and to contribute wisdom and strength to the integrated development of cross-strait agriculture.\nIn addition, from December 7 to 11, the 2023 Zhejiang Agriculture Expo Nantou County Specialty Agricultural Products Sales and Promotion Event was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, with 41 exhibitors from Taiwan participating. The Taiwan farmers and businesspeople who participated brought specialty agricultural products such as tea, coffee, flowers, fruits, and seafood, which were warmly welcomed by Hangzhou citizens. Zhejiang will create more sales platforms for products from Taiwan to enter the Zhejiang market, provide convenient conditions for Taiwan youths and businesspeople to invest in agriculture in Zhejiang, and fully integrate into Zhejiang's rural revitalization and modernization process.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 2023 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year selection, jointly organized by institutions on both sides of the Strait, attracted more than 15 million participants from both sides to vote, and the character “融” (rong, meaning “integrate”) won the highest number of votes. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","A single character, “rong” (融), represents the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. It reflects the plain wishes of people on both sides and the prospects for cross-Strait relations. One character speaks a thousand words, and it reflects the collective will of the people.\nDeepening cross-Strait integrated development benefits both sides of the Strait today and achieves merit for the nation for generations to come. We thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on “promoting integration through exchanges, through benefits, and through emotional bonds.” We formulated and issued, and promoted the implementation of, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.” We have hosted important exchange activities such as the Straits Forum, the Straits Youth Development Forum, the Straits Youth Festival, and the Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month, and invited people from all fields and sectors on the island to visit and exchange. We have further improved systems and policies to enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and provided more platforms and better conditions for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to integrate into the mainland's new development pattern and participate in high-quality development.\nWe hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will join hands to push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, push cross-Strait integrated development to go deeper and more substantively, and share the development dividends of “harmony and joy” in cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587252.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","The National Medical Products Administration recently issued the \"Work Plan on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Promoting Innovative Development of Regulation of Drugs, Medical Devices, and Cosmetics,\" supporting Fujian in trying out pilot measures first in the field of drug regulation. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","To fully implement the Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, the National Medical Products Administration recently issued the Work Plan on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Promoting Innovative Development in the Regulation of Drugs, Medical Devices and Cosmetics (hereinafter the “Work Plan”). Adhering to institutional innovation, serving the people's livelihood and implementing measures in phases, the Work Plan promotes the integrated development of the cross-Strait pharmaceutical industry and ensures the safety of the use of drugs and medical devices.\nThe Work Plan focuses on innovative development in the regulation of drugs, medical devices and cosmetics, and puts forward seven key tasks. Among them, it mentions supporting Fujian in taking the lead and pioneering in exploring the integrated development and innovative inheritance of traditional Chinese medicine across the Taiwan Strait. It supports Taiwan-funded medical institutions in Fujian Province in introducing established proprietary Chinese medicine formulas and experience-based prescriptions of renowned senior traditional Chinese medicine practitioners that are registered in the Taiwan region and whose “curative effects are reliable, distinctive advantages are prominent, and adverse reactions are few.” Such medical institutions may carry out registration of institutional preparations and filing for the preparation of Chinese medicine preparations using traditional processes within Fujian Province, and the human-use experience and history of use of these formulas in the Taiwan region, where they meet requirements, are recognized. Institutional preparations that comply with relevant regulations may be dispensed and used in medical institutions within Fujian Province. Traditional Chinese medicine is a treasure of the Chinese nation and a common asset of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This measure will help the two sides work together to promote the preservation of the core and innovation in traditional Chinese medicine, and its inheritance and development.\nThe Work Plan also proposes that, by giving full play to Fujian's unique advantages in relation to Taiwan and its pioneering and demonstrative role, Fujian will actively explore innovative regulatory service mechanisms for drugs, medical devices and cosmetics. It supports the development of Taiwan-funded drug marketing authorization holders, Taiwan-funded medical device registrants and Taiwan-funded cosmetics registrants within Fujian Province. It supports Fujian in handling filings for the import of first-class medical devices from the Taiwan region, as declared by agents of imported medical devices within the province. It supports registrants of imported medical devices from the Taiwan region in carrying out registration applications for Class III medical devices within the mainland within Fujian Province. It supports Fujian in carrying out regulatory science research on drugs across the Taiwan Strait and in continuously strengthening civil exchanges in the pharmaceutical field across the Strait.\nWe believe that the issuance of the Work Plan will further promote innovative development in the regulation of drugs, medical devices and cosmetics, deepen the integrated development of medical care between Fujian and Taiwan, and help Fujian build a demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development and a first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses on the mainland.\nShenzhen Satellite TV:\nFirst question: This year, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have continued to be lively. Could the spokesperson please introduce the recent exchange activities in all fields across the Taiwan Strait? Second question: Hsiao Bi-khim recently claimed, when asked about cross-Strait issues, that “maintaining the status quo is the greatest common denominator of the international community.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?\nOn the first question: We continue to promote the resumption of cross-Strait exchanges and the normalization of personnel exchanges, which has been welcomed by compatriots on both sides, and exchanges in all fields across the Strait continue to be lively. Today, we would like to report recent exchange activities in Shandong and Guangdong.\nIn Shandong, from November 17 to 18, Liaocheng in Shandong held a Cross-Strait Dance Art Exchange Event, at which more than 60 artists and dance professionals from both sides of the Strait exchanged and shared views on building cross-Strait dance associations and the development of dance art. On November 25, Qingdao in Shandong held the Cross-Strait (Qingdao) Economic, Trade and Cooperation Conference, at which about 200 guests, including Taiwan businesspeople and leaders of Taiwan associations and Taiwan-funded enterprises from various places, gathered to discuss cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and industrial cooperation. From December 9 to 16, Qingdao in Shandong held the “Ink Welcomes the New Year, Sharing Cross-Strait Ties” online calligraphy and painting event linking Qingdao and Taichung fellow-townspeople to welcome the Spring Festival, and the “Heart to Heart, Creating the Future Together” exchange camp for Taiwan university students. About 30 calligraphers and painters from both sides of the Strait engaged in online appreciation and exchange of calligraphy and painting, and 20 Taiwan university students visited Qingdao on site to learn about the city's development and employment and entrepreneurship opportunities.\nIn Guangdong, on November 30, as the grand finals of the 2nd Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao E-Sports League concluded in Shenzhen, the Shenzhen Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month came to a successful close. More than 30 events during the Exchange and Integration Month attracted wide attention from compatriots on both sides of the Strait, with more than 2,000 participants from all walks of life in Taiwan. From December 6 to 9, the grand finals of the 5th “Fun in Guangdong, Fun for All—2023 Cross-Strait Youth Creative Short Film Competition” were held in Chaozhou, Guangdong. The competition was launched in Taiwan in September, and more than 400 youth teams from Taiwan submitted entries. Six teams advanced to the grand finals, presenting in visual form the traditional characteristics of the Chaoshan region and the aesthetic beauty of Lingnan culture in Chaozhou.\nWith so many cross-Strait exchange activities this year, many young people from Taiwan came to the mainland for the first time. They share a common feeling, which can be summed up in three words: “It's different.” They say that what they see on the mainland is different from the information they received in Taiwan. They used to think that mainland people would reject Taiwan people, dislike Taiwan people, and that the mainland was relatively backward, but once they came, they found the mainland to be prosperous, progressive and full of opportunity, and mainland compatriots to be friendly and warm. They hope to come again often and not let negative information from the island limit their imagination. We warmly welcome more compatriots from Taiwan, especially young people from Taiwan, to come to the mainland to take a look, and they will surely gain many unexpected rewards.\nOn the second question: The current state of cross-Strait relations is that there is only one China in the world, the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China are not to be divided. Maintaining the status quo means not allowing “Taiwan independence” separatism to undermine this status quo.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587255.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The Taiwan Ministry of Finance recently announced that starting January 2024, it will stop imposing “anti-dumping duties” on mainland-made footwear, which means island residents may be able to buy cheaper mainland-made footwear products. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We have noted the relevant situation. Cross-Strait economies are highly complementary, and products the mainland exports to Taiwan can effectively meet Taiwan's market demand. Ceasing to levy the “anti-dumping duties” on mainland-made footwear will give Taiwan residents more choices, allowing them to obtain good-quality, inexpensive mainland footwear and receive tangible benefits and preferences.\nHowever, Taiwan's economic authorities still continue to levy “anti-dumping duties” on products such as towels produced in the mainland. Taiwan should treat mainland enterprises fairly and properly handle the relevant issues. Industry on both sides of the Strait should also strengthen communication and consultation to seek solutions satisfactory to both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently clamored that he does not support signing a services trade agreement with the mainland, and said that if the services trade agreement passes, large numbers of mainlanders will enter Taiwan to “steal Taiwanese people’s rice bowls,” which would affect local business. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement was reached by authorized representatives of both sides after multiple rounds of negotiations. After ten years of storms and tempering, more and more people on the island, especially in the industry, have come to recognize that the Cross-Strait Services Trade Agreement is a mutually beneficial, win-win agreement. It helps strengthen cross-Strait service industry cooperation and create more employment opportunities, helps raise the level of cross-Strait service industries and jointly meet the challenges of economic globalization, and helps the economic development of both sides, especially Taiwan’s economy.\nAfter carefully reading the 24 clauses of the Services Trade Agreement, one can see that this agreement will not only not harm the interests of Taiwanese businesses and will not “snatch Taiwanese people’s rice bowls,” but on the contrary will give Taiwanese businesses broad development space and opportunities by further promoting the liberalization and facilitation of cross-Strait services trade. Lai Ching-te deliberately smeared the Services Trade Agreement to pursue the narrow interests of his own party and fabricated groundless “threats.” It is he who “smashes the rice bowls of the Taiwanese people.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that a new batch of custard apple packing plants and orchards in Taitung County, Taiwan, have been registered with the General Administration of Customs, which will create favorable conditions for the import of Taiwan custard apples into the mainland. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","We have consistently upheld the concept that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family.” On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we have made every effort to do practical things, good deeds, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. Since the beginning of this year, we, together with the General Administration of Customs, have actively responded to the wishes of the Kuomintang of China, Taitung County, and other parties for the mainland to resume importing sugar apples from the Taiwan Region. On the basis of a comprehensive assessment, the General Administration of Customs announced on June 20 the resumption of importing sugar apples from the Taiwan Region into the mainland. We have maintained close communication with Taitung County and accelerated the registration and review of sugar apple packing plants and orchards to prepare for the import of sugar apples into the mainland. After careful review by the General Administration of Customs, on December 8, a new batch of Taitung County sugar apple operators, including 34 packing plants and 1263 orchards, were registered. To date, a total of 37 packing plants and 1288 orchards in Taitung County have been registered. These orchards and related operators may sell sugar apples that meet inspection and quarantine requirements to the mainland. Packing plants and orchards that have not yet passed the review may continue to rectify and apply in accordance with the rectification requirements.\nAs long as the relevant side adheres to the “1992 Consensus” and opposes “Taiwan independence,” and complies with relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we are willing to hold talks with relevant parties on the island on supporting the resumption of importing Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland. We are willing to continue upholding the concept that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family,” and to work together with relevant parties on the island to promote the resumption of importing more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, benefiting Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587253.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","U.S. Joint Chiefs of Staff Vice Chairman Grady said that the U.S. Congress could, through a supplementary appropriation budget outside the regular budget, determine that the U.S. Department of Defense can continue to provide security assistance to Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan. May I ask for the spokesperson’s comment?","What calculations do certain US politicians have in listing the Chinese Taiwan region alongside countries in the world that are currently mired in war? Do they intend to follow the same playbook and turn Taiwan into a battlefield engulfed in flames? If war breaks out in the Taiwan Strait due to “Taiwan independence” or the intervention of external forces, and Taiwan becomes a battlefield, the people of Taiwan will only be coerced into becoming “cannon fodder.”\nWe firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. This position is clear and consistent. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming Taiwan, and truly implement the important consensus reached at the China-US leaders' meeting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently proposed the election slogan “Choose the right people, walk the right path.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","I have seen public opinion pointing out that her so-called “right people” refers to “Taiwan independence workers,” and the “right path” refers to the path of “Taiwan independence.” Everyone is clear that “Taiwan independence workers” are “troublemakers,” “peace wreckers,” and “war makers,” and that the path of “Taiwan independence” is an evil path and a dead end. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots, for the sake of their own peace and well-being, will firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587254.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The Director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office, Sun Xiaoya, recently claimed that Taiwan has suffered a serious cyberattack that not only affects people’s daily lives but also attempts to hollow out its “democratic system.” She also falsely accused the mainland of seeking to interfere in Taiwan’s 2024 election. Lai Qingde subsequently echoed this, saying it once again shows that “the United…","Elections in the Taiwan region are purely China's internal affair, and brook no interference from any external force. At the China-US leaders' meeting in San Francisco, the US side made solemn political commitments to the Chinese side on the Taiwan question. US President Biden explicitly stated that the US does not support “Taiwan independence.” The US side should honor its commitments, stop sending erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence,” and stop interfering in elections in the Taiwan region.\nAs an out-and-out “Taiwan independence worker” and a thoroughgoing “troublemaker,” Lai Ching-te feigns deafness and muteness. He does not dare to mention that the US side has clearly stated it does not support “Taiwan independence,” and can only come up with cherry-picked snippets to deceive the public and win votes. We believe the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will not be fooled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587249.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, Teacher Qu Guizhi of Taipei First Girls' High School published a video denouncing the “de-Sinicization” of Taiwan's education curriculum guidelines, which has gained high viewership on both sides of the Strait. Teacher Qu pointed out that Taiwan's so-called “curriculum reform” over the past twenty-odd years has always been carried out under the guiding principle of the “ghost of de-Sinicization,” and…","I have seen this video, and I have also seen many people on the island respond to it. In fact, Teacher Ou has voiced what many teachers, parents, and scholars on the island truly think, and has spoken out with a just voice. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are using every means to promote “de-Sinicization” on the island, attempting to sever the cultural ties between the two sides of the Strait, deceiving Taiwan's people, causing confusion over historical memory and distortion of national identity among Taiwan's younger generation, with harm that will be lasting. Protests and criticism from all sectors of Taiwan have continued.\nIt must be pointed out that no act of “de-Sinicization” can change the Chinese cultural identity and Chinese national identity deeply rooted in Taiwan's society, nor can it sever the historical connections and blood ties between the two sides of the Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, acting recklessly and abandoning their roots, will surely face even stronger opposition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587251.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The results of Taiwan's 2023 character of the year selection were announced. The character “缺” (lack) ranked first among 58 candidate characters, while “蛋” (egg) and “诈” (deceit) ranked second and third. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. Whether it is “shortage” (“缺”) or “fraud” (“诈”), both reflect that Taiwan's ordinary people are very dissatisfied with 2023 and in a very bad mood. Where does the source of this chaos lie? Everyone can see clearly: it is precisely because the DPP authorities, in pursuit of their own private interests, engage only in political infighting and disregard people's livelihood needs, that grassroots people suffer greatly and cry out in distress nonstop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声记者","I would like you to introduce the recent measures taken in various localities to help Taiwan compatriot-invested businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development.","On November 28, Zhuhai in Guangdong Province issued the “Service Guide for the High-Quality Development of Taiwan-Invested Enterprises in Zhuhai.” The “Service Guide” highlights three features. First, it showcases Zhuhai's promising industrial development prospects, systematically introducing new policies and new platforms such as the “4+3” industrial clusters and the “5.0 Industrial New Space.” Second, it presents Zhuhai's strong measures to help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises achieve high-quality development, across five areas: the overall environment, business management, policy support, rule-of-law guarantees, and living and development. Third, it integrates offline services, online business handling mini-programs, online service websites, WeChat official accounts and other service formats, further facilitating Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in integrating into life in Zhuhai. The issuance of the “Service Guide” is a beneficial attempt by localities to innovate service measures and improve and implement policies and measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises. It is intended to create a higher-quality business environment for Taiwan businesspeople and to help Taiwan-invested enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development. We hope Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople will take the issuance of the “Service Guide” as an opportunity to actively take part in Zhuhai-Taiwan economic and trade exchanges and write a new chapter of integrated development for Zhuhai and Taiwan.\nOn December 20, the “Promotion Event for Taiwan Businesses' Investment in the Mainland,” co-hosted by the Economic Affairs Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the Department of Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs of the Ministry of Commerce, the Straits Exchange Association for Economic and Trade, the Straits Economic and Technological Cooperation Center, and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises, will be held in Beijing. Under the guidance of the Economic Affairs Bureau of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the Department of Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs of the Ministry of Commerce, the event invites representatives of local commerce authorities and local Taiwan Affairs Offices, representatives of Taiwan-invested enterprises in various provinces and municipalities with investment intentions, representatives of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Investment Enterprises, and some chief representatives of Taiwan-invested enterprises in Beijing, about 200 people in total. The Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, the General Administration of Customs and other departments will comprehensively introduce policies for the development of small and medium-sized enterprises, measures to facilitate cross-Strait trade, and the investment and business environment on the mainland, as well as the history and achievements of Taiwan businesses' investment on the mainland. Fujian, Chongqing, Guizhou, Jilin and other four provinces and municipalities will present their investment advantages and project needs. Interested Taiwan businesses are welcome to register to attend.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","December 1 marks the 80th anniversary of the publication of the Cairo Declaration. Could you tell us what commemorative activities the mainland held? What is the significance of holding related commemorative activities under the current cross-Strait situation?","On December 1, 1943, the governments of China, the United States, and Britain issued the Cairo Declaration, which clearly stipulates that “all the territories Japan has stolen from China, such as Manchuria, Formosa, and the Pescadores, shall be restored to the Republic of China.” After World War II, the Cairo Declaration provided an important basis in international law for China to recover Taiwan and its affiliated islands, which had been seized and stolen by Japanese militarism. It is an important international legal document recognized throughout the world.\nOn November 30, the Shanghai Institutes for International Studies, together with the Shanghai East Asia Institute, the Shanghai Cross-Strait Relations Research Society, and the Shanghai Taiwan Studies Association, held an academic seminar titled “Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of the Cairo Declaration.” Experts and scholars from relevant mainland universities and research institutions explored in depth the historical and practical significance of the Cairo Declaration. The scholars attending unanimously agreed that the so-called “undetermined status of Taiwan” being clamored for by some forces on the island and internationally is a challenge to the international order established after World War II. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. This has unquestionable historical facts and legal foundations and is also generally recognized by the international community. Any conduct that disregards international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration, and denies or challenges the one-China principle will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231213_12587256.htm"],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","According to reports, an institution on the island recently compiled the top ten public grievance incidents since 2020, more than half of which involve people's livelihood. These include “opening imports of Lai pork,” “vaccine procurement / high-end vaccine controversy,” “egg shortages and imported egg controversy,” “513 major blackout and energy issues,” and “Southeast Asian fraud cases,” among others. What…","There is a scale between heaven and earth, and its weight is the common people. For political gain, the DPP authorities have disregarded the people’s livelihood needs and well-being, which will inevitably provoke the resentment and disdain of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","Recently, at a DPP election rally, Tsai Ing-wen claimed that the 2024 election is not a choice between \"war and peace,\" but that the people of Taiwan must choose \"peace with dignity.\" May the spokesperson comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” means war. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to the well-being of the people. We believe that compatriots in Taiwan will distinguish right from wrong, see through the DPP authorities’ deceptive propaganda and electoral tricks, and make the right choices on matters concerning “peace versus war” and “prosperity versus decline.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","As New Year's Day, the Spring Festival, the winter vacation and other holidays and breaks approach, many Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan students on the mainland are very concerned about flight tickets back to Taiwan. What arrangements have the two sides made for flights during this year's winter vacation and Spring Festival?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. Students, businesspeople and compatriots from Taiwan hope to return home smoothly for the holiday and reunite with their families. We feel for their wishes deeply. Relevant departments on the mainland will, guided by the purpose of serving exchanges between compatriots on both sides and facilitating the return home of Taiwan compatriots, actively make all the preparations for the cross-Strait Spring Festival extra flights. But resolving this issue also requires cooperation from the Taiwan side. We hope the Taiwan side will listen more to the feedback from Taiwan students, businesspeople and compatriots, adopt attitudes and approaches that meet public expectations, and not deliberately set up obstacles that affect the return home and family reunions of the broad mass of Taiwan students, businesspeople and compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Recently the “2023 National Taiwan Affairs Association Chairmen’s Symposium” was held in Beijing. It has been rumored that the Taiwan Affairs Office encouraged Taiwan businesspeople to vote in Taiwan enthusiastically, and the Taiwan side has pointed out that this symposium was an obvious “election interference.” What is your comment on this? Second question: The Mainland Affairs Council has said…","On the first question, it must first be pointed out that now any exchange activities across the Strait are being labeled as “interfering in elections” by the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities and certain forces. This is highly abnormal and is a usual trick of the DPP to deceive voters.\nThe 2023 National Taiwan Business Association Chairmen’s Symposium was held in Beijing on December 7. Taiwan businesspeople from various regions conducted in-depth discussions and exchanges on the theme of “supporting Taiwan businesses and enterprises in integrating into the new development pattern and participating in high-quality development.” Relevant officials from the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Commerce, and other departments, along with relevant experts, introduced at the meeting the relevant policies of the mainland’s comprehensive deepening of reform and expanded high-level opening-up, as well as the latest measures to support the development of Taiwan businesses and enterprises, and answered questions on issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople. Representatives of the attending Taiwan businesspeople shared a consensus: the new development pattern on the mainland is accelerating its formation, high-quality development is being comprehensively promoted, economic development prospects are bright, and opportunities are unprecedented. They called on Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople to actively participate in cross-strait economic and industrial cooperation, to skillfully seize major opportunities such as the Great Western Development and high-quality development under the Belt and Road Initiative, to actively develop domestic markets, and to expand export channels. Broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople have benefited from various policies and measures that enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and have achieved substantial development. They should take a broad view of the situation, uphold justice, and actively participate in the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.\nWe comprehensively implement the important instructions and directives of General Secretary Xi Jinping on Taiwan work and the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, actively expand cross-strait exchanges and contacts, and introduce major measures to deepen cross-strait integrated development, helping Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development. Advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization is a major historic opportunity for Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople to participate in national rejuvenation, and it will open broader space for cross-strait economic cooperation and integrated development. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople will follow the trends of the times and work together to steer cross-strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, contributing to deepening cross-strait integrated development and strengthening the economy of the Chinese nation.\nOn the second question, there has never been any so-called “observation group” from the mainland. The DPP authorities fabricated this out of nothing, concocted false information, and hyped it up extensively, with no purpose other than to smear the mainland, stir up “anti-China” sentiment, and deceive voters.\nOn the third question, we understand that the culture and tourism administrative departments are verifying the specific circumstances.\nOn the fourth question, we actively support cross-strait cultural exchange and cooperation and welcome Taiwan performing artists to develop their careers on the mainland. We hope that Taiwan performing artists will consciously carry forward professional conduct and artistic ethics and establish a good social image.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: KMT candidate Zhao Shaokang said that if elected, he would demand that the mainland allow Taiwan to send military observers to observe military deployments in coastal areas, but he would not agree to the mainland sending military observers to Taiwan. What is your comment on this? Second question: Luo Senchuan, a Taiwanese online writer who privately published banned books in the mainland, was…","First question. I noted related reports that Mr. Zhao first emphasized that Taiwan will not “seek independence.” “Taiwan independence” and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The DPP authorities obstinately hold to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and collude with external forces to continuously engage in provocations to seek “independence.” This is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Our determination to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is unwavering. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the grave danger of “Taiwan independence,” make the right choice between “peace and war” and “prosperity and decline,” help return cross-strait relations to the track of peaceful development, and safeguard their own security and well-being as well as peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond question. According to information obtained from the relevant departments, the defendants involved are suspected of the crime of producing, selling, and disseminating obscene materials for profit. The case is being handled in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","December 15 marks the 15th anniversary of the full launch of the two-way \"Three Links\" across the Taiwan Strait. Over these 15 years, what impact have the \"Three Links\" had on cross-Strait exchanges, and what enlightenment do they offer for promoting the development of cross-Strait relations?","2008 marked a historic turn in cross-Strait relations, opening a new chapter of peaceful development. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) resumed consultations and negotiations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Through the signing of relevant agreements by the two sides, cross-Strait air direct links, sea direct links, and direct postal service were officially implemented, mainland enterprises were able to invest in Taiwan, and the full, direct, two-way “Three Links” that cross-Strait compatriots had long anticipated were realized.\nIn the 15 years since, the cross-Strait “Three Links” have promoted the flow of people, goods, and capital across the Strait, greatly facilitated exchanges between people on both sides, played an important role in advancing the common interests of compatriots on both sides, and the broad masses of Taiwan people have also benefited. This also fully shows that by adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation can continue to deepen, the prospects for cross-Strait relations are broad, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be safeguarded and enhanced.\nRegrettably, the DPP authorities have undermined the foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, disrupted the institutionalization of cross-Strait economic cooperation, and harmed the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people. Only by returning to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait relations be fundamentally improved, the spillover effects of the cross-Strait “Three Links” be continuously expanded, and more people on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan people, be able to enjoy the fruits of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, many restaurants selling sauerkraut fish have appeared on the streets of Taiwan, with people lining up in long queues, and it has been extremely popular. How does the spokesperson view Taiwan residents’ fondness for mainland cuisine?","Taiwan has excellent black carp, grouper, and perch. I believe they would taste very good in sour cabbage fish stew, and it is also very suitable for eating in winter. In the past, Taiwan’s bubble milk tea, braised pork rice, and fried chicken cutlets were very popular on the mainland, and now the mainland’s luosifen, plum blossom cake, sour cabbage fish, and coconut chicken have set off wave after wave of “food fever” in Taiwan. This fully demonstrates that the two sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, customs, and tastes, and the same culinary preferences and cultural tastes. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to join in exchanges of discovering delicious food and discovering good things, and we also welcome more Taiwan friends to come to the mainland to take a look, check in at more local foods, and taste more local specialties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","Media commentator Kuo Cheng-liang on the island recently stated on a political talk show that he does not believe the conditions for “Taiwan independence” exist, and that his own position is increasingly leaning toward peaceful reunification. He also mentioned that even American scholars have openly advised that the possibility of peaceful reunification cannot be ruled out for Taiwan, yet Taiwanese people are…","Reunification is the trend of history and the right path. “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, because achieving unification by peaceful means is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and to the entire nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should seek peace together, safeguard peace together, and share peace together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The mainland’s trade barrier investigation concerning Taiwan will expire on January 12 next year. What is the current progress of the investigation, and what measures might be taken? Second question: In the first 11 months of this year, cross-Strait import and export data declined by about 16%. Against this backdrop, how will the mainland advance the normalization of cross-Strait economic and…","On the first question: As we understand it, the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan on the mainland is proceeding in an orderly manner, and the final conclusions of the investigation will be released in accordance with law and regulations. We support the relevant competent authorities in studying and taking appropriate measures based on the final conclusions of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan and in accordance with relevant regulations.\nOn the second question: Since the beginning of the year, the mainland's economy has been recovering and improving, showing characteristics of strong resilience, great potential, and ample vitality. Economic growth in the first three quarters was 5.2% year-on-year, ranking among the top of the world's major economies. From January to September, cross-Strait trade totaled nearly 200 billion US dollars, maintaining a high level. Cross-Strait economic and trade relations have strong endogenous momentum and enormous room to expand into broader fields and rise to higher levels, and we are very confident about this.\nRealizing the normalization of cross-Strait economic and trade relations is a shared wish of compatriots on both sides and aligns with their common interests. The mainland, in line with the mainstream public opinion among Taiwan compatriots that they want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, has promoted the resumption of cross-Strait direct flight routes and “mini three links” flights, laying a good foundation for normalizing personnel exchanges and regularizing exchanges between the two sides. We issued the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait,” continuing to advance major measures to deepen the integrated development of both sides of the Strait. We have held cross-Strait economic and trade events such as the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, helping Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-invested enterprises integrate into the mainland's new development pattern and achieve high-quality development. We have earnestly implemented preferential measures benefiting Taiwan and its people, such as the “31 measures,” the “26 measures,” and the “22 measures for agriculture and forestry,” and have genuinely worked to solve the difficulties and problems facing Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises. Going forward, we will continue to work hard to advance the normalization of cross-Strait economic and trade relations.\nIn contrast, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have not only failed to take concrete steps to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but have also continually escalated, repeatedly amending rules and setting up barriers, maliciously obstructing and undermining the normal exchange and cooperation of cross-Strait economies and harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We hope that compatriots on both sides will work together to return cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development as soon as possible, realize the normalization of cross-Strait economic and trade relations at an early date, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nOn the third question: As I mentioned just now, the defendant is suspected of the crime of producing, selling, and disseminating obscene materials for profit, and the relevant case is being handled in accordance with law. As for the consultation and contact mechanism between the Straits Exchange Association and the Straits Exchange Foundation, as everyone knows, because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and unilaterally undermine the common political foundation across the Taiwan Strait, the consultation and contact mechanism between the Straits Exchange Association and the Straits Exchange Foundation has been interrupted and is at a standstill.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, American scholars including Ge Laiyi published an article proposing that if Lai Ching-te wins the election, the DPP should freeze the “Taiwan independence party platform.” What is the spokesperson's comment?","Everyone can see that the DPP clings tightly to the “Taiwan independence” party platform and adheres to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence.” Over the past seven years, it has continuously colluded with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” It is the true destroyer of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of turmoil for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and even in the Asia-Pacific region.\nIt must be pointed out that “Taiwan independence” harms the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots and runs counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island that seeks peace, development, exchange and cooperation. The future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national reunification. We believe that Taiwan compatriots will make the right choice at the critical moment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”记者","Tsai Ing-wen recently said that this year Taiwan's target for international tourist arrivals is 6 million visits. Wang Kuo-tsai, head of Taiwan's transportation authority, said that next year, whether or not Mainland tourists come to Taiwan, the target of 12 million visits must be reached. Many operators complain that this is merely a “government achievement” rather than an achievement for operators. For travel…","We have always kept our doors open to and warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. The crux of and obstacle to the current cross-Strait tourism deadlock lies with the DPP authorities. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion and, as soon as possible, fully restore cross-Strait direct flights in the air, direct shipping at sea and the “mini three links,” and promptly lift the ban prohibiting travel agencies on the island from operating group tours to the mainland.\nWe hope that compatriots on both sides will work together to push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development as soon as possible, and to achieve the healthy development of cross-Strait tourism and two-way exchanges at an early date, thereby enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231213_12587241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-12-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, after China criticized the US littoral combat ship “Gifford” for illegally intruding into waters adjacent to Ren’ai Jiao (Second Thomas Shoal), the United States said it will continue to operate in international waters, including the South China Sea and the Taiwan Strait, in accordance with international law. On December 6, a US Navy anti-submarine patrol aircraft transited the Taiwan Strait. What is…","China has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands, including Ren’ai Jiao, and their adjacent waters. The US warship, without authorization from the Chinese government, illegally intruded into waters adjacent to Ren’ai Jiao, seriously damaging China’s sovereignty and security, violating international law and basic norms of international relations, and undermining regional peace and stability. China has consistently respected the navigation and overflight rights that countries enjoy in the South China Sea in accordance with international law, but firmly opposes any action that, in the name of freedom of navigation and overflight, endangers China’s sovereignty and security.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The US should never attempt to challenge China’s firm will to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity at any time. Under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and China’s domestic law, the waters of the Taiwan Strait are respectively China’s internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone, and exclusive economic zone; there is absolutely no so-called “international waters.” International law of the sea also has no such concept as “international waters” at all. The US claim that the Taiwan Strait is “international waters” is intended to manipulate the Taiwan question and create a pretext to threaten China’s sovereignty and security. China firmly opposes this.\nChina once again urges the US to exercise caution in its words and deeds on the Taiwan Strait and South China Sea issues, stop provocations and troublemaking, implement with practical action the important consensus reached by the heads of state of the two countries, and create a favorable atmosphere for the healthy and stable development of military-to-military relations.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16273595.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-12-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japan's National Institute for Defense Studies recently released the 'China Security Strategy Report 2024'. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Reports of this kind from the Japanese side have consistently been based on preconceived positions and harbor sinister intentions. They slander and smear China's legitimate and reasonable national defense and military development. They are highly irresponsible and even less professional, and we firmly oppose them. In recent years, Japan has continuously breached the constraints of its pacifist constitution, sought to develop offensive weapons, and turned back the wheel of history, endangering regional peace and stability and arousing high vigilance and strong concern among neighboring countries and the international community.\nChina firmly adheres to a defensive national defense policy, and the Chinese military has always been a steadfast force for safeguarding world peace. Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves; the Japanese side has no right to make irresponsible remarks about it. We urge the Japanese side to immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop spreading false narratives, stop using the hyping of a “Chinese military threat” as a pretext for its own military expansion and armament, and not further lose the trust of Asian neighbors and the international community.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16273595.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-12-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 15. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on December 15, in response to the final investigation conclusion announced by the Ministry of Commerce that day on the Taiwan trade barrier investigation, that the investigation shows the DPP authorities have unilaterally restricted large numbers of mainland products from entering Taiwan,…","Zhu Fenglian said that we support the relevant competent departments, in light of the final conclusions of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan, in studying and taking corresponding measures in accordance with the relevant regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231215_12587673.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-12-18","Wang Wenbin","The Paper","It’s reported that the US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said on Saturday that the US State Department has approved a USD 300 million sale of life cycle support and equipment to Taiwan for its Command, Control, Communications and Computers, or C4, capabilities. What’s China’s comment?","By announcing another arms sale to China’s Taiwan region, the US has blatantly violated the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. This move seriously undermines China’s sovereignty and security interests, harms peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and sends a wrong message to separatist forces seeking “Taiwan independence”. China deplores and strongly opposes this and has made solemn démarches to the US side.\nThe Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. No matter how many weapons the US provides to the Taiwan region, it will neither change the historic course of China’s reunification, nor weaken the Chinese people’s firm will in safeguarding our national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US to seriously honor its commitment to one-China and not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop arming Taiwan and causing a dangerous trend, stop creating factors that could heighten tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and stop conniving at and supporting the separatists’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” by force. China will and must be reunited. China will take resolute and strong measures to safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity and take countermeasures against relevant companies involved in arms sales to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347659.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231218_11206304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2023-12-19","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that the U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency recently announced a US$300 million arms sale to Taiwan to provide command, control, communications, computer lifecycle support and related equipment. What is your comment on this?","Wu Qian: The US sale of arms to the Taiwan region of China seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué. It seriously damages China's sovereignty and security, seriously threatens peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and sends a wrong signal to ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied and firmly oppose it.\nThe Taiwan question has always been the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. We demand that the US stop arming Taiwan, translate its stated non-support for ‘Taiwan independence’ into concrete action, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, and not go further down the wrong and dangerous path. ‘Using Taiwan to contain China’ is doomed to fail, and ‘seeking independence by force’ is a dead end. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is strengthening its training and combat readiness, resolutely defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/16275274.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16278494.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-12-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council answers reporters' questions\n(December 19, 2023)\nQ: According to reports, 41 village chiefs in Taipei City are accused of traveling to the mainland for tourism, accepting hospitality from the mainland side, and returning to Taiwan to engage in propaganda supporting specific candidates. The Taipei District Prosecutors Office conducted searches and summoned village chiefs for questioning on the grounds of violating the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act.” What is your comment?\nA:\nIn recent period, we have continuously received reports from Taiwan residents and people from all walks of life that when they come to the mainland for normal exchanges and visits, they often face questioning, intimidation, and obstruction by relevant institutions of the DPP authorities, and some have even been framed with fabricated charges and investigated. Personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields between the two sides have been carried out for more than 30 years. The chilling and oppressive atmosphere created by the DPP authorities has caused broad dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents, many of whom question whether the DPP has returned Taiwan to the former “martial law” era.\nWe deeply understand the grievance of Taiwan residents suffering authoritarian repression, and the DPP's reckless actions are unpopular. The trend of cross-Strait exchanges cannot be stopped. No winter can prevent the arrival of spring. The strength of the people will eventually break through artificial obstacles on the road of cross-Strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231219_12588499.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-12-21","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","Reports show that the Chinese leader said Beijing would reunify with Taiwan, but the timing has not yet been decided. Can I get your reaction?","During his meeting with President Biden in San Francisco this November, President Xi Jinping outlined China’s principled position on the Taiwan question. He pointed out that the Taiwan question remains the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. China takes seriously the positive statements made by the United States in the Bali meeting, and the US side should take real actions to honor its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan, and support China’s peaceful reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347662.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231221_11209251.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-12-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 21st dispatch: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on December 21st that the Customs Tariff Commission of the State Council issued an announcement that day deciding to suspend the tariff concessions on some products under the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA). For a long time, the DPP authorities have…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that in June 2010, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides of the Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA). Over the years, the mainland has consistently and earnestly fulfilled its commitments, promoting and ensuring the entry into force and implementation of ECFA, and bringing tangible benefits to relevant enterprises and people on both sides of the Strait, especially in Taiwan. However, before coming to power, the DPP attacked ECFA, and after taking office, it not only failed to take practical measures to remove discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but also grew increasingly brazen in amending rules and setting up obstacles, maliciously obstructing and undermining normal economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. This has seriously hindered the implementation of ECFA, forcing relevant mainland departments to suspend the tariff concessions on some ECFA products. Such issues could have been properly resolved through cross-Strait consultations, but the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” This has undermined the political basis for cross-Strait consultations, making related issues difficult to resolve properly, and compatriots on both sides have suffered greatly as a result. We hope that cross-Strait relations will return to the correct track of peaceful development, and that both sides can, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” consult to resolve all kinds of issues in cross-Strait economic and trade relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231221_12588863.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 21st dispatch: Responding to recent remarks by Lai Ching-te, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 21st that Lai Ching-te's provocative remarks are extremely dangerous and overreaching. They will only bring enormous harm to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, will only push Taiwan toward the brink of war and…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that Lai Ching-te has blatantly peddled the “two-state theory,” advocated “Taiwan independence” separatism, and clamored to “seek independence through force.” This once again proves that he is a stubborn “Taiwan independence worker,” a thoroughgoing “peace wrecker,” and the source of danger of war in the Taiwan Strait. It once again shows that the DPP, for the sake of its own party interests, is willing to tie the people of Taiwan to the war chariot and make them cannon fodder, and once again exposes the true face of Lai, who deceives votes under the pretext of “peace protecting Taiwan.”\nZhu Fenglian stated that “Taiwan independence” means war, and is irreconcilable with peace in the Taiwan Strait and contrary to the interests of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger of “Taiwan independence,” make the right choice between “peace and war” and “prosperity and decline,” promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development, safeguard their own security and well-being, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231221_12589023.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-12-22","Wang Wenbin","NBC","It’s reported that Chinese leader said China will reunify Taiwan with the mainland. While this is a known policy position, does this raising of the Taiwan issue in such a direct manner at the highest level with the United States imply that there is a change in China’s tone or determination on the Taiwan issue, in particular ahead of Taiwan election?","During his meeting with President Biden in San Francisco this November, President Xi Jinping outlined China’s principled position on the Taiwan question. The readout of the meeting was released soon after their discussion. President Xi pointed out that the Taiwan question remains the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. China takes seriously the positive statements made by the United States in the Bali meeting, and the US should match its action with its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop arming Taiwan and support China’s peaceful reunification.\nIt needs to be pointed out that resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. Our position of advancing reunification is consistent, rock-solid and unshakable. China will realize reunification, and this is unstoppable.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347663.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231222_11209870.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2023-12-22","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Top US and China military officials spoke for the first time in more than a year yesterday. Do you have any details to offer and was Taiwan among the topic discussed?","Competent authorities have issued the readout on the video conversation between member of the Central Military Commission (CMC) and Chief of the CMC Joint Staff Department Liu Zhenli and Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Charles Brown at US request. The readout mentioned the Taiwan question, which you may refer to.\nWe hope the US will work with China to implement the important common understanding between the two presidents during their meeting in San Francisco on resuming mil-to-mil communication and exchange and carry out relevant exchange and cooperation on the basis of equality and mutual respect.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347663.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231222_11209870.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-12-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Beijing, December 22, Xinhua News Agency: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 22nd that because grouper imported into the mainland from the Taiwan region repeatedly tested positive for the prohibited drugs malachite green and crystal violet, and oxytetracycline exceeded permitted levels, the General Administration of Customs suspended imports of grouper from…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that as long as the two sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” the two sides are one family, and matters within a family can be easily discussed and resolved. We are willing to work with relevant parties on the island to continue helping restore the import of Taiwan’s agricultural and fishery products into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231222_12589138.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On December 25, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that the relevant local customs authority announced the same day that it would relax the limit on the quantity of Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers may carry on direct routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu, increasing the limit from the current 4 bottles per person to 6 bottles. We welcome and support this.\nTo facilitate travel between the two sides, since 2006 the mainland's customs has relaxed the limit on Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers may carry on direct routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu, increasing it from 2 bottles per person to 4 bottles. In recent years, people in Kinmen and Matsu have strongly called for a further relaxation of the quantity limit. To implement the \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,\" to support accelerated integrated development between Xiamen and Kinmen and deepened integrated development between Fuzhou and Matsu, and to build the \"same-city living circles\" of Xiamen–Kinmen and Fuzhou–Matsu, we have actively responded to the demands of people in Kinmen and Matsu and further relaxed the quantity limit on Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers may carry on direct routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu. We believe this policy will bring more benefits to Taiwan compatriots, especially people in Kinmen and Matsu. Whatever is conducive to deepening cross-Strait integrated development and to enhancing the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, we will do wholeheartedly and with full effort, making good things happen and making real things work well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231225_12589731.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2023-12-26","Mao Ning","China Review News","On December 22 local time, US President Joe Biden signed into law the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024, which contains negative China-related content. What’s China’s comment?","Despite China’s opposition, the US passed and signed into law the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024 that contains negative China-related content. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this and has made serious démarches to the US side.\nThe Act interferes in China’s internal affairs, preaches US military support to Taiwan, and violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. We urge the US to honor the commitment of its leader of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, stop manipulating the Taiwan question and stop endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Act pictures China as a threat, suppresses Chinese companies and limits normal economic, trade and people-to-people exchanges between China and the US, which serves no one’s interest. The US needs to abandon the Cold War mentality and ideological prejudice and create a favorable environment for China-US cooperation in trade and other sectors.\nWe urge the US to work with China to deliver on the important outcome and common understandings of the San Francisco summit. Negative China-related content in the Act should not be implemented. If the US insists on going ahead with it, China will take resolute and strong measures to firmly safeguard its sovereignty, security and development rights and interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347666.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202312/t20231226_11213135.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear journalists, I will moderate today's press conference. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Hou Yu-ih, the Kuomintang’s candidate for Taiwan’s leader, recently released his cross-Strait political platform, including “two major goals,” “three supervisory channels,” and “four main axes of strategic depth,” stating that if elected, he will advance dialogue and consultation, as well as exchanges and cooperation, with the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait mean that the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be enhanced; tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait mean that their interests and well-being will be harmed. From 2008 to 2016, on the basis of adhering to the ‘1992 Consensus’ and opposing ‘Taiwan independence’, both sides across the Strait created a prosperous era of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations, bringing tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, and injecting positive energy into the prosperity and stability of the Asia-Pacific region. But after the DPP authorities came to power in 2016, they stubbornly adhered to the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist position, refused to acknowledge the ‘1992 Consensus’, colluded with external forces to seek ‘independence’ and provoke confrontation, and step by step pushed Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war and disaster, making itself the greatest source of turmoil endangering regional stability.\nAt present, Taiwan stands at a crossroads as to where it is headed. As long as we adhere to the ‘1992 Consensus’ and oppose ‘Taiwan independence’, cross-Strait relations can return to the track of peaceful development, cross-Strait consultation and negotiation can resume, and everything can be discussed and is open to good-faith discussion. We sincerely hope that compatriots on both sides will join hands to jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and create a new chapter of prosperous development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590237.htm"],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te claimed in an interview that if he is elected, “the risk of war across the Strait will be the lowest,” because his path is “the most correct, and also the practice of the international community.” What comments do you have on this?","“Taiwan independence” means war. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, continuously escalating tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait, and step by step pushing Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war and disaster. Many international media outlets consider Taiwan now to be “the most dangerous place on Earth” and say the situation in the Taiwan Strait is “at its most dangerous moment.” Lai Ching-te, a leading figure of the DPP authorities who calls himself a “Taiwan independence worker,” claims that his risk of being elected is the lowest. Do you believe that? Will the people of Taiwan believe it? I think even he himself does not believe it.\nIn addition, I must emphasize that adhering to the one-China principle is the widely shared consensus of the international community. Opposing “Taiwan independence” and safeguarding peace is the right path for humanity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590236.htm"],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The U.S. “FY2024 National Defense Authorization Act,” which contains negative content concerning Taiwan, has been signed into law, and the DPP authorities expressed gratitude. What is your comment?","Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. The US side has insisted on inserting Taiwan-related content into the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024,” openly making remarks on the Taiwan question and brutally interfering in China's internal affairs. This seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and causes serious damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this.\nSome people on the US side say they hope for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but in fact they are accelerating the arming of Taiwan, “handing knives” and “delivering guns and cannons” to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, inciting confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and fanning the flames in the Strait. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the solemn political commitments it made to China on the Taiwan question, to translate its statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions, to refrain from implementing the negative Taiwan-related provisions of the above-mentioned act, to immediately stop arming Taiwan, to stop the conduct of “destroying Taiwan” and “harming Taiwan,” and to stop interfering in Taiwan's elections.\nThe DPP authorities claim that “war is not an option for Taiwan,” yet they are intensifying “relying on the US to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force,” even at the cost of the lives and well-being of the people on the island, and are doing their utmost to cater to the US in turning Taiwan into a “powder keg” and a “minefield island.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “Taiwan independence” means war. No matter how many weapons the DPP authorities obtain from the United States, they cannot shake our firm resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification, and they cannot withstand our strong capability to crush the “Taiwan independence” scheme and safeguard national sovereignty.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590235.htm"],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","On December 18, after a 6.2-magnitude earthquake struck Jishishan County, Gansu Province, people from all walks of life and the general public in Taiwan expressed concern and sympathy and actively provided assistance. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On the evening of December 18, an earthquake of magnitude 6.2 struck Jishishan County, Gansu Province, causing casualties and property losses. After the disaster occurred, Taiwan-related groups and individuals expressed their concern and sympathy to the affected compatriots through various means. Taiwan-invested enterprises and businesses, including the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, Taiwan associations in various localities, the Want Want Group, Shanghai Guanlong Valve Co., Foxconn, Baojian Group, Dongya Machinery, Minth Group, and Pou Chen Group, actively donated money and supplies to the disaster area. According to incomplete statistics, as of December 26, Taiwan-invested enterprises and businesses had donated more than 40 million yuan in money and supplies. This once again fully demonstrates that cross-Strait compatriots are one family, and the bonds of kinship, of blood being thicker than water and of mutual support, cannot be severed or blocked. We express our heartfelt thanks for the concern and assistance extended by Taiwan-related groups and individuals as well as the broad masses of Taiwan-invested enterprises and businesses!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590234.htm"],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Starting January 1, 2024, the extension of the island's compulsory military service period from 4 months to 1 year will officially take effect, applying to Taiwan youth born from 2005 onward. Since this policy was introduced, it has sparked many controversies on the island, along with protests and boycotts by Taiwan youth. Recently, many Taiwan youth have taken to the streets, loudly protesting the actions of the…","After the DPP authorities introduced the \"one-year extension of compulsory military service,\" controversy and criticism have continued without end. The DPP authorities turn a deaf ear and a blind eye to the opposition of the island's public, the worries of Taiwan's young people, and the concerns of these young people's parents. Let us consider why the DPP authorities insist on going their own way and persisting obstinately. Isn't it simply to prepare for war, and to coerce Taiwan's young people into going to the battlefield as cannon fodder for \"Taiwan independence\"!\nRecently, to coordinate with the restoration of compulsory service to one year, the DPP authorities launched the so-called \"Study-and-Service 3+1 Program,\" which received only 5 applications. This fully demonstrates that more and more Taiwan people, especially Taiwan's young people, have come to see clearly that \"Taiwan independence\" means war, and that the DPP authorities' promise that \"young people will not go to the battlefield\" is nothing more than a way to win votes by deception. The DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to manipulate \"using force to seek independence\" will only aggravate tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait, seriously harm the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan, and sacrifice the future of Taiwan's young people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590233.htm"],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","香港“中评社”记者","As the 2024 Taiwan regional elections approach, it is rumored that the DPP authorities will bar mainland Taiwan compatriots from returning to Taiwan to vote, on the grounds that respiratory diseases on the mainland are severe. What is your comment?","On the 24th, the National Health Commission held a press conference to introduce the prevention and treatment of winter respiratory diseases. Data show that on December 22, the total number of outpatient and emergency respiratory disease visits at medical institutions at Grade II and above across the country was 8.2% lower than the same period last week and 30.02% lower than the peak, with the overall trend continuing to fluctuate downward.\nThe return of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland to Taiwan to vote is their right. If the DPP authorities dare to exploit this issue and act rashly by depriving Taiwan compatriots on the mainland of their right to vote, it will only make the world see more clearly their authoritarian and undemocratic true face, and it will only be spurned by the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Regarding the mainland’s release of the investigation results on trade barriers against Taiwan, Lai Ching-te said that the mainland’s finding is one-sided, and that its release right after Kuomintang Vice Chairman Xia Li-yan arrived on the mainland for a visit is “election interference” behavior. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","It is understood that KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan, at the invitation of Taiwanese business associations in several places, led a delegation from December 13 to 22 to Sichuan, Jiangxi, Guangdong, Fujian, Chongqing and other places to attend relevant activities of local Taiwanese associations. Lai Ching-te forcibly linked this matter to the release of the trade barrier investigation results, which is nothing more than an attempt to shirk responsibility and confuse the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","台湾联合报记者","The first question: The mainland recently announced the suspension of ECFA tariff concessions on 12 petrochemical products from Taiwan. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council called this political manipulation aimed at “interfering in the elections.” If the competent authorities on both sides of the Strait continue not to hold consultations on this matter, and Taiwan does not adjust its trade restriction measures,…","On the first question: the Straits Exchange Framework Agreement (ECFA) was signed and implemented on the common political basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" Any issues related to ECFA can be properly resolved through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" stance and refuse to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations, which is the fundamental reason why ECFA-related issues are difficult to resolve. At the same time, the Customs Tariff Commission of the State Council also clearly stated in its December 21 announcement that it hopes the authorities in Taiwan will take effective measures to lift trade restrictions on the mainland.\nIf the DPP authorities persist in their obstinate course, continue to stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" stance, and refuse to repent, we support relevant departments in taking further measures in accordance with regulations.\nOn the second question: \"Taiwan independence\" means war, which is the shared view of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the extreme harmfulness of \"Taiwan independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","The Customs Tariff Commission of the State Council recently issued an announcement suspending tariff concessions on some products under the ECFA. Island industry associations are worried that more such measures will follow and hope that both sides can sit down and talk properly. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Regarding the relevant mainland authorities' suspension of tariff concessions under ECFA on some products, I have already answered this question earlier. If the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on their \"Taiwan independence\" position and refuse to repent, we support the relevant authorities in taking further measures in accordance with regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","According to reports, after 41 village chiefs in Taipei were summoned for questioning, relevant departments in Kaohsiung recently also indicted 18 incumbent village chiefs, on the grounds that they accepted mainland funding to help specific candidates campaign. While cross-Strait exchanges have been resuming briskly, the DPP authorities keep investigating grassroots village chiefs who visited the mainland for…","My colleague Zhu Fenglian has already answered the reporters' question on this matter. I will add a supplementary response to your question. What you mentioned reminds me of an ancient saying and an ancient poem. Everyone here should understand them, though young people in Taiwan who have been poisoned by the “de-Sinicized curricula,” such as the “108 Curriculum Guidelines,” may not have heard of them. The ancient saying is: “If one wants to charge someone with a crime, one will never lack excuses.” Grassroots people in Taiwan, including village chiefs, have engaged in exchanges and visits to the mainland for many years. Yet now they are occasionally subjected to questioning, intimidation and obstruction by relevant DPP authority agencies, and some have even been framed with charges and investigated. Is the DPP authority trying to intimidate grassroots people by shouting and killing, acting so viciously? Is it creating a “green terror”? We understand the grievances of Taiwan people suffering from authoritarian suppression, and we firmly believe that the trend of cross-Strait exchanges cannot be stopped. As the famous poem “Guiyuan Pu” by Yang Wanli, a poet of the Song dynasty, says: “Ten thousand mountains will not let one stream run free, / They block it, so the sound of the stream roars day and night. / When it reaches the foot of the mountains ahead, / The mighty stream emerges before the village.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Two questions. First, Lai Ching-te said in a recent interview that “opposition parties” playing the “war card” in elections is cooperating with the mainland’s “big external propaganda.” He also said, “Hong Kong was forced to walk into mainland China and lost the whole world; Taiwan must not take the backward path of pro-China.” What response does the Taiwan Affairs Office have? Second, the Tariff Commission of…","On the first question: Hong Kong's return to the motherland opened a new chapter in Hong Kong's history. The practice of \"one country, two systems\" has achieved success in Hong Kong that is recognized around the world. Hong Kong has now emerged from the pandemic and achieved overall recovery. It is maintaining its unique status and advantages, consolidating and enhancing its positions as an international financial center, shipping center and trade center, and advancing toward a new milestone in the journey from good governance to prosperity. It can be said that the \"Pearl of the Orient\" retains its splendor and, with strong support from the country, shines with an even more dazzling light. Lai Qingde, driven by his nature of seeking \"Taiwan independence,\" disregards the facts, smears Hong Kong, and attempts to win votes by deceit. This despicable trick is being seen through by more and more Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the second question: In June 2010, on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus,\" the two sides of the Taiwan Strait signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA). Before the DPP took office, it attacked ECFA. After taking office, it not only refused to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" but also colluded with external forces to pursue \"independence\" and provoke confrontation, pushing Taiwan toward the danger of war. It also escalated discriminatory trade restriction policies against the mainland, seeking to enjoy the benefits of ECFA while violating ECFA and relevant WTO rules. As a result, the relevant mainland authorities had to suspend the tariff concessions on some ECFA products.\nThe relevant authorities' decision to suspend tariff concessions on some ECFA products is reasonable and lawful, well-founded and measured, and is a normal economic act. In the face of the facts, the DPP authorities' distorted claims collapse on their own, and the so-called claim that the mainland is \"interfering in Taiwan's elections with a two-handed policy\" is even less tenable. The DPP authorities' repeated manipulation of these two tactics will only make the compatriots on both sides of the Strait see ever more clearly their self-interest, see that they lack sincerity in improving cross-Strait relations, and see that they have neither the intention nor the capability to solve the vital interests of the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","With the Spring Festival approaching, what assistance has the mainland side provided to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses returning to Taiwan for the New Year?","Chinese people have a longstanding tradition of family reunions during traditional festivals. To meet the needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded businesspeople returning home for the Lunar New Year, airlines operating cross-Strait routes have launched preferential group-purchase ticket plans, and local Taiwan Affairs Offices and Taiwan associations will also provide timely services and assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","A promotional campaign for Taiwan investment in the mainland was held in Beijing recently. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","On December 20, the “Taiwan Business Investment in the Mainland Promotion Event” was held in Beijing. Responsible officials from relevant bureaus of the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Commerce and other departments, along with experts and scholars from relevant research institutions, explained at the meeting the policies and measures on attracting foreign investment in the mainland, deepening integrated development between Fujian and Taiwan, benefiting Taiwan compatriots, and supporting the development of small and medium-sized enterprises. Responsible persons from commerce departments of some provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, along with enterprise representatives, promoted their investment environments on site, providing feasible paths to help Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development. Over 140 Taiwan-invested enterprise representatives, about 240 people in total, attended the event. Attending Taiwan businesspeople generally said that the event was novel in form and rich in content, that the timely and thorough promotion of the relevant policies was exactly what they needed, that it played an important role in further strengthening their confidence in investing and boosting their confidence in operations, and that it made them clearer about their next investment plans on the mainland.\nThis year, the mainland's economy has been steadily improving, becoming the most important engine of world economic growth. We will, as always, share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, increase policy support, promote high-level opening up, optimize the investment environment related to Taiwan, create more platforms and provide more opportunities for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development, so that the achievements of cross-Strait integrated development benefit Taiwan compatriots to a greater extent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Today is the last regular press conference of 2023. I would like the spokesperson to comment on cross-Strait relations over the year that is ending. Also, what is your outlook for the development of cross-Strait relations in 2024?","Once again, as the year draws to a close, thank you, media friends, for your attention to and support of cross-Strait affairs and the press briefing work of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office over the past year. As is customary, at the first press conference of the new year, we will review the exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait in 2023 and look ahead to cross-Strait relations in the new year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","This year marks the 45th anniversary of reform and opening up and the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative. How do you evaluate the role played by Taiwan businesspeople working on the mainland in reform and opening up and in Belt and Road construction?","Taiwan businesspeople are participants in and beneficiaries of the mainland's reform and opening up. Many Taiwan enterprises, keeping pace with reform and opening up, have grown from small to large and from weak to strong. They have made important contributions to the mainland's economic and social development, to promoting cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, to enhancing the welfare of compatriots on both sides, and to advancing the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nIn recent years, we have taken cross-Strait integrated development as our focus, encouraged and supported Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises in participating in the implementation of major national development strategies, and actively supported their participation in the Belt and Road Initiative, achieving positive results in trade, industrial cooperation, park construction, and other areas. We hope that Taiwan businesspeople will seize the major historic opportunity of comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization, actively participate in major national strategies and the joint construction of the Belt and Road Initiative, and achieve new and greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Following the release and implementation of the \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,\" relevant departments have accelerated the implementation and advancement of the work. Could the spokesperson introduce the progress of measures in…","Since the release of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” the rule-of-law departments, including the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice, have thoroughly implemented the spirit of the document, actively promoted it, taken initiative, and strengthened policy guidance and support. Fujian Province has strengthened primary responsibility, innovated and improved working mechanisms, and jointly promoted the effective implementation of the rule-of-law measures in the “Opinions.”\nRegarding expanding the scope of practice for Taiwan residents as lawyers, the Ministry of Justice actively implemented the spirit of the document, jointly conducted research with the Supreme People's Court, held discussions and exchanges with Taiwan resident lawyers and Taiwan young legal professionals, fully heard opinions and suggestions, accelerated the work of expanding the scope of practice for Taiwan resident lawyers, and continued to improve policies for opening legal services to Taiwan.\nRegarding establishing business institutions for Taiwan commercial and civil arbitration, the Fujian Provincial Department of Justice issued on December 20 the “Registration and Management Measures for Establishing Business Institutions in Xiamen by Taiwan Arbitration Institutions,” which allows Taiwan commercial and civil arbitration institutions to establish business institutions in Xiamen and conduct arbitration business involving Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan as well as foreign-related matters for civil and commercial disputes arising in commercial, maritime, intellectual property, investment and other fields, and clearly specifies matters such as application conditions and acceptance and registration procedures. The “Measures” take effect on January 1, 2024.\nRegarding procuratorial work, the Supreme People's Procuratorate guided the Fujian Provincial Procuratorate to take the lead in issuing several measures for procuratorial organs to implement the “Opinions,” further creating a favorable rule-of-law environment and institutional arrangements and service measures that provide convenience to the people through judicial services. It deepened the standardized reform of compliance for Taiwan-related companies involved in cases, and promoted a rule-of-law environment for attracting businesses and benefiting enterprises in accordance with the law. At present, procuratorial organs in Fujian, Zhejiang, Jiangsu and other places have all handled successful compliance cases for Taiwan companies. Procuratorial organs in Zhangzhou have actively innovated their working mechanisms and took the lead in exploring a “one office, multiple roles” system for Taiwan-related procuratorial work. Leveraging the Taiwan-related procuratorial liaison offices set up in Zhangzhou, where Taiwan compatriots live and Taiwan companies are concentrated, they further explored appointing Taiwan compatriots as procuratorial liaison officers, hearing officers, public interest litigation observers and other “multiple roles,” and implemented fixed-point reception, regular circuit visits and targeted services for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies. They also built a rule-of-law publicity base for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies in the Zhangzhou Taiwanese Investment Zone, using the power of the rule of law to safeguard the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies and help advance cross-strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS记者","First question: Recently, Chao Shao-kang wrote that the KMT does not identify with communism, has never been “pro-Communist,” and will absolutely not promote unification negotiations during his term, as there are no conditions for unification across the Taiwan Strait today. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?\nSecond question: It has been rumored that a Taiwanese Yiguandao believer was detained after…","First question: We hope that relevant people on the island will say more things that are conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and do more things that enhance mutual trust and understanding across the Strait. Peaceful reunification means equal consultation and joint discussion toward unification. Only when dialogue replaces confrontation, cooperation replaces strife, and win-win outcomes replace zero-sum games can cross-Strait relations advance steadily and far, and the long-standing political differences between the two sides be gradually resolved. The motherland will eventually be reunified, and reunification will certainly happen. We sincerely hope that all Taiwan compatriots will pursue unification just as they pursue their life's happiness, and actively participate in the righteous cause of advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland.\nSecond question: I am not aware of the situation you mentioned. We have consistently supported normal religious exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council's remarks on this are nothing more than an attempt to obstruct normal exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Under ECFA, there are related products in petrochemicals, steel, textiles, and machinery. Tariff concessions for the petrochemical portion have already been suspended. Outside observers are concerned about whether steel and chemical fiber products will be included in the next wave of the list. What is your comment? Second question: We note that the mainland side first suspended part of the ECFA…","On the first question, the DPP authorities stubbornly cling to the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations. This is the fundamental reason why ECFA-related issues are difficult to resolve. If the DPP authorities insist on their own course, persist in the “Taiwan independence” position, and refuse to repent, we support the relevant departments in taking further measures in accordance with regulations.\nOn the second question, regarding the suspension of tariff concessions on some products under ECFA, I already gave a very detailed answer just now. The investigation into Taiwan's trade barriers has clear facts and a reasonable basis, and the measures the relevant departments took based on the investigation results are well-founded and appropriately calibrated. The resumption of imports of grouper from Taiwan was taken in keeping with our philosophy that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” on the basis of a comprehensive assessment of the rectification measures taken by Taiwan's agricultural and fishery operators. It reflects our consistent respect for, care for, and benefit to Taiwan compatriots, and it also reflects our attention to the demands and interests of grassroots people, including Taiwan's farmers and fishermen.\nAs for whether Taiwanese businesses' investment in the mainland will be affected, the numbers speak for themselves. From January to November this year, the number of newly established Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland increased by 26.8% year on year, and the actual amount of Taiwan capital utilized increased by 39.9% year on year. This fully demonstrates that the bright prospects for cross-Strait economic exchanges, cooperation and integrated development have not changed, that Taiwanese businesses' determination to invest in the mainland has not changed, and that the mainland remains the best destination for Taiwanese investment.\nWhether the mainland's economic prospects are promising is something Taiwanese businesspeople understand best, and their investment data is the most convincing evidence. In advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization, Taiwanese businesses and enterprises will have more opportunities and a larger stage for development, and they will certainly continue to achieve greater and better development, as they always have.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","We have noted that \"Taiwan Studies,\" sponsored by the Taiwan Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, was officially launched recently. It is the mainland's first English-language academic journal on Taiwan-related matters. May I ask whether the spokesperson has any relevant knowledge of this journal, and what is your assessment of its significance?","The international community, especially many ordinary people abroad, still have a very limited understanding of the historical context and legal facts of the Taiwan question, and some even hold mistaken perceptions. In view of this, the Taiwan Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences has launched the English-language academic quarterly “China Taiwan Studies” on the basis of the authoritative academic journal “Taiwan Studies.” I believe that the launch of the English quarterly will help us explain the Chinese government's policy toward Taiwan to the international community in English in a more comprehensive, accurate, and clear manner. It will also help the international community better understand the origins and current status of the Taiwan question, and better understand and comprehend the Chinese government's policy toward Taiwan, so that they will more actively understand and support the Chinese government and the Chinese people in their just cause of resolving the Taiwan question and completing national reunification.\nToday's press conference is now concluded. As the new year approaches, I thank the media reporters for their attention to and coverage of the work of the Taiwan Affairs Office press conferences over the past year. I also wish all the reporter friends a happy new year and all the best in everything. And I wish our Taiwan compatriots, elder brothers and sisters, a happy new year and good fortune! (In Hokkien)","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202312/t20231227_12590230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2023-12-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","At the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office on December 27, a reporter asked: According to reports, after 41 Taipei village chiefs were summoned for questioning, relevant departments in Kaohsiung recently also listed 18 incumbent village chiefs as defendants on the grounds that they accepted mainland funding to help specific candidates campaign. Amid the restoration of lively cross-Strait exchanges, the DPP authorities keep investigating grassroots village chiefs who visit and exchange on the mainland on suspicion of violating the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” and other grounds. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?\nChen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions, saying that what you mentioned reminds me of an ancient saying and an ancient poem. The ancient saying is “If one wants to accuse someone of a crime, one will never lack excuses.” Grassroots people in Taiwan, including village chiefs, have been coming to the mainland for exchanges and visits for many years, yet now they are from time to time subjected to interrogation, intimidation, and obstruction by relevant DPP authorities, and some have even had crimes fabricated against them and been investigated. Is the DPP authorities shouting and killing like this, acting so viciously, meant to intimidate grassroots people? Is it creating “green terror”? We understand the grievance of the people of Taiwan suffering from authoritarian suppression, and we firmly believe the trend of cross-Strait exchanges cannot be stopped. As the Song dynasty poet Yang Wanli wrote in his famous poem “Guiyuan Pu”: “Ten thousand mountains do not allow a single stream to run, yet they block it, and the sound of the stream roars day and night. Once it reaches the front where the mountain foot ends, the majestic stream flows out into the village ahead.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231227_12590232.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2023-12-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","US media recently reported that Taiwan will send about 600 military personnel to the United States to receive training on weapons Taiwan has purchased but not yet received. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The US side’s development of military ties with the Taiwan region seriously violates the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously undermines China’s sovereignty and security, seriously damages peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the US side to pull back from the brink, stop the dangerous act of arming Taiwan, and fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete action. Those who play with fire will end up burning themselves. We warn the DPP authorities that their attempt to rely on external forces to “seek independence through force” will ultimately end in failure.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16276896.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-12-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","","The year 2023 marks the first year for fully implementing the guiding principles laid down at the 20th CPC National Congress. On military diplomacy, we acted on Xi Jinping Thought on Strengthening the Military and Xi Jinping Thought on Diplomacy, followed the guidance of head-of-state diplomacy, took high-level exchanges as important means, focused on practical cooperation and gave emphasis to multilateral platforms. We have broken new ground, forged ahead with enterprise and fortitude, enhanced the quality and efficiency of international military cooperation and achieve high-quality development.\nFirst, military diplomacy served the overall political and diplomatic objectives of China.\nUnder the strategic guidance of head-of-state diplomacy, leaders of the Central Military Commission (CMC) had strategic communication with defense and military leaders of Russia, the United States, Vietnam, Cambodia, Pakistan, South Africa, etc., and deepened bilateral strategic cooperation. The Chinese military enhanced consultation and dialogue and expanded practical cooperation with relevant militaries to put into practice the achievements of head-of-state diplomacy.\nSecond, military diplomacy resolutely safeguarded national sovereignty, security and development interests.\nIn response to the negative and wrong rhetoric and infringements and provocations made by certain countries on the Taiwan question and the South China Sea issue, while taking actions to protect our rights in accordance with laws and regulations, the Chinese military also made diplomatic representations, and timely refuted, warned and exposed the wrongdoings and negative moves of relevant countries, and made clear China’s positions through MND spokesperson and the media.\nThirdly, we have expanded foreign-related military operations.\nThe PLA organized and conducted 34 joint training, exercises and international military games including the China-Russia “Beibu Unity-2023” joint exercise, the “Aman youyi-2023” joint exercise with southeast Asian countries, the China-Cambodia “Golden Dragon 2023” joint exercise, the China-Laos “Friendship Shield-2023” joint exercise. Through expanded bilateral and multilateral exercises and training, the PLA has deepened mutual trust and cooperation with the militaries of relevant countries, and played a positive role in maintaining regional stability.\nFourthly, we have made innovative efforts in multilateral diplomacy.\nThe tenth Beijing Xiangshan Forum and the third China-Africa Peace and Security Forum hosted by China were widely attended and welcomed. We attended multilateral events including the Shangri-La dialogue, the Defense Ministers' Meeting of the Member States of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization, the ASEAN Defense Ministers Meeting Plus (ADMM+), and actively introduced major initiatives such as the Global Security Initiative and promoted international consensus for peace and cooperation.\nFifthly, we have contributed to building a community with a shared future for mankind.\nThe PLAN Ark Peace hospital ship visited Kiribati, Tonga, Vanuatu, Solomon Islands, and Timor-Leste. The Chinese military medical expert teams continued to work in Zambia, Cambodia and Laos, and provided medical service to the local people. PLA Air Force Y-20 transport aircraft carried out humanitarian relief missions to Afghanistan and Nepal. PLA Navy vessels rushed to Sudan to evacuate Chinese nationals. The Chinese military also actively participated in UN peacekeeping and vessel protection operations, consistently providing public security goods to the international community.\nEmbracing the world for peace, the Chinese military will always follow the guidance of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, and stay committed to expanding and deepening relations with foreign militaries, strengthening practical exchanges and cooperation, and making due contributions to world peace and common development.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16276902.html","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2023-12-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The election of the leader of the Taiwan region will be held in January next year. Taiwan's defense authorities said that Taiwan's military will remain highly alert during the election period, closely monitor the movements of the PLA, and respond prudently. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities deliberately hype the so-called “mainland military threat” and stir up a tense atmosphere, entirely to seek electoral gain. As for the so-called movements of the Taiwan military, the PLA has them fully under control. We will, as always, take all necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16276906.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2023-12-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","","The US Act makes groundless hypes about the so-called “China military threat”, grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, and severely harms China’s national sovereignty, security and development interests. The Chinese military strongly deplores and firmly opposes to that.\nThe US military expenditure tops the world and is larger than those of the next nine countries combined, accounting for 40% of the total global military expenditure. On the one hand, the US is accelerating its military development, intensifying military deployment in the Asia-Pacific, strengthening bilateral military alliance, and piecing together AUKUS and QUAD. On the other hand, it is making an issue of China, hyping up the so-called“China military threat” out of thin air. Such manipulations intensify block confrontation and arms race and cause a severe impact on the current international security system and global governance system. We urge the US to abandon the out-dated security vision and zero-sum cold war mentality, view China and China’s military development in an objective and rational light, instead of being obsessed with the pursuit for hegemony.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any country to have official and military contact with Taiwan in any form. The US is manipulating the Taiwan question in various forms, which is a very dangerous gamble. We urge the US to fully realize the severe harm of the China-related content in the NDAA, stop arming Taiwan under any excuses and by any means, stop its provocations by using Taiwan to contain China, and take concrete actions to maintain regional peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16276907.html","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2023-12-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's defense authorities recently said that since December of this year, several Chinese mainland sounding balloons have flown across the \"median line of the Taiwan Strait.\" The release of balloons by the mainland ahead of the election of Taiwan's leader has led outside observers to speculate. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Regarding the balloon incident, please check with the competent authorities.\nTaiwan is part of China, and there is absolutely no so-called “median line of the Strait.” The DPP authorities hyping so-called “mainland election interference” is merely their habitual election tactic, aimed at stirring up confrontation and attempting to deceive votes. This old trick has been seen through by more and more Taiwan people.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16276912.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2023-12-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Answers Reporters' Questions\n(December 30, 2023)\nQuestion:\nThe 2024 Taiwan regional leader candidates' televised debate was held on the 30th. At the debate, Lai Ching-te, the DPP candidate, claimed \"Taiwan's sovereignty is independent\"; distorted the \"1992 Consensus\" and clamored that the two sides \"are not subordinate to each other\"; slandered the mainland as the \"greatest threat to Taiwan's survival\" and declared that he would \"strengthen national defense\" and that Taiwan's people should \"unite as one to face the threat from China\"; and smeared the cross-Strait Service Trade Agreement as something that \"would affect all trades and industries and also cause unrest in Taiwan's society,\" among other things. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?\nAnswer:\nAt the debate on the 30th, Lai Ching-te promoted \"Taiwan independence\" fallacies, peddled the \"two-state theory,\" slandered and attacked the mainland, clamored to \"seek independence through force,\" and his words were full of confrontational thinking. This once again exposed his true colors as a stubborn \"Taiwan independence worker,\" a \"destroyer of cross-Strait peace,\" and a \"creator of military danger and peril in the Taiwan Strait.\"\nSince taking office in 2016, the DPP authorities have refused to acknowledge the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" pursued a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist line, engaged in provocations aimed at independence, arbitrarily undermined the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, brutally obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and continuously pushed up tensions and instability in the Taiwan Strait. They are the biggest source of turmoil that has plunged Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war and peril, and the chief culprits for the serious obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and the serious damage to the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. As the leading figure of the DPP authorities and the current DPP chairman, Lai Ching-te cannot escape responsibility for this.\nI solemnly warn Lai Ching-te that \"Taiwan independence\" and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Our actions opposing the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist scheme are resolute and forceful; our ability to crush \"Taiwan independence\" actions and safeguard national sovereignty is invincible; and our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is unwavering.\nThere is only one China in the world; the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will not tolerate division. This is the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. As long as we uphold the \"1992 Consensus\" and oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" cross-Strait relations can return to the right track of peaceful development, cross-Strait consultations and negotiations can resume, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation can proceed smoothly, and compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, can enjoy good days of peace, tranquility and prosperity. I sincerely hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme harm of \"Taiwan independence\" and the danger of Lai Ching-te undermining peace in the Taiwan Strait and stirring up confrontation between the two sides, make the right choice between \"peace and war\" and \"prosperity and decline,\" push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being, and jointly create a new situation of prosperity and development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202312/t20231230_12590800.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-01","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answers reporters' questions\n(January 1, 2024)\nQuestion:\nOn January 1, 2024, Tsai Ing-wen delivered her last New Year's address during her term, reviewing her administration's achievements over eight years in areas such as reform, economic development, strengthening “national defense,” and cross-Strait relations. On cross-Strait relations, she claimed to “not provoke and not submit,” hoped that cross-Strait exchanges would quickly resume in a healthy and orderly way, and sought a long-term path of stable peaceful coexistence across the Strait based on “peace, parity, democracy, and dialogue,” and so on. What is your comment on this?\nAnswer:\nSince 2016, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have obstinately adhered to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refused to acknowledge the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” fabricated and peddled the “two-state theory,” colluded with external forces to plot “independence” and provoke confrontation, arbitrarily undermined the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, brutally obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and continuously pushed up tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. The so-called “Tsai Ing-wen line” is the “Taiwan independence” line, a line of confrontation, and a line that harms Taiwan. It is the greatest source of chaos that has brought Taiwan to the brink of war and disaster, damaged the interests of the public, and endangered regional stability.\nTsai Ing-wen says in words that she wants to “maintain the status quo” and hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, but in reality she has stepped up “seeking independence through armed force” and “seeking independence by relying on external powers,” pushed “de-Sinicization,” vigorously promoted “cultural Taiwan independence” and “decoupling and breaking supply chains,” seriously damaged the interests of compatriots in Taiwan, and brought enormous harm to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” is irreconcilable with peace in the Taiwan Strait and runs counter to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Continuing the “Tsai Ing-wen line,” taking the wrong path of provocation to seek independence and the old road of cross-Strait confrontation, will only take Taiwan further from peace and prosperity and closer to war and decline. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of the Democratic Progressive Party's line and policies, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence,” make the right choice at the crossroads of where to go, push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240101_12591023.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua, Beijing, January 4 — TAO spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on the 4th, saying: Attacking and smearing the mainland is a habitual tactic of the DPP in island elections. Elections are meant to be a concentrated review of political parties and candidates, and those who are questioned should prove their innocence or admit their mistakes. However, many DPP politicians lack personal integrity and their words and conduct are improper. Once their misdeeds, such as corruption, graft, or moral degeneration, are exposed, they habitually frame others and shift blame, trying to use fabricated claims and hype about mainland “interference in the election” to cover up their disgraceful behavior and divert attention. Such “dirty tricks” and bad strategies, when used too often, will only make people laugh and will not fool the Taiwan public.\nA reporter asked: DPP Legislative Yuan candidate Lo Chih-cheng was exposed in leaked private nude selfie videos, and Lo claimed that “overseas cyber troops are manipulating and interfering in the election.” On the 3rd, Lai Ching-te said that this matter shows that “China will stop at nothing to interfere in this election.” What is your comment on this? Chen Binhua made the above remarks in answering this question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240104_12591656.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-01-08","Mao Ning","China News Service","The US State Department on January 6 released the Joint Statement on the Trilateral US-Japan-ROK Indo-Pacific Dialogue, expressing their concerns over China’s maritime claims in the South China Sea and escalatory behavior, and saying that they will continue their trilateral maritime security and law enforcement cooperation in accordance with international law. The three countries also reaffirmed the importance of…","China noted the US-Japan-ROK dialogue and their joint statement. We express serious concerns about the statement’s rhetoric on China. We firmly oppose relevant countries’ attempt to cobble together exclusionary groupings in the name of cooperation, grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs, attack and smear China and stoke confrontation and antagonism.\nThe situation in the South China Sea is generally stable. China is committed to safeguarding our own territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, while properly managing differences with countries directly concerned through dialogue and consultation. Certain non-regional country has sought to flex muscles and incite confrontation in the South China Sea, which is not conducive to peace and stability in the region.\nI want to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affairs that brooks no foreign interference. The key to keeping the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable lies in upholding the one-China principle and firmly opposing separatist moves toward “Taiwan independence”.\nThe Asia-Pacific is a pacesetter of peace and development, not a chessboard for geopolitical contests. We urge relevant parties to earnestly respect regional countries’ effort for peace and stability, abandon the Cold War mentality, stop creating bloc confrontation and stop fueling tensions in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347674.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240108_11219687.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-08","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwanese officials said three Chinese balloons detected flying over the Taiwan Strait on Sunday threatened aviation safety. Can the Foreign Ministry offer assurance that Chinese balloons flying over the Taiwan Strait are not a threat to international civil aviation?","I’m not aware of the specifics you mentioned and it’s not related to China’s foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347674.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240108_11219687.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-09","Mao Ning","AFP","Elections will be held in the Taiwan region this Saturday. Lai Ching-te just now said that the Chinese mainland is resorting to all means to interfere with this election. What’s your comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Elections in the Taiwan region are China’s internal affairs. Questions on those elections are not related to China’s foreign affairs. I’d refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council regarding your question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347675.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240109_11220528.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-10","Mao Ning","AFP","China successfully launched the Einstein probe satellite and sent it into orbit yesterday. And that launch appeared to trigger Taiwan authorities to issue an emergency alert, which caused quite a lot of concerns among the public in Taiwan. Did the Chinese side know in advance that the launch would trigger such an alert and was it a deliberate time to coincide with the last few days of Taiwan election campaign?","It’s not related to China’s foreign affairs. It is pretty clear what the DPP authorities is trying to do by misleading the public and sowing panic.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240110_11221227.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-10","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan’s de facto “Ambassador to the United States” has met with the US House of Representatives Speaker Mike Johnson on Tuesday. Does China have any comment on this meeting?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. China firmly opposes the US having any form of official contact with the Taiwan region. The US needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, stop official contact with the Taiwan region, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and refrain from interfering in elections in the Taiwan region in any form. The DPP authorities’ attempt to solicit support from the US and other countries for “Taiwan independence” will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240110_11221227.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-11","Mao Ning","China Review News","Ethiopia and Somaliland signed a memorandum of understanding (MOU). It is reported that Ethiopia will give formal recognition to the Republic of Somaliland in the MOU, which raised controversy in the Horn of Africa. What is your comment on that?","China stands for upholding the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and supports countries in safeguarding sovereignty and territorial integrity. Somaliland is part of Somalia. China supports the Federal Government of Somalia in safeguarding national unity, sovereignty and territorial integrity. Meanwhile, we hope that regional countries will handle regional affairs well through dialogue and achieve common development by having friendly cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347677.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240111_11222239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-11","Mao Ning","AFP","The Taiwan Affairs Office has said the election candidate Lai Ching-te poses a severe danger to cross-Strait ties. We haven’t noticed any similar comments regarding other election candidates, and in addition, the Taiwan Affairs Office also urged voters in Taiwan to make the correct choice. What candidate does the mainland want to see win the election? Do China’s comments represent interference in Taiwan’s…","This question is not related to China’s foreign affairs. I’d refer you to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council regarding your question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347677.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240111_11222239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-11","Mao Ning","Beijing Youth Daily","It’s reported that Argentina’s Foreign Minister Diana Mondino met with Miao-hung Hsie, representative of the “Taipei economic and cultural office in Argentina”, on December 26, 2023. Sources said that this marks the first time for Argentina’s Foreign Minister to set aside the one-China principle and have “inter-governmental” relations with Taiwan. What’s China’s comment?","I noted relevant reports. Argentina has clarified to China that what you said is just hyping-up and reiterated that the government of Argentina values its relationship with China and will stay committed to the one-China principle. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Argentina also made clarifications to local media outlets. I’d like to stress that Taiwan is part of China and upholding the one-China principle is widely held consensus of the international community. Over the past five decades and more since China and Argentina established diplomatic ties, successive Argentinian administrations have upheld the one-China principle. China stands ready to work with Argentina to deepen our political mutual trust and advance the steady growth of China-Argentina comprehensive strategic partnership.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347677.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240111_11222239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-11","Mao Ning","Reuters","I have two questions on the elections in Taiwan. First, US officials said yesterday that the White House will send an unofficial delegation to Taiwan after the elections. What’s China’s comment? Second, the US yesterday said that any interference in Taiwan elections should be opposed. Reports say this is a warning for China. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s response?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. China firmly opposes the US having any form of official contact with the Taiwan region. The US needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues, stop official contact with the Taiwan region and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The US must not interfere in the elections in the Taiwan region in any form, or do anything harmful to China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan question is China’s internal affairs. Elections in the Taiwan region are purely China’s internal affairs that brook no external interference. China deplores and strongly opposes the US’ unwarranted comments on Taiwan’s elections. I need to stress that the Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests and is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, honor the commitment made by US leaders, stop interfering in elections in the Taiwan region in any form and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will take resolute and strong measures to safeguard its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347677.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240111_11222239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-11","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","The National Security Council spokesperson was quoted in the FT article, saying that there’s a clear precedent for sending former senior officials to Taiwan after the election, that this is consistent with the US one-China policy and consistent with the status-quo, and that as its time is after the election, it means it’s not endorsing one candidate or another candidate. Do you reject the assertion that this is…","China firmly opposes the US having any form of official contact with the Taiwan region. We ask the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués and prudently and properly handle Taiwan-related issues. The US must not interfere in elections in the Taiwan region in any form, and it must not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347677.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240111_11222239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-01-11","Chen Binhua","国台办发言人陈斌华10日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 10 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered a reporter's question on the 10th, saying: The fact that over the past eight years cross-Strait relations have plunged sharply, changing from peaceful development to tension and confrontation, fully proves that the so-called “Tsai Ing-wen line” is the “Taiwan independence” line, a line…","Chen Binhua said: “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water, and they run counter to the interests and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan. Only when the Taiwan Strait region is peaceful and stable and cross-Strait relations develop peacefully can compatriots in Taiwan enjoy good days of peace, tranquility and prosperity. We sincerely hope that compatriots in Taiwan will clearly recognize the extreme harm of the DPP's “Taiwan independence” line and the extreme danger of Lai Ching-te provoking cross-Strait confrontation and conflict. At this crossroads of where cross-Strait relations are headed, we hope they will make the right choice and together create a new chapter of fraternal mutual assistance among compatriots and prosperous development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240111_12592825.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-01-12","Mao Ning","CRI","Recently the National Security Council of the White House held a press call on Taiwan elections via teleconference. An anonymous official from the White House said that the US is committed to the one-China policy, does not support “Taiwan independence” and supports cross-Strait dialogue. The official added that the US does not take a position on the ultimate resolution of cross-Strait differences, provided they…","We noted the remarks of the US official. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and the political foundation of the China-US relationship. “Taiwan independence” is the biggest threat to cross-Strait peace and stability and is doomed to failure.\nUS leaders have repeatedly said that they are committed to the one-China policy, do not support “Taiwan independence”, do not support “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, and do not seek to use the Taiwan question as a tool to contain China. We hope the US will honor these commitments, handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly, stop official interactions with Taiwan, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and refrain from interfering in the elections of the Taiwan region in any form. If the US truly hopes to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it needs to explicitly oppose “Taiwan independence” and support China’s peaceful reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347678.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240112_11222890.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-12","Mao Ning","NTV","Regarding the election that is going to be held tomorrow, I understand that they have been reiterating that the Taiwan election is a domestic matter, but how do you think that the result of the election will affect the relationship between China and Taiwan?","The elections of the Taiwan region are China’s internal affairs. Regardless of the result, it will not change the basic fact that Taiwan is part of China and there is only one China in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347678.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240112_11222890.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-01-12","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that all 140 of Taiwan's active F-16V Block 20 fighter jets have been upgraded, and that before 2026 it will still procure 66 F-16V Block 70 fighter jets from the United States. What comments do you have on this?","For their own private interests, the DPP authorities are spending the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents on American weapons. This cannot stop the irreversible trend toward the complete reunification of the motherland, and will only push Taiwan into a perilous situation of war and danger. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains on high alert at all times and will take all necessary measures to resolutely crush any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16279991.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-01-13","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 13 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the evening of the 13th regarding the election results in the Taiwan region:\nThe results of the two elections in the Taiwan region show that the DPP cannot represent mainstream public opinion on the island. Taiwan is China's Taiwan. This election cannot change the basic pattern and development direction of cross-Strait relations, cannot change the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides to draw ever closer together, and cannot stop the trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified.\nOur position on resolving the Taiwan question and completing national reunification has been consistent, and our resolve is as firm as a rock. We will uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces. We will work with the relevant political parties, groups, and figures from all walks of life in Taiwan to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, jointly promote Chinese culture, and advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240113_12593548.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-14","Not identified in source","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, January 13 (Reporters Chen Jianxing and Liu Chang): The 2024 election of Taiwan's leader and legislators was held on January 13. Vote counting results show that DPP candidates Lai Ching-te and Hsiao Bi-khim were elected as Taiwan's leader and vice leader. Of the 113 seats in Taiwan's legislature, the Kuomintang won 52 seats, the DPP 51 seats, the Taiwan People's Party 8 seats, and independents and those without party nomination 2 seats.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240114_12593552.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","AFP","US senior delegation met with Lai Ching-te and Tsai Ing-wen in Taiwan today. What is your response to this?","The elections in Taiwan are the affairs of a region in China. China firmly opposes the US having any form of official interaction with Taiwan and interfering in Taiwan affairs in any way or under any pretext. We urge the US to have a clear understanding of the extreme complexity and sensitivity of the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and act seriously in accordance with the commitments that have been reaffirmed multiple times by the US leaders to not supporting “Taiwan independence”, “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, and not seeking to use the Taiwan question as a tool to contain China. The US needs to exercise extreme prudence in handling Taiwan-related issues, and must not obscure and hollow out the one-China principle in any form or send any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","CCTV","The government of the Republic of Nauru officially announced its decision to recognize the one-China principle, break the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities and seek to reestablish diplomatic ties with China. What’s your comment?","As an independent sovereign country, the Republic of Nauru announced that it recognizes the one-China principle, breaks the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities and seeks to reestablish diplomatic ties with China. China appreciates and welcomes the decision of the government of the Republic of Nauru.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. It’s what has been affirmed in Resolution 2758 of the UN General Assembly and is a prevailing consensus among the international community. China has established diplomatic relations with 182 countries on the basis of the one-China principle. The Nauru government’s decision of reestablishing diplomatic ties with China once again shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends. China stands ready to work with Nauru to open new chapters of our bilateral relations on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","CCTV","After the results of the two elections for 2024 in the Taiwan region were released, the Spokesperson of the Russian Foreign Ministry Maria Zakharova said that the Russian side opposes any form of Taiwan’s independence, and called on all outside forces to refrain from provocative actions undermining regional stability and international security. What is China’s comment on this?","We appreciate the remarks of the Russian side. In fact, aside from Russia, many countries and international organizations, including Indonesia, Viet Nam, Cambodia, Laos, Bangladesh, the Philippines, Sri Lanka, Nepal, South Africa, Egypt, Ethiopia, Zimbabwe, Kazakhstan, Uzbekistan, Tajikistan, Belarus, Serbia, Hungary, Papua New Guinea, Cuba, Venezuela, the SCO and the Arab League, have, through issuing statements and press communiqués or answering questions from the press, publicly reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle, their firm support for China’s effort to safeguard the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, their opposition to any form of “Taiwan independence” and their support for China’s cause toward reunification. This is the voice of justice and peace from the international community. It reflects the extensive consensus of the international community in firmly upholding the UN Charter and the basic norms governing international relations, and embodies the trend of the times and of history. We thank these countries for their understanding of and support for China’s just position.\nWhatever changes take place in Taiwan, the basic fact that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China will not change. Taiwan has never been a country and will never be one. We believe that the international community’s prevailing consensus on upholding the one-China principle and long-standing and overwhelming adherence to this principle will become more solid. The Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference and striving for national reunification will win more understanding and support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","Phoenix TV","Taiwan’s foreign affairs office said that China’s reiterated groundless remarks in response to questions concerning the elections of Taiwan that “the Taiwan question is China’s internal affairs” were not in line with the perception of the international community and the cross-Strait status quo. It called on the Chinese government to respect the results of the elections and face up to the reality. What’s your comment?","The elections of the Taiwan region belong to the affairs of a region in China. Whatever the results of the election, the basic fact that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China will not change; and the international community’s prevailing consensus on upholding the one-China principle will not change.\nBoth sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the US and the UK 80 years ago stipulates clearly that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan, shall be restored to China. Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation jointly published by China, the US, the UK and the Soviet Union in 1945 stipulates that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. Later Japan accepted the Potsdam Proclamation and announced unconditional surrender. These legally binding international instruments provide the historical and jurisprudential basis for the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Although the two sides across the Taiwan Strait have yet to be reunified, the sovereignty and territory of China has never been severed and the legal status and fact that Taiwan is part of China’s territory have never changed. This is the real status quo of the Taiwan question. China will achieve national reunification and Taiwan will inevitably return to the embrace of the motherland.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","NHK","Why did the government of Nauru announce the decision to cut diplomatic relations with the Taiwan authorities after the elections in Taiwan?","The government of Nauru announced that it recognizes the one-China principle, breaks the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities and seeks to reestablish diplomatic ties with China. This is a choice made independently by Nauru as a sovereign country. It shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","China News Service","According to media reports in Taiwan, the US, Japan and several European countries said that they plan to send delegations to the Taiwan region to “express congratulations” following the elections. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","The elections of the Taiwan region are China’s internal affairs. Regardless of the result, the basic fact that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China will not be changed.\nThe one-China principle is the political premise on which China establishes and develops diplomatic relations with other countries, a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. Anyone in the international community who violates the one-China principle is interfering in China’s internal affairs and infringing upon China’s sovereignty, and will face the joint opposition of the Chinese people and the international community. China deplores and strongly opposes relevant countries’ wrong practices violating the one-China principle, including issuing statements and “expressing congratulations”. We’ve lodged serious démarches.\nI noted that following the elections in the Taiwan region, many countries and international organizations have publicly reiterated their commitment to the one-China principle, expressed opposition to “Taiwan independence” in any form and supported China’s reunification. This is the voice of justice and peace from the international community. We believe that the international community will continue to adhere to the one-China principle, and support the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving to achieve national reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","Global Times","On January 14, in response to media queries on the elections in the Taiwan region, the Singaporean Foreign Ministry spokesperson “welcomed” and “congratulated” the elections. What’s China’s comment?","China has immediately made solemn démarches to Singapore. Singaporean leaders stated on multiple occasions that the Taiwan question is “a deep red line” for China. China values this statement and hopes that Singapore will strictly abide by the one-China principle and uphold the overall friendly relations between China and Singapore with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-15","Mao Ning","Reuters","A Taiwan official just said that China has lured Nauru with monetary support. May we know how much money is China going to give Nauru?","As a sovereign country, the Republic of Nauru independently made the right choice to announce that it recognizes the one-China principle, breaks the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities and seeks to reestablish diplomatic ties with China. This fully shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347679.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240115_11224225.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-01-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 15 (dispatch): Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a question on the 15th, saying: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s sacred territory. This is a historical and legal fact and a universal consensus of the international community. We appreciate that relevant countries have made the correct choice by following the trend of the times. Facts have repeatedly proven that adhering to the one-China principle is what the people want and the general trend of history.\nA reporter asked: Nauru has announced that it is severing its so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities and intends to re-establish diplomatic relations with China. What is your comment on this? Chen Binhua made the above statement in response to the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240115_12593861.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","CCTV","In the past few days, countries have been openly stating that they support the one-China principle, respect China’s territorial integrity and oppose interference in China’s internal affairs. Can you give us more details?","Since January 13, countries and international organizations have been openly reaffirming their commitment to the one-China principle, firm support for China’s effort of upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposition to any form of “Taiwan independence” and support for China’s reunification. Apart from what has been mentioned yesterday, a large number of countries, including Pakistan, the Maldives, Myanmar, Iran, Syria, Tunisia, Palestine, Turkmenistan, Kyrgyzstan, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Central Africa, Niger, Equatorial Guinea, Comoros, Lesotho, Somalia, Djibouti, Mali, Burundi, Gambia, Vanuatu, Tonga, Kiribati, Dominica, Nicaragua, and Bolivia as well as the African Union also clearly stated their support for the one-China principle and opposition to “Taiwan independence”. We applaud and appreciate the just position of these countries and organizations.\nWe are convinced that the international community will continue to, in accordance with the one-China principle, support the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and striving to achieve national reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","AFP","The US State Department issued a statement, saying that while the Government of Nauru’s action to sever its diplomatic relationship with Taiwan is a sovereign decision, it is nonetheless a disappointing one. What is your response to the US State Department’s statement?","The US has pointed fingers at the decision independently made by a sovereign country, tried every means to smear China’s diplomacy and encouraged the Taiwan region to expand “international space”. This gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously interferes in China’s internal affairs and severely contravenes the basic norms governing international relations. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this.\nI would like to stress that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and the one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing international consensus. The government of Nauru’s decision to restore diplomatic relations with China once again shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends. China urges the US to act seriously in accordance with the commitments that have been reaffirmed multiple times by the US leaders to not supporting “Taiwan independence”, “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, handle Taiwan-related issues with utmost prudence, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","CRI","It’s reported that the Taiwan authorities yesterday accused the mainland of long-term suppression of the island’s “diplomatic space” and luring Taiwan’s so-called “diplomatic allies.” What’s your comment?","There is but one China in the world, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do and is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends. We are convinced that more countries will choose to stand on the right side of history and the side of international justice and make the right decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of their countries and peoples.\nI want to stress that the one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community. The Chinese government never barters away principles. The DPP authorities in Taiwan disregard the prevailing trend of history, refuse the one-China principle, make every effort to expand the so-called “international space”, and conduct separatist activities seeking “Taiwan independence”. This is doomed to failure and will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","After the government of Nauru announced the decision to break the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities on January 15, Taiwan’s foreign affairs office said that Nauru cutting “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan at this time is not only China’s revenge on Taiwan’s “democratic elections”, but also a direct challenge to international order. What is your response?","By making these remarks, the Taiwan authorities are calling white black. The Taiwan question has nothing to do with democracy, but bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The “Taiwan independence” forces are using “democracy” to cover up their hidden agenda of dividing the country. Their attempt is doomed to failure.\nTalking about international order, the return of Taiwan to China is an important part of the international order established after the second World War. This is clearly stipulated in the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. Resolution 2758 adopted at the 26th Session of the UN General Assembly in 1971 makes it clear that there is no “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” in the world. Upholding the one-China principle is safeguarding international order. Challenging the one-China principle is challenging international order, and will meet the joint opposition of the international community.\nAcross the world, 182 countries have already established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. Nauru decided to stand with the overwhelming majority of the international community and restore diplomatic ties with China. This is the right choice in line with its long-term interests and will open up a brighter future for its development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Philippines’ President Marcos said the following on the Taiwan election results: We look forward to close collaboration, strengthening mutual interests, fostering peace and ensuring prosperity for our peoples in the years ahead. Marcos wrote this on X on Monday night. He also referred to the new leader in Taiwan as President-elect. What is the Chinese Foreign Ministry’s response?","The remarks of Philippines’ President gravely violate the one-China principle and the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the Philippines, seriously go against the Philippines’ political commitments to China, and blatantly interfere in China’s internal affairs. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this and has immediately lodged strong representations to the Philippine side. This morning, Assistant Foreign Minister Nong Rong summoned the Philippine Ambassador to China Jaime Florcruz to lodge serious démarche and urge the Philippines to present a responsible response to China.\nThe election result of the Taiwan region cannot change the dynamics and direction of cross-Strait relations and cannot hold back the prevailing trend that China will and must achieve reunification. We would like to make it clear to the Philippines that it should refrain from playing with fire on the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the joint communiqué of establishing diplomatic ties between China and the Philippines, immediately stop the wrong words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nWe suggest President Marcos read more to develop a proper understanding of the ins and outs of the Taiwan question and come to a right conclusion.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-16","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","It’s reported that the US House of Representatives recently passed the Taiwan Non-Discrimination Act of 2023, requiring the Secretary of the Treasury to use America’s influence in International Monetary Fund (IMF) to support Taiwan’s membership in this organization. What’s your comment?","The US passed the so-called act to grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs and attempt to manipulate the Taiwan question for political purposes to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan.” We strongly deplore and firmly oppose this, and have made serious representations to the US side.\nTaiwan does not have any ground, reason, or right to join the UN, or any other international organization whose membership is confined to sovereign states. On October 25, 1971, the 26th Session of the General Assembly of the United Nations adopted, with an overwhelming majority, Resolution 2758, which decides to recognize the representatives of the Government of the People's Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations, and to expel forthwith the representatives of the Taiwan authorities from the place which they unlawfully occupy. Once and for all, UNGA Resolution 2758 resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN. It also made it clear that there can only be one seat representing China at the UN, and that is the People’s Republic of China.\nOver the past half century and more, Resolution 2758 has been observed by the UN, special agencies such as IMF, and other international and regional organizations. Any issues regarding the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.\nThe US should fully understand the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question and immediately stop using the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs, sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces and undermining China-US relations, and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347680.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240116_11225099.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-17","Mao Ning","CGTN","Taiwan media claimed that sources say Nauru’s surprise break of “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan was achieved through behind-the-scenes manipulation by a former president of the country. While Taiwan was still assessing and having consultations on Nauru’s demand for economic aid, the mainland took the opportunity to persuade Nauru to switch ties. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","To recognize the one-China principle, break “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and seek to restore diplomatic relations with China is the collective decision of the Nauru cabinet and a right choice independently made by Nauru as a sovereign country. We noted that the parliament of Nauru unanimously adopted a resolution yesterday, supporting, endorsing and affirming the Nauru government’s decision to resume diplomatic relations with China and committing itself to strengthening Nauru’s diplomatic ties with China and the cordial relations between the two sovereign nations. This once again shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and where the arc of history bends.\nThe “sources” of the so-called claims are nothing but ill-intentioned speculation. Those who see “dollar diplomacy” as a go-to tool need to understand that there are things that money cannot buy. The one-China principle is a fundamental principle that cannot be traded and a prevailing international consensus.\nChina is the world’s second largest economy. Restoring and developing diplomatic relations and carrying out practical cooperation in various fields with China promise broad prospects and will bring unprecedented development opportunities for Nauru.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347681.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240117_11228034.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-17","Mao Ning","Reuters","Nauru had ties with China in 2002, but it switched to Taiwan in 2005 and now it has switched back to China. Our question is, when will China establish an embassy in Nauru and vice versa, when will Nauru establish an embassy in Beijing?","We will release the specific arrangements on the reestablishment of diplomatic ties between China and Nauru in due course.\nI want to stress that as a collective decision made at the cabinet meeting, Nauru recognizes the one-China principle, breaks “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and seeks to reestablish diplomatic relations with China. This meets the aspiration of the people in Nauru, serves Nauru’s long-term interests, and is on the right side of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347681.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240117_11228034.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-17","Mao Ning","Reuters","Does China see Nauru as a reliable partner given it has switched ties before? What guarantees does China have from Nauru for the country not to go back to Taiwan again?","China appreciates and welcomes Nauru’s decision to break “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and seek to resume diplomatic relations with China. We believe this is a right choice. China is ready to work with Nauru to open up a new chapter in our bilateral relations on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347681.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240117_11228034.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear journalist friends, today is the first regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office in 2024. Before we begin, I would like to wish everyone a Happy New Year. Please go ahead with your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","In his 2024 New Year's message, General Secretary Xi Jinping emphasized, “Reunification of the motherland is a historical inevitability, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait must work together with one heart to share the great glory of national rejuvenation.” How should this be deeply understood and implemented?","General Secretary Xi Jinping's speech is rich in content and of great significance. It pointed out the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified, and set forth earnest expectations for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. Only by realizing the reunification of the motherland can the hidden danger of “Taiwan independence” separatism be fundamentally eliminated, the schemes of external forces to “use Taiwan to contain China” be thoroughly defeated, and the country's sovereignty, security, and development interests be safeguarded; only then can the special state of long-term political confrontation across the Strait be ended, lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait be achieved, the wisdom and strength of compatriots on both sides be better united, our common home be better maintained and built, and a happier and more beautiful future be created for all Chinese sons and daughters and the Chinese nation.\nOn the new journey of working together with one heart to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, Taiwan compatriots will, together with mainland compatriots, share the dignity and glory of a great nation, and take pride in being upright Chinese. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's 2024 New Year message, adhere to uniting the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great process of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594388.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》记者","Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, published a New Year message titled “Firm Direction, Pioneering Progress” in the first issue of 2024 of the journal “Cross-Strait Relations.” Please interpret the main points of this message.","Director Song Tao issued a New Year's message on January 2, extending, on behalf of the Taiwan Work Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, New Year's blessings and sincere greetings to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. In the message, Director Song Tao reiterated the central government's major policies toward Taiwan, reviewed and summarized Taiwan-related work in 2023, and called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to unite as one, work hand in hand, and join in the great cause of national reunification and create a bright future for national rejuvenation together.\nIn the message, Director Song Tao used “five adherences” to explain Taiwan-related work for 2024, making clear our stance, positions and policy orientation of continuing to oppose “Taiwan independence” and interference by external forces, promoting exchanges and cooperation across all areas across the Strait, deepening the integrated development of both sides, enhancing the well-being of compatriots' kinship, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of national reunification. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold righteousness, grasp the general trend, firmly stand on the right side of history, and join us in working together to return cross-Strait relations to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594385.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Please summarize the development of cross-Strait relations in 2023 and look ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2024.","In 2023, under the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we fully implemented the overall strategy of the new era for the Party to resolve the Taiwan question, firmly grasped the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations, broadly united Taiwan compatriots, resolutely opposed “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, solidly promoted peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and firmly advanced the process of national reunification.\nWe implemented General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions to “promote integration through connectivity, promote integration through benefits, and promote integration through emotional bonds,” formulated and issued the 《Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone》, and continued to deepen cross-Strait integrated development. We took into account the concerns of our compatriots, and promptly resolved the registration problems of some Taiwan food enterprises, resumed the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, helped Taiwan compatriots conveniently use mobile payments on the mainland, and provided assistance for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to share in development opportunities on the mainland. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises continue to be optimistic about the mainland market. The number of Taiwan-invested projects on the mainland and the actual amount of Taiwan capital used have increased significantly, and cross-Strait trade has remained at a high level.\nWe responded to the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, seized the favorable opportunity of the transition in epidemic prevention and control, adopted effective measures, and promoted the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Strait and the normalization of exchanges and cooperation. We held important exchange activities such as the Straits Forum, the annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, and the “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams — Exchange and Seminar Activities for Compatriots on Both Sides of the Strait,” and invited people from all fields and sectors on the island to visit and exchange. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to deeply understand that only by adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” can the Taiwan Strait enjoy peace and stability, cross-Strait relations develop, and the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait be guaranteed.\nWe adhere to the policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” resolutely carry out major struggles against separatism and interference, defeat all forms of “independence” provocations and external interference schemes, further consolidate the international community's pattern of adhering to one China, and seized the strategic initiative in realizing the complete reunification of the motherland.\nIn the new year, we will adhere to the policy of “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems,” adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland; continue to promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, continuously expand personnel exchanges across the Strait, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and promote emotional connection between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold righteousness, grasp the general trend, firmly stand on the right side of history, and join us in removing interference and jointly promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594383.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The results of two elections in Taiwan in 2024 have been announced. What impact will these results have on the direction of cross-Strait relations? What are the overall considerations of mainland policy toward Taiwan for the coming period?","Elections in the Taiwan region are local affairs of China. The results of the two elections in the Taiwan region this time show that the DPP cannot represent mainstream public opinion on the island. The election results cannot shake the status and fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-strait relations, and cannot stop the historical trend of the motherland’s inevitable reunification.\nWe will unwaveringly uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, comply with the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and resolutely and unswervingly oppose “Taiwan independence,” maintain peace, expand exchanges, promote cooperation, deepen integration, and advance reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594378.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","Please summarize the development of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2023, and tell us your expectations for cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2024.","In 2023, we actively responded to the common wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. Working together with all sectors in Taiwan, after the transition in COVID-19 prevention and control, we pushed cross-strait economic exchange and cooperation forward through difficulties, with steady progress, and cross-strait economic exchange, cooperation, and integrated development made positive headway.\nFirst, Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland had overall stable production and operations, and cross-strait trade remained at a high level. According to General Administration of Customs statistics, cross-strait trade in 2023 totaled US$267.836 billion, remaining at a high level; the mainland remained the largest source of Taiwan's trade surplus. According to Ministry of Commerce statistics, from January to November 2023, the mainland newly approved 6,936 Taiwan-invested projects (including those reinvested through third locations), up 26.8% year on year, and actually utilized Taiwan capital amounted to US$2.69 billion, up 39.9% year on year. Cross-strait industrial cooperation continued to deepen, supply chains were stable, the structure of Taiwan investment was further optimized, and the confidence of Taiwan businesses to accelerate and expand investment and continue developing on the mainland grew firmer.\nSecond, we actively created favorable conditions for cross-strait economic exchange and cooperation. We held the 2023 Taiwan Business Spring Festival Symposium, releasing positive signals of restoring and strengthening cross-strait exchange and cooperation after the transition in epidemic prevention; we promoted the restoration of cross-strait direct flight routes and the resumption of “Small Three Links” sailings; we invited major Taiwan industrial and commercial groups and representatives of the business community to visit, guided cross-strait business circles toward win-win cooperation, and deepened cross-strait industrial cooperation; we promptly resolved registration issues for some Taiwan food companies and resumed imports of Taiwan chilled white hairtail, frozen mackerel scad, sugar apples, and grouper; and we continued to do a good job in internship, employment, and entrepreneurship support for Taiwan youth.\nThird, the “promoting integration through connectivity, benefits, and emotional bonds” approach achieved breakthrough progress. In September 2023, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” was officially issued, incorporating Fujian-Taiwan integrated development into the national development strategic plan. This fully reflects the great importance that the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core attaches to strengthening cross-strait exchange and cooperation and deepening cross-strait integrated development. The Opinions include content on “deepening cross-strait industrial cooperation,” which has important guiding significance for localities to leverage their resource endowments and regional advantages and strengthen industrial cooperation with Taiwan. The State Council approved the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan,” focusing on three key areas—industry, market, and people's livelihood—and striving to build a new engine for cross-strait industrial innovation and development, a new high ground for scientific and technological innovation cooperation, a new hub for social and cultural exchange, and a new platform for exchange and cooperation between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait and the Hong Kong, Macao, and related regions.\nFourth, Taiwan businesses made remarkable progress in integrating into the new development pattern and participating in high-quality development. We took practical measures to help Taiwan businesses transform, upgrade, and pursue smart manufacturing and digital transformation, actively expanded domestic market demand, promoted the connection of cross-strait supply chain technologies and rules, accelerated the integration of key factors such as technology, talent, and markets, and actively explored new models of cross-strait enterprise cooperation. We guided Taiwan businesses to orderly shift production capacity to the central and western regions and Northeast China. Localities and relevant departments innovated their approaches by holding Taiwan-related economic and trade activities such as the Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, the Zhejiang·Taiwan Cooperation Week, the Dongguan Taiwan Business Expo, and the Yuntai Conference, as well as industry matchmaking activities such as the 2023 Cross-Strait Robotics and Intelligent Automation Industry Matchmaking Event, the Longyan Cross-Strait Machinery Industry Expo, and the Liaoning-Taiwan Petrochemical Industry Cooperation Promotion Conference, continuously helping Taiwan businesses inject new momentum, seize new opportunities, switch to new tracks, and achieve new development. We continued to promote the listing of quality Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland A-share market; to date, a cumulative total of 62 Taiwan-invested enterprises have been listed.\nIn the new year, we will fully implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on Taiwan work and the CPC's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and continue to promote cross-strait economic exchange and cooperation, so that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises feel a greater sense of gain, security, well-being, and participation in the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594376.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Two questions. First, last September, the “Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were officially issued. Please introduce what measures have been launched so far to promote the implementation of the “Opinions”?…","Question one. Since the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were issued, the central government and relevant national ministries and commissions have taken the initiative, proposed innovative measures, and strengthened policy support. Fujian Province has reinforced its primary responsibility, established a coordinated implementation mechanism, innovated working methods, and jointly promoted the effective implementation of all tasks and measures in the “Opinions.”\nThe National Immigration Administration issued ten entry-exit policy measures to support Fujian in building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, further facilitating personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan. The State Administration for Market Regulation issued “seven measures,” focusing on the fields of standards, metrology, and certification and accreditation, to support Fujian in building a cross-Strait standards interoperability service platform. The National Medical Products Administration issued the “Work Plan on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development? Promoting Innovative Development in Drug, Medical Device and Cosmetics Regulation,” which adheres to institutional innovation, serves the people’s livelihood, and is implemented step by step, to promote the integrated development of cross-Strait pharmaceutical industries and ensure the safety of drugs and medical devices. The Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs issued the “Opinions on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in the Field of Agriculture and Rural Affairs,” to support Fujian in deepening agricultural and rural exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan. The Ministry of Commerce, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the National Development and Reform Commission, and the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology jointly issued the “Several Measures on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development in the Field of Economy and Trade,” which proposes 14 measures across five aspects: supporting Fujian in expanding opening-up and cooperation with Taiwan, supporting high-quality development of Fujian-Taiwan trade, deepening the integrated development of Fujian-Taiwan advantageous industries, helping Taiwan-invested enterprises in Fujian integrate into the domestic circulation, and promoting accelerated integrated development in key areas, to further support economic and trade exchanges and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan. The General Administration of Customs guided the Fuzhou and Xiamen Customs in announcing and implementing a policy relaxing the quantity limits on Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers may carry on direct routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu. Fujian Province issued the “Implementation Opinions of the CPC Fujian Provincial Committee and the Fujian Provincial People’s Government on Implementing the ‘Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,’” which focuses on jointly building and sharing the “first home” for Taiwan-invested enterprises and Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, and makes policy arrangements providing equal treatment to compatriots on both sides of the Strait in areas including study, research, employment and entrepreneurship, social participation, convenient payment, medical and social insurance, grassroots governance, and rule of law construction for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian.\nIn 2024, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the National Development and Reform Commission will take the lead in coordination, make overall plans, and advance work on policy implementation, evaluation and adjustment, and summarization and promotion. The central government and relevant national ministries and commissions will, within the framework of the “Opinions,” further propose innovative measures and fully support Fujian in exploring new mechanisms, new paths, and new models for deepening cross-Strait integrated development. Fujian Province will continue to reinforce its primary responsibility, innovate working methods, and promote the effective implementation of all measures.\nQuestion two. After reading about the incident involving “Little Yiyi” online, I felt especially warm, as if love were being passed on.\nThis winter, “Ice City” Harbin has become a hot tourist destination, winning over countless fans. Its unique charm of ice and snow has also attracted many Taiwan compatriots, especially children. I believe that whether they are called “Little Pineapple” or “Little Angelica,” Taiwanese children, like “Little Mandarin Orange,” “Little Wild Mushroom,” and “Little Panda,” are all children of our own Chinese family and will surely be loved and warmly welcomed without limit. We warmly welcome Taiwanese children and adults to visit the mainland more often, to take in its magnificent landscapes and see the new face of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594362.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Could the spokesperson summarize the main situation of exchanges and dialogues with Taiwan's political parties, groups and representative figures in 2023? What plans are there in this regard for 2024?","In 2023, on the political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we consolidated mutual trust, strengthened exchanges, deepened understanding, and built consensus with political parties, groups, and representative figures in Taiwan. Together we promoted the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, safeguarded peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefited compatriots on both sides of the Strait, achieving positive results.\nFirst, we strengthened exchanges and contacts with Taiwan’s political parties. Senior leaders of Taiwan political parties, including Xia Liyan and Lien Sheng-wen, vice chairs of the Kuomintang (KMT), and Wu Cheng-tien, chairman of the New Party, led delegations to visit the mainland on multiple occasions, and central leaders met with them. Through attending cross-strait exchange activities, touring and inspecting, and holding symposiums and seminars with relevant parties on the mainland, the delegations engaged in dialogue and exchanged views with us on the situation in the Taiwan Strait, cross-strait relations, and related issues affecting the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. This consolidated political mutual trust between the two sides and built consensus on developing cross-strait relations and promoting exchanges and cooperation.\nSecond, Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and representative figures actively participated in cross-strait exchange activities. At the 15th Straits Forum, the 3rd “Working Together to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriot Exchange and Seminar Activities,” the 6th Straits Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the 5th Zhongshan Forum, and other events, we engaged in exchanges and communication with the KMT, the New Party, the People First Party, the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union, and other political parties and representative figures, building consensus. We voiced positive messages calling for adherence to the “1992 Consensus,” opposition to “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference, deepening cross-strait exchange and cooperation, promoting integrated development, benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and jointly promoting national rejuvenation. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led a delegation to the mainland to worship ancestors and visit, and brought Taiwan youth and students to exchange views. Teachers and students from five mainland universities, including Peking University, visited Taiwan at the invitation of the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation. Both events drew wide attention and positive appraisal from all sectors on both sides of the Strait and had a positive significance for promoting exchanges between compatriots on both sides, especially young people, and for advancing the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.\nThird, exchanges between cross-strait cities have gradually resumed and expanded. Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an and several other county and city heads from Taiwan led delegations to visit relevant localities on the mainland and held exchange activities, playing a positive role in promoting exchanges and cooperation between relevant cities and counties across the Strait in various fields and in enhancing the well-being of people in both places.\nIn the new year, with an eye to the situation in the Taiwan Strait and changes in the development of cross-strait relations, we will continue to thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important instructions and directives and the Party Central Committee’s decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work. On the political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will further consolidate and deepen mutual trust with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and representative figures, strengthen exchanges and dialogue, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594364.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","海峡之声记者","Please spokesperson summarize and introduce the progress and main characteristics of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2023, and what are the plans for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2024?","In 2023, against the new backdrop of the smooth transition in mainland China’s COVID-19 prevention and control, we actively promoted the swift restoration of normal cross-Strait exchanges. After a gap of three years, people from all walks of life across the two sides resumed exchanges in many forms. Personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields quickly warmed up and continued to heat up. In 2023 there were about 3 million cross-Strait trips, and the number of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland increased 7.4 times over the previous year. Several new characteristics emerged, mainly the following:\nFirst, the mainland actively promoted the normalization and routinization of cross-Strait exchanges and travel. In 2023, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a New Year’s message and successively sent congratulatory letters to the 15th Straits Forum, the 6th Straits Forum on Cross-Strait Youth Development, and the 10th anniversary annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit. These expressed policy positions of continuing to work for the promotion of cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, the deepening of integrated development across all fields between the two sides, and the benefit of Taiwan compatriots. They fully reflected deep concern, care and solicitude for the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, inspired compatriots on both sides to move toward each other, strengthen exchanges, expand cooperation and advance hand in hand, sharing the broad opportunities of Chinese-style modernization, and effectively guided the direction of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nSecond, compatriots on both sides showed high enthusiasm for exchanges, and the sentiment that “the two sides of the Strait are one family” grew even stronger. With the smooth transition in COVID-19 prevention and control, relevant mainland authorities promptly took measures to facilitate cross-Strait personnel travel. The enthusiasm of compatriots on both sides for exchanges and interaction ran high, and tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots eagerly took part in events such as the Straits Forum, the 2023 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, and the Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month. Many Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, came to the mainland for the first time, saw with their own eyes the thriving development of the mainland, and personally felt the warm and friendly sincerity of mainland compatriots. Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwan university students to the mainland for exchanges and visits, and mainland university teachers and students were invited to return the visit to Taiwan for exchanges, which were broadly recognized by people on both sides. At the Hangzhou Asian Games and the Chengdu Universiade, Taiwan athletes constantly felt the atmosphere and warmth of “home ground.” The cross-Strait music exchange variety show “Sheng Sheng Bu Xi · Baodao Ji” produced by Hunan Broadcasting Mango TV, and the music short film in which singers from both sides sang “Tomorrow Will Be Better” together, produced by the CCTV Film Channel, sang out the voices of compatriots on both sides.\nThird, exchange activities were rich and varied, and exchanges in all fields were comprehensively heating up. Localities and departments actively held cross-Strait exchange activities with innovative forms and diverse participants, providing more platforms for people on both sides to exchange ideas, deepen mutual understanding and strengthen friendship. Cross-Strait cultural exchanges continued to heat up, folk belief exchanges had rich content, grassroots exchanges took diverse forms, and youth student exchanges were splendid. Exchanges were widely carried out in education, publishing, medicine and health, sports, news, trade unions, women, ethnic minorities, religion and other fields and sectors. Tens of thousands of Taiwan residents came to worship at the Mazu Ancestral Temple on Meizhou Island, and took part in ceremonies honoring the Yellow Emperor, Yan Emperor, Fuxi, Guandi, Kaizhang Sage King and other sacrificial rites. Thousands of Taiwan village and neighborhood chiefs and other grassroots representatives visited and exchanged views in various parts of the mainland. Youth-oriented exchange activities such as the 3rd Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, the 11th Straits Youth Festival, and the 10th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour brought young people from both sides closer together. The “Cross-Strait Innovative Design Competition · Huacan Award,” the 6th China Design Award Competition, the “We Love · 7th Cross-Strait Youth Short Film Competition,” the 3rd IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival, and the Straits Minnan Music Award Competition attracted many Taiwan youth to participate.\nFourth, integrated development continued to deepen and achieved new progress and results. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” were officially issued. Localities and departments actively worked to implement policies and measures that benefit Taiwan and its people more thoroughly and in detail, and the systems and policies that safeguard the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure they enjoy equal treatment on the mainland were further improved. More and more Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, found a stage on the mainland to realize their dreams, becoming witnesses, participants and beneficiaries of Chinese-style modernization. In 2023, 25 Taiwan youths and three teams mainly composed of Taiwan youths were awarded provincial- and municipal-level May Fourth Youth Medals and May Fourth Youth Medal Collectives (including nominee honors). The China Musicians Association, the China Photographers Association and the China Theatre Association newly admitted seven Taiwan artists and writers as members, and the Chinese Writers Association newly admitted two members.\nThe facts fully prove that compatriots on both sides share the same language, culture, lineage and homeland. The desire to visit each other, exchange and cooperate is the natural sentiment and simple aspiration of compatriots on both sides, and it cannot be obstructed by the DPP authorities. In the new year, we will continue to uphold the concept that “the two sides of the Strait are one family,” actively advance exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, continuously expand personnel exchanges across the Strait, deepen integrated development across the Strait, promote compatriots on both sides to jointly carry forward Chinese culture, and foster spiritual kinship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594372.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和《看台海》新媒体记者","Some public opinion holds that after Lai Ching-te takes office, he will go further in promoting “Taiwan independence” separatism, and the possibility of peaceful reunification has been lost. What is your comment on this? What will the mainland firmly do in the next stage to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference?","“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water, and can only bring profound disaster to Taiwan. Our actions opposing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme are resolute and forceful. Our ability to crush “Taiwan independence” acts and safeguard national sovereignty is invincible, and our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is firm and unwavering.\nThe results of the two elections in Taiwan this time fully show that the DPP does not represent Taiwan or all Taiwan compatriots. “Take down the DPP,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” want peace rather than war, want development rather than decline, and want exchange rather than separation, is the mainstream public will on the island. This election cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-strait relations, cannot change the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides to draw closer and closer together, and cannot stop the trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and inevitably will be reunified.\nWe will continue to adhere to the policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” to adhere to the policy of placing our hopes on the Taiwan people, and to unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594375.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Two questions. First question: According to reports, relevant authorities in Taiwan recently issued a “core critical technology list” restricting the outflow of advanced technologies such as semiconductor manufacturing. At the same time, they announced a so-called “amendment” adding the “crime of extraterritorial use of trade secrets of core critical technologies.” Taiwan's economic authorities said the direction…","On the first question: the formation and development of the cross-Strait industrial and supply chains is the result of the joint action of market rules and corporate choices. Strengthening cross-Strait industrial cooperation and building more solid industrial and supply chains accords with the wishes and interests of industries and enterprises on both sides. The DPP authorities blindly follow the United States, pursue “decoupling and breaking chains” and a “small yard, high fence” approach, and create obstacles to cross-Strait industrial cooperation. This seriously undermines the cross-Strait economic and trade order. It not only violates the principles of the market economy and fair competition and directly harms the interests of industries and enterprises on both sides, but it also increases instability in cross-Strait industrial and supply chains and weakens Taiwan's industrial advantages and voice in global industrial and supply chains. Such conduct, relying on others' whims and cutting off one's own income, is truly incredibly foolish.\nOn the second question: as we have said, the DPP cannot represent mainstream public opinion on the island. “Take the DPP off the shelves”: opposing “Taiwan independence,” wanting peace rather than war, wanting development rather than decline, and wanting exchange rather than separation, is the mainstream public opinion on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Nauru has announced that it is severing so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities and intends to re-establish diplomatic relations with China. What is your comment?","This is the tenth country to sever so-called “diplomatic” relations with Taiwan since the DPP came to power. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory. This is a historical and legal fact and a common consensus of the international community. We appreciate the relevant country for making the correct choice in line with the trend of the times. Facts have repeatedly proven that adhering to the One-China Principle is the will of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: After being elected, Lai Ching-te said that cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges can reduce risks, that exchange must replace containment and dialogue must replace confrontation for peaceful coexistence, and that only peaceful, equal, and democratic dialogue best serves the interests of the people on both sides of the Strait. What response does the Taiwan Affairs Office have? Second question: After…","Question one: On the basis of the one-China principle, there are no obstacles to exchanges between us and any political party or group in Taiwan. Replacing confrontation with dialogue, struggle with cooperation, and zero-sum with win-win is the only way cross-Strait relations can progress steadily and go far. The DPP's obstinate adherence to the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance is the fundamental obstacle to its exchanges with us.\nQuestion two: This reflects everyone's concern that the DPP may aggravate tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. What I want to emphasize is that elections in the Taiwan region cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-Strait relations, cannot change the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides to draw closer and grow more intimate, and cannot stop the trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, as it certainly will be.\nWe are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, and we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the greatest effort.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","英国独立电视台记者","First question: Lai Ching-te has said he “wants to restart dialogue with the Chinese government.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's attitude toward this? Second question: The Taiwan Affairs Office previously stated that unification is the common aspiration of the people on both sides of the Strait. On what basis did you make this statement?","On the first question, we have repeatedly stressed that the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, is the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. Only by upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" embodying the one-China principle can the two sides across the Strait engage in communication and dialogue; otherwise, any dialogue or exchange is out of the question.\nOn the second question, regarding why unification is the common aspiration of the people on both sides of the Strait, I would like to tell this foreign friend that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, and the influence of Chinese culture is deeply rooted. The Chinese civilization has outstanding unity, which fundamentally determines that the cultures of all the ethnic groups of the Chinese nation are integrated into one, and that they remain firmly cohesive even when encountering major setbacks. It determines the shared conviction that the territory cannot be divided, the country cannot be in chaos, the nation cannot be scattered, and the civilization cannot be severed. It determines that national unification will always be the core of China's core interests, and that a strong and unified country is where the destiny of all ethnic groups lies. The fact that the two sides have not yet been fully reunified is a wound left by history to the Chinese nation. Shaped and determined by history and culture, the deepest aspiration of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait is to heal the historical wound and seek national reunification. This is the culture of us Chinese and the value pursuit of us Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240117_12594361.htm"],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","湖北广播电视台记者","After the 2024 election of the Taiwan regional leader concluded, U.S. President Biden immediately stated, “We do not support Taiwan independence.” What is your comment?","We have noted relevant statements from the US side. The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. Whether in Bali or in San Francisco, US President Biden repeatedly stated that the US adheres to the one-China policy, does not support “Taiwan independence,” and does not support “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” We hope the US side will put the above statements into practice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Before the Taiwan regional elections, relevant mainland departments said they were studying further measures, such as suspending the tariff concessions under the ECFA early harvest list for agricultural and fishery products, machinery, auto parts, textiles, and other products. What is the current progress? Will the mainland fully terminate ECFA in the future?\nSecond question: After being elected,…","First question: It is understood that relevant departments are studying, based on relevant clauses of the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) and relevant policies and regulations, further measures such as suspending tariff concessions under the ECFA Early Harvest for products including agricultural and fishery products, machinery, auto parts, and textiles.\nECFA was signed and implemented on the common political basis of the “1992 Consensus.” The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations. This is the fundamental reason why relevant issues are difficult to resolve.\nSecond question: I have already answered this just now, and I reiterate: the DPP’s stubborn adherence to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” is the fundamental obstacle to its engagement with us.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","First question: some commentary holds that after the DPP's election victory, the situation of cross-Strait political confrontation and military standoff will intensify, and the mainland side will accelerate the unification process. What is your comment?\nSecond question: the Taipei District Prosecutors Office recently summoned retired Miaoli police officer Liu Jiasheng and others who went to the mainland for…","First question: The public concern on the island about the DPP's continued “governance” largely stems from the worry that the DPP may continue to pursue “independence” provocations, undermine cross-Strait relations, and harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. If the DPP does not repent and goes further and further down the evil path of provoking independence, it will only push Taiwan into a dangerous situation and bring profound calamity to Taiwan. We are willing to create broad room for peaceful reunification, and we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort.\nSecond question: As is well known, the reason the DPP authorities concocted and forcibly pushed the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” is precisely to suppress and persecute dissenters, to intimidate and punish Taiwan people who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, and to create a “green terror.” Including the case you cited, the facts prove that the “Anti-Infiltration Act” has long since become a political tool for the DPP authorities to pursue narrow party interests, and it is an out-and-out “evil law.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","After the conclusion of Taiwan’s 2024 leadership election, former U.S. Deputy Secretary of State James Steinberg and former White House National Security Advisor Stephen Hadley led a delegation to visit Taiwan. What is your comment?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. We have already made our position clear on the election results in the Taiwan region of China. Regardless of the election results, they cannot change the basic fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China.\nThe one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and it is also the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. We firmly oppose any external force interfering in China’s internal affairs on any pretext. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear.\nWe urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, to put into practice its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: From Nauru's “severing of diplomatic ties” with Taiwan, it can be seen that Beijing is giving Lai Ching-te no observation period at all. In the future, there may be routine tightening measures in diplomacy, economics and trade, and the military, with the ultimate aim of warning the DPP. May I ask whether the mainland's use of “high-pressure tactics” will produce a “double-edged sword” effect, and…","Please do not use “Beijing” to refer to the mainland side from now on.\nOn the first question, I would like to stress three points. First, there is only one China in the world, and the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China is beyond dispute. The status of Taiwan as part of China, and never a country, cannot be changed. Any act that distorts facts, denies, or challenges the one-China principle will end in failure. The fact is that since the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) came to power in 2016, 10 countries, including Nauru, have successively severed so-called “diplomatic relations” with the DPP authorities.\nSecond, the DPP started out by pursuing “Taiwan independence” and persistently holds a separatist position. It uses the hard-earned money of people on the island to pursue “diplomatic breakthroughs” and buy international recognition, deceiving the Taiwan public. Its essence is to attempt to negate the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and to undermine China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. We naturally must oppose and contain it. What we uphold is the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nThird, Taiwan compatriots are our flesh-and-blood kin, and the people on both sides of the Strait are one family, bound by blood ties. Because they have been poisoned by “Taiwan independence” ideology, and because political differences across the Strait have yet to be resolved, some Taiwan compatriots have developed misperceptions about the nature of cross-Strait relations and the issue of national identity. We are willing to maintain sufficient patience and tolerance, continuously deepen the understanding of the mainland among broad Taiwan compatriots, gradually reduce their misunderstandings and doubts, and help them move out of the misconception of being deluded by “Taiwan independence” ideology. We hope and believe that broad Taiwan compatriots can firmly stand on the right side of history and be upright Chinese. Only with a strong motherland to rely on can Taiwan compatriots have greater room for international development, stand taller and with more confidence on the international stage, and be safer and more dignified.\nOn the second question, “peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. Achieving national reunification peacefully best serves the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots.\nOur not committing to renouncing the use of force is by no means directed at Taiwan compatriots. It is directed at interference by external forces and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. Taiwan is part of China, and the Chinese government has the right and the responsibility to adopt all necessary means to safeguard national unity and sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will continue to pursue the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatism.\nOn the third question, the “1992 Consensus” reached by the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan, in which each side orally expressed that both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle, has played an irreplaceable and important role in establishing basic mutual trust across the Strait, conducting dialogue and consultation, and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. It is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of cross-Strait relations. We have repeatedly emphasized that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld, there are no obstacles to exchanges between us and any political party or group in Taiwan. As long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld, matters across the Strait can always be discussed and resolved.\nIn recent years, the DPP authorities have stubbornly maintained a “Taiwan independence” position, denied, distorted, and stigmatized the “1992 Consensus,” seriously undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait relations and harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will correctly understand the important significance of the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely resist “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, join hands with mainland compatriots, and together promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and create a bright future for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","In response to Lai Ching-te taking office, some members of the public have called on the mainland to cancel economic measures benefiting Taiwan and to apply greater pressure on Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's response?","Our major policy guidelines toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will thoroughly implement the overall strategy the Party has adopted for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to work for promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development across all cross-Strait fields, improve systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, promote the joint promotion of Chinese culture across the Strait, and foster heartfelt connection among compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","As the Spring Festival approaches, please spokesperson introduce what convenience measures the mainland will provide for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots returning home for the New Year?","Under the arrangements for cross-Strait air transport, cross-Strait airlines may operate no more than 890 passenger flights per week in total between 61 mainland airports and 10 Taiwan airports. Direct cross-Strait air links have greatly facilitated travel between the two sides and have played an important role in advancing the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nSince last year, as pandemic prevention and control has entered a new stage, we have followed the shared wishes of compatriots on both sides for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and have actively promoted the resumption of direct cross-Strait flight routes. At present, 14 mainland cities operate more than 500 passenger flights per week on cross-Strait routes, carrying more than 80,000 passenger trips. Although cross-Strait flights and passenger volume have grown compared with the pandemic period, because of the limited number of airports, cross-Strait travel remains considerably inconvenient overall, and there remains a very strong call from people on both sides for the full resumption of direct cross-Strait flight routes.\nThe Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and students, businesspeople, and compatriots from Taiwan hope to return home smoothly to celebrate with their families. We are willing to provide convenience to the greatest extent possible. The DPP authorities should, as soon as possible, remove unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport and meet the needs of people on both sides, especially the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-17","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The online selection of the “Top 10 Cross-Strait Relations News of 2023” was officially launched on January 16. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The online voting event for the “Top 10 Cross-Strait Relations News of 2023,” hosted by China Taiwan Net, officially launched yesterday (January 16). Voting will close at 5:00 p.m. on January 23. A total of 14 news items have been shortlisted this year, including major events reflecting the overall trend of peaceful development in cross-strait relations as well as heartwarming stories of integrated cross-strait development. Since its launch in 2005, this event has been successfully held for 18 consecutive sessions. It has drawn attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait and has had a wide influence across both sides. This year’s event will combine netizen votes with expert opinions, and the final results will be officially announced on January 24. We welcome netizens on both sides of the Strait to vote and interact through China Taiwan Net’s website, its official Weibo and WeChat accounts, and the “Today Taiwan” WeChat public account, among other cross-strait new media platforms, to select the “Top 10 Cross-Strait Relations News” for this year.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240117_12594356.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-01-18","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Philippine Defense Secretary on Wednesday accused the Chinese Foreign Ministry of insulting President Marcos Jr. during a news briefing earlier this week, stooping to what he called “low talk.” What’s your response?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and concerns the sentiment of the 1.4 billion Chinese people. The remarks of the Philippine side seriously violate the one-China principle and the joint communiqué of establishing diplomatic ties between China and the Philippines, seriously go against the Philippines’ political commitment to China, and blatantly interfere in China’s internal affairs. It is completely legitimate and necessary for China to state our solemn position. The one-China principle is a red line and bottom line. China will never accept anyone making provocations on the Taiwan question and will resolutely fight back.\nWe urge the Philippines to earnestly uphold the spirit of the joint communiqué of establishing diplomatic ties between China and the Philippines, adhere to the one-China principle, and stop wrong words and deeds on issues relating to Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347682.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240118_11228791.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-24","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","With the resumption of bilateral ties with Nauru, does China plan to step up investment and trade with Nauru and also offer financial aid to the Pacific country? Are there any details as to what type of investments or trade or how much of financial aid?","Today, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi and Nauru’s Minister for Foreign Affairs and Trade Lionel Rouwen Aingnimea, who is on a visit to China at our invitation, signed Joint Communiqué on the Resumption of Diplomatic Relations Between the People’s Republic of China and the Republic of Nauru in Beijing. Our two countries decided to reestablish diplomatic relations at the ambassadorial level, effective as of this day. Nauru has become the 183rd country to have diplomatic relations with China.\nThe reestablishment of diplomatic ties between China and Nauru once again demonstrates that there is but one China in the world, the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal Government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. It’s an indisputable fact, a prevailing international consensus and a widely accepted basic norm governing international relations. China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity brook no challenge, the Resolution 2758 adopted by the UN General Assembly allows no distortion, the historic trend toward China’s reunification will not be stopped, and no country should be absent from the world’s big family committed to the one-China principle.\nChina’s relations with Pacific island countries have continued to deepen. The reestablishment of diplomatic ties between China and Nauru represents the shared aspiration of Nauru and the Pacific islands countries, and serves the fundamental and long-term interests of China and Nauru. The two countries have started a new chapter in bilateral relations and opened the door of friendly cooperation and common development. China will uphold the “four full respects” policy and work with Nauru in various fields based on equality, mutual respect, mutually beneficial cooperation, openness and inclusiveness for the benefit of the two peoples and their future generations.\nThere are still a handful of countries who still have so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan. We call on these countries to recognize the trend, seize the historic opportunities, and stand on the side of the international community, on the side of international justice and on the right side of history. Yet it’s never too late to welcome new friends. China stands ready to turn a new page with these countries on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240124_11232304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-24","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The Philippines’ President Marcos Jr. last night in an interview openly reiterated that the Philippines is committed to the one-China policy and that has not changed and will not change. The Philippines does not endorse Taiwan independence. Taiwan is a province of China and the matter they will be brought together again is an internal matter. What’s China’s comment?","We appreciate the Philippines reaffirming its commitment to the one-China policy and emphasizing that Taiwan is a province of China and the Philippines does not endorse “Taiwan independence.”\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Realizing the complete reunification in China is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. Any attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” is doomed to failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240124_11232304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-25","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Daily","China National Intellectual Property Administration said recently, by the end of 2023, China (excluding Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan) owned 4.015 million domestic invention patents, making itself one of the world’s leading countries in the area of IP. How do you see the impact of China’s achievements in innovation and IPR protection on the world?","The number of invention patents is an important indicator to measure a country’s scientific and technological development and economic growth. In 1985, China officially implemented its first Patent Law. It used to take 31 years for China to have 1 million domestic invention patents in force, but now it only takes one year and a half to have another one. China has become the first country in the world with more than 4 million domestic invention patents in force, whose impetus for innovation and vitality for development continue to thrive and upgrade.\nAccording to the Global Innovation Index 2023 issued by the World Intellectual Property Organization last year, China ranked 12th, becoming the world’s highest ranking middle-income economy, and outnumbered all other countries for the first time in terms of its ownership of the top 100 science and technology clusters worldwide. This reflects that the international community has spoken highly of China’s innovation capability.\nBy stepping up IPR protection, China has brought new opportunities to expand mutually beneficial cooperation with other countries. In recent years, China has continued to improve the mechanisms for international IP cooperation, and established cooperative relations on IP with more than 80 countries and regions and international organizations. We have actively responded to and addressed the concerns and requests on IP of foreign companies, strictly protected their IPR in accordance with the law, and stayed committed to building a market-oriented, law-based and internationalized business environment. Foreign companies have become more and more satisfied with China’s IPR protection, and an increasing number of foreign companies have come to invest and operate in China to share the dividends of China’s development and its supersize market.\nWith enhanced sci-tech innovation capability, China has provided new driving forces for green and sustainable development in the world. China has fully leveraged the role of patent in promoting sci-tech innovation and the development of new industries and new arenas to boost the rapid development of green and low-carbon industries represented by electric vehicles, lithium batteries and solar cells. Key Chinese companies with top ten sales of new energy vehicles own over 100,000 international patents in force and the number is on a trajectory of rapid growth. China is also among the leading countries in terms of the growth rate of international patent applications for solid-state batteries and the number of international patent applications for solar cells. These have effectively boosted the development of global green and low-carbon technologies and industries of the future.\nChina’s achievements in IP development have become a distinct manifestation of its high-quality development and Chinese modernization. Going forward, we are confident that China’s potential of innovation-driven development will be further unleashed, which will lay the basis for and empower the advancement of high-quality development and the building of a new development paradigm, and make greater contribution to the innovation-driven development of the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347687.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240125_11233259.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-25","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Japanese business leaders visited China and met with Premier Li Qiang this week. According to Japanese media reports, one of their concerns is on China’s Counterespionage Law and the detention of Japanese nationals accused of engaging in espionage activities. Will China take measures to ensure the lawful rights and interests of the Japanese business community in China are protected?","First, to answer your question about the Counterespionage Law: according to the principle of sovereignty, every country has the right to safeguard national security through domestic legislation, which is a universal practice. All the law enforcement and judicial activities of China are carried out based on facts and the law. Companies that conduct lawful operation have nothing to worry about. We welcome companies from all countries, including Japanese companies, to seize China’s development opportunities and share in China’s development dividends, so as to realize greater development.\nYou mentioned the visit to China by the delegation of Japan’s economic sector. I would like to share with you more about the visit.\nThis morning, Premier of the State Council Li Qiang met with the delegation of Japan’s economic sector led by Chairman of the Japan Business Federation Tokura Masakazu, Chairman of the Japan-China Economic Association Shindo Kosei and Chairman of the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry Kobayashi Ken at the Great Hall of the People. Over 200 leaders of Japan’s major companies attended the meeting.\nPremier Li Qiang stated that the China-Japan relations are at an important juncture of taking stock of the past and envisioning the future. In November last year, President Xi Jinping met with Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in San Francisco and the two leaders reached important common understandings, providing important strategic guidance for the growth of China-Japan relations. All sectors in China and Japan need to work together to revisit our original aspiration of the normalization of diplomatic relations between the two countries, adhere to the right direction of peace, friendship and cooperation and implement the political consensus that they should be cooperative partners rather than threats to each other, so as to bring the China-Japan relations back to the track of sound development. China hopes that Japan can properly handle historical, Taiwan-related and other issues of principle.\nPremier Li Qiang pointed out that the two countries’ economy are deeply connected. Economic and trade cooperation are playing an important role in our bilateral relations as an anchor and propeller. China stands ready to work with Japan to tap on our potentials for cooperation, continue to share development opportunities, support companies from our two countries to enhance cooperation in such areas as technological innovation, digital economy, green development, healthcare and elderly care and together keep industrial and supply chains stable and unimpeded for higher-level complementarity and mutual benefit. We hope that the economic sector in Japan will play a positive role in advancing win-win cooperation between China and Japan. China is committed to its fundamental national policy of opening up and will continue to foster a market-oriented, law-based and internationalized business environment. We welcome companies from Japan and other countries to continue to invest in China and hope that Japan will do better in providing an open, fair and non-discriminatory business environment for Chinese companies in Japan.\nHeads of the three groups from Japan’s economic sector stated that Japan and China are each other’s important neighbor. They hope that the two countries will return to their original aspiration of friendship, enhance close exchanges between all sectors and at all levels, and build a constructive and stable Japan-China relationship based on common strategic interests. China is a major engine driving global economic growth. The Japanese economic sector is deeply encouraged by China’s sound and steady economic growth and would like to work with China to enhance cooperation in trade, environmental protection, the green economy, healthcare, rehabilitation and other areas, promote cross-border travel, advance regional economic cooperation and make positive contribution to the growth of Japan-China relations and peace and prosperity in Asia and beyond.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347687.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240125_11233259.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-25","Wang Wenbin","Bloomberg","You said that the Japanese side should work harder. What aspect they should work hard on? Can you tell us?","I just briefed you on the meeting between Premier Li Qiang and the Japanese delegation from the economic sector. I would like to reiterate that the various sectors in China and Japan need to work together to revisit our original aspiration of the normalization of diplomatic relations between the two countries, adhere to the right direction of peace, friendship and cooperation and implement the political consensus that they should be cooperative partners rather than threats to each other. We also hope that Japan can properly handle historical, Taiwan-related and other issues of principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347687.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240125_11233259.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-25","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The US Navy destroyer USS John Finn transited through the Taiwan Strait on Wednesday. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","On the US destroyer USS John Finn’s transit through the Taiwan Strait, the Spokesperson for the PLA Eastern Theater Command has issued a statement on China’s solemn position.\nI would like to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and China remains unwavering in our determination to defend the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. After the elections in the Taiwan region, we have seen negative statements and actions from the US side, which sent wrong messages to “Taiwan independence” forces. What the US did violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and contravenes the commitments repeatedly reiterated by US leaders of not supporting “Taiwan independence”, not supporting “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan”, and not seeking to use the Taiwan question as a tool to contain China. The US needs to stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop infringement and provocative moves, stop creating troubles undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347687.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240125_11233259.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first: according to reports, Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities said that the mainland's responses regarding Taiwan's elections do not conform to international perception or the current state of cross-Strait relations, and called on the mainland to respect the election results. What comment does the spokesperson have? The second: a recent survey by a US-Taiwan think tank concluded that…","I will answer the first question first. Taiwan regional elections are local affairs of China. The results of these two Taiwan regional elections show that the Democratic Progressive Party cannot represent mainstream public opinion on the island. No matter how the situation on the island changes, it cannot change the basic fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. It cannot change the universal consensus of the international community to uphold the one-China principle, and it cannot change the historical trend that China will eventually achieve reunification. Eighty years ago, China, the United States, and the United Kingdom issued the Cairo Declaration, which clearly stipulated that “Taiwan, the Chinese territory that Japan stole, shall be returned to China.” Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation, jointly issued by China, the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Soviet Union in 1945, stipulates that “the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” Resolution 2758, adopted by the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly in 1971, made clear that there is only one China in the world, and that there are no “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” This series of documents with international legal effect confirms the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory.\nIt must be emphasized that China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the legal status and fact that Taiwan is part of China's territory have never changed. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan will never be a country, “Taiwan independence” will never succeed, and the attempts of external forces to split China will never succeed. The reunification of the motherland is the destiny of Taiwan. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will speak through action and will always be an iron wall defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nNow I will answer the second question. Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests. We adhere to striving for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. But if “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces provoke, coerce, or even cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is the firm will of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, and it is the sacred mission of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question: It has been reported that the US Department of Defense recently released its first “National Defense Industrial Strategy,” which proposes cooperation with Indo-Pacific countries to build a strong defense industrial base and production capacity in order to prepare for potential future conflicts in the region. A US Assistant Secretary of Defense said that China poses an…","I will answer the first question first. The US report deliberately uses China as a pretext, hypes a nonexistent “China threat,” and we firmly oppose this. Facts have repeatedly proven that the development of China’s military strength has always been the development of a force for world peace. This is a matter of public consensus in the international community, and the US slanders and accusations are completely invalid. At the same time, we must point out that China firmly opposes the United States forming small cliques in the Asia-Pacific region and fomenting bloc confrontation.\nRegarding your second question, yesterday my colleague, Senior Colonel Shi Yi, spokesperson of the Eastern Theater Command, already made a statement on this matter. I want to emphasize that whether it is “using Taiwan to contain China” or “relying on the United States to seek independence,” both are doomed to fail.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan’s defense department recently issued an announcement stating that the PLA conducted joint sea-air combat readiness patrols around the island of Taiwan. Spokesperson, what is the purpose of this military action?","Recently, the PLA Eastern Theater Command organized routine joint sea and air combat readiness patrols in the sea and airspace around Taiwan island, further raising the level of realistic training and enhancing the combat capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe PLA will continue to train and prepare for combat, and will continue to regularly organize relevant military operations.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Taiwan military has signed a contract with the American Institute in Taiwan, under which the United States will provide “missile system technical support services” to Taiwan from this year through 2027, with a total amount of about NT$770 million (about US$24 million). In addition, the Taiwan military plans to purchase T-11 parachutes from the United States for use by special forces.…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no interference from any external force. For their own selfish interests, the DPP authorities squander the hard-earned money of ordinary Taiwan people on buying US equipment. This is utterly quenching thirst with poison, and will only push Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and peril.\n“Taiwan independence” is a deadly poison, and it leads only to a dead end. A few US-made weapons cannot buy Taiwan's security. To defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the Chinese People's Liberation Army has always dared to act and is sure to win.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Taiwan's \"Ministry of National Defense\" has successively detected airborne balloons from the mainland approaching or flying over Taiwan's airspace, and the Taiwanese public is paying close attention. May I ask the spokesperson to further explain which units release these airborne balloons and what their purpose is?","First, let me correct one statement: Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called “Ministry of National Defense.” As for the balloon issue you raised, please inquire with the competent authorities. We believe the DPP authorities' related hype is a habitual tactic to stir up cross-Strait opposition and confrontation. It is meaningless and doomed to fail.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have three questions. First, on the 5th, the United States, South Korea, and Japan held their first trilateral Indo-Pacific dialogue. In the joint statement issued afterward, China was mentioned many times, either by name or implicitly. On the South China Sea issue, the three sides strongly reaffirmed their firm commitment to international law, upheld freedom of navigation and overflight, and opposed any…","Let me answer the first question. China has noted that the United States, Japan, and South Korea held relevant dialogues and issued related documents, and China expresses strong dissatisfaction with the improper content concerning China in those documents. China firmly opposes certain countries cobbling together exclusive “small circles,” brutally interfering in China’s internal affairs, attacking and smearing China, and inciting confrontation and antagonism. On the South China Sea issue, China firmly safeguards its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, while committing to properly resolve differences with the relevant parties concerned through dialogue and consultation. Individual extraregional countries flaunting military strength and inciting confrontation in the South China Sea are not conducive to peace and stability there. Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference.\nOn the second question: We are highly concerned about the relevant exercises NATO recently held, and we have also noted some improper remarks about China made recently by the NATO Secretary General. As a regional military organization, NATO has since its founding repeatedly launched and participated in wars, and in recent years it has continuously encroached on the Asia-Pacific, using the nonexistent so-called “China threat” to stir up bloc confrontation and threaten regional security. It can be said that NATO is a walking “war machine,” bringing turmoil wherever it goes. We urge NATO to stop fabricating lies and stop its dangerous conduct that stirs up trouble in the Asia-Pacific. It should view China and the development of the Chinese military objectively and rationally, and do more good for world peace, rather than the opposite.\nOn the third question: We believe that the Philippines developing alliance relations with relevant countries must not undermine China’s legitimate rights and interests in the South China Sea. At the same time, we firmly oppose the United States meddling and stirring up trouble on the South China Sea issue, egging on and supporting the Philippine side in infringing on rights and provoking incidents, and aggravating maritime tensions. On maritime disputes, China adheres to peaceful settlement through negotiation and consultation, while firmly safeguarding its own territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-01-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have three questions. First, after the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States in San Francisco, the two militaries have carried out exchanges at multiple levels and in multiple fields. Please introduce the plans for China-US military exchanges in 2024. Second, you just mentioned that the 19th annual meeting of the Western Pacific Naval Symposium will be held in Qingdao in April this…","On the first question: I have just introduced the relevant situation, particularly the meeting of the China-U.S. Military Maritime and Air Safety Consultation Mechanism. It must be stressed that for the two militaries of China and the United States to carry out communication and exchanges, they must first establish correct strategic judgments of each other, and must be based on equality and mutual respect. This year marks the 45th anniversary of the establishment of China-U.S. diplomatic relations. We hope that the U.S. side will earnestly respect China's core interests, view China and the Chinese military's development objectively and rationally, implement the important consensus reached by the heads of state of the two countries together with the Chinese side, and jointly promote the healthy, stable and sustainable development of relations between the two militaries.\nOn the second question: The United States is a member of the Western Pacific Naval Symposium. In accordance with the requirements of the Symposium's Charter, the Chinese side has already sent invitations to attend to all member states and observer states. We look forward to deepening exchanges and cooperation with all countries and making positive contributions to building a community with a shared future for mankind in the oceans.\nOn the third question: The Eastern Theater Command has already made a statement on this matter. On the Taiwan question, our policy has always been clear, and can be summarized as three nevers: Taiwan will never be a country, “Taiwan independence” will never succeed, and the scheme of external forces to split China will never succeed.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/16283052.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-01-26","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwanese officials have said that the Chinese mainland seeks to seize Taiwan’s “diplomatic relations.” In fact, it does not rule out the possibility that the Chinese mainland will use the Tuvalu elections to maliciously manipulate issues and influence specific candidates. What does the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have to say about this?","The resumption of China-Nauru diplomatic ties shows to the world again that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. The big family of nations committed to the one-China principle will continue to expand, which is a fact that will not change no matter how “Taiwan independence” and their supporters think otherwise or what the DPP authorities say. We urge a handful of countries who still keep so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan to keep up with the trend of the times and join the family of nations that endorse the one-China principle as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347688.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240126_11234178.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-26","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Director of the Office of the Central Commission for Foreign Affairs Wang Yi will visit Thailand today and will meet with the US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan. Do you have any details to offer on his visit?","To maintain strategic communication between Director Wang Yi and Advisor Jake Sullivan is an important common understanding between the two presidents of China and the US. During the new round of meetings, Director Wang Yi will state China’s position on issues such as China-US relations and the Taiwan question and exchange views with the US on international and regional issues of mutual interest.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347688.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240126_11234178.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-01-30","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi visited Thailand from January 26 to 29. Can you brief us on the highlights of the visit? What results have been achieved and what common understandings have been reached through the visit?","Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi visited Thailand upon invitation from January 26 to 29.\nDuring the visit, Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Her Royal Highness Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn and Prime Minister Srettha Thavisin respectively. Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Parnpree Bahiddha-Nukara held annual consultation and jointly met the press.\nThe Thai side stated that Thailand highly values the Thailand-China comprehensive strategic cooperative partnership and attaches great importance to enhancing its friendly cooperation with China. Thailand firmly upholds the one-China principle and does not conduct any official interaction with Taiwan. Thailand congratulates China on holding a successful Central Conference on Work Relating to Foreign Affairs and agrees with President Xi Jinping’s proposal of building an equal and orderly multipolar world and a universally beneficial and inclusive economic globalization. Thailand stands ready to work with China to jointly build a China-Thailand community with a shared future, strengthen coordination on regional and international issues, carry out substantive cooperation on implementing the three global initiatives, enhance Belt and Road cooperation, uphold multilateralism, oppose decoupling and severing of supply chains, and keep the industrial and supply chains stable and smooth.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi said China and Thailand are as close as one family. Our two countries are good neighbors, good friends and good partners. We will celebrate the 50th anniversary of China-Thailand diplomatic relations next year. China will focus on building a China-Thailand community with a shared future for enhanced stability, prosperity and sustainability, strengthen practical cooperation across the board and add new dimensions to China-Thailand relations. Our two countries are comprehensive strategic cooperative partners. Enhanced friendship and mutual trust between China and Thailand helps safeguard peace in Asia, maintaining close and mutually beneficial cooperation between China and Thailand help energize regional development, and accelerated progress in building a China-Thailand community with a shared future will make humanity’s future more promising.\nDuring the visit, the two sides reached a series of common understandings:\nFirst, enhancing high-level exchanges. The two sides will work together to put into action important common understandings between leaders of our two countries, deepen strategic guidance, continue to render each other support on issues that bear on each other’s core interests and major concerns and jointly plan for events celebrating the 50th anniversary of China-Thailand diplomatic relations next year.\nSecond, focusing on mutually beneficial cooperation. The two sides will actively advance high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, speed up the construction of the China-Thailand Railway, fully implement the vision of interconnected development of China, Laos and Thailand, and complete the building of the Trans-Asian Railway’s mid-line section at an early date. The two sides will strengthen cooperation in such fields as agricultural trade, NEVs, digital economy and green development to benefit the two peoples with the dividend of building a China-Thailand community with a shared future.\nThird, boosting people-to-people and cultural exchanges. One of the highlights of the visit is the signing of the agreement between the two sides on the mutual exemption of visa requirements for holders of ordinary passports. The two countries will usher in a visa-free era. We will jointly enhance the public foundation for the China-Thailand community with a shared future. The bilateral people-to-people exchanges will be brought to a new height. The two sides will strengthen law enforcement and security cooperation and jointly fight transnational crimes including online gambling and telecom fraud for a secure and worry-free environment for the bilateral exchanges and cooperation.\nFourth, strengthening multilateral coordination. The two sides will stay committed to the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence, firmly oppose zero-sum game and winner-takes-all, practice true multilateralism and open regionalism, build a peaceful, safe and secure, prosperous, beautiful and amicable home for China and ASEAN, accelerate the consultation on a code of conduct in the South China Sea, and jointly safeguard ASEAN centrality. China supports Thailand in serving as the co-chair of Lancang-Mekong cooperation and in building a Lancang-Mekong community with a shared future of peace and prosperity.\nThe two countries signed cooperation documents including a protocol regarding the export of Thai agricultural products to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347690.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202401/t20240130_11236312.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-01-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 30 — On January 30, the Civil Aviation Administration of China announced the cancellation of the southbound flight offset on route M503 and the activation of connecting routes W122 and W123 for M503, operated from west to east. In response, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on the 30th, saying that route M503 lies within the Shanghai Flight Information Region, and that establishing and activating this route is a routine part of mainland civil aviation airspace management.\nChen Binhua said that since route M503 was opened in March 2015, it has operated smoothly, safely and reliably, and has played a positive role in improving flight operations, meeting people’s livelihood needs and promoting economic development.\nHe said that the cancellation of the southbound flight offset on M503 and the activation of connecting routes W122 and W123 operated from west to east are intended to ease flight growth pressure in the relevant regions, ensure flight safety, reduce flight delays, safeguard passengers’ rights, and meet the needs of air transport development in the Asia-Pacific region. They are also conducive to improving cross-Strait flight operations and further facilitating personnel exchanges across the Strait, and are in line with the common interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240130_12597035.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear journalist friends, hello everyone. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Today's press conference is hosted by me. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","As the Spring Festival approaches, we note that some localities have begun visiting and extending greetings to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Does the TAO have any related arrangements? Please introduce the relevant details.","Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland are builders of the mainland’s economic and social development, participants and contributors to comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization, and also active promoters and firm defenders of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots. Party committees and governments at all levels have consistently attached importance to and cared about the work, study, and life of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth on the mainland, as well as the production and operation of Taiwan enterprises. At the end and beginning of each year, they also visit and extend greetings in various ways, listen to opinions and suggestions, and coordinate the resolution of difficulties.\nAs the traditional Chinese festival of Spring Festival approaches, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has issued letters of condolence to the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises and the provincial Taiwan associations, extending sincere condolences and festive greetings to the broad masses of Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan youth. It encourages them to actively integrate into advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization and to achieve new and greater development. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council also recently issued a notice requiring Taiwan Affairs Offices in all localities to carry out, during the Spring Festival, visits, condolences, and New Year friendship gatherings with rich content and diverse forms, going deep into enterprises, factories, and schools, so that Taiwan compatriots in various places can live comfortably and spend a warm New Year.\nLocalities, following the requirements of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council’s notice, have carried out a variety of heartwarming activities. Let me give a few examples.\nJiangsu Provincial Governor Xu Kunlin went to Suzhou to investigate Taiwan-funded enterprises and held a symposium, gaining an in-depth understanding of enterprise development, earnestly listening to opinions and suggestions, and encouraging everyone to seize the opportunities of the new era and firmly build confidence in development. Taiwan Affairs Offices across Jiangsu actively carried out diverse activities such as symposiums and exchanges, visits and condolences, and spring greeting gatherings, sending New Year greetings to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.\nThe Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office carried out the “Going to the Grassroots, Making Friends” New Year blessing activity, presenting the “Policy Service Package” to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in Beijing. It continued to advance the “I Do Practical Things for Taiwan Compatriots” series of activities, and sent New Year calendars, spring couplets, the character “福” (fortune), and dragon-year mascots. It also organized representatives of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in Beijing to watch the large-scale Chinese-style dance drama “Li Bai,” so that Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan youth, and Taiwan students felt the warmth of home thousands of miles away.\nChongqing carried out a series of visits, condolences, and friendship activities, extending festive condolences and Spring Festival greetings to Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan students, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan enterprises in Chongqing. It visited and condoled more than 1,700 Taiwan compatriots in Chongqing and representatives of cross-Strait marriage families, carefully organized a 2024 New Year exchange activity for representatives of Taiwan compatriots in Chongqing, and organized everyone to make dumplings together, write spring couplets, send blessings, and share the New Year’s Eve dinner, welcoming the Spring Festival together.\nThe Gansu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office went deep into Taiwan enterprises across localities to investigate and offer condolences, learned about the production and operation of Taiwan-funded enterprises, comforted local Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, and held provincial New Year tea gatherings for Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan students, and Taiwan businesspeople, as well as spring tea gatherings for Taiwan compatriot dependents.\nThe Guangzhou Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office visited and condoled more than 1,000 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan dependents and more than 70 Taiwan enterprises. It organized Taiwan youth in Guangzhou to carry out the spring welcoming activity “Savoring Chinese Culture, Admiring the Fragrant Snow of Liuxi,” and to take part in the “Most Beautiful Guangzhou” photography competition. Cross-Strait youth together admired the plum blossoms in full bloom across more than 3,000 mu along the Liuxi River, together appreciated the historical depth of Chinese culture and Lingnan culture, and together welcomed the Dragon Year Spring Festival.\nThe Shenyang Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, together with the municipal Taiwan Federation and the Municipal Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, jointly held the “Joyfully Welcome the New Spring, Together Talk of Reunion” New Year friendship gathering, where representatives of Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan students, and Taiwan businesspeople in Shenyang came together, enjoyed winter scenery, experienced the joy of ice and snow, and jointly welcomed the festive Spring Festival.\nLiaocheng City in Shandong Province carried out the “Cross-Strait Welcoming Spring Together, Ink Fragrance Carries Blessings” activity, organizing calligraphers and painters to write more than a hundred couplets and “福” characters for local Taiwan compatriots and mail them to their relatives on the island. It will also carry out full-coverage visits and condolences to local Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan students, and extend New Year greetings to them.\nThe Zhangping Taiwan Farmers’ Entrepreneurship Park in Fujian will carry out New Spring visits and condolence activities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, and hold a cherry blossom cultural and tourism festival, where farmers from Zhangping and Taiwan will spend the festival together, enjoy the scenery together, and discuss good ideas for integrated development of cross-Strait agriculture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597329.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Some officials on the island have claimed that the mainland side will, before Lai Ching-te, the newly elected leader of Taiwan, takes office on “5.20,” “increase pressure on Taiwan through political, economic and military means,” in order to influence the content of Lai's inaugural address and put pressure on his cross-Strait policy. What is your response?","The results of Taiwan’s elections fully demonstrate that the mainstream public opinion on the island is: peace rather than war, development rather than decline, exchanges rather than estrangement, and cooperation rather than confrontation. After the election concluded, broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots hope to improve and develop cross-Strait relations, and worry that the DPP will continue to pursue “independence” provocations and aggravate tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. If the DPP does not repent, turns its back on public opinion, and continues down the evil path of seeking “independence” and provoking, or the old path of cross-Strait confrontation, it will only push Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597330.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","香港《经济导报》记者","After the two elections in Taiwan concluded, the island immediately saw negative economic effects, including net selling by foreign investors (overselling) and an expanded depreciation of the New Taiwan dollar. Some public opinion holds that Lai Ching-te's election may increase Taiwan's security risks, and that the foreign capital “flight wave” fully reflects foreign investors' distrust and anxiety. What is your…","We have noted the relevant reports. What you mentioned reflects foreign investors' concern that the DPP stubbornly insists on separatist “Taiwan independence” positions and continues to seek “independence” and provoke, which aggravates the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait and thereby harms their own vital interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","After Lai Ching-te was elected, society on the island became pessimistic about economic prospects. People worry that the suspension of ECFA would seriously affect the development of industry and commerce on the island. “If cross-Strait relations are bad, it means goods cannot get out and people cannot get in, and everyone can only live a hard life.” What comments do you have on this?","Facts from both positive and negative cases have long proven that when cross-strait relations are good, Taiwan does well. They have also long proven that ECFA is a good agreement that benefits Taiwan compatriots, a “good deal” that all sectors on the island care about, and by no means the “poison” that the DPP slanders it as. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family; when relatives look on each other with affection, things go well. No one hopes more than we do that cross-strait relations will be good, and that Taiwan compatriots can enjoy good days of peace, tranquility, and prosperity. As for whether ECFA can continue to take effect and be implemented, it depends on what cross-strait policy line the DPP authorities pursue, including whether they can face up to public concerns and take concrete measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597327.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Rosenberg, Chairman of the American Institute in Taiwan, recently said that “UN Resolution 2758 did not decide Taiwan’s status, did not exclude any country from establishing ‘diplomatic relations’ with Taiwan, and did not exclude Taiwan from meaningful participation in the UN system space,” and this view has sparked controversy. Public opinion on the island questions whether the US is playing a two-faced game and…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. This is a fact confirmed by a series of international treaties and documents, including the 1943 Cairo Declaration, the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation, and UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 of 1971, and it is also the solemn commitment the United States made in the three China-US joint communiqués.\nApart from being part of China, Taiwan has no other international legal status. Any words or deeds that distort the authority and validity of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 are ignorant, malicious, and ultimately futile.\nWe urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués in practice, implement its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” in earnest, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597326.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","Ren Xueli, a well-known U.S. expert on the Taiwan Strait, recently said that Lai Ching-te faces many constraints, so she is not very worried that he will move toward formal “Taiwan independence.” What she is more worried about is that certain people in the United States may incite or even force Lai Ching-te to take dangerous actions that are not in Taiwan's interests but that he cannot oppose, just as Tsai…","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Anti-China forces in the United States always want to play the “Taiwan card,” pour fuel on the fire and stir up trouble in the Taiwan Strait, putting Taiwan in danger and harming the interests of the Taiwan people, with sinister intentions. Facts have already proven, and will continue to prove, that we will leave no room whatsoever for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and we will make not the slightest compromise or concession to any external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597325.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The New York Times recently cited a pre-election public opinion poll on the island, which found that only 34% of respondents consider the US a “trustworthy country,” down 11% from 2021. This shows that Taiwan residents are full of contradictions and doubts about whether the US is trustworthy. What comment do you have on this?","This fully shows that more and more people in Taiwan have come to recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders cannot be relied upon. The United States, at all times, only looks after its own interests, and its so-called “support for Taiwan” actually harms and destroys Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597323.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Taiwan regional legislature will hold elections for its presiding officer and deputy presiding officer on February 1. Because neither the Kuomintang nor the DPP has won a majority of seats, the voting intentions of the Taiwan People's Party, which holds 8 legislative seats, are considered to have a decisive impact on the election result. What comments do you have on this?","In the two elections held on the island this month, 60% of voters cast their ballots for the Kuomintang and the Taiwan People’s Party, fully demonstrating that the DPP, after eight years in power with abuse of governing power, has lost the people’s support. As for the Taiwan regional legislative elections you mentioned, public opinion on the island has pointed out that the two major “opposition parties,” which advocate “taking the DPP off the shelves” and a change of ruling party through elections, should follow the island’s public opinion, strengthen cooperation, and provide effective oversight and strong checks on the DPP, so as to live up to the public’s expectations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Wang Yi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and director of the Central Foreign Affairs Office, met with US National Security Advisor Sullivan in Bangkok and discussed the Taiwan question. Taiwan's foreign affairs department responded, saying it thanks the US side for reiterating its firm position of supporting the maintenance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It claimed that…","The one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. It is also the political foundation on which we have established diplomatic relations with 183 countries around the world. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” stance and arbitrarily provoke “independence,” making them the greatest “troublemakers” for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视海峡两岸记者","The Straits Exchange Foundation said that in 2023 it assisted in handling 102 cases of Taiwan residents stranded in the mainland, an increase of 19 cases over 2022, a year-on-year rise of 22.9%. It stated that these cases are mostly related to business failures in the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","We continuously optimize the business environment for Taiwan-related matters. Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland are generally doing well, and they are confident about investing and doing business on the mainland. We uphold the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” and do everything we can to resolve practical problems arising from exchanges between cross-Strait compatriots and to protect their lawful rights and interests. For the very few Taiwan compatriots who are stranded on the mainland due to illness, documents, or other personal reasons, relevant departments and localities care deeply. They have consistently provided active medical assistance and living care and, according to the wishes of the individuals concerned, have helped them return to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, Taiwan residents have been enthusiastically discussing Wong Kar-wai's mainland TV drama “Blossoms Shanghai.” Some public opinion on the island holds that the connection between Taiwan and Shanghai is very deep, and that island audiences are easily moved after watching “Blossoms Shanghai.” We note that in recent years, mainland TV series have consistently held considerable appeal for Taiwan residents.…","《繁花》 (Blossoms) tells the story of ordinary people from across the country gathering on the Shanghai Bund during the wave of reform and opening-up in the 1990s, seizing opportunities and striving hard to make their way. It praises an indomitable, upward-striving spirit. After it aired, it sparked heated discussion and wide resonance online and among drama fans, including fans in Taiwan.\nIncluding 《繁花》, outstanding cultural works such as mainland film and television dramas have been quite popular on the island in recent years. Besides the merit of the works themselves, this is also because compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same written language and the same ancestry, and their emotions are connected, so they readily grasp the plots and resonate emotionally. This is the power of culture! The common cultural roots and emotional resonance of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait will not diminish, even as time passes, even across mountains and seas, and even when artificially obstructed. They have never changed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Trump recently criticized Taiwan in an interview for stealing American chip business and refused to say whether he would \"defend Taiwan.\" Taiwan's external exchange department responded that Taiwan-U.S. economic and trade relations are close. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The US has always followed “America First”; Taiwan may go from “chess piece” to “discarded piece” at any time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","东方卫视记者","First question: Taiwan's compulsory military service was changed from four months to one year. Recently, the first batch of one-year conscripts in Taiwan enlisted, but this move has caused constant complaints and criticism on the island. Young people in Taiwan have also pessimistically said they must “fend for themselves.” What comment do you have on this? Second question: Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an recently said…","On the first question: after the DPP authorities introduced a one-year extension of the compulsory military service period, complaints and criticism have continued to mount on the island, which shows that this move is unpopular. The DPP authorities are attempting to “pursue independence through force,” making Taiwan’s young people cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence,” and their intentions are deserving of condemnation. I must emphasize that as long as the root of “Taiwan independence” is not eliminated, peace across the Taiwan Strait will remain difficult to secure. Only by rejecting “Taiwan independence” can peace in the Taiwan Strait be effectively guaranteed and the people of Taiwan be able to live in peace and without worry.\nOn the second question: Taipei City has invited Shanghai to take part in its Lantern Festival events for many years, and this year Shanghai will continue to send a delegation in response to the invitation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and members of a family should naturally visit and interact with one another more often.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","First question: The MAC website recently updated content on acts suspected of violating the Hong Kong National Security Law, stating that if Taiwan residents fund Hong Kong residents who have been wanted through online subscription and crowdfunding platforms, they will be charged with suspected offenses of funding others to split the country. What is your comment?\nSecond question: According to reports, the DPP…","Question one: The National Security Law for Hong Kong is the anchor that keeps Hong Kong's long-term stability and long-term prosperity and stability secure. Safeguarding national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity is a common obligation of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Hong Kong and Taiwan.\nQuestion two: The DPP authorities established this so-called center to further manipulate “cognitive warfare,” with the aim of making their lies more convincing, making their opponents suffer more, and deceiving more votes. We believe that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots have already seen through it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Following Nauru's severing of so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan, a senior Tuvaluan official said that after domestic elections, it will re-examine its “foreign relations” with Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. Adhering to the one-China principle is a common understanding of the international community; it is the general trend and the aspiration of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The Civil Aviation Administration announced yesterday that starting February 1, the M503 offset route will be cancelled, which has drawn high attention from all sectors in Taiwan. The closest distance of this route to the \"median line of the Taiwan Strait\" is 7.8 kilometers, and Taiwan authorities and U.S. think tanks believe this is blurring the \"median line of the Taiwan Strait\" and exerting…","On the first question: The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. There is no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” Route M503 is a civil aviation route within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. Opening this route is to alleviate congestion on the relevant airspace routes and to ensure aviation safety.\nOn the second question: Under the arrangements for cross-Strait air transport, cross-Strait airlines may arrange no more than 890 passenger flights per week in total between 61 waypoints on the mainland and 10 waypoints in Taiwan. Direct cross-Strait air links have greatly facilitated travel between people on both sides and have played an important role in increasing the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nSince last year, as epidemic prevention and control has entered a new stage, we have followed the common wishes of compatriots on both sides and actively promoted the resumption of waypoints on direct cross-Strait air routes. At present, 14 mainland cities operate over 500 passenger flights per week on cross-Strait routes, carrying more than 80,000 passenger trips. Although cross-Strait flights and passenger volumes have increased compared with the epidemic period, because of limited waypoints, cross-Strait travel overall remains quite inconvenient. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople eagerly hope that direct cross-Strait waypoints will fully resume as soon as possible.\nWe have long been preparing for the full resumption of cross-Strait air routes. The DPP authorities should, as soon as possible, cancel the unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport and meet the travel needs of people on both sides, especially the Taiwan public.\nOn the third question: Regarding the opening of cross-Strait sightseeing tourism, on May 19, 2023, the mainland's tourism authority publicly announced the resumption of travel agencies operating group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents. As for mainland tourists traveling to Taiwan, the obstacle does not lie on the mainland side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","The Taipei Ningxia Night Market recently drew attention for holding a “Subject Three” dance competition, and some have jokingly called it “dancing to rule Taiwan.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","\"Subject Three\" (Kemu San) has recently been very popular online. People often see that a song or a dance step quickly becomes a craze on both sides of the Strait through social media platforms. I noticed that a related competition recently held at the Ningxia Night Market in Taipei saw enthusiastic public participation and cheers all around, and I think this novel form of creativity is quite good. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' worry about so-called \"dancing Taiwan into unification\" is as ridiculous as their recent ban on the import of Guangxi river snail noodles from the mainland. Regarding things like \"Subject Three\" and river snail noodles that are loved by Taiwan's young people, the reason why the pan-green politicians and \"Taiwan independence\" elements always treat them as a major enemy has only one answer: it is because these things come from the mainland. In the eyes of these pan-green politicians and \"Taiwan independence\" elements, eating river snail noodles will be \"united front\" work, and dancing \"Subject Three\" will be \"dancing unification,\" which is entirely \"anti-China\" to the point of being anti-intelligence. What I want to say is that people on both sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, customs, and traditions, and compatriots on both sides, especially young people, have the same food preferences and cultural tastes, and influence each other in popular culture and lifestyles, which is entirely normal. Now, young people in Taiwan like to eat mainland snacks, like to watch mainland films and television dramas, and like to sing the \"divine songs\" of mainland short-video platforms, which has already become a trend and a way of life. Some Democratic Progressive Party politicians and \"Taiwan independence\" elements cannot keep up with the pace of young people and manipulate for political self-interest, and will only be abandoned by young people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Regarding the mainland’s removal of restrictions related to the M503 air route, the Mainland Affairs Council responded that this is another instance, following the mainland’s “unilateral” announcement of the use of the northbound route in 2018, of the mainland publicly announcing related measures without cross-Strait consultation. It is also deliberately using civil aviation to “package improper…","First question. First, the M503 route is a civil aviation route, so the Mainland Affairs Council’s relevant claims are completely untenable. Second, the M503 route lies within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. The route was activated to ease congestion on related airspace routes and to ensure aviation safety. Third, establishing and activating this route is routine work in mainland civil aviation airspace management and does not require consultation with the Taiwan side. As for the Mainland Affairs Council’s intimidation that “[they] will bear the consequences,” Taiwan public opinion has already criticized it.\nSecond question. Regarding floating balloons, since Taiwan compatriots have doubts, I am willing to answer questions and clear up confusion. First, floating balloons are mostly the independent actions of private enterprises. As far as I understand, several hundred to a thousand floating balloons appear in the sky around the world every day. Second, the floating balloons we mentioned are all above 3,000 meters in altitude. They are not the atmosphere balloons hung for weddings or mall openings. I saw Taiwan media report that just yesterday, relevant Taiwan authorities reported a so-called floating balloon coming from the mainland at an altitude of 20,000 feet. Third, floating balloons are mostly used for livelihood purposes such as weather monitoring, and they have been around for a long time. This is nothing new. I advise the DPP authorities not to keep creating such issues for political hype and to stop inciting cross-Strait confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Some Taiwan media recently said that the mainland side provided remuneration to Tuvalu media to report content unfavorable to Taiwan, and attempted to interfere in Tuvalu’s election, undermining the so-called “diplomatic relations” between the two places. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The One-China Principle is the political foundation and premise for our establishment and development of diplomatic relations with countries around the world. Past, present and future, we will absolutely never trade the One-China Principle.\nBuying “recognition” and maintaining “diplomatic allies” with money is a routine tactic of the DPP authorities. To gain political self-interest, they seek “independence” internationally and lavishly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people. This is pure and simple “checkbook diplomacy” and “sucker diplomacy.” It harms Taiwan and its people, becomes a laughingstock, and marks their road to ruin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","海峡之声记者","The mainland recently announced that it will study suspending tariff concessions on some products on the early harvest list under the ECFA. Taiwan's economic authorities said they will lead different industries to jointly seek business opportunities in India, Thailand, and Germany. What is your comment on this?","The statements and actions of the DPP authorities both show that they have no sincerity in facing up to and solving problems, and they cannot solve the issues that Taiwan enterprises and the public truly care about.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Reportedly, Republican Congressman Diaz-Balart and Democratic Congressman Bera, co-chairs of the “Congressional Taiwan Caucus” of the US House of Representatives, recently led a delegation to Taiwan, where they met with Tsai Ing-wen, Lai Ching-te, and Hsiao Bi-khim. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic relations with China, including the United States, and the Taiwan region of China. The US Congress, as part of the US government, should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and stop sending any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","We note that the results of the two elections held in Taiwan in 2024 show that the younger generation on the island is playing an increasingly important role and is an important force that will influence the future development of cross-Strait relations. What will the mainland do in the coming period to attract more Taiwan youth to actively take part in cross-Strait exchanges and integrated development?","The hope of the nation and the future of the people lie with the youth. We warmly welcome Taiwan's young people to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams. We will continue to work with all regions and departments to further improve the systems, policies, and measures that support Taiwan youth in studying, interning, finding employment, and starting businesses on the mainland. We will support cross-strait youth in carrying out diverse exchanges and cooperation, and we will create better conditions and provide more support for Taiwan youth to take part in cross-strait exchanges and integrated development.\nThe mainland is a fertile ground of hope and a great stage for Taiwan youth to grow, develop their talents, and advance their careers. We hope more Taiwan youth will come to the mainland to walk around, look, and try their luck. We believe they will certainly broaden their horizons and seize opportunities, find greater value in personally taking part in the process of cross-strait integrated development and the great rejuvenation of the nation, realize greater dreams, and become an important force supporting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202401/t20240131_12597328.htm"],[2,"2024-01-31","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Taiwan has restored a one-year military service system, and many parents worry about accidental exchanges of fire in the Taiwan Strait. Some of these parents endorse the “1992 Consensus,” and some hold different positions, but overall all of them hope for peace across the Taiwan Strait. The mainland side has also stressed that the last resort is not directed at ordinary Taiwan people. In the view of the TAO, what…","We have repeatedly stated that our refusal to renounce the use of force is directed at a small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and external interference, and is absolutely not directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. As for the concerns of Taiwan residents you mentioned, the DPP's continued rule in Taiwan has heightened concern across Taiwan's sectors, including ordinary people, about the tense and volatile situation in the Taiwan Strait, and even about what you called “accidental exchange of fire.” This shows that people have an increasingly clear understanding of the “Taiwan independence” nature of the DPP. I want to say to these Taiwan compatriots: the more clearly one opposes “Taiwan independence,” and the more resolutely one acts to stop “Taiwan independence,” the more likely peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will be, and the more at ease everyone can feel.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. As the Year of the Dragon Spring Festival approaches, I extend my wishes to the cross-Strait and overseas media friends present, and to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, for a happy New Year and a prosperous Year of the Dragon. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202401/t20240131_12597320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-02-02","Wang Wenbin","The New York Times","The Washington Post reported that Russia had imported more than USD 20 million worth of high-tech precision tooling from Taiwan that can be used in the production of advanced drones. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s stance on this?","I am not aware of that, but I know that Russia stays committed to the one-China principle and firmly opposes “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347693.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240202_11238857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-06","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Guatemala’s Foreign Minister told Reuters on Monday that the country plans to reach out to China to develop formal trade ties, although it plans to maintain its existing relations with Taiwan. Would such an approach by Guatemala be agreeable to the Chinese side?","There is but one China in the world, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. It is also the fundamental prerequisite and political foundation for China to conduct cooperation with all countries including Guatemala.\nOne hundred and eighty-three countries in the world have established diplomatic ties with China, which fully shows that supporting the one-China principle is where the public opinion trends and the arc of history bends. We hope that the new government of Guatemala will follow the general trend and make the right decision as early as possible which will serve the fundamental and long-term interests of the country and the people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347695.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240206_11241581.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-07","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","Governor of Tokyo Koike Yuriko is visiting Taiwan today and will meet Tsai Ing-wen and Lai Ching-te. What’s your response?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and basic trust between the two countries. China strongly opposes official interaction of any form between Taiwan and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. Regarding what you asked, we have expressed concerns to Japan and hope that the relevant party will stay alert and distance themselves from the possibility of being used by “Taiwan independence” forces for political purposes.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347696.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240207_11242572.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-08","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The Philippine Defense Secretary has ordered the military to boost the number of troops and structures in the remote Batanes islands less than 200 kilometers from Taiwan to fortify Manila’s territorial defense capabilities. What’s China’s comment?","China and the Philippines are neighbors across the sea. Friendly exchanges predominate in the history of our bilateral relations. A close neighbor can be more helpful than a distant relative. Neighbors should get along with each other based on the principle of good-neighborliness, friendship, mutual respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity, and non-interference in each others’ internal affairs.\nI want to stress again that the Taiwan question is at the heart of China’s core interests and is a red line and bottom line that must not be crossed. Relevant parties in the Philippines need to understand it clearly, tread carefully and don’t play with fire on this question to avoid being manipulated and eventually hurt.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347697.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240208_11243683.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-08","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Taiwan authorities announced yesterday that a man wanted for suspicion of scam was successfully repatriated from Poland this year. Has China lodged representations to Poland on this?","Liu Hongtao, a resident of Taiwan, China, is suspected of telecom fraud. China made the request to Poland for extradition in accordance with the law to combat crimes and protect the lawful rights and interests of the victims. This is completely legitimate and lawful. China attaches great importance to the protection and advancement of human rights, stands firmly against torture, and has achieved remarkable progress in human rights protection in the judicial area. The ruling by the European Court of Human Rights and its rejection of Poland’s appeal application shows no respect for facts and falls short of justice and fairness. The ruling has no factual ground and is legally untenable. It is in the common interests of the international community to enhance enforcement and judicial cooperation and jointly combat cross-border crimes. China has successfully carried out enforcement and judicial cooperation, including extradition, with many countries, and will continue to work with the rest of the international community to jointly combat cross-border crimes and promote personnel, economic and trade exchanges.\nThere is but one China in the world; Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory; and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We urge Poland to adhere to the one-China principle, handle Taiwan-related issues in a prudent and proper manner and uphold the overall interest of China-Poland relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347697.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240208_11243683.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-02-08","Zhu Fenglian","国台办发言人朱凤莲7日答记者","XINHUA NEWS AGENCY, BEIJING, February 7 — Taiwan's tourism authority announced on the 7th that the group tour plan for Taiwan residents to travel to the mainland, originally scheduled to open after the Spring Festival, will no longer proceed as of today. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 7th, saying: Taiwan residents have long looked forward…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that this will only once again make Taiwan residents and the tourism industry dissatisfied with the DPP authorities’ political manipulation of tourism, obstructing exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and harming the well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240208_12599085.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 14: On the afternoon of the 14th, a fishing boat from Fujian was driven away by the Taiwan side in waters off Kinmen, causing all four people on board to fall into the sea, two of whom died. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said that we express deep condolences and sincere sympathy to the compatriots who died and their families, and…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that over the years, we have upheld the concept of “cross-Strait families are one,” and have done a great deal of work to safeguard the normal fishing operations of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. In particular, we have set up reception facilities for Taiwan fishermen in many coastal areas, providing Taiwan fishing boats and fishermen with assistance such as shelter, supplies, emergency rescue, and relief. In contrast, on the Taiwan side, for some time, the DPP authorities have forcibly seized mainland fishing boats under various pretexts and treated mainland fishermen in a brutal and dangerous manner. This is the main reason why this vicious incident occurred.\nZhu Fenglian stated that we strongly demand that the Taiwan side immediately find out the truth of the incident and assist the families of the deceased fishermen in properly handling the aftermath. We solemnly warn relevant parties on Taiwan to respect the historical fact that fishermen on both sides of the Strait have operated in the traditional fishing grounds of the Taiwan Strait, to ensure the personal safety of mainland fishermen, and to resolutely prevent such incidents from happening again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240215_12600008.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office, said on February 17 that the violent incident on February 14, in which the Taiwan side forcibly expelled mainland fishing boats and two fishermen died, aroused strong indignation across all sectors of the mainland and seriously hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","Zhu Fenglian said: The two sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. Fishermen on both sides of the Strait have fished on the traditional fishing grounds in the waters between Xiamen and Kinmen since ancient times, and there is absolutely no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters.” The mainland side holds goodwill toward Taiwan compatriots, but it will never tolerate the Taiwan side's disregard for the life and property safety of mainland fishermen. The Taiwan side should release the boats and people as soon as possible, properly handle the aftermath, investigate the facts thoroughly, seriously punish the relevant responsible persons, and give an account to the families of the victims and to compatriots on both sides. The mainland side reserves the right to take further measures, and all consequences shall be borne by the Taiwan side.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240217_12600298.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-18","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 18: The Fujian Coast Guard Bureau will strengthen its maritime law enforcement forces and carry out regular law enforcement patrol operations in the waters between Xiamen and Kinmen. In response, TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian said that on February 14 the Taiwan side forcibly drove away Mainland fishing boats, causing the deaths of two fishermen. This treatment of human life as worthless and this hostile attitude have aroused strong indignation across all sectors on the Mainland, seriously hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides, and seriously undermined cross-Strait relations. Regular law enforcement patrols by Mainland maritime authorities help maintain normal order in the relevant waters and safeguard the lives and property of Mainland fishermen. We firmly support this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240218_12600421.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 19 (dateline): Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 19th: After the vicious incident on February 14, in which relevant Taiwan authorities brutally treated mainland fishing boats and two fishermen died, relevant parties in Fujian Province and Quanzhou City continued to communicate with the crew members’ families. They decided that on the 20th, personnel from the Quanzhou Red Cross and others would accompany the families to Kinmen to bring back the two survivors and handle related aftermath matters.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that relevant Taiwan authorities should provide convenience for the crew members’ families and relevant personnel traveling to Kinmen, make proper arrangements, earnestly address their legitimate concerns, cooperate in handling the aftermath, and avoid further harming the feelings between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240219_12600642.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-02-20","Mao Ning","CCTV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi is visiting Spain. King Felipe VI and Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez met with him respectively. Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Minister for Foreign Affairs, European Union and Cooperation José Manuel Albares Bueno held talks and jointly met the press. This is Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s first visit after the Chinese New Year. What major outcomes has this visit achieved, and what role has it…","China and Spain are comprehensive strategic partners. Last year, the two countries marked the 50th anniversary of diplomatic relations and Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez paid a successful visit to China. While meeting with Prime Minister Sánchez, President Xi Jinping proposed that the two countries advance a bilateral relationship with strategic focus. The two sides identified the good experience that has enabled the long-standing friendship between the two countries, which is a commitment to mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit, and made plans together for the growth of bilateral relations. Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s visit to Spain is his second visit to the country in six years. It is aimed to deliver the important common understandings between the leaders of the two countries and get the second 50 years of China-Spain diplomatic relations off to a good start. Spain received Foreign Minister Wang with great hospitality. The visit achieved its objectives and has been a full success.\nThe visit accentuated the strategic stability of China-Spain relations. No matter how the international situation changes, China and Spain have followed the tradition of mutual respect, mutual trust, equality and win-win cooperation, advanced bilateral relations with a steadfast policy of friendship, and supported each other on issues of core interests and major concerns. Having friendly relations with China is a consensus in Spain supported by the royal family, the government and the people. The two sides agreed to continue the momentum of high-level exchanges, cultivate friendship between Chinese and Spanish peoples, and give each other understanding and support on efforts to safeguard national unity and solidarity among ethnic groups. Spain reiterated its firm adherence to the one-China policy.\nThe visit highlighted the bright prospects for open cooperation. China and Spain have deepened economic and trade cooperation in recent years. China has become Spain’s largest trading partner outside the EU and the second largest consumer of its olive oil. Spain is China’s second largest source of imported pork. Chinese companies have actively participated in photovoltaic and wind power development in Spain, and expanded third-party market cooperation. During the visit, the two sides reiterated that they will adhere to open cooperation and promote a number of landmark and demonstrative projects in telecommunications, medical care, electric vehicles and green energy.\nThe visit served to deepen exchanges and mutual learning between the two civilizations. Both China and Spain are ancient civilizations with a time-honored history. Last year, the two sides launched the China-Spain Year of Culture and Tourism, which gave fresh boost to exchanges and mutual learning between the two civilizations. The two sides have been engaged in giant panda cooperation for more than 40 years. The giant pandas living in Spain have bred six cubs in recent years, more than anywhere else in Europe. Giant panda cooperation epitomizes the China-Spain and China-Europe friendship. The Spanish people warmly welcomed and expressed appreciation for China’s announcement that it will send a new pair of young pandas to Spain after the return of the panda family currently living in Spain whose agreement has expired.\nThe visit provides stability for China-Europe relations and the world. Spain is a major EU country. China and Spain share the same or similar views on major international and regional issues. Spain stressed that good relations with China are of great significance to Spain, Europe and the world, and spoke highly of President Xi Jinping’s important ideas such as building a community with a shared future for mankind and the Belt and Road Initiative. The two sides reiterated that they will work together to meet global challenges, promote the sound and stable development of China-Europe relations through China-Spain friendship, and provide a stronger force of stability for a volatile and turbulent world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347699.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240220_11247457.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-20","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwanese authorities called on Beijing to be rational following the incident that involved the Chinese boat and Taiwanese coast guard. Taiwan also said that it will insist to protect its waters. Do you have any comment on this?","This is not a matter related to foreign affairs. I’d refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347699.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240220_11247457.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-02-21","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on February 21 that after the incident on February 14 in which Taiwan's side brutally treated mainland fishing vessels and two fishermen died, a responsible person from the relevant Taiwan authorities claimed that the coast guard personnel's “law enforcement” process was not improper, attempting to cover up their violent conduct; some people on the island made outrageous remarks with an arrogant attitude. Only under strong demands from compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the families of the deceased did the relevant Taiwan authorities admit that Taiwan's coast guard vessel had rammed and caused the mainland fishing boat to capsize, resulting in casualties, but they still shirked responsibility with various excuses and concealed the truth of the incident.\nZhu Fenglian said that three feet of ice does not form in a single day, and this capsizing incident is by no means an isolated case. Since the Democratic Progressive Party came to power in May 2016, Taiwan's side has repeatedly brutally treated mainland fishermen and frequently arbitrarily detained mainland fishing vessels and fishermen. These incidents have seriously harmed the interests of mainland fishermen, caused considerable economic losses to the mainland fishing community, and hurt the feelings of mainland compatriots. We strongly condemn Taiwan's brutal treatment of mainland fishermen, strongly condemn its disregard for human life, its “violent law enforcement,” and its deliberate concealment of the facts, and express our strong indignation at the completely inhumane, indifferent words and deeds Taiwan's side has shown since the incident.\nZhu Fenglian stressed that when lives are at stake, disclosing the truth is only right and proper. We solemnly demand that the relevant Taiwan authorities promptly make the facts public, severely punish the responsible persons, meet the reasonable demands of the families of the deceased, sincerely apologize to the families of the deceased, and give the families of the deceased and compatriots on both sides of the Strait an account. We will resolutely safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of our compatriots and will never allow such incidents to happen again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240221_12601135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-02-22","Mao Ning","Reuters","Today, Mike Gallagher and other US lawmakers emphasized during their visit to Taiwan that the US will continue to support Taiwan, no matter who becomes the next US president. What’s your comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China opposes any form of official interaction between the US and Taiwan authorities and rejects US interference in Taiwan affairs in whatever form or under whatever pretext. We urge the US to be mindful of the extreme complexity and sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, prudently and properly handle issues relating to Taiwan, stop official contact with Taiwan and stop sending any wrong signal to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence”.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347701.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240222_11248543.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-22","Mao Ning","Fuji TV","The international community is closely watching the incident in the Taiwan Strait. No side wants to see any escalation. In China’s view, what’s the most appropriate way to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait?","First of all, cross-Strait issues are not diplomatic issues, so I’d refer you to competent authorities.\nTo uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, the key is to adhere to the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347701.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240222_11248543.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-02-22","Mao Ning","CCTV","It’s reported the Pentagon said the US Department of State has approved the potential sale to Taiwan of advanced tactical data link system upgrade planning worth USD 75 million. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. Such sales undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, and harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China always firmly opposes them. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop selling arms to Taiwan and having military contact with Taiwan, and stop creating factors that could cause tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China will take strong and resolute measures to firmly defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347701.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240222_11248543.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-02-23","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that the U.S. Department of Defense recently issued a statement saying the U.S. State Department has approved a sale to Taiwan of a tactical data link system upgrade program valued at about US$75 million. What is your comment on this?","Zhang Xiaogang: We firmly oppose the US selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China, and this position is firm and clear. For some time, the US has been brazenly manipulating Taiwan-related issues, attempting to fuel ‘Taiwan independence’ arrogance through arms sales to Taiwan, military assistance, and other means. These actions seriously damage China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously damage China-US relations between the two militaries, brutally interfere in China's internal affairs, and push up tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Taiwan question is the first insurmountable red line in China-US relations, and the US arming Taiwan is an extremely dangerous ‘gamble’. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the ‘August 17 Communiqué’. We urge it to stop selling weapons to Taiwan and US-Taiwan military ties, stop arming Taiwan in any way, and stop the provocative behavior of ‘using Taiwan to contain China’. With concrete actions, it should safeguard the overall situation of China-US military relations and regional peace and stability. China will take resolute and forceful measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/TopStories/16288508.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16288451.html",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-02-26","Mao Ning","AFP","According to a Taiwan official, the new Prime Minister of Tuvalu said that the relationship between Taiwan and Tuvalu is “firm and everlasting.” I have two questions. First, what’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment on Tuvalu’s recent election results? Second, what’s the Foreign Ministry’s view on the relations between Tuvalu and Taiwan?","Upholding the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. One hundred and eighty-three countries in the world have established diplomatic ties with China based on the one-China principle. A handful of countries who still have so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan region should choose to stand on the right side of history and make the right decision that truly serves their fundamental and long-term interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347703.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202402/t20240226_11250118.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 2024 Taiwan Work Conference was recently held in Beijing. Please introduce the overall considerations clarified at the meeting regarding the situation and tasks facing Taiwan work, and how cross-Strait relations will be promoted in the next step?","The 2024 Taiwan Work Conference was held in Beijing from February 22 to 23. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the conference and delivered a speech. The conference fully affirmed the achievements in Taiwan work over the past year, deeply analyzed the situation in the Taiwan Strait for the current and future period, and put forward clear requirements for doing this year's Taiwan work well.\nThe conference stressed that over the past year, Taiwan work has pressed forward with determination and advanced through difficulties, promoting new progress in cross-Strait relations and consolidating and expanding the international community's pattern of adhering to one China. We must unify our thinking and actions with the Party Central Committee's analysis and judgment of the situation in the Taiwan Strait and its decisions and deployments on Taiwan work, and further grasp the strategic initiative for realizing the complete reunification of the motherland.\nThis year marks the 75th anniversary of the founding of New China and is a key year for achieving the goals and tasks of the 14th Five-Year Plan. In accordance with the deployments and requirements of the conference, and guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, we will comprehensively implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the CPC and the Second Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee. We will resolutely implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” and promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of national reunification. We will expand exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields and deepen cross-Strait integrated development. We will promote joint promotion of Chinese culture by both sides and foster spiritual kinship between compatriots on both sides. We will resolutely combat “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and contain interference by external forces, firmly support patriotic and unification forces on the island, broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We will uphold and strengthen the Party's comprehensive leadership over Taiwan work, consolidate and expand the results of the thematic education campaign, and enhance the synergy of Taiwan work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602538.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The 2024 “Celebrating the Lantern Festival, Welcoming Reunion” Taiwan business networking event was recently held in Beijing. Taiwan business representatives in attendance expressed their confidence in continuing to take root and develop on the mainland, and their hope for promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. Please introduce the relevant details of the event. What will be done next to…","On February 24, the \"Celebrate the Lantern Festival · Welcome Reunion\" Taiwan business fellowship event was held in Beijing. Approximately 200 people attended, including the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Straits Exchange Foundation, responsible persons from relevant provinces and municipalities, and representatives of Taiwan business and industry circles and Taiwan business people and compatriots in the mainland.\nDirector Song Tao extended New Year greetings to Taiwan business people and compatriots, and encouraged compatriots on both sides of the Strait to seize the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified, uphold the national righteousness of safeguarding national reunification, and adhere to the broad road of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. He called on them to overcome interference and remove obstacles, and jointly advance the great cause of national reunification. Taiwan business representatives at the event gave enthusiastic responses and expressed their expectation that both sides of the Strait should maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus,\" and strengthen cooperation and expand exchanges. They believed that the mainland's economy has strong resilience and good prospects, and that Taiwan businesses and enterprises should firmly maintain confidence in developing roots on the mainland, seize opportunities in advancing Chinese-style modernization, and achieve better and faster development.\nGoing forward, we will adhere to the people-centered development philosophy and the original intention of benefiting and bringing prosperity to compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We will continue to share development dividends with Taiwan business people and compatriots, help Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern, and participate in new quality productive forces and high-quality development. We will firmly promote the peaceful development and integration development of cross-Strait relations, and continuously enhance the sense of gain and well-being of Taiwan business people and compatriots in the mainland. With compatriots on both sides of the Strait united in heart and direction, and walking forward hand in hand, we will certainly create a bright future for cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 2024 joint enrollment of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan students by mainland universities was officially launched recently. In what ways can Taiwan students register?","This year, the application process for Taiwan high school graduates to enroll in mainland universities will begin on March 1. Taiwan students may participate through three channels.\nFirst, take the joint enrollment examination for overseas Chinese, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan students. This year's examination registration period is March 1 to 15. Taiwan high school graduates may register on the examinee-side website of the National Unified Enrollment Management System (www.eeagd.edu.cn/lzks/).\nSecond, apply to mainland universities using the results of Taiwan's “Scholastic Assessment Test” (“学测”), “General Scholastic Ability Test” (“统测”), or “Subject Tests” (“分科测验”). Among these, candidates who took the “学测” may log in to the system for enrolling Taiwan high school graduates based on Taiwan's “学测” results on the mainland general university website (www.gatzs.com.cn/z/tw/) from March 1 to 15 this year and apply to 423 mainland universities. Candidates who took the “统测” may apply to 28 institutions within Fujian Province, and candidates who took the “分科测验” may apply to 10 undergraduate universities in Fujian, including Xiamen University.\nThird, participate in the separate enrollment programs for Taiwan students offered by Jinan University, Huaqiao University, and 8 universities in Fujian. For specific enrollment information and timing, please follow the official websites of the relevant universities.\nIn addition, Taiwan compatriots who wish to pursue master's and doctoral studies at mainland universities may log in to the Mainland General University Enrollment Information Network for Compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan (www.gatzs.com.cn) to learn about application information and register for the Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan graduate student enrollment examination.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602526.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","During the recently concluded Lantern Festival, various localities held Lantern Festival gatherings of diverse forms, in which compatriots on both sides of the Strait celebrated the festival together. Please introduce the relevant details.","Before the press conference, we played the music videos of two songs. One is “Not Parting” (《不散》), a duet in Mandarin and Minnan dialect by mainland singer Li Tingting and Taiwan singer-songwriter Wei Huinik. The other is “Mountains and Waters on the Same Road” (《山水同路》), produced jointly by musicians from both sides and performed by Taiwan singer Ouyang Nana. These two songs are blessings to compatriots on both sides for celebrating the Spring Festival and the Lantern Festival together. They express the affection and warmth of young people across the Strait being together, and also convey the aspirations of compatriots on both sides for a better future. Mountains and waters on the same road, never abandoning one another, a new journey begins in spring, and the days ahead are full of promise.\nDuring the Spring Festival and the Lantern Festival, various places on the mainland carried out diverse New Year visits and gatherings. I believe Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises who spent the New Year on the mainland have strong feelings about this. I would like to report some of these developments.\nIn Beijing, the 2024 “Kaohsiung · Beijing Characteristic Week” was held under the theme “Dragon Soars Across the Strait, Celebrating the Lantern Festival.” It was held simultaneously in Dongcheng District, Beijing, and Kaohsiung, Taiwan, with live connections. More than 100 Beijing residents and more than 200 Taiwan residents together experienced intangible cultural heritage such as Taiwan Ge-Arh opera and Beijing inside-bottle painting, and enjoyed programs such as cross-Strait co-created comic dialogue, choral singing by primary school students from both sides, and Taiwan youth Hanfu performances, celebrating the Lantern Festival together.\nIn Shanghai, relevant parties and the Taiwan Ren Jian Educational and Cultural Foundation jointly hosted the “2024 Joyful Lantern Festival and 13th Shanghai Culture and Arts Festival” at Fo Guang Shan in Kaohsiung, Taiwan. Under the theme “Spring Comes to Shanghai — Joint Exhibition of Shanghai Young Artists,” it opened a Spring Festival feast for people on both sides to “jointly celebrate the lunar New Year and share Shanghai culture.” It attracted many Taiwan residents to visit, and the event will continue until April 7.\nGuangdong held “Dragon Soars Across the Bay Area, One Tree of Blossoms — 2024 Guangdong, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Youth Lantern Festival Gala.” Taiwan features such as the electronic “Third Prince” (SanTaizi) dance, Taroko brocade weaving, the folk song “Taibalang,” and baseball and softball sports appeared on the gala stage together with dozens of Taiwan youth. The gala performed culture of common origin shared across both sides of the Strait and Hong Kong and Macao, displayed the vitality and dreams of youth from Guangdong, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, and highlighted the historical roots and close bonds of “Cross-Strait Families.”\nJiangsu, Fujian, Shandong, Hubei, Chongqing and other places also held rich and colorful Lantern Festival activities. Nanjing organized Nan-Tai youth representatives to make Qinhuai lanterns together, and Nantong held a “Love in Nantong, Our Lantern Festival” exchange event. In Yongfu Cherry Blossom Tea Garden in Zhangping Taiwan Farmers’ Entrepreneurship Park, a “Piano Concert Among Cherry Blossoms” was held, featuring prominent musicians from both sides performing on the same stage. Liaocheng held a traditional cultural exchange event titled “One Family Across the Strait, Lantern Festival in the Ancient City.” Wuhan held the “Dragon Soars in Prosperous Times, Celebrating Reunion Together” event, featuring folk art performances, lantern riddles, lantern making, and exhibitions. Chongqing organized representatives of cross-Strait marriage families from Chongqing and Taiwan to gather together and welcome the Lantern Festival.\nIn addition, Xiamen Television launched the “Joy Is Enough” Cross-Strait Lantern Festival Poetry and Music Gala on the Lantern Festival. Branch venues were set up in northern, central, and southern Taiwan. Under the main theme “Watching Lanterns and Singing Together, Feelings Connect Across the Strait; Reciting Poetry and Listening to Music, Dreams of Chinese Unity Come True,” the gala used lanterns as its guide, riddles as its embellishment, and music to convey emotion. It organically integrated classic ancient poetry with original Minnan dialect songs, classic old songs, folk music, and martial arts. Through live connections and virtual technology, it led audiences on both sides of the Strait to savor traditional Chinese culture and revisit the hometown sounds and feelings shared by Fujian and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The US recently announced that the US State Department has approved a upgrade program for the Advanced Tactical Data System worth US$75 million. This is the 13th such sale during Biden’s term, and the first US arms sale to Taiwan since the 2024 Taiwan leadership election. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to stop selling arms to Taiwan.\nThe DPP authorities’ attempts to “rely on the US to plot independence” and “use force to plot independence” will only bring the danger of war to the Taiwan Strait area and push Taiwan compatriots into perilous circumstances. The DPP authorities should immediately stop conduct that harms the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602527.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","On January 30, the Civil Aviation Administration announced the cancellation of the north-to-south flight offset on the M503 route. How has the adjusted and optimized operation of the M503 route performed over the past month? When will the two connecting routes of M503, W122 and W123, be activated for west-to-east operation?","Starting February 1, the restriction requiring flights on the M503 route to deviate westward when flying from north to south has been lifted. Over the past month, the overall operation of this route has been safe and stable. On average, aircraft from the mainland, Hong Kong and Macao, and international airlines have operated 65 flights per day, including 53 southbound flights and 12 northbound flights, which fully demonstrates the safety and reliability of this route. Facts prove that the optimized operation of the M503 route is conducive to improving cross-Strait flight operations, further facilitating travel and exchanges between the two sides, and is in line with the common interests of compatriots on both sides.\nIt is understood that preparatory work for the connecting routes W122 and W123 of the M503 route, which will operate from west to east, is actively underway, and they can be put into use once everything is ready.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602530.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","U.S. Secretary of State Blinken's recent so-called “dinner menu theory” has drawn attention in Taiwan's public opinion, and many netizens on the island worry and lament that “Taiwan is merely a dish on the American menu.” We also note that a recent report published by the U.S. think tank “Center for Strategic and International Studies” points out that some international experts believe that, in their countries…","What you have described shows that the international community is increasingly recognizing the essence of the Taiwan question, and seeing clearly that it is the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, as well as external forces seeking to use “Taiwan independence” to contain China's development, that are undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. History and reality have fully proven that “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and any indulgence or support for “Taiwan independence” forces is a sabotage of peace in the Taiwan Strait.\nWhy are more and more Taiwan people beginning to no longer trust the United States? Because they have clearly seen that the United States always puts its own interests first, and that Taiwan is, to the United States, purely a “chess piece” for containing China's development. So-called “supporting Taiwan” is in fact harming and destroying Taiwan, and Taiwan may at any time change from a “chess piece” to a “discarded piece.” Everyone may have noticed the poster “Going Home” issued by the Eastern Theater Command on February 24. The four lines in the poster, “Little hands grasp big hands, hand in hand we escape the pit of fire; lighting lamps drives away demons, and only going home brings victory,” vividly illustrate one thing: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and outsiders cannot be relied upon.\nWe hope that all sectors of Taiwan society and the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will work with us to jointly advance peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and to safeguard the peaceful home in which compatriots on both sides live in tranquility. Only this can bring real and tangible benefits and well-being to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602529.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","After the vicious incident on February 14 in which a Taiwan vessel rammed a mainland fishing boat, causing deaths and injuries among fishermen, public opinion on the island widely questioned the self-contradictory explanations and buck-passing of Kuan Bi-ling (管碧玲), chairperson of Taiwan’s “Ocean Affairs Council.” It was argued that the chairperson failed in the job and should bear “political responsibility.”…","As everyone has seen, Kuan Bi-ling has turned the handling of the “2·14” serious ship collision incident into a personal political show, concealing the truth, shirking responsibility, and telling lie after lie. Not only has she not offered a single word of apology to the victims, she has also kept placing obstacles in the way of post-incident handling. She is extremely cold-blooded and contemptible. I advise this lady: put yourself in others' shoes, stop continuing to harm the families of the victims, and give the victims' families and compatriots on both sides of the Strait an account as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602532.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After the “2·14” malicious ship collision incident, the Taiwan side deliberately concealed the facts of the case, shirked responsibility, and used the incident to incite cross-Strait confrontation. What is your comment?","On February 14, the Taiwan side rammed a mainland fishing vessel in the waters between Xiamen and Kinmen, causing four fishermen to be killed or injured. This seriously hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides and aroused strong indignation across all sectors of the mainland and widespread doubt in island public opinion. Half a month has passed since the incident, and the DPP authorities have not expressed any apology. Regarding the truth of the incident, the DPP authorities have concealed facts, lied, misled, and contradicted themselves, attempting to cover up the truth and shirk responsibility. Some politicians and media on the island, disregarding the facts, have talked wildly, been arrogant, and shown no humanity. We express strong indignation and condemnation of this.\nWe solemnly demand that the Taiwan side make the facts and truth public as soon as possible, severely punish the responsible persons, apologize to the victims' families, meet the legitimate demands of the victims' families, and give an account to the victims' families and compatriots on both sides of the strait. We will firmly safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of our compatriots and will not allow such incidents to happen again. The mainland side reserves the right to take further measures, and the Taiwan side shall bear all consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602537.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","After the “2·14” malicious ship collision incident, the mainland's coast guard authorities announced they would carry out regular law enforcement patrols. Some public opinion on the island says the mainland wants to use this to “pressure” Taiwan before “5·20” and may turn Xiamen and Kinmen waters into a “Diaoyu Islands-ization,” dispatching coast guard ships to regularly enter Taiwan's so-called “prohibited and…","The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The waters off Xiamen and Kinmen have been traditional fishing grounds for fishermen on both sides of the Strait since ancient times, and there is fundamentally no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters.” The mainland's coast guard carrying out routine law enforcement patrols is conducive to maintaining normal order in the relevant waters and safeguarding the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602535.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Question one: The Taiwan side originally planned to allow Taiwan travel agencies to organize group tours to the mainland starting March 1, but suddenly called a halt before the Lunar New Year, claiming it had not received a goodwill response from the mainland side. What is the TAO's response? Question two: The Taiwan MAC recently emphasized that the ship collision incident has entered Taiwan's “judicial process,”…","First question. In early 2020, it was the DPP authorities who announced a ban on Taiwan travel agencies organizing group tours to the mainland. In November 2023, it was also the DPP authorities who promised to lift the “group travel ban” in March this year. Later, it was again the DPP authorities who went back on their word and reimposed the ban on group tours. These facts fully prove that the DPP authorities never intended to solve the problem from the start and were merely going through the motions.\nAs early as last May, we announced the resumption of travel agencies’ operation of group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents, and we have made all necessary preparations. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for sightseeing, to see its magnificent landscapes and the new face of development across the mainland.\nSecond question. The “February 14” incident, in which a Taiwan vessel rammed a mainland fishing boat and caused deaths and injuries among fishermen, occurred half a month ago. Over these past half month, the families of the victims have endured being separated from their loved ones forever, and each day has felt like a year. We solemnly demand that the Taiwan side promptly disclose the facts of the case, severely punish those responsible, apologize to the families of the victims, meet their reasonable demands, and give the families of the victims and compatriots on both sides of the Strait a satisfactory account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","During this Spring Festival, colored lanterns from Shanghai appeared at the “2024 Taipei Lantern Festival,” sending New Year blessings to Taiwan compatriots and attracting many Taiwan residents to view and take photos. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","Shanghai's participation in the Taipei Spring Festival Lantern Festival has been a long-standing tradition and is an important exchange activity between the two cities. It reflects the good wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to celebrate the traditional festival together and to strengthen exchange and cooperation. This year, Shanghai's lanterns take “Enjoy Shanghai, Celebrate the New Year” as their theme, showcasing Shanghai's features of “architecture that can be read, neighborhoods suitable for strolling, and a city with warmth.” The exquisite lanterns have attracted large numbers of Taiwan residents to “check in” and take photos, and the scene on site was lively and enthusiastic.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","As we all know, since the DPP came to power in 2016, the communication channels between the two cross-Strait associations have been suspended. In handling this incident, how did the two sides communicate, and how well did they coordinate with each other? Some people on the island have called on both sides to sit down and talk for the well-being of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, and that at least ARATS and…","After the “2·14” malicious ship-collision incident, groups, organizations, and individuals on the island and in Kinmen expressed concern, extended condolences to the survivors and the families of the deceased, and provided necessary assistance to family members entering the island. We are grateful for this.\nDialogue and consultation across the Strait is our consistent position. The reasons why the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanisms have stalled are well known, and the solution is clear. As long as the DPP authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, the door to cross-Strait consultation and negotiation can be opened at any time. We will continue to work to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to enhance their well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202402/t20240228_12602533.htm"],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","During the Spring Festival, Taiwan residents have shown a particular fondness for the mainland TV drama “Empresses in the Palace.” Since the Spring Festival of 2022, the number of people watching it online has increased year by year, and this year the number of simultaneous online viewers set a record of over 60,000. Many people said that while watching a good show, chatting with everyone creates the atmosphere…","“Empresses in the Palace” (《甄嬛传》) has been broadcast for 12 years and has remained enduringly popular on both sides of the Strait, becoming a top TV series every Spring Festival. I have seen reports in island media saying that watching “Empresses in the Palace” has become a new choice for Taiwan people's New Year entertainment. Many people say that while watching a good drama and chatting with everyone, they feel the true atmosphere of the New Year.\nI have also seen messages from Taiwan netizens saying that watching “Empresses in the Palace” during the New Year has become a way to reunite with “old friends.” Here, I would like to recommend a few “new friends” to our Taiwan friends. Films released recently, such as “Hot Blooded Dragon” (《热辣滚烫》), “Ride On 2” (《飞驰人生2》), and “The Annual Meeting Must Go On” (《年会不能停》), and TV dramas such as “Blossoms” (《繁花》), “Coming and Going from the South” (《南来北往》), and “Life in the Smoke” (《烟火人家》), are all very good. We hope that while enjoying excellent film and television works, compatriots on both sides of the Strait will come to better appreciate the charm of Chinese culture and savor the happiness of working hard for a better life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","First question: During this year's Spring Festival holiday, the cross-Strait “mini three links” routes transported 27,000 mainland visitors, and single-day passenger flow exceeded 4,000 for the first time, a new high this year. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Second question: Lee Ta-wei, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, stated at the “2024 Mainland Taiwanese Businesspeople Spring…","The first question. During the Spring Festival, the cross-Strait “Mini Three Links” routes launched a “Sea Spring Transport” service to make it convenient for Taiwan compatriots to travel back and forth across the Strait to visit relatives and friends, celebrate the New Year and go sightseeing. According to statistics, the four “Mini Three Links” passenger routes, namely Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Lianjiang Huangqi to Matsu, deployed a total of 18 vessels providing 4,703 passenger seats, with 73 round-trip sailings per week, amounting to 146 voyages. From January 26 to February 23, the “Mini Three Links” routes operated a total of 580 voyages and carried 98,695 passenger trips. Of these, the Xiamen-Kinmen route operated 452 voyages and carried 90,485 passenger trips; the Quanzhou-Kinmen route operated 24 voyages and carried 1,983 passenger trips; and the Matsu routes from Fuzhou and Lianjiang operated 104 voyages and carried 6,227 passenger trips. This was the first time since the resumption of the Matsu routes that passenger seats were fully occupied.\nThe second question. The root cause of the current tensions and turbulence in cross-Strait relations, and the solution, are both very clear. The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and negotiation. Only by upholding the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can the two sides carry out communication and dialogue; otherwise, no dialogue or exchange would be possible at all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The first question: regarding the Kinmen boat collision incident, the mainland side assigned representatives to consult with Taiwan's Coast Guard Administration in Kinmen on handling the aftermath, but no consensus has been reached so far. Can you explain the state of these consultations? The second question: at present, cross-Strait tensions are rising, the mainland has strengthened maritime law enforcement, and…","First, after the relevant parties in Fujian Province and Quanzhou City maintained continuous communication with the families of the fishermen concerned, the Quanzhou Red Cross Society and others sent personnel to accompany the families to Kinmen on February 20 and bring back two surviving fishermen.\nThe crux of the problem now is that the Taiwan side should promptly make the facts public, severely punish the responsible persons, apologize to the families of the victims, and meet the reasonable demands of the families of the victims, so as to give an account to the families of the victims and to compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Relevant authorities in Taiwan should genuinely demonstrate sincerity and goodwill in resolving the problem, handle the aftermath properly, and avoid further harming the emotional bonds between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond, we understand this concern among Taiwan residents. Likewise, mainland fishermen are also worried about whether they will be treated brutally by relevant authorities in Taiwan. The fundamental cause of the concerns among people on both sides is that the DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, incite “anti-China and hatred of China” sentiment, stir up confrontation between the two sides, and cause cross-Strait relations to become tense.\nFor people on both sides of the Strait to feel secure, the most urgent task is for the Taiwan side to demonstrate sincerity in resolving the problem, promptly make the facts public, severely punish the responsible persons, apologize to the families of the victims, meet the reasonable demands of the victims' families, and genuinely prevent such incidents from happening again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","In the Kinmen fishing boat incident, the enforcement action by Taiwan's “Coast Guard Administration” resulted in loss of life, and I believe all parties are very saddened. According to the Taiwan “Coast Guard Administration,” this was a “three-no speedboat” (no name, no ship certificate, no port of registry). Can we return to the starting point of the problem and, in addition to pursuing the Taiwan side's…","The starting point for addressing the current issue is to clarify how the incident occurred. The Taiwan side should promptly disclose the facts of the matter, severely punish the relevant responsible persons, apologize to the families of the victims, satisfy the reasonable demands of the families of the victims, and provide an account to the families of the victims and compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This is the most urgent task in handling the “2·14” vicious ship collision incident.\nRegarding maintaining operational order in the relevant waters, the mainland side has in recent years taken various measures to strengthen the management of fishermen's sea operations. Toward Taiwan fishermen, we treat them with fraternal kindness, establishing Taiwan fishermen reception points along the coast to provide Taiwan fishing boats and fishermen with shelter from storms, supplies, water, emergency rescue, and other assistance. The relevant authorities in Taiwan should respect the long-standing fact that fishermen from both sides have operated in traditional fishing grounds, stop detaining mainland fishing boats and treating mainland fishermen in rough and dangerous ways, and ensure the safety of fishermen's lives and property.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Taiwan's administrative department recently proposed in a report that it would train civil society organizations, including schools, to form so-called \"emergency response teams.\" The report has drawn criticism from public opinion on the island, which views it as putting the sending of students to the battlefield on the agenda. What is your comment on this?","From “extending compulsory military service by one year” to launching the so-called “Study-and-Service 3+1 Program” and then establishing the so-called “Emergency Response Teams,” the DPP authorities are step by step forcing Taiwan’s young people onto the battlefield and making them cannon fodder. Why has it come to this? The people of Taiwan and Taiwan’s young people should give this serious thought.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","A US politician has proposed that, because US aid funds promised to Pacific island countries have not been delivered in full, Palau and the Marshall Islands, two Taiwan “diplomatic allies,” may turn to China, and has used this as a pretext to pressure the United States. Could the spokesperson comment?","Adhering to the one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a general trend and the will of the people. Some politicians in certain countries should see clearly the trend of history and stop interfering in other countries’ internal affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Some argue that the various conveniences and preferences the mainland grants to Taiwan are rooted in “cross-Strait being one family” and the One-China foundation. If the Taiwan authorities repeatedly undermine this foundation, the mainland can only withdraw the conveniences and preferences. What is your assessment of this?","In recent years, the DPP authorities have stubbornly clung to the “Taiwan independence” position and refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” They have maliciously obstructed exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, causing the achievements of peaceful development in cross-Strait relations to keep slipping away, seriously hurting the feelings of compatriots on both sides, and seriously damaging the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. We uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” and we always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continuously improving the institutions and policies that enhance their well-being. We are willing to provide broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will never leave any space for “Taiwan independence” separatism. Any “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their conduct that undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and harm the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan’s “Legislative Yuan” established the so-called “11th Taiwan-U.S. Congressional Members Friendship Association.” At the founding meeting, Han Kuo-yu said, “Work with the United States is the most important, and thank the United States for its long-term support of Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan residents are well aware that the US always pursues “America First” and will never truly take Taiwan's interests and Taiwan's people to heart. Those who willingly serve as “chess pieces” manipulated by outsiders will inevitably become “discarded pieces.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Outside attention has focused on which agreement was used for the return of these two mainland fishermen. The mainland side did not sign the handover certificate, and some outside observers believe the mainland refused to sign because the Mainland Affairs Council required the mainland Red Cross to sign. Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council Zhan Zhihong said it was only a transmission of documents, and…","It should be emphasized that we brought back two surviving fishermen, not a so-called “repatriation.” After the “February 14” vicious ship collision incident, through communication between relevant parties in Fujian Province and Quanzhou City and the families of the fishermen, on February 20, relevant personnel from the Quanzhou Red Cross accompanied the families to Kinmen and brought back the two surviving fishermen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","The Fujian Coast Guard announced that it will carry out routine patrols in the waters of Jinmen and Xiamen. On February 19, it boarded and inspected a Kinmen tourist yacht, and many tourists felt frightened and panicked. Will this harm the interests of tourists and fishermen and the relationship across the Taiwan Strait?","This will not cause any problem of tourist panic. The Fujian Coast Guard enforces the law in accordance with the law in its own waters, maintains normal order in the relevant waters, and safeguards the lives and property of fishermen and passengers. Its law enforcement is civilized, open and transparent, and is entirely justifiable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: After the Xiamen-Kinmen fishing boat incident, cross-strait antagonism rose sharply, and people across all sectors worried that gunfire could break out at any time. This shows that the cross-strait fishing operations agreement and interaction arrangements really need to be sat down and discussed. But as everyone knows, the official channels on both sides currently have no room for dialogue.…","First question. Dialogue and consultation between the two sides of the Strait have always been our consistent position. The reasons for the stalling of the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism are well known, and the solution is clear. As long as the DPP authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China principle, the door to cross-Strait consultations and negotiations can be opened at any time.\nSecond question. Relevant personnel of the Quanzhou Red Cross, entrusted by the families, communicated with relevant Taiwan authorities on the aftermath of the vicious ship collision incident of “2·14,” which has nothing to do with cross-Strait consultations and negotiations. The reasons for the halt of the institutionalized cross-Strait consultation mechanism are well known. Only by returning to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait consultations and negotiations resume.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","Kuan Bi-ling, Chairperson of Taiwan's “Ocean Affairs Council,” said that far more mainland fishing boats were detained during the Ma Ying-jeou era than during the Tsai Ing-wen administration. She said this single law enforcement case has now become a “political contest,” which the people of Taiwan do not wish to see. What comments do you have on this?","Half a month has passed since the “2·14” vicious ship-collision incident. The explanations from relevant Taiwan authorities about how the incident unfolded have been contradictory. They deflect public doubts and dare not directly respond to the legitimate demands of the families of the deceased fishermen to make the truth public. This is unacceptable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Wu Chun-li, \"director of the China Affairs Department\" of the DPP, said in an online lecture recently that the DPP's \"Taiwan independence\" party platform is already a historical document. What impact does the mainland believe this statement may have on cross-Strait relations?","Any political party in Taiwan that acknowledges the one-China principle will face no obstacles in its exchanges with us. As long as the DPP changes its “Taiwan independence” position, the door to exchanges and dialogue with us is open. But if it insists on the “Taiwan independence” position and refuses to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, then exchanges and dialogue are out of the question.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202402/t20240228_12602524.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-02-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the US Marine Corps and the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force conducted island-seizing exercises on Kyushu and Okinawa. Some analysts believe this demonstrates the response capability of the US-Japan alliance amid the current increase in China's military presence in relevant waters. Other reports say that Japan is studying and formulating residents' evacuation plans to respond to a Taiwan Strait crisis,…","We have noted the relevant reports. It must be pointed out that defense cooperation between relevant countries should not target third parties, much less use China as a pretext. Deliberately seeking excuses, sensationalizing tensions, and creating confrontation is an extremely irresponsible and dangerous act, and it runs counter to the good intentions of regional countries that seek peace and development.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and no external interference is permitted. Historically, Japan launched a war of aggression against China and carried out a colonial rule over Taiwan lasting half a century, committing crimes too numerous to record and bearing grave historical responsibility toward the Chinese people. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect on its history of aggression, stop creating trouble on the Taiwan question, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community through concrete actions.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16289929.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-02-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, China’s foreign minister delivered a keynote speech at the Munich Security Conference, pointing out that China aims to be a stabilizing force in a turbulent world. Some US media have hyped that in recent years the mainland has increased military pressure on Taiwan, deploying ships and aircraft around the island almost every day, and that Chinese military aircraft frequently cross the “Taiwan Strait…","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and there is absolutely no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” The training and exercises conducted by the Chinese People's Liberation Army in the Taiwan Strait area are legitimate acts to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. They are a deterrent countermeasure against external interference and “Taiwan independence” provocations, and a necessary action to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We will continue to strengthen training and combat preparedness, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16289929.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-02-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Taiwan will allocate NT$13.37 billion in a multi-year budget to purchase 500 Stinger missiles from the US. Lai Ching-te recently told personnel from the US Hudson Institute that the US government is promoting the normalization of arms sales to Taiwan and helping Taiwan enhance its self-defense capabilities, and that Taiwan will continue to strengthen its asymmetric combat capabilities. What…","First of all, it must be pointed out that no matter how much weaponry is purchased with the hard-earned money of the common people, it cannot change the basic fact that Taiwan is Chinese territory, and it cannot stop the historical trend of national reunification. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “seeking independence through force” has no way out, and will only push Taiwan into an extremely dangerous situation of grave peril and war.\nThe US side has repeatedly violated the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, in particular the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué,” has breached its political commitments made on the Taiwan question, has continued to sell arms to Taiwan, and has strengthened US-Taiwan military collusion. This seriously infringes upon China's sovereignty and security, emboldens the “Taiwan independence” faction, and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to resolutely crush any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16289929.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-03-08","Mao Ning","Reuters","The chief of Lithuania’s counter-intelligence said yesterday that Chinese interference in Lithuania’s elections cannot be ruled out due to Lithuanian support for Taiwan. What’s your comment?","China always stays committed to the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs. We’re not interested to and will not interfere in Lithuania’s internal affairs and elections. We hope that relevant people in Lithuania will stop making irresponsible comments on China and creating trouble and difficulties for the bilateral relations. Otherwise, Lithuania will end up hurting its own interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347711.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240308_11256472.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-03-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: The government work report submitted to the Second Session of the 14th National People's Congress for deliberation proposes that we must adhere to the overall strategy of the new era for resolving the Taiwan question. According to reports, in recent times, US congressmen have successively made visits to Taiwan, and the US government has again approved arms sales to Taiwan. The Taiwan side has said it…","Wu Qian: Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and any indulgence or support for “Taiwan independence” forces is a sabotage of peace across the Strait. The United States should abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop any form of official exchange with the Taiwan region of China, stop arming Taiwan, and translate its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” into concrete action, and stop sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the One-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, and collude with external forces to continuously provoke “Taiwan independence” schemes. This is the root cause of the persistent tension and turbulence across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities must bear all consequences arising from this.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins. “Across the vast sea and sky, what are we waiting for to return?” We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never leave the slightest room for “Taiwan independence” separatist actions. The People's Liberation Army will continue to strengthen military training and combat readiness, resolutely work to thwart “independence” and promote unification, and always remain an iron wall defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/ztjzh/16292602.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-03-12","Wang Wenbin","TASS","CIA Director William Burns told the Senate that the US will continue its support for Ukraine to bolster the Ukrainian government, indirectly contain China and send a message to China about Taiwan or the South China Sea. What’s your comment?","These remarks show that what the US truly cares about is not Ukraine, but using the Ukraine crisis to realize its own geopolitical strategic goals.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. Any attempt by anyone of meddling in the Taiwan question is doomed to failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347713.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240312_11259678.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-12","Wang Wenbin","RIA Novosti","A Pentagon official said earlier that the administration of US President Joe Biden in the defense budget for the year 2025 for the first time requested the authority to provide weapons from American warehouses to aid Taiwan. What’s China’s comment on this?","We have noted relevant reports. We’ve made clear time and again that competition is not the defining feature of China-US relations and that competition between major countries cannot solve the problems facing China and the US. By claiming to “outcompete” others, what the US refers to is not healthy competition of becoming one’s better self and making progress together but vicious competition of trying to trip the other and recklessly gamble at the cost of the fundamental interests of the two peoples and even the future of humanity. It will only push the two countries toward confrontation and conflict.\nAs Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi pointed out last week, if the US is obsessed with suppressing China, it will eventually harm itself. We hope the US will correct its wrong perception of China, discard the mentality of zero-sum game, and give up the illusion of “outcompeting China.” We hope that the US will work with China in the same direction, gradually translate the San Francisco vision into reality and promote the sound, steady and sustainable development of China-US relations.\nI would like to stress that China is firmly opposed to US’s military ties with Taiwan and its effort of arming Taiwan. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs. China will take steps to firmly uphold its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347713.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240312_11259678.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-13","Wang Wenbin","The Associated Press","My first question is that Hsiao Bi-khim visited Washington this week. What’s China’s comment? My second question is that social media users in Taiwan have widely shared an AI deepfake video about US Congressman Rob Wittman pledging military support for Taiwan if DPP candidates win the election held on January 13. Rob Wittman accused the mainland of attempting to interfere in Taiwan politics and using TikTok for…","On your first question, China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the Taiwan region and the US and is closely following the developments.\nOn your second question, we will not comment on faked videos. What I want to stress is that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Elections in the Taiwan region are the affairs of a region in China that brook no foreign interference. The US should fully understand the highly sensitive nature of the Taiwan question, stay committed to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and act on the US leader’s assurances of not supporting “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347714.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240313_11260196.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-13","Wang Wenbin","The Associated Press","What is China’s comment on AI deepfake videos and on whether these videos can be used to interfere in other countries’ internal affairs?","We have all along opposed interference in other countries’ internal affairs. And I would also like to point out that the elections in the Taiwan region are the affairs of a region in China, in which no foreign country has the right to interfere.\nIf you are interested in China’s position on AI, I’d refer you to Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s elaborations on this topic at the press conference held on the margins of the two sessions, in which he proposed three principles.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347714.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240313_11260196.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear journalist friends, good day. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I will be hosting today's press conference. Now, please go ahead with your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","On March 6, General Secretary Xi Jinping, while visiting members of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang attending the CPPCC session, emphasized that the Revolutionary Committee should further find its proper position in the overall picture of Taiwan work, give full play to its strengths, and actively take initiative. It should better unite all patriotic forces at home and abroad, on the island…","The central government's basic policy on Taiwan is clear and consistent. We will earnestly study and comprehend the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches, adhere to the overall strategy the Party has adopted for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, firmly grasp the leading role and initiative in cross-Strait relations, and unswervingly advance the great cause of national reunification. We will uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, promote economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, deepen integrated development across all fields between the two sides, and unite all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation, including compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to jointly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland and jointly create the great undertaking of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nFor a long time, the democratic parties have given full play to their respective strengths, actively offered suggestions, carried out extensive work, and made important contributions to promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepening mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides, and advancing the development of cross-Strait relations. The Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will strengthen liaison and communication with the democratic parties and people's organizations, jointly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches, and do well in Taiwan work in the new era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605919.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Please have the spokesperson interpret the Taiwan-related content in this year's Government Work Report.","The “Government Work Report” is an important document in which the State Council reports to the National People's Congress, and in effect to the entire nation, on the previous year's work results, proposes the policy priorities for the current year and even the direction and goals of national development for a period to come. It is also an important embodiment of people's democratic politics. The Taiwan-related content of this year's “Government Work Report” focuses on elaborating the major policies, principles, positions, and task objectives of current work on Taiwan, which carries important guiding significance for doing this year's Taiwan work well.\nAt present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, but the basic pattern and development direction of cross-Strait relations have not changed and cannot change, and the historical process of a strong country, national rejuvenation, and cross-Strait unification is even more unstoppable. We will thoroughly implement the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work. We will uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” adhere to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” continuously improve institutions and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, promote the joint promotion of Chinese culture on both sides, and foster spiritual connection between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We will firmly crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatism and curb interference by external forces. We will resolutely support patriotic unification forces on the island, broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, solidly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, unswervingly advance the great cause of national reunification, and safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nWe hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the trends of the times and the situation, recognize the benefits and harms, grasp the broad trend of history, hold fast to the great righteousness of the nation, and join mainland compatriots in creating the glorious cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation, and share the dignity and honor of being Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605918.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","The Taiwan-related section of this year's Government Work Report emphasized “unwaveringly advancing the great cause of national reunification” and did not mention “peaceful reunification.” Does this represent a change in the mainland's position?","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification, most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and to strive with the utmost sincerity and effort for the prospect of peaceful reunification. However, we will never promise to abandon the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is directed at external interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and its root cause is the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to continuously carry out provocations for “independence.” We have firm will, full confidence and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台国广记者","Recently, three figures with heavyweight influence in Taiwan's semiconductor field, namely former ITRI President Shih Chin-tai, former TSMC Vice President of Research and Development Lin Ben-jian, and Academia Sinica academician Hsieh Chang-tai, jointly published an article in US media. They pointed out that the United States is attempting to use the “CHIPS Act” to gain control of Taiwanese enterprises'…","This article largely reflects the doubts of Taiwan's industrial sector about the DPP authorities' unprincipled and bottomless attachment to and catering to external forces, as well as concerns about the hollowing out of Taiwan's advantageous industries, the suppression of core enterprises, and the weakening of their competitive advantages. Once Taiwan's industrial development autonomy and its voice in the global industrial and supply chains are both lost, one has to ask how much “nest egg” Taiwan would still have? The outcome would be nothing other than a change from “chess piece” to “discarded piece.” Therefore, the views of these industry experts are by no means alarmist, but a “warning word to the wise” for Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605913.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","During this year's two sessions, “developing new quality productive forces” sparked widespread discussion. Will the mainland soon introduce new measures to encourage Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in the mainland's high-quality development?","Developing new quality productive forces is an inherent requirement and an important focus for promoting high-quality development. Taiwan businesses and enterprises will inevitably be participants and contributors, and will also be beneficiaries. We will maintain consistency and continuity in policy formulation and implementation, build a policy support system with greater intensity and stronger targeting, strengthen the leading role of scientific and technological innovation, optimize the guarantee of factor allocation, and help Taiwan businesses and enterprises anchor the direction of building a modern industrial system, promote the upgrading of traditional industries, the growth of emerging industries, and the cultivation of future industries, strengthen new momentum for high-quality development, and achieve better and faster development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台央视《海峡两岸》栏目记者","Regarding the “February 14 malicious ship collision incident”: on March 5, mainland personnel left Kinmen and returned. How this incident will develop has attracted wide attention. Under what circumstances would the two sides resume dialogue and consultation on this matter? Will the mainland still send personnel to Kinmen or to the island of Taiwan to handle this matter?","As for why the family members of the victims and the relevant personnel left Kinmen, they gave a complete explanation that day, and I believe everyone has already understood. Human life is at stake. It was clearly the Taiwan side’s brutal treatment of mainland fishermen that caused the fishing boat to capsize and people to be killed and injured. Yet since the incident, the families have not even received a single apology or obtained the truth. The Taiwan side is still using a so-called “investigation procedure” to delay resolving the issue and a so-called “law enforcement” process to shirk responsibility. They are truly “three nos”: heartless, unrighteous, and unreasonable. Only if the DPP authorities face the problem, correct their attitude, and show sincerity in solving it can post-incident consultations on the “2·14” vicious collision incident resume. If they intend to delay and get by, they are probably miscalculating.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605917.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Zhong Mingxuan, an internet celebrity on the island considered “pro-green,” traveled to Beijing and Shanghai for the first time. He shared his experiences online, including taking high-speed rail, experiencing QR-code payment, and touring Beijing's hutongs. He said the trip changed his understanding of the mainland, exclaiming, “Mainland technology is advanced” and “I really like this place.” These…","“Seeing is believing.” What is the mainland really like? We hope that compatriots on the island, especially young friends, will not simply believe one-sided accounts or spread rumors. Instead, they should come to the mainland in person to take a look and find the answer. The answers will surely be varied, but the most basic and most universal one is “different”: the mainland is different from what the “Taiwan independence” forces and green-media pundits say. For example, high-speed trains on the mainland have backrests. Mainland residents can not only afford tea eggs and pickled mustard tuber, but also live quite well. And, as Zhong Mingxuan said, the mainland is very advanced and interesting, and mainland compatriots are very friendly and warm-hearted: “The food is good, the cities are developed, and the people are quite warm-hearted.”\nI want to stress that “the mainland is not frightening.” Those who create information cocoons on the island and smear the mainland are the ones who are truly frightening. “The mainland is not backward.” Those who lie with their eyes open and talk nonsense are the ones who are truly backward. We warmly welcome Taiwan's young friends to come to the mainland more often. We believe everyone will find the trip worthwhile and, like Zhong Mingxuan, will “come to like this place.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605909.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Regarding the “2·14” malicious ship-collision incident, consultations between the two sides have yielded no results to date. Taiwan’s coast guard authorities have said that during the consultations, the mainland side insisted on demands that do not conform to Taiwan’s “legal system,” preventing the two sides from reaching consensus. What is your comment on this?","Thirty days have passed since the “2·14” vessel collision incident, and the Taiwan side still has not provided a convincing account of the process and truth of the incident. Moreover, its responses to questions raised by all sectors of society have been contradictory and full of loopholes, and its attitude has been inconsistent, showing that it does not really want to solve the problem but instead keeps creating new problems. Political circles and public opinion across the island have long condemned this. The DPP authorities refuse to reflect on and examine their own problems, and instead try to distort and smear the legitimate and reasonable demands of the victims' families in order to divert attention and shift responsibility. This is outrageous.\nWe will not tolerate or indulge the DPP authorities' brutal conduct, which disregards the safety of mainland fishermen and their property and hurts the feelings of compatriots on both sides. We once again solemnly demand that the Taiwan side make the facts and truth public as soon as possible, severely punish the responsible persons, apologize to the victims' families, meet the legitimate demands of the victims' families, and give an account to the victims' families and compatriots on both sides of the strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","March 1 was the first day Taiwan travel agencies resumed organizing group tours to the mainland. According to reports from Taiwan media, on that day at least 50 tour groups with more than a thousand island residents traveled to the mainland. Taiwan tourism operators call on the DPP authorities to respond to island residents' enthusiasm for travel and to lift the “group tour ban” on travel to the mainland after…","Residents of Taiwan have a strong interest and desire to travel to the mainland, and the island’s tourism industry has also repeatedly called on the DPP authorities to lift the ban as soon as possible. Since last year, Taiwan’s relevant authorities have several times claimed to have drawn up plans to resume Taiwanese travel agencies organizing group tours to the mainland, but in February this year they announced that the originally planned arrangements would no longer be implemented. Such flip-flopping and abuse of power seriously harm the interests of the island’s travel industry and deprive people from all walks of life of their freedom to travel. It has already aroused public anger and lost public support on the island.\nThe full resumption of cross-Strait tourism is entirely the responsibility of the DPP authorities. In the face of the calls from the island’s tourism industry, and in light of the excitement of Taiwanese tourists who have recently “scrambled” for the chance to travel to the mainland, the DPP authorities should immediately stop political manipulation, readily accept good advice, and change course.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","海峡之声电台记者","After the “2.14” serious ship collision incident, the DPP authorities took the opportunity to side with the US’s so-called “international waters theory” for the Taiwan Strait, echoing the US claim that “the Chinese Communist Party’s unilateral declaration of its position on Taiwan and the Taiwan Strait is to turn the Taiwan Strait into an internal sea.” They attempted to link it to so-called “freedom of…","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese territory, and China enjoys sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. Under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea and China's domestic law, the waters of the Taiwan Strait are, respectively, China's internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone and exclusive economic zone; there is no so-called 'international waters.' In fact, international law of the sea has no concept of 'international waters' at all.\nUnder relevant provisions of the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea, foreign vessels may 'innocently pass' through parts of the Taiwan Strait waters, and the Taiwan Strait has long been one of the busiest trade transport channels in the world. The DPP authorities, in order to 'rely on foreign powers to seek independence,' are willing to sell out national interests, ignore facts and cater to US fallacies, and cooperate with external forces in hyping. Truly, their 'selling out Taiwan' has no bottom line, and their 'harming Taiwan' has no ceiling.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605915.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","This year’s Government Work Report mentioned the target of 5% growth in gross domestic product for 2024, and also mentioned key work areas such as future industries, the digital economy and rural revitalization. In your view, in which areas can Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots seize opportunities?","The annual economic growth target in this year's Government Work Report is set at around 5%. This target has been scientifically demonstrated. It conforms to the annual requirements of the 14th Five-Year Plan and basically matches the potential for economic growth. It is a positive and achievable goal. It also shows that even in the face of uncertainty in external factors, the mainland's economy still has bright prospects and will continue to consolidate and strengthen its basic trend of long-term positive development. This will open up broader space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to take root on the mainland and participate in high-quality development.\nThis year's Two Sessions wrote the development of new quality productive forces into the Government Work Report for the first time. It requires giving full play to the leading role of innovation, deeply cultivating and growing emerging industries, forward-looking layout of future industries, and promoting industrial innovation through technological innovation. This will create more opportunities for strengthening cross-Strait industrial cooperation. Cross-Strait industries have complementary advantages. Taiwan-funded enterprises have technological advantages in advanced manufacturing, new materials, biomedicine and other fields, a solid foundation in big data, artificial intelligence and other areas, and rich experience in modern agriculture and modern service industries. They should follow the requirements of high-quality development, seize the opportunities of developing new quality productive forces, actively lay out future industries, participate in the innovative development of the digital economy, share in the dividends of mainland rural revitalization policies, and actively devote themselves to cross-Strait integrated development.\nWe will continue to introduce measures for deepening cross-Strait integrated development, improve policy measures that benefit the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, continue to implement equal treatment, improve service levels, optimize the business environment, and provide stronger policy support for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland for development. We will help everyone open up new frontiers for their careers on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","In the fiscal year 2025 budget proposal recently released, the US government listed a separate item for Taiwan for the first time. A US official said this move is intended to help Taiwan strengthen its deterrence capabilities and demonstrates US security commitments to Taiwan. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","First, I must emphasize that Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to put into practice its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” to stop arming Taiwan, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","On the first question: the negotiations between the two sides over the “2·14” vicious ship-collision incident have yielded no results, and mainland personnel recently returned to Quanzhou. The DPP authorities said that since March 1, the waters between Xiamen and Kinmen have become calm, with no special circumstances. The follow-up handling of this incident has drawn great attention from all sides. Online public…","First question: This reflects the DPP authorities’ true attitude of trying to muddle through. What measures we take next will depend on what attitude the DPP authorities adopt in handling the “2·14” vicious ship collision incident, and what account they give to the families of the victims and to compatriots on both sides. If the DPP authorities evade the issue and keep stalling, we will take further measures, and all consequences shall be borne by the Taiwan side.\nSecond question: Only if the DPP authorities abandon the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and stop colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke can compatriots from all walks of life in Taiwan, including military personnel, enjoy peaceful and tranquil good days.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Kuo Cheng-liang, a former Taiwan lawmaker, recently disclosed the reasons for his departure from the DPP, stating bluntly that the DPP is a “Taiwan independence” party and that “Taiwan independence” discourse is a dead end that cannot go on. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP is a “Taiwan independence” party, as everyone knows. In terms of ideology, in October 1991, the DPP wrote into its party constitution, by amending its party platform, the establishment of “a Taiwan Republic with sovereign independence and the enactment of a new constitution.” This is the “Taiwan independence party platform.” In terms of practice, whether during the periods when Chen Shui-bian or Tsai Ing-wen was in power, the DPP has always schemed to carry out “Taiwan independence” separatism, attempting to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, in which both sides belong to one China.\nNo matter how the DPP “argues” or how it packages itself, in short, “Taiwan independence” means splitting Taiwan away from China. On this, more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, will never agree; Chinese sons and daughters at home and abroad will never agree; and the invincible Chinese People's Liberation Army will never agree. “Taiwan independence” was a dead end in the past, and it is an absolutely impassable dead end now and in the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","At the just-concluded National Two Sessions, besides issues such as opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification, we also noted that cross-Strait film, television and cultural exchanges were another Taiwan-related topic widely discussed by deputies and members. Committee member Feng Yuanzheng, when answering a Taiwan Strait interview, movingly recalled his performances in Taiwan. At the “committee…","I have also noted the situations you mentioned. The Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests and the national sentiments of the Chinese people, and it concerns the overall situation of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. It is only natural that NPC deputies and CPPCC members, who are representatives of all regions, ethnic groups, and sectors across the country, pay attention to cross-Strait issues and care about Taiwan work. The State Council Taiwan Affairs Office will voluntarily accept the NPC’s work supervision and legal supervision and the CPPCC’s democratic supervision, listen to and adopt the opinions and suggestions of deputies and members, earnestly handle the suggestions and proposals of deputies and members, and continuously promote high-quality development of Taiwan work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","On the first question: the spokesperson said that the responsibility for not fully restoring cross-Strait tourism lies with the DPP authorities. Both sides bear responsibility for opening up tourism across the Strait. May I ask whether the spokesperson encourages both sides to be willing to take the first step in opening up tourism? On the second question, continuing from what Qiu Guozheng said about worrying…","On the first question: compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese, and they all want to travel more, get closer, and build deeper ties, and hope to be able to exchange freely without obstacles. To date, the DPP authorities have not lifted the bans and restrictions on civilian exchanges from the mainland to Taiwan, and the few exchanges that do take place must all go through what Taiwan calls “special case applications.” The DPP authorities still have not lifted the ban on group tours by Taiwan residents to the mainland, and they use various overt and covert means to suppress and intimidate Taiwan residents who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, creating a “green terror” that has left many Taiwan compatriots wanting to come to the mainland but unable to, or afraid to.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We will continue to work toward normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and making exchanges and cooperation in all fields routine. The DPP authorities should face up to the desire of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges, promptly remove all artificial barriers, and stop all obstruction and suppression of cross-Strait personnel exchanges.\nOn the second question: I am confident and steady, and I sleep fairly well. It's only that my work is busy, so I often don't get enough sleep. History is the best textbook and the best wake-up call. If you want Taiwan's military personnel, including the individual you mentioned, and all sectors of Taiwan society to sleep soundly and rest easy, you might revisit the prosperity and grandeur of the peaceful development period across the Strait from 2008 to 2016 and look for answers there. The answer lies in Taiwan. If everyone makes the effort to look, they will surely find a shortcut to resting easy and sleeping soundly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","Chiu Kuo-cheng, head of Taiwan's defense authorities, recently said that, in response to the “enemy situation” and to strengthen training, the Taiwan military will increase the frequency of precision munitions firing this year, and the frequency of U.S. military personnel coming to Taiwan for “training assistance” will also increase. What is your comment on this?","This once again proves that the DPP authorities’ desire for peace is false, while their attempt to “seek independence by force” is real. The US’s “support for Taiwan” is false, while its “destruction of Taiwan” is real.\nThe DPP authorities are lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people to buy weapons from the US to “embolden themselves,” and are forcibly introducing measures on the island such as “extending the compulsory military service period by one year.” They are slavishly cooperating with the US in so-called military training plans, step by step tying Taiwan compatriots to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coercing young people in Taiwan into becoming “cannon fodder.” The US always puts its own interests first. To the US, Taiwan is merely a “chess piece” for containing China’s development, and so-called “support for Taiwan” is actually “harm to Taiwan” and “destruction of Taiwan.” Taiwan may go from being a “chess piece” to a “discarded piece” at any time.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Attempting to “seek independence by force” or “rely on external forces to seek independence” will only plunge Taiwan into dire warfare and danger, and will ultimately lead to its own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240313_12605911.htm"],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","The National Arts Fund recently published the application guide for its 2025 fine arts creation funding projects, which states that “Taiwan-region literary and arts workers who are employed by or studying at art institutions, units, or higher education institutions in mainland China” may apply. Please introduce the situation regarding the National Arts Fund’s opening to Taiwan compatriots.","The National Arts Fund's opening to Taiwan compatriots is an important measure in implementing the “Several Measures on Promoting Cross-Strait Economic and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation.” Since its establishment, the National Arts Fund has been open to Taiwan-funded institutions or entities registered on the mainland. Eligible institutions may apply for the National Arts Fund's stage arts creation projects, fine arts creation projects, communication and exchange promotion projects, and arts talent training projects. Since 2019, the National Arts Fund has been open to applications from Taiwan cultural workers working or studying on the mainland who are under 40 years of age, for the Young Artistic Creative Talent Funding Project.\nThis year, to continue encouraging compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly promote Chinese culture, the National Arts Fund has further expanded the scope of funding, increased funding intensity, and opened individual projects within the fine arts creation funding projects for application. Eligible Taiwan compatriots are welcome to submit application materials between April 15 and June 15 this year through the National Arts Fund website (http://www.cnaf.cn) by logging into the “National Arts Fund Funded Project Management System.” The National Arts Fund Management Center will, in accordance with the provisions of the National Arts Fund Charter, organize expert review, submit the results to the National Arts Fund Council for deliberation, determine funded projects and funding amounts, and carry out supervision. Eligible Taiwan compatriots are welcome to register and apply.\nWe will continue to support and encourage more Taiwan cultural workers to participate in the development of the mainland's cultural undertakings, walk in step with outstanding mainland cultural workers, become promoters and contributors to inheriting and carrying forward Chinese culture, and jointly create and share cultural prosperity, deepening cross-strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","The head of Taiwan's veterans affairs authorities recently said in the legislature that force should not be used against mainland fishing boats that have allegedly “crossed the line,” because “the people on the other side are also Chinese.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are, of course, proud and upright Chinese. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and are full of confrontational thinking. They ignore the historical fact that fishermen from both sides of the Taiwan Strait have operated in the traditional fishing grounds of the Taiwan Strait, and they continue to treat Mainland fishermen in brutal and dangerous ways. This practice goes against public opinion and is vile in nature, and it is also the main cause of the “2·14” vicious ship-collision incident. For this, we strongly condemn it and demand that they prevent such incidents from happening again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question: Regarding the Kinmen boat collision incident, can the two sides handle follow-up issues in accordance with the “Kinmen Agreement”? The second question: Among the agreements mentioned in the ECFA text, including those on services trade and goods trade, as well as the dispute settlement mechanism, does the mainland side believe further improvement is needed? Lai Hsing-yuan, former chair of the…","On the first question, I have already answered very clearly. Only when the DPP authorities face the problem, adopt a proper attitude, and demonstrate sincerity in solving the problem can consultations on the aftermath of the “February 14” malicious ship-collision incident resume.\nOn the second question, the ECFA states very clearly in its preamble: “The Parties agree to progressively reduce or eliminate trade and investment barriers between them and create a fair trade and investment environment, in accordance with the basic principles of the World Trade Organization (WTO), taking into account their economic conditions.” The basic principle of the WTO is non-discrimination. The two sides signing the ECFA to promote trade liberalization across the Strait should, in principle, proceed on the basis of normalized cross-Strait trade. However, considering that the two sides are one family, and so that compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, could be the first to enjoy the benefits of the ECFA, we agreed to advance the normalization and liberalization process at the same time, even though the Taiwan authorities still restricted the import of more than 2,000 mainland agricultural and industrial products, an abnormal and discriminatory situation. We implemented the Early Harvest Program first, and taking into account the economic conditions of both sides, we did not require equivalence between the two sides in the quantity or trade value of early-harvest products. To put it plainly, the mainland let Taiwan go first.\nChapter II of the ECFA, “Trade and Investment,” clearly states that the Parties agree that, on the basis of the early harvest in trade in goods and trade in services, they will begin consultations on agreements on trade in goods and trade in services no later than six months after the entry into force of the agreement, and complete them as quickly as possible. The mainland has consistently implemented the relevant provisions of the agreement earnestly. However, for reasons that are well known, the signing of the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services has not taken effect, and the consultations on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods were forced to be suspended. I note that there has been a great deal of reflection and self-examination on this on the island recently.\nThe Taiwan side's approach does not conform to the ECFA's objective of “progressively reducing or eliminating trade and investment barriers between them and creating a fair trade and investment environment.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS记者","Regarding whether mainland fishing boats may pass through the “prohibited and restricted waters” off Kinmen, the Mainland Affairs Council first said they may, in accordance with the 2015 “Liuwudian Channel Agreement.” Taiwan's Coast Guard later denied this, saying it is not permitted, and that dredging vessels passing through this channel must notify in advance, or they will be driven away. We note that several…","What you just reported left me with mixed feelings. Some Taiwanese officials and departments often fail to understand the situation, fail to understand history, and fail to understand their own regulations. Their statements are contradictory and very unprofessional.\nJust look at Taiwan's own internal management documents, and you can tell whether their claims are wrong or right. The mainland dredging vessel you mentioned, which appeared in the Liuwudian channel, was carrying out routine, regular channel dredging operations. As for why the Taiwan side makes such a fuss over a normal operation like this, the reason is self-evident.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-13","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","The first question: The Taiwanese film “Zhou Chu Removes the Three Evils” was released in mainland China on March 1, and as of yesterday its box office had exceeded 400 million RMB. How does the spokesperson view the phenomenon of Taiwanese films being box-office hits on the mainland? At the same time, the mainland TV drama “Blossoms” has also sparked a binge-watching craze in Taiwan. Going forward, how can…","On the first question, the Taiwan films and mainland TV series you mentioned have both earned a good reputation on both sides of the Strait. This shows that compatriots on both sides, who share the same language and culture, especially resonate and empathize with each other. We have consistently supported and actively promoted cross-strait film and television exchange and cooperation, and we encourage relevant Taiwan businesses to develop on the mainland.\nI noticed that Wang Jing, the female lead of “Zhou Chu Removes Three Evils,” said in an interview on the island that she had not expected the film’s box office on the mainland to exceed 400 million yuan. What I want to say is that the vastness of the mainland is something many Taiwan performers find hard to imagine, and it is also something they long for. We hope that the film and television communities on both sides of the Strait will further strengthen cooperation, create more film and television works that compatriots on both sides love, jointly carry forward Chinese culture, enrich the leisure lives of ordinary people on both sides, promote the common development of the cross-strait film and television industries, and build up and strengthen the film and television industry of the Chinese nation.\nOn the second question, I am not aware of the specific circumstances you described. But, as you said, no job is inherently high or low, and young people from Taiwan and young people from the mainland should likewise be equal, regardless of status. Many young people on the mainland work as food-delivery riders. Why shouldn’t young people from Taiwan be able to deliver food? Of course, to my understanding, very few young Taiwanese work as food-delivery riders on the mainland, and the case you mentioned should be extremely rare. But in any case, as long as one works hard and strives upward, that deserves respect.\nIn recent years, we have adhered to the development philosophy centered on the people and the concept of “One Family Across the Strait,” and we have continuously created better conditions and provided greater room for Taiwan youth to study, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland, which has been widely welcomed and generally affirmed. In 2023, the mainland’s economy recovered and improved overall, with gross domestic product exceeding 126 trillion yuan, growing by 5.2%, ranking among the front of the world’s major economies, and it remains an important engine of global growth. Since the beginning of this year, the mainland’s economy has continued its trend of recovery and improvement, and the first quarter is expected to get off to a good start. The basic trend of stable economic performance and long-term improvement has not changed and will not change, and the mainland remains the best choice for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to find jobs and start businesses. In the future, we will continue to introduce policies and measures and build platforms to provide more opportunities and create better conditions for Taiwan youth to pursue, build, and realize their dreams on the mainland.\nOn the third question, compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and it is natural for them to visit each other often and keep in regular contact. On the political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we welcome political parties, groups, and personages from all walks of life in Taiwan to visit and exchange views on the mainland, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nToday’s press conference concludes here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240313_12605907.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-14","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","Taiwan dispatched coast guard boats today to rescue a capsized fishing vessel from the mainland near Kinmen. Can you confirm this and provide more details?","It’s not related to foreign affairs. I’d refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347715.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240314_11260824.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-03-15","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the U.S. government’s FY2025 budget bill separately listed Taiwan for the first time, authorizing the use of U.S. stockpiled weapons to assist Taiwan in strengthening its so-called “deterrence capability.” U.S. Army Green Beret special forces advisers have been stationed in Taiwan for the long term to help train Taiwan’s amphibious special operations forces. What comments does the spokesperson have on…","Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the first insurmountable red line in China-US relations. Recently, the US side has hollowed out, emptied, and distorted the one-China principle through means such as arms sales and military assistance to Taiwan and sending personnel to assist Taiwan's military training. This has sent a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and seriously undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Whoever indulges or supports “Taiwan independence” will surely bring disaster upon themselves and reap the bitter fruit. We urge the US side to immediately stop all forms of official exchanges and military contacts with the Taiwan region of China, stop arming Taiwan, and take concrete steps to honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.” The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains highly vigilant, firmly defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely crushes the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16294412.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-03-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On March 15, a formation of Fujian Coast Guard vessels conducted law enforcement patrols in accordance with the law in waters near Kinmen. In response, Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the Taiwan Affairs Office stated that since the \"February 14\" vicious ship collision incident occurred, the DPP authorities have shown no remorse for their callous disregard for human life, have ignored the legitimate demands of the families of the victims, and have even attempted to use their internal investigation procedures as an excuse to evade responsibility and cover things up, provoking shared opposition and strong indignation from compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including the people of Kinmen. Taiwan is part of China, and the mainland coast guard's law enforcement patrols in waters near Kinmen are a legitimate act to maintain order in the relevant maritime areas. We will not tolerate and will absolutely not indulge the DPP authorities' brutal conduct of disregarding the safety of mainland fishermen's lives and property and harming the feelings of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities must give the families of the victims and compatriots on both sides an account as soon as possible; the mainland reserves the right to take further measures, and all consequences shall be borne by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240315_12606371.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-18","Lin Jian","News 1 Korea","It’s said that people from Taiwan will participate in the Summit for Democracy that opens today in the ROK. What’s China’s comment? My second question is what’s China’s comment on the DPRK this morning firing another ballistic missile in a month?","On your first question, China firmly opposes the ROK inviting the Taiwan authorities to participate in the so-called Summit for Democracy. There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Any attempts by external forces to interfere in China’s internal affairs, and connive at and support “Taiwan independence” are doomed to failure. China has strongly urged the ROK to abide by the one-China principle and stop providing podium for or supporting “Taiwan independence” forces. The world will not be deceived by the DPP authorities’ attempt to seek larger space for “Taiwan independence” activities under the banner of “democracy” and “human rights,” which will only make itself look bad and is doomed to failure.\nOn your second question, China noted relevant reports and that the ROK and the US held joint military drill targeting the DPRK. China believes that upholding peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula serves the common interests of all sides.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347717.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240318_11262087.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-18","Lin Jian","TASS","My first question is that Russian President Putin today in a press conference following the president election said that attempts made by China’s enemies, such as provocations around Taiwan, are doomed to failure. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment? My second question is that Putin was elected as President. Does China expect him to visit China?","On your first question, China highly commends President Putin’s statement. There is but one China in the world, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations.\nOn your second question, I have nothing to offer at the moment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347717.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240318_11262087.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-03-18","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 18 — Mainland coast guard vessels rescued two people in distress near Kinmen on March 18. Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answering reporters' questions on the same day, said: The mainland side adheres to a people-centered approach and has always placed great importance on safeguarding the lives and property of people on both sides of the Strait. The two sides of the Strait are one family. When sudden emergencies occur at sea, mutual rescue and mutual support are only natural. This reflects humanitarian spirit and further highlights the blood ties between compatriots on both sides.\nChen Binhua said that, according to what is known, at about 4 a.m. on March 18, the Fujian coast guard discovered an unnamed sport fishing boat that had lost power and was calling for help in the waters of Weitou Bay, and rescued two people. Both people were from Kinmen. The coast guard immediately provided medical aid and humanitarian care, supplying hot water, food, and cotton-padded clothing, and assigned dedicated personnel to accompany them. At present, the two people are in normal physical condition and have already called home to report their safety. The Fujian side will arrange for personnel and a vessel to return them to Kinmen as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240318_12606837.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-19","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan’s vice leader-elect Hsiao Bi-khim arrived in the Czech Republic today and will speak to a think tank there. What’s your comment?","China strongly opposes official interaction of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. This position is consistent and clear.\nIn multiple official documents, including the joint statements and joint communiqué between the government of China and the Czech government, the government of the Czech Republic solemnly committed to stick to the one-China policy, respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and recognize that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. China urges the Czech Republic to follow its commitment, strictly restrain certain politicians, immediately stop the egregious moves that undermine the national credibility of the Czech Republic and its relations with China. We urge the Czech Republic to take effective measures to undo the negative influence of the incident. Our message to “Taiwan independence” separatists is that whoever engages in “Taiwan independence” will be held accountable by history; whoever in the world creates “one China, one Taiwan” will get burned for playing with fire and taste the bitter fruit of their own doing.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347718.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240319_11262628.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-03-19","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华19日答记者","XINHUA, Beijing, March 19 — In response to the recent surreptitious visit to the Czech Republic by Taiwan's incoming vice president Hsiao Bi-khim, State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on the 19th, saying: We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between our diplomatic partners and the “Taiwan region of China” under any pretext. We urge the Czech side to…","Chen Binhua pointed out that the DPP authorities collude with external forces and devise so-called “diplomatic” breakthroughs in every way, serving the purpose of “Taiwan independence.” This harms the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots, cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and is not conducive to peace and stability in the Taiwan region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240319_12607096.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-21","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","According to US Admiral John Aquilino who is the leader of the Indo-Pacific Command in the address or speech given to the US House Armed Services Committee on Wednesday, China is building its military and nuclear arsenal on a scale not seen since World War II, and all signs suggest that China is sticking to its ambitions to be ready to invade Taiwan by 2027. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on this US…","The Asia-Pacific region is a pacesetter of peace and development, not an arena for geopolitical games. It is the US, not China, that stokes confrontation and creates division in the Asia-Pacific.\nMy solemn message to the US side: Taiwan is part of China and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and brooks no foreign interference. Our policy is quite clear—we will continue to strive for peaceful reunification with greatest sincerity. Our bottom line is also quite clear—we will never allow Taiwan to be separated from the motherland. Some in the US are attempting to play up the so-called “China threat”, heighten the tension across the Taiwan Strait and stoke confrontation. China firmly opposes this. To ensure cross-Strait peace, it is essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence”. No one should underestimate the determination, resolve and capability of the Chinese people in safeguarding our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347721.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240321_11264985.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-21","Lin Jian","Dragon TV","Solomon Islands’ Prime Minister Manasseh Sogavare reportedly praised China’s achievements in fueling the economy during a speech on March 20. He said that his country has been struggling to make headway in economic growth for the past several decades with the “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan. He added that his wise decision to break “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and establish diplomatic ties with China put the…","Since the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Solomon Islands in September 2019, the two countries have enjoyed fast growth of bilateral relations, friendly cooperation in various fields, and fruitful results which have brought tangible benefits to the people in Solomon Islands. What has happened proves that the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries meets the expectation of the two peoples, follows the prevailing trend in the international community, and serves the common interests of the two peoples.\nThe fast growth of the bilateral relations since the establishment of our diplomatic ties fully demonstrates that establishing and developing relations with China based on the one-China principle is a right choice that stands the test of time and history. It’s never too late to welcome new friends. As long as we engage with each other, we will usher in a bright future. For a handful of countries who still maintain the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan region, the example set by Solomon Islands deserves some serious thought.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347721.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240321_11264985.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-03-22","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","The Prime Minister of Eswatini Russell Mmiso Dlamini visited Taiwan recently, during which he met with Tsai Ing-wen, Lai Ching-te and “Premier of the Executive Yuan” Chen Chien-jen, attended the welcome dinner hosted by head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs office Wu Jaushieh, visited Taiwan’s companies and universities and held the Seminar on Exploring Investment Opportunities in the Kingdom of Eswatini. What is…","We noted the recent visit to Taiwan by the Prime Minister of Eswatini Russell Mmiso Dlamini. This is a grave provocation to the one-China principle and China’s sovereignty. China firmly opposes this.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a prevailing international consensus that brooks no challenge. On the visit to Taiwan by the Prime Minister of Eswatini, I would like to stress the following two points:\nFirst, over the past 56 years of the so-called “diplomatic ties” between Eswatini and the Taiwan region, the people of Eswatini hardly received any tangible benefits and Eswatini’s national development hardly achieved any progress. We believe the people of Eswatini know this well. The Taiwan authorities squander the taxpayers’ money to support some bigwigs in Eswatini to maintain the so-called “diplomatic ties.” This kind of relationship is worth nothing to people in Taiwan and in Eswatini.\nSecond, over 180 countries and international organizations reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle after the elections in the Taiwan region. Recently, Nauru reestablished diplomatic ties with China, cutting the number of countries that have the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan region to only 12. Undeniable facts once again show that one China is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. Certain persons in power in Eswatini run counter to the trend of the times and maintain the so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan region. Such moves find no support and will not persist.\nWe believe that the people of Eswatini will see clearly the truth about “Taiwan independence” and recognize the perils of the deformed “dollar diplomacy” between Taiwan and Eswatini. We urge certain persons in power in Eswatini to see squarely the prevailing consensus in the international community, refrain from being self-deceptive or deliberately undermining the one-China principle, which is a basic norm governing international relations, and realize their errors and mend their ways as soon as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347722.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240322_11266265.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-03-22","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 22 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the repatriation of the two Kinmen persons in distress who were rescued on the 18th, on the 22nd.\nA reporter asked: On March 18, mainland coast guard rescued two Kinmen persons in distress. The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said that day that they would be repatriated as soon as possible, but it is understood that the two have not yet returned. What progress has been made in handling this matter?\nChen Binhua said that at around 4 a.m. on March 18, the Fujian Coast Guard discovered a sea-fishing boat without a registered name calling for help in the waters of Weitou Bay and rescued two people. Both were from Kinmen. In keeping with the concept of “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family,” we have provided medical assistance and humanitarian care to the two over the past few days, offered thoughtful services in various respects, and allowed them to call their families to report that they were safe.\nChen Binhua said that, according to our understanding, the two men are a man surnamed Hu and a man surnamed Wu. The man surnamed Hu is an active-duty member of the Taiwan military. He did not truthfully state his identity and fabricated false occupational information, deliberately concealing it. The relevant departments need to further verify and understand the situation. As for the man surnamed Wu, the relevant Fujian authorities repatriated him to Kinmen today.\nChen Binhua emphasized that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are bound by blood ties. When sudden dangers arise, they rescue each other and look out for one another. This has always been the case, and it should be so.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240322_12607884.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-25","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","It’s reported that on March 23, Paraguay’s President Santiago Peña wrote on Platform X that the 66-year “diplomatic ties” between Paraguay and Taiwan run deep, which does not affect Paraguay’s trade with China. Paraguay continues to export soybeans to China. Both Taiwan and Paraguay are surrounded by major powers. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. Standing up for the one-China principle is the right thing to do and is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends.\nDespite the fact that China is the world’s top importer of soybean, our official data shows that China’s soybean imports from Paraguay have been zero in recent years. If the government of Paraguay truly puts national development and its people’s wellbeing close to its heart, the desirable thing to do is to see the prevailing trend and stand on the right side of history, instead of relying on petty tricks and looking for chances to exploit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347723.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240325_11270445.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-03-25","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 25 (dateline): Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 25th that Mr. Ma Ying-jeou will lead Taiwan youth to Guangdong, Shaanxi, Beijing, and other places from April 1 to 11 to seek roots, engage in exchanges, participate in activities including the “Jiachen (2024) Qingming Memorial Ceremony for the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan,” and make visits. We welcome Mr. Ma Ying-jeou to lead the delegation on this visit, and hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will jointly inherit and promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture of honoring ancestors with reverence and remembering one’s origins, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various fields, including cross-Strait youth exchanges, enhance mutual understanding and spiritual affinity, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, benefit compatriots on both sides, and jointly promote the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240325_12608226.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","A symposium on studying and implementing the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important remarks on Taiwan-related matters at the two sessions was recently held in Beijing. Please introduce the relevant situation. How will the Taiwan Affairs Office implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important remarks in the next step?","On March 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, together with the Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, the Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League, and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, convened a symposium in Beijing to earnestly study, fully understand, and thoroughly implement the important speech General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered on Taiwan work on March 6, when he visited CPPCC members from the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, the science and technology sector, and the environment and resources sector attending the Second Session of the 14th National Committee of the CPPCC. The meeting stressed that General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech is far-sighted, profound in thought, and rich in meaning. It clarified the basic tasks, work priorities, and policy measures for Taiwan work under the new circumstances, and profoundly pointed out the historical position and mission of relevant parties and mass organizations, including the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, in the overall picture of Taiwan work. It has strong political, ideological, guiding, and targeted character, provides important theoretical guidance and practical direction for Taiwan work, and is the fundamental guideline for doing Taiwan work well.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, as the dedicated departments responsible for Taiwan work, will earnestly study and implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech, resolutely carry out the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, shoulder the mission and responsibility of national reunification, promote the spirit of historical initiative, firmly grasp the leadership and initiative in cross-Strait relations, and actively promote exchange, cooperation, and integrated development across all fields between the two sides. They will unite all patriotic forces that can be united, both at home and abroad and on the island, continuously expand the forces opposing “independence” and promoting reunification, and jointly advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608829.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","On March 19, the Central Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission jointly held the Fujian Provincial Symposium on Deepening Cross-Strait Integration Development in Pingtan. Please introduce the relevant details.","To implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important remarks on Taiwan-related matters during the two sessions, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission jointly held a symposium on deepening cross-Strait integrated development in Fujian Province in Pingtan on March 19. Responsible persons from the two departments, Luo Dongchuan, Deputy Secretary of the Fujian Provincial Party Committee, and responsible persons from relevant prefecture-level cities and departments attended the meeting.\nSong Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at the meeting that General Secretary Xi Jinping's important remarks on Taiwan-related matters point the way for advancing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and building a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone of high quality. Director Song Tao emphasized that it is necessary to adhere to the policies of exploring a new path for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and building a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continuously promote new results in cross-Strait integrated development.\nGuo Lanfeng, member of the Party Leadership Group of the National Development and Reform Commission, said that the NDRC will next support Fujian Province in creating a world-class business environment, formulate opinions on special measures to relax market access to promote integration between Fujian and Taiwan, and push industrial cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan to become more substantive and deeper. Deputy Secretary Luo Dongchuan said that Fujian Province will focus on building the “three major demonstration models” of social integration, economic integration, and emotional integration across the Taiwan Strait, actively build a new pattern of integration across the entire region, and push the construction of the demonstration zone to achieve new progress.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608828.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The head of Taiwan’s finance authority recently said relevant departments and agencies have conducted “financial war games,” and that if cross-Strait war broke out, they could consider raising taxes or fees to raise “war-readiness funds.” This has prompted questions on the island about whether they are discussing a “war tax.” What comment do you have?","This shows that the DPP authorities are deliberately creating tension and confrontation, using hype and manipulation of “war preparedness” to pursue their party's narrow interests. This runs completely counter to their professed claim of “seeking to ease tensions in the Taiwan Strait.” If they are allowed to go down the wrong path of “Taiwan independence” to the bitter end, the broad masses of Taiwan's compatriots will be the greatest victims.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","The DPP authorities recently announced that live-fire shooting will be conducted in April at Kinmen's main island, Lieyu and other places, which has raised questions in public opinion on the island. The Taiwan military said the relevant practice is routine, regular training firing and is not targeted. What is your comment?","Whether it is “routine” training or “targeted” provocation, the DPP authorities know better than anyone. Kinmen compatriots, having experienced firsthand the transition between peace and war, have come to cherish peace all the more and oppose war, and they have already made the right choice between “firing cannons” and “building bridges.” We are closely monitoring the movements of Taiwan's military in Kinmen. If they provoke trouble and dare to act rashly, they will surely be defeated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608825.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The DPP recently stated that the “Sunflower Student Movement” ten years ago had an important and far-reaching impact on Taiwan’s political development. Lin Fei-fan, who served as its so-called “commander-in-chief” at the time, claimed that the movement blocked the agenda for cross-Strait integration and laid the consensus foundation for mainstream Taiwan public opinion to see Taiwan as “Taiwan of the world”…","Lin Fei-fan’s remarks amount to a self-incriminating confession. They show that the leaders of the so-called “Sunflower Student Movement” at the time were not considering the improvement of the island’s economy and people’s livelihoods, but rather blocking the momentum toward improvement and development of cross-Strait relations, so that they could seek political self-interest and pursue “Taiwan independence” separatism. The Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Services failed to take effect, and follow-up negotiations on the Cross-Strait Agreement on Trade in Goods and other ECFA follow-up consultations were also forced to halt. Whether this has been a blessing or a curse for Taiwan’s development, the facts have already given the answer.\nWe note that many Taiwan media outlets have recently reflected deeply on this, and many industry figures have pointed out that Taiwan thereby missed a window of development opportunity. The actions of Lin Fei-fan and others are by no means “love for Taiwan,” but rather a downright “harm to Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command recently said that China will be prepared to “forcibly invade Taiwan” by 2027. The head of Taiwan's security department said it will conduct the necessary analysis of the relevant information. What comments do you have on this?","Some people in the United States with ulterior motives keep concocting so-called “time points,” hyping up the mainland's “military threat” and stirring up a war atmosphere across the Taiwan Strait. This is merely an excuse to interfere in the Taiwan issue and to make money for the US military-industrial complex. If the US government truly wishes to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, it should stop fanning the flames and take practical action to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to put into practice its statements of not supporting “Taiwan independence.”\nThe DPP authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests, willingly serve as pawns of external forces in “using Taiwan to contain China.” They constantly pursue “independence” and provoke, even at the cost of the lives and well-being of the people on the island. They eagerly cater to the United States by playing the “porcupine” and building “fortresses,” turning Taiwan into a “powder keg” and a “landmine island.” They absolutely are not doing this for the good of Taiwan's compatriots. They will only push Taiwan ever closer to the dangerous brink of war.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants. It is a sacred mission and a just cause. When and by what means to resolve the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Li Dawei, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that the Taiwan side wants to resume cross-Strait dialogue, but the mainland has consistently responded with “the One-China principle and the 1992 Consensus,” which clearly shows it has no such willingness. He hopes the other side will set aside prejudices so that the two sides can engage in exchanges and dialogue. What comments do you have on this?","The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle, clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the political foundation for dialogue and consultation between the two sides’ associations. If the Taiwan side truly wants to resume cross-Strait dialogue, it should return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Otherwise, merely talking about cross-Strait dialogue is truly insincere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608827.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Question one: Mr. Ma Ying-jeou will visit the mainland again in early April. Ma Ying-jeou's office executive director Hsiao Hsu-tsen recently said that after the cross-Strait leaders' meeting held in Singapore in 2015, he hopes to meet old friends again this time, and will fully respect the arrangements made by the mainland side. Can the spokesperson say whether this wish is likely to be realized?\nQuestion two:…","On the first question, we will properly arrange Mr. Ma Ying-jeou's visit. We welcome Mr. Ma Ying-jeou to visit with his delegation, are willing to provide necessary assistance, and wish Mr. Ma Ying-jeou a smooth trip.\nOn the second question, I currently have no information to provide.\nOn the third question, as you said, we all know Mr. Lee Wen-chung's party background and political experience. What I want to say is that, no matter who it is and whatever views he may have held in the past, we welcome anyone who is now willing to participate in promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of the one-China principle. Only when the DPP authorities abandon the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, stop colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, change their confrontational mindset of “opposing China on everything,” and return to the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, can peace and stability be maintained in the Taiwan Strait area.\nOn the fourth question, the heart's illness must be cured with the heart's medicine, and the person who tied the bell must untie it. We are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and representatives on the basis of the one-China principle. The DPP's obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position is the fundamental obstacle to its interaction with us.\nOn the fifth question, the completion of the legislation under Article 23 of the Basic Law has filled the gap in the national security maintenance system and mechanism of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and provides an important institutional guarantee for the prosperity, stability and long-term order of Hong Kong. The DPP authorities have launched fierce attacks on this, which is nothing more than fear that Hong Kong will maintain prosperity and stability, making their slanders against “one country, two systems” untenable.\nThe DPP authorities are accustomed to intimidating the public, saying where one can and cannot go, as if the travel destinations of people on the island must be designated by them. What I want to emphasize is that we have consistently encouraged and supported normal and healthy exchanges between Hong Kong and Taiwan, and we protect the lawful and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots need have no concerns at all when traveling to and from Hong Kong and the mainland. They can come happily and return safely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Gansu Tianshui malatang has recently become a viral sensation and has also drawn considerable attention from many Taiwanese netizens. From Zibo barbecue to the Harbin Ice and Snow World, Taiwanese tourists have been a common sight. Many young people born after 2000 (“00后”) on the island have said that after going to the mainland in person, they changed their original views, saying that “the mainland is not what…","Every time I see news like this, I always feel warm and moved. From learning the “Subject Three” dance from Guangxi, to checking in at the ice city of Harbin, from “planting grass” for Sichuan sour cabbage fish, to the craze for Gansu spicy hot pot, mainland food, scenery, and popular culture are especially likely to become hugely popular among Taiwan compatriots, especially young people. Ultimately, this is because the two sides are one family with the same people and customs. We are all Chinese, born with Chinese taste buds and loving this flavor. As for the claim that “the mainland and the DPP say different things,” we welcome compatriots on the island to come to the mainland often to see for themselves, and we also hope they will think deeply about why the DPP authorities deliberately deceive and keep deceiving people again and again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","广东广播电视台记者","The Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference 2024 will be held in Boao, Hainan, from the 26th to the 29th. Please introduce the relevant situation of Taiwan personnel attending the events.","It is understood that the Taiwan industry and commerce representatives currently confirmed to attend the 2024 Annual Conference of the Boao Forum for Asia mainly include Chan Huo-sheng, Chairman of the Cross-Strait Common Market Foundation; Cher Wang, Chairwoman of HTC; Chen Wen-chi, Chairman of the VIA Group; and Chen Yen-chi, Chief Representative of Taishin International Bank. We welcome Taiwan industry and commerce representatives to actively take part in the Boao Forum Annual Conference, and necessary services and reception will be provided.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Solomon Islands Prime Minister Sogavare (索加瓦雷) recently praised China’s achievements in promoting economic development and said that the decision to cut ties with the Taiwan authorities and establish diplomatic relations with China was wise. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","We highly commend the Solomon Islands for making the correct choice based on its own national interests and the interests of its people. At present, 183 countries around the world have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of adhering to the one-China principle. Facts have repeatedly proven that the one-China principle is the common understanding of the international community and reflects the people's wishes and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","On March 18, the mainland coast guard rescued two people in distress near Kinmen. Among those rescued, a man surnamed Wu was sent back to Kinmen on the 22nd. Could the spokesperson introduce the latest progress?","The relevant departments are further verifying and understanding the relevant situation. After the situation is verified, the relevant personnel will be properly dealt with.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","The drama 'Seeking Flavors', created by dozens of outstanding performers from both sides of the Strait, is about to be staged at the National Centre for the Performing Arts. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The cross-strait theatrical production “Seeking Flavor” was jointly produced by the Cultural Troupe of the All-China Federation of Trade Unions, the Beijing Federation of Literary and Art Circles, and the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office, and dozens of talented performers and staff from both sides of the Strait took part in its creation. Starting from a bowl of beef noodles, the play moves from Taiwan's military dependents' villages to Beijing's hutongs. Through the heartwarming story of a four-generation family's partings and reunions, it tells a special homecoming story and conveys the deep kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Since its premiere in early 2023, “Seeking Flavor” has received wide acclaim and has performed more than 30 times in Beijing, Shanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, and other places. It was selected for the first batch of the “Beijing Great Drama List” and as an outstanding production at the 18th China Theatre Festival, among other honors. Next, the production team of “Seeking Flavor” will tour Shijiazhuang, Xi'an, Chongqing, Guangxi, and other places. Everyone is welcome to come and watch.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","香港TVB记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou will lead Taiwan youth to visit and exchange in Shaanxi, Guangdong, Beijing and other places in April. Which official figures from the mainland will Mr. Ma meet during this visit? Will such visits and exchanges become regular?","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou is about to visit, and everyone is paying close attention to it. We will properly arrange the relevant activities for Mr. Ma's visit.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and they should naturally visit each other often. On the political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we welcome Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life to visit the mainland often for exchanges, to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","The Legislative Council of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region recently unanimously passed local legislation under Article 23 of the Basic Law. The DPP claimed this proves the mainland’s political commitment of “one country, two systems” is “completely untrustworthy,” and declared that it would firmly defend Taiwan’s “national sovereignty and democratic freedom.” What is your comment?","After the Hong Kong “Safeguarding National Security Ordinance” was passed, Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Mr. Lee Ka-chiu especially emphasized that freedoms of the press, speech, and assembly in Hong Kong remain fully protected. The DPP authorities, disregarding the facts, have made snide remarks about the Hong Kong national security ordinance, which is purely political manipulation aimed at pursuing “independence.” To this, the more than 7.5 million Hong Kong citizens, who are weary of chaos and yearn for order, will absolutely not accept it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","海峡之声电台记者","Taiwan media reported that on the 23rd, local time, US President Biden signed the “Government Appropriations Act, Fiscal Year 2024,” which includes provisions for providing no less than $300 million in so-called “free military aid” to Taiwan. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The U.S. side insisted on passing and signing a bill with negative content concerning Taiwan, which seriously interferes in China's internal affairs and seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this. We urge the U.S. side to translate its statements of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions, to stop arming Taiwan in any way, and to stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities' “relying on the U.S. to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” for the sake of their own party's private interests are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","Recently, the words and actions of Wang Xiaofei (汪小菲) at Da S’s (大S) residence in Taipei have drawn netizens’ attention. Some mainland netizens criticized that this may maliciously intensify cross-Strait contradictions and hoped the Taiwan Affairs Office could step in and manage it. What is your response?","Cross-Strait intermarriages have reached nearly 400,000 couples. The marriage between Wang Xiaofei and Da S is only one of those 400,000, and it will not escalate cross-Strait contradictions. Cross-Strait is one family, and intermarriage makes kin upon kin. I bless all cross-Strait marriages and hope that destined couples will grow old together. For the very few failed marriages, I also hope the parties can part on good terms, each going their own way in peace and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The ECFA has been in effect for more than ten years. Recently, around the tenth anniversary of the so-called “Anti-Service Trade Agreement Movement” on the island, reflections and self-examination have continued across Taiwan, with calls for the incoming Democratic Progressive Party team to pursue policies and routes that are conducive to peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to earnestly safeguard…","Since ECFA and its Early Harvest Program took effect, they have brought real benefits to cross-strait industries, especially related industries and people in Taiwan, and have won general public recognition. However, the product and service trade areas covered by the early harvest account for only a very small part of cross-strait trade in goods and services. The two sides should have conducted substantive negotiations on the various objectives of ECFA, such as trade in goods, trade in services, investment, and economic cooperation. They should have signed and implemented separate agreements to bring more benefits and greater development space to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan people and enterprises. However, for reasons well known to all, the subsequent Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement under ECFA was signed but has not taken effect, and negotiations on the Cross-Strait Trade in Goods Agreement were forced to be interrupted, which has affected the implementation of the agreements. This is indeed a major setback and regret for the development of Taiwan’s economy and industries and for the advancement of the interests of the people.\nThe facts of the past ten years have made more and more Taiwan people and enterprises realize that when cross-strait relations are good, Taiwan will be good, and Taiwan people and enterprises can gain more interests and well-being. The DPP authorities should face the mainstream public opinion on the island, which favors peace over war, development over decline, exchange over separation, and cooperation over confrontation. They should promptly remove the artificial barriers and restrictions that obstruct and undermine cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and adopt policy lines that are conducive to the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608826.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","台湾联合报记者","The mainland side has mentioned that cross-Strait personnel exchanges totaled 3 million person-trips last year, while Taiwan's statistics show that only 220,000 mainland residents visited Taiwan last year. Cross-Strait exchanges now show “fewer from the mainland, more from Taiwan.” Is this conducive to the mainland's vision of “wanting peace, wanting development, wanting exchanges and wanting cooperation” across…","The current state of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait is extremely abnormal, and the cause lies on the Taiwan side. To date, the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities have not lifted the bans and restrictions on private exchanges between the mainland and Taiwan. The very few visits to Taiwan that do take place must go through the so-called “special case application” process on the Taiwan side. They have also not lifted the ban on group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents, and they have taken various overt and covert measures to suppress and intimidate Taiwan residents who participate in cross-strait exchanges, creating a “green terror.” As a result, many Taiwan compatriots want to come to the mainland but cannot, or dare not.\n“Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation” is not a unilateral concept of the mainland, but a shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides. We will continue to work to restore normalized cross-strait personnel exchanges and to make cross-strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields routine. The DPP authorities should face the aspiration of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges, remove all artificial obstacles as soon as possible, and stop blocking and suppressing cross-strait personnel exchanges and interactions in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Officials of the DPP authorities have claimed that the mainland may use the return of the sea anglers detained at Kinmen to negotiate with and pressure the Taiwan authorities. How do you respond? The family members of the rescued person who has not yet been returned have expressed great concern. Chen Yu-chen, a KMT-affiliated public representative, said the mainland side is willing to arrange for family members…","We will properly handle this person in accordance with law and regulations, and in a reasonable and humane manner, and we will fully take into account the wishes of their family members. We also hope to be able to properly handle the matter after verifying the situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视“直新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that Lai Ching-te recently visited Taiwan’s “self-built submarine” and called for accelerating submarine production. What is the spokesperson’s comment on Taiwan’s production of submarines and the impact on Taiwan Strait security?","Spending Taiwan residents' hard-earned money on these useless things will not make Taiwan safer; it will only make Taiwan compatriots increasingly uneasy. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that separatism and confrontation have no way out, and that the delusion of “seeking independence through force” is even more presumptuous.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","The “Referendum Proposal on Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge,” initiated by the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge Construction Promotion Association, has completed the co-signatures of 734 proposers as required by relevant regulations, but the DPP authorities did not reply in writing within the filing period. Chen Cang-jiang, chairman of the association, questioned whether the DPP authorities are deliberately obstructing it.…","Xiamen-Kinmen integration is the greatest opportunity for Kinmen's development. To get rich, one must first build roads, so building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is the common call and urgent wish of Kinmen compatriots. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' move fully exposes their mindset of standing against the interests of Kinmen compatriots and deliberately restricting Kinmen's development.\nWe have always kept the interests and well-being of Kinmen compatriots in mind. In recent years, we have adopted measures that benefit Kinmen and its people, such as supplying water to Kinmen and further relaxing the limits on the number of bottles of Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers traveling on direct routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu may carry. Preliminary technical preparations for connecting Kinmen by electricity, gas and bridge are also largely complete. The Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, released last year, outline the attractive vision of “Xiamen and Kinmen facing each other across the water, and Gulangyu and Kinmen linked by a bridge.” We are willing to work together with Kinmen compatriots to remove obstacles and turn this promising vision into vivid reality as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The youth edition of the Kunqu opera “The Peony Pavilion,” jointly created by both sides of the Taiwan Strait, caused a sensation after its premiere in Taipei in 2004. Recently, the original cast returned to Taiwan to stage 20th-anniversary performances in Kaohsiung, Taipei, Hsinchu, and other places, sparking enthusiastic responses. May the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","The Youth Edition of “The Peony Pavilion” is a classic Kunqu opera production jointly created by the Suzhou Kunqu Opera Theatre of Jiangsu Province and renowned Taiwanese writer Mr. Pai Hsien-yung, together with elite Kunqu artists from both sides of the Strait. Since its premiere in Taipei in 2004, it has been performed 20 times in Taiwan and toured nearly 500 times at home and abroad, attracting more than 800,000 audience visits. It has been widely acclaimed and has sparked a “Kunqu craze.”\nFrom March 11 to April 1 this year, 76 performers and staff of the Jiangsu Provincial Kunqu Opera Theatre traveled to Taiwan to take part in the 20th anniversary celebration performances of the Youth Edition of “The Peony Pavilion.” The performances were led by original cast members, Plum Blossom Award winners of Chinese drama and National First-Class Actors Shen Fengying and Yu Jiulin, and included eight performances in three cities: Kaohsiung, Hsinchu, and Taipei. Twenty years later, the cross-Strait creators and performers returned to the premiere venue to launch the anniversary performances. This is a reunion after a long separation and also what everyone had hoped for, and it has won the love and welcome of Taiwan audiences and opera fans. As early as February, tickets for several performances had already sold out. Audience reaction at every performance was very enthusiastic, with many saying they were “deeply moved.” Even those watching Kunqu for the first time could feel the ultimate beauty of traditional opera and the profound depth of China's outstanding traditional culture.\nWe wish the anniversary performances every success, and we hope more Taiwan audiences, especially young audiences, will enjoy the beauty of Kunqu and gain a deeper understanding and appreciation of the splendid and long-standing history and culture of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202403/t20240327_12608824.htm"],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, Li Qiyue, Chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Tourism Development Association, said the DPP authorities’ “group tour ban” has caused great hardship for the island’s tourism industry, and that they especially look forward to the opening of Taiwan to mainland tourists. What is the crux of why cross-Strait tourism cannot be fully restored? When can it be fully restored?","The fact that cross-Strait tourism cannot be fully restored is entirely the responsibility of the DPP authorities. Group tours by Taiwan residents to the mainland have been banned for four years. On the issue of resuming travel by Taiwan residents to the mainland, the DPP authorities, out of political considerations, have flip-flopped, abused their power, and acted recklessly. They have already provoked public outrage and lost popular support on the island.\nAs early as last May, we announced the resumption of travel agencies’ group tour business for Taiwan residents to the mainland, and we have made all the necessary preparations. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for tourism, to tour our magnificent rivers and mountains and see the new face of development across various places. As for when mainland tourists can go to Taiwan, as you mentioned, the DPP authorities must create the conditions for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-03-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Some Taiwan media reported that in recent years, Taiwan’s industrial investment has shifted from focusing on mainland China to going global, with investment on the mainland falling sharply, and sixty percent of Taiwanese businesses that went to the mainland reporting declining profits and a pessimistic view of the mainland market. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwanese media outlet you mentioned has no journalistic professional ethics. For years it has specialized in talking down the mainland, yet the facts have repeatedly exposed its lies.\nThe mainland economy did indeed encounter some difficulties in the past two years due to the epidemic. However, last year it overcame pressure and recovered and improved, with GDP exceeding 126 trillion yuan and growing 5.2%, with its growth rate ranking among the top of the world's major economies. Its contribution to world economic growth exceeded 30%, making it the largest engine of world economic growth. Since the beginning of this year, the mainland economy has continued its trend of recovery and improvement. From January to February, value added of industrial enterprises above designated size grew 7% year on year, the service production index grew 5.8% year on year, and the total value of goods imports and exports grew 8.7% year on year, of which exports grew 10.3% and imports grew 6.7%. In terms of Taiwan-funded investment, last year the mainland's newly approved Taiwan-funded projects (including investments transferred through third places) and actually utilized Taiwan capital grew 31.7% and 37.1% year on year, respectively.\nThe 2024 annual meeting of the China Development High-Level Forum, which just concluded, was attended enthusiastically by nearly 100 CEOs of large multinational enterprises, who generally believe that China is a market with fast development and strong vitality, and expressed that they will continue to increase their investment in China in research and development, manufacturing, and market expansion. This fully shows that global capital remains optimistic about the mainland and looks forward to its development. As Chinese-style modernization advances comprehensively, the mainland's cultivation and development of new quality productive forces and its promotion of high-quality development will provide more market opportunities and broader development prospects for domestic and foreign investors. The mainland was in the past, is now, and will certainly in the future be the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest and do business. Taiwan businesspeople who are confident and take root on the mainland will surely achieve greater and better development.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202403/t20240327_12608821.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-03-28","Lin Jian","Global Times","On March 27, the Office of the Spokesperson of the US Department of State released a readout on the call between Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu and Deputy Secretary of State Kurt Campbell, saying the call was part of ongoing efforts to maintain open lines of communication between the US and China and responsibly manage competition in the relationship. Campbell underscored the importance of maintaining peace and…","On March 27, Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu had a phone call with US Deputy Secretary of State Kurt Campbell at US request. They exchanged views on the current China-US relations and international and regional issues of mutual interest.\nVice Minister Ma said the two presidents successfully met in San Francisco and established the San Francisco vision. Both sides need to deliver on the important common understandings and outcomes reached at the San Francisco summit meeting, and work to put China-US relations on a steady, sound and sustainable trajectory.\nVice Minister Ma elaborated on China’s position on Taiwan, Hong Kong, the South China Sea and economic, trade, scientific and technological issues. He asked the US side to seriously abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and respect China’s core interests, stop turning economic, trade, scientific and technological issues into political and security issues, stop irresponsibly pointing fingers at Hong Kong, and start playing a constructive role in safeguarding peace and stability in the South China Sea instead of doing the opposite.\nVice Minister Ma also stated China’s principled position on the Korean Peninsula issue and the Ukraine crisis.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347726.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240328_11272629.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question: the waters around Xiamen and Kinmen have remained tense since February 14. The Taiwan military plans to conduct live-fire shooting exercises in April on areas including Kinmen Island and will impose control over the surrounding waters. The Taiwan military says these are routine training with no specific target. Will the Ministry of National Defense take a targeted…","On the first question: Every move of the Taiwan military is within the PLA's grasp. Any provocative conduct by the DPP authorities will end in failure.\nOn the second question: The relevant exercises and training are normal arrangements within the plan, aimed at enhancing the PLA's ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The relevant parties need not be unduly alarmed. Regarding similar exercises and training activities, the PLA will continue to carry them out as planned in the future.\nWe firmly oppose the irresponsible remarks made by US military personnel on the Taiwan question. Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, which brooks no foreign interference. We are willing to strive with the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts toward the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will never allow Taiwan to split away from the motherland.\nThe Chinese People's Liberation Army is on full-time alert and ready to fight at any time. With a combat posture of “Always Ready,” it will defeat any interference by external forces and crush any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, someone on social media shared a satellite image of a bombing and shooting range in Inner Mongolia that is built to the same scale as Taipei’s Bo’ai Special District. In addition, at the Gaoli Mountain Tactical Training Center in Jiangsu, a building is regarded as a Taoyuan taekwondo hall in Taiwan. All sectors believe this is highly targeted. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Only people with ulterior motives will take it personally. As long as there is no “Taiwan independence,” there is no need to be anxious.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Cross-Strait military tensions remain high. On the 7th, Taiwan's “Minister of National Defense” Chiu Kuo-cheng, while answering questions from “legislators,” said that after then-U.S. House Speaker Pelosi visited Taiwan, he clearly revised the division of responsibilities and implemented it, changing the definition of “first strike” so that, as long as a PLA physical aircraft crossed the boundary line, Taiwan's…","Taiwan is part of China. Where does this so-called “Minister of National Defense” come from? We warn the DPP authorities not to act rashly, or they will be seeking their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, not long ago a Chinese coast guard vessel entered the so-called “prohibited waters” of Taiwan's Kinmen for the first time to carry out law enforcement patrols. Could the spokesperson say whether this is a countermeasure by the mainland to the vicious “2·14” ship collision incident?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan, and there is absolutely no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters” in the Xiamen-Kinmen waters. The mainland coast guard authorities conduct routine law enforcement patrol operations, which help maintain normal order in the relevant waters and safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. In the “2·14” vicious ship-collision incident, the DPP authorities treated human lives with contempt, shirked responsibility, and passed the buck. This has aroused public outrage among compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and they must give everyone a clear and explicit account. The PLA is closely monitoring the maritime situation and is making full preparations to handle emergencies, resolutely safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait area.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that China and NATO held the 8th Security Policy Dialogue not long ago. Could the spokesperson further introduce the relevant situation?","Earlier this month, the Office of International Military Cooperation of the Central Military Commission and the Security Department of the International Military Staff of NATO exchanged views on the international and regional situation, bilateral defense exchanges, and other issues of common concern. The Chinese side expressed concern and clarified its position on NATO's eastward expansion into the Asia-Pacific, the Taiwan question, and other matters, and both sides agreed to maintain communication and dialogue. In addition, since the beginning of this month, China has also held a security policy dialogue with the EU and a defense ministry working dialogue with Germany.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A U.S. congressional delegation is visiting Taiwan and met with Taiwan's “president” Tsai Ing-wen. The U.S. Congress recently approved more military aid to Taiwan, and Tsai expressed gratitude for it. The U.S. Congress stated that it will continue to support Taiwan's self-defense capabilities and continue to provide corresponding support. What is your comment on this?","First, a correction to one statement in the question: it is the leader of the Taiwan region, not a so-called Taiwan “president,” because Taiwan is part of China. As everyone knows, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. China firmly opposes any form of official exchange and military contact between the US and the Taiwan region, and firmly opposes US arms sales to the Taiwan region. We strongly urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle, not to harm China's sovereignty and security interests, and not to interfere in China's internal affairs.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, this year's Government Work Report's section on Taiwan emphasizes “resolutely advancing the great cause of reunification of the motherland” and does not mention “peaceful reunification.” Some analysts believe that the report simplifies its description of Taiwan-related content, which does not mean the mainland will reduce its actions toward Taiwan, and that in the future the mainland will…","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never allow Taiwan to split from the motherland. It must be emphasized that the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the “divine needle that pins down the seas” for maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Achieving the complete reunification of the country is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people.\nIn opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification, the PLA has always let its actions speak, and it has always been resolute and professional. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: the more rampant the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, the less likely peaceful resolution becomes. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to train and prepare for combat, and with an unshakable will and formidable capabilities, will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, in January this year, a spokesperson said that the China and US militaries were maintaining communication and coordination on the meeting of the Military Maritime Consultative Agreement mechanism. What is the current progress? What other activities will the Chinese and US militaries hold this year? Second, during the US-Philippines defense ministers’ call on the 27th, Austin…","On the first question. To implement the important consensus reached by the heads of state of China and the United States at their San Francisco meeting, since the beginning of this year, under the joint efforts of both sides, the military forces of China and the United States have steadily resumed dialogue and consultations on the basis of equality and mutual respect. On January 8 and 9, China and the United States held the 17th Defense Policy Coordination Talks in Washington, D.C., in which both sides engaged in in-depth exchanges of views on issues of mutual concern, including advancing the development of military-to-military relations and issues related to Taiwan, the South China Sea, and maritime and air security. From January 5 to 19, the Chinese side assisted the U.S. side in conducting on-site surveys in Guangxi and Hunan to locate the remains of U.S. military personnel who went missing in China during World War II. At present, preparations for the China-U.S. Maritime Military Safety Consultative Mechanism meeting are progressing smoothly, and we will release information at an appropriate time. In addition, both sides are coordinating communication and exchanges in other areas.\nThis year marks the 45th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the United States. We hope the U.S. side will genuinely respect the core interests of China, meet the Chinese side halfway, translate the important consensus of the two heads of state into concrete action, and jointly promote the healthy, stable and sustainable development of military-to-military relations.\nAs for your second question, I have already elaborated in detail on China's policy on the South China Sea issue earlier. You asked how China views the actions of the Philippine and U.S. militaries in the South China Sea. I believe this can be answered with two “nots”. First, it must not harm China's sovereignty, security and maritime rights and interests; second, it must not undermine peace and stability in the South China Sea region.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first: The UK and Australia recently signed a new defense agreement. The UK plans to send a carrier strike group to cruise the Indo-Pacific next year, submarines will be stationed at Australian bases, and Australian soldiers will receive training on UK submarines. In your repeated answers to questions just now, you have mentioned that “outsiders are unreliable.” Some analysts believe…","Regarding the first question: China has repeatedly expressed its strong opposition to the military cooperation among the US, UK, and Australia. The so-called “trilateral security partnership” among the US, UK, and Australia is, in essence, using military cooperation to stir up military confrontation, increase the risk of nuclear proliferation, intensify the arms race in the Asia-Pacific, and undermine regional peace and stability. This product of Cold War mentality is highly targeted and highly harmful, challenges rules, and is unpopular.\nRegarding the second question: I would like to respond on two levels. At the specific level, as I just mentioned, the PLA is cracking down on “independence” and promoting reunification, sleeping with its weapons at the ready and maintaining a combat posture of being “always prepared.” At the macro level, the PLA has ample strategic composure. No matter how the winds and waves blow, it stays as calm as strolling leisurely through a courtyard.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-03-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the Washington think tank “Center for Strategic and International Studies” published a research report stating that “if the United States becomes involved in a Taiwan Strait conflict, its key ammunition stockpiles would be exhausted within a week. Such ammunition shortages would weaken U.S. deterrence and increase the likelihood of further conflict breaking out in the Taiwan Strait.” U.S. think tanks…","Think tanks publish research reports from different perspectives, but my response to them is consistent: the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16297346.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-03-29","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan’s navy chief will visit the United States next week to attend a military ceremony and discuss naval cooperation, according to sources. Would the Foreign Ministry wish to comment?","We’ve noted the reports. China firmly opposes military collusion between the US and Taiwan.\nThere is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations. China urges the US to fully recognize the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question and the grave harm of relevant issues, deliver on its commitments with concrete actions, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop official interactions and military contact with Taiwan, and refrain from sending any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347727.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202403/t20240329_11273630.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-03","Wang Wenbin","AFP","President Xi Jinping and US President Joe Biden had a phone call last night. President Xi said that if the US is adamant on containing China’s hi-tech development, China is not going to sit back and watch. Can the Foreign Ministry clarify what he meaned by saying “China is not going to sit back and watch”?","First, let me use this opportunity to brief you on the phone conversation between the two presidents.\nLast night, President Xi Jinping spoke with US President Joe Biden on the phone at the request of the latter. The two presidents had a candid and in-depth exchange of views on China-US relations and issues of mutual interest.\nPresident Xi Jinping noted that his San Francisco meeting with President Biden last November opened a future-oriented San Francisco vision. Over the past months, their officials have acted on the presidential understandings in earnest. The China-US relationship is beginning to stabilize, and this is welcomed by both societies and the international community. On the other hand, the negative factors of the relationship have also been growing, and this requires attention from both sides.\nPresident Xi Jinping stressed that the issue of strategic perception is always fundamental to the China-US relationship, just like the first button of a shirt that must be put right. Two big countries like China and the United States should not cut off their ties or turn their back on each other, still less slide into conflict or confrontation. The two countries should respect each other, coexist in peace and pursue win-win cooperation. The relationship should continue moving forward in a stable, sound and sustainable way, rather than going backward.\nPresident Xi Jinping underlined three overarching principles that should guide China-US relations in 2024. First, peace must be valued. The two sides should put a floor of no conflict and no confrontation under the relationship, and keep reinforcing the positive outlook of the relationship. Second, stability must be prioritized. The two sides should refrain from setting the relationship back, provoking incidents or crossing the line, so as to maintain the overall stability of the relationship. Third, credibility must be upheld. The two sides should honor their commitments to each other with action, and turn the San Francisco vision into reality. They need to strengthen dialogue in a mutually respectful way, manage differences prudently, advance cooperation in the spirit of mutual benefit, and step up coordination on international affairs in a responsible way.\nPresident Xi Jinping stressed that the Taiwan question is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. In the face of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external encouragement and support for them, China is not going to sit on its hands. He urged the US side to translate President Biden’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions. The US side has adopted a string of measures to suppress China’s trade and technology development, and is adding more and more Chinese entities to its sanctions lists. This is not “de-risking,” but creating risks. If the US side is willing to seek mutually beneficial cooperation and share in China’s development dividends, it will always find China’s door open; but if it is adamant on containing China’s hi-tech development and depriving China of its legitimate right to development, China is not going to sit back and watch.\nPresident Xi Jinping stated China’s position on Hong Kong-related issues, human rights, the South China Sea, and other issues.\nPresident Joe Biden noted that the US-China relationship is the most consequential relationship in the world. The progress in the relationship since the San Francisco meeting demonstrates that the two sides can advance cooperation while responsibly managing differences. President Biden reiterated that the United States does not seek a new Cold War, its objective is not to change China’s system, its alliances are not targeted against China, the US does not support “Taiwan independence,” and the US does not seek conflict with China. The US follows the one-China policy. It is in the interest of the world for China to succeed. The US does not want to curtail China’s development, and does not seek “decoupling” from China. The US will send Secretary of the Treasury Janet Yellen and Secretary of State Antony Blinken to visit China shortly to strengthen dialogue and communication, avoid miscalculation and promote cooperation, so as to advance the relationship on a stable path and jointly respond to global challenges.\nThe two presidents also exchanged views on the Ukraine crisis, the situation on the Korean Peninsula, and other issues.\nThe two presidents found the phone call to be candid and constructive. The two sides agreed to stay in communication, and tasked their teams to deliver on the San Francisco vision, including advancing the consultation mechanisms on diplomatic, economic, financial, commercial and other issues as well as mil-to-mil communication, carrying out dialogue and cooperation in such areas as counternarcotics, artificial intelligence and climate response, taking further steps to expand people-to-people exchanges, and enhancing communication on international and regional issues. The Chinese side welcomed visits to China by Secretary of the Treasury Janet Yellen and Secretary of State Antony Blinken in the near future.\nYou asked about China’s position on China-US economic ties. We have repeatedly pointed out that in recent years, China’s exports of electric vehicles, lithium batteries and photovoltaic products have increased. This is a result of international division of labor and market demand and has contributed to the green development of the world. It is quite clear to all whether it is “excess production capacity” that the US is truly concerned about. As for who is engaged in non-market practices, the fact is there for all to see. The US side has adopted a string of measures to suppress China’s trade and technology development. This is not “de-risking,” but creating risks. These are typical non-market practices. I believe people are quite familiar with China’s position on this. We will firmly safeguard our legitimate and lawful rights and interests and uphold the multilateral trade system.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347730.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240403_11276141.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-03","Wang Wenbin","AFP","A magnitude 7.5 earthquake hit the waters near Taiwan this morning, causing heavy casualties. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council said that the Chinese mainland is paying close attention to the disaster and would like to provide disaster relief to the people in Taiwan. Is there any response so far from relevant departments of Taiwan?","I’d refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347730.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240403_11276141.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-04-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On April 3, a strong earthquake occurred in Taiwan. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said that relevant parties on the mainland are highly concerned, extend sincere condolences to Taiwan compatriots affected by the disaster, will closely follow the disaster situation and subsequent developments, and are willing to provide disaster relief assistance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240403_12610538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-04-09","Mao Ning","CCTV","US Deputy Secretary of State Kurt Campbell recently said in an interview that AUKUS’ submarine capabilities have enormous implications in cross-Strait circumstances, and that there is a commonality of spirit with respect to the need to send clear messages on conduct with respect to either the South China Sea or the Taiwan Strait. He said every country in the Indo-Pacific wants very much to make clear that what…","Those comments are not based on facts. They paint a wrong picture of the reality in this region and contain some false, vicious and inflammatory accusations. China strongly deplores and opposes this.\nI want to stress that the real purpose of AUKUS is to incite bloc division and military confrontation through military cooperation based on exclusive circles. This is typical Cold War mentality. It heightens the risk of nuclear proliferation, exacerbates arms race in the Asia-Pacific and undermines regional peace and stability. China and many regional countries have expressed grave concerns and opposition over this.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. What is the US really up to by linking the AUKUS submarine plan with the Taiwan question? China has unwavering will in upholding its sovereignty and territorial integrity. No one should underestimate or misjudge it.\nNone of the AUKUS countries is a party directly concerned on the South China Sea issue and they should not interfere in the effort of parties concerned to settle disputes through negotiation and consultation. The recent heightening of tensions in the South China Sea and rise of confrontation in the region has everything to do with the US co-opting its allies.\nChina is neither the one that created the Ukraine crisis nor a party to it. We have and will continue to play a constructive role in promoting the political settlement of the issue. China urges the US to reflect on its behavior, stop fanning the flame, stop smearing and attacking the normal relations between China and Russia, and stop shifting the blame to China.\nChina is a force for world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of the international order. On peace and security issues, China has the best record among major countries. The international community has a fair judgment on this and the US is in no position to point fingers at China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347732.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240409_11278626.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 10, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou has led Taiwan youth to visit and exchange on the mainland for the past two years. During his visit to Sun Yat-sen University this time, he said there is still great room for development in cross-Strait youth exchanges, and that young people on both sides should be given more opportunities to get to know each other. What comment do you have?","The foundation of cross-Strait relations lies among the people, its driving force lies in the people, and its hope lies in the youth. Young people on both sides should shoulder important responsibilities, unite and show mutual care, and work hand in hand. We have consistently advocated and actively promoted cross-Strait youth exchanges, and we will, as always, create good conditions for cross-Strait young people to learn from and draw on each other, and provide more convenience for Taiwan youth to study, work, start businesses, and live on the mainland. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou has twice led Taiwan youth to visit and exchange on the mainland, and has invited teachers and students from five mainland universities to exchange visits to Taiwan. He has made important contributions to promoting cross-Strait youth exchanges, and we fully affirm this.\nAt present, the main obstacle to cross-Strait youth exchanges is obstruction and restriction by the DPP authorities. We will unite all sectors of cross-Strait society to work together, overcome obstacles, and actively carry out various activities that promote cross-Strait youth exchanges, so that more young people across the Strait can come to know and understand one another, walk together with one heart, and continuously inject youthful vitality into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612357.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","At 10:00 a.m. on April 3, a magnitude 7.3 earthquake struck the waters off Hualien, Taiwan. Circles across the mainland expressed sympathy and provided assistance. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Chinese nation has always had the fine tradition of sinking or swimming together and helping one another in times of need. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are bound by blood and share a bond as strong as gold. Over the years, in the face of major natural disasters, compatriots on both sides have empathized with one another, helped one another, and overcome difficulties together.\nAfter the magnitude 7.3 earthquake struck the sea area off Hualien, Taiwan, on April 3, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council expressed deep concern at the first opportunity, mourned the compatriots who died in the earthquake, and extended sympathy to the injured compatriots. The All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, the Red Cross Society of China, and the Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League each issued letters of condolence. Taiwan Affairs Offices in Fujian, Guangxi, and other localities expressed sympathy to the disaster area. Peking University, Sun Yat-sen University, Wuhan University, Xiamen University, and several other universities opened a dedicated temporary hardship subsidy channel for students from families affected by the Taiwan earthquake. Various localities donated funds to relevant parties in Taiwan through multiple channels.\nWe are closely following the disaster and subsequent developments, and we are willing to provide assistance, including post-disaster resettlement, to compatriots in Hualien County affected by the disaster. We also wish the affected compatriots safety and an early rebuilding of their homes!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612355.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","When Mr. Ma Ying-jeou visited the former residence of Sun Yat-sen in Guangdong, he said he earnestly hopes that both sides of the Strait will cooperate, avoid war, strive for peace, revitalize China, and jointly create peace and prosperity, which is also the greatest wish of us Chinese of our generation. What comment do you have?","Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is the right path to safeguarding peace across the Strait, promoting common development across the Strait, and benefiting compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides should work together with one heart to realize the Chinese Dream, share the responsibility of national rejuvenation, and enjoy the glory of national rejuvenation together. The DPP authorities persistently adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and continuously collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at “independence,” which is the root cause of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will join us in upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, jointly promoting peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and jointly devoting ourselves to the great cause of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612359.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Will General Secretary Xi Jinping meet with Mr. Ma Ying-jeou this afternoon?\nSecond question: In the phone call between the heads of state of China and the United States, General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed, “As for the separatist activities of the ‘Taiwan independence’ forces and external connivance and support, we will not stand idly by.” The Chairman of the “American Institute in Taiwan…","Question one: Regarding Mr. Ma Ying-jeou leading Taiwan youth to visit and exchange on the mainland, we will, together with the relevant departments and localities, make proper arrangements.\nQuestion two: The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués in concrete actions, to implement its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, going against the mainstream public opinion on the island that favors peace over war, development over decline, exchange over separation, and cooperation over confrontation. This will only lead Taiwan into peril and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nQuestion three: Regarding the rescued personnel in Kinmen, the relevant situation is still being verified and understood. Taiwan public representatives have expressed the hope of accompanying family members to visit the rescued person surnamed Hu, and we will provide relevant assistance.\nQuestion four: Nearly two months have passed since the “February 14” vicious ship collision incident, and the DPP authorities have gone back on their word, shirked responsibility, and placed obstacles in the way of post-incident consultations, still showing no sincerity in resolving the problem. Only if relevant parties in Taiwan face the problem and meet the reasonable demands of the families for truth, apology, accountability, and compensation can the incident be properly resolved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","During his recent trip to Taiwan, American Institute in Taiwan Chair Rosenberger said that this year marks the 45th anniversary of the “enactment” of the “Taiwan Relations Act.” He said this Act, together with the three China-US joint communiqués and the “Six Assurances,” are the basic principles of US policy toward Taiwan, and stressed that the US must ensure Taiwan has self-defense capabilities. What is your…","The one-China principle is the political foundation and fundamental premise for the establishment of China-US diplomatic relations and the development of diplomatic ties. The so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and “Six Assurances” of the US side seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously violate the basic norms of international relations, and crudely interfere in China's internal affairs. They are entirely wrong, illegal, and null and void. The Chinese government has firmly opposed them from the very beginning. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions, to put its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” into practice, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612353.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","U.S. Deputy Secretary of State Campbell recently said that the “AUKUS” submarine agreement among the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia will promote peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","Such remarks are extremely dangerous. The so-called “trilateral security partnership” among the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia is essentially using military cooperation to incite military confrontation, pursuing one’s own security at the expense of others’ security, which can only make the region less secure. Any attempt to use relevant military cooperation to intervene in the Taiwan question is interference in China’s internal affairs, violates the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, and we firmly oppose it. We urge the relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle and their solemn commitments to China, and to be prudent in their words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Worshipping ancestors during Qingming is a Chinese tradition shared by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly worshipping ancestors in Shaanxi, Henan, Sichuan and other places during this year’s Qingming period.","As the human ancestor of the Chinese nation, Xuanyuan Huangdi is an important symbol of the long-standing and continuous Chinese civilization and an important emblem of the ever-flourishing Chinese nation. He is also the spiritual bond that unites all Chinese descendants. Each year during the Qingming Festival, the public sacrificial ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi held at the Huangdi Mausoleum is a traditional grand event in which all Chinese descendants seek their roots, trace their origins, unite their hearts, and forge their spirit. On April 4 (Qingming Festival), the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese and Their Relatives, and the People's Government of Shaanxi Province solemnly held the “Public Sacrificial Ceremony to Xuanyuan Huangdi for the Qingming Festival of the Year of Jiachen (2024)” at the Huangdi Mausoleum in Huangling County, Yan'an, Shaanxi Province. Over 50 representatives of Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life attended, including former Chairman of the Kuomintang Ma Ying-jeou and former Chairman of the New Party Yu Mu-ming, and they planted trees at Qiaoshan, Huangdi Mausoleum.\nThe Ancestor Worship Ceremony at Huangdi's Hometown for the Year of Jiachen will be held on April 11 (the third day of the third lunar month) at Huangdi's Hometown in Xinzheng, Zhengzhou City, Henan Province. The ceremony is jointly sponsored by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the People's Government of Henan Province, the Henan Provincial Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese and Their Relatives, the All-China Taiwan Federation, and the China Yan-Huang Culture Research Association. The ceremony follows the theme of “Same Roots, Same Ancestors, Same Origin; Peace, Amity, and Harmony” and nine agenda items, and ancestor worship is held both on-site and online. More than one hundred Taiwan compatriots, including grassroots representatives from Taiwan, Taiwanese businesspeople on the island, media reporters, and representatives of Taiwanese youth in Henan, will participate in the on-site worship. The joint worship of the Yellow Emperor by Taiwan compatriots will be held at the Huangdi Leicang Temple (Huangdi Great Temple) in Taoyuan, Taiwan.\nThe “8th Cross-Strait Leizu Cultural Exchange Event” will be held in Yanting County, Sichuan, from April 16 to 21. Leizu was the principal consort of Xuanyuan Huangdi and the great mother of the Chinese nation. She was also the inventor and creator of sericulture and silk culture, and, together with Huangdi and Yandi, she is one of the human ancestors of China. This year's event includes seven items: an opening ceremony, a worship ceremony, the Leizu Sericulture and Silk Culture Exchange Meeting, the Cross-Strait Economic, Trade, and Cooperation Consultation Meeting, and others. Leizu worship activities will also be held simultaneously on the island. More than one hundred Taiwan compatriots, including representatives from all sectors of Taiwan society and young students, will participate in the activities.\nThe joint efforts of compatriots from all walks of life on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to inherit the excellent traditional Chinese culture are of great significance in strengthening the sense of national belonging, dignity, and honor among compatriots on both sides. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to seek their roots, worship their ancestors, and honor their origins.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612354.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","During the just-concluded Qingming holiday, many Taiwan compatriots returned to the mainland with their family members to worship their ancestors and sweep tombs, and the “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes also reached a peak in passenger traffic. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The resumption of the “Mini Three Links” routes has played a positive role in promoting close personnel exchanges across the Strait. According to statistics, during the Qingming holiday from April 1 to 6, the “Mini Three Links” routes operated a total of 118 voyages and carried 16,818 passengers. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and we welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland via the “Mini Three Links” routes to take a look around, to pay respects to ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","After the magnitude 7.3 earthquake in waters off Taiwan’s Hualien, multiple parties on the mainland offered assistance. Taiwan’s MAC said, “there is no need for mainland assistance in disaster relief,” and some people on the island criticized the MAC for still conducting “cognitive warfare” at this critical moment. May I ask the spokesperson for comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are flesh-and-blood brothers who have always shared weal and woe and looked out for one another. In the face of major natural disasters and sudden accidents, compatriots on both sides always lend each other a helping hand and tide over difficulties together. We hope the relevant parties in Taiwan will not engage in political manipulation and will not block compatriots on both sides from helping each other out of family affection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","The Taiwan MAC report says the Macau government has listed Macau’s “Sun Yat-sen Memorial Hall” as a cultural heritage site under evaluation. This will affect the hall’s management, use and disposal, and if it is “forcibly sold” in the future, the Macau government will have the right of first refusal. What is your view on the constant reports that the hall may be sold or “taken over” by the mainland?","The so-called “takeover” claim is entirely baseless speculation and political manipulation. The Macao SAR Government has, in accordance with the law, included the relevant memorial hall in the list of immovable cultural relics. It is lawful, compliant, reasonable and proper.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和“看台海”新媒体记者","We note that mainland new energy vehicles attract great attention from Taiwan residents, and many Taiwan residents have sighed that they are “good to use and fashionable” but regret that they “cannot be bought.” For mainland new energy vehicles, drones and other products, the DPP authorities have consistently used various pretexts to block their entry into the island. What comment do you have?","It is only natural that Mainland new energy vehicles, drones and other products are favored by Taiwan consumers because of their advantages in technological innovation, product diversity, a well-developed industrial chain, high market recognition and global deployment.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have set up many obstacles to Mainland products that are useful and fashionable, carrying out “ban and blockade” measures, which do not win public support. We hope they will genuinely respect the consumer choice rights of Taiwan residents, truly safeguard the vital interests of Taiwan residents, and allow Taiwan residents to enjoy more good products and good services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwan youth on a visit and exchange to the mainland. We have seen that some companies, including Tencent, have invited Taiwan youth to intern. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Is the mainland willing to provide necessary assistance for Taiwan youth internships?","We note that during this visit to Shenzhen, Taiwanese youth not only received internship invitations from Tencent, but also received the “call to action” of the “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” Taiwan Youth Shenzhen Internship Program, and many Taiwanese young people responded actively by scanning codes and taking photos on site to record the moment. This is a good thing. In recent years, we have actively created conditions and built platforms and provided services for Taiwanese youth to intern, work and start businesses in the mainland. Take the “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” Taiwan Youth Shenzhen Internship Program as an example: this program has been running for 17 years, and more than 2,000 Taiwanese youth have taken part. This year's internship program has already launched, with registration closing on June 9. So far, more than 1,200 internship positions and more than 800 employment positions have been collected, including those at well-known enterprises such as Tencent, BYD, Skyworth, the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, China Merchants Bank and Ping An Securities.\nMany Taiwanese youth have broadened their horizons, accumulated experience and strengthened their abilities through taking part in internship programs, and have gained more and broader understanding of the mainland. We welcome Taiwanese youth with dreams to take part in internship programs in various parts of the mainland. Please pay attention to the internship guidance information released in various localities and register in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Bolivian government recently expressed concern to mainland China over the earthquake in Hualien, Taiwan. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities said that Bolivia had been “beguiled” by the Chinese government into “spreading untrue remarks internationally that belittle Taiwan’s sovereignty,” and falsely accused the mainland of conducting “cognitive warfare.” Earlier, Geng Shuang, Deputy Permanent Representative…","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China. The One-China Principle is a widely shared consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations, and it is also the political foundation on which 183 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China. Natural disasters are merciless, and the international community's expression of concern over the Hualien earthquake in Taiwan reflects humanitarianism. At such a difficult moment, the DPP authorities still did not forget to use the opportunity to promote the “Taiwan independence” concept. This once again exposes them as habitual practitioners of so-called “cognitive warfare.” They are unpopular, and they will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","The commander of Taiwan’s navy recently sneaked into the United States to take part in related activities hosted by the US Navy. Some foreign media say this move is part of the US “Joint Island Defense Concept,” and that “the US will coordinate with Japan, the Philippines, Taiwan and others to confront the PLA along the ‘First Island Chain’.” What comment do you have?","The United States keeps fabricating various concepts and exploiting various pretexts to strengthen its military collusion with Taiwan, China, which is extremely irresponsible. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange and military contact between the United States and Taiwan, China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to put into practice its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities colluding with external forces to “seek independence through force” will certainly fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240410_12612351.htm"],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The Taiwan-based Chinese Humanistic Buddhism Federation recently donated 30 precious cultural relics lost overseas to the National Cultural Heritage Administration. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Every Chinese cultural relic bears the long and far-reaching history of China. Bringing home cultural relics that have been lost overseas is a shared aspiration of all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots. In 2014, Venerable Hsing Yun of Taiwan’s Fo Guang Shan Monastery donated to the State Administration of Cultural Heritage, free of charge, the head of a Northern Qi Shakyamuni Buddha statue, a first-class national cultural relic that had been donated by believers. In March 2016, a ceremony was held at the National Museum of China, drawing wide attention from all walks of life on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. In recent years, Taiwan residents have continuously donated Buddhist cultural relics lost overseas to Taiwan temples such as Fo Guang Shan, hoping they will be returned to the Mainland. This time, the Taiwan Chinese Buddhist Federation carefully selected 30 polychrome sculptures from the Song, Jin, and Ming-Qing periods from among the relics donated by its members, and sent them back to the Mainland in batches. On March 25, a cultural relic donation ceremony was held at the National Museum of China, where the relics were solemnly donated to the State Administration of Cultural Heritage. These cultural relics embody the profound accumulation of China’s long history and are vivid testimony to the brilliant and diverse Chinese culture. They once again demonstrate the deep love and high reverence for Chinese culture held by the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Various sectors in Taiwan are paying close attention to whether General Secretary Xi Jinping will meet with Ma Ying-jeou. When asked whether this would help peace across the Taiwan Strait, Chiu Tai-san, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that culture and exchanges can allow both sides to further understand each other. He also suggested that Ma should tell the mainland side: “The so-called soft and…","We uphold the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” and we always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, doing good deeds, doing real things, and solving difficulties for them. At the same time, we firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” and will not leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. What Taiwan compatriots truly hate is the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation, which endangers peace across the Taiwan Strait and harms Taiwan’s development prospects and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Han Kuo-yu, Speaker of Taiwan's Legislative Yuan, posted on Facebook during the Qingming Festival to express his reverence for ancestors. Because the post mentioned that “Qingming tomb-sweeping and ancestor worship has a history of thousands of years in our country” and used the phrase “Taiwan region,” he was attacked by the Green camp for “echoing the mainland.” What comments do you have on this?","Chinese people on both sides of the Strait respect their ancestors and carry on the excellent traditional Chinese culture from generation to generation. “Taiwan independence” elements have made remarks about this, which fully expose their forgetting of their ancestry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The second phase of the so-called “U.S.-Taiwan 21st Century Trade Initiative” negotiations on agriculture, labor, environment, and other issues continues. Taiwan says this could expand opportunities for Taiwan's agricultural products to be sold in the U.S. What is the spokesperson's comment?","We firmly oppose any agreements with substantive sovereignty implications or official nature that countries having diplomatic relations with China, including the United States, sign with the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities, in pursuit of their own political gain, are willing to sacrifice the interests of island enterprises and the public, and this does not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","广东广播电视台记者","The DPP authorities, disregarding strong opposition from all sectors of society on the island, insist on raising electricity prices starting in April, with an average increase of 11%. Industrial and commercial circles on the island have complained bitterly, saying rising operating costs can only be passed on to consumers, will inevitably cause overall price fluctuations, and that the misery index will keep…","We have noted the relevant situation. From frequent power outages to repeated electricity price increases, Taiwan compatriots are caught in the middle, suffering greatly, and they all understand clearly where the crux of the problem lies. What to do in the future is worth deep reflection by Taiwan compatriots. Industries and enterprises that are major electricity users should plan early, find the right path, and respond appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The Taiwan military expects to begin receiving the first batch of 38 M1A2T tanks at the end of this year. It is reported that these newly procured tanks have all been fitted with the so-called “urban warfare” upgrade kits developed by the US military. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military collusion between the United States and the Taiwan region. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “seek independence by force” is overreaching and will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","Czech media reported that during Hsiao Bi-khim’s visit, a “suspicious vehicle” that was tailing her narrowly caused a traffic accident, and the Czech police said the driver of the vehicle was a mainland military diplomat. What is your comment?","We have consistently opposed any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. The DPP authorities collude with external forces and devise all kinds of so-called “diplomatic” breakthroughs. This cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and it does not contribute to peace and stability in the Taiwan region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","After the Hualien earthquake in Taiwan, the Taiwan Affairs Office immediately said it could provide assistance, but the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refused. However, the concern and care of mainland people for Taiwan compatriots were not blocked as a result. Some mainland netizens donated or provided help to affected Taiwan compatriots through online platforms, and received a large number of likes…","I believe the goodwill shown by mainland netizens has certainly been felt by Taiwan compatriots. This also fully proves that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are blood-related brothers, who have always shared hardships and supported each other. We hope relevant parties in Taiwan will stop engaging in political manipulation and stop obstructing the mutual family-affection-based assistance of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Taiwan’s competent transportation authority recently said that, without mainland tourists, the target for overseas travelers visiting Taiwan this year will be lowered from 12 million visits to 10 million visits. Public opinion on the island calls on the DPP authorities to seek a solution and not let Taiwan’s tourism industry become a political sacrifice. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation across all sectors between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. In contrast, the DPP authorities have consistently obstructed exchanges across all sectors between the two sides. They claim that they have been releasing goodwill continuously since last year, but to this day they still have not formally opened the door to mainland residents visiting Taiwan for exchanges, nor lifted the ban on Taiwan residents joining group tours to the mainland. Where is this so-called “goodwill”? We have not seen it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-10","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Some Taiwan media reported that the US Trade Representative recently released the “2024 Foreign Trade Barriers Assessment Report,” urging the DPP authorities to fully open the island’s campus market to US beef and its products, and calling for the abolition of the ban on using related foods in campus meals. What is your comment on this?","Facts once again show that the United States always puts its own interests first and does not care at all about the well-being and interests of the Taiwan people. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opinion, have successively relaxed import restrictions on products with problematic hazards, such as “Lai pork,” “US beef” and “nuclear food,” repeatedly trading the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots for the support of external forces for its “independence” pursuits, thereby seeking partisan private gain. This will certainly be firmly opposed by Taiwan compatriots.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240410_12612339.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-04-11","Mao Ning","NBC","Japan’s Prime Minister Kishida is on a state visit to the US where the main focus is the expansion of security ties to counter China, including missile systems and the possibility of Japan joining AUKUS. President Biden has also invited the Philippines’ President Marcos to join their talks. What is China’s view of this strategic alliance in the Indo-Pacific? And what is China considering as potential repercussions?","Despite China’s serious concerns, the US and Japan attacked and smeared China on the Taiwan question and maritime issues, grossly interfered in China’s domestic affairs and violated the basic norms in international relations. China deplores and opposes it, and has made serious démarches to relevant parties.\nUS-Japan relations should not target other countries, harm their interests or undermine regional peace and stability. China firmly opposes the Cold War mentality and small group politics. China firmly rejects anything that creates and drives up tensions and may undermine other countries’ strategic security and interests.\nI want to stress that there is but one China. This is a historical fact and international consensus. The Taiwan question is purely China’s domestic affair and brooks no external interference. Both the US and Japanese governments have made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question. In particular, Japan bears serious historical responsibilities for its aggression against Taiwan and colonial rule over the island, and should all the more honor its words and act prudently. We urge the US to translate President Biden’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions.\nChina’s activities in the East China Sea and South China Sea are in full compliance with international law and there’s nothing wrong about them. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China’s inherent territory. We will take firm measures against illegal moves that violate China’s sovereignty. China has indisputable sovereignty over Nanhai Zhudao and its adjacent waters. China stands ready to continue properly handling maritime issues with parties concerned through dialogue and consultation and jointly upholding peace and stability in the South China Sea. In the meantime, no one should violate China’s territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and China remains steadfast in safeguarding our lawful rights.\nThe US and Japan have misrepresented the facts, violated China’s territorial sovereignty and breached international law and basic norms in international relations. They pose the real threat to regional peace and stability.\nI want to emphasize that China is always a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of the international order. We will never allow any country to interfere in China’s domestic affairs, harm its interests, and smear its image. China will defend its sovereignty, security and development interests, and stay committed to the peace, stability and lasting prosperity of the Asia-Pacific region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347734.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240411_11280275.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-11","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Can I ask you to clarify a little bit? You made serious démarches to relevant parties? Is that specifically the US and Japan? What was the reason for that?","We made serious démarches to relevant parties because the US-Japan Joint Leaders’ Statement attacked and smeared China on Taiwan-related, maritime and other issues and blatantly interfered in China’s internal affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347734.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240411_11280275.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-12","Mao Ning","CCTV","The leaders of the US, Japan and the Philippines held their first trilateral summit in Washington on April 11, and issued a Joint Vision Statement after the summit. We noted that despite the US’s previous claim that this summit and the US-Japan-Philippines cooperation “is not aimed at” China, the Statement discussed the South China Sea issue at length, blamed China on the East China Sea issue and contained…","We noted this. I would like to make the following points:\nFirst, China strongly opposes the practice of bloc politics by relevant countries. We firmly oppose any acts that stoke and drive up tensions and harm other countries’ strategic security and interests. We are seriously against forming exclusive groupings in this region. Japan and the Philippines have every right to develop normal relations with other countries, but they should not introduce bloc confrontation into this region, still less engage in trilateral cooperation at the expense of other countries’ interests. To know whether the trilateral summit and cooperation is truly not aimed at China, the answer is right there in the trilateral statement. What else could it be if it’s not a smear and attack against China?\nSecond, the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that no one can interfere. The biggest threat to cross-Strait peace now is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and external connivance and support for them. If relevant countries truly care about cross-Strait peace and stability and want the world to be safe and prosperous, they should uphold the one-China principle, unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and support China’s reunification. This is the right way to ensure peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. No one should underestimate the will and capability of the Chinese people to safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThird, China has indisputable sovereignty over Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands and Nanhai Zhudao. Our activities in the East China Sea and South China Sea are lawful, justified and beyond reproach. China does not accept relevant countries’ groundless accusation and deliberate smears against us on the East China Sea and South China Sea. China does not accept the illegal arbitral award on the South China Sea or any unilateral moves based on the award. The situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable. Certain countries keep seeking backing from non-regional countries as they infringe on China’s sovereignty and rights and make provocations at sea. What they have done has escalated the tensions. Certain country outside the region keeps fueling the flame and stoking confrontation. This is flagrant. Let me stress once again that China will firmly guard its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests and we remain committed to properly settling bilateral maritime issues through dialogue and consultation with countries directly concerned. And we resolutely oppose non-regional countries meddling and sowing discords to escalate the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347735.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240412_11280916.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-04-12","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that the Taiwan Navy commander recently made a sneaking visit to the US military's Indo-Pacific Command headquarters in Hawaii and attended related US military activities. Some commentary holds that this visit is part of the US implementation of the “Joint Island Defense Concept,” aimed at coordinating with the Taiwan authorities to counter Chinese military power within the “First Island Chain.” What…","The Chinese side firmly opposes any form of official exchange and military contact between the US and China's Taiwan region. This position is clear and explicit. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and resolving the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, which brooks no external interference.\nThe so-called 'First Island Chain' is a product of Cold War geopolitics, and any attempt to contain China is nothing but wishful thinking. The Chinese side urges the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to genuinely implement its commitment not to support 'Taiwan independence,' and to immediately stop US-Taiwan military collusion and official exchanges. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that those who willingly act as 'chess pieces' will inevitably be discarded as pawns. If they attempt to 'seek independence through force,' there is only a dead end. For any form of 'Taiwan independence' separatist act, the People's Liberation Army will strike back head-on.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16300540.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-04-16","Lin Jian","Reuters","The top US diplomat for East Asia Mr. Kritenbrink met with Chinese officials from the Foreign Ministry as well as the Taiwan Affairs Office this week. The US State Department said that they discussed Middle East developments, the South China Sea and Taiwan issues, but did not provide a lot of details. Could we understand what were the key discussions at the meetings, especially on the Middle East, given the phone…","On April 15, Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Ma Zhaoxu met with US Ambassador to China Nicholas Burns, Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs Daniel Kritenbrink and National Security Council Senior Director for China and Taiwan Affairs Sarah Beran. We have released a readout which you may refer to.\nAt the meeting, the two sides, in line with the common understandings reached by the two presidents at the San Francisco meeting and the recent phone call, had candid, in-depth and constructive communication on promoting China-US dialogue and cooperation in various fields and properly managing differences, and exchanged views on the Middle East, Ukraine, the Korean Peninsula nuclear issue and other international and regional hotspots. The two sides agreed to continue implementing the San Francisco vision, maintain exchanges at various levels and further stabilize and grow China-US relations.\nYou also mentioned Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s phone calls with foreign ministers of Iran and Saudi Arabia . Let me briefly go over China’s principled positions which were made clear by Foreign Minister Wang Yi. He said that China firmly opposes the attack on Iran’s embassy in Syria and that the attack is a serious violation of international law. In the meantime, we noted that Iran said its counterattack is not targeted at any neighboring country and Iran is willing to continue taking a good-neighborly and friendly policy.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stressed that the ongoing escalation in the Middle East is the latest spillover of the Gaza conflict. There should be no more delays in implementing the UN Security Council Resolution 2728, realizing an unconditional and durable ceasefire, truly protecting civilians and ensuring humanitarian aid. Palestinians have long been denied their legitimate national rights. This has been the most persisting injustice in modern-day world, the root cause of the Palestinian-Israeli question and the crux of the Middle East issue. The right way forward is to implement the two-State solution as soon as possible, establish an independent State of Palestine, and restore the legitimate national rights of Palestine so that the two states of Palestine and Israel will live side by side in peace. The international community needs to show more initiative, support full UN membership for Palestine, and call for a more broad-based, more authoritative, and more effective international peace conference to work out a timetable and roadmap for the two-State solution. China also stands ready to step up communication and coordination with all parties to that end.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347737.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240416_11282539.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-17","Lin Jian","Hubei Media Group","President of Suriname Chandrikapersad Santokhi just concluded his state visit to China. Can I have your comment on the visit?","From April 11 to 17, President Chandrikapersad Santokhi paid a state visit to China at China’s invitation. This is the first visit to China by a head of state of Latin America and the Caribbean countries this year. The visit coincides with the fifth anniversary of the strategic cooperative partnership and the fifth anniversary of the signing of Belt and Road cooperation plan between the two countries. During the visit, President Xi Jinping held talks with President Chandrikapersad Santokhi, and Premier Li Qiang and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference Wang Huning met with him respectively. Leaders of the two countries had in-depth exchanges of views and reached broad common understandings on bilateral relations and issues of mutual interest.\nThe talks between President Xi Jinping and President Chandrikapersad Santokhi were highly productive. The two presidents agreed to consolidate political mutual trust, enhance trade and economic cooperation, expand cultural and people-to-people exchanges, and have closer coordination on international affairs. The two sides reiterated their mutual understanding and support on issues that bear on each other’s core interests and major concerns. The Suriname side reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle, opposition to all forms of “Taiwan independence” and support for Chinese government’s effort to realize national reunification. President Xi Jinping noted that China is ready to work with Suriname to deepen Belt and Road cooperation and form closer synergy on development strategies; China welcomes Suriname’s engagement in multilateral cooperation under the frameworks of the Global Development Initiative (GDI), the Global Security Initiative (GSI) and the Global Civilization Initiative (GCI); and China stands ready to work with Suriname and the wider developing world to jointly build a community with a shared future for mankind. President Chandrikapersad Santokhi spoke highly of President Xi Jinping’s extraordinary global leadership, appreciated China’s pursuit of national rejuvenation on all fronts through Chinese modernization, and commended the Belt and Road Initiative, and the GDI, GSI and GCI proposed by President Xi Jinping.\nWitnessed by the two presidents, the two sides signed 11 cooperation documents, covering areas of economy, trade, investment, education, media, green development and digital economy. The two sides issued a joint press communiqué , agreeing to step up cooperation in such areas as blue economy, energy minerals, infrastructure, energy, agriculture, finance, science and technology, culture, sports and poverty alleviation, promote the overall cooperation between China and Latin America and the Caribbean countries, work together for the success of the Fourth China-Caribbean Economic and Trade Cooperation Forum, and continue their advocacy for addressing climate change and promoting sustainable development of the international community.\nPresident Chandrikapersad Santokhi’s visit is a great success. China stands ready to take this visit as an opportunity to work with Suriname to fully deliver on the important common understandings between the two presidents, promote the steady and sustained development of China-Suriname strategic cooperative partnership and write a new chapter of China-Suriname friendship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347738.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240417_11283184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-18","Lin Jian","AFP","As an election is held in Solomon Islands this week, a major candidate named Peter Kenilorea said today that if he becomes the next Prime Minister, he will scrap the security agreement with China. He also said before that he would seek to reestablish relations with Taiwan. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","I would like to reiterate that China upholds the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, and supports the people of Solomon Islands in choosing a development path that suits their national conditions. Commitment to the one-China principle is the right thing to do and is where the global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. This is the political foundation of the relations between China and Solomon Islands. We have a comprehensive strategic partnership featuring mutual respect and common development for a new era. A healthy and stable China-Solomon Islands relationship is in the interest of both countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347740.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240418_11284201.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-04-19","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲当日就此答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 19 (electronic dispatch): On the 19th, the Civil Aviation Administration of China announced that the W122 and W123 connecting routes of the M503 airway will be operated from west to east. Chen Fenglian (note: spokesperson Zhu Fenglian), spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the same day, saying that the operation of the…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that route M503 is located within the Shanghai Flight Information Region, and that establishing and operating this route is a routine task of mainland civil aviation airspace management. Since the flight offset on M503 was cancelled, overall operations have been safe and stable, effectively improving cross-Strait flight operations and further facilitating personnel exchanges between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240419_12614441.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-04-22","Wang Wenbin","TASS","Foreign ministers of the G7 issued a communiqué after their meeting in Italy last Friday, saying they are “concerned about the situation in the East and South China Seas” and reiterate their “opposition to any unilateral attempts to change the status quo.” The communiqué also mentioned issues related to Xizang, Hong Kong and Taiwan. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","We strongly deplore and firmly reject the manipulation of China-related issues at the G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting. The comments from the meeting are a deliberate mischaracterization of the facts and truth, and a blatant interference in China’s internal affairs.\nChina’s position on relevant issues is consistent and clear. The most effective way to ensure cross-Strait peace and stability is to uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence.” With the concerted efforts of China and ASEAN countries, the South China Sea has been generally peaceful and stable and there is no issue with freedom of navigation. China always puts the people at the center of its endeavors and strives to deliver the benefit of development to all Chinese people. Hong Kong has restored order and is set to thrive, and Xinjiang and Xizang enjoy social harmony, prosperity and stability where people of all ethnic groups live a happy life. A survey by a renowned international institution shows that the Chinese government’s satisfaction rate among the Chinese people has been above 90 percent for years running.\nAs the largest developing country, China is committed to the welfare of the world while working hard to achieve its own development. According to the World Bank, China’s contribution to global economic growth has long been higher than that of the G7 countries combined. China advocates an equal and orderly multipolar world and universally beneficial and inclusive economic globalization, upholds the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, and believes in open cooperation and mutual benefit. The G7, however, has held fast to the Cold-War mentality, cobbled together small exclusive groupings, and escalated regional tensions and conflicts. It has also engaged in trade protectionism and disrupted world economic order under the pretext of de-risking and less reliance. We urge the G7 to change the habit of deflecting blame, stop interfering in other countries’ internal affairs and holding back other countries’ development at once, and work with the rest of the world to uphold peace, enhance cooperation and advance development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347742.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240422_11286222.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-24","Wang Wenbin","CNN","Concerning the legislation that was passed by the United States’ lawmakers dealing with both Taiwan and TikTok, a two-part question. First, what will China’s message be on this as Secretary of State Antony Blinken travels the country? Secondly, what is the view of the Chinese government, should ByteDance challenge this legislation or would it be better to leave the American market altogether?","On TikTok, we have clearly stated China’s principled position and I have nothing more to add today.\nOn Secretary Blinken’s visit, we spoke on it a few times in the past two days. The head of the MFA Department of North American and Oceanian Affairs also gave a background briefing. You may refer to what has been said.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347744.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240424_11288545.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-24","Wang Wenbin","New York Times","Will the timing of the Senate bill’s passage affect the discussions with Secretary Blinken in the coming days and does China have a comment on the USD 8 billion in funding to Taiwan and the Indo-Pacific that were part of the bill?","We’ve shared our views in detail regarding Secretary Blinken’s visit to China, which you may refer to.\nI would like to stress that getting closer militarily between the United States and the Taiwan region will not make the latter safer or save “Taiwan independence” from failure. It will only heighten tensions and the risk of conflict and confrontation in the Taiwan Strait, and will eventually backfire. The US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leader’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan, stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait and stop endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China will closely follow the developments of the bill and take resolute measures to safeguard its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347744.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240424_11288545.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping met Ma Yingjiu and his delegation in Beijing on the 10th and delivered an important speech on cross-Strait relations. Please interpret it.","On April 10, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China Central Committee Xi Jinping met with Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation in Beijing and delivered an important speech on developing cross-Strait relations and jointly creating a better future. Against the backdrop of new situations and new changes in cross-Strait relations, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a speech on Taiwan from the perspective of the overall interests and long-term development of the Chinese nation. The speech has a lofty vision, a broad scope, and rich connotations. It has pointed out the direction for the development of cross-Strait relations and is the fundamental guideline and action plan for work on Taiwan in the new era.\nFrom the historical height of the development of the Chinese nation, General Secretary Xi Jinping revealed the historical fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation, declared the firm will and determination to advance opposition to \"Taiwan independence\" and promote reunification, demonstrated sincere concern for enhancing the well-being and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, emphasized the important significance of forging a sense of community of the Chinese nation, expressed care and concern and earnest expectations for young people on both sides of the Strait, and called on compatriots on both sides to work together with one heart to achieve national rejuvenation.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping spoke with compatriots in Taiwan about history, discussed the present, and talked about the future. His words are both warm and philosophical, with strong appeal, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait have responded enthusiastically, which is of great significance and far-reaching influence on the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615818.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Taiwanese youths who accompanied Mr. Ma Ying-jeou on his visit to the mainland said that through the visit and exchanges they gained a completely new understanding of Chinese culture and also felt its cultural impact: “Out of a full score of 100, I’d give it 1,000.” What is your comment on this? What cross-Strait youth exchange activities are planned next?","Everyone has noticed that the Taiwanese youth who visited have gained a great deal from their trip to the mainland. We have consistently advocated and actively promoted cross-Strait youth exchanges, and we are pleased to see more Taiwanese youth come to the mainland to exchange ideas and gain insights. Over the coming months, various localities will hold a range of exchange activities for Taiwanese youth, such as the Straits Forum Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the Cross-Strait Youth Donghu Forum, the Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour, the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, and the Straits Youth Festival.\nWe sincerely invite Taiwanese youth, especially those who have never been to the mainland, to come and see for themselves, to personally experience the mainland's development and progress and Chinese culture, and to deepen mutual understanding among young people on both sides of the Strait. We will also continue to create more conditions for and provide more support to the growth, development and success of cross-Strait youth. We hope that young people on both sides will learn from and inspire one another, move forward together in step, pass on the baton of history well, and contribute their youthful energy to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and realizing national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615817.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The recent visit and exchanges in the mainland by Ma Ying-jeou's delegation sparked heated discussion on the island, and calls for peace and exchange across the Strait have grown louder. Ma called on Lai Ching-te to accept the olive branch extended by the mainland and to accept the “1992 Consensus.” What comments do you have on this?","Peace, not war; development, not decline; exchange, not separation; cooperation, not confrontation: this is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwan youth to visit and exchange on the mainland. This conforms to the mainstream public opinion on the island and to the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and has won wide praise. The DPP authorities have long insisted on a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, interfered with and sabotaged cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, colluded with external forces in provocations aimed at “independence,” and thereby plunged the Taiwan Strait into tension and turmoil, arousing strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition among compatriots on both sides. Only by following the will of the people and the general trend, returning to the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, and acknowledging the basic fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation, can favorable conditions be created for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and reliable guarantees be provided for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and for the welfare of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615816.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The Ministry of Commerce recently announced that starting April 20, anti-dumping duties will be imposed on imported polycarbonate originating in the Taiwan region. Please introduce the specific situation.","The Ministry of Commerce has conducted an anti-dumping investigation into imported polycarbonate originating in the Taiwan region. It is understood that during the investigation, the competent authorities strictly conducted the investigation in accordance with relevant laws, regulations, and WTO rules, widely heard the opinions of all interested parties, fully protected the rights of all parties, and objectively, fairly, and impartially reached the final investigation conclusion. It has decided to impose anti-dumping duties ranging from 9% to 22.4%. We are willing to actively assist the enterprises involved in expanding into the mainland market in a law-abiding and compliant manner, and in sharing the development opportunities of the mainland’s new quality productive forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","On the 10th, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation in Beijing and said, “We sincerely invite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to visit, and we are also glad to see mainland residents visit our treasured island of Taiwan more.” Does this mean the mainland side will consider opening up tourism to Taiwan for mainland residents?","General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech reflects the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to grow ever closer and to deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Although there are still some artificial obstacles and barriers to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation on the island, we believe that as long as compatriots on both sides work together and remove these obstacles, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation will usher in a bright future. We will take active measures to promote exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, including tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Since April, cross-Strait exchange activities have continued to be lively. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant situation of recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Recently, relevant departments and localities have held a series of cross-Strait exchange activities with rich content and diverse forms. I would like to briefly introduce them to you.\nIn terms of cultural exchanges, on April 6, the “13th Haipai Culture and Arts Festival,” co-hosted by the China Cultural Exchange Association, the Shanghai Municipal Bureau of Culture and Tourism, and the Taiwan Rensian Cultural Education Foundation, was held at Fo Guang Shan in Kaohsiung, Taiwan. The Shanghai Puppet Theatre's large-scale mythological puppet play “Hua Shan Child Prodigy” visited the island again after five years, making its debut in Kaohsiung. It presented to the Taiwan public the cultural appeal of puppet theater, a national intangible cultural heritage, and pili glove puppetry, which share a common lineage, and demonstrated the inheritance and innovation of China's outstanding traditional culture.\nIn terms of folk belief exchanges, the “Mazu Returns Home to Her Mother's Temple” activity at the Mazu Ancestral Temple in Meizhou Island, Putian, was officially launched on April 9. The activity will continue throughout the year. More than 200 Mazu temples and about 4,000 Mazu devotees from the island have already gone to Meizhou to pay homage to the ancestor and offer incense. On the day of the launch ceremony, Mazu temples and cultural institutions from Kaohsiung, Changhua, New Taipei, Tainan, Penghu, Yunlin, Yilan, Taoyuan, Keelung, Hualien, Miaoli, and other counties and cities in Taiwan went to pay homage to the ancestor and offer incense. Nearly 50 temples from both sides of the Strait, with a total of more than 3,000 people, took part.\nIn terms of cross-Strait ethnic minority exchanges, the “2024 Chinese Family Celebrates Guangxi's ‘March Third Festival’ with Guangxi-Taiwan Ethnic Groups” activity was held in Guangxi from April 9 to 15. This is the first large-scale cross-Strait ethnic minority exchange event this year, and the ninth time that ethnic minority compatriots from both sides of the Strait have gathered in Guangxi. More than 200 Taiwan indigenous compatriots from 8 ethnic groups in 11 counties and cities, including Taipei, Hualien, and Taitung, carried out a series of friendship and visiting exchange activities with ethnic compatriots in Guangxi under the theme “Gathering for March Third in Full Bloom, Harmony in Baguixi,” jointly promoting the excellent traditional culture of the Chinese nation. On April 10, the opening ceremony of the “Chinese Family · 2024 Cross-Strait Ethnic Groups Celebrate the ‘March Third Festival’” and the 11th Fujian Province “March Third” She Culture Festival under the theme “Fu Zi Tong Xin, Love China” was held. Ethnic compatriots from both sides of the Strait gathered in Fu'an and chatted warmly about their family bonds.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The first phase of the Taiwan military’s “Han Kuang 40” exercise began on the 19th, and the “live-troop drills” will be held in July. We note that in this year’s exercise, the Taiwan military for the first time incorporated a so-called scenario for responding to the “threat of mainland roll-on/roll-off ships.” May I ask what the spokesperson’s comment is?","The DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to constantly plot “independence” and provoke, and their incitement of cross-strait opposition and confrontation, are the root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. We have the determination and the capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.\nYesterday was the 75th anniversary of the founding of the People's Liberation Army Navy. Belatedly, we extend birthday greetings to the People's Navy, and wish it to strive for a strong navy from the sea, to safeguard the country's sovereignty and territory well, and to protect the well-being and interests of people on both sides of the Strait well.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Reportedly, multiple island-based representatives have called for the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” to not be used as a tool to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges. Amending the “Anti-Infiltration Act” could create more room for free cross-Strait exchanges. In addition, public opinion on the island has called for abolishing this vicious law rather than amending it. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Facts have long proven that the so-called “anti-infiltration law” is merely a political tool used by the DPP authorities to suppress dissenters, create a “green terror,” and seek partisan private interests. It is an out-and-out “evil law,” and from the very beginning it has been strongly questioned and criticized by all sectors of the island. Acting against popular will and going against the trend of the times, and deliberately creating cross-Strait opposition and provoking confrontation, will inevitably backfire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, several private education institutions in Taiwan held a joint press conference to condemn the DPP authorities' education reform policies and “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines for causing many problems in the island's education sector. In particular, they cited the reduction of class hours and content for history and Chinese language, which constantly distorts the true meaning of the language…","The DPP authorities, for the purpose of promoting 'Taiwan independence' and 'de-Sinicization,' have disregarded strong opposition from all sectors on the island and insisted on implementing so-called education reform policies and 'Taiwan independence' curriculum guidelines. They have deliberately distorted Chinese history and attempted to sever cultural connections across the Strait. This not only causes confusion in historical memory and distortion of national identity among Taiwan's younger generation, but also leaves compatriots in Taiwan spiritually and culturally like water without a source and trees without roots. It further damages cross-Strait relations, intensifies cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, and causes boundless harm. The DPP authorities' reckless conduct of abandoning their roots and forgetting their ancestors will certainly meet with strong opposition and firm boycotts from compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation. Chinese culture is the spiritual lifeline of the Chinese nation and the common spiritual home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The right of Taiwan compatriots to receive Chinese cultural education and to understand national history, as Chinese descendants, is a right that should be guaranteed. We hope all Taiwan compatriots will be guardians, inheritors, and promoters of Chinese culture, strengthening their sense of belonging, identity, and honor as members of the Chinese nation. We also hope Taiwan compatriots will come to the mainland to find the roots of their culture and bloodline, and to make up for the lessons they did not receive in Taiwan.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615813.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The 77th World Health Assembly will be held in Geneva, Switzerland, on May 27. The DPP authorities plan to have the newly appointed “Minister of Health and Welfare” lead a delegation to hold talks with relevant countries at that time. What is your comment on this?","Regarding Chinese Taiwan’s participation in World Health Organization activities, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is also the fundamental principle affirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1. The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, causing the political foundation for Taiwan’s participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. What they really care about is not the health of Taiwan’s people but making political capital out of attending or crashing meetings to deceive the island’s public, and the result can only be self-humiliation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The National Immigration Administration’s Exit-Entry Administration Bureau supports the implementation of ten entry-exit policy measures for the construction of the Fujian Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, which have now been in effect for over 100 days. Taiwan compatriots who hold Taiwan compatriot permits in Fujian enjoy many conveniences in transportation, finance, telecommunications, and…","The National Immigration Administration is accelerating the application of Taiwan compatriot permits in a more convenient way, and is working to build Fujian into a “Taiwan Compatriot Permit Convenience Application Demonstration Zone.” Since the implementation of the ten entry-exit policy measures to support Fujian in building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, phased results have been achieved, with positive outcomes in promoting personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan and in facilitating the residence and daily life of Taiwan compatriots in Fujian.\nFirst, the number of cross-Strait trips has increased substantially. Since the beginning of this year, 90,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots have applied for five-year Taiwan compatriot permits in Fujian, a year-on-year increase of 56.4%. 11,000 person-times have applied for one-time Taiwan compatriot permits, a year-on-year increase of 2 times. 230,000 Taiwan compatriots have entered through Fujian ports, a year-on-year increase of 2.6 times. 54,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots visiting Fujian have enjoyed convenient customs clearance services, and more than 4,400 vessels traveling between Fujian and Taiwan have enjoyed round-the-clock, 7×24-hour customs clearance services.\nSecond, life and development for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian have become more convenient. At present, Taiwan compatriots in Fujian who hold Taiwan compatriot permits can enjoy 242 service conveniences in 16 fields, including transportation, finance, and telecommunications. Since the beginning of this year, the identity authentication service platform for entry-exit documents of the National Immigration Administration has provided free real-time identity verification services to 664,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots in Fujian, facilitating their handling of government affairs, public services, and internet applications in Fujian.\nThird, entry-exit services have become higher quality and more efficient. All entry-exit service windows of the Fujian Provincial Public Security Department have set up “Taiwan Compatriot and Taiwan Enterprise Dedicated Windows,” which handle entry-exit documents, settlement and household registration, policy consultation, and other business for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. Service points for Taiwan compatriots have also been set up at 10 Taiwan businessperson and Taiwan enterprise associations. The 12367 service platform of the National Immigration Administration serves Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises around the clock and provides telephone services in Hokkien. Since the beginning of this year, it has provided 36,000 person-times of telephone consultation services on Taiwan-related matters, promptly responding to and resolving the needs and expectations of Taiwan compatriots in the entry-exit field.\nWe will continue to work with relevant departments to further expand the application areas and service scope of Taiwan compatriot permits, so that Taiwan compatriots can enjoy better services and more convenience.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615814.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Some media outlets on the island report that Lai Ching-te recently invited Cheng Wen-tsan to serve as chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation. Cheng has shown a relatively moderate attitude toward cross-Strait relations, and Lai may be trying to let the mainland side feel goodwill through this personnel arrangement. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the development of cross-strait relations and the “pillar that pins down the sea” for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is the precondition for the authorized negotiation and liaison mechanism between the ARATS and the SEF. Regardless of who serves as head of the SEF, whether the consultation mechanism between the two associations can be restored depends crucially on whether the Taiwan authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and acknowledge the basic fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","First question: Not long ago, during Mr. Ma Ying-jeou’s visit to Beijing, “the Chinese nation” became a key phrase. Yet the Mainland Affairs Council said that “the descendants of Yan and Huang are merely an ancient Chinese legend” and that “the discourse on the Chinese nation is a trap.” Some analysts believe this shows that the DPP authorities do not accept the goodwill of the mainland. What is the…","On the first question, people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same blood, the same culture and the same history. They all belong to the Chinese nation and are descendants of Yan and Huang; they are all Chinese. This iron-clad fact cannot be denied or profaned. The DPP authorities and their politicians, driven by their innate inclination toward “independence” and their narrow political self-interest, have forgotten their ancestors and betrayed their nation. As unworthy descendants, they are despised, and if they do not change course, they will surely be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait should join hands to firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, firmly work together to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, firmly forge a sense of community for the Chinese nation, and firmly realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nOn the second question, the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The relevant bill passed by the US Congress that includes Taiwan-related content seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. It sends a wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and we firmly oppose it. We urge the US side to honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, and to stop arming Taiwan in any form.\nPeace rather than war, development rather than decline, exchange rather than separation, and cooperation rather than confrontation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opinion and willing to serve as pawns for external forces seeking to “use Taiwan to contain China,” are leading Taiwan toward danger. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that their attempts to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on outside powers” are doomed to fail.\nWe hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will fully recognize the danger of the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to “seek independence through force,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and join us in promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and in building a peaceful home where compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live in security. Only this can bring real and tangible benefits and well-being to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615812.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","“New quality productive forces” has been a high-frequency term regarding China's economy since March. Since the two sessions of the National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, the mainland has made specific arrangements for optimizing and upgrading industrial and supply chains, cultivating emerging industries, and advancing the innovative development of the digital…","New quality productive forces are advanced productive forces in which innovation plays the leading role, characterized by high technology, high efficiency, and high quality, and conforming to the new development philosophy. Developing new quality productive forces is an intrinsic requirement and an important focus for promoting high-quality development. It is highly inclusive and highly open, and will provide new opportunities and new momentum for Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-invested enterprises to integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development. The DPP authorities deliberately smear this and promote threat narratives about it. This is a routine tactic for obstructing cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and it is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation in Beijing on the 10th. Public opinion believes this will create an opportunity for the two sides of the Taiwan Strait to break the deadlock. The US State Department said, “We encourage ways to reduce tensions and promote cross-strait relations, and support both sides in continuing dialogue on the basis of dignity and respect.” What comment do…","General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation in Beijing and delivered an important speech, injecting stability and positive energy into cross-Strait relations. As General Secretary Xi Jinping pointed out, compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese; there is no psychological knot that cannot be untied, no problem that cannot be discussed, and no force that can separate us. On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we welcome political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life in Taiwan to come to the mainland for exchanges and communication, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The Japanese government recently said that, in view of concerns over China's maritime activities and the so-called “Taiwan contingency,” it has decided to designate 16 airports and ports in Hokkaido, Okinawa and other places as “specified-use airports and ports,” and to modify and expand them. What is your comment on Japan's increasingly obvious moves to intervene in the Taiwan Strait situation?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. This is a fact confirmed by a series of international treaties and documents, including the 1943 Cairo Declaration, the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation, and UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 of 1971, and is also a solemn commitment made by Japan in the four China-Japan political documents. Japan bears historical responsibility on the Taiwan question and should deeply reflect on history, draw lessons, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Last September, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” were officially issued. Please tell us what measures Fujian Province has introduced since the release of the Opinions, and what progress has been made so far.","Since the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were issued, the central government and relevant ministries and commissions have taken the initiative, proposed innovative measures, strengthened policy support, established coordinated implementation mechanisms, innovated working methods, and jointly promoted the implementation of the tasks and measures in the “Opinions.” The Fujian Provincial Party Committee and Provincial Government have strengthened their主体 responsibility, attached great importance to the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, formulated implementation measures for carrying out the “Opinions,” and issued the first batch of 15 measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots. In facilitating Taiwan compatriots’ travel and daily life, deepening Fujian-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation, and encouraging Taiwan compatriots to find employment and start businesses, they have earnestly carried out a batch of practical matters that Taiwan compatriots can perceive and access, advancing the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone with positive progress.\nFirst, significant new progress has been made in building a common home. Infrastructure connectivity has been pushed to full coverage, with some “Small Three Links” and air direct routes resumed, and passenger flow has grown substantially. The policy support and service system for Taiwan compatriots coming to Fujian to find employment and start businesses has been continuously improved. Fuzhou, Xiamen, and Pingtan have offered more than 2,000 rent-free and public rental housing units to Taiwan compatriots. The City of Fuzhou has made every effort to build the Fuzhou-Matsu “Same-City Living Circle,” supporting Matsu residents in enjoying the same treatment as local residents in Fuzhou, and launched the “Fuzhou-Matsu Same-City Pass” for Matsu residents. Cardholders can enjoy seven convenience service measures in Fuzhou, including public transportation discounts and free admission to four major cultural attractions.\nSecond, significant new progress has been made in deepening economic and trade cooperation. Last year, Fujian added more than 2,100 Taiwan-invested enterprises, with actual utilization of Taiwan investment reaching over 7 billion yuan. We have continuously optimized the business environment related to Taiwan and expanded development paths for Taiwan enterprises. For example, a Taiwan brand has, for the first time, joined the mainland’s “Big Family” of time-honored brands. Four Taiwan brands, including “Zhengxin” and “Taizu,” were awarded Xiamen Time-Honored Brand plaques.\nThird, significant new progress has been made in strengthening emotional bonds. In 2023, nearly 280 cross-Strait exchange activities, including the Straits Forum and the Straits Youth Festival, were successfully held, with positive results. Taiwan compatriots from the island visited Fujian 573,000 person-times. The number of national-level Straits Cross-Strait Exchange Bases has reached 26, the highest among all mainland regions. From May to December 2024, Sanming City will hold a series of Straits Cross-Strait Snack Culture Exchange activities, including a Cross-Strait Snack Food Carnival, the Shaxian Snack Taiwan Tour, and the Shaxian Snack Tourism and Culture Festival together with the Straits Cross-Strait Food Festival. These will include snack shop check-ins, short video creation, a snack food marathon, and visits to Taiwan youth entrepreneurship parks. More than 1,000 Taiwan compatriots are invited to participate, using “food” to make friends and “food” to connect hearts, enhancing cross-Strait food and culture exchanges.\nNext, Fujian Province will earnestly fulfill its主体 responsibility and continue to work on four aspects, namely promoting social integration, economic integration, emotional integration, and whole-area integration, to accelerate the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240424_12615815.htm"],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体记者","Question one: KMT Legislative Yuan caucus whip Fu Kun-chi plans to visit Beijing in the near future. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation? Question two: Han Kuo-yu, head of Taiwan's legislative body, has taken over as chairman of the “Taiwan Democracy Foundation.” Will the mainland side revoke the relevant disciplinary measures against the “Taiwan Democracy Foundation”? Question three: Rumors…","First question: Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should visit each other often, growing ever closer and more intimate. On the basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus,\" we are willing to hold dialogue and exchange views with people from all walks of life in Taiwan, jointly work to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nWe welcome Mr. Fu Kun-chi to lead a delegation on a visit, and we also welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan to visit and exchange on the mainland.\nSecond question: We firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and will never leave any room for \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. This is our consistent and firm position.\nThird question: Since the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait came into effect and began implementation, it has brought tangible benefits to the cross-Strait business sector, especially related business circles and the general public in Taiwan. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their party's narrow interests, have continuously and increasingly altered rules and set up obstacles, maliciously obstructing and undermining the normal cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, which has now led to uncertainty in the implementation of ECFA. If the DPP authorities continue to stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" position and refuse to repent, we support the relevant departments in studying further measures in accordance with relevant regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","First question: Taiwan media reported that the Hualien earthquake has severely hit local tourism, and many industry practitioners hope the mainland will soon reopen to mainland tourists visiting Taiwan. A tourism association figure called on the DPP authorities to lift the “group tour ban,” saying, “Whether Taiwan really needs the mainland tourist market, everyone knows in their hearts.” What is your comment?…","First question: The mainland has consistently insisted on promoting the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and the normalization of exchanges in all fields. To date, the DPP authorities have not lifted the “group tour ban” and have not opened up to allow mainland residents to visit Taiwan for exchanges. Only by removing these obstacles can favorable conditions be created for restoring normal cross-strait tourism and personnel exchanges.\nSecond question: We welcome Mr. Fu Kun-chi to visit with a delegation, and we also welcome people from all sectors of Taiwan to come to the mainland for visits and exchanges. We are willing to uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” to respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and to work together with relevant parties on the island to benefit Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: The Civil Aviation Administration of China recently announced the activation of airway M503's W122 and W123 connecting routes, which operate from west to east. The following day, the Taiwan side announced that 21 sorties of PLA military aircraft appeared near the “median line of the Taiwan Strait,” and claimed this would increase “national security risks.” Taiwan's civil aviation authorities also…","First question. First of all, we must emphasize that there is no so-called “median line of the Strait,” nor is there any so-called “national security” issue. The implementation of the connecting routes W122 and W123 of airway M503, operating from west to east, is a routine airspace optimization work carried out within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. Its main purpose is to improve the operational efficiency of airspace in the Fuzhou and Xiamen areas and improve flight punctuality.\nSince the connecting routes W122 and W123 were officially implemented on January 4, 2018, operating from east to west, they have operated safely and smoothly for more than six years. In putting these connecting routes into operation from west to east, the mainland side has fully taken into account the route conditions of Kinmen and Matsu airports and retained sufficient safety separation. It has also fully considered the operating airspace environment of the W122 and W123 connecting routes and formulated multiple contingency plans and safeguard measures, including for abnormal weather conditions.\nSecond question. As I have already stated, the competent authorities conducted the investigation strictly in accordance with relevant laws, regulations and WTO rules, widely listened to the views of all interested parties, fully protected the rights of all parties, and reached the final investigation conclusion objectively, fairly and impartially. We are willing to assist the enterprises involved in expanding into the mainland market in a lawful and compliant manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","During his visit to the mainland, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou invited teachers and students from many universities to exchange visits to Taiwan. Will the mainland side make relevant arrangements? Will this become the normal model for future exchanges between teachers and students of universities across the Strait?","We actively support and encourage closer exchanges among young people across the Strait, so that they can enhance mutual understanding and learn from each other through interaction. At present, the biggest obstacle to exchanges between teachers and students across the Strait is the control and restrictions imposed by the DPP authorities. Only when the DPP authorities comply with the wishes of the broad Taiwan compatriots, remove political barriers, and lift the bans and restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges, especially on mainland compatriots entering the island for exchanges, can all forms of cross-Strait exchange return to normal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","中国广播电视总台国广记者","Reports indicate that former Kuomintang Chairwoman Hung Hsiu-chu will lead nearly 200 Taiwan youths to visit Zhejiang in July for direct one-on-one interaction and exchanges with mainland youth. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang of China and chairperson of the Chinese Green Goose Peace Education Foundation, is currently in the mainland participating in exchange and visiting activities. At the invitation of the mainland side, Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu went to Shenzhen, Huizhou, Foshan and Guangzhou in Guangdong from April 20 to 27 to attend cross-Strait exchange activities and visit.\nThe foundation of cross-Strait relations lies with the people, its driving force lies with the people, and its hope lies with young people. We will continue to work with enlightened figures from all walks of life in Taiwan, including Chairperson Hung Hsiu-chu, to actively carry out cross-Strait youth exchange activities, create favorable conditions for young people on both sides of the Strait to learn from and inspire each other, provide more support for Taiwan youth to study, find employment, start businesses and live on the mainland, and enable more young people across the Strait to come to know one another, share common aspirations and walk together, continuously injecting youthful vitality into the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: Spokesperson, why has the one Kinmen person rescued by the mainland side still not been sent back? Second question: Is there any new progress on the “2·14” ship collision incident?","First question: The relevant situation is still being verified and understood. A Taiwan public representative hopes to accompany family members to visit the rescued personnel surnamed Hu, and we will provide relevant assistance.\nSecond question: The aftermath of the “2·14” serious ship collision incident has not been resolved for a long time. The fundamental reason is that relevant departments of the DPP authorities have gone back on their word and shirked responsibility, creating obstacles to post-incident negotiations. We urge the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation and promptly show sincerity in resolving the issue; otherwise, they must bear the consequences.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202404/t20240424_12615808.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Defense Minister Dong Jun recently held a video call with US Defense Secretary Austin. Please further introduce the relevant situation. What are China’s expectations for the development of China-US military relations going forward?","On the evening of April 16, Defense Minister Dong Jun held a video call with U.S. Secretary of Defense Austin. The two sides candidly and in depth exchanged views on China-U.S. military relations, the Taiwan question, the South China Sea issue, and other international and regional hot issues of common concern, and achieved positive and pragmatic results. This call is an important measure to implement the consensus of the two heads of state in the military field, and it has positive significance for maintaining the overall stability of China-U.S. military relations.\nSince the end of last year, the two militaries have smoothly held a series of exchange and cooperation activities, which have played a positive role in promoting the stabilization and improvement of military relations. We hope the U.S. side will move toward China. We hope both sides will take harmony as most precious, stability as paramount, and trustworthiness as the foundation as the basic guidelines for military interaction. On the basis of equality and mutual respect, we hope to build a military relationship free of conflict and confrontation, with open and pragmatic cooperation and gradually accumulated mutual trust, so that it truly serves as the stable cornerstone for the development of relations between the two countries.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The commander of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command recently said that the mainland's goal is to have the capability to \"attack Taiwan\" by 2027, and that joint military activities by China and Russia in the Indo-Pacific region have continued to increase. What is your comment on this? How can the two sides across the Taiwan Strait avoid accidental armed conflict?","Taiwan is Chinese territory, and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. On the issue of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the PLA always maintains a combat posture of being “ready at all times.”\nOn the question of how to avoid accidental clashes across the Strait, I would like to respond that as long as no one pursues “Taiwan independence,” there is no need to be anxious.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Taiwan military recently held the computer wargame exercise of the “Han Kuang 40” drill, extending the exercise from the previous five days and four nights to eight days and seven nights. Notably, the Taiwan military will for the first time include in this year's exercise a so-called scenario for responding to the “threat of Mainland roll-on/roll-off ships.” What is your comment?","The DPP authorities, attempting to “seek independence through force,” will only aggravate tensions across the Taiwan Strait and only harm the security and well-being of Taiwan residents. The “Han Kuang tabletop exercises” have turned out to be a dead end, and “seeking independence through force” is doomed to fail no matter how it is plotted.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The leaders of the United States and Japan recently issued a joint statement announcing a major upgrade of U.S.-Japan security. U.S. Forces Japan headquarters will be reorganized into a joint operational command, the U.S. side will give the U.S. Forces Japan headquarters more authority, and it is considering appointing a four-star general to lead U.S. forces in Japan. Some commentary says this clearly targets…","The US-Japan alliance is a product of the Cold War and a bilateral arrangement. It should not target third parties, nor should it undermine regional peace and stability. Japan once went down the path of militarism, launched wars of aggression, committed grave crimes against humanity, and brought profound disasters to the region and the world. Instead of sincerely reflecting on this, Japan has once again shown a dangerous posture of strengthening its military and expanding its armed forces. For some time, the United States and Japan have intensified military collusion, stirred up bloc confrontation, and used the groundless “China threat” as a pretext to form targeted “small circles.” This runs entirely counter to the trend of the times, and will only make the world increasingly see through the schemes of the US-Japan alliance to harm regional peace and stability. We urge the countries concerned to stop creating opposition and confrontation, otherwise this will only heighten regional tensions and ultimately backfire on themselves.\nI also want to stress that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After the mainland recently announced the activation of the M503 route, more than 20 mainland military aircraft appeared near the “Median Line of the Taiwan Strait.” Some analysts believe this breaks the tacit understanding between the two sides that has existed for many years and may make military relations between Taiwan and the mainland more tense. What is your comment on this?","Regarding the considerations behind this route, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office has already responded. Here, I will repeat what I said just now in answering a question from a Taiwan reporter: as long as they do not engage in “Taiwan independence,” there is no need to be overly worried.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the US President's Assistant for National Security Affairs recently said that the US will “take all measures to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait,” ensure that a “Taiwan contingency” will never happen, and will continue to provide Taiwan with the means of self-defense. The US Deputy Secretary of State said that the AUKUS submarine agreement among the US, UK and Australia will…","“The Taiwan contingency” originates from the United States stirring up trouble. If the U.S. truly wishes to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, immediately stop arming Taiwan, and immediately stop all official U.S.-Taiwan exchanges and military contacts.\n“AUKUS” is a product of the United States, the United Kingdom, and Australia clinging to Cold War mentality. It will only intensify tensions, incite confrontation, and undermine peace. Regional countries including China have expressed serious concern and firm opposition. Any attempt to use military cooperation to interfere in the Taiwan question is interference in China's internal affairs, violates the one-China principle and the basic norms of international relations, and endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan region. The Chinese People's Liberation Army bears the sacred mission of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Toward all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external connivance and support, it will never stand idly by and will never show mercy.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the US-Japan-Philippines summit recently issued a joint statement expressing “serious concern” over the situation at Second Thomas Shoal and China's “dangerous and aggressive” conduct in the South China Sea and East China Sea. It urged China to abide by the ruling in the South China Sea arbitration case and called for a peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question. What is China's comment?","The joint statement by the United States, Japan, and the Philippines disregards facts, reverses right and wrong, and makes unwarranted accusations against China. We express our strong dissatisfaction with it and firmly oppose it.\nChina has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands and their adjacent waters, which rests on abundant historical and legal grounds. The territorial scope of the Philippines has been determined by a series of international treaties, including the 1898 Treaty of Peace between the United States and Spain, the 1900 Treaty between the United States and Spain on the Cession of Outlying Islands of the Philippines, and the 1930 Treaty Concerning the Delimitation of the Boundary between British North Borneo and the American Philippines. These treaties have never included China’s Nansha Islands or Huangyan Island. The Philippine side is fully aware of this.\nThe Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands have been Chinese territory since ancient times. They were first discovered, named, and utilized by Chinese people, and have been within China’s maritime defense jurisdiction since the early Ming Dynasty. Japan seized the Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands during the First Sino-Japanese War. According to international legal documents such as the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, the Diaoyu Islands have already been returned to China under international law. This is a matter of public consensus. Japan’s attempt to muddy the waters on the question of sovereignty over the Diaoyu Islands is utterly a delusion.\nThe so-called ruling in the South China Sea arbitration case is nothing but a worthless piece of paper. The arbitral tribunal in the South China Sea arbitration violated the principle of “state consent,” exceeded its authority in adjudicating the case, and rendered a biased ruling. It seriously violated the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and general international law. Its ruling is naturally illegal and null and void, and China will never accept or recognize it. Incidentally, on the question of accepting international arbitration, the United States has a very bad historical record. Setting aside illegitimate arbitration, even when rulings are legitimate, the United States has on multiple occasions refused to accept them. We demand that the United States carefully reflect on itself before accusing others.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The governments of the United States, Japan, and the Philippines have all made solemn commitments to China on the Taiwan question. We demand that the above-mentioned countries honor their commitments, immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and stop undermining regional peace and stability. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will, as always, firmly defend its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and firmly safeguard regional peace and stability.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Koo Li-hsiung, who has been listed by the mainland as a “diehard Taiwan independence” element, is reportedly set to take over as head of Taiwan's defense department. He publicly stated this morning that after taking office, his top goal is to keep pushing back the timetable of possible military actions by the mainland. How does the spokesperson view his remarks?","“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water; it is a dead end. The PLA resolutely fights “independence” and promotes reunification, and will defeat all separatist schemes.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-04-25","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, US President Biden recently signed a foreign aid bill with a total value of about 950 billion yuan... [note: see correction below]","On the first question: Taiwan is the Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests and the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed, and it tolerates no foreign interference. Recently, the US side has hollowed out, emptied, and distorted the one-China principle through means such as arms sales and military aid to Taiwan, sending serious erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. This will only intensify tensions in the Taiwan Strait and seriously undermine peace and stability there. “Taiwan independence” and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Indulging and supporting “Taiwan independence” will surely bring fire upon oneself and bitter consequences.\nOn the second question: China has consistently held that defense and security cooperation between relevant countries must not harm the interests of third parties or undermine regional peace and stability.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/04/25/10756639.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-04-26","Wang Wenbin","Dragon TV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with US Secretary of State Antony Blinken this morning. Can you share more details?","This morning, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi held talks with US Secretary of State Antony Blinken in Beijing.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi noted that the overall China-US relations have been stabilized from further deterioration, but negative factors continue to rise and build. Our approach, position and expectations when it comes to China-US relations have been consistent. We always view and develop this relationship in light of the need for a community with a shared future for humanity, and follow the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation proposed by President Xi Jinping with an emphasis on respecting each other’s core interests.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi said that last November, President Xi Jinping and President Joe Biden had a successful meeting in San Francisco and charted the “San Francisco vision” for a stable, sound and sustainable bilateral relationship. It is the job for both sides to deliver on that vision. In a volatile and transforming world, the first question we should answer to make this relationship work is: do we want China and the US to be partners or rivals? Get this wrong, and steady development of China-US relations will hang in the balance. If the US keeps seeing China as its primary rival, the relationship will keep running into difficulties and challenges.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stressed that the Taiwan question is the number one red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. China asked the US to strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and not to send any form of wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatists. The US needs to act on President Biden’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and not using Taiwan as a tool to contain China. The US should stop arming Taiwan and support China’s peaceful reunification.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi pointed out that no one shall deprive the Chinese people of their right to development. The US has employed all kinds of measures to hit China on trade, economy and technology. This is not fair competition, but steps to contain and block China. It is not de-risking but risk-building. The US said it does not seek to contain China’s economy, decouple or bar China’s progress in science and technology. It should honor those words. The US needs to stop spreading the false narrative of “Chinese overcapacity”, lift illicit sanctions on Chinese businesses and halt the Section 301 tariffs which are against WTO rules.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stressed that the Asia-Pacific should not become a wrestling ground for major countries. We hope the US will make the right choice, work with China, engage in sound interactions in the Asia-Pacific, stop forming groupings exclusive to one another, stop coercing regional countries to take sides, stop deploying land-based medium-range missiles, stop harming China’s strategic security interests, and stop undermining the hard-won peace and stability in the region.\nSecretary Blinken noted that the US and China have the most consequential bilateral relationship in the world. It is important for both sides to responsibly manage this relationship. The US continues to follow its one-China policy and does not support “Taiwan independence.” The US does not seek to change China’s system, has no intention to have conflict with China, and does not seek to decouple from China or hold back China’s development. A growing and successful China is good for the world. The US is ready to work with China to build on the common understandings of the two presidents in San Francisco, step up dialogue and communication, effectively manage differences, avoid misperception and miscalculation, and work for a stable and growing US-China relationship.\nThe two sides also exchanged views on the Ukraine issue, the Palestinian-Israeli conflict, the DPRK, Myanmar and other issues.\nThe two sides agreed that the meeting was candid, substantive and constructive. The two sides agreed to continue following the guidance of the two presidents and work to stabilize and advance China-US relations. They recognized the progress in dialogue and cooperation in various fields since the San Francisco meeting and agreed to speed up implementing the important common understandings reached by the two presidents in San Francisco, maintain high-level exchanges and interactions at various levels, continue mil-to-mil communication and consultations in various fields, further cooperation in counternarcotics, climate change and AI, and take measures to expand people-to-people exchanges. The two sides stand ready to strengthen communication in international and regional hotspots.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347746.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240426_11289913.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-04-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on April 27 that compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are one family. In the face of major natural disasters, compatriots on both sides have always supported each other and overcome difficulties together. After the magnitude 7.3 earthquake in the waters off Hualien, Taiwan on April 3, the mainland side immediately expressed deep concern and heartfelt sympathy, and stated its willingness to provide disaster relief assistance to affected compatriots. We understand that residents in the Hualien disaster area hope to have stable, relatively convenient and comfortable prefabricated housing as soon as possible. The mainland side is willing to provide help and will make donations through cross-strait Red Cross organizations, and hopes the relevant supplies can enter the island smoothly and quickly reach the disaster-affected residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240427_12616489.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-04-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council Answers Reporters' Questions\n(April 28, 2024)\nQuestion: Today, the Ministry of Transport and the Civil Aviation Administration of China announced that, through existing liaison channels under the cross-Strait consultation framework, they have urged the Taiwan side to resume cross-Strait maritime passenger direct sailings and to expand the resumption of cross-Strait air passenger direct flights to mainland destinations. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?\nAnswer:\nCross-Strait direct shipping and flights have greatly facilitated travel between the two sides and have played an important role in advancing the common interests of compatriots on both sides. Since last year, as epidemic prevention and control has entered a new stage, we have followed the mainstream public opinion among Taiwan compatriots, who want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and have actively promoted the resumption of cross-Strait air and maritime direct flights and sailings and the \"Small Three Links\" (direct mini-links). Although the number of cross-Strait air passenger direct flights and passenger volume have increased compared with the epidemic period, overall travel between the two sides remains quite inconvenient due to limited destinations, and cross-Strait maritime passenger direct sailings have not yet resumed. People on both sides of the Strait have a very strong desire for the full resumption of cross-Strait air and maritime direct services. We hope the Taiwan side will fully consider the demands of people on both sides and of shipping companies, and as soon as possible fully resume cross-Strait maritime passenger direct sailings, including the Pingtan–Taipei, Pingtan–Taichung, Xiamen–Taichung, Xiamen–Keelung, and Damaoyu (Zhejiang)–Keelung routes, and restore direct air passenger flights between the mainland and Taiwan to 30 mainland destinations, including Tianjin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202404/t20240428_12616801.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-04-29","Lin Jian","China Daily","On April 24 local time, US President Joe Biden signed into law a military aid package, which contains negative articles on China. What is China’s comment on this?","China firmly rejects the US passing and signing into law the military aid package containing negative content on China. We have lodged serious representations to the US.\nThis package gravely infringes upon China’s sovereignty. It includes large military aid to Taiwan, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The legislation undermines the principles of market economy and fair competition by wantonly going after other countries’ companies in the name of “national security,” which once again reveals the US’s hegemonic and bullying nature. It advocates sanctions on China in disregard of the huge amount of work China has done to help the US address its fentanyl crisis. The legislation also threatens to impose unilateral sanctions and long-arm jurisdiction over normal economic and trade exchanges between China and Iran under the framework of international law, which creates serious obstacles for China-US cooperation in relevant areas.\nWe urge the US to respect China’s core interests and major concerns, and not to implement these negative articles concerning China. Otherwise China will take strong and resolute measures to safeguard our sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347747.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240429_11291103.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-04-29","Lin Jian","Beijing Youth Daily","The documentary film The Yangtze River by Japanese director Ryo Takeuchi was shown on April 26 at the Beijing International Film Festival. Earlier, Chinese Ambassador to Japan Wu Jianghao attended the premiere of the documentary in Tokyo. The tremendous change along the Yangtze River over the past decade documented by the film touched the audience from both countries and sparked heated discussion. Do you have any…","I also noted this film and watched a clip of it. From a unique perspective and with superb shooting skills, the documentary The Yangtze River illustrated the tremendous changes along the river over the past decade, providing an epitome of China’s economic and social development in the new era. The documentary presented both the breath-taking landscape and the industrial people and their heart-warming stories. The sincerity and goodness channeled by the director and leading characters through the documentary transcend time, distance, language and nationality, and struck a chord among audience from various backgrounds. We hope that more Japanese media and people from the art community will present stories of China in a vivid and truthful way from an objective perspective to enhance the mutual understanding and friendly sentiments between the people of China and Japan. We also hope that friends from various countries will get to know more about China through this documentary and come to China to feel the robust progress of Chinese modernization for themselves.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347747.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202404/t20240429_11291103.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-03","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","XINHUA, Beijing, May 3 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 3rd, saying that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and we have always cared about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. On the premise of adhering to the one-China principle, we have made proper arrangements for Taiwan region’s participation in global health affairs.…","Chen Binhua said that our position on the issue of Chinese Taiwan region's participation in World Health Organization activities has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is also the fundamental principle affirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This has caused the political basis for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. This situation was entirely caused by the DPP authorities.\nChen Binhua said that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The US side should immediately stop using the World Health Assembly to hype Taiwan-related issues. It should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions, rather than saying one thing and doing another, and stop continuously indulging “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240503_12617747.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-06","Lin Jian","CCTV","At a seminar held by a US think tank, Mark Lambert, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State in the Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs and China Coordinator said that Resolution 2758 does not endorse, equate to, or reflect an international consensus on the one-China principle and has absolutely no bearing on countries’ sovereignty choices with respect to their relationships with Taiwan. He said the resolution…","Mark Lambert’s remarks are a total distortion of the resolution and facts. They misrepresent the history, and tread upon the international law and basic norms of international relations. It is shocking and outrageous that a US State Department official overseeing China-US relations would speak so irresponsibly and brazenly tell and spread lies. The Chinese side has strongly protested to the US side on those remarks.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is an undeniable fact, a universal consensus of the international community and a basic norm in international relations. One hundred and eighty-three countries in the world, including the US, have established and are advancing diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle.\nResolution 2758 adopted at the 26th Session of the UN General Assembly in 1971 stated in black and white that it “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations, and to expel forthwith the representatives of Chiang Kai-shek from the place which they unlawfully occupy at the United Nations and in all the organizations related to it.” The resolution made it clear that the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN; Taiwan is not a country but a part of China’s territory. It makes clear Taiwan’s status as a non-sovereign entity. UNGA Resolution 2758 resolved once and for all politically, legally and procedurally the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN. The resolution also made clear that there can only be one seat representing China at the UN and precluded the possibility of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nSince the adoption of the resolution, the one-China principle has been observed by the UN and its specialized agencies on the Taiwan question. Taiwan is referred to as “Taiwan, province of China” in all UN’s official documents. It was clearly stated in the official legal opinions of the Office of Legal Affairs of the UN Secretariat that “the United Nations considers ‘Taiwan’ as a province of China with no separate status,” and the “‘authorities’ in ‘Taipei’ are not considered to... enjoy any form of government status.”\nThe Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations must and can only be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states. Taiwan, a province of China, has no basis, reason or right to join the UN or its relevant agencies. This is stipulated in the UN Charter and is the principle that all UN member states must follow and an obligation that they should fulfill.\nAs a major country and permanent member of the UN Security Council, the US is supposed to take the lead in observing the UNGA resolutions and abiding by international law and basic norms in international relations, but it does just the opposite. The US deliberately distorted UNGA’s Resolution 2758 and propagated the narrative of so-called “Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system” to hollow out the one-China principle, embolden and support “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and serve its pernicious aim of suppressing China. Such an attempt to turn back the wheel of history and ignore global opinion will only be resisted and opposed by the international force for justice and will not succeed.\nUNGA Resolution 2758 brooks no challenge, and the one-China principle is unshakable. To play the “Taiwan card” is to drive oneself into the wall. Supporting Taiwan will inevitably backfire. We urge the US to stand on the side of the majority of countries in the world, stand on the right side of history, follow the solemn decision made by the UNGA, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on the US leader’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan,” and stop stepping on China’s baseline and red line on the Taiwan question in any way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240506_11293362.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-06","Lin Jian","DPA","Germany’s Foreign Minister said last weekend that she did not rule out the possibility of the German frigate Baden-Württemberg crossing the Taiwan Strait during its mission starting from tomorrow. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","Let me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China will not waver in its resolve to safeguard the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China respects countries’ right to navigation in accordance with international law, but firmly opposes any country making provocations and threatening China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation. The Asia-Pacific is a pacesetter of global peace and development. We hope countries outside the region will do more things that are conducive to peace, stability and prosperity and join the effort to safeguard the development of the region, instead of making provocations and creating trouble for the peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240506_11293362.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-06","Lin Jian","China Daily","The Commissioner of Public Inquiry into Foreign Interference in Federal Electoral Processes and Democratic Institutions of Canada issued the Initial Report on May 3, saying that “China currently stands out as the most persistent and sophisticated foreign interference threat to Canada.” Canadian Prime Minister Justin Trudeau asserted previously that China tried to interfere in the election but failed. The report…","We’ve repeatedly stressed China’s commitment to the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs. China has never and will never have any interest in interfering in Canada’s internal affairs. The so-called “China’s foreign interference” is nothing but a lie to serve political purposes.\nChina strongly deplores and opposes this so-called “Initial Report.” We reject its groundless accusations and vilification, and have lodged serious protests to Canada.\nThe so-called Report is riddled with speculative wording such as “possible”, “may” and “potential.” It says its arguments are mainly supported by “intelligence”, but adds that “intelligence is not proven fact” and provides no real evidence. Such ideologically driven reports are the product of some self-serving Canadian politicians, who deliberately seek to confuse and mislead the public with false accusations and self-contradictory allegations. This is extremely irresponsible.\nCanada has long had a record of grossly interfering in China’s domestic affairs on issues concerning our core interests such as Taiwan, Xinjiang, Xizang, and Hong Kong. Canada is the one that actually needs to stop foreign interference activities.\nChina urges Canada to respect and face up to the facts, ditch its ideological bias and immediately stop groundless attacks and smears against China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347749.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240506_11293362.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-09","Lin Jian","China Daily","It is reported that the elected-leader Lai Ching-te of the Taiwan region said that he looks forward to strengthening cooperation with Japan after May 20 and that any contingency for Taiwan is a contingency for Japan and vice versa. What’s China’s comment?","“Any contingency for Taiwan is a contingency for Japan.” This is a dangerous but apparently miscalculated notion preached by some in Japan. By repeating and hyping that rhetoric, the DPP authorities are essentially telling the world that their underlying logic is to ingratiate themselves with Japan, sell Taiwan out and seek “Taiwan independence” through soliciting foreign support. It once again reminds people that “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference are the biggest undermining factor for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Let me stress that the one-China principle is a universal consensus. No separatist attempt for “Taiwan independence” will get anywhere, whatever its form or pretext.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240509_11301939.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-10","Lin Jian","Xinhua News Agency","Can you brief us on President Xi Jinping’s visit to Hungary?","On May 9 local time, President Xi Jinping attended the welcoming ceremony in Budapest held by Hungarian President Tamás Sulyok and Prime Minister Viktor Orbán and held separate talks with them. President Xi met with the press with Prime Minister Orbán. Leaders of the two countries announced the decision to upgrade the China-Hungary relationship to an all-weather comprehensive strategic partnership for the new era.\nPresident Xi noted Hungary was one of the first countries to recognize the People’s Republic of China. The relationship is now at its best in history. Our traditional friendship has taken deep roots among the two peoples and our cooperation reaped fruitful outcomes in various fields. This year marks the 75th anniversary of diplomatic ties between China and Hungary. The two sides need to take stock of the valuable experience and chart the way forward. First, we need to uphold equality, follow a development path suited to our national conditions, and keep our future firmly in our own hands. The long-lasting friendship between China and Hungary is neither targeted against nor subject to restrictions from any third party. Second, we need to uphold mutual trust and mutual assistance, always render each other understanding and firmly support each other in safeguarding our respective sovereignty, security and development interests. Third, we need to uphold win-win cooperation, expand cooperation in various fields within the framework of the Belt and Road Initiative and forge synergy between our respective development strategies. Fourth, we need to uphold fairness and justice, stand on the right side of history, and strive to make positive contributions to the cause of peace and development of mankind.\nPresident Xi underlined China appreciates Hungary’s long-term commitment to a friendly policy toward China and its unequivocal and firm support for China on issues related to Taiwan, Hong Kong and human rights. China firmly supports Hungary in pursuing a development path suited to its national conditions and stands ready to cement political mutual trust with Hungary, strengthen exchanges between the two countries’ governments, legislatures and political parties and continue to firmly support each other’s core interests and major concerns. China’s modernization will surely bring more opportunities to Hungary and other countries in the world. China welcomes Hungary to become a companion on the Chinese path to modernization. China is ready to work with Hungary to further synergize development strategies of the two countries, leverage the role of mechanisms such as the China-Hungary Inter-Governmental Belt and Road Cooperation Committee, advance cooperation in infrastructure, green energy and other fields in an orderly manner, and complete the construction of the Hungary-Serbia railway as scheduled. We will actively expand cooperation in emerging areas such as clean energy and artificial intelligence. It is hoped that Hungary will take the opportunity of taking on the rotating presidency of the EU in the second half of this year to promote the steady and sound development of China-EU relations. The cooperation between China and Central and Eastern European countries (CEEC) has a strong internal driving force. It is hoped that Hungary will continue to play an important role in promoting the China-CEEC cooperation to better benefit people of various countries.\nFollowing the talks, leaders of the two countries witnessed the exchange of multiple bilateral cooperation documents on Belt and Road cooperation, economy and trade, investment, science and technology, culture and agriculture. The two sides issued the Joint Statement Between the People’s Republic of China and Hungary on the Establishment of An All-Weather Comprehensive Strategic Partnership for the New Era and the Outcome List of President Xi Jinping’s State Visit to Hungary.\nDuring his trip to Europe, President Xi was given high-level reception by leaders of all three countries and warm welcome from the people there. From the shepherd’s song in Hautes-Pyrénées to the cheering crowds in Serbia and to the same young Hungarian girl who presented flowers to President Xi 15 years ago as well as this time, these moving and heart-warming moments reflect that the friendship between China and relevant countries is deeply rooted in people’s hearts and the bilateral relationships enjoy profound public support. We have every confidence in the prospects of China’s relations with France, Serbia and Hungary, and will work to make the China-EU relations more strategic, stable, constructive and mutually beneficial and promote the steady and sustained progress in China-EU relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347753.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240510_11302655.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-10","Lin Jian","Phoenix TV","It’s reported that “Taiwan’s Representative in Japan” Hsieh Chang-ting said that 37 Japanese Diet Members plan to attend the “president-elect’s inauguration” to be held on May 20. What’s China’s comment?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan has never been a country and there’s no such thing as “president of Taiwan”.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Japan made a clear commitment in the China-Japan Joint Statement, “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this position of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its position under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation made it clear that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out, and what the Cairo Declaration mainly touches upon is that the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese shall be restored to China. Japan has more than once made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question, including not supporting “two Chinas”, “one China, one Taiwan” or “Taiwan independence,” and only maintaining people-to-people and region-to-region exchanges with Taiwan. This is what happened in history and the stance and principles that Japan must uphold.\nWe seriously urge Japan to adhere to the principles and spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, take concrete actions to demonstrate its commitment to the one-China principle, refrain from emboldening and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in whatever form, and keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable rather than do the opposite. Our message to the DPP authorities: making provocations to seek “Taiwan independence” with external forces will not succeed; anyone who sell the national interests of the country will be held accountable by history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347753.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240510_11302655.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-10","Lin Jian","China Review News","A question on the interaction between Japan and Taiwan. It’s reported that on May 9, Tsai Ing-wen conferred a medal on former Japanese Ambassador to China Hideo Tarumi in Taipei, in recognition of his contributions to Taiwan-Japan relations. Tarumi said that Taiwan and Japan work hand in hand with close affinity, and he has a stronger sense of identity with Taiwan. On that day, Lai Ching-te also met with Tarumi…","The person you mentioned has frequently made irresponsible remarks after retirement and done things against professional ethics that breach the commitment of the Japanese government to the one-China principle. We urge Japan to abide by the principles and spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, strengthen discipline on the person concerned, and not interfere in China’s internal affairs or send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in whatever form. The DPP authorities purposely staged the political theater to ingratiate with Japan, sell Taiwan out and seek “Taiwan independence” by soliciting foreign support. This self-degrading act will only expose themselves to more ridicule in the world.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347753.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240510_11302655.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-13","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Registration for the 77th World Health Assembly (WHA) will close today. Taiwan has not received an invitation. The DPP authorities claim that its absence from the WHA will cause a “gap” in global anti-epidemic efforts. What’s the Chinese government’s comment?","There is but one China in the world. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, is consistent and clear, that is, this must be handled under the one-China principle, which is also a fundamental principle demonstrated by the UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nChina’s Taiwan region, unless given approval by the Central Government, has no basis, reason or right to participate in the WHA. After coming into power in 2016, the DPP has refused to recognize the 1992 consensus and been hellbent on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence.” As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. Hence, China has decided not to approve the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA. This decision has sufficient reason and a solid legal basis. It’s not just about upholding the one-China principle but also about the sanctity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions.\nFor quite some time, the DPP authorities and certain country have been deliberately distorting and challenging UNGA Resolution 2758, trumpeting the notion that Taiwan’s status is undetermined, and advocating support for Taiwan’s participation in the United Nations multilateral forums, including the WHA. These moves mislead international public opinion and challenge the one-China consensus among the international community. They trample on the international law and basic norms governing international relations, and seek to turn back the wheel of history. Such attempts will not succeed.\nThe DPP authorities and some countries claim that Taiwan’s absence from the WHA will cause a “gap” in global anti-epidemic efforts and use it as an excuse to demand “Taiwan’s meaningful participation” in the WHO. That’s a politically-driven and completely false claim. The Chinese Central Government has made proper arrangement for the Taiwan region’s participation in global health affairs on the condition that the one-China principle is upheld. Over the past year alone, medical and technical experts from China’s Taiwan region applied for participation in WHO technical activities 21 times, which involved 24 participants, and all the applications were approved by the Chinese Central Government. There is an International Health Regulations Contact Point in the Taiwan region for it to promptly access and report to the WHO concerning information related to health emergencies. Facts fully reflect that the Chinese Central Government has every sincerity and has taken credible and active measures to address the health issues that our compatriots in Taiwan care about, and that their rights to health are duly protected.\nThe one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. China’s decision of not letting the Taiwan region participate in this year’s WHA has received wide support and understanding from the international community. Challenging the one-China principle will end up nowhere and turning back the wheel of history will not succeed. Any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” and use Taiwan to contain China will only be met with firm opposition from the international community and is doomed to failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347754.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240513_11303853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-13","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华当日就此答记者","Beijing, May 13 (Xinhua) — The registration for the 77th World Health Assembly will close on the 13th, and Taiwan will once again be unable to attend the World Health Assembly. Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on this matter the same day.","Chen Binhua pointed out that regarding the question of the Taiwan region’s participation in WHO activities, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is also the fundamental principle affirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. From 2009 to 2016, on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which both sides upheld as embodying the one-China principle, the Taiwan region participated in the World Health Assembly as an observer under the name “Chinese Taipei,” through cross-Strait consultations. This was a special arrangement made through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” causing the political foundation for the Taiwan region’s participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. That the Taiwan region cannot attend the meeting is entirely the result of the DPP authorities.\nChen Binhua said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and are one family. We have always cared about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and we have made appropriate arrangements for the Taiwan region’s participation in global health affairs. In the past year, Taiwan medical technical experts participated in 21 batches of WHO technical activities, totaling 24 person-times. Under the framework of the International Health Regulations, any public health emergency information that WHO notifies to various places is also promptly available to the Taiwan region. Obviously, the Taiwan region’s channels of communication and cooperation with WHO in technical fields are fully open, its channels for obtaining information and support on various public health emergencies are fully effective, and the health rights of Taiwan compatriots are effectively guaranteed.\nChen Binhua pointed out that recently, the DPP authorities, taking advantage of the international community’s attention to global public health issues, have repeatedly manipulated the question of the Taiwan region’s participation in the World Health Assembly. Their real aim is to use this to highlight the so-called “sovereign status,” and their true intention is “seeking independence through health,” challenging the basic framework of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle. The DPP authorities’ deceptive and provocative conduct has long been seen through by compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the international community, and it is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240513_12619917.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-14","Wang Wenbin","AFP","According to reports, the US and Taiwan “navies” conducted some joint drills in the Pacific last month. Can you confirm that?","I noted that it's reported that the US and Taiwan vessels had “unplanned encounters.” I want to stress that China is firmly opposed to the US’s military contact with Taiwan. This position is consistent and unequivocal. We urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and stop its wrong behavior of having military contact with Taiwan. We also have a clear message for the DPP authorities: seeking “Taiwan independence” and resisting reunification with force is bound to fail. They can be assured of that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347755.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240514_11304421.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-15","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State in the Bureau of East Asian and Pacific Affairs and China Coordinator said that \"Resolution 2758 does not endorse, equate to, or reflect an international consensus on the one-China principle.\" A program director of the German Marshall Fund of the United States said that “the PRC’s positions” on UN Resolution 2758 “are not consistent with international law.” What is your…","The past few weeks saw repeated ill-intentioned comments from some US officials to challenge the authority of UNGA Resolution 2758, calling Taiwan’s status “undetermined” and trumpeting for Taiwan’s “meaningful participation” in the UN system. Those comments distort the facts and history, tread on international law and the basic norms of international relations, and breach the US’s own commitment.\nTaiwan has been part of China since ancient times. This is a historical fact; it is also the international consensus. The 1943 Cairo Declaration and the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation clearly stipulated that Taiwan, a Chinese territory stolen by Japan, shall be restored to China. These documents with international legal effect formed an integral part of the post-WWII international order and also affirmed Taiwan’s status as China’s inalienable territory from a legal perspective.\nOn October 25, 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 with an overwhelming majority. The Resolution resolved once and for all the question of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the United Nations as a political, legal and procedural issue. It made clear that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is a part of China, not a country. It also made clear that there is only one seat of China in the United Nations, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal representative, precluding “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nThe US is a signatory to the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. In the three China-US joint communiqués, the US clearly states that “the government of the United States of America recognizes China’s position that there is only one China and Taiwan is part of China.” US leaders have, on multiple occasions, reaffirmed the commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” However, the US is now publicly questioning and misinterpreting UNGA Resolution 2758, fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, and trumpeting for the participation of Taiwan in the UN system which requires sovereign statehood. What the US is doing violates its own commitment and aims to turn back the wheel of history.\nThe US’s distortion and slander of UNGA Resolution 2758 is reminiscent of the US’s recent claim that UNSC Resolution 2728 demanding an immediate ceasefire in Gaza is “non-binding.” Both cases reflect the US’s selective approach to international law and the basic norms of international relations, and the US's bullying and double standard. However, gone are the days when hegemony and power politics dominated international relations. Any country, including the US, that tries to challenge the UNGA Resolution and the one-China principle will only find it futile. Fifty-three years ago, before UNGA Resolution 2758 was adopted with an overwhelming majority, the US came up with the so-called “dual representation” proposal in an attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” which was discarded. Today, any US attempt to go against the trend of the times, play the “Taiwan card” and use Taiwan to contain China will only end up in greater failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347756.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240515_11305026.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear reporters, good day. Today's press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office is hosted by me. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Ahead of '5·20', what is the mainland's assessment of the content of Lai Qingde's inaugural address concerning cross-Strait relations? How will the mainland respond?","Peace rather than war, development rather than decline, exchange rather than separation, and cooperation rather than confrontation is the mainstream public opinion on the island. Whether to follow public opinion and take the right path of peaceful development, or to defy public opinion and take the evil path of provocation and confrontation, concerns the interests and well-being of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, the future development of Taiwan, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It is a question that the new leader of the Taiwan region must seriously face and clearly answer.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. We have consistently upheld the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and interference by external forces, continue to expand exchanges and cooperation across all cross-Strait fields, constantly deepen cross-Strait integration and development, and resolutely promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620421.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the “Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum” and several other pro-unification groups in Taiwan, together with social sectors on the island, launched a signature campaign for a peace declaration titled “Cherish Peace, Win-Win for Both Sides of the Strait.” They demand that Lai Ching-te, the incoming new leader of the Taiwan region, declare that he will abide by the One China principle and be…","Taiwan unification-oriented groups, together with social circles, launched a signature campaign for the peace declaration “Cherish Peace, Win-Win for Both Sides,” demanding that the new leader of the Taiwan region abide by one China, restart cross-Strait consultations, safeguard exchanges and travel between compatriots on both sides, and correct the “de-Sinicized literature and history curriculum guidelines.” This demonstrates the clear stance of far-sighted people from all walks of life on the island and clearly expresses just demands that conform to the fundamental interests of Taiwan compatriots. It reflects the common voice of the broad Taiwan compatriots, who want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We affirm and appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620418.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","The 26th Straits Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Investment Fair will open in Fuzhou soon. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 26th Straits Forum (Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Investment Fair), co-hosted by the TAO of the State Council and the People's Government of Fujian Province, will open in Fuzhou, Fujian, on May 16. Over 30 years of development, the “Straits Forum” has become a renowned comprehensive economic and trade exchange event across the Taiwan Strait. It has attracted more than 10,000 Taiwanese enterprises and over 30,000 Taiwanese business guests in total, playing an important role in exploring new paths for integrated development across the Strait and promoting smooth economic and trade cooperation between the two sides.\nThe theme of this year's Straits Forum is “Deepen Cross-Strait Integration, Build the First Home,” focusing on implementing the Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. It emphasizes “facilitating integration through connectivity, facilitating integration through benefits, and facilitating integration through emotional bonds.” Activities include the opening ceremony and the Cross-Strait Exchange and Interaction Sharing Meeting, the 2024 Cross-Strait Chamber of Commerce Cooperation and Exchange Activities, the 30th Anniversary Docking and Exchange Meeting of the Fuzhou Taiwan Business Association, and the 7th Fuzhou-Matsu Consultation Meeting. Meanwhile, supporting thematic exchange platforms will be set up, including the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Achievements Release and Industrial Cooperation Promotion Zone. It is expected that more than 50 industrial and commercial delegations from the island and over 1,000 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesspeople will attend. We welcome media friends to visit and report on the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620409.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","人民日报海外版记者","Many in the DPP authorities’ new “governing” team have strong “Taiwan independence” coloring, including several “Taiwan independence” diehards on the list. Some analysts believe that the risk of “Taiwan independence” will continue to rise in the coming period, and the situation across the Taiwan Strait will become more complex and grave. What countermeasures does the mainland side have in response?","For some time now, the DPP authorities have stubbornly adhered to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, condoned and allowed hardline “Taiwan independence” die-hards to openly promote the “two-state theory,” extensively colluded with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, deliberately stirred up and intensified confrontation and opposition across the Strait, violently obstructed and restricted normal exchanges across the Strait, and continuously driven up tensions and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” separatism betrays the great righteousness of the nation and runs counter to the great trend of popular sentiment. It seriously endangers national sovereignty, security, and development interests. In response, we will never tolerate it, will never show leniency, and will never stand idly by. For those die-hard elements whose “Taiwan independence” words and deeds are vile and whose secessionist activities are rampant, the state will introduce legal measures to strictly punish, in accordance with law, the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country.\nThe legal measures introduced by the state to punish “Taiwan independence” are aimed at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” elements and their separatist activities, and by no means at Taiwan compatriots. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, conform to the great trend of history, recognize the extreme harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, resolutely resist and oppose any “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, and, through concrete actions, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and protect their own safety and well-being. Together with compatriots on the mainland, they should work hand in hand to build a bright future of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620417.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","In recent years, some so-called Taiwan “celebrity commentators” have fabricated false information such as “mainland people cannot afford tea eggs” and “mainland high-speed trains have no backrests,” spreading rumors and smearing the mainland. This often sets netizens on both sides of the Strait against each other, and mainland residents are very indignant about it. There are reports that the mainland side is…","For some time, a handful of so-called Taiwan “famous commentators,” including Huang Shicong, Li Zhenghao, Wang Yichuan, Yu Beichen and Liu Baojie, have ignored the facts of the mainland’s development and progress. They have deliberately fabricated false and negative information about the mainland and widely disseminated it through TV, the internet, newspapers and other media. Their erroneous remarks have deceived some people on the island, stirred up hostility and confrontation, and hurt the feelings between compatriots on both sides. The facts are clear and the circumstances are serious. The mainland will punish the above five individuals and their family members in accordance with the law.\nSilence toward and tolerance of evil amount to unfairness and harm to goodness. Public opinion is not a place beyond the law. Any act of fabricating or spreading rumors, disturbing social order, or damaging national honor and interests will be punished in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620415.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Recently, the DPP authorities released a short video on social media calling for support for Taiwan's participation in this year's World Health Assembly. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","On the issue of Taiwan, China’s participation in World Health Organization activities, we have repeatedly stated our position: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, thereby undermining the political foundation for handling this issue. The DPP authorities refuse to abandon their “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and do not change their confrontational mindset. They persist in political manipulation, attempting to mislead perceptions and deceive the public. Their political schemes will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620412.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Mainland coast guard vessels have recently carried out law enforcement patrols several times in waters near Kinmen. Some public opinion holds that the vicious ship-collision incident of \"February 14\" has still not been properly resolved, and that the mainland's move is putting pressure on the DPP authorities. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. Mainland coast guard units conducting routine law enforcement patrols in waters near Kinmen in accordance with the law are a legitimate measure to maintain the operational order in the relevant waters. We will absolutely not tolerate and will never condone the brutal conduct of the DPP authorities, who disregard the safety of life and property of mainland fishermen and harm the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities must give an account to the families of the victims and to compatriots on both sides of the Strait as soon as possible; otherwise, the DPP authorities will bear all consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620411.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Lan Mo-ke, Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs and Coordinator for China Affairs at the US Department of State, recently claimed that “China is distorting UN General Assembly Resolution 2758,” and that the aim is to “isolate Taiwan” in the international community and restrict Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system or other international organizations. He also said…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, confirm China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. In 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all the lawful rights of the People’s Republic of China in the United Nations and to recognize the representatives of the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China at the United Nations. This thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all of China, including Taiwan, at the United Nations. The United Nations is an intergovernmental international organization composed of sovereign states, and Taiwan, being part of China, is simply not qualified to join. Taiwan’s participation in the activities of international organizations must be handled under the one-China principle.\nRecently, some people in the United States have repeatedly tried to twist General Assembly Resolution 2758, which fully exposes their contempt for history and their malicious intent. The U.S. side does not abide by international law or the basic norms of international relations, and has repeatedly distorted and challenged the authority of General Assembly Resolution 2758. This fully proves that it ignores historical and legal facts and is confronting the international community, and that it runs counter to the solemn political commitments the U.S. government itself made in the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués through concrete actions, to implement its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620414.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Reports indicate that US President Biden recently signed into law a foreign military aid package that includes military aid to Taiwan. The DPP authorities have expressed gratitude. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this move by the US side. The US side should fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete action, stop arming Taiwan in any way, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. In order to pursue the private interests of one party, the DPP authorities are willing to serve as pawns of external forces in “using Taiwan to check China,” and they are bringing Taiwan into a dangerous situation. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: their attempts to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “seek independence by force” are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240515_12620410.htm"],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Some media reported that the tourism authorities of the DPP authorities operate accounts on mainland social media platforms such as Weibo and WeChat to market Taiwan tourism, and this year they plan to open an account on Xiaohongshu. Some Taiwan residents say the DPP authorities are applying “double standards.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","As you said, the DPP authorities' approach is an out-and-out “double standard.” The scale and dividends of the mainland tourism market are enormous, and no person or institution can ignore them. On one hand, the DPP authorities try to conceal things and attempt to enjoy the dividends of cross-Strait relations, while on the other hand they disregard public opinion, go back on their word, and act obstinately, continuously creating obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and contacts and harming the interests and well-being of cross-Strait industries and the public. We advise them to change course as soon as possible, to truly keep the interests and well-being of the island's industries and public at heart, and to take concrete actions to create conditions for the normal resumption of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","Aquilino, the recently retired commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, said in an interview, “Taiwan should emulate Israel,” and that Taiwan mobilized 360,000 people in one day to respond to “military operations the PLA may launch against Taiwan at any time.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. Some anti-China forces in the United States previously hyped “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow,” and now clamor for “Taiwan to emulate Israel,” sending an extremely dangerous signal. Facts prove that wherever the United States fans the flames, that place suffers. Their attempt to copy this familiar playbook to Taiwan again exposes their sinister intent to exploit Taiwan, drain Taiwan, and sacrifice Taiwan.\nThe United States always adheres to “America First,” and a “chess piece” can become a “discarded piece” at any time. Whether the United States is “supporting Taiwan” or “harming Taiwan,” and whether the DPP authorities are “safeguarding Taiwan” or “bringing disaster to Taiwan,” we believe the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will have a clear understanding and rational judgment. Only by resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively maintained, and only then can the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the development prospects of Taiwan be effectively guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Recently, Fu Kun-chi, Whip of the KMT Caucus in the Legislative Yuan, demanded that the DPP change “China” to “Mainland” in its proposal wording, which has been widely endorsed by island public opinion and the public. What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact. The practices of the relevant persons you mentioned are reasonable and lawful, and set things right at the root, and they naturally receive the support of mainstream public opinion on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","The mainland recently announced that it will take the lead in resuming tourism from Fujian residents to Matsu. Public opinion and industry on the island praised this as a “timely rain” for Taiwan's tourism industry, and hope that the DPP authorities will respond actively, seize the opportunity, and return cross-Strait tourism to normal as soon as possible. However, the DPP authorities said that “cross-Strait…","On April 28, a responsible person from the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced arrangements for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan while meeting with a visiting delegation of Kuomintang public representatives led by Mr. Fu Kun-chi. This is a concrete measure to implement the important remarks made by General Secretary Xi Jinping when he met with Ma Ying-jeou and his delegation. It is also a positive response to the expectations of Taiwan's public and tourism industry for the resumption of cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and it has been welcomed by the public and industry on the island.\nThe DPP authorities, out of political self-interest and disregarding the wishes and interests of the island's industry and public, can only smear and attack the mainland, which does not win public support. We advise them to heed the strong calls of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait for normalized personnel exchanges and regularized exchanges in all fields, and to lift the various unreasonable restrictions and bans as soon as possible, creating conditions for the normal resumption of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: the spokesperson just mentioned that the mainland will introduce legal measures to punish “Taiwan independence” diehards. When exactly will these be introduced at the earliest, and what specific measures will they include? Second question: regarding Lai Ching-te's “May 20” inaugural speech, what does the mainland want to say to Lai Ching-te? What does the mainland want to hear? Lai has repeatedly…","Question one: Regarding the national legal measures to punish “Taiwan independence,” please wait and see the specific content of the measures.\nQuestion two: Regarding the inaugural speech of the new leader of the Taiwan region, I have already answered a similar question earlier. I wish to emphasize again that as long as any political party in Taiwan acknowledges the one-China principle, there are no obstacles to its engagement with us. As long as the DPP abandons its “Taiwan independence” position, dialogue and exchanges can proceed.\nQuestion three: Fujian Province will organize travel agency survey groups to visit Matsu at an appropriate time.\nQuestion four: Applying online to renew the Mainland Resident Travel Permit for Taiwan is a practical measure to facilitate travel by mainland residents. As for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced relevant arrangements on April 28.\nQuestion five: These two departmental rules are powerful measures by the National Security Agencies to implement the national strategy of comprehensively advancing the rule of law. They are of great significance for lawfully combating illegal and criminal activities, strictly regulating and fairly and civilly enforcing the law, and protecting the lawful rights and interests of individuals and organizations.\nThe mainland side has consistently encouraged and supported exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, actively promoted exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, and protected the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with law. The DPP authorities maliciously hype this up, deceive and intimidate the people of Taiwan, and interfere with and obstruct normal exchanges across the Strait. This does not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Alperovitch, a think-tank scholar who once served as an adviser to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense, recently published an article advocating means such as “sabotaging TSMC equipment” to make the Chinese mainland understand that “armed invasion of Taiwan” cannot gain TSMC. Some pan-green media on the island claim that this is the United States “protecting Taiwan.” What is…","For some time, American anti-China forces have treated TSMC as a “weapon” and as “cannon fodder,” repeatedly floating remarks such as “blow up TSMC,” “sabotage TSMC's equipment,” and “remotely paralyze TSMC.” This thoroughly exposes their base mindset and evil nature. The US always puts “American interests” first. It is not only TSMC; everything about Taiwan is, in their eyes, something that can be discarded at any time.\nRelevant Green camp media's forced twisting of the US's remarks about “destroying Taiwan” into “protection” is an insult to the intelligence of Taiwan's people. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to see that the deeper “reliance on the US” goes, the more severe the “destruction of Taiwan” becomes, which will only plunge Taiwan's people into profound disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","On the first question: Cheng Wen-tsan and Chiu Chui-cheng will take up the posts of Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation and Head of the Mainland Affairs Council, respectively. Cheng Wen-tsan said that the foundation's establishment and operations are based on the relevant regulations of Taiwan, and that he will handle related matters in accordance with them. Chiu Chui-cheng said that if negative factors…","First question: The Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan were born under a One-China framework in response to exchanges among the people on both sides of the Strait. They should play a positive role in developing cross-Strait relations and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides, rather than undermining the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and placing obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. As long as they acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China principle, cross-Strait relations can return to the correct track of peaceful development.\nSecond question: The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) remains committed, as always, to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the process of peaceful reunification of the country. It continues to play a positive role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields and in safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体记者","First question: The Hu surnamed angler from Kinmen who was rescued earlier is still on the mainland. He himself has applied for voluntary discharge, which took effect at 0:00 on May 8. Does this help bring this case to a swift conclusion, and what is the current status of the investigation? Second question: Where is the crux of the reason the “2·14” serious ship collision incident has still not been resolved?","First question: relevant information is still being verified. Second question: the crux of why the “2·14” malicious ship collision incident has not been properly resolved is that relevant departments of the DPP authorities have gone back on their word and shirked responsibility, creating obstacles to post-incident consultations. We urge the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation and promptly show sincerity and take concrete actions to solve the problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Reportedly, the Taiwan People’s Party plans to hold a rally on the 19th to “settle accounts” with the DPP authorities by sorting out the policies they have failed to deliver. It said, “The DPP that started out in straw sandals has long since disappeared; the DPP now is only bound up with corruption.” What is your comment?","The people have a scale in their hearts. Over the past eight years, the DPP authorities have been arrogant, domineering, and have acted in defiance of the trend of history. Livelihood problems on the island have emerged one after another, and corruption and collusion between black-gold forces and officials have occurred frequently. The great majority of Taiwan compatriots are strongly dissatisfied, and this is something the DPP's various lies and deceptions cannot cover up.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","Wu Chao-hsieh, who is about to take office as Secretary-General of Taiwan’s “National Security Council,” recently published an op-ed in a U.S. media outlet claiming that Taiwan Strait peace must be regarded as an “international issue” for cross-Strait relations to “stably safeguard the status quo.” In addition, last month the United States and Taiwan conducted a “joint military exercise.” What is your comment?","The Taiwan question concerns China's core interests. We firmly oppose, and will never allow, any external interference. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related matters with caution.\nWu Chao-hsieh is a stubborn “Taiwan independence” die-hard, and everyone can clearly see his face of seeking independence. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how hard you scheme to win over external forces to seek independence and provoke, you cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can you change the outcome that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: You just mentioned that “famous commentators” in Taiwan would be punished. Many of them are not Taiwan officials, and Taiwan protects freedom of speech. Will such punishment make the distance between the people on both sides of the Strait grow ever larger? Second question: Fu Cha (Li Yanhe), chief editor of Eight Banners Culture, was detained by Shanghai State Security authorities in March last…","First question: Public opinion is not a place beyond the law, and freedom of speech is not a talisman or shield for committing wrongdoing.\nSecond question: Regarding the case of the person you mentioned, the relevant departments will handle it in accordance with the law.\nThird question: We have already commented many times on cross-Strait relations over the past eight years. Since 2016, the DPP authorities have stubbornly persisted in the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. They have deliberately escalated cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, extensively colluded with external forces to carry out provocations for independence, and continuously escalated tension and volatility in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-15","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","First question: since taking office, the DPP authorities have constantly engaged in “de-Sinicization.” In recent years, news of damage to artifacts at the National Palace Museum in Taipei has frequently emerged. What comments does the spokesperson have? Second question: after six years of renovation, the Taiwan History Museum has reopened, and during this period its original Suzhou garden landscape was replaced…","Question one: We express serious concern about this matter. Chinese precious cultural relics are treasures of the Chinese nation, witnesses to and carriers of China's long history and brilliant culture. They bear the cultural lineage and historical bonds that cannot be severed between the two sides, and embody the shared humanistic sentiments of the Chinese people. Ensuring the safety of these relics is the basic responsibility of the relevant parties in Taiwan.\nQuestion two: Figures and public opinion from all walks of life on the island have already raised questions and expressed opposition. I want to emphasize that any \"de-Sinicization\" schemes cannot erase the imprint of Chinese culture on Taiwanese society, nor can they dilute the Chinese national identity of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will consciously act as guardians and inheritors of Chinese culture.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240515_12620401.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-16","Wang Wenbin","Kyodo News","It’s reported that former Japanese Prime Minister Taro Aso met yesterday with visiting Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an in Tokyo and they discussed people-to-people exchanges between Japan and Taiwan. What’s your comment?","China’s position on the Taiwan region’s external exchanges is consistent and clear, that is, they must be handled in line with the one-China principle. We urge Japan to abide by the principles and spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and act on its commitment of adhering to the one-China principle and only maintaining people-to-people and sub-regional exchanges with Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347757.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240516_11305611.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-17","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","It’s reported the Taiwan authorities have long been bribing Guatemala’s President and resorting to “dollar diplomacy” in exchange for political support. The Taiwan authorities have recently taken similar moves on Guatemala again. But the office of Guatemala’s President indicated that President Bernardo Arévalo might decline attending the so-called “inauguration ceremony” on May 20. What’s your comment?","To squander taxpayers’ money for “dollar diplomacy” is the DPP authorities’ go-to tactic to buy foreign politicians’ presence to keep up appearance. Such moves are designed to serve “Taiwan independence” separatism and personal political calculations. Ultimately it’s the interests of the people in Taiwan that will suffer. Facts show that the DPP authorities’ “dollar diplomacy” not only brings no good to the development of relevant countries, but breeds corruption. We believe the government and people of Guatemala are clear-eyed about this.\nWe reiterate that upholding the one-China principle is the right thing to do and is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. This is not something you can put a price on. We hope and believe that Guatemala will make the right decision as early as possible that follows the prevailing trend and serves the interest of its people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347758.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240517_11306433.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-05-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the US guided-missile destroyer “Halsey” recently transited the Taiwan Strait and then rushed into China's Xisha territorial waters. It claimed that the establishment of straight baselines around the Xisha Islands under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea is illegal, and said the US will sail, fly, and operate wherever international law permits. What is your comment?","Regarding the U.S. warship’s passage through the Taiwan Strait, its unauthorized entry into the Xisha inland waters and territorial sea, and its public hype, we are strongly dissatisfied and firmly oppose them. We have lodged stern representations with the United States, and the spokespersons of the Eastern Theater Command and the Southern Theater Command have also responded.\nUnder the current situation in the Taiwan Strait, the United States has deliberately created provocations and trouble, threatening China’s sovereignty and security, sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and undermining regional peace and stability. The Xisha Islands are inherent Chinese territory. As early as 1996, the Chinese government publicly announced the baselines of the territorial sea of the Xisha Islands. These measures conform to international law and international practice. The United States is not a party to the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, yet it has repeatedly invoked the Convention and even dispatched warships to unlawfully enter the inland waters and territorial sea of the Xisha Islands. This is a provocative act that violates China’s sovereignty, threatens China’s national security, and endangers regional peace and stability, and it is a typical act of hegemony and bullying. The aforementioned erroneous conduct of the United States is not conducive to maintaining the stabilizing trend in China-U.S. relations between the two countries and their militaries. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army remains at a high state of alert at all times, resolutely counters any infringing and provocative acts, and firmly safeguards national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16309490.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to US media reports, the Taiwan authorities are seeking to increase the number of so-called military attachés at the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Office in Honolulu” from 4 to 10, in order to closely coordinate with the US Indo-Pacific Command and share intelligence. Other reports say Taiwan and the US Navy conducted joint military exercises in the Western Pacific in April. What comment do you have?","We have noted the relevant reports. The DPP authorities are colluding with external forces to stir up trouble, attempting to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” and “resist reunification by force,” which is doomed to fail. The U.S. side should fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, stop any form of official exchanges and military contacts with the Taiwan region of China, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and earnestly implement its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence.” The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests. The Chinese side will resolutely and decisively strike back against all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and any external connivance or support for them.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16309490.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-05-20","Wang Wenbin","Xinhua News Agency","Could you share with us more details about Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s visit to Tajikistan?","At the invitation of Tajikistan’s Minister of Foreign Affairs Sirojiddin Muhriddin, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi paid an official visit to Tajikistan. During the visit, Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with President of Tajikistan Emomali Rahmon and held talks with Minister of Foreign Affairs Muhriddin. The two foreign ministers signed cooperation documents between the two foreign ministries and jointly met the press.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi said during the meeting and talks that no matter how the international landscape may evolve, China will always be a trustworthy friend and partner for Tajikistan. China stands ready to work with Tajikistan to expand trade, unleash the potential in connectivity, promote cooperation in mineral resources, broaden cooperation in emerging areas, such as new energy and green transition, and help Tajikistan accelerate industrialization, upgrade socioeconomic development, embark on a successful path of development and rejuvenation and bring tangible benefits to the people of Tajikistan.\nTajikistan noted that China is its important strategic partner, and advancing its relations with China is a priority in its foreign policy. Tajikistan will, as always, firmly uphold the one-China principle, view Taiwan as an inalienable part of China’s territory, oppose “Taiwan independence” in any form and support the Chinese government’s effort to achieve national reunification.\nBoth sides are of the view that what China and Tajikistan have achieved together under the strategic guidance of President Xi Jinping and President Emomali Rahmon—establishing the comprehensive strategic partnership in the spirit of good-neighborliness and friendship, agreeing to, in line with the trend of the times, build a community for security, a community of development between China and Tajikistan, and, on that basis, a China-Tajikistan community with a shared future—is a vivid example of how neighbors can and should get along by embracing mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit. This is also a shining example of state-to-state relations. Looking to the future, the two sides need to focus on cooperation in the following areas. First, firmly support each other’s core interests. Second, continue to tap the great potential of mutually beneficial cooperation. Third, accelerate people-to-people and cultural exchanges. China welcomes Tajikistan’s 14-day visa-free policy for eligible Chinese citizens and looks forward to having more young people from Tajikistan to study in China. Fourth, firmly uphold regional security and stability and deepen counterterrorism cooperation. The two sides need to strengthen efforts to fight terrorism, separatism and extremism, step up border control, enhance exchange and consultation on efforts against foreign interference and jointly guard against “color revolution.” China supports the establishment of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) Anti-Drug Center in Dushanbe. Fifth, maintain close multilateral coordination. The two sides need to strengthen the China-Central Asia mechanism and make it a success, bolster coordination within the UN, the SCO and other multilateral frameworks, practice true multilateralism, and advocate an equal and orderly multipolar world and universally beneficial and inclusive economic globalization. Tajikistan will fully support China’s work as the next rotating chair of the SCO.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347759.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240520_11307868.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-20","Wang Wenbin","Anadolu Agency","Taiwan’s new leader Lai Ching-te was inaugurated today. And in his first speech, he said China and Taiwan are not subordinate to each other and emphasized Taiwan has sovereignty. What’s China’s comments?","I’d refer you to competent authorities on specific questions. Let me stress that “Taiwan independence” leads nowhere. No matter what banner or pretext the separatists use, “Taiwan independence” is doomed to failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347759.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240520_11307868.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-20","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","For some time, some in the US have been spreading claims that distort UNGA Resolution 2758, saying that the Resolution “did not make a determination on the status of Taiwan...and does not preclude Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is not a country. It has been an inalienable part of China’s territory since ancient times. The international community has long reached the conclusion on this. It is a vital component of the post-WWII international order. The 1943 Cairo Declaration explicitly demands that “all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Manchuria, Formosa, and the Pescadores, shall be restored” to China. The 1945 Potsdam Proclamation further stipulates that the “terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” Japan in both the 1945 Japanese Instrument of Surrender and the 1972 China-Japan Joint Communiqué pledged to observe the above-mentioned term of the Potsdam Proclamation. Be it in legal or factual terms, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China.\nUNGA Resolution 2758 settled the question of who shall represent the whole of China, that is, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN. The Resolution made it clear that there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China and a non-sovereign entity. It reaffirmed the one-China principle. Over the past half a century and more since the adoption of the Resolution, UN secretaries-general and their spokespersons, in their Taiwan-related remarks, have clearly stated the UN is guided by UNGA Resolution 2758 and committed to the one-China principle. The official legal opinions of the Office of Legal Affairs of the UN Secretariat made it pretty clear that Taiwan is “an integral part” of China and that “the United Nations considers ‘Taiwan’ as a province of China with no separate status.” The number of countries that have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle has jumped from over 60 to 183. This clearly demonstrates that the one-China principle is not only a prevailing international consensus, but also a basic norm of international relations.\nSome in the US claim that UNGA Resolution 2758 “did not make a determination on the status of Taiwan” and “does not preclude Taiwan’s meaningful participation in the UN system.” This is a lie. They are trying to reopen the closed case that Taiwan is part of China—a matter already settled by the international community once and for all—to deny UNGA Resolution 2758 and the one-China principle. This move that turns back the wheel of history is a challenge to not only China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also international justice and conscience and the post-WWII international order. This is extremely preposterous and dangerous.\nChina will and must achieve reunification. No one or force can hold it back. Our message to some in the US: The trend of the world is surging forward. Those who follow the trend will prosper; those who go against it will perish. Those who challenge the one-China principle will be swept away by the trend of the times; those who turn back the wheel of history will be run over by it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347759.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240520_11307868.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-20","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","At recent events for friendly exchanges, leaders from various countries and international organizations and people from various social sectors who are friendly towards China have openly stated their commitment to the one-China principle, support for China’s effort to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity, and opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference in China’s internal…","Over the past few days, leaders and political parties from countries that have diplomatic relations with China, people from various sectors friendly towards China and heads of major international organizations attended friendly exchange activities organized by China to review the journey of establishing diplomatic ties with China and achievements of cooperation with China. They all speak with a strong voice for the just commitment to the one-China principle and demonstrated a firm stance against “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference in the Taiwan question.\nThe one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community, a basic norm governing international relations and also the political foundation and premise for China to develop relations with countries in the world. Facts prove once and again that upholding the one-China principle is a universal consensus and is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. The overwhelming majority of countries and international and regional organizations in the world stand firmly with the Chinese government and people and support China’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” and promoting reunification.\nI want to stress that there is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. No matter what political changes may take place in Taiwan, it cannot change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, the world’s abiding commitment to the one-China principle, and still less the historical trend that China will and must achieve reunification.\nThe political manipulation and self-serving stunts on the Taiwan question by certain politicians in a handful of countries grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs and violate the one-China principle. China strongly condemns this and will take all necessary measures to firmly uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nNothing shall hold back the trend of history. The pursuit of “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. External interference in China’s internal affairs and encouragement and support for “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere. Using Taiwan to contain China is doomed to failure. The Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving for national reunification will enjoy wider and wider understanding and support from the international community. The day will come when China will be fully reunified.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347759.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240520_11307868.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-20","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","BEIJING, May 20 (Xinhua) — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded on the 20th to the content regarding cross-Strait relations in the “5·20” speech by the leader of the Taiwan region. He said that at present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause lies in the DPP's obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist…","Chen Binhua pointed out that the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Our resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is as firm as a rock, our ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is invincible, and our actions to oppose “Taiwan independence” secession and foreign interference are resolute and forceful. We will not tolerate or indulge any form of “Taiwan independence” secessionist conduct.\nChen Binhua said that the motherland must be reunified, and it will inevitably be reunified. No matter how the situation on the island changes and no matter who is in power, the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China cannot be changed, the basic framework and development direction of cross-Strait relations cannot be changed, and the historical trend of the eventual reunification of the motherland cannot be blocked. We will fully implement the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question, unwaveringly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, make efforts to promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240520_12621472.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-20","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 20th: The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, continue to carry out provocations for “independence” and expand so-called “international space.” Their actions completely depart from mainstream public opinion on the island and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan…","Chen Binhua pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The One-China Principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community, upheld and abided by by the vast majority of countries in the world. It is where righteousness lies and what the people's hearts desire. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and other countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China, and we strongly condemn their interference in Taiwan affairs by any means or under any pretext. We urge the United States and relevant countries to immediately correct their mistakes, abide by the One-China Principle and the serious political commitments they have made to China, handle the Taiwan question with prudence and appropriateness, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240520_12621528.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-21","Wang Wenbin","People’s Daily","Lately, leaders of many countries and international organizations reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle and support for China’s reunification. Can you give us more details and what’s your comment?","Over the past few weeks, leaders of many countries and international organizations have reaffirmed the commitment to the just cause of upholding the one-China principle, which shows that upholding the one-China principle is where global opinion trends.\nKazakh President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev said that Kazakhstan is firmly committed to the one-China principle and this position will never change. President of Uzbekistan Shavkat Mirziyoyev noted that the elections in the Taiwan region are China’s internal affair and other countries have no right to interfere or point fingers at it. He stressed once again that Uzbekistan’s commitment to firmly upholding the one-China principle will never waver. President of Kyrgyzstan Sadyr Japarov expressed firm support for China on issues concerning Taiwan, Xinjiang, Hong Kong and Xizang. Pakistan’s President Asif Ali Zardari said Pakistan firmly upholds the one-China principle and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, which is beyond any doubt. Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro noted there is but one China in the world and in the UN-centered international system. This is a fact that is beyond doubt. Any attempt to undermine the one-China principle is doomed to failure. Kiribati President and Foreign Minister Taneti Maamau stated support for the right position that China upholds on ensuring national reunification, sovereignty and territorial integrity and Kiribati’s commitment to UNGA Resolution 2758. The 33rd Ordinary Session of the Council of the League of Arab States at the Summit Level adopted a resolution reaffirming the commitment to the one-China principle. The Prime Minister of Guyana Mark Phillips noted he does not support Taiwan in joining any international organization that requires sovereign statehood or participating in international conferences. The Prime Minister of Tonga Hu’akavameiliku said Tonga is committed to the one-China principle and firmly supports UNGA Resolution 2758. Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov stated that on the Taiwan question, Russia supports China in realizing national reunification and this position is very clear. The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Serbia Marko Djuric said Serbia has only one policy on the Taiwan question, that is the sovereignty and territorial integrity of the friendly and brotherly China is inviolable. Serbia firmly supports the one-China principle, recognizes China within its full borders and believes that how to resolve issues including the Taiwan question is China’s own affair. Sri Lanka’s Speaker of Parliament Mahinda Yapa Abeywardana, Botswana’s Speaker of the National Assembly Phandu Tombola Chaka Skelemani, Lao Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Saleumxay Kommasith, Office of the Palestinian President, Iran’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs, as well as Director-General of the United Nations Office at Geneva, Director-General of the United Nations Office at Vienna, Secretary-General of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development, Director General of the International Atomic Energy Agency, Director General of the World Intellectual Property Organization, Secretary General of the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies, Executive Director of the South Centre and Secretary-General of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization openly reaffirmed their commitment to upholding the one-China principle, following the UNGA Resolution 2758 and opposing all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatism.\nAs Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi pointed out, the one-China principle cannot be violated, separatist attempts for “Taiwan independence” are doomed to fail and the general trend of China’s reunification is irreversible. Each time “Taiwan independence” separatists make waves, it reinforces the global consensus that the one-China principle must be upheld and garners understanding and support for China’s position—a good example of the old Chinese adage “a just cause enjoys the support of many.” The abiding commitment of the international community to the one-China principle is unshakable and the trend of the history of China realizing complete reunification is unstoppable. Anyone trying to challenge the one-China principle and hinder China’s reunification is attempting the impossible and will only wreck their own reputation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347760.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240521_11309084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-21","Wang Wenbin","Hubei Media Group","We noted lawmakers and former political figures from a handful of countries that have diplomatic relations with China attended the “inauguration ceremony” of Lai Ching-te or sent congratulations to Lai. What’s China’s comment?","China strongly opposes official interaction of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. This position is consistent and clear. The wrongful words and actions of a handful of countries and political figures violate the one-China principle and basic norms governing international relations, constitute blatant interference in China’s internal affairs, undermine the sovereignty and territorial integrity of China, and damage the peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China strongly condemns those words and actions.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation and prerequisite for China to grow ties with other countries. The definition of the one-China principle is very clear, that is, there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. We ask relevant countries and politicians to stop their political manipulation on the Taiwan question, stop sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatists, and stop those wrongdoings that breach its credibility among the international community and hollow out the one-China principle.\nAs I have said, over the past few days, political leaders and people from various sectors in many countries have reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle and firm support for China’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving for national reunification. The world has spoken up for justice. This once again demonstrates that the international community’s abiding commitment to the one-China principle is unshakable, the one-China principle must not be violated and the historical trend of China’s reunification cannot be reversed. To use Taiwan to contain China is to play with fire and will definitely backfire. China will take all necessary measures to firmly safeguard its interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347760.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240521_11309084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-21","Wang Wenbin","CRI","Could you share more details on Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s visit to Kazakhstan?","On May 20, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi paid an official visit to Kazakhstan. Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Kazakhstan’s President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev and held talks with Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Murat Nurtleu. The two foreign ministers signed a protocol with revisions of and supplements to the agreement on establishing the China-Kazakhstan Cooperation Committee and met the press together.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi said that under the personal guidance and efforts of President Xi Jinping and President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev, China and Kazakhstan forged a permanent comprehensive strategic partnership and, on that basis, decided to build a China-Kazakhstan community with a shared future, which have set the bar even higher, opened up new prospects and injected new impetus for bilateral relations. China stands ready to work with Kazakhstan to focus on implementing the common understandings reached by the two presidents, carry forward our traditional friendship, deepen mutually beneficial cooperation, and bring benefits to the two countries and peoples. Kazakhstan firmly upholds the one-China principle and supports China’s opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism and effort to achieve national reunification as early as possible. This is much appreciated by China. China will, as always, support Kazakhstan in safeguarding national independence, sovereignty, and territorial integrity, and oppose any interference in Kazakhstan’s internal affairs.\nThe Kazakhstan side noted that Kazakhstan is a good partner that China can always trust. Strengthening friendship with China is a priority in Kazakhstan’s foreign policy. The deep friendship between the two presidents is an engine for Kazakhstan-China friendship and cooperation, and has guided bilateral relations into another “golden 30 years.” Kazakhstan stands ready to work with China to strive for the sustained and fast growth of bilateral relations in the spirit of good-neighborliness, friendship and mutual respect. The Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative and the Global Civilization Initiative put forward by President Xi are conducive to global security and sustainable development. Kazakhstan commends and actively supports the three initiatives. Kazakhstan is firmly committed to the one-China principle and this position will never change.\nBoth sides are of the view that the Kazakhstan-China relations have followed the prevailing trend of the times. Our ever-lasting friendship, high-level mutual trust, and commitment to sharing weal and woe together have come to define our bilateral relations. The two countries agreed to continue to draw on the complementarity of each other’s industrial and market advantages, conduct high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, and create more favorable conditions to step up cooperation in China-Europe freight trains. Both sides believe that China-Kazakhstan people-to-people and cultural cooperation enjoys bright prospects and will make full use of Luban Workshop, Confucius Institute and other platforms, speed up the establishment of cultural centers in each other’s countries and build closer bonds and amity between the two peoples. Both sides commended the success of the China-Central Asia Summit in Xi’an. With the Secretariat of the China-Central Asia mechanism launched in Xi’an, we look to work with other Central Asian countries to strengthen the mechanism, make it a success, and provide a strong boost to building a closer China-Central Asia community with a shared future. Both sides stressed the importance to uphold the international system with the UN at its core and the international order underpinned by international law, implement the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative and the Global Civilization Initiative, unequivocally oppose unilateralism, hegemonism and bullying, and make global governance more just and equitable.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347760.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240521_11309084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-21","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","The US Secretary of State Antony Blinken has congratulated Taiwan’s new leader. Does the Ministry have any comment on this?","What the US has done seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and breaches its political commitment to maintaining only cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the Taiwan region. This sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and opposes it, and has made serious protests to the US.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests and is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. China firmly opposes official interaction in any form between Taiwan and the US and opposes US interference in Taiwan affairs in any form or under any pretext. We urge the US to correct its wrongdoing at once, act on President Biden’s commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and not using Taiwan as a tool to contain China, stop fudging and hollowing out the one-China principle, stop emboldening and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form and stop disrupting peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” leads nowhere and anyone who connives at and supports “Taiwan independence” is doomed to failure. No external interference can hold back the trend toward China’s reunification. Any attempt to challenge the one-China principle and endanger China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity will be met with China’s resolute response.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347760.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240521_11309084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-21","Wang Wenbin","Beijing Youth Daily","Recently, Taiwan’s “foreign affairs department” issued a statement protesting the mainland’s condemnation over the Taiwan authorities’ bribery of Guatemalan leaders and officials in exchange for political support. What’s your comment?","The facts and evidence on DPP authorities’ “dollar diplomacy” with Guatemala are clear and solid. Guatemala’s former president openly admitted that when in office, he had received bribery from the Taiwan authorities in exchange for maintaining so-called “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. Last year, Taiwan’s hospital project in Guatemala was involved in a corruption case. Relevant Guatemalan officials were put into jail. This is just one example of the Taiwan authorities’ “dollar diplomacy.” No matter how angrily they protest or try to deny it, the fact that they sought political support through “dollar diplomacy” will not change.\nAround the world, 183 countries have established diplomatic ties with China. That proves the DPP authorities’ reckless pursuit of “Taiwan independence” and secession to be futile and self-deceptive. Whatever the DPP authorities does, it will not shake the one-China principle, and will not hinder the unstoppable trend toward China’s reunification. We hope that Guatemala and the very few other countries will come to recognize where the trend leads and make the right decision soon.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347760.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240521_11309084.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-21","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council Answers Reporters’ Questions\n(May 21, 2024)\nQuestion: Yesterday, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, in a spokesperson’s statement, characterized the “May 20” speech by the leader of the Taiwan region as sending dangerous signals of seeking “independence” and provocation, and as fully exposing the nature of “Taiwan independence.” Could the spokesperson elaborate on this?\nAnswer:\nThe speech by the leader of the Taiwan region yesterday was filled from beginning to end with hostility and provocation, lies and deception. Its “Taiwan independence” position has become even more radical and reckless. It loudly promoted separatist fallacies such as so-called “sovereign independence,” “no subordinate relationship between the two sides of the Strait,” and “self-determination of Taiwan residents,” and desperately begged external forces for backing and encouragement, attempting to push for the “internationalization of the Taiwan question,” continuing to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” It can be described as a thoroughgoing “confession of Taiwan independence.” This fully proves that it is a betrayer of mainstream public opinion on the island and a saboteur of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the region.\nIn the speech, the leader of the Taiwan region deliberately packaged and, in an attempt to cover up, declared that “the Republic of China on Taiwan is a sovereign and independent country,” that “the Republic of China and the People’s Republic of China are not subordinate to each other,” and that Taiwan is “the name of our country.” This is peddling the “two-state theory” and pursuing “Taiwan independence” rebranding. It shows that, at the very outset of taking office, it hastily revealed its true “Taiwan independence” face, with an extremely arrogant attitude and increasingly radical positions. It must be pointed out that Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times; its historical lineage is clear and its legal and factual basis is well established. The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The leader of the Taiwan region not only failed to answer the fundamental question of the nature of cross-Strait relations, but also sought to change the nature of cross-Strait relations. This is a serious provocation against the one-China principle.\nIn the speech, the leader of the Taiwan region advocated that “the future of the Republic of China on Taiwan will be decided jointly by 23 million people,” using “self-determination of Taiwan residents” to conceal its “Taiwan independence” ambitions. It must be pointed out that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and its future can only be decided jointly by more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan.\nIn the speech, the leader of the Taiwan region boasted of Taiwan’s “strategic position on the ‘First Island Chain’,” calling it “a highlight of the ‘world democratic chain’,” “the key to the global democratic supply chain,” and “Taiwan of the world.” Its purpose is simply to beg external forces to support and encourage its provocative “independence” schemes, and to wholeheartedly serve as the “vanguard” and “spearhead” of external forces in containing China’s development. It must be pointed out that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan, the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and foreign interference will not be tolerated. No matter how servilely the leader of the Taiwan region begs external forces for favor and help, it is merely a “pawn.” “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” will only lead to self-inflicted disaster, and the “pawn” will inevitably become a “discarded pawn.”\nIn the speech, the leader of the Taiwan region strongly played up the mainland’s “threat” and “gray coercion,” and agitated for “raising the awareness of all people to defend the country and their homes,” “strengthening national defense capabilities,” and “exerting deterrence.” It must be pointed out that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and belong to the same Chinese nation. No one hopes more than we do to achieve national reunification through peaceful means. However, in response to the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to carry out provocations to seek “independence,” we must counter and punish. The leader of the Taiwan region incited “anti-China” sentiment, attempting to “seek independence by force,” which will only push Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war and calamity, bringing profound disaster to the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan.\nIn the speech, the leader of the Taiwan region, under the banner of “peaceful coexistence and common prosperity,” spoke empty words about “replacing confrontation with dialogue and containment with exchanges,” and claimed that tourism exchanges and students coming to Taiwan for study could be resumed across the Strait, causing some who do not understand the situation to mistakenly believe that it has goodwill and sincerity in improving cross-Strait relations. It must be pointed out that the fact that mainland residents and students cannot travel to or study in Taiwan was entirely caused by the DPP authorities. Not only has the leader of the Taiwan region failed to repent, but it has also attached the precondition of “bilateral reciprocity” to tourism and study. Where is the sincerity in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and improving the island’s economy and people’s livelihoods in this?\nI must emphasize that no matter what he says or how he says it, it cannot change the status of Taiwan as part of China or the facts; it cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-Strait relations; it cannot change the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides to draw closer and grow ever closer; and it certainly cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified. Complete reunification of the motherland must be achieved, and it will certainly be achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240521_12621863.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-22","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the meeting of the SCO Foreign Ministers Council yesterday. Can you share more details with us?","On May 21 local time, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the Meeting of the Council of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization Member States in Astana, the capital of Kazakhstan.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi noted that the Shanghai Spirit of mutual trust, mutual benefit, equality, consultation, respect for diversity of civilizations and pursuit of common development has become a fundamental guidance for the SCO to grow from strength to strength and a banner in building a new type of international relations. The more fluid and turbulent the world is, the more important that we stay committed to the Shanghai Spirit, keep to the right direction, and safeguard common interests, respond to various challenges and uphold fairness and justice more effectively through making the SCO more substantive and stronger.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi made four proposals. First, uphold strategic independence, maintain solidarity and coordination, and never allow external forces to turn the region into an arena for geopolitical games. Second, jointly protect security and guard against risks, step up coordination, follow the guidance of the Global Security Initiative, and make relentless effort to safeguard world peace. Third, work for universal benefit and achieve development through cooperation. China stands ready to work with all parties to enable high-quality synergy between the Belt and Road Initiative and the development strategies of all SCO member states, and create more opportunities for development. Fourth, uphold openness and inclusiveness, deepen exchanges and mutual learning, respect each unique civilization, and deepen mutual understanding among people of various countries.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stated China’s solemn position on the Taiwan question. He noted that the Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the biggest disrupting factor to cross-Strait peace. Those like Lai Ching-te have betrayed their nation and ancestors. What they have done is simply disgraceful. No matter what gimmicks they play, they will not stop China’s complete reunification and Taiwan’s return to the embrace of the motherland. All “Taiwan independence” separatists will see their names written on the wall of shame. China appreciates SCO member states’ firm commitment to the one-China principle. We believe SCO member states will continue to support the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and striving for national reunification.\nForeign ministers attending the meeting spoke highly of the role and development achievements of the SCO. They agreed that in face of the complex international and regional landscape, member states need to carry forward the Shanghai Spirit, tap the potential for cooperation, uphold openness and inclusiveness, step up cooperation in political, economic and security areas, promote connectivity, work for common development and prosperity, and make new contribution to world peace and sustainable development. The foreign ministers condemned all forms of terrorism, and agreed to intensify fighting against terrorism, separatism and extremism, and safeguard peace and stability in the region. Parties expressed the belief that we need to address hotspot issues through political and diplomatic means, respect countries’ sovereignty and territorial integrity, uphold the authority of the UN Charter, oppose unilateralism, and build a multipolar world.\nThe meeting made full preparation for the meeting of the SCO Council of Heads of State in Astana in July.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347761.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240522_11309860.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-22","Wang Wenbin","Global Times","Pakistani President Asif Ali Zardari stated during a recent interview that Pakistan firmly upholds the one-China principle and stressed that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. What’s your comment?","President Zardari has, on behalf of Pakistan, reaffirmed Pakistan’s firm commitment to the one-China principle and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” His remarks reflect the firm support for China’s legitimate stance and, more importantly, the common aspiration of countries that uphold fairness and justice, and fully demonstrate that the commitment to the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. China commends President Zardari for his remarks.\nChina and Pakistan are all-weather strategic cooperative partners and ironclad friends. We will firmly support each other on issues concerning our respective core interests and major concerns, and jointly build a closer China-Pakistan community with a shared future.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347761.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240522_11309860.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","AFP","About the military exercises that China is currently conducting around Taiwan. The US General has said today these military drills are concerning. What’s your reaction to these comments from the US side?","The PLA Eastern Theater Command has issued a press release about the joint drills, which you may refer to. The joint drills of the PLA Eastern Theater Command are a necessary and legitimate move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist moves and send a warning to external interference and provocation. It is fully consistent with international law and common practices.\nI need to stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is both a fact based on history and the true status quo, and it will remain so in the future. “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail. The Chinese people will not be deterred from defending our sovereignty and territorial integrity. The 1.4 billion strong Chinese people will resolutely push back any separatist activity for “Taiwan independence”. Anyone seeking “Taiwan independence” will find themselves crushed by the historic trend of China’s complete reunification.\nWe urge the US to stop conniving at or supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and stop meddling in China’s internal affairs. Any attempt to endanger China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity will be met with China’s resolute response.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","China has launched what it calls “punishment” drills around Taiwan today and tomorrow. I have a few questions. Would China announce any no-fly or no-entry zones during the drills? And has China informed foreign countries, airlines or ships about the drills?","The PLA Eastern Theater Command has issued a press release about the joint drills, which you may refer to. The joint drills of the PLA Eastern Theater Command are a necessary and legitimate move to crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their separatist activities and send a warning to external interference and provocations. It is fully consistent with international law and common practices.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","TV Asahi","Yesterday, Director-General of the MFA Department of Asian Affairs Liu Jinsong met with Chief Minister of the Embassy of Japan Akira Yokochi. On the Taiwan question, what did the Chinese side say? What was the position that was expressed?","We have released a readout on the meeting between Director-General Liu Jinsong and Chief Minister of the Embassy of Japan, which you may refer to. Japan has repeatedly made negative moves on the Taiwan question, and China has made serious protests and expressed our serious position. We urge the Japanese side to abide by the principles and spirits of the four political documents between China and Japan and fulfill its commitment to the one-China principle with concrete actions. The Japanese side should not connive at or support “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form and should safeguard cross-Strait peace and stability, rather than doing the opposite.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","China Review News","It’s reported Michael McCaul, the chairman of the foreign affairs committee in the US House of Representatives, said he will lead a delegation to visit Taiwan at the end of May and congratulate Taiwan’s “new leader” on his inauguration. What’s China’s comment?","China firmly opposes official interaction in any form between Taiwan and the US and opposes US interference in Taiwan affairs in any form or under any pretext. The US Congress is part of the US government and supposed to strictly adhere to the one-China policy followed by the US. Any visit by congressional members to Taiwan will seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, interfere in China’s internal affairs, undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and send a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nChina urges the US to seriously abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, not arrange for any visit by members of the Congress to Taiwan, stop official interaction with Taiwan, stop creating tensions in the Taiwan Strait and act on the US commitment to maintaining only cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the Taiwan region and not supporting “Taiwan independence”. Otherwise, all consequences arising therefrom must be borne by the US.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","On May 20, Chinese Ambassador to Japan Wu Jianghao sent a serious warning to the Japanese side over its recent negative moves on the Taiwan question. Wu said that “If Japan ties itself onto the chariot of splitting China, the Japanese people will be led into a pit of fire.” It’s reported that on May 22, Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshimasa Hayashi said that Wu’s remarks were “extremely inappropriate.” What’s…","The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. It bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and is a red line that must not be crossed. Some in Japan have been making negative moves on Taiwan, including repeating the preposterous and dangerous notion that “any contingency for Taiwan is a contingency for Japan”, which seriously violates the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan and the commitments Japan has made.\nAmbassador Wu Jianghao categorically and rightfully stated China’s position. They are based on facts and the intention is sincere and earnest. His words are entirely proper and necessary. Let me stress once again that no one should underestimate the resolve, will and ability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Anyone bent on interfering in China’s internal affairs and holding back China’s reunification will pay a heavy price.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-23","Wang Wenbin","Reuters","After the drills around Taiwan this week, is China planning more “punishment” drills of such? And also does China plan to escalate its drills further?","Each time “Taiwan independence” separatists make waves, it garners stronger effort from China and the rest of the world to defend the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347762.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240523_11310575.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-23","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华23日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 23 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 23rd and pointed out that the PLA's “Joint Sword-2024A” exercise around Taiwan island is a resolute punishment for the provocative “independence”-seeking remarks in the Taiwan region leader's “May 20” speech. It is a stern warning to external forces that condone…","Chen Binhua pointed out that as soon as the leader of the Taiwan region took office, he openly challenged the one-China principle, brazenly peddled the “two-state theory,” and attempted to push the Taiwan question toward “internationalization,” continuing to “seek independence by relying on outside forces” and “seek independence by force,” trying to push Taiwan onto a dead end. In response, we will absolutely not tolerate it, will not show leniency, and will not leave any room whatsoever for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. If the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces persist in their course, or even take a desperate gamble, we will take decisive action and resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, firmly defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nChen Binhua said that reunification is the trend of history and the right path for humanity, while “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent that goes against the will of the people. We must uphold the right path and stop the countercurrent. It must be pointed out that all our countermeasures are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and are by no means aimed at the broad Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots will firmly stand on the right side of history, be upright and proper Chinese, clearly distinguish right from wrong, act in accordance with justice, and join mainland compatriots in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, and firmly safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240523_12622467.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-24","Wang Wenbin","CCTV","The 77th World Health Assembly (WHA) will open on May 27. We learned that many countries have expressed support for China’s position on Taiwan-related issues at the WHA. What’s China’s comment?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, is consistent and clear. It must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. This is a fundamental principle reaffirmed in UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nFor eight consecutive years from 2009 to 2016, China made special arrangement for the Taiwan region’s participation in the WHA on the basis of the adherence of both sides of the Taiwan Strait to the one-China principle. After coming into power in 2016, the DPP has refused to recognize the 1992 Consensus, which embodies the one-China principle, and has been hellbent on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence.” As a result, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. To uphold the one-China principle and the sanctity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China has decided not to approve the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA. This decision received extensive support and understanding from the international community. Over the past few weeks, the overwhelming majority of countries have reaffirmed to China their commitment to UNGA Resolution 2758, firm support for the one-China principle and opposition to Taiwan’s participation in the WHA. Over 100 countries wrote to the WHO Director-General or expressed via other means their support for China’s position. It once again proves that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends, and shows that the vast majority of countries uphold the just position on Taiwan-related issues at the WHA. A just cause enjoys the support of many. The abiding commitment of the international community to the one-China principle is unshakable. The “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda will not succeed. Any attempt that runs contrary to the one-China principle or to play the “Taiwan card” and engage in political manipulation is bound to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347763.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240524_11311210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-24","Wang Wenbin","AFP","The Philippines said today it has opened a coast guard post in the north of the country. They said it’s a response to what they call “China’s military buildup” near Taiwan over the past two years. What’s your response to that?","I’m not familiar with what you said. We urge the Philippines to stay committed to the one-China principle and stay prudent when it comes to the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347763.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240524_11311210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-24","Wang Wenbin","AFP","A question on Guatemala. The Guatemalan Exporters Association said yesterday that China banned the entry of Guatemala’s coffee and macadamia nuts. Is this true? If it’s true, what’s the reasons for the ban?","There’s no diplomatic relations between China and Guatemala. I’ve not heard of what you said.\nWhat I will say is that there is only one China in the world. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. It is also the fundamental prerequisite for China to carry out cooperation with all countries including Guatemala.\nPresident Bernardo Arévalo of Guatemala met with the Taiwan region’s leader via video link this week and Minister of Foreign Affairs of Guatemala Carlos Ramiro Martínez went to Taiwan to attend the so-called “inauguration ceremony” on May 20. These moves trample on the one-China principle. We condemn those moves. Such situation is not conducive to the cooperation between Guatemala and China, including Guatemala’s export to China. We hope relevant officials will recognize the trend of the world and proceed from the interests of the country and the people to make the right decision soon which serves its people’s interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347763.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240524_11311210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-24","Wang Wenbin","AFP","Another question on the military drills around Taiwan. The US’s high official yesterday strongly urged China to act with restraint. What’s your reaction to these US remarks?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. The US is in no position to point its fingers at China. The tensions in the Taiwan Strait are caused by the DPP authorities’ attempt to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence” and the attempt of some in the US to use Taiwan to contain China in the name of regional peace and stability. If the US truly wants to keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, it should unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence”. China will never tolerate any attempt by anyone to provide an umbrella for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities under whatever pretexts. The world has spoken up for justice. Over the past few days, political leaders and people from various sectors in many countries have reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle and support for China’s opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and the cause for national reunification. This once again demonstrates that the international community’s abiding commitment to the one-China principle is simply unshakable.\nAttempts for “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere. Anyone who connives at and supports “Taiwan independence” will get burned for playing with fire. Nothing will deter China from upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We will do anything necessary to thwart any attempt for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347763.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240524_11311210.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-05-24","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the Eastern Theater Command conducted joint exercises around Taiwan island. A U.S. official said this has aggravated tensions in the Taiwan Strait and is worrying. What is your response?","Recently, the Eastern Theater Command of the People’s Liberation Army organized land, naval, air, and rocket forces to conduct joint exercises around Taiwan island to test the combat capabilities of the joint forces. This action targets the arrogance of ‘Taiwan independence,’ and deters external forces from interfering and intervening. It is entirely reasonable, lawful, legitimate, and necessary.\nSince taking office, the leader of the Taiwan region has seriously challenged the one-China principle, openly peddled the ‘two-state theory,’ and schemed to ‘seek independence through force’ and ‘seek independence by relying on foreign powers,’ pushing Taiwan compatriots toward the perilous brink of war. This is playing with fire, and those who play with fire will burn themselves.\nTaiwan is Chinese Taiwan. How to resolve the Taiwan question is the internal affair of over 1.4 billion Chinese people. The People’s Liberation Army is safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity through concrete action. Each time ‘Taiwan independence’ provokes us, our countermeasures will advance one step further, until complete national reunification is achieved.","","http://www.news.cn/mil/2024-05/24/c_1212365434.htm","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-05-27","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","US lawmakers have expressed support for Taiwan’s defense. This is during a trip to the island just days after China ended military exercises there. For example, Representative Michael McCaul said that he would be calling on relevant parties to speed up arms shipments for the purposes of deterrence. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment on these remarks?","In disregard of China’s strong opposition, relevant members of the US Congress still decided to visit Taiwan, which violates the one-China principle, the three China-US joint communiqués, and the US government’s own political commitment to maintaining only unofficial relations with the Taiwan region, and sends a severely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes it and has made serious protests to the US. We will take necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes military contact between the US and Taiwan and any attempt to arm Taiwan. We urge relevant members of the US Congress to stop playing the “Taiwan card,” stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop supporting and conniving at “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop undermining China-US relations and cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347764.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240527_11312337.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-05-27","Mao Ning","Global Times","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a decision on its website on May 22 on countermeasures against 12 US defense corporations and 10 senior executives. Is this China’s response to US sanctioning of Chinese companies for Russia-related issues and the US side attending the “inauguration” of the leader of the Taiwan region?","China announced the relevant decision in the No.7 decree of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on May 22. China firmly opposes unilateral sanctions and long-arm jurisdiction that have no basis in international law or authorization of the UN Security Council. We will continue to take all measures necessary to protect our legitimate and lawful rights and interests. China urges the US to deeply reflect on its behavior, face up to its responsibility for the outbreak and escalation of the Ukraine crisis, stop vilification and pressuring, and stop abusing illicit unilateral sanctions.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. No country, organization or individual shall underestimate the strong determination, will and ability of the Chinese government and people in defending our nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, or imagine that they could step on or even cross the line on the Taiwan question without paying any price.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347764.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240527_11312337.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-27","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华27日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 27 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered a reporter's question on the 27th, pointing out that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. The 77th World Health Assembly's decision not to include Taiwan-related proposals on the assembly agenda once again shows that the international community's pattern of…","Chen Binhua said that compatriots in Taiwan are our own kin, and we have always kept the health and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots in our hearts. We will continue to effectively safeguard the health rights of Taiwan compatriots, including by arranging for medical technology experts from Chinese Taiwan to participate in WHO technical activities, and promptly notifying the Taiwan region, through relevant channels, of public health emergencies reported by the WHO.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240527_12623375.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-05-28","Mao Ning","Phoenix TV","It’s reported that the spokesperson of the US State Department issued a statement last weekend and expressed “concern over the People’s Liberation Army joint military drills around Taiwan.” What’s your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The US has no right to make irresponsible remarks on it. Our joint drills around the Taiwan island are a resolute punitive response to the provocation for “Taiwan independence” made by the leader of the Taiwan region in his May 20 speech and a serious warning to external forces that connive at and support “Taiwan independence” and interfere in China’s internal affairs. It is a just move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and is necessary, legitimate and fully consistent with international law and common practices.\nAfter coming into office, the Taiwan region’s leader did not even wait before laying bare his true identity as a separatist for “Taiwan independence.” His speech on May 20 is a declaration of his agenda for “Taiwan independence,” which fully reveals his nature as a “worker for Taiwanese independence.” What has happened shows once again that the most dangerous change to the cross-Strait status quo and the biggest source of damage to cross-Strait peace are the separatist moves for “Taiwan independence” and connivance and support from US-led external forces.\nIn disregard of China’s firm opposition, the US is the one that acted wrongly first by sending a delegation and issuing a congratulatory statement by the Secretary of State on the so-called “inauguration ceremony,” which sent a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The groundless accusation the US then made against China’s lawful and legitimate steps to uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity just compounded its mistake. We urge the US to fully recognize the fundamental nature and dangerous ambition of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and the grave harm and enormous risks of “Taiwan independence” separatism to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to China-US relations, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor the commitment made by US leaders on the Taiwan question and stop emboldening and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form.\nOur resolve to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity will not waver. Our determination to oppose external interference in China’s internal affairs will not change. “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere and anyone who plays with fire by supporting “Taiwan independence” will get burned. Anyone who seeks to challenge the one-China principle will invariably fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347765.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240528_11313156.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Hello everyone, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Lai Ching-te's “May 20” speech was filled with hostility and provocation, falsehoods and deception. The “Taiwan independence” stance has become even more radical and reckless. This has caused great concern in Taiwan society, which believes his speech, centered on “resisting China and seeking independence,” seriously undermines the prospects for peace in cross-Strait relations and may make the situation in the…","Lai Qingde's remarks are extremely arrogant in attitude and extremely vile in nature. They betray the great righteousness of the nation and defy the trend of popular sentiment. They are a blatant provocation to the One-China principle and a serious undermining of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If allowed to develop, they will surely lead to a deadly war in the Taiwan Strait and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. In response, we will absolutely not tolerate, absolutely not appease, and absolutely not stand idly by; we must counter and we must punish. The more blatant the provocation, the fiercer the countermeasures. If the DPP authorities insist on taking the dead-end road of “Taiwan independence,” they will surely bring disaster upon themselves and reap the consequences.\nOur will to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve national reunification is as firm as a rock. Our ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is invincible, and our actions to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference are resolute and forceful. No matter how the situation on the island changes and no matter who is in power, it cannot change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-Strait relations, and cannot stop the historical trend toward the eventual reunification of the motherland. We will fully implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, unwaveringly uphold the One-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, strive to promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and resolutely advance the great cause of reunifying the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623902.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","In Lai Ching-te’s “5·20” speech, he said that “in 1921, Chiang Wei-shui stated that Taiwan is the ‘guardian of the first gate of world peace,’” and also made statements with a strong “Taiwan independence historical view,” such as “in 1624, Taiwan set out from Tainan, marking the beginning of globalization.” What is your comment on this?","The historical and legal fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and must not be changed. The remarks in question are full of lies and deception, distort history by transplanting and twisting facts, and fully expose their “Taiwan independence” nature.\nMr. Chiang Wei-shui was one of the leaders of the anti-colonial movement during the period of Japanese colonial rule over Taiwan. He loudly proclaimed: “Taiwanese clearly belong to the Chinese nation” and “Compatriots must unite, for unity is powerful.” His aim was to resist Japanese colonial rule and fight for the freedom of the Chinese nation. Lai Ching-te and his ilk use Mr. Chiang Wei-shui's words to dress up their malicious scheme to “seek independence by relying on external powers.” This is a betrayal of the spirit of the Chinese nation and a desecration of Mr. Chiang Wei-shui.\nLooking back at history: in 1624, Dutch colonists invaded southern Taiwan and colonially ruled Taiwan for 38 years, until 1662, when the national hero Zheng Chenggong expelled the Dutch colonists and recovered Taiwan. In order to carry out “de-Sinicization,” Lai Ching-te and his ilk have used the humiliating history of Dutch colonization of Taiwan as a tool to promote a “Taiwan independence historical view.” They have forgotten their ancestors and cut off their own roots. They not only are ashamed before their forebears but are also sinners of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623897.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: In his “5·20” speech, Lai Ching-te said Taiwan is the “helmsman of peace,” that it will uphold the so-called “four insistences,” and that it will maintain the status quo. What is your comment? Second question: Recently, many Taiwanese entertainers have publicly expressed views such as “Chinese on both sides of the Strait are all part of the Chinese nation,” and they have been attacked by the green…","First question. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, the fact that the Mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China, has never changed and will not be changed.\nThe DPP authorities say they hope for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, but in fact they stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” position, incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and step up efforts to push “seeking independence by relying on external forces” and “seeking independence by force,” attempting to split Taiwan from China. What they are doing is not the “helmsman of peace” at all; it is clearly a “driver of war.”\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest source of turmoil, leading to war and danger on Taiwan, harm to the interests of the public, and instability in the situation across the Taiwan Strait. We hope broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will fully recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of the DPP's stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” line, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development, and safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.\nSecond question. As everyone has seen, in recent days nearly a hundred Taiwanese performing artists have expressed their attitudes toward cross-Strait relations and their identity as descendants of the Chinese nation in various ways. Some reposted the “Unification” poster first released by CCTV News; some told their fans about the origins of their ancestral homes and names that they learned from their elders; still others said that both sides are descendants of the Chinese nation and hoped for more exchanges. Taken together, these are a relay of expressions that both sides are Chinese. These are natural, sincere expressions of feeling.\nLai Ching-te and certain people in the DPP, out of political self-interest, have deliberately created cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and have pinned a so-called “forced declaration” label on these Taiwanese performing artists. This fully illustrates two points. First, the DPP authorities are very guilty and afraid that compatriots on both sides will draw closer and visit one another. They not only deliberately ignore the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that wants peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, but also suppress and slander in every way. Second, the DPP authorities are escalating the creation of a “green terror,” so that many people in Taiwan do not dare to speak their minds.\nWe actively support Taiwanese performing artists coming to the Mainland to take part in various performance activities, jointly promote the prosperous development of cross-Strait cultural markets, and promote emotional resonance and spiritual harmony among compatriots on both sides. We also welcome young friends from Taiwan to come to the Mainland to watch various performance activities and experience the wonderful life on the Mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623901.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》栏目记者","Although cross-Strait relations have been tense recently, quite a few Taiwan compatriots still come to the Mainland to take part in various exchange activities. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","Localities and departments across the country are implementing the spirit of the 2024 Cross-Strait Work Conference, continuously advancing cross-Strait exchanges and promoting the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Here we briefly introduce the main recent economic, trade and cultural exchange activities.\nIn terms of economic and trade exchanges, on May 9, the first cross-Strait ESG cooperation and exchange event was held in Zhenjiang, Jiangsu. More than 260 heads of relevant enterprises, financial institutions and industry associations, along with experts and scholars, focused on the theme of “Sustainable Development, Progress Through Innovation,” concentrating on green finance in the carbon market and the development and practice of green trading, to promote coordinated cross-Strait ESG development and explore cooperation in new quality productive forces. On May 16, the Taiwan Division of the 11th “Qingchuang Cup” Guangzhou Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition concluded successfully, with 56 Taiwanese youths registering to compete in 21 projects across industries including artificial intelligence, biopharmaceuticals and health, and intelligent connectivity. From May 24 to 27, the 7th Digital China Summit held in Fuzhou set up a “Cross-Strait Integration Zone” for the first time. The Fujian International Communication Center and the Beijing Cross-Strait Science and Technology Innovation Center organized nearly 20 Taiwan-invested enterprises with more than 50 projects to exhibit, showcasing innovative achievements in cross-border data flows, cross-Strait integrated intelligent computing, professional qualification certification, medical innovation cooperation, and joint scientific and technological research and development. From June 12 to 15, the “2024 Zhejiang·Taiwan Cooperation Week” will be held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang. Taiwan-related industrial and commercial groups, industry associations, enterprises, and representatives of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan youths, totaling more than 1,500 people, will carry out exchanges, seminars and cooperation around the theme of “new quality productive forces and Zhejiang-Taiwan integrated development.”\nIn terms of cultural exchanges, from May 16 to 18, the “2024 Changdao Xianyin Temple Mazu Spring Ceremony and Cross-Strait Prayer for Blessings Ceremony” was held in Yantai, Shandong, with more than 20 social organizations from both sides of the Strait and more than 200 temple representatives participating. From May 25 to 31, the cross-Strait media exchange event “Pursuing Chinese Modernization: Seeing Guizhou—Entering Zunyi” was held in Guizhou. Media professionals from both sides of the Strait conducted in-depth interviews and experiences through live broadcasts, short videos, and micro-videos, documenting changes in Guizhou’s economic and social development, tourism and culture, rural revitalization, and ethnic customs. On May 28, the Taiwan Youth Special Competition of the “New Era, I Will Speak” Guangzhou Outstanding Grassroots Speaker Competition was successfully held. Taiwanese university students studying at Sun Yat-sen University, Jinan University, and Guangzhou University of Chinese Medicine, along with Taiwanese youths in Guangzhou, competed on the themes of “Inheriting Excellent Traditional Lingnan Culture,” “Supporting Public Welfare and Volunteer Services,” and “Pursuing Dreams Through Employment and Entrepreneurship.” From May 30 to June 3, the 2nd “Rainbow Cloud Meeting” overseas Taiwan compatriots Yunnan tour activity will be held in Kunming, Baoshan, Xishuangbanna and other places in Yunnan, where compatriots from both sides will gather, share family ties, and discuss cooperation.\nIn terms of serving Taiwan youths, on May 23, the 2024 Beijing Job Fair Special Session for Taiwanese Students was successfully held in Beijing. The organizer offered Taiwanese job seekers 1,378 quality employment positions in popular industries including technology research and development, engineering management, artificial intelligence, and education and training. On May 25, the 19th Taiwan Talent Xiamen Matchmaking Event was held in Xiamen, where more than 280 Taiwanese professionals held talks and matchmaking with more than 50 employers, 9 Taiwan youth innovation and entrepreneurship bases, and 4 policy consulting institutions. As graduation season arrives, we welcome young Taiwanese students to come to the mainland to seek opportunities to realize their dreams, and we also encourage Taiwanese students studying on the mainland to stay and develop there. We will continue to provide support and opportunities for Taiwanese youths to intern, start businesses, and find employment on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623894.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","In his “5·20” speech, Lai Ching-te loudly touted Taiwan’s so-called “democratic achievements,” claiming Taiwan is a highlight of the “global democratic chain” and a “light of the world.” What is your comment?","In saying these things, Lai Ching-te is essentially peddling “Taiwan independence” under the guise of “democracy,” attempting to deceive the island's public, mislead international audiences, and seek political self-interest.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities use so-called “democracy” to package “separatism,” which is nothing more than an attempt to beg external forces to bolster and encourage their provocations to seek “independence,” serving as a “pawn” for external forces seeking to contain China's development. It must be pointed out that Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, admitting of no foreign interference. Attempting to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” will only bring bitter consequences, and the “chess piece” will inevitably become a “discarded piece.”\nUnder the banner of “democracy,” the Lai Ching-te authorities practice “green terror,” seriously harming the interests of the Taiwan people. They arbitrarily distort history, manipulate ethnic antagonism, and divide Taiwan society; they keep an online army, monopolize the media, control public opinion, and strive to suppress political opponents; they engage in rampant transactions of power for money, pursuing personal and party interests; they abuse administrative and judicial resources to intimidate and suppress people who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, creating a “chilling effect”; at the cost of the safety and well-being of the Taiwan people, they submit to the interests of anti-China external forces; they fabricate and direct a “cognitive warfare” farce, spread false information attacking and smearing the mainland, and incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation...... Is this what the Lai Ching-te authorities hold up as “democracy”?\nDifferences in systems are not an obstacle to reunification, much less an excuse for separation. Using “democracy” as packaging and borrowing “peace” as cover cannot conceal their “Taiwan independence” malicious intent. It will only cause enormous harm to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, push Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war, and bring profound disaster to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the Chinese nation, join hands with compatriots on the mainland, firmly uphold the one-China principle, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, firmly safeguard their own interests and well-being, and promote the return of cross-Strait relations to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623898.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","May the spokesperson please introduce the progress of work on building the Fujian Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone?","On building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in Fujian, on April 28, Fujian Province released 13 policy measures in three areas: facilitating Taiwan compatriots' exchanges, work, and daily life in Fujian; supporting the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises; and encouraging Taiwan compatriots to work, start businesses, and receive training and study in Fujian. The policy orientation emphasizes “convenience,” focusing on aspects closely tied to the daily lives of Taiwan compatriots to provide policy convenience. The policy benefits emphasize “practicality,” focusing on the actual needs and interests of Taiwan enterprises investing in Fujian and offering tangible, concrete policy preferences. Policy implementation emphasizes “efficiency”: when the policies were released, the service windows, contact persons, and contact information for each policy were also made public simultaneously, effectively promoting the efficient implementation of relevant policies.\nIn addition, the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone has continued to optimize its “One-Stop Government Service Platform for Taiwan Affairs,” creating, linking, and merging information from the Taiwan Residence Permit and the Taiwan Compatriot Travel Permit for Mainland China, becoming the first to achieve mutual recognition of the two Taiwan compatriot identity documents. It has expanded application scenarios of the Taiwan Residence Permit in government services, public services, and internet fields, sorting out 45 routine application scenarios across 3 categories in the first phase. It has achieved fully online handling of business registration for Taiwan compatriot-registered enterprises, launched a “one card for appointments, consultations, and payments, for convenient medical care” service for Taiwan compatriots, and installed 24-hour self-service all-in-one terminals in communities where Taiwan compatriots live. So far, it has served more than 2,300 person-times of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","On May 23 and 24, the PLA Eastern Theater Command organized land, naval, air, and rocket force units from the theater to conduct military exercises around Taiwan Island. Taiwanese media noted that the name of this exercise was “Joint Sword-2024A.” Does the spokesperson's “A” mean there will be a “B” or even a “C”? Will exercises of this scale become routine in the future?","The PLA's “Joint Sword-2024A” exercise around Taiwan island is a resolute punishment for the “May 20” speech by Taiwan's leader, which plotted “independence” and was provocative. It is a stern warning to external forces that condone and support “Taiwan independence” and interfere in China's internal affairs. It is a just action to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. As long as “Taiwan independence” provocations continue, the PLA's actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not stop for a moment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","On May 20, Lai Ching-te, leader of the Taiwan region, referred in his inaugural speech to the so-called “neither subordinate to each other” across the Taiwan Strait. According to a public opinion poll released by Taiwan media, 53% of the public has no confidence in the Lai authorities’ handling of cross-strait relations, higher than the 36% who have confidence. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","More than half of Taiwan's people lack confidence in how the DPP authorities handle cross-Strait relations. This reflects the public's worry and dissatisfaction with the Lai Ching-te authorities' obstinate pursuit of “independence” and provocations, and proves that Lai Ching-te is a betrayer of the mainstream public opinion on the island. Whether one acknowledges the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China is a touchstone for testing whether the Taiwan side is sincere, and also the golden key to improving and developing cross-Strait relations. Only by returning to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development, and only then will peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be practically guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Ma Ying-jeou recently harshly criticized Lai Qingde's inaugural speech as the “new two-state theory,” saying cross-Strait relations may face unpredictable risks and challenges. What kind of atmosphere on the island do you think Ma's concern reflects?","Lai Ching-te's remarks blatantly peddle the “two-state theory,” attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence.” His attitude is arrogant and the nature of his remarks is vile. They seriously undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, seriously harm the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and seriously undermine Taiwan's development prospects. Far-sighted people in Taiwan have expressed deep concern, which reflects the common voice of broad Taiwan compatriots and the mainstream public opinion on the island: they want peace, not war; development, not decline; exchange, not separation; and cooperation, not confrontation. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and a road of no return. Acting against the tide and against the will of the people, it will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The 77th World Health Assembly is being held in Geneva, Switzerland. During the assembly, many countries have repeatedly expressed support for the one-China principle. What is your comment?","On May 27, the General Committee and the plenary session of the 77th World Health Assembly each made decisions to clearly refuse to include Taiwan-related proposals on the agenda of the Assembly. During the World Health Assembly, more than one hundred countries expressed clear support for China's position, including by sending letters specifically to the Director-General of the World Health Organization. This fully demonstrates that the one-China principle represents the aspirations of the people and righteousness, that the international community's pattern of adhering to one China is unshakable, and that the World Health Organization's handling of Taiwan-related matters in accordance with the one-China principle has received firm support from the international community.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to participate in international organizations and their activities by bypassing cross-strait consultation and relying on the support of external forces will not work. Each time the DPP authorities stir up trouble and provoke, the international community's consensus on adhering to one China is consolidated a little further. Attempts to challenge the one-China principle will only lead to a loss of support and running into walls everywhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623896.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","A Taiwan media outlet applied to interview the World Health Assembly and was required to provide a Chinese passport. Taiwan authorities said this was discrimination, and that the practice of the UN system violates the maintenance of press freedom. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The UN system has long handled Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and has made corresponding provisions accordingly. These provisions must be respected and observed. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, and under various pretexts, they stir up trouble and provoke at international occasions. This will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Recently, the PLA organized the “Joint Sword-2024A” exercise around Taiwan island. The DPP authorities alleged that it was a “unilateral military provocation” by the mainland, and declared that they would “safeguard democracy and freedom, and defend sovereignty” through concrete actions. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities’ statement is a complete reversal of black and white and self-deception. Upon taking office, the leader of the Taiwan region brazenly challenged the one-China principle, extensively peddled the “two-state theory,” and promoted “seeking independence by relying on external forces” and “seeking independence by force.” This is a blatant provocation. The “Joint Sword—2024A” exercise is a resolute punishment for its provocations to seek “independence” and a just act to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities’ so-called “safeguarding Taiwan” advances an adventure to seek “independence” at the cost of the lives and property of Taiwan’s people. If they do not know to pull back from the brink, they will only push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","The PLA recently conducted the \"Joint Sword-2024A\" exercise around Taiwan Island. This exercise covered a wider area, came closer to Taiwan Island, involved a larger force, and carried a stronger combat implication. What does this mean? Will such exercises become routine?","As soon as the leader of the Taiwan region took office, he brazenly challenged the one-China principle, blatantly peddled the “two-state theory,” attempted to “internationalize” the Taiwan question, continued to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “seek independence through force,” and tried to push Taiwan into a dead end. In response, we will not tolerate, will not appease, and will leave no room whatsoever for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. The PLA’s “Joint Sword-2024A” exercises around Taiwan are a resolute punishment of the “May 20” speech by the leader of the Taiwan region for its provocative pursuit of “independence,” a stern warning against external forces that condone and support “Taiwan independence” and interfere in China’s internal affairs, and a righteous action to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nIt should be pointed out that all of our countermeasures are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference, and are by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, distinguish right from wrong, and act in accordance with righteousness. Together with compatriots on the mainland, let us firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, resolutely safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623900.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Regarding the “Joint Sword-2024A” military exercise, the spokesperson for the UN Secretary-General recently stated in response to media questions that, according to UN Resolution 2758, “Taiwan is a province of China.” What comments does the spokesperson have?","We highly appreciate the relevant statement by the United Nations. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 fully reflects this and solemnly affirms it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The Ministry of Commerce recently announced that it has launched an anti-dumping investigation into copolymer polyoxymethylene products originating in the Taiwan region. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","It is understood that on April 22, the Ministry of Commerce received an anti-dumping investigation application from relevant mainland enterprises. After conducting a review in accordance with the provisions of the Anti-Dumping Regulations, it announced the initiation of an anti-dumping investigation into imports of copolymerized polyoxymethylene originating from the European Union, the United States, Taiwan region and Japan. The competent authorities will advance the investigation process in accordance with relevant laws, regulations and WTO rules and make a final ruling. We hope that the enterprises involved will actively cooperate with the relevant investigation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Cross-Strait tourism has been at a standstill since Lai Ching-te took office, causing great impact on Taiwan’s tourism industry. Taiwan tourism operators have recently called on the DPP authorities to lift the “group travel ban” on June 1, to restore Taiwan-side group travel to the mainland, and to give the tourism industry a normal operating environment. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Since the mainland side announced on May 19 last year the resumption of receiving Taiwan residents on group tours to the mainland, the Taiwan side has been slow to respond, and the “group tour ban” has still not been lifted to this day. The tourism industry on the island is strongly dissatisfied. The DPP authorities should face up to the demands of Taiwan residents and the tourism industry, and create the conditions for the normal resumption of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Vatican Secretary of State Pietro Parolin recently said he hopes to set up a permanent office in China. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The relevant departments have already expressed their position on this. The One-China Principle is a generally recognized code of conduct in international relations and a common understanding of the international community. Relevant countries should properly handle Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the One-China Principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","The spokesperson of the U.S. State Department recently responded to Taiwanese media, noting that Lai Ching-te's “5·20” speech pledged to ensure peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and maintain the status quo, called on the mainland to exercise restraint and not engage in “provocation and intimidation,” and said that the U.S. “One China policy” has not changed and will not change. What is your comment on…","Lai Ching-te’s remarks are a thoroughgoing “Taiwan independence confession.” The DPP authorities and external forces such as the United States are putting on a double act, reversing black and white, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait can see this very clearly. If the US side sincerely hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should adhere to the one-China principle and its commitments to China, and clearly oppose “Taiwan independence” through concrete action.\nThe trend of history cannot be reversed, and the will of the people cannot be defied. No matter how the United States and Taiwan collude and make trouble, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the trend that China will be, and must be, reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623895.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","广东广播电视台记者","The 4th 'Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams: Cross-Strait Compatriot Exchange and Seminar' is being held in Guangdong today. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The fourth “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” opened this morning (the 29th) in Guangdong and will last two days. The event is jointly organized by the Cross-Strait Relations Research Center and Taiwan unification groups, and hosted by the Guangdong Cross-Strait Civil Exchange Promotion Association. More than 200 guests from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao will engage in in-depth dialogue, seminars, and visits and exchanges under the theme “Guarding Our Common Home, Creating the Future of the Nation.” They will discuss three topics: “national spirit and cultural confidence,” “national rejuvenation and the strength of youth,” and “national faith and national reunification.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240529_12623899.htm"],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Cross-Strait relations have never been as severe as they are now. The two sides have nearly “torn apart,” and there seems to be no room for reversal. May I ask the spokesperson, is there truly no going back for cross-Strait relations?\nSecond question: Lai Ching-te recently said he hopes to increase mutual understanding, comprehension, forgiveness and reconciliation with the mainland. May I ask the…","First question: The statement that “cross-Strait relations can no longer go back” is itself a false proposition. Cross-strait relations have been moving forward all along, toward the goal of national reunification. Our determination to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve national reunification is as firm as a rock, our ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is invincible, and our actions to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference are resolute and forceful. No matter how the situation on the island changes and no matter who is in power, they cannot change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, cannot change the basic structure and development direction of cross-strait relations, and cannot halt the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified. Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. We will fully implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, unwaveringly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite broad Taiwan compatriots, strive to promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.\nSecond question: If they sincerely want to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, they should immediately abandon the “Taiwan independence” position, stop provocations aimed at “seeking independence,” and return to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle.\nThird question: Regarding the matter of Taiwanese performers, there is, to some extent, a lack of respect for Taiwanese performers. When Taiwanese performers perform on the mainland, some natural and heartfelt expressions occur in their interactions with fans, and they say some things. Must they be slapped with the label of “political statements” by some people on the island just for saying those things? We must ask: Do they not have the right to express themselves? Who wants to silence them?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The Ministry of Commerce recently issued an announcement deciding to place several US companies involved in arms sales to the Taiwan region on the Unreliable Entity List. Please explain.","The U.S. companies Boeing Defense, Space & Security, General Atomics Aeronautical Systems, and General Dynamics Land Systems have repeatedly sold offensive weapons such as missiles, military drones, and tanks to Taiwan, China, thereby indulging and supporting \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. This seriously endangers China's national security, seriously violates China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, seriously contravenes the one-China principle and the provisions of the China-U.S. three joint communiqués, especially the \"August 17 Communiqué,\" and seriously undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. In accordance with the Foreign Trade Law, the National Security Law, and the Provisions on the Unreliable Entity List, the mainland has decided to place the above companies on the Unreliable Entity List and take corresponding measures. This is a normal law enforcement action taken by the mainland in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-05-29","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","Hsu Shu-po, Chairman of the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce, said on the 27th that stability in cross-Strait economic and trade relations and the opening of tourism are very important, and he expects good news that group tourists will be allowed to travel by the end of the month. Will the mainland side allow mainland tour groups to travel to Taiwan?","On April 28, the mainland tourism authorities announced arrangements related to mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism, responding in good faith to the expectations of Taiwan people and the tourism industry. The current problem is that the DPP authorities have been slow to respond and keep using “who will release goodwill first” as an excuse and obstacle. The DPP authorities' refusal to lift the ban on group tours to the mainland for Taiwan people is substantively depriving Taiwan people of their legitimate rights and harming the interests of Taiwan's tourism industry.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202405/t20240529_12623891.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The PLA Eastern Theater Command recently conducted the “Joint Sword-2024A” exercise around Taiwan island. Has the spokesperson's expected effect been achieved? Will there be follow-up exercises named “B,” or even “C” or “D”?","The joint exercises held by the PLA Eastern Theater Command struck down the arrogance of “Taiwan independence,” deterred external forces from interfering, and achieved the intended purpose. Regarding your question about “B” or “C” or “D,” what I want to say is that every time the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke us, our countermeasures will advance one step further, until the complete reunification of the motherland is achieved. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army, represented by the “Yang Gensi Company,” has the glorious tradition of the “three disbeliefs”: not believing there is a mission it cannot complete, not believing there is a difficulty it cannot overcome, and not believing there is an enemy it cannot defeat.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have three questions. First, you mentioned earlier when you came in that it is raining heavily outside. Recently, the media has often used the phrase “high winds and rough seas” to describe the situation in the Taiwan Strait. How does the Ministry of National Defense assess the Taiwan Strait situation described as “high winds and rough seas”? Second, after the Eastern Theater Command recently conducted…","Regarding the first question, recently, with “Taiwan independence” provocations and external interference, the situation in the Taiwan Strait has heated up somewhat. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains on constant alert and resolutely crushes all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes. As for the “high winds and turbulent waves” you just mentioned, the PLA has full confidence; as far as we are concerned, “no matter how the winds and waves rise, we remain steady in the fishing boat.”\nRegarding the second question, in my view, some Taiwanese media outlets are always eager to publish “self-hyped” news, which stems from a mistaken perception of their own strength.\nRegarding the third question, recently, under the strategic guidance of the heads of state of the two countries, the two militaries of China and the United States have strengthened communication and exchanges. This situation was hard-won and is worth cherishing even more. But we must also see that on certain issues the U.S. side has disregarded China's core interests and major concerns and artificially created risks of confrontation, which is the fundamental reason for the ups and downs in China-U.S. military relations. We hope the U.S. side will move toward China in the same direction, genuinely implement the important consensus reached by the two heads of state, adhere to the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence, and win-win cooperation, and add more positive factors to the stable and healthy development of military relations between the two countries. Regarding your question about whether the defense ministers of China and the United States will meet during the Xiangshan Forum, if the two defense ministers do meet, we will hold a media briefing at the first opportunity, and we welcome media friends to follow closely.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that Taiwan leader Lai Ching-te delivered his so-called “inauguration” speech on May 20, touting “no subordination” between the two sides, falsely claiming that mainland military actions are the “greatest strategic challenge to peace and stability,” clamoring that “there can be no illusions about peace,” and agitating to “strengthen national defense forces.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te's “5·20” speech is full of deception toward Taiwan compatriots, malice toward the mainland people, sycophancy toward his “foreign masters,” and delusions of “seeking independence through force.” It is a confession of “relying on foreigners to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force.” The People's Liberation Army firmly opposes this and will respond with forceful actions.\nTaiwan has been Chinese territory since ancient times. Its historical record is clear, and its legal and factual basis is unambiguous. The Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation clearly stipulate that Taiwan, which Japan stole from China, shall be returned to China. United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 clarifies that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. Not long ago, the spokesperson for the United Nations Secretary-General clearly stated that Taiwan is a province of China. The DPP authorities disregard this basic fact, obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” stance, incite confrontation across the Strait, and serve as a pawn of external forces to contain China, constituting a serious challenge to the international order and a serious undermining of regional peace. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the greatest real threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe tide of the world is vast and mighty: those who follow it prosper, and those who defy it perish. The reunification of the motherland is an irresistible historical trend. “Taiwan independence” means war, and separatism brings no peace. The Chinese People's Liberation Army bears the sacred mission of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It stands always on high alert, ready for combat, and resolutely will crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and firmly defeat all interference by external forces.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Philippine Secretary of National Defense Teodoro recently refused to comment on the People’s Liberation Army Eastern Theater Command’s exercises around Taiwan island, saying it is “China’s internal affair.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, a view widely recognized by the international community, including the Philippines.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: The US State Department recently issued a statement saying the US is deeply concerned about the mainland's military exercises encircling Taiwan and calls on the mainland to exercise restraint. A US Department of Defense spokesperson said it is closely monitoring the Chinese military exercises and expressing concern about them. What is the spokesperson's comment on…","Let me first answer your first question. Taiwan is part of China, and how to resolve the Taiwan question is the affair of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. It brooks no finger-pointing from the US side. Only by stopping all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and stopping colluding with external forces to provoke can we sincerely ease the situation in the Taiwan Strait. Reunification of the motherland is the will of the people. The PLA speaks through its actions and has always been the vanguard in fighting “independence” and promoting reunification.\nAs for your second question, we have already issued authoritative information on this, and the specific circumstances can be inquired about from the China Coast Guard. You just asked what signal this action sent. I think the signal is very clear: Taiwan is an inseparable part of China.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to Japanese media reports, 20 Chinese field-grade officers visited Japan in mid-to-late May. Some analysts say this is the first visit to Japan by a PLA officer delegation since 2019. Please confirm. Second, will the China Coast Guard conduct normalized patrols and law enforcement east of Taiwan island?","On the first question, at the invitation of the Japanese side, the 13th batch of the PLA young and middle-aged officer delegation visited Japan from May 14 to 20. During the visit, the delegation visited the Japanese Ministry of Defense and the National Institute for Defense Studies, held discussions and exchanges, and toured the Ground Self-Defense Force Health School, the Air Self-Defense Force Komaki Base, and the Maritime Self-Defense Force Maizuru Base, among others. We are willing to work with the Japanese side to continue our joint efforts to enhance understanding, build mutual trust, manage differences, and promote the development of bilateral defense relations.\nOn the second question, for the specific circumstances, please inquire with the China Coast Guard. As a principle, we will make decisions independently according to developments and changes in the situation.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-05-30","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, the mainland side believes that Lai Ching-te’s political speech is a “Taiwan independence” confession, and the PLA recently conducted military exercises around the island of Taiwan. The spokesperson just said that “Taiwan independence” means war and that separatism brings no peace, and reiterated the military’s position of “fighting ‘Taiwan independence’ and promoting reunification.”…","Let me first answer your first question. We are willing to make the utmost sincere effort and do our best to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we absolutely do not promise to renounce the use of force. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest real threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait. As long as “Taiwan independence” is not eliminated, the Taiwan Strait cannot be at peace. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army has the confidence and capability to safeguard the country’s sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity.\nAs for your second question, why would we communicate with the US side in advance? The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We demand that the US side stop official exchanges and military contacts between the US and Taiwan, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and create a favorable atmosphere for military-to-military exchanges through practical actions.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16313455.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-05-31","Mao Ning","AFP","A follow-up question on Donald Trump. Donald Trump mentioned Taiwan at a recent campaign event. Do you have any comment on this? And does China fear Trump may become the next US President?","The US presidential election is the domestic affair of the US. I would not comment on campaign rhetoric.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463230.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202405/t20240531_11367990.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-05-31","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 31. Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on May 31 that the Customs Tariff Commission of the State Council has issued a announcement deciding that, starting June 15, 2024, the preferential tariff rates under the Cross-Strait Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) will be suspended for imported products originating from Taiwan…","Chen Binhua pointed out that ECFA was signed by both sides across the Strait on the common political basis of the ‘1992 Consensus’, and that if problems arise during its implementation, they can be properly resolved through cross-Strait consultation. However, the Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to the ‘Taiwan independence’ position, refuse to acknowledge the ‘1992 Consensus’, loudly promote ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist fallacies, and incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation as well as economic ‘decoupling and breaking of supply chains’. This seriously undermines the foundation for cross-Strait consultation and the implementation of ECFA, and is the fundamental reason why the relevant mainland authorities had to further suspend tariff concessions on some ECFA products. Facts have once again proven that pursuing ‘Taiwan independence’ means there will be no peace and no development; it can only bring disaster and harm to Taiwan, and only damage the interests of Taiwan’s enterprises and people.\nChen Binhua stressed that we have always respected, cared for and benefited Taiwan compatriots, and have always taken a positive attitude toward promoting cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation. We will continue to welcome and support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in investing and developing on the mainland, will take the lead in sharing with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization, will provide more equal treatment to Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, will continue to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and will benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait even more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202405/t20240531_12624451.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-06-03","Mao Ning","NOS","Last week, a Dutch marine ship passed through first the South China Sea then the Taiwan Strait as part of a bigger freedom of navigation exercise in the region. Is China aware of this transit through the Taiwan Strait? Have Chinese marine vessels for instance also monitored the ship? How does China view this passing?","I’d refer you to competent authorities for the specifics. Let me say that China respects countries’ right to navigation in accordance with international law, but firmly opposes undermining China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation. The Asia-Pacific is a shining example of peace and development. We hope countries outside the region will do things that are conducive to regional peace and stability, instead of making provocations and stirring up trouble for the peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463231.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240603_11375826.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-03","Mao Ning","Dragon TV","On June 2, defense ministers of the US, Japan and the ROK held a trilateral meeting in Singapore and issued a joint press statement, in which they blamed China, saying “they strongly oppose any unilateral attempts to change the status quo in the waters of the Indo-Pacific,” “emphasized the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait,” “called for the peaceful resolution of cross-Strait issues,”…","We noted this. The US, Japan and the ROK used their trilateral defense ministers’ meeting and trilateral vice foreign minister-level dialogue to advance the so-called “Indo-Pacific Strategy,” point fingers on the Taiwan question, grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs, once again deliberately attack and vilify China on maritime issues and sow discord between China and neighboring countries. Such moves seriously violate basic norms governing international relations. China strongly deplores and opposes this.\nFirst, China firmly opposes the practice of bloc politics, anything said or done to instigate or intensify tensions and undermine other countries’ strategic security and interests, and the attempt to form exclusive groupings in the Asia-Pacific. The US needs to act on its word that the revitalization of its alliances is not targeted at China and stop seeking selfish gains at the expense of other countries’ strategic security and the wellbeing of the people in the Asia-Pacific.\nSecond, the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community and basic norm in international relations. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The biggest threat to cross-Strait peace now is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and external connivance and support for them. If relevant countries truly care about cross-Strait peace and stability and want the world to be safe and prosperous, they should uphold the one-China principle, unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and support China’s reunification.\nThird, China will always defend its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. We are committed to properly settling bilateral maritime issues with countries directly concerned through dialogue and consultation. That said, we firmly oppose countries outside the region meddling with and escalating the situation. In recent years, the US has been inciting and supporting certain countries in provoking China and infringing on China’s sovereignty and maritime rights at sea, and frequently conducted joint military exercises and close-in reconnaissance with its allies in waters close to China, including the South China Sea, to flex muscles and intensify tensions in the region. This has become the biggest threat and challenge to regional peace and stability.\nFourth, China’s basic position on the Korean Peninsula issue is consistent. We believe that ensuring peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula and advancing the political settlement of the Korean Peninsula issue serves the common interests of all parties. Resorting to military deterrence and imposing sanctions and pressure will only intensify differences and heighten tensions. We urge relevant parties to be prudent in words and deeds and refrain from fueling the tension in the Korean Peninsula which is already highly complex and challenging. We will continue to handle Korean Peninsula affairs based on their merits and our own position.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463231.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240603_11375826.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-04","Mao Ning","AFP","Palau, a Pacific island, was hit by a cyberattack recently. Palau claimed that Chinese hackers were behind it. Taiwan has condemned the attack and offered support. What’s China’s comment?","I’m not familiar with what you mentioned. Let me say broadly that China firmly opposes and cracks down on all forms of cyberattacks in accordance with law. Taiwan is part of China. We hope that relevant country will recognize as soon as possible the prevailing trend and make an early decision that serves its own long-term interest.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463232.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240604_11376600.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-05","Mao Ning","TASS","US President Joe Biden in an interview with Time magazine said he does not rule out using US military force in the case of military conflict between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. No pressure or threat will erode the determination, will and ability of the Chinese government and people to defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people. We urge the US to fully recognize the inherent nature and dangerous ambition of “Taiwan independence” separatists, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor the commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463233.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240605_11377111.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-06","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Taiwan president Lai Ching-te congratulated Indian leader Narendra Modi on his election victory and Modi said he looked forward to closer ties with Taiwan. How does the Ministry respond?","First of all, there is no such thing as “president” of the Taiwan region. As for your question, China opposes all forms of official interactions between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic relations with China. There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. India has made serious political commitments on this and is supposed to recognize, be alarmed about and resist the Taiwan authorities’ political calculations. China has protested to India about this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240606_11381984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-06","Mao Ning","PTI","You said China protested to India. Why you have to protest to India about somebody else’s wishing the leader of India?","India has diplomatic relations with China. China opposes all forms of official interactions between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic relations with China. This position is very clear and India knows this well.\nOn the one-China principle, India has made serious political commitments and is supposed to recognize, be alarmed about and resist the Taiwan authorities’ political calculations, and refrain from doing things that violate the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240606_11381984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-06","Mao Ning","Reuters","First question, Ukraine’s First Deputy Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiha expressed his hope that China will attend the Summit on Peace in Ukraine to be held in Switzerland. Could you share more information with us on his consultation with the Chinese side in Beijing? Second, Palau’s President told Reuters that he expected China to attempt to meddle in a national election at the end of this year. What’s China’s response?","On your first question, yesterday, China and Ukraine held consultation between our two foreign ministries in Beijing and exchanged views on bilateral relations and the Ukraine crisis. China has released information, which you may refer to. On the Summit on Peace in Ukraine to be held in Switzerland, we have made clear China’s position several times. China will continue to promote talks for peace in our own way and work with other parties to accumulate conditions for the political settlement of the crisis.\nOn your second question, China follows the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs. We will not and have no interest in interfering in other countries’ internal affairs. The one-China principle is the prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. Around the world, 183 countries have already established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. The very few countries who still maintain so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan region should come to stand on the right side of history and make a right decision that truly serves their own fundamental and long-term interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463234.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240606_11381984.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-07","Mao Ning","Al Jazeera","According to US government press release, the State Department has approved the sales of F-16 spare parts and relevant services worth US$80 million to Taiwan. What is the Ministry’s comment?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. Such sales gravely undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and send a gravely wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this.\nWhat happened shows once again that the biggest threat to cross-Strait peace and stability and the biggest source of damage to the cross-Strait status quo are the separatist moves for “Taiwan independence” and connivance and support for such moves from US-led external forces. “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with cross-Strait peace as fire with water. The DPP authorities attempt to seek independence through the use of force and the US is hellbent on helping advance that agenda by arming Taiwan. This is against the trend of the times, which will only escalate cross-Strait tensions and lead nowhere.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. China urges the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop selling arms to Taiwan and having military contact with Taiwan, stop creating factors that fuel tensions in the Taiwan Strait, stop endangering cross-Strait peace and stability, and stop going further down this wrong and dangerous path. We will take strong and resolute measures to defend our national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463235.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240607_11414848.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-06-07","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency recently announced that it has approved two arms sales to Taiwan worth about 300 million U.S. dollars in total, including plans to provide F-16 fighter spare parts and related services to Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","The US sale of weapons to the Taiwan region of China seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17” Communiqué. It seriously damages China's sovereignty and security interests and seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We are strongly dissatisfied with this, firmly oppose it, and have made stern representations to the US side.\nThe Taiwan question is the first insurmountable red line in China-US relations. The US side is bolstering and encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, pushing up cross-Strait tensions, and step by step pushing Taiwan toward danger, which will ultimately harm itself as well. China urges the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately withdraw the aforementioned arms sales plan to Taiwan, stop arming Taiwan in any way, and act concretely to uphold the overall state of military relations. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16314537.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-06-12","Lin Jian","Dragon TV","Recently, Japanese scholars Seiya Matsuno and Shigeo Nasu donated a large amount of historical files on Japan’s bacterial warfare to the Yiwu archives hall and the Historical Facts Exhibition Hall of Bacterial Warfare of the Japanese Invaders in Yiwu, with a written message that says “Japan-China friendship” and “Never again should there be war between Japan and China”. What’s China’s comment?","During WWII, in blatant violation of international law, the Japanese army launched horrendous bacterial warfare against the Chinese people and conducted gruesome human experimentation, which were heinous crimes against humanity. The historical files you mentioned show once again there are solid proofs for the bacterial warfare launched by Japanese militarists and there’s no room for denial.\nWe commend the courage of those in Japan who reveal the historical truth and face it squarely. Japan needs to face up to and reflect on its history of militarist aggression, draw lessons from it, get rid of the specter of militarism that still haunts it, and never let history repeat itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463237.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240612_11430519.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear journalist friends, hello! Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I have no content to release proactively. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently claimed that mainstream public opinion in Taiwan endorses Lai Ching-te’s policy proposals on the development of cross-Strait relations, and opposes the mainland’s so-called “composite pressure” on Taiwan. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te’s “5·20” speech is a thoroughgoing “Taiwan independence confession.” It has caused all sectors on the island to worry that the situation in the Taiwan Strait will become even more tense and turbulent over the next four years. If, as the Mainland Affairs Council claims, all is well, why do media polls show that more than half of Taiwan’s residents are uneasy about Lai Ching-te’s cross-Strait policy? Why do conscripted soldiers desert frequently in Taiwan, and why do pilots “pay compensation to apply for retirement”? Why do the demands of Taiwan’s industrial and commercial circles to oppose “decoupling and breaking chains” in cross-Strait economic and trade relations keep coming? Why do commentaries and articles calling for stabilizing the Taiwan Strait situation and restoring and expanding cross-Strait exchanges fill the island’s media pages? The facts are clear: peace rather than war, development rather than decline, exchange rather than separation, and cooperation rather than confrontation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ self-serving talk and attempts to cover up the truth only prove once again that they are betrayers of the island’s mainstream public opinion.\nIt should be pointed out that all of our countermeasures are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and are by no means aimed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, follow the trend of history, recognize the extreme harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, firmly resist and oppose any “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and external interference, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being through concrete action.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627175.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The 16th Straits Forum is about to convene. Please have the spokesperson introduce the preparations for this forum.","The 16th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in mid-this-month. The forum's main session will take place on the morning of June 15, and the concentrated activities will last for one week, with the main venue set in Xiamen. Relevant prefecture-level cities in Fujian and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone will also hold related events. This forum is co-hosted by 86 units from both sides of the Strait. It adheres to the positioning of “civilian, grassroots, and broadly inclusive,” continues the theme of “expanding civilian exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and sets up four sections: grassroots exchanges, youth exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges, with a series of 50 events arranged. At present, preparations for the forum are basically complete. The forum organizing committee has invited representatives of Taiwan political parties, representatives of host units, industry representatives, association heads, and about 7,000 guests from all sectors, including the Youth, Women's, and Workers' federations, science, education, culture, health, agriculture, fisheries, water conservancy, and folk belief circles, to attend. Media reporters are welcome to visit for interviews and coverage.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627178.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Defense Minister Dong Jun repeatedly stated solemn positions on the Taiwan question during the 21st Shangri-La Dialogue, which drew much attention. The DPP responded, saying, “China should immediately abandon its verbal attacks, military intimidation, and high-handed suppression against Taiwan,” should face up to the cross-Strait relationship of “not subordinate to each other,” and that Taiwan society opposes…","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China, and its historical course is clear and its legal facts are plain. The DPP is working hard to hitch itself to and cooperate with external forces, attempting to fool the island's people and mislead international audiences by fabricating false narratives such as responding to a so-called \"mainland threat.\" It is well known that \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference are the greatest source of the danger of war across the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the \"Taiwan independence\" position, challenge the one-China principle, incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and attempt to \"seek independence by relying on foreign powers\" and \"seek independence through military force.\" This seriously violates mainstream public opinion on the island and seriously undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and it will only bring profound calamity to Taiwan compatriots. If they insist on going their own way, they will surely bring disaster upon themselves and reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627177.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","The mainland side has decided to further suspend tariff concessions on some ECFA products. Island public opinion points out that this is a follow-on chain effect of Lai Ching-te’s “May 20” speech, which moved toward the “independence” faction, and that those harmed are Taiwan’s people, good products, and business. What is your comment?","They have voiced the common aspirations of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and have also shown that ECFA was originally a good agreement that benefits Taiwan and its compatriots. The tariff reductions and exemptions on ECFA early harvest products enjoyed by the Taiwan side are far greater than those enjoyed by the mainland side. If the Lai Ching-te authorities do not know when to stop and continue to rashly advance on the evil path of “Taiwan independence,” they will only bring greater harm to Taiwan's people, goods, and commerce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627176.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","Koo Li-hsiung, head of Taiwan’s defense department, recently claimed that as long as the PLA attacks aircraft, ships, and facilities in flight, and any aerial or maritime entity enters the 12-nautical-mile “air and sea area” without permission, Taiwan can order the exercise of the “right of self-defense” and launch a “self-defense counterattack.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. Where does the so-called “right of self-defense” come from? The DPP authorities' attempt to “draw lines and set prohibitions” on our just actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is sheer overestimation of their own abilities. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities not to play with fire. Anyone who dares to act rashly will only bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the Chang'e-6 ascender, carrying lunar samples, took off from the far side of the Moon and successfully entered its planned lunar orbit. The five-star red flag unfurled on the far side of the Moon and the “中” character mark it left behind have sparked heated discussion among netizens on both sides of the Strait. Some Taiwanese netizens said, “As Taiwan compatriots, we share in the honor.” What comment…","Chang'e-6 completed the world's first sampling from the far side of the Moon and returned to orbit. It is a historic step in China's exploration of outer space and a historic step in mankind's peaceful use of outer space, and a shared glory for Chinese people at home and abroad. Our journey is toward the stars and the sea, and our destination is the vast universe. Our spacecraft and our dream of flight will soar higher and farther, bringing more emotion and glory to Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","A Taiwanese high school student recently said in an interview that only one or two questions on the exam involved Chinese history, and that some students did not know “what Chinese history is,” which sparked heated discussion among netizens on both sides. A Taiwanese scholar harshly criticized the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence curriculum guidelines” for making Taiwanese students “hate and despise the…","In pursuit of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have vigorously carried out “de-Sinicization.” The so-called “education reform” policies and “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines they have introduced deliberately distort Chinese history and attempt to sever the historical ties across the Strait. This not only deprives Taiwan youth of the legitimate right to learn their own national culture and understand their own national history, poisons the younger generation in Taiwan, and leaves Taiwan compatriots as spiritually and culturally rootless duckweed, unable to experience the pride and happiness of being upright Chinese people, but also incites hostility across the Strait, undermines cross-Strait peace, and plants the seeds of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Such “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines are nothing other than “poisonous curriculum guidelines.” Far-sighted people on the island deeply loathe them and have repeatedly called for setting things right. We believe that Taiwan compatriots will one day be able to have a correct curriculum.\nThe beauty of the Chinese land is everywhere. What is missing from Taiwan's textbooks can be found on the mainland. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young students, to come to the mainland to experience the charm of Chinese culture firsthand, seek their cultural roots, and make up for the lessons they did not receive in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627172.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","According to reports, mainland actor Hu Ge, who is popular with young people on both sides of the Strait, traveled to Taiwan today (12th) to take part in cultural exchange activities. Can the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation?","At the invitation of the Taipei Audio-Visual Association, mainland actor Hu Ge is traveling to Taipei today to attend the “Dialogue with Youth” event, where he will engage in dialogue and exchange with cross-Strait young film and television creators. This will provide a rare opportunity for exchange among young people on both sides of the Strait. I think “Baozong Visits Baodao” is a good thing that compatriots on both sides of the Strait welcome.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The offshore trestle of Section A1 of the Xiamen section of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge has been more than 80% completed, and all construction work is progressing smoothly. CCTV News client has also produced an online interactive product to promote “cloud-based” bridge building. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is the common call and urgent wish of the people of Xiamen and Kinmen. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development,” released last year, further outlined the beautiful vision of “Xiamen and Kinmen facing each other across the sea, Lu Island and Jinmen connected by bridge,” and the infrastructure construction on the Xiamen side of the Xiamen-Kinmen bridge connection has now been essentially completed.\nRecently, the China Media Group's CCTV News client produced a “cloud-based” bridge-building interactive product, which will be officially launched on June 15. We welcome netizens on both sides of the Strait to help, and together cross the shallow Xiamen-Kinmen Strait and build a bridge to Kinmen in the cloud. Those who keep it in mind will surely receive an echo. We also hope that the physical Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge can soon become a reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Singapore's Defence Minister Ng Eng Hen (黄永宏), when asked at the Shangri-La Dialogue for advice on the Taiwan question, immediately stated that the Taiwan question is a red line, that Taiwan is not Ukraine, and that China does not need any other country to provide any advice on the Taiwan question. What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and brooks no interference from outside. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. We appreciate the understanding and support of the international community for the Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” and striving to complete national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","Cheng Wen-tsan, Chairperson of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that regarding how to pragmatically handle the reality of “separate governance and separate establishment” across the Taiwan Strait, the mainland, Taiwan, and different camps within Taiwan would have different policies, and that the mainland side should allow SEF personnel to travel to the mainland to care for Taiwanese businesses,…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait, a fact that no one, no party, and no force can evade or deny. As long as the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is acknowledged, there will be no obstacle to dialogue and exchanges between the two associations.\nWe will, as always, care for and support the development of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland, and share the fruits of the mainland's development and progress with Taiwan businesses and enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Recently, US-Taiwan military collusion has been frequent. The US side recently approved a 300 million US dollar arms sale plan for Taiwan, nearly 30 US arms dealers went to Taiwan in a group to attend the so-called “Defense Industry Forum,” and there are reports that the US Department of Defense has set up a “secret project team” to accelerate the coordination of military assistance to Taiwan. Taiwan’s “Ministry…","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and Taiwan, China, including arms sales to Taiwan. Whether under the name of “arms sales,” “military aid,” or any other pretext, the aim is to lead the flames of war toward Taiwan, and the intent is sinister. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué,” stop selling arms to Taiwan, stop arming Taiwan, and stop sending any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe DPP authorities attempt to “seek independence by relying on external forces” and “seek independence through force,” which will only push Taiwan toward a perilous situation of war and bring profound disaster upon the compatriots in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627174.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","The mainland side has repeatedly stated clearly that ECFA was signed and implemented on the common political basis of the “1992 Consensus.” The Mainland Affairs Council says that ECFA was negotiated in accordance with the basic spirit of the World Trade Organization (WTO), and the preamble of ECFA expressly states “in accordance with the basic principles of the World Trade Organization (WTO).” The mainland’s…","The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for cross-Strait consultations; the 23 cross-Strait agreements, including ECFA, were all signed on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” The basic principle of the World Trade Organization (WTO) is non-discrimination. When the two sides signed ECFA to promote trade liberalization across the Strait, it should have been carried out on the basis of normalized cross-Strait trade. However, considering that both sides are one family, and in order for compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots, to be the first to enjoy the benefits of ECFA, we agreed, under the abnormal and discriminatory circumstances in which the Taiwan authorities still restrict the import of more than 2,000 kinds of mainland agricultural and industrial products, to advance the normalization and liberalization process at the same time by first implementing the Early Harvest Program. Moreover, taking into account the economic conditions of both sides, we did not require that the products under the Early Harvest Program be reciprocal in quantity, trade value, and other respects when implemented. Such a special arrangement fully reflects our consistent adherence to and practice of the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family.” If everything were based on WTO rules, how could there be this good agreement that makes unilateral concessions to Taiwan?\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities are attempting to use the WTO mechanism to negotiate and resolve ECFA-related issues. The purpose is to “internationalize” the Taiwan question, and what it harbors is the “Taiwan independence” malicious intent. Our position is clear: this road is blocked.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240612_12627173.htm"],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","The traditional Chinese festival of the Dragon Boat Festival has just passed. Please introduce the relevant situation regarding Taiwan compatriots participating in festival customs and cultural activities in various places.","Around the Dragon Boat Festival, a wide variety of colorful activities were held across the Chinese mainland. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait celebrated the traditional Chinese festival together and shared the fraternal bond of blood ties. Here I would like to introduce the relevant details.\nVarious folk culture activities in Jiangsu Province marked the Dragon Boat Festival in diverse forms. Suzhou held several cross-strait compatriot friendship events, including “Thick Zongzi Fragrance, Cross-Strait One Family,” where compatriots from both sides wrapped zongzi together. Nantong held the theme exchange event “Love in Nantong, Our Dragon Boat Festival,” where Taiwan compatriots, relatives of Taiwan compatriots, and representatives of cross-strait marriage families gathered together to experience folk culture. Suqian held the Cross-Strait (Suqian) “Our Festival · Dragon Boat Festival” Dragon Boat Invitational Race. More than one hundred Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youths participated, including members of a study tour group of Taiwan university students studying traditional Chinese culture and an agricultural and fishery industry exchange delegation from Yilan County. Fourteen dragon boat teams from both sides of the Strait competed on the same course, celebrating the festival together.\nIn Fujian, the 17th “Tan Kah Kee Cup” and “Jing Xian Cup” Cross-Strait Dragon Boat Race and the 9th China Dragon Boat Tug-of-War Open were held, attracting 42 teams from both sides of the Strait. In addition, activities such as “Harmonious Dragon Boat Festival Sentiment, Fujian-Taiwan Are One Family — Fujian and Taiwan Compatriots Celebrate the Dragon Boat Festival Together” and “Rich Dragon Boat Festival Sentiment, Zongye Fragrance Drifting, Cross-Strait Compatriots Talk About Well-Being” were successively carried out in various parts of Fujian.\nIn Zhuhai, Guangdong, local Taiwan youths were organized to take part in the innovation and entrepreneurship exchange activity “Salute to Youth · Pursuing Dreams in Zhuhai.” They visited the Zhuhai Dragon Boat Folk Culture Art Exhibition, a refined agricultural industry project, and Lianjiang Village, a typical village for rural revitalization. They also watched the 2024 Guangdong Provincial Dragon Boat Open and shared stories of putting down roots and building businesses in Zhuhai. Through an immersive experience of inheriting the festival culture, they celebrated the holiday together.\nChongqing held a Cross-Strait Marriage and Family Dragon Boat Festival exchange event themed “Women Hearts Connected, Cross-Strait Affection Integrated.” Taiwan compatriots and relatives of Taiwan compatriots living in Chongqing gathered together, wrapping “Tongxin” zongzi, weaving flower and grass fans, and making aromatherapy hammers. They celebrated the holiday through fun folk activities and experienced the charm of traditional Chinese culture.\nDuring the Dragon Boat Festival, a Gansu-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange Month was held in Gansu Province. It included 20 detailed activities, such as the Cross-Strait Badminton Friendship Tournament, the Cross-Strait Famous Calligraphy and Painting Joint Exhibition in Gansu, a self-driving motorcycle tour of Gansu by Taiwan compatriots, and a Taiwan small and medium-sized enterprise products exhibition. More than 1,200 representatives from all sectors of Taiwan participated. Compatriots from both sides explored the roots of Fuxi culture and Xiwangmu culture, enjoyed the scenery of the Gobi Desert and the Qilian Snow Mountains, visited the new appearance of rural development, and experienced the achievements of rural revitalization.\nHubei held the “One Family Across the Strait, Joy in the Dragon Boat Festival Sentiment” special concert of youth ethnic instrumental music from Hubei and Taiwan universities. Hunan held activities such as “Same Origin, Looking Toward the Future · Same Heart, Same Direction, Talking About Development,” a Dragon Boat Festival garden tour for cross-strait compatriots.\nIn addition, the China Media Group's special Dragon Boat Festival program “Rowing Toward Home — Singing of the Blue Waters on the Dragon Boat Festival 2024,” in its segment “Going Home for the Festival,” told the story of the Qu clan descendants in Wanguqiao Village, Yichang, Hubei, and the Baopu Village in Changhua City, Taiwan. The two sides made a “Dragon Boat Festival Appointment” and have gathered together to celebrate the Dragon Boat Festival for seven consecutive years. The story has sparked heated discussion among netizens, who praised this mutual journey across mountains and seas.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾中视记者","The spokesperson just mentioned “Bao Zong Comes to Treasure Island” (宝总到宝岛). The drama 《Blossoms Shanghaied》, starring Hu Ge, is very popular in Taiwan. There are reports that Cheng Wen-tsan, chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, facilitated this. What is your response? Under what circumstances did this trip by Hu Ge to Taiwan come about?","I note that this gentleman has already denied any involvement in this matter. In this matter, some people are willing to ride the hype and claim credit, which shows that mainland film and television stars visiting Taiwan for cultural exchange is a good thing that wins hearts and is welcomed. We are glad to see more Taiwan movie and drama fans able to meet the mainland stars they like. I also think this is simply an ordinary matter that does not need to go to great lengths or use any connections to maneuver. Ordinary matters are better handled with an ordinary mindset.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Recently, a Taiwan tour group traveled to the mainland for sightseeing, and one member was “detained” and did not return until several days after the other members had returned to Taiwan. Please explain the situation. Second question: A Taiwan internet user reported that while setting up a stall at the Nanjing Art Book Fair, he was taken away by police for “questioning” because the photography…","First question. We have consistently encouraged and supported normal and healthy cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. We will continue to create better conditions for Taiwan residents to travel to the mainland and provide better products and services. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have absolutely no need for any concerns when coming to the mainland; they can come happily and return home safely.\nSecond question. We understand that on May 31, a Taiwan resident was found by law enforcement inspectors displaying suspected obscene pictures while participating in an art market event in Nanjing. Police subsequently summoned him for questioning and handled the matter in accordance with the law and regulations. After identification by public security authorities, 58 of the items he was carrying were found to be obscene articles, which constituted “transporting obscene articles.” With active assistance from the local Taiwan Affairs Office, the police quickly handled the matter in accordance with the law. Taking into account that the person genuinely did not understand the relevant mainland regulations, they decided to “not impose administrative penalties” on him. He left the case handling center that same evening and returned to Taiwan several days later.\nThe facts of this case are clear, the evidence is conclusive and sufficient, and the police review and handling were lawful, standard, and civilized. The DPP authorities are making groundless accusations and hyping the matter, using it as an opportunity to intimidate residents of the island. I must emphasize once again that as long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have absolutely no need for any concerns when coming to the mainland; they can come to the mainland happily and return to Taiwan safely.\nThird question. Director Song Tao's remarks are consistent with our consistent position. The core of the “1992 Consensus” is embodying the one-China principle, and its core meaning is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","A technology company in Fujian recently flew a drone to Kinmen to scatter political leaflets, causing disruption locally. What is your comment?","This is a spontaneous act by mainland netizens expressing their hope for reunification and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” The launch and landing of small civil aircraft and the release of floating objects in relevant areas should be conducted in accordance with law and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS记者","First question: Recently, a mainland man piloted a small boat into the Tamsui River estuary. Kuan Bi-ling, director of the “Ocean Affairs Council,” said the man once served as captain of a mainland naval vessel. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's comment on this? Will relevant units ask him about the situation when he returns to the mainland? Second question: What is the progress in handling the incident…","Let me answer the second question first. We are still verifying and understanding the situation.\nAs for the first question: this is purely an individual act. The DPP authorities have no need to be overly alarmed and to stage a political manipulation with great fuss. After this man returns to the mainland, we will punish him in accordance with relevant regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities did not lift the “group tour ban” on travel to the mainland starting June 1. Instead, they said that tour groups planned before June 1 may continue, calling this “conditional relaxation.” What comment do you have on this? What considerations does the mainland side have regarding the restoration of normal cross-strait tourism, and what measures will it take?","We have always warmly welcomed compatriots from Taiwan to visit the mainland for tourism, to experience splendid Chinese culture, to feel the changes in the mainland’s development, and to share in its progress. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opinion and the demands of the island’s industry, refuse to lift the “group tour ban.” This brutally deprives Taiwan residents of their legitimate rights and interests and seriously harms the interests of Taiwan’s tourism industry. It is unpopular and will inevitably backfire.\nThe mainland’s competent tourism authorities announced relevant arrangements on April 28, and preparatory work is currently advancing in an orderly manner. We will follow the established plan and continue to promote the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and the normalization of exchanges in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","The mainland side has decided to further suspend tariff reductions on some ECFA products. Multiple island industry and commerce groups have called on the Lai Ching-te authorities to consult with the mainland side as soon as possible to avoid the entire agreement being suspended. What comments do you have on this? Will the mainland side take more economic sanctions, including suspending tariff reductions on more…","ECFA was signed and implemented on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” Any issues related to ECFA can be properly resolved through cross-Strait consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” However, if the Lai Ching-te authorities ignore public opinion and even create more problems, we support relevant departments in studying further measures in accordance with relevant regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体记者","First question: The advance-reconnaissance group from Fuzhou bound for Matsu, originally scheduled to depart on June 10, has been abruptly suspended. The mainland side said it conflicted with the Dragon Boat Festival holiday itinerary, and the Chairman of the Lianjiang County Council said the matter involved political considerations. How do you respond to this explanation? When will the advance-reconnaissance…","First question: The mainland's competent tourism authority announced relevant arrangements on April 28. At present, preparatory work is advancing in an orderly manner, and we will, in accordance with the established plan, continue to promote the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and the regularization of exchanges in all fields. Regarding the Fuzhou–Matsu “scouting tour group” you mentioned: because Fuzhou will hold important festival activities during this year's Dragon Boat Festival, the dates of those activities conflict with the original itinerary of the Fuzhou Tourism Association's inspection delegation. Therefore, it was decided that the inspection activity to Matsu will be postponed. Once specific dates are determined, the Taiwan side will be notified. We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, including cross-strait tourism, and we are optimistic about their success.\nSecond question: Regarding this extremely erroneous remark, mainland compatriots and netizens have already voiced strong dissatisfaction. I must emphasize that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The history is clear and the legal facts are unambiguous. Taiwan has never been a country, not in the past, and it will never be one in the future. This is the common understanding of the international community and a basic common sense of international relations. We hope he will take some remedial lessons.\nThird question: Since the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) came into effect, it has brought tangible benefits to cross-strait industries, especially Taiwan's related industries and the public. By the end of 2023, Taiwan enterprises had enjoyed cumulative tariff reductions of more than US$9 billion. Facts have long proven that ECFA is a good agreement that benefits Taiwan compatriots. If the DPP authorities truly believe ECFA has little effect, why have they repeatedly said they hope the mainland will not abolish ECFA?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","After the second season of the Mainland TV drama *Joy of Life* aired, it once again sparked a binge-watching craze on the island, especially among young people born after 2000, who love the show very much. Against the backdrop of the DPP authorities' forceful promotion of “de-Sinicization” education, Mainland costume dramas continue to draw viewing crazes on the island. How do you view this contrast?","I have noted that after the second season of 《Qing Yu Nian》 aired, as with the first season, it has aroused lively discussion and wide acclaim online and among viewers on both sides of the Strait, especially young Taiwan viewers. Some viewers said the second season maintains interesting plotlines and rich elements of Chinese culture, and is a long-awaited classic. Others said that, influenced by the storyline, they went to look up and learn about the many Tang poems and Song lyrics featured in the show. These timeless masterpieces are cultural treasures shared by Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.\nThe second season of 《Qing Yu Nian》 is popular on the island. This fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, and ancestry, have a common cultural root, and readily form emotional resonance with excellent cultural works such as film and television dramas. “Though tempered and struck a thousand times, it remains firm, withstanding winds from every direction.” The Chinese cultural gene flowing in the blood of broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots cannot be changed, no matter how the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces try to carry out “de-Sinicization” or undermine cross-Strait cultural exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","This year marks the centennial of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy, and commemorative activities are being held on both sides of the Strait. A retired Taiwan military general called for “driving out ‘Taiwan independence’ and revitalizing China” at the Whampoa Centennial commemorative activities on the island. What is your comment on this?","I have also noted the fervent declaration of this retired general. It can be said that every word carries weight and every sentence rings with resolve. It has stirred the deep-rooted, profound patriotic sentiment of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait and has drawn wide attention and unanimous praise from netizens on both sides. Whampoa Military Academy, founded a century ago, is a precious historical treasure shared by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The appeal made by retired Taiwan generals during the centennial commemoration of Whampoa fully demonstrates the Whampoa people on the island's commitment to upholding the Whampoa spirit of patriotism and revolution, and their steadfast pursuit of national reunification and the rejuvenation of China. This once again shows that no matter how painstakingly the DPP authorities attempt to \"de-Sinicize,\" they cannot sever the Chinese heart of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, cannot weaken the Chinese sentiment of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and cannot block the Chinese Dream of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","Regarding the mainland’s decision to further suspend tariff concessions on some ECFA products, the DPP authorities, trying to downplay the concerns of relevant industry operators on the island and public dissatisfaction with its governance, said the follow-on impact is “within controllable range.” What is your comment on this?","Whether the impact is controllable is something the relevant industry players on the island feel most keenly and have the most right to speak on, and it is not something the DPP authorities can conceal with empty words. Since the DPP authorities do not wish to suspend ECFA, they should change their approach of pursuing “independence” and provoking confrontation, eliminate trade barriers against the mainland, and restore and expand normal cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Regarding the opening of ECFA-related products, by what means does the mainland consider it appropriate for the two sides of the Strait to handle this?","Under WTO rules, Taiwan should lift trade restrictions on the mainland. In every WTO trade policy review concerning Taiwan, the Secretariat's reports have mentioned this, and the mainland has clearly expressed concern in its statements, urging Taiwan to fulfill its WTO commitments and amend non-compliant measures. But the DPP authorities still adopt discriminatory trade policies against the mainland and continue to unilaterally restrict the import of more than 2,500 mainland products. They are the troublemakers of cross-Strait trade and the instigators behind the repeated suspension of tariff reductions for ECFA early-harvest products.\nThe 23 cross-Strait agreements, including ECFA, were all signed on the common political basis of the '1992 Consensus.' Any issue related to ECFA can only be resolved through cross-Strait consultation on the basis of the '1992 Consensus.'","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","The Japanese government recently released a draft plan to evacuate residents of five municipalities in Okinawa and the Sakishima Islands to prefectures in Kyushu and Yamaguchi Prefecture. Some Taiwanese media have said the Japanese government formulated the relevant plan in response to the so-called “Taiwan contingency.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","As is well known, the root cause of tension in the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' obstinate adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, and their eagerness to cater to external forces' scheme of “using Taiwan to contain China,” continually provoking through “independence” maneuvers. If the relevant countries sincerely hope to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they must adhere to the One-China Principle, clearly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and not send any wrong signal in any form to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-12","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","Recently, the defense ministers of the United States, Japan and South Korea held talks in Singapore and stated: “We strongly oppose attempts to unilaterally change the status quo by force in the Indo-Pacific, emphasize the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and agree to establish a new joint military exercise covering multiple domains.” What is your comment?","For some time, the United States has continuously sought to draw some countries into expressing so-called “concern” about “peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.” Its essence is to find a pretext for interfering in China’s internal affairs and meddling in the Taiwan question. It must be pointed out that the culprits undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are precisely the DPP authorities, who constantly plot independence and provoke, and certain external forces, which frequently engage in interference. If relevant countries truly hope for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they should earnestly adhere to the one-China principle and clearly and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.”\nToday’s press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240612_12627170.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-06-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","US President Biden, in an interview with Time magazine, said that if military conflict breaks out across the Taiwan Strait, the possibility of US military intervention cannot be ruled out. Paparo, commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, also said the US military plans to make large-scale use of drones, unmanned surface vessels, and underwater systems to defend Taiwan. According to reports, 27 US defense…","Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and how to resolve the Taiwan question is the internal affair of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, which brooks no foreign interference. It must be pointed out that \"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable, and \"Taiwan independence\" means war. We urge the US side to clearly recognize the ambitions and harm of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, earnestly abide by its commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" stop sending any seriously wrong signals in any form, and avoid aggravating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that \"resisting reunification by force\" is a dead end, and no matter how many weapons they buy with the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people, it will be futile. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue its training and combat preparations without pause, will keep striking at \"independence\" and promoting reunification without stopping, will not hesitate to thwart foreign interference, and will resolutely fulfill its mission of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16315985.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that Lai Ching-te recently inspected the “Sea Front Brigade” in Taitung and posed for a photo with the “Hsiung Feng III” missile vehicle, stating that he will “use land to control the sea” in order to counter the PLA. The head of Taiwan's defense department said that if the PLA enters within 12 nautical miles of the island of Taiwan, threatening Taiwan's “sea and air space,” the island will exercise…","Taiwan is part of China, so what “right of self-defense” could there possibly be? The Lai Ching-te authorities are deliberately putting on a show to bolster their courage, which only further reveals their essentially weak nature, fierce in appearance but timid within. The PLA has always been an invincible and powerful force, and will resolutely counterattack and punish any provocation aimed at seeking “independence.” For “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to obstruct the PLA is no different from a moth flying into a flame. The more they make a racket, the faster they will perish.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16315985.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-06-17","Lin Jian","China Daily","The G7 Leaders’ Communiqué again hyped up China-related issues, making irresponsible comments on the situation in the Taiwan Strait, pointing fingers on issues related to the East China Sea, the South China Sea, Hong Kong, Xinjiang and Xizang, and trumpeting up so-called “Chinese overcapacity.” What is China’s comment on this?","The G7 Leaders’ Communiqué again used China-related issues to vilify and attack China, resorting to the same old false accusations that have no factual, legal or moral basis and are filled with arrogance, bias and falsehood.\nThe G7 does not represent the world. The seven countries only account for 10 percent of the world’s population; year after year their share in global economy has kept dropping; even combined, they contribute less than China to global economic growth; and their economic aggregate in terms of purchasing power parity has already been surpassed by BRICS countries. The G7 has long strayed from its original purpose of coordinating for stability in the global economic environment, and has increasingly become a political tool to perpetuate US and Western supremacy. It puts its own rules and decisions above the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and the international law, and has lost its ability to represent the world and credibility among the international community.\nThe G7 is acting against the world trend of peaceful development. While claiming to safeguard world peace, the G7 keeps drawing lines along difference in ideology and values, hyping up the false narrative of “democracy vs. autocracy,” forming exclusive groupings and inciting bloc confrontation, fanning up flames and shirking responsibilities in regional conflicts, sending military vessels and aircraft into the Asia-Pacific to create tensions, and arming Taiwan to threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. These wrongful moves that disrupt international order and harm peace and security are being increasingly disdained and rejected by forces for good in the world.\nThe G7 is no longer on the right path of win-win cooperation. In recent years, the US has repeatedly overstretched the concept of national security, abused export control measures, rolled out unilateral sanctions, fiercely gone after Chinese companies, and encouraged its allies to take the same wrong moves. This seriously violates the principles of market economy and fair competition and disrupts the international economic and trade order. The G7’s “Chinese overcapacity” allegation is unsupported by facts or the laws of economy. It is just an excuse for protectionism and undermines the global effort for green and low-carbon transition and cooperation on climate response. The G7 is the one truly responsible for “economic coercion” as it continues to politicize and weaponize trade, which is a reversal of our globalized world where countries’ interests are already deeply integrated. Such behavior will eventually backfire on the G7 itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463240.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240617_11437274.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-19","Lin Jian","Yonhap News Agency","The ROK-China diplomatic and security dialogue was held in Seoul yesterday. According to the readout from the ROK Foreign Ministry, China noted at the dialogue that its policy on the Peninsula issue remains unchanged and China is ready to continue to play a constructive role in solving the Peninsula issue. The Chinese side also met with ROK Foreign Minister Cho Tae-yul, and said that China hopes the engagement…","On June 18, Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Sun Weidong and Deputy Director of the Office for International Military Cooperation of the Central Military Commission Zhang Baoqun co-chaired the first China-ROK 2+2 vice-ministerial level diplomatic and security dialogue with Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Kim Hong Kyun and Director General of International Policy Bureau of the Ministry of National Defense Lee Seung-buhm of the ROK in Seoul. The two sides communicated their diplomatic and security policies, and had candid and in-depth exchanges of views on bilateral relations and international and regional issues of mutual interest. On the same day, Vice Foreign Minister Sun Weidong and relevant officials also met with ROK Foreign Minister Cho Tae-yul.\nBoth sides stressed that they value and would like to grow the good neighborly relations and mutually-beneficial cooperation between the two countries. They agreed to actively carry out dialogue and exchanges at all levels and in various areas, step up communication, enhance political mutual trust and advance practical cooperation through dialogue mechanisms including the high-level strategic dialogue between the foreign ministries, the 2+2 diplomatic and security dialogue and the track 1.5 dialogue, and promote the sound and steady development of the China-ROK strategic cooperative partnership. The two sides agreed to enhance exchanges at the sub-national level and between the youth to steadily improve the friendly relations between the two peoples. China stated its solemn position on issues bearing on China’s core interests and major concerns, such as the Taiwan question, and asked the ROK to handle these issues properly. The ROK reiterated that it remains unchanged in its position of respecting the one-China principle.\nThe Chinese side pointed out that China champions the common, comprehensive, cooperative and sustainable security vision, practices true multilateralism, advocates that countries’ legitimate security concerns should be respected, advances global security cooperation through dialogue and consultation, and opposes hegemonism, unilateralism and power politics. China and the ROK, having both benefited from economic globalization, need to jointly safeguard the stable and unimpeded global industrial and supply chains, reject turning economic issues into political or security issues, and oppose all forms of trade protectionism and moves to build walls and set up obstacles.\nThe two sides communicated their positions and views on the Korean Peninsula issue. China stressed that safeguarding peace and stability on the Peninsula is consistent with the common interests of all parties, including China and the ROK. How the Korean Peninsula issue developed into the current situation and where the crux lies is clear. The pressing task is to cool down the situation, avoid escalation of confrontation and rivalry, and keep to the major direction of political settlement. China has always determined its position on the merits of the matter itself and will continue to play a constructive role in its own way in the Peninsula affairs.\nThe ROK mentioned the engagement and cooperation between the DPRK and Russia. The Chinese side noted that the DPRK and Russia, as friendly and close neighbors, have the legitimate need for exchanges, cooperation and development of relations. Relevant high-level engagement is the bilateral arrangement between two sovereign countries. Holding the first vice-ministerial level diplomatic and security dialogue between China and the ROK was agreed quite early on by the two sides in light of the need of growing bilateral relations and has no particular link to the engagement between other countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463242.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240619_11438422.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-20","Lin Jian","China News Service","It’s reported that the Defense Security Cooperation Agency of the US Department of Defense said in two press releases that the State Department has made a determination approving military sales of Switchblade 300 and ALTIUS 600M-V Unmanned Aerial Vehicles as well as relevant equipment and training manuals to Taiwan for an estimated cost of US$ 360 million in total. What’s China’s comment?","In disregard of China’s repeated opposition and serious protests, the US once again sold arms to China’s Taiwan region. Such sales seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The sales undermine China’s sovereignty and security interests, harm China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and send a gravely wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly condemns and firmly opposes this.\nThe US’s frequent arms sales to Taiwan embolden the DPP authorities as they cling to the stance of “Taiwan independence” and make deliberate provocations on the one-China principle. This once again shows that the separatist moves for “Taiwan independence” and connivance and support for such moves from US-led external forces are the biggest threat facing cross-Strait peace and stability and source of damage to the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. Let me stress that the DPP authorities’ attempt to seek independence through military build-up and what the US has done to assist that agenda will only backfire and lead nowhere.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. No one should underestimate China’s firm determination and ability to oppose “Taiwan independence” and safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. China urges the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, revoke its wrongful decisions to sell arms to Taiwan, stop the dangerous trend of arming Taiwan, stop wrongful moves to connive at and support “Taiwan independence” forces, and stop endangering cross-Strait peace and stability. We will take strong and resolute measures to defend our national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463243.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240620_11439108.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-21","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","We’ve seen reports that the US and China held informal nuclear talks in March. Apparently, Chinese representatives told their US counterparts at the meetings that they wouldn’t resort to atomic threats over Taiwan. Can you confirm that these talks happened? We are curious were they Track II talks? And do you have any other details?","I will not comment on China-US Track II talks.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463244.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240621_11439741.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-06-21","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency recently announced that the U.S. side has approved two batches of arms sales to Taiwan totaling about 360 million U.S. dollars, including two types of drones and supporting system services. What comments do you have on this?","The United States' sale of weapons to Taiwan, China seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” seriously violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously damages the military-to-military relations between China and the United States and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and threatens the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We firmly oppose this and have lodged stern representations with the US side.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to “seek independence by force” and the United States' insistence on “aiding independence by force” are the greatest threats to current peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The United States frequently sells arms to Taiwan, using the hard-earned money of Taiwan people to fatten its own military-industrial complex, and is willing to turn Taiwan into a “powder keg.” This is nothing less than robbery and murder for money, and is the height of selfishness and hypocrisy. The DPP authorities' “seeking independence by relying on outsiders” means that no matter how many weapons they buy, they cannot bring security; they will only draw the flames of war to Taiwan, and the “chess piece” will ultimately become a “discarded piece.”\nWe urge the US side to earnestly honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan in any way, and maintain through concrete actions the hard-won stabilization of China-US relations and the military-to-military relationship. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will fully strengthen training and combat readiness and firmly crush all schemes of “Taiwan independence” secession.","","https://xinwen.bjd.com.cn/content/s667529d6e4b07e497a96efe1.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Dear journalist friends, good afternoon! Welcome to the special press conference jointly held by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and relevant departments.\nThe situation in the Taiwan Strait is currently complex and grave. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, loudly promote “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, and attempt to “seek independence by relying on external forces” and “seek independence through force,” which seriously violates mainstream public opinion on the island, seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously endangers national sovereignty, security, and development interests. Toward stubborn elements who engage in vile “independence”-related words and deeds and rampant “independence” activities, we will absolutely not tolerate, will absolutely not show leniency, will absolutely not stand by and let it be, and must counter and punish them.\nTo severely crack down on the crime of “Taiwan independence” stubborn elements splitting the country and inciting to split the country, on May 26, the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of State Security, and the Ministry of Justice jointly formulated and issued the “Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with the Law the Crime of ‘Taiwan Independence’ Stubborn Elements Splitting the Country and Inciting to Split the Country,” which was released and took effect today.\nTo help everyone fully and accurately understand this important judicial document concerning Taiwan, our office has specially invited Ma Yan, Presiding Judge of the Second Criminal Division of the Supreme People's Court and member of its Judicial Committee; Zhang Qingbin, Deputy Director of the Major Crimes Procuratorial Department of the Supreme People's Procuratorate; Sun Ping, Deputy Director and first-level inspector of the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security; and Tian Xin, Director of the Lawyer Work Bureau of the Ministry of Justice, to introduce and interpret the background of formulation, main content, and key provisions of this judicial document.\nFirst, we invite Presiding Judge Ma Yan of the Second Criminal Division of the Supreme People's Court to introduce the background of formulation and main content of the “Opinions.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","","Ladies and gentlemen, good afternoon! I would like to brief you on the relevant circumstances of the issuance of the Opinions.\n1. Background to the formulation of the Opinions. The Constitution of the People's Republic of China expressly stipulates that Taiwan is a sacred part of the territory of the People's Republic of China. The Anti-Secession Law expressly stipulates that safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is a common obligation of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and that the state will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to separate Taiwan from China under any name or by any means, thereby clarifying the state's red lines and bottom lines on the Taiwan question. The Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China stipulates the crime of secession of the state and the crime of inciting secession of the state, which provide ample legal basis for holding die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements criminally liable in accordance with the law.\nFor some time, a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements have been carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities on a large scale, seriously endangering peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and seriously harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Holding die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements who split the country and undermine national unification criminally liable in accordance with the law is an inevitable requirement of the rule that laws must be observed and violations must be pursued, and an appropriate measure to defend national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity.\nTo thoroughly implement Xi Jinping Thought on the Rule of Law and the CPC's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of State Security and the Ministry of Justice, after study and deliberation, jointly formulated the Opinions.\n2. Main content of the Opinions. Based on the provisions of the Anti-Secession Law, the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China and other laws, as well as relevant judicial interpretations, the Opinions clearly stipulate the overall requirements, standards for conviction and sentencing, and procedural norms for lawfully punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements for the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state. The Opinions consist of 22 articles in total. The main contents include the following:\nFirst, targeting separatist conduct, clarify the standards for determining the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements. In response to separatist conduct by a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements who organize, plan and carry out “legal Taiwan independence,” “relying on external forces to seek independence,” “seeking independence through armed force” and similar acts, the Opinions, in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law, specify the concrete circumstances in which the crime of secession of the state and the crime of inciting secession of the state apply to die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, and stipulate the determination of “ringleaders,” “serious crimes,” “active participation” and similar concepts involved in the relevant crimes, providing clear guidance for judicial handling of cases.\nSecond, based on the principle of strict punishment in accordance with the law, reaffirm circumstances such as aggravated punishment and the non-application of statutes of limitations. In response to conduct by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements colluding with external forces to seek independence, the Opinions, in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law, specify that those who collude with foreign countries or overseas institutions, organizations or individuals to commit the crimes of secession of the state or inciting secession of the state shall be punished more severely in accordance with the law. For criminal conduct that is continuous or ongoing, the Opinions emphasize that the statute of limitations is calculated from the day the criminal conduct ends. For die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements who evade investigation or trial after a case has been filed for investigation by the public security or state security authorities or accepted by the people's court, the statute of limitations does not apply.\nThird, adhere to the principle that punishment must fit the crime, reflecting the basic requirements of the criminal policy of combining leniency and severity. On the basis of adhering to strictness in accordance with the law, the Opinions fully implement the criminal policy of combining leniency and severity, ensuring that severity is applied where severity is warranted, leniency is applied where leniency is warranted, and punishment fits the crime. The Opinions specifically stipulate that where a die-hard “Taiwan independence” element voluntarily abandons the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” no longer engages in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and takes measures to mitigate or eliminate the harmful consequences or prevent their expansion, and this conforms to the relevant provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law, the case may be withdrawn, not prosecuted, or the suspect may be not prosecuted on one or more of several suspected offenses.\nFourth, follow legal procedures and standardize the handling of cases of the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements. The Opinions stipulate that criminal suspects and defendants enjoy the right to defense in accordance with the law. They clarify that trials in absentia may be applied in accordance with the law to cases of the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, and make clear provisions on procedural rights such as the right to defense and the right to appeal in trials in absentia.\nFifth, tighten the criminal legal net and reinforce the rule-of-law defense line against “Taiwan independence.” To effectively prevent and punish other crimes committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements beyond secession of the state and inciting secession of the state, the Opinions stipulate in the supplementary provisions that other crimes, such as the crime of providing funding for activities that endanger national security committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, may be handled with reference to the Opinions.\nIt should be pointed out that the Opinions target only a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and their separatist activities, and do not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nGoing forward, the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of State Security and the Ministry of Justice will guide local people's courts, people's procuratorates, public security organs, state security organs and judicial administrative organs to strictly implement the Criminal Law, the Criminal Procedure Law and the Opinions, resolutely punish in accordance with the law the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state committed by die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, and firmly defend national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity.\nThank you all!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The “Opinions” clearly define the specific circumstances under which the crime of splitting the country and the crime of inciting to split the country apply to “Taiwan independence” diehards. Could you introduce in detail how the “Opinions” stipulate this?","Chen Binhua: This question is to be answered by Judge Ma of the Supreme People's Court.\nMa Yan, member of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court and presiding judge of the Second Criminal Division:\nThank you for the reporter's question. Article 103 of the Criminal Law provides for the crime of splitting the State and the crime of inciting to split the State. Whoever organizes, plans, or carries out the splitting of the State or the undermining of national unity constitutes the crime of splitting the State; whoever incites the splitting of the State or the undermining of national unity constitutes the crime of inciting to split the State.\nRegarding the crime of splitting the State, the Opinions stipulate four specific circumstances and one catch-all provision. First, initiating and establishing a “Taiwan independence” separatist organization, planning and formulating a “Taiwan independence” separatist action program, plan, or scheme, and directing members of the “Taiwan independence” separatist organization or other persons to carry out activities to split the State or undermine national unity. This is a typical mode of conduct for the crime of splitting the State.\nSecond, through formulating, amending, interpreting, or abolishing relevant regulations of Taiwan, or through “referendums” and similar means, attempting to change the legal status of Taiwan as part of China. This mainly targets the “Taiwan independence” die-hards who manipulate “legal Taiwan independence.”\nThird, through promoting Taiwan's accession to international organizations open only to sovereign states, or conducting official exchanges or military contacts with other countries, attempting to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” in the international community. This circumstance mainly targets the separatist conduct of “Taiwan independence” die-hards who expand so-called “international space” and seek independence by relying on foreign forces or by military means.\nFourth, using their authority to extensively distort or falsify the fact that Taiwan is part of China in the fields of education, culture, history, and news media, or suppressing political parties, groups, or individuals that support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national unification. In order to achieve the goal of splitting the country, “Taiwan independence” die-hards use their authority to manipulate “gradual Taiwan independence” and suppress the righteous forces supporting unification. Because the harm is severe, this has been stipulated as a circumstance of the crime of splitting the State.\nRegarding the crime of inciting to split the State, the Opinions stipulate one specific circumstance and one catch-all provision. They explicitly provide that whoever, for the purpose of separating Taiwan from China, stubbornly promotes the “Taiwan independence” separatist proposition and its separatist action program, plan, or scheme shall be convicted and punished for the crime of inciting to split the State.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台看台海和日月潭天新媒体记者","Question: How will public security organs implement the 'Opinions' to crack down on 'Taiwan independence' diehards?","Chen Binhua:\nThis question will be answered by Vice Minister Sun Ping of the Ministry of Public Security.\nSun Ping, Deputy Director of the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security and first-grade inspector:\nThank you for your question. The Opinions jointly issued by the “Two High Courts and Three Ministries” provide public security organs with more powerful legal weapons to combat, in accordance with the law, “Taiwan independence” diehards who commit the crimes of splitting the country and inciting to split the country. They also provide more precise guidance on accurately determining crimes and correctly applying procedures.\nWith regard to the criminal acts of “Taiwan independence” diehards who split the country or incite to split the country, public security organs will handle cases strictly in accordance with statutory procedures and, together with relevant departments, pursue their criminal liability in accordance with the law. For the principal offenders and those whose crimes are serious, we will place particular emphasis on combating them and punish them severely in accordance with the law.\nAt the same time, for those who voluntarily abandon the “Taiwan independence” secessionist position, no longer engage in “Taiwan independence” secessionist activities, and take measures to mitigate or eliminate the consequences of harm or prevent the expansion of harm, and who meet the statutory conditions, public security organs may, after approval in accordance with the law, also withdraw the case in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","人民法院报记者","'Taiwan independence' is a grave crime of splitting the country. How do the 'Opinions' embody strict punishment of die-hard 'Taiwan independence' elements?","Chen Binhua: This question should be answered by Presiding Judge Ma of the Supreme People's Court.\nMa Yan, member of the Adjudication Committee of the Supreme People's Court and presiding judge of the Second Criminal Tribunal: The crime of splitting the state and the crime of inciting to split the state are listed in Chapter 1 of the Special Part of the Criminal Law, and they are among the most serious crimes by nature. \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities seriously endanger national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity. Therefore, the Opinions adhere to a position of strictly punishing according to law the crimes of splitting the state and inciting to split the state committed by \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners, which can be summarized as \"three strictnesses\":\nFirst, tighten the legal net. The Opinions focus on \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners whose words and deeds promoting \"independence\" are egregious and whose activities plotting \"independence\" are rampant. By sorting out and listing typical \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct, they clarify the specific circumstances in which the crimes of splitting the state and inciting to split the state apply to \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners, so as to precisely combat and punish them. At the same time, they clarify that other crimes committed by \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners, such as the crime of funding activities that endanger national security, may be handled by reference to the Opinions, weaving a tighter legal net to punish \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners.\nSecond, strictly pursue accountability. Given that \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners mainly operate in the Taiwan region and abroad, the Opinions expressly provide that cases of splitting the state and inciting to split the state by \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners may apply the in absentia trial procedure according to law. For provocateurs who refuse to repent and brazenly plot \"independence\" and provoke, the Opinions provide that where the criminal conduct of \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners in splitting the state or inciting to split the state is in a continuous or ongoing state, the prosecution period is calculated from the day the criminal conduct ends. These provisions are mutually connected and reflect the resolute attitude of punishing \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners without leniency.\nThird, severely punish. The Opinions highlight the focus of combating these crimes and, for circumstances of serious harm that deserve severe punishment, specify the criteria for determining \"grave circumstances\" and \"active participation\" in the crimes of splitting the state and inciting to split the state, providing guidance for strict punishment. For example, the Opinions provide that a person who repeatedly participates in separatist activities of a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist organization, or who plays a backbone role in such an organization or actively assists the principal offender in organizing or leading it, shall be deemed to have \"actively participated\" in the crime of splitting the state and shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years and not more than ten years according to law. A person who commits inciting to split the state where the circumstances are serious, the consequences are grave, or the impact is especially egregious shall be deemed to have committed a \"grave crime\" and shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years according to law. In addition, those who collude with foreign or overseas institutions, organizations or individuals to commit the crimes of splitting the state or inciting to split the state shall be punished more severely according to law.\nIt should be emphasized that strictly punishing according to law the crimes of splitting the state and inciting to split the state committed by \"Taiwan independence\" hardliners is a general assessment. While adhering to overall strictness, the Opinions also include some provisions for leniency, in order to fully implement the criminal policy of combining leniency with severity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The 'Opinions' mention that die-hard 'Taiwan independence' elements may be tried in absentia. Could you introduce the specific provisions and the main considerations behind them?","Chen Binhua:\nThis question will be answered by Deputy Procurator-General Zhang Qingbin of the Supreme People's Procuratorate.\nZhang Qingbin, Deputy Director of the Major Crimes Prosecution Department of the Supreme People's Procuratorate:\nThank you for your question. According to the relevant provisions on trial in absentia procedures in Chapter 3 of Part 5 of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, for crimes that seriously endanger national security where timely trial is required, public prosecution may be brought against defendants located abroad in accordance with law, upon approval by the Supreme People's Procuratorate. These provisions demonstrate the state's firm resolve to combat crimes that seriously endanger national security and provide a clear legal basis for severely punishing serious crimes that endanger national security.\nThe “Opinions” restate and clarify this provision. They target “Taiwan independence” diehards who turn their backs on the righteousness of the nation and go against the wishes of the people, and who seriously endanger national sovereignty, security, and development interests. For those diehards whose “separatist” words and deeds are vile and whose separatist activities are rampant, no matter where they are, they will not escape the punishment of national law.\nAs long as our law enforcement and judicial authorities determine that timely prosecution and trial are necessary, then with the approval of the Supreme People's Procuratorate, public security organs and state security organs may transfer cases to the people's procuratorate for prosecution in accordance with law even when the criminal suspect is not present. If the people's procuratorate, after review, determines that the facts of the crime are clear, the evidence is reliable and sufficient, and criminal liability should be pursued in accordance with law, it may file public prosecution with the people's court. If the people's court, after review, finds that the conditions for applying trial in absentia are met, it shall decide to hold a court hearing.\nFor those “Taiwan independence” diehards who remain deluded and stubbornly unrepentant, do not harbor any illusions. As long as they have committed crimes of splitting the country or inciting secession, we will absolutely not tolerate them, will not show leniency, will not stand idly by, and will certainly pursue them to the end and severely punish them in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the criminal acts of “Taiwan independence” diehards in splitting the country and inciting secession, how are the statute of limitations for prosecution specifically prescribed?","Chen Binhua:\nThis question will be answered by Deputy Minister Sun Ping of the Ministry of Public Security.\nSun Ping, Deputy Director of the Legal Affairs Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security and First-Grade Inspector:\nThank you, reporter, for your question. According to Articles 87, 88, and 89 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China and the relevant provisions on crimes endangering national security, different prosecution periods are stipulated for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting secession, depending on the circumstances of the crime. Taking as examples those who are “principal offenders” or whose crimes are “grave”: the crime of inciting secession carries a maximum statutory penalty of more than five years of fixed-term imprisonment, and its prosecution period is fifteen years; the crime of splitting the country carries a maximum statutory penalty of death, and its prosecution period is twenty years; for crimes of splitting the country that are exceptionally egregious, have exceptionally severe consequences, and for which criminal liability must be pursued in accordance with law, prosecution may still be pursued in accordance with law even after the twenty-year prosecution period has expired, once it has been reported through legal procedures and approved by the Supreme People's Procuratorate.\nAccording to the provisions of the “Opinions” issued by the two supreme judicial organs and three ministries, I would like to stress two further points. First, if a crime of splitting the country or inciting secession is committed continuously or is an ongoing act, the time during which the continuous or ongoing state persists is not counted toward the prosecution period; the prosecution period begins only from the day the crime ends. This means that as long as the splitting acts of “Taiwan independence” diehards do not stop, the sword of legal accountability will remain hanging overhead.\nSecond, if, after a crime of splitting the country or inciting secession has been put on file for investigation, or a people's court has accepted the case, the criminal suspect or defendant evades investigation or trial, the limitation on the prosecution period does not apply. In other words, for “Taiwan independence” diehards who commit crimes of splitting the country or inciting secession, once the investigating authorities have opened a case for investigation or a people's court has accepted the case, no matter where they flee, they will be held accountable for life in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Some Taiwan residents may worry that this judicial document will affect their freedom of speech and may have concerns about participating in cross-Strait exchanges. What is the spokesperson’s response?","Using criminal justice measures to punish those who commit crimes of splitting the country and to safeguard the country's core interests is a common practice worldwide. Taiwan is part of China, and the country will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means. Punishing “Taiwan independence” die-hards for splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country in accordance with the law is reasonable, just and lawful.\nThe “Opinions” make clear, from the title to the body text, that criminal punishment measures target only the extremely few die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements whose words and deeds are vile and whose “independence” plotting is rampant, along with the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country that they commit. They do not involve the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest source of disaster that brings war danger to the Taiwan Strait and harms the interests of the people of Taiwan. Only by severely punishing “Taiwan independence” separatist crimes in accordance with the law can Taiwan compatriots enjoy the dividends of peaceful cross-Strait development and truly live in peace and tranquility.\nWe always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and we warmly welcome and support the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots in taking part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields and sharing the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, follow the great trend of history, fully recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of “Taiwan independence” separatism, stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and with practical action safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being. We hope they will work with compatriots on the mainland to jointly create a bright future of peaceful cross-Strait development and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","法治日报记者","Please introduce the relevant provisions of the “Opinions” on the right to defense of criminal suspects and defendants, and the main considerations behind them.","Chen Binhua:\nThis question will be answered by Tian Xin, Director of the Lawyers Affairs Bureau of the Ministry of Justice.\nTian Xin, Director of the Lawyers Affairs Bureau of the Ministry of Justice:\nThank you, friend from the press, for your question. According to the provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People’s Republic of China, criminal suspects and defendants enjoy the right to defense in accordance with the law. When “Taiwan independence” diehards are suspected of crimes such as splitting the state or inciting the splitting of the state, and are held criminally liable in accordance with the law, they enjoy procedural rights such as the right to defense in accordance with the law.\nArticles 16 and 19 of the Opinions provide specific provisions on how criminal suspects and defendants may entrust defenders, reflecting the unity of combating and deterring crime with lawfully safeguarding the rights and interests of criminal suspects and defendants. When criminal suspects, defendants, or their close relatives entrust lawyers for defense, they shall comply with the Criminal Procedure Law, the Lawyers Law, the Legal Aid Law, and other laws and regulations, as well as the provisions of these Opinions. For example, in trial in absentia proceedings, a defendant has the right to entrust one or two defenders, or to have a close relative entrust them on the defendant’s behalf. Where a defendant and their close relatives have not entrusted a defender, the people’s court shall notify the legal aid institution to assign a lawyer to provide defense for the defendant.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","香港《中评社》记者","The “Opinions” explicitly punish “Taiwan independence” diehards. Besides the 10 people the mainland side has already announced, will others also be involved?","I will answer this question. For “Taiwan independence” diehards who commit the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country as stipulated in the Opinions, national law enforcement and judicial organs will take resolute punitive measures and punish them strictly according to law, without leniency. I advise the “Taiwan independence” diehards, in the face of the net of punishing “independence” and the sword of criminal law, to recognize the situation as early as possible, rein in before the cliff, and quickly and thoroughly reform their past wrongs.\nThank you, journalists. Today's special press conference is now concluded. Thank you also to the chief judges, department heads, and bureau chiefs for attending. Xinhua News Agency will be authorized to publish the full text of the Opinions shortly. We welcome everyone to keep following the reporting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240621_12629599.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-21","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 21 — On the 21st, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a special press conference, inviting Ma Yan, member of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court and head of the Second Criminal Division of the Supreme People's Court; Zhang Qingbin, deputy director of the Major Crimes Prosecution Department of the Supreme People's Procuratorate; Sun Ping, deputy…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, pointed out that using criminal judicial means to punish separatist criminals and safeguard the core interests of the country is a common practice of countries around the world. Punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards according to law for the crimes of separating the country and inciting separation of the country is reasonable, lawful and proper. The “Opinions,” from the title to the main text, clearly state that the criminal punishment measures target only an extremely small number of diehards whose words and deeds in support of “independence” are egregious and whose “independence”-seeking activities are rampant, and the crimes of separating the country and inciting separation of the country that they commit. They do not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nHe said that “Taiwan independence” is the greatest source of disaster that brings war and peril to Taiwan and harms the interests of the people. Only by punishing “Taiwan independence” separatist crimes severely according to law can Taiwan compatriots enjoy the dividends of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and live peaceful and tranquil good lives. We advise “Taiwan independence” diehards to recognize the situation as soon as possible, pull back from the brink without delay, and quickly repent and change their ways. (Reporters: Shi Longhong, Zhao Bo, Shang Hao, Liu Huan)","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240621_12629682.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-06-24","Mao Ning","CCTV","It was reported that the foreign affairs office of the Taiwan region released a statement on June 20, criticizing the recent Joint Statement Between the People’s Republic of China and Malaysia on Deepening the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership towards China-Malaysia Community with a Shared Future, which reiterates Malaysia’s commitment to the One China Policy, and says that “Taiwan is an inalienable territory…","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is the political foundation for China to establish and grow diplomatic relations with all countries in the world, including Malaysia. In the 1974 joint communiqué between China and Malaysia on establishing diplomatic relations, the government of Malaysia unequivocally acknowledged the position of the Chinese government that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Malaysian side reiterated this position in the recent high-level exchanges with China. This fully shows that the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the right thing to do. The Taiwan authorities’ statement advocating Taiwan’s so-called “country” status further exposes their “Taiwan independence” agenda. That, however, will only be rejected and disdained and will not shake the abiding commitment of the international community to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463245.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240624_11440521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-24","Mao Ning","CCTV","On June 21, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a decision on its website on countermeasures against Lockheed Martin’s entities and senior executives. Do you have any further comment?","The US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, interfere in China’s internal affairs, and undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In accordance with the law, China took countermeasures against relevant company’s entities and senior executives that are engaged in arms sales to Taiwan.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. No country, organization or individual shall underestimate the strong determination, will and ability of the Chinese government and people to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity, or be under the illusion that they could tread or even cross the line on the Taiwan question without any consequence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463245.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240624_11440521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-24","Mao Ning","AP","A report released today from the cybersecurity firm Recorded Futures has claimed that Chinese hackers have stepped up cyberattacks and attempted hacking of dozens of Taiwanese organizations, including government and critical technology companies. These attacks were observed between November 2023 and April 2024. The report also states that these hacks are likely “state-sponsored.” Does the Foreign Ministry have…","I am not aware of the specifics you mentioned. What I can tell you is that this is not the first time that the company you mentioned has fabricated disinformation on so-called “Chinese hacking operations.” There is absolutely no professionalism or credibility to speak of in what the company does.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463245.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240624_11440521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-25","Mao Ning","China Review News","On June 24, the spokesperson of the US State Department condemned China’s Guidelines on Imposing Criminal Punishments on Diehard “Taiwan Independence” Separatists for Conducting or Inciting Secession, saying that China’s decision will escalate the situation and undermine stability, and that China should exercise restraint and stop any unilateral attempt to change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait. What is the…","China deplores and strongly opposes the remarks made by the US side. Every sovereign state has the sacred right to safeguard its national unity and territorial integrity. It is a universal practice to punish secessionists and safeguard the core interests of the country through criminal jurisdiction. No external force is in any position to point fingers. The investigation on the criminal responsibility for hellbent attempts of Taiwan separatist forces to split the country and undermine national unity is necessary for making sure the law is abided by and anyone who breaks the law is brought to justice. It is critical for safeguarding the one-China principle and national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity, and for upholding the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe true status quo in the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait as fire with water. The greatest threat to cross-Strait peace is “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign interference and disruption. If the US side truly hopes to contribute to peace and stability in the region, it should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop interfering in China’s internal affairs and stop sending any wrong signal in any form to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463246.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240625_11441266.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-06-25","Mao Ning","Beijing Youth Daily","We noted that the Senior Officials Meeting of the Second Horn of Africa Peace Conference was held in Beijing yesterday. Can you share with us more details?","The Senior Officials Meeting of the Second Horn of Africa Peace Conference was convened in Beijing yesterday. Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Chen Xiaodong attended the meeting and delivered opening remarks. Senior officials from the foreign affairs departments and diplomatic envoys of countries in Horn of Africa such as Ethiopia, Djibouti, Kenya, Somalia, Sudan, South Sudan and Uganda attended the meeting. Participants had a full exchange of views in an atmosphere of solidarity and candor. They together reviewed the positive outcomes achieved by China and Horn of Africa countries in implementing the Outlook on Peace and Development in the Horn of Africa since the first peace conference in 2022. They also reached important five-point consensus on implementing the Outlook going forward.\nFirst, focusing on peace. The parties reaffirmed the desire to solve differences and disputes in the region through peaceful means and welcomed China to play a constructive role for regional peace. Second, focusing on security. The parties stressed the need to follow the guidance of the Global Security Initiative and enhance cooperation in such areas as military, anti-terrorism, demining and training. Third, focusing on cooperation. The parties reaffirmed that they will jointly advance high-quality Belt and Road cooperation. Fourth, focusing on development. The parties are committed to further implementing the Global Development Initiative, supporting the effort of fostering a development framework of “two axes plus two coastal areas” in the Horn of Africa, accelerating the building of industrial belts and economic belts and enhancing independent development capability. Fifth, focusing on governance. The parties reiterated that they will strengthen communication and coordination, advance the reform of international governance system and jointly defend the legitimate rights of the Global South.\nChina stands ready to work with Horn of Africa countries to strive for in-depth implementation of the Outlook, focus on the three main goals of security, development and governance, jointly promote peace, cooperation and common development, and help turn the Horn of Africa into a region of peace, cooperation, development and prosperity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463246.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240625_11441266.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 16th Straits Forum, held recently, has drawn close attention from people on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce what achievements this Straits Forum has produced.","The 16th Straits Forum was successfully held in Xiamen, Fujian, on June 15. A total of 35 series events have been held, and 15 more events will be held, with fruitful results.\nFirst, Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the forum and delivered a speech, and held a symposium with 50 Taiwan compatriot representatives who have received honors from mainland systems such as the Youth League, the Federation of Trade Unions and the Women's Federation in recent years. This fully reflects the Party Central Committee's care, concern, commendation and encouragement for Taiwan compatriots who actively participate in cross-Strait integrated development.\nSecond, a large number of Taiwan compatriots enthusiastically took part in the forum, demonstrating that the people on both sides are one family. More than 7,000 Taiwan compatriots crossed the sea to attend, setting off a wave of civil exchanges across the Strait. More than half were attending the forum for the first time, and the proportions of first-time visitors and Taiwan youth reached new highs. This fully shows that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' obstruction and restriction of cross-Strait exchanges is unpopular, and that the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society is that it wants peace, development, exchange and cooperation. During the forum, a group of Taiwan compatriots described in detail their advanced achievements in developing careers on the mainland, using their vivid personal practice to illustrate cross-Strait integrated development.\nThird, the implementation of the 《Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone》 was carried through the entire forum. During the forum, the Ministry of Education and the All-China Women's Federation jointly issued 31 measures to support the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in areas such as cross-Strait educational exchanges and cooperation on women's affairs. The Memorandum on Joint Participation of Cross-Strait Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises in Building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in Fujian was signed. Fujian Province offered more than 1,600 internship and employment positions for Taiwan youth and established a Kinmen Hometown Villagers Service Station at Wutong Wharf. Xiamen and Kinmen signed multiple cooperation projects in areas such as elderly care services and youth employment and entrepreneurship. Some 10.17 million cross-Strait residents participated in the “cloud” builder network relay activity for the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge, fully expressing their shared hope of building a “same-city living circle” for Xiamen and Kinmen.\nFourth, focusing on developing new quality productive forces, the forum served Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the process of Chinese-style modernization. Events were held including the Cross-Strait Forum on Cooperation and Development in the Big Health Industry, the Chamber of Commerce Development Forum, the Forum on Integrated Development of Agriculture and Rural Areas, and the Finance Forum, encouraging Taiwan compatriots to share the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization. The construction of the “Taiwan Compatriots and Enterprises Landing Data Port No. 1” and the “Maritime Silk Road Credit Chain” was advanced, tapping the potential of digital empowerment and building a bridge for data exchange between cross-Strait enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630843.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the “Opinions on Punishing ‘Taiwan independence’ Diehards for the Crimes of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession in Accordance with Law” (hereinafter the “Opinions”), recently issued and implemented by the mainland, a few DPP public representatives have advocated that Taiwan take so-called “countermeasures.” What is your comment on this?","Punishing in accordance with the law the extremely few “Taiwan independence” diehards who engage in vicious pro-independence rhetoric and rampant separatist activities is a necessary measure to truly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and effectively protect the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. It conforms to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society, which wants peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We advise certain people on the island to recognize the situation, not to disregard public opinion, and not to go against the tide.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630841.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Regarding some people on the island who once advocated “Taiwan independence” but whose positions have since changed, will the mainland side still pursue their criminal liability?","The “Opinions on Punishing ‘Taiwan Independence’ Stubborn Elements for the Crime of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession in Accordance with the Law” were formulated strictly in accordance with the law, adhering to a balance between leniency and severity and ensuring that punishment fits the crime. If a “Taiwan independence” stubborn element voluntarily abandons the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, no longer engages in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and takes measures to mitigate or eliminate the harmful consequences or prevent the harm from expanding, then in cases that meet relevant provisions, some or even all criminal liability may be lawfully waived.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630839.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The Taiwanese newspaper Liberty Times reported that some TV stations on the island cooperated with mainland official media to produce a program called “Guiding the Wind Direction,” in which mainland resident correspondents, under instructions from the Taiwan Affairs Office, participated in the entire production process and “supervised” on site. The Mainland Affairs Council said that media outlets cooperating with…","The report in 《Liberty Times》 is a thoroughly fake news story, pure fabrication. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are using this paper to maliciously smear and attack the mainland and to deceive and mislead the people on the island, with extremely sinister intentions. The DPP authorities are accustomed to directing green-camp media and the internet troops they keep to carry out cognitive fraud against the people of Taiwan, dividing Taiwan society and inciting hostility and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. They arbitrarily frame, persecute, intimidate, and punish media that hold different positions, launch a “green terror” campaign, create a chilling effect, and brutally deprive Taiwan residents of their legitimate rights and interests, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan people and undermining the development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the deceptiveness and harmfulness of the DPP authorities' manipulation of public opinion, and will act in practice to safeguard their own legitimate rights and interests. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to immediately stop acts that, for political self-interest, harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and undermine the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Lai Qingde recently told the US magazine Time in an exclusive interview that the description of the two sides as “two countries not subordinate to each other” is based on facts, and that Tsai Ing-wen and Ma Ying-jeou have both previously put forward positions of “not subordinate to each other.” What is your comment?","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This fact cannot and will not change. Lai Qingde's so-called “mutually non-subordinate” theory is a typical “Taiwan independence” fallacy. It has neither historical or legal basis nor factual support, and fully exposes his malicious “Taiwan independence” intentions. Lai Qingde and the DPP authorities' continued stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” position and their provocation of the one-China principle will only seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and bring profound disaster to the Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630840.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently told the U.S. magazine Time in an exclusive interview: “We should engage with China with dignity and on an equal basis”; “China should show sincerity toward Taiwan's democratically elected legitimate government”; every cross-Strait issue should be mutually beneficial; and exchanges and cooperation should be guided by the shared belief of promoting the well-being of the people on both sides…","We have consistently supported and promoted cross-Strait dialogue and consultation on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and have actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The root cause of the obstruction of cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges is the DPP authorities’ stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and their refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” Lai Ching-te says “promoting the well-being of the people on both sides of the Strait” and “moving toward peace and common prosperity in the future,” but in reality he repeatedly peddles the “two-state theory,” incites cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and accelerates efforts to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “seek independence by force.” If allowed to develop, this will surely bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots.\nCompatriots in Taiwan must recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of the DPP authorities’ stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” line, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and push cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development. Only in this way can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being truly be safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630842.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The DPP recently held a seminar discussing the so-called “how the mainland influences Taiwan's elections through Mazu temples.” The Mainland Affairs Council said that it is not only Mazu, but also Baosheng Dadi, Guan Gong, and Shennong Dadi, all of which are “tools of CCP united front work against Taiwan.” This claim has caused an uproar in island public opinion, which believes that the DPP authorities are once…","Cross-Strait culture shares the same roots and origins. Large numbers of Taiwan believers continually travel to ancestral temples on the mainland to burn incense, engage in exchanges, worship ancestors, seek their roots, and pray for safety. This is their heartfelt spiritual need, and a vivid portrayal of the Cross-Strait family bond.\nWe consistently advance cross-Strait exchanges, including exchanges on folk beliefs. The DPP authorities have on multiple occasions unreasonably obstructed normal cross-Strait exchanges in religious and folk belief and culture, arousing strong dissatisfaction among temples and believers on the island. The DPP authorities have falsely claimed that folk beliefs such as Mazu are “United Front tools,” which is a great disrespect to religious circles on both sides of the Strait and a desecration of folk beliefs such as Mazu.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海记者","Taiwanese online influencer “Bo-te Wang” claimed that starting in late July, more and more Taiwanese online influencers will travel to the mainland for sightseeing and filming, hosted by the Cross-Strait Youth Association, under the invitation name of participating in the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month. He said this is the mainland “spending money on a cultural united front toward Taiwan.” What is your comment…","You may have noticed that recently, on platforms such as YouTube and Xiaohongshu, videos of foreign bloggers traveling in the mainland under the 144-hour visa-free transit policy have been extremely popular, with total views exceeding 1 billion. In fact, it is even more convenient for Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland, and they can set off on a trip at any time. Taiwan compatriots need only hold a Taiwan Compatriot Permit to enter without a visa, and they can use a Taiwan mobile phone number and bank card to link apps such as Alipay or WeChat for quick mobile payments. By high-speed rail, they can reach directly 95% of cities with populations over 500,000. They can enjoy the magnificent natural scenery of the mainland, experience its long history and culture, taste its delicious local specialties, witness its thriving economy and technology, and enjoy its progressive social life. Many Taiwan self-media personalities have already been, or are now, recording and sharing what they see and hear in the mainland through videos, which enhances mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides and dissolves mutual barriers and misunderstandings. This is something that people on both sides of the Strait are very pleased to see, and it is a good thing.\nThe internet has memory. The influencer you mentioned has also visited the mainland for exchanges and tourism many times. As long as he is willing to come to the mainland to convey positive energy, we welcome him to come again. But if he arbitrarily pins labels on people and intimidates peers, we believe people on both sides of the Strait will not support it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","According to Taiwan media reports, a parent in Taiwan recently said that when they talked with their child, who is in senior high school, about “Yu the Great Controls the Floods,” they were surprised that the child had no idea who Yu the Great was, which the parent found hard to believe. The parent questioned, “Is it the ‘108 Curriculum Guidelines’ at work?” What is your comment on this?","From “not knowing what Chinese history is” to being completely unaware of “who Yu the Great is,” the “poisonous curriculum guidelines” that the DPP authorities insist on implementing are gradually alienating Taiwan's young people from the roots of Chinese culture, provoking deep concern in Taiwan society.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation, and Chinese culture is the shared spiritual root of compatriots on both sides. No one may deprive Taiwan compatriots of the right to receive education in Chinese culture and to learn the history of the nation. With summer vacation approaching, we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan's young people, to come to the mainland: listen to the story of Yu the Great controlling the floods in Beichuan, Sichuan, his hometown; go to Yongzhou, Hunan, to recite Liu Zongyuan's “Record of the First Time Feasting and Touring West Mountain”; go to Shaoxing, Zhejiang, to copy Wang Xizhi's “Preface to the Poems Composed at the Orchid Pavilion”; and in Chibi, Hubei, imagine the Battle of Red Cliffs. What has been erased from Taiwan textbooks can all be found, seen, and experienced on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","According to relevant economic data on the island, from January to May this year, Taiwan's outbound investment increased by 60.8% compared with the same period last year, but its investment in the mainland fell by about 15.7%, and its share of Taiwan's total outbound investment dropped to 8.7%. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities are obstructing and restricting Taiwanese businesses from investing in the mainland and are promoting “decoupling and severing supply chains” in cross-Strait economic and trade relations. This fully demonstrates that the DPP authorities are obstructers and saboteurs of cross-Strait economic cooperation. They are acting against the mainstream public opinion on the island and harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan enterprises and the public.\nIt should be pointed out that Taiwanese businesspeople and compatriots are participants in and beneficiaries of cross-Strait economic cooperation, and they have the greatest say on the mainland’s business environment and the bright prospects of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. From January to May this year, cross-Strait trade reached US$109.23 billion, up 8.2% year on year. The contracted amount of Taiwanese investment in the mainland continued to grow steadily, with a clear trend of capital increases, production expansion, and reinvestment of profits. The mainland remains the first choice for Taiwanese businesses to invest, start businesses, and develop their lives. In the future, as we accelerate the building of a new development pattern, steadily promote high-quality development, and foster and strengthen new quality productive forces, the mainland’s economy will continue to demonstrate enormous vitality, potential, and bright prospects. It will be fully capable of providing stronger momentum for advancing cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and of opening up broader space.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","After the mainland announced its list of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and sanctions measures, the Mainland Affairs Council said that “the two sides are not subordinate to each other, and sanctions are illegal and invalid.” How will the “Opinions” the mainland has now issued take effect on Taiwan?","Taiwan is part of China. This is an indisputable legal fact and a general consensus of the international community. The state's punishment of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements for the crime of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country in accordance with the law has a solid legal basis and sufficient legal grounds. It is an inherent part of safeguarding national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity, and a just act to protect the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Regardless of where die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements who violate the law may be, the state's law enforcement and judicial authorities will pursue them to the end and punish them severely in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The U.S. government recently decided to sell arms to Taiwan worth approximately US$360 million. The DPP authorities expressed gratitude. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. For political self-interest, the DPP authorities use the hard-earned money of Taiwan compatriots to buy weapons, attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” This will only bring a dangerous situation of war and calamity to the Taiwan region and profound disasters to Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities should immediately stop harming the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and stop acts that endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe US, time and again, has sold arms to Taiwan. Its intention is to lead the flames of war to Taiwan, and its motives are malicious. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the “August 17 Communiqué.” It should stop selling weapons to Taiwan, stop arming Taiwan, and stop sending any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630837.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The mainland has issued the “Opinions,” Article 21 of which states, “For ‘hardcore Taiwan independence separatists,’ crimes such as the crime of providing funding for activities that endanger national security and other crimes may be handled with reference to these Opinions.” May I ask whether this provision applies to foreigners, for example, U.S. officials who support Taiwan’s accession to the…","I will answer the first question first. This judicial document targets the very few “Taiwan independence” diehards who behave viciously in promoting “independence” and engage in rampant “independence” activities. National law enforcement and judicial organs will handle cases strictly in accordance with the law, precisely punish crimes, and resolutely defend national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity.\nSecond question. The provisions of this judicial document are very rigorous, so please quote the relevant articles accurately and completely. The provision you mentioned targets those who “abuse their authority to blatantly distort and alter the fact that Taiwan is part of China in fields such as education, culture, history, and news media.”\nNational law enforcement and judicial organs will handle cases strictly in accordance with the law, precisely punish crimes, and resolutely defend national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity.\nThird question. The “Opinions” clearly indicate, from the title to the main text, that the punitive measures target the very few “Taiwan independence” diehards who behave viciously in promoting “independence” and engage in rampant “independence” activities, as well as the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country that they commit. Any “Taiwan independence” diehard who breaks the law, regardless of where they are, will be pursued to the end and severely punished according to law by national law enforcement and judicial organs.\nIt should be pointed out that this judicial document does not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and we warmly welcome and support the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields and sharing in the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization. We hope Taiwan residents will firmly oppose the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and enjoy with peace of mind the dividends of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The special promotion meeting on the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone was held in Xiamen, Fujian, on the 14th. What important role does this meeting play in advancing cross-Strait integration?","On June 14, Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, presided over a special promotion meeting on the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in Xiamen, Fujian. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, the National Development and Reform Commission and other relevant departments of 50 central and state organs, as well as relevant responsible persons of Fujian Province, attended the meeting.\nThe meeting summarized the work achievements since the release of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” and exchanged work experience. The meeting specified five key areas. First, cross-Strait integrated development should continuously deepen in concepts and approaches, continuously improve in policies and systems, and continuously make breakthroughs in practical exploration. Second, it is necessary to promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen integrated development in all fields across the Strait, and let Taiwan compatriots share the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization and enjoy the development and progress of the Chinese mainland. Third, it is necessary to apply high-quality development requirements throughout the entire process of cross-Strait integrated development, deepen cross-Strait economic integration, always respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, improve policies and systems that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and expand the scope of benefit and sense of gain for people on both sides of the Strait. Fourth, it is necessary to broaden the fields and channels of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, provide more convenience for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to study, live, work and start businesses on the Chinese mainland, and promote building a sense of the Chinese nation's community consciousness and safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation through exchange, interaction and integration. Fifth, it is necessary to explore and innovate on the experience and practices of the new path for cross-Strait integrated development, study and resolve difficult and blocked issues in policy implementation, and strengthen the overall coordination and implementation of responsibilities for integrated development work.\nNext, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will, together with relevant departments of central and state organs and relevant parties in Fujian Province, implement the spirit of the meeting, continue to introduce policy measures to help build the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, and promote new progress and new results in the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The TV drama “But Hope the Person Lives Long,” adapted from Teresa Teng's real-life experiences, recently premiered. Subsequently, mainland actor Hu Ge visited Taiwan. Some island media pointed out that this shows the mainland side has seized mainstream public opinion and demonstrates cultural confidence. What comments do you have on this?","The cross-Strait co-produced TV drama 《May We Last Forever》 has been a hit on Beijing TV and Jiangsu TV. Deng Lijun's story and sweet singing have stirred the memories and emotional resonance of mainland audiences. Mainland TV dramas such as 《Blossoms Shanghai》 and 《Joy of Life 2》 have been broadcast on the island and sparked a binge-watching craze. The lead actor of 《Blossoms Shanghai》, Hu Ge, traveled to Taiwan for cultural exchanges and was also warmly welcomed by Taiwan audiences. This kind of “two-way engagement” in the cultural and artistic fields reflects the shared aspirations and fond expectations of people on both sides of the Strait for cross-Strait film and television exchanges and cooperation.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share cultural roots, blood ties, and emotional bonds. The foundation for cross-Strait film and television cooperation is solid, and its prospects are broad. We welcome artists, creators, and production institutions from both sides of the Strait to engage in in-depth film and television cultural exchanges and cooperation, produce more high-quality audiovisual works such as films, TV, and radio programs, and create more shared memories of our era and more enjoyment of the cinematic arts for people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","The DPP authorities do not allow mainland media whose travel to Taiwan was interrupted by the epidemic to resume their on-site presence, and they adopt strict “case-by-case review” to restrict certain mainland media from traveling to Taiwan. Mainland reporters stationed in Taiwan must undergo “interviews” with officials of the Mainland Affairs Council and the “Ministry of Culture.” What is your comment?","Having media reporters from each side of the Taiwan Strait stationed in the other for on-site reporting helps promote cross-Strait exchanges and advance the development of cross-Strait relations. The mainland side has long encouraged and supported Taiwan media reporters coming to the mainland for on-site reporting, and provides high-quality service guarantees and reporting convenience.\nThe DPP authorities previously used epidemic prevention and control as a pretext to abruptly suspend the normal rotation of mainland media reporters stationed in Taiwan, affecting the normal work of the stationed media and harming the legitimate rights and interests of the reporters themselves. We express strong dissatisfaction. We urge the DPP authorities to stop obstructing and interfering with mainland reporters’ on-site reporting in Taiwan, stop undermining normal news exchange and cooperation across the Strait, and genuinely respect and safeguard the rights and interests of mainland reporters reporting in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS记者","First question: The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said that recently, the number of retired military and police personnel detained after going to the mainland has increased, with at least 8 cases in the past year. It called on members of the public with specific identities to take extra care when traveling to the mainland. What comments does the Chinese side have on this?\nSecond question: After…","First question: The so-called “appeal” by the Mainland Affairs Council is purely a malicious and misleading attempt. We have consistently encouraged and supported exchanges and interactions between the two sides in all fields, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have no need to have any concerns about traveling to the mainland. They can come in high spirits and leave satisfied. The DPP authorities, for political self-interest, obstruct and restrict cross-strait exchanges, continuously smear the mainland, and mislead and intimidate the people of Taiwan. This is not in line with popular sentiment.\nSecond question: Regarding the situation of the man surnamed Hu that you mentioned, with the assistance of relevant parties, on June 23, family members of the man surnamed Hu went to Quanzhou to visit him. At present, his physical condition is good. Relevant departments will handle the related issues appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","After the release of the \"Opinions\" on punishing hardline \"Taiwan independence\" separatists on the mainland, some overseas experts said that a vicious spiral is rising between the two sides of the Strait. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Do you feel that a vicious spiral is rising?","This judicial document, from its title to its text, makes clear that the punitive measures target a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards whose words and deeds are vile and whose “independence”-plotting activities are rampant, as well as the crimes they commit in splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country.\nWe hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, follow the great trend of history, clearly recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and in taking concrete action to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","While participating in island-based activities marking the centenary of the Whampoa Military Academy, Lai Ching-te claimed that \"wherever the Republic of China is, the Whampoa spirit is there,\" and some in the DPP also smeared the mainland as \"fake Whampoa, real united front.\" What comments do you have on this?","The Whampoa Military Academy was a product of the First KMT-CPC Cooperation. The historical currents of saving the nation and the people in its early years forged the Whampoa spirit of “patriotism and revolution,” which has become a historical memory shared by both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Compatriots on both sides jointly commemorate the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy. Retired Taiwanese servicemembers and residents of the island have voluntarily come to the mainland to take part in commemorative activities and have called for peace across the Strait and national reunification. This is a true embodiment of the Whampoa spirit and a vivid portrayal of the two sides of the Strait being one family.\n“All under heaven, Whampoa is one family.” The Whampoa bond between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait cannot be severed by anyone or any force. Lai Ching-te and the “Taiwan independence” forces deliberately sever the Whampoa bond and distort Whampoa history. This is disrespect toward the Whampoa forebears and a desecration of the Whampoa spirit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Washington Post recently revealed that Paparo, the newly appointed commander of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command, said in an interview that if mainland China attacks Taiwan, the U.S. will implement a “Hellscape” strategy, deploying unmanned equipment on a large scale to turn the Taiwan Strait into an “unmanned hell.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. Some anti-China forces in the United States previously hyped up a “Taiwan destruction plan,” and now they are clamoring to turn the Taiwan Strait into “hell,” sending out a very dangerous signal and fully exposing the true intention of the U.S. side to destroy Taiwan rather than sacrifice its own interests. Wherever the United States stirs up trouble, the people there will suffer. We firmly oppose any interference by external forces in the Taiwan question. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués through concrete actions, to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, to stop interfering in the Taiwan question, and to stop stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait.\nFor political self-interest, the DPP authorities are willing to serve as pawns of external forces in “using Taiwan to contain China,” and are leading Taiwan into a dangerous situation. Attempting to “rely on the United States to seek independence” and “seek independence through force” is a dead end, and will only bring danger of war to Taiwan and profound disaster to the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630836.htm"],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: The mainland recently issued the “Opinions” to punish “Taiwan independence” diehards. If the defendant is overseas, will the mainland request the relevant country to transfer them to the mainland through extradition mechanisms? Second question: The 35th Golden Melody Awards ceremony will be held in Taipei this weekend, and several mainland singers have been nominated. The 61st Golden Horse Awards…","First question. For “Taiwan independence” diehards who break the law, no matter where they are, national law enforcement and judicial authorities will pursue them to the end and punish them severely in accordance with the law.\nSecond question. We have always supported music and film exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, and we welcome industry players on both sides working together to continuously deepen the integrated development of cultural fields across the two sides. We hope to restore normal personnel exchanges across the Strait as soon as possible and make exchanges in all fields routine, so that singers and performers on both sides can communicate and travel smoothly and present more high-quality film, television and music works to audiences on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Some Taiwan entertainers recently claimed they had received a so-called “cooperation invitation” plan from a mainland media company, which intends to have Taiwan entertainers and online celebrities who are willing to cooperate form a “Taiwan Yonghe Party” and run in elections, and also demands payment of 100,000 yuan as a “sincerity deposit.” In response, Taiwan's Ministry of the Interior said, “The public should…","Hyping up such a crudely made fraudulent letter, attempting to throw dirt on the mainland and using crude lies to intimidate Taiwan’s people fully demonstrates that the DPP authorities’ political manipulation has no bottom line. We hope Taiwan’s people will fully recognize the methods and intentions of the DPP authorities in manipulating “cognitive warfare” and creating a “green terror.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","This year marks the centenary of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy. Please introduce the commemorative activities held on the mainland.","The spirit of Whampoa is a precious shared spiritual heritage of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. On the centennial of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy, the mainland held a series of commemorative events. On June 17, a commemorative symposium marking the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy and the 40th anniversary of the founding of the Whampoa Alumni Association was held at the Great Hall of the People. General Secretary Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter, fully affirming the historical contributions of the Whampoa Military Academy and the positive contributions of the Whampoa Alumni Association. He expressed earnest hopes to Whampoa alumni and their relatives at home and abroad, and emphasized the need to continue to inherit and carry forward the Whampoa spirit of “patriotism and revolution,” and to broadly rally strength for the common realization of the Chinese Dream. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the symposium and delivered a speech. Some Taiwan representatives were invited to attend the symposium.\nVarious localities also held series of commemorative symposiums, academic seminars, visits to the former site of the Whampoa Military Academy, essay and speech contests, and calligraphy, painting, and photography exhibitions to commemorate the revolutionary experiences and moving deeds of Whampoa teachers and students, jointly honor the great achievements of Whampoa's predecessors, and thoroughly elaborate the historical value and contemporary significance of the Whampoa spirit. These related activities further consolidated the strength of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly inherit and carry forward the Whampoa spirit and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","On the first question, some people's representatives have pointed out that the incident involving the fisherman surnamed Hu is tied to the “2·14” Kinmen–Xiamen ship collision incident, and that unless the “2·14” vicious ship collision incident is resolved, the fisherman surnamed Hu cannot return home. How does the Taiwan Affairs Office comment on this?\nOn the second question, many scholars at home and abroad have…","The first question concerns the “2·14” serious ship-collision incident. The Taiwan side treated mainland fishermen in a rough and dangerous manner, causing their fishing boat to capsize and people to be killed and injured. More than four months after the incident, the DPP authorities are still dragging their feet on resolving the problem, shirking responsibility, going back on their word, and constantly placing obstacles in the way of post-incident consultations. We urge the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation, show sincerity as soon as possible in resolving the problem, and give the families of the victims and compatriots on both sides of the Strait an account.\nThe second question: promoting cross-Strait exchange and cooperation has been our consistent policy. We support and promote dialogue and consultation between the two sides on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and actively promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus.” This is the fundamental reason that obstructs dialogue and exchanges across the Strait.\nAs for the third question, at the last press conference I responded to “Why do we need to go back? Cross-Strait relations have kept advancing.” Why do we say this? Because compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same blood, the same culture, and the same history, and, more importantly, we share a common responsibility to the nation and common hopes for the future. We implement clear and consistent major policies on Taiwan affairs. We will fully implement the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan issue in the new era, unwaveringly adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, strive to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-06-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The mainland recently issued judicial documents on punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards in accordance with the law. At its regular press briefing, US State Department spokesperson Miller condemned the Chinese side for “words and actions that undermine stability and escalate the situation,” said that “threats and legal warfare cannot peacefully resolve cross-Strait differences,” and urged the Chinese side to…","Using criminal justice means to punish secessionist criminals and safeguard core national interests is a common practice of countries around the world. Taiwan is part of China, and it is reasonable, justified and lawful for the state to punish \"Taiwan independence\" diehards in accordance with the law for the crimes of secession and inciting secession. Only by strictly punishing \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist crimes in accordance with the law can we truly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and effectively protect the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Our punishment of \"Taiwan independence\" diehards in accordance with the law is precisely to stop \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist acts and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The United States has no right to make irresponsible remarks or interfere in China's internal affairs. The United States must act in practice to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, fulfill its commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" and avoid sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities that there is no way out for pursuing division and confrontation, and that the scheme of \"relying on the US to seek independence\" is doomed to fail.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202406/t20240626_12630834.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240626_12630838.htm"],[0,"2024-06-27","Mao Ning","Global Times","It was reported that on June 25, the Japanese government decided at a cabinet meeting and issued relevant order to expand the continental shelf in the waters of the Ogasawara plateau region east of Chichijima in Ogasawara islands. The expansion covers about 120,000 square kilometers. Under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), Japan will have preferential right to the seabed resources in…","We noted that back in 2012, the Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf (CLCS) adopted the “Recommendations of the Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf in regard to the submission made by Japan on 12 November 2008” relating to the outer limits of the extended continental shelf in Ogasawara. Rather than revising its claims in accordance with the recommendations of the CLCS, Japan has unilaterally expanded its claims, which contravenes the stipulations of UNCLOS and universal practice. It’s important to note that the outer limits of extended continental shelf can only be final and binding when they are delimited on the basis of the recommendations of the CLCS. Otherwise, they shall not be acknowledged by the international community. China believes that any application on the outer limits of extended continental shelf filed by the State Party should strictly abide by the principle of common heritage of mankind enshrined in UNCLOS, and should not infringe on international seabed or harm the overall interests of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463248.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240627_11442587.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command said that the US military will implement a plan called “Hellscape” (地狱景观), which, through large-scale use of drones, unmanned surface vessels, and unmanned underwater vehicles, will turn the Taiwan Strait into an unmanned hell in order to respond to “attacks from mainland China.” A US Navy news website also recently explained the plan in detail. What is the…","Those who clamor to turn others’ homes into hell should first prepare to go to hell themselves. Some people on the US side, in order to “use Taiwan to contain China,” are willing to turn the Taiwan Strait into a “living hell,” which is utterly depraved. This again shows that “Taiwan independence” diehards who fantasize about “seeking independence by relying on the United States” will ultimately be unable to escape the fate of becoming “pawns” and then “discarded pieces.”\nTaiwan belongs to China, and China does not allow division. In defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity and countering interference by external forces, the Chinese People’s Liberation Army has always been ready to fight hard battles and to win them. As for the threats and intimidation of certain people, we have never fallen for this.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","At the centennial celebration of the founding of the Whampoa Military Academy held on the island, Taiwan regional leader Lai Ching-te said he does not accept “ending the war with the first battle,” and stated that the greatest challenge facing the Taiwan military is the mainland's intention to “annex Taiwan and eliminate the Republic of China.” In addition, Lai Ching-te has repeatedly promoted “mutual…","The Whampoa Military Academy is a historical memory for all Chinese people, recording the bloody struggle for national revival. The Whampoa spirit is the spirit of “patriotism and revolution.” Whampoa alumni have always had a glorious history and fine traditions of patriotism and revolution, and they are an important force in advancing the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation. Lai Qingde and his ilk, who attempt to distort history and split the country, will surely face the judgment of history and the severe punishment of the law.\nThere is only one China in the world, Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, the Government of the People's Republic of China is the sole legitimate government representing all of China, and the One-China Principle is the common consensus of the international community. No matter how the DPP authorities distort and deny this, they cannot change this basic fact, and they cannot sever the blood ties and kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. It must be emphasized that each time the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke, our countermeasures advance one step further; this is the progression and prelude to ultimately resolving the Taiwan question. In crushing the “Taiwan independence” armed forces, the PLA has always been like catching turtles in a jar, with ease.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the live-force subjects of Taiwan's “Han Kuang 40” exercise will be conducted from July 22 to 26. Taiwan's defense authorities said this year's “Han Kuang” exercise will not be as “spectacular” as in previous years, because the large-scale firepower display item overseen by the Taiwan region leader has been cancelled, and it instead claims to closely approximate actual battlefield…","The DPP authorities stage the so-called “Han Kuang Exercises” every year, but no matter how they are performed, they are all just theater, and they cannot change the outcome that “Taiwan independence means certain death.”","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to reports, the Philippine military claimed that on June 17, a China Coast Guard vessel rammed a Philippine vessel carrying out a resupply mission to Ren'ai Jiao, injuring one Philippine crew member. Officials of the US State Department and Department of Defense have both accused the Chinese side of obstructing the Philippines' resupply operation, saying the US remains…","On the first question, the Nansha Islands, including Second Thomas Shoal (Ren'ai Jiao), are inherent Chinese territory, and there is ample historical and legal basis for this. Recently, the Philippine side has, in breach of its word, repeatedly sent vessels to ram into the waters of Second Thomas Shoal, attempting to transport construction materials, weapons, and ammunition to the warship it illegally grounded there. This is the direct cause of the escalation of the situation. In particular, on June 17, the Philippine side deliberately rammed Chinese vessels in a dangerous manner and threw stones at Chinese personnel. These actions seriously violate the provisions of international law, seriously endanger the safety of personnel and vessels on both sides, and seriously undermine regional peace and stability. In the face of the Philippines' infringement and provocation, China naturally must take rights-protection and law-enforcement measures. This is entirely reasonable, lawful, professional, and standardized.\nIt should be emphasized that the Ren'ai Jiao issue has nothing to do with the United States. It is extremely dangerous and utterly irresponsible for the United States to encourage and support the Philippines' infringement and provocation. As for the United States' repeated use of the Mutual Defense Treaty between the United States and the Philippines to threaten China, this is completely useless.\nAs for the statements by former U.S. military officials on the “Philippines as a tool,” the international community has its own judgment. Whether it is the “Saigon moment” in history or the “Kabul debacle,” they remind me of Mr. Kissinger's famous saying: “To be an enemy of America can be dangerous, but to be an ally of America can be fatal.”\nOn the second question, Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and resolving the Taiwan question is the internal affair of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, which brooks no foreign interference. The United States' attempt to scare the Chinese military through so-called military exercises is an entirely impossible mission.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Japanese government has released a draft plan to evacuate residents of Okinawa and the Sakishima Islands to prefectures in Kyushu and to Yamaguchi Prefecture. Some analysis holds that the Japanese government formulated the relevant plan to “respond to” a so-called “Taiwan contingency.” Not long ago, China's ambassador to Japan said, “If Japan ties itself to the chariot of splitting…","Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and Taiwan affairs have nothing to do with Japan. The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests, concerns the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and is an insurmountable red line. China opposes Japan’s use of the so-called “Taiwan contingency” to play up regional tensions. The greatest current threat to peace across the Taiwan Strait is “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and the connivance and support that external forces give them. Japan long colonized Taiwan and committed grave historical crimes against the Chinese people, too numerous to record. It should especially reflect on itself and be cautious in its words and deeds. We urge the Japanese side to earnestly abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents and the commitments it has made to date, and to stop using the Taiwan question to stir up confrontation. It must be emphasized that the one-China principle is a common consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. Anyone or any force that dares to interfere in China’s internal affairs or obstruct China’s reunification will surely be met with a head-on blow from more than 1.4 billion Chinese people.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the defense ministers of China and the US held an in-person meeting during the Shangri-La Dialogue. How do you assess the current state of China-US military relations? Will the two militaries carry out more exchanges in the next step?","Since last November, the Chinese and US militaries have resolutely implemented the important consensus of the two heads of state, steadily resumed dialogue and consultation on the basis of equality and mutual respect, and achieved positive and pragmatic results. During this year's Shangri-La Dialogue, the defense ministers of China and the United States held an in-person meeting and conducted active, pragmatic, and constructive strategic communication on issues including China-US relations, the military relationship between the two sides, Taiwan, and the South China Sea. From June 25 to 29, a delegation from the National Defense University of the People's Liberation Army of China visited Washington, D.C., to hold a China-US National Defense University strategic dialogue. It can be said that the current stabilization of China-US military relations has been hard-won and deserves to be cherished by both sides.\nIt must be emphasized that developing China-US military relations must uphold harmony as the most precious, stability as paramount, and good faith as the foundation. We hope the US side will correct its perception of China, genuinely respect China's sovereignty, security, and development interests, and move toward China in the same direction, so as to promote healthy and stable development of relations between the two countries and their militaries.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-06-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the PLA has conducted many exercises and training activities around Taiwan, and the media often describes the island as being “encircled from three sides” or “four sides.” Taiwan's so-called “Chief of the General Staff,” when questioned by the legislature recently, said that the PLA threat may shift from drills to actual combat, and that the Taiwan military must adjust its operational thinking so it can…","For the DPP authorities, “encirclement of Taiwan on four sides” is something they need to get used to. It should be pointed out that the relevant PLA actions target the separatist activities of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and are not aimed at the Taiwan public. As long as they do not engage in “Taiwan independence,” why should they be trembling with fear?","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16319157.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-06-28","Mao Ning","AFP","The US said that Deputy Secretary of State Kurt Campbell held a call with Executive Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu. During the call, Campbell said that the US’s defense commitments to the Philippines were ironclad and raised serious concerns about Chinese actions in the South China Sea. What did Ma Zhaoxu say on that call?","On June 27, Executive Vice Foreign Minister Ma Zhaoxu had a phone conversation with US Deputy Secretary of State Kurt Campbell. The two sides had a candid and in-depth exchange of views on the current China-US relations and issues of mutual interest. Ma Zhaoxu elaborated on China’s just position on issues related to Taiwan, Xizang, the South China Sea and Ukraine, and asked the US to act on President Biden’s “five-noes” commitment, earnestly respect China’s sovereignty, security and development interests, and play a positive role for the steady development of China-US relations, rather than doing the opposite.\nMa Zhaoxu stressed that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” will backfire. The US should fully see through the separatist nature of the DPP authorities and its grave harm to cross-Strait peace and stability, abide by the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming Taiwan, and act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence.” Xizang-related issues concern China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US should stop emboldening the “Tibet independence” forces in any form and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs taking Xizang-related issues as an excuse. The root cause of the current tension around Ren’ai Jiao is that the Philippines has abandoned the consensus reached with China and challenged China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity by sending a large amount of construction materials to the illegally grounded vessel in an attempt to achieve permanent occupation of Ren’ai Jiao. The US side should stop emboldening and supporting the provocations of the Philippine side and take concrete actions to maintain peace and stability in the South China Sea. China’s position on the Ukraine issue is objective and just. The US side should stop groundlessly smearing and scapegoating China, and stop obstructing the normal trade and economic exchanges between China and Russia. China firmly opposes the abuse of illicit unilateral sanctions and long-arm jurisdiction by the US side, and will firmly safeguard the legitimate and lawful rights and interests of Chinese entities and individuals.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463249.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202406/t20240628_11444031.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-06-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 28 (electronic dispatch). TAO spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 28th, pointed out that the mainland side has issued and implemented judicial documents on punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards in accordance with the law. These documents do not target or involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. They are aimed at an extremely small number of “Taiwan…","Zhu Fenglian said that this set of claims and conduct by the DPP authorities is a complete political manipulation of slandering and smearing the mainland and threatening and intimidating the Taiwan people, and we strongly oppose it.\nZhu Fenglian pointed out that the DPP authorities fabricate pretexts to deceive the people on the island, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, and incite cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, completely contrary to the mainstream public opinion on the island, which demands peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. Taiwan people have a strong interest and willingness to travel to the mainland, and the tourism industry on the island has also consistently called on the DPP authorities to lift the ban on Taiwan travel agencies organizing group tours to the mainland as soon as possible. The DPP authorities not only fail to respond to public opinion, but instead brutally intimidate and obstruct Taiwan people from traveling to the mainland, undermining cross-Strait exchanges, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan people and related businesses, depriving people from all walks of life of their freedom of travel, and winning no popular support.\nZhu Fenglian said that we call on compatriots in Taiwan to see through the DPP authorities' political self-interest that harms the interests of the people. We welcome and support compatriots in Taiwan to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and to protect their legitimate rights and interests in accordance with law. Compatriots in Taiwan who take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation need have no concerns about traveling to the mainland; they may come in high spirits and leave with full satisfaction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202406/t20240628_12631508.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-02","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua answers reporters' questions\n(July 2, 2024)\nQuestion: After Lai Ching-te took office, he repeatedly mentioned “mutual non-subordination,” which has provoked strong dissatisfaction on the mainland. On the 1st, Liang Wen-chieh, Deputy Minister of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council, said in an interview that “if one does not treat the other side as a country and turns a blind eye to the People's Republic of China,” that would be “a very absurd thing.” Apart from the “Constitution,” in other legal systems, “all our practices treat the other side as a country.” What is your comment on this?\nAnswer:\nThe remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council once again expose the essence of the DPP authorities: obstinately clinging to “Taiwan independence” secession and continuously carrying out provocation and confrontation.\nThe historical course of the Taiwan question is clear, and the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China is plain. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided. The status of Taiwan as part of Chinese territory has never changed and will never be allowed to change.\nSince taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities have disregarded facts, distorted legal principles, and blatantly peddled the “two-state theory,” which has provoked strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Taiwan compatriots see clearly. Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” rhetoric cannot deceive the people of Taiwan, and cannot whitewash his essence as a “Taiwan independence worker” and a “troublemaker.” Any act that challenges the one-China principle and provokes compatriots on both sides of the Strait will surely be punished and will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240702_12632392.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-02","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华2日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 2: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua, answering reporters' questions on the 2nd, said: The mainland side has issued judicial documents on punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with law, which are not directed at broad Taiwan compatriots. DPP politicians have deliberately conflated broad Taiwan compatriots with die-hard “Taiwan independence”…","Chen Binhua pointed out that these practices by the DPP authorities completely disregard facts, reverse right and wrong, are malicious slander and smears against the mainland, and are blatant deception and intimidation of the people of Taiwan.\nChen Binhua pointed out that punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting secession in accordance with the law is reasonable and lawful. Taiwan is part of China. The country will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means. Only by strictly punishing the crime of “Taiwan independence” separatism in accordance with the law can we truly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and effectively protect the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Any “Taiwan independence” diehard who breaks the law, wherever they may be, will be pursued to the end by the country’s law enforcement and judicial organs and strictly punished in accordance with the law.\nChen Binhua said that we once again emphasize that punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting secession in accordance with the law is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity, and is also a righteous act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, follow the great trend of history, fully recognize the harm and deceptiveness of “Taiwan independence,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait with concrete actions, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We have always and will continue to warmly welcome and support Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in all fields, increasing their understanding of the mainland, sharing the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization, and jointly creating the great cause of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240702_12632394.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-07-03","Mao Ning","Reuters","According to the Taiwanese side, there were three Indonesians on a Taiwan fishing boat that China Coast Guard seized in Kinmen yesterday. Could we have more details about this incident?","I do not have the details. I’d refer you to the competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463252.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240703_11446517.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-03","Mao Ning","AFP","I just want to follow up on the question about the Taiwanese fishing boat followed just now by my colleague. The statement from the Taiwan side says that five fishers were detained and the boat was detained by the Chinese Coast Guard, including the three Indonesians. And we’ve noted just now the Chinese Coast Guard’s statement doesn’t make any mention of their detentions. So is the Foreign Ministry able to…","I do not have the details. I’d refer you to the competent authorities.\n***********************************************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463252.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240703_11446517.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-07-03","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 3 (dispatch). Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 3rd and introduced that, recently, the Fujian Coast Guard boarded, inspected, and detained, in accordance with law, a Taiwan fishing vessel suspected of illegal fishing in the waters off Quanzhou. The vessel violated the summer fishing moratorium regulations by conducting trawl operations in violation of the rules. This was normal law enforcement by the mainland coast guard, aimed at maintaining the order of fishery production, marine fishery resources, and the ecological environment in the relevant waters. The relevant departments will handle the matter in accordance with law and regulations.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, the Fujian Coast Guard boarded and detained a Taiwan fishing vessel in waters near Quanzhou. Please explain the situation. Chen Binhua gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240703_12632643.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on July 5 that the 7th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum will be held from July 6 to 12 in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, as well as in Ningbo, Jinhua, Lishui, and other places. The opening session and main forum will be held in Hangzhou on the afternoon of July 8. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Offices of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, and Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China and Chairperson of the China Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, will attend the forum by invitation. About 800 guests from relevant parties across the Strait, youth representatives from all sectors, and others will take part in forum-related activities. Media reporters are welcome to visit and report.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240705_12633075.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 5 — In response to a DPP people's representative's malicious smearing of the mainland coast guard for lawfully boarding, inspecting, and detaining a Taiwanese fishing vessel suspected of illegal fishing off the coast of Quanzhou, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said at a press conference on July 5 that the relevant actions of the mainland coast guard are proper and lawful. Some people in the DPP are talking nonsense and engaging in political manipulation with sinister intent, which does not help resolve the issue.\nA reporter asked: Recently, the mainland coast guard lawfully boarded, inspected, and detained a Taiwanese fishing vessel suspected of illegal fishing off the coast of Quanzhou. A DPP people's representative maliciously smeared this action, saying, \"Recently the mainland has provoked tensions in both the East China Sea and the South China Sea and has systematically escalated confrontation.\" What is your comment on this? Chen Binhua gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240705_12633312.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-07-11","Lin Jian","AFP","The “defense ministry” of Taiwan said today it detected 66 Chinese military aircraft around the island in a 24-hour window, a record high in recent years. Does it have anything to do with the NATO Summit?","I’d refer you to competent authorities on the specific question. Let me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s defense ministry.” The Chinese people will never waver in our will and resolve to uphold China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463257.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240711_11452358.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-12","Lin Jian","Xinhua News Agency","On July 11, NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg emphasized again at the closing press conference of the NATO Summit that China has become a decisive enabler of Russia’s war against Ukraine. He said that China’s joint military exercise with Belarus fits into the pattern of working together in supporting Russia’s war on Ukraine. He added that China is taking more assertive behaviors in Hong Kong and the South…","China strongly condemns the irresponsible and provocative remarks made by the NATO Secretary General against China, which are steeped in Cold War mentality and ideological bias, and consist of baseless accusations. In his remarks, the NATO Secretary General attacked China’s system, blatantly interfered in China’s internal affairs, and distorted China’s domestic and diplomatic policies. He sought to shift blames and mislead the international community on Ukraine and pointed fingers at China’s normal military development and relations with relevant countries. We strongly deplore and firmly oppose it.\nChina has already made its position clear on the Ukraine issue and the NATO Summit. I would like to emphasize that, for a long time, the NATO Secretary General, in disregard of the facts and China’s protests, repeatedly smeared and hurled attacks at China. He has been playing up the “China threat” narrative and inciting suspicion about China and anti-China sentiments in an apparent attempt to cooperate with certain parties to suppress and contain China. These clumsy stunts have sounded the alarm for many in the world and remind people what risks and challenges NATO, as a vestige of the Cold War and a product of bloc confrontation and bloc politics, will bring to world peace and stability.\nChina urges certain Western politician, whose political life is approaching an end, not to fan the flames, make provocations, and shift blames for the sake of trying to leave behind some kind of legacy. China will stick to the path of peaceful development and inject more stability and positive energy into world peace and stability through its own development and international cooperation. China will also firmly safeguard its sovereignty, security and development interests. To see China as NATO’s imaginary enemy will only backfire on NATO itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463258.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240712_11453092.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-12","Lin Jian","China Review News","It’s reported that the Defense of Japan 2024 white paper adopted at Japan’s Cabinet meeting today stressed that Japan finds itself in the most severe security environment of the post-war era. According to the white paper, China has been intensifying its military activities, North Korea has been advancing its nuclear and missile development, and Russia has been observed engaging in joint patrols with China—those…","The Defense of Japan 2024 white paper gravely interferes in China’s internal affairs, again seeks to play up the “China threat” narrative, and hypes up regional tensions. We deplore and reject this.\nChina is committed to the path of peaceful development and a defense policy that is defensive in nature. China’s defense development and military activities are legitimate and justified. Our joint patrols with other countries are consistent with international law and customary international practice. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. In recent years, the root cause of the cross-Strait tensions has been “Taiwan independence” separatists’ reckless activities emboldened and supported by external forces. Japan invaded and exercised colonial rule over Taiwan and bears serious historical responsibilities for the suffering it imposed on the Chinese people. Japan is in no position to point its fingers on the Taiwan question.\nGiven Japan’s history of militarist aggression during the last century, Japan’s military and security moves have been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. In recent years, Japan has been drastically readjusting defense policy, increasing defense spending annually, easing restrictions of weapon exports, and seeking military breakthrough. It has triggered strong concerns from the world. We urge Japan to deeply reflect on its history of aggression, champion peaceful development, stop finding pretexts for its own military buildup, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the wider international community through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463258.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240712_11453092.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-07-12","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Taiwan military sent letters to some temples on the island asking whether they could be used as ammunition storage sites in wartime, which has provoked strong backlash in some counties and cities. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have noted the relevant reports. The DPP authorities remain obstinate and unrepentant, “seeking independence by armed force,” and they are trying to drag the flames of war into religious venues, even willing to use the people of Taiwan as “human shields.” Their total lack of a bottom line is shocking. Unification is the right path, and “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. No matter where “Taiwan independence” elements hide, they will have nowhere to escape, and any scheme to “resist unification by armed force” will collapse.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16323997.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-07-12","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Answers Reporters' Questions\n(July 12, 2024)\nQuestion: The mainland recently issued judicial documents on punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements. The DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and smeared these documents, deliberately conflating the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots with a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in an attempt to confuse the public, spread rumors, stir up panic, and coerce the broad public into serving as cover for “Taiwan independence.” What is your comment?\nAnswer:\nThe situation across the Taiwan Strait is currently complex and grave. The DPP authorities are obstinately pushing the separatist “Taiwan independence” line, refusing to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and persistently colluding with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke confrontation. This is the root cause of the danger of war, social division and confrontation, and harm to the interests of the people across the Taiwan Strait. Lawfully punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements for the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity, and a just act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. It conforms to common practice around the world and is reasonable, lawful and justified.\n1. Criminal punishment measures target only a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements\nThe Opinions on Lawfully Punishing Die-Hard “Taiwan Independence” Elements for the Crimes of Secession of the State and Inciting Secession of the State make clear, from the title through the main text, that criminal punishment measures target only a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements whose words and deeds in support of “independence” are egregious and whose “independence” activities are rampant, along with the crimes of secession of the state and inciting secession of the state that they commit. The crime of secession of the state includes four specific circumstances:\nFirst, initiating or establishing a “Taiwan independence” separatist organization; plotting, formulating or drafting a “Taiwan independence” separatist action program, plan or scheme; or directing members of a “Taiwan independence” separatist organization or other persons to carry out activities to split the country or undermine national unification.\nSecond, through formulating, amending, interpreting or abolishing relevant regulations of the Taiwan region, or through “referendums” and similar means, attempting to change the legal status that Taiwan is part of China.\nThird, through promoting Taiwan's accession to international organizations that are open only to sovereign states, or through official exchanges or military contacts with other countries, attempting to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan” or “Taiwan independence” in the international community.\nFourth, abusing their authority to extensively distort or falsify the fact that Taiwan is part of China in the fields of education, culture, history and news media, or suppressing political parties, groups or individuals that support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification.\n2. Criminal punishment measures do not target the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots\nThis judicial document was formulated strictly in accordance with the law, with precisely targeted objects of punishment. It does not target, and does not involve, the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Any political party, group or individual in Taiwan that does not split the country, and that recognizes that people on both sides of the Strait are Chinese and members of one family, faces no obstacles to exchanges and interactions with the mainland. For those who were once misled onto the path of “Taiwan independence” but have clearly and positively changed their stance, as long as they no longer engage in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and genuinely take measures to mitigate or eliminate the harmful consequences, they may, in accordance with the law, be exempted from some or all criminal liability.\n3. Taiwan compatriots are drawing a clear line between themselves and die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements through their actions\nUnder the great pressure of the judicial document, the DPP authorities and some “Taiwan independence” politicians have maliciously created information cocoons, deliberately conflating the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots with a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements. They seek to use smears of the judicial document to incite cross-Strait antagonism, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, coerce the broad public into serving as cover for “Taiwan independence,” and seriously infringe on the legitimate rights and interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The facts prove that more and more Taiwan compatriots have seen through the sinister intentions of the DPP authorities. They refuse to be deceived, coerced or intimidated, and have made clear in various ways that they do not wish to be “made into Taiwan independence,” drawing a clear line between themselves and die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements through their actions. Recently, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have been vibrant and full of highlights, which is the most powerful rebuttal to the DPP authorities' smears and slander.\nBy lawfully and precisely punishing a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, the mainland side is in fact showing sincere care for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and demonstrating its responsibility to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and to protect the well-being of compatriots. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople working on the mainland are direct participants in and beneficiaries of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They have the most direct experience of the mainland's development and progress and of the prospects for cross-Strait relations, and they have the most authority to speak on these matters. As we accelerate the construction of a new development paradigm, steadily promote high-quality development, and foster and grow new quality productive forces, the mainland's economy will continue to demonstrate enormous vitality, potential and bright prospects. It is fully capable of providing stronger impetus for deepening cross-Strait integrated development and benefiting the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and of opening up broader space. We will, as always, warmly welcome and support the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various forms, deepening their understanding of the mainland, becoming witnesses, builders and beneficiaries of Chinese-style modernization, and working hand in hand with mainland compatriots to create a bright future of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240712_12635046.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-07-15","Lin Jian","CCTV","On July 12, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a decision on its website to take countermeasures against six US military companies and five senior executives. Do you have any further comment?","The US arms sale to China’s Taiwan region seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, interferes in China’s internal affairs, and undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In accordance with the law, China is taking countermeasures on principal US contractors that have recently sold arms to Taiwan and their senior executives, and on military companies that have engaged in US arms sales to Taiwan or attended the Taiwan-US Defense Business Forum in Taiwan in recent years.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. No country, organization or individual shall underestimate the strong determination, will and ability of the Chinese government and people to defend our sovereignty and territorial integrity, or be under the illusion that they could tread or even cross the line on the Taiwan question without any consequence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463259.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240715_11454130.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-17","Lin Jian","Reuters","Former US President Donald Trump has given an interview, in which he said Taiwan should pay for its defense. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","Let me reiterate once again that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference. We are opposed to making China an issue in US elections.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240717_11455286.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-17","Lin Jian","China News Service","In November 2023, China and the US held consultations on arms control and non-proliferation in Washington DC. During the past few weeks, some US senior official accused China of declining a new round of consultations with the US and not providing a substantive response to the suggestions that the US put forward. What’s China’s comment?","Over the past weeks and months, despite China’s firm opposition and repeated protest, the US has continued to sell arms to Taiwan and done things that severely undermine China’s core interests and the mutual trust between China and the US. This has seriously compromised the political atmosphere for continuing the arms control consultations. Consequently, the Chinese side has decided to hold off discussion with the US on a new round of consultations on arms control and non-proliferation. The responsibility fully lies with the US.\nChina stands ready to maintain communication with the US on international arms control in line with the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, but the US must respect China’s core interests and create necessary conditions for dialogue and exchange.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240717_11455286.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-07-18","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: On July 12, the Japanese Cabinet approved the 2024 edition of the “Defense of Japan White Paper”, which designates China as Japan’s “greatest strategic challenge ever”, holds that China’s military activities are increasingly active and have expanded from the first island chain to the second island chain, that there is a possibility of escalation in tensions across the Taiwan Strait, and claims that the…","Zhang Xiaogang: Japan's new edition of the Defense White Paper is full of clichés. It is nothing more than using China as a pretext, deceiving the Japanese public, misleading the international community, and creating excuses for its expansion of military strength. We are strongly dissatisfied with this, firmly oppose it, and have already lodged solemn representations with the Japanese side.\nChina's normal maritime and aerial activities, carried out in accordance with international law and relevant domestic law, are legitimate and reasonable and beyond reproach. The Diaoyu Islands and their affiliated islands have been Chinese territory since ancient times. Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and the Taiwan question brooks no interference from external forces. The greatest current threat to peace across the Taiwan Strait is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” and the connivance and support of external forces for them. Japan's colonial rule over Taiwan for 50 years committed crimes too numerous to record even with all the bamboo in the land, and Japan should especially reflect on itself, and be cautious in its words and deeds. China-Russia defense cooperation is built on the basis of non-alliance, non-confrontation and not targeting any third party. It is open and aboveboard, and helps safeguard international and regional peace and stability and uphold international fairness and justice.\nHistory has proven and will continue to prove that China has always been a force for peace, stability and progress in the world. China never seeks to challenge anyone, but nor does it fear any challenge. Developing our military strength is entirely for safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests, and for maintaining world and regional peace and stability. By contrast, Japan: think of its militarist history, look at its sharp increases in defense budgets, its accelerated development of offensive weapons, its continual relaxation of arms and equipment exports, and its forming of cliques and camp confrontation. How could the world not worry that it will repeat the old path and evil course of aggression and expansion? During World War II, how many innocent people in the Asia-Pacific region died under the sabers of Japanese militarism? Even Japanese media do not hide that this white paper aims to “forge blades,” and Japan's scheme to strengthen its military and expand its arms is plain to see. The international community should remain highly vigilant.\nWe urge the Japanese side to profoundly draw lessons from history, stop smearing and accusing China, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, be cautious in words and deeds in the military and security field, and win the trust of Asian neighbors and the international community through practical actions.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16325451.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-07-19","Lin Jian","AFP","Former US President Donald Trump in his acceptance speech for the Republican presidential nomination said that he will restore peace in the world and warned that a growing specter of conflict hangs over Taiwan and all of Asia. What’s your comment on his speech?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference. We are opposed to making China an issue in US elections.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463264.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240719_11456798.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-19","Lin Jian","Beijing Youth Daily","It was reported that on July 18, the Hsun Hu No.9 patrol vessel of the “Coast Guard Administration of the Ocean Affairs Council” of Taiwan and the aircraft-carrying patrol vessel Sagami of Japan Coast Guard carried out a joint drill to the south of Japan’s Boso Peninsula, Chiba Prefecture, and in waters near Izu Oshima. According to the reports, this is the first joint maritime exercise between Japan Coast Guard…","We strongly deplore and firmly oppose Japan’s joint maritime exercise with the Taiwan region, and have lodged protests with Japan. Japan has made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question, including not supporting “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan” or “Taiwan independence.” These are the stance and principles that Japan must uphold. We urge Japan to adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, correct the wrongdoing at once, refrain from conniving at or supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form, stay prudent on issues related to the East and South China Seas, and stop disrupting cross-Strait peace and stability and China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463264.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240719_11456798.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-22","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan started its annual Han Kuang military drills today. It’s reported that the drills this year include wartime overseas supply-delivery missions. Do you have any comment on that?","That’s not a question about China’s foreign affairs. What caused the tension in the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities’ persistent agenda for “Taiwan independence” and provocations which receive support and connivance from external actors. Let me make clear that any attempt to heighten tensions and to seek “Taiwan independence” or resist reunification through the demonstration or use of force will simply fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463265.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240722_11457963.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-07-22","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters' questions\n(July 22, 2024)\nQuestion: Lai Ching-te recently attended the National Congress of the Democratic Progressive Party and declared that he wants to “build our own country: Democratic Taiwan,” to “oppose annexation and ensure national sovereignty,” and to establish a “Taiwan-subjectivity national identity,” among other things. What is your comment on this?\nAnswer:\nLai Ching-te openly clamored to establish a so-called “Taiwan-subjectivity national identity,” once again exposing his true face of stubbornly adhering to the “Taiwan independence” stance and carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nTaiwan is part of China. Although cross-Strait reunification has not yet been achieved, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided. Taiwan has never been a country and can never become a country.\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese, sharing the same bloodline, the same culture, and the same history. Over the long course of history, the Chinese nation jointly built the territory of the motherland, including the treasure island of Taiwan; jointly wrote Chinese history; jointly created Chinese culture; and jointly nurtured the national spirit. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have always been one family.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party, disregarding history, disregarding facts, and disregarding the will of the people, stubbornly adheres to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” refuses to accept the one-China principle, pursues “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence,” deceives the Taiwan people, incites hatred toward the mainland, obstructs and sabotages cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, leads to tension in cross-Strait relations, endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and harms the interests of compatriots on both sides.\nCompatriots on both sides should unite, fully recognize the essence and harm of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, proceed from national righteousness, Taiwan's future, and the well-being of compatriots, resolutely oppose the “Taiwan independence” provocations of Lai Ching-te and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, actively participate in the just cause of advancing peaceful reunification of the motherland, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240722_12637220.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-07-23","Mao Ning","Phoenix TV","US State Department spokesperson, when responding to a question, said that the Taiwan region “has been purchasing military equipment from the United States to the tune of billions of dollars, and the military equipment that they have purchased supports American manufacturing, industry, and technology. It has not been in any way charity from the United States.” What’s your comment?","The US keeps stressing the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, while making tons and tons of money out of the pockets of people in Taiwan. Taiwan is China’s Taiwan, not a chess piece for the US to interfere in China’s internal affairs. US arms sales to Taiwan violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. China firmly opposes it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463266.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240723_11458771.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-24","Mao Ning","Reuters","Foreign Minister Wang Yi today held talks with his Ukrainian counterpart in Guangzhou, according to sources. Are you able to provide any further information on what was discussed?","This morning, Foreign Minister Wang Yi held talks with Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmytro Kuleba in Guangzhou.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi noted that China and Ukraine are friends to each other. Everything that stands out in bilateral exchanges is about friendship and cooperation. The two countries established a strategic partnership more than a decade ago, and have respected each other and treated each other as equals. Mutually beneficial cooperation has made steady headway. The presidents of our two countries stressed the importance to view and envision bilateral relations from a long-term perspective, and make sure that bilateral relations and cooperation will keep moving forward. We need to follow this guidance, maintain communication and exchanges, enhance mutual trust, carry forward our traditional friendship, promote the people-to-people bond, and achieve sound and steady growth of China-Ukraine relations.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi said the third plenary session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China ushered in a new journey of comprehensively deepening reform. China’s all-round modernization endeavor will bring new opportunities to people from all countries. Ukraine is one of the first countries to support and participate in Belt and Road cooperation. In recent years, China has remained Ukraine’s largest trading partner and the largest exporter of agricultural products. In the first half of this year, our bilateral trade has shown a momentum of rapid growth, demonstrating the space and potential of bilateral cooperation. The two sides need to give full play to cooperation mechanisms between the two countries and enhance practical cooperation in various fields. China will continue to increase food imports from Ukraine and work together to keep logistics corridors open and ensure global food security. Foreign Minister Wang thanked the Ukrainian side for the help it provided for the evacuation of Chinese nationals, especially the Chinese students in Ukraine, when the conflict broke out. He also expressed the hope that Ukraine will continue to work effectively to keep Chinese personnel and institutions safe in Ukraine.\nThe two foreign ministers exchanged views on the Ukraine crisis. Foreign Minister Wang noted that the Ukraine crisis has entered its third year, the conflict continues and there is the risk of escalation and spillover. China remains firmly committed to working for a political settlement of the crisis. President Xi Jinping laid out four principles which provide the fundamental guidance for seeking a political settlement of the Ukraine crisis. On this basis, China and Brazil jointly issued six common understandings that include the three principles for deescalating the conflict, the three elements for peace talks and the three appeals on humanitarian protection. The common understandings also highlight the need to prevent nuclear risks and protect the stability of industrial and supply chains. The common understandings represent the broadest common ground of the international community and have been widely supported and endorsed. China believes that all conflicts ultimately have to be resolved at the negotiating table, and the solutions to any dispute can only be found through political means. Recently, both Ukraine and Russia have expressed to varying degrees the willingness to negotiate. Although the conditions and timing are not yet ripe, we support all efforts conducive to peace and will continue to play a constructive role to enable a ceasefire and resume the peace talks. China cares about the humanitarian situation in Ukraine and will continue to provide humanitarian aid supplies.\nForeign Minister Kuleba said that China is a great country. China and Ukraine are each other’s strategic partners and important economic and trade partners. Ukraine supports China’s position on the Taiwan question and will remain committed to one China. Ukraine hopes to work with China to implement the important common understandings between the two presidents, cement political mutual trust, activate cooperation in such areas as trade and agriculture, and strengthen subnational and sister-cities exchanges. Ukraine highly appreciates China’s active and constructive role to promote peace and uphold the international order. Ukraine attaches importance to China’s views, and has looked closely at the six common understandings issued by China and Brazil on the political settlement of the Ukraine crisis. Ukraine is willing and ready to have dialogue and negotiation with Russia. And of course, negotiations should be rational, substantive and aimed at achieving just and lasting peace.\nThe two sides also exchanged views on international and regional issues of mutual concern. For anything specific, a readout will be released, which you may refer to.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240730_11463267.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240724_11459539.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office held a press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee has been successfully held. How will the spirit of the plenary session be implemented in Taiwan work?","From July 15 to 18, the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was successfully held in Beijing. This session was a very important meeting held at a critical time when Chinese modernization is comprehensively advancing the great cause of building a strong country and national rejuvenation. The meeting focused closely on the theme of advancing Chinese modernization in mapping out strategic measures for further comprehensively deepening reform. The “Decision of the CPC Central Committee on Further Comprehensively Deepening Reform and Advancing Chinese Modernization,” which the meeting reviewed and adopted, is a programmatic document guiding further comprehensive deepening of reform on the new journey, and provides strong impetus and institutional guarantees for Chinese modernization.\nThe Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee clarified the goals and tasks for advancing cross-Strait relations and the great cause of national reunification on the new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country. It also brings rare opportunities, opens broad space for high-quality development of Taiwan work, and is of great significance.\nWe will fully implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee, earnestly turn the spirit of the plenary session into a powerful force for advancing Taiwan work, improve the working mechanisms for Taiwan affairs, improve the systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and deepen cross-Strait integrated development.\nWe will thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the Party Central Committee's decisions and deployments on Taiwan work, firmly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly grasp the leadership and initiative in cross-Strait relations, resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and the schemes of external interference, and firmly advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637777.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was successfully held. Centered on the theme of advancing Chinese modernization, the session charted strategic measures for further comprehensively deepening reform. What new opportunities will this provide for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and for Taiwan compatriots to share in Chinese modernization?","The “Decision of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Further Deepening Reform Comprehensively and Advancing Chinese Modernization,” adopted by the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Party, puts forward more than 300 important reform measures in total, making systematic arrangements for further comprehensively deepening reform. This will provide strong impetus and institutional guarantees for Chinese modernization, and will also create better conditions and open up broader space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to take root and develop on the mainland.\nWe will comprehensively implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Party Central Committee, genuinely turn the spirit of the plenary session into a powerful force for advancing Taiwan work, promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development in all fields, and let Taiwan compatriots be the first to share the development opportunities of Chinese modernization and share in the development and progress achievements of the mainland. We will adhere to the requirement of high-quality development throughout the entire process of cross-Strait economic and cross-field exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continuously improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and expand the coverage of benefits and the sense of gain for people on both sides of the Strait. We will broaden the areas and channels for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, provide more conveniences for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to study, live, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland, and promote, through exchanges, interaction, and integration, the consolidation of a sense of the community of the Chinese nation and the safeguarding of our common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637776.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was successfully held. The DPP authorities made irresponsible remarks about it, saying they would closely monitor the relevant documents and “assess possible impacts.” What is your comment?","The Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was a very important meeting held at a critical time when China is comprehensively advancing the building of a strong country and the great cause of national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization. The “Decision of the CPC Central Committee on Further Deepening Reform Comprehensively and Advancing Chinese-Style Modernization,” which the meeting deliberated and adopted, is a programmatic document guiding further comprehensive deepening of reform on the new journey, and it provides strong impetus and institutional guarantees for Chinese-style modernization.\nThe prosperity of the country and the rejuvenation of the nation are closely tied to the future and destiny of Taiwan compatriots. We will continue to uphold the development philosophy centered on the people, respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots as always, share with Taiwan compatriots the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization ahead of others and share the achievements of development and progress on the mainland, continuously improve systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and steadily strengthen Taiwan compatriots' sense of gain, happiness, and honor.\nIn recent days, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland have followed closely and widely discussed the relevant decisions of the Third Plenary Session. They say they are deeply encouraged and greatly inspired, have clearer and more positive expectations for the future development of the mainland, and are full of confidence and anticipation about putting down roots and developing on the mainland. They hope to share in the major opportunities on the mainland, cooperate hand in hand with mainland enterprises, and take part in cross-strait integrated development. We firmly believe that as Chinese-style modernization advances comprehensively and more Taiwan compatriots join in, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises will have broader room for development, larger stages, and more opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637775.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 7th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was successfully held recently. What results were achieved?","From July 6 to 12, the 7th Straits Forum on Youth Development was held in Hangzhou, Ningbo, Jinhua, Lishui and other places in Zhejiang. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office; Yi Lianhong, Secretary of the CPC Zhejiang Provincial Committee and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Zhejiang Provincial People's Congress; and Hong Xiuzhu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang and Chairperson of the Chinese Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, attended the opening session of the forum and delivered speeches. More than 1,100 guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait and youth representatives from all walks of life gathered together. Centered on the forum theme of “Working Together with One Heart, Co-creating the Future,” the forum was divided into three chapters—pursuing dreams, building dreams, and realizing dreams—and achieved positive results through exchange, communication, and the building of consensus.\nWith the enthusiastic participation of youth on both sides and strong support from all parties, this session of the forum was the largest in its history, with more than 700 young people from Taiwan attending. The forum held five themed study camps in several places in Zhejiang—“Intangible Cultural Heritage,” “E-commerce Live Streaming,” “Film and Television Culture,” “Beautiful Countryside,” and “Science and Technology Innovation”—and carried out activities including jointly offering sacrifices to the Yellow Emperor Xuanyuan. Youth from both sides ate, lived, and traveled together, deepening mutual understanding and friendship, and jointly experiencing the profound foundations of China's outstanding traditional culture and the vigorous vitality of the mainland's economic and social development. During the forum, Zhejiang Province issued a series of measures to help Taiwan youth come to Zhejiang for development, including providing internship and employment opportunities, supporting them in settling down and establishing careers, accelerating the construction of entrepreneurship and employment bases for Taiwan youth in Zhejiang, and helping Taiwan youth establish technology enterprises in Zhejiang, actively creating a favorable environment and providing strong guarantees for Taiwan youth to come to Zhejiang for development.\nWe will continue to thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's letter of congratulations to the 6th Straits Forum on Youth Development, continue to hold well exchange activities such as the Straits Forum on Youth Development, promote mutual learning and heart-to-heart communication among youth on both sides, grasp the trend of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, and contribute youthful strength to promoting the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637774.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","The DPP authorities released so-called threat alerts of “missile and rocket attacks on specific areas of Taiwan” during this year’s “Han Kuang 40” exercise on the island. Many temples on the island were required to sign “ammunition pre-storage point support agreements,” which sparked panic and questions. Some public opinion holds that the DPP authorities are following the “baton” of the United States in…","The DPP authorities cling closely to the US side and stubbornly press ahead with “relying on external forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force,” leading to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait and seriously threatening the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. They hype up the so-called “mainland threat,” squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people on buying weapons from the US, and go to great lengths to cater to the US. Step by step, they tie Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coerce Taiwan’s people into becoming “Taiwan independence cannon fodder.” More and more Taiwan people strongly oppose and resent this. They fully recognize that “relying on the US” will only “harm Taiwan,” and that “seeking independence through force” is a dead end. The DPP authorities should abandon their schemes to “seek independence through force” and “rely on external forces to seek independence,” and stop leading Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and calamity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637771.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","US scholar Bonnie Glaser recently wrote that she suggested the US government encourage the two sides of the Taiwan Strait to establish a reliable “secret communication channel” to avoid miscalculation. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said, “The cross-strait communication and consultation mechanisms are already very complete; whether the two sides communicate is entirely up to the mainland’s whim.” What comment…","As is well known, the “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for cross-Strait communication, dialogue, consultation and negotiation. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This is the fundamental cause and crux of the halt in institutionalized communication and consultation across the Taiwan Strait. As long as the one-China principle is acknowledged and both sides return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” there will be no obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges.\nIt should be pointed out that Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait to decide, and outsiders are not allowed to meddle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The 2024 Cross-Strait Taipei Summer Travel Expo was recently held. More than 100 representatives from 12 mainland provinces participated in the exhibition, attracting the attention of many Taiwan residents. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To deepen cross-Strait tourism exchange and cooperation, and to better promote the mainland's tourism resources to Taiwan compatriots, 155 representatives of the tourism industry from 12 mainland provinces and municipalities participated in the 2024 Cross-Strait Taipei Summer Travel Expo held in Taipei from July 12 to 15. The mainland pavilion of the expo set up 75 booths, held 90 distinctive culture and tourism promotion sessions, and 28 art performances. It launched “Travel Following TV Dramas,” allowing Taiwan people to appreciate the scenery of Xinjiang through the popular TV series “My Altay”; and set up a photo area for experiencing traditional Chinese Hanfu clothing, allowing Taiwan people to feel the beauty of traditional culture. Taiwan people watched performances, participated in interactions, and tasted food at the mainland pavilion, gaining an in-depth understanding of the new look of the development of mainland tourism formats. Many people, especially “first-time visitors,” expressed hope to have the opportunity to travel to the mainland as soon as possible.\nSince its establishment, the Cross-Strait Taipei Summer Travel Expo has become an important platform for mutual trust and resource sharing among cross-Strait tourism industries, and has played a positive role in deepening cross-Strait tourism exchange and cooperation. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a look, and we will continue to create better conditions and provide better services for Taiwan people to travel to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” (hereinafter the “Opinions”) proposes “supporting exchanges between primary and secondary schools in Fujian and Taiwan, and cooperation in youth sports programs with distinctive features such as…","To implement the \"Opinions\" in earnest, in January this year, relevant departments of Fujian Province jointly issued the \"Measures for the Establishment and Management of the Fujian-Taiwan Baseball and Softball Regional Development Center,\" proposing the implementation of a baseball and softball promotion project to drive cooperation in youth-oriented sports programs with distinctive characteristics such as baseball and softball, and has achieved phased progress. First, a Fujian Provincial Baseball Team was established through \"joint Fujian-Taiwan team formation\" and participated in the Chinese Baseball League. Second, a \"1+4+10\" Fujian-Taiwan baseball and softball regional development system was built as the main platform for promoting and popularizing baseball and softball in various localities (1 provincial-level center, 4 high-level competition bases, and 10 prefecture-level city centers). On this basis, in accordance with the target of 100 schools each year, at least 300 primary and secondary schools across the province will be promoted to carry out baseball and softball programs (a target of 300 schools in 3 years). Third, platforms for Fujian-Taiwan sports exchanges such as the Cross-Strait Sports Carnival have been built, and cross-Strait competition exchanges and civil association interactions have been widely carried out, with Fujian-Taiwan sports exchanges maintaining a lively momentum.\nFrom August 4 to 11, relevant institutions from both sides of the Strait will jointly hold the 2024 Dongsen Cup Cross-Strait (Lianchéng) Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament and the 5th Cross-Strait (Lianchéng) Youth Baseball Culture Festival in Lianchéng County, Fujian Province, under the theme \"Youth of Baseball, Dreaming of the Future.\" At that time, 8 youth baseball teams from both sides of the Strait will be invited to participate in the competition and other exchange activities. Media friends are welcome to pay attention to and report on this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The relevant mainland authorities announced in April this year that after direct sea passenger service between Pingtan and Taiwan resumed, group tourism for Fujian residents to Taiwan would also be resumed. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently responded that the two should be considered separately, and that it does not accept “exchange conditions.” Liang Wen-chieh, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs…","The Pingtan-Taiwan maritime passenger direct route is an important transportation link between the two sides of the Strait. In November 2011, the Pingtan-Taiwan maritime passenger direct route began operations, with the passenger-cargo roll-on/roll-off ferry \"Haixia Hao\" carrying traffic between the two sides. It was equipped with world-advanced shipping technology and strict safety management. Until its suspension in February 2020, it had carried a cumulative total of 994,000 passenger trips, of which 443,000 trips were by Taiwan compatriots, accounting for 44.5%, playing an important role in personnel exchanges across the Strait.\nThe maritime voyage from Pingtan to Taichung takes only 2 to 2.5 hours, and to Taipei about 2.5 to 3 hours. Relying on the direct maritime route, Pingtan and Taiwan can achieve a \"one-day working and living circle.\" Restoring the Pingtan-Taiwan maritime passenger direct route as soon as possible will greatly facilitate Fujian residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism, while also facilitating Taiwan residents coming to Fujian for exchanges, and will create the necessary conditions for resuming group tourism to Taiwan by Fujian residents. This is a beneficial measure that responds to the needs of people on both sides of the Strait and facilitates travel between them. The DPP authorities distort facts and repeatedly seek excuses to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, using them to fob off island residents. This disregards and harms the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and is not popular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637769.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, some individual media outlets on the island reported that the mainland coast guard engages in “double-standard enforcement,” “threatening, intimidating and driving away Taiwan fishing boats,” while turning a blind eye to mainland “three-no” fishing boats. What is your comment on this?","The relevant reports completely distort the facts and have ulterior motives. We are currently in the summer fishing moratorium period, and the coast guard is enforcing the law in accordance with regulations to maintain fishing production order, marine fishery resources, and the ecological environment in the relevant waters. Certain island media outlets with specific stances are attempting, through distortion, smears, and fabricated lies, to intimidate Taiwan fishermen and stir up hostility and confrontation across the Strait. Their attempts will not succeed. We hope that Taiwan compatriots, especially our fishermen friends, will open their eyes and not be deceived.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637768.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, recently said in an interview that the mainland is intimidating and coercing Taiwan through “military intimidation, economic coercion, and legal punishment,” and demanding acceptance of the One-China Principle, which is “the main cause of the tense and distant cross-Strait relations and the main source of instability in the status quo across the…","The relevant remarks completely disregard the facts and reverse black and white.\nWe have always respected, cared for, and benefited Taiwan compatriots, have consistently worked actively to promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and have remained committed to safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. The root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' refusal to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, and their obstinate adherence to a \"Taiwan independence\" stance. Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has continuously conducted \"Taiwan independence\" provocations, created hostility and confrontation across the Strait, undermined peace in the Taiwan Strait, harmed the well-being of compatriots, and seriously challenged the one-China principle. We firmly oppose this, and it must be countered and punished.\nPoll results on the island show that most Taiwan residents welcome the resumption of cross-Strait exchanges and reduced tensions. This once again demonstrates that peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. We advise the Lai Ching-te authorities to heed public opinion, recognize the situation, and abandon the illusions of \"resisting China and rejecting unification\" and \"seeking independence by relying on external forces.\" Any act that challenges the one-China principle and splits the country will inevitably fail. Any scheme that obstructs exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and creates cross-Strait opposition and confrontation will inevitably come to nothing.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637773.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan’s legislature recently passed a resolution requiring the DPP authorities to lift the “group tour ban,” and Taiwan’s tourism industry has also called for relaxing it as soon as possible. The DPP authorities said they will still review current policies on a rolling basis depending on cross-Strait interactions, while hoping the mainland will meet them halfway. What comment do you have?","The resolution passed by the island’s people’s representative body to lift the “group tour ban” conforms to the eager expectations of the broad Taiwan compatriots and the island’s tourism industry. The DPP authorities, disregarding public opinion and the demands of the island’s industry, have long delayed lifting the “group tour ban.” This forcibly deprives the Taiwan public of legitimate rights and seriously harms the interests of Taiwan’s tourism industry. We hope the DPP authorities will follow public opinion and take practical action to promote the resumption of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台台海之声和看台海新媒体记者","Recently, the online buzzword “city不city,” invented by some foreign bloggers in China, has spread to Taiwan. Through the interpretation of Taiwan's young people, “city不city” has become a word expressing affection for the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","The visa facilitation measures implemented by the Chinese government to facilitate foreigners’ entry and exit and to promote international exchanges and cooperation have let the world see a China of high-quality development and high-level opening. Compared with foreign friends, Taiwan compatriots find travel to the mainland even more convenient. Holding a five-year valid Taiwan Compatriot Permit, they can come over at any time without a visa endorsement. By linking Taiwan mobile phone numbers and bank cards to apps such as Alipay or WeChat, they can eat, stay, travel, and play on the mainland without obstacles.\nWe welcome and look forward to Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, coming to the mainland for a spontaneous trip. With just a plane ticket, a backpack, and a mobile phone, you can check in at scenic spots across the mainland, experience local customs, feel the splendor of Chinese culture, and savor local specialty snacks. Come to the mainland to look around, and you will find that the mainland is real, multidimensional, and lovable, and that mainland compatriots are kind, enthusiastic, and hospitable. Once you come, you will surely feel that it was not enough and want to come again, and again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","First, Lai Ching-te recently delivered a speech at the DPP National Congress entirely in Hokkien. In addition, the education authority under the DPP authorities recently announced that the “Hokkien Language Proficiency Certification Test” will be renamed the “Taiwan Taiyu Language Proficiency Certification Test.” What comment do you have on this?\nSecond, US presidential candidate Trump and his team have recently…","First question. This is yet another farce by the DPP authorities, who have painstakingly pursued “de-Sinicization.”\nThe Minnan and Hakka dialects spoken by Taiwan compatriots are the same as those spoken by compatriots in Fujian and Guangdong. They are regional branches or variants of Chinese that formed over a long history and were brought to Taiwan by early settlers from the Fujian and Guangdong areas. (Minnan) “Taiyu” is Minnan, which was passed from Fujian to Taiwan in ancient times, and people on both sides can understand each other. (Hakka) The Hakka dialect spoken by Taiwan compatriots was passed from Guangdong to Taiwan. The Hakka spoken on both sides is the same, and people on both sides can understand each other.\nThe DPP authorities’ attempt to make political hay out of dialect names is pure self-deception. No matter how they fiddle with it, they cannot erase the imprint of Chinese culture on Taiwan society, nor can they dilute the Chinese national consciousness of Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question. People on the island see very clearly that the United States always pursues so-called “America First,” and Taiwan will not be an exception. The DPP authorities are willing to be “chess pieces” and stubbornly “rely on the United States to seek independence.” Without principle or bottom line, they attach themselves to and cater to external forces, and they are going all the way down the evil path of selling out and harming Taiwan. The “chess piece” will ultimately become only a “discarded piece,” pushing Taiwan into a perilous situation and bringing profound harm to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Lo Wen-jia, Vice Chairman and Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that he is 100% sincere in promoting cross-Strait exchanges, and that his personal participation in events such as the Kinmen-Xiamen open-water swim race is all about extending goodwill. “If we never get a response, we will also get tired; once we are tired, the timing will be missed, and that would be a pity.” What…","One hundred percent goodwill requires one hundred percent action. The key is to adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and its core is a shared understanding of the basic fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation.\nWe will continue to work for promoting economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, deepening integrated development across the Strait in all fields, and improving the institutions and policies that enhance the well-being of compatriots in Taiwan. We have successively announced the resumption of group tours by mainland residents to Taiwan and the arrangements for mainland residents to travel to Taiwan, responding in good faith to the expectations of the Taiwan public and the tourism industry. We have issued policy documents to promote the construction of the Fujian Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. Regrettably, the DPP authorities not only have not responded to our goodwill, but have continued to crudely intimidate and obstruct Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland for exchanges, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and this is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”记者","It is summer vacation, and cross-Strait youth exchange activities are taking place one after another in various parts of the mainland. Please briefly introduce the relevant situation. Although the DPP authorities deliberately raised the travel warning for visiting the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao regions to “orange,” a large number of Taiwanese youths are not intimidated and are actively participating in…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should visit each other often, growing closer and more intimate. Recently, the enthusiasm for cross-Strait youth exchanges has continued to rise, and broad numbers of Taiwan youth have eagerly joined various cross-Strait exchange activities.\nOn July 3, the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Summit opened in Beijing, and several hundred Taiwan youth took part in a series of activities, including an internship and employment promotion event, the Beijing-Taiwan Youth Life Festival, and a Cross-Strait Youth Digital Music Night. On the same day, the opening ceremony of the 21st Taiwan Compatriot Youth Thousand-Person Summer Camp of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots and a Cross-Strait Youth Gala Evening were held in Fuzhou.\nOn July 8, the 7th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, and more than one thousand cross-Strait youth took part in forum activities on “intangible cultural heritage,” “e-commerce live streaming,” “film and television culture,” “technological innovation,” and other topics.\nOn July 21, the 2024 Cross-Strait Entrepreneur Elite Summit and Cross-Strait Youth Internship, Employment and Entrepreneurship Seminar opened in Kunshan, Jiangsu. The event aims to build a bridge connecting the emotions and careers of cross-Strait youth and to provide more convenience for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland.\nOn July 23, the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month opened in Suzhou, Jiangsu. More than two thousand Taiwan youth embarked on the Opera Journey, Arts Journey, Poetry Journey, Flavor Journey, Village Journey, and Innovation Journey in Suzhou, taking part in nearly 40 series of activities, including night market and garden tours, a Cross-Strait Food Festival, Hanfu experiences, calligraphy and painting sketching, Kunqu opera tracing, a sports carnival, and a Youth Animation Week. As the theme song of the Culture Month, “The Blue Sea of Youth,” sings, “The same dream, an endless future, merge into the sea of our youth.” It is said that a palm-leaf fan that can “fan away troubles” was the most popular souvenir of the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, bringing both coolness and good cheer.\nThis summer, the Straits will witness wave after wave of young people working together with a spirit of vitality and strength. Many Taiwan youth came to the mainland for the first time, saw with their own eyes the achievements of the mainland’s economic and social development, personally experienced the warmth and friendliness of mainland compatriots, deeply experienced the excellent traditional Chinese culture, and gained many insights and rewards. Cross-Strait youth shared their hearts through exchanges and built trust through interaction, jointly injecting youthful vitality and powerful momentum into promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. We welcome more Taiwan youth to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development in various ways, to advance hand in hand with mainland youth, share development opportunities, and create lasting well-being together.\nIt should be pointed out that Taiwan residents have a strong interest and willingness to travel and exchange on the mainland, and the industry on the island has also consistently called on the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to lift the ban on Taiwan travel agencies organizing group tours to the mainland as soon as possible. We hope the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will heed public opinion, stop brutally intimidating Taiwan residents from traveling and exchanging on the mainland, and stop harming the interests of Taiwan residents and related businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637770.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, Raymond Greene, the new director of the “American Institute in Taiwan,” recently met with Lai Ching-te and mentioned the U.S. “one China policy.” Taiwanese media noticed that the words “one China” were “muted” in the press release of the DPP authorities. May I ask how the spokesperson comments?","Adhering to the One-China principle is a widely shared consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. The DPP authorities' practice of deceiving themselves and others is extremely laughable and fully exposes their “ostrich mentality.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","Taiwanese media reported that a member of the public posted online a video showing that, while waiting at Taoyuan Airport to board a flight to Shanghai, they were asked by Mainland Affairs Council personnel to fill out relevant information. Some netizens on the island commented that the DPP's move was to create panic and add surveillance. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities' practice is entirely political manipulation. In pursuit of political self-interest, they disregard people's livelihood needs and well-being, and use all sorts of excuses and methods to interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges. The reason they do this is that they fear compatriots on both sides drawing closer and visiting one another, fear that Taiwan's people will come to understand the real situation on the mainland, and fear that the lies they have carefully fabricated will be exposed.\nTaiwan people who have visited the mainland all know very clearly that there is no so-called “travel risk” on the mainland at all. The DPP authorities' tactics of intimidating the public can neither fool people nor stop them. They will only increase Taiwan people's resentment and opposition toward the “green terror.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Cross-Strait consultations on the “2·14” vicious ship collision incident, originally scheduled to be held today in Kinmen, were postponed due to a typhoon. Could you introduce until when the postponement will last? What progress and consensus were the originally planned negotiations expected to achieve?\nSecond question: Reports indicate that the “Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” may be held in August.…","First question. Communication is currently under way on this matter, and we hope the relevant issues can be properly resolved through consultation.\nSecond question. We have consistently supported and actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups, counties and cities, and people from all walks of life, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” We will jointly oppose interference and sabotage by the DPP authorities, promote the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Strait and the routinization of exchanges in all fields, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云ETtoday记者","The two sides of the Strait had originally planned to hold consultations today in Kinmen on the “2·14” serious ship collision incident, but they were postponed due to the typhoon. Can this be interpreted as the incident now re-entering consultations? Can the Taiwan Affairs Office reveal what the key reason was for prompting both sides to resume negotiations? Liang Wen-chieh, Deputy Chairperson of the Mainland…","Everyone should have seen the announcement: affected by Typhoon No. 3 “Gaemi” this year, the Xiamen-Kinmen route at the Wutong Passenger Terminal was suspended for the entire day on July 24. We hope to maintain communication on this and properly resolve the related matters.\nAs for the approach taken by the Mainland Affairs Council personnel you mentioned, as long as they acknowledge the one-China principle and return to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” there will be no obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央通讯社”记者","After the release of the judicial documents on punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards, has the mainland's Taiwan-related authorities received any feedback from Taiwan businesspeople, or from Taiwan residents working or living on the mainland?","The mainland has issued judicial documents on punishing diehard “Taiwan independence” elements. Compatriots and businesspeople from Taiwan are paying close attention and discussing them enthusiastically. In summary, Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople generally hold two attitudes toward the judicial documents:\nFirst, they believe that issuing the judicial documents demonstrates the mainland’s firm resolve to punish diehard “Taiwan independence” elements. In the future, diehard “Taiwan independence” elements will certainly pay for their criminal acts. This can effectively curb “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, strictly crack down on lawbreakers, form a deterrent, and also give them a chance to turn back from the wrong path.\nSecond, they believe the targets of the judicial documents are clearly defined and specific. They are aimed at diehard “Taiwan independence” elements rather than the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, representing a precise strike against “Taiwan independence.”\nIt can be seen that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople have a very clear understanding of this judicial document. On the one hand, they see clearly that “Taiwan independence” is the greatest source of disaster that brings war and peril to Taiwan and harms their own interests. Only by severely punishing “Taiwan independence” separatist crimes in accordance with the law can everyone enjoy the dividends of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and live in peace and tranquility. On the other hand, they also see clearly that the judicial documents target diehard “Taiwan independence” elements rather than the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and that the interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots are being effectively protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Some Taiwan media said that mainland-issued judicial documents punishing “Taiwan independence” have caused concern among multinational companies on the mainland, which are considering transferring their Taiwan employees out. The DPP authorities said, “Try not to send Taiwan employees to work on the mainland.” What is your comment on this?","Using criminal justice measures to punish those who split the country and to safeguard core national interests is common practice in countries around the world. The judicial document we issued was formulated strictly in accordance with law, with precisely defined targets. It applies only to a very small number of 'Taiwan independence' diehards whose 'independence' remarks and actions are egregious and whose 'independence' activities are rampant, and to the crimes of splitting the country and inciting secession that they commit.\nBroad numbers of Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwanese employees working at multinational companies, need have no concerns as long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities. They can study, work and live on the mainland with complete peace of mind. We will, as always, respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to build a first-class business environment that is market-oriented, rule-based and internationalized, and help Taiwan compatriots share the broad opportunities and bright prospects of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The Taiwan fishing boat “Dajinman No. 88” was seized by the mainland side for fishing across the line in waters off Kinmen and Xiamen. Does the spokesperson have any new explanation on this case?","On July 2, the Fujian Coast Guard lawfully seized the Taiwanese fishing vessel “Da Jin Man 88,” which is suspected of illegal fishing. The relevant authorities are handling the matter lawfully and in accordance with regulations, while lawfully protecting the legitimate rights and interests of the relevant crew members.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻云ETtoday记者","First question: The fishing boat “Da Jin Man 88” did violate regulations first, but when cross-Strait relations were good, many matters could be discussed and resolved through consultation. Now that cross-Strait communication mechanisms have been cut off, outside observers believe the mainland side is intending to “kill the chicken to scare the monkey” this time. What is your assessment? Second question: Will the…","On the first question: We are currently in the summer fishing moratorium period, and the Fujian Coast Guard is carrying out normal law enforcement operations to maintain fishing production order, marine fishery resources, and the ecological environment in the relevant waters.\nOn the second question: The relevant authorities are handling the matter and will deal with it in accordance with laws and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","Chiu Chui-cheng (邱垂正), chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, recently said in an interview that the mainland’s judicial documents punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards “seriously harm cross-Strait relations” and are a very typical “lawfare.” He said Taiwan residents should carefully consider the necessity of traveling to the mainland and to Hong Kong and Macao. What is your comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait; it is the source of trouble that leads to the danger of war in the Taiwan Strait, social division and confrontation, and damage to people's interests. Punishing in accordance with the law the extremely small number of hardline “Taiwan independence” diehards whose words and deeds related to “independence” are egregious and whose “independence” activities are rampant is an inherent requirement and a necessary step to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to genuinely safeguard the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe mainland side has issued and implemented judicial documents on punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards in accordance with the law, which target only an extremely small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards. Cowed by the enormous pressure of the judicial documents, the DPP authorities deliberately conflate the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots with the extremely small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards, attempt to drag innocent people in as scapegoats for “Taiwan independence,” smear the judicial documents, incite cross-Strait confrontation, and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges. This seriously infringes upon the legitimate rights and interests of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nIt must be pointed out that the sinister intentions and deceptive tactics of the DPP authorities have been seen through by more and more Taiwan compatriots. Everyone can see that recently, one group after another of Taiwan compatriots have eagerly come to the mainland to visit, demonstrating through concrete actions their wish and determination to actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and support the development of cross-Strait relations. We sincerely welcome and support the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation through various forms, injecting confidence and vitality into the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240724_12637772.htm"],[2,"2024-07-24","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","Admission results for mainland students pursuing master’s and doctoral programs in Taiwan for the 2024 academic year were announced on the 15th, the lowest in 14 years since Taiwan began admitting degree-seeking mainland students. Some island scholars have argued that the DPP authorities should guarantee the convenience and fair treatment of mainland students coming to Taiwan. What is your comment?","There are two situations I hope everyone can understand. First, we have long been committed to providing mainland students from Taiwan with treatment equal to that of mainland students, offering support and guarantees in areas such as medical care, internships, and employment, and we have also established scholarships. Second, as everyone can see, the DPP authorities have artificially restricted cross-Strait exchanges and mainland students studying in Taiwan, and have subjected mainland students in Taiwan to many unfair treatments. We advise the DPP authorities to remove political barriers as soon as possible and genuinely safeguard the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan, so that mainland students will regain the willingness to study in Taiwan and island universities can develop better.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202407/t20240724_12637766.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, it has been reported that the \"Rim of the Pacific 2024\" military exercise is being held around Hawaii, and one of its subjects is sinking a 40,000-ton amphibious assault ship. Some analysts believe this is a demonstration aimed at China. The U.S. Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, CQ Brown, recently said that if China and the United States came into conflict over the Taiwan…","Regarding the first question: We have noted the relevant reports. If anyone wants to use military exercises to frighten China or to make empty threats against China, that is entirely a pipe dream. The Chinese military has always been fearless of evil, unafraid of ghosts, and unintimidated by pressure. It has the resolve, the capability, and the means to defeat all invading enemies and to defend national sovereignty, security, and development interests.\nRegarding the second question: In accordance with the annual cooperation plan between the Chinese and Russian militaries, on July 25 the two sides jointly organized a joint aerial strategic patrol in relevant airspace over the Bering Sea. This is the eighth joint aerial strategic patrol organized by the two militaries since 2019, which further tests and enhances the coordination capabilities of the two air forces and deepens strategic mutual trust and practical cooperation between the two militaries. This action is not directed at any third party, is in line with international law and international practice, and is unrelated to the current international and regional situation.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media reports, after obtaining the key component, an electro-optical periscope, Taiwan's first self-built submarine, the “Hai Kun,” is undergoing follow-up verification work and may conduct sea trials in September. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities' “seeking independence through force” is entirely a path to self-destruction. No matter how many weapons they build or how much equipment they buy, it is only a waste of public resources and mere window dressing. If the “Hai Kun” were used for “seeking independence through force,” it would sooner or later become fish in the net of the PLA.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the Taiwan military organized the “Han Kuang 40” exercise, which focused on scenario-free realistic combat. For the first time, it released a sample of “unit rules of engagement” carry card, aiming to enhance the “legality” and legitimacy of the Taiwan military’s use of force. The exercise also rehearsed subjects such as the transfer of overseas materiel. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities have exhausted every trick, attempting to dress up separatist activities in the cloak of “legal” and “legitimate.” This is merely self-deception. The DPP authorities have deliberately turned the island into a battlefield and the people into human shields, attempting to “pursue independence by force” and “resist reunification by force.” This is sheer overestimation of their own strength, and in the end there is only one dead end.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lai Ching-te, leader of the Taiwan region, recently said that the mainland's “gray harassment” of the Taiwan Strait and surrounding areas is increasing day by day. Taiwan's defense authorities have, starting recently, added English-language broadcasts to drive away mainland military aircraft, and for the first time released information on PLA Rocket Force test launches and China Coast Guard vessel activities…","The DPP authorities are merely showing off and whistling in the dark to bolster their courage. The PLA’s actions are not deterred by any reconnaissance interference, and our determination to defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering.\nOn the afternoon of July 25, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, and reporters on site asked questions.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that a recent Japanese government assessment, analyzing the PLA's military exercises last year, concluded that the PLA now has the full capability to complete the seizure of an island within a week. Under joint operations by all service branches, the PLA would need only a few days to go from maritime and airspace blockade of Taiwan to landing large ground forces on the island. May I ask what the…","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. China will eventually be reunified, and reunification will inevitably be achieved. We adhere to striving for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and coerce, or even cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on foreign powers for self-strengthening” has no way out, and “resisting reunification by force” is a dead end. We will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness, resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nOn the afternoon of July 25, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, and reporters asked questions on site.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-07-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to foreign media reports, Japan recently conducted a joint maritime exercise with Taiwan. The reports said this exercise targeted the current situation in the East China Sea and South China Sea. How does the spokesperson comment on this?","We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose Japan's joint maritime training with the Taiwan region of China. We urge Japan to abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, immediately correct its mistake, not condone or support the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form, and not create disruptions to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait or to China-Japan relations.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16327032.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-07-29","Lin Jian","China News Service","It’s reported that Silvia García, President of the Central American Parliament, just concluded her visit to China. Could you share more details about the visit with us?","At the invitation of Chairman Zhao Leji of the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, President of the Central American Parliament Silvia García led the leadership of the Parliament on a visit to China—the first of its kind—from July 21 to 27. Chairman Zhao Leji and Chairman Wang Huning of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference met with the delegation respectively. The two sides had a cordial and in-depth exchange of views on issues of mutual interest and reached common understandings on further deepening friendly cooperation. Both sides were of the view that the decision made by the Central American Parliament last August to revoke the “permanent observer” status of Taiwan’s “Legislative Yuan” and accept the National People’s Congress of China as a permanent observer is of historic importance. They agreed that the decision shows again that the one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. The one-China principle is where the global opinion trends and the arc of history bends, and what serves the interest of the Central American Parliament and the people of Central American countries.\nIn addition to Beijing, the delegation visited Shanghai and Shenzhen, and learned more about China’s development. President García and members of the delegation reaffirmed the commitment of the Central American Parliament to the one-China principle and support for China’s reunification. Strengthening solidarity and cooperation with China helps Central American countries seize opportunities for development and prosperity. The Central American Parliament stands ready to deepen exchanges with the National People’s Congress at various levels to learn from China’s development experience, contribute to greater mutual understanding, trust and cooperation between Central American countries and China, and jointly promote South-South cooperation, multipolarity in the world and democracy in international relations. The Chinese side expressed readiness to work with the Central American Parliament and relevant countries to advance China’s relations with countries in Central America to deliver more benefits for Chinese and Central American peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463973.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240729_11462477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-29","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the ASEAN Plus Foreign Ministers’ Meetings and paid an official visit to Laos over the past couple of days. Can you share more information with us?","From July 25 to 27, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers’ Meeting , the ASEAN Plus Three Foreign Ministers’ Meeting , t he East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting and the ASEAN Regional Forum Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Vientiane, Laos and paid an official visit to Laos. On the margins of the meetings, Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the first informal trilateral meeting between the foreign ministers of China, Russia and Laos , and met with his counterparts from over ten countries and international organizations, including India , Russia , Japan , the UK , the ROK , the EU , the Philippines and the US . China has released readouts which you may refer to.\nAt the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted that China and ASEAN are friendly neighbors and close partners who have always supported each other, and more importantly, one community with a shared future sticking together through thick and thin. Recent years have seen fruitful results in building the China-ASEAN community with a shared future. Economic and trade ties have continued to thrive, people-to-people and cultural exchanges have quickly bounced back, more solid progress has been made in enhancing connectivity, and the two sides keep finding new areas where we can work together. The dialogue and cooperation between China and ASEAN is the best example of the fruitful and vigorous cooperation in the Asia-Pacific. Four things have made it possible: good neighborliness, sincerity, common development, and openness and inclusiveness. The third plenary session of the 20th Central Committee of the CPC made an overall plan for further deepening reform comprehensively with a view to advancing Chinese modernization. China will continue to firmly support the strategic independence of ASEAN, support strengthening the regional cooperation mechanisms with ASEAN at the center, and build a peaceful, safe and secure, prosperous, beautiful and amicable home for China and ASEAN. We stand ready to share China’s opportunities with ASEAN countries, and join hands with them to advance the modernization process of Asia.\nAt the ASEAN Plus Three Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted that over the past two decades and more, as one of the most well-established mechanisms for regional cooperation in East Asia, the ASEAN Plus Three mechanism has brought regional countries together to deepen practical cooperation in various areas and meet challenges such as the financial crisis and COVID-19. China stands ready to fully leverage the mechanism to deepen economic integration and enhance connectivity, to enhance crisis response and maintain stability, to expand cooperation in emerging areas and galvanize development, and to promote people-to-people exchanges and build up consensus among ASEAN Plus Three countries, so as to provide new impetus for the development of the wider region.\nAt the 14th East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted that the East Asia Summit needs to keep to the right direction, enhance solidarity and coordination, contribute to long-term peace and prosperity in the region, and safeguard international fairness and justice. First, jointly upholding the open and inclusive regional framework, and guarding against forming exclusive groupings by certain countries from outside the region. Second, jointly adhering to rules in the region recognized by all, rather than letting certain countries put their own “rules” above international laws and regional rules recognized by all. Third, jointly providing new quality driving force for connectivity, since decoupling, severing supply chains and “small yard with high fences” will only fragment the regional economy. Fourth, jointly invigorating the East Asia Summit to promote balanced progress of both of its wheels—political security and economic development.\nAt the 31st ASEAN Regional Forum Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, Foreign Minister Wang Yi made a four-point proposal on responding to the challenges we face today. First, upholding the vision for peace and keeping to the path of common, comprehensive, cooperative and sustainable security. Second, remaining committed to the ASEAN way, enhancing mutual trust through dialogue and safeguarding security through cooperation. Third, consolidating the foundation for cooperation to provide greater impetus for confidence building measures and preventive diplomacy. Fourth, stepping up dialogue and consultation. No matter how complex the issue is, we need to stay committed to dialogue and consultation. No matter how intense the conflict is, we should never give up effort to seek political settlement.\nDuring his visit to Laos, Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with General Secretary of the Lao People’s Revolutionary Party and President of Laos Thongloun Sisoulith and Prime Minister Sonexay Siphandone respectively, and held talks with Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Saleumxay Kommasith . Foreign Minister Wang Yi stressed that China and Laos have formed an unbreakable community with a shared future. China will continue to be the most reliable friend and most trustworthy partner of Laos. We are ready to share reform and development experience with Laos in a timely way, jointly enhance governance capacity and advance the socialist cause. We would like to deepen cooperation with Laos on all fronts and provide driving forces for Laos’ economic growth. We also support Laos for assuming the rotating presidency of ASEAN and for playing a bigger role in international and regional affairs.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi also elaborated on China’s position on the Taiwan question and the South China Sea issue on separate occasions in Laos. He stressed that the Taiwan question is one hundred percent China’s internal affair, which no foreign forces have the right to interfere in. To truly uphold cross-Strait peace, one must firmly reject all “Taiwan independence” moves. Recently China reached provisional arrangement with the Philippines on humanitarian resupply of living necessities to Ren’ai Jiao. The Philippines needs to honor its commitment, stop flip-flopping and going back on its word, and not backpedal or create problems again. Otherwise, China will make a resolute response. Foreign Minister Wang Yi also reiterated China’s principled position on the Palestinian question and the Ukraine crisis, and stressed that China will continue to play a constructive role for ceasefire and political settlement.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463973.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240729_11462477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-29","Lin Jian","AFP","After the US-Japan 2+2 meeting in Tokyo, the US and Japan issued the joint statement and said that China’s foreign policy seeks to reshape the international order for its own benefit at the expense of others. What’s China’s comment?","The joint statement issued by Japan and the US lacks factual basis. The statement frames and attacks China’s foreign policies and grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs. The statement falsely accuses China on maritime issues and points fingers at China’s normal military development and defense policy. The statement propagates “China threat,” and creates scare through the talk of regional tensions. China deplores and opposes it.\nChina is a force for world peace, a contributor to global development and a defender of international order. China is committed to the path of peaceful development and a defense policy that is defensive in nature. China’s defense development and military activities are justified and reasonable. China always keeps its nuclear strength at the minimum level as required by national security. China does not pose a threat to any country.\nIt is Japan and the US that are pursuing their agenda at the expense of other countries’ security interests and the welfare of people in the Asia-Pacific. The US and Japan keep emphasizing regional peace and security and a rule-based order, all the while ganging up to form exclusive clubs, engage in group politics, incite bloc confrontation, and disrupt regional peace, security and stability. On top of that, Japan and the US have been seeking to strengthen the Cold War relic of “extended deterrence,” and developing the so-called “nuclear deterrence.” This will drive up regional tensions and trigger nuclear proliferation and conflict risks.\nIssues related to Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, and Xizang are purely China’s internal affairs and brook no external interference. The biggest threat to cross-Strait peace at present is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. If Japan and the US truly care about cross-Strait peace and stability, what they should do is uphold the one-China principle, oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, and support China’s reunification.\nChina will always defend its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. We are committed to properly settling bilateral maritime issues with countries directly concerned through dialogue and consultation. The real provocative actions are the constant meddling by the US and other countries outside the region, including their muscle flexing in waters off China’s coast, including the East and South China Seas.\nWe call on the US and Japan to immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop creating confrontation, stop triggering a new Cold War, do what is conducive to regional strategic stability, and not become a source of danger and disruption for peace and tranquility in the Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463973.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240729_11462477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-07-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters’ questions\n(July 29, 2024)\nQ: According to reports from Taiwan media citing informed sources, cross-Strait consultations on the “2·14” ship collision incident are scheduled to be held in Kinmen on July 30. Personnel from both sides will go to Kinmen on the 29th to discuss details, and the formal consultations will begin on the 30th, at which they will sign a consensus document. The mainland side will send a section chief of the Association for Relations across the Taiwan Straits and other relevant persons, while the Taiwan side’s members include personnel from the Mainland Affairs Council, the Straits Exchange Foundation, and the Coast Guard Administration. What is your response?\nA: Recently, the Jinjiang Red Cross will send personnel to accompany family members to Kinmen to handle relevant matters through consultation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202407/t20240729_12638859.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-07-30","Lin Jian","Reuters","The Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China said several international lawmakers attending their summit in Taipei had received phone calls and emails from Chinese officials and that it was an attempt to affect the summit. Do you have a comment on that matter?","The so-called “alliance” you mentioned is hellbent on attacking China on various issues and spreading lies and rumors about China and has no credibility to speak of. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. China firmly opposes official interaction of any form between the Taiwan authorities and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. We urge relevant lawmakers to abandon ideological bias, stop using the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs, and act in the interest of bilateral ties, not otherwise.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463972.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240730_11463119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-30","Lin Jian","AFP","My question follows on the Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China. The Taiwanese leader Lai Ching-te has addressed that summit. And he said that “a threat from China to any country is a threat to the world.” And he also has urged global democracies to unite against what he calls “authoritarian expansion.” What’s China’s response to these remarks?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. As I’ve just said, the so-called “alliance” you mentioned is hellbent on attacking China on various issues and spreading lies and rumors about China and has no credibility to speak of.\nLet me stress once again that “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with cross-Strait peace as fire with water. Separatism for “Taiwan independence” is the most serious challenge facing the international order, the most dangerous attempt to alter the status quo that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, and the biggest detriment to cross-Strait peace. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ attempts to seek “Taiwan independence” by force will prove to be futile. They are not making Taiwan any safer by squandering money on weapons, but are turning Taiwan into a cash machine for the countries selling the weapons. No matter how they try to beef up “national defense” and pedal the “democracy versus authoritarianism” narrative, they will not stop the trend towards China’s reunification.\nThe one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and prevailing international consensus. It is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ attempt to seek independence, make provocations and resist reunification by force will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463972.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240730_11463119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-30","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Just now you said that Lai Ching-te has used force to seek independence. I’m just wondering, can you give us one example of a time that he’s used force?","Just now I mentioned how the Lai Ching-te authorities have been trying to seek “Taiwan independence” by force. They are not making Taiwan any safer by squandering money on weapons. No matter how they try to beef up so-called “national defense,” they will not stop the trend towards China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463972.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240730_11463119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-30","Lin Jian","Beijing Youth Daily","My colleague asked a question about the Japan-US 2+2 meeting and the Japan-US ministerial meeting on extended deterrence. In addition to these two events, the Japan-Australia-India-US Foreign Ministers’ Meeting was also held in Tokyo on Sunday and Monday. The joint statement issued by the Japan-US 2+2 meeting criticized China’s foreign policy. What’s China’s comments?","Despite China’s grave concerns, Japan and the US grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs on Taiwan, Hong Kong, Xinjiang, and Xizang, and falsely accused China on maritime issues. Under the Cold War mentality, those two countries have been practicing bloc politics, inciting bloc confrontation, damaging regional peace and stability, and harming other countries’ security interest. China firmly opposes this and has lodged serious protests with the Japanese side through diplomatic channel. We call on Japan to view China in an objective and rational light, stop its political manipulation on China’s domestic affairs, stop making provocations on maritime issues, stop ganging up with countries outside the region to create division and confrontation in the region, follow a path of peaceful development, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the wider international community through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202407/t20240731_11463972.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240730_11463119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-07-31","Lin Jian","China Review News","It’s reported the leader of the Taiwan region Lai Ching-te said on July 30 at the summit of the “Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China” that the Chinese mainland misinterprets the UNGA Resolution 2758 to restrict Taiwan’s international participation and to construct a basis for “the use of force against Taiwan.” What’s your response?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an undeniable fact.\nThe UNGA Resolution 2758 settled once and for all the question of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the United Nations. The Resolution made it clear that there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China, not a country. It also made clear that there is only one seat of China in the United Nations, and the representatives of the Government of the People’s Republic of China are the only lawful representatives of China to the United Nations, precluding “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” The one-China principle is observed by the UN and its specialized agencies on the Taiwan question. Taiwan is referred to as “Taiwan, province of China” in all UN’s official documents. It was clearly stated in the official legal opinions of the Office of Legal Affairs of the UN Secretariat that “the United Nations considers ‘Taiwan’ as a province of China with no separate status,” and the “‘authorities’ in ‘Taipei’ are not considered to ... enjoy any form of government status.”\nUNGA Resolution 2758 contains unequivocal recognition of the one-China principle—a basic norm and prevailing consensus for the global community, there is no way to “misinterpret” that. Taiwan, being part of China, simply does not qualify for “sovereign status”. The Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations should and can only be handled in line with the one-China principle. Taiwan is definitely not inherently entitled to “participation in international organizations.”\nI would like to stress again that the one-China principle is unshakable and the trend of China realizing reunification is unstoppable. “Taiwan independence” separatism is a dead end. Whatever the Lai Ching-te authorities say or do, it does not change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China or the legal status of the UNGA Resolution 2758, and still less the historic trend that China will and must achieve reunification.\n***********************************************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240801_11464132.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202407/t20240731_11463810.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-01","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","It’s reported that after China-Japan foreign ministers’ meeting on July 26, China altered and published the Japanese Foreign Minister’s remarks. China’s readout stated that Japan’s commitment to the one-China position remains unchanged and that Japan’s control on semiconductor export is not targeted at any particular country, and Japan is willing to maintain constructive communication with the Chinese side to…","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and prevailing international consensus. It’s also the political premise on which China establishes and develops diplomatic relations with any country in the world. Japan made a clear commitment on this in the 1972 China-Japan Joint Statement , which says “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this position of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its position under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” According to my knowledge, Japanese Foreign Minister Yoko Kamikawa reaffirmed Japan’s position during the meeting, which has not changed.\nWhen it comes to semiconductors, certain country, to perpetuate its supremacy, has been turning normal economic cooperation and trade into political and security issues, either enticing or coercing other countries to join its tech blockade against China, and deliberately disrupting global supply and industrial chains. We have noted that Japanese officials have repeatedly stated publicly that their export control measures on semiconductors are not directed at any particular country. China will work with countries around the world to stay open and pursue cooperation, and keep the global semiconductor industrial and supply chains stable.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240801_11464855.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240801_11464776.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-08-01","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 31 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to a question on July 31 that the so-called \"Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China (IPAC)\" is a patchwork of extreme anti-China elements who are accustomed to provoking trouble on Taiwan-related issues, fabricating and spreading rumors and lies. We have repeatedly expressed our…","Chen Binhua pointed out: In fact, after the founding of the People's Republic of China in 1949, it became the sole legitimate government representing all of China. This was a change of regime while the international legal subject, China, remained unchanged, and China's sovereignty and inherent territory did not change. The People's Republic of China naturally and fully enjoys and exercises China's sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The 26th session of the UN General Assembly in 1971 adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore the lawful seat of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations. This thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all China in the United Nations, and made clear that China has only one seat in the United Nations, and that there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nChen Binhua said: The one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. It is also the political foundation on which 183 countries have established diplomatic relations with China, and it fully reflects international justice and the will of the people. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and repeatedly collude with anti-China forces in the United States and Western countries to slander and attack UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. This cannot shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle, and will only make the international community more clearly aware that Taiwan is a part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240801_12639454.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-08-02","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that the Canadian Navy frigate HMCS Montreal transited the Taiwan Strait on July 31. The Canadian Defence Minister subsequently reiterated Canada’s commitment to a “free, open and inclusive” Indo-Pacific. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Zhang Xiaogang: The Eastern Theater Command has responded to the Canadian frigate “Montreal” transiting the Taiwan Strait and to the hype surrounding it. China has lodged solemn representations with the Canadian side through military diplomatic channels. Canadian warships harassing and disrupting the situation in the Taiwan Strait send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and seriously endanger peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It should be pointed out that the Canadian side's high-profile hyping of its wrongful conduct to boost its sense of presence, and its brazen search for excuses to mislead public opinion, is an error compounded by further errors. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We solemnly warn the Canadian side to abide by the one-China principle, be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, and avoid affecting the development of bilateral relations and military-to-military relations between the two countries.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/TopStories/16329123.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16329088.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-08-08","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲8日答记者","BEIJING, August 8 (Xinhua) — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 8th, pointing out that the DPP authorities deliberately conflate the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots with a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements, attempting to use innocent people as shields for “Taiwan independence.” Their attempt to smear the…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that Taiwan is part of China, and the country will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. Punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements according to law for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity, and a just act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. People on both sides of the Strait strongly support the measures to punish “independence” according to law. They believe that precisely targeting die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements is effective, and they fully recognize that punishment according to law targets only a tiny minority of die-hard elements who engage in egregious pro-independence words and deeds and rampant independence-seeking activities, and who commit the crimes of splitting the country and inciting its splitting. It does not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian said that the purpose of removing the bad apples that undermine cross-Strait relations is to fundamentally safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to ensure the security and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. More and more Taiwan compatriots have seen through the DPP authorities’ sinister intentions and deceptive tactics, and have shown a strong desire to take part in cross-Strait exchanges, actively participating in exchanges and supporting the development of cross-Strait relations. According to statistics, from January to June this year, cross-Strait personnel exchanges totaled 2.083 million person-trips, up 99.5% year on year, of which 1.928 million trips were made by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland, up 103.2% year on year. This fully shows that the historical tide of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is rolling forward and will not be affected by the lies and deceptions of the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will grasp the historical trend, uphold the righteousness of the nation, draw a clear line with die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, actively take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and jointly safeguard our common home, the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240808_12641254.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions\n(August 13, 2024)\nQuestion: On July 2, mainland coast guard officers seized a Taiwanese fishing vessel, the “Da Jin Man 88,” suspected of illegal fishing in waters near Quanzhou. Today, apart from its skipper, Mr. Hong, the other four crew members have all returned to Taiwan. What is your comment?\nAnswer: The relevant mainland authorities attach great importance to protecting fishery resources and maintaining normal order in the relevant waters. The coast guard enforces the law in accordance with the law while also safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of the relevant crew members. For the four persons whose violations were minor, criminal liability will not be pursued, and they were arranged to return on August 13. One person suspected of illegal fishing is still under further investigation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240813_12642292.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-08-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the DPP authorities may once again seek to purchase E-2D early warning aircraft from the United States. In addition, the Taiwan defense department's military delegation in the US recently signed an “advance planning for upgrading information and communications systems” tender with the “American Institute in Taiwan,” aimed at enhancing the data link capabilities of the Taiwan military's…","The DPP authorities are lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people to purchase U.S. weapons. This is entirely an act of selling out, harming, and ruining Taiwan, and is nothing more than a self-consolation to cater to the U.S. side.\nWe firmly oppose the United States engaging in any form of official exchanges and military contacts with Taiwan, China, and urge the U.S. side to genuinely abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan, and work with China in the same direction to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16331688.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-08-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council answers reporters' questions\n(August 16, 2024)\nQuestion: The DPP authorities recently said that relevant mainland departments “abuse vague and unclear laws to detain people, treating Taiwanese who advocate democracy and freedom as “Taiwan independence” separatist forces or spies”; that they “intimidate” Taiwan and carry out “cognitive warfare.” What is your comment?\nAnswer: The remarks of the DPP authorities are a completely malicious distortion that misleads public opinion. They deliberately confuse a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements with the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and deliberately confuse espionage crimes with normal exchange activities between people on both sides of the Strait. They not only seek to deceive and intimidate the Taiwan public and harm their interests, but also attempt to cover up their sinister intent of provoking “independence,” splitting the country and undermining cross-Strait relations.\n“Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is the root of war danger, social division and confrontation, and harm to people's interests in the Taiwan Strait. Only by eliminating the “害群之马” (the “bad apples”) who undermine cross-Strait relations can we truly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and effectively safeguard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. People on both sides of the Strait strongly support the measures to punish “independence” in accordance with the law. They fully recognize that what is punished in accordance with the law is a very small number of die-hard elements whose words and deeds are vile and whose “independence” plotting is rampant, and that it does not involve the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nWe firmly support normal and healthy cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, and we protect the lawful and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. We hope that in a safe and healthy exchange environment, compatriots on both sides can exchange with peace of mind and come and go with confidence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240816_12643098.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-08-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 16 (dispatch): Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a question on the 16th, saying: We note that the relevant Taiwan authorities have released the conclusions of their investigation into the “February 14” malicious ship collision incident. The so-called “investigation conclusions” disregard the facts and deliberately shirk responsibility, which we cannot accept. The relevant parties in Taiwan should publicly disclose the facts truthfully, strictly punish those responsible, and ensure that similar incidents do not happen again.\nA reporter asked: On the 16th, the Kinmen District Prosecutors Office announced the investigation conclusions of the “February 14” collision incident. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on this? Zhu Fenglian made the above statement in response to the question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240816_12643128.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-08-19","Mao Ning","Reuters","Two German military vessels plan to transit through the Taiwan Strait next month. What’s the Ministry’s comment?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. The key to keeping the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable lies in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence.” China opposes attempts to undermine China’s territorial sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240819_11475916.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240819_11475763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-21","Mao Ning","CCTV","General Secretary of the Communist Party of Viet Nam (CPV) Central Committee and State President To Lam concluded his state visit to China. Could you share more details with us, including the major outcomes and highlights of the visit?","General Secretary of the Communist Party of Viet Nam (CPV) Central Committee and State President To Lam was invited to pay a state visit to China from August 18 to 20. This was Comrade To Lam’s first overseas visit after taking office as General Secretary. He was given high-level reception in China. General Secretary and President Xi Jinping and General Secretary and State President To Lam had talks and a good chat over tea. Premier Li Qiang of the State Council, Chairman Zhao Leji of the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, and Chairman Wang Huning of the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference met with him respectively.\nThe top leaders of the two parties and two countries made strategic planning on deepening the China-Viet Nam community with a shared future and provided political guidance for the growth of bilateral ties in the next stage. Both sides were of the view that the common ideals and beliefs are the red genes passed down from generation to generation between the two parties, forming the traditional friendship between the two countries that “So profound is the friendship between Viet Nam and China, because we are both comrades and brothers.” As the two governing communist parties in today’s world, the CPC and the CPV should uphold their original aspiration of friendship, continue their traditional friendship, keep in mind their common mission, uphold the leadership of the Communist Party and the socialist system, jointly promote the development of the cause of socialism in the world, and contribute to the peace and progress of humanity.\nBoth sides agreed that during the critical period of development and revitalization in both countries, China and Viet Nam should firmly follow the path jointly set by the elder generation of leaders of the two countries, in particular, General Secretary Xi Jinping and General Secretary Nguyen Phu Trong, solidify a development pattern of greater political mutual trust, more solid security cooperation, deeper mutually beneficial cooperation, stronger popular support, closer multilateral coordination and better handling of differences, and advance the building of a China-Viet Nam community with a shared future that carries strategic significance.\nBoth sides agreed that it’s important to maintain close strategic communication and high-level exchanges and step up institutional cooperation in strategic areas such as diplomacy, national defense and security; expand cooperation in the synergy between the Belt and Road Initiative and the “Two Corridors, One Economic Belt” initiative, accelerate the “physical connectivity” of railway, highway and port infrastructure, enhance the “institutional connectivity” of smart customs, and jointly build secure and stable industrial and supply chains. Taking the opportunity of celebrating the 75th anniversary of the establishment of China-Viet Nam diplomatic relations next year, the two sides should jointly hold a series of activities such as the China-Viet Nam Year of People-to-People Exchanges to consolidate the popular support of the two countries.\nBoth sides agreed to uphold the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence and other basic norms governing international relations, promote an equal and orderly multipolar world and a universally beneficial and inclusive economic globalization, uphold international fairness and justice and the common interests of developing countries, work to build a community with a shared future for mankind, and contribute to world peace and development. Viet Nam reaffirmed that it firmly pursues the one-China policy, and recognized that there is but one China in the world, that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and that the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. It supports the peaceful development of cross-Strait ties and China’s reunification, firmly opposes all forms of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and will not develop any forms of official ties with the Taiwan region.\nBoth sides issued a joint statement, which fully demonstrates the outcomes of the visit. Relevant departments and local governments of the two countries signed multiple bilateral cooperation documents on Party schools, connectivity, industry, finance, customs inspection and quarantine, health, news organizations and media, locality, and people’s livelihood, which say a lot about the progress in building the China-Viet Nam community with a shared future.\nStanding at the new starting point of historic importance, China stands ready to work with Viet Nam to follow the guidance of the important common understandings between the top leaders of the two parties and two countries, focus on the six overall goals of “greater political mutual trust, more solid security cooperation, deeper mutually beneficial cooperation, stronger popular support, closer multilateral coordination and better handling of differences”, enhance political mutual trust, strengthen mutually beneficial cooperation, deepen people-to-people and cultural exchanges, deepen and solidify the building of the China-Viet Nam community with a shared future, promote each other’s socialist modernization and contribute to world peace and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240821_11477550.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240821_11477444.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-21","Mao Ning","AFP","At a regional security forum held in Taiwan today, Lai Ching-te noted China’s growing authoritarianism abroad. The former US ambassador to the UN and the former Japanese prime minister will also address the forum. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair which brooks no external interference.\nIt is the DPP authorities’ go-to tactic to mislead the public and engage in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities under all kinds of pretexts. However, no matter what they say or do, the DPP authorities cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, or stop the historic trend that China will achieve reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240821_11477550.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240821_11477444.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-22","Mao Ning","Hubei Media Group","Special Envoy of the United Nations Secretary-General on Myanmar Julie Bishop visited China recently. Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with her. Could you share more details with us?","At the invitation of the Chinese side, Special Envoy of the UN Secretary-General on Myanmar Julie Bishop visited China on August 20 and 21. Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister Wang Yi, and Special Envoy for Asian Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs Deng Xijun met with her respectively. They had in-depth exchange of views on the Myanmar issue.\nChina respects Myanmar’s sovereignty, independence, national unity and territorial integrity, and stays committed to non-interference in Myanmar’s internal affairs and the Myanmar-owned and Myanmar-led peace process. China supports ASEAN’s role as the main channel and hopes that ASEAN’s five-point consensus on Myanmar and Myanmar’s new five-point roadmap will create good momentum for each other and be effectively implemented. China supports the UN in playing a constructive role in the political settlement of the Myanmar issue, and stands ready to provide support and assistance to the Special Envoy in performing her duties. We hope the Special Envoy will uphold an objective and just position, handle relations between all parties in a balanced manner, bear in mind the long-term interests of the Myanmar people, and help the Myanmar side find an effective way to bridge differences.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240822_11478124.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240822_11478102.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-22","Mao Ning","Reuters","Paraguay has said recently that it is open to trade deals with China through the trade bloc Mercosur despite maintaining diplomatic ties with Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","On the normalization of China-Paraguay relations, China made clear its position more than once. We hope the government and leader of Paraguay will follow the trend of history, meet the aspiration of its people, stand on the right side of history as early as possible, join the overwhelming majority of the international community and make the right decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the country.\nChina values trade and economic cooperation with Mercosur and Latin American countries. I believe with the joint effort of all parties, such cooperation will achieve positive progress.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240822_11478124.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240822_11478102.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-23","Mao Ning","Reuters","Are you able to tell us whether China has invited Eswatini which maintains “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan to the upcoming Forum on China-Africa Cooperation?","On the FOCAC Summit, there will be more details that we can share in due course. Please stay tuned. Let me stress that the one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community. Around the world, 183 countries have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. We hope the very few countries who still maintain so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan will see clearly the trend of history and make a right decision that truly serves their own interests at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240823_11478906.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240823_11478853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-08-23","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","The head of Taiwan’s office of external affairs Lin Chia-lung and secretary-general of Taiwan’s security council Wu Jaushieh will arrive in Washington this week for talks with senior US government officials. This is Taiwan’s senior officials’ first visit to the US since Lai Ching-te took office as “president” in May. What’s China’s comments?","First of all, there is no such thing as “president” of Taiwan. As for your question, China firmly opposes any form of official exchange between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, deliver on the commitments made by the US leaders on the issues related to Taiwan, handle the Taiwan-related issues with utmost prudence, stop any official exchanges with Taiwan, stop upgrading its substantive relations with the region, and stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202408/t20240823_11478906.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202408/t20240823_11478853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-08-23","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲23日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 23 (Electronic dispatch): Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 23rd, saying: “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. The Lai Ching-te authorities' obstinate adherence to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to…","Zhu Fenglian said that the Lai Qingde authorities have been going all out to hype the so-called “China threat,” wantonly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people on buying weapons and waging militaristic adventures, step by step tying Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coercing Taiwan’s people to become “cannon fodder for Taiwan independence.” Yet they repeatedly claim to hope for peaceful cross-Strait development. This once again exposes the hypocritical face and sinister nature of the Lai Qingde authorities, who, under the guise of peace, are vigorously pursuing “independence through force” and “independence by relying on external forces.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202408/t20240823_12644660.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-08-29","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that when Lai Ching-te heard the report on Taiwan authorities' 2025 budget, he said that Taiwan's 2025 “defense budget” once again hit a new high, reaching NT$647 billion (about US$19.76 billion), and that Taiwan is determined to enhance its own defense capabilities. In addition, Taiwan media recently disclosed photos of the new-generation medium-range ballistic missile “Chien Tien-2” being…","Wu Qian said: Taiwan is a province of China. How can there be a “defense budget”! It must be pointed out that as long as the DPP authorities pursue “Taiwan independence,” there will be no peace, and the more they provoke, the faster they will perish. On the question of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, no one should harbor the illusion that the PLA will not act, and once it does, it will strike with a heavy hammer. Before the powerful Chinese People's Liberation Army, the so-called “capabilities” of the “Taiwan independence” armed forces are nothing more than a mayfly trying to shake a tree, unable to withstand a single blow.","","http://www.news.cn/world/20240829/662e8a6b8c274b2cb8537900d439048b/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-09-02","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua, Beijing, September 2 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on September 2 that as long as both sides adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” the two sides of the Strait are one family, and matters within one family can be easily discussed and resolved. We are willing to uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one…","Chen Binhua said that due to repeated cases of non-compliant citrus fruits shipped from the Taiwan region to the mainland, including the detection of quarantine pests, out of consideration for ensuring biosecurity and the health of mainland consumers, the General Administration of Customs suspended imports of citrus fruits (including wendan pomelos) from the Taiwan region starting August 3, 2022. For some time, Fu Kunqi, Executive Director of the Central Policy Committee of the Kuomintang, and other figures, as well as Hualien County and other parties in Taiwan, have repeatedly expressed to the mainland their strong desire to resume imports of wendan pomelos to the mainland, and have organized operators to carry out rectification and improve product quality to ensure the safety of wendan pomelos exported to the mainland. Recently, Hualien County provided rectification materials from some operators. Based on a comprehensive assessment of the relevant rectification measures and compliance with the relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, the General Administration of Customs decided to resume imports of wendan pomelos from the Taiwan region starting September 2. Wendan pomelos exported to the mainland must come from registered packing plants and orchards.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240902_12646813.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-04","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","On Eswatini. It’s the only African country not participating in FOCAC. What’s the latest view from the Chinese Foreign Ministry on ties with Eswatini? More broadly, can you characterize the ties between the two countries that exist right now both from a political and economic perspective?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is a prevailing consensus in the international community. African countries widely support the one-China principle and view their cooperation with China as helpful for Africa’s economic prosperity and sustainable development.\nDeveloping official relations with the Taiwan region is not in Eswatini’s interest. We believe Eswatini will eventually see the prevailing trend in the world and make the right decision accordingly.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240904_11485051.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240904_11484972.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-09-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters’ questions\n(September 5, 2024)\nQuestion: Recently, Lai Ching-te said in an exclusive interview: “China is not seeking to invade Taiwan because of territorial issues. Its real aim is to change the rules-based world order to achieve hegemony. It will never accept the ‘1992 Consensus’ of the one-China principle, because once it is accepted, it would mean ceding Taiwan’s sovereignty. If the sovereignty of the Republic of China or Taiwan is absent, then everything is empty talk.” What is your comment on this?\nAnswer: Lai Ching-te has constantly engaged in “Taiwan independence” provocations, loudly hyping the so-called “China threat,” refusing to accept the “1992 Consensus,” and trying hard to cater to the anti-China rhetoric of external forces. He has gone all out to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on external forces,” entirely serving his “Taiwan independence” stance and his separatist schemes. His nonsense completely substitutes concepts and confuses right and wrong, fully exposing his sinister intent to seek “Taiwan independence,” split the country, and undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait.\nTaiwan has never been a country, and it will never become one. There is fundamentally no so-called “sovereignty.” Ending the political confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, completing national reunification, and safeguarding the territorial and sovereign integrity of China are the defense of the fruits of World War II and of the postwar international order.\nComplete reunification of the motherland is a historical inevitability and a general trend, and no person or force can block it. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots should see through Lai Ching-te’s stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” position and his implementation of separatist activities, and fully recognize the danger and harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism. Starting from the righteousness of the nation, and from safeguarding their own security and interests, they should resolutely oppose Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities’ “Taiwan independence” provocations and reckless conduct, and work to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240905_12647943.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-06","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华6日答记者","XINHUA, Beijing, September 6 — State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on the 6th, saying that, according to understanding from the relevant departments, the Wenzhou Municipal People's Procuratorate in Zhejiang Province charged defendant Yang Zhiyuan with the crime of splitting the state. After a lawful open trial, the Wenzhou Intermediate People's Court publicly…","Chen Binhua pointed out that since the Wenzhou, Zhejiang, National Security Bureau took criminal coercive measures against Yang Zhiyuan in August 2022 in accordance with the law, national judicial organs have strictly handled the case according to law, fully guaranteed Yang Zhiyuan and his defenders' procedural rights under the law, and made the handling of the case public in accordance with the law.\nA reporter asked: Taiwan media reported that Taiwan resident Yang Zhiyuan was recently “secretly sentenced” to nine years by the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council said the Yang Zhiyuan case proves that the “22 Opinions on Punishing Independence” target all Taiwan people, and “any Taiwanese can be convicted as a 'Taiwan independence' separatist,” and it urged people to carefully consider whether travel to the mainland is necessary. What is your comment on this? Chen Binhua made the above response.\nChen Binhua said that the court's trial found that between 2008 and 2020, Yang Zhiyuan, in order to split the country and seek “Taiwan independence,” publicly promoted the separatist “Taiwan independence” position through “'Taiwan Nation Party'” and “One Side One Country Action Party” and other “Taiwan independence” organizations in Taiwan, and actively carried out acts such as formulating “Taiwan independence” separatist action plans and plotting to promote “Taiwan nation-building” and joining the United Nations, thereby splitting the country and undermining national reunification.\nThe court held that Yang Zhiyuan's conduct violated Article 103, paragraph 1 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China and constituted the crime of splitting the country. Yang Zhiyuan has long participated in separatist activities, actively promoted the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, and played a core role in “Taiwan independence” organizations such as the “Taiwan Nation Party.” The nature of his conduct is egregious. Based on the facts, nature, circumstances and degree of social harm of Yang Zhiyuan's crimes, the above judgment was made in accordance with the law.\nChen Binhua said that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities maliciously smear the just act of national judicial organs punishing “independence” in accordance with the law. They attempt to use this case once again to conflate the vast majority of Taiwan's people with a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” separatists, and to conflate the daily life of the public with illegal and criminal activity. They try to change concepts and confuse right and wrong, intimidate and obstruct Taiwan compatriots from participating in normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and incite cross-Strait confrontation.\nChen Binhua stressed that the documents on punishing “independence” only target the very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” separatists who engage in egregious pro-independence words and deeds and rampant secessionist activities, and the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country they commit. They do not target or involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. From January to August this year, more than 2.6 million Taiwan compatriots came to the mainland to visit and exchange, which is precisely a practical refutation of the lies and rumors of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240906_12648263.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-09","Mao Ning","DPA","According to German media report, two German military vessels will transit through the Taiwan Strait in mid-September. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We made our position clear on similar questions. The waters of the Taiwan Strait, from both shores toward the middle of the Strait, are China’s internal waters, then territorial sea, then contiguous zone, and then exclusive economic zone. China respects countries’ right to navigation in relevant waters in accordance with China’s laws and international law, including UNCLOS. But we firmly oppose any act of provocation under the pretext of freedom of navigation by relevant countries that harms China’s sovereignty and security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240909_11487817.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240909_11487663.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-09","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","I just want to follow up on a question about the German plan to transit the Taiwan Strait. You said that the Taiwan Strait was internal waters and contiguous zone. Is that the whole of the Strait or is that just parts of the Strait? My question is, how much of the Strait is international waters from the Chinese perspective? And how much of it is internal waters and contiguous zones?","The waters of the Taiwan Strait, from both shores toward the middle of the Strait, are China’s internal waters, then territorial sea, then contiguous zone, and then exclusive economic zone. I think I already answered your question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240909_11487817.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240909_11487663.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-09","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Just to follow up. Do you recognize that the center of the Taiwan Strait is international waters in which there is freedom of navigation for all nations? In your statement now on your understanding of the waters, you didn’t actually say that it’s international waters. So is the center of the Strait beyond 12 nautical miles on either side of the Strait international waters in which any nation can travel freely?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are China’s territory. The waters of the Taiwan Strait, from both shores toward the middle of the Strait, are China’s internal waters, then territorial sea, then contiguous zone, and then exclusive economic zone. China respects countries’ right to navigation in relevant waters in accordance with China’s laws and international law, including UNCLOS. But we firmly oppose any act of provocation under the pretext of freedom of navigation by relevant countries that harms China’s sovereignty and security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240909_11487817.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240909_11487663.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 11, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua first introduced the progress made in implementing the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for the Integrated Development of the Two Sides of the Taiwan Strait and Building a…","Dear media friends, good afternoon. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nFirst, let me brief you on the progress of implementing, over the past year, the effort to explore a new path for cross-Strait integrated development in Fujian. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” was issued on September 12 last year, and it will reach its one-year mark tomorrow. Over the past year, relevant central and state departments have acted proactively, strengthened policy empowerment, and issued a series of supporting documents and policy measures for implementing the Opinions in this field. Fujian Province has strengthened primary responsibility, established a coordinated implementation mechanism, formulated implementation opinions for carrying out the Opinions, and has so far released two batches totaling 28 policy measures. Xiamen, Fuzhou, Pingtan, Longyan, and other cities and prefectures have issued regional policy measures implementing the Opinions. Overall, the construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone has produced a batch of pioneering experiences and a batch of original achievements in Taiwan-related integrated development. Fujian is increasingly becoming the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to “land on the mainland.”\nIn social integration, channels for Taiwan compatriots’ travel have become smoother. “Small Three Links” routes have continued to be added, increasing from 26 round trips per week at the resumption of service to a maximum of 182 round trips. In the first half of this year, 434,000 Taiwan compatriot entries were made through Fujian ports, an increase of 1.65 times. Life for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian has become more convenient, and the social application of Taiwan compatriot residence permits has essentially achieved the same convenience as mainland resident ID cards. In the first half of this year, issuance of five-year Taiwan compatriot permits rose 46.6% year on year, and issuance of Taiwan residence permits rose 2.63 times year on year. Employment and entrepreneurship for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian has become more secure. Three batches of directly recognized Taiwan-region vocational skill qualification catalogues have been published, covering 50 occupations in total, and more than 1,500 Taiwan compatriots have obtained corresponding certificates through direct recognition. Social participation of Taiwan compatriots in Fujian has become broader; some Taiwan compatriots have served as, or been hired as, heads or legal representatives of social organizations such as Taiwan-invested enterprise associations, and as arbitrators, mediators, and jurors.\nIn economic integration, Fujian-Taiwan economic and trade have grown steadily. In the first half of this year, Fujian-Taiwan trade totaled RMB 46.46 billion, up 4.9% year on year, and the province newly established 1,121 Taiwan-invested enterprises, up 27.4% year on year. Financial cooperation has innovated and developed: a cross-Strait industrial investment fund initiated by Taiwan businesspeople, the first of its kind on the mainland, has been established. We took the lead in opening a channel for Taiwan compatriots to invest in the mainland with their self-owned overseas RMB, completed the first cross-border direct RMB transfer by a Taiwan compatriot into the mainland to buy commercial housing, and launched the cross-Strait integrated digital RMB bond. Industry standards interoperability continues to advance: a cross-Strait standards interoperability information and service platform has gone online, and 226 cross-Strait interoperable standards have been developed cumulatively.\nIn emotional integration, civil exchanges have become increasingly active. In the first half of this year, Fujian held more than 100 Taiwan-related exchange activities, including the 16th Straits Forum, with cumulative participation of over 15,000 Taiwan compatriot person-times. Youth exchanges have deepened: the 12th Haiqing Festival Summit, the Straits Youth Forum, and other activities were successfully held. Characteristic sports exchanges such as baseball, softball, and dragon and lion dancing have been active, with a cross-Strait youth baseball invitational tournament held in Liancheng and a cross-Strait dragon and lion dance competition held in Zhangping. Platforms for cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship have been strengthened: there are now 49 provincial-level or higher Taiwan youth employment and entrepreneurship bases, and a cumulative total of more than 48,000 Taiwan youth have come to Fujian for internships, employment, and entrepreneurship.\nNext, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the National Development and Reform Commission, together with relevant central and state departments and relevant parties in Fujian Province, will thoroughly implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee and practice the concept of “Cross-Strait Family, One Family.” We will highlight promoting integration through connectivity, benefits, and emotion, continuously improve and introduce innovative measures, steadily advance the construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone, and fully support Fujian in taking greater steps and achieving more accomplishments in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649297.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","It has been over 100 days since Lai Ching-te took office as leader of the Taiwan region. During this period, he has repeatedly made “Taiwan independence” remarks, highlighting his obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” position. He has also colluded with external forces to continuously engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” and outside observers generally believe the prospects for…","Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly held to the “Taiwan independence” position and vigorously promoted separatist fallacies, seriously challenging the one-China principle and seriously undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. In response, we will absolutely not tolerate it and will not appease it.\n“Taiwan independence” is a scourge and a dead end; it cannot succeed and cannot overturn anything. We have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to thwart any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. If “Taiwan independence” forces dare to take risky gambles, we will take all necessary measures to resolutely and thoroughly crush them!\nThe foundation of cross-Strait relations lies among the people, and its driving force comes from the people. Although the current situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields have not stopped, broken off, or diminished this year. In the first half of the year, personnel exchanges across the Strait increased by 99.5% year on year, the number of newly established Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland increased by 9.2% year on year, and cross-Strait trade rose by 7.6% year on year. This once again proves that no force can change the desire of compatriots on both sides to move closer and become like family, and no force can stop the momentum of cross-Strait relations moving forward.\nThe initiative in the development of cross-Strait relations has always rested with the mainland, and it has always been on the right side of history. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, improve systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, continuously expand cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, and unswervingly advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649296.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te posted on social media claiming that next year the so-called “defense” total budget will continue to increase and “asymmetric combat capabilities” will be further strengthened. What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. What so-called \"national defense\" budget could there be? The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" stance. Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has been blatantly challenging the one-China principle, colluding with external forces to keep creating tension across the Taiwan Strait, and continuously pushing \"using force to seek independence.\" According to Taiwan media reports, since the DPP authorities took office, Taiwan's defense budget has risen year after year, and in 2024 it was nearly double that of eight years earlier. The hard-earned money of Taiwan's people could have been used to improve their livelihoods, but the DPP authorities are squandering it extravagantly on the dead-end road of militarism. Not only has this failed to bring Taiwan so-called \"security,\" it has instead accelerated turning Taiwan into a \"powder keg\" and a \"minefield island,\" leaving Taiwan's people deeply worried.\nUnification is the right path; \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end. We have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to crush all \"Taiwan independence\" provocations. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: their attempts to \"use force to seek independence\" or \"use force to resist unification\" are sheer overestimation of themselves, like throwing eggs against a stone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649295.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The 79th session of the UN General Assembly opened yesterday (September 10). The DPP authorities declared that this year's primary task in promoting participation in the United Nations is to assist the international community in “correctly understanding” UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, clamoring that the resolution is “unrelated to Taiwan” and that “China has no right to represent Taiwan in the UN system.”…","United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 is a political document that embodies the one-China principle. Its legal effect is fully confirmed by international practice, and it brooks no distortion, let alone challenge. We have stated our position on many occasions before. Today I will once again restore the facts and set the record straight from three aspects: historical facts, the consultation process of Resolution 2758, and international practice.\nFrom the perspective of historical facts, Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times. The Linhai Shuitu Zhi (临海水土志) from the Three Kingdoms period contains the earliest account of Taiwan. The Sui dynasty government dispatched troops to Taiwan three times. After the Song and Yuan dynasties, successive central governments of China began to establish administration over the Penghu and Taiwan and to exercise administrative jurisdiction. In 1684 the Qing government established Taiwan Prefecture, and in 1885 it changed Taiwan into a province, the 20th province of China at the time. In 1894 Japan launched the First Sino-Japanese War of aggression against China, and the following year forced the defeated Qing government to cede Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. The 1943 Cairo Declaration, the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation, and the 1945 Instrument of Surrender of Japan all affirm that China recovered Taiwan in law and in fact. On October 25, 1945, Chen Yi, Chief Executive of Taiwan Province, declared the restoration of Taiwan in Taipei: “From this day forward, Taiwan and the Penghu Islands have formally re-entered the territory of China. All land, people and governance are placed under Chinese sovereignty.” After the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China was founded in 1949, it replaced the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. This was a change of regime in which China, as the subject of international law, underwent no change; China’s sovereignty and inherent territory were not altered. The Government of the People’s Republic of China naturally enjoys and exercises full sovereignty over China, including sovereignty over Taiwan. After the Chiang Kai-shek clique, defeated in the civil war, retreated to Taiwan, it confronted the central government under the so-called name of the “Republic of China,” and the two sides of the Taiwan Strait thereby fell into a special state of long-term political confrontation. The Taiwan question is merely a legacy of China’s civil war, and China’s sovereignty over Taiwan has never changed.\nFrom the perspective of the full consultation process of Resolution 2758, before the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly in 1971 voted to adopt Resolution 2758, it first overwhelmingly rejected two proposals involving Taiwan: the “Two Chinas representation proposal” and the “One China, One Taiwan and Taiwan self-determination proposal.” This means that the United Nations, on the premise of recognizing that Taiwan is part of China, restored the representation and seats of all China, including Taiwan, to the Government of the People’s Republic of China, while the territorial scope of the international legal person “China” was not affected in any way, and Taiwan’s status as part of China has never changed. Resolution 2758 embodies the UN Charter and its purposes, resolving the question of China’s representation in the UN clearly, fairly and thoroughly in political, legal and procedural terms. It also makes clear that China has only one seat in the UN, and that there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” China’s representation in the UN is, of course, the representation of all China, including Taiwan.\nFrom the perspective of international practice, official UN documents refer to Taiwan as “Taiwan, Province of China.” A legal opinion issued by the Office of Legal Affairs of the UN Secretariat stresses that “the United Nations considers that Taiwan, as a province of China, has no independent status.” For many years, the United Nations and its specialized agencies have followed the one-China principle in handling matters involving Taiwan. On the premise of the one-China principle, China has established diplomatic relations with 183 countries. The basis for the establishment of China-US diplomatic relations is likewise the one-China principle. The US side, in the three China-US joint communiqués, also clearly acknowledged that the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government of China, and acknowledged that there is only one China and that Taiwan is part of China. This fully demonstrates that the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations, and it is also the great righteousness of the international community and the will of the people.\nThe DPP authorities maliciously distort UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, falsely claiming that “the resolution has nothing to do with Taiwan” and using “representation” as a pretext. This is a distortion of facts, a trampling of international law, and a blatant challenge to international order and rules. Its aim is to build momentum for “Taiwan independence” and to undermine the international community’s consensus on upholding the one-China principle. Those who lose the way have little help, and evil cannot prevail over righteousness. No matter how the DPP authorities fabricate stories, and no matter how they collude with external forces to stir up trouble, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. They cannot shake the international community’s pattern of upholding the one-China principle, and they cannot stop the trend that China will inevitably be reunified and will surely be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649294.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Media on the island have reported that after the mainland issued judicial documents punishing “Taiwan independence” and published a reporting mailbox, some Taiwan businesspeople have already been reported and harassed, and therefore many Taiwan businesses have withdrawn from the mainland. Is this the case? What is the current situation?","The relevant reports deviate from the facts and have ulterior motives.\nThe issuance of judicial documents to punish “independence” and the establishment of a mailbox for reporting clues about “Taiwan independence” diehards are necessary measures to punish “Taiwan independence” diehards. They target only a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards who engage in egregious words and deeds promoting “independence” and in rampant “independence”-seeking activities, and they target the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country that these diehards commit. They are not aimed at, and do not involve, the broad Taiwan compatriots. From January to August this year, more than 2.6 million Taiwan compatriot visits were made to the mainland for visits and exchanges, which is the most powerful refutation of the DPP's lies and rumors.\nDeliberately spreading rumors and confusing the public by conflating the vast majority of Taiwan people with a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards is a deceptive trick by “Taiwan independence” forces to muddy the waters, and also a manifestation of their guilty conscience and cowardice. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will open their eyes, more resolutely draw a clear line with “Taiwan independence” diehards, and more eagerly come to the mainland for visits and exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: The Taiwan Affairs Office recently set up a special column on its website for punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and also published a reporting email address for die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements. Since the email address was published, has it received any leads? If relevant reports are received, how will they be handled?\nSecond question: During the Olympics, the Evergreen…","On the first question, the judicial documents on punishing 'independence' target only a very small number of 'Taiwan independence' diehards whose words and deeds involving 'independence' are egregious and whose 'independence'-scheming activities are rampant, as well as the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country that they commit. They do not target or involve the broad compatriots in Taiwan. After setting up a reporting mailbox targeting 'Taiwan independence' diehards, people on both sides of the Strait have responded with practical actions to this justice of punishing 'independence' according to law, reflecting the common voice of compatriots on both sides who oppose 'Taiwan independence' and support cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We will carefully verify and screen the clues we receive, handle them in accordance with law and regulations, and resolutely crack down on the very small number of 'Taiwan independence' diehards and their separatist activities.\nOn the second question, we have noted the relevant reports. We hope the Evergreen Group will uphold national righteousness, stand firm on its position, adhere to the '1992 Consensus,' oppose 'Taiwan independence,' and, through practical actions, maintain and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. I also emphasize once again that our attitude of welcoming and supporting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest and develop on the mainland has been consistent and clear. At the same time, we will never allow those who support 'Taiwan independence' and undermine cross-Strait relations to make money on the mainland or to do things that smash their own rice bowl.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649293.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Regarding the mainland’s announcement that it will resume imports of Taiwan pomelos, the Mainland Affairs Council said this move treats economic and trade relations as a “united front tool.” It said the mainland side’s approach of “first squeezing, then granting favors” does not help the development of cross-Strait agricultural and fishery industries or positive interaction. What is your comment on this?","It is no surprise that the DPP authorities attack and smear the mainland. Whenever the mainland introduces measures beneficial to Taiwan compatriots, they oppose them across the board; whatever is beneficial to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they deliberately go against. In their minds, there is only political manipulation for the private interests of one party, with no regard for the interests and well-being of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Chang Li-shan, magistrate of Yunlin County, recently said she is glad to see the mainland side resume importing Taiwan's pomelos. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We have noted the remarks of Magistrate Zhang Lishan. We have consistently upheld the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and we will do our utmost to do real good, good deeds, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. As long as they adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” and comply with relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we are willing to discuss with relevant parties on the island matters concerning the import of Taiwanese agricultural products into the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","This summer vacation, quite a few Taiwanese internet celebrities traveled to Xinjiang, marveling at its beautiful scenery, people, food and goods, and saying it is a place everyone should visit at least once in their lifetime. The Mainland Affairs Council said, “The mainland using Taiwanese internet celebrities to tell China’s story well has now become a very important part of the CCP’s united front work,” and a…","Beautiful Xinjiang belongs to mainland compatriots and also to Taiwan compatriots. It is only natural that a Taiwanese internet celebrity blogger, personally present, would marvel at and take pride in it. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to enjoy its magnificent mountains and rivers, taste various delicacies, experience local customs, feel the mainland's development and progress, and share what they have seen and heard and their genuine feelings. This is very meaningful for deepening mutual understanding and friendship between the people on both sides of the Strait.\nRegarding the remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council and certain Green-camp politicians, I have “three questions.” First, is Xinjiang not beautiful? Was the Taiwanese internet celebrity wrong to say so? Second, the mainland's beautiful scenery and development and progress are naturally a good story. Must internet celebrities, just because they come from Taiwan, only be allowed to tell bad stories and not good ones? Third, you cannot bear to see anything good and do not allow others to speak well of it. What exactly is your mindset? What are you afraid of?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649290.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视“海峡两岸”记者","The DPP authorities recently said that they have already shown goodwill toward mainland tourists visiting Taiwan, that “Taiwan has extended an olive branch for a long time,” and called on the mainland to open group tours and independent travel as soon as possible. What comments do you have on this? What are the next steps to promote the normalization of cross-Strait tourism?","At the beginning of 2020, the DPP authorities, using the epidemic as a pretext, adopted a series of unilateral restrictive measures, including banning mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, closing the “mini three links,” canceling a large number of direct cross-Strait flight routes, and prohibiting travel agencies on the island from conducting tourism business to the mainland, thereby blocking the path for cross-Strait tourism development. As the epidemic came under control, in May 2023 the mainland announced the resumption of receiving group tours from Taiwan residents. In April this year, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that it would take the lead in resuming travel by Fujian residents to Matsu, and after the resumption of cross-Strait maritime passenger direct links, would resume group tours by Fujian residents to the island; from August 9 to 11, the first group tour by Fujian residents to Matsu took place. At present, the mainland has resumed issuing travel visas for Fujian residents traveling to Matsu. On August 30, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that it would resume travel by Fujian residents to Kinmen, and related “trial groups” will depart soon. These measures are positive responses to the expectations of people and the tourism industry in Taiwan for the resumption of cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and have been welcomed by the public and the industry on the island.\nFor some time, the DPP authorities have been inconsistent and untrustworthy in lifting the “group tour ban order” on island residents traveling to the mainland. In June, they even raised the travel alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland to “orange,” and recently media reported that they would reject applications by Taiwan’s travel industry to charter ships to the mainland on the pretext of so-called “national security concerns.” The facts show that the DPP authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, disregard the legitimate rights and interests of the public on the island and the tourism industry, and continue to engage in political manipulation. This is the real obstacle to restoring normal cross-Strait tourism. The DPP authorities should face squarely the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan’s people and the interests of Taiwan’s tourism industry, and lift the unreasonable restrictions on Taiwan residents’ group tours to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649292.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The recently popular mainland-made game \"Black Myth: Wukong\" has been highly acclaimed and has also drawn attention and heated discussion from the island's industry and public. Some public opinion on the island hopes that cross-Strait cultural industry cooperation can be strengthened to jointly explore the treasures of Chinese culture. What is your comment on this?","The mainland enterprise-produced AAA game “Black Myth: Wukong” has recently begun global release, drawing wide attention and discussion from players around the world, and it has also been sought after and well received by young people and gamers on the island. The reasons for this are, on the one hand, that the game itself is well crafted, offers a good experience, and is highly entertaining; on the other hand, its story and characters are drawn from “Journey to the West” and incorporate a large number of Chinese cultural elements such as ancient architecture, Eastern aesthetics, and traditional-style music, which players on the island find very familiar and approachable. After all, we are all Chinese who grew up reading the Four Great Classical Novels, and many people dreamed as children of owning a magical golden-hooped staff.\nTaiwanese companies once mined the treasure trove of Chinese culture to produce classic games such as “Chinese Paladin,” “Xuan-Yuan Sword,” and “Romance of the Three Kingdoms,” which were highly sought after by young people on both sides of the Strait, especially game players. This also proves from one side that the profound and vast Chinese culture is a precious common wealth of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and an inexhaustible treasure for the creative and innovative development of the cross-Strait gaming industry. According to relevant industry reports, in the first half of this year, the overseas market sales revenue of independently developed mainland games reached 8.554 billion US dollars, and domestic market actual revenue reached 147.267 billion yuan, showing a good momentum of development. So-called AAA games refer to single-player games produced with “A lot of money,” “A lot of resources,” and “A lot of time.” “Black Myth: Wukong” has broken the long-standing monopoly of Europe and the United States over AAA games and is regarded as a symbol of the rise of the mainland's gaming industry. We welcome Taiwanese young people to develop in the mainland's gaming industry, support stronger exchanges and cooperation between the cross-Strait gaming industries, and jointly grow the cultural and creative industry of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649289.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields have been very active this summer. Please spokesperson introduce the highlights and features. What are the next steps to further promote exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait?","According to statistics, from January to August this year, cross-strait personnel exchanges totaled nearly 3 million person-trips, up 70% year on year. After entering the summer vacation season, despite the various interference and obstruction from the DPP authorities, the enthusiasm of compatriots on both sides for exchanges and interactions has continued to rise. Exchange activities in all fields have been rich in content, diverse in form, and outstanding in highlights.\nFirst, youth exchanges have been unprecedentedly active, with Taiwan youth enthusiastically participating and gaining much. A series of cross-strait youth brand exchange activities were successfully held, including the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the 21st Thousand-Person Summer Camp for Taiwan Compatriot Youth, the 7th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, the 12th Strait Youth Festival, the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Vitality Carnival, and the Taiwan Youth Inner Mongolia Frontier Tour. Cross-strait youth joined hands to compose a youthful movement of mutual learning and walking together with one heart. The first Cross-Strait Youth Short Video and Micro-Drama Exchange and Research Visit, the 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Archaeology Study Camp, the “Metaverse Exploration Team”—Taiwan Youth Summer Residence Activity, and other cross-strait youth cultural exchange activities have shone one after another. The 2024 Cross-Strait Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament and the 5th Cross-Strait Youth Baseball Culture Festival, held in Liancheng, Fujian in early August, saw cross-strait primary school students use the ball as a medium to exchange skills and deepen friendship in a happy atmosphere.\nSecond, cultural exchange activities have continued to shine, fully demonstrating the charm of traditional Chinese culture and the contemporary spirit of China. The “15th Cross-Strait Film Exhibition — Mainland Film Exhibition” was held in Taipei and Taoyuan in early July, with eight excellent mainland films screened in Taiwan. Activities such as cross-strait filmmakers' forums and meet-the-creators events between film crews and audiences were welcomed and loved by Taiwan residents. The 9th Chinese Cultural Heritage Study Camp, the 14th Strait Quyi Joyful Gathering, the 2024 Beautiful China Creative Tour and other activities were held in various parts of the mainland, promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly carry forward China's outstanding traditional culture.\nThird, compatriots on both sides jointly commemorated national history and shared the bonds of blood ties, which became a new highlight of summer exchange activities. In July and August, the Nanjing touring exhibition “Our Family's Cross-Strait Story” was successfully held, vividly displaying the history of migration to Taiwan and highlighting the shared memories of cross-strait blood ties. Relevant parties on both sides separately organized multiple activities marking the 400th anniversary of Zheng Chenggong's birth and the 362nd anniversary of the recovery of Taiwan, jointly commemorating the deeds and spirit of the national hero. More than 100 ethnic minority representatives from both sides gathered in Inner Mongolia to experience the long history of the Great Wall and enjoy the scenery of grassland ecology. From August 15 to 16, the 6th Symposium on the History of the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the Inheritance of the Anti-Japanese War Spirit was held in Yunnan. Nearly 200 participants from both sides, including retired generals, experts and scholars, teachers and student representatives, took part, jointly remembering the history of the War of Resistance and carrying forward its spirit. On August 22, the 1st Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Music Festival was held in Hunan, with cross-strait young singers singing and dancing and sounding a movement of peace and friendship.\nIn the second half of the year, localities and departments will also hold a series of cross-strait exchange activities in sports, youth, culture, folk beliefs and other fields. We will uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” unite compatriots on both sides, break through the various obstacles set up by the DPP authorities, actively promote exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, continuously expand cross-strait personnel exchanges, deepen cross-strait integrated development, and promote spiritual connection among compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240911_12649291.htm"],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","It is reported that Cho Jung-tai, head of Taiwan’s executive authority, recently said he is considering hosting international sports events under the name “Taiwan” in the future, to raise “Taiwan’s visibility.” What is your comment?","The “Olympic model” is a principle universally recognized in the international sports community for handling the Taiwan question, and a principle that sports circles on both sides of the Strait jointly follow. It accords with the fundamental interests of both sides, especially the sports circles of Taiwan, and for many years it has provided basic institutional guarantees for promoting sports exchanges and cooperation across the Strait and for supporting athletes from both sides in participating in international sporting events.\nSeveral years ago, “Taiwan independence” forces on the island, with the indulgence of the DPP authorities, manipulated the so-called “Tokyo Olympics Taiwan Name Referendum,” which was rejected by public opinion on the island. History is not far off. The sports circles of Taiwan call on the DPP authorities to cherish the hard-won achievements of cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation, stop political manipulation, and not keep making mistakes at the expense of the rights and interests of the sports community. The DPP authorities, pursuing the aim of “independence,” attempt to “stain” sports with politics and “make trouble” at sporting events. They have no way out and will only reap the bitter fruit of their own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","According to Taiwan media reports, recently Taiwan's relevant authorities threatened to investigate and punish retired Major General Tsang Yu-hsia over his plan to travel to Hong Kong to attend the “Global Overseas Chinese Promoting China's Peaceful Reunification Conference.” What comments do you have on this?","This is an individual case, but it is certainly not an isolated one. In recent years, the DPP authorities have obstinately clung to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and repeatedly fabricated charges against, suppressed, and persecuted people on the island who support cross-Strait exchanges and national reunification. The fundamental purpose is to deter cross-Strait exchanges, interaction, and integrated development, to obstruct compatriots on both sides from drawing closer and jointly working toward unification, and to create conditions for carrying out their “Taiwan independence” schemes. Under the “green terror,” anyone could be the next victim. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will uphold justice and jointly oppose the DPP authorities’ abuse of power and reckless conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, Ko Wen-je, Chairman of the Taiwan People's Party, has been “hunted” by the DPP and is entangled in lawsuits, which has drawn great attention. Some public opinion holds that this will have a major impact on the island's political ecosystem, that Taiwan has “formally entered the Lai Ching-te era,” and that cross-Strait relations face greater variables, with prospects that are even less optimistic. What is…","Since taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities have repeatedly manipulated judicial, administrative and other means, misusing public institutions for private purposes and excluding those who differ, and have blatantly created a \"green terror\" on the island. Their aim is to hunt down people from all walks of life who do not support the DPP and do not identify with \"Taiwan independence,\" in pursuit of the private interests of one person and one party, and to clear obstacles for carrying out \"Taiwan independence.\" Those who commit many unrighteous acts will eventually destroy themselves. The Lai Ching-te authorities are acting recklessly and will inevitably be repudiated by public opinion.\nI want to emphasize again that \"Taiwan independence\" is a reverse current of history and a dead end; reunification is the great trend of history and the right path. No matter how the situation on the island changes and no matter who holds power, it cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, cannot change the basic framework and development direction of cross-Strait relations, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","台湾“中国时报”记者","On cross-Strait tourism, Taiwan still has various restrictions that have not been lifted, while the mainland currently allows Fujian residents to travel to Kinmen and Matsu. Building on this hard-won achievement, when can we welcome mainland group tourists to visit Taiwan?","I have already stated very clearly just now that cross-Strait tourism cannot be fully restored, and the responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities should promptly lift the unreasonable restrictions on group tours by Taiwan residents to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","台湾“联合报”记者","The first question: Ko Wen-je, chairman of the Taiwan People’s Party and former Taipei mayor, who identifies with the concept of “one family across the Strait,” was recently detained over the Core Pacific City case. Does the Taiwan Affairs Office have any further comment on this case?\nThe second question: Yang Chih-yuan was recently sentenced on the mainland to nine years in prison for the crime of splitting the…","Question one: We note that public opinion on the island believes that Lai Ching-te, in order to seek political gain, has continuously created a “green terror” and used judicial means to suppress dissenters, which has caused strong concern in Taiwan society. We will continue to follow relevant developments.\nQuestion two: In accordance with the relevant provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People’s Republic of China, the judgment in this case has been served on Yang Zhiyuan and his defense counsel in accordance with the law. Regarding family visits, the relevant authorities will handle them in accordance with the law.\nQuestion three: It is understood that Li Yanhe is currently in good physical condition, and the relevant mainland authorities will hear this case in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The Yang Zhiyuan case has not yet been concluded in the first-instance trial. According to the relevant provisions of the 22 Articles on Punishing “Taiwan Independence,” will the mainland side allow Yang Zhiyuan to hire a lawyer to appeal and defend himself?\nSecond question: The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. Is there any new progress in the case of the captain surnamed Hong of the “Da Jin…","I will first answer the questions concerning the “Dajinman 88.” The relevant authorities are handling the matter and will deal with it in accordance with law and regulations.\nRegarding the third question you raised, the issue of the Kinmen “scouting tour groups.” At present, the various tasks for Fujian residents traveling to Kinmen for tourism are advancing steadily. A scouting tour group traveling to Kinmen, formed by some tourism operators in Xiamen, has recently submitted an inspection application to the relevant Taiwan authorities. If the Taiwan side approves it, I believe what you mentioned, that the trip could take place before the National Day Golden Week, is entirely achievable, but the key is for the Taiwan side to approve the scouting tour groups to Kinmen as soon as possible. Next, we will also continue to advance, in accordance with the established work arrangements, group tourism by Fujian residents to the island via direct maritime passenger services.\nReturning to the first question you raised, the Yang Chih-yuan case. We have already given very detailed information on this case before. Based on the facts, nature, circumstances, and degree of harm to society of Yang Chih-yuan's crime, the relevant judicial authorities sentenced him under the crime of “splitting the state” to nine years of fixed-term imprisonment and three years of deprivation of political rights, in accordance with law. Yang Chih-yuan and his defenders have been fully guaranteed all their procedural rights, and the relevant departments and judicial authorities have publicly disclosed the handling and trial of the case in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Relevant Taiwan authorities said that the mainland side’s resumption of imports of Taiwan pomelos this time is limited to designated packing plants and supply orchards in Hualien, and that they cannot predict whether the resumption of exports of other agricultural and fishery products to the mainland will follow the same model. Please explain the relevant situation.","This year, Hualien County has expressed a strong desire to resume the import of Taiwan's Wentou pomelos into the mainland, and has organized operators to carry out rectification to improve product quality and ensure the safety of pomelos exported to the mainland. On the basis of comprehensively assessing the relevant rectification measures and conforming to relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, the relevant mainland authorities have, in accordance with regulations, registered packing plants and orchards that meet the conditions. I would like to stress again that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and “Taiwan independence” is opposed, the two sides of the Strait are one family, and we can fully discuss and resolve the issue of importing Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, on the premise of conforming to relevant inspection and quarantine regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视直新闻记者","According to Taiwan media reports, Chang Tsun-feng, chairman of the Pingtung branch of the Unification Alliance Party, and Huang Jung-te, its secretary-general, were accused of “colluding with China to interfere in elections” for organizing grassroots residents of Pingtung to visit and exchange on the mainland. Recently, the Pingtung District Court in Taiwan issued a first-instance verdict sentencing them to four…","In order to pursue “Taiwan independence” separatism, the DPP authorities abuse public power and resort to any means. They have repeatedly manipulated the judiciary to suppress island personages who participate in cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. In particular, on “groundless” charges, they have targeted pro-unification organizations and figures on the island for persecution, continuously reinforcing a “green terror.” We strongly condemn this.\nSupporting and pursuing national reunification is a great righteous cause of the nation, and it should be affirmed and supported by the entire nation. Broad Taiwan compatriots should fully recognize the sinister intentions of the DPP authorities, firmly oppose their abuse of power and reckless conduct, and resolutely support cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央广记者","This summer, the popularity of mainland cultural and tourism markets has continued to climb. By contrast, under the influence of the DPP authorities' “group tour ban” on mainland tourists, Taiwan's tourism industry has experienced an unprecedented “cold winter.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Since 2020, the DPP authorities have used the pandemic as an excuse to ban mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, and suspended Taiwan travel agencies’ group tour business to the mainland. As early as May 2023, the mainland had already announced the resumption of group tours for Taiwan residents to the mainland, and in April this year it made arrangements for Fujian residents to take group tours to Taiwan. But the DPP authorities not only impose arbitrary restrictions on lifting the “group tour ban,” change their minds repeatedly, and show no sincerity, but recently they have also refused the charter ship applications from Taiwan’s tourism industry on the pretext of “security concerns.” Such political parties and politicians who ignore public opinion and engage in political manipulation will inevitably bring a “winter” to Taiwan’s tourism industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","First question: Recently, news that the domestic restaurant brand Hengtaifeng is about to close 14 stores, including those in Beijing and Tianjin, has drawn attention on both sides of the Strait. The industry generally believes this is related to business conditions, but some media on the island have used it to hype up a supposed economic downturn on the mainland. What is the spokesperson’s comment?\nSecond…","On the first question: It is understood that this is a business operation decision made by the enterprise based on market demand, shareholder wishes and other factors. I have noted that media outlets such as China News Service and China Media Group have published many fairly comprehensive analytical reports on this. The company also said that it remains optimistic about the mainland market and will continue to follow developments and trends in the mainland catering industry, and it hopes to join hands with its partners again in the near future to create new glory. The mainland remains the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest and do business, and we will continue to create better conditions and provide better services for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop on the mainland.\nOn the second question: It is only human nature for Taiwanese entertainers to introduce their ancestral hometowns and express identification with being sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. What is wrong with that? Just as I have worked and lived in Beijing for decades, when someone asks where I am from, I naturally answer \"Fujianese.\" Cyber-violence by pan-green internet troops against some entertainers once again proves that \"Taiwan independence\" is \"Taiwan poison\" and that \"anti-China\" means anti-intelligence. The long-term \"de-Sinicization\" on the island has been extremely poisonous and has caused endless harm.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Foxconn recently announced it will increase its investment on the mainland, investing 1 billion yuan in RMB to build a new business headquarters building in Zhengzhou, Henan. Public opinion holds that this is Taiwan businesses and enterprises responding with action to the so-called “de-Sinicization” of supply chains, and also a vote of confidence in the mainland's business environment. What comment do you have?","Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises that have long put down roots on the mainland have the most direct and genuine experience of the mainland's rich production factors, complete industrial support, and favorable business environment. We will fully implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee, improve systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and create more opportunities and broader space for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to participate in Chinese-style modernization and help them achieve greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","Regarding the mainland coast guard's normalized law enforcement in Kinmen waters and its provision of a hotline for Taiwanese fishermen seeking help, Kuan Bi-ling, chairperson of Taiwan's Ocean Affairs Council, said, “If the China Coast Guard enters Taiwan's ‘prohibited or restricted waters’ or crosses the ‘median line,’ it is harassment. The Coast Guard Administration will firmly guard our territorial waters.”…","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The waters off Xiamen and Kinmen have since ancient times been traditional fishing grounds for fishermen on both sides of the Strait, and there is simply no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters.” The mainland coast guard's routine law enforcement patrols in the waters off Xiamen and Kinmen help maintain order in the relevant fishing waters and safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","Raymond Greene, the newly appointed director of the Taipei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT), held a press conference recently for the first time, saying: “Taiwan is not the only target of China's efforts to change the status quo through intimidation and coercion; the possibility of jointly producing military equipment with Taiwan is not ruled out; the U.S. side looks forward to receiving relevant…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo of the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” They are the disruptors of the status quo in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues appropriately, be prudent in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, stop any form of military contact with the Taiwan region of China, not allow the leader of the Taiwan region to “transit” through the United States, and not send any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-11","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","After Lin Yi-chen stated on a mainland variety show that she is a “Chengdu person,” it sparked heated discussion on the island. Although some pro-green cyber troops hurled abuse and attacks at her, most Taiwan netizens expressed support for her. What comment does the spokesperson have?","I already answered this question just now. Why would such a matter, which accords with common sense, cause controversy on the island? The root cause is that the DPP authorities have long pursued “de-Sinicization,” and “Taiwan independence” forces have long engaged in “cultural Taiwan independence.”\nThank you all. Today's press conference concludes here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240911_12649283.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-13","Mao Ning","Reuters","A German Defense Ministry official today said ships from the country transiting through the Taiwan Strait were not directed to anyone, and they are, in fact, supporting the international principle of freedom of navigation. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and prevailing international consensus. The Taiwan question is not about freedom of navigation but about China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We respect countries’ right to navigation in relevant waters in accordance with China’s laws and international law, including UNCLOS. But we firmly oppose any act of provocation under the pretext of freedom of navigation that harms China’s sovereignty and security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240913_11490441.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240913_11490398.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-09-14","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's defense authorities recently said that the PLA, constrained by the natural geography of the Taiwan Strait, insufficient landing craft and logistical capabilities, and other factors, does not yet fully possess the formal combat capability to launch a comprehensive attack on Taiwan. What is the spokesperson's comment?","The statement by the DPP authorities is absurd and laughable, and is purely self-deception. Complete reunification of the motherland is a historical inevitability and the trend of the times, and no person or force can stop it. The PLA has reliable means to turn a natural chasm into a thoroughfare, and has the strong capability to defeat any desperate resistance by “Taiwan independence” armed forces. We firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16338632.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-14","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the German Defense Minister said two German Navy vessels sailed through the Taiwan Strait. A German official said this transit was to safeguard freedom of navigation. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","On September 13, two German warships transited the Taiwan Strait and publicized it openly. The Eastern Theater Command of the People's Liberation Army organized sea and air forces to follow and guard the German warships throughout. Freedom of navigation does not mean freedom to run amok, and it cannot be used to provoke and harm China's sovereignty and security. The Chinese military remains on high alert, will take strong measures to thwart all provocative schemes, resolutely defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly safeguards peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16338632.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-09-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters’ questions\n(September 14, 2024)\nQuestion: On September 12, at a seminar marking the 60th anniversary of the “Taiwan People’s Self-Salvation Movement Manifesto,” Lai Ching-te declared that the threat of “communism annexing Taiwan” still exists and is even stronger than before, and that for Taiwan’s “democracy and freedom” and for future generations, the “Taiwan People’s Self-Salvation Movement” must continue to be advanced. What is your comment?\nAnswer: The so-called “Taiwan People’s Self-Salvation Movement Manifesto,” which at the time was raised under the banner of opposing the authorities’ dictatorship and autocracy, put forward separatist fallacies such as “establishing a nation through a new constitution” and “joining the United Nations under the name of Taiwan.” It is an unmistakable “Taiwan independence manifesto.” Lai Ching-te holds it in the highest esteem, attempting to use it to “wash people’s minds,” which once again confirms his true identity as a “Taiwan independence golden grandson” and fully exposes his sinister intention to pursue “Taiwan independence” separatism and escalate cross-Strait hostility and confrontation. Under the pretext of “democracy and freedom,” forcibly indoctrinating the broad Taiwan public with the “Taiwan independence” views of a small number of people is a trick that Lai Ching-te and the DPP constantly and habitually engage in. If this is allowed to continue, it will only push Taiwan toward the danger of war, bring profound disasters to Taiwan compatriots, and force the public and even future generations to bear the bitter consequences of the “Taiwan independence” provocation.\nSince taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities, in pursuit of “Taiwan independence” separatism, have abused public power, used any means necessary, arbitrarily carried out political persecution and judicial persecution, and brazenly suppressed anti-“independence” forces and patriotic reunification forces on the island, creating a “green terror” on the island. Island public opinion has described their conduct as “democratic regression,” “the death of the judiciary,” and “freedom in peril.”\nThe future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to reunification, and they are certainly not an excuse for separation. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will truly understand the true meaning of democracy and freedom, recognize that the “green terror” is a trampling of democracy and freedom, recognize that “Taiwan independence” separatism is a threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait and to their own safety, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, firmly safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, and work with compatriots on the mainland to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation, and truly realize the aspiration to be masters of their own house.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240914_12650248.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-18","Lin Jian","China News Service","It’s reported that in a statement issued on September 17, US Defense Security Cooperation Agency said that the US State Department approved a military sale to Taiwan of return, repair, and reshipment of spare parts for aircraft and related equipment for an estimated cost totaling US$ 228 million. What’s China’s comments?","The US’s arms sale to China’s Taiwan region seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The sale severely undermines China’s sovereignty and security interests, harms China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and sends a wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly condemns and firmly opposes this, and has lodged strong protests to the US side. As a firm countermeasure, China has announced sanctions against nine US military companies.\nThe US’s frequent arms sales to Taiwan embolden Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities as they cling to the stance of “Taiwan independence” and make deliberate provocations on the one-China principle. This once again shows that the separatist moves for “Taiwan independence” and connivance and support for such moves from US-led external forces are the biggest threat facing cross-Strait peace and stability and cause the greatest disruption to the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. Let me be clear, the DPP authorities’ attempt to seek independence through military buildup and what the US has done to assist that agenda will only backfire and lead nowhere.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. No one should underestimate China’s firm determination and ability to oppose “Taiwan independence” and safeguard its sovereignty and territorial integrity. China urges the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop the dangerous trend of arming Taiwan, stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence,” and stop endangering cross-Strait peace and stability. We will take strong and resolute measures to firmly defend our national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240918_11492497.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240918_11492426.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-09-18","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","XINHUA News Agency, Beijing, September 18. Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 18th that adhering to the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” the Mainland side, starting from August 1, 2005 and March 20, 2007, in two batches, exempted 34 agricultural products originating from Taiwan, including fresh fruits, vegetables and…","Chen Binhua stated: We have always respected, cared for, and benefited Taiwan compatriots, and we are committed to promoting economic, cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and deepening integrated development in all fields between the two sides. We will, as always, welcome and support Taiwanese farmers and Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to develop. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” brings no peace and no development, and can only “endanger Taiwan” and “harm Taiwan.” Supporting “Taiwan independence” means aiding and abetting tyranny and bringing misfortune upon oneself, and can only damage one's own vital interests. We hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, including farmers and fishermen, will recognize the extreme danger and harmfulness of the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” line, actively safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and join compatriots on the mainland in creating lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240918_12651062.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-19","Lin Jian","Anadolu Agency","To follow up on the Hezbollah incident, it is understood that pager devices used in the attack were originally produced by a Taiwanese company. The devices have this company’s brand on them. Do you have any information if this company has cooperation with Israel or Mossad?","I have no information on that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202409/t20240919_11493204.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202409/t20240919_11493206.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-09-19","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Remarks by Chen Binhua, Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, in Response to a Reporter's Question\n(September 19, 2024)\nQuestion: The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency recently announced the sale of military items worth approximately US$228 million to the Taiwan region of China. The DPP authorities said this helps Taiwan enhance its self-defense capabilities and “asymmetric combat capabilities.” What is your comment?\nAnswer: The foundation for the establishment of China-U.S. diplomatic relations is the one-China principle, namely that the United States recognizes the Government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and acknowledges that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. The premise is that the U.S. government accepts the three principles put forward by China for establishing diplomatic ties: “severing diplomatic relations with Taiwan, withdrawing troops, and abrogating the treaty.” The U.S. has repeatedly sold weapons to the Taiwan region of China, which seriously violates the principles of China-U.S. diplomatic relations, seriously violates the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” and seriously infringes on China's sovereignty and security interests. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has lodged a strong condemnation, expressed firm opposition, and announced sanctions against nine U.S. defense companies. We firmly support this and urge the U.S. side to immediately stop arming Taiwan, immediately stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete actions.\n“Taiwan independence” is utterly incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait. It is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and a major source of turmoil for peace and stability in the Asia-Pacific region. Since the DPP authorities took office, they have obstinately clung to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, attempted to “seek independence by force” and “resist reunification by force,” continuously escalated cross-Strait confrontation, repeatedly courted and sought help from external forces, and relentlessly engaged in military buildup and preparations for “independence.” Compatriots in Taiwan must recognize that the DPP authorities, under the guise of “defending Taiwan,” are in essence “harming Taiwan,” and must recognize the danger that “Taiwan independence” will inevitably lead to war, and firmly oppose and stop their actions.\nWe have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat “Taiwan independence” provocations and interference by external forces. No one and no force should imagine that we will swallow the bitter fruit of damage to national sovereignty, security, and development interests. We warn the DPP authorities: do not misjudge the situation, and do not dare to take risks, for you will surely bring about your own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240919_12651290.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-09-20","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that on September 16, local time, the U.S. State Department approved a case for spare parts and technical support for Taiwan’s fighter aircraft, valued at about US$228 million. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Zhang Xiaogang: The United States' sale of weapons to Taiwan, China seriously violates the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the “8·17” Communiqué. It seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests and seriously undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We express strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition, and have lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\n“Taiwan independence” is the greatest cancer to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The United States' “aiding independence by force” sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, is pushing Taiwan step by step into a perilous situation of war and danger, seriously endangers the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and seriously escalates tensions across the Taiwan Strait. It must be stressed that Taiwan's security depends on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. American-made weapons are not the DPP authorities' “talisman” but their “death rope” leading to self-destruction.\nThe Taiwan question is the first red line in China-U.S. relations that must not be crossed. We urge the United States to earnestly honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” stop military collusion between the United States and Taiwan, and stop arming Taiwan in any way, and to maintain stable, healthy, and sustainable development of relations between the two countries and the two militaries through concrete actions. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to strengthen military training and combat readiness, take resolute and forceful measures, and resolutely thwart any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and external interference.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16339643.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 25, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held a press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","In recent years, the mainland has highlighted whole-process people’s democracy and demonstrated confidence in its system. The DPP authorities, however, have repeatedly smeared the mainland’s political system and hyped the so-called narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism.” What is your comment on this?","Recently, the grand rally celebrating the 70th anniversary of the founding of the National People's Congress and the 75th anniversary of the founding of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference was solemnly held in Beijing. General Secretary Xi Jinping clearly pointed out that democracy is a common value of all humanity and an important concept that the Communist Party of China and the Chinese people have always upheld.\nDeveloping whole-process people's democracy is one of the essential requirements of Chinese-style modernization. Whole-process people's democracy is democracy along the entire chain, in all aspects, and with full coverage. It has not only complete institutional procedures but also complete practices of participation. We implement the system of people's congresses as our form of state, and we implement basic political systems such as the multi-party cooperation and political consultation system led by the Communist Party of China, the system of regional ethnic autonomy, and the system of grassroots self-governance by the masses. In the practice of whole-process people's democracy, all the people practice democratic election, democratic consultation, democratic decision-making, democratic management, and democratic supervision in accordance with the law, and manage state affairs through various channels and forms in accordance with the law. This is the most extensive, most genuine, and most effective socialist democracy.\nIt should be pointed out that democracy is not an ornament, and it is not something to be displayed for show, but is used to solve the problems that the people need to solve. Democracy that reflects public opinion is true democracy; democracy that brings welfare to ordinary people is true democracy. Different systems are not an obstacle to unity, much less a pretext for division. The DPP authorities, in pursuit of the narrow partisan interests of one party, use the banner of “democracy against authoritarianism” to maliciously smear and attack the mainland, manipulate “resisting China and protecting Taiwan,” heighten hostility and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and harm the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people. This is a betrayal of the essence of democracy. Seeking “minority replacing majority” or “minority oppressing majority” is an insult to the value of democracy. Suppressing public opinion and creating a “green terror” is trampling on the spirit of democracy. The so-called democracy of the DPP authorities is entirely fake democracy that serves “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652490.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","At present, tourism by Mainland residents to Matsu has been fully resumed. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation of Mainland residents traveling to Matsu. Recently, some tourism operators in Xiamen, Fujian formed a “trail-treading group” to Kinmen. On September 22, the “inaugural tour group” traveling to Kinmen was warmly welcomed by Kinmen residents. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Regarding Mainland residents traveling to Matsu, it is understood that many Mainland residents have already applied for tourist visa endorsements for Matsu. As the National Day holiday approaches, I believe there will be a wave of peak tourism to Matsu.\nRegarding Mainland residents traveling to Kinmen, it is understood that a “trial group” formed by the Xiamen Tourism Association and four travel agencies authorized to organize group tours to Taiwan departed from Xiamen’s Wutong Pier on September 18 to inspect Kinmen, and returned to Xiamen by boat from Kinmen’s Shuitou Pier on September 20. This three-day tourism inspection laid a good foundation for Mainland residents’ travel to Kinmen. On September 22, the “inaugural tour group” of Mainland residents traveling to Kinmen arrived in Kinmen via the “Xiao San Tong,” and was warmly welcomed by the Kinmen County Government and local residents, adding a new chapter to cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation. Today (the 25th), 27 Mainland residents are traveling to Kinmen on individual tours. We believe that more and more Mainland tourists will travel to Kinmen. We hope they will have a good tourism experience in Kinmen, and we also hope that the Taiwan authorities will truly proceed from the well-being of people on both sides and ensure the smooth progress of cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652476.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities have been vibrant recently. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","In September, relevant departments and localities held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities that were rich in content, diverse in form, and highly effective. In early September, the 28th Lu-Tai Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference, the 2024 Guizhou-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Symposium, the 15th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo, the 2024 Fujian Cross-Strait Young Entrepreneurs Economic and Trade Exchange Activity, the 16th Chongqing-Taiwan Week, the 15th Tianjin-Taiwan Investment Cooperation Negotiation Conference, and the 27th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum were successively held. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises actively took part, fully demonstrating their optimism about the prospects of Chinese-style modernization and their enthusiasm for participating in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nIn addition, the 2024 Liaoning-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Week is being held in Shenyang, Dandong, Benxi, and other places in Liaoning. The event runs from September 23 to 28, with the theme “Revitalization Writes a New Chapter, Integration Creates the Future.” Focusing on modern agriculture, equipment manufacturing, fine chemicals, medical health and wellness, culture and tourism, and other industries, it promotes Liaoning-Taiwan cooperation. Arrangements include Taiwan investment policy briefings, Liaoning-Taiwan modern agriculture cooperation promotion meetings, and on-site visits, helping Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises take part in the strategy to revitalize Northeast China and jointly explore new development space.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Last September, the State Council approved the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan.” Please introduce the achievements Dongguan has made in deepening cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation over the past year.","Under the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan” approved by the State Council, and with the support of the central government and relevant national departments, Guangdong Province and Dongguan City have taken on their main responsibility and acted proactively. They have formulated and issued implementation plans and specific supporting measures. Building on the foundation of Dongguan-Taiwan exchange and cooperation and the resource endowments of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, and combining the city’s characteristics of “science and technology innovation plus advanced manufacturing,” they have continuously optimized the development environment for Taiwan-invested enterprises and actively improved policy measures to enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. They have carried out high-standard planning and construction of the “Dongguan-Taiwan High-Tech Industrial Park,” held a series of distinctive and effective cross-Strait exchange activities such as the Dongguan Taiwan Famous Brands Expo, and accelerated the construction of a number of major projects. This July, the 2024 annual inter-provincial and departmental joint conference on Dongguan’s deepening of cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation was successfully held, pushing Dongguan’s cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation to go deeper and produce real results.\nThe Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China clearly stated that we must “build institutional mechanisms that support comprehensive innovation.” The State Council Taiwan Affairs Office will work with the National Development and Reform Commission and other departments to support Guangdong Province and Dongguan City in accelerating the construction of the policy system and implementation mechanisms of the “Overall Plan for Deepening Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Cooperation in Dongguan.” We will build a common industry, common market, and common home across the Taiwan Strait, implement a series of policy measures in deepening Dongguan-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation, facilitating travel and life for Taiwan compatriots, and encouraging Taiwan compatriots to work and start businesses in Dongguan. We will create a vivid practice of deepening cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation in Dongguan and explore effective paths for deepening cross-Strait innovation and development cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652482.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Regarding the mainland's announcement of canceling zero-tariff treatment for 34 Taiwan agricultural products, the Mainland Affairs Council said this is “economic coercion” against Taiwan for political reasons, and does not help maintain cross-Strait relations. What is your comment on this?","The so-called “economic coercion” claim is a complete distortion of the truth.\nSince 2005, in order to expand sales of Taiwan agricultural products on the mainland, the mainland side has successively announced zero-tariff measures for 15 kinds of fruit, 11 kinds of vegetables, and 8 kinds of aquatic products produced in Taiwan, bringing real benefits to Taiwan compatriots. Regrettably, in recent years, the DPP authorities have obstinately insisted on the “Taiwan independence” stance, continuously engaged in provocations to seek independence, escalated hostility and confrontation across the Strait, and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. To this day, they still unilaterally restrict the import of more than 1,000 agricultural products from the mainland into Taiwan, which seriously harms the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In view of this, the mainland side has decided to stop implementing the policy of exempting 34 agricultural products from Taiwan from import tariffs, starting September 25. The DPP authorities should take concrete actions to stop harming cross-Strait relations and stop damaging the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652483.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, the national security authorities published an article on their official WeChat account, “Exposing the ‘Taiwan independence’ cyber army ‘Anonymous 64’,” revealing that the true background of this hacker organization is the Cyber Environment Research Center of the Cyber Warfare Wing under Taiwan’s Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command. The organization frequently carries out…","The Lai Ching-te authorities claim verbally that they hope for peaceful cross-Strait development, yet behind the scenes they instruct and manipulate Taiwan's military intelligence agencies to carry out cyberattacks and sabotage against the mainland, twist right and wrong, spread rumors, and vilify the mainland's political system and its policies on a large scale. They persistently incite cross-Strait confrontation, desperate for chaos. This fully exposes their hypocritical face and sinister nature: under the guise of peace, they obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait relations and seek \"Taiwan independence\" separatism. In the face of the arrogant aggression of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, national security organs faithfully fulfilled their mission and resolutely took countermeasures, effectively safeguarding national security and cross-Strait stability. This is a righteous act of punishing \"independence\" in accordance with the law.\nThe complete reunification of the motherland is a historical inevitability and a general trend, and it cannot be blocked by anyone or any force. Broad Taiwan compatriots should see clearly the true face of the Lai Ching-te authorities, which obstinately hold to the \"Taiwan independence\" stance and carry out activities to split the country. Starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own interests and well-being, they should resolutely oppose the provocative and risky \"Taiwan independence\" conduct and work to safeguard peace across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652479.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Taiwan’s MAC Minister Chiu Chui-cheng recently said that the mainland links the Taiwan question with national rejuvenation, and that its Taiwan policy will only become “more and more arbitrary and provocative,” but that Taiwan’s determination to “defend sovereignty and the democratic system” is firm, and that “Taiwan will never surrender.” What is your comment on this?","The people on both sides of the Strait see very clearly who is trying to split the country and who is working to rejuvenate China; who is provoking with “independence” schemes and who is promoting peace across the Strait; who is willing to serve as a “pawn” for external forces and who is enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nResolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, continue to promote cross-strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development across all fields between the two sides, and firmly advance the great cause of national reunification. We would like to give the DPP authorities two sentences: “Reunification is the trend of the times; how could separation last? ‘Taiwan independence’ is a dead end; evil deeds will eventually be punished.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Reportedly, the DPP authorities plan to substantially increase next year’s “media policy and business promotion fee” budget by 65%, to over NT$1.49 billion. This has caused an uproar in public opinion, which believes the move aims to strengthen control over the media and cyber armies and further restrict freedom of speech. What is your comment on this?","From “14.5 million” to “1.49 billion,” the sharp increase in related budgets fully exposes the DPP authorities' ambition to further increase their support for online troll armies and attempt to comprehensively manipulate public opinion. For the sake of political self-interest, the DPP authorities fabricate and spread false information in all aspects and across the entire chain. Through the online troll armies they support, they stir up trouble on the internet, suppress dissenters, tear society apart, and create a “green terror,” leaving people in panic and the atmosphere in chaos. Facing strong dissatisfaction and criticism from all sectors on the island, the DPP authorities not only have not stopped or restrained themselves, but have become even more reckless. This will inevitably lead to rampant online bullying and widespread internet rumors, seriously disrupting social order in Taiwan and seriously harming the interests of Taiwan's people. Those who commit many wrongs will eventually destroy themselves, and the DPP's evil deeds will certainly be repaid by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Taiwan media reported that DPP legislator Shen Boyang and others recently urged all party caucuses to jointly support the “Legislative Yuan” in passing a so-called “UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 does not involve Taiwan” resolution text, so that Taiwan “has the right to join international organizations.” What comment do you have?","This so-called “resolution text” is completely untenable and serves entirely to pursue “Taiwan independence.”\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. Resolution 2758, adopted by the 26th session of the UN General Assembly in 1971, was a decision by the United Nations, on the premise of recognizing that Taiwan belongs to China, to restore the rights and seat of representation of all of China, including Taiwan, to the government of the People’s Republic of China. The historical facts are clear and the legal basis is definite.\nThe DPP’s attempt to promote the so-called “UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 Does Not Concern Taiwan resolution text” is a deliberate distortion of facts, a wanton trampling of international law, and an open challenge to international order and rules. This fully exposes that its nature of stubbornly insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position has not changed at all; it fully exposes that it cares only about seeking political gain and completely disregards the economic and social development of the island and the interests and well-being of the people; and it fully exposes that it is willing to serve as a “chess piece” of anti-China forces in the United States and the West, and its vicious intention of pushing Taiwan toward the danger of war and conflict. More and more people in Taiwan will open their eyes and clearly see the extreme danger and harm of the DPP’s “Taiwan independence” separatist line.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652485.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Lai Ching-te authorities recently said that the mainland has redefined the “1992 Consensus,” leaving Taiwan no room to interpret the “meaning of one China,” and that accepting the “1992 Consensus” would mean “surrendering Taiwan's sovereignty” and acknowledging that Taiwan is part of the People's Republic of China. What comment do you have?","The \"1992 Consensus\" was reached by the two cross-Strait associations, authorized by both sides, after repeated communication and consultation and an exchange of letters and telegrams. Each side orally expressed the consensus that \"both sides of the Taiwan Strait uphold the one-China principle.\" Its core meaning is that \"both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national reunification.\" The \"1992 Consensus\" fully embodies the political wisdom of Chinese on both sides of the Strait in seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and it clearly defines the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. No matter how the Lai Ching-te authorities change their rhetoric, distorting or denying the \"1992 Consensus\" is contrary to fact and futile.\nThe \"1992 Consensus\" is the anchor that steadies the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations. Practice has repeatedly proved that only by adhering to this political foundation can cross-Strait relations go steadily and far; deviating from it will only make the situation in the Taiwan Strait turbulent and unstable. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize that the Lai Ching-te authorities deliberately distort the \"1992 Consensus\" to incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation and to undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, which is the essence of their \"independence\" scheme. We hope they will cherish and uphold the \"1992 Consensus\" and jointly push cross-Strait relations back onto the right track.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652478.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding the mainland’s announcement that it is canceling zero-tariff treatment for 34 Taiwan agricultural products, a spokesperson for the Taiwan executive authority said consultations should return to the framework and rules of the World Trade Organization (WTO), that dialogue should replace confrontation, and that disputes should be resolved through pragmatic communication. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities' attempt to discuss the relevant issues through mechanisms of the World Trade Organization is entirely aimed at \"internationalizing\" the Taiwan question and harbors the malicious intent of \"Taiwan independence.\"\nTwo points need to be reiterated: First, the basis for cross-Strait consultations is the \"1992 Consensus,\" not the framework and rules of the World Trade Organization (WTO). Second, the zero-tariff treatment that the mainland previously applied to 34 agricultural products imported from Taiwan was a measure introduced out of commitment to the concept of \"cross-Strait families are one family\" and to promoting the normalization of cross-Strait trade. However, the DPP authorities obstinately insist on their \"Taiwan independence\" position, continuously engage in provocations aimed at seeking independence, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and unilaterally restrict the import of more than 1,000 agricultural products from the mainland into Taiwan. This is the crux of the problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The Mainland previously announced the resumption of imports of pomelos from the Taiwan region. What is the current situation of pomelo imports into the Mainland, and what has been the reaction of the industry on the island?","It is understood that since Taiwan pomelos were allowed to be imported again on September 2, multiple batches have been sold to the mainland. Farmer friends on the island said it is “like receiving a Mid-Autumn Festival gift,” believing it helps expand sales and resolve the problem of overproduction. However, the DPP authorities are unhappy about this and indiscriminately accuse the mainland of carrying out “division and united front work” against Taiwan. This fully shows that they do not care about the interests of farmers on the island and act out of partisan self-interest, fearing that compatriots on both sides will draw closer and share in well-being. Who is thinking of Taiwan’s farmers and who is harming their interests? Taiwan’s farmer friends have their own judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Lai Ching-te, at a recent DPP event, falsely claimed: “We must insist that the Republic of China and the People's Republic of China are not subordinate to each other, insist that sovereignty must not be infringed upon or annexed, and insist that the future of the Republic of China Taiwan is to be decided jointly by 23 million people,” and said, “We must continue to strengthen national defense capabilities.” What…","Lai Ching-te's remarks this time once again exposed his vicious nature of stubbornly clinging to the “Taiwan independence” position, carrying out “Taiwan independence” separatism, and constantly engaging in provocation and confrontation.\nAlthough the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and will never be allowed to be divided, and Taiwan's status as part of Chinese territory has never changed and will never be allowed to change. Lai Ching-te's so-called “not subordinate to each other” and “upholding sovereignty” claims have neither historical or legal basis nor conform to objective facts.\nTaiwan is Chinese Taiwan. The future of Taiwan lies in national reunification, which can only be decided jointly by the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots. Lai Ching-te and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have persistently engaged in provocations to seek independence, advocated “relying on foreign powers to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force,” and placed the people of Taiwan in the dangerous situation of “provoking war for ‘Taiwan independence,’” seriously deviating from the trend of history, and they are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652487.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","This year marks the 400th anniversary of the birth of the national hero Zheng Chenggong (Koxinga), and both sides of the Taiwan Strait have successively held various commemorative activities. For some time, however, the DPP authorities have repeatedly attached smearing labels such as “colonizer” to Zheng Chenggong. Public opinion on the island points out that at root this is the “Taiwan independence view of…","For a long time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have pursued “de-Sinicization,” vigorously promoted “cultural and educational Taiwan independence,” and used “Taiwan independence historical outlook” to poison Taiwan's people, especially the younger generation, attempting to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides of the Strait, instigating antagonism and division on the island, creating spiritual estrangement among compatriots, and paving the way for “Taiwan independence.”\nThe historical thread and legal and factual basis showing that Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times are clear. The vast majority of Taiwan compatriots, including members of ethnic minorities, migrated from the mainland to Taiwan at different periods in history. A large number of historical books and documents record the scenes of the Chinese people developing Taiwan, dating back as early as the Three Kingdoms period. After the Song and Yuan dynasties, successive central governments of China began to establish administrative jurisdiction over Penghu and Taiwan. In 1662, national hero Zheng Chenggong expelled the Dutch colonialists and recovered Taiwan. In 1684, the Qing government established Taiwan Prefecture, and in 1885 Taiwan was changed to a province. In April 1895, Japan forced the Qing government to cede Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. In 1945, with victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan, on October 25 China recovered Taiwan both in law and in fact. Since 1949, although the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully unified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and Taiwan's status as part of China's territory has never changed. The “Taiwan independence historical outlook” distorts historical facts, abandons the great righteousness of the nation, and is a complete lie and a poison that deludes people, fully exposing the vile nature of “Taiwan independence” separatists who acknowledge colonialists and invaders as their fathers, forget their ancestry, and cut off their own roots.\n“Taiwan independence” has never been history, nor is it reality, and it will never have a future. No matter how the Democratic Progressive Party authorities manipulate, they cannot change the history and fact that the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait share the same roots, the same language, and the same culture; they cannot sever the bond of Chinese culture that links compatriots on both sides of the Strait, nor erase the Chinese national gene in the blood of Taiwan compatriots. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must work together to eradicate this “malignant tumor” of the “Taiwan independence historical outlook,” and firmly safeguard the common homeland and cultural roots of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652477.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视直新闻记者","According to reports from US media, after the US State Department announced in mid-this-month an arms sale to Taiwan with a total value of US$228 million, the US government is planning to provide Taiwan with a new round of military aid totaling US$567 million. What is the spokesperson’s comment on the US side’s successive arms sales to Taiwan?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to the Taiwan region of China. Whether labeled “arms sales,” “military aid,” or “financing,” or under any other name, what the United States gives Taiwan is nothing but a pile of things it itself does not want and false promises, while the people of Taiwan are left only with the increasingly dangerous situation of being sunk deeper into a “powder keg” and “ammunition depot.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Taiwan's security authorities recently claimed that the mainland is conducting so-called “cultural infiltration” against Taiwan, using soft issues such as culture as packaging to gradually increase Taiwan residents' identification with the Chinese nation and Chinese culture. What is your comment on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the Chinese nation. Chinese culture is the spiritual lifeblood of the Chinese nation and the common spiritual home of compatriots on both sides. The identification of Taiwan residents with the Chinese nation and Chinese culture is a gene engraved in their bones, and there is no need for any so-called “infiltration.” The DPP authorities regard Chinese culture as a major enemy, use “Taiwan independence historiography” to split Chinese culture apart, and maliciously smear normal and natural cultural exchanges across the Strait. This only shows that they have forgotten their ancestors, betrayed the nation and gone against the will of the people.\nChinese culture is the greatest common denominator of compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides speak Chinese, write Chinese characters, celebrate Chinese festivals and worship Chinese gods. They carry forward Chinese culture, uphold traditional national values and promote the creative transformation and innovative development of Chinese culture. This is the daily life of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, and it is also their steadfast commitment. We will work with Taiwan compatriots to be guardians, inheritors and promoters of Chinese culture, continuously strengthen the aspiration, integrity and confidence to be Chinese, continuously strengthen the sense of belonging, identity and honor of the Chinese nation, and firmly build a sense of community for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Videos of Norwegian Prime Minister Støre being interviewed by China Media Group on a high-speed train during his visit to China have sparked heated discussion in public opinion on the island. Netizens on the island commented, “Judging from the interview footage, it is fast and stable,” and “the mainland's technology and development are plain to see.” Some netizens also said they hope that in the future they can…","The mainland has built and operates the world's largest and most advanced high-speed rail network and railway network. Total railway mileage has exceeded 160,000 kilometers, including 46,000 kilometers of high-speed rail. Compatriots from Taiwan can enjoy the convenient travel of covering a thousand li in a day by taking high-speed rail. We warmly welcome compatriots from Taiwan to come to the mainland to ride high-speed rail, see beautiful scenery, enjoy delicious food, and make friends. It is worth mentioning that the Fuzhou-Xiamen high-speed railway has been built to the point closest to the Taiwan Strait, only 200 kilometers from Taiwan Island. We believe that with the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, this 200-kilometer distance will be “reset to zero,” and the dream of people on both sides of the Strait traveling across the Strait by high-speed rail will be realized.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The mainland’s live-streaming e-commerce market continues to maintain strong growth momentum. Live-streaming e-commerce, with its strong interactivity and intuitiveness, has attracted a large number of young consumers. Recently, the 5th Cross-Strait E-Commerce Shopping Festival, “920 Love You,” was officially launched. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant details.","Since 2019, China Taiwan Net has planned and launched the cross-strait e-commerce public welfare event, the “920 Love You” Cross-Strait E-commerce Shopping Festival. The emergence of the e-commerce shopping festival has built a more direct and diversified platform for cross-strait economic exchanges, provided broader development space and entrepreneurial opportunities for young people on both sides, and become a new model for enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Through e-commerce platforms, not only can the rich products and quality services of the mainland market be presented to Taiwan compatriots, but more opportunities are also provided for Taiwan’s distinctive products to enter the mainland market, further promoting cross-strait circulation of goods and prosperity of trade, and deepening mutual understanding and recognition of each other’s ways of life among people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","A report recently released by the US Department of Defense shows that among the armaments Taiwan received from the United States last December, some munitions had expired, packaging was disorderly, and bulletproof vests were damp and moldy. Personnel of the “American Institute in Taiwan” also said that the US munitions shipped to Taiwan “look like clearing out things no one wants.” What is your comment?","This report once again demonstrates a fact: the United States always puts its own interests first, and its pawns may be discarded at any time, and Taiwan will be no exception. For the sake of its selfish “Taiwan independence” interests, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, swallow their humiliation and accept in full all the scrap metal and junk the US has cleared out, and on the other hand, continue to willingly serve as the US's “ATM,” lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents. This will not only fail to bring security to the people of Taiwan, but will also push them into the dangerous situation of war. We hope that compatriots across Taiwan will raise their vigilance, resolutely resist the DPP authorities' conduct of “relying on outsiders to seek independence,” and resolutely oppose the US and Western schemes to “use Taiwan to contain China.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240925_12652475.htm"],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, Taiwan writer Pai Hsien-yung, together with the Suzhou Kunqu Opera Theatre, brought the complete youth version of “The Peony Pavilion” to Peking University to mark its 20th anniversary, and it was warmly welcomed. Please introduce the relevant situation. What other cross-Strait cultural exchange activities have taken place recently?","From September 14 to 16, the 20th anniversary celebration performance of the complete youth edition of “The Peony Pavilion” was successfully held in the Centennial Commemorative Auditorium of Peking University. This is the second revival of the production at Peking University after 19 years, and the fifth visit to Yanyuan (Peking University campus). It was warmly welcomed by Kunqu opera fans. Over two decades, this Kunqu classic, jointly created by opera artists from both sides of the Strait, remains “youthful,” is deeply loved by compatriots on both sides, has strong appeal among cross-Strait young audiences, and demonstrates the enduring vitality of China’s outstanding traditional culture. We hope that cultural practitioners on both sides will join hands to make greater contributions to inheriting and promoting China’s outstanding traditional culture and to advancing its creative transformation and innovative development.\nFrom September 20 to 24 and from September 27 to October 4, the 15th Cross-Strait Children’s Art Exhibition held tour exhibitions in New Taipei and Hualien, respectively. Over 14 years, the Cross-Strait Children’s Art Exhibition has held tour exhibitions across Taiwan every year, and has become an important art platform where tens of thousands of young people from both sides grow and exchange together. This year’s exhibition took “Together” as its theme. Children from both sides, with “Searching for Flying Fish at Sea,” “Strolling Through Night Markets Together,” and “Visiting the Panda Family,” brought colorful and childlike art works that offer the public a rich and diverse artistic experience. Taiwan residents are welcome to bring their children to visit the exhibition and exchange.\nOn September 24, the awards ceremony of the 7th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong, Macau Drone Aerial Photography Competition 2024 was held in Shenzhen. This year’s competition took “Home” as its theme and highlighted integrated development. The competition showed three features. First, the number of works and participants from Taiwan increased significantly. This year’s competition received 768 works from across the Taiwan Strait, Hong Kong and Macau, of which 43 were from Taiwan, with nearly 100 participants, a record high in the seven competitions. Second, cross-Strait contestant exchange and creation camps were added. The cross-Strait exchange camp for the main competition unit was held in Shenzhen, where 32 contestants carried out 72 hours of timed creation around 8 themes including “urban change,” “low-altitude economy,” and “Hakka culture.” The cross-Strait exchange camp for the campus competition unit was held in Hinggan League, Inner Mongolia, where 14 teams from 12 universities carried out 72 hours of timed creation. Third, a contestant exchange meeting and a “Contestants’ Night” event were held to promote exchange among cross-Strait youth.\nWe will continue to welcome and support broad Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation, and jointly promote the prosperity and development of Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报南方+记者","The Liaoning aircraft carrier group sailed through waters northeast of Taiwan on the 18th. The DPP said, “We call on China to accept the objective fact that the two sides of the Strait are ‘not subordinate to each other,’ stop all suppression and military threats, and not become a regional troublemaker or creator of danger.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, upholding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and protecting the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are the sacred duties of the People’s Liberation Army. The Democratic Progressive Party and its authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and continue to engage in provocation and confrontation. They are the greatest threat and source of chaos causing tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. No matter how they distort right and wrong or confuse black and white, they cannot change the objective fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, nor can they change the historical trend that the two sides will inevitably be unified. Nor can they change the fate that “Taiwan independence” will inevitably perish.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Since April this year, electricity prices across the island have been raised comprehensively. While residents are forced to cope with high electricity prices, several DPP authority departments have been exposed for increasing their electricity budget allocations. Island public opinion has criticized this as “stripping three layers of skin off taxpayers.” The root cause is that the DPP authorities disregard…","Since coming to power, the DPP authorities have invariably pursued political self-interest and served \"Taiwan independence\" in everything they do. Money that could have been used to improve people's livelihoods has been wasted on buying weapons to curry favor with external forces, and squandered on raising \"cyber armies\" and suppressing dissidents. The island's \"five shortages\" problem has not been resolved for a long time, and has in fact become even more serious. Regarding the corruption, incompetence, cold-heartedness and greed of the DPP authorities, we believe that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots and industry figures will see more and more clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday新闻云记者","First question: A 22-year-old university graduate surnamed Guo is being investigated by relevant mainland authorities on suspicion of fraud. Where did the case involving Guo take place? In addition, Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council stated that the relevant mainland authorities did not notify it of the “restriction of personal freedom” in accordance with relevant agreements. Could the spokesperson provide further…","First question. It is understood that Taiwan resident Kuo Yu-hsuan, after arriving in the mainland on August 27, is suspected of committing fraud crimes in multiple locations, and has been investigated by the relevant authorities according to law; the case is currently under investigation. The relevant mainland authorities are handling the case strictly in accordance with the law and are protecting his lawful rights and interests according to law.\nCracking down on all kinds of illegal and criminal activities according to law, and actively safeguarding the life and property safety and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, is our consistent position. As for the reasons why the implementation of cross-Strait agreements has been affected, the reasons are well known.\nSecond question. It is understood that this is an economic case in which a Taiwan compatriot is suspected of false declaration resulting in tax evasion. People with ulterior motives are using this to mislead public opinion and intimidate the Taiwan public, which does not win hearts.\nThird question. The Lai Ching-te authorities, behind the scenes, instructed and manipulated Taiwan's military intelligence agencies to carry out cyber attacks and sabotage against the mainland, distorting right and wrong, spreading rumors, extensively vilifying the mainland's political system and policies, and persistently inciting cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism. The national security organs have faithfully fulfilled their mission and resolutely carried out countermeasures, effectively safeguarding national security and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait; this is a just act of punishing \"independence\" according to law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","Cross-Strait relations have become increasingly tense since Lai Ching-te took office, yet the Straits Exchange Foundation's expenditure budget for next year is several tens of millions of New Taiwan dollars higher than this year's, which has sparked controversy. Taiwan media said bluntly that if the Straits Exchange Foundation makes no major breakthrough or cannot resume exchanges with the Association for…","Only by returning to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism between the two associations be restarted, and only then can the Straits Exchange Foundation perform its due functions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: The Mainland Affairs Council recently announced that same-sex partners may first marry in a third location and then return to Taiwan to register their marriage with the household registration authorities. What is the spokesperson's comment on this? In addition, the Mainland Affairs Council said that if a mainland same-sex partner wants to obtain a Taiwan ID card, it depends on the mainland side's…","On the first question: The Civil Code specifically provides for the basic procedures for applying for marriage and registering a marriage. The subjects of marriage refer to a man and a woman who meet the legal conditions for marriage. Same-sex marriage registration applications do not comply with mainland law. Questions involving household registration should be directed to the relevant competent authorities.\nOn the second question: The mainland side strictly handles cases in accordance with the law and protects the legitimate rights and interests of the relevant persons in accordance with the law.\nYou may have noticed that we recently launched the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account and Channels account. We welcome friends who care about cross-strait relations to follow and share them. We will promptly and comprehensively report the central government's policies on Taiwan and our work through the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account, the Channels account, and the “Taiwan Affairs Office Releases” accounts on Toutiao and Weibo, to people on both sides of the strait. If you have any opinions or suggestions, you may leave text or voice messages through the official account.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202409/t20240925_12652424.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-09-26","Lin Jian","KBS","Yesterday, a Japanese Maritime Self-Defense Force destroyer for the first time sailed through the Taiwan Strait. Japanese media commented that this is a response to China’s military activities near Japan and is an assertion of freedom of navigation. What’s China’s position?","The Taiwan question concerns China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is the political foundation of China-Japan relations and a red line that must not be crossed. The Chinese military has handled in accordance with laws and regulations the entering into the Taiwan Strait of a Japanese Maritime Self-Defense Force vessel. China is highly vigilant on Japan’s political intention behind this move and has protested to the Japanese side.\nJapan made a clear commitment on this in the 1972 China-Japan Joint Statement, which says “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this position of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its position under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” We urge Japan to honor its commitment and act prudently on the Taiwan question, and refrain from causing disruption to its relations with China and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495585.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495348.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-26","Lin Jian","Reuters","Naval vessels from New Zealand and Australia sailed through the Taiwan Strait on Wednesday, according to a statement from the New Zealand Defense Minister. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","China handles foreign warships’ transit through the Taiwan Strait in accordance with laws and regulations, and meanwhile we stay vigilant against any acts that might jeopardize China’s sovereignty and security.\nLinks:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495585.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495348.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japanese Maritime Self-Defense Force vessels transited the Taiwan Strait on the 25th. Is the Chinese side aware of the situation? What comments does it have on this?","On September 25, the Japanese destroyer “Lian,” the Australian destroyer “Sydney,” and the New Zealand replenishment ship “Aotearoa” transited the Taiwan Strait. The PLA conducted full-process tracking and warning on them. China firmly opposes the provocative acts carried out in the name of “freedom of navigation,” which send erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces and endanger China's sovereignty and security.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We urge the relevant countries to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, stop stirring up trouble on the Taiwan question, and stop undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Chinese People's Liberation Army remains highly vigilant and on guard, and will firmly counter all threats and provocations.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Taiwan’s defense authorities submitted the 2025 budget proposal to the legislature, with total defense spending of NT$667 billion (about RMB 148 billion). Reportedly, Taiwan’s army has begun to greatly procure various types of drones this year, mainly for urban battlefield surveillance and attack missions. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities stubbornly persist in their “Taiwan independence” stance, disregard public opinion, and act recklessly. They go further and further down the path of reckless warmongering and do more and more to waste public money and labor. What they bring to the people of Taiwan is not security but danger, pushing Taiwan step by step into the perilous situation of war. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: those who commit many unrighteous acts will bring about their own destruction. No matter how many weapons they buy, they cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” being doomed. The People's Liberation Army has ample capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the first F-16V that Taiwan purchased from the US is expected to leave the factory and be delivered at the end of September, and 26 US drone manufacturers have come to Taiwan. The director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei office recently said that the possibility of joint US-Taiwan arms production in the future cannot be ruled out. However, some media have revealed that a large…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. At present, the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and the indulgence and support of external forces. It should be pointed out that whether it is US arms sales to Taiwan or so-called joint weapons production activities, they are by no means for \"protecting Taiwan.\" Rather, they treat the DPP authorities as a \"sucker\" and Taiwan as an \"ATM,\" dumping outdated and obsolete surplus weapons on Taiwan to fatten their own military-industrial complex. We warn the DPP authorities that \"the chess piece will ultimately become a discarded piece,\" and those who cater to the US side and harm Taiwan will not escape the severe punishment of history and the law. The People's Liberation Army will take all necessary measures to resolutely thwart any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes and interference by external forces.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A PLA pilot interviewed in the documentary 《淬火》 (Quenching) said that he could never forget the scene of seeing the island of Taiwan while flying the J-20. Outsiders therefore speculate that the J-20 once took part in patrol missions across the Taiwan Strait. Please have the spokesperson verify this.","Taiwan is China's territory. PLA aircraft may go wherever they wish; there is no need to make a fuss about it.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: According to reports, the Taiwan defense authorities said that on the 26th they detected mainland Chinese military aircraft operating around the Taiwan Strait. Some experts say the exercise is meant to prevent foreign forces from intervening. What is the purpose of China's exercise and training activities this time? Second question: Regarding the intercontinental ballistic…","Regarding the first question, the PLA's organization of exercises and drills in the sea and airspace around Taiwan island is justified and reasonable. We will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness, and regularly organize relevant military operations.\nRegarding the second question, the Rocket Force's launch test of an intercontinental ballistic missile complies with international law and international practice. Before the launch, China issued a notice clearly specifying the prohibited navigation areas and times, and notified the relevant countries through military diplomatic channels, which fully demonstrates the openness and transparency of the Chinese military.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to foreign media reports, Japan's Ministry of Defense recently announced a large-scale reorganization of the Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force, establishing a new “marine corps” and an “alert and defense group.” It also plans to increase the defense budget and build a small satellite network. Some analysts believe Japan may be preparing to cooperate with US involvement in the Taiwan Strait situation.…","We have noted relevant moves by the Japanese side. In recent years, the Japanese side has accelerated the adjustment of its operational force system, sped up the development of new operational domains, and built up long-range strike capabilities. The tendency to retrace the path of militarism has become more pronounced. This seriously violates Japan's “Peace Constitution” and the principle of “exclusively defensive defense,” and is even more a destruction of the post-war international order. We urge the Japanese side to draw lessons from history, exercise caution in the military and security field, and do more things that help safeguard regional peace and stability, rather than acting recklessly.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, the US Navy recently published its strategic guidance for naval operations, stating that mainland China has the world’s largest shipbuilding capacity and that the US should prepare for a conflict with China in 2027. What comments do you have on this? Second, the mainland’s Ministry of State Security recently exposed the Taiwan “Anonymous 64” organization and disclosed that its…","Regarding the first question, the words and deeds of the US side expose its deep-rooted Cold War mentality and bellicose nature. I want to emphasize that China has no intention to challenge or replace the United States. China's development is aimed at enabling the Chinese people to live better lives and at providing new opportunities for world peace and development. Today's China is firmly and unwaveringly advancing the great cause of building a strong country and achieving national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization, and no external force can stop it. The Chinese military fears no threats or challenges and resolutely safeguards national sovereignty, security, and development interests.\nRegarding the second question, please direct inquiries on this aspect to the relevant competent authorities.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. defense news website recently reported that the U.S. plan to provide Taiwan with nearly $570 million in “security assistance” has entered its final stage. This is the largest package to date, and will be used for projects such as training, stockpiling, anti-armor, air defense, and drones, with the aim of defending Taiwan against attacks by the Chinese (mainland) military. What is your comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. China has consistently and firmly opposed the United States selling weapons to Taiwan, China's Taiwan region. The US's actions seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously harm China's sovereignty and security interests, and send a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces. It must be pointed out that the US seeks to “use Taiwan to contain China,” using military aid and arms sales to embolden the DPP authorities and encourage the arrogant momentum of “Taiwan independence.” This will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and will ultimately backfire on the US, dragging itself into the abyss of disaster.\nWe urge the US to stop its military collusion with Taiwan, stop arming Taiwan in any way, and avoid interfering with the development of China-US and inter-military relations. Taiwan is part of China. Taiwan and the Chinese mainland are “just across the strait,” and we will never allow Taiwan to be “far away at the ends of the earth.” The Chinese People's Liberation Army will not yield one inch in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will resolutely thwart any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and interference by external forces.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-09-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Taiwan's defense department website published a message saying that the Taiwan military recently detected various types of mainland Chinese fighter jets, helicopters, and drones, as well as amphibious ships and roll-on/roll-off ships loading ground troops, which organized a joint landing drill near the waters of Dacheng Bay, Dongshan, Fujian. The defense department said the Taiwan military…","The relevant PLA exercises and training activities are routine arrangements within the annual plan, aimed at comprehensively improving the troops' ability to fulfill their missions and tasks. The actions of the PLA are not deterred by any reconnaissance interference. The DPP authorities should genuinely recognize the PLA's formidable capabilities and firm resolve, acknowledge the reality that \"Taiwan independence\" cannot succeed, and thoroughly abandon the illusion of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism.\nIn just a few days, New China will welcome its 75th birthday! Over 75 years of stormy change, the Communist Party of China has led the Chinese people in writing a magnificent epic and creating achievements that will go down in history. Over 75 years of iron-blooded glory, under the absolute leadership of the Communist Party of China, the People's Liberation Army has been reborn through fire in revolutionary forging, has grown strong in historical reshaping, and has advanced vigorously in confronting risks and challenges. It has always been an iron Great Wall defending national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and always a firm force for maintaining world peace and stability. Today's China is comprehensively advancing the great undertaking of building a strong nation and rejuvenating the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization. The People's Liberation Army, anchored to the goal of the centenary of the military's founding, is striving hard and advancing bravely toward becoming a world-class military! Here, we wish our great motherland peace, prosperity, and flourishing!","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16341107.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-09-27","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","In August this year, Shigeru Ishiba visited Taiwan and met with leader of Taiwan. How do you view the relationship between Japan and Taiwan after Ishiba’s election?","Taiwan is a province of China and there is no “leader of Taiwan.” China has made clear its position concerning your question. China is always firmly opposed to Japanese political figures visiting China’s Taiwan region. This position is crystal clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495593.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495353.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-30","Lin Jian","CCTV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi attended the General Debate of the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly in New York. Can you share more details with us?","On September 28 local time, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs Wang Yi attended the General Debate of the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly at the UN Headquarters in New York, and delivered a statement entitled “Building on Past Achievements and Forging Ahead Together Toward a Community with a Shared Future for Mankind.”\nForeign Minister Wang Yi noted we are facing a changing and turbulent world and meanwhile, we are also embracing a world full of hope. The security of all countries is tied together, the development of all countries is deeply integrated, each civilization has its own strengths and countries should all enjoy sovereign equality. The United Nations embodies the aspirations of people across the world for lasting peace and common prosperity, and bears witness to the glorious journey of the international community coming together in pursuit of progress. The role of the UN should be strengthened, not weakened.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi elaborated on the significance of Chinese modernization to the world. He pointed out that the People’s Republic of China will soon celebrate the 75th anniversary of its founding. Over the past 75 years, no matter how the world changes, China’s dedication has not changed. It is dedicated to pursuing happiness for the Chinese people and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. It is also dedicated to human progress and world harmony. In the course of seeking its own development, China has kept in mind the common interests of the whole world, generating new opportunities for the world through its own development. The Third Plenum of the 20th CPC Central Committee made an important decision on further deepening reform comprehensively to advance Chinese modernization. It set in motion a new journey where China joins hands with the world in common development and progress. Chinese modernization will contribute robustly to world peace and stability, to the common development for all, to improving global governance, and to the advancement of human civilization. Every step in China’s development is an increase in the force for peace. China does not only care about its own development. We are ready to develop hand in hand with all countries. China believes that different civilizations should respect and learn from one another, and jointly contribute to the progress of human civilization.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stated China’s proposal on improving global governance and noted that President Xi Jinping has put forth the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative and the Global Civilization Initiative in recent years. They carry China’s wisdom for resolving various difficult issues confronting humanity, and bring impetus from China for improving global governance. China’s proposal is to put development at the top of the global agenda, uphold the equity and openness of the international system, stay firmly committed to a path of green, low-carbon and sustainable development, and support the UN’s role as the main channel for global AI governance. China maintains that all countries’ right to independently choose their path of human rights development should be respected. No country should impose its own will on others.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stated China’s stance on the Taiwan question and stressed that Resolution 2758 once and for all resolved the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the UN, and made clear that there is no such thing as “two Chinas,” or “one China, one Taiwan.” On this matter of principle, there is no gray zone or room for ambiguity. Foreign Minister Wang Yi also made clear China’s position on hotspot issues, including the Ukraine crisis, the question of Palestine, the issue of Afghanistan and the Korean Peninsula.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495598.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495359.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-30","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s defense ministry said on Sunday that it was on heightened alert after detecting multiple waves of missile firing in Inner Mongolia, Gansu, Qinghai and Xinjiang. Does China have a comment on this?","Taiwan is a province of China and there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s defense ministry.” This is not a question about China’s foreign affairs either.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495598.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495359.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-09-30","Lin Jian","Phoenix TV","The White House announced on its website the decision to provide around US$ 567 million military assistance to China’s Taiwan region. What’s China’s comment?","The US again provides weapons to China’s Taiwan region, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. The move is in fact emboldening Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities as they cling to the stance of “Taiwan independence” and make deliberate provocations on the one-China principle. This once again shows that the separatist moves for “Taiwan independence” and connivance and support for such moves from US-led external forces are the biggest threat facing cross-Strait peace and stability and cause the greatest disruption to the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. Let me be clear, “Taiwan independence” separatism is a dead end and what the US has done to assist the “Taiwan independence” attempt by arming Taiwan will only backfire.\nWe urge the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop arming Taiwan in any form. No matter how many weapons the US provides to the Taiwan region, it will never weaken our firm will in opposing “Taiwan independence,” and safeguarding China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\n*********************************************\nDuring the National Day holiday, there will be no regular press conference from October 1 to 7. The press conference will resume on October 8. During the holiday, questions can be submitted to the Spokesperson’s Office via fax, email or WeChat.\nHappy National Day Holiday!\nLinks:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495598.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495359.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-09-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 30 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, briefed reporters on the 30th in response to questions. As the National Day “Golden Week” holiday approaches in 2024, the mainland tourism market will see a surge in demand. According to statistics, the first batch of 1,256 scenic spots on the mainland has launched promotional activities for…","Chen Binhua said: We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland for sightseeing in the golden autumn season, to enjoy the magnificent rivers and mountains, explore brilliant Chinese culture, experience local customs, and feel the mainland's development and progress. We believe everyone will broaden their horizons and find the trip worthwhile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240930_12653751.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-09-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, September 30 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on September 30, pointing out: Since the DPP authorities took office, they have stubbornly adhered to the 'Taiwan independence' separatist position and, in pursuit of 'Taiwan independence' separation, have curried favor with and sought help from external forces. The DPP…","Chen Binhua said that we firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to Taiwan region of China. In the three China-US joint communiqués, the US side made solemn commitments on the Taiwan question, but the US side’s actions encourage and embolden reckless “Taiwan independence” adventurism and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the One-China Principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming Taiwan, and stop sending any wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202409/t20240930_12653763.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On October 3, a fire broke out at Antai Hospital in Donggang, Pingtung, Taiwan, causing 9 deaths and multiple injuries. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that we are deeply pained by the occurrence of such an accident, mourn the Taiwan compatriots who unfortunately died, and sincerely extend condolences to the families of the deceased and to the injured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241003_12654190.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-08","Mao Ning","Reuters","Tsai Ing-wen will visit the Czech Republic this month, officials said on Monday. Will the Foreign Ministry like to comment on this?","China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We firmly oppose anyone who seeks “Taiwan independence” visiting countries with diplomatic ties with China under any pretext. We urge the Czech Republic and relevant countries to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and not to provide facilitation for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form or do things that harm bilateral relations with China. We also have a clear message for the DPP authorities: seeking “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail, and any political manipulation and attempt to solicit foreign support for that agenda will prove futile.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495605.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495369.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-08","Mao Ning","CCTV","It was reported that China has evacuated Chinese nationals in Lebanon in two batches. Has the evacuation work basically completed? Can you share more details?","Since the abrupt escalation of tensions between Lebanon and Israel, we have acted in the spirit of the important guidance of General Secretary Xi Jinping. The Foreign Ministry worked closely and round the clock with the Ministry of Transport, the Civil Aviation Administration and Chinese embassies in Lebanon, Cyprus and other countries to protect the safety of Chinese nationals with utmost effort and swiftly transfer and evacuate them. With the concerted efforts of all sides, we have enabled the safe evacuation from Lebanon of 215 Chinese nationals, including three Hong Kong residents and one Taiwan compatriot, in two batches by ship and chartered plane respectively. We would like to express our thanks to Air China, China COSCO Shipping and Ningbo Zhongmeng Hanglian, which have actively supported and participated in the transfer and evacuation operation.\nThe current Lebanon-Israel situation is still complex and severe. The Chinese Embassy in Lebanon remains open and continues to provide guidance and assistance to help a few Chinese nationals who are still there keep themselves safe.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495605.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495369.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters' questions\n(October 8, 2024)\nQuestion: Lai Ching-te recently claimed at an event in Taipei, “In terms of age, the People's Republic of China can absolutely never be the motherland of the people of the Republic of China; rather, the Republic of China may be the motherland of people over 75 years old in the People's Republic of China,” and “If anyone wants to wish the People's Republic of China a happy birthday, do not use the word ‘motherland.’” This “motherland theory” has caused controversy on the island and has been criticized by all walks of life. What is your comment?\nAnswer:\nLai Ching-te's remarks substitute concepts and confuse right and wrong. By highlighting political differences across the Strait and deliberately severing the historical connection between the two sides, he continues to peddle his “new two-state theory” of “mutual non-subordination between the Republic of China and the People's Republic of China,” and seeks to control the national identity and ethnic identity of Taiwan compatriots. Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” fallacy, old wine in a new bottle, once again exposes his unrepentant “Taiwan independence” stance and his sinister intention to escalate hostility and confrontation.\nTaiwan is China's sacred territory; its historical lineage is clear and its legal facts are plain. On October 25, 1945, the Chinese government declared the “restoration of the exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan.” On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. This was a change of regime while China, as a subject of international law, did not change. China's sovereignty and inherent territory have not changed, and the Government of the People's Republic of China naturally enjoys and exercises full sovereignty over China, including sovereignty over Taiwan.\nAlthough the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided and will not be divided. The fact that the Mainland and Taiwan belong to one China has never changed and will not be changed. No matter what “historical paradoxes” or “Taiwan independence fantasies” Lai Ching-te puts forward, they cannot change the objective fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and they cannot extinguish the sense of motherland among Taiwan compatriots. We hope broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will fully recognize the Lai Ching-te authorities' schemes to seek “independence,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and effectively safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241008_12654836.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-10-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the US government recently approved military assistance worth about US$567 million for the Taiwan region of China, mainly for training, anti-armor, drones and other programs. What comments do you have on this?","The US side, disregarding China’s firm opposition, insists on providing military assistance to the Taiwan region of China. This seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously endangers China’s sovereignty and security interests, and seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We strongly condemn this and have lodged solemn representations with the US side.\nIn recent years, the US side has acted in bad faith and, by all means, repeatedly provided military aid and arms sales to Taiwan. It has sent serious erroneous signals to ‘Taiwan independence’ forces, fanned the flames on the Taiwan question, escalated regional tensions, and step by step pushed Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war and disaster. It must be emphasized that arming Taiwan is abetting ‘Taiwan independence’, ‘Taiwan independence’ means war, and ‘using Taiwan to contain China’ will only backfire.\nWe urge the US side to stop facing China with ‘two faces’, to abandon its two-faced approach on the Taiwan question, and to stop arming Taiwan, so as not to cause further interference with and damage to China-US relations and military-to-military relations. The People’s Liberation Army of China has always strengthened its training and combat readiness and comprehensively enhanced its ability to win battles. It resolutely counters and strikes back against ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist activities and external interference, and firmly defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.news.cn/20241009/56437f270e744789a2ce5afb5321e43e/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-10-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council Answers Reporters' Questions\n(October 9, 2024)\nQuestion: It has been reported that Tsai Ing-wen will soon make a visit to European countries such as the Czech Republic. What is your comment?\nAnswer:\nThe DPP authorities, under various pretexts, carry out \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and deceive the international community. No matter what they say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the fate of \"Taiwan independence\" being a dead end, and do not help peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait or the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We urge relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle, handle the Taiwan question with prudence, not send wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and not provide any platform for them to spread \"Taiwan independence\" separatist fallacies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241009_12655042.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-10","Mao Ning","AFP","Leader of the Taiwan region Lai Ching-te delivered a speech today, stressing that there must be no “annexation or encroachment” upon Taiwan’s sovereignty. What is China’s comment?","Lai Ching-te’s words attempt to sever the historical connections between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. He is again peddling various versions of “Taiwan independence” narrative, such as “China and Taiwan are not subordinate to each other” and “Taiwan has sovereignty.” It once again exposed that he is hellbent on advancing “Taiwan independence” and has the ill intention of heightening tensions in the Taiwan Strait for his selfish political interest.\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. No matter what they say or do, the Lai Ching-te authorities cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, or stop the historical trend that China will and must achieve reunification. The attempt to seek independence and make provocations will lead nowhere.\nThe one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and prevailing international consensus. Taiwan has never been a country and will never be a country, and thus has no so-called sovereignty. Upholding the one-China principle, opposing “Taiwan independence” and opposing “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan” is our consistent position on the Taiwan region’s external exchanges and participation in international activities.\nLet me stress once again that China opposes all forms of official interactions between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic relations with China, and interference in China’s internal affairs in any way and under any excuse. We urge the few foreign politicians who visit Taiwan to correct their wrong words and deeds, stop meddling in China’s internal affairs, and stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” and heightening tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495612.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495379.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-10","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 10 — In response to the content on cross-Strait relations in the so-called “Double Ten” speech that Lai Ching-te delivered in Taipei on the 10th, Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said in answer to questions that in his speech, Lai Ching-te continued to advocate the “New Two-State Theory” of “mutual non-subordination,” fabricated “Taiwan…","Chen Binhua said that realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is the greatest dream of the Chinese nation since modern times, and it has always been closely related to the future and destiny of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. After the Opium War of 1840, in order to defeat foreign aggression, win national liberation and achieve national reunification, generations of Chinese people fought heroic and moving struggles. Mr. Sun Yat-sen took the lead in calling out “Revitalize China,” led the Revolution of 1911 to success, and explored a path toward realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Taiwan has been a sacred territory of China since ancient times. In modern times it was occupied by foreign aggressor forces, and the people of Taiwan suffered greatly. In 1945, the Chinese people won the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan, and Taiwan was subsequently restored. After 1949, due to the continuation of the Chinese civil war and interference by external forces, the two sides of the Strait fell into a special state of long-term political confrontation. However, Taiwan has always been part of China’s territory, Taiwan compatriots have always been members of the Chinese nation, the government of the People’s Republic of China has always been the sole legal government representing all of China, including Taiwan, China has always been the great motherland of all Chinese people, and adhering to the one-China principle has always been the common consensus of the international community.\nHe pointed out that different systems are not an obstacle to reunification, much less an excuse for separation. The current struggle against “Taiwan independence” separatism is not a contest of systems, but a struggle between reunification and separation. Lai Ching-te has schemed to fabricate pretexts for splitting the country, forcibly indoctrinated his “Taiwan independence” position, repeated the old tune of “democracy against authoritarianism,” and, under the pretext of so-called “democracy and freedom,” continued to “rely on foreign forces to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence,” attempting to tie Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot. His provocations to seek “independence” are the root cause and source of chaos for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and will bring disaster to the people of Taiwan.\nChen Binhua said that under the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China, the people of all ethnic groups across the country have worked with united effort and courage, ushering in a bright prospect for realizing national rejuvenation. The ideals for which countless martyrs and sages have striven have become reality on the land of China. At present, we are closer than at any period in history, and have more confidence and capability, to achieve the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and we are also more confident and capable of making new and greater contributions to the noble cause of world peace and development. Taiwan’s future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Regardless of what Lai Ching-te says, it cannot change the legal status of Taiwan as part of China or the fact and reality that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. We have the confidence and capability to achieve the complete reunification of the motherland. No one and no force can stop the historical trend of national rejuvenation and national reunification. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference schemes, actively promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, continue to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and resolutely advance the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241010_12655319.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-11","Mao Ning","AFP","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken held a press conference in Vientiane today. He said that China shouldn’t use Taiwan’s national day speech as a pretext for provocative action. What is China’s comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The key to keeping the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable lies in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence.” The US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495616.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495386.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-11","Mao Ning","China Review News","On October 10, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a decision on its website to take countermeasures against three US military companies and ten senior executives. Do you have any further comment?","China firmly opposes US arms sales to China’s Taiwan region. The US has, once again, provided China’s Taiwan region with huge military aid recently, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982. Such sale seriously interferes in China’s internal affairs, and gravely undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In accordance with China’s Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law, China decided to take countermeasures against relevant military companies and senior executives of the US.\nI would like to stress that “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with peace of the Taiwan Strait as fire with water. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ attempt to reject reunification through the use of force is futile. No matter how many weapons they buy, they cannot stop the historical trend toward China’s reunification. The US’s decision to help advance that independence agenda by arming Taiwan will only push Taiwan towards the danger of military conflict. No matter how many weapons it sells, it will not shake our resolve to oppose “Taiwan independence” and defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. China urges the US to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming the Taiwan region in any form and stop conniving at and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We will continue taking strong and resolute measures to defend our national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495616.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495386.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, October 12 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 12th: Regarding the relevant departments' study of further measures based on the conclusions of the investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan, we express strong support.\nShe pointed out that responsibility for this situation lies entirely with the Taiwan side. The direct cause is that since the investigation was launched, the DPP authorities have taken no improvement measures to lift trade restrictions on the mainland. The fundamental cause is that the DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” undermining the political foundation of cross-Strait consultation and making it difficult to resolve cross-Strait trade disputes through consultation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241012_12655786.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-14","Mao Ning","AFP","China has announced that it is conducting military drills in the waters around Taiwan. Could the Foreign Ministry give us more information on the specific goal and content of the drills? Could you please tell us when the drills will end? How does the Ministry respond to those voices claiming that China is undermining regional peace and stability?","What you asked about is not related to China’s foreign affairs and I’d refer you to competent authorities. What I can tell you is that “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with cross-Strait peace as fire with water, and provocations by “Taiwan independence” forces will be responded with countermeasures. China has always been committed to maintaining regional peace and stability, to which countries in this region bear witness. For anyone who cares about peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, they need to stand against “Taiwan independence” first and foremost.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495389.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-14","Mao Ning","NHK","The Spokesperson of the US Department of State expressed serious concerns over the military drills. What’s your comment on that?","Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. If the US truly cares about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and regional prosperity, it needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan,and stop sending any wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495389.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-14","Mao Ning","The Paper","From October 11 to 14, Premier Li Qiang paid an official visit to Laos and Viet Nam. Could you share with us the details and major outcomes of the visit?","Laos and Viet Nam are China’s socialist friends and neighbors. This is Premier Li Qiang’s first visit to the two countries after he took office, which produced fruitful results.\nFirst, demonstrating the strategic importance of building the community with a shared future. The Lao side stressed that the Lao party, government and people have, as always, viewed China as their close and good neighbor, friend, comrade and partner. The Vietnamese side highlighted that the Vietnamese party and government have, as always, viewed its relations with China as the strategic choice and top priority in its foreign policy. China shared the view with Laos and Viet Nam that their respective development offers opportunities to the other country’s development and is a positive factor in regional and global development. We agreed to continue approaching the bilateral relations from a strategic height and long-term perspective, firmly support each other in advancing the cause of socialism and exploring modernization with respective characteristics, deliver on the important common understandings between the top leaders of our parties and countries, and achieve more practical progress in building a community with a shared future.\nSecond, reaffirming the principled position on major issues. Both Laos and Viet Nam reaffirmed their firm commitment to the one-China principle, their firm opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form, and their firm support for the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative and the Global Civilization Initiative. The three sides believed it’s important to oppose bloc confrontation, power politics, and unilateralism in any form, and agreed to step up coordination and collaboration in multilateral mechanisms, actively conduct cooperation under the above-mentioned three initiatives, and advocate an equal and orderly multipolar world and a universally beneficial and inclusive economic globalization.\nThird, agreeing to deepen comprehensive strategic cooperation. China and Laos will continue advancing the synergy between Belt and Road Initiative and Laos’ strategy of transition from a land-locked to a land-linked country, expanding practical cooperation in various areas, such as trade, investment, industrial capacity, electricity and minerals, speeding up the development along the China-Laos Railway and the implementation of “juxtaposed border control,” and delivering more tangible progress in China-Laos cooperation across the board. China and Viet Nam will enhance the synergy of development strategies, strengthen the “physical connectivity” of railway, highway and port infrastructure, and the “institutional connectivity” such as smart customs, and provide stronger underpinning to boost trade and investment facilitation and keep supply chains stable and unimpeded. We actively look into building pilot cross-border economic cooperation zones and expand cooperation in emerging areas, including information technology, new energy, digital economy and important minerals. Both China and Viet Nam will host events in celebration of the 75th anniversary of the establishment of bilateral diplomatic relations and the China-Viet Nam Year of People-to-People Exchanges in 2025.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495389.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-10-14","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that Lai Ching-te recently delivered a so-called “Double Ten” speech, hyping the “new two-state theory” that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other”, and smearing mainland China’s “invasion and annexation” of Taiwan. On October 14, the PLA Eastern Theater Command organized the “Joint Sword-2024B” exercise. Senior U.S. officials said China has no reason to exert…","Wu Qian: Lai Ching-te and his ilk have forgotten their ancestors and deliberately severed the historical ties across the Taiwan Strait, wildly stirred up hostility and confrontation between the two sides, and sought to confuse and change the facts and perceptions that Taiwan and the mainland belong to one China. This fully exposes their true face as “destroyers of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises.” We will absolutely not tolerate this, and we must counter it. Taiwan is China's sacred territory; its historical record is clear, its legal basis and facts are unambiguous, and it is widely recognized by the international community. Taiwan has never been a country and will never become one. The independence-seeking schemes and provocations of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, and interference by external forces, are the root cause of the disruption of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and will only bring disaster to the Taiwan people.\nThe PLA's exercises are precisely aimed at “Taiwan independence.” We want to make “Taiwan independence” elements understand in language they can grasp that the sword hangs over their heads, and that independence-seeking means a dead end. It must be pointed out that this exercise is not aimed at Taiwan compatriots. We wish to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we will never leave even the slightest room for “Taiwan independence.” “Joint Sword-2024B” is not a repetition of 2024A but a step up in pressure aimed at “Taiwan independence.” Each time “Taiwan independence” provokes, the PLA's actions will advance one step further, until the Taiwan question is completely resolved.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no one or force may interfere in any way, by any means, or under any pretext. Relevant parties should stop tolerating and supporting “Taiwan independence” and stop undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. National reunification is an irresistible trend of history and an unshakable national imperative. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will grasp the trend of history, see clearly where the future lies, stand on the right side of history, and join us in opposing independence and promoting reunification, sharing the supreme glory of national unification and national rejuvenation.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16345356.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-10-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 14 — State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua said on October 14 that, after carefully verifying and screening clues submitted by people on both sides of the Strait to the TAO's “Taiwan independence” diehard clue reporting mailbox, it has decided to impose punishment in accordance with law on Shen Boyang, Tsao Hsing-cheng, and “Black Bear Academy.”","Chen Binhua stated: After verification, the “Black Bear Academy,” under the support of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and external interference forces, under the guise of “lectures,” “training,” “outdoor drills,” and even “parent-child activities,” has openly cultivated “violent ‘Taiwan independence’ elements” and blatantly engaged in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. It is an absolute “Taiwan independence” base. Shen Boyang, as head of the “Black Bear Academy,” has organized and planned “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, vigorously promoted “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, maliciously peddled “Taiwan independence” propositions and “anti-China” ideology to Taiwan residents, especially young people, and widely spread the seeds of violent conflict in the Taiwan Strait. Tsao Hsing-cheng has provided huge financial support for the “Black Bear Academy” in carrying out criminal activities to split the country, vigorously advocated “resisting unification by force” and “the whole people as soldiers,” and invested in and backed the production of “Taiwan independence”-themed film and television dramas, instilling the spiritual poison of “opposing China and plotting independence” in various ways. Shen and Tsao’s “Taiwan independence” ideas are stubborn, their “independence”-related remarks are outrageous, their “independence”-plotting conduct is vile, and they arbitrarily “lean on outsiders to resist China.” They are blatantly splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country, seriously endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nChen Binhua stated that the mainland side has decided to list Shen Boyang and Tsao Hsing-cheng as “stubborn ‘Taiwan independence’ elements,” impose sanctions on the “Black Bear Academy,” Shen Boyang, and Tsao Hsing-cheng, prohibit Shen, Tsao, and their family members from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions, restrict cooperation between the “Black Bear Academy” and its affiliated institutions, as well as Shen and Tsao, and mainland-related organizations and individuals, and absolutely not allow their affiliated enterprises and financial backers to profit on the mainland. In accordance with the relevant provisions of the “Opinions on Punishing ‘Taiwan Independence’ Stubborn Elements in Accordance with the Law for the Crime of Splitting the Country and Inciting the Splitting of the Country,” we will also take all other necessary punitive measures and hold them accountable for life in accordance with the law.\nChen Binhua emphasized that for “Taiwan independence” stubborn elements and “Taiwan independence” bases whose words and actions involving “independence” are vile and whose activities plotting “independence” are rampant, we absolutely will not tolerate or appease them, and will certainly strike hard and punish them severely. We welcome enthusiastic members of the public, especially Taiwan compatriots, to continue actively providing new clues about the criminal activities of the “Black Bear Academy,” Shen Boyang, and Tsao Hsing-cheng in splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country.\nChen Binhua stated that in the face of the historical trend of national rejuvenation and the reunification of the motherland, “Taiwan independence” elements will ultimately pay a painful price for what they have done. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will open their eyes wide, recognize the extreme danger and harmfulness of “Taiwan independence,” voluntarily draw a clear line between themselves and the “Black Bear Academy” and “Taiwan independence” stubborn elements such as Shen Boyang and Tsao Hsing-cheng, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, and work hand in hand with compatriots on the mainland to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, and create lasting well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241014_12656119.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 14 – Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 14th that today the Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People's Liberation Army organized forces from the theater's army, navy, air force, and rocket force, positioned in the Taiwan Strait, northern Taiwan Island, southern Taiwan Island, and east of Taiwan Island, to carry out…","Chen Binhua said that national reunification is an irresistible historical trend and an unchallengeable matter of national righteousness. Our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is as firm as a rock, our ability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is invincible, and our actions to punish those plotting “independence” provocations and to crush separatist schemes are resolute and forceful. Our countermeasures target the separatist conduct of “Taiwan independence” diehards and interference by external forces, and they are by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will uphold national righteousness, follow the historical trend, fully recognize the extreme danger and harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, firmly safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, and join hands with mainland compatriots to jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241014_12656241.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-15","Mao Ning","AFP","Pentagon Press Secretary stated on Monday that the People’s Liberation Army (PLA) exercise around Taiwan yesterday is irresponsible, disproportionate, and destabilizing. What’s China’s comment?","Relevant information has been released by competent Chinese authorities. Let me stress that Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. To truly uphold cross-Strait peace and stability, one must unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495633.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495392.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-15","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","The Japanese Deputy Cabinet Secretary said today that Japan had expressed its concerns about the drills around Taiwan and that it also scrambled fighter jets around the island of Yonaguni, which is very close to the west side of the island of Taiwan. Did China inform the Japanese government before they conducted the drills either from the military or from the coast guard so that there will be no concern for the…","Relevant information on that has been released by competent Chinese authorities, and I just made clear China’s position. I’d refer you to competent authorities for more information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495633.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495392.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-10-15","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the US Government Accountability Office recently accused Raytheon of fraud in the 2013 “Patriot” missile system procurement case and the 2017 radar system procurement case, involving selling overpriced missiles and radars to Taiwan. KMT-affiliated elected representatives in Taiwan sharply criticized the conduct of US arms dealers as being like a fraud syndicate. What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to the Taiwan region of China. It should be pointed out that the relevant reports only reveal the tip of the iceberg. In recent years, the DPP authorities have done everything they can to flatter, and have repeatedly begged their American masters to buy weapons. A great deal of the islanders' hard-earned money has been squandered, yet what they have received is a pile of scrap metal. Those who have been fattened are a group of corrupt officials and arms dealers, and this has aroused growing opposition and dissatisfaction among the island's people.\n“Sky-high prices” and “obsolete goods” are the two “famous trademarks” of US arms sales to Taiwan. From moldy bulletproof vests to expired ammunition, and then to missile radars with inflated prices, it is clear that in the eyes of the Americans there is only “American interests.” “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and outsiders cannot be relied upon. Those who attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence” will ultimately bring about their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16345898.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-10-15","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华15日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 15 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions on the 15th, saying that since Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly adhered to the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist position and has continuously piled up, escalated and loudly promoted his ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist propositions. Whether it was the…","Chen Binhua pointed out that Lai Ching-te, in his speech, claimed that “the Republic of China has already taken root in Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu.” This is a deliberate attempt to sever the historical connection between the two sides of the Strait, hollow out the meaning of One China, and seek to turn the so-called “Republic of China” into “Taiwan independence” in essence, using the name of the so-called “Republic of China” to carry out “Taiwan independence” in reality, which is deceptive and misleading. By making the “two-state theory” from an abstract concept concrete and clear, covering multiple aspects such as the economy and society, he is instilling its “Taiwan independence” position into the public and putting it into practice, mobilizing society to pursue separatist “Taiwan independence.” By claiming “mutual non-subordination” and promoting so-called “Taiwan sovereign independence,” he is changing the nature of cross-Strait relations, openly challenging the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, and seeking to promote a disguised “de jure Taiwan independence.” By claiming that “the People's Republic of China has no right to represent Taiwan” and that Taiwan must go to the world, he is challenging the basic structure of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle and the post-World War II international order, intensifying efforts to “internationalize the Taiwan question,” begging external forces to endorse its “Taiwan independence” acts, and his “rely on outsiders to seek independence” malice is plainly evident. Lai Ching-te's words and deeds are peddling the “two-state theory” and inciting “Taiwan independence” separatism! He is deliberately provoking and undermining cross-Strait relations! Where is any “moderation” or “goodwill”? Lai Ching-te is a thorough “Taiwan independence worker” and “peace saboteur.”\nChen Binhua said that the current struggle against “Taiwan independence” separatism is, in essence, a struggle against separatism and for safeguarding national unification. The series of resolute and forceful countermeasures we have taken in recent days is a just act by a sovereign state to punish acts that attempt to split the country and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity; it is also a firm safeguard of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and of the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities that with every provocation by the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, our punishment and countermeasures will advance a step further, until complete reunification of the motherland is achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241015_12656577.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-16","Mao Ning","NHK","A report released by the US Center for Strategic and International Studies on October 15 said that next year Beijing could use the 20th anniversary of its Anti-Secession Law to revise the law and justify Taiwan’s unification through military means. Do you have any comment on that?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495636.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495396.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","In his “Double Ten” speech, Lai Ching-te said that “the People’s Republic of China has no right to represent Taiwan,” and said he would “deepen Taiwan’s cooperation with the international community.” What is your comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the government of the Republic of China as the sole legitimate government representing all of China. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted at the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly in 1971, restored the representation and seat of all of China, including Taiwan, to the government of the People's Republic of China on the premise of recognizing that Taiwan belongs to China. Taiwan's status as part of China has never changed and never can change. The People's Republic of China naturally represents the Taiwan region, and has always represented the Taiwan region.\nLai Ching-te's setting “China” against “Taiwan” is an out-and-out separatist “Taiwan independence” stance. Lai Ching-te's advocacy of so-called “cooperation with the international community” is aimed at “seeking independence by relying on outside powers.” Internationally, it seeks to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan.” What it exposes is his stubborn “Taiwan independence” nature, what it damages is China's sovereignty, and what it challenges is the basic framework of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle. We hope the international community will not be misled or deceived by Lai Ching-te and will recognize his true intention of pursuing “Taiwan independence” and presumptuously attempting to challenge the post-World War II international order.\nChina has always been a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, and a guardian of the international order. At present, we are closer than at any time in history to, and more confident and capable of, realizing the goal of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and we are also more confident and capable of making new and greater contributions to the noble cause of human peace and development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656824.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台华语环球节目中心《中国新闻》记者","The Mainland Affairs Council said that Lai Ching-te’s so-called “October 10” speech reaffirmed expectations for the restoration of equal, healthy and orderly exchanges across the Strait, and called on the mainland to properly understand his goodwill. What is your comment?","We have consistently supported and promoted dialogue and consultation across the Taiwan Strait on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. Adhering to the concept of “one family across the Strait,” we actively respond to the common voice of compatriots on both sides who want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and have adopted a series of measures to actively promote exchanges between compatriots on both sides.\nLai Ching-te stubbornly maintains the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly advocates the “new two-state theory” of “mutual non-subordination.” Under the premise of denying that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, he seeks so-called “equal exchanges,” which is merely changing tactics and deceiving public opinion, and is in no way well-intentioned. In fact, for some time, the DPP authorities, for the private interests of their party and themselves, have stopped at nothing to obstruct and restrict cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. This includes using the so-called “national security concerns” as a pretext to vigorously suppress and obstruct the normal contacts of compatriots on both sides, and carrying out a “green terror” on the island, depriving people from all walks of life of their freedom of travel. These are the real obstacles to normalizing cross-strait personnel exchanges and regularizing exchanges and cooperation.\nWho is truly promoting exchanges and seeking well-being for compatriots on both sides, and who is saying one thing and doing another, broad Taiwan compatriots have clear eyes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Some in the pan-green camp on the island said that Lai Ching-te’s so-called “Motherland Theory” explains cross-Strait issues using “ROC logic,” and goes beyond the old “Taiwan independence” faction’s “nation-building theory” of “deconstructing the Republic of China and establishing the Republic of Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te's remarks are a “historical paradox” that swaps concepts, a “Taiwan independence fantasy” with muddled logic, and a separatist fallacy that puts old wine in new bottles. Their purpose is to change disguises and add another layer of camouflage, using the old shell of the so-called “Republic of China” to market its new “Taiwan independence” arguments, deceiving public opinion and fooling the people.\nTaiwan has never been a country, and it will never become a country. Whether it is the “ancestral land theory” or the “nation-building theory,” both are separatist fallacies of “Taiwan independence.” Any words or deeds that challenge the one-China principle or attempt to split the country are destined to fail, and any words or deeds that constrain Taiwan compatriots' national and ethnic identity or intensify cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism will not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656818.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Mr. Ma Ying-jeou recently said in a speech that Taiwan should not become a pawn. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China. Cross-Strait issues should be discussed by the two sides themselves; they cannot and should not be handled through others, and foreign interference must not be allowed. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. They share the same roots and origins, the same culture and the same ethnicity, and they are a family whose blood is thicker than water. The historical fact and legal basis that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and that compatriots on both sides belong to one nation have never changed and cannot change. Matters internal to China are, of course, to be resolved by the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait themselves, and they have the wisdom to do so. There is no need for outsiders to meddle, and external forces must not be allowed to interfere. Compatriots on both sides should join hands and hearts, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and, on the basis of the one-China principle, through dialogue and communication, pool wisdom, seek common ground while setting aside differences, and strive to resolve political confrontation at an early date, achieve lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait, and complete the great cause of national reunification. Let our descendants grow up and live in a shared homeland that is harmonious, peaceful, prosperous, and dignified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656823.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Minister of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that the crux of cross-Strait issues lies in the mainland's unwillingness to face the fact that the \"Republic of China\" exists, and that the goal of \"annexing Taiwan\" has not changed. He said Taiwan will not submit to \"the Chinese military threat.\" What is your comment on this?","The crux of the current cross-Strait issue lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities' stubborn adherence to a “Taiwan independence” position. They advocate the “new two-state theory,” incite hostile confrontation across the Strait, constantly make trouble and provoke, and deliberately aggravate tensions. This has brought war and danger to Taiwan and harmed the interests of Taiwan's people.\nUnification is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. It is the future of Taiwan and the interest of Taiwan's compatriots. It must not be smeared or slandered, and it certainly cannot be obstructed or resisted. The Lai Ching-te authorities have long attempted, by hyping up the “mainland threat” and using so-called “democracy and freedom” as a pretext, to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “seek independence by force.” They are trying to tie Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and coerce the people of Taiwan into becoming “Taiwan independence cannon fodder.”\nWe are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force. This is directed at external interference and at a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. It is by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan's compatriots. We hope that Taiwan's compatriots will recognize the true “Taiwan independence” face and the extreme harmfulness of the Lai Ching-te authorities, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and earnestly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656817.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's retired major general and former chairman of the Huang Fu-hsing Party Branch of the KMT, Tsang Yu-hsia, was fined by the DPP authorities for attending an event in Hong Kong and had his monthly retirement pension suspended for five years. What is your comment?","Driven by its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have vigorously suppressed dissenting forces on the island and repeatedly used pretexts to persecute people who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, which we strongly condemn. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan's compatriots will clearly recognize the grave harm of the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and “green terror,” and resolutely oppose their perverse actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视直新闻记者","The U.S. arms manufacturer Raytheon has been exposed for multiple instances of inflated prices and fraud in arms sales to Taiwan, and Taiwan's defense authority has confirmed that this is indeed the case. Koo Li-hsiung said, “The U.S. government itself is also a victim.” Island public opinion points out that the DPP authorities have absolutely no room to bargain, and all losses will ultimately have to be borne by…","The United States' sale of weapons and equipment to Taiwan seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and seriously damages China's sovereignty and security interests. Raytheon has repeatedly participated in arms sales to Taiwan, and we have imposed sanctions on it. This incident fully exposes the ugly face and pitiful plight of the DPP authorities: for the sake of their party's own interests, they squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwan people, willingly serve as the US's “cash machine,” and, even after being cheated, still make excuses for the party that harmed them. We believe more and more islanders have seen clearly that “relying on the US” only “harms Taiwan,” and that “using force to seek independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","Before the National Day “Golden Week” holiday, the mainland announced that over a thousand scenic spots would waive admission fees for Taiwan's “first-time visitors,” which was widely welcomed by the public on the island. The DPP authorities, however, called the mainland's measure a “united front act.” What is your comment?","On September 30, 1,256 Grade A scenic spots on the Chinese mainland launched promotional activities for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. Taiwan compatriots who apply for a Taiwan compatriot permit for the first time (issuance count 01) are exempted from or receive reductions in ticket fees for visiting the scenic spots within one year. The activities were warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. It is understood that during the National Day “Golden Week” holiday, many Taiwan compatriots enjoyed discounts at the above scenic spots. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to travel to the mainland, and we are also glad to see more scenic spots offering ticket discounts for Taiwan compatriots visiting, continuously improving their travel experience.\nRegarding the preferential policy measures for Taiwan issued by the mainland, the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces habitually label them “united front activities.” It is necessary to set the record straight here. The full name of “united front” (统战) is “统一战线” (united front). During the War of Resistance, it was precisely through KMT-CPC cooperation, which established an anti-Japanese national united front, that the whole nation's military and civilians, united in hatred of the enemy and resolute in purpose, fought bloody battles, defeated the Japanese invaders, and won the great victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japan. Taiwan was thereby restored, ending its tragic history of being occupied and colonized by foreign powers. The united front has always been an important instrument for the Communist Party of China to unite hearts and gather strength. In the new era and on the new journey, the main task of the united front is to adhere to great unity and great solidarity, continuously consolidate and develop the broadest patriotic united front, and widely gather all the wisdom and strength of the Chinese nation, forming a vivid situation in which all Chinese people at home and abroad are of one mind and jointly contribute to the great cause of national rejuvenation.\nTaiwan compatriots are part of the Chinese nation. We will continue to unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, do practical good deeds for them, help them solve difficulties, gather their wisdom and strength, and jointly contribute to the great cause of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656822.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, the mainland announced that it would impose punishment on Shen Boyang, Tsao Hsing-cheng, and the \"Black Bear Academy\" in accordance with the law. The DPP authorities said the mainland is \"coercing and intimidating\" the Taiwan people and \"undermining the free and democratic society.\" What comments do you have on this?","With the support of the DPP authorities and external interfering forces, the \"Black Bear Academy\" openly fosters \"violent Taiwan independence elements\" and blatantly engages in \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. Shen Boyang and Tsao Hsing-cheng hold stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" ideas, make arrogant pro-independence remarks, engage in vicious pro-independence conduct, and recklessly \"rely on foreign powers to resist China.\" They blatantly split the country and incite the splitting of the country, seriously endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Our announcement of sanctions against them has full factual and legal basis, and is a just measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and safeguard the vital interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nWhat we punish in accordance with the law is the extremely small number of stubborn elements who engage in vicious pro-independence words and actions and rampant pro-independence activities, and their crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country. It does not involve the broad Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities deliberately confuse the public and distort and smear the facts, and by fabricating false narratives of so-called \"mainland threat\" and \"democracy and freedom,\" they deceive the public at home and cling to outside forces abroad. This cannot conceal the nature and conduct of their undermining of cross-Strait relations and splitting of the country. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will open their eyes, see through the sinister intentions of the \"Taiwan independence\" forces in inciting cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, consciously draw a clear line with the stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" elements, and join mainland compatriots in promoting cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, safeguarding our shared Chinese national home and creating lasting well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656820.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","The Ministry of Commerce recently issued an announcement that, based on the conclusions of its investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan, it will study taking further measures. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said, “The mainland is using economic and trade as a political weapon to coerce Taiwan into submitting to its political positions.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities have for a long time unilaterally restricted the import of large quantities of mainland products, harming the interests of relevant mainland industries and enterprises. This is an objective fact. Since the relevant department released its final conclusion on the trade barrier investigation concerning Taiwan, the DPP authorities have not only taken no practical measures to lift trade restrictions on the mainland, but have become even more extreme, obstructing normal cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation and harming the interests of mainland enterprises and the well-being of the people. Our study of further measures based on the conclusion of the trade barrier investigation is a necessary response to the DPP authorities’ obstinate and unrepentant attitude and conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656819.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","On October 1, the first local regulation on Taiwan-related matters in the cultural field, the “Fujian Province Regulations on the Protection of Fujian-Taiwan Relations Archives,” formally took effect. Please briefly introduce the relevant details.","On July 24 this year, the Standing Committee of the Fujian Provincial People's Congress adopted the “Fujian Province Regulations on the Protection of Min-Taiwan Relations Archives,” which took effect on October 1. This is the mainland's first special local regulation on Taiwan-related matters in the cultural field, and the first special provincial-level legislation on Taiwan-related matters since the issuance of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.”\nFujian is the main ancestral home of Taiwan compatriots. In the course of exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan, a large number of Min-Taiwan relations archives with rich content have been formed. These archives attest to the historical origins of the two sides of the Strait, reflect the course of cross-Strait exchanges, and carry the memory of the Chinese nation. They are historical proof that both sides of the Strait share the same roots, the same culture and ancestry, and belong to one China. At present, a large number of Min-Taiwan relations archives are scattered among the people. It is very necessary and meaningful to further strengthen their protection and utilization and to establish this in the form of legislation.\nThe “Regulations” have 25 articles. They set out the definition and scope of Min-Taiwan relations archives and make provisions on the legislative purpose, protection principles, safeguard mechanisms, responsible entities, division of responsibilities, and protection and utilization. In particular, on protection and utilization, the “Regulations” propose measures such as promoting shared use of resources, increasing research and development efforts, and advancing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. These are of important significance for deepening the revitalized use of Min-Taiwan relations archives, safeguarding the shared bloodline, shared culture and shared history of both sides of the Strait, promoting spiritual affinity between compatriots on both sides, and strengthening their identification with the country, the nation and the culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait cultural and tourism exchange activities.","In terms of film and television exchanges, the 4th IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival was successfully held in Pingtan, Fujian, from October 11 to 13. A total of 2,264 short films and 256 feature films were submitted, the highest number of entries in the festival’s history. In the end, 9 works from Taiwan made it into the top 50, and 4 of them won awards. The IM Cross-Strait Film Festival has become the largest-scale and highest-level youth film exchange activity across the Strait. On this platform, young directors from both sides have interacted through their works and deepened understanding.\nIn terms of cultural exchange, the game “Black Myth: Wukong” has become a hit among young people across the Strait, breaking out of its niche. Recently, the Straits Economic and Technological Cooperation Center and the Shanxi Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office jointly organized the inaugural group of the “Taiwan Youth Exploration of Sanjin Culture” tour, “Viewing ‘Jin’ Ancient Architecture, Seeking ‘Wu’ History.” Themed around “Black Myth: Wukong,” the tour visited ancient buildings and historic sites in Shanxi, tasted treasures of Chinese culture, reflected on the lineage of the national spirit, and immersively experienced the charm of China’s excellent traditional culture. It received an enthusiastic response from Taiwan youth.\nIn terms of tourism exchange, from September 26 to 28, Zhuhai held the “Beautiful China · Zhuhai Journey” visit event, inviting more than 70 tourism operators from counties and cities across Taiwan. The event linked cities in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area. It carefully designed and launched four themed tourist routes for Taiwan compatriots. During the event, industry representatives from both sides signed a framework agreement on friendly cooperation in tourism exchanges. We warmly welcome and support the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots in taking part in cross-Strait cultural and tourism exchanges and cooperation. We welcome more Taiwan youth to come to the mainland and personally experience the charm of China’s excellent traditional culture. We will continue to create better conditions and provide better services for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","After the escalation of the situation in Lebanon, among the personnel evacuated by China was one Taiwan compatriot, who said in an interview that he had always known that his homeland is China, and that he did not only come to think so when being evacuated. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides are all Chinese, and safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots is our duty. For a long time, we have always attached great importance to protecting the safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. From providing consular document services to assisting in handling civil disputes and economic and criminal cases involving Taiwan abroad; from evacuations from Libya, Yemen, and Sudan, to the outbreak of the Israel-Palestine conflict and Taiwan compatriots overseas facing dangers such as typhoons and earthquakes, we have maintained close contact with Taiwan compatriots locally and provided timely assistance. I want to stress once again: no matter where they are or what difficulties they encounter, the great motherland will always be a strong backing for broad Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","On the 75th anniversary of National Day, many Taiwan entertainers have expressed their blessings in various ways. What is your comment?","On the occasion of the 75th anniversary of the founding of New China, many Taiwanese entertainers spontaneously posted congratulatory remarks on internet media and social platforms and reposted related images, expressing their pride and sense of honor as members of the Chinese nation and as Chinese. We highly appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The United States keeps hyping up the so-called “Chinese military threat,” advocates that Taiwan enhance its self-defense capabilities, and continues to sell arms to and provide military aid for Taiwan. The DPP authorities, cooperating with the US side, hype up strengthening “self-defense forces,” saying they will cultivate 400,000 civilian forces across Taiwan to participate in “whole-of-society defense.” What…","Everything the United States says and does is aimed at selling weapons to Taiwan in order to serve its domestic military-industrial complex. It has absolutely nothing to do with protecting the Taiwan people or being for Taiwan's good. Some in the United States should not underestimate the danger and recklessness of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities' secessionist schemes for \"Taiwan independence,\" and even less should they underestimate China's firm will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nSince the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have wanted to pursue \"independence\" yet are timid and fearful at heart, and so they have wholeheartedly become \"pawns\" of external forces, cooperating with the United States to turn Taiwan into a \"porcupine of war,\" regardless of pushing the Taiwan people into the abyss of disaster. Now they are also engaging in a so-called \"whole-of-society defense,\" attempting to coerce all Taiwan people onto the \"Taiwan independence\" bandwagon and make them victims of their secessionist schemes. \"Taiwan independence\" is a scourge and a dead end, but the \"Taiwan independence\" forces cannot turn the tables or accomplish anything. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: if they attempt to \"seek independence by relying on the United States\" or \"seek independence by force,\" they are seeking their own dead end and bringing about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656816.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","The Ministry of Commerce recently announced further measures based on the conclusions of its investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan. Taiwan's “Economic and Trade Office of the Executive Yuan” responded that the mainland side should follow WTO rules for consultation to resolve disputes, and should not be treated as “the worst example of disrupting international trade order.” What comment do you have?","In accordance with the non-discrimination principle of the WTO and relevant mainland regulations, the relevant departments conducted a trade barrier investigation into the trade restriction measures the Taiwan region has imposed on the mainland, and reached a conclusion that they constitute trade barriers. Taking further measures based on the investigation’s conclusion is legitimate, lawful, fair, and reasonable.\nThe DPP authorities, on the one hand, obstinately hold to the “Taiwan independence” stance, constantly provoke by seeking “independence,” interfere with and undermine cross-Strait economic, trade, and exchange cooperation, and slander and smear the mainland, inciting cross-Strait confrontation. On the other hand, they claim they are willing to consult and dialogue with the mainland. This is a typical double-dealing tactic. They are the “worst example.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, results of the island media's “Annual Survey on Cross-Strait Relations” showed that 54% of the public believe that remarks by Lai Ching-te such as “the Republic of China and the People's Republic of China are not subordinate to each other, and we absolutely do not accept the ‘1992 Consensus’” do more harm than good to cross-Strait relations; 87% of the public believe it is necessary for both sides to…","This opinion poll once again indicates from one perspective that the mainstream public opinion on the island is: to want peace rather than war, development rather than decline, exchange rather than separation, and cooperation rather than confrontation. The DPP authorities ignore public opinion and go against the tide, continuously peddling separatist fallacies such as the “new two-state theory” of “mutual non-subordination,” repeatedly colluding with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, and forcibly obstructing normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This pushes up tensions across the Taiwan Strait, undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, goes against popular sentiment, and will surely be condemned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Some public opinion on the island points out that Lai Ching-te advocates the so-called “new two-state theory” and insists on the “Taiwan independence” line, and is an out-and-out “troublemaker.” What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, out of selfish partisan interests, stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, package and peddle the so-called “mutually non-subordinate” “new two-state theory,” incite hostile confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, attempt to “rely on foreign forces to seek independence” and “seek independence through force,” seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Broad Taiwan compatriots must recognize the deceptiveness and harmfulness of Lai Ching-te’s remarks, and recognize Lai Ching-te’s true face as a “Taiwan independence worker” and “peace wrecker.” Through practical actions, they must resolutely oppose and stop Lai Ching-te’s “Taiwan independence” provocations and risky adventures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","The DPP authorities’ “representative to the United States” recently told a US media outlet in an exclusive interview that, to ease the delays in US arms sales to Taiwan, Taiwan and the US have begun dialogue on jointly producing and developing weapons, and plan to produce or assemble in Taiwan the arms purchased from the US, making Taiwan a link in the military supply chain. What comment do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop “arming Taiwan,” stop military cooperation with Taiwan's military, and stop encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to seek “independence by force.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how many troops Taiwan has or how many weapons it acquires, and no matter whether external forces intervene, if they dare to take a desperate risk, they will surely bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: People on both sides of the Strait seem to feel “worry and numbness” about military exercises. For example, stock markets on both sides of the Strait were not significantly affected by this exercise. Public opinion polls in Taiwan also show that the public hopes to “maintain the status quo.” How does the Taiwan Affairs Office respond? Second question: “Joint Sword-2024B” has ended, but mainland…","Question one: On that day, Taiwan stocks fell sharply, causing nervousness and concern among investors and drawing attention and discussion from all sectors of Taiwan society. This is a fact. Peace, development, exchange and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. Lai Ching-te's provocations for 'independence,' deliberately escalating cross-Strait tensions and endangering peace in the Taiwan Strait, run counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island. This too is a fact.\nQuestion two: As long as 'Taiwan independence' provocations continue, our actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not stop for a moment.\nQuestion three: Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. China Coast Guard law enforcement patrols in Chinese waters are meant to maintain operational order in the relevant waters and to protect the lives, property and legitimate rights and interests of Chinese fishermen, including Taiwanese fishermen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","台湾联合报记者","Question one: The Ministry of Commerce recently issued an announcement that it is studying further measures based on the conclusions of its investigation into trade barriers against Taiwan. What specific measures will or may the mainland take? Question two: The Taiwan Affairs Office said that after carefully verifying and screening information reported by people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to the mailbox…","On your first question: since the relevant mainland departments issued the final conclusion of the investigation into cross-Strait trade barriers, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have not only failed to take substantive measures to remove discriminatory trade measures against the mainland, but have escalated them, maliciously obstructing normal cross-Strait economic, trade, and cooperative exchanges. This has damaged the interests of relevant mainland industries and enterprises and forced the mainland to suspend part of the tariff concessions on Taiwan products under ECFA. We firmly support the competent authorities in studying further measures in accordance with relevant regulations, based on the conclusion of the investigation into cross-Strait trade barriers. As for what measures, please stay tuned.\nOn your second question: since we set up a reporting mailbox for \"Taiwan independence\" diehards, people on both sides of the Strait have responded to this just act of punishing \"independence\" in accordance with the law with concrete actions, and we have so far received hundreds of reporting leads. For reports from the public, we will work with the relevant departments to carefully verify and screen them. As for how they are verified, that is our internal work.\nOn your last question: regarding the remarks made in Matsu by the person you mentioned. I want to stress that the \"1992 Consensus\" is the clear path and the right way; there is no need to create a \"1926 Consensus.\" What they should do is carefully review the glorious history of consultations between the two sides' organizations that produced results, benefited the people on both sides, and promoted the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, find the right answer, and not start from scratch.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The island's “five shortages” problem has not been resolved, and now a “new five shortages” has emerged: “shortage of electricity, shortage of talent, shortage of infrastructure, shortage of the ability to resolve cross-Strait tensions, and shortage of the willingness of overseas partners to give practical commitments.” Taiwan's industry says that since Lai Ching-te took office he has provoked the mainland and…","The \"five shortages\" that Taiwan's economy has long faced could have been addressed by strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development. The Taiwan Industry Federation recently released a white paper of policy recommendations for industry, which clearly stated: \"The mainland has to date been the main source of Taiwan's trade surplus, its largest investment destination, and its most important trading partner. Given that the two sides are geographically close, share a language, and have the same culture, there is no reason not to engage in dialogue, communication, and cooperation.\" This fully reflects the eager expectation of Taiwan's business community and of people in all trades for the normalization of cross-Strait exchanges and the regularization of cooperation.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities obstinately hold to the \"Taiwan independence\" position, constantly stirring up confrontation across the Strait, pushing for economic decoupling, industrial supply-chain severance, and the cutting off of personnel flows. This seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It not only worsens Taiwan's \"five shortages\" problem, but also creates a sixth shortage: the \"lack of stability.\" Facts have already proven, and will continue to prove, that pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" means no peace, and Taiwan will have no development.\nQuestion from Bloomberg (US):\nUS media have reported that Tsai Ing-wen may travel to the United States before the US presidential election. What is the spokesperson's comment?\nAnswer: We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between any country that has diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","During the National Day “Golden Week” holiday, group tours and individual tours by mainland residents to Kinmen have resumed, bringing renewed liveliness to the Kinmen customs clearance building, and was warmly welcomed by local residents. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Since the resumption of the travel endorsement for mainland residents to visit Kinmen, the market response has been enthusiastic. It is reported that several thousand mainland residents have applied for documents to travel to Kinmen. During the National Day Golden Week holiday, the Xiamen-Kinmen “Small Three Links” route was suspended due to a typhoon. After it resumed on October 4, a tour group of 120 people departed from Xiamen for Kinmen on the 5th and was warmly welcomed by local residents. These all show that compatriots on both sides of the Strait eagerly look forward to stronger exchanges. The DPP authorities should promptly cancel the unpopular “group tour ban” and create conditions for the revival of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","Taiwanese actor Wu Kang-jen recently signed with a mainland Chinese agency, which has drawn public attention. Online users have revealed that Wu once took part in the “Sunflower” movement and have questioned whether his “stance is problematic.” What comments do you have on this?","We have consistently encouraged and supported strengthening civil exchanges across the Strait in all fields. For Taiwan compatriots, including youth, grassroots people, and performing artists, if they previously had a vague understanding of cross-Strait relations, said wrong things, or even did wrong things, we welcome them as long as they draw a clear line with “Taiwan independence,” recognize the one-China principle, recognize that they are Chinese, are willing to take part in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and are willing to come to the mainland for exchanges and development. We will work to help them develop well and realize their dreams, provide a stage for them, and increase our support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241016_12656815.htm"],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","Several political parties and civic groups on the island recently held an event in New Taipei City, calling for a clear line to be drawn from “Taiwan independence” forces and expressing their desire and determination for peace, exchanges, opposition to war, and joint promotion of reunification. What is your comment on this?","The views of relevant Taiwan political parties and groups reflect the deep concern of the island’s public about the dangers of war in the Taiwan Strait, and their strong aspiration for peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and for exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides. They demonstrate a sense of national righteousness and align with the mainstream public opinion on the island. We highly appreciate them.\nHow cross-Strait relations develop concerns the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Lai Ching-te constantly fabricates “Taiwan independence” fallacies, promotes separatist positions, incites hostility and confrontation across the Strait, and deliberately aggravates cross-Strait tensions. He seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and will bring disaster to Taiwan’s public. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriot population can see through his deception and the harm it causes, firmly oppose provocations to seek “independence,” and, together with compatriots on the mainland, push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-16","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that, based on clues received through the reporting mailbox, it has imposed punishment in accordance with the law on Shen Boyang, Tsao Hsing-cheng, and the \"Black Bear Academy.\" Will the authorities regularly release relevant information based on reported clues in the future?","Punishing Shen Boyang, Tsao Hsing-cheng, and “Black Bear Academy” in accordance with the law is a just act of punishing “independence” in response to the voices of people on both sides of the Strait. It is a powerful penalty and a resolute crackdown on the provocations of “Taiwan independence” forces seeking “independence.” Our resolve to safeguard national sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock, our will to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes is unwavering, and our capability is invincible. We will continue to punish stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with the law for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country. Stubborn provocations to seek “independence” will certainly bring painful costs.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241016_12656802.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-17","Mao Ning","China Daily","It’s reported Taiwan announced the official operation of its newly established office in Mumbai, India, which will be the third office Taiwan has set up in the country. What’s China’s comment?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China strongly opposes all forms of official contact and interaction between Taiwan and countries having diplomatic relations with China, including the establishment of representative offices for each other. We have lodged solemn representations to the Indian side.\nThe one-China principle is a serious political commitment made by the Indian side and serves as the political foundation for China-India relations. China urges the Indian side to strictly abide by the commitments it has made, prudently and properly settle the Taiwan-related issues, not to conduct any form of official interaction with Taiwan and avoid disturbing the process to improve the China-India relationship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495639.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495403.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-18","Mao Ning","Reuters","Could the Foreign Ministry confirm whether it asked South Africa to close the “Taiwan representative office” in the country?","The one-China principle is the political foundation for China to establish and grow diplomatic relations with other countries in the world. It is also a universally recognized norm in international relations and where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. We commend South Africa’s right decision to move the Taipei Liaison Office in South Africa outside the administrative capital Pretoria. “Taiwan independence” finds no support from the people and will only fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495646.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495406.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-18","Mao Ning","China Review News","It’s reported that Timor-Leste’s President Jose Ramos-Horta in a recent interview responded to criticisms from Western countries over the close relations between Timor-Leste and China and the Chinese mainland’s “ aggressive ” actions in the Taiwan Strait. He said Western criticism was steeped in hypocrisy, adding that “it’s the Chinese helping us,” “Long before we were born as an independent state, the whole…","We noted relevant report and highly commend President Jose Ramos-Horta’s remarks. His words once again show that upholding the one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and is where global opinion trends and the right thing to do. The vast majority of countries and international and regional organizations stand firmly with the Chinese government and the Chinese people. The abiding commitment of the international community to the one-China principle is unshakable. The Chinese people’s just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving for national reunification will enjoy wider and wider understanding and support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495646.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495406.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-21","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","It’s reported that on October 20, a US destroyer and a Canadian frigate made a transit of the Taiwan Strait. What’s China’s comment?","On the US and Canadian warships’ transit through the Taiwan Strait, the PLA Eastern Theater Command has made a response. Let me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is not about freedom of navigation but about China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We firmly oppose any act of provocation under the pretext of freedom of navigation that threatens China’s sovereignty and security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495654.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495409.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-21","Lin Jian","Reuters","US presidential candidate Donald Trump made a series of remarks about his relationship with Chinese leader and how he thinks China would view US support for Taiwan during an interview over the weekend. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","As we’ve said more than once, we have no comment on US presidential elections and oppose anyone in the US making China an issue in the presidential elections. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495654.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495409.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-23","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s Defense Ministry said it is monitoring a Chinese aircraft carrier passing through the Taiwan Strait. Can China confirm this? And a follow-up to that, Taiwan defense minister referring to the military drills earlier this month today said an actual blockade would be an act of war. Does China have any comment on this?","Taiwan is a province of China. There is no so-called “defense ministry” or “defense minister” of Taiwan. What you asked about is not about foreign affairs either. Taiwan is part of China’s territory. It is just normal for China’s aircraft carrier to carry out relevant activities.\nLet me stress that whatever the Taiwan authorities say or do, they cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Nor can they change the trend that the two sides of the Strait will and must be reunified.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495667.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495423.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-25","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwanese leader Lai Ching-te visited Kinmen today and he said in a speech that he “would not yield an inch of ground in defense of Taiwanese territory.” What is the Ministry’s comment on Lai’s visit and his remarks?","Taiwan is part of China’s territory. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China will not change, and the historic trend that the two sides of the Strait will and must be reunified will never be reversed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495435.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-25","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","We’ve learned that head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs office Lin Chia-lung is visiting Guatemala and Guatemalan President Bernardo Arévalo will meet with him. What is your comment on this?","We noted the reports. Let me stress that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. On this day 53 years ago, the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 that restored the lawful seat of the People’s Republic of China in the UN. The fact that 183 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China fully proves that the Taiwan authorities’ attempt to use countries having so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan for political manipulation and “Taiwan independence” agenda will lead nowhere. It will not shake the prevailing consensus on the one-China principle, or stop the overriding trend towards China’s reunification.\nMore and more people with vision in Guatemala are aware that establishing diplomatic relations with China is in the fundamental and long-term interests of Guatemala and its people. We hope the Guatemalan government will see this trend, meet its people’s aspirations, and make the right choice at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495435.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-25","Lin Jian","AFP","The Wall Street Journal reported today that Vladimir Putin had asked Elon Musk not to activate his Starlink satellite internet service over Taiwan and that he asked this as a favor to China. Can the Ministry confirm this and does the Ministry have a comment on this?","I’m not aware of what you mentioned.\n******************************************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495435.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-10-25","Lin Jian","The following question was raised after the press conference","On this day 53 years ago, the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 and restored the lawful seat of the People’s Republic of China at the UN. For some time, some in the world have spread claims that “the Resolution did not make a determination on the status of Taiwan” and supported Taiwan’s “meaningful participation” in the UN events. Could I have your comment on this?","On October 25, 1971, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 with an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all the rights of the People’s Republic of China at the UN, to recognize the representatives of the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China to the UN, and to expel forthwith the representatives of the Taiwan region from the UN and all the organizations related to it. Once and for all, the resolution resolved the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the UN. It made clear that there is no such thing as “two Chinas,” or “one China, one Taiwan.” As an inalienable part of China’s territory, Taiwan does not have any ground, reason, or right to join the UN, or any other international organization whose membership is confined to sovereign states. On this matter of principle, there is no gray zone or room for ambiguity.\nIn recent years, some forces in the West have deliberately distorted UNGA Resolution 2758, falsely claimed that “the Resolution did not make a determination on the status of Taiwan,” and emboldened and supported “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, which has seriously harmed peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Let me stress once again that any move that attempts to deny the one-China principle and undermine the authority and efficacy of Resolution 2758 turns back the wheel of history, challenges the post-war international order, and is doomed to failure. China will and must realize reunification. This is an overwhelming trend of history that no one or force can stop.\nThe restoration of the lawful seat of the People’s Republic of China at the UN is of great significance to China and has a far-reaching impact on the UN and the world. For 50 plus years, China has all along worked in solidarity with people from all countries, upheld international fairness and justice, and made important contribution to the cause of the UN and world peace and development. China has also upheld the authority and sanctity of the UN, and deepened its cooperation with the UN in various areas. Going forward, China will stay committed to peaceful development and to reform and opening up, create new opportunities for the world through our own development, and work with other parties to uphold the founding mission of the UN, practice true multilateralism, build a community with a shared future for mankind, and create a better world.\nLinks:","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495676.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495435.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 25 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated in response to a question on the 25th that the Lai Ching-te authorities obstinately adhere to a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance and blatantly promote their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist propositions, advocating the \"new two-state theory\" of \"mutual non-subordination.\"…","Zhu Fenglian said that Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland was a victory achieved through the joint resistance of all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots. It demonstrates the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and it is worth commemorating and celebrating together by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nShe pointed out that in 1894, Japan launched the First Sino-Japanese War to invade China, and the following year forced the defeated Qing government to cede Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. On December 1, 1943, the governments of China, the United States, and the United Kingdom issued the Cairo Declaration, which clearly declared that the purpose of the three countries was that Japan be stripped of all the territories it had stolen from China, such as Northeast China, Taiwan, and the Penghu Islands, and that they be returned to China. On July 26, 1945, the Potsdam Proclamation, jointly signed by China, the United States, and the United Kingdom and later joined by the Soviet Union, reaffirmed that “the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” In September of the same year, Japan signed the Instrument of Surrender, promising to “faithfully fulfill the obligations of the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation.” On October 25, the Chinese government announced the “resumption of exercising sovereignty over Taiwan” and held the “China Theater Taiwan Province Surrender Ceremony” in Taipei. Thus, through a series of documents with international legal effect, China recovered Taiwan both legally and in fact. On the 79th anniversary of Taiwan's return to the motherland, compatriots on both sides of the Strait commemorate this major historical event in various ways, which is of great significance for remembering the heroic deeds of revolutionary martyrs, reviewing the historical achievements of compatriots on both sides of the Strait in jointly resisting foreign aggression, and carrying forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance.\nZhu Fenglian said that the Taiwan question arose from the weakness and turmoil of the Chinese nation and will inevitably come to an end with the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. She hoped that the broad Taiwan compatriots will remember the history of Taiwan's martyrs' resistance against Japan, deeply understand the great significance of Taiwan's restoration, recognize the essence and harm of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' pursuit of “Taiwan independence” separatism, uphold a correct view of history, nation, and state, and join mainland compatriots in advancing the process of national reunification, sharing the dignity and glory of a great country and taking pride in being upright and honorable Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241025_12658717.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 26 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 26th, pointing out that October 25 marks the 79th anniversary of the Restoration of Taiwan. The restoration of Taiwan and its return to the motherland is an important achievement of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, in winning the victory of the…","Chu Feng-lien said that “Taiwan independence” has no future. Taiwan's future lies in the complete reunification of the motherland and in the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The history of Taiwan's return to China must not be forgotten, and the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the two sides of the Strait cannot be stopped. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will, with a sense of responsibility to history and the nation, follow the trend of history, stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and join us in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and pursuing a beautiful future of peaceful reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241026_12658786.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, October 27 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 27th and pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have tried to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence,”…","Zhu Fenglian said: We firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. The US side has repeatedly gone back on its leader's commitment of “not supporting Taiwan independence,” abetting reckless “Taiwan independence” adventurism and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose this and urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” to stop arming Taiwan, and to stop sending any wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241027_12658983.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-10-29","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s “ministry of defense” has signed formal agreements with the US allowing it to buy attack drones from two companies. This is to aid in the island’s defense. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment on this deal?","Taiwan is a province of China and there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s ministry of defense.” China’s firm opposition to the military contact between the US and Taiwan is consistent and clear. The two US companies you mentioned and relevant senior executives in charge are under sanctions by China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495695.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495455.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the TAO press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping emphasized during his recent inspection in Fujian that Fujian must continue to take greater steps in exploring a new path for the integrated development of the Taiwan Strait. Build the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone well. Promote cross-Strait cultural exchanges, jointly carry forward Chinese culture, and enhance the national identity, cultural identity, and…","We will thoroughly study and implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech during his inspection in Fujian, and fully advance the implementation of the 《Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development》, achieving new progress and new results, and producing a batch of landmark outcomes.\nFirst, take greater steps in improving the cross-Strait integrated development policy system. At present, the National Immigration Administration, the Ministry of Education and other departments have issued a series of policy documents supporting the construction of the Fujian Demonstration Zone, further granting authorization and empowerment for its construction. Fujian Province has issued three batches of 45 policy measures, making them tangible and accessible to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, providing reassurance and comfort, and fully reflecting the mainland's sincere intention to do practical and good deeds for Taiwan compatriots. Next, we will continue to study and issue a batch of new supporting policy measures, continuously improve and introduce innovative measures, create better conditions for more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop in the Demonstration Zone, and share more development opportunities.\nSecond, take greater steps in implementing equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Fujian has thoroughly implemented the first batch of 225 equal-treatment items, abolished temporary residence registration for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian, and realized “settle wherever they wish” for Taiwan compatriots settling and registering household in Fujian; launched the digital “First Home” service platform, basically realizing “one-stop query” and “all-online handling” services for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian; a batch of Taiwan compatriots obtained corresponding mainland skill certificates by directly recognizing Taiwan professional qualifications; a batch of Taiwan compatriots serve as heads of social organizations and as arbitrators, mediators, jurors, etc.; a batch of Taiwan compatriots were equally honored with various levels and types of awards, so that Taiwan compatriots have greater assurance in employment and entrepreneurship in Fujian, broader participation in Fujian's social life, and the “First Home” for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises coming to the mainland is widely recognized. Next, we will launch more social integration projects and grassroots governance positions that facilitate Taiwan compatriots' participation, expand the number of Taiwan-funded enterprises joining the “Fujian Time-honored Brands” and “China Time-honored Brands”, accelerate building the “same-city living circles” of Xiamen–Kinmen and Fuzhou–Matsu, encourage schools, hospitals and research institutions to hire more Taiwan compatriots, and continue to implement residents' treatment for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian in buying homes, universal elderly care, emergency assistance for those temporarily in difficulty, and enrollment in the “five social insurances and one housing fund”, so that Taiwan compatriots are willing to come, able to stay, able to integrate, and able to develop well.\nThird, take greater steps in promoting integrated economic development between Fujian and Taiwan. To date, Fujian has cumulatively attracted more than 25,000 Taiwan-invested projects, actually utilizing over 33 billion US dollars of Taiwan investment; cross-Strait trade between Fujian and Taiwan has cumulatively exceeded 1.5 trillion yuan, economic and trade cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan has grown steadily, financial cooperation has developed innovatively, and the mutual recognition of industry standards continues to advance; the Demonstration Zone has become one of the most closely connected regions for cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. Next, we will study and issue special measures to relax market access to promote Fujian-Taiwan integrated development, continue to support key Fujian–Taiwan integrated development projects, promote full connectivity of infrastructure between Fujian and Taiwan, and work to build a three-dimensional, comprehensive hub of channels for Taiwan. We will further optimize the business environment for Taiwan-related affairs in Fujian, deeply advance the Xiamen comprehensive reform pilot, establish the Fuzhou–Matsu industrial cooperation zone, build the Pingtan cross-Strait common market pioneer zone, improve the cross-Strait standards mutual recognition service platform, deepen cooperation in Fujian–Taiwan advantageous industries, and provide Taiwan businesses and enterprises with more development opportunities and greater development space.\nFourth, take greater steps in expanding cultural and people-to-people exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan. This year, Fujian has cumulatively held more than 200 important Taiwan-related exchange events, with over 25,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots participating, and the Demonstration Zone has become the most active region for civil exchanges across the Strait. A series of brand events welcomed and beloved by compatriots on both sides, including the 16th Straits Forum, the 12th Straits Youth Festival, the Cross-Strait Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament, and the cross-Strait compatriots' Mid-Autumn Festival gathering, have become important platforms and carriers promoting exchanges, mutual understanding and integration among people on both sides, bringing compatriots closer together. Next, we will continue to consolidate cultural bonds across the Strait, and expand exchanges on ancestor-seeking and pilgrimage, and exchanges among clansmen, fellow townsmen and in-law relatives. We will continue to implement the project to display and trace Fujian–Taiwan historical origins, carry out the protection and utilization of archival documents on Fujian–Taiwan relations, and innovate ways and means of promoting traditional Chinese culture, so that the foundation of cross-Strait integrated development becomes more solid and its momentum stronger, and so that the spiritual affinity of compatriots on both sides increasingly becomes vivid reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659832.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, senior officials of the Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation have made statements denying the “1992 Consensus.” Lo Wen-chia, Secretary-General of the SEF, said that the “1992 Consensus” cannot be found in SEF archives or correspondence, and that the “1992 Consensus” is already outdated and a more forward-looking framework is needed to discuss the future of cross-Strait relations.…","The historical background and important role of the “1992 Consensus” are very clear.\nIn October 1992, ARATS and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan held working-level consultations in Hong Kong on the issue of “cross-Strait notarial certificate use.” During these consultations, the two sides each proposed expression schemes on how to express their adherence to the one-China principle in cross-Strait affairs consultations. Among them, the Eighth Scheme (oral) proposed by SEF of Taiwan read: “In the process of both sides of the Taiwan Strait jointly striving for national unification, although both sides adhere to the principle of one China, they have different understandings of the meaning of one China.” ARATS believed that this scheme demonstrated the attitude of the Taiwan authorities and SEF in pursuing unification and adhering to the one-China principle. Therefore, after SEF's letter confirmed its expression scheme, ARATS, in its reply letter, put forward the key points of ARATS's oral expression: “Both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle and strive for national unification. However, in cross-Strait affairs consultations, the political meaning of one China is not involved.” ARATS also attached SEF's Eighth Scheme to the letter as an annex. SEF's reply letter raised no objection to this. Thus, the two sides reached a consensus that each orally expresses that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle,” which was later called the “1992 Consensus.” Although the “1992 Consensus” is an oral expression by each side, both its process and content have clear documents and written records, as solid as iron and fully traceable.\nThe core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and jointly strive for national unification.” The “1992 Consensus” is important because it clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations: the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and cross-Strait relations are neither “state-to-state relations” nor “one China, one Taiwan.” This not only conforms to objective facts but also aligns with the relevant current regulations of both sides, allowing both sides to set aside differences, establish mutual trust, and open the door to exchanges and dialogue. The essence of the “1992 Consensus” is seeking common ground while putting aside differences: seeking the great common ground of one China while setting aside the minor differences across the Strait, fully demonstrating that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have the ability and wisdom to properly resolve their own problems.\nThe “1992 Consensus” laid the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. It is precisely because of this political foundation that cross-Strait negotiations could be launched, cross-Strait party exchanges could be promoted, and institutionalized cross-Strait consultation and liaison mechanisms could be established. It is precisely because of this political foundation that comprehensive, direct, two-way “Three Links” could be realized, opening a new era of large-scale exchanges, interactions, and cooperation in economic, social, cultural, and other fields, greatly enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. It is precisely because of this political foundation that arrangements for Taiwan's participation in activities of international organizations such as the World Health Assembly and the International Civil Aviation Organization could be made reasonably and appropriately. It is precisely because of this political foundation that in 2015 the first meeting between leaders of both sides since 1949 took place, with direct dialogue and communication between the leaders on both sides, bringing cross-Strait political interaction to a new height. Since 2016, the DPP authorities have stubbornly maintained a “Taiwan independence” position and continuously distorted, or even denied, the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermining the political foundation of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Their purpose is only one: to dogmatically pursue “Taiwan independence.”\nHistorical facts fully prove that when the one-China principle is upheld, cross-Strait relations can improve and develop, and Taiwan compatriots benefit; when the one-China principle is abandoned, cross-Strait relations become tense and turbulent, harming the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the anchor that keeps peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Any remarks that deliberately distort history, deny the important role of the “1992 Consensus,” or claim that the “1992 Consensus” is outdated do not help improve and develop cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659831.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Could the spokesperson introduce recent cross-Strait cultural exchange activities?","We actively support cross-Strait cultural exchanges and encourage compatriots on both sides to jointly promote Chinese culture. Here are several recent cross-Strait cultural exchange activities.\nFrom October 23 to 25, the first Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit was successfully held in Beijing. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, and Wei Xiaodong, Chairman of the Beijing Municipal Committee of the CPPCC, attended the opening ceremony and delivered speeches. Liu Chao-hsuan, Chairman of the Taiwan Chinese Culture Sustainable Development Foundation, and more than 200 Taiwan guests attended. Under the theme “Inheritance, Promotion, and Development,” the summit held an opening ceremony and a literary main forum, along with 7 sub-forums, including a cultural and creative forum, a cross-Strait quyi masters dialogue, a Four Seas Culture Forum, a cross-Strait calligraphy and painting masters dialogue, a film forum, a television forum, and a cross-Strait clan culture forum. It also featured quyi performances, an exhibition of works by cross-Strait calligraphy and painting masters, a performance of the drama “Seeking Flavor” (《寻味》), and visits and exchange activities, achieving a series of positive results.\nFrom October 22 to 24, the 2024 Chinese Ji Gong Culture Festival was held in Tiantai, Zhejiang Province. More than 700 believers from both sides of the Strait, as well as Malaysia, Thailand, and other places, attended, including more than 400 Taiwan guests. The festival included activities such as the 815th anniversary memorial ceremony of Ji Gong's enlightenment in the Jiachen year and a tour of Ji Gong's hometown sacred sites. It guided believers to understand and promote the Ji Gong culture of selfless altruism, helping the poor and the needy, and standing up against injustice, as well as the spirit of harmony, and strengthened the affection, friendship, and kinship of compatriots on both sides.\nFrom October 20 to 28, the 5th season of the “Shu Show on the Palm” cross-Strait new media experience activity was held in Sichuan. Under the theme “Seeking Beauty on the Sichuan-Tibet Highway,” the activity invited more than 40 media practitioners from both sides of the Strait to visit and shoot at 20 points along the Sichuan-Tibet Highway. Covering a distance of more than 1,500 kilometers, the participants fully displayed the beauty of mountains and rivers, culture, industry, and the Sky Road through text and images, short videos, and live streams along the route. It drew wide attention from people on both sides, especially Taiwan youth.\nIt is worth mentioning that using songs and short dramas to portray cross-Strait youth exchange stories has become a highlight of cultural exchanges this year. Xiamen Television, China Taiwan Network, and the All-China Taiwan Affairs Federation's Taiwan Compatriot Home jointly produced the original song “Waiting for You to Come Home,” which blends Mandarin and Hokkien to convey homeland feelings through the local dialect and sing of the sincere hope for cross-Strait reunion. The Yunnan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office and the Yunnan Branch of China News Service created the song “Yuntai Ballad” based on the love story between a Tibetan youth of Shangri-La and a youth from Taoyuan, Taiwan, and produced a 5-episode micro short drama, “Dreaming of Shangri-La,” conveying the steadfast and lasting strength of cross-Strait youth exchanges.\nI would like to preview two cultural exchange activities. On October 31, the 5th Cross-Strait Media Summit will be held in Beijing. The theme of this summit is “Cross-Strait Media Integrated Development Under a New Changing Landscape,” and representatives from cross-Strait media and academia have been invited to attend.\nFrom October 31 to November 3, the 15th Straits (Xiamen) Cultural Industries Fair and Trade Expo will be held in Xiamen. This year's fair highlights the inheritance of cultural ties, with relevant people from both sides competing on the same stage to promote the integrated development of cross-Strait cultural and creative design. During the fair, activities such as cross-Strait folk artist exchange dialogues and a cross-Strait youth city walk will also be held. We welcome journalist friends to cover the event then.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659824.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Before the National Day holiday, the mainland announced that over 1,000 scenic spots would reduce or waive admission fees for Taiwan “first-time travelers,” which was widely praised by people on the island. Are there any new scenic spots participating in this promotional activity?","It is understood that, following more than 1,200 scenic spots on the mainland launching promotional activities for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland, another batch of mainland scenic spots has announced that Taiwan compatriots holding Taiwan Compatriot Permits for the first time may visit the scenic spots within one year free of admission fees. These include 70 AAAAA-rated scenic spots such as the Hulunbuir Grassland Scenic Area in Inner Mongolia, the Longmen Grottoes in Henan, the Huangshan Scenic Area in Anhui, the Huashan Scenic Area in Shaanxi, the Emei Mountain Scenic Area in Sichuan, and the Qinghai Lake Scenic Area in Qinghai, as well as 725 AAAA-rated scenic spots such as the Shenyang Imperial Palace in Liaoning and the Chinese Wushu Garden at Jingwumen in Tianjin. To date, nearly 2,500 mainland scenic spots in total have launched promotional activities for Taiwan \"first-time visitors.\" Taiwan \"first-time visitors\" can learn in a timely manner about the scenic spots' fee-reduction and exemption measures through the scenic spots' websites, entrance signage, and relevant travel agencies. The catalogue of scenic spots (AAAAA and AAAA) launching the second batch of promotional activities will be published on the WeChat official account \"Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\"\nWe warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to travel to the mainland, and we are also pleased to see more mainland scenic spots adopt preferential measures for Taiwan compatriots' sightseeing, continuously enhancing the travel experience of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659823.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》栏目记者","October 25 marks the 79th anniversary of Taiwan’s Restoration Day. Although the DPP authorities have deliberately downplayed and denied the historical significance of Taiwan’s restoration, all sectors on the island and civil groups have commemorated the day and called for restoring “Taiwan Restoration Day” as a statutory holiday. What is your comment on this?","The restoration of Taiwan to the motherland was a victory won through the joint resistance of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and is worth commemorating together by compatriots on both sides. Instead of commemorating the restoration of Taiwan, the Lai Ching-te authorities have repeatedly promoted and glorified the history of foreign colonization of Taiwan by the Netherlands, Japan, and others, in order to construct a “Taiwan independence view of history” and fabricate a historical basis for its “new two-state theory.” This is an open denial of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the world anti-fascist war, a serious desecration of the enormous national sacrifices made by compatriots on both sides, and a typical case of forgetting one's ancestry and being a disgrace to the nation.\nWe note that recently, multiple groups and people from all walks of life on the island have commemorated this major historical event in various ways, mourning the heroic deeds of the martyrs, highlighting the historic achievements of compatriots on both sides in jointly resisting external aggression, and promoting the great spirit of the War of Resistance. Taiwan compatriots have a glorious tradition of patriotism. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots, starting from national righteousness, will uphold a correct view of history, nation, and state, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, and work together with compatriots on the mainland to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and pursue a bright future of peaceful reunification, sharing the dignity and glory of being Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659827.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, some people on the island pointed out that Shi Muming, executive director of the Tainan Confucius Temple Cultural Foundation, took advantage of his position to promote “Taiwan independence” awareness in Confucius Temple guided tours, questioning whether “the Confucius Temple is becoming a ‘Taiwan independence’ temple.” What is your comment on this?","Chinese culture is the root and the sense of belonging of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Confucius was a great thinker of ancient China, and Confucianism is an important cornerstone of traditional Chinese culture. Confucian temples are important venues for commemorating Confucius, passing on Confucian thought, and promoting Chinese culture. The Confucian temples across Taiwan originated on the mainland, which proves that both sides share the same roots, the same culture, and the same ethnicity. The “Taiwan independence” forces on the island, using various means and schemes, pursue “gradual Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization,” attempting to weaken and sever Taiwan's ties with the mainland, erase the imprint of Chinese culture in Taiwanese society, dilute the Chinese national consciousness of Taiwan compatriots, change the fact that both sides belong to one China, and interfere with and undermine the development of cross-Strait relations. Their intentions are malicious and the harm is enormous. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will join us in resolutely opposing “independence” and promoting reunification, strengthen confidence in Chinese culture, safeguard our common homeland of the Chinese nation, create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and contribute to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan's “representative” to the US recently told US media, “Taiwan's people are ready to fight” and “do not need US military help,” which drew condemnation from all walks of life on the island. Some public opinion holds that such “war-provoking” remarks are detrimental to Taiwan's situation and to cross-Strait relations, needlessly increase risks for Taiwan, and escalate cross-Strait tensions. What is your…","These remarks once again expose the ugly face of the Lai Ching-te authorities, which, for the sake of narrow partisan interests, are willing to turn Taiwan into a battlefield and bind the Taiwan public to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot. In recent period, from allocating NT$647 billion in defense budget to purchasing U.S. weapons at high prices; from establishing the so-called \"Whole-of-Society Defense Resilience Committee\" and agitating to train 400,000 militia members, to covertly supporting the \"Black Bear Academy,\" and even demanding that high school students sign \"wartime youth service consent forms\"; from plotting to stockpile ammunition in temples to discussing stockpiling food and medical supplies... all of this fully shows that the Lai Ching-te authorities are accelerating \"preparing for war to seek independence.\" If they are allowed to persist recklessly, Taiwan will only face greater danger of war.\nAs the DPP authorities' escalating provocations to seek \"independence\" have led to the disastrous consequences of a tense and turbulent cross-Strait situation, Taiwan's people are seeing more and more clearly and are increasingly voicing their call to oppose \"Taiwan independence\" and pursue peace. The DPP authorities must face up to the mainstream public opinion on the island, stop \"seeking independence through force,\" and stop \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659825.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, various places on the mainland have held colorful economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, various localities, focusing on implementing the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee, have held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities in diverse forms and with rich content, achieving good results.\nFocusing on strengthening cross-Strait technology and industry cooperation, and encouraging Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop new quality productive forces according to local conditions, activities such as the 27th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum and the 5th Cross-Strait (Shaanxi) Economic, Trade and Science and Technology Cooperation Conference were held. These guide and support Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises to integrate into high-quality development, seize the opportunities of high-standard joint construction of the Belt and Road, and achieve better and faster development.\nFocusing on strengthening cross-Strait agricultural and characteristic industry cooperation, activities such as the 2024 Guizhou-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cooperation Exchange Symposium and the Liaoning-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Week were held. These encourage the central, western and northeastern regions to leverage their resource endowments and industrial advantages, and guide Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to shift production capacity to and optimize their layouts in the central, western and northeastern regions.\nFocusing on deepening integrated development and helping Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises expand domestic markets, activities such as the 19th Gan-Taiwan (Lushan) Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation and Exchange Conference, the 18th Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week, and the 15th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo were held. Among them, the Gan-Taiwan Conference signed 34 Taiwan-invested projects, the Hubei·Wuhan Taiwan Week signed 46 projects, and the Dongguan Taiwan Expo had 423,000 person-times of participation both online and offline.\nThese activities have continuously strengthened their function as windows for enhancing mutual understanding and exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, fully played their role as platforms for promoting cross-Strait industrial cooperation and integrated development, and fully expressed the shared voice of compatriots on both sides who want peace, development, exchange and cooperation. They have continuously injected positive energy into promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Liang Wenjie, deputy head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that “one China,” as discussed by the “National Unification Council” and the “National Unification Guidelines,” is a historical fact, but that nearly 70% of Taiwan's residents currently agree that “the Republic of China has taken root in Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu, and is not subordinate to the People's Republic of China.” He said…","It must be emphasized that One China is not only history, but also present reality and fact. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people, including the 23 million Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan’s future can only and must be decided jointly by all Chinese people. The DPP authorities, under the pretext of so-called “freedom,” hijack public opinion and drag ordinary Taiwan people in as cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence.” Their intentions deserve condemnation, and their conduct is shameful. We believe the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots have a clear understanding of this, will not be deluded, and will not be coerced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Luo Wen-jia, Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that the foundation will give two sika deer named “Hehe” and “Pingping” to the Fuzhou Zoo, and asked for the relevant details to be introduced. Luo said he hopes the two sides can move toward a path of peace rather than a path of hatred. What comments do you have on this?","Giving gifts requires sincerity. Rather than showing off insincerely, it is better to do some practical things. Returning to the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and acknowledging the basic fact that both sides belong to one country and one nation, the cross-Strait two agencies can conduct communication and consultation to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said at the Tamsui District, New Taipei City branch of the Coast Guard Fleet that over the next seven years, 11 large vessels of more than 1,000 tons will be completed, so that everyone will have better equipment to face various forms of threats more safely, and will have more confidence in safeguarding the “national territory and maritime boundaries.” What comment do you have on this?","It must be pointed out that Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called “national territory and maritime frontier.” The Lai Ching-te authorities' collusion with external forces to constantly plot “independence” and provoke is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the greatest source of chaos that has pushed Taiwan into the danger of war. The Lai Ching-te authorities' attempt to “seek independence by force” is like an ant trying to shake a tree, overestimating its own strength. It is a dead end. The more they invest in so-called “preparing for war to seek independence,” the less they will care for the people's livelihoods in Taiwan, and the greater the harm they will ultimately bring to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Taiwan’s education authorities have required high school students to sign a “Wartime Youth Service Consent Form” and promote the so-called “national defense for all, everyone’s responsibility.” The DPP authorities are also reviewing the so-called “energy and food reserves.” What is your comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” means war, and it is irreconcilable with peace in the Taiwan Strait. No parent wants their child to be swept onto the battlefield because of “Taiwan independence.” The DPP authorities deliberately seek to “seek independence by force” and compel Taiwan's young people to serve as cannon fodder. This is the greatest threat to the security and well-being of the broad Taiwan public, especially Taiwan's young people. Only by resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” can peace in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded, the people of Taiwan be able to live in peace and without worry, and Taiwan's young people have a better future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","US Republican presidential candidate Trump, in a recent interview on the Taiwan question, said that if he is elected and “the CCP uses force against Taiwan,” he will impose tariffs of 150% to 200% on mainland China. He also said, “If Taiwan wants US protection, it should pay protection money.” What comment do you have?","Whether the United States truly wants to “protect Taiwan” or “harm Taiwan,” I believe most Taiwan compatriots have already made a rational judgment and clearly know that the United States always pursues “America First,” and Taiwan may at any time turn from a “chess piece” into a “discarded pawn.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The mainland snack “Huang Fei Hong Peanuts,” which is beloved by Taiwan residents, was recently banned from import and sale in Taiwan by the DPP authorities on the pretext of “protecting related industries on the island.” Taiwan residents expressed bewilderment, and some island netizens posted photos saying they were “secretly eating it.” What is your comment?","For many years, we have adhered to the concept of “cross-strait families are one” and taken measures to help Taiwan agricultural products enter the mainland market and help Taiwan enterprises and farmers expand their domestic sales on the mainland. Taiwan farmers have gained real benefits. In contrast, the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on their “Taiwan independence” stance, continuously carry out provocations aimed at “independence,” escalate cross-strait hostility and confrontation, and obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. To this day, they still unilaterally restrict the import of more than 1,000 agricultural products from the mainland into Taiwan. This not only hinders the normal conduct of cross-strait agricultural trade but also seriously harms the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. It is unpopular.\nThe fundamental reason the DPP authorities have so loudly “banned imports” and “strictly limited purchases” of the spicy peanuts you mentioned is that they come from the mainland. This shows that the DPP authorities’ persistent political manipulation has reached the point where they cannot tolerate even small peanuts. In fact, as cross-strait exchanges continue to expand, more and more mainland leisure snacks have attracted the attention and affection of Taiwan people. Whether spicy peanuts, luosifen, konjac snacks, or flower-filled pastries, they have sparked one “snack craze” after another in Taiwan. We will continue to work hard to enrich the “snack boxes” of Taiwan people, with more varieties and more diverse flavors. We also welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to see for themselves, check in at more food destinations, and discover more local specialty snacks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659822.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, from January to August this year, both Taiwan's tourism headcount and its tourism output deficit hit record highs, and the DPP authorities' target of “10 million overseas visitors to Taiwan” is nearly certain to “fall through.” Some industry figures on the island point out that poor cross-Strait atmosphere is also a major drawback for Taiwan's tourism. What is your comment on…","Taiwan's tourist arrivals and the tourism revenue deficit have both hit record highs, highlighting the increasingly difficult plight of the island's tourism operators and grassroots people, and revealing that the DPP authorities' perverse actions continue to harm the interests and well-being of tourism operators and the public.\nSince 2020, the DPP authorities, using the COVID-19 epidemic as a pretext, have banned mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan and suspended island travel agencies from operating group tours to the mainland. To this day, they still disregard mainstream public opinion on the island and ignore the voices and demands of Taiwan's tourism industry and grassroots people. They refuse to lift the “group tour ban,” and recently they have also rejected applications from Taiwan's tourism industry for chartered vessels on the pretext of so-called “security concerns.” They are the originators of the predicament facing Taiwan's tourism industry. The DPP authorities should face squarely the concerns of Taiwan's tourism operators and grassroots people, remove the obstructive restrictions on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, and take practical measures on the issue of Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","The National Immigration Administration recently said that since the beginning of this year, it has issued a total of 994,000 Taiwan compatriot permits, and Taiwan compatriots have entered the mainland a total of 2.961 million person-times, up 68.4% year on year. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council said that regarding the mainland’s “various united front measures luring people to go to the mainland,” the public…","Expanding personnel exchanges across the Strait and deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation are the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides, and they serve the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The data on Taiwan compatriots' travel to the mainland this year once again shows that seeking peace, development, exchange and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and the common voice of Taiwan compatriots. We will continue to improve the systems and policies that promote the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and continue to create conditions and provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland, so that they are willing to come, able to stay, and able to develop well. We advise the DPP authorities to heed the will of the people and remove as soon as possible the various obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","According to statistics from the Xiamen Entry-Exit Frontier Inspection Station, as of October 19, the annual passenger volume on the cross-Strait “Small Three Links” passenger shipping routes has exceeded 1 million passenger trips, a year-on-year increase of 87.6%. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To facilitate exchanges between people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, this year we have increased the number of flights on the cross-Strait “mini three links” passenger routes. The four “mini three links” passenger routes—Mawei to Matsu, Huangqi to Matsu, Quanzhou to Kinmen, and Xiamen to Kinmen—now operate 210 flights per week. As of October 19, annual passenger volume on the “mini three links” routes had surpassed one million, reaching 1.0039 million passenger trips.\n“Mini three links” is the most important and most convenient channel for exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, especially between Fujian and Taiwan, and has played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integrated development and enhancing the well-being of people on both sides. We welcome our Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland via the “mini three links” routes to visit, seek roots and pay respects to ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchanges and cooperation. We hope the DPP authorities will, with the well-being of the people on both sides at heart, remove all artificial restrictions as soon as possible and achieve full normalization of the “mini three links.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","The European Parliament recently passed a so-called resolution on “the PRC’s erroneous interpretation of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and its continued military provocations around Taiwan,” claiming that “China distorts international rules to obstruct Taiwan’s participation in international organizations” and calling on the EU to use diplomatic and economic means to contain China. What comments do you have…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The European Parliament's adoption of the relevant resolution seriously violates the one-China principle and the public commitments the European side made on the Taiwan question when it established diplomatic relations with China. It sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We strongly express our dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this.\nThe 26th session of the UN General Assembly in 1971 adopted Resolution 2758, by which the United Nations, while recognizing that Taiwan belongs to China, restored the lawful rights and seats of the whole of China, including Taiwan, to the government of the People's Republic of China. The historical facts are clear and the legal basis is unambiguous. We urge the European side to adhere to the one-China principle, correct its mistake, and handle the Taiwan question with prudence and appropriateness. We warn the DPP authorities that any scheme to win over or cling to external forces to pursue “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Regarding Lin Chia-lung’s “intrusive visit” to Guatemala, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs recently pointed out that Guatemala should recognize the trend and make the right choice. Taiwan’s external affairs authority said, “China harbors sinister intentions and is attempting to undermine and divide friendly countries’ relations with Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","183 countries around the world have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of adhering to the one-China principle. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community; it reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times. We believe the relevant countries will eventually recognize the trend of the times and stand on the right side of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","From November 5 to 10, the 7th China International Import Expo will be held in Shanghai. Please spokesperson introduce the exhibition participation of Taiwan-invested businesses and enterprises.","The 7th China International Import Expo will open on November 5 at the National Exhibition and Convention Center in Shanghai. This year, 18 Taiwan-invested businesses, enterprises, and products from fields including electronic information, machinery and equipment, shipping and logistics, light industry and food, and biotechnology and pharmaceuticals will exhibit. We welcome people from all walks of life across the Taiwan Strait to visit and discuss cooperation at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央广记者","Recent polls on the island show that DPP support has fallen to a seven-month low. Forty-seven percent of residents are dissatisfied with the Lai authorities’ handling of cross-Strait relations, and most residents believe cross-Strait relations will not improve at this stage, with 34% believing they will worsen. What is your comment?","Relevant public opinion polls reflect Taiwan residents’ concern and dissatisfaction with the Lai Ching-te authorities’ willful pursuit of “independence” and provocations. They once again show that the mainstream public opinion on the island is: peace, not war; development, not decline; exchange, not separation; and cooperation, not confrontation.\nSince taking office, Lai Ching-te has obstinately held to the “Taiwan independence” stance, refused to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” and repeatedly peddled separatist fallacies such as the “new two-state theory” of “not subordinate to each other.” He has repeatedly sought “independence by relying on external forces” and “independence by force,” obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, severely harmed the interests of Taiwan compatriots, and seriously threatened peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We advise the Lai Ching-te authorities to heed public opinion, recognize the situation, abandon illusions of “Taiwan independence,” and not rush recklessly down the wrong path, or they will certainly reap the consequences. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will continue to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, join mainland compatriots in promoting peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, refuse to serve as “cannon fodder for Taiwan independence” through concrete actions, earnestly safeguard their own interests and security, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202410/t20241030_12659826.htm"],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Regarding some scholars’ proposal that the United States put forward a permanent solution to Taiwan’s status, former U.S. Deputy Secretary of State Steinberg recently wrote that “U.S. ‘strategic ambiguity’ toward Taiwan remains the way to maintain peace in the Taiwan Strait, and the United States should find a ‘status quo’ that all parties can coexist with.” What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Resolving the Taiwan question is the Chinese people’s own affair, to be decided only by the Chinese people and to be settled only by the Chinese people. The current status of the Taiwan question is that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides have not yet been reunified, China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity have never changed. The US side should abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, and not send any wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The head of Taiwan’s economic competent authority recently proposed setting up green power plants in the Philippines and Japan and transmitting electricity to Taiwan via submarine cable or by ship. What comments do you have on this? In addition, many people in Taiwan have proposed that both sides of the Strait cooperate rather than confront. Given that water supply has already been connected between Kinmen and…","We have noted the relevant reports. This is nothing more than a trick by the DPP authorities to shift focus, as they are at a loss over the island's power shortage problem. Taiwan's economic development has long faced difficulties such as water and power shortages, which could be addressed by strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integration and development. However, the DPP authorities, in pursuit of their own selfish interests and disregarding the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people, have engaged in political manipulation, causing water and power shortages on the island to grow increasingly severe.\nOur attitude has always been consistent and clear: as long as something is conducive to enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and deepening cross-Strait integration and development, we will make our utmost efforts to do it. The \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring New Paths for Cross-Strait Integration and Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integration Development Demonstration Zone\" explicitly calls for advancing electricity, gas, and bridge connections between Xiamen and Kinmen, and between Fuzhou and Matsu, among other measures. We are willing to work together with all sectors on the island to eliminate interference and strive to realize these fine aspirations at an early date. The DPP authorities should face up to the demands of the Taiwan people and industry, stop obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integration and development, and stop conduct that damages cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First, what is the latest progress on the return to Taiwan of the captain of the Taiwanese fishing boat “Da Jin Man 88”? Second, the DPP authorities recently said that if the Mainland “blockades” the Taiwan Strait, it would be “a serious act of war,” and countries will not stand idly by since shipping would be affected. What comment do you have on this? Third, the Biden administration has so far made 17 arms…","On the first question, it is understood that the relevant departments are handling it in accordance with the law and regulations.\nOn the second question, the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, colluding with external forces to continuously engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” which is the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities have ulterior motives: by continuously hyping the so-called “mainland threat,” they seek to deceive Taiwan's public and to manipulate “resisting China” as a pretext, serving as an excuse to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and “prepare for war to seek independence.” We hope that broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and work with us to seek peace, safeguard peace, and share peace.\nOn the third question, the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, colluding with external forces to continuously engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” which is the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Since Lai Ching-te came to power, he has vigorously promoted the so-called “two states not subordinate to each other” “new two-state theory,” deliberately undermining normal cross-Strait exchanges, scheming to “rely on the United States to seek independence” and “seek independence by force,” continuously escalating cross-Strait confrontation and opposition, and leading to the danger of war in the Taiwan Strait. The United States continuously plays the “Taiwan card,” insists on arms sales to Taiwan and arming Taiwan, schemes to “use Taiwan to contain China,” and repeatedly sends wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, encouraging the DPP authorities to engage in risky “Taiwan independence” adventures and provocations.\nWe have always been committed to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and promoting exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides, but we will never sit idly by on “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference. The measures we have taken are legitimate and necessary actions to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","In response to the Hangzhou municipal government leading a delegation to Taiwan to attend the “Two Lakes Forum,” Liang Wen-chieh (梁文杰), deputy head of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the Nantou County government has been reminded that city exchange activities should comply with the relevant norms of cross-Strait exchanges and must not echo or cooperate with the CCP’s “united front” propaganda. What is…","The “Two Lakes Forum,” jointly organized by the Hangzhou Municipal People’s Government and the Nantou County Government, has been held for 16 consecutive sessions so far and has played an important role in strengthening exchanges and cooperation between the two places and enhancing the well-being of compatriots. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have obstructed it and set up various restrictions, which reflects their hypocritical face of saying one thing and doing another, and also fully reflects their “Taiwan independence” nature of trying every means to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-10-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视新闻记者","The U.S. recently announced its latest arms sale to Taiwan, totaling about US$1.988 billion. Raymond Greene, Director of the Taipei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan, said: “Arms sales to Taiwan are to strengthen Taiwan's reserve combat capability and balance cross-Strait military capabilities”; “The U.S. has military deployments in the Pacific, and the possibility of a full-scale war across the Taiwan…","We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to China’s Taiwan region. The US side should take concrete measures to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to translate the US leader’s commitment of “not supporting Taiwan independence” into concrete action, to stop arming Taiwan, and to stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nWe solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: buying weapons cannot buy security; it will only make Taiwan even more ominous and perilous in war. “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and external interference cannot block the trend of national reunification, nor shake our resolve and determination to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202410/t20241030_12659811.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-10-31","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say the U.S. Department of Defense announced approval of a US$1.988 billion arms sale to Taiwan, including surface-to-air missile systems and radar systems. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Zhang Xiaogang said that the United States' sale of weapons to Taiwan region of China seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, gravely infringes China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously undermines China-U.S. relations and endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and sends an erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly condemns and firmly opposes this, and has lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nZhang Xiaogang said that the U.S. side has violated its own commitments and is arming Taiwan ever more intensively, emboldening “Taiwan independence” forces and attempting to accelerate pushing Taiwan toward a perilous situation of warfare and danger. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities buy U.S. weapons as a “loyalty pledge,” while the U.S. draws the blood of Taiwan's ordinary people to fatten its own military-industrial complex. Facts have repeatedly proven that “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference are the root cause of disruption to the status quo across the Strait, the creation of cross-Strait crises, and the endangerment of regional stability.\nZhang Xiaogang stressed that the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. China urges the U.S. side to genuinely recognize the serious consequences of arming Taiwan and inviting disaster, and not to go further down the wrong path. A few U.S.-made weapons cannot change the military balance between the two sides of the Strait, and they cannot stop the historical trend of China's eventual reunification. The Chinese People's Liberation Army continues to strengthen training and combat readiness, comprehensively enhance its ability to win, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/20241101/56eb947bea6e4442a1d6b684a7d5b8b0/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-11-04","Mao Ning","Global Times","According to reports, Palau’s incumbent President Surangel Whipps, who is also a candidate for the general election, claims that China has been ratcheting up pressure and asked him to sever the country’s “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. Reports also said that another candidate Tommy Esang Remengesau Jr. denied analysis and comments labeling him as pro-China. Do you have any comment?","Around the world, 183 countries have already established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. The prevailing historical trend of endorsing the one-China principle is unstoppable. Only a very small number of countries in the world, including Palau, still maintain the so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan region. Such practice not only goes against the interests of these countries and their people and against UNGA Resolution 2758, but also violates China’s sovereignty, and thus needs to be corrected.\nChina urges these countries to fulfill their obligations under international law, stand on the right side of history and make right decisions that truly serve their fundamental and long-term interests at an early date. As a Chinese idiom goes, “those who suit their actions to the times are wise.” It will be welcome for China to see people with vision in these countries to recognize the prevailing trend of history and the times and respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and choose to stand on the right side of international fairness and justice at an early date. It’s never too late to make new friends. China stands ready to open up new chapters for relations with these countries on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495707.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495476.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-07","Mao Ning","The New York Times","Two questions from The New York Times. First, how will China respond to President Trump’s claim about blanket tariffs on goods from China? Second, what is China’s response to President Trump’s claim that China will not invade Taiwan?","On your first question, we do not answer hypothetical questions. But broadly speaking, let me reiterate that there is no winner in a trade war, nor will the world benefit from it.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan question is the most important and most sensitive issue in China-US relations. China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between the US and Taiwan. This position is consistent and clear. The US government needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and prudently handle Taiwan-related issues, so as to avoid severe damage to China-US relations and cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495720.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495487.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-07","Mao Ning","EFE","How does China assess the progress of the reconciliation and political transition efforts in Myanmar since 2021 and what specific role is it playing to support this process?","China’s position on the Myanmar issue is very clear. We support Myanmar in upholding independence, sovereignty, national unity and territorial integrity, support all parties in Myanmar in achieving political reconciliation through friendly consultation, and support Myanmar in resuming the political transition process.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495720.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495487.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-11-07","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 7 — Regarding the so-called assessment report recently released by the DPP authorities, which claims that the mainland has repeatedly used national security as grounds to restrict the personal freedom of Taiwan residents and has not notified the Taiwan side as required by relevant cross-Strait agreements, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State…","Chen Binhua said that we will, as always, sincerely care for compatriots in Taiwan, continue to improve systems and policies that enhance the well-being of compatriots in Taiwan, continuously inject positive energy and new momentum into exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, so that compatriots on both sides grow ever closer and more intimate through exchange, interaction and integration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241107_12661826.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-11-08","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan’s coast guard today said that it would be giving people cash rewards for reporting the presence of foreign military ships in its waters and they included the PRC ships in that. Does China have a comment on this new policy?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495722.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495496.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-12","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","A deputy German economy minister is in Taiwan this week for talks with officials there and executives. He’ll also visit TSMC. Does the Foreign Ministry want to comment on this visit?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a universally recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community as well as the political foundation of China-Germany relations. We urge Germany to abide by the one-China principle, stop official exchange with Taiwan authorities in whatever form, and stop sending wrong signals to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495734.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495502.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Questions now begin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation recently announced that it has invited faculty and students from seven mainland universities, including Peking University and Tsinghua University, to visit Taiwan in late November. Will this invited visit take place smoothly?","This April, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led young people from Taiwan on a visit to the mainland. Young people across the Taiwan Strait crossed mountains and seas and formed deep friendships. The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation invited teachers and students from seven mainland universities, including Tsinghua University, Peking University, and Fudan University, to travel to Taiwan at the end of November to exchange views with teachers and students from relevant universities on the island and to pay visits.\nWe have consistently advocated and actively promoted exchanges among young people across the Taiwan Strait, and we are pleased to see them visiting each other often and growing closer. This visit reflects a two-way effort by young people on both sides. Young people in Taiwan also very much look forward to young people from the mainland visiting Taiwan, and we hope the delegation of teachers and students from mainland universities can travel to Taiwan smoothly for exchanges. We welcome more young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to take a look around, make friends, and build bonds of friendship, and to deepen mutual understanding and build trust with young people on the mainland through exchanges and interaction, continuously gathering youthful strength to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663267.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that “the mainland's economy continues to be sluggish,” and that local governments freeze enterprise funds or impose fines on grounds such as fraud, reminding Taiwan businesses to be aware of the risks of investing on the mainland. What is your comment on this?","This claim is entirely baseless fabrication, a routine tactic used by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to smear the mainland.\nThe mainland's economy has strong momentum and resilience, and its market-oriented, rule-of-law, and internationalized business environment continues to improve. In the first three quarters of this year, the mainland's economy grew 4.8% year on year, placing it among the leading growth rates of the world's major economies. Among these, investment in high-technology industries grew 10% year on year, maintaining double-digit growth for seven consecutive months, providing strong support for the accelerated formation of new quality productive forces and the accelerated transformation and upgrading of the economic structure. Old and new growth drivers are accelerating their transition: investment in technological upgrading of the manufacturing sector grew 9.5%, and integrated circuit output and exports grew 26% and 22% year on year, respectively. The \"Global Innovation Index 2024 Report\" released recently shows that the mainland is one of the economies whose innovation capacity has risen most rapidly over the past decade, and its innovative development is demonstrating powerful momentum and broad prospects. As the major reform measures determined by the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee are increasingly implemented and take effect, and as the package of incremental policies continues to release development momentum, the mainland's economic development prospects are bright, providing stronger impetus for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening integrated development, and opening up broader space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to take root and develop on the mainland.\nIn the near future, relevant localities and departments will hold activities such as the industrial chain and supply chain matchmaking event for Taiwan-funded manufacturing enterprises, and the first Cross-Strait Service Industry Conference together with the 13th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Service Industry Forum, creating more platforms for Taiwan-funded enterprises to seize the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663270.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","To continuously advance the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, Fujian Province has recently held a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant details.","To actively explore a new path for cross-strait integrated development and steadily advance the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, Fujian has recently taken active steps to promote cross-strait agricultural and forestry exchanges and held two large-scale events.\nFrom November 6 to 9, the 19th Cross-Strait (Sanming) Forestry Expo and the 3rd Cross-Strait (Sanming) Rural Integrated Development Forum were successfully held in Sanming. Under the theme “Committed to Converting Lucid Waters and Lush Mountains into Assets, Focusing on Cross-Strait Integration,” the forum fully showcased new achievements in forestry reform such as Sanming's forest tickets and forestry carbon tickets, and vivid practices in promoting the value conversion of ecological products. More than 10 events were held, including the Bamboo and Wood Industrial Chain and Fujian-Taiwan Modern Agriculture Industrial Integration Investment Promotion Conference. More than 370 enterprises in categories such as understory economy, forestry machinery and “bamboo replacing plastic” displayed and sold their products. The event attracted more than 3,700 guests and businesspeople from both sides of the Strait to attend and exhibit, including more than 500 guests from Taiwan. Visitors numbered over 200,000 person-times, and transaction volume reached nearly 60 million yuan.\nFrom November 16 to 18, the 16th Cross-Strait Tea Expo will be held in Wuyishan City. Co-hosted by the Cross-Strait Tea Exchange Association, the China Tea Circulation Association, the Taiwan Farmers' Association, the Taiwan Region Tea Manufacturing Industry Association and other cross-strait organizations and groups, the expo has planned four major themed pavilions: the “Tea for the World” Pavilion (including the Taiwan Pavilion), the Tea Creativity Pavilion, the Fine Tea Pavilion and the New Tea Beverage Pavilion. The Taiwan Pavilion has 175 booths, with more than 140 Taiwan tea enterprises exhibiting, and a series of experiential exchange activities related to tea for cross-strait youth will be held, fully showcasing the latest achievements of “Coordinated Development of Three Teas and Integrated Development.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663259.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, relevant departments publicly solicited opinions on the (draft) Private Economy Promotion Law. What opportunities will the formulation and implementation of the Private Economy Promotion Law bring to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises developing on the mainland?","The draft of the 《People's Republic of China Private Economy Promotion Law (Draft for Public Comment)》 has been released for public comment across society. The draft clarifies the state's principles of treating the private economy equally, ensuring fair competition, providing equal protection, and promoting common development. It sets out specific provisions in areas including fair competition, investment and financing, technological innovation, business conduct, service guarantees, rights protection, and legal liability, putting into practice the requirements for equal treatment and equal protection of the private economy and encouraging and supporting its growth and expansion.\nThe 《Private Economy Promotion Law》, as the first basic law specifically dedicated to promoting and safeguarding the development of the private economy, will help further optimize a stable, fair, transparent, and predictable environment for private economic development. It will help stabilize market expectations and boost development confidence, and it will certainly play an important role in further promoting the sustained, healthy, and high-quality development of the private economy. Taiwan-funded enterprises will also certainly benefit from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663269.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, many cross-Strait film, television and cultural exchange activities have been held in succession. Please introduce the relevant information.","Film and culture are important vehicles for inheriting and promoting outstanding Chinese culture, and they are also forms of exchange that young people on both sides of the Strait enjoy. Cross-Strait film and cultural exchange activities have been dense in recent days.\nOn November 12, the 2024 Second Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival Awards Ceremony was held in Xiamen. The event was hosted by the Fujian Provincial Federation of Literary and Art Circles and the Jimei District Government of Xiamen, in cooperation with relevant Taiwan professional associations, under the theme “Tides Across the Strait, Images of Youth.” A total of 965 works from 168 universities on both sides of the Strait and abroad were exhibited, including 93 works from Taiwan.\nOn November 13, the annual gathering of cross-Strait filmmakers, the Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival, will open in Xiamen, with nearly one hundred Taiwan filmmakers invited to attend. During the activities from the 13th to the 16th, multiple events will be held, including a Taiwan film screening, a Taiwan film exchange meeting and the Golden Rooster Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Youth Short Film Season. During this period, nine Taiwan films, including 《816》, 《悲情城市》 and 《海上花》, will be screened. Eight Taiwan films currently in production will be promoted through the Golden Rooster Award platform, and some Taiwan directors will take part in creative exchange camps, deepening cross-Strait film exchange and cooperation.\nFrom November 14 to 18, Wuhan, Hubei will host the 10th “Golden Swallow” Cross-Strait Micro-Film and Micro-Video Competition and Creative Exchange Meeting. The theme of this year's competition is “Outside the Window,” symbolizing cross-Strait youth breaking down spiritual barriers and jointly creating a better future. A total of 154 works from more than 20 universities on both sides of the Strait participated in the competition.\nWe welcome journalists to follow and report on these cross-Strait film and cultural exchange activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","A mainland cargo ship ran aground after striking a reef at Yeliu, Taiwan. Taiwan scholar Su Ziyun said that the mainland and Taiwan have signed a “cross-Strait shipping agreement,” and it is very possible that ferries could be used to carry PLA personnel to assist in landing operations. What is your comment?","The relevant claims are sheer nonsense.\nIn November 2008, the Straits Exchange Foundation (ARATS) and Taiwan's Strait Exchange Foundation (SEF) signed the 《Cross-Strait Maritime Transport Agreement》, enabling direct sea passenger and cargo shipping. Direct cross-strait transport has greatly facilitated exchanges between people on both sides and economic exchanges, and has played an important role in advancing the common interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. This is a fact that is plain for all to see.\nIt should be noted that the cargo ship you mentioned, “Yuzhou Qihang,” was stranded at Keelung Port due to an accident. Later, because of a typhoon that changed direction, it applied to leave port to seek shelter from the storm, but it was not permitted to leave until the morning of October 29. After the ship left port, it was caught by the typhoon and trapped. Its application for tugboat rescue failed due to the excessively high waves and winds, and its repeated requests to return to Keelung Port were rejected. That evening, the ship lost power and ran aground near Yehliu. All crew members were forced to abandon ship for emergency safety. Some people on the island have disregarded the safety of mainland crew members and property, exploiting a maritime vessel distress incident to fabricate rumors and smear the mainland. We firmly oppose this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 15th China International Aviation and Aerospace Exhibition is being held in Zhuhai. Island public opinion is paying close attention to new aircraft models such as the J-35A, which the mainland has shown for the first time, and some believe they will pose a “new threat” to Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","The 15th China International Aviation & Aerospace Exhibition was held in Zhuhai from November 12 to 17, with 1,022 enterprises from 47 countries and regions participating. Airshow tickets were “hard to come by,” and the show also attracted many Taiwan youth and Taiwan media professionals, who came to watch the dynamic demonstrations of cutting-edge equipment across the “air, space, sea, and land” domains at the Zhuhai Airshow.\nThe mainland’s innovative achievements and formidable strength in the aviation, aerospace, and defense fields are a solid and enormous protection for the broad Taiwan compatriots, freeing them from the serious threats of “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The first question: On October 30, the three astronauts of Shenzhou-19 successfully entered China's space station, which drew attention and discussion on the island. Some Taiwan youth said, “I hope that in the future we can see Taiwan astronauts dedicating themselves to and contributing to China's space endeavor.” What is your comment? The second question: Lai Ching-te recently said that strengthening Taiwan's…","First question. Exploring the vast universe, developing the aerospace industry, and building a space power are the aerospace dream that the Chinese nation has pursued without ceasing. After years of effort, we have step by step realized the dream of leaving the Earth, exploring the universe, and roaming in space, and China’s aerospace undertakings have achieved a series of brilliant accomplishments that have drawn worldwide attention. This time, three astronauts of Shenzhou-19 entered China’s space station smoothly, achieving the fifth “space rendezvous” in China’s aerospace history, and the mission was successfully completed. This is the shared glory of all Chinese people, including compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. As long as cross-Strait relations are good, I believe there will certainly be a place for Taiwan compatriots to take part in relevant space experiments and exploration.\nSecond question. Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called “maritime frontier.” The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” deliberately “prepare for war to seek independence,” escalate cross-Strait confrontation, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and gravely harm the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Attempting to “seek independence through armed force” is like a mantis trying to shake a tree; it is doomed to fail. Only by abandoning the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” giving up the illusion of “seeking independence through armed force,” and stopping provocations to seek “independence” can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait truly be safeguarded and the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots effectively ensured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663265.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”记者","Andy Lau’s performance of “Chinese People” at his Taipei concert recently received an enthusiastic response, but it was attacked by the Green camp on the island. Some Green camp politicians called Andy Lau a “Communist-fawning entertainer” not worth seeing, and said that performing “Chinese People” “is a very Chinese-style design” and amounts to “united front” work. What is your comment on this?","Liu Dehua's concert in Taiwan was warmly welcomed by Taiwanese fans. The song “《Chinese People》” that he performed was composed by a Taiwanese musician, and its classic lyrics “hand in hand, no distinction between you and me, we walk forward with heads held high, letting the world know we are all Chinese” not only drew an enthusiastic response from the audience on site but also aroused wide resonance among Chinese descendants at home and abroad. Some Green-camp politicians, forgetting their ancestry, tried to use political manipulation to interfere with normal musical exchange, and they were condemned by public opinion on the island in unison.\nCompatriots on both sides are all 《Chinese People》, all 《Descendants of the Dragon》, have a 《Chinese Heart》, speak 《Chinese》, and love 《China in the Lights》. 《Love My China》 is the dignity and glory of every Chinese descendant. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will uphold the national righteousness of being Chinese, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and join mainland compatriots in jointly promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and creating the great cause of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663257.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The first question: During the campaign, Trump repeatedly alleged that “TSMC stole the US chip industry.” Some media have disclosed that, in order to prove to Trump that “it is a good guy,” TSMC has agreed to the US request and will suspend the supply of relevant chips to mainland Chinese customers starting November 11. What is your comment?\nThe second question: According to media reports, Elon Musk recently…","Question one: Promoting cross-Strait industrial cooperation is conducive to the development of cross-Strait enterprises and to enhancing the livelihood and welfare of compatriots on both sides. Relevant reports have once again proven that the US plays the “Taiwan card” and raises tensions in the Taiwan Strait in order to “use Taiwan to contain China.” The DPP authorities, scheming to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” blindly follow the US in “decoupling and breaking supply chains,” and are setting up more and more artificial obstacles to relevant cross-Strait industrial cooperation. What is ultimately harmed is the interests of enterprises on the island, what is weakened is the advantage of Taiwan's relevant industries, and Taiwan will further miss opportunities for industrial development.\nQuestion two: The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and collude with external forces to continuously provoke “independence,” pushing Taiwan step by step toward the danger of war. Relevant developments show that the DPP authorities' blind provocation of “independence” will only harm and destroy Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","Lithuania’s “prime minister-designate” Paluckas recently said that allowing a representative office to be set up in the country under the name “Taiwan” was a major diplomatic mistake. He pledged that after taking office he would seek to fully restore diplomatic relations with mainland China and repair the diplomatic rift between the two countries caused by the Taiwan question. What comment do you have on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. We hope relevant countries will recognize the trend, correct their mistakes as soon as possible, and stand on the right side of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","First question: Some people in the pan-green camp have said that Taiwan should view positively the US saying it will charge Taiwan a “protection fee,” which means the US is willing to protect Taiwan. What is your comment? Second question: This year's “Double Eleven” shopping carnival, as in previous years, stirred up a frenzy in Taiwan. Taiwanese media reported that sales in categories such as camping and travel…","On the first question: Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has obstinately held the “Taiwan independence” position, has relied on external forces without any bottom line, and has attempted to “seek independence by relying on outsiders” and “seek independence by force,” seriously harming the interests of Taiwan compatriots and seriously threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The United States always pursues “America First,” and I believe most Taiwan compatriots have already made rational judgments. I solemnly warn the DPP authorities: paying “protection money” cannot buy security; the deeper the reliance on the US, the greater the destruction of Taiwan, which will only bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan.\nOn the second question: The annual “Double Eleven” e-commerce shopping festival on November 11 is a very popular online shopping season on the mainland, and Taiwan people enthusiastically respond to it and actively participate. This year, some e-commerce platforms have introduced services such as free cross-border shipping for some products and local returns, fully meeting the diverse product demands and logistics choices of Taiwan consumers. We welcome more Taiwan people to join mainland compatriots in sharing a safe and convenient online shopping environment, and we are pleased to see Taiwan people gain tangible benefits.\nIt should be pointed out that mainland e-commerce platforms are platforms that meet the diverse product demands and logistics choices of Taiwan consumers, and will never become a tool for diehard “Taiwan independence” elements to “seek independence and make money.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663264.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Wu Fengshan, the newly appointed chairman of SEF, said, “The two sides of the Taiwan Strait have been separated and divided for 75 years.” Although the cross-Strait policies of past Taiwan leaders have differed, “the firm stance of defending Taiwan and upholding the sovereignty and independence of the Republic of China has remained consistent.” He hopes that ARATS will simultaneously build up goodwill, and that…","In 1945, the Chinese people achieved the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan, and Taiwan was freed from Japanese colonial rule and returned to the embrace of the motherland. After 1949, due to the continuation of the Chinese civil war and interference by external forces, the two sides of the Taiwan Strait fell into a special state of long-term political confrontation. However, Taiwan has always been, and will never be changed or allowed to be changed, an inalienable part of Chinese territory. This is a historical fact, a legal basis, and above all an objective reality.\nSince 2016, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have stubbornly insisted on the “Taiwan independence” position, continuously distorted and even denied the “1992 Consensus,” and unilaterally undermined the political foundation of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the consultation and exchanges between the two sides' cross-Strait institutions. This is the crux of the political deadlock across the Taiwan Strait. Our position is clear and consistent: as long as the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle as the common political foundation, is acknowledged, the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits can resume communication and consultation, and cross-Strait relations can return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663272.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","中评社记者","According to reports, Taiwan’s Ministry of the Interior will apply to dissolve the “Chinese Unification Promotion Party” on the grounds that it “clearly endangers the constitutional order,” which has drawn attention. Some public opinion on the island holds that this move is aimed at suppressing unification-leaning forces on the island. What is your comment on this?","Upholding the reunification of the motherland and opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference conforms to the greater interests of the nation and the trend of history, and is a righteous cause. Based on its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have repeatedly suppressed political rivals and used all kinds of means to arbitrarily suppress and persecute patriotic reunification forces on the island, and we strongly condemn this. The perverse actions of “Taiwan independence” forces will surely be judged by history and by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241113_12663266.htm"],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","The mainland recently opened tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for Fujian residents. Please introduce the current progress.","According to statistics from immigration and exit-entry administration authorities, as of October 31, a total of 58,735 applications for travel endorsements from mainland residents to Kinmen and Matsu had been accepted, including 54,319 applications for Kinmen and 4,416 for Matsu. A total of 5,074 mainland residents traveled to Kinmen and Matsu, including 4,551 to Kinmen and 523 to Matsu. The data show that mainland residents have a high enthusiasm for traveling to Kinmen and Matsu, and we hope they have good travel experiences.\nNext, we will continue to advance group tours by mainland residents to the island according to the established work arrangements. We hope the DPP authorities will face up to the voices and demands of Taiwan’s tourism industry and grassroots people, and remove as soon as possible the obstructions and restrictions on personnel exchanges across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Lai Shih-pao, a Kuomintang people's representative, said that in Trump's eyes Taiwan is “the size of the tip of a pen,” while the DPP authorities have always followed the United States' lead, and Taiwan's “bargaining chips” for dealing with Trump's unpredictability are continuously being lost. What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The DPP authorities, for the sake of one party’s private interests, have obstinately insisted on being pawns for outside forces playing the “Taiwan card,” and will ultimately become discarded pawns. We hope Taiwan compatriots will recognize the situation, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and earnestly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: Trump's election as US president may lead to a 60% tariff on the mainland. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said it hopes Taiwan businesspeople can make good plans, implying that it may become more difficult for them to do business on the mainland later. How do you respond? Second question: The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation recently announced that it would invite students and faculty from mainland…","On the first question: After more than 40 years of development, cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation have continuously expanded in scale, risen in level, and broadened in fields, maintaining a good momentum of development. According to statistics from relevant departments, from January to September this year, cross-Strait trade volume reached 212.44 billion US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 9%, of which the mainland's exports to Taiwan were 55.67 billion US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 10.6%, and imports from Taiwan were 156.77 billion US dollars, a year-on-year increase of 8.5%; the mainland newly established 5,725 Taiwan-invested enterprises, a year-on-year increase of 5.6%. Relevant data show that strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development are in line with the mainstream public opinion on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their own private gain, are obstructing this in every way and even forcibly pushing for “decoupling and breaking chains” in cross-Strait economic relations, which violates market rules and harms the well-being of compatriots; they will not succeed.\nThe Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China has laid out a grand blueprint for further comprehensively deepening reform and advancing Chinese-style modernization, and it will certainly provide stronger momentum and open up broader space for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation. We will actively improve institutions and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development, and promote the results of cross-Strait economic cooperation to better benefit the livelihoods of people on both sides of the Strait and bring well-being to compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question: After the news about mainland university faculty and students being invited to visit Taiwan was released, Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwanese young people, enthusiastically discussed it and had high expectations. We have seen the many proposals and appeals from Taiwanese netizens, and we will actively encourage and support youth exchanges in all fields across the Strait, and create more platforms and more opportunities for youth exchanges across the Strait. The relevant parties in Taiwan should promptly lift all kinds of restrictions on mainland residents entering Taiwan for exchanges, so that more Taiwanese young people have the opportunity to interact with outstanding young people from the mainland's sports and cultural circles.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","The first batch of HIMARS rocket launchers that Taiwan's military purchased from the US recently arrived in Taiwan, and photos of Taiwanese soldiers training in the US to receive the rocket launchers were also exposed. What comments does the spokesperson have?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We firmly oppose any form of military cooperation between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop “arming Taiwan,” and stop encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to “seek independence by force.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the U.S.” will only “harm Taiwan,” and “seeking independence by force” is an even more dead-end road.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Taiwan residents are very concerned about whether the mainland university faculty and students invited to Taiwan are going smoothly with their entry application procedures. Everyone very much hopes to see them arrive in Taiwan on the 27th. Second question: Tsao Hsing-cheng recently held a press conference and filed a so-called “criminal private prosecution” against two officials of the Taiwan…","On your first question: the mainland's invitation to university faculty and students to visit Taiwan for exchanges is a return visit to the exchanges with relevant mainland universities that Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwanese young students on in April this year. After the relevant news was released, young people in Taiwan discussed it enthusiastically and looked forward to it greatly. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. Only by visiting each other more often and keeping in closer contact can we continuously deepen mutual understanding, learn from each other, build harmony, and grow closer and more affectionate. We hope the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will heed the calls of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, promptly remove the various restrictions on exchanges between compatriots on both sides, and make exchanges between young people across the Strait smoother.\nOn your second question: the series of farces staged recently by Tsao Hsing-cheng exactly exposes his own guilt and fully reveals his \"Taiwan independence\" nature and his embarrassment of being fierce in appearance but timid inside. \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and \"Taiwan independence\" elements are grasshoppers that will not survive the autumn. We will unwaveringly safeguard national unification, sovereignty, and territorial integrity, and resolutely crack down on all \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and their separatist acts in accordance with the law.\nOn your third question: Tsao Hsing-cheng said he is afraid of the penalties the mainland has imposed in accordance with the law on his efforts to seek \"independence.\" This fully reveals his guilty conscience and fear under the net of the law against \"Taiwan independence,\" and it precisely proves that our just action of punishing \"independence\" in accordance with the law has struck at the vital point of the \"Taiwan independence\" diehards.\nAs for how individuals view this: just actions win broad support, one who acts openly and honestly has nothing to hide, and so-called \"countermeasures\" are purely a farce.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","The Civil Aviation Administration recently announced the cross-Strait flight arrangements for this winter-spring season. Compared with last year, the number of cross-Strait flights has fallen from over 900 to over 700, and the approved destinations have dropped from 33 to 21. What is the response of the Taiwan Affairs Office?","At present, cross-Strait flight routes are disrupted by the interference of the DPP authorities, and the destinations have not fully returned to normal. It is understood that the flight plans reported by airlines for the winter-spring season include flight plans for the 14 mainland destinations currently in service, as well as flight plans for mainland destinations not yet resumed. Among them, the flight plans for the 14 mainland destinations that have resumed service are basically consistent with those for the summer-autumn season, while the flight plans for mainland destinations not yet resumed have been substantially reduced. The deliberate obstruction by the DPP authorities is the main factor affecting the restoration of cross-Strait routes, destinations, and flights.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","On the 8th, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress announced a plan for resolving local government debt, with a scale at a record high. It aims to address local governments' fiscal difficulties and to boost demand and drive economic growth. May I ask the spokesperson: Will insufficient fiscal funds affect cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation?","First, what you have mentioned and the issue you raised are entirely two different matters. The relevant decision adopted by the NPC Standing Committee on November 8 is strong support for local finances. It will greatly ease local governments' pressure to resolve hidden debt and further expand local governments' fiscal space.\nSecond, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation are good for compatriots on both sides, and their intrinsic driving force lies among the people; they are an ever-flowing source of living water. Even in the face of constant obstruction and sabotage by the DPP authorities, the desire for peace, development, exchange and cooperation remains the strongest common voice of compatriots on both sides. I believe that compatriots on both sides, working together and moving toward each other, will surely make cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation deeper, more substantive, steady and far-reaching.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","First question: Some people on the island have pointed out that Taiwan's US$20 billion in arms purchases from the US have not yet been delivered. They worry that after Trump takes office, the US may push weapons manufacturing onto Taiwan for contract production and then sell the weapons back to Taiwan at high prices, which amounts to “skinning one cow twice.” What is your comment? Second question: According to…","First question: The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on \"seeking independence through force,\" squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people, and willingly act as America's \"cash machine.\" They are bent on pursuing a dead-end path of selling out and harming Taiwan, which will only make Taiwan more dangerous and place it in a state of war. The outcome of \"seeking independence by relying on outside forces\" can only be being subject to others' control, bringing profound disaster to Taiwan's compatriots.\nSecond question: For the sake of narrow party interests, the DPP authorities arbitrarily squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people on purchasing weapons and waging war, tying Taiwan to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot and coercing Taiwan's people to become \"cannon fodder for Taiwan independence,\" which has met with growing dissatisfaction and opposition from Taiwan's people. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that \"seeking independence through force\" is a path to certain ruin, and any scheme to seek \"independence\" by relying on external forces is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-13","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Raymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office, said that Taiwan's defense budget has increased by 8% compared with last year, that the United States is pleased to see the DPP authorities not only increase defense spending but also invest more broadly in defense resilience in other fields, and that he greatly admires the military and conscription reforms promoted by Lai Ching-te.…","“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on “seeking independence through force,” are willing to turn the island into a battlefield, tie Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” war chariot, and waste money that could be used to improve people’s livelihoods on buying weapons and currying favor with external forces. This will not only fail to buy “security”; it will instead accelerate turning Taiwan into a “powder keg” and a “landmine island,” and accelerate the process of making island residents, especially young people, “cannon fodder.”\nWe warn the DPP authorities that no matter how many weapons the “Taiwan independence” elements acquire, if they dare to take reckless risks, they will certainly bring about their own destruction. The reunification of the motherland is a historical inevitability. “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference cannot stop the trend of history, and cannot shake our determination and will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification.\nThe press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241113_12663233.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-11-14","Lin Jian","Reuters","Sources say that former Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen is planning a visit to Canada next week. Do you have any comment?","China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We firmly oppose any “Taiwan independence” separatist visiting countries with diplomatic ties with China under any pretext. We urge relevant country to abide by the one-China principle and uphold the political foundation of bilateral relations with concrete action.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495748.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495512.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-15","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te is planning to stop in Hawaii and maybe Guam on a visit overseas in the coming weeks, sources told Reuters. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment on that?","The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus. The Taiwan authorities’ political manipulation activities and separatist provocations using countries having so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan will lead nowhere. It will not shake the solid and strong international commitment to the one-China principle, or stop the overriding historical trend towards China’s reunification. On the so-called “transit” in the US by leader of the Taiwan region, we always firmly oppose the US’s arrangement for such kind of “transit” trip. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués, not to allow Lai Ching-te to “transit,” not to send any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces, and take concrete actions to uphold China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495752.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495514.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-11-15","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say Taiwan is considering large-scale military procurement from the United States to demonstrate its determination to strengthen defense to the new U.S. government. The U.S. side has publicly disclosed information that Taiwan's military secretly sent personnel to the U.S. for training to receive “HIMARS” rocket launchers, and Taiwan's defense authorities have confirmed that 11 “HIMARS” rocket launcher…","China urges the United States to immediately stop arming Taiwan and to stop its dangerous acts that undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities sell out Taiwan's interests to win the favor of their US masters, and vainly plot to “rely on external forces to seek independence.” This will only push Taiwan into a grave and perilous state of war. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter what weapons they buy, they will crumble at a single blow and will surely bring about their own destruction. The PLA will comprehensively strengthen military training and combat readiness, fully enhance its ability to win battles, and resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and interference by external forces.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16352402.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-11-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, November 15 (electronic dispatch): Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 15th, saying: The Taiwanese fishing vessel “Da Jin Man No. 88” violated the Fisheries Law of the People's Republic of China and other relevant legal provisions by conducting fishing operations illegally within a fishing ban zone during the fishing moratorium. The mainland coast guard carried out law enforcement actions in accordance with the law, and the relevant departments handled the matter in accordance with laws and regulations. This effectively safeguarded the fishery production order, marine fishery resources, and ecological environment in the relevant sea areas, and effectively deterred illegal and irregular conduct. After the relevant departments imposed penalties in accordance with laws and regulations, the captain, surnamed Hong, returned on November 15.\nChen Binhua said that on July 2, coast guard authorities in Fujian seized the Taiwanese fishing vessel “Da Jin Man No. 88” in the sea east of Weitou, Quanzhou, within a fishing ban zone. The vessel was suspected of using bottom trawl nets that violated the minimum mesh size requirements during the fishing moratorium.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241115_12663985.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-11-19","Lin Jian","AFP","A follow-up on the Hong Kong court sentencing. Taiwan has also condemned the sentencing. What is the Foreign Ministry’s response?","Taiwan is a province of China and what you asked about is not a matter related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495761.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-20","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s Foreign Minister Lin Chia-lung met with Belgian lawmakers and European Parliament members in Brussels on Tuesday as he starts a week-long trip in Europe. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","I’d like to correct you first: Taiwan is a province of China, and there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s foreign minister.” The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and the political bedrock of China-EU relations. China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between its Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The EU should abide by the one-China principle, stop any form of official interaction with the Taiwan authorities, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Our message to the Taiwan authorities: Attempts to create “one China, one Taiwan” or “two Chinas”, and advance “Taiwan independence” agenda will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495765.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495526.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-11-21","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: According to U.S. media reports, U.S. Department of Defense officials said that China refused to hold a China-U.S. defense ministers’ meeting during the ASEAN Defence Ministers’ Meeting-Plus because of U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. What is China’s comment on this?","Wu Qian: The failure to hold a China-U.S. defense ministers’ meeting during this ASEAN Defence Ministers’ Meeting-Plus is entirely the responsibility of the U.S. side. The U.S. cannot, on the one hand, harm China’s core interests on the Taiwan question, and on the other hand carry on exchanges with the Chinese military as if nothing had happened. The urgent task is for the U.S. side to immediately correct its mistake, genuinely respect China’s core interests, and work to create favorable conditions for high-level exchanges between the two militaries.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/16353454.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16353420.html",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-11-22","Lin Jian","AFP","Lai Ching-te will visit three Pacific island nation allies at the end of this month in his first overseas trip since taking office. Does China have a comment on this?","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and prevailing international consensus. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ political manipulation activities and provocations using trips to countries having so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan will lead nowhere. It will not shake the solid and strong international commitment to the one-China principle, or stop the overriding historical trend towards China’s reunification. We urge relevant countries to see clearly the trend of history at an early date, and make the right decision that truly serves their fundamental and long-term interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495778.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-22","Lin Jian","Reuters","Just step back on the question about Lai’s visit to the Pacific nations. Does China request any assistance from any other nations to not allow him to travel to those countries perhaps? Has there been any other request to the United States or any other countries in the region to stop this visit from happening?","As I just said, the one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495778.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-22","Lin Jian","The following question was raised after the press conference","Has China demanded the US not to allow Taiwan’s Lai to transit in US territory when he travels to the Pacific?","President Xi Jinping in the meeting between Chinese and US Presidents in Lima stressed that the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-US relations and they must be observed. Cross-Strait peace and stability and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are irreconcilable as water and fire. If the US side cares about maintaining peace across the Taiwan Strait, it is crucial that it sees clearly the true nature of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities in seeking “Taiwan independence,” handles the Taiwan question with extra prudence, unequivocally opposes “Taiwan independence,” and supports China’s peaceful reunification.\nI want to reiterate that China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, firmly opposes any visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and firmly opposes any form of US connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitments, including not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop any official interactions with the Taiwan region, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China remains resolutely determined to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and oppose interference in our internal affairs by external forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495778.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495533.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-25","Mao Ning","China News Service","It’s reported that on November 24, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Andrei Rudenko told TASS in an interview that “Naturally, the issue of Taiwan is in the exclusive competence of our Chinese colleagues. However, we see that Washington, in violation of the one-China principle, is strengthening military-political contacts with Taipei under the slogan of maintaining the ‘status quo’, and increasing arms supplies.…","We noted the reports. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. China highly commends Russia’s just position of staying committed to the one-China principle and opposing the attempt of using Taiwan to contain China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495782.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-25","Mao Ning","AFP","According to Japanese media, the United States is working with Japan on contingency plans for a possible future emergency involving Taiwan. These plans would see the United States deploy missile units on Japan’s Nansei Islands as well as in the Philippines. Is China aware of such plans and does it have any comments on the report?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. The key to upholding cross-Strait peace and stability is to remain committed to the one-China principle. China firmly opposes relevant countries using the Taiwan question as an excuse to strengthen military deployment in the region, heighten tensions and confrontation, and disturb regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495782.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-25","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Lithuania’s incoming Prime Minister Paluckas said he is open to restoring diplomatic relations with China three years after a trade dispute led to Beijing downgrading its ties. The incoming Prime Minister signals support for repairing ties by returning envoys to both capitals, but he stressed that his administration won’t reverse course on current policies that include maintaining trade links with Taiwan. Does…","We noted relevant statement from the Lithuanian side. As is widely known, Lithuania’s wrongful acts on issues concerning Taiwan are the root cause of the fraught relations between China and Lithuania. China’s door remains open to dialogue and we hope that Lithuania will return to the right path of upholding the one-China principle, abide by the political commitments in the communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Lithuania, and accumulate enabling conditions for the normalization of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495782.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-25","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan defense ministry said today that it had detected a Chinese balloon passing over waters yesterday northwest of the island. This is the first such balloon it has reported since April. Can you provide details about the situation or do you have any comment?","First of all, there is no such thing as “Taiwan defense ministry” and the question is not related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495782.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495536.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-27","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","The G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting Statement said the group seeks constructive and stable relations with China and stands ready to cooperate with China to address global challenges. In the meantime, the group asks China to stop supporting Russia’s defense industry, plays up the allegation of China’s “overcapacity” and makes irresponsible remarks on issues related to the East China Sea, the South China Sea, Taiwan,…","Since the beginning of this year, we’ve made clear China’s solemn position on the G7’s erroneous remarks related to China on multiple occasions. Given that the G7 members say they seek constructive and stable relations with China and stand ready to cooperate with China to address global challenges, they should champion the spirit of mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit and act on their words accordingly rather than smear and attack China.\nChina has been objective and just on the Ukraine crisis and actively promoted talks for peace. China has never provided weapons to parties to the conflict and strictly controls the export of dual-use articles, even drones for civilian use, and opposes using civilian drones for military purposes. The normal economic ties and trade between China and Russia should not be disrupted or coerced by any third party. The so-called allegation of China’s overcapacity has been proved a false one by a large number of informative facts and statistics. We hope relevant countries will keep an open mind and pursue fair competition. China’s position on issues related to the East China Sea, the South China Sea, Taiwan, Xinjiang, Xizang and Hong Kong is consistent and clear-cut. We firmly oppose the G7 undermining China’s sovereignty and interfering in China’s internal affairs. We urge G7 countries to abide by the purposes and principles of the UN Charter and the basic norms governing international relations and look after their own affairs.\nAs we speak, changes unseen in a century are unfolding at a faster pace in our world and international peace and development are facing unprecedented challenges. As a responsible major country, China always upholds fairness and justice, advocates openness and inclusiveness and brings benefits to the world through its development. We hope the G7 countries will stop indulging in geopolitical games, discard the narrow zero-sum mindset and make concrete contributions to international solidarity and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495789.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495544.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","On November 16, President Xi Jinping met with US President Joe Biden in Lima. President Xi stressed that the Taiwan question is the first red line that must not be challenged, and asked the US side to handle the Taiwan question with extreme caution. Please interpret this for us.","The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests, the foundation of the political basis of China-U.S. relations, and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech clarified China’s solemn position on the Taiwan question and has important guiding significance for doing our Taiwan work well. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the reunification of the motherland.\nOur determination to crush the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatists and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering, our capability is unbreakable, and our actions are resolute and forceful. We will never allow anyone or any force to separate Taiwan from China in any form. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the danger and harm of Lai Ching-te authorities’ pursuit of “Taiwan independence” separatism and their undermining of cross-Strait relations, and join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist actions and jointly pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667273.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Wu Feng-shan, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that if the two sides reached the “1992 Consensus,” then the mainland should clarify where the “Republic of China” stands within the “1992 Consensus.” What is your comment?","In 1945, the Chinese people achieved the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan, and Taiwan returned to the embrace of the motherland. Not long afterward, due to the continuation of the Chinese Civil War and interference by external forces, the Taiwan Strait fell into a special state of political confrontation. However, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed and cannot change. The reunification of the two sides of the Strait is an end to political confrontation; it is not a recreation of territory and sovereignty.\nOn August 1, 1992, the “National Unification Council” of the Taiwan authorities reached a “conclusion” on the question of the meaning of “one China” when the two sides' associations discussed matters of a practical nature. It stated: “Both sides of the Strait adhere to the principle of one China, but each side has different understandings of its meaning;” the Taiwan authorities “have formulated the Guidelines for National Unification and begun taking steps toward unification.” This “conclusion” indicated the Taiwan authorities' position that Taiwan is part of Chinese territory, that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle,” and that they pursue unification.\nIn response, the then head of the Straits Exchange Association issued a statement pointing out that confirming that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle” was of very important significance for practical negotiations between the two sides. Afterward, through the Hong Kong talks between the two associations and the exchange of letters and telegrams, both sides reached a consensus to each verbally express that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle,” which was later known as the “1992 Consensus.” The essence of the “1992 Consensus” is seeking common ground while shelving differences: seeking the common ground of one China while preserving the minor differences between the two sides. Regarding the political meaning of “one China,” the Straits Exchange Foundation stated that they had “different understandings,” and the Straits Exchange Association stated that it “does not involve this in practical negotiations.” In other words, the “1992 Consensus” temporarily shelved the disagreement over the political meaning of “one China” on the premise that both sides expressed their adherence to the one-China principle.\nIt was on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” that the two sides launched consultations and negotiations, advanced inter-party exchanges between political parties, and opened the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, from which compatriots on both sides have benefited.\nThe process and content of the “1992 Consensus” are clear, documents and written records are unambiguous, and the achievements benefiting compatriots on both sides are plain to see. The “1992 Consensus” has played an irreplaceable and important role in establishing political mutual trust between the two sides, conducting dialogue and consultation, and improving and developing cross-Strait relations. Those engaged in cross-Strait affairs should have an accurate understanding of this. I would like to emphasize once again that as long as the Taiwan Straits Exchange Foundation returns to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and acknowledges the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation, the cross-Strait talks between the two associations can resume.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667267.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, while attending a youth event, Lai Ching-te put forward the so-called “three options for peace” to high school students present. He negated the signing of a cross-Strait peace agreement and the “1992 Consensus,” again agitated for “mutual non-subordination” across the Strait, and claimed that “upholding sovereignty” and “standing together with the democratic camp” are his “path to peace.” What is your…","Facing minor students, Lai Ching-te uses deceptive rhetoric to mislead and induce young students to accept his “Taiwan independence” separatist proposition, intending to make innocent young people victims of “Taiwan independence.” His conduct is shameful, and his intentions deserve condemnation.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their independence-seeking provocations are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te's so-called “path of peace” is a self-destructive path that disregards the safety and well-being of Taiwan's youth and the broad masses, and, under the banner of “peace,” prepares for and provokes war. It is a path that pushes Taiwan step by step toward the brink of war and self-annihilation. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan's youth, will see through the “Taiwan independence” nature of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, firmly hold their own destiny in their own hands, resolutely oppose their independence-seeking provocations, and lead Taiwan out of danger onto a lasting and sustainable path of peace.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667268.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","At a recent KMT anniversary event, Ma Ying-jeou once again sharply criticized Lai Ching-te for pushing the “new two-state theory” of “not subordinate to each other,” and assessed Lai's “Taiwan independence” position as “neither necessary, nor feasible, nor practical.” He hopes the KMT will uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” fully safeguard cross-Strait peace and stability, and protect the…","Unification is the historical trend and the right path; “Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history and a dead end. The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” advocate the “new two-state theory,” deliberately provoke “independence,” and attempt to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence.” They defy the tide and depart from the general trend, and they will surely fail. On the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen liaison and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people of insight, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and push forward national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667271.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Wang Jin-pyng, former head of Taiwan's legislature, recently established the cross-party think tank “Centrist Peace Alliance” on the island, stating that he will work to promote peace across the Taiwan Strait. He subsequently visited Zhangzhou, Fujian to worship ancestors and tour, saying he hopes both sides can work together for peace, and that compatriots currently need to strengthen their national identity,…","Maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The basis and prerequisite for realizing this shared aspiration is adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” As long as one accepts that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, there is no obstacle to our dialogue and communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals.\nMr. Wang Jin-pyng’s return to his hometown to pay respects to his ancestors reflects the Chinese nation’s fine tradition of honoring ancestors and remembering one’s origins, reflects the aspiration to inherit and promote the fine traditional Chinese culture, and reflects the strong desire of broad Taiwan compatriots to strengthen cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are Chinese and are one family connected by blood. Promoting the fine traditional Chinese culture is a shared obligation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation is a shared responsibility, and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is a shared mission. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will uphold our shared national righteousness, conform to the trend of history, and join mainland compatriots in promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, advancing the reunification of the motherland, and creating a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667263.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan's tourism deficit is expected to widen further this year, with the difference between outbound and inbound travelers reaching ten million person-times and the deficit reaching NT$730 billion. Some commentators and industry operators on the island have pointed out that the sharp decline in mainland tourists has caused a plunge in the number of visitors to Taiwan, and that tense…","The DPP authorities’ obstinate pursuit of “independence,” their provocations, which have intensified cross-Strait confrontation, and their deliberate obstruction and sabotage of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation are the direct cause of Taiwan’s tourism industry falling into deep difficulties. Facts prove that “Taiwan independence” is “Taiwan poison.” Pursuing “Taiwan independence” means there will be no peace in the Taiwan Strait, and Taiwan will have no development. As long as the DPP authorities lift the “group tour ban” and remove the obstacles and restrictions on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, we will, on the basis of resuming mainland residents’ travel to Matsu and Kinmen, study further expanding mainland residents’ travel to Taiwan and strengthen cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667262.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","In response to Lü Lishi, a former Taiwan Navy captain and retired major who said in an interview at the Zhuhai Airshow that he wanted Taiwan residents to know “how strong China is,” a Democratic Progressive Party people's representative has proposed amending the “Act Governing Relations Between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area,” expanding the regulated group from retired generals to “personnel…","I am not sure whether the DPP people’s representative who made the proposal has seen the old Taiwan film “Eight Hundred Heroes” and sung its theme song “China Will Surely Be Strong,” but I know that many Taiwan compatriots were educated to be upright and proper Chinese, and once sang “China Will Surely Be Strong” with surging hearts, expressing their ardent hope for China’s prosperity and the rejuvenation of the nation. Mr. Lü Lishi’s remarks after visiting the Zhuhai Airshow came from the heart, expressing sincere national sentiment, and they stirred strong resonance among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The buffoonish antics of the DPP people’s representatives not only puncture the lies of the so-called “democracy” and “freedom of speech” they tout, but also expose their fear in the face of the mainland’s great strength.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667260.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. What important cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities will various localities hold before the end of the year?","Recently, all localities have thoroughly implemented the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee, holding a series of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities in diverse forms and with rich content around promoting cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges, strengthening cross-Strait industrial cooperation, and deepening cross-Strait integrated development. These activities have built platforms and provided convenience for Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises to expand into the mainland market and seize market opportunities as Chinese-style modernization advances comprehensively.\nFrom November 3 to 6, the 20th Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum was held in Nanning, Guangxi. Xia Liyan, Vice Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, Huang Mingzhi, Chairman of the Supervisory Committee of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, and more than 700 Taiwan political and business figures, ethnic minorities, grassroots people, and young people attended the forum. The forum took “Advancing Exchanges and Cooperation, Deepening Integrated Development” as its theme, focusing on helping Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises gain a deeper understanding of the policy dividends of the Western Development strategy and actively participate in Guangxi-Taiwan exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development.\nFrom November 16 to 20, the 16th Straits Cross-Strait Tea Industry Expo was held in Wuyishan City, Fujian. Under the theme “Coordinated Development of the Three Teas and Integrated Development,” this year's expo included exhibitions of achievements, trade negotiations, cooperation and exchanges, and tea tourism experiences. The Taiwan Farmers' Association, the Nantou County and Pinglin District (New Taipei City) farmers' associations, and more than 10 tea industry associations on the island organized 143 Taiwan enterprises to exhibit, covering 14 counties and cities in Taiwan. The number of exhibiting Taiwan enterprises and the exhibition area both reached record highs for all previous sessions. During the expo, the cumulative number of visitors reached more than 298,000 person-times, with on-site transaction volume of 387 million yuan, of which the Taiwan Pavilion accounted for 19.01 million yuan.\nOn November 19, the first Cross-Strait Service Industry Conference and the 13th Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Service Industry Forum were held in Chongqing. Under the theme “Innovative Services, Co-creating the Future,” the conference and forum focused on service industry and youth exchanges, discussing cooperation and common development. More than 400 people attended, including well-known entrepreneurs from the Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao regions and representatives of business and trade associations. At the meeting, the “Joint Initiative on Exchanges, Cooperation, and Integrated Development of Cross-Strait Service Industries” was released, proposing to promote deep integration of traditional and innovative service industries across the Strait, strengthen cross-Strait youth exchanges and people-to-people communication, and promote green, low-carbon, and sustainable development of the cross-Strait service industry.\nOn November 20, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a symposium for Taiwan businesspeople in Suzhou City, Jiangsu Province, meeting with nearly 100 Taiwan business and industry groups and representatives of Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland for discussion and exchange. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the symposium and delivered a speech, emphasizing that the mainland's economy is advancing steadily and continuously improving, and remains the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots to develop their careers. We will implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee, improve systems and policies promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and help Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots develop new quality productive forces and integrate into the new development pattern. Representatives of Taiwan business and industry groups, Taiwan-funded enterprises, and Taiwanese youth starting businesses on the mainland said in their remarks that the prospects for economic development on the mainland are bright, that they are full of confidence in putting down roots and developing on the mainland, and that they will actively participate in cross-Strait industrial chain and supply chain cooperation, integrate into the new development pattern, and achieve high-quality development.\nOn November 21, the Taiwan-funded manufacturing enterprises industrial chain and supply chain matchmaking conference and the 2024 Cross-Strait Machinery Industry Exchange Conference were held in Suzhou City and Nantong City, Jiangsu Province, respectively. The activities focused on cultivating new quality productive forces and promoting win-win cooperation between cross-Strait enterprises, attracting enthusiastic participation from industry operators. Director Song Tao visited the exhibition booths of the Taiwan-funded manufacturing enterprises industrial chain and supply chain matchmaking conference, encouraging Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to seize the opportunities of comprehensively advancing Chinese-style modernization and develop better and faster on the mainland. Through stages including supply and demand release, key project roadshows, and matchmaking negotiations, the Taiwan-funded manufacturing enterprises industrial chain and supply chain matchmaking conference provided investment, financing, and project matchmaking platforms for enterprises in fields such as electronic information and new energy vehicles. The Machinery Industry Exchange Conference took “Intelligent Machinery Empowering New Quality Productive Forces” as its theme. More than 100 cross-Strait experts, scholars, and entrepreneurial representatives conducted in-depth exchanges on topics such as AI applications and green energy conservation, exploring innovative cross-Strait cooperation models and high-quality development paths for the machinery industry.\nFrom December 9 to 10, the 2024 Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit will be held in Xiamen, Fujian. Centered on implementing the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory letter to the 10th Anniversary Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, it will bring together cross-Strait business and industry forces, jointly committing to advancing cross-Strait economic and industrial cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","We note that the “Taiwan Public Opinion Foundation” recently released a poll. Regarding the U.S. claim that Taiwan must pay “protection money,” 51% of Taiwan residents disagree. And 57% do not believe the U.S. government would send troops to “help defend Taiwan,” a new high. What is your comment?","The public opinion poll data you mentioned once again shows, from one angle, that whether the United States is “protecting Taiwan” or “harming Taiwan,” and whether the DPP authorities are “safeguarding Taiwan” or “bringing disaster to Taiwan,” more and more Taiwan compatriots have a clear understanding. They have broken through the information cocoon that the DPP authorities have tried hard to build, seen through its deceptive rhetoric, made rational judgments, and refused to pay the bill for “Taiwan independence,” and even more so refuse to be sacrificed for “Taiwan independence.”\nThe so-called “protection fee” has already triggered strong backlash across all sectors on the island, especially among young people. I have seen many Taiwan youths leaving comments on social media pointing out that if the United States is allowed to take whatever it wants, Taiwan's National Health Insurance funds will be squeezed. Others point out that the DPP's blind “reliance on the United States” will only accelerate “harming Taiwan” and push Taiwan toward the abyss of disaster. The DPP authorities should face up to the mainstream public will on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. They should stop “seeking independence through armed force” and “seeking independence through reliance on outsiders,” and stop all “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241127_12667256.htm"],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce the recent cross-Strait exchange activities in various fields. What important cross-Strait exchange activities will various localities hold before the end of the year?","Recently, exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have continued to heat up, with exchange activities in all fields flourishing.\nOn November 11, the 11th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour Closing Camp and Guangdong-Taiwan Exchange Achievements Showcase was held in Guangzhou. Themed \"Coming Together, Dreams Become More Wonderful,\" the event incorporated Lingnan characteristic culture and guided youth on both sides of the Strait to jointly inherit and promote China's outstanding traditional culture. From June to November, the event organizers organized visits along 11 themed routes in batches, widely attracting youth from both sides of the Strait and achieving good results.\nFrom November 27 to 30, the \"Meet in Chang'an, Hearts United on the Path of Medicine: 2024 Cross-Strait Health Cooperation and Exchange Conference\" will be held in Xi'an, Shaanxi Province. The event will have a scale of about 350 people, including approximately 100 well-known experts in Taiwan's medical field, young scholars, and student representatives. Themed \"Deepening Medical and Health Cooperation to Enhance the Well-being of Compatriots on Both Sides of the Strait,\" the conference includes plenary speeches, sub-forums on medical innovation and technology cooperation exchanges, sub-forums on traditional Chinese medicine and wellness cooperation exchanges, visits and exchanges at medical institutions, and a ceremony to worship the Yellow Emperor at his mausoleum.\nOn December 5, the second \"Youth Power, Happy Home — Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month\" event will be held in Shenzhen, Guangdong Province. During the event, the Fifth Cross-Strait Student Baseball League Finals and the Second \"Guangming Cup\" Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Cycling Race, along with 43 other exchange activities, will be held. By building cross-strait youth exchange platforms, the event will continue to create better conditions and more opportunities for the growth, development and success of young people on both sides of the Strait.\nFrom December 5 to 16, Shaxian District of Sanming City, Fujian Province, will jointly host with the Taishang Youshi Network the 2024 China (Shaxian) Snack Tourism and Culture Festival and the Cross-Strait Food Carnival. Themed \"Savoring Both Sides of the Strait, Gathering Fragrance in Shaxian,\" the event includes cross-strait food exhibitions, a snack food run, a special snack culinary skills invitational competition, a Shaxian snack culture short video creation contest (special session for Taiwanese university students), a thousand-person snack skills experience, and other cross-strait food exchange activities. More than 600 Taiwan compatriots will be invited to participate and experience the cultural origin of shared food traditions across the Strait. A few days ago, the well-known Shaxian snacks were displayed at Ximending in Taipei, and Lien Sheng-wen, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, along with other representatives from Taiwan's circles, attended and were warmly welcomed by Taipei residents.\nOn December 8, the 2024 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Marathon will be held in Kunshan, Jiangsu Province. The race will feature 10 groups of 200 \"Cross-Strait Hand-in-Hand\" entries, in which Taiwanese and mainland runners register together. Local Kunshan enterprises and Taiwanese enterprises and cultural institutions are invited to participate in the marathon expo and carnival, displaying cross-strait cultural products with distinctive features and providing a platform for marathon enthusiasts on both sides to exchange and strengthen friendship.\nBefore the end of the year, winter exchange activities with local characteristics will be launched one after another. We will promptly release information about these activities, and we welcome journalist friends to pay attention to and interview these exchange events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","A delegation of mainland university faculty and students invited by the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation departed for Taiwan today (the 27th). What expectations does the spokesperson have for this trip? What plans and measures does the mainland have to further promote cross-Strait youth exchanges?","The mainland university faculty and student delegation visiting Taiwan, led by Academician Qiu Yong, Party Secretary and Chairman of the University Council of Tsinghua University, and composed of 40 faculty and students from 7 universities, departed this morning. It will conduct exchanges with 6 universities and 1 high school in Taiwan, and visit relevant historical and cultural sites in Taiwan. Previously, all sectors of Taiwan society, especially young students, expressed high expectations and a warm welcome for the delegation's visit. We hope the delegation has a smooth trip in Taiwan, and we look forward to cross-Strait young students using this opportunity to strengthen exchanges and interaction, enhance mutual understanding, and deepen their friendship.\nCross-Strait youth are the most active and positive factor in advancing the development of cross-Strait relations, and they should be strongly supported by all sectors on both sides of the Strait. We will, as always, promote cross-Strait youth exchanges and continue to build more platforms and create more opportunities for cross-Strait youth to learn from and draw on each other and to communicate from the heart, so that cross-Strait youth grow ever closer and more intimate through exchange, interaction, and integration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","The first question: the Taiwan “Grassroots Influence Foundation” published its latest poll, which shows that 48% of the public believe Lai Ching-te's cross-Strait policy may cause the danger of war, and expressed unwillingness to join the so-called “civilian strength training.” What comment does the spokesperson have on this? The second question: Lai Ching-te recently said that several important cabinet members…","First question: The Lai Ching-te authorities, in pursuit of “Taiwan independence,” are “stirring up trouble and provoking war.” This has already made Taiwan residents fearful and deeply worried, and they refuse to serve as “cannon fodder for Taiwan independence.”\nSecond question: Regardless of who serves in what positions in the new U.S. government, this cannot change the status of Taiwan as part of China. The Lai Ching-te authorities, blindly “relying on the U.S. to seek independence,” will inevitably face the pitiful fate of becoming a “discarded pawn.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","During the APEC summit, Singapore’s leader told the Chinese side that Singapore opposes “Taiwan independence” and firmly adheres to the one-China principle. Taiwan’s “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” said the mainland was spreading “untrue remarks.” Subsequently, Singapore’s official website published a related press release, slapping the face of the DPP authorities. Public opinion on the island directly accused…","Facts have repeatedly shown that the One-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a general consensus of the international community, and it reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times. “Taiwan independence” has lost support and is at a dead end. The DPP authorities, disregarding the facts and deceiving the people on the island, will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: The Liberty Times reported that the Taiwan Affairs Office recently dissuaded Taiwanese businesses from withdrawing investment and factories from the mainland, and asked them to cooperate with a new investment strategy to help cope with the economic and trade shocks following Trump's inauguration. The Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland has strengthened national security oversight and…","First question: The relevant reports are pure fabrication and malicious rumor. Recently, relevant parties have successively held Taiwan business symposiums, industrial chain and supply chain matchmaking meetings, and industry exchange meetings to introduce the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization and to support Taiwan businesspeople in integrating into the new development pattern and participating in high-quality development. Broad numbers of Taiwan businesspeople have responded actively and participated enthusiastically, fully proving that the broad opportunities of the mainland's new round of reform and opening up cannot be slandered and discredited, and that Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots' pursuit of enterprise on the mainland cannot be stopped by deception and intimidation.\nSecond question: The essence of the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and the essence of cross-Strait relations is that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. The DPP authorities have fabricated the false narrative of \"democracy confronting authoritarianism,\" attempting to deceive the island's public and mislead international perception. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, collude with external forces to seek \"independence\" and provoke, escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is the greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Upholding the one-China principle and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" is the common consensus of the international community. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: separatism and confrontation have no way out, and the delusion of \"seeking independence by relying on external forces\" is doomed to fail.\nQuestion from Taiwan's CTV News:\nFirst question: Today in the morning, there was news from Taipei saying that the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held on December 17. Can this be confirmed? Second question: The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation invited a visiting delegation of mainland university teachers and students, including Olympic champion Ma Long, to visit Taiwan for exchanges. It was warmly welcomed by Taiwan's young people, but it was described as a \"united front\" tactic. What is your response?\nFirst question: We have consistently supported and actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Shanghai Municipality and Taipei City have maintained contact and communication regarding the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum this year. Once the relevant arrangements are determined, we will release information in a timely manner.\nSecond question: I have already clarified the matter of the united front earlier, explaining in detail the important significance and main tasks of the united front work. We have consistently advocated and actively promoted cross-Strait youth exchanges, and we welcome cross-Strait youth coming and going frequently and getting closer to each other. This visit is a youthful appointment and a two-way mutual pursuit between young people on both sides of the Strait, and it is eagerly anticipated by all sectors of the island, especially young students. The visiting delegation of mainland university teachers and students, as the name suggests, is about exchanges among university youth and students. I do not know what these people on the island are actually afraid of. Do they want cross-Strait youth to exchange or to fall out? We hope that all sectors on both sides will work together to return cross-Strait youth exchanges to their vibrant and energetic essence, and we also wish the visiting delegation smooth exchanges and visits in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The DPP authorities recently said that Lai Ching-te plans to make a sneak visit to three Pacific island countries in the near future, and that whether his trip will “transit” through the U.S. states of Hawaii and Guam is “still under planning.” What is your comment?","The so-called “transit” by the leader of the Taiwan authorities is essentially “relying on external forces to seek independence.” Any attempt to create “one China, one Taiwan,” “two Chinas,” or any other provocation that violates the one-China principle will certainly be opposed by the entire Chinese people. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","On the 25th, the Taiwan Travel Agents Association, local travel associations and other groups, along with major tourism associations, went to Taiwan’s “Tourism Administration” to make a petition, hoping the authorities would accelerate communication to open up mainland visitors to tour Taiwan and immediately lift the “group tour ban” on travel to the mainland. What is your comment on this?","We have consistently and clearly supported normalizing personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and normalizing exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait, including tourism. This is in the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. The tourism industry on the island has long suffered from the “group travel ban,” and its demands are legitimate and reasonable. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities should face up to the mainstream public opinion among broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots, who want peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, and the appeals of the tourism industry, and remove as soon as possible the various obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","KMT elected representatives and public opinion on the island have pointed out that as Trump is about to return to the White House, and before official cross-Strait dialogue can be resumed, there is an urgent need to establish a risk-avoidance mutual trust mechanism to prevent minor frictions from escalating into major conflicts and to jointly maintain peace in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities’ continued provocations aimed at seeking “independence” are the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. The “1992 Consensus” is the cornerstone for building mutual trust and dialogue and consultation across the Strait. As long as the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is upheld and “Taiwan independence” is opposed, peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait will be guaranteed, and cross-Strait relations can return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Regarding the possibility that Li Zhenxiu may become the first mainland-spouse people’s representative, the Mainland Affairs Council said that public officials cannot hold “dual nationality.” Li Zhenxiu said, “It is very absurd to be elected but unable to take office.” Some public opinion on the island holds that the DPP authorities are trampling on the “dignity of the Constitution and laws.” What…","First question: There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. The DPP authorities' deliberate political manipulation is a deliberate provocation against the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China.\nSecond question: Xinhua News Agency has already made an objective and truthful report on President Xi Jinping's meeting with U.S. President Joe Biden in Lima. The DPP authorities disregard the facts, are habitual liars, and go to great lengths to create an information cocoon on the island, blocking true information that is unfavorable to them. Where they cannot block it, they resort to so-called “cognitive warfare” to confuse right and wrong and deceive the public.\nThird question: We have always supported normal, lawful, and compliant film exchange activities across the Taiwan Strait. Speaking of promoting cross-Strait film and cultural exchanges, the mainland already abolished the quota limit on Taiwan films screened on the mainland in 2010. We also hope that the island will abolish the quota limit on mainland films screened in Taiwan, so that more Taiwan audiences can see good and excellent mainland films. As for recommending films, you may follow some well-known film review websites on the mainland.\nFourth question: According to relevant regulations of the Ministry of Civil Affairs, a certificate of (no) marriage registration record may be issued for notarization matters related to Taiwan. It should be noted that the Civil Code of the People's Republic of China has specific provisions: the parties to a marriage refer to a man and a woman who meet the legal conditions for marriage. Same-sex couples applying for marriage registration do not comply with the provisions of mainland law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","Taiwan’s foreign affairs department claims that, in order to consolidate so-called “allied” relations, next year’s “confidential budget” will be increased by more than 50% over this year, reaching a six-year high. Public opinion on the island questions why the foreign affairs budget keeps rising year after year while the number of the Taiwan authorities’ “diplomatic allies” continues to decline. What is your comment?","Spending money to buy “recognition” and maintain “diplomatic relations” is a routine tactic of the DPP authorities. To seek political gain and obtain so-called “diplomatic recognition,” they lavishly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s ordinary people. This out-and-out “checkbook diplomacy” and “sugar daddy diplomacy” harms Taiwan and its people and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Regarding the demands of the Taiwan Travel Agents Association and tourism operators, the Mainland Affairs Council says the biggest obstacle to cross-Strait tourism exchanges is that the mainland does not allow mainland tourists to visit Taiwan. What is your comment? The spokesperson just mentioned that the mainland is studying further expanding travel to Taiwan by mainland residents. Is there a…","On the first question, it must be pointed out that the obstacles preventing the normalization and regularization of cross-Strait tourism lie with the DPP authorities. We have already resumed tourism by mainland residents to Matsu and Kinmen. If the DPP authorities lift the “group tour ban” and remove the various obstacles restricting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and interactions, we will actively study expanding tourism to Taiwan by mainland residents, not only to Taiwan Island but also including Penghu. However, the premise is that the DPP authorities must remove the various obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation and exchanges in all fields.\nOn the second question, the motherland will eventually be reunified, and reunification is inevitable. This is the irresistible historical trend. The mainland's adoption of the socialist path is the choice of history, demonstrating remarkable institutional and governance advantages and strong vitality, and it has won the sincere support and backing of more than 1.4 billion people. We advocate achieving peaceful reunification in accordance with the principle of “one country, two systems.” The mainland will continue to unwaveringly follow the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics, while Taiwan would keep its existing social system and way of life unchanged, with the two systems coexisting and seeking common development. We hope that relevant political parties, groups, and individuals on the island will join us in grasping the historical trend, upholding the great righteousness of the nation, jointly promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and realizing national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-11-27","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan media reported that in recent years Taiwan's US arms purchase quota has been “bought to the bottom,” causing the so-called “force structure improvement plans” of the Taiwan military over the past three years to all be weapons projects that the US has long failed to deliver and that remain unfinished. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming Taiwan, and stop encouraging the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to “seek independence by force.”\nThe DPP authorities’ “relying on external forces to seek independence” will only end with them being at others’ mercy. Buying weapons from external forces cannot buy security; it only squeezes island society and livelihood spending, only makes the people on the island feel less secure, and only makes Taiwan more prone to bloodshed and war.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202411/t20241127_12667244.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-11-28","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te will stop over in Hawaii and Guam during his trip to the Pacific. Does China have a comment on this?","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ political manipulation and separatist provocations by visiting countries having so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan will lead nowhere. It will not shake the solid and strong international commitment to the one-China principle or stop the overriding historical trend towards China’s reunification. We have all along opposed official interactions between the US and the Taiwan region, opposed any visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and opposed any form of US connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495793.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495546.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-11-28","Mao Ning","AFP","Reuters has reported that China is likely to launch military drills near Taiwan around or shortly after Lai Ching-te’s visit to the Pacific. What is China’s comment on this?","I made clear China’s position on Lai Ching-te’s visit just now, and your question is not about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495793.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495546.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-11-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to foreign media reports, anonymous Taiwan officials said Taiwan has submitted, through informal channels, a list of arms purchase requests to the United States, with a total amount reaching 15 billion U.S. dollars. Scholars believe this move is the Lai authorities' statement to the U.S. of the “Taiwan identity protection fee principle.” Many people on the island have said, “There is no need to buy, and…","The DPP authorities are willing to be the “chump” and the “ATM” of the United States. Disregarding public opposition, they are using the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people to pay “protection money” to the United States. What they will get is not protection, but further exploitation and use. Faced with the powerful People's Liberation Army of China, any attempt to “rely on the U.S. to seek independence” or “seek independence through force” is futile. The people on the island see this very clearly. If the DPP authorities remain stubborn and unrepentant, they will ultimately only be playing with fire and bringing about their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16354972.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-11-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Lai Ching-te plans to transit Hawaii during his trip in late November or early December. What is your comment? Will the PLA take corresponding military countermeasures?","We firmly oppose any country conducting any form of official exchange with the Taiwan region of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities’ political manipulation and provocations aimed at “independence” are futile and cannot stop the historical trend of China’s inevitable unification. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not to send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces, and to maintain China-US relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army bears the sacred mission of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and will resolutely crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and firmly thwart all interference by external forces.\nOn the afternoon of November 28, the Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference,\nReporters asked questions on site.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16354972.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-11-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","At the recent Zhuhai Airshow, several domestically produced equipment items, including the J-35A, made their first public appearances, attracting high attention from international public opinion. Some US figures have said that China has become the second country after the United States to possess two stealth fighter models at the same time. They say this will pose a strong challenge to US air superiority and…","On the first question: this year's China International Aviation and Aerospace Exhibition was a complete success, and five highlights deserve attention.\nFirst,\nMany weapons and equipment made their debut. The medium stealth multirole fighter J-35A, the HQ-19 surface-to-air missile weapon system, new reconnaissance and strike unmanned aerial vehicles, the carrier-based fighter J-15T, the carrier-based electronic warfare aircraft J-15D, and the carrier-based helicopter Z-20J were publicly displayed for the first time.\nSecond,\nInternational exchanges became more open. Air forces from 42 countries sent official delegations. Activities such as the International Military Flight Training Exchange Conference and the unmanned intelligent systems seminar attracted representatives from more than 30 countries. Foreign military friends sent birthday wishes to the Chinese Air Force, demonstrating the beautiful vision of “the same blue sky, a shared world.” For the first time, the exhibition also opened the cargo hold of the Y-20 aircraft to the public.\nThird,\nAerial performances were spectacular. The PLA Air Force “August 1st” Aerobatic Team and the “Red Eagle” Aerobatic Team performed jointly with the Russian “Warriors” Aerobatic Team, dancing across the blue sky. The J-35A's “Mach ring” and the Su-57's “falling leaf” maneuver stunned the audience. Russian pilot Sergey Bogdan's solo flight covering thousands of kilometers to attend the exhibition sparked heated discussion among netizens.\nFourth,\nThe exhibition covered equipment across all domains and dimensions. The Navy organized live equipment displays for the first time. An integrated dynamic demonstration pattern of “air, sea and land” was built for the first time. The exhibition covered all fields of “land, sea, air, space, electromagnetic and network,” multidimensionally showcasing the development achievements and cutting-edge technological accomplishments of China's aerospace and defense sectors.\nFifth,\nUnmanned intelligent equipment systems made their appearance. The exhibition specially opened unmanned aerial vehicle and unmanned vessel exhibition areas. Items such as the large unmanned combat boat “Orca,” the “Robotic Wolf” combat unit, and the “Baidi” aerospace fighter model drew immense attention once they appeared. Visitors exclaimed in admiration at the intelligent unmanned equipment, saying, “The past has not yet gone, and the future has already arrived.”\nEvery November is a time of glory for the Chinese Air Force, and this year is no exception. Over 75 years, from nothing to something, and from weak to strong, from “not enough planes, so fly each one again” to “integrated air and space, with both offense and defense capabilities,” the People's Air Force has forged an extraordinary “comeback path.” As the Chinese Air Force grows stronger, some countries may feel “sour.” This is understandable, but fabricating rumors and making slanders is wrong. As everyone knows, the growth and strengthening of the Chinese military has always been the growth and strengthening of the force for world peace. We do not pursue hegemonism, but we will never tolerate bullying by hegemonism. At 75 years old, the People's Air Force is in its prime and will always, under the strong leadership of the Party, soar high with lofty ambitions. Words alone are not enough, so please watch the video.\nOn the second question: Taiwan is part of China. What does it have to do with Japan and the United States? What do they need to respond to? If the media reports are true, the relevant movements by the US and Japan are very dangerous. No matter what situation arises, the PLA will take forceful measures to resolutely defeat interference by external forces and resolutely crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist plot.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16354972.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-11-28","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Kyodo News reported on the 21st that Japanese Defense Minister Gen Nakatani, during a meeting with Chinese Defense Minister Dong Jun in Laos on that day, expressed serious concern about the activities of the Chinese military around Japan, and said it is extremely important for the defense departments of the two countries to maintain frank communication. What is your comment on this?\nOn the 25th of this month,…","On the first question. On the afternoon of November 21, Minister of National Defense Dong Jun held frank and constructive talks with Japanese Minister of Defense Nakatani Gen in Vientiane, Laos. Minister Dong refuted Japan's groundless accusations, stressing that Japan should abide by the four China-Japan political documents and truly implement the political consensus of being “cooperative partners and not threats to each other” and the strategic mutually beneficial relationship. Minister Dong also exchanged views with Nakatani Gen on arrangements for China-Japan defense exchanges in the next stage.\nChina and Japan are close neighbors, and the bilateral relationship has significance beyond the two countries. Developing China-Japan defense relations depends on keeping the overall picture and the long term in view. We hope Japan will move toward China in the same direction, correct the course of bilateral relations, deepen practical exchanges and cooperation, and jointly safeguard the overall state of China-Japan relations and regional peace and stability.\nOn the second question. First, to clarify: Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” The Democratic Progressive Party authorities hype up a so-called “mainland military threat” only as a pretext to deceive Taiwan's people and manipulate politics with “anti-China” sentiment. The root cause of the current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and collude with external forces to constantly provoke with schemes for “independence.” The measures taken by the People's Liberation Army are legitimate and necessary actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that attempting to “seek independence by force” is a dead end and will ultimately lead only to their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16354972.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-11-29","Mao Ning","Reuters","Has China directly told the US not to allow Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te to visit Hawaii and Guam while he is on the Pacific tour?","In the meeting between Chinese and US Presidents in Lima, President Xi Jinping stressed that the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-US relations and they must be observed. Cross-Strait peace and stability and “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are irreconcilable as water and fire. If the US side cares about maintaining peace across the Taiwan Strait, it is crucial that it sees clearly the true nature of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities in seeking “Taiwan independence,” handles the Taiwan question with extra prudence, unequivocally opposes “Taiwan independence,” and supports China’s peaceful reunification.\nLet me reiterate that China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, firmly opposes any visit by the leader of the Taiwan authorities to the US in any name or under whatever pretext, and firmly opposes any form of US connivance and support for “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitments, including not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop any official interactions with the Taiwan region, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China remains resolutely determined to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and oppose interference in our internal affairs by external forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495796.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495552.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-11-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua, Beijing, November 29 — Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan responded to protests and appeals from the island's tourism industry to the “Tourism Administration” by saying that “the obstacle to cross-Strait tourism exchange lies with the mainland side.” In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office's call to lift the “group travel ban,” it said that “the mainland side has no sincerity in opening up…","Chen Binhua said that since 2020, the DPP authorities, using the COVID-19 epidemic as a pretext, have banned mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan and suspended the operation of group tours to the mainland by travel agencies on the island. As early as May 2023, the mainland had already announced the resumption of group tours for Taiwan residents to the mainland, and in April and August of this year, it made arrangements for mainland residents to travel to Matsu and Kinmen and for group tours to the island, respectively. However, to this day, the DPP authorities still ignore the shared aspirations of compatriots in Taiwan for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, disregard the appeals and demands of Taiwan's tourism industry and grassroots people, persist in refusing to lift the \"group tour ban,\" fail to give a substantive response to the Taiwan tourism industry's application for chartered vessel service from Pingtan to Taiwan, and do not respond directly to calls for the full restoration of cross-Strait passenger direct flights and routes, and have even raised the travel alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland to \"orange.\" The facts are abundantly clear: the crux of and obstacles to cross-Strait tourism issues lie entirely with the DPP authorities.\nHe also said that I would like to reiterate that as long as the DPP authorities lift the \"group tour ban\" and remove the various obstacles restricting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and contacts, we will actively study expanding travel to Taiwan by mainland residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202411/t20241130_12667857.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-01","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua, Beijing, December 1 (electronic dispatch): Regarding Lai Ching-te's “transit” through Hawaii under the pretext of visiting the Pacific island countries, Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, stated on the 1st in response to inquiries that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side on this matter. We firmly oppose official exchanges…","Chen Binhua said that since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have stubbornly persisted in a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, continuously engaged in provocations to seek “independence,” and constantly escalated cross-strait confrontation, seriously threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harming the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. No matter what tricks the Lai Ching-te authorities use to manipulate for “independence,” they cannot shake the basic framework of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle, and they cannot stop the historical trend that China will eventually be reunified. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, recognize the “Taiwan independence” nature and harms of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241201_12668021.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-01","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 1 (dateline): Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded on the 1st when asked: The US selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China is a serious violation of the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, particularly the August 17 Communiqué, and we firmly oppose it. The US side should fulfill its solemn political…","Chen Binhua stated: We solemnly warn the Lai Qingde authorities that buying weapons cannot buy security, “protection money” cannot protect “Taiwan independence,” and “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail. Attempting to “use force to seek independence” will only bring danger and disaster to Taiwan and ultimately lead to self-destruction. The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests, and no one or force should underestimate the Chinese people’s firm will and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241201_12668026.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-12-02","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s leader Lai Ching-te has held a phone call with former United States House Speaker Nancy Pelosi as Lai’s on a Pacific trip that includes a stop in Hawaii. And during the call, Lai and Pelosi discussed “China’s military threats,” according to a spokesperson for Lai. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, and firmly opposes any form of US moves to aid or abet “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. We urge the US to fully see the separatist nature of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, fully understand the grave damage of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, fully abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop meddling in affairs related to Taiwan, which are China’s internal affairs, and stop aiding and abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495801.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495554.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-02","Lin Jian","China Review News","It’s reported that during his “visit” to Taiwan, Paraguay Foreign Minister Ruben Dario Ramirez Lezcano said on November 29 “Paraguay is open to establish diplomatic, consular or commercial relations with China without conditions,” but he added “We don’t accept any condition to break our relations with Taiwan.” What’s your response?","The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. It is also the political foundation and important prerequisite for China to develop bilateral ties with other countries. The one-China principle bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and there is no room for negotiation or compromise.\nParaguay needs to establish an accurate and full understanding of the one-China principle, recognize as early as possible where the arc of history bends, stand on the side of the vast majority of countries in the world, and on the side of international fairness and justice, and make the decision that truly serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the people of Paraguay.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495801.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495554.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-12-02","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency recently announced that the U.S. has approved an arms sales plan to Taiwan valued at about US$385 million. What is your comment on this?","Wu Qian: US arms sales to Taiwan region of China seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the provisions of the August 17 Communiqué. They seriously damage China's sovereignty and security interests, undermine China-US relations and China-US military-to-military relations, and endanger peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose this, and have lodged stern representations with the US side.\nUS arms sales to Taiwan have long been notorious. The US claims to be upholding peace and promoting stability, but in practice it interferes in internal affairs and undermines peace, and the international community has long seen this clearly. Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities are willing to sacrifice the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, paying “protection fees” to the US with the hard-earned money of ordinary people in an attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” In the end, they will only be like moths drawn to a flame, seeking their own destruction.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the foundation of the political basis of China-US relations, and it is the first red line that China-US relations must not cross. We urge the US side to genuinely honor its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” to stop arming Taiwan in any way, and to uphold the overall picture of China-US relations and military-to-military relations through concrete actions. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness and will resolutely thwart any “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and interference by external forces.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16355587.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-12-03","Lin Jian","Reuters","Does China plan to hold more war games around Taiwan once Lai Ching-te returns at the end of the week?","The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. Nothing will deter China from upholding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. China will be closely watching the situation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495804.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495558.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-05","Lin Jian","Phoenix TV","The Foreign Ministry just announced on its website the decision to take countermeasures against 13 US military companies and six senior executives. Do you have further comment on this?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests. In recent months, the US has announced multiple arms sales to China’s Taiwan region. This gravely violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, interferes in China’s internal affairs, and undermines China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In accordance with the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law of the People’s Republic of China, China decided to take countermeasures against relevant military companies and senior executives of the US.\nLet me stress that “Taiwan independence” is as incompatible with peace in the Taiwan Strait as fire with water. The US attempts to assist in the “Taiwan independence” agenda by arming Taiwan. This will not shake our firm resolve to oppose “Taiwan independence” and realize national reunification, and will only push Taiwan towards military danger.\nChina urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, act on the US leaders’ commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop arming Taiwan at once, and stop abetting and aiding separatists’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495808.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495561.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-05","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s leader Lai Ching-te spoke with US Speaker of the House Mike Johnson over the phone yesterday. Does China have a comment on this phone call?","In recent weeks, we have made clear our serious opposition more than once to the US’s arranging for Lai Ching-te’s “stopovers” and having official interactions with the Taiwan region. Let me stress once again that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. We urge the US to fully understand the grave damage that “Taiwan independence” separatist activities do to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, fully abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on the US leaders’ commitments, including not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China will take resolute and strong measures to defend our nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495808.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495561.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-06","Lin Jian","China Review News","It’s reported that the leader of China’s Taiwan region Lai Ching-te has concluded his “stopovers” in Hawaii and Guam of the US. What’s your comment？","By arranging for the “stopovers” of the leader of China’s Taiwan region Lai Ching-te in Hawaii and Guam, having official interactions with the Taiwan region, helping Taiwan expand so-called “international space,” and providing platforms for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, the US gravely violated the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués. The actions it took undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and send a severely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores this and has lodged strong protests to the US side.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations and a basic norm in international relations. The Taiwan question is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are as incompatible with peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as fire with water. China urges the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on the US leaders’ commitment, including not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop its official interactions with Taiwan, stop obscuring and hollowing out the one-China principle, stop abetting and aiding the separatist forces and their activities in any form, and take concrete actions to stabilize China-US relations and contribute to peace in the Taiwan Strait.\nLet me stress that attempts to solicit US support for “Taiwan independence” or use the Taiwan question to contain China will lead nowhere. No one should underestimate the firm resolve, will and ability of the Chinese government and people to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495818.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495569.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-06","Lin Jian","Reuters","I would also like to ask about Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te and his return. Does China plan to stage more war games around the island as a result?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations. China remains unwavering in its resolve to defend our nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495818.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495569.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-06","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Just to follow up again on this one. Taiwan leader Lai said on Friday that he was confident of deeper cooperation with the next administration of Donald Trump. This is coming after he had a call earlier with US Republican House Speaker Mike Johnson. Can you comment on the confidence of deeper cooperation with the next Donald Trump administration?","We have made clear our serious position on this more than once. China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the US and the Taiwan region, and firmly opposes any form of US moves to aid or abet “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities.\nWe urge the US to fully see the separatist nature of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, fully understand the grave damage that “Taiwan independence” separatist activities do to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, fully abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop meddling in affairs related to Taiwan, which are China’s internal affairs, and stop aiding and abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495818.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495569.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-06","Lin Jian","AFP","Paraguay’s Foreign Ministry said yesterday that they have canceled the visa of a Chinese diplomat and given him 24 hours to leave the country due to what they called “interference in internal affairs.” Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","The delegation of the Chinese government has been in Paraguay upon invitation to attend the 19th session of the Intergovernmental Committee for the Safeguarding of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of UNESCO. The relevant department of Paraguay—a member state of the UN and UNESCO and the host country of the 19th session meeting—made unfounded and unjustified accusation and demand against a relevant member of the Chinese delegation. This is seriously inconsistent with international practice. China is firmly opposed to it.\nLet me stress that there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is what has been affirmed in Resolution 2758 of the UN General Assembly and is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus among the international community. It is right and just to defend and uphold the one-China principle, no matter where we are. There’s no so-called “interference in internal affairs.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495818.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495569.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-06","Lin Jian","AFP","I just wanted to return to follow up quickly on Taiwan. And there were some specific comments from Lai Ching-te. He said today while in Palau that Taiwan and China were “not subordinates to each other.” Do you have any specific response to these comments?","The biggest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and those external forces who aid and abet those separatists. Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities have been engaging in separatist activities for “Taiwan independence” under various pretexts. No matter what they say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they stop the overriding historical trend toward China’s reunification. To try to achieve “Taiwan independence” by seeking foreign support will surely end in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495818.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495569.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-12-06","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲6日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 6 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, answered a reporter's question on the 6th, saying that regarding Lai Ching-te's “transit” through the United States, we have stated our solemn position many times. Lai Ching-te's conduct during the “transit” has once again proven that the so-called “transit” is merely a pretext, and is in fact a…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible like fire and water. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly cling to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and escalate cross-Strait confrontation; they shamelessly rely on external forces and continue to provoke and seek independence internationally; they deliberately “seek independence by force,” attempting to tie the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, which will ultimately bring profound disaster to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nZhu Fenglian said that we urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, and fulfill its solemn commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” through concrete action. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the United States to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” are a dead end and are doomed to fail. We will not leave any room whatsoever for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and we will firmly thwart any interference by external forces and any “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241206_12669362.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-07","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲6日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 6 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered a reporter’s question on the 6th, saying: The DPP authorities, in collusion with specific media and internet troll armies on the island, have subjected members of the delegation of mainland university faculty and students visiting Taiwan, who congratulated the “Chinese Taipei team,” to…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet fully reunified, the fact that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed. There is no problem with the use of the term “Chinese Taipei.” The DPP authorities have loudly used the occasion to threaten relevant institutions carrying out cross-Strait exchanges, attempting to create “green terror,” which fully exposes their nature of insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position and inciting cross-Strait confrontation. What are they afraid of, that they so maliciously obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation? People on both sides of the Strait see very clearly: they are afraid of compatriots on both sides getting closer and forming friendships; they are afraid that the people of Taiwan will understand the real situation on the mainland and the sincere friendliness of mainland compatriots; they are afraid that their carefully fabricated lies will be exposed; they are afraid that their “anti-China card” will fail.\nZhu Fenglian said that the foundation of cross-Strait relations lies among the people, and its driving force lies with the people; the results of exchanges and cooperation benefit compatriots on both sides. As long as something is conducive to enhancing compatriots’ kinship and well-being, and conducive to deepening mutual understanding and recognition, we will do it with heart, sincerity, and effort, and we will certainly do it well. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides and the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society. Any scheme to obstruct or undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation will ultimately fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241207_12669413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-12-09","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan’s ministry of defense said today it detected Chinese warships and coast guard vessels in waters surrounding Taiwan and said that the People’s Liberation Army has restricted the airspace off the Chinese coast. What is China’s comment? Is China conducting military drills around Taiwan?","First of all, there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s ministry of defense.” Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. China will firmly defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495824.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495571.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-10","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan said today that China’s recent deployment of ships in waters around the island is bigger than the military drills in 2022 after then US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi visited Taipei. Does the Foreign Ministry have comment on this and is China currently conducting or does China plan to conduct military drills around Taiwan this week?","I’d refer you to competent Chinese authorities for the specific question. What I can tell you is that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and China will firmly defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495828.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495574.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-11","Mao Ning","AFP","A senior security official in Taiwan told AFP today that apparent military drills conducted by China this week around the island are aimed at drawing a red line ahead of the incoming US presidential administration of Donald Trump. Can the Foreign Ministry confirm today these Chinese military drills and does it have any comment?","I would refer you to the competent Chinese authorities for your specific question. Let me say that the Taiwan question is the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-US relations and this has always been our position. Upholding the one-China principle is the key to ensuring peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. China will firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495833.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495577.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 11, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first announced that the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival will soon be held, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone, and welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Before taking questions, I would like to announce an event to everyone.\nFrom December 18 to 24, the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival will be held in Harbin, Heilongjiang Province, and relevant prefectures and cities. Under the theme \"Ignite Ice and Snow, Walk Together,\" the festival will hold the launch ceremony, the cross-Strait youth short video showcase and awards on December 19, and during the period will also host multiple activities including a cross-Strait youth exchange symposium, a tour of venues for the 9th Asian Winter Games, ice and snow experiences, and visits and exchanges. Currently, registration by Taiwan compatriots is enthusiastic and participation is very high, with approximately 1,000 Taiwan compatriots, mainly Taiwan youth, expected to take part in the ice and snow festival activities.\nWinter in Heilongjiang is a fairyland of ice and a kingdom of snow. The festival highlights ice and snow characteristics, aligns with the characteristics of youth, and features novel and lively forms and rich, substantive content. Combining participation and fun, it will let everyone personally experience the joy of ice and snow, and experience the vastness of our motherland's territory and the magnificence of winter in Longjiang. We believe that Taiwan compatriots participating in the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival will certainly not have made the trip in vain. We welcome media reporters to visit and cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670558.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","It is reported that Ma Yingjiu will soon lead Taiwan youth to the mainland to attend relevant events and make a visit. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Ma Ying-jeou will lead Taiwan youth to Heilongjiang and Sichuan from December 18 to 26 to attend and visit the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival. We welcome Ma Ying-jeou’s visit with his delegation again, and we will make all necessary arrangements for the activities. China has a long history, brilliant culture, vast territory, and magnificent mountains and rivers, and it is the common home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Young people across the Strait carry the future and hope of cross-Strait relations. We hope that compatriots on both sides, especially young friends, will visit each other often and move about more, jointly carry forward and promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture, work hand in hand to advance exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, and together protect and build our common home, striving for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670557.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The 2024 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting was held in Xiamen on the 9th and 10th. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 2024 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Annual Meeting was successfully held in Xiamen, Fujian Province, from December 9 to 10. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, sent a congratulatory letter on behalf of General Secretary Xi Jinping and the CPC Central Committee. The letter highly affirmed the summit's important contributions to promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. It encouraged the summit to continue playing its bridging and linking role, to enhance cross-Strait exchanges and interaction, to promote high-quality development of cross-Strait economic cooperation, and to grow the Chinese nation's economy. It also expressed the hope that compatriots and entrepreneurs on both sides, upholding national righteousness and keeping pace with the trend of the times, would grasp the correct direction for the development of cross-Strait relations and jointly write a splendid chapter of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nSong Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, met with representatives of Taiwanese entrepreneurs during the summit. He further elaborated on the powerful momentum and favorable conditions that Chinese-style modernization brings to cross-Strait economic cooperation, and looked ahead to the bright prospects for integrated development across the Strait. The Taiwanese entrepreneur representatives attending expressed, one after another, their anticipation of deepening cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, and their confidence in investing in the mainland's development.\nMore than 700 industrial and business figures from both sides of the Strait attended the annual meeting. Centered on the theme “Building a Cross-Strait Industrial Chain for a New Era and Promoting Integrated Economic Development across the Strait,” they conducted in-depth discussions on topics including promoting cross-Strait industrial internet innovation, building the “first home” for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses entering the mainland, and innovating the cross-Strait financial services system. The atmosphere of exchange was warm, fully demonstrating the shared desire of industry circles on both sides to strengthen exchange and cooperation.\nWe will thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on work concerning Taiwan and the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee. We will promote economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, deepen integrated development in all fields across the Strait, support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses in participating in the construction of Chinese-style modernization, share the mainland's achievements in development and progress, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","“Spring Festival—Social Practices of the Chinese People in Celebrating the Traditional New Year” was recently inscribed on the UNESCO Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Compatriots in Taiwan are delighted and say, “This is excellent Chinese traditional culture.” What comment do you have?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, a crucial moment for bidding farewell to the old and welcoming the new and for family reunions, and the most important cultural symbol in the hearts of the sons and daughters of China. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and are descendants of the Yan and Huang emperors. We are all Chinese, and we deeply understand that the Spring Festival embodies the Chinese nation’s and Chinese civilization’s pursuit of values of peace, harmony and coherence. Fifty days from now, we will welcome the Spring Festival of the Lunar Year of the Snake. We sincerely wish that people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will celebrate the Spring Festival together and jointly promote the rich and colorful Spring Festival culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》栏目记者","Recently, the working conference of the inter-ministerial coordination mechanism for promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation was held in Beijing. Please introduce the relevant situation.","This October, General Secretary Xi Jinping, while inspecting Fujian, gave important instructions on Taiwan work, stressing “taking greater strides in exploring a new path for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait” and “building a well-functioning demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development,” further setting clear goals and pointing the direction for exploring a new path for integrated development across the Strait and building the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone.\nTo implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions on Taiwan work, on December 3 the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission, together with 48 central and state organs and relevant departments and Fujian Province, convened in Beijing an inter-ministerial coordination mechanism meeting on promoting cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange, and cooperation. The meeting studied and discussed the policies (matters) that Fujian Province requested central and state organs to support, deployed key tasks for the next stage, and further promoted the thorough and detailed implementation of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.”\nNext, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will continue, together with central and state organs, relevant departments, and Fujian Province, to practice the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” emphasize promoting integration through connectivity, through benefits, and through affection, continuously improve and roll out innovative measures, and fully support Fujian in taking greater strides and achieving more success in exploring a new path for integrated development across the Strait and building the demonstration zone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Chen Yu-chen, a Kuomintang people's representative, recently invited relevant parties and financial figures from the island to conduct an on-site inspection in Kinmen. She said she hopes banks and securities firms will set up branches in Kinmen, making Kinmen a pilot area for cross-Strait financial pilot programs. What comments do you have on this?","In April 2009, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait (ARATS) and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) signed the “Cross-Strait Financial Cooperation Agreement.” Under this framework, the two sides established a financial supervision cooperation mechanism and a currency clearing mechanism, and successively introduced relevant policies to open up cross-Strait financial industries, providing important support for the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial cooperation. In 2023, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were issued, explicitly proposing tasks and measures such as supporting the building of a multi-level cross-Strait financial market, innovating ways of cross-Strait social capital cooperation, and creating a “same-city living circle” for Xiamen and Kinmen.\nWe are willing to explore, together with compatriots in Kinmen, new paths and new models for integrated development in the cross-Strait financial field, and to share the new opportunities brought by the mainland's deepening of financial system reform.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670553.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","A delegation of 40 teachers and students from mainland universities has just completed a 9-day, 8-night visit to Taiwan, and the itinerary was very successful. What is your assessment of the delegation’s visit? What measures will be taken next to further promote exchanges between young people across the Strait?","A mainland university faculty and student delegation consisting of 40 teachers and students from 7 universities, led by Qiu Yong, academician, Party Secretary of Tsinghua University and Director of its University Council, visited Taiwan for exchanges from November 27 to December 5. During their stay in Taiwan, the delegation held exchanges with 6 universities and 1 senior high school in Taiwan, and also visited Taiwan's historical and cultural sites and corporate exhibition halls.\nWe have seen that all walks of life in Taiwan warmly welcomed and actively supported this reciprocal youth appointment. Taiwan residents saw the youthful bearing of mainland youth represented by Olympic champions Ma Long and Yang Qian, and saw their sincerity and goodwill in getting to know Taiwan. Taiwan children received Ma Long's autographed table tennis paddles. Some said, \"We are very happy, the whole family likes Ma Long,\" while others said, \"I feel more motivated to practice, and I hope to have a chance to come to the mainland to learn table tennis.\" The mainland faculty and student delegation also felt the warmth and friendliness of the Taiwan people. Wherever they went, the voices of \"Welcome to Taiwan\" and \"Thank you for coming\" never stopped. They felt the genuine willingness of Taiwan residents to exchange with the mainland. They received many handwritten letters and postcards from Taiwan residents, as well as many small gifts carefully prepared by Taiwan people... Many Taiwan youths and members of the delegation arranged to meet again next year, looking forward to more exchanges across the Strait. Through their own actions and efforts, they promoted cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, drew compatriots on both sides closer together, and demonstrated the deep affection between compatriots.\n\"We share the same mountains, rain and clouds; the bright moon, how could it belong to two different homelands?\" We will, as always, support and promote cross-Strait youth exchanges, continue to build more platforms and create more opportunities for cross-Strait youth to learn from and draw on each other, and to exchange heart to heart, so that cross-Strait youth can contribute even greater strength to promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670556.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, some audiovisual works involving Taiwan-related themes have won awards in selection and commendation activities such as the “Five One Project.” Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, the Publicity Department of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China issued a decision commending the winners of the 17th national “Five One Project” awards for spiritual civilization construction. The Taiwan-themed documentary “Letters Home Across the Strait” and the variety show “Sheng Sheng Bu Xi · Baodao Season” won the “Excellent Work Award” in the television drama/film and online literature and art categories, respectively. The “4th Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao Excellent Audiovisual Works Online Exhibition” selected 35 works, including “Gui Qu Lai Xi — Cross-Strait Century of Whampoa Memories” and “Liu Mingchuan in Taiwan 1884–1891 (Traditional Chinese Edition),” as “Hairong Outstanding Work Awards.” We warmly congratulate the production units and personnel of the above award-winning works!\nWe will support more production units and individuals in participating in the creation and dissemination of literary and artistic works on cross-Strait themes, including films, television dramas, documentaries, short videos, micro-short dramas, and songs, tell cross-Strait stories well, promote Chinese culture, and inject more positive energy into the development of cross-Strait relations. We also hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively follow and support literary and artistic works on cross-Strait themes and join hands to promote the vigorous development of cross-Strait cultural undertakings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670550.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","What achievements has Yunnan Province made in cross-Strait agricultural exchange and integration? Please introduce them.","Yunnan Province thoroughly implements the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” and a series of policies that benefit Taiwan and its people. It gives full play to Yunnan's unique advantages in climate, environment, and resources, as well as Taiwan's strengths in management, marketing, and technology. Focusing on industries such as “Yun flowers,” “Yun tea,” “Yun coffee,” and “Yun fruit,” it vigorously promotes high-quality development of Yunnan's plateau characteristic agriculture, opens markets at home and abroad, builds brand effects, and makes positive contributions to supporting rural revitalization and serving Yunnan's high-quality, leapfrog development.\nIn flowers and tea, Taiwan-invested flower enterprises represented by Kunming Tongyi Biotechnology Co., Ltd., Yunnan Xiuhai Biotechnology Co., Ltd., and Yuxi Juyang Horticulture Co., Ltd. lead innovative development. Juyang Horticulture Co., Ltd. has set up 5 production bases in Yunnan and exports more than 3 million plants of various flower products each year. Taiwan-invested tea enterprises represented by Kunming Tianfu Tea Co., Ltd. of the TenFu Group, Lancang Yuling Ancient Tea Garden Development Co., Ltd., and Yunnan Dayou Tea Co., Ltd. have elevated Pu'er tea, renowned at home and abroad, to a new realm as an ecological, green, healthy, and wellness beverage.\nIn coffee and fruit, Taiwan-invested coffee enterprises represented by Lianxing Tropical Crops Development (Yunnan) Co., Ltd. and Yunnan Yunshan Coffee Co., Ltd. are dedicated to improving and cultivating coffee varieties and to roasting and deep processing of coffee beans, injecting new momentum into the development of Yunnan's coffee industry. Taiwan-invested fruit enterprises represented by Yunnan Bafang Agricultural Science and Technology Development Co., Ltd., Wenshan Tainong Agriculture Co., Ltd., and Yuanquan Fruit and Vegetable Planting Co., Ltd. grow ecological, high-value-added fruits such as lemons, avocados, strawberries, and raspberries. Among them, a cumulative 2,337 mu of avocado orchards have been planted in Baoshan, with output this year expected to approach 500 tons. The first batch of avocados was exported to Singapore in November, realizing the dream of bringing Yunnan avocados to the world.\nWe welcome more Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to develop in Yunnan, to further deepen exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development between Yunnan and Taiwan in agriculture, and we also welcome more consumers to support high-quality agricultural products such as flowers, tea, coffee, and fruit produced by Taiwan-invested enterprises in Yunnan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","It is reported that the 2024 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held in Taipei on December 17. Please introduce the relevant situation.","It is understood that, after consultation between the cities of Shanghai and Taipei, the 2024 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum is scheduled to be held in Taipei on December 17, and Shanghai City will send a delegation to Taiwan to attend the forum. The theme of this forum is “Smart Governance, Sustainable Future,” and it will promote interaction and exchanges between the two cities in areas such as friendly transportation, river management, and humanistic cities. During the forum, the two cities will also sign relevant memoranda of exchange and cooperation. We hope the forum can proceed smoothly and be a success.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Guangdong Province recently held colorful cross-Strait exchange activities. Could you introduce the relevant situation?","Recently, various parts of Guangdong have held cross-Strait exchange activities in diverse forms. Here I will introduce two of the main activities.\nOn December 5, the opening ceremony of the 2nd Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Month and the 5th Cross-Strait Student Baseball League Finals, themed “Youth Power, Happy Homeland,” was held in Shenzhen, with more than 3,000 people from all sectors across the Strait and young people participating. The Integration Month runs from late November to late December, with 43 series of activities covering culture, education, technology, sports, grassroots, youth, folk beliefs, and other fields, and is expected to attract more than 10,000 compatriots from both sides of the Strait. The Integration Month focuses on youth elements and showcases the image of youth. For the first time, it held the “Crossing the Strait, Dancing Youth” cross-Strait youth street dance exchange competition, held several consecutive Taiwan youth Shenzhen entrepreneurship tour events, further expanded the scale of the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League Finals, and added two new categories, women’s baseball and softball, attracting nearly 500 players from 19 Taiwan teams.\nOn December 10, the “2024 Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Media Guangzhou Tour” was launched in Guangzhou. Under the theme “Exploring the Charm of Guangzhou’s Three Veins and Experiencing Chinese-Style Modernization,” 36 media professionals from 25 media outlets across the two sides of the Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao used a citywalk format to immerse themselves in Guangzhou’s thousand-year-old urban, cultural, and commercial veins, covering science and technology innovation, Lingnan culture, Taiwan youth entrepreneurship, and more. They comprehensively, multi-levelly, and broadly understood the achievements of integrated development between Guangzhou and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council recently stated that during the visit of a mainland university faculty and student delegation to Taiwan, PLA joint combat readiness patrols and other military operations continued. The Taiwan people cannot accept the mainland side’s “political maneuver” of “exchanges with one hand, military intimidation with the other.” What is your comment on this?","The statements of the DPP authorities are completely aimed at confusing public perception. The visit to Taiwan by a delegation of mainland university faculty and students for exchanges and exploration received a warm welcome and a friendly response from the people of Taiwan, fully demonstrating that the mainstream public opinion on the island is for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We will continue to vigorously support and promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and enhance the interests and well-being of people on both sides of the Strait.\nAt the same time, we firmly oppose the conduct of “Taiwan independence” separatists colluding with external forces to provoke “independence” and undermine cross-strait relations. Lai Ching-te’s roaming visit to Pacific island countries, during which he opportunistically “transited” the United States, peddled the “Taiwan independence” position under the guise of “democracy,” misled international perception, and attempted to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” We must counter and punish such provocations.\nWe hope the people of Taiwan will recognize the malicious intent of the DPP authorities in stubbornly insisting on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, continuously carrying out provocations to seek “independence,” and escalating hostility and confrontation across the Strait. We hope they will recognize the severe harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and earnestly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670554.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities demanded that general education courses at military colleges and universities on the island delete the course “Modern Chinese History,” replace it with “World History,” and reduce the credits for related courses, including those on Sun Tzu's “Art of War.” What comments do you have on this?","Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have vigorously pursued “de-Sinicization.” Previously they introduced the so-called “education reform” policy and “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines, and this time they have again revised military academy courses on the island, so that military academy students cannot learn about the history of the War of Resistance and cannot learn the wisdom of ancient Chinese people. They are attempting, through various means, to cut off the historical and cultural ties across the Strait, thereby deceiving the people of Taiwan and tricking Taiwan's young people into going into battle for “Taiwan independence” as its cannon fodder. This requires a high level of vigilance.\nFacts have already proven and will continue to prove that no act of “de-Sinicization” can sever the historical ties across the Strait or the blood ties between compatriots on both sides, much less change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. The reckless conduct of the DPP authorities will certainly meet with increasing firm opposition from more and more Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670552.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The DPP caucus in Taiwan's legislature recently posted on social media in support of the South Korean president's declaration of martial law, and then deleted the post. This drew strong criticism from all quarters on the island, which believe the DPP is using so-called “democracy” to package its inner desire to suppress “opposition” forces, and to divide the two sides and create imaginary enemies for ideological…","The DPP is 'fake democracy, real dictatorship'. It vigorously carries out 'green terror' on the island. Its record of misdeeds is plain for all to see, and it has lost popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","Regarding the possibility that the US may ask TSMC to transfer advanced process technology to the United States, the DPP authorities recently said, “It will sooner or later be produced in the United States,” and confirmed that TSMC’s board of directors will move to the United States in the first quarter of next year. Former TSMC Chairman Liu Deyin said, “Moving technology to the US will lose tens of billions of…","TSMC has become the “pledge of allegiance” the DPP authorities use to curry favor with the United States. As some public opinion on the island has said, with the DPP authorities resolutely and without bottom line “relying on the United States to seek independence,” it is only a matter of time before TSMC becomes “AmeriTSMC.” If the DPP authorities are allowed to unscrupulously “sell out Taiwan,” the advantages of Taiwan’s related industries will inevitably be weakened, and the interests of enterprises and the public on the island will inevitably be harmed. When Taiwan’s utility has been squeezed dry, the “chess piece” will become a “discarded piece,” and enterprises and the public on the island are seeing this more and more clearly.\nIt must be pointed out that many Taiwanese enterprises have achieved rapid development by participating in cross-Strait cooperation, which fully proves that the right path is for both sides of the Strait to join hands to strengthen the Chinese nation’s economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670551.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","The character “争” (zhēng, meaning “contend” or “strive”) was selected as the 2024 Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year. The organizers stated that the character “争” contains profound insights into the direction of cross-Strait relations: how to seek development in “competition,” how to seek consensus in “non-contention,” and how to pursue a better future for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait by…","“Striving” and “not striving” embody the traditional wisdom and value pursuits of the Chinese people. “As Heaven moves with vigor, the gentleman strives unceasingly to improve himself.” “Striving” is our attitude and direction on matters of principle. To safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, we must strive; to oppose separatism and foreign interference, we must strive; to achieve the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation, we must strive.\n“As the earth's terrain is receptive, the gentleman supports all things with breadth of virtue.” “Not striving” reflects our tolerance and deep affection toward our own flesh and blood. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family; matters within the family should be discussed and handled together, and they can all be properly resolved. We fully consider the realities of Taiwan, fully listen to the opinions and suggestions of all sectors of Taiwan society, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. We will improve the systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides, and work hand in hand to create the great cause of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","Taiwan-funded enterprise Want Want Group and CICC Capital recently launched industrial fund cooperation in Xiamen. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On December 6, the launch meeting for the cooperation between the Taiwan-invested enterprise Want Want Group and the CICC Capital Industry Fund was held in Tong’an, Xiamen. The Xiamen Municipal Industrial Guidance Fund, the Xiamen Tong’an Science and Innovation Parent Fund, and the Xiamen Free Trade Zone Industrial Guidance Fund all took part, providing ample capital support for the fund’s operations. This industrial fund cooperation will help promote the upgrading and innovation of Xiamen’s food, beverage, and retail industries, help attract more high-quality enterprises to settle in Xiamen and form industrial agglomeration effects, deepen Fujian-Taiwan cooperation, promote the construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone, and promote integrated development in the food sector across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","The mainland recently introduced the \"Fujian Cross-Strait Integration Measures Benefiting Taiwan,\" and the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said this is the mainland's consistent \"integration to promote unification\" tactic, aimed at \"using Taiwanese people's money to boost the economy.\" What comments do you have on this?","The policy measures we have introduced to support Fujian in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone aim to provide Taiwan compatriots studying, working and living in Fujian with the greatest possible convenience, the best possible conditions and the strongest possible guarantees. They fully demonstrate our goodwill in benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait and our sincerity in promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and they have won wide praise from compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities have slandered and smeared these measures in an attempt to obstruct Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises from participating in the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. This is entirely the “Taiwan independence” nature at work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","When Lai Ching-te recently made a \"transit\" stop in Hawaii, he claimed falsely that \"the biggest current challenge is the threat from China,\" and regarding Taiwan's future development plans, he threatened that he \"hopes to strengthen national defense capabilities.\" What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, and firmly oppose the “transit” of Taiwan's leader through the United States under any name or any pretext. Lai Ching-te's so-called “transit” is in essence “seeking independence by relying on external forces,” attempting to mislead international public opinion and the people on the island by peddling his “Taiwan independence” position.\nThe greatest challenge to current cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, collude with external forces, and frequently engage in provocations aimed at independence, binding Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to abandon as soon as possible their illusions of “seeking independence by force” and “seeking independence by relying on external forces,” and to stop “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. Only by returning to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development, and only then can Taiwan's development prospects be effectively safeguarded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241211_12670555.htm"],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The Mainland Affairs Council said that, given that the Hong Kong national security law and judicial documents on punishing “independence” “threaten the personal safety of Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland,” lifting the ban on group tours to the mainland requires evaluation. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities deliberately muddy the waters and use excuses to refuse to lift the “group travel ban” to the mainland. This further exposes their nature of pursuing “independence” and confrontation, and shows they have no willingness to promote personnel exchanges across the Strait or to bring benefits to Taiwan's tourism industry and grassroots people. This has provoked stronger dissatisfaction and opposition from the island's industry and broad Taiwan compatriots.\nWe uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” always respect, care for, and bring benefits to Taiwan compatriots, and consistently support normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and normalizing exchanges in all fields, including tourism. We warmly welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for sightseeing and tourism, visit relatives and friends, exchange visits, and study and work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The British House of Commons recently passed a so-called motion on “Taiwan’s international status,” stating that “UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 did not establish the PRC’s sovereignty over Taiwan, nor did it mention Taiwan’s status in the United Nations.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude, saying this move shows a stance of “supporting Taiwan.” What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. A handful of British politicians have provoked trouble on the Taiwan question, seriously violating the one-China principle. We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose this.\nIt must be stressed that Taiwan has no international legal status other than being a part of China. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted at the 26th session in 1971, restored to the People's Republic of China all of its lawful rights and the seat of the entire China, including Taiwan, in the United Nations, on the premise that Taiwan is part of China. The historical facts are clear and the legal basis is well-defined.\nWe urge the British side to abide by the one-China principle, correct its mistakes, and handle the Taiwan question with prudence and appropriateness. We warn the DPP authorities that colluding with external anti-China forces to concoct a clumsy political farce cannot shake the basic international consensus on upholding the one-China principle, and it will certainly not stop the historical trend toward China's inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Richard Bush, former Chairman of the Board of Directors of the American Institute in Taiwan, and several other well-known US experts on the Taiwan Strait issue said that the DPP authorities’ plan to increase military spending and buy large quantities of US arms is “not feasible and not useful,” which is seen as “pouring cold water” on the DPP authorities and a “wake-up call.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The DPP authorities are attempting to “pursue independence by force.” They are lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people to buy weapons and paying hefty “protection fees” and submitting a “loyalty pledge.” This is nothing but quenching thirst with poison, and it will only make Taiwan's situation dangerous and make war a grave and perilous prospect. The deeper they rely on outsiders to pursue independence, the more they harm Taiwan, and in the end they will only be courting destruction like moths drawn to flame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Recently, island internet celebrity “Ba Jiong” interviewed internet celebrity Chen Boyuan and released a so-called “CCP united front” documentary, which has sparked great controversy in Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s response?","First of all, it must be pointed out that this is yet another clumsy trick by the DPP authorities, who stage-manage and manipulate “cognitive warfare” and create “green terror.”\nSince the beginning of this year, more and more compatriots from Taiwan have shared what they have seen and heard during their travels, visits, and exchanges on the mainland through online platforms, effectively puncturing the “information cocoon” deliberately created by the DPP authorities and their hired cyber armies, and hitting a nerve for some people on the island. Feeling panicked, they have hurriedly resorted to various means of suppression and intimidation. From “slandering mainland journalists for supervising program production on the island,” to “hyping up the so-called Taiwanese entertainers invited to form parties and run for election,” to “falsely claiming that the mainland is buying Taiwanese influencers for cultural united front work against Taiwan,” they have continuously engaged in malicious hype, smears, and defamation. These shameless acts have been unanimously opposed and condemned by netizens on both sides of the strait.\nThe tide of cross-Strait exchanges is surging forward and will not stop or be interrupted. The participation of more than 3 million Taiwan compatriot visits in cross-Strait exchanges this year fully proves this. We continue to support and promote exchanges in all fields across the Strait, and we welcome more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to see for themselves, to understand the mainland and come to like it. We hope that people on both sides of the strait will clearly see through the DPP authorities' scheme to manipulate public opinion and escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and will support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation through concrete actions, promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe must emphasize that supporting cross-Strait exchanges is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. The DPP authorities' use of a handful of Taiwan youth to manipulate cognitive warfare, in an attempt to incite cross-Strait antagonism and deter cross-Strait exchanges, will not succeed. We hope that Taiwan's young people will distinguish right from wrong, uphold justice, maintain goodwill, and walk the right path, and inject positive energy into the development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The Taiwan side recently stated that the PLA has recently established seven airspace reservation zones east of Zhejiang and Fujian, that the PLA has a very large number of vessels and a very wide range of activities, and that this is intended to convey the message that the Taiwan Strait is “internalized as inland waters”; however, the mainland side has not announced any related military activities to date. May I…","We are highly vigilant against the moves of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces colluding with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke, and we will never stand by idly. We will take necessary measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","Renowned writer Chiung Yao recently passed away at her home in New Taipei, Taiwan, prompting people on both sides of the Strait to express their condolences. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Ms. Chiung Yao is a Taiwanese writer of significant influence who harbors deep affection for the mainland, and she played a positive role in promoting cross-Strait literary exchanges and film and television cooperation. We express deep condolences on the passing of Ms. Chiung Yao and extend sincere sympathy to her family.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻记者","Wang Jin-pyng, former head of Taiwan’s legislative body, recently put forward a new discourse on cross-Strait relations, advocating that “the two sides’ governing authorities are not subordinate to each other, and sovereignty is the same but not divided.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s view on this?","The historical context and legal facts clearly show that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. We are willing, on the basis of upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” to engage in exchanges, dialogue and communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups and individuals, listen to opinions and suggestions from all sectors on developing cross-Strait relations, oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and jointly work for national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The first question: the so-called documentary produced by “Ba Jiong” has drawn attention on the island. Some extreme netizens on the island have condemned Internet celebrities who traveled to the mainland and demanded that they produce “evidence of the money they were paid.” Are you concerned that when inviting Taiwan self-media or Internet celebrities to take part in activities on the mainland in the future,…","On the first question: Evil cannot prevail over righteousness, and those who are clean will remain clear. Taiwanese internet celebrities and self-media practitioners who come to the mainland to enjoy beautiful scenery and delicacies, experience diverse ways of life, and share stories of goodness and beauty do so openly and honestly. We believe more young people from Taiwan will step out of their \"cocoons\" and walk toward the light. We will, as always, support and promote exchanges between young people across the Strait, and we warmly welcome more young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to take a look, see for themselves, share what they see and hear, and deepen understanding.\nOn the second question: Young people on the mainland, represented by the visiting delegation of mainland university faculty and students, have left a deep impression on the people of Taiwan with their youthful, vibrant, learned, elegant, courteous, and friendly image, and have been warmly welcomed by the people of Taiwan. The DPP authorities and some Green camp politicians, out of political self-interest, have hyped this up on a large scale, confused the public, and taken the opportunity to incite confrontation between the peoples on both sides of the Strait and obstruct exchanges and interactions between young people across the Strait. Their intentions are very vicious, and they have also harmed the affection between compatriots on both sides. We believe that the great trend of stronger exchanges between young people across the Strait and drawing closer to one another is irresistible.\nThe press conference ends here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241211_12670543.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-12-12","Mao Ning","Reuters","Various sources indicate that to forge ties with the incoming US administration, two high-ranking officials from Taiwan have been dispatched to Washington, DC to meet with President-elect Trump’s team. What is your response to this?","Our position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués and handle the Taiwan question with prudence, and not to send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495839.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495582.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2024-12-12","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","We’ve learned that Taiwan’s “deputy foreign minister” Wu Chih-Chung today attended the inauguration ceremony of “president” of Somaliland as a “special envoy” for Lai Ching-te. What’s China’s comment?","We noted relevant reports. Let me stress once again that there’s only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. The DPP authorities’ attempt of seeking “Taiwan independence” through foreign support and their secession attempt are doomed to fail.\nChina highly commends the government of Somalia for upholding the one-China principle. We firmly support Somalia in safeguarding sovereignty and territorial integrity. China firmly opposes mutual establishment of official institutions or any form of official exchanges between Taiwan authorities and Somaliland. We urge relevant parties in Somalia to see the trend of history sooner rather than later, and strictly uphold the one-China position.\n**************************** *************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241217_11495839.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495582.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2024-12-13","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan leader Lai Ching-te recently “transited” through the US states of Hawaii and Guam. The PLA has not released any news of holding military exercises. Taiwan's defense authorities said the mainland has imposed restrictive measures on coastal airspace, and the scale of warships recently deployed around the island is larger than ever before. The Taiwan military has established a “response center” and will…","Wu Qian said that safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, safeguarding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and safeguarding the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait are the sacred duty of the People's Liberation Army. “Troops have no constant disposition, water has no constant form.” Whether to hold drills and when to hold them are decided independently by us according to our own needs and the situation of struggle. Whether or not drills are held, the PLA will not be absent or go soft in the fight against “independence” and for promoting reunification. Any conduct of “relying on external forces to seek independence” or “seeking independence through force” will inevitably be severely punished and is doomed to fail.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/20241213/2f7c3d565da14c2a8f228f7c3e6df651/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-12-16","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s defense ministry said today that it has received 38 advanced Abrams battle tanks from the US. Does China have a comment on this?","Let me first correct you by pointing out that there is no such thing as “Taiwan’s defense ministry.” China is firmly opposed to the US’s military ties with and arms sales to China’s Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal. China calls on the US to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, stop arming Taiwan, and stop abetting and aiding separatists’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup. The Taiwan authorities’ attempt of seeking “Taiwan independence” through military buildup and soliciting foreign support for that agenda will not succeed. China will firmly defend its sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241218_11501316.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241217_11495596.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲17日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 17. Regarding the 2024 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum, which has concluded, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 17th, saying that since this year's forum was due to be held in Taipei City, Shanghai City, following past practice and work needs, sent a delegation to Taiwan. However, some delegation…","Zhu Fenglian said that the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been held continuously since 2010 and has achieved fruitful exchange results. The 2024 forum was held in Taipei from December 16 to 17. Representatives of the two cities engaged in in-depth exchanges and interactions, reached many positive common understandings, signed two memoranda of exchange and cooperation, achieved new results in deepening cooperation between the two cities, brought tangible benefits to people in both cities, and drew wide attention and welcome from compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and belong to one family, and they should frequently visit each other and strengthen exchanges and cooperation. We will work together with the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and advance the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241217_12671940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 17: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on the 17th, saying: We welcome the early resumption of travel to Taiwan by mainland residents, including residents of Shanghai, and the DPP authorities should remove as soon as possible the restrictions and obstruction on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and on exchanges…","Zhu Fenglian said that we uphold the concept that “cross-Strait families are one family,” and we consistently respect, care for and benefit compatriots in Taiwan. We have consistently and explicitly supported normalizing cross-Strait personnel exchanges and normalizing exchanges in all fields, including tourism. Shanghai's intentional statement on Taiwan-related tourism during the Twin Cities Forum accords with the common wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchange and cooperation. It accords with the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, especially compatriots in Taiwan, and has been welcomed by the island's public and tourism industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241217_12671941.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2024-12-19","Lin Jian","TASS","US Secretary of State Antony Blinken said in an interview with The Foreign Affairs that the US is aligning policies with Europe and with key partners in Asia and that China’s complaint is the greatest evidence of the success of the US’s approach. Blinken also said that Taiwan is not just China’s business but the world’s business and it is because the world would be influenced if there were to be a crisis over…","China views and advances its relations with the US in accordance with the three principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation, and works to firmly defend its sovereignty, security and development interest. We believe that a new Cold War should not be fought and cannot be won. Containing China is unwise, unacceptable and bound to fail. When meeting with President Biden in Lima, President Xi Jinping listed seven experiences and inspirations drawn from the past four years of China-US interactions that point the way forward for bilateral relations. We hope it will register with the US side and the two sides will work together towards that end.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no external interference. The greatest challenge to cross-Strait peace is “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign interference and disruption. The US should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241219_11506257.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241219_11505778.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-12-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On the afternoon of December 19, a fire broke out at the Quanlian Warehouse in Dadu District, Taichung City, killing 9 people and injuring 8. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said: “We express our condolences to the compatriots who died in this unfortunate incident, and we extend sincere sympathy to the families of the deceased and to the injured compatriots.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241220_12672872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-12-21","Zhang Xiaogang","N/A — spokesperson statement (no press Q)","","Recently, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2024 “Report on China's Military and Security Developments.” It distorts China's national defense policy, speculates about China's military development, brazenly interferes in China's internal affairs, and goes to great lengths to slander and smear the Chinese military, playing up the so-called “China military threat” narrative. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this.\nChina firmly follows the path of peaceful development and consistently adheres to a defensive national defense policy. It actively fulfills the international responsibilities of a major-power military and puts the Global Security Initiative and the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind into practice through concrete actions, providing more public security goods to the international community. On the contrary, the United States uses its military advantage to maintain unipolar hegemony, forcibly pursues “regime change,” incites “color revolutions,” and frequently resorts to extreme pressure. In recent years it has illegally waged wars and military operations against Iraq, Syria, Afghanistan and other countries, causing extremely severe civilian casualties and property losses and a massive humanitarian disaster: hundreds of thousands dead, millions injured, and tens of millions displaced. Facts prove that the confrontational, offensive and adventurous nature of U.S. military strategy is increasingly intensifying. The United States, addicted to war, has become the greatest disruptor of the international order and the greatest threat to global security.\nChina's nuclear policy is the most stable, consistent and predictable of all nuclear-weapon states. We adhere to a nuclear strategy of self-defense and a policy of no first use of nuclear weapons, and we always keep our nuclear forces at the minimum level required by national security needs. We develop nuclear weapons not to threaten other countries but for defense and self-defense, to safeguard national strategic security. By contrast, the United States possesses the world's largest and most advanced nuclear arsenal, yet it stubbornly maintains a policy of first use. It has invested heavily in upgrading its “triad” nuclear forces, has in recent years repeatedly conducted subcritical nuclear tests, and is accelerating the development of new nuclear warheads. Nuclear submarine cooperation among the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia seriously impacts the international nuclear nonproliferation regime and gravely undermines international and regional peace and stability. The U.S. should earnestly engage in self-reflection, reduce the role of nuclear weapons in its national and collective security policies, and give the international community a responsible account.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair, the core of China's core interests, and the first insurmountable red line in China-U.S. relations. The Chinese people resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No matter when, and no matter who tries to split Taiwan away from China, the Chinese people and the Chinese military will never accept it. The Chinese military's exercises in the sea and airspace near Taiwan target outside interference and provocations by “Taiwan independence” forces; they are a necessary and righteous measure to defend sovereignty and territorial integrity. The U.S. is intensifying its military collusion with the Taiwan region and accelerating the arming of Taiwan through arms sales and military aid. This seriously violates the one-China principle, only emboldens the arrogance of “Taiwan independence,” raises tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and could even lead to conflict and war. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, to recognize the extreme danger of “Taiwan independence” separatism and the grave consequences of playing with fire, to stop official U.S.-Taiwan exchanges and military contacts, to stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and not to go further down the wrong path.\nMilitary-to-military relations are an important component of China-U.S. relations. We attach importance to them and maintain candid and effective communication with the U.S. through military diplomatic channels. We hope the U.S. will meet us halfway, view the development of China and the Chinese military with a positive and rational attitude, take harmony as most precious, stability as paramount and good faith as fundamental as the basic guidelines for military exchanges, and, on the basis of equality and mutual respect, build a military relationship of no conflict, no confrontation, open and pragmatic cooperation, and gradually accumulated mutual trust, truly serving as a stabilizing cornerstone for the development of bilateral relations.\nFor more than twenty years, the U.S. has cobbled together and published, year after year, such deceptive and hypocritical reports merely to find excuses for its own military buildup and to mislead public opinion. We urge the U.S. to stop fabricating false narratives, correct its mistaken perceptions of China, and promote the healthy and stable development of relations between the two countries and their militaries.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16360252.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2024-12-22","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲22日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 22 (dispatch): The US side announced a new round of military aid and arms sales plans for Taiwan, and the DPP authorities expressed thanks immediately. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered a reporter’s question on the 22nd, saying: We firmly oppose any provision of weapons to the Taiwan region of China by the…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference are the greatest threats to peace in the Taiwan Strait. We demand that the US immediately stop arming Taiwan and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution. We warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the US to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” are a road to self-destruction. We will take firm and forceful measures to resolutely defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241222_12673103.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-12-23","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say the U.S. government recently approved the provision of military assistance worth about $571.3 million to Taiwan, and the U.S. State Department on the same day approved $295 million in arms sales to Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The United States' provision of military aid and arms sales to the Taiwan region of China seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué. It brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, sends a wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” secessionist forces, and seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose and strongly condemn this, and we have lodged stern representations with the U.S. side.\nThe Taiwan question is the first red line in China-U.S. relations that must not be crossed, and the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués are the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. The U.S. side has violated its solemn political commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” and is attempting to create a stormy situation in the Taiwan Strait and push Taiwan into a dangerous position of war and peril. This is extremely irresponsible, extremely dangerous, and extremely wrong.\nWe urge the U.S. side to immediately stop military aid and arms sales to Taiwan, stop military contacts with the Taiwan region of China, and stop stoking the fire in the Taiwan Strait. China will take resolute and forceful measures to thwart the “Taiwan independence” secessionist scheme and counter external interference, including by the United States, and will firmly defend national reunification and peace in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2024/12/23/11012320.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-12-24","Mao Ning","CCTV","On December 23 local time, US President Joe Biden signed into law the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2025,” which contains negative content on China. What is China’s comment on this?","The US determined to sign into law the “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2025” containing negative content on China, playing up the “China threat” narrative year after year. It has kept trumpeting for military support to Taiwan, abusing state power to go after Chinese sci-tech and economic development, limiting trade, economic and people-to-people exchanges between China and the US, undermining China’s sovereignty, security and development interests and disrupting efforts of the two sides in stabilizing bilateral relations. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this and has lodged serious protests to the US.\nWe urge the US to get rid of its Cold War mentality and ideological bias, view China’s development and China-US relationship objectively and rationally, earnestly observe the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop arming Taiwan, stop politicizing and weaponizing sci-tech, economic and trade issues, stop finding pretext for increasing military expenditure and maintaining hegemony, and not to implement these negative articles concerning China. Otherwise, China will take strong and resolute measures to safeguard our sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241224_11517236.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241224_11517221.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Public opinion in Taiwan is highly concerned about the Central Economic Work Conference. How will the mainland side implement the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference, promote the development of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises on the mainland, advance cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and deepen cross-Strait integrated development?","The Central Economic Work Conference was an important meeting held as the Party deeply studied and implemented the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China. General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the meeting, comprehensively summarizing this year's economic work, profoundly analyzing the current domestic and international economic situation, systematically deploying the economic work tasks for next year, and clearly elaborating the regularities of doing economic work well in the new era. It laid the foundation for solidly doing economic work next year and achieving a good start to the “15th Five-Year Plan,” providing direction and fundamental guidance.\nWe will thoroughly implement the important speech by General Secretary Xi Jinping and the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference. We will both grasp the general trend and be confident, and also face difficulties squarely and remain clear-headed. We will comprehensively implement the overall requirements and policy orientations for next year's economic work, focus on target-oriented guidance, and strive to achieve an optimal combination of steady growth, stable employment, and reasonable recovery of prices. We will grasp policy orientations, emphasize timing and intensity, do things as early as possible and firmly, and ensure sufficient intensity. We will strengthen systematic thinking, focus on the coordination of various policies and reform and opening-up measures, and amplify policy effects. Around the nine key tasks that the meeting deployed for next year, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will work with relevant departments to actively support Taiwan-funded enterprises in expanding the domestic market, promote innovation cooperation and integration of industrial and supply chains between enterprises on both sides of the Strait, and encourage Taiwan-funded enterprises to participate in the cultivation and growth of emerging industries such as industrial internet, artificial intelligence, and the Internet of Things, as well as the layout and construction of future industries. This will help broad masses of Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots participate in the development of new quality productive forces, cultivate new growth drivers, and integrate into the new development pattern and participate in high-quality development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673904.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","福建广电台海时刻新媒体记者","KMT Vice Chairman Xia Li-yan recently said in an interview that the “1992 Consensus” is a vague phrase, and that using it causes no difficulty or harm at all. The only problem with not using it is that the “1992 Consensus” has been stigmatized by the DPP. He said that everyone wants to find another narrative to replace the “1992 Consensus,” but unfortunately, no one can find one. What is your comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the nature of cross-strait relations. It is the political foundation for the development of cross-strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The history of cross-strait relations repeatedly proves that when one acknowledges the “1992 Consensus” and adheres to the one-China principle, cross-strait relations can improve and develop, and Taiwan compatriots benefit; when one denies the “1992 Consensus” and deviates from the one-China principle, cross-strait relations become tense and turbulent, and the interests of Taiwan compatriots are harmed. We hope that all sectors on the island will meet us halfway, uphold the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations, and jointly commit to the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","This year marks the 25th anniversary of Macao's return to the motherland. Since Macao's return, “One Country, Two Systems,” “Macao people governing Macao,” and a high degree of autonomy have been fully guaranteed and fully embodied. Far-sighted people on both sides of the Strait and in Hong Kong and Macao have repeatedly said that the practice of “One Country, Two Systems” in Hong Kong and Macao has achieved…","The brilliant achievements Macao has made since its return to the motherland prove to the world that “one country, two systems” has distinct institutional advantages and strong vitality. It is a good system for keeping Hong Kong and Macao prosperous and stable over the long term, a good system for serving the building of a strong country and the great cause of national rejuvenation, and a good system for achieving peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation between different social systems. Over the past 25 years, Macao's major economic indicators have advanced to the front ranks worldwide, and people's livelihood and well-being have greatly improved. Its gross domestic product has grown seven-fold, and it has become one of the wealthiest cities in Asia. Visitor arrivals to Macao were just over 7 million in 1999; as of December 7 this year, they had reached 32.545 million. Per capita GDP exceeds MOP 559,000, and average life expectancy of residents is 83.1 years, both ranking among the top in the world. This fully shows that “one country, two systems” is entirely workable, achievable, and popular, and that “the motherland is reliable, and reunification brings benefits.”\nWe will continue to unite Taiwan compatriots, actively explore the “two systems” plan for Taiwan, and enrich the practice of peaceful reunification. The specific form of “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan's actual conditions, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully consider the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. We believe that “one country, two systems” will be re-recognized by Taiwan compatriots, and in the process of compatriots on both sides jointly working to achieve peaceful reunification, the scope and substance of the “two systems” plan for Taiwan will be fully demonstrated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673903.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Kuo Cheng-liang, a former DPP legislator, recently visited Zhangzhou City, Fujian, to pay respects to his ancestors, saying, “I feel like fallen leaves returning to their roots, which proves that the bond of historical, cultural, and blood ties is the strongest.” He has been attacked by some pan-Green figures on the island. What is your comment on this?","Honoring ancestors and cherishing one’s home village are fine traditions of the Chinese nation. They carry the Chinese people’s remembrance of and longing for their forebears and ancestral homeland, and are a cultural gene rooted in the blood of the Chinese people. When Taiwan compatriots return to their home villages to trace their roots, relatives and fellow clansmen on the mainland always welcome them warmly. This is the value pursuit of Chinese culture and also the warmth of us Chinese. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to trace their roots and pay respects to their ancestors, to learn more about the new face of their ancestral homeland, and to deeply feel the kinship and friendship passed down through blood. Some people on the island, driven by their “Taiwan independence” nature, make remarks about this, forgetting their ancestry, which is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that Shanghai authorities distributed a “Taiwan Compatriot Service Handbook” to attendees at the venue of the “Twin Cities Forum.” Pan-Green figures on the island questioned whether it was a “united front handbook,” and the Mainland Affairs Council said it “does not welcome this.” What is your comment on this?","The “Taiwan Compatriot Service Handbook” prepared by Shanghai is intended to provide practical information and service guidance to Taiwan compatriots, making it convenient for them to study, work, seek employment, start businesses, and live in Shanghai. What the Democratic Progressive Party authorities and ‘Taiwan independence’ forces ‘do not wish to see’ is not a small ‘service handbook,’ but cross-strait exchanges and interactions.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities and ‘Taiwan independence’ forces often attach the label of ‘united front’ to the mainland’s policies that benefit Taiwan and people’s livelihoods and to cross-strait exchange activities, attempting to stigmatize the united front. I have previously clarified the original meaning of the united front, and today I would like to explain further. In plain terms, the ‘united front’ means making friends and promoting unity. Taiwan compatriots are our relatives and family. It is only natural, upright, and entirely reasonable for us to communicate and exchange with them, strengthen unity, and seek their benefit and well-being. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ ‘united front conspiracy theory’ fully exposes their dark mindset and vicious intentions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","The U.S. 'FY2025 National Defense Authorization Act', which contains negative Taiwan-related content, has been signed into law. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and brooks no foreign interference. The U.S. side has obstinately inserted negative content related to Taiwan into the “FY2025 National Defense Authorization Act,” attempting to further arm Taiwan and stoke the fire in the Taiwan Strait by handing over the knife. This blatantly interferes in China's internal affairs, seriously violates the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, sends a serious wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and causes grave damage to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We express strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nWe demand that the U.S. side earnestly abide by the solemn political commitments it made to China on the Taiwan question, translate its statement of not supporting “Taiwan independence” into concrete actions, and immediately stop arming Taiwan. We warn the DPP authorities: no matter how they collude with external forces or how many American weapons they buy, they cannot stop the historical trend of China's reunification. Should they dare to take such a risk, they will surely bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673899.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The US Department of Defense recently released its “2024 China Military Power Report,” stating that the PLA has a series of means to “force Taiwan into negotiations.” Taiwan is strengthening its response to the PLA’s threats, including developing asymmetric warfare capabilities and improving “whole-of-society resilience.” What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “report” released by the US side deliberately stirs up hostility and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, encourages Taiwan to buy arms and prepare for war, crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs, and seriously violates the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués. We express strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop hyping Taiwan-related issues, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the US to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” have no way out. No one and no force should underestimate, much less misjudge, our firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673898.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","On the evening of December 19, the showcase of outstanding works and award ceremony of the Cross-Strait Youth Short Video Competition were held in Harbin. The competition's works not only documented the good food, fun activities, and beautiful scenery throughout the mainland, but also expressed the love of life of young people on both sides of the Strait. They have been widely disseminated across both sides of…","The Cross-Strait Youth Short Video Competition is organized by the Organizing Committee of the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival. It has two parts, online and offline. Online, it broadly solicits works from cross-Strait youth. Offline, online influencers and Taiwan youth carried out a “48-hour extreme shoot” in Harbin. The competition received 1,402 short videos shot by cross-Strait youth. After selection by a professional jury, 40 award-winning works were produced, including 2 Grand Prizes, 4 First Prizes, 6 Second Prizes, 8 Third Prizes, and 20 Excellence Awards.\nCross-Strait youth used their cameras to record what they saw and heard in various parts of the mainland, expressing their love of life, their aspirations for the future, and their feelings for the nation and home. For example, as soon as Taiwan youth arrived in Harbin, they experienced the dual charm of romance and food: some danced the “Subject Three” on Central Street, and some were warmly “fed” by restaurant owners. Another example is the Grand Prize-winning work “Returning Deer,” which tells the story of a Taiwan youth volunteering at the Jiangsu Dafeng Milu National Nature Reserve. Some Taiwan youth filmed their unique experiences of riding a driverless taxi and a driverless minibus in Guangzhou. There was also the sense of “we must strive for self-improvement” that arose when Taiwan youth visited the Exhibition Hall of Crimes of the Japanese Army’s Unit 731 during the War of Aggression Against China, which resonated strongly with netizens on both sides of the Strait. In sum, the successful holding of the competition provided a platform for cross-Strait youth to showcase their talents and deepen exchanges, and played a positive role in enhancing mutual understanding and friendship among cross-Strait youth.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","When Lai Ching-te recently met with scholars from the US Brookings Institution, he said, “China continues to use military actions to escalate pressure on Taiwan and attempts to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait; we thank the United States and other democratic countries for expressing concern over China’s conduct in undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.” What comment do you have on…","These remarks distort right and wrong, with the aim of confusing public perception and misleading international opinion and the people on the island.\nThere is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and are not permitted to be divided. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China principle, stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, and constantly collude with external forces to carry out independence-seeking provocations. They are the disruptors of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Strait.\nIn response to “Taiwan independence” provocations, the forceful countermeasures we have taken are a resolute punishment of the Lai Qingde authorities for their continuous promotion of separatist claims and engagement in separatist activities. They are a just act to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and a necessary measure to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” provocations and external interference, and join us in safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673902.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","First question: As the New Year's Day, Spring Festival and winter vacation holidays approach, compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan students on the mainland are concerned about return flight tickets to Taiwan. What arrangements are there for flights during this winter vacation and the Spring Festival this year? Second question: According to reports, a mainland scholar published an article in the journal…","First question. It is understood that the relevant competent authorities have made arrangements to further improve the work on cross-Strait direct flights, requiring mainland airlines operating cross-Strait routes and the relevant airports to center their work on the goal of “safety, convenience, and warmth,” so as to provide more high-quality and convenient services for cross-Strait compatriots traveling back and forth. Regarding Spring Festival extra flights across the Strait, the relevant competent authorities will actively respond to cross-Strait travel demand, especially the needs of Taiwan compatriots returning home for family reunions and traveling to the mainland to visit relatives or go sightseeing, and will support cross-Strait airlines in applying to operate Spring Festival extra flights.\nSecond question. That is the personal view of a scholar. What I want to emphasize is that since 1949, the Communist Party of China, the Chinese government, and the Chinese people have always regarded resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland as a historic mission that we will pursue unwaveringly. The motherland must be reunified and will certainly be reunified; this is an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in the new era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673896.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Taiwanese media reported that US Secretary of State Antony Blinken recently said in an interview that the Taiwan question is not only China's internal affair but a matter for everyone. He said that if Taiwan suffers a crisis due to China's actions, no country will be immune or unaffected. What comments do you have on this?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait to decide among themselves, and outsiders have no right to meddle. “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces are the greatest threats to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. If the US side sincerely hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence, clearly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and support China's peaceful reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Ou Guizhi (区桂芝) and several other Taiwan education figures recently staged a collective protest at the forum “Comprehensive Health Check of Taiwan’s Thirty Years of Education Reform,” harshly condemning the DPP authorities for continuing to implement “de-Sinicization” education policies in an attempt to sever cross-Strait ties and undermine the development of cross-Strait relations. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately push “de-Sinicization.” They have rolled out so-called “education reform” policies and “Taiwan independence” curriculum guidelines, deliberately distort Chinese history, and attempt to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides. They poison Taiwan’s younger generation and deprive Taiwan’s youth of their legitimate right to learn Chinese culture and understand the history of the Chinese nation. The result is that Taiwan compatriots become spiritually and culturally rootless duckweed. The aim is to undermine kinship between compatriots, incite hostility across the Strait, and peddle their “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda. Such “Taiwan independence” education reform is a poisonous “education reform” in every sense, and it will only plant the seeds of tension and conflict in the Taiwan Strait. Far-sighted people on the island strongly oppose it. This is a righteous and proper act of responsibility toward young people, and we appreciate it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673900.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","福建海峡卫视记者","The Supreme People's Court recently released a new batch of typical cases on the people's courts protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On December 19, the Supreme People's Court released a new batch of typical cases on protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Selected from recent years, these representative examples show how the people's courts, grounded in their judicial functions, serve and safeguard cross-Strait integrated development and effectively protect the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. They provide specific guidance for trials involving Taiwan-related matters and promptly respond to the judicial concerns of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. They have strong exemplary and guiding significance for improving the quality and effectiveness of Taiwan-related trials and for doing solid and good work in Taiwan-related judicial affairs.\nThese cases involve cross-Strait marine ecological protection, protection of the investment rights of Taiwanese businesses, intellectual property protection, and the resolution of Taiwan-related disputes at their source. They reflect the efforts and achievements of the people's courts in fully giving play to their judicial functions, consistently implementing equal treatment in Taiwan-related judicial work, equally protecting the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, safeguarding the investment and property security of Taiwan compatriots in the mainland, boosting the confidence of Taiwan compatriots in investing in the mainland market, strengthening the confidence of Taiwan-funded enterprises in starting businesses and operating in the mainland, optimizing a market-oriented and rule-of-law business environment, and actively serving cross-Strait integrated development. This will create better conditions and provide better guarantees for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to take part in building Chinese-style modernization and share in the fruits of the mainland's development and progress.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Fujian Province recently announced that it will promote the establishment of the “Fuzhou-Matsu Industrial Cooperation Park” and promote Fujian-Taiwan air and sea routes and logistics channels such as the “Silk Road Maritime Transport.” Please introduce the relevant situation.","The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for the Integrated Development of the Two Sides of the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Integrated Cross-Strait Development” explicitly proposes “establishing the Fuzhou-Matsu Industrial Cooperation Park.” Fuzhou City has earnestly implemented the relevant arrangements, actively promoted the establishment and development of the Fuzhou-Matsu Industrial Cooperation Park, designated the Culu Island area in Guantou Town, Lianjiang County, as a pilot zone, and allocates funds each year to support the development of Matsu enterprises in the Fuzhou-Matsu Industrial Cooperation Park.\nFujian will accelerate the construction of a three-dimensional, comprehensive hub of channels for Taiwan. It will continue to advance the construction of relevant airports; accelerate the construction of port-rail intermodal transport channels, promote the construction of railway channels behind ports, and further strengthen the level of port-rail and road-rail intermodal transport; and promote the networking of Fujian-Taiwan sea and air routes with logistics channels such as the “Maritime Silk Road Shipping,” accelerating the construction of sea-rail intermodal logistics channels. The people of Fujian and Taiwan share the bond of kinship in people and land. We support making connections between the two sides possible as early and as widely as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2024 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo and the Cross-Strait Flower Expo were recently held in Zhangzhou, Fujian. Please introduce the relevant situation and the achievements obtained.","From December 20 to 23, 2024, the 2024 Cross-Strait Modern Agriculture Expo · Cross-Strait Flower Expo was successfully held in Zhangzhou City, Fujian Province. Themed “Cross-Strait Agricultural Situation, Integrated Development,” the expo brought together people from the agricultural sectors on both sides of the Strait to discuss cooperation and seek common development, achieving positive results in the following three areas.\nFirst, practically advancing cross-Strait agricultural cooperation. At the opening ceremony, it was announced that the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office had approved the establishment of eight Taiwan Farmers’ Entrepreneurship Parks in Fujian: Nanjing in Zhangzhou, Tongan in Xiamen, the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, Shaowu in Nanping, Xiapu in Ningde, Yongchun in Quanzhou, Shanghang in Longyan, and Dongshan in Zhangzhou. This is a concrete measure to implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.” It provides a new platform for deepening integrated development of cross-Strait agriculture and rural areas, and more options for Taiwan agricultural and fishery practitioners to participate in rural revitalization on the mainland. During the expo, around topics of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan farmers, such as agricultural support policies and market expansion, special promotion meetings and market seminars were held. Through interpreting policies, analyzing trends, and guiding practice, these activities helped Taiwan compatriots and farmers better integrate into the mainland market and participate in comprehensive rural revitalization.\nSecond, promoting exchanges among cross-Strait business operators. This expo invited more than 300 Taiwan agricultural and fishery industry figures to participate. Attending guests offered views on the integrated development of cross-Strait agriculture, Taiwan farmers and businesspeople shared their development stories, and cross-Strait youth discussed their friendship. Representatives expressed that cross-Strait agriculture has complementary advantages and that the mainland offers vast space, and that this will encourage more Taiwan farmers and compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to come to the mainland to pursue and realize their dreams.\nThird, effectively expanding sales channels for cross-Strait specialty agricultural products. The expo set up an indoor exhibition area of 38,500 square meters and an outdoor exhibition area of 84,000 square meters, centrally displaying agricultural, forestry, and fishery products, fruits, vegetables, tea, horticulture and floral landscaping, cultural and creative design, and distinctive foods from both sides of the Strait. More than 700 enterprises from both sides of the Strait exhibited, and more than 60 large agricultural wholesale markets, leading e-commerce enterprises, and distributors from the mainland went to negotiate purchases. The boutique pavilion and theme street, composed of more than 100 enterprises from Taiwan, were very popular. The four-day expo attracted nearly 300,000 visitor-times for viewing and shopping, on-site sales reached 230 million yuan, and a batch of letters of intent for cooperation were signed, fully demonstrating the enormous potential and bright prospects of cross-Strait agricultural exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","Former U.S. National Security Advisor O’Brien recently said that “Taiwan is very rich,” so the new U.S. government is unwilling to continue bearing Taiwan’s “defense spending,” and Taiwan will need to purchase American-made weapons systems on a large scale in the future to balance the trade deficit between the two sides. Taiwan’s “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” said that Taiwan will continue to demonstrate its…","We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan, China. This position is consistent and clear. The relevant reports once again confirm that the United States consistently follows “America First,” and that what Americans care about is only “American interests.” For the sake of party self-interest, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are willing to sacrifice the interests of the people on the island by fawning on the United States, acting as its “ATM.” They will ultimately be discarded as a “pawn” once they have served their purpose. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that if they attempt to collude with external forces to provoke and seek “independence,” they will surely bring the consequences upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: Ma Ying-jeou has visited the mainland three times for exchanges, and netizens on both sides of the Strait are very interested in when he will go to see the pandas. The Taipei Zoo currently has only female pandas, which faces the problem of being unable to breed the next generation. Will the mainland side use this visit to push for new pandas to be sent to Taiwan? Second question: The Shanghai…","Regarding the first question, the giant panda is a national treasure deeply beloved by people on both sides of the Strait and an embodiment of peace and friendship. The hearts of people on both sides of the Strait are connected, and we should jointly cherish and maintain this, to deepen the warm feelings between compatriots.\nRegarding the second question, we welcome mainland residents, including residents of Shanghai, to resume travel to Taiwan at an early date, and we will actively study expanding travel to Taiwan by mainland residents. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities should create conditions for normalizing the resumption of cross-Strait tourism, rather than creating obstacles.\nThe relevant statements by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities disregard facts, shift blame onto others, and attempt to confuse public perception and shirk responsibility. In March this year, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities briefly lifted the “group tour ban” on travel to the mainland, but in June they went back on their word and reimposed the “group tour ban.” Last August, they used the so-called “reciprocity principle” as a pretext for refusing to lift the “group tour ban.” Regarding the statements of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, I have “three questions”: First, has the “group tour ban” not yet been lifted? Second, has the application from Taiwan's travel industry for a chartered-boat special program from Pingtan to Taiwan still gone unanswered? Third, do they still maintain the “orange” travel alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland?\nThe facts are abundantly clear: the crux of and obstacles to cross-Strait tourism issues lie entirely with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities should engage in self-reflection, correct their mistakes, and promptly remove the various obstacles they have placed on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202412/t20241225_12673901.htm"],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Shen Boyang, a DPP elected representative who founded the “Black Bear Academy” and clamors for “resisting China and defending Taiwan,” recently launched a so-called “thousand-person character formation ‘Defend Taiwan’” campaign. It was discovered that photos of the event were taken with mainland drones, and this drew ridicule and criticism from public opinion on the island. What is your comment on this?","Shen Boyang is a “Taiwan independence” stubborn element on the list. The farce he staged under the name of “protecting Taiwan” is in fact “anti-China,” fully exposing his vicious intention to deliberately incite confrontation between the two sides of the Strait.\nEconomic, trade and exchange cooperation across the Taiwan Strait is close, and mainland products are everywhere in the Taiwan market. Shen Boyang and his ilk use mainland products to “oppose the mainland” — truly “double standards and two faces,” which only adds to the ridicule.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The “group tour ban” on Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland has still not been lifted. The Kaohsiung Travel Agents Association recently invited 150 mainland travel industry operators to attend a winter international travel fair, expressing hope for the normalization of cross-Strait tourism. The association’s chairman said that if the “group tour ban” is not lifted, travel operators on the island will…","Peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the common aspirations of Taiwan society and the shared voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities should face up to the concerns of Taiwan's tourism operators and grassroots people, stop obstructing and restricting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, and take concrete measures on the issue of Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland for tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question: The Mainland Affairs Council previously suggested that the Taiwan Tourism Association and the Strait Tourism Association communicate about resuming cross-Strait tourism. Taiwanese media reported that the Taiwan Tourism Association and the Strait Tourism Association had originally planned to communicate on this matter in Beijing on December 5, but this was called off afterward due to unforeseen…","For your first and second questions, I will respond to them together. We have consistently and clearly supported promoting the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the normalization of exchanges in all fields. The crux of the current issues in cross-Strait personnel exchanges lies entirely with the DPP authorities. We will actively study expanding tourism by mainland residents to Taiwan, not only to Penghu but also to Taiwan Island proper.\nAs for the third question, Taiwan resident Zhou and 3 others are suspected of the crime of “organizing and using heterodox secret societies to undermine the implementation of law,” and have been lawfully arrested by public security authorities in Guangdong Province. The relevant authorities will handle the case in accordance with the law and lawfully protect the legitimate rights and interests of the parties involved.\nThe DPP authorities’ political manipulation of this matter cannot conceal the fact that they have stopped at nothing to interfere with and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The DPP authorities have set up numerous obstacles to cross-Strait tourism, made things difficult for and obstructed cross-Strait city exchanges, clamored for “decoupling and severing supply chains” between the two sides, and unreasonably obstructed cross-Strait religious and folk belief cultural exchanges. Their dismal record is well documented, and they are the real obstacle to normalizing personnel exchanges and normalizing exchange and cooperation across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: At the “Twin Cities Forum,” Shanghai authorities announced that they would actively promote group tours to Taiwan for Shanghai residents. Afterward, the MAC said it hoped the matter could be taken up through the cross-Strait “mini two associations” for discussion. Compared with the earlier ban on the director of Shanghai's Taiwan Affairs Office attending a conference in Taiwan, does this highlight…","First question: First, regarding cross-Strait tourism, we have repeatedly emphasized that we will actively study expanding travel by mainland residents to Taiwan. Second, your question expresses the doubts and dissatisfaction of public opinion and the public on the island regarding the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' obstruction and interference with cross-Strait tourism cooperation.\nSecond question: Regarding Mr. Ma Ying-jeou's visit to the mainland this time leading a delegation, we made proper arrangements for all the activities, and the problems you mentioned do not exist.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","Shi Xue-yan, a former Nantou County councilor and a mainland spouse, was recently stripped of her public office as a legislator by Taiwan's “Ministry of the Interior.” Taiwan media are paying attention to whether the DPP authorities will conduct a comprehensive review and follow up by removing mainland spouses who serve as village or neighborhood chiefs and other public offices. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. The DPP authorities are stirring up “green terror” on the island and deliberately manipulating it for political purposes, openly persecuting mainland spouses who hold public office on the island and brutally depriving them of their legitimate rights to participate in Taiwan’s political affairs. We are seriously concerned about this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Taiwan media reported that Raymond Greene, Director of the Taipei Office of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT), recently met with senior executives of United Microelectronics Corporation (UMC). Within the island’s semiconductor industry, there is concern that after TSMC, UMC will also be pushed to build factories in the United States, and that Taiwan’s advantages in the semiconductor industry will be…","With the DPP authorities unilaterally and unscrupulously catering to the United States, this concern is by no means 'the groundless worry of the man of Qi who feared the sky would fall'.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2024-12-25","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","The first batch of 38 US-sold M1A2T tanks recently arrived in Taiwan. Island media called the tank “the strongest on the planet,” and the Taiwan military said it expects retraining for the replacement to begin in early February next year. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to the Taiwan region of China. The U.S. side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and reflect its commitment not to support 'Taiwan independence' in concrete actions, rather than encouraging and tolerating the adventurous conduct of 'Taiwan independence' and deliberately undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nNo person or force should underestimate the Chinese government's and Chinese people's firm determination, strong will, and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. 'Taiwan independence' separatist acts and external interference cannot shake our determination and will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification, and still less can they stop the historical trend that the motherland inevitably will and must be reunified.\nToday's press conference is now concluded.\nLadies and gentlemen of the press, today is the last regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council in 2024. I would especially like to thank all of you and your media outlets for your attention to and support of the press releases and publicity work of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council over the past year. As 2025 approaches, I wish all of you present, and all compatriots who follow the Taiwan Affairs Office press conferences, a happy New Year and that all your wishes come true!\nThank you all.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202412/t20241225_12673890.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2024-12-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the first batch of M1A2T main battle tanks Taiwan purchased from the United States has arrived in Taiwan, marking the first time in 30 years that Taiwan’s military has acquired a new-type tank. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Zhang Xiaogang said, we urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, earnestly fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence,” immediately stop arming Taiwan, and stop its dangerous conduct that undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “seeking independence by relying on the United States” and “resisting reunification by force” are doomed to fail. A few U.S.-made weapons cannot be a lifesaver; they are merely “living targets” on the battlefield. The People's Liberation Army of China will comprehensively strengthen training and combat readiness, comprehensively enhance its ability to win, and resolutely crush any “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and interference by external forces.","","https://www.news.cn/world/20241226/2dfa7ee0157f4180b02f84aa95419c9d/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2024-12-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command said that China's increased militarization in the Taiwan Strait area has prompted the US to keep selling arms to Taiwan. Under the Taiwan Relations Act, the US is ready at any time to defend Taiwan and provide Taiwan with defensive weapons and services, and is confident of winning in a Taiwan Strait conflict. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Zhang Xiaogang said that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and tolerates no interference from any external forces. In recent years, the United States has attempted to hollow out the One-China Principle, saying one thing and doing another on the Taiwan question, escalating military aid and arms sales to Taiwan, sending serious wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We solemnly warn the US: “using Taiwan to contain China” will never succeed. The PLA has the confidence and ability to thwart all external interference, crush the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.news.cn/world/20241226/2dfa7ee0157f4180b02f84aa95419c9d/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2024-12-27","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced on its website the decision to take countermeasures against seven US defense corporations and related senior executives. Do you have any further comment?","Recently, the US has, once again, provided China’s Taiwan region with huge military aid and arms sales and its “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2025” contains negative articles on China. Such acts seriously violate the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously interfere in China’s internal affairs, and seriously undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In accordance with the provisions in the Law of the People’s Republic of China on Countering Foreign Sanctions, China decided to take countermeasures against seven US defense corporations and related senior executives.\nSeeking “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail. What the US has done to assist the “Taiwan independence” attempt by arming Taiwan will only backfire. Its relevant act containing negative articles on China is filled with Cold War zero-sum mentality and ideological bias. Without factual basis, it plays up the “China threat” narrative, trumpets for military support to Taiwan and tries to find a pretext for increasing military expenditure and maintaining hegemony, which disrupts regional peace and stability.\nWe urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions in the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, immediately stop arming Taiwan in any form, view China’s development and China-US relationship objectively and rationally, not to implement these negative articles concerning China and stop wrong words and deeds that harm China’s interests. China will continue to take all measures necessary to firmly safeguard our sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202412/t20241227_11521820.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202412/t20241227_11521821.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-01-06","Guo Jiakun","AFP","The Taiwan authorities yesterday said that in 2024, Taiwan’s government faced an average of 2.4 million cyberattacks per day, with most of them attributed to Chinese cyber forces. Can you confirm that?","That’s not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202501/t20250106_11527766.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202501/t20250106_11527763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-01-08","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 8 (Electronic Dispatch): State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua responded to reporters’ questions on the 8th, saying that around one hundred undersea cable damage incidents occur globally each year, and they are common maritime accidents. Before the basic facts and responsibility for the accident have been clarified, the DPP authorities have fabricated claims out of thin air and deliberately hyped undersea cable accidents as the so-called mainland “gray zone threat.” This fully demonstrates that they will manipulate “anti-China” and “resist-China” sentiment by any means necessary, without any bottom line.\nA reporter asked: According to reports, undersea communication cables outside Keelung Port were recently suspected of being damaged by a cargo ship dragging its anchor. The DPP authorities declared this “not a simple accident,” reflecting an escalation of the mainland’s “gray zone” actions against Taiwan. What is your comment? Chen Binhua gave the above response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250108_12676819.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-08","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 8 (electronic dispatch): Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that at about 9:00 a.m. on January 7, a magnitude 6.8 earthquake struck Dingri County, Rikaze City, Tibet, causing heavy casualties and property losses. After the earthquake, General Secretary Xi Jinping attached great importance to it and gave important instructions. Relevant parties implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important instructions, fully carried out rescue and disaster relief, and properly resettled the affected people. Compatriots and people from all walks of life in Taiwan have expressed concern and sympathy for the disaster area through various forms, reflecting the bond between compatriots on both sides, where blood is thicker than water and we help each other in times of need. We express our gratitude for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250108_12676827.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","On January 15 at 10:00 a.m., the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua summarized cross-Strait relations in 2024 and looked ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2025, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporters, good day! Welcome to the first regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council in 2025.\nThe year 2024 marked the 75th anniversary of the founding of New China. The Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China made systematic arrangements for further comprehensively deepening reform and advancing Chinese modernization. All undertakings of reform, development and stability have marched forward with great strides, and brilliant achievements have attracted the attention of the world. General Secretary Xi Jinping has been steering the course, guiding the direction of cross-Strait relations. He met with Ma Ying-jeou and a delegation of Taiwan youth, drew an inviolable red line on the Taiwan question during the Sino-US leaders’ meeting, and declared the major policies for Taiwan on a series of important occasions and major events, which have aroused strong resonance among compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nUnder the strong leadership of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we have firmly grasped the initiative in cross-Strait relations, demonstrated greater capacity in curbing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, taken greater strides in deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, and accumulated greater momentum in advancing the process of national reunification, pushing cross-Strait relations forward in the right direction.\nFirst, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation have continued to expand, and compatriots on both sides have gained deeper mutual understanding. We have worked hard to break through obstruction and restrictions, continuously promoted the full restoration of cross-Strait “Three Links” and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and encouraged compatriots on both sides to jointly inherit and carry forward Chinese culture. We implemented measures to waive admission fees for Taiwan’s “first-time visitors” to scenic spots, and successfully held the 16th Straits Forum, the Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Winter Sports Festival, and other exchange activities. Our promotion of delegations of mainland university faculty and students visiting Taiwan has won warm welcome and broad support from all sectors on both sides. More Taiwan youth and grassroots people have come to the mainland to personally experience the splendid landscapes and myriad developments of the motherland. Through practical actions, compatriots on both sides have shown that the history, culture, and blood ties across the Strait share a common origin and are inseparable, and that compatriots on both sides are a family sharing weal and woe.\nSecond, cross-Strait integrated development has deepened continuously, and compatriots in Taiwan have shared more development opportunities. The Third Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the CPC deliberated and adopted the “Decision of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Further Comprehensively Deepening Reform and Advancing Chinese Modernization,” and all undertakings of reform, development and stability have marched forward with great strides, creating broader space for compatriots in Taiwan to participate in the cause of building a strong country and realizing national rejuvenation. We uphold the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” always respect, care for, and benefit compatriots in Taiwan, implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, and actively do practical good deeds and solve difficulties for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The “Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” continued to be implemented, and integrated development between Fujian and Taiwan achieved new progress and new results. We held the 2024 annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit and other cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities, supporting Taiwan businesses and enterprises in integrating into the new development pattern and achieving high-quality development, making it more convenient for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest and do business on the mainland.\nThird, we adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely and forcefully carry out struggles against separatism and interference. We successively conducted the “Joint Sword-2024A” and “Joint Sword-2024B” exercises, issued and implemented the “Opinions on Punishing According to Law the Crimes of ‘Taiwan Independence’ Diehards for Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession of the Country,” and published a new list of “Taiwan independence” diehards, effectively cracking down on the provocative acts of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces seeking “independence.” We resolutely curb the schemes of external forces to interfere, resolutely safeguard the authority of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and consolidate and expand the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle. More and more people on the island have recognized the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland and have voiced their hope for cross-Strait relations to return to the right track of peaceful development.\nOn the eve of the New Year 2025, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a New Year’s address extending New Year’s greetings to Chinese people at home and abroad, stressing that “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family; no one can sever our blood ties, and no one can stop the historical trend of national reunification.” In the new year, we will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, broadly unite compatriots in Taiwan to jointly promote the forward development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification. We hope that the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan will strengthen their national confidence as upright and proud Chinese, join us in shouldering responsibilities for building Chinese modernization, contribute to the realization of complete national reunification, and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678399.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","General Secretary Xi Jinping emphasized in his 2025 New Year message: “Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family. No one can sever our blood ties, and no one can stop the historical trend of national reunification.” How should this be deeply understood and implemented?","General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech is rich in content and profound in thought. It profoundly reveals that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same bloodline, culture, and history, as well as shared responsibility for the Chinese nation and shared hopes for the future. The distance of the Strait cannot sever the flesh-and-blood kinship of compatriots on both sides; differences in systems cannot change the historical and objective fact that both sides belong to one country and one nation; the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces going against the tide and external forces' interference cannot stop the historical trend of cross-Strait reunification. The complete reunification of the motherland must and will be achieved.\nWe will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's 2025 New Year's address, actively promote cross-strait exchanges, interactions, and integration, work hard to enhance the well-being of compatriots, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, and, on the basis of adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” broadly unite compatriots in Taiwan to jointly advance cross-strait relations and the process of advancing the reunification of the motherland. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will uphold national righteousness, shoulder historical responsibility, jointly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and work tirelessly with compatriots on the mainland to achieve the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678400.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","1月2日，中共中央台办、国务院台办主任宋涛发表题为《同心同向奋楫笃行》的新年寄语。请予解读。","On January 2, Director Song Tao issued a New Year's message on behalf of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, extending New Year's greetings and sincere best wishes to the broad Taiwan compatriots. In his message, Director Song Tao reaffirmed the central government's basic policies on Taiwan work, reviewed and summarized the Taiwan work of 2024, and pointed out that over the past year we have worked to expand cross-Strait exchanges, focused on enhancing the well-being of compatriots, and devoted all our efforts to safeguarding our common home. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait have responded in unison, weathered storms together, and shared a common destiny. They are proud of and take pride in the development achievements of the motherland and have made positive contributions to its great development. He called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to be united in heart and direction, to work diligently and resolutely, and to join hands in striving tirelessly to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the complete reunification of the motherland.\nThe message also set out the key priorities for Taiwan work in 2025, stating that we will continue to adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely combat “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, continue to expand cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, continuously enhance mutual understanding and recognition, promote the advancement of cross-Strait relations, and push forward the process of national reunification. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, shoulder their historical responsibility, and, together with compatriots on the mainland, contribute to the great cause of national reunification and create a bright future of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","On January 7, a magnitude 6.8 earthquake struck Dingri County, Shigatse City, Tibet. People from all sectors on the island expressed concern and sympathy in various ways, and Taiwan compatriots and enterprises actively donated money and goods to the disaster area. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On January 7, a magnitude 6.8 earthquake struck Dingri County, Rikaze City, Xizang, causing major casualties. After the disaster occurred, relevant departments on the mainland mobilized rescue efforts in full force, doing their utmost to protect the lives and property of the people, and earthquake relief work has been carried out in an orderly, effective, and efficient manner. Various sectors and members of the public in Taiwan have expressed concern and sympathy for the disaster area and provided donations through various means. According to incomplete statistics, as of January 10, donations of money and goods from the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises as well as Taiwan-invested companies such as Foxconn, Want Want, Ding Xin, and President Enterprises totaled more than RMB 32 million. Relevant groups, institutions, and entertainers on the island have also reached out to the disaster area, donating money and goods. This once again reflects the bond between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, who are of one blood and support each other. We express our gratitude for the concern and assistance given by relevant groups and individuals in Taiwan, as well as by Taiwan-invested businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","With the traditional Spring Festival approaching, will the Taiwan Affairs system organize visits and condolences to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and we have always cared about and looked after Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses on the mainland. As the Spring Festival approaches, leaders of the Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will visit and extend greetings to Taiwanese businesspeople, compatriots, and youth, hold discussions and social gatherings with them, and listen to their opinions and suggestions. Various localities will also successively visit and extend greetings to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businesses, hold New Year social gatherings, listen to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople, and coordinate the resolution of practical difficulties, so that Taiwan compatriots in every locality can live comfortably and spend a warm New Year. Taking this opportunity, we also extend New Year's blessings and sincere greetings to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and wish everyone the blessings of the Year of the Snake, a happy family reunion, and joy and peace! I would also especially like to wish (Hokkien) all our Taiwan compatriots a happy New Year, great prosperity in the new year, and peace and safety for your families!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Please introduce the exchanges and dialogues conducted in 2024 with Taiwan political parties, groups and representative figures. What plans are arranged for 2025?","In 2024, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we maintained positive interaction with relevant political parties, groups and representative figures in Taiwan, consolidated and enhanced mutual trust, strengthened exchanges and interactions, and achieved positive results.\nFirst, we provided direction for the development of cross-Strait relations. On April 10, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Ma Ying-jeou, former chairman of the Kuomintang, and young people from Taiwan who accompanied him, and delivered an important speech. He elaborated on the major policies toward Taiwan under the new circumstances, steering the development of cross-Strait relations and effectively guiding its direction. It drew wide attention and high praise from across the Taiwan Strait and the international community, and had a major and far-reaching impact.\nSecond, we added momentum to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Representative figures of Taiwan's political parties, including Ma Ying-jeou, Hung Hsiu-chu, Hsia Li-yen and Lien Sheng-wen, were invited to attend the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival, the Cross-Strait Symposium on Jointly Promoting Chinese Culture, the 4th “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar Event,” the 7th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the 16th Straits Forum, and various local economic, trade and cultural exchange events. They voiced positive views in favor of adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and benefiting compatriots on both sides. Wang Jin-pyng and other well-known figures in Taiwan returned to their ancestral homes to trace their roots and worship their ancestors, and visited and exchanged views, adding another good story to “Cross-Strait Compatriots Are One Family.”\nThird, we gathered wisdom for the future of cross-Strait relations. Senior leaders of the New Party, the People First Party, the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union and other parties, including Wu Cheng-tien, led delegations to visit on multiple occasions. People of insight from both sides of the Strait held dialogues on the situation in the Taiwan Strait, cross-Strait relations and related issues. They reached broad consensus on firming up the conviction of unification, developing cross-Strait relations and promoting exchanges and cooperation, and issued a strong call to oppose the separatism of “Taiwan independence” and foreign interference and to safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation.\nFourth, we brought benefits to compatriots in Taiwan. Several county and city heads from Taiwan led delegations to visit. Goodwill delegations from the Kinmen County people's representative body and the Penghu County Council visited and exchanged views on the mainland. The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum was held smoothly. Exchanges in the fields of cross-county, cross-city and urban exchanges continued to expand, and their practical effects kept emerging. Concrete progress was made in promoting the resumption of travel to Taiwan by mainland residents, the import of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, and the exchange of experience in urban management and grassroots governance.\nIn the new year, we will, with a view to the situation in the Taiwan Strait and changes in cross-Strait relations, thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions and the Party Central Committee's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work. On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will continue to strengthen exchanges with relevant political parties, groups and representative figures in Taiwan, build consensus, consolidate mutual trust, and promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, uniting broad Taiwan compatriots to work together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678393.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","Recently, the DPP authorities once again slandered and smeared the judicial documents issued by the mainland to punish hardline \"Taiwan independence\" separatists as affecting cross-Strait exchanges, and hyped up claims that Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland face personal safety risks. What comments do you have on this?","The “Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with Law ‘Taiwan Independence’ Die-Hards for the Crimes of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession” is a major measure targeting the DPP authorities’ obstinate insistence on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” and their continuous provocations to pursue independence. It is a due and necessary step to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and to effectively protect the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. In response, the DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and smeared it, wantonly spreading rumors and intimidating the public in an attempt to obstruct and undermine cross-strait exchanges and escalate cross-strait confrontation. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nI must reiterate that the judicial documents target only a very small number of “Taiwan independence” die-hards whose words and deeds in promoting independence are egregious and whose independence-seeking activities are rampant. They do not involve the broad masses of Taiwan residents. We warmly welcome broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to look around, visit, and exchange, coming happily and returning safely. Through their own firsthand experience, the DPP authorities’ rumors will collapse on their own. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan residents will no longer be deceived and coerced by them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","In his New Year’s Day speech, Lai Ching-te continued to peddle “Taiwan independence” fallacies and clamored about so-called “democracy against authoritarianism.” What comments do you have?","In his speech, Lai Ching-te continued to promote the “new two-state theory” of “mutual non-subordination,” propagate separatist views, and incite hostility and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. He fabricated the so-called false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” attempting to deceive people on the island and mislead international public opinion. This once again exposes his die-hard “Taiwan independence” nature and his sinister intention to escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, as well as his ugly posture of currying favor with and pledging allegiance to external forces, and his scheme of “relying on outsiders to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force.” Such tricks cannot fool anyone and will absolutely not succeed.\nLai Ching-te repeatedly harps on the old tune of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” yet he keeps doing the work of undermining democracy under the banner of “democracy and freedom.” May I ask: abusing administrative and judicial resources to openly persecute parties, groups and individuals that advocate cross-Strait exchanges and support reunification—what kind of democracy is this? Vigorously carrying out a “green terror,” inciting populism and tearing society apart—what kind of democracy is this? Disregarding public will and ignoring public interests, and brutally depriving the Taiwan public of their legitimate rights to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation—what kind of democracy is this? Controlling the media, raising an online troll army, suppressing public opinion, arbitrarily cracking down on dissenters, and creating a “chilling effect”—what kind of democracy is this? Squandering taxpayers' money and “selling out Taiwan” without any bottom line—what kind of democracy is this? Writing and directing a farce of “cognitive warfare” on its own, creating “information cocoons,” misleading public opinion, and inciting “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment—what kind of democracy is this? In a word, the so-called “democracy” in the mouths of the DPP authorities is “DPP rule” (“民进党作主”), a fake democracy that serves “Taiwan independence.”\n“Taiwan independence” forces colluding with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at independence are the root cause of cross-Strait tensions and the disruption of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. In response, we will not yield one half step, and we will not stop for a single step in punishing and combating “Taiwan independence.” “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; reunification is the way out. We hope that Taiwan compatriots, starting from the greater interests of the nation and their own well-being, will stand with us in the same heart and direction, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” provocations and external interference, jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, jointly promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and jointly create a bright future for cross-Strait relations and the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678392.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Please briefly introduce the cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2024, including its main characteristics. What is your outlook for cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2025?","In 2024, driven strongly by the improving and stabilizing mainland economy, cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation advanced steadily while making progress, and cross-Strait economic integration and development continued to deepen.\nFirst, cross-Strait economic exchanges showed a new look. The annual meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit was successfully held in Xiamen. Chairman Wang Huning, on behalf of General Secretary Xi Jinping and the CPC Central Committee, sent a congratulatory letter, encouraging compatriots and entrepreneurs on both sides of the Strait to jointly write a brilliant chapter of national reunification and national rejuvenation. The Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum, the Straits Forum, the first Cross-Strait Service Industry Conference, the Agricultural Expo·Flower Expo and other cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities were successfully held, continually expanding the breadth and depth of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. Taiwan businesses and enterprises actively participated in the seventh China International Import Expo and other exhibitions, developing the domestic market and expanding development space. According to General Administration of Customs statistics, in 2024 total cross-Strait trade reached US$292.971 billion, up 9.4% year on year. Of this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$75.189 billion, up 9.8% year on year; mainland imports from Taiwan were US$217.782 billion, up 9.3% year on year. According to Ministry of Commerce statistics, in 2024 the mainland newly established 7,941 Taiwan-invested enterprises, up 1.6% year on year.\nSecond, deepening cross-Strait integrated development has taken new steps. The key tasks deployed in the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” are advancing steadily, supporting policies continue to be improved, and various measures are beginning to show results. From January to November 2024, cross-Strait trade between Fujian and Taiwan totaled RMB 85.22 billion, up 3.2% year on year; Fujian newly established 2,117 Taiwan-invested enterprises, up 16% year on year. In 2024, 920,000 Taiwan compatriot entries were made through Fujian ports, up 53.3% year on year.\nThird, cross-Strait industrial cooperation has achieved new progress. Cross-Strait industrial cooperation platforms such as the Straits Industrial Cooperation Zone, the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone, the Kunshan Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Pilot Zone, and the Dongguan Cross-Strait Innovation Development Cooperation Zone are advancing steadily. Fujian newly established 8 Taiwan farmers’ entrepreneurship parks. A batch of key Taiwan-invested projects with high technological content and major industrial impact have gone into production one after another. Localities, drawing on their resource endowments and industrial strengths, have innovatively held cross-Strait industry matchmaking activities, guiding Taiwan businesses and enterprises to seize the opportunities of developing new quality productive forces, accelerate transformation and upgrading, optimize industrial layout, and take firmer root on the mainland for better and faster development.\nFourth, Taiwan compatriots’ sense of gain and well-being from participating in cross-Strait economic integration and development has risen markedly. Systems and policies that enhance the welfare of Taiwan compatriots continue to be implemented in detail, the scope of equal-treatment benefits keeps expanding, and the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises are effectively protected. Localities earnestly do practical things, good things, and things that solve difficulties for Taiwan businesses and compatriots, improve service levels, help Taiwan compatriots and enterprises overcome production and operation difficulties, and provide convenience for integrating into life on the mainland. Cross-Strait youth exchange activities have been innovatively held, supporting Taiwan youth in coming to the mainland to work, start businesses, and realize their dreams. A large number of quality Taiwan-invested enterprises have listed on the mainland; to date, the cumulative total has reached 65.\nIn the new year, we will fully implement the spirit of the Third Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee and the Central Economic Work Conference, continuously improve policy measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, optimize the business environment related to Taiwan affairs, and help Taiwan compatriots and enterprises achieve high-quality development on the mainland. We will fully implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” encourage the introduction of more policy measures deepening cross-Strait integrated development, advance the construction of cross-Strait industrial cooperation platforms, build highlands for concentrated development of Taiwan enterprises, and raise the level of cross-Strait industrial and supply chain cooperation. We will step up efforts to help Taiwan businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern, strengthen docking and linkage with the domestic market, and share in the opportunities of developing new quality productive forces and the dividends of high-level opening to the outside world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678395.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Recently, several Taiwan unification-leaning groups held a rally to express support for Taiwan retired general Gao Anguo, who was detained and denied visits by the DPP authorities on suspicion of violating the “National Security Law.” What is your comment?","The so-called “National Security Act” of the Taiwan region is an out-and-out evil law. Based on its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities use the evil law to commit violence, continuously suppress political rivals and dissidents, and create “green terror.” Recently, they have escalated their persecution of organizations and individuals who advocate unification and support unification. This fully shows that under “green authoritarianism,” Taiwan has no freedom to oppose “Taiwan independence” or to pursue unification.\nWe are deeply concerned about this and strongly condemn it. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: those who do wrong will eventually bring about their own destruction, and the reckless actions of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will certainly face the judgment of justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Please introduce the 2024 cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields. What are the main characteristics? What are the plans for 2025?","In 2024, we actively promoted the normalization and routinization of cross-Strait exchanges and travel, and supported all sectors on both sides in carrying out exchanges and cooperation in a variety of forms. Cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields continued to recover and expand, playing an important role in strengthening friendship between compatriots on both sides, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and promoting the development of cross-Strait relations. The main characteristics are as follows:\nFirst, cross-Strait exchanges and travel made positive progress, and the scale of personnel exchanges continued to grow. Relevant authorities on the mainland continuously took measures to facilitate cross-Strait personnel travel, enabling mainland residents to travel to Matsu and Kinmen, working hard to promote group tours by mainland residents to Taiwan, waiving admission fees to scenic spots for Taiwan “first-time visitors,” and actively supporting people from all sectors on the mainland in exchanges in Taiwan. In 2024, cross-Strait personnel exchanges totalled 4.405 million person-trips, up 53.8% year on year; of these, Taiwan compatriots made 4.023 million trips to the mainland, up 54.3% year on year, and mainland residents made 382,000 trips to Taiwan, up 49.2% year on year.\nSecond, exchanges and cooperation in all fields achieved remarkable results, and compatriots on both sides grew ever closer. Over the past year, people from all sectors on both sides, especially from all sectors in Taiwan, took part very enthusiastically in cross-Strait exchanges. Cultural exchanges across the Strait continued to be lively, exchanges on folk customs and beliefs were rich in content, grassroots exchanges took diverse forms, and exchanges in education, publishing, medicine and health, sports, news media, trade unions, women, ethnic minorities, religion and other fields and sectors were widely carried out. Tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, came to the mainland for the first time, personally experiencing the magnificent landscapes and myriad aspects of the motherland and feeling the emotion and glory of being Chinese. Large-scale events such as the 16th Straits Forum, the Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit, and the Cross-Strait Symposium on Jointly Promoting Chinese Culture were successfully held, bringing together the consensus and strength of compatriots on both sides to strengthen exchanges and cooperation and jointly promote Chinese culture.\nThird, cross-Strait youth exchanges were rich and colorful, injecting vigorous vitality into the development of cross-Strait relations. Young people have become the most active group in current cross-Strait exchanges. Over the past year, young people from both sides crossed mountains and seas to keep their youthful appointment together, taking part in a series of signature cross-Strait youth exchange activities such as the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the Straits Youth Development Forum, the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, the Straits Youth Festival, and the Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour, composing moving chapters of mutual, two-way engagement between young people on both sides. Relevant parties created a series of activities highly popular with Taiwan youth, such as the Cross-Strait Youth Vitality Carnival, the Cross-Strait Youth Ice and Snow Festival, the Cross-Strait Inter-University Alliance Baseball Games, and the Cross-Strait Youth Short Video Competition, building new platforms for cross-Strait youth exchanges. Academician Qiu Yong, Party Secretary of Tsinghua University, led a delegation of mainland university faculty and students on a return visit at the invitation of Taiwan, which drew close attention and warm welcome from all sectors in Taiwan; Mr. Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwan university students to the mainland for exchange visits, engaging in lively interaction with faculty and students of Peking University and Sun Yat-sen University.\nFourth, cross-Strait integrated development achieved important results and went deeper and more substantive. Relevant departments and Fujian Province actively implemented the Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, and the policy support system for Taiwan compatriots to study, work and live in Fujian was further improved, with Fujian-Taiwan integrated development achieving marked results. The systems and policies guaranteeing the welfare of Taiwan compatriots and their equal treatment on the mainland were further improved, and more and more Taiwan compatriots have found stages on the mainland to realize their dreams, personally taking part in the process of Chinese-style modernization. A group of Taiwan compatriots joined social organizations such as the China Writers Association, the China Photographers Association, the China Folk Literature and Art Association, and the China Musicians Association, deeply taking part in the development of various mainland undertakings and receiving commendations.\nNo matter what interference and obstacles are encountered, exchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides must not stop, must not be cut off, and must not be reduced. In 2025, we will thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” widely unite people from all sectors in Taiwan, continuously promote the normalization and routinization of cross-Strait exchanges and travel, constantly expand exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, work hard to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and let compatriots on both sides open their hearts and build trust through interaction, promote heart-to-heart harmony, and gather mighty strength for promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678394.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Island media are paying attention to the repeated public statements by Colby, who was nominated by Trump as Deputy Secretary of Defense, that if conflict breaks out in the Taiwan Strait, “TSMC’s wafer fabs in Taiwan should be destroyed,” and that this “is not a decision Taiwan alone can make.” What is your comment?","This once again confirms that TSMC is, in the eyes of some people in the US, a piece of fat meat on the chopping board: if it cannot be obtained, it must be destroyed. It also once again exposes the true face of the US, which always puts “American interests first” and never considers Taiwan's interests or the feelings of its people. It further warns Taiwan compatriots to recognize that the deeper the DPP authorities “rely on the US,” the more they “harm Taiwan” and “destroy Taiwan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","In an interview on cross-Strait tourism, Lai Ching-te said, “What truly obstructs cross-Strait exchanges is China, not Taiwan. We hope to have healthy and orderly exchanges with China on an equal and dignified basis,” and suggested that the Taiwan Travel Association and the Strait Tourism Association could first hold negotiations. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te, in his answer to questions, used “Taiwan” and “China” to refer to the two sides of the Strait. This is an outright “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy. This once again proves that the DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and repeatedly engage in provocations to seek “independence,” which is the fundamental reason why cross-Strait consultation and dialogue cannot be resumed.\nWe have consistently and actively promoted the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Strait and the routinization of exchanges in all fields. On cross-Strait tourism, in May 2023 we announced the resumption of group tours by Taiwan residents to the Chinese mainland. In April and August 2024, we successively made arrangements for Fujian residents to travel to Matsu and Kinmen and for group tours to the island of Taiwan, and took measures to effectively promote them. In December 2024, we clearly stated that we welcome mainland residents, including Shanghai residents, to resume travel to Taiwan at an early date, and that we will actively study expanding travel to Taiwan by mainland residents.\nIn contrast, the DPP authorities, in 2020, used the COVID-19 epidemic as an excuse to ban mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan, and suspended the business of island travel agencies operating group tours to the mainland. To this day, the “group tour ban” has not been lifted. In June 2024, they also raised the travel alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the Chinese mainland to “orange,” refused to respond to the full resumption of cross-Strait passenger direct flights and routes, and have been slow to respond to the charter application from Pingtan to Taiwan submitted by Taiwan's tourism industry. The list of the first batch of mainland residents' group tours to Taiwan still sits on the desks of relevant departments of the DPP authorities. The facts could not be clearer, and Lai Ching-te's statements are turning black into white and making a counterattack by accusing others.\nThe DPP authorities ignore the difficulties facing the island's tourism industry and disregard the appeals of operators and the public. They keep delaying and obstructing the normalization of cross-Strait tourism, purely out of selfish motives, fearing that mainland residents will come to Taiwan and that people on both sides of the Strait will draw closer, causing the “information cocoon” they carefully constructed to collapse, and causing the “Taiwan independence” propositions they loudly promote to lose their market. The key to resuming mainland residents' travel to Taiwan lies in whether the DPP authorities can, as soon as possible, remove the various obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250115_12678391.htm"],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","On the 1st, the National Immigration Administration marked the first anniversary of the implementation of the ten entry-exit policy measures supporting Fujian in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. Please introduce what results the “ten measures” have achieved since their implementation.","One year after the National Immigration Administration implemented ten measures in support of Fujian’s construction of the Cross-Strait Integration Development Demonstration Zone, personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan have continued to grow more active, Taiwan compatriots’ handling of affairs has become more convenient and efficient, and living in Fujian has become more convenient for Taiwan compatriots. These measures have been widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots and have effectively helped deepen integration across all areas between the two sides.\nFirst, the number of Taiwan compatriots coming to Fujian has grown substantially. In 2024, Taiwan compatriots applied for Taiwan Compatriot Permits in Fujian 359,000 times, up 25% year on year, already surpassing the 2019 level. Taiwan compatriots entering Fujian from abroad numbered 920,000 times, up 53.3% year on year, and Fujian’s status as the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to land on the mainland has become increasingly prominent.\nSecond, the service system for Taiwan compatriots has become more complete. In 2024, the number of Taiwan compatriots applying to settle in Fujian continued to rise, including both entrepreneurs who have worked on the mainland for many years and young people who have just entered society. High-quality, efficient immigration services have provided strong support for Taiwan compatriots to live, start businesses, study, and work in Fujian. Fujian has become the first home where Taiwan compatriots build, pursue, and realize their dreams.\nThird, living in Fujian has become more convenient for Taiwan compatriots. The National Immigration Administration has continued to advance the construction of a demonstration zone for the convenient use of Taiwan Compatriot Permits in Fujian, providing free real-time identity verification services to Taiwan compatriots and making it easier to handle government affairs, public services, and internet applications. At present, Taiwan compatriots holding Taiwan Compatriot Permits in Fujian can enjoy 242 convenience services across 16 fields, including transportation, finance, and telecommunications.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Someone on the island has said “the mainland is luring Taiwan compatriots to apply for ID cards.” Lai Ching-te said, “The public should not go astray for temporary benefits; the DPP authorities declared that they have found that some people hold “Chinese ID cards,” and will expand investigation; if more and more people hold mainland ID cards, it may aggravate “national security risks.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities' remarks on this matter are yet another ploy of their manipulation of \"cognitive warfare\" and their implementation of a \"green terror.\" Residents of Taiwan who come to the mainland to study, work, live, or settle do so by their own independent choice. The DPP authorities take the opportunity to hype the \"mainland threat,\" intimidating and restricting the independent choices of Taiwan's people and depriving them of the opportunity for greater and better development. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\n\"Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family.\" We welcome Taiwan residents who view the mainland's development prospects favorably and choose to settle on the mainland, and we will process their applications in accordance with the law and regulations. In the future, we will continue to create better conditions, and provide greater scope, for Taiwan compatriots to study, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland. We welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to seize opportunities and come to the mainland to achieve greater and better development for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Please introduce the flights and routes of the 2024 cross-Strait “small three links” passenger service and the passenger traffic.","The “Xiao San Tong” routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially between the people of Fujian and Taiwan. They have played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integration and development and enhancing the well-being of the people on both sides. In 2024, the “Xiao San Tong” routes operated 8,817 trips, carrying 1,367,228 passengers, representing year-on-year increases of 67.2% and 78.8%, respectively. At present, the four “Xiao San Tong” passenger routes—Mawei to Matsu, Huangqi to Matsu, Quanzhou to Kinmen, and Xiamen to Kinmen—operate a total of 210 trips per week. Since the resumption of tourism by Fujian Province residents to Matsu and Kinmen, as of the end of December, 193 people had traveled to Matsu in group tours and 885 people had traveled individually; 2,834 people had traveled to Kinmen in group tours and 39,751 people had traveled individually.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the Mainland via the “Xiao San Tong” routes to look around, to trace their roots and honor their ancestors, to visit relatives and friends, and to engage in exchanges and cooperation. The DPP authorities should put the well-being of compatriots on both sides first, and as soon as possible remove all artificial restrictions to achieve full normalization of the “Xiao San Tong.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The online selection of the 'Top Ten Cross-Strait Relations News of 2024' was officially launched on January 14. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The online selection event 'Top Ten Cross-Strait Relations News of 2024,' hosted by China Taiwan Network, officially launched on January 14, and voting will close at 5 p.m. on January 21. A total of 14 news items have been shortlisted, covering major events in the development of cross-Strait relations in 2024. The final results will be announced after combining netizen voting with expert opinions. Since its launch in 2005, the event has been held successfully for 19 sessions. It has become an authoritative brand event that takes stock at the turn of the year, sorts out the direction of cross-Strait relations, and comments on major cross-Strait news events, and it has exerted broad influence on both sides of the Strait. We welcome netizens on both sides to vote and interact through the China Taiwan Network website and new media platforms on both sides, such as Weibo and WeChat official accounts, and together select the 'Top Ten Cross-Strait Relations News' of 2024.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwanese media reported that the DPP authorities’ 2025 “media policy and business promotion fee” budget reached a high of NT$1.49 billion, a sharp increase of nearly 70% over last year. The “promotion fee,” used to feed online armies and organize events, is even far higher than the “media promotion fee.” The Ministry of Digital Affairs has also budgeted over NT$30 million to hire “cleaners.” Public opinion has…","The sharp surge in related budgets and funding shows that the DPP authorities are repeating their old tricks of “spending the people's money to wash the people's brains,” and going even further. To cover up their incompetence in governance, the DPP authorities habitually manipulate public opinion on the island to conduct a “large-scale internal propaganda” effort to paint a false picture of peace, and they foster cyber armies to attack dissenters and smear the mainland. All sectors of the island have long reached a public consensus on this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","First question: the island is paying close attention to whether this year’s cross-Strait tourism “Small Two Meetings” consultations will be launched, and whether cross-Strait tourism can welcome the arrival of spring warmth. Second question: the Mainland Affairs Council said that Taitung County Magistrate Rao Ching-ling’s recent visit to the mainland, related activities of which were not reported in advance, and…","First question. We do not oppose resuming institutionalized consultations between the two associations, but consultations must have a foundation. As long as both sides return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” there will be no obstacle to dialogue and exchanges between the two associations.\nSecond question. County Magistrate Rao Qingling's visit to Beijing this time was mainly to promote the Taitung County sugar apples. After arriving in Beijing, we arranged for Director Song Tao to meet with County Magistrate Rao and his delegation and to listen to the opinions and suggestions of people from all sectors in Taitung on the development of cross-Strait relations. County Magistrate Rao “followed the host's arrangements” and, during the meeting, spoke on behalf of county residents, thanked the mainland side for restoring and expanding the import of Taitung sugar apples, and welcomed mainland compatriots to visit Taitung for tourism and exchanges. Such exchanges and interactions have the goal and purpose of doing practical good, doing good deeds, and solving difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, and of enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people, which is why they gained their support and recognition. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' threat to punish and suppress people who promote and participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation has once again exposed their true face of going against mainstream public opinion on the island and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. As long as something is supported by compatriots on both sides and is beneficial to them, we will keep doing it and do it even better. We will uphold the concept of “a close family across the Strait,” consistently respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts together with people from all sectors in Taiwan, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development, and continuously seek benefits and well-being for compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Will the mainland resume allowing mainland students to study in Taiwan this year? Second question: Lo Wen-chia, vice chairman and secretary-general of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that “cross-Strait issues were created by history since 1949,” and that the SEF has always respected the history it has traversed in the 35 years since its founding. What is your response to this? Third…","First question: We have always been committed to providing Taiwanese students studying at mainland universities with treatment equal to that of mainland students, and to providing support and guarantees in medical care, internships, employment, and other areas, and we actively create conditions for cross-Strait youth exchanges. However, the DPP authorities say they hope the mainland will allow mainland students to study in Taiwan, yet in practice they artificially restrict mainland students from studying in Taiwan, impose unreasonable restrictions on mainland students in Taiwan, and treat them unfairly. Faced with these discriminatory restrictions and the DPP authorities' poor attitude, can mainland parents feel at ease letting their children study in Taiwan? Can the willingness of mainland students to study in Taiwan be unaffected? The DPP authorities should stop political manipulation as soon as possible and genuinely safeguard the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan. That is what real goodwill looks like.\nSecond question: Since 1949, although the two sides have not yet been fully reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and Taiwan's status as part of China has never changed. The Communist Party of China has always regarded resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland as a historical mission it will pursue unwaveringly. It has united and led compatriots on both sides of the Strait to advance the situation in the Taiwan Strait from tense confrontation toward easing and improvement, and then onto the path of peaceful development, with cross-Strait relations continuously achieving breakthroughs.\nThe historical background and important role of the '1992 Consensus' are very clear. In 1992, under authorization from both sides of the Strait, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait and the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan reached, through the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, the '1992 Consensus,' under which each side orally expressed that 'both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.' This historical process and its content are documented in clear records, and they cannot be denied or distorted by anyone or any force. The reaching of the '1992 Consensus' reflects the political wisdom of both sides of the Strait in seeking common ground while setting aside differences and conducting equal consultations, and it fully demonstrates that the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have the ability and wisdom to resolve their own problems.\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China. As long as the country is not split and both sides recognize that compatriots on both sides are Chinese, all sectors on both sides of the Strait can sit down and conduct extensive and in-depth consultations on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation.\nThird question: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China's territory. At a time when the tourism industry and grassroots people in Taiwan are calling for mainland tourists to be allowed to visit Taiwan, and while we are actively studying the expansion of travel by mainland residents to Taiwan, some people on the island deliberately hype this up, which is clearly motivated by ulterior intentions.\nFourth question: The National Palace Museum in Beijing and the National Palace Museum in Taipei share the same roots and the same lineage. They are an integral whole, and they are a cultural and historical testament that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation. The national treasures and cultural relics collected by the National Palace Museums on both sides of the Strait are the crystallization of Chinese civilization and the inheritance of China's long history and brilliant culture. They carry the cultural lineage and historical ties that cannot be severed between the two sides, and they embody the shared humanistic sentiment of Chinese people at home and abroad.\nWe welcome exchanges and cooperation between the National Palace Museum in Beijing and the National Palace Museum in Taipei to jointly inherit and promote China's excellent traditional culture. However, we solemnly warn the DPP authorities to have a correct understanding of history and culture, and not to forget their ancestors while holding their ancestors' legacy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, Shi Xueyan, a mainland spouse residing in Taiwan and former councilor of Nantou County, was removed from her council position by the DPP authorities on the so-called “nationality” issue. In addition, five village chiefs may be removed from their positions for the same reason. The Mainland Affairs Council said that holding public office precludes “dual nationality,” and that this has nothing to do with…","There is only one China in the world. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. How could there be a so-called “dual nationality” issue? The DPP authorities’ practice is a deliberate provocation against the historical and legal fact that both sides belong to one China. They intend to use this to create trouble, which will certainly be opposed and will surely backfire on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","US think tank “Council on Foreign Relations” recently released its annual “Conflict Risk Assessment Report.” For the eighth consecutive year, it has listed the Taiwan Strait crisis as a “Level 1 risk,” with a likelihood of “moderate” and an impact on US interests at the “highest level.” What comments do you have on this?","The current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, obstinately uphold a separatist “Taiwan independence” stance, and continually collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. If the US side hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and clearly oppose “Taiwan independence.” We hope that compatriots in Taiwan, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” provocations and external interference, and join us in jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","川报封面新闻记者","Some mainland researchers recently named 16 new spider species after songs by Taiwan singer Jay Chou, such as “Rewind Ai Spider” (倒带艾蛛) and “Dragon Fist Ai Spider” (龙拳艾蛛), which has sparked heated discussion among netizens on both sides of the Strait. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Young people on both sides of the Strait are full of vitality, have active minds, and distinctive personalities. They like to express themselves and communicate in relaxed and natural ways, which shows that young people on both sides, nourished by Chinese culture, share a common cultural foundation, cultural taste and emotional resonance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-15","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Reports indicate that the “Chongqing Municipality Regulations on Promoting Investment by Taiwan Compatriots” took effect on January 1, 2025. What opportunities will the implementation of the Regulations provide for the next stage of development for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises?","The “Chongqing Municipality Regulations on Promoting Investment by Taiwan Compatriots” have been in effect since January 1 of this year. The Regulations consist of 31 articles, covering multiple aspects including further implementing equal treatment, clarifying key support areas and support methods, and effectively protecting lawful rights and interests.\nSpecifically, in terms of supporting young Taiwanese, the Regulations clearly encourage Taiwan youth to find employment and start businesses. Taiwan youth may enjoy public employment and entrepreneurship services, as well as policy support such as entrepreneurship-guaranteed loans, one-time entrepreneurship subsidies, and admission to entrepreneurship incubation parks, including in policy interpretation consultation, employment and entrepreneurship guidance, and training and education. In terms of serving Taiwan compatriots, the Regulations actively promote the shift from “convenient issuance of certificates” to “convenient use of certificates,” support Taiwan compatriots in joining academic social organizations as well as professional and industry social organizations in economics, science and technology, culture, and arts, and enjoying rights and fulfilling obligations in accordance with the organizations' charters; and support Taiwan compatriots in participating in trade unions in accordance with law. In terms of helping Taiwan businesses and enterprises, the Regulations maximally open the scope of market access. Taiwan enterprises investing in Chongqing may enjoy the relevant treatment for promoting high-quality development of private enterprises, and they may receive policy support in participating in innovation, medical care, agriculture and forestry, and financial cooperation, as well as in transformation and development, participation in state-owned enterprise reform, and participation in government procurement.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202501/t20250115_12678390.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-01-16","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Marco Rubio, Donald Trump’s nominee for Secretary of State, said yesterday at a confirmation hearing that China was the most potent and dangerous near-peer adversary that the US has ever faced. Rubio also said that the US must show China that it will pay too high a price if it invades Taiwan. Does China have a comment on this?","China’s development is characterized by a distinct historical logic and strong endogenous driving force. There is nothing to hide about our goal, which is to deliver a better life for the people and make greater contribution to the world. We view and handle China-US relations in line with the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence, and win-win cooperation put forward by President Xi Jinping, and resolutely safeguard our own sovereignty, security, and development interests. The US needs to establish a right perception towards China, and stop its illegitimate attacks and smears on China.\nTaiwan is part of China and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. The greatest challenge to cross-Strait peace is “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and foreign interference and disruption. The US needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, act on its commitment of not supporting “Taiwan independence,” stop abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202501/t20250116_11536700.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202501/t20250116_11536633.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-01-16","Guo Jiakun","The Paper","It’s reported that Taiwan “foreign minister” Lin Chia-lung will attend the inauguration of Palau’s President as the “special envoy of Taiwan president” from January 15 to 18. What’s your comment?","Taiwan is a province of China. There is no such thing as “president” or “foreign ministry” of Taiwan. There’s only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. The DPP authorities’ attempt of seeking “Taiwan independence” through foreign support and their secession attempt are doomed to fail.\nWe also noted that while the DPP authorities are trying to consolidate their so-called “diplomatic relations,” friendly personages in countries such as Tuvalu, Palau and the Marshall Islands expressed to us on multiple occasions their willingness of establishing or restoring normal diplomatic relations with China. China establishing or restoring diplomatic ties with these countries is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends, and is only a matter of time. Let me reiterate that it’s never too late to make new friends and China stands ready to open up new chapters for relations with these countries on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202501/t20250116_11536700.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202501/t20250116_11536633.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-01-17","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan’s Central News Agency reported that Taiwan leader Lai Ching-te recently claimed, in a speech, that China, Russia and other countries are threatening the rules-based international order and seriously affecting peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific and globally. What is your comment?","Wu Qian said that Lai Ching-te and his ilk are ignorant of their own history and are spouting nonsense. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly stipulate that Taiwan returns to China, and this is an important component of the international order after World War II. The fruits of victory in World War II must be respected and upheld, and Taiwan has no international legal status other than being part of China.\nWu Qian stated that, in fact, Lai Ching-te's authorities' collusion with external forces to continuously carry out independence-seeking provocations has become the greatest source of chaos undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and even the Asia-Pacific region. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te's authorities and “Taiwan independence” elements: “seeking independence through force” is nothing more than a mantis trying to stop a chariot. It is entirely digging one's own grave. Those who pursue “Taiwan independence” will never come to a good end, and the PLA will never show the slightest hesitation in striving for reunification by suppressing “Taiwan independence.” We have every reason to believe that Taiwan should return, and when it returns, the world will be wide.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/20250117/333bf21e2ab349a8a577e620d63f8631/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-01-17","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The 076 amphibious assault ship, the lead vessel Sichuan, recently held a launching and naming ceremony in Shanghai, drawing intense attention from public opinion at home and abroad. Some Taiwanese media claimed that the 076 ship's multi-dimensional amphibious landing capability is astonishing and that its deployment will be the most dangerous moment for Taiwan. Some foreign media have also hyped that the ship…","Wu Qian said that developing necessary weapons and equipment based on national defense needs is common practice among countries around the world. The independent development and construction of the Type 076 amphibious assault ship is a normal arrangement made with a view to national security needs and the overall development of naval construction. Its purpose is to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and to better maintain world and regional peace and stability. The ship is a new type of amphibious assault ship independently developed by China, innovatively applying electromagnetic catapult and arresting technology. It can carry fixed-wing aircraft, helicopters, amphibious equipment, and so on, and has strong amphibious combat and far-seas operational capabilities. After the ship is launched, equipment commissioning, mooring trials, sea trials, and other work will be carried out as planned.\nWu Qian emphasized that China has always adhered to the path of peaceful development and has consistently pursued a defensive national defense policy without wavering. The launch of the Type 076 amphibious assault ship is a normal arrangement in the development of naval equipment, and it is not directed at any specific target, region, or country.","","http://www.news.cn/politics/20250117/333bf21e2ab349a8a577e620d63f8631/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-01-17","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 17 — The Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced on the 17th that it will soon resume group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai. Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions from reporters that day, saying that the mainland side has always upheld the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” has consistently supported normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and regularizing exchanges in all fields, and works for the benefit of Taiwan compatriots. The mainland's tourism authorities' announcement that they will soon resume group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai is a concrete step in response to the eager expectations of compatriots on both sides for stronger exchanges and contacts. It accords with the common aspirations of Taiwan compatriots for peace, development, exchange and cooperation. We actively support this and welcome it.\nHe said that we hope the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will face up to mainstream public opinion on the island and the calls from the industry, lift the “group tour ban” as soon as possible, cancel the travel advisories against island residents traveling to the mainland, and fully resume cross-Strait passenger direct flights to all destinations, so as to create favorable conditions for personnel exchanges and exchanges in all fields across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250117_12678740.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-17","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华17日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 17 — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on the 17th, saying that preparations for resuming group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai are actively underway. The crux and obstacle to cross-Strait tourism issues lies with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, not with whether the…","Chen Binhua said that we have always adhered to the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and have continued to work to promote personnel exchanges, tourism and other exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, releasing goodwill. The key now is whether the DPP authorities can face up to mainstream public opinion and industry calls in Taiwan and, as soon as possible, lift the various obstacles and restrictions on cross-Strait tourism exchanges, so as to create favorable conditions for personnel exchanges and cooperation across the Strait. All sectors of Taiwan society and the public are waiting to see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250117_12678984.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-01-20","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","We’ve learned that Myanmar’s Tatmadaw and ethnic armed organization Myanmar National Democratic Alliance Army (MNDAA) held peace talks and signed a ceasefire agreement in Kunming. Can you brief us on the background and details of the peace talks?","In mid-January 2025, with China’s mediation and effort to drive progress, the Myanmar government and Myanmar National Democratic Alliance Army held the seventh round of peace talks in Kunming, Yunnan. The two sides reached and signed a formal ceasefire agreement, and stopped fighting at 12 a.m. on January 18, 2025, Beijing time. The two sides thanked China for facilitating the results of this round of peace talks.\nDeescalating tensions in northern Myanmar serves the common interests of all parties in Myanmar and regional countries, and is conducive to ensuring the safety and security, stability and development of the China-Myanmar border area. China and Myanmar are friendly neighbors, and we firmly oppose wars and turbulence in Myanmar. We hope that all parties will maintain the momentum of ceasefire and peace talks, earnestly implement existing common understandings, take the initiative in deescalating the situation on the ground, and further negotiate and settle relevant issues through dialogue.\nChina firmly supports Myanmar in safeguarding independence, sovereignty, national unity and territorial integrity, firmly supports Myanmar’s effort to keep the country peaceful and stable and grow its economy, and firmly supports Myanmar in realizing political reconciliation at an early date and advancing its domestic political agenda under the framework of the constitution. China stands ready to actively promote talks for peace and provide support and help for the peace process in northern Myanmar.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202501/t20250120_11541005.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202501/t20250120_11541143.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-01-21","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that on January 21, a strong earthquake occurred in southern Taiwan, causing injuries and property losses. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We are deeply concerned about the earthquake disaster, extend condolences to the affected residents, and sincerely hope that affected residents will quickly restore normal production and living order.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250121_12679806.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 24 (Electric) — Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 24th that we are pleased to see that the travel scouting groups from Fujian and Shanghai have submitted requests to relevant Taiwan authorities for inspection visits, and we hope that tourism operators from both places can smoothly carry out their visits to Taiwan for inspection, laying a good foundation for the resumption of group tours to Taiwan by residents of the two places.\nA reporter asked: As we understand it, today the Fujian and Shanghai tourism scouting groups have submitted applications to Taiwan's relevant authorities for inspection visits to the island. Are you aware of the situation? Chen Binhua made the above remarks in response.\n\"This is indeed the case,\" Chen Binhua said. As we understand it, after the Ministry of Culture and Tourism recently announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, the cross-Strait tourism industries have actively communicated and connected, and enthusiasm for restoring and expanding cross-Strait tourism exchanges is running high.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250124_12680589.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-01-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, January 24 (electronic dispatch). Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions on the 24th, stating that Taiwan residents have the freedom and right to choose to settle on the mainland. In the future, we will, as always, create better conditions and provide greater scope for Taiwan compatriots to study, work, start businesses and settle on the mainland.\nA reporter asked: The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that, after verification, three Taiwan residents hold “Chinese mainland ID cards,” and their Taiwan identities have been cancelled. It will continue to verify relevant residents and, if there is evidence, will revoke the household registration of the persons concerned in accordance with regulations. What is your comment on this? Chen Binhua made the above remarks in response.\nHe pointed out that the DPP authorities are hyping this up with the aim of intimidating and restricting Taiwan residents' independent choices, and are using every means to interfere with and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and integrated development. This is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202501/t20250124_12680592.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-01-27","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","We have learned that President Xi Jinping’s special representative, Vice President Han Zheng received high-level reception when attending President Trump’s inauguration not long ago. Meanwhile, some Taiwanese media outlets reported that Taiwan’s so-called “Legislative Yuan” said recently that its so-called “president” Han Kuo-yu got reception from the U.S. at an unprecedented high level when he led a delegation…","On January 20, President Xi Jinping’s special representative, Vice President Han Zheng attended the inauguration ceremony of President Donald Trump at U.S. invitation. He was seated on the dais of Capitol Rotunda, the main venue of the inauguration ceremony, and exchanged greetings and spoke with leaders of relevant countries and U.S. political dignitaries there.\nChina is firmly opposed to any form of official interactions between the U.S. and the Taiwan region. As for the so-called “high-level reception” relevant person of the Taiwan authorities got from the U.S., it is apparently disinformation self-bestowed by Taiwan authorities for self-consumption.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202501/t20250127_11546848.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202501/t20250127_11546757.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-02-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","XINHUA, Beijing, February 5. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to a reporter's question on the 5th: “We were shocked to learn of the passing of Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun and are deeply saddened. The Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits has sent a message of condolence to the family of Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun. Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun inherited her family's scholarship, devoted herself to promoting Chinese culture, took part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various fields for many years, and accompanied Mr. Gu Zhenfu in attending the ‘Wang-Gu Talks’ and ‘Wang-Gu Meeting,’ making positive contributions to improving and developing cross-Strait relations. Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun upheld the ‘1992 Consensus’ and actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges. We express profound grief at the passing of Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun and extend our deepest condolences to her family.”\nA reporter asked: Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun passed away on February 4. What comments does the mainland side have? Zhu Fenglian made the above remarks in her response.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250205_12682360.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 5 — Lai Ching-te recently, while attending the Straits Exchange Foundation's “Mainland Taiwan Businesspeople Spring Festival Event,” once again promoted “mutual non-subordination,” saying he would continue the so-called “four insistences” cross-Strait policy and that both sides should “replace containment with exchanges and confrontation with dialogue.” In response, Zhu…","Zhu Fenglian said that the starting point and goal of developing cross-Strait relations is to enhance the well-being of compatriots. However, the DPP authorities say one thing and do another, and for political self-interest they are willing to harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” means there will be no peace in the Taiwan Strait, and plotting separation will only harm and destroy Taiwan. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own well-being, will join us in firmly opposing all provocations to plot independence, jointly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, jointly promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and jointly create a beautiful future for cross-Strait relations and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250205_12682362.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-02-07","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan said that it detected six Chinese balloons off the island today. Is this true and does China have a comment on this?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250207_11550953.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250207_11550963.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-07","Lin Jian","Antara","With President Xi Jinping meeting with Sultan Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei Darussalam and Thai Prime Minister Paetongtarn Shinawatra yesterday, was there any specific discussion regarding the Myanmar issue, which affects ASEAN’s credibility as a regional organization?","Yesterday, President Xi Jinping met with and held talks with Brunei’s Sultan and Thai Prime Minister respectively who are visiting China, and they exchanged views on international and regional issues of mutual interests. We’ve released readouts which you may refer to.\nOn the Myanmar issue, let me reiterate that China and Myanmar are friendly neighbors. China’s position on this issue is clear-cut. We follow the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, support Myanmar’s effort to safeguard independence, sovereignty, national unity and territorial integrity, support various parties in Myanmar in carrying out friendly consultation toward political reconciliation, and support Myanmar in resuming the political transition process.\nMyanmar is an indispensable important member of the ASEAN family. China supports ASEAN in maintaining solidarity, playing a positive and constructive role as the main channel in mediation on the Myanmar issue and implementing ASEAN’s five-point consensus on Myanmar to help stabilize and deescalate the situation in Myanmar.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250207_11550953.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250207_11550963.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-02-07","Zhu Fenglian","国务院台办发言人朱凤莲7日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 7. Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a reporter’s question on the 7th, saying that she does not oppose the “Little Two Associations” communicating on specific issues in cross-strait tourism after cross-strait tourism resumes. However, she opposes using communication through the “Little Two Associations” as a pretext to…","Zhu Fenglian said that after the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan by residents of Fujian and Shanghai, a reconnaissance group composed of tourism operators from Fujian and Shanghai promptly requested to Taiwan's relevant authorities a visit to Taiwan for inspection. This shows that we have a positive attitude and keep our word in resuming mainland residents' travel to Taiwan, and it has been widely welcomed by Taiwan's tourism industry and public. However, the passive response and disguised obstruction by the DPP authorities are like a bucket of cold water poured over their enthusiasm.\nShe pointed out that, as is well known, the crux and obstacle to cross-Strait tourism lies in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities, not in whether the “Small Two Organizations” communicate. Communication between the “Small Two Organizations” is not a precondition for resuming cross-Strait tourism. At the beginning of the COVID-19 epidemic in early 2020, the DPP authorities disregarded the relevant cross-Strait agreements and unilaterally imposed a comprehensive ban on mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, and also prohibited island travel agencies from operating group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents, all without communicating with the mainland side through the “Small Two Organizations.” In 2024, mainland residents' travel to Matsu and Kinmen resumed successively, also without communication through the “Small Two Organizations.” However, to further resume mainland residents' travel to Taiwan, in November 2024, we considered the request of the Straits Tourism Association in Taiwan and agreed to its visit to the mainland and to meet with the Straits Tourism Association of the mainland, but the Taiwan side unexpectedly cancelled the itinerary at the last minute on the grounds of insufficient budget. Before the Spring Festival, when the reconnaissance groups from Fujian and Shanghai requested Taiwan's relevant authorities to visit Taiwan for inspection, the Straits Tourism Association of the mainland also simultaneously notified the Beijing Office of the Taiwan Tourism Association. We do not oppose the “Small Two Organizations” contacting and communicating on specific issues in cross-Strait tourism after cross-Strait tourism resumes, but we oppose using the name of “Small Two Organizations” communication as a pretext to actually obstruct mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan.\nZhu Fenglian said that the DPP authorities, driven by their inherent nature of seeking “independence” and confrontation, as well as political self-interest, turn a deaf ear to the mainstream public opinion and the calls of the industry in Taiwan, and turn a blind eye to the damage to the interests of grassroots people and operators in Taiwan. They repeatedly obstruct, restrict, and set up barriers to cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in various fields with untenable excuses. This is not popular, and the industry on the island has expressed extreme disappointment and strong indignation. If they do not change course and persist in acting selfishly, they will surely lose even more public support and reap the consequences of their own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250207_12682881.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-02-10","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It’s reported that a few days ago, U.S. President Trump met with Japanese Prime Minister Shigeru Ishiba. In the Joint Leaders’ Statement, the two leaders emphasized the importance of maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, opposed any attempts to unilaterally change the status quo by force or coercion, and expressed support for Taiwan’s meaningful participation in international organizations.…","The part of the U.S.-Japan joint statement on China constitutes open interference in China’s domestic affairs, and an attack and smear against China, which is also aimed at scare-mongering in the region. China deplores and firmly opposes this, and has lodged serious protests with the U.S. and Japan.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and is at the core of China’s core interests, which brooks no external interference. Both the U.S. and Japanese governments have made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question. In particular, Japan bears serious historical responsibilities for its aggression against Taiwan and colonial rule over the island, and should all the more act prudently on the Taiwan question. The biggest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait at present is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. If relevant countries truly care about peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, what they should do is to uphold the one-China principle, and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” The Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations must and can only be handled in line with the one-China principle. Taiwan has no basis, reason or right to join international organizations that only sovereign countries join.\nDiaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have always been part of China’s territory. China’s activities in relevant waters are fully legitimate and lawful.\nChina has all along followed the WTO rules. The so-called China’s economic aggression is purely groundless.\nWe call on the U.S. and Japan to abide by the one-China principle and honor their commitments, immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces in any form, earnestly respect China’s territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, stop manipulating China-related issues, and take concrete actions to play a constructive role for the peace and development in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250210_11552122.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250210_11552101.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-11","Guo Jiakun","Nikkei","According to the information on the website of Japan Coast Guard, the buoy installed in waters to the northeast of Taiwan has disappeared. The Japanese government believed that it’s because China removed the buoy. Is this judgment of the Japanese government consistent with the actual situation? If this is true, would you please explain the reason and purpose for China to do so?","China’s installation of hydrometeorological buoy in relevant waters is consistent with both domestic and international laws. The buoy has completed its task at the site. According to the actual need of science observation, relevant Chinese agencies have implemented voluntary and technical adjustment regarding the buoy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250211_11552999.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250211_11552937.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-12","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Two U.S. ships sailed through the Taiwan Strait this week, which was the first transit there since Donald Trump’s inauguration. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","The PLA Eastern Theater Command has made a response.\nLet me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question has nothing to do with freedom of navigation but bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China firmly opposes any country challenging or threatening China’s sovereignty and security under the pretext of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250212_11553791.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250212_11553735.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-12","Guo Jiakun","Kyodo News","It’s reported that the Japanese Defense Minister and the U.S. Defense Secretary will hold talks in Japan in late March, during which they will talk about the Taiwan question. Will this affect Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s plan to visit Japan?","The recent U.S.-Japan Joint Leaders’ Statement contains irresponsible remarks on issues relating to Taiwan, which interfered in China’s internal affairs. China has made serious protests to the U.S. and Japan to express our strong opposition.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and is at the core of China’s core interests, which brooks no external interference. Both the U.S. and Japanese governments have made serious commitments to China on the Taiwan question. In particular, Japan bears serious historical responsibilities for its aggression against Taiwan and colonial rule over the island, and should all the more act prudently on the Taiwan question. We urge the U.S. and Japan to abide by the one-China principle and their own commitments, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs at once, and stop manipulating China-related issues.\nOn the specific visit you mentioned, I have no information to share.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250212_11553791.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250212_11553735.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning everyone, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Please introduce the situation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait celebrating the Spring Festival and Lantern Festival.","The Year of the Snake marks the first Spring Festival celebrated as a “Intangible Cultural Heritage Edition.” Rich and colorful intangible cultural heritage (ICH) projects have given this year’s Spring Festival across the Taiwan Strait a much stronger sense of ritual. Jiangsu Province held the “Year-End Flower Charm, Spring Brings Blessings” event, where Taiwan compatriots and their relatives experienced ICH crafts such as year-end flowers and rubbing. Shandong Province held a series of events including “Shandong Charm Conveys Affection, the Snake Brings Auspiciousness; Both Sides of the Strait Gather to Celebrate the Spring Festival” and “One Family Across Mountains and Seas: Shandong and Taiwan Reunite,” bringing together Shandong natives on both sides of the Strait online and offline to welcome spring and send blessings. Henan Province organized folk activities for Taiwan compatriots in Henan, including ICH paper-cutting, Hanfu gatherings, writing spring couplets, and handicraft making, so that everyone could share the strong Spring Festival atmosphere together. Wuhan held a series of “Festive Spirit Welcomes the New Spring, ICH Celebrates the Lunar New Year” activities, where more than 200 Taiwan compatriots and Wuhan residents experienced ICH folk culture such as “Wuhan paper-cutting” together. Guangzhou organized cross-Strait youth to carry out “Joyful Lunar New Year” ICH cultural activities, jointly experiencing ICH tie-dyeing and traditional New Year customs. Quanzhou, under the theme “World Heritage China New Year,” carried out ICH cultural activities such as “Two Dongshi Stones of Fujian and Taiwan Count the Palace Lanterns Together” and “Ink Fragrance, Warm Feelings Across the Strait” to welcome spring and send blessings.\nDuring the Spring Festival, folk artists from Jiangsu Province displayed ICH cultures such as the distinctive Qinhuai colored lanterns, Suzhou embroidery, woodblock New Year pictures, Huishan clay figurines, and Nanjing paper-cutting at the 2025 New Taipei Lantern Festival, which were warmly welcomed by New Taipei residents. The Wuhan Gaolong dragon and the Miaoli “Huobang” (bàng) dragon jointly took part in the Miaoli “Auspicious Dragon Patrol Village” spring welcoming activity, and also joined the Nantou Lantern Festival to add to the festivities. The Chongqing Acrobatic Troupe gave 10 spectacular acrobatic performances at Fo Guang Shan in Kaohsiung, attracting more than 10,000 viewers. The 2025 Cross-Strait Spring Festival Fireworks Gala, themed “Golden Snake Brings Auspiciousness; Both Sides of the Strait Welcome the Spring,” was held simultaneously in Xiamen and Kinmen on the first day of the first lunar month, conveying the shared hopes of people on both sides of the Strait for a better future. “Happy Chicken Popcorn: 2025 Cross-Strait Children’s New Spring Joy Gala” was broadcast simultaneously on both sides through Xiamen TV and Taiwan’s children’s channel MOMO TV, allowing audiences on both sides to deeply experience the warmth and vitality of “Dele (Hokkien: “where to go”) for the Lunar New Year? Xiamen welcomes you li (Hokkien: “you”)!”\nToday is the Lantern Festival, the 15th day of the first lunar month. The “Moon Full City·Ai Gathers the Greater Bay Area” 2025 Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao-Taiwan Youth Lantern Festival Gala will air tonight. Youth from Guangdong, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan who work and build their futures in the Greater Bay Area will together experience the charm of the Bay Area during this first ICH-themed Spring Festival, immersively experiencing ICH cultures such as Meizhou Hakka fire-dragon dancing, Foshan lion dancing, Guangzhou Xicun kiln, Zhuhai crane dance, Nansha qilin dance, and Cantonese opera, and showcasing the enthusiasm of Guangdong, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan youth for inheriting and promoting the excellent traditional Chinese culture through interactive exchanges. Xiamen TV will also present “Joy Is Enough: 2025 Cross-Strait Lantern Festival Poetry and Music Gathering” tonight. Centered on the shared promotion of Chinese culture on both sides of the Strait, it uses original poetry and music to make excellent traditional Chinese culture “come alive” and Minnan distinctive culture “rise into the trend,” vividly presenting the local dialects and sentiments of Fujian and Taiwan, demonstrating that the two sides are one family, and expressing shared feelings of reunion. At Quanzhou Tianhou Temple, the 19th Quan-Penghu “Begging for Turtles” prayer folk cultural activity is underway, where Cross-Strait natives together add the finishing touches to a “giant rice turtle” weighing 58,800 jin (5.88 × 10⁴ jin). Mazu temples from Quanzhou and Taiwan will also gather in Quanzhou to hold the Xunpu Mazu “Heavenly Fragrance Patrol Around the Borders” folk activity, jointly praying for blessings for both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683865.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 9th Asian Winter Games was grandly held in Harbin, drawing close attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Could the spokesperson introduce the participation of Taiwan athletes and compatriots in this Asian Winter Games?","We welcome the Chinese Taipei delegation to the 9th Asian Winter Games and extend our congratulations to Chinese Taipei athletes for their outstanding performances and results on the field. A total of 103 members of the Chinese Taipei delegation are participating in this Asian Winter Games, of whom 67 athletes are competing in multiple events including speed skating, short track speed skating, figure skating, ice hockey, curling, alpine skiing, cross-country skiing, and biathlon.\nSince the Games began, Chinese Taipei athletes have received warm support and encouragement from mainland spectators both on and off the field. In addition, many Taiwan compatriots have participated in activities such as the torch relay and opening ceremony of the Asian Winter Games, several Taiwan-funded enterprises have provided sports equipment for the Games, and many Taiwan compatriots have traveled to Harbin to watch the competitions, cheering for athletes from both sides of the Strait and experiencing the charm of winter sports together with compatriots on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683861.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Hsiao Hsu-tsen, executive director of the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation, led nearly 40 students from the “Da Jiu Academy” to visit and exchange views in Beijing on February 10. Please introduce the relevant details.","The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation organized a group of young students to Beijing mainly to take part in the series of “Dual Olympic City, Youth Appointment” Taiwan Youth Beijing Winter Season activities. Taiwan youth friends will experience winter sports in Beijing, experience Beijing's Spring Festival and Lantern Festival customs, visit Beijing's famous scenic spots and modern high-tech enterprises, and interact with students from mainland universities. We welcome Taiwan young students to come to the mainland more often to see and learn, so that young people on both sides can learn from and inspire each other and grow together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","It is understood that Zhangping in Fujian is preparing the 2nd Straits Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Conference. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From February 18 to 21, the Second Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Conference will be held in Zhangping, Fujian. Themed '\"Nong\" Qing Mi Yi \"Ying\" Yuan Ji Hui' ('Agricultural' Sentiment, Sweet Affection, 'Cherry Blossom' Destined Encounter), the conference features diverse content and forms, including an opening ceremony and 13 sub-events. These include a cross-Strait young farmers' creative agricultural products exchange market; the Haixia Cross-Strait (Longyan) Young Flower Tea E-commerce Livestreaming Festival; cross-Strait young farmers jointly planting the 'Same Roots Forest'; interactive exchanges between the National Taiwan Entrepreneurship Parks and Taiwan farmers; a Cross-Strait Snacks and Food Carnival; the 'Spring Comes to Yongfu · Cross-Strait Young Farmers Grand Reunion'; and the Haixia Hakka Descendants Ancestral Homeland Short Video Creation Competition. Cross-Strait young farmers will engage in in-depth exchanges and learn from each other through means such as sharing entrepreneurship stories of young farmers.\nAt present, Taiwan farmers and agricultural enterprises are registering enthusiastically and are highly motivated to take part. Nearly 500 people are expected to attend the exchange conference, including representatives of Taiwan county and township farmers' associations, young farmers' associations, and agriculture-related business associations, as well as mainland new-generation farmers and Taiwan farmer representatives. During the event, more than 100,000 cherry trees in the thousand-mu tea garden of the Zhangping Taiwan Farmers Entrepreneurship Park will enter their peak bloom. Media reporters are welcome to visit and report, and to join us for a spring flower tea appointment.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The “2025 Taipei Lantern Festival” was held in Taipei from February 2 to 16. By convention, delegations from Shanghai were invited to take part. However, the DPP authorities have repeatedly refused to issue entry permits to two Shanghai delegations. What is your comment?","Since 2015, Shanghai has been invited to send delegations to Taiwan to participate in the Taipei Lantern Festival for ten consecutive years. Shanghai lanterns have been warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots, and people on both sides of the Strait jointly celebrate the Spring Festival in a joyful and harmonious atmosphere. However, the DPP authorities have repeatedly interfered with and undermined civil exchanges across the Strait, and refused to issue entry permits to the Shanghai delegation to Taiwan to participate in the 2025 Taipei Lantern Festival. The DPP authorities' political manipulation knows no bottom line. It disrupts the peaceful atmosphere of compatriots on both sides celebrating the Spring Festival, violates the common wish of compatriots on both sides to visit each other often, and interferes with the normal order of cross-Strait relations and cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. It is unpopular and should be condemned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683859.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","US President Trump recently said he would impose high tariffs on imports of computer chips and semiconductors, and again claimed that 98% of chip business has gone to Taiwan, expressing hope that these industries will return to the United States. The DPP authorities said they will propose four “countermeasures” to “strengthen Taiwan-US industrial cooperation.” What comment do you have?","The U.S. practices of unilateralism and trade protectionism once again prove that the United States always upholds “America first.” Facts have repeatedly shown that the more the DPP authorities “rely on the United States,” the deeper the harm to Taiwan. So-called “countermeasures” are nothing but “selling out Taiwan to curry favor with the United States”; they will only undermine the foundations of Taiwan's industrial development and sacrifice the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683858.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","During the Spring Festival holiday, the cross-Strait “mini three links” passenger routes welcomed a surge of compatriots from both sides traveling home to visit relatives and for tourism. Could the spokesperson introduce the situation of the cross-Strait “mini three links” during the Spring Festival?","During the Spring Festival, the cross-Strait “mini three links” routes have continued to operate smoothly, facilitating cross-Strait residents, especially Taiwan compatriots, in visiting relatives and friends, celebrating the Spring Festival, and sightseeing. According to statistics, the four “mini three links” passenger routes—Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Huangqi in Lianjiang to Matsu—deployed a total of 16 vessels providing 8,542 passenger seats, with 126 round-trip flights per week, totaling 252 trips. From January 14 to February 5, the “mini three links” routes operated 807 trips in total, carrying 121,000 passenger trips. Of these, the Xiamen-Kinmen route operated 551 trips, carrying 107,000 passenger trips; the Quanzhou-Kinmen route operated 86 trips, carrying more than 6,600 passenger trips; and the Matsu routes (Mawei-Matsu and Huangqi-Matsu) operated 170 trips, carrying more than 7,600 passenger trips.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","It is reported that the 23rd “Two Ma Spring Lantern Festival” event was held in Fuzhou, and Taiwan's Lianjiang County took part together to celebrate the Lantern Festival. The DPP authorities questioned the mainland's deliberate promotion of the message that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are connected by blood ties. What comments do you have on this?","The Lantern Festival, as a traditional festival of the Chinese nation, carries the shared cultural memory and national sentiment of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. On a festive occasion of reunion, it is entirely normal for fellow villagers from both places to gather together and celebrate the holiday. The DPP authorities, out of selfish interest in pursuing “independence,” have meddled with this, interfered with civil exchanges across the Strait, and harmed the feelings of compatriots on both sides. This is not in line with popular sentiment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”记者","Recently, some Republican U.S. House members proposed a so-called \"resolution\" calling on the U.S. to abolish the One-China Policy and restore \"formal diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. The DPP authorities said they were grateful. What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. It is the political foundation and fundamental premise for the establishment of China-U.S. diplomatic relations and the development of diplomatic ties between them. A few U.S. politicians, disregarding historical and legal facts and disregarding the commitments the U.S. side made on the one-China principle in the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, are attempting to turn back the wheel of history, and we firmly oppose this. It must be pointed out that no matter how the DPP authorities scheme to “rely on the United States to seek independence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot change the outcome that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te again played up the mainland’s “threat” to Taiwan, claiming that in recent years there have been more and more mainland espionage cases against Taiwan, and that the mainland’s “united front” work against Taiwan has become increasingly serious. What is your comment?","Everyone is probably used to this kind of claim and this set of tactics. In order to pursue “independence,” the DPP authorities need to relentlessly “oppose China,” constantly exaggerate the mainland’s “threat,” and treat cross-strait exchanges and cooperation as floods and ferocious beasts. This is the internal logic behind Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities repeatedly fabricating lies, deceiving and intimidating the Taiwan public, and inciting cross-strait opposition and confrontation. Though they have racked their brains, they have run out of tricks, and they cannot fool people.\nThe tide of cross-strait exchanges is surging forward and will not stop or be cut off. We will continue to actively promote the normalization and routinization of exchanges across all fields between the two sides, and continue to improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, so that compatriots on both sides of the Strait can continuously deepen mutual understanding and friendship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683862.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently released a so-called “Report on the Situation in Mainland China,” which grossly distorts and smears the political, economic and social conditions on the mainland. What is your comment?","The so-called “report” by Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council distorts facts and smears the mainland. Its purpose is to deceive and mislead the island’s public and to manipulate “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the DPP authorities’ habitual tactics of manipulating cognitive warfare and creating information cocoons, as well as their malicious intent to intimidate cross-Strait exchanges and interactions and to escalate cross-Strait hostility and confrontation.\nWhat the mainland is like, you may come and see for yourselves. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland in person and see for themselves. Anyone who comes and experiences it will surely be astonished and proud of the mainland’s tremendous development and progress, and the DPP authorities’ rumors will inevitably collapse on their own and be exposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683864.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台“台海之声”、“看台海”和“日月谭天“记者","In the 2025 Spring Festival film season, mainland box office receipts surpassed 10 billion yuan, setting a historical record. The film “Ne Zha 2” achieved both high word-of-mouth and high box office, sparking heated discussion on the island. A Taiwanese media commentator said, “This represents the strengthening of cultural strength and national power,” and “This is a story of the Chinese people themselves,” and a…","I saw data yesterday showing that the box office of 《Ne Zha 2》 has already surpassed 9 billion yuan. As everyone can see, several films released during this year’s Spring Festival drew inspiration from excellent traditional Chinese culture, reflected the profound cultural connotations of the Chinese nation, demonstrated cultural confidence, and sparked a “Chinese style” craze. 《Feng Shen Part Two: The Battle of Xiqi》, 《Detective Chinatown 1900》, and 《The Legend of the Condor Heroes: The Great Hero》 have been released simultaneously in many overseas locations and have drawn enthusiastic responses. 《Ne Zha 2》 will also be officially released in many countries and regions around the world starting tomorrow (February 13).\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots, origins, language, and culture. Chinese culture is the spiritual root and sense of belonging for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The discussion among Taiwan people about films such as 《Ne Zha 2》 fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share a common historical memory and deep emotional resonance with Chinese culture. We hope that the relevant films can be released in Taiwan as soon as possible, so that more Taiwan people can directly experience the charm of Chinese culture and understand the powerful strength and strong momentum of the development of the mainland’s film and cultural industry. We also welcome Taiwan compatriots visiting and exchanging on the mainland to set aside time to watch films on the mainland and check in at film shooting locations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683856.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The DPP authorities recently said that, for information and communication security reasons, government agencies and public schools are fully prohibited from using the AI large model launched by the mainland AI startup DeepSeek. What is your comment?","Since its release, the AI large model of DeepSeek, an artificial intelligence company on the mainland, has quickly topped the mobile app download rankings in more than 100 countries and regions, and is widely welcomed by internet users around the world. We welcome Taiwan's people to use the AI large models launched by mainland companies, and we also actively support cooperation between cross-Strait enterprises in the field of artificial intelligence.\nThe DPP authorities, driven by a “fear of China” and “anti-China” mindset, are both fearful of and resentful toward mainland high-tech products, and readily ban them outright in the name of safety. This will only harm the interests of Taiwan's businesses and people. This absurd approach of using “anti-intellectualism” to oppose “China” has already provoked disgust and opposition from all sectors of the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The Bureau of International Organization Affairs of the U.S. State Department recently posted on the X platform, saying that Taiwan's exclusion from important international forums, including the World Health Assembly, “directly and negatively affects the well-being of the American people and the entire international community,” and that Taiwan should be restored to participate in the World Health Assembly as an…","On the question of the Taiwan region of China participating in World Health Organization activities, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The one-China principle is the fundamental principle for handling Taiwan-related issues, as confirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. This has caused the political basis for the Taiwan region’s participation in the World Health Assembly to cease to exist. This situation was entirely created by the DPP authorities.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. The US side should immediately stop using the World Health Assembly to hype Taiwan-related issues, and should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","US Secretary of State Rubio, while visiting Guatemala, claimed that “the US will do its utmost to help Guatemala develop its relations with Taiwan.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The One-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. It is what the people desire and the trend of the times. Currently, 183 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of adhering to the One-China principle. We hope relevant countries will recognize the trend of the times and stand on the right side of history.\nIt must be emphasized that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We urge the US side to abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and “relying on the US to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","When Lai Ching-te attended the \"2025 Mainland Taiwanese Business Spring Festival Event,\" a Taiwanese businessman confronted him on the spot, telling him \"Don't cause trouble.\" Some public opinion has pointed out that in recent period, the actions of the DPP authorities have left Taiwanese businesses and the public feeling pessimistic and resentful. What is your comment on this?","The Lai Qingde authorities, for their own private interests, have resorted to every means of political manipulation, poisoning the island's political atmosphere and harming the interests of the people. It is only natural that they face opposition from broad sections of Taiwan compatriots. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities' pursuit of “independence” and provocations seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and they do not win popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台国广记者","Reportedly, Mr. Wang Zhiceng, son of former ARATS Chairman Mr. Wang Daohan, traveled to Taiwan yesterday (the 11th) to pay respects to Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun. The DPP authorities imposed many restrictions, requiring Mr. Wang Zhiceng and his delegation not to accept media interviews and not to have any other itineraries, among other things. What is your comment on this?","With the assistance of the Koo Kung-liang Foundation for Culture and Education, Mr. Wang Zhizhong, son of Mr. Wang Daohan, former chairman of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS), led a delegation to Taiwan on February 11 to pay respects to Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun. During the process of handling the relevant procedures, Taiwan's relevant authorities, through the foundation, required Mr. Wang and his delegation not to accept media interviews or arrange other itineraries while in Taiwan. Considering the foundation's situation, Mr. Wang and his delegation went directly to the memorial hall to pay their respects upon arrival in the morning, and hurriedly returned to the mainland in the evening. While being interviewed by mainland media, they expressed their grief for Ms. Gu Yanzhuoyun and their hopes for cross-Strait exchanges. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have imposed arbitrary restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges at every turn, once again fully demonstrating that their so-called \"goodwill\" and \"freedom of speech\" are empty slogans in name only, and exposing their resistance and obstruction toward all cross-Strait exchange activities, including those among the people.\nMs. Gu Yanzhuoyun personally experienced important moments in the history of cross-Strait relations, such as the \"Wang-Koo Talks,\" and made positive contributions to promoting cross-Strait exchanges. Beginning with the \"Wang-Koo Talks,\" the two sides' authorized institutions carried out a series of dialogues and consultations on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus,\" reaching 27 agreements and many common understandings that have brought tangible benefits to the people on both sides of the Strait, especially to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will join us in firmly upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" and on that basis push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, bring well-being to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and work for the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","The Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced before the Spring Festival that it would resume group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, and the cross-Strait tourism industries have actively communicated and coordinated. However, the Mainland Affairs Council recently said that reconnaissance tour groups coming to Taiwan should be discussed by the tourism “small two associations” before…","After the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, a scouting group composed of tourism operators from Fujian and Shanghai quickly submitted a request to Taiwan's relevant authorities to visit Taiwan for inspection. This shows that we have a positive attitude and keep our word in resuming tourism to Taiwan by mainland residents, which has been widely welcomed by Taiwan's tourism industry and public. However, the passive response and disguised obstruction by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have been like pouring a bucket of cold water on their enthusiasm.\nAs is well known, the crux and obstacle of cross-Strait tourism issues lie in the interference and obstruction by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, not in whether the “Small Two Associations” have communicated. Communication between the “Small Two Associations” is not a prerequisite for resuming cross-Strait tourism. In early 2020, after the COVID-19 epidemic broke out, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, disregarding relevant cross-Strait agreements, unilaterally banned mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan in full and also prohibited travel agencies on the island from operating group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents, all without communicating with the mainland side through the “Small Two Associations.” In 2024, mainland residents' travel to Matsu and Kinmen resumed successively, also without communication through the “Small Two Associations.” However, to further resume mainland residents' travel to Taiwan, in November 2024 we considered the request of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan and agreed to its visit to and meeting with the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits. The Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan, however, temporarily cancelled its itinerary on the grounds of insufficient budget. Before the Spring Festival, when the Fujian and Shanghai scouting groups submitted their requests for inspection visits to Taiwan's relevant authorities, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits also simultaneously notified the Beijing office of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan. We do not oppose the “Small Two Associations” contacting and communicating on specific issues in cross-Strait tourism after tourism is resumed, but we oppose using the pretext of “Small Two Associations” communication to actually obstruct mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan.\nDriven by their inherent nature of seeking “independence” and confrontation, and by political self-interest, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have turned a deaf ear to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and the calls of the industry, and have turned a blind eye to the losses suffered by grassroots people and operators in Taiwan. Again and again, on various untenable pretexts, they have obstructed and banned cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields and erected barriers. This does not win popular support. The industry on the island has already expressed extreme disappointment and strong indignation. If they do not change course and continue to act selfishly and stubbornly, they will surely lose even more support and reap the bitter consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Some foreign media reported that the South African government has issued an ultimatum to the Taiwan authorities’ representative office in South Africa, demanding that it move out of Pretoria, the capital of South Africa, by the end of March. What is your comment?","The one-China principle is the basic norm of international relations and the universal consensus of the international community; it is the wish of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 7th that it opposes the DPP authorities using the pretext of “mini Two Associations” communication to actually obstruct mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan. The DPP authorities responded, deliberately stressing that mainland visitors' tourism to Taiwan, such as scouting tour groups from Fujian and Shanghai, should first go through “mini Two…","On February 7, we already stated our position on the relevant issues. I must emphasize again that the crux and obstacle of cross-Strait tourism lies in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities, not in whether the “Little Two Associations” have communicated. Communication between the “Little Two Associations” is not a prerequisite for resuming cross-Strait tourism. We do not oppose the “Little Two Associations” communicating on specific issues in cross-Strait tourism after tourism resumes, but we oppose using the name of communication between the “Little Two Associations” as a pretext to actually obstruct mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan. Since Taiwan’s relevant side claims it is “already prepared,” it should immediately allow mainland pre-tour inspection groups to visit the island for inspection, rather than stalling and making excuses on any pretext.\nAfter the mainland announced before the Spring Festival that it would resume group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, the DPP authorities’ various behaviors have once again shown that they have no sincerity whatsoever in welcoming mainland residents to travel to Taiwan and in resuming cross-Strait tourism exchanges. What they have is political calculation: fabricating excuses to deceive residents and businesses on the island, and trying to shift blame to the mainland and evade responsibility. The eyes of the people on the island and of all sectors are sharp. Who is truly working to resume and expand cross-Strait tourism and other exchanges with the well-being of Taiwan compatriots in mind, and who is ignoring the mainstream public opinion and business interests of the island, blindly pursuing “independence” and confrontation, and irresponsibly obstructing cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, is becoming clearer to everyone. We hope the DPP authorities will change course, stop obstructing and restricting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, show sincerity on the issue of mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, and take pragmatic measures.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683863.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台CGTN记者","After the leaders of the United States and Japan met, they issued a joint statement that mentioned the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and supported Taiwan's meaningful participation in international organizations, and opposed “China's unilateral change of the status quo by force or coercion.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs, and no external interference is tolerated. The so-called joint statement that talks about the Taiwan question and brazenly interferes in China’s internal affairs is something we firmly oppose. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and to stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Japan, as a country bearing historical responsibility on the Taiwan question, should draw lessons from history, be prudent in its words and deeds, abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and handle Taiwan-related matters with caution. We warn the DPP authorities: the scheme to split the country by relying on external forces is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250212_12683860.htm"],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","中央广电总台央广记者","It is reported that during the Spring Festival, many Fujian residents went to Kinmen and Matsu to celebrate the Lunar New Year together with Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the situation of mainland residents traveling to Kinmen and Matsu during this year’s Spring Festival holiday.","According to information, from January 28 to February 7 (from Lunar New Year’s Eve to the tenth day of the Lunar New Year), there were 5,232 individual tourist trips and 30 group tourist trips by Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu. Since the resumption last year of processing travel endorsements for mainland residents to visit Kinmen and Matsu, there have been 61,756 individual tourist trips and 3,289 group tourist trips by Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu. This Spring Festival holiday is the first Spring Festival since the resumption of Fujian residents’ tourism to Kinmen and Matsu, and going to Kinmen and Matsu to celebrate the Lunar New Year with Taiwan compatriots has become a new choice for Fujian residents during the Spring Festival. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait come and go, sharing joy and harmony. This is exactly the scene that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should have when they celebrate the traditional Chinese festival together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The first question: The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that it refused to issue permits for a Shanghai municipal group to visit Taiwan to take part in the “2025 Taipei Lantern Festival” because the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office obstructed Taiwan businesspeople from returning to Taiwan to take part in SEF activities. What is your comment? The MAC also said that, due to pressure from Taiwan…","First question. The so-called remarks by the Mainland Affairs Council are completely a reversal of right and wrong and a confusion of public perception. The DPP authorities violate the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, arbitrarily obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait civil exchange activities that have been held for many years, such as the Shanghai-Taipei Lantern Festival exchange, and their reasons are extremely absurd.\nIn fact, the DPP authorities label Taiwan businesses on the mainland as “national security threats,” and frequently use the so-called “anti-infiltration law” to suppress and persecute Taiwan businesses, obstructing Taiwan businesses from investing and developing on the mainland and harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan businesses. This approach, which ignores the will of the people and goes against the trend, has already been rejected by Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses. We advise the DPP authorities to immediately stop their malicious smears and blame-shifting, and to truly do some practical things for the public.\nSecond question. The mainland has consistently upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and actively promotes personnel exchanges across the Strait and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including tourism. In 2023 we announced the resumption of receiving group tours from Taiwan residents to the mainland, and Taiwan residents may travel freely to the mainland. In 2024 we made arrangements for mainland residents to travel to Matsu and Kinmen and for group tours to the island, and this January we announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai. We continue to make active efforts and create conditions for normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait.\nIn contrast, the DPP authorities have repeatedly obstructed, restricted and erected barriers to cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields. This includes implementing so-called “case-by-case approval” for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for exchanges, rejecting the application by the island's tourism industry for charter boats from Pingtan to Taiwan, refusing to respond to appeals to fully restore cross-Strait passenger direct flight routes and destinations, refusing to lift the “group tour ban” and so-called “orange” alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland, and now using “mini two-association” communication as a pretext to obstruct group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai. Under these circumstances, it is difficult for mainland residents to feel the goodwill of the DPP authorities.\nIt must be pointed out again that, out of its inherent nature of seeking “independence” in opposition and its political self-interest, the DPP authorities turn a deaf ear to the mainstream opinion in Taiwan and the voices of the industry, and turn a blind eye to the damage to the interests of grassroots people and the industry in Taiwan. Repeatedly using various untenable reasons to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields is not popular. If they do not change course and persist in acting selfishly, they will lose even more popular support.\nThird question. You may have a misunderstanding about the “Olympic model.” The “Olympic model” is the basic norm for handling Taiwan-related issues in the field of sports, and does not involve news media or other fields, or areas outside the events themselves. Including the Harbin Asian Winter Games, the relevant venues and documents for international sports events held on the mainland all followed the “Olympic model.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","The 2025 Spring Festival Gala of China Media Group has drawn wide attention. Unlike previous years, performers from Hong Kong, Taiwan, and Macau on this year's program list are no longer labeled “China Hong Kong,” “China Taiwan,” or “China Macau.” What does this move mean? Will it be handled this way from now on?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and compatriots in Hong Kong and Macao all belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. During the Spring Festival, the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, performing artists from both sides of the Strait and from Hong Kong and Macao gather together without distinction and take part in various Spring Festival gala activities. This accords with and embodies the national sentiment of family and national reunion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question: The Taiwan side has repeatedly mentioned that free independent travel by mainland tourists to Taiwan has still not resumed, that currently only Fujian residents are permitted to travel to Kinmen and Matsu, and that last year the number of Taiwan residents going to the mainland was severely out of balance with the number of mainland residents coming to Taiwan. What is your response? Will you…","The first question: After we announced the resumption of group tourism to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, residents of both places very much hope to visit Taiwan. But the reality is that the DPP authorities have repeatedly obstructed, restricted, and erected barriers to cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields. This includes implementing so-called “case-by-case approval” for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for exchanges, rejecting applications from Taiwan’s tourism industry for chartered boats from Pingtan to Taiwan, refusing to respond to calls for the full restoration of cross-Strait passenger direct flights and routes, refusing to lift the “group tour ban” and the so-called “orange” alert for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland, and now obstructing group tours to Taiwan by residents of Fujian and Shanghai on the pretext of “mini two-association” communication. Under these circumstances, the so-called “serious imbalance” between the figures for Taiwan residents coming to the mainland and mainland residents going to Taiwan is entirely the responsibility of the DPP authorities. Under these circumstances, it is hard to even talk about promoting more mainland residents from more provinces and cities traveling to Taiwan for tourism.\nThe second question: The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation for Education and Culture organized a youth student delegation to Beijing to take part in the “Double Olympic City, Youth Appointment” series of activities for the Taiwan Youth Beijing Winter Season. We have consistently supported and actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, especially exchanges between young people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-12","Zhu Fenglian","日本共同社记者","From February 10 to 12, US warships transited the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","The PLA Eastern Theater Command has already stated its position on this. The Taiwan question concerns China’s core interests. We firmly oppose, and will never allow, any external interference, and we have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related matters prudently and properly, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.\nToday’s press conference is concluded here. Happy Lantern Festival to everyone, may you eat tangyuan, reunite with family, and may happiness fill your homes. (Min Nan) On the Lantern Festival night of the fifteenth day of the first lunar month, every household celebrates reunion. (Hakka) A round full moon, a feeling of togetherness; one bowl of tangyuan, one family united. Wishing Taiwan compatriots a joyful reunion on the Lantern Festival!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250212_12683854.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-02-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, after the recent meeting between the leaders of the United States and Japan, the two countries issued a joint statement emphasizing the importance of maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and opposing any unilateral change to the situation in the Taiwan Strait by force or coercion. Recently, the US destroyer Johnson and the ocean survey ship Bowditch transited the Taiwan…","The relevant content of the joint statement by the United States and Japan crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs and makes groundless smears and accusations against China. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposes this. Regarding the passage of U.S. vessels through the Taiwan Strait, the Eastern Theater Command has already responded.\nIt must be emphasized that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. No military provocation by the U.S. military can change this fact. On the contrary, such provocations can only repeatedly expose the consistent hypocrisy and double standards of the United States before the international community, and can only repeatedly stimulate the determination and will of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland. The Chinese People’s Liberation Army will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness, firmly carry out struggles against separatism and foreign interference, and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16369676.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-02-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On February 13, a gas explosion occurred at the Shin Kong Mitsukoshi department store in Taichung City, causing multiple casualties. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 14th that we are heartbroken over the occurrence of such an accident, we mourn the compatriots who unfortunately died, and we express our sincere condolences to the families of the deceased and to the injured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250214_12684246.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-02-17","Guo Jiakun","Yonhap News Agency","Foreign Ministers of the ROK, the U.S. and Japan held talks on February 15 in Munich, Germany. The three countries said for the first time in their joint statement that they support “Taiwan’s meaningful participation in appropriate international organizations,” strongly oppose “any unilateral attempts to change the status quo by force or coercion in the waters of the Indo-Pacific, including the South China Sea,”…","We firmly oppose relevant countries’ attempts to put together small circles to interfere in China’s internal affairs, attack and smear China, and stoke confrontation and antagonism. We’ve lodged serious protests with relevant countries.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China, which brooks no external interference. The key to upholding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait lies in abiding by the one-China principle, and firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism. The Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations must and can only be handled in line with the one-China principle.\nLet me stress that the Asia-Pacific is a stellar example of peace and development, not a chessboard for major-power rivalry. We call on relevant parties to earnestly respect regional countries’ effort for peace and stability, abandon the Cold War mentality, stop creating bloc confrontation and stop fueling tensions in the region. China will firmly safeguard territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and meanwhile, stays committed to properly handling differences through dialogue and consultation with countries concerned.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250217_11556446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250217_11556426.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-17","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Earlier this week, the U.S. State Department removed the words “we do not support Taiwanese independence” from a fact sheet on Taiwan relations on its website. Have you discussed this with the U.S. and do you have any comment now?","There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. It is a prevailing international consensus and basic norm governing international relations, and also a solemn commitment the U.S. has made in the three China-U.S. joint communiqués.\nHistory cannot be tampered with, facts cannot be denied, and truth cannot be distorted. U.S. State Department updated its fact sheet on relations with Taiwan and gravely backpedaled on its position on Taiwan-related issues. This move severely violates the one-China principle and three China-U.S. joint communiqués, goes against international law and basic norms of international relations, and sends a seriously wrong signal to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.” This is another example of the U.S. clinging to its wrong policy of “using Taiwan to contain China.”\nWe urge the U.S. to immediately correct its wrongdoings, abide by the one-China principle and three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence, stop using Taiwan to contain China, stop upgrading its substantive relations with Taiwan, stop helping Taiwan expand so-called “international space,” stop emboldening and supporting “Taiwan independence,” and avoid further severe damage to China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250217_11556446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250217_11556426.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-17","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The Japanese Ministry of Justice says that it’s going to revise its family law rules to allow Taiwan, Palestine and other non-national state regions or districts to be listed as a place of origin for people from those places. So currently, someone from Taiwan is listed as coming from China. In the future, they’ll be able to be listed as coming from Taiwan. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and compatriots from both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same Chinese nation. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference. Japan committed aggression against Taiwan and exercised colonial rule over the island. It bears serious historical responsibilities to the Chinese people, and should act all the more prudently on the Taiwan question. We urge the Japanese side to abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan. No gimmicks on the Taiwan question, and do not send any conflicting or wrong signals.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250217_11556446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250217_11556426.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-17","Guo Jiakun","Follow-up","So in your criticism now, are you saying that the change on the family law rules in Japan violates the founding documents of Japan-China relations and violates Chinese sovereignty?","Adherence to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan is a solemn political commitment Japan has made to China. Let me stress again that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no foreign interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250217_11556446.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250217_11556426.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-02-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 17 — The US State Department website recently revised its content on ‘US-Taiwan relations’ and deleted the expression ‘does not support “Taiwan independence”’. The DPP authorities expressed their thanks. In response, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered questions on the 17th, saying: We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, correct its mistakes, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and stop sending any wrong signals that condone or support the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces.\nShe pointed out that Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The relevant move is a serious regression in the US position on the Taiwan question. It seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs, sends serious erroneous signals to the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces, and will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nZhu Fenglian said: We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that ‘relying on the US to seek independence’ is a dead end. No matter how Taiwan and the US collude and stir things up, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the trend that China will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250217_12684675.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-02-19","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The FT reported earlier today that three Chinese warships are sailing about 150 miles off the east coast of Australia and that puts them within the Australian exclusive economic zone (EEZ). Last year, when an Australian warship sailed through China’s EEZ and the Taiwan Strait, China called that a violation of Chinese sovereignty. Do you see the Chinese ships being within the same area that the Australian ship was…","I’m not familiar with what you mentioned. I’d refer you to the competent Chinese authorities for relevant question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250219_11558920.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250219_11558915.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-25","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan’s coast guard has said that it has detained a Chinese ship registered in Togo after underseas telecom cable was severed. Could you confirm that? And did the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","I’m not familiar with what you mentioned, and this is not a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250225_11561975.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250225_11561939.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-26","Lin Jian","Reuters","The Taiwan authorities say that China ’ s mainland has set up a drill zone for “shooting training” without prior notice around 40 nautical miles off the island’s southwest coast. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","This is not a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250226_11562770.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250226_11562688.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-26","Lin Jian","Beijing Youth Daily","It’s reported that the Trump administration has released US$5.3 billion in previously frozen foreign aid, including US$870 million designated for military assistance to Taiwan. What’s China’s comment?","We are deeply concerned over relevant reports. China has all along opposed U.S. military assistance to China’s Taiwan region, which has severely violated the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, undermined China’s sovereignty and security interests, and sent a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the U.S. to stop arming Taiwan and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China will closely follow the situation and firmly defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250226_11562770.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250226_11562688.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-02-26","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s coast guard said it detained a cargo ship crewed by eight Chinese nationals yesterday after a subsea telecom cable was severed off the island. Can the Foreign Ministry confirm this and give any more details?","I answered this question yesterday. This is neither a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250226_11562770.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250226_11562688.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Now please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, General Secretary Xi Jinping attended a symposium on private enterprises and delivered an important speech, stressing that the development prospects of the private economy in the new era and on the new journey are broad and full of potential, and that now is the right time for private enterprises and private entrepreneurs to show their talents. Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-invested…","On February 17, General Secretary Xi Jinping attended a symposium with private entrepreneurs in Beijing and delivered an important speech. He fully affirmed the major achievements made in the development of the private economy and its important contributions to national economic and social development, and made comprehensive arrangements for promoting the healthy and high-quality development of the private economy in the current and coming period. The speech was lofty in vision, profound in thought, and rich in meaning. It deeply reflected concern for and attention to private enterprises and the private economy, sent important signals for promoting the healthy and high-quality development of the private economy, and further demonstrated the firm determination and clear stance of consistently supporting the development and growth of the private economy.\nWe resolutely implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech. We actively improve the institutions and policies for promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, continuously implement and refine policy measures that benefit the well-being of compatriots on both sides, steadily strengthen policy provision for deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and genuinely work for the benefit and welfare of compatriots on both sides. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises will remain confident, enterprising, and adaptable to change, adapt to the new requirements of high-quality development on the mainland, seize the new opportunities of developing new quality productive forces on the mainland, and actively take part in the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, jointly strengthening the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686456.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The two sessions of the National People’s Congress and the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference are about to convene. We note that more and more Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, are paying attention to the two sessions and to the development of whole-process people’s democracy on the mainland. What is your comment?","The National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference are important platforms that intensively reflect and deeply practice whole-process people's democracy. They are also important windows through which Taiwan compatriots can understand the socialist system with Chinese characteristics.\nDeveloping whole-process people's democracy is one of the essential requirements of Chinese-style modernization. Whole-process people's democracy is democracy along the entire chain, in all directions and covering everything. It not only has complete institutional procedures, but also complete practice of participation. In the practice of whole-process people's democracy, all the people exercise democratic election, democratic consultation, democratic decision-making, democratic management and democratic supervision in accordance with the law. They manage state affairs in accordance with the law through various channels and forms. It is the broadest, most genuine and most effective socialist democracy.\nOpinions and suggestions submitted by NPC deputies and CPPCC members during the National Two Sessions that are conducive to promoting national reunification are all earnestly heard and studied by us. In recent years, more and more Taiwan compatriots have also been paying attention to and learning about the Two Sessions, and have actively offered suggestions for developing cross-Strait relations through many channels. We will create more conditions and provide more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to observe, experience and take part in whole-process people's democracy. We will fully listen to everyone's opinions and suggestions, improve systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, firmly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and, together with broad Taiwan compatriots, advance national reunification and seek national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686455.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","光明日报记者","Exchanges are an important way to enhance mutual understanding and friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. What cross-Strait exchange activities in various localities recently deserve special attention?","Entering March, relevant departments and local governments will hold cross-Strait exchange activities with rich content and diverse forms. Here is a brief preview for everyone.\nIn cultural exchange, the first Cross-Strait Folk Culture, Sports, and Arts Fair will open in Shanwei City, Guangdong Province. The event has eight sections, including “Fine Moon over Qinghu Lake, Shared Round Across the Strait” and “Folk Origins Run Far, Cross-Strait Families Are One,” covering temple fair and garden tours, intangible cultural heritage performances, poetry recitation, and folk custom exploration. The ancestor-worship ceremony at the Hometown of the Yellow Emperor in the Year of the Snake will be held in Zhengzhou, Henan. Through online and offline activities, compatriots on both sides of the Strait will jointly commemorate their ancestors, pass on culture, and feel that both sides share the same roots, the same language, and the same ethnicity. The 2025 Cross-Strait Confucian Culture Spring Assembly will be held in Qufu, Shandong, including activities such as young people from both sides jointly offering sacrifices to Confucius, the “Approaching Confucius” Taiwan Youth Study Tour Confucian Learning Experience Camp, and the Cross-Strait Analects Reading and Writing Relay Competition. Compatriots from both sides will recite the Analects together and pass on the classics. The “Come to Hubei for the Cherry Blossoms” spring cherry-blossom viewing event for Taiwan compatriots will be held in Hubei, allowing compatriots from both sides to deeply experience the cultural richness of Jingchu during the season when cherry blossoms are in full bloom.\nIn youth exchange, a series of “Youth Soars, Taiwan Youth Month in Guangzhou” activities will be launched in Guangzhou. Under the theme “Youth Soars, Realizing Dreams in the City of Rams,” the events include a launch ceremony and five sub-activities: the “Invitation to the City of Rams” job fair for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, the 2nd Guangzhou Taiwan Youth Speaker Competition, and the Taiwan youth volunteer activities for the 15th National Games. These will provide support for the growth and development of Taiwanese youth and for Taiwanese youth entrepreneurship projects settling in Guangzhou, helping Taiwanese youth pursue, build, and realize their dreams in Guangzhou.\nIn ethnic minority exchange, the 2025 “One Family of China: Guangxi and Taiwan Ethnic Groups Celebrate the Guangxi March Third Festival” activity will be held in Guangxi. Taiwanese ethnic minority compatriots will meet with the various ethnic groups of Guangxi for the tenth time in Guangxi, carrying out a series of friendship and visiting exchange activities, celebrating ethnic festivals together, and sharing the bonds of kinship between compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 2025 joint enrollment of Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan students at mainland universities has recently officially launched. Please introduce the relevant situation.","After years of development, the achievements of mainland higher education are plain to see, and the quality of talent cultivation continues to improve. We have consistently supported and warmly welcomed more Taiwan youth with aspirations to apply to mainland universities, and we will also create better conditions for Taiwan students to grow and succeed on the mainland and to realize their life ideals.\nCurrently, Taiwan students who hold a Taiwan Compatriot Permit for Travel to the Mainland or a Taiwan Residence Permit, along with a valid identity document proving residence in Taiwan, and who possess the corresponding prerequisite academic qualifications, may apply to undergraduate or graduate programs at mainland universities through multiple pathways.\nThere are four pathways for applying to undergraduate programs at mainland universities: First, by taking the Joint Admission Examination for Overseas Chinese, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Students (referred to as the “National Joint Admission Examination”), and registering online via the “Candidate Terminal of the National Joint Admission Management System” from March 1 to 15. Second, by applying based on Taiwan's General Scholastic Ability Test (GSAT) results (referred to as “GSAT Admission”), and registering online from March 1 to 31 through the system for “Mainland China's General Higher Education Institutions' Admission of Taiwan High School Graduates Based on Taiwan's GSAT Results.” Third, by taking the joint admission examination of Jinan University and Huaqiao University. Fourth, by applying to some Fujian universities based on Taiwan's Comprehensive Assessment and subject placement test results and by taking the independent admission examinations for Taiwan region, among other methods. For details, please follow the official websites of each university.\nFor applying to graduate programs at mainland universities, candidates may take the Graduate Examination for Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Regions (referred to as the “HMT Graduate Examination”). Registration for the 2025 HMT Graduate Examination is expected to begin in early March. Candidates are requested to pay close attention and register online through the “Mainland (Chinese Mainland) Higher Education Institutions Enrollment Information Network for Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan” by logging in with their “Chsi” (学信网) account.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686448.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the head of Taiwan's education authority said that, to “protect young people from being targeted by the united front,” the island has comprehensively banned public and private universities on the island from exchanges and cooperation with mainland universities such as Jinan University and Huaqiao University, and prohibited senior high and vocational schools from encouraging or assisting students in…","As I have just introduced, students in Taiwan may take the joint enrollment examination of Jinan University and Huaqiao University to study at these two universities. Jinan University and Huaqiao University are well-known universities on the mainland, whose academic standards and social reputation are renowned at home and abroad. Jinan University’s predecessor, Jinan Academy, was established as early as 1906. Over the years, the two universities have trained many outstanding students, including students from Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan, and overseas Chinese, making important contributions to strengthening ties between the mainland and Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. The claim by relevant figures in the DPP authorities that so-called “protecting young people from united front work” is sheer nonsense and utterly absurd.\nIn recent years, the DPP authorities have turned pale at the mere mention of “united front” and oppose anything related to China as a matter of course. Their wicked deeds are too numerous to count. Recently, they have become even more creative and increasingly extreme, even banning normal exchanges and cooperation between cross-strait universities and the normal study and enrollment of Taiwan students. Under the pretext of guarding against “united front” work, they are in fact interfering with and obstructing cross-strait educational exchanges. They have reached a point with no bottom line and no limits, and will surely meet strong opposition from universities and secondary schools on the island, as well as from young students and their parents.\nIt must be pointed out that the united front is about uniting hearts, consensus, wisdom, and strength; it seeks consistency amid respect for diversity, finds the greatest common denominator, and draws the largest circle of common ground. United front work is bright and legitimate. The DPP authorities routinely smear united front work, which fully exposes their inner panic. They are trying by any means to control the thinking of Taiwan’s people, to deprive them of their right to choose higher education, and to serve their separatist schemes for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686451.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Reports say that from May, Japan's Ministry of Justice will allow Taiwanese residing in Japan to change the “China” listed as their registered place of origin to “Taiwan.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The relevant Japanese actions attempt to create “two Chinas” and “one China, one Taiwan.” They seriously violate the one-China principle and seriously interfere in China's internal affairs, and we firmly oppose them. Japan, as a country bearing historical responsibility on the Taiwan question, should learn from history, be cautious in its words and deeds, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that misjudging the situation and “relying on external forces to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that he hopes to negotiate with the mainland side on mainland students coming to Taiwan but has not received a response. The mainland, on the one hand, restricts mainland students from coming to Taiwan, while on the other hand actively courts Taiwan students to study on the mainland. The mainland should not treat academic exchanges…","We respond to this question with three points. First, the mainland has always been the promoter of exchanges and interactions between all sectors on both sides of the Strait, while the DPP has consistently been the obstacle and saboteur. The DPP authorities' statements distort the facts and reverse right and wrong.\nSecond, the DPP authorities persistently manipulate the \"anti-China, resist-China\" narrative, relentlessly exaggerate the \"threat\" from the mainland, treat normal cross-Strait exchanges as floods and wild beasts, and smear exchanges between students and young people across the Strait as \"united front conspiracies.\" Their purpose is to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, escalate hostility and confrontation across the Strait, and create information cocoons and poison public sentiment in pursuit of \"independence.\" This reactionary conduct is firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThird, as long as the DPP authorities maintain their mindset of opposition and confrontation, cross-Strait relations cannot improve. If they sincerely hope that mainland students will resume studying in Taiwan, they should remove as soon as possible the various obstacles they have placed on cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, rather than trying every trick to create the illusion that cross-Strait dialogue and consultation are possible without acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686453.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Relevant Taiwan authorities said that the Togo-flagged cargo ship “Hong Tai,” which has mainland ties, was involved in dragging and damaging the No. 3 Taiwan-Penghu submarine cable, and stopped the vessel as a so-called “caught in the act.” What is your comment?","Around one hundred undersea cable damage incidents occur globally each year, and they are common maritime accidents. The DPP authorities, before the basic facts and responsibility for the accident have been clarified, deliberately exaggerated the matter and attempted political manipulation, which does not win public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Taiwan media reported that the island civic group “Taiwan FactCheck Center” recently acknowledged that it has received funding from Soros's “Open Society Foundations.” Some public opinion on the island has disclosed that the US Agency for International Development and other departments have, openly or covertly, supported and tolerated multiple civic groups on the island, which for years have cooperated with the…","These developments have let the world see the true face of certain so-called “foundations” and think tanks in the US, which are accustomed to inciting “color revolutions” around the world and stirring up chaos. They also prove that the so-called international “support for Taiwan” that the DPP authorities keep talking about is, in fact, an illusion bought with money and manufactured by themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, said in a recent interview that because more and more Taiwanese people are applying in the mainland for residence permits, settlement permits, and identity cards, the Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area will be amended to bring related matters under regulation, and Taiwanese people are reminded of…","The DPP authorities deliberately confuse the concepts of various documents such as Taiwan compatriot certificates and residence permits, and suppress the relevant personnel, with the aim of threatening and intimidating Taiwan residents and disrupting and undermining exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait. Now they are using this as a pretext, claiming that they will revise the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area.” Their intentions are sinister and their impact is bad. This is a serious challenge to cross-strait relations, and if they obstinately persist, they will surely reap the bitter fruit of their own actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686454.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","On cross-Strait tourism, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council, recently reiterated that tourism should first be discussed through the mini cross-Strait two-agency channel. He claimed that the past was the “Tourism 1.0 era,” and that operators on the island complain they earned only “fatigue” and “garbage,” so a high-quality “Tourism 2.0 era” must be built. What comment do you have?","So-called “Tourism 1.0” and “Tourism 2.0” are merely excuses and tricks the DPP authorities have devised to interfere with and obstruct mainland residents traveling to Taiwan. They first made communication between the two tourism associations (the “small two associations”) a precondition, and now they are trying to deny the major achievements of cross-Strait tourism exchange and cooperation since 2008 and the enormous benefits these brought to Taiwan residents and businesses. This completely disregards the facts and reverses right and wrong. Relevant Taiwan authorities once estimated that from July 2008 to the end of June 2012, the cumulative number of mainland visitors to Taiwan exceeded 3.98 million person-trips, bringing more than NT$202.3 billion in revenue to Taiwan's economy. Are these real and solid returns “garbage”?\nThe crux and obstacle of cross-Strait tourism issues is the interference and obstruction by the DPP authorities. The root cause is that, in pursuit of “independence,” they deliberately interfere with and undermine personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait. Their so-called “welcoming mainland visitors to Taiwan” is merely a deceptive pretext, and the “small two associations” communication they propose is merely a shield. The more the DPP authorities obstruct in every way, the less popular they become.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686450.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》提问","Recently, Lai Ching-te said, “To prevent the CCP’s united front work, we will continue to push for ‘national security legal reform.’” The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that it will conduct a comprehensive review and is studying the various issues. What is the response?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and no one can sever our bonds of blood and kinship, nor can anyone block the historical trend of the reunification of the motherland. Out of its nature of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities disregard the mainstream public opinion on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. They keep manipulating judicial and administrative means to create “green terror,” obstruct cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, escalate hostile confrontation, and undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. This conduct, which turns back the wheel of history and goes against the historical trend, will surely be opposed and reviled by the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","US President Trump recently again singled out “Taiwan stealing America's chip business,” warning that if Taiwan cannot move its chip industry to the US, “we will be very unhappy.” In addition, US media reported that the US government is pushing a plan for TSMC and Intel to form a “joint venture,” and island concerns that TSMC will become “American TSMC” continue to grow. What comments does the Chinese side have…","Recent Taiwan public opinion shows that concern and doubt among all sectors on the island about TSMC becoming “AmeriTSMC” are rapidly increasing. In pursuit of private gain, the DPP authorities give in to every demand of external forces. They use Taiwan’s semiconductor industry and strong enterprises as a stepping stone for “relying on external forces to seek independence,” and even hand them over as a “souvenir gift,” repeatedly selling out the interests and well-being of Taiwan residents and enterprises. This conduct, which treats “selling out Taiwan” not as shameful but as an honor to curry favor with the U.S., is opposed by more and more Taiwan residents and enterprises.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","福建海峡卫视记者","The US State Department website recently revised its content on “US-Taiwan Relations,” deleting the expression “does not support Taiwan independence.” What comments does the spokesperson have?","Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. The relevant move is a serious regression in the position of the United States on the Taiwan question. It seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, sends a serious and wrong signal to 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces, and will only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, correct its mistakes, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and stop sending any wrong signals that condone or support 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces.\nWe warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the United States to seek independence” is a dead end. No matter how Taiwan and the United States collude and make trouble, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the trend that China will and must be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","It is reported that U.S. Secretary of State Rubio, when interviewed on whether the United States would defend Taiwan if the mainland took action against Taiwan, responded that the U.S. opposes any form of coercion or forcible change to the status quo, and said it will not give up supporting Taiwan’s participation in international forums. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. There is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and are not to be divided. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” position and persistently collude with external forces in provocations to seek “independence,” pushing Taiwan step by step toward a dangerous situation of ominous and perilous war. This is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, recognize the extreme danger of “Taiwan independence,” and stop sending any wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686446.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently met with Matt Pottinger, former US Deputy Assistant to the President for National Security Affairs, and said he hopes to work with the United States to build a so-called “non-red supply chain” and “ensure that Taiwan, the United States and global democratic partners continue to maintain technological advantages.” What comment do you have?","We firmly oppose the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' conduct of “selling out Taiwan to flatter the United States” and “relying on foreign powers to seek independence.”\nThe economies on both sides of the Strait each have their own strengths in capital, markets, technology and talent, and the industrial and supply chains across the Strait are closely linked. Promoting cross-Strait industrial cooperation is conducive to the development of enterprises on both sides and to enhancing the livelihood and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Lai Ching-te violates the laws of the market economy and blindly follows the United States in pursuing “decoupling and severing supply chains.” He claims to want Taiwan to retain its technological advantages, but in substance he curries favor with the United States by selling off Taiwan's advantageous industries, sacrificing Taiwan's development prospects, and smashing the “rice bowls” of Taiwan's people. The United States has always pursued “America First.” When Taiwan's value has been squeezed dry, the outcome will be a change from “chess piece” to “discarded piece,” and enterprises and the public on the island are seeing this more and more clearly. Under these circumstances, Lai Ching-te is still repeating the clichéd rhetoric of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” and, under the banner of “democracy,” begging for mercy and selling himself out to others. It is truly laughable and pitiful!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686445.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed that this year he will give priority to pushing for a special budget to bring the island’s defense budget above 3% of GDP. What comments do you have?","The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” attempt to “seek independence by force” and “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” blindly obey external forces, and do not hesitate to squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwan people on so-called “protection fees.” It must be pointed out that currying favor with foreigners and selling out Taiwan is like asking ghosts to fill a prescription. It will only tie the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to the chariot of “Taiwan independence” and push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Taiwan is Taiwan of China. No one and no force may attempt to split Taiwan from China. The more than 1.4 billion Chinese people will never accept it, and the valiant and skilled People’s Liberation Army of China will never accept it. Whether it is 3% or 10%, it will not only fail to protect Taiwan but will instead turn Taiwan into a “powder keg.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250226_12686444.htm"],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","It is reported that the “Halifax Taipei Forum” was recently held in Taipei, and Lai Ching-te took the opportunity to tout Taiwan’s so-called “democratic achievements” and spread “Taiwan independence” fallacies. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The Halifax Forum is accustomed to hyping China-related issues and stubbornly adheres to an anti-China stance. The DPP authorities and their affiliates spent money to invite it to hold events in Taiwan, staging a duet of anti-China activity and “independence” plotting. Lai Ching-te took the opportunity to spread “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies and peddle the false narrative of “democracy against authoritarianism,” once again exposing the “Taiwan independence” nature and sinister intent to inflame hostility across the Taiwan Strait and to “rely on outsiders to seek independence.”\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end. No matter how the DPP authorities try to win over external forces to embolden themselves, or how they hide behind the banner of “democracy” to pursue division, they cannot change the objective fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, nor can they change the broad consensus and stable pattern of the international community in upholding the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","It is reported that the DPP authorities are considering procuring US$7 billion to US$10 billion worth of arms from the United States, hoping to win the support of the Trump administration with this. What is your comment?","Spending money to curry favor is a habitual trick of the DPP authorities, including donating money to some US think tanks in exchange for so-called “pro-Taiwan” research reports and inviting anti-China politicians to visit Taiwan. Now they are also willing to spend billions of NT dollars to make a “pledge of allegiance” to the United States, turning Taiwan into a “powder keg.” Fat is for American arms dealers; suffering is for Taiwan's ordinary people; harm is to Taiwan's peace. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “protection money” cannot protect “Taiwan independence,” and “chess pieces” will ultimately become “discarded pieces.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairman of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently again smeared the judicial documents punishing “Taiwan independence,” falsely claiming that the mainland “arbitrarily restricts the personal freedom of Taiwan residents,” and hyped up personal safety risks of traveling to the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","We have emphasized many times the judicial document on punishing diehard “Taiwan independence” elements. This judicial document targets only a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements who have committed egregious pro-independence acts and engaged in rampant secessionist activities, and it does not involve the broad mass of Taiwan people.\nWe always welcome the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots to take part extensively in exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides, create convenient conditions and provide high-quality services for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland, and protect the personal safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. At the same time, we handle all kinds of illegal acts in accordance with law and regulation. We will continue to improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and promote the normalization and routinization of exchanges across all fields between the two sides, which helps compatriots on both sides continuously deepen mutual understanding and friendship. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to look around, visit, and exchange, so that their own firsthand experiences will prove the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' rumors baseless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Lai Ching-te said that in a rapidly changing international situation, “Taiwan is a player, not a pawn, and Taiwan will certainly find a way to win amid change.” What is your comment?","This claim is self-deceiving and laughable. The DPP authorities depend on others for survival and are at the mercy of others. What grounds do they have to call themselves “players of chess”? If the DPP authorities continue to serve as “pawns” for external forces, the only outcome will be becoming “discarded pieces.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The film “Ne Zha 2” has recently been released in full across Hong Kong and Macau and has been enthusiastically welcomed. Netizens on the island have called out to the DPP authorities, hoping they will break through quota restrictions so that the film can “land in Taiwan” as soon as possible. What is your comment?","Taiwan residents want to see “Ne Zha 2” in Taiwan, just as naturally as they love the electronic-music “Third Prince.” Since its release, this film has won broad public recognition for its innovative interpretation of China’s outstanding traditional culture, its gripping storyline, and its stunning animation. Good films naturally attract audiences, and many Taiwan compatriots have already watched this film on the mainland. Nearly 400,000 Taiwan netizen comments call for it to be shown in Taiwan as soon as possible. We hope the relevant authorities in Taiwan will listen to the voice of the public, allow more excellent mainland films into Taiwan’s cinemas, and let Taiwan compatriots enjoy more outstanding cultural products.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Regarding the Taiwan authorities’ accusation that the cargo ship “Hong Tai” was involved in dragging anchor and cutting the No. 3 submarine cable between Taiwan and Penghu, does the TAO have more detailed information? Second question: The “indecent photo” controversy involving Cao Xingcheng and the extramarital affair of DPP legislator Zhao Tianlin both involve people from the mainland. Some…","On the first question, we are verifying the relevant situation. The DPP authorities, before the basic facts and responsibility for the accident have been clarified, have deliberately sensationalized the matter, attempting political manipulation, which is unpopular.\nOn the second question, some people are morally corrupt and act recklessly. Rather than apologizing and reflecting on their conduct, they try to fabricate things out of nothing to divert attention. This is truly shameless and outrageous!\nOn the third question, espionage is a criminal act that endangers national security. The relevant authorities are cracking down on it in accordance with the law in order to safeguard national security and maintain normal order in cross-Strait exchanges. It has nothing to do with whether cross-Strait relations are regressing.\nOn the fourth question, the crux and obstacle of the cross-Strait tourism issue is the DPP authorities' interference and obstruction. The fundamental reason is that, in pursuit of “independence,” they deliberately interfere with and undermine cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields. Their so-called “welcome to mainland tourists to Taiwan” is merely a deceptive pretext, and their claim to communicate through the “small two associations” is just a shield.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","川报封面新闻记者","Recently, several Taiwan entertainers, including Taiwan entertainer Wang Dalu, who are active in cross-Strait development, may face criminal liability for suspected evasion of military service on the island. What comments do you have?","We do not comment on individual cases. What deserves reflection is that the DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and constantly “pursue independence by force,” purchase large quantities of so-called advanced weapons, incite cross-strait confrontation, and attempt to turn Taiwan into a “powder keg” and Taiwan’s people into cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence.” This will inevitably meet with opposition from the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Regarding the fact that the director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office was denied entry to Taiwan while the director of the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office was approved, the Mainland Affairs Council explained that the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office refused the MAC's invitation to meet, whereas the Hubei Taiwan Affairs Office agreed to meet with MAC officials; it also said that when…","First question. The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the head of the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office agreed to meet with it, which is not true. Whether it was the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office or the Hubei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, both visited Taiwan during the Spring Festival, bringing the warm wishes of local compatriots to Taiwan compatriots, celebrating the holiday together and welcoming the New Year together. The DPP authorities insist on politically manipulating such exchange activities that have been carried out for years, which is both laughable and detestable.\nAs for the personal safety of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland, we have always adhered to the concept of “Both sides of the Strait are one family,” and attach great importance to protecting the personal safety and lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. Wherever Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland and whatever difficulties they encounter, we will provide timely assistance.\nSecond question. This is yet another crude trick by the DPP authorities to incite “green terror” through their proxy forces, and the criticism from public opinion on the island has hit the nail on the head.\nLast year, young people from the island came to the mainland for exchanges, interacting warmly with mainland students, and the atmosphere was harmonious and joyful. Teachers and students from mainland universities who visited Taiwan were also warmly welcomed by all sectors of the island. Young people from both sides have come and gone, learning from and drawing on each other, which is welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities are afraid of young people across the Strait getting closer to each other, afraid that the lies they have fabricated will be exposed, and afraid that their “anti-China card” will lose its effect. They have extended the claws of political manipulation into campuses, and by changing tactics they have suppressed and persecuted teachers and students who support cross-Strait exchanges, in an attempt to create a “chilling effect,” incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and obstruct cross-Strait youth exchange and cooperation. Their intentions are sinister, with no bottom line and no limit. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that strengthening exchanges and interactions between young people across the Strait is the common wish of compatriots on both sides, and that acting against this trend will certainly meet strong opposition from young people across the island.\nThird question. In pursuit of advocating “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have vigorously carried out “de-Sinicization” and smeared the mainland, causing confusion in the historical memory and distortion of national identity among Taiwan’s young generation. Some young people in Taiwan have never even heard of the words “descendants of Yan and Huang” (炎黄子孙) and do not know what they mean. People from all walks of life and public opinion on the island have raised questions and objections to this, and strongly hope the situation will change.\nIt must be pointed out that compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. No act of “de-Sinicization” can sever the historical ties across the Strait or the blood connection between compatriots on both sides, and it cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China. We will, as always, support and promote cross-Strait youth exchanges, and continue to build more platforms and create more opportunities for young people across the Strait to learn from and draw on each other and to engage in exchanges. We sincerely invite Taiwan’s young people, especially those who have never been to the mainland, to bravely break through the information cocoons created by the “Taiwan independence” forces, come to the mainland to take a look and see for themselves, and continuously form and deepen a correct understanding of cross-Strait relations and an objective understanding of the mainland through what they see and experience firsthand, and to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations by participating in cross-Strait exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-02-26","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","On the first question: since 2020, the mainland has suspended the admission of degree students to study in Taiwan due to the epidemic. Relevant parties in Taiwan are studying allowing mainland students from third locations to study in Taiwan. The Mainland Affairs Council recently said it “welcomes and will cooperate,” what is your comment on this? On the second question: regarding the incident in which the…","On the first question: We have never regarded Taiwanese students studying at universities on the mainland as outsiders. For many years, we have worked hard to provide them with the same treatment as mainland students, and Taiwanese students' sense of gain, security, and happiness has significantly increased.\nIn contrast, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have set unreasonable restrictions and treated mainland students unfairly when they come to study in Taiwan. May I ask everyone: under the current severe situation in the Taiwan Strait, in the face of cold shoulders and cold words, why should mainland students swallow their pride and go to study in Taiwan? Can their parents be at ease? If the Democratic Progressive Party authorities sincerely hope that mainland students will study in Taiwan, they should change their wrong practices as soon as possible and genuinely safeguard the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan.\nOn the second question: As is well known, the fundamental reason affecting the implementation of cross-Strait agreements is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle.\nOn the third question: You mentioned that Taiwan residents have a sense of fear. This is precisely because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities often intimidate and suppress Taiwan compatriots on the basis of fabricated charges for normal exchanges, visits, and tourism to the mainland, attempting to use the so-called \"anti-infiltration law\" to create a \"chilling effect\" and \"green terror\" on the island, which is unpopular. Peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island, and no one can suppress the desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer to each other, nor can anyone stop the great trend of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202502/t20250226_12686439.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-02-27","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan’s defense ministry today said it detected 45 Chinese aircraft and 14 warships near the island today. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment on this?","There is no so-called “defense ministry” in Taiwan. And this is not a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202502/t20250227_11565165.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202502/t20250227_11565127.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: According to media reports, more than 30 countries, including Russia, China, and the United States, recently took part in the “Komodo-2025” multilateral naval exercise held in Indonesia. Can the spokesperson confirm this? Second question: According to Taiwanese media reports, the US government will soon unfreeze US$870 million in “security assistance” for Taiwan. In addition,…","Regarding the first question: We have noted the relevant reports. China sent embassy representatives to take part in relevant activities of the multinational maritime joint exercise “Komodo-2025.”\nRegarding the second question: The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any form of US-Taiwan military ties, and we firmly oppose US arms sales to the Taiwan region of China. “Relying on the US to seek independence” is a dead end. The DPP authorities are pouring taxpayer money, which should benefit the people, into a bottomless pit of “harming and destroying Taiwan.” They will inevitably end up playing with fire and burning themselves.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: Some media reported that the Facebook account for the “Golden Cobra” exercise posted that Taiwan had sent personnel to participate, but then deleted “Taiwan.” What is the spokesperson’s comment? Second question: DeepSeek is currently a hot topic, and all walks of life are conducting in-depth exploration of it. I wonder whether you have noticed this phenomenon, and whether the…","On the first question: We have noted the relevant reports and the practice of the US side of deleting content. China firmly opposes any country carrying out any form of official exchanges or military contact with Taiwan region of China, and this position is unwavering.\nOn the second question: Of course I pay attention to DeepSeek, and I have the app on my phone. My team and I sometimes use artificial intelligence software to conduct some searches when preparing for the Ministry of National Defense’s press conferences. In this field, our policy is very clear. China has consistently advocated that the development of artificial intelligence should follow the principles of “people-centered” and “intelligence for good,” and ensure that relevant weapon systems always remain under human control.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command recently said that in recent years, PLA activity around Taiwan has clearly increased, and in February alone, “spy balloons” and combat ships and aircraft were repeatedly dispatched around the island. When the mainland “attacks Taiwan,” it very likely “uses exercises to cover its true purpose.” Separately, Taiwanese media reported that officials from the US Indo-Pacific…","As for the specific tactics you mentioned, I will not comment here. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. We are willing to strive with the utmost sincerity and effort for the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force. This is directed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external interference. As long as anyone pursues “Taiwan independence,” they will certainly be met with a sudden and crushing counterattack by the People's Liberation Army. We also warn certain people on the US side not to try to “steal a chicken” over the Taiwan question, for what they would lose if they fail is more than just a handful of rice.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first: reportedly, the live-troop drill time for Taiwan’s “Han Kuang 41” exercise will be greatly increased, and, under US encouragement, the mobilization of reserve forces will be expanded to a scale of 3,000 people. What comments does the spokesperson have? The second: this year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the world anti-fascist war and the 80th anniversary of the…","On the first question: The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The United States attempts to “use Taiwan to contain China” and indulges the DPP authorities’ “Taiwan independence” adventurism and provocations. In the end, this will inevitably bring disaster upon itself.\nThe DPP authorities fantasize about “relying on the United States to seek independence” and “resisting reunification by force.” This is a serious miscalculation of the situation, public opinion, and the balance of strength. It is overestimating themselves and extremely dangerous. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: a mantis trying to stop a chariot can only bring about its own destruction, and sooner or later we will come to deal with you.\nOn the second question: We will solemnly commemorate the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. As for the specific arrangements you asked about, I currently have no information to release.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan’s defense authorities said the PLA conducted live-fire exercises yesterday at a distance of about 70 kilometers from the coast of the island. Is this report true? If so, please further introduce the relevant situation.","The remarks made by the relevant Taiwan authorities on the PLA's routine training and exercises are pure hype. We demand that they stop playing tricks and riding on hot topics.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Taiwan's defense authorities recently issued a notice of a draft amendment to Article 4 of the “Implementation Measures for the Selection and Training of Volunteer Soldiers,” relaxing restrictions on applicants' height, eyesight, tattoos, and other requirements. What is the spokesperson's comment?","In the face of the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, any small maneuver by the DPP authorities is a waste of effort; in the end, it can be said that “scheming too cleverly, one ends up ruining one’s own life.” The PLA has pointed out on many occasions that pursuing “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. For those who refuse to wake up, let them crash their heads bloody against the facts.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-02-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, the US Secretary of State accepted an exclusive interview with Fox News. The host asked, “If the mainland plans to occupy Taiwan in 2027, and you are woken up at 2 a.m. because intelligence shows Taiwan will be occupied, what would the US do?” Rubio responded that the US has committed to preventing such an event, and he also admitted on the program that the mainland’s current military strength is nearly…","I listened carefully to your question and first clarify one term: it is reunification, not occupation. Taiwan is Taiwan of China, and how to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves. Others have no right to point fingers.\nIf everyone has no other questions, I will formally introduce the faculty and student representatives from Renmin University of China. Renmin University is the first new-type regular university founded by our Party. It was born amid the flames of the War of Resistance Against Japan, is hailed as the “vanguard of the revolution” and the cradle of “builders of the People’s Republic,” and has produced a large number of heroes and role models.\nOn the afternoon of February 27,\nfaculty and student representatives of Renmin University of China\nobserve the Ministry of National Defense\nregular\npress conference\nNot long ago, faculty and student representatives of Renmin University went to the frontier line, stood guard and patrolled alongside officers and soldiers, and experienced the hardships of defending the nation’s borders. Some students said that the beautiful borders of a great country need more young people to guard them, and that the finest youth should blossom where the motherland needs it most. I strongly agree with this. Renmin University serves the people. We look forward to students carrying on the red gene, keeping the nation and all under heaven in their hearts, striving hard on the track of youth, writing “poetry and distant places,” and heading toward “the sea of stars.”\nFinally, I will announce another piece of good news. To better introduce China’s national defense and military development, our news release work will soon increase in frequency and scale. The Ministry of National Defense’s regular release frequency will rise from the current twice a month to three times a month, and the scope of media attending press conferences will be further expanded to invite more Chinese and foreign media to join our big family. Questions are the voice of the times. An open Chinese military welcomes everyone’s questions, including tricky and unusual ones. We look forward to meeting with journalist friends more often, communicating more, and developing together, and witnessing together this era of stormy change in which the Chinese military has great achievements.\nRegistration fax: (+86) 010-6201 8356\nEmail: modio2022@qq.com\nDeadline: March 10, 2025\nReminder: Please provide a sealed media application letter, including an introduction to the media organization, journalist information, contact details, etc.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16371699.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-02-28","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 28 — In response to Lai Ching-te's remarks at an event commemorating the \"February 28\" Incident, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered questions on February 28, saying that the \"February 28\" Incident, which took place 78 years ago, was a righteous action by Taiwan compatriots to resist authoritarian rule and fight for…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that while Lai Ching-te repeatedly claims to promote “Taiwan unity,” when commemorating the “2·28 Incident,” he not only fails to heal the social rifts in Taiwan based on historical facts, but instead engages in extensive political manipulation, touts “Taiwan independence” fallacies, promotes separatist propositions, hypes the “mainland threat,” and once again fully exposes his malicious intent to stubbornly insist on “Taiwan independence” separatism, incite confrontation and antagonism, and deliberately aggravate cross-Strait tensions. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will uphold correct views of history, nation, and state, objectively understand the “2·28 Incident,” not be deceived or misled by the DPP authorities, and, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own well-being, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202502/t20250228_12686959.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-03-03","Lin Jian","CCTV","U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio recently blamed China on issues of Taiwan, economy and trade, COVID-19 and Indo-Pacific affairs in an interview by U.S. media outlet. What is China’s comment?","Rubio’s remarks are steeped in the Cold-War mentality and full of lies and false accusations. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this, and has lodged serious protests with the U.S.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is the real status quo of the Taiwan Strait. The U.S. has distorted the one-China principle, and insisted on using Taiwan to contain China, and the Taiwan authorities have sought “independence” under the support and connivance of the U.S. These are the most fundamental changes to the status quo of the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan question is the most crucial, sensitive and explosive issue in the China-U.S. relations. If the U.S. does not hope to trigger confrontation, they must stop crossing or trampling on the red line of the Taiwan question.\nTrade and tariff wars have no winners. The U.S.’s attempts to politicize and weaponize trade and economic issues, levy tariff hikes on Chinese imports under the pretext of fentanyl, and create blocks to its normal trade, investment and economic cooperation with China will only harm its own economic interests and international credibility. China stands ready to work with the U.S. to address each other’s concerns through dialogue and consultation on the basis of equality and mutual respect. In the meanwhile, we will take all measures necessary to safeguard our legitimate rights and interests.\nThe origins-tracing of COVID-19 is a serious science issue. It is “extremely unlikely” that the pandemic was caused by a lab leak—this is the authoritative conclusion reached by the experts of the WHO-China joint mission following their field trips to the lab in Wuhan and in-depth communication with researchers. It is a conclusion based on science, which is widely recognized by the international community and the science community. More and more clues in the international science community point possible COVID origins to various parts of the world, and a global perspective is needed to carry out origins-tracing work in multiple countries and regions, in particular the U.S. The U.S. needs to immediately stop slinging mud on and scapegoating China.\nThe Asia-Pacific is a pace-setter in cooperation and development, not a chess board for geopolitical rivalry. History and facts show time and again that treating other countries as a chess piece, pawn or even cannon fodder is the U.S.’s go-to tactic. The U.S. should not project its own hegemonic mentality onto China. Attempts to stoke bloc confrontation in the Asia-Pacific run counter to the trend of the times and go against the common aspiration of regional countries. These moves will win no support and be doomed to failure.\nOur message to the U.S.: a lie told a thousand times cannot be a fact, the world will not be fooled by such baseless vilification against China, and megaphone diplomacy does no good to China-U.S. relations. We will be committed to viewing and developing our relations with the U.S. on the basis of the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation put forward by President Xi Jinping. Meanwhile, we will firmly defend national sovereignty, security and development interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250303_11567318.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250303_11567417.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters' questions\n(March 4, 2025)\nQ: After the Taiwan education authorities prohibited exchanges between the island and three mainland universities including Jinan University, they recently added seven more mainland universities, including Beihang University and Beijing Institute of Technology, to the list of institutions banned from exchange and cooperation. What is your comment?\nA:\nBeihang University, Beijing Institute of Technology and other universities are world-renowned engineering institutions. Since their founding, they have nurtured many talents, and their research achievements have been widely applied in aerospace, mathematics, artificial intelligence, electronic information, chemical materials and other fields, making important contributions to industrial development and scientific and technological progress on the mainland and in the world, and not only in the military science and technology field. The DPP authorities' ban on Taiwan universities engaging in exchange and cooperation with these seven high-level institutions harms the interests of Taiwan universities and exposes their laughable narrow-mindedness and arrogance, like a frog in a well or the self-important king of Yelang.\nThe DPP authorities have repeatedly extended political hands into cross-strait educational exchanges recently, fully demonstrating that their thinking is “opposing everything Chinese” and provocative confrontation, and that what they do is obstruct exchanges and cooperation and undermine cross-strait relations. Educators and young students on the island have already condemned this strongly.\nThe motherland's mainland has achieved a development miracle recognized worldwide, which depends greatly on the substantial progress of mainland education and science and technology. We are willing to provide convenience for broad Taiwan students to share the high-level education on the mainland, and the doors of mainland universities will always be open to Taiwan compatriots with lofty aspirations. The Unified Examination for Overseas Chinese, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Students by mainland general colleges and universities is currently open for online registration, and broad Taiwan youth are welcome to register actively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250304_12687649.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-03-05","Lin Jian","Reuters","An investor group backed by BlackRock has agreed to buy a majority stake in the Hong Kong-based company that runs ports along either side of the Panama Canal. This would give a U.S. firm control of key docks in that area amid pressure from the White House. Does the Ministry have any comment on this?","We have no comment on the relevant commercial deal. The government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region made a response to the operation of the ports by the relevant Hong Kong company. Let me say more broadly that China supports Chinese companies, including those from Hong Kong SAR, in investing and doing business overseas. Hope they can have access to a fair and just business environment everywhere they go. We oppose any abuse of coercion and pressuring in international trade and economic relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250305_11568916.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250305_11568706.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-03-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: How will China's national defense budget be arranged in 2025?","Wu Qian: The Chinese government adheres to the policy of coordinating national defense development with economic development and reasonably determines the scale of defense spending. In recent years, to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests and to meet the needs of China's military transformation with Chinese characteristics, the Chinese government, while promoting the sustained and healthy development of the economy and society, has generally maintained a reasonable and steady growth of defense spending, promoting the synchronous improvement of national defense strength and economic strength.\nTaking into account the overall needs of national security and development, ensuring that the modernization of national defense and the armed forces keeps pace with the modernization of the country, comprehensively enhancing strategic capabilities for safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and realizing the centenary goal of building the armed forces on schedule, the 2025 national general public budget arranges defense expenditure of 1.81 trillion yuan, an increase of 7.2% over the previous year's actual execution, of which central-level expenditure is 1.78 trillion yuan, an increase of 7.2% over the previous year's actual execution. The increased defense spending will mainly be used in the following areas: First, vigorously developing new-domain and new-quality combat forces, overall strengthening the building of traditional combat forces, and building a new configuration of services and arms. Second, advancing the building of reconnaissance and early warning, joint strike, battlefield support, and integrated support systems and capabilities, ensuring the successful conclusion of the 14th Five-Year Plan for military construction. Third, strengthening realistic military training, promoting connotative development of military academies, and building a new system for cultivating military talent. Fourth, continuously deepening national defense and military reform, improving supporting policies and systems in areas such as military human resources, and improving conditions for troops' training and combat readiness and for officers' and soldiers' work and living support.\nIt should be pointed out that the Chinese government, in accordance with the National Defense Law, the Budget Law, and other laws and regulations, includes the annual defense expenditure budget in the draft government budget, which is reviewed and approved by the National People's Congress, and is managed and used in accordance with the law. The total defense expenditure budget is published. China actively participates in the UN military expenditure transparency system, and its budget scale, structure, and basic uses are open and transparent. Compared with major military powers such as the United States, China's defense spending is relatively low in terms of its share of gross domestic product, its share of national fiscal expenditure, per capita national defense spending, and per capita military personnel spending, among other measures.\nThe world is not at peace, and peace needs to be defended. China has not yet achieved complete reunification, and it is also one of the countries with the most complex security environment on its periphery. The Chinese military faces severe challenges in safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, among other areas. China's limited defense spending is both a necessity for responding to complex security challenges and a need to meet the expectations of the international community and fulfill its responsibilities as a major country. It helps the Chinese military provide more public security goods and make greater contributions to building a community with a shared future for mankind.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/ztjzh/16373832.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-09","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: Taiwan's defense authorities recently said that the mainland is continuously escalating its “military threat” across the Asia-Pacific and even globally, openly challenging the international order and undermining the status quo of regional stability. Separately, Taiwanese media reported that the Taiwan military is studying the possibility of having all women of eligible age on the island serve in the…","Wu Qian: There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. The One-China principle is a common consensus of the international community. In 1945, Taiwan's return to the Chinese map was the fruit of victory in the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and it is an undeniable historical fact. For some time, the DPP authorities have intensified “Taiwan independence” separatist provocations, attempting to “seek independence by relying on the United States” and “refuse unification by force.” This has aroused the common indignation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and will surely be subject to the reckoning of history and justice.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. A few American-made weapons cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” toward extinction. The DPP authorities are using the hard-earned money of ordinary people to buy weapons from their foreign masters, which is nothing more than a mantis trying to stop a chariot. What role could it possibly play?\nThe motherland will inevitably be reunified; this is the trend of the times and a matter of justice, and it is both the result of strength and the will of the people. The People's Liberation Army has always been an activist in striving for “independence” and promoting unification. In recent years, circumnavigation of the island and military deterrence have become routine. The more “Taiwan independence” elements make noise, the tighter the rope around their necks will be drawn, and the sharper the sword hanging over their heads will become. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: turn back from the precipice while there is still time; those who persist in their delusion face a dead end.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/ztjzh/16373832.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-03-10","Mao Ning","CCTV","We noted that when responding to a question about Taiwan at the press conference during the two sessions last week, Foreign Minister Wang Yi said that the only reference to the Taiwan region in the U.N. is “Taiwan, Province of China.” Some believe this statement shows the Chinese mainland’s tougher policy on Taiwan. What’s your view?","Resolution 2758 adopted in 1971 by the U.N. General Assembly made it clear that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is not a country, and Taiwan is part of China. It also made clear that there is only one seat of China in the United Nations, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal representative in the U.N. This resolution is observed by the U.N. and its specialized agencies as evidenced by their reference to Taiwan as “Taiwan, Province of China.” It was clearly stated in the official legal opinions of the Office of Legal Affairs of the U.N. Secretariat that “the United Nations considers ‘Taiwan’ as a province of China with no separate status.” This is the U.N.’s consistent position, which is well documented.\nOn the Taiwan question, China’s position is consistent and clear. We stay committed to the one-China principle and the 1992 Consensus. We stand ready to work with the greatest sincerity and exert utmost efforts to achieve peaceful reunification. Meanwhile, China will take all necessary measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250310_11572149.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250310_11572088.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-10","Mao Ning","NHK","Taiwan’s “ministry of economic affairs” announced that it will attend the World Expo in Osaka, Japan in an unofficial capacity. What is China’s comment?","We firmly oppose any kind of official interactions between the Taiwan region and any country that has diplomatic ties with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250310_11572149.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250310_11572088.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-10","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","There are reports that the U.S. has promised to accelerate arms shipments to Taiwan. Can you comment?","China is firmly opposed to the U.S.’s military ties with and arms sales to China’s Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-U.S. relations. China calls on the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop selling arms to the Taiwan region and having military contact with Taiwan, stop creating factors that fuel tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and stop endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250310_11572149.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250310_11572088.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear reporters, welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The national “Two Sessions” has just concluded, and the Taiwan-related content of each year’s “Report on the Work of the Government” attracts wide attention. Please interpret the Taiwan-related content in this year’s “Report on the Work of the Government.”","This year's Government Work Report content on Taiwan comprehensively implements the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and the Second and Third Plenary Sessions of the 20th Central Committee, implements the decisions and arrangements of the CPC Central Committee on Taiwan work, and fully reflects the three \"never changed.\"\nFirst, our basic position on the Taiwan question has never changed. We will unswervingly uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" firmly oppose and contain any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist act and external interference, and consolidate the basic pattern of the international community adhering to the one-China principle. Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. We have the confidence and the capability to resolve our own family matters well.\nSecond, our sincerity and goodwill in seeking benefits and welfare for Taiwan compatriots have never changed. We will continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, expand personnel exchanges across the Strait, support the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, enable Taiwan compatriots to share in the development opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization, create better conditions for young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to pursue and realize their dreams, and broadly unite Taiwan compatriots to jointly advance cross-Strait relations.\nThird, our determination to advance the great cause of reunifying the motherland has never changed. We firmly hold the initiative and the leading role in cross-Strait relations, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, resolutely combat provocations of \"Taiwan independence,\" steadfastly advance the process of reunifying the motherland, and continuously shape the inevitable trend toward the reunification of the motherland. This accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and is the shared expectation of all Chinese descendants.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689650.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Some commentary has noted that the Taiwan-related content in the Government Work Reports of 2024 and 2025 only stressed “unswervingly advancing the great cause of national reunification” and did not mention “peaceful reunification.” Does the spokesperson’s position mean that the mainland’s stance has changed?","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. It is the best way to achieve the reunification of the motherland and is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to the Chinese nation. In resolving the Taiwan question, we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces provoke and force the issue, or even challenge the bottom line and cross the red line, we will be compelled to take resolute measures.\nAt present, the situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause lies in the Democratic Progressive Party authorities colluding with external forces to continuously carry out provocations in pursuit of independence, seriously endangering cross-Strait relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and steadfastly advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689648.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","We note that this year's Government Work Report for the first time proposed “improving the institutions and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation.” Public opinion holds that this shows the mainland will do better in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, enabling Taiwan residents coming to the mainland to integrate better and achieve greater development. What is your…","This year's Government Work Report put forward “improving the systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation,” which fully demonstrates our determination to continuously advance cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepen cross-Strait integrated development. It aims, through more innovative and comprehensive policies and measures, to provide firmer guarantees for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, to push cross-Strait integrated development to go deeper and more solidly, and to promote the forward development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe will further optimize and refine our systems and policies, and strive to continuously expand and deepen personnel exchanges across the Strait and cooperation in all fields. We will attract more Taiwan compatriots to broadly take part in cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, jointly promote Chinese culture, continuously enhance mutual understanding and friendship, and strengthen their sense of gain, happiness, and security.\nWe will continue to support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the mainland's high-quality development, improve the targeting and precision of policies that benefit the people and support enterprises, promote the implementation of equal treatment, and support Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises in integrating into the mainland to develop better and faster. We will continue to implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” promote the implementation of “using connectivity to promote integration, using benefits to promote integration, and using emotion to promote integration,” continuously expand the levels and fields of cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development, and provide better conditions and inject strong impetus so that Taiwan compatriots and enterprises can share the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization.\nChinese-style modernization is a shared cause of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Taiwan compatriots are Chinese people and members of the Chinese nation, and they have every reason to take part in the great process of Chinese-style modernization and share the supreme glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will practice the development philosophy centered on the people and the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, make earnest and concerted efforts to do practical good deeds for Taiwan compatriots and help them solve their difficulties, and enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, especially grassroots people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689649.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","The 2025 Taiwan work conference was held in Beijing in late February. It emphasized resolutely cracking down on “Taiwan independence” provocations and, for the first time, put forward the formulation “shaping the inevitable trend of national reunification.” How should this new formulation be interpreted? How will the mainland “shape the trend”?","The key factor determining the direction of cross-Strait relations is the development and progress of the mainland. Since the new era, the mainland has steadily advanced high-quality development and steadily raised the productivity of new quality, and its economic strength, technological capacity, comprehensive national strength, and international influence have continued to grow. The Chinese path to modernization has taken solid steps, the foundation and capacity for resolving the Taiwan question are stronger, and this has effectively shaped the trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified.\nThe motherland must be reunified, and it will inevitably be reunified. This is the historical conclusion of the development of cross-Strait relations, an inevitable requirement of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in the new era, and a historical trend that no person or force can stop. In the new era and on the new journey, we will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely and forcefully crack down on “Taiwan independence” provocations, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, resolutely oppose interference by external forces, and broadly unite Taiwan compatriots to jointly advance cross-Strait relations and push forward the process of national reunification.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end; outsiders are unreliable, and unification cannot be stopped. We sincerely hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will see the situation clearly, follow the historical trend, strengthen national self-confidence in being upright Chinese people, walk in unison with mainland compatriots, complete the great cause of national reunification at an early date, jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and share in the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689647.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","During Trump’s meeting with Zelensky, the two sides argued repeatedly, which fueled the “doubt-the-US” theory on the island. The head of Taiwan’s external affairs department said that “Taiwan and Ukraine have ‘four major differences’ in terms of strategic location, current status and other aspects,” so “there is no need for the doubt-the-US theory.” What comment do you have on this?","First of all, it must be pointed out that the Taiwan question and the Ukraine question are fundamentally different. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is permitted.\nThe DPP authorities previously loudly touted “Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow,” trying to rely on outside forces to embolden themselves and incite “anti-China” sentiment, and now they hastily and deliberately try to draw a distinction. This self-contradictory, self-refuting behavior precisely exposes their flustered and guilty state. No matter how the DPP authorities argue, they cannot change their position of depending on others’ whims and being at others’ mercy. No matter how many “reassurances to the people” they issue, they cannot change the essence of “selling out Taiwan for personal glory,” and they cannot dispel the deep concern among the broad Taiwan compatriot population that “pawns” will inevitably become “discarded pawns.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689642.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, after the Lai Qingde authorities banned exchanges with three mainland universities including Jinan University, they also placed seven mainland universities including Beihang University on the list of universities banned from exchange and cooperation. Public opinion generally holds that since taking office last year, the Lai Qingde authorities have obstructed and restricted cross-Strait personnel…","Since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office in May last year, they have disregarded the mainstream public opinion on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. They have used administrative, judicial, and public opinion means, employing every possible tactic to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, restrict Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, and persecute island groups and individuals who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges. They have indeed compiled a record of misdeeds and committed numerous wrongdoings.\nThe DPP authorities have deliberately and persistently obstructed cross-Strait personnel exchanges and tourism cooperation. They refuse to lift the “group ban,” have raised the “orange” travel alert for Taiwan residents visiting the mainland, and have obstructed the full restoration of cross-Strait passenger air direct flight routes and flights. Using various excuses, they have resisted and delayed group tours by residents of Fujian and Shanghai to Taiwan. They have restricted and intimidated Taiwan compatriots applying for mainland certificates, and have required public employees to sign “written undertakings” stating that they have not applied for mainland identity documents, creating a “new green terror.” They have continuously subjected village and neighborhood chiefs who visit and exchange with the mainland to judicial persecution, abused their power to oppress the public, and created a “chilling effect.” They have required relevant departments to fully ban the use of DeepSeek (深度求索) software, and prohibited public schools from purchasing and using mainland information and communications products, including hardware and software. Without any basis, they have placed more than one hundred organizations, including the Chinese Academy of Sciences, the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, and Confucius Institutes, on so-called “restricted” lists, obstructing Taiwan professionals from participating in the development of mainland science, technology, and cultural undertakings. They have continually imposed obstacles and restrictions on mainland delegations and personnel visiting Taiwan for exchanges. They have repeatedly reached political hands into the professional field of cross-Strait education exchanges, prohibiting exchanges and cooperation between the island and ten mainland universities, including Jinan University and Beihang University, which has provoked condemnation from the island's education and public opinion circles.\nThe above is only a partial list, and their actions have grown increasingly extreme, with ever more varied tactics. This fully demonstrates that the Lai Ching-te authorities are a stumbling block to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and a disruptor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Those who do wrong will eventually bring about their own downfall. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities that the desire of compatriots on both sides to draw closer to one another cannot be suppressed, and the trend of exchanges and cooperation cannot be blocked. Their reckless and perverse actions will inevitably backfire, and they will pay a painful price.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689646.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Fujian Province recently issued the fourth batch of policy measures to advance the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. Could the spokesperson introduce the latest progress in Fujian's construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone?","On February 27, Fujian Province released the fourth batch of 17 policy measures to advance the construction of the demonstration zone for cross-Strait integrated development. The policies released this time are another important step in Fujian Province's thorough implementation of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” (the “Opinions”). The new batch of policy measures has three notable highlights:\nFirst, they closely follow the deployment and arrangements of the “Opinions.” They introduce policy measures such as piloting allowing Taiwan enterprises to establish broadcasting and television program production and operation companies in Fujian, supporting Taiwan compatriots' participation in marine fishery aquaculture cooperation in Ningde, and supporting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises' participation in biotechnology and medical industry cooperation in Putian, further refining and implementing the “Opinions.”\nSecond, they highlight the needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Focusing on the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, they provide targeted support in areas such as employment and entrepreneurship, daily convenience, and protection of rights and interests. Through measures such as direct recognition of professional skill qualifications, online renewal and reissuance of residence permits, and the opening of cross-Strait marriage and family hotlines, they address practical problems that Taiwan compatriots face in integrating into daily life in Fujian.\nThird, they make concerted efforts to provide more development opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Measures such as operating incentives for Matsu enterprises settling in the Matsu Industrial Cooperation Park in Fuzhou, which serves as a pilot zone, providing more than one hundred exclusive positions in Ningde's lithium battery industry enterprises for Taiwan compatriots, and offering a 30% discount to Taiwan compatriots who purchase Sanming forestry carbon tickets—these are all genuine “practical benefits.” They are committed to bridging the “last mile” of policy implementation, ensuring rapid application and immediate use, and enhancing the sense of gain for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises.\nSince the release of the “Opinions,” Fujian Province has successively released four batches totaling 62 policy measures, which have received a positive response. In the future, Fujian Province will continue to be guided by the orientation of “integration and demonstration,” and promote the translation of policies from “on paper” to “on the ground.” We believe that as the dividends of these policies continue to be released, more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will share opportunities and win a common future in this land of Fujian, which is close to our people and our soil.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, US President Trump and TSMC Chairman C.C. Wei jointly announced that TSMC will invest at least another $100 billion in the United States. This has intensified concerns across the island that “TSMC” is becoming “American TSMC” (美积电), and worries that it will weaken Taiwan’s industrial advantages. Although the Lai Ching-te authorities claim that they “had no prior knowledge of it,” they still deny that it…","The DPP authorities' claims are a case of accepting insults without wiping off the spit and of covering up one lie with another. The so-called “beneficial to the industry”: is that beneficial to the American industry? In order to “rely on the US to seek independence,” the DPP authorities' willingness to sell out Taiwan is shocking in its lack of bottom line. The US is relentlessly pressing forward, hollowing out TSMC and draining Taiwan dry, while the DPP authorities let themselves be manipulated at will. When have they ever taken the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the interests of industry to heart? Taiwan residents' worry that TSMC will turn into “American TSMC” is not “needless worry”; and Taiwan's transformation from “pawn” to “discarded piece” is also a doomed outcome.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689643.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, the DPP authorities required civil servants, public school teaching staff and other public employees to fill out a “written pledge of not having household registration on the mainland and holding a mainland identity card,” which provoked backlash from relevant individuals, who publicly stated they would refuse to sign. Commentary on the island criticized this as “abuse of power and illegal,” and as a…","The DPP authorities have escalated to create a “green terror,” which has met with strong opposition from the public on the island and fierce criticism from public opinion. Quite a few people have expressed their stance by refusing to sign. Out of their independence-seeking nature, the DPP authorities stubbornly hold a confrontational mindset and continually use various pretexts and methods to interfere with and obstruct normal cross-strait exchanges and personnel travel, escalating hostility and confrontation between the two sides and undermining the development of cross-strait relations. Such misdeeds deprive people of freedom of choice and turn the “democracy and human rights” they tout into a joke.\nThe Taiwan Compatriot Permit facilitates Taiwan compatriots’ travel between the two sides, and the Taiwan residence permit provides Taiwan compatriots with equal treatment in enjoying basic public services while living and working on the mainland. These identity documents accord with popular will and win the hearts of the people, and since their introduction they have been widely welcomed and affirmed by Taiwan compatriots. Public security organs on the mainland have always attached great importance to protecting personal information security in accordance with law, and they strictly guard against and severely crack down on the illegal theft of personal information from identity documents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689645.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Taiwanese media revealed that “diehard Taiwan independence” element Shen Boyang not only owns two undeclared properties in the United States, but has also long received financial subsidies from the United States. Some public opinion on the island questions whether Shen is “taking money to do the job and serving as a US mouthpiece,” while the DPP authorities do not consider this a problem. What is the…","Some people on the island treat “Taiwan independence” as a business. They profit from “independence” themselves, rake in fortunes, yet urge other people's children to go to the battlefield as cannon fodder. They take foreigners' money to work for foreigners, go all out to toady to and fawn over the US, and yet talk nonsense to incite “anti-China, resist-China” sentiment. Shen Boyang's conduct upholds “US interests” and calculates personal gain. He is servile and obsequious, which is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","US President Trump and Vice President Vance quarreled repeatedly with Ukrainian President Zelensky during their meeting, which sparked heated discussion on the island. Public opinion holds that the Lai Ching-te authorities should see the situation clearly, actively pursue cross-Strait peace, and avoid leading Taiwan into the abyss. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","This fully shows that more and more Taiwan residents have come to recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders cannot be relied upon. They also recognize that the Lai Ching-te authorities' attempts to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence by relying on outsiders” are a wrong path and a perilous road, which will only make Taiwan's situation more dangerous and war more ominous. If they are allowed to rush ahead recklessly, they will surely fall into an abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》记者","Regarding the mainland’s 7.2% growth in national defense spending this year, Taiwan’s MAC said it hopes “the mainland will exercise rationality and restraint, communicate and dialogue with the Taiwan authorities, jointly bear responsibility for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the region, and not take military provocative actions.” What comment do you have?","In accordance with the National Defense Law, the Budget Law, and other laws and regulations, the mainland side includes its annual national defense expenditure budget in the draft government budget. It is reviewed and approved by the National People’s Congress, managed and used in accordance with the law, and the total national defense expenditure budget is publicly announced. The mainland’s national defense expenditure is open, transparent, reasonable, and moderate. It is entirely necessary for defending national sovereignty, security, and development interests, and necessary for safeguarding world peace.\nThe DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped up the so-called “military threat” from the mainland, while doing their utmost to curry favor with external forces that extract benefits from Taiwan. They persistently “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence,” while turning a deaf ear to the appeals of Taiwan people who hope to improve livelihoods and welfare and to “avoid war and seek peace.” Who is the destroyer of cross-strait peace and the creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis is self-evident.\nThe DPP authorities deliberately exaggerate tensions in the Taiwan Strait and attempt to incite cross-strait confrontation merely to blur the focus and evade criticism and opposition from all sectors of the island regarding their unscrupulous “selling out of Taiwan” and paying “protection money.” No matter how the DPP authorities powder their faces or talk around in circles, they cannot change their essence of “currying favor with the United States and selling out Taiwan” and their cowardice. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and unification cannot be stopped. No matter how much military spending the DPP authorities allocate or how much “protection money” they pay, they cannot change the outcome of a dead end for “using force to resist unification,” nor can they stop the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250312_12689644.htm"],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The Taiwan-related content of the Government Work Report shows that the Mainland will continue to actively expand cross-Strait exchanges this year. Could you introduce the exchange activities planned in the near future?","Recently, various parts of the Chinese mainland have held cross-Strait exchange activities in diverse forms. Here we introduce several of the main activities.\nFrom late January to mid-March, the 2025 Straits Cross-Strait (Qingliu) Cherry Blossom Culture Season was held in Qingliu County, Sanming City, Fujian Province. More than 350 Taiwan compatriots from New Taipei, Pingtung, Taichung, Tainan and other places in Taiwan participated. More than 80 Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots with intentions to invest and start businesses established regular contact with the local area. The culture season took the theme “Fujian-Taiwan Cherry Bond, Warm Spring Blossoms,” and carried out more than 10 events, including cross-Strait youth film viewing, intangible cultural heritage exchanges and investment promotion. Participants experienced in depth the splendid view of the cherry blossom gardens covering more than 2,000 mu (about 300,000 cherry trees) operated by Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan farmers, the unique natural scenery of the national-level hot spring geopark, and the charm of Qingliu's traditional Hakka culture.\nIn early March, the 7th Straits Cross-Strait Wenchang Culture Exchange Event and the 9th Straits Cross-Strait Leizu Culture Exchange Event were successively held in Zitong and Yanting, Mianyang, Sichuan Province. More than 600 people, including cross-Strait culture scholars, Taiwan businesspeople representatives and young students, participated. During the events, a series of activities were held, including cultural exchange visits, economic and trade cooperation discussions, and cross-Strait youth student study tours. Using Chinese cultural allusions as a link, these activities promoted cross-Strait cultural exchange and economic and trade cooperation, and strengthened the emotional bonds between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nIn addition, to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' travel and exchange in Yunnan, Yunnan Province has, since March 2025, exempted the first ticket fee at 320 tourist attractions for Taiwan compatriots who hold a Taiwan Compatriot Permit issued for the first time (issuance count 01), for travel to Yunnan within one year from the date of issuance. These include 9 AAAAA-rated scenic spots such as the Shilin Stone Forest in Kunming, the Three Pagodas of Chongsheng Temple in Dali, the ancient town of Lijiang and Jade Dragon Snow Mountain, as well as 124 AAAA-rated, 142 AAA-rated and 45 other scenic spots. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to visit, tour, study, and exchange in beautiful Yunnan, to better experience “a life called Yunnan.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Colby, the nominee for US Deputy Secretary of Defense, recently said that Taiwan's military spending is far from sufficient and should approach 10% of GDP. His future goal is “to avoid triggering unnecessary conflict between Taiwan and mainland China, and to buy time for the United States to improve the US-China military imbalance.” What comment does the spokesperson have?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We firmly oppose any form of U.S.-Taiwan military ties, and demand that the United States abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop “arming Taiwan,” and stop encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to “use force to seek independence.” We also solemnly warn the DPP authorities that, willing to act as “pawns” of external forces, they will ultimately become “discarded pieces.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities said that the PLA’s unannounced live-fire exercises in waters southwest of Taiwan are “a blatant violation of international practice, posing a high threat, and a blatant provocation and sabotage of regional security and stability.” What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, and the PLA organizing exercises and training around the Taiwan Strait is lawful, reasonable, and entirely justified. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces, continue to provoke by plotting “independence,” and are the greatest source of chaos and a real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The relevant PLA exercises demonstrate our firm determination, resolute will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: as long as “Taiwan independence” provocations continue, countermeasures will not stop for a moment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾“梅花新闻网”记者","In February, Taiwan's exports to the United States exceeded its exports to the mainland and Hong Kong combined for the first time in 24 years. In addition, the share of Taiwanese business investment in the mainland has also been surpassed by Taiwanese business investment in the United States. Faced with the phenomenon of cross-Strait economic and trade \"decoupling,\" what methods will the mainland adopt to respond?","The DPP authorities' push to “decouple” cross-Strait economic and trade relations and “break the chain” of industries goes against the laws of economic development and harms the immediate interests of compatriots on both sides, and it will not succeed. In 2024, cross-Strait trade reached US$292.971 billion, an increase of 9.4% year on year. In January and February of this year, cross-Strait trade again got off to a strong start, reaching US$43.176 billion, an increase of 8.8% year on year. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$11.245 billion and imports from Taiwan were US$31.931 billion, increasing by 8.4% and 8.9% respectively. This fully demonstrates that the momentum of cross-Strait economic cooperation remains strong, that the industrial and supply chains remain stable, and that cross-Strait economic exchanges are continuing to strengthen rather than weaken.\nWe will actively improve policies and systems that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, support Taiwan businesses and enterprises in developing on the mainland, continue to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, bring benefits to compatriots on both sides, and, in the process of building a new development pattern and achieving high-quality development, open up new space for further strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation.\nShenzhen Satellite TV's “Straight News” program:\nRaymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office, recently said in an interview that “what the United States is doing in Taiwan is making Taiwan stronger, safer, and more prosperous,” and that the United States and Taiwan could jointly build a “supply chain without China” in areas such as drones and robotics. What is your comment?\nSome people on the US side talk about “supporting Taiwan” but actually engage in “harming Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan.” They force TSMC to add up to US$100 billion in additional investment in the United States so that the US can have the world's largest chip industry. Is this making “America great again,” or making Taiwan “stronger”? When TSMC gradually becomes “US TSMC,” how much competitive advantage will Taiwan's industries still have, and can Taiwan still “prosper”? Some people on the US side have repeatedly clamored to turn Taiwan into a “porcupine.” Is this making Taiwan safer, or turning it into a powder keg that could explode at any moment? For decades, Taiwan's economic development has benefited from stable cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. Forcibly “decoupling and cutting chains” benefits Taiwan, or benefits the United States?\nThese questions deserve deep reflection from all sectors of Taiwan society. We also see that more and more people on the island have increasingly seen clearly what the United States is doing. The DPP authorities' blind pursuit of “independence by relying on the United States” will only lead to being at the mercy of others.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently stated that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 “did not confirm that Taiwan is part of the People's Republic of China, nor authorize the People's Republic of China to represent Taiwan at the United Nations,” and that the mainland “deliberately distorts the text of the resolution, releasing wrong information to the international community“. May I ask for the spokesperson's…","UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 is a political document that embodies the one-China principle. It clearly, fairly and thoroughly resolves, politically, legally and procedurally, the question of China's representation in the United Nations, and it also makes clear that China's seat in the United Nations is unique, and that there is no question of “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” China's representation in the United Nations is, of course, the representation of all of China, including Taiwan.\nThe DPP authorities maliciously distort UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. This is a distortion of facts, a trampling of international law, and an open challenge to international order and rules. Its purpose is to build momentum for “Taiwan independence” and to undermine the international community's consensus and pattern of upholding the one-China principle. No matter how they maneuver, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, cannot shake the international community's pattern of upholding the one-China principle, and cannot stop the historical trend that China is bound to be reunified and will certainly be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","The head of Taiwan’s external affairs department recently said Taiwan will continue to strengthen its own defense capabilities, and will establish with its “allies” a defense concept and system of a “single theater,” so that the Taiwan Strait becomes a “moat” that is hard to cross. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Many people in the DPP authorities are still living in the past, still thinking the Taiwan Strait is a natural barrier that is hard to cross. Knowing they cannot “resist unification by force,” they want to bring in external forces to embolden themselves. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that we have more than enough capability to reduce to ashes any force that “seeks independence and resists unification.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Recently, several Taiwanese entertainers reposted “Taiwan Province, China” on Weibo, expressing support for One China. The Mainland Affairs Council called this a “united front tool” of the mainland, and said it would review whether artists' conduct “involves cooperation with the CCP's party, government or military and violates the Act Governing Relations between the Two Sides of the Taiwan…","First question. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory and has never been a country. This is a historical and legal fact that cannot be denied or disputed. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, including performing artists, are upright Chinese. It is only natural for them to express their identification with the country and their opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism, which embodies national righteousness. The DPP authorities frequently resort to threats, intimidation and retaliation, attempting to restrict and deprive Taiwan compatriots of freedom of thought and freedom of speech. This fully exposes the hypocrisy of the “democracy and freedom” they advertise.\nSecond question. On March 14, 2005, the Third Session of the Tenth National People's Congress adopted the Anti-Secession Law by an overwhelming majority vote. This is a law that defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity, opposes and contains “Taiwan independence” separatism, promotes the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advances the process of national reunification, and maintains peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region in line with the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Since its promulgation and implementation, the law has played a unique and major role in firmly upholding the one-China principle, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the process of national reunification.\nWe will continue to earnestly implement the Anti-Secession Law, continue to strengthen the use of rule-of-law methods and forces, firmly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, and unswervingly advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Wang Yi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs, emphasized at the press conference on foreign affairs at the third session of the 14th National People’s Congress that the only title for Taiwan at the United Nations is “Taiwan Province of China,” and that Taiwan has never been a country. This has caused some controversy on the island. What comment do you have…","Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 fully reflects and solemnly affirms this. The United Nations and its specialized agencies strictly adhere to it, as is documented. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and this is also the core meaning of the “1992 Consensus.”\n“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. It is the best way to realize the reunification of the motherland and is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and to the Chinese nation. On the basis of adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we will widely unite Taiwan compatriots, actively explore a “two systems” plan for Taiwan, enrich the practice of peaceful reunification, promote the development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of reunifying the motherland. At the same time, we will take all necessary measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and we firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS电视台记者","First question: Recently, a mainland spouse who runs the account “Yaya in Taiwan” on a social media platform in Taiwan was reported for advocating “armed unification” remarks, and the Taiwan authorities launched an investigation. Her residence permit in Taiwan on the basis of dependent-relative status was revoked, and she faces a series of problems including family separation. What is the spokesperson's comment…","First question: The DPP authorities are using every means to heavily suppress voices with different positions on the island. This again exposes that the “freedom” they tout is the freedom to agitate for “Taiwan independence” and to advocate “resisting China.” It is both hypocritical and double-standard. If the DPP authorities are allowed to abuse administrative and judicial means, the legitimate rights and interests of the Taiwan public will be seriously infringed.\nI also noted that Taiwan media reported that Internet celebrity “Ba Jiong” claimed that he was the one who reported to the “National Immigration Agency.” About this person, I have a 16-character comment: Petty sneaks, mere cock-crowing and dog-stealing thieves. Those who act as tigers’ accomplices will surely be severely punished.\nSecond question: We have noted the relevant situation. The Taiwan side should treat mainland enterprises fairly and properly handle the relevant issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently published a poll claiming that 70% of Taiwan public opinion supports that cross-Strait tourism should resume only after communication through the tourism “Small Two Associations.” What is your comment?","Do you all trust the Mainland Affairs Council's public opinion polls? Are they credible? How were the final statistics obtained? How were they weighted? Professionals can all understand this, and Taiwan's society and media have their own public judgments.\nRegarding the resumption of cross-Strait tourism, we have stated our position on many occasions. The crux and obstacle to cross-Strait tourism is interference and obstruction by the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities have repeatedly cited communication through the “small two associations” as an excuse, and their purpose is to obstruct and delay the resumption of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","中央广电总台央广记者","A National People's Congress deputy recently said in an interview that measures to punish diehard “Taiwan independence” elements could be planned and implemented in more detail through legislative work at the NPC Standing Committee level, or through rules and regulations at the State Council level. What is the spokesperson's evaluation?","The state punishes diehard “Taiwan independence” elements according to law for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country. This is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity, and also a righteous act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The relevant suggestions by National People's Congress deputies reflect the aspiration of compatriots on both sides to strictly punish, according to law, the “bad apples” who undermine cross-Strait relations, to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and to live peaceful and tranquil days.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Taiwanese media reported that the DPP authorities are accelerating the so-called “national security legal reform,” and are considering changing the period after which Hong Kong residents in Taiwan may apply for permanent settlement from one year of residence to four years. They also plan to add a “long-term residence” option beyond residence and settlement, in order to reduce so-called security risks. What is…","The DPP authorities are fickle and erratic; all of their conduct reflects the weakness and timidity in their hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-12","Chen Binhua","台湾“梅花新闻网”记者","One hundred years ago today, Mr. Sun Yat-sen passed away at Peking Union Medical College Hospital in Beijing, and today marks the 100th anniversary of his death. Mr. Sun Yat-sen's final political testament to the Chinese people before his death was “peace, struggle, save China.” What inspiration does this offer for current cross-Strait relations and China's future development?","This year marks the 100th anniversary of the passing of Mr. Sun Yat-sen. We understand that Beijing, Jiangsu, Guangdong, and other places, as well as relevant democratic parties and groups, will hold commemorative activities.\nMr. Sun Yat-sen was a great national hero, a great patriot, and a great pioneer of China’s democratic revolution. He devoted his entire life to pursuing national reunification and the revitalization of China, and is revered by all Chinese descendants. At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will join us in carrying on Mr. Sun Yat-sen’s wishes, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and work hand in hand to advance the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250312_12689632.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-03-13","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwan president Lai Ching-te said today that China has deepened its influence campaign and infiltration against the island. He also said that China has used Taiwan’s democracy to absorb various members of society. How does the Ministry respond to this?","Taiwan is part of China. There is no so-called president in Taiwan. What you mentioned is not a question on foreign affairs. What I can tell you is that no matter what they say, the DPP authorities cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and the trend that China must achieve reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250313_11574297.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250313_11574313.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-13","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office's remarks on Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” separatist words and deeds\n(March 13, 2025)","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 13th that Lai Ching-te, after convening a so-called “national security high-level meeting” today and in his remarks after the meeting, once again promoted the separatist fallacy of “mutual non-subordination” across the Strait, falsely claimed that “Taiwan is a sovereign and independent democratic country,” vigorously played up the “Mainland threat,” defined the Mainland as a “hostile foreign force,” and put forward so-called “17 strategies” to “respond to five threats.” His stubborn “Taiwan independence” stance and his reckless provocation and confrontation once again prove that he is a thorough “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nOn the one hand, Lai Ching-te “sells out Taiwan for personal glory”; on the other hand, he acts recklessly. On the island, he escalates the creation of a “green terror,” suppresses political dissidents, incites “resistance to China and anti-China sentiment,” escalates cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, restricts and obstructs cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, and vigorously pushes cross-Strait “decoupling and severing of chains.” All of this serves his “Taiwan independence” separatist aims, shifts the focus of internal contradictions on the island, and eases his governing predicament. This fully exposes his evil nature: for the private interests of one party and one person, he does not hesitate to “worsen” society on the island, tie the ordinary people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and push Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and peril.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China's sacred territory. It has never been, and will never be, a country. Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people; this is an indisputable historical and legal fact and an unchangeable status quo across the Strait. Our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is as solid as a rock, and our capability is invincible. We will never allow anyone or any force to split Taiwan from China, and we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute measures.\nWe solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: those who play with fire will burn themselves. Those who forget their ancestry have never come to a good end; those who betray the motherland will surely be spurned by the people and judged by history; those who engage in “Taiwan independence” separatism can only be ground to powder; all conduct that goes against the tide and defies the disapproval of the world will bring about its own destruction. The trend of the motherland's inevitable reunification is surging forward, and no one and no force can stop it; all scheming tricks with ill intent are destined to fail!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250313_12689915.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-03-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the incoming US deputy secretary of defense said the question of Taiwan's status is not extremely important to the US, but the US has important security interests in Taiwan, and Taiwan should substantially raise its defense spending to about 10% of GDP. An official of Taiwan's defense department said that maintaining Asia-Pacific stability and the status quo across the Taiwan Strait is a…","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The United States attempts to “use Taiwan to contain China,” and is stepping up the arming of Taiwan. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have taken the opportunity to increase defense spending, seriously harming the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are indulging in the golden-millet dream of “relying on the US to seek independence,” and are willing to serve as “pawns,” selling out Taiwan and harming its people, and will ultimately be discarded like worn-out shoes.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16375006.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-14","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Japanese media reported that a Japanese naval vessel transited the Taiwan Strait in February. A Japanese defense official said this involves the use of the Self-Defense Forces and that they would not comment on it, but expressed serious concern about increased activity by Chinese military forces around Japan, and said Japan will respond calmly and resolutely. What comment does the spokesperson have?","China respects the navigation rights enjoyed by all countries under international law, but firmly opposes any country stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait, infringing on China's sovereignty and security, and sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nIt must be emphasized that the activities of the Chinese military in the relevant sea and airspace conform to international law and international practice, and are justified, reasonable and beyond reproach. Japan's baseless accusations against China's normal training and exercises are firmly opposed by us.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16375006.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-03-17","Mao Ning","CCTV","Recently, the Foreign Ministers of the G7 issued the Statement of the G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting and the G7 Foreign Ministers Declaration on Maritime Security and Prosperity to propagate China-related issues again. They made irresponsible remarks on the Taiwan question and maritime issues and expressed concerns over the alleged provision of weapons and dual-use components to Russia by China, China’s so-called…","The joint statement of the G7 Foreign Ministers’ meeting and their declaration are a deliberate mischaracterization of the facts and truth, which seek to vilify China and interfere in China’s internal affairs. We strongly deplore and firmly reject that and have lodged serious protests with relevant countries.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, which brooks no external interference. The situation in the South China Sea is generally stable. Freedom of navigation and overflight in the South China Sea has never been an issue. The G7 should stop sowing discord and provoking disputes. China has all along been promoting talks for peace on the Ukraine issue, never provided lethal weapons to any party to the conflict and exercised strict export control over dual-use articles. We absolutely reject the G7’s blame-shifting.\nChina is committed to peaceful development, follows a national defense policy that is defensive in nature and always keeps its nuclear strength at the minimum level required by national security. China’s national defense spending is made to safeguard our nation’s sovereignty, security and development interests and it is open, transparent, reasonable and appropriate. The G7 says nothing about the U.S.’s responsibility in disarmament and the risks of nuclear proliferation posed by AUKUS, and chooses to direct the issue at China instead. This is out-and-out double standards. The narrative of “Chinese overcapacity” has been proved false by facts. The G7 should stop politicizing and weaponizing trade and economic ties and stop undermining the international economic order and destabilizing global industrial and supply chains.\nWe call on the G7 to see the trend of history, discard the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop undermining China’s sovereignty and interfering in China’s internal affairs and stop stoking antagonism and bloc confrontation. They need to focus on major issues including addressing global challenges and promoting global development and do more things that are conducive to international solidarity and cooperation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250317_11577262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250317_11577237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-17","Mao Ning","Global Times","It was reported that recently, a Japanese Diet member submitted a letter of inquiry to the Japanese government, saying that the 1972 China-Japan Joint Statement contains the words that “The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this position of the…","There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. China firmly opposes official interaction of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-Japan relations.\nIn 1972, the Chinese and Japanese governments signed the China-Japan Joint Statement, in which the Japanese side explicitly pledged that “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this position of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its position under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation reiterates that the “terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” And the 1943 Cairo Declaration explicitly demands that “all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Manchuria, Formosa, and the Pescadores, shall be restored” to China. These documents not only confirm the fact that Taiwan belongs to China, but also constitute the legal basis for ending the state of war between the Allied Nations and Japan and building the post-war international order in the Asia-Pacific. They certainly are legally binding.\nIn 1978, China and Japan signed the Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, in which the two sides affirmed that the China-Japan Joint Statement “constitutes the basis for relations of peace and friendship between the two countries and that the principles set out in that statement should be strictly observed.” The treaty was signed by the Chinese and Japanese governments, and officially came into effect after deliberation and approval by the legislators of the two countries. It affirmed the principles and contents of the joint statement in legal terms and is certainly legally binding.\nTaiwan has been back under China’s sovereign jurisdiction for 80 years. The Japanese side attempted to obscure historical facts regarding the Taiwan question, which severely misleads the Japanese people, violates the Japanese government’s promise of adhering to the one-China principle, challenges the political foundation of China-Japan relations and sends a significantly wrong message to the “Taiwan independence” forces. We firmly oppose this. We seriously urge the Japanese side to abide by the principles and spirit of the four political documents with China, earnestly fulfill relevant legal obligations, act prudently on the Taiwan question and honor its promise of adhering to the one-China principle with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250317_11577262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250317_11577237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-17","Mao Ning","CCTV","Sources say that the Taiwan authorities are going to set foreign missions in a handful of countries or use the term “Taiwan” over “Taipei” in relevant institutions. What’s your comment?","The one-China principle is a well-recognized norm in international relations, a prevailing consensus in the international community and the political foundation for China to establish and grow its relations with other countries. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan is never a country, not in the past, and never in the future.\nFor quite some time, the DPP authorities have used exchange and cooperation in economy, trade, technology, culture, and education, among other fields, as a pretext to drill through the rock-solid international commitment to the one-China principle, and expand so-called “international space.” They have coerced or cajoled other countries through dollar diplomacy and bribes to set new institutions or rename existing ones in some countries, tempt them to cross, trample on or make moves on the margins of the red line of the Taiwan question, and destroy their relations with China. Our message to the DPP authorities is that China’s reunification cannot be hindered, and relying on external forces for independence cannot succeed.\nChina has all along opposed official interaction of any form between the Taiwan authorities and countries that have diplomatic relations with China. We hope relevant countries will see through the Taiwan authorities’ ill-intentioned schemes, abide by the one-China principle with concrete actions, and uphold the political foundation of their relations with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250317_11577262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250317_11577237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-17","Mao Ning","China Daily","We have learned that the Chinese military has conducted drills near the Taiwan Strait. Some believe this has something to do with the U.S. State Department’s recent revisions to the statements on its Taiwan policy on its website and “Taiwan independence” forces’ unconscionable acts. What’s China’s comment?","The U.S. has recently taken a series of wrong steps on the Taiwan question. In particular, the U.S. State Department removed important statements that show the U.S. is committed to the one-China policy and does not support “Taiwan independence” in the fact sheet of its so-called relations with Taiwan on the website, which shows the U.S. gravely backpedaled on its position on Taiwan-related issues. This is another egregious example of the U.S.’s intention of using Taiwan to contain China, and its move to abet and aid “Taiwan independence”, which sends a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China’s relevant military operation is necessary, lawful and legitimate in order to defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. It’s a firm response to external forces who are hellbent on abetting and aiding “Taiwan independence”, and a warning to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces’ unconscionable acts.\nLet me stress that the Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests and the one-China principle is the bedrock of the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. If the foundation is shaken, whatever above it cannot stand. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. The pursuit of “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere. Those who attempt to use Taiwan to contain China will get burned for playing with fire. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, honor the solemn commitment made by U.S. administrations on the Taiwan question, stop crossing the line and making provocations, handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence, and avoid further severe damage to China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250317_11577262.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250317_11577237.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-17","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华17日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 17 (dateline): Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions on the 17th and said: Unification is the historical trend and the right path; “Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. The Taiwan Information, Communications and Electronics Force (ICEF), which “relies on the internet to seek…","Chen Binhua said that in September 2024, the national security organs, in order to safeguard national security and stability in the Taiwan Strait, publicly released the article “Exposing the ‘Taiwan Independence’ Cyber Army ‘Anonymous 64’,” which effectively exposed and criticized the various despicable tactics of Taiwan's cyber-electronic warfare forces and issued a warning and deterrence. However, under the instigation and connivance of the DPP authorities, Taiwan's cyber-electronic warfare forces have shown no remorse and have repeated their old tricks. Willing to serve as the lackeys of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, they continue to carry out cyberattacks and infiltration against the mainland by every means, going further and further down the wrong path and sinking deeper and deeper.\nChen Binhua said that he hopes Taiwan compatriots will recognize the sinister intentions and grave harm of the DPP authorities' stubborn insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, their constant provocations in pursuit of independence, and their escalation of hostility and confrontation across the Strait. He hopes they will firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, earnestly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being, and work together with compatriots on the mainland to create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250317_12690601.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-17","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华17日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 17 dispatch: Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions on March 17 and said that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's sacred territory. The PLA's exercises near Taiwan are a resolute punishment for Lai Ching-te's continued promotion of the “Taiwan independence”…","Chen Binhua pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Since Lai Ching-te came to power, he has obstinately held to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. He has repeatedly advocated the “new two-state theory” of “mutual non-subordination,” intensified restrictions on and obstruction of cross-strait exchanges, and forcibly pushed for cross-strait “decoupling and severing of links.” At the same time, he has accelerated collusion with external forces to “sell out Taiwan and beg for help,” attempting to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on foreign powers.” His conduct seriously provokes the one-China principle, seriously undermines cross-strait relations, continuously pushes Taiwan toward the perilous situation of war and calamity, and seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. In response, we will not tolerate or appease it, and we will resolutely take counter-measures and punishment.\nChen Binhua stressed that the Taiwan question concerns national dignity and the national sentiment. It is the core of China's core interests and an inviolable red line. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: if you dare to provoke and play with fire, you will only bring about your own destruction and be smashed to pieces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250317_12690603.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-03-19","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","It’s reported that during his visit to the U.S. in February, Japanese Prime Minister Shigeru Ishiba jointly announced with U.S. President Donald Trump that the U.S. and Japan will oppose any attempts by the Chinese government to unilaterally change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait by force or coercion. Also early in February, a Japanese Maritime Self-Defense Force vessel sailed through the Taiwan Strait.…","Foreign Minister Wang Yi will travel to Japan to attend the 11th China-Japan-ROK Trilateral Foreign Ministers’ Meeting and co-chair the Sixth China-Japan High-Level Economic Dialogue. We made the announcement and shared relevant information yesterday, which you may refer to.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no external inference. Japan bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people for its colonial rule over Taiwan. It must act with extra prudence on this issue. As for the China-related negative moves of Japan you mentioned, China lodged serious protests with Japan immediately after those moves.\nThe China-Japan relationship is at a crucial juncture for improvement and development. We hope Japan will act on its pledges of comprehensively advancing the China-Japan strategic relationship of mutual benefit and building a constructive and stable China-Japan relationship fit for the new era, and we hope it will remove obstacles against the improvement and development of the bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250319_11578652.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250319_11578554.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-20","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华20日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, March 20 – Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered a reporter's question on the 20th, saying that over the years, the immigration management departments of public security authorities have introduced a series of policy measures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots in obtaining documents and passing through customs, and to facilitate the…","Chen Binhua pointed out that recently, the DPP authorities have constantly confused public perception, attempting to conflate the Taiwan Residence Permit with the Mainland Resident Identity Card, misleading and intimidating the Taiwan people. We solemnly clarify that the Taiwan Residence Permit and the Mainland Resident Identity Card are two completely different types of documents. The Taiwan Residence Permit is a document introduced to meet the needs of Taiwan compatriots for study, entrepreneurship, employment, and daily life on the mainland, serving as a proof of Taiwan compatriot identity. Taiwan compatriots applying for the Taiwan Residence Permit do not need to hold mainland household registration or give up their Taiwan household registration, and the relevant rights and obligations they enjoy in Taiwan should not be affected.\nHe said that since the introduction of the Taiwan Residence Permit, it has been widely welcomed by Taiwan compatriots, and permit holders have enjoyed great convenience in study, entrepreneurship, employment, and daily life on the mainland. All relevant departments on the mainland have consistently followed the requirements of relevant laws and regulations, strictly protecting the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots who hold the permit, so that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots can use it with peace of mind.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250320_12691200.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-03-21","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","According to reports, Taiwan’s “Legislative Yuan” appointed Iwasaki Shigeru, the former chief of the Joint Staff of Japan’s Self-Defense Forces, as a consultant. What’s your comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-Japan relations. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. Japan bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people over the Taiwan question and should act with extra prudence and honor its promise of adhering to the one-China principle with concrete actions. We’ve lodged protests with the Japanese side. The DPP authorities’ separatist provocations with foreign support are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250321_11579916.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250321_11579804.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-24","Guo Jiakun","China Review News","According to what has been released by China’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs, while he was in Japan, Foreign Minister Wang Yi talked about the Taiwan question with Japanese political figures. He stressed that the four political documents between China and Japan have made clear provisions on the Taiwan question, which must be strictly implemented without ambiguity or backsliding. Can you further brief us on China’s…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interest, and bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and basic trust between the two countries.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the recovery of Taiwan. Japan undeniably bears historical responsibilities on the Taiwan question. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the U.S. and the UK in 1943 stated in explicit terms that Taiwan is a territory that Japan had stolen from the Chinese, and shall be restored to China. Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation jointly issued by China, the U.S., the UK and the Soviet Union in 1945 stipulates that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. On August 15, 1945, Japan accepted the Potsdam Proclamation and announced unconditional surrender. Later in 1972, Japan pledged in the China-Japan Joint Statement that it firmly maintains its position under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation. The Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan signed in 1978 clearly stated that the principles set out in the statement should be strictly observed. The treaty was deliberated and approved by the legislators of the two countries, and together with the China-Japan Joint Statement, constitute legally binding documents that provide guidance for the bilateral ties. The above-mentioned historical evidence and legal basis fully show that abiding by the one-China principle is the serious political commitment and obligation under international law that Japan must follow.\nThe false narrative, including “a Taiwan emergency is a Japanese emergency” and “the China-Japan Joint Statement is not legally binding”, will gravely erode the political foundation of China-Japan relations. Such narrative is not only wrong, but also very dangerous. We urge Japan to deliver on its commitment, handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence and take concrete actions to maintain the momentum of improvement and development in China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250324_11580922.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250324_11580936.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-26","Guo Jiakun","AFP","A Chinese influencer Liu Zhenya left Taiwan yesterday after her residency permit was revoked for advocating that China should unify Taiwan by military means. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","I didn’t notice relevant reports. Let me stress that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250326_11582391.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250326_11582373.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-03-26","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","A report by the U.S. intelligence agencies published yesterday said China remains the top military and cyber threat to the U.S. This report said Beijing was making “steady but uneven” progress on capabilities it could use to capture Taiwan. What comment does the Ministry have on this?","The U.S. issues irresponsible and biased reports like this year after year, seeks to promote the false “China threat” narrative and fans up major-country rivalry, so that there could be an excuse to suppress China and perpetuate U.S. supremacy.\nChina’s development has a long historic thread and is robust and self-driven. Our goal is very clear and there’s nothing to hide about it: we strive to make sure that the Chinese people can lead a better life and China can contribute more to the world we live in. We have no intention to surpass or supplant anyone.\nThe Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. Nothing will deter China from rejecting “Taiwan independence” and defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No one shall underestimate or miscalculate China’s resolve.\nAs the saying goes, “To a man with a hammer, everything looks like a nail.” China is not a mirror image of the hegemonic U.S. The U.S. needs to stop viewing its ties with China from the outdated Cold War perspective, stop containing China in the name of “strategic competition”, and stop aiding or abetting “Taiwan independence” in any form. The U.S. should stop falsely picturing China as a threat and work with China for a steady, sound and sustainable China-U.S. relationship.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250326_11582391.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250326_11582373.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear reporters, welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","A symposium marking the 20th anniversary of the Anti-Secession Law was held in Beijing not long ago, drawing high attention on the island. Some public opinion on the island holds that the mainland has its own pace in opposing “Taiwan independence” and punishing secession, and is paying attention to the mainland's emphasis on using the law to punish “Taiwan independence” and secession. What is your comment?","The practice over the 20 years since the implementation of the Anti-Secession Law fully proves that this important law has significant practical effect and far-reaching historical impact. It has deterred 'Taiwan independence' separatism, contained external interference, safeguarded national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maintained peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoted the development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification, and protected the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nThe Anti-Secession Law clearly stipulates: \"'Taiwan independence' separatist forces, under any name or by any means, cause the fact of Taiwan's secession from China, or a major incident entailing Taiwan's secession from China occurs, or the possibilities for peaceful reunification are completely exhausted, the state may employ non-peaceful means and other necessary measures to protect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity.\" This draws an impassable red line for 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces. We will continue to earnestly implement the Anti-Secession Law, continuously enrich and improve the institutional system of 'punishing independence according to law,' resolutely defeat all manner of 'Taiwan independence' separatist and external interference schemes, firmly safeguard our common home as the Chinese nation, comprehensively advance the great cause of building a strong country and national rejuvenation, and steadily advance the great cause of national reunification.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692204.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Some island public opinion points out that Lai Ching-te has defined the mainland as a “hostile foreign force” and put forward so-called “17 strategies,” which amounts to “martial law returning, ‘Taiwan independence’ challenges,” and “green terror rule.” What is your comment on this? How will the mainland respond to Lai’s remarks?","Since 1949, we have united Taiwan compatriots and promoted the Taiwan Strait situation from tense confrontation to easing and improvement, and then onto the path of peaceful development. Cross-strait relations have continuously achieved breakthrough progress. These achievements were hard won and are extremely precious. Lai Ching-te has spoken recklessly, defining the mainland as a “hostile foreign force” and equating cross-strait relations with a “hostile relationship.” This is turning back the wheel of history, provocatively challenging the mainland side, and aggravating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. It fully confirms that he is a “destroyer of cross-strait peace” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nThe “17 strategies” that Lai Ching-te put forward against the will of the people have thoroughly exposed the ugly face of anti-peace, anti-exchange, anti-democracy, and anti-humanity. What he says and does is intended to incite “anti-China and resistance to China,” to obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and to create “terror politics and green dictatorship” on the island.\nUnification is the trend of history and the right path. “Taiwan independence” is a reverse current of history and a dead end. We will never tolerate or appease any act that harms the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, undermines the development of cross-strait relations, or endangers peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We must resolutely counter and severely punish such acts. We believe that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots can recognize the serious harm that Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities have inflicted on Taiwan and its people. Starting from safeguarding their own rights and interests and peace in the Taiwan Strait, they will struggle against the reactionary actions of the Lai Ching-te authorities and prevent their schemes from succeeding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692203.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","We noted that this morning (the 26th), the website of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council added a \"Column for Reporting Vile Acts by 'Taiwan Independence' Thugs and Accomplices Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots\" to its special page \"Punishing 'Taiwan Independence' Diehards in Accordance with the Law.\" May I ask what considerations lie behind this?","Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have frequently fabricated charges to suppress different opinions on the island, stifled freedom of speech, and threatened, intimidated, and persecuted political opponents as well as political parties, groups and individuals on the island that support the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. Certain “Taiwan independence” organizations, “Taiwan independence” diehards, public officials and wing internet celebrities act as henchmen and accomplices, aiding and abetting in wrongdoing. We are gravely concerned about this and it must be severely punished.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council's government website today launched the “Special Column for Reporting Egregious Acts by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Henchmen and Accomplices Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots,” precisely to hold accountable the above egregious acts and the principal culprits. Those who have been persecuted or who are aware of relevant leads are welcome to send information to the reporting mailbox jubao@suremail.cn. We will handle these matters appropriately, expose them at an appropriate time, hold criminals with conclusive evidence and grave offenses accountable according to law, and at the same time strictly protect the information and rights and interests of whistleblowers in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692202.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","环球网记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te and the DPP have promoted the so-called “national security reform,” declaring that they will amend multiple laws, including the so-called “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area,” the “Hong Kong and Macau Relations Act” and the “Anti-Infiltration Act.” They have also urged other parties to stop being “agents of the Chinese Communist Party” and…","Lai Ching-te's authorities are scheming to amend these \"laws\" precisely to open the door for further implementing \"green terror\" on the island. This would allow them to commit evil acts by relying on evil laws, escalate their persecution of political opponents, incite \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, and restrict and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, as well as exchanges between Taiwan and Hong Kong and Macao. Lai Ching-te is vigorously pursuing \"green authoritarianism\" and \"Taiwan independence dictatorship,\" which seriously violates the trend of history and the mainstream public opinion on the island. It will inevitably meet opposition and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692201.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","On the first question: at the Yushan Forum, Lai Qingde recently said that Taiwan would work with its democratic partners to strengthen the “non-red supply chain,” and that Taiwan's industries would “be rooted in Taiwan, deployed globally, and marketed to the whole world.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this? On the second question: this year, Taiwan's military's “Han Kuang Exercise,” using a…","Regarding the first question, the economies on both sides of the Strait each have their own characteristics and complementary advantages. Cooperation in cross-Strait industrial and supply chains is a natural outcome of economic development. It is a cooperation system formed by enterprises on both sides making independent choices and optimizing allocation based on market rules, which is conducive to the development of enterprises on both sides and to improving the livelihood and well-being of compatriots on both sides. If this supply chain can be said to have any color, then benefiting Taiwan and benefiting its people is its basic color.\nLai Ching-te violates economic and market laws, catering to external forces to pursue a so-called “non-red supply chain.” The aim is to revive the old tune of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” and in essence, by selling off Taiwan's advantageous industries, sacrificing Taiwan's development prospects, and smashing the “rice bowls” of Taiwan's people, to obtain external forces' support for his pursuit of “independence.” Economic ties across the Strait cannot be decoupled and supply chains cannot be severed. Lai Ching-te's forcible manipulation of “decoupling and severing of chains” will only cause a boomerang that hits Taiwan's own industries, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan's enterprises and people will be harmed. Selling out Taiwan for the sake of “independence” will only harm and ruin Taiwan.\nRegarding the second question, no matter how the Democratic Progressive Party authorities posture and bluster, they are a “hollow show” that merely changes the packaging while keeping the same contents, and they are a “flower frame” that cannot withstand a single blow. The People's Liberation Army has the firm will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Any scheme to “use force to seek independence” or “rely on outsiders to seek independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692200.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Shen Yu-chung, Deputy Minister of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, said that \"the mainland must bear the main responsibility for obstacles and risks in cross-Strait exchanges,\" and that for the mainland \"not unification means independence,\" which has led to obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and rising risks. What is your response to this?","This argument completely reverses right and wrong and confuses truth with falsehood. As everyone knows, the Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. For the sake of their own party and personal interests, they repeatedly use various pretexts to create “green terror” on the island, going to every length to restrict and obstruct cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and scheming to “decouple, break chains, and reduce flows” across the Strait. In recent times, from deliberately obstructing cross-strait personnel exchanges and the resumption of tourism, to suppressing and persecuting island groups and individuals that support and participate in cross-strait exchanges, to restricting and intimidating Taiwan compatriots from applying for mainland documents, and prohibiting exchanges and cooperation with some mainland universities, their record is even more replete with wrongdoing and they grow ever more extreme. The facts fully prove that the Lai Ching-te authorities are the greatest obstacle to cross-strait exchanges and interactions and the greatest source of risk to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Green mountains cannot hide it; in the end the waters flow east.” No matter what interference and obstruction they encounter, exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait cannot stop, cannot be cut off, cannot be reduced, and will not stop, will not be cut off, and will not be reduced. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will work with us, remove interference, break down obstacles, promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, advance cross-strait relations, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692199.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广记者","The launch event for the new book “Taiwan Question Cadre Reader” was recently held in Beijing. Liang Wen-chieh, deputy head of the Mainland Affairs Council, said, “After the new book is released, we will try to study it.” He said most of the reader's content is “the CPC's existing policies and positions toward Taiwan,” and that as long as “the CPC authorities continue to exert compound pressure on Taiwan” and…","The revised *Cadre Reader on the Taiwan Question* devotes a special chapter for the first time to systematically explaining the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. It also adds content on the development of cross-strait relations and key events since 2014, as well as important measures in Taiwan work. It has been released for public sale both online and offline.\nWe welcome Taiwan compatriots to pay attention to and read this new book, to fully understand the historical course of the Taiwan question and the glorious process by which the Communist Party of China has led the people in advancing national reunification, to understand the mainland’s major policies toward Taiwan, and to actively take part in cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. Work with us to promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After TSMC Chairman C.C. Wei announced increased investment in the United States, US President Donald Trump once again “raised” the investment amount. Regarding questions on the island about TSMC “moving out en masse,” the DPP authorities said they are “optimistic about its outcome.” What comments do you have on this?","Under the DPP authorities’ eager accommodation and handing it over, TSMC has become a fat piece of meat on the chopping block, to be carved up at will. That they can “welcome with optimism” the transformation of TSMC into “AmeriTSMC” shows that in the eyes of the DPP, there is only the narrow interest of one party and one person. They do not care in the slightest about the well-being of Taiwan compatriots or the interests of the industry. In order to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” they will only go further and further down the road of “selling out Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan.” What Taiwan’s industry and public have lost is not only today’s jobs, but also future development opportunities. It is only natural that island society questions and is full of worry about Lai Ching-te, a “professional Taiwan-seller,” who abuses power and acts recklessly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692198.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, two new measures facilitating residents of Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan were officially implemented. Please, spokesperson, introduce the relevant information. We understand that Taiwan compatriots have already handled relevant business in Xiamen, and they evaluated the “dual-certificate linkage” as providing great convenience to Taiwan compatriots, with an excellent experience. Some Taiwan compatriots…","On March 20, immigration and exit-entry management departments of public security organs officially released two policy measures facilitating Taiwan compatriots, namely \"dual-certificate linkage\" and the electronic Taiwan Resident Temporary Travel Permit. These have brought convenience to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots and have been warmly welcomed by them. As you put it, this is the best gift for Taiwan compatriots during the Spring Equinox season. As long as something helps enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, we will persist in doing it, making good things happen and making real things work well. We will continue to uphold the concept that \"cross-Strait compatriots are one family,\" continuously improve the systems and policies under which Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal treatment, provide better and more convenient conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, find employment, start businesses and live on the mainland, create a more comfortable and considerate environment, and let the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots feel the benefits, have access to them, and feel secure and reassured.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692196.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The Taiwan MAC recently commissioned scholars to produce a so-called “report” claiming that the Mainland's statement that the Taiwan Strait is not international waters is aimed at “confusing public perception and opposing US freedom of navigation.” It further claims that, recently, through amendments to laws, law enforcement, and PLA actions, the Mainland intends to “internalize the Taiwan Strait” in order to…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese territory, and China holds sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. Under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and China's domestic law, the waters of the Taiwan Strait are respectively China's internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone and exclusive economic zone, and there is no so-called “international waters.” In fact, international maritime law has no concept of “international waters” at all. China respects the right of navigation that countries enjoy in the relevant waters of the Taiwan Strait in accordance with Chinese law and international law, including the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, but firmly opposes illegal activities by certain countries that provoke and endanger China's sovereignty and security in the name of “freedom of navigation.”\nIn order to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” the Lai Ching-te authorities have abandoned their ancestors, become slaves to foreigners, and are willing to sell out national interests. They fabricate so-called “reports” that ignore the facts in order to cater to the fallacious arguments of the United States and cooperate with external forces' hype. This is disgraceful, and in the end it will be in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Taiwanese media reported that Taiwan's tourism deficit keeps worsening: in 2024, the island's total passenger trip deficit was 8.992 million trips, and the tourism output deficit was about NT$692.2 billion. Meanwhile, the DPP authorities' obstruction of restoring cross-Strait tourism has made the industry on the island even more miserable. What is your comment?","We have consistently upheld the concept of “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” actively promoted cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and the goodwill and sincerity we have shown are plain for all to see. In 2023 we announced the resumption of group tours to the mainland for Taiwan residents, and Taiwan residents may freely travel to the mainland. In 2024 we made arrangements for mainland residents to travel to Matsu and Kinmen and for group tours to the island. This January we announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai. By contrast, the DPP authorities have repeatedly obstructed, restricted and set up barriers to cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields. This is the root cause of Taiwan's tourism industry turning into a “tourism disaster.” We deeply sympathize with the predicament of Taiwan's tourism industry and related grassroots residents, and we understand their voices and appeals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The head of Taiwan's education authority recently said that when island primary and secondary schools carry out exchange activities, priority is given to schools in Europe, the U.S., Northeast Asia and so on, and regarding cross-Strait exchanges, they “avoid them if possible.” The head of Taiwan's labor authority said that it is necessary to prevent the mainland from carrying out “united front infiltration”…","These remarks show that the DPP authorities “oppose everything China does,” and that their pursuit of “independence” has reached a point of losing reason and resorting to any means to obstruct and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.\nWe have consistently upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and we have actively promoted exchanges and cooperation in all fields and personnel exchanges across the Strait. By contrast, the DPP authorities, clinging to “opposing China and resisting China,” constantly hype up so-called “united front infiltration threats.” In essence, they fear that compatriots on both sides will grow closer and visit each other often, and they worry that Taiwan’s public will thereby come to understand the real mainland and expose the “information cocoons” they have carefully fabricated. We want peace, development, exchange, and cooperation; these are the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides and the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society. Any scheme running counter to them is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692197.htm"],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Sacrificing to ancestors during Qingming is a Chinese tradition passed down by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation of compatriots from both sides jointly worshipping ancestors in Shaanxi, Henan, and other places during this year’s Qingming Festival.","On the morning of April 4 (Qingming Festival), the “Yisi (2025) Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi,” jointly hosted by the Shaanxi Provincial People's Government, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, and the All-China Returned Overseas Chinese Federation, will be solemnly held at the Mausoleum of the Yellow Emperor in Huangling County, Yan'an City, Shaanxi Province. During the period, activities including the “Taiwan Compatriots' Roots-Seeking Trip to Shaanxi” and the “Cross-Strait Cultural and Art Exhibition” will be held.\nOn March 31, the “Yisi Year Yellow Emperor Hometown Ancestor Worship Grand Ceremony,” jointly hosted by the Henan Provincial People's Government, the CPPCC Henan Provincial Committee, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the All-China Returned Overseas Chinese Federation, the All-China Taiwan Compatriots Association, and the China Yanhuang Culture Research Association, will be held in Xinzheng, Zhengzhou, Henan. During the period, activities including the “Taiwan Kunpeng Elite Association Central Plains Cultural Study Trip” and the “Yellow Emperor Culture Forum” will be held.\nXuanyuan Huangdi is the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation, and the Mausoleum of the Yellow Emperor is the spiritual emblem of Chinese civilization. Compatriots from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait jointly worship Xuanyuan Huangdi, a tradition with a long history. This is of great significance for inheriting and promoting excellent traditional Chinese culture and for strengthening Taiwan compatriots' sense of national identity, belonging, and honor.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","What is the main purpose of the mainland's military exercises held near the Taiwan Strait in recent years? Is it possible that a military blockade could become a strategic option in resolving the Taiwan question?","The DPP authorities and the “Taiwan independence” forces, in collusion with external forces to plot independence and provoke, are the root cause of the tension in the Taiwan Strait. We have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly advance the great cause of national reunification. The PLA’s military exercises around Taiwan Island are a deterrent and punishment against “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and foreign interference. They are a necessary and righteous measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","According to reports, the first prefabricated pier and abutment of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Xiamen section) project was recently hoisted into place, marking the project’s entry into a new stage. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is a shared call and a pressing wish of the people of Xiamen and Kinmen. We have always kept the interests and well-being of the Kinmen people in our hearts. In recent years, we have implemented a number of measures that benefit Kinmen residents, including supplying water to Kinmen and further relaxing the limits on the quantity of Taiwan kaoliang liquor that passengers may carry on direct “Small Three Links” routes between coastal Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu. From the 21st to the 23rd of this month, as Fujian marks the 30th anniversary of its formal commitment to “Kinmen-Matsu water supply,” Jinjiang City in Fujian Province is holding a series of events under the theme “Drinking From the Same River, Discussing Cross-Strait Ties Together,” to review the course and achievements of Fujian's water supply to Kinmen. Since water supply to Kinmen began in August 2018, Fujian has supplied a cumulative total of more than 40 million tonnes of water to Kinmen, solving the water shortage problem for Kinmen compatriots.\nThe “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring New Paths for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” issued in 2023, clearly proposes to “explore a model for jointly building infrastructure across Xiamen and Kinmen, and accelerate the progress of electricity, gas, and bridge connections with Kinmen.” Like the people of Kinmen, we eagerly look forward to the early realization of the “New Three Links” and are steadily advancing the relevant work.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The Mainland spouse “Yaya,” who was determined to have incited “armed unification,” had her residency status in Taiwan under family reunification revoked by the DPP authorities, and was ordered to leave within a deadline. She was forced to leave Taiwan yesterday and separated from her three children. Two other Mainland spouses will also be ordered to leave within a deadline for the same reason. What comment does…","First question. Cross-Strait marriage groups are a vivid portrayal of “both sides of the Strait being one family,” and mainland spouses are family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities boast of “freedom, rule of law, and human rights,” yet they repeatedly abuse judicial means to bully cross-Strait marriage groups, forcing these families apart. This goes against human relations and is heartless and inhumane.\nSecond question. We will properly handle the relevant reported information and ascertain the facts and evidence. For those with conclusive evidence and of a vile nature, we will expose them at an appropriate time, and, in accordance with relevant laws, hold these henchmen and accomplices legally accountable, with lifelong accountability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The “Special Column for Reporting Vicious Acts by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Thugs and Accomplices in Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots” mentions “certain ‘Taiwan independence’ organizations, ‘Taiwan independence’ elements, public officials and wing internet celebrities acting as thugs.” Have the “specific individuals” in Taiwan been identified? What specific measures will be taken in the future? Second…","As for the first question, I have already answered it. Watch and see.\nAs for the second question, we are not aware of the specific circumstances of the case you mentioned. We care about the living and working conditions of all Taiwan compatriots who work, live, start businesses, and study on the mainland, and we welcome and support the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots in participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields. We will continue to create convenient conditions and provide quality services for Taiwan compatriots to live, find employment, and start businesses on the mainland, and will safeguard the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises should also abide by the laws and regulations of the mainland and operate in accordance with the law.\nSince the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” the cross-Strait consultation and communication mechanism between the two associations has long been suspended, as is well known. The so-called “SEF's written inquiry answered by the ARATS by phone” is pure fabrication. The DPP authorities should stop fabricating false information to deceive the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","Following the DPP authorities' recent investigation into public officials who obtained mainland ID cards, MAC Minister Chiu Chui-cheng recently further stated that they will investigate whether Taiwanese entertainers who develop their careers in the mainland hold mainland ID cards. If they do, their Taiwan identities will be cancelled, and they will no longer be allowed to use a Taiwan identity to carry out…","The DPP authorities have repeatedly trumpeted the investigation of Taiwan compatriots holding relevant certificates from the mainland. Their purpose is to create a “green terror,” obstruct and sabotage compatriots on both sides from drawing closer to each other, and continue to deceive the public on the island and pursue “Taiwan independence” behind closed doors. Sima Zhao's intentions are obvious to every passerby. Such perverse conduct has already met with strong dissatisfaction and resolute opposition from a growing number of people on the island.\nI must emphasize once again that all relevant mainland departments have always strictly protected the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots holding certificates in accordance with relevant laws and regulations. Taiwan compatriots can use them with peace of mind.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that certain U.S. lawmakers recently drafted the so-called “Taiwan Support Act,” which proposes that in official communications and documents between the U.S. and Taiwan, “Taiwan” replace “Chinese Taipei.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. Some American politicians keep putting forward Taiwan-related bills that violate the US government's one-China policy and contain negative content. They seek personal political gain and harm China's core interests. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop sending any wrong signals that condone or support the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Any scheme to play the “Taiwan card” or pursue “using Taiwan to contain China” will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","According to reports, a police officer in Taoyuan City was investigated and held accountable by his police precinct because his Douyin account avatar bore the words “I love my country” and his bio said “I am Chinese.” A principal in Taoyuan City was also exposed by DPP personnel for posting videos on Douyin saying “I love you, China” and “Cross-Strait is one family.” The Taoyuan Education Bureau said it will…","This is an unadulterated contemporary “literary inquisition,” and another vile act by the Lai Ching-te authorities, who are vigorously carrying out “green terror” and creating a “chilling effect.” It is a brutal deprivation of the basic rights and freedoms of Taiwan residents. The Lai Ching-te authorities routinely resort to threats, intimidation, and retaliation, attempting to restrict the freedom of thought and freedom of speech of Taiwan compatriots, and to let the world see through the hypocrisy of the so-called “democracy” they advertise.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","The South African Department of International Relations and Cooperation website recently renamed the “Taipei Liaison Representative Office” in South Africa as the “Taipei Business Office.” In response, Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities protested “South Africa's practice of cooperating with China to suppress Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","The practice of the South African government shows that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and that adhering to the one-China principle is where righteousness lies and the trend of the times. We appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan's defense department recently stated that, in response to the PLA's “gray-zone harassment” around Taiwan, the Taiwan military carried out a five-day “immediate combat readiness drill.” It also said that on the 17th, dozens of PLA aircraft sorties crossed the “median line of the Taiwan Strait” into Taiwan's airspace, in coordination with warships conducting “joint combat readiness patrols.” What is your…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and there is no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” The PLA's exercises near Taiwan Island are a resolute punishment of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities for their continuous promotion of “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies and their escalation of confrontation between the two sides; they are a powerful deterrent against the provocations of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces seeking “independence,” and a necessary step to defend national sovereignty and maintain peace in the Taiwan Strait. Whether the Taiwan military calls its activities “drills” or “exercises,” they are all pretentious and overestimate their own capabilities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The joint statement by the Group of Seven (G7) foreign ministers, recently released, claims “opposition to any unilateral attempt to change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait by force or coercion,” and supports Taiwan’s participation in international organizations. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities said they “highly welcome and sincerely thank” it. What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose certain countries making irresponsible remarks about the Taiwan question in so-called “statements” and brazenly interfering in China’s internal affairs. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to provoke and seek “independence.” They are the disruptors of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of turmoil for peace and stability in the Strait. If relevant countries sincerely hope for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they should adhere to the one-China principle and support China’s peaceful reunification, rather than challenging the one-China principle and repeatedly stirring up trouble on the Taiwan question.\nAs for the question of the Taiwan region of China participating in international organizations, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","Taiwan's “representative to the United States” recently said in an interview that, in responding to defense matters concerning mainland China, Taiwan and the United States keep discussing which US-made weapons are most suitable to purchase. He also said that Taiwan is improving its military reserves and food supplies so that it can withstand any measures by the mainland to isolate Taiwan. What comment do you have?","We firmly oppose any form of U.S.-Taiwan military ties and strongly demand that the U.S. side stop arming Taiwan. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” scheming to “seek independence by relying on external forces” and “seek independence by force.” While squandering the hard-earned money of the people to buy weapons from the United States, they are also buying disaster. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how many weapons they buy from external forces, they cannot shake our resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification, and they cannot withstand our strong capability to crush the separatist schemes of “Taiwan independence” and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","日本广播协会记者","Reports say that last month, the Shanghai Intermediate People's Court publicly pronounced its verdict in the case of Lee Yen-ho, editor-in-chief of Taiwan's Bagi Culture. Please introduce the detailed content of the verdict.","The Shanghai No. 1 Intermediate People's Court publicly pronounced the first-instance judgment in the Li Yanhe case on February 17, 2025, in accordance with law, openly and fairly. After the pronouncement, the party concerned stated in court that they submitted to the law and admitted guilt, and did not file an appeal within the statutory appeal period. The relevant judgment has taken legal effect in accordance with law. As for the sentence, the party concerned and their family members are very clear about it. As a spokesperson, I would not have wanted to publicly discuss specific details. The DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped judicial cases and slandered the mainland's judicial system, which is entirely with ulterior motives.\nAs far as I understand, the Shanghai No. 1 Intermediate People's Court publicly pronounced the first-instance judgment on February 17, 2025, sentencing Li Yanhe to three years' imprisonment for the crime of inciting secession of the state, deprivation of political rights for one year, and a concurrent confiscation of personal property of RMB 50,000. During the enforcement of the penalty, the relevant parties will protect the rights and interests of the party concerned and their family members in accordance with law.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202503/t20250326_12692186.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-03-26","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","BEIJING, March 26 (Xinhua) -- Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua responded to questions on March 26 that, after the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council's government website launched the “Special Column for Reporting Vile Acts by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Thugs and Accomplices Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots” at 8 a.m. that day, it attracted great attention and reports came in eagerly. As of 5 p.m.…","Chen Binhua said that we will further verify the relevant reported information, adhere to facts as the basis and law as the criterion, and hold these thugs and accomplices accountable in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202503/t20250326_12692209.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan region leader Lai Ching-te recently promoted the separatist fallacy that the two sides are “not subordinate to each other,” and defined the mainland as a “hostile foreign force.” In mid-March, the PLA conducted military exercises near the Taiwan Strait. Some commentators say this is a countermeasure against Lai’s “Taiwan independence” separatist remarks and the recent collusion between Taiwan and the…","Heaven wants it to perish, so it first drives it mad. Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country, not in the past, not now, and never will be in the future.\nRecently, the Eastern Theater Command of the Chinese People’s Liberation Army organized sea and air forces around the Taiwan Strait area to conduct combat readiness patrols and joint exercises, testing and improving the troops’ ability to fight. This is a forceful deterrent against “Taiwan independence” elements and a stern warning to external interfering forces, entirely justified and entirely necessary.\nThe People’s Liberation Army will firmly implement the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question: be on alert at all times, ready to fight at any moment, and certain of victory in battle, and resolutely crush all schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism!","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first: according to reports, the Fujian aircraft carrier recently departed port to begin its seventh sea trial. Some analysts say the focus of this trial may be catapult takeoff and arrested landing tests for carrier-based aircraft. Can you confirm this?\nThe second: according to reports, in response to China’s 2025 defense budget increase, Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary recently said…","Regarding the first question, I currently have no information to release. However, it should be noted that the Fujian aircraft carrier's sea trials are a normal arrangement in the construction process, so everyone should keep a calm mind.\nRegarding the second question, on China's national defense expenditure for 2025, China has already given a detailed explanation. Its scale, structure, and purpose are open and transparent and beyond reproach. In fact, Japan, as a country that launched wars of aggression during World War II, is the least qualified to point fingers at other countries' defense spending. What the international community should be highly vigilant about is that in recent years Japan has repeatedly breached the constraints of its “pacifist constitution” and its commitment to an “exclusively defense-oriented policy,” greatly increased its defense spending, developed long-range offensive capabilities, and gone further and further down the road of military expansion. This is what deserves high vigilance and joint opposition from the world, especially from countries that love peace and from those that once suffered Japanese militarist aggression. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. We urge the Japanese side to learn from history, be cautious in its words and deeds in the military and security field, and stop distorting the interpretation of China's defense policy and military strategy, so as not to further lose the trust of Asian neighbors and the international community. It must be stressed that the Taiwan question has nothing to do with Japan, and Japan is the least qualified to bring up Taiwan. Only by adhering to the one-China principle and resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be guaranteed.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to foreign media reports, the Group of Seven (G7) recently held a foreign ministers' meeting and issued a joint statement saying that the G7 is concerned about China's expansion of its nuclear arsenal, expresses serious concern over the situation in the East China Sea and South China Sea, emphasizes that maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is very important, and opposes unilaterally…","The Group of Seven, disregarding the facts and maliciously slandering China, has crudely interfered in China's internal affairs. We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose this. China adheres to a policy of no-first-use of nuclear weapons and a self-defensive nuclear strategy, and has always kept its nuclear forces at the minimum level required for national security. In the nuclear domain, the Group of Seven should earnestly engage in self-reflection; it has no qualification whatsoever to lecture China.\nOn the issues of the East China Sea and the South China Sea, China is working with the countries concerned to peacefully resolve disputes through dialogue and consultation, while firmly safeguarding its own territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and resolutely opposing provocations and troublemaking by external countries that undermine regional peace and stability. Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question brooks no foreign interference. The one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations, and any force that attempts to separate Taiwan from the motherland will surely be utterly defeated.\nWe urge the Group of Seven to abandon Cold War mentalities and ideological prejudices, stop pointing fingers at the affairs of other countries, and stop always wanting to play the role of “schoolmaster.” The Chinese military has never put up with such things.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Ministry of State Security recently publicly disclosed information on four Taiwan cyber, communications, and electronic warfare personnel. What is your comment?","Heaven’s net is vast; its meshes are wide, yet nothing escapes. If you want to play with fire, don’t think you can get away. Any “Taiwan independence” diehard who engages in acts to split the country will not escape severe punishment under domestic law, not a single one.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first: media reports say the PLA is building at least three barges that can be used to land on Taiwan. These barges are equipped with bridges more than 100 meters long that can span the beach to let tanks drive ashore. Can the spokesperson confirm this? The second: on the 21st of this month, Lai Ching-te, leader of the Taiwan region, announced that soldiers’ salaries would be increased…","Regarding the first question on weapons and equipment, I have no information to release.\nRegarding the second question, any “armed resistance to unification” gimmicks by the DPP authorities are nothing more than an egg hitting a stone. They cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified. The People's Liberation Army has more than enough capability to reduce to ashes any forces that “plot independence and resist unification.”","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command recently said that the mainland’s drills around Taiwan are a “rehearsal for invading Taiwan,” and that the current focus of US forces will be on the Indo-Pacific region. The DPP side in Taiwan interprets that the mainland’s military training may shift from exercises to actual war. Taiwan recently held its first “Small Han Kuang” exercise to improve its military’s…","The PLA’s related exercises and training are aimed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and the interference of external forces. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no foreign interference is permitted. The relevant actions of the PLA Eastern Theater Command around the Taiwan island enhance its real combat capability for counter-separatism and counter-interference. They are necessary actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and they are also a powerful deterrent against the reckless actions and collusive provocations of the US and Taiwan.\nRegarding the interpretation from the DPP side that you just mentioned, I want to tell them that any idea of making a last-ditch stand cannot change the fate of a dead end.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-03-27","Wu Qian","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: In recent years, the mainland has repeatedly held military exercises near the Taiwan Strait. The Wall Street Journal recently reported under the headline “China Is Ready to Blockade Taiwan,” while some Western military experts believe the action the mainland is more likely to take is “isolation and pressure.” What comments does the spokesperson have? Second question: In…","Regarding the first question, Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to handle themselves. The relevant reports you mentioned maliciously stir up confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and their intentions are sinister. The PLA's military training and exercises targeting Taiwan are aimed at the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external interference, with the purpose of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.\nRegarding the second question, it must be pointed out that “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and interference by external forces are the root causes of tension in the Taiwan Strait situation. We are willing to strive with the utmost sincerity and make the greatest efforts to realize the prospect of peaceful reunification, but we will never allow Taiwan to split away from the motherland. The more “Taiwan independence” makes a commotion, the faster it will die.\nBefore concluding, I would like to introduce teacher and student representatives from Beijing Institute of Technology, and welcome you to observe the Ministry of National Defense's regular press conference. Beijing Institute of Technology is the first science and engineering university founded by our Party and the first national defense industry institution of higher education in New China. In the 85 years since its founding, it has forged a “red path of education” that puts moral education first and combines political integrity with professional expertise, a “path of national defense and strengthening the nation through weaponry” dedicated to national defense, and a “path of innovative development” that is open, inclusive, and pursues excellence. It has produced a large number of outstanding scientists and educators, leaders of the times, and pillars of the nation.\nToday's BIT students are living in a prosperous era and bear important responsibilities. We hope you will carry forward the school's red genes of “Yan'an roots, military-industrial soul, and leaders of the vanguard,” study diligently and research persistently, scale the peaks of science, forge the backbone of a great nation with steel-willed determination, and defend the vast rivers and mountains with the sword of technology.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16377330.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-03-31","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth describes “warrior country” Japan as “indispensable for tackling Chinese aggression” on Sunday. Does the Chinese Foreign Ministry have any comment on his remarks?","China always believes that military and security cooperation between the U.S. and Japan should not target any third country, or endanger regional peace and development. By calling China a “threat” and using it as a pretext, the U.S. has been instigating ideological antagonism, stoking division and confrontation, and even inciting certain countries to be the cannon fodder of U.S. supremacy. Regional countries need to stay on high alert and guard against such practice. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-fascist War. Japan in particular needs to learn from history and be prudent in military and security areas.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that no one can interfere. We urge certain people in the U.S. to give up the illusion of “using Taiwan to contain China”, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués with concrete actions, and honor the commitment made by the U.S. on Taiwan-related issues. Japan committed aggression against Taiwan and exercised colonial rule over the island. It bears serious historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. Japan should abide by the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan, act prudently on the Taiwan question, and refrain from sending wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202503/t20250331_11585144.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202503/t20250331_11585142.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-01","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","U.S. Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth recently said that he would provide “credible deterrence” in the Indo-Pacific region, including in the Taiwan Strait. And then today we had China holding its latest drills around Taiwan. I’m wondering if you wish to comment on this current situation.","The PLA Eastern Theater Command and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have made announcements on the joint exercises. The drills are a serious warning and an act of containment against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and a legitimate and necessary move to defend national sovereignty and uphold national unity.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs that brook no external interference. The DPP authorities are hellbent on seeking “Taiwan independence,” and attempt to solicit external support for that agenda and divide the country. Such attempt is just futile and doomed to fail. The historical trend that China will and must achieve reunification is unstoppable.\nOn the remarks made by certain person in the U.S., I’ve made a response yesterday. Let me stress again that military and security cooperation between the U.S. and Japan should not target any third country, or endanger regional peace and development. By calling China a “threat” and using it as a pretext, the U.S. has been instigating ideological antagonism, and stoking division and confrontation. Regional countries need to stay on high alert and guard against such practice. On the Taiwan question, we urge certain people in the U.S. to give up the illusion of “using Taiwan to contain China,” abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués with concrete actions, and honor the commitment made by the U.S. on Taiwan-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250401_11585896.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250401_11585853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-01","Guo Jiakun","AFP","I just have a couple of other questions on the drills that were announced this morning. I wonder if you could give any more information on them specifically, on whether they will or have included live fire exercises and also how long they will go on for. And then the second question is about the cartoon that was posted by the Eastern Theater Command online that shows Lai Ching-te as an insect being roasted over…","I have answered the question about the joint military drill just now. As for the specifics you mentioned, I’d refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250401_11585896.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250401_11585853.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-04-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On April 1, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said that the joint training and exercises conducted by the PLA Eastern Theater Command around Taiwan Island are a resolute punishment for the reckless and provocative attempts by the Lai Ching-te authorities to pursue “Taiwan independence,” a solemn warning to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces who are deliberately undermining peace in the Taiwan Strait, and a necessary move to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nLai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, brazenly defines the mainland as a “hostile foreign force,” and puts forward the so-called “17 strategies,” wantonly provoking the mainland, inciting “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and intensifying tensions across the Taiwan Strait. This fully confirms their status as “disruptors of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises,” and thoroughly exposes their ugly face of opposition to peace, opposition to exchanges, opposition to democracy, and opposition to humanity. In response, we will absolutely not tolerate it, absolutely will not show leniency, and must firmly counter and severely punish it.\n“Taiwan independence” means war; pursuing “Taiwan independence” means pushing the people of Taiwan into the perilous situation of deadly war and danger. Our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is as firm as a rock, and our capabilities are invincible. We will never allow anyone or any force to split Taiwan from China, and we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nIt must be pointed out that our countermeasures are aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and are by no means aimed at the broad Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, be upright Chinese, distinguish right from wrong, act in accordance with righteousness, and, together with compatriots on the mainland, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, firmly safeguard our common Chinese national home, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250401_12693173.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-01","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 1: Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Zhu Fenglian, responding to questions on the 1st, said: Whether it is “Ya Ya,” “En Qi,” “Xiao Wei,” or the group of more than 400,000 mainland spouses, behind each person is a cross-Strait marriage and family. The DPP authorities have repeatedly abused the judiciary and fabricated charges to bully mainland spouses, forcing cross-Strait…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that this is yet another trampling by the DPP authorities of the basic rights of cross-Strait marriage families, yet another vicious act by which they vigorously create “green terror” and a “chilling effect” on the island, and yet another scheme to deliberately incite “anti-China, resist-China” sentiment and escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation.\nShe said that the DPP authorities' conduct once again exposes that the “democracy” they tout is “democracy as decided by the DPP,” and that “freedom” is only the freedom to advocate “Taiwan independence.” If the DPP authorities are allowed to continue carrying out “Taiwan independence” authoritarianism and ideological censorship, island society will fall into a situation where people are punished for their words and everyone lives in fear. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will have a clear understanding of this, dare to struggle, and safeguard their own rights and interests. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: for the vile conduct of “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices in persecuting mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable and punish them severely in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250401_12693330.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-04-02","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","It’s reported that the U.S., EU, Japan and some others made remarks on the joint exercises around Taiwan Island conducted by the People’s Liberation Army on April 1. They oppose unilateral changes to the status quo, including through force or coercion, and said that there is no justification for China’s irresponsible threats and military pressure operations near Taiwan. What’s China’s comment?","The accusation of a handful of countries and organizations against China is a mischaracterization of the facts and truth and an interference in China’s internal affairs. China deplores and opposes this. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affairs that brook no external interference. “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external forces that abet and aid them are the ones that undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. If certain countries and organizations truly want peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, they should follow the prevailing trend of international commitment to the one-China principle, abide by their political commitments made to China, earnestly respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and oppose “Taiwan independence” in any form.\nMoves to clamor for “Taiwan independence” mean separating China, support for “Taiwan independence” means interference in China’s internal affairs, and attempts to abet “Taiwan independence” mean destabilizing the Taiwan Strait. China’s joint exercises is a severe punishment against the Lai Ching-te authorities’ aggressive provocation to seek “Taiwan independence,” a stern warning to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces who deliberately undermine peace across the Taiwan Strait, and a responsible move to defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. No external force is in any position to point fingers at this.\nAs long as provocations for “Taiwan independence” last, our punishment against “Taiwan independence” will continue. We will never ever allow anyone or any force to separate Taiwan from China in any form. We will take all measures necessary to firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250402_11587335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250402_11587357.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-02","Guo Jiakun","AFP","The Philippines’ military chief said yesterday that the Philippines would inevitably be involved if there were a conflict over Taiwan. He also said that China was actively infiltrating Philippine institutions, including the military. Would the Foreign Ministry like to respond to these comments?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and is at the core of China’s core interest. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that no one can interfere in. We urge certain people in the Philippines to refrain from making provocations and playing with fire on the Taiwan question. Those who play with fire will perish by it. We also oppose relevant personnel calling white black and making groundless accusations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250402_11587335.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250402_11587357.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-04-02","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: It is reported that in response to the military exercises conducted by mainland China in the Taiwan Strait in early April, the DPP authorities said the actions undermine regional stability and the international order, and some countries including the United States claimed they oppose unilaterally changing the status quo by force or coercion. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Zhang Xiaogang: The Lai Ching-te authorities are wildly plotting “independence” and provoking, intensifying cross-Strait tension and confrontation, and are rushing headlong down the path of “relying on outside forces to seek independence” and “using force to resist unification.” The PLA Eastern Theater Command has organized combat-oriented joint exercises around Taiwan island. They demonstrate the strong capability to strike at “Taiwan independence” provocations and convey the determination and will to defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. These exercises are a powerful deterrent against the reckless and deliberately war-provoking acts of “Taiwan independence” elements. They are entirely justified, necessary and reasonable.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” will only bring war and danger to Taiwan and plunge Taiwan compatriots into deep suffering. Whoever plays the “Taiwan card” to interfere in China's internal affairs will stir up trouble in the region and harm themselves, and will end up bearing a burden too heavy to endure. Facts have repeatedly proven that the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and the Lai Ching-te authorities are the greatest challenge to the current situation across the Taiwan Strait. They are unmistakable “crisis makers” and “troublemakers.”\nWe warn the Lai Ching-te authorities that those who play with fire will burn themselves, and the more they provoke, the faster they will perish. If certain countries truly want peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, they must adhere to the one-China principle and stop sending wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The PLA will continue to strengthen training and combat readiness, keep enhancing its real combat capability to counter separatism and interference, resolutely crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, and firmly advance the process of national reunification.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/xb/News_213114/NewsRelease/16378588.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16382969.html",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-04-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, April 2 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions on April 2, saying: The joint exercises and training conducted by the PLA around Taiwan island and the “Strait Thunder-2025A” drills organized in the relevant waters in the central and southern parts of the Taiwan Strait are necessary measures to safeguard national…","Zhu Fenglian pointed out that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities are blatantly propagating the “Taiwan independence” fallacy and constantly seeking “independence” and provoking trouble, delusionally trying to change the status quo that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. This seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harms the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. If left to develop, it will only push Taiwan compatriots into a dangerous situation of war and peril, and it must be firmly curbed and resolutely punished.\nShe said that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and support China's reunification.\nZhu Fenglian said that we have full confidence and sufficient ability to unite the broad Taiwan compatriots to firmly promote the development of cross-Strait relations, oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, firmly safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250402_12693540.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-04-03","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Daily","It’s reported that during a press conference on April 1, in response to China’s joint exercises around Taiwan Island, Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshimasa Hayashi said that the Japanese government has major concerns and is closely following the relevant situation. Japan has expressed its concerns to China through diplomatic channels. What’s China’s comment?","Japan’s words and actions blatantly violate the one-China principle. We strongly deplore and firmly oppose that, and have lodged serious protests with Japan. China’s joint exercises are aimed at warning and containing “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and it is a legitimate and necessary action to defend China’s national sovereignty and uphold national unity. Japan has no right to point fingers at this, still less interfere with it. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and basic trust between the two countries. Japan committed innumerable crimes during its colonial rule over Taiwan of more than 50 years, and bears serious historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. It should act all the more prudently. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-fascist War. We urge Japan to deeply reflect on history, uphold the principles in the four political documents between China and Japan and honor its solemn commitments on the Taiwan question, immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and abide by the one-China principle with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250403_11588149.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250403_11588114.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-07","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","A delegation led by Taiwanese national security adviser Joseph Wu was just in Washington to meet with the Trump administration for a special channel meeting. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes any official interaction between the U.S. and Taiwan in any form. This position is consistent and clear. We made protest to the U.S. side and call on the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop any official interaction with China’s Taiwan region, stop meddling in the Taiwan question, and stop creating factors that fuel tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ attempts to solicit U.S. support for “Taiwan independence” will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250407_11589637.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250407_11589639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-04-09","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to US media reports, the US Secretary of Defense signed a secret internal guidance memo, which identifies China as the \"sole pacing threat,\" allegedly prioritizing \"denial of the mainland's seizure of Taiwan\" and strengthening US homeland defense. Please comment on that.","We have noted relevant reports. It seems that the US side's \"paranoia toward China\" is increasingly severe. Viewing China as a threat is a serious strategic miscalculation that will only lead to disastrous consequences. It must be emphazised that China will and must achieve reunification. It is an unstoppable historical trend that no one or force can hold it back.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250415-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16379693.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-09","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Taiwan has received the first F-16V fighter jet ordered from the US, with an additional 65 scheduled to be delivered by the end of 2026. Some analysts suggest that this move is aimed at countering the increasingly modernized air force of the Chinese mainland. Please comment on that.","We have noted relevant reports. This is yet another instance of the double standard of the US where it broke its solemn political commitments, breached the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, grossly interfered in China's internal affairs, and undermined peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. I want to underline that the US arms sales to Taiwan cannot change the strength contrast between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait much less impede the historical and inevitable trend of China's reunification. The Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities have squandered taxpayers' money, which should have been used to benefit the people, to fill the bottomless hole of harming and ruining Taiwan. The attempts to solicit US support for \"Taiwan independence\" and to resist reunification by force will only plunge Taiwan into a dangerous and precarious situation of war and ultimately lead to its own destruction.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250415-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16379693.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-09","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the G7 Foreign Ministers and the European Union's High Representative issued a statement on the joint exercises around Taiwan island conducted by the PLA in early April. The statement accused China of making \"provocative actions\" that escalate tensions across the Strait, opposed any unilateral actions to threaten the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Please comment on that.","Relevant countries and organizations blatantly violate the one-China principle and grossly interfere in China's domestic affairs. We strongly deplore and resolutely oppose this. The joint drills of the PLA Eastern Theater Command around Taiwan Island deter the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces with overwhelming power and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is a firm commitment to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and safety and well-being of our compatriots in Taiwan.\nThe Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China and how to resolve it brooks no foreign interference. The PLA remains in a combat-ready posture to fight against \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and pursue national reunification. We will resolutely thwart any separatist attempt for \"Taiwan independence\" and external interference.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250415-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16379693.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-04-11","Lin Jian","Dragon TV","It’s reported that when meeting with Secretary General of the North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) during his visit to Japan on April 9, Japanese Prime Minister Ishiba said a strong NATO benefits Japan, and Japan will continue to play a leading role in deepening cooperation between NATO and the partners in the Indo-Pacific. The two sides made negative remarks related to China on the issues of the East China…","We noted this. Japan colluded with NATO to groundlessly interfere in China’s domestic affairs, act as a scaremonger in the region, and incite antagonism and confrontation. China deplores and opposes this.\nThe Asia-Pacific, a stellar example of cooperation and development, does not need military blocs, major-country confrontation or groupings that trumpet a new Cold War. As a regional defensive organization, NATO should not reach beyond its geographical scope and mandate defined by its treaty. Due to historical reasons, Japan’s military and security moves have been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-fascist War. Japan should learn from history, stay committed to the path of Asia-Pacific cooperation, and play a constructive role in upholding and promoting peace, stability, development and prosperity in the region and beyond. Spearheading NATO’s drift into the Asia-Pacific will not do Japan any good.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250411_11593654.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250411_11593008.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-11","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwanese prosecutors have said that they have charged a Chinese cargo ship captain for violating the telecommunications management act by destroying submarine cable-related facilities. Does China have a response to this latest development?","This is not a question related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250411_11593654.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250411_11593008.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-11","Lin Jian","Global Times","It’s reported by American media that Chinese officials indicated to their U.S. counterparts at a China-U.S. dialogue on cybersecurity last December that it was behind cyber attacks on key U.S. infrastructure and linked it to the U.S.’s support for Taiwan. Top Trump administration officials have said the U.S. will pursue more offensive cyber strikes against China. What’s China’s comment?","This report is filled with lies and misinformation highly inconsistent with facts.\nWhen it comes to “Volt Typhoon,” China has clearly denied the U.S.’s groundless accusations on various occasions. We shared with the U.S. side the reports released by Chinese cybersecurity institutions and pointed out the relevant cases are just vilification and scapegoating against China by U.S. intelligence institutions. China has made it rather clear to the U.S. on various occasions that China opposes the U.S. using the cyber issues to interfere in China’s internal affairs and America’s attempt to use the Taiwan question to contain China is doomed to failure.\nLet me stress that China has clearly expressed concerns to the U.S. in multiple ways on the U.S. administration authorizing the Pentagon to conduct cyberattacks on other countries of their own accord, on America’s cyberattacks on China’s key infrastructure, the cyber and military cooperation between the U.S. and Taiwan and other issues. We have asked the U.S. to take a responsible attitude and avoid miscalculation. China will take what is necessary to safeguard its own cybersecurity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250411_11593654.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250411_11593008.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-04-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Japanese media outlets recently disclosed that the Japan-US joint exercise Keen Edge 24 featured a \"Taiwan contingency\" scenario for the first time by simulating fighter jets launching anti-ship missile strikes against a PLA landing fleet. What's your comment?","It is our consistent position that military cooperation between the US and Japan should not target any third party or jeopardize regional peace and development. The Taiwan question is an internal affair of China, and resolving it is a matter for the Chinese. The hype over a so-called \"Taiwan contingency\" by certain parties is nothing but an attempt to fan the flames and stir up troubles. No one should underestimate the strong will and ability of the Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Those who insist on using the \"Taiwan card\" to interfere in China's internal affairs or even overreach themselves with military provocations, will inevitably pay an unbearable price.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250416-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16381002.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Lai Ching-te stated that Taiwan would refrain from imposing retaliatory tariffs against the US. Instead, he asserted that \"enduring hardship is a means of self-improvement\" and pledged to make large-scale purchases of US agricultural, industrial, and energy products, as well as weapons. Please comment on that.","The Lai Ching-te authorities disregard the interests of local industries and residents, and curry favor with its \"foreign master\" for support. In essence, it is \"offering up Taiwan's resources to win the favor of the US.\" Such unconditional concessions will only deplete Taiwan's future and undermine the well-being of the people. The attempts of the DPP authorities to solicit US support for \"Taiwan independence\" and resist reunification by force will prove a dead end.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250416-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16381002.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning everyone, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广记者","Worshipping ancestors during Qingming Festival is a Chinese tradition passed down by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. What joint ancestor-worship events were held across the Strait during this year's Qingming Festival?","Qingming ancestor worship is a custom of the Chinese nation that has continued for thousands of years, and “pay heed to the end and remember the beginning” is a virtue jointly revered by Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. Recently, Xia Liyan, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, led a delegation to visit the mainland. He attended the Yi-Si Year Yellow Emperor Ancestral Worship Ceremony in Xinzheng, Henan, and paid respects at the Sun Yat-sen Mausoleum in Nanjing, Jiangsu. Wu Chengdian, Chairman of the New Party, led a delegation to Huangling, Shaanxi, to attend the Yi-Si Year Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi. Xiao Xucen, Executive Director of the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation for Education and Culture, led Taiwanese youth to Qufu, Shandong, to take part in the 2025 Cross-Strait Spring Confucius Culture Festival and Confucius Memorial Ceremony. Representative figures from relevant parties and groups on the island, as well as grassroots residents, also actively took part in joint cross-strait ancestral worship activities. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait worshipping their ancestors together, drinking water while remembering its source and not forgetting one’s roots, is of great significance for strengthening the sense of belonging, identity, and honor of cross-strait compatriots toward the Chinese nation. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to seek their roots, pay respects to ancestors, remember distant origins, and visit and exchange, and to jointly guard the common spiritual homeland of the Chinese nation together with compatriots on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695879.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","With the development of new media technology, emerging online film and television formats such as short videos and micro-short dramas are increasingly popular among young people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. What cross-Strait youth cultural exchange activities have taken place recently?","Young people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are full of vitality, have active minds, and have distinctive personalities. We have consistently supported and actively promoted exchange activities among young people across the Strait. Here are three recent cultural exchange activities for young people across the Strait.\nSubmissions for the 5th IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival opened on April 9. The festival is calling for narrative or non-narrative short films of 10 to 30 minutes from university students and young directors across the Chinese-speaking world. It encourages young creators to use images as a means of sincerely expressing social development in a diverse era, in order to support and witness the growth of young film and television creators at universities. Submissions close on June 10.\nThe 2nd “Colorful Taiwan in Beijing” Cross-Strait Youth Short Film Competition has been included in the “Film+” series of the 15th Beijing International Film Festival. Under the theme “Youth Sharing the Screen, Walking Together,” it is divided into five sections: “Everyday Light and Shadow,” “Future Vision,” “Cultural Imprint,” “Travelogue,” and “Witnessing Services.” It encourages people to use the lens to record the colorful lives on both sides of the Strait, to use technology or show how technology makes life better, to inherit China’s excellent traditional culture, to showcase the beautiful rivers and mountains of the motherland through travel stories, and to witness all aspects of Beijing-Taiwan integration and services for Taiwan compatriots. Submissions close on May 20.\nThe “Chasing Dreams in Zhejiang · Creating the Future” micro-drama online competition was launched in Zhejiang on April 1. It encourages young people across the Strait to use images as a bond and present, in micro-dramas, short videos and other formats of 2 to 10 minutes, the contemporary thinking and youthful expression of young people on both sides. It also conveys the core values and rich connotations of Chinese culture and promotes deeper exchange and cooperation among young people across the Strait in artistic creation. Submissions for the competition close on May 25.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The US has announced an additional 145% tariff on mainland China. Although TSMC has pledged an additional 100 billion US dollars in investment in the US, the US still claims it will impose a 32% tariff on Taiwan. This has caused an uproar across the island. Critics attacked the DPP authorities for boasting that their relationship with the US is “as solid as a rock,” only to be “stabbed in the back.” Lai Ching-te…","In the face of the United States’ reckless imposition of tariffs and its unilateral provocation of a global trade war, we resolutely implemented necessary countermeasures at the first opportunity. This is not only to safeguard our own legitimate rights and interests, but also to defend the rules of international trade and international fairness and justice. Our firm stance and forceful measures have won widespread recognition and support from the international community, and many countries have chosen to stand with China and oppose American bullying and hegemony. I have noted that public opinion and netizens on the island have praised the mainland for the backbone and confidence it has shown in responding.\nIn order to pursue “independence,” the Lai Ching-te authorities took the initiative to sell out Taiwan’s core advantageous industries, only to receive high US tariffs on Taiwan. This shattered the illusion of a US-Taiwan relationship that they had deliberately fabricated, and turned “chess piece” into “discarded piece.” Disregarding the interests of the people and the prospects of industrial development, the Lai authorities put forward a “big purchases, big investments” plan to curry favor with the US. They are servile and “turn the left cheek and then offer the right.” Such conduct of “kneeling to the US and selling out Taiwan” is despicable.\nFacts have proven that as long as the two sides of the Strait are at peace and compatriots are united in heart, we can jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation, jointly resist external risks, and jointly create the great cause of national rejuvenation that will make Chinese people on both sides of the Strait proud and uplifted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695886.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office's government website recently launched a “Reporting Column on Vicious Acts by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Thugs and Accomplices in Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots,” which has drawn great attention on the island. In response, the DPP authorities said that the mainland “has no jurisdiction” over Taiwan. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Many reporting emails were received on the…","Taiwan is part of China, and the state will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means. Against \"Taiwan independence\" diehards who break the law, no matter where they are, the state's law enforcement and judicial organs will pursue them to the end and punish them severely in accordance with the law. As for certain \"Taiwan independence\" organizations, \"Taiwan independence\" elements, public officials, and mobilized online influencers who serve as henchmen and accomplices for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities in threatening and intimidating political opponents, and in suppressing and persecuting political parties, groups, and individuals on the island who support the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, we will not stand idly by. We have the authority, and the obligation, to take action under both law and reason.\nThe launch of the \"Special Column for Reporting Despicable Acts by 'Taiwan Independence' Henchmen and Accomplices Who Persecute Taiwan Compatriots\" has a solid legal basis and sufficient legal grounds. It is a just act that responds to the call of people on both sides of the Strait to punish \"independence,\" and a necessary measure to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Since the column was launched, it has been warmly received and reports have come in actively. To date, we have received more than 3,000 reporting emails. The reported targets are relatively concentrated and the content is fairly detailed, fully reflecting the deep resentment among people on both sides of the Strait toward the wrongdoing of \"Taiwan independence\" henchmen and accomplices. We will adhere to facts as the basis and the law as the standard, and after verifying the relevant reported information, we will hold these henchmen and accomplices accountable and punish them severely in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695884.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The livestream of American internet celebrity “Jiakangge” (甲亢哥) during his trip to China has sparked a “China craze” across the global internet and also heated discussion on the island. Many Taiwanese young people in the mainland have called out to the island: “Come to the mainland, seeing is believing.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s attitude toward Taiwanese internet celebrities coming to the mainland?","This American internet celebrity, through live-streaming from cities including Shanghai, Beijing and Zhengzhou, has shown the world a real, friendly and multidimensional China. This includes China's profound cultural heritage, the hospitable people of various places, and the advanced and convenient use of technology. Their content has drawn wide attention across the global internet and has once again sparked a “China craze.” We welcome people and things that objectively present China and enhance the understanding of today's China among people around the world.\nMany Taiwan netizens have expressed various curiosity and admiration about this phenomenon. We welcome the broad Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwan internet celebrities, to come to the mainland to take a look around, to have all kinds of cultural, technological and life experiences, and to share what they see and hear with friends across the Strait in a spirit of goodwill and sincerity, so as to enhance mutual understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, Lo Wen-chia, deputy chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, claimed that since the China-U.S. trade conflict, the mainland's advantage as the “world's factory” no longer exists, and the number of Taiwanese businesspeople remaining on the mainland has fallen sharply, possibly to less than one-fifth of the peak period. He also said, “Consumption on the mainland is shrinking, and the economy is like a…","Some people in the DPP one moment spread the “mainland threat theory” and the next moment spread the “mainland economic recession theory.” This is a typical “split personality” that is not only self-contradictory but has long been slapped in the face by the two miracles of rapid economic development and long-term social stability that the mainland has created over several decades.\nWhether the mainland’s economic prospects are good is best answered by the facts. Despite many external challenges, the mainland’s economy is resilient, has great potential, and has ample confidence and capacity. Over the years it has steadily advanced new-type industrialization and accelerated the cultivation of new quality productive forces, and its endogenous drivers of economic development have clearly strengthened, maintaining an industrial economy that is growing in both quantity and quality. Its manufacturing output has ranked first in the world for 15 consecutive years, accounting for about 30% of the global total. Looking at import and export trade, in the first quarter of this year the total value of goods trade was 10.3 trillion yuan, up 1.3% year on year, and import and export growth has clearly been recovering month by month. Looking at the consumer market, in January and February of this year, total retail sales of consumer goods reached 8.37 trillion yuan, up 4.0% year on year. The “everyday vitality” of the consumer market continues to rise, and domestic demand has increasingly become the main driver and stable anchor of economic growth.\nWhether cross-Strait economic cooperation is good is for Taiwan businesspeople to say most authoritatively. Facing an external environment of intertwined upheavals, the mainland’s advantages of a broad stage for enterprise, vast market prospects, stable policy expectations, and a good security situation have stood out even more, and it has consistently been the best choice for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to invest and build their businesses. In January and February of this year, cross-Strait trade reached 310.34 billion yuan, up 10% year on year. Actual use of Taiwan capital on the mainland was 710 million US dollars, up 83.7% year on year. A total of 921 new Taiwan-invested enterprises were established. More and more Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots are proving with their actual actions that “decoupling and breaking supply chains” is unpopular and that integrated development is the way forward.\nOut of its nature of pursuing “independence,” the DPP authorities are accustomed to smearing the mainland and disrupting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The lies they fabricate are no match for the facts. They cannot deceive Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots, and they cannot stop the steps of compatriots on both sides of the Strait as they exchange, cooperate, and seek common development together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695883.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","In the face of the US’s tariff bullying, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, have made concessions to the US, and on the other hand, have clamored for strict prevention of mainland goods being transshipped through Taiwan to launder their origin and evade US tariffs, and for reviewing whether to adjust the duty-free preferential measures for small parcels under NT$2,000. What comment do you have on this?","Enterprises on both sides of the Strait are both Chinese enterprises, and the economies on both sides both belong to the economy of the Chinese nation. The United States has recklessly imposed tariffs and stirred up trade wars worldwide, threatening the economic development and people’s well-being on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides should unite in adversity, jointly confront external risks and challenges, and firmly safeguard their legitimate development rights and interests and the interests of the Chinese nation.\nThe DPP authorities disregard the interests of enterprises and people on the island. They not only kneel and bow obsequiously to the US, but also intensify efforts to push for “decoupling and severing chains” across the Strait. Their evil intention to seek “independence” and the essence of selling out Taiwan are fully exposed. We have firm confidence, strong will, and sufficient capability to counter any economic bullying and to combat provocations seeking “independence” and external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","According to reports, TSMC and Intel have reached a preliminary agreement to establish a joint-venture chip manufacturing company, in which TSMC will hold 20%. Taiwan's United Microelectronics Corporation (UMC) is also evaluating a merger with the U.S. company GlobalFoundries to form a U.S. company, with the ultimate goal of replacing TSMC. Doubts on the island about the United States hollowing out Taiwan's…","The concerns of Taiwan’s industry are not unfounded. TSMC has long since become the “pledge of allegiance” for the DPP authorities’ “relying on the US to plot independence,” and it is only a matter of time before Taiwan’s semiconductor industry is handed over on a platter by Lai Ching-te, this “professional seller of Taiwan.”\n“Establishing something is as difficult as ascending to heaven; its collapse is as easy as singeing a feather.” If the DPP authorities are allowed to continue down the evil path of “selling out Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan,” Taiwan’s industry and people will lose not only their current jobs but also future development opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","广东广播电视台“触电新闻”记者","Recently, Colby, who is about to take office as US Deputy Secretary of Defense, said that he agrees with President Trump’s view that Taiwan’s “defense budget” should approach 10% of GDP, and that one of his goals after taking office is to avoid unnecessary conflict between Taiwan and Beijing. What is your comment on this?","The relevant remarks are intended to sell more weapons to Taiwan and serve the interests of the American military-industrial complex. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are wasting money that could be used to improve people’s livelihoods on buying weapons and currying favor with external forces, and are paying “protection money” to the United States. This not only fails to buy “security,” but will also accelerate pushing Taiwan into a perilous situation of war and danger. If the United States sincerely hopes for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, oppose “Taiwan independence,” and support China’s reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan’s security authorities said the mainland is focusing on issues such as Lai Ching-te’s “3.13 speech,” “TSMC’s investment in the United States,” and “PLA joint combat readiness patrols” to conduct “cognitive warfare” against Taiwan. The aim is to create social antagonism on the island, and it is increasingly using AI tools to assist in generating and spreading controversial…","This statement reverses black and white. It is the Lai Ching-te authorities’ customary trick of manipulating “cognitive warfare” to smear the mainland.\nFor the sake of his party and his own private interests, Lai, on the one hand, recklessly provokes “independence” and does not hesitate to tie the ordinary people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot; on the other hand, with no bottom line, he “fawns over the US and sells out Taiwan,” completely disregarding the interests and well-being of the island’s industries and people. When the people of Taiwan voice grievances, naturally voices of questioning and opposition will arise. The Lai Ching-te authorities are attempting to use the mainland’s “cognitive warfare” to silence the many voices, which fully exposes their inner weakness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报南方+记者","The foreign ministers of the Group of Seven and the High Representative of the European Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy issued a joint statement expressing concern about China's “provocative” actions, especially the large-scale military exercises recently held around Taiwan. They said that maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait serves the interests of the G7 and the broader…","The PLA's military exercises around Taiwan Island are a deterrent and punishment against “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and interference by external forces, and a necessary and just action to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nSome countries claim to care about “peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait,” but in essence they meddle in the Taiwan question and interfere in China's internal affairs. It must be pointed out that it is the DPP authorities who undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. By colluding with external forces to carry out “independence” provocations, they have caused tensions in the Taiwan Strait. If the countries concerned truly want peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and clearly oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","A US House Representative recently introduced the “Taiwan International Solidarity Act,” claiming that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 does not involve Taiwan, and calling on the US government to use its influence to resist the mainland's “distortion of Resolution 2758 in international organizations.” What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China and has no other international legal status. Resolution 2758, adopted by an overwhelming majority at the 26th session of the UN General Assembly in 1971, restored the representation and seat of all of China, including Taiwan, to the government of the People's Republic of China, on the premise that the UN recognized Taiwan as part of China. The historical facts are clear, and the legal basis is clear.\nThe so-called US bill disregards historical and legal facts, ignores the authority of the General Assembly resolution, and goes to great lengths to interfere in China's internal affairs. We firmly oppose it. A handful of US politicians should immediately stop their erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues and stop promoting erroneous Taiwan-related bills. We warn the DPP authorities that no matter how they rely on external forces to seek “independence” and stir up trouble, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695881.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that “democratic countries of the northern hemisphere” all want to win over excellent Taiwanese businesspeople, and that investing in “decoupling from China and moving toward the North” can allow one to establish a foothold in Taiwan and deploy globally. He also said, “Taiwan should seize every moment of geopolitical and economic change to push in the direction suitable for its…","Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. This is both history and fact. The future and destiny of Taiwan lie in national reunification, and the well-being of compatriots is bound up with national rejuvenation. Cross-Strait cooperation in industrial and supply chains is the outcome of the market’s pursuit of optimal allocation of resources and the product of the independent choices of cross-Strait industries and enterprises. It conforms to the laws of economic development and to the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. No one and no force can shake the overall pattern of mutually complementary, mutually beneficial, and win-win cross-Strait economic cooperation, nor can anyone stop the overall trend of deepening cross-Strait integration. Moving west to the mainland and putting down roots there is the best choice for Taiwan businesses and enterprises.\nThe so-called “Global North” is a concept that the Lai Ching-te authorities fabricated for the sake of “de-Sinicization and anti-China” policies. The “democratic countries” he speaks of are hollowing out Taiwan’s industries. The Lai Ching-te authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces, in pursuit of “independence,” have deliberately deceived the Taiwan public and attempted to distort the investment direction of Taiwan enterprises. Their aim is to decouple and sever cross-Strait economic ties. In the end, what they weaken is Taiwan’s autonomy in economic development, and what they harm are the immediate interests of Taiwan businesses and enterprises. This is purely harmful to and destructive of Taiwan. It is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695882.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The United States has dispatched a retired general to serve as senior observer of Taiwan's annual “Han Kuang 41” wargame exercise and as an “adviser” to Taiwan's Chief of the General Staff. This represents an upgrade of US-Taiwan military exchanges to the point where both sides have begun “planning coordination,” but there is still a large gap before joint operations. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any form of US-Taiwan military contact, and demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with great caution, and stop encouraging “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to “seek independence through force.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “relying on the United States to seek independence” is a wrong path, and “seeking independence through force” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, the island's competent authority for internal affairs said that an inspection found that of 22 social organizations handling cross-Strait exchange and new resident-related business, 19 were not functioning normally, and 6 of them failed to improve by the deadline and have been dissolved, which has sparked widespread questioning and criticism from all sectors of society on the island. What comment do you…","“Anyone who wants to pin a crime on another will always find an excuse.” This is yet another vicious act by the DPP authorities, who are running amok with “green terror” on the island and creating a “chilling effect.” This both exposes their sinister intent to stubbornly seek “independence,” provoke, and deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and reveals their fearful and guilty conscience at seeing compatriots on both sides of the Strait draw closer and their scheme go bankrupt. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: the desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer cannot be suppressed, and the momentum of exchange and cooperation cannot be blocked. Acting recklessly and going against the trend will surely bring retribution upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, Commander of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command Paparo, while attending a U.S. Senate hearing, said that the United States should vigorously enhance autonomous systems and deploy them in the Taiwan Strait, in order to create a “hellscape” to deter China from attacking Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affairs and brooks no interference from any external force. Some people on the US side have continuously incited and hyped up so-called “hellish scenes,” which blatantly exposes the sinister intention of US anti-China forces, who, out of political self-interest, are willing to ruin Taiwan. We demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop interfering in the Taiwan question, stop fanning the flames and stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait, and not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThis again proves that the DPP authorities' collusion with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation will only bring the danger of war to Taiwan and push Taiwan's people into the abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday新闻云记者","Question one: The US launched a tariff trade war that has hit many Taiwan businesses on the mainland. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office understands the current production and business situation of Taiwan businesses on the mainland? Some Taiwan businesspeople have said that, to keep their supply chains from falling into difficulty, they may move their production lines out of the mainland in the future.…","First question. After four decades of trials and tempering, cross-Strait economic cooperation has formed long-term mutually beneficial relations and a stable pattern of industrial and supply chain cooperation. This is the result of economic laws at work and market-based autonomous choices, and it conforms to the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nIn the short term, due to high tariff barriers, export-oriented enterprises, including Taiwan-invested enterprises on the Mainland, will be affected to some extent in their production and operations. But in the long term, the supporting conditions and fundamental trend of the Mainland's stable and positive economic development will continue, and we have full confidence that we can continue to be a major contributor to world economic growth and a stabilizing anchor, opening up broader space for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development. We always respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, and we will actively improve institutions and policies that promote cross-Strait economic, trade, and cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, help Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the Mainland adapt to change, respond, transform and upgrade, expand domestic demand, better integrate into the new development pattern, participate in high-quality development, and share the dividends of Chinese-style modernization. On April 18, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, will convene a symposium of Taiwan businesspeople in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province, to hear the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the Mainland. Please follow the relevant reports.\nSecond question. The DPP authorities are accustomed to using so-called “espionage” as a pretext, deliberately playing up the “Mainland threat” and inciting “anti-Chinese and anti-China sentiment,” with the aim of diverting the island's public discontent over their incompetent governance and “selling out Taiwan and provoking war.” This routine is nothing new; Taiwan's public has long seen enough of it and seen through it. The tide of cross-Strait exchanges is surging forward and will neither stop nor be cut off. We firmly support, and will take forceful measures to promote, normal and healthy cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and to protect the lawful and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law.\nThird question. From fabricating charges to force mainland spouses to be separated from their families, to ordering mainland spouses to supplement their certification documents, the DPP authorities are creating a “green terror,” escalating cross-Strait confrontation, and are increasingly resorting to any means and disregarding human relations.\nMainland spouses are family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots. Regarding the DPP authorities' vicious acts of provoking in pursuit of “independence” and increasingly making things difficult for and persecuting mainland spouses, tearing apart Taiwan society, broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots should rise up together in opposition and bravely defend their own rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695880.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695885.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","On April 13, Expo 2025 Osaka opened in Japan. Previously, Japan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs clearly refused to allow Taiwan to participate in the Expo in an official capacity. Although the DPP authorities participated under a corporate name, the name of the pavilion is “TECH WORLD.” On the island, the abbreviation “TW” is being hyped as a hint at “Taiwan,” and so-called “diplomatic breakthroughs” are being…","This kind of “self-congratulatory” behavior is utterly self-deceiving, like covering one's ears while stealing a bell. The DPP authorities are accustomed to making small moves on various occasions, weaving a so-called “international presence” illusion in an attempt to fool the island's people and mislead international opinion. No matter how they maneuver, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they will only make themselves a laughingstock.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Despite the Lai Ching-te authorities restricting cross-Strait exchanges on various pretexts and inciting “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, KMT Vice Chairman Xia Liyan and Hsiao Hsu-tsen, Executive Director of the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation, recently each led delegations to visit the mainland. Some public opinion holds that this highlights that cross-Strait exchanges accord with the will of the people and…","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, not enemies; both belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. It is something no political force can stop for family members to visit each other frequently and draw closer to one another. The DPP authorities are acting against the trend of the times, obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and harming the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Their scheme is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Recently, Taiwanese singer TANK, Lü Jianzhong, successfully underwent Asia’s first combined heart-liver transplant at the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University and was discharged after recovery. He posted, “Thank the motherland, thank Hangzhou,” which sparked heated discussion among Taiwanese netizens, who praised the mainland’s medical technology as leading developed countries. What is your comment?","We congratulate Mr. Lü on the success of his surgery and his recovery and discharge from the hospital! His treatment experience has been a relay of life across the Strait and a vivid portrayal of compatriots on both sides of the Strait being bound by blood and sharing deep brotherly affection.\nIn recent years, the mainland's medical undertakings have developed rapidly and its medical standards have continuously improved, providing better guarantees for Taiwan compatriots who live and seek medical care on the mainland. We will continue to uphold the concept of “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” continuously improve the systems and policies under which Taiwan compatriots enjoy equal treatment, and provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots to access basic public health services, take the physician qualification examination and the health professional technical qualification examination, apply for physician practice registration, practice medicine for short periods, and so on. We also actively encourage and support cross-Strait medical and health exchanges, and we welcome people in Taiwan's medical and pharmaceutical fields to visit and exchange views on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Taiwanese writer Lung Ying-tai recently published an op-ed in The New York Times criticizing Lai Ching-te for “turning a blind eye” to the dissatisfaction of people on the island, and for “creating panic and provoking confrontation” on the island. She cited a poll of ten thousand people on the island, stating that 73% of the public said they would choose to surrender if mainland China attacks Taiwan. What…","Relevant circumstances show that the Lai Ching-te authorities’ continued scheming for “independence” and provocations have already triggered strong dissatisfaction and deep concern among all sectors on the island. “Taiwan independence” means war. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” will only throw Taiwan into chaos and push the broad Taiwan compatriots into the perilous situation of war and disaster. More and more Taiwan residents have recognized the danger and harm of “Taiwan independence provoking war.” They have recognized that they must not become sacrificial victims of Lai Ching-te’s reckless push for “Taiwan independence,” and that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and unification cannot be stopped. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: any scheme that goes against the will of the people and defies the general trend of history will be rejected and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question. According to statistics published by the General Administration of Customs, in the first quarter of this year, mainland exports to Taiwan grew 8.3% and imports from Taiwan grew 17.8%. Cross-Strait trade outperformed the mainland’s overall foreign trade. Given such close cross-Strait economic and trade ties, is Lai Ching-te’s proposal to “break away from China and enter the North” a good idea?…","First question: Moving west to the Mainland and putting down roots on the Mainland is the best choice for Taiwan businesses and enterprises. Over the years, cross-Strait industrial and supply chain cooperation has been the result of market pursuit of optimal resource allocation and the product of independent choices by industries and enterprises on both sides. It conforms to economic development laws and to the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides. No one and no force can shake the broad pattern of complementary advantages, mutual benefit, and win-win cooperation between the two sides’ economies, nor can anyone halt the overall trend of ever-deepening cross-Strait integrated development.\nSecond question: Statements that promote the separatist fallacy of “one side, one country” are a blatant provocation to seek independence. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. It has never been a country, a historical and legal fact that cannot and must not be denied. The DPP authorities are vigorously engaged in “de-Sinicization,” disregarding history and distorting facts, attempting to use “Taiwan independence” textbooks to sever the historical and cultural ties across the Taiwan Strait, causing confusion in historical memory and distortion of national identity among the younger generation in Taiwan. Such a betrayal of one’s ancestors will inevitably be strongly opposed and reviled by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月潭天”记者","China Media Group’s “Looking at the Taiwan Strait” recently launched the online event “Travel the Mainland Following the Films.” Many Taiwan netizens actively participated with lively interaction, recounting mainland film shooting locations and cultural landmarks as readily as their family treasures. In their messages, they expressed hope to find inspiration in excellent mainland film and television works and to…","The “Follow the Movies to Tour the Mainland” campaign launched by relevant media platforms, as well as recent events in which Fuzhou and Xiamen offered Taiwan compatriots traveling to coastal Fujian via the “Mini Three Links” routes free tickets to screenings of 《哪吒之魔童闹海》, have been warmly welcomed and actively embraced by Taiwan compatriots. This fully reflects the appeal of excellent mainland film and cultural works and the charm of Chinese culture they carry, and demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same culture, the same ancestry, and cultural genes that resonate emotionally.\nSpring in March is the season for outings. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to follow the guides and come to the mainland to check in at the birthplaces or filming locations of films and TV works they love. For example, the films 《长安三万里》 and 《封神第二部：战火西岐》 were successively released in theaters on the island over the past two months. Taiwan friends who like these two films can check in at Xi'an in Shaanxi and Anyang in Henan to experience firsthand the long history and brilliant splendor of Chinese culture. I have also noticed that many Taiwan friends like the TV dramas 《去有风的地方》 and 《难哄》. These friends can check in at Dali in Yunnan and Chongqing to experience romantic scenery and everyday life firsthand, and enjoy the excitement of “one drama making a city famous.” Whether it is natural scenery or pastoral life, every check-in spot will surely make the trip worthwhile for Taiwan friends and help them understand “a different mainland.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250416_12695878.htm"],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The 2025 “Mazu Returns Home Across the World” event launched in Putian, Fujian, has drawn great attention from believers on the island. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On March 29, the 2025 “Mazu of the World Returns Home” event was launched on Meizhou Island in Putian, Fujian. The event was hosted by the Board of Directors of the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple, with more than 110 representatives of Mazu cultural groups and nearly 10,000 guests attending, including 145 representatives from 25 Taiwan Mazu cultural groups. One hundred divided-incense Mazu statues entered the venue to pay homage to the ancestral temple and offer incense. The hanging of the dou (dou) and the transfer of the incense burners were carried out in sequence, symbolizing the continuation of Mazu's protection. During the event, more than 10 intangible cultural heritage projects were also displayed, including Mazu offerings, Meizhou women's headdresses and costumes, ship model making, and Mazu cake making. “Mazu of the World Returns Home” returns to the shared spiritual homeland of the sons and daughters of both sides of the Strait, and it guards the cultural roots passed down through generations of the Chinese nation. According to statistics, since the beginning of this year, 227 groups totaling more than 4,600 person-times of Mazu devotees from the island have come to Meizhou Island to pay homage to the ancestral temple and offer incense.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan media reported that the island's annual \"Han Kuang 41\" exercise began a 14-day \"computer-based war game\" on the 5th, with scenarios based on possible actions such as the so-called PLA \"gray-zone harassment\" and \"shifting from exercise to attacking Taiwan.\" What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and collude with external forces to plot “independence” and provoke, attempting to “pursue independence by force” and “rely on foreign powers to seek independence.” They are the source of disaster and turmoil undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and unification cannot be blocked. No matter how many “war games” or “exercises” the DPP authorities conduct, they cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” as a dead end, nor can they stop the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: On April 8, Taiwan's National Immigration Agency required former mainland-born residents who settled in Taiwan to supplement and submit a “certificate of loss of original household registration.” Does the Taiwan Affairs Office know how many former mainland-born residents have returned to the mainland to handle household registration cancellation certificates? Second question: On February 25, the…","On the first question: it involves household registration management matters, which relevant departments have consistently handled in accordance with laws and regulations.\nOn the second question: according to reports in Taiwan media, this year there was one incident of a submarine cable break caused by a Taiwanese fishing vessel, and three natural breaks caused by non-human factors. The DPP authorities have continuously hyped the “Hong Tai” cargo ship, and without investigation, accused the vessel of cutting the submarine cable. This is entirely “conviction first, investigation later.” Taiwan's judicial departments have become political tools of the DPP authorities for “resisting China,” and have no credibility whatsoever.\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250416_12695847.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-04-17","Lin Jian","Reuters","Do you have any more information on the Taiwanese nationals deported from Cambodia to China recently?","China commends the Cambodian government for handling relevant issue in accordance with the one-China principle. We stand ready to continue deepening law enforcement cooperation with Cambodia and relevant countries to crack down on online gambling and scam, protect the safety of Chinese citizens overseas and their lawful rights and interests, and ensure normal order of cross-border exchanges between China and relevant countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250417_11596227.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250417_11596153.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-21","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The U.S. and the Philippines will start their flagship annual military drills today. The exercise has come as Beijing and Manila are obviously in a dispute over the South China Sea. A Philippine general who directed drills said Manila is treating them as an exercise “ for our defense.” Would the Ministry like to respond on that?","With the world being hit by unilateralism, protectionism and bullying, countries in this region have been calling for greater solidarity, coordination, and joint efforts to keep the region stable and respond to challenges. Against this backdrop, the Philippines chose to conduct the large-scale military drills with this country outside the region and brought in strategic and tactical weapons to the detriment of regional strategic stability and regional economic prospects, which puts them on the opposite side of regional countries. This act has been detested and opposed by regional countries.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and is at the core of China’s core interest. China firmly opposes any country using the Taiwan question as an excuse to strengthen military deployment in the region, heighten tensions and confrontation, and disturb regional peace and stability. We urge relevant sides not to make provocation on the Taiwan question. Those who play with fire will perish by it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250421_11600794.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250421_11599248.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-21","Guo Jiakun","AFP","I have a question about Myanmar. We are seeing reports that this week, the Myanmar National Democratic Alliance army will hand control of the strategic town of Lashio back to the Myanmar junta forces. The consensus is that the deal has been brokered under pressure from China. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","China and Myanmar are friendly neighbors. China’s position on the Myanmar issue is very clear. We follow the principle of non-interference in other countries’ internal affairs, support Myanmar in safeguarding independence, sovereignty, national unity and territorial integrity, support various parties in Myanmar in carrying out friendly consultation toward political reconciliation, and support Myanmar in resuming the political transition process.\n***************************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250421_11600794.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250421_11599248.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-04-22","Guo Jiakun","Spanish Daily ABC","A follow-up question on my previous one, also regarding Pope Francis’ passing. Pope Francis publicly expressed several times his desire to visit China and meet with Chinese leader. I would like to ask, would the Vatican breaking diplomatic ties with Taiwan be a precondition on such a visit ever happening?","In recent years, China and the Vatican have maintained constructive engagement, conducted useful exchanges, and had extensive communication on international issues.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. More and more countries have come to recognize and abide by the one-China principle. We hope relevant countries will see where the arc of history bends and come back to the right path of upholding the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250422_11601566.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250422_11601529.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-04-24","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the US, the Philippines and other countries are conducting Exercise Balikatan. As part of drills, the US military has, for the first time, deployed anti-ship missile system to the Luzon Strait north of the Philippines. Some analysts believe that this is to simulate the blockade of the Bashi Channel during a crisis in the Taiwan Strait. The Philippines and the US also organized Exercise Cope…","We always hold that military cooperation between countries should not target or hurt the interests of any third party, nor should it jeopardize regional peace and stability. The South China Sea should be a sea of peace, cooperation and friendship. However, the Philippines holds a candle to the devil by currying favor and colluding with the US and other outside countries to make provocations. It frequently conducts the so-called joint patrols and exercises, and invites and deploys strategic and tactical weapons, which seriously undermines the common interests of regional countries. We firmly oppose any country strengthening military deployment in the region and provoking tensions and confrontation under the excuse of the Taiwan question. Regardless of external challenges and turbulence, the Chinese side will resolutely safeguard our territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and firmly maintain peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250424-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16382785.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-24","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, as revealed by Taiwan media outlets, there is a wave of resignation inside the troops of Taiwan. Many military officers on the ground chose early decommissioning or resignation to avoid fighting in war. Some analysts think that it's because they don't want to be cannon fodder for \"Taiwan independence\" separatists. What's your comment on this? Secondly, the Japanese Ministry of…","On your first question, this is another evidence that \"Taiwan independence\" separatists have no support from the people of Taiwan and will collapse like a house of cards.\nOn your second question, we firmly oppose the Japanese side playing up the so-called \"China military threat\", hyping up tensions in the region, and deliberately provoking confrontation. China follows a path of peaceful development and pursues a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. Our military development is aimed at safeguarding our national sovereignty, security and development interests. We have no intention to challenge or threaten any country. Engagements and cooperation between the Chinese and Russian militaries feature non-alignment, non-confrontation and non-targeting any third party.\nIn recent years, the Japanese side has drastically increased defense budget, and sought breakthroughs in military build-up. Its behaviors have led to serious concerns among its Asian neighbors and the international community. We urge the Japanese side to recalibrate its strategic perception of China, stop provoking bloc confrontation, be prudent with its words and actions in the military and security domain, and contribute more to regional peace and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250424-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16382785.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-24","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command said in a recent Senate hearing that \"China's increasingly aggressive actions near Taiwan are not just exercises, but rehearsals for attacking Taiwan\". He suggested that the US should significantly advance autonomous systems and deploy them in the Taiwan Strait, so as to build a \"hellscape\" to deter China. What's your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese, which brooks no foreign interference. Some individuals of the US side point fingers at and make groundless speculations on the legitimate and necessary measures taken by the Chinese side to safeguard our national sovereignty and territorial integrity. They also attempt to bluff us with a fancy slogan. This exposes their true motive of clinging to US hegemony and selfish interests at the cost of destroying others' homeland. Threats and intimidation will never work on China or the Chinese military.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250424-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16382785.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-24","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, it's reported that the troops in Taiwan started the computer-assisted command post drill (computer-simulated war games) under Exercise Han Kuang 41 on April 5. The drill will last for 14 days and 13 nights. The scenarios include the so-called potential operations by the Chinese mainland, such as \"gray-zone harassment\" and \"transition from exercise to war\". Koo Li-hsiung, Head of…","On your first question, the military elements of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces put on a flashy show by conducting exercises. This does nothing more than embolden and comfort themselves. No matter how many drills they carry out, they will not be able to escape from their destined failure.\nOn your second question, for its selfish gains, the DPP authorities hysterically hype up the so-called \"mainland's threat\", stir up social panic, and double down on their \"combat readiness for Taiwan independence\". If left unchecked, their behaviors will surely plunge Taiwan into war. The DPP authorities' so-called \"whole-of-society defence\" actually harms the whole society, as they take the Taiwan island as a battlefield and coerce the local people into cannon fodders for \"Taiwan independence\". Their actions are shameful. The PLA is committed to fighting against \"Taiwan independence\" separatists, promoting national reunification, and safeguarding China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope our Taiwan compatriots recognize the true nature of the DPP authorities as a source of chaos and disasters, take active actions to oppose \"Taiwan independence\", and protect their own well-being and livelihood. We hope the two sides of the Taiwan Strait will join hands to promote national reunification and rejuvenation.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250424-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16382785.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-04-24","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports from Taiwan media, the US side sent a retired four-star army general, who was also a former commander of US Forces Korea, to serve as the senior observer for the war games of this year's Han Kuang Exercise. In addition, the war games revealed five potential patterns of joint operations between Taiwan and the US in wartime. May I have your comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military collusion between the US and Taiwan. To embolden and support \"Taiwan independence\" separatists is to ruin peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Those who do that will get burned for playing with fire, and taste the bitter fruit of their own doing. We urge the US side to stop stirring up troubles on the Taiwan question, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, and deliver on its promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\". We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that those who solicit US support for \"Taiwan independence\" will be stabbed in the back, and be abandoned as a useless pawn.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/04/china-250424-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16382785.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-04-30","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan says Somalia has banned entry to its citizens amid dispute over Taiwan’s ties with Somaliland as Somalia is under Chinese pressure. What is the Foreign Ministry’s response to this?","China noted that recently, the Somali federal government has announced that it would not accept travel documents issued by the Taiwan authorities, whether for arrival in or transit through Somalia, in accordance with Somalia’s Constitution and UNGA Resolution 2758. Somalia’s government reiterated its commitment to the one-China principle and stressed that hosting each other’s “representative office” and having official interactions between the Taiwan authorities and Somaliland directly infringes on Somalia’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThis is a legitimate measure taken by Somalia as a sovereign country to safeguard its lawful rights and interests. It demonstrates Somalia’s firm commitment to the one-China principle, which China highly commends. There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is enshrined in the UNGA Resolution 2758. It is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends.\nSomaliland is part of Somalia’s territory. China firmly supports the Somali federal government’s effort to safeguard national unification, sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly opposes the Taiwan authorities and Somaliland hosting each other’s institution or having any form of official interaction.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202504/t20250430_11614172.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202504/t20250430_11614167.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to today's regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, Song Tao, Director of the CPC Central Committee Taiwan Affairs Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, attended cross-Strait exchange events held in Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Sichuan, and other places in succession. He met with important Taiwan figures including Hung Hsiu-chu, Lien Sheng-wen, and Liu Chao-hsuan, drawing close attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Please…","Recently, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, successively met with a delegation led by Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, in Nanjing, Jiangsu, on April 17; on the 18th, he held a symposium with mainland Taiwanese business representatives and visited some Taiwan youth participating in “Nanjing Taiwan Week”; on the 19th, he met with Taiwan guests including Alex Lu, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, in Hangzhou, Zhejiang; on the 20th, he attended the cross-Strait grassroots livelihood development exchange conference themed “Strengthening Exchanges on People's Livelihood and Enhancing the Well-being of Compatriots”; and on the 21st, he met in Chengdu, Sichuan, with a delegation led by Liu Chao-hsuan, the Taiwan-side chairman of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, and on the 22nd, he attended the 2025 Straits Integrated Development Exchange Conference in Sichuan themed “Jointly Cultivating New Momentum and Promoting Integrated Development.” Against the complex backdrop of the DPP authorities' continuous obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, which escalates confrontation and opposition, and of the United States' wanton imposition of tariffs that shock the global economic order, these activities were important measures by the CPC Central Committee's Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council to actively promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to show concern for and support Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises. They sent a clear signal: unwavering determination to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, sincere concern for the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, and firm and forceful opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces.\nPeople from all walks of life on the island, Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, took an active part in the above activities. They said that this strengthened the confidence of Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises to firmly take root in mainland development, and that the institutional advantages and economic resilience of the mainland are the fundamental guarantee for withstanding risks. The mainland has a complete industrial system, a broad market space, and enormous investment and consumption potential, and governments at all levels show concern for and support Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises. Taiwan-funded businesses and enterprises support the countermeasures the state has taken against the United States, and are confident that they, together with the country, can win this tariff war and achieve sustained and healthy development on the mainland. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should visit each other often and engage in deeper exchanges. The DPP authorities seek to create a “chilling effect” on cross-Strait exchanges; this is unpopular and destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698515.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","厦门卫视记者","Could the spokesperson introduce recent cross-Strait youth exchange activities? Also, what internship and employment activities are there for Taiwan youth?","First question. Entering the second quarter, cross-Strait youth exchange activities continued to be active.\nFrom April 17 to 22, the “Jiangsu·Nanjing Taiwan Week” was held in Nanjing, Jiangsu. Under the theme “Good Nanjing, Taiwan — Together Toward the Future,” more than a thousand Taiwan industry and commerce groups, grassroots residents, youth representatives and mainland representatives took part in more than 20 events covering history and culture, grassroots communities, urban management, youth arts and many other fields, comprehensively showcasing the achievements of Jiangsu's high-quality economic and social development and deepening exchanges and interactions between Jiangsu and Taiwan in all fields.\nOn April 18, the second “Starting from Pottery, Dancing in Foshan” Fo-Tai series of cultural exchange activities and the launch ceremony for the Taiwan Youth Study Action were held in Foshan City, Guangdong Province, with nearly 300 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth participating. Combining Foshan's Lingnan cultural characteristics with its advantages in manufacturing and vocational training, the activities launched the “Walking Together with Beauty · Career Creation in Foshan” premium Taiwan youth study route, covering beauty, food, home design, livestreaming sales and other content. They promoted the signing of cooperation agreements by 10 cross-Strait industry associations and institutions, and released the “Several Measures of Foshan City to Support Taiwan Youth in Internships, Employment and Entrepreneurship,” providing more platforms and conveniences and empowering Taiwan youth to develop in Foshan.\nOn April 18, the 2025 Straits (Xiamen) Baosheng Cixi Cultural Activities across the Taiwan Strait were launched at the Qingjiao Cixi Ancestral Temple in Haicang District, Xiamen City. More than 600 representatives of temples and believers from both sides of the Strait gathered in Haicang to jointly take part in the folk ceremony. Themed “Youthful Cross-Strait Charm, Passing Down Cixi's Legacy,” this year's activities used exchanges between folk temples as the link, showcasing the inheritance and development of the folk culture of Baosheng Dadi (Emperor Baosheng). During the activities, the Haicang District Taiwan Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Sharing Conference was held, actively building a platform and providing opportunities for Taiwan youth coming to Xiamen to develop, through policy interpretation, exchange and sharing, and on-site visits.\nSecond question. In just over a month, students at Taiwan's universities will enter their summer vacation, and all localities have made preparations for internship and employment activities for Taiwan youth on the mainland. I would like to report several of them.\nFrom April 21 to 26, the Sichuan-Taiwan Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference, themed “Gathering in Tianfu, Building Dreams in Sichuan,” was held in Chengdu, with more than 160 Taiwan youth and cross-Strait media representatives attending. At the exchange conference, 746 enterprises operating in Sichuan released 6,793 internship and employment positions for Taiwan youth, and issued the “Chengdu Taiwan Youth Service Ambassador” initiative to help Taiwan youth take root in, integrate into, and realize their dreams in Sichuan.\nThe 2025 “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” internship and employment activity for Taiwan youth was officially launched in Shenzhen in mid-April, offering Taiwan youth more than 1,200 internship positions and 1,800 employment positions, including positions at Fortune Global 500 companies and industry leaders such as Tencent, BYD, Mindray, SF Express and Bank of China, covering technology, finance, law, healthcare and other industries. This year's internship and employment activity offered community governance positions for the first time, providing flexible internship periods of 1 to 6 months and 277 positions that can convert from internship to formal employment.\nOn April 26, Xiamen City held the “Come Forward for Employment, Dreaming in Huli — First Taiwan University Graduate Employment, Internship and Trainee Two-Way Matching Conference.” More than 50 enterprises offered over 600 positions, and more than 200 Taiwan students from 59 universities took part in the matching conference. Going forward, Huli District of Xiamen will also set up an online recruitment platform to provide practical and efficient employment services, helping more Taiwan students to find employment, internships and trainee positions in Xiamen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The National Film Administration and China Media Group recently launched the “Chinese Film Consumption Year” campaign, which has drawn wide attention and praise from Taiwan compatriots. Many Taiwan compatriots said they have already snapped up discount coupons and plan to follow the films on a trip to the mainland during the May Day holiday. What comments do you have on this?","It is understood that during this year's May Day holiday, more than 10 new films will be released, including “Dumpling Queen,” “Unique,” and “Hunting Gold: The Game,” covering multiple genres such as drama, action, comedy, and animation, to meet audiences' diverse viewing needs. In addition, the film “Stories of Xigui,” set in the Xigui tea mountains of Lincang, Yunnan, and telling a story of cross-Strait young people in which tea serves as the medium, letters convey emotions, and home is the place to return to, held its premiere ceremony in Kunming, Yunnan on April 29 and will soon be screened widely. It will also launch offline experience activities titled “Follow the Film to Taste Tea” and “Find the 100 Most Stylish Teahouses.” The film “Ne Zha 2,” which has broken multiple global animated film records and is deeply loved by audiences, will continue to be screened until May 31. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland and share the May Day film feast, unlocking countless viewing experiences: stepping into cinemas to enjoy the charm of light and shadow, and stepping out to visit filming locations or taste the foods featured in the films, making the viewing experience richer.\nThe “China Film Consumption Year” campaign runs throughout the year, covering all key release periods, and centers on cross-industry and cross-departmental coordination around film. Its content is rich, its benefits are increasing, and it offers many tangible advantages. We welcome broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to keep following it and participate enthusiastically, and to come to the mainland to experience the joy and beauty of linked “film, television and cultural tourism.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698507.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","Recently, the Ministry of Commerce and five other departments issued the “Notice on Further Optimizing the Departure Tax Refund Policy to Expand Inbound Consumption,” lowering the minimum refund threshold for departure tax refunds from 500 yuan to 200 yuan and raising the cash refund cap from 10,000 yuan to 20,000 yuan, which has drawn great public attention. May I ask whether this policy applies to residents of…","The relevant optimized departure tax refund policy applies to Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. The policy has three main highlights:\nFirst, expanding tax refund stores so Taiwan compatriots can shop at more good stores. This policy proposes optimizing the layout of tax refund stores and encouraging localities to add departure tax refund stores in places frequented by overseas travelers, such as large shopping malls, pedestrian streets, tourist attractions, resort areas, cultural and museum venues, airports, passenger ports and hotels. It supports qualified regions in creating a number of departure tax refund special streets and improving the accessibility of tax refund stores.\nSecond, increasing the number of tax-refundable goods so Taiwan compatriots can buy more good products. This policy proposes lowering the starting threshold for departure tax refunds from 500 yuan to 200 yuan. On the one hand, this lowers the threshold for tax refund shopping; on the other hand, it promotes an increase and expansion of tax refund stores, allowing more specialty shops, souvenir shops, gift shops and others with lower average transaction values to join the tax refund stores, providing a broader range of product choices.\nThird, optimizing tax refund services so Taiwan compatriots can get refunds more conveniently. This policy optimizes the handling process, improves the departure tax refund management system, raises store invoicing efficiency and shortens passenger waiting times. It also substantially raises the cash tax refund limit from 10,000 yuan to 20,000 yuan, and encourages relevant institutions to provide tax refund services through multiple methods, such as mobile payment, bank cards and cash, to better meet diversified payment service needs.\nSome netizens have estimated that when Taiwan compatriots use their Taiwan compatriot permits and shopping receipts to process departure tax refunds on the mainland, it is equivalent to enjoying a 10% discount. We also remind Taiwan compatriots who shop on the mainland to remember to process their tax refunds before returning to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698512.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","First question: According to reports, Taiwan's competent authority for internal affairs recently launched a “Information Disclosure Zone for Exchanges of Religious and Other Groups to the Mainland,” requiring religious and social groups to fill in travel dates, locations, purposes, and other details before going to the mainland, and to publicly disclose them. What comments do you have on this? Second question: A…","On the first question: This is the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' unreasonable obstruction of normal cross-Strait exchanges in religious and folk belief culture, another trick in its large-scale \"green terror\" and creation of a \"chilling effect,\" and a brutal deprivation of the basic rights and freedoms of temples and believers on the island. This despicable trick cannot suppress the desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer to each other, nor can it stop the great trend of cross-Strait exchanges and integration, and it will inevitably fail under the joint opposition of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nOn the second question: We have also noted this program. It is understood that this variety show focuses on the senior population and creates a journey to fulfill life bucket lists for elderly travelers across various places. During the first stops in Quanzhou and Zhangzhou, Ms. Lin from Taiwan participated in her first ancestral worship ceremony in her life at the Lin Clan Ancestral Hall in Wushi Town, Zhangpu County, Zhangzhou, Fujian Province, fulfilling her family's 300-year wish to trace its roots. This journey to find roots across the strait vividly presents the inseparable bloodline ties between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, fully embodying the idea that \"both sides of the Strait are one family.\" As a netizen commented, \"The call of blood is more accurate than any navigation.\" Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are relatives, and all of China, including the mainland and Taiwan, is the common home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We sincerely welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a look around and seek their roots and sense of belonging, and we also support the film and television circles on both sides of the Strait in launching more good programs and works that reflect the shared language, culture, destiny, and fate of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The United States announced additional tariffs on Taiwan. Lai Qingde said that trade consultations with the US will be conducted on the basis of zero tariffs, which has triggered widespread doubts within Taiwan's industry sector, which believes it will have a major impact on the island's agriculture, fisheries and grassroots industries. What is your comment?","Under “America First,” the United States is wielding the “tariff stick” around the world, undermining the multilateral trading system and impacting the world economic order. This has also turned the so-called “reshoring” of Taiwan businesses and the “New Southbound” policy promoted by the DPP authorities into a laughingstock. The DPP authorities not only refuse to correct their mistakes, but keep making them again and again. They treat promoting cross-Strait “decoupling and severing of chains” as a bargaining chip in negotiations with the US and as a pledge of loyalty to the US. This will only make Taiwan more subject to US manipulation, make it more convenient for the US to hollow out Taiwan's advantageous industries and turn Taiwan into a dumping ground for US agricultural products, and further harm Taiwan's economic development rights and the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and outsiders are unreliable. We welcome more industries, farmers, and fishermen on the island to come to the mainland to participate in exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development. The mainland has a sound economic foundation, strong resilience, and great potential, its long-term outlook is favorable, and it has always been the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots to invest and start businesses, and a solid backing for resisting risks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","According to reports, in 2024 TSMC’s Arizona plant in the US continued to lose money, while its plant on the mainland made substantial profits. Even so, TSMC announced that it would expand its investment in the US by US$100 billion. Island public opinion pointed out that people should recognize which markets are more worthy of increased investment. What comment do you have on this?","For the sake of private gain, the DPP authorities have given external forces whatever they demand, treating Taiwan's semiconductor industry and TSMC as a “pledge of loyalty” for “relying on the United States to seek independence,” and handing them over as a “souvenir gift.” They have repeatedly sold out the interests and well-being of the people and enterprises of Taiwan. This behavior, which does not regard “selling out Taiwan” as shameful and instead takes pride in “fawning over the United States,” is opposed by more and more people and enterprises in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","A recent poll published on the island shows that public satisfaction with Lai Ching-te's governance has dropped to just 47.1%, a decline of nearly 10 percentage points from the previous poll, and for the first time, satisfaction and dissatisfaction have formed a “death cross.” Some public opinion analysis holds that this shows the public is highly skeptical of the authorities' abuses of power, such as political…","The people have their own scales. The people of Taiwan want economic development, social stability and peace in the Taiwan Strait, but Lai Ching-te keeps creating political disputes and suppressing dissidents, stirring up cross-Strait confrontation, seeking “independence” and provoking, hollowing out Taiwan's advantageous industries, and selling out Taiwan and inciting war. His conduct runs completely counter to the interests and well-being of the people of Taiwan, naturally arousing growing dissatisfaction and opposition among the people of Taiwan, and will inevitably be abandoned by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, Shen Yu-chung, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the share of Taiwanese businesses' investment in the mainland in Taiwan's total outbound investment fell from 83.8% in 2010 to 7.5% in 2024, and he advocated that Taiwanese businesses accelerate their withdrawal from the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities, driven by their nature of seeking “independence,” are accustomed to fabricating rumors and smearing others, interfering with cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. The lies they fabricate crumble in the face of facts.\nThe economies on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation's economy, and compatriots on both sides are a community of shared destiny. The mainland's economy is stable and trending positively, and can open broader space for deepening cross-strait integrated development. Facing a turbulent external environment, the mainland's advantages of a large stage, broad market prospects, stable policy expectations and good security are further highlighted, and it has always been the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to invest and do business. In the first quarter of this year, cross-strait trade reached US$70.56 billion, up 15.2% year on year; actual use of Taiwan investment on the mainland was US$1.26 billion, up 127.1% year on year; and 1,592 new Taiwan-invested enterprises were established. More and more Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots are proving with concrete actions that the mainland has always been the best choice for investment and business by broad Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises.\nIn the face of the United States' indiscriminate imposition of tariffs, the motherland's mainland took firm and forceful countermeasures at the first opportunity, demonstrating its determination to defend national development interests, international fairness and justice, and order and rules, and showcasing its confidence in maintaining its own economic development. We will study and resolve the problems and difficulties faced by Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises, implement equal treatment, increase support, strengthen the connection of cross-strait industrial and supply chains, support Taiwan-funded enterprises in participating in the implementation of major national strategies, help Taiwan enterprises transform and upgrade, expand the domestic market, integrate into the new development pattern, and achieve high-quality development. We hope broad Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will remain confident, take a long-term view, actively participate in cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, join hands to resist external risks and challenges, and jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698513.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Recently, the US think tank Brookings Institution released a poll showing that the proportion of Taiwan residents who consider the US “untrustworthy” or “very untrustworthy” increased by 13.9 percentage points compared with the previous survey. The proportion who consider the US “very positive” or “positive” decreased by 20.8 percentage points. And 46.7% consider it “impossible” or “very unlikely” that the US…","Why are more and more Taiwan people not trusting the United States? I believe the main reason is that Taiwan people have clearly seen that the United States always pursues “America First,” and that Americans care only about “American interests.” In the eyes of Americans, Taiwan's real value lies in being “fat meat,” an “ATM,” and a tool for containing the mainland. What has the United States recently done to Taiwan? It is forcing Taiwan to do four things: first, it is forcing Taiwan's core advantageous industries, represented by TSMC, to transfer to the United States through investment or joint ventures; second, it is demanding that the DPP authorities raise the defense budget and spend more of Taiwan people's hard-earned money on American weapons; third, it is trying to arm Taiwan, clamoring to turn Taiwan into a “war porcupine,” inciting “people's war in the streets,” pushing Taiwan's youth onto the battlefield, and turning temples in the island into ammunition depots; fourth, it intends to impose high tariffs on Taiwan, seriously impacting related industries.\nIs the United States “protecting Taiwan” or “harming Taiwan,” and are the DPP authorities “safeguarding Taiwan” or “destroying Taiwan”? The facts speak for themselves, and Taiwan people can certainly see this more and more clearly. If the United States is allowed to take whatever it wants, then when Taiwan's value has been drained dry, the outcome will inevitably be a change from “chess piece” to “discarded piece.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698508.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","According to Philippine media reports, the Philippine government has relaxed restrictions on interactions with Taiwan authorities’ officials, including allowing Philippine officials to visit Taiwan. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region of China. The Philippine side should abide by the one-China principle, stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. No matter how the DPP authorities cling to external forces to provoke “independence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","First question: The Taiwan Affairs Office’s WeChat official account recently published “Questions and Answers on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758,” which has drawn attention on both sides of the Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council said of this: “UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 does not mention Taiwan, does not confirm that Taiwan is part of the People’s Republic of China, and does not authorize the…","First question. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted by the 26th session in 1971, restored the lawful rights and seat of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations, representing all of China including Taiwan, on the premise of recognizing that Taiwan belongs to China. The historical facts are clear, and the legal basis is well-founded.\nFor 54 years, the United Nations and its specialized agencies have handled Taiwan-related issues strictly in accordance with the one-China principle and the spirit of General Assembly Resolution 2758. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, for the purpose of seeking “independence,” deliberately distort General Assembly Resolution 2758, which is a distortion of the facts, a trampling of international law, and a blatant challenge to the international order and rules. No matter how the Democratic Progressive Party authorities fabricate stories, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. They cannot shake the international community's adherence to the one-China principle, and they cannot stop the trend that China will inevitably be reunified and will certainly be reunified.\nIn response to the Democratic Progressive Party authorities ignoring historical and legal facts and colluding with external forces to distort and smear General Assembly Resolution 2758 in an attempt to mislead Taiwan's public and international opinion, the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account released six articles in the “Questions and Answers on General Assembly Resolution 2758 series” from April 23 to 28. These articles thoroughly explained the core meaning of General Assembly Resolution 2758, restored the facts, corrected the record, and enhanced the correct understanding of the one-China principle among Taiwan compatriots and the international community. The series of Q&A articles drew wide attention and discussion from people on both sides of the Strait, with more than 21 million views.\nSecond question. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Regarding the question of Taiwan's participation in World Health Organization activities, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is also the fundamental principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which has led to the disappearance of the political foundation for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly. The fact that Taiwan cannot attend is entirely the result of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. What they truly care about is not the health and well-being of Taiwan's people, but making political capital by creating disturbances and piggybacking on meetings to deceive the people on the island. The result will only be self-humiliation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698509.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, while attending an event, Lai Ching-te once again touted the “two-state theory,” claiming that as long as “China” is willing to engage in exchanges and cooperation with equal dignity, seeking peaceful and mutually beneficial development across the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te once again promoted the “two-state theory.” This is a blatant provocation to seek independence, and once again exposes his true face as a “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and a “creator of Taiwan Strait crises.”\nBoth sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. No matter what Lai Ching-te says or does, he cannot change this historical and legal fact. The root cause of the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermine the common political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, and collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking independence.\nWe have repeatedly stressed that as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and both sides recognize that they belong to one China, the two sides can conduct dialogue and consultation. Denying the “1992 Consensus,” deviating from the one-China principle, and plotting “Taiwan independence” and division make dialogue and consultation between the two sides impossible. The DPP authorities’ so-called “equal dignity” is an attempt to change the historical and legal fact that both sides belong to one China, and to achieve cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges on the basis of the “two-state theory.” Their scheme will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698514.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Taiwan's education authorities said they have asked relevant departments to study and take stock of the university departments and institutes involved in “national security, confidential, and core key technology projects.” After compiling the results, these will be included in enrollment restrictions for Mainland students for the 2025 academic year, to facilitate follow-up control and effectively ensure…","This is yet another piece of evidence that the DPP authorities artificially restrict cross-Strait exchanges and mainland students studying in Taiwan. The DPP authorities have repeatedly reached their political hand into the field of cross-Strait educational exchanges. Previously, they banned exchanges and cooperation between the island and 10 mainland universities, and now they want to tinker with the majors for admitting mainland students. This repeatedly exposes their sinister intent to “oppose everything from the mainland,” obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and undermine cross-Strait relations.\nThe mainland has achieved a development miracle recognized worldwide, which would not have been possible without the great progress in education and science and technology. Guided by the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” the doors of many universities are open to Taiwan students who strive to improve themselves. We welcome young people on the island with ambitions to take the entrance examinations for mainland universities, and we will create better conditions for them to grow and succeed on the mainland. We hope that young people on both sides of the Strait will set lofty goals, walk together, and contribute the energy of youth to realizing their life ideals and the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","A poll on the island shows that 59.3% of the public opposes the DPP's push for a “great recall.” The KMT recently said that the true “great recall” is to “recall the dictator, recall Lai Ching-te.” What is your comment on this?","Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has persistently adhered to a separatist “Taiwan independence” position. On the one hand, he has schemed to promote “independence,” provoked confrontation, escalated cross-Strait hostility, and fawned on the United States, selling out Taiwan and pledging allegiance. On the other hand, he has further escalated the creation of “green terror” on the island, suppressed political opponents, engaged in large-scale judicial persecution, and aggravated social division, which has aroused strong dissatisfaction across all walks of life in Taiwan. Lai Ching-te is attempting to accelerate the pace of “Taiwan independence” through dictatorial centralization of power. This seriously violates the trend of history and the mainstream public opinion on the island, and it is doomed to fail. We hope compatriots across Taiwan will see clearly the evil essence of Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, who will stop at nothing to seek “independence,” will firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and “green terror,” and will safeguard their own interests and welfare and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait through practical actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","To cooperate with the so-called “17 strategies” proposed by Lai Ching-te, Taiwan's “Tourism Administration” recently required Taiwan tourism operators to dissuade Taiwan residents from traveling to the mainland, which has drawn criticism from the island's industry. What comments do you have on this?","This absurd farce by the DPP authorities exposes their hypocritical face of supposedly “taking care of Taiwan's tourism industry” and reveals their guilty panic over fear that Taiwan's people will learn the real situation on the mainland.\nThe mainstream public opinion on the island, calling for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, cannot be ignored by anyone, and the wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer to one another cannot be suppressed by anyone. The DPP authorities' demand that tourism operators on the island dissuade Taiwan residents from traveling to the mainland is cutting off their livelihoods and breaking their rice bowls. Their attempt to prevent Taiwan residents from traveling to the mainland is even more perverse, trampling on human rights. We welcome compatriots from Taiwan to visit the mainland more often and to participate more in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We are willing to provide convenience and good service for everyone, so that everyone can feel the warmth of “cross-Strait families are one family” and share in the fruits of the mainland's development and progress.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","First question. The United States has announced it will impose a 32% tariff on Taiwan, and island public opinion has pointed out that this will directly affect 15% to 20% of Taiwan’s GDP this year. The “response strategy” put forward by the Lai Ching-te authorities has been criticized as “pie-in-the-sky relief” and “a drop in the bucket,” sparking strong dissatisfaction across all sectors of the island. What is…","First question. The United States has provoked tariff and trade wars across the globe, seriously undermining the multilateral trading system and shocking the world economic order, and also seriously harming cross-strait economic and trade development. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should join hands to meet external challenges and jointly safeguard legitimate development rights and the overall interests of the Chinese nation. In response to the United States' indiscriminate imposition of tariffs, the mainland of China immediately and resolutely launched countermeasures, demonstrating our backbone and confidence in striking back against tariff bullying, effectively defending international fairness, justice, order, and rules, and safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities have been excessively servile, allowing themselves to be pushed around at will. Their so-called “countermeasure strategy” is in fact a “plan to please the United States through large-scale purchases and large-scale investment.” Disregarding the people's livelihood and habitually “selling out Taiwan,” they are soft when facing the United States and kneel when dealing with it, arousing strong dissatisfaction across all sectors of society on the island. The Lai Ching-te authorities are violating economic laws and market rules, catering to external forces in pushing for “decoupling and severing supply chains” across the Strait. What they damage is the competitiveness of Taiwan's enterprises, what they deprive is the development rights of Taiwan compatriots, and what they weaken is the economic prospects of Taiwan. If they persist in their obstinacy, they will surely reap what they sow.\nSecond question. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' incitement of hostility and confrontation across the Strait will only aggravate turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Pursuing militarism will only seriously harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Their attempt to “seek independence through force” will only bring war and danger to Taiwan. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society. No one can sever the blood ties and kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and no one can stop the steps of compatriots on both sides of the Strait in pursuing common development. Only by firmly pursuing the path of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations can we maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and safeguard the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Reports say this year's “Urban Resilience Exercise” on the island will be held in central Taiwan in mid-July, and six temples in Taichung City have been designated as arms storage points. Earlier, the DPP authorities planned to turn Taiwan's 13,000 convenience stores into “wartime hubs,” to facilitate “distributing rations and medical supplies in the event of war breaking out across the Taiwan Strait.” What is…","The Lai Ching-te authorities have been going all out to exaggerate the so-called “mainland threat” and are accelerating “preparing for war to seek independence,” once again proving that they are “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises.” This will only provoke even stronger dissatisfaction and opposition from the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾中视新闻记者","Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council recently said that Taiwan residents may not register household status on the mainland, or they will lose their Taiwan identity. The criteria for determining whether someone has registered include, in addition to holding a mainland resident identity card, a residence permit. What is your comment on the Mainland Affairs Council’s repeated tightening of related policies?","The competent mainland authorities have long issued Taiwan Compatriot Permits, Residence Permits and Settlement Permits to Taiwan compatriots. The three types of documents carry different functions. The Taiwan Compatriot Permit is a travel permit for Taiwan residents traveling to and from the mainland, and it is a document that Taiwan residents must obtain to travel to and from the mainland. The Residence Permit is a document issued by the mainland to meet the convenience needs of Taiwan compatriots for study, work and daily life on the mainland. The purpose of the mainland issuing these two documents is to provide convenience and benefit to the people, and Taiwan compatriots do not need mainland household registration to apply for either of them. The Settlement Permit is a temporary, transitional document issued to Taiwan residents who have been approved to settle and register households on the mainland, and is held for a short term.\nThe mainland side has always actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and has done its utmost to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and to help them develop on the mainland. Taiwan compatriots holding the card-type Taiwan Compatriot Permit may travel to and from the mainland at any time within its five-year validity period. Holders of the Residence Permit may legally enjoy a number of basic public services on the mainland, as well as conveniences in accommodation and transportation. At the same time, the personal information of Taiwan compatriots who obtain these documents is effectively protected according to law. Facts prove that these policies are highly praised by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and these documents are increasingly welcomed by more Taiwan compatriots, who find them useful, practical and easy to use.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” disrupt normal cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, and seek to push for “decoupling, severing links and reducing flows” across the Strait. They repeatedly engage in political hype, deliberately confuse various types of documents, and intimidate and obstruct Taiwan compatriots from applying for various documents. Their aim is to create a “green terror,” obstruct and sabotage the rapprochement between compatriots on both sides, and deceive the public on the island in order to pursue “Taiwan independence” behind closed doors. This reckless conduct has met with strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition from an increasing number of people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698511.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","The Taiwan education authorities recently promoted so-called teaching materials related to “Recognizing the Chinese Threat” and “National Identity,” which has drawn criticism from public opinion on the island. They believe that education has become a political tool for the DPP authorities to promote “gradual Taiwan independence,” and that this will have a profound impact on young students' value perceptions and…","The DPP authorities, out of selfish interests in seeking “independence,” have once again stretched political hands into education, an undertaking that should impart knowledge and cultivate virtue. Their aim is to use textbooks and classrooms to “wash minds” and forcibly instill erroneous “Taiwan independence” ideas in young students, cultivating a social base for stirring up cross-Strait confrontation.\nTaiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China’s territory. This is a fact that cannot be changed and will not be tolerated to be changed. The Chinese cultural genes flowing in the bloodline of Taiwan compatriots cannot be erased by any human factor. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: anyone who splits the country is a disgrace to the nation, and anyone who creates cross-Strait confrontation will eventually burn themselves playing with fire.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","According to reports, the non-governmental organization “Taiwan Information Environment Research Center” recently published a research report stating that in 2024 nearly 40,000 Taiwan residents took part in cross-Strait exchange activities, about 3% more than in 2023, with agricultural and tourism exchange activities the most numerous. These are common industries through which the mainland applies political…","First, it must be pointed out that this report is entirely driven by ulterior motives. It is a routine trick of the DPP authorities in manipulating “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment.\nIn fact, in 2024 the number of Taiwan residents who took part in cross-Strait exchanges was far more than 40,000. The desire to expand cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion across all sectors of Taiwan. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, with deep blood ties, a common cultural heritage and close interest integration. No force can separate us, and there is no reason not to exchange and cooperate. The path of cross-Strait exchanges was walked out by compatriots on both sides, and the foundation of economic cooperation was built by enterprises on both sides. Following the wishes of compatriots, in line with economic laws, it benefits compatriots on both sides.\nThe DPP authorities and their auxiliary forces, out of their “Taiwan independence” nature, fear cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, are afraid of compatriots on both sides drawing closer, and hope the two sides will “decouple, break chains and reduce flows.” Out of this sinister mindset, they have plotted and schemed to obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, attempting to reinforce a “green terror,” create a “chilling effect,” and suppress anti-“independence” people. Their reckless actions cannot change the trend of vigorous development of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and cannot stop the steady deepening of cross-Strait integrated development. More and more Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots are demonstrating through practical action that breaking down barriers through exchange, replacing confrontation with cooperation, and creating the future through integration is the right path for developing cross-Strait relations and safeguarding their own interests and well-being. “When the Great Way prevails, the world belongs to all.” The door to cross-Strait exchanges will only open wider, and the road to integrated development will only grow broader.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The mainland has stressed that PLA exercises target “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. However, during PLA exercises earlier this month, a simulated strike destroyed the LNG receiving station at Yong'an Fishing Port in Kaohsiung. If the LNG receiving station were damaged, it would cause large-scale power outages across Taiwan, and the impact would not be limited to “Taiwan independence” elements; the broad…","It must be pointed out that what we are cracking down on is the separatist words and deeds of the Lai Ching-te authorities, what we are countering is their provocations aimed at “independence,” and what we are safeguarding is peace in the Taiwan Strait. It is absolutely not aimed at the broad Taiwan compatriots. The Lai Ching-te authorities provoked first, and the PLA countered afterward; the deterrent actions taken are legitimate, necessary, and reasonable.\nWe hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will discern right from wrong, further recognize the danger and harm of “Taiwan independence” provoking conflict, firmly oppose and stop any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, and effectively safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报报业集团《封面新闻》记者","Recently, some media on the island reported that after Honduras severed ties with Taiwan, its white shrimp industry collapsed, and a presidential candidate proposed that, if elected, he would seek to restore diplomatic ties with Taiwan. The head of Taiwan's department responsible for external affairs said Taiwan helps its “allies” in South America prosper through economic plans, and that if other countries wish…","After China and Honduras signed the early harvest arrangement under their free trade agreement in February 2024, China has continued to reach agreements with Honduras step by step and advance trade cooperation, including on white shrimp. At the end of September 2024, Honduran white shrimp officially entered the mainland market. The DPP authorities and certain media outlets on the island with particular positions have repeatedly and deliberately hyped this issue. This is a complete distortion of the facts and is driven by ulterior motives.\nThe one-China principle is a broad consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. It reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme to achieve so-called “diplomatic breakthroughs,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","On April 26, the KMT launched a protest rally, and large numbers of Taiwan residents gathered on Ketagalan Boulevard in Taipei to strongly protest the Lai Ching-te authorities’ “dictatorship” and “green terror.” What is your comment on this?","We have noted the relevant situation. The Lai Ching-te authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, continuously engage in provocations to seek “independence,” obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, leading to tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. They use every means to suppress dissenters and persecute people who support cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and the shadow of “green terror” hangs over the island. Without any bottom line, they fawn over the United States and pledge loyalty, kowtowing in the face of US bullying and extortion and handing over Taiwan's interests on a platter. Less than a year after Lai Ching-te took office, Taiwan has fallen into political chaos, a development predicament, and a security crisis, causing widespread public resentment. The April 26 rally is a concentrated expression of Taiwan people's anger and dissatisfaction with Lai Ching-te's reckless and retrograde conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, some videos on new media platforms such as Xiaohongshu and Douyin have used the so-called “shortcut to Taiwan” as a gimmick, drawing much attention from netizens. Some people have also discussed trying to travel to Taiwan this way to take part in the so-called “World Veterans Games.” What is your comment on this?","We have noted the relevant situation. It must be pointed out that mainland residents traveling to Taiwan must hold the designated documents, namely the Mainland Residents' Travel Permit to Taiwan and its endorsement. We encourage and support normal personnel exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, while also reminding the relevant individuals not to falsely claim they are going to a third location as a pretext for making a detour to Taiwan, so as to avoid infringement of their personal rights and interests and failure to ensure their personal safety. Relevant netizens should not believe, spread, or attempt to travel to Taiwan to attend events or sports competitions via a detour through a third location or similar methods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202504/t20250430_12698510.htm"],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Regarding the KMT’s “4·26” mass rally, Lai Ching-te said, “If you want to protest, you should go to Beijing.” What comments do you have?","In the nearly one year since Lai Qingde took office, he has stubbornly clung to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” ignoring the mainstream public opinion on the island calling for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, as well as the widespread call for improved people's livelihoods. He has been currying favor with the United States, selling out Taiwan, seeking “independence,” and provoking confrontation, carrying out a “green terror” campaign, arbitrarily persecuting political rivals, and provoking strong dissatisfaction among the Taiwanese people. The April 26 rally was a concentrated reflection of this public opinion. Those who do wrong will eventually bring about their own downfall; those who act recklessly and go against the tide will inevitably reap the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-04-30","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council has determined that applying for a Taiwan settlement permit in the mainland is equivalent to obtaining mainland household registration. What is your comment on this? Second question: The DPP’s push for a “mass recall” has also sparked disputes within the party, and some DPP members have said that people should not “smear or paint red” others just because they hold…","First question. As I have already said, the Taiwan Compatriot Permit and the Residence Permit do not require mainland household registration. The Permit for Settlement is a temporary, transitional certificate issued to Taiwan residents who have been approved to settle in the mainland, and is held for a short period.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities deliberately confuse the various types of certificates. In essence, they aim to intimidate and obstruct Taiwan compatriots from applying for the various certificates, to create “green terror,” and to obstruct and sabotage compatriots on both sides of the Strait from drawing closer and visiting one another, closing the door on the island to pursue “Taiwan independence.” This reckless course has met with increasing strong dissatisfaction and opposition from more and more Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question. The Lai Ching-te authorities have abused their power and acted recklessly, “selling out Taiwan and provoking war,” which has aroused growing dissatisfaction and anger among more and more Taiwan residents.\nThird question. The reunification of the motherland is an unstoppable historical trend. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and, with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort, strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. However, we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is aimed at “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces.\nThe current situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause is that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and intensify collusion with external forces, continuously carrying out provocations to seek “independence,” and increasingly pushing Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war. The “Anti-Secession Law” has drawn an insurmountable red line for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and provides ample legal basis for the struggle against separatism and interference. We have firm resolve, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202504/t20250430_12698478.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-05-08","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan leader Lai Ching-te told Western diplomats in an event marking the end of World War Two that Taiwan and Europe are facing the threat of “a new authoritarian bloc”. Do you have any comment on the remarks?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, the World Anti-Fascist War, and the restoration of Taiwan. Taiwan’s restoration to China in 1945 is a victorious outcome of WWII and an integral part of the postwar international order. A series of instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, have all affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan, and laid the groundwork of the postwar international order.\nIt’s the DPP authorities’ go-to tactic to cover up its nature of seeking “Taiwan independence” under the pretext of “democracy” and “freedom.” No matter what they say or do, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China’s territory, nor can they change the prevailing international consensus on the one-China principle.\nWe ask relevant countries to abide by the political commitments that they made to China on the Taiwan question, stop the behavior of relevant personnel that goes against these commitments, stop supporting such political stunt of those separatist forces, and stop sending any wrong signal to them.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250508_11617555.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250508_11617542.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-05-08","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that during the Philippine-U.S. \"Balikatan\" exercise, the Chinese aircraft carrier Shandong appeared in the waters north of the Philippines. Some analysts believe this might be a response to the Philippine-U.S. military exercise, or to the Philippine patrol vessel's entering into the waters near Huangyan Dao. Furthermore, the Philippine Navy spokesperson claimed that the Philippine military and…","The Shandong aircraft carrier task group was conducting its annual training mission in relevant waters to further test and enhance the integrated combat capabilities of the carrier task group. This is in accordance with international law and common practice, and is not directed at any specific country or target.\nCertain individuals in the Philippines are colluding with external forces such as the U.S., to \"stir up the sea\" for selfish gains, undermining peace and stability in the South China Sea region. They even attempt to play with fire on the Taiwan question. We sternly warn the Philippine side to cease its infringements and provocations, and stop offending China's core interest in any form. China will continue to take resolute and forceful measures to defend its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250508-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16384872.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-05-12","Lin Jian","China Daily","It was reported that on May 9, the Taiwan authorities issued wrongful comments on the contribution of the Communist Party of China to the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, specifically regarding what is said in the China-Russia joint statement. The Taiwan authorities said that the “Republic of China’s sovereignty over Taiwan” was “confirmed in the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam…","Relevant rhetoric once again revealed that it is the DPP authorities’ go-to tactic to distort history and facts and spread disinformation. It also shows their nefarious inclination to use any means possible to advance their separatist agenda.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, the World Anti-Fascist War, and the restoration of Taiwan. Under the national united front against Japanese aggression advocated and built by the Communist Party of China, Chinese sons and daughters, unintimidated and united in their efforts, made great sacrifices to defeat the Japanese militarists and wrote a heroic chapter of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. Taiwan’s restoration to China in 1945 is a victorious outcome of WWII and an integral part of the post-war international order. A series of instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, all confirm China’s sovereignty over Taiwan, which is solidly rooted in history and the law.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Although the two sides across the Taiwan Strait have yet to be reunified, the fact that the Chinese mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China and that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China has never and will not be changed. This is the true status quo in the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan is never a country, not in the past, and never in the future.\nNo matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the fact—supported by history and the law—that Taiwan is part of China’s territory, nor can they change the prevailing international commitment to the one-China principle. China will be reunified, and this is unstoppable.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250512_11619489.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250512_11619456.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-05-13","Lin Jian","Reuters","About the China-CELAC summit which opened this morning. Our question is, why are the Haiti and Saint Lucia flags at the summit, given both countries have ties with Taiwan?","The China-CELAC Forum is an important platform for mutually beneficial cooperation between China and Latin American and Caribbean States. China always welcomes and supports CELAC member states in participating in activities within the framework of the Forum.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250513_11621984.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250513_11622040.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","On May 7, President Xi Jinping published a signed article in Russian media stressing that this year marks the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, and that Taiwan's return to China is an important part of the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order. The Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and a series of other documents with international legal force have all confirmed…","The signed article by President Xi Jinping published in Russian media clarified the Chinese government's solemn position on the Taiwan question. Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times; its historical course is clear, and its legal basis and facts are plain. In April 1895, after defeat in the First Sino-Japanese War, the Qing government was forced to cede Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. On December 1, 1943, the governments of China, the United States and the United Kingdom issued the Cairo Declaration, announcing that the three powers' purpose was that Japan would return to China all the territories it had stolen from China, such as Northeast China, Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. On July 26, 1945, the Potsdam Proclamation, jointly signed by China, the United States and the United Kingdom and later joined by the Soviet Union, reaffirmed that “the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out.” In September of the same year, Japan signed the Instrument of Surrender, promising to “faithfully fulfill the obligations of the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation.” On October 25, the Chinese government announced the “resumption of the exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan” and held the “Ceremony of Accepting the Surrender of Japanese Forces in Taiwan Province, China Theater” in Taipei. Thus, through a series of documents with international legal effect, China recovered Taiwan both legally and in fact. United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted in 1971, fully reflects and solemnly confirms the one-China principle, namely that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China.\nWe uphold the one-China principle and firmly oppose the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and interference by external forces. This is not only an inevitable requirement for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and defending the country's core interests, but also a due meaning of upholding international fairness and justice, defending the fruits of victory in World War II, and maintaining the postwar international order. The international community should respect historical facts and the authority of the UN General Assembly resolution, and understand and support the Chinese government and the Chinese people in their just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving to complete national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700646.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","During this year's May Day holiday, many Fujian tourists chose Kinmen as their first destination for outbound travel, and four “Mini Three Links” passenger routes also welcomed a surge of cross-Strait compatriots visiting relatives and friends and traveling. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During this year’s May Day holiday, the cross-strait “Mini Three Links” routes continued to operate smoothly, facilitating visits to relatives and friends and tourism for people on both sides of the Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots. According to statistics, four “Mini Three Links” passenger routes—Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Huangqi in Lianjiang to Matsu—deployed a total of 17 vessels, providing an average of 8,568 passenger seats per day. From May 1 to May 5, the “Mini Three Links” routes operated more than 180 trips in total, carrying more than 29,000 passengers, an increase of 127.3% year on year. Among them, more than 12,000 were Taiwan compatriots, an increase of 1.9% year on year.\nTo meet the demand of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for visiting relatives and friends and for tourism, Fuzhou, Xiamen, Quanzhou, and other places launched “Mini Three Links” holiday tourism packages. First, they launched free-admission measures for Taiwan compatriots during the May Day holiday and carried out discount ticket programs for Taiwan compatriots. Second, they offered fashionable tourism activities for Taiwan compatriots visiting the mainland, such as “photographing” airplanes and “eating” on high-speed trains. Third, centered on cross-strait cultural exchange, they launched cultural tourism projects such as intangible cultural heritage experiences and museum exhibitions for “tasting culture.” At the same time, the “Mini Three Links” passenger terminals arranged dedicated staff to patiently explain relevant policies to Taiwan compatriots, provide tourism consultation and transportation route inquiry services, and worked with meteorological departments to forecast severe weather in advance. They also inspected the pontoon ports and fire-fighting and lifesaving facilities in advance to ensure the routes are comfortable and safe.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The 3rd Session of the 4th Council of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) was held in Beijing on May 13. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Third Meeting of the Fourth Council of the Straits Exchange Foundation... (corrected below)","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","On May 7, while paying a state visit to Russia and attending the ceremony marking the 80th anniversary of the victory in the Great Patriotic War of the Soviet Union, President Xi Jinping published a signed article in Russian media, emphasizing that “no matter how the situation on the island of Taiwan changes, and no matter how external forces create trouble, the historical trend that China will eventually be…","The signed article published by President Xi Jinping in Russian media solemnly declared that the historical trend toward national reunification is irresistible. It demonstrates our strategic composure and firm resolve, and sends a clear political signal. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus”, resolutely and forcefully crack down on “Taiwan independence” provocations, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development across the Taiwan Strait, resolutely oppose interference by external forces, broadly unite Taiwan compatriots to jointly advance cross-Strait relations and the process of national reunification, and strive to shape the inevitable trend of national reunification.\nTaiwan is China's sacred territory. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving complete reunification of the motherland is the shared wish of Chinese people at home and abroad. It is the historical trend, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. Although the DPP authorities currently obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and are colluding with external forces to continuously carry out provocations for “independence”, leading to tension across the Taiwan Strait and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, they cannot change the objective fact that both sides belong to one country and one nation, cannot change the universal consensus and basic framework of the international community adhering to the one-China principle, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually and inevitably be reunified. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will follow the historical trend, join hands with compatriots on the mainland to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and make unremitting efforts to achieve national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700647.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Recently, the website of a Taiwan administrative agency removed the term \"Han people\" from its description of Taiwan's population and replaced it with \"other population.\" Public opinion on the island has criticized this as a further step by the Lai Ching-te authorities toward \"de-Sinicization\" and \"de-ancestralization.\" What is your comment on this?","This practice is absurd and utterly ridiculous. Those in the DPP authorities who do these things, especially those who belong to the so-called “remaining population,” I don't know what face they think they have to face their ancestors?! Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same blood, the same culture, and the same history. We all belong to the Chinese nation and are descendants of the Yan and Huang emperors. We are all Chinese, and this is an objective fact that no one can change. Out of their inherent nature of seeking independence and their political self-interest, the DPP authorities resort to all kinds of tricks to push “de-Sinicization,” severing the historical and cultural ties across the Strait. This is unpopular, will not succeed, and will surely be rejected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700639.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan media reported that, to protest the DPP authorities' suppression and persecution of mainland spouses, social organizations on the island called on the public to hold a “Support Mainland Spouses, Oppose Persecution” large-scale march on the 10th. What is your comment on this?","Out of “Taiwan independence” nature and political self-interest, the DPP authorities treat the hundreds of thousands of mainland spouses differently and deliberately make things difficult for them. This is blatant political manipulation and political persecution. Their actions have met with increasing opposition and criticism from more and more Taiwan residents and public opinion, and this rally and march is precisely a concentrated reflection of this public sentiment.\nThe mainland is the maiden home of the vast majority of mainland spouses, and mainland compatriots are their relatives and family members. When wind and rain come, we are obligated, both emotionally and rationally, to shelter the vast majority of mainland spouses from the wind and rain, and to extend a helping hand and provide support to them in safeguarding their legitimate and proper rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700641.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The website of the quarterly Foreign Policy recently published an article by a U.S. foreign affairs expert titled “Trump Should Restrain Taiwan,” which points out that the Trump administration should clearly tell Lai Ching-te that the United States opposes Taiwan “independence,” and move early to contain Lai's provocations against the mainland, so as to avoid Lai's authorities miscalculating and drawing the…","In recent times, a growing number of foreign media outlets, experts and scholars have voiced concern and condemnation over the extreme danger and harmfulness of Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” provocations. The current situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave. The root cause lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities' refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and their collusion with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.”\nI want to stress that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and resolving it is a matter for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait to decide. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Lai Ching-te is about to complete one year in office. Some polls on the island show that 79.5% of the public is dissatisfied with his governance, including 40.5% who are dissatisfied with his handling of cross-Strait relations. May I ask for your evaluation of Lai Ching-te’s first year in office in terms of cross-Strait relations?","Since taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities have acted against mainstream public opinion on the island. They refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, loudly promote separatist fallacies, keep manipulating “anti-China” sentiment, escalate the creation of a “green terror,” and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. They fabricate the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism” to delude the island's public and mislead international opinion. Disregarding economic laws, they seek to “decouple” cross-Strait economic and trade ties and “sever” industrial chains, harming the interests and well-being of island enterprises and people. They curry favor with and pledge allegiance to external forces, selling out Taiwan and harming Taiwan, scheming to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence.” Their actions heighten cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and fully confirm that they are “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises.”\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. No matter what Lai Ching-te says or does, this objective fact cannot be changed. The two sides will eventually be reunified, and reunification is inevitable; no matter how the situation on the island changes or how external forces interfere, they cannot stop this historical trend. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, resolutely safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, and work together to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700645.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the DPP authorities held a so-called “80th anniversary of victory in the European War” commemorative event. Some public opinion on the island has pointed out that this event serves the “Taiwan independence historical view.” In his speech, Lai Ching-te deliberately emphasized the “victory in the European War” while ignoring the victory of the Chinese nation's War of Resistance, distorting the history of…","The Second World War was an unprecedented catastrophe in human history. China, as the main battlefield in Asia, suffered enormous national sacrifice, with military and civilian casualties totaling as many as 35 million, and achieved the great victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. The return of Taiwan to China is precisely an important component of the fruits of victory in the Second World War and of the postwar international order. This history records both the suffering of the Chinese nation and the glory of the Chinese nation.\nLai Ching-te’s speech distorts the history of World War II, switches concepts, confuses right and wrong, and attempts to equate the righteous history of the anti-fascist and anti-aggression struggle of World War II with the DPP’s evil schemes to seek the division of the country. Using the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism” to deceive the people on the island and mislead international public opinion, he is smuggling in his “Taiwan independence” position. This once again exposes his obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature and the ugly face of forgetting his ancestry and betraying the nation.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. Learning from the past to understand the future, compatriots on both sides of the Strait should strengthen their confidence in being upright Chinese, remember history, cherish peace, unite as one, jointly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and create a better future for the Chinese nation. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and his ilk: 80 years ago, China was able to defeat the vicious Japanese invaders and restore Taiwan to China’s territory. Today, 80 years later, the strengthened Chinese nation is even less likely to allow Taiwan to split away from China. Those who pursue “Taiwan independence” separatism will absolutely come to no good end!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700644.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","Taiwan media reported that the DPP authorities are accelerating the procurement of “Patriot” missiles, have drawn Taiwan's Marine Corps to form combat units to guard the “Greater Taipei area,” and have repeatedly conducted so-called drills to respond to a “PLA attack on Taiwan.” Public opinion on the island believes these moves are preparations for Lai Ching-te to “flee at the critical moment.” What is your…","No matter how many weapons the DPP authorities buy or how many “exercises” they hold, they cannot change the fact that “Taiwan independence” leads to a dead end, nor can they stop the historical trend of the motherland’s inevitable reunification. The DPP authorities and politicians know this full well, yet for political self-interest, on the one hand they stir up “resisting China and defending Taiwan,” repeatedly “provoke and incite conflict,” and completely disregard the lives of the people, dragging Taiwan compatriots along as cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence”; on the other hand, they plan escape routes for themselves, hoping to slip away. Such conduct is sinister, despicable, and contemptible. As for the chief culprits of “Taiwan independence,” we will never let them go unpunished. We will hold them accountable for life and deliver historical judgment and the punishment of justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700638.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","On March 26, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office’s government website launched a “Reporting Column on Heinous Conduct by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Thugs and Accomplices Persecuting Taiwan Compatriots.” What is the current situation regarding the reports received? What punitive measures will be taken against the persons reported?","As of May 13, the column had received nearly 6,000 reporting emails, which fully reflects the public's deep loathing of the “Taiwan independence” henchmen and accomplices for their vile acts of undermining cross-strait exchanges and cooperation and persecuting Taiwan compatriots. We will adhere to facts as the basis and law as the standard. After verifying the relevant reported information, we will hold these henchmen and accomplices accountable and severely punish them in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700642.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The New Taiwan dollar exchange rate has recently surged sharply. Public opinion on the island believes this may be related to the US-Taiwan tariff negotiations, with the US demanding, through clauses similar to the “Plaza Accord,” that the New Taiwan dollar voluntarily appreciate in order to reduce the trade deficit with Taiwan. This is another hard blow to the island's industrial sector after the US announced…","Faced with the US's tariff bullying and extreme squeezing of Taiwan, the DPP authorities have long “raised the white flag” and knelt down to beg for mercy. The so-called “negotiations” with the US are merely a show, and will only bring the US side's further demands. Lai Ching-te has claimed that he wants Taiwan's people to “treat suffering as a tonic,” and the “response strategy” he proposed is in fact a “plan to please the US through large-scale purchases and large-scale investment,” a submission and begging for mercy that “sells out Taiwan and kneels to the US.” In the face of common risks and challenges, Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should join hands to safeguard their right to development and national dignity. We are concerned about the difficulties faced by industries and enterprises on the island, and welcome relevant industries and enterprises to come to the mainland to invest and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700640.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","环球网记者","Lai Ching-te recently attended a memorial for Hatta Yoichi in Tainan and said that Taiwan’s relationship with Japan is not just like friends, but like family. Island public opinion criticized him for selective amnesia regarding the painful past of Japanese invaders in the colonial era who massacred Taiwan’s people. What is your comment?","This year marks the 130th anniversary of Japan's occupation of Taiwan, and also the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's defeat of the Japanese invaders and the restoration of Taiwan. Eighty years ago, all sons and daughters of China, including Taiwan compatriots, struggled on with united hearts, facing death without fear. They paid enormous sacrifices to defeat the vicious Japanese militarism, defended national sovereignty and national dignity with blood and lives, and wrote the glorious chapter of the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan.\nAs is well known, during the half century that Japan occupied Taiwan, its crimes were too numerous to record, bringing profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. The Japanese colonial regime brutally suppressed the anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots, and several hundred thousand Taiwan compatriots paid for it with their blood and lives. It forcibly implemented the so-called “Kominka Movement” (imperialization movement), attempting to eradicate the national identity of the Taiwanese people. It plundered Taiwan's resources through the so-called policy of “agricultural Taiwan, industrial Japan.” Lai Ching-te disregards historical facts, refuses to mention at all the calamities suffered by Taiwan compatriots, and instead vigorously promotes the so-called “Taiwan-Japan sentiment,” glossing over and beautifying Japan's colonial rule. This betrayal of the nation is despicable. No matter how he distorts history and fabricates false narratives, he cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can he change the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified.\nWe hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, remember the heroic anti-Japanese deeds of Taiwan's martyrs, deeply recognize the great significance of Taiwan's restoration, clearly recognize the serious harm caused by the Lai Ching-te authorities' pursuit of “Taiwan independence” and separation, and take pride in being upright Chinese. Together with compatriots on the mainland, they should advance the process of national rejuvenation and the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","A recent article in Singapore's \"Lianhe Zaobao\" pointed out that a series of recent democratic regressions by the DPP authorities, including continued tightening of freedom of speech and purging of dissenters, have left Taiwan's \"democracy and freedom\" as a mere facade, with its substance gradually being lost. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities are “fake democracy, real dictatorship.” They are vigorously carrying out “green terror” and “dictatorial politics” on the island. Such reckless acts naturally attract wide questioning and opposition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, multiple power outages have occurred repeatedly in many parts of Kaohsiung and Tainan, causing public concern about a power shortage crisis after the island's “nuclear power drops to zero.” Some public opinion on the island questions whether the DPP authorities' forceful promotion of the “nuclear-free homeland” energy policy has led to repeated electricity price increases on the island, while outages…","In recent years, Taiwan has experienced multiple large-scale power outages, such as the “3·3” island-wide blackout, and accidents affecting tens of thousands of users have occurred repeatedly. For example, Taoyuan City alone recorded 35 power outage incidents within a single month, in April 2024. Ironically, however, Taiwan’s electricity prices have “risen five times in four years,” with a total increase of nearly 50%. The island’s industry and general public are deeply harmed and suffering greatly. At its root, the DPP authorities, defying economic laws and disregarding the well-being of the people, have neither the will nor the ability to solve the island’s economic and livelihood problems.\nThe structural challenges facing Taiwan’s economic development can be fully resolved by expanding cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development. We hold a positive attitude toward cross-Strait electricity grid interconnection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, Lai Qingde accepted an exclusive interview with *Nikkei*, claiming that the mainland uses the free trade system to dump low-priced goods around the world and advocates establishing a global semiconductor “non-red supply chain.” He said that under the premise of equal dignity he is willing to engage in exchanges and cooperation with the mainland and seek peaceful coexistence and common prosperity across…","For a long time, the mainland has practiced the concept of free trade, abided by and implemented World Trade Organization rules, and made important contributions to safeguarding the global multilateral trading system and the stability and smooth flow of industrial and supply chains. The Lai Ching-te authorities, on the one hand, shamelessly sell out Taiwan and curry favor with the United States, imposing high tariffs on the United States in a “strike the left cheek and then offer the right” posture. On the other hand, they advocate “non-red supply chains,” attempting to decouple and cut off cross-Strait economic ties and use ideology to lead an economic “small circle.” This fully exposes their essence of kowtowing to and fawning over the United States.\nTaiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. As long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and both sides recognize that they belong to one China, both sides can engage in dialogue and consultation. The so-called “equal dignity” of the Lai Ching-te authorities is an attempt to change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and to achieve cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges on the basis of the “two-state theory.” Their scheme will never succeed.\nThe historical trend that China will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified, cannot be stopped. Our will to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification is as firm as a rock, and our capability is invincible. Pursuing “Taiwan independence” and separatism leads only to a dead end. All schemes that go against the trend and against the overall interests of the nation are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","台湾中视新闻记者","First question. The Golden Statue of Minister Xiao Taifu from Fujian Quanzhou's Fumei Temple recently traveled to Taiwan to take part in a pilgrimage tour around the island. Some reports in Taiwan have hyped this, claiming that “the CCP united front has infiltrated the Baishatun Mazu pilgrimage.” The Mainland Affairs Council said it dispatched personnel to conduct inspections throughout the trip. What is your…","First question. Fujian and Taiwan share similar customs and cultures, and most of Taiwan’s folk beliefs were brought over by migrants from Fujian and other places. For a long time, folk belief temples on both sides of the Strait have maintained lively exchanges, and grassroots believers across the two sides are closely connected. The worship of Wang Ye (Royal Lords) is a representative example.\nFumei Temple in Quanzhou enshrines Lord Xiao, and there has long been the custom of “sending the royal boat” out to sea. Historically, several royal boats drifted across the Strait to Taiwan, and local residents built Royal Lord temples where the boats landed to worship them, regarding Fumei Temple as their ancestral temple to commemorate this rare connection. This year marks the 100th anniversary of the arrival of Fumei Temple’s royal boat “Jietaili” (捷泰利号) at Dongshi Port in Chiayi, Taiwan. The Lord Xiao divine image of Fumei Temple has entered Taiwan, and together with relevant temples it is holding commemorative celebrations, which is a good thing for cross-Strait folk belief exchanges. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are obstinately plotting “independence” and, with a confrontational mindset, are interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, harming the emotional bonds and interests of compatriots on both sides, including folk belief followers. This is unpopular and will inevitably meet with resolute opposition from compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question. We have consistently upheld the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and we continue to provide convenience and services for Taiwan students who come to the mainland to study and pursue further education, helping more Taiwan students realize their life dreams on the mainland. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have repeatedly reached into the education field with political hands. Even ordinary Taipei high school students have been blocked from attending their preferred universities simply because they were born on the mainland. Who is thinking of Taiwan’s young people and who is standing against their interests is clear at a glance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The Mainland Affairs Council says that personnel from Quanzhou's Fumei Temple came to Taiwan to take part in a circuit pilgrimage (绕境) without applying. Can you confirm under what name the relevant Fumei Temple personnel applied to come to Taiwan? Grassroots folk-belief exchanges across the Taiwan Strait are very active, but given that the Taiwan side is currently restricting cross-Strait exchanges, temple…","Cross-Strait folk beliefs, especially exchanges between temples honoring Xiao Wang Ye, Mazu and Guan Di, have been very active. Ancestral temple deity statues touring the island to provide spiritual guidance and comfort to Taiwan believers has been practiced for many years and is deeply welcomed by Taiwan compatriots, especially believers. What I want to ask is: why do the DPP authorities repeatedly obstruct and restrict these long-standing exchange and celebration activities? Why do they so readily pin the label of “united front” on things that win the hearts of the Taiwan people? At present, Taiwan's economy and people's livelihood face many structural problems and salient issues, and the island also faces severe challenges such as U.S. high-tariff bullying. Can the DPP authorities do something that wins the hearts of the people?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Lai Ching-te recently said in an interview that he had no choice but to define “China” as a “foreign hostile force” under the “Anti-Infiltration Act,” so that the “national” system could be adjusted. The purpose is to ensure “national” security and social stability and to keep the Taiwan people safe and secure in the long run. What comment do you have on this?","Since taking office, Lai Ching-te has stubbornly held to a separatist “Taiwan independence” stance. He manipulates “anti-China and resist-China” rhetoric, incites cross-Strait confrontation, aggravates the “green terror,” and obstructs cross-Strait exchanges. Moreover, he spouts nonsense by defining the mainland as a “hostile foreign force.” What he says and does is pushing Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and calamity and leaving the people of Taiwan in constant anxiety.\nTaiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Only by jointly promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and hand in hand advancing national reunification can we uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and enhance the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. This is the broad road; it is the only way to make Taiwan society harmonious and peaceful and to let the people of Taiwan live and work in contentment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","On April 30, the mainland animated film “Chang’an Sanwanli” was released in Taiwan. In addition to the Mandarin version, a Hokkien version was specially launched, which has been welcomed and praised by island audiences. One viewer said, “It is incredibly familiar; I look forward to more mainland films being shown in Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","“Chang’an Three Thousand Li” is a rare animated film masterpiece. Centered on the legendary stories of Tang poets such as Takaichi and Li Bai, the film cleverly weaves in 48 classic Tang poems, fully showcasing the grand literary atmosphere of the High Tang, and allows audiences to deeply feel the sentiment of love for family and country and the charm of Chinese culture. When “Chang’an Three Thousand Li” was screened in Taiwan, a Min Nan dialect version was specially dubbed, offering some Taiwan audiences a more intimate viewing experience and adding a distinctive flavor to the film. I watched the Mandarin version very carefully, and I also watched some clips of the Min Nan version. As a Min Nan person, I find it very intimate. We hope more excellent mainland film and television works will be screened in Taiwan, and we are also glad to see industry players on both sides join hands to create more outstanding works.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","The US House of Representatives recently passed two Taiwan-related bills, including the “Taiwan Assurance Implementation Act,” which requires the US State Department to regularly review and lift restrictions on interactions with Taiwan, and claims that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 “does not involve Taiwan’s sovereignty.” The DPP authorities expressed gratitude for this. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan has no international legal status other than being part of China. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted at the 26th session in 1971, returned the representation and seat of all China, including Taiwan, to the government of the People’s Republic of China, on the premise of recognizing that Taiwan belongs to China. The historical facts are clear and the legal basis is clear.\nWe demand that the United States abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop fabricating wrong Taiwan-related bills, and stop sending any wrong signals that condone or support “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Any scheme to play the “Taiwan card” and “use Taiwan to contain China” will surely fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","The Beijing Higher People's Court recently released a batch of typical cases safeguarding the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The representative cases of protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, released by the Beijing Higher People's Court, were selected from recent years in which Beijing courts, based on their judicial functions, served and safeguarded cross-Strait integrated development and effectively protected the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. They are an active measure by the people's courts to earnestly implement the Supreme People's Court's “36 Judicial Measures Benefiting Taiwan.”\nThese cases involve areas such as intellectual property protection, labor rights protection, connection between litigation and mediation, substantive resolution of disputes, efficient enforcement, and convenient litigation services. They reflect the efforts and achievements of the people's courts in equally protecting the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait in the judicial field related to Taiwan, continuously implementing equal treatment, focusing on improving the quality and effectiveness of resolving Taiwan-related disputes, optimizing a market-oriented and rule-of-law business environment, and actively serving cross-Strait integrated development. They are intended to continuously create a favorable rule-of-law environment for the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to work, live, start businesses and operate on the mainland, to participate in the construction of Chinese-style modernization, and to share in the fruits of development and progress on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Diplomats from Haiti and Saint Lucia, Taiwan's “diplomatic allies,” attended the 4th Ministerial Meeting of the China-LAC Forum this year, which has sparked heated discussion on the island. The DPP authorities said that these diplomats do not represent their governments. What is your response to this?","The China-LAC Forum is an important platform for China's mutually beneficial cooperation with Latin American and Caribbean countries. We have always welcomed and supported CELAC member states' participation in activities within the framework of the Forum. Adhering to the one-China principle is a norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. We hope the countries concerned will follow the trend of the times and make the right choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","四川日报封面新闻记者","Recently, both sides of the Strait held colorful food and culture exchange activities. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots and origins, and their food culture is passed down in an unbroken line. I would like to introduce two events related to cuisine. From April 21 to 27, the sixth season of the cross-Strait new media creation event “Sichuan Cuisine on the Tip of the Tongue: Show It on Your Phone” was successfully held in Sichuan. Under the main theme of “Seeking Flavors in Sichuan,” the event invited more than 40 participants, including media from both sides of the Strait, Taiwanese food bloggers, and Taiwanese youth self-media creators. Through learning experiences, restaurant visits and tastings, themed filming, and online livestreams, they went deep into six cities including Chengdu, Deyang, Meishan, and Zigong. Around more than 50 kinds of Sichuan food and 14 cultural and tourism sites, they carried out field trips and creative work, producing more than 200 works under the topic “When Taiwan’s Stomach Meets Sichuan Flavor,” showcasing Sichuan’s distinctive cuisine and the bond of Sichuan and Taiwan through food.\nOn May 13, nine Shaxian snack shops, authorized by the Shaxian Snack Trade Association of Sanming, Fujian, opened simultaneously in Taipei, New Taipei, Taoyuan, and other places. This is the first time that the “national snack” found across the mainland has opened stores on the island, allowing Taiwan compatriots to taste authentic Shaxian snacks right at home. This authentic flavor represents not only the fresh and savory taste that crosses the strait, but also the resonance of everyday life that shows “cross-Strait compatriots are one family.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","台湾东森电视台记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te accepted an exclusive interview with Japanese media and said he hopes that the two sides of the Strait can engage in exchanges and cooperation on the basis of equal dignity, turning confrontation into dialogue. What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s response to the above remarks?","The so-called “dignity parity” of the Lai Ching-te authorities is an attempt to change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and to achieve cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges on the basis of the “two-state theory.” Its scheme will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250514_12700643.htm"],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that holding a mainland residence permit is equivalent to holding mainland household registration or a passport, and also amounts to acquiring mainland identity. It said the power to interpret the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” rests with the Mainland Affairs Council and will not be affected by different…","The Mainland Affairs Council's statement is arrogant and high-handed. Clearly, the DPP authorities do not care at all about the function of the residence permit and do not consider the vital interests and practical needs of Taiwan compatriots. Using the residence permit as a pretext is merely an excuse, and its fundamental purpose is to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, intimidate the island's people, and serve “Taiwan independence.”\nWe will continue to uphold the concept of a “cross-Strait family,” do our best to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and assistance for their development on the mainland, and continue to protect, in accordance with law and effectively and forcefully, the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots who hold the residence permit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","More than 100 days have passed since US President Donald Trump took office. Academia Sinica in Taiwan recently released a survey showing that after Trump took office, 46.7% of the public feel pessimistic about the future of US-Taiwan relations, and 60% of the public worry that “the US side may harm Taiwan by reaching an agreement with mainland China.” What is your comment on this?","This shows that more and more Taiwan people have come to recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, that outside powers are unreliable, that the United States consistently pursues “America First,” and that to the United States Taiwan is a “chess piece” to be abandoned after use. The lie of US “support for Taiwan” that the DPP authorities have racked their brains to fabricate is increasingly unable to fool people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-14","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","The DPP authorities did not receive an invitation to the 78th World Health Assembly (WHA). The head of Taiwan’s external affairs department said they will go to take part in WHA-related activities, and hopes the WHA will not become a “venue for CCP political manipulation.” What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities obstinately hold to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. As a result, the political basis for Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly no longer exists. This situation was entirely created by the DPP authorities, and they know it full well.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and are one family. We have always cared about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and we have made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health affairs. The DPP authorities' repeated manipulation of the issue of Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly stems entirely from their nature of seeking “independence” and their political self-interest. They aim to challenge the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle. Their deceptive conduct and provocative behavior will certainly be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait and by the international community, and they are destined to end in failure.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250514_12700620.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-05-15","Lin Jian","Xinhua News Agency","The 78th World Health Assembly (WHA) will open on May 19. Taiwan has not yet been invited to attend. Does the Chinese government have any comment on that?","China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, is consistent and clear. That is, this must be handled in line with the one-China principle, which is also a fundamental principle as demonstrated by the UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. China’s Taiwan region, unless given approval by the Central Government, has no basis, reason or right to participate in the WHA. Due to the DPP authorities’ persistent separatist stance, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. To uphold the one-China principle as well as the sanctity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China has decided not to approve the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA.\nFor quite some time, the DPP authorities and certain countries have been blatantly turning back the wheel of history by deliberately distorting and challenging UNGA Resolution 2758 to challenge the one-China principle. They are essentially trying to challenge not only China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also international justice and prevailing consensus as well as the post-war international order. China’s decision of not approving the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA has wide support and understanding from the international community. It shows that commitment to the one-China principle is where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends, and what the greater national interests entail. The international community’s commitment to the one-China principle is not to be challenged or shaken. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, it does not change the fact that the two sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China and Taiwan is part of China, nor can it stop the trend towards China’s ultimate and inevitable reunification. “Taiwan independence” leads nowhere and provocations for this agenda are doomed to failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250515_11623657.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250515_11623651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-05-15","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities recently held their first-ever event commemorating Victory in Europe (V-E) Day of WWII at the Taipei Guest House, which once served as the Governor-General's residence during Japan's colonial rule. During the event, Lai Ching-te made the unfounded claim that Taiwan and Europe are now facing threats from a so-called \"new authoritarian bloc.\"…","Lai Ching-te has been engaging in authoritarian practices, intensifying the \"green terror\" on the island, provoking cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and heightening tensions and instability in the Taiwan Strait. He is a true \"saboteur of cross-Strait peace\" and \"creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.\" In a shameless attempt to seize the spotlight and assert his presence, Lai Ching-te stood on the ground once trampled by Japanese invaders and brazenly peddled deceptive rhetoric. By distorting the history of WWII and inserting separatist narratives, he has betrayed the Chinese nation, which is a disgraceful act beneath contempt.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, as well as the recovery of Taiwan to China. Taiwan's return to China is an important part of the victory of WWII and the post-war international order. A number of international legal instruments including the\nCairo Declaration\nand the\nPotsdam Proclamation\nhave affirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan in clear-cut terms. This is an indisputable fact supported by history and the law. The historical trend that China will and must achieve reunification is unstoppable. Any words or deeds that forget the ancestry or solicit external support for \"Taiwan independence\" is surely disdained by the people and condemned by history.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250515-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16386248.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-05-19","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19. Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office said on the 19th that the political manipulation of the DPP authorities is unpopular and will not succeed. We will, as always, support and encourage cultural exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait, welcome Taiwanese performing artists to come to the mainland to develop, and take necessary measures…","Chen Binhua said that in recent years, more and more Taiwan performing artists have come to the mainland to develop their careers, sharing in the opportunities of the mainland's cultural industry development and finding a bigger stage to realize greater dreams. Based on their own experiences, they have spoken out from the heart, expressing their identification that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and belong to one family, their support for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and peaceful development, and their hope that compatriots on both sides will draw closer, visit each other, and get along well. Their spontaneous actions have been widely welcomed and praised by people on both sides of the Strait.\nHe pointed out that the DPP authorities have labeled these Taiwan performing artists with the “united front” tag and vowed to investigate and punish them, which seriously infringes on the basic rights and freedom of speech of Taiwan compatriots and fully exposes the hypocritical nature of their touted “democracy, freedom and human rights” and their ugly face of manipulating “anti-China and resisting China” and undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250519_12701580.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-19","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 19 — The 78th World Health Assembly refused to include the Taiwan-related proposal on its agenda. In response, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 19th when asked by reporters that the relevant decision of the 78th World Health Assembly once again demonstrates that adherence to the one-China principle is the common consensus of…","Chen Binhua said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. We have always kept the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots in mind. Given that the Taiwan region has not participated in the World Health Assembly, we have made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan region's participation in global health affairs. Over the past year, Taiwan region medical and technical experts participated in 11 batches of WHO technical activities, totaling 12 person-times. Under the framework of the International Health Regulations, any public health emergency information that the WHO notifies to various regions is available to Taiwan region in a timely manner, and Taiwan region is also able to notify the WHO in a timely manner. It can be said that the channels for Taiwan region's participation in communication and cooperation with the WHO in technical fields are fully unobstructed, the channels for obtaining information and support on various public health emergencies are fully effective, and the health rights of Taiwan compatriots are substantively guaranteed.\nHe pointed out that for some time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have colluded with external forces and repeatedly made an issue of participation in the World Health Assembly, deliberately distorting and challenging the fundamental principles affirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution WHA25.1. This not only challenges China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also challenges international justice and common consensus, and challenges the international order established after World War II. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that any provocation to seek “independence” will certainly meet resolute countermeasures, and any scheme to collude with external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250519_12701595.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-20","Chen Binhua","台湾地区领导人近来讲话中涉两岸关系内容答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 (Electric): Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office answered reporters' questions on May 20 regarding the content related to cross-Strait relations in recent remarks by Taiwan's leader. A reporter asked: Today, Taiwan's leader delivered a speech marking the first anniversary of taking office and accepted a media interview after the speech. Earlier,…","Chen Binhua said, “‘Taiwan independence’ separatism and peace across the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water, and confrontation runs counter to exchange and dialogue. Only by ceasing provocations aimed at pursuing ‘independence’ will cross-Strait relations have room to maneuver. Only by strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation will the tense situation across the Taiwan Strait ease. Only by recognizing that both sides belong to one China will cross-Strait consultation and dialogue have a foundation.”\nHe pointed out that the recent remarks by the Taiwan region’s leader, on the one hand, still adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and the wrong line of “seeking independence by relying on foreign forces” and “seeking independence by force.” They hype the “mainland threat,” perpetuate the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” stir up cross-Strait confrontation, push for cross-Strait economic “decoupling and severing of links,” advance the “17 countermeasures,” and obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. On the other hand, they put on a hypocritical show, claiming willingness to engage in exchanges and cooperation with the mainland on the premise of “equal dignity,” and attempting to restore cross-Strait consultation and dialogue on the basis of the “two-state theory.” This two-faced tactic is unoriginal and futile, and it is destined to fail.\nChen Binhua said that no matter what the Taiwan region’s leader says or how they say it, they cannot change Taiwan’s status as part of China, cannot change the direction and pace of cross-Strait relations moving forward, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will be and must be reunified. We will fully implement the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces. On the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to hold dialogue and communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and individuals on cross-Strait political issues and on matters related to advancing the process of national reunification. We will actively expand cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and jointly create a beautiful future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250520_12701793.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-05-22","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Taiwanese official Lin Chia-lung said yesterday that whether or not Taiwan is a country is not up to Beijing. It’s Taiwan’s business what its name is. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","Taiwan is never a country. These remarks are sheer “Taiwan independence” provocations that only reveal this person’s presumptuousness and ignorance.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. The future of Taiwan can only be decided by the over 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our Taiwan compatriots. China will realize reunification. This is a historical trend that no force can stop.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250522_11630692.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250522_11630780.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-05-22","Mao Ning","AFP","Yesterday the DPP in Taiwan expelled five of its party members for allegedly spying for Beijing. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","I’m not familiar with that, and this is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250522_11630692.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250522_11630780.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-05-22","Mao Ning","China Review News","It was reported that Prime Minister of Solomon Islands Jeremiah Manele issued a statement, reaffirming the Solomon Islands government’s steadfast commitment to the one-China policy, and directing all government ministries, agencies, and officials to fully comply with the government’s policy. What is your comment?","China highly appreciates Solomon Islands government’s firm support for the one-China principle and upholding this just position. There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is enshrined in the UNGA Resolution 2758. It is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. Upholding the one-China principle and supporting China’s reunification is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends, and the right thing to do.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250522_11630692.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250522_11630780.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-05-23","Mao Ning","TVB","It was reported that recently Taiwan’s “Hong Cai Tou 6” fishing boat was detained by Japanese official vessels for violating fishing regulations and was then released after paying a huge bail. China last year protested to Japan over its detention of Taiwanese fishing boats. Did China protest to Japan this time?","The Chinese government attaches great importance to safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of Chinese fishermen, including those from the Taiwan region. According to the China-Japan Fisheries Agreement, Japan has no right to take enforcement measures against Chinese fishing vessels in relevant waters. China has protested to Japan over its detention of the fishing boat “Hong Cai Tou 6”, and asked the Japanese side to immediately correct the wrongdoing, and take effective measures to prevent similar incidents from happening again.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250523_11631403.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250523_11631472.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-05-28","Mao Ning","Reuters","Japan’s military has reported that the Liaoning aircraft carrier group has sailed past the southern Japanese islands and is heading into the Western Pacific and that Japan is keeping a close watch. May I ask why are the carriers sailing so close to Japan, and is China sending a message to Japan, the United States and Taiwan?","I’d refer you to competent authorities for specifics. What I can tell you is that China’s military vessels’ activities in relevant waters are fully consistent with international law and international practice. We hope Japan will view this from an objective and reasonable perspective.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250528_11635366.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250528_11635389.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on May 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","On May 20, the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office expressed a firm position on Lai Qingde's recent multiple remarks involving cross-Strait relations. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said it hopes the mainland will realistically face the objective fact that the “Republic of China” exists, listen to the goodwill extended by the Taiwan side, and that only through interaction based on “equal dignity”…","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an objective fact that no one in Taiwan, and no political party, can evade or deny. As long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and both sides recognize that they belong to one China, the two sides can engage in dialogue and equal consultation. Denying the “1992 Consensus,” departing from the one-China principle, and scheming for “Taiwan independence” separatism make dialogue and consultation between the two sides impossible. If the so-called “equal dignity” of the Lai Ching-te authorities is equated with the so-called “two-state theory,” it is an attempt to change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. This would create obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and consultation and would only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703174.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Island polls show that in the year since Lai Ching-te took office, 53% of the public are dissatisfied with his governance performance. This is the highest dissatisfaction rate at the one-year mark of any Taiwan region leader’s inauguration in nearly 30 years. The Lai authorities’ performance in handling cross-Strait relations and responding to the US tariff war has been especially questioned, with dissatisfaction…","Since taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities have obstinately adhered to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and the erroneous lines of “relying on foreign powers to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force.” They have vigorously hyped the “mainland threat” and repeatedly fabricated the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” stirring up cross-Strait confrontation, pushing for the decoupling and severing of cross-Strait economic ties, and increasingly obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Facing high tariffs imposed by the United States, they have kowtowed all the way and tried hard to pledge loyalty, further cementing their reputation as “professional sellers of Taiwan.” Their perverse actions, omnipotence in infighting, and incompetence in governance seriously depart from mainstream public opinion on the island and seriously harm the immediate interests of Taiwan's businesses and people. Media on the island have described this as “a year of disappointment, a year of anger,” and multiple poll results have fully expressed the strong dissatisfaction of all sectors of Taiwan society. If the Lai Ching-te authorities continue to insist on their own way, they will surely face a backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703173.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, in an interview, used “corporate merger” as a metaphor for cross-Strait unification, claiming: “China is the larger company and Taiwan is the smaller company. If you want to merge with my company, you have to set conditions. It is not Taiwan that sets the conditions, letting you say yes or no.” What is your comment on this?","Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that both sides belong to one China has never changed. Completing national reunification is the long-cherished wish of compatriots and a matter of great national righteousness. On the basis of the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” we are willing to exchange views extensively with people from all parties, sectors, and strata in Taiwan on cross-Strait relations and national reunification, conduct in-depth consultations, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703172.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","The Mainland Affairs Council said it will continue to comprehensively assess the timing and conditions for resuming cross-Strait maritime passenger direct sailings, based on cross-Strait travel demand and the overall cross-Strait situation. What is your comment?","Cross-Strait maritime passenger routes are important channels for people on both sides of the Strait to travel back and forth. Fully restoring direct cross-Strait maritime passenger services is conducive to exchanges between compatriots on both sides. Whether it is the rapid restoration of the “mini three links” maritime passenger routes after the epidemic or the unremitting efforts made to resume the “three links,” they all demonstrate our sincerity and good faith in seeking well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nAt present, compatriots in Taiwan are eagerly looking forward to the restoration of direct cross-Strait maritime passenger services. We attach great importance to this and have made relevant preparations. There are no obstacles on the mainland side to restoring normal cross-Strait maritime passenger routes. The Taiwan side should fully consider the demands of people on both sides of the Strait and of shipping companies, and restore as soon as possible direct cross-Strait maritime passenger services, including the Pingtan–Taipei, Pingtan–Taichung, Xiamen–Taichung, Xiamen–Keelung and Zhejiang Damaiyu–Keelung routes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","The Second Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit opened in Beijing this morning (May 28). Please introduce the participation of cultural figures from both sides of the Strait and the highlights of the activities.","The Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit is a grand gathering for exchanges among cultural figures on both sides of the Strait. This morning, the Second Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit opened in Beijing, with more than 800 representatives from cultural fields on both sides of the Strait attending.\nThis summit features five sub-forums: the Culture Forum, the Cultural and Creative Forum, the Film and Television Forum, the Calligraphy, Painting, and Photography Forum, and the Four Seas Culture Forum. On the 29th, the Sixth Cross-Strait Media Summit will be held, and on the 30th, the closing performance “Glory of China, Voices Across the Strait” will take place, with artists and performers from both sides of the Strait performing on the same stage. During the summit, multiple exhibitions and performances will be held simultaneously, including an intangible cultural heritage exhibition, a photography exhibition, shadow puppet and glove puppet performances, a cross-strait college student film screening, and a screening event for “Ne Zha 2.” Cultural exchange visits will also be arranged to the Palace Museum, the National Museum of China, and Panjiayuan. Media reporters are welcome to cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台华语环球节目中心《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the DPP authorities' plan to investigate and punish Taiwanese entertainers who cooperate with the mainland's united front work against Taiwan, a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said the mainland will “take necessary measures to safeguard their legitimate and proper rights and interests.” The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that many of these entertainers' actions were things…","Taiwanese performers expressing identification with Chinese culture and with the idea that 'compatriots on both sides are one family' is a genuine expression of feeling, and it is their freedom and right. The DPP authorities deliberately distort it, exposing their own inner panic. In order to incite 'anti-China and resist-China' sentiment, the DPP authorities keep hyping so-called 'united front threats' and, in increasingly extreme and unscrupulous ways, intimidate and suppress groups and individuals on the island who support and take part in cross-Strait exchanges. The aim is to obstruct cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and to create a 'politics of terror and green dictatorship' on the island.\nThe motherland mainland will always be the strong backing of broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots, and our family of more than 1.4 billion people will always be the greatest source of confidence and support for them. We will, as always, support and encourage cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation, welcome Taiwanese performers to come to the mainland to develop, and take necessary measures to safeguard their lawful and legitimate rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703168.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","《海峡之声》广播电台记者","Recently, US Secretary of State Rubio said that building deterrence against China’s “invasion of Taiwan” should start with “Taiwan’s self-defense capabilities.” Paparo, commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, said that plans have been made to deter and stop the mainland’s “military invasion” of Taiwan, and advocated creating a “hellscape” to respond. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and tolerates no external interference. Some people on the US side harbor sinister intentions. They constantly hype the so-called “military threat” from the mainland, persistently clamor that “Taiwan should tie down the mainland,” and exaggerate the atmosphere of war in the Taiwan Strait. All of this is merely a pretext for interfering in the Taiwan question and for enriching the US military-industrial complex. Facts have repeatedly proven that the United States has always put “American interests first,” and that what it does is to “harm” and “ruin” Taiwan, treating the compatriots of Taiwan as cannon fodder.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. We will never allow any force to turn this treasure island into a “hell.” The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop stirring up trouble and fanning the flames in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703167.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The US journal Foreign Affairs recently published an article saying that the US position on the Taiwan question is like “walking a tightrope.” The US is committed to strengthening Taiwan's military capabilities, but this increases the risk of Taiwan provoking conflict. The US should make clear that it does not support Taiwan “independence,” including publicly criticizing the words and deeds of Taiwan's leader…","Recently, more and more foreign experts and scholars have publicly voiced their concern and criticism over Lai Ching-te's separatist “Taiwan independence” provocations, which threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region. We appreciate these rational voices, and we also hope that more people of insight will recognize that the fundamental cause of the current complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, and continuously collude with external forces to carry out independence-seeking provocations.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and clearly oppose “Taiwan independence.” We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, starting from national righteousness and their own well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” provocations and foreign interference, and join us in jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703166.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Wu Fengshan, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), said that since 2016, although the mainland unilaterally suspended dialogue because the Taiwan side has not accepted the “1992 Consensus,” the channels for cross-Strait communication have remained open and exchange affairs have never been interrupted. What is your response?","The “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the premise for the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism. On this matter of principle, our position has been consistent and clear. The reasons for the current stalling of the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism are well known, and the solution is clear. As long as the DPP authorities acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, the two sides can conduct dialogue and consultations.\nOn the one hand, the DPP authorities set up all kinds of obstacles to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation; on the other hand, they attempt to create the illusion that cross-Strait dialogue and consultations are possible without acknowledging the “1992 Consensus.” This two-faced tactic has long been seen through by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703171.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Recently, during a visit to the United States, the Secretary-General of Taiwan’s executive authority said that Taiwan will further expand its investment in the US to help “make America great again,” which has caused an uproar in public opinion on the island. What is your comment?","This once again proves that the Lai Ching-te authorities have no bottom line in their servile, “currying favor with the US and selling out Taiwan” conduct. Faced with the US's indiscriminate imposition of tariffs and the severe damage to Taiwan's development rights and interests, the Lai Ching-te authorities not only lack the courage to say “no” to economic bullying, but also lack the ability to safeguard the legitimate interests of enterprises and people on the island. Instead, they continuously pledge loyalty and curry favor with the US at the expense of the island's advantageous industries, people's well-being and economic prospects. Giving in again and again will inevitably lead the US to press for more, and Taiwan will be squeezed dry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have adopted various means to obstruct and restrict personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and cooperation and exchanges in all fields. At present, prices on the island are rising and living costs are climbing. Tourism operators have called on the Lai authorities to put fewer political considerations first and to lift cross-Strait travel restrictions as…","Since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have schemed to obstruct cross-strait personnel exchanges and tourism cooperation. They refuse to lift the “group tour ban,” raised the travel warning for Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland to “orange,” issued the so-called “2025 Mainland China Travel Safety Handbook,” and obstructed the full resumption of cross-strait passenger shipping routes and direct flight routes. They have used various excuses to resist and delay group tours by residents of Fujian and Shanghai to Taiwan, and have even demanded that Taiwan tourism operators dissuade Taiwan residents from traveling to the mainland. These reckless actions have made the tourism industry on the island even more difficult, and public grievances keep accumulating.\nThe two sides are separated by only a shallow strait, and compatriots on both sides are one family. It is only natural for people to want to go and see the places where their compatriots live. This is beneficial both to the development of cross-strait tourism and to the development of cross-strait relations. We have always upheld the concept of “one family across the Strait,” actively promoted the resumption of cross-strait tourism, and made positive efforts to this end. As long as the DPP authorities remove the various obstacles they have set up for cross-strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, cross-strait tourism can resume, cross-strait residents can frequently visit each other, and industries, enterprises, and practitioners in tourism, accommodation, civil aviation, and shipping can profit from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","On May 18, at the opening ceremony of the 27th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Fair, Fuzhou City released the second batch of policies for pilot implementation in building the Fuzhou-Matsu “same-city living circle.” Please introduce the relevant situation. The Mainland Affairs Council smeared and attacked these measures as “propaganda of united front work that offers empty promises, attempting to divide Taiwan.”…","To promote the construction of the Fuzhou–Matsu \"same-city living circle\" and bring benefits to Taiwan compatriots, the Fuzhou municipal government released the second batch of pilot policies for building the Fuzhou–Matsu \"same-city living circle\" during the 27th Cross-Strait Economic, Trade and Culture Fair. This batch contains 10 measures in three areas: integrating into the cross-Strait common market, improving living convenience, and deepening civil exchanges. They will further promote industrial cooperation between Fuzhou and Matsu and provide more support for Matsu enterprises and residents in import and export trade, opening up the common market, implementing equal treatment, and enhancing cultural exchanges.\nThe first batch of policies that the Fuzhou municipal government introduced last year to build the Fuzhou–Matsu \"same-city living circle\" has truly benefited Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesses, and Taiwan youth, and has been warmly welcomed by the people of Matsu, achieving good results. The second batch of policies released this time focuses on areas that Matsu fellow residents strongly call for, have great demand for, and urgently need. It provides more convenience for Matsu fellow residents living in Fuzhou and better conditions and more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesses, and Taiwan youth to start businesses and develop in Fuzhou. Its value is higher and it is full of sincerity.\nEvery time the mainland introduces measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities oppose them without exception; whatever the mainland does that benefits Taiwan compatriots, they spread slander and smear it extensively. We have long grown used to this, because they have only partisan political calculations in mind and no regard at all for the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Admiral Paparo, commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, recently said China could fully possess the “capability to attack Taiwan” by 2027. The head of Taiwan's defense authorities demanded that Taiwan's military accelerate training to achieve the substantive combat readiness goal of “high readiness” and the corresponding mindset by 2027. He also said Taiwan needs to strengthen “national security exchanges with…","In order to seize political self-interest, the DPP authorities, following the lead of the U.S. side and cooperating in every step, have turned Taiwan into a “powder keg,” provoking conflict and pushing the people of Taiwan into peril, with sinister intent. Regardless of how the situation on the island changes, and regardless of how external forces interfere, the historical trend that China will be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified, cannot be stopped.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and is not subject to any foreign interference. No one should underestimate the firm resolve, strong determination, and great capability of the Chinese people and the Chinese military to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities' attempts to “rely on external forces to seek independence,” “use force to seek independence,” and “prepare for war to protect independence” are wishful thinking and an overestimation of themselves, and will only lead to their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the first documentary film recording the living conditions of Taiwan veterans, “Sunset · Homecoming,” was officially released. Some Taiwan compatriots who have watched the film said that the story of veterans longing for home and returning home across 70 years is moving, reflecting the national wounds caused by cross-Strait separation, and that they hope relatives will no longer be separated and the…","There was a time when the separation across the Strait left countless families with bitter, unforgettable wounds and even irreparable regrets. After two years of searching, visiting, and on-location filming, the crew of the documentary 《日暮·归乡》 (Sunset Homecoming) took six veterans who went to Taiwan as protagonists, each with different ancestral origins, backgrounds, and identities, and used real footage to record their longing for their homeland and their hopes for reunion with their families. The film was released on May 10, allowing more people to understand the common wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for an early reunion, and to feel the deep affection that blood is thicker than water. Separated only by a narrow strip of water, yet as close as a few feet and as distant as the ends of the earth, the fact that the two sides of the Strait have not yet been fully unified is a wound that history has left to the Chinese nation. Chinese on both sides of the Strait should jointly shoulder the righteous duty of the nation, work toward national reunification, and heal the wounds of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","On the first question: Lai Ching-te's May 20 speech rarely mentioned cross-Strait relations and instead focused on strengthening Taiwan-US relations. Some scholars on both sides of the Strait believe that “not mentioning” is not a good thing, showing that cross-Strait relations are becoming more difficult. Some public opinion holds that, under pressure from factors such as the island's “US-skepticism” and public…","On the first question, on May 20 I already commented on the remarks made by the leader of Taiwan's region in his speech that day and in his earlier media interviews, and expressed our position and stance.\nI want to stress again that “Taiwan independence” separatism and peace across the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water, and confrontation runs counter to exchange and dialogue. Only when provocative acts of seeking “independence” stop will there be room for easing cross-Strait relations; only when cross-Strait exchange and cooperation are strengthened will tensions in the Taiwan Strait be eased; only when both sides recognize that they belong to one China will there be a basis for cross-Strait consultation and dialogue.\nWhether or not the leader of Taiwan's region says it, what he says, or how he says it, cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the direction and pace of cross-Strait relations moving forward, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably and certainly be reunified. We will fully implement the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question, uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, actively expand cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, continuously deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and work together to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nOn the second question, public security authorities have already issued a detailed “Police Situation Bulletin,” and I have nothing more to add.\nIn recent years, under the instigation of the DPP authorities, Taiwan's cyber and electronic warfare forces have frequently carried out cyber attacks and espionage, “Taiwan independence” propaganda, system sabotage and other activities against the mainland's internet, causing interference with the security of the mainland's cyberspace and other matters. Their nature is extremely vile. In the next step, public security authorities will resolutely safeguard national security and the lawful and legitimate rights and interests of enterprises and the people, publicly issue wanted notices for the above-mentioned individuals in accordance with the law, and resolutely crack down on them through all kinds of judicial channels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703170.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Could you tell us about the preparations for the 17th Straits Forum? The Mainland Affairs Council said that, to prevent the mainland from using the Straits Forum for “political manipulation” against Taiwan, it does not recommend that local government personnel attend and discourages Taiwan residents from participating. What comments do you have on this?","The Straits Forum adheres to the positioning of “civilian nature, grassroots character, and broad participation.” It is a civilian exchange activity deeply loved by people on both sides of the Strait. Since 2009, it has been successfully held 16 times, and it is an important platform for promoting extensive exchanges among all sectors across the Strait and advancing civilian exchanges and cooperation. Through the Straits Forum, compatriots on both sides make exchanges, friends, and heartfelt connections, nurture their friendship, enhance their well-being, and draw closer to each other. The DPP authorities' prohibitive and restrictive measures against certain Taiwan participants in the Straits Forum have once again exposed their sinister intention to restrict and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, and have once again proven that Lai Ching-te's supposed willingness to engage in exchanges and cooperation with the mainland is nothing but a lie and empty talk.\nNo one can ignore the mainstream public opinion on the island that wants peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. No one can suppress the aspiration of compatriots on both sides to draw closer to each other, and no one can extinguish the enthusiasm of Taiwan's people to take part in cross-Strait exchange activities such as the Straits Forum. The DPP authorities' interference and obstruction are unpopular and will not succeed. We will continue to actively promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, bringing benefits and well-being to compatriots on both sides. Relevant parties are speeding up preparations for the 17th Straits Forum, and specific details will be released soon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, Cheng Ying-yao, head of Taiwan’s education authorities, publicly said that at this stage, exchanges between the island’s primary, secondary and university schools and the mainland are not encouraged, and are even prohibited or opposed, which has sparked controversy. What is your comment?","For the purpose of seeking “independence” and private political gain, the DPP authorities have, on various pretexts, increasingly obstructed and undermined normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They have repeatedly reached political hands into the field of education and deliberately sabotaged normal cross-Strait educational exchanges, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan's young students. Such practices are unpopular and despicable. We will continue to create convenient and favorable environments for cross-Strait educational exchanges and exchanges among young students, and provide better conditions and greater scope for Taiwan's young students to study, work and start businesses on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The DPP authorities require mainland spouses to make up the “Certificate of Loss of Original Nationality” within a set time limit. According to reports, more than 8,000 people still have not submitted it, and in a little over a month they may face the penalty of having their household registration in Taiwan cancelled. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities demand that mainland spouses in Taiwan provide so-called “proof of loss of original nationality,” otherwise they threaten to cancel the household registration in Taiwan of some mainland spouses. As I understand it, a considerable number of these people settled in Taiwan ten or twenty years ago. Therefore, the DPP authorities' demand and approach are simply contrary to common sense, contrary to human relations, and unreasonable. Such a brutal approach stems entirely from their “independence”-seeking nature and political self-interest, with the aim of creating a “chilling effect” and inciting confrontation between the two sides. Toward the DPP authorities' blatant political manipulation and political persecution, Taiwan compatriots, including mainland spouses, have already expressed condemnation and opposition.\nThe mainland is the maternal home of the vast number of mainland spouses. When storms come, we must, in both sentiment and reason, protect the legitimate and lawful rights and interests of cross-strait marriage and family groups and shelter them from the wind and rain. For those “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices who cooperate with the DPP authorities in persecuting mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely without leniency.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202505/t20250528_12703169.htm"],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","On the 20th, Lai Ching-te delivered a speech marking the first anniversary of his inauguration, repeatedly stressing the need to deepen Taiwan-U.S. relations. He said Taiwan’s future economic path is “rooted in Taiwan, positioned globally, and strengthening the United States.” Public opinion on the island points out that Lai’s so-called economic transformation is nothing but “decoupling from China and embracing…","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and the erroneous line of “seeking independence by relying on outside forces,” which will only lead Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation. The stable industrial and supply chains across the Strait and the mutually beneficial, win-win economic cooperation are the result of decades of market forces at work, and also the result of Taiwan businesses actively taking part in cross-strait integrated development. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their selfish interest in “seeking independence,” are taking the long way around. They attempt to use politics and ideology to interfere with normal cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and to push for the decoupling and severing of cross-strait economic chains. This is unpopular and will not succeed; it will only seriously harm the interests of Taiwan enterprises and the prospects for Taiwan’s economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-05-28","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS记者","First question: Recently, a mainland man opened a snack shop in Chiayi. Because he could not understand Taiwanese Hokkien and was worried about miscommunication, he placed a notice sign at the shop entrance. As a result, some internet users on the island launched a campaign against him, and he had to announce a closure and apologize. A few days ago, a mainland spouse was also detained for livestreaming near an…","First question. This reminds me of the lines from the famous poem \"Seven-Step Poem\" by the renowned Three Kingdoms-era poet Cao Zhi: \"Beans are boiled over burning bean stalks; the beans weep in the pot. We were born from the same root, why must you press me so urgently!\" Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins and are one family. When compatriots from Taiwan come to the mainland, mainland compatriots welcome them warmly. I have heard many Taiwan compatriots, including the Taiwan guest representatives who attended the Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit yesterday, express their feelings: \"Mainland compatriots treat us very well\" and \"The best treatment we get anywhere in the world comes from mainland compatriots.\" The notice board displayed by the mainland spouse you mentioned was intended to facilitate communication with customers. Some netizens in Taiwan launched online attacks against them, forcing the business to close. This is inhumane, and we strongly condemn it. For a mainland spouse who traveled thousands of miles away and works hard for their family, shouldn't we show a bit more tolerance and care? Doesn't Taiwan boast that its most beautiful scenery is its people? Aren't simplicity, kindness, warmth and friendliness the traditional virtues of Taiwan society? If Taiwan society has truly fallen ill, how did it come to this? Who and which party brought it about? We earnestly hope that compatriots from all walks of life in Taiwan will reflect deeply.\nRegarding the incident you mentioned of the mainland spouse's livestream being subjected to deportation proceedings: Recently, incidents infringing upon and damaging the lawful rights and interests of mainland spouses have frequently occurred on the island. As I just emphasized, the mainland is the maternal home of the vast number of mainland spouses. In times of storm, we must, both reasonably and emotionally, shelter them from the wind and rain. For \"Taiwan independence\" thugs and accomplices who persecute mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely without leniency. We demand that the Taiwan side be fair and just, not interfere with normal judicial procedures through political manipulation, and genuinely protect the rights and interests of mainland spouses in Taiwan.\nSecond question. Regarding the despicable individual \"Ba Jiong\" you mentioned, my response is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, manipulating \"anti-China and resist-China\" rhetoric, inciting cross-strait confrontation, and obstructing cross-strait exchanges, harming the emotional bonds and interests of compatriots on both sides. This does not win popular support and will inevitably be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides. For \"Taiwan independence\" thugs and accomplices who cooperate with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to persecute Taiwan compatriots, including the \"Ba Jiong\" you mentioned, we will hold them accountable for life and punish them severely according to law.\nRegarding the internet celebrity \"Guanzhang\" you mentioned coming to the mainland to livestream. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwan internet celebrities, to come to the mainland to look around, enjoy the magnificent mountains and rivers of the motherland, taste local specialty foods, and experience our splendid culture, advanced technology and colorful life. Based on goodwill and seeking truth from facts, sharing what they see and hear with audiences on both sides helps increase mutual understanding. We believe the internet celebrity you mentioned will have a smooth and pleasant trip to the mainland this time.\nAs long as they abide by the law, Taiwan compatriots can feel completely at ease coming to the mainland, as if returning home. Everyone will find that the mainland is beautiful, advanced and safe, and that mainland compatriots are kind, warm and friendly. Once you come, you will certainly want to come again.\nThe press conference today ends here. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202505/t20250528_12703153.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-05-29","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","It’s reported that China removed a buoy located in the exclusive economic zone to the south of Yonaguni Island of Okinawa. Why did China remove this buoy?","China’s installation of a meteorological observation buoy in waters east of Taiwan, which are under China’s jurisdiction, is consistent with China’s domestic laws and international law. It is learned that competent Chinese authorities are maintaining the buoy as needed by relevant work.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250529_11636603.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250529_11636440.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-05-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","In his recent speech, Lai Ching-te said that Taiwan would continue to strengthen its defenses and avoid war by preparing for it. Will the PLA conduct military exercises as countermeasures as before?","As long as Lai Ching-te continues his provocations for \"Taiwan independence\", there will be no tranquility in the Taiwan Strait and no stability for our Taiwan compatriots. We warn the DPP authorities that \"Taiwan independence\" separatists will come to no good end. The PLA will remain combat-ready at all times, enhance combat readiness, and safeguard our national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250529-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16388775.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-05-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first is the Commander of the US Army Pacific recently claimed that China's increasingly aggressive behavior in the Indo-Pacific had made the situation more dangerous. He said that no one would have imagined that Beijing would conduct drills simulating a blockade of Taiwan five years ago, but now such moves were commonplace. In addition, head of the US Indo-Pacific Command said that the…","For your first question, Taiwan is part of China. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, which brooks no external interference. For the cross-Strait situation, there is no factor more destabilizing than the provocations made by the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists and the disruptions by foreign forces. It's legitimate, necessary, lawful and justified for the Chinese side to take actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the US side to stop fanning the flames on the Taiwan question. Such behaviors would only backfire.\nFor your second question. Don't be fooled by Lai Ching-te's reckless provocations now. When the day comes, people like him will be the first to run away. For the PLA, defeating military elements of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces is like shooting fish in a barrel. Those notorious separatists have no chance to escape.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250529-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16388775.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-05-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The draft of the Japanese defense ministry's\nDefense White Paper 2025\nwas revealed. The draft claims that China is ramping up its nuclear, missile, maritime and aviation capabilities; that PLA's activities near Taiwan demonstrate that Beijing is trying to improve its combat capabilities; and strengthened China-Russia military cooperation is a concern for Japan. What's your comment on this?","In the draft of its\nDefense White Paper,\nthe Japanese side repeats its irresponsible comments about China's military development, and points fingers at China's legitimate military activities and external military cooperation. We are strongly opposed to this. This year marks the 80th year of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. At this special historical juncture, it's even more important for Japan to reflect on its behaviors, instead of making unfounded smears and accusations against others. We urge the Japanese side to follow the path of peaceful development, act prudently in the domain of military and security, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the rest of the international community with concrete actions.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250529-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16388775.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-05-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Head of Taiwan's defense authorities Koo Li-hsiung reportedly said in an interview that US forces and alliances across Asia was crucial for holding Beijing in check. He also expressed hope for the US to expedite arms sales to Taiwan to help Taiwan address military threats from China.What's your comments on this?","The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China, which brooks no interference. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and greatest effort. However, should the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists make provocations, challenge our bottom lines, or even cross the red lines, we will have to take decisive measures. The US side supports \"Taiwan independence\" separatists through arms sales. Such acts are self-defeating and will push Taiwan into the abyss of war.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250529-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16388775.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-05-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question is about the PLA aircraft carrier Liaoning and its task fleet. They are currently off the southeast coast of Taiwan. The Taiwan authority said that they have taken joint intelligence means to monitor relevant operations throughout the whole process. Some people suggest that the PLA will probably conduct military exercises before or after the Dragon Boat Festival. Can you…","On your first question. Relevant military activities organized by the PLA recently are routine arrangements according to our annual training plan.\nOn your second question, as we all know, China is unwavering in our commitment to peace, development and international order. The biggest threat to the current cross-Strait situation comes from separatist activities for \"Taiwan independence\" and support from foreign forces. If relevant countries truly care about stability in the Taiwan Strait, they should abide by the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/05/china-250529-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16388775.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-05-30","Lin Jian","Reuters","It’s reported that the U.S. is planning to increase weapon sales to Taiwan to levels above where they were during President Donald Trump’s first term. How would such a move affect U.S.-China relations? What measures might China take in response?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-U.S. relations. China firmly opposes the U.S.’s arms sales to China’s Taiwan region, and urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, stop selling arms to Taiwan and stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions in the Taiwan Strait. China is firmly resolved to defend its national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250530_11637703.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202505/t20250530_11637639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-06-01","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that the U.S. Secretary of Defense made negative remarks about China at the 22nd Shangri-La Dialogue, playing up the “China military threat.” What is your comment?","The US side is accustomed to using the Shangri-La Dialogue to stir up disputes, sow discord and confrontation, and seek private gains. The remarks by the US Secretary of Defense are filled with deep-rooted hegemonic logic, bullying conduct and Cold War mentality. They seriously provoke China's sovereignty and rights and interests, distort China's policy positions, seriously disregard the joint efforts of regional countries to work together to maintain prosperity and stability, and seriously deviate from the common aspiration of all countries in the world to seek peace and development. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it.\nThe conduct of the US side is clear to the whole world. For its own selfish interests, it has launched tariff and trade wars and extracted heavy taxes everywhere. It forms “small circles” and engages in bloc confrontation, causing deep concern among countries. It strengthens military deployments in the Asia-Pacific, brutally interferes in other countries' internal affairs, and incites tensions. Facts have repeatedly proven that the US side, acting against the trend of the times and obstinately persisting in its course, will inevitably backfire on itself.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. The US side has no right to make irresponsible remarks, and it should not fantasize about using it as a bargaining chip to contain China. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and any interference by external forces. Our resolve and will are as firm as a rock, and our capabilities and means are strong and reliable.\nThe South China Sea is internationally recognized as one of the busiest and safest shipping lanes. China will continue to adhere to resolving differences with the countries concerned through dialogue and consultation, to safeguard territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests in accordance with law and regulations, and to work hand in hand with regional countries to build a sea of peace, friendship and cooperation. The United States, fearing that the South China Sea will not be in turmoil, forms cliques and stirs up trouble, and is the greatest threat to regional peace and stability.\nChina has always been a guardian and builder of peace and development in the Asia-Pacific region. The Chinese military will work with regional countries to jointly oppose hegemonism that undermines the Asia-Pacific, oppose introducing geopolitical conflicts into the Asia-Pacific, and oppose any country or force creating war and chaos here. We will actively practice the concept of a community with a shared future for mankind and the “Three Global Initiatives,” and work hand in hand to maintain long-term peace, stability and prosperity in the Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.yzwb.net/news/txs/202506/t20250601_215517.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-06-04","Lin Jian","China Daily","Recently at the Shangri-La Dialogue, a European leader linked the Taiwan question with the Ukraine issue, alluded to so-called “China threat” on the South China Sea issue, and suggested that NATO has the ground to “be involved” in the Asia-Pacific. What’s China’s comment?","We firmly oppose relevant remarks. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. The Taiwan question and the Ukraine crisis are not comparable at all. China firmly opposes any remarks and moves that seek to mischaracterize or distort the nature of the Taiwan question, and urges relevant parties to abide by the one-China principle through concrete actions and respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe current situation in the South China Sea is generally stable. There isn’t any problem with the freedom of navigation and overflight that countries enjoy in accordance with the law. China stands for properly resolving maritime disputes and differences through negotiation and consultation with countries directly concerned on the basis of respecting historical facts. Countries outside of the region need to respect the efforts of regional countries to uphold peace and stability in the South China Sea, instead of instigating tensions and creating disputes.\nAs a regional defensive organization, NATO has no right to reach beyond its geographical scope and mandate defined by its treaty. China firmly opposes NATO’s attempt to advance eastward into the Asia-Pacific, stir up tensions and create confrontation in the region, and sabotage regional and even global peace and stability. Asia-Pacific countries do not welcome NATO in the Asia-Pacific and the region certainly does not need an Asia-Pacific NATO.\nLet me stress that Asia is the common home for China and other Asian countries. In recent years, thanks to the joint effort of regional countries, Asia has maintained rapid growth and become a pacesetter in global growth and peaceful development. China stays committed to the principle of amity, sincerity, mutual benefit and inclusiveness in neighborhood diplomacy, firmly opposes bloc confrontation and never seeks so-called sphere of influence. Relevant parties should not make ill-intentioned speculation or sow discord between Asia-Pacific countries based on Cold War mentality. What they should do is to contribute to peace, stability and prosperity in the Asia-Pacific.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250604_11640779.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250604_11640760.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-06-04","Zhu Fenglian","对第二届海峡两岸中华文化峰会的有关言行答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 4 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters’ questions on the 4th regarding the relevant remarks and actions of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council concerning the Second Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit.\nA reporter asked: Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council described the Second Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit as a “great…","Zhu Fenglian said that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same culture, and the same ancestry; they are one family, as close as blood and bound by a common destiny. Chinese culture has a long history and profound depth, and it is the spiritual root and sense of belonging for compatriots on both sides. The Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit is a major gathering for exchanges among cultural figures from both sides. The second Summit, held recently under the theme “Inheritance · Promotion · Development,” brought together more than 800 representatives from culture, academia, and other fields on both sides to discuss ways to carry forward and promote Chinese culture. Island-based participants at the meeting expressed their recognition of “both sides of the Strait are one family” and that “we are all Chinese,” and said they would keep in mind their responsibilities and mission in cultural inheritance. This is their freedom and right, and it is also a true reflection of mainstream public opinion on the island, which wants peace, development, exchange, and cooperation.\nShe pointed out that the DPP authorities, for the sake of their political self-interest in pursuing “independence,” disregard mainstream public opinion on the island, exaggerate so-called “united front threats,” incite “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, and intimidate and suppress island groups and individuals who support peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and participate in cross-Strait cultural exchanges. They have escalated their obstruction and restriction of cross-Strait exchanges and contact, creating a “chilling effect.” This is nothing short of “terror politics, green dictatorship.” Their brutal conduct and sinister intentions have already been opposed and condemned by public opinion and the people on both sides of the Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: those who forget their ancestry never come to a good end, and reckless actions against the will of the people are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250604_12704680.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-05","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, June 5 — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on the 5th that, upon investigation, Shen Tucheng, father of die-hard “Taiwan independence” element Puma Shen, serves as the person in charge of the Taiwanese company Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., which has trade and business cooperation with certain enterprises on the Mainland and has profited economically from them. The Mainland authorities will never allow affiliated enterprises of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements to profit on the Mainland. It has decided to impose sanctions on Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., prohibit it from conducting any transactions or cooperation with Mainland organizations, enterprises or individuals, and will take other necessary measures against it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250605_12704739.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-06-06","Lin Jian","EFE","It was reported that when meeting with Lai Ching-te in Taipei, Guatemalan President Bernardo Arévalo said that he intends to take the ties between Guatemala and Taiwan “to the next level.” What is China’s comment?","There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a prevailing consensus in the international community, which brooks no challenge. The DPP authorities use so-called “diplomatic allies” to seek political gains. This is self-deceiving and will not stop the inevitable reunification of China.\nThe fact that 183 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China fully proves that upholding the one-China principle is the right thing to do, and it is where the public opinion trends and the arc of history bends. Recognizing the one-China principle, developing relations with China, and sharing opportunities for development are what truly serve the fundamental interests of Guatemala and its people. We urge the government of relevant country to see the ultimate trend, meet its people’s aspirations, and make the right choice at an early date.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250606_11642581.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250606_11642615.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-06-09","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US is transporting a new batch of M1A2 tanks to Taiwan and plans to increase its arms sales to Taiwan over the next four years. New arms sales may surpass that of the first Trump administration. In addition, a former official of the US military said that about 500 US military personnel are operating in Taiwan, which is over ten times of the number previously disclosed by the US Congress.…","This is another solid piece of evidence that the US side and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are taking efforts to violate China's core interests, change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and escalate regional tensions. Who is making provocations despite strong opposition from the Chinese side? Who is undermining cross-Strait stability and repeatedly stirring up troubles? We believe we all know the answers. The Chinese side is strongly dissatisfied and firmly opposed to this act.\nThe Taiwan question is at the very core of China's core interests, and is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. We urge the US side to stop its military collusion with Taiwan in any form; otherwise it will get burnt for playing with fire and gain more harm than good. We warn the DPP authorities that US weapons cannot save them, and soliciting external support for \"Taiwan independence\" will only fail. The PLA will continue to strengthen military training and combat readiness and enhance its capability to fight and win. We will take resolute measures to thwart \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and external interference.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250609-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16390352.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-06-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on June 9 that the 17th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in mid-June. The forum’s main session will be held on the morning of the 15th, and concentrated activities will last one week. The forum’s main venue is in Xiamen, and relevant prefecture-level cities in Fujian and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone will also hold related activities. This session adheres to the positioning of “civilian, grassroots, and broad-based,” continues the theme of “expanding civilian exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and sets up four sections: grassroots exchanges, youth exchanges, cultural exchanges, and economic exchanges. At present, preparations for the forum are steadily advancing and progressing smoothly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250609_12705360.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on June 11, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first introduced the preparations for the 17th Straits Forum, and announced that Mr. Ma Ying-jeou will lead Taiwan youth to attend the Straits Forum and other activities. She then answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Before your questions, I will first announce two items.\nThe first item concerns the Straits Forum. The Straits Forum is a civil exchange activity welcomed by people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The 17th Straits Forum will be held in Xiamen, Fujian, on June 15. The main venue of the forum will be in Xiamen, and relevant prefecture-level cities in Fujian and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone will hold related activities. This forum adheres to the positioning of “civilian, grassroots and broad-based” character, continues the theme of “expanding civil exchanges and deepening integrated development,” and arranges a series of 56 activities in four sections: main conference activities, as well as youth exchanges, grassroots exchanges, cultural exchanges and economic exchanges. More than 7,000 representatives from Taiwan political parties and from unions, youth groups, women's groups, folk belief groups, agriculture, fisheries and water conservancy, culture and tourism, health, industry, commerce and finance, and other sectors are expected to be invited to attend.\nThe forum's press center will accept media interview applications from June 9 to 11, until 12:00 noon. Media reporters are welcome to come and cover the event.\nThe second item: Ma Ying-jeou, former chairman of the Kuomintang of China, will lead young people from Taiwan to Fujian and Gansu from June 14 to 27 to attend the 17th Straits Forum, the 2025 (Yisi year) public ceremony commemorating Fuxi, the ancestor of Chinese civilization, the activity to jointly promote Chinese culture across the Taiwan Strait (Dunhuang), and other activities, and to make visits. We welcome Mr. Ma Ying-jeou to lead the delegation to visit. We will make appropriate arrangements for the related activities and provide necessary convenience.\nAt present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and severe, but cross-strait exchanges and cooperation must not stop, must not be cut off, and must not be reduced. We, as always, welcome people from all walks of life in Taiwan and Taiwan compatriots at large to visit and exchange on the mainland often, to work hand in hand with us to strengthen exchanges and cooperation, to inherit and promote the excellent traditional Chinese culture, and to work for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705865.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705866.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","On June 5, President Xi Jinping held a phone call with US President Donald Trump at Trump’s request, stressing that the United States should handle the Taiwan question with prudence and avoid putting China and the United States in a dangerous situation of conflict and confrontation, which a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists could drag them into. In the current cross-Strait situation, how does…","The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests, and the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech sets out China's solemn position on the Taiwan question and provides the fundamental guidance for us in doing Taiwan work well.\nThe DPP authorities and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces obstinately hold to the \"Taiwan independence\" stance, constantly \"seeking independence through force\" and \"relying on external forces to seek independence,\" and colluding with external forces to carry out provocations seeking \"independence.\" They are the source of trouble for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nWe firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference. We will uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" unite broad Taiwan compatriots, and resolutely advance the country's reunification and national rejuvenation. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence, implement its commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence\" in earnest, avoid sending wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and not allow the schemes of a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" separatists to disrupt the overall situation of China-US relations to succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705867.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","The Tianhe District Branch of the Guangzhou Municipal Public Security Bureau recently issued a “Bounty Notice,” offering rewards for the arrest of 20 DPP authority hackers suspected of carrying out cyberattacks. This is also the first time public security organs have taken enforcement action to “draw the sword” against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that the…","On June 5, the Tianhe Branch of the Guangzhou Public Security Bureau issued a “Bounty Notice” that detailed how the DPP authorities’ “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command” (“资通电军”) directed and carried out illegal cyberattack activities, involving multiple violations of law and crimes, and placed a bounty on 20 criminal suspects who took part in carrying out cyberattacks. This is the public security organs drawing a sword against the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces through law enforcement action, and a concentrated crackdown on the organized cyber illegal and criminal conduct of Taiwan’s “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command.”\nBoth sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Anyone who endangers the country’s sovereignty, security, and development interests will not escape the sanctions of national law. The DPP authorities manipulated the “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command” to frequently carry out indiscriminate attacks and sabotage against mainland network facilities, disrupting social order and harming the interests of the people; the facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive. Next, we will continue to take effective measures in accordance with the law and pursue this to the end, and will absolutely not show leniency. First, we will make use of various judicial channels to severely crack down on the 20 wanted criminal suspects in accordance with the law. Second, we will place all personnel of the “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command” under key supervision, and once their illegal and criminal activities are discovered, will severely crack down on them in accordance with the law. Third, we will resolutely crack down in accordance with the law on the DPP authorities’ secret collusion with external forces to manipulate the “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command” to carry out cyberattacks and other illegal and criminal activities against mainland network facilities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705859.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","环球网记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently announced sanctions against companies affiliated with “Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang. Shen Boyang said that his family are traders, and that since being listed as a “Taiwan independence” diehard, business has dropped by half. He said this kind of punishment ultimately sacrifices the mainland’s own production interests. What comment do you have on this?","We absolutely will not tolerate, and absolutely will not indulge, die-hard “Taiwan independence” figures and their affiliated enterprises that engage in egregious “independence”-related conduct and rampant separatist activities. They must be severely punished in accordance with the law. Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., headed by Shen Tu-cheng, father of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang, has trade and business cooperation with certain mainland enterprises and has profited from it. We have decided to impose sanctions on Zhaoyi Co., Ltd. in accordance with the law, prohibiting it from conducting any transactions or cooperation with mainland organizations, enterprises, and individuals, and we will take other necessary measures against it. This demonstrates our resolute position that we will never allow affiliated companies of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figures to profit on the mainland. It also shows through facts that pursuing “Taiwan independence” harms oneself and others, and that it is absolutely impossible to escape justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705862.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","《人民政协报》记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait youth exchange activities.","Since May, cross-Strait youth exchange activities have been lively.\nOn May 22, the 7th Cross-Strait (Hubei) Youth Donghu Exchange Season was launched. Themed “Youth with Purpose, Creating the Future Together,” the exchange season features three sections, “Youth Experiences,” “Youth Innovation,” and “Youth Communication,” sharing stories of Taiwanese youth building careers in Hubei.\nFrom May 23 to 26, a delegation of young Taiwanese entrepreneurs in the cultural and creative industries visited well-known enterprises and cultural and creative industry clusters in Shenzhen, and held the “2025 Meet at Culture and Expo” cross-Strait cultural and creative industry youth entrepreneur roadshow, to see firsthand the achievements of Shenzhen’s special economic zone construction and the current state of its cultural and creative industry development.\nOn May 28, the 6th Kunshan Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Industry Salon was held. Themed “Industrialized Development of Artificial Intelligence (AI),” the event saw cross-Strait young scholars jointly discuss cutting-edge AI technologies.\nEntering June, localities will continue to hold youth exchange activities rich in content. The Jiangsu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office will launch the project solicitation activity for the 2025 Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition; the Guizhou Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office will hold multiple activities, including the “Qian-Taiwan Youth ‘Village BA’ Basketball Friendship Match” and the “‘Light and Shadow Guizhou Journey · Youth Shared Dream’ — 3rd Taiwan Youth Dream Guizhou Tour”; the Gansu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office will hold the 2nd “Longtai Cultural Exchange Month” activities; the Henan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office will hold a series of “Henan Province Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Month” activities; and the Shandong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office will hold the 2025 Lu-Taiwan Youth Cultural Exchange Festival, “Meet in Qilu, Bonded with China.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Film and television exchanges continue to be a highlight of cross-Strait exchanges. Could the spokesperson introduce what film and television cultural exchange activities have taken place recently?","Indeed, film and television exchange is one of the highlights of cross-Strait cultural exchange this year. Following the “Mainland Film Showcase” of the 16th Cross-Strait Film Festival, which brought seven popular mainland films to Taiwan audiences, the “Taiwan Film Showcase” of the 16th Cross-Strait Film Festival opened in Ya'an, Sichuan on June 7, screening six outstanding Taiwan films, which have been well received by mainland audiences.\nFrom June 13 to 22, the Shanghai International Film Festival will screen several films co-created by filmmakers from both sides of the Strait. The film *Bronze and Sunflower*, directed by well-known Taiwan director Chen Kun-hou together with filmmakers from both sides and based on a representative children's literature work by well-known mainland writer Cao Wenxuan, will hold its premiere on June 16. Several films involving Taiwan performers, such as *Twenty-Four Flavors* and *Father and Son, for Example*, have also entered the screening program.\nIn addition, China Media Group launched the special program *Rowing Toward Home and Country, Shen Shui Sings in Praise of the Duanwu Festival* during the Dragon Boat Festival. Among its segments, *Love Each Other* has been viewed over 30 million times online. Dr. Mao Ming-huan from Taipei told in the program the story of his studies, career and family in Shenyang. His Taiwanese accent already carries a strong Northeastern flavor, and both Taipei and Shenyang have become his hometowns. If everyone listens to the song *Love Each Other*, sung across the distance by children from Shenyang and Taipei, I believe you can deeply feel the warmth and affection of “both sides of the Strait are one family.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the DPP authorities forcibly pushed for the renaming of “Zhongzheng Road,” which triggered strong backlash and forced them to suspend it. Some public opinion has pointed out that this is merely another “de-Sinicization” manipulation by the DPP authorities and another “cultural purge.” What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities are incompetent in governance, and while they pursue “de-Sinicization” and “gradual Taiwan independence,” they come up with endless tricks and schemes. This fully exposes their “independence-seeking” nature and their willingness to stop at nothing for political self-interest. The strong backlash within Taiwan's society fully shows that the Taiwan public is weary of and disgusted with the DPP authorities' political manipulation. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Changing street names is no substitute for changing “the road”; only by abandoning “Taiwan independence” is there a way out.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Wu Feng-shan, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan, recently said that he hopes the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits will “treat the more than 23 million people of Taiwan with a correct attitude,” and that the two sides will patiently negotiate a framework for a “new cross-Strait relationship” and work together to pursue mutual benefit and common prosperity. What is your comment?","The Mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, Taiwan is part of China, and cross-Strait relations are not “state-to-state relations” or “one China, one Taiwan.” This is the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations, and it cannot and will not be changed. On this basis, ARATS and Taiwan's SEF reached the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle and established the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations. I would like to reiterate that as long as both sides return to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and acknowledge the fact that the two sides belong to one country and one nation, the dialogue and communication mechanism between the two organizations can be restarted.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705863.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently gave an interview in which he put forward a “corporate merger theory,” arguing that “the two sides of the Strait can discuss mergers, and the mainland can set conditions.” Some public opinion on the island holds that, at least at the civil or informal level, the two sides could begin discussing “setting conditions for each other.” What comments do you have on this?","Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots, and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Reunification is a historical conclusion; it is the general trend, the righteous cause, and the will of the people.\nOn the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to exchange views extensively and conduct in-depth consultations with political parties, sectors, and social strata in Taiwan on cross-Strait relations and national reunification, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification. We welcome people from all walks of life on the island to actively offer suggestions on the prospects of achieving peaceful reunification of the motherland, and to explore with us the “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan and enrich the practice of peaceful reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705864.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, Singaporean Foreign Minister Vivian Balakrishnan, in a speech at the U.S. think tank Hudson Institute, said that conflict in the Taiwan Strait is “not inevitable” and that “no Southeast Asian country is willing to become a proxy battlefield.” What is your comment on this?","These remarks reflect the concern of countries in the region about the US fanning the flames in the Asia-Pacific to maintain its own hegemony, and clearly express their unwillingness to become a “proxy battlefield.” The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, reflecting the will of the people and the trend of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Chinese J-10C fighter jet and PL-15 missile demonstrated overwhelming superiority in the India-Pakistan air combat, drawing great attention from public opinion on the island. Some public opinion points out that this has shattered the DPP authorities' fantasy of “using force to resist unification,” and once again reveals the objective reality of the vast disparity in military strength across the Taiwan Strait.…","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance, seeking to “rely on foreign powers to pursue independence” and “resist reunification by force,” which is entirely overestimating themselves and seeking their own dead end. We have firm confidence, strong resolve, and powerful capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and achieve national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The DPP authorities earlier required 12,000 mainland spouses to supplement the so-called “certificate of loss of original nationality,” and the three-month deadline is approaching. According to reports, only over 3,000 have so far completed the supplementary submission, and many mainland spouses who cannot provide the certificate will face the penalty of having their household registration in Taiwan cancelled.…","Cross-Strait marriage families are a vivid embodiment of \"cross-Strait compatriots are one family.\" Mainland spouses in Taiwan are our relatives, and are also family and kin to Taiwan compatriots. Like Taiwan residents, they work and live on the island and should rightfully receive fair treatment from Taiwan society. The DPP authorities have repeatedly discriminated against and suppressed mainland spouses in Taiwan, and have repeatedly abused administrative and judicial means to bully and persecute parties to cross-Strait marriages, pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" to the point of violating human relations and extinguishing human nature. These brutal practices have been met with strong condemnation and opposition from public opinion on the island and from broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council's government website has launched a \"special column for reporting vicious acts by 'Taiwan independence' enforcers and accomplices who persecute Taiwan compatriots.\" We hope that those who are persecuted or who are aware of relevant clues will send the relevant information to the reporting email address. Based on facts and guided by law, we will hold accountable and severely punish, in accordance with the law, those \"Taiwan independence\" enforcers and accomplices who cooperate with the DPP authorities in persecuting mainland spouses in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the “Archives of the Taiwan Volunteer Corps” were selected for the national-level registry, drawing attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait. What is the significance of this for commemorating the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. The inclusion of the “Taiwan Volunteer Corps Archives” in the sixth batch of the “Chinese Archival Documentary Heritage List” is of positive significance. The Taiwan Volunteer Corps was a unit formed by Taiwan compatriots during the War of Resistance that directly participated in the War of Resistance for the motherland. The “Taiwan Volunteer Corps Archives” are preserved in the Second Historical Archives of China, the Fujian Provincial Archives, the Nanping Municipal Archives and the Wuyishan Municipal Archives. The 625 original archival documents, as conclusive physical evidence, truly and completely record the entire process of the Taiwan Volunteer Corps, from its formation and anti-Japanese activities to its return to Taiwan, with the purpose of “defending the motherland and recovering Taiwan.” They restore the history of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly resisting foreign aggression and restoring Taiwan, and powerfully prove the objective fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China and that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are connected by blood and share a common destiny.\nWe hope that compatriots in Taiwan will work with us to tell well the story of the “Taiwan Volunteer Corps Archives” documentary heritage, carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance, adhere to the One-China Principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, resolutely safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and work together to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705858.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, a media outlet in Taiwan reported that before the opening of the second Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit, the mainland side arranged closed-door meetings for senior executives of some media outlets, put forward requirements for propaganda work targeting Taiwan, and asked the Taiwanese media attending to assist in “intelligence gathering” for the “Nine-in-One” elections next year after they return to…","The relevant reports are entirely groundless and maliciously fabricated.\nOut of political self-interest in pursuing “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities habitually instruct specific media and their kept internet troll armies to commit cognitive fraud against the Taiwan public, attempting to attack and smear the mainland as obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, inciting “anti-China and resisting China,” and vigorously pursuing “green dictatorship and terror politics,” which seriously infringes on the interests of the Taiwan public. The fabrications and smears of the green media on the island cannot intimidate the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots who are committed to maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, nor can they stop the trend of cross-Strait exchanges. The DPP authorities’ crude tricks also cannot deceive the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and they cannot stop the direction and pace of the forward development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","On April 5, Zhang Liqi, a Taiwanese youth teaching at Huaqiao University, had his Taiwan identity canceled by the DPP authorities for obtaining a Taiwan residence certificate. This is the first case of an investigation involving a holder of a Taiwan residence certificate. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The Settlement Permit has been in use for many years. It is a temporary, transitional identity document issued to Taiwan residents who have been approved to settle in the mainland, and it is held for a short period. Holding a Settlement Permit does not mean obtaining mainland household registration (hukou). If a holder does not complete household registration procedures with mainland public security authorities within the prescribed time, the holder will not have mainland household registration, and their Settlement Permit will also expire and become invalid.\nThe relevant remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council reveal its true face of arrogance, bullying, and oppression of the weak. They expose its sinister intent to abuse the judicial system to persecute ordinary people and to threaten and intimidate Taiwan compatriots. Such retrograde actions seriously harm the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan residents and seriously undermine exchanges between the peoples on both sides of the Strait, and they have met with growing dissatisfaction and firm opposition from more and more Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwanese internet celebrity “Curator” Chen Zhihan recently traveled to Shanghai and Hangzhou and livestreamed on YouTube. Many people on the island say his trip will break the green camp’s lies. The “Taiwan independence” internet celebrity “Minnan Wolf” said that “Curator” is walking the path he once walked. What comment do you have?","I have seen that Mr. Chen arrived in Shanghai yesterday, and I wish him a smooth and pleasant trip.\nWe welcome compatriots in Taiwan, including Taiwan internet celebrities, to come to the mainland for various fresh and high-quality experiences, including sampling local specialty foods, riding convenient and comfortable transportation, and purchasing quality goods. We hope everyone can share their experiences with friends on both sides of the Strait in a friendly and objective manner and enhance mutual understanding.\nIt must be emphasized that anything that helps enhance mutual understanding among people on both sides of the Strait will, we believe, be supported and welcomed by people on both sides. Conversely, deliberate acts that interfere with and obstruct mutual understanding between people on both sides, stir up mutual discord, or undermine mutual trust will only be opposed and condemned by people on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","According to reports, the Trump administration plans to substantially increase arms sales to Taiwan in its second term, with the scale of arms sales approved over the next four years expected to exceed the total of its first term, which was US$18.3 billion. The US is also pressuring Taiwan's “opposition party” not to obstruct the DPP authorities from raising the defense budget. In addition, Lai Qingde said…","We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to Taiwan, China, and urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with prudence, stop selling arms to Taiwan, stop “arming Taiwan,” and stop supporting and encouraging the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in “seeking independence through force.”\nRecently, a domestic opinion poll in Taiwan showed that more than 60 percent of respondents believe that the US demand for Taiwan to raise its arms procurement payments is intended to sell more weapons and earn more money. This fully proves that more and more people in Taiwan have recognized the sinister intentions of the United States in treating Taiwan as an “ATM” and a “powder keg.” But the Lai Ching-te authorities, in order to seek personal gain for “Taiwan independence,” have defied public opinion, disregarded Taiwan's domestic security interests, willingly allowed themselves to be butchered, and without any bottom line, “sold out Taiwan” and “harmed Taiwan.” This conduct of “relying on outside forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705860.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视直新闻记者","Reportedly, a European national leader attending the 22nd Shangri-La Dialogue said that if Russia were allowed to occupy parts of Ukraine's territory without restraint, “what would happen to Taiwan?” What is your comment?","First, it must be pointed out that the Taiwan question and the Ukraine question are fundamentally different. The most fundamental difference is that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is entirely China's internal affair, brooking no external interference. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. Relevant countries should adhere to the one-China principle through practical actions, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","US Vice President JD Vance recently said that in the future the United States will no longer fight meaningless wars or become entangled in endless conflicts, and will shift toward a strategy based on protecting core US interests. Public opinion on the island points out that Vance's remarks overturn the theoretical basis of “Taiwan independence,” and that if conflict breaks out in the Taiwan Strait, it can be…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no foreign interference is tolerated. The United States should handle the Taiwan question with caution and avoid dragging China and the US into the dangerous situation of conflict and confrontation because of a very small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists. The US “backing Taiwan” lie fabricated by the DPP authorities at great cost has already collapsed on its own. More and more people in Taiwan are coming to realize that the United States always pursues “America first,” that Taiwan is merely a “chess piece” for the US to contain the mainland, and that relying on outsiders is unreliable and “Taiwan independence” is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250611_12705861.htm"],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Some media have revealed that, apart from Shen Boyang, DPP politicians including Zheng Lijun, Ke Jianming, Zhang Honglu, Huang Jie, Gu Lixiong and He Zhiwei have all been making “mainland money” through their families. Island public opinion has criticized that these people, on the one hand, manipulate ideology to “oppose and resist China,” and on the other hand, rake in huge profits on the mainland. They are…","Shen Boyang and his ilk wildly incite “anti-China” sentiment and tout “Taiwan independence” purely to seek personal gain. To pursue personal interests, they are willing to harm the interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, which is despicable and shameless. The criticism from island public opinion shows that the people's eyes are sharp, and right and wrong reside in people's hearts. We will never allow anyone to earn money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","The TAO announced punitive measures against companies linked to “Taiwan independence” diehard Puma Shen. Will further punitive measures be taken, and if so, what specifically?","Punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang and his affiliated companies in accordance with the law is a forceful sanction and a resolute crackdown on the provocations of “Taiwan independence” forces seeking “independence.” If “Taiwan independence” elements misjudge the situation and persist headstrong, they will only pay a more painful price.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The “Taiwan Democracy Culture and Education Foundation” recently released poll results showing that 66% of respondents on the island believe the Trump administration may sell out Taiwan for US interests, and 67% of respondents believe the US mainly treats Taiwan as a bargaining chip in its game with mainland China. Only 12% believe the US truly wants to “defend Taiwan.” What is your comment?","The relevant opinion poll reflects broad Taiwan compatriots' widespread skepticism about the United States playing the “Taiwan card” and their concern about their own future and destiny. It also shows that more and more people in Taiwan recognize the essence of the United States' policy of “America First,” see through the DPP's attempt to sell Taiwan cheaply in pursuit of one party's narrow self-interest, and recognize that pawns will inevitably become discarded pieces.\nWe hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will join us in promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and in building a peaceful home where compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live in tranquility. Only this can bring real benefits and well-being to Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The mainland TV drama “Legend of Zang Hai” has held a place in the “top ten most-watched in Taiwan today” for seven consecutive days. Island media reported that the drama made viewers keep watching without wanting to stop, and listed its memorable lines. What is your comment on the growing popularity among island residents of mainland film and television works?","Entering the new era, we have promoted cultural prosperity, and the construction of the cultural industry has continued to achieve new progress and new accomplishments. A large number of original cultural masterpieces have emerged, earning high recognition from the market and widespread love from audiences. Compatriots on both sides share the same writing system and ethnicity and have a common cultural root, so they naturally feel emotional resonance with outstanding cross-Strait film and television works. TV dramas, films and documentaries produced on the mainland are increasingly liked and recognized by Taiwan residents.\nWith summer vacation approaching, more than 60 films will be scheduled for release, and several TV dramas are poised to launch. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to the mainland to experience a feast on the big screen. We hope that more outstanding mainland film and television works can be shown in Taiwan in a timely manner, and we are pleased to see cross-Strait industry players join hands to create more excellent works that bring audiences on both sides more shared memories of the era and more enjoyment of light and shadow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声记者","According to U.S. media reports, retired U.S. Army Major General Mark Montgomery told Congress that about 500 U.S. military personnel are active in Taiwan, ten times the figure the U.S. side disclosed earlier. He also agitated for increasing the number of U.S. military personnel in Taiwan “to 1,000,” but did not specify the identity or status of these personnel. May I ask what the spokesperson's comment is on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and not attempt to cross red lines or play with fire on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities should stop their tactic of “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” and abandon their fantasy of “seeking independence by force of arms.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国新闻社记者","According to reports, the Mainland Affairs Council is drafting amendments to the “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” to strengthen the management mechanism for travel to the mainland, Hong Kong, and Macao. In the future, Taiwan public officials traveling to the mainland, Hong Kong, or Macao will need to apply for and obtain approval. What is your comment on this?","For some time, the DPP authorities have continuously obstructed and restricted cross-strait exchange and cooperation, and have intimidated and suppressed Taiwan people who take part in cross-strait exchanges. Whether they are pushing for so-called amendments to “regulations” or strengthening control and review, the essence is self-serving “independence-seeking” interests. They are vigorously staging a “green terror,” fully exposing their hypocritical face of saying one thing and doing another. This will only meet with increasing opposition and condemnation from the people of Taiwan.\nFacts have proven, and will continue to prove, that neither intimidating and restricting Taiwan compatriots from participating in cross-strait exchanges nor fabricating rumors and smearing the mainland can suppress the popular will for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. Nor can they block the historical tide that cross-strait exchange and cooperation cannot stop, cannot be cut off, and cannot be reduced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","U.S. Secretary of Defense Hegseth said at the 22nd Shangri-La Dialogue, “China's threat to Taiwan may be imminent, and if China attempts to seize Taiwan, it will bring devastating consequences.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no interference from any external force. Some people in the US keep hyping the so-called “China threat theory” and exaggerating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is making excuses to interfere in the Taiwan question and serves the US's own political interests. We firmly oppose this. The US side should adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop fanning the flames in the Taiwan Strait region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报封面新闻记者","Recently, at the “2025 European Day Dinner” on the island, Lai Ching-te said he hopes to further establish an institutionalized mechanism for economic, trade and investment relations with Europe, and to promote the signing of a “Taiwan-EU Economic Partnership Agreement.” He said Taiwan will actively cooperate with democratic countries including those in Europe to jointly build a “non-red supply chain” that is…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between our diplomatic partners and the Taiwan region of China, and the signing of any agreement with sovereign implications or official character. Lai, catering to the wishes of external forces who are trying to build a so-called “non-red supply chain” and rehashing the old tune of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” is violating economic and market laws. In exchange for external forces’ support for his plotting of independence, he is selling off Taiwan’s advantageous industries, sacrificing Taiwan’s development prospects, and smashing the “rice bowls” of the Taiwan people. Such a scheme, which wastes people’s effort and money and sells out Taiwan by clinging to outside powers, is bound to be opposed and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","The mainland opened tourism for Fujian residents to Matsu and Kinmen last year. What is your view of the current state of cross-Strait tourism? Is there a plan to further extend tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for residents of the 20 cities in the original Haixi region?","We have stated our position on the relevant issues many times. It must be pointed out that the crux of and obstacle to cross-Strait tourism issues lie in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities. We have always upheld the concept that \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" and we have continued to make efforts and release goodwill to promote exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including cross-Strait personnel exchanges and tourism. The DPP authorities should remove, as soon as possible, all the obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation, and create conditions for cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Taiwanese internet celebrity “Guanzhang” (Curator) is traveling in Shanghai and livestreaming the entire trip. Was Guanzhang’s visit to the mainland at the invitation of the mainland? Is his livestreaming throughout Shanghai legal and compliant?","As far as I know, Mr. Chen and his team traveled to Shanghai on their own. As for some of his activities during his time in Shanghai, they should be conducted in compliance with the relevant laws and regulations.\nI also have a piece of news to share with everyone.\nLast September, after the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” was officially launched, people on both sides of the Strait showed much care and attention, and we thank them. We have noted that many people are very interested in the Taiwan issue and hope to obtain more information. To this end, we will hold a Taiwan-related knowledge quiz activity on the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” to help people on both sides of the Strait learn more about basic Taiwan-related knowledge and understand the central government's policies toward Taiwan and the work done by various regions and departments.\nThe Taiwan-related knowledge quiz will be held once a month for 12 consecutive issues. Today, the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will publish the first issue, with 20 questions. Friends who follow the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” may leave their answers in the comment section. Netizens who answer all questions correctly and rank among the top 10 in likes will receive an exquisite souvenir. This souvenir was carefully selected by us: it is a shell-carving work titled 《Treasure Island Taiwan》, designed by a national first-class craftsman and hand-made by pupils at Pingtan's primary schools. It embodies the meaning of “little hands joining both sides of the Strait, with ‘shell’ (贝) adding visible sincerity,” and expresses the shared wish of compatriots on both sides that they are connected by blood and by hand and long for reunion. The answer period is 14 days. At our next press conference, we will announce the list of netizens who received the first-issue souvenirs. We look forward to everyone's active participation.\nThank you all. This press conference is now concluded.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250611_12705833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-06-13","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the Taipei School of Economics and Political Science Foundation recently held an unofficial \"chief-of-staff\" level war-gaming on a Taiwan crisis for the first time. The former \"Chief of the General Staff\" of the Taiwan military, the former Chairman of the US Joint Chiefs of Staff, and the former Chief of Staff of the Japan Self-Defense Forces participated the event. In addition, the US and…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no external interference. Any action that emboldens the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to seek secession will undermine cross-Strait peace and stability. Whoever does that is bound to get burnt for playing with fire, and taste the bitter fruit of its own doing. We urge relevant countries to truly abide by the one-China principle, and stop sending any wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. In front of the prevailing trend of the ultimate andcertain reunification of China, any scheme to solicit foreign support for independence and contain China with Taiwan is doomed to failure.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250613-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16391242.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-06-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answers reporters' questions\n(June 13, 2025)\nQ: It is understood that Taiwan's “Tourism Administration” has refused the application of mainland personnel to enter the island to hold the 2025 Cross-Strait Taipei Summer Travel Expo. What is your comment on this?\nA:\nWe have always upheld the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” actively supported promoting the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and the regularization of exchanges in all fields, responded to the eager expectations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchanges and visits, and taken practical measures on cross-Strait tourism issues to benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In contrast, the DPP authorities, for the sake of their political self-interest in seeking “independence,” have repeatedly delayed and obstructed the resumption of cross-Strait tourism. Now they are arbitrarily interfering with travel expos and other tourism industry exchange and cooperation matters, once again exposing their vicious intention to cut off cross-Strait exchanges and visits, and their ugly face of disregarding the plight of the industry and not caring about the livelihood of the people.\nThe mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that seeks peace, development, exchange, and cooperation cannot be ignored by anyone, and the wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to come closer and visit each other cannot be suppressed by anyone. The various reckless acts of the DPP authorities that go against the will of the people and the trend of the times have already aroused widespread dissatisfaction and opposition in Taiwan's industry and among the public, and they will inevitably face a backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250613_12706294.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-06-17","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Bloomberg has reported that the Taiwanese authorities, in response to U.S. pressure, have added Huawei and SMIC, the chip company, to Taiwan’s version of the entities list. Does China have a response to this?","China opposes the U.S. politicizing tech and trade issues, overstretching the concept of national security, abusing export control and long-arm jurisdiction, and maliciously blocking and suppressing China. The DPP authorities’ kneeling and ingratiating themselves with the U.S. will only hurt and ruin Taiwan’s interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250617_11651839.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250617_11651778.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-06-18","Guo Jiakun","China Daily","On June 17 local time, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said in his chair’s summary after hosting the G7 Summit that they stressed the importance of constructive and stable relations with China, while calling on China to refrain from market distortions and overcapacity, and expressed serious concerns about China’s destabilizing activities in the East and South China Seas and the importance of maintaining peace…","The G7 Summit once again manipulated issues related to China. The G7 made irresponsible remarks on Taiwan, the South China Sea, and the East China Sea, falsely accused China of “overcapacity” and “market distortion”. This constitutes interference in China’s internal affairs and violation of the basic norms governing international relations. China firmly opposes this and has lodged strong protests with relevant parties.\nThe biggest factor undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces. If the G7 truly cares about peace in the Taiwan Strait, it should abide by the one-China principle, categorically oppose “Taiwan independence”, and support China’s reunification.\nAt present, the situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable. The G7 should respect the joint efforts of regional countries to resolve issues through dialogue and consultation and maintain peace and stability, and stop using maritime issues to sow discord between regional countries and escalate regional tensions.\nThe so-called “market distortions” and “overcapacity” accusations are absolutely false. The G7 use them as an excuse for their trade protectionist practices, and to essentially contain and suppress China’s industrial progress, and politicize and weaponize economic and trade issues.\nChina once again urges the G7 to see the overwhelming global trend, abandon the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop instigating conflict and confrontation, and act in the interest of the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250618_11652681.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250618_11652470.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-06-20","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te on Thursday ordered defense and security units to step up their monitoring and intelligence efforts in response to China’s military activities, which he said have not abated even as tensions rise in the Middle East. Do you have any comment on this?","The DPP authorities just won’t pass up any chance of newsjacking. Yet no matter what they say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the inevitability of China’s reunification. To seek independence through military build-up will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250620_11654061.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250620_11654029.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-06-20","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","According to authorities in Taiwan, in the past 24 hours, 46 PLA planes crossed the median line in the Strait. What is China’s reason for these flights? Does it have anything to do with the British and Japanese naval vessels that went through the Strait or with the visit of U.S. congressmen to Taiwan recently?","The Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. China respects countries’ lawful right to navigation in relevant waters of the Taiwan Strait, but firmly opposes any country making provocations or threatening China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250620_11654061.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250620_11654029.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-06-23","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Youth Daily","We noted that the temporary flight evacuating Chinese nationals from Iran has arrived in China from Turkmenistan recently. Can you share with us the progress in China’s evacuation work from Iran and Israel?","Acting on the decisions and plans of the Party Central Committee, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, China’s diplomatic and consular missions in Iran and other countries, the Ministry of Transport and the Civil Aviation Administration worked together for the evacuation of 3,125 Chinese nationals from Iran to safety. Among them, there are a 10-month-old baby, a 70-year-old senior, and citizens from Hong Kong and Taiwan. As the Chinese nationals who are willing to leave Iran have all been safely evacuated, the large-scale and well-ordered evacuation of Chinese personnel in Iran has been completed by the Chinese government. At the same time, China’s Embassy in Israel helped and organized the evacuation of over 500 Chinese nationals from Israel to safety, and helped some nationals from the UK, India and Poland safely evacuate.\nDuring the evacuation, countries, including Iran, Azerbaijan, Turkmenistan, Armenia, Türkiye, Iraq, the UAE, Oman, Kuwait, Egypt and Jordan, offered China valuable support. We express sincere appreciation for that.\nStill, some Chinese nationals choose to stay in Iran and Israel. Our Ministry reminds them to stay safe. Our colleagues in Chinese diplomatic and consular missions in Iran and Israel have stayed on their post, and will continue to do everything possible to offer Chinese nationals there assistance.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250623_11655211.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250623_11655121.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-06-23","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: on the 22nd, Taiwan’s leader began the first lecture of the so-called “Ten Lectures on National Unity.” What is your comment on the content of the speech that involves cross-Strait relations?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that Lai Ching-te's speech on the 22nd was full of lies and deception, hostility and provocation. It deliberately distorted and fragmented history, vigorously peddled separatist “Taiwan independence” fallacies, attempted to fabricate and cobble together a basis for constructing a “Taiwan independence” narrative, and used propaganda hype to seek political gain for his push for the “great recall” political struggle. It is a blatant “Taiwan independence” manifesto that incites cross-strait antagonism and confrontation, and a hodgepodge of error-ridden “Taiwan independence” sophistry, fully exposing his obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature.\nIn his speech, Lai Ching-te deliberately falsified Taiwan's history, denied the fact that Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times, denied that Taiwan's Indigenous peoples migrated to Taiwan directly or indirectly from the mainland, and disregarded the fact that successive Chinese governments have exercised jurisdiction over Taiwan. This is a distortion and trampling of history.\nIn his speech, Lai Ching-te ignored the historical fact that compatriots in Taiwan and on the mainland, united in heart and mind, jointly resisted external aggression, paid tremendous sacrifices to defeat foreign invaders, and brought Taiwan back to the embrace of the motherland. He linked the patriotic, homeland-loving, and land-loving sentiments of Taiwan compatriots with so-called “Taiwan independence,” attempting to delude the people of Taiwan. This is a betrayal and crime against the glorious patriotic tradition of the Taiwanese people and the sacrifices and contributions of countless martyrs.\nIn his speech, Lai Ching-te twisted concepts, obliterated the fruits of victory in World War II, and disregarded a series of legal documents with the force of international law, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. He challenged and distorted UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, falsely claimed that “Taiwan does not belong to China,” and advocated “mutual non-subordination.” This completely violates international law and is a blatant challenge to the authority of international law.\nIn his speech, Lai Ching-te spouted arrogant rhetoric, ignored the common aspiration of Taiwan's people for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and loudly propagated the so-called “mainland threat,” advocated pushing forward the “17 response strategies,” manipulated “anti-China and resist-China” rhetoric, and strengthened “green terror,” obstructing cross-strait exchanges and interactions. This completely goes against the wishes of the people.\nHistory cannot be altered, facts cannot be denied, and right and wrong cannot be reversed. All historical, factual, and legal evidence concerning Taiwan proves that Taiwan has been an inseparable part of Chinese territory since ancient times. Abundant archaeological discoveries and historical literature prove that the Chinese people were the first to develop and build Taiwan. Since the Song and Yuan dynasties, successive Chinese central governments began to establish administration over Taiwan and exercise administrative jurisdiction. In 1885, the Qing government made Taiwan a province, the 20th province of China at that time. In April 1895, Japan forced the Qing government to sign the unequal Treaty of Shimonoseki and seized Taiwan. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the United States, and the United Kingdom in 1943; the Potsdam Proclamation jointly signed by China, the United States, and the United Kingdom in 1945, later joined by the Soviet Union; and the Instrument of Surrender of Japan signed by Japan all clearly stipulated that Taiwan must be returned to China. On October 25, 1945, the Chinese government recovered Taiwan and the Penghu Islands and resumed exercising sovereignty over Taiwan. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was proclaimed, becoming the sole legal government representing all of China and the sole legal representative of China in the international arena. This is a case where, with the international legal subject unchanged, a new regime replaced the old one; China's sovereignty and inherent territory were not changed as a result, and the government of the People's Republic of China naturally enjoys and exercises full sovereignty over Taiwan. Since then, a series of political documents between China and Japan have also confirmed the fact that Taiwan returned to China. Taiwan is part of China, and Taiwan has never been a country. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community.\nLai Ching-te's various fallacies fabricated in defiance of history, reality, and legal principles will only be swept into the dustbin of history. The future of Taiwan can only be decided jointly by the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. No matter how hard Lai Ching-te schemes, he cannot change the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle, and certainly cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will be reunified and must be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250623_12707976.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","On June 25 at 10:00 a.m., the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first announced the fee reduction policy for “first-time visitors” (首来族) applying for Taiwan Compatriot Permits, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Good morning, everyone, and welcome to our regular press conference. Before taking questions, I would like to announce a piece of news. To further facilitate travel between the mainland and Taiwan compatriots and expand personnel exchanges and cooperation between the two sides, and after consultation between the Ministry of Finance, the National Development and Reform Commission and the National Immigration Administration, it has been decided that from July 1, 2025 to December 31, 2027, the fee for applying for a Taiwan compatriot permit will be waived for “first-time visitors” from Taiwan. The National Immigration Administration will organize the specific implementation of this policy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708363.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 17th Straits Forum has drawn close attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Could the spokesperson introduce what achievements this Straits Forum has produced?","The 17th Straits Forum Conference was successfully held in Xiamen, Fujian, on June 15. To date, the Straits Forum has held 42 series events, with 14 more events to be held, and has achieved fruitful results.\nWang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the Forum Conference and delivered a speech. Before the conference began, he met with representatives of the Taiwan guests attending the Forum, reaffirming the policies, positions, and attitudes of adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and firmly and unswervingly advancing the cause of national reunification. He stressed that the mainland “always grasps the overall situation of cross-strait relations from the perspective of the overall interests and long-term development of the Chinese nation, and firmly serves as a strong backing and reliance for Taiwan compatriots,” which resonated with compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nDespite the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' determined attempts to interfere and obstruct the preparations for this Forum, more than 7,000 Taiwan compatriots enthusiastically attended, of whom Taiwan youth accounted for over 40%. This fully demonstrates that frequent exchanges, mutual visits, and closeness between relatives are the common wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and that cross-strait exchange and cooperation reflect the will of the people and the trend of the times; no one can suppress or block it. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou, former Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, attended the Forum for the first time and led young students on a visit in Fujian. In his speech at the Forum Conference, Mr. Ma said, “Although cross-strait relations face many challenges at present, the emotional bonds and exchanges between the peoples on both sides of the Strait cannot be severed,” expressing the common voice of the people on the island. During the Forum, Taiwan guests from all sectors actively called for the early realization of normalized personnel exchanges across the Strait and regularized exchanges in all fields, hoping that cross-strait relations will soon return to the right track. This Forum added five new events, including the Cross-Strait Emergency Firefighting Integrated Development Forum, further broadening the scope of cross-strait exchanges.\nTaking the second anniversary of the issuance of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” as an opportunity, this Forum focused on showcasing the phased achievements in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone and demonstrated Fujian's new look of region-wide integrated development in promoting cross-strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation. During the Forum, a series of Taiwan-related policy measures and cooperation projects were released and implemented, such as the “Several Measures on Financial Support for Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” jointly issued by the People's Bank of China and the State Administration of Foreign Exchange; Fujian Province officially released the country's first online financial application scenario for Taiwan compatriots based on “dual-certificate linkage”; the Fujian Provincial Modern Marine Fisheries Innovation Cross-Strait Science and Technology Cooperation Base was unveiled; the local standard “Mazu Ceremony Shared Across the Taiwan Strait” was officially released; and 10 Fujian-Taiwan agricultural and rural integrated development cooperation projects were signed. These concrete actions and forceful measures pushed the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone to go deeper and be more substantive.\nThe Forum centered on “Intangible Cultural Heritage Chinese New Year,” the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, and carried out a series of cultural exchange activities deeply loved by Taiwan compatriots, all centered on shared historical memories, national sentiment, and cultural roots across the Strait. At the Forum Conference, Lin Ming-tsung, Chairman of the Taiwan Association of Relatives of Anti-Japanese Martyrs, shared the story of the Lin family of Wufeng and their ancestors' devotion to Taiwan's restoration and service to the nation through the war of resistance, awakening Taiwan compatriots' sense of national consciousness and feelings of family and country. At the Cross-Strait Literature Forum, guests from both sides paid tribute to Chinese classics through poetry gatherings. On the cross-strait dragon boat race course, compatriots on both sides rowed with vigor and competed fiercely, drawing strength from remembering the past and reflecting on history. At the opening ceremony of the Cross-Strait Guandi Tourism and Cultural Festival, compatriots on both sides performed the intangible cultural heritage dance “Fish Leaping, Joyful Songs,” praying for national peace and prosperity. At the Straits Youth Forum, the creative team of the Hokkien-language version of “Chang'an Three Myriad Li” used Hokkien dialect to recreate the thousand-year-old Tang sounds, joining Taiwan youth in promoting Hokkien culture. In addition, the Organizing Committee invited more than 1,400 Taiwan compatriots to watch the film “Ne Zha 2,” which was highly praised by Taiwan guests attending the Forum. Through these immersive cultural experiences, Taiwan compatriots truly and vividly felt the profound heritage and boundless charm of Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708362.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Question: Spokesperson, what important cross-Strait exchange activities will be held in various localities this summer?","The energy and enthusiasm for exchange among compatriots on both sides of the Strait continue to erupt, and exchanges across all sectors on both sides are flourishing and remain vibrant, playing an important role in improving the atmosphere of cross-strait exchange and building momentum to drive the development of cross-strait relations.\nThe exchange activities in June were rich and colorful. The Sichuan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office successively held the 10th Cross-Strait Students' Giant Panda Conservation Experience Camp and the 2025 “Cultural Resistance Tour of Sichuan and Chongqing” cross-strait media reporting activity, in which cross-strait university faculty and students, descendants of War of Resistance veterans, scholars researching the history of the War of Resistance, and media actively participated. The Jiangsu Grand Theatre's original ethnic dance drama “Dream of the Red Chamber” was performed four times in a row at the Taipei Performing Arts Center, offering a cultural feast to Taiwan audiences, and nearly 6,000 Taiwan audience members deeply experienced the profound heritage and unique charm of Chinese traditional aesthetics. Shenzhen launched a series of activities under the “Shenzhen Taiwan Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Empowerment Program,” building a larger platform and providing more precise services for Taiwan youth studying, starting businesses and working in Shenzhen.\nEntering the summer vacation, cross-strait exchanges have become even more lively, with more highlights in various fields. In cultural exchange, the following will be held: the 2025 Cross-Strait Visit on Chinese Traditional Culture and Modernization, the 2025 Cross-Strait Chinese Studies Academy, the Shaanxi-Taiwan Cultural Exchange Week, the 2025 Cross-Strait Dachen Hometown Culture Festival, the “Enjoy the Mountains and Seas, Meet in Hunan” 2025 Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Exchange and the 2nd Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Music Festival, the 7th Cross-Strait Great Yu Culture Exchange Event, and the 3rd Cross-Strait Tibetology Symposium.\nIn educational exchange, the following will be held: the 2025 Beijing-Taiwan Education Exchange Week, Qingtai Teacher Study Tour, the 2025 Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Basic Education Exchange, the “Dreaming on the Pearl River · Guangzhou-Taiwan Exchange Season,” and the 17th Straits Forum · Cross-Strait Vocational Education Forum, among other activities. These will build bridges for universities and teachers and students on both sides, and for professionals in all fields, to share educational resources, create development opportunities together, and seek cooperation for mutual benefit.\nIn youth exchange, the following will be launched successively: the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the Yu-Taiwan Youth Poetry Gathering, the Lu-Taiwan Youth Culture Exchange Season, the Cross-Strait (Hubei-Taiwan) Youth Jingchu Tour, and other exchange activities that young people on both sides enjoy.\nWe sincerely welcome people from all sectors of Taiwan society to actively take part, to come to the mainland more often to see and experience things for themselves, and to personally participate in cross-strait exchange, cooperation and integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Reportedly, a conference commemorating the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration will be held around October 25. Please introduce the relevant situation. What is the significance of holding such commemorative activities under the current situation in cross-Strait relations?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the world’s anti-fascist war, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. The restoration of Taiwan is an important achievement of the victory in the War of Resistance, a great triumph forged through the courageous and bloody struggle of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and is worthy of joint commemoration by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The commemorative conference marking the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan will be held around October 25.\nThe history of Taiwan’s restoration irrefutably proves that Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait form a community of shared destiny. The DPP authorities have continuously engaged in provocations to seek independence, peddled “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, disregarded historical facts, glossed over and glorified Japan’s colonial rule, and betrayed the nation, which is disgraceful. Looking back to learn for the future, we hope that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will join us in remembering the history of the War of Resistance, defending the fruits of Taiwan’s restoration and its return to the motherland, upholding the great righteousness of the nation, firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, safeguarding our shared home of the Chinese nation, jointly promoting the reunification of the motherland, and jointly realizing the great dream of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708360.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Ma Ying-jeou led Taiwanese youth to the mainland to take part in the 17th Straits Forum and other activities, promoting exchanges and interactions between people on both sides of the Strait, and was widely praised by all sectors on the island. However, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council called Ma’s conduct, in cooperating with the mainland’s “united front,” a “disqualifying act.” What is your comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, as close as blood and water, and should frequently visit each other, deepen mutual understanding, and cooperate for mutual benefit. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou leading Taiwanese youths to take part in cross-Strait exchange activities such as the Straits Forum reflects the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and has been fully affirmed and positively evaluated by compatriots on both sides. Out of its nature of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities deliberately obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, attempt to sever the bonds of kinship between compatriots on both sides, turn back the wheel of history, go against public opinion, and have lost popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the Israel-Iran conflict has become grave. The Chinese Embassy in Israel issued a notice for Chinese citizens to register for evacuation, and Taiwan residents holding Taiwan Compatriot Permits may also register. In response, the Mainland Affairs Council said the mainland is using this to shape an image of itself as a “protector of Taiwan’s people.” What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese. We have always attached great importance to safeguarding the safety and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. From providing consular document services to assisting with foreign civil disputes involving Taiwan residents as well as economic and criminal cases, and from natural disasters such as typhoons and earthquakes to emergency evacuation of citizens during war and conflict, we have contacted local Taiwan compatriots at the first opportunity and provided necessary assistance.\nAfter the Israel-Iran conflict broke out, relevant departments and the Chinese embassies and consulates in Iran and Israel immediately activated the emergency consular protection mechanism. They requested that both countries effectively ensure the safety of Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots, promptly issued relevant reminders and guidelines, maintained close contact with local compatriots, guided them in taking safety precautions and emergency evacuation measures, and devoted all efforts to assisting Chinese citizens in safely relocating and evacuating. At present, some Taiwan compatriots have safely evacuated to neighboring countries.\nWe will continue to make every effort to assist Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots, in relocating and evacuating. Taiwan compatriots who need assistance may contact the Chinese embassy or consulate in the local area at any time, or call the 12308 consular protection hotline.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708354.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Since the issuance of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” what progress has been made in the construction of the demonstration zone? How will it be advanced next?","On June 15, the special promotion meeting on building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone was held in Xiamen, Fujian Province. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, attended the meeting and delivered a speech. Relevant responsible comrades from central and state organs including the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission, as well as from Fujian Province, attended the meeting.\nThe meeting summarized the work achievements since the release of the \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone\" (hereinafter the \"Opinions\"), exchanged work experience, put forward considerations for the next steps, and laid a good foundation for the high-quality construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. The meeting specified six important tasks: First, centered on the goals and tasks of building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, strengthen a sense of responsibility and mission, enhance planning and promotion, and introduce more innovative measures and integrated development achievements. Second, leverage Fujian's unique advantages regarding Taiwan and its pioneering and demonstrative role, strengthen policy and institutional innovation, and commit to promoting economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait. Third, firmly grasp the key focal points of cross-Strait integrated development and enhance the coordination of policy measures for cross-Strait integrated development. Fourth, focus on cross-Strait integrated development, strengthen innovation and breakthroughs, optimize the business environment related to Taiwan, strengthen care and assistance for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and attract more Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to develop in the Chinese mainland and participate in the process of Chinese-style modernization. Fifth, respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, promote the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the routinization of exchanges and cooperation, enhance the sense of belonging and identity of Taiwan compatriots, and promote spiritual affinity among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Sixth, open up channels for young people from Taiwan to develop in the Chinese mainland, and expand the circle of common friends and careers for young people across the Taiwan Strait.\nSince the release of the \"Opinions,\" the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission, together with relevant departments and Fujian Province, have, centered on implementing the \"Opinions,\" continuously improved the policy system and working mechanisms, issued supporting documents, and promoted the implementation of a series of policy measures in detail. They have achieved a batch of pioneering integrated development results and formed some experiences and practices of pilot testing and breaking through difficulties, and the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone has made remarkable progress. Next, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will, together with relevant departments of the central and state organs and relevant parties in Fujian Province, implement the spirit of the meeting, step up efforts to promote the work, and carry out policy implementation, assessment and adjustment, summarization and promotion, to help achieve the high-quality construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708359.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","On the 24th, the leader of the Taiwan region delivered the second of his so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity.” What comments do you have on the content of the speech concerning cross-Strait relations?","President Lai Ching-te's speech on the 24th is a confession of “Taiwan independence” that amounts to “separatism” in practice, and it is a loud effort to strengthen “Taiwan independence” identity. In the speech he repeated the old “Taiwan independence” tune, deliberately distorted history, and tried to create hatred and dissatisfaction, deepening social division on the island and fostering a social atmosphere of “anti-China, resisting China.” He is using this to build political momentum for suppressing opposition forces and promoting the “great recall.” He again hyped the “new two-state theory” that the two sides “are not subordinate to each other,” deliberately incited provocation, and raised tensions across the Taiwan Strait. He recklessly smeared cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, slandering the public’s hope for peace and stability and the mainland’s goodwill and sincerity toward compatriots as “united front infiltration threats,” and he has tried hard to manipulate “resisting China to protect Taiwan” and stir up cross-Strait confrontation. Taiwan’s public does not agree with this and is not buying it.\nAlthough the two sides have not yet been fully reunified, both sides belong to one China, and the historical and legal fact that compatriots on both sides are both Chinese has never changed and will not be changed. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, Taiwan’s future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to national rejuvenation. Only by jointly promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and working together toward the complete reunification of the country can we reach the broad road of safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and advancing the interests and well-being of compatriots, and only that is the right choice for promoting harmony and tranquility in Taiwan society and allowing Taiwan compatriots to live and work in peace and contentment. We hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will see through the hypocritical face and clumsy tricks of the Lai Ching-te authorities, and join us in opposing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and jointly create the glorious cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708361.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Reportedly, Lai Ching-te said that this year marks the 100th anniversary of the founding of the National Palace Museum, and at that time the National Palace Museum in Taipei will cooperate with U.S. museums and does not plan to cooperate with the Palace Museum on the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","The Palace Museum and the National Palace Museum in Taipei share the same roots and are bound by blood. They house treasures of the historical and cultural heritage of the Chinese nation, carry the shared memories of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and are precious assets jointly owned by compatriots on both sides. Compatriots on both sides have a responsibility to jointly pass on and promote the Chinese historical and cultural heritage.\nDriven by their nature of seeking “independence” and by political self-interest, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, vigorously promote “cultural Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization,” and on the other hand they make a great show of using the treasures of Chinese culture. How ironic, and how pitiful! We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: the profound historical and cultural ties across the Strait cannot be severed by anyone, and the imprint of Chinese culture on Taiwan’s society and compatriots cannot be erased by anyone. Those who forget their ancestry and abandon their nation will surely face the reckoning of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","On the 23rd, the US House of Representatives passed the so-called “Taiwan Non-Discrimination Act,” which requires the US government to support Taiwan’s accession to the International Monetary Fund (IMF), its participation in economic surveillance, its receipt of technical assistance, and eligibility for its personnel to serve at the IMF. What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Some members of the U.S. Congress have rehashed defunct bills related to Taiwan, which seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. We firmly oppose this. We urge the U.S. side to stop advancing relevant negative bills concerning Taiwan and to stop sending any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nIt must be pointed out that the International Monetary Fund is a specialized agency of the United Nations, and only sovereign states are qualified to participate. Taiwan, as part of China, has no right to participate.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The US claim to impose high tariffs on Taiwan continues to cause concern across all sectors of the island. Recently, nearly 70 unions on the island formed the “Taiwan Labor Action Alliance for Responding to the Tariff Shock,” pointing out that at least 500,000 workers could be affected. However, the Lai Ching-te authorities have so far held no discussions or communication with labor groups. They demand to…","Taiwan’s economic development is highly dependent on foreign trade, and it is a beneficiary of economic globalization. Any bullying behavior that undermines normal economic and trade order and fairness and justice will directly harm Taiwan’s economic interests and people’s livelihoods.\nFaced with unilateral bullying through tariff increases and the deliberate manipulation of the appreciation of the New Taiwan dollar, the DPP authorities have bowed and scraped. They not only have failed to take forceful measures to protect the vital interests of Taiwan residents, but instead have intensified their “appeasement and kowtowing to the US,” selling out Taiwan’s advantageous industries and begging with their tails wagging. This conduct of disregarding people’s livelihoods and submitting without any bottom line, which seriously harms the interests of island residents, naturally triggers dissatisfaction and protests across island society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said that besides mainland passports, ID cards and residence permits, if Taiwan residents obtain a “border tourism passport” on the mainland, even if it has expired, it is equally “illegal,” and will result in the cancellation of their Taiwan identity. What is your comment on this?","It is understood that issuing one-time-valid travel documents to Taiwan residents who take part in the China-Russia border group visa-free tourism is a convenience measure provided to Taiwan residents for border tourism in the Mainland, and is not conditional on Taiwan compatriots having household registration in the Mainland. This measure has been implemented for many years and has provided convenient services to the Taiwan compatriots concerned. The DPP authorities have engaged in political hype about it and abused administrative and judicial means to infringe on the interests of the people, intending to create a “green terror” and threaten and intimidate Taiwan compatriots. They act recklessly and go against the tide, and they will surely reap the bitter fruit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Reports say that before any professional assessment and internal consensus, the Lai Ching-te authorities are set to invest ten billion US dollars in the U.S. Alaska natural gas pipeline project, but this project has little to do with Taiwan's security and energy stability. Lai Ching-te's move has been questioned as a blatant “selling out of Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","If the relevant reports are true, the only thing that can be said is that the DPP authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, have no bottom line in “currying favor with the US and selling out Taiwan.” Such despicable conduct will naturally be questioned and opposed by the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, media on the island revealed that the “Black Bear Academy” launched a “disaster prevention kit” priced at NT$1,380, claiming the cost could be “handled for NT$300,” and that “resisting China and protecting Taiwan” has become “resisting China to make money.” What is your comment?","The “Taiwan independence” base “Black Bear Academy,” backed by the DPP authorities and external interfering forces, on the one hand openly cultivates “violent Taiwan independence elements,” loudly promotes “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, and engages in long-term “Taiwan independence” separatist activities; on the other hand, it runs a business that profits from “independence,” raking in enormous sums by selling war fear. We hope the people of Taiwan will see through its face of greed and murder, recognize the grave harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, avoid being deceived, and refuse to be coerced or exploited.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Lai Qingde has defined the mainland as an “external hostile force,” which has provoked widespread questioning in public opinion on the island. In response, the DPP said that the mainland has long used a “state of hostility” to define cross-Strait relations, and that recently it has escalated and strengthened its various “coercive actions” against Taiwan, which is the only fundamental cause of the deterioration of…","The relevant statements by the DPP authorities completely distort right and wrong and reverse black and white. For some time, Lai Ching-te has obstinately adhered to a “Taiwan independence” stance, incited “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment on the island, suppressed cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and colluded with external forces in an attempt to “seek independence by force.” He is, without any exaggeration, a “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and are members of one family. We have always respected, cared for and benefited Taiwan compatriots, improved the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and firmly stand as Taiwan compatriots' strong backing and reliance. We will not tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, and we will resolutely crack down on them. This is a just measure to defend national sovereignty, security and development interests, and a necessary measure to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will stand with us to firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and jointly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan’s economic authority said it has included 601 entities on its “export control list,” including mainland chip research and development companies such as Huawei and SMIC. Some investors on the island worry that the related “export ban” will hit Taiwan’s semiconductor companies. What is your comment on this?","On the tariff bullying that damages Taiwan, the DPP authorities kneel and plead without any bottom line. Yet toward mutually beneficial cross-Strait economic cooperation, they repeatedly undermine it in secret and frequently deploy vile tactics. They even treat cooperating with the United States in suppressing mainland enterprises as a “pledge of loyalty” to demonstrate allegiance to the US and “rely on foreign powers to seek independence.” Such despicable conduct is disgraceful. We will take forceful measures to resolutely safeguard the normal order of cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, and to protect the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: technological blockades cannot slow the pace of mainland technological innovation, and attempts to “decouple and break chains” cannot delay the mainland's industrial upgrading. Any act by the DPP authorities that undermines cross-Strait economic cooperation will only harm the competitiveness of Taiwan's own enterprises and narrow Taiwan's own room for economic development. Facts have repeatedly proven that joining hands across the Strait to jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation is the right path under heaven.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708355.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","《团结报》记者","A foundation on the island recently invited retired US and Japanese generals to conduct a “Taiwan Strait defense wargame.” A retired US general said that the two key factors in whether the US decides to intervene are the causes of a Taiwan Strait conflict and whether Taiwan has the will to defend itself. A retired Taiwanese military figure said that the most likely cause of a Taiwan Strait conflict is “Taiwan…","The Lai Ching-te authorities are accustomed to using pretexts such as “seminars” and “war games” to win over external forces to create momentum and boost courage for their provocations seeking “independence.” The more such activities they hold, the more the people of Taiwan will see the essence and intentions of the United States, which always pursues “America first” and treats Taiwan as a “pawn,” and the more they will see the sinister face of the Lai Ching-te authorities, who, for political self-interest, engage in militarism and “seek independence through force.” It must be stressed that no matter how the Lai Ching-te authorities collude with external forces and make trouble, they cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the People's Bank of China and the State Administration of Foreign Exchange launched the “Financial 12 Measures” supporting Fujian in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development, which has drawn wide attention from the island's business community. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” the People’s Bank of China and the State Administration of Foreign Exchange jointly issued the “Several Measures on Financial Support for Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.”\nThe “Several Measures” focus on building the cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone. They support Fujian in exploring a new path for deepening cross-strait integrated development in the financial sector, helping to advance cross-strait exchanges, interactions, and integration. The “Several Measures” put forward 12 policy measures in four areas: optimizing the financial ecosystem of the cross-strait shared “living circle” and serving the construction of the “first home” for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises entering the mainland; supporting high-level opening pilots for cross-border trade in Fuzhou, Xiamen, and Quanzhou; supporting facilitation of cross-border investment and financing under the capital account; and comprehensively strengthening financial regulation and effectively preventing and resolving financial risks. These measures will further facilitate life for Taiwan compatriots in Fujian and provide more financial support for Taiwan-funded enterprises operating in Fujian.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","参考消息记者","Since the “Opinions on Punishing According to Law the Crime of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession by Stubborn ‘Taiwan Independence’ Elements” were issued and implemented a year ago, they have played an important role in deterring “Taiwan independence” separatism and maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council recently said, “These measures have no binding force…","The state's punishment in accordance with the law of diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements for the crime of splitting the country and inciting to split the country is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and is also a just act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The issuance of the \"Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with the Law the Crime of Splitting the Country and Inciting to Split the Country by Diehard 'Taiwan Independence' Elements\" enriches and improves the system of relevant national laws and practices, has effectively deterred the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their separatist conduct, safeguarded peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and helps strive for a bright prospect of peaceful reunification across the Strait. It has received high attention and broad understanding and support from both sides of the Strait and the international community.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the state will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to split Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. Punishing diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements for the crime of splitting the country and inciting to split the country in accordance with the law is reasonable, justified, and lawful. The judicial documents targeting \"Taiwan independence\" are aimed at an extremely small number of diehard \"Taiwan independence\" elements who engage in vicious words and deeds related to independence and rampant activities plotting independence. The net of justice is vast, and criminal acts of splitting the country and inciting to split the country will all be severely punished by law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708358.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声电台记者","According to reports, the US House Appropriations Committee recently passed the “FY2026 National Defense Appropriations Act,” in which US$500 million will be used for the “Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative,” including providing Taiwan with newly procured defensive weapons and services, military education and training, and more. What comment do you have on this?","Some people in the US Congress insist on inserting negative content concerning Taiwan into relevant bills, attempting to concoct pretexts and a basis for “arming Taiwan.” Such moves brazenly interfere in China’s internal affairs, violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We firmly oppose them.\nWe urge the US side to earnestly abide by the serious political commitments it has made to China on the Taiwan question, stop deliberating the relevant bills, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs. We warn the DPP authorities: no matter how many weapons they obtain from the US, they cannot stop the historical trend of China’s reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708357.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, military collusion between Taiwan and the United States has been frequent. U.S. Pacific Fleet Commander Koehler claimed falsely that China is strengthening its \"aggression\" or blockade drills against Taiwan, and that the U.S. has already included Taiwan in its \"deterrence mission area.\" What comments do you have on this?","First, let me correct one point: Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called \"aggression.\" The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, to handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, to put into practice its commitment not to support \"Taiwan independence,\" not to send erroneous signals to \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist forces, and not to let the scheme of a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" secessionists to undermine the overall situation of China-US relations succeed.\nIn order to serve the narrow private interests of one party and one individual, the DPP authorities constantly come up with new tricks, packaging \"relying on the United States to seek independence\" and \"seeking independence by force,\" attempting to tie the ordinary people of Taiwan to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot, seriously harming the interests and well-being of compatriots in Taiwan. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: stop the schemes of \"relying on foreign powers to seek independence,\" abandon the illusion of \"seeking independence by force,\" and if you dare to take risks, you will surely bring about your own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Taiwanese internet celebrity “Guanzhang” Chen Chih-han recently traveled to the mainland for tourism and, in livestreams, repeatedly called on Taiwanese people to come to the mainland in person and expose the lies of the DPP authorities, which drew attacks from Green camp politicians and internet troops. Some commentary on the island has noted that after “Guanzhang” broadcast from the mainland, many young people…","For a long time, the DPP authorities and Green camp politicians have persistently manipulated the “oppose China and resist China” narrative, attempting to block channels through which compatriots on the island can learn about the real situation on the mainland and misleading Taiwan's society and public about the mainland. As more and more compatriots in Taiwan go to the mainland to take a look and share what they have seen and heard, the lies fabricated by the DPP authorities are being exposed one by one, and the “information cocoon” they have created is collapsing.\nWe note that more and more compatriots in Taiwan, especially young friends, are taking the initiative to break through the information walls carefully built by the DPP authorities, learning about the mainland in various ways and discovering the “different mainland.” We welcome and look forward to Taiwan compatriots listing various places on the mainland as tourist check-in spots and putting quality mainland goods into their shopping carts. The deeper the exchanges, the more people will feel that the mainland's scenery is beautiful, its goods are good, and its people are even better, and the more they come, the closer their hearts will be.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250625_12708356.htm"],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Regarding the G7 summit’s hyping of the so-called “importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait,” Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s external affairs authority, said that “maintaining peace and stability in Taiwan has become an international consensus.” How does the spokesperson respond to this?","Some countries have been making irresponsible remarks on the Taiwan question and crudely interfering in China’s internal affairs, and we firmly oppose this. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and tolerates no interference from any external force. The greatest current threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the Lai Ching-te authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, who stubbornly cling to a “Taiwan independence” position and, under various pretexts, collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking independence. Relevant countries should recognize the danger and harm of “Taiwan independence” provocations, adhere to the one-China principle through concrete actions, properly handle the Taiwan question, and avoid sending erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: any provocation aimed at seeking independence will be met with firm countermeasures, and any scheme to collude with external forces to seek independence is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报封面新闻记者","Recently, Taiwan’s famous poet Cheng Chou-yu and musician Peter Chen have passed away one after another, prompting many people on both sides of the Strait to express their mourning. What comments do you have?","Mr. Cheng Chou-yu and Mr. Chen Peter are both well-known Taiwanese cultural figures who harbor deep affection for the Chinese mainland and have played a positive role in promoting the development of poetry and music exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. We express deep condolences on the passing of the two gentlemen and extend sincere sympathy to their families.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻记者","Taiwan will hold the first batch of voting in the \"grand recall\" on July 26, in which 24 Kuomintang elected representatives face challenges to their continued tenure, and the DPP has characterized this vote as \"opposing communism and protecting Taiwan.\" What comments do you have on this?","Since taking office, the Lai Ching-te authorities have obstinately adhered to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. In pursuit of “one-party dominance,” they have advanced “Taiwan independence” separatism, disregarding the widespread calls from people on the island for improved livelihoods and the mainstream public opinion on the island calling for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. Under the name of “democracy,” they practice “dictatorship” in substance and engage in severe political infighting, using political intimidation, manipulation of the judiciary, incitement of public opinion and other means to suppress the “opposition” parties, as well as groups and individuals who support the development of cross-Strait relations, by every means possible. They have further intensified “green terror” and created a “chilling effect,” provoking strong dissatisfaction and deep fear among Taiwan residents about “green dictatorship and terror politics.” We hope compatriots in Taiwan will fully recognize and firmly oppose the DPP authorities' political manipulation, and never allow their scheme to succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: Taiwanese internet celebrity “Curator” recently, while live-streaming a tour in Shanghai, was asked by local residents what country he was from. He did not respond on the spot, but on returning to the tour bus he stated that he was a “person of the Republic of China.” How does the TAO view Taiwan people's identification with themselves? Some people online have reported that “Curator” is a “Taiwan…","The first question: compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same blood, the same culture, and the same history. Both belong to the Chinese nation, and they are all Chinese. This is an objective fact that no one can change.\nBecause the “Taiwan independence” forces on the island have long promoted “de-Sinicization” in the fields of culture and education, some Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, have been misled. As more and more Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland, they have used what they have seen and heard firsthand to break through the “information cocoon” created by the DPP authorities and expose the rumors slandering the mainland spread by the DPP authorities. During Mr. Chen’s six-day trip to the mainland, the “Museum Director” expressed admiration for the achievements of the mainland’s modernization more than once, confronted his previous biased perceptions of the mainland more than once, and after returning to Taiwan he called on Taiwan residents to travel to the mainland and experience it for themselves. As the saying goes, “seeing once is better than hearing a hundred times.” We warmly welcome everyone to come to the mainland, which will certainly enhance objective understanding of the mainland and correct understanding of cross-Strait relations.\nThe second question: Hong Qichang, chairman of the Taiwan Industry, Economy and Construction Research Association, led members of the island’s biotech industry to Beijing for a visit and exchange from June 10 to 12. The delegation visited the high-level autonomous driving demonstration zone of the Beijing Economic-Technological Development Area, the Yizhuang Cell Therapy R&D and Pilot Base, and the Cross-Strait Science and Technology Innovation Center, and held a discussion and exchange with the biotech group of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit. We welcome people from all fields and sectors on the island to visit the mainland, strengthen industrial exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and better benefit Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-06-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Recently, the DPP authorities rejected the application for mainland personnel to enter the island to hold the 2025 Straits Forum Taipei Summer Travel Expo, provoking widespread dissatisfaction and opposition from the island’s industry. In response, Luo Wenjia, Vice Chairman and Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said that exchange and “united front” are only one line apart, and that the…","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have obstructed exchange and cooperation activities that have long been carried out in the cross-Strait tourism industry, and have slapped the so-called labels of “united front work and infiltration” on normal cross-Strait exchanges. This not only exposes their stubborn intent to pursue “Taiwan independence” and provoke, and their deliberate, sinister intention to interfere with and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, but also reveals their guilty conscience and cowardice in fearing that compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer to each other would bankrupt their scheme for “Taiwan independence.” The tide of cross-Strait exchanges is surging forward and will not stop or break off. We will continue to actively promote the normalization and regularization of cross-Strait exchanges in all fields, and continue to improve the systems and policies that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, so that compatriots on both sides of the Strait continuously deepen mutual understanding and friendship.\nOn June 12, the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account released the first installment of the “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” activity, with 20 questions covering the historical origins of the Taiwan question and recent major cross-Strait exchange activities. Netizens at home and abroad enthusiastically took part in the quiz. The quiz activity closed on the 25th. The top ten netizens with correct answers and the most likes on their comments will each receive an exquisite souvenir. These ten netizens, in order, are: netizen “Haohao” from Hebei, netizen “Xue” from Japan, netizen “Zhang Wei” from Jiangsu, netizen “Jiajia” from Beijing, netizen “COSMIC” from Sichuan, netizen “Jan” from Guangdong, netizen “啟政” from Taiwan, netizen “可塔羅” from Taiwan, netizen “Shen Bin” from Tianjin, and netizen “Zhao Jiongjiong” from Hong Kong.\nNetizens posted comments expressing their hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will join hands and work together to advance national reunification. Some netizens wrote hoping that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait sit together around one table, chat about everyday life, and share the joy of family reunion. The Chinese nation will surely join hands to create prosperity together and share in the glory of rejuvenation!” Some netizens shared their experiences of traveling to Taiwan and wished that “cross-Strait relations keep getting better, cross-Strait exchanges keep increasing, and cross-Strait compatriots keep growing closer;” and another netizen recounted how, in 2017, he took his father from Taiwan back to Dangshan, Anhui to worship their ancestors: “This was the first time I returned to my hometown. I met relatives on the mainland and added them on WeChat. It really felt very good. I hope that in my lifetime I can see cross-Strait reunification.”\nWe extend congratulations to these ten netizens. Please send a private message to the editor of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account, providing the relevant mailing address and contact information so that the souvenirs can be sent promptly. On July 7, the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account will publish the questions for the second installment of the “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” activity. We look forward to even more netizens paying attention and participating!\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202506/t20250625_12708344.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to media reports, sea trial of PLANS Fujian is steadily advancing and the PLA Navy will soon have three operational aircraft carriers. Does that mean China's third aircraft carrier will be commissioned soon? What role will the three carrier task groups play in safeguarding China's overseas interests and maintaining regional stability? Second, it is reported that the US side…","On your first question, building a strong and modernized navy is a century-old dream of the Chinese nation. China builds aircraft carriers in line with our national security needs and the development of equipment and technology. Starting from scratch, the PLA Navy has made leapfrog progress in aircraft carrier development. After successive commissioning of PLANS Liaoning and PLANS Shandong capable of ski jump launch, we now have the first carrier with electromagnetic catapult launch, PLANS Fujian. It should be emphasized that China develops weapons and equipment only to safeguard our national sovereignty, security and development interests. The Chinese military remains a staunch force for world peace. The more capable we are, the stronger the force in defending peace and preventing war.\nOn your second question, we firmly oppose any form of military collusion between the US and China's Taiwan region. Such collusion, be it military aid, arms sale or under any other excuse, reveals the extremely malicious intention of the US to mislead Taiwan into the flames of war, harming Taiwan itself and destroying its interests. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. We warn the DPP authorities that \"soliciting US support for independence\" is doomed to fail, and \"resisting reunification by force\" is a dead end.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, it is reported that the poll initiated by the Democratic Culture and Education Foundation in Taiwan showed that 66% of the respondents believed that the US may sell out Taiwan for its own interests; 67% believed that the US mainly uses Taiwan as a bargaining chip in its rivalry with the Chinese mainland. What's your take on that? Second, the leader of the Taiwan region Lai Ching-te…","On your first question, the US always puts its own interests first and this won't be different when it comes to the Taiwan question. Acting as a pawn, the DPP authorities cannot escape the fate of being abandoned. Many more compatriots in Taiwan have now realized that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, foreign support is unreliable, and China's reunification is inevitable. Those who act against the trend of reunification and attempt to separate the country will never have a good end.\nOn your second question, Taiwan is a part of China. It has never been and will never be a country. Lai Ching-te has distorted historical facts and made up false theories with an ill attempt to provoke for independence and escalate tensions across the Strait. His delirious talks will never change the legal fact that Taiwan is a part of China and the international community's commitment to the one-China principle, and will never stop the historical trend that China will and must be reunified. The PLA shows zero tolerance towards \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. We will strengthen military training and combat readiness and resolutely safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The DPP authorities claimed that 46 PLA fighter jets crossed the Taiwan Strait and six PLA vessels circled around Taiwan within 24 hours, which is the largest PLA operation around the island recently. What's your comment on this?","PLA military drills around the Taiwan Island are necessary actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, as well as stern warnings against the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and the interference of external forces. They are fully justified, legitimate, and reasonable. The Lai Ching-te authorities have taken continued actions to seek independence, which could push Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war. They are the culprits who undermine security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and will surely be disdained by the people and judged by the time.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A former commander of the US Pacific Command has reportedly said that 2027 is a critical year for the PLA not only to attack Taiwan but also to become a world-class military. The Chinese side now sails its aircraft carriers and other large vessels beyond the Second Island Chain to put pressure on Taiwan, Japan and the US. He called it \"gunboat diplomacy\". Do you have any comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people, which brooks no foreign interference. The operation and training activities conducted by Chinese aircraft carrier task groups conform to international law and practices, and do not target at any third party. In addition, China has never done such things as \"gunboat diplomacy\". We urge the US side not to perceive China with its own hegemonic mindset, and stop misinterpreting China's legitimate actions with false ideas.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US Secretary of Defense recently claimed at a congressional hearing that China is a \"pacing threat\", and that the US will prioritize re-establishing deterrence in the Indo-Pacific region to \"achieve peace through strength\". The One Big Beautiful Bill of the US would allocate 12 billion US dollars for the \"Pacific Deterrence Initiative\", further strengthening combat readiness of US forces…","Zero-sum game should not be the way that major countries handle each other, and peaceful coexistence should be a bottom line both China and the US hold. China's development poses no threat to other countries and we never resort to deterrence or coercion preferred by some certain country.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair which brooks no foreign interference. The US side has repeatedly gone back on its own words and kept arming Taiwan, which would only backfire. We urge the US side to have an objective and rational perception of China, stop blaming China on everything, and stop deceiving and misleading the US public and the international community, so as to create favorable conditions for developing state-to-state and mil-to-mil relations between China and the US.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, it is reported that this year's enrollment in military academies in Taiwan has been hotly discussed, with the number of female cadets in many academies surpassing that of male cadets. \"When male soldiers are not enough, female soldiers have to fill the gap\". Such a situation does not reflect gender equality, but rather a fact that no one want to throw their lives away for \"Taiwan…","There is a good point in your first question, no one want to throw their lives away for \"Taiwan independence\". It is unworthy and meaningless to be cannon fodders for the armed forces of \"Taiwan independence\".\nOn your second question, Lai Ching-te and his kind are trying to find all kinds of ways to pay \"protection fees\" to their US masters, which squandered hard-earned money of the people in Taiwan. This is exactly \"selling off the farmland of one's family without being conscience-stricken\". We warn the DPP authorities that their attempts to solicit US support for \"Taiwan independence\" and resist reunification by force will only fail.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, during its summit in the Hague from June 24 to 25, NATO accused China of providing Russia with key support in the Russia-Ukraine conflict, and expressed concerns over the South China Sea, the East China Sea and the Taiwan question. NATO Secretary General recently said that China is significantly strengthening its military capabilities, building the world's largest navy, and expanding its…","China adheres to the path of peaceful development, and is committed to a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. China's military development is purely aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests. China-Russia cooperation does not target at any third party, nor will it be interfered by any third party.\nAs a product of the Cold War and the largest military bloc in the world, NATO stirs up troubles and provokes conflicts and wars in various regions, making itself a true war machine. In recent years, NATO has overstretched its geographic boundary stipulated by its own Treaty, and ill-expanded its power and authority, arousing high vigilance among regional countries. We firmly oppose NATO using China as an excuse to \"expand eastward into the Asia-Pacific\" and urge NATO to reflect on its own behaviors, change course, and contribute more to global security and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-06-26","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, Taiwan's first indigenous submarine Hai Kun recently completed its maiden sea trial. Do you have any comment on that?","The \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces tried very hard to build the submarine Hai Kun only to find a form of psychological comfort. It can be easily defeated by the PLA.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/06/china-250626-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16394114.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-06-27","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Czech media report that when Taiwan’s Hsiao Bi-khim was in Prague earlier last year, the Chinese embassy closely followed her car. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on this report?","By allowing diehard “Taiwan independence” separatist Hsiao Bi-khim to visit, the Czech Republic has seriously violated the one-China principle and its political commitment to China, and grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs. China has expressed its strong concern and firm opposition.\nLet me stress that Chinese diplomats always observe the laws and regulations of host countries. China urges the relevant party to avoid being incited or used by “Taiwan independence” forces, and refrain from creating troubles, spreading rumors, and disrupting and undermining the bilateral relations. No matter how the DPP authorities seek independence by soliciting foreign support in whatever form, they cannot cover up their ill intentions and will certainly fail in their attempts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250627_11660620.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250627_11660512.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-06-30","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwan’s “vice president” Hsiao Bi-khim said that she would not be intimidated by Beijing after the government accused Chinese Embassy staff of planning to “ram” her car during an official visit to the Czech Republic in March last year. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","First of all, Taiwan is part of China and there is no such thing as “vice president” of the Taiwan region. Chinese diplomats always observe the laws and regulations of host countries. No matter how the DPP authorities seek independence by soliciting foreign support and sow discord between China and countries with diplomatic ties with us, they cannot cover up their ill intentions, still less succeed in their attempts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202506/t20250630_11661711.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202506/t20250630_11661730.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-06-30","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On June 30, Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters’ questions.\nQuestion: On the 28th, the leader of the Taiwan region delivered a speech at the DPP National Congress, and on the 29th delivered the third lecture of the so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity.” What comments do you have on the content concerning cross-Strait relations in these two speeches?\nAnswer:\nLai Ching-te’s speech ignored the strong opposition from all sectors of the island, once again tore apart Taiwan’s public opinion, once again provoked “Taiwan independence” schemes, and further undermined cross-Strait relations.\nIn his speech, Lai Ching-te hyped the so-called “mainland threat,” rehashed the old tune of “Taiwan independence,” escalated cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, and once again spouted a string of fallacious arguments that violate legal principles and historical facts and disregard mainstream public opinion on the island. He distorted UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and challenged the authority of international law; he switched concepts and confused right and wrong, continued to peddle the fallacy that the two sides of the Strait are “not subordinate to each other,” severed the legal and historical ties between the two sides, and hurt the national sentiments of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. He has completely forgotten his ancestors and abandoned the nation. He persistently manipulated “anti-China and resist-China” and slandered and smeared the mainland’s sincere intention to bring well-being to compatriots in Taiwan, once again exposing his panic and resistance toward compatriots on both sides of the Strait growing closer, becoming like family, and integrating with one another.\nTaiwan is part of China’s territory. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. The historical thread is clear, and the legal and factual basis is clear; no person or force can deny it, and denial will not be tolerated. The restoration of Taiwan is an important part of the post-World War II international order, and it is also a victory achieved by compatriots on both sides of the Strait in jointly defending national dignity and safeguarding our common homeland. History must be remembered, and its achievements must not be trampled. Anyone who acts against the overall interests of the Chinese nation and pursues retrogressive actions is destined to fail; those who challenge national territorial sovereignty and pursue “Taiwan independence” separatism have only one dead end.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait all hope for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. We firmly comply with the aspirations of compatriots on both sides for a better life, and are committed to deepening peaceful development and integrated development across the Strait, respecting, caring for, and benefiting compatriots in Taiwan, so that compatriots in Taiwan gain more sense of achievement, happiness, and belonging. We hope that the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature of the Lai Ching-te authorities, see through their hypocritical face, and expose their crude tricks, and join us in firmly being companions on the path of national rejuvenation and defenders of peace across the Strait, working together for the great cause of national reunification and creating the great undertaking of national rejuvenation!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202506/t20250630_12709315.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-07-01","Mao Ning","AFP","The U.S. Justice Department said yesterday that it has taken down a network that allegedly helped North Koreans obtain remote IT work with companies to raise funds for the country’s weapons program. Six Chinese nationals and two Taiwan citizens have been indicted for their involvement. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","China opposes unilateral sanctions that have no basis in international law or authorization of the UN Security Council. We will do what is necessary to defend the legitimate and lawful rights and interests of Chinese nationals.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250701_11662827.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250701_11662767.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-07-02","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 2 (Reporter) – Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to reporters' questions on the 2nd regarding the content related to cross-Strait relations in the fourth lecture of the so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity” delivered by the leader of the Taiwan region on the 1st. He said that Lai Ching-te's speech once again exposed his sinister intention to “seek independence by relying on foreign forces” and “seek independence by force.” It runs counter to the mainstream public will on the island that yearns for peaceful development, disregards the safety of life and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, deliberately provokes cross-Strait confrontation and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Pushing ahead on the wrong path of “selling out Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan,” he is, without a doubt, a “peace destroyer,” a “war peddler” through and through, and a true “trouble maker.”\nHe said that Lai Ching-te advocates so-called “fighting for Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu,” but in fact he is fighting for the narrow private interests of the Democratic Progressive Party and for its “Taiwan independence” obsession. He is willing to tie innocent people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and have young people go to the battlefield, making them victims of his separatist schemes. He plays up the so-called “military threat from the mainland” to cover up the separatist nature of his constant provocation and “seeking independence by force.” He claims to be “standing together with democratic countries,” but in fact he is paying more “protection money” and submitting a “loyalty pledge” in exchange for the backing and encouragement of certain external forces.\nHe emphasized that “Taiwan independence” is the greatest disaster for Taiwan. As long as “Taiwan independence” is not eliminated, the Taiwan Strait will not know peace for a single day. The deeper Lai Ching-te's “seeking independence,” the more severe the “destruction of Taiwan” will be. Only by resolutely opposing and forcefully containing “Taiwan independence” separatism can peace in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded and the people of Taiwan able to live and work in peace.\nHe pointed out that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu are all sacred territory of China. Compatriots on both sides are all Chinese. As long as “Taiwan independence” separatism is not pursued, the two sides can share peace and seek common development together. At the same time, we will not tolerate or indulge in any “Taiwan independence” separatist acts in any way. We have the firm will, strong determination, and great ability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and their own well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250702_12710138.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-07-03","Mao Ning","Global Times","According to reports, the U.S. House of Representatives recently unanimously adopted the so-called “Taiwan Non-Discrimination Act,” requiring the U.S. government to support China’s Taiwan region in joining the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to gain eligibility for participating in economic surveillance, receiving technical assistance, and employment opportunities within the IMF. What is your comment on it?","There is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. Taiwan does not have any ground, reason, or right to join the UN, or any other international organization whose membership is confined to sovereign states. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, observe the international law and basic norms of international relations, stop advancing that act, stop using the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs, and stop sending wrong signals to the separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250703_11664465.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250703_11664482.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-07-06","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华6日答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 6 (Electronic dispatch): Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a reporter's question on the 6th, saying that the Civil Aviation Administration of China announced on July 6 that connecting route W121 for air route M503 has been put into use. This measure is intended to ease the pressure of flight growth in relevant areas, ensure…","Chen Binhua pointed out that route M503 is located within the Shanghai Flight Information Region, and establishing and activating this route is a routine part of mainland civil aviation airspace management. Since the activation of M503 and the connecting routes W122 and W123, overall operations have been safe and stable, effectively improving cross-Strait flight operations and further facilitating personnel exchanges across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250706_12710653.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-07","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On July 7, Typhoon “Danas” made landfall in Taiwan, causing casualties and property losses. Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said that relevant parties on the mainland are highly concerned about this, express condolences for the Taiwan compatriots who died, extend sympathy to the families of the deceased and to the injured, and hope that the affected people will soon restore normal production and living order.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250707_12710918.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-07-08","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Taiwan's military will conduct the Han Kuang-41 live-troop exercise starting from July 9. The exercise will focus on such subjects as the so-called \"response to gray-zone harassment\", \"joint anti-landing operations\" and \"resilient defense on the Island\". Meanwhile, many US weapons will make their debut during the exercise. What's your comment?","The Han Kuang exercise is nothing but a bluffing and self-deceiving trick played by the DPP authorities to hijack Taiwan compatriots on-board its \"Taiwan Independence\" war chariot. The DPP authorities are harming Taiwan out of its selfish interests. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that \"seeking independence by force\" is a dead end. Whatever subjects they drill and whatever weapons they use, the PLA's resolute countermeasures against \"Taiwan Independence\" would not be deterred, nor would the overwhelming and irresistible trend of China's national reunification be stopped.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250708-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16395884.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-08","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Lai Ching-te delivered the fourth lecture of his so-called \"10 lectures on Unity,\" in which he once again played up the so-called \"mainland military threat,\" called for increased \"defense\" spending, and urged Taiwan's military to \"fight for Taiwan, Penghu, Jinmen, and Mazu.\" Please comment on that.","Taiwan is a province of China. Therefore, how is it possible for it to have a budget for so-called national defense? Lai Ching-te has distorted history and facts and made up lies to cloak his separatist plot for \"Taiwan independence.\" He has hyped up the so-called mainland threat to stoke security anxiety and manipulate public opinions in Taiwan. By doing that, he is attempting to militarize Taiwan's society and leave the island's future to the mercy of external forces. Lai Ching-te's call to \"fight for Taiwan, Penghu, Jinmen and Mazu\" is in fact a call to fight for the the DPP authorities' interests and \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. It will only lead Taiwan people to the dead-end of \"resisting reunification with force\" and \"selling out and ruining Taiwan.\"\nThe two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. Taiwan, Penghu, Jinmen and Mazu are all inalienable parts of China's sacred territory. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese. The louder Lai and his like clamor for separatism, the faster they will court their demise. Any \"Taiwan independence\" armed forces that support them will be buried together. The PLA has full capability and confidence to thwart all separatist activities for \"Taiwan independence\" and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250708-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16395884.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-07-09","Mao Ning","AFP","Today, Taiwan kicked off its annual military drills, which will, for the first time, feature newly delivered U.S. high-tech rocket systems. Taiwan said the drills are aimed at sending a message that it is capable of and confident in safeguarding its “sovereignty” and “liberal and democratic lifestyle.” What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","Our firm opposition to the military ties between the U.S. and Taiwan is consistent. The DPP authorities’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup and soliciting foreign support will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250709_11668073.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250709_11668031.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-07-09","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on July 9 that the 8th Straits Youth Development Forum will be held from July 10 to 15 in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, as well as in Jiaxing, Ningbo, Wenzhou, Jinhua and other places in Zhejiang. The opening ceremony of the forum and the launch ceremony of the “Zhejiang-Taiwan Youth Exchange Season” will be held in Hangzhou on the morning of July 11. Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang and chairperson of the China Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, has been invited to attend the forum. Guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait and youth representatives from various sectors, about 1,000 people in total, will take part in the forum's related activities. Media reporters are welcome to go and cover it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250709_12711173.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-09","Chen Binhua","国务院台办发言人陈斌华答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, July 9 — On July 9, the Ministry of Commerce announced that it would place eight Taiwan-region entities on the export control list for dual-use items. In response, Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, answered reporters' questions, saying: Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly held to the “Taiwan independence” position and…","Chen Binhua pointed out that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and abetting “independence” is an evil path. Enterprises, groups, and individuals who willingly serve as henchmen for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and who take part in or incite the crime of splitting the country, will surely be severely punished according to law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250709_12711187.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-09","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The Taiwan military began the “Han Kuang 41” exercise on July 9. This exercise has doubled in duration, and the number of participants is the highest in history. For the first time, the so-called “mainland's 2027 attack on Taiwan” has been used as the scenario, and it has been combined with the “Urban Defense Resilience Exercise.” New training content has also been added, including “gray zone…","Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua responded to the question, saying: The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence.” To incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, they repeatedly waste the people’s hard-earned money, vigorously pursue a “whole people are soldiers” policy, go to great lengths to bind Taiwan’s residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and constantly escalate cross-Strait tensions. They attempt to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence through war preparation.” They will only further undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and bury the security and well-being of Taiwan’s people.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and unification cannot be stopped. No matter how the DPP authorities put on airs and militarize, they are a hollow show that cannot withstand a single blow. No matter how many “drills” the DPP authorities conduct, they cannot change the fate that “Taiwan independence” will inevitably fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend of the motherland’s inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250709_12711384.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-07-14","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The head of Taiwan's military agency has reportedly announced the establishment of Taiwan's first HIMARS company, and that it will greatly improve the Taiwan military's precision strike and overall defense capabilities. In addition, Taiwan's military agency has approved the acquisition of 168 units of US M109A7 self-propelled howitzers. Do you have any comment?","In order to solicit US support for \"Taiwan independence\", the DPP authorities are selling Taiwan's interests to flatter the US and squandering the hard-earned money of the Taiwan people to pay protection fees. Buying US weapons to embolden themselves is useless and self-deceiving. Resisting reunification by force is a dead end. War provocations made by the \"Taiwan independence\" armed forces are futile, and will only lead to self-destruction.\nOn the afternoon of July 14, 2025, Senior Colonel Jiang Bin, Deputy Director-General of the Information Office of China's Ministry of National Defense (MND) and Spokesperson for the MND, answers recent media queries concerning the military. (Photo by Sun Yue)","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250714-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16396793.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-14","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the DPP authorities stated that the activation of the W121 extension of the M503 route by the Civil Aviation Administration of China intends to reduce the depth of Taiwan's air defense and shorten its early warning time, which would ultimately eliminate the \"median line of the Taiwan Strait\", thereby posing military threats to Taiwan. Some media reports said that the activation came just…","Taiwan is a part of China and there is no so-called \"median line of the Taiwan Strait\". The establishment and activation of relevant route is a routine work carried out by the competent authorities based on the needs of civil aviation development and management. It is beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities used it as an excuse to hype up the so-called \"military threats from the mainland\" for their selfish gains, attempting to create security anxiety, intensify antagonism and confrontation, and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges. Their scheme would never be welcomed nor succeed.\nThe root cause for the current tension across the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' collusion with external forces in their continuous provocations for \"Taiwan independence\". We hope that all Taiwan compatriots can see through the true nature of the DPP authorities in seeking independence, realize the serious harm of \"Taiwan independence\", firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, and jointly safeguard cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250714-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16396793.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-07-15","Lin Jian","Reuters","Paraguay’s president has said that the country is preparing to receive Lai Ching-te next month. Lai is also expected to visit Belize. He could very well make stopovers in the United States during his transit. Has China already warned the U.S. not to allow Lai to transit and if so, what was the U.S.’s response to that?","On the so-called “diplomatic ties” between Paraguay and China’s Taiwan region, China has made its position clear more than once. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and an international consensus. Upholding the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends.\nPeople from various sectors of Latin American countries, including from Paraguay, have visited China in recent years. There is a widely shared view among them that Paraguay needs to stop turning its back on China, stop being an outlier of the international community, and recognize the one-China principle and make a change in its relations with China sooner rather than later. We urge the current administration of Paraguay to stop going against the trend of the times, and reject being manipulated and used by “Taiwan independence” forces. It needs to listen to the aspiration of the people of Paraguay, and make the right choice that truly serves the fundamental and long-term interests of its people at an early date. We also hope that relevant Latin American and Caribbean countries will see the prevailing trend, act prudently on Taiwan-related issues, and join the big family of China-LAC friendship and cooperation at an early date.\nRegarding the possible stopover in the U.S. you mentioned, China firmly opposes any form of official interactions between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region. We oppose any visit to the U.S. by leaders of the Taiwan authorities for whatever reason or under whatever pretext. The U.S. should not in any way aid or abet “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities. The U.S. needs to fully understand the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250715_11671030.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250715_11671019.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-07-15","Lin Jian","AFP","Japan said yesterday that China’s military activity in the region could seriously impact Japan’s national security. Does China have a response to this comment?","I think you are referring to the Defense of Japan 2025 that was just released. The white paper reflects a wrong perception of China, interferes in China’s internal affairs and peddles the false “China threat.” China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this, and has protested with Japan.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and how to settle it is a matter for the Chinese ourselves. China is committed to peaceful development. China’s national defense policy is defensive in nature, and our defense development and military activities are legitimate and justified. China’s military cooperation with other countries is fully consistent with international law and international practice.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. We urge Japan to deeply reflect on its historical crime, draw lessons from history, and stop finding pretexts for its military buildup by talking up “tensions” in the neighborhood and issues related to China. It needs to avoid further losing the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250715_11671030.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250715_11671019.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-07-16","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japan recently officially released the 2025 edition of its “Defense White Paper,” continuing to call China “the greatest strategic challenge unprecedented,” falsely claiming that China is “unilaterally changing the status quo by force,” and making remarks on the Taiwan question. May the spokesperson comment?","In order to find excuses to loosen its own military restrictions, the Japanese side has fabricated a false narrative, extensively played up the “China threat,” and brutally interfered in China's internal affairs. The Chinese side is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposes this, and has lodged stern representations with the Japanese side.\nJapanese militarism once brought profound disasters to China and its Asian neighbors. Instead of seriously reflecting, the Japanese side has once again shown a dangerous posture of strengthening the military and expanding armaments: it has sharply increased its defense budget, continuously relaxed restrictions on arms exports, cobbled together military “cliques” to engage in bloc confrontation, and even from time to time there have been murmurs about revising the “three non-nuclear principles.” These actions seriously violate Japan's “Peace Constitution” and its “exclusively defense-oriented” principle, seriously undermine the postwar international order, pose a major challenge to peace and stability in the Asia-Pacific region, and have aroused high vigilance and deep concern among Asian neighbors and the international community.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japan and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. The return of Taiwan to China in 1945 was an important component of the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order. We urge the Japanese side to profoundly draw lessons from history, stop smearing and accusing China, genuinely abide by the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents and the commitments it made on the Taiwan question, and take concrete actions to promote the healthy and stable development of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_31192890","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear journalist friends, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I have no content to release proactively. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te's so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity” have sparked strong controversy, opposition, and criticism on the island, and the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office has refuted each lecture. Has Lai Ching-te's speech crossed the red line? How will the mainland counter it?","Lai Ching-te's so-called \"Ten Lectures on Unity\" is filled with lies and deception, hostility and provocation; it deliberately distorts and fragments history, cobbles together and vigorously peddles \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist fallacies, and incites confrontation and antagonism across the Strait. It can be described as a hodgepodge of \"Taiwan independence\" heresies riddled with errors, and a \"Taiwan independence\" social mobilization that bewitches people on the island. It fully demonstrates that his \"Taiwan independence\" nature is incorrigible, and fully proves that he is an out-and-out \"disruptor of peace,\" a thoroughgoing \"peddler of war,\" and a veritable \"troublemaker.\"\nThe root cause of the current tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities and Lai Ching-te obstinately hold to the \"Taiwan independence\" position and continually engage in provocations to seek independence, going down the wrong path of \"Taiwan independence\" secession to the very end. Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of Chinese territory, and we will absolutely not allow \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist forces to split Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. Any secessionist force or act that splits the motherland will surely be met with a head-on blow from the entire Chinese people!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712560.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广“海峡飞虹”记者","A spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that the announcement of the activation of the W121 connecting route of M503 is intended to ease the pressure of flight growth in the relevant areas and is beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities claimed that this move violates relevant International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) regulations,…","Route M503 is within the Shanghai Flight Information Region. The activation of the M503 route W121 connecting route is a routine task of mainland civil aviation airspace management, conforms to the norms of the International Civil Aviation Organization, and does not require consultation with the Taiwan side.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities are taking the opportunity to engage in political manipulation and to slander and smear the mainland. Their intention is to confuse the public, deceive the people on the island, and incite hostility and confrontation across the Strait. This is unpopular and is doomed to be fruitless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712558.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The TAO recently announced penalties against affiliated companies of Shen Boyang, a stubborn “Taiwan independence” diehard, and several media outlets have successively exposed Shen Boyang's two-faced conduct. Taiwan's security authorities said this is the mainland's first “cross-border repression,” directly attacking a specific Taiwan people's representative, and that it is “stepping on the red line of Taiwan's…","Certain \"Taiwan independence\" diehards, on the one hand, are arrogant and reckless in their provocative remarks seeking \"independence,\" and under the banner of \"resisting China and protecting Taiwan,\" attack and smear cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation; on the other hand, they are hypocritical, double-standard, and profit-driven: they profit personally from \"Taiwan independence,\" and their family members profit from cross-Strait trade. Such rotten apples and shameless individuals have been punished in accordance with the law and exposed and condemned by public opinion; they have brought it upon themselves.\nTaiwan is part of China, and the state will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to split Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. It is reasonable, justified and lawful to punish \"Taiwan independence\" diehards in accordance with the law for the crimes of secession and inciting secession. The DPP authorities deliberately fabricate charges on the island and suppress dissidents, carrying out a \"green terror.\" \"Taiwan independence\" diehards behave viciously in their pro-independence words and deeds, and their activities seeking \"independence\" are rampant. They are in cahoots with each other, \"fake democracy, real dictatorship,\" and their conduct completely violates the spirit of democracy and seriously infringes basic human rights. What face do they have to talk about democracy?!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712555.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","We have noted that the General Administration of Customs recently revoked the customs registration of a company named Sicuens International CO. LTD. It is reportedly a company that was re-registered under a new name from Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., owned by Shen Tu-cheng, the father of “Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang. Is this true?","Indeed, as you said, the relevant information of this company registered as “Taiwan, China” is consistent with that of Taiwan Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., and the mainland customs has revoked its registration. Taking lawful disciplinary measures against affiliated enterprises of “Taiwan independence” diehards is a powerful deterrent to, and a resolute crackdown on, the provocations of “Taiwan independence” forces seeking independence. We will never allow anyone to make money on the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nIf “Taiwan independence” elements misjudge the situation and persist in their own way, they will only pay an even more painful price.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","SEF spokesperson Li Baowen recently said in an interview that the amount of Taiwanese investment in the mainland as a share of Taiwan's total outbound investment continues to decline and may be even lower this year. Due to US-China strategic competition, mainland export conditions will not be good in the future. Seventy percent of Taiwanese businesses on the mainland saw their profits decline last year, and…","Facing a turbulent external environment, the mainland's economy has operated steadily overall, some indicators have continued to improve, new growth drivers have grown stronger, and the momentum of high-quality development has continued. The General Administration of Customs recently announced that in the first half of this year, the mainland's goods trade imports and exports totaled 21.79 trillion yuan, up 2.9% year on year, setting a record high for the same period in history. Among them, exports were 13 trillion yuan, up 7.2%. According to data released by Taiwan's financial regulatory authorities, in the first quarter of this year, the profits of listed and OTC-listed companies in Taiwan from their investments on the mainland reached NT$115.6 billion, a record high for the same period in history.\nThis fully demonstrates that cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development are continuing to benefit enterprises and people on both sides, and that the mainland is a stable, safe, and promising investment destination for Taiwan businesses and enterprises. The DPP authorities, for the sake of partisan self-interest, have repeatedly talked down the mainland's economy, obstructed cross-Strait economic cooperation, and pushed so-called “decoupling and severing of chains.” Their reckless and wanton actions are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712554.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台华语环球节目中心《中国新闻》记者","Recently, the mainland added eight Taiwan entities to its export control list for dual-use items. The Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland has once again weaponized economic and trade measures, which deviates from mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and is entirely unhelpful to peaceful and stable cross-Strait relations. What is your comment?","Who is recklessly provoking “independence” and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait? Who is going against the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and obstructing and restricting cross-strait exchanges and cooperation? And who is “blindly following the United States,” “selling out Taiwan for personal glory,” and recklessly pursuing “decoupling and breaking supply chains,” damaging cross-strait economic and trade cooperation? Compatriots on both sides of the Strait see this clearly, and the DPP authorities cannot deny it.\nEight Taiwan-region entities, including Hanxiang Aviation Industry Co., Ltd., deliberately cooperated with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in “seeking independence through armed force.” The facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive. Listing them on the export control control list is a necessary measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is also a just action to maintain normal order in cross-strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation and to protect the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. It is lawful, legitimate, proper, and necessary.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712557.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","《团结报》记者","Strengthening cross-Strait science and technology exchanges benefits the well-being of compatriots on both sides. What policies supporting Taiwan compatriots have been introduced recently in the field of cross-Strait science and technology exchanges?","Recently, the National Natural Science Foundation of China has established the “National Natural Science Foundation of China Research Fund Project for Taiwan Compatriots,” to create favorable conditions for promoting cross-Strait academic exchanges and scientific research cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the restoration of Taiwan. Please introduce the commemorative activities held in various localities.","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. The restoration of Taiwan is an important outcome of the victory of the War of Resistance, a great triumph forged by all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, through successive generations of bloody struggle, and it is worth commemorating together by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nFrom May 26 to 30, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, together with Heilongjiang Radio and Television, produced and launched the radio drama “Taipei Girl.” Set against the backdrop of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland returning to their hometowns after Taiwan's restoration and the Taiwan Volunteer Corps carrying out work behind enemy lines on both sides of the Strait, the drama shows the joy of Taiwan compatriots at returning to the embrace of the motherland and recreates the history of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly resisting foreign aggression. On July 2, the Straits Forum · Cross-Strait Shipbuilding Culture Exchange Event, themed “Striving for Strength Through the Sea · Jointly Guarding Our Homeland — Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War and the 80th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration,” successfully concluded in Fuzhou. On July 7, the Program Production Center of the Film Satellite Channel, the Shanxi Provincial Department of Culture and Tourism, the Cross-Strait Exchange Foundation of the Straits Exchange Association, and other relevant parties jointly held the “‘Echoes of the Yellow River’ — Cross-Strait Concert Commemorating the Victory of the War of Resistance and the 80th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration.” Using an artistic form combining live scene performances and interwoven stage settings, the concert showed compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance and Taiwan's restoration, recalling the national glory forged in blood, celebrating the course of the nationwide resistance, and extolling the great spirit of the War of Resistance.\nFrom July 18 to 25, the “Commemorating Anti-Japanese War Heroes Together, Sharing Chinese Culture Together — 2025 Hubei-Taiwan Teachers and Students History and Literature Teaching Observation and Exchange Meeting” will be held in Hubei, where a hundred teachers and students from both sides of the Strait will jointly study Chinese history and the history of the War of Resistance, and personally experience the charm of Chinese culture and the spirit of the nationwide War of Resistance. From July to August, the Gansu Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office, together with Northwest Normal University, will carry out an essay and short video competition themed “Remembering the Years of Resistance, Sharing National Rejuvenation.” From August 4 to 30, Fuzhou, Sanming, and other cities in Fujian Province will hold activities commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the War of Resistance and Taiwan's restoration, including a documentary flash-mob choral performance by youth from both sides of the Strait, an exhibition of calligraphy works by generals from both sides of the Strait, and exhibitions on the War of Resistance theme from both sides of the Strait.\nWe welcome media reporters to fully cover these activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","The 13th Xiamen-Kinmen Strait Crossing Swim was originally scheduled for July 26. The DPP authorities, citing the claim that the event “has united front overtones” and “involves maritime safety,” said they would carefully assess whether it is necessary to hold it. What comments do you have on this?","The Xiamen-Kinmen Strait Crossing is a mass sports event that has been held for many years in succession and is deeply loved and welcomed by people on both sides of the Strait. It is understood that the 13th Xiamen-Kinmen Strait Crossing was originally scheduled for July 26, hundreds of participants from both sides of the Strait were ready, and relevant authorities in Xiamen and Kinmen had also made careful preparations. However, the DPP authorities suddenly and arbitrarily obstructed it, violating the wishes and expectations of people on both sides of the Strait for exchanges, mutual visits, and closer ties. Such abuse of power is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Reports say that, in response to the so-called “mainland threat,” Taiwan's education authorities have completed 13 textbooks on “understanding the China threat,” which are expected to be used successively after the new school year starts in September this year. The Mainland Affairs Council required that when compiling these textbooks, attention be paid to the fact that the claim that “the people of mainland China…","The DPP authorities disregard facts and distort history, attempting to use newly compiled textbooks to exaggerate the so-called “mainland threat,” incite “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, and spread “Taiwan independence” claims, further poisoning Taiwan's young people after the “Taiwan independence curriculum guidelines.” Their conduct is detestable and their intentions are deserving of condemnation. We strongly condemn this.\nBoth sides of the Strait belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. The vast rivers and mountains are the common home of Chinese people on both sides. On this vast, beautiful, and rich land of the mainland, there is a glorious Chinese history and a brilliant Chinese culture. Ancient sages and the masters of the various schools of thought lived here, and Qu Yuan, Li Bai, Du Fu, Wang Wei, Bai Juyi, and Su Dongpo sang here. Here stand the Great Wall of ten thousand li, the Yellow River with its nine bends, and the rolling Yangtze River. Here are the autumn winds over horses in the northern frontier and the spring rains and apricot blossoms of Jiangnan. Here are hundreds of millions of hardworking and brave people and a development miracle recognized by the world. This is the common inheritance and pride of Chinese people on both sides, and it cannot be erased or defamed by whatever textbooks the DPP authorities fabricate. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to see for themselves how magnificent our rivers and mountains are, and to experience the pride of being upright Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712553.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","《中国日报》记者","Taiwanese media reported that, following the passage of the so-called “Taiwan International Solidarity Act” by the US House of Representatives, a US senator recently introduced a Senate version of the bill, which states “opposition to changing Taiwan’s status without the consent of the people of Taiwan,” and encourages the United States to cooperate with allies and partners to jointly oppose “China undermining…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. In 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all rights in the United Nations to the People's Republic of China and recognizing the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. This thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of China's representation in the United Nations, including Taiwan. History cannot be altered, and facts cannot be distorted.\nThe relevant bill seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and we firmly oppose it. We urge the US side to stop advancing relevant negative bills concerning Taiwan and stop sending any wrong signals to \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Taiwan media reported that Lai Ching-te plans to “visit” Paraguay, Guatemala, and Belize in August, and during this period intends to “transit” through New York and Dallas in the United States. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose Lai Ching-te's \"transit\" through the United States on any pretext or in any form. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and not send any wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities that \"seeking independence by relying on the United States\" is a futile effort and is doomed to fail.\nThe one-China principle is a common understanding of the international community and a basic norm of international relations, upheld and observed by the vast majority of countries in the world. It represents justice, the wishes of the people, and the trend of the times. We hope that relevant Latin American and Caribbean countries will recognize the trend of the times, handle Taiwan-related matters prudently, and join the big family of China-Latin America friendship and cooperation at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712559.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","Regarding the KMT’s anti-Japanese veterans being invited to participate in activities commemorating the 80th anniversary of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War, the head of Taiwan’s defense department said that the mainland has consistently tried to divide Taiwan society through “united front tricks and cognitive warfare,” and told…","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, as well as the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. The Chinese people’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was a great war in which justice triumphed over evil, light over darkness, and progress over reaction; it was an important component of the World Anti-Fascist War. The DPP authorities have smeared the commemoration of the victory in the war as “united front tactics and cognitive warfare,” fully exposing their ugly face of going against the trend of history and against the common values of human society.\nThe War of Resistance Against Japan was a just struggle in which all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation united in one heart, shared the same hatred against the enemy, and resisted the aggression of Japanese militarism. More than 80 years ago, the guerrilla battlefields behind enemy lines opened up under the leadership of the Communist Party of China and the frontal battlefields commanded by the Kuomintang cooperated to form a strategic situation of jointly resisting the Japanese invaders. Our invitation to Kuomintang veterans to take part in the commemorative activities is respect for historical facts and praise for their achievements in fighting bloody battles to defend the homeland. The DPP authorities not only refuse to hold war-commemoration activities, but also threaten and intimidate these veterans. Their intentions are deplorable and their conduct is shameful, and they will certainly face firm opposition from the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712556.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台《海岸两岸》记者","The 8th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was recently held in Zhejiang. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation of the forum and what achievements it produced?","From July 10 to 15, the Eighth Straits Forum for Youth Development was held in Hangzhou, Jiaxing, Ningbo, Wenzhou, Jinhua, and other places in Zhejiang Province. The forum had a scale of about 1,000 people, including more than 700 young people from Taiwan who came from the island to attend. Under the theme “Cross-Strait Torch, Youthful Strength,” the forum held an opening ceremony, keynote speeches, a ceremony in which Taiwan youth representatives apprenticed themselves to mainland intangible cultural heritage masters, the Zhejiang-Taiwan Youth Exchange Season, and the “Strait Cup” Cross-Strait Famous University Baseball and Softball Elite Tournament, among other activities. Cross-Strait youth also went to various places in Zhejiang to take part in theme study camps. Zhejiang has used the Youth Development Forum as a guide to build exchange and cooperation platforms for Taiwan youth coming to Zhejiang, continuously deepened cooperation in education, arts, culture, and other fields, and issued policies supporting Taiwan youth in starting businesses and finding jobs in Zhejiang.\nWe will continue to thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important discourse on Taiwan work and his congratulatory letter to the Sixth Youth Development Forum, continue to hold well youth exchange activities such as the Youth Development Forum, put General Secretary Xi Jinping’s care and concern for young people into practice, and enable cross-Strait youth to achieve greater and better development in the great cause of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","The DPP authorities required 12,000 mainland spouses to submit the so-called “proof of loss of original nationality” before June 30. According to reports, several thousand mainland spouses have still not submitted the proof and are worried about losing their Taiwan status. What is your comment on this?","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have deliberately targeted mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan for many years, some for more than 20 years, and, although the statute of limitations has long since expired, have set a deadline requiring them to pay the so-called “loss of original nationality certificate” fees. This is a typical act of unlawful abuse of power and hostility toward the people, and it has already drawn criticism and opposition from public opinion on the island and Taiwan society.\nThe large community of mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan is already an important member of Taiwan society. They are family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots, and they have contributed to Taiwan's economic and social development in a variety of roles. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' differential treatment and deliberate repression have once again exposed their “Taiwan independence” nature, and show that the “democracy” and “human rights” they talk about are lies.\nThe mainland is the maternal home of the large number of mainland spouses. We care deeply about the lives and circumstances of the mainland spouse community on the island. When wind and rain come, we must, both emotionally and rationally, shelter them. We will absolutely not show leniency toward the “Taiwan independence” enforcers and accomplices who persecute mainland spouses, and we will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250716_12712552.htm"],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","环球网记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan demanded that the mainland give an explanation and apology for “Chinese embassy personnel in the Czech Republic attacking the motorcade of Hsiao Bi-khim during her visit to the Czech Republic.” What is your response?","First, we have consistently and clearly opposed any form of official exchange between our diplomatic partners and the Chinese Taiwan region, and we resolutely oppose relevant countries providing a political stage for “Taiwan independence” separatists. Relevant countries should adhere to the one-China principle and not be provoked or exploited by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nSecond, Chinese diplomatic personnel have always abided by the laws and regulations of the host country. The so-called “attack” incidents that relevant countries and the DPP authorities have hyped are fabricated, and black has been turned into white.\nFinally, the DPP authorities have once again maliciously hyped this incident, with the aim of inciting hostility and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how often a lie is repeated, it will never become true, and that continually staging farces will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Summer vacation has always been the peak season for cross-Strait youth exchanges. Please introduce the cross-Strait youth exchange activities from July to August.","As summer vacation arrives, the enthusiasm for cross-Strait youth exchanges is rising as high as the midsummer heat, and a series of cross-Strait youth exchange activities have been held one after another. They provide platforms for Taiwan youth to visit, study, intern, and start businesses on the mainland, and create conditions for cross-Strait youth to exchange, interact, connect hearts, and grow closer to each other.\nSince early July, exchange activities that cross-Strait youth enjoy have been launched one after another, including the Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum, the opening ceremony of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots' Taiwan Youth Summer Camp for a Thousand Taiwan Compatriots and Youth, the Shaanxi-Taiwan Cultural Exchange Week, the Cross-Strait (Hubei-Taiwan) Youth Jingchu Tour, the Lu-Taiwan Youth Cultural Exchange Season, the Taiwan Youth Tianfu Tour, the “Love Beijing, Love Taiwan” series essay collection and award ceremony, the 2025 “WAY! Come to Shenzhen” Taiwan Youth Internship in Shenzhen, and the 2025 Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Exchange Activities.\nNext, the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, “Building Dreams on the Pearl River · Guangzhou-Taiwan Exchange Season,” “Building Dreams on the Pearl River · Spreading Wings and Soaring — 2025 Taiwan University Students' Guangzhou Internship Experience Activity,” the 3rd “Five Continents Hakka Music” Cultural Exchange Conference in Longyan, the Cross-Strait (Lianchen) Youth Baseball Culture Festival, and other series of cross-Strait youth exchange activities will soon take place one after another in Jiangsu, Guangdong, Fujian and other places. We sincerely invite Taiwan youth, especially Taiwan young friends who have never been to the mainland, to come to the mainland to walk around and see for themselves. We welcome more Taiwan youth to take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, make friends and build heartfelt bonds with mainland youth, march forward hand in hand, and continue to gather youthful strength to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The DPP authorities said that five mainland applications, including Xiaohongshu, Weibo, Douyin, WeChat, and Baidu Netdisk, “pose extremely high information security risks.” They advised the public not to download or use them and demanded that all relevant public officials delete them. What comments do you have on this?","Why are these mainland application software programs so popular among Taiwan residents, especially young people? It is because they enable Taiwan residents to obtain information more efficiently, enjoy more convenient life services, and have more fun with social sharing. The DPP authorities' pretext of so-called “information security” reveals their own inner “insecurity.” They fear that Taiwan residents will learn about the real situation on the mainland through various means, fear that the “information cocoon” they have painstakingly built will be broken, and fear that compatriots on both sides will enhance understanding and draw closer through the exchange of information. The DPP authorities are seeing enemies everywhere, abusing power, and acting against the tide; they will surely meet with opposition from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","It is reported that a Zhejiang deep-sea fishing vessel recently successfully rescued a Taiwan deep-sea fishing vessel in international waters. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The WeChat official account of the TAO of the State Council previously reposted relevant reports from the Farmers' Daily. Here, I would like to brief everyone on the relevant situation again.\nOn May 29, the Taiwan-registered distant-water fishing vessel “Ri Da Zhan” suffered a sudden mechanical failure and lost control while drifting in the Strait of Malacca shipping lane. The Zhejiang distant-water fishing vessel “Shunxing 9” immediately came to its aid, overcoming severe weather to conduct full-scale rescue efforts. Its company, Shunxing Distant-Water Fishing Company, provided remote guidance. After 7 days and 7 nights of continuous towing, they finally escorted the “Ri Da Zhan” to safe waters off Taiwan, ensuring the safety of the 51 crew members aboard the vessel in distress. After returning to Taiwan, Weida Fishery Company, to which the “Ri Da Zhan” belongs, immediately sent a letter of thanks stating, “The professionalism and noble character displayed by the crew of the ‘Shunxing 9’ in this rescue operation profoundly embody the fraternal bond between fishermen on both sides of the Strait.”\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family; blood is thicker than water, and brotherly affection runs deep. In the face of major natural disasters and emergencies, compatriots on both sides empathize with each other, lend each other a helping hand, and overcome difficulties together. This emergency rescue at sea once again shows that the kinship of compatriots across the Strait, sharing weal and woe and watching out for one another, cannot be severed or blocked.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","南方日报 南方+记者","July 1 this year marks the 28th anniversary of Hong Kong's return to the motherland. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council issued a report saying that the “Hong Kong people governing Hong Kong with a high degree of autonomy” promised by the mainland has “become distorted,” and has gradually turned into “central government governing Hong Kong with comprehensive control,” and that Hong Kong society has been subjected…","On the 28th anniversary of Hong Kong’s return to the motherland, Hong Kong has once again been ranked the “world’s freest economy,” its position as an international financial center has remained firmly third in the world, its world competitiveness has risen to third globally, its inflow of foreign direct investment ranks third globally, and the International Mediation Institution has established its headquarters in Hong Kong. These are strong examples of Hong Kong moving from order to prosperity and revitalizing with vigor. They reflect broad international recognition of Hong Kong’s stability, freedom, and prosperity, fully demonstrate the strong vitality of “one country, two systems,” and show that Hong Kong’s future will certainly be even better.\nThe DPP authorities have no qualifications to pass judgment on Hong Kong affairs. Their attempt to smear and attack “one country, two systems” in order to cover up their own governance incompetence, and to obstruct folk exchanges between Hong Kong and Taiwan, will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Following warnings about risks in the Taiwan Strait from U.S. periodicals Foreign Affairs and Foreign Policy, the UK's Financial Times and The Economist recently also published articles pointing out that the situation in the Taiwan Strait is quite dangerous. Public opinion on the island points out that this shows the international community is worried that Lai Ching-te's radical course will trigger a Taiwan…","We have noted that more and more foreign experts and scholars, as well as internationally renowned journals and international public opinion, have expressed concern about the situation across the Taiwan Strait and have publicly criticized Lai Ching-te's \"Taiwan independence\" provocations in words and deeds. The current situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and the root cause lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities' refusal to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, their stubborn adherence to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" and their continued collusion with external forces to engage in provocations seeking \"independence.\"\nWe hope that Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of the DPP authorities' stubborn adherence to the \"Taiwan independence\" line, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, and join us in pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development and in earnestly safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","After Taiwan’s education authorities banned mainland students from majoring in so-called “key technology departments,” they recently sent a letter to universities across the island saying that if teachers are concerned that course content may involve cross-Strait issues, they may refuse to let mainland short-term exchange students audit their classes. What comment do you have?","This is yet another piece of evidence of the DPP authorities' artificial restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges and their unreasonable restrictions on mainland students studying in Taiwan. In pursuit of political gain, the DPP authorities have, from banning and restricting exchanges and cooperation between Taiwan universities and 10 mainland universities, to prohibiting exchanges between Taiwan primary and secondary schools and the mainland, to controlling mainland students' enrollment in so-called “key technology departments” and refusing mainland exchange students' audits of relevant courses, again and again stretched their dark hands into the field of cross-Strait education exchanges. Their interference and obstruction of cross-Strait education exchanges has reached a point with no bottom line and no floor. These perverse acts will certainly be opposed and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, two large Japanese companies withdrew investment from a well-known Taiwan department store. Public opinion on the island holds that Japanese companies made this decision out of concern that the Taiwan Strait situation remains tense, and that their expectations for the Taiwan market have dropped, amounting to “voting with their feet.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities continue to \"seek independence through force\" and \"seek independence by relying on foreign powers,\" undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and raising tensions, pushing Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and calamity. This will inevitably damage Taiwan's economic development prospects and affect foreign investors' confidence in the Taiwan market.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","台湾东森电视记者","First question: A young Taiwanese musician recently said on social media that he had been invited to the mainland to take part in performances commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan and the restoration of Taiwan. During filming, he was asked to shout “I love the Yellow River” and “I love China.” He believes this practice is full of political purpose, while the…","On the first question: I have just introduced the situation of this cross-Strait concert.\nAs far as we understand, the concert was very smooth and very successful, and the Taiwanese performing artists who took part expressed that they were very excited and very moved. I personally also think: what is wrong with shouting \"I love the Yellow River\" and \"I love China\"? Commemorating the victory of the War of Resistance and the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration together in various ways by people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait is a remembrance of the heroic deeds of martyrs and an expression of national sentiment, and it deserves to be affirmed and actively participated in by compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question, regarding your mention of the Taiwan authorities restricting Huawei and SMIC. Technological blockades cannot stop the pace of mainland technological innovation, and attempts to \"decouple and sever chains\" cannot slow the mainland's industrial upgrading. There are many cases of this; encirclement will only unleash greater innovative vitality and stronger upgrading momentum on the mainland. The DPP authorities' practice of undermining cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation for political purposes will only harm the competitiveness of Taiwan's own enterprises and restrict the prospects for Taiwan's economic development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The 12th World Games will be held in Chengdu, Sichuan, on August 7. Could you introduce the registration of Taiwan athletes to participate in the Games? Has the mainland invited Taiwan guests to attend the opening and closing ceremonies? What is your position on implementing the “Olympic model” at this World Games? Should cross-Strait media also follow the “Olympic model” in news reporting?","The 12th World Games will open on August 7 in Chengdu, Sichuan Province, and preparations are steadily advancing. We welcome Taiwan athletes and sports circles to attend or observe this Games. For information on registration of Taiwan athletes to compete, please follow the information released by the Organizing Committee.\nThe “Olympic model” is a principle jointly followed by international sports organizations and sports circles on both sides of the Strait. It has been and will continue to be implemented for all international sports events held on the mainland. The “Olympic model” does not involve news media or other fields or areas outside the events.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","四川日报封面新闻记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said that cross-Strait tour groups cannot resume because the mainland unilaterally demands that the Taiwan side accept the “1992 Consensus” as a political precondition, and that the mainland is obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. What is your comment?","As is well known, the crux of and obstacles to cross-Strait tourism lie entirely in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities. It is a case of the thief shouting “stop thief”: it is the DPP authorities who have repeatedly manipulated cross-Strait tourism for political purposes. To seek “independence” and political self-interest, they are, deep down, unwilling to see cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, including the resumption of cross-Strait tourism. This approach, which disregards the wishes and interests of Taiwan's tourism industry and public, will only provoke greater dissatisfaction and opposition, and it is becoming increasingly unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Regarding the mainland side's recent announcement that it will activate the M503 route's W121 connecting route, some public opinion on the island holds that the mainland's move shows clear “lawfare” intent and is also a response to Lai Ching-te's so-called “Ten Lectures.” What comments do you have on this?","The activation of the W121 connecting route to airway M503 is intended to ease congestion on relevant airspace routes and the pressure of flight growth in the relevant regions, ensure flight safety, reduce flight delays, safeguard passengers’ rights and interests, and further facilitate personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. It is in the common interest of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-16","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Regarding the mainland's inclusion of eight Taiwanese entities on its export control list for dual-use items, some scholars on the island analyzed that the mainland's move is more political symbolism than substance, or is a countermeasure against provocations of “Taiwan independence,” such as Lai Ching-te's so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity.” What comments do you have on this?","Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has obstinately adhered to the “Taiwan independence” stance and has widely promoted separatist fallacies, attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “pursue independence through force.” Some Taiwan enterprises and institutions have deliberately colluded with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, threatening peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The nature of this conduct is egregious.\nIn accordance with relevant laws and regulations, the Ministry of Commerce has decided to place eight Taiwan entities, including Aerospace Industrial Development Corporation (Hanxiang Aviation Industry Co., Ltd.), on its export control list for dual-use items, prohibiting the export of dual-use items to them. This is a necessary measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and it is also a resolute punishment for the reckless provocations of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces seeking “independence.”\nThat concludes today’s press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250716_12712530.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-07-18","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwan’s deputy leader Hsiao Bi-khim said in a press conference today that “aggressive military posturing by China is counterproductive” and that “defending the status quo with China is consistent with the interests of the entire region.” Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on the remarks?","Taiwan is part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people and Chinese people only. The real status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The biggest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the fact that the two sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China and the prevailing international commitment to the one-China principle, nor can they change the trend towards China’s ultimate and inevitable reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250718_11673038.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250718_11673005.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-07-24","Guo Jiakun","China Review News","It’s reported that the South African government issued a notice, saying that the Taipei Commercial Office situated in Pretoria will no longer be recognized. South Africa has called upon Taipei to relocate its Commercial Office from the capital, Pretoria, to Johannesburg. The Taipei Liaison Office in Cape Town will be referred to as the Taipei Commercial Office. What’s China’s comment?","The one-China principle is the political foundation for China to establish and develop diplomatic relations with other countries. It is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community. China commends South Africa’s own decision that you mentioned. It is a positive action in keeping with the one-China principle and UNGA Resolution 2758. This is also reflective of the strength of the China-South Africa all-round strategic cooperative partnership in the new era. We will continue standing firmly together with South Africa on issues bearing on each other’s core interests.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250724_11676510.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250724_11676529.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-07-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On July 26, Taiwan’s “great recall” of legislators held its first round of voting, and the KMT achieved a landslide victory, retaining all 24 seats. What is your comment on the voting results?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying: We have noted the relevant situation. Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature and its ambition for “one-party dominance,” the DPP authorities, disregarding the livelihood and well-being of people on the island, have repeatedly stirred up political strife, resorted to any means to suppress political rivals, created a “green terror,” and intensified social division, fully exposing their hypocritical face of “fake democracy and real dictatorship.” The voting results show that the DPP's political manipulation completely goes against the will of the people on the island and has lost popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250727_12714385.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-07-28","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","It’s reported that the head of Taiwan’s so-called foreign affairs department recently made a “private” trip to Japan and met with Japanese politicians, including former economic security minister Sanae Takaichi and director of the LDP Youth Division Nakasone Yasutaka. What’s China’s comment?","By allowing Lin Chia-lung to make the so-called “private” trip, Japan provided a platform for “Taiwan independence” forces to engage in anti-China separatist activities, seriously violated the basic norms governing international relations and the principles in the four political documents between China and Japan, and sent out a gravely wrong signal. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes it. We’ve lodged serious representations to the Japanese side in Beijing and Tokyo and made strong protests.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and basic trust between the two countries. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, the World Anti-Fascist War, and the restoration of Taiwan. Japan’s colonial rule over Taiwan lasted for more than 50 years and Japan bears serious historical responsibilities to the Chinese people.\nWe urge Japan to abide by the principles in the four political documents between China and Japan, act on its solemn commitment, deeply reflect on and learn lessons from history, act all the more prudently on the Taiwan question, not to harm China’s sovereignty in any way and not to send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Japan should never underestimate the firm resolve, will and ability of the Chinese people to safeguard sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250728_11678340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250728_11678284.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-07-28","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Yesterday, the Taiwan authorities’ recall vote against lawmakers from Kuomintang failed. What’s China’s comment?","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council made statements on this. The results of the vote demonstrate that the DPP authorities’ political manipulation goes against the will of the people on the island and finds no support. Let me stress that there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affairs, which brooks no external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250728_11678340.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250728_11678284.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-07-29","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The Financial Times and Bloomberg reported that the “president” of Taiwan Lai Ching-te was not going to be able to transit the U.S. on his apparently planned trip to South America. The Trump administration has apparently declined to allow him to transit New York. Has the Chinese government had any contact with the U.S. government ahead of this, asking the U.S. government not to allow Lai Ching-te to transit…","First of all, Taiwan is a province of China and there is no such thing as “president.” China noted relevant reports. Let me underscore that China firmly opposes any form of official interaction between the U.S. and the Taiwan region and firmly opposes any trip by leader of the Taiwan region to the U.S. in any name or under whatever pretext. This position is consistent, clear and firm. We hope the U.S. will abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence, and promote the steady, sound and sustainable development of China-U.S. relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250729_11679085.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250729_11679055.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-07-30","Guo Jiakun","Xinhua News Service","It’s reported that owing to the U.S.’s refusal of the stopover in New York, Lai Ching-te put off his plan to visit the so-called “diplomatic allies” in Latin America. What’s your comment?","Let me stress again that the one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. The commitment to the one-China principle is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends, and the right thing to do. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ separatist provocations will lead nowhere, still less shake the solid and strong international commitment to the one-China principle or stop the overriding historical trend towards China’s reunification.\nWe also hope Taiwan’s so-called “diplomatic allies” will not be repeatedly swayed or used by “Taiwan independence” forces. Instead, they should get a clear sense of where things are headed, change their course, and make the right decision that meets the historical trend and serves people’s long-term interests as early as possible.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250730_11679797.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250730_11679709.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Britain's Defense Secretary John Healey said on July 27 during his visit to Australia that the UK is ready to engage in a fight in the Pacific if conflict breaks out over Taiwan. What's your comments on this?","The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China, which brooks no foreign interference. We urge the UK side to be prudent on its words and actions concerning the Taiwan question, refrain from sending wrong signals to separatist forces for \"Taiwan independence\", and avoid undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. No one should underestimate the firm will and strong ability of the PLA to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, it's reported that the Philippine Defense Secretary said that the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is shifting its focus from combating domestic insurgency to external defense, and will take firm measures against China's \"aggressive\" behaviors in the South China Sea. The Philippine side is strengthening defense cooperation with the US, Australia, Japan and India. What's your…","On your first question, relevant remarks of the Philippine side misrepresent the facts and attempt to cast itself as the victim. China's Nanhai Zhudao is beyond the limits of the Philippine territory, which has long been defined by a series of international treaties. The Philippine side illegally occupies some islands and reefs of China's Nansha Qundao, repeatedly makes provocations and harassment against the Chinese side at sea, and seduce foreign forces to make waves in the South China Sea. It has become the source of trouble and dangers. The Chinese side never wavers in our resolve and will to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and will take resolute countermeasures against any provocations by the Philippine side in accordance with laws and regulations.\nOn your second question, there are many negative comments about this TV show in Taiwan. The DPP authorities are criticized for stoking anxiety about war and making provocations, in an attempt to plunge Taiwan into war and make ordinary people of Taiwan to serve as \"Taiwan independence\" cannon fodder. Their scheme to force compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait into conflict and to harm and ruin Taiwan will find no support and is doomed to failure.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, the Taiwan region recently conducted the Han Kuang 41 exercise, with the duration doubled from last year. Many US weapon systems made their debut in the exercise. The drills mobilized record-high personnel, and included subjects on in-depth defense and protracted warfare. What's your comments on that? Second, the US Air Force recently held Exercise Resolute Force Pacific in the…","On your first question, the Han Kuang exercise is no more than a show. It cannot change the destined failure of separatists seeking \"Taiwan independence\". The drills will only expose the vicious calculation of the DPP authorities to harm and ruin Taiwan in the name of protection, and to coerce the people of Taiwan into being cannon fodder. We warn the DPP authorities that too many vile deeds will lead to one's self-destruction, and whatever they do will be of no avail. We firmly oppose any forms of military collusion between the US and the Taiwan region, and request the US side to earnestly abide by the promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\", stop sending wrong signals to separatist forces, and stop disrupting peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOn your second question, the Pacific should be an ocean of peace, not a place to stir storms. Holding onto its Cold-War mentality, the US side keeps flexing its muscles in the Asia Pacific, forms exclusive blocs under the guise of military exercises, and coerces and puts pressure on others. Its behaviors damage peace and stability in the Asia Pacific. Come what may, we will remain composed. The Chinese military has full confidence and capability to overcome any risks and challenges, safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, and remain a staunch force for global and regional peace.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, in response to the Chinese mainland inviting the Kuomintang (KMT) veterans to observe the military parade on September 3, the DPP authorities warned those veterans that whoever attends relevant events would lose their retirement benefits. What's your comments on this? My second question is that Hsiao Bi-khim reportedly said that Taiwan does not seek conflict with China and will not…","On your first question, the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression is a righteous fight in which all the Chinese people united together against the invasion of Japanese militarists. The DPP authorities threatening and intimidating these war veterans are shameful behaviors that betray the nation, history and conscience.\nOn your second question, Taiwan is China's Taiwan. No one is more committed to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait than we are. The root cause of cross-Strait tension lies with the DPP authorities obstinately pushing for \"Taiwan independence\" and colluding with foreign forces to make provocations. In the face of separatist activities, the PLA will not sit idly by, and will continue to speak with actions to safeguard our national sovereignty, territorial integrity and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that according to sources, the US administration denied permission for Lai Ching-te to stop in New York en route to Latin America. At the same time, Lai's office said that there are no immediate plans for his overseas travel. May I have your comments on this?","Upholding the one-China principle is what justice demands, and is where the public opinion trends and the arc of history bends. The Chinese side firmly opposes any forms of official interactions between China's Taiwan region and any other countries. We require the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with extra prudence, and work with us to promote the steady, sound and sustainable development of China-US relations.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the troops of Taiwan recently conducted the Han Kuang 41 exercise, which, for the first time, included the so-called urban resilience drills and had chain supermarkets participating in air defense simulation drills. During the exercise, multiple districts of Taiwan were stricken by a typhoon. When victims turned to the military for help, Lai Ching-te said that they should not rely on the troops…","The Han Kuang exercise is no more than a show. The Lai Ching-te authorities are too busy with their bluffing shows to care about the people of Taiwan stricken by natural disasters. They will be despised for sure.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the US side dispatched over 400 observers, including active and retired military officers, to the Han Kuang 41 exercise. May I have your comments on this?","The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China, which brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any forms of military collusion between the US and the Taiwan region. We warn the DPP authorities that a useful fool will eventually become an abandoned tool, and that soliciting US support for \"Taiwan independence\" and resisting reunification by force will not succeed.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, in the Extended Deterrence Dialogue attended by their heads of foreign and defense departments, the US and Japan held multiple tabletop exercises to strategize a scenario in which a conflict broke out in East Asia and the US is pressured to use nuclear weapons. May I have your comments on this? Secondly, it's reported that the troops of Taiwan plan to purchase five more types of…","On your first question, as a victim of nuclear explosions, the Japanese side should have a profound realization that a nuclear war must not be fought and cannot be won. However, some individuals of the Japanese side attempt to upgrade the so-called extended deterrence of the US, push for the introduction and even the use of nuclear weapons through \"nuclear sharing\", and provoke arms race. It's a very dangerous development. The Chinese side urges the US and Japan to abandon their Cold-War mentality, reduce the role of nuclear weapons in national and collective security policies, and take concrete actions to uphold strategic stability and regional peace and security.\nOn your second question, here is what I want to say: the \"Taiwan Independence\" armed forces are overreaching themselves and their efforts are futile.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-07-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to the UK media, the US is pushing Japan and Australia to clarify what role the two countries will play if a war over Taiwan breaks out, which frustrated the two countries. Could you please comment on this?","I will not comment on hypothetical questions. But I want to emphasize that some external forces always want to use the Taiwan question to make trouble and challenge the core interests of China. Such behavior is extremely dangerous and will not succeed. It's known to all that the US side can only be fair-weather friends for its allies and partners. We hope relevant countries will not be cat's paws for others, which will end up harming themselves, and will not disrupt peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/07/china-250730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16399849.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 30, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te declared in his so-called “Ten Lectures on Unity” that “the People's Republic of China has never governed Taiwan.” A mainland scholar published an article with solid arguments exposing the Lai authorities' distortion of “factual control” into “legal ownership.” In response, the Mainland Affairs Council said, “Since 1945, Taiwan has been continuously governed by the Republic of China, and the Republic…","The historical course of the Taiwan question is clear, and the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China is plain. Lai Ching-te's fallacies have neither historical nor legal basis, nor do they conform to objective facts. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the government of the Republic of China as the sole legal government representing all of China. This was a change of regime in which the subject of international law, China, did not change; China's sovereignty and inherent territory did not change; and the government of the People's Republic of China naturally fully enjoys and exercises China's sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding facts and talking nonsense, have repeatedly peddled the fallacies and lies that the two sides are “not subordinate to each other.” They will only increase tension in the Taiwan Strait, only undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait, and only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. No matter what they say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and they cannot block the inevitable trend toward national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715106.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The DPP authorities have demanded that 13 so-called \"Reading China Threat\" supplementary textbooks be used at the start of the new school year in September. Public opinion on the island has criticized this move as systematic \"Taiwan independence\" brainwashing that will seriously harm the cognition of young people on the island and cross-Strait relations. What is your comment on this?","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and vigorously promote “de-Sinicization.” Disregarding history and distorting facts, they attempt to use “Taiwan independence” textbooks to sever the historical and cultural ties across the Taiwan Strait, causing confusion in the historical memory of the younger generation in Taiwan and distortion of national identity. Such acts of forgetting one’s ancestry and acting against the historical current will inevitably be firmly opposed and despised by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Those who abuse their authority to grossly distort and falsify the fact that Taiwan is part of China in the field of education, and the personnel involved, will also inevitably be punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715105.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广“海峡飞虹”记者","Typhoon “Danas” caused severe disaster in many parts of Taiwan. The DPP authorities’ ineffective disaster relief and various cold and arrogant remarks and actions have sparked public resentment. Public opinion has criticized Lai Ching-te’s disaster response as mere political theater, saying he “cares only about the recall and not about people’s livelihoods.” What is your comment?","We are concerned about the compatriots affected by “Danas” and hope they can soon restore normal production and daily life. The DPP authorities have ignored the needs of disaster victims and been slow and ineffective in disaster relief. This once again exposes their true face of “putting politics above everything” and having only party self-interest in mind, and once again exposes the hypocrisy of the DPP authorities and Lai Qingde, who advertise themselves as “democratic” and “loving Taiwan.” Public opinion on the island and residents of the disaster areas have widely criticized them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","The U.S. “reciprocal tariffs” on Taiwan have yet to be determined, and the New Taiwan dollar has appreciated significantly. This has prompted widespread concern among industry operators on the island that the DPP authorities will compromise and make concessions to the United States, substantially opening up zero or low tariffs on U.S. imports of beef, chicken, pork and automobiles, among other products. Related…","Driven by their nature of “relying on foreign powers to seek independence,” the DPP authorities “flatter the US and sell out Taiwan” without any bottom line. They keep the process of trade negotiations with the US side shrouded in secrecy and even engage in political manipulation, which once again confirms that they have neither the intention nor the ability to safeguard the island's economic development and the well-being of its people. A sharp appreciation of the New Taiwan dollar will severely hit Taiwan's export trade and have a huge impact on Taiwan's economy. If Taiwan, under the dual pressure of tariffs and exchange rates, becomes a “dumping ground” for foreign products and a “leek patch” for foreign capital to harvest, the island's agriculture and fisheries, traditional industries and small and medium-sized enterprises will bear the brunt. The health and food safety of the people will be seriously harmed, and the momentum and autonomy of Taiwan's economic development will be further weakened. The DPP authorities let the United States take whatever it wants. It is Taiwan that is sacrificed, and Taiwan compatriots who are harmed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715103.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Luo Wen-jia, Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that all cross-Strait consultations, dialogues, and exchanges are aimed at ensuring and striving for greater benefits for Taiwan; if consultations, exchanges, and negotiations ultimately result in the “erosion” of Taiwan's rights, then this is not the purpose of exchanges. What comments do you have on this?","In June 2008, ARATS and SEF resumed consultations and negotiations on the basis of the \"1992 Consensus.\" They subsequently signed 23 agreements in succession, realizing comprehensive, direct, two-way \"three links\" across the Taiwan Strait and resolving many practical issues concerning the vital interests of compatriots on both sides. This enhanced the common well-being of compatriots on both sides, and Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses have benefited from it. Promoting dialogue and consultation across the Strait is our consistent position, and its starting point and ultimate aim are to continuously enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nThe DPP authorities, on the one hand, stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" position, continuously distort and deny the \"1992 Consensus,\" and unilaterally undermine the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations and of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. They deliberately obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and severely harm the interests and well-being of broad Taiwan compatriots. On the other hand, they constantly fabricate lies and shirk responsibility, attempting to deceive the Taiwan public and cover up their wrongdoing in undermining cross-Strait consultations and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. This despicable conduct of saying one thing and doing another cannot withstand the facts. It does not win hearts and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715102.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the recent topic of “Taiwanese are Chinese,” the MAC said that the relationship between Taiwan and the mainland has never been a matter of Chinese people and Chinese culture, but a matter of systems and ideas, and that Taiwan people want to live a free and democratic life and do not like the mainland’s social system. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The 23 million Taiwan compatriots are all members of the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to unification, much less an excuse for separation. The current struggle against “Taiwan independence” and separatism is not a contest of systems, but a struggle between unification and separation, and a confrontation between justice and evil.\nSince coming to power, the Lai Ching-te authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, have on the one hand gone to every length to suppress political opponents on the island, creating a “chilling effect” and carrying out widespread “green terror.” On the other hand, they have stubbornly clung to the “Taiwan independence” position and continually engaged in provocations aimed at “independence,” trying to tie Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” war chariot. Their conduct completely violates the spirit of democracy, and the essence of their “fake democracy, real dictatorship” has long been seen through by the world.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715104.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The opening of the W121 connecting route to M503 has drawn attention on the island. How has this connecting route performed since it began operating?","Since the W121 connecting route of M503 was put into use, overall operation has been safe and stable. From July 21 to 24, a total of 61 flight sorties were actually operated, averaging about 15 sorties per day. This shortened the distance of relevant routes, eased airway congestion, and reduced flight delays. Facts have proven that the use of the W121 connecting route of M503 further facilitates personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and is in the common interests of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715101.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","The US House of Representatives recently passed the “FY2026 National Defense Appropriations Act,” which includes $500 million for the “Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative” to provide Taiwan with defense materiel and military education and training assistance. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and tolerates no external interference. Some members of the US Congress have insisted on inserting negative content concerning Taiwan into relevant bills. This brutally interferes in China’s internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and sends an erroneous signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We firmly oppose this.\nThe Taiwan question is the first insurmountable red line in China-US relations. The US side should abide by the political commitments it has made to China on the Taiwan question, stop deliberating the relevant bills, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how many weapons they obtain from the United States, they cannot shake our firm resolve to resolve the Taiwan question and complete national reunification, and they cannot stop our strong capability to crush “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715100.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","《中国日报》记者","The US House of Representatives recently passed the so-called “Taiwan Conflict Deterrence” act. The DPP authorities said that so far in this session of the US Congress, more than 20 bills directly providing “aid to Taiwan” and more than 20 bills or resolutions mentioning “aid to Taiwan” have been introduced. What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The current session of the U.S. Congress has concocted multiple bills related to Taiwan, repeatedly sending serious erroneous signals to the Lai Ching-te authorities and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We firmly oppose this. The United States should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with prudence.\nNo matter how the DPP authorities “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” and no matter how external forces create disruption, the historical trend that the motherland will be reunified, and will inevitably be reunified, cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Cross-Strait exchange activities during the summer vacation continue to be lively. Please spokesperson briefly introduce what cross-Strait exchange activities will take place in August?","Summer has always been the peak season for cross-Strait exchanges. This August, Beijing, Hebei, Shanghai, Fujian, Henan, Hubei, Guizhou, Yunnan, Xinjiang, as well as Xiamen, Shenzhen, Shenyang, and Guangzhou, will host a series of cross-Strait exchange activities in diverse forms and rich content, covering youth, sports, culture, economy and trade, folk beliefs, ethnic minorities, and other fields.\nIn youth exchanges, the 2025 Henan Province Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Month, the 13th Strait Youth Gathering, the 2nd Cross-Strait Youth Convergence, the \"2025 Journey Through Jingchu: Cross-Strait (Hubei) Youth Industrial Heritage Study Camp,\" the first Qiantai Youth Big Data Industry Development Exchange Week, and other activities will be launched one after another.\nIn sports exchanges, various localities will host the 2025 Strait Inter-School Sports Alliance Baseball Games (Shanghai and Beijing stops), the 6th Strait (Liancheng) Youth Baseball Culture Festival, the 2025 Strait Student Baseball League (Urumqi stop), the Cross-Strait Villages of the Same Name Basketball Invitational, the Cross-Strait Youth Badminton Exchange Competition, the \"Rolling Across the Strait, Setting Sail for Dreams\" Youth Roller Skating Culture Exchange, the \"Guangzhou-Taiwan Youth Sports Carnival,\" and other activities.\nIn cultural exchanges, the second session of the Cross-Strait Guoxue Academy Study Tour Lecture Series, the 7th Yunnan Tea Horse Ancient Road Photography Experience Camp, the Ji-Taiwan Tai Chi Culture Exchange Meeting, the \"Same Origin Notes 2025: Sea Gathering Research Camp,\" the Quanzhou-Taiwan Summer Cultural Tourism Exchange Season, the \"Music Fun in Haicang\" 2025 Strait (Xiamen) Folk Music Exchange, the 3rd \"Five Continents Hakka Sounds\" Cultural Exchange Meeting, and others will kick off.\nIn folk belief and ethnic minority exchanges, the 17th Strait Fude Culture Theme Activities will be held in both Kinmen and Huli District of Xiamen; the 2025 Strait (Hubei) Youth Chan Culture Study Activities and the 9th Hubei-Taiwan Ethnic Minority Women's Meeting in Enshi will be held in Hubei.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, the 13th Yunnan-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation Symposium will be held in Kunming and other locations, focusing on helping Taiwan compatriots and enterprises gain a deeper understanding of the dividends of the Western Development policy and actively participate in cooperation and integrated development between Yunnan and Taiwan.\nThe holding of these activities fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and that they want to exchange and love to exchange. Regardless of how many disruptions and obstacles they encounter, exchanges and cooperation among compatriots on both sides will not stop, break off, or diminish. We sincerely welcome more Taiwan compatriots to take part in cross-Strait exchanges, to enjoy the beauty of our rivers and mountains, witness the new face of China, and feel the kinship of our compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","After Typhoon “Danas” struck Taiwan, the island suffered its most serious power outage in recent years. Offshore photovoltaic facilities subsidized by the DPP authorities, totaling three hundred million, were blown down, and there even emerged a phenomenon of “the more solar panels, the longer the outage.” Some public opinion on the island has pointed out that “natural disaster plus man-made disaster” exposes the…","Of all the myriad matters under heaven, the people's livelihood is the greatest. But in the eyes of the DPP authorities, “livelihood” is not “the people's livelihood” but “the DPP's business.” To seize party interests, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, act against the will of the people, deceive the people's hearts, seize the people's benefits, and act recklessly. On the other hand, they are incompetent in governance and have neither the will nor the ability to solve the island's energy problems. So-called “green electricity” is merely a pretext and means for DPP politicians to line their own pockets, and the Taiwan people have suffered from it for a long time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","The DPP authorities recently claimed that during the World University Games in Germany, staff of the mainland delegation repeatedly pressured the organizers and interfered with Taiwan delegation activities, “infinitely escalating to the Olympic model.” What is your comment?","Regarding the question you raised, the Chinese Students' Sports Federation already explained the situation on July 24 and clarified the facts. The “Olympic model” is a common rule recognized by the international sports community for handling the Taiwan question, and a principle that sports circles on both sides of the Strait abide by. It provides a basic institutional guarantee for promoting cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation and for supporting athletes from both sides in taking part in international sporting events. The DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated rumors and stirred up trouble, challenging the “Olympic model” in order to use sports to pursue “independence.” People from all walks of life on the island, including the sports community, should distinguish right from wrong, recognize its “Taiwan independence” malicious intent, and not dance to its tune.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s external exchange authority, recently made a provocative visit to Japan, during which he met members of the Liberal Democratic Party, Japan’s ruling party. What comments do you have?","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has made stern representations to Japan on this matter and lodged strong protests. It must be pointed out that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China.\nJapan once stole Taiwan and ruled it as a colony, and it bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on this issue. Japan should fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, learn from history, abide by the one-China principle, the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and the solemn commitments it has made on the Taiwan question, and immediately stop all wrongful words and deeds. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: 80 years ago, we defeated the Japanese aggressors and recovered Taiwan. Eighty years later, any scheme of “relying on foreign powers to seek independence” and any attempt to split Taiwan from China is wishful thinking and will only fail even more completely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202507/t20250730_12715099.htm"],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","It is reported that the 13th Straits Youth Gathering will be held in Fujian in early August. Please introduce the relevant information.","The centralized activities of the 13th Strait Youth Gathering will be held in Fuzhou from August 1 to 7. During the centralized activities, 25 events will be held, including the Strait Youth Heart-Connecting Gathering, the Cross-Strait College Student Leadership Camp, “Entering the CPPCC—Taiwan Youth Speak,” and the Strait Youth Weather Gathering.\nSince 2013, this event has been successfully held for 12 consecutive sessions, attracting a cumulative total of more than 41,000 cross-Strait youth participants, including more than 23,000 Taiwan youth. It is an exchange platform widely welcomed and loved by cross-Strait youth. This year's event takes “Inheriting Chinese Culture and Continuing Blood Ties” as its theme and covers fields such as rural revitalization, culture and sports, digital technology, innovation and entrepreneurship, folk religion, and grassroots governance. We welcome more Taiwan youth to come to the mainland and join mainland youth in this great cross-Strait youth gathering. We believe everyone will find joy and friendship here and return home with full harvests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan’s Vice President Hsiao Bi-khim recently said that Taiwan has reaffirmed its position of maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, called for dialogue between the mainland and the Taiwan authorities on the basis of “parity and respect,” and said that “Taiwan’s choice to safeguard the status quo is the most responsible for the entire region.” What is your comment on this?","The purpose of these remarks is to confuse public opinion and mislead international public opinion and the public on the island. The DPP authorities have always said one thing and done another: on the one hand, they put on a show of wanting to engage in dialogue and consultation with the mainland; on the other hand, they stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" position, loudly promote separatist fallacies, deliberately sabotage peace across the Taiwan Strait, and constantly collude with external forces to seek \"independence\" and provoke confrontation. Their so-called \"equality and respect\" is an attempt to achieve cross-Strait dialogue on the basis of not recognizing the one-China principle, and their so-called \"preserving the status quo\" is in essence an attempt to continue dividing the country and creating \"de facto Taiwan independence.\"\nOur position on cross-Strait dialogue and consultation is consistent and clear. Only by abandoning \"Taiwan independence\" and acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait have a solid guarantee, and only then can cross-Strait dialogue and communication have a foundation of mutual trust.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","The US House of Representatives recently passed a Taiwan-related amendment prohibiting the US Department of Defense from displaying maps that show Taiwan as part of China. The legislator who proposed it said this reflects a simple reality: “China is China, and Taiwan is Taiwan.” What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. This is both an iron-clad fact and a common consensus of the international community. The relevant bills in the US Congress and the remarks of certain members of Congress are a challenge to the one-China principle and an affront to the national feelings of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. We firmly oppose this and strongly condemn it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","According to reports, a think tank of Taiwan's “National Science and Technology Council” recently released a report stating that the mainland's market share in the mature-process chip sector is expected to surpass Taiwan's within two years, and that it will comprehensively dominate the direction of development of major technology products. What is your comment on this?","We attach great importance to technological innovation and market application. Relying on a complete industrial system and rich application scenarios, high-tech industries such as semiconductors and artificial intelligence have developed rapidly in recent years. Driven by global market demand, they have built a certain competitive advantage in the field of mature-process chips. In the future, we will continue to rely on our industrial foundation and the advantage of an extremely large market, keep promoting deep integration of technological innovation and industrial innovation, and create better conditions for the development of high-tech industries, including the semiconductor industry. We hope the two sides will strengthen cooperation and integrated development in relevant industries and join hands to strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation. We also welcome Taiwan businesses and companies to seize opportunities, continue to invest in the mainland, put down roots here, and achieve better development in the new round of scientific and technological revolution and industrial transformation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Recently, North China and other mainland regions have continued to suffer heavy rainfall, causing major disasters. The Mainland Affairs Council has expressed condolences to relevant mainland parties. What is your comment on this? Do you know the disaster situation for Taiwan compatriots in the affected areas?\nSecond question: Regarding the first round of voting results in Taiwan’s “mass recall” of…","First question: recently, Eastern, Northern, and Northeastern China have continuously suffered heavy rainfall, triggering floods and geological disasters that have caused major casualties and property losses in Beijing, Hebei, Jilin, Shandong, and other places. The Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council attach great importance to this, and General Secretary Xi Jinping has issued important instructions on flood control and disaster relief work. Relevant departments and localities have thoroughly implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions, fully carried out rescue and disaster relief work, made every effort to reduce casualties, and fully ensured the safety of people's lives and property. At present, disaster relief work is being carried out urgently, and people in the affected areas have been properly resettled. According to our understanding, no Taiwan compatriots have been killed or injured in the disaster so far. Taiwan Affairs Offices in the relevant localities will promptly learn whether Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in the area have been affected, and will provide assistance in a timely manner.\nSecond question: regarding the statements by Lai Ching-te that you mentioned. Lai Ching-te's remarks are entirely self-deception, fully exposing his obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature. The Democratic Progressive Party suffered a crushing defeat in the vote on July 26, which fully shows that its “resisting China and seeking independence” runs counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island and is rejected by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nThird question: regarding the World University Games in Germany that you mentioned. The China Students' Sports Federation has already issued an explanation. The International University Sports Federation has also stated its position, supporting the legitimate conduct of the Chinese delegation.\nI want to emphasize that the “Olympic model” is a basic principle jointly observed by the international and cross-Strait sports communities. Any international sports event must fully and accurately implement the “Olympic model,” and there should be no “names, flags, anthems, and emblems” or materials, logos, and slogans that violate the “Olympic model.” Displays involving politics, religion, or race are not permitted at venues of international sports events. We resolutely oppose the Democratic Progressive Party authorities using sports to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. Any act that attempts to violate the basic principles of the international and cross-Strait sports communities, and that interferes with sports events for political purposes and political private gain, will not win public support and is destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","The British newspaper Financial Times recently reported that Japanese government officials told Japanese companies in Taiwan that if they need to evacuate employees because of a conflict breaking out in the Taiwan Strait, the companies will “only be able to rely on themselves.” According to the report, since 2022, several large Japanese companies have conducted simulated evacuations of their employees in Taiwan…","The root cause of the current tense situation across the Taiwan Strait is that the Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, persistently “seeking independence through armed force” and “seeking independence by relying on external support,” and constantly pushing Taiwan toward the danger of war and bloodshed. Relevant countries should recognize the true nature of Lai Ching-te as a “peace breaker” and “troublemaker,” clearly oppose “Taiwan independence,” and support the just cause of China’s reunification. Only in this way can regional peace and stability truly be maintained, and the security and interests of their own people be protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","The 2025 World Artificial Intelligence Conference (WAIC) was held in Shanghai, and its series of cross-Strait AI integration development events has drawn great attention. Please introduce the relevant details.","The 2025 World Artificial Intelligence Conference Cross-Strait Artificial Intelligence Integration and Innovation Development Forum and exhibition activities were successfully held in Shanghai from July 26 to 29. This series of activities was hosted by the Straits Economic and Technological Cooperation Center under the theme “Leading the New Journey, Integrating for the Future.” The forum brought together more than one hundred scholars and industry and commerce representatives from both sides of the Strait, focusing on topics such as AI infrastructure, large model applications, and the reshaping of industrial ecosystems, and conducted in-depth discussions on development paths for integration in the field of artificial intelligence across the Strait. The exhibition showcased the development achievements and cutting-edge technological breakthroughs in key links of the artificial intelligence industry chain on both sides of the Strait. The series of activities effectively built a platform for technological demonstration and in-depth dialogue in artificial intelligence across the Strait, and it attracted extensive attention and positive evaluations from participants in all sectors.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-07-30","Chen Binhua","台湾东森电视台记者","First question. International media mostly reported the results of the July 26 “great recall” under headlines such as “Taiwan voters reject recall of ‘pro-China’ ‘legislators.’” Some analysis holds that the voting results will send a signal to the international community that “Taiwan public opinion may lean toward mainland China,” and also show that the “anti-China card” the DPP habitually plays has failed. What…","First question: In the first round of voting on July 26, Taiwan’s people already cast votes against the so-called “great recall,” showing that the DPP authorities’ political manipulation and their so-called “resist China, protect Taiwan” line violate the mainstream public opinion on the island and are unpopular.\nSecond question: We have noted the relevant reports. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose Lai Ching-te’s “transit” to slip into the United States on any pretext or in any form. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We warn the Lai Ching-te authorities that “relying on the US to seek independence” is a waste of effort and is doomed to fail.\nToday’s press conference Q&A session ends here. Next, we announce the winners of the second “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” event.\nOn July 7, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” published the questions for the second “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” event. As of the 28th, the netizens who answered correctly and ranked in the top ten by comments and likes, in order, are: “浩浩”, “持彩练当空舞”, “小天”, “风景”, “缘分的天空”, “JIAOZI”, “瓦瓦”, “玉小莹”, “云深”, and “刚刚好”.\nNetizens wrote one after another expressing their hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will understand, exchange with, and visit each other. One netizen wrote, “A strait can separate geography, but it cannot separate roots tied by blood.” Another said, “I can still recite ‘Sun Moon Lake’ without missing a word.” There were also Taiwan netizens who described their story of putting down roots in Zhengzhou and said, “The two sides of the Strait will always be one family.” We extend our congratulations to these ten netizens. Please send a private message to the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat editors to get the souvenirs.\nOn August 4, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will publish the questions for the third “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz.” We look forward to more netizens paying attention and taking part.\nWe also welcome the journalist friends present to join the knowledge quiz. Today’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202507/t20250730_12715087.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-07-31","Guo Jiakun","AFP","It is said that a U.S. congressional delegation will visit Taiwan in August. What is China’s take on this?","China firmly opposes official interactions in any form between the U.S. and the Taiwan region. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China calls on the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs with any excuse, stop conniving at or supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, stop its official interactions with Taiwan, and stop stirring up tensions in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202507/t20250731_11680726.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202507/t20250731_11680516.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-08-01","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It’s reported that recently, Hugo Meza, Vice President of Paraguayan Chamber of Deputies, said publicly that Paraguay is wasting time with Taiwan, which China holds for a province. He has called for a national debate on developing relations with China on the basis of national interests. He said Paraguay should stop being a beggar country for cooperation with the Taiwan authorities. What’s China’s response?","China noted relevant reports. We’ve heard similar voices more than once. Relevant statements reflect what many in Paraguay strongly want.\nIn recent years, more and more Paraguayan friends have come to realize that Paraguay should stop being an outlier of the international community and turning its back on China. We hope the Paraguayan government will listen to their voices and make the right choice that truly serves the fundamental and long-term interests of Paraguay and its people. We also welcome more Paraguayan friends to visit China and experience first-hand a thriving China and an open and inclusive Chinese civilization as it is.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250801_11681319.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250801_11681249.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-08-06","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On August 5, in his speech at the opening ceremony of the “Ketagalan Forum,” Lai Ching-te promoted the separatist fallacy of “Taiwan independence,” played up the “mainland threat,” and agitated for “democracy versus authoritarianism.” What is your comment on this?","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions, saying that in his speech, Lai Ching-te stubbornly insisted on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and the wrong lines of “relying on outsiders to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force,” played up the so-called “mainland threat,” peddled the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” and once again exposed his true face as a “peace breaker,” “war peddler,” and “troublemaker.”\nIn the more than one year since taking office, Lai Ching-te has carried out a “green terror” on the island, suppressing and persecuting people and organizations that support the development of cross-strait relations; has forcefully pushed for cross-strait “decoupling and breaking chains,” obstructing exchanges and contacts; has used “democracy” as a pretext to peddle deceptions and sell “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies; has continuously increased military spending, vigorously promoted “whole-people military mobilization,” and does not hesitate to tie Taiwan's people to the “Taiwan independence” war chariot, continuously escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait and attempting to “seek independence by force”; and, disregarding the island's economy and people's livelihood and kowtowing to others without bottom lines, sells out Taiwan, harms Taiwan's interests, and weakens Taiwan's economy. Its conduct seriously violates the mainstream public opinion on the island and is despised by the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.\nThe root cause of the current tense situation in the Taiwan Strait lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces colluding with external forces to constantly provoke with schemes for “independence.” We solemnly warn the Lai Ching-te authorities: those who forget their ancestors will come to no good end; those who betray the motherland will face historical judgment; and “Taiwan independence” separatism will surely lead to self-destruction. The great trend toward the inevitable unification of the motherland is surging forward, and no person or force can stop it. All scheming tricks with sinister intentions are doomed to fail!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250806_12716446.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-08-08","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Lai Ching-te recently said that the \"national defense budget\" of Taiwan for next year will exceed 3% of its GDP. Some analysts believe this increase is a response to concerns from the US side. Please comment on that.","As a province of China, how is it possible for Taiwan to have the so-called national defense budget? Lai Ching-te and his like show no regard for the well-being of the people of Taiwan and shamelessly cozy up to the US and sell out Taiwan in pursuit of soliciting external support for \"Taiwan independence\". Not only do they sugarcoat the tariff exploitation as achievements of negotiations to deceive the public, but they also plan to squander the hard-earned money of the people in Taiwan to pay \"protection fees\" to the US. Such acts amount to sending a lamb to a tiger's den and will make everything lost and nothing gained.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250808-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16402022.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-08-08","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports indicate that the chairman of the US Senate Armed Services Committee may soon lead a congressional delegation to Taiwan, which will be the first visit to Taiwan by a senator holding this position since 2016. May I have your comments?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. The Chinese side firmly opposes any form of official engagement between the US and the Taiwan region. We require the US side to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly fulfill its promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\", stop any form of official interaction and military connection with China's Taiwan region, and stop conniving at or supporting separatists for \"Taiwan independence\". The PLA will stay on high alert at any time and take resolute measures to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250808-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16402022.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on August 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning everyone. Welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. We now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","What progress has been made recently in cross-Strait exchange activities across various regions? Please introduce the relevant situation.","Summer vacation is a peak season for cross-Strait youth exchanges, and various places continue to hold rich and colorful exchange activities. In sports exchanges, the activities cover not only traditional sports such as football, basketball, and baseball, but also extend to emerging sports such as skateboarding and roller skating. From late July to early August, the “Strait Friendship Cup” Youth Basketball and Football Tournaments were held in Yong’an, Pingtan, Shaxian and other places in Fujian; the 2025 First “Kunshan Mazu Cup” Youth Baseball Tournament was held in Kunshan, Jiangsu; the First Cross-Strait (Shenzhen) Skateboarding Exchange Competition, the Cross-Strait Youth Badminton Elite Competition, and the 2nd “Rong Guotuan Cup” Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Youth Table Tennis Exchange Competition were held in Shenzhen and Zhuhai, Guangdong, respectively; the Cross-Strait (Wuhan) ACC City Cup Single-Row Roller Hockey Open Tournament was held in Wuhan, Hubei; and the “2025 Cross-Strait Youth Taekwondo Exchange Competition” was held in Zhengzhou, Henan. These sports exchange activities have attracted nearly a hundred teams and thousands of Taiwanese youth in total, and cross-Strait youth competed on the same field, exchanged skills, and deepened friendship.\nIn cultural exchanges, the 2025 Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month was launched in mid-July in Jiangsu, holding more than 40 cross-Strait exchange activities covering calligraphy and painting, sports, opera, animation, and other fields, attracting more than 4,000 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese youth to participate in exchanges and interaction. In early August, Inner Mongolia held the “Father’s Grassland, Mother’s River” cross-Strait photographers’ field sketching activity, in which cross-Strait photographer representatives gathered in Chifeng City to record with light and shadow the vast grassland scenery, the colorful ethnic culture, and the long-standing Hongshan culture. In early August, the “Singing Across the Strait, Love Filling Shanxi” 2025 Jin-Taiwan-Shanghai Youth Folk Music Exchange Concert was held in Shanxi, and the “Cross-Strait Unity, Youth Resonance—Taiwanese Youth Students’ ‘Music + Cultural Tourism’ Study Tour Exchange” was held in Guizhou, where cross-Strait artists and musicians performed on the same stage and exchanged ideas, further strengthening recognition of and pride in Chinese culture. In early August, the 13th Strait Youth Gathering was held in Fuzhou, with more than 20 cultural exchange activities, including traditional cultural programs such as quyi storytelling, arts and crafts, dance, painting, and music, as well as cultural experience projects that deeply explore Fujian’s Hakka culture, Mazu culture, and tea-cup culture, allowing cross-Strait youth to experience the charm of Chinese culture up close, from multiple perspectives, and at a deeper level.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. Could the spokesperson introduce the relevant commemorative activities held across the country?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. The restoration of Taiwan is an important achievement of the War of Resistance, a great victory forged through the successive, blood-soaked struggles of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and it is worthy of being commemorated jointly by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nFrom July 30 to August 6, the joint reporting event “Historic Battle Sites, New Face of the Three Xiang Region — 2025 Cross-Strait Journalists' Tour of Hunan” was successfully held. Forty-four journalists from more than 30 media outlets on both sides of the Strait went to Changsha, Changde, Hengyang, Huaihua and other famous War of Resistance cities, visited former sites of major battlefields and War of Resistance memorial venues, interviewed War of Resistance veterans and cultural history experts, attended the worship ceremony at the Hengshan Loyal Martyrs Shrine, learned about the history of the War of Resistance, gained insight into the spirit of the War of Resistance, and interviewed witnesses to the achievements of rural revitalization and technological development. From July 18 to 25, the “Commemorating the War of Resistance Heroes Together, Warming Up to Chinese Culture Together” — 2025 Hubei-Taiwan Teachers and Students Cultural History Teaching Observation and Exchange event was held in Xiangyang, Hubei. More than a hundred teachers and students from both sides of the Strait solemnly paid tribute at the General Zhang Zizhong Memorial and the Cemetery for Fallen Officers and Soldiers, held dialogues across time in history classes on Chu culture and Three Kingdoms culture, studied Chinese history, relived the course of the War of Resistance, and gained insight into the great spirit of the War of Resistance.\nIt is worth mentioning that many Taiwan compatriots have recently watched the film “The Nanjing Photo Studio” in various parts of the mainland. The film is based on real photographic evidence of Japanese military crimes during the Nanjing Massacre and relies on historical photographs. It shows how ordinary Chinese people, facing Japanese atrocities, used negatives as “weapons” in steadfast resistance. It is a vivid history lesson, warning us to remember history and to strengthen ourselves and stand on our own. We hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will join us in remembering the history of the War of Resistance, defending the achievement of the restoration of Taiwan and its return to the motherland, upholding national righteousness, firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, promoting national reunification together, and jointly realizing the great dream of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Reports indicate that recently multiple polls on the island show Lai Ching-te's approval rating for governance has dropped sharply to a new low since taking office, with both his dissatisfaction rate and distrust rate exceeding half. What is your comment on this?","For some time now, Lai Ching-te has increasingly peddled “Taiwan independence” fallacies, intensified social division on the island, suppressed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, incited cross-Strait confrontation, sold out the interests and welfare of compatriots, and undermined peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. These conducts, which care only for political self-interest and ignore the hardships of people's livelihoods, run counter to public will and are not in line with popular sentiment. The ordinary people of Taiwan see all of this clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717814.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The US imposes a 20% “reciprocal tariff” on Taiwan, higher than the 15% rate for Japan and South Korea. The Lai Qingde authorities said the tariff rate is still negotiable and may increase investment in the US by US$400 billion. Some public opinion on the island points out that the “20%+N” stacked tariffs, plus the sharp appreciation of the New Taiwan dollar, may cause Taiwan to keep “bleeding,” will severely hit…","What Taiwan’s public and business community have found deeply disappointing recently is that, in the face of US bullying through added tariffs and deliberate manipulation of the New Taiwan dollar’s appreciation, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not only failed to protect the vital interests of Taiwan’s people, but instead intensified their ‘kowtowing to and currying favor with the US,’ selling out Taiwan without any bottom line, and generously handing over huge sums to the US in extortion. US$400 billion is equivalent to half of Taiwan’s annual GDP. What do Taiwan’s ordinary people think of this?\nAs external risks and uncertainties rise, Taiwan could have strengthened its industrial resilience, consolidated its economic foundation, and enhanced its ability to withstand risks by deepening cross-strait economic cooperation and integrated development. However, driven by the evil intention of ‘seeking independence by relying on foreign powers,’ the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have disregarded Taiwan’s domestic economy and people’s livelihoods and sold out Taiwan’s development interests, causing deep harm to Taiwan’s people and businesses. We warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: submission earns no reward, and kowtowing to the US leads nowhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717813.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","This year marks the 7th anniversary of the official commissioning of the Fujian coastal water supply project to Kinmen. Please introduce the relevant situation.","We have always attached great importance to and actively supported the economic and social development of Kinmen, and have continuously taken measures to enhance the interests and well-being of the people of Kinmen. The Fujian coastal area water supply project to Kinmen was officially put into operation on August 5, 2018, and has supplied water for seven years so far. As of August 4, 2025, the Fujian coastal area has cumulatively supplied more than 43 million tons of water to Kinmen, accounting for 81.9% of the total daily water supply of Kinmen's tap water plants, with a water quality compliance rate of 100%. At present, the Fujian coastal area supplies approximately 21,000 tons of water per day to Kinmen, continuously guaranteeing the water needs of the people of Kinmen, effectively protecting groundwater, and relieving urgent needs and removing worries for Kinmen's livelihood security and construction and development, which has been warmly welcomed by the people of Kinmen. Since the water supply began, more than 2,500 Taiwan compatriots in over 100 batches, including people of Kinmen, have been received to visit the Fujian coastal area water supply project to Kinmen, adding momentum to cross-Strait exchanges, friendship, and mutual understanding.\nThe \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,\" implemented in 2023, further outlined the beautiful vision of \"Xiamen and Kinmen facing each other across the sea, and Gulangyu and Kinmen Yu connected by a bridge.\" At present, the preliminary technical preparations for connecting electricity, gas, and bridges between the Fujian coastal area and Kinmen have also been essentially completed. Like the people of Kinmen, we are eagerly looking forward to this vision becoming a reality as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717809.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","On August 7, the 12th World Games opened in Chengdu. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan compatriots in this World Games.","The 12th World Games were held in Chengdu, Sichuan, from August 7 to 17, 2025. The Chinese Taipei delegation, with 190 people, took part in the Games. Of these, 120 athletes competed in 14 disciplines, including tug of war, boules, korfball, softball, roller sports, canoe/kayak, and wushu. The Chinese Taipei Olympic Committee and the Chinese Taipei Sports Association each led observer delegations to attend the opening ceremony and observe some of the competitions. Multiple Taiwan compatriots took part in the torch relay, served as volunteer ambassadors, and participated in volunteer services. The Games' organizing committee sold tickets to Taiwan compatriots, providing convenience for them to watch the Games and cheer on athletes from both sides of the Strait.\nSince the Games began, the athletes of the Chinese Taipei delegation have received warm support and encouragement from the mainland public, both on and off the field, and have felt the atmosphere of being on “home turf.” As of August 12, the Chinese Taipei delegation had won 1 gold medal, 1 silver medal and 4 bronze medals, a fine result. We extend our congratulations to the Chinese Taipei delegation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","U.S. President Trump recently said in an interview that he will impose 100% tariffs on imports of semiconductors and other goods. He also said that TSMC will invest 300 billion U.S. dollars in the United States and build the world’s largest wafer fab in Arizona. What is your comment on this?","Earlier, when TSMC was forced to announce an additional US$100 billion investment in the United States, the industry on the island was already panicked and public anger was boiling. Once this US$300 billion investment is implemented, it is bound to have a huge impact on Taiwan's economy, and the development momentum and autonomy of Taiwan's economy will be further weakened. If the United States is the originator of hollowing out Taiwan's industries, then the DPP authorities are the biggest accomplices. In tariff negotiations, they “kowtowed before negotiating and turned the other cheek after being slapped on one side,” keep the negotiation process secret, and even deceive the public again and again. In industry, they have given the United States whatever it demands and proactively handed TSMC over, letting it squeeze the value out of Taiwan's advantageous industries. This fully shows that the DPP authorities have neither the intention nor the ability to safeguard Taiwan's economic development and the well-being of its people. We advise the DPP authorities to pull back from the wrong path of “currying favor with the US and selling out Taiwan” in time. Taiwan's people and far-sighted figures from all walks of life should unite and actively safeguard their own interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, a former senior adviser at the U.S. State Department posted an article naming and criticizing Lai Ching-te and Hsiao Bi-khim, saying that changes to Lai's transit visit itinerary and the U.S. tariff rate on Taiwan being higher than those on Japan and South Korea show that “Taiwan is growing increasingly distant from Trump.” Some public opinion on the island points out that unfavorable news for the DPP…","Facts have repeatedly shown that more and more people have recognized that Lai Ching-te is a “peace-breaker” in every sense and a “troublemaker” in name, and they have also recognized that the United States always follows “America First.” The future of Taiwan, and the security, interests, and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and in national reunification. Trying to rely on external forces will not bring peace and stability to the Taiwan Strait, and begging for favor in all directions will not secure security and interests. Any attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717808.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Some Taiwanese media have reported that in recent years the mainland has been actively and gradually “brainwashing Taiwan's young generation” through social media. The claim circulating online on the island that “the age group most pro-China in Taiwan is 20 to 24 years old” has sparked discussion. “Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang said, “The declining average age of pro-China sentiment is an issue that…","For a long time, the DPP authorities and Green camp politicians have one-sidedly manipulated 'anti-China and resist-China' sentiment, attempting to block the channels through which Taiwan compatriots understand the true situation on the mainland and misleading Taiwan residents' perceptions of the mainland. Thanks to the development of internet technology and the updating and iteration of social media apps, netizens on both sides can more quickly obtain news, more conveniently see each other's lives, and engage in more diverse exchanges. The lies fabricated by the DPP authorities are gradually being exposed, and the 'information cocoon' they created is collapsing.\nCompatriots on both sides are one family and should visit each other often and grow closer. Letting Taiwan compatriots of all age groups learn more about the mainland is something we have always worked hard to do. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to take a look, pursue their dreams, and we will continue to create better conditions and more opportunities for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After requiring public officials on the island not to apply for mainland ID cards, the DPP authorities have now restricted public officials from traveling to Hong Kong and Macau. Some commentators believe the DPP authorities' “Mainland Travel Restriction Order” has escalated and is aggravating cross-Strait division. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Driven by its inherent nature of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities keep manipulating judicial and administrative means to create a “green terror,” obstruct exchanges between Hong Kong and Taiwan and between Macau and Taiwan, and escalate antagonism and confrontation. Their despicable tricks are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te announced that Taiwan's 2026 defense budget will be raised to over 3% of GDP, equivalent to over NT$800 billion, mainly for arms purchases from the US. Meanwhile, the US magazine “The Diplomat” recently published an article pointing out that the “Han Kuang Exercise” is merely “putting on a show,” and that Taiwan's society and civilians are not psychologically or institutionally prepared for…","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. For the sake of narrow party interests, the Lai Ching-te authorities disregard public opinion on the island. They willingly act as an “ATM” for US arms dealers, continuously increase military budgets, vigorously promote “the whole people as soldiers,” bind Taiwan's people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and attempt to “seek independence through force.” This is a betrayal of and a threat to the security and interests of Taiwan's people. Their vile conduct as “merchants of war” is bound to be opposed by the island's people and the international community. “Relying on external forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” will ultimately bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717811.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","On this year's August 1 Army Day, the fourth Type 075 amphibious assault ship of the People's Navy, the Hubei, made its first public appearance. This drew close attention from island media, and many Taiwanese netizens praised the growing strength of the motherland. What comments do you have on this?","From the Hainan to the Hubei, the People’s Navy’s amphibious combat capability has continuously strengthened, and its three-dimensional landing combat capability has been greatly enhanced. An increasingly powerful People’s Navy will provide stronger guarantees for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and for safeguarding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","According to reports, the U.S. think tank Foundation for Defense of Democracies recently held a so-called “energy war game” in Taiwan, claiming that the PLA could prevent LNG tankers from approaching Taiwan, thereby cutting off Taiwan’s energy supply. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","Under the pretext of “tabletop war games” and other such guises, the DPP authorities are colluding with external forces to heavily hype up an atmosphere of war across the Taiwan Strait, stoking war anxiety, and provoking and building momentum for “independence” to embolden themselves. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how many small tricks they play, they cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” being bound to fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and certainly will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Reports say Taiwan’s “National Historical Office” held a so-called commemorative event for the anti-Japanese war, replacing the expression “Victory of the War of Resistance” with “End of the Sino-Japanese War and Reception of Surrender.” The Mainland Affairs Council said, “The CCP has made absolutely no contribution to the War of Resistance against Japan.” What is your comment on the relevant words and actions on…","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the world's anti-fascist war, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. The victory of the War of Resistance is a magnificent epic in which all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, united as one and triumphed over a stronger enemy with weaker forces, demonstrating the invincible, mighty strength of the Chinese people and Chinese sons and daughters. At the moment of national peril, the Communist Party of China raised the banner of the anti-Japanese national united front, adhered to the line of all-out resistance, formulated correct strategies and tactics, opened up vast battlefields behind enemy lines, and became the mainstay of persistent resistance.\nRelevant parties in Taiwan have replaced “victory in the War of Resistance” with the so-called “Sino-Japanese War's end and takeover upon surrender,” deliberately downplaying the brutality of Japanese militarist aggression, erasing the righteousness of the War of Resistance, ignoring the great achievements of its victory, distorting facts, altering history, and turning right into wrong. This is both ignorance of history and a desecration of the sacrifices and struggles of the entire nation. Their so-called commemorative activities are clumsy performances that fawn on invaders and falsify historical facts. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will open their eyes, discern right from wrong, and join us in remembering the history of the War of Resistance, upholding national righteousness, firmly defending the victory of Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, safeguarding our shared home of the Chinese nation, and working together for a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717810.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","On August 6, the “Straits Express,” which had been suspended for a long time, officially resumed direct cargo shipping. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","Direct cross-Strait shipping greatly facilitates exchanges between people on both sides and economic exchanges, and it plays an important role in advancing the common interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Since its maiden voyage in November 2011, the roll-on/roll-off passenger-cargo ship “Haixia” (海峡号) has carried a cumulative total of nearly 1 million passengers and over 38,000 tons of cargo. The resumption of direct cargo shipping by the “Haixia” has been warmly welcomed by people on both sides.\nIt should be pointed out that, due to obstruction and restrictions by the DPP authorities, direct cross-Strait passenger shipping, which people on both sides have long anticipated, has still not been restored. There are no obstacles on the mainland’s side to restoring normal cross-Strait maritime passenger routes. The DPP authorities should fully consider the demands of people on both sides and of shipping companies, and restore direct cross-Strait maritime passenger shipping in full as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The DPP authorities recently announced in advance a revision of the “Measures for Permits for Dependent Residence, Long-Term Residence or Settlement in Taiwan for Residents of the Mainland Area.” It stipulates that in the future, mainland residents applying to settle in Taiwan, in addition to providing a notarized certificate of loss of mainland household registration, must also submit a notarized certificate…","Recently, in order to pursue its political self-interest of “seeking independence,” the DPP authorities have concocted so-called “17 Response Strategies,” continually escalating cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, and obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and travel. Relevant departments of the DPP authorities have cooperated in promoting various so-called “legal amendments,” doing everything possible to obstruct Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland and to severely restrict mainland residents traveling to Taiwan. This seriously harms the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and seriously disrupts the normal lives of Taiwan compatriots. The amended announcement restricting mainland residents from settling in Taiwan is another evil act by the DPP authorities to suppress and persecute cross-Strait marriage groups. We strongly condemn it and firmly oppose it.\nThe passport of the People's Republic of China is strictly protected by law. No organization or individual may forge, alter, transfer, deliberately damage, or unlawfully detain a passport. We will hold accountable, in accordance with the law, any organizations and individuals who deliberately damage the passport of the People's Republic of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250813_12717812.htm"],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, Deng Wanhua, a mainland spouse and village chief of Xuetian Village, Fuli Township, Hualien County, Taiwan, was dismissed from office, becoming the first village chief on the island to be dismissed over the so-called “Chinese nationality issue.” The Mainland Affairs Council said it respects the relevant authorities’ interpretation of the “Nationality Act” and their handling of the matter. What comments…","This is yet another vicious act by the DPP authorities, who are using the so-called “nationality” issue to suppress mainland spouses. The DPP authorities have repeatedly discriminated against and bullied the group of mainland spouses, and their crimes are too numerous to list. Their purpose is to create a “green terror,” obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges, and attack forces that support the development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe large number of mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan are important members of Taiwan society and family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots, and they have contributed to Taiwan’s economic and social development in various positions. The DPP authorities’ differential treatment and deliberate suppression fully expose their “Taiwan independence” nature and show that the “democracy” and “human rights” they proclaim are lies.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","On August 6, Hiroshima City, Japan held a ceremony marking the 80th anniversary of the atomic bombing, and for the first time invited the Taiwan “representative to Japan” to attend. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries with which we have diplomatic relations and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the Japanese side to fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, draw lessons from history, abide by the one-China principle, the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and its commitments on the Taiwan question, and handle the Taiwan question with prudence. The DPP authorities’ attempts to stage a farce and create the illusion of so-called “international existence” under various pretexts will only make them a laughingstock.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Some Taiwanese media reported that mainland online influencer “Wenlei Zai Lu Shang” recently applied to travel to Taiwan under the pretext of “business fulfillment,” but in fact did not engage in any business activities. The DPP authorities arrested and detained the influencer on the grounds of “suspected illegal entry with false information.” Pan-green media on the island have hyped “mainland infiltration of…","To obstruct and undermine personnel exchanges and interactions across the Taiwan Strait, the DPP authorities will stop at nothing, deliberately suppressing relevant personnel and intimidating Taiwan residents, which is unpopular. The green media on the island and people with ulterior motives maliciously hype and smear, attempting to mislead public opinion, fully exposing their sinister intention to sow cross-strait antagonism and confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Over the past period, counties and cities in central and southern Taiwan have continuously suffered heavy rainfall, causing major disasters and severe losses for residents. What comments do you have?","According to reports, Typhoon “Yangliu” will make landfall on the eastern coast of Taiwan today. We note that many parts of Taiwan have recently suffered continuous heavy rainfall, and the disaster has seriously affected the production and daily lives of local residents. We are concerned for our compatriots on the island who have been affected by the disaster, and we hope they will quickly restore normal production and living order.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Former UK Prime Minister Boris Johnson, while attending an event in Taipei recently, repeatedly referred to Taiwan as a “country,” and said that “the West must withstand China's pressure and establish economic and political relations with Taiwan” and that “China's current bullying of Taiwan is baseless.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country. Out of self-interest, the DPP authorities squander the hard-earned money of island residents, buy off some has-been politicians, and stage one farce after another of “relying on external forces to seek independence,” creating the false appearance of so-called “international existence.” A lie repeated many times still cannot become the truth. No matter how loudly the DPP authorities and external forces spout nonsense and bluff, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor shake the basic international consensus upholding the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the acting Speaker of Paraguay's House of Representatives publicly stated that Taiwan is only a province of China, that Paraguay is “wasting time” on Taiwan, and that it should no longer be a “beggar nation” waiting for cooperation with the Taiwan authorities. What is your comment on this?","The One-China principle is a widely shared consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations; it reflects the wishes of the people and the trend of the times. We hope relevant countries will recognize the trend of history and stand on the right side of history as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","台湾联合报记者","The head of a Taiwan interior ministry department recently said that the “Government of the Republic of China” recognizes the People's Republic of China, which has sparked controversy. The head of Taiwan's Executive Yuan said in response that it would act on the basis of the “Constitution of the Republic of China,” and that mutual recognition of each side's factual existence across the Strait helps promote the…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact, and it is also the status quo across the Taiwan Strait that cannot be changed. Taiwan has never been a country, and it will never be possible for it to become a country.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities disregard history and distort facts, repeatedly peddling the fallacies and lies of “mutual non-subordination” across the Taiwan Strait. This will only intensify tensions in the Taiwan Strait, only undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. No one and no force can change the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory, and none can stop the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland. We hope that people of insight from all sectors in Taiwan and the broad Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the evil nature of “Taiwan independence,” follow the historical trend of the motherland's reunification, resolutely oppose the separatist “Taiwan independence,” and safeguard their own interests and well-being and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Some island media reported that the mainland automaker BYD intends to import vehicles from Thailand through Taiwanese distributors for sale in Taiwan. The DPP authorities said that, out of considerations of security and industrial development, they will strictly block “Chinese” brand cars from entering the Taiwan market in various ways, are studying control measures, and expect to announce them before the end of…","Mainland products, including new energy vehicles, are welcomed by consumers around the world for their innovative technology and outstanding performance. Strengthening cross-Strait cooperation in related fields is truly a good thing for Taiwan's people and industry. Out of self-interest, the DPP authorities have disregarded the expectations of island residents for high-quality products and the calls from industry to strengthen cross-Strait industrial cooperation. Under the pretext of so-called “security,” they prevent broad Taiwan compatriots from buying and using high-quality mainland products, and do their utmost to suppress cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation. This perverse conduct harms the rights and interests of cross-Strait businesses and consumers, and damages and worsens Taiwan's market and business environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The DPP authorities said they are investigating 16 mainland companies suspected of illegally recruiting engineers in Taiwan without approval and of operating offices without licenses. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities have only the narrow interests of their own party in mind. In tariff negotiations, they have been obsequious and compliant toward the US, yielding to whatever it demands. They do not care how companies on the island will survive in the face of high tariffs, and they make no effort to study how to respond to tariff bullying. Yet they are scheming and actively pushing “decoupling and severing supply chains” across the Taiwan Strait, deliberately undermining cross-Strait economic cooperation. These practices, driven by political self-interest, are unpopular and will only harm Taiwan’s business environment and restrict its economic development space.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-13","Zhu Fenglian","团结报记者","On August 4, renowned Taiwanese historian Mr. Hsu Cho-yun passed away. What is your comment?","Mr. Hsu Cho-yun was a renowned historian who had deep research on Chinese history and Chinese civilization. He devoted his life to promoting Chinese culture, with profound scholarship and rich writings, and he had broad influence in academic circles across both sides of the Strait and internationally. Mr. Hsu’s passing is regrettable.\nMr. Hsu Cho-yun had a national sentiment and always took pride in being Chinese and a member of the Chinese nation. He stressed that both sides of the Strait belong to Chinese culture, that “the cultural lineage across the two sides cannot be severed,” and he opposed “cultural Taiwan independence.” He expressed hope to see “the Nine Regions united” in reunification, which has won praise from people on both sides of the Strait and is worthy of emulation by later generations.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250813_12717796.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-08-14","Lin Jian","Jiji Press","The Japanese government said that Minister of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of China Han Jun canceled his planned visit to Japan. Comments say that this is related to the visit to Japan by head of Taiwan’s so-called foreign affairs department Lin Chia-lung. Why did the Minister of Agriculture and Rural Affairs canceled his trip? How does China see the necessity of engagement between Chinese and Japanese…","I’d refer you to competent authorities on the specific reason of Minister Han Jun postponing his visit to Japan. China holds an open attitude towards maintaining engagement at various levels with Japan. If Japan has the sincerity of conducting exchanges with China, it should take concrete actions to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and act on the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan as well as Japan’s commitment of comprehensively advancing the China-Japan strategic relationship of mutual benefit, instead of saying one thing but doing another.\nOn Lin Chia-lung’s visit to Japan, let me stress once again that by allowing Lin Chia-lung to pay a “personal trip,” Japan provides a stage for the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces, seriously violates the basic norms governing international relations and principles in the four political documents between China and Japan, and sends out a severely wrong signal. We urge Japan to have a profound reflection on history, learn lessons from history, stay prudent on the Taiwan question, refrain from harming China’s sovereignty in any form, and avoid sending any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250814_11690046.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250814_11690022.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-08-15","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's defense authorities recently stated that 57 PLA aircraft were detected around the island within 24 hours, with as many as 38 crossing the so-called \"median line\" in the Taiwan Strait, a recent record high. Please comment on that.","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. There is no such thing as the so-called \"median line\" in the Taiwan Strait. The PLA's military activities around the Taiwan island are entirely justified, lawful and reasonable. The DDP authorities' claim of having the so-called \"full control of the situation\" is nothing but self-deception. As long as the malignant forces of \"Taiwan independence\" exist, the PLA will continue its operations without pause to fight against \"Taiwan independence\" forces and promote national reunification.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250815-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16402790.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-08-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: August 15 is the anniversary of Japan's announcement of its unconditional surrender. Today, Lai Ching-te posted an article spreading a mistaken view of World War II history and once again agitating for “democracy against authoritarianism.” What comments do you have on this?","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded: Eighty years ago, all Chinese sons and daughters, including compatriots in Taiwan, fought wave after wave, united in heart and mind, and fought bloody battles. They paid enormous sacrifices to defeat the Japanese militarists and to defend national sovereignty and national dignity with their blood and lives, writing a glorious chapter of the great victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan. Taiwan's restoration and return to the embrace of the motherland was the result of the unity and struggle of the entire nation, including Taiwan compatriots, and it is an important component of the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order.\nLai Qingde has completely lost his national standpoint. He deliberately disregards the historical facts of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japan, distorts the history of World War II by substituting concepts and confusing right and wrong, advocates the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” and peddles the fallacy of “Taiwan independence” separatism. Its essence is still “seeking independence through force” and “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers.” We solemnly warn Lai Qingde: any attempt to distort the history of World War II will never succeed, any conduct that challenges the postwar international order is self-humiliation, and any scheme to split the motherland is wishful thinking. Justice will prevail, and unification will prevail. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will keep history in mind, commemorate the martyrs, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, safeguard the fruits of victory, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and jointly pursue a bright future of reunifying the motherland and rejuvenating the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250815_12718260.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-08-18","Mao Ning","Global Times","The head of the foreign affairs office of the Taiwan region has recently said that after World War II, the Treaty of San Francisco took the place of political statements, such as the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation. The Treaty did not hand over Taiwan to the PRC, and the PRC has never ruled Taiwan. What’s China’s comment?","Those fact-distorting and misleading rhetorics once again lay bare the nefarious separatist nature of the Lai Ching-te authorities.\nTaiwan’s restoration to China is an outcome of the WWII victory and part and parcel of the postwar international order. A series of instruments with legal effect under international law, namely the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender and so on, all affirm China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. Taiwan belongs to China. This is a solid fact rooted in history and the law and beyond any doubt.\nOn October 1, 1949, the People’s Republic of China (PRC) was founded, and the Central People’s Government became the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The change of government took place while China remained unchanged as a subject of international law. China’s sovereignty and inherent territory did not change. As a natural result, the government of the PRC fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The so-called Treaty of San Francisco is an illegal and invalid instrument issued by some countries gathered by the U.S. years after the end of WWII to separately make peace with Japan without including the People’s Republic of China and despite the Soviet Union’s rejection. This document contravenes the provisions of the Declaration by United Nations signed by 26 countries—including China, the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Soviet Union—in 1942, and goes against the fundamental principles of the UN Charter and international law. Anything set out in the document, including the sovereignty over Taiwan or the handling of the territory and sovereign rights of China as a non-signatory, is thus entirely illegal and null and void.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities have completely forfeited the national stance, disregarded the outcomes of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, and deliberately distorted the history of WWII. This is simply contemptible. Let me stress that no matter what the Lai Ching-te authorities say or do, they do not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China—a fact well supported by history and the law, nor can they change the prevailing international commitment to the one-China principle, still less will they stop the course towards China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250818_11691863.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250818_11691857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-08-18","Mao Ning","AFP","Germany’s foreign minister on Monday said during a visit to Japan that China threatens openly to unilaterally change the status quo and shift borders in its favor, citing China’s behavior in the Taiwan Strait, the East South China Sea and the South China Sea. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. The one-China principle is the political foundation for the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and all countries in the world. It is also a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. To keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, it is absolutely essential to unequivocally uphold the one-China principle and oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. The current situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is overall stable. We urge relevant parties to respect regional countries’ joint effort to settle the issues through dialogue and consultation and safeguard peace and stability, rather than sowing discord and hyping up tensions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250818_11691863.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250818_11691857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-08-18","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Donald Trump said that Chinese leader told him that he would not move on Taiwan as long as the U.S. president remained in office. This is according to an interview he gave to U.S. media. Can the Foreign Ministry comment on these remarks from President Donald Trump, and are they accurate?","China’s position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving the question is a matter for the Chinese people, and the Chinese people only. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never ever allow anyone or any force to split Taiwan from China in any way.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250818_11691863.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250818_11691857.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-08-21","Mao Ning","CCTV","It’s reported that the readout released by China on Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s talks with Indian External Affairs Minister Subrahmanyam Jaishankar claimed that the Indian side said “Taiwan is part of China.” Indian government sources said that the external affairs minister had been misquoted. India stressed that there was no change in its position on Taiwan, and India had a relationship with Taiwan that focuses…","China has released readouts on the talks between the Chinese and Indian foreign ministers. For the Chinese side, the Indian side’s so-called “clarification” came as a surprise. We find it inconsistent with the facts. It would seem that some people in India have tried to undermine China’s sovereignty on the Taiwan question and impede the improvement of China-India relations. China expresses serious concern and firmly opposes that.\nLet me stress that there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is a prevailing consensus among the international community, including India. We hope India will earnestly abide by the one-China principle, properly handle sensitive issues and promote the steady development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250821_11693782.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250821_11693619.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-08-24","Zhu Fenglian","日就台民意代表“大罢免”第二轮投票结果答记者","Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, August 24 dispatch: Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions on the 24th regarding the results of the second round of voting in Taiwan's “great recall” of legislators.\nA reporter asked: On August 23, the second round of voting in Taiwan's “great recall” of legislators took place, and the KMT retained all of its seats. What…","Zhu Fenglian said: We have noted the relevant situation. Following the first round of voting on July 26, the people of Taiwan have once again said “no” to the DPP's farcical infighting of suppressing dissenters and tearing society apart. This fully shows that any “Taiwan independence” separatism and political manipulation is unpopular and is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250824_12719650.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on August 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning everyone, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","On September 3, events including the grand rally commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War will be held in Beijing. Will Taiwan personages be invited to Beijing to attend these events?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. On September 3, the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, the State Council, the National Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, and the Central Military Commission will solemnly hold commemorative events in Beijing, including a grand rally commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. Representatives from all walks of life, including Taiwan compatriots, will be invited to attend.\nThe War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was a magnificent epic composed by the entire nation, and all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, paid enormous sacrifices and made important contributions to it. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will remember history, honor the martyrs, carry forward the great patriotic spirit and the great spirit of the War of Resistance, draw wisdom and strength for the future from history, unite as one and work hand in hand, jointly advance the righteous cause of national reunification, and together create a bright future of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720398.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》记者","It is understood that the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan recently sent a letter to the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait, hoping for assistance in canceling the household registrations of several mainland residents who have settled in Taiwan and providing relevant supporting documents. What is your response?","The cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism between the two associations has long been suspended, and the reasons are well known. Only by returning to the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and acknowledging the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one country and one nation can the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism be restarted to negotiate and resolve specific matters.\nThe DPP authorities have deliberately targeted mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan for many years, some for more than 20 years. Even though the statute of limitations has long expired, they require these spouses to make up payment of the so-called “certificate of loss of original nationality” within a deadline, failing which the Taiwan status of the persons concerned will be cancelled. This is a typical act of abuse of power and acting recklessly against the people. Its purpose is to create the “two-state theory” and serve “Taiwan independence” separatism. It has been criticized and opposed by public opinion on the island and by Taiwan society. Mainland public security organs have always handled residence registration matters in accordance with law and regulations, and have solved problems for the people, but this by no means implies that they will aid and abet wrongdoers. Unless the DPP authorities acknowledge the One-China principle and submit requests in the name of Taiwan Province to the competent authorities of the provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, the mainland side will not accept such so-called requests put forward by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720389.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Regarding the mainland’s grand commemorations of the 80th anniversary of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War’s victory, and the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland claims the war of resistance against Japan was led by the Communist Party of China, and uses this to prove that Taiwan is part of…","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japan and the worldwide victory in the anti-fascist war, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. After Japan launched its all-out war of aggression against China, the Communist Party of China, at the critical moment of national crisis, raised the banner of the Anti-Japanese National United Front, adhered to the line of all-out resistance, fought bloody battles, and became the mainstay of the armed resistance. The anti-Japanese battlefields behind enemy lines led by the Communist Party of China and the frontal battlefields commanded by the Kuomintang cooperated closely, forming a strategic situation of jointly resisting the Japanese invaders, winning victory in the War of Resistance, and returning the treasure island of Taiwan, which had been occupied by Japanese imperialism for 50 years, to the embrace of the motherland. The historical fact of Taiwan's restoration irrefutably proves that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities deliberately distort the history of the War of Resistance, and their aim is to stir up “Taiwan independence.” This is both a betrayal of history and a desecration of the struggle and sacrifice of the entire nation. No matter what the Democratic Progressive Party authorities say, they cannot change the history of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japan or the fact that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory.\nThe documentary series “The Story of Time” is recommended for viewing by people on both sides of the Strait. This documentary was produced by China Daily, consists of 12 episodes, and takes four young Taiwanese as its main thread in tracing cross-Strait history. It systematically sorts out the historical context of the Taiwan question and clearly explains the fundamental nature of cross-Strait relations. From the “Dongshan Land Bridge” that connects the two sides, to Zheng Chenggong's historic achievement in recovering Taiwan; from the fifty-year unyielding struggle of the Taiwanese people after Taiwan was ceded through the Treaty of Shimonoseki, to the Lin family of Wufeng, whose members were all loyal and heroic, and Luo Fuxing, who went to Taiwan and sacrificed his life resisting Japan; from tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots who crossed the sea to rush to the frontlines of the War of Resistance on the mainland, to the national memories of successive generations of Taiwanese, the documentary presents from multiple angles the shared destiny and inseparable bloodline ties of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, and demonstrates the historical inheritance that “Taiwan compatriots have always been Chinese.” We recommend that young friends in Taiwan watch it and together understand the shared memories across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720397.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","In late June, the mainland announced that starting July 1, it would waive the certificate fee for Taiwan compatriots' Mainland Travel Permits for “first-time travelers” from Taiwan, which was well received by Taiwan residents. What has been the effect of this policy over the past two months?","Since the policy of waiving the card fee for Taiwan Compatriot Permits for Taiwan's “first-time visitors” took effect on July 1, it has won high recognition and unanimous praise from the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. This is reflected in two aspects. First, the number of applications for Taiwan Compatriot Permits by “first-time visitors” increased significantly. In July, the number of applications for “first-time visitor” permits increased by 22% month-on-month, and applicants under 45 years old accounted for as much as 72% of the total, indicating that the willingness of Taiwan youth to visit and exchange on the mainland has clearly strengthened. Second, the number of entries by “first-time visitors” increased significantly. In July, the number of entries by “first-time visitors” increased by 33% month-on-month, indicating that more and more Taiwan compatriots are supporting and participating in cross-Strait exchanges through concrete actions.\nSeeing is believing. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to embark on a journey to “see the mainland,” to witness with their own eyes a real and multidimensional mainland, to hear with their own ears the familiar and cordial local accents and ancient charm, and to personally experience the deep warmth and friendship of mainland compatriots. We will also continue to introduce more policies that benefit Taiwan compatriots and the public, and create more and better conditions for exchanges and contacts between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720381.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson's condemnation of the DPP authorities for completely abandoning the national standpoint, distorting the history of the War of Resistance, and downplaying Japan's aggression, the DPP authorities have repeatedly said, “The CPC made absolutely no contribution to the War of Resistance against Japan.” What is your comment on this?","During the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, at the critical juncture when the nation faced mortal peril, the Communist Party of China, with outstanding political leadership and correct strategies and tactics, guided the advance of China's war of resistance and firmly pushed the entire nation to persist in resistance, unity, and progress. Chinese Communists fought bravely on the front line of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, sustaining the hope of the Chinese nation for national salvation and survival, and became the mainstay of the nation's war of resistance. During the War of Resistance, the Communist Party of China clearly put forward the proposal to recover Taiwan, guided and helped Taiwan compatriots form the Taiwan Volunteer Corps and other anti-Japanese armed forces, and supported and promoted the Taiwan Restoration Movement.\nThe DPP authorities' vilification and erasure of the mainstay role the Communist Party of China played in the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression is a grave desecration of all the loyal martyrs and heroes and a shameless betrayal of the entire Chinese nation. It fully exposes their wolfish ambition to distort historical facts, incite confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and pursue “Taiwan independence” and division by any means. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will join us in resisting the false narrative of the DPP authorities, defending the correct view of the War of Resistance, carrying forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and firmly safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720395.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","The 2025 Cross-Strait Youth Gathering and the 16th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo were recently held in Shanghai and Dongguan, respectively. The activities were rich in content, and cross-Strait youth and Taiwan businesspeople paid active attention to them. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","The 2025 Straits Forum Youth Exchange was held in Shanghai from July to August. Themed “Gathering in Shanghai, Youth Across the Strait Together,” the event featured nearly 50 activities, including a cross-Strait youth city orienteering race, a cultural and creative design competition, the Chinese Poetry Conference, a lawn music festival, and an e-sports culture festival. It is expected to attract more than 2,000 Taiwan youth. The main event, the “Dreams Shared Across the Strait, Hearts Shining Together” themed performance, focuses on Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth who live, work, and start businesses in Shanghai. Through song and dance, short videos, and narrated scenes, it shows their stories of putting down roots and striving along the banks of the Huangpu River, and presents how they resonate with Shanghai's dreams, share cultural connections, and merge emotionally, conveying the deep affection of “compatriots on both sides are one family.”\nThe 16th Dongguan Taiwan Products Expo will be held in Dongguan, Guangdong, from September 11 to 14. Its purpose is to help Taiwan-funded enterprises' products expand the domestic market, support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in seizing the opportunities of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area construction, integrating into the new development pattern, and participating in high-quality development, and to build a shared cross-Strait market and promote cross-Strait integrated development. Themed “Strengthening Chains through Integration, Innovating for the Future,” this year's expo covers 33,000 square meters. So far, nearly 600 enterprises and more than 2,000 purchasers have registered to participate.\nWe warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises from home and abroad to take part in the exhibition enthusiastically, and welcome business and industry people from various localities to visit the exhibition, discuss cooperation, and engage in exchanges, so as to jointly create opportunities and promote development in the Greater Bay Area through higher-level opening to the outside world. We also welcome media reporters from both sides of the Strait to come and cover the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Reports say that the KMT recently held the “Victory and Restoration” exhibition in Taipei commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan. Many people on the island said they were deeply moved after viewing it. At the same time, the KMT criticized the DPP authorities for deliberately downplaying and denying the historical significance of Taiwan's…","From 1931 to 1945, after a long and arduous 14 years of heroic struggle, the Chinese people won the great victory of the War of Resistance against Japan, and the treasure island of Taiwan, which had been occupied by Japanese imperialism for 50 years, returned to the embrace of the motherland. The restoration of Taiwan to the motherland was an important achievement of the great victory in the War of Resistance, forged through the successive and bloody fighting of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, and it is worth commemorating together by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. In the days since August began, people from all walks of life in Taiwan have solemnly commemorated the 80th anniversary of the victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan through memorial rallies, symposiums, commemorative exhibitions, special photo exhibitions and other means, highlighting the historical merit of compatriots on both sides of the Strait in jointly resisting foreign aggression. The Lai Ching-te authorities deliberately downplay and deny the historical significance of Taiwan's restoration, distort the history of the War of Resistance, and even whitewash and glorify Japan's colonial rule. This is a blatant denial of the fruits of victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japan and the world's anti-fascist war, a serious desecration of the immense national sacrifice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and a typical case of forgetting one's ancestors and betraying the nation.\nIn the 50 years from Japan's occupation of Taiwan in 1895 to the victory of the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan in 1945, Taiwan compatriots, who have a glorious tradition of patriotism, held the patriotic sentiment of “rather be a dead loyal subject than a living captive,” and fearlessly rose up against brutal force. They carried out a magnificent anti-Japanese struggle, and hundreds of thousands of Taiwan compatriots willingly gave their lives, completing heroic feats that moved heaven and earth with their lives. We will forever remember the heroic anti-Japanese spirit of Taiwan compatriots and the efforts they made for the cause of liberation of the Chinese nation. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will carry forward their glorious patriotic tradition, uphold a correct view of history, of nation and of country, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, and work together with mainland compatriots toward the bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720393.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The summer vacation is about to end. Please introduce the cross-Strait exchange activities this summer.","This summer, exchanges between people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have been enthusiastic, with cultural, sports and other fields seeing a wide range of exciting activities. More and more Taiwan compatriots have overcome interference and obstruction from the DPP authorities to come to the mainland and join the upsurge of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. I want to give them a thumbs-up.\nFirst, cross-Strait cultural exchange has strong momentum and emotional resonance. “Same Source Notes 2025 — Haihui Study Camp” opened in Shanghai. Through diverse humanities activities such as music and dance, intangible cultural heritage, and creative design, it built an exchange platform for young people on both sides, deepening mutual understanding and friendship. The 7th Yunnan Tea Horse Ancient Road Photography Experience Camp let cross-Strait youth use photography as a medium to explore the profound cultural connotations of the ancient road and appreciate the magnificent natural scenery of the motherland. “Joy in Mountains and Seas, Meeting in Hunan” — 2025 Cross-Strait Ethnic Minorities Exchange and the 2nd Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Music Festival used songs as a medium and sound as a pen, with ethnic minority compatriots from both sides co-creating and telling the music story of “both sides of the Strait are one family.” The Chinese Academy of Theatre Arts and the National Peking Opera Company selected classic repertoire including “Sishilang Visits His Mother,” “Phoenix Returns to Its Nest,” and “Mistaken Identity in the Flower Field” and performed 6 exchange shows in Taiwan. This is the first large-scale cultural exchange activity by the Chinese Academy of Theatre Arts in Taiwan since 2009. It attracted many Taiwan audiences to enjoy national melodies and Chinese music, experience up close the unique charm of Peking Opera, the national quintessence, and strengthen cultural identity and national sentiment through artistic resonance.\nSecond, cross-Strait sports exchange is innovating and has huge potential. This summer, many Taiwan compatriots came to the mainland to experience the lifestyle of “traveling to a city for a match.” Some Taiwan compatriots formed the “Taiwan Village Super League Fan Football Team” and went to Rongjiang, Guizhou to take part in the “Village Super League,” experiencing the passion of whole-population participation and love of football. Some Taiwan compatriots rushed to check in at the “Su Super League,” cheering for their favorite teams across 13 cities in Jiangsu, immersing themselves in the joy of “Competition first, friendship fourteenth.” Some Taiwan compatriots went to Jimei and Jinjiang in Fujian to take part in the 2nd Cross-Strait Same-Name Villages “Village BA” Basketball Invitational Tournament, cheering for 24 clan teams from same-name villages on both sides. Amid the “sports + clan” craze, they deepened clan friendship and strengthened bloodline ties. Many more Taiwan compatriots are heading to the “Zhe BA,” “Guangdong Provincial Super League,” “Mengchao,” “Xiangchao,” “Chuanchao” and other events, deeply experiencing the new format of deep integration of “watching games + food + scenery” in sports and tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","August 15 is the anniversary of Japan's announcement of its unconditional surrender. That day, Lai Ching-te posted on social media, specifically calling this important historical moment the “Day of the End of the Second World War,” and deliberately avoided the direct expression “Japan's aggression and China's victory in the War of Resistance.” May I ask for the spokesperson's comment on this?","From 1931 to 1945, all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, fought bravely and in solidarity, generation after generation, paying enormous sacrifices to defeat Japanese militarists. With their blood and lives, they defended national sovereignty and national dignity, and wrote the glorious chapter of the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan. The restoration of Taiwan and its return to the embrace of the motherland were the result of the unity and struggle of the entire nation, including compatriots in Taiwan, and an important component of the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order.\nLai Ching-te has completely lost his national position. He deliberately ignores the historical facts of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance Against Japan, distorts World War II history through conceptual substitution and confusion of right and wrong, and promotes the false narrative of “democracy against authoritarianism,” peddling the separatist fallacy of “Taiwan independence.” Its essence is still “seeking independence through force” and “relying on outsiders to seek independence.” We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te that any attempt to distort the history of World War II is bound to fail, any action that challenges the postwar international order is self-humiliation, and any scheme to split the motherland is wishful thinking. Justice will prevail, and unification will prevail. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will remember history, commemorate the martyrs, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, safeguard the fruits of victory, and resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and jointly pursue the bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","On August 23, the second round of voting in the “Great Recall” of Taiwan’s people’s representatives took place. Public opinion on the island holds that the “Great Recall” failed, tariff negotiations with the United States were frustrated, and cross-strait tensions have escalated. As a result, Lai Ching-te’s approval rating for governance has dropped sharply, and cross-strait relations may improve in the future.…","The results of the great recall fully demonstrate that any “Taiwan independence” political manipulation, including “resisting China and seeking independence,” is unpopular and is bound to fail. The root cause of the tense and turbulent cross-Strait relations is that the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” and collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke. Only by adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and recognizing that both sides of the Strait belong to one China can the two sides engage in dialogue and consultation, and cross-Strait relations improve and develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视记者","Taiwanese internet celebrity “Museum Director” Chen Chih-han visited Shenzhen in August and used live streams to showcase mainland technology, infrastructure, and livelihood development. He bluntly said he had been deceived by the DPP for years, and criticized the Taiwan authorities for distorting history for political gain. Public opinion on the island believes his change reflects the awakening of Taiwan’s youth…","This year marks the 45th anniversary of the establishment of the Shenzhen Special Economic Zone. From a fishing village in the South China Sea to a global benchmark, Shenzhen has used reform as its brush and innovation as its ink, and has shown the courage to break through, create, and get things done, writing a stirring poem of Chinese-style modernization. Compatriots from Taiwan, including Taiwanese internet celebrities, have recently come to Shenzhen one after another to observe from multiple angles and experience its cutting-edge technology, boundless vitality, and happy, well-provided-for people's lives in modern development. It is only natural that a sense of pride in being an upright Chinese person arises.\nOn social platforms in Taiwan, many Taiwanese netizens have liked videos that objectively share conditions on the mainland, and have voiced that “the two sides of the Strait are one family, we are Chinese.” We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to see for themselves and experience together the pride and honor of being Chinese. If I have the chance to chat face to face with our Taiwan fellow countrymen, I would say to them: “I was born in Guangdong, and I am Chinese. Our Taiwan fellow countrymen were born in Taiwan, and they are also Chinese. We are all Chinese.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720385.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","According to U.S. media reports, more than 500 Taiwanese military personnel took part in this year's U.S. military \"Northern Strike\" exercise, and for the first time the simulated combat scenario was shifted from Europe to the \"Indo-Pacific\" region. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities' attempts to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and to “resist unification by armed force” are entirely an overestimation of their own strength and a path to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Taiwan media, citing a Reuters report, said the US government may take a stake in TSMC. The head of Taiwan’s economic department said they would inquire with TSMC about the situation but had no specific response measures. This has caused widespread concern in the island’s industry that this US move would weaken the foundations of Taiwan’s industry. What comments do you have on this?","Taiwan's industry is deeply worried that the United States may weaken Taiwan's industrial advantages, because there are too many precedents for this. For its own private interests, the DPP authorities have let the United States take whatever it demands, bowing and scraping unreservedly, and even serving as an accomplice to the tiger. They are selling out Taiwan without any bottom line, and the harm falls on the interests and well-being of Taiwan's many enterprises and people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","According to Taiwan media reports, the United States recently imposed “reciprocal tariffs” on Taiwan, which has hit Taiwan’s traditional industries extremely hard. According to statistics on the island, as of August 15, the number of people who had to take unpaid leave due to US tariffs increased by more than 650 compared with the end of July. Among the nearly 4,000 people on unpaid leave, manufacturing workers…","The US imposition of a “20%+N” stacked tariff on Taiwan has turned the DPP authorities' painstaking fabrication of the “best in history” Taiwan-US relationship into a joke. The DPP authorities' shameless and absurd conduct of “kowtowing to the US and selling out Taiwan” without any bottom line is both disgraceful and ridiculous.\nThe increase in US tariffs on Taiwan and the appreciation of the New Taiwan dollar have hit small and medium-sized enterprises and traditional manufacturing industries on the island hardest. These affect the livelihoods of millions of people on the island. Many enterprises on the island now face difficult circumstances due to rising costs and shrinking orders, and large numbers of employees have been forced to take “unpaid leave,” with their interests and well-being continually harmed. Out of political calculation of “seeking independence by relying on outsiders,” the DPP authorities allow the US to demand whatever it wants, conceal the truth from the public, and go further and further down the wrong path of “selling out Taiwan” and “destroying Taiwan,” and they have already reaped the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720391.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Under the superimposed \"20%+N\" tariffs that the US has forcibly imposed on the Taiwan region, public sentiment on the island is accelerating its shift from \"relying on the US\" to \"resenting the US.\" Recent polls by multiple media outlets and think tanks show rising negative views of the US among Taiwan residents. Among them, a report by the US Hopkins Association shows that 40.5% of Taiwan residents hold negative…","Increasing facts are making Taiwan’s public realize that adhering to “following the US in everything, looking to the US for everything, and taking the US as the only standard” is a complete mistake, and that the US has always pursued “America First.” The DPP authorities, at the cost of the people’s well-being and the island’s economic prospects, have groveled and pledged allegiance to the US, and will ultimately face the fate of being squeezed dry by the US.\nThe future of Taiwan, and the security, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. The mainland has a sound economic foundation, strong resilience and great potential, and its long-term outlook remains positive. It has always been the best choice for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots to invest and do business, and a solid backing against risks. We welcome Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople to come to the mainland more often to take part in exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, and to share opportunities and create development together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","《团结报》记者","Taiwan media reported that German Foreign Minister recently said during a visit to Japan that China has repeatedly “publicly threatened to unilaterally change the status quo” in the Taiwan Strait, East China Sea and South China Sea regions. What is your comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait, an indisputable historical and legal fact, and a common consensus of the international community, which no person or force can distort or shake.\nThe situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable at present. Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","海峡之声广播电台记者","Taiwan media reported that the island's administrative agency recently passed the 2026 annual general budget, in which the defense budget reaches NT$949.5 billion, accounting for 3.32% of forecast GDP, a record high. Island public opinion has criticized the Lai Ching-te authorities for cooperating with the US in hollowing out Taiwan. What comment do you have?","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance. For the sake of one party’s private interests, they seek to “seek independence by force,” disregard public opinion on the island, and lavishly squander the hard-earned money of the people. They vigorously promote “the whole people as soldiers,” bind Taiwan’s people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and escalate tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is the greatest threat to the security and interests of the Taiwan people. Acting as an “ATM” for American arms dealers and catering to whatever outside forces demand, they waste money that could have been used to improve people’s livelihoods and develop the economy on buying weapons and pleasing outside forces. This is not only useless but will push Taiwan into a disastrous situation. The trend toward unification is unstoppable. “Relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail, and “seeking independence by force” will surely lead to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720387.htm"],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Reportedly, the Taiwanese internet personality “Guanzhang” said earlier during an exchange in Macau that he could not open accounts on “Douyin” and Bilibili. However, on August 22 he completed real-name verification of an account on “Douyin.” What comments do you have on this? What conditions must Taiwan compatriots meet to register accounts on Douyin and Bilibili?","Douyin, Bilibili and other online social platforms have clear rules regarding applications by netizens, including Taiwan compatriots, to open accounts. As long as Taiwan compatriots apply in accordance with the rules, they can open accounts after review and approval and share information with mainland netizens. We welcome our Taiwan compatriots to share in the opportunities of mainland internet development, and we are glad to see cross-Strait netizens, on the basis of complying with mainland laws and regulations and the rules of the relevant online social platforms, enhance mutual understanding, learn from and draw on each other, follow and like each other, and enhance friendship and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The DPP authorities recently investigated and penalized so-called Taiwanese entertainers who “echo” the mainland. The head of Taiwan's culture department said that, in accordance with the law, they communicated with the entertainers and understood their views. The Mainland Affairs Council said it has successively notified 25 Taiwanese entertainers, and that if they do not reply within the explanation period, they…","For some time, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have intensified their obstruction and restriction of cross-Strait exchanges and travel, and have spared no effort in suppressing and obstructing Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, seriously harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities' investigation and punishment of Taiwan entertainment personnel is, in essence, an attempt to continuously hype the so-called “united front threat,” and to intimidate people on the island who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges. It is entirely unpopular.\nIt must be pointed out that Taiwan compatriots, including entertainment personnel, as Chinese people, expressing their identification with the country and their opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism is a genuine outpouring from the heart. It is their legitimate right and interest. We will continue to support and encourage cross-Strait cultural exchanges and cooperation, welcome Taiwan entertainment personnel to come to the mainland to develop their careers, and take necessary measures to safeguard their legitimate rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The Mainland Affairs Council said it prohibits public officials from attending commemorative activities marking the victory in the War of Resistance, such as the September 3 military parade on the mainland. It reminded Taiwan residents not to take part in related activities, and said that any “cooperative behavior” with the mainland will be penalized in accordance with the law. It also said that some public…","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. It is worth commemorating together for compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and Taiwan compatriots should not and cannot be absent from related commemorative activities. The DPP authorities have deliberately distorted the history of the War of Resistance, and have threatened and intimidated, and interfered with and obstructed, Taiwan compatriots participating in War of Resistance commemorative activities. Their despicable conduct of betraying history and betraying the nation is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: According to a Reuters report, Commander of the U.S. Strategic Command Adm. Cotton stated in Congress in March this year that the Chinese military will have the capability to seize Taiwan by 2027. This is the fourth U.S. military general in recent years to issue the warning that \"the mainland will attack Taiwan.\" At present, military expenditures on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are on an upward…","Question one. Our policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to realize the reunification of the motherland, and it is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to the Chinese nation. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and, with the greatest sincerity and the utmost effort, strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. However, we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. Our national defense spending grows in a reasonable and stable manner in order to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, and to ensure that the modernization of national defense and the armed forces keeps pace with the modernization of the country.\nThe United States, out of consideration of “America First,” treats Taiwan as a “pawn” to “use Taiwan to contain China,” and keeps fabricating pretexts to “arm Taiwan.” The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are doing their utmost to cater to external forces, repeatedly hyping up the so-called “military threat” from the mainland, and turning a deaf ear to the calls of people on the island who hope to improve livelihood and welfare and to “avoid war and seek peace.” This will seriously harm the interests and well-being of the Taiwan people and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nIt should be pointed out that the reason peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are currently in jeopardy, and the reason cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanisms have come to a standstill, is fundamentally that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and keep colluding with external forces to pursue “Taiwan independence” through force and to rely on outside support for “Taiwan independence.” These separatist actions of “Taiwan independence” have undermined peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region, harmed the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and challenged the will and determination of all Chinese people. They are destined to fail.\nThe historical process of cross-Strait reunification is unstoppable. We are committed to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations on the basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” We also hope that people from all sectors on the island will join us in upholding the one-China principle, consolidating and strengthening mutual trust, deepening exchanges and cooperation, jointly maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and firmly holding the future and destiny of Taiwan in the hands of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.\nQuestion two. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. We will invite representatives from all sectors, including Taiwan compatriots, to attend relevant commemorative activities.\nThe great spirit of the War of Resistance is a precious spiritual treasure of the Chinese people, and will forever inspire the Chinese people to overcome all difficulties and hardships and strive to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The issuance of the commemorative medal for the “80th Anniversary of the Victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression” is precisely to carry forward and pass on the great spirit of the War of Resistance. This honor belongs to all Chinese people who made outstanding contributions to the victory in the War of Resistance.\nQuestion three. The remarks of the Mainland Affairs Council are black and white reversed and confuse right and wrong, and once again expose the separatist essence of “Taiwan independence” of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nThe Chinese people’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression was both a fight for national independence and state sovereignty and a fight for world peace and justice. During the War of Resistance, the Chinese people suffered the greatest losses, made the greatest sacrifices, and endured the longest struggle, and the heroic Chinese people made enormous contributions to the World Anti-Fascist War with their blood and lives. The memory and truth of history cannot be erased, and it is not to be tampered with. We are holding commemorative activities solemnly in order to remember history, honor the martyrs, cherish peace and create the future. We aim to learn from history, rally the mighty force to defend peace and justice, and firmly oppose all forms of hegemonism and power politics.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait have seen that at this important historical moment of the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not dare to offer even a word of criticism of the brutal aggressors, and make not the slightest mention of the suffering that Taiwan compatriots endured under 50 years of Japanese colonial rule; yet they have deliberately and groundlessly slandered the commemorative activities held on the mainland. Such a colonial-worshipping mindset completely lacks a national standpoint and is a shameless betrayal of the entire Chinese nation. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: those who fawn over colonizers and foreign interference forces, betray national interests and defy the trend of the times will surely be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Taiwan media reported that the Kaohsiung Branch of the Taiwan “High Court” recently sentenced Chang Tsun-feng, chairman of the Pingtung chapter of the Taiwan “Unification Alliance Party,” and Huang Jung-te, its secretary-general, each to 4 years and 6 months in prison and two years of deprivation of “civil rights,” on the so-called charge of allegedly interfering in island elections. What comment do you have on this?","In pursuit of “Taiwan independence” and separation, the DPP authorities abuse public power for private ends and use any means. They have repeatedly manipulated the judiciary to suppress people on the island who take part in cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. In particular, they have used baseless charges to target, in a pointed way, organizations and people on the island who support cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and they continue to reinforce the “green terror.” We strongly condemn this. Those who serve as henchmen and accomplices for “Taiwan independence” will ultimately face legal punishment. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will fully recognize the sinister intentions of the DPP authorities, resolutely oppose their totalitarian pursuit of “independence” and their reckless abuse of power, and firmly support cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报记者","Japan and Taiwan signed the so-called “Memorandum of Cooperation on Information Sharing regarding Immigration and Exit-Entry Management Matters” on the premise of a “Taiwan contingency,” to prevent “spies” from taking advantage of the chaos to enter Japan during a cross-Strait conflict. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. Japan carried out a 50-year colonial rule over Taiwan and committed crimes too numerous to record. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people’s defeat of the Japanese invaders and the recovery of Taiwan. The Japanese side should deeply reflect on history, abide by the One-China Principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, as well as the solemn commitments the Japanese government made to China on the Taiwan question, and be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities’ “relying on external forces to seek independence” is a dead end. Anyone who dares to provoke will surely bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Gordon, a scholar at the Brookings Institution and former US Vice President’s National Security Adviser, wrote that, as US security guarantees are no longer as firm as before, Taiwan has limited options to avoid being sold out by the Trump administration, but it can still play “three cards,” namely “raising defense spending, increasing investment in the United States, and handling the ‘Taiwan independence’ issue…","These remarks once again expose that the United States has always pursued “America First,” using so-called “security guarantees” as bait to make the DPP authorities willingly pay “protection money.” The end of “Taiwan independence” is being “discarded as a pawn.” No matter what cards the DPP authorities play in collusion with external forces, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern of the international community adhering to the One-China Principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Taiwan currently has no “operating” nuclear power plants. Will the “Cross-Strait Agreement on Nuclear Power Safety Cooperation,” signed by the two sides in 2011, be affected by this? How is the agreement currently operating? In addition, the “referendum to restart the Third Nuclear Power Plant” failed on August 23. If Taiwan restarts nuclear power in the future, is it possible for the mainland to…","First question: The “Cross-Strait Nuclear Power Safety Cooperation Agreement” was signed and implemented on the common political foundation of the “1992 Consensus.” The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and have unilaterally undermined the common political foundation across the Strait. This has caused the suspension of dialogue and consultation between the two cross-Strait associations, and it has also created obstacles to the implementation of relevant agreements.\nWe adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people. On matters that concern the health and safety of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, we attach great importance, act responsibly, and respond and handle matters promptly and appropriately, doing our utmost to safeguard the rights and interests of compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question: These practices by the DPP authorities are aggravating the “green terror” and creating a “chilling effect.” They are vile and shameless, and they win no popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-08-27","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, a Taiwanese guest on an online interview program said that under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, the mainland has become the world's second-largest economy, several hundred million people have been lifted out of poverty, and it has reached the world's cutting edge in fields such as technology. He said the DPP is a “makeshift troupe” that cannot compare at all with the Communist Party,…","Facts have repeatedly shown that more and more Taiwan compatriots see clearly the vile nature of the DPP authorities’ abuse of power and their scheming to pursue “independence” and stir up trouble in Taiwan, and have a clearer understanding of, and a sharper critique of, the DPP and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces for inciting “anti-Communist, anti-China” sentiment and escalating cross-Strait confrontation and opposition.\nSince its founding 104 years ago, the Communist Party of China has never forgotten its original aspiration or its mission, and has unswervingly worked for the well-being of the Chinese people and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Under the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China, the Chinese people and the Chinese nation have achieved the great leaps from standing up, to growing rich, to becoming strong. We have comprehensively built a moderately prosperous society and are comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization. The governing achievements and governance capacity of the Communist Party of China are recognized worldwide.\nUnder the leadership of the Communist Party of China, we are better positioned, more confident, and more capable of completing the great cause of reunifying the motherland, so that compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live better lives. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland more often to look around and experience the ever-changing development on the mainland, to witness with their own eyes and personally take part in the process of Chinese-style modernization and national rejuvenation, and to share the pride and happiness of being upright Chinese.\nNow I announce: On August 4, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” published the questions for the third “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” event, and netizens enthusiastically took part in answering. As of August 25, the netizens who answered correctly and ranked in the top ten by comments and likes, in order, are: “小陈小陈”, “轩窗载月”, “湫”, “春天”, “狗尾草”, “大海”, “永凯”, “辛至秦”, “时刻准备着”, and “校园网事”. We extend our congratulations to these ten netizens. They will receive an exquisite souvenir, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope everyone will work together to continue promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn September 8, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will publish the questions for the fourth “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” event. We look forward to more netizens paying attention and taking part!\nToday’s press conference ends here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202508/t20250827_12720376.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250827_12720382.htm"],[1,"2025-08-28","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Taiwan authorities recently approved the 2026 budget, with defense spending amounting to 949.5 billion New Taiwan dollars, accounting for about 3.32% of its GDP. This is the first time since 2009 that its defense spending has exceeded 3% of GDP. It is in response to U.S. pressure to ramp up military investment. Not long ago, Lai Ching-te announced a target of increasing the defense budget…","Peace, development, exchange and cooperation are common aspirations of the general public in Taiwan. The Lai Ching-te authorities keep going further down the evil path of seeking independence by force and continue to serve as a cash machine and make unconditional concessions to the U.S. at the cost of Taiwan's resources. Such moves will ultimately lead to self-destruction. The PLA will continuously enhance combat readiness and our ability to fight and win, and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250828-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16405526.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-08-28","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, an article posted in the U.S. magazine The Diplomat claimed that this year's Han Kuang 41 Exercise is nothing more than a show, and that the society and people of Taiwan are unprepared for war, both psychologically and institutionally. What is your comment on this?","We have expressed our views on the so-called Han Kuang exercise. The public have sharp eyes and they have long seen through the self-deceiving tricks of the DPP authorities. It is also clear to all that seeking independence and resisting reunification by force is doomed to fail.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250828-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16405526.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-08-28","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The upcoming parade in Beijing has drawn great attention. May I ask how the mainland side views the contributions of Nationalist army troops in battles during the War of Resistance? In addition, at the State Council Information Office press conference, it was announced that Kuomintang veterans of the anti-Japanese war would be invited to attend the parade as observers. May the spokesperson introduce the relevant…","The War of Resistance Against Japan was a just struggle in which all Chinese people united as one, shared a common hatred of the enemy, and resisted the aggression of Japanese militarism. More than 80 years ago, the guerrilla battlefields behind enemy lines opened up under the leadership of the Communist Party of China and the frontal battlefields commanded by the Kuomintang cooperated and joined forces, forming a strategic situation of jointly resisting Japanese aggression. Our invitation to Kuomintang veterans to participate in commemorative activities is a tribute to their bloody battles and merit in defending the country and their homes. For specific details, the State Council Information Office press conference provided an introduction.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250828-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16405526.html",0,5,1,""],[1,"2025-08-28","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, according to Japanese media reports, Japan has deployed the Sea Guardian large unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) to conduct surveillance and imaging activities against China Coast Guard (CCG) vessels over the waters surrounding Diaoyu Dao. This type of UAV has carried out multiple missions since April this year. Does the Chinese side know about the information collection activities of…","On your first question, Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. We urge the Japanese side to immediately cease all activities complicating maritime and airspace situations near Diaoyu Dao. China will continue to take effective measures to firmly safeguard our territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.\nOn your second question, the overall situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea remains stable. The Taiwan question is an internal affair of China, which brooks no external interference. To uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, we must abide by the one-China principle and firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts. We urge relevant parties to cease their erroneous words and deeds that fuel conflicts and heighten tensions.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/08/china-250828-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16405526.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-08-29","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Can you please tell us whether foreign troops will also march in next Wednesday’s military parade? With Russia and North Korea’s heads of state in attendance, can we expect to see soldiers from those two particular countries? Can you tell us whether any Taiwanese veterans or politicians will be attending?","We welcome Russian President Vladimir Putin and DPRK Supreme Leader Kim Jong-un to China for events marking the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. For your specific question, I’d refer you to competent authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250829_11698363.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250829_11698385.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-08-29","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","U.S. Senator Roger Wicker, Chair of the Senate Armed Services Committee, has arrived in Taipei. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","China firmly opposes any form of official interactions between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region. The visit by the U.S. Congress member seriously violated the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, harmed China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and sent a seriously wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly deplores this.\nThere is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China asks the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs and abetting and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces under any pretext, stop official interactions with China’s Taiwan region, and stop creating tensions for the situation across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202508/t20250829_11698363.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202508/t20250829_11698385.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-08-29","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On September 3, commemorative activities marking the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan will be grandly held in Beijing. Some people in the DPP authorities have threatened that former KMT political appointees who attend relevant activities on the mainland will face risks, and that as long as “indicative figures” go, they will be investigated and prosecuted. What…","Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council responded to questions, saying that the victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan was a victory of the entire nation and an important component of the victory of the world's anti-fascist war. To achieve national liberation and the restoration of Taiwan, and to defeat Japanese fascism, all Chinese sons and daughters, including Taiwan compatriots, made enormous sacrifices and important contributions. Representatives of all sectors of Taiwan who came to Beijing to attend the 80th anniversary commemoration of victory in the War of Resistance Against Japan reflect adherence to national righteousness and to upholding justice and conscience. They are upright and above reproach, and conducive to cross-Strait compatriots remembering history, commemorating martyrs, carrying forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance, and jointly working for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities are in a state of extreme alarm over this, obstructing and threatening it in every way. They have completely lost their national standpoint, abandoned justice and conscience, seriously violated the wishes of cross-Strait compatriots, seriously harmed the emotional bonds between cross-Strait compatriots, and fully exposed their \"Taiwan independence\" nature, which is despicable and vile and deserves contempt. Regarding individuals within the DPP authorities who openly clamor to act as \"Taiwan independence\" thugs and accomplices, we will hold them accountable according to law and resolutely crack down on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202508/t20250829_12720887.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On September 3, the grand rally marking the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War was solemnly held in Beijing. That same day, Lai Qingde posted on social media passing judgment on the commemorative rally, declaring that “Taiwan does not hold guns to commemorate peace” and “believes more that the…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions as follows: September 3 is the Commemoration Day of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, the “Victory Day” that gives Chinese people at home and abroad a sense of pride and triumph. At a time when the whole nation is celebrating and solemnly commemorating the 80th anniversary of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, Lai Ching-te has spouted nonsense, glorified aggression, and incited antagonism and confrontation. He has completely disregarded the arduous and heroic great war that Chinese people at home and abroad fought to save the nation from destruction; the great history that Chinese people forged with blood and lives in the struggle for national independence and liberation; and the immense national sacrifices and major historical contributions that Chinese people made to save human civilization and defend world peace. His remarks have completely lost any national standpoint, openly defied justice and conscience, seriously hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and fully exposed the ugly face and evil nature of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, which betray history, betray the nation, desecrate the martyrs, and extinguish conscience.\nTaiwan is part of China, and Taiwan compatriots are part of the Chinese nation. In the fight for national liberation and the restoration of Taiwan, to defeat Japanese fascism, all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, did not fear brutal force; they united in hatred of the enemy and rose up in resistance. They fought for the survival of the nation, for the rejuvenation of the nation, and for human justice, and ultimately achieved the first complete victory in resisting foreign invasion since modern times. Taiwan was then restored and returned to the embrace of the motherland. Our solemn commemoration of the 80th anniversary of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War is meant to jointly remember history, cherish the martyrs, cherish peace, and create the future. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will firmly stand on the right side of history and on the side of human civilization and progress, continue the patriotic tradition, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, safeguard the fruits of victory, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” and separatism, and join compatriots on the mainland in pursuing the bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nWe solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and his kind that any attempt to distort the history of the War of Resistance and World War II will never succeed; any act that challenges the postwar international order and the conscience of human justice will inevitably fail; and any scheme that sets itself against all Chinese people and seeks to split the country will bring about its own destruction. Justice will prevail, the people will prevail, and unification will prevail!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250904_12721978.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-09-05","Guo Jiakun","The Paper","In response to the Foreign Ministry Spokesperson’s remarks on the Philippines allowing the visit by head of the foreign affairs department of the Taiwan authorities, Philippine Defense Minister Gilbert Teodoro said that China should not impose its red line on the Philippines and that it’s the Philippines’ sovereignty to accept Taiwan officials. Teodoro said no government official met with Lin Chia-lung and the…","China has stated its solemn position on the Philippines allowing the visit by head of the foreign affairs department of the Taiwan authorities. The Philippines has repeatedly adopted wrong and provocative words and deeds on Taiwan-related issues, violated basic norms governing international relations and its commitment on Taiwan-related issues, and kept undermining its relations with China and trampling on China’s red line. The Philippines will pay the price and all consequences arising therefrom must be borne by the Philippines.\nWe noted that Philippine Defense Minister Gilbert Teodoro and other people made irresponsible remarks and deliberately made provocations on the Taiwan question and other China-related issues on multiple occasions. They blatantly challenged China’s core interest, red line and bottom line. China never tolerates and firmly opposes such moves. Our message to the Philippines is that for anyone in the Philippines who tries to be a troublemaker on the Taiwan question, interfere in China’s internal affairs, or undermine China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, their action will only backfire. We urge those individuals to quit their theatrics and stop making provocations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250905_11703299.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250905_11703156.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-08","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","The Foreign Ministry announced countermeasures on Japanese Councillor Shi Ping. What is your comment?","Shi Ping used to be a Chinese national. After he obtained Japanese nationality in Japan, he joined those who are anti-China in Japan and has deliberately unleashed disinformation and vilification against China, by making egregiously nefarious comments on Taiwan, Diaoyu Dao, historic issues, Xizang, Xinjiang and Hong Kong. After being elected a member of Japan’s National Diet, he visited and paid respect to Yasukuni Shrine. What he did seriously violated the principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and the one-China principle, constituted grave interference in China’s internal affairs, and undermined China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In response to his actions, China has decided to take countermeasures against Shi Ping, effective as of today.\nLet me point out that Shi Ping, for his selfish agenda, has betrayed his ancestors and conscience by joining anti-China forces in making provocations and troubles. China’s countermeasures are aimed to warn and hold to account Shi Ping and his kind. There are consequences for such dishonorable deeds.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250908_11704444.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250908_11704383.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-10","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","It was reported that the former leader of the Taiwan region Tsai Ing-wen visited Japan. What is China’s comment?","China has protested to Japan and cautioned it over Tsai Ing-wen’s visit to Japan. We firmly oppose any visit by “Taiwan independence” separatists to countries establishing diplomatic ties with China under whatever pretext. Tsai is the former leader of China’s Taiwan region. There is no rationale that can ever justify her trip to Japan or make it permissible, nor can they hide the trip’s real purpose—to seek foreign support for “Taiwan independence”.\nJapan bears historical responsibilities on the Taiwan question and should therefore act all the more prudently on related issues. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, the World Anti-Fascist War, and the restoration of Taiwan. We call on Japan to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, properly handle relevant issues, not interfere in China’s internal affairs in any form, and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatists.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250910_11705901.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250910_11705822.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 10, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear friends of the media, hello! Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Today happens to be Teachers' Day, and I extend holiday greetings to teachers and education workers across the country! Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The September 3 military parade has drawn great attention on the island. Taiwan compatriots have repeatedly praised the brilliant development achievements and strong military capabilities of the motherland's mainland, and said that it has strengthened their sense of national pride. At the same time, they feel deeply uneasy about the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces' reckless provocations in…","September 3 is the Commemoration Day of the Victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression. It is the “Victory Day” that Chinese descendants at home and abroad hold their heads high about and will never forget. Together with peace-loving people of the world, the Chinese people, through a grand military parade, jointly remember history, commemorate the martyrs, cherish peace, and create the future. General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech and the September 3 military parade demonstrated the Chinese nation's firm confidence in advancing toward great rejuvenation. They are also a firm declaration by the Chinese military as a guardian of world peace, and a declaration of our era from the Chinese people, promoting progress toward a community with a shared future for mankind.\nSome Taiwan compatriots attended the ceremony in person, while many more watched the parade live through various means. They expressed that “the September 3 military parade is the pride of the entire nation,” and media on the island reported that “Taiwan residents, whether they went to the scene or watched or followed it via television or the internet, all felt honored.” In the parade, each marching formation was majestic and imposing, and new weapons and equipment made a shocking debut. These demonstrated the PLA's systemic combat capabilities and new-domain, new-quality combat power, and also showed our determination and ability to safeguard peace and defend justice, as well as our determination and ability to maintain unification and oppose “Taiwan independence.” All Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots, were filled with joy and pride at being Chinese.\nThe desire for peace, development, exchange and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. The Lai Ching-te authorities have continuously increased defense budgets, attempting to “seek independence through force,” which will only make Taiwan even more perilous and war-prone, and make Taiwan residents even more anxious and uneasy. It is only natural that more and more Taiwan compatriots oppose this. We hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will join us in remembering history and commemorating the martyrs, continue the patriotic tradition, carry forward the great national spirit and the great spirit of the War of Resistance, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, firmly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and jointly accomplish the great cause of national reunification for generations to come and create a bright future for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723061.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said that the CPC side claims to have led the War of Resistance and holds events such as the September 3 military parade, aiming to strengthen the narrative of the one-China principle. “The CPC has made no contribution to the War of Resistance and is merely using the war to build itself up.” What is your comment on this?","At the \"most dangerous moment\" when the Chinese nation faced national subjugation and racial extinction, in order to liberate the nation and restore Taiwan and defeat Japanese fascism, all the sons and daughters of China, including Taiwan compatriots, fearlessly stood up against brute force with shared hatred against the enemy, fought for national survival, fought for national rejuvenation, and fought for human justice. In the end, they achieved the first complete victory in resisting foreign invasion since modern times. During the arduous 14-year War of Resistance, the Communist Party of China, with outstanding political leadership and correct strategies and tactics, guided the direction of China's resistance, and firmly promoted the whole nation to persist in resistance, unity and progress, opposing compromise, division and retreat. The Communist Party of China held high the banner of the Anti-Japanese National United Front, resolutely safeguarded, consolidated and developed the united front, adhered to independence and self-reliance and unity in resistance, and upheld the overall situation of unity in the War of Resistance. Chinese Communists fought bravely on the front lines of the War of Resistance, sustaining the hope of the Chinese nation's salvation and becoming the mainstay of the whole nation's resistance. The pillar role of the Communist Party of China was the key to victory in the War of Resistance.\nThe guerrilla battlefields behind enemy lines led by the Communist Party of China and the frontal battlefields led by the Kuomintang cooperated with and attacked the enemy from both sides, forming a strategic posture jointly resisting Japanese aggression. Statistics show that from September 1931 to September 1945, the anti-Japanese soldiers and civilians in the Northeast annihilated more than 170,000 Japanese troops, and the Eighth Route Army, the New Fourth Army and the South China Anti-Japanese guerrilla forces annihilated more than 527,000 Japanese troops, dealing heavy blows to the Japanese invaders and boosting confidence in the resistance. The vast guerrilla battlefields behind enemy lines resisted 60% of the Japanese invading forces in China, gradually becoming the main battlefield. They frustrated the arrogant scheme of Japanese fascism to quickly destroy China and enslave the Chinese nation, making important contributions to winning the great victory of the War of Resistance.\nHistory is history, and facts are facts; they cannot be tampered with or erased. The DPP authorities not only avoid mentioning the victory in the War of Resistance and Japan's defeat, but also harbor deep colonial nostalgia, repeatedly glorifying the history of aggression and the aggressors and colonizers. Their words and deeds have lost national standing and have no national integrity at all. They severely hurt the feelings of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and challenge the justice and conscience of human society. What right and qualifications do such scum of the nation have to make irresponsible remarks about the history of the War of Resistance and the commemorative activities for its victory?!\nWe hope that broad compatriots in Taiwan will firmly stand on the right side of history and on the side of the progress of human civilization, continue the patriotic tradition, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, defend the fruits of victory, and resolutely oppose all \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes that distort the historical truth of the War of Resistance, deny the achievements of the victory, and smear the merit of the historical War of Resistance, and pursue with compatriots on the mainland a beautiful future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723060.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Despite repeated intimidation and obstruction by the DPP authorities, Taiwan compatriots who were invited eagerly came to Beijing to participate in the commemorative activities for the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance, and they expressed their excitement and pride as Chinese. What is your comment on this?","September 3 is the anniversary of the 80th year of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is a day of victory for Chinese descendants at home and abroad, and a grand festival belonging to the Chinese people and to all peace-loving countries and peoples. At this glorious and important moment, representatives from all sectors of Taiwan, undaunted by the intimidation and obstruction of the DPP authorities, eagerly came to Beijing to attend the relevant commemorative events. Together with compatriots on the mainland, they remembered history, mourned martyrs, defended hard-won achievements, guarded our homeland, and forged the future. They expressed, in various ways, their excitement and pride as Chinese, and through concrete action, they demonstrated their profound feelings for country and family and their national righteousness. We highly appreciate this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723059.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Some DPP politicians have claimed that the mainland side “falsely claims that the Communist Party led China’s War of Resistance and possessed sovereignty over Taiwan after the war.” They have also said that the “Allied Powers” of that time have degenerated into “aggressor countries and authoritarian states,” while the “Axis Powers” of that time have become democratic countries. What is your comment?","The relevant remarks completely distort history and confuse right and wrong.\nDuring the 14 years of the War of Resistance, all Chinese sons and daughters worked together in unity and fought with great bloodshed. At the cost of approximately 35 million casualties, they achieved the great victory of the War of Resistance against Japan, supported the eastern main battlefield of the world anti-fascist war, and made significant contributions to saving human civilization and defending world peace. The Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japan and the world anti-fascist war were a great decisive battle between justice and evil, light and darkness, and progress and reaction. The Allied powers at that time, through a series of documents with force under international law, such as the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, confirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan and required Japan to return Taiwan, the Penghu Islands, and other Chinese territories that it had seized, to China. After the victory of the War of Resistance, the precious island of Taiwan, which had been occupied by Japanese imperialism for as long as 50 years, returned to the embrace of the motherland. The history of Taiwan's restoration irrefutably proves that Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory.\nReunification and separation are not a dispute over systems, but a contest between justice and evil, light and darkness, and progress and reaction. The DPP authorities have exaggerated the so-called “mainland threat,” manufactured and peddled “war anxiety,” and hyped the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism.” They attempt to deceive the public on the island, mislead international public opinion, and incite division and confrontation in the world. Their intentions are sinister and their methods despicable, fully exposing their sycophantic mindset and their true nature of seeking “independence.”\nAny attempt to distort the history of World War II or deny its victorious outcomes will not succeed. Any scheme to obstruct reunification or divide the country is doomed to fail, and any act that undermines the postwar international order will run into a wall. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of Chinese territory, nor can they stop the historical trend that China will ultimately be reunified and surely will be. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and the international community will fully recognize the essence of the Taiwan question, adhere to the one-China principle, and join us in upholding the correct historical view of World War II, resolutely safeguarding the postwar international order, and firmly defending international fairness and justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723058.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said in an interview that he hopes cross-Strait negotiations and exchanges will uphold “equal dignity,” and should not be premised on “Taiwan giving up ‘sovereignty’ and accepting the one-China principle.” He said that as long as one faces the fact that the “Republic of China” exists and faces the will of the Taiwanese people, he believes many issues can be easily resolved. What is your…","Lai Ching-te is once again turning black into white and confusing right with wrong, peddling the “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy and using glib words to deceive Taiwan's public and public opinion.\nThe mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, Taiwan is part of China, and cross-Strait communication, consultation and negotiation must of course be conducted on the basis of the one-China principle. From 2008 to 2016, cross-Strait consultations resumed on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, signed a series of agreements, and reached a series of common understandings. After the DPP came to power in 2016, it refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” leading to the interruption of cross-Strait communication and consultation. As long as the DPP authorities return to the common political foundation of the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” and stop “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, cross-Strait consultations and negotiations can resume. Otherwise, they are all empty talk and deceptive tricks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723056.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, the Taiwan Industry Federation released its “2025 Industry Federation White Paper.” Its cross-Strait policy section centers on “avoiding miscalculation and seeking peaceful coexistence across the Taiwan Strait” and proposes multiple recommendations, including loosening cross-Strait exchanges and grasping changes on the mainland to open up diverse business opportunities, which has resonated with industry…","The white paper of the Taiwan Industry Association reflects the deep concern of Taiwan's industrial and commercial circles about the current situation in the Taiwan Strait, and expresses questioning and opposition to the DPP authorities' cross-Strait policies. At present, the United States has imposed a “20%+N” tariff on Taiwan, and many industries and enterprises on the island face survival difficulties. For them, the vast mainland market is both a way out of their predicament and an opportunity for survival and development. Both sides of the Strait can, by deepening integrated development and raising the level of industrial and supply chain cooperation, jointly respond to external risks and challenges and strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation. However, the DPP authorities violate the laws of the market economy and clamor to build a so-called “non-red supply chain.” They kowtow to the United States whenever it acts, even though reality repeatedly slaps them in the face, and they still dream of “relying on the U.S. to resist China.” They are engaged in promoting “decoupling and supply chain severance” across the Strait. In order to serve the private interests of one party and a few individuals, they disregard the survival of enterprises, and they will ultimately provoke public outrage and lose all popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said that Taiwan will strengthen its defense forces, with next year's defense budget reaching more than 3% of GDP and expected to reach more than 5% of GDP before 2030. He also said, “As long as there is equality and dignity, we are willing to engage in exchange and cooperation with China to promote peace and common prosperity across the Taiwan Strait.” What comment do you have?","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly hold to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “seek independence through force.” They let external forces take whatever they want, keep raising “protection money” and serve as an “ATM,” recklessly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people, and rush down the evil path of warmongering. This not only fails to buy security and peace, but also squeezes and sacrifices the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan society, harming the present and the descendants to come. The future of Taiwan, the security and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, all depend on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland. Only when the Lai Ching-te authorities abandon their separatist ambitions for “Taiwan independence” and return to the one-China principle will there be a fundamental guarantee of peace in the Taiwan Strait, the well-being of Taiwan’s people be better protected and enhanced, cross-Strait exchanges proceed smoothly, and Taiwan compatriots have true dignity.\nThe so-called “equal dignity” of the Lai Ching-te authorities is an attempt to restore cross-Strait dialogue and consultation without acknowledging the one-China principle, and to change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. In reality, it creates obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. It is doomed to be a waste of effort and will absolutely not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723055.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","It has been two years since the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were issued and implemented. Please introduce what progress has been made in the construction of the demonstration zone, and how it will be advanced next.","Two years after the release of the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” the demonstration effect of the cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone has gradually emerged and its influence has steadily expanded. Construction of the demonstration zone has achieved phased progress.\nFirst, it has become more convenient for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to access the “First Home” service. The digital “First Home” service platform has gone online, essentially enabling Taiwan compatriots in Fujian to use “one-network query” and “full online handling” services. Since its launch, it has handled more than 12,000 service matters for Taiwan compatriots. Public legal service centers for Taiwan-related affairs have been set up in five areas including Fuzhou, Xiamen and Pingtan. A platform for ascertaining the law of the Taiwan region, serving all provincial courts, has been built, and the mainland's first Taiwan-related maritime dispute resolution center has been established. Many Taiwan compatriots have joined relevant social organizations in Fujian Province. A group of Taiwan teachers are working full-time teaching in Fujian, and nearly 2,200 Taiwan students are enrolled at universities.\nSecond, economic, trade and personnel exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan continue to be vibrant. Eight new Taiwan farmers' entrepreneurship parks have been established, and 14 Taiwan enterprises were recognized for the first time as mainland “time-honored brands.” The mainland's first cross-strait industrial investment fund initiated by Taiwan businesspeople, with a scale of 786 million yuan, has been established, and it was the first to open a channel for Taiwan compatriots' overseas-owned renminbi investment in the mainland. The mainland's first cross-strait common-standards information and service platform has been built. A cumulative 308 cross-strait common standards have been developed, and the number of Taiwan region vocational skills qualification items directly recognized has increased to 60. The number of “small three links” passenger sailings has been further increased, rising from 210 sailings per week in 2024 to 252 sailings in 2025. From January to August this year, more than 1.73 million passenger trips were made between Fujian and Taiwan, up 36.4% year on year. More than 670,000 Taiwan compatriot travelers entered through Fujian ports, up 15.5% year on year.\nThird, humanities and social exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan have continued to deepen. Civil exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan continue to expand. From January to August this year, a cumulative total of about 28,000 person-times of Taiwan compatriots came to Fujian to take part in various Taiwan-related activities, up 40% year on year. A large number of Taiwan youth have come to Fujian for internships, employment and entrepreneurship. The mainland's first local regulation on Taiwan-related special matters in the cultural field, the “Fujian Province Regulations on the Protection of Fujian-Taiwan Relations Archives,” was issued, and 54,900 archival documents, including “memories of migration to Taiwan,” have been collected. A pilot scheme allowing Taiwan businesses to invest in and establish radio and television program production and operation companies in Fujian has been implemented, and seven Taiwan businesses have been introduced so far.\nFourth, cross-strait integrated development across Fujian is maintaining good momentum. A series of measures to equalize, extend inclusiveness of, and make convenient basic public services in Xiamen and Kinmen have been implemented. Fuzhou has successively released two batches of Fuzhou-Matsu integration measures. The issuance of the “Fuzhou-Matsu Same-City Pass” and the “Xiamen-Kinmen Same-City Card” has provided more convenience for compatriots in Kinmen and Matsu. Construction of the Sanming Cross-Strait Rural Integrated Development Pilot Zone and other projects has been accelerated, and distinctive highlights of local cross-strait integration practices continue to emerge.\nThe Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will continue to work with relevant departments of the central and state organs and with Fujian Province to thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on Taiwan work and the CPC Central Committee's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work. They will practice the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” emphasize promoting integration through connectivity, benefits and emotional bonds, and, with more concrete measures and greater effort, promote construction of the demonstration zone to high standards and high quality, supporting Fujian in taking greater strides and achieving more results in exploring a new path for cross-strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723057.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The International Civil Aviation Organization will hold its assembly in Montreal, Canada, this month. US Congress members recently wrote to the ICAO Secretary-General proposing that Taiwan be invited to send representatives to attend. Taiwan's foreign affairs department expressed gratitude. What comments do you have on this?","Regarding Taiwan’s participation in international organizations, including activities of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués in practice, to be prudent in its words and actions on the Taiwan question, and not to send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “seek independence by relying on external support” within international organizations and the international community is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央广记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that, given the current economic downturn on the mainland, difficulties faced by enterprises, and the continued impact of the US-China trade war, Taiwan businesses must carefully assess before investing on the mainland. What is your comment on this?","This year, under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we have intensified the implementation of a more proactive and effective macroeconomic policy, ensuring that the economy operates steadily while making progress, and that high-quality development has achieved new results. The Mainland’s major economic indicators are performing well, new quality productive forces are developing actively, and reform and opening up continue to deepen, demonstrating strong vitality and resilience. In the first half of this year, the Mainland’s GDP grew 5.3% year on year. From January to July, the value added of industrial enterprises above designated size in the Mainland grew 6.3% year on year, total retail sales of consumer goods grew 4.8%, fixed-asset investment grew 1.6%, and foreign trade grew 3.5%.\nThese solid economic indicators are sufficient to make the DPP authorities’ lies collapse on their own. Disregarding the dire situation in which many Taiwan enterprises have been hit by the “double blow” of tariffs and exchange rates, the DPP authorities remain eager to hype the so-called “Mainland economic collapse theory.” Facts have repeatedly shown that the so-called “predictions” by the DPP authorities over many years that the Mainland would decline have not come true. On the contrary, the more they predict decline, the faster we develop, and the wider the gap in economic strength between the two sides grows.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","A spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office previously said that unless the DPP authorities make the request in the name of Taiwan Province, the mainland will not cooperate with the Taiwan side's request to provide “household registration cancellation” certificates for mainland spouses. Mainland spouses on the island have expressed affirmation and gratitude toward the motherland for sheltering them from wind and…","The DPP authorities force cross-strait marriage families to separate and flesh and blood to be torn apart. They compel mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan for more than 20 years to supplement a so-called “certificate of loss of household registration,” and they politically suppress cross-strait marriage family members who have been elected to relevant public offices on the island, depriving them of their legitimate rights. Each of these evil acts aims to manufacture so-called “nationality” issues and manipulate the “two-state theory.”\nWho is disrupting the peaceful lives of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and who is making mainland spouses in Taiwan feel insecure, is self-evident. The DPP authorities abuse their power and act recklessly, using every means to suppress and persecute mainland spouses. They severely disrupt their normal lives and harm their interests and well-being. They are the chief culprits behind the instability and insecurity of mainland spouses’ lives in Taiwan. Now they attempt to deceive the public and shift the blame onto others, which is utterly shameless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan demanded that cultural departments summon Taiwanese entertainers who “echo the CCP,” and said that some Taiwanese entertainers have indeed engaged in cooperation with the CCP's party, government and military. This time, they were only given verbal warnings, with “action to be taken if they reoffend.” Taiwan's cultural authorities issued an open letter warning entertainers…","Taiwanese performing artists who have developed careers on the mainland, based on what they have seen and experienced, express their pride as Chinese, their identification with the country and nation, and their opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism. This is their will and their right, and it also reflects the will of the people and the trend of the times. The DPP authorities’ attempt to silence them, and their various wrongful acts, will only let the world see through the hypocrisy of their so-called “freedom and democracy,” the brutality with which they obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and their guilty conscience in fearing that compatriots on both sides will meet each other halfway. The DPP authorities should reflect on themselves: why are Taiwanese performing artists flocking to the mainland and choosing it as the stage for their careers? We will, as always, welcome and support Taiwanese performing artists who develop on the mainland, and we will firmly safeguard their legitimate rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723054.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Entering September, cross-Strait economic, trade and cultural exchanges are in full swing. Please introduce the relevant information.","In September, all parts of the mainland actively held colorful and content-rich cross-Strait economic, trade, and cultural exchange activities, widely invited people from all sectors in Taiwan to visit, actively expanded cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and continuously deepened cross-Strait integrated development.\nIn economic and trade exchanges: From September 1 to 4, the 29th Lu-Tai Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference was held in Weifang, Shandong Province, mainly including the thematic events of the Cross-Strait Science and Technology Innovation and Industrial Integration Development Conference and the Advancement Meeting on the Construction of the Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone. From September 14 to 18, the 17th “Chongqing•Taiwan Week” will be held in Chongqing, covering five major sections—important events, economic and trade, youth, humanities, and grassroots exchanges—and 13 sub-events, with more than 500 participants from both sides of the Strait, including guests from the island and Taiwan compatriots in Chongqing. From September 15 to 21, the 17th Hunan-Taiwan Economic, Trade, and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation Conference will be held in Changsha, Hunan Province, and other places, under the theme “Sharing New Opportunities, Integrating Toward the Future.” About 400 Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots are expected to attend, to jointly promote industrial cooperation and integrated development between Hunan and Taiwan. From September 16 to 19, the 2025 Guizhou-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Symposium will be held in Guiyang, Guizhou Province, and other places, aiming to strengthen Guizhou-Taiwan industrial cooperation and promote youth exchanges, with more than 400 Taiwan guests expected to attend. From September 19 to 21, the 28th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum will be held in Beijing, featuring one main forum, four parallel forums, and N series of supporting events, to help Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises seize opportunities from the development of new quality productive forces on the mainland and achieve high-quality development.\nIn cultural exchanges: The 2025 Cross-Strait Zhouyi Cultural Exchange Event will be held in Anyang, Henan Province, from September 19 to 21, attracting more than 200 Zhouyi scholars and experts from both sides of the Strait and Taiwan youth. The main activities include the Taiwan Youth Visit Anyang series of activities, the “Civilization Through Characters, Eternal Cultural Lineage” oracle bone script experience activity, the King Wen of Zhou sacrificial ceremony, the academic seminar on the inheritance and development of Zhouyi as intangible cultural heritage, and the academic seminar on Zhouyi and modernization. These activities will enhance the understanding of compatriots on both sides of the Strait of Chinese traditional culture, including the Shang Dynasty civilization and the origin and evolution of oracle bone script.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that the US imposing stacked tariffs on Taiwan, the mass recall’s crushing defeat, and the impact of wind disasters were all unexpected events, “three black swans.” This sparked criticism from island public opinion, which holds that Lai is trying to find a “fig leaf” for his incompetent governance and loss of popular support. What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te’s statement is entirely an attempt to shirk responsibility. Lai Ching-te and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” kowtow to external forces all the way in exchange for their support, sell out Taiwan without any bottom line, suppress dissidents and stir up political strife for the sake of party self-interest, disregard people’s livelihoods, and fail in disaster relief. Their conduct has been widely opposed by the public on the island, yet they still refuse to reflect on their faults and show no remorse, which is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the mainland’s first 8K space-themed documentary film, “Blue Star Beyond the Window,” officially premiered, drawing high attention from Taiwan compatriots. Many young people from Taiwan said after watching it that the film brings not only visual impact but also a sense of pride in being Chinese. What comments do you have on this?","Exploring the vast universe, developing the space industry, and building a space power is the space dream that the Chinese nation has tirelessly pursued. After years of effort, we have gradually realized the millennia-old dream of the Chinese nation to leave the Earth, explore the universe, and travel through outer space, and the space industry has achieved world-renowned glorious accomplishments. The film 《Blue Planet Outside the Window》 is based on the six-month on-orbit residency mission of the Shenzhou-13 flight crew, the first of its kind. Its main footage was shot by Shenzhou-13 astronauts acting as cinematographers aboard China's space station. For the first time, it comprehensively records the complete process of astronauts from departure, to working and living in space, to returning to the ground. It presents audiences with an extraordinary journey full of Chinese-style space aesthetics, and this is a shared glory belonging to all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation.\nOur journey is toward the stars and the sea, and our path leads to the vast universe. China's space industry and its dream of flight will soar higher and farther, bringing more emotion and glory to compatriots on both sides of the strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723052.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s external exchange department, recently sneaked a visit to the Philippines. The Philippines subsequently reaffirmed, through a statement and remarks by its foreign minister, that it adheres to the One China Policy and does not recognize Taiwan as a “sovereign state.” Some public opinion holds that Lin Chia-lung’s trip lost face and was self-humiliating. What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We have consistently and clearly opposed any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic ties with China’s Taiwan region, and we firmly oppose relevant countries providing a political stage for “Taiwan independence” figures. The Philippines should abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the China-Philippines diplomatic communiqué, stop playing with fire and crossing red lines on the Taiwan question, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on outside forces to seek independence” is a dead end. No matter how they cling to external forces to seek “independence” and stir up trouble, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the international community’s common consensus and basic framework of adhering to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250910_12723053.htm"],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","A public opinion poll recently launched by CGTN among approximately 12,000 respondents in 40 countries worldwide showed that 66.7% of respondents know about the history of Taiwan's restoration, and the awareness rate among Asian respondents is as high as 73.5%. Most respondents clearly stated that Taiwan's return to China is a fruit of victory in World War II, and that any “Taiwan independence” separatist act is…","The great victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japan thoroughly shattered Japanese militarism's scheme to colonially enslave China, effectively defended national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and completely washed away the national humiliation of repeated defeats in resisting foreign aggression since modern times. More than 80 years ago, to win the final victory in the war against Japan and rebuild the postwar order, the heads of state of China, the United States, and the United Kingdom held a conference in Cairo and issued the Cairo Declaration. The Cairo Declaration clearly proclaimed: “Japan shall be stripped of all the islands in the Pacific Ocean which it has seized or occupied since the beginning of the First World War; all territories Japan has stolen from China, such as Manchuria, Taiwan, and the Pescadores, shall be restored to China.” The content and spirit of the Cairo Declaration were further reaffirmed in the Potsdam Proclamation of July 1945. The Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation became important international legal grounds for the restoration of Taiwan and its return to China, and China's sovereignty over Taiwan is an important component of the postwar international order. Since 1949, although cross-Strait reunification has not yet been achieved, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided, and the fact that China holds sovereignty over Taiwan and that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China has never changed.\nThe above public opinion poll results show that history can never be forgotten, much less falsified. In recent years, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have stubbornly adhered to their “Taiwan independence” stance, continuously engaged in provocations aimed at “independence,” and clamored that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other” and “Taiwan's sovereignty is independent,” scheming to split Taiwan away from China. Their conduct seeks to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and deny China's sovereignty over Taiwan. It is a challenge to the postwar international order and a sabotage of the fruits of the world's victory in the anti-fascist war. We hope the international community will stand on the side of human civilization's progress and more broadly understand and support the Chinese people's just cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving to complete national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","Reports indicate that the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held on September 25. Can the spokesperson confirm this? How does the mainland assess the important role the “Twin City Forum” has played in the development of cross-Strait relations?","The Shanghai–Taipei City Forum has been held continuously since 2010 and has become an important platform for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We have consistently supported and actively promoted exchanges and cooperation between cross-Strait cities, and relevant parties in Shanghai and Taipei have maintained communication regarding this year’s “Shanghai–Taipei City Forum.” We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, counties and cities, and people from all walks of life to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and personnel exchanges, and to benefit compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Recently, in a video titled “Appointment with Officers and Soldiers,” Lai Ching-te (赖清德) advocated: “Only by preparing for war can we avoid war; as long as our will is firm, authoritarianism cannot take away the democracy and freedom we cherish.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities obstinately hold the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, use false narratives such as “democracy versus authoritarianism” to agitate for war preparations, and, for the private interests of one party and one person, disregard the life safety and welfare of Taiwan compatriots, and are willing to push Taiwan into a dangerous situation of deadly conflict and war. I solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities that the trend of reunification is unstoppable, “seeking independence by relying on outsiders” is doomed to fail, and “seeking independence by force” will surely lead to self-destruction.\nQuestion from Zhejiang Daily's “Tide News”:\nTaiwan media reported that Taipei City intends to use a robot dog manufactured by a mainland manufacturer to assist in patrolling sidewalks, but the DPP authorities opposed it on the grounds that there are “information security concerns.” They also stated that the use of mainland-manufactured information and communication products requires approval, and Taipei City has not yet applied. What is the spokesperson's comment?\nMainland enterprises are based on innovation and development, actively integrating into global industrial and supply chains, and their products have been recognized by the market and are widely welcomed by consumers around the world. The DPP authorities, disregarding public welfare and industry interests, use the pretext of so-called “security” to obstruct the use of high-quality mainland products and use administrative intervention to disrupt market order, all for their own private interests. This reckless conduct harms the rights and interests of enterprises and consumers on the island and damages and worsens Taiwan's market and business environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: The September 3 military parade drew great attention from the international community. Most Western public opinion focused on the new weapons displayed at the parade, believing that the mainland intends to send a warning to the United States and the Taiwan region. From the standpoint of the Taiwan Affairs Office, what message does this parade send to the Taiwan side?\nSecond question: Chiu…","First question. We are solemnly commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, in order to remember history, honor martyrs, cherish peace, and create the future. The September 3rd Parade demonstrated the systematic combat capabilities of the PLA and its new-domain and new-quality combat power. It demonstrated our determination and ability to safeguard peace and defend justice, as well as our determination and ability to safeguard national reunification and oppose “Taiwan independence.” It greatly inspired the national spirit and national strength of all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and should keep the history of the national war of resistance firmly in mind and establish a correct view of history, nation, and country. We should adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” jointly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces, and safeguard, build, and develop the homeland that belongs to the Chinese people.\nSecond question. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, colluding with external forces to plot “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the destroyers of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the instigators of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait.\nThe future of Taiwan and the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots lie in national reunification. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' attempt to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” will only make them more of a “pawn” for external forces, and they will ultimately face the fate of being “discarded.” Their attempt to “seek independence by force” will only make Taiwan more dangerous and war-prone. This is entirely overestimating their own strength and seeking a dead end. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end: outsiders cannot be relied upon, and reunification cannot be stopped. We have firm will, strong determination, and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThird question. Since 2002, Jilin University has held the “Northern Winter Camp” for 21 consecutive sessions, and its ice and snow cultural experiences and academic exchanges and cooperation are deeply loved by teachers and students on the island, especially young friends. Similar exchange activities between universities across the Strait have been carried out for many years. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have arbitrarily obstructed them and pinned labels on normal cross-Strait education exchanges, fully exposing their sinister intention to deliberately escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation.\nSince the beginning of this year, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have escalated and intensified their obstruction and restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges. In particular, they have treated exchanges between cross-Strait universities and young students as an “eyesore and thorn in the flesh.” This includes banning island colleges and universities from exchange and cooperation with 10 mainland schools such as Jinan University and Beihang University, and repeatedly obstructing cross-Strait primary and secondary school education exchange and cooperation. All of this is aimed at manipulating “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment and creating a “green terror.” We ask: if even normal exchange and cooperation between cross-Strait universities and the normal enrollment and study of Taiwan students are to be banned, where is the “democracy” that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities advertise? Where is the “freedom”? As for why they are so afraid of cross-Strait youth exchanges, it is simply that they fear their fabricated “Taiwan independence” narrative will be exposed and the “information cocoons” they have woven will be broken.\nFourth question. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are accustomed to using so-called “gray-zone harassment” as an excuse, deliberately playing up the “mainland threat” and inciting “anti-China and hatred of China.” The aim is to divert the island's public's dissatisfaction with their incompetent governance and their “selling out Taiwan and provoking war.” This routine has no novelty. Taiwan's people have long seen it, seen through it, and grown tired of it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities recently claimed that the mainland is conducting undersea oil and gas drilling in waters near Dongsha Island, violating international legal norms such as the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and bringing uncertain risks to regional stability. What is your comment?","China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands and the waters adjacent to them, including the waters near Pratas Island (Dongsha Island) that you mentioned. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China and should jointly safeguard the country’s territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, as well as the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The DPP authorities are using this for political hype, which is entirely motivated by ulterior motives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The DPP authorities have promoted the National Palace Museum's exhibition of cultural relics in the Czech Republic and other activities, planning to display more than one hundred national-treasure-level cultural relics for the first time. Some public opinion points out that the DPP authorities are using the name of \"cultural exchange\" to carry out \"cultural Taiwan independence\" in substance. What is your comment…","Historical and cultural heritage, including cultural relics of the Palace Museum, is precious wealth left to us by our ancestors. It carries the cultural genes and shared memory of the Chinese nation, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait have a responsibility to protect and pass it on well. On the one hand, the DPP authorities vigorously promote “cultural Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization,” and on the other hand, they extensively exploit treasures of Chinese culture to manipulate for “Taiwan independence.” How ironic this conduct is, and how ugly this face is! We warn the DPP authorities that any act of defiling or damaging national treasures and cultural relics will be met with unanimous condemnation by the entire nation and the merciless judgment of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-10","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question. Chen Chiu-cheng, Chairman of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, visited the United States and gave a speech claiming that \"maintaining the status quo of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is in the common interests of Taiwan and the United States.\" How does the Taiwan Affairs Office view Taiwan's side releasing the expression \"maintaining the status quo of peace and stability across the…","First question. First, we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and not provide them with any stage for political performances.\nSecond, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position, continuously collude with external forces to engage in provocations to seek “independence,” and push Taiwan step by step into a dangerous situation of war and disaster. They are the destroyers of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability across the Strait.\nFinally, “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. We hope compatriots in Taiwan will, starting from national righteousness and their own well-being, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” provocations and interference by external forces, and work with us to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond question. General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the meeting commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, which greatly inspired the national spirit and strength of all Chinese people and fully demonstrated the confident, self-reliant, united and striving spirit of all Chinese people. In his speech, General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed: “All officers and soldiers of the entire military must faithfully fulfill their sacred duties, accelerate the building of a world-class military, resolutely safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity, provide strategic support for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and make greater contributions to world peace and development!”\nOur major policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. “Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question, the best way to achieve national reunification, and most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures.\nThird question. We cherish peace, but we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatism. At present, the DPP authorities and Lai Ching-te obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and continuously engage in provocations to seek “independence,” which is the root cause of threats to security across the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan is a sacred and inseparable part of China’s territory. We will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to separate Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. Any separatist force and act aimed at splitting the motherland will surely be met with a head-on blow from all Chinese people!\nOur refusal to promise to renounce the use of force is directed at “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and is by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope compatriots in Taiwan will, starting from their own security and well-being, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation.\nThat concludes today’s press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250910_12723073.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-09-12","Lin Jian","Reuters","The head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs office is now in Europe. Can I have your comment on that?","Taiwan is a province of China and the person you mentioned a local official of that province in charge of foreign affairs.\nThere’s only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We have consistently and unequivocally opposed any form of official interaction between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. No country should provide any platform for “Taiwan independence” separatists. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes it and has protested to relevant countries.\nWe urge relevant European countries to abide by the one-China principle, and take effective measures at once to stop “Taiwan independence” separatists from visiting Europe. The Taiwan authorities must know that seeking “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail and any attempt to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250912_11707735.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250912_11707489.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-12","Lin Jian","AFP","China says that its aircraft carrier the Fujian sailed through the Taiwan Strait to carry out research trials and training missions in the South China Sea. The navy said that this is not directed at any specific target. Can the Foreign Ministry give any additional comment on this and if this means that the Fujian will soon enter active service?","Relevant information was released by the Chinese navy. China’s third aircraft carrier, the Fujian, passed through the Taiwan Strait to carry out scientific research tests and training missions in the South China Sea. The cross-sea tests and training for the Fujian is a regular arrangement in the aircraft carrier’s construction process, and it is not aimed at any specific target.\nLet me stress that the Chinese vessel’s activities in relevant waters are fully in line with China’s domestic laws and international law.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250912_11707735.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250912_11707489.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-15","Lin Jian","CCTV","During his recent visit to the U.S., Chiu Chui-Cheng, head of the Mainland Affairs Council of China’s Taiwan region, met with both Democratic and Republican members of the U.S. Congress and delivered a speech at the U.S. think tank the Heritage Foundation. Chiu said, “Mainland China has become the greatest threat to the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait,” and sought to play up the possibility of Taiwan…","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is the true status quo regarding the Taiwan Strait. The greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait comes from the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. China firmly opposes any form of U.S.-Taiwan official interactions and military contacts, and firmly safeguards our nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the U.S. to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop sending wrong messages to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. No matter how the DPP authorities peddle the “mainland threat” narrative, hype up tensions across the Taiwan Strait, and squander the taxpayers’ money in exchange for external support for their “independence” agenda, they cannot change the fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China. Still less can they stop the inevitability of China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250915_11708660.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250915_11708567.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-15","Lin Jian","Reuters","The American Institute in Taiwan said in a statement that mainland China intentionally mischaracterizes documents from the World War II era, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Treaty of San Francisco, to try to support its campaign against Taiwan. They also said that Beijing’s narratives are “simply false, and none of these documents determined Taiwan’s ultimate political status.”…","The statement of relevant U.S. institution seeks to distort the facts and mislead the public. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this.\nThe restoration of Taiwan to China is an important part of the outcomes of WWII victory and post-war international order. A series of instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, have all clearly affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. The question regarding the status of Taiwan has already been completely settled following the victory of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression in 1945. The so-called Treaty of San Francisco is a document that is illegal, null and void, and issued by the U.S. and some countries after WWII, excluding the People’s Republic of China and the Soviet Union, to seek a separate peace deal with Japan.\nLet me stress that there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an undeniable historical and legal fact, which no one or force can change. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and stop abetting and aiding “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in any form.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250915_11708660.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250915_11708567.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-16","Lin Jian","China Daily","We noted that Foreign Minister Wang Yi just concluded his visit to Austria, Slovenia and Poland. Can you share more details about the visit?","From September 12 to 16, at the invitation of Austria, Slovenia and Poland, Foreign Minister Wang Yi visited the three countries. In Austria, he met with Federal President Alexander Van der Bellen and held talks with Foreign Minister Beate Meinl-Reisinger. In Slovenia, he met with President Nataša Pirc Musar, Prime Minister Robert Golob, and President of the National Council Marko Lotrič, and held talks with Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign and European Affairs Tanja Fajon. In Poland, Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with President Karol Nawrocki, and held talks and jointly chaired the fourth meeting of the China-Poland Intergovernmental Committee with Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Radosław Sikorski. The visit achieved good results. It served to consolidate the traditional friendship between China and these European countries, and build consensus on deepening cooperation, promoting development and safeguarding peace.\nThe visit deepened bilateral relations. Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted that China stands ready to step up strategic communication with the three countries, deepen China-Austria green cooperation, expand China-Slovenia practical cooperation, advance China-Poland cooperation on the Belt and Road Initiative, and strengthen cultural and people-to-people exchange. China and Poland issued the Fourth Meeting of Poland-China Intergovernmental Committee Joint Conclusions. Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted that China and Europe should be friends rather than rivals, and should cooperate rather than confront each other. He expressed the hope that Austria, Slovenia and Poland will play a positive role in fostering an objective and rational understanding on China in the EU, and help advance the sound and steady development of China-EU relations. Leaders of Austria, Slovenia and Poland all noted that they value the relations with China, stand ready to maintain high-level exchanges with China, and stressed that Europe and China are partners and need to enhance constructive dialogue and cooperation. All three countries said they welcome Chinese companies to invest and engage in cooperation in Europe.\nSecond, the visit promoted the correct view of World War II history. Foreign Minister Wang Yi emphasized that this year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War. The Chinese people paid a huge price and made significant contribution to the victory in the Asian theater of World War II and the World Anti-Fascist War. The outcomes of the victory, including the restoration of Taiwan to China, must be upheld. “Taiwan independence” forces’ attempts to split the country and undermine the post-war international order are doomed to failure. The leaders of Austria, Slovenia, and Poland gave high recognition to the Chinese people’s tremendous sacrifices and outstanding contribution for the WWII victory, and reiterated their firm adherence to the one-China policy.\nThird, the visit reflected shared commitment to world peace and promoting global governance reform. Foreign Minister Wang Yi stated that in a turbulent world, China and Europe need to jointly resist and reject unilateralism and power politics. The Global Governance Initiative, put forth by President Xi Jinping, aims at reforming and improving the global governance system and meets the shared aspirations of the international community. China is willing to strengthen solidarity and cooperation with all other countries, firmly uphold the international system with the United Nations at its core, and work together to build a more just and equitable global governance system. The leaders of Austria, Slovenia and Poland spoke highly of China’s development achievements and sense of responsibility as a major country. They welcomed and affirmed the importance of China’s Global Governance Initiative, and expressed their willingness to strengthen communication and coordination with China, safeguard the authority of the United Nations, uphold multilateralism, and join hands for world peace and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250916_11709475.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250916_11709281.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-09-16","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, the aircraft carrier Fujian recently conducted sea trials and passed through the Taiwan Strait to operate in the South China Sea. What comments do you have on this? Does this sea trial mean the Fujian is about to be handed over and commissioned?","Jiang Bin said that recently, China’s third aircraft carrier, the Fujian, passed through the Taiwan Strait and went to relevant waters of the South China Sea to carry out test and training missions. This is a normal arrangement in the course of aircraft carrier construction, in line with relevant international law and international practice, and it is not directed at any specific country or target.\nJiang Bin stated that China adheres to the path of peaceful development and pursues a defensive national defense policy. We always advance aircraft carrier construction according to the needs of national security and the development of equipment and technology. As a major national weapon, the Fujian will surely play its due role in defending national sovereignty, security, and development interests.","","https://www.news.cn/politics/20250916/24ea01cc56ca496cbae390ae84effd7a/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-09-17","Lin Jian","CCTV","It was reported that the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) claimed that the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation and other documents “did not determine Taiwan’s ultimate political status.” A U.S. State Department spokesperson said when asked to comment that the AIT comments accurately conveyed the U.S.’ stance and that the Chinese mainland “distorted” the WWII-era documents to support its “coercive”…","I responded to similar questions earlier this week. The restoration of Taiwan to China is an important part of the outcomes of WWII victory and post-war international order. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the U.S. and the UK in 1943 stipulates clearly that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan, shall be restored to China. The Potsdam Proclamation jointly published by China, the U.S., the UK and the Soviet Union in 1945 stipulates that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. In the same year, Japan signed the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, pledging to carry out the provisions of the Potsdam Declaration in good faith. These instruments with legal effect under international law have all clearly affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. As a signatory to the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, the U.S. is fully aware of the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China. Yet the U.S. blatantly rehashes the fallacy that Taiwan’s status is “undetermined” and smears China’s legitimate actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity to deliberately mislead international public opinion. What the U.S. has done severely violates international law and the basic norms in international relations and sends a gravely wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nHistory should not be distorted. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community. The U.S.’s unilateral distorted interpretation will not shake the international community’s overwhelming commitment to the one-China principle. China urges the U.S. to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop manipulating the Taiwan question, stop abetting and aiding “Taiwan independence” in any form and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs. No individual or force can ever hold back China from being reunified.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250917_11710263.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250917_11710000.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-09-18","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The “American Institute in Taiwan” (AIT) recently stated in an interview with a Taiwanese media outlet that the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and other documents “have not determined Taiwan’s ultimate political status.” In response to the media’s inquiry, a spokesperson of the US Department of State also said, “China distorts World War II-era documents to support its coercive…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that Taiwan’s status is very clear: it is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. It has belonged to China since ancient times, belongs to China now, and its historical course and legal facts are crystal clear.\nA series of documents with international legal effect, including the 1943 Cairo Declaration, the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation, and the 1945 Instrument of Japan’s Surrender, clearly confirm China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. In October 1945, Taiwan was restored and returned to China, and the Chinese government resumed the exercise of sovereignty and administrative jurisdiction over Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. The question of Taiwan’s status was thoroughly resolved when the Chinese people won their War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. On October 1, 1949, the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legal government representing all of China. This was a change of regime within a situation in which the subject of international law, China, did not change. China’s sovereignty and inherent territory and borders did not change, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China naturally fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The status of Taiwan as part of China has not changed.\nThe return of Taiwan to China is an important component of the victory of World War II and the postwar international order. As a signatory to the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, and as one of the victorious powers of World War II, the United States is perfectly clear about the historical and legal facts that Taiwan belongs to China and was returned to China. Yet it has openly rehashed the fallacy of so-called “undetermined status of Taiwan,” smearing and slandering China’s legitimate actions to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maliciously misleading international public opinion, seriously violating international law and the basic norms of international relations, and sending a serious wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop manipulating Taiwan-related issues, stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatism, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs.\nThe DPP authorities, through specific media outlets and some American institutions, have staged a “double act” that distorts history and clamors for the “undetermined status of Taiwan” theory, attempting to fabricate historical and legal bases for their pursuit of “independence” and create a false appearance of so-called “international support.” This clumsy trick of self-deception is doomed to be in vain and will never succeed. History cannot be tampered with. Taiwan’s status as belonging to China is settled, and the great cause of national unification will certainly be accomplished. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme to “rely on foreign forces to seek independence,” and no matter how external forces create trouble, the historical trend that China will eventually be reunified, and will surely be reunified, is unstoppable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250918_12724366.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-09-22","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Lin Chia-lung, the official in Taiwan responsible for the island’s overseas affairs, recently visited Vienna, a week after Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s visit to the Austrian capital. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on Lin’s visit to Vienna?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory.\nThe one-China principle is the political foundation of the establishment and development of diplomatic relations between China and Austria. It’s also a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic relations with China. We urge relevant countries to abide by the one-China principle, stop providing a platform to “Taiwan independence” separatists, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\n“Taiwan independence” and attempts to solicit foreign support for that agenda will not succeed. No matter how the DPP authorities try to grab attention, show up in foreign countries, or try to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan,” they will not succeed and no such attempts will ever affect the overwhelming international commitment to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250922_11713277.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250922_11713177.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-23","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","The foreign ministers of South Korea, Japan and the United States have issued a joint statement expressing concern about increasingly frequent destabilizing activities around Taiwan and voiced strong opposition to unlawful maritime claims. How does the Foreign Ministry respond to that?","The U.S., Japan and the ROK made irresponsible remarks on the Taiwan question and maritime issues, which amount to interference in China’s internal affairs and groundless accusations against China. We deplore and reject those remarks.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, which brooks no external interference. The greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait comes from the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. To maintain cross-Strait peace and stability, one must uphold the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle, stop abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities in any form, and not send any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe current situation in the South China Sea is generally stable. China, while firmly defending its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, remains committed to the proper settlement of differences with countries concerned through dialogue and consultation. Relevant countries need to respect regional countries’ joint efforts to handle issues through dialogue and consultation and uphold peace and stability, and stop creating tension or stoking confrontation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250923_11714190.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250923_11714020.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-24","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","It’s reported the Taiwan authorities have imposed semiconductor exports curbs on South Africa, citing national security concerns. Taiwan’s so-called “Ministry of Economic Affairs” announced in a statement export restrictions on the shipment of 47 categories of goods to South Africa to call on the country to have discussions with them as soon as possible. The restrictions will take effect in 60 days. This decision…","The Taiwan authorities’ action is a deliberate move to destabilize global chip industrial and supply chains and counter the prevailing international commitment to the one-China principle by weaponizing chips. Such political manipulation will only end in failure. In recent years, China’s chip industry has thrived rapidly. Our mature chip capacity accounts for about 28 percent of the global market, and the advanced chip sector has produced groundbreaking outcomes. According to South African customs, in 2024, the mainland’s chip exports to South Africa tripled the amount from the Taiwan region. Taiwan’s measures will not substantively affect South Africa’s relevant industry, and will only backfire.\nChina commends the South African government resolutely moving forward the relocation of Taiwan’s institution there. We stand ready to expand cooperation in various fields, including chips, with South Africa and achieve greater progress in promoting the all-round strategic cooperative partnership in the new era between the two countries.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250924_11716001.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250924_11715972.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-24","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Just to go back to the thing between Taiwan and South Africa. Taiwan has said that China applied pressure to South Africa to close this representative office or move it. Would the Ministry like to comment on that accusation?","Upholding the one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. It is also the foundation for China to develop relations with other countries. We commend the South African government’s abiding commitment to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250924_11716001.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250924_11715972.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 24, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua first expressed condolences for the Taiwan compatriots who died in the overflow of the Matai'an Creek landslide dam in Hualien County, and expressed sympathy to the families of the deceased and the injured. He then answered reporters' questions on recent…","Dear members of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Affected by Typhoon “Ragasa,” the Matai'an River barrier lake in Hualien County overflowed, causing casualties and property losses. Here, we express our condolences to the Taiwan compatriots who unfortunately died, and extend our sympathy to the families of the deceased and the injured. We hope the affected residents will soon restore normal production and living order. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed he has “three major missions,” including so-called “facing the Chinese threat, taking good care of Taiwan,” “increasing the defense budget to protect the lives and property of the people of Taiwan,” and “changing the situation where investment on the island is all in the mainland, so that enterprises establish a foothold in Taiwan and deploy globally.” What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te once again peddles the \"mainland threat,\" once again stirs up \"seeking independence through force\" and \"seeking independence by relying on outside powers,\" and once again obstructs and restricts cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, fully exposing his \"independence\" nature as a \"disrupter of cross-Strait peace\" and a \"manufacturer of Taiwan Strait crises.\"\nSince taking office, Lai Ching-te has obstinately clung to his \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, disregarding the interests and well-being of the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. He has escalated efforts to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, forcibly promoting the decoupling and severing of cross-Strait economic chains. Without any bottom line, he sells out Taiwan and fawns on foreign powers, letting external forces take whatever they want. He is rushing down the evil path of pursuing war at any cost, even at the risk of pushing Taiwan into the dire peril of war and danger. What he says and does has already seriously harmed the interests of enterprises and the public on the island. If he does not repent, he will only bring even greater harm to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725432.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","During his visit to the United States, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, said that the mainland should face the fact that the “Republic of China Taiwan” exists, abandon “military coercion and united front infiltration against Taiwan,” choose to handle cross-Strait relations in a manner of “equality, harmony, peace, dialogue, and win-win cooperation,” and engage in dialogue with…","The so-called “Republic of China Taiwan” simply does not exist! Whether in terms of history, legal principle, or fact, it is proven that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and that Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and constantly collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, which is the root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. Their so-called narratives of a “mainland threat” and “democracy versus authoritarianism” are fabricated and completely turn right into wrong. The so-called “equal dialogue” is an attempt to restore cross-Strait dialogue and negotiation without acknowledging the “1992 Consensus.” It is entirely harboring sinister intent and a pipe dream.\nThe “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and negotiation. The DPP authorities declare willingness to engage in dialogue and exchange while vigorously promoting the separatist fallacy of “Taiwan independence.” This self-contradictory approach shows that they have no sincerity whatsoever in restoring cross-Strait dialogue and negotiation; it is mere hypocritical pretense intended to deceive the Taiwan people. The DPP authorities “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” blindly cater to U.S. interests needs, submit without principle, sell out Taiwan without bottom line, and willingly act as pawns. Their words and deeds are truly both pitiable and shameful.\n“‘Taiwan independence’ is a dead end, and unification cannot be stopped.” The DPP authorities attempt to “seek independence through armed force” and “seek independence by relying on external powers,” which violates the mainstream public opinion on the island and sells out the fundamental interests of the nation. They will not succeed and are destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725430.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Hsu Kuo-yung, Secretary-General of the DPP, said, “There is no such thing as a Taiwan Restoration Day.” He said that in 1945, when Japan surrendered, US General MacArthur ordered Chiang Kai-shek's representative to take over Taiwan on behalf of the Allied powers, which triggered criticism from public opinion on the island. The KMT condemned his remarks as distorting history and “absolutely absurd.”…","Xu Guoyong's claims are utterly absurd. They show that the Democratic Progressive Party and the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, in pursuit of their selfish interests in \"independence,\" are blatantly telling lies with their eyes open, arbitrarily distorting history, and have no national integrity at all. They are, without qualification, evil forces and traitors to the nation.\nThe restoration of Taiwan to China is an important component of the fruits of victory in World War II and of the postwar international order. The question of Taiwan's status was thoroughly resolved when the Chinese people won the War of Resistance Against Japan in 1945. A series of documents with international legal force, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Instrument of Japan's Surrender, clearly confirm China's sovereignty over Taiwan. Historical facts cannot be altered: Taiwan's status as part of China is settled. No matter how much nonsense the Democratic Progressive Party and its politicians talk, and no matter how they collude with external forces to clamor the fallacy that \"Taiwan's status is undetermined,\" they cannot distort or shake the historical and legal fact that Taiwan belongs to China.\nTraitors to history, to the nation, and to the country's unity will surely face righteous judgment and the punishment of history. No person or force can stop the historical trend that China will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will firmly stand on the right side of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and foreign interference, and join compatriots on the mainland in creating a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725428.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Taiwan's defense department recently released a new edition of the “Taiwan Whole-of-Society Security Guide” handbook, listing six so-called “patterns of military threat” facing Taiwan. For the first time, it includes content guiding Taiwan residents on how to respond to a “military invasion,” and it specifically reminds the public to be wary of claims of “Taiwan's surrender,” which it says are false information.…","The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” attempting to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence by relying on external forces.” They constantly escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation and seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They have racked their brains to produce and release this booklet, with the aim of peddling war anxiety and intimidating and coercing the Taiwan people. Their means are despicable and their intentions are sinister.\nWe cherish peace, but we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatism. We hope the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan, starting from national righteousness and their own safety and well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence provoking war,” and join us in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and safeguarding our common home for compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725426.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","With the Mid-Autumn Festival approaching, what activities are being held in various localities for cross-Strait compatriots to celebrate the festival together?","In just a few days it will be the Mid-Autumn Festival. We hereby extend our advance best wishes to all our Taiwan compatriots for a full moon and a reunited family, and for good health and happiness for all your households! We also wish all our fellow townsfolk 序大 (meaning “elders”) a full moon, a reunited family, and good health and happiness for all your households (Hokkien)!\n“The moon is brightest at the Mid-Autumn Festival.” In the hearts of the Chinese people, the full autumn moon is a symbol of reunion, fulfillment, and eternity. It is the day when family members travel across mountains and seas to gather together, the most profound and tender expression of longing for relatives and friends, and the most sincere prayer that “we share the same moon even a thousand li apart” and that “our golden land will never be incomplete.” We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to celebrate the festival, and we have also prepared a rich and colorful program of festive activities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople across the mainland. Fujian, which is separated from Taiwan only by a strip of water, will host more than 20 Mid-Autumn Festival friendship events across the province, inviting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in Fujian to gather together and share their family bonds. Among them, “Moon Is Brightest in the Hometown — 2025 Cross-Strait (Zhangzhou) Mid-Autumn Gala” will be held in Dongshan County, Zhangzhou on October 5. Themed “Common Roots · Common Origin · Common Circle of Hearts,” the gala will feature Hokkien songs, scenic re-enactments of cross-strait family letters, glove puppetry, and Taiwanese opera performances, inviting compatriots from both sides of the Strait to perform together under the banner of “One Family Across the Strait,” drawing a “circle of hearts” of cross-Strait integration. Quanzhou City will host the “Quanzhou and Taiwan Share the Moon, Nourish a United Heart” Mid-Autumn friendship gala organized by the Quanzhou Taiwan Association. Nanping City will host the “Full of Mid-Autumn Moon, Family Reunited Under the Full Moon” event, where cross-strait compatriots celebrate the festival together and reunite. Sanming City will host multiple events, including the Hakka Culture Festival in Ninghua, the ancestral home of the Hakka, and the 13th Shibi Hakka Forum.\nIn addition, Jiangsu will hold more than 10 celebratory activities, including the 2025 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival series “Twin Blossoms, Lanterns Lighting Both Sides of the Strait.” Taizhou, Changzhou, Suzhou, Nantong, Yancheng, and other cities will invite Taiwan compatriot representatives to sample local delicacies and celebrate the festival together. Henan will hold the “2025 Meet Taiwan, Flowers in Bloom and a Full Moon” Henan-Taiwan employees’ Mid-Autumn friendship gala. Anhui will hold the 2025 Hefei Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala, themed “Luzhou Moon · Country and Family Reunited.” Shandong will hold the “Shared Heart, Shared Origin, Blended Across the Strait” Cross-Strait One Family Mid-Autumn friendship event. Sichuan will hold the “Trendy Moon-Worship Ceremony” Mid-Autumn moon-worship grand ceremony and the 3rd Liujiang Ancient Town Bright Moon Festival, inviting Taiwan compatriots to experience traditional Mid-Autumn moon-worship customs and take part in the “Lanterns Reflecting the Moon” lantern-floating ritual. Hubei will hold the “Youth Share a Heart, Creating the Future Together” — 2025 Hubei-Taiwan Youth Sports Training Camp and Mid-Autumn Cultural Theme Garden Party, as well as a Mid-Autumn gala for Taiwan youth in Hubei, allowing cross-strait youth to celebrate the “Mid-Autumn Carnival” together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","According to reports, the US House of Representatives recently passed a new version of the “National Defense Authorization Act,” which would allocate US$1 billion for the so-called “Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative,” an increase of more than three times the 2025 appropriation. It also includes provisions requiring the US Department of Defense to cooperate with Taiwan to promote joint programs and inviting…","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We firmly oppose the United States engaging in any form of military contact with Taiwan, China, and firmly oppose the U.S. Congress promoting negative bills related to Taiwan. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop reviewing the relevant bills, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and not go further and further down the wrong path. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail, and that if they dare to take a reckless risk, they will surely bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725416.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Taiwan-U.S. tariff negotiations have not yet been concluded, but a Taiwanese agricultural products delegation recently signed a letter of intent with U.S. industry operators, pledging to purchase more than US$10 billion (about NT$301 billion) in agricultural products within four years. Some public opinion on the island has criticized the Lai Ching-te authorities for offering this to the United States as…","Faced with economic bullying by the US, the DPP authorities have consistently compromised, retreated, and sought to curry favor, allowing the US to demand whatever it wants. Everyone is clear that, thanks to the hard work of Taiwan's agricultural and fishing workers, Taiwan's agricultural products are very abundant. Large-scale purchases of US agricultural products will inevitably impact Taiwan's agricultural product market, undermine the prices and sales of Taiwan's agricultural products, and affect the income of Taiwan's agricultural and fishing workers. This “kowtowing to the US and selling out Taiwan” conduct of the DPP authorities will turn Taiwan into a dumping ground for US agricultural products and seriously harm the development of Taiwan's agriculture and fisheries.\nIncreasing facts are making the people of Taiwan realize that the US has always followed the principle of “America first.” By sacrificing the well-being of the people and the economic prospects of the island in order to fawn over and pledge allegiance to the US, the DPP authorities will ultimately not escape the fate of Taiwan being devoured and drained dry by the US.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725420.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, a poll by the Taiwan Issues Research Center found that 70.2% of the island's public believe cross-Strait relations have deteriorated over the past six months, while only 9.1% believe they have improved. The Mainland Affairs Council responded that this poll is consistent with the MAC's own polls, and that the reason is “mainland aircraft fly back and forth every day, so in the eyes of the public,…","Why was the Taiwan Strait calm from 2008 to 2016, and why has it become increasingly stormy since May 2016? The DPP authorities should engage in soul-searching and self-reflection. In March this year, Lai Ching-te brazenly defined the mainland as a “hostile foreign force,” put forward the so-called “17 strategies,” wantonly provoked the mainland, incited “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and aggravated tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is a serious undermining of cross-Strait relations and the direct cause of their deterioration, and it fully confirms that he is a “destroyer of cross-Strait peace” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nAs for the polls showing that 9.1% of people on the island still believe cross-Strait relations have improved, this is because we have actively responded to the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, actively removed obstacles, and promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. It is also the result of compatriots who hold high expectations for the development of cross-Strait relations and dare to break through the obstruction of the DPP authorities, exchanging them for real action.\nThe Mainland Affairs Council is the Taiwan authorities’ department specifically in charge of cross-Strait affairs. Its primary duty should be to promote cross-Strait negotiation and dialogue and to promote cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. Yet now it has abandoned its proper business and become the vanguard inciting cross-Strait confrontation and obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. The Mainland Affairs Council cannot escape blame for the deterioration of cross-Strait relations over the past half year.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725423.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","U.S. Senator Ted Cruz wrote to U.S. Secretary of State Rubio and Transportation Secretary Duffy, hoping to enable Taiwan to join the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO). Lin Chia-lung, head of the foreign affairs department of the DPP authorities, expressed thanks, saying “the mainland's obstruction of Taiwan's participation in the International Civil Aviation Organization has already posed potential…","Regarding the Taiwan region’s participation in international organizations, including activities of the International Civil Aviation Organization, our position has been consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Taiwan, as part of China, has no right to join the International Civil Aviation Organization. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, colluding with external forces, have fabricated various pretexts to demand participation in the ICAO Assembly and other activities. Their real aim is to challenge the basic framework of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle. Their political tricks and provocative conduct will inevitably be resolutely thwarted.\nWe have always attached importance to the needs of Taiwan compatriots in the aviation sector. The channels for the Taiwan region to obtain ICAO standards, recommended practices, and related materials are unobstructed, and the Taiwan region has convenient flight connections with many cities around the world. Facts have proven that Taiwan’s aviation safety and its air exchanges with other regions have nothing to do with whether the Democratic Progressive Party authorities participate in ICAO activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725414.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Recently, Guan Biling, head of Taiwan's “Ocean Affairs Council,” said, “The mainland's entry into waters under Taiwan's jurisdiction is mostly harassment, not law enforcement; law enforcement power remains firmly in Taiwan's hands”; “mainland fishing boats crossing the boundary have even been found poisoning fish and damaging habitats”; and she hopes to cooperate with the mainland to jointly address marine waste…","Taiwan is part of China. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese territory, and China has sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. Law enforcement patrols by the mainland’s maritime coast guard in the relevant waters are lawful and legitimate, and aim to maintain the order of fishery production, marine fishery resources, and the ecological environment of those waters. If the DPP authorities dare to provoke trouble, they must bear all the consequences that follow.\nThe waters around Kinmen, Matsu, and related islands have long been traditional fishing grounds where fishermen from both sides work together. The mainland side has always attached great importance to the protection of fishery resources and the marine ecological environment, and has actively taken effective measures to promote the sustainable development of marine fisheries and protect the ecological environment of the relevant waters.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202509/t20250924_12725418.htm"],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","On September 20, the Sixth “920 Love You” Cross-Strait E-commerce, Technology and Culture Festival opened, drawing attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant details.","On September 20, the 6th \"920 Love You\" Cross-Strait E-Commerce, Technology and Culture Festival opened grandly in Beijing. This event is a cross-Strait e-commerce public welfare brand planned and initiated by China Taiwan Network and the Cross-Strait Internet Exchange Working Committee of the China Internet Association.\nThe main contents of this session include: producing and launching the micro-short drama \"Ningbo · Encounter,\" carefully creating the cross-Strait integrated tea series of oolong tea called \"Zhi Zhi Li,\" holding the first on-site donation of the \"Reunion Gold\" themed precious metal commemorative coin, and displaying the painting \"Homecoming Picture\" jointly created by a well-known painter and young people from both sides of the Strait. The event continues to center on \"technology + culture + e-commerce,\" building a quality platform for Taiwan enterprises to expand into the mainland market and for Taiwan youth to start businesses on the mainland. Everyone is welcome to follow and take part in the related activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","According to reports, Lai Ching-te recently delivered a video speech at a related event, loudly hyping the so-called “mainland military threat” and fomenting “democracy versus authoritarianism.” What is your comment?","Lai Qingde has made a great fuss over the so-called “mainland military threat” and once again rehashed the old tune of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” exposing once again his obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature and his vicious intent to escalate cross-Strait confrontation. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how they cling to external forces to seek “independence” through provocation, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern and common consensus in the international community of adhering to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","It is reported that former Taiwan leader Tsai Ing-wen recently slipped into Japan for a private visit. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose our diplomatic allies providing a stage for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Japan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question, and should especially reflect deeply on history, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and handle Taiwan-related issues with the utmost caution. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that no matter how they change their tricks to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” they will end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","On the first anniversary of the DPP authorities' “Whole-of-Society Defense Resilience Committee,” they held a so-called “Taiwan Resilience International Forum,” further deepening so-called “international cooperation.” What is your comment on this?","For the sake of narrow party interests, the DPP authorities collude with external forces to vigorously promote “all-people defense,” constantly escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. They are even willing to tie Taiwan residents to the chariot of “Taiwan independence.” We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “seeking independence by force” will only accelerate their demise. We have the firm will, resolute determination, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to smash all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Reports say that some Taiwanese businesspeople on the mainland recently received notices from Taiwan's National Immigration Agency requiring them to provide a written reply within 10 days explaining whether they have obtained a Mainland Residence Permit. The Mainland Affairs Council said of this that the persons concerned should have been reported, and that “it is better to reply as soon as possible.” What…","Driven by its separatist nature of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities keep interfering with and obstructing normal cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel through all kinds of pretexts and methods, creating “green terror” and escalating confrontation across the Strait. Such reckless acts will inevitably meet with strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition from more and more Taiwan residents. We will continue to provide convenience for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland, continue to help Taiwan compatriots who have obtained permits develop on the mainland, and continue to protect, in accordance with the law and effectively, the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots who have obtained permits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, Taiwan’s economic authorities added 279 entities from mainland China and from countries such as Pakistan, Iran, and Mexico to their export control entity list. Taiwanese companies must obtain a permit issued by Taiwan’s “Bureau of Foreign Trade” in advance before exporting to enterprises on the entity list. What is your comment on this?","At a time when the United States is using stacked high tariffs to coerce and hollow out Taiwan's industries, the DPP authorities, instead of actively safeguarding the interests of Taiwan's enterprises and people, are eagerly clinging to and cooperating with the United States in its efforts to suppress mainland enterprises, undermining cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation and harming the economy of the Chinese nation. Such reckless conduct fully proves that the DPP authorities, in pursuing “independence,” care only for their own private interests and have completely placed themselves on the opposite side of the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Regarding the State Council's approval of the establishment of the Scarborough Shoal National Nature Reserve, the DPP authorities claimed that the mainland has no right to “illegally and unilaterally delimit” it. What is your comment?","Huangyan Island is an inherent part of China's territory, and China has indisputable sovereignty over Huangyan Island and its adjacent waters. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, as well as the overall interests of the Chinese nation, is a shared responsibility that compatriots on both sides cannot shirk. The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces to deliberately hype and provoke, have betrayed the nation, which is despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum was originally scheduled to be held in Shanghai from September 25 to 27. The Taipei City Government suddenly called a halt just before the event. Regarding this, there are rumors that it was because the “memorandum of cooperation” (MOU) between the two sides had not been finalized, and others say it was due to technical obstruction by the DPP authorities. May I ask…","First question. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese and members of one family. They should naturally visit each other more and exchange more, growing closer with each exchange. We have consistently and actively supported and promoted cross-Strait exchanges between localities, including the city exchanges you mentioned. The DPP authorities, out of selfish political interest in pursuing “Taiwan independence,” have tried every means to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, which does not win public support.\nSecond question. We are on the broad road of national reunification and national rejuvenation. It conforms to the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and its prospects are bright. The Lai Ching-te authorities are on the evil path of “Taiwan independence,” which splits the country and betrays the nation. If they persist in their obstinacy, they will only fall into the abyss and be smashed to pieces.\nAt present, the Lai Ching-te authorities have escalated their manipulation of ideology. They distort the historical truth of the War of Resistance Against Japan, deny the fruits of victory in that war, downplay and deny the historical significance of Taiwan's restoration, kowtow to the United States and curry favor with Japan without any bottom line, clamor for the fallacy that “Taiwan's status is undetermined,” and even shout that “there is no Taiwan Restoration Day.” They seek to find a basis and pretext for “Taiwan independence” separatism and deliberately heighten hostility and confrontation across the Strait. This is the root cause of the tense situation in the Taiwan Strait and the biggest obstacle to cross-Strait dialogue.\nTaiwan and the mainland belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. We uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus.” On this basis, we are willing to conduct extensive and in-depth consultations on cross-Strait relations and national reunification with people from Taiwan's political parties, sectors and all walks of life, jointly promote the development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of national reunification. As long as compatriots on both sides move toward each other, there will be more and more common ground and an ever brighter common vision.\nThird question. Our sincerity in promoting cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation has not changed. The policy announced earlier this year to resume group tours to the island by residents of Fujian and Shanghai remains in effect. The DPP authorities deliberately distort the actual function of civil organizations in the cross-Strait tourism industry, attempting to politicize contact between the two sides and to make it a precondition for resuming travel to Taiwan by mainland residents. This fully shows that the crux of and obstacle to cross-Strait tourism issues lies in the DPP authorities' interference and obstruction.\nAs for resuming mainland students studying in Taiwan, we have explained this many times before. The DPP authorities have continuously obstructed and restricted cross-Strait educational exchanges and cooperation, ignoring the willingness of Taiwan's education community and young students to take part in cross-Strait exchanges. They have artificially restricted mainland students from studying in Taiwan and imposed unreasonable restrictions on and unfair treatment of mainland students in Taiwan. How can this make mainland students willing to study in Taiwan? Can their parents feel at ease letting their children study in Taiwan? We advise the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation as soon as possible and genuinely protect the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan. That is the right way to resolve the relevant issues.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Taiwan's coast guard has recently been gradually receiving six thousand-ton-class patrol ships that can carry weapons systems for close-range defense missions. Some public opinion points out that the DPP authorities' move is an attempt to turn the coast guard into a “naval reserve,” blurring the boundary between law enforcement and combat. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and continuously collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. They attempt to “seek independence by force” and “rely on external forces to seek independence,” which is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The more they invest in so-called “preparing for war to seek independence,” the less they care for the livelihoods of ordinary Taiwan people, and the greater the harm they will ultimately bring to Taiwan. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “seeking independence by force” is like a mayfly trying to shake a tree. It is overestimating its own strength, and will only lead to its own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","According to reports, the US destroyer USS Higgins and the British frigate HMS Richmond recently transited the Taiwan Strait and engaged in harassment and provocation. What comments do you have?","The Taiwan question concerns China's core interests. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are part of China's territory, and China has sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose any harassment or provocation of the Taiwan Strait by relevant countries. We will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and protect the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Defense Minister Dong Jun, speaking on the Taiwan question at the 12th Beijing Xiangshan Forum, said that “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes will never be allowed to succeed, and that China is ready at all times to thwart any external armed interference. In response, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said that Taiwan is working to maintain peace and the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, but in the eyes…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait, an immutable historical and legal fact, and a general consensus of the international community, which no one or no force can distort or shake. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" and under the pretext of \"maintaining peace,\" they engage in \"seeking independence through military force\" and \"seeking independence by relying on foreign powers.\" They are the disruptors of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the source of trouble for peace and stability in the Strait. \"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will, from the standpoint of national righteousness and their own well-being, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" provocations and interference by external forces, and join us in safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been postponed, and the Mainland Affairs Council and the Taipei City government have given different explanations. Will the “Twin City Forum” continue to be held before the end of the year?","We have consistently supported and actively promoted urban exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait. Shanghai and Taipei have maintained communication regarding this year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups, counties and cities, and people from all sectors to promote cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and personnel exchanges, and to benefit compatriots on both sides with fruitful cooperation results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","According to reports, Lin Chia-lung, head of the DPP authorities’ external exchange department, recently made a provocative visit to Europe, peddling “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies. What comments do you have?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests. We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose relevant countries providing a political stage for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the European side to abide by the one-China principle, handle the Taiwan question prudently and appropriately, and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nWe solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how they collude with external forces or attempt any form of so-called “diplomatic breakthrough” in service of the goal of “Taiwan independence,” it will be in vain. They cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot shake the common understanding and basic framework of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Representatives of Taiwan's tourism industry recently appealed at the first Cross-Strait (Hunan) High-Quality Tourism Development Conference, calling on Lai Ching-te's authorities to lift as soon as possible the “group travel ban” prohibiting Taiwan travel agencies from going to the mainland, and to open mainland tourists' travel to Taiwan. Early this year, the mainland agreed to allow residents of Shanghai and…","We have consistently and clearly supported cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including tourism. Normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and making exchanges in all fields routine is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides. We appreciate that people of insight from all walks of life on the island have actively campaigned and called for this, and enthusiastically devoted themselves to cross-Strait exchanges.\nThe DPP authorities ignore the strong desire of Taiwan’s tourism industry and public for improved livelihoods, strengthened cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and the development of cross-Strait relations. They have racked their brains to obstruct and restrict normal exchanges between people on both sides in pursuit of “independence.” This will only invite greater dissatisfaction and opposition, and they are increasingly losing popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","河南广电大象新闻记者","Recently, the “American Institute in Taiwan” claimed that the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and other documents “did not determine the ultimate political status of Taiwan.” The DPP authorities immediately echoed and agitated the “undetermined status of Taiwan” theory, once again asserting that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other.” What is your comment?","Taiwan's status is very clear: it is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. It belonged to China in the past and belongs to China now. The historical facts are clear, and the legal facts are unambiguous.\nA series of documents with international legal effect, such as the 1943 Cairo Declaration, the 1945 Potsdam Proclamation, and the 1945 Japanese Instrument of Surrender, clearly confirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan. In October 1945, Taiwan was recovered and returned to China, and the Chinese government resumed exercising sovereignty and administrative jurisdiction over Taiwan and the Penghu Islands. The question of Taiwan's status was thoroughly resolved when the Chinese people won the War of Resistance Against Japan. On October 1, 1949, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China was declared established, replacing the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legal government representing all of China. This was a change of regime with no change in China as a subject of international law; China's sovereignty and inherent territorial boundaries did not change. The Government of the People's Republic of China naturally fully enjoys and exercises China's sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The status of Taiwan as part of China has not changed.\nThe return of Taiwan to China is an important component of the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order. As a signatory to the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, and as one of the victorious countries of World War II, the United States is fully aware of the historical and legal facts that Taiwan belongs to China and was returned to China. Yet it openly rehashes the fallacy of “undetermined status of Taiwan,” defames China's legitimate actions in defending its national sovereignty and territorial integrity, maliciously misleads international public opinion, seriously violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, and sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it. We urge the US side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop manipulating Taiwan-related issues, stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatism, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities, by manipulating certain media outlets and several American institutions, staged a coordinated performance that distorted history and clamored for the “theory of undetermined status of Taiwan,” attempting to create a historical and legal basis for their pursuit of “independence” and a false appearance of so-called “international support.” This clumsy trick of self-deception is doomed to be futile and will absolutely not succeed. History cannot be altered: Taiwan's status as belonging to China is settled, and the great cause of unification will certainly be accomplished. No matter how the Democratic Progressive Party authorities scheme to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” and no matter how external forces stir up trouble, the historical trend that China will eventually be unified, and certainly will be unified, cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-09-24","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Regarding the postponement of the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum, the KMT criticized the MAC for mainly stalling over the “bilateral cooperation memorandum of understanding (MOU),” and said that the small pandas and penguins that Shanghai and Taipei were to exchange were also halted on the pretext of epidemic prevention review. Is the TAO aware of the relevant situation?","As I have already made clear, we have consistently supported and actively promoted cross-Strait city exchanges and cooperation, including the “Twin Cities Forum.” Compatriots on both sides of the Strait and citizens of the two cities should indeed visit each other more often, exchange more, and grow closer through frequent contact. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their selfish “independence” interests, are doing everything they can to obstruct and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and this does not win popular support.\nNow I will announce the winners of the fourth round of the Taiwan Knowledge Quiz with prizes. On September 8, the WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” released the questions for the fourth round of the “Taiwan Knowledge Quiz,” and netizens participated enthusiastically. As of September 22, the netizens who answered correctly and ranked in the top ten by likes on their comments were, in order: “Juggernaut,” “Yu Zailin,” “Simple Love,” “Song Rushi,” “Chunying,” “Hupan,” “Chuisi Haitang,” “Zhang Shiliu,” “Wo Shi Renjian Chouchang Ke,” and “Qiancheng.” We congratulate the ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite souvenir, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope everyone will continue to care about Taiwan work, actively take part, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn October 13, the WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” will release the questions for the fifth round of the “Taiwan Knowledge Quiz.” We look forward to more netizens, including the reporter friends present here, paying attention to and taking part!\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all. Happy Mid-Autumn Festival to everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202509/t20250924_12725413.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-09-25","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Lin Chia-lung is in New York having events on the sidelines of the general debate of the UN General Assembly. What’s China’s comment?","We noted relevant media reports. By letting Lin Chia-lung visit New York during the UNGA session, the U.S. provides a public stage for the provocation of “Taiwan independence” separatists, which amounts to gross interference in China’s internal affairs and serious violation of the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués. It sends a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes it.\nThe DPP authorities sent Lin Chia-lung to New York during the UNGA session to interact with so-called “diplomatic allies” and certain U.S. politicians, and make opportunist attempts wherever possible with a political scheme light as day to solicit foreign support for “Taiwan independence,” including from the U.S. We would like to make it clear to the DPP authorities and those bent on separatism that no good will come of their unjust cause and any provocation aimed at “Taiwan independence” will inevitably backfire.\nOur message to the very few countries still maintaining so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan: do not be manipulated and used again and again by “Taiwan independence” forces. It is time to see that the one-China principle is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends. Tying themselves to the “Taiwan independence” bandwagon will not get them anywhere.\nThere is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The abiding commitment of the international community to the one-China principle is unshakable. Nothing will stop China from complete reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250925_11717166.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250925_11716956.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-09-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the 12th Beijing Xiangshan Forum was successfully held in Beijing recently and has attracted high attention from both domestic and foreign media. Could you please provide more details?","The 12th Beijing Xiangshan Forum was successfully held from September 17 to 19. General Zhang Youxia, Vice Chairman of the Central Military Commission, attended and addressed the welcome dinner. Admiral Dong Jun, Minister of National Defense, attended the opening ceremony of the forum and made a keynote speech. The forum was warmly received and well spoken of both at home and abroad. The appeal and influence of this year's forum have been further enhanced. There are three highlights.\nFirst, the forum carried more profound historical significance and showed a clearer vision for the future. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, of the founding of the United Nations, and of the restoration of Taiwan. In particular, President Xi Jinping formally proposed the Global Governance Initiative. Participants at the forum, focusing on addressing global challenges and resolving pressing issues, contributed ideas and suggestions to improving the global governance system, and pooled positive forces to promote global governance through constructive approaches and measures.\nSecond, the composition of participants was diverse and balanced, making the \"Xiangshan Spirit\" more appealing. Adhering to the concept of \"equality, openness, inclusiveness and mutual learning\", over 1,800 attendees, including official representatives, experts, scholars and observers from more than 100 countries, regions and international organizations gathered together, engaging in candid exchanges regardless of the size of their respective nations. We did not stick to fixed positions, but sought common ground; we were not confrontational rivals, but sincere interlocutors who listened to each other. Many netizens commented that this could only be seen in China, and such intense yet harmonious discussions were particularly precious.\nThird, the dialogues and exchanges were extensive and in-depth, with China's propositions attracting significant attention. The topics of the forum were set to provide strategic guidance and address realistic issues, so that participants could engage in meaningful discussions and achieve real results. Additionally, for the first time, the forum organized high-end interviews, hosted a briefing on China's Armed Forces in UN Peacekeeping Operations, and arranged participants to visit an exhibition of innovations and achievements in national defense science and technology. Attendees felt that a stronger Chinese military means greater assurance for world peace.\nA just journey with many companions gets far. The Chinese military is willing to work with all parties to further strengthen strategic communication, deepen military mutual trust, and carry out higher-level security cooperation, so as to provide strong support for global governance and jointly build a community with a shared future for humanity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/09/china-250925-prc-mndb01.htm","",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-09-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's military authorities submitted a budget proposal of over 1 trillion new Taiwan dollars, and planned to once again serve as a dumb cash machine by procuring more weapons. However, a U.S. official recently revealed that U.S. President Donald Trump did not approve 400 million-dollar military aid to Taiwan this summer. Could you please comment on this?","The DPP authorities is called \"dumb cash machine\" every time it buys weapons from external forces. Spending more money on arms procurement will not bring security, but only squeeze out social and livelihood spending and push Taiwan to the brink of war. We hope the U.S. side will abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, exercise extra caution in handling the Taiwan question, truly deliver on its promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\", and refrain from disrupting peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/09/china-250925-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16411977.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-09-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first one is that it's reported that interactions between the Chinese and U.S. sides increased recently, with a video call between two defense leaders as well as a meeting between the Chinese Defense Minister and a delegation of US House lawmakers. Do you have any comment on this? The second question is that Taiwan established the world's first research center named after Shinzo Abe. Lai…","On your first question, at his recent phone call with U.S. President Donald Trump, President Xi Jinping emphasized that China and the U.S. are fully capable of helping each other succeed and prospering together for the good of the two countries and the whole world. China is positive about and open to developing its military relations with the U.S.. We always deal with the U.S. side based on the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation. We hope the U.S. side will work with us in the same direction to build a military-to-military relationship featuring equality, mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and greater stability.\nOn your second question, we all know that during its colonial rule over Taiwan of more than 50 years, Japan committed countless atrocities, inflicting great suffering upon Taiwan compatriots. We celebrated the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and of the restoration of Taiwan this year. Lai Ching-te tries to curry favor with Japan, who once colonized Taiwan. His words and actions are disdained by the people.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/09/china-250925-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16411977.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-09-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The American Institute in Taiwan claimed that documents such as the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation \"did not determine Taiwan's ultimate political status\", and a U.S. State Department spokesperson echoed this comment. In addition, the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council peddled the narrative of the so-called mainland's forcible takeover of Taiwan during his visit to the U.S.. What is your…","The false remarks of the U.S. side misrepresent the fact and mislead the public. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposed to this. The restoration of Taiwan to China is an integral part of the outcomes of WWII victory and the post-war international order. The 1943 Cairo Declaration clearly stipulates that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan, shall be restored to China. The Potsdam Proclamation issued in 1945 reiterates that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. In the same year, Japan signed the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, pledging to carry out the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation in good faith. These instruments with legal effect under international law have all clearly affirmed China's sovereignty over Taiwan.\nAs a signatory to the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, the U.S. is fully aware of the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China. Yet, it blatantly rehashes the false narrative that \"Taiwan's status is undetermined\", and smears China's legitimate actions to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, in order to mislead international public opinion. Such acts gravely violate international law and the basic norms governing international relations, and send a seriously wrong signal to separatist forces for \"Taiwan independence\".\nSeparatist activities seeking \"Taiwan independence\" pose the most serious threat to the post-war international order and the greatest damage to peace in the region. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop manipulating the Taiwan question, and stop aiding and abetting \"Taiwan independence\" in any form. We warn the DPP authorities that \"Taiwan independence\" leads nowhere and reunification is unstoppable. We will never allow any separatist schemes to succeed, and are ready to thwart any external interference at any time and to safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/09/china-250925-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16411977.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-09-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that videos of China's V-day parade were aired 24/7 on many media outlets and we-media accounts in Taiwan, with online views exceeding 5 million. Many Taiwan compatriots praised the development achievements of the motherland and its strong military capabilities. A recent poll also showed a growing \"pro-mainland\" sentiment among the youth in Taiwan. What is your take on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait all belong to the Chinese nation and are members of one and the same family. The 14-year arduous history of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression witnessed compatriots from both sides of the Strait fighting side by side to resist foreign aggression and recover Taiwan. This great victory belongs to all the sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. The purpose of China's grand commemorative events to mark the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War is to remember history, honor fallen heroes, cherish peace and create a better future.\nThe future of Taiwan and the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots depend on national reunification. We hope our Taiwan compatriots will understand the situation and follow the overwhelming trend of the times. They are hoped to join hands with their compatriots from the Chinese mainland, to promote the great spirit of the Chinese nation and the spirit of the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, strengthen the national confidence of being a Chinese with integrity, resolutely oppose separatist activities for \"Taiwan independence\" and external interference, and create a bright future of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/09/china-250925-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16411977.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-09-26","Guo Jiakun","Kyodo News","It’s reported that former Japanese Prime Minister and Liberal Democratic Party’s supreme adviser Taro Aso met on September 25 with Taiwan’s “ Legislative Speaker. ” He said that “Taiwan is a country that shares fundamental values with Japan.” What’s China’s comment?","This is not the first time that certain Japanese politician has made provocations on the Taiwan question. The behavior constitutes serious violation of the one-China principle and the guiding principles of the four political documents between China and Japan and gross interference in China’s internal affairs. We strongly deplore and oppose it and have protested to Japan through diplomatic channels. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation explicitly stated that all the territories Japan had stolen from the Chinese, such as Taiwan and the Penghu Islands, shall be restored to China. That is an important component of the post-war international order.\nTaiwan is a province of China and has never been a country. The Taiwan question bears on China’s core interests and the political foundation of China-Japan ties and basic trust between the two countries. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. It is also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. Japan bears historical responsibilities to the Chinese people on the Taiwan question and should act all the more prudently. We urge Japan to abide by the principles and spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, properly handle Taiwan-related issues, act on its commitment of “fully understanding and respecting” the fact that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People's Republic of China,” and stop official interactions with Taiwan under whatever pretext. Japan must not make any provocation or take any dangerous move on the Taiwan question, and should not underestimate the firm resolve, will and ability of the Chinese people to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250926_11718172.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250926_11717872.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-29","Guo Jiakun","Xinhua News Agency","Ahead of UNGA’s 80th session, several U.S. lawmakers released a statement, accusing the Chinese mainland of “misrepresentation of UNGA Resolution 2758,” claiming that the mainland has sought to “falsely conflate UNGA Resolution 2758 with its ‘One China Principle’” and “diplomatically isolate Taiwan,” and calling on the international community to “support Taiwan’s meaningful participation in” the UN and its…","The Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation explicitly demand that all the territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese, such as Formosa and the Pescadores, shall be restored to China. This constitutes an important part of the post-WWII international order. Taiwan is part of China. It was based on this fact and prerequisite that in 1971, the 26th session of UNGA adopted Resolution 2758 with an overwhelming majority, restoring all lawful rights of the People’s Republic of China in the UN. The resolution reaffirmed that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and there is no such thing as “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nTo this day, UNGA Resolution 2758 remains a valid and relevant document. It established not only the iron rule that must not be bent, but also an absolute principle that is part and parcel of the existing international order. Anything said or done to challenge the resolution amounts to an attempt to shake the foundation of the post-war international order and interfere in China’s internal affairs. Such attempts will not succeed.\nFrom a historic perspective, during UNGA’s deliberation on the draft of Resolution 2758, a couple of countries put together a “dual representation” proposal to create “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.” The proposal never passed and was ditched. What did not happen back then will certainly not happen today.\nFrom a legal perspective, the UNGA Resolution resolved once and for all the question of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the UN. The resolution has extensive legal authority. From 1971 to 1972, agencies of the UN system successively expelled “representatives” of the Taiwan authorities and restored the lawful seats of the People’s Republic of China in accordance with the resolution. The UN Secretariat also issued clear legal opinions emphasizing that “Taiwan has no independent status as a province of China.”\nIn practice, since the adoption of UNGA Resolution 2758, the UN system and other international and regional organizations have adhered to the one-China principle and made it clear that any matter related to the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations shall be handled under the one-China principle. The UN official documents refer to Taiwan only as “Taiwan, province of China.” In total, 183 countries have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle.\nLet me stress once again that the future of the Taiwan region lies in the reunification of China. With a strong and prosperous motherland, our Taiwan compatriots will enjoy broader space for development and they will feel more secure and dignified. Nothing whatsoever will ever stop China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250929_11719907.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250929_11719904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-29","Guo Jiakun","China Review News","The Taiwan authorities have in recent weeks sent people in various capacities to visit countries under different pretexts. Can I have your comment on that?","We have noted the developments.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities send people in so-called “private” or “unofficial” capacity to countries in the name of promoting trade, tech and culture, through which they blatantly peddle disinformation and fallacies to advance their separatist agenda, woo external forces to back their quest for “Taiwan independence” and hide their embarrassing governing incompetence through boastful acts. They’ve put on a hideous show in front of the world only to once again lay bare their nefarious agenda and despicable game. Nothing they do will ever change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, or the overwhelming international commitment to the one-China principle.\nLet me stress again that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. The one-China principle is the prerequisite and basis for the establishment and development of diplomatic ties between China and all other countries. Certain Western politicians, to seek selfish interests, are hellbent on having official interactions with the Taiwan region. That is bound to have an impact on bilateral trust and mutually beneficial cooperation with China. We urge the countries concerned to adhere to their political commitment to China, honor their commitment to one-China through concrete action, make sure that relevant politicians make a clean break with “Taiwan independence” separatists, and not continue to stand on the opposite side of over 1.4 billion Chinese people.\nNothing will stop the Chinese people from realizing our just cause of national reunification. Nothing will cut the overwhelming international commitment to the one-China principle. Any attempt to challenge the one-China principle, the international rule of law, or the international order will be jointly rejected by the entire Chinese nation and the people of any peace-loving country that supports justice.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250929_11719907.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250929_11719904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-29","Guo Jiakun","China Daily","The Taiwan authorities have recently released the latest National Ocean Policy White Paper, claiming that in recent years, the activities of the coast guard vessels from the mainland around Diaoyu Dao disturbed Japanese vessels and fishing ships in relevant waters. They added that the mainland used that to demonstrate their sovereignty over the disputed island. What’s China’s comment?","Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have always been China’s territory. Facing provocation that harms China’s territorial sovereignty, the Chinese government absolutely needs to do everything necessary in its response. The countermeasures are legitimate, lawful and fully justified.\nBoth sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. To uphold national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the shared responsibility of all Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities have called white black, betrayed their ancestors, completely forfeited the national stance, and undermined the interests of the Chinese nation as a whole. Their moves once again reveal how far the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces would go without any moral boundary in order to seek selfish political gains. What awaits them is contempt from the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait and the judgement of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250929_11719907.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250929_11719904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-29","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The Wall Street Journal reported that Chinese negotiators are pushing the U.S. to change the U.S.’s stance on the Taiwan question. The Chinese negotiators are asking the U.S. to officially declare that it “opposes” Taiwan independence. Previously, the statement from the U.S. has been that it “does not support” independence. Can you confirm that China is requesting the U.S. to oppose Taiwan independence? And can…","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is also the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. Upholding the one-China principle absolutely entails opposing “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250929_11719907.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250929_11719904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-29","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Just now you said upholding the one-China principle entails opposing “Taiwan independence.” The U.S. does not uphold the one-China principle. The U.S. has a one-China policy which is different. So is your request to the U.S. now that they change the one-China policy which they uphold to oppose the independence of Taiwan?","I have responded to the issue. We urge the U.S. to handle Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250929_11719907.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250929_11719904.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-09-30","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","A senior official from Taiwan is in Poland and has said that Taiwan and Europe both face the same threat from authoritarianism. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on these remarks?","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is the political foundation for China to establish and develop diplomatic relations with other countries. The principle is also a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. China firmly opposes any form of official interactions between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We urge relevant country to strictly abide by the one-China principle, stop providing platforms for “Taiwan independence” separatists’ activities, and not send any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities send people to countries in various names, through which they blatantly spread disinformation and fallacies to advance their separatist agenda. They peddle the so-called “mainland threat” and “democracy v.s. authoritarianism” narratives, woo external forces to back their quest for “Taiwan independence,” and incite antagonism and confrontation, having no scruples at all about spiking up tension and revealing their nefarious agenda to the world. Nothing the DPP authorities say or do will ever change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, or the overwhelming international commitment to the one-China principle, and still less the inevitability of China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202509/t20250930_11721876.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202509/t20250930_11721739.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-10-08","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Taiwan regional leader Lai Ching-te, in a recent interview with a US radio program, again promoted the “new two-state theory” that “the two sides of the Strait are not subordinate to each other,” falsely claimed that mainland military exercises undermine peace and stability in the “Indo-Pacific” region, and urged raising Taiwan’s defense budget and, together with the “democratic camp,” exerting…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions, saying that Lai Ching-te, once again, is turning black into white and making grandiose claims. Once again, he is fanning the “mainland threat” narrative, peddling the “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy, clamoring about “seeking independence through force” and “seeking independence by relying on external forces,” and deceiving Taiwan residents and international public opinion, fully exposing his “Taiwan independence” nature as a “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nSince taking office more than a year ago, Lai Ching-te has defied the mainstream public opinion on the island, obstinately insisted on the “Taiwan independence” position, blatantly promoted separatist fallacies, constantly incited “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, continuously escalated cross-Strait confrontation and intensified tensions in the Taiwan Strait, and recklessly pursued military buildup and “preparing for war to seek independence,” pushing Taiwan toward the perilous edge of war. At the same time, he has pandered to foreign powers without principle, sold out Taiwan without bottom line, lavishly squandered the hard-earned money of the people, subserviently surrendered to and kowtowed to external forces, allowed external forces to take whatever they wanted, severely damaged the vital interests of Taiwan's enterprises and people, and recklessly sacrificed Taiwan's economic lifeline and development prospects.\nTaiwan is part of China's territory. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact, and it is an unchangeable status quo across the Taiwan Strait. We cherish peace, but we will never tolerate “Taiwan independence” separatism, and we will never stand by while “Taiwan independence” forces sell out and destroy Taiwan. We have firm will, strong determination and great capability to smash all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and protect the security and well-being of Taiwan residents.\nWe solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities that the trend of reunification is unstoppable, “seeking independence by relying on external forces” is destined to fail, and “seeking independence through force” will hasten their own destruction. Any act relying on external forces will bring humiliation upon itself, any traitor to the nation will face righteous judgment, and any scheme to split the motherland will meet firm countermeasures. Reunification will surely prevail, and “Taiwan independence” will surely perish. Lai Ching-te and the “Taiwan independence” forces are no more than a mayfly trying to shake a tree, and they will eventually be swept into the garbage heap of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251008_12727332.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-10-10","Guo Jiakun","China News Service","On October 10, Lai Ching-te delivered an address, in which he once again made “Taiwan independence” remarks, asking the mainland to “cease its distortion of United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758” and saying Taiwan “will work to uphold the status quo” and “ensure peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.” What’s your comment on that?","Lai Ching-te’s address called white black and confused right and wrong. He peddled the false narrative of “democracy v.s. authoritarianism,” repeated the same old fallacies for “Taiwan independence,” and distorted and challenged historical facts and international consensus. These words once again laid bare his true nature as a diehard troublemaker, danger-creator and warmonger.\nThere is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of the Chinese territory. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The biggest threats to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait at present are the separatist activities for “Taiwan independence” and external interference. The Lai Ching-te authorities made up various disinformation in an attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” and resist reunification through military buildup. Such moves will only push Taiwan towards the danger of military conflict. To maintain cross-Strait peace and stability, one must uphold the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Opposition to “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan” and support for the complete reunification of China are part of the international community’s commitment to the one-China principle.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and the restoration of Taiwan. International legal instruments, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, have affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. Taiwan’s restoration to China is an important outcome of the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War. Once and for all, UNGA Resolution 2758 resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the issue of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, at the UN. It solemnly confirms and fully demonstrates that the one-China principle is not only the iron rule that must not be bent, but also an absolute principle that is part and parcel of the existing international order. Any attempt to tamper with historical facts or challenge Resolution 2758 amounts to challenges to China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, the UN’s authority and the post-war international order. Such moves blatantly turn back the wheel of history. They are not only ridiculous but also extremely dangerous.\nChina firmly opposes any form of official interactions between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. We urge the few foreign politicians who are visiting Taiwan to stop interfering in China’s internal affairs and stop abetting and supporting “Taiwan independence” activities at once. These wrongful words and moves, be it for selfish gains or for the malign attempt of using Taiwan to contain China, are all miscalculating, and it is just futile to try to stop China’s inevitable reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251010_11729410.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251010_11729208.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-10","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan will build a new multi-layered air defense system called “T-Dome.” Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","The Lai Ching-te authorities’ attempt of seeking “Taiwan independence” and resisting reunification through military buildup will only push Taiwan towards the danger of military conflict. To uphold peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, one must uphold the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” China is firmly opposed to the U.S.’s arms sales to and military ties with China’s Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251010_11729410.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251010_11729208.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-10-10","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that the construction of “Hai Kun,” Taiwan's first self-built submarine, has run into difficulties and may not be delivered on schedule. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities, disregarding the safety and well-being of the Taiwan people and squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents on “using force to seek independence,” are stubbornly persisting on the evil path of harming, endangering, and ruining Taiwan, which will only push Taiwan into an abyss of disaster. The “Taiwan independence” armed forces spent huge sums assembling a so-called “self-made submarine,” which is utterly powerless in the face of the PLA. This is pure overestimation of their own strength, and will only bring about their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16414538.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-10-10","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Lai Ching-te today delivered a so-called “Double Ten” speech in Taipei. What comments does the spokesperson have on the content of the speech concerning cross-Strait relations?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Only by adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait be effectively guaranteed, can Taiwan compatriots enjoy good lives, and can Taiwan's economy gain greater room for development and certainty through cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development. Conversely, if one departs from the one-China principle, denies the “1992 Consensus,” and promotes “Taiwan independence” separatism, the situation across the Taiwan Strait will become tense and turbulent, and the vital interests of Taiwan's economy and people will be seriously harmed.\nIn his speech today, Lai Ching-te stubbornly insisted on the “Taiwan independence” position, played up the “mainland threat,” clamored about “democracy versus authoritarianism,” distorted World War II history and the UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, attempted to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on outsiders,” and pushed for military expansion and war preparations. What he said and did will only undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, intensify tensions across the Strait, increase the burden on the Taiwan public, sabotage Taiwan's economic lifeline and development prospects, and bring disaster to Taiwan's society.\nThe fact that Taiwan belongs to China is clear, and its status is definite. The historical trend of national reunification is advancing irresistibly. No matter what Lai Ching-te says or does, he cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the international consensus that Taiwan belongs to China, and cannot stop the historical trend that China will eventually be reunified and will surely be reunified. Ensuring that compatriots on both sides of the Strait can live better lives is the starting point and destination of our development of cross-Strait relations. Only by adhering to the one-China principle, opposing “Taiwan independence,” jointly promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and working together to advance the complete reunification of the country is it the broad road to maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots, and the correct choice for promoting social harmony and tranquility in Taiwan and allowing Taiwan compatriots to live and work in peace and contentment. We will unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and together create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251010_12727696.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-11","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: This morning, the Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau issued a “Reward Notice,” offering a public reward for clues to the illegal and criminal activities of 18 core members of the Taiwan military’s “Psychological Warfare Brigade.” What is your view on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to a question by saying that the psychological warfare battalion of the Political Warfare Bureau of the Taiwan military has for a long time used despicable means such as setting up anti-propaganda websites, producing reactionary games, fabricating audio and video content, and operating reactionary radio stations to smear and attack the mainland, promote “Taiwan independence” fallacies, and incite the splitting of the country. The public security authorities issued bounty notices for 18 core members of the battalion suspected of illegal and criminal activities. This is a concrete action to implement the “Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with the Law the Diehard ‘Taiwan Independence’ Elements for the Crimes of Splitting the Country and Inciting the Splitting of the Country,” and is a just action to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\n“Taiwan independence” is a reverse current of history and a calamity for both sides of the Strait. Any organization or individual that serves as an accomplice to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and assists in their wrongdoing will surely be severely punished by law. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide clues to relevant illegal and criminal activities, firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, firmly safeguard national unity, and firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own safety and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251011_12727879.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 15, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua first announced new policies facilitating travel between Taiwan compatriots and the mainland, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent cross-Strait hot issues.","Dear journalist friends, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nTo further expand opening up and make it more convenient and secure for Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland, relevant functional departments plan to soon expand the range of ports where Taiwan residents can apply for mainland entry permits upon arrival to all qualifying ports. Taiwan compatriots, whether flying directly from Taiwan to the mainland or coming to the mainland via Hong Kong, Macao, or foreign countries, may apply for a valid Taiwan compatriot permit for one entry at any of the above ports upon arrival. Details of the policy measures and the list of ports for on-arrival application will be released in a timely manner by the relevant functional departments.\n\"Cross-Strait families are one family,\" and Taiwan compatriots are our flesh and blood. We have always attached importance to listening to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan compatriots. The introduction of the above policies is aimed at creating more open, convenient, and secure conditions for Taiwan residents to travel to and from the mainland, further promoting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation, helping cross-Strait relations advance steadily toward peaceful development and integrated development, and safeguarding the common interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728585.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said, “The Republic of China has merged with Taiwan into one body; without Taiwan there would be no Republic of China.” Without “sovereignty,” there is also no “country.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait, an immutable historical and legal fact, and a common understanding of the international community, which no one or no force can distort or shake. Taiwan has never been a country, and it will never become one.\nLai Ching-te's repeated promotion of the “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy is a rehashing of the “Taiwan independence” position, a clumsy patchwork of sophistry, and even a wanton trampling of the national sentiments of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. It fully exposes his ignorance of historical and legal facts, and his disregard for the interests and well-being of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. His actions will only intensify tensions in the Taiwan Strait, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. We believe that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots have a clear understanding of this, will not be deceived, and will not be coerced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728584.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Taiwan's Global Views magazine released its latest poll showing that the two politicians whose favorability has dropped the most this year are Lai Ching-te and Cho Jung-tai. After the “great recall,” the public hopes that the DPP authorities will strengthen “economic and employment stability,” “maintain cross-Strait peace,” and “strengthen communication with the public.” What is your comment on this?","Recent public opinion polls on the island fully reflect the strong dissatisfaction and widespread opposition of Taiwan's people to the Lai Ching-te authorities' various misdeeds, including unprincipled sycophancy toward foreign powers, a bottomless willingness to sell out Taiwan, militarism, “preparing for war to seek independence,” large-scale “green terror,” and obstruction of cross-Strait exchanges. Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities insist on defying the mainstream public opinion on the island, which wants peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and disregard the well-being of the island's people. They will only cause Taiwan's people to suffer more, be harmed more, and complain more, will only put them further on the opposite side of the island's people, and will become increasingly unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","In his so-called “Double Ten” speech, Lai Ching-te claimed that he would build a so-called “Taiwan Shield” air defense system and raise Taiwan's defense spending to 3% to 5% of GDP. What is your comment on this?","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly hold to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position. For the sake of one party’s private interests, they attempt to “seek independence through military force,” lavishly squander the hard-earned money of the people, and vigorously promote “the whole people as soldiers,” tying Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot. This is the greatest threat to the security and interests of Taiwan residents. They are willing to serve as the “ATM” of American arms dealers, wasting money that could have been used to improve people’s livelihoods and develop the economy on purchasing weapons and pleasing external forces. Not only can this not buy “security,” it will also accelerate pushing Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of ominous and perilous war. The trend toward national reunification is unstoppable. “Seeking independence by relying on the US” is doomed to fail, and “seeking independence through military force” will only accelerate self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728582.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","U.S. Secretary of Commerce Lutnick recently said that he will reach a trade agreement with Taiwan, adhering to the “fifty-fifty” concept for U.S.-Taiwan chip manufacturing. The DPP authorities denied this, saying the two sides are continuing to consult on tariff issues. The industry on the island said the U.S. side is engaging in extortion, which is unfair to Taiwan and TSMC. What is your comment on this?","The remarks of senior US government officials have once again let the world see the true face of the United States, which always adheres to “America First,” as well as the laughability of the DPP authorities’ claim of “the best Taiwan-US relations in history” and the pitiful outcome that their one-sided compromise and concessions only win step-by-step pressure and deeper digging into their soft spots by the United States. Integrated circuits are Taiwan’s most competitive core advantage industry, yet it has now been reduced to a “weak industry” that the United States can freely plunder. The root cause lies in the DPP authorities, who, in order to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” can only kowtow to the United States without principle and sell out Taiwan without bottom line. To borrow from the recently viral online song 《没出息》 that has become popular on both sides of the Strait, Taiwan’s advantage industries should have been “calm, composed, and at ease,” but now they are “flustered, frantic, and stumbling and scrambling.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728580.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the mainland television drama “The Silent Honor” has been airing widely, drawing attention and coverage from island media. Some island media say the drama rarely uses the real names of historical figures and recounts real events, and is intended to strengthen “united front” work targeting Taiwan. What comment do you have?","A TV series now airing has a line, “若一去不回，便一去不回” (“If one goes and does not return, then one does not return”), which concisely embodies the fearless, dauntless spirit with which Chinese Communists and revolutionary forebears sacrificed themselves to achieve the liberation of the people and the reunification of the country. The steadfastness and loyalty, the struggle and sacrifice of martyrs such as Wu Shi, Zhu Feng, Chen Baocang, and Nie Xi will not be forgotten by the people, and history will not forget them! Their ideals, convictions, and strength of will will surely inspire compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strive tirelessly to complete the great cause of reunifying the motherland at an early date and to realize the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728579.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The KMT chairmanship election has held several rounds of debates, and claims that the mainland is interfering in the election have circulated in the Blue camp. What is your comment? How do you view this KMT chairmanship election?","We are paying attention to the Kuomintang chairperson election, but this is an internal affair of the Kuomintang. The remarks of some mainland netizens do not represent the official position.\nThe “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations. It is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the linchpin of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Historical experience across the Strait repeatedly proves that when the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” are upheld, cross-Strait relations improve and develop, and Taiwan compatriots benefit. When the “1992 Consensus” is denied and the one-China principle is abandoned, cross-Strait relations become tense and turbulent, and the interests of Taiwan compatriots suffer. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with the new leadership of the Kuomintang of China to advance relations between the two parties and across the Strait, to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728577.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Taiwan's “Democratic Culture and Education Foundation” recently released a poll showing that about 60% of respondents believe Taiwan should engage in exchanges with the mainland and avoid war. The latest poll by the United Daily News shows that the proportion dissatisfied with Lai Ching-te's handling of cross-Strait relations rose from 43% last year to 63%, and 88% of respondents advocate that both sides must…","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society and the common voice of compatriots on both sides. Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has obstinately held to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, continuously hyped the “mainland threat,” attempted to “seek independence through force” and “rely on external forces to seek independence,” and increasingly obstructed and restricted cross-strait exchange and cooperation. He has forcibly pushed to “decouple and sever chains” in cross-strait economic relations, intensified cross-strait confrontation, and led to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Island opinion polls show that his actions go against public opinion and lack popular support.\nWe hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, starting from the great righteousness of the Chinese nation and their own security and well-being, will join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence provoking conflict,” safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and protect our common home, the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728581.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Shen Yu-chung, Deputy Minister of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that the mainland continues to use religious exchanges for united front work against Taiwan, and that it is now “the one Mazu principle”: “There is only one Mazu in the world. Mazu is an inseparable and sacred part of China, and Taiwan’s Mazu is also part of China’s Mazu.” He said it could even become “the one Guan Gong principle.”…","Both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation. Mazu, Guan Gong, and the vast majority of folk beliefs on the island originated on the mainland, and their ancestral temples are on the mainland. These are undeniable facts. I would like to ask this person from the Mainland Affairs Council five questions. First, is there only one Mazu in the world? Second, is Mazu a Chinese deity who has been revered for thousands of years by people along the southeastern coast and even by overseas Chinese and people of Chinese descent? Third, is Taiwan's Mazu a branch deity divided from the Mazu Ancestral Temple on Meizhou Island in Fujian? Fourth, like Mazu, is there only one Guan Gong in the world? Fifth, what exactly are you afraid of, that you seek to prevent Taiwan's people from worshipping Mazu and Guan Gong?\nThe large number of Taiwan believers traveling to the mainland for pilgrimages, exchanges, seeking their roots and ancestors, and praying for peace are a spiritual need that springs from their hearts. What is wrong with that? The DPP authorities have repeatedly pinned the label of “united front” on this. That very fact proves that united front work is open and aboveboard, and that it helps compatriots on both sides draw closer, strengthen unity, and deepen kinship. Their repeated interference with and obstruction of normal cross-Strait exchanges in religious and folk belief and culture precisely shows that they do not want to see “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family,” and instead want to create “cross-Strait family hatred,” spreading the poison of hatred and fear in order to seek “independence.” Such reckless actions are against the will of the people and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728578.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","In his so-called “Double Ten” speech, Lai Ching-te once again falsely accused the mainland of distorting UN General Assembly Resolution 2758. The Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the mainland side's position paper on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 aims to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, and demanded that the mainland face the so-called “fact that the two sides of the Strait are not…","There is only one China. The Mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided and must not be divided. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all of China, including Taiwan, at the United Nations, solemnly affirming and fully embodying the one-China principle. History cannot be altered, and facts cannot be distorted.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist position, deny the “1992 Consensus,” constantly spread “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, and deliberately undermine the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, scheming to separate Taiwan from China. Their actions seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, severely harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and also create serious obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and communication. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the “Taiwan independence” nature of the DPP authorities as “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises,” join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, safeguard their own interests and well-being through concrete actions, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251015_12728583.htm"],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","A deputy under secretary of the US Department of Agriculture’s Trade and Foreign Agricultural Affairs Department recently sneaked into Taiwan. He claimed the purpose of the trip was to push Taiwan to fulfill its commitment to increase purchases of multiple US agricultural products by 30% over the next four years, and to secure new sales. What is your comment?","Faced with economic bullying by the United States, the DPP authorities, in pursuit of their own political interests, have consistently compromised, made concessions, and catered to and flattered the United States, and Taiwan’s industries and people have already suffered greatly as a result. Taiwan’s agricultural products are abundant, yet large-scale purchases of American agricultural products will only turn Taiwan into a dumping ground for American agricultural products. This will directly hit the prices and sales of local agricultural products in Taiwan, seriously harm the development rights and interests of Taiwan’s agricultural and fishery sectors, and seriously affect the livelihoods of Taiwan’s farmers and fishers. More and more facts are making the people of Taiwan see clearly that the United States always pursues “America First” and cares only about “American interests.” In the eyes of Americans, the true value of Taiwan is as “fat meat” and an “ATM,” and as a pawn and tool for its attempt to contain China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","海峡之声广播电台记者","The defense department of the DPP authorities recently released a report that heavily played up the mainland's “military threat,” claimed it would strengthen so-called “asymmetric + resilience” combat capability, and touted achievements in US-Taiwan military exchanges and cooperation. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, vigorously hype the so-called “mainland threat,” attempt to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence through war preparations,” and accelerate the push to turn “all of Taiwan into a battlefield.” This further undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and sacrifices the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan, once again confirming that they are “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\n“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. In pursuit of political self-interest, the DPP authorities are willing to turn Taiwan into a battlefield and the people into cannon fodder, wasting money that could have been used to improve people's livelihoods on buying weapons and fattening foreign arms dealers. This will only push Taiwan into a more dangerous situation of war and peril. We have firm will, strong determination and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and foreign interference, and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","《团结报》记者","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration. Many films and TV works commemorating this great victory have recently been released, drawing wide attention and praise from audiences on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. The restoration of Taiwan was an important achievement of the War of Resistance's victory, a great victory forged through the successive, bloody struggles of the entire Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. To commemorate this great victory, many film and television works have been released and broadcast recently. Here I will introduce two of them.\nThe first is the historical documentary “Taiwan·1945,” which mainly selects important historical facts and representative figures from the three major stages of “preparation, takeover and reconstruction” in Taiwan from 1943 to the end of 1946, before and after Taiwan's restoration. From the perspectives of political and military takeover, economic and social reconstruction, and cultural and educational restoration of the original, it探寻 in depth the magnificent historical scenes of Taiwan's return to the motherland. The series has 6 episodes, broadcast on CCTV's Documentary Channel from October 10 to 15; it was also broadcast on CCTV's Chinese International Channel on the 11th and 12th, with three episodes shown each day back to back.\nThe second is the historical documentary “Grandpa's Battlefield: Interviews with the Descendants of Taiwan's Anti-Japanese Fighters.” The film widely collects precious oral accounts from 18 descendants of Taiwan's anti-Japanese fighters, and for the first time discloses a large number of precious historical materials, including family-held photographs, letters and last writings from prison. It faithfully recreates the tragic choice of our anti-Japanese forebears, who “would rather see every person die in battle than lose Taiwan,” and systematically presents the 50-year history of the anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots from 1895 to 1945. It vividly confirms the historical and legal fact that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of China,” and profoundly expresses the feelings for country and family of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, who share the same roots and jointly resist external aggression. The film has been broadcast across the internet since September 30.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","During this year’s Mid-Autumn Festival, various localities held rich and colorful festival activities, which were widely praised by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The full moon of the Mid-Autumn Festival symbolizes family reunion and a happy life, and it is rooted in the cultural genes of every Chinese descendant. During the Mid-Autumn holiday, various localities held colorful get-together activities for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Here I will introduce two important events.\nOn October 4, the 2025 Cross-Strait Compatriots' Mid-Autumn Get-Together Event, “Blessings Gather Under the Mid-Autumn Moon, ‘Ship’ Carries Cross-Strait Affection,” co-hosted by Fuzhou and Matsu, was held in Fuzhou. Before the event began, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, attended the cross-Strait Mid-Autumn tea gathering, visited and extended greetings to Taiwan compatriots from all sectors, and then took part in the get-together with Lien Sheng-wen, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Matsu community figures, representatives of Taiwan compatriots living in Fujian, and about 200 Taiwan compatriots. Under the full moon, compatriots on both sides watched performances, sang and danced, and shared joy, together wishing that tomorrow across the Strait will be even better.\nOn October 6, the 2025 Mid-Autumn Festival Gala of China Media Group was simultaneously broadcast on multiple TV channels and radio frequencies of China Media Group and on new media platforms at home and abroad. The gala consisted of three major chapters, “Mountain Full of Moon,” “This Is My Hometown,” and “One Round of Autumn,” and covered traditional Chinese elements such as moonlight, landscapes, instrumental music, dance, cultural relics, and intangible cultural heritage. Through innovative cultural expression, the application of new technology, and integrated dissemination, it fused the profound foundations of national culture with a distinctive spirit of the times. Using the cultural bond of the “Mid-Autumn” festival, it further rallied compatriots on both sides and Chinese people at home and abroad around a shared sense of national and family feeling and cultural identity, and it drew wide attention and welcome. As of October 9, the gala had reached 1.98 billion audience views worldwide, and more than 50 media outlets from Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan had reposted and recommended content related to the gala.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","During this year’s National Day and Mid-Autumn Festival holidays, four “Small Three Links” passenger routes welcomed a surge of cross-Strait compatriots visiting relatives and friends and traveling. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During this year's National Day and Mid-Autumn Festival holidays, the cross-Strait “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes continued to operate smoothly, facilitating visits to relatives and friends and tourism for people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially Taiwan compatriots. According to statistics, four “Mini Three Links” passenger routes, namely Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Lianjiang Huangqi to Matsu, deployed a total of 17 vessels, providing an average of 38 daily sailings and 9,228 passenger seats. From October 1 to 8, the “Mini Three Links” passenger routes operated 296 trips in total, carrying more than 49,000 passenger trips, a year-on-year increase of 193.2%. Passenger volumes on the Fuzhou and Xiamen “Mini Three Links” routes both hit record highs since the routes opened.\nTo meet the demand of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait for visiting relatives and friends and for tourism, Fuzhou, Xiamen, Quanzhou and other places have continuously optimized service guarantees for the “Mini Three Links” routes. First, they predicted passenger flows in advance for the holidays and made use of the online ticketing system. Xiamen promptly coordinated an increase of two sailings per day to ensure sufficient capacity. Second, they optimized customs clearance services. The “Mini Three Links” passenger terminals provide dedicated consultation services for Taiwan compatriots, and port authorities carried out safety risk inspection and management of port passenger terminal operations in advance, and fully opened inspection channels. Third, they held the cultural and tourism event themed “Flowers in Festive Attire Celebrate the National Day,” allowing people on both sides to celebrate together and reflecting the bright prospects of integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","We note that the mainland recently used the “Unreliable Entity List” to sanction three U.S. companies involved in arms sales to Taiwan. What is your comment?","Regarding the US company's so-called military technology cooperation with Taiwan region of China in defiance of China's strong opposition, which seriously undermines China's sovereignty, security and development interests, we firmly oppose it and will hold it legally responsible in accordance with the law.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the national sentiments of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. It is the core of China's core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-US relations. Anyone or any organization that plays with fire on the Taiwan question, including by participating in “arming Taiwan,” will not be able to escape unscathed and will inevitably pay a painful price.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Recently, a mainland musician created the song “Good-for-Nothing” using past videos of Wang Shih-chien, a DPP legislator in Taiwan. The song has become a hit across both sides of the Strait, prompting many netizens to imitate and create their own versions. Wang himself responded, calling it “breathtaking” and “full of vitality and creativity.” What comment do you have?","I will not comment on this song or the people in the song video. I will only comment on the phenomenon.\nI have also watched many versions of 《没出息》 (Méi Chūxi, “Hopeless”), and I am truly amazed by the creativity of netizens on both sides of the Strait. This phenomenon emerged for two reasons. First, compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language and culture, so they can understand the meaning of those few idioms and find the point of the wordplay. Second, it is easy to combine them with one's own circumstances and current events and express emotional resonance. I have also seen many comments. For example, some people think that “匆匆忙忙、连滚带爬” (hurried and scrambling) captures the chaos of middle age, while some Taiwan netizens say that it is precisely “these hopeless political figures in Taiwan who make Taiwan's future scramble along.” Likewise, some people think that “从从容容、游刃有余” (calm and unhurried, with room to spare) expresses an attitude of calm and composure toward life, while others use it to describe the mainland's composure in its Taiwan work and in resolving the Taiwan question. In short, we welcome this natural, interesting and joyful grassroots interaction between the two sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Sanae Takaichi was recently elected president of Japan’s Liberal Democratic Party. In the past, Takaichi repeatedly hyped the “Taiwan question” and even claimed that if a “Taiwan contingency” occurred, Japan would certainly be drawn in. Lai Ching-te posted a message congratulating Takaichi, calling Takaichi “a firm friend of Taiwan.” What comments do you have on this?","We have noted the relevant election results. Japan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. The Japanese side should adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, honor its political commitments on the Taiwan question, and handle Taiwan-related matters with the utmost caution. We solemnly warn the Lai Qingde authorities that no matter how they curry favor and show goodwill to outside powers, “relying on external forces to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","The 2025 informal meeting of APEC (Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation) leaders will be held in the Republic of Korea from October 31 to November 1. The Taiwan authorities have appointed Lin Hsin-yi (林信义) to attend. What is your comment on this?","Regarding the participation of relevant personnel from the Chinese Taipei region in Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) activities, our position is clear and consistent: it must conform to the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","The Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau recently issued a “Reward Notice,” offering rewards to the public for information on criminal activities by 18 core members of the Taiwan military’s “Psychological Warfare Unit.” DPP officials said, “China’s threats against Psychological Warfare Unit cadres are creating a chilling effect.” What is your comment on this?","The Psychological Warfare Battalion of the Political Warfare Bureau of the Taiwan military has for a long time used despicable means such as setting up anti-propaganda websites, producing reactionary games, fabricating audio and video content, and operating reactionary radio stations to smear and attack the Mainland, promote “Taiwan independence” fallacies and incite national division. The public security authorities issued bounty notices for 18 core members of the battalion suspected of illegal and criminal activities. This is a concrete action to implement the “Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with the Law the Crimes of Diehard ‘Taiwan Independence’ Separatists and Incitement to Separate the Country,” and it is a just act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\n“Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history and a scourge for both sides of the Strait. Any organization or individual that abets “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and acts as their accomplice will surely be severely punished by law. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide clues to related illegal and criminal activities, resolutely oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, firmly safeguard national reunification, and firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","On the first question, the Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau recently issued a reward notice soliciting criminal clues on 18 core backbone members of the Taiwan military's “Psychological Warfare Brigade.” It will severely punish those who behave badly in accordance with the law, with the maximum penalty being the death penalty, lifelong accountability, or trial in absentia. How will the mainland carry out…","First question. Taiwan is part of China. The public security authorities’ issuance of bounty notices for 18 core members of the Psychological Operations Battalion of the Taiwan military who are suspected of unlawful and criminal conduct is a concrete action to implement the 《Opinions on Punishing ‘Taiwan Independence’ Die-Hards for the Crimes of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession in Accordance with the Law》. It is a just act that safeguards the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. The public security authorities’ collection of clues about the case through this method complies with relevant provisions of the 《Criminal Procedure Law of the People’s Republic of China》.\nJudicial authorities will carry out investigation, prosecution, trial, and other work strictly in accordance with relevant laws and regulations. In accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law, the lawful rights and interests of criminal suspects will be fully protected. In accordance with the principle that responsibility for crimes is borne individually, family members or relatives of the suspects who are not suspected of any crime will not be pursued arbitrarily.\nSecond question. Regarding the so-called “female agent” you mentioned, I am not aware of the situation you describe. Fabricating so-called “espionage” and exaggerating the “threat from the mainland” are the usual tricks of the DPP authorities and the green camp media.\nThird question. Since the policy on waiving the document fee for Taiwan compatriot permit applications by Taiwan “first-time visitors” was released, it has won high recognition and unanimous praise from Taiwan compatriots, and the number of Taiwan compatriot permit applications has continued to grow. “Seeing is believing.” Whether they come to visit and sightsee or simply to attend a concert or competition, we welcome Taiwan “first-time visitors” to the mainland. We will continue to promote the introduction of more policies that benefit Taiwan compatriots and bring people on both sides of the Strait together, creating more and better conditions for exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nFourth question. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, and ancestry, and they naturally feel an emotional resonance with excellent film and television works from both sides. We hold a positive attitude toward resuming tourism between the two sides and urge the DPP authorities to remove, as soon as possible, the various obstacles they have set up for it. We have also consistently supported cultural exchange and cooperation between the two sides in film, television, music, and other fields, and we encourage cultural and arts workers on both sides to visit each other frequently and communicate heart to heart. We are pleased to see more “mutual engagement” in the cultural and arts fields across the Strait. What prevents mainland film and television performers from going to Taiwan for exchanges with peace of mind is the policies and practices of the DPP authorities, which incite confrontation and hostility between the two sides and obstruct exchanges and interactions across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","Recently, when Lai Qingde was interviewed, he referred to the rumor that the mainland “will not send troops to attack Taiwan” during Trump's term, and claimed that if Trump could get the mainland to “give up the use of force against Taiwan,” he would certainly be a Nobel Peace Prize laureate. What is your comment?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. The future and destiny of Taiwan are in the hands of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, to be resolved by Chinese people on both sides themselves, and no external interference will be tolerated. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position. For the sake of narrow party interests, they kowtow to external forces and cater to them, attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and to “seek independence by force.” This is pure wishful thinking and will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","According to reports, the DPP authorities have proposed a “Taiwan model” to expand investment in the US, building a semiconductor industry cluster and supply chain cooperation in the US. Island public opinion has criticized this as yet another move by the DPP authorities to use the island’s semiconductor industry as a “tribute” in tariff negotiations with the US. What comment do you have on this?","The United States continues to use tariffs and other means to coerce and hollow out Taiwan's industries. The DPP authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests, completely disregard the interests of Taiwan's businesses and people, and stubbornly sacrifice advantageous industries such as semiconductors. The so-called “Taiwan model” is nothing more than a fig leaf for “kneeling to the US and selling out Taiwan.” It is bound to force capital, technology, and talent on the island to keep flowing to the United States, which will seriously harm the development of Taiwan's industries. The DPP authorities, with no bottom line in selling out Taiwan and currying favor with foreign powers, have caused opposition from the island's people and industry circles to keep rising. It has already aroused public outrage and lost all popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Several candidates for the Chairperson of the Kuomintang have recently put forward their cross-Strait policy positions. For example, Hau Lung-pin proposed that the mainland should declare \"Taiwan will not pursue independence, and the mainland will not use force.\" Lo Chih-chiang proposed taking the \"1992 Consensus\" as the foundation and restoring the prosperity of peace across the Taiwan Strait. Chang Ya-chung…","We do not comment on the positions of individual candidates in the Kuomintang chairperson election. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with the Kuomintang to advance the development of relations between the two parties and across the Taiwan Strait, to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, the U.S. Senate passed the annual “National Defense Authorization Act,” which retains $1 billion in military aid appropriations for Taiwan and recommends inviting Taiwan to participate in the Rim of the Pacific (RIMPAC) exercise and to jointly develop and produce drones. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. We firmly oppose the inclusion of Taiwan-related content in relevant U.S. congressional bills, and firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We warn the DPP authorities that “relying on the U.S. to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, some people in the DPP authorities, under the pretext of economic, trade, technology, culture, and other matters, have visited relevant countries and taken the opportunity to peddle and spread “Taiwan independence” fallacies. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose relevant countries providing a political performance stage for “Taiwan independence” elements. Relevant countries should adhere to the one-China principle through concrete actions and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme, or what pretexts they use to lure external forces into standing by them and emboldening their evil acts of seeking “independence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","On October 10, the DPP authorities held a so-called celebration event, claiming that foreign guests from delegations from Japan, Sweden and other countries, as well as “officials from friendly and non-friendly countries stationed in Taiwan,” attended. What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between countries that have diplomatic ties with us and the Taiwan region of China. Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle through concrete actions and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately. The DPP authorities are accustomed to creating the illusion of so-called “international support” on various occasions. Their efforts are wasted, and they only invite ridicule.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","The Taiwan SEF recently said that although ARATS did not directly reply to its request for assistance in providing household registration cancellation certificates and a list for mainland spouses, it learned through the notarization association channel between the two sides that relevant mainland authorities are actively working on providing assistance. Could you further explain the situation?","As is well known, because the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, the dialogue and communication mechanism between the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits and the Straits Exchange Foundation has long been suspended.\nRelevant mainland authorities always handle household registration matters in accordance with law and regulations, solve problems for the people, and provide shelter from wind and rain for mainland spouses. They will never cooperate with the DPP authorities' unreasonable demands that deliberately target mainland spouses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-15","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan's military will hold three exercises in October, namely \"Lu Sheng,\" \"Hai Qiang,\" and \"Tian Long,\" strengthening training intensity and reforming systems to respond to possible potential threats. What comments do you have on this?","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are staging these flashy performances, which are nothing more than posturing and whistling in the dark to boost their courage. In order to “prepare for war and plot independence,” they are lavishly wasting the people's hard-earned money and waging war recklessly. Knowing it cannot be done, they insist on doing it anyway, and are willing to tie the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” war chariot, which will ultimately bring profound disaster to Taiwan. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: peaceful development is the right path, and “seeking independence through force” is a dead end. We have the firm will, determination, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to thoroughly crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes.\nThe question-and-answer session of the press conference ends here.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the core interests of the country and the national feelings of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. Completing the reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters, and work on Taiwan is “a matter of great importance to the nation,” attracting worldwide attention.\nIn order to better explain the central government's policies on Taiwan, clarify the mainland's positions and stances on deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, promoting the development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the reunification of the motherland, and to promptly respond to concerns at home and abroad about Taiwan-related issues, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council's press conferences will increase in frequency starting this month, from the current twice a month to once a week, held on Wednesdays at 10:00 on working days. Live broadcast arrangements on television, online video, and in text remain unchanged. We hope media friends will continue to pay attention to and support the press work of the Taiwan Affairs Office.\nThank you all.\nToday's press conference ends here.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251015_12728591.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2025-10-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US Senate and House of Representatives have passed the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA), which involves multiple negative provisions related to China. Its explicit appropriation of one billion USD for so-called Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative aims to strengthen defense cooperation between the US and Taiwan region and incorporate Taiwan region into the Rim of the Pacific…","The negative provisions related to China in the US NDAA constitute a blatant interference in China's internal affairs. It hurts China's sovereignty, security and development interests, and undermines global peace and stability. China is firmly opposed to such contents. The Taiwan question is the reddest red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. The US is playing with fire by using the \"Taiwan card\". Providing arms to Taiwan is an extremely dangerous gamble that will cost the US a lot. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, truly deliver on its promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\", refrain from sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and stop military interactions in any form with China's Taiwan region to protect the relations between the two countries and two militaries as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251017-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16416311.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-10-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","In his so-called October 10 speech, Lai Ching-te clamored for increasing defense budget, establishing T-Dome air defense system and building \"whole-of-society defense resilience\", and claimed that peace was won through strength. May I have your comment?","In his relevant remarks, Lai Ching-te distorted historical facts and international jurisprudence, and peddled the same old separatist narrative for \"Taiwan independence\". Lai used his whole bag of tricks to pander to foreign power, deceive the people in Taiwan, and provoke cross-Strait confrontation. This is yet another evidence that he is undermining peace and creating troubles. It exposed his malicious intention of selling out and ruining Taiwan.\nIn disregard of the well-being of the people in Taiwan, the DPP authorities keep barrelling down the wrong path of seeking independence by force, and try to embolden themselves with the T-Dome, which is just a castle in the air. Their behaviors are pushing Taiwan closer to the brink of war, and they are the ones who sow choas and disrupt peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that soliciting foreign support for independence and resisting reunification by force will not succeed. The PLA stays a strong force safeguarding the unity of our motherland. We will continue to enhance our real combat capabilities in countering separatist activities and foreign interference, and take resolute measures to safeguard national sovereignty, territorial integrity and cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251017-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16416311.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-10-20","Guo Jiakun","China News Service","It’s reported that Paraguayan First Vice President of the Chamber of Deputies Hugo Meza once again openly called for “a serious and broad debate” to explore possible diplomatic and trade ties between Paraguay and China. He stressed that it concerns Paraguay’s long-term interests. What’s China’s comment?","The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community and a fundamental norm in international relations. Maintaining so-called “diplomatic ties” with Taiwan authorities will lead nowhere. It will not shake the solid and strong international commitment to the one-China principle, or stop the overriding trend of the times towards China’s reunification.\nUpholding the one-China principle is the right thing to do. It is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends. We urge the governments of the very few individual countries, including Paraguay, to see the true picture, listen to the voice of the visionaries, not to turn a blind eye to the will of the people, and make the right political decision at an early date that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of their people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251020_11736645.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251020_11736625.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-21","Guo Jiakun","AFP","U.S. President Donald Trump voiced doubt on Monday that China would invade Taiwan, expressing confidence in his relationship with Chinese leader. When asked about an earlier Pentagon assessment that China’s mainland was eyeing 2027 to attempt to seize Taiwan, Trump said, “I think we’ll be just fine with China. China doesn’t want to do that.” Trump also said he would travel to China early next year. What is the…","China’s position on the Taiwan question remains consistent and clear. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and a matter for the Chinese ourselves to resolve. We stand ready to strive for peaceful reunification with utmost sincerity and the greatest effort, but we will never ever allow anyone or any force to separate Taiwan from China in any way.\nRegarding your question on heads-of-state diplomacy, let me stress that heads-of-state diplomacy plays an irreplaceable role in providing strategic guidance for China-U.S. relations. The two heads of state maintain close communication and exchanges. For the specifics you asked about, I have no information to share at the moment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251021_11737578.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251021_11737437.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-21","Guo Jiakun","Kyodo News","Japan’s Liberal Democratic Party head Sanae Takaichi was just elected as Japan’s Prime Minister. What’s the Foreign Ministry’s comment on that and expectation of the new prime minister? How will that affect China-Japan ties?","China noted the result of the vote and considers it Japan’s internal affair. China and Japan are each other’s neighbors. China’s fundamental position on its relations with Japan is consistent and clear. We hope Japan will work with China, observe the principles laid down in the four political documents between the two countries, honor its political commitments on major issues concerning history and Taiwan, uphold the political foundation of the bilateral relationship, and fully advance the China-Japan strategic relationship of mutual benefit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251021_11737578.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251021_11737437.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 22, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to the TAO's regular press conference. Questions now begin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The mainland previously announced that a conference marking the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration will be held around October 25. Will guests from Taiwan be invited to attend?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. The restoration of Taiwan is an important achievement of the victory in the War of Resistance. It is a great victory forged through the successive, courageous, and bloody struggles of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and it is worth commemorating together by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe conference commemorating the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan is being held to unite Chinese descendants at home and abroad, including compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to jointly remember the history of the War of Resistance, to honor the martyrs who fought against Japan, to defend the victorious achievement of Taiwan’s restoration and return to the motherland, to safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, and to jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation. The commemorative conference will invite representatives from all sectors, including Taiwan compatriots, to attend, and visits and exchange activities will be organized before and after the conference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729896.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The International Academic Seminar on the 80th Anniversary of the founding of the United Nations will be held in Wuhan on October 18. Please introduce the relevant information.","On October 18 and 19, the international academic seminar “The 80th Anniversary of the United Nations: The Future of World Order, International Law, and Multilateralism,” co-hosted by Wuhan University and Benha University of Egypt, was held in Wuhan, Hubei Province. Zhao Shitong, Deputy Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the opening ceremony and delivered a speech. Representatives of international organizations, including former UN Deputy Secretary-General Suárez and Secretary-General Kamaline of the Asian-African Legal Consultative Organization, along with experts from nearly 20 countries, including Egypt, the United Kingdom, the United States, and Russia, as well as domestic universities, research institutions, and relevant departments, a total of about 150 people, attended.\nThe experts at the meeting held that commemorating the 80th anniversary of the founding of the United Nations must firmly defend the fruits of victory in World War II and the postwar international order, resolutely uphold the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations, and acknowledge the historical and legal fact, confirmed by international legal documents such as the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, that Taiwan is part of China. Any conduct that distorts or challenges UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 not only threatens China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, but also challenges the authority of the United Nations and attempts to undermine the postwar international order.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729893.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The results of the KMT chairperson election have been announced. What comments does the spokesperson have on this? What considerations and plans does the mainland have for the next stage of exchanges between the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang?","On October 19, Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, sent a congratulatory message to Ms. Cheng Li-wun on her election as Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China. Ms. Cheng Li-wun replied to General Secretary Xi Jinping the same day to express her gratitude. General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory message points the way forward for the development of relations between the Communist Party and the Kuomintang and of cross-Strait relations. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of the congratulatory message: on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will strengthen communication, contact, and exchanges with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and representative figures, including the Kuomintang of China. We will unite the broad Taiwan compatriots, strengthen the courage, backbone, and confidence of being Chinese, deepen exchange and cooperation, promote common development, advance national reunification, firmly safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, protect the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and join hands to create a more beautiful future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729897.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said public servants are banned from attending mainland commemorations of the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, and requires school staff, political parties, legal persons, people's organizations or relevant individuals to abide by the rules and not to take part in activities led by the mainland or that echo mainland positions. What comment do you have?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. The restoration of Taiwan was an important achievement of victory in the War of Resistance and is a shared memory and shared glory of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This year, compatriots on both sides and discerning people from all sectors, upholding national righteousness and a correct view of history, have held a series of commemorative events for the victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan in many places on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots in Taiwan have actively participated, and together with compatriots on the mainland they have remembered history, mourned the martyrs, and shared the pride and dignity of being upright Chinese.\nThe DPP authorities, stubbornly adhering to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, have distorted and denied the historical facts and achievements of the War of Resistance, and have intimidated and suppressed Taiwan compatriots who participate in related commemorative activities. Their conduct has completely lost a national standpoint, and it has already been, and will increasingly be, opposed and reviled by the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Please introduce the situation of cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields in October.","Entering October, various localities have continued to hold cross-Strait economic, trade, and cultural exchange activities with rich content and fruitful results, further deepening cross-Strait integrated development. Here I will introduce several main activities.\nIn terms of economic and trade exchanges, from October 22 to 25, the 2025 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference and Cross-Strait Intelligent Equipment Manufacturing Matchmaking Event were held in Zhengzhou, Henan. Co-hosted by the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office and the People’s Government of Henan Province, the event took “Intelligent Manufacturing, Integrating the Future” as its theme, focusing on advanced manufacturing, the big health industry, electronic information, modern technology, the digital economy, green and low-carbon development, and other fields. It will further consolidate and expand Henan-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation and exchanges, and promote the integrated development of Henan-Taiwan industries.\nIn terms of cultural exchanges, on October 17, the award ceremony of the 3rd Cross-Strait Animation Dubbing Competition was held in Xiamen. Under the theme “Sound Tides, Animation Brilliant,” dubbing enthusiasts from both sides of the Strait actively participated and submitted 3,256 high-quality animation dubbing works, of which 536 works came from Taiwan participants, and 24 Taiwan teams and individuals won awards. More than 150 guests from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait and award-winning contestants attended the award ceremony, together spreading the cross-Strait voices of youth, culture, and integration.\nOn October 18, the “Chinese Attire, Shared Rhythm” 2025 Cross-Strait Hanfu Carnival, hosted by Xiamen TV, successfully concluded. The event was launched in May and included online and offline activities such as a short video competition, ancient-style garden tours, intangible cultural heritage experiences, an autumn gathering, and artistic performances. It built an exchange platform for Hanfu enthusiasts on both sides of the Strait to appreciate, beautify, and create together, attracting nearly one thousand Hanfu enthusiasts from both sides. Through Xiamen TV, Hanfu clubs across the Strait, and Hanfu enthusiasts’ accounts, the event spoke out in unison, and interactive dissemination was carried out using the event’s IP. Its dissemination on social platforms at home and abroad exceeded 80 million views.\nIn terms of youth exchanges, on October 21, the closing ceremony and exchange achievement exhibition of the 12th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour were held in Guangzhou. More than 1,200 guests, representatives of teachers and students from both sides of the Strait gathered to comprehensively review the fruitful results of Guangdong-Taiwan exchanges in 2025. Under the theme “Coming Together, Dreams Are More Wonderful,” this year’s Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour organized thousands of cross-Strait youth to go deep into various parts of Lingnan, experience the vitality of high-quality development in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, and inject youthful vitality into promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe hereby give advance notice: on October 29, the Chinese Xiandu Ceremony to Worship Xuanyuan Huangdi in the Year of Yisi (2025) will be held in Lishui, Zhejiang. Hosted by the People’s Government of Zhejiang Province, the event takes “Hearts of the Four Seas Worship the Ancestor, Common Prosperity Writes a New Chapter” as its theme. More than 400 representatives from compatriots on both sides of the Strait, overseas Chinese, and all walks of life will attend. Everyone is welcome to follow it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报 南方+记者","The Xiamen Municipal Public Security Bureau recently issued a bounty notice seeking clues to the illegal and criminal conduct of 18 core members of the Taiwan military’s “Psychological Warfare Battalion.” In response, the Mainland Affairs Council said the mainland “intimidates Taiwan residents through arbitrary arrests and arbitrary prosecutions, creating the false appearance of long-arm jurisdiction.” What is…","The DPP authorities manipulate the “Psychological Warfare Brigade” to smear and attack the mainland, spread “Taiwan independence” fallacies, and incite the splitting of the country. The facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive. The public security authorities issued bounty notices for 18 core backbone members of the Taiwan military's psychological warfare brigade who are suspected of illegal and criminal acts. This is a concrete action to implement the “Opinions on Punishing ‘Taiwan Independence’ Diehards for the Crimes of Secession and Incitement to Secession in Accordance with the Law,” and a just act to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nTaiwan is part of China. Anyone who endangers the country's sovereignty, security, and development interests will not escape the sanction of national law. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide relevant clues to illegal and criminal acts, firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, firmly uphold national reunification, and firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and welfare.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729890.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","CCTV’s “Ri Yue Tan Tian” recently named five Taiwanese companies as outer support enterprises for the Taiwan military’s “Psychological Warfare Battalion.” The Mainland Affairs Council said, “The mainland intends to use evil laws for punishing ‘independence’ to intimidate Taiwan businesses,” and that it is carrying out “legal warfare” and “psychological warfare.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The relevant authorities’ crackdown in accordance with the law on the DPP authorities’ and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces’ online activities to seek “independence” is a just and necessary measure to safeguard national security and the legitimate rights and interests of the people and enterprises. Heaven’s net is vast; though its meshes are wide, nothing escapes. Those who serve as henchmen and tools of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will inevitably be severely punished in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities said in a report that “China remains Taiwan's largest external threat,” and that they will continue to “enhance relations with partner countries through comprehensive diplomacy,” safeguard democratic values, and create “added value” for the world through economic and technological cooperation. What comment does the spokesperson have?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, which is the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Under the guise of “democracy,” “economy and trade,” “technology,” and other pretexts, the DPP authorities engage in the dirty business of “relying on external forces to seek independence.” Their so-called “mainland threat” and “democracy versus authoritarianism” false narratives completely twist right and wrong and confuse public perception. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how many petty tricks they play, they cannot change the fate that “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","厦门卫视记者","On the 21st, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council held a so-called “International Seminar on the Situation in Mainland China and Cross-Strait Relations under U.S.-China Competition,” at which Chiou Chwei-jeng and Wu Chao-hsieh once again clamored “Taiwan independence” fallacies and hyped up a “mainland military threat.” They declared that the cross-Strait policy remains “unchanged in determination to defend…","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position and continuously collude with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at seeking independence. This is the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait situation. Driven by their inherent nature of seeking independence, they set up a stage and recruit participants to hold so-called \"international seminars,\" which are nothing more than an attempt to collude with external forces to hype up the so-called \"mainland threat,\" to agitate the false narrative of \"democracy versus authoritarianism,\" and to deceive the public on the island and mislead international opinion. Such a farce is utterly unoriginal and is purely self-entertainment. As for their so-called \"equal dialogue,\" it is an attempt to resume cross-Strait dialogue and consultation without acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus,\" thereby changing the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. In reality, it is creating obstacles to cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, and it is destined not to succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Reportedly, in recent years the DPP authorities have actively tried to seek signing so-called “trade agreements” with multiple countries, but nearly all countries have shown a cold attitude toward the DPP authorities, are unwilling to advance the relevant trade negotiations, or have delayed signing trade agreements whose negotiations have already been completed. What is the spokesperson’s comment on this?","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ attempt to expand so-called “international space” under the guise of economy and trade will only hit walls everywhere and end in failure. Bringing benefits to compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait is both the starting point and the end point of our efforts to develop cross-Strait relations. We have always upheld the concept that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family,” respecting, caring for and benefiting Taiwan compatriots. Through strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integration and development, we strive to enable compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to live better lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Taiwan media reported that Lache, founder of a US defense technology company, recently said that the mainland may take action against Taiwan in 2027. He opposes US involvement in a war and said Taiwan should be turned into a “super-spiky porcupine.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. Relevant remarks once again expose the sinister intention of some people in the US who, out of political and economic interests, treat Taiwan as a chess piece and are willing to destroy Taiwan at any cost. If they are allowed to have their way, they will only push Taiwan into the perilous situation of war and turn Taiwan compatriots into cannon fodder.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. We will never allow the DPP authorities to collude with any external forces to turn this treasure island into “hell.” The US side should abide by the One-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop fanning the flames and adding fuel to the fire in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”和“看台海”新媒体记者","According to reports, some Taiwanese veterans were refused loans by banks on the island after being placed on the mainland's wanted list, which has caused dissatisfaction in the pan-green camp. Some DPP elected representatives said this is the island's banks “enforcing sanctions on behalf of the mainland,” and demanded that the DPP authorities intervene and investigate. What is your comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” is a countercurrent of history and a scourge across the Strait. Any organization or individual that abets or aids the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces shall be severely punished by law and rejected by the people, and must pay the price for their illegal and criminal acts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Taiwan media reported that the Taiwan Judges Association recently sent six judges to Azerbaijan to attend the annual meeting of the International Association of Judges, but they ultimately were not granted visas or entry permits, and did not receive any notice of refusal or explanation of reasons. Some media on the island say the failure to attend was due to reasons on the mainland side. What comment does the…","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a broad consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities fabricate lies and deceive the public; their efforts are in vain and are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","After Cheng Li-wun was elected Chairperson of the KMT, the mainland side said it is willing to promote the development of relations with the KMT and of cross-Strait relations on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said that mainstream public opinion in Taiwan opposes the “1992 Consensus” and does not accept the mainland…","The development of cross-Strait relations has repeatedly proven that the “1992 Consensus” is the anchor of peace in the Taiwan Strait. Upholding the “1992 Consensus” can bring peace to both sides of the Strait, and Taiwan compatriots will benefit. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” deny the “1992 Consensus,” and undermine the development of cross-Strait relations. They have placed themselves in opposition to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and will surely be scorned by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","At the international academic seminar marking the 80th anniversary of the United Nations, two new books were released: “Compilation of Archival Materials on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758” and “Collection of Legal Studies on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758.” Please introduce the relevant situation.","To commemorate the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and the 80th anniversary of the founding of the United Nations, to thoroughly refute all kinds of “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, to firmly oppose interference by external forces in the Taiwan question, and to resolutely uphold the international system centered on the United Nations, the international order based on international law, and the basic norms of international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter, relevant parties have organized the compilation of the “Compilation of Archives on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758” and the “Collection of Legal Research on UN General Assembly Resolution 2758.”\nThe “Compilation of Archives” thoroughly sorts out the archives on the UN's discussions of China's representation and the Taiwan question, clearly showing that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 originated from the one-China principle, followed the one-China principle in its formation process, and fully reflects and solemnly confirms the one-China principle. The text of the resolution does not contain the word “Taiwan,” which precisely further proves that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Erroneous proposals that attempted to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan self-determination” were thoroughly rejected by the UN General Assembly.\nThe “Collection of Legal Research” restores the relationship between UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and the one-China principle from different angles, with standardized establishment of facts, clear legal basis and rigorous logical argumentation. It emphasizes that long before the founding of the United Nations, the fact that Taiwan is part of China was already confirmed by international treaties and recognized by the international community, including the United States. The universal legal binding force of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 has continued to be consolidated and strengthened through the extensive practice of international organizations and states.\nThe truth and legal principles carried by historical archives are forceful and clear. Any act that distorts or challenges UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 disregards the facts, departs from legal principles, and is bound to end in complete defeat.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the US and Taiwan held a so-called “defense industry conference.” “President of the US-Taiwan Business Council” Han Rubo said that after Taiwan passes the “special arms procurement budget,” there will be more large-value arms sales cases, and next year may be the year with the highest total US arms sales to Taiwan. What comment does the spokesperson have on this?","We have consistently, clearly, and firmly opposed U.S. arms sales to Taiwan, China. In pursuit of political self-interest, the DPP authorities are lavishly squandering hard-earned money that could be used to improve people's livelihoods and develop the economy, in order to curry favor with external forces and beg for false “protection.” This will only make Taiwan even more dangerous and perilous in war, bringing profound disaster to the Taiwan compatriots. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that the reunification of the motherland is unstoppable, and that “relying on the U.S. to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” are doomed to be like a mantis trying to stop a chariot, bringing about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","海峡卫视记者","Reports indicate that recently mainland residents who illegally crossed to Taiwan were detained by the DPP authorities. Taiwan's “Coast Guard Administration” stated that it does not rule out that the mainland is using illegal crossing cases for “cognitive warfare.” What is your comment on this?","Mainland residents traveling to Taiwan are subject to relevant management regulations. Relevant departments will handle related violations seriously. The DPP authorities are taking the opportunity to hype this and attack and smear the mainland. This is entirely with ulterior motives and misleads the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Wu Feng-shan, chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said recently that the two sides of the Strait share weal and woe, and that the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits should “patiently persuade your top leaders” to restart the cross-Strait two-association dialogue mechanism. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","In 1992, with authorization from both sides of the Strait, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan, through the Hong Kong talks and subsequent exchanges of letters and telegrams, reached the “1992 Consensus,” under which each side orally expresses that “both sides of the Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” It was on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” that cross-Strait consultations and negotiations began. From 2008 to 2016, the two institutions resumed consultations on the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, signed a series of agreements, reached numerous common understandings, and played an important role in improving the economic well-being of people on both sides of the Strait and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe “1992 Consensus” is the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the linchpin of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. It is the precondition for the authorized consultations between ARATS and SEF. Since May 2016, because the DPP authorities have refused to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” the dialogue and communication mechanism between ARATS and SEF has been at a standstill. If the DPP authorities want to restart the dialogue and communication mechanism between the two institutions, they must recognize the “1992 Consensus.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729895.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Taiwan internet celebrity “Curator” Chen Chih-han recently said he will come to Beijing on October 25. Could the spokesperson share your views on this? Will he be invited to attend the commemorative events marking the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration?","Question one. Beijing is a thousand-year-old ancient capital and also an international metropolis. The song “Welcome to Beijing” expresses the warm welcome that Beijingers extend to guests from all directions to experience the rich historical and cultural heritage and the vibrant energy of a modern city. To facilitate travel between Taiwan and the mainland for compatriots, we have introduced a series of convenience measures. For example, Taiwanese “first-time visitors” applying for a Taiwan Compatriot Permit are exempt from the certificate fee, and Taiwan compatriots who have not obtained a Taiwan Compatriot Permit may apply for a one-time valid Taiwan Compatriot Permit at any eligible port of entry. Now, Taiwan compatriots can “come whenever they want and leave whenever they like” when visiting the mainland. We welcome Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwanese internet celebrities, to come to Beijing and other parts of the mainland to take a look around, to engage in various cultural, technological, and lifestyle experiences, to talk about exchange, cooperation, and the future, and to discover, understand, and come to like the mainland in various ways, sharing what they see and experience and the opportunities they find with more friends.\nQuestion two. The conference marking the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan will invite representatives from all sectors of society, including compatriots from Taiwan, to attend. We also welcome compatriots from Taiwan to join mainland compatriots in commemorating history and honoring the martyrs in various ways, and to share the pride and dignity of being upright and proud Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Paraguayan Chamber of Deputies First Vice President Mesa recently again publicly stated that a “serious and broad” discussion should be held on the possibility of Paraguay and China establishing diplomatic and economic relations, and said the issue concerns the country’s long-term interests. What comment does the spokesperson have?","Adhering to the One-China principle is international justice, the will of the people, and the trend of the times. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme to showcase their so-called “diplomatic existence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the One-China principle. We hope relevant countries will follow the will of the people and the trend of the times, and soon stand on the right side of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, US President Trump said in an interview, “China does not want to launch an ‘attack’ on Taiwan, and it will get along very well with China on the Taiwan issue.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves and can only be decided by the Chinese people. It must be pointed out that the DPP authorities' persistent collusion with external forces to provoke “independence” is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort. At the same time, we will absolutely leave no space for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","TSMC Chairman Wei Che-chia said that it will accelerate the expansion of production capacity and technological upgrades at its Arizona plant. However, some foreign media have pointed out that the plant's rare earth inventory can only sustain 30 days, and if it cannot obtain rare earth supplies from the mainland, its production capacity will be paralyzed. Some public opinion on the island holds that the two sides…","The competent authorities have previously clarified their position on rare earth export controls. The mainland’s high-tech industries are developing rapidly, with new industries and new business formats constantly emerging. This has laid a good foundation and created broad space for cross-Strait cooperation in cutting-edge fields such as artificial intelligence. The semiconductor industry, Taiwan’s advantageous sector, could develop better through strengthened cross-Strait cooperation, yet it is now being repeatedly “sacrificed” by the DPP authorities as a bargaining chip for their political self-interest. Public opinion on the island reflects the consensus of Taiwan’s industry and public: the DPP authorities’ “selling out Taiwan” knows no bottom line, their “reliance on the US” has no future, and it is not popular. Moving in the same direction as the mainland, deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and jointly withstanding external risks and challenges is the right path.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251022_12729891.htm"],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question. General Secretary Xi Jinping’s congratulatory message to Cheng Li-wun, newly elected chairperson of the Kuomintang (KMT), and Cheng Li-wun’s reply both mention “safeguarding the common interests of the Chinese nation.” May I ask the spokesperson whether this is a new “secret password” for cross-Strait relations, in addition to the “1992 Consensus”?\nSecond question: Some public opinion in Taiwan…","On the first question. Our position is very clear: the \"1992 Consensus\" is the common political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to conduct extensive and in-depth democratic consultations on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation with political parties, groups, and representative figures in Taiwan, to promote the forward development of cross-Strait relations, to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, welfare for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.\nOn the second question. We consistently uphold the concept that \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, take the lead in sharing the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization with Taiwan compatriots, actively do practical things, good deeds, and resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, and continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nOn the third question. We uphold the concept that \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" and actively promote personnel exchanges across the Strait, including tourism, and exchanges and cooperation in all fields. The crux and obstacles of cross-Strait tourism issues, including the fact that group tours to Taiwan by residents of Fujian and Shanghai cannot proceed, are entirely the responsibility of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities.\nOn the fourth question. General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory message has pointed the way for the development of relations between the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang and of cross-Strait relations. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of the congratulatory message, and on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" strengthen communication, contact, exchanges, and interactions with political parties, groups, and representative figures in Taiwan, including the Chinese Kuomintang; unite broad Taiwan compatriots; strengthen the aspiration, backbone, and confidence of being Chinese; deepen exchanges and cooperation; promote common development; advance national reunification; firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait; and join hands to create a more brilliant future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nOn the fifth question. Peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. We are willing, on the political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to work together with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, welfare for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation. We are also willing, on the existing common political foundation, to strengthen high-level exchanges with the Chinese Kuomintang, consolidate and enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interactions, respond to the wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and join hands to work toward national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China is being held in Beijing. The session will deliberate the “Recommendations of the CPC Central Committee on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development.” Under the “15th Five-Year Plan,” how will the mainland further advance Taiwan-related work and further strengthen…","The first question. From October 20 to 23, the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was held in Beijing. This session is a very important meeting held at a critical time when China is comprehensively advancing the building of a strong nation and the great cause of national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization. The session will deliberate and adopt the \"Recommendations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Formulating the Fifteenth Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development,\" which will provide top-level design and strategic planning for the development over the next five years and will certainly guide us toward the victorious goal of fully building a modern socialist country. We will thoroughly study, understand and implement the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Party Congress, fully implement and carry out General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, do a good job in Taiwan affairs work in the new era, steadily promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and unswervingly advance the great cause of national reunification.\nThe \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period is a critical period for laying a foundation and making a comprehensive effort to basically realize socialist modernization. The mainland's economic foundation is stable, with many advantages and strong resilience and great potential. The supporting conditions and fundamental trend of long-term positive development have not changed, and the institutional advantages of socialism with Chinese characteristics, the advantages of a super-large market, the advantages of a complete industrial system, and the advantages of abundant talent are becoming more prominent. High-quality economic and social development on the mainland during the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period will provide more opportunities for the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. We will adhere to the development philosophy centered on the people, continuously improve systems and policies to promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, implement equal treatment, and continuously enhance Taiwan compatriots' sense of gain, happiness and security. We will uphold the philosophy that \"compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,\" continue to share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, support the development of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises on the mainland, create better conditions for Taiwan youth to develop on the mainland, and encourage and support more Taiwan compatriots to participate in economic and social development on the mainland, sharing in the development opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization.\nThe great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots, together with compatriots on the mainland, will seize the trend of history, actively promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, join hands to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and jointly work toward the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nThe second question. We have consistently supported and actively promoted exchange and cooperation between cities across the Taiwan Strait. The Shanghai municipal government and the Taipei city government have maintained communication regarding this year's \"Shanghai-Taipei City Forum.\" We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups, counties and cities, and people from all walks of life to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and personnel exchanges, for the benefit of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","On the first question: Recently, NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang and TSMC's vice president of operations celebrated at TSMC's Arizona plant the successful rollout of the first NVIDIA chip produced on U.S. soil, marking the formal start of AI chip mass production in the United States. How do you evaluate the change in TSMC's role in the global supply chain?\nOn the second question: The United States continues to strengthen…","First question. Under pressure from the United States and the sacrifice by the DPP authorities, TSMC has gradually become “AmeriTSMC.” Taiwan’s core advantageous industries are being proactively sold out by the DPP authorities, which will only leave Taiwan even more at the mercy of the United States and further harm the vital interests of Taiwan’s enterprises and people.\nSecond question. The mainland has consistently and actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepened cross-Strait integrated development. It will continue to improve institutions and policies, support Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises in integrating into the new development pattern and participating in high-quality development, and open up even broader new horizons for cross-Strait cooperation in technology and industry. We believe that Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises will surely find a stage for innovation in the process of Chinese-style modernization and continuously create new achievements.\nThird question. The mainland’s economy is resilient, has great potential and abundant vitality. Its scale effects and full industrial chain advantages continue to stand out, and it holds an irreplaceable and important position in global industrial and supply chains. So-called “decoupling from China” will only be like lifting a rock only to drop it on one’s own feet.\nIn the face of an uncertain international economic situation, Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises should take action, turn crises into opportunities, actively embrace new quality productive forces, accelerate enterprise transformation and upgrading, cultivate new drivers of development, and better integrate into the new development pattern, participate in high-quality development, and share in the dividends of Chinese-style modernization. The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, currently underway, will make top-level design and strategic planning for national economic and social development over the next five years, and will certainly provide broader development space and valuable opportunities for all market players, including Taiwan-funded enterprises. We will continue to release policy dividends and steadily expand institutional opening-up in rules, regulations, management and standards, to help Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises adapt to the new environment, open up new markets, jointly withstand external risks and seek greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Taiwan region Vice President Hsiao Bi-khim recently said she has committed to expanding investment in the United States, not only TSMC but also the entire ecosystem and other parts, from suppliers to designers and even other chip manufacturers, all of which will cooperate with US companies such as Intel to enhance their productivity. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The DPP authorities shamelessly kowtow and cater to the US without any bottom line. They have repeatedly compromised and given ground in the face of US grabs and plunder: first TSMC, then the entire industry chain. In the end, they will be “cutting flesh to feed a tiger,” with insatiable greed. The broad masses of Taiwan residents and the industry sector are seeing this more and more clearly, and feeling the pain more and more deeply.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-22","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Cheng Li-wun recently said the “1992 Consensus” is a secret code for passing through, and hoped to have the opportunity to visit the mainland and meet with General Secretary Xi Jinping. Will the Taiwan Affairs Office make related arrangements for this?","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek national rejuvenation. We are also willing, on the existing common political basis, to strengthen high-level exchanges with the Kuomintang of China, consolidate and enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, respond to the wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and work hand in hand toward national rejuvenation.\nHere is another piece of news to share with everyone.\nTo strengthen news release work targeting Taiwan, we have opened the “Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” account on the Facebook platform, which released its first content on October 21. Together with the “国台办发布” accounts on Toutiao and Weibo, the “国务院台办” WeChat official account, and the Channels account, this account promptly releases important information on work targeting Taiwan to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including explaining the central government's policies toward Taiwan and showcasing the development achievements of the Chinese mainland and the results of exchange and cooperation between various localities and departments and Taiwan, helping compatriots on both sides strengthen exchanges and build consensus. Netizens at home and abroad are welcome to follow, and to join in encouraging the development of cross-Strait relations and the advancement of the process of national reunification.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251022_12729860.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-10-23","Guo Jiakun","Yomiuri Shimbu","When Fumio Kishida and Shigeru Ishiba took office as Japanese prime minister, Chinese leaders sent them congratulatory messages. Will China send a congratulatory message to Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi?","China made proper arrangements according to diplomatic practices. China and Japan are each other’s close neighbors. China’s fundamental position on its relations with Japan is consistent and clear. We hope that Japan will work with China, observe the principles laid down in the four political documents between the two countries, honor its political commitments on major issues concerning history and Taiwan, uphold the political foundation of the bilateral relationship, and fully advance the China-Japan strategic relationship of mutual benefit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251023_11739485.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251023_11739394.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-24","Guo Jiakun","NHK","When answering a question about the congratulatory message to Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi at yesterday’s press conference, the Chinese side responded that China made proper arrangements according to diplomatic practices. Can you confirm it?","As you just said, I answered a relevant question yesterday. Let me stress once again that China made proper arrangements according to diplomatic practices. China and Japan are each other’s close neighbors. China’s fundamental position on its relations with Japan is consistent and clear. We hope that Japan will work with China, observe the principles laid down in the four political documents between the two countries, honor its political commitments on major issues concerning history and Taiwan, uphold the political foundation of the bilateral relationship, and fully advance the China-Japan strategic relationship of mutual benefit.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251024_11740246.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251024_11740195.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-24","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Youth Daily","According to Reuters, German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul also said in the interview, “Our one-China policy continues unchanged and we decide on its design. This also includes that there must be no violent change of the status quo.” Can I have your comment on that?","There’s but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China. The government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is the most complete and accurate and only definition of the one-China principle. There is no justification or room for individual definition.\nThe greatest threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait comes from the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. To maintain cross-Strait peace and stability, one must uphold the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” Those who only call for no change of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and do not oppose “Taiwan independence” are actually aiding and abetting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, which will disrupt peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nWe hope Germany will strictly abide by the one-China principle and unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251024_11740246.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251024_11740195.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-10-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, stated on the 24th: Today, the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, in accordance with the Constitution, adopted a decision to establish October 25 as Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day by law, and to stipulate that the state will hold commemorative activities through various forms. This solemn decision by the permanent body of the highest organ of state power concentrates the common aspirations and collective will of all Chinese descendants, including compatriots in Taiwan. It is a powerful measure to defend the restoration of Taiwan, its return to the motherland, and this important historical fact and national glory.\nIn 1945, after 14 years of unyielding bloody struggle, the Chinese people defeated the savage Japanese militarist aggressors and won the great victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. On October 25 of that year, the Taiwan Province Surrender Ceremony of the Chinese Theater was held in Taipei. From then on, Taiwan and the Penghu Islands returned to China’s sovereign jurisdiction. The restoration of Taiwan is an important achievement of the victory in the War of Resistance; it is important conclusive evidence that the Chinese government resumed exercising sovereignty over Taiwan; it is an important link in the historical facts and legal chain showing that Taiwan is part of China; and it is a common national memory of all Chinese descendants.\nIn recent years, National People’s Congress deputies, members of the CPPCC, and many people from all walks of life in Taiwan who are committed to the cause of national reunification have repeatedly proposed establishing “Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day” and holding commemorative activities at the national level. The Party Central Committee attaches great importance to this and has made arrangements, fully demonstrating the Communist Party of China’s firm will to defend national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity, and to resolve the Taiwan question and realize the complete reunification of the motherland. The Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress, in accordance with public opinion, decided to establish Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day in the name of the state on the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. This will certainly inspire Chinese descendants at home and abroad to remember history, defend its achievements, safeguard peace, and create the future together, to carry forward the patriotic tradition, the great spirit of the War of Resistance, and the great national spirit, to more firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and to more resolutely safeguard our common Chinese homeland.\nHistory endures because it is remembered, and justice shines because it is defended. We will take the establishment of Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day as an opportunity to actively hold various commemorative activities and carry out nationwide patriotic education on Taiwan-related matters. We will unite the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan, jointly remember history and cherish the memory of martyrs, work hand in hand to advance the great cause of national reunification, and together create a bright prospect for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251024_12730285.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-24","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, the DPP authorities, on suspicion of violating the so-called “National Security Act” and of attempting to organize on behalf of the mainland, sentenced retired Taiwan military general Gao Anguo (高安国) to 7 years and 6 months in prison. What is your comment on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by stating that this is yet another evil act by the DPP authorities in abusing the judiciary to suppress and persecute patriotic and unification forces on the island. We strongly condemn this.\nThe DPP authorities have continuously suppressed political dissenters, and in particular have wantonly persecuted organizations and individuals who oppose “Taiwan independence” and advocate unification. This is entirely rooted in the essence of “Taiwan independence,” and is for the sake of the private interests of one party. We hope that all sectors of Taiwan society will fully recognize the essence of this case and jointly oppose the abuse of power and persecution of patriotic individuals. We solemnly warn relevant institutions and personnel on the island that if they stand on the opposite side of the people's voice and historical justice, and serve as henchmen and running dogs of separatist “Taiwan independence” forces, they will inevitably face the judgment of history and the strict punishment of the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251024_12730291.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-10-27","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","Premier Li Qiang concluded his official visit to Singapore yesterday. Can you share more information about the visit? How does China view the significance of the visit?","Premier Li Qiang paid a successful official visit to Singapore from October 25 to 26. During the visit, he met and had talks with Acting President Eddie Teo and Prime Minister Lawrence Wong, and attended the China-Singapore Business Roundtable together with Deputy Prime Minister Gan Kim Yong. The visit achieved fruitful outcomes and bears great significance to enriching and developing the China-Singapore all-round high-quality future-oriented partnership.\nThe two sides are committed to all-round cooperation and deeper political mutual trust. This year marks the 35th anniversary of China-Singapore diplomatic relations. The two sides will follow the strategic guidance of the leaders, cherish the commitment made when establishing diplomatic ties, carry forward the traditional friendship, and deepen and add more substance to bilateral relations. Singapore reiterated its commitment to the one-China principle and firm opposition to “Taiwan independence.”\nThe two sides are committed to the characterization of developing high-quality partnership and mutual benefit. The two countries will work for more achievements in key cooperation projects, including the China-Singapore Suzhou Industrial Park and the China-Singapore Tianjin Eco-City. The two sides will improve and upgrade their cooperation from complementing production factors to joint innovation, from bilateral to tripartite cooperation, and from participating in global division of labor to jointly taking the lead in rules-making.\nThe two sides are committed to the “future-oriented” direction and greater synergy of strategies. Premier Li Qiang stressed that the recommendations for formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan, which was deliberated over and adopted at the fourth plenary session of the 20th CPC Central Committee, provide important opportunities for China-Singapore cooperation in the coming years. Singapore extended congratulations on the successful convening of the fourth plenary session and expressed the hope that the 15th Five-Year Plan will benefit the region and beyond. The two sides reiterated that they will uphold multilateralism and free trade and jointly work for greater development.\nThe development of China and Singapore creates important opportunities for each other. China stands ready to work with Singapore to uphold mutual respect, mutual trust and open cooperation, share development outcomes and create a better future while helping each other succeed, and make greater contribution to regional peace, stability and development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251027_11741741.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251027_11741651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-27","Guo Jiakun","China Review News","China set October 25 as Commemoration Day of Taiwan’s Restoration, which received a lot of attention from international media. Could you share with us more details? What’s your comment on that?","In 1945, the Chinese people, after 14 years of strenuous struggle with tremendous sacrifice, won the great victory in the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. On October 25 that year, the ceremony to accept Japan’s surrender in the Taiwan Province of the China war theater was held in Taipei, which put Taiwan and Penghu Islands back under China’s sovereign jurisdiction.\nTaiwan’s restoration is an important outcome of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression, a piece of irrefutable evidence that China resumed exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan, a key part of the fact that Taiwan is part of China supported by both history and law, and the shared memory of all Chinese as a nation.\nIt is in this context that as the nation marks the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, the Standing Committee of the National People’s Congress decided to designate October 25 as the commemoration day of this historic occasion. The designation shows the firm stance of the Chinese people of all ethnic groups to uphold the one-China principle and defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the shared aspiration of Chinese sons and daughters at home and abroad, including our Taiwan compatriots, and the firm resolve of the Communist Party of China in pursuing the historic mission and realizing China’s complete reunification.\nThe restoration of Taiwan is an important part of the outcomes of WWII victory and post-war international order. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus in the international community and a basic norm in international relations. The creation of the commemoration day will greatly cement the international consensus that there is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We hope countries in the world will stay committed to the one-China principle, promote a correct historical perspective on World War II, firmly uphold the outcomes of the victory of World War II, and support the just cause of the Chinese people to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and achieve complete reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251027_11741741.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251027_11741651.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-10-28","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan’s Lin Chia-lung said that he was not worried that U.S. President Donald Trump would “abandon” the island at his upcoming meeting with Chinese leader, and he said “Taiwan-U.S. relations are very stable,” hence why he is not concerned. How does China view this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The biggest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait at present is the separatist activities of “Taiwan independence” forces and the external connivance and support they receive. China firmly opposes any official interaction between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region in any form. We call on the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and exercise extra prudence regarding the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities continues to seek foreign support for “Taiwan independence” and use all kinds of platforms to peddle separatist narratives, spread disinformation and mislead the public. Their moves are rather disgraceful and bound to fail. Nothing the DPP authorities say or do will ever change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China’s territory, still less the inevitability of China’s reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251028_11742618.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251028_11742415.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-10-28","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, said on October 28 that Shen Boyang initiated and established the “Taiwan independence” separatist organization, extensively promoted “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, and has long engaged in criminal activities to split the country. He is an unrepentant “Taiwan independence” diehard. The public security authorities opening a case and conducting an investigation into him is a concrete action to implement the “Opinions on Punishing in Accordance with the Law the ‘Taiwan Independence’ Diehards for the Crimes of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession,” and is a just and necessary step to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard national unity.\nChen Binhua said that “Taiwan independence” separatist activities are the greatest real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and “Taiwan independence” diehards are national traitors and criminals who undermine cross-Strait relations, split the country, and seek “independence” to provoke conflict. Cracking down hard and severely punishing the very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards who engage in vicious “independence” rhetoric and rampant “independence” activities in accordance with the law is aimed at safeguarding the interests and well-being of the broadest Taiwan compatriots and defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots will clearly distinguish right from wrong, resolutely oppose the separatist conduct of “Taiwan independence,” join hands to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, and jointly safeguard the common home of compatriots on both sides and create a long-lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251028_12730830.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Chen Binhua, Director of the Information Bureau and spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, first introduced the new spokesperson, Peng Qing’en, Director of the Economic Bureau. Peng Qing’en then presided over the press conference and answered reporters’…","Dear reporter friends, hello! Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. I am very pleased to introduce the office’s new spokesperson and Director of the Economic Bureau, Peng Qing’en. Today’s press conference will be hosted by him. I hope that, just as you supported me, Feng Lian and previous spokespersons, you will support Director Qing’en in doing a good job with press briefings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/closing)","","Dear journalist friends, good morning! I am very glad to get acquainted with you all. Today is my first time hosting a Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. In this new position, I will promptly, accurately, and comprehensively introduce our policies and measures toward Taiwan and our various work initiatives, strengthen communication and exchange with you, and work together to enhance mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was held in Beijing and deliberated and adopted the “Recommendations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development.” How will the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session be implemented in Taiwan-related work?","From October 20 to 23, the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was successfully held in Beijing. This session was a very important meeting held on the new journey toward the second centenary goal. The “Recommendations of the CPC Central Committee on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development,” deliberated and adopted at the session, systematically plan and strategically deploy economic and social development over the next five years. It is a programmatic document that ensures decisive progress in basically achieving socialist modernization, and it will certainly have a major and far-reaching impact on the development of the Party and the country.\nThe Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the CPC clarified the goals and tasks of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the cause of national reunification on the new journey of building a modern socialist country in all respects. It reflects the strategic positioning of Taiwan work in the process of strengthening the nation and rejuvenating the Chinese nation. It opens broad space and provides strong momentum for doing Taiwan work well in the new era, and it carries important guiding significance.\nWe will deeply study, understand, and implement the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the CPC. We will comprehensively implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on Taiwan work and the overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and external interference, and continuously improve systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation. We will deepen cross-Strait integrated development, encourage and support more Taiwan compatriots to take part in economic and social construction on the mainland, and share in the development opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization. We will unite broad Taiwan compatriots to jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and together achieve the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731169.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","On October 25, the rally commemorating the 80th anniversary of the Restoration of Taiwan was solemnly held in Beijing, attracting great attention from public opinion and the public on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation and its significance.","On the morning of October 25, the conference commemorating the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration was held in Beijing. Wang Huning (王沪宁), member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, attended and delivered a speech. The commemorative conference thoroughly implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech at the conference commemorating the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, under the theme of “Remembering History Together, Defending Achievements, Safeguarding Our Homeland, Creating the Future Together.” About 500 representatives from all walks of life, including Taiwan compatriots, attended.\nThe victory in the War of Resistance and the Restoration of Taiwan are great victories of the entire nation and a great glory shared by the Chinese people and the Chinese nation. The conference explained the important significance of the Party and state establishing the Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, and called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly shoulder historical responsibility, jointly safeguard the major achievements of the victory in the War of Resistance, carry forward the national spirit with patriotism at its core, adhere to the basic policy of “peaceful reunification, one country, two systems,” adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” adhere to promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and deepening cross-Strait exchanges and integration, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, forge a strong sense of the community of the Chinese nation, safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, share the bright prospects of national reunification, and jointly create the glorious undertaking of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe conference drew high attention from compatriots on both sides of the Strait and triggered strong reactions. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will thoroughly implement the decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee and the spirit of the conference, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and strive together to realize the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731167.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, attended the conference marking the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and delivered a speech stating that achieving unification by peaceful means is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and to the entire Chinese nation, and that after peaceful…","General Secretary Xi Jinping pointed out, “‘Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems’ is the best way to achieve national reunification. It embodies the Chinese wisdom of embracing all rivers and the breadth of great tolerance. It fully takes into account Taiwan’s actual situation and is conducive to Taiwan’s long-term stability and security after reunification.” Peaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan’s economic and social development and will bring real benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The mainland has a large population, a vast market, and strong industries, and it can fully accommodate products and enterprises from Taiwan. Drawing on the mainland’s super-large market and economies of scale, combined with Taiwan’s own technological strengths and talent advantages, Taiwan’s economic development will regain new vitality. With cross-Strait interconnection and full connectivity, Taiwan’s energy and resource security will be strengthened and its infrastructure construction will develop. Sharing public services and public resources across the Strait will bring more convenience to the lives of Taiwan compatriots and allow them to share the achievements of Chinese-style modernization. In the inheritance and nurturing of Chinese culture, the creativity of Taiwan compatriots will be fully stimulated, and their spiritual and cultural life will become even richer and more colorful. With a strong motherland as their backing, Taiwan’s security and development interests will be fully protected, and Taiwan compatriots will stand taller and more confidently in the international arena, safer and with greater dignity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731164.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","On October 24, the 18th session of the Standing Committee of the 14th National People's Congress adopted a decision to establish October 25 as Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day by law. Recently, overseas Chinese and compatriots in Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan have held commemorative activities one after another, actively supporting the above decision. What comment do you have?","On the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, the establishment of Taiwan Restoration Day as a national commemorative day demonstrates the unwavering position of all the nation's ethnic groups in upholding the one-China principle and defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It is also the shared wish of Chinese people at home and abroad, including compatriots in Taiwan.\nAccording to incomplete statistics, as of October 28, Chinese embassies, consulates, and missions in more than 30 countries, including the United States, Russia, the United Kingdom, and France, held commemorative activities. Overseas Chinese and Taiwan compatriots residing in Hong Kong and Macao also spontaneously expressed their support for the relevant decision of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress through forums, statements, and other means. This fully demonstrates the firm will and strong determination of all Chinese people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it also fully reflects and effectively consolidates the broad international consensus that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China.\nResolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will unite broad Taiwan compatriots, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and work together with one heart to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”、“看台海”和“日月谭天”记者","On October 24, the 18th session of the Standing Committee of the 14th National People's Congress made a decision to establish October 25 as Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day by law. What is the significance of establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day?","In recent years, National People's Congress deputies, members of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, and many representatives of Taiwan communities dedicated to the cause of national reunification have repeatedly proposed establishing a Taiwan Restoration Day and holding commemorative activities at the national level. The Party Central Committee attaches great importance to this, General Secretary Xi Jinping personally made the decision, and the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress strictly followed legal procedures, deliberated and adopted the relevant decision to establish Taiwan Restoration Day in the name of the state on the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. This fully accords with the wishes of the people and embodies the will of the state. It highlights the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and it declares the firm determination of all Chinese ethnic groups to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification. It reflects the common consensus of the international community to uphold the one-China principle, and it will surely lead compatriots on both sides of the Strait to inherit and carry forward the patriotic tradition and the great spirit of the War of Resistance and the great national spirit, and inspire all sons and daughters of China to unite and strive for national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731168.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","The “Taiwan Public Opinion Foundation” released its October poll, showing that Lai Ching-te’s satisfaction with his governance remains persistently low. As many as 53% of the public “disagree” with his governing approach, and 27% say they “strongly disagree,” indicating that public resentment on the island continues. What comment do you have?","Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly insisted on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, disregarding the interests and well-being of broad Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. He has grown ever more extreme in obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and has forcibly pushed to decouple and sever cross-Strait economic chains. Without any bottom line, he sells out Taiwan and curries favor with foreigners, allowing external forces to take whatever they want. He races down the evil path of warmongering, not hesitating to push Taiwan into the peril of war. Poll results fully confirm that Lai Ching-te’s conduct is unpopular. If he insists on his own way, he will only harm Taiwan even more and provoke greater public resentment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that the mainland’s demand that Taiwan accept the “1992 Consensus” means that Taiwan is part of China. Based on the so-called “sovereignty and democracy of Taiwan,” the DPP authorities will not accept this political premise. What is your comment?","In 1992, after consultation, the two sides across the Taiwan Strait reached a consensus, expressed orally by each side, that “both sides of the Strait adhere to one China,” namely the “1992 Consensus.” The “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation and the linchpin of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Upholding the “1992 Consensus” allows cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, and allows Taiwan compatriots to benefit. Denying the “1992 Consensus” and deviating from the one-China principle will make cross-Strait relations tense and turbulent and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities have for a long time smeared, fabricated rumors about, and stigmatized the “1992 Consensus,” seriously undermining the common political foundation of cross-Strait relations and harming the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will correctly understand the important significance of the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely resist “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, and work hand in hand with compatriots on the mainland to promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and jointly create a bright future for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","The US think tank RAND Corporation recently published a report pointing out that the provocative words and actions of the Lai Qingde authorities have invited strong countermeasures from the mainland. The US should not allow the Lai authorities to take measures that may anger the mainland by relying on US support. It should urge the Lai authorities to ensure they do not aggravate cross-Strait tensions or undermine…","Relevant reports indicate that more and more people internationally have come to recognize Lai Ching-te as a “troublemaker” and a “peace breaker.” To maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, it is necessary to stop Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities from plotting “independence” and provoking confrontation. Only by achieving unification can peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait be fundamentally guaranteed.\nTaiwan is Chinese Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait to settle themselves, and no foreign interference will be tolerated. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and, with the utmost sincerity and greatest effort, strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. However, we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is directed at “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","The head of Taiwan's defense department recently admitted that it is very difficult for the F-16 fighter jets purchased from the US to be delivered on schedule, and for the Taiwan military's self-built submarine to be completed and delivered. Some island public opinion points out that the defense department's high budget is seriously inflated, and an official said, “A few pieces of paper can cheat several hundred…","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and seek to “pursue independence by force” and “pursue independence by relying on foreign powers.” This is pure wishful thinking and a dead end. Under the banner of “strengthening defense,” they lavishly squander the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people, and it is full of shady dealings that cannot be disclosed. Taiwan’s people deeply loathe this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have stepped up efforts to investigate the possession of mainland identity documents by civil servants on the island. What comments do you have on this? Can the outside world find a way to obtain information from the mainland side on whether Taiwan compatriots hold mainland identity documents?","Taiwan residents’ voluntary application for mainland identity documents is a lawful right they enjoy. Our handling of relevant certificates for Taiwan compatriots to travel to the mainland or to study, work, start businesses, or live on the mainland is intended to provide better services and convenience for everyone, and it has been widely praised by Taiwan compatriots, who consider them useful, practical, and easy to use.\nThe DPP authorities have adopted various means to threaten and intimidate Taiwan compatriots, creating a “green terror” and obstructing and undermining closer ties between people on both sides of the Strait. Their actions seriously infringe on the personal privacy of Taiwan compatriots and do not have public support. I must emphasize again that information on Taiwan compatriots’ applications for various mainland certificates and the certificate information itself are strictly protected by the relevant departments and cannot be accessed by outsiders.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Regarding the mainland's establishment of Taiwan Restoration Day, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said, “‘Taiwan Restoration Day’ commemorates October 25, 1945, when the ‘Republic of China,’ as representative of the Allies, accepted the surrender of Japanese troops in Taiwan. It has ‘nothing to do with the People's Republic of China, and nothing to do with the CCP, which made no positive contribution to…","The victory of the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan are great victories of the entire nation and a shared glory of the Chinese people and the Chinese nation.\nDuring the War of Resistance, the Communist Party of China held high the banner of the Anti-Japanese National United Front, adhered to the line of all-out resistance, formulated correct strategies and tactics, and opened up vast battlefields behind enemy lines, becoming the mainstay in sustaining the resistance. The battlefields behind enemy lines led by the Communist Party of China and the frontline battlefields led by the Kuomintang coordinated with each other and attacked the enemy from both sides, forming a strategic posture jointly resisting Japanese aggression. The Communist Party of China clearly put forward the proposal to recover Taiwan, guided and helped Taiwan compatriots organize armed anti-Japanese forces such as the Taiwan Volunteer Corps, and supported and promoted the movement to restore Taiwan. The restoration of Taiwan is worth being remembered and upheld jointly by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Public opinion has noted that the communiqué of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China emphasized “promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the great cause of national reunification,” without mentioning “peaceful reunification.” What is the implication of this?","Our major policy toward Taiwan is consistent and clear. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification. We are willing to create broad room for peaceful reunification and will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort. However, we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. Peaceful reunification requires the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, moving toward each other. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will join us in resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, firmly and unswervingly advancing the great cause of national reunification, jointly creating lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and sharing the glory of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","October 25 is the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s Restoration Day. On that day, Lai Ching-te released a video touting the so-called “Battle of Guningtou” and other events, saying that “peace must rely on strength, and a single agreement cannot achieve true peace.” What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te's words and deeds not only expose his lack of reverence for history and his betrayal of the nation, but also expose his delusional attempts to “resist unification by force” and “seek independence by force.” “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable like fire and water; only the unification of the two sides can forever keep Taiwan at peace.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The TAO spokesperson recently opened an account on Facebook, which drew attention from Taiwan netizens. The Mainland Affairs Council reminded the public that if anyone cooperates with relevant mainland reward notices by providing clues or reporting through Facebook's private messaging function, they may face more than seven years of imprisonment. What comment do you have?","After the Facebook account of the “spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” was launched, it received many messages of blessing and support from netizens on the island, and some netizens also left messages hoping to help find relatives on the mainland. This reflects the concern of Taiwan compatriots about the development of cross-Strait relations, their need for access to accurate information, and their heartfelt desire to enhance friendship among compatriots. We take every message seriously and will continue to make good use of this new communication platform to do more practical good deeds and help solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots.\nThe DPP authorities are treating this as a formidable enemy, resorting to threats and intimidation, which seriously infringes on the basic rights of Taiwan compatriots and fully exposes the hypocritical nature of their touted “freedom of speech.” “Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history and a scourge for cross-Strait relations. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide relevant clues to illegal and criminal activities, and we will strictly protect the information and legitimate rights and interests of whistleblowers in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","What recent cross-Strait economic, trade and cultural exchange activities have there been?","Recently, cross-Strait economic, trade, and cultural exchange activities have continued to be lively. Following the Henan–Taiwan meeting, this morning (October 29), the 16th Tianjin–Taiwan Investment and Cooperation Negotiation Conference opened in Tianjin. It was co-hosted by the Tianjin Municipal People's Government, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Straits Exchange Association, and the Tianjin Municipal Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference. During the conference, activities including a cross-Strait youth employment and entrepreneurship development exchange meeting, a Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei and Taiwan health industry exchange meeting, the 5th Haihe Forum on the Cross-Strait Common Market, and key industry matchmaking and inspection tours will be held. Around 800 participants attended, including senior Taiwan political and business figures, heads of industry associations and major enterprises, as well as the heads of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, and some Taiwan-invested enterprise associations.\nIn terms of cultural exchange, the 16th Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industry Expo and Trade Fair will be held in Xiamen from October 30 to November 2. This edition focuses on promoting cross-Strait exchanges. The scale of Taiwan's participation has been further expanded, with 12 cross-Strait themed exhibitions being set up, including an exhibition on the achievements of integrated development of rural construction and rural innovation in Fujian and Taiwan. More than 200 cross-Strait themed activities, including industry matchmaking, academic seminars, youth exchanges, and intangible cultural heritage displays, will be held simultaneously.\nFrom October 28 to 30, the inaugural Straits Cross-Strait Tea Development Forum, co-hosted by the Institute of Ethnic Literature and the Intangible Cultural Heritage Research Center of the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences and the Straits Economic and Technological Cooperation Center, was held in Haicang District, Xiamen. The forum aims to deepen cross-Strait tea culture exchanges and cooperation and promote the sustainable development of the tea industry. Representatives of Taiwan tea-related industry associations, tea merchants, and other cross-Strait tea sector figures attended.\nFrom October 31 to November 2, the 10th World Mazu Culture Forum will be held in Putian City, Fujian. This year, the forum will set up 11 sub-venues both at home and abroad for the first time. Experts, scholars, youth representatives from around the world, overseas Chinese, and compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan will gather together to build a comprehensive international humanities exchange platform that integrates culture, academics, economy and trade, and youth exchange. In addition, Putian City will also hold a series of folk customs activities commemorating the 1,038th anniversary of Mazu's ascension to immortality from October 29 to 31.\nFrom November 2 to 4, the Zhu Xi Culture Promotion Week, commemorating the 895th anniversary of Zhu Xi's birth, will be held in Youxi, Sanming, Fujian. About 150 cross-Strait experts, scholars, and industry representatives will, through cultural experiences, academic seminars, and industrial integration, help link cross-Strait industries and inject new momentum into the inheritance and innovation of Zhu Xi culture and the coordinated development of cross-Strait rural areas.\nWe welcome cross-Strait media reporters to visit and report on these events at that time.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Recently, the U.S. Senate Foreign Relations Committee voted to approve four negative Taiwan-related bills, including the so-called “Porcupine” and “Taiwan International Solidarity” acts, which clamor for simplifying the procedures for arms sales to Taiwan so that Taiwan enjoys the same treatment as NATO allies. The DPP authorities welcomed this and said they look forward to the U.S. government implementing arms…","We firmly oppose the US Congress's promotion of negative Taiwan-related bills, and we firmly oppose any form of official exchanges and military contacts between the US and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop “arming Taiwan,” stop deliberating relevant bills, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs. The DPP authorities, scheming to “seek independence through force” and “prepare for war to seek independence,” shamelessly beg for false “protection” from external forces. This will only make Taiwan more dangerous and more prone to war, and it will sacrifice the safety and well-being of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","During the first Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, besides holding a conference marking the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, what other commemorative activities did the Mainland hold?","The restoration of Taiwan is important conclusive evidence that the Chinese government resumed exercising sovereignty over Taiwan. It is an important link in the historical fact and legal chain that Taiwan is part of China, and it is a shared glory of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and a shared national memory of all Chinese people. The state has, by law, designated October 25 as Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. This has drawn close attention and enthusiastic responses from all sectors on both sides of the Strait. In recent days, relevant departments and localities have held various forms of celebrations and commemorative events, in which Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life have eagerly taken part.\nThe CPC Central Committee Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a reception to mark the establishment of Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. The exhibition 《Indomitable Treasure Island, Loyal Hearts Toward the Motherland: Exhibition on the History of Taiwan Compatriots’ Resistance to Japan》 opened at the Memorial Hall of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression. The Central Committee of the Revolutionary Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang held a symposium titled “Remember History, Create the Future: Symposium on Establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day.” The Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League convened a symposium on establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, and held a themed special exhibition and the concert 《Forging the National Spirit Together: Concert on Establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day》. The All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots held a series of celebration activities for Taiwan compatriots from all sectors to mark the establishment of Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. The Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Research Institute of Tsinghua University jointly held a symposium on the theme “The Significance of the State Establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day.” Jiangsu Province held a “Special Symposium on Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day” at the Memorial Hall of the Compatriots Massacred by the Japanese Invaders in Nanjing. Shanghai, Guangdong, and many other places also held symposiums, photo and archive exhibitions, and other events on the theme of establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. The China Museum of Taiwan Ancestral Ties and the Communication University of China jointly held the academic exchange meeting “Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of the Restoration of Taiwan: Construction of Chinese National Identity and Integrated Development Across the Strait.” The Fujian Provincial Association for Ethnic Unity and Progress and the Taiwan Association of Mayors and Township Heads of Ethnic Minorities jointly initiated the “Cross-Strait Songs Together, Running Together for Rejuvenation” activity commemorating the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan, held simultaneously in Yong’an City, Fujian, and Yilan County, Taiwan.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait who took part in the activities expressed that establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day accords with the wishes of people on both sides of the Strait and with the trend toward national reunification. It is of great significance in uniting compatriots on both sides to safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, advancing the great cause of national reunification, and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731163.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Lai Ching-te said that political parties should support the DPP's so-called amendments to the “National Security Ten Laws.” The Taiwan executive branch said that, in response to cognitive warfare such as false information, it has planned 21 law amendments and expects to complete draft amendments by the end of the year. What comments do you have on this?","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and are eager to push forward so-called “legal amendments.” This is aimed at using evil “law” to commit evil acts, further creating a “green terror” and a “chilling effect,” escalating cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and opening the door to plotting a “Taiwan independence dictatorship.” Peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society. The Lai Ching-te authorities ignore the livelihood and public opinion on the island, continuously tear apart Taiwan society, seriously undermine cross-Strait relations, and lead to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. All such reckless actions will be opposed, and they are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731161.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The Taiwan external affairs department stated in a report that the US has said it will cooperate with its international allies to respond to China’s rare earth export control measures. The DPP authorities are studying building, together with the US and Western countries, a so-called “non-red supply chain” for global critical minerals to respond to the “China rare earth war.” What comment do you have on this?","The formation of industrial and supply chains is the result of optimal allocation of resources under the laws of the market economy. The DPP authorities have proactively served as the “vanguard” and “pawn” of external forces in containing China. By selling off Taiwan’s advantageous industries, sacrificing Taiwan’s development prospects, and smashing the “rice bowls” of Taiwan’s people, and by echoing the so-called “non-red supply chain,” they aim to exchange external support for their “independence” scheme. Their unlimited willingness to sell out Taiwan and their unprincipled clinging to outside forces can only bring the United States’ even more unscrupulous extraction and plunder, harm the interests of Taiwan’s industries and enterprises, and destroy the future of Taiwan’s economy and people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","Recently, SEF Secretary-General Lo Wen-chia said, “How could there be religious exchanges without religious freedom?” and told Taiwan residents, “Don’t believe the religious exchanges the mainland describes for united front purposes.” Officials of the DPP authorities have also said, “The mainland treats religion as a political tool.” What is your comment on this?","These claims are a complete smear and slander. They once again expose the DPP authorities' fear of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer together, and their sinister intention to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges. We have consistently pursued a policy of freedom of religious belief, manage religious affairs in accordance with law, and support religious circles on both sides of the Strait in carrying out exchanges in accordance with law and regulations. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, carry out a “green terror” for the sake of their party's private interests, and stop at nothing in intimidating and suppressing religious groups and figures on the island to keep them from engaging in normal religious exchange activities on the mainland. Who is infringing on religious freedom, and who is interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges in all areas, including religious exchanges—the people on the island are seeing more and more clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: Sun Tian-ping, the second son of General Sun Li-jen, recently revealed that he has formally submitted an application to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, hoping to relocate his father's remains back to his hometown for burial. What is the current progress of this matter at the Taiwan Affairs Office, and what is your view on it? Second question: After you assumed the post of…","First question: We will further look into and verify the relevant situation.\nSecond question: It will continue to be retained.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","The US magazine Time recently published an article by an expert from the think tank Defense Priorities, which directly pointed to Lai Ching-te’s style as a “reckless leader,” saying he is making Taiwan “the most dangerous flashpoint in the world,” and called on US President Donald Trump to restrain “the reckless and high-profile Lai Ching-te.” What is your comment on this?","We have noted that recently more and more foreign experts, scholars, and international public opinion have expressed concern about the situation across the Taiwan Strait, and have publicly criticized Lai Ching-te's provocative words and deeds regarding “Taiwan independence.” The current situation across the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and its fundamental cause is that the Lai Ching-te authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, stubbornly insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” and continuously collude with external forces to provoke “independence”-seeking. Lai Ching-te is an out-and-out “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait,” a “creator of Taiwan Strait crises,” and a true “troublemaker.”\nI must emphasize that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and resolving it is a matter for Chinese on both sides of the Strait themselves. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme harm and destructiveness of the DPP authorities' stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” line, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, work with us to push cross-Strait relations back onto the correct track of peaceful development, and effectively safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202510/t20251029_12731159.htm"],[2,"2025-10-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Since you became a spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office, the TAO now has four spokespersons, which is a relatively large number historically. You have served as director of the Haiyan Research Center (海研中心) and now serve as director of the Economic Bureau. Will you, in your role as spokesperson this time, strengthen publicity on cross-Strait economic and trade affairs? Second question: The…","First question. We will, as always, do our press work on Taiwan affairs well, and our arrangements have not changed.\nSecond question. We will take seriously every comment on the Facebook account of the “Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.” We will continue to make good use of this new communication platform, do more practical things, good things, and solve more difficulties for Taiwan compatriots.\nFinally, I will release one more message. On October 13, the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” released the questions for the fifth “Taiwan-related Knowledge Q&A” event, and netizens enthusiastically took part in answering. As of October 27, the top ten netizens with correct answers and the most likes on their comments, in order, were: “机灵鬼,” “美好的回忆,” “猴子派来的救兵,” “美丽新世界,” “好山好水,” “白萧,” “杨俊升,” “小火苗,” “晨,” and “小不点.” We congratulate the above ten netizens. They will receive the exquisite commemorative gift, the shell carving 《宝岛台湾》 (“Treasure Island Taiwan”). We hope everyone will continue to care about Taiwan affairs work, actively take part, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn November 10, the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will publish the questions for the sixth “Taiwan-related Knowledge Q&A” event. Stay tuned!\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202510/t20251029_12731155.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-10-30","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","It was reported that, according to the latest poll in Paraguay this month, 58.3 percent of Paraguayans believe that establishing diplomatic ties with China is very important, and 29.8 percent believe it is important. The two combined accounts for nearly 90 percent of the respondents. Several Paraguayan MPs urged the Paraguayan government to establish diplomatic relations with China and sever the so-called…","We noted the reports. In recent years, we have heard time and again the strong call of people from various sectors in Paraguay to develop relations with China. The poll once again demonstrates the keen desire of the Paraguayan people for the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Paraguay.\nWe would like to stress again that China’s reunification is unstoppable. Maintaining so-called “diplomatic relations” with the Taiwan authorities does not serve the fundamental and long-term interests of Paraguay and its people, and also goes against the prevailing consensus of the international community on upholding the one-China principle. We urge the Paraguayan government to heed the call of its people, embark on the right course as early as possible, come to the right side of history, and make the right decision to recognize the one-China principle and sever so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202510/t20251030_11744169.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202510/t20251030_11744014.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-10-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","October 25 is the Commemoration Day of Taiwan's Restoration. However, Lai Ching-te did not mention anything about Taiwan's restoration on the day. Instead, he released a statement clamoring for the Battle of Guningtou. He said that \"the conviction of the Taiwanese people and military to defend Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu has never wavered\". What's your comment on this?","On the occasion of the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, the designation of the Commemoration Day of Taiwan's Restoration in the name of the state fully responds to people's aspirations and reflects the national will. It underscores the historical and juridical fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and demonstrates the firm resolve of all ethnic groups across the nation to oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification. It also embodies the broad consensus of the international community on upholding the one-China principle. This move will undoubtedly guide compatriots on both sides of the Strait in carrying forward and promoting the tradition of patriotism, the spirit of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, and the great national spirit, inspiring all Chinese people to unite in striving for national reunification and rejuvenation.\nLai Ching-te and his ilk stand on the opposite side of history, against compatriots across the Strait and in defiance of the international consensus. Their attempts to \"seek independence by force\" and \"resist reunification by force\" are nothing but a mantis trying to stop a chariot, overestimating their own strength. They are doomed to be buried by the historical trends and face the severest judgment by justice.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251030-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16420391.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-10-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, the so-called US-Taiwan Defense Industry Conference 2025 was held in the US recently. The two sides discussed joint R&D and production of weapons, and more US arms sales to Taiwan. What's your comment?","The DPP authorities are pandering to the US for selfish interests at the expense of Taiwan's interests and seeking independence by force at the cost of Taiwan's resources, dragging the people in Taiwan down into an abyss. No matter how much weaponry the DPP authorities plans to buy from the US, it will not change the military strength comparison across the Strait, nor the desolate fate of \"Taiwan Independence\".\nThe US should fully recognize the high sensitivity and severe consequences of its arms sales to Taiwan, stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question which concerns China's core interests, and take concrete actions to deliver on its promise of not supporting \"Taiwan independence\".\nThe PLA will firmly smash any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist plot and foreign interference, and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity with stronger capabilities and more reliable means.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251030-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16420391.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-10-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The recent hit TV series Silent Honor has sparked widespread interest across the Strait on TV series related to the reunification of China. Some young people in Taiwan said that the series helped them learn about a lesser-known chapter in the history of cross-Strait relations and found it deeply moving. What's your comment?","I have noticed that a growing number of people are reading history and paying tribute to heroes and martyrs after watching relevant television dramas. This will undoubtedly strengthen the resolve and sense of duty among compatriots on both sides of the Strait in advancing the great cause of national reunification. I firmly believe that family reunion and national reunification is the common aspiration of our people, and reunification is an unstoppable historical trend. The unfinished cause of the martyrs will ultimately be accomplished.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251030-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16420391.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-10-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to media reports, Lai Ching-te recently stated that strengthening national defense was not a provocation, and Taiwan must show \"firm opposition to annexation, opposition to invasion, and opposition to advancing unification.\" What is your comment on this? Second, you just mentioned Defense Minister Dong Jun's participation in the 12th ADMM-Plus. Is there any plan to meet the…","Regarding the first question, Lai Ching-te and his ilk have consistently used deceptive rhetoric to mislead the public, concealing their sinister intention of pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" and provoking conflicts. Their actions are nothing but schemes that harm and destroy Taiwan. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that national reunification is an unstoppable historical trend, and those who \"seek independence by force\" will only court their own destruction.\nRegarding the second question, China maintains an open attitude towards developing military-to-military relations with the US. We hope the US side will work with us in the same direction to build a military-to-military relationship featuring equality, mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and greater stability. Concerning the specific matter you mentioned, I have no information to release at this time.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251030-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16420391.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-10-30","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, on October 25, the Commemoration Day of Taiwan's Restoration, Jilin-1, a commercial satellite, released multiple high-resolution images of Taiwan. From the satellite's view, every street in Taiwan is clearly visible. Local media commented that technological development in mainland is impressive — \"when commercial satellites can detect these facilities so clear, military satellites are…","Regarding the first question, it is perfectly normal for Chinese satellites to capture images of the magnificent landscapes of China's Taiwan region. No need to make a big deal out of it.\nRegarding the second question, given Japan's history of militarist aggression, Japan's military and security moves are closely watched. In recent years, Japan has substantially increased its defense budget, continuously relaxed restrictions on arms export, and sought military breakthroughs. There are greater concerns over Japan's commitment to the exclusively defense-oriented policy and the path of peaceful development. We urge the Japanese side to act prudently in military and security areas, and earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the international community with concrete actions.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/10/china-251030-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16420391.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-11-05","Mao Ning","Reuters","Taiwanese officials said today that China has “attached many conditions” to Chinese Taipei’s participation in next year’s APEC summit, including the one-China principle. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","Participating as a regional economy under the one-China principle and abiding by the terms set forth in the relevant APEC MoU and usual practices—this is the political prerequisite for Chinese Taipei’s participation in APEC. China’s position on this issue is clear and firm.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251105_11747551.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251105_11747484.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 5, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Chen Binhua, Director of the Press Bureau and spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, first introduced the new spokesperson, Zhang Han, Director of the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Bureau. Zhang Han then presided over the press conference and answered reporters'…","Dear journalist friends, hello! Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. I am very pleased to introduce our office's new spokesperson and Director of the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Bureau, Ms. Zhang Han. Today's press conference will be hosted by Director Zhang Han. I hope you will support Director Zhang Han in doing a good job with Taiwan-related news briefings, just as you supported me, Zhu Fenglian, and Peng Qing'en.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/closing)","","Dear reporter friends, good morning, and welcome to the press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Taking this opportunity, I extend greetings to all Taiwan compatriots. I will host today’s press conference, and I hope that going forward I can work together with all of you to effectively introduce the mainland’s policies toward Taiwan and enhance understanding, comprehension, and trust among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The full text of the 《Recommendations of the CPC Central Committee on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development》 has been released. Some public opinion points out that the “15th Five-Year Plan” recommendations deploy work on Taiwan in a dedicated chapter, run through the main thread of integrated development, and closely link the “great cause of national reunification” with…","The “Recommendations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development” lists “promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the great cause of reunification of the motherland” as an important component of the “15th Five-Year Plan.” It sets out the goals and tasks of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing reunification of the motherland on the new journey of comprehensively building a modern socialist country, reflecting the strategic positioning of work on Taiwan in the process of building a strong country and achieving national rejuvenation.\nWe will thoroughly study and grasp the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, fully implement Comrade Xi Jinping’s important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, do a good job of work on Taiwan in the new era, solidly promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and unswervingly advance the great cause of reunification of the motherland.\nThe “15th Five-Year Plan” period is a critical time for laying a solid foundation and exerting full effort to basically achieve socialist modernization, and it holds a pivotal position of carrying on the past and opening the future in the process of basically achieving socialist modernization. The mainland’s economic foundation is stable, has many advantages, strong resilience and great potential. The supporting conditions and basic trend of long-term positive development have not changed, and the advantages of the socialist system with Chinese characteristics, the advantages of an ultra-large market, the advantages of a complete industrial system, and the advantages of abundant talent resources are becoming even more evident. The implementation of the “15th Five-Year Plan” will certainly provide more development opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. We will uphold the concept of “both sides of the Strait are one family,” advance high-quality construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone, strengthen industrial cooperation, promote cross-Strait economic cooperation, continuously improve systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, implement equal treatment, create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, work and live on the mainland, encourage and support more Taiwan compatriots to participate in the economic and social development of the mainland, share the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization, continuously enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, promote the joint inheritance and promotion of Chinese culture on both sides, and foster heartfelt connection among compatriots.\nWe will adhere to the One-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely combat “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, unite broad Taiwan compatriots, grasp the historical trend, actively promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and join hands to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation and jointly pursue the great cause of reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732709.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Public opinion on the island has widely noted that the mainland side has recently launched a series of measures. These include establishing a Taiwan Restoration Memorial Day, introducing new policies to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' entry into the mainland, holding an international academic symposium marking the 80th anniversary of the founding of the United Nations, increasing the frequency of Taiwan Affairs…","This year marks the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. We have established Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day in the name of the state and held commemorative activities at the national level. This fully reflects the wishes of the people and the will of the state. It is a forceful defense of the important historical fact and national glory of Taiwan's restoration and return to the motherland, and it will surely guide compatriots on both sides of the Strait to inherit and carry forward the patriotic tradition, the great War of Resistance spirit, and the great national spirit, and inspire all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation to unite and strive for national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the core interests of the country and the national sentiments of the Chinese people. We have a responsibility to guide compatriots on both sides of the Strait to remember history, defend achievements, safeguard peace, and create a shared future. We have a responsibility to bring benefits to compatriots on both sides and to enhance their well-being. We have a responsibility to help Taiwan compatriots recognize the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, recognize the essence of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces as bringing disaster to and harming Taiwan, and recognize the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified.\nWe will thoroughly study and understand the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, comprehensively implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan work and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and interference by external forces, respect, care for, and benefit Taiwan compatriots, continue to deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, share the opportunities and achievements of Chinese modernization, and work together with broad Taiwan compatriots to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly contribute to the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732708.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","We note that recently there has been considerable discussion across the Taiwan Strait about prospects after unification. Xinhua News Agency recently published an article under the byline “Zhong Taiwen” titled “Development of Cross-Strait Relations and Unification Are Beneficial,” which has drawn great attention on the island. What comment do you have? Please further introduce what benefits unification would bring…","Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. National reunification is the historical verdict on the development of cross-Strait relations. Everything we have done to promote the development of cross-Strait relations is aimed at enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides and realizing their aspiration for a better life. Completing national reunification is a just cause, one that benefits the present, the future, and generations to come.\nOn October 25, Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the CPPCC, proposed at the conference marking the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration that after peaceful reunification, with a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan will be “better in seven aspects”: economic development will be better, energy and resource security will be better, infrastructure construction will be better, security guarantees will be better, external exchanges will be better, the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will be better, and spiritual and cultural life will be better.\nThe article “Benefits of Cross-Strait Relations Development and Reunification,” published by Xinhua News Agency under the byline “Zhong Taiwen,” elaborates on the many benefits of reunification. In brief, after reunification, with a strong motherland as its backing, the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan compatriots will improve, development space will expand, they will be safer and more dignified, their backbone will be stiffer and their confidence greater on the international stage, Taiwan will enjoy lasting peace, and its people will live and work in contentment. Taiwan compatriots will share the dignity and glory of our great country together with compatriots on the mainland, and usher in a bright future of prosperity and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732706.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","On November 3, the National Immigration Administration issued a policy stating that starting November 20, the scope of ports that can issue one-time-valid Taiwan Resident Travel Permits to and from the Mainland will be expanded. Forty-two port immigration offices, including Tianjin Port, will be added to handle one-time-valid Taiwan Resident Travel Permits for Taiwan compatriots who do not hold valid entry-exit…","“Both sides of the Strait are one family.” Compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh and blood. We have always attached importance to listening to the opinions and suggestions of Taiwan compatriots, and are committed to creating convenient conditions for Taiwan residents to travel to the mainland, so that compatriots on both sides of the Strait grow ever closer and ever more intimate. Recently, the entry-exit administration departments issued a policy: starting November 20, the number of ports from which mainland China can issue one-time-valid Taiwan compatriot permits will be increased to 100.\nIf Taiwan compatriots have not applied for a Taiwan compatriot permit in advance and want to take a “spontaneous trip,” they only need to bring their Taiwan-issued entry-exit documents and identity card. They can take a plane or ship directly to the mainland from anywhere in the world, submit an application at the port of entry, and receive a Taiwan compatriot permit valid for one entry and exit within 30 minutes. With this document, they can travel in the mainland for 3 months. If 3 months is not enough, they can also apply on the spot at any entry-exit administration department at or above the county level in the mainland for a card-type Taiwan compatriot permit valid for 5 years. After submitting the application form and relevant documents, they can obtain the document in as little as 4 days.\nTaiwan compatriots can also have a card-type Taiwan compatriot permit processed through a local travel agency in Taiwan, without any other procedures, and can travel to the mainland at any time within 5 years.\nFor Taiwan “first-time visitors” who have never been to the mainland, not only is the permit free of charge, but there are also more than a thousand scenic spots they can visit without paying admission.\nTaiwan compatriots coming to the mainland is not only convenient but also safe. Whether obtaining a permit or entering and exiting, Taiwan compatriots will not have any marks made on their documents. In accordance with relevant laws and regulations, the relevant mainland departments strictly, forcefully, and effectively protect the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots who obtain permits.\nFrom the above introduction, I believe everyone now has a full understanding of the policy conveniences and information security for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland, and has also felt the sincerity and goodwill of the mainland. A family should visit each other often, and we warmly welcome all Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a walk and see for themselves the real situation on the mainland and personally experience the deep friendship of mainland compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732704.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","When Lai Ching-te recently attended a Taiwan military event, he claimed that the mainland continues to carry out “gray-zone harassment” in the air and sea areas around Taiwan. He said Taiwan must demonstrate its determination to protect its homeland, and must “firmly oppose annexation, oppose aggression, and oppose advancing reunification,” safeguarding peace through strength. What is your comment on this?","“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and unification is the trend of the times, which no person or force can stop. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will clearly see the evil nature and serious harm of “Taiwan independence,” firmly oppose the separatist conduct of “Taiwan independence,” and actively join the just cause of advancing the reunification of the motherland, safeguarding their own interests and well-being and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait through concrete action.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, China Media Group broadcast the documentary 'Restoration of the Land: Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration'. Please introduce the relevant situation.","As the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration approaches, the six-part documentary series “Reclaiming the Land: Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration,” jointly produced by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, and China Media Group, is currently airing on CCTV's General Channel and CCTV Chinese International Channel. The series has two notable features:\nFirst, a clear theme. “Reclaiming the land” means, as the name suggests, that “China's territory has been recovered and light has been restored.” The series mainly tells the historical truth of how Taiwan was ceded in 1895 and returned to the embrace of the motherland in 1945. Through historical research and interviews with experts, scholars, and witnesses, it exposes the exploitation and oppression of colonial rule and shows the heroism of Taiwan's patriotic fighters, who said “better to die as righteous citizens than to live as captives.” It confirms that Taiwan's restoration is an important part of the fruits of victory in World War II and of the postwar international order, and it shows the historical trend that China will ultimately be unified and must be unified.\nSecond, innovation in historical source material. The production team drew on the latest research on Taiwan-related issues in recent years, visited participants, and consulted historical records. Many materials are disclosed for the first time, such as the original press communiqué of the Cairo Declaration dated December 1, 1943, held by the Library of Congress of the United States, and the handwritten family letter that Taiwanese anti-Japanese fighter Lin Zhengheng wrote to his mother after being seriously wounded. The series uses a dual-track narrative of history and the present. It reflects history through the stories of historical figures and their connections to today, and it uses AI to restore historical figures and scenes. Showing the small to reveal the large and the past to illuminate the present, it presents its theme more vividly and engagingly.\nThis is a television work of high quality that combines ideological depth with storytelling. Many friends on both sides of the Taiwan Strait who have watched it say the series is highly rigorous, scholarly, and theoretical. It both upholds the authentic history of Taiwan's restoration and forcefully corrects the “Taiwan independence” view of history. History is the best textbook. We believe that compatriots on both sides of the Strait and Chinese descendants at home and abroad, after watching, will remember history, defend its achievements, and more actively join the cause of opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference and advancing the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732703.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The Chinese commercial satellite “Jilin-1” recently released eight space-view satellite images covering various parts of Taiwan, which drew attention and heated discussion from netizens on both sides of the Strait. Many Taiwanese netizens searched the satellite images for their own homes. Some commentary on the island pointed out that this demonstrates the mainland's satellite technological strength and its firm…","Taiwan is the treasured island of the motherland. With the continuous improvement of the mainland’s technological capabilities, we measure our territory more precisely, guard our homeland more solidly, and embrace the future more confidently. As netizens put it, this is “a view of home from above.” Whether it is the majestic Great Wall or the beautiful Sun Moon Lake, whether it is Shanghai with its towering skyscrapers or the bustling Taipei Port, they are all magnificent rivers and mountains of the motherland and beautiful homes of the Chinese nation. We sincerely welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a look around, enjoy its magnificent rivers and mountains, witness the scenery of Shenzhou, and feel the warmth of home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732702.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Public security authorities recently opened a case investigation into Shen Boyang, a diehard “Taiwan independence” figure. The DPP authorities said that mainland China has continuously issued lists of people to be punished for “independence,” sanctions, and case investigations, and that in the future it may submit the list to Interpol, issue Red Notices for global pursuit, and demand extradition to serve…","The net of the law is vast; its meshes are wide, yet nothing escapes. Any “Taiwan independence” diehard who breaks the law, wherever they are, we will take all necessary measures to punish them and hold them accountable under the law for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“台海之声”记者","Public security authorities recently opened a criminal investigation into Shen Boyang, a die-hard “Taiwan independence” element. The Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland has no jurisdiction over Taiwan, that relevant laws and norms have no binding force on Taiwan residents, and that the Taiwan public will never accept the mainland’s “interference, intimidation, or coercion.” What comments do you have…","Taiwan is part of China, and “Taiwan independence” is a criminal act of splitting the country and betraying the nation. The public security authorities have opened a criminal investigation into suspected separatism by the die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang and will pursue his criminal liability in accordance with the law. This is legitimate and lawful. It is a concrete action to implement the 《Opinions on Punishing “Taiwan Independence” Die-Hards for the Crimes of Secession and Incitement to Secession in Accordance with the Law》, and it is a just and necessary measure to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard national reunification. The related judicial and law enforcement actions target only a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figures whose words and deeds are egregious and whose separatist activities are rampant, along with the crimes of secession and incitement to secession they have committed. They do not target or involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities deliberately conflate the broad Taiwan public with a very small number of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figures in order to intimidate the public. This reveals their guilty conscience and fear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251105_12732701.htm"],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently claimed that Qian Li, a mainland spouse, promoted “armed unification” on her Facebook account and that her Taiwan status and household registration have been revoked. What is your comment?","Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have abused their power and acted recklessly, frequently fabricating charges to persecute mainland spouses in Taiwan. Even visits by mainland spouse associations to their hometowns for family visits and exchanges have been labeled as “united front infiltration.” Judging from the so-called “evidence” cited in the reports, this is yet another case of the DPP authorities persecuting mainland spouses on baseless charges. It fully exposes that the so-called “freedom and democracy” the DPP authorities advertise is nothing but “green terror,” where those who comply prosper and those who resist perish.\nIt is inevitable that mainland spouse groups stand up to defend their own rights in the face of unreasonable repression and persecution by the DPP authorities. We firmly support mainland spouses in actively defending their rights and interests, and we deeply care about their lives and circumstances in Taiwan. When storms come, it is only right, both emotionally and rationally, that we shield them from the wind and rain. For the “Taiwan independence” accomplices and lackeys who persecute mainland spouses, we will show no leniency; we will hold them accountable in accordance with the law and punish them severely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The 8th China International Import Expo will be held in Shanghai from November 5 to 10. Please introduce Taiwan businesses' and enterprises' participation in the CIIE. What opportunities does the CIIE bring to Taiwan businesses and enterprises?","The 8th China International Import Expo (CIIE) opened today (November 5) at the National Exhibition and Convention Center in Shanghai. This year's CIIE has 23 Taiwan companies exhibiting, with an exhibition area of about 1,730 square meters, covering industries such as food, technology and equipment, consumer goods, medical devices and healthcare, and services trade. We welcome people from all walks of life across the Taiwan Strait to visit the CIIE in Shanghai and to discuss cooperation.\nThe Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China proposed that we should actively expand independent opening-up and promote innovative development of trade. The CIIE is a major measure by which we proactively open our market to the world, a great innovation in the history of international trade development, and also an important platform for helping Taiwan businesses and companies share the fruits of Chinese-style modernization and the opportunities of high-level opening-up. Taiwan companies can use the CIIE to showcase their products, connect with high-quality resources, expand domestic sales channels, and widely discuss cooperation, actively integrating into the mainland's new development pattern.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","In terms of economic and trade exchanges, the second phase of “Shen i Taiwan: Meeting with ‘Courtesy’—Shenzhen-Taiwan Creative Design Tour,” the 21st Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum, and the 17th Straits Cross-Strait Tea Expo will be held this month in Shenzhen, Nanning in Guangxi, and Nanping in Fujian, respectively.\nIn terms of agricultural exchanges, at the end of October, the first Straits Cross-Strait (Jiangsu) Harvest Season of Agriculture and Fisheries was held in Nantong, Jiangsu. In early November, the 4th Straits Cross-Strait (Sanming) Rural Integrated Development Forum will be held in Sanming, Fujian.\nIn terms of cultural exchanges, on October 31, the Shandong touring exhibition of “Our Family's Cross-Strait Stories” was held at the Shandong Museum, and the 2025 Straits Cross-Strait Chinese Character Culture Series of Activities was held in Haicang District, Xiamen City, Fujian. From November 5 to 13, the 2nd Straits Cross-Strait Street Dance League will be launched in Shenzhen.\nIn terms of film and television exchanges, on October 31, the 3rd Straits Cross-Strait Chinese Photography Awards and the 6th Straits Cross-Strait Image Culture Week were held in Zhejiang. In early November, the 2025 China Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival special unit “Xiamen-Kinmen Light and Shadow Link” will be officially launched in Xiamen, the series of carnival activities of the 11th “Golden Swallow” Straits Cross-Strait Micro-Film and Micro-Video Competition will be held in Wuhan, and the 11th “China Cultural Forum” will open in Beijing. In addition, CMG's “Straits Cross-Strait” program has launched the series of special documentaries “Baodao Chongguang” and the online interactive video archive on the history of Taiwan's restoration, “Things About Taiwan's Restoration,” which have been officially put online.\nIn terms of sports exchanges, the 15th National Games will be held in Guangzhou from November 9 to 21, inviting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth representatives in Guangzhou as well as Taiwan guests to attend the opening ceremony and watch the competitions. The 2025 Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Taiwan Ice and Snow Carnival series of exchange activities will be held in Zhangjiakou, Hebei, in late November.\nIn terms of grassroots and folk belief exchanges, on October 31, “Zhejiang Roots, Cross-Strait Hearts” will invite Zhejiang-origin fellow-townsmen associations in Taiwan to visit Zhejiang for exchanges. From November 8 to 11, the 3rd Straits Cross-Strait Qingshui Patriarch Cultural Exchange Event will be held in Quanzhou, Fujian, and the 10th Nan'an Fengshan Cultural Activity Week will be held in Quanzhou, Fujian.\nWe warmly welcome broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to actively take part in cross-Strait exchange activities. We also welcome media friends to interview and report on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","DPP Secretary-General Hsu Kuo-yung recently said, “Taiwan is Taiwan, and it is not subordinate to China,” and “Chinese culture is also part of Taiwan culture.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. This historical and legal fact cannot be changed and will not change. Chinese culture has a long history and profound depth, and is the spiritual root and belonging of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Taiwan culture is part of Chinese culture, and its roots are in the mainland. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and any provocative act seeking “independence” will be met with a head-on blow. Anyone who forgets their ancestry and abandons the nation will be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi met with personnel from Taiwan during the APEC meeting and posted related photos on social media using an incorrect designation. What is your comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The relevant conduct of the Japanese side seriously violates the one-China principle, the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and the basic norms of international relations. It sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces, and we firmly oppose it.\nJapan bears historical responsibility on the Taiwan question and should especially reflect deeply on its history, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and handle Taiwan-related issues with the utmost caution. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that any scheme to “rely on foreign forces to seek independence” and attempt to split Taiwan from China is wishful thinking, and will only fail more thoroughly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Cho Jung-tai, head of the Executive Yuan, recently put forward “four preconditions” for high-level cross-Strait exchanges, claiming that as long as the mainland does “not set preconditions, not put labels on, and not insist that Taiwan is part of it,” and takes the position that “the Republic of China and the People's Republic of China are not subordinate to each other” in dialogue, Taiwan would be willing to…","As long as the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” are acknowledged, the two sides can resume contact and consultation. The DPP authorities, on the one hand, vigorously promote the “two-state theory” and openly carry out “Taiwan independence” provocations; on the other hand, they glibly talk about so-called contact and consultation. This is entirely deceiving public opinion and deceiving the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","湖北广电记者","According to reports, AutoNavi (Gaode Map) has achieved full coverage in Taiwan, offering lane-level navigation, real-time traffic conditions, and other features. Its voice announcements have switched to localized expressions such as “左转” (turn left) and “右转” (turn right), with clear and accurate pronunciation. Some netizens on the island praised it as useful, saying, “It feels like the distance to the mainland…","I do not have the specific details. What I want to say is that the pursuit of a good and convenient life is the right of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. With the development and innovation of science and technology and the upgrading and improvement of industries and services, more and more mainland products and services have become the daily choice of the Taiwan public. We welcome this and hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots can enjoy good mainland products and good services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The US magazine Foreign Affairs recently published an article by a US think tank expert stating that Lai Qingde’s various “independence”-seeking provocations since taking office have increased the likelihood of the mainland using force to achieve unification. To reduce the risk of war between China and the US over the Taiwan question, the US should respect China’s core position, issue a new joint communiqué or…","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, persistently fabricate and spread “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, vigorously stir up “green terror,” and attempt to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “seek independence by force,” continuously escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait. Their true face as “peace wreckers,” “war peddlers,” and “troublemakers” is not only being seen through by more and more island residents, but has also aroused concern and criticism from international strategic and academic circles.\nChina's reunification will only bring more development opportunities to all countries and inject more positive energy into the prosperity and stability of the Asia-Pacific region and the world. “Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest efforts, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Public security authorities recently opened a case against “Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang. In response, Taiwan’s security authorities said that, in addition to strengthening security protection for the individuals and enterprises on the mainland’s list of “Taiwan independence” diehards, they will also investigate “groups and individuals on the island that cooperate with mainland reporting and…","The DPP authorities, driven by their “Taiwan independence” nature, abuse public instruments for private purposes and use every means, arbitrarily persecuting patriotic unification forces on the island, intimidating and threatening Taiwan residents, and continuously strengthening “green terror.” We strongly condemn this. The perverse actions of the “Taiwan independence” forces will surely be judged by history and the people.\nIt must be emphasized that the relevant judicial and law enforcement actions target only a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards whose words and deeds are vicious and whose “independence” activities are rampant, and the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country that they commit. They do not target or involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will fully recognize the DPP authorities' sinister intentions and firmly oppose their totalitarian scheming for “independence” and their abuse of power and reckless conduct, and actively provide relevant clues to illegal and criminal activities. We strictly protect informants' information and lawful rights and interests in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","According to reports, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council has strengthened the prior notification mechanism for public officials traveling to the mainland, Hong Kong, and Macao, and plans to establish a spot-check mechanism. If it is found that someone has traveled to the mainland, Hong Kong, or Macao without application, an investigation and corresponding measures will be initiated. What is your comment on this?","Driven by its essential nature of pursuing “independence,” the DPP authorities keep obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges as well as exchanges between Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, and vigorously carry out “green terror.” This goes against mainstream public opinion on the island and will only meet with growing opposition and condemnation from Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","US President Trump recently said that since TSMC has brought chip production to the US and much of Taiwan's business to the US, the US will control 50% of the chip market within two years. Internet users on the island have said, “We hand over our chips and then get kicked,” and “Taiwan has no bargaining chips left.” What comment do you have?","Taiwan’s semiconductor industry is a precious asset of all Taiwan compatriots. In order to “rely on the United States to pursue independence,” the DPP authorities have servilely taken the initiative to sell out Taiwan’s core advantageous industry, disregarding the needs of industry and people’s livelihoods and letting the United States dominate it at will. This destroys the foundation of the industry and chills the hearts of the people, and in the end they will be like lifting a rock only to drop it on their own feet.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","On October 31, four mice flew into space aboard the Shenzhou-21 crewed spacecraft to take up residence in China’s space station, sparking heated discussion among netizens on both sides of the Strait. Some netizens named the “space mice” Congcong, Rongrong, Youren, and Youyu. What is your comment?","After years of hard work, China's space industry has achieved a series of world-renowned, glorious accomplishments. This mouse's journey into space has become yet another example of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly focusing on space exploration, reflecting everyone's sincere pride in and expectations for the advancement of mainland aerospace technology. We are pleased to see cross-strait netizens taking part in this ingenious way and sharing in this glory together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Question one: Last week, Director Song Tao of the Taiwan Affairs Office met with Hsiao Hsu-tsen, incoming Vice Chairman of the KMT, in Tianjin, which has given the outside world much room for imagination. May I ask the spokesperson what opportunities for exchange, development, and cooperation between the KMT and the CPC may arise in the future? In 2026, will the KMT and the CPC interact through activities…","On the first question: Whatever is conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to bringing compatriots on both sides closer together, we will actively promote. On the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing, together with political parties, groups and personages from all walks of life in Taiwan, including the Kuomintang of China, to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations: seeking well-being for compatriots, peace for the Taiwan Strait, unification for the country and rejuvenation for the nation.\nOn the second question: It is the lawful right of Taiwan compatriots to apply for mainland-related identity documents, and relevant application information and document data are strictly protected by law. The relevant acts of the DPP authorities are yet more evidence of their depriving Taiwan compatriots of legitimate rights and creating a \"green terror.\" They will surely meet strong opposition and firm resistance from broad Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the third question: Thank you for your attention. This is a normal work arrangement. I believe that in future press conference work we will come to understand each other better, be able to better present the mainland's policies toward Taiwan, and enhance the friendship between compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The Jilin-1 commercial satellite of the Chinese mainland recently released eight satellite images covering various parts of Taiwan from a space perspective, while also showing PLA fighter jets conducting training around the Taiwan Strait. Some public opinion on the island believes this is the mainland releasing a \"military and technological dual signal\" as a warning. May I ask whether the mainland…","Question one: When science and technology flourish, the nation flourishes; when science and technology are strong, the country is strong. From aerospace exploration to deep-sea exploration, from artificial intelligence to quantum information, the mainland's scientific and technological strength continues to rise, providing stronger guarantees for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and for protecting the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nQuestion two: I noted the relevant topic. This was a personal creative idea from netizens. The idea has sparked heated discussion among people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, reflecting the shared wish of compatriots on both sides for early reunion and their fervent hope for the complete reunification of the motherland. Regarding the personal ideas of netizens, the DPP authorities are gripped by fear and hysteria. They escalate the matter to the level of so-called \"cognitive warfare\" and make a great fuss, attacking and smearing the mainland. Their aim is nothing more than to create tension in the Taiwan Strait and heighten confrontation between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First, Zheng Liwen, the newly elected chair of the KMT, emphasized in a recent exclusive interview with Deutsche Welle that she believes all the contradictions across the Taiwan Strait can be resolved through peaceful dialogue. The KMT must shoulder the most critical role. She also stated that an arms race is not a wise path to bring peace, and that the key is whether the two sides currently have an opportunity…","First question: “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait. The development of cross-Strait relations has repeatedly proven that the “1992 Consensus” is the anchor of peace in the Taiwan Strait. Upholding the “1992 Consensus” can bring peace to both sides, and Taiwan compatriots will benefit. On the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen contact and communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and people of insight, promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and promote the reunification of the motherland.\nSecond question: Taiwan is Chinese territory, and resolving the Taiwan question is the affair of the Chinese people themselves; it brooks no foreign interference. Out of partisan self-interest, the DPP authorities stubbornly “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” which will ultimately only harm the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan.\nThird question: The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and how to resolve it is the affair of the Chinese people themselves; it brooks no foreign interference. Achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared wish of all Chinese descendants, and it is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the aspiration of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS记者","The 2026 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (AEPC) will be held in Shenzhen, and public opinion on the island is paying attention to whether Taiwan can attend. The DPP authorities stated that last year they facilitated the mainland side offering a written assurance, hoped the mainland side would fulfill its commitment, and said “we are equal members,” and “the world also needs Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","As the host of next year's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) events, we will handle the participation of the Taiwan region in meetings in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions and practices of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-05","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The mainland has introduced new policies to facilitate entry for Taiwan compatriots, while the Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation have reminded Taiwan compatriots of the risks of travelling to the mainland. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said that from last year through the end of September this year, it had received 212 reports of Taiwan residents who, after travelling to the…","We always welcome Taiwan compatriots to participate broadly in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and we create convenient conditions and provide quality services for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. At the same time, we will crack down on all kinds of illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law, and actively safeguard the lives, property, and legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities are confusing right and wrong and maliciously hyping related topics in an attempt to intimidate and threaten Taiwan residents, obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, and escalate cross-Strait confrontation. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nAs long as they abide by the law and discipline, Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland can be just as if they were returning home, relaxed and safe. Everyone will find that the mainland is beautiful, advanced, and safe, and that mainland compatriots are kind, warm, and friendly. Once you have come, you will certainly want to come again.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251105_12732697.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-06","Mao Ning","Beijing Daily","It’s reported that on November 3, the government of Japan announced the 2025 Autumn Conferment of Decorations on Foreign Nationals. Receiving the Order of the Rising Sun, “Taiwan’s Representative in Japan” Hsieh Chang-ting said on social media that day he will continue his contributions to the “friendship between Taiwan and Japan”. What’s China’s comment?","What’s Japan up to by conferring orders on those who peddle “Taiwan independence” narratives? Is it an intentional move to embolden “Taiwan independence” separatists? What message does Japan want to send to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces?\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and bears on the political foundation of China-Japan ties and basic credibility of Japan. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. China urges Japan to take a hard look at its responsibility for the war crimes, abide by the one-China principle and the guiding principles of the four political documents between the two countries, be prudent on the Taiwan question, and stop sending any wrong signals to separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251106_11748399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251106_11748200.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-06","Mao Ning","Reuters","The U.S. State Department said on Wednesday that Taiwan must be allowed full and equal participation when China hosts APEC next year. What’s China’s response?","China will actively fulfill its duty as the host of APEC in 2026 and ensure the smooth participation of all sides. On Chinese Taipei’s participation in APEC, I’ve clearly stated China’s stance.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251106_11748399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251106_11748200.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-06","Mao Ning","Reuters","A senior Fijian diplomat visited Taiwan this week who met with a senior Taiwanese official. This is a very unusual trip given that Fiji only has foreign relations with Beijing. What’s China’s response?","China firmly opposes any form of official interactions between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. Fiji’s relevant official’s visit to Taiwan severely violated Fiji’s political commitment to the one-China principle. China strongly deplores it and has lodged serious protests with Fiji. Taiwan’s disgraceful moves will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251106_11748399.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251106_11748200.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-11-07","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the Taiwan's army recently held a commissioning ceremony for the M1A2T tanks. Lai Ching-te claimed that strengthening Taiwan's defense is aimed at maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, asserting that only strength can bring true peace. Please comment on that.","The \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are fully aware of the comparison of military strength across the Strait. Their high-profile theatrics are nothing more than an attempt to embolden themselves and deceive the people in Taiwan. No display of US-made weapons by the troops of Taiwan can undermine the resolve and capability of the People's Liberation Army in safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The desperate resistance by \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces will not stop the rolling wheels of the time. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and his ilk that seeking \"independence\" by force is a dead end. Only by completely abandoning their separatist attempts and following the historical trend toward national reunification can bring true peace to Taiwan.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251107-prc-mndb01.htm","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/11/07/11394620.shtml",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-11-07","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Today marks the tenth anniversary of the historic meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Strait. Mr. Ma Ying-jeou posted on Facebook to elaborate on the significance of the meeting and its far-reaching impact on cross-Strait relations, and called on the DPP authorities to pull back from the cliff’s edge, change the “resist China, protect Taiwan” policy that does not serve the interests…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that the historic meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Taiwan Strait held on November 7, 2015, was a major initiative by the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core to lead and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the cause of national reunification. It pioneered direct dialogue and communication between the leaders of the two sides, raised cross-Strait political interaction to a new height, and became an important milestone in the development of cross-Strait relations. The meeting consolidated the key role and function of the “1992 Consensus” as the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and demonstrated that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait are fully capable and wise enough to solve problems within the nation and the Chinese people, keeping the destiny of the Chinese nation firmly in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.\nThe historic meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the subsequent development of cross-Strait relations have fully proven that as long as we uphold the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and recognize that people on both sides are Chinese and one family, compatriots on both sides can sit down together, enhance mutual understanding, accumulate mutual trust, resolve differences, and seek consensus. Cross-Strait relations can then develop peacefully, peace and stability can be maintained across the Taiwan Strait, and the well-being of compatriots on both sides can be enhanced. Conversely, denying the “1992 Consensus,” deviating from the one-China principle, plotting “Taiwan independence” separatism, inciting “resisting China and safeguarding Taiwan,” and creating hostility and confrontation between the two sides would make cross-Strait consultation and dialogue impossible, plunge the Taiwan Strait into danger and war, and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nReunification is the trend of history and the right path. “Taiwan independence” is a reverse current of history and a dead end. Only by resolving the political confrontation across the Taiwan Strait at an early date and moving toward the complete reunification of the motherland can lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait be ensured. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen dialogue, communication, and exchanges with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and representative figures, including the Kuomintang, to jointly advance the development of cross-Strait relations, secure peace in the Taiwan Strait, bring well-being to compatriots, and achieve national rejuvenation. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will work with us in harmony and unity, jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the cause of national reunification, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, steadfastly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides, and jointly create a bright future of national rejuvenation and reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251107_12733521.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-10","Lin Jian","China Review News","Responding at the Diet on November 7, Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said that a Taiwan emergency involving the use of military vessels and military force from the Chinese mainland could constitute a “survival-threatening situation” for Japan. According to its legislation, Japan’s Self-Defense Forces could exercise the right of collective self-defense if such a situation is recognized as “survival-threatening.”…","Several days ago, the Japanese leader blatantly made wrongful remarks on Taiwan at the Diet that imply the possibility of armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait. It constitutes a gross interference in China’s internal affairs and violates the one-China principle, the principles set forth in the four political documents between China and Japan, and basic norms in international relations. This is highly inconsistent with the political commitments made by the Japanese government so far and is egregious in terms of both the nature and impact. China deplores and opposes that and has made serious démarches and protests to Japan.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. How to solve the Taiwan question and achieve reunification is China’s own affair that doesn’t tolerate any foreign interference. What signal is the Japanese leader trying to send to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces? Is Japan up to challenge China’s core interests and stop its reunification? Where exactly does Japan want to take its relations with China?\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. Japan committed innumerable crimes during its colonial rule over Taiwan. For the leader of Japan to try to wade into cross-Strait affairs is an affront to international justice, a provocation to the post-WWII order, and a serious blow to China-Japan relations. China must and will achieve reunification. We, the Chinese people, have every resolve, will and conviction to thwart any external interference in and obstruction to China’s reunification. China urges Japan to immediately stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, stop making provocations and crossing the line, and stop going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251110_11750313.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251110_11749991.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-10","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s Hsiao Bi-khim called for greater support for Taiwan in a rare speech to a European Parliament group in Brussels on Friday. We also know that Tsai Ing-wen is expected to give an address in Berlin today. My question is, what does the Chinese Foreign Ministry make of this apparent strengthening of outreach by Taiwan to Europe? What advice or considerations would you give to European lawmakers and policy…","China has protested to the European Parliament over “Taiwan independence” politicians attending the “Inter-Parliamentary Alliance summit” in the building of the European Parliament. The European side noted that the European Parliament’s commitment to the one-China policy has not and will not change, relevant meeting was not held at the invitation of the European Parliament, relevant individuals were not invited by the Parliament and the Parliament leadership did not have any contact with them. The personal actions of individual MEPs do not represent the official position of the European Parliament.\nThe Inter-Parliamentary Alliance (IPAC) is funded by multiple anti-China institutions and is accustomed to spreading disinformation about China. The DPP authorities use IPAC, a group that has no credibility at all, to solicit foreign support for their separatist agenda. The political theatrics staged by “Taiwan independence” politicians and IPAC are merely aimed at grabbing attention. Such attempts are doomed to fail.\nLet me reiterate that whatever gambits the DPP authorities and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces resort to and whatever “outreach” they try to seek, it will only make their separatist agenda more evident and can never change the inevitability of China’s reunification. We hope the European Parliament will make no mistake about the true nature of the DPP authorities, abide by the one-China principle, refrain from sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” forces, and avoid being used.\nAs for the certain leading figure for “Taiwan independence” you mentioned, let me point out that China’s position is consistent and clear. China firmly opposes any “Taiwan independence” separatists visiting countries having diplomatic ties with China under any pretext. We urge Germany to abide by the one-China principle, unequivocally oppose all “Taiwan independence” moves, refrain from sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and earnestly uphold the overall bilateral relations with China. Certain leading figure for “Taiwan independence” who has already left office is still making every futile attempt to solicit foreign support for the independence agenda. The ill-intentioned attempts will never succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251110_11750313.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251110_11749991.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-12","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It was reported that the Japanese government held the autumn conferment of decorations ceremony on November 11, and conferred the Order of the Rising Sun on “Taiwan’s Representative in Japan” Hsieh Chang-ting. Later that day, Hsieh said on social media that he will continue working for the “friendship between Taiwan and Japan.” What is China’s comment?","China has made clear its position on this issue before. The Japanese government took another wrong step on Taiwan by proposing and promoting the conferment on someone advocating “Taiwan independence.” China firmly opposes this.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests. It bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations and the basic credibility of Japan, and is a red line that must not be crossed. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. China seriously urges Japan to deeply reflect on its responsibility for the war crimes, abide by the principles and spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, honor its commitments on upholding the one-China principle with concrete actions, stay prudent on the Taiwan question, and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251112_11751644.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251112_11751582.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear reporters, good day. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The full text of the “Proposals of the CPC Central Committee on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development” has been released, attracting wide attention on the island. Some public opinion on the island holds that the proposal's emphasis on “accelerating high-level self-reliance and self-strengthening in science and technology and leading the development of new quality…","The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China deliberated and adopted the Proposal on Formulating the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development. It has continued to arouse high attention and heated discussion across all sectors of the island. Industries on the island, including electronic information, machinery manufacturing, and food processing, have expressed their hope to deeply participate in the implementation of the “15th Five-Year Plan.” Many Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises have said that the “15th Five-Year Plan” will inject strong momentum into complementary advantages and integrated development across the Taiwan Strait. It is an important opportunity for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to integrate into the new development pattern and participate in modernization.\nDuring the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, we will continue to focus our efforts on cultivating and strengthening emerging and future industries, strengthening original innovation and key core technology research, and promoting the deep integration of scientific and technological innovation with industrial innovation. As we continue to advance meeting new supply with new demand and creating new demand with new supply, scientific and technological innovation will give rise to new industries, new models, and new momentum. This will create a more favorable environment for cross-strait economic cooperation and integrated development in all fields. We will continue to improve systems and policies that promote cross-strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, and open up broader and more diverse new horizons for cross-strait economic cooperation and integrated development. We hope that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will seize the historic opportunity presented by the formulation and implementation of the “15th Five-Year Plan,” explore with us paths for the deep integration of cross-strait technology and industrial innovation, and share in the abundant achievements of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734325.htm"],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The symposium “Negotiations and Consultations in Cross-Strait Relations: Finding Solutions by Looking Back” was recently held in Taipei. Participants called for enhancing cross-Strait communication and dialogue on the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and resuming cross-Strait negotiations. This has drawn attention from public opinion on the island. What is your comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It is on the basis of the “1992 Consensus” that the two sides launched negotiations, signed a series of agreements, reached many common understandings, and effectively promoted the economic well-being of people on both sides and effectively safeguarded peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe historical wheel of national reunification and national rejuvenation is rolling forward. The sooner the Taiwan question is resolved and the country is reunified, the more beneficial it will be to Taiwan’s development and the better life Taiwan compatriots will be able to enjoy. Compatriots on both sides are all Chinese and are one family with blood ties. They are fully capable and wise enough to discuss family matters among themselves and to keep the destiny of the Chinese nation firmly in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734324.htm"],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, Su Chi, honorary chairman of the Taipei Forum Foundation, called on Taiwan's political parties to jointly face “changes unseen in a century” and jointly promote cross-Strait dialogue. He said this is the only way out for the situation in Taiwan, which is already grave, and that otherwise the changes will become a “dismal endgame.” What is your comment?","The historical process of cross-Strait reunification cannot be stopped. \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and confrontation leads nowhere. Only by pushing cross-Strait relations toward the goal of complete reunification of the motherland can lasting peace across the Taiwan Strait be ensured and enduring well-being for the Chinese nation be created together. We are willing, on the common political basis of adhering to the one-China principle and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to conduct extensive and in-depth democratic consultations with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and representative figures on cross-Strait relations and Taiwan's future, to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and revival for the nation. We hope that political parties and all sectors of society on the island will recognize the trend of history, uphold national righteousness, join us in safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and work together to create a bright new chapter of national rejuvenation and motherland reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734323.htm"],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, DPP Secretary-General Hsu Kuo-yung declared that the elements of a state are only “people, territory, sovereignty, and the capacity to engage with other countries”; blood, language, religion, and culture are not. He also said, “His ancestors came from Quanzhou, but he is a Taiwanese.” What is your comment?","Taiwan has never been a country, and it will never become one. The historical facts and legal basis of cross-Strait relations both prove that there is only one China, that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and that this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The vast majority of countries, along with international organizations including the United Nations, adhere to the one-China principle.\nXu Guoyong talks nonsense and speaks falsehoods, seeking to find so-called “justification” for “Taiwan independence” and separatism. This is purely self-deception. Those who forget their ancestors, betray their nation, and split their country have never come to a good end, and all of them will be nailed to the pillar of shame of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","A columnist for the U.S. newspaper The New York Times recently said bluntly at an event on the island, “The era when one could be confident that the United States would definitely ‘support Taiwan’ has gone forever,” and that the DPP authorities should not take any radical action. In response, the head of Taiwan's defense authority said, “Taiwan and the U.S. have consensus on security issues.” What is your comment…","Recently, many foreign media outlets, experts, and scholars have spoken out to criticize the Lai Ching-te authorities for being reckless and rash and for repeatedly engaging in provocations seeking \"independence.\" This shows that more and more people have come to recognize their true face as \"peace spoilers\" and \"troublemakers,\" and it also shows that \"seeking independence by relying on foreign powers\" is a futile illusion. The future of Taiwan, the security and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' stubborn adherence to the separatist line of \"Taiwan independence,\" firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, and join us in pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development and in earnestly safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734322.htm"],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","厦门卫视记者","Starting November 5, smart customs clearance began to be promoted at two ports, Xiamen Gaoqi International Airport and Wutong Passenger Terminal. The Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” passenger route welcomed the first batch of Taiwan compatriots to pass through customs by facial recognition. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Beginning on the 5th of this month, the National Immigration Administration has promoted the application of smart clearance at 12 open ports, including Xiamen Gaoqi International Airport and the Wutong Passenger Terminal, and has also expanded the scope of personnel eligible for smart clearance to Taiwan residents holding a Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents valid for five years. Compared with the previous express channel clearance, which required multiple steps such as “presenting documents, scanning documents, and submitting documents,” travelers can now clear customs directly through “facial recognition,” further improving the convenience of clearance for inbound and outbound passengers.\nThe Wutong Passenger Terminal, where the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” passenger route is located, is the mainland's largest passenger port for travel to Taiwan. Since the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” passenger route began operating on January 2, 2001, the annual passenger volume on this golden channel connecting both sides of the Strait has grown from more than 20,000 passenger trips at the outset to more than 1.25 million passenger trips in 2024. It has witnessed the era-defining leap in cross-Strait personnel exchanges from “case-by-case approval” to “express clearance” and then to “smart clearance.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae recently said in answering questions in the Diet that if a “Taiwan contingency” occurred, an emergency situation involving the use of force by the other side could constitute a “survival-threatening situation” in which Japan may exercise the right of collective self-defense. Some public opinion holds that Takaichi's remarks mean that if the mainland were to take actions such…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The vile remarks on Taiwan that Japan's leader openly made in the Diet seriously violate the one-China principle and brazenly interfere in China's internal affairs. We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose them. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has lodged solemn representations and strong protests with the Japanese side.\nOn the Taiwan question, Japan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people, and during its fifty years of colonial enslavement of Taiwan it committed crimes too numerous to recount. Eighty years ago, we defeated the Japanese invaders, recovered Taiwan, and ended Japan's occupation and plunder of Taiwan. Eighty years later, anyone who attempts to challenge China's core interests or hopes to obstruct China's great cause of reunification will not be tolerated or accepted by the Chinese government, the Chinese people, or the Chinese military. Japan should deeply reflect on history, draw lessons from it, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, honor its political commitments on the Taiwan question, and handle Taiwan-related matters with the utmost care. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that any scheme to rely on external forces to separate Taiwan from China is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734321.htm"],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","According to reports, the “Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China” (IPAC) held its annual meeting at the European Parliament building, and “Taiwan independence” figures such as Hsiao Bi-khim attended and delivered speeches. The DPP authorities touted this as “a historic step in Taiwan's diplomacy and a new stage in Taiwan-Europe relations.” What is your comment?","The so-called “Transnational Parliamentary Alliance on China Policy” is nothing more than a small clique formed by a group of extreme anti-China elements. We firmly oppose its renewed meddling on Taiwan-related issues. The DPP authorities colluding with such an organization to stage a farce will only make themselves a laughingstock and bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities.","In November, exchanges across all fields between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait continued to be lively. On the 2nd, the “Cross-Strait Together” Youth Cycling Relay Race was held in Suqian, Jiangsu. A concurrent “experience visits, in-depth interaction, and industry matching” event was also held to help Taiwanese youth get a close look at the latest developments in Jiangsu's economic growth and rural construction. From the 4th to the 8th, the “Rongtong Cross-Strait, Chasing Dreams in Tianfu” 2025 Cross-Strait (Sichuan-Chongqing) Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference was held in Chengdu, building a platform for cross-Strait youth to exchange experience in employment and entrepreneurship and to integrate into the construction of the Chengdu-Chongqing twin-city economic circle. From the 6th to the 9th, the 4th Cross-Strait (Sanming) Rural Integrated Development Forum was held in Sanming, Fujian, actively exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development and promoting exchanges and integrated development in cross-Strait characteristic modern agriculture, forest health and wellness industries, and rural co-construction and co-governance. On the 8th, the Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao Internet Development Forum of the World Internet Conference Wuzhen Summit was held in Wuzhen, Zhejiang. Internet practitioners, cultural creators, and rural builders from both sides of the Strait gathered to share practical experience and innovative concepts in the internet era. From the 9th to the 14th, a series of art and cultural activities, including the Palace Museum's family musical “Duanduan” and the photography exhibition “Record of the Four Seasons of the Forbidden City: Image Records of the 24 Solar Terms in the Palace,” were held at the Buddha's Light Mountain Buddha Memorial Hall in Kaohsiung.\nFrom the 12th to the 16th, the 2025 “Keyin π, Hakka Voice” Cross-Strait (Longyan) Hakka Youth Storytelling Exchange Competition will be held in Longyan, Fujian. Hakka youth from both sides of the Strait will jointly carry forward the Hakka spirit of honoring ancestors, reporting to origins, and loving the nation and homeland. From the 15th to the 20th, the 3rd “Zhejiang-Taiwan Literature Week” will be held in Quzhou, Zhejiang. During this period, activities including the “Silent Glory” report meeting and a cross-Strait literary integration development exchange conference will also be held. On the 21st and 22nd, the Cross-Strait (Qingdao) Youth Exchange and Development Conference will be held in Qingdao, Shandong. About 200 young friends from both sides of the Strait will share friendship and plan development together during the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","November 7 of this year marks the tenth anniversary of the historic meeting between the leaders on both sides of the Strait. On that day, Mr. Ma Ying-jeou posted on Facebook to elaborate on the significance of the meeting and its far-reaching impact on cross-Strait relations, and called on the DPP authorities to pull back from the cliff’s edge, change the “resist China, protect Taiwan” policy that does not serve…","The historic meeting between the leaders of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait held on November 7, 2015, was a major measure taken by the CPC Central Committee with Xi Jinping at its core to lead and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification. It opened a precedent for direct dialogue and communication between the leaders of the two sides, raised political interaction across the Strait to a new height, and became an important milestone in the development of cross-Strait relations. The meeting consolidated the key role and function of the “1992 Consensus” as the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and demonstrated that Chinese on both sides of the Strait have the full capacity and wisdom to resolve the internal issues of the country and the nation, keeping the destiny of the Chinese nation firmly in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.\nThe historic meeting between the leaders of the two sides and the subsequent course of cross-Strait relations have fully demonstrated that as long as we adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence,” and recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and are one family, compatriots on both sides can sit down and talk, enhance mutual understanding, accumulate mutual trust, resolve differences, and seek common ground. Cross-Strait relations can then develop peacefully, peace and stability can be maintained across the Taiwan Strait, and the well-being of compatriots on both sides can be enhanced. Conversely, denying the “1992 Consensus,” departing from the one-China principle, scheming for “Taiwan independence” and separatism, inciting “resisting China and protecting Taiwan,” and creating hostility and confrontation between the two sides will leave cross-Strait consultation and dialogue with no foundation, push the Taiwan Strait toward the danger of war, and harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nUnification is the trend of history and the right path. “Taiwan independence” is a reactionary current of history and a dead end. Only by advancing cross-Strait relations toward complete reunification of the motherland can lasting peace in the Taiwan Strait be ensured. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen dialogue, communication, and exchanges with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and representative figures, including the Kuomintang, to jointly advance the development of cross-Strait relations, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek rejuvenation for the nation. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will work with us in harmony and unity, move forward together, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great cause of national reunification, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, firmly safeguard the common home of the Chinese nation and the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and jointly create a bright future of national rejuvenation and reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The secretary-general of the Lai Clan Association of Fujian Province appealed to Lai Ching-te: “The roots of Taiwan's Lai clan are in the mainland. Refusing to recognize ancestors and refusing to recognize the motherland is a crime against heaven.” Some public opinion has noted that “the Lai surname people are all Chinese” is not only an indisputable truth, but also a fact that Lai Ching-te cannot “lai” (deny or…","The stele at the Lai family ancestral temple in Pinghe County, Zhangzhou City bears this ancestral precept: “Children must be filial to their parents; those who are unfilial are sinners against heaven.” Among the main thoroughfares in urban Taipei are Zhongxiao West Road and Zhongxiao East Road, and Zhongxiao, Renai, Xinyi, and Heping are the four main thoroughfares in Taipei City. These examples all show that loyalty to the country and filial piety toward elders are traditional virtues and values that Chinese on both sides of the Strait commonly revere. Anyone who attempts to split the country or betray the nation is a person without loyalty or filial piety, and will be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that a “Taiwan initiative worker” was denied entry to the World Summit for Social Development at the United Nations and was asked to “change nationality.” Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities said that the UN system has long refused entry to people holding “Republic of China passports,” which has seriously infringed the basic human rights of Taiwan residents to participate in international…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The UN system has long handled Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle confirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, including the issue of personnel from the Taiwan region of China entering UN-related venues. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” openly challenge the one-China principle generally recognized by the international community, create trouble and provocations at international occasions, and will inevitably fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, whether mainland e-commerce platforms Taobao and Pinduoduo can enter Taiwan has drawn attention from public opinion on the island. The head of Taiwan's economic authority said that under Taiwan's laws they are not permitted to operate in Taiwan, and that they will further study how to strengthen the management of overseas e-commerce. What comments do you have on this?","Mainland e-commerce platforms provide cross-Strait residents with a rich variety of affordably priced goods, and they are widely recognized and welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. If mainland e-commerce platforms can go online on the island, they will serve Taiwan residents and enterprises locally, which is a good thing that brings convenience and benefit to the people. The DPP authorities obstruct this and arbitrarily restrict mainland e-commerce platforms from setting up local operations on the island. This again proves that, in order to seek “independence,” they blindly “oppose China,” habitually stand on the opposite side of Taiwan residents, and that whatever they say and do goes against popular will and loses public support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","A Taiwan representative body recently released data showing that from 2021 to 2024, the rate of Taiwan military personnel leaving service early, before completing the minimum active service period, was as high as 24.47%, and compensation amounts exceeded NT$890 million. Some public opinion holds that this result was to be expected, and that young Taiwanese are using “early departure from service” to express that…","The DPP authorities, for their own selfish interests and overestimating their own strength, vainly attempt to “use war to seek independence,” wage reckless militarism, coerce the public into serving as cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence,” and push the vast Taiwan compatriots into dangerous situations of war and peril. It is only natural that Taiwan’s ordinary people and young people do not agree with or cooperate with this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Cable News Network (CNN) recently revealed that Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s external affairs department, who had earlier made a trip to New York, tried to host a banquet for US officials, but in the end no one attended. In response, Lin Chia-lung said that a cognitive warfare group was involved behind the CNN report. What comment do you have on this?","The DPP authorities’ explanation is entirely self-deception, merely an attempt to solemnly cover up their predicament. This once again proves that no matter how the DPP authorities cling to external forces and play petty tricks, it is all in vain. It cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can it shake the basic pattern of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","海峡卫视记者","The DPP authorities recently proposed a plan to redesign New Taiwan dollar banknotes, which has sparked doubts and criticism. Some public opinion on the island points out that spending large sums on redesigning banknotes and changing street names are all part of the same political playbook of the DPP authorities, aimed at removing every element brought to Taiwan from the mainland and completely severing ties with…","This is yet another farce in the DPP authorities' deliberate and meticulous campaign of “de-Sinicization.” It includes revising curriculum guidelines, deleting the term “Han people,” changing street names, and plans to revise the design of the New Taiwan dollar, among other things. In order to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides, the DPP authorities employ all sorts of tricks and stop at nothing. These political manipulations are doomed to be in vain, because the historical fact and current reality that both sides of the Strait belong to one China cannot be changed, and the Chinese national identity of Taiwan compatriots cannot be erased.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","The public security authorities recently opened a criminal investigation into Shen Boyang, a stubborn “Taiwan independence” element. According to CCTV, the mainland side may conduct “global arrests” or “cross-border judicial cooperation” through INTERPOL, which has drawn attention from Taiwan’s public opinion. Taiwan’s National Police Agency said that “freedom of speech is a fundamental human right guaranteed by…","Taiwan is part of China, and “Taiwan independence” is a grave crime of splitting the country and betraying the nation. Pursuing criminal liability against a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards in accordance with law, and taking law enforcement and judicial action, is a just and necessary step to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard national unity. Any “Taiwan independence” diehard who breaks the law will face all necessary punitive measures wherever they may be, and will be held accountable for life in accordance with law. These actions target only a very small number of “Taiwan independence” diehards whose words and deeds on “independence” are egregious and whose secessionist activities are rampant. They are not aimed at, and do not involve, the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Public security organs recently opened a criminal investigation into die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang. Outside observers interpret the mainland’s relentless pursuit of the Shen case as indicating that it already holds concrete evidence. Can you explain the situation? What kind of evidence will the mainland use to request cross-border judicial cooperation from Interpol? Or will it…","I will answer the second question first. Today is the 159th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen. The mainland has always regarded Mr. Sun Yat-sen as a great figure worthy of respect shared by people on both sides of the Strait. Next year marks the 160th anniversary of his birth, and the 14th Meeting of the Standing Committee of the 14th National Committee of the CPPCC recently adopted a decision on holding activities to commemorate the 160th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's birth. Mr. Sun Yat-sen consistently and firmly upheld national unity and ethnic solidarity, and clearly opposed all words and deeds that split the country or split the nation. His spirit and vision are a shared treasure of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. A key purpose of our solemn commemoration of the 160th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's birth is to learn from, inherit, and carry forward his precious spirit, unite all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots, and strive unremittingly to realize the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation.\nAs for the first question: Splitting the country is a serious criminal act. Shen Boyang initiated and established a \"Taiwan independence\" separatist organization, loudly promoted \"Taiwan independence\" separatist fallacies, and has long engaged in criminal activities to split the country. Pursuing criminal liability against him in accordance with the law and taking law enforcement and judicial action is a just and necessary step to implement the \"Opinions on Punishing 'Taiwan Independence' Diehards for the Crime of Splitting the Country and Inciting Secession in Accordance with the Law\" and to safeguard national unity. For \"Taiwan independence\" diehards such as Shen Boyang, who undermine cross-Strait relations and split the country, we will take all necessary measures to punish them and hold them accountable for life in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: The DPP authorities have continued to investigate and deal with persons who have registered household residence on the mainland or applied for mainland passports or ID cards. Taiwan's “Ministry of the Interior” says that as of the end of October, about 50 people had been reported to household registration authorities for cancellation of their Taiwan household registration. What is your comment on…","First question. It is the lawful right of Taiwan compatriots to apply for mainland-related identity documents, and information about such applications and the documents themselves is strictly protected by law. The DPP authorities’ relevant conduct is yet another piece of evidence of their stripping Taiwan compatriots of their legitimate rights and creating a “green terror.” It will surely meet strong opposition and firm resistance from the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question. To further facilitate travel by Taiwan compatriots to and from the mainland, guided by the principles of “greater openness, maximum convenience, and greater security,” on November 3, mainland immigration and exit-entry administration authorities announced that the number of ports authorized to issue one-time Taiwan Compatriot Permits will be expanded from 58 to 100, and this policy will officially take effect on the 20th of this month. Currently, immigration and exit-entry administration authorities across various localities are carrying out preparations in an orderly manner, and we believe Taiwan compatriots will definitely have a better experience traveling to the mainland in the future.\nSince the beginning of this year, in order to facilitate Taiwan compatriots’ travel to the mainland and their work and life on the mainland, we have thought what Taiwan compatriots think and worried about what they worry about. Immigration and exit-entry administration authorities have successively introduced a series of policy measures, including: waiving certificate fees for Taiwan’s “first-time visitors” applying for Taiwan Compatriot Permits; issuing electronic Taiwan Resident Temporary Travel Documents to Taiwan compatriots who have lost their Taiwan Compatriot Permits and urgently need to travel by bus or air; allowing Taiwan compatriots to use facial recognition for expedited clearance at ports such as Gaoqi in Xiamen; and allowing Taiwan compatriots to apply for card-type Taiwan Compatriot Permits at the same time as obtaining one-time Taiwan Compatriot Permits upon arrival. These measures have been warmly welcomed by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and the number of Taiwan Compatriot Permit applications and the number of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland have continued to grow.\nThe Mainland Affairs Council’s claims are purely subjective speculation and will only be proven wrong by reality. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society and the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Yet the DPP authorities have schemed relentlessly to obstruct exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. May I ask, what exactly are you afraid of?\nThird question. Respecting, caring for, and benefiting Taiwan compatriots, cracking down on all kinds of illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law, and actively safeguarding the life, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, are our consistent attitude and consistent practice. The Mainland Affairs Council has repeatedly and maliciously hyped related issues, attempting to intimidate and threaten the Taiwan public and obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel. Its intentions are sinister.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed that 2025 is the year Taiwan rises: not only have export values continued to set new highs, but employment conditions are also the best in 25 years. He expects Taiwan’s economic growth rate to exceed 5% this year, ranking not only first among the Four Asian Tigers but also surpassing the mainland. What is your comment on this?","The purpose of developing the economy is to improve people’s livelihood and well-being and let the people live better lives. At present, the island’s advantageous industries are being forced to relocate their production capacity and lose their advantageous technologies because of the United States’ predatory extraction and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities’ fawning on the United States and selling out Taiwan. Traditional industries face survival difficulties because of the high tariffs imposed on them, and thousands of practitioners struggle to make a living. If the DPP authorities continue to ignore the interests and well-being of enterprises and the public, and insist on fawning on foreign powers and selling out Taiwan, letting themselves “feast” while the people “suffer,” they will eventually be abandoned by the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, Hsiao Tsung-huang, director of the National Palace Museum in Taipei, said that the National Palace Museum's artifacts were “brought to Taiwan when the Republic of China was in power,” are “property of the Republic of China,” and have been in Taiwan for 75 years, having “formed many connections with this land and become part of the nourishment of Taiwan's culture.” What is your comment?","This remark completely contradicts historical fact and basic common sense; it is a bait-and-switch and utterly absurd. As is well known, the roots of Taiwan culture are Chinese culture, and its regional characteristics are merely the enrichment and development of Chinese culture in a particular geographical and historical setting. It is not a so-called “another culture” independent of Chinese culture. The vast majority of the collections of the National Palace Museum in Taipei come from the Chinese mainland. They are an important part of the historical and cultural heritage of the Chinese nation, serving both as irrefutable proof that both sides of the Strait belong to one China and as a vivid expression of the inheritance of Chinese culture in Taiwan.\nOn the one hand, the DPP authorities have vigorously promoted “cultural Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization.” On the other hand, they harbor sinister intentions, seeking to alter the Chinese cultural genes of the treasures of the Palace Museum in order to manipulate them for “Taiwan independence.” How ironic their conduct is, and how ugly their face! Historical facts cannot be altered, and the cultural roots cannot be severed. Any scheme to use the treasures of Chinese culture to promote “Taiwan independence” separatism is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","There have been reports that the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum, which had been decided to be postponed, may be held at the end of December. Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an said the time is not yet set, and that he will continue consultations with Shanghai and will hold the forum on the principles of equality, dignity, goodwill and mutual benefit. Can the Taiwan Affairs Office introduce the current progress?","Shanghai and Taipei City have maintained communication regarding holding this year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and one family. We have consistently supported cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in all fields, including city-to-city exchanges, and we welcome compatriots visiting each other often and engaging in more exchanges, promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhancing the family affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwan media report that the DPP authorities hope to follow the model of the “Taiwan Representative Office in Lithuania” by establishing a “representative office” named “Taiwan” in Tallinn, the capital of Estonia, while Estonia insists on naming it “Taipei.” What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange or establishment of official institutions between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. We hope the relevant countries will adhere to the one-China principle and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness. The DPP authorities attempt to make a fuss over related issues and manipulate them for “independence”; they are increasingly seen through by the international community and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+ 记者","The Mainland side has stated that it will handle matters concerning the Taiwan region's participation in meetings in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions and practices of the APEC memorandum of understanding. In response, the DPP authorities said, “The Mainland's move seriously violates APEC norms and practices, and it will coordinate with like-minded countries to jointly counter it.” What…","Our position on Taiwan’s participation in APEC-related activities is consistent and clear. Under the one-China principle, Taiwan participates in APEC activities under the name “Chinese Taipei” and as a regional economy, in accordance with the provisions and practice of APEC’s relevant memorandums of understanding. This is the political premise for Taiwan’s participation in APEC activities. The DPP authorities are twisting black and white and hyping this without cause, which is entirely futile.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251112_12734329.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-12","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","At the November 12 press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, a reporter asked: China's first electromagnetic catapult aircraft carrier, the Fujian, recently officially entered service, marking the mainland's entry into the “three-carrier era,” which has drawn great attention from public opinion on the island. Some media said this fully demonstrates the significant improvement of the mainland's…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to inquiries, saying that from the Liaoning to the Shandong and then to the Fujian, the arrival of the “three-carrier era” is a major achievement of our national defense and military construction and a solid step of the People's Liberation Army advancing toward a world-class military. Chinese sons and daughters at home and abroad all feel proud of this. The People's Navy is increasingly powerful and is plowing through the deep blue sea. It will more forcefully defend our vast sea frontiers, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and thwart any forces and schemes that infringe upon or split China's sacred territory.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251112_12734320.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-13","Lin Jian","People’s Daily","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said last week that the mainland’s use of force on Taiwan could constitute a “survival-threatening situation” for Japan. It’s reported that during Diet deliberations, Sanae Takaichi said her remark is in line with the government’s position and she will not retract it. What’s China’s comment?","In the Diet last week, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made provocative remarks on Taiwan which imply the possibility of armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait. Despite China’s serious démarches and protests, she still refused to change course and take back what she had said. The wrongful remarks grossly violate the one-China principle, the guiding principles set forth in the four China-Japan political documents, and the basic norms of international relations. That constitutes a blatant interference in China’s internal affairs, a challenge to China’s core interests, and infringement on China’s sovereignty. China firmly opposes and will by no means tolerate such remarks. The Japanese side must correct its wrongdoing at once and retract the unjustified remarks. Otherwise, all the consequences arising therefrom must be borne by the Japanese side.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the recovery of Taiwan. Japan committed innumerable crimes during its colonial rule in Taiwan. Over the last century, Japanese militarists have waged aggression more than once under the pretext of “survival-threatening situation.” For example, Japan brazenly created the September 18th Incident under the pretext of exercising the right of self-defense. Its aggression against China inflicted untold suffering on the people of China, the rest of Asia, and the wider world. What’s Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi up to by reviving the phrase “survival-threatening situation”? Is Japan going to repeat its past mistakes of militarism? Does Japan try to once again make enemy with the Chinese and other Asian people? Does Japan attempt to subvert the post-WWII international order?\nTaiwan belongs to China. How to resolve the Taiwan question and realize national reunification is a matter for the Chinese people to decide and brooks no interference by any external force. The attempt by the leader of Japan to wade into cross-Strait affairs is a serious affront to international justice, a blatant provocation to the post-WWII order, and a great blow to China-Japan relations. If Japan dares to attempt an armed intervention in the cross-Strait situation, it would be an act of aggression and definitely meet a firm response from China. We will firmly exercise our right to self-defense under the U.N. Charter and international law and defend China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. Our message to Japan is clear: Japan must fully repent for its war crimes, immediately stop its wrong and provocative statements and moves that interfere in China’s internal affairs, and stop playing with fire on the Taiwan question. Those who play with fire will perish by it!","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251113_11752756.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251113_11752486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-13","Lin Jian","CCTV","In response to a question from Japanese media on November 12 regarding Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on “Taiwan contingency,” the U.S. State Department spokesperson said that the U.S. is committed to preserving peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and opposes any unilateral changes to the status quo. The U.S. supports cross-Strait dialogue, and hopes that differences will be resolved by peaceful means, free from…","On Sanae Takaichi’s wrong remarks, China has stated its solemn position. Let me reiterate that the Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and brooks no external interference. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop abetting and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop harming China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251113_11752756.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251113_11752486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-13","Lin Jian","RIA Novosti","The G7 foreign ministers yesterday expressed their remaining concerns regarding China’s military build-up and rapid increase of nuclear weapons arsenal. They urged Beijing to demonstrate its commitment to stability. I wonder what’s China’s comment on this statement?","With regard to the joint statement of G7 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting that you mentioned, let me stress that the joint statement once again represents a mischaracterization of facts, a deliberate vilification of China, and a gross interference in China’s internal affairs. China deplores and opposes that.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people, which tolerates no external interference. The situation in the East China Sea and the South China Sea is generally stable. The G7 should stop using maritime issues to stoke disputes, escalate tensions and undermine regional peace and stability. China has always been aboveboard on the Ukraine crisis. China has never provided lethal weapons to any party to the conflict and strictly controls the export of dual-use articles. We never accept the G7’s blame-shifting or groundless accusation.\nWith regard to peace and security, China is the major country with the best track record. China is firmly committed to peaceful development and a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. China always keeps its nuclear strength at the minimum level required by national security. The G7 turns a blind eye to the U.S.’s special and primary nuclear disarmament responsibility and the nuclear proliferation risks from AUKUS while directing the issue at China. This is a typical move of confusing right with wrong.\nChina’s measures to standardize and refine its export control system comply with international common practices and aim to better defend world peace and regional stability and to fulfill its international obligations. The so-called “China’s overcapacity” and “non-market practices” have been proven false by facts and have no merits at all. The G7 should stop politicizing and weaponizing trade issues to refrain from disrupting international economic order and global industrial and supply chains.\nChina once again urges the G7 to take a clear grasp of the global trend, abandon the Cold War mentality and ideological bias, stop manipulating issues related to China, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and make more contributions to solidarity and cooperation in the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251113_11752756.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251113_11752486.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-11-13","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council said on November 13 that Taiwan internet celebrities Wen Tzu-yu (温子渝, online name \"Ba Jiong\" (八炯)) and Chen Po-yuan (陈柏源, online name \"Min Nan Wolf\" (闽南狼)) have for a long time released and disseminated remarks inciting the splitting of the country, such as \"resisting China and protecting Taiwan\" and \"relying on the United States to seek independence,\" have extensively attacked and smeared the mainland's policies benefiting Taiwan and the people, bullied and persecuted mainland spouses in Taiwan and Taiwan compatriots who support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and served as thugs and accomplices for \"Taiwan independence,\" aiding and abetting evil with a bad influence. The public security organs issued a notice offering rewards for clues to their illegal and criminal activities; this is a concrete action to punish, according to law, the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country, is a just act responding to the call of cross-Strait citizens to punish \"independence,\" and is legitimate and necessary.\n\"Taiwan independence\" thugs and accomplices who commit wrongdoing and act as henchmen for evil are despised by people on both sides of the Strait. Such petty and despicable people must be severely punished according to law and held accountable for life. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide relevant clues to illegal and criminal activities, resolutely oppose any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct, firmly safeguard our common Chinese home, and join hands to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251113_12734519.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-14","Lin Jian","CCTV","It’s reported that Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi in the Diet this week avoided stating whether her administration adheres to the Three Non-Nuclear Principles. There are also reports saying that when asked about the possibility of acquiring nuclear submarines, Chief Cabinet Secretary Minoru Kihara said Japan has not ruled out any options. Japanese Defense Minister Shinjiro Koizumi publicly called for Tokyo to…","China is seriously concerned over Japan’s military and security moves recently. While Japan claims to be a peace-loving country and advocates a world free of nuclear weapons, the Sanae Takaichi administration has been making ambiguous statements about the Three Non-Nuclear Principles and implying the possibility of quitting the principles. Japanese senior officials even claimed that Japan has not ruled out the possibility of possessing nuclear submarines. These fully reveal that Japan is making a major negative policy shift, which sends a dangerous signal to the international community.\nDuring World War II, Japanese militarists’ war of aggression and brutal crimes against humanity inflicted untold suffering on the region and beyond. In recent years, Japan has been drastically readjusting its security policy, increasing defense spending year after year, relaxing restrictions on arms export, seeking to develop offensive weapons, and going further down the wrong path of military buildup. Last week, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made provocative remarks on Taiwan which imply the possibility of armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait. Owing to these moves by Japan, its neighboring countries in Asia and the international community have to strongly call into question and worry about: Has Japan truly made a clean break with militarism? Is Japan sincerely committed to the exclusively defense-oriented policy and the Three Non-Nuclear Principles? Will Japan still act on its commitment to peaceful development?\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the recovery of Taiwan. We urge Japan to repent for its history of aggression, stick to the path of peaceful development, stop finding excuses for its military buildup, and take concrete actions to earn the trust from its Asian neighbors and the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251114_11753607.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251114_11753464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-14","Lin Jian","Global Times","It’s reported that according to the Pentagon, U.S. Department of State approved the sale to Taiwan of non-standard components and repair support for F-16, C-130, and Indigenous Defense Fighter aircraft for an estimated total cost of US$330 million, marking the first such transaction in President Donald Trump’s second term. What’s China’s comment?","The U.S.’s arms sale to China’s Taiwan region grossly violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué of 1982, infringes on China’s sovereignty and security interests, contravenes international law, and sends a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China deplores and opposes that.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and is the first red line that cannot be crossed in China-U.S. relations. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ commitment on Taiwan-related issues, stop abetting and aiding separatist forces’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup, and take concrete actions in the interests of China-U.S. relations and cross-Strait peace and stability. China will do what is necessary to firmly defend China’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251114_11753607.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251114_11753464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-14","Lin Jian","Nippon TV","Japanese ambassador in Beijing was summoned last night by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which I think is quite a rare case in recent years, calling the top leader of the embassy. Could you tell us the reason why this time China insisted on face-to-face protests against Japanese ambassador?","Last night, Vice Foreign Minister Sun Weidong summoned Japanese ambassador to China. China released a readout on that. The root cause lies in Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s extremely wrongful, dangerous and provocative remarks on Taiwan and her refusal to change course and retract what she had said. That grossly interferes in China’s internal affairs, violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, damages the post-WWII international order, contravenes the one-China principle and the guiding principles set forth in the four China-Japan political documents, disrupts the political foundations of China-Japan relations, and hurts the Chinese people’s sentiments. We also noted that many politicians and people with vision in Japan raised caution and criticism.\nChina cherishes peace and values good faith. That said, when it comes to China’s sovereignty, territorial integrity and any other issues concerning China’s core interests, no one shall ever expect any compromise or concession from China. No one shall have the illusion that China will swallow the bitter fruit that undermines its interests. Whoever dares to challenge China’s bottom line will face a resolute, head-on blow and be shattered against the great wall of steel forged by over 1.4 billion Chinese people. For anyone who dares to hold back China’s reunification: Failure will be their fate.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251114_11753607.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251114_11753464.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-11-14","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi recently said that if the Chinese mainland uses military vessels and other forces against Taiwan, it would cause a situation threatening Japan's survival, and the Japanese Self-defense Force could exercise the right of collective self-defense in accordance with law. Do you have any comment?","The erroneous remarks on Taiwan made by the Japanese leader constitute a gross interference in China's internal affairs, and a serious violation of the one-China principle, the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and the basic norms governing international relations. The remarks have challenged the post-war international order, and sent very wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. Such words are egregious in nature and have caused very negative impact. They are extremely irresponsible and dangerous.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. This year, we commemorated the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. Should the Japanese side fail to draw lessons from history and dare to take a risk, or even use force to interfere in the Taiwan question, it will only suffer a crushing defeat against the steel-willed PLA and pay a heavy price.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251114-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16421952.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-14","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to information from relevant Taiwan agencies, nearly a quarter of the volunteer soldiers recruited in the past four years failed to complete the minimum service year and chose to pay compensation to be demobilized in advance. Please comment on that.","This number shows that more people in Taiwan have seen through Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities' malicious and selfish intention of hijacking the public to seek \"Taiwan independence\". A growing number of young people in Taiwan have now refused to be cannon fodder. \"Taiwan independence\" will not only cost the young generation their future and even their lives, but also destroy the future of Taiwan. We hope compatriots in Taiwan can be more courageous in saying no to \"Taiwan independence\" to protect their own security interests and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251114-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16421952.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-11-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi recently stated that if mainland China were to use force against Taiwan, it could constitute a “survival-threatening situation” for Japan. After China’s stern representations, Takaichi still falsely claimed that the remarks conform to the Japanese government’s views, and shows no intention to retract or cancel them. What comments do you have on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that Taiwan is the sacred territory of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the shared aspiration of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people. As for the means, it is entirely a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and no external force may interfere. Japan and its leaders have no qualifications whatsoever to make irresponsible remarks, let alone resort to veiled threats in an attempt to obstruct China's great cause of reunification.\nJapan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. After the First Sino-Japanese War, Japan forcibly occupied Taiwan and carried out a colonial rule lasting half a century. During the Japanese occupation, the people of Taiwan suffered enormous calamity: hundreds of thousands of compatriots were killed, the people were reduced to “slaves of a lost nation,” and they had no political rights, freedom of religion, or cultural freedom. The mineral resources and livelihood materials of the Treasure Island were plundered frantically. The crimes committed by Japanese invaders in Taiwan are too numerous to record, forming the darkest page in Taiwan's history. The entire Chinese military and civilian population, including Taiwan compatriots, fought bloodily, defeated the Japanese militarist aggressors, won the great victory of the War of Resistance Against Japan, and recovered Taiwan. On the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan, instead of reflecting on its history of crimes and drawing lessons from its painful past, Japan's Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi has put forward blatant remarks concerning Taiwan with a hostile attitude, attempting to interfere in the situation across the Taiwan Strait, deny the fruits of victory in the War of Resistance, and challenge the post-war international order. The Chinese government and the Chinese people will absolutely not accept, will not tolerate, and will not indulge this. If Japan does not immediately correct its mistakes and retract its erroneous remarks, it must bear all consequences arising therefrom. If it dares to intervene militarily in the Taiwan question, we will strike it head-on and resolutely crush it.\nThe Taiwan question concerns China's core interests and the national sentiments of all Chinese people. We have the firm will, strong determination, and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No matter how external forces create trouble, the historical trend that China will be reunified, and will surely be reunified, cannot be stopped. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will fully recognize the danger and harmfulness of such acts, and will join us in safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation and in upholding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the safety and well-being of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251114_12735097.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The US Department of Defense announced a sale of arms to Taiwan, China, worth about US$330 million. The DPP authorities immediately expressed thanks. What is your comment?","Spokesperson Chen Binhua of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responding to questions, said: We firmly oppose the United States selling weapons to the Taiwan region of China. This position is consistent and clear. This move by the US seriously harms China's sovereignty and security interests and sends a serious wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the US to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17” Communiqué, to stop condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and to handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Since the Lai Qingde authorities took office, they have constantly curried favor with outsiders and pledged allegiance, pursued militarism, lavishly squandered the hard-earned money of the Taiwan people, and gone to great lengths to turn Taiwan into a “powder keg,” sacrificing the security and well-being of the Taiwan public. We solemnly warn the Lai Qingde authorities that “relying on outside forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” are a road to a dead end. We will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251115_12735208.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-17","Mao Ning","CCTV","Several days ago, some individual Japanese politician said China was “overreacting” to Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan. Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Minoru Kihara said the Japanese government’s position on the Taiwan question remains unchanged and is consistent with the 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement. What is China’s response?","China has made its serious position clear several times on Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s wrongful remarks on Taiwan. The remarks seriously violate the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and cause fundamental damage to the political foundation of China-Japan relations.\nDuring the discussions on resuming China-Japan diplomatic ties, China explicitly put forth three principles: the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole and legal government representing the Chinese people; the Taiwan Province is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China; and the so-called “Taiwan-Japan Treaty” is illegal and invalid and must be abrogated.\nIn 1972, the two countries signed the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement and officially established diplomatic relations. Three places in the Joint Statement are related to the Taiwan question. First, in the opening paragraphs, it is written that the Japanese side “reaffirms its position that it intends to realize the normalization of relations between the two countries from the stand of fully understanding ‘the three principles for resuming diplomatic relations’ put forward by the Government of the People’s Republic of China.” Then Article 2 says that “the Government of Japan recognizes that Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China.” And Article 3 says that “the Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.”\nIn 1978, the two countries signed the Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, which explicitly stated that the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement “constitutes the basis for relations of peace and friendship between the two countries and that the principles set out in that statement should be strictly observed.” The treaty affirmed the principles and contents of the joint statement in legal terms and set out the legal parameters for China-Japan relations.\nIn 1998, the two sides released the China-Japan Joint Declaration on Building a Partnership of Friendship and Cooperation for Peace and Development, in which Japan undertook to “continue to maintain its stand on the Taiwan question which was set forth in the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement” and “reiterated its understanding that there is one China.” It’s stated in the document that Japan will continue to only maintain its exchanges of private and regional nature with Taiwan, which ruled out the legal possibility of Japan developing official relations with Taiwan.\nIn 2008, the China-Japan Joint Statement on All-round Promotion of Strategic Relationship of Mutual Benefit stipulated clearly in Article 5 that “The Japanese side reiterated that it will continue to abide by its position on the Taiwan question stated in the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement.”\nThe above is what is laid out in the four political documents between China and Japan regarding the Taiwan question. It constitutes the solemn commitment made by the Japanese government and has a legal effect under international law. There is no room whatsoever for ambiguity or misinterpretation. Whichever political party or person is in power in Japan, they must always abide by the commitment of the Japanese government on the Taiwan question. We urge Japan to approach history and relations with China in a responsible way, stop crossing the line and playing with fire, retract the wrongful remarks and seriously act to honor Japan’s commitment to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251117_11754686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251117_11754501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-17","Mao Ning","Kyodo News","The Director-General of the Japanese Foreign Ministry’s Asian and Oceanian Affairs Bureau, Kanai Masaaki, is expected to arrive in China today. He will hold talks with China concerning Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan. What’s China’s comment? Besides, the Chinese government has called on Chinese tourists to avoid traveling to Japan due to rising security risks there. Can you give us any examples?","On the talks you mentioned, we will release timely information when available. Let me stress that regarding Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s wrongful remarks on Taiwan, China has and will continue to lodge strong démarches and protests with Japan, seriously ask Japan to immediately reflect on and correct its wrongdoing, retract the wrongful remarks and stop making provocations on China-related issues.\nOn your second question, for some time, there has been an increase in crimes targeting Chinese nationals in Japan, as well as extreme and threatening remarks targeting China from Japanese right-wing provocateurs and internet users. China is highly concerned about this and it’s fully justified for competent authorities to release the alerts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251117_11754686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251117_11754501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-17","Mao Ning","The Asahi Shimbun","The announcement of the results of a Japan-China joint opinion poll and the Tokyo-Beijing Forum have been postponed at the request of China. How does the Foreign Ministry view the significance of the opinion poll and the forum? What is your comment on the postponement?","On the opinion poll, the provocative remarks recently made by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan have seriously eroded the political foundation of China-Japan relations and poisoned public opinion. The environment and conditions for the joint opinion poll have changed enormously, so how much the results reflect reality and the timing of the announcement need to be re-considered. The responsibility lies completely in the wrong remarks of the Japanese leader.\nOn the postponement of the Beijing-Tokyo Forum, this was decided after consultation between the co-hosts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251117_11754686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251117_11754501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-17","Mao Ning","TV Asahi","Chinese authorities have issued notices, advising Chinese nationals to avoid traveling to Japan for the time being. This may affect many Chinese and dampen people-to-people exchanges between the two countries. What is China’s comment?","The wrongful remarks by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan have seriously hurt the feelings of the Chinese people and poisoned the atmosphere for people-to-people exchange between China and Japan. Japan needs to remain committed to the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, correct the wrong remarks and actions at once, and avoid causing further damage to China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251117_11754686.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251117_11754501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-11-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that the US State Department approved a total of about US$330 million in arms sales to Taiwan, including “non-standard aviation spare parts and components” for related aircraft models and maintenance services. What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Zhang Xiaogang said that the U.S. sale of weapons to Taiwan, China seriously violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, brutally interferes in China's internal affairs, harms China's sovereignty and security interests, and sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied with and firmly oppose this, and we have lodged solemn representations with the U.S. side.\n“It must be stressed that ‘using arms to aid independence’ will only bring disaster upon oneself, and ‘using Taiwan to contain China’ will not succeed,” Zhang Xiaogang said. “We urge the U.S. side to immediately stop its vicious practice of arming Taiwan, and avoid impacting and affecting the development of China-U.S. and military-to-military relations. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's ordinary people on buying weapons is merely quenching thirst with poison. ‘Relying on outsiders to seek independence’ and ‘using arms to resist reunification’ are doomed to fail. We will take all necessary measures to firmly defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.”","","https://cn.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202511/18/WS691bababa310942cc4991e87.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2025-11-18","Mao Ning","DPA","After holding the high-level financial dialogue with Vice Premier He Lifeng, German Vice Chancellor and Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil said that the two sides talked about the Taiwan question, and the German government is concerned about possible escalation of cross-Strait tensions. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and brooks no interference by any external forces. The key to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is to uphold the one-China principle and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251118_11755479.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251118_11755239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-18","Mao Ning","CCTV","Recently, we’ve seen intense criticism from China on Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan. Some believe that relations between the two countries have hit the lowest point in recent years. Where do you think the relationship is headed?","The current situation in China-Japan relations is caused by Prime Minister Takaichi’s blatant remarks on Taiwan. Those remarks grossly interfered in China’s internal affairs, violated the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries, and eroded the political foundation of bilateral relations.\nChina stands firm to defend its core interests and international justice. Japan must retract its erroneous remarks, repent and change course, offering a clear and satisfactory answer to the Chinese people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251118_11755479.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251118_11755239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","CCTV","Many analysts have pointed to the fact that Sanae Takaichi is the first Japanese prime minister to explicitly describe a hypothetical scenario concerning Taiwan as a “survival-threatening situation.” It implies that Japan could exercise the right of “collective self-defense” if such a situation occurs, which makes Japan’s armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait a possibility. That would be unacceptable to China…","The right of collective self-defense set forth in the UN Charter is created to safeguard the collective security of the international community and prevent the revival of fascist forces. Japan has been restricted from exercising this right since the end of World War II. The Potsdam Proclamation clearly states that Japan should not “re-arm.” Japan commits in its Constitution to “forever renouncing war and the threat or use of force as means of settling international disputes” and established the exclusively defense-oriented principle. Together they codified Japan’s obligations as a defeated country.\nA brief look at history will show us that to use “survival-threatening situation” and “self-defense” as a pretext is a go-to tactic for Japanese militarism to launch aggression. In 1931, Japan called whether it could seize “Manchuria” as “survival-threatening,” and used that as a pretext to carry out the September 18th Incident and invaded and occupied Northeast China. Japan later claimed that to defend “the Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere” was an existential battle for Japan, enlarging its war of aggression to the entire Asia. Whether to attack Pearl Harbor was also deemed as “survival-threatening” to Japan, which ignited the Pacific War.\nThe alarm has been sounded. The historical tragedy must not repeat itself. As we mark the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, the international community must guard against and firmly thwart any attempt of reviving militarism, jointly uphold the post-WWII international order and safeguard world peace.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","CGTN","On November 18 local time, the 80th session of the UN General Assembly deliberated on the reform of the Security Council. The Chinese representative explicitly pointed out in his remarks that Japan “is totally unqualified to seek a permanent seat on the Security Council.” What is your comment?","According to the UN Charter, the Security Council bears primary responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security. Japan waged a war of aggression during the Second World War, inflicting profound sufferings on the people of Asia and the world. To this day, Japan still has not fully repented for its war crimes. Some in Japan continue to advocate a wrong perception of World War II history, and they still pay tribute to the Yasukuni Shrine, and distort, deny and even whitewash Japan’s history of aggression. The erroneous remarks of Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs, trample on international law and basic norms in international relations, and challenge the post-WWII international order. A country like this is in no position to take up the responsibility for maintaining international peace and security, and is unfit for permanent membership of the Security Council.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","AFP","Prosecutors in Taiwan charged seven people, including a person from Chinese mainland, on Tuesday with violating national security after they allegedly collected military secrets for Chinese mainland. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","This is not related to foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","NHK","We’ve learned that China has notified Japan it will suspend the imports of Japanese aquatic products. Can you share the details and the reason for this?","Japan made a commitment to fulfill the regulatory responsibility of guaranteeing the quality and safety of its aquatic products exported to China. This is the prerequisite for China’s import of Japanese aquatic products. However, Japan has so far been unable to provide the technical materials under its commitment.\nLet me reiterate that because of Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s egregious moves and erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan and other major issues of principle, there has been strong outrage and condemnation from the Chinese people. Under current circumstances, there will be no market for Japanese aquatic products even if they enter China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","Reuters","Yesterday, Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary Kihara when asked about whether Japan plans to retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s remarks about Taiwan responded by saying those remarks were in line with Japan’s long-standing views. Do you have any comment on this?","Let me stress that Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have fundamentally eroded the political foundation of China-Japan relations and triggered strong outrage and condemnation from the Chinese people. China seriously urges Japan to retract the erroneous remarks, stop making provocations on issues concerning China, take practical steps to admit and correct the wrongdoing, and uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations. If Japan refuses to retract them or even continue to pursue the wrong course, China will have to take strong and resolute countermeasures and all consequences arising therefrom will be borne by Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-19","Mao Ning","BBC","Just to follow up on the previous question, you said if Prime Minister Takaichi did not retract her comments, China would take further countermeasures. What further financial and diplomatic pressure is China threatening?","I just elaborated on China’s position. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan damaged the political foundation of China-Japan relations. China has every reason to take countermeasures. Japan needs to, first and foremost, retract the erroneous remarks and take practical steps to redress the wrongdoing. Otherwise, China will have to take further measures.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251119_11756196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251119_11756095.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 19, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning everyone, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The National Immigration Administration announced that starting November 20, the number of ports that can issue one-time-valid Mainland Travel Permits for Taiwan Residents will be expanded to 100. What is the current status of preparations?","Starting tomorrow, the number of ports from which the mainland can issue a single-entry Taiwan compatriot permit (台胞证) will increase to 100. Preparations are in place, and we sincerely invite Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for a “trip you can set off on at a moment’s notice.” The 100 ports include 56 air ports, 27 waterway ports, and 17 railway and road ports. From Kashgar and Khorgos in the northwest to Fuyuan Port and Suifenhe in the northeast, and from Youyiguan and Mohan in the southwest to the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge and Pingtan Port in the southeast, Taiwan compatriots can enter conveniently and safely and fully feel the warmth of “home.”\nIf Taiwan compatriot friends have not applied in advance for a five-year valid Taiwan compatriot permit, then upon arriving at any of the above ports, they may apply for a single-entry Taiwan compatriot permit at the application window of the exit-entry administration authority at the port by presenting a valid Taiwan identity card, Taiwan-area entry-exit documents, and application photos. The entire process takes only 30 minutes. Taiwan compatriots who plan to take “Mini Three Links” routes and enter through Fujian ports may apply for a single-entry permit at the port window, or apply online by logging into the “National Immigration Administration 12367” app or the “National Immigration Administration 12367” mini program on WeChat or Alipay. In the “single-entry Taiwan compatriot permit application” column, they fill in the 《Application Form for Taiwan Residents’ Travel Permit to the Mainland》 and upload the application materials as required. Once approved, they can collect the permit upon arrival at the entry port. Whether Taiwan compatriots apply for permits or enter and exit the mainland, no marks will be placed on their documents. In accordance with relevant laws and regulations, the competent mainland authorities strictly, forcefully, and effectively protect the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots.\nWe also especially note that Taiwan compatriot friends visiting the mainland for the first time may enjoy two exclusive benefits: first, no document fee is charged when applying for a Taiwan compatriot permit; second, they may visit more than 3,000 scenic spots free of charge. Many Taiwan compatriots have praised these convenience measures and look forward to coming to the mainland to see it for themselves. Winter has arrived, and we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to the northeast and northwest to take part in winter sports or ice-and-snow cultural tourism activities, to visit relatives and friends, go sightseeing, and trace their roots and pay respects to their ancestors. We will continue to create better conditions and provide better services for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736028.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 11th Chinese Culture Forum was recently held in Beijing. Participants from both sides of the Strait said that the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China made important arrangements for “vigorously developing cultural undertakings” and “accelerating the development of cultural industries,” and that Chinese people on both sides of the Strait can do much in jointly…","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture; both speak Chinese, write Chinese characters, savor Chinese flavors, and celebrate Chinese festivals. Chinese culture is the root of the spirit and the place of belonging for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China made important arrangements for \"vigorously developing cultural undertakings\" and \"accelerating the development of cultural industries,\" and at the same time pointed out \"deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and jointly inheriting and promoting Chinese culture,\" painting a bright prospect and injecting powerful momentum for promoting cross-Strait cultural exchanges and cooperation.\nThe soul of a nation is cultivated and shaped through culture. We will thoroughly study, understand, and implement the spirit of the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, comprehensively implement Xi Jinping Thought on Culture and the overall strategy of the new era for the Party's resolution of the Taiwan question, deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, promote the joint inheritance and promotion of Chinese culture across the Strait, tighten the emotional bonds and interest linkages between the two sides, enhance the identification of compatriots on both sides with Chinese culture and the Chinese nation, forge a sense of the community of common destiny across the Strait, and consolidate the foundation for the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and cultural exchange activities.","In terms of economic and trade exchanges, from November 10 to 14, the 21st Guangxi-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation Forum was held in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region. Themed “Sharing New Opportunities in the AI Era, Advancing New Development of Guangxi-Taiwan Cooperation,” the forum deepened the integrated development of AI industry empowerment and industry application scenarios in Guangxi-Taiwan cooperation.\nFrom November 17 to 20, the “Seeking Development · Promoting Integration: Famous Taiwan Enterprises Visit Longyan” event was held in Longyan, Fujian. Nearly 80 Taiwan-funded enterprises gathered in Longyan, focusing on industry matchmaking in areas including machinery manufacturing, electronics and information, and agricultural product processing, and sharing new opportunities for economic and trade cooperation.\nIn terms of cultural exchange, on November 4, the 2025 “Memories of Migration to Taiwan” Taiwan compatriot ancestral homeland visit was held in Zhangzhou, Fujian. More than 100 kinsmen from both sides of the Strait gathered together, using ancestry as a link and memory as a bridge, to share stories of blood ties and trace the roots of the nation. The book “Stories Behind ‘Memories of Migration to Taiwan’” was launched at the event.\nFrom November 18 to 27, the Overseas Taiwan Compatriots Jiangsu Visit was held in Jiangsu. Dozens of Taiwan compatriots living in the United States traveled to Nanjing and other places for economic and trade inspection and cultural exchange, paid respects at the Sun Yat-sen Mausoleum, visited the Sun Yat-sen Memorial Hall, and donated to the Nanjing Massacre Victims Memorial Hall the book “The Nanjing Massacre” by Chinese American Yin Jijun, to promote compatriots at home and abroad jointly remembering history, honoring martyrs, cherishing peace, and creating the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The 5th “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams—Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar Activity” will be held in Chengdu. Please introduce the relevant information.","The “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriot Exchange and Seminar Activity” is jointly organized by the Cross-Strait Relations Research Center and Taiwan patriotic reunification groups, and has been successfully held four times since 2021. The fifth event will be held in Chengdu, Sichuan Province, on November 20–21. Representatives from relevant parties across the Taiwan Strait, leaders and representatives of political parties and groups, experts and scholars, and representatives of Taiwan compatriots and young people from Taiwan will discuss, around the theme of the victory of the War of Resistance against Japan and Taiwan’s restoration, and promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and exchanges on advancing the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2025 Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival series of activities drew attention from young people on both sides of the Strait, and many of them took part and exchanged ideas through film and television works. Please introduce recent cross-Strait film and television exchange activities. How do you view exchange and cooperation in film and television between young people and film industry…","Recently, new cross-Strait film and television exchange activities have kept emerging. During the 2025 Golden Rooster and Hundred Flowers Film Festival, a series of cross-Strait film exchange activities was successfully held. First, more than 50 well-known Taiwan film actors took part in the activities, and 15 Taiwan films, including *Seediq Bale* and *角头：斗阵欸*, were screened. Second, the 6th Cross-Strait, Hong Kong, Macao and Youth Short Film Season collected 144 outstanding Taiwan short films, creating a platform for cross-Strait young filmmakers to exchange and discuss. Third, the Golden Rooster promotion conference, Taiwan special session, focused on promoting 9 Taiwan film projects and 5 literary IPs. Fourth, the “Xiamen-Kinmen Light and Shadow Connect” series of activities was held for the first time, and more than 3,000 Taiwan compatriots took part in the Golden Rooster Hundred Flowers Film Life Season’s preferential benefit activities and the live cinema broadcast of the Golden Rooster Awards closing ceremony through convenient channels.\nOn November 13, the Yunnan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office supported businesspeople on both sides in jointly creating and releasing two micro-drama series, *《山海心语 花香两岸》* and *《果然有你》*. These two micro-dramas were performed by Taiwan farmers and Taiwan businesspeople themselves, telling stories of Taiwan farmers and businesspeople putting down roots in Yunnan and realizing their dreams, and reflecting new achievements in cross-Strait film and television cooperation and the integration of media and industry. We believe that after watching them, even more Taiwan compatriots will go to Yunnan to enjoy the flowers, taste the fruits, and see the beautiful scenery.\nWe have always supported cultural exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in film, television, music, and other fields, and we are glad to see cultural workers on both sides visit each other often and collaborate to create more outstanding works, jointly inherit and carry forward the fine traditional Chinese culture, and promote the integrated development of cross-Strait audiovisual industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","According to US media reports, in the Taiwan-US tariff negotiations the United States has demanded that Taiwan invest between 350 billion and 550 billion US dollars in the United States. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities said they are negotiating supply chain cooperation with the US using the “Taiwan model.” Some on the island have argued that this will seriously impact and crowd out Taiwan’s…","The United States has continuously used tariffs and other means to coerce and hollow out Taiwan's industries. Faced with U.S. squeezing, the DPP authorities have been groveling all the way and straining to show their loyalty. This has caused Taiwan residents great pain recently, and we are deeply concerned. US$350–550 billion is equivalent to about 44% to 69% of Taiwan's 2024 gross domestic product (Note: US$796.904 billion), and about 58% to 92% of Taiwan's foreign exchange reserves as of October this year (Note: US$600.2 billion). If the reports are true, they can only show that, in order to pursue “relying on foreigners to seek independence,” the DPP authorities are handing over the hard-earned money of Taiwan residents on a silver platter, completely disregarding the interests of Taiwan residents and businesses. The so-called “Taiwan model” is purely a “kneel-to-the-US model,” a fig leaf for selling out Taiwan. It will inevitably cause funds, technology, and talent on the island to keep flowing to the United States, and will seriously harm the development of Taiwan's industries. The so-called “Taiwan-US supply chain cooperation” is even more a blatant plunder and seizure of Taiwan's advantageous industries by the United States. From “fifty-fifty split” to “taking the whole pot,” Taiwan's core industrial advantages have been lost, and employment, investment, and development momentum on the island will suffer a devastating blow.\nMore and more facts have made Taiwan residents realize that the United States always pursues “America first.” By fawning over and pledging loyalty to the United States at the expense of the well-being of the public and the island's economic prospects, the DPP authorities will ultimately face the fate of Taiwan being sucked dry by the United States. We warn the DPP authorities: damaging the foundations of Taiwan's industrial development and the interests and well-being of its residents for the sake of a party's or an individual's private interests is a despicable act that will surely be condemned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736020.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The DPP authorities said that in 2024, 2.77 million person-times of people traveled to the mainland, and from January to September this year, the figure was 2.344 million person-times. From January to October this year, 169,000 mainland residents visited Kinmen and Matsu for sightseeing. Insiders revealed that although there is a \"group travel ban,\" some island operators have organized groups to travel to the…","These figures show that the restrictions and limitations imposed by the DPP authorities cannot stop compatriots on both sides from drawing closer to each other. We have consistently upheld the concept of “one family across the Strait” and actively promoted personnel exchanges across the Strait, including tourism, and cooperation and exchanges in all fields. We warmly welcome compatriots from Taiwan to visit the mainland more often, experience the splendid Chinese culture, feel the changes and development of the mainland, and share in the mainland's progress. We will follow the principles of “greater opening, greater convenience and greater safety,” create convenient conditions for compatriots from Taiwan coming to the mainland, and provide quality services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Public security authorities issued a reward notice soliciting leads on the illegal and criminal activities of Taiwanese internet celebrities Wen Tzu-yu and Chen Po-yuan, and will give meritorious persons rewards of RMB 50,000 to 250,000 as appropriate. Will reward notices be issued against more “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices in the future, and what are the standards of the relevant reward mechanism?","Wen Tzu-yu and Chen Po-yuan have for a long time published and disseminated remarks inciting national separation, such as \"resist China, protect Taiwan\" and \"rely on the US to seek independence,\" vehemently attacked and smeared the mainland's policies benefiting Taiwan and its people, bullied and persecuted mainland spouses in Taiwan and Taiwan compatriots who support peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and served as henchmen and accomplices of \"Taiwan independence,\" aiding wrongdoers and causing grave harm. Public security authorities issued a notice offering rewards to collect clues to their illegal and criminal activities. This is a concrete action to punish, in accordance with law, crimes of separating the country and inciting separation of the country, and it is a righteous step responding to the calls of people on both sides of the Strait to punish \"Taiwan independence.\" The reward measures in the reward notice will be implemented by the public security authorities in accordance with relevant laws and regulations.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. A very small number of bad apples, such as hardline \"Taiwan independence\" diehards and their henchmen and accomplices, commit wrongdoing and act as accomplices, and the vast majority of Taiwan residents deeply detest their conduct and support their being severely punished in accordance with law. The relevant punitive measures target only hardline \"Taiwan independence\" diehards and their henchmen and accomplices, and do not involve the broad masses of Taiwan residents. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide relevant clues to illegal and criminal activities, and firmly oppose any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736022.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","It is reported that Taiwan's \"Sanhe Practical Research Institute\" held a forum on the morning of the 15th, inviting representatives of the New Party and young people to engage in in-depth discussion of cross-Strait relations and their future direction around the theme \"Peaceful Reunification, One Country, Two Systems Taiwan Plan: Seven Betters.\" What is your comment on this?","“Peaceful reunification, one country two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification, and it is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides and the Chinese nation. The historical wheel of national reunification and national rejuvenation is rolling forward. The sooner the Taiwan question is resolved and the motherland reunified, the more it will benefit Taiwan’s development and the better life Taiwan compatriots will be able to have.\nPeaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan’s economic and social development and will bring tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, as more and more far-sighted people on the island have already recognized. We welcome Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and far-sighted people from all walks of life, including the New Party, to offer suggestions for the “two systems” Taiwan plan and to contribute wisdom and strength to achieving national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736021.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Public security authorities recently issued a bounty notice seeking clues to the illegal and criminal activities of Taiwanese internet celebrities 温子渝 and 陈柏源. The Mainland Affairs Council said the mainland intends to disrupt social morale in Taiwan, and that Taiwan residents who cooperate with the mainland's bounty by providing relevant clues will be investigated in accordance with the law. What comments do you…","Many Taiwan residents have expressed contempt for the Mainland Affairs Council’s intimidation, and have distanced themselves from Shen Boyang, Wen Tzu-yu, Chen Bo-yuan and their ilk by various means. The public security organs issued a notice offering rewards for information on the illegal and criminal activities of these two individuals. This is a concrete action to punish, in accordance with law, the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country, and a righteous act in response to the call from compatriots on both sides of the Strait to punish “independence.” We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide relevant information on illegal and criminal activities through relevant channels. The relevant authorities will strictly protect the informants’ information and lawful rights and interests in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736024.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently called on Han Kuo-yu to support Shen Po-yang, a diehard “Taiwan independence” element whom mainland public security authorities have opened a case to investigate. Han Kuo-yu criticized Lai Ching-te for “being sick himself and making others take the medicine,” stating that if Lai truly wanted to help Shen Po-yang, he should abolish the DPP's “Taiwan independence” party platform and retract…","“Taiwan independence” stubborn elements commit wrongdoing, and they deserve punishment and will certainly be severely punished. Faced with the sword of punishing “independence” being drawn, the DPP authorities and the stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements are flustered and panicked, attempting to shift contradictions and divert attention. The DPP authorities’ provocations to seek “independence” are the source of tension and turmoil in cross-strait relations, and the stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements are the vanguard of seeking “independence” nurtured by the DPP authorities. Only by upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, and resolutely punishing stubborn “Taiwan independence” elements can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots be effectively protected.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736025.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the U.S. Department of Defense announced a military sales project to the Taiwan region of China worth approximately US$330 million. Han Rubo (韩儒伯), chairman of the American Chamber of Commerce in Taipei (“American Institute in Taiwan”-linked business association, as described), said that this arms sale shows the U.S. side’s commitment to helping Taiwan’s military maintain high readiness rates, and that…","We firmly oppose the United States providing weapons to Chinese Taiwan in any form. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, stop “arming Taiwan,” and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.\nIn pursuit of political self-interest, the DPP authorities willingly serve as an “ATM” for American arms dealers, squandering the hard-earned money of the island’s people and begging for the false “protection” of external forces. This will only make Taiwan more dangerous and bring grave disasters to Taiwan compatriots. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that the reunification of the motherland is unstoppable, and that “relying on the United States to seek independence” and “seeking independence through force” are doomed to be a mantis trying to stop a chariot, bringing about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”记者","On March 26, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office government website launched the “Special Column for Reporting Vicious Acts by ‘Taiwan Independence’ Thugs and Accomplices Who Persecute Taiwan Compatriots.” What is the current status of the reports received? What punitive measures will the mainland side take against the individuals reported?","Since the mailbox for reporting the heinous acts of “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices began operating, reports have poured in, and more than 10,000 reporting emails have been received. This fully demonstrates the attitude of people on both sides of the Strait in wanting to severely punish “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices, and it also reflects the common voice of people on both sides of the Strait in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advancing the great cause of national reunification. We support relevant departments in cracking down strictly on “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices, based on facts and in accordance with the law, and holding them accountable for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Reports say the DPP authorities are seeking for Lai Ching-te to “transit” through the United States before the end of the year. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose Lai Qingde's visits to the United States under any pretext or in any form. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, and not send any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We solemnly warn the Lai Qingde authorities that their attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence” is a waste of effort and is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Kuomintang Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun recently met with Greene, head of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office. Greene said that the United States never seeks confrontation or conflict across the Taiwan Strait, that its current top priority is to avoid war, and that it ensures any cross-Strait differences are handled in a peaceful manner without coercion. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no external interference. “Taiwan independence” is the greatest threat to peace in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the US side to abide by the One China principle and the relevant provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues appropriately, and be cautious and prudent on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","KMT Vice Chairman Chang Jung-kung (张荣恭), during a recent visit and exchange in Kunshan, Jiangsu, said in a discussion with Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots: “Only by getting along with the mainland can we benefit the people, and only by sharing prosperity can Taiwan thrive,” and proposed the concept of “harmonizing with the mainland to revitalize Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","The greatest truths are simple. Only by upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” can there be peace across the Taiwan Strait; only with peace across the Strait can Taiwan compatriots live and work in peace and contentment. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work together with the political parties, groups and personages of all walks of life in Taiwan, including the Kuomintang, to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, advance the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and bring benefits to compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi's erroneous remarks and actions regarding Taiwan continue to cause an uproar in international public opinion. A five-language online poll by China Media Group's CGTN shows that 91.1% of respondents said Japan should reflect on its historical responsibility and fully respect China's sovereignty and territorial integrity; 88.9% condemned Japan for attempting to interfere in…","We have also seen this public opinion poll. The poll results show that history will not be forgotten, and even less can it be altered. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi openly put forward provocative remarks concerning Taiwan. She sought to interfere in the situation across the Taiwan Strait, deny the fruits of victory in the War of Resistance, and revive militarism. This tramples on international justice, challenges the postwar international order, and seriously damages China-Japan relations, and it inevitably provokes strong questioning and concern from the international community.\nIt must be reiterated that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The Japanese side should immediately stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop provocations and crossing lines, and not go further and further down the wrong path. We hope that broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will fully recognize the danger and harmfulness of the relevant Japanese conduct, join us in resolutely crushing all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, and safeguard the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251119_12736018.htm"],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Regarding the erroneous remarks and actions of Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi concerning Taiwan, Lai Ching-te falsely claimed that China is carrying out a “compound attack” on Japan, that China should not become a “troublemaker for regional peace and stability,” and should “return to the track of the rules-based international order.” The head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department said it would use…","The root cause of tensions in the Taiwan Strait lies in the DPP authorities' obstinate adherence to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and their collusion with external forces to provoke “independence” moves. As everyone has seen, many foreign media outlets, experts and scholars have recently spoken out to criticize the Lai Ching-te authorities for being reckless and rash, repeatedly provoking “independence” moves, and being “peace breakers” and “troublemakers” in the Taiwan Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that “relying on external forces to seek independence” is a futile fantasy. Any conduct of colluding with external forces to provoke “independence” will surely be met with a head-on counterattack, and anyone who forgets their ancestors and betrays the nation will be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","On the 14th, Song Tao, Director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, met in the Peace Hotel in Shanghai with a visiting delegation led by Chang Jung-kung, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China. This was the second KMT vice chairman that Director Song has met since Cheng Li-wun was elected KMT chairperson. Outside observers are paying attention to whether both sides have discussed Cheng Li-wun’s visit to…","On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang of China in all fields and at all levels, and enhance mutual trust and cooperation. Anything that is conducive to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, we are willing to actively promote.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Regarding recent erroneous remarks by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi involving Taiwan, Ma Ying-jeou, Hung Hsiu-chu, and others have posted criticisms of Takaichi, expressing “deep concern” over her reckless remarks, and holding that “cross-Strait issues cannot be left to foreign intervention and must be discussed by the two sides themselves.” What is your comment on this?","We have noted the voices of relevant figures on the island. The Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and it should and can only be resolved by Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. Sanae Takaichi openly made provocative remarks on Taiwan and brazenly interfered in China's internal affairs. We firmly oppose this and will not tolerate it. Should Japan dare to meddle in Taiwan Strait affairs, we will surely strike back head-on and thoroughly crush its aggressive designs.\nWe hope broad Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, be upright Chinese, distinguish right from wrong, act in accordance with righteousness, and, together with compatriots on the mainland, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, resolutely safeguard our shared home of the Chinese nation, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Question one: Recently it was reported that the Mainland Affairs Council did not approve the application of the Deputy Director of the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office to travel to Taiwan, which may create variables for the December “Twin Cities Forum.” Will the mainland side adjust the level of its representatives to continue applying to come to Taiwan for consultations, or will it re-evaluate? Question…","First question. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should frequently visit and get closer to one another. We support holding the “Twin Cities Forum.” The Democratic Progressive Party authorities, for the sake of their own party's political self-interest, have stubbornly adhered to their “Taiwan independence” stance and repeatedly obstructed and sabotaged cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, which is unpopular.\nSecond question. The clumsy performance of these two clowns further exposes their outward fierceness but inward weakness, their panic and fear. The net of the law is vast; the likes of Wen Ziyu and Chen Boyuan will certainly pay the price for their illegal and criminal acts.\nThird question. The mainland public security authorities' issuance of notices offering rewards for clues on the illegal and criminal activities of Wen Ziyu and Chen Boyuan is a concrete action to punish, in accordance with the law, the crime of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country. It is a just measure responding to the calls of people on both sides of the Strait to punish “Taiwan independence.” The scope of the relevant measures is very clear: they do not target, and do not involve, the broad body of Taiwan compatriots. The positive response of people on both sides of the Strait to the relevant measures reflects their deep hatred of the evil conduct of “Taiwan independence” hired thugs and accomplices. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' threats and intimidation in response seriously infringe the basic rights of Taiwan compatriots and fully expose the hypocritical nature of their claim to “freedom of speech.”\nFourth question. “Taiwan independence” is the root of turmoil that undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and harms the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. Using criminal justice measures to punish those who split the country and to safeguard core national interests is a common practice in countries around the world, and it is also a just and necessary measure to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nFifth question. I must emphasize once again that using criminal justice measures to punish those who split the country and to safeguard core national interests is a common practice in countries around the world. The “Taiwan independence” separatist forces have racked their brains to bolster their own courage, which precisely reveals their inner panic. We warn the stubborn “Taiwan independence” diehards not to harbor any illusions: the sword of punishment for “independence” hangs high, and those who plot “independence” will certainly be punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: The application by the deputy director of the Shanghai Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office to visit Taiwan was rejected, which may affect the holding of the “Twin Cities Forum.” What is the current progress? Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an responded that he hopes the “Twin Cities Forum” will not be too complicated and can proceed smoothly. What is your comment? Second question: The DPP authorities claimed…","First question. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family and should naturally visit each other often and grow closer. We support holding the “Twin Cities Forum,” and relevant parties have maintained communication all along. The DPP authorities, for the political self-interest of their party and themselves, obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” position, repeatedly obstruct and undermine cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and this does not win public support.\nSecond question. Mainland China’s artificial intelligence technology is innovating rapidly and benefiting the world. Many large language models are widely used across industries and also provide the public with personalized learning and convenient life services. Out of political self-interest in pursuing “independence,” the DPP authorities are both fearful of and resentful toward mainland high-tech products, and they readily impose restrictions in the name of safeguarding security. This will only harm the interests of Taiwan’s businesses and people, and it is resented and opposed by all sectors of the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-19","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","According to reports, the DPP authorities recently said that this week they will send a “National Defense Manual for All People” to every household in Taiwan, to increase the public’s preparedness for various emergencies, including possible military action by mainland China against Taiwan. Some DPP officials said this shows “Taiwan’s determination to self-defend” and lets people on both sides of the Strait know…","The DPP authorities stubbornly persist in the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, scheming to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence through war preparations,” continuously escalating cross-Strait confrontation and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Their deliberate fabrication of the so-called handbook, full of lies and inverting black and white in an attempt to intimidate and coerce Taiwan residents and spread fear of war, is vile in means and sinister in intent. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots will stand on the right side of history, firmly oppose Taiwan independence provoking war, and join us in jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251119_12736015.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-20","Mao Ning","Global Times","Regarding Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on hypothetical situations on Taiwan, many Chinese people believe that Japan bears historical responsibility on the Taiwan question and is least of all in a position to talk about situations concerning Taiwan. What is your comment?","In history, Japan forcibly occupied Taiwan and exerted colonial rule on the island for half a century. Under Japanese occupation, the people in Taiwan suffered enormously. Hundreds of thousands of our compatriots in Taiwan were killed, the people had no political rights, no freedom of religious belief or freedom of culture whatsoever, and Taiwan’s mineral resources and life supplies were massively plundered. The crimes and atrocities that Japanese aggressors committed in Taiwan were innumerable and they form the darkest page in the history of Taiwan.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of China’s recovery of Taiwan. Japan must never forget that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Taiwan is none of Japan’s business. If Japan creates trouble on Taiwan, Japan will not get away with it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251120_11757114.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251120_11756952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-20","Mao Ning","CCTV","It’s reported that regarding Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan, Japanese senior officials claimed that the comments do not alter the government’s existing position and that Japan does not intend to retract them. Does China accept Japan’s explanation?","I’m not sure what exactly Japan meant by “the Japanese government’s existing position.” When it comes to the Taiwan question, the position of the Japanese government is supposed to be upholding the one-China principle and abiding by the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, instead of being deliberately ambiguous, and still less turning back the wheel of history.\nEighty years ago, Chinese soldiers and civilians, including our compatriots in Taiwan, defeated the Japanese aggressors after heroic and strenuous fighting, achieved the great victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and realized Taiwan’s return to the motherland. Treaties and instruments such as the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender clearly affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. China’s recovery of Taiwan is an outcome of the WWII victory and an integral part of the postwar international order.\nIf there has truly been no change to the Japanese government’s position on the Taiwan question, the Japanese leader should not have linked it to a so-called “survival-threatening situation,” and should not have acted against China’s red line over and over while claiming that there has been no change to Japan’s position. Merely stating that the position “has not changed” does not resolve China’s concerns. Japan needs to take seriously what it has heard from China, retract the erroneous remarks, and take practical steps to honor its commitments to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251120_11757114.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251120_11756952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-20","Mao Ning","NHK","According to Reuters’ report, the ROK’s Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism is notified by the Chinese side that the China-Japan-ROK Culture Ministers’ Meeting that was scheduled for this month will be postponed. What’s your comment?","The extremely erroneous remarks made by the Japanese leader on Taiwan have hurt the sentiments of the Chinese people and posed a challenge to the postwar international order. They have disrupted the foundation and atmosphere of trilateral cooperation among China, Japan and the ROK. As a result, the conditions are not yet ready for holding the relevant meeting.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251120_11757114.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251120_11756952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-20","Mao Ning","NHK","On importing Japanese aquatic products to China, you said at yesterday’s press conference that Japan has so far been unable to provide the technical materials under its commitment. Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary said at a press conference this morning that the two sides are going through the technical matters. If Japan has the technical materials ready and provides them to China, will China consider immediately…","On the import of Japanese aquatic products to China, competent authorities of China will conduct science-based assessments and rigorous reviews in accordance with laws and regulations to ensure that relevant aquatic products meet China’s standards.\nAs we said yesterday, because of the Japanese leader’s erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan and other major issues of principle, there has been strong indignation from the Chinese people. Under current circumstances, there will be no market for Japanese aquatic products even if they enter China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251120_11757114.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251120_11756952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-20","Mao Ning","Reuters","Lai Ching-te has taken to social media today to show his support for Japan by eating sushi for lunch, as his social media account shows. Does the Ministry have any comment on this?","Whatever show the Lai Ching-te authorities put on, it does not change the fact that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan and it is an inalienable part of China’s territory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251120_11757114.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251120_11756952.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-21","Mao Ning","Reuters","There have been a number of social media posts by Chinese diplomats about the Japanese Prime Minister’s remarks on Taiwan. For example, a post made by the embassy in Manila was accompanied by a series of cartoons. Some analysts say this constitutes China relaunching its “wolf warrior diplomacy.” What does the Foreign Ministry make of this assessment?","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made blatant and erroneous remarks on Taiwan. Those remarks implied the possibility of Japan’s armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait, eroded the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and triggered outrage and condemnation from the Chinese people. China will resolutely respond should anyone trample on the red line when it comes to the Taiwan question. The international community should draw its attention to what Japan is up to and whether Japan is still committed to the path of peaceful development.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251121_11757769.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251121_11757685.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-21","Mao Ning","AFP","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said today that she wants constructive and stable ties with China and that the country’s stance on Taiwan remains unchanged. Does the Foreign Ministry have any additional comment on this? (Similar question from Kyodo News)","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made blatant and erroneous remarks on Taiwan. Those remarks implied the possibility of Japan’s armed intervention in the Taiwan Strait, triggered outrage and condemnation from the Chinese people, and eroded the political foundation of China-Japan relations. China has made clear its firm opposition.\nIf Japan truly hopes to develop the strategic relationship of mutual benefit with China and make the relationship a constructive and stable one fit for the new era, Japan needs to uphold the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries and its political commitments, retract the erroneous remarks at once, and take practical steps to honor its commitments to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251121_11757769.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251121_11757685.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-24","Mao Ning","CNR","It’s reported that regarding China’s letter to the UN Secretary-General on Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, the Japanese government spokesperson said to reporters during the G20 Summit that China’s claims that Prime Minister Takaichi has altered Japan’s position on Taiwan is “entirely baseless.” The spokesperson said Japan has repeatedly explained to the Chinese side the gist…","China has articulated its position multiple times on Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. Those remarks seriously violate the principles laid down in the four political documents between China and Japan, and has fundamentally eroded the political foundation of China-Japan relations.\nWe’ve noted the Japanese side’s reference to Japan’s “consistent position” on the Taiwan question. But what exactly do they mean by this so-called “consistent position?” Can Japan articulate this “consistent position” in its entirety to the public? If Japan merely keeps repeating that its position has not changed without specifying what that position is and meanwhile keeps crossing the line, then this kind of repetition means nothing but empty words, and simply fudges and hollows out the one-China position.\nThe one-China principle is an unshakable prevailing consensus in the international community. If there has truly been no change to the Japanese government’s position on the Taiwan question, Japan should unequivocally uphold the one-China principle, and abide by the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries and honor the commitments Japan has made, including what has been stated in the 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement that “the Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China,” and “the Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” Why can’t Japan fully and accurately reiterate this position?\nChina urges the Japanese side to take seriously what it has heard from China, do serious soul-searching and correct its wrongdoing, act to honor its commitment to China, and stop pursuing its misguided course, still less say one thing but do another.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251124_11758891.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251124_11758881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-24","Mao Ning","Reuters","I want to ask about the comments by the Japanese defense minister over the weekend who said about the deployment of the missile unit to the Yonaguni Island. He said that medium-range surface-to-air missile units were planned to deploy in Yonaguni to protect the island’s safety. “We believe that having this unit in place will actually lower the chances of an armed attack against our country, so I don’t agree with…","Japan’s deployment of offensive weapons in Southwest Islands close to China’s Taiwan region is a deliberate move that breeds regional tensions and stokes military confrontation. Given Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, this move is extremely dangerous and should put Japan’s neighboring countries and the international community on high alert.\nThe Potsdam Proclamation explicitly stipulates that Japan shall not be permitted to “re-arm for war.” The Japanese Constitution, which enshrines pacifism, also established Japan’s exclusively defense-oriented policy. It is alarming, however, that in recent years, Japan has drastically readjusted its security policy, increased defense budget year after year, relaxed restrictions on arms export, sought to develop offensive weapons, and planned to abandon its three non-nuclear principles. Japan’s right-wing provocateurs are trying every means to break free from the pacifist constitution, going further down the path of military buildup and leading Japan and the region to disastrous outcomes.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the recovery of Taiwan. China will never allow Japan’s right-wing provocateurs to turn back the wheel of history, never allow external forces to lay their hands on China’s Taiwan region, and never allow the resurgence of Japan’s militarism. China is resolved in and capable of defending national and territorial sovereignty.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251124_11758891.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251124_11758881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-24","Mao Ning","NHK","Japan’s Prime Minister Takaichi said after G20 Summit that she didn’t have the chance to talk to Premier Li Qiang, and she also commented that Japan remains open to various dialogue with China. Could you tell us your comment on this?","Japan should take China’s concerns seriously, retract the erroneous remarks on Taiwan, and show Japan’s sincerity for dialogue with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251124_11758891.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251124_11758881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-24","Mao Ning","NHK","Some Japanese media reported yesterday that China has rejected Japan’s proposal to hold a trilateral meeting with South Korea and Japan in January. Can the Foreign Ministry give us any comment on this?","China, Japan and the ROK have not agreed on a date for the tenth trilateral summit meeting. The Japanese leader’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have damaged the foundation and atmosphere for China-Japan-ROK cooperation. Conditions are not right at the moment for a trilateral summit meeting.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251124_11758891.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251124_11758881.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-25","Mao Ning","Global Times","Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan is met by outrage from the Chinese people. There are, however, individuals in Japan who claimed that it’s the Republic of China (ROC) rather than the People’s Republic of China (PRC) who accepted Japan’s surrender, so the PRC is not in a position to discuss the Taiwan question. What’s your comment?","The ones who make such claims either do not know the history or deliberately seek to distort it and disregard international law.\nIn 1945, Japan signed the Instrument of Surrender, explicitly undertook to carry out the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation in good faith and unconditionally return Taiwan to China. China resumed exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan and recovered Taiwan both in law and in practice. In 1949, the PRC government replaced the ROC government. This is a change of government in which China, as a subject under international law, did not change and China’s sovereignty and inherent territorial boundaries stayed unchanged. Thus, the government of the People’s Republic of China naturally and fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over the Taiwan region. The 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement states that the Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an ironclad fact and shall not be bent or distorted.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251125_11759947.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251125_11759683.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-25","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Just after the phone call between President Xi and President Trump, there was a phone call between President Trump and Prime Minister Takaichi of Japan. And they discussed the Japan-U.S. alliance and its importance for the region and other bilateral issues, some of which weren’t announced. Does China have a reaction to that phone call? And do you have any concern about Japan and the U.S. and their views toward…","The phone call between the leaders of the U.S. and Japan is a matter between the U.S. and Japan. I have no comment on that. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair which brooks no interference by any external forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251125_11759947.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251125_11759683.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-25","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Since the relations between Japan and China got worse over the last two weeks, Chinese authorities have frozen its regulatory reviews of Japanese movies for airing in Chinese movie theaters and more than 20 concerts featuring Japanese musicians have been canceled across Chinese cities including in Beijing. Is this part of the Chinese government’s retaliatory response to Japan? Is there an official directive or…","Exchanges and cooperation between China and Japan have recently been affected because of the erroneous remarks made by the Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan. The remarks gravely hurt the sentiments of the Chinese people and poisoned the atmosphere for exchanges between the two countries. Japan needs to redress its wrongdoing at once and stop creating irritations on China-related issues.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251125_11759947.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251125_11759683.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-26","Mao Ning","People’s Daily","On November 25, on whether Japan’s policy regarding existential threats remains unchanged, the Japanese government adopted a statement at a cabinet meeting saying that Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks at the parliamentary committee meeting does not change Japan’s consistent position. The statement stressed that the determination will be made by considering all available information based on the specific…","On Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, China has stated its serious position more than once. Those remarks seriously violate the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, erode the political foundation of China-Japan relations, and challenge the post-war international order. China has made clear its firm opposition. The remarks have been questioned and criticized by visionary people inside Japan, and met with condemnation from the international community.\nThe Japanese government’s November 25 statement continues to repeat that its position on Taiwan is either “consistent” or “unchanged”. That is hardly adequate. What China and the international community want are answers to these questions: What exactly does the Japanese side mean by what they call “consistent position”? Does the Japanese side still follow the one-China principle? The Japanese side should honestly, accurately and fully articulate what that “consistent position” is. Soft-pedaling the issue, putting out unspecified notions without touching on the essence of the issue, and hoping that somehow the issue would resolve itself—such kind of approach will certainly not go anywhere.\nNot only that, the Japanese side, instead of turning back from the wrong course, again made irresponsible remarks in the statement regarding the Taiwan question and interfered in China’s internal affairs. Let me stress that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. How to resolve the Taiwan question and realize national reunification is purely China’s own affair and not for Japan to point fingers or even meddle in it. China once again urges the Japanese side to take seriously what it has heard from China, reflect on and correct its wrongdoing, retract the erroneous remarks without delay, and take practical steps to honor its commitments to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251126_11760672.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251126_11760587.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-26","Mao Ning","AFP","The U.S. top envoy in Taiwan Raymond Greene said today that he welcomes a US$40 billion military spending plan announced today by Taiwan. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on these remarks by Raymond Greene or on Taiwan’s new military spending plan?","China opposes official interactions and military ties between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region. This position is consistent. The DPP authorities will not succeed in resisting reunification and seeking “independence” through military buildup.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251126_11760672.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251126_11760587.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Peng Qing’en answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporters, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","人民日报记者","On November 24, President Xi Jinping held a phone call with US President Trump, stressing that Taiwan's return to China is an important part of the post-war international order. China and the United States once fought side by side against fascism and militarism, and at present they should jointly uphold the fruits of victory of World War II even more. What is your interpretation?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. In his call with the US President, President Xi Jinping set out China's principled position on the Taiwan question and stressed that both countries should jointly uphold the fruits of victory in World War II. President Xi's important remarks carry significant guiding importance for our work on Taiwan affairs.\nWe will unite compatriots on both sides of the Strait to remember history together, defend hard-won achievements, cherish peace, and create the future. We will firmly oppose separatist acts for “Taiwan independence,” work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, protect our common home of the Chinese nation, and create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737227.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","《参考消息》记者","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi's erroneous remarks involving Taiwan have sparked continuing protests from all sectors on the island, yet Lai Ching-te has expressed support for Takaichi and defended her, and has even posted on social media a photo of himself eating Japanese food, saying it \"fully demonstrates the solid friendship between Taiwan and Japan.\" What is your comment on this?","Takaichi Sanae’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan crudely interfere in China’s internal affairs, seriously violate international law and the basic norms of international relations, seriously undermine the post-war international order, seriously violate the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and seriously hurt the feelings of the Chinese people. Japan should immediately reflect, correct its mistake, and retract its erroneous remarks on Taiwan.\nLai Qingde eats the rice of currying favor with Japan and does the dirty business of selling out Taiwan. His words and deeds are nauseating and once again let the world see his ugly face of forgetting his ancestors and betraying the nation. We solemnly warn the Lai Qingde authorities: any conduct that relies on external forces will surely bring humiliation upon itself, and any traitor to the nation will surely face righteous judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737224.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中国日报记者","China recently announced the suspension of imports of Japanese aquatic products. The DPP authorities, in order to “show support for Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi,” announced the full lifting of import restrictions on Japanese food, which has drawn widespread questioning on the island. What is your comment on this?","We have noted the relevant reports, and we have also noted the strong questioning from island residents over the DPP authorities’ disregard for public opinion in comprehensively lifting the ban on related Japanese products. For their own selfish interests, the DPP authorities have disregarded the health of the public, fully exposing their “Taiwan independence” essence and their ugly, unprincipled sycophancy toward Japan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","福建厦门卫视记者","Reports indicate that construction of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Xiamen section) is progressing smoothly. Recently, a first Kinmen delegation visited the construction trestle up close to personally experience the project's development. Could you please provide more information?","Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is the common call and urgent wish of the people of Xiamen and Kinmen. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” issued in 2023, clearly proposed to “explore a model of joint infrastructure construction between Xiamen and Kinmen, and accelerate the connection of electricity, gas and bridges with Kinmen.” Among these, the Xiamen section of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge project began construction in October 2023, and its cross-sea section adopts a segmented design with two-way four to eight lanes. The Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Dadeng Island to Kinmen section) is about 4.5 kilometers long and is planned to be built to expressway standards with two-way six lanes and a design speed of 100 kilometers per hour. On November 15, more than 40 Kinmen compatriots visited the Xiamen section of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge project under construction for the first time, witnessing with their own eyes this cross-sea project, which carries the beautiful vision of both places, advancing steadily. They each expressed a strong hope for the bridge to open to traffic as early as possible.\nOnce the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is fully open to traffic, it will bring convenience to travel between the two places, add impetus to Kinmen's economic development and the improvement of people's livelihoods, and Xiamen and Kinmen will become a closer “same-city living circle.” In addition, after the bridge is completed, water, electricity and gas can be sent to Kinmen through pipelines in the bridge body, improving Kinmen's development environment. It will also complement the navigation of the maritime “Mini Three Links,” adding passage routes between Xiamen and Kinmen. The DPP authorities should face squarely the interests and demands of Kinmen townsfolk, stop political calculations, sincerely work for the people's benefit, and support the early completion and opening to traffic of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737221.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","香港中评社记者","On November 17, more than 30 groups, including the Taiwan Labor Party, the Taiwan Social Harmony Forum Preparatory Committee, and the Cross-Strait Peaceful Development Forum, jointly issued a statement solemnly protesting Sanae Takaichi's wrong remarks involving Taiwan. They stated that the Taiwanese people refuse to be sacrificed to Japanese militarism, and demanded that Sanae Takaichi immediately withdraw her…","Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and no external force has the right to interfere. Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae openly issued provocative remarks on the Taiwan question, crossing an untouchable bottom line and red line, and sparking strong outrage among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Broad Taiwan compatriots are solemnly protesting this and demanding that Takaichi Sanae immediately retract her remarks and make a public apology. This is a just cause.\nJapan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. After the First Sino-Japanese War, Japan forcibly occupied Taiwan and carried out a colonial rule lasting 50 years. The crimes Japan committed in Taiwan are beyond counting. History does not permit reversal, achievements must be defended, and justice must be upheld. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must uphold national righteousness, resolutely oppose all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference. Any external force that dares to provoke will surely bring about its own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","大象新闻记者","Reports indicate that in July this year, two Taiwan compatriots were seriously injured by five Japanese men while walking on a street in Tokyo. Japanese police recently stated that they have arrested the attackers involved. What is your comment on this?","This year, public security in Japan has been unsettled, with multiple incidents of tourists, including Taiwan compatriots, being attacked. Recently, the Japanese Prime Minister publicly made blatantly provocative remarks concerning Taiwan, seriously worsening the atmosphere of people-to-people exchanges. Extreme anti-China and anti-Chinese acts by right-wing elements in Japanese society have increased, posing major risks to the personal and life safety of tourists. Taiwan compatriots are our flesh and blood. We strongly condemn such violent acts, and the Japanese side should punish the perpetrators severely as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","新华社记者","A Taiwanese polling organization recently released its November public opinion survey, showing that 50.2% of the public disapproves of Lai Ching-te's performance, and that the past five months have been his “most resented period.” In an online vote, as many as 80.4% of people consider Lai the “most disappointing leader,” and his support rate on “making cross-Strait relations most peaceful” is only 0.5%. What is…","The people have a scale in their hearts. Since the Lai Ching-te authorities took office, they have violated mainstream public opinion on the island, refused to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” stubbornly adhered to the “Taiwan independence” position, loudly promoted separatist fallacies, continuously manipulated “anti-China and resist-China” rhetoric, escalated the creation of “green terror,” and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. They have disregarded economic laws, schemed to “decouple” cross-Strait trade and economy and “sever” industrial chains, harming the interests and well-being of enterprises and people on the island. They have currying favor with and pledging loyalty to external forces, selling out Taiwan and harming Taiwan, and attempting to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence.” Their actions have heightened cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, leading to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. They run counter to the wishes of the Taiwanese people, and therefore they lack popular support and public anger is boiling over.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737225.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台《海峡两岸》记者","KMT Chairperson Zheng Liwen recently said that only by accepting One China can Taiwan's survival be ensured. She also questioned the DPP: “If Taiwan can have the freedom to advocate ‘Taiwan independence,’ why can't it have the freedom to advocate unification?” Some public opinion holds that Zheng Liwen insists on the position that both sides belong to One China more firmly than past KMT senior officials. What is…","There is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is an immutable historical and legal fact. Adhering to the one-China principle allows cross-Strait relations to improve and develop and keeps the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable. Deviating from the one-China principle and denying the “1992 Consensus” will plunge the situation in the Taiwan Strait into tension and turmoil and will seriously harm the interests and well-being of the Taiwan public. “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. For their own selfish gain in pursuing “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities keep suppressing dissenters, muzzling speech, creating a “green terror,” and persecuting organizations and individuals who advocate improving cross-Strait relations. This seriously deviates from the hearts and minds of the people on the island. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly advance the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737226.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities.","Recently, there have been many economic, trade, and cultural exchange activities. In terms of economic and trade exchanges, from November 19 to 22, the 2025 Shantou-Taiwan Industrial and Commercial Cooperation and Development Conference was held in Shantou, Guangdong Province. More than 400 industrial and commercial figures and youth representatives from both sides of the Taiwan Strait gathered in Shantou, and through activities such as collaborative innovation matchmaking for distinctive industries, they discussed new opportunities for cooperation and drew a new vision for development together. From November 22 to 25, the Second Cross-Strait (Qingdao) Youth Exchange and Development Conference was held in Qingdao, Shandong Province, with a total of more than 360 cross-Strait youths and entrepreneurs participating. From November 23 to 25, the 7th World Chinese Entrepreneurs Convention was held in Meizhou, Guangdong Province, with approximately 850 participants, including principal leaders of major overseas and domestic associations and chambers of commerce, prominent overseas Chinese leaders, and well-known business people.\nIn terms of cultural and film and television exchanges, on November 12, the award ceremony of the 8th China Design Award, themed “Smart Creation, Future Design, Symbiotic Coexistence,” was held in Ningbo, Zhejiang. Representatives of award winners from the Taiwan Strait regions and Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, experts and scholars, and corporate representatives, more than 400 guests in total, gathered in Ningbo to appreciate design innovation achievements and explore new paths for the development of Chinese design. On November 13, the award ceremony of the 3rd Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival and the “Seeing Jimei” Youth Film Festival was held in Jimei District, Xiamen. More than 400 film and television experts, university faculty and students, and young filmmakers from both sides of the Strait gathered to share a date with light and shadow. From November 16 to 19, the “Chaochuang Donghai · Xiangju Liangan — 2025 Cross-Strait Beautiful Countryside Sustainable Development Seminar” was successfully held in Ningbo, Zhejiang. About 140 cross-Strait experts and scholars, leading business figures, and entrepreneurial youth participated, exchanging views on topics such as universities empowering rural areas, the application of digital technology, and upgrading of agricultural industry chains, and contributing wisdom and suggestions for rural revitalization on both sides of the Strait. From November 22 to 26, the Taiwan Youth Film, Television, and Cultural Talent Exchange Camp was held in Beijing. Dozens of cross-Strait professionals in film, television, and culture, including directors, screenwriters, actors, and cinematographers, gathered to discuss opportunities for cross-Strait film and television cooperation and prospects for industrial integration. From November 28 to December 3, the Taipei exhibition of the 16th Cross-Strait Children’s Art Exhibition will open at the Taiwan Art Education Center, displaying nearly 300 outstanding works by young people from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong, Macao, and Chinese communities in Malaysia, offering audiences an artistic feast full of childlike charm and deep thought.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","香港凤凰卫视记者","KMT Vice Chairman Hsiao Hsu-tsen said in a recent interview that cross-Strait dialogue and exchanges accord with mainstream public opinion, that the KMT’s line remains unchanged, and that on the basis of “one China, separate areas” and the authentic “1992 Consensus,” it pursues cross-Strait dialogue, reconciliation and maintaining communication. What comment do you have?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The core meaning of the “1992 Consensus” is that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China and jointly strive to seek national reunification. Historical facts fully prove that by upholding the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, cross-Strait dialogue and consultation can be resumed, cross-Strait relations can be improved and developed, and the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides can be safeguarded and enhanced. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and all sectors of society, including the Kuomintang, to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and bring benefits to compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, Taiwan's education authorities required students to register online before traveling to the mainland, to conduct a self-review within one month after the activity ends, and to report an overview of their itinerary. Public opinion on the island criticized the DPP authorities for restricting cross-Strait exchanges and vigorously carrying out a “green terror.” What comments do you have on this?","This move is yet another trick by the DPP authorities to obstruct exchanges between young students across the Strait. It once again exposes their stubborn scheming for “independence,” their provocations, their deliberate and sinister intent to escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and their fear of cross-Strait youth drawing closer, which is fierce in appearance but timid inside.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. The DPP authorities have escalated their obstruction and restriction of cross-Strait exchanges in all fields. This runs counter to the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society and to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: public opinion cannot be reversed, popular sentiment cannot be defied, and those who do wrong will bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中新社记者","Deng Wanhua, a mainland-born spouse who previously served as village chief of Hualien, was dismissed over the issue of “Chinese nationality.” The Hualien County Government Appeals Committee recently resolved to revoke the original decision. The DPP authorities said that under the “Nationality Act,” mainland-born spouses who hold elected public office must renounce the nationality of the People's Republic of…","There is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are Chinese. It is the legitimate right of mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan to participate in local social governance and serve local residents. The DPP authorities, out of their “Taiwan independence” nature, openly peddle the “two-state theory,” arbitrarily deprive mainland spouses of their lawful rights and interests, suppress and bully the mainland spouse community, and repeatedly challenge the historical and legal fact that the two sides of the Strait belong to one China. We strongly condemn this. We warn the DPP authorities that any vicious acts and tricks that undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait or harm the interests of compatriots on both sides will surely backfire on them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737222.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Please introduce the results achieved by the 5th “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar.”","On November 20 and 21, the Fifth “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” was successfully held in Chengdu, Sichuan, with more than 200 people attending, including representatives of unification-supporting figures from the island, among them leaders of 28 Taiwan patriotic unification groups, as well as relevant parties from both sides of the Strait, experts and scholars, and guests from Hong Kong and Macao.\nWang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, sent a congratulatory letter to the event, extending congratulations on its convening and greetings to attendees from both sides of the Strait and from Hong Kong and Macao. He pointed out that General Secretary Xi Jinping solemnly declared at the rally marking the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War that the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable, and that victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan are the great victory and great glory of the Chinese nation, profoundly demonstrating that a strong and unified country is the great principle on which the destiny of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, depends. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the opening ceremony, read out Comrade Wang Huning's congratulatory letter, and delivered remarks. Wang Xiaohui, Secretary of the Sichuan Provincial Committee of the Communist Party of China and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Sichuan Provincial People's Congress, said that Sichuan will actively promote exchanges and cooperation between Sichuan and Taiwan in all fields.\nDuring the event, around the theme of “Remembering History, Defending Achievements, Safeguarding Our Homeland, Creating the Future,” attendees conducted in-depth exchanges and discussions from three aspects: “Taiwan compatriots' anti-Japanese struggle and the restoration of Taiwan,” “historical facts of the restoration and Taiwan's status,” and “the prospects of rejuvenation and national identity,” and reached five important consensuses, including: remembering the history of the War of Resistance and carrying forward the patriotic tradition; defending the fruits of the War of Resistance and upholding one China; safeguarding our common homeland and opposing separatism and interference; gathering the strength of compatriots and shouldering historical responsibility; and advancing the process of unification and jointly planning the great cause of rejuvenation. These consensuses fully express the strong desire of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly remember the history of the restoration and to carry forward patriotism and the great national spirit, and they voice the righteous determination of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to resolutely defend the fruits of victory in World War II and firmly safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","南方日报 南方+记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Minister of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that the Straits Exchange Foundation once considered opening an account on the mainland's Weibo platform, but gave up because the application requires selecting \"Taiwan, China,\" which he described as \"self-demeaning,\" and because speech would also be subject to official control. What is your comment on this?","The Mainland Affairs Council and the Straits Exchange Foundation of Taiwan were born under a “one China” framework in response to exchanges between the people on both sides of the Strait. The MAC’s primary responsibilities and core business should be to promote cross-Strait consultation and dialogue and to facilitate cross-Strait exchanges. Instead, it has become the vanguard in inciting cross-Strait confrontation and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. The mainland’s internet is open and managed in accordance with the law. The MAC’s malicious hyping of the Weibo account issue is nothing more than an attempt to attack and smear the mainland and to deceive Taiwan residents. This trick has no novelty. The MAC and the SEF should return to their proper duties and do more things that advance cross-Strait exchanges and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","福建东南卫视记者","Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae's provocative remarks on Taiwan have triggered criticism from all sectors of the island, yet Lin Jialong, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, publicly supported Takaichi and asked Taiwan residents to travel to Japan more and buy Japanese products to show support. He also said, “The CPC's military expansion targets Taiwan and all the countries of the First Island…","At present, Japan is attempting to stir up trouble using Taiwan, and the DPP authorities are attempting to collude with external forces to create trouble. They are, without any qualification, destroyers of peace in the Taiwan Strait and makers of trouble. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. If any external force dares to interfere in Taiwan Strait affairs, we will certainly strike back head-on. For political self-interest, the DPP authorities are servile and fawning toward external forces. They are rehashing the “first island chain” concept, which is full of Cold War mentality, and deliberately escalating confrontation between the two sides of the Strait. This will only plunge Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war and peril.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Outsiders cannot be relied upon, and unification cannot be stopped. The DPP authorities' attempt to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” is doomed to fail. We have firm will, strong determination, and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and external interference, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251126_12737223.htm"],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Die-hard 'Taiwan independence' element Shen Boyang recently went to the Netherlands and continued to claim a so-called 'counterattack against China's wanted notice'. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Shen Boyang and the DPP authorities are fierce in appearance but timid inside. Colluding with some anti-China forces to stage a self-hyped farce only exposes their guilt and fear as the sword of punishing “Taiwan independence” is drawn. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and the legal net for punishing “Taiwan independence” will only tighten. We will severely crack down on the illegal and criminal activities of “Taiwan independence” elements who split the country and incite secession, and hold them accountable for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","人民政协报记者","According to reports, a bipartisan group of U.S. senators recently proposed a bill advocating writing the “Six Assurances” to Taiwan into law and strengthening congressional oversight, to prevent the U.S. government from deviating from its commitments to Taiwan without congressional review. What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose the negative actions concerning Taiwan by certain US politicians. The so-called “Six Assurances” of the United States seriously violate the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and seriously violate the basic norms of international relations. They are entirely wrong, illegal and null and void. We made our opposition clear long ago.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently claimed that the mainland is intensifying “infiltration” of Taiwan through six major methods, including “coerced leaking of secrets, infiltration of grassroots organizations, infiltration of political parties, technology leakage, interference in elections, and gray-zone harassment,” with infiltration targets reaching local government, political parties, military personnel,…","The relevant remarks are completely baseless fabrications and slander, and are a routine trick used by the DPP authorities to manipulate “resisting China and protecting Taiwan” and seek political gain. The DPP authorities stubbornly persist in a separatist “Taiwan independence” position, constantly incite cross-strait confrontation, continuously exaggerate so-called mainland “threats,” and readily label normal cross-strait exchanges and interactions as “infiltration,” intending to use this to suppress political rivals and intimidate Taiwan residents. This not only exposes their true face of conducting “green terror” and “Taiwan independence authoritarianism,” but also reveals their guilty and timid fear of cross-strait compatriots getting closer and becoming relatives. Such retrograde actions will certainly meet firm opposition from compatriots on both sides of the Strait and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”记者","Recently, Japan announced the deployment of missiles in a sensitive area only 110 kilometers from Taiwan, continuously intensifying regional tensions. What comments do you have?","Japan’s deployment of offensive weapons in areas close to Taiwan deliberately creates regional tension and provokes military confrontation. This trend is extremely dangerous. The Potsdam Proclamation explicitly stipulates that Japan shall be “prohibited from rearmament,” and Japan’s “Peace Constitution” also establishes the principle of “exclusively defense-oriented policy.” But what the world must be wary of is that Japanese right-wing forces are trying hard to break through the constraints of the “Peace Constitution,” going further and further down the path of militarism and leading Japan and the region toward disaster.\nTaiwan is China’s Taiwan. We will never allow external forces to meddle in the Taiwan region of China, and we will never allow Japanese militarism to rise from the dead. We have the firm will, strong resolve, and great capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to crush all external interference.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","香港经济导报记者","The British magazine The Economist recently published an article pointing out that Taiwan has contracted “Taiwan disease.” Although Taiwan’s high-tech industry is well developed, the continuous shrinkage of its traditional industries and the ever-widening wealth gap are undeniable facts. The DPP authorities have neither the intention nor the ability to improve the situation, and only keep pushing to “decouple and…","At present, the imbalance in Taiwan's economic development has intensified and uncertainty has risen. The high-tech industry is suffering talent loss due to technology coercion by the United States and other Western countries, and traditional industries are struggling under the “double squeeze” of tariffs and exchange rates. The wealth gap continues to widen.\nThe DPP authorities, out of self-serving interest in pursuing “independence,” have neither the intention nor the capacity to improve the island's livelihood. Instead, they fawn on foreign powers without principle and sell out Taiwan without limit, violating the laws of the market economy and plotting to “decouple” cross-Strait economic and trade relations and “cut off” industrial chains. What they sever is the lifeline of Taiwan's small and medium-sized enterprises, and what they destroy is the prospect of Taiwan's economic development. They harm the present and leave harm for future generations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台“看台海”记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan recently said that long-term public opinion polls show that more than 80% of Taiwan residents do not support 'one country, two systems'. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. It is the best way to achieve national reunification and is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to the Chinese nation. At present, more and more far-sighted people on the island have come to recognize the benefits of “one country, two systems.” Through various means, they are offering suggestions and plans for a “two systems” Taiwan scheme, contributing wisdom and strength to achieving national reunification.\nDriven by its nature of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities maliciously attack and smear “one country, two systems,” which is pure distortion of right and wrong. The fact is that the practice of “one country, two systems” has achieved universally recognized success in Hong Kong and Macao. Since their return to the motherland, Hong Kong has steadily held its position as an international financial center, ranking third in the world. Its world competitiveness has risen to third globally, and its inflow of foreign direct investment ranks third in the world. This fully demonstrates the remarkable institutional advantages and strong vitality of “one country, two systems.”\nMany Taiwan residents are now discussing reunification, discussing the specific content of a “one country, two systems” Taiwan scheme, and imagining what Taiwan will look like after reunification. One thing can be said with great certainty: the specific form in which “one country, two systems” is realized in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan's actual conditions, will fully absorb opinions and suggestions from all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and will fully attend to the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. We believe that as compatriots on both sides work together to achieve peaceful reunification, the scope and substance of the “two systems” Taiwan scheme will be fully revealed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Regarding recent media reports that Japan spent 13.1 billion yen to cultivate pro-Japanese figures in Taiwan, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, said that Japan and Taiwan share similar ideas and have common interests. What comments do you have on this?","Relevant remarks once again expose the ugly face of the Lai Ching-te authorities, who, for the sake of party self-interest, betray the nation and “cater to Japan and sell out Taiwan” without principle or bottom line. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “catering to Japan to plot independence” leads only to a dead end. No matter how they collude with external forces or stir up trouble, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the trend that China will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, the US-China Economic and Security Review Commission suggested in its annual report that Taiwan fund the Philippines’ upgrade of its military bases. Media reports revealed that the United States demanded Taiwan pay between 350 billion and 550 billion US dollars to upgrade Philippine military bases, which was mocked as “treating Taiwan as an ATM.” What is your comment?","These remarks once again show that in the eyes of Americans, Taiwan's true value lies in being “fat meat” and an “ATM,” a pawn to contain the mainland and a tool to serve the United States. The DPP authorities are incapable of safeguarding the legitimate interests of the Taiwan people. Instead, they extravagantly squander the hard-earned money of the island's people and eagerly submit and curry favor with the United States. The outcome will inevitably be that they are discarded once used.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","台湾“中视”新闻记者","It is reported that the head of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office liaison office recently arrived in Taiwan to discuss the preparatory work for the “Twin City Forum.” Lin Yi-hua, Deputy Mayor of Taipei, said that both sides are coordinating and that it is expected to be held in late December. Does the TAO think there will again be a situation of “rushing to hold it, rather than postponing it to hold it well”?…","Shanghai and Taipei have maintained communication about holding this year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum. We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including exchanges between cities on both sides of the Strait, and we hope that through more interaction and exchange, we can continuously increase the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides and deepen heart-to-heart connection between them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","台湾TVBS记者","Lai Ching-te recently published an article in the US newspaper The Washington Post claiming that “in response to the constant military threat from the CCP against Taiwan, the defense budget must be raised by US$40 billion,” and this morning convened a high-level meeting on the “Defending Democracy and Taiwan National Security Action Plan.” What is your comment?","For its own selfish interests, the DPP authorities have let external forces take whatever they want, wasting money that could have been used to improve people’s livelihoods and develop the economy on buying weapons and pleasing external forces. This will only push Taiwan into disaster. The trend toward reunification cannot be stopped; “relying on the United States to seek independence” is doomed to fail, and “seeking independence by force” will surely lead to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently said in an interview that if the Kuomintang cannot play a role in turning the tide, Taiwan may not live to see a \"peaceful election\" in 2028. How does the spokesperson view Cheng Li-wun's concern?","The root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable, and run counter to the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. We hope compatriots on both sides will uphold the great righteousness of the nation and follow the trend of history. We hope they will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-11-26","Peng Qing'en","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The deputy director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office recently applied to visit Taiwan and was rejected by the Mainland Affairs Council. A relevant person on the Taiwan side stated, “The mainland has issued judicial documents to punish ‘Taiwan independence’ and carries out ‘cross-border repression’ against Taiwan residents. It shows no goodwill at all and is even full of hostility. Directors…","First question. The law enforcement and judicial measures we have taken are concrete actions to punish, in accordance with the law, the crimes of splitting the country and inciting to split the country. They are a righteous response to the call of people on both sides of the Strait to punish “Taiwan independence.” The Democratic Progressive Party authorities deliberately linked this with their wrong policies that obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, confusing right and wrong, with malicious intent to find excuses for their evil acts that undermine cross-Strait relations. This will not fool Taiwan residents.\nSecond question. As long as the Shanghai Municipality and the Taipei City government can reach a consensus, we would be glad to see it.\nNow I will announce the winners of the sixth issue of the “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz.”\nOn November 10, the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account published the questions for the sixth issue of the “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz” event, and netizens enthusiastically participated in answering. As of November 24, the top ten netizens who answered correctly and ranked highest in likes on their comments are, in order: “我爱看台海,” “厚积薄发,” “伟祥,” “启明,” “紫薇,” “缘分的天空,” “福建小李,” “知言,” “归舟,” and “思贤.” We extend our congratulations to these ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite souvenir, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope everyone will continue to care about Taiwan work, actively participate, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn December 8, the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” WeChat official account will publish the questions for the seventh issue of the “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz” event. Stay tuned!\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202511/t20251126_12737229.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-27","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","Prime Minister Takaichi said yesterday at the debate with opposition party leaders that “having renounced all rights and claims under the Treaty of San Francisco, we are not in a position to recognize Taiwan’s legal status.” Does China accept that statement?","China’s recovery of Taiwan is a victorious outcome of WWII and an integral part of the postwar international order. A series of instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, have all affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. The question regarding the status of Taiwan was already resolved once and for all when the Chinese people won the victory of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression in 1945. On October 1, 1949, the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) was established and has since been the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is a change of government in which China, as a subject under international law, did not change and China’s sovereignty and inherent territorial boundaries stayed unchanged. Thus, the government of the PRC naturally and fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over the Taiwan region. The 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement states that “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.”\nThe so-called “Treaty of San Francisco” was issued with the exclusion of important parties to the WWII, such as the PRC and the Soviet Union, in order to seek a separate peace deal with Japan. The document goes against the provision that each government pledges not to make a separate armistice or peace with the enemies in the Declaration by United Nations signed by 26 countries in 1942, including China, the U.S., the UK and the Soviet Union and violates the UN Charter and the basic principles of international law. Anything set out in the treaty, including on the sovereignty over Taiwan or the handling of the territory and sovereign rights of China as a non-signatory, is thus entirely illegal and null and void.\nPrime Minister Takaichi deliberately chose not to mention the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation—two international legal documents with full effect and underscored in the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement, the Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, and other bilateral treaties and she singularly brought up the illegal and invalid “Treaty of San Francisco.” That once again shows that the prime minister remains unwilling to own up to the wrongdoing and turn back from the erroneous course, and continues to damage the political foundation of China-Japan relations established under the spirit of the four political documents between the two countries, showing no regard for the authority of the UN and openly challenging the postwar international order and basic norms in international law, and even seeks to play up the so-called notion that Taiwan’s status is undetermined. That just compounds the wrongdoing. China firmly rejects that and calls for utmost vigilance from the international community. We once again urge the Japanese side to reflect on and correct its wrongdoing, retract the erroneous remarks, and take practical steps to honor its commitments to China and do what is least expected of Japan as a UN member state.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251127_11761822.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251127_11761781.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-27","Guo Jiakun","NHK","Reports suggest that U.S. President Trump asked Japan’s Prime Minister Takaichi to lower the volume on Taiwan. Can you confirm if this was influenced by his earlier conversation with President Xi?","The phone call between the leaders of the U.S. and Japan is a matter between the U.S. and Japan. I have no comment on that. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair which brooks no interference by any external forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251127_11761822.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251127_11761781.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, the Chinese and US militaries held the second working group meeting and the annual session of the Maritime Military Communication Agreement (MMCA) from November 18 to 20 in Hawaii. How does the Chinese side evaluate the current China-US military-to-military relationship? Are there any other planned exchanges between the two sides in the near future? Secondly, the Japanese side…","On your first question, representatives from the Chinese and US militaries held the second working group meeting and the annual session of the Maritime Military Communication Agreement (MMCA) in Hawaii from November 18 to 20. The meetings were held to implement the consensus between the Chinese Defense Minister and the US Secretary of War on strengthening communication and exchanges between troops on the ground to avoid misunderstanding and miscalculation, manage risks and crises, and add positive factors to building a stable and positive mil-mil relationship featuring equality, mutual respect, and peaceful coexistence. As for exchanges in the near future, the two sides maintain contact at the working level. We will release information in due course.\nAs for your second question, the Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China. How to solve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, and has nothing to do with Japan. This year marks the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration. Instead of repenting for its war crimes of invading and colonizing Taiwan, Japan is taking an extremely wrong approach by suggesting military intervention into a so-called Taiwan contingency. This dangerous approach will uproot the post-WWII international order, and lead Japan to repeat the mistakes of its militarist past. The PLA has strong capabilities and reliable means to defeat any aggressors. Should the Japanese side dare to cross the red line and invite troubles to itself, it is destined to pay a heavy price.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/11/27/11430434.shtml",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The PLA started military operations in the waters of the northern Yellow Sea near the Bohai Strait on November 23 and the operations will run through until December 7. Are these exercises intended to warn Japan? Recently, the Chinese military sent messages through multiple channels about its readiness to fight and win at any time. Given that the Japanese side rejected to retract relevant remarks, will the PLA…","The root cause for deteriorating relations between China and Japan lies in that Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi blatantly made erroneous remarks relating to Taiwan. Since Japan's surrender in 1945, it was the first time for a Japanese leader to publicly clamor for something like \"what's happening in Taiwan is directly linked to Japan\" and relate it to the right of collective self-defense. Such claims revealed for the first time Japan's intent to have armed intervention in the Taiwan question. It was also the first-ever threat using force against China made by Japan. Relevant remarks, which blatantly challenge China's core interests, are extremely wrong, dangerous and egregious. It is the Chinese military's sacred duty to safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity. We will show no mercy to any aggressive moves and crush them with a head-on blow.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It was reported that the Japanese government sold its domestically produced Patriot air-defense missiles to the US. It was the first export of deadly weapons since Japan relaxed controls on its arms export. Besides, the Liberal Democratic Party of Japan has started discussions on revising its three security documents, including the revision of its three non-nuclear principles and increasing its defense spending.…","It is an ironclad fact that Japan was a defeated country in WWII. International treaties and instruments such as the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, explicitly ban Japan from rearmament. The international community must be on high alert against Japan's revisionist attempts to break away from the restraints of its pacifist Constitution by brazenly expanding its military build-up, drastically increasing its defense budget, expediting the revision of its security policies, relaxing restrictions on weapons export, and attempting to revoke the three non-nuclear principles. It is even attempting to intervene militarily on the Taiwan question. These moves pose serious threats to regional peace and stability.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. People around the world, especially those from China and other victimized countries in Asia, will never forget the catastrophe brought by Japanese Fascists. The specter of Japanese militarism must never be allowed to haunt the world again. We urge the Japanese side to fully repent for its war crimes and immediately abandon dangerous attempts in constitutional revision and military build-up. Any attempt to repeat the evil path of aggression and expansion and undermine the post-WWII international order will not succeed.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Japanese media reports, a JSDF representative noted that if the Chinese aircraft carrier PLANS Fujian were to engage in military actions in the Taiwan Strait, Japanese and American forces would be able to destroy it. What's your comment?","A simple response to such ignorant remarks: sheer illusion. One should never overestimate its own strength.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","After China took countermeasures against Sanae Takaichi's provocative remarks, the head of Taiwan's so-called external affairs department alleged that Taiwan would support Japan at critical moments as the mainland is bullying Japan through economic coercion and military threats. Lai Ching-te posted pictures on social media of himself eating Japanese food to show his support for Japan. What's your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te has already been disgraced for fawning over Japan. This time, he is so obsequious that he's even licking Japan's boots. We warn the DPP authorities that any attempt to pursue \"Taiwan independence\" by soliciting support from external forces is doomed to fail. Anyone who betrays the nation and seeks to divide the country will be nailed to the pillar of shame.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, according to media reports, US Ambassador to Japan and Deputy Spokesperson for the US Department of State both mentioned this month that the US-Japan Security Treaty applies to the defense of the Diaoyu Dao. Some analyzed that the US intends to counter China's increasing pressure on Japan. What's your comment? Secondly, as was reported by Taiwan media on November 23, Taiwan's Marine…","On your first question. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made blatant and erroneous remarks on Taiwan. Those remarks implied the possibility of Japan's armed intervention in a Taiwan contingency, which triggered outrage and condemnation from the Chinese people. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands are China's inherent territory. No matter what the US or Japan say or do, this fact will not change and China's resolve in safeguarding its national sovereignty and territorial integrity will not be wavered. Certain individuals in the US should act in ways that befit their positions and contribute to regional peace and stability, instead of provoking tensions and stirring up chaos.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China, which brooks no foreign interference. We firmly oppose any form of military collusion between the US and the Taiwan region. We warn the DPP authorities that any attempt to seek \"Taiwan independence\" by soliciting support from external forces or reject reunification by force is doomed to failure.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","An investigation reveals that in recent years, Japan has spent over 13.1 billion yen in Taiwan on cultivating pro-Japanese influencers and relevant propaganda efforts. What's your comment?","During its colonial rule of Taiwan, Japan aggressively enforced the so-called Kominka (Imperial Subject) Movement. Today, it is investing heavily in a more covert campaign of ideological and cultural infiltration targeting the people of Taiwan. This is an attempt to whitewash its own history of aggression and to strip the island's younger generation of their national and cultural identity as Chinese. History must not be distorted, nor can family ties be severed. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait must heighten their vigilance against Japan's political manipulation, resolutely oppose any betraying acts of fawning over Japan and forsaking one's ancestors, and be proud and upright Chinese.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It was reported that the DPP authorities launched a massive mailing campaign to distribute civil defense handbooks to households across the island from November 19, marking an effort to strengthen public preparedness for emergencies, including the possibility of a military attack from the Chinese mainland. An official of the DPP authorities said that it shows Taiwan's determination to defend itself and people…","The so-called handbooks concocted by the DPP authorities are packed with lies. They spread fear of war and create a tense, impending-war atmosphere, inciting confrontation and hostility across the Strait. This runs completely counter to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan, which desires peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. It fully exposes the DPP authorities' malicious intent to seek \"Taiwan independence\" by force and military buildup. We believe that our fellow Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities' true nature of harming Taiwan and will take active actions to jointly oppose the separatist forces' reckless attempts for \"Taiwan independence\", safeguard their own security and well-being as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We hope the compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together to achieve national reunification and the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, the recent maiden sea trial by China's first Type 076 amphibious assault ship, PLANS Sichuan, has attracted international attention. Could you please brief us more on the major improvements of the Type 076 compared to its predecessor, Type 075, in terms of combat capabilities and core technologies? Additionally, does the PLA Navy have a clear plan for mass production and systematic…","On your first question, as a new-generation amphibious assault ship, PLANS Sichuan will play a significant role in advancing the PLA Navy's transformation and modernization, as well as enhancing its capabilities of far seas operations. China's independent research and development of amphibious assault ships and other military equipment serves China's national security and supports the overall development of the PLA Navy. The goal is to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, and to better protect peace and stability in the region and beyond.\nOn your second question, it is the Chinese military's sacred duty to safeguard national sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity. We will show no mercy to any aggressive moves and crush them with a head-on blow.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-11-27","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lai Ching-te announced a special defense budget of NT$1.25 trillion over the next eight years, claiming that the mainland intends to use force to \"coerce reunification, compel surrender and annex Taiwan\". He also proposed two security action plans. What's your comment? Besides, he said that the mainland would complete preparations for reunification by force in 2027. What's your comment?","Taiwan is a province of China, and there is no such thing as president in the region. Separatist actions for \"Taiwan independence\" and interference from external forces constitute the biggest threat to peace across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities keep generating war scares, constantly devising new and costly schemes under the guise of soliciting external support for \"Taiwan independence\" or seeking \"Taiwan independence\" by force. These so-called plans are completely futile. They cannot stop the historical trend of national reunification and will only accelerate the demise of the \"Taiwan independence\" separatists.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/11/china-251127-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16424122.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2025-11-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On November 26, Lai Ching-te convened a so-called “National Security High-Level Meeting” and unveiled a so-called “Action Plan for Safeguarding Taiwan's National Security in a Democratic Taiwan.” At the press conference after the meeting, he touted “‘Democratic Taiwan’ is a sovereign and independent country” and other “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, greatly played up the mainland…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that Lai Ching-te's separatist fallacies are full of hostility and confrontation, paranoia and arrogance, fully showing that his \"Taiwan independence\" stance is obstinate and unrepentant, his separatist position is radical and risky, his provocations are reckless, and his betrayal and harm to Taiwan have grown worse. His so-called \"action plan\" exaggerates the \"mainland threat\" in an attempt to \"seek independence through military force\" and \"seek independence by relying on external forces.\" It is a \"war-provoking plan\" and \"Taiwan-destroying plan\" of military adventurism that brings disaster to Taiwan. This once again exposes his fierce face as a \"peace disruptor,\" \"crisis creator,\" and \"war instigator.\"\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. It has never been a country and will never become one. The status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that there is only one China in the world, that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and this has not changed and must not be changed. Unification is a historical conclusion. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to unification, much less an excuse for separation. \"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" is the best way to realize national reunification. The \"two systems\" plan for Taiwan is a \"peaceful plan\" and a \"plan that loves Taiwan.\" It will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully safeguard the interests and sentiments of Taiwan compatriots.\nSince Lai Ching-te took office, he has disregarded the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society, stubbornly persisted in the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, deliberately incited \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, and continued to escalate tensions across the Taiwan Strait. Following his designation of the mainland as a \"hostile foreign force\" in March this year and his release of the so-called \"17 strategies,\" he has now released a so-called \"action plan\" and \"13 specific actions.\" Persisting down this evil path of undermining cross-Strait relations and plotting \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, he will only push Taiwan step by step into the abyss of disaster and the danger of war.\n\"Taiwan independence\" means war, and it is a dead end. The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests. It concerns the national sentiments of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people and is an absolute red line that must not be crossed. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces dare to cross the red line, we will certainly act resolutely and strike head-on. We have firm resolve, strong determination, and formidable capability to crush all \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts and external interference, to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to safeguard the security and well-being of the Taiwan people. The great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable, and the complete reunification of the motherland will certainly be achieved. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities: do not play with fire, for those who play with fire will burn themselves. \"Seeking independence through military force\" and taking desperate risks will only dig their own grave!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202511/t20251127_12737433.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-11-28","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Yesterday, Foreign Minister Wang Yi had a call with his French counterpart and the Chinese readout said that he asked the French to cooperate on the core issues of both sides. We understand obviously Taiwan is one of the core issues of the Chinese state. Did Wang Yi have any specific mention about cooperating on the issue of Taiwan to the French? Does China plan to bring this issue up again when President Macron…","We’ve released a readout about the phone call you mentioned. On the exchanges between the Chinese and French presidents, I have no information to share at the moment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251128_11762812.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251128_11762706.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-28","Mao Ning","Global Times","Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks have been opposed and criticized by visionary people in Japan and the wider world. Yet, the Taiwan authorities kept backing Takaichi. Days ago, Lai Ching-te conveyed his “support” by eating sushi, and Taiwan’s “foreign affairs department” said that the mainland’s letter to the UN Secretary-General “contains rude and unreasonable content.” What’s your comment?","Japan exerted colonial rule on Taiwan for half a century and committed innumerable crimes there. The DPP authorities keep ingratiating themselves with Japan to seek “Taiwan independence”. That is simply disgraceful.\nPrime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan interfere in China’s internal affair, send a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and China’s recovery of Taiwan. Japan should deeply reflect on its war crimes, learn lessons from history, adhere to the one-China principle, and exercise utmost prudence when it comes to the Taiwan question. We ask the Japanese side to retract the erroneous remarks, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and take practical steps to honor its commitments to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251128_11762812.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251128_11762706.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-28","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","Your colleague made a statement yesterday that the San Francisco Treaty is illegal and invalid. Is it the contention of the Chinese government that state of war still exists between Japan and 47 other parties of the treaty?","As my colleague stressed yesterday, the so-called “Treaty of San Francisco” was issued with the exclusion of important parties to the WWII, such as the People’s Republic of China and the Soviet Union, in order to seek a separate peace deal with Japan. The document goes against the provision of not making a separate armistice or peace with the enemies in the Declaration by United Nations signed by 26 countries in 1942, including China, the U.S., the UK and the Soviet Union, and violates the UN Charter and the basic principles of international law. Anything set out in the treaty on the sovereignty over Taiwan or the handling of the territory and sovereign rights of China as a non-signatory, is thus entirely illegal and null and void.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251128_11762812.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251128_11762706.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-11-28","Mao Ning","Bloomberg","China did sign a peace treaty with Japan in 1978, correct? This is after the Treaty of San Francisco. So in 1978 the Chinese position was that they did accept the San Francisco Treaty. And now your position is you don’t accept the San Francisco Treaty. Is that correct?","Your understanding is not correct. China has never recognized anything set out in the “Treaty of San Francisco,” including on the sovereignty over Taiwan or the handling of the territory and sovereign rights of China as a non-signatory, and has never accepted the treaty. The 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement clearly states that “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” The four political documents between China and Japan provide clear provisions on the Taiwan question and other issues, and together they constitute the political foundation of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202511/t20251128_11762812.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202511/t20251128_11762706.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-01","Lin Jian","Global Times","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said previously that “Having renounced all rights and claims under the ‘Treaty of San Francisco,’ we are not in a position to recognize Taiwan’s legal status.” On November 28, Japan’s Foreign Minister Toshimitsu Motegi when asked about whether it means that Japan does not recognize China’s sovereignty over Taiwan repeated what’s said in the “Treaty of San Francisco,” and…","The Japanese side keeps hiding and fudging its position on the Taiwan question. Whenever asked, the Japanese side simply would not mention the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender—all of which made clear that Taiwan be restored to China, nor the four political documents that serve as the political foundation of China-Japan relations, nor the political commitment made by the Japanese government to the one-China principle. All the Japanese side has done is dodging the issue by claiming that its position “remains unchanged.” Not even once has the Japanese side fully articulated what exactly that position is.\nPerhaps what the Japanese side would not clarify is not just its position on the Taiwan question. Today, December 1, marks the 82nd anniversary of the Cairo Declaration. This document, together with a series of other international legal instruments, stipulates China’s sovereignty over Taiwan, and they are vital outcomes of the World Anti-Fascist War and an integral part of the postwar international order. Japan has an obligation under international law to observe those documents, which is the prerequisite for Japan to be readmitted to the international community after the war. But the Japanese side does not even mention a word about those instruments with full effect under international law, and instead keeps quoting a document that excludes China and some other Asian countries who suffered the most from Japanese aggression and colonialism. That is a clear sign of oblivion to the horrible memory of Japan’s militarist aggression, a serious disregard for the history of the World Anti-Fascist War, and a blatant challenge to the authority of the UN and the postwar international order. The Japanese side has in recent years been revamping the security and defense policies, beefing up the defense budget year after year and seeking to revise its three non-nuclear principles. Some forces in Japan have been trying hard to break free from the Pacifist Constitution and Japan’s legal obligations as a defeated country in WWII. They never truly learned the lessons from history, never truly did any soul-searching about Japan’s war atrocities or looked at them squarely, and never truly sought to prevent the revival of militarism in Japan. They hope that by whitewashing and not mentioning the true history, they could somehow make the world forget and release Japan from its obligations, but the world will not be deceived.\nThe course of history must not be reversed, and the bottom line of peace must not be crossed. Japan prevaricated to downplay the situation while continuing down the wrong path. China would absolutely not accept that. On issues of principle, an evasive attitude will not get the Japanese side anywhere. We urge the Japanese side to learn the lessons of history, do soul-searching, take seriously what it has heard from the Chinese side, simply retract the erroneous remarks as it should and take practical steps to honor its political commitments to China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251201_11764222.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251201_11764036.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-02","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","In the letter to the UN Secretary-General on November 24, Japan’s Permanent Representative to the UN said that China’s assertion that Japan would exercise the right of self-defense even in the absence of an armed attack is erroneous; Japan’s fundamental defense policy is the posture of passive defense strategy, which is exclusively defense-oriented; the remarks by the Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi are…","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan openly challenge the victorious outcomes of World War II and the post-war international order, and constitute a serious violation of the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations. China’s letter to the UN Secretary-General setting out our solemn position was entirely justified and necessary.\nThe letter by the Japanese side is full of erroneous views and lies. The Japanese side mentioned in the letter the so-called “consistent position” on the Taiwan question. But as to what exactly this “consistent position” is, the Japanese side has continued to evade the question and has yet to give China a direct answer. We ask the Japanese side once again: Can the Japanese government provide the international community with a complete and accurate explanation of its “consistent position” on the Taiwan question as laid down in the four political documents between the two countries?\nThe Japanese side claims that Japan adheres to a “passive defense strategy, which is exclusively defense-oriented,” and asserts that Takaichi’s remarks were grounded in this position. Taiwan is Chinese territory. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and brooks no external interference. Yet Takaichi linked Japan’s “survival-threatening situation” with a “Taiwan contingency,” implying the use of force against China. Is this what the Japanese side’s “passive defense strategy, which is exclusively defense-oriented,” means?\nIn Article 2(4) of Chapter I, the Charter of the United Nations stipulates that “All Members shall refrain in their international relations from the threat or use of force.” As the sitting leader of a defeated country in WWII, Takaichi threatened a victorious country with the use of force in case of a “survival-threatening situation.” How could the Japanese side have the audacity to claim that it “has always respected and adhered to international law, including the UN Charter”?\nThe Japanese side also insinuates accusations regarding the defense development and “coercive measures” of other countries. This is nothing but blame-shifting. In fact, since Japan’s defeat, right-wing forces within Japan have never ceased attempts to whitewash its history of aggression. Japan has increased its defense budget for 13 consecutive years, removed the ban on exercising the right to collective self-defense, relaxed restrictions on arms exports more than once, developed the capability to strike enemy bases, attempted to alter the “three non-nuclear principles,” further hollowed out the provisions on Japan clearly stipulated in the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, and gone back on its commitments made in the constitution. It is the Japanese side, not others, that has been “engaged in the prolonged expansion of military capabilities”, taking “coercive measures” and attempting “unilateral changes to the status quo despite opposition from neighboring countries.”\nGiven all these reasons, the Permanent Mission of China to the UN once again sent a letter to the UN Secretary-General and reiterated the Chinese side’s stern position. This year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. China firmly opposes the Japanese side reversing the course of history, challenging the postwar international order, and honoring the militarists. We once again urge the Japanese side to earnestly do soul-searching, rectify its wrongdoings, fulfill its obligations as a defeated country, take practical steps to honor its commitments to China and the international community, and stop reneging on its words again.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251202_11765147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251202_11764961.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-02","Lin Jian","TV Asahi","It’s reported that some Japanese organizations, such as the Japan-China Friendship Parliamentarians’ Union and Keidanren (Japan Business Federation), have conveyed to the Chinese side their willingness to visit China in the near future. Will China arrange their visits?","We noted the reports and also found that many visionary people in Japan are deeply concerned over the negative influence and grave consequences of Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. The Chinese side urges the Japanese side to do soul-searching, rectify its wrongdoings, retract Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks, stop harming the sentiments of the two peoples, take practical steps to honor its political commitments to China, and create necessary conditions for the normal exchanges between the two countries. We hope relevant Japanese organizations will play a more positive role in Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251202_11765147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251202_11764961.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-02","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Taiwan’s “foreign minister” said that the dispute between China and Japan could drag on for a year. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment on that?","Taiwan is part of China, and there is no such thing as “foreign minister” of Taiwan. The difficulty facing China-Japan relations is simply due to Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. The Japanese side should honor its political commitments to China, retract the erroneous remarks and take practical steps to do soul-searching and correct its wrongdoings. Any external force who dares to meddle in the affairs on the Taiwan Strait will face a resolute, head-on blow from China. The DPP authorities’ ill-intentioned attempts are rather disgraceful and their moves to seek independence by soliciting foreign support will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251202_11765147.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251202_11764961.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-03","Lin Jian","Reuters","A Taiwan official said that it looks forward to reestablishing ties with Honduras and has been in touch with both presidential candidates ahead of their election. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","The one-China principle is the political foundation and fundamental prerequisite for China-Honduras relations. Over the past two years and more since the two countries established diplomatic ties, the relationship has grown rapidly with fruitful cooperation in various fields. China-built agricultural technology schools were completed. Procurement agreements on over 10,000 tons of whiteleg shrimps were signed by Chinese and Honduran companies. Tobacco from Honduras entered the Chinese market. In 2024, China’s imports of Honduran coffee increased by 14 times year on year. China also offered Honduras coffee greenhouses and plantation toolkits, and provided multiple batches of humanitarian supplies when Honduras was hit by hurricane, flooding and other disasters. Cooperation in human resource training, government scholarship, tourism and other fields gives a strong boost to the capacity building in long-term development of Honduras. These achievements fully demonstrate that the relationship has delivered tangibly to the Honduran people and serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the two countries and two peoples.\n“Taiwan independence” separatist activities go in the opposite direction of where the arc of history bends. It is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251203_11766027.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251203_11765754.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-03","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Donald Trump signed into law a bill that calls on the Department of State to regularly review U.S.-Taiwanese relations and look for ways to deepen the U.S. and Taiwan relationship. Does the Chinese Foreign Ministry have any comment?","China firmly opposes official exchanges between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region in any form. This position is consistent and clear.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. The one-China principle is the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. The U.S. government made a clear commitment in the China-U.S. Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations—“The United States of America recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. Within this context, the people of the United States will maintain cultural, commercial, and other unofficial relations with the people of Taiwan.” China urges the U.S. to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, approach the Taiwan question with extra prudence, stop U.S.-Taiwan official exchanges, and stop sending any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251203_11766027.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251203_11765754.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 3, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","On the 27th, the 19th meeting of the Standing Committee of the 14th Fujian Provincial People's Congress voted to adopt the \"Fujian Province Regulations on Promoting Cross-Strait Standards Connectivity.\" This is the mainland's first legislation in this field, and another innovative legislation in Fujian Province's Taiwan-related affairs. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone explicitly propose 'building a cross-Strait common standards service platform and encouraging cross-Strait industry, academia, research institutions, and enterprises to jointly formulate common industry standards.' In recent years, Fujian has made beneficial explorations in cross-Strait standards commonality, continuously deepening cross-Strait standards commonality and formulating a cumulative total of 308 cross-Strait common standards.\nOn November 27, the 19th session of the Standing Committee of the 14th Fujian Provincial People's Congress voted to adopt the Fujian Province Regulations on Promoting Cross-Strait Standards Commonality. It is the first local regulation enacted with promoting cross-Strait standards commonality as its theme, and it will take effect on January 1, 2026. The regulations highlight the two characters 'Tong' (通, connect) and 'Tong' (同, common). They timely solidify into regulations the mature experience and innovative practices that Fujian Province has developed in recent years, and encourage compatriots on both sides to join hands in cross-Strait standardization cooperation through jointly selecting topics, developing, comparing, and applying standards. This is another pioneering legislation in Fujian's Taiwan-related field, and it is of great significance for building a cross-Strait common market, enhancing cross-Strait livelihood and welfare, and deepening cross-Strait integrated development.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738390.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","December 1 marks the 82nd anniversary of the Cairo Declaration. However, Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae has disregarded international legal documents including the Cairo Declaration, attempted to interfere in the situation in the Taiwan Strait, and to this day refuses to retract her erroneous remarks on Taiwan-related matters. What is your comment?","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's victory in the War of Resistance against Japan, the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, and the 82nd anniversary of the publication of the Cairo Declaration. The Cairo Declaration and a series of other international legal documents are major achievements of the world's anti-fascist war. They clarify China's sovereignty over Taiwan at the level of international law and constitute an important part of the postwar international order. Abiding by their relevant provisions is an international legal obligation that the Japanese side must bear.\nThe erroneous remarks by Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae on Taiwan interfere in China's internal affairs, send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and endanger peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect on its historical responsibility, retract its erroneous remarks, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, and abide by the one-China principle and its political commitments to China through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738389.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, there has been a lot of news online about Taiwan compatriots applying for mainland identity documents. Could the spokesperson please introduce in detail the application conditions, procedures, and required materials for these documents.","Taiwan residents' voluntary application for mainland identity documents is their lawful right. To prevent people with ulterior motives from confusing the public and distorting the facts, and to facilitate Taiwan compatriots' applications for relevant mainland documents, I would like to take this opportunity to provide a complete and accurate explanation of the conditions, procedures, and required materials for Taiwan residents to apply for mainland Residence Permits, Settlement Permits, and Resident Identity Cards. We have carefully prepared charts to help everyone better understand the situation (charts shown).\nFirst, the Taiwan Residents' Residence Permit is a document specially issued by the relevant competent mainland authorities to meet Taiwan compatriots' needs for convenience in studying, working, and living on the mainland.\nAccording to the Measures for the Issuance of Residence Permits to Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Residents, Taiwan residents who have come to the mainland to live for more than six months and who meet one of the conditions of lawful and stable employment, lawful and stable residence, or continuous enrollment in school may apply according to their own wishes. Taiwan compatriots applying need only fill out the Application Form for the Residence Permit for Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan Residents, present their own Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents for inspection, and submit proof materials of their residential address, employment, and schooling on the mainland to the police station or household registration service hall designated by the public security organ of the county-level people's government where they live. The application can then be processed normally.\nSecond, the Taiwan Residents' Settlement Permit is issued to Taiwan residents approved to settle on the mainland. It is the certificate they present to the household registration authority of their place of settlement when handling permanent household registration.\nAccording to the Administrative Measures for Chinese Citizens' Travel to and from Taiwan and other relevant provisions, Taiwan residents who meet circumstances such as joining direct relatives on the mainland, being the spouse of a mainland resident, investing on the mainland, or being talent in specialized fields may apply for settlement with the exit-entry administration institution of the public security organ at or above the county level of their intended place of settlement. When applying, applicants shall submit the Application Form for Taiwan Residents' Settlement on the Mainland, photographs for identity documents, a valid Taiwan identity card and exit-entry documents, and supporting documents corresponding to the grounds for their application. Upon approval, the exit-entry administration institution of the public security organ will issue a Notice of Approval for Settlement and a Taiwan Residents' Settlement Permit. Starting January 1, 2024, the mainland's exit-entry administration authorities implemented a policy encouraging Taiwan residents to settle and establish household registration in Fujian, supporting Taiwan compatriots in realizing \"settling wherever they wish to settle\" (愿落尽落) in Fujian.\nThird, the Mainland Resident Identity Card. According to relevant provisions of the Resident Identity Card Law of the People's Republic of China, Taiwan residents who settle on the mainland shall apply for a resident identity card when handling permanent household registration. After Taiwan residents hold the Notice of Approval for Settlement and the Taiwan Residents' Settlement Permit and complete permanent household registration with the public security organ in the place of their permanent household registration, the procedure for applying for a resident identity card is the same as for mainland residents.\nHere, I must emphasize several points again. First, Taiwan residents' application for the above documents is entirely voluntary. Second, we have also noted that some illegal institutions have falsely advertised online that they can handle mainland identity card applications on behalf of Taiwan residents and profit from it. I must remind Taiwan compatriots that in the process of applying for the above documents, apart from the document production fee charged by the issuing institution, any paid service provided by any non-official institution or individual under the name of agency, intermediary, or any other name is illegal and in violation of regulations. Be vigilant against being deceived. Third, in accepting, reviewing, and approving applications, the relevant competent mainland departments will strictly protect the relevant application materials of Taiwan residents in accordance with the law, and will not disclose the personal information or document information of the applicants. I also remind Taiwan compatriots once again to properly safeguard their documents and personal privacy information to prevent leaks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738388.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently advocated that establishing \"the One Country, Two Systems Taiwan Plan\" is a red line that Taiwan society must not touch, and claimed that on this basis, exchanges and political dialogue between the island's political parties, legal persons, civil groups, and others and the mainland must be controlled. What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te has arbitrarily restricted the freedom of Taiwan residents to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and brutally deprived ordinary people of their right to pursue a better life, fully exposing the essence of his “terror politics and green dictatorship.”\n“One Country, Two Systems” is a peaceful plan, a democratic plan, a well-intentioned plan, and a win-win plan. After unification, with a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan compatriots will enjoy better livelihoods and greater development space, and will be safer and more dignified. Internationally, they will stand taller and be more confident, Taiwan will remain forever peaceful, and its people will live and work in contentment. Taiwan compatriots will join compatriots on the mainland in sharing the dignity and glory of our great country and ushering in a bright future of prosperity and stability.\nThe Taiwan question is the core of the core of China's core interests. It concerns the national sentiment of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people and is an absolute red line that must not be crossed. If the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to cross the red line, we will certainly act resolutely and strike back hard. We will continue, on the basis of adhering to the one-China principle, to exchange views extensively with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life on cross-Strait relations and the question of national reunification, conduct in-depth consultations, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738384.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Today (December 3), the Ministry of Justice issued the “Announcement on the Scope of Civil Cases Involving Taiwan Matters in Which Taiwan Residents Who Have Obtained Mainland Legal Professional Qualifications and Mainland Lawyer Practice Certificates May Act as Representatives in Mainland People's Courts,” and asks the spokesperson to introduce the relevant situation.","Today (December 3), the Ministry of Justice issued Announcement No. 16, stating that, starting December 3, 2025, Taiwan residents who have obtained the National Legal Professional Qualification and hold a lawyer's practice certificate may expand their scope of civil case representation on the mainland from the original five categories comprising 237 items to nine categories comprising 299 items, adding 62 new items including maritime and admiralty matters, personality rights, property rights, and competition disputes.\nThis opening measure will create more opportunities and provide broader space for Taiwan's legal professionals to seek employment and development on the mainland and to take part in the cross-Strait legal services market. We will adhere to the concept of \"cross-Strait families are one family,\" continuously improve systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic, cultural exchange and cooperation, and encourage and support more Taiwan compatriots to participate in the economic and social development of the mainland and share in the development opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738385.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Fujian Coast Guard carried out routine law enforcement patrols in waters near Kinmen in accordance with the law. Relevant Taiwan authorities claimed that mainland coast guard patrols are routine harassment and are by no means law enforcement patrols, which not only affects cross-Strait relations but also undermines regional peace and stability. What is your comment on this?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The coast guard authorities conduct regular law-enforcement patrol operations. This is both a legitimate measure to uphold normal navigation and operating order in the relevant waters in accordance with law, and a necessary measure to safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” position and to this day continue to take dangerous and brutal measures against mainland fishing boats and fishermen, threatening the lives and property of mainland fishermen. This is the root of turmoil that undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and harms the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities should immediately stop interfering with and disrupting the normal operations of mainland fishermen, and stop provoking incidents and creating trouble.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Several cross-Strait exchange activities have recently been held in Fujian. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From November 4 to December 15, the 29th Shaxian Snack Tourism and Cultural Festival and the 3rd Cross-Strait Food Carnival were held in Shaxian District, Sanming City, Fujian Province. The event included 14 cross-Strait exchange activities in diverse forms, deeply integrating the appeal of national-level intangible cultural heritage craftsmanship with cultural tourism experiences, and built platforms for cross-Strait industry matchmaking and youth exchanges. This event invited nearly 200 Taiwan compatriots to participate, including more than 100 people from the catering industry and more than 80 young people from Taiwan.\nFrom November 16 to 20, the 17th Straits Tea Industry Expo was held in Wuyishan by Nanping, Fujian Province. A total of 873 exhibitors, including 173 Taiwan-funded enterprises, participated in the expo. During the event, more than 10 exchange activities were held, including the cross-Strait folk tea-tasting competition, the \"Dear, Come Taste Tea\" cross-Strait youth check-in season in Wuyishan, the theme arts evening \"Tea Fragrance Across the Strait, the Moon Shines Together,\" and the \"Tea Fragrance Across the Strait, Exploring Tea Connections Together\" tea culture exchange, promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait in jointly inheriting and carrying forward Chinese tea culture and deepening cross-Strait tea industry exchanges and cooperation.\nFrom November 26 to 28, the 2nd \"Qilin Craftsman\" Cup Cross-Strait (Pingtan) Vocational Skills Competition was held in Pingtan, Fujian. Nearly 100 contestants from Taiwan in fields such as esports, drones, internet marketing, tour guiding, coffee, mixology, hairdressing, and homestays registered to compete. During the event, Pingtan released six newly added projects that directly recognize Taiwan vocational qualifications and three special vocational competence projects for integrated cross-Strait development, promoting the mutual recognition of vocational standards across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, at an event held by the DPP, Lai Ching-te claimed, “Taiwan absolutely does not belong to any part of China,” “Taiwan is a sovereign and independent country, its name is the Republic of China, and it is not subordinate to the People's Republic of China. Its future will be decided jointly by the 23 million people who live on this land.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te’s separatist fallacies are full of hostility and confrontation, bias and arrogance. The obstinacy of his “Taiwan independence” stance and the rampancy of his provocative confrontation fully expose the evil nature of someone who, for the sake of his party and himself, is willing to tie the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and push Taiwan toward the dangerous brink of deadly conflict. He is an out-and-out “peace wrecker,” “crisis creator,” and “war instigator.”\nThe fact that Taiwan belongs to China is clear, and its status is definite. All of the historical, factual, and legal evidence proves that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. It has never been a country and will never become one. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. Taiwan’s future can only be decided jointly by all 1.4 billion-plus Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots.\n“Taiwan independence” means war, and it is a dead end. No person or force should underestimate the Chinese people’s firm resolve, strong will, and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. China will eventually be reunified, and the historical trend of reunification is unstoppable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","Lai Ching-te recently publicly opposed the Kuomintang's plan to \"amend laws\" to safeguard the \"political participation rights\" of mainland spouses in Taiwan. Chu Jung-tai, head of Taiwan's executive body, said that \"the 'amendment of the Nationality Law' involves the issue of dual allegiance.\" What comments do you have on this?","Mainland spouses are family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots, and builders and contributors to Taiwan society. They deserve recognition and respect, and their legitimate rights and interests, including political participation, should be protected. Driven by its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have openly peddled the “two-state theory,” arbitrarily stripped mainland spouses of their lawful rights and interests, and suppressed and bullied the mainland spouse community. They have continuously challenged the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China. We strongly condemn this. We warn the DPP authorities that any vicious act or trick that undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and harms the interests of compatriots on both sides will surely backfire. We will not go easy on the “Taiwan independence” accomplices and henchmen who persecute mainland spouses. We will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738382.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the US “U.S.-China Economic and Security Review Commission” suggested in its annual report that the United States, through overseas arms sales cases, let Taiwan provide non-weapon support services to help upgrade US military bases in the Philippines. Public opinion on the island was in an uproar, demanding that the Lai Qingde authorities publicly explain to the people the content of their private…","For political self-interest, the Lai authorities are servile and fawning toward external forces, pandering to and kowtowing to the United States without principle, and selling out Taiwan without limit. The United States always follows “America First” and cares only about “American interests.” In American eyes, Taiwan’s true value is as “fat meat” and an “ATM,” a chess piece for containing the mainland and a tool in service of America. We warn the Lai authorities that by colluding with external forces to stir up trouble and undermining regional peace and stability, and by going down the evil path of “relying on outsiders to plot independence” to the bitter end, they will inevitably meet the fate of playing with fire and burning themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, the Colombian Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a statement saying it adheres to the one-China principle and denied that it will establish an office in Taiwan. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities expressed protest. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Facts have repeatedly proven that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle is just and in line with the trend of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","The first satellite of Taiwan's “Formosat-8” program was recently launched successfully in the United States aboard a SpaceX Falcon 9. In this regard, Lai Ching-te has been agitating to “make Taiwan an indispensable key role in the international space industry chain and build a new “divine mountain protecting Taiwan.”” What is your comment?","The Lai Ching-te authorities are accustomed to exaggerating and hyping, colluding with outsiders, deceiving the public, and misleading public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently wrote an op-ed in the U.S. newspaper The Washington Post promoting the so-called “four major key directions of Taiwan’s core strategy in facing changes in regional security,” saying that he will add defense budget for U.S. arms purchases and strengthen Taiwan’s asymmetric combat capabilities.","Lai Ching-te, in pursuit of political private gain, unprincipledly fawns on foreign powers, sells out Taiwan without any bottom line, pursues militarism and “preparing for war to seek independence,” lavishly squanders the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people, does not hesitate to turn Taiwan into a “powder keg,” coerces the public into serving as cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence,” and pushes the broad Taiwan compatriots into a dangerous situation of war and calamity. He is an out-and-out “peace wrecker,” a thoroughgoing “war peddler,” and a veritable “troublemaker.”\nThe future of Taiwan and the security, interests, and well-being of Taiwan compatriots lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' obstinate adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist line, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, join us in pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development, and effectively safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","海峡之声广播电台记者","Reportedly, “calm and composed, with ease to spare; in a rush, scrambling and tumbling” has been named one of the top ten buzzwords of 2025. The phrase comes from an online song adapted from the remark “hopeless” by DPP legislator Wang Shih-chien, which also brought Wang attention. Recently, when Wang was asked whether he would visit the mainland for exchanges, he put forward so-called “four conditions,” such as…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China; cross-Strait relations are not state-to-state relations. The person you mentioned, on the one hand, relies on the popularity of the adaptation of “Good for Nothing” to attract attention online, and on the other hand spouts outlandish remarks to seek presence. This self-contradictory showmanship is truly “good for nothing.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","湖北广电记者","The “Beautiful Island Electronic Post” recently released a poll. On cross-Strait issues, nearly half of the public believe it is necessary to maintain the “1992 Consensus.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Only by upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” can there be peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and can compatriots in Taiwan live and work in peace and contentment. Making cross-Strait relations better and better, and bringing more and more benefits and well-being to compatriots, is the shared aspiration of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.\nAt present, “Taiwan independence” separatism poses a serious threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will act with righteousness, uphold the “1992 Consensus,” and oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Taiwanese media reported that the island’s annual “Autumn Struggle” mass rally kicked off in Taipei on November 30. Island residents took to the streets to express demands including opposing war, calling for peace, opposing the DPP authorities’ hollowing out of Taiwan to curry favor with the United States, and opposing increases in the defense budget. What is your comment?","In order to seek private gains from “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities are rushing to “use military force to seek independence” and “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” which is facing growing opposition from the people of Taiwan. The Lai Ching-te authorities are stubbornly pressing ahead, and their fate is doomed to be tragic.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","It is reported that the US is negotiating an agreement with Taiwan, requiring Taiwan to make new investments in the United States in advanced industries such as semiconductor manufacturing and to help train American workers. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities, for the sake of their party’s narrow interests, are shamelessly currying favor with the United States and selling out Taiwan. In order to win a smile from the United States, they are willing to exhaust Taiwan’s resources and cripple Taiwan’s own industries, showing not the slightest regard for the livelihoods and future of the 23 million Taiwan compatriots. They have lost basic reason and conscience.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, in an op-ed in US media, claimed he would invest NT$1.25 trillion as a special defense budget, which caused an uproar across all sectors on the island. Public opinion on the island criticized Lai Ching-te for “playing with fire,” holding that apart from preparing for war, all other livelihood matters would be unable to move forward and that Taiwan was being treated as an ATM. What is your…","Lai Ching-te shamelessly kowtows to foreign powers without principle and sells out Taiwan without bottom line. He is racing down the road of plotting “independence,” provoking conflict, and waging militarism. He lavishly squanders the people's hard-earned money and vigorously promotes “all-people militarization.” Regardless of the cost, he is willing to turn Taiwan into a battlefield and the people into cannon fodder, wasting money that could be used to improve people's livelihoods on buying weapons and fattening foreign arms dealers. This will only push Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation of war and peril.\n“Taiwan independence” means war. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence incites war.” We resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and join us in pushing cross-Strait relations back onto the track of peaceful development, and in earnestly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities: do not play with fire, for those who play with fire will burn themselves. “Seeking independence through force” and taking desperate risks will only dig their own graves!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251203_12738387.htm"],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Starting November 20, the number of ports from which the mainland can issue a Taiwan Compatriot Travel Permit valid for a single entry and exit has increased to 100, which has drawn widespread praise from Taiwan compatriots who travel to the mainland. Can you introduce the application status of Taiwan compatriots as of today?","Starting November 20, immigration and exit-entry administration authorities have increased to 100 the number of entry ports at which one-time valid Taiwan compatriot permits can be issued, from Beijing Capital International Airport and Shenzhen Huanggang to Xinjiang's Horgos and Guangxi's Youyiguan. Port-based permit services are now available to Taiwan compatriots, and many Taiwan compatriots have already enjoyed convenient and efficient permit services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","深圳卫视直新闻记者","Recently, the DPP authorities announced that they will impose anti-dumping duties on imported beer from the mainland and certain hot-rolled flat-rolled steel products, retroactive to July 3 of this year, for a period of 5 years. What is your comment on this?","The economies across the Taiwan Strait are highly complementary. The products that the Mainland exports to Taiwan meet Taiwan’s market demand, giving Taiwan residents and enterprises more choices and substantial economic benefits.\nFacing the changing global economic and trade landscape, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have unjustifiably blamed Mainland enterprises for their ineffective efforts to relieve industrial difficulties, while groveling and kowtowing to the United States, which is shameful. We hope that business communities on both sides will strengthen communication and exchanges, seek solutions satisfactory to both sides through friendly consultation, and jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","A Taiwan “Control Yuan member” said that in recent years mainland internet-famous foods such as luosifen, spicy strips and wax-bottle candy have been able to enter Taiwan directly through express delivery and logistics operators by exploiting a “loophole” that exempts small parcels from inspection. He has applied for an automatic investigation, which has prompted complaints from island residents. What comment do…","The two sides of the Strait share the same language, culture, customs and habits. It is entirely normal for young people on both sides to have the same food preferences and cultural tastes. Now, Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, eating mainland snacks, watching mainland TV dramas, and singing mainland pop songs have become a trend and a new way of life. DPP politicians, deviating from popular will and public opinion, obstinately cling to a mindset of \"opposing anything from the mainland.\" For private gain, they persist in political manipulation, and they will only be rejected by the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Regarding recent media reports that Japan spent 13.1 billion yen to cultivate pro-Japanese figures in Taiwan, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, said that Japan and Taiwan share similar ideas and have common interests. What comments do you have on this?","Relevant remarks once again expose the ugly face of the Lai Ching-te authorities, who, for the sake of party self-interest, betray the nation and “cater to Japan and sell out Taiwan” without principle or bottom line. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “catering to Japan to plot independence” leads only to a dead end. No matter how they collude with external forces or stir up trouble, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they change the trend that China will inevitably be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","Some media reported that a New Zealand navy replenishment ship recently transited the Taiwan Strait, and that the PLA tracked and monitored it throughout. What comments do you have?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. The actions of relevant countries send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We will resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","《团结报》记者","The 93rd General Assembly of the International Criminal Police Organization (INTERPOL) will be held in Morocco from November 24 to 27. Recently, a US lawmaker proposed a bill supporting Taiwan’s accession to INTERPOL, claiming that Taiwan’s inability to access global criminal information would affect global security. What comments do you have on this?","Regarding Taiwan region’s participation in international organizations, including activities of INTERPOL, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. Taiwan, as part of China, has no right to join INTERPOL.\nChina and INTERPOL have made detailed and appropriate arrangements for Taiwan region’s participation in cooperation within the framework of the organization. Channels for information sharing and case cooperation between Taiwan region’s police agencies and the national central bureaus are unobstructed. Certain foreign politicians fabricate all kinds of pretexts and repeatedly hype and manipulate the so-called issue of Taiwan joining international organizations, including INTERPOL. This is entirely with ulterior motives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","On November 26, Lai Qingde convened a so-called “national security senior-level meeting” and put forward a so-called “Action Plan for Safeguarding the National Security of a Democratic Taiwan.” At the post-meeting press conference, he promoted “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies such as “‘Democratic Taiwan’ is a sovereign and independent country,” loudly exaggerated the mainland “threat,” and clamored to…","Lai Ching-te's separatist fallacies are filled with hostility and confrontation, obstinacy and arrogance, fully demonstrating that his \"Taiwan independence\" stance is intransigent, his separatist proposals are radical and risky, his provocations are unrestrained, and his betrayal and harm to Taiwan are growing ever more severe. His so-called \"action plan\" vigorously hypes the \"mainland threat,\" attempting to \"seek independence through force\" and \"seek independence by relying on foreign powers.\" It is a \"war-provoking plan\" and \"Taiwan-destroying plan\" of bellicose militarism that brings disaster to Taiwan. This has once again exposed his evil face as a \"peace wrecker,\" \"crisis creator,\" and \"war instigator.\"\nTaiwan is Taiwan of China and has never been a country, and it never will become one. The status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that there is only one China in the world, and both the mainland and Taiwan belong to one China; this has not changed and will not be allowed to change. Reunification is a historical conclusion. Differences in systems are not an obstacle to reunification, much less an excuse for separation. \"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" is the best way to realize national reunification. The \"two systems\" plan for Taiwan is a \"peaceful plan\" and a \"plan that cherishes Taiwan,\" which will fully take into account Taiwan's actual circumstances, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nSince taking office, Lai Ching-te has disregarded the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society, stubbornly adhered to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, and deliberately plotted to incite \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, continuously aggravating cross-Strait tensions. Following his designation of the mainland as a \"hostile foreign force\" in March this year and his release of the so-called \"17 strategies,\" he has now released the so-called \"action plan\" and \"13 specific actions.\" Going down the evil path of undermining cross-Strait relations and plotting \"Taiwan independence\" separatism to the bitter end, he will only push Taiwan step by step into the abyss of disaster of war and danger.\n\"Taiwan independence\" means war, and it is a dead end. The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests, concerns the national sentiments of over 1.4 billion Chinese people, and is an absolutely inviolable red line. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces dare to cross the red line, we will certainly act resolutely and strike back hard. We have firm will, strong determination, and formidable capability to crush all \"Taiwan independence\" separatist acts and external interference, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan. The great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable, and the complete reunification of the motherland will certainly be realized. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: do not play with fire, for those who play with fire will burn themselves; \"seeking independence through force\" and taking desperate risks will only dig one's own grave!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Lai Ching-te recently announced that NT$1.25 trillion will be invested in a “special defense budget.” Raymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office, welcomed it on social media. Wellington Koo, head of Taiwan's defense authorities, said that preliminary coordination with the U.S. side has been completed, and the U.S. Department of Defense has provided items, quantities, prices,…","For the narrow partisan interests of the DPP authorities, money that could have been used to improve people's livelihoods and develop the economy is being wasted on currying favor with external forces. Buying weapons not only fails to buy “security” but also accelerates pushing Taiwan into peril. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that servility and militarism are a dead end.\nWe firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and Taiwan Region of China. The U.S. side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence and appropriateness, and stop sending any erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Recently, Xu Chunying, chairperson of the Taiwan People's Party's New Residents Committee and a mainland spouse, was detained and held incommunicado. The TPP said it currently does not know the grounds for Xu's case, and hopes the investigating authorities will “not wrongly accuse or let go, follow due legal procedures and the principle of investigative secrecy, and not repeat arbitrary political manipulation.”…","For the sake of its selfish gains from pursuing “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated charges to persecute and suppress the mainland spouse community on the island, constantly incited “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, and created a “green terror” on the island. We firmly oppose this. The “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices who cooperate with the DPP authorities in persecuting mainland spouses will certainly receive the punishment they deserve.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The spokesperson has just introduced the situation regarding Taiwan residents applying for Mainland Residence Permits, Settlement Permits and Identity Cards. Fujian once issued relevant policies. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office's emphasis on introducing the relevant situation this time means that more relevant policies will be promoted in the future to make it easier for more Taiwanese…","Regarding the questions you raised, I have already given a detailed introduction just now. We have also released relevant charts and information, which will help everyone understand the situation better.\nI want to emphasize that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and are one family. Everyone should visit each other more often and exchange more, growing closer and closer. No matter how much interference and obstruction there is, exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait cannot stop, cannot be cut off, and cannot be reduced, and they will not stop, will not be cut off, and will not be reduced. We have always upheld the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” We continuously introduce policies to increase cross-Strait exchanges and civilian contacts and actively promote the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and the routinization of exchanges in all fields. We will further provide more convenience for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland and more help for Taiwan compatriots to develop on the mainland. At the same time, we will continue to protect, in accordance with law and effectively, the personal information security of Taiwan compatriots applying for certificates.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: Does the mainland's current introduction of the relevant certificate application procedures represent a change in cross-Strait policy? Does the mainland now allow Taiwan residents to hold dual household registrations in the mainland? Second question: On the 2nd, the White House announced that U.S. President Donald Trump had formally signed the “Taiwan Assurance Implementation Act,” which requires…","First question: Taiwan is part of China, and there is only one China in the world.\nSecond question: We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and China’s Taiwan region, and this position is consistent and clear. The relevant so-called “act” by the US side brazenly interferes in China’s internal affairs, seriously violates the one-China principle and the spirit of the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and sends a seriously wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We express strong dissatisfaction with and firm opposition to this. We urge the US side to abide by its solemn political commitments on the Taiwan question and not to have any form of official contact with the Taiwan region.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","台湾TVBS记者","Lai Ching-te, when meeting with Taiwan compatriots in North America yesterday (the 2nd), claimed that the “1992 Consensus” and the “one-China principle Taiwan plan” are “one country, two systems,” and that the future would be “patriots administering Taiwan” as defined by the mainland, and that “we must turn Taiwanese into Chinese.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te’s remarks are sinister in intent. Their purpose is to intimidate Taiwan compatriots and to absolve the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatists of responsibility for denying the ‘1992 Consensus’, undermining cross-Strait relations, and stubbornly pursuing ‘Taiwan independence’ separatism.\nThe ‘1992 Consensus’ is the consensus reached in 1992 by ARATS and SEF, authorized to do so, that each side expresses orally that ‘both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle’. It clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations and is the common political foundation for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\n‘One country, two systems’ is an institutional arrangement after national reunification. It is a peaceful plan, a democratic plan, a good-faith plan and a win-win plan. Its concrete form of realization in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan’s actual circumstances, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. Taiwan’s future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots depends on national reunification. We will unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to jointly explore a ‘two systems’ Taiwan plan, enrich the practice of peaceful reunification, and resolutely promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-03","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Recently, Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an said that the “Twin City Forum” is currently planned to be held at the end of December, and many details are being coordinated. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office will arrange to meet with Chiang Wan-an at that time, how you evaluate the Taipei City Government's leading a delegation to Shanghai to attend a meeting during Chiang's tenure, and what significance this has…","The Shanghai Municipality and Taipei City have maintained communication about holding the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum. Our position of supporting the holding of the “Twin City Forum” has been consistent. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will visit each other more often and exchange more, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nToday's press conference concludes here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251203_12738377.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-04","Lin Jian","CCTV","Media reports say that on December 3 at a plenary session of the House of Councillors, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi referred to the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement, saying that the Japanese side “understands and respects” the Chinese government’s position that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China.” What is China’s comment?","The reports have been proved to be inaccurate. Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi merely said that “the Japanese government’s basic position regarding Taiwan remains as stated in the 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement, and there has been no change to this position,” and nothing more.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251204_11766780.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251204_11766635.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-05","Lin Jian","CGTN","It’s reported that in a pretaped interview at DealBook Summit to the New York Times days ago, Lai Ching-te made irresponsible remarks on the situation across the Taiwan Strait. What’s China’s comment?","The event of relevant U.S. media outlet provided a platform for the Taiwan authorities’ leader to peddle separatist rhetoric for “Taiwan independence.” This is a serious violation of the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and sends a gravely wrong signal to the separatist forces. China firmly opposes that.\nLai Ching-te’s remarks once again revealed his nature as a diehard separatist seeking U.S. support for “Taiwan independence” and proved him as a provocateur and saboteur of peace. We urge the U.S. side to fully grasp the great sensitivity of the Taiwan question and act on their leader’s commitment. Whatever Lai says and does, his separatist agenda will not succeed.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251205_11767729.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251205_11767615.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-05","Lin Jian","Reuters","Can the government confirm whether the Chinese military is currently massing a large number of naval and coast guard vessels in the East China Sea, the South China Sea, the Taiwan Strait and into the Pacific. Are these regular drills or is China planning something else? Japan’s Defense Minister said today that China has been expanding and stepping up its military activities in the area surrounding Japan. How does…","I’d refer you to competent authorities for what you mentioned. Let me stress that China is committed to a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. The Chinese navy and China Coast Guard carry out activities in relevant waters in strict accordance with China’s domestic laws and international law. There is no need for relevant parties to overreact and overinterpret, still less should they make groundless accusations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251205_11767729.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251205_11767615.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-08","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","It was reported that on December 3, regarding Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan, Vice-President of the Liberal Democratic Party Taro Aso expressed support for Takaichi’s attitude. What is China’s comment?","This Japanese politician’s remarks demonstrate that Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi and the right-wing provocateurs behind her still misjudge the situation, refuse to do soul-searching or correct the wrongdoings, turn a deaf ear to criticism in and outside Japan, downplay and whitewash interference in other countries’ internal affairs and threat of force in disregard of facts, show no basic respect to international law and basic norms of international relations, and attempt to break free from the post-war international order and revive militarism in Japan by stoking conflict and confrontation. This should put Japan’s Asian neighbors and the international community on high alert.\nIt needs to be pointed out that attempting to grab attention and reap public support by provoking China is malign in nature and very dangerous. We urge the Japanese side to seriously reflect on and repent for its wrongdoing, simply retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks, stop playing with fire, and avoid going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251208_11768841.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251208_11768723.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-08","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","What is the Foreign Ministry’s reaction to the Trump administration’s newly released National Security Strategy, given that it says that the U.S. does not support any unilateral change to the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and also discusses the U.S. and its allies’ capacity to deny any attempt to seize Taiwan? What do you make of the document’s mentioning of the Quad grouping of nations as well?","We noted the “National Security Strategy” report released by the U.S. government. China always believes that China and the U.S. stand to gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation. Upholding mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation is the right way for China and the U.S. to get along with each other and is the only right and realistic choice. China stands ready to work with the U.S. to sustain the steady development of the bilateral relationship and at the same time will firmly defend its sovereignty, security and development interests. We hope the U.S. will work with China in the same direction, act on the important common understandings reached between heads of state of the two countries, step up dialogue and cooperation, properly manage differences, promote the steady, sound and sustainable development of China-U.S. relations, and inject more certainty and stability into the world.\nOn the Taiwan question, we stress that Taiwan is China’s Taiwan and is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people and Chinese people only that brooks no external interference. The U.S. needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, honor its leaders’ commitment, approach the Taiwan question with extra prudence, stop abetting and aiding separatist forces’ attempt to seek “Taiwan independence” and resist reunification through military buildup. China will never flinch in defending its sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251208_11768841.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251208_11768723.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-09","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","We noted that recently neighboring countries including Russia vocally opposed Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. Pakistan, Laos, Cambodia and other countries openly reaffirmed their support to the one-China principle. Media outlets and academics from regional countries stated that the atrocities committed by the Japanese military during WWII inflicted untold sufferings on Asia…","Over the last century, under the pretext of “survival-threatening situation,” Japanese militarists waged a war of aggression against China and other Asian countries, taking millions of lives and committing horrendous atrocities across the continent.\nDuring WWII, among the three mass killings of civilians committed by the Japanese military, over 300,000 were murdered in the Nanjing massacre, an estimated 100,000 Filipino civilians were killed in just one month in the Manila massacre, and the death toll of the massacre in Singapore was tens of thousands. It’s documented in the International Military Tribunal for the Far East Judgment that the Japanese military created over 100 large-scale massacres in Malaysia, Indonesia, Myanmar, Thailand and other places.\nPrisoners of war (POWs) from Allied nations were treated cruelly by the Japanese military, among whom 27 percent were killed after capture. In the Bataan Death March, about 15,000 U.S. and Philippine POWs died under maltreatment.\nHundreds of thousands of Southeast Asian people and Allied POWs who had been forced into slave labor by the Japanese military perished in building the Burma-Thailand Railway. Over four million Chinese workers forcibly recruited by the Japanese military died or injured because of overwork under brutal conditions.\nWomen and girls from China, the Korean Peninsula, Southeast Asia, the Netherlands and other countries and regions were brutally forced into sexual slavery by the Japanese military as “comfort women.”\nJapan’s war crimes must not be erased and the verdict on its history of aggression must not be changed. Any tolerance on the provocative words and deeds of Japanese right-wing forces will only revive the specter of militarism and once again put the Asian people in danger. Countries have the responsibility and obligation to join hands in thwarting any attempt to revive militarism and Fascism, defending the outcomes of WWII victory, upholding the post-war international order and safeguarding world peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251209_11769586.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251209_11769561.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-09","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Dutch media reported that a Chinese language news website in Hungary published the names of Dutch spies who met with representatives from Taiwanese intelligence. Does China have any comment on this report?","I haven’t seen the reports.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251209_11769586.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251209_11769561.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-10","Guo Jiakun","NOS","Yesterday, Dutch media reported that Dutch and Taiwanese security officers’ activities were published online and this was done by the Chinese side. Could you please respond to these allegations?","I’m not familiar with that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251210_11770455.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251210_11770291.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-10","Guo Jiakun","Asahi Shimbun","Regarding the issue of “radar illumination,” Japanese defense minister said today “The essence of the problem is...the Chinese side conducted intermittent radar illumination.” I want to ask whether the aircraft has locked radar on Japanese aircraft intermittently. Can the Foreign Ministry confirm it?","China has stated its serious position on that more than once. The facts are very clear. Yesterday, the Japanese side said they received no prior notification of China’s flight drill. Today, they admitted that they did receive the information beforehand. In addition to that inconsistency, the Japanese side continues to beat around the bush without explaining why they sent warplanes into China’s pre-announced exercise zones and repeatedly engaged in hostile surveillance and disruptive maneuvers to create a crisis situation and generate media hypes. Is the Japanese side trying to divert attention and mislead the international community?\nThe Japanese side needs to face up to what actually caused the current difficulties facing China-Japan relations, do serious soul-searching and correct its wrongdoing, and retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan as it should.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251210_11770455.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251210_11770291.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-10","Guo Jiakun","NHK","Japan’s defense minister said today that Japanese SDF fighter jets did not direct radar at Chinese carrier-based aircraft and that China’s notice lacked details on the drills and Japan did not receive sufficient information to avoid what was a dangerous situation. What’s your comment?","I just responded to relevant questions and I’m sure you heard me clearly. Yesterday, the Japanese side said they received no prior notification of the flight drill from China. Today, they admitted that they did receive the information beforehand. Such inconsistency proves that it was Japan who first deliberately made harassment and then spread disinformation. The Japanese side is the provocateur responsible for orchestrating this political stunt. We urge the Japanese side to face up to what actually caused the current difficulties facing China-Japan relations, do serious soul-searching and correct its wrongdoing, and retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan as it should.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251210_11770455.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251210_11770291.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on December 10, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua first announced information about the upcoming 2025 Cross-Strait CEO Summit annual meeting, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, hello everyone. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. I will first announce an important information item on cross-Strait exchange activities.\nThe 2025 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Annual Meeting will be held in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province, from December 16th to 17th. This year's annual meeting takes “Focusing on Transformation and Innovation, Deepening Multi-Chain Cooperation” as its theme, and will hold in-depth exchanges and discussions on topics including seizing the historic opportunity of formulating and implementing the “15th Five-Year Plan,” helping Taiwanese businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern, and deepening the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. About 800 people, including members and affiliates of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Council, cross-Strait entrepreneurs, and relevant experts and scholars, will attend the event.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739703.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Fujian Province recently released the fifth batch of policy measures implementing the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone.” Please introduce the relevant situation.","On December 2, Fujian Province released the fifth batch of policy measures for implementing the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development Across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Cross-Strait Integrated Development” (hereinafter referred to as the “Opinions”). The batch covers 12 specific measures in three areas: supporting the development of Taiwan enterprises and Taiwan businesspeople; optimizing tax services for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises; and promoting cross-Strait trade, cultural, and tourism exchanges and cooperation. The measures include increasing land and sea-use guarantees, opening intelligent tax-handling platforms, and supporting Taiwan compatriots in opening Shaxian snack outlets in Taiwan. This batch of measures actively responds to the demands of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. They are specific, pragmatic, and effective, and will further accelerate the construction of a new pattern of integrated development across all of Fujian.\nSince the Opinions were released in September 2023, Fujian Province has successively released four batches totaling 62 measures. Adding this batch's 12 measures brings the total to 74 measures. Policy implementation has achieved remarkable results. The sense of gain among Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises has continued to grow, and the measures have won broad recognition and active response from all sectors on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739702.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The mainland social platform Xiaohongshu has over 3 million users in Taiwan, 70% of whom are post-90s. It has become a social media platform frequently used and favored by people in Taiwan, especially young people. On December 4, the DPP authorities, citing reasons such as “failing multiple cybersecurity indicators” and “high incidence of fraud,” imposed a “provisional ban” of one year on Xiaohongshu. What is the…","This brings to mind the famous line from the Zuo Zhuan, Duke Huan, Year Ten: “A commoner is not guilty, but possessing a jade is his crime.” As everyone knows, Xiaohongshu is a social platform positioned as a “lifestyle and interest community,” and it is deeply loved by the people of Taiwan, especially young people, for its rich and diverse everyday content, its community atmosphere close to youth interests, and its convenient modes of interaction. Through Xiaohongshu, they learn about the real situation on the mainland and interact warmly and amicably with mainland netizens, which has caused the “information cocoon” deliberately created by the DPP authorities and their smears against the mainland to collapse and fail. Therefore, the DPP authorities are like a thorn in the back, mortified and enraged. The so-called “information security” cited as the reason for the ban exposes their inner fear and “unease.”\nAs for the so-called “anti-fraud,” according to reports in local media on the island, Facebook was involved in nearly 60,000 fraud cases on the island last year, and this year has already exceeded 30,000, far more than the number of cases the DPP authorities accuse Xiaohongshu of involving. Therefore, the DPP authorities, in the name of “anti-fraud,” are in reality “anti-democracy.” Their high-handed conduct tramples on democracy and impairs freedom, brutally deprives the people of Taiwan, especially young people, of their right to know and their freedom to use social platforms, and seriously harms the livelihoods of island residents who earn their living through Xiaohongshu.\nFrom blocking mainland shopping platforms and video platforms to now banning mainland social platforms, the DPP has become a true “people-banning and people-blocking” authority that stands against the common people. Whatever Taiwan's people commonly use must be banned, and whatever Taiwan's young people love to use must be blocked. Wrongdoing brings its own downfall. The DPP authorities act recklessly, and they will surely reap the bitter consequences. Their perverse actions cannot stop the people of Taiwan, especially young people, from the tide of public opinion seeking to understand the mainland and to make friends and build mutual understanding with mainland compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739701.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","In an interview with The New York Times recently, Lai Ching-te claimed that Taiwan's economic growth rate this year reached 7.37%. He presumptuously claimed that he is “willing to help China and cooperate to solve the various economic problems China faces,” and hoped that the mainland side “should not consider how to expand territory, but should think about how to take better care of the Chinese people.” What…","Lai Qingde talks recklessly and overestimates himself, attempting to mislead public opinion and deceive the people by playing games with numbers.\nSince the beginning of this year, the mainland's major economic indicators have performed well, new quality productive forces have developed actively, and reform and opening up have continued to deepen, demonstrating strong vitality and resilience. In the first three quarters, the mainland's GDP exceeded 101.5 trillion yuan, up 5.2% year on year, with an increase of about 4 trillion yuan. The growth in just these three quarters reached more than 80% of Taiwan's total economic output. It is expected that Taiwan's full-year GDP this year will be lower than the GDP of many provinces on the mainland. I really don't know where Lai Qingde gets his confidence.\nIn order to “seek independence by relying on foreign powers,” Lai Qingde violates economic laws and forcibly pushes for cross-Strait “decoupling and breaking of supply chains.” He disregards the fact that Taiwan's advantageous industries are being forcibly hollowed out by outsiders, ignores the serious difficulties facing Taiwan's traditional industries, and vigorously fawns on external forces and pledges allegiance to them. This will only further sell out and harm Taiwan.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the country is the shared aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. The economies on both sides of the Strait belong to the economy of the Chinese nation. We always adhere to the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” are committed to strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and sharing with Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739700.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, the US Secretary of Commerce said that in the US-Taiwan tariff negotiations, the US seeks more than $300 billion in investment from Taiwan into the US and assistance in training US semiconductor workers, and its ultimate goal is to move Taiwan’s entire semiconductor supply chain to the United States. In response, netizens on the island criticized the DPP authorities as “beyond saving,” and public…","The Lai Ching-te authorities, in order to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” have submitted to the United States without bottom line. In tariff negotiations they have “kneeled before talks even began” and “offered the right cheek after being slapped on the left,” and they have even repeatedly deceived the public. In industry, they have let the United States take whatever it wants, proactively handing TSMC over and allowing it to drain the value of Taiwan’s advantageous industries. Earlier, TSMC was forced to announce an additional US$100 billion investment in the United States, which has already caused panic in the island’s industry and boiling public resentment. If this US$300 billion investment is implemented, it will inevitably have a huge impact on Taiwan’s economy, and Taiwan’s economic development momentum and autonomy will be further weakened. We are seriously concerned about this. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and far-sighted people from all sectors will unite and take action, resolutely oppose the Lai Ching-te authorities’ servile conduct toward the United States, and actively safeguard their own interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739699.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, while attending a forum on the island, Lai Ching-te falsely claimed that the name “Republic of China” helps unite people and is written into the “constitution,” which helps unite Taiwan's society, that Taiwan is already a “sovereign independent state” and there is no need to declare “Taiwan independence” again. He also said that in the face of future threats from the mainland, Taiwan must “unite the…","Lai Ching-te’s separatist fallacies once again expose his obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” position and his constant provocations to seek “independence,” stirring up opposition and confrontation. He is an unvarnished “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait,” a “creator of Taiwan Strait crises” and an “instigator of war.” Lai Ching-te’s countless perverse acts continue to tear Taiwan’s society apart, cause confusion over national identity and ethnic identity, seriously undermine cross-strait relations, and seriously harm the security and well-being of the island’s people. They are bound to be opposed and doomed to fail.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact, and an unchangeable status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te and his authorities can only let Taiwan enjoy peace and tranquility by abandoning the “Taiwan independence” position and returning to the correct track of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed, at a Taiwan military education mobilization training event, that “China continues to expand its ambition to annex Taiwan. Peace cannot be obtained by signing a single peace agreement, nor by submitting to the demands of the ‘aggressor.’ Even if reconciliation work is to be carried out, it must be backed by strong power.” What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and completing national reunification is the Chinese people's own affair, a just cause for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. So-called “aggression” and “annexation” are entirely false rhetoric used by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to deceive the public and mislead public opinion.\nLai Ching-te obstinately adheres to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and stubbornly persists on the evil path of provocation for “independence” and warmongering. He has vigorously hyped the so-called mainland “military threat,” incited “anti-China and resist-China,” and attempted to “seek independence by force” and “resist unification by force.” This will only push Taiwan into disaster and is entirely overestimating oneself and bringing about one's own destruction. No matter what the Lai Ching-te authorities say or do, they cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” being bound to fail, nor can they stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be unified and must be unified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Taiwan foreign affairs authorities recently said, “The Republic of China and the People’s Republic of China are not subordinate to each other,” and that after World War II, the Treaty of San Francisco replaced the Potsdam Proclamation and the Cairo Declaration, and that “the People’s Republic of China has never once ruled Taiwan, which is a historical fact.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","The so-called “San Francisco Peace Treaty” was a product of the United States rallying a very small number of countries to conclude a separate peace with Japan after World War II. This “treaty” violates the 1942 Declaration by United Nations, which stipulates that “each government signing the Declaration shall not make a separate armistice or peace with the enemies,” and also violates the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties, which stipulates that “a treaty does not create obligations or rights for a third State without its consent.” It has no authority to dispose of Taiwan’s sovereignty or of any sovereign rights and territory involving China, a non-signatory state. It is illegal and void and has no effect under international law. This is the solemn position the Chinese government has held from the very beginning, namely that it never recognizes the treaty.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. A series of international legal documents, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly and unequivocally confirm China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. The Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China replacing the “Government of the Republic of China” was a change of regime while the international legal person, China, remained unchanged. It did not change Taiwan’s status as part of China’s territory. The DPP authorities, relying on a void treaty, once again rehash the hackneyed claim of cross-strait “mutual non-subordination,” attempting to confuse the public and mislead opinion. They challenge the one-China principle recognized by the international community and completely ignore the facts. They will only humiliate themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739698.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi recently said that Japan's position of “understanding and respecting” China's statement in the 1972 Japan-China Joint Communiqué that “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People's Republic of China” has “not changed in the slightest”; she also said that Japan's basic position on the Taiwan issue is consistent with the Japan-China Joint Communiqué and has…","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already expressed its solemn position on this. I must emphasize again that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi openly made erroneous remarks about Taiwan in the Diet, brazenly interfering in China’s internal affairs. Faced with questions and criticism from China and the international community, Takaichi has merely brushed them off with “our position has not changed.” We cannot accept this. The Japanese side should earnestly reflect on this and immediately withdraw its erroneous remarks.\nOut of the evil nature of its pursuit of “independence,” Lai Ching-te has catered to Takaichi’s erroneous remarks and completely abandoned the national standpoint. His fawning toward Japan is contemptible and futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739697.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Reports say that the U.S. Congress recently released the latest text of the National Defense Authorization Act, which authorizes up to US$1 billion in military assistance to Taiwan for fiscal year 2026. It requires the U.S. Secretary of War to launch a joint unmanned systems development plan with Taiwan before March 2026, and to add plans for increasing opportunities for integrated U.S.-Taiwan coast guard…","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan region of China. Certain relevant US Congressional bills insisted on inserting negative Taiwan-related provisions, which seriously violate the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, crudely interfere in China’s internal affairs, and send serious wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the US side to abide by the solemn political commitments it made to China on the Taiwan question and to stop “arming Taiwan.” The DPP authorities’ “relying on the US to seek independence” cannot buy security and peace; it will only bring calamity to the present and will inevitably lead to their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The United States recently released its National Security Strategy report, which mentions Taiwan 8 times, including Taiwan's position in the semiconductor industry and its important strategic location, and claims that it “does not support any unilateral actions that change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait.” Lai Ching-te said that he thanks the US for making the containment of cross-Strait conflict a priority,…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is the Chinese people's own business and brooks no foreign interference. The DPP authorities stubbornly hold a separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to scheme for “independence” and provoke, which is the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, honor the solemn political commitments made by US leaders, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, stop condoning and supporting the separatist “Taiwan independence” forces in “seeking independence by force,” and stop sending any erroneous signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “relying on foreign forces to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251210_12739696.htm"],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Lai Ching-te recently said in an interview with The New York Times that he supports TSMC or the semiconductor industry going to the United States, Japan, and Europe to promote prosperity and progress in the world. Hsiao Bi-khim, in an interview with US media, said that TSMC's investment in building an ultra-large chip plant in the United States is of great significance: besides expanding Taiwan's global…","This once again proves that the Lai Ching-te authorities are a thoroughgoing “professional at selling out Taiwan” and a shameless “fraud ring.” Clearly, the precious assets accumulated through the hard work of several generations of Taiwan's people are being plundered and hollowed out, yet they dress it up as “promoting world prosperity and progress.” Clearly, the interests of the island's industries, enterprises, and people are being handed over and sacrificed, yet they still gloat about “contributing to U.S. manufacturing.” Such pandering to the United States, selling out Taiwan, and glossing over their faults is utterly shameless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that during Ma Ying-jeou's eight years in office he “locked the economy into the mainland,” and that he “has not seen any so-called peace dividend.” The Kuomintang criticized Lai for pushing Taiwan toward war after taking office, and for not forgetting to engage in “cognitive warfare.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","From 2008 to 2016, on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" the two sides across the Strait opened up a new situation of peaceful development, and compatriots on both sides were able to share in the fruits of development and well-being. The two sides' cross-Strait associations signed 23 agreements, resolving a series of issues directly concerning the vital interests of people on both sides of the Strait. Cross-Strait trade, investment, and industrial cooperation advanced deeply, and Taiwan's enterprises and people benefited from it. Cross-Strait personnel exchanges became more convenient, deepened the affection between compatriots on both sides, narrowed psychological distances, and safeguarded peace in the Taiwan Strait.\nSince Lai Ching-te took office, he has obstinately held to the secessionist \"Taiwan independence\" position, defied the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society, scheming to stir up \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, colluding with external forces to continually engage in provocations to seek independence, acting recklessly and going against the trend of history. This has led to tense and turbulent conditions in the Taiwan Strait, seriously harmed the vital interests of compatriots in Taiwan, and caused widespread resentment. No matter how Lai Ching-te twists black into white and talks nonsense, he cannot cover up the facts or deceive the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Recently, Wu Feng-shan, Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said when meeting with a delegation from the US National Committee on American Foreign Policy that the core of Lai Ching-te's cross-Strait policy is to replace confrontation with “dialogue of equality and dignity” and to replace encirclement with “healthy and orderly exchanges,” thereby promoting cross-Strait cooperation. What comment does the…","Lai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, distorts and denies the “1992 Consensus,” and maliciously obstructs and restricts cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. He is an out-and-out “peace wrecker,” “crisis maker,” and “war instigator.” His falsely claimed “equality and dignity” is in essence advocacy of a “new two-state theory,” attempting to change the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China.\nOur position on cross-strait dialogue and negotiation is consistent and clear. Only by abandoning “Taiwan independence” and acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, will cross-strait dialogue and communication have a basis of mutual trust, and will cross-strait relations be able to return to the track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","On December 6, maritime authorities conducted their first search and rescue emergency drill in the southern Taiwan Strait, followed by a fleet of vessels carrying out a special law enforcement operation in the central Taiwan Strait waters. Taiwan's coast guard authorities said that the mainland, under the guise of law enforcement, is in essence “harassing” Taiwan, and is confusing the location of the sea areas to…","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese territory, and China holds sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. The maritime administration authorities of the Ministry of Transport, in accordance with law, regularly conduct safety supervision and management of navigation, anchoring, operations, and other activities related to maritime traffic safety in the Taiwan Strait. The aim is to maintain the navigational environment and navigation order of these waters and to ensure that maritime transport is safe, orderly, and unobstructed. The DPP authorities, disregarding the fact and legal principle that Taiwan is part of China, constantly spread the separatist fallacy of “Taiwan independence” and attempt to split Taiwan away from China. Their conduct seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and will inevitably bring bitter consequences upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","Wang Hung-wei, a KMT-affiliated people’s representative, recently said that Ukraine, which is still fighting a war, has military spending accounting for 31% of its total expenditure, while Taiwan’s defense budget next year will account for 33% of the total budget, and that “Taiwan really seems to have a tendency toward becoming Ukraine.” May I ask what the spokesperson’s comment is?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and is fundamentally different from the Ukraine issue.\nWar is a catastrophe for civilization. According to statistics from the United Nations, the World Bank, and others, the Russia-Ukraine conflict has displaced more than 10 million Ukrainians. Large numbers of homes, hospitals, schools, energy facilities, and other infrastructure have been destroyed, economic activity and supply chains have been disrupted, unemployment has soared, inflation has been severe, and food supplies have fallen short. Ukrainian people are enduring the profound suffering of broken families and shattered lives.\nFor the sake of narrow party interests, the Lai Ching-te authorities are racing down the wrong path of seeking independence, provoking confrontation, and pursuing militarism. They plan to use more than 30 percent of Taiwan’s total budget for next year to “seek independence through force,” which will bind the Taiwan public to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and lead them into an abyss of disaster.\nWe hope that Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the extreme danger and harm of Lai Ching-te’s “Taiwan independence provocation,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and genuinely safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and their own security and well-being. We solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities: “Taiwan independence” means war. Attempting to “seek independence through force” is nothing but a mantis trying to stop a chariot, an overestimation of one’s own strength, and it will only dig their own grave!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Recently, a U.S. scholar said that Taiwan faces the mainland's “blockade risk,” and that the U.S. and Taiwan should consider strengthening energy resilience cooperation, with personnel from departments such as the Department of Energy and the Nuclear Regulatory Commission taking turns stationing in Taiwan, to ensure that Taiwan is not subjected to “armed coercion” and that its energy system is not sabotaged. May…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China, and firmly oppose anyone hyping up the “mainland threat” to create a pretext for interfering in the Taiwan question. The US should adhere to the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues with the utmost caution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently gave a detailed introduction to the rules for Taiwan compatriots applying for mainland identity documents. In response, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the operation of the single cross-Strait identity system is an important foundation for the order of personnel exchanges across the Strait, and that the mainland, in order to advance united front work, has indiscriminately…","Taiwan compatriots are our family and relatives. For many years, public security organs have always handled relevant mainland identity documents for eligible Taiwan compatriots in accordance with laws and regulations, in order to protect their legitimate rights. The DPP authorities have continuously set obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, and have obstructed and interfered with Taiwan compatriots applying for relevant mainland identity documents. This is unpopular, and it will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","It is reported that an elementary school in Taipei insists on singing the old version of its school anthem, whose lyrics include “becoming upright and proper Chinese,” and this has upset the Green camp. A DPP Taipei City councilor demanded that the matter be dealt with. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese nation; all are Chinese. School songs carry forward historical memory and cultural roots, and “be an upright Chinese” is the shared identity of compatriots on both sides. DPP politicians have abandoned the national standpoint and engaged in political manipulation, which is despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, a Caribbean country, recently held parliamentary elections in which the opposition New Democratic Party won, and the ruling party, which is closely tied to the DPP authorities, lost. This has sparked concern on the island about “diplomatic severance.” Please comment.","There is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. At present, 183 countries in the world have established diplomatic relations with China. Following the trend of history and the tide of the times is the right choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Taiwan's Liberty Times reported that General Secretary Xi Jinping may meet with Kuomintang Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun around the Lunar New Year; the meeting is said to be premised on the so-called “three tickets.” The Kuomintang has refuted the relevant reports as fabrications, reiterating that the KMT adheres to its cross-Strait line of “opposing Taiwan independence to avoid war, and upholding the…","On the first question: The Liberty Times has always been known for false reporting, and I believe everyone has become used to it. The relevant report is pure fabrication out of nothing, and the DPP and related green media are maliciously hyping and spreading rumors, with the aim of smearing and undermining normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, suppressing political dissidents, and gaining votes and political benefits. Their intentions are obvious to all, as the saying goes, “Everyone on the street knows Sima Zhao's ambition.”\nWe are willing, on the basis of the shared political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang and other political parties, groups, and people of insight on the island, consolidate and enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, respond to the wishes of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and work hand in hand toward the national rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nOn the second question: The DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest, have deliberately banned Xiaohongshu, brutally depriving Taiwan people, especially young people, of their right to know and their freedom to use social media platforms. This has seriously harmed the livelihoods of people on the island who earn a living through Xiaohongshu, and has already aroused strong dissatisfaction and opposition among Taiwan people, especially young people.\nWe welcome Taiwan compatriots to share the development opportunities of the mainland's internet, and we are pleased to see netizens on both sides of the Strait enhance mutual understanding and friendship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Hsiao Bi-khim recently gave an interview to US media discussing cross-Strait issues, aggressively hyping the mainland's “threat,” clinging closely to the United States, claiming that preventing conflict is a shared task for Taiwan and the US, that “Taiwan is a proactive partner,” and that supporting a strong Taiwan is part of maintaining peace, stability, and balance of power in the Indo-Pacific. May I ask what…","This is yet another clumsy performance by the DPP authorities in hyping up the “mainland threat” and clamoring to “seek independence by relying on outside forces,” which fully exposes their “Taiwan independence” nature as “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “manufacturers of Taiwan Strait crises.” No matter how the DPP authorities cling to external forces to seek “independence,” it is all in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Reportedly, in South Korea's electronic arrival card declaration system, Taiwan is labeled as \"China (Taiwan).\" The DPP authorities expressed concern and made representations, but have not received a direct response. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a broad consensus of the international community. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot shake the basic international pattern of adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","The Twin Cities Forum, currently the highest-level official exchange across the Taiwan Strait and often regarded by outside observers as an important indicator of cross-Strait atmosphere, was announced as postponed three days before its originally scheduled opening date this year. May I ask: if the Twin Cities Forum can be held in December this year, would that mean official cross-Strait channels are expected to…","The “Twin City Forum” is a city exchange platform between Shanghai and Taipei. The two cities have maintained communication about holding this year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum. We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including cross-Strait city exchanges, and hope that through more visits and exchanges we can continuously increase the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides and promote heart-to-heart understanding between them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","This year marks the 80th anniversary of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 80th anniversary of the restoration of Taiwan. At this special juncture in time, the Taiwanese anti-Japanese film “Seediq Bale” (Parts I and II) has announced it will be released in mainland cinemas on December 12 and 13. What is your comment on this?","This year, people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait have jointly commemorated the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance and of Taiwan’s restoration in various ways, remembering and honoring the deeds of martyrs and heroes, and expressing common national sentiment. Japan bears historical guilt toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question, and in the 50 years of colonial enslavement of Taiwan it committed towering crimes. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will remember history, honor the martyrs, defend the achievements, and create the future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Wang Yi, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs, recently said during talks with German Foreign Minister Wadephul in Beijing that Taiwan's status has been “locked in seven times,” which has drawn attention in cross-Strait public opinion. Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities responded, saying, “The Chinese side only speaks of what is advantageous to itself, and…","Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times. Its historical thread is clear, and its legal basis and facts are plain. Comrade Wang Yi gave a comprehensive, complete and clear account of this, which helps increase the international community's understanding of and adherence to the one-China principle.\nNo matter how the DPP authorities concoct stories or how many times they argue unreasonably, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. They cannot shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle, and they cannot stop the historical trend that China will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation recently held a “Taiwan Business Financial and Legal Advisors Meeting,” claiming that Taiwan businesses investing in the mainland should carefully evaluate production allocation and market diversification, and calling on Taiwan businesses to enhance their “awareness of risks of operating on the mainland.” What is your comment on this?","The founding purpose of Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation is “Chinese, well-intentioned, and service-oriented,” but now it is going against this purpose and has become the vanguard in inciting cross-Strait confrontation and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. Whether the mainland is suitable for investment and business is something Taiwanese businesspeople and enterprises have the greatest say in. Instead of putting effort into solving the island's economic and livelihood problems, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, unscrupulously cooperate with the US in hollowing out Taiwan's industries, and on the other hand, scheme to slander the mainland's business environment and undermine cross-Strait economic cooperation. They are the true “risk makers.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","U.S. President Trump recently signed the so-called “Taiwan Assurance Implementation Act.” The DPP authorities hyped it as “a big step forward in Taiwan-U.S. relations,” saying they will work more closely with the United States in all areas to jointly safeguard regional peace, stability and prosperity. What is your comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, and handle Taiwan-related issues with the utmost caution. In order to pursue the private interests of one party, the DPP authorities are willing to serve as pawns of external forces in “using Taiwan to contain China.” They are bringing Taiwan to a dangerous situation and undermining regional peace and stability. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end. Outsiders cannot be relied upon, and unification cannot be stopped. The DPP authorities' attempt to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: the spokesperson criticized the Democratic Progressive Party authorities for blocking Xiaohongshu under the pretext of “cybersecurity and fraud.” What is your view on the fact that mainland netizens also need to “climb over the wall” to use platforms such as Facebook? Second question: recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities said that the SEF had sent a letter to Xiaohongshu but…","Let me answer the second question first. As is widely known, because the DPP authorities refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle, the communication and dialogue mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation and Taiwan's Straits Exchange Foundation has long been suspended. The DPP authorities have arbitrarily and recklessly banned Xiaohongshu, which has drawn condemnation from Taiwan public opinion and strong opposition from the Taiwan public. I believe that if you were a user of Xiaohongshu, you would also oppose it.\nFirst question: The reasons the DPP authorities cited for banning Xiaohongshu are fundamentally unconvincing in Taiwan, and they have met with comprehensive opposition from all sectors of Taiwan society. The media and people from all walks of life have pointed out one after another that this brutal action deliberately targets a mainland social media platform and is a politically motivated manipulation with ulterior motives.\nWe support the lawful and compliant use of various social media platforms. We will also always adhere to a people-centered approach, strictly crack down on telecommunications fraud, online fraud, and other illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law, and actively safeguard the lives, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-10","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Media reports say that the Honduran presidential election completed 99% of the vote count on the 9th local time, and the two leading candidates both mentioned before the election their intention to restore “diplomatic relations” with Taiwan. What is your comment?","The one-China principle is a universal consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. The vast majority of countries in the world establish and develop diplomatic relations with China on the basis of the one-China principle. The remarks by relevant personnel in Honduras seriously violate the one-China principle and send a wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We urge the relevant personnel to immediately correct their mistake and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence. The DPP authorities' attempt to use this opportunity to pursue so-called “diplomatic breakthroughs” is a waste of effort and is doomed to fail.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251210_12739709.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-11","Guo Jiakun","China-Arab TV","It was reported that regarding the Taiwan-related remarks at the Diet, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi recently said that as Japan and China have various kinds of outstanding issues, it is all the more important to uphold the policy of reducing issues and enhancing understanding and cooperation. She also said Japan is open to dialogue at various levels with China. A few days ago Japan once again discharged…","Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have not only triggered strong outrage among the Chinese people, but also met with increasing opposition and criticism that is objective and reasonable in Japan. I’ve noted that the former editor-in-chief of Sekai Magazine and former president of Iwanami Shoten said Takaichi has repeatedly mentioned having “dialogues” with China, but meaningful dialogue must be based on mutual respect, equality and efforts to understand the other side. “Her current attitude does not meet the conditions for genuine dialogue.” These comments point to the essence of the issue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251211_11771129.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251211_11770955.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-11","Guo Jiakun","Nippon TV","Today, China’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs has urged the Chinese people to refrain from visiting Japan due to the earthquake. Is this part of the countermeasures against the Japanese Prime Minister’s remarks on “Taiwan contingency?”","On your question, the consular alert issued by China is very clear. Recently several earthquakes have hit Japan, causing injuries of many, tsunami has been observed in multiple places of Japan, and over 100,000 people have received instructions to evacuate. Relevant authorities of Japan have published notification saying there may be bigger earthquakes following this. With a sense of responsibility for Chinese nationals’ safety and health, the Chinese government has issued a timely consular alert. It is the duty of our diplomatic service to protect the safety of Chinese nationals overseas, and this is also how we serve the people through diplomacy.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251211_11771129.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251211_11770955.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-11","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On the 10th, Lai Ching-te, in an interview with the media, said that he opposes “unilateral actions” that use violence or coercion to change regional peace and stability, and that Taiwan will firmly maintain the status quo and strengthen its defense capabilities. On the same day, he also posted that “democracy is Taiwan's only direction,” and that Taiwan will join hands with like-minded…","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that Lai Ching-te is once again distorting right and wrong and spouting nonsense. He is again agitating for “seeking independence through force” and “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers,” and again hyping the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” attempting to deceive the Taiwan public and mislead international public opinion. Under the guise of “democracy” and “peace,” he is waging war recklessly and colluding with external forces to persistently seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. This once again exposes his obstinate “Taiwan independence” nature and his true face as a “destroyer of peace,” a “crisis creator,” and a “war instigator.”\nSince Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly upheld the “Taiwan independence” stance, widely propagated separatist fallacies, and continuously incited confrontation and hostility across the Taiwan Strait. For the sake of his own party and personal interests, he has squandered public funds on a large scale, pursuing “preparing for war to seek independence” and “arming the entire population,” and has pushed Taiwan into the perilous situation of war and danger, binding the public to the mad chariot of “Taiwan independence” separatism. On the island, he has implemented “authoritarian rule,” repeatedly trampled on democracy and impeded freedom, abused the judiciary to suppress and persecute political opponents, and continuously created “green terror” and a “chilling effect.” Lai Ching-te is filled with confrontational thinking, seriously violates public opinion on the island, and gravely undermines democracy and the rule of law. He is both the originator of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of social division and confrontation in Taiwan. He has no qualifications whatsoever to speak of “democracy” and “peace.”\nPeace is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and reunification is the only direction for Taiwan's future. The current struggle against “Taiwan independence” separatism is not a dispute over systems, but a struggle between reunification and separation, and a confrontation between justice and evil. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification, but we will leave no room whatsoever for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, proceeding from the great righteousness of the nation and their own security and well-being, will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist line, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and join us in safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and creating a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251211_12739961.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-12","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Youth Daily","Tomorrow marks the 12th National Memorial Day for Nanjing Massacre Victims. On the occasion of the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and amid the current tensions between China and Japan caused by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, how will China commemorate the day?","This year marks the 88th anniversary of the Nanjing Massacre. In accordance with the decision ratified by the National People’s Congress, China will host the annual national memorial commemoration for the victims of the Nanjing Massacre to honor those who lost their lives.\nThe massacre in Nanjing is a horrendous crime committed by Japanese militarists. There is no room for denial. The slaughter of 300,000 Chinese people forms the darkest page in human history. Japanese militarists’ war of aggression against China and other Asian countries under the pretext of the so-called “survival-threatening situation” and untold crimes against humanity are nothing but a disgrace in the history of human civilization.\nInternational legal instruments, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, clearly stated the opposition against aggression, the punishment of war criminals and the elimination of militarism. The International Military Tribunal for the Far East was established by the Allied Nations for the trial of Japanese war criminals. However, the Japanese government has long abetted the right-wing forces’ retrogressive moves. Several prime ministers and political dignitaries have paid tribute to the Yasukuni Shrine, where class-A war criminals are honored. Some politicians have publicly called into question the Murayama Statement which showed reflection on and apologies for Japan’s colonial rule and aggression. The Japanese side even attempted to whitewash its war crimes and change the verdict on its history of aggression by revising textbooks more than once. Those egregious moves constitute a blatant challenge to the post-war international order and an affront to human conscience. This triggered strong indignation and vigilance in the international community.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War as well as China’s recovery of Taiwan. Eighty years ago, the Chinese people, after heroic and strenuous fighting, defeated Japanese militarism, recovered the territories, including Taiwan, stolen by Japanese aggressors, defended national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and upheld international fairness and justice. Eighty years on, the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable. China will never allow Japan’s right-wing forces to turn back the wheel of history, never allow external forces to lay their hands on China’s Taiwan region, and never allow the resurgence of Japan’s militarism. Japanese militarism is the enemy of people worldwide. China will work with all peace-loving countries and people to jointly safeguard the outcomes of World War II victory and the post-war international order. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect on and learn from history, make a clean break with militarism, and take concrete actions to get rid of the specter of militarism that still haunts it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251212_11771774.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251212_11771726.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-12","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","The Japanese government has been recently refusing to explicitly reiterate Taiwan-related statement set forth in the four political documents between China and Japan and has kept dodging the issue by repeating that its position “remains unchanged.” At the same time, the DPP authorities echoed Japan’s erroneous remarks and deeds by lifting import restrictions on Japanese seafood and sending groups to visit Japan…","Over the 50-year occupation and colonial rule, Japan has committed innumerable crimes in Taiwan. Hundreds of thousands of our Taiwan compatriots were murdered by the Japanese military, accounting for about one-fifth of the population at that time. Under Japan’s massive economic plundering and spiritual enslavement, 70 percent of Taiwan’s land was occupied, and natural resources, including coal and gold mines, were destructively exploited. Over half of the rice produced in Taiwan was shipped to Japan, while the local people were starved to death. Many Taiwanese were used as forced laborers, among whom 40 percent died. Around 200,000 young Taiwanese were forced to serve in the Japanese military and tens of thousands of them died as the “cannon fodder” of Japanese militarism. More than 2,000 Taiwanese girls and women were forced to become “comfort women.” The Taiwanese, who were slaves living on a conquered island, had no political rights, freedom of belief or cultural freedom.\nThe DPP authorities have turned a blind eye to the countless tragedies and evidence, and instead blatantly glossed over Japan’s colonial rule by using the term “end of the war” to fudge historical facts and avoid mentioning “the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression” or “Taiwan’s recovery.” The DPP authorities have whitewashed Japan’s colonial rule and oppression on Taiwan as “development” and “contribution,” turning its back on the Chinese nation, selling Taiwan out to ingratiate with Japan, and serving as the accomplices and pawns of Japanese militarism.\nAs we mark the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, the Japanese leader once again cited “survival-threatening situation” regarding the Taiwan question. It amounts to a challenge to human conscience and international justice, and has undoubtedly met with strong outrage from the Chinese people and the international community. What awaits the “Taiwan independence” separatists who have betrayed their ancestors is contempt from the people and the judgment of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251212_11771774.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251212_11771726.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-12","Guo Jiakun","The following question was raised after the press conference","Japanese Defense Minister Shinjiro Koizumi spoke with the U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth over the phone. Both sides expressed “serious concern” over the “radar illumination” incident, saying that China’s actions “increase regional tensions.” What is China’s response?","We’ve responded to this issue more than once. The facts are very clear. The Japanese side’s wishful, contradictory and self-deceiving remarks lay bare its real intention of creating tensions and spreading disinformation. We urge the Japanese side to face up to the crux of the current difficulties in China-Japan relations, earnestly reflect on and correct its wrongdoing, and retract Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, rather than diverting attention and creating more troubles.\nWe hope the international community will tell right from wrong and not be deceived by the Japanese side. Japan’s allies, in particular, need to see clearly the Japanese side’s intentions and avoid being misled by it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251212_11771774.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251212_11771726.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-15","Guo Jiakun","Kyodo News","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced today countermeasures against Shigeru Iwasaki, former senior official of Japan’s Self-Defense Forces. What’s the reasons behind this move?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and is the red line that must not be crossed. China firmly opposes Shigeru Iwasaki, the former chief of the Joint Staff of Japan’s Self-Defense Forces, taking the post of so-called “political consultant” of the Taiwan authorities. We have protested to the Japanese side more than once and took countermeasures against Iwasaki. Rather than reflect on and correct his wrongdoings, Iwasaki went down the wrong path by colluding with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and making provocations. This amounts to a severe violation of the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, a blatant interference in China’s internal affairs, and a grave infringement on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity. In response to his egregious moves, China, in accordance with the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law, announced in the decree of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs countermeasures against Shigeru Iwasaki for his collusion with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and provocations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251215_11773003.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251215_11772954.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-12-15","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It was reported the Japanese side backtracked on what they previously said about the flight training of Chinese carrier-based aircraft, claiming that they received the Chinese side's notification beforehand, but didn't get sufficient information on the specifics, including the training duration and area, to avoid accidents. What's your comment?","The facts of the incident are clear and the evidence is irrefutable. The Japanese side has no ground to defend or deny its wrongdoing. On December 6, PLANS 101 of the naval task group led by PLANS Liaoning notified the Japanese side that the task group would conduct carrier-based aircraft flight training, with Japanese Ship (JS) 116 confirming receipt of the message. Later on, PLANS 101 again notified the Japanese side that the training was expected to start from 1500 and last for about 6 hours, mainly to the south of the carrier, with JS 116 again confirming receipt of the message. Against this backdrop, Japanese fighter jets still intruded into the training zone multiple times to harass the Chinese side. Therefore, the Japanese side shall bear all the responsibility on endangering flight safety.\nThe Japanese side has once again lied to its own people and misled the international community by hyping up a regular military training of the Chinese side as a so-called security threat and portraying itself, the real provoker, as a victim. We therefore are entitled to ask the following questions: Is this an attempt by the Japanese side to divert attention from the severe consequences sparked by the erroneous remarks on Taiwan made by Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi? Is the Japanese side trying to use this incident to create excuses to break away from the post-war system, to loosen restrictions on its military development, and to revive the spectre of its militarist past? We strongly urge the Japanese side to squarely face up to the crux of the current difficulty in China-Japan relations, and earnestly reflect on and rectify its wrongdoings. Those despicable moves and political manipulation to evade the real issue, to divert attention, or to recriminate will never work.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251215-prc-mndb01.htm","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/12/15/11464974.shtml",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-15","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the US has recently released a new version of its\nNational Security Strategy\n, stating that it does not support any unilateral changes to the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The\nNational Defense Authorization Act\napproved by the US House of Representatives also contains a number of negative provisions related to Taiwan. In addition, at the Reagan National Defense Forum, the US Secretary…","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is part of China.This is an undeniable fact based on historic and jurisprudential evidences and it is the true status quo of the Taiwan Strait that should not be changed. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese, which brooks no external interference. Any attempt to contain China with Taiwan will be futile. The US side should earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US Joint Communiqués, stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and stop fueling tensions across the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the US will recalibrate its strategic perception of China, work with China towards the same direction, stay committed to the principle of non-conflict and non-confrontation, and foster a stable and positive military-to-military relationship featuring equality, mutual respect, and peaceful coexistence. This will inject greater certainty and positive factors into the China-US relations and world peace and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251215-prc-mndb01.htm","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/12/15/11464974.shtml",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-15","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It was reported that Lai Ching-te recently said the PLA would possess the capability to seize Taiwan by 2027, so Taiwan must be fully prepared for the worst possible scenarios, continue to strengthen its self-defense capabilities, safeguard regional peace, and deter wars by enhancing readiness. Please comment on that.","Lai Ching-te has repeatedly hyped up the so-called military threat from the mainland, deliberately escalating cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism. His so-called preparations are nothing but peddling war anxiety in all kinds of ways and creating excuses for his erroneous policy of provoking war through \"Taiwan independence\" schemes. The Lai Ching-te authorities' separatist provocations are the most malignant tumor harming and destroying Taiwan. Reunification across the Strait is the best choice to ensure Taiwan's lasting peace and stability. We hope our Taiwan compatriots see through the extreme danger and grave harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' reckless attempts to seek independence by enhancing readiness, and resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, thereby ensuring peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as their security and well-being.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251215-prc-mndb01.htm","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/12/15/11464974.shtml",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-12-16","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","On December 15, Japan’s Foreign Minister Toshimitsu Motegi during a session at the House of Councillors made a statement regarding the Taiwan question that the Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi insisted that the…","We noted the remarks. The Japanese foreign minister yesterday repeated some of the clauses regarding the Taiwan question stated in the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement—“Article 3 of the document states that the Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” But we also noted that the Japanese side did not reiterate the important clause of the document which states “the Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China” and “Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China.” We also noted that the Japanese side when citing the Cairo Declaration only mentioned “Manchuria, Formosa, and The Pescadores” and deliberately sidestepped the important information that they are “territories Japan has stolen from the Chinese.” The Japanese side also juxtaposed the Sino-Japanese Joint Statement and the so-called Treaty of San Francisco, violating the commitments it has made and principles in international law, attempting to rehash the fallacy that Taiwan’s status is “undetermined” and interfering in China’s domestic affairs. Judging from those latest statements, the Japanese side apparently continues to equivocate and plant misperceptions on critical issues, hoping they could mislead public opinion and somehow get past the issue. China firmly opposes it.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi last week made an authoritative and detailed statement that Taiwan’s status as Chinese territory has been affirmed by seven historical and legal facts. The major content is as follows: The 1943 Cairo Declaration stated clearly that all the territories Japan had stolen from China, such as Taiwan, must be restored to China. The 1945 Potsdam Proclamation stipulated that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. On August 15, 1945, with Japan’s defeat in the war, the Japanese Emperor undertook to carry out the provisions of the Potsdam Proclamation in good faith and announced Japan’s unconditional surrender. On October 25, 1945, the Chinese government announced that it would resume the exercise of sovereignty over Taiwan. On October 1, 1949, the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China replaced the government of the Republic of China, became the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and thus began to exercise sovereignty over all of China’s territory, including Taiwan. The 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement provided clear provisions on the Taiwan question. The 1978 Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, ratified by the two countries’ legislatures, affirmed that the principles set out in the 1972 Joint Statement should be strictly observed.\nI must point out the following facts. In September 1972, during the negotiations on the normalization of diplomatic relations between China and Japan, the then Treaty Bureau Chief of Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs Takashima Masuo clearly stated the position of the Japanese government by saying that “It is Japan’s consistent position that Taiwan should be restored to China.” In November 1972 after the normalization of diplomatic relations between China and Japan, the then Japanese Prime Minister Kakuei Tanaka and Foreign Minister Masayoshi Ōhira at the Diet session openly stated that “Disputes between the Chinese mainland and Taiwan are China’s internal affairs” and “Opposition between the People’s Republic of China and Taiwan is a domestic matter of China.” In February 1975, the then Foreign Minister Kiichi Miyazawa at the Diet said “Cross-Strait conflict should be regarded as a civil war in legal terms.” Besides, in 1998 the Chinese and Japanese governments issued the China-Japan Joint Declaration on Building a Partnership of Friendship and Cooperation for Peace and Development, which includes a very important statement—“The Japanese side continues to maintain its stand on the Taiwan issue which was set forth in the Joint Communiqué of the Government of Japan and the Government of the People’s Republic of China and reiterates its understanding that there is one China.”\nLet me stress that this year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. It is also the 80th anniversary of the recovery of Taiwan. Japan once invaded and exercised colonial rule over Taiwan for 50 years, committed innumerable crimes and bears historical responsibilities on the Taiwan question. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and Japan is in no position to make any interference.\nWe once again urge the Japanese side to abide by the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, earnestly do soul-searching and correct its wrongdoings and retract the erroneous remarks made by Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251216_11774382.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251216_11774310.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-16","Guo Jiakun","China-Arab TV","Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s recent visit to the United Arab Emirates (UAE), Saudi Arabia and Jordan is at a critical stage of the preparation for the second China-Arab States Summit in 2026. What are the outcomes and significance of this visit? Could you offer more information on the preparation for the second China-Arab States Summit?","Foreign Minister Wang Yi’s visit to the UAE, Saudi Arabia and Jordan was a full success. During the visit, a series of new consensus and new outcomes were achieved on implementing the important common understandings reached by President Xi Jinping and the leaders of the three countries and promoting bilateral relations between China and the three countries and China-Arab States cooperation.\nThis visit further enhances political mutual trust between China and Arab States. Foreign Minister Wang Yi stated that China always stands together with the Global South and small and medium-sized countries. China firmly safeguards the common interests of developing countries, supports the three countries in upholding strategic autonomy and pursuing the paths suited to their respective national conditions. China is always the most trustworthy strategic partner of the three countries. The three countries reaffirmed their commitments to the one-China principle and reiterated that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The three countries expressed support to China for making the second China-Arab States Summit a success.\nThis visit further promotes China-Arab States cooperation in various fields. Both sides agreed to further align our development strategies, deepen cooperation in traditional fields, expand cooperation in emerging and future industries, enrich our partnerships and bring more benefits to the peoples.\nThis visit further deepens China-Arab States coordination on all fronts. The three countries spoke highly of and expressed support for the four major global initiatives proposed by President Xi Jinping and commended China’s fair and just position on the Palestinian question and other issues. Both sides agreed to strengthen solidarity and collaboration, jointly safeguard regional peace and stability, and together promote global multipolarity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251216_11774382.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251216_11774310.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-16","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Daily","It’s reported that the head of Taiwan’s “foreign affairs department” Lin Chia-lung when asked about how to maintain friendly ties with Honduras in the competition with the Chinese mainland said that Taiwan builds a relationship of trust and prosperity. What’s China’s comment?","The Taiwan authorities’ “dollar diplomacy” under the disguise of “trust” and “prosperity” cannot cover up their inclination to use any means possible to advance the “Taiwan independence” agenda, nor can it deceive public opinion and the people in Taiwan. The “Taiwan independence” forces and the DPP authorities go in the opposite direction of where the arc of history bends, and their attempts are doomed to fail.\nSince the establishment of China-Honduras diplomatic relations, the two countries reaped fruitful cooperation outcomes in various fields, the long-term development capability of Honduras has been effectively boosted, and the two countries and two peoples benefited greatly. Facts fully prove that upholding the one-China principle is the right choice that accords with the trend of history and our times, and serves the fundamental interests of relevant countries and their peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251216_11774382.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251216_11774310.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-17","Guo Jiakun","Phoenix TV","It’s reported that head of Japan’s National Security Secretariat Ichikawa Keiichi articulated Japan’s position on Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan and refuted China’s statements during his recent conversations with officials from the UK, France, Germany and Canada. He said Takaichi’s remarks at the Diet didn’t change the Japanese side’s consistent position on Taiwan. Some in Japan claimed that…","What the Japanese side said and did is yet another example of how some in Japan knowingly distort facts, refuse to correct their wrongdoings, and attempt to feign innocence for sympathy in the international community.\nIt’s not the first time that the right-wing forces in Japan have concocted false narratives. They depicted Japan’s war of aggression against Asian neighbors as “the liberation of Asia,” downplayed the horrendous Nanjing Massacre as “the Nanjing incident,” whitewashed the infamous Unit 731 as a “public health research unit,” and dismissed forced labor and “comfort women” as “voluntary acts.” After the war, Japan has described itself as a “victim” of the war while avoiding mentioning that militarism is the source of the warfare. It claims to uphold the exclusively defense-oriented principle and the passive defense strategy, but has removed the ban on exercising the right to collective self-defense, kept relaxing restrictions on arms exports, and even attempted to revise its three non-nuclear principles.\nPrime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have been met with the Chinese people’s indignation as well as opposition and criticism from Japan and some other countries. What the Japanese side should do is to listen to these calls and do soul-searching rather than make futile attempts to persuade other countries into believing their groundless explanations. We urge some in Japan to stop spreading false narratives, face up to the history, reflect on and correct the wrongdoings, retract the erroneous remarks, honor the commitments, and act responsibly to offer China and the international community a satisfactory answer.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251217_11775178.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251217_11775184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-17","Guo Jiakun","Nippon TV","After Japanese Prime Minister’s remarks on Taiwan, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs held meetings with ambassadors from Southeast Asian countries and others based in Beijing to convey criticism on Japan and ask them to support China’s position. Could you share with us the purpose of this action?","China’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs maintains normal working relations with embassies of all countries in Beijing.\nThe one-China principle is a universally recognized basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus of the international community including Southeast Asian countries. The erroneous remarks on Taiwan made by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi seriously violate international law and basic norms governing international relations, and blatantly challenge the outcomes of WWII victory and international justice. The dangerous trend of reviving Japanese militarism has put regional countries and peoples on high alert. Defending the postwar international order, human conscience and justice serves the common interest of all sides and is a must choice. We noted that recently many regional countries have once again stressed their commitment to the one-China principle, opposition to “Taiwan independence,” support for China’s reunification, as well as their vigilance and resistance to the possible revival of militarism. The Japanese side needs to heed the calls, do soul-searching and correct its wrongdoings, instead of creating confusion and trouble.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251217_11775178.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251217_11775184.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 17, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing room. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Good morning everyone, welcome to today's press conference. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The 2025 Central Economic Work Conference was held in Beijing from December 10 to 11, and Taiwan businesses and compatriots are following it closely. How should the spirit of the Central Economic Work Conference be implemented to promote the development of Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland?","At the important historical juncture when the 14th Five-Year Plan is about to conclude successfully and the 15th Five-Year Plan is about to begin, the Central Economic Work Conference was held in Beijing from December 10 to 11. General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the conference, summarizing economic work in 2025, analyzing the current economic situation, and arranging economic work for 2026, providing scientific guidance for ensuring a good start and a strong beginning for the 15th Five-Year Plan.\nBuilding on an in-depth summary of this year’s economic work and an accurate assessment of next year’s development situation, the conference pointed out the policy orientation of “seeking progress while maintaining stability, and improving quality and efficiency” for next year’s economic work. The conference stated, “We must fully tap economic potential, we must pursue policy support and reform and innovation in parallel, we must achieve both ‘flexibility in letting go’ and ‘good management,’ we must closely combine investment in material goods with investment in people, and we must strengthen our own capabilities to meet external challenges.” It clarified the key tasks for next year’s economic work and provided fundamental guidance for doing well in next year’s economic work.\nThe conference provides stable expectations, innovative momentum and important opportunities for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech, the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee, and the Central Economic Work Conference. We will continuously improve policies and institutions that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and help Taiwan compatriot businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises seize development opportunities in the 15th Five-Year Plan period, and continuously support them in integrating into the new development pattern and participating in high-quality development. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will see the big picture clearly, strengthen their confidence, seize opportunities, put down roots on the mainland, stay proactive and enterprising, share the bright prospects of Chinese-style modernization, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740876.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 2025 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting was held in Nanjing over the past two days. Please spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","The 2025 Annual Meeting of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit was held in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province, from December 16 to 17. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the opening ceremony, delivered a speech, and met with entrepreneur representatives from both sides of the Strait. Chairman Wang Huning pointed out that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, the economies of both sides belong to the Chinese nation's economy, and when the nation prospers and the country grows strong, compatriots on both sides will fare better. During the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, the cause of Chinese-style modernization will open up a brand-new situation and continue to write a new chapter in the two miracles of rapid economic development and long-term social stability. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will seize the opportunities of the times and jointly create long-lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.\nAbout 800 people, including council members and members of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Council, entrepreneurs from both sides of the Strait, and relevant experts and scholars, attended the annual meeting. Centering on the theme of “Focusing on Transformation and Innovation, Deepening Multi-chain Cooperation,” they engaged in in-depth exchanges and discussions on topics such as how Taiwan-funded businesses can seize the opportunities of the 15th Five-Year Plan's formulation and implementation, accelerate integration into the new development landscape, take part in high-quality development, and deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. Taiwanese business representatives at the meeting expressed one after another that they are full of confidence in the mainland's development and will continue to actively take part in cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740875.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台华语环球节目中心《中国新闻》记者","The DPP authorities plan to amend the “Measures for Taiwan Region Civil Servants and Persons of Specific Status Entering the Mainland Area.” The amendment stipulates that heads of local counties and cities, some civil servants, and other personnel applying to visit relatives on the mainland or attend the funerals of relatives will have the scope of eligible kin changed from within the fourth degree to within the…","This is yet another vicious act by the DPP authorities to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and visits. The DPP authorities have racked their brains to obstruct and restrict Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, and they have fabricated charges to suppress and persecute groups and individuals on the island that actively take part in cross-Strait exchanges, trying to block cross-Strait compatriots from getting closer to each other. This abuse of power will surely be rejected by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740869.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","On December 18, the Hainan Free Trade Port will officially launch island-wide customs closure operations. This is a landmark measure of the mainland’s unwavering expansion of high-level opening to the outside world and its promotion of an open world economy, and it has drawn high attention from Taiwan businesses. What opportunities and benefits will it bring to Taiwan businesses?","Starting December 18, 2025, the Hainan Free Trade Port will officially launch full-island customs closure operations. This is a landmark measure by the mainland to steadfastly expand high-level opening to the outside world and promote the building of an open world economy.\nAfter the customs closure, the Hainan Free Trade Port will fully implement a special regulatory model of “open at the first line, control at the second line, and free within the island,” and the tax preferential policies centered on “zero tariffs, low tax rates, and a simplified tax system” will fully release their dividends. These will both reduce enterprises' production costs and strengthen development vitality, and will improve the quality of consumer supply and build an international tourism consumption center. At the same time, trade management will become more relaxed and convenient, and regulatory models will become more precise and efficient. A series of innovative measures involving trade liberalization, investment facilitation, financial opening, and other aspects will bring more opportunities and benefits to Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises. Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises can rely on the institutional opening advantages of the free trade port to expand new space and achieve new development in Hainan, better integrate into the national new development pattern, and share in the new development opportunities of the free trade port.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740870.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the 2025 Cross-Strait Annual Chinese Character was announced in Taipei. Netizens from home and abroad enthusiastically participated, with a total of over 15.82 million votes cast. The character “勢” (shì) was elected as the 2025 Cross-Strait Annual Chinese Character with over 1.28 million votes. What comments do you have on this?","The character “势” (shì, meaning momentum or trend), chosen by a high vote of netizens at home and abroad, was selected as the Cross-Strait Chinese Character of the Year. It demonstrates that netizens, especially compatriots on both sides of the Strait, share a common perception of the pulse of the times, and it signals that the historical trend toward national reunification and national rejuvenation is surging forward, irresistible.\nThe selection of “势” is a footnote that the compatriots on both sides of the Strait have written, in the most plain manner, to the process of national reunification in the new era: unification is the righteous trend of history, and it will inevitably converge into an unstoppable torrent of the times. Looking at the historical law of “the general trend,” resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all sons and daughters of the Chinese nation, and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. More and more Taiwan compatriots, upholding the great righteousness of the nation, are taking the initiative to take part in the great cause of national rejuvenation, using their actions to write “Cross-Strait families are one.” Looking at the people’s hearts, which are “irresistible,” more and more Taiwan compatriots see clearly the truth that “Taiwan independence” forces bring disaster and harm to Taiwan, and they firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist actions and external interference, safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Looking at the mission of “acting in accordance with the trend,” we continuously deepen cross-Strait economic and social integrated development, continuously introduce policy measures that benefit Taiwan and its people, and push cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation toward greater depth and substance. We let Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises share development opportunities, enhance the spiritual affinity of compatriots, and build a firmer foundation, more conditions, and greater momentum for advancing the reunification of the motherland.\nAs Taiwan compatriots have said: choosing “势” is choosing hope, choosing the future! This hope is the fervent desire to “ride the momentum upward” and jointly realize the Chinese Dream. This future is the vision of “gathering momentum into a tide” to jointly promote unification. We will unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, walk together with one heart, grasp the historical trend, increase interests and well-being through exchanges and cooperation, strengthen spiritual affinity through integrated development, and join hands to gather the mighty momentum driving national reunification and national rejuvenation, jointly opening a vast prospect for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740872.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","As the end of the year approaches, cross-Strait exchange activities continue to be full of highlights. Here are several of them.\nFrom December 5 to 15, the 3rd Cross-Strait Food Carnival was held in Shaxian, Sanming, Fujian. During the event, more than 10 featured exchange activities were carried out, including the Cross-Strait Food Exhibition, a cooking skills exchange competition, and a “Intangible Cultural Heritage Snack Show · Tasting Shaxian Flavors Together” food culture exchange experience, attracting nearly 800 participants from both sides of the Strait. The event set up 278 food sales booths, gathering nearly 500 kinds of characteristic snacks and foods from both sides of the Strait, and received a cumulative total of over 800,000 visitor trips, achieving two-way impetus for cross-Strait food culture exchange and industrial empowerment.\nOn December 12, the opening ceremony of the 3rd “Cross-Strait Zhen Youth, Hand in Hand Toward the Future” — Cross-Strait Exchange and Integration Series Activities and the 6th Cross-Strait Student Baseball League Finals was held in Shenzhen. More than 1,000 people from all walks of life and young people from both sides of the Strait attended. Among them, the Cross-Strait Student Baseball League Finals drew 20 teams from the island, with more than 500 athletes, coaches and referees competing.\nIn addition, we would also like to recommend to people on both sides of the Strait a reference work that systematically introduces Taiwan's history: 《台湾百科全书·历史》 (Encyclopedia of Taiwan · History). The book was published by China Encyclopedia Publishing House. It contains 1,369 entries totaling 960,000 characters. The entries cover from prehistoric culture to the mid-20th century, summarizing major events, important phenomena, representative figures and related works in Taiwan's history. Using detailed historical materials, it clarifies the historical facts that Taiwan has belonged to China since ancient times and that compatriots on both sides are of the same blood and share the same cultural origins. We welcome everyone to pay attention to this authoritative and serious historical book.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","On the 10th, the third “China’s Policy Paper on Latin America and the Caribbean” was released. The document reiterates that the one-China principle is an important political foundation and prerequisite for China’s development of relations with all countries. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities falsely claimed, “This document attempts to distort right and wrong and mislead the international community.” What is…","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. Adhering to the one-China principle is just and in line with the trend of history. “Taiwan independence” is a reversal of history and will ultimately be crushed by the irresistible tide of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Some Taiwanese performers have been labeled “pro-China entertainers” for expressing their identity. The head of Taiwan's culture department said that “pro-China” is a false issue, that they welcome Taiwanese entertainers developing careers on the mainland, but that they cannot cooperate by making “armed unification” statements. We note that in recent years, not only have Taiwanese entertainers come to the…","The DPP authorities, under the pretext of so-called “investigation,” have threatened and intimidated Taiwan performing artists. This is completely unpopular and cannot stop the momentum of Taiwan people participating in cross-Strait exchanges and sharing in the development opportunities of the mainland. For many years, generations of Taiwan performing artists have passed on and promoted Chinese culture, actively participated in cross-Strait cultural exchanges and cooperation, and used practical actions to illustrate “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” In the past two years, the mainland’s performance market has shown explosive growth. In the third quarter of this year alone, more than 1,000 concerts were held, with over 12 million audience members, and Taiwan performing artists held more than 100 solo concerts on the mainland. The mainland has provided a broad stage for Taiwan performing artists, and their participation has also enriched the mainland’s performance market. The “mutual pursuit” between the two sides in the fields of culture and the arts has promoted cross-Strait cultural exchanges.\nIn addition, traveling to one city for a single song and following concerts to tour the mainland has become a new lifestyle trend for many Taiwan compatriots. We actively support cross-Strait cooperation and exchanges in film, television, music, and other fields. We welcome Taiwan performing artists to come to the mainland to take part in various cultural performance activities, and we also welcome Taiwan compatriots to make use of increasingly convenient policies to come to the mainland at any time to watch various cultural performances and experience the vibrant cultural tourism life on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740868.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently recommended a noodle shop run by a mainland spouse, saying “Taiwan is a diverse and open society.” Island public opinion criticized Lai for cheap theatrics, arguing that he is trying to use eating a bowl of noodles to cover up his violations of human rights and discrimination against a specific group. What is your comment?","Cross-Strait marriages and families are the most vivid and direct embodiment of “cross-Strait being one family,” and they deserve the best blessings and the most considerate care. Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has obstinately clung to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, regarding the mainland spouse community as a thorn in the eye and a bone in the throat. He has abused various means to deprive them of their legitimate rights and has done everything possible to oppress and persecute them, seriously disrupting the peaceful lives of cross-Strait marriages and families. While disregarding human decency and bullying and persecuting the mainland spouse community on the island, Lai puts on an act to create a false image. It is pure showmanship, utterly hypocritical, and cannot fool compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan's defense authority recently said, “If the mainland announces that it will carry out composite military operations around the Taiwan Strait, it will raise the readiness level in response to the threat and conduct immediate combat-readiness drills to prevent a shift from exercise to real war; if the enemy launches a sudden attack, all units will implement distributed control without waiting for orders, and…","The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the root cause of disruption to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that “seeking independence by force” is like a mayfly trying to shake a tree—it is overestimating oneself, and it will only lead to self-destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently proposed a special budget of US$40 billion for purchasing arms from the United States. The New York Times recently exposed some details of a classified US Department of Defense report, pointing out that mainland China already has sufficient missile forces to destroy advanced US weapons before they can be deployed to defend Taiwan, meaning the US has lost its ability to “defend Taiwan.” What…","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves and brooks no foreign interference. The Lai Ching-te authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests, keep seeking “independence” and provoking, continuously raise defense budgets, vigorously push “the whole people as soldiers,” and bind Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot. They attempt to “seek independence by relying on outside forces” and “seek independence through armed force,” which poses a threat to the security and interests of Taiwan residents. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, outsiders are unreliable, and unification cannot be stopped. We have firm will, strong determination, and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, to firmly oppose interference by external forces, and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740866.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Taiwan media reported that after the DPP authorities introduced the \"group travel ban\" restricting travel to the mainland, the ways in which island residents sightsee on the mainland have become more diverse. In 2025, the number of cross-Strait sightseeing travelers differed by nearly 3.8 million person-times, and the sightseeing deficit was NT$152 billion. Some island scholars say that cross-Strait group travel…","The mainland has consistently upheld the concept that \"cross-Strait compatriots are one family\" and has actively promoted the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the regularization of exchanges in all fields, including tourism. The goodwill and sincerity it has shown are plain for all to see. Recently, guided by the principles of \"great opening, greatest convenience, and greater safety,\" we increased the number of ports that can issue a one-time valid Taiwan compatriot permit to 100, creating convenient conditions and providing quality services for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland.\nThe crux and obstacle of cross-Strait tourism issues lies with the DPP authorities' interference and obstruction. The fundamental reason is that they deliberately interfere with and undermine personnel exchanges and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait in all fields in order to seek \"independence.\" Their disregard for the hopes and interests of Taiwan's tourism industry and public has already provoked strong dissatisfaction and opposition from all sectors of the island and has become increasingly unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","According to reports, the DPP authorities will cooperate with temples across Taiwan to hold 16 so-called “Taiwan All-People Security Guidance” briefings. On the 9th, at the first event held at Keelung's Qing'an Temple, the organizers claimed that the mainland is a “bad neighbor,” loudly played up the mainland's “military threat,” and incited “resisting China and protecting Taiwan.” This has prompted public…","This is a profanation of religious belief. The DPP authorities have repeatedly intimidated and suppressed island figures who take part in cross-Strait exchange activities on religion and folk beliefs. They have even slandered Mazu and Guan Gong as “united front tools.” Now they are turning temples that were once pure and peaceful into “ammunition depots” for storing weapons and places for agitating for war, and using them as tools to deceive votes, create hatred, and promote the fallacies of “Taiwan independence.” There is a folk saying, “People are doing it, and heaven is watching.” The vile conduct of DPP politicians has already been strongly questioned by public opinion on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Taipei City Councilor Miao Po-ya recently claimed that even in a state of war, Taiwan could maintain normal life like Ukraine, with work, school, and businesses all operating as usual. This caused an uproar in public opinion, and netizens on the island harshly criticized her for “glorifying war.” What comments do you have on this?","Green camp politicians turned a blind eye to the suffering that war brings to the people, and even put forward cold-blooded remarks glorifying war. They are utterly inhumane and have been condemned by all sectors and public opinion on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","The DPP authorities, citing an “emergency on fraud crime prevention,” have tentatively “banned” Xiaohongshu for one year. This has been questioned as “illegal expansion of power” and has triggered strong backlash on the island. The island’s internal affairs authority and the Mainland Affairs Council said that this is “a general emergency measure necessary in accordance with law,” unrelated to cross-Strait policy…","The DPP authorities’ defense is rather flimsy and weak. According to media reports on the island, there were nearly 60,000 fraud cases involving Facebook on the island last year, and this year the number has already exceeded 30,000, far more than the number of so-called “involved” Xiaohongshu cases that the DPP authorities have cited. The DPP authorities’ deliberate use of brutal blocking measures against Xiaohongshu is entirely a “double standard” political manipulation. Their so-called “crackdown on fraud” is a pure pretext with ulterior motives; the real aim is to seek “independence,” deliberately incite so-called “resisting China and safeguarding Taiwan,” cut off cross-Strait exchange channels, and deprive the Taiwan public, especially young people, of their right to know and their freedom to use social media platforms. The DPP authorities’ vile conduct has already provoked strong dissatisfaction and opposition among the Taiwan public, especially young people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251217_12740874.htm"],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视直新闻记者","Nikkei Asia recently revealed that TSMC is considering producing more advanced 4-nanometer chips at its second factory in Japan than originally planned, which has sparked concern on the island about the loss of the core advantages of Taiwan's semiconductor industry. Some public opinion has questioned whether the outward migration of TSMC's advanced technology could cause it to become “US-TSMC” or “Japan-TSMC.”…","The concerns of Taiwan residents about the future development of the semiconductor industry are by no means alarmist. The DPP authorities have long treated TSMC as a tool for submitting and currying favor with the US and Japan. In pursuit of their own political self-interest, they do not hesitate to squeeze Taiwan's semiconductor industry dry, becoming accomplices who let external forces freely plunder the interests of Taiwan compatriots. Broad Taiwan compatriots and far-sighted people in the industry should boldly speak out and take action to safeguard their own well-being and the future development of the industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","The Wall Street Journal recently published an article claiming that the PLA would “attack Taiwan” in three steps, and listed so-called “best times to attack Taiwan” and “best landing sites,” which has drawn attention on the island. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants. It is a sacred mission and a just cause. Resolving the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. At present, the situation in the Taiwan Strait is complex and grave, and the fundamental cause lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities’ stubborn insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and their continuous collusion with external forces to provoke and seek independence. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the harmful and destructive nature of the “Taiwan independence” provocations by the Lai Ching-te authorities, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, join us in safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The United States recently released its National Security Strategy report, which mentions Taiwan many times and claims it “does not support any unilateral actions that change the status quo in the Taiwan Strait.” Lai Ching-te posted a message expressing thanks. What comments do you have on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. It concerns the national feelings of over 1.4 billion Chinese people and brooks no external interference. There is only one China in the world; the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. It must be pointed out that “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and avoid dragging China and the United States into a dangerous state of conflict and confrontation because of a handful of “Taiwan independence” separatists.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The results of the “Taiwan 2025 Character of the Year” poll hosted by Taiwan’s United Daily News were announced recently, and the “bà” (罷) in “recall” (罷免) was selected as this year’s character. What is your comment?","Everyone who has been paying attention to cross-Strait relations should have noticed that in recent years, Taiwan's annual representative character has become a barometer reflecting the public mood and opinion on the island. The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, loudly promote separatist fallacies, and continuously escalate cross-Strait confrontation, causing tension and turmoil across the Taiwan Strait. Without principle, they kowtow to the United States, and without bottom line, they sell out and harm Taiwan, scheming to “decouple” cross-Strait economic and trade relations and “cut off” industrial chains, which seriously damages the interests and well-being of businesses and residents on the island. Again and again, they have provoked political struggles and, by any means necessary, suppressed political opponents and created “green terror,” intensifying social division and the opposition of public opinion. From “贪” (greed) in 2024 to “罢” (recall) in 2025, this reflects the strong dissatisfaction of Taiwan society with the Lai Ching-te authorities. Their words and deeds run counter to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society, which wants peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and they have lost popular support, provoking widespread public resentment.\nWe note that apart from the character “罢,” more than half of the top ten representative characters are negative words, including “诈” (deceit), “淹” (flood), “灾” (disaster), “乱” (chaos), and “裂” (split). These reflect the anger of Taiwan residents at the Lai Ching-te authorities for placing political calculations above people's livelihood needs and harming Taiwan and its people, as well as their dissatisfaction with social turmoil. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the danger and harm of “Taiwan independence,” consciously draw a clear line between themselves and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, and work together with compatriots on the mainland to promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said in the House of Councillors, when questioned, that the Taiwan question should be resolved peacefully through dialogue. What comments do you have?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and no external interference is tolerated. Japan should earnestly reflect, correct its mistakes, and withdraw its erroneous remarks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The US Senate recently passed the so-called “Porcupine Act,” which requires amending the “Arms Export Control Act” to simplify the process of US arms sales to Taiwan. The DPP authorities have said they welcome it. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose the US Congress advancing negative bills related to Taiwan, and firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, stop “arming Taiwan,” stop reviewing relevant bills, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs. Out of its self-interested pursuit of “independence,” the DPP authorities are willing to let external forces turn the treasured island into a “war porcupine” and turn Taiwan’s people into cannon fodder, at the mercy of others. This is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新闻记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that resuming cross-Strait tourism should first be communicated through the \"small two associations.\" The Taiwan Tourism Association sent a letter to the Haixia Tourism Association in February. Does the Haixia Tourism Association currently have a willingness to communicate, and what are the preconditions for communication?","The root of the problems and obstacles in cross-Strait tourism lies entirely with the DPP authorities. Driven by their inherent nature of confrontation in pursuit of “independence” and by their political self-interest, the DPP authorities turn a deaf ear to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and the appeals of the industry, and are blind to the interests of Taiwan's grassroots people and businesses. They have repeatedly used various untenable excuses to block and restrict cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in various fields, erecting barriers and checkpoints. This is unpopular, and the island's industry has expressed extreme disappointment and strong indignation. The DPP authorities should reflect on themselves, correct their mistakes, and remove as early as possible the various obstacles they have set up to cross-Strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","On December 17 last year, the “Twin City Forum” was held in Taipei, where the Vice Mayor of Shanghai stated at the forum that Shanghai would actively promote group tours to Taiwan for Shanghai residents. There has been no follow-up progress. This year's Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held in Shanghai on December 28, and Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an will lead a delegation to attend. Cross-Strait tourism…","As agreed by relevant parties in Shanghai and Taipei, the “2025 Shanghai-Taipei City Forum” will be held in Shanghai on December 28. Under the theme “Technology Changes Life,” the forum will promote the sharing of experience and interactive exchange between the two cities in areas such as technology and medical care, rail transit, and health and elderly care through discussion and exchange. During the forum, the two cities will sign relevant memoranda of exchange and cooperation to further deepen exchanges and cooperation between Shanghai and Taipei in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-17","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs recently issued a decision to take countermeasures against Shigeru Iwasaki, former Chief of Joint Staff of Japan's Self-Defense Forces, who took up the post of political adviser to the DPP authorities in 2025. May I ask what the standard for the mainland's sanctions is, and whether other Japanese officials will be subject to measures by the mainland side for words and actions…","The relevant departments have already provided an explanation on this. The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests and an insurmountable red line. The DPP authorities’ collusion with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, and their selling out of national interests, will surely face the judgment of history.\nJapan should not underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. It should abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251217_12740862.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-18","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","It’s reported that amid China’s military activities, a land lease deal was signed on December 15 by Japan’s Defense Ministry on the easternmost island of Okinawa for the deployment of a mobile surveillance radar unit to monitor Chinese aircraft carriers and airplanes in waters between Okinawa’s main island and the Miyako Island, the sources said. Construction work is expected to begin next year, where around 30…","We noted the reports. It needs to be stressed that countries enjoy freedom of navigation and overflight in relevant waters and airspace in accordance with the international law.\nDue to Japanese militarists’ history of aggression and other reasons, Japan’s moves in military and security areas have been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. The Japanese side kept strengthening targeted military deployment near China’s Taiwan region and even claimed it will deploy mid-range missiles. This time, it went even further by deploying radar unit and troops to secretly monitor its neighbor. Given the erroneous and dangerous remarks made by Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan, we must question: Is the Japanese side making trouble and provocations at one’s doorstep to find a pretext for its military buildup and missions overseas? Is the Japanese side once again going down the wrong path of militarism to a dead end laid out by the right-wing forces? We urge the Japanese side to learn from history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251218_11775856.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251218_11775796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-18","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The U.S. has announced a package of arms sales to Taiwan worth up to US$11 billion, making it one of the largest sales. I wonder if the Foreign Ministry have any comment on this?","The U.S. blatantly announced its plan to sell massive advanced weapons to China’s Taiwan region. This move grossly violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, infringes on China’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity, undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and sends a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes and strongly condemns it.\nThe “Taiwan independence” separatist forces on the island attempt to advance their independence agenda and resist reunification through military buildup, squander the taxpayers’ money to purchase weapons, and even risk turning Taiwan into a “powder keg.” Such moves will not reverse the inevitable failure of “Taiwan independence,” and will only push the Taiwan Strait into the danger of military conflict at a faster pace. For the U.S., assisting the “independence” agenda by arming Taiwan will only backfire, and using Taiwan to contain China will never succeed.\nThe Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests, and is the first red line that must not be crossed in China-U.S. relations. No one shall underestimate the firm will and strong capability of the Chinese government and the Chinese people in safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, act on its leaders’ serious commitments, and immediately stop the dangerous act of arming Taiwan. China will take resolute and strong measures to defend its national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251218_11775856.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251218_11775796.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-19","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","Foreign media reported that the U.S.’s large-scale arms sales to Taiwan announced yesterday were to “assist Taiwan in maintaining sufficient self-defence capabilities, commensurate with the threat it faces.” What is China’s comment?","We’ve stated China’s serious position on this issue yesterday. The U.S.’s massive arms sales to China’s Taiwan region grossly interfere in China’s internal affairs, undermine China’s sovereignty, security and territorial integrity, disrupt peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and send a seriously wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and others. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes this, and has immediately lodged serious protests with the U.S. side.\nLet me stress that China’s core interests must not be eroded, the Taiwan question must not be interfered in, and China’s bottom line must not be crossed. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. Any move of arming Taiwan will face serious consequences. The real threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the separatist activities of the Lai Ching-te authorities and external interference. The so-called “assistance in response to threat” to Taiwan will only embolden “Taiwan independence” separatists, put the people in Taiwan on a “powder keg,” push the Taiwan Strait towards danger, and inevitably increase the risk of China-U.S. conflict and confrontation.\nNo one or force should underestimate the strong will and capability of the Chinese government and people to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. No matter how many advanced weapons are sold to Taiwan, this will not reverse the inevitability towards China’s reunification. China will take all measures necessary to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, act on the serious commitments made by U.S. leaders, stop the dangerous move of arming Taiwan, stop disrupting peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and stop sending wrong messages to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251219_11776971.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251219_11776886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-19","Guo Jiakun","Nippon TV","Part of senators of the United States have submitted a resolution which is expressing support for Japan and on the other hand criticizing China’s economic and military pressure towards Japan. Does the Ministry have any reaction to this?","To safeguard the outcomes of WWII victory and defend the post-war international order is the common responsibility of the international community, including China and the U.S. Justice lies in everyone’s heart. It needs to be stressed that after Prime Minister Takaichi made the erroneous remarks, there has been indignation from the Chinese people as well as objective and rational opposition and criticism from Japan, U.S. strategists and international commentators. What the Japanese side should do is to listen to these calls and do soul-searching rather than persuade other countries into believing their groundless explanations and shift the responsibility and seek endorsement. We once again urge the Japanese side to sincerely repent for and correct its wrongdoings, retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks as it should, fully and accurately articulate its political commitments made on the Taiwan question in the four political documents between China and Japan, and fulfill its obligations as a defeated country stipulated in documents with full effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251219_11776971.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251219_11776886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-19","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Daily","We noted that recently, Japanese politicians, academics, non-governmental organizations and civil groups criticized Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks and moves on Taiwan and a string of dangerous signals of military buildup sent by the Japanese government. They called on the government to retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s remarks. What’s your comment?","We noted these voices. Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan made on November 7 and Japan’s recent moves to remilitarize have been met with vigilance and opposition from the neighboring countries. More and more Japanese political dignitaries and people have expressed their objection. A senior Diet member said that in history, there have been innumerable examples of politicians stoking external crisis which triggered people’s indignation and evolved into real survival-threatening situation. As a result, people paid a huge price. Recently, when questioning Prime Minister Takaichi at the Diet, a member stressed that children should never be sent to the battlefield or get involved in warfare. Takakage Fujita, the secretary-general of the Association for Inheriting and Propagating the Murayama Statement, said that recent remarks by Takaichi point Japan towards a dangerous direction of the pre-emptive use of military force, and Japan must not permit any political faction to steer the nation back towards the path of war. According to some Japanese media, there is no guarantee that what Prime Minister Takaichi did will not put Japan on a course of fascism once chosen by militarists.\nEighty years ago, the Japanese people, offered an empty promise of victory in the war, paid a heavy price for the complete failure. The history and reality show that returning to militarism will only lead a country astray to a dead end. To make a clean break with militarism and embrace the path of peaceful development is an important prerequisite for Japan to get the trust and understanding of the international community, especially its Asian neighbors, and is the right choice that meets the fundamental interests of the Japanese people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251219_11776971.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251219_11776886.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-12-19","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Defense Security Cooperation Agency stated on December 18 that the U.S. has approved arms sales to Taiwan totaling more than $11.1 billion. Some commentators say this is the largest weapons sales plan the U.S. has ever made to Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The United States has announced a large-scale arms sales plan for the Taiwan region of China. This seriously violates the One-China Principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, seriously damages China's sovereignty and security interests, seriously undermines China-US strategic mutual trust, and sends a serious wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China is strongly dissatisfied with and firmly opposes this, and has made solemn representations to the United States.\nThe complete reunification of China is an irresistible historical trend that no force can stop. The “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, at the cost of the security and well-being of the Taiwan compatriots, are willing to fatten American arms dealers with the hard-earned money of ordinary people, attempting to “seek independence through force.” In the end, this can only be like a moth flying into a flame, leading to their own destruction. The United States has repeatedly broken its word and betrayed trust, indulging and supporting “Taiwan independence,” and will inevitably bring disaster upon itself. We urge the United States to genuinely fulfill its commitment not to support “Taiwan independence” and to immediately stop arms sales to Taiwan. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to strengthen training and preparedness for combat, take forceful measures to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely thwart the “Taiwan independence” separatist and external interference schemes.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2025/12/19/11474060.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-12-19","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: On December 19, the US “National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2026” was signed into law, including provisions on Taiwan such as allocating $1 billion for the “Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative.” What is your comment?","State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua responded to questions, saying: The US side has inserted erroneous content related to Taiwan into the “FY2026 National Defense Authorization Act,” attempting to further “arm Taiwan,” interfere in China’s internal affairs, and send serious erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it.\nWe demand that the US side abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not implement the Taiwan-related provisions of the act, eliminate their negative impact, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that no matter how much they “rely on the US to seek independence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the fate that “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail, and cannot stop the historical trend of China’s inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251219_12741379.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-20","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Recently, mainland coast guard vessels again entered the “prohibited waters” off Kinmen for law enforcement patrols. Is the TAO aware of the situation, and what is your comment?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying: Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu are all part of China. The waters between Xiamen and Kinmen have been traditional fishing grounds for fishermen on both sides of the Strait since ancient times, and there is absolutely no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters.” The mainland coast guard's regular law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters help maintain maritime operating order and protect the life and property safety of fishermen on both sides. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: face up to the history and objective facts of fishermen on both sides jointly working on traditional fishing grounds, and stop arbitrarily detaining and seizing mainland fishing boats and their crews, or resorting to dangerous and rough methods against them. Otherwise, they must bear all consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251220_12741465.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-22","Lin Jian","Xinhua News Agency","Recently, a senior official in charge of security and defense at the Japanese Prime Minister’s Office told reporters that Japan should have nuclear weapons. Japanese Defense Minister later said that they left open the possibility of Japan reviewing its non-nuclear principles in the future. These remarks were met with strong criticism from various sectors in Japan and its neighboring countries, including Russia.…","China is shocked that a senior official from the Japanese Prime Minister’s Office who is close to Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi brazenly claimed that Japan should have nuclear weapons. Japan’s Chief Cabinet Secretary declined to make clarifications on the remarks. Asked about possible revisions to the three non-nuclear principles, Japan’s Defense Minister said “all options would be discussed.” Given previous Japanese media reports that Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi plans to revise the three non-nuclear principles, the above-mentioned statements amount to a blatant challenge to the postwar international order and the nuclear non-proliferation regime, a serious threat to regional and international peace and stability, and a U-turn from Japan’s commitment to “peaceful development.” Stressing that the idea is a “personal view” is not convincing at all. The international community should be on high alert and firmly against it.\nFirst, relevant remarks seriously violate Japan’s due obligations under international law. Instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, clearly stipulate: Japan should be completely disarmed and not maintain such industries as would enable the country to re-arm for war. As a non-nuclear-weapon State Party to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, Japan must fully abide by the provisions of “not receiving, manufacturing, acquiring or transferring nuclear weapons.” These are non-negotiable obligations under international law that Japan must fulfill and should not be used as bargaining chips for political gains.\nSecond, relevant remarks severely undermine peace and stability in the Asia-Pacific and beyond. The international nuclear non-proliferation regime is an important part of the postwar international order. Japan’s attempt to possess nuclear weapons gravely challenges the authority and effectiveness of the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons, risks undermining countries’ effort of upholding the international nuclear non-proliferation regime and sabotages the hard-won peace and stability after WWII. Japan’s statements have been met by opposition from many countries. LDP senior officials, members of both ruling and opposition parties and civil groups were shocked and said that such remarks shall never be tolerated and the three non-nuclear principles shall be strictly observed.\nThird, Japanese right-wing forces’ remilitarization ambition is rather apparent. Former Japanese political leaders claimed Japan is capable of manufacturing nuclear weapons. Japan has long been manufacturing and possessing plutonium stocks far beyond what is needed for civilian nuclear power programs. Japan is a non-nuclear-weapon state capable of producing weapon-level plutonium. If Japan further pushes the envelope and continues to challenge international justice and test the bottom line of the international community, China’s response will be a firm “No”. Over the years, the Japanese right-wing forces have been advancing Japan’s military buildup. The latest statement by the senior official from the Japanese Prime Minister’s Office of “possessing nuclear weapons” is an example of how Japanese right-wing forces are trying to “remilitarizing” and “rearming” Japan. It also says a lot about why Prime Minister Takaichi could make such erroneous and dangerous remarks concerning Taiwan on November 7. After coming into office, Prime Minister Takaichi has hyped up the “survival-threatening situation” and kept blurring policy boundaries. She has taken a number of steps to cross the red line and played deaf to domestic and international criticisms. Many with vision in Japan have warned against that. We cannot but ask: Where exactly is the Takaichi Administration taking Japan?\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. Japanese militarists waged a war of aggression and committed inhumane atrocities, creating the darkest page in human history. Despite the defeat, Japan has never been able to fully eliminate the scourge of militarism in the country. Some forces inside Japan have not only failed to reflect on Japan’s history of aggression, but also been extremely unhappy about the postwar international arrangement. If the right-wing forces in Japan are left free to develop powerful offensive weapons, or even possess nuclear weapons, it will again bring disaster to the world. China and all peace-loving countries in the world are on high alert and firmly opposed to the dangerous tendency Japan has shown on the issue of nuclear weapons, and strongly urge Japan to abide by international law and its Constitution and stop the venturing and provocative moves towards owning nuclear weapons. Japan must not seek to challenge the postwar international order, and stop plunging further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251222_11780748.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251222_11780592.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-22","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","A high-level LDP official from Japan is visiting Taiwan today. He’s on a three-day visit, and he is expected to meet Taiwanese president Lai Ching-te. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","Taiwan is a province of China and there is no such thing as “president.” Let me stress that Japanese LDP lawmakers’ visit to China’s Taiwan region violates the one-China principle, the four political documents between China and Japan and Japan’s own commitments made to China. China firmly opposes the visit and has protested to the Japanese side.\nThere is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. We once again urge the Japanese side to reflect on and correct its wrongdoings, retract Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks, and not to interfere in China’s internal affairs. The DPP authorities will not succeed in seeking “Taiwan independence” by ingratiating themselves with Japan. Their disgraceful acts will only lead to a dead end.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251222_11780748.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251222_11780592.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-24","Lin Jian","CCTV","It’s reported that the remarks by a senior official from the Japanese Prime Minister’s Office that “Japan should have nuclear weapons” have shocked many in and outside Japan. That has been met with criticism from Japanese former political dignitaries, members of both ruling and opposition parties, and civil groups as well as strong opposition from neighboring countries. A former Japanese political dignitary said…","We noted the reports and the protests and petitions from civil groups across Japan.\nIt’s by no means an isolated incident that a senior official from the Japanese Prime Minister’s Office made such remarks. In recent years, Japan has removed the ban on exercising the right to collective self-defense, developed intermediate-range offensive weapons, increased military deployment, restructured the command systems, and expanded the area and scope of Self-Defense Forces activities. This amounts to a severe violation of provisions in instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration and the Potsdam Proclamation, and of Japan’s own Constitution. Only two months into office, Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi has accelerated military buildup, hit the defense-spending target of two percent of GDP two years early, further relaxed restrictions on arms exports, pushed forward the revision of the three documents on security and defense, including National Security Strategy, discussed the revision on the three non-nuclear principles, and implied the introduction of nuclear-powered submarines.\nThose remarks of the Japanese official—supposedly someone close to Prime Minister Takaichi—came on the heels of her erroneous remarks on Taiwan. This is yet another attempt of the Japanese side to intentionally test the bottom line of the international community and reveal the long-standing wrongful proposition and ambition of Prime Minister Takaichi and Japanese right-wing forces to keep remilitarizing Japan. It sends an extremely dangerous signal. These moves challenge the post-war international order, threaten regional peace and stability, and do not serve the interest of the Japanese people. China and all other peace-loving countries will respond to those developments together and firmly prevent the resurgence of Japanese militarism.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251224_11786235.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251224_11785912.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Peng Qing’en answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the 2025 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit Annual Meeting was held in Nanjing, drawing wide attention. Business and industry representatives from both sides attending the meeting exchanged views in depth on topics such as seizing the opportunities of the “15th Five-Year Plan” and deepening the integrated development of cross-Strait industrial and supply chains. They unanimously agreed that the…","This year's annual meeting of the summit is a cross-strait business community exchange and cooperation gathering held in the year the mainland is about to enter the opening year of the 15th Five-Year Plan. It is of great significance for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to seize the historic opportunities of the formulation and implementation of the 15th Five-Year Plan, to accelerate their integration into the new development pattern and participation in high-quality development, and to deepen the integrated development of cross-strait industrial and supply chains.\nWang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, delivered an address at the annual meeting, saying: The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the CPC has provided top-level design and strategic planning for development during the 15th Five-Year Plan period. It will surely inject new momentum into promoting cross-strait economic cooperation and common development, and open new prospects for promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advancing the great cause of national reunification. We hope that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will better contribute to jointly strengthening the Chinese nation's economy and jointly creating lasting well-being for the Chinese nation. This reflects our sincere goodwill in supporting Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in taking root and developing, and it also points the way for them to participate in high-quality development.\nDuring the annual meeting, how to seize the opportunities of the 15th Five-Year Plan and develop together became a hot topic of exchange among the cross-strait entrepreneurs present. Entrepreneurs from different fields and perspectives looked ahead to the development opportunities embedded in the 15th Five-Year Plan and discussed in depth new paths for cross-strait economic cooperation in which industrial chains, supply chains, innovation chains and value chains work in coordination. They said that through exchanges they have deepened their understanding of industrial layout and development priorities, and that in future cooperation they will precisely match needs and optimize industrial models, creating conditions for the integration of multiple chains. We will, as always, actively support cross-strait industrial cooperation, continuously improve the institutions and policies that promote cross-strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepen cross-strait integrated development, and help Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded enterprises seize opportunities of the 15th Five-Year Plan and better develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742050.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","人民日报记者","On December 23, the “7th Symposium on the History of the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance Against Japan and the Inheritance of the Anti-Japanese War Spirit, and Book Launch of ‘Chronology of Major Events in the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance Against Japan’” was held in Beijing, attracting attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On December 23, the 7th Symposium on the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance Against Japan and the Inheritance of the Spirit of the Anti-Japanese War, together with the launch of the new book “Chronicle of Major Events of the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance Against Japan,” was held at the Chinese Academy of History. The symposium was co-hosted by the China Society for the History of the Anti-Japanese War and the Taiwan Restoration Memorial Association, and more than 120 guests from both sides of the Strait attended.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance and also the 80th anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. During the discussions, participants from both sides of the Strait systematically reviewed the anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots, thoroughly demonstrated the historical contribution of the Chinese people’s War of Resistance to the victory of the world anti-fascist war, profoundly explained the major significance and far-reaching impact of establishing Taiwan Restoration Day, and sternly criticized and exposed Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan and distorted view of history. This reflects the important role of the War of Resistance symposium in promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to “share historical materials, jointly write history and jointly carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance.”\nAt the event, the “Chronicle of Major Events of the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance Against Japan,” co-compiled by experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait and published by Zhonghua Book Company, was released. The chronicle contains more than 600,000 characters in total. Using the annalistic format, it records major events of the War of Resistance year by year, month by month and day by day, objectively and in detail presenting the course of the heroic resistance against Japan by Chinese soldiers and civilians. The traditional-character edition will also be published in the near future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","新华社记者","Today (December 24), public security authorities issued a reward notice, seeking clues to the illegal and criminal activities of Taiwan residents Jian Wensheng and Chen Shunjin, who controlled Togolese-flagged vessels such as the “Hong Tai 58” and have for a long time smuggled frozen goods into the mainland. In February this year, the DPP authorities falsely accused the “Hong Tai 58” incident, in which Taiwan…","After investigation by public security authorities, two Taiwan residents, Jian Wen-sheng and Chen Shun-chin, were found to be habitual smugglers who operated vessels including the “Hong Tai 58” and long engaged in smuggling frozen goods to the mainland. The public security authorities have now issued a reward notice for these two individuals and hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide clues about illegal and criminal activity. The relevant authorities will strictly protect the information and lawful rights and interests of informants in accordance with law.\nThe “Hong Tai 58” incident that occurred in February this year was in fact Jian and Chen operating the “Hong Tai 58” vessel to engage in smuggling crimes. The DPP authorities disregard the facts of the case and maliciously hype mainland “gray-zone harassment” in an attempt to provoke confrontation across the Strait. We warn the DPP authorities that shielding and tolerating smuggling crimes and using them as an opportunity for political manipulation to undermine cross-Strait relations will certainly meet with the joint opposition of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and will certainly bring about their own downfall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742045.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","香港中评社记者","Recently, the Taiwan executive authorities passed draft amendments to so-called “national security laws” and other laws, stating that those who advocate for foreign countries or the mainland region to launch war against Taiwan, or to adopt non-peaceful means to eliminate the so-called “sovereignty of the Republic of China,” will be severely punished, and that penalties will be increased for active-duty military…","The Lai Ching-te authorities obstinately insist on their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, disregard the mainstream public opinion on the island that it wants peace, development, exchange and cooperation, deliberately incite \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, attempt to \"seek independence by relying on external forces\" and \"seek independence by force,\" and continuously aggravate tensions in the Taiwan Strait. This is the concrete action of their so-called \"17 strategies,\" aimed at escalating cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, undermining cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and recklessly creating a \"green terror\" and a \"chilling effect,\" in service of their \"Taiwan independence dictatorship\" and \"green dictatorship.\" We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the \"Taiwan independence\" line of the Lai Ching-te authorities, and join us in firmly opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, and firmly opposing their attempt to drive the Taiwan Strait toward war.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742049.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","北京日报记者","Gu Lasi, former spokesperson for the Office of the Leader of Taiwan's regional authorities, recently claimed at the launch of his new book that he “is not Chinese,” and that there is no ethnic group in the world called the “Chinese nation.” He also said that Taiwan currently faces a “mainland threat,” and that besides military preparedness and energy resilience, identity is also a “national security issue.” What…","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. Taiwan's Indigenous peoples are a branch of the ancient Yue people, who migrated to Taiwan from the mainland, either directly or indirectly. This is supported by a large body of archaeological findings and is also recognized by Taiwan's Indigenous ethnic groups. Some petty villains, for political gain, have abandoned their ancestors and betrayed their roots, defying common sense and losing basic humanity and conscience. It is shameful, sad, and pitiful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中新社记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan released a so-called \"Observation and Analysis Report on the Situation 26 Years After Macao's Handover,\" which claims that Macao's \"shortage of professional talent has led to challenges for economic diversification\" and that \"Macao's independent media has been repeatedly suppressed this year.\" What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities, driven by their inherent aim of seeking “independence,” maliciously attack and smear the practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong and Macao. Their claims are entirely ignorant of the facts and irresponsible. The achievements of the successful implementation of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong and Macao are plain for all to see. Over the 26 years since Macao’s return to the motherland, “one country, two systems,” “Macao people governing Macao,” and a high degree of autonomy have been fully guaranteed and completely realized. Macao’s main economic indicators have entered the top ranks globally, people’s livelihood and well-being have greatly improved, and it has become one of the wealthiest cities in Asia. Macao’s brilliant achievements since its return to the motherland prove that “one country, two systems” has significant institutional advantages and strong vitality, and is a good system for keeping Hong Kong and Macao prosperous and stable over the long term.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中国日报记者","Recently, the DPP authorities sent representatives to attend the first “Silicon Peace Summit” held in the US, claiming that Taiwan can play a key role in the “global semiconductor democratic supply chain.” What is your comment on this?","We oppose the United States providing a stage for “Taiwan independence” separatists. Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, in order to seek “independence,” deliberately incite ideological confrontation and push the so-called false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” which does not win popular support. The so-called “democratic supply chain” is in essence Lai Ching-te’s authorities going against economic laws and market laws and catering without any bottom line to external forces. They trade away Taiwan’s advantageous industries, sacrifice Taiwan’s development prospects, and smash the “rice bowls” of Taiwan’s people in exchange for external forces’ support of their pursuit of “independence.” What they say and do will only aggravate tensions in the Taiwan Strait, increase the burden on Taiwan’s people, and bury Taiwan’s economic lifeline and development prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742047.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The British magazine The Economist recently published an article saying that although Taiwan's recent economic figures are good, ordinary people do not feel prosperous, which has become the “Taiwan disease.” The head of Taiwan's economic department responded, “We have no disease. Those who say we have a disease are the ones who are sick,” which drew criticism on the island of “self-important ignorance” (夜郎自大).…","It is a fact that Taiwan's economic development faces rising uncertainty and intensifying imbalance, and it is also a fact that the wealth gap keeps widening and ordinary people do not feel their living conditions improving. Out of the selfish interests of one party and one clique, and ignoring the risk that Taiwan's high-tech industry is being forcibly hollowed out by Western countries, and disregarding the plight of the island's traditional industries struggling under high tariffs, the DPP authorities continue to pander to foreign powers without principle, sell out Taiwan without bottom line, and blindly gloss over reality and deceive the public. Such self-deceiving words and deeds cannot conceal their incompetence in governance. Ultimately, the root of the \"Taiwan disease\" is the DPP authorities' harboring of malicious intent to seek \"independence\" and provoke conflict; the lesion is the DPP authorities' reckless disregard for people's livelihoods; and the symptoms are the DPP authorities' shameless servility, exhausting Taiwan's resources to win the favor of outside forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742048.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently claimed that he plans to invest NT$1.25 trillion as a “special defense budget.” Subsequently, media on the island revealed that small companies in Tainan and Kaohsiung, including renovation and shoe-trading firms, have one after another won defense project bids worth several hundred million New Taiwan dollars. Commentary on the island said that “southern traditional industries have turned…","In order to “use military force to seek independence,” the DPP authorities are lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s ordinary people to buy foreign weapons, while taking the opportunity to enrich themselves and engage in corruption. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the sinister intentions and ugly faces of the DPP authorities, use practical actions to keep a close watch on their own wallets, and not be deceived again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251224_12742046.htm"],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent economic, trade and other cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Cross-strait exchanges remained brisk from the beginning of the year through its end. Here I will mainly introduce some of the activities held this month.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, the Yangtze River Delta Taiwan Business Economic and Trade Cooperation Summit (Chuzhou) was held in Chuzhou, Anhui, with more than 200 attendees, including heads of the National Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and some Taiwan business associations. The Guizhou-Taiwan Health and Wellness Industry Exchange was held in Guizhou, where enterprise representatives, experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait jointly explored new opportunities for the integrated development of the cross-Strait health and wellness industry. The 18th Huanyu Productivity Forum was held in Beijing, where experts, scholars and business representatives from both sides of the Strait discussed the opportunities and challenges of a new round of technological change. A briefing and experience-sharing meeting on listing policies for Taiwan-funded enterprises was held in Shenzhen, exchanging views on mainland listing policies, how Taiwan businesses and enterprises can seize opportunities in the mainland capital market, and how to help with the digital transformation of manufacturing. The 2025 Cross-Strait (Zhangping) “Tongxin Cup” Taiwan-Style Oolong Tea King Competition and brand promotion event was held at the Taiwan Farmers' Entrepreneurship Park in Zhangping, Fujian, collecting about 3,500 tea samples from both sides of the Strait.\nIn cultural exchanges, the classic production “This Life of Mine” by the Beijing Qu Opera Troupe was performed three times in Taipei, attracting nearly 1,300 viewers. The Cross-Strait Young Filmmakers Creation Tour was held in Nanping, Fujian, with more than 150 young filmmakers from both sides of the Strait engaging in in-depth exchanges on strategies for adapting historical and cultural IP into film and television, and on models linking film with the cultural tourism industry. The “Warm Sounds for the Winter Solstice, Creative Echoes in Jiangcheng” Han-Taiwan Youth Lifestyle and Culture Season theme music market was held in Wuhan. The first Cross-Strait Folk Customs and Sports Performance and Guan Gong Loyalty and Righteousness Culture Exchange Conference was held in Shanwei, Guangdong Province, with more than 600 Taiwan compatriots gathering in Shanwei to trace their shared cultural roots.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and a family should visit often and get to know each other's relatives. As the winter vacation approaches, we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young students, to take a “spur-of-the-moment trip.” Go to “Erbin” to see the ice and snow and fly to Sanya to enjoy the sea breeze; travel to “Chang'an” to step back into the Tang Dynasty, and come to Beijing to visit the Forbidden City after snowfall; come to Chongqing for spicy hotpot and to Shenyang to enjoy the “erren zhuan” folk performance; go to Guangzhou to taste morning tea and to Hangzhou to visit the “Six Little Dragons”; come to Shanghai to see its urban bustle and to Suzhou to admire its small bridges and flowing streams. Personally experience snowy northern China, warm Lingnan, fiery Sichuan and gentle Jiangnan; take in magnificent landscapes, taste exquisite cuisine, and appreciate the rich and splendid history and culture, the thriving economy and technology, and the warmth of compatriots everywhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","On the 19th, the caucuses of the Kuomintang and the Taiwan People’s Party in Taiwan’s legislature jointly held a press conference and announced that they would submit a motion to impeach Lai Ching-te. Meanwhile, the “Impeach Lai Ching-te” petition launched on the island’s internet has reportedly gathered more than 8 million signatures, according to statistics. What comments do you have on this?","We have noted the relevant reports. The Lai Qingde authorities, disregarding the livelihood and well-being of the people on the island and seeking political gain for themselves, have continually manipulated and provoked political strife, sparking strong opposition from Taiwan’s people. The relevant situation shows that Lai Qingde stubbornly insists on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” repeatedly tramples on democracy and undermines freedom, abuses judicial power to persecute political opponents, carries out a “green terror,” and creates a “chilling effect.” He defies public opinion and has lost the hearts of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Wu Feng-shan, chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) in Taiwan, recently announced his resignation. Public opinion on the island has pointed out that the foundation for SEF dialogue was set by the DPP authorities, and that if they do not want the SEF to function, it will make little difference no matter who takes office. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermining the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. Only by returning to the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can the cross-Strait two agencies' communication mechanism be restarted and the Straits Exchange Foundation perform its due functions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","上海东方卫视记者","Cai Mingyan, head of Taiwan’s security department, said, “China is accustomed to cross-border suppression or threats against ‘Taiwan independence’ figures and Taiwan-friendly figures.” He said such operations often backfire and are merely symbolic, and that “Taiwan-friendly figures do not care whether they can enter China.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China, and “Taiwan independence” is a criminal activity that splits the country and stirs up trouble in the Taiwan Strait. Lawfully and strictly punishing “Taiwan independence” separatist crimes is a just and necessary measure to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to combat illegal and criminal activity. “Taiwan independence” forces and anti-China forces collude and conspire with each other, which precisely exposes their guilty conscience and trembling fear as the sword of punishing “independence” is drawn. We will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, and we will never allow any external forces to aid and abet wrongdoing or interfere in China’s internal affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan media reported that Lai Ching-te said he will fully establish a “democratic defense mechanism” in response to the mainland's listing of Taiwan's “Information, Communications and Electronic Force,” “psychological warfare brigade,” and certain individual “legislators” as targets for punishment of “Taiwan independence” advocates. Some DPP authorities said, “We have requested that the international community…","The law enforcement and judicial measures taken by the relevant departments against “Taiwan independence” diehards for the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country are an inherent part of defending national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity. They are also righteous actions to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and they are in line with the common practice of countries around the world.\nThe net of justice is vast, and though its mesh is sparse, nothing escapes it. Anyone who endangers national sovereignty, security, and development interests will not escape the sanctions of national law. Any organization or individual that acts as a tiger’s accomplice or aids the wicked in serving the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces will certainly be severely punished by law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","香港经济导报记者","The Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced countermeasures against Iwasaki Shigeru (岩崎茂), former Joint Staff Chief (统合幕僚长) of the Japan Self-Defense Forces. In response, Lai Ching-te said, “China intends to shape a chilling effect to block international support for Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","We have taken countermeasures against the relevant personnel who colluded with the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and remain unrepentant. These measures are well-founded, reasonable, and lawful.\nNo matter what the Lai Ching-te authorities say or do, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China's territory, cannot shake the international community's adherence to the one-China principle, and cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and surely will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Hagiuda Koichi, acting secretary-general of Japan's Liberal Democratic Party, and others recently made an unwelcome visit to Taiwan and met with Lai Qingde. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","We firmly oppose the Japanese side’s relevant intrusive visit. We demand that Japan draw lessons from history, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents through concrete actions, and stop all wrong words and deeds concerning Taiwan. The DPP authorities’ attempt to collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke will inevitably fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","The lease agreement between China and Japan is about to expire, and the last two giant pandas residing in Japan will return to China at the beginning of 2026. In this regard, a Japanese lawmaker said that the giant pandas at the Taipei Zoo were gifted by mainland China, and that Japan has been holding consultations on animal exchanges between Japanese zoos and the Taipei Zoo. What is your comment?","The wild words and delirious talk of certain Japanese politicians are a pipe dream.\nIt must be emphasized that the giant pandas gifted to Taiwan by the mainland in 2008 were given by mainland compatriots to Taiwan compatriots. They are an important achievement of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, deeply loved by Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, and have brought them joyful times and fond memories. As “national treasures,” giant pandas are worth cherishing together by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that dare to make giant pandas a tribute to ingratiate themselves with Japan will surely incur the wrath of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","南方日报、南方+记者","The US Defense Security Cooperation Agency announced arms sales to the Taiwan region of China valued at about US$11 billion. The DPP authorities immediately expressed gratitude, claiming it demonstrates their “determination for self-defense,” and that together with “like-minded countries” they are firmly defending “free and democratic values.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the first red line that the China-US relationship must not cross. The United States has unilaterally announced a massive arms sales plan to Taiwan, brutally interfering in China's internal affairs and seriously violating the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, in particular the \"August 17\" Communiqué. This seriously undermines China's sovereignty and security interests and sends a seriously wrong signal to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces. We firmly oppose this and strongly condemn it. We demand that the United States immediately stop \"arming Taiwan,\" stop indulging and supporting the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, honor the commitments made by US leaders, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities are obstinately \"relying on the United States to seek independence\" and \"seeking independence through force,\" constantly peddling so-called \"defense resolve,\" and are willing to turn Taiwan into a \"powder keg\" and an \"ammunition depot,\" and to make Taiwan's people cannon fodder for \"Taiwan independence.\" This will only bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots and fully exposes their true, vicious face as \"destroyers of peace,\" \"creators of crisis,\" and \"instigators of war.\" All sectors in Taiwan should recognize the evil nature of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, who recklessly \"sell out Taiwan and provoke war\" without any bottom line. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that the reunification of the motherland is irresistible. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces dare to cross the red line, we will certainly strike back decisively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","福建东南卫视记者","On December 19, the U.S. \"National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2026\" was signed into law, which includes Taiwan-related content such as appropriating 1 billion U.S. dollars for the \"Taiwan Security Cooperation Initiative.\" What comments do you have on this?","The US has inserted erroneous content concerning Taiwan into the “FY2026 National Defense Authorization Act,” attempting to further “arm Taiwan” and interfere in China's internal affairs, and sending a serious wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it.\nWe demand that the US abide by the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, not implement the Taiwan-related provisions of the act, eliminate their negative impact, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how they “rely on the US to seek independence,” they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot change the outcome that “Taiwan independence” will inevitably fail, and cannot stop the historical trend of China's inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Chen Ming-chi, Deputy Head of Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities, told foreign media: “China's pressure on Taiwan has become a ‘hybrid threat,’ with the goal of annexing Taiwan and forcing the people of Taiwan and the international community to abandon Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is China's internal affair. Completing the reunification of the motherland is a matter for the Chinese people themselves and a just cause for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities hype the false narratives of so-called “threats” and “annexation,” attempting to delude Taiwan residents and mislead international public opinion. No matter how they maneuver, it will be in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","《参考消息》记者","Regarding the mainland’s exposure of the DPP authorities’ use of the pretexts of “trust” and “prosperity” to indiscriminately implement “dollar diplomacy,” Taiwan’s foreign affairs department said, “The Rong Bang Plan is value-based, centers on the well-being of the people, and promotes the cooperative concept of international shared prosperity and development.” What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “value-based” approach claimed by the DPP authorities is in essence “based on Taiwan independence,” deliberately inciting ideological confrontation in order to seek “independence.” The so-called “people’s well-being at the core” is in fact “people’s well-being as tribute,” squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s ordinary people to exchange for so-called “diplomatic space,” which is shameless and despicable. “Taiwan independence” is a dead-end road that cannot be traveled. No matter how meticulously the DPP authorities scheme and play petty tricks, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor shake the international community’s pattern of adhering to the One-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Mainland coast guard vessels again entered Kinmen’s “prohibited waters” for law enforcement patrols. Does the Taiwan Affairs Office know the situation, and what comments do you have?","Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu are all part of China. The waters off Xiamen and Kinmen have been traditional fishing grounds for fishermen on both sides of the Strait since ancient times, and there is fundamentally no so-called “prohibited or restricted waters.” The mainland coast guard carries out regular law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters, which helps maintain order in maritime operations and protects the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities to face the history and objective facts of fishermen on both sides of the Strait working together in traditional fishing grounds, and to stop groundlessly detaining mainland fishing boat crews and treating them with dangerous and brutal methods. Otherwise, they must bear all the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Taiwan’s Ministry of Health and Welfare recently said Taiwan has achieved hepatitis C elimination ahead of schedule and will apply to the WHO for certification by year-end under the name “Chinese Taipei,” “to avoid being rejected or having the certification sent to China.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. Handling Chinese Taiwan’s participation in World Health Organization activities in accordance with the one-China principle is the fundamental principle affirmed by UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1. We have long been committed to advancing the prevention and treatment of viral hepatitis, have always cared about the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and have made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan’s participation in global health undertakings, so that the health rights of Taiwan compatriots are effectively guaranteed. The DPP authorities politicize health issues that concern the health and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, attempting to challenge the basic international pattern of adhering to the one-China principle. They are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-24","Peng Qing'en","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: SEF Chairman Wu Feng-shan recently announced that he will step down at the end of the year, saying that during his tenure he proposed meeting with the head of ARATS to thoroughly clarify the “1992 Consensus,” and that he had contacted ARATS hoping to visit the schools for the children of Taiwan businesspeople on the mainland, among other things, and ARATS has left these messages unanswered. What…","First question: Because the DPP authorities refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One-China Principle, the communication and dialogue mechanism between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits has long been suspended. As soon as both sides return to the common political basis of the “1992 Consensus,” the dialogue and communication mechanism between the two organizations can be restarted immediately. For figures from all walks of life in Taiwan who support the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, as long as they have a correct understanding of the nature of cross-Strait relations, we welcome them to visit and exchange in the mainland in their individual capacity as Taiwan compatriots.\nSecond question: After investigation by public security authorities, it has been found that Taiwan residents Jian Wensheng and Chen Shunjin are habitual smugglers who operated vessels such as the “Hongtai No. 58” and have long smuggled frozen goods into the mainland. Public security authorities have now issued a bounty notice for these two individuals, and hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide clues to illegal and criminal activities. The relevant authorities will strictly protect the information and lawful rights and interests of informants in accordance with the law.\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251224_12742061.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-25","Lin Jian","AFP","Nasry Asfura has been declared the winner of Honduras presidential election. Asfura has pledged to reestablish diplomatic ties with Taiwan. What is China’s comment on Asfura’s election and this campaign promise?","The presidential election is the domestic affair of Honduras. China respects the choice of the Honduran people and stands ready to work with Honduras to advance the bilateral relationship on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251225_11786962.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251225_11786942.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","China's international military cooperation in 2025 is impressive. Can you further brief us on that?","This year, with a pioneering spirit and proactive efforts, work related to China's military diplomacy has been conducted in a way that kept in alignment with the overall work of the Party and the state, adhered to the strategic guidance of head-of-state diplomacy, and focused on contributing to the improvement of combat readiness.\nFirstly, we have strengthened strategic communication with countries including Russia, the US, and European countries. A Vice Chairman of the CMC visited Russia upon invitation. The Defense Minister had virtual and in-person meetings with the US Secretary of War, and paid visits to France and Germany. China and Indonesia held the first Joint Foreign and Defense Ministerial Dialogue under the 2+2 mechanism. Senior military leaders of China and the UK held bilateral talks. We have deepened institutional consultations with defense authorities of several countries. All these efforts have strengthened China's military ties with other countries and fostered a more favorable strategic security environment.\nSecondly, we successfully hosted the SCO Defense Ministers' Meeting, the China-LAC States Defense Forum, and the inaugural Young Leaders Conference of the China-Africa Peace and Security Forum in China. At the UN Peacekeeping Ministerial, China put forward proposals in support of the reform and transformation of UNPKOs. The Beijing Xiangshan Forum has become more attractive and influential. Multilateral military diplomacy builds consensus and sends out the voice of the Chinese military.\nThirdly, the joint exercises and training with foreign militaries featured many highlights. These include China-Russia joint naval exercise and joint aerial strategic patrol, China-Malaysia Aman Youyi joint exercise, China-Egypt Eagles of Civilization joint air force training, and China-Serbia Peace Guardian joint army training. Through these realistic exercises and training, we have enhanced our capabilities to jointly respond to security challenges.\nFourthly, we responded to violations and provocations made by relevant countries concerning Taiwan and the South China Sea with timely diplomatic representations and press releases to counter misinformation and defend national interests. The MND increased the frequency of press releases, expanded media participation, and launched an account on the X platform to help overseas audiences to get better access to information on the Chinese military.\nIn the coming year, we will thoroughly implement Xi Jinping Thought on Strengthening the Military and Xi Jinping Thought on Diplomacy, actively practice the four major global initiatives, and promote high-quality development of international military cooperation, so as to provide support for achieving the military's centenary goal and to open a new chapter in major-country military diplomacy with Chinese characteristics.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, regarding the introduction of nuclear-powered submarines, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said, \"We will not rule out all options.\" An official from the Prime Minister's Office stated that Japan should possess nuclear weapons. Additionally, the Japanese Ministry of Defense recently released a report, claiming that China's defense spending is growing rapidly and China is…","China's defense expenditure is reasonable, moderate, and remains below the global average as a share of GDP. The operations of the Chinese military in relevant waters are fully in compliance with international law and international practice, and brook no interference or provocation. We urge Japan to cease its false narratives and halt targeted deployments against China. We will take resolute countermeasures against any harassment or provocation.\nIn recent years, Japan has relentlessly pursued remilitarization and accelerated its military buildup, with an increasingly visible and dangerous tendency towards a militarist revival. To cover up its underlying ambitions, Japan has repeatedly used China as a pretext. Not long ago, Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made erroneous remarks concerning the Taiwan question. Now, right-wing forces in Japan have thrown away their hypocritical mask and are openly advocating for nuclear armament. These actions constitute a direct defiance of international norms, a blatant challenge to the bottom line of international justice, the post-WWII international order, and the global non-proliferation regime. They pose a severe threat to peace and stability in the region and beyond. What Japan is doing runs directly counter to its own professed commitment to peaceful development. We call upon all peace-loving nations and peoples to take action to resolutely contain the revival of militarism by Japan's right-wing forces, and prevent the world from sliding into turmoil or reliving tragedies of the past.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, the US recently announced that the 19th US-China Defense Policy Coordination Talks were held from December 15 to 16. The US side stressed that America's interests in the Indo-Pacific are significant and it stands ready to defend them. Could you please brief us more on that? Did the two sides clarify specific plans and arrangements for military-to-military engagement next year? The…","On your first question, China has its principle in developing military relations with the US: China's sovereignty, dignity and core interests brook no infringement. The US talks a lot about engaging with China. At the same time, it keeps undermining China's sovereignty and security. This two-faced approach—saying nice words but doing badthings—is very hypocritical and will not work on China. Challenging China's red lines and bottom lines will come at a cost. We urge the US side to immediately correct its wrongdoings, stop all infringements and provocations, and do not challenge China's resolve in safeguarding our sovereign rights and interests.\nOn your second question, the negative provisions in the USAct concerning Taiwan grossly interfere in China's internal affairs. They have sentextremelywrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and seriously undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The US side has violated its commitments byincreasing arms sales to Taiwan. This will only embolden the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and push the Taiwan Strait closer to the abyss of military conflict. The DPP authorities are letting the US to exploit and exhaust the island at the cost of the well-being of the people in Taiwan.\nUsing Taiwan to contain China is doomed to fail, and seeking independence by force is a path to self-destruction. We urge the US side to fully recognize the sensitivity of the Taiwan question, strictly observe the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, exercise utmost caution in handling Taiwan-related matters, stop arming Taiwan in any form, and take concrete actions to maintain the overall stability of state-to-state and military-to-military relations between China and the US.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, Lai Ching-te stated in a media interviewthe need to \"seek peace through strength\", reiterated that the relationship between the US and Taiwan is \"as solid as a rock\", and promoted a $40 billion arms procurement. The head of Taiwan authorities'defense department also claimed that the US emphasizes the shared responsibilities of allies in defense, and that Taiwan must continue to promote a…","The root cause of the current cross-strait tensions and instabilities lies in the DPP authorities' provocative pursuit of \"Taiwan independence\" in collusion with external forces. Lai Ching-te, with his unprincipled subservience to the US, reckless militarization, and escalation of cross-strait confrontation, is an out-and-out saboteur of peace and instigator of war. Therefore shame on him that he talked about \"peace\" and hisempty boast of \"strength\" was ignorant. It is little more than over estimating and deceiving oneself. We sternly warn the DPP authorities thatnational reunification is unstoppable. Those who act as pawns will inevitably be discarded and those who betray the nation and engage in secession will be nailed to the pillar of historical shame.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, it was reported that the Taiwan authorities' security bureau recently stated that around 3,600 sorties of PLA aircraft had been detected around the island this year, setting a new record. PLA aircraft and ships had conducted 39 joint combat readiness patrols. In response, Taiwan authorities' defense department claimed to have formulated contingency procedures in response to mainland…","On your first question, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The PLA's regular training and combat readiness exercises around the Taiwan island, as well as theoperations to counter separatism and foreign interference, are entirely justified, necessary, and legitimate, with an aim to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The PLA will relentlessly combat separatist activities to advance the cause of reunification. For every provocation made by the \"Taiwan independence\" forces, we will respond by increasing pressure and pushing forward resolutely until the complete reunification of the motherland is achieved. We sternly urge the DPP authorities to face reality, follow the overwhelming trend of the times, abandon their separatist schemes of \"Taiwan independence\" once and for all and cease all provocative actions that could lead to conflicts. This is the only correct choice.\nOn your second question, the history of Japanese militarist aggression is an indisputable fact and its heinous crimes cannot be concealed. How Japan treats this part of history serves as a litmus test for its moral conscience and genuine commitment to peace. We therefore urge Japan to cease its evasion, obfuscation, and deception, and offer a sincere apology and genuinely atone for its crimes. Only by taking such actions can it truly earn the trust of its Asian neighbors and the wider international community.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US Department of War recently released Annual Report to Congress: Military and Security Developments Involving the PRC. Please comment on that.","Year after year, the US releases such reports, which grossly interfere in China's internal affairs, deliberately misrepresent China's national defense policy, groundlessly speculate on China's military development, and smear the normal activities of the Chinese military. Filled with wrong perceptions of China and geopolitical prejudices, these reports hyped up the so-called China's military threat to mislead the international community. We express strong dissatisfaction and resolute opposition to this.\nChina steadfastly pursues a defensive national defense policy, adheres to the military strategy of active defense, and advances the modernization of national defense and armed forces with high quality. These efforts are solely aimed at safeguarding national sovereignty, security and development interests. China has always been a force for peace, stability and progress in the world. The Chinese military actively implements the Global Security Initiative, acts in strict compliance with domestic and international laws, safeguards its legitimate rights and interests in a reasonable and measured manner, endeavors to provide international public security goods, and works with other militaries to foster the building of a community with a shared future for humanity.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people. The PLA defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity. Its efforts to combat separatist activities and promote reunification are entirely justified and unwavering. The US has no right to interfere. China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea islands and reefs and their adjacent waters. While certain countries within the region have infringed upon and provoked China and external forces have meddled and stirred up trouble, China's resolute defense of its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests is legitimate, lawful, rational and restrained. It is worth pointing out that the US has deliberately rallied its allies to send naval and air forces to China's doorstep for close-in harassment. The necessary measures taken by the Chinese military in response are beyond reproach. The fundamental solution to avoiding maritime and air incidents is for the US and its allies to cease all dangerous and provocative actions. We urge the US to adopt a correct perception of China, view China and the development of the Chinese military objectively, stop fabricating false narratives, cease stoking division and confrontation, and avoid leading the state-to-state and military-to-military relations astray.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to US media reports, the PLA would \"attack Taiwan\" in three steps, listing the so-called optimal attack timing and optimal landing sites. Recently exposed details from a classifiedUS Department of War report suggest that the mainland could destroy advanced US weapons before they reach Taiwan, indicating that the US is no longer capable of \"defending Taiwan\". Please comment on that.","Certain media outlets have speculated about the operations of the PLA with ulterior motives, fueling unwarranted \"war anxiety\", which only undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and utmost effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force and reserve the option to take all necessary measures. Should \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces provoke and even cross the red line, we will have no choice but to take resolute and decisive measures. The PLA stands ready at all times to fight and win, and will resolutely defeat any schemes for \"Taiwan independence\" or any form of external interference.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan authorities' defense department, PLANS Fujian passed through the Taiwan Strait on December 16 for the first time. It claimed to maintain close monitoring of the situation. Please comment on that.","The passage is part of the routine training of PLANS Fujian.Similar activities will continue to be organized as needed in the future. We urge the \"Taiwan independence\" armed forces to recognize the reality and abandon futile struggles and illusions.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Japan has not only taken frequent acts around the Taiwan Strait but has also been taking more operations in the South China Sea. It has built an ammunition depot in the Philippines and deepened defense cooperation with the Philippines and Vietnam, which includes weapons exports and the normalization of troop deployments. What's China view on Japan's systematic intervention in the South China Sea?","Japan is not a party to the South China Sea issue. Worse still, it once invaded and illegally occupied China's Xisha Qundao and Nansha Qundao. What Japan needs to do is to engage in serious soul-searching, rather than making wavesin the South China Sea, provokingconfrontation and undermining regional peace and stability. We hope relevant countries will see through Japan's sinister intentions. Counting on external forces to make troublesin the South China Sea will prove fruitless, and letting in the wolfwill only backfire.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2025-12-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question: recently, the Japanese and the US air forces conducted their respective tactical exercises over the Sea of Japan. The drills involved two US B-52 bombers and six Japanese fighter jets. Japan stated that the purpose was to reaffirm that Japan and the US will not tolerate any unilateral attempts to change the status quo by force. External analysis suggests that this move is…","On your first question, China has consistently emphasized that military cooperation between the US and Japan should not target third parties, much less undermine regional peace and stability. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference. The PLA's determination to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is rock-solid. If anyone attempts to interfere in China's internal affairs through military provocation, we will never tolerate or indulge such actions and will respond with resolute countermeasures.\nOn your second question, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has already responded to it. We urge Japan not to repeat its mistakes, to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and to immediately cease all erroneous words and actions regarding Taiwan. The DPP authorities' fawning posture and attempts to curry favor with Japan are despicable and their schemes to seek \"independence\" by relying on external forces are doomed to fail.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2025/12/china-251225-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16429147.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2025-12-26","Lin Jian","RT TV","The Japanese government approved the draft budget for fiscal year 2026 on December 26, with the defense budget exceeding JPY nine trillion, hitting a new record. What is China’s comment?","We noted the reports. Despite recent international criticism over latest military and security developments in Japan, the Japanese side has shown no inclination to mend its conduct, and instead plans to again hike defense budget, further revealing Japanese right-wing forces’ motive to remilitarize Japan and resurrect militarism.\nGiven the Japanese militarists’ innumerable war crimes, Japan’s military and security moves have always been closely watched by its Asian neighbors and the international community. Since the new Japanese government took office, it has been notably accelerating military buildup. From Prime Minister Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan that threatens the use of force against China, to the remarks of a senior official of the Japanese Prime Minister’s office calling for Japan’s possession of nuclear weapons, and to the proposed revision of the three national security documents and the idea of altering the three non-nuclear principles, Japan is deviating further and further away from the path of peaceful development and moving in a dangerous direction.\nIn recent years, Japan has removed the ban on exercising the right to collective self-defense, developed the so-called “capability to strike enemy bases,” strengthened cooperation on extended deterrence, and built its frontier islands into front lines, which clearly goes beyond Japan’s “exclusively defense-oriented” policy. Terms such as “self-defense” and “counterstrike” are used by Japanese right-wing forces to gloss over their attempt to breach the postwar international order and stipulations in Japan’s Constitution, and deceive and stoke public opinion. These moves have put the international community on high alert.\nThe Japanese people are also victims of militarism. Some in Japan pointed out that raising defense spending does not bring peace and stability. Rallies have been held across Japan in strong protest of the Japanese government’s military expansion. Some scholars also note that the defense budget hike will weigh heavily on Japan’s economy and eventually be borne by the ordinary people in Japan.\nChina will work with all peace-loving countries to push back any dangerous move designed to resurrect militarism or cultivate neo-militarism, and jointly defend the outcomes of WWII victory.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251226_11788128.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251226_11787943.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-29","Lin Jian","CCTV","Starting from this morning, the PLA Eastern Theater Command is conducting military drills in areas near the Taiwan Island. Some said the drills are carried out in response to the US$11.1 billion arms sales to Taiwan announced by the U.S. this month. What’s your comment?","The spokesperson of the PLA Eastern Theater Command has made an announcement of the military drills. The drills are a punitive and deterrent action against separatist forces who seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup, and a necessary move to safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nLet me stress that to advance their separatist agenda, the DPP authorities are turning Taiwan into a powder keg. Their massive and desperate arms purchase further reveal their true nature as provocateurs, saboteurs of peace and war-mongers. Anyone who tries to arm Taiwan to contain China will only embolden the separatists and push the Taiwan Strait closer to the peril of armed conflict.\nThe Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests. Nothing will deter China from defending national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. Anyone who crosses the line or makes provocations on the question will be met with China’s firm response. All attempts to hold back China’s reunification will invariably fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251229_11789802.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251229_11789718.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-29","Lin Jian","Reuters","I just want to follow up on what’s been said today about the war games around Taiwan. Could you tell us if the trigger of these games was due to the US$11.1 billion arms sales to Taiwan? Is the United States the so-called “external interference forces” that the Eastern Command is referring to? (Similar question from NHK)","Let me stress once again that nothing will deter China from defending national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. Anyone who crosses the line or makes provocations on the question will be met with China’s firm response.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251229_11789802.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251229_11789718.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-29","Lin Jian","RIA Novosti","Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov said earlier that Russia stands against “Taiwan independence” in any form and will support China in defending national unity and territorial integrity in case of the possible escalation in the Taiwan Strait. I wonder what’s China’s comment on this?","China commends Russia’s long-standing support for China on the Taiwan question. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. Nothing will ever deter China from defending its national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251229_11789802.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251229_11789718.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2025-12-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On December 29, the Eastern Theater Command organized the “Justice Mission-2025” exercise around Taiwan island. Some foreign media have commented that this military exercise targets the recent large-scale U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The Eastern Theater Command promptly released information on organizing the “Justice Mission-2025” exercise. This exercise is a serious warning to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external interference, and a legitimate and necessary move to defend national sovereignty, security, and territorial integrity. Recently, external forces have repeatedly overstepped and crossed lines on the Taiwan question, attempting to embolden the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, aggravating cross-Strait confrontation, seriously harming China's sovereignty and security, and seriously undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The Lai Ching-te authorities, without bottom line, pander to and cling to external forces and arrogantly seek “independence” and provocation, becoming the source of trouble that undermines the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and aggravates tensions.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are incompatible like fire and water, and external forces that condone and support “Taiwan independence” will only bring fire upon themselves and reap the consequences. We urge the relevant countries to abandon the fantasy of “using Taiwan to contain China,” stop stirring up trouble on the Taiwan question, and not challenge China's determination and will to safeguard its core interests. We warn the DPP authorities that “relying on external forces to seek independence” is doomed to fail and “resisting unification by force” is a dead end. The Chinese People's Liberation Army will not hesitate to fight “independence” and promote unification, and will continue to organize actions against secession and interference, resolutely safeguarding national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity.","","http://www.news.cn/20251229/8f8a21d2aa6948b9a43a010d560f6242/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2025-12-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Beginning on December 29, the PLA Eastern Theater Command organized forces from the army, navy, air force and rocket force to conduct the “Justice Mission-2025” exercise around Taiwan island. What is your comment?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, responded to questions by saying that the relevant military operations of the People's Liberation Army are a solemn warning to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and to external interfering forces, and a necessary and righteous measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Lai Ching-te authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, with their unprincipled kowtowing to foreign powers and unscrupulous selling out of Taiwan, regardless of the cost to Taiwan's economic development and people's livelihood and welfare, are racing down the evil path of colluding with external forces to plot “independence,” provocation, and military adventurism. They seriously undermine cross-Strait relations, seriously threaten peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. For any “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, we will not tolerate it, will not appease it, and will surely deal a painful blow.\nTaiwan is Taiwan of China. Any external force that attempts to intervene in the Taiwan question or interfere in China's internal affairs will surely be smashed bloody against the iron wall and copper bulwark of the Chinese People's Liberation Army. The historical trend toward national reunification is unstoppable, and no one should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. The relevant military operations are directed at “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference. They aim to contain “Taiwan independence” colluding with external forces to stir up trouble in the Taiwan Strait, and to fundamentally safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. They are by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist line, and join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, firmly guarding our common homeland of the Chinese nation, and jointly creating a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251229_12743367.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2025-12-30","Lin Jian","AFP","Regarding the ongoing live-fire drills conducted by China’s People’s Liberation Army around Taiwan. Yesterday you mentioned that they were a response to actions by external forces. U.S. President Donald Trump has said that the drills do not worry him and he has said it’s just something China has done for the last couple of decades. What is China’s reaction to Donald Trump’s perspective on these drills?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The military drills by the PLA are a punitive and deterrent action against separatist forces who seek “Taiwan independence” through military buildup, and a necessary move to safeguard China’s national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251230_11790799.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251230_11790696.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-31","Lin Jian","China News Service","China has recently taken countermeasures and punitive and deterrent measures on Taiwan-related issues. Following the PLA’s military drills near the Taiwan Island, Russia, Cuba, Serbia, Venezuela, Zimbabwe, Pakistan and other countries expressed their support. What’s China’s comment?","Several dozen countries have expressed support in various forms for China following its latest countermeasures and military drills concerning the Taiwan region. They reiterated their commitment to the one-China principle, opposition to external interference in China’s internal affairs and support for China’s effort to defend sovereignty and territorial integrity. They noted in particular: Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and “Taiwan independence” in whatever form must be rejected. We highly commend those countries for their firm support.\nWe reaffirm once again that China will never waver in its resolve to safeguard national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity. China will never waver in its resolve to defend the nation’s reunification and vital interests. China will never waver in its resolve to deter “Taiwan independence” separatist forces from colluding with external forces and destabilizing the Taiwan Strait. Anyone who crosses the line or makes provocations on the Taiwan question will be met with China’s firm response. All attempts to hold back China’s reunification will invariably fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251231_11796371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251231_11796240.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-31","Lin Jian","CCTV","It was reported that Japan, Australia, an EU agency and some European countries have openly expressed concerns over China’s military drills near the Taiwan Island. What is your response?","China firmly rejects the wrongful statements from these countries and institution and has lodged serious protests with them. They turn a blind eye to the separatists’ massive military buildup attempts aimed at “Taiwan independence” and speak nothing of the external interference in China’s internal affairs, and slam China for its just and necessary action to defend sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is absolute hypocrisy and distortion.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair which brooks no external interference. The fundamental status quo of the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China, and the biggest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is “Taiwan independence” forces’ separatist activities and external connivance and support for these activities. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and basic norm in international relations. It is also the political foundation for China’s relations with all 183 countries having diplomatic ties with China. Japan, Australia and certain European countries made a clear commitment to one-China when establishing diplomatic ties with China. We once again call on these countries and institution to abide by their commitment, stop interfering in China’s internal affairs, and stop aiding and abetting separatism for “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251231_11796371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251231_11796240.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-31","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","A group of Japanese business executives has postponed its trip to China, which was planned to take place in late January and the reasons they gave were challenges in securing meetings with Chinese officials. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on this postponement of the major Japanese business delegation’s trip to China in January?","We noted the reports and also found that many visionary people in Japan are deeply concerned over the negative impact and grave consequences of Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. We urge those in the Japanese government to take concrete actions, face up to the root cause for the current situation in China-Japan relations, reflect on and correct the wrongdoing, retract the erroneous remarks of Takaichi, and create necessary conditions for the normal exchanges between China and Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251231_11796371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251231_11796240.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2025-12-31","Lin Jian","TV Tokyo","Japanese Councillor Shi Ping wrote on social media today that he plans to visit Taiwan early next year and that since he is banned from entering China, by entering Taiwan he is proving Taiwan is an independent country with no connection to China. What’s China’s comment?","The nasty words and deeds of a disgrace like him are not worthy of comments.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202512/t20251231_11796371.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202512/t20251231_11796240.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on December 31, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Recently, the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce jointly issued the “Catalogue of Encouraged Industries for Foreign Investment (2025 Edition),” which will take effect on February 1, 2026. Does the Catalogue apply to Taiwan businesses and Taiwan-funded investment, and what benefits will it bring?","The new edition of the Catalogue of Industries Encouraging Foreign Investment focuses on scientific and technological innovation and developing new quality productive forces, demonstrating our firm determination to expand high-level opening to the outside world. The Catalogue guides more foreign capital toward advanced manufacturing, modern services, the central and western regions, the Northeast region, and Hainan Province. It will provide strong guidance for Taiwan businesses investing, setting up operations, and transforming and upgrading on the Mainland. We will help Taiwan businesses seize the historic opportunity of the formulation and implementation of the 15th Five-Year Plan, encourage and support deeper cooperation between cross-Strait industrial and supply chains, and achieve better development in the new wave of reform and opening up.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The Eastern Theater Command of the People's Liberation Army began organizing forces from the army, navy, air force, and rocket force on December 29 to conduct “Justice Mission-2025” exercises around Taiwan Island, which have drawn great attention and strong shock on the island. What comments do you have on this?","The relevant military operations of the People's Liberation Army are a solemn warning to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and to external interference. They are a necessary and righteous measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Lai Ching-te authorities are pursuing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, engaging in unprincipled sycophancy toward foreign powers and boundless betrayal of Taiwan, and are willing to sacrifice Taiwan's economic development and people's livelihood and welfare. They are racing down an evil path of colluding with external forces to provoke “independence,” engaging in warmongering. This seriously undermines cross-strait relations, seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. We will show absolutely no tolerance and no leniency toward any “Taiwan independence” separatist act, and we will certainly strike back hard.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. Any external force that attempts to interfere in the Taiwan question or intervene in China's internal affairs will surely be bloodied and battered against the impregnable fortress of the Chinese People's Liberation Army. The historical trend toward national reunification is irresistible. No one should underestimate our strong determination, firm will and formidable capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. The relevant military operations target “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and external interference. They are aimed at containing “Taiwan independence” forces that collude with external forces to bring chaos to the Taiwan Strait, and at fundamentally safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. They are by no means directed at broad Taiwan compatriots. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist line, and join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, firmly safeguarding our shared home of the Chinese nation, and jointly creating a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743799.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the PLA’s “Justice Mission-2025” military exercise, some public opinion on the island pointed out that the DPP’s wrong cross-Strait policy has led to the danger of war across the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","The relevant military operations of the PLA are a solemn warning to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and external forces that interfere, and are a necessary and righteous act to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Lai Ching-te authorities are engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, servile toward foreign powers without principle, selling out Taiwan without bottom line, and at the cost of Taiwan’s economic development and people’s welfare, they are racing down the wrong path of colluding with external forces to seek “independence” through provocation, and engaging in warmongering. They are seriously undermining cross-strait relations, seriously threatening peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harming the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. For any “Taiwan independence” separatist act, we will never tolerate it, never appease it, and will certainly strike hard.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","On December 26, Taiwan’s legislative body voted to pass the motion to impeach Lai Ching-te. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te obstinately clings to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence.” In pursuit of political self-interest and disregarding the livelihood and welfare of the island's people, he has repeatedly trampled on democracy and impaired freedom. He has abused the judiciary to suppress and persecute political dissenters, vigorously promoted “green terror” and created a “chilling effect,” and constantly manipulated and stirred up political bloodbaths. Defying public will and losing popular support on a large scale, he will inevitably face strong opposition from the Taiwanese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said, “The obstacles to current cross-Strait exchanges still lie with the mainland; the mainland is still conducting compound pressure against Taiwan, and Taiwan hopes to create a favorable cross-Strait atmosphere.” What is your comment on this?","These claims disregard facts and reverse black and white. The ringleader inciting cross-Strait confrontation and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges is the DPP authorities. Since taking office, the DPP authorities, out of self-interest in pursuing “independence,” have repeatedly used all kinds of pretexts and methods to obstruct and restrict normal cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel, carry out a “green terror,” create a “chilling effect,” and escalate cross-Strait antagonism. Their perverse actions have met with increasing dissatisfaction and firm opposition from more and more Taiwan residents.\nExchanges and cooperation between compatriots on both sides cannot be stopped. We have always adhered to the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family.” We welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland and take part in exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, share in the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743792.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent economic, trade and other cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","At the turn of the year, compatriots on both sides of the Strait moved toward each other and held many colorful exchange activities, jointly expressing their hopes for the new year and their aspiration for a peaceful and good life. Let me introduce some of these activities.\nThe 2026 Meizhou Island Mazu Ancestral Temple New Year's Eve blessing ceremony series of events was held in Putian, Fujian, including a music gala, a blessing ceremony, and a fireworks show. The opening of the championship game of the 6th Straits Student Baseball League, “Huaxia Golden List,” was held simultaneously in Xiamen and Kinmen, with more than 600 youth from both sides competing and exchanging skills. The 22nd Taiwan Student “Northern Customs” Winter Camp was held in Changchun, Jilin, where nearly 100 Taiwan youth experienced ice and snow culture together with teachers and students of Jilin University. The opening ceremony of the “2025 Taiwan Youth Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Ice and Snow Season” was held in Beijing, and the event will continue until February of next year. The exchange activity “Compatriots from Taiwan Join Hands in Longyu, Promoting Integration and Talking About the New Year” was held in Lanzhou, Gansu, where Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan business representatives from the locality discussed development opportunities together and shared deep feelings of home and friendship. The first Wuhan Taiwan Food Festival was held in Wuhan, where dozens of Taiwan food vendors and Wuhan food experts invited Wuhan residents to savor the flavors of Taiwan and enjoy the fireworks of the New Year's Eve. The special screening event “Chinese White Dolphin” for the “Welcome the New Year with Cross-Strait Family Fun” program was held in Zhuhai, with nearly 100 cross-Strait families participating, deepening their understanding of ecological protection achievements and strengthening their sense of shared responsibility for protecting our home.\nOver the past year, many Taiwan compatriots crossed mountains and seas to come to the mainland to enjoy beautiful scenery, savor delicious food, and experience the myriad sights of the country. The vast land of China is a common home for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The snowy plateau closest to the sky and the north and south of the Tianshan Mountains farthest from the sea welcome Taiwan compatriots to explore; the Greater and Lesser Khingan Mountains covered in ice and snow and the warm-as-spring Xishuangbanna are waiting for Taiwan compatriots to visit and check in. In the new year, we warmly welcome compatriots from Taiwan to listen to the wind at Kanas, to view Nam Co Lake, to watch the clouds by the Ussuri River, and to gaze into the distance from the Pamir Plateau—to embark on a spontaneous journey to the mainland. “The mainland is so vast—welcome to come and see.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","The 2025 Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Modern Agriculture Matchmaking Event will be held in the near future. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From December 22 to 26, the Cross-Strait Agricultural Exchange Association and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, together with relevant parties in Xiamen, Fujian Province, organized the 2025 Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Modern Agriculture Matchmaking Event. Under the theme “Cross-Strait Agriculture, Rural Areas and Farmers: Integrated Development,” the event invited about 350 people from agricultural circles on both sides of the Strait to participate. Participants jointly discussed production-sales matching, shared views on industrial cooperation, and explored integrated development together, achieving positive results.\nDuring the event, high-quality industrial projects from 17 Taiwan Compatriot Innovation and Entrepreneurship Parks were released collectively, and 12 green cultivation and breeding, deep processing and specialty seedling products and technologies were promoted and introduced. This both demonstrated the mainland's favorable investment and entrepreneurial environment and showcased high-quality, characteristic technology products from Taiwan farmers and enterprises, facilitating a batch of substantive cooperation results, with 20 market entities signing letters of intent on site.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently said, in an exchange with university students on the island, that saying “I am Chinese” in Taiwan means bearing an “original sin” of unknown origin, which is the result of the DPP’s 30 years of malicious manipulation. “I am Chinese” is a natural cultural and historical identity and should not be demonized by the DPP. What comments do you have on this?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Compatriots on both sides belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. This is historical fact, cultural recognition, genetic heritage, and legal reality, and no one can deny it. The DPP authorities, out of their inherent nature of plotting independence, have deliberately manipulated “de-Sinicization,” attempting to sever the historical and cultural ties across the Taiwan Strait, to deceive the Taiwan public, to cause confusion in historical memory and distortion of national identity among Taiwan’s younger generation, with endless harm. Voices of protest and criticism from all sectors of Taiwan society continue to grow. The DPP authorities’ political manipulation is doomed to be in vain and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743795.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Recent polls on the island show that the proportion of Taiwan residents who consider the DPP “not trustworthy,” “lacking governing capacity,” and “not clean” is above 50% in each case. What is your comment?","The relevant public opinion poll reflects Taiwan residents' strong dissatisfaction with the DPP authorities, who ignore the interests and well-being of the public, obstinately provoke 'independence,' stir up political strife, suppress political opponents, and insist on 'catering to foreign powers and selling out Taiwan.'\nSince Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly adhered to the 'Taiwan independence' separatist position, disregarded the interests and well-being of broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, further obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and forcibly pushed for 'decoupling and severing chains' in cross-Strait economic ties. With no bottom line, he 'caters to foreign powers and sells out Taiwan,' letting external forces take whatever they want. He lavishly spends Taiwan residents' hard-earned money on purchasing foreign weapons while taking the opportunity to profit and engage in corruption, pushing Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and peril. We hope broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the evil nature and ugly face of the DPP authorities, and voluntarily draw a clear line between themselves and 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces and their activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743796.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","新华社记者","The Taiwan executive authorities recently passed a draft amendment to the Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area, which proposes to add provisions that include elected representatives and county and city heads who left office less than three years ago in the categories of persons required to obtain permission to travel to the mainland, among other things. The Mainland…","Driven by its inherent desire to seek \"independence,\" the DPP authorities have schemed to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and undermine cross-Strait relations. On the island, they are vigorously pursuing \"Taiwan independence dictatorship\" and \"green terror,\" leaving Taiwan's society anxious and everyone feeling insecure. They have met with growing opposition and condemnation from the people of Taiwan. Facts have already proven, and will continue to prove, that the popular will for peace, development, exchange and cooperation cannot be suppressed, and the surging tide of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743791.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Regarding retired Taiwanese generals who traveled to the mainland to attend the Seventh Symposium on the History of China's War of Resistance Against Japan and the Inheritance of the Anti-Japanese War Spirit, Taiwan's \"Veterans Affairs Council\" said, \"the heroes of the War of Resistance are all in Taiwan,\" and that whether this trip violated regulations will be handled by the competent authorities. What is your…","On December 23, relevant groups from both sides of the Strait jointly held the 7th Symposium on the History of the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the Inheritance of the Spirit of the War of Resistance in Beijing, and released the jointly compiled *Chronicle of Major Events in the Chinese Nation’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression*. Since 2017, relevant groups from both sides of the Strait have jointly held seven war-of-resistance symposiums. Experts and scholars, retired generals, and teacher and student representatives from both sides have conducted in-depth discussions of the history of the War of Resistance from many angles, producing fruitful research results that have been widely recognized across both sides.\nThe Chinese people’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression was an arduous and extraordinary great war. Under the banner of the anti-Japanese national united front initiated by the Communist Party of China, the Chinese people, with iron-hard bones, fought strong enemies and, with their flesh and blood, built a Great Wall. They achieved the first complete victory in resisting foreign aggression since modern times.\nHistory is the best textbook and the best sobering agent. We will continue to support people from all sectors on both sides of the Strait, especially young people, in jointly studying the history of the War of Resistance and carrying forward its spirit. The actions of relevant parties in Taiwan that distort the historical facts of the War of Resistance, obstruct cross-Strait academic symposiums and exchange and cooperation, and suppress people on the island who take part in cross-Strait exchanges do not win popular support and are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","In response to the recent U.S. announcement of large-scale arms sales to Taiwan, China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs recently announced countermeasures against 20 U.S. defense companies and 10 senior executives. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. Regarding the participation of US companies and personnel in arming Taiwan, which crudely interferes in China’s internal affairs, we will take countermeasures against them in accordance with law and regulations.\nThe Taiwan question concerns the national sentiments of more than 1.4 billion Chinese people; it is the core of China’s core interests and the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. Any country or force that plays with fire on the Taiwan question will surely pay the price. We once again urge the US side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop the dangerous acts of arming Taiwan, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution. The DPP authorities’ “relying on the US to seek independence” and “seeking independence by force” are doomed to fail and will be met with a heavy blow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743790.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding the mainland coast guard’s entry into the so-called “prohibited waters” of Kinmen again for law enforcement patrols, the Taiwan coast guard authorities said, “The mainland coast guard insists on forming fleets to harass, disregarding navigation safety and creating extreme navigation risks for passing vessels.” What is your comment on this?","Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu are all part of China. There is fundamentally no so-called “prohibited waters.” The claim of “disregarding the navigation safety of passing vessels” is pure nonsense. Mainland coast guard departments are conducting law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters in accordance with the law precisely to maintain normal navigation and operational order in those waters and to safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. For a long time, the DPP authorities have ignored the history and objective facts of fishermen on both sides jointly operating in traditional fishing grounds, and have arbitrarily detained mainland fishing boat crews and even adopted dangerous and brutal methods against them. This is the chief culprit that creates navigation risks for passing vessels and seriously threatens the lives and property of fishermen.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743785.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, in an interview, once again touted the “new two-state theory,” claiming that the mainland has launched five kinds of threats against Taiwan, including to “national sovereignty” and “confusing identity,” and that Taiwan needs to increase the strength of its “porcupine” self-protection. He also said that peace cannot rely on a piece of paper, and that its greatest mission is to safeguard…","Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has stubbornly insisted on the “Taiwan independence” position, blatantly spread separatist fallacies, and continuously incited confrontation and antagonism across the Taiwan Strait. For the sake of one party and one person’s private interests, he has vigorously pursued “preparing for war to seek independence,” heightening cross-Strait tensions. This will only turn our treasured island into a battlefield and make Taiwan residents cannon fodder. His true face as a “peace-breaker,” “war peddler,” and “troublemaker” has been seen through by more and more Taiwan residents. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Only cross-Strait reunification can keep Taiwan at peace forever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","First question: On the 29th, the PLA began the “Justice Mission-2025” exercises around the Taiwan island. The DPP authorities said that the mainland is “challenging the international order, undermining the status quo of security and stability, and must not misjudge the situation and become a troublemaker for regional peace.” What comments do you have on this? Second question: Lai Ching-te recently said in an…","First question. The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities seek to confuse right and wrong and mislead public opinion. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and are racing down the evil path of colluding with external forces to “seek independence by force.” They are, without any exaggeration, “peace wreckers,” thoroughly “crisis makers” and truly “war instigators.” The relevant military operations of the PLA are a solemn warning against the provocations of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and the interference of external forces. They are a necessary and just measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and are lawful, reasonable and entirely justified.\nSecond question. Lai Ching-te's authorities have repeatedly colluded with external forces to “seek independence by force,” which will only drive Taiwan into a dead end. We have always upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and we continue to share development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots and share the fruits of Chinese-style modernization. Lai Ching-te's authorities' provocations for independence undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and they will surely reap what they have sown.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Lai Ching-te recently presided over a meeting of the so-called “Whole-of-Society Defense Resilience Committee” and said, “The threats posed by hostile foreign forces to Taiwan continue to rise, and we need to more actively involve all of society.” He demanded that “whole-of-society defense resilience move toward legalization, establish popularization of cross-generational resilience education, and promote…","For the sake of its party’s private interests, the DPP authorities are willing to tie the Taiwan people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, completely disregarding the safety and well-being of ordinary Taiwan people, and they will surely be scorned. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “seek independence through force” will only accelerate their own demise.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","In March this year, the DPP authorities required 12,000 mainland spouses residing in Taiwan to submit so-called “household deregistration certificates” within three months, and later extended the deadline to the end of December. According to Taiwanese media, nearly 1,000 mainland spouses have still not submitted the certificates and face cancellation of their household registration. What comments do you have on this?","Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have given mainland spouses who have settled in Taiwan for more than 20 years a deadline to supplement and submit the so-called “de-registration certificate,” otherwise threatening to revoke their settled status. This seriously disrupts the peace of cross-Strait marriages and families. It is completely contrary to common sense and human relations, and is a typical case of arbitrary abuse of power and acting against the people. We firmly oppose this and strongly condemn it.\nAny vicious act or trick that undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait or harms the interests of compatriots on both sides will surely backfire. We advise the DPP authorities to immediately stop political manipulation and withdraw the black hand that suppresses and persecutes cross-Strait marriages and families.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the order for the 2026 lottery for mainland film screening quotas in Taiwan was announced. Hit films such as 《Ne Zha 2》 and 《Nanjing Photo Studio》 cannot be shown on the island, once again prompting the island's film industry to call on the authorities to reexamine the “quota lottery” policy targeting mainland films. What is your comment on this?","In 2025, the mainland film market produced a large number of outstanding works that won both critical acclaim and box office success, setting a record with total box office revenue exceeding 50 billion yuan. \"Ne Zha 2\" took the global animated film box office crown with a total of 15.446 billion yuan, and \"Nanjing Photo Studio\" achieved a double harvest of word-of-mouth and box office thanks to its historical gravitas. Regrettably, these excellent films have faced various political restrictions in Taiwan imposed by the DPP authorities.\nWe have consistently supported cross-Strait film exchange and cooperation, and as early as 2010 we had already lifted the quota restrictions on the public screening of Taiwan films in the mainland. The DPP authorities should lift the quota restrictions on the public screening of mainland films in Taiwan as soon as possible, so that more Taiwan residents can watch excellent mainland films in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The mainland's universities' recruitment of graduate students from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan is about to begin. Please introduce the relevant information.","It is understood that mainland Chinese universities' graduate admissions for students from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan will start soon. Taiwanese students who hold a “Taiwan Compatriot Permit for Travel to the Mainland” and a valid proof of identity or a “Taiwan Resident Certificate” for residence in Taiwan, and who have the corresponding prerequisite educational qualifications, may register on the “Mainland China Graduate Admissions Information Website for Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan” between January 4 and 11, 2026, to apply for graduate programs at more than 200 mainland universities, following the relevant requirements and procedures. It is worth mentioning that the 2026 graduate entrance examination for mainland Chinese universities targeting Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan has added a Fuzhou test center on top of the existing five test centers in Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, Hong Kong, and Macao, and Taiwanese students may choose accordingly.\nAfter years of development, the scientific research capacity, academic standards, and talent cultivation quality of mainland higher education have improved markedly, and its achievements are plain for all to see. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwanese students to apply to mainland universities, and we will continue to create better conditions for Taiwanese students to grow and succeed in the mainland and to realize their life ideals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743793.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Public security authorities recently issued a reward notice, seeking, in accordance with law, clues on Taiwan residents Jian Wensheng and Chen Shunjin, who operated vessels including the “Hong Tai 58” to smuggle frozen goods into the mainland over a long period, a criminal offense. In response, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council and the “Coast Guard Administration” said the mainland has no jurisdiction over Taiwan…","The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The public security organs' issuance of a reward notice and solicitation of criminal clues concerning relevant persons in Taiwan has sufficient legal basis.\nThe DPP authorities remain silent on the criminal gang that operated the “Hongtai 58” for smuggling, yet they slander the mainland with “gray-zone harassment.” After the mainland public security organs disclosed the facts of the criminal gang, they still engaged in muddled arguments, evaded the issue, and took the opportunity to promote “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies and undermine cross-Strait relations. Their despicable words and deeds will certainly be opposed by compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, the US Department of Defense's “China Military Power Report” stated that the PLA is steadily advancing its capability to achieve a “strategic decisive victory” on the Taiwan issue by 2027, and that if the mainland deems it necessary, it could launch four military options against Taiwan, including “joint blockade operations and joint landing operations.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is Chinese territory. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of all Chinese descendants, is a matter for the Chinese people themselves, and brooks no foreign interference. We have the firm resolve, steadfast will, and strong capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and foreign interference, and to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, when Lai Ching-te met with Japanese politicians who sneaked into Taiwan (窜台), he claimed that Taiwan and Japan both face issues such as “the expansion of authoritarianism and the challenges of red supply chain risks,” and expressed hope for deeper exchange and cooperation between the two sides. What is your comment on this?","To win external forces' support for its pursuit of “independence,” the Lai Ching-te authorities have once again trotted out the old tune of “democracy against authoritarianism.” They disregard the danger of Japanese right-wing forces going further and further down the path of militarism and recklessly wage war, and they unprincipledly kowtow to Japan. They ignore the predicament of the island's high-tech industry being forcibly hollowed out by Western countries, and they sell out Taiwan without any bottom line. The Lai Ching-te authorities' “relying on outsiders to seek independence” will surely be thoroughly crushed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202512/t20251231_12743789.htm"],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","The DPP authorities said that former Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, former Minister of Justice and other politicians have visited Taiwan in succession recently, demonstrating the resilience of Taiwan-Japan relations at their “historically best,” and expressed hope to jointly meet challenges in regional security, economic and trade fields. What is your comment on this?","Japan has frequently spread erroneous remarks and taken wrong actions on Taiwan-related issues recently, and we firmly oppose this. We demand that Japan deeply reflect on the lessons of history, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents through concrete actions, and stop all wrong words and deeds related to Taiwan. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: currying favor with Japan to seek\n“\nindependence” is causing trouble for Taiwan. It is a path and a dead end that cannot succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, Asfura won the Honduran presidential election, and before the election he had promised that after being elected he would \"restore diplomatic relations\" with Taiwan. Taiwan authorities' personnel told media in an interview that \"restoration of diplomatic relations can be anticipated.\" What comments do you have on this?","Since China established diplomatic relations with Honduras, the cooperation between the two has borne rich fruit, which accords with the fundamental interests of both countries and both peoples. The one-China principle is a common understanding of the international community and a basic norm of international relations. Honduras's new leadership should proceed from the interests of its own people and choose to stand on the right side of history, rather than the opposite.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","《团结报》记者","Regarding the PLA's “Justice Mission-2025” exercise, U.S. President Trump said he is not worried about the situation around the Taiwan Strait and stated that China has been conducting naval exercises in the region for 20 years. What is your comment on this?","The relevant military operations by the People’s Liberation Army are a stern warning against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and interference by external forces, and a necessary and righteous act to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and collude with external forces to plot “independence” and provoke, which is the root of trouble undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We will not tolerate or appease any “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct. The historical trend that China will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","日本广播协会记者","At the start of the new year, do both sides of the Strait plan to hold exchange activities in areas such as sports, food and culinary culture, and festivals? If this has not yet been determined, can you introduce which cross-Strait exchange programs are usually or expected to be carried out during this period?","Next February, we will welcome the 2026 Year of the Horse Spring Festival, the traditional Chinese festival. At that time, the strong festive atmosphere will fill the homes of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and people from all walks of life across the Strait will hold a series of rich and wonderful activities, celebrating the New Year joyfully together and jointly wishing for good health in the new year and family reunion. I believe that in the festive atmosphere of the traditional Chinese festival, you will more deeply feel that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese, and that blood is thicker than water, with kinship ties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently said in an interview that she hopes to have an opportunity to visit the mainland in the first half of next year, and if possible, to arrange a meeting with mainland leaders. What is your comment on Cheng Li-wun’s visit to the mainland and the itinerary she hopes for?","We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions at all levels with the Kuomintang, enhance mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, oppose “Taiwan independence,” safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, benefit compatriots on both sides, and join hands to create national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The Mainland Affairs Council said that the “Twin-City Forum” had just ended, and the mainland’s announcement of military exercises is a two-pronged tactic: “engaging in exchanges on one hand while intimidating on the other.” It said the mainland is the “troublemaker” for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?\nSecond question: Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an said, “Any…","The first question: The relevant remarks are pure distortion of black and white and confusion of right and wrong.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, loudly propagate separatist fallacies, constantly incite cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, collude with external forces to carry out constant \"independence\" provocations, extravagantly squander the people's hard-earned money in an attempt to \"rely on foreign powers for independence\" and \"seek independence through force,\" and are rushing down the wrong path of militarism. This seriously undermines cross-Strait relations, seriously threatens peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. The relevant military actions of the People's Liberation Army are a solemn warning to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and external forces interfering, and are a necessary and just measure to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nThe second question: This year's \"Twin Cities Forum\" has successfully concluded and achieved a series of results. We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including exchanges between cities on both sides of the Strait, and are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to work together with political parties, groups, and people from all sectors in Taiwan to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe third question: The relevant reports are pure fabrications and malicious rumors with sinister intentions. As long as civil and commercial activities are lawful and compliant, they are protected by law. The mainland's e-commerce market is thriving with enormous potential, and we welcome broad Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwanese internet celebrities, to come to the mainland for exchanges and cooperation and share new development opportunities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","The mainland side has consistently promoted large-scale cross-Strait exchanges. Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an recently delivered remarks at the “Twin Cities Forum,” expressing hope that the Taiwan Strait would no longer see waves and roaring. After the Twin Cities Forum concluded, the mainland side immediately launched military exercises. May I ask, since there are both exchanges and military exercises, what is the…","The root cause of the current tense and volatile situation in the Taiwan Strait lies in the Lai Ching-te authorities' stubborn insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and their collusion with external forces to carry out independence-seeking provocations. For the sake of their own party interests, the Lai Ching-te authorities have continuously colluded with external forces to carry out independence-seeking provocations, vigorously pursuing “relying on outside forces to seek independence,” “seeking independence through force,” and “seeking independence through war preparations.” If they are allowed to persist recklessly, Taiwan will only slide into disaster.\nThe relevant military operations of the PLA are a solemn warning to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and to external interference, and are a necessary and just action to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te authorities' “Taiwan independence” separatist path, and join us in resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, firmly safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation, and jointly creating a beautiful future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2025-12-31","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","May I ask the spokesperson: Amid the current tensions across the Taiwan Strait, what will the mainland side do to maintain or achieve peace across the Strait, so that Taiwan's people can see hope for peace? In your view, what can Taiwan's side do to make the mainland feel the prospects for peace?","The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests. Our will to safeguard national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering. Any vicious act of provocation that crosses the line on the Taiwan question will be resolutely countered, and any sinister scheme to obstruct China’s reunification will not succeed. “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and the connivance and support of external forces are the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. To maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, we must adhere to the one-China principle and clearly oppose “Taiwan independence.”\nNow I will announce the winners of the 7th “Taiwan-Related Knowledge Quiz.”\nOn December 8, the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” released the questions for the 7th “Taiwan-Related Knowledge Quiz,” and netizens enthusiastically took part. As of December 29, the top ten netizens who answered correctly and received the most likes on their comments, in order, were: “薛丁珲”, “武偃文修”, “小年”, “和衷”, “陈健泽”, “忆子任”, “岸衡”, “除缺巫山不是云”, “澜同”, and “鼎岸”. We congratulate these ten netizens, who will each receive the exquisite souvenir, a shell carving titled “Treasure Island Taiwan” (《宝岛台湾》). On January 5, 2026, the WeChat official account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will release the questions for the 8th “Taiwan-Related Knowledge Quiz.” We hope everyone will continue to follow and actively participate.\nToday is the last day of 2025. Taking this opportunity, I wish all our journalist friends a happy New Year, and I thank you very much for your concern and support for the press briefings of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council over the past year. I also take this platform to extend New Year greetings to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, wishing everyone good health, a happy family, and new gains in the year ahead.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202512/t20251231_12743783.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-01-02","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Not long ago, the PLA Eastern Theater Command held the “Justice Mission-2025” exercise. Lai Ching-te claimed that this military exercise brings uncertain risks to regional stability, and the United States, Japan, Australia, the Philippines, the EU and others have made remarks about the exercise, hoping the mainland will maintain restraint and opposing unilateral changes to the status quo across the Taiwan Strait.…","The PLA Eastern Theater Command successfully organized the “Justice Mission-2025” exercise, comprehensively testing the integrated joint combat capabilities of the task forces, fully demonstrating our powerful strength to “deter independence, promote reunification, and counter interference,” and clearly signaling that any provocative act that crosses the line on the Taiwan question will be firmly countered, and that any sinister scheme to obstruct China's reunification will never succeed.\nTaiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, which brooks no foreign interference.\nThe PLA's organization of anti-separatist and anti-interference operations around Taiwan Island is entirely justified and necessary, and is beyond reproach.\nThe greatest status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the strait belong to one China, and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct and the indulgence and support of external forces. No one cherishes peace in the Taiwan Strait more than we do,\nbut we will never accept anyone or any force using the maintenance of peace in the Taiwan Strait as a pretext to tie our hands in curbing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities; we will never allow anyone or any force, under the banner of peace, to interfere in China's internal affairs and stir up trouble in the Taiwan Strait.\nWe urge the relevant countries and institutions to strictly adhere to the one-China principle, stop indulging and supporting the “Taiwan independence” forces, and stop meddling and stirring up trouble on the Taiwan question. We hope that the broad Taiwan compatriots will genuinely recognize the extreme danger and harm of Lai Ching-te's “Taiwan independence” provocation, prevent themselves from being deceived and coerced by the “Taiwan independence” forces, and effectively safeguard their own security and well-being and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nThe PLA will continue to strengthen training and combat preparedness, stand ready at all times to counter provocations aimed at “independence,” resolutely thwart all schemes of external interference, and defend national sovereignty, unification, and territorial integrity.","","https://news.bjd.com.cn/2026/01/02/11500255.shtml","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2026-01-04","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: according to Taiwan media reports, some DPP legislators have proposed amending Taiwan’s current “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” to define cross-strait relations as “Taiwan and the People’s Republic of China,” and to delete the words “before national reunification” from the original text. What comment do you have on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying: We are highly concerned about the relevant developments. This proposal disregards the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society and the peace and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, blatantly challenges the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, and attempts to change the Taiwan Strait status quo that there is only one China in the world and that the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. It openly promotes \"de jure Taiwan independence\" and deliberately escalates cross-Strait tensions, undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the region. Its intentions are malicious and its nature is vile, fully demonstrating that the Lai Ching-te authorities and the DPP are unmistakable \"peace wreckers,\" \"crisis makers,\" and \"war instigators.\"\n\"Taiwan independence\" means war; it is a dead end and a road to ruin. We have full confidence and sufficient capability to crush any form of \"de jure Taiwan independence\" scheme, and we will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means!\nHistory has proven, and will continue to prove, that pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism has no good end and will only result in total defeat. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces dare to take risks and cross the red line, we will certainly act resolutely in accordance with the Anti-Secession Law and deliver a head-on blow. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the evil nature and serious harm of \"Taiwan independence,\" firmly stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, and join us in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and safeguarding our shared Chinese national home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260104_12744504.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-01-05","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Taiwan officials see the capture by Donald Trump of Venezuela’s Maduro as a powerful deterrent to Beijing. They’ve also added that it highlights the U.S.’s ability to defeat militaries that are equipped with Chinese-made weapons. Finally, they’re also seeing it as a signal to adversaries of the U.S. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China. How to resolve the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves, and no external forces are in the position of making any interference. The DPP authorities’ disgraceful attempts of soliciting external support to seek “Taiwan independence” and resisting reunification through military buildup are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260105_11806736.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260105_11806730.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-01-06","Mao Ning","AFP","The Japanese lawmaker Hei Seki is in Taiwan at the moment. He said that his visit would show that Taiwan is an “independent country.” Does the Foreign Ministry have a response to this?","The bluster of a despicable man is not worth any comment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260106_11807319.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260106_11807212.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-01-07","Mao Ning","NHK","China’s Ministry of Commerce yesterday made an announcement to strengthen export controls on dual-use items destined for Japan. The 2026 Catalogue of Dual-Use Items and Technologies Subject to Export Licensing Administration released by the Chinese government includes rare earths-related items. Are rare earths products covered by yesterday’s announcement of tightening export control measures on Japan? The…","I’d refer you to competent authorities for anything specific. Let me stress that Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan violated China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, blatantly interfered in China’s internal affairs, and threatened the use of force against China. With the aim of defending national security and interests and fulfilling non-proliferation and other international obligations, China took measures in accordance with laws and regulations, which is fully legitimate, justified and lawful. We urge Japan to face up to the root cause of the issue, do soul-searching, rectify its wrongdoings and retract the erroneous remarks by Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260107_11807882.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260107_11807855.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 7, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua first announced two decisions: listing Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao as “diehard Taiwan independence” elements, and listing Chen Shu-yi as a “Taiwan independence” accomplice and henchman. He then answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button…","Dear journalists, Happy New Year. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\nFirst, I will announce two decisions made by the mainland side. First, Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao are listed as 'Taiwan independence' diehards, and punitive measures will be imposed on them in accordance with the law. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots, the same language, and the same culture, and wanting peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides. Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao have persisted in acting against the public interest, and their 'Taiwan independence' crimes are numerous, which has aroused strong indignation among compatriots on both sides. Many people have reported to the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, demanding that the two individuals be punished.\nLiu Shih-fang blatantly promotes 'Taiwan independence' separatist fallacies, extensively suppresses Taiwanese personnel who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, persecutes mainland spouses in Taiwan, does everything possible to create obstacles to cross-Strait personnel exchanges, and blocks channels of communication and exchange between compatriots on both sides. Cheng Ying-yao extensively promotes provocative remarks aimed at seeking 'independence,' organizes the compilation of 'Taiwan independence' textbooks that poison young people on the island, and obstructs cross-Strait educational exchanges and cooperation. Liu and Cheng are stubborn in their 'Taiwan independence' ideology, arrogant in their 'independence'-related remarks, and vile in their 'independence'-seeking conduct. They openly split the country and incite the splitting of the country, seriously damage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, gravely endanger the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and seriously harm the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nIn accordance with relevant laws and regulations, the mainland side has decided to include Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao on the list of 'Taiwan independence' diehards and impose sanctions on them. Liu, Cheng, and their family members are prohibited from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions. Cooperation between Liu and Cheng's affiliated institutions and relevant mainland organizations and individuals is restricted. Their affiliated enterprises and financial backers are absolutely not allowed to profit on the mainland, and all other necessary punitive measures will be taken, with permanent accountability pursued in accordance with the law. We welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait to continue providing clues regarding the illegal and criminal activities of Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao.\n'Taiwan independence' separatism is a grave calamity for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. Punishing a very small number of 'Taiwan independence' diehards in accordance with the law is aimed at fundamentally safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and protecting the vital interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. It is by no means directed at the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the harmful nature, sinister intentions, and ugly faces of the very small number of 'Taiwan independence' diehards, consciously draw a clear line with Liu Shih-fang, Cheng Ying-yao, and other 'Taiwan independence' diehards, resolutely oppose 'Taiwan independence' separatist conduct, firmly promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation, and jointly create lasting well-being for compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond, Chen Shu-yi, the 'green judicial henchman,' is listed as a 'Taiwan independence' henchman and accomplice, and permanent accountability will be pursued in accordance with the law. After investigation, it has been found that Chen Shu-yi, a prosecutor of Taiwan's 'Supreme Prosecutors Office,' has willingly served as a 'Taiwan independence' henchman and accomplice, fabricated charges, manufactured false cases, persecuted Taiwanese personnel who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, intimidated Taiwanese residents, and created a 'green terror.' Chen Shu-yi's actions are vile in nature and grave in criminal conduct. We hereby continue to solicit from cross-Strait society clues and evidence of Chen Shu-yi's illegal and criminal activities (which may be sent to the email address: jubao@suremail.cn). We will base our actions on facts and the law, and will severely punish Chen Shu-yi in accordance with the law and pursue permanent accountability.\nNow, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745027.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","In his 2026 New Year message, President Xi Jinping stressed that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are of one blood, and the historical trend of national reunification cannot be stopped.” What is the Taiwan Affairs Office's interpretation of this, and how will it be implemented?","President Xi Jinping’s New Year’s address is lofty in vision, profound in thought and rich in meaning. It profoundly points out that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same culture and lineage, and form a community of shared destiny, bound by blood and sharing honor and disgrace. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese descendants. As the process of building a strong country and advancing national rejuvenation moves forward in all respects, we have greater capability, greater confidence and greater resolve to turn this aspiration into reality. The wheel of history for national reunification and national rejuvenation rolls forward. Complete reunification of the motherland must be achieved, and it certainly will be.\nWe will thoroughly implement the spirit of President Xi Jinping’s New Year’s address, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and interference by external forces, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will follow the trend of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, and work with us to jointly safeguard the beautiful homeland of the Chinese nation, create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and share the great glory of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745026.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council, delivered a New Year’s message titled “Forging Ahead Together, Creating Well-Being” (《携手奋进 共创福祉》). Please interpret it.","On January 2, Director Song Tao issued a New Year message. He first extended, on behalf of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, New Year greetings and sincere regards to Taiwan compatriots across the island. The message reviewed the work on Taiwan affairs in 2025, describing it as a year in which all Chinese people remembered history and shared in glory, Chinese-style modernization carried on the past and opened the future, and cross-strait relations advanced through difficulties while the momentum for national reunification gathered strength. It noted that over the past year, cross-strait exchanges and cooperation achieved a series of new progress, the forces protecting the peace and tranquility of our shared home grew stronger, and more measures benefiting the well-being of Taiwan compatriots were introduced. It called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to follow the trend, seize the momentum, and join hands to create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation and jointly write a splendid chapter of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe message set out the key tasks for Taiwan affairs this year, making clear that we will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification. We will create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, work, and live on the mainland, further expand exchanges and cooperation, deepen integrated development, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, support patriotic unification forces on the island, and carry out dialogue and consultation on cross-strait relations and national reunification with Taiwan's political parties, political groups, and far-sighted people from all sectors. We hope Taiwan compatriots will work with us to firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation and join in the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745025.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Please summarize the development of cross-Strait relations in 2025 and look ahead to cross-Strait relations in 2026.","2025 was a year in which cross-Strait relations moved forward through difficulties and the motherland's unification gathered momentum. We firmly grasped the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations, pushed cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development to a higher level, demonstrated a greater ability to deter “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, accumulated stronger momentum for advancing national reunification, and gathered more powerful strength for advancing the great cause of national rejuvenation.\nFirst, break through obstacles and continue expanding cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We have worked to break through the obstruction and restrictions of the DPP authorities, continued to expand travel and exchanges between people on both sides across all fields, and promoted closer and deeper cross-Strait cooperation, bringing compatriots on both sides closer together. We have substantially increased ports where Taiwan compatriots can apply for permits upon arrival, and introduced policies such as waiving the Taiwan Compatriot Permit fee for “first-time visitors” and airfare discounts, providing “wider opening, greatest convenience and greater safety” for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. We successfully held the Straits Forum, the Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit, the Cross-Strait Grassroots Livelihood Development Exchange Conference and other exchange activities, leading a wave of cross-Strait exchanges. The number of Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan youth and “first-time visitors” coming to the mainland has increased substantially. More and more Taiwan compatriots personally appreciate the magnificent beauty of the motherland's rivers and mountains, feel the myriad sights of Chinese-style modernization, and experience the unique charm of Chinese culture, taking pride in being upright and dignified Chinese people.\nSecond, continue to deepen cross-Strait integrated development and share the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization. The Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th CPC Central Committee deliberated and adopted the recommendations for the 15th Five-Year Plan, which provide top-level design and strategic blueprint for the next five years, provide powerful impetus for Chinese-style modernization, and also open broader space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises to put down roots and develop on the mainland. We respect, care for and benefit Taiwan compatriots, implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and promote the effective implementation of policies and measures benefiting Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. We have pushed forward high-quality construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, issued a new batch of policies and measures to deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and Fujian's integrated development has achieved new progress and new results. We held the 2025 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit annual meeting and dozens of cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities, sharing with the broad mass of Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization. We effectively responded to external tariff bullying, defended the Chinese nation's economy, and safeguarded the interests of Taiwan businesses and enterprises on the mainland. More and more Taiwan compatriots have profoundly recognized that both sides of the Strait are a community of shared destiny that cannot be separated, and that the mainland has always been a strong backing for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.\nThird, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and firmly safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation. We held a symposium marking the 20th anniversary of the implementation of the Anti-Secession Law, carried out the “Strait Thunder-2025A” and “Justice Mission-2025” drills and exercises, firmly defended national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely safeguarded the common interests of compatriots on both sides and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We have punished, in accordance with the law, die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and their henchmen and accomplices, effectively deterring “Taiwan independence” separatist forces from seeking “independence” and provocations. We have firmly upheld the authority of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, continued to consolidate the one-China pattern in the international community, and effectively curbed external forces playing the “Taiwan card.” We unite broad Taiwan compatriots, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” jointly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, firmly safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation, and keep the destiny of the nation firmly in the hands of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. More and more people on the island see the historical trend that the motherland will inevitably be reunified, and have voiced hope for cross-Strait relations to return to the track of peaceful development.\nOn the eve of the New Year 2026, President Xi Jinping delivered a New Year's address, extending New Year's greetings to Chinese people at home and abroad, in which he stressed: “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are bound by blood, and the historical trend of national reunification cannot be stopped.” In the new year, we will thoroughly implement the overall strategy of the new era for resolving the Taiwan question, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, unite broad Taiwan compatriots, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will continuously strengthen their resolve, backbone and confidence as Chinese people, and join us in unremitting efforts to promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification, and strive together for a better future for the Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745024.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","The spokesperson just announced two decisions by the mainland side. In recent years, the mainland has published multiple batches of lists of “Taiwan independence” diehards and “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices. How many people are currently on each of these lists? Will the mainland further intensify punishment and bring them to justice? Some public opinion on the island claims that the mainland's…","“Taiwan independence” elements are criminals who split the country and undermine cross-Strait relations, and are also national traitors who incite war for “independence” and harm the interests and well-being of compatriots. To date, we have published a list of 14 diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and 12 “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices. Any “Taiwan independence” element who breaks the law, wherever they are, will face all necessary measures, be punished in accordance with the law, and be held accountable for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745018.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Please briefly introduce the cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2025, including its main characteristics. What is your outlook for cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation in 2026?","2025 was the concluding year of the 14th Five-Year Plan. Under the strong leadership of the Communist Party of China Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, the Chinese mainland's economy has forged ahead against headwinds and developed toward new and better directions, providing strong support and powerful impetus for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integration and development.\nFirst, sustained and healthy development of Taiwanese compatriot businesses and enterprises on the mainland. Localities have introduced a series of measures to continuously support the development of Taiwanese compatriot businesses and enterprises on the mainland. Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland have maintained stable production and operations, and Taiwanese investment and cross-Strait economic and trade have maintained a growth momentum. From January to October last year, the mainland newly established 6,423 Taiwan-funded enterprises, with actual utilized Taiwan investment of US$1.75 billion, up 53% year on year. From January to November, cross-Strait trade reached US$285.395 billion, up 7.3% year on year.\nSecond, cross-Strait integrated development has taken new steps. We have strengthened policy supply and improved supporting policies, and promoted the implementation of key tasks for the construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone. More than 30 units have issued a series of supporting documents and policy measures, and a new pattern of integrated development across all of Fujian is taking shape. From January to October last year, trade between Fujian and Taiwan reached RMB 72.82 billion, 2,043 Taiwan-funded enterprises were newly established, and actual utilization of Taiwan investment reached US$670 million.\nThird, cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation have opened new horizons. We have adopted a series of policy measures to facilitate cross-Strait personnel exchanges and promote cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, held numerous cross-Strait economic and trade exchange events, and extensively invited business associations and prominent business figures from the island to visit. More and more Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland to experience its magnificent landscapes and rapidly changing development. According to statistics, cross-Strait airlines operate more than 610 passenger flights per week. From January to November last year, 'mini three links' services operated 10,997 times, up 38.69% year on year, carrying 1.7543 million passengers, up 45.77% year on year.\nFourth, new progress has been made in building cross-Strait cooperation platforms. We steadily advance the Straits Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone and cross-Strait cooperation platforms such as Pingtan, Kunshan, and Dongguan, promote the opening of emerging mainland industrial chains to Taiwanese compatriot businesses and enterprises, and encourage localities to precisely carry out cross-Strait industrial matchmaking. A batch of key Taiwan-funded projects have gone into production, and cross-Strait industrial and supply chain cooperation continues to rise in level, expand in scope, and grow in resilience.\n2026 is the opening year of the 15th Five-Year Plan. We will be guided by the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, the successive plenary sessions of the 20th Central Committee, and the Central Economic Work Conference. We will thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on Taiwan work and the overall strategy of the Party in the new era for resolving the Taiwan question, continuously improve the institutions and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, advance high-quality construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone, strengthen industrial cooperation, and promote cross-Strait economic cooperation. We will implement the policy of granting Taiwan compatriots equal treatment, providing more opportunities, a better environment, and a broader stage for Taiwan compatriots to settle down and develop on the mainland. We will actively help Taiwanese compatriot businesses and enterprises integrate into the new development pattern and achieve high-quality development, advance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and jointly grow the Chinese nation's economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745023.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","A mainland blogger self-funded the purchase of “Jilin-1” satellite imagery and exposed the residence and workplace of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council claimed that if the mainland does not take down the relevant content, it would “have no choice but to review cross-strait exchanges in response.” Subsequently, the DPP authorities demanded that relevant…","“Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang is a disgrace to the nation and a lawbreaker who has undermined cross-Strait relations, split the country, and stirred up conflict in pursuit of “independence.” This blogger's spontaneous act reflects the broad public's firm opposition to “Taiwan independence” and their contempt for what Shen Boyang has said and done.\nThe DPP authorities brutally suppressed relevant accounts and threatened to “review cross-Strait exchanges,” fully confirming that they are birds of a feather with Shen Boyang. This fully exposes the hypocrisy of their so-called “freedom of speech” and fully reveals their true face of inciting cross-Strait opposition and confrontation and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges. In punishing “Taiwan independence” diehards, our will is as firm as a rock, and our actions are resolute and decisive.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","Please introduce the situation of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2025. What are the main characteristics? What are the plans for cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges in various fields in 2026?","In 2025, we resolutely broke through the obstruction and restrictions imposed by the DPP authorities, continuously advanced cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in various fields, and continuously improved the institutional and policy arrangements for Taiwan compatriots to integrate into mainland development. Over the past year, cross-Strait exchanges have been vibrant and full of highlights, and compatriots on both sides have grown closer, with deep feelings of friendship. Specifically, the following characteristics have emerged:\nFirst, the scale of cross-Strait personnel exchanges has continued to expand. Over the past year, following the principle of \"greater openness, greatest convenience, and enhanced safety,\" we announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, and introduced measures such as waiving the document fee for the Taiwan compatriot certificate for \"first-time visitors\" (首来族) from Taiwan, expanding the number of ports where Taiwan compatriots can apply for documents on arrival from 58 to 100, issuing electronic temporary Taiwan compatriot certificates to Taiwan compatriots who have lost their documents, and including Taiwan compatriots in the pilot scope of the policy allowing passage without presenting documents. This series of convenience measures has continuously released momentum to support and promote exchanges between compatriots on both sides and created favorable conditions. In 2025, cross-Strait personnel exchanges exceeded 5 million person-trips, reaching a six-year high.\nSecond, cross-Strait exchange activities have been outstanding. Over the past year, regions and departments held diverse and content-rich cross-Strait exchange activities. Cross-Strait cultural exchanges and grassroots exchanges continued to surge, and exchanges and cooperation were widely carried out in education, publishing, medicine and health, sports, news, trade unions, women, ethnic minorities, religious belief, and other fields and sectors. Tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots enthusiastically participated in large-scale cross-Strait exchange events such as the 17th Straits Forum and the 2nd Straits Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit, demonstrating a new atmosphere of heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides in the new era and on the new journey. Around the important milestone of the 80th anniversary of Taiwan's restoration, we held the Conference Commemorating the 80th Anniversary of Taiwan's Restoration, established a reception for Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, and published and distributed the \"Chronicle of Major Events in the Chinese Nation's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression.\" Compatriots on both sides jointly remember history and carry forward the spirit of the War of Resistance.\nThird, cross-Strait youth exchanges have been vibrant. Regions and departments either upgraded and expanded existing large-scale flagship events or created new exchange platforms, incorporating and making good use of elements such as intangible cultural heritage, Chinese animation (国漫), and sports. Cross-Strait youth exchange activities such as the 2025 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the 5th Straits Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, and the 12th Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour attracted tens of thousands of Taiwan youth to the mainland, where they made friends, exchanged hearts with mainland youth, discussed their friendship together, and worked hand in hand toward a shared future.\nFourth, practices of cross-Strait integrated development have achieved phased results. Relevant departments and Fujian Province actively implemented the \"Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,\" vigorously promoted pilot practices of policies that benefit Taiwan and its people, provided better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, work, and live in Fujian, and pushed the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone to take solid steps forward. The system of equal-treatment policies has become increasingly complete, and Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth have actively joined mainland development, shared its opportunities, and reaped fruitful results in professional exchanges and project cooperation.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share common blood, common culture, and common history, bear common responsibility for the nation, and share common hopes for the future. In 2026, we will resolutely implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important exposition on work concerning Taiwan and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. We will continuously deepen cross-Strait exchange, interaction, and integration, strive to promote heart-to-heart connection between compatriots on both sides, solidly advance peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and unwaveringly advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745022.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","A Taiwan poll shows that on issues related to cross-Strait conflict, more than 60% of Taiwan residents do not want themselves or their family members to go to the battlefield. What is your comment?","Facts prove that more and more Taiwan compatriots have come to recognize that “Taiwan independence” means war. They recognize that the Lai Ching-te authorities' insistence on seeking independence will only bring war to Taiwan, and that condoning and supporting “Taiwan independence” will only turn themselves and their families into cannon fodder.\nPeace is the common pursuit of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and unification is the only direction for Taiwan's future. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots, starting from the great righteousness of the nation and from their own security and well-being, will resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, join us in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and creating a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","The “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes across the Strait have now been in operation for 25 years. How do you evaluate the role of the “Mini Three Links” in promoting exchanges and contacts across the Strait?","The “Xiao San Tong” (Mini Three Links) routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially between the people of Fujian and Taiwan. They have played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integration and development and enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. The “Xiao San Tong” began with routes between Xiamen and Kinmen and between Matsu and Mawei, and now there are four regular routes, closely linking Fujian’s coast with Kinmen and Matsu, and opening a new era of direct civilian exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. At present, the “Xiao San Tong” has become the “first pathway” for building a “first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses on the Mainland,” the “golden artery” deepening economic and trade cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan and even across the Taiwan Strait, and the “emotional bond” promoting deep integration across the Taiwan Strait. To date, the “Xiao San Tong” has safely transported more than 26 million passengers.\nWith the shortest voyage and the most convenient means, the “Xiao San Tong” has genuinely brought the hearts of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait closer. Its successful practice vividly proves that moving closer and visiting relatives is what the hearts of the people on both sides desire, and an irresistible trend of the times. With the support of the people and the gathering of collective strength, the path of cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development will surely grow ever broader.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745020.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Please introduce the exchanges and dialogues conducted in 2025 with Taiwan political parties, groups and representative figures. What are the plans for 2026?","In 2025, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we maintained positive interaction with relevant political parties, groups and representative figures in Taiwan, consolidated and enhanced mutual trust, strengthened exchanges and cooperation, and achieved positive results.\nFirst, we provided direction for the development of cross-Strait relations. On October 19, General Secretary Xi Jinping of the CPC Central Committee sent a congratulatory message to Cheng Li-wun on her election as Chairperson of the Kuomintang (KMT), pointing out that over the years the two parties have, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, worked to safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and enhanced the well-being and emotional ties of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, with positive results. On the same day, Cheng Li-wun replied to General Secretary Xi Jinping to express her thanks. General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory message has pointed the way for the development of relations between the two parties and cross-Strait relations, and has drawn wide attention and high praise from all sectors on both sides of the Strait and from the international community.\nSecond, we commemorated the 80th anniversary of Japan's defeat in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan, jointly remembering history and defending its achievements. Representatives of political parties and groups in Taiwan, including the KMT, the New Party, the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union and the People First Party, were invited to attend the commemorative events marking the 80th anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. Wang Huning, Chairman of the CPPCC National Committee, met with Hung Hsiu-chu and other representatives of Taiwan circles attending the commemorative events, encouraging compatriots on both sides of the Strait to bear in mind together the history of the national war of resistance, defend the fruits of victory in the war of resistance, and join hands to advance peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the process of national reunification. The restoration of Taiwan is a shared glory of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and a national memory of all descendants of the Chinese nation. Relevant political parties, groups and sectors in Taiwan held commemorative and celebratory events in diverse forms, honoring the heroic deeds of martyrs, expressing national sentiment, sharing the pride and dignity of being upright Chinese, and safeguarding the common homeland of the Chinese nation.\nThird, we added momentum to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Ma Ying-jeou, Hung Hsiu-chu, Wu Cheng-tien, Lin Ping-kun and other representative figures from the KMT, the New Party, the People First Party, the Non-Partisan Solidarity Union and other parties and groups led delegations to the mainland to take part in cross-Strait exchange activities such as the 17th Straits Forum, the Cross-Strait Grassroots Livelihood Development Exchange Conference, and the 2025 Cross-Strait Compatriots' Mid-Autumn Festival Friendship Gathering, and to visit and tour, voicing positive views on adhering to the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nFourth, we brought benefits to compatriots in Taiwan. Relevant parties on both sides of the Strait jointly held the 5th “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar,” reaching five points of consensus, including adhering to one China and safeguarding the common homeland. People of insight from all sectors on both sides of the Strait held dialogues on issues such as the situation in the Taiwan Strait, cross-Strait relations and prospects for unification, issuing a strong call to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and to promote national reunification and the realization of national rejuvenation. Several county and city heads from Taiwan led delegations to visit, the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum was successfully held, and exchanges between counties, cities and municipalities across the Strait continued to expand, with results steadily emerging. Tangible progress was made in areas such as the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, cross-Strait youth exchanges, and the sharing of experience in urban management and grassroots governance.\nIn the new year, we will focus on the situation in the Taiwan Strait and changes in the development of cross-Strait relations. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions and directives and the Party Central Committee's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work. On the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will deepen exchanges with relevant political parties, groups and representative figures in Taiwan, enhance mutual understanding, and consolidate mutual trust, uniting broad numbers of compatriots in Taiwan to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to contribute to the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745021.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","According to Taiwan media reports, a DPP elected representative has proposed amending the current “Act Governing Relations between the Peoples of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” in Taiwan, using “Taiwan and the People’s Republic of China” to define cross-Strait relations, and deleting the words “before national reunification” from the original provision. Other media reports say the proposer has withdrawn…","We are paying close attention to the relevant developments. This proposal disregards the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and the peace and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, openly challenges the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, and attempts to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, in which there is only one China and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. It blatantly promotes “de jure Taiwan independence”, deliberately escalates tensions across the Taiwan Strait, undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the region, and its intentions are malicious and its nature is vile. This fully demonstrates that the Lai Ching-te authorities and the DPP are unmistakable “disruptors of peace”, “makers of crisis” and “instigators of war”.\n“Taiwan independence” means war; it is a dead end. We have full confidence and sufficient capability to crush any form of “de jure Taiwan independence” schemes, and we will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan away from China under any name or by any means!\nHistory has proven, and will continue to prove, that “Taiwan independence” separatism will never end well and will only lead to total defeat. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to take desperate risks and cross the red line, we will certainly act resolutely in accordance with the Anti-Secession Law and deliver a head-on blow. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the evil nature and serious harm of “Taiwan independence”, firmly stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and join us in safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and protecting our common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260107_12745019.htm"],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Taiwan's “Beautiful Island Electronic Journal” recently released its latest poll, showing 52.2% of the public are dissatisfied with Lai Ching-te's governance, and dissatisfaction has exceeded 50% for six consecutive months. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","For some time now, the Lai Ching-te authorities have escalated their peddling of “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies and constant provocations toward “independence,” obstructing and restricting cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. They manipulate “anti-China and resist-China” rhetoric, suppress political dissidents, create a “green terror,” and deepen social division on the island. They forcibly push cross-Strait economic “decoupling and severing of supply chains,” hollow out Taiwan’s advantageous industries, and, with no bottom line, sell out Taiwan and pledge loyalty to external forces, harming the interests and well-being of enterprises and the public on the island. These acts, which serve only political self-interest while disregarding people’s livelihood and development, seriously depart from mainstream public opinion on the island and are not supported by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","In his New Year’s speech, Lai Ching-te extensively played up the so-called “ambition of China’s expansion” and its “threat” to Taiwan, and agitated for “strengthening national defense and security resilience and comprehensively building effective deterrence and democratic defense mechanisms.” What is your comment?","We have already made a written response on this, stating our position. Lai Ching-te's remarks are full of lies and delusional talk, hostility and malice. He once again peddles the “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy, incites cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, rehashes the old line of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” and attempts to delude Taiwan's public and mislead international opinion. This once again exposes that his “Taiwan independence” stance is stubborn and his confrontational mindset is obstinate, fully confirming that he is an out-and-out “peace breaker,” “crisis manufacturer,” and “war instigator.”\nSince taking office, Lai Ching-te has defied the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society, obstinately clung to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, continuously concocted separatist fallacies, deliberately escalated cross-Strait opposition, and aggravated tensions in the Taiwan Strait. In pursuit of political self-interest, he has lavishly squandered the people's hard-earned money, vigorously pursued “preparing for war to seek independence” and “everyone a soldier,” tied the people to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, and pushed Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war. He toadies to and surrenders to external forces, selling out Taiwan, and seriously harming the vital interests of Taiwan's people and enterprises. Within the island, he implements “authoritarian rule,” wantonly tramples on democracy, undermines the rule of law, and restricts freedoms, vigorously carrying out “green terror” and partisan persecution, and creating a “chilling effect.” Who with such a record of wrongdoing has the qualifications and face to talk about “democracy,” “freedom,” “justice,” and “solidarity”?\nNo matter what Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor the inevitable fate of “Taiwan independence” being defeated. The great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable, and the complete reunification of the motherland will surely be achieved. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the evil nature and grave harm of “Taiwan independence,” firmly stand on the right side of history, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and join us in safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and jointly creating a fine new chapter of national rejuvenation and motherland reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan’s security authorities recently released a so-called “report” claiming that in 2025 the mainland, in combination with military exercises and other timing, carried out a so-called “comprehensive intrusion” against Taiwan’s key infrastructure, with cyberattacks averaging 2.63 million per day. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities are accustomed to fabricating rumors, slandering, and smearing the mainland, and to manipulating “resist China, protect Taiwan,” attempting to divert public dissatisfaction with their incompetent governance and to seek political self-interest. In fact, the DPP authorities frequently direct military intelligence agencies and cyber forces to launch cyberattacks and sabotage against the mainland. Relevant mainland departments have previously solved and made public the criminal facts of cyberattacks against the mainland by organizations involved, including the Taiwan military's “Psychological Warfare Battalion,” Taiwan's Wang Shi Art Creation Company, and “Anonymous 64.” The so-called “report” from the DPP authorities is nothing but a guilty conscience and a counterattack!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","KMT legislator Chen Yu-chen proposed a “draft amendment to certain articles of the Offshore Islands Development Act,” which adds provisions to establish “free trade demonstration zones” in Kinmen and Matsu. The Green camp criticized this as paving the way for a “One Country, Two Systems” experimental zone. The Mainland Affairs Council said that the cross-Strait situation is complex at present, and that matters…","We welcome and support anything that benefits the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including the development of Kinmen and Matsu. The DPP authorities, in pursuit of political self-interest, disregard the wishes of the public and the development needs of Kinmen and Matsu, ignore the livelihoods and appeals of the people of Kinmen and Matsu, stand against public opinion, and have lost popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Liu Shih-fang, Shen Boyang, and others, who were previously listed as “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices, have also been listed as “Taiwan independence” die-hard elements. How does the mainland plan to clarify and handle this? Second question: Regarding the mainland's publication of the lists of “Taiwan independence” die-hard elements and “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices, the…","First question. If “Taiwan independence” henchmen and accomplices incite secession of the country, and their words and deeds of splitting the country become more rampant and their criminal acts more serious, they will be listed as “diehard Taiwan independence” elements.\nSecond question. We have answered many times that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","The United States recently sent troops to forcibly take control of Venezuelan President Maduro and his wife and transfer them out of the country, which has drawn attention. Commentators on the island are worried that the mainland will imitate the U.S. approach to justify taking action against Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","The US has brazenly used force against a sovereign state. This seriously violates international law, infringes on another country's sovereignty, and threatens regional peace and security. We firmly oppose this. This is the first point I want to make.\nSecond point: Taiwan is China's Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. If the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces dare to take a desperate risk and cross the red line, we will certainly take resolute measures and deal them a head-on blow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS电视台记者","First question: The Taiwanese internet celebrity “Good Night Chicken,” who is serving a sentence in Cambodia, is about to be released, and there are rumors that he will be deported to mainland China. Does the Taiwan Affairs Office have more information? Second question: Recently, Japanese Senator Seki Hei, who was sanctioned by the mainland and barred from entering it, went to Taiwan and promoted the idea that…","First question: I have noted the relevant reports. We will handle the relevant matters in accordance with the law.\nSecond question: The ravings of petty villains are not worth commenting on.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-07","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Regarding a Green-camp legislator's proposal to amend the “Cross-Strait People's Relations Act,” the Taiwan Affairs Office stated that if “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to take risks and touch the red line, they will take resolute measures in accordance with the “Anti-Secession Law.” Could you further explain what measures would be taken? Some public opinion in Taiwan holds that this…","First question. On January 4, we already stated our position on this matter. I would like to stress two points again. First, we have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to crush any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. Article 8 of the Anti-Secession Law expressly provides: “In the event that ‘Taiwan independence’ secessionist forces should act under any name or by any means to cause the fact of Taiwan’s secession from China, or that major incidents entailing Taiwan’s secession from China should occur, or that possibilities for a peaceful reunification should be completely exhausted, the State may employ non-peaceful means and other necessary measures to protect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.” This clearly draws a red line that must not be crossed. We will never stand by and let any form of “de jure Taiwan independence” go unchecked. Whoever breaks the law will surely be smashed to pieces.\nSecond, the DPP authorities constantly promote “Taiwan independence” fallacies, carry out provocations aimed at independence, incite “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, seriously undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Compatriots in Taiwan must truly recognize the grave harm of “Taiwan independence,” and join us in resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguarding the common home of the Chinese nation.\nSecond question. The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at independence. “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct seriously undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and seriously harms the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We will absolutely not tolerate it and will not show leniency.\nOur compatriots in Taiwan are our flesh and blood. We have always upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” respect, care for, and bring benefits to Taiwan compatriots. We have always firmly held the initiative and leadership in cross-Strait relations, and promoted cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development. Our sincerity and goodwill in increasing the family affection and well-being of compatriots on both sides will not change, and our measures will not stop. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the evil nature and ugly face of the DPP authorities, consciously draw a clear line with the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and their activities, join us in maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, jointly safeguarding the beautiful common home of the Chinese nation, and firmly advancing the great cause of national reunification.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260107_12745029.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-01-09","Mao Ning","Beijing Daily","On January 8, Foreign Minister Wang Yi and the Chairperson of the African Union (AU) Commission Mahmoud Ali Youssouf chaired the ninth China-AU Strategic Dialogue at the AU headquarters. Could you share more details? How does China view its current relations with the AU?","The AU is a banner for Africa to seek strength through unity. China always develops relations with the AU from a strategic height and long-term perspective. The dialogue is an important strategic communication between China and the AU after the newly elected leadership of the AU Commission took office. Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Chairperson Mahmoud Ali Youssouf had an in-depth exchange of views on China-Africa relations, China-AU cooperation and international and regional issues of mutual interest, which deepened strategic mutual trust, enhanced mutual support, and consolidated solidarity and cooperation.\nBoth sides agreed that under the strategic guidance of President Xi Jinping and African leaders, China-Africa relations have grown by leaps and bounds and entered a new stage of jointly building the all-weather China-Africa community with a shared future for the new era. Both sides agreed to continue firmly supporting each other on issues concerning core interests and major concerns and to enhance communication, coordination and mutual support in respective major initiatives. The two sides will jointly uphold the international order based on international law and safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of the Global South. The AU side reaffirmed its firm commitment to the one-China principle and firm support for all efforts by the Chinese government to achieve national reunification.\nWe stand ready to work with the AU to implement the outcomes of the dialogue and continue to explore the full potential for practical cooperation between the two sides to deliver more tangibly for the Chinese and African people.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260109_11810122.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260109_11810157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-01-09","Mao Ning","Reuters","U.S. President Donald Trump told The New York Times he would be “very unhappy” if China sought to change the status quo over Taiwan during his presidency, as analysts draw comparisons between the U.S.’s strike on Venezuela and what lessons China might take from it. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment on President Trump’s remarks?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and brooks no external interference.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260109_11810122.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260109_11810157.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-01-12","Mao Ning","Beijing Youth Daily","It’s reported Taiwan said on January 9 that the Taiwan-related part in the Joint Press Release of the China-African Union Strategic Dialogue is a serious distortion of facts and undermines the island’s “sovereignty,” and called the African Union (AU) aligning with Beijing’s stance regrettable. What’s China’s comment?","The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. It is also the political foundation of relations between China and African countries. The 2024 Beijing Summit of the Forum on China-Africa Cooperation adopted the Beijing Declaration, in which participating African countries and the AU Commission reaffirmed their firm commitment to the one-China principle and reaffirmed that there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. They also expressed their firm support to all efforts by the Chinese government to achieve national reunification. The Joint Press Release of the 9th China-AU Strategic Dialogue fully and faithfully represents the consistent and clear stance of the African side on the Taiwan question. The AU Commission Chairperson Mahmoud Ali Youssouf said in an interview on Friday that “We will be on board with China on the issue of one-China principle forever.”\nWe urge the Taiwan authorities to see the facts and stop its poor political stunts that will only disgrace itself.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260112_11811345.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260112_11811154.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning everyone, welcome to the press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Now we begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Regarding the Taiwan Affairs Office’s announcement that it has listed Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao as die-hard “Taiwan independence” separatists and Chen Shu-yi as a “Taiwan independence” thug and accomplice, the DPP authorities said, “The mainland has no jurisdiction over the Taiwan people,” and that they will take necessary action and draft countermeasures. What comments do you have on this?","Taiwan is Taiwan of China. Anyone who endangers the country's sovereignty, security, or development interests will not escape the sanctions of national law. Die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" elements and their accomplices who split the country, undermine cross-Strait relations, and harm the interests and well-being of compatriots will be punished in accordance with the law and held accountable for life. They have brought this upon themselves.\nPunishing die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" elements and their accomplices in accordance with the law is an inherent part of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and is also a just action to safeguard the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. We act in accordance with justice and the law, and we will absolutely not show leniency or hesitation.\nWe hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will clearly recognize the harmful nature, sinister intentions, and ugly faces of the very few \"Taiwan independence\" elements who harm Taiwan, resolutely draw a clear line with them, firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The TAO recently announced that Liu Shih-fang and Cheng Ying-yao have been listed as “diehard ‘Taiwan independence’ elements,” and Chen Shu-yi as a “‘Taiwan independence’ thug and accomplice.” In response, Lai Ching-te said, “I am proud of any people who are subjected to cross-border repression by China,” and “China’s hand will never be allowed to reach into this land of Taiwan.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. “Taiwan independence” elements split the country and undermine cross-Strait relations. We will take all necessary punitive measures and hold them accountable for life in accordance with the law. The more frantic “Taiwan independence” elements become on the path to “Taiwan independence,” the tighter the rope against “independence” will be pulled. Awaiting them will be the judgment of justice and a fate of disgrace and ruin.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746149.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Taiwan media reported that the “KMT-CCP Forum” will take place in Beijing, and senior Kuomintang officials will travel to the mainland. Can this be confirmed? The DPP questioned whether the KMT is trading for tickets to the “KMT-CCP Forum” by repeatedly blocking arms procurement bills, and called on the KMT not to cooperate with mainland “united front” propaganda. What is your comment on this?","Our position is clear: on the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to, together with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang, strengthen exchanges and interactions, maintain positive interaction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait. If there is relevant information in this regard, we will release it in a timely manner.\nIt should be pointed out that the DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist position, attempt to \"seek independence by relying on external forces\" and \"seek independence by force,\" constantly fabricate rumors and slander, obstruct and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, incite \"anti-China and resist-China\" sentiment, and create a \"green terror,\" seeking to deceive the Taiwan people and gain political self-interest. Their actions completely violate the mainstream public opinion on the island that seeks peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, seriously harm the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots, and push Taiwan into a precarious situation of turmoil and danger of war. All sectors of Taiwan society have expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","At the beginning of the new year, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have been lively and vibrant.\nIn cultural exchange, the 15th Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao Film Directors Seminar, sponsored by the China Film Directors' Guild, was held in Guangzhou from January 11 to 12. Nearly 200 film directors from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao gathered together and discussed topics such as the new wave of film technology and film creation in a diversified market. They unanimously looked forward to strengthening exchanges among film directors and further promoting joint film cooperation and creation.\nIn youth exchange, in mid-to-late January, cross-strait youth exchange activities themed on welcoming the Spring Festival, ice and snow experiences, and similar topics were successively held in Beijing, Tianjin, Shandong, Hubei, Sichuan, and other places. It is estimated that more than 1,000 Taiwan youths will take part in the relevant activities.\nReading ten thousand books is not enough; one must also travel ten thousand miles. In the new year, we will continue to open our doors and welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young people, to come to the mainland. Use your feet to measure the magnificent mountains and rivers of our great motherland, use your heart to feel the profound heritage of Chinese civilization, and use your eyes to observe the development and changes across the mainland. If you love the cultural charm of the poetry and lyrics you've read, come and see for yourself the red walls and black-tiled roofs, the misty rain of Jiangnan, and the zen temples. If you are passionate about lively sports, come and watch the “Provincial Super League” and the “Village Super League” in person. If you are curious about how artificial intelligence is changing life, come and experience driverless vehicles and drone shows on the spot, or even try drone farming. If you prefer down-to-earth city life, go to the alleys and markets of various places to experience the most authentic everyday life and the deep friendship among compatriots.\nIn the new year, we welcome more Taiwan compatriots to begin a new journey to the mainland, and we believe that even more pleasant surprises are waiting for everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Earlier, the spokesperson mentioned that after the “Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson” Facebook account was launched, some Taiwan netizens left messages hoping to help find their relatives on the mainland. What progress has been made so far?","Since the “Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” Facebook account was opened in October 2025, it has received high attention from the Taiwan public, who hope to receive some help through this platform. Recently, we received nearly 10 messages from Taiwan netizens hoping we would help them find their relatives on the mainland. We take every help-seeking message seriously, and have coordinated with relevant local Taiwan Affairs Offices to promptly contact and communicate with Taiwan netizens, understand and verify the situation, and actively advance the search for relatives. Thanks to the joint efforts of many parties, there is good news to report: the provincial, municipal, and county-level Taiwan Affairs Offices of Hubei Province, Huanggang City, and Huangmei County worked closely together and have helped one of the Taiwan netizens find his relatives who had been separated for many years in Huangmei. Arrangements are being discussed for his return home to worship his ancestors.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, connected by blood. When Taiwan compatriots come to seek their relatives, the Taiwan Affairs Office will certainly help (in Hakka)! Compatriots on both sides are one family, and frequent visits bring hearts closer together (in Hokkien)! We welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to pay more attention to the “Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” Facebook account. We will also continue to strengthen information release and services, and provide practical help and support for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to seek relatives and roots, exchange, and visit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746145.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Recently, films, TV shows and games produced on the Mainland have become increasingly popular among Taiwan residents, especially Taiwan youth. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, mainland film, television, games, and other cultural industries have flourished, with outstanding works emerging frequently, and they are widely welcomed at home and abroad. Outstanding products that blend traditional cultural elements with modern innovation and fashion are especially popular among island residents, particularly young people.\nIt is understood that the first AIGC (AI-generated content) animated film, “Reunion Decree” (团圆令), will be released nationwide in the near future. The film centers on the animated IP characters “Tuanzi” and “Yuanniu” (团仔 and 圆妞), based on the giant pandas “Tuantuan” and “Yuanyuan” that the mainland gifted to Taiwan residents. It tells the story of Tuanzi and Yuanniu, who overcome hardships to finally reunite, vividly interpreting the blood-is-thicker-than-water fraternal bond between compatriots on both sides of the Strait and their spirit of solidarity and self-improvement. Everyone is welcome to watch it when it is released.\nIn addition, the game “Wuthering Waves” (鸣潮) is an action game featuring Eastern aesthetics. Because of its profound Chinese cultural heritage, delicate storyline, and innovative gameplay, it has been well received by young people and gamers on the island, and has repeatedly ranked in the top ten on Taiwan's overall charts, demonstrating the innovative strength and cultural appeal of mainland games.\nFrom “Ne Zha” to “Reunion Decree,” and from “Black Myth: Wukong” to “Wuthering Waves,” numerous mainland film, television, game, and other works have helped Taiwan youth deepen their understanding of the profound heritage of Chinese culture and continuously strengthen their cultural identity and confidence. We welcome Taiwan youth to actively take part in the development of mainland film, television, and game industries, support closer exchange and cooperation between industries on both sides, and jointly grow the cultural and creative industry of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746144.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Japanese Diet member Seki Hei (石平), who has been sanctioned by the mainland, made a provocative visit to Taiwan. Lai Ching-te falsely claimed that his action proved the so-called “Republic of China and the People's Republic of China are not subordinate to each other.” However, Seki Hei's visit was met with protests from Taiwan residents, who denounced him as a “traitor” and as one who “forgets his…","Lai Ching-te, together with a few traitors to the nation and petty villains, has staged a farce, fabricating and spreading “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, which is disgraceful. No matter what petty tricks the DPP authorities play, they cannot change the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. They cannot change the destined fate of “Taiwan independence” to fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend of the motherland's inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The Straits Exchange Foundation recently said that cross-Strait relations in 2026 are highly uncertain, but it will still make its utmost efforts and act with the greatest goodwill to promote the resumption of dialogue between the two sides, or even between the two associations, on the premise that no political preconditions are set, and on the basis of consensus among the people of Taiwan. What comment do you have?","If cross-Strait relations are uncertain, the root cause is just one: the DPP authorities obstinately persist in the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and constantly collude with external forces to plot “independence” and provoke confrontation. The solution is clear. Peace, development, exchange and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island and the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. As long as the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is acknowledged, the two cross-Strait associations can resume their dialogue and consultation mechanism, and cross-Strait relations can return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The New York Times recently reported, citing informed sources, that the US is close to reaching a trade agreement with Taiwan, under which US import tariffs on Taiwan would be lowered to 15%, and TSMC would invest in building at least five more semiconductor plants in Arizona. Island residents and public opinion have questioned whether the DPP authorities are trading investment for tariff reductions, which would…","The so-called agreement is an economic plunder of Taiwan by the United States using high tariffs as a means, a scheme to “drain the blood” of Taiwan’s industries. This not only exposes the self-interested nature of “America First,” but also exposes the sinister intent of the United States in treating Taiwan as a pawn.\nFaced with blatant bullying and plunder by external forces, the DPP authorities not only refuse to resist but instead actively cater to them, treating the island’s core technological advantages as a “pledge of loyalty” offered to external forces to curry favor. In tariff negotiations they have “knelt before negotiating,” and before economic extortion they have “offered the right cheek after being struck on the left.” The “sell-out coupons” keep growing, and in the end they will only destroy Taiwan’s economic development prospects and harm the long-term interests of the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746146.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","The Taiwan Affairs Office recently listed “green judicial enforcer” Chen Shu-yi as an accomplice of the “Taiwan independence” enforcers, to be held accountable for life in accordance with law. In response, the “Taipei Bar Association” issued a statement saying that the mainland’s move has no legal legitimacy whatsoever, has no effect on the practice of Taiwan’s judicial system, and hopes all sectors will unite to…","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Our punishment of a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their thugs and accomplices in accordance with the law is a righteous action to safeguard national unification and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and a necessary measure to protect the common home of the Chinese nation and safeguard the vital interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Any “Taiwan independence” separatist who breaks the law, wherever they are, will face all necessary punitive measures and be held accountable for life in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that Taiwan is “facing increasingly severe threats from hostile foreign forces,” that it must firmly do a good job of “countering the united front, anti-infiltration and anti-annexation,” and that in the 2026 “nine-in-one” elections, the two elections in 2028, and even every island-wide election after that, “hostile foreign forces will all intervene.” What is your comment on this?","Whenever there is an election on the island, the DPP's habitual tactic is to attack and smear the mainland and manipulate \"resisting China and protecting Taiwan\" in order to seek political gain. This sinister intention and despicable practice have long been seen through. It not only cannot fool Taiwan's people, but will also be spurned by them.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746151.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Reports say that Su Chia-chyuan has been appointed chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, and public opinion on the island is watching whether he can bring “spring blossoms” to cross-Strait relations. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities stubbornly hold to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism between the two organizations be restarted, and only then can the Straits Exchange Foundation perform its proper functions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The MAC previously said it would respond to a Mainland blogger's exposure of satellite images of Shen Boyang's residence by “comprehensively reviewing cross-Strait exchange practices.” This has raised concern on the island that cross-Strait exchanges will be fully tightened. In response, the MAC said, “it depends on the other side's actions,” and the matter is still under study. What is your comment?","“Taiwan independence” die-hard Shen Boyang is a national traitor who undermines cross-Strait relations and splits the country, and his actions are despised by the broad masses. In order to shield Shen Boyang and a handful of other “Taiwan independence” die-hards, the DPP authorities have not hesitated to stand against the broad masses on the island, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and harm the legitimate rights and interests of island residents to participate in cross-Strait exchanges, which is unpopular. Strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is the will of the people and the trend of the times, and no person or force can stop it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, the United States sent troops to forcibly seize Venezuelan President Maduro and his wife and transfer them out of the country, which has drawn intense attention on the island. A Time magazine article stated that what Taiwan should really worry about is the United States' attention being consumed by Venezuela, causing Taiwan to lose the United States as its “backer,” and that China does not need any…","Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair, and resolving the Taiwan question is the Chinese people’s own business and a just cause of safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity. “Outsiders are unreliable,” and the DPP authorities, who “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” will only become the “discarded pawns” of external forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746147.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan's legislature recently again blocked the NT$1.25 trillion special defense budget; this draft has been blocked multiple times since last December. What is your comment on this?","Earlier, a CGTN poll among global netizens showed that 90% of respondents believe the DPP authorities' acceleration of arming Taiwan has pushed the Taiwan public into a dangerous situation of war. Polls on the island also show that more than 60% of the public are unwilling for themselves or their family members to go to the battlefield. These circumstances reflect a high degree of consensus in Taiwan society that buying weapons cannot buy “security” and will only accelerate pushing Taiwan into danger. They also reflect the strong dissatisfaction of Taiwan residents with the DPP authorities squandering the people's hard-earned money to curry favor with external forces and fatten foreign arms dealers. In pursuit of party interests, the DPP authorities keep increasing defense budgets, vigorously promote “all people as soldiers” and agitate “war panic,” binding Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and scheming to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence.” This is a real threat to the security and interests of the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","湖北广电记者","It is reported that the first APEC Senior Officials’ Meeting of this year will be held on the mainland in February. Relevant Taiwan authorities said they will actively participate, have coordinated entry and exit arrangements with all parties, and that last year, when they traveled to the mainland for meetings under this arrangement, they faced no suppression. What comment do you have?","As the host of this year's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) events, we will handle the participation of the Taiwan region in meetings in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions and practices of the APEC Memorandum of Understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have successively passed four draft amendments to security-related laws, as well as draft amendments such as the “Cross-Strait People’s Relations Act.” Public opinion on the island points out that these are concrete moves to advance Lai Ching-te’s so-called “17 strategies,” aimed at further restricting cross-Strait exchanges, and that behind them is the DPP authorities’ political…","Lai Ching-te's so-called “17 strategies” completely go against the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society, which calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and fully confirm that he is a “destroyer of cross-Strait peace” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.” The DPP authorities' recent moves are of sinister intent, attempting to further create “green terror,” plot “Taiwan independence dictatorship,” and open the door for undermining cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. These vile acts that are anti-peace, anti-exchange, anti-democracy, and anti-humanity will be opposed and are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746150.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Regarding the Internal Administration Committee of the Legislative Yuan of Taiwan’s recent review of the draft amendment to the “Anti-Infiltration Act,” the Mainland Affairs Council said that the crimes and penalties currently stipulated in the “Anti-Infiltration Act” are far from sufficient, “and no matter what provisions are set, the CCP can find loopholes,” and “amendments cannot keep up with the CCP’s…","The so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” is merely a political tool fabricated by the DPP authorities to suppress political rivals, intimidate the people of Taiwan, and seek partisan gain. It is an out-and-out “evil law” that, from the very beginning, has faced serious doubts and criticism from all sectors on the island. Driven by its “independence-seeking” nature, the DPP authorities are scheming to revise this “evil law” in order to use it further to commit evil deeds: to intensify efforts to obstruct and restrict cross-strait exchanges and escalate confrontation, to infringe upon the freedom of speech and personal liberty of Taiwan’s people, and to create a “green terror.” This both exposes their true face of pushing “Taiwan independence authoritarianism,” and shows that they are stern in appearance but timid inside, fearing that compatriots on both sides will draw closer together. It has already met with increasingly strong condemnation and opposition from the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Taiwan media reported that the mainland is using competitions, selection processes and other means to recruit Taiwan students to visit the mainland for exchanges, in order to carry out “united front” work. Some Green camp politicians said they have applied for an investigation and will look in depth into whether supervision and management mechanisms such as the “cross-strait education exchange activity…","These claims are entirely baseless and have sinister intentions. The DPP authorities frequently use “infiltration threats” as a pretext to carry out a “green terror” on the island, and by any means obstruct and sabotage normal cross-Strait exchanges and contacts. In particular, they have repeatedly “sealed” normal student and educational exchanges, fully exposing their stubborn intent to provoke secession and their malicious aim of deliberately escalating cross-Strait confrontation. Facts fully prove that the DPP authorities are the greatest obstacle to cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, and the greatest risk to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The desire of compatriots on both sides to draw closer and the trend toward cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation cannot be stopped. Any act that turns back the wheel of history and defies the will and wishes of the people will inevitably be met with backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Wang Yi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs, recently visited Africa, clarified China’s position on the Taiwan question, and stressed opposition to “Somaliland” colluding with the Taiwan authorities to pursue “independence.” Taiwan’s foreign affairs department said that the mainland’s relevant actions “seriously challenge international order and peace” and…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. No matter how the DPP authorities twist black and white, or how they collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke, they cannot shake the international community’s pattern of adhering to the one-China principle, nor change the fate that “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Taiwanese internet celebrity “Curator” Chen Zhihan was recently indicted by the New Taipei District Prosecutors Office on suspicion of violating laws including “intimidation of security and incitement of others to commit crimes.” Some public opinion on the island points out that this is the DPP authorities manipulating the judiciary to intimidate and restrict the public from criticizing the authorities. What is…","The DPP authorities are abusing judicial means to intimidate and suppress Taiwan residents who support cross-Strait exchanges, attempting to create a “green terror” and restrict the freedom of Taiwan residents. Its essence is to serve “Taiwan independence,” and it will surely be opposed and reviled.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Governments and officials of many countries have recently spoken out, reaffirming adherence to the one-China principle, opposing any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity and interference in China’s internal affairs, and firmly supporting all efforts by the Chinese government to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Adhering to the one-China principle is a recognized norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. The international community broadly understands and supports the just cause of the Chinese people in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and striving to achieve national reunification. We appreciate and thank them for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","A U.S. think tank recently released a so-called report claiming that if mainland China achieves unification by “attacking” Taiwan, it will pay multiple costs in economic development, military capability, social stability and the international community. What is your comment on this?","The so-called “academic research” of certain US think tanks is in fact “taking money to do the job” and has ulterior motives. They are accustomed to hiding behind the banner of “academia” to peddle the “China threat theory,” hype up tense atmospheres across the Taiwan Strait, sow discord in the feelings of compatriots on both sides, and serve their intention of “using Taiwan to contain China.”\nWe emphasize three points here. First, Taiwan is part of China, and the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. The way to resolve it is for Chinese people to decide, and no foreign interference will be tolerated. Second, achieving the complete reunification of the motherland accords with the common aspiration and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. It is a just cause, not a so-called “attack.” Third, the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests. No one should underestimate our firm determination, steadfast will, and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","According to reports, Singapore's Senior Minister Lee Hsien Loong recently said that peace across the Taiwan Strait is crucial, and that various parties claiming to maintain the status quo are, in their actual actions, escalating tensions. Taiwan's foreign affairs department said this statement does not fully conform to reality: “The CPC keeps expanding its armaments and oppressing Taiwan, and its ultimate goal…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation. They are the source of trouble and turmoil that undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the status quo across the Strait. “Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. To maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, it is essential to clearly oppose “Taiwan independence.” The people on both sides of the Strait understand this clearly, and the international community sees it clearly too.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","US President Trump recently told The New York Times in an interview that the Chinese side believes Taiwan is part of China and that the Chinese side will decide how to handle the Taiwan question, which has drawn attention on the island. Some island public opinion says the US has once again made clear its position of “abandoning Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves. We will resolutely safeguard China's sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260114_12746148.htm"],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","《团结报》记者","Recently, Taiwan's security authorities released a so-called “Analysis Report on the Operational Methods of the CCP's Cognitive Warfare Against Taiwan in 2025,” claiming that the mainland uses “analyzing social conditions through data analysis and building diverse channels to release controversial information” and other cognitive warfare operations against Taiwan, spreading disputed messages. What is your comment?","This so-called “report” distorts facts and smears the mainland. Its purpose is to deceive and mislead people on the island, manipulate “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, attempt to divert the public's dissatisfaction with the DPP authorities' incompetence in governance, and seek political gain. Many cases exposed in Taiwan have repeatedly proven that it is the DPP authorities who are the habitual offenders of “cognitive warfare.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: In recent years, hyping “mainland interference in Taiwan's elections” has become one of the main public opinion topics during Taiwan's elections and “great recalls.” Taiwan will hold its “nine-in-one” elections in 2026, and there are reports on the island that the “KMT-CPC Forum” will be resumed. May I ask how the mainland side will ensure that consensus reached in talks with Taiwan's political…","First question. Whenever there is an election on the island, the DPP's routine tactic is to attack and smear the mainland and manipulate the \"resist China, protect Taiwan\" narrative in order to gain political advantage. This sinister scheme and despicable practice have long been seen through. It not only fails to fool the Taiwan public but will also be rejected by them.\nAs for cross-Strait political party exchanges, our policy is consistent and clear. On the political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to engage in dialogue and communication and strengthen exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life who have insight. Together we will oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and bring benefits to compatriots on both sides.\nSecond question. We have noted that recently, a Taiwanese dessert shop was subjected to online bullying for using the words \"qing ti\" (青提) to label \"green grapes,\" and a department store was attacked by the Green camp's online troops for selling homework bags printed with simplified Chinese characters. Let us think: why does Taiwan's society repeatedly show such irrational and even pathological phenomena? The root cause lies in the fact that since the DPP authorities took office, driven by their inherent aim of seeking \"independence,\" they have deliberately manipulated \"de-Sinicization,\" attempting to sever the historical and cultural ties across the Strait and deceive and mislead the Taiwan public. This has caused confusion in historical memory and distortion of national identity among Taiwan's younger generation. They have forcibly promoted \"Taiwan independence\" curriculum guidelines and textbooks, deleted the expression \"Han people,\" and made political maneuvers over street names. They have also exaggerated the use of mainland terms in the daily lives of Taiwan residents into so-called \"cultural infiltration,\" and even linked it to the so-called \"upholding of Taiwan's subjectivity.\" All these practices are malicious and absurd.\nCompatriots on both sides are of the same Chinese nation. Chinese culture is the greatest common denominator of compatriots on both sides. Speaking Chinese, writing Chinese characters, and celebrating Chinese festivals are traits ingrained in the bones of compatriots on both sides. Where is this so-called \"infiltration\"? The DPP authorities use the \"Taiwan independence view of history\" to split Chinese culture apart, maliciously smear normal and natural cultural exchanges across the Strait, and manipulate \"cultural Taiwan independence\" and \"de-Sinicization.\" They have forgotten their ancestors and lost their origins, and they have no popular support.\nWe will work with Taiwan compatriots to continuously advance cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, jointly promote Chinese culture, jointly advance the creative transformation and innovative development of Chinese culture, be guardians, inheritors, and promoters of Chinese culture, and continuously strengthen the aspiration, backbone, and confidence of being Chinese, as well as the sense of belonging, identity, and honor of the Chinese nation.\nThird question. Despite the adverse impact of the external environment and the continued obstruction and sabotage by the DPP authorities, Taiwan-invested businesses and cross-Strait economic and trade relations have maintained their growth momentum. From January to November 2025, cross-Strait trade reached US$285.395 billion, up 7.3% year on year. Of this, the mainland's imports from Taiwan were US$209.390 billion, up 5.9% year on year, and the mainland's exports to Taiwan were US$76.005 billion, up 11.2% year on year. From January to October 2025, the mainland newly established 6,423 Taiwan-invested enterprises, and actual use of Taiwan investment reached US$1.75 billion, up 53% year on year. The potential for cross-Strait economic cooperation is great and its resilience is strong. The trend of continuously benefiting the livelihoods and economic growth of compatriots on both sides has not changed.\nCross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development, and the long-term mutually beneficial relationship and stable industrial and supply chains formed between the two sides, are the result of economic laws and market-driven choices. The DPP authorities' promotion of so-called \"decoupling and severing chains,\" the \"New Southbound Policy,\" and \"moving away from China and toward the United States\" cannot change the broad trend of economic integration and development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-14","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Reportedly, TSMC subsidiary TSMC Arizona spent US$197 million to acquire land in Phoenix, Arizona, USA, for operations and production use. What comments do you have on this?","We will not comment on individual cases of corporate operations.\nIt should be pointed out that the semiconductor industry is a precious asset of Taiwan compatriots. Under US pressure and at the sacrifice of the DPP authorities, TSMC (台积电) has gradually turned into “American TSMC” (美积电). Taiwan's core advantageous industries have been voluntarily sold out by the DPP authorities, which will only leave Taiwan even more at the mercy of the US, cause it to lose economic competitiveness, and seriously harm the interests of the Taiwan public and the prospects of its industrial development.\nThis concludes the press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260114_12746140.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-01-16","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","The U.S. and Taiwan signed a trade deal on Thursday that cuts tariffs on many of Taiwan’s exports and directs new investment into the U.S. technology industry. Does the Foreign Ministry have any comment?","China firmly opposes the negotiating and signing of any agreement with sovereign connotations and an official nature between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic relations with China. The U.S. needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260116_11814196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260116_11814163.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-01-16","Guo Jiakun","Nippon TV","Japan’s former chief cabinet secretary visited Taiwan and held talks with “president” Lai. Lai stated that we appreciate Japanese Prime Minister’s consistent emphasis on peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Does China have any comment on this?","Taiwan is a province of China and there is no such thing as “president” of Taiwan. There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic relations with China. We urge the Japanese side to earnestly abide by the one-China principle, and refrain from sending any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We would also like to stress that the most important thing for Japan now is to retract the erroneous remarks of Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260116_11814196.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260116_11814163.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-01-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","There are concerns in Taiwan that the mainland might follow what the US did to Venezuela to legitimize the use of force against the island. Meanwhile, some international media argued that if Beijing were to adopt a similar approach, it would face much higher risks and costs. What's your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese, which brooks no interference from external forces. For us, to deal with the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces is like catching a turtle in a jar, and all options that can punish the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces remain on the table.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/01/china-260116-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16437829.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-01-16","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A poll in Taiwan found that more than 60% of respondents were unwilling to fight in a war, or to have their family members do so. What's your comment on this?","This once again proves that the overwhelming majority of people in Taiwan desire peace, development, exchange and cooperation, not confrontation or conflict, even less to fight a war. Defying the people's wishes, the Lai Ching-te authorities are pursuing separatist goals by stoking tensions. More people will see through their nature of undermining peace, provoking crisis and inciting wars. I believe that no one is willing to be cannon fodder for \"Taiwan independence\" schemes. The separatist forces who go against the will of the people are doomed to be thrown into the dustbin of history.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/01/china-260116-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16437829.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on January 21, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Peng Qing’en answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, good morning! Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","新华社记者","Recently, after the conclusion of US-Taiwan tariff negotiations, the US Department of Commerce announced that the US reciprocal tariff rate applied to Taiwan's goods will generally not exceed 15%. Taiwan's semiconductor and technology companies will make at least US$250 billion in new direct investment in the United States, and the Taiwan authorities will also provide at least US$250 billion in credit guarantees.…","The so-called US-Taiwan trade negotiations are in essence the United States using tariffs as a club for extreme pressure, coercing Taiwan into substantially increasing investment in the United States and attempting to hollow out Taiwan's advantageous industries. The so-called consensus reached is merely a bargaining chip that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities use to sell out the well-being of the Taiwan people and the interests of industrial development; it is a capitulation letter that bows and scrapes in the face of economic bullying.\nNext, Taiwan will bear a massive investment commitment of 500 billion US dollars and face the enormous risk of transferring 40% of its semiconductor supply chain to the United States, in exchange for merely lowering the already unreasonable so-called \"reciprocal tariff\" rate from 20% to 15%. Whether this account is fair and reasonable is obvious to anyone with clear eyes. But the DPP authorities not only feel no shame about this but instead take pride in it, attempting to deceive the Taiwan public, glorifying \"compromise at all costs\" as an \"important breakthrough,\" dressing up unilateral bullying as \"equal cooperation,\" and packaging total kneeling as the \"Taiwan model.\" They are letting the United States strip Taiwan's industries bare and plunder everything, and squeeze the Taiwan people dry. Such incompetence and shamelessness will only completely destroy Taiwan's development prospects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747243.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","人民日报记者","According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, total cross-strait trade in 2025 reached US$314.33 billion. Mainland exports to Taiwan grew 11.2%, and mainland imports from Taiwan grew 6.0%. Analysts in island public opinion believe this fully demonstrates that cross-strait economic cooperation has strong momentum, resilience, and great potential. What comments does the Chinese side have on…","In 2025, despite the adverse impact of the external environment and the obstruction and sabotage of the DPP authorities, cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges continued to grow steadily. This fully demonstrates that strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development is the right path that serves the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Any scheme to push for \"decoupling and severing chains\" across the Strait and to weaken cross-Strait economic ties is retrograde and doomed to fail.\nAs the mainland's economy continues to develop healthily and sustainably during the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period, and as high-level opening up and the development of an open economy make remarkable progress, the foundation for cross-Strait economic cooperation and integrated development will become more solid, its fields will continue to expand, and its level will keep rising. This will better benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait and help strengthen the Chinese nation's economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747244.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","香港凤凰卫视记者","The United States and Taiwan recently reached a so-called “trade agreement.” U.S. Commerce Secretary Lutnick said in an interview that this agreement is a “strategic priority” for the DPP authorities to maintain U.S. “goodwill,” and is not simply a commercial transaction. The U.S. goal is to shift 40% of Taiwan's semiconductor supply chain capacity to the United States during Trump's term. What comments do you…","The so-called “trade agreement” reached between the United States and Taiwan is in essence a “contract of sale” colluded by external forces and “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. It aims to plunder the sweat and blood of Taiwan residents and hollow out the foundations of Taiwan’s industries, and it damages the future of Taiwan’s people and industries.\nThe massive US$500 billion investment is roughly 80% of Taiwan’s foreign exchange reserves, equivalent to having every Taiwan resident hand over NT$680,000 as a political donation for the DPP authorities’ “relying on outside powers to seek independence.” If 40% of semiconductor capacity were transferred to the United States, Taiwan’s core industrial advantage would vanish, and the “Technology Island” would become a “hollow island.” The DPP authorities are trying hard to conceal the painful price Taiwan pays, using the hard-earned money of the island’s people to curry favor with the United States. Selling out Taiwan and bringing disaster upon it could hardly be more extreme.\nThe outcome of the US-Taiwan tariff negotiations fully proves that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders cannot be relied upon. Without a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan can only become a fat piece of meat in the eyes of external forces, a lamb at the mercy of others.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747240.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","香港中评社记者","Regarding the appointment of Su Jiaquan as Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office recently said that only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can the cross-Strait two-organization dialogue and communication mechanism be restarted and the SEF be able to play its proper role. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan…","Taiwan’s relevant authorities cannot fail to know the history of interaction between the Straits Exchange Foundation and the two associations across the Strait. Why would they deliberately confuse the public? What is their intention?\nFrom the moment the Straits Exchange Foundation was established, its purpose was “Chinese, well-intentioned, and service-oriented.” In the course of conducting business-related consultations with the Straits Exchange Foundation, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits clearly pointed out that specific issues in exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are internal affairs of China and should be resolved through consultation in line with the one-China principle. On August 1, 1992, the Taiwan authorities issued a “conclusion” on the meaning of “one China” when the Straits Exchange Foundation and the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits were negotiating business-related agreements, confirming that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” That same year, the two associations, authorized by both sides of the Strait, reached through the Hong Kong talks and the exchange of letters and telegrams a consensus that each side would orally express that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait adhere to the one-China principle.” This was later called the “1992 Consensus.” It was on this basis that the two sides of the Strait began consultations and negotiations, advanced inter-party exchanges between the political parties on both sides, and opened the path of peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, from which compatriots on both sides have benefited.\nThe “1992 Consensus” clearly defines the nature of cross-Strait relations, and is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the linchpin of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The history of cross-Strait relations has repeatedly proven that recognizing the “1992 Consensus” and adhering to the one-China principle allows cross-Strait relations to improve and develop, and allows Taiwan compatriots to benefit. Denying the “1992 Consensus” and deviating from the one-China principle will cause cross-Strait relations to become tense and turbulent, and will harm the interests of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747241.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","《参考消息》记者","The DPP authorities recently released a so-called “report” claiming that in 2025 the mainland carried out “comprehensive hacking” of the island’s critical infrastructure through cyberattacks. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities are accustomed to fabricating rumors, slandering, and smearing the mainland, and do not hesitate to escalate cross-Strait confrontation in order to cover up their governing incompetence, divert public dissatisfaction, and seek political gain.\nIn fact, the DPP authorities have repeatedly directed military intelligence agencies and cyber forces to carry out cyber attacks and sabotage against the mainland and to spread illegal and harmful information. According to statistics, in 2025 relevant departments investigated and handled nearly 4,000 cyber attack incidents originating from the Taiwan direction, a 25% increase over 2024. Their attacks focused on stealing secrets from and attacking key sectors on the mainland, including transportation, finance, technology, and energy. Relevant departments have previously solved and made public the criminal facts of organizations involved in cyber attacks against the mainland, including the Taiwan military’s “Psychological Warfare Battalion,” Taiwan’s Wang’s Research and Creative Art Company, and “Anonymous 64.” The DPP authorities’ so-called “report” is nothing but a guilty conscience and a reversal of black and white.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747239.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中国日报记者","Some foreign media reported that China has pressured European countries to ban Taiwan political figures from entering their countries. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities have attacked and smeared this. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between diplomatic partners and the Taiwan region of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. The small moves of the DPP authorities cannot shake the one-China pattern of the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, when Lai Ching-te met with an Arizona delegation from the United States, he said that in recent years the United States has become Taiwan's largest destination for outward foreign direct investment, and hoped that both sides would sign an agreement to avoid double taxation as soon as possible, to help companies such as TSMC deeply cultivate in the United States over the long term and create high-paying…","The United States has always put “America's interests first” and is accustomed to wielding the “tariff club” to benefit itself at others' expense. So-called US-Taiwan trade and supply chain cooperation will only squeeze Taiwan dry and force Taiwan to cut off its own sinews and bones. In the eyes of Americans, Taiwan's value is not that of a “supply chain partner” but that of a “chess piece” for “using Taiwan to contain China,” a “money tree” for the military-industrial complex, and an “ATM” for manufacturing reshoring. According to reports, TSMC's labor costs at its US factories are more than twice those of its Taiwan factories, its equipment depreciation costs are as much as four times higher, and its gross margin is one-eighth that of its Taiwan factories.\nIn order to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” the DPP authorities have repeatedly sacrificed flesh to feed the tiger, and now want to greatly increase TSMC's investment in the United States to create so-called “high-paying jobs” for America. What will be destroyed is only the root of the island's industry, and what will be chilled is only the hearts of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747242.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","A mainland spouse recently posted online, “I hope unification comes soon so I can write in simplified characters,” and an official on the island said that if mainland spouses of this kind apply for permanent residency, they will be strictly reviewed in the future and cannot obtain citizenship simply because time has passed. In addition, Taiwan’s National Immigration Agency recently revoked the residence permit of…","Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, out of their “Taiwan independence” nature, have arbitrarily infringed upon the rights and interests of mainland spouses and oppressed and bullied the mainland spouse community, going to every extreme. They have seriously undermined the peaceful family lives of cross-Strait marriages and seriously harmed the legitimate rights and interests of cross-Strait marriage groups. We strongly condemn this. As for the “Taiwan independence” accomplices and henchmen who persecute mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely without leniency.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260121_12747238.htm"],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Recently, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have remained active.\nIn the area of youth, from January 20 to 27, the Hubei-Taiwan Ice and Snow Bond · Jingchu Shares This Moment Cross-Strait Youth Skiing Culture Festival was held in Wuhan and Xiangyang, Hubei, with a total of more than 150 Taiwan youth participating. From January 21 to 23, the 32nd Taiwan Compatriot Youth Winter Camp of the All-China Taiwan Federation held its opening ceremony and general camp activities in Hangzhou, Zhejiang. Twenty-six distinctive sub-camps will be held in 24 provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities across the country, and more than 1,000 Taiwan youth are expected to participate. In mid-to-late January, the second “Dynamic Jincheng · Ice and Snow Experience Camp” was held in Tianjin, and more than 400 Taiwan youth will come to Tianjin to experience the joy of ice and snow sports.\nIn the area of culture, on January 15, the campus youth edition of the Kunqu opera “The Peony Pavilion” was performed for the first time in Taipei, attracting more than 900 theater enthusiasts from the island. The production was performed by 50 students from 29 universities on the mainland and in Macao, and brought island audiences a classic production of nine excerpts, including “Strolling in the Garden,” “Startled from Dreams,” and “Expressing Feelings.” A Taiwan student audience member said that there are quite a few young people in Taiwan who love Peking opera and Kunqu opera, and hoped there would be more such performances in the future, and also hoped to exchange and learn with peers on the mainland who share the same interests.\nIn the new year, we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to walk around and take a look. I believe the mainland always has a scene that can capture your attention, a dish that can touch your taste buds, and a warmth that can move your heart.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","北京日报记者","Please introduce the situation of cross-Strait personnel exchanges for the full year 2025.","In 2025, despite the DPP authorities' continued escalation of restrictions and prohibitions, cross-strait personnel exchanges increased significantly compared with 2024, by 1.0445 million person-trips, reaching 5.4495 million person-trips, a year-on-year increase of 23.6%. Among them, Taiwan residents traveled to the mainland 4.8918 million person-trips, an increase of 0.8688 million person-trips from the previous year, or 21.6%; mainland residents traveled to Taiwan 557,700 person-trips, an increase of 175,700 person-trips from the previous year, or 47.4%.\nDespite the DPP authorities' deliberate efforts to obstruct and impose restrictions, cross-strait personnel exchanges in 2025 still reached a considerable scale, and exchanges and cooperation in all fields remained active. We sincerely welcome more and more compatriots in Taiwan to come to the mainland to take a look, see the magnificent rivers and mountains of the motherland, and experience the vibrant and thriving scenes of the mainland's economic and social development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中国台湾网记者","Su Chia-chuan, incoming Chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that his top priority after taking office is to restore healthy exchanges between the two cross-Strait associations, which is absolutely a very good thing for the people on both sides. What is your comment on this?","The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. From 2008 to 2016, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) signed a series of agreements on the basis of the “1992 Consensus.” After these agreements took effect, they brought tangible benefits to compatriots on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots. Since May 2016, the DPP authorities have obstinately adhered to the “Taiwan independence” stance and refused to recognize the “1992 Consensus.” They have unilaterally undermined the political foundation of cross-Strait consultations and negotiations and of the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, deliberately obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and seriously harmed the interests and welfare of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nI must emphasize again: only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle can the two cross-Strait associations resume their dialogue and consultation mechanism, and cross-Strait relations return to the correct track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Recently, the Taiwan legislature launched impeachment proceedings against Lai Ching-te and successively held two public hearings, at which representatives from all sectors of the island listed Lai Ching-te’s various misdeeds. Island public opinion has pointed out that this is a trial of Lai Ching-te by public opinion. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te obstinately clings to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence.” In pursuit of political self-interest and disregarding the livelihood and welfare of the island's people, he has repeatedly trampled on democracy and impaired freedom. He has abused the judiciary to suppress and persecute political dissenters, vigorously promoted “green terror” and created a “chilling effect,” and constantly manipulated and stirred up political bloodbaths. Defying public will and losing popular support on a large scale, he will inevitably face strong opposition from the Taiwanese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, a Japanese scholar has advocated that China, in a moment of crisis, will manipulate the narrative that “the Japanese should not take risks for Taiwan,” in order to shake Japanese society’s pro-Taiwan consciousness, weaken the US-Japan alliance, and ultimately cause Taiwan to lose its resolve to resist. What is your comment?","These remarks exaggerate the atmosphere of tension in the Taiwan Strait and hype war anxiety, with vicious intentions. Japan bears historical responsibility on the Taiwan question. It should deeply reflect on history and learn its lessons, and even more so, it should fully recognize the high sensitivity of the Taiwan question. It should abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, be prudent in its words and actions on the Taiwan question, and stop sending any wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","福建东南卫视记者","Several recent procurement cases by Taiwan's defense authorities have sparked controversy. Following reports that a renovation company and a shoe factory had won military equipment contracts, and that a tea company had won a server contract, a NT$45.5 million military procurement case was recently exposed, in which the winning company was originally engaged in wholesale and retail of tobacco and alcohol, food,…","In order to “use military force to seek independence,” the DPP authorities are lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s ordinary people to buy foreign weapons, while taking the opportunity to enrich themselves and engage in corruption. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the sinister intentions and ugly faces of the DPP authorities, use practical actions to keep a close watch on their own wallets, and not be deceived again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that a mainland coast guard vessel appeared in waters near Pratas Island on the 14th. Taiwan's coast guard authorities demanded that it “stop all harassing acts” and threatened that they “will take all necessary measures” in response. What is your comment on this?","The mainland coast guard conducted law enforcement patrols in the waters near Dongsha Island. This is aimed at maintaining normal navigation and operating order in the relevant waters and safeguarding the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, and it is a lawful and legitimate action. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China. If they dare to make trouble in the relevant waters, they must bear all consequences arising from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, one mainland surveillance drone entered the airspace near Pratas Island. Taiwan's defense authorities said that this irresponsible act by the PLA has seriously undermined regional peace and stability and violates international legal norms. What is your comment on this?","The Southern Theater Command organized drones to conduct normal flight training in the airspace near Dongsha Island, China. It is completely proper and lawful. The DPP authorities, disregarding the fact and legal principle that Taiwan is part of China, stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and constantly engage in provocations to seek “independence.” They are unmistakably “troublemakers.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, regarding the Taiwan executive authorities' revision of the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act,” the Mainland Affairs Council said that “a verdict of not guilty does not mean truly innocent” in the cases under the “Anti-Infiltration Act,” that infiltration in many cases was carried out through covert means, and that it hopes the public will report such cases to help law enforcement agencies clarify the…","The relevant remarks by the DPP authorities once again prove that they have no regard for the rule of law and care only for political self-interest. The so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” is merely a tool the DPP authorities use to suppress and persecute political opponents, creating a “green terror” and “Taiwan independence dictatorship.” It is a thoroughly “evil law” that obstructs and undermines cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.\nThe DPP authorities’ vicious conduct, constantly shouting about killing and beating, intimidating, threatening, and fabricating charges, has already met with strong opposition from more and more Taiwan people. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. No one can suppress the desire of compatriots on both sides to draw closer, and no one can block the trend of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Taiwan media reported that recently some Taiwanese residents had their household registration in Taiwan revoked by the DPP authorities for applying for a one-time “China Border Tourism Passport.” Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council claimed that applying for mainland documents requires giving up “Taiwan identity.” What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities use various pretexts to intimidate Taiwan's people and restrict their freedoms, creating a “green terror.” This fully exposes their ugly face of vigorously pursuing “Taiwan independence autocracy,” and it has met with strong condemnation and opposition from more and more Taiwan people. We advise the DPP authorities to do more things that benefit the immediate interests of Taiwan's people, and to stop constantly trying to intimidate and harm Taiwan's people in all kinds of ways, or they will surely be backfired upon.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Chang Tsun-feng, chairman of the Pingtung chapter of Taiwan’s “Unification Alliance Party,” and Huang Jung-te, its secretary-general, were charged with interfering in Taiwan’s leadership and legislative elections on the instructions of the Taiwan Affairs Office, and were each sentenced to 4 years and 6 months in prison and deprivation of civil rights for 2 years. What comment do you have?","The relevant accusations are groundless and purely fabricated. Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have continuously manipulated the so-called “mainland interference in elections,” abused the judiciary to persecute organizations and individuals on the island that support and take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, created a “green terror,” and implemented “Taiwan independence dictatorship.” We strongly condemn this. “Taiwan independence” forces and their thugs and accomplices will ultimately face the trial of justice and the severe punishment of the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, a man surnamed Qiao, from an airline on the island, was found to have been attempting to obtain intelligence for mainland intelligence units by offering a bribe to officials of the Mainland Affairs Council. After the bribe was refused, the Taiwan “High Court” sentenced him to six months in prison for offering bribes under the crime of corrupt bribery. What is your comment?","The Lai Ching-te authorities have repeatedly hyped the “mainland threat” and escalated cross-Strait confrontation, running counter to the mainstream public opinion on the island, which wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. It is unpopular and will inevitably be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Zhou Manzhi, a mainland-born spouse who serves as chairperson of the “Taiwan New Immigrants Care Association,” was accused of organizing in Taiwan on the instructions of, and with funding from, the mainland. She was previously acquitted by the Kaohsiung Branch of Taiwan’s “Supreme Court,” but the Taiwan “Supreme Court” found that the original judgment’s investigation was incomplete and remanded it. Recently, the…","The relevant situation once again exposes the DPP authorities' despicable practice of fabricating charges and persecuting mainland spouses. The DPP authorities are going against the mainstream public opinion on the island calling for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. They keep exaggerating the so-called “united front infiltration threat,” and have escalated and resorted to any means to intimidate and suppress groups and individuals on the island who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges. Their purpose is to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and create a “politics of terror” and “green dictatorship” on the island. Their reckless behavior goes against popular sentiment and will inevitably be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","台湾《中国时报》记者","Regarding the “trade agreement” recently reached between the US and Taiwan: the mainland has consistently maintained that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair and does not allow external forces to interfere. But when Taiwan and the US have reached such a huge investment and tariff agreement, apart from verbal protests, is the mainland side substantively unable to prevent Taiwan from participating in the…","Compatriots in Taiwan are our family, and Taiwan enterprises are enterprises of the Chinese nation. We firmly oppose the DPP authorities’ pursuit of “Taiwan independence,” and their collusion with external forces to hollow out Taiwan, which harms the vital interests of Taiwan enterprises and people. We will resolutely safeguard the development rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the overall interests of the Chinese nation.\nThe so-called “supply chain restructuring” of the DPP authorities is, in fact, their collusion with external forces in an attempt to push for economic decoupling and severing of cross-Strait economic ties. The outcome of the Taiwan-US trade negotiations is clearly the United States’ large-scale exploitation and plunder of Taiwan, a blatant case of economic bullying. Facts have repeatedly shown that those who sell out national interests will ultimately be nailed to the pillar of shame of history, and that wanton seizure and plunder will inevitably meet resistance and backlash.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","中新社记者","Taiwan media reported that OnePlus (Shenzhen) Technology Co., Ltd., a mainland mobile phone brand, is suspected of recruiting more than 70 engineers in Taiwan, with remittances totaling about NT$2.3 billion. The Shilin District Prosecutors Office in Taipei indicted two Taiwanese staff members under the “Act Governing Relations between the People of the Taiwan Area and the Mainland Area” and issued a wanted notice…","The DPP authorities are making a great fuss over a single corporate case, intending to stir up cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, obstruct cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, and plot the \"decoupling and severing of chains\" across the Strait. This practice harms the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, does not win popular support, and is doomed to fail.\nETTV (Taiwan):\nThe Taiwan authorities are currently investigating CtiTV reporter Lin Chen-yu, stating that they have preliminarily established that he is suspected of bribing active-duty Taiwanese military personnel and collecting classified military information, and they assess that related funds may be linked to the mainland side. What is your comment on this?\nThe DPP authorities have abused judicial means to intimidate and suppress political opponents and have recklessly slapped the \"infiltration\" label on people, and this is not the first time. Creating \"green terror\" for the narrow interests of one party and one individual and inciting cross-Strait opposition and confrontation will inevitably meet with opposition.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-21","Peng Qing'en","台湾《联合报》记者","KMT Vice Chairperson Hsiao Hsu-tsen recently said in an interview, regarding reports that she would visit the mainland at the end of this month and that the “KMT-CPC Forum” would be resumed, that there is currently no further information and that media reports have discrepancies in their information. In addition, KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently said that once the relevant activities are confirmed, they will…","We are willing, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang, maintain positive interactions, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, benefiting compatriots on both sides. If there are new developments on the issues you are concerned about, we will release information in a timely manner.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260121_12747230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-01-27","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Japan’s Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said that any crisis in Taiwan could spur Tokyo and Washington to take joint action to rescue their own citizens. She added that in such a situation, there was no way Japan could abandon its long-time ally, the U.S. Would the Ministry like to comment?","The Japanese side should be reminded that the 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement states that “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” The 1978 Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, ratified by the two countries’ legislatures, affirmed that the principles set out in the 1972 Joint Statement should be strictly observed.\nA series of instruments with legal effect under international law, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation, and the Japanese Instrument of Surrender, require that all the territories Japan had stolen from China, such as Taiwan, must be restored to China, and Japan should be “completely disarmed” and not maintain such industries as “would enable her to re-arm for war.” Japan’s Constitution also made strict restrictions on the country’s military forces, the right of belligerency and the right to war.\nThese are political commitments that Japan must strictly honor and legal obligations that they cannot deny. The Japanese side claims to act within the scope of law but has kept their gross interference in China’s domestic affairs and even threatened the use of force against China. This is self-contradictory. Japan committed innumerable crimes during its colonial rule over Taiwan of half a century, and bears serious historical responsibilities to the Chinese people. Either from the perspective of history or law, the Japanese side is in no position to interfere in the affairs of China’s Taiwan region. The remarks by the Japanese side once again reveal the Japanese right-wing forces’ ambitions to provoke antagonism, make trouble, and take the opportunity to keep remilitarizing Japan and to challenge the post-war international order. This has severely threatened regional peace and stability and the political foundation of China-Japan relations. The international community must stay on high alert and firmly reject that. We once again urge the Japanese side to abide by the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan and Japan’s own political commitments made to China, do soul-searching, correct its wrongdoings, and stop their manipulation and reckless moves on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260127_11846105.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260127_11846080.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on January 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han first announced that the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum” will be held in Beijing on February 3, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Ladies and gentlemen, journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. First, I will announce a piece of news.\nAfter consultations between relevant parties of the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum” will be held in Beijing on February 3. The forum is co-hosted by the Haixia Research Center of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Kuomintang National Policy Research Foundation. The theme of this session is “Prospects for Cross-Strait Exchange and Cooperation.” Representatives of the KMT and the CPC, as well as representatives, experts, and scholars from cross-strait sectors including tourism, industry, technology, healthcare, and environmental protection, will attend the forum. They will engage in in-depth exchanges and discussions on cross-strait exchange and cooperation in tourism, industry, environment, and sustainable development, and jointly discuss the development of cross-strait relations and seek the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748343.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Recently, KMT Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun said that mainstream public opinion in Taiwan highly anticipates cross-Strait exchanges, that she has felt goodwill and sincerity from the mainland side, and that she hopes the KMT will shoulder its historic responsibility to promote a “thaw” in cross-Strait relations and ease the current tense situation. What is your comment?","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and personages, including the Kuomintang of China, maintain positive interaction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and bring benefits to compatriots on both sides. The upcoming KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum is a concrete manifestation of the two parties’ efforts to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, welfare for the people, and rejuvenation for the nation. It conforms to mainstream public opinion on the island and to the expectations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748340.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Taiwan's legislative body held a review meeting on the “impeachment case against Lai Ching-te.” Lai refused to attend and give an explanation, and was harshly criticized by legislators from the Kuomintang and the Taiwan People's Party as “arrogant and guilty,” “contemptuous of public opinion,” and “dereliction of duty, incompetence, and moral failure.” What comments do you have on this?","Lai Ching-te stubbornly clings to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence.” To seek political gain, disregarding the well-being of the people on the island, he keeps manipulating the judicial system to crack down on political opponents, repeatedly tramples on and undermines democracy and freedom, and attempts to implement a “green dictatorship.” This seriously deviates from mainstream public opinion on the island and will inevitably face a backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748334.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently said at an economic forum: “The determination to defend national sovereignty will not change; the commitment to upholding a democratic and free way of life will not change; the effort to maintain peaceful development across the Taiwan Strait will not change; under equal dignity, the commitment to maintaining dialogue and exchanges with China to promote peace and common prosperity will not…","Lai Ching-te is accustomed to confusing right and wrong and reversing black and white. The facts are: Lai Ching-te stubbornly holds to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refuses to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and seriously provokes the one-China principle; he “relies on foreign powers to seek independence” and “seeks independence through force,” constantly aggravating tensions in the Taiwan Strait; he disregards the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society, which wants peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and persistently manipulates “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment; he goes further in creating a “green dictatorship,” implementing “Taiwan independence autocracy,” and deliberately scheming to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Facts have repeatedly proven that Lai Ching-te is an out-and-out “peace wrecker,” “crisis creator,” and “war instigator.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748339.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, news that the mainland's high-speed rail operating mileage has exceeded 50,000 kilometers has sparked heated discussion on the island. Some public opinion holds that Taiwan has long been plagued by energy shortages and aging infrastructure. If it introduces mainland capital and technology, then tunneling through the Central Mountain Range and improving transportation in Hualien and Taitung would not be…","The mainland's high-speed rail construction has attracted worldwide attention. Since the 14th Five-Year Plan, the mainland has built and put into operation more than 12,000 km of high-speed rail, and 128 counties have entered the high-speed rail era. The total high-speed rail mileage has now reached 50,400 km, covering 97% of cities with urban populations of more than 500,000, and forming the world's largest and most modernized high-speed rail network. Speeding high-speed trains make distances 'smaller,' dreams 'bigger,' and faraway places no longer distant.\nPeaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development. With a strong motherland as backing, every aspect of Taiwan, including infrastructure construction, will be better. Taiwan compatriots will share with compatriots on the mainland the dignity and glory of our great country and the achievements of Chinese-style modernization, and usher in a prosperous, stable and bright future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748338.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Data recently released by Taiwan's authorities show that in 2025, the total value of Taiwan's imported consumer goods reached US$49.4 billion, a record high. Nearly one-quarter (24.5%) came from the Mainland, ranking first. Mainland goods have always been loved by Taiwan consumers for their high quality and good value. What is your comment?","The mainland possesses the world's largest, most complete, and best-supported industrial system, and its manufacturing output has ranked first in the world for many consecutive years. Intelligent, green, and integrated development is accelerating. From leisure snacks, home appliances, and mobile phones to high-end equipment such as new energy vehicles and industrial robots, a dazzling array of “Made in China” products has entered households, reached every corner of the world, and led consumer fashion. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share a common cultural tradition and living habits, so mainland consumer goods are naturally well loved by the people of Taiwan. Strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development is the right path that serves the common interests of compatriots on both sides. We will continue to work hard so that Taiwan compatriots can share the fruits of mainland development in food, clothing, housing, transportation, and other aspects of life. We also welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to look around and personally experience its rapidly changing development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748337.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism released the 2026 edition of the model group travel contract template, which includes the “Model Contract for Mainland Residents Traveling to the Taiwan Region.” Attention has been drawn to the fact that the text was updated in sync, even though cross-Strait tourism recovery is currently blocked. The Taiwan “Tourism Administration” said that if the mainland side…","From 2013 to 2014, the current model contracts for group tours were issued one after another, including five model contracts for group tourism and mainland residents traveling to Taiwan. This revision is a comprehensive revision of the current texts. In 2024, the mainland side resumed tourism by Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu. This revision of the model contract for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan will help meet market demand in a timely manner, further regulate market order, and protect the lawful rights and interests of tourists and travel agencies.\nDriven by its inherent tendency to oppose “independence” and by its political self-interest, the DPP authorities have turned a deaf ear to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and the appeals of the industry. They have turned a blind eye to the harm done to the interests of grassroots people and operators in Taiwan. They have repeatedly used various pretexts to obstruct and restrict tourism and exchanges in all fields and set up barriers. This is unpopular. The Taiwan industry has expressed extreme disappointment and strong indignation. If they do not change course and continue to act selfishly, they will certainly lose even more public support and reap the consequences.\nThe mainland side has always adhered to the concept of “cross-strait families are one.” We have continued to make efforts and release goodwill to promote cross-strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in tourism and other fields. Our sincerity in resuming tourism by mainland residents to the island has not changed. The key now is whether the DPP authorities can face up to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and the appeals of the industry, and create favorable conditions for cross-strait personnel exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748336.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the results of the US-Taiwan tariff negotiations, public opinion on the island is worried that if 40% of Taiwan's semiconductor supply capacity moves to the United States within the next 3 years, it will severely damage Taiwan's economy. A large exodus of high-tech talent, including midstream and downstream industrial chains, would occur, which would be a loss that Taiwan cannot recover from for decades…","Faced with the forced relocation of Taiwan's entire semiconductor industry chain to the United States, public opinion on the island, the industry, and the general public are all worried, and only the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are still striving to gloss over the situation. For the sake of “relying on foreign powers to seek independence,” the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, without any bottom line, fawn on the United States and sell out Taiwan, “kneeling to hand over” Taiwan's semiconductor industry advantages. Yet they leave the people and industry on the island to bear irreversible losses. This will inevitably cause panic in the industry and widespread public resentment, and they will surely bring this upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Taiwan media reported that, in the name of “preventing minors from encountering unsuitable content and potential cybersecurity risks,” Taiwan's Ministry of Digital Affairs has for the first time proposed a list of high-risk cybersecurity apps, including Douyin, Weibo, WeChat, Xiaohongshu and Baidu Netdisk, for reference by education authorities. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities have hyped so-called “security risks” of mainland applications with sinister intentions. By depriving the people of Taiwan, especially young people, of the right to know and the freedom to use social platforms, cutting off cross-Strait exchange channels, and deliberately inciting so-called “resisting China, protecting Taiwan,” they reveal their inner fear and “unease.” The DPP authorities act recklessly and will surely reap what they sow. Their perverse actions cannot stop the tide of public opinion, as the people of Taiwan, especially young people, seek to understand the mainland and come to know and be close to mainland compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748333.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, a Taiwanese retired serviceman entered a scenic spot on the mainland with a Taiwan military retirement certificate and demanded free admission on the same basis as retired PLA servicemen, drawing attention online. May I ask whether Taiwan’s retired servicemen can be treated on the same basis as retired PLA servicemen on the mainland?","Since 2024, some scenic spots on the mainland have implemented a number of convenience measures for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. Among them, for Taiwan compatriots who obtain a Taiwan Compatriot Permit for the first time (issuance number 01), ticket fees at mainland scenic spots and attractions are waived or reduced for one year. The scope of application of these convenience measures is clearly limited to Taiwan compatriots who are \"first-time visitors.\"\nFor the specific provisions on the ticket concession policy for retired members of the Chinese People's Liberation Army at scenic spots, you may look them up yourself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202601/t20260128_12748335.htm"],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have frequently alleged that the mainland has strengthened “espionage infiltration” against Taiwan, especially “bribing” personnel at all levels of Taiwan's military and retired personnel. What is your comment on this?","For the sake of one-party political self-interest and the delusion of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated lies to deceive and intimidate the Taiwan public, fabricated charges to suppress political opponents, wantonly manipulated the judiciary, and created a “green terror.” This has stirred up growing public resentment and opposition on the island, and their reckless actions are bound to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","A figure from Taiwan’s agricultural sector has pointed out that the “15th Five-Year Plan” provides new opportunities for cross-Strait agricultural exchanges, that there is broad room for cooperation between Taiwan and the mainland, and that Taiwan should make the right choice between “leaning on the U.S. to resist China” and “creating a new situation of cross-Strait win-win cooperation.” What is your comment on this?","The “15th Five-Year Plan” Recommendations adopted by the Fourth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Communist Party of China explicitly propose “accelerating the modernization of agriculture and rural areas and steadily advancing the comprehensive revitalization of rural areas.” They systematically arrange key tasks, including enhancing agriculture's comprehensive production capacity and the quality and efficiency of its benefits, promoting the construction of livable, business-friendly, and beautiful villages, and improving the effectiveness of policies that strengthen agriculture, benefit farmers, and enrich rural residents. These tasks provide more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan farmers to take part in the mainland's high-quality development. Cross-Strait agricultural cooperation has complementary advantages and broad space. The mainland has always been the best choice for Taiwan enterprises and farmers to take root and develop. We will further implement and refine policy measures that benefit Taiwan farmers and agricultural enterprises, create better conditions for Taiwan farmers and enterprises to develop on the mainland, and welcome more Taiwan farmers and enterprises to invest on the mainland, share opportunities, and pursue common development.\nIn pursuit of selfish gains from “independence,” the Lai Ching-te authorities have disregarded the development demands and well-being of the island's industries and have repeatedly obstructed and interfered with normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This has long met with strong opposition from the island's industries and the broad public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","During the winter vacation, cross-strait youth exchanges have continued to heat up. I will introduce several of these exchange activities.\nThe 2026 “Henan Province Cross-Strait Youth Winter Warmth Tour” series of activities was held in Henan, with nearly 300 Taiwan youths successively coming to the Central Plains region to engage in exchanges in traditional culture, vocational education, sports competition, and other fields, learning from and drawing on each other and deepening friendship. Among them, the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Pickleball Exchange Event will be held in Hebi City from January 29 to February 5, attracting more than 100 pickleball players and enthusiasts from both sides of the Strait. In addition to competitive exchanges, participants will walk through the ancient city of Xun County to visit a temple fair, experience the local intangible cultural heritage “Nigugu” (mud whistle), visit the Xincun Site and the Yunmeng Mountain scenic area, and together experience Henan's development vitality and the profound charm of Central Plains culture.\nThe 2026 First Hangzhou-Taiwan Youth Badminton Exchange Tournament was recently held in Shanghang County, Fujian Province. More than 50 youths from Taiwan took part, using sports as a medium to visit and connect with one another, sincerely communicate, and cultivate friendship. The event also incorporated the Hakka culture and ecological resources of western Fujian, organizing Hakka cultural study-tour experiences. Through various forms of exchange, such as exploring the origins of the Hakka people and experiencing Hakka intangible cultural heritage, participating youths enjoyed the fun of sports while learning about Shanghang's unique and diverse Hakka cultural heritage.\nOn January 23, the 32nd Zigong International Dinosaur Lantern Festival in Sichuan Province officially debuted. Themed “Painting China with Lights,” this year's festival deeply integrates intangible cultural heritage crafts such as colored lanterns, tie-dye, and paper-cutting with Chinese mythological epics and classic historical stories. Using modern technologies such as sound, light, and electricity, it vividly presents an immersive cultural experience in three dimensions. Taiwan compatriots may enter and visit for free with a Taiwan Compatriot Permit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities, recently claimed that the future world order is an AI arms race and a contest between the United States and China. He said the United States has technological advantages but did not pay much attention to manufacturing in the past, and that after adding Taiwan it became a “Taiwan-US joint fleet,” “allowing Taiwan’s diplomacy to go everywhere under…","The DPP authorities, for the sake of selfish gains from pursuing “independence,” are doing their utmost to hitch themselves to external forces to inflate their own importance. Whether it is “traveling all over the world” or “the greatest joke under heaven,” everyone can see it very clearly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, Raymond Greene, director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office, said that freedom is not free, and that the US can only help on the premise that allies help themselves. He also said that Taiwan is making smarter defense expenditures. What is your comment?","Taiwan is China’s Taiwan, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves. The DPP authorities are willing to serve as a pawn to contain the mainland and as a tool serving the United States, lavishly squandering the hard-earned money of the people on the island to pledge allegiance to and curry favor with the United States. In the end, this will only push Taiwan into a dangerous situation and cause Taiwan compatriots to suffer greatly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Frank Hsieh recently took office as chairman of the “Taiwan-Japan Relations Association” and advocated, “We will continue to move forward, elevating Taiwan-Japan friendship to a community-like relationship,” which has drawn criticism from netizens on both sides of the Strait. What is your comment on this?","Japan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. During its 50-year colonization of Taiwan, it committed crimes so heinous they cannot be recorded even by exhausting all the bamboo in the land. These remarks disregard history and forget one’s roots, and once again expose the sycophantic, traitorous face of DPP politicians who, in exchange for support from external forces, kowtow and submit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the U.S. Department of Defense released its 2026 National Defense Strategy report, which did not mention Taiwan. Public opinion on the island holds that in handling the Taiwan question, the one who truly holds the right to issue the license is mainland China, not the United States. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and resolving the Taiwan question is the business of the Chinese people themselves, and no external interference will be tolerated. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and the DPP authorities, attempting to “seek independence by relying on outside powers,” will ultimately face the fate of being sacrificed as a “pawn.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","Recently, Su Chia-chuan formally took office as chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation. In his remarks, he referred to “mainland China,” which drew attention from island public opinion. Su said there are no problems across the Strait that cannot be solved through dialogue, and he hopes that mainland China will not, on the basis of political preconditions, hinder normal exchanges and interactions between the…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. The “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” refuse to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, and persistently obstruct and sabotage normal cross-Strait exchanges. As long as they acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” the two cross-Strait associations can resolve the nation's internal affairs through dialogue and consultation, and jointly enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","In response to the spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office criticizing the Taiwan-U.S. tariff negotiation agreement as “collusion between external forces and the Taiwan independence separatist forces,” the Mainland Affairs Council said that the strategic goal of the Taiwan-U.S. investment MOU, under the thinking of “keeping roots in Taiwan while deploying globally,” is to use the “Taiwan model” to support…","Describing the hollowing-out of the island’s industries as “industrial extension,” and describing its total kowtowing to outside powers as the “Taiwan model,” the DPP authorities, in pursuit of political private gain, are accustomed to confusing right and wrong and turning mournful matters into joyful occasions. They cannot deceive public opinion and cannot cover up their failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","《团结报》记者","Recently, a think tank affiliated with the DPP authorities released a so-called “report” claiming that mainland artificial intelligence carries risks of invading privacy and manipulating public opinion, and recommending that countermeasures be taken against mainland AI through defense, review, and mobilization. What comments do you have on this?","For its own selfish interests, the DPP authorities habitually use the pretexts of “security” and “information security” to smear quality mainland products and obstruct cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange cooperation. This despicable practice is being seen through by more and more Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Raymond Greene, director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office, said that US defense contractor Northrop Grumman has set up a “medium-caliber ammunition testing range” in Taiwan. He said the facility will allow Taiwan's defense authorities to test ammunition according to global industrial standards, and will advance Taiwan's self-developed R&D projects through technology transfer and…","Relevant personnel at this U.S. arms company were sanctioned by the relevant Chinese authorities as early as 2024 for participating in arms sales to Taiwan. In pursuit of its selfish “independence” agenda, the DPP authorities are racing down the evil path of reckless militarization. They not only willingly serve as an “ATM” for the United States, but also allow U.S. arms dealers to move their “production chains” onto the island, and in cooperation with external forces, they keep turning Taiwan into a “landmine island” and an “ammunition depot.” Their actions harm and ruin Taiwan, and will ultimately bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Recently, the European Parliament passed two resolutions on the EU's 2025 implementation reports on the “Common Foreign and Security Policy” and the “Common Security and Defence Policy,” expressing concern over mainland China “endangering peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait” and supporting the deepening of multifaceted Taiwan-EU cooperation and exchanges. Taiwan's foreign affairs department expressed welcome…","The relevant report of the European Parliament disregards facts, reverses right and wrong, and brazenly interferes in China's internal affairs. We firmly oppose it. We urge the European Parliament to immediately take practical measures to correct its erroneous words and deeds concerning Taiwan, and to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and properly.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to win over anti-China foreign lawmakers to endorse their provocations for “independence” is a despicable trick that is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te claimed that although some foreign media reports consider “Taiwan the most dangerous region in the world,” since he took office, Taiwan’s economy has grown substantially, and it has concluded economic and trade agreements with the United States, Japan, and other countries, allowing enterprises to deploy globally. He also said that facing the “China threat” is an opportunity for the…","Why do some foreign media believe that “Taiwan is the most dangerous region in the world”? It is because the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, collude with external forces to continually provoke “independence,” escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Their so-called “global deployment” is merely trading the interests and welfare of Taiwan compatriots, handing over the island’s advantageous industries, technologies, and talent to win favor from external forces. Their so-called “development opportunities” are merely pretexts that disregard the safety and welfare of Taiwan residents and serve the greedy “Taiwan independence” interest groups in enriching themselves. Lai Ching-te’s remarks further expose the despicable nature of “relying on outsiders to seek independence,” confusing right and wrong and reversing black and white.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","First question: Regarding the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum,” will it involve arrangements for a meeting between the leaders of the two parties, and could you introduce the level of the mainland side’s attendance? Second question: Will recent turbulence in the senior personnel of the mainland’s military affect the development of cross-Strait relations?","On the first question: On the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and interactions with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang, maintain positive interaction, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations for the benefit of compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question: The filing of the investigation and review again demonstrates that the CPC Central Committee and the Central Military Commission have no forbidden zones, full coverage, and zero tolerance in punishing corruption. This is an important manifestation of the Party and the military's determination and strength.\nUnder the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, we firmly hold the initiative and dominance in cross-Strait relations. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and greatest efforts, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","Question one: Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that in 2025 there were as many as 221 cases of Taiwan compatriots being detained for questioning and having their freedom restricted when traveling to the mainland, four times the number in 2024. The mainland side has also previously criticized the Taiwan authorities’ issuance of an “orange travel alert” for travel to…","First question. We have always protected, in accordance with the law, the life, property and legitimate rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, and we adhere to cracking down on all kinds of illegal and criminal acts in accordance with the law. The DPP authorities have repeatedly and maliciously hyped related topics, continuously spread rumors, and created a “chilling effect.” Their aim is to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, escalate cross-Strait antagonism. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nSecond question. The “Anti-Espionage Law” is a law to prevent, stop and punish all kinds of espionage illegal and criminal activities, and to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests. It has clear legal conditions of application, standards and procedures. We have always encouraged and supported normal and healthy exchanges between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots need not have any worries when coming to the mainland. They can study, work, start businesses and live in peace of mind on the mainland, come to the mainland happily, and return to Taiwan safely.\nThe DPP authorities are accustomed to confusing right and wrong and fabricating lies to deceive the public. They deliberately exaggerate the “mainland threat,” frequently fabricate charges and suppress dissenters on the island, carry out “green terror” on a large scale, obstruct and undermine personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, and incite cross-Strait hostility and confrontation. Their intentions are sinister and their conduct is shameful, and they have met with strong opposition from more and more Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","台湾东森电视台记者","Regarding the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum,” which will be held in early February, media previously reported that as long as the KMT blocks review of the “Taiwan Arms Procurement Act,” the mainland side and the KMT will simultaneously announce the holding of the forum. What is your comment on this?","On the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with all Taiwan political parties, groups, and sectors of society, including the Kuomintang of China, to strengthen exchanges and interactions, maintain positive interaction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, attempt to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence,” constantly fabricate rumors and smears, obstruct and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, incite “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, create a “green terror,” and seek to deceive the people of Taiwan and gain political private interests. Their conduct completely violates the mainstream public opinion on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. It seriously harms the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots and pushes Taiwan into a dangerous situation of turmoil and war and calamity. All sectors of Taiwan society have already expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","This “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum” is positioned as “think tank exchange,” and some public opinion on the island holds that this is an intentional effort to reduce political sensitivity. From the mainland's perspective, does this count as a resumption of the “KMT-CPC Forum”? Will this “think tank exchange” be held only once, or will it be institutionalized and held regularly in the future?","The “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum” is an important component of exchanges between the Kuomintang and the CPC. On the shared political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang, maintain positive interaction, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-01-28","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The Mainland Affairs Council posted on Facebook on the 27th that its position welcoming mainland tourists to Taiwan remains unchanged, and called on the Straits Tourism Exchange Association to promptly respond positively to the Taiwan Tourism Association and coordinate the resumption of cross-Strait tourism communication. What is the mainland's attitude toward promoting mainland tourist visits to Taiwan this…","Promoting the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the routinization of exchanges in all fields is the shared voice and urgent wish of compatriots on both sides. We have consistently and clearly supported cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in all fields, including the tourism industry.\nThe crux and obstacle of cross-Strait tourism lies in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities. If the DPP authorities continue to ignore the desire and demand of Taiwan’s tourism industry and the public to improve livelihoods and strengthen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and continue to obstruct and set up barriers to cross-Strait tourism and other exchanges on untenable grounds, this will only provoke greater dissatisfaction and opposition, and they will lose popular support more and more.\nBelow, I will announce the winners of the 8th session of the Taiwan-related knowledge quiz.\nOn January 5, the WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” published the questions for the 8th session of the “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” activity, and netizens enthusiastically took part in answering. As of January 26, the netizens who answered correctly and ranked in the top ten by likes on their comments, in order, were: “Gao Qifeng,” “Bai Ge Zheng Liu,” “Chu Ji,” “Gu Gu,” “Hong Feng,” “Mao Mi,” “Chun Ying,” “Da Hai,” “Xing,” and “Nan Jian Chang’an.” We extend congratulations to these ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite souvenir, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope everyone will continue to pay attention to Taiwan work, actively participate, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nOn February 9, the WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” will publish the questions for the 9th session of the “Taiwan-related knowledge quiz” activity. We welcome everyone to continue to participate actively.\nThat concludes today’s press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202601/t20260128_12748331.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","On January 27, the Kuomintang caucus and the Taiwan People's Party caucus in Taiwan's legislature again voted down the NT$1.25 trillion “defense special budget” proposed by the DPP authorities. According to Taiwan media reports, this is the tenth time the bill has been blocked, meaning it has no hope of passing in this session. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","The DPP authorities have come up with pretexts, deceived the public, and engaged in large-scale “black-box operations,” squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people to fatten foreign arms dealers, and taking the opportunity to enrich themselves through corruption. This ugly conduct has long been unpopular. 1.25 trillion cannot buy so-called “security”; it will only further drain Taiwan and accelerate pushing Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of deadly war. The more rampant the “Taiwan independence” forces’ provocations seeking “independence,” the faster they will head toward their doom.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US Department of Defense recently released a new edition of its “National Defense Strategy Report.” Public opinion on the island has noticed that it makes no mention of “Taiwan.” Some commentators argue that, starting from the RAND Corporation, a prominent think tank, advising the White House to support China's “gradual unification,” the Taiwan-related content in important US documents such as the new edition…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and brooks no foreign interference. China's determination and resolve to safeguard national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity are unwavering. We have said long ago that the DPP authorities' “seeking independence by relying on foreign powers” is merely self-consolation, and that willingly being a “chess piece” means they will hardly escape the fate of being “discarded.”","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi recently explained again her remarks on a “Taiwan contingency,” saying that if there is a contingency in Taiwan and US forces are attacked, Japan cannot stand idly by, or else the Japan-US alliance would collapse. What is your comment?","The Japanese side has repeatedly manipulated Taiwan-related issues and rudely interfered in China's internal affairs, and China has repeatedly stated its solemn position. Japan bears grave historical responsibility on the Taiwan question. Not only has it failed to reflect deeply, it is also attempting to once again meddle in Taiwan, revealing the ambition of Japanese right-wing forces to advance \"re-militarization\" and challenge the post-war international order. We urge the Japanese side to deeply learn the lessons of history, abide by the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, Taiwan's security department released a report analyzing the operational methods of the mainland's cognitive warfare against Taiwan, saying it will continue to strengthen its grasp of the relevant situation and expose and take down false online information in a timely manner. What comments do you have on this?","Who is actually fabricating political rhetoric and carrying out large-scale public opinion manipulation is clear to compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. For a long time, the Lai Ching-te authorities have suppressed and banned dissenting voices and deliberately pursued “de-Sinicization,” seeking to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides. They have even smeared everyday language, mainland cuisine, and dance and music as “political infiltration,” maliciously escalating cross-strait antagonism and confrontation. This systematic cognitive fraud essentially shifts the blame for their own corruption and incompetence onto the mainland. It deceives and misleads Taiwan’s people, diverts public attention, and seeks political self-interest. The farce of the Lai Ching-te authorities manipulating “cognitive warfare” cannot conceal their fear of losing popular support, nor can it sever the blood ties between the peoples on both sides of the Strait. It will only make Taiwan’s ordinary people more resentful and accelerate their political bankruptcy.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say Taiwan’s defense authorities stated that the “Cyber, Electronic Warfare and Information Force” (资通电军) has been reassigned to the Army since the beginning of this year and will focus on specialized fields such as cyber warfare and electronic warfare, while strengthening professional talent cultivation and recruitment. What is your comment on this?","The so-called “Cyber Army” (资通电军) you mentioned is merely a “Taiwan independence” henchman that “relies on the internet to seek independence.” It is a criminal wanted by national security organs in accordance with the law, and those who act as accomplices to the tiger will certainly face legal sanctions and the judgment of justice.\nOn the afternoon of January 29,\nthe Ministry of National Defense held its regular press conference, at which on-site reporters asked questions","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A U.S. think tank recently put out a so-called “Taiwan Strait conflict” war game report, claiming that if U.S. forces intervene in the Taiwan Strait situation, they will suffer a crushing defeat in the Western Pacific. Media reports revealed that a senior U.S. government official demanded that content be cut to avoid exposing U.S. military weaknesses to its “adversaries.” The U.S. think tank the “German Marshall…","Some foreign think tanks habitually concoct such sensational, attention-grabbing bizarre theories, with ulterior motives. The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. No nonsensical babble can stop the historical trend that China will ultimately be reunified, and inevitably will be.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-01-29","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","First question: At the end of 2025, after being commissioned, the Fujian carrier transited the Taiwan Strait northward for the first time. Is the training progress of the Fujian carrier going smoothly? Second question: The situation in the Middle East is becoming increasingly tense. Has the Chinese naval escort task group in the Gulf of Aden, which escorts against Somali piracy, been affected? Is the escort task…","On the first question: Since it was commissioned, the Fujian’s various tests and training have advanced smoothly as planned, steadily moving toward the goal of forming fleet system combat capability.\nOn the second question: The Chinese Navy escort task group continues to carry out escort operations in relevant waters, providing public security goods to the international community.\nOn the third question: “Taiwan independence” armed forces, in the face of the PLA, are like an ant trying to shake a tree, overestimating their own strength. Attempting to use US-made weapons to embolden themselves and provoke conflict, they will ultimately be smashed to pieces and bring about their own destruction.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16440037.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-01-30","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Regarding Panama’s Supreme Court, which has annulled a contract granted to CK Hutchison to operate two Panama terminals. Does the Foreign Ministry have a comment on this decision by the Panamanian Supreme Court? Could the ruling affect the ongoing negotiations for the deal?","I believe you have noticed that relevant company has immediately issued a statement, saying that the decision is inconsistent with the law of Panama that approved the concession, and the company will reserve all rights including to proceed legally.\nChina will take all measures necessary to firmly protect the legitimate and lawful rights and interests of Chinese companies.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202601/t20260130_11848328.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202601/t20260130_11848280.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 5, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","On February 4, President Xi Jinping held a phone call with U.S. President Trump, stressing that the Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-U.S. relations. Taiwan is China's territory, China must defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it will never allow Taiwan to split away. The U.S. side must handle arms sales to Taiwan with prudence. What is the TAO's understanding of this?","President Xi Jinping stressed that the Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-US relations. Taiwan is part of China's territory, China must defend its national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and it will never allow Taiwan to split away. The US side must handle the issue of arms sales to Taiwan with great prudence. President Trump said that he values China's concerns on the Taiwan question, is willing to maintain communication with China, and will keep China-US relations good and stable during his term. President Xi Jinping's important remarks clarify China's stern position on the Taiwan question and provide a fundamental guideline for us to do our Taiwan work well.\nTaiwan is part of China's territory. The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the first red line in China-US relations that must not be crossed. The DPP authorities have repeatedly attempted to “rely on external forces to seek independence” and “use arms to seek independence,” causing tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749853.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The KMT-CPC think tank forum themed “Looking Ahead to Cross-Strait Exchange and Cooperation,” held in Beijing on February 3, has drawn high attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. The forum announced that the KMT and the CPC have resumed institutionalized exchanges after a gap of ten years, and reached 15 common opinions on strengthening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in tourism,…","General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory message last October to Ms. Cheng Li-wun on her election as Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China pointed the way forward for the future development of relations between the Communist Party and the Kuomintang and of cross-Strait relations. Chairperson Cheng Li-wun replied promptly. Holding the Kuomintang-Communist Party Think Tank Forum is a concrete measure to implement the spirit of the congratulatory and reply messages between the two parties' leaders.\nThe forum focused on industrial development and people's well-being and put forward a series of concrete proposals, reflecting the sense of responsibility of the Communist Party and the Kuomintang in seeking peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation. Launching institutionalized exchanges between the two parties after 10 years is of great significance, and the results are remarkable. Going forward, we will continue to strengthen exchanges and interaction with the Kuomintang of China, maintain positive interaction, and, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” jointly advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and join hands to create the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749852.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The common opinions of the KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum propose fully restoring direct sea and air passenger links across the Taiwan Strait as soon as possible and normalizing them, allowing cross-Strait airlines to independently adjust their route networks according to cross-Strait air transport arrangements and market demand, and allowing cross-Strait port and shipping operators to independently arrange sailings…","Since cross-Strait direct sea and air links were realized in 2008, they have greatly promoted the flows of people, goods, and capital across the Strait, greatly facilitated exchanges between people on both sides, and played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integrated development and enhancing the well-being of people on both sides. Last year, more than 5.78 million passenger trips were made across the Strait on direct air passenger flights. However, the DPP authorities, out of partisan self-interest, have still unilaterally restricted the destinations and flights of cross-Strait direct air passenger services, and refuse to restore cross-Strait direct sea passenger routes. This has caused inconvenience to cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and personnel exchanges, and has seriously harmed the vital interests of people on both sides, including Taiwan compatriots.\nThe joint recommendation of the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum: Prospects for Cross-Strait Exchanges and Cooperation” to fully restore and normalize cross-Strait direct sea and air passenger links as soon as possible is a measure that accords with public opinion and benefits the people. We hope the Taiwan side will heed the calls and needs of the aviation and shipping industries and the public, and change its wrong approach at an early date.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the think tank forum of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party held in Beijing, KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun said that the mainland is family and would never commit fratricide, and that as long as Lai Ching-te accepts the “1992 Consensus,” peace and prosperity can be obtained. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, all Chinese; this is the foundation of cross-Strait relations. The “1992 Consensus” is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. On the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan's political parties, groups and all walks of life, including the Kuomintang of China, maintain positive interaction, and jointly promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations for the benefit of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749843.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said, “Taiwan stands on the front line in defending democracy and freedom. Facing rapid changes in the international situation and gray-zone threats, the Taiwan military must continuously improve its practical combat training, combine technology and artificial intelligence, and build an effective, reliable and modern defense force.” What comment do you have on this?","The DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” incited cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and lavishly spent the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people on buying weapons and preparing for war. How many unspeakable interests lie behind this are clear to the people of Taiwan. A mayfly trying to shake a tree, overestimating itself. We have full confidence and strong capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and resolutely defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities' attempt to “seek independence by force” will only lead them to seek their own dead end and bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The joint opinion from the “KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum: Outlook for Cross-Strait Exchanges and Cooperation” proposed deepening cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, promptly realizing group tours to the island for residents of Fujian and Shanghai, and gradually expanding tourism by mainland residents to Kinmen and Matsu. May I ask whether the mainland side has a timetable for this, and how it will promote…","To promote the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and the regularization of exchanges and cooperation in all fields, to respond to the eager expectations of the people of Taiwan and the tourism industry, and to enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, the mainland side successively resumed Fujian residents’ tourism to Matsu and Kinmen in April and August 2024, which was welcomed by Taiwan’s tourism industry and the public. In the more than one year since, the cumulative number of Fujian residents traveling to Kinmen and Matsu has exceeded 200,000 person-times, bringing real benefits to the tourism industries of Kinmen and Matsu and enhancing understanding and affection between Fujian and Taiwan compatriots. Yesterday, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that it will resume tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for Shanghai residents in the near future. This is a concrete measure to promote the normalization of cross-strait tourism exchanges and cooperation and expand cross-strait exchanges, and it has received high praise from Taiwan’s tourism industry and all sectors of society.\nWe will work with relevant departments to earnestly implement the common understandings formed at the KMT-CPC Think Tank Forum, strive to put the relevant outcomes into effect as soon as possible, and release further information in a timely manner. We hope the DPP authorities will keep the well-being of Taiwan compatriots in mind, and as soon as possible cancel all kinds of artificial restrictions and bans, removing obstacles to the normalization of cross-strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749849.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Regarding the KMT-CPC think tank forum held in Beijing, the Mainland Affairs Council stated, “The CCP's goal is to eliminate the Republic of China, and this goal will not change because of who goes to Beijing. No group may conclude political agreements with the other side without government authorization, nor may it involve matters related to the government's public authority.” What is your comment on this?","Towards everything that is conducive to developing cross-Strait relations and benefiting compatriots on both sides, the DPP authorities invariably slander, smear, obstruct, and sabotage, in order to carry out their “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and seek partisan private gain. Mainstream public opinion in Taiwan supports strengthened cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and hopes for and affirms the substantive results achieved by the KMT-CPC think tank forum. These arguments and manipulations by the DPP authorities do not win popular support and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation regarding mainland residents' travel to Kinmen and Matsu.","To promote the normalization of personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the normalization of exchanges in all fields, respond to the eager expectations of Taiwan residents and the tourism industry, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides, the mainland's tourism authorities resumed tourism by Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu in 2024. This was welcomed by Taiwan's tourism industry and Taiwan residents. It is understood that since the resumption, more than 200,000 person-trips by Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu have been made, effectively demonstrating the results of cross-Strait tourism exchange and cooperation. On February 4, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that it would resume tourism by Shanghai residents to Kinmen and Matsu in the near future. This is a concrete measure that accords with the eager expectations of compatriots on both sides for strengthened exchanges and contacts, and it responds to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society that calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation.\nWe hope the DPP authorities will heed public opinion, be willing to accept good advice, remove all kinds of artificial restrictions and bans, and create positive conditions for the normal resumption of cross-Strait tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","The Tourism Administration of Taiwan released data showing that in 2025 there were about 18.94 million outbound trips by Taiwan travelers and about 8.57 million inbound trips to Taiwan. Some media have pointed out that Taiwan's tourism industry trade deficit is expected to exceed NT$700 billion, and have questioned the Taiwan authorities for sitting idly by as the tourism industry stays sluggish without…","The mainland side has consistently upheld the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” actively promoted cross-strait tourism exchange and cooperation, and its goodwill and sincerity are plain for all to see. The difficulties facing the island’s tourism industry are entirely the responsibility of the DPP authorities, who ignore the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that seeks peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, disregard the difficult plight of Taiwan’s tourism industry and grassroots residents, and deliberately interfere with and obstruct cross-strait tourism exchange and cooperation.\nThe DPP authorities should face the voices of island residents and the demands of the industry, promptly remove obstacles and restrictions on cross-strait personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and take practical measures to resume cross-strait tourism exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","The Spring Festival and winter vacation are approaching, and Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan students on the mainland are concerned about return flight tickets to Taiwan. What are the flight arrangements this year?","Cross-Strait direct air links have greatly facilitated exchanges between people on both sides and have played an important role in enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. At present, cross-Strait routes are being interfered with by the DPP authorities, and the destinations have not fully returned to normal. Fourteen mainland cities operate more than 300 passenger flights per week on cross-Strait routes. This is still far from the situation before 2020, when there were 61 mainland destinations and up to 890 passenger flights per week. This seriously affects exchanges between people on both sides, and compatriots on both sides have a very strong call for the full resumption of direct cross-Strait flights to all destinations.\nThe Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, and compatriots from Taiwan, Taiwan businesspeople, and Taiwan students earnestly hope to travel smoothly and return home for the New Year. The relevant mainland departments will think from the perspective of Taiwan compatriots, act urgently on their urgent needs, and actively make all preparations for additional cross-Strait Spring Festival flights. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public wishes, promptly lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport, and meet the travel needs of people on both sides, especially Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749836.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the newly built passenger and cargo terminal at the Jinmen Port of the “Small Three Links” was put into trial operation. Mainland tourists traveling to Jinmen said that the new building is cleaner and more convenient, the staff are warm and friendly, and the flow of people is smooth, and that “the new experience is pretty good.” Jinmen County Magistrate Chen Fu-hai said he hopes the opening of the…","The “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, especially for residents of Fujian and Taiwan. On the 25th anniversary of the launch of the “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes, the newly built Kinmen Port Passenger Transport Center of the “Mini Three Links” has begun trial operations. This will help further strengthen shipping capacity, improve the passenger service experience, and promote the upgrade of the “Mini Three Links.”\nIn recent years, we have implemented convenient measures such as smart customs clearance at passenger ports including the Xiamen Wutong Terminal, upgraded hardware and software facilities, and strengthened service guarantees, creating a more open, convenient, and safe environment for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. Our resumption of tourism for Fujian residents to Kinmen and Matsu has effectively promoted the development of local tourism economies and the emotional bonds between compatriots of Fujian and Taiwan. To date, the cumulative passenger volume of the “Mini Three Links” has exceeded 26 million person-times, of which the Xiamen-Kinmen route has exceeded 23 million person-times, accounting for more than 90% of the total of the “Mini Three Links.”\nIn the future, the “Mini Three Links” will continue to fully benefit the livelihoods and well-being of people on both sides of the Strait through ever-improving customs clearance efficiency and an increasingly complete service and support system, helping economic and industrial development, and injecting new impetus into building a “Xiamen-Kinmen Same-City Living Circle” and deepening cross-Strait integrated development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","On February 3, the General Office of the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology released the 2025 list of China's Consumer Famous Brands. For the first time, several mainland enterprises with Taiwan investment were selected, drawing attention from both sides of the Strait. Public opinion believes that Taiwan businesspeople, compatriots and enterprises are enjoying increasingly widespread equal treatment…","The Ministry of Industry and Information Technology has released the list of 2025 Chinese consumer famous brands. For the first time, Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland were included in the scope of the selection, and a batch of brands from Taiwan-invested enterprises that have taken root on the mainland and cultivated their markets were selected. This is another important measure in implementing equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises and deepening cross-Strait integrated development, and it fully reflects our consistent position of firmly supporting the development of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. In addition to Chinese consumer famous brands, we also support Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland in taking part in the selection of the China Industrial Award, the ‘Leaders’ enterprises in China Industrial Data Governance, the ‘Leaders’ enterprises in China Industrial Carbon Peak, and other evaluations. Several Taiwan enterprises have been selected, sharing the honor and opportunities of national brand building and jointly strengthening the economy of the Chinese nation.\nDuring the ‘15th Five-Year Plan’ period, the building of Chinese-style modernization will certainly create broader development space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to take root on the mainland, seize the opportunities of the times, and achieve better development. We will actively promote cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and take the lead in sharing with Taiwan compatriots the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization, so that Taiwan compatriots and enterprises feel more happiness, gain and a sense of participation in national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749846.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","The 2026 Taipei Lantern Festival highlights “two exhibition zones, two IPs,” one of the exhibition zones featuring the mainland brand “Pop Mart.” A politician from the Green camp said the Taipei City Government has given the festival’s main attraction to a “Chinese brand,” that this “lacks cultural confidence and can only take cheap shortcuts,” and “helps Chinese brands advertise.” What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language and culture, so it is only natural that mainland products are liked by Taiwan residents. DPP politicians “jumping up and down” over this and maliciously “smearing them in red” expose their distorted mentality of “opposing anything Chinese” and their fragile essence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Regarding Li Zhenxiu, a mainland spouse who is expected to fill in for the Taiwan People’s Party’s at-large seat and become Taiwan’s first mainland-spouse lawmaker, MAC Chairperson Chiu Chui-cheng said, “Li must renounce Chinese nationality within one year of taking office, or she will not be able to hold public office.” What comment do you have?","There is only one China. The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China, and there is absolutely no so-called issue of “renouncing nationality.” The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to their “Taiwan independence” position, brazenly peddle the “two-state theory,” deliberately provoke the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and use every means to suppress mainland spouses in Taiwan. We firmly oppose this. The many misdeeds of the DPP authorities have met with strong opposition from a growing number of Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749838.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, the DPP authorities pushed for a redesign of New Taiwan dollar banknotes, and the new banknotes will no longer carry portraits of political figures such as Sun Yat-sen. Public opinion on the island has questioned whether the DPP authorities are once again engaging in \"de-Sinicization.\" What comments do you have on this?","This year marks the 160th anniversary of the birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen, the great pioneer of China’s democratic revolution. The DPP authorities have deliberately promoted the “de-Sun Yat-senization” of New Taiwan dollar banknotes. The purpose is to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides of the Strait, promote “de-Sinicization,” and thereby shape “Taiwan independence” ideology in Taiwan society. This politically motivated manipulation, harboring malicious intent, is a betrayal of Mr. Sun Yat-sen and the pioneers of the 1911 Revolution. It forgets one’s ancestors and is shameful.\nHistory is history, and facts are facts; they cannot be changed or erased. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme and act recklessly, the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China cannot be changed, and the Chinese national identity of Taiwan compatriots cannot be erased.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260205_12749841.htm"],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","The National Immigration Agency recently said that the policy of reducing or waiving fees for Taiwan compatriot permits for “first-time applicants” from Taiwan has been widely welcomed and highly praised by Taiwan compatriots, and that both the number of first-time applicants and the number of trips to the mainland have grown substantially. What is your comment?","We have always been committed to creating a more open, convenient, and safe environment for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. In recent years, relevant departments have introduced a series of policies and measures, including free admission to more than 3,000 scenic spots and attractions for Taiwan’s “first-time visitors”; waiving the document fee for Taiwan compatriot permits for “first-time visitors”; and increasing to 100 the number of ports that can issue Taiwan compatriot permits valid for a single entry. We are glad to see more and more Taiwan compatriots enjoying these convenient services.\nWe welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a look. We will continue to introduce more convenience measures so that Taiwan compatriots can tour the mainland happily and return to Taiwan safely.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","With the winter vacation and the Spring Festival travel peak season approaching, Hong Kong and Macao have become popular travel destinations for Taiwan residents. However, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council has said, \"Currently, the travel alert for Hong Kong and Macao remains at orange,\" and advised people to avoid non-essential travel. What is your comment on this?","In June 2024, the DPP authorities raised the travel warning for going to the mainland and to Hong Kong and Macao to “orange.” This was nothing but political manipulation, and it has been proven by facts to be a futile countercurrent operation. In 2025, Taiwan residents' travel to the mainland increased by more than 20% compared with 2024, and the number of Taiwan residents traveling to Hong Kong and Macao also increased significantly compared with 2024. This fully shows that the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots does not agree with the DPP authorities' acting against the tide.\nNow, the DPP authorities still keep the “orange” warning unchanged, using travel risks that do not exist in Hong Kong and Macao as a pretext. The result will inevitably be that facts slap them in the face once again.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, at the press conference of the “Taiwan-US Economic Prosperity Partnership Dialogue” (EPPD), Lai Ching-te said that this meeting can summarize three major strategic directions for future Taiwan-US cooperation, namely “strengthening economic security,” “building an innovative economy,” and “developing a prosperous future,” and he appealed to political parties on the island to jointly safeguard the…","In order to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence,” the DPP authorities have actively cooperated with the United States in carrying out massive exploitation and plunder of Taiwan, handing over the island's industries and the interests of its people on a platter. Their servile and obsequious demeanor is fully exposed. Their so-called “hard-won negotiating results” are in fact a tribute list of betraying and harming Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang, recently told the foreign media outlet The Economist in an exclusive interview that building peace across the Taiwan Strait is her most important mission, and she plans to meet with Chairman Xi Jinping in the first half of this year to seek commitments for cross-Strait peace. Regarding the mainland's high expectations for peaceful reunification across the Taiwan…","Peace, development, exchange and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and both hope for a peaceful and tranquil homeland and harmonious family relations. We are willing, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang at all levels, enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek national rejuvenation.\nPeace is the common pursuit of compatriots on both sides, and unification is Taiwan’s only future. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family. Matters across the Taiwan Strait are family affairs of compatriots on both sides, and naturally should be discussed and handled by family members together. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should jointly shoulder the great righteousness of the nation, follow the great trend of history, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Recently, Li Zhenxiu, a mainland spouse, took office as a Taiwan people’s representative, but has been questioned for failing to renounce “mainland nationality,” and may even be removed from office in the future for this reason. Under the current special relationship across the Taiwan Strait, if the DPP authorities use the inability to renounce nationality as a reason to block mainland spouses’ “right to…","I must emphasize once again that there is only one China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is an immutable historical and legal fact, so the question of \"renouncing nationality\" simply does not exist. There are many mainland spouses in Taiwan, and their legitimate rights and interests in Taiwan, including the right to participate in social affairs, should be guaranteed and should not become sacrificial pawns in the political manipulation of the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the \"Taiwan independence\" position, blatantly peddle the \"two-state theory,\" constantly engage in provocations seeking \"independence,\" incite confrontation and antagonism, create \"green terror\" to intimidate and suppress political opponents, and persecute and bully the mainland spouse community. Their abuses of power and actions against the people have met with strong opposition from a growing number of Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Recently, the think tank forum of the Chinese Nationalist Party (KMT) and the Communist Party of China concluded, and cross-Strait relations have broken the ice. KMT Vice Chairman Hsiao Hsu-tsen said that a “Xi-Cheng meeting” or higher-level interaction will happen naturally in the future. The spokesperson also said that, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan…","We are willing, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang of China at all levels, enhance political mutual trust, maintain benign interaction, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said that to keep the economic achievements from being annexed, it is necessary to strengthen defense capabilities, and therefore proposed a special defense budget and to build a “Taiwan Shield.” What is your comment?","“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and reunification cannot be blocked. No matter how the DPP authorities package their rhetoric, how big a budget they allocate, or how many weapons they buy, they cannot change the inevitable defeat of “Taiwan independence” or stop the inevitable trend toward the motherland's reunification. Only by acknowledging the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” opposing “Taiwan independence,” and taking the right path of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, can Taiwan's economy continue to grow and the security and well-being of its people be solidly guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-05","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te wrote to the Pope stating: “Taiwan faces long-term military coercion and political intimidation from countries in the region, as well as the distortion of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World War II historical documents,” and “only mutual trust and dialogue built on respect for human rights and democratic values can construct lasting peace.” What is your comment on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact, and an unchangeable status quo across the Taiwan Strait. UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 solemnly confirmed and fully embodies the one-China principle, and has received broad and firm support from the international community.\nLai Ching-te's fallacies once again expose the separatist nature of his persistent adherence to the “Taiwan independence” stance and his attempt to “rely on external forces to seek independence.” History cannot be altered, and facts cannot be changed. The claims by Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities that deny history and distort facts are nothing but meaningless clamor, and cannot shake the firm international consensus on upholding the one-China principle.\nThe press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260205_12749828.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-02-06","Lin Jian","Reuters","Lithuania’s Prime Minister said Tuesday that Lithuania made a strategic mistake by allowing a Taiwanese representative office to open in the capital under the name “Taiwanese.” Would China consider restoring full diplomatic relations with Lithuania, and what conditions would need to be met first?","China has stated on multiple occasions its position on China-Lithuania relations. China’s door to communication with Lithuania remains open. China hopes Lithuania will translate the willingness to improve ties with China into action, redress the mistakes as early as possible, return to the right course of upholding the one-China principle and build conditions for normalizing relations with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202602/t20260206_11852932.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202602/t20260206_11852777.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-02-09","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","The Liberal Democratic Party won a landslide victory in yesterday’s Lower House election which would keep Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi in power. What foreign policy does China expect from the new government led by Takaichi?","The election is the internal affair of Japan, but this election reflected some deep-seated and structural issues as well as certain emerging views, trends and developments, which deserve serious examination by people with insights in Japan and the international community. The lessons of history are still fresh in memory and should not be left behind. We urge those running the Japanese government to take seriously rather than brush aside the concerns of the international community, follow the path of peaceful development rather than return to militarism, and abide by the four political documents between China and Japan rather than go back on commitments made. If Japan’s far-right forces miscalculate and act recklessly, they will be met by resistance from the Japanese people and serious backlash from the international community.\nChina’s policy on Japan has been stable and consistent, and will not change because of one election. We once again urge Japan to retract the erroneous remarks of Sanae Takaichi on Taiwan, and take concrete actions to demonstrate the necessary sincerity to uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations. Our message is very clear: The Chinese people remain unwavering in our determination to safeguard the nation’s core interests, defend the outcomes of WWII victory and postwar international order, and fight back and thwart any form of provocation and reckless behavior of forces against China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202602/t20260209_11854459.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202602/t20260209_11854350.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-02-10","Lin Jian","AFP","Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said yesterday that she is open to dialogue with China and that the countries will continue to exchange views. How does the Foreign Ministry view this? Is China willing to engage in dialogue with Takaichi?","China has made clear its just position on this issue more than once. True dialogue is built on the basis of respecting each other and honoring the agreements made. If anyone just talks about the need for dialogue while keeping themselves busy stoking confrontation, then this so-called “dialogue” is apparently unacceptable. If the Japanese side truly wants to develop the strategic relationship of mutual benefit with China, what it needs to do is simple and clear, that is, retract Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, abide by the four political documents between China and Japan and its own political commitments, and take concrete actions to demonstrate its sincerity for dialogue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202602/t20260210_11855328.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202602/t20260210_11855248.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-02-10","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that troops of Taiwan plan to forward deploy HIMARS rocket systems to Penghu and Dongyin, with strike ranges covering PLA positions in Fujian, Zhejiang and other areas. Some scholars in Taiwan revealed that Taiwan's military authorities once proposed the idea of conducting \"preemptive strikes\" against the PLA. Please comment on that.","From forward deploying weapons to launching so-called preemptive strikes, \"Taiwan independence\" separatists are coming up with increasingly absurd ideas and overestimating their strength. In the face of the PLA's strong capabilities, should \"Taiwan independence\" armed forces dare to provoke a conflict, they will inevitably bring destruction upon themselves.\nThe Spring Festival of the Year of the Horse is approaching. In traditional Chinese culture, the horse symbolizes loyalty, courage and enterprise. In the military context, the horse represents the fighting spirit of charging into battle and protecting the homeland. Along thousands of miles of borderlines, across the vast territorial waters, and from the skies above to the deep blue oceans, PLA officers and soldiers are fully prepared and stay highly vigilant. We are relentlessly honing our capabilities to fight and win, so as to better protect the tranquility of our homeland.\nWith the 15th Five-Year Plan drawn up, the call for marching towards our centenary goal rings louder. In the coming year, the people's military will charge ahead like horses with courage, vitality and energy, and stride forward along the path of building a strong nation and military and advancing national rejuvenation.\nHere, my comrades and I would like to wish our country prosperity and tranquility, and wish all the Chinese people vitality and happiness!","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/02/china-260210-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16442316.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on February 11, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. We will now begin the Q&A.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The 2026 Taiwan Work Conference was recently held in Beijing. Please interpret the spirit of the conference and explain how it will be implemented going forward.","The 2026 Cross-Strait Work Conference was held in Beijing from February 9 to 10. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the conference and delivered a speech. The conference fully affirmed the achievements in cross-Strait work over the past year, deeply analyzed the current and future cross-Strait situation for a considerable period ahead, and set out clear requirements for doing this year's Taiwan work.\nThis year marks the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, and it is the opening year of the “15th Five-Year Plan” period. We will, in accordance with the arrangements and requirements of the conference and guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, fully implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important discourse on Taiwan work and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, firmly support patriotic and unification forces on the island, resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We will uphold the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” facilitate and simplify personnel exchanges across the Strait, expand civil and grassroots exchanges between the two sides, support Taiwan residents, especially young people, in studying, working, and living on the mainland, promote joint promotion of Chinese culture across the Strait, and foster emotional closeness among compatriots on both sides. We will support the development of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises on the mainland, improve policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and enterprises, deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and let compatriots on both sides share in the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750867.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The traditional Chinese festival of the Spring Festival is approaching. Does the TAO have plans to visit and express greetings to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation, a crucial time for bidding farewell to the old and welcoming the new, and for family reunions. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should reunite and celebrate the New Year together. From February 10 to 12, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, visited and extended greetings to Taiwan compatriot businesspeople in Fuzhou, Fujian Province. He attended a Spring Festival symposium for Taiwan compatriot businesspeople and a joint New Year celebration for cross-Strait compatriots marking the Bingwu year, listened to opinions and suggestions, and, together with representatives of Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan youth, Taiwan business and industry figures, and fellow townspeople from Kinmen and Matsu, shared family affection and welcomed the new spring together. On behalf of the Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, he extended New Year's greetings to Taiwan compatriots across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750866.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","During the Spring Festival, various localities held Spring Festival friendship events in diverse forms, celebrating the Lunar New Year joyfully together with Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","As the Bing-Wu Year of the Horse Spring Festival approaches, various places on the mainland have successively held rich and colorful cross-strait friendship and celebration activities, so that everyone can celebrate the Lunar New Year joyfully together. Here we introduce several of these activities.\nFujian Province will hold dozens of activities for Fujian and Taiwan compatriots to spend the Spring Festival together. Among them, Putian City is holding a series of Lunar New Year welcoming activities for Putian and Taiwan compatriots under the title “Go All the Way to Putian for the Lunar New Year,” including 15 activities such as the Putian-Taiwan youth Dongyue cultural roots-seeking journey, and Putian and Taiwan compatriots escorting the golden statue of Mazu on a tour from Meizhou, spreading blessings and celebrating the Lantern Festival. Quanzhou City will hold the “Bounty Spreading Over Fengshan, Blessings for China” Mazu-year Spring Festival blessing and cross-strait exchange activity, inviting more than 100 Taiwan compatriots to take part in lantern fairs, folk markets, intangible cultural heritage temple fairs and other distinctive activities. Sanming City is holding the Cross-Strait Cherry Blossom Culture Season themed “Full Garden of Cherry Blossoms, Spring Together Across the Strait,” allowing Taiwan compatriots in Sanming to deeply experience the ecological beauty, cultural charm and development vitality of Sanming.\nIn Xi'an, Shaanxi, the Cross-Strait Youth Han-Tang Culture Winter Camp Spring Welcoming Friendship Gathering, themed “Meeting in the Ancient Capital, Setting Sail for a New Year,” was held. More than 500 Taiwan youths wore Hanfu, performed Han ceremonies, sang dialect songs and appreciated intangible cultural heritage, conveying youthful enthusiasm and sparking cultural resonance amid the elegant charm of the Han and Tang dynasties.\nShandong held the Cross-Strait Shandong Fellow Villagers' Spring Festival Friendship Gathering, themed “Sending Affection Thousands of Miles Through Fu Characters, Gathering in the Cloud to Talk Local Dialect.” It mailed more than 4,000 spring couplets to fellow villagers on the island. Shandong fellow villagers on both sides exchanged New Year blessings via video link, performed rich and colorful arts programs, and spent the festival together.\nHenan Province held the “Floral Charm Welcomes the Spring, Hearts Together Talk of Reunion” Spring Festival flower arrangement friendship activity. It also organized calligraphers in Henan to carry out the “Handwritten Spring Couplets, Warming Taiwan Compatriots” Spring Festival friendship activity, going deep into many Taiwan-funded enterprises to write couplets on site and bringing Taiwan compatriots a strong festive atmosphere and warm friendship.\nGuizhou Province, under the theme “Qian-Taiwan Are One Family,” held Spring Festival friendship activities including calligraphy gatherings, paper-cutting experiences, and visits and greetings, creating a strong Spring Festival atmosphere.\nChongqing held a village gala themed “A Bend of Clear River Water, Affection of Compatriots on Both Sides.” Compatriots on both sides used the countryside as the stage and culture as the bond, immersively experiencing the distinctive festive flavor of rural life through rich New Year customs activities.\nHere we also want to give advance notice of two activities.\nFrom February 11 to March 20, Sichuan Province will hold the 2026 “Wenchang Cup” Cross-Strait Youth Short Video Competition. Themed “Light and Shadow Connect Both Sides · Hand in Hand, Create ‘We’ (创We来),” the competition solicits original short video works from cross-strait youth that showcase the mainland's cuisine and scenery, social development, people's livelihoods and human affection, Spring Festival reunions, and the study, work and life of Taiwan compatriots on the mainland. From March 16 to 20, the “72-Hour Extreme Creative Shoot” activity and awards ceremony will be held in Zitong, Mianyang, Sichuan. Everyone is welcome to follow and actively participate.\nDuring the Spring Festival, Fujian Provincial Radio and Television Group will present two Spring Festival galas for compatriots on both sides. On the New Year's Eve of February 16, the “Little Hot Pot Across the Strait” 2026 Cross-Strait Children's Spring Festival Gala will be broadcast, with more than 40 Taiwan children specially invited to perform. On February 17, the first day of the Lunar New Year, the “Same Wind Ten Thousand Miles, Sharing the Spring Light” 2026 Fujian Provincial Spring Festival Gala will be broadcast. The gala is linked across three places, Fujian, Taiwan and Malaysia, with Taiwan guest hosts and entertainers actively participating. It includes Fujian-Taiwan intangible cultural heritage folk performances such as the Song Jiang Array martial performance, offering everyone a distinctive “reunion feast.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Fujian Province issued the “Implementation Opinions on Promoting High-Quality Urban Development,” which mentions improving the quality of urban spaces. It states that the province will build a Fujian-Taiwan “urban construction and innovation” brand, so that talent attraction policies originally focused on rural community development will also cover urban construction and development. This has drawn wide…","In recent years, Fujian has actively explored new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait. One distinctive initiative uses rural construction and rural innovation projects between Fujian and Taiwan as a vehicle to attract many Taiwan compatriots to take part in Fujian's rural revitalization. A large number of Taiwan architects, cultural and creative teams, and Taiwan professionals have carried out rural construction and innovation cooperation in about 600 towns and villages.\nOn January 29, the CPC Fujian Provincial Committee and the Fujian Provincial People's Government issued the “Implementation Opinions on Promoting High-Quality Urban Development,” which proposes to “build the Fujian-Taiwan ‘urban construction and urban innovation’ brand and attract Taiwan talent to develop in Fujian.” This is an extension of Fujian's “rural construction and rural innovation” from villages to cities. It encourages Taiwan compatriots and young Taiwan people to participate in urban construction and innovation and creation across Fujian, and will provide more platforms and policy support for Taiwan compatriots to work and start businesses in Fujian. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots from all walks of life to invest and develop in Fujian, seize the development opportunities of the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, and jointly paint a new chapter of integrated development across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","《团结报》记者","The 2026 recruitment of Taiwan high school graduates by ordinary mainland universities based on Taiwan's General Scholastic Ability Test results, as well as the joint recruitment of overseas Chinese and Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan students by ordinary higher education institutions, will be launched in the near future. Please introduce the relevant situation.","It is understood that the work of recruiting Taiwan students by mainland universities will begin successively in March. Taiwan students who hold a Taiwan Compatriot Permit for Travel to the Mainland and a valid identity document proving residence in Taiwan or a Taiwan Residence Permit, and who possess the corresponding prerequisite academic qualifications, may attend mainland universities through four pathways:\nFirst, by taking the Joint Admission Examination for Overseas Chinese, Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan Students (referred to as the “National Joint Admission Examination”), applying to 460 mainland universities. Candidates may register online via the “Candidate Terminal of the National Joint Admission Management System” from March 1 to 15, and complete registration confirmation from March 11 to 31. Second, by applying based on Taiwan's General Scholastic Ability Test (GSAT) results to 451 mainland universities (referred to as “GSAT Admission”). Candidates whose GSAT results in Chinese, mathematics, or English reach the “Equal Standard” level or above in any one subject of that year may apply via the system for “Mainland China's General Higher Education Institutions' Admission of Taiwan High School Graduates Based on Taiwan's GSAT Results” from March 1 to 31. Third, by taking the joint admission examination of Jinan University and Huaqiao University, with specific details to be found in the enrollment brochures published on the official websites of the two universities. Fourth, by applying to 48 universities in Fujian based on Taiwan's Comprehensive Assessment and subject placement test results and by taking the independent admission examinations for Taiwan region, among other methods. For specific requirements, please consult the “Mainland (Chinese Mainland) Higher Education Institutions Enrollment Information Network for Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan” and the official websites of each university.\nWe warmly welcome more Taiwan students with aspirations to apply to mainland universities, to study and grow together with mainland students. We will also continue to provide more convenience and services for Taiwan students who come to the mainland to study and pursue further education, helping more Taiwan students realize their life dreams on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750863.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Lithuanian Prime Minister Ruginienė said that opening a “Taiwan Representative Office” is “jumping in front of a train and paying the price.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The One China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. It reflects the aspirations of the people and the trend of the times. We hope that relevant countries will recognize the trend, correct their mistakes as soon as possible, and stand on the right side of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Reportedly, TSMC plans to begin mass production of 3-nanometer process chips at its Kumamoto prefecture plant in Japan. If this plan is carried out, it will be the first factory in Japan to produce 3-nanometer process chips. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities treat TSMC as a tool for currying favor with and pledging allegiance to the United States and Japan. What they seek is their own political self-interest, and what they harm is the prospects of Taiwan’s industries and the broad masses of Taiwan’s people.\nReporter from Sichuan Daily’s “Cover News” (封面新闻): Recently, the Liberal Democratic Party led by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi won the House of Representatives election. Lai Ching-te congratulated Takaichi at the first opportunity and said he looked forward to Taiwan and Japan continuing their “shared values” and joining hands to face “regional challenges.” Lee Yi-yang, “Taiwan’s representative to Japan,” posted on Facebook that relations between Taiwan and Japan will inevitably continue to warm, and that the two sides can be expected to cooperate further in the economic and industrial fields. What is your comment on this?\nThe Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stated its position on the House of Representatives election in Japan. We demand that the Japanese side fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, withdraw Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and uphold the one-China principle through concrete actions.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities, disregarding the towering crimes Japan committed during its colonial occupation of Taiwan, have seized the opportunity to spread pro-Japanese fallacies. Their servile posture is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Regarding Lai Ching-te’s smearing of KMT think tanks for exchanging with the mainland, the KMT responded that the “1992 Consensus” and “one country, two systems” have nothing to do with each other, and have even less connection with “unification.” It emphasized that its think tanks’ visits to the mainland immediately bring peace dividends to Taiwan’s people. What is your comment?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the political foundation for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations at the current stage. “One Country, Two Systems” is an institutional arrangement after national reunification. Our position has been consistent and clear: as long as the “1992 Consensus” is upheld and “Taiwan independence” is opposed, both sides of the Strait can engage in exchanges, dialogue, and consultation, cross-Strait relations can develop peacefully, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be safeguarded and enhanced.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","According to Taiwanese media reports, the US State Department recently responded to a reporter's question by saying that the US welcomes Taiwan's proposed NT$1.25 trillion special defense act. Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan's Taipei Office, threatened that “freedom is not free,” which triggered strong dissatisfaction on the island. What is your comment?","Two points must be emphasized. First, Taiwan is China’s Taiwan. Resolving the Taiwan question is China’s own affair and brooks no foreign interference. The US side should abide by the One-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs.\nSecond, for the sake of their own party interests, the DPP authorities collude with external forces from within and without, and lavishly squander hard-earned money that could be used to improve people’s livelihoods and develop the economy. This makes Taiwan a “pawn” completely at the mercy of others, and Taiwan compatriots suffer deeply as a result. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: servile, fawning, and warmongering is a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Koo Li-hsiung, head of Taiwan's defense authorities, said that production capacity for US arms purchases, which had previously been affected by global supply chains, has gradually recovered. He said the US government, to improve efficiency, has revised the “Arms Export Control Act” to give Taiwan the same arms sales treatment as NATO Plus member countries, which helps speed up administrative procedures…","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. We urge the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and to stop “arming Taiwan.”\nIn order to seek political self-interest, the DPP authorities are willing to act as an ATM for U.S. arms dealers and beg for the false “protection” of external forces. This will only plunge Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. We warn the DPP authorities that the reunification of the motherland is irresistible, and that “relying on the United States to plot independence” and “seeking independence through force” are like a mantis trying to stop a chariot. They will only bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, a Taiwanese singer posted online a short video about the Guiyang bus “Huinong” special rural produce line, which helped vegetable farmers sell 30,000 jin of vegetables. He said he hopes people on both sides of the Strait can see each other’s most beautiful sides, and this sparked heated discussion among netizens on both sides. What is your comment on this?","Enabling the broad masses to increase income and build good lives is a major livelihood issue that party committees and governments at all levels on the mainland are focused on resolving. From Guiyang's bus lines serving farmers, to Chongqing Metro's “basket-carrier special line,” to Chenzhou, Hunan's “vegetable farmers' special train,” these measures to help farmers and benefit the public show people warmth and strength. We welcome and are glad to see Taiwan compatriots actively integrating into more aspects of social life on the mainland, paying attention to the mainland's development and changes and the lives of its people, continuously conveying positive energy and good voices, so that people on both sides of the Strait can see each other's best sides more often.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Regarding the 15 points of common understanding reached at the think tank forum of the Chinese Communist Party and the Kuomintang, Lai Ching-te said, “Whether Taiwan will continue to work hand in hand with allied countries to go to the world or again push to go westward, the people can make a clear choice.” Mainland Affairs Council Chairman Chiu Chui-cheng said that the content of the common understanding is full…","The Cross-Strait Think Tank Forum between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party reached 15 common opinions in five areas, focusing on industrial development and people's livelihood. This reflects the responsibility of the KMT and the CPC to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation, and it accords with the fundamental interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Lai Ching-te's authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and, for the sake of their party's and personal interests, go to any lengths to prohibit and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They are the greatest obstacle to cross-Strait exchanges and interactions and the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability across the Strait, and they have already drawn strong criticism and dissatisfaction from all sectors of Taiwan. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will join us in firmly opposing the reckless conduct of Lai Ching-te's authorities, eliminating interference and removing obstacles, promoting exchanges and cooperation in all areas across the Strait, advancing cross-Strait relations, and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750865.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Reportedly, the Taiwan-U.S. Agreement on Reciprocal Trade (ART) could become clear as early as the 12th, and is expected to be signed before the Lunar New Year. Some people on the island point out that the Taiwan side will agree to reduce the tariff on U.S.-made passenger cars and automobile parts to “zero tariff” from the effective date of the agreement, that the tariff on health supplements will also be reduced…","The DPP authorities are attempting to “seek independence by relying on foreign powers,” and in the Taiwan-US trade negotiations they have unprincipledly courted the US and sold out Taiwan without any bottom line. If the relevant reports are true, Taiwan's traditional industries will be seriously impacted, and the food safety of the public will also be left without guarantee. The DPP authorities are letting the US demand whatever it wants, sacrificing the prospects of Taiwan's industrial development and harming the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people. They will surely be repudiated by Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Recently, the controversy over whether Li Zhen-xiu, a Mainland spouse and at-large legislator of the Taiwan People's Party, will renounce Chinese nationality has drawn wide attention. The Mainland Affairs Council stated that the mainland side has made clear it will not allow Li Zhen-xiu to renounce Chinese nationality, which amounts to depriving Li of the right to serve as a legislator in Taiwan, and that the…","There is only one China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. There is simply no so-called issue of “renouncing nationality.” The DPP authorities stubbornly cling to their “Taiwan independence” stance and blatantly peddle the “two-state theory,” deliberately provoking the historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and unscrupulously suppressing mainland spouses in Taiwan. We firmly oppose this. For “Taiwan independence” thugs and accomplices who persecute mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable under the law for life and punish them severely without leniency.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Affected by interference from the DPP authorities, cross-Strait flight routes have not yet fully returned to normal, which seriously affects exchanges between people on both sides. Compatriots on both sides strongly hope that all cross-Strait direct flight routes will fully resume, but the MAC has said, “Without group tour sources, airlines fly one flight and lose money on the next, so the incentive is not…","Cross-Strait direct air routes have greatly facilitated travel between the two sides and have played an important role in enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. At present, cross-Strait routes are being interfered with by the DPP authorities, and the destinations have not yet fully returned to normal. The mainland's 14 cities operate more than 300 cross-Strait passenger flights per week, which still falls far short of the situation before 2020, when the mainland had 61 destinations and up to 890 passenger flights per week. This seriously affects travel between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and there is a very strong call from people on both sides of the Strait for the full resumption of cross-Strait direct flight destinations.\nThe mainland has always upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and actively promoted cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and the goodwill and sincerity it has shown are plain for all to see. In 2023 we announced the resumption of receiving group tours from Taiwan residents to the mainland; in 2024 we resumed Fujian residents' travel to Kinmen and Matsu; in 2025 we announced the resumption of group tours to Taiwan for residents of Fujian and Shanghai; and in early 2026 we again announced that we would resume travel to Kinmen and Matsu for Shanghai residents. Yet the DPP authorities not only have not responded positively, but have repeatedly obstructed, restricted and erected barriers to cross-Strait tourism and exchanges in all fields. The crux and obstacle of the current cross-Strait tourism problem lies entirely in the interference and obstruction by the DPP authorities.\nWhether there are passengers for cross-Strait routes, the data speak for themselves. According to statistics, in 2025 more than 5.78 million passenger trips were made between the two sides by air passenger direct flights, and the average load factor of cross-Strait routes reached 80%, fully reflecting the strong demand for cross-Strait direct flights. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion and lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport as soon as possible, and allow cross-Strait airlines to arrange flight plans independently according to market demand. Whether there is demand for flights should be decided by the market, and the DPP authorities can lift the restrictions and find out for themselves.\nReporter from the People's Political Consultative Conference Daily: On February 10, the results of the 2025 “Three Rural Issues” Figures Recommendation Activity were officially announced. Taiwan compatriot Guo Yangfu was selected as a 2025 “Three Rural Issues” figure. What is your comment on this?\nAccording to information, the 2025 “Three Rural Issues” Figures Recommendation Activity took “Looking Ahead to the 15th Five-Year Plan, Striving Forward on a New Journey” as its theme, and recommended 12 annual “Three Rural Issues” figures and 1 tribute team. Taiwan compatriot Guo Yangfu, who has started and developed a business in Ezhou, Hubei, was recommended and selected. He became the third Taiwan compatriot to receive this honor in the 20 years since the activity was held. This is another concrete measure to implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriot farmers and Taiwan farmers and deepen cross-Strait integrated development. We will further implement and refine policies and measures that benefit Taiwan farmers and Taiwan enterprises, create better conditions for Taiwan farmers and Taiwan enterprises to develop on the mainland, and look forward to more Taiwan compatriots actively participating in the high-quality development of the mainland, writing new stories of compatriots on both sides of the Strait joining hands to realize the Chinese Dream.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750861.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750864.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","The Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that it will resume tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for Shanghai residents in the near future. The Mainland Affairs Council responded: “A proposal raised on a special political occasion is obviously a political manipulation; restricting residents of specific provinces and cities from sightseeing in Kinmen and Matsu is unreasonable, and we will not regard this round of…","Adhering to the concept of “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family,” we will actively promote and fully facilitate any measure that is conducive to advancing cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots. The Ministry of Culture and Tourism recently announced that it will resume tourism by residents of Shanghai to Kinmen and Matsu. This is a concrete measure to normalize cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation and expand cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. This measure conforms to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan that seeks peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and it has been welcomed by Taiwan's industry and the public. The tourism industry and public in Kinmen and Matsu are especially eager for it.\nThe remarks made by the Mainland Affairs Council are entirely indifferent to the well-being of Taiwan's people and do not benefit cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation. We hope they will stop political manipulation, genuinely respond to the public's expectations, and take concrete action to lift the various bans and restrictions that affect cross-Strait exchanges and interactions.\nReporter from Henan Radio and Television “Daxiang News”\n: Recently, Taiwan's coast guard authorities claimed that they will carry out so-called “security maintenance work” during the Spring Festival, mobilizing various types of vessels and boats to pre-position to respond to gray-zone harassment from the mainland. What is your comment on this?\nThe Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. If the DPP authorities dare to provoke trouble during this festive season, they must bear all the consequences arising from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently said, “the US-China-Taiwan trilateral relationship maintains four constants,” and KMT Vice Chairman Hsiao Hsu-tsen said that the international landscape has already changed, that Lai still clings to the “new two-state theory,” “wants to fight a war with the mainland,” and that his strategy is completely wrong. What comment do you have?","Lai Ching-te's remarks fully expose his sinister intention to “seek independence by relying on the United States” and “rely on external forces to seek independence,” as well as the “Taiwan independence” nature of a “disruptor of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and a “manufacturer of Taiwan Strait crises.” All of Taiwan's history, facts, and law prove that Taiwan is Chinese territory and an inseparable part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no foreign interference is permitted. No matter how the Lai Ching-te authorities shamelessly and without bottom line curry favor with the United States and devise schemes to fabricate the US “support for Taiwan” lie, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle. We have firm will, strong determination, and great capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260211_12750862.htm"],[2,"2026-02-11","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Jimmy Lai, founder of “Next Media,” was recently sentenced to 20 years in prison. The Mainland side has released a white paper titled “The Practice of Safeguarding National Security in Hong Kong under ‘One Country, Two Systems’,” stating that this case is a judgment that safeguards national security. It also released figures showing that as of January, 98 people had been prosecuted under the Hong…","First question. We firmly support the Hong Kong SAR in fulfilling its constitutional responsibility to safeguard national security, and we have handed down a just sentence for Jimmy Lai, the principal culprit of anti-China, Hong Kong-destabilizing elements, for crimes including conspiring and colluding with external forces to endanger national security.\nJimmy Lai is the \"mastermind\" of the anti-China, Hong Kong-destabilizing gang; the evidence is ironclad and his crimes are grave. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities ignored the conclusive evidence in the Jimmy Lai case and openly championed him under the pretext of so-called \"democracy and freedom,\" attacked and smeared \"one country, two systems,\" once again exposing their nature of attempting to destabilize Hong Kong, pursue \"independence,\" and seek political gain. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to immediately stop political manipulation, or they will surely be severely punished.\nSecond question. An important aspect of the 2026 Taiwan Work Conference is to uphold the concept of \"Cross-Strait Family Affinity,\" facilitate and ease personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, expand civil and grassroots exchanges between the two sides, support Taiwan residents, especially young people, in coming to the mainland to study, work and live, and promote the two sides jointly promoting Chinese culture and fostering emotional connection between compatriots on both sides.\nHere we announce two fan interaction activities for the new media accounts of the Taiwan Affairs Office.\nIn the past year, the new media accounts of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have received extensive attention and support from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We sincerely thank you, and we hope to further shorten the distance between us through these two fan interaction activities.\nThe first is the fan feedback activity for the WeChat official account \"Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.\" From June 2025 to January 2026, we held 8 sessions of Taiwan-related knowledge quizzes on the WeChat official account \"Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council,\" with a total of nearly 140,000 readings and nearly 8,000 fans enthusiastically participating in answering. For each session, the top 10 fans who answered correctly and ranked highest in likes, totaling 80 fans, received carefully prepared carved-shell souvenirs. To thank the fans for their active participation, we have specially invited 2 representatives from the award-winning fans of the 8 sessions to attend the press conference on site and observe it, and we will give them a special cultural and creative souvenir. The Taiwan-related knowledge quiz activity consists of 12 sessions in total. We welcome friends on both sides of the Strait to follow and participate in the 9th to 12th sessions of the Taiwan-related knowledge quizzes.\nThe second is the call for entries for the Lunar New Year video and photo collection under the Facebook account of the \"Spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council,\" titled \"Year of the Horse Spring Festival Outings, Surprises in Sharing the Festive Spirit.\" From February 11 to March 2, fans on both sides of the Strait can use videos or photos to record memorable moments related to the Spring Festival and send them to a designated email address or to the Facebook account backend. We will select 20 outstanding works and give exquisite souvenirs. We warmly welcome fans on both sides of the Strait to participate actively.\nToday is Southern Little New Year, and in five days we will welcome the Lunar Year of the Horse Spring Festival. We take this opportunity to wish compatriots on both sides of the Strait a Happy New Year in advance and wish everyone good fortune in the New Year. (In Southern Min dialect) We wish our fellow Taiwanese good luck and success, may all things go smoothly on the horse's journey. (In Hakka) We wish everyone a flying start to the new year, and may good luck gallop in with ten thousand horses. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to celebrate the Spring Festival with relatives and friends, reunite with family, and welcome the new spring, with flowers blooming all the way from mountains to sea.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202602/t20260211_12750872.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-02-12","Lin Jian","AFP","Lai Ching-te said in an interview that if Taiwan were “annexed” by China, “the next countries under threat would be Japan, the Philippines, and others in the Indo-Pacific region.” What is China’s response?","Lai Ching-te’s remarks once again reveal his nature as a diehard separatist for “Taiwan independence.” He has fully proven himself to be the saboteur of peace, maker of crises and instigator of war. “Taiwan independence” is the root of all threats to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Whatever Lai Ching-te says or does, it does not change the fact backed by history and law that Taiwan belongs to China, or the world’s abiding commitment to the one-China principle, and still less the inevitability of China’s reunification. Seeking independence by soliciting foreign support and resisting reunification through military buildup are just futile and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202602/t20260212_11857764.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202602/t20260212_11857627.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-02-12","Lin Jian","AFP","Lai Ching-te said that he “would like Taiwan and Europe to enhance cooperation in the defense industry and on defense technology.” What is your response?","I have made it very clear that seeking independence by soliciting foreign support and resisting reunification through military buildup are just futile and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202602/t20260212_11857764.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202602/t20260212_11857627.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-02-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Today, Hong Kong media exposed that relatives of Liu Shih-fang, head of the department in charge of internal affairs in Taiwan, invested for profit on the mainland and provided political donations to Liu, revealing that Liu allowed only his relatives to “make red money” while not allowing the public to engage in exchanges. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying that we have noted the relevant reports and are investigating and handling the relevant matters in accordance with law and regulations. We will absolutely not allow die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and their relatives to invest, do business, or profit on the mainland, and we will absolutely not allow those who support “Taiwan independence” and undermine cross-Strait relations to earn money on the mainland while doing things that bite the hand that feeds them.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and pursuing “Taiwan independence” harms oneself and others. Die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements are base in character and profit-driven, which is despicable. “Taiwan independence” elements and the enterprises and individuals who provide them support, which undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and harm the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, will certainly be severely punished. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will see through the hypocritical face and ugly nature of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, consciously draw a clear line with them, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, and jointly maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202602/t20260227_12752858.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-02-28","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","As was reported, Lai Ching-te recently made noises about accelerating the buildup of asymmetric capabilities, and pushed hard for advancing arms purchases from the US and the approval of related budgets, so as to \"ensure security of the island and maintain peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific\". What's your comment on this？","Lai Ching-te and his ilk, driven by partisan and personal interests, have recklessly squandered public funds to purchase US-made weapons. This will only drain Taiwan's coffers faster, push Taiwan closer to the peril of war, and drag the people in Taiwan down into an abyss. We sternly warn the DPP authorities that seeking independence by soliciting foreign support is doomed to fail, and resisting reunification by force is a dead end. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will see through the very dangerous and destructive nature of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, stand with us to resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" schemes and foreign interference, and take concrete actions to safeguard their own safety and well-being, as well as peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/02/china-260228-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16445043.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-03-03","Mao Ning","Reuters","Some analysts suggested that China may take bolder action to stake its territorial claims, including in Taiwan, while the U.S. is distracted in the Middle East conflict. Do you have any comment on this assertion? And also, some analysts said that U.S. actions in Venezuela and Iran may hinder oil supplies to China and weaken their diplomatic allies. Do you have any comment on this assertion as well?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese ourselves.\nOn your second question, China firmly opposes violating any country’s sovereignty and security with the use of force in international relations. Energy security is of vital importance to the world economy. Ensuring stable and unfettered energy supply is a responsibility for all. China will do what is necessary to safeguard its energy security.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260303_11867987.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260303_11867941.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 4, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","The National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference are about to convene. We have noted that more and more Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, have expressed concern. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","The people's congress system is China's fundamental political system, and the system of multi-party cooperation and political consultation led by the Communist Party of China is China's basic political system. The National People's Congress and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference are important platforms that intensively reflect and thoroughly practice whole-process people's democracy. The Fourth Session of the 14th CPPCC National Committee, which opens today, and the Fourth Session of the 14th National People's Congress, which opens tomorrow, are important meetings held in the first year of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period. They include agendas such as discussing and deliberating the government work report and the outline of the \"15th Five-Year Plan,\" will outline the country's development blueprint for the next five years, and reveal the logic and direction of the country's future development.\nBy following and understanding the two sessions, compatriots in Taiwan can better understand the mainland's democratic political system and the country's economic and social development, experience the whole-process people's democracy and the achievements of Chinese-style modernization on the mainland, understand the country's future development direction, and grasp their own development opportunities within it. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan, including the broad Taiwan youth, will actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, and jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and create a bright future of national rejuvenation and reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753742.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","During the Spring Festival holiday, the cross-Strait 'Mini Three Links' passenger routes have seen a surge of cross-Strait compatriots returning home to visit relatives and travel. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During the Spring Festival, the cross-strait “mini three links” routes continued to operate smoothly, facilitating cross-strait residents, especially Taiwan compatriots, in visiting relatives and friends, celebrating the festival, and sightseeing. Statistics show that the four “mini three links” passenger routes—Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Lianjiang Huangqi to Matsu—deployed 15 vessels providing 9,413 passenger seats, with 126 round-trip sailings per week, totaling 252 trips.\nFrom February 2 to February 26, the “mini three links” routes operated more than 850 sailings, up 4.66% year on year, carrying 152,400 passenger trips, up 27.61% year on year. Passenger flow on the Xiamen–Kinmen and Fuzhou–Matsu routes both reached new highs since resumption. During the Spring Festival, the “mini three links” ports provided one-stop travel services to fully ensure that passengers could travel efficiently and conveniently. The passenger terminals held activities such as on-site calligraphy blessings by calligraphers and created a distinctive “Blessings Fill the Port” scene, allowing cross-strait passengers to feel the festive and harmonious atmosphere of the New Year while waiting to board.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Around the Spring Festival, departments and localities across the mainland showed care and concern for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait spent the holiday together and welcomed the new spring together. Taiwan compatriots expressed that they felt the warmth of home. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On the occasion of the Spring Festival, Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, visited Fuzhou in Fujian to extend greetings and condolences to Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots. He attended a Spring Festival symposium for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots and a friendship event titled “Seeking Development, Promoting Integration: Compatriots on Both Sides of the Strait Celebrate the Spring Festival of the Bingwu Year Together.” Some staff from the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises, presidents of local Taiwan business associations, representatives of Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan compatriots, and Taiwan youth, important figures from the business community on the island, and more than 220 compatriots from Matsu and Kinmen attended. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait crossed the Strait and gathered together, using shared cultural roots as a bond and shared ties of home as a bridge, to come together for this warm reunion.\nGovernments at all levels on the mainland and Taiwan Affairs Offices in various localities have visited Taiwan-funded enterprises in their jurisdictions and extended greetings and condolences to Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots, expressing concern and care, widely soliciting opinions, and helping Taiwan businesses and enterprises resolve practical problems. At the same time, various localities have also held rich and colorful friendship and Spring Festival activities for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides celebrated the Spring Festival together in a spirit of reunion and joy, and Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots felt the warm bond of one family across the Strait and jointly looked forward to a reunited family and nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te repeatedly mentioned mainland China while attending the “Mainland Taiwan Businesspeople Spring Festival Event,” which drew attention. Lai said he hopes cross-Strait exchange and cooperation can move in a direction of peaceful coexistence. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately uphold a separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and deliberately provoke confrontation in pursuit of “independence.” This is the root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. We have said many times that both sides of the Strait are Chinese and are one family. As long as the DPP authorities recognize the “1992 Consensus” and stop “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, cross-Strait dialogue and consultation can resume, and peaceful development of cross-Strait relations can be achieved. Peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is conducive to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, promoting harmony and tranquility in Taiwan society, and ensuring that Taiwan compatriots can live and work in peace and contentment. It is the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times. Following the trend and following the will of the people is the wise choice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Recently, the United States and Israel launched military operations against Iran. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and relevant Chinese embassies and consulates issued notices reminding Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots, to evacuate as soon as possible, and Taiwan compatriots who need to evacuate may register. The DPP authorities, however, falsely claimed that it is “risky” for Taiwan compatriots to…","Taiwan compatriots are citizens of China and are our own flesh and blood. From the evacuation of citizens from Libya, Yemen and Sudan, to the outbreak of the Israel-Palestine conflict and the dangers faced by Taiwan compatriots overseas from typhoons, earthquakes and other hazards, we have maintained close contact with Taiwan compatriots in the relevant locations and promptly provided assistance. We will, as always, take all necessary measures to protect the safety of Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots. When Taiwan compatriots need assistance, they may contact the Chinese embassy or consulate in the local area at any time, or call the 12308 consular protection hotline. Wherever they are and whatever difficulties they encounter, the great motherland is the staunch backing of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.\nAt a critical moment concerning the safety of Taiwan compatriots, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities still engage in political manipulation, losing their conscience and extinguishing their humanity. What they fear most is seeing “both sides of the Strait are one family, and true feelings are revealed in times of adversity.” They strive to place political schemes above the safety of the people's lives. Their coldheartedness and selfishness are fully exposed, and they will inevitably meet firm opposition from the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753741.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","In response to the mainland side’s disclosure that Liu Shih-fang’s relatives hold positions at mainland enterprises and its announcement that it will investigate and handle the matter in accordance with law and regulations, Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council on the 28th issued its first “2026 China Mainland Economic Risk Warning.” It reminds Taiwan businesspeople who go to the mainland to invest, operate…","Media reports have drawn wide attention from all sectors on the island. The key issue now is that the DPP authorities must directly answer whether Liu Shih-fang's relatives are profiting in the mainland, and whether the Green camp is engaging in double standards by, on the one hand, suppressing and persecuting people who take part in cross-Strait exchanges, while on the other hand using relatives to “earn red money” in the mainland. They should not shift the focus or talk around the issue.\nOur punitive measures apply only to a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their affiliated enterprises and backers, and do not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan business people, or Taiwan-funded enterprises. The DPP authorities are deliberately confusing the public, fabricating so-called “risks” with the aim of intimidating the people of Taiwan, creating a “chilling effect,” and obstructing and sabotaging cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Their “Taiwan independence” provocations have led to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait, their persecution of people engaged in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation is full of crimes, and their push for cross-Strait “decoupling and severing of supply chains” is riddled with misdeeds. It is the DPP authorities themselves who should “rein in before the cliff.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753740.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, the British Financial Times published a report titled “Bring Mainland Chinese Tourists Back to Taiwan,” stating that the mainland has made a political gesture on cross-Strait tourism and launched the reopening measures without obtaining substantive concessions from Taiwan. It said Taiwan should show greater flexibility and handle tourism separately from politics. The article has resonated with the…","We have actively promoted cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and the goodwill and sincerity we have shown are plain to see. We will actively promote and fully facilitate any measures that are beneficial to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots.\nWe hope that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will comply with the wishes of the people, take the well-being of the Taiwan public seriously, and take concrete actions to lift all kinds of restrictions on cross-Strait exchanges, including tourism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753738.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, the US Supreme Court ruled that the reciprocal tariffs implemented by President Trump in 2025 are invalid. Analysts on the island believe this ruling completely overturns the legal basis of the Taiwan-US tariff agreement. The concessions the Lai Ching-te authorities previously made to accommodate the US, together with their exorbitant purchase commitments and the 500 billion US dollar investment pledge,…","The United States, using tariffs as a big stick for extreme pressure, has hollowed out and stripped Taiwan's industries, and this economic bullying is unpopular. The DPP authorities, disregarding the well-being of the Taiwan people, have groveled to the US without bottom lines and sold out Taiwan. They have promised huge purchases, substantially opened markets, and cooperated in transferring core industries on the island. The result is that they spent a fortune on a “worthless ticket.” Facts have once again proven that the DPP authorities, in order to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” willingly act as pawns and will only bring the consequences upon themselves and become a laughingstock.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753739.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中新社记者","During the Spring Festival, the Zhejiang Xiaobaihua Yue Opera Theatre, the Shanxi Iron Flower (“打铁花”) troupe, and others traveled to Taiwan to perform, and were warmly welcomed and highly praised by the people of the island. Some people on the island have pointed out that they hope the two sides can always exchange through art and culture and never through the flames of war, that the two sides must be peaceful,…","During the Spring Festival, the Zhejiang Xiaobaihua Yue Opera Theatre took its two plays, \"My Grand View Garden\" and \"The Garden of Love,\" to Taiwan for performances, and the Shanxi Gaoping intangible cultural heritage project of \"striking iron flowers\" (dǎ tiě huā) also performed in Taiwan. They were well received and praised by audiences on the island, especially young audiences, demonstrating the unique charm and strong appeal of outstanding traditional Chinese culture. The love and identification of Taiwan compatriots with Chinese culture once again confirm that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots, the same culture, and the same ethnicity. The appeals from relevant people on the island also voice the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation.\nChinese culture is the root and the spiritual home of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We are willing to work with Taiwan compatriots to continuously advance cross-Strait cultural exchanges and cooperation, jointly safeguard the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and join hands to let Chinese culture shine even more brilliantly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753736.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","光明日报记者","The historical drama “The Years of Peace” was recently broadcast on both sides of the Strait and has sparked heated discussion. Public opinion holds that it uses a long-buried piece of history to awaken people's cherishing of peace and their recognition of the historical trend toward reunification. What is your comment on this?","The TV drama 《太平年》 takes the “Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms” period as its historical backdrop and explores the grand question of “how peace is achieved.” It shows that Chinese civilization has outstanding unity, and it expresses the Chinese nation’s spiritual conviction of opposing division and pursuing unification, as well as its sense of national feeling embodied in the saying “those who benefit the realm must strive for it.”\nHistory is the best textbook and the best sobering agent. The attention and discussion by audiences on both sides of the Strait regarding the plot of 《太平年》 and the history behind it fully reflect that peace is a common pursuit of compatriots on both sides. We sincerely hope that all Taiwan compatriots will cherish peace as they cherish their own eyes, pursue unification as they pursue life’s happiness, firmly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and actively take part in advancing the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260304_12753737.htm"],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the United States and Taiwan signed the so-called \"reciprocal trade agreement.\" The US will reduce the \"reciprocal tariff\" on Taiwan from 20% to 15%. Taiwan has committed to implementing zero tariffs or lowering tariffs on most industrial and agricultural products imported from the US, and to increasing purchases from the US by 84.8 billion US dollars. Island media believe that the so-called \"reciprocal…","The so-called “agreement” is in fact a bullying and suppression of Taiwan by the United States, and even more a contract of selling out Taiwan in which the DPP authorities seek to bind themselves to the United States and be manipulated by it across the economy, industry, security, and the so-called defense sectors. It harbors all kinds of malicious intent, including pushing for “decoupling and severing supply chains” across the Taiwan Strait and attempting to “rely on outsiders to seek independence” and “seek independence by force.”\nThe DPP authorities, not hesitating to drain Taiwan’s assets, serve as the vanguard for external forces’ “using Taiwan to contain China,” turning Taiwan into a dumping ground for American products. In the end they receive only “empty-handed in both people and money” yet remain complacent. This unprincipled act of selling out Taiwan and unconditional capitulation runs counter to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and harms the vital interests of Taiwan’s enterprises and people. It will inevitably be met with retribution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Various places on the mainland have held rich and colorful activities for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to celebrate the Spring Festival together. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During the Spring Festival, various places on the mainland held a rich variety of welcoming-the-new-year activities, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait celebrated the Lunar New Year together.\nFujian Province organized a series of Min-Taiwan cultural exchange activities. Fuzhou City held the 2026 Spring Festival New Year Reception and conducted a series of in-depth visits and condolence activities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. Quanzhou City held the 2026 “Fellow Villagers Love Each Other as One Family” Spring Festival gathering for Taiwan compatriots, and the Quanzhou Tianhou Temple held the 20th Quan-Penghu “Qigui” (Turtle-Begging) folk cultural activity. On Meizhou Island in Putian City, a Mazu golden statue blessing and inspection tour was held, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait gathered in Mazu’s hometown to enjoy folk customs and celebrate the festival together. Liancheng County in Longyan will hold the 2026 Min-Taiwan martial arts exchange activities, including a cross-Strait martial arts and lion dance performance, and a parade of intangible cultural heritage folk customs.\nIn Suzhou, Jiangsu, cross-Strait families who are spending the New Year in Suzhou collectively “returned to their mother’s home.” Nearly a hundred members of cross-Strait marriage families shared cross-Strait specialties such as sesame oil chicken soup and oyster omelet, and shared stories about Spring Festival customs. The Hebei Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office held a Spring Festival reception for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, with more than 110 representatives of Taiwanese businesspeople and compatriots from Beijing, Tianjin, Shandong, and various parts of Hebei gathering together to share their experiences and achievements in participating in the coordinated development of the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei region, and to talk about family ties and develop common interests together.\nExcellent cultural programs from various places were invited to perform on the island, providing a colorful cultural feast for the island’s residents. The Zhejiang Xiaobaihua Yueju Opera Troupe held five cultural exchange performances in Taoyuan and Taipei, and every show was sold out, with Taiwanese opera fans immersing themselves in the gentle Yue-style singing and experiencing the excellent traditional Chinese opera culture. The documentary “Cross-Strait Faith Customs—Anxi City God Festival,” produced by relevant units in Fujian Province, was broadcast on the island. Using the thousand-year-old faith customs as a bond, it looks back at the migration history of the early Min-Taiwan settlers and shows the vivid practice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait jointly revering the City God and protecting the cultural heritage.\nIn addition, on the first day of the Lunar New Year, Xiamen TV recorded the “‘Joyful Xiamen’ 2026 Cross-Strait Children’s Spring Festival Happy Gathering,” which was broadcast simultaneously on both sides of the Strait. On the Lantern Festival, Xiamen TV launched the “‘Happiness Is Enough’ 2026 Cross-Strait Lantern Festival Poetry and Music Gathering,” providing a cultural feast under the theme “The same moon shines over the four seas, and we share the reunion together.” The Fujian Broadcasting and Film Group conducted the “2026 Cross-Strait Radio Spring Festival Grand Broadcast,” themed “Horses Trample the Spring Breeze, Fortune Fills Both Sides of the Strait,” which was disseminated through 52 radio stations on the mainland, 48 in Taiwan, and new media matrices.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding the matter of relatives of “Taiwan independence” die-hard Liu Shih-fang investing in the mainland for profit and providing political donations, what is the current progress of the investigation? What specific punitive measures will be taken going forward? Will the restrictive measures against “Taiwan independence” die-hards, their affiliated enterprises, and their financial backers be further expanded…","Against diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and the enterprises and individuals who support them, we will act on the basis of facts and in accordance with the law, and take all necessary measures to strike hard. We will never allow those who support “Taiwan independence” and undermine cross-Strait relations to make money on the Mainland while biting the hand that feeds them.\nOur punitive measures target only a very small number of diehard “Taiwan independence” elements and their affiliated enterprises and backers, and do not involve the broad Taiwan compatriots. We will, as always, actively promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, do more real and good things for Taiwan compatriots, and continuously enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Taiwanese pan-green media personality Fan Qifei, in a video, described her positive impressions of traveling on the mainland, saying that the mainland had been demonized too severely in Taiwan in the past, and she was attacked by \"Blue Birds.\" What comments do you have on this?","We actively support mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, including media professionals, to come to the mainland to see the real situation with their own eyes and personally experience the mainland's development and progress and the friendship among compatriots. The green-camp media and the cyber army on the island's habitual tactic of “demonizing” the mainland is increasingly unable to deceive anyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","Recently, US President Trump said in an interview that Taiwan “stole our chip business, they need our protection, but they haven't paid,” which has drawn attention on the island. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities stubbornly “rely on the US to seek independence,” repeatedly catering to and currying favor with the US. They are willing to sacrifice the long-term interests of Taiwan’s people and destroy Taiwan’s economic development prospects. In the end, they will inevitably become “fish and meat” to be carved up at will and “ATMs” to be drained at will.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that cross-Strait relations this Spring Festival could be regarded as having \"ended satisfactorily,\" and \"Taiwan's goodwill has always been there, and we hope the mainland can release more goodwill and maintain mutual respect.\" What comments do you have on this?","The Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, so they should celebrate the Lunar New Year together with joy, jointly wishing for a prosperous new spring and family reunion for the nation and for every household.\nWe consistently uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” do practical things, good things, and help resolve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots, full of goodwill and sincerity. But we will absolutely not tolerate, and will never tolerate, any “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct. We will continue to resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and oppose interference by external forces. On the basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and the shared political foundation of opposing “Taiwan independence,” we will, together with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, said at the mainland Taiwan business Spring Festival event that Taiwanese businesses currently investing and operating in mainland China face internal economic risks in the mainland, external risks such as the US trade war, and cross-Strait political risks. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities have consistently slandered the mainland's economic development prospects and smeared its business environment, yet the facts have repeatedly exposed their lies.\nIn 2025, the mainland successfully achieved its main targets for economic and social development. The economy forged ahead under pressure and developed toward new and better directions, demonstrating strong resilience and vitality. Gross domestic product (GDP) reached a new level of over 140 trillion yuan for the first time, and its growth rate continued to rank among the highest of the world's major economies. Scientific and technological innovation produced fruitful results, the construction of a modern industrial system continued to advance, and new quality productive forces developed steadily.\nReform and opening up took new steps, livelihood security became more robust, and social stability was maintained. These conditions provide an excellent environment and broad space for innovative development by all types of business entities, including Taiwan enterprises. The great achievements, good current situation, and development trends of cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation have already proven, and will continue to powerfully prove, that the mainland was, is, and will remain the best choice for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople to invest and start businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","This year’s Taipei Lantern Festival: as in previous years, Shanghai sent a delegation to participate, but at a lower level. The Mainland Affairs Council said in response that it did not receive applications from the director and deputy director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office, and stated that it does not accept entry permits for the “top leaders” of Taiwan-related systems to come to Taiwan unless they are…","We have consistently supported exchanges and cooperation in all fields, including city-to-city exchanges across the two sides, and hope that through more visits and exchanges we can continuously enhance mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides and promote emotional connection. The DPP authorities, out of political self-interest in seeking “independence,” have repeatedly added their own “scripts” and set unreasonable conditions to obstruct mainland personnel from traveling to Taiwan, interfering with and undermining normal cross-Strait exchanges. Their conduct runs counter to mainstream public opinion on the island and has met with opposition from the public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","Recently, Hong Kong media exposed that relatives of Liu Shih-fang, head of the Taiwan authority in charge of internal affairs, invested for profit on the mainland and made political donations to Liu. The mainland side said it will handle the relevant issues in accordance with law and regulations. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council responded that the mainland, by using Hong Kong media to spread vicious messages…","“Taiwan independence” is illegal and criminal activity that splits the country and stirs up trouble in the Taiwan Strait. Punishing die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements in accordance with the law is a just and necessary measure to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nNo matter how the DPP authorities argue, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. They also cannot conceal the hypocritical double standard of the “Taiwan independence” forces, who on one hand promote separatist “Taiwan independence” fallacies and wantonly undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, harming the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and on the other hand profit from relatives investing and doing business on the mainland and accept benefits from them.\nOur punishment of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements, their affiliated enterprises and their bankrollers is reasonable and lawful, and the reaction of public opinion on both sides of the Strait has been very gratifying.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, the United States and Israel launched military strikes against Iran. Some public opinion on the island worries that the mainland will follow the US approach and take action against Taiwan. Some commentary also says that the US use of force worldwide will make the mainland more cautious about using force against Taiwan. What comment do you have?","Taiwan is China's territory. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and when and how it is resolved is entirely a matter for the Chinese people themselves. It is a just cause to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and brooks no foreign interference. If “Taiwan independence” separatist forces dare to take risks and cross the red line, we will certainly take resolute measures and deal them a head-on blow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","北京广播电视台记者","Recently, the Straits Exchange Foundation held a “Mainland Taiwanese Businesses Spring Festival Event.” In his remarks, SEF Chairman Su Chia-chuan said that the SEF will continue to promote healthy and orderly cross-Strait exchanges on the principles of equality and dignity. As long as it benefits the well-being of the people, we are willing to extend an olive branch to improve cross-Strait relations. What is…","We have always actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and enhanced the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. At present, the obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation lie entirely in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities. Only by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the One China principle, can the two associations resume their dialogue and consultation mechanism, and only then can cross-Strait relations return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-04","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Before the Spring Festival, the Mainland announced it would open tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for Shanghai residents. Is there currently any specific progress or plan for the opening?","On February 4, the Ministry of Culture and Tourism announced that tourism by residents of Shanghai to Kinmen and Matsu will resume in the near future. These measures respond to the eager expectations of compatriots on both sides for strengthened exchanges and cooperation. The relevant measures are being implemented, and any new progress will be announced to the public.\nI now announce the situation regarding the ninth quiz on Taiwan-related knowledge.\nOn February 9, the WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” released the questions for the ninth “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz” activity, and netizens enthusiastically participated in answering them. As of March 2, the netizens who answered correctly and ranked in the top ten by likes on their comments were, in order: “徐立讯”, “Monk猴”, “张根晟”, “山河映”, “Lu”, “浪漫夏日”, “湖畔”, “狗尾草”, “黄雅妮”, and “大包包”. We extend our congratulations to these ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite commemorative shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope that netizens will continue to care about the work concerning Taiwan, actively take part, and promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe WeChat official account of the “State Council Taiwan Affairs Office” will soon release the questions for the tenth “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz.” Everyone is welcome to enthusiastically take part in answering!\nThat concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260304_12753743.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-03-09","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Over the weekend, the “premier” of Taiwan Mr. Cho visited Japan to watch a baseball game. I think he saw the Taiwanese beat the Czech Republic. When he was asked about the visit, he said he made a “personal visit” and it was nothing official about his visit to Tokyo. Do you accept his explanation that this was a personal visit? Do you have any further comment about his trip to Japan?","With unspeakable motives, Cho Jung-tai sneaked into Japan to carry out provocation for “Taiwan independence.” This is a rather despicable move.\nChina remains highly vigilant and firmly opposed to the Japanese side trying to create gray areas or push the envelope on the Taiwan question. The Japanese side will pay the price for emboldening the provocations and acting recklessly and shall bear all responsibility for the consequences of such action. China will continue to firmly push back separatism for “Taiwan independence,” oppose external interference, and defend national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260309_11871584.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260309_11871477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-09","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Taiwan has said that the number of PRC military aircraft around the island has fallen significantly over the last 10 days. I wonder if you could tell us what the reason is for this reduction in military aircraft flights near Taiwan?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260309_11871584.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260309_11871477.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-03-09","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: recently, Cho Jung-tai, head of Taiwan’s administrative authority, used a so-called “private schedule” as a pretext to make an unofficial visit to Japan to watch a ball game. What is your comment?","Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded to questions by saying: The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly hold to a separatist “Taiwan independence” stance and, by any means necessary, “seek independence by relying on external powers,” making them unmistakable “destroyers of cross-Strait peace” and “creators of Taiwan Strait crises.” Leading figures of the DPP authorities, under the name of so-called “private itineraries,” are in fact carrying out provocations aimed at independence, and their petty sneaking and thievery is contemptible. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the malicious intent and harm of the DPP authorities' independence-seeking schemes, and join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and external interference, earnestly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and resolutely guard the common homeland of the Chinese nation.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no external interference. Japan's tolerance of visits by leading figures of the DPP authorities violates the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, and sends a seriously wrong signal to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. We firmly oppose this. Japan should deeply reflect on history, draw lessons from history, earnestly reflect on and correct its mistakes, and stop manipulating and provoking on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260309_12754744.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-03-10","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Taiwan is considering selling debt for the first time to finance overseas investments in its foreign partner countries. This is part of the democracy’s efforts to resist the diplomatic isolation imposed by China. Would the Foreign Ministry like to comment?","The DPP authorities often use trade and investment as a front for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities abroad to expand so-called “international space.” Such malignant schemes will not succeed. The despicable tactics of the DPP authorities will never change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, evidenced by both history and law. Nor will it ever undermine international commitment to the one-China principle or stop the complete reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260310_11872314.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260310_11872097.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-03-10","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: The Government Work Report proposes resolutely combating “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, opposing interference by external forces, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great cause of national reunification. What comments does the spokesperson have?","Zhang Xiaogang: Unification is the right path and the trend of history; “Taiwan independence” is a counter-current and a dead end. The DPP authorities are attempting to “seek independence by relying on outsiders” and “seek independence by force,” pushing Taiwan step by step into a perilous situation of war and danger. They have become the greatest disruptor of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the root of trouble for peace and stability in the Strait. What the people of Taiwan most hope for is to live peaceful days and enjoy tranquil years, not to be tied to the chariot of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces as cannon fodder. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should join hands to oppose “Taiwan independence” and oppose interference by external forces, and together create a bright future of national reunification and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.\nWe are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. This is aimed at an extremely small number of “Taiwan independence” separatists and their separatist activities, as well as interference by external forces, with the purpose of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The People's Liberation Army will solidly advance military training and combat readiness, comprehensively enhance its ability to win wars, and resolutely crush the schemes of “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, resolutely safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait region.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/ztjzh/16447761.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-03-11","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the 2026 Goodwill Cruising and Training Squadron of Taiwan's naval force has set sail to visit its so-called diplomatic allies in Central and South America for a \"large-scale goodwill mission\". Do you have any comment on this?","The so-called goodwill mission is merely an excuse for the DPP authorities to solicit foreign support for \"Taiwan independence\". The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. It is the political foundation for China's relations with all the 183 countries who have diplomatic ties with China. We hope that countries in the relevant region can follow the historical trend of the times and make, at an early date, the right decision that serves the fundamental and long-term interests of their peoples. We warn the DPP authorities that no form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities or political manipulation can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, or alter the international community's support for the one-China principle. Such attempts are futile.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/03/china-260311-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16447956.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-03-13","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","We see a report that says a major U.S. arms package for Taiwan is ready for President Trump to approve and could be signed right after his trip to China. Would you like to comment on this?","China’s firm opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear. The U.S. needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiques, especially the August 17 Communique of 1982, stop arms sales to Taiwan, and take concrete actions to uphold the steady growth of China-US relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260313_11874728.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260313_11874556.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-03-14","Chen Binhua","人就赖清德炮制所谓“民主即主权”等谬论答记者","Spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office Answers Reporters' Questions on Lai Ching-te's Fallacies Such as “Democracy Is Sovereignty”\nOn March 14, Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, answered reporters' questions.\nToday, Lai Ching-te attended the so-called “Seminar on 30 Years of Direct Election of the Leader of the Taiwan Region and Democratic Resilience,” where he…","In response to questions, Chen Binhua said that Lai Ching-te's speech is yet another “Taiwan independence confession” painstakingly pieced together and packaged. It once again arrogantly challenges the one-China principle and fully exposes how his “Taiwan independence” nature is unrepentant and his sinister intentions are plain to see.\nHe pointed out that Lai Ching-te seeks a basis for so-called “national status” for Taiwan, which does not exist, in so-called “direct election democracy,” fabricates a “Chinese threat to Taiwan,” clamors to “defend sovereignty,” and manufactures a false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism.” He incites confrontation and opposition across the Taiwan Strait and completely distorts Taiwan's history, departing from basic facts. The purpose is to delude the public, confuse the public, incite “resisting China to protect Taiwan,” and plot to “seek independence by force” and “resist unification by force.” In essence, this undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and pushes Taiwan toward war.\nChen Binhua stated that the two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The historical context is clear and the legal facts are clear. Although the two sides have not yet been fully unified, China's sovereignty and territorial integrity have never been divided. Taiwan has never been a country and will never become one; the so-called “sovereignty” simply does not exist. No matter how the Taiwan region holds its elections or whom it elects, this cannot change Taiwan's status as part of China, cannot sever the unbreakable historical and legal ties across the Taiwan Strait, and cannot overturn the iron rule that Taiwan's future can only be decided jointly by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. Different systems are not an obstacle to unification, and they are certainly not an excuse for separation. We will never allow anyone or any force to use the banner of democracy to carry out “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes. Lai Ching-te and his ilk should not miscalculate; if they dare to take risks, they will surely bring about their own destruction!\nChen Binhua stated that no matter what Lai Ching-te says or does, it cannot change the basic pattern of cross-Strait relations, much less stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will certainly be reunified. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the ambitions and selfish desires of Lai Ching-te and the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, stand on the right side of history, and join us in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, firmly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and protecting our common home, the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260314_12755592.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-03-18","Lin Jian","Phoenix TV","Last week, Lai Ching-te said at an event that Japan’s colonization of Taiwan was aimed at promoting the “Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere.” The statement provoked outrage among the people in the Taiwan region. Can I have your comment on that?","The Lai Ching-te authorities brazenly used the false narrative of Japanese aggressors to whitewash Japan’s aggression and colonial rule. This is a grave affront to history and despicable betrayal to the nation. Japan exerted colonial rule on the island for half a century, brutally suppressed the resistance of our Taiwan compatriots, massively plundered resources, and inflicted severe damage on Taiwan’s economy and culture and people’s wellbeing. This historic tragedy filled with blood and tears is deeply etched in the memory of the Chinese nation and shall never be forgotten or distorted.\nMore than 80 years ago, Taiwan was restored to its motherland, which ended its days in the shackles of colonial rule. It was a great victory achieved through strenuous struggles and tremendous sacrifice of the entire Chinese nation together, including our Taiwan compatriots. We will never ever allow anyone to justify colonialism or reverse history’s verdict on aggression. The remarks you mentioned once again laid bare Lai Ching-te’s true agenda: selling Taiwan out to ingratiate with Japan, seeking “Taiwan independence” and making provocations. The Lai Ching-te authorities think that they could reverse the process of China’s reunification by distorting history, whitewashing colonial atrocities and peddling their “Taiwan independence” historical narrative. It will only lead to their own demise.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260318_11876954.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260318_11876825.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-03-18","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that some DPP politicians recently smeared the mainland's embassy in Israel for helping Taiwan compatriots register for evacuation as \"political manipulation.\" The DPP authorities have also used the Middle East situation to pressure the blue and white camps, demanding that the review of the defense budget be accelerated. What is your comment on this?","“In the flames of war there is no mercy, but the motherland has love.” Jiang Bin said, “Taiwan compatriots are our family, bound by blood as thick as water. In every moment of crisis and every emergency evacuation of nationals, we devote all our efforts to protect our compatriots’ safety and bring our relatives home. This is the deep care of the great motherland for every Chinese person, and a consistent practice of putting the people and human life first.”\nJiang Bin said that the DPP authorities not only show indifference to the safety of Taiwan’s people and fail to act to help Taiwan compatriots trapped in war escape from conflict, but they actually obstruct them from accepting the mainland’s evacuation assistance, and even take the opportunity to seek political self-interest, single-mindedly pursuing “seeking independence by force.” They have extinguished their conscience and lack all humanity. This is despicable, and they will surely be condemned.","","https://www.news.cn/politics/20260318/86bb74c6b739457794e6917906f1b0e8/c.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 18, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Dear journalists, hello everyone! Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. I would also like to especially welcome the teachers and student representatives of Renmin University of China, including several Taiwanese teachers and students, who have come to observe the press conference. Thank you to all of society for its attention to and support for the work on Taiwan affairs and the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Fourth Session of the 14th National People's Congress approved the Outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan. What is your interpretation of the special chapter on Taiwan in the Outline? How will the TAO implement it?","On March 12, the Fourth Session of the 14th National People's Congress voted to adopt the Outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan for National Economic and Social Development. The Outline provides top-level design and strategic planning for work on Taiwan during the 15th Five-Year Plan period, and sets out the goals and tasks of promoting peaceful development of cross-strait relations and advancing the cause of national reunification in the course of comprehensively building a modern socialist country. The Outline clearly proposes that we must thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, firmly hold the initiative and dominance in cross-strait relations, enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and firmly safeguard our common home of the Chinese nation.\nIn specific arrangements: First, promote cross-strait economic cooperation. Continuously introduce and implement policies and measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies, guide Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan companies to actively integrate into and serve the construction of the new development pattern, support Taiwan companies in putting down roots and developing on the mainland, participate in national regional development strategies and the Belt and Road Initiative, strengthen industrial cooperation, and build a common cross-strait market. Support the high-quality construction of the Fujian cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone, and promote the construction of key cross-strait cooperation platforms such as Pingtan, Kunshan, Dongguan and the Straits Industrial Cooperation Zone. Support the building of multi-level cross-strait financial markets and encourage eligible Taiwan-funded companies to list on the mainland.\nSecond, deepen cross-strait exchanges. Improve systems and policies that promote cross-strait economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, expand personnel exchanges across the Strait, and promote exchange, interaction and integration across the Strait. Deepen cooperation between the two sides in education, healthcare and other fields, as well as in social security and sharing of public resources. Promote cultural exchange across the Strait, jointly inherit and carry forward Chinese culture, and enhance Taiwan compatriots' national identity, cultural identity and state identity. Strengthen exchanges with youth, grassroots and other groups, and continue to create better conditions for Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to pursue their dreams. Implement the policy of giving Taiwan compatriots equal treatment, and create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, work and live on the mainland. Unite broad Taiwan compatriots and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.\nWe will thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, and in line with the requirements of the 15th Five-Year Plan Outline, unite broad Taiwan compatriots, grasp the historical trend, and actively promote peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations, working together toward the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756173.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The Fourth Session of the 14th National People’s Congress deliberated and approved this year’s “Report on the Work of the Government.” How will the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office implement the Taiwan-related content of the “Report on the Work of the Government”?","This year is the opening year of the “15th Five-Year Plan.” The Taiwan-related content in this year's Government Work Report focuses on elaborating the major policies, principles, positions, and goals and tasks of current work on Taiwan, and has important guiding significance for doing this year's Taiwan work well.\nThe “14th Five-Year Plan” has been successfully concluded; our country's economic strength, scientific and technological strength, national defense strength, and comprehensive national strength have reached new heights, Chinese modernization has taken new solid steps, and a firmer foundation has been laid for advancing the great cause of national reunification. The implementation of the outline of the “15th Five-Year Plan” will certainly provide broader development opportunities for the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. We will thoroughly implement the overall strategy of the Party for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era and the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee on Taiwan work, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” uphold the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family,” deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, let compatriots on both sides share the opportunities and achievements of Chinese modernization, promote personnel exchanges and heart-to-heart connection across the Strait, and advance the joint inheritance and promotion of Chinese culture by both sides. We will resolutely combat “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, unite the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, firmly support the forces that favor patriotic reunification, firmly grasp the initiative and leading role in cross-Strait relations, and unswervingly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756172.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Some public opinion holds that this year’s Government Work Report emphasizes “resolutely combating the ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces.” Compared with last year’s report, which stated “resolutely opposing ‘Taiwan independence’ separatism,” this year’s wording is more explicit in attitude and stronger in force. What is your comment?","“Taiwan independence” separatist forces seriously undermine national sovereignty and territorial integrity, incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and constitute the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and they will only bring profound harm to Taiwan compatriots. On the question of principle concerning the safeguarding of national sovereignty and territorial integrity, our will is as firm as a rock, and our stance has always been consistent. We will not tolerate and will not show leniency toward any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity, and we have full confidence and strong capability to thwart any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme.\nThe more “Taiwan independence” provocations escalate, the more fiercely we will strike back. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and join us in resolutely striking against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, safeguarding their own security and welfare and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","TV dramas such as “The Silent Glory” have sparked a viewing craze on the island, and have also become a hot topic among deputies and members of the CPPCC during the 2026 Two Sessions. The stage play “The Cold Moon Silent: The Legend of Wu Shi,” adapted from this drama, has also been widely praised by audiences on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","General Wu Shi was a native of Fuzhou, Fujian. It is understood that relevant Fuzhou authorities, drawing on the plot of the TV drama “The Silent Glory,” created the immersive on-location drama “Cold Moon, Silent Sound — The Legend of Wu Shi.” Incorporating elements such as Fuzhou dialect nursery rhymes and tea culture, it adopts a dual-track narrative structure of “present-day reunion + historical retrospection” to present audiences with the legendary story of a hero. “In silence, one hears thunder.” The deeds of the martyrs still stir the blood today. Everyone is welcome to visit Wu Shi's former residence and watch the drama, and to share together the patriotic sentiments of the martyrs in turbulent times, jointly carry forward and promote their fearless spirit, and actively devote ourselves to the just cause of promoting the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Regarding the Fourth Session of the 14th National People's Congress passing the 《Law of the People's Republic of China on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress》, the head of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council stated: “This law carries the implication of punishing ‘independence,’ treats opposing ‘independence’ and promoting reunification as the same thing, and gives the possibility of legal punishment. This is…","The unity, struggle, and common prosperity of all ethnic groups are the lifeblood, the source of strength, and the hope of the Chinese nation. Formulating the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress lays a legal foundation for forging a sense of community for the Chinese nation and advancing the building of a community for the Chinese nation. It is of great significance for comprehensively advancing the cause of ethnic unity and progress, and for driving the people of all ethnic groups across the country to unite and struggle together for the great cause of building a strong nation and national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same language and culture, the same blood and origins, and both belong to the Chinese nation. We are a community of shared destiny, bound by blood and sharing weal and woe. We will thoroughly implement the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress, further deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, cultivate the common interests of compatriots on both sides, jointly promote Chinese culture, enhance Taiwan compatriots’ identification with the nation, culture, and the state, and work hand in hand to create a great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nThe DPP authorities, in pursuit of “independence” for their own private gain, have deliberately muddled the facts and fabricated so-called “risks.” The aim is to frighten the people of Taiwan and create a “chilling effect.” For acts by “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that split the nation and undermine ethnic unity, we will take all necessary measures and punish them in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756162.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, due to turbulence in the Middle East, Taiwan's domestic energy supply faces the danger of cut-offs of oil and gas, and all sectors on the island are highly concerned about energy resource reserves and supply. This has also drawn public attention to the fact that last October the mainland side first proposed that after unification Taiwan would enjoy “seven betters,” including “after peaceful…","Achieving unification by peaceful means is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and to the entire Chinese nation. Peaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development and will bring tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. Among these benefits is that, with a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan's energy and resource security will be better guaranteed.\nDuring the \"14th Five-Year Plan\" period, the mainland formed an energy supply system driven by multiple sources, including coal, oil, natural gas, nuclear power, and renewable energy. Traditional energy has maintained stable and increased production; new energy has been developed to the fullest extent possible, with its share rising rapidly. Wind and photovoltaic power generation accounts for about 22% of total electricity consumption across society. New types of energy storage, frontier hydrogen energy, virtual power plants, charging and swapping infrastructure, and other new business forms have seen increased deployment. The mainland's energy supply has tremendous resilience and broad potential. Take electricity as an example: at present, major countries around the world are developing artificial intelligence and related industries, and the development of the AI industry highly depends on a stable electricity supply. The mainland has already built the world's largest clean electricity supply system, with an average power supply reliability rate exceeding 99.9%. In 2025, total electricity consumption exceeded 10 trillion kilowatt-hours for the first time, surpassing the combined electricity consumption of the United States, Germany, Japan, and India. Among them, electricity consumption in July and August each exceeded 1 trillion kilowatt-hours for two consecutive months, setting a world record, with no power rationing and no price increases. Such full-capacity electricity supply is more than sufficient to meet the electricity needs of Taiwan's enterprises and can also free Taiwan's households from the inconvenience and worry of summer power use and rationing.\nThe 14th National People's Congress, whose Fourth Session has just concluded successfully, deliberated and approved the outline of the \"15th Five-Year Plan.\" The outline makes strategic arrangements for accelerating comprehensive green transformation of economic and social development and building a Beautiful China during the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period. We will accelerate the construction of a new energy system, continuously consolidate the foundation for energy and resource security, and continuously advance the construction of an energy powerhouse. After peaceful reunification, the two sides will achieve interconnection and mutual access, with everything connected wherever possible. This will fully be able to make up for Taiwan's shortages in electricity, natural gas, crude oil, and other areas, provide a reliable guarantee for Taiwan's energy and resource security, and allow Taiwan compatriots to enjoy cheaper, cleaner, and more stable energy supply, reducing the burden of energy use on families and businesses.\nMr. Sun Yat-sen once said: \"Unification is the hope of all Chinese citizens. If unification can be achieved, the whole nation will enjoy blessings; if not, the whole nation will suffer harm.\" We are willing to provide stable and reliable energy and resource security for Taiwan compatriots so that they may enjoy better lives. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots and mainland compatriots will work hand in hand to create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756171.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Regarding the question of whether, if the US continues fighting in the Middle East, mainland China would consider it an opportunity to act against Taiwan, US Deputy Secretary of Defense Colby said that the US is closely watching the reactions of other potential adversaries, and that the strength demonstrated by this US military operation has a deterrent effect. What comment do you have?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. It concerns China’s core interests and the national sentiments of the Chinese people, and brooks no foreign interference. No one and no force should underestimate our firm resolve, steadfast will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","《团结报》记者","The special chapter on Taiwan in the Outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan points out that we must deepen cross-Strait exchanges, improve the systems and policies that promote cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, expand personnel exchanges across the Strait, and advance cross-Strait exchanges, interactions and integration; promote cross-Strait cultural exchanges, jointly inherit and carry…","The special chapter on Taiwan-related affairs in the Outline makes important arrangements and sets clear requirements for cross-strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, pointing the way for cross-strait exchange work over the next five years.\nOver the next five years, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will, together with localities and departments, thoroughly study and implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important expositions on Taiwan work and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, earnestly implement the Taiwan-related work arrangements in the Outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan, and strive to promote high-quality development of cross-strait exchange work. We will continue to introduce policies and measures that facilitate and ensure cross-strait personnel exchanges, continuously expand and deepen exchanges and cooperation in all fields and at all levels across the Strait, strive to restore and expand cross-strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and promote closer contact and deeper exchanges between compatriots on both sides. We will continue to unite broad Taiwan compatriots and carry out cultural exchanges and cooperation in various forms, jointly inherit and carry forward excellent Chinese culture, and support broad Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, in participating in the development of Chinese culture, so that Chinese culture shines even more brilliantly in the new era, injecting vigorous vitality into the development of cross-strait relations. We will earnestly implement the Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, and support Fujian-Taiwan integrated development in taking new steps and opening new prospects. We will continue to deepen integrated development in all fields of cross-strait relations, continuously improve the systems and policies that support Taiwan compatriots in coming to the mainland to study, work and live, unswervingly implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots, support Taiwan compatriots in broadly participating in the development of all undertakings on the mainland, and share in the achievements of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","The outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan places the development of new quality productive forces, adapted to local conditions, in a more prominent and important strategic position, and stresses deepening the integration of technological innovation and industrial innovation. What opportunities will this bring to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises developing on the mainland?","The “15th Five-Year Plan” period is a critical time for laying the foundation and making comprehensive efforts to basically achieve socialist modernization, and it occupies an important position of linking the past and the future in the process of basically achieving socialist modernization. The Outline of the “15th Five-Year Plan” makes strategic arrangements for building a modern industrial system and promoting deep integration of scientific and technological innovation with industrial innovation. In upgrading traditional industries, Taiwan enterprises can use coordinated innovation across upstream and downstream links to achieve digital transformation and intelligent upgrading, and to bring about vibrant high-end, intelligent and green development. In growing emerging industries, Taiwan enterprises can develop new technologies, new products and new scenarios, enter new fields and new tracks, and move up to the high end of industrial and value chains. In cultivating future industries, Taiwan enterprises can make good use of the mainland's technology and industrial resources, actively integrate into the innovation ecosystem, and gain broader room for development. In short, the “15th Five-Year Plan” is a period of great development for the mainland, and also a period in which Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises can achieve much.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Regarding the so-called “nationality” dispute involving Li Zhenxiu, an at-large legislator of the Taiwan People’s Party, the Mainland Affairs Council said it recommends that people in situations such as “children born in mainland China to cross-Strait marriages who lived in mainland China as children” confirm whether they had household registration in mainland China, so as to avoid problems with their Taiwan…","The DPP authorities have repeatedly manipulated the household registration issue of mainland spouses and their children, and deliberately confused it with the so-called “nationality” issue. Their purpose is to suppress and persecute mainland spouses, deprive them of their legitimate rights, and smuggle in the “two-state theory.” We strongly condemn this, will take necessary measures to shelter mainland spouses from the storm and safeguard the legitimate rights of cross-Strait marriage families, and at the same time resolutely crack down on the chief culprits who arbitrarily suppress and persecute the mainland spouse group.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","The Supreme People's Court work report, deliberated and adopted at the Fourth Session of the Fourteenth National People's Congress, explicitly proposed to “severely punish die-hard ‘Taiwan independence’ elements,” and mentioned “convicting and sentencing Li Yanhe according to law for inciting secession of the country and undermining national unification.” Scholars assess that this report demonstrates the…","Using criminal justice measures to punish criminals who incite secession of the country is a legitimate and necessary move to safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that will not work. We will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China under any name or by any means. If “Taiwan independence” elements dare to break the law, they will certainly be hit hard by judicial action.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","According to reports, Taiwan's “Chinese Culture Association” has begun pushing for a “renaming” to remove the term “Chinese.” It will first change the English name to present itself as “Taiwan,” and the English name is expected to be changed to “National Cultural Association of Taiwan.” What is your comment on this?","China has a long history and a vast civilization. Chinese culture, which has continued without interruption and endlessly renewed itself, is the common spiritual home and spiritual lifeblood of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and a firm bond that sustains national emotion and unites national identity. The move by Taiwan's “Chinese Culture General Association” is a farce in which the DPP authorities have intensified their “de-Sinicization” in the cultural field and manipulated “de-Chinaization.” Its essence is an attempt to sever the cultural roots that both sides share and to create the false perception that “Taiwan culture is independent of Chinese culture.” Changing the English name first and the Chinese name later is a typical case of a guilty conscience. It is an attempt to furtively and step by step hollow out the meaning of “Chinese” and pave the way for the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme. We firmly oppose this.\nTaiwan culture is rooted in Chinese culture. This is a basic fact and a collective consensus among the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and it cannot be altered or denied. Any attempt to use a name change to advance “Taiwan independence” separatism or to sever the national roots violates the trend of history and hurts national sentiment. It will certainly be firmly opposed by all Chinese people and has absolutely no future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756157.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson’s rebuttal of Lai Qingde’s “Taiwan independence” fallacies at the so-called “30th Anniversary of Taiwan’s Direct Presidential Election and Democratic Resilience Seminar,” the DPP authorities said, “The essence of cross-Strait relations lies in a contest of systems,” and “The mainland should conduct dialogue with the democratically elected legitimate government…","The Lai Ching-te authorities, under the pretext of so-called \"universal values,\" treat democracy as a fig leaf for suppressing dissidents, \"resisting China and protecting Taiwan,\" and colluding with external forces. They attempt to delude the public, confuse public perception, incite cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, \"relying on foreign forces to seek independence\" and \"using force to resist unification.\" Their sinister intentions are plainly evident.\nDifferent systems are not an obstacle to reunification, much less an excuse for separation. The relationship across the Taiwan Strait is absolutely not a contest of systems, but a struggle between unification and separation. The so-called \"contest of systems\" is a pretext used by the DPP authorities to seek independence, a trick to deceive Taiwan compatriots and the international community.\nNo matter what Lai Ching-te and his kind say or do, they cannot change the status of Taiwan as part of China, cannot sever the unbreakable historical and legal ties across the Taiwan Strait, and cannot overturn the iron law that the future of Taiwan can only be decided jointly by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. In the face of the trend of the times in which the two sides of the Strait will inevitably be reunified, and in the face of the determination and will of 1.4 billion-plus compatriots to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, any scheme to split the country and resist reunification is wishful thinking.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756158.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Affected by the situation in the Middle East, nearly one hundred Taiwan compatriots who had been stranded there for several days were smoothly evacuated with the assistance of Chinese embassies and consulates abroad, and returned to Taiwan via transit in Shanghai. Several Taiwan compatriots who received assistance said in media interviews, “Thank the motherland, it was the mainland that helped us come home.” The…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. We are always concerned for the safety of Chinese citizens overseas, including Taiwan compatriots. Recently, affected by the situation in the Middle East, many Taiwan compatriots have been stranded locally. Recently, the Chinese Consulate General in Istanbul coordinated with relevant parties to assist 93 Taiwan compatriots in switching to mainland flights to Shanghai, promptly processed Taiwan Compatriot Permits for them, and helped them transfer and return to Taiwan smoothly. In addition, many other Taiwan compatriots have sought help through the China Consular Service app, the 12308 consular protection hotline, and other channels. Chinese embassies and consulates abroad, including the Chinese Embassy in Iran, the Embassy in Israel, and the Consulate General in Dubai, have all assisted Taiwan compatriots in returning to Taiwan or evacuating to safe areas. Compatriots who received assistance expressed their feelings one after another: “No matter when, the motherland is always there,” “We personally experienced that compatriots on both sides are one family,” and “The Taiwan Compatriot Permit is a talisman.”\nThe DPP authorities are indifferent to the calls for help from stranded Taiwan compatriots, heartless, incapable, and inactive. Yet they repeatedly attack and slander the mainland side for its care and protection of Taiwan compatriots, which is truly shameless. Who truly keeps Taiwan compatriots in their hearts, and who truly shelters them from wind and rain? The facts are in front of us, and justice lies in people’s hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756156.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","According to a Reuters report from the United Kingdom, a large-scale arms sales case to Taiwan covering advanced interceptor missiles is being prepared for submission to President Trump for approval, and Trump may sign it after visiting China. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any relevant countries selling weapons to China’s Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the issue of arms sales to Taiwan prudently, and maintain the stability of China-U.S. relations and peace in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, stated at a forum on the island that the mainland is distorting UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 in an attempt to rationalize “use of force against Taiwan and suppression of Taiwan's international participation,” while the US side refuted the mainland's claims. “China's distortion is a political manipulation, not an international legal…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. In 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all rights of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. This thoroughly resolved, politically, legally and procedurally, the question of representation of all of China in the United Nations, including Taiwan. That there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China's territory is the common understanding of the international community.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding the irrefutable facts and legal principles, have on various occasions and in various ways continuously distorted and attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, openly challenging the basic norms of international relations and the consensus of the international community. Such efforts are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Recently, the United States announced that it will launch so-called “unfair trade practices” investigations under Section 301 against some trading partners, including the Taiwan region of China. Some analysts on the island believe that the DPP authorities have let the United States do as it pleases while the United States has not gone easy on Taiwan in return, which is unacceptable. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities pursue “blind obedience to the US” and “looking only to the US,” shamelessly kowtowing to the US without principle and selling out Taiwan without bottom line, exerting every effort to cling to the US at the cost of the well-being of Taiwan's people and the economic prospects of the island. However, unilateral compromise and concession not only fail to earn any pity, but have only brought step-by-step predatory demands. In the end, they will inevitably be devoured and squeezed dry, which is truly ridiculous, detestable, and sad.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260318_12756154.htm"],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: In implementing the outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan, the Taiwan Affairs Office mentioned restoring cross-Strait tourism cooperation. Does this mean that the mainland side is expected to announce a full restart of group tours from the mainland to Taiwan or of independent travel by mainland tourists to Taiwan?\nSecond question: On March 4, Wang Huning, Chairman of the National Committee of the…","First question. We have consistently and clearly supported and actively promoted the restoration of normal personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and the normalization of exchanges in all fields, including tourism. The DPP authorities, using various excuses to obstruct cross-Strait tourism cooperation, are engaging in a practice that is unpopular. The DPP authorities should heed the mainstream public opinion on the island that calls for exchanges and cooperation, and make the right decision as soon as possible.\nSecond question. Both sides of the Strait are Chinese and are one family, and Chinese on both sides have the wisdom and ability to properly handle their own affairs. Mr. Sun Yat-sen was a great national hero, a great patriot, and a great pioneer of China's democratic revolution. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should learn from, inherit, and carry forward his precious spirit, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, hand in hand advance the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Recently, Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang, attended the “Speaking in Peacetime” forum and said that cross-Strait peace is not merely Taiwan’s wishful thinking, and that she also perceives the great goodwill and sincerity the mainland has shown. She said the peaceful relationship across the Strait should be stable and institutionalized. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and all hope for a peaceful and tranquil homeland and for family members to live in harmony. We will actively promote and fully facilitate any measures that are conducive to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and to enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work together with Taiwan’s political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang of China, to strengthen exchanges and interactions and maintain positive interaction, in order to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","台湾中视记者","First question: KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently said in an interview that she hopes to meet General Secretary Xi Jinping on the mainland between April and June this year, and that the KMT and the CPC should hold consultations to steer cross-Strait relations in a peaceful direction. What is your response?\nSecond question: The mainland recently announced that it would open tourism to Kinmen and Matsu for…","First question: Wanting peace, development, exchange and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion on the island. On the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and interactions with the Kuomintang at all levels, enhance political mutual trust, maintain positive interaction, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, seek well-being for compatriots, and seek national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation.\nSecond question: The DPP authorities have consistently used various pretexts to obstruct and restrict the resumption of cross-Strait tourism. The DPP authorities should heed the mainstream public opinion on the island that wants exchange and cooperation, respond to the interest demands of Taiwan residents and the tourism industry, change their unpopular practices as soon as possible, and make the right decision quickly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said at the so-called “Yushan Forum” on the island: “Peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait are essential elements of world security and prosperity. Faced with rapid changes in geopolitics and the intensifying of non-traditional threats and gray-zone interference, Taiwan is determined to safeguard peace and stability in the region, and to seek peace through strength. Taiwan must…","The DPP authorities’ plotting for independence and provocations are the root of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities, attempting to “seek independence through force” and “resist reunification through force,” continuously escalate tension in the Taiwan Strait and do not hesitate to tie the Taiwan public to the “Taiwan independence” chariot. They are unmistakably “destroyers of cross-Strait peace,” “creators of the Taiwan Strait crisis,” and “instigators of war.” We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the ambitions and private desires of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, firmly oppose the “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct, resolutely maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and safeguard our common Chinese national home.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: In February 2025, the Shanghai No. 1 Intermediate People’s Court sentenced Li Yanhe, chief editor of Taiwan’s Eight Banners Culture, to three years in prison for inciting secession of the state, deprived him of political rights for one year, and confiscated personal property of 50,000 yuan. When will Li be released? What is his current situation?\nSecond question: The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation…","First question: Li Yanhe is a criminal who incited the subversion of state power and undermined national unity. The facts of his crime are clear, and the judicial authorities conducted a public trial in accordance with the law. Li pleaded guilty and accepted the verdict in court. As for the question of his prison term, the relevant parties will handle the matter in accordance with the law.\nSecond question: We have noted the relevant reports. In recent years, the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation has actively carried out cross-strait exchange activities, which have drawn wide attention and positive appraisal from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait, and have played a positive role in promoting exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, especially young people, and in promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. We are willing, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with political parties, groups, and personages from all walks of life in Taiwan to strengthen exchanges and cooperation and people-to-people contacts across the Taiwan Strait in all fields, promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","台湾东森电视台记者","Reportedly, a recent poll of American academics shows that most mainland residents are friendly toward Taiwan, with as many as 80% hoping to strengthen cross-Strait cultural and economic exchanges. If conflict is unavoidable, only 30% of the public support a full-scale attack on Taiwan. What is your comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We have always upheld the concept of “one family across the Strait,” actively supported and promoted personnel exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, and enhanced the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and the greatest effort. However, we will never allow the destruction of national sovereignty and territorial integrity, we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we reserve the option of taking all necessary measures. Any separatist forces and acts seeking to split the motherland will surely be met with a head-on blow from the entire Chinese people!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Japan's “Japan-ROC Diet Members' Consultative Council” chairman Furuya Keiji clamored at the “Yushan Forum” that “Japan is determined to protect Taiwan, Taiwan's democracy, and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait,” and falsely claimed that “no attempt to unilaterally change the status quo should be allowed, and a change in Taiwan's situation must never be allowed to happen.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no interference from any external force. The remarks made by the person you mentioned seriously violate the one-China principle. This is overreaching, and we firmly oppose it. Japan bears historical responsibility toward the Chinese people on the Taiwan question. Japan should fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question, draw lessons from history, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and stop all wrong words and deeds concerning Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Reports indicate that Lai Ching-te may make a sneak visit to Eswatini in April, and Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities said they have received an invitation from the other side. The outside world is concerned about whether he will transit through Europe during the visit. What is your comment on this?","We consistently handle the external exchanges of the Taiwan region in accordance with the One China principle, and firmly oppose any act that attempts to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” internationally. Relevant countries should properly handle related issues in accordance with the One China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-18","Chen Binhua","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","According to reports, two of the latest Type 055 guided-missile destroyers are about to be commissioned into the Chinese People's Liberation Army Navy. Some scholars analyze that this will significantly enhance the navy's ability to deter and strike “Taiwan independence” forces. What is your comment on this?","We will not tolerate “Taiwan independence” in any form, and we will not show it any leniency. We will certainly strike it head-on and resolutely crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and external interference. Our will to fight “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard national reunification and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock, and our capabilities are growing ever stronger.\nToday's press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260318_12756152.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-03-19","Lin Jian","Yonhap News Agency","In response to the ROK listing Taiwan as “China (Taiwan)” on its electronic arrival card system, the Taiwan authorities have said that they will change the designation of “Korea” to “South Korea” on some of its entry and exit documents. What is China’s comment on this?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. We believe the ROK will continue to adhere to the one-China principle, which is clearly stated in the China-ROK joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations, and will handle the Taiwan question accordingly.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260319_11877725.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260319_11877656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-19","Lin Jian","Reuters","U.S. intelligence agencies in an annual report about global threats said China does not have plans currently to invade Taiwan next year in 2027, seeking instead to control the island without any use of force. What does China have to say about that report and this matter?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that brooks no external interference. The U.S. needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués and act all the more prudently on the Taiwan question. Relevant U.S. agencies and personnel need to discard ideological bias and Cold-War and zero-sum mentality, form a correct perception of China, and stop peddling the “China threat” narrative.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260319_11877725.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260319_11877656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-19","Lin Jian","Reuters","Following the question I had earlier about the report from U.S. intelligence agencies, they said that Japan has shown a “significant shift” from its previous rhetoric on Taiwan, and this is referring to Prime Minister Takaichi’s remarks about a hypothetical Chinese attack on Taiwan. The Japanese government responded this morning, rejecting the U.S.’s assessment, and said that its position on how it determines an…","Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan blatantly interfered in China’s internal affairs. The remarks signal Japan’s intention to attempt armed intervention on the Taiwan question, and constitute a threat of force against China. China has more than once made clear its serious position. The report you cited shows that the international community is increasingly aware of the egregious nature and impact of those remarks and remains vigilant against Japan’s dangerous provocations. Japan’s claim that it “has not changed its position” is hardly convincing. That kind of attitude will not possibly enable Japan to establish trust with its Asian neighbors and the international community. We urge Japan to reflect on its behavior and change course, act on the four political documents between China and Japan and Japan’s own commitments and abide by the pacifist clause of the Japanese Constitution. Time for Japan to stop going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260319_11877725.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260319_11877656.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-20","Lin Jian","Kyodo News","It’s reported that the Japanese prime minister and the U.S. president in their meeting underlined the importance of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. What is China’s comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair, and resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese. To maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, one should unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism. China is firmly resolved in defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260320_11878433.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260320_11878245.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-20","Lin Jian","Nippon TV","At this morning’s Japan-U.S. summit, Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi said Japan has been consistently open to dialogue with China. Do you have any comment on this?","China has made clear its just position on this issue more than once. True dialogue is built on the basis of respecting each other and honoring the agreements made. If anyone just talks about the need for dialogue on the one hand, while on the other, keeps stoking confrontation, then this so-called “dialogue” is apparently unacceptable. If the Japanese side truly wants to improve its relations with China, it needs to abide by the four political documents between China and Japan and its own commitments, retract the erroneous remarks on Taiwan at an early date, seriously reflect on and correct its wrongdoings, and take concrete actions to uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260320_11878433.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260320_11878245.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-24","Lin Jian","AFP","Taiwan said that it would skip for the first time a high-level World Trade Organization meeting in Cameroon. Taiwan said that Cameroon had designated the island as a province of China in paperwork issued to its delegation. What is the Foreign Ministry’s comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations is consistent and clear, that is, it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The one-China principle is the political prerequisite for the Taiwan region’s participation in the WTO. The DPP authorities are engaging in political manipulation despicably under the pretext of participation in the WTO conference to create disruption and serve their “Taiwan independence” agenda. There is no way they will succeed.\nAs the international economic and trade order faces severe challenges with unilateralism and protectionism on the rise and the multilateral trading system gravely impacted, it is of special significance that the WTO holds a ministerial conference in Africa again after a decade. China firmly supports Cameroon in making this WTO Ministerial Conference a success.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260324_11880206.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260324_11880190.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-24","Lin Jian","Reuters","This is according to a draft reviewed by Reuters. Japan will downgrade its description of ties with China from “one of the most important” to instead describing China as an important neighbor and the relationship as “strategic and mutually beneficial.” This is in an annual diplomatic report that is being under review by the government. Does China have any comment on this?","The root cause of the current situation facing China-Japan relations is Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, which have sparked outrage from the Chinese people and tested the red line of the post-war international order. If the Japanese side truly wants to improve and develop relations with China, it needs to abide by the four political documents between China and Japan and its own commitments, retract the erroneous remarks on Taiwan as soon as possible, do soul-searching and correct its wrongdoings, and take concrete actions to uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260324_11880206.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260324_11880190.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-24","Lin Jian","Global Times","We’ve learned that this morning, a member of the Japanese ‌Self-Defense Forces broke into China’s embassy in Tokyo. Could you share more details with us?","On the morning of March 24, a man who claimed himself to be a sitting officer of Japan’s Self-Defence Forces scaled the wall and broke into the Chinese embassy in Tokyo. The individual admitted ‌that his actions were illegal and threatened to ‌kill Chinese diplomats in the so-called “name of god.”\nChina is deeply shocked at this incident and has lodged strong démarches and protests with Japan. The incident is a serious violation of the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations and posed a grave threat to the safety and security of Chinese diplomatic personnel and facilities. The incident is egregious in both nature and impact. The incident once again highlighted the danger of the rampant spread of far-right impact and neo-militarism in the country. It also reveals the toxicity of the Japanese government’s erroneous policies on vital issues concerning China-Japan relations such as history and Taiwan, and Japan’s failure in maintaining discipline in SDF and in fulfilling its responsibility to protect the Chinese diplomatic and consular premises and personnel.\nChina asks the Japanese side to thoroughly investigate the incident at once, bring the full weight of law to bear on the perpetrator and fully account for the incident. The Japanese side must ensure the safety and security of Chinese diplomatic and consular premises and personnel, reflect on and correct its erroneous policies on China and get rid of the root cause for such incidents once and for all. The international community needs to stay on high alert against Japan’s accelerating rightward turn and loss of control inside the rapidly expanding SDF.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260324_11880206.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260324_11880190.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-25","Lin Jian","Reuters","Has the Japanese side given China any assurance after the break-in that something like this will not happen again? Does this incident risk widening the schism between Tokyo and Beijing?","The incident once again highlighted the danger of the rampant spread of far-right impact and neo-militarism in the country. It also reveals the toxicity of the Japanese government’s erroneous policies on vital issues concerning China-Japan relations such as history and Taiwan, and Japan’s failure in maintaining discipline in Self-Defense Force and in fulfilling its responsibility to protect the Chinese diplomatic and consular premises and personnel. With regard to what measures the Japanese side will take to properly handle the incident and get rid of the root cause for such incidents once and for all, I suggest you ask the Japanese side. The international community, including China, is watching.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260325_11880943.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260325_11880819.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on March 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to the TAO press conference. Please begin asking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, a Taiwanese civic group visited the Xiamen section of the Xiamen-Jinmen Bridge and the construction site of Xiamen Xiang'an Airport. They praised the rapid progress of these two projects and were also amazed by the mainland's infrastructure capabilities. We note that the mainland side proposed last October that after reunification, Taiwan would have “seven betters,” including: “After peaceful…","At last week’s press conference, we explained “more secure energy and resource supply,” one of the “seven betters,” which drew close attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Today, in response to everyone’s expectations, we will further explain why infrastructure construction in Taiwan can be “better” after reunification.\nDuring the “14th Five-Year Plan” period, the mainland’s major infrastructure has continued to be upgraded, and its overall scale ranks first in the world. The total mileage of the integrated transportation network exceeds 6 million kilometers, including a total highway mileage of 5.49 million kilometers and a total railway mileage of over 165,000 kilometers. The total high-speed rail mileage reaches 50,400 kilometers, covering 97% of cities with urban populations of over 500,000. The aviation network covers 92.6% of prefecture-level cities. The length of 220-kilovolt and higher transmission lines is nearly 960,000 kilometers, the mileage of oil and gas pipeline networks exceeds 190,000 kilometers, and the total storage capacity of reservoirs exceeds 1 trillion cubic meters, forming an ultra-large-scale network advantage.\nTechnological innovation capacity has been greatly enhanced. Breakthroughs have continuously been achieved in areas such as long-span bridges, large-scale water conservancy projects, and next-generation mobile communications. A large number of core technologies with independent intellectual property rights have been formed, and many “super projects” have amazed the world.\nInternational connectivity has been extended and expanded. The China-Europe Railway Express and the “Silk Road Maritime Express” reach cities and ports in dozens of countries and regions, and the China-Laos Railway, the Jakarta-Bandung High-Speed Railway and others have been completed and put into operation. It can be said that the grand blueprint envisioned by Mr. Sun Yat-sen in his “Plans for National Construction” has long been realized, and many achievements have far exceeded what Mr. Sun Yat-sen imagined.\nDuring the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, we will accelerate the construction of a modern infrastructure system to provide strong support for building a powerful country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the nation. Among the 109 major projects in the “15th Five-Year Plan,” 23 are directly related to infrastructure. These will not only further enhance the construction of transportation, water conservancy, energy and other infrastructure, but also strengthen the construction of major science and technology infrastructure, information and communication networks, computing power networks and other new infrastructure.\nAfter reunification, the mainland’s powerful infrastructure construction capacity will provide strong support for upgrading and modernizing Taiwan’s infrastructure. Transportation, energy, agriculture and forestry, water conservancy, urban renewal and other infrastructure in the Taiwan region will be rebuilt and upgraded, and the lives of Taiwan compatriots will inevitably gain more convenience as a result. For example, we can help quickly build a high-speed railway around the island and build more expressways connecting the east and west of the main island. Cross-Strait infrastructure connectivity will gradually become a reality. For instance, we can jointly build the Strait Express Route, which has been studied for many years, turning a “natural chasm into a smooth passage,” so that Taiwan residents can depart from the main island and drive along the Beijing-Taipei Expressway to Beijing for sightseeing. In short, peaceful reunification will be the starting point for a completely renewed infrastructure and new infrastructure in Taiwan. We hope compatriots in Taiwan will pursue peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Strait as they pursue a happy life, making the homes where they work and live more accessible, more convenient and better.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757320.htm"],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Agriculture is one of the earliest, most broadly based, and most effective areas of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. This March marks the fifth anniversary of the “22 Measures on Agriculture and Forestry.” Please introduce the concrete results of relevant policies over the past five years. Some Taiwanese agricultural figures have pointed out that the “15th Five-Year Plan” provides new opportunities for…","In March 2021, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, the State Forestry and Grassland Administration, and other departments jointly issued the “Several Measures to Support Taiwan Compatriot-Invested Enterprises in Developing Agriculture and Forestry on the Mainland” (referred to as the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures”). Over the past five years, localities have adapted policies to local conditions and times, continuously promoting their implementation in detail, supporting Taiwan farmers and enterprises in achieving better development on the mainland. Here we would like to introduce some developments to everyone.\nFirst, land security has become more adequate. Localities have strictly implemented the requirements of the “Agriculture and Forestry 22 Measures” concerning the transfer of land management rights and the management of facility agricultural land. They have streamlined approval procedures, shortened processing timelines, and optimized land services. For example, over the past five years, Gansu has helped Taiwan enterprises transfer more than 10,000 mu of land. Zhejiang has innovated a “standard land” land supply model and assisted several Taiwan enterprises in obtaining land approval. Fujian has built a province-wide forest rights trading platform and established a digital system, providing information release, policy consultation, and transaction guidance services for forest rights transfers by business entities including Taiwan compatriots and enterprises.\nSecond, financial support has become more robust. Localities have promoted Taiwan compatriots and enterprises’ enjoyment of equal agricultural support and benefit policies, their application for various subsidies, and facilitation of financing. For example, Xinjiang has helped Taiwan-funded agricultural enterprises obtain subsidies, rewards, and equity investments exceeding 10 million yuan. Fujian has innovated by building a cross-border credit service platform and issuing financial credit certificates for Taiwan businesspeople and compatriots, providing convenient financial services to certificate holders, including high credit limits, lower loan interest rates, fee exemptions, and fast-track channels. Hainan, Chongqing, Jiangxi, Jiangsu, and other places have launched financial services such as biological resource collateral loans, government risk compensation funds, Taiwan agricultural loans, and agricultural credit loan programs, expanding financing channels.\nThird, platform development has become more diversified. As of the end of 2025, among the 36 Taiwan Farmers Entrepreneurship Parks approved for establishment in 14 provinces, 10 parks have been approved to build modern agricultural industrial parks. Industrial clustering effects are prominent, and their radiating and driving roles are evident, making them gathering places where Taiwan farmers and compatriots take root and develop on the mainland. Relevant departments have set up the Cross-Strait Rural Integrated Development Pilot Zone in Sanming, Fujian, support the holding of rural integrated development forums, and explore pathways for cross-Strait cooperation in rural industries, rural construction, and rural governance, creating new platforms and new opportunities for exchange and cooperation among Taiwan and mainland practitioners and scholars.\nFourth, integrated development has deepened. Taiwan compatriots are supported in participating in the selection and commendation of honorary titles. Xie Dongqing, Wu Yunzhen, and Guo Yangfu, three Taiwan compatriots, were named “Agriculture, Rural Areas and Farmers” figures. Taiwan compatriots and enterprises are encouraged to participate in revitalizing rural areas on the mainland. Ningxia, Heilongjiang, Inner Mongolia, and other places have incubated and cultivated a batch of benchmark Taiwan-funded agricultural product processing enterprises. Fujian has invested a cumulative 687 million yuan over five years to support Taiwan youth in participating in rural construction and rural innovation. Zhejiang has invited Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to participate in demonstration rural planning projects such as the “Taipei Town” in Jinhua. Hainan has implemented a “zero tariff” policy allowing Taiwan enterprises to enjoy duty-free treatment on self-use production equipment in the Hainan Free Trade Port. Guangdong and Fujian encourage Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to jointly participate in drafting technical standards.\nThis year marks the opening year of the “15th Five-Year” Plan. The outline of the “15th Five-Year” Plan explicitly proposes “accelerating the modernization of agriculture and rural areas and steadily advancing the comprehensive revitalization of rural areas,” systematically deploying key tasks such as enhancing agricultural comprehensive production capacity and the quality and efficiency of benefits, promoting the construction of livable, workable, and beautiful rural areas, and improving the effectiveness of policies supporting agriculture, benefiting rural residents, and enriching farmers. These provide many opportunities for Taiwan farmers and compatriots to participate in high-quality development on the mainland. We are willing to take the lead in sharing development opportunities in agriculture and forestry on the mainland with Taiwan compatriots, further improve policy measures that enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and ensure equal treatment, create better conditions for Taiwan farmers and enterprises to develop on the mainland, and welcome more Taiwan farmers and enterprises to invest and start businesses on the mainland, sharing opportunities and pursuing development together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757316.htm"],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce what recent cross-Strait exchange activities there have been?","Spring is here, with flowers in bloom and grass growing lush and orioles flying about. Exchange activities across all fields between the two sides of the Strait are taking place one after another. Here, I will introduce several major recent activities.\nFrom March 12 to 14, the Meizhou Mazu Ancestral Temple in Putian, Fujian, and the Tianhou Temple in Matsu jointly organized a root-seeking and ancestor-worship journey to commemorate the 25th anniversary of the passenger route of the “Small Three Links” (direct transport, trade, and postal links between Kinmen/Matsu and Fujian). Some Taiwan Mazu believers who had participated in the maiden voyage of the “Small Three Links” gathered again at the Mazu Ancestral Temple. 650 Mazu believers from temples such as the Qingong Temple in Fengyuan District, Taichung, also came to the Mazu Ancestral Temple to pay homage, joining mainland believers in carrying forward and promoting Mazu culture.\nOn March 20, the “Together in Spirit to Welcome the Spring, Hand in Hand to Create a New Chapter” 2026 Taiwan Businesspeople and Enterprises Symposium and Spring Welcoming Friendship Gathering was held in the Haicang Taiwan Investment Zone, Xiamen, Fujian. More than 100 Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan youth shared their views on opportunities for development that the 15th Five-Year Plan and the construction of the cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone bring to Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople, as well as on optimizing the business environment, discussing development together.\nFrom March 21 to 23, representatives from all walks of life in Kinmen County, chairpersons of 30 temples, and more than 2,000 believers of Guan Yu crossed the Strait to Longhai and Dongshan in Zhangzhou, Fujian, to carry out Guan Yu cultural exchange activities, continuing the cross-Strait bond of incense and fellowship and promoting the spirit of loyalty and righteousness embodied by Guan Yu.\nOn March 20, the 2026 “Wenchang Cup” Cross-Strait Youth Short Video Competition successfully concluded in Zitong, Mianyang, Sichuan. The competition was launched on February 11 and adopted a combination of “online work collection and offline extreme creative shooting.” More than 1,700 original short video works were collected, and over 100 young self-media creators from both sides of the Strait took part in the offline activities. The 43 outstanding award-winning works show that young people on both sides of the Strait convey their longing for a good life through vivid imagery, tell the common roots and inheritance of Wenchang culture across the Strait through the language of the lens, and express their confidence and passion for jointly promoting Chinese culture through sincere interaction. On March 21, Zitong also held the 8th Cross-Strait Wenchang Culture Exchange Activity, where more than 600 guests from both sides of the Strait gathered at the Wenchang ancestral shrine to inherit Chinese cultural heritage and talk about fraternal bonds between compatriots. To help more Taiwan compatriots understand Wenchang culture and the “Spirit of the Two Bombs,” all Taiwan compatriots may visit the Qiqushan Scenic Area and the Liangdan City Scenic Area in Zitong County free of charge with their Taiwan compatriot permit from March 20, 2026, to March 20, 2027.\nOn March 21, the 2026 Su-Taiwan Neighborhood Gathering and Chinese Traditional Sports Exchange Competition opened in Suqian, Jiangsu. The competition includes 10 events in total, including an original square dance competition, the Luoma Lake Bicycle Open, the first “Overlord Cup” Cross-Strait Chinese Chess Open, and a traditional martial arts exchange competition. The competition will continue until the end of June, and more than 4,500 compatriots from both sides of the Strait are expected to take part, fully enjoying the charm of Chinese traditional sports and gaining a deeper understanding of Jiangsu’s achievements in economic and social development.\nIn addition, the drama “Taste of Searching” (《寻味》), a cross-Strait production co-produced by the All-China Federation of Trade Unions, the Beijing Federation of Literary and Art Circles, and the Beijing Taiwan Affairs Office, centers on the story of Kuomintang veterans crossing the Strait to search for relatives and reflects the separations and reunions of four generations. It will begin a new round of national tours from early April to early June, performing in Chengdu, Xiamen, Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Zhuhai, Suzhou, Shanghai, and other cities. Since its premiere in early 2023, the play has been widely acclaimed and has won several honors, including Outstanding Production at the 18th China Drama Festival. We welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait to watch this excellent drama together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Regarding tourism by Shanghai residents to Kinmen and Matsu, Lo Wen-chia, Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, recently said that the SEF is ready to hold detailed consultations on the entry-related rules for Shanghai residents entering Kinmen and Matsu, at any time the other side is ready. What is your comment?","Restoring tourism for Shanghai residents to Kinmen and Matsu accords with the mainstream public opinion on the island that it wants peace, development, exchange and cooperation, and the mainland side will actively respond to the expectations and calls of the Taiwan public and the tourism industry and continue to advance the relevant work. The key now is whether the DPP authorities can face up to the mainstream public opinion on the island and the calls of the industry, and create favorable conditions for personnel exchanges and cooperation across the Strait.\nAs for exchanges between the two cross-Strait associations, it is well known that the DPP authorities obstinately insist on their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist position, refuse to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation, and have caused the dialogue and consultation between the two associations to stall. Only by acknowledging the \"1992 Consensus\" can the two associations resolve, through dialogue and consultation, the internal affairs of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities recently said that because Cameroon, the host of the 14th WTO Ministerial Conference, listed the name of Taiwan's delegation on the courtesy visa as “Taiwan, Province of China,” Taiwan will be absent from this conference and will express its strongest condemnation of Cameroon. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China, and the One-China Principle is a basic norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, refuse to acknowledge the One-China Principle, and make unreasonable trouble at relevant World Trade Organization meetings, which will only bring humiliation upon themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, a US intelligence community report assessed that China currently has no plan to “forcibly attack Taiwan” in 2027, and is more inclined to use non-military options to achieve unification. However, it is also continuously strengthening the PLA's military preparedness, and regards unification as an important condition for realizing national rejuvenation by 2049. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is Chinese Taiwan. The question of Taiwan is China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. The United States should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question.\n“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question, and resolving the Taiwan question and completing the reunification of the motherland is an inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and, with the utmost sincerity and the greatest efforts, strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification. But we will never allow national sovereignty and territorial integrity to be undermined, and we will never promise to renounce the use of force, reserving the option of taking all necessary measures. At present, the root cause of the complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait is that the DPP authorities collude with external forces to continuously engage in “Taiwan independence” provocations. In response, we will absolutely not tolerate and will not appease. We have the firm will, full confidence, and sufficient capability to defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757319.htm"],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Regarding the mainland’s formulation of the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress, Lo Wen-jia, Secretary-General of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said that the cross-Strait issue is a question of “democracy”; ethnicity is a problem of the past, while democracy is for the present and future. “We hope that one day in the future China will pass laws promoting democracy in China.” What is your comment on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait all belong to the Chinese nation and are all Chinese. The natural emotional bond and national identity that come from being “blood-related and mutually supportive” cannot be changed by anyone. Taiwan's future lies in national reunification, and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots is tied to the rejuvenation of the nation.\nRecently, the DPP authorities have repeatedly made unfounded comments and spread rumors and smears about the Law on Promoting National Unity and Progress. The purpose is to incite confrontation between the two sides of the Strait and create a “chilling effect” on the island. Cross-Strait relations are not a contest between systems; they are a struggle between unification and separation. For the sake of narrow party interests, and under the banner of “democracy,” the DPP authorities have carried out “green terror” and “Taiwan independence autocracy” on the island, abused the judiciary to persecute and oppress political opponents, and repeatedly trampled on democracy, impaired freedom and undermined the rule of law. What face do they have to talk about “democracy”?\nThe Straits Exchange Foundation was founded with the principle of being “Chinese, well-intentioned, and service-oriented.” We hope it will not forget this founding principle, will engage in less malicious political manipulation, and will do more things that are beneficial to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to the well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757317.htm"],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, regarding the South Korean electronic arrival card that labels Taiwan as “CHINA (TAIWAN),” Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities said that, in accordance with the principle of reciprocity, starting from March 1, the name “Korea” originally listed on Taiwan's “Alien Residence Certificate” will be changed to “South Korea,” and they demanded that the South Korean side respond before the 31st. If there is no…","Adhering to the one-China principle is righteous and reflects the trend of the times. No matter what small maneuvers the DPP authorities engage in, they cannot change the objective fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can they shake the basic pattern of the international community's adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te said at the so-called “Yushan Forum” on the island that Taiwan has always pursued peace and is actively enhancing its self-defense capabilities. In the future, whether in democratic governance, supply chain resilience, maritime security, or regional stability, Taiwan is willing to share responsibilities with countries of like-minded ideals, work together to solve problems, and be free from the threat…","The DPP authorities are accustomed to peddling \"Taiwan independence\" separatist fallacies under the name of \"forums\" and colluding with anti-China politicians to stage a farce of so-called \"international presence.\" Lai Ching-te brazenly deceives the outside world with the island's advantageous industries and once again plays the old tune of \"democracy versus authoritarianism,\" attempting to delude Taiwan residents and mislead international public opinion. This once again exposes their obstinate \"Taiwan independence\" nature and their sinister intent to escalate cross-Strait confrontation.\nIt must be stressed again that there is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. No matter how the DPP authorities try to win over external forces to stand by them and bolster their courage, they cannot change the fate of \"Taiwan independence\" being bound to fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be unified and certainly will be unified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, the situation in the Middle East has been turbulent. US President Trump called on several countries to send warships to escort vessels, but the call was met with indifference. Some people in the Green camp on the island urged the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to cater to the United States and send warships for escort missions, which drew harsh criticism from island public opinion as “harmful…","Some people on the island, for their own narrow political interests, willingly serve as pawns of external forces, and do not hesitate to harm the interests of the people of Taiwan and lead Taiwan into a dangerous situation. Their evil nature and sycophantic faces have already been spurned by the people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that recently a mainland coast guard vessel entered the so-called “restricted waters” of Dongsha Island. Taiwan's Coast Guard Administration said, “It does not rule out that China is using gray-zone harassment to test Taiwan's surveillance and response capabilities in the Dongsha waters.” What comments do you have on this?","Taiwan is part of China. Mainland coast guard vessels conducted law enforcement patrols in the waters near Dongsha Island to maintain normal navigation and operating order in the relevant waters and to safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. These actions are legitimate and lawful, and have been welcomed by fishermen on both sides. The DPP authorities are maliciously hyping this, attempting to incite confrontation between the two sides, and they will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Media reported that Tsai Cheng-yuan, a former KMT legislator and well-known current affairs commentator, was sentenced by the DPP authorities for “business embezzlement” and will soon be imprisoned. What is your comment?","Out of their “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have repeatedly manipulated the judiciary to persecute political opponents. They wantonly suppress and persecute figures from all sectors in Taiwan who do not identify with the DPP or support “Taiwan independence,” intensifying the “green terror.” This has aroused strong indignation among broad Taiwan residents, and public opinion on the island has also pointed out that Taiwan’s judiciary has become a political tool for the DPP authorities to implement dictatorial rule. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that those who commit many wrongs will bring about their own downfall. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces that act recklessly against the trend will surely be spurned by the people and face righteous judgment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Lai Ching-te recently put forward remarks lauding the “Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere” and glorifying Japan's colonial rule over Taiwan, causing an uproar in island public opinion. Experts and scholars on the island have cited one after another the crimes of massacre and sweeping campaigns committed by Japanese colonialists in Taiwan, criticizing the Lai authorities for distorting history for the sake of…","As is well known, during the half century in which Japan occupied and colonially ruled Taiwan, it brutally suppressed the anti-Japanese struggle of Taiwan compatriots, ruthlessly plundered Taiwan's resources through the so-called “agricultural Taiwan, industrial Japan” policy, forcibly implemented the “Kominka Movement,” and sought to change the national and ethnic identity of Taiwan's people. Its crimes are numerous and beyond count, bringing profound suffering to Taiwan compatriots, and it is the darkest page in Taiwan's history. Broad masses of Taiwan compatriots fought wave after wave to resist Japanese aggression and colonial rule, and hundreds of thousands of compatriots paid with their blood and lives. Lai Qingde disregards historical facts and vigorously glosses over and beautifies Japan's colonial rule. This is a distortion of history, a desecration of martyrs, and a betrayal of the nation. It once again exposes his ugly essence of “currying favor with Japan and selling out Taiwan” and plotting “independence” and provocation.\nWe will never allow anyone to speak on behalf of colonialism or to overturn the verdict on aggression, and we will never allow any external forces to interfere in the Taiwan question or in China's internal affairs. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must forever remember the glorious history of all Chinese sons and daughters, who paid enormous sacrifices to defeat the vicious Japanese militarists and to defend national sovereignty and national dignity with their blood and lives. We resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, join hands to advance the process of reunifying the motherland, and together create a bright future for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757318.htm"],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae recently met with US President Trump and stated that peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are indispensable elements of regional security and global prosperity. She expressed support for peacefully resolving cross-Strait issues through dialogue and opposed any party unilaterally changing the status quo by force or coercion. The DPP authorities expressed their gratitude.…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The greatest current threat to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the Lai Qingde authorities’ obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, colluding with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” We firmly oppose certain countries making remarks on the Taiwan question and interfering in China’s internal affairs. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rely on external forces to split the country is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The recent turmoil in the Middle East has disrupted energy exports from some countries in the region. A Taiwanese web portal launched an online poll on this topic, and more than 60 percent of the participants said they were most worried that the Middle East conflict would cause oil prices on the island to rise. What is your comment on this?","The situation in the Middle East continues to be turbulent, seriously threatening global energy security and affecting the economic development and livelihood improvement of all parties. It is reasonable for the island’s public to be worried about this. In fact, Taiwan’s oil prices have indeed risen recently. This also shows that without peace there is no development, and without peace there are no good days.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The Democratic Progressive Party has long used the banner of “non-nuclear” to win public support, with the slogan “Non-Nuclear Homeland by 2025.” However, Lai Ching-te recently said that the No. 2 and No. 3 nuclear power plants in Taiwan have conditions for restarting, and Taipower is already preparing the restart procedures. Commentary on the island points out that over the past 10 years, the DPP's opposition to…","“Anti-nuclear” and “Taiwan independence” are two “sacred tablets” that the DPP has long held on to. They are political tools it has long used to deceive the public, attack political rivals, and seek private gain. The former has already been proven wrong by facts, and the latter has likewise been proven to be a road to nowhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, the DPP authorities convened a so-called “All-of-Society Defense Resilience Committee Meeting” to discuss the overall plan for the 2026 “urban resilience exercise.” The exercise is expected to run from April to August this year, combined with the annual “Han Kuang Exercise,” with the goal of establishing a more complete “crisis response system.” What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking “independence,” which is the root cause of the tensions in the Taiwan Strait. The biggest current “crisis” in Taiwan is that the DPP authorities, going against the mainstream public opinion on the island that wants peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, are rushing down the wrong path of “seeking independence through force” and “relying on external forces to seek independence,” even willing to push Taiwan toward war. “Seeking independence through force” leads to a dead end. The DPP authorities' drills, one after another, are all just for show, pretentious posturing that overestimates their own ability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Lai Ching-te recently boarded Taiwan's self-built submarine “Hai Kun” and said the vessel is a strategic weapon for “countering blockade and deterring the mainland,” but public footage shows that the vessel's craftsmanship is crude, its quality is worrying, and it has safety hazards. Island public opinion has widely criticized the DPP authorities for using Taiwan people's hard-earned money to create a “political…","Rather than thinking about how to improve people's livelihood and well-being, the DPP authorities are exhausting people's resources and wasting money for the sake of “Taiwan independence” private interests, engaging in militarism. Their actions will not bring security to Taiwan, but will only make the situation in the Taiwan Strait more dangerous and perilous. There are also unspeakable deals such as dividing up spoils among interest groups, which Taiwan's people deeply detest. Seeking separation and confrontation has no way out, and fantasizing about “seeking independence through force” is even more self-overestimating. We have firm resolve, strong determination, and powerful capabilities to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes, safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","北京广播电视台记者","Recently, on the 12th anniversary of the so-called “Sunflower Student Movement,” Lai Ching-te said, “Facts have proven that Taiwan should go out to the world and not go back, in order to show greater resilience and competitiveness amid changes in the global economy.” What is your comment?","In 2014, the DPP instigated the so-called “Sunflower Student Movement,” obstructed the entry into force of the Cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement, and undermined the follow-up consultations on the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA), including the Cross-Strait Trade in Goods Agreement. Taiwan’s economic development has suffered greatly as a result. Twelve years have passed, and the DPP has not only shown no reflection, but has become even more obstinate and extreme. It has placed one party’s private political interests above the vital well-being of the people and the interests of industrial development. Under the banner of the so-called “going out to the world,” it cooperates with outside forces to hollow out Taiwan’s advantageous industries and forcibly pushes for “decoupling and severing supply chains” in cross-Strait economic relations. It persists obstinately on the evil path of selling out and harming Taiwan, and the result will only be even more grievous harm to Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation recently announced personnel changes, and reports say this will affect the foundation's exchanges with the mainland. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","In recent years, the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation has actively carried out cross-Strait exchange activities, which have received extensive attention and positive appraisal from all walks of life on both sides and have played a positive role in promoting exchanges between compatriots on both sides, especially young people, and in advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. On the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life to jointly strengthen exchanges and cooperation in all fields and personnel exchanges across the Strait, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”记者","First question: KMT Chairperson Zheng Liwen recently said that Taiwan does not need to choose sides between China and the US, and that on promoting the improvement of cross-Strait relations, the mainland side will release equal goodwill and replace confrontation with dialogue. What is your comment?\nSecond question: The founder of NVIDIA rarely spoke about the Taiwan Strait at the GTC developer conference, calling…","On the first question: Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. We are willing, on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang (KMT), to strengthen exchanges and contacts, maintain positive interaction, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nOn the second question: Industrial development cannot do without a peaceful and stable external environment, and this is even more true for the artificial intelligence and semiconductor industries, which are highly dependent on global industrial and supply chains. The reason relevant entrepreneurs have this concern is that the DPP authorities keep colluding with external forces to provoke “independence” and confrontation, causing tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait.\nOn the third question: Mainland TV dramas are popular in Taiwan and well loved by audiences on the island, which fully shows that Chinese culture is the common root and sense of belonging for both sides of the Strait. People naturally develop emotional resonance with outstanding film and television cultural works. This cultural identity and emotional bond cannot be severed by anyone. Compatriots on both sides are connected by blood and share the same culture, and cross-Strait film and television cooperation has a solid foundation and broad prospects. We actively support cross-Strait film and television cultural exchanges and cooperation, and we welcome artists, creators, and production institutions from both sides to collaborate and create more excellent film and television cultural works, creating more beautiful memories of the times and cinematic enjoyment for audiences on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-03-25","Zhu Fenglian","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Recently, a Taiwanese tech blogger attended Apple’s spring new product launch in Shanghai. In a short video they posted, they said, “happiness is so simple,” ate shengjianbao they had long missed, and ordered a favorite coffee. This drew attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait, and many mainland netizens left comments suggesting, “You should learn to use delivery platform coupons.” Previously, a…","Recently, a number of Taiwan internet celebrities active on social media have shared what they saw and experienced on the mainland, and netizens and fans have responded enthusiastically. This is a good thing for promoting mutual understanding and exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait.\nWe have stated many times that we warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, including internet celebrities and media professionals, to come to the mainland to visit and see for themselves. They can check in at mountains, plateaus, plains, coasts, glaciers and other landscapes across the mainland, experience everyday life in cities and villages where tradition and modernity blend, study at more than 500 mainland universities for further education, and pursue internships, employment and entrepreneurship in all walks of life to realize their dreams. We will continue to create more convenience for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, who come to the mainland, and we hope that more and more Taiwan compatriots will want to come to the mainland, love the mainland and visit the mainland often, to pursue a different life experience.\nI now announce the situation of the 10th Cross-Strait Knowledge Quiz campaign.\nOn March 9, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” published the questions for the 10th “Cross-Strait Knowledge Quiz” campaign, and netizens enthusiastically took part in answering. As of March 23, the top ten netizens who answered correctly and ranked highest in likes on their comments were, in order: “Good Mountains and Good Waters,” “Nezha,” “Yu Zailin,” “A Good Book,” “Yixianju,” “Wang Dafei Is Not Fat,” “Little Hero,” “Simple Love,” “continue,” and “Teacher Fish.” We extend congratulations to these ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite souvenir, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.”\nOn April 7, the WeChat account of the “Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council” will publish the questions for the 11th “Cross-Strait Knowledge Quiz” campaign. Everyone is welcome to take part enthusiastically in answering!\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202603/t20260325_12757324.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260325_12757315.htm"],[1,"2026-03-26","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, according to reports, the U.S. Office of the Director of National Intelligence recently released\n2026 Annual Threat Assessment of the U.S. Intelligence Community\n. It's assessed in the document that the Chinese mainland does not plan to attack Taiwan in 2027, and prefers to achieve unification without the use of force. In recent years, the U.S. side has been keen on peddling…","On your first question, the Taiwan question is purely an internal affair of China. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese, which brooks no foreign interference. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, be prudent on its words and actions concerning the Taiwan question, stop sending wrong signals to separatists seeking \"Taiwan independence\", and take concrete actions to maintain the overall stability of China-U.S. state-to-state and military-to-military relations.\nOn your second question, Taiwan is part of China. China will and must achieve reunification. It is an unstoppable historical trend that no one and no force can hold back. We will strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and utmost effort, but we make no promise to renounce the use of force. Should separatist forces seeking \"Taiwan independence\" dare to cross the red lines, they will only face a thunderous crackdown.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/03/china-260326-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16451420.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-03-26","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, PLANS Dongguan and PLANS Anqing completed their first formation training and live-fire training after being commissioned to the PLA Eastern Theater Command Navy. It's believed by some experts that the two latest Type 055 guided-missile destroyers will significantly enhance the capabilities of the PLA Navy in deterring and countering forces pushing for \"Taiwan independence\". What's your comment on this?","Achieving the complete reunification of China is the right thing to do. It represents the prevailing trend of the world and has the overwhelming support of the people. The PLA will continue to strengthen military training and enhance combat readiness. We will take resolute measures against separatist forces seeking \"Taiwan independence\" and stand against external interference with stronger capabilities and through more diversified means. There is no escape should the \"Taiwan independence\" armed forces put up a stubborn resistance.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/03/china-260326-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16451420.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-03-26","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lai Ching-te recently said at an event that Japan's colonization of Taiwan was intended to promote the Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere. His remarks were criticized as \"endorsing militarism in Japan\", sparking strong backlash in Taiwan. Do you have any comment on this?","Lai Ching-te's remarks, characterized by the absence of conscience and moral baseline, are truly shocking. His obsequious flattery of Japan, who once colonized Taiwan, is despicable. As is widely known, Japanese militarists, under the guise of \"co-prosperity\", committed atrocities such as killing, pillaging and the enslavement of people. Lai Ching-te has ignored Japanese aggressors' heinous crimes of slaughtering hundreds of thousands of Taiwan compatriots, and betrayed history to whitewash Japanese colonialism. Such a disgrace to the Chinese nation like him will be nailed to the pillar of shame.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/03/china-260326-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16451420.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-03-26","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Outcome documents of the recent US-Japan summit once again underlined that peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is an indispensable element. However, according to reports, a major U.S. arms package for Taiwan, which includes advanced interceptor missiles, is ready for President Trump's approval and could be signed after his visit to China. Do you have any comment on this?","It's a consistent and clear position of China in opposing U.S. arms sales to China's Taiwan region. The U.S. side needs to recognize the high sensitivity and severe consequences of arms sales to Taiwan, earnestly abide by the one-China principle and stipulations of the three China-US joint communiqués, exercise utmost caution in handling the Taiwan question, and take concrete actions to build a stable China-U.S. relations and preserve cross-Strait peace and stability.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/03/china-260326-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16451420.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-03-30","Mao Ning","CCTV","This morning, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs put on its website the decision to take countermeasures against member of Japan’s House of Representatives Keiji Furuya. Can you share more information on that?","The Taiwan question is at the core of China’s core interests and a red line that cannot be crossed. China has lodged serious protests with the Japanese side over the visit to China’s Taiwan region by Keiji Furuya, member of Japan’s House of Representatives. In disregard of China’s repeatedly stated position regarding the Japanese leader’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan, Keiji Furuya failed to reign in his wrong behavior, and continued to collaborate with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in taking provocative moves, which constitutes serious interference in China’s internal affairs and violation of China’s sovereignty and core interests. In response to his egregious moves and in accordance with the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law of the People’s Republic of China, China announced in the form of MFA decree countermeasures against Keiji Furuya as an action of warning and deterrence. China will take any additional punitive measure if deemed necessary in the future.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260330_11883723.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260330_11883715.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-30","Mao Ning","A Tarde","The Japanese ambassador in Brazil said in a recent interview that Japan is willing to settle its diplomatic strain with China about Taiwan and stabilize the relationship between the countries. Is the Chinese government open to start a dialogue about this issue with Japan?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair and the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-Japan relations. Dialogue should be built on the basis of respecting each other and honoring the agreements made. One cannot just talk about dialogue while at the same time eroding the other side’s core interests. The Japanese side needs to reflect on and correct its wrongdoings, abide by the four political documents between China and Japan and its own commitments, and take concrete actions to display sincerity for dialogue.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260330_11883723.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260330_11883715.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-03-30","Mao Ning","Reuters","The question is about the U.S. senators in Taiwan. We would like to seek a comment on this visit by four U.S. senators who are in Taiwan right now. How does China view the visit coming ahead of the expected visit by Trump to China? Also this morning China has announced sanctions against a Japanese lawmaker. Would China similarly sanction the four U.S. senators?","China has all along opposed official contact between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region, and has lodged serious protests with the U.S. side. The U.S. should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question prudently and properly, stop any form of official contact with China’s Taiwan region, stop sending any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and take concrete actions to uphold the overall China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. China’s position on issues related to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear. We will do what is necessary to firmly safeguard our sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202603/t20260330_11883723.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202603/t20260330_11883715.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-03-31","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","Beijing, March 30 (Xinhua) — Zhu Fenglian, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 30th that China’s countermeasures against relevant Japanese pro-Taiwan politicians are just actions based on Chinese law, defending national interests, and in line with international practice. The Taiwan question is the core of China’s core interests and an insurmountable red line. Furuya Keiji has persistently colluded with “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and stirred up trouble, seriously interfering in China’s internal affairs and seriously harming China’s sovereignty and core interests. We firmly oppose this and are taking countermeasures in accordance with the law, as a warning to others.\nA reporter asked: In response to the vile conduct of Japanese House of Representatives member Furuya Keiji concerning Taiwan, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced countermeasures against him today. What is your comment? Zhu Fenglian gave the above response.\nShe stressed that the DPP authorities, for the sake of party self-interest, servilely cling to external forces and, forgetting their roots and selling out the nation’s interests, will surely be judged by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202603/t20260331_12758190.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 1, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Fujian recently released the first batch of interim landmark achievements in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone, covering three categories: policies, projects, and platforms. Please introduce the relevant situation. What are the plans for advancing the construction of the demonstration zone next?","Since the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” were issued, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, the National Development and Reform Commission, and other departments, together with Fujian Province, have conscientiously implemented them, strengthened policy and institutional innovation, and the demonstrative effect of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone has gradually emerged and its influence has steadily expanded, with construction of the demonstration zone achieving phased progress.\nRecently, Fujian Province released the first batch of phased landmark achievements in building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. Among them, there are seven policy achievements, including: preliminarily forming a policy system for building the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone; a batch of Fujian-Taiwan enterprises and enterprises in Kinmen and Matsu regions earning “time-honored brand” recognition; expanding the range of product categories in the small-scale commodity trading markets for Taiwan; the Xiamen free trade zone leading in services for Taiwan compatriots; the “same-city living circles” of Xiamen-Kinmen and Fuzhou-Matsu advancing steadily; taking the lead in establishing a multi-tiered housing security system for Taiwan compatriots; and the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone building a “digital living circle” for cross-Strait social integration. There are five project achievements, including: normalized operation of the “small three links” restored after the epidemic; Fujian adding eight Taiwan farmers’ entrepreneurship parks, achieving full provincial coverage; issuing mainland China’s first local regulation specifically addressing Taiwan-related matters in the cultural field; the water supply project from Fujian to Kinmen becoming a model of cooperation in cross-Strait livelihood fields; and building the mainland’s largest iron ore transshipment port and storage and transportation base for Taiwan. There are five platform achievements, including: building the “first home” digital service platform for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises; the Straits Forum becoming the largest and most broadly participated cross-Strait civil exchange event; building a “one city, one feature” cross-Strait cultural exchange brand system for ancestral-homeland faith and customs; pioneering the joint formation of a Fujian-Taiwan provincial baseball team, which achieved results at the National Games; and establishing the “cross-Strait professional qualifications integrated service center,” among others.\nDuring the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will continue, together with relevant departments, to thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important exposition on work concerning Taiwan, the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, and the CPC Central Committee’s policy deployment on work concerning Taiwan. They will emphasize promoting integration through exchanges, integration through benefits, and integration through emotional bonds, and will use more concrete measures and greater effort to promote construction of the demonstration zone to higher standards and quality, support Fujian in taking greater strides in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development, and achieving greater development and more results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","Reportedly, after many years of joint efforts by both sides across the Strait, the ashes of several more martyrs who worked on the hidden front in Taiwan were returned to the mainland before this Qingming festival, to rest in their homeland. What is your comment?","Qingming Festival is a traditional Chinese festival for honoring ancestors and remembering the dead. Remember history, mourn the martyrs, and inspire the future. The heroic deeds of righteous people will not be forgotten by the people, and history will not forget them. Their ideals, convictions and strength of character will surely inspire compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strive unremittingly toward the early completion of the great cause of national reunification and the realization of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758543.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Lai Ching-te recently said that Taiwan has already integrated into the U.S.-led “non-red supply chain,” which can ensure Taiwan's competitive advantage in the future. Public opinion on the island, however, holds that Taiwan should deeply integrate into the mainland's robotics industry chain in areas such as chips, and seize the opportunities of the times. More and more Taiwan residents recognize that embracing…","The DPP authorities claim to be building a so-called “non-red supply chain,” which is nothing more than handing over Taiwan's industries to others in order to realize their scheme of “relying on outsiders to seek independence.” Cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation is mutually beneficial and has brought tangible benefits to Taiwan compatriots. More and more Taiwan compatriots see the convenience and opportunities brought by cross-Strait integrated development.\nThis year is the opening year of the 15th Five-Year Plan. During the 15th Five-Year Plan period, we will promote the deep integration of technological innovation and industrial innovation, and open up new frontiers in optimizing and upgrading traditional industries, cultivating and growing emerging industries, and proactively laying out future industries. This will certainly open up broader space for cross-Strait industrial cooperation and provide more opportunities for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises.\nWe always adhere to the concept that “Cross-Strait Are One Family,” deepen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and integrated development, and let compatriots on both sides share in the achievements and opportunities of Chinese-style modernization. We also welcome broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots to take part in the mainland's high-quality development and jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758548.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, Executive Yuan President Cho Jung-tai, when questioned about the fact that mainland pork imports must come from animals never fed ractopamine while Taiwan is not held to the same requirement, said, “Taiwan's food safety is a world standard, not a Chinese standard.” What is your comment?","On food safety, we adhere to putting the people and human life first. On the issue of lean meat essence, we adhere to the strictest food safety standards, and we strictly prohibit the import of any pork containing lean meat essence, earnestly protecting the people's lives and physical health.\nIn order to pursue the narrow interests of one party, the DPP authorities are willing to sacrifice the lives and health of Taiwan compatriots in order to “kneel to the US and sell out Taiwan.” Going against the wishes of the Taiwan public, they insist on opening the import of American pork containing ractopamine, which has triggered public outrage and opposition on the island. On the island, there have been a series of incidents, such as the controversy over American pork being “origin-washed” and the court victory of certain counties and cities in banning “ractopamine pork” from school meals. These fully show that the DPP authorities' approach is unpopular and that they should give the public a responsible explanation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","上海东方卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that, affected by the Middle East conflict, Taiwan’s oil supply is tight, which in turn has hit the plastic raw materials market, and recently a “plastic-hoarding wave” has swept the island, with a “medicine-shortage wave” possibly to follow. Public opinion on the island points out that, faced with these difficulties, the DPP authorities only say “oil and gas supplies are assured,” and their…","The so-called “no worries about oil and gas supply” put forward by the DPP authorities is nothing more than self-consolation over “inability to supply oil and gas,” and is even more a deception of the public. The DPP authorities have neither the will nor the ability to address the people's livelihood crisis on the island; they only keep evading. Taiwan's social sectors have long been strongly dissatisfied with this.\nAfter peaceful reunification, cross-Strait interconnection and full connectivity will be realized. The mainland's complete industrial system and stable market supply capacity will become the most solid support for Taiwan compatriots, fully able to make up for Taiwan's shortages in crude oil, natural gas, industrial raw materials, and other areas. No matter how turbulent the external situation becomes, we can provide timely guarantees for Taiwan's energy and resource security and the supply of industrial production materials, so that Taiwan compatriots will no longer have to worry about shortages of various energy sources and materials.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758547.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the mainland’s Taiwan policy of “high-quality advancement of cross-Strait integrated development” aims, through institutionalization, to have Taiwan compatriots integrate into their daily lives. By granting equal treatment, it seeks to draw Taiwan businesses and capital into its industrial supply chains, creating an illusion of…","The broad masses of Taiwan's people are our flesh-and-blood kin. For a long time, we have upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” actively promoted economic and cultural exchange and cooperation across the Strait, deepened integrated development across all fields, implemented the policy of equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots, and continually achieved new progress and results. This fully demonstrates our goodwill in benefiting and bringing well-being to Taiwan compatriots, and our sincerity in promoting peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. It has won high support and wide acclaim from Taiwan compatriots.\nDriven by its “Taiwan independence” nature and fearing that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will draw closer together, the DPP authorities deliberately incite confrontation and opposition across the Strait. They persistently slander, smear, and obstruct and sabotage everything that is conducive to developing cross-Strait relations and benefiting compatriots on both sides. This is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758549.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","In response to the egregious Taiwan-related conduct of Japanese Diet member Keiji Furuya, China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs recently announced countermeasures against him. Japan said China's countermeasures are “regrettable.” What is your comment?","I must stress again that the Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and an uncrossable red line. Furuya Keiji has openly interfered in China's internal affairs on the Taiwan question and seriously infringed on China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. The countermeasures China has taken are reasonable and lawful. Japan should deeply reflect on history, draw lessons from history, earnestly reflect on and correct its mistakes, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and must not allow anyone or any force to stir up trouble on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758546.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Jeffrey Sachs, professor at Columbia University in the United States, stated again in an interview with Taiwanese media that “believing the United States will ‘protect’ Taiwan is a very dangerous mistake.” This warning echoes the increasingly heated “doubt-the-US” discourse on the island. What comment do you have on this?","At present, many foreign experts and scholars have publicly spoken out, expressing concern and criticism over the DPP authorities' fawning on foreign powers, selling out of Taiwan and provocations, which harm the interests of Taiwan residents and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait. These rational voices have also received much attention and support.\nThe future of Taiwan and the security, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots have always depended on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland. More and more Taiwan residents are coming to realize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders cannot be relied upon. The DPP authorities' “relying on the US to seek independence” cannot buy security or protection; in the end, they will only become “discarded pawns,” bringing calamity now and lasting harm without end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Raymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan’s Taipei Office, said that Taiwan should overcome political divisions and quickly pass the “special defense budget,” in response to President Trump’s call that “defense spending should account for 5%.” Lai Ching-te, meanwhile, touted that “now is the most closely connected moment for Taiwan-U.S. economic relations.” What comment do you have on…","The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, be prudent in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop interfering in China's internal affairs.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities, for the selfish interest of “independence,” keep increasing the defense budget and willingly serve as the “ATM” of American arms dealers. Faced with blatant plunder by external forces, they not only offer no resistance at all but actively cater to them, even deliberately glorify it, deceiving public opinion and the people on the island. Their intentions are sinister and their conduct is shameful. The Lai Ching-te authorities' “seeking independence through force” and reckless gamble will only dig their own grave.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Regarding former Taiwan People's Party Chairman Ko Wen-je being sentenced at first instance to 17 years in prison and six years of deprivation of civil rights, the Mainland Affairs Council said that judicial cases in Taiwan are independently tried by judicial organs, “and there is no need for the mainland to point fingers, let alone to seize the opportunity to fish for united front benefits.” Meanwhile, an online…","In pursuit of political self-interest, the DPP authorities have relentlessly manipulated the judiciary to suppress and persecute political opponents. Their perverse actions have aroused growing opposition among the island's public. Right and wrong are judged by people's hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","Regarding the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office’s statement that, after peaceful reunification, it will assist Taiwan in building a high-speed rail around the island and east-west expressways, the Mainland Affairs Council said, “Such statements focus mainly on material interests and have limited appeal to Taiwan society, and cross-Strait differences cannot be resolved simply by construction.” What comment do…","All of our efforts to advance cross-Strait relations are aimed at enhancing the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides and realizing their aspiration for a better life. National reunification is an irresistible historical trend. Peaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development and bring tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. This is the greatest attraction. The sooner reunification is achieved, the more beneficial it will be for Taiwan's development and the more it will help Taiwan compatriots live better lives.\nFor the sake of its own party interests, the DPP authorities stubbornly pursue “independence” and refuse unification, which will only deprive the Taiwan public of the right to pursue a better life. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will actively join the righteous cause of advancing the reunification of the motherland and build our common homeland into an even better place.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Worshipping ancestors during Qingming is a Chinese national tradition shared by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the situation of joint ancestor worship by compatriots on both sides across the mainland during this year's Qingming.","Xuanyuan Huangdi is the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation. Every year during the Qingming season, the public memorial ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi held at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum is a traditional grand event for all Chinese descendants to trace their roots and forge their spirit. On April 5, the “Bingwu 2026 Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi,” co-hosted by the Shaanxi Provincial People's Government, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, and the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese, will be solemnly held at the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum in Huangling County, Yan'an City, Shaanxi Province. This year's ceremony includes nine programs, such as singing the “Ode to the Yellow Emperor,” reverently reading the memorial text, and offering a sacrificial ceremony with music and dance. During the public memorial period, multiple activities will also be held, including “Continuing the Cultural Lineage and the Path of Revival”—Huangling Roots-Seeking, and “Nine Regions Share One Root, Both Sides of the Strait Share One Lineage”—the 19th Cross-Strait Culture and Art Exhibition.\nFrom March 31 to April 5, the 2026 Cross-Strait Confucius Culture Spring Assembly was held in Qufu, Shandong. The Spring Assembly will host multiple activities, including Cross-Strait Education Lectures, Cross-Strait Youth Joint Confucius Worship, the Cross-Strait Ritual and Music Carnival cum Chongsheng Coming-of-Age Ceremony, the “Into Confucius” Taiwan Youth Journey Confucian Learning Experience Camp, the Cross-Strait Youth Hanfu Culture Exchange, and the Cross-Strait Analects Reading and Writing Conference. More than 900 Taiwan guests have been invited to attend.\nFrom April 2 to 4, the 10th Kaizhang Holy King Culture Festival will be held in Yunxiao, Zhangzhou, Fujian. Centered on the cultural core of “Kaizhang Great Auspiciousness, Roots and Kinship Across the Four Seas,” the festival has invited more than 200 Taiwan compatriots, descendants of the 87 Kaizhang surnames from around the world, and fellow villagers from home and abroad to jointly witness the grand ceremony and experience the bloodline kinship and cultural resonance that transcend regions. From April 4 to 5, the Luo Clan Ancestral Hall in Dongyuan, Quanzhou, and the Guo Clan Ancestral Temple in Baiqi will also invite clan members from the island to jointly hold ancestor worship activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260401_12758544.htm"],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","On whether Taiwan agricultural products should give up the mainland market, the DPP authorities said, “has been working hard to help expand stable overseas markets that are not subject to political interference.” What is your comment?","The DPP authorities obstinately hold to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly carry out provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” They treat promoting the “decoupling and severing of chains” in cross-Strait economic relations as a bargaining chip in economic and trade negotiations with the United States and as a “loyalty pledge” to show allegiance to the US. They obstruct the normal conduct of cross-Strait agricultural product trade, squeeze the room for development of Taiwan's agriculture, and damage the vital interests of Taiwan farmers.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share similar dietary structures and eating habits. The mainland has always been an important export destination for Taiwan agricultural products, and it has always been the best choice for Taiwan farmers and Taiwan-funded agricultural enterprises to take root and develop.\nAdhering to the concept that “Cross-Strait Are One Family,” we have adopted a series of measures, including expanding the range of products permitted for market access and implementing tariff reductions and exemptions. We have successively introduced a large number of special policy measures benefiting Taiwan farmers and agricultural enterprises, genuinely enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We welcome Taiwan farmers and Taiwan agricultural enterprises to come to the mainland to invest and start businesses, share opportunities and pursue development together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Taiwan media reported that Kinmen County Magistrate Chen Fu-hai recently led a delegation to visit the Mainland Affairs Council to explain issues such as “adding more flights on the mini three links” and “developing diversified tourist sources,” hoping the DPP authorities can understand Kinmen's needs and support its economic prosperity. What is your comment?","The “Mini Three Links” routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between people on both sides of the Strait, especially between Fujian and Taiwan, and have played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integration and development and enhancing the well-being of people on both sides. Compatriots on both sides are one family. We welcome our Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland via the “Mini Three Links” routes to take a look around, seek their roots and ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchanges and cooperation.\nThe mainland has always upheld the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” continues to make efforts to promote personnel exchanges across the Strait, tourism and other exchanges and cooperation in various fields, and extends goodwill. We will continue to advance work on tourism by mainland residents to Kinmen, and actively respond to the expectations and calls of Taiwan residents and the tourism industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","《团结报》记者","On whether cross-Strait religious exchanges can help both sides understand each other, the Mainland Affairs Council said the crux of cross-Strait issues lies not in whether mutual understanding exists, but in differing perceptions of “political systems and happy lives.” What is your comment?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture, and Chinese culture is the root and sense of belonging that connects the hearts of compatriots on both sides. Through exchanges in all fields across the Strait, including religion and folk beliefs, to enhance understanding, deepen comprehension, draw closer, and create the future together, is the shared voice of compatriots on both sides. Over the long term, this has played an important positive role in the development of cross-Strait relations.\nDriven by their “independence” agenda and personal selfish interests, the DPP authorities have repeatedly used institutional differences as an excuse to interfere with and obstruct exchanges across the Strait in all fields. Fearing that the “information cocoon” they carefully built will be broken, their scheme to deceive the public and divide the two sides has failed. People on the island are seeing this more and more clearly, and they are increasingly disgusted by the DPP authorities' despicable conduct.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Taiwan media reported recently that Chinese spouse Xu Chunying was indicted by the New Taipei District Prosecutors Office under the “Anti-Infiltration Act” and other offenses for allegedly “assisting a specific candidate in elections under instructions from the mainland.” The Mainland Affairs Council said, “The CCP’s intervention in and exploitation of Chinese spouse groups follows a highly organized chain of…","The Xu Chunying case is yet another vicious example of the DPP authorities' judicial persecution of mainland spouses. Recently, the DPP authorities have done everything they can to suppress and persecute mainland spouses, through intimidation, detention, sentencing and so on, too numerous to list. Mainland spouses have become the largest group of victims of the “green terror.” Why? Because they come from the mainland, and to the DPP authorities they are “to be captured and punished without fail.” Is this the “democracy and freedom” that the DPP authorities constantly talk about? I must emphasize that for the henchmen and accomplices involved in investigating, trying and judicially persecuting mainland spouses, we will punish them according to law, hold them accountable for life, and show no leniency whatsoever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","The Taiwanese film “The Sunshine Girls' Chorus” is set to enter the mainland market. The producer labeled the film with “Chinese Taiwan region” on social media, which sparked controversy on the island. Taiwan's culture authority said it had asked the production team to clarify as quickly as possible, and said: “The mainland has always used all kinds of means and methods for united front work. Beyond achieving…","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. “Chinese Taiwan” is a standard expression consistent with the one-China principle. The labeling by the relevant film industry operators reflects objective facts, is normal and reasonable, and is beyond reproach.\nThe entry of Taiwan films into the mainland market is a good thing that shares the broad opportunities of the mainland market and achieves mutual benefit and win-win results for the film and television industries on both sides. The DPP authorities are running a “green terror” campaign on the island, readily attaching the “united front” label to normal cross-Strait exchanges. This fully exposes their sinister intent to restrict and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions and to incite cross-Strait opposition and confrontation. Their actions harm the interests of Taiwan businesses and the public and are unpopular. We have consistently supported cross-Strait film, television and cultural exchange and cooperation, and we welcome Taiwan film and television operators to provide more excellent works for compatriots on both sides. We will firmly safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan businesses. No political suppression can block the momentum of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”记者","Recently, multiple achievements in the construction of the PLA's unmanned combat systems were disclosed, and a series of “new-quality combat capability” equipment appeared together, drawing wide attention on the island. Public opinion holds that this equipment will enhance the PLA's ability to deter and strike “Taiwan independence.” What is your comment?","We resolutely crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist acts and foreign interference. Our will to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity is as firm as a rock, and our capabilities are growing ever stronger.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Reportedly, the mainland-linked flag-of-convenience cargo ship “Hong Tai 58,” registered in Togo, was found to have dragged and severed the No. 3 submarine cable between Taiwan and the Penghu. A mainland captain surnamed Wang was sentenced to three years' imprisonment with civil damages. Captain Wang, however, denies the act of damaging the cable. What is your comment?","After investigation by public security authorities, Taiwan residents Jian Wensheng and Chen Shunjin operated vessels including the “Hong Tai No. 58” and for a long time smuggled frozen goods into the mainland. In December 2025, public security authorities issued a reward notice for these two individuals, hoping that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will actively provide clues to illegal and criminal activities.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding the facts of the case, shield and condone smuggling crimes. They smear the “Hong Tai No. 58,” which was manipulated by a Taiwanese smuggling gang, as a flag-of-convenience vessel with a mainland background, and use a mainland-born captain whom they directed to engage in political manipulation. Their methods are despicable, and they will certainly meet with the joint opposition of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Taiwan's defense chief Koo Li-hsiung recently said, when asked whether US arms sales to Taiwan will proceed as scheduled, that Taiwan has received a letter from the US assuring its willingness to sell, that it is in close communication with the US on the specific details of the arms sales, and that it has received no notice of a delay. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities, scheming to “rely on the United States to pursue independence” and “use force to pursue independence,” beg for false “protection” from external forces. This will plunge Taiwan into danger, and in the end they will only be like an egg striking a stone, seeking their own destruction.\nI must stress again that we firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question, stop selling arms to Taiwan, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","On the mainland's position that the one-China principle is the political premise for Taiwan's participation in WTO activities, Taiwan's foreign affairs department said, “Taiwan joined the WTO under the name ‘Separate Customs Territory,’ and there is no unilateral claim by China.” What is your comment?","Regarding the participation of the Taiwan region of China in international organization activities, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, and the World Trade Organization is no exception. The DPP authorities keep spreading “Taiwan independence” fallacies and use crude tactics to stage a farce on the WTO platform. This cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can it shake the international community's pattern of adhering to the one-China principle. Their conduct truly is like a mayfly trying to shake a tree, overestimating its own strength.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","台湾TVBS电视台记者","KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun is about to visit the mainland. What does the mainland side expect? What topics will the two sides focus on?","Since assuming the chairmanship, KMT Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun has repeatedly expressed her wish to visit the mainland. To promote KMT-CPC relations and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the CPC Central Committee and General Secretary Xi Jinping have welcomed and invited KMT Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun to lead a KMT delegation to visit Jiangsu, Shanghai, and Beijing from April 7 to 12. Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun expressed thanks and gladly accepted the invitation. We will communicate with the KMT side regarding Chairwoman Cheng Li-wun's visit and make appropriate arrangements.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","Chairperson Zheng Liwen of the Kuomintang will soon visit the mainland. May I ask when the mainland side will arrange for her to meet General Secretary Xi Jinping? The Taiwan Strait has long been viewed as a source of regional instability. What message does the mainland side hope this invitation visit will send to the outside world? Can we expect cross-Strait exchanges between the KMT and the CPC to return to…","I will answer your series of questions comprehensively.\nWe attach great importance to the visit to the mainland by the Kuomintang (KMT) delegation led by KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun, and we will properly arrange all activities.\nThe KMT Chairperson leading a delegation to visit the mainland for the first time in 10 years is an important part of exchanges and dialogue between the KMT and the Communist Party of China (CPC) under the new circumstances. It conforms to the needs of cross-strait relations development, the common wishes of compatriots on both sides, and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation. Strengthening exchanges and dialogue between the KMT and the CPC will have an important positive impact on maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and interactions and maintain positive interaction with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, including the KMT, to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and benefit compatriots on both sides.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. We believe that political parties and political figures who follow public opinion and do what they should do will be recognized and supported by the people of Taiwan.\nBoth sides of the Strait are Chinese and are one family. Matters across the Taiwan Strait are internal family affairs of compatriots on both sides, and they should naturally be discussed and handled by family members. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait are fully capable and wise enough to resolve their own affairs and to safeguard and build their own homeland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: please have the spokesperson introduce the arrangements for the visit to the mainland by Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang. What outcomes are expected? Second question: regarding the Penghu-registered fishing boat “Da Jin Man No. 8,” which is suspected of being detained in mainland waters for illegally selling fuel, please have the spokesperson introduce the current situation.","Question one. The CPC Central Committee and General Secretary Xi Jinping invited Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Chinese Kuomintang, to lead a delegation on a visit. This will point the way, open up broad space, and inject strong momentum for the development of relations between the two parties and across the Strait in the correct direction. It reflects the sense of responsibility of the Chinese Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China in seeking peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation. We always uphold the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” and will continue to support personnel exchanges across the Strait and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides, and realize their aspirations for a better life.\nQuestion two. The relevant departments are verifying the situation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","After the news of Cheng Li-wun's visit to the mainland was announced, a U.S. State Department spokesperson said: “Meaningful cross-strait exchanges should focus on dialogue without preconditions between mainland leaders and Taiwan's democratically elected government, which also includes interaction between the mainland and other Taiwan political parties. The United States supports cross-strait dialogue and…","Taiwan is Chinese Taiwan, and the Taiwan question is an internal affair of China. Both sides of the Strait are Chinese, and are one family. Matters across the Strait should naturally be discussed and handled by the family members. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait have full wisdom and ability to resolve their own affairs and to protect and build their own homeland.\nHistory and reality prove that as long as we uphold the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” the Taiwan Strait can remain peaceful and stable, and Taiwan compatriots will benefit. Conversely, the Taiwan Strait will become tense and turbulent, and the interests of Taiwan compatriots will suffer. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work together with the parties, groups, and all sectors of society in Taiwan, including the Chinese Kuomintang, to strengthen exchanges and interactions, maintain positive interaction, pursue peace in the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-01","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Regarding the recent dispute over the appointment of Chinese spouse Li Zhenxiu and the Xu Chunying case, the mainland side has stated that it will punish according to law, and hold accountable for life, those who act as henchmen and accomplices in investigating, prosecuting and persecuting Chinese spouses, and will show no leniency. Will the mainland side publicly announce, in the near future, accountability…","The mainland is the maternal home of the vast number of Chinese spouses, and we deeply care about the lives and circumstances of the Chinese spouse community on the island. When storms come, we must, both emotionally and rationally, shelter them from the wind and rain. For the “Taiwan independence” henchmen and accomplices who persecute Chinese spouses, we will show no leniency; we will hold them accountable according to law and punish them severely.\nToday’s press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260401_12758538.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-04-07","Mao Ning","AFP","My question is about Cheng Li-wun visiting the mainland this week. Her visit is taking place around a month before Donald Trump is due in China. And there are some suggestions that Trump and President Xi will discuss U.S. arms sales to Taiwan when they meet. So first I wondered if you could tell us if Cheng Li-wun and President Xi are going to meet and whether they would discuss arms sales to Taiwan?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Cross-Strait relations are not a foreign affairs issue. China has always opposed military contact between the U.S. and the Taiwan region. This position remains clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260407_11887704.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260407_11887644.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 8, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Questions are now open.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Regarding Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun’s visit to the mainland with a delegation, a spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office previously said that cross-Strait matters are family affairs and should be discussed and handled among family members. The Mainland Affairs Council responded that the mainland’s statement highlights its intention of “opposing intervention” and “internalizing the cross-Strait issue.”…","Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and we are all Chinese and members of one family. Cross-Strait affairs are a family matter for compatriots on both sides and should be discussed and handled by family members. Compatriots on both sides have ample wisdom and ability to solve their own problems. On the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work with Taiwan's political parties, groups and individuals, including the Chinese Kuomintang, to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation. The DPP authorities, out of selfish “Taiwan independence” interests, engage in slander and smears, which is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759510.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Regarding KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun's visit to the mainland with a delegation, a YouTube poll shows that 60% of netizens believe the visit has a positive impact on the Blue camp's county and city magistrate elections this year, giving it a boost. What is your comment?","Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun led the KMT delegation to visit the mainland and conducted dialogue and exchanges on the common political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” This conforms to the mainstream public opinion on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. It is of great significance for promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and safeguarding the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and it will be recognized and supported by Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759509.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","During Qingming, many Taiwan compatriots crossed the Strait to various parts of the mainland to worship ancestors and reunite with relatives and friends. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Honoring the departed and remembering ancestors, respecting forebears, and cherishing one's hometown are excellent traditions of the Chinese nation. During the Qingming holiday, many Taiwan compatriots took part in worship activities on both sides of the Strait. Some came to Shaanxi to attend the Bingwu (2026) Qingming Public Memorial Ceremony for Xuanyuan Huangdi and, together with mainland compatriots, expressed their reverence and gratitude toward Xuanyuan Huangdi, the humanistic ancestor of the Chinese nation. Others returned to ancestral homelands on the mainland to carry out ancestor visits, root-seeking, and clan fellowship activities, fully reflecting that “both sides of the Strait are one family.” Here, I would like to highlight several ancestor worship activities to be held in Fujian.\nFrom April 10 to 11, more than 40 members of the Huang Clan Association of Miaoli County, Taiwan, will travel to Shaowu in Nanping to visit ancestors and seek roots. Huang clan members from both sides will jointly worship Huang Qiao Gong and revisit the family instructions and family rules of Huang Qiao, continuing blood ties and kinship.\nOn April 12, an ancestor worship event for the Chen Clan of Fengshan, Chiayi, Taiwan, will be held in Nan'an City, Quanzhou. More than 200 relatives from both sides, including more than 70 Taiwan compatriots, will take part in ancestor worship, genealogy matching, clan fellowship, and other activities.\nOn April 17, the 2026 “Mazu Returns Home to Visit Her Mother” event will be launched on Meizhou Island in Putian. Representatives of nearly 100 Mazu cultural institutions, including more than 60 Taiwan Mazu cultural groups, and nearly 10,000 guests will jointly pay homage to Mazu and pray for peace together. On the same day, the “Mazu Hometown · Youth Vision” Putian–Taiwan University Youth Meizhou Island Video Creation Camp will be held, with more than 10 university students from both sides of the Strait gathering on Meizhou to hold a short video creation competition.\nIn addition, the 10th Pingtan Cross-Strait Workers' Cycling Race cum the 6th Cross-Strait Workers' Cycling Tour will be held in Pingtan, Fujian, from April 18 to 19. More than 1,000 cyclists from both sides are expected to take part. The race course combines features such as the Pingtan coastal highway and island fishing villages. Athletes will take in island scenery through both competitive racing and leisurely riding, enjoy the fun of cycling, and deepen compatriot friendship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Reportedly, during the Qingming Festival, the “mini three links” passenger shipping routes saw a peak of Taiwan compatriots returning home to worship ancestors. Please have the spokesperson introduce the relevant situation.","The “Small Three Links” passenger shipping routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between people on both sides, especially between Fujian and Taiwan. During the Qingming Festival holiday, passenger traffic on the “Small Three Links” routes peaked. Relevant port units strengthened passenger service and assurance, reinforced organization and dispatch, and opened “green channels” to ensure that “Small Three Links” passenger ships travel with priority. The “Family Reunion” kinship channel for border inspection clearance at the Xiamen-Kinmen “Small Three Links” port and the convenient dedicated channel for “large baggage” are open around the clock. The Fuzhou-Matsu “Small Three Links” port added 6 round-trip ship sailings to meet passenger travel needs. The Quanzhou-Kinmen “Small Three Links” port, together with the Fujian-Taiwan Origin Museum, held “Qingming Roots-Seeking, Cross-Strait Common Origin” activities at the port and a Fujian-Taiwan roots-seeking cultural exhibition to strengthen emotional resonance among compatriots on both sides. According to statistics, from April 1 to 6, the “Small Three Links” routes carried a total of 34,100 passenger trips, up 9.49% year on year.\nCompatriots on both sides are one family, and we welcome more Taiwan relatives to come to the mainland through the “Small Three Links” routes to seek roots, worship ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759505.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","The 6th China International Consumer Products Expo will be held in Haikou, Hainan. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan enterprises at this Expo.","The 6th China International Consumer Products Expo will be held in Haikou, Hainan Province, from April 13 to 18. It is understood that this year's Expo sets up a Taiwan Characteristic Exhibition Area for the first time, where 20 Taiwan enterprises will bring quality products such as distinctive cultural and creative items, biotech and health products, fashion goods and selected foods. The mainland market, with a population of over 1.4 billion, is large enough and is the most promising consumer market in the world. We welcome more quality Taiwan products to enter the mainland market, and we will continue to build more market-oriented and professional platforms so that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises can share the opportunities of mainland development and put down roots in the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","The mainland motorcycle brand “Zhang Xue Motorcycles” won the championship at the World Superbike Championship, sparking heated discussion among netizens on the island. Many believe that the quality of mainland manufacturing has reached world-class standards, boosting the confidence of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, and that industries across the Strait should deepen cooperation to further build and…","As everyone can see, robots, drones, new energy vehicles, and motorcycles—more and more outstanding mainland brands and products are going global, drawing worldwide attention, gaining widespread recognition, and becoming consumers' first choice. Relying on a complete industrial system and a deep industrial foundation, mainland manufacturing continues to set new records. During the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, we will continue to focus on promoting high-quality development and building a modern industrial system with advanced manufacturing as its backbone. The mainland is a fertile ground for innovators and entrepreneurs, opening up broader space for cross-Strait industrial cooperation. We warmly welcome compatriots and Taiwan companies to take root and develop on the mainland, deepen cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and integrated development, and jointly grow the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759506.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan called on the mainland side to lift the restrictions it unilaterally imposed starting in April 2020 and to resume admitting mainland students to pursue degrees in Taiwan. It said that Taiwan has always welcomed mainland students, but because of mainland policy restrictions, the number of new mainland students admitted to Taiwan has been zero for five consecutive…","This claim is a pure distortion of black and white, and a fabrication and smear. In recent years, the DPP authorities have obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and have disregarded the strong desire of Taiwan's education sector and young students to take part in cross-Strait exchanges. They have severely restricted and suppressed cross-Strait education exchange and cooperation. On one hand, the DPP authorities prohibit island universities and colleges from engaging in exchange and cooperation with Jinan University, Beihang University and 10 other universities. They use various pretexts to obstruct cross-Strait education exchange and cooperation at all levels, from primary and secondary schools to universities, and impose various unreasonable restrictions and unfair treatment on mainland students studying in Taiwan. On the other hand, the DPP authorities “check the water meters” of some Taiwan university presidents, deans and teachers who come to the mainland for exchanges, cut their funding and block their projects, and intensify the “green terror.” These political manipulations seriously harm the normal conduct of cross-Strait education exchange. We advise the DPP authorities to listen more to the will and sentiment of the people on the island and to manipulate less and shift blame and shirk responsibility less.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The AI short film “Rescue a Fox on the Snowy Mountain” became a hit on the mainland and then spread to Taiwan. “Have you ever rescued a fox on a snowy mountain?” became a catchphrase on major social platforms across the island, with netizens and well-known entertainers producing all kinds of derivative works. What is your comment?","Clever and interesting forms of creation and exchange have been loved and spread by netizens on both sides of the Strait, showing that compatriots on both sides share the same Chinese cultural heritage and are naturally in tune in cultural aesthetics and tastes, resonating highly. The rapid development of mainland artificial intelligence technology has provided new tools and new space for netizens on both sides to express their creativity and innovation, inspiring enthusiasm and vitality for joint creation. We are glad to see netizens on both sides make good use of new technology for vivid and interesting creative expression and interaction, and we are glad to see compatriots on both sides exchange more, visit more often, and develop together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The US will impose a 100% high tariff on imported pharmaceuticals. Although the DPP authorities claim to have secured preferential treatment, the list of US tariff preferences does not mention Taiwan. What is your comment?","The United States always adheres to “America First” and cares only about “American interests.” More and more facts are making Taiwan's residents realize that U.S. predatory seizure does not reason, and that the servile begging of the DPP authorities earns no pity whatsoever. The so-called “preferential treatment” of the DPP authorities is in fact U.S. bullying and squeezing of Taiwan, and the DPP authorities' sycophantic submission at the cost of Taiwan's economy, which harbors the DPP's malicious intent to “rely on the United States to pursue independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759507.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said that the US has become Taiwan's largest overseas investment destination and export market, that Taiwan's investment in the mainland has dropped to 3.7%, and that Taiwan will continue to deepen cooperation with the US to safeguard global supply chain security. What is your comment?","For the sake of its one-party political self-interest, the Lai Qingde authorities keep pledging loyalty to the US and attempt to push for “decoupling and severing chains” in cross-Strait economic relations, damaging the interests and well-being of the island's industries and people. Their brazen claim of “deepening cooperation with the US and safeguarding the security of global supply chains” is, in essence, “relying on the US to sell out Taiwan,” further exposing how they will stop at nothing and plot meticulously to “rely on outsiders to seek independence.”\nAccording to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, in the first two months of this year, the total volume of cross-Strait trade maintained a steady growth momentum, reaching US$52.54 billion. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan grew by 28.1%, and mainland imports from Taiwan grew by 19%. This fully shows that cross-Strait economic ties cannot be decoupled or severed, and that deepening cross-Strait integrated development accords with the common interests of compatriots on both sides and with market rules. The Lai Qingde authorities' scheme to undermine cross-Strait economic ties is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759508.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, the “joint statement” issued after talks between Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi Sanae and French President Macron emphasized the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and urged the peaceful resolution of cross-Strait issues through constructive dialogue. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities expressed gratitude. What comment do you have on this?","Resolving the Taiwan question is China’s own affair and brooks no foreign interference. The so-called “joint statement” makes irresponsible remarks on the Taiwan question and interferes in China’s internal affairs, which we firmly oppose. Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle and stop sending erroneous signals to “Taiwan independence” forces. The DPP authorities’ attempt to rely on external forces to split the country is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan's agriculture authorities said that, regarding Taiwan's commitment not to impose special safeguard (SSG) tariffs on U.S. agricultural products, they assess the impact on the island's industries as limited. This has caused widespread concern in the island's agricultural sector that an influx of U.S. agricultural products will seriously impact related industries such as chicken, pork, and beef, and…","Faced with U.S. economic bullying, the DPP authorities have consistently compromised, conceded, flattered, and fawned, allowing the United States to take whatever it wants and turning Taiwan into a dumping ground for U.S. agricultural products. This will inevitably seriously impact Taiwan's agricultural product market, affect the incomes of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery producers, and inevitably cause concern among the island's agricultural sector and consumers. The DPP authorities' “kneeling to America and selling out Taiwan” knows no bottom line. What it harms is the interests of Taiwan residents, and what it sacrifices is the future of Taiwan's agriculture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260408_12759504.htm"],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Recently, CNN in the United States reported that military pressure in the Taiwan Strait has risen, prompting some Taiwan residents to inquire about emigrating overseas and to plan the transfer of their assets abroad. In response, a DPP politician said, “Only preparing for war can prevent war; we call on the public to give priority to defending Taiwan.” What comment do you have on this?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and collude with external forces to provoke “independence” schemes, causing tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities extensively promote “preparing for war to seek independence” and “the whole populace as soldiers,” binding the public to the separatist “Taiwan independence” war chariot, which is why Taiwan residents are so worried. It must be pointed out that only by adhering to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus” can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be substantively guaranteed, and only then can Taiwan compatriots have good lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Kuan Bi-ling, head of Taiwan's “Ocean Affairs Council,” said that mainland official vessels have continuously “harassed” Taiwan's main island and outlying islands, “which is both unfair to the people on both sides and does not help improve cross-Strait relations.” What is your comment?","These remarks completely contradict the facts and are purely malicious smears and hype. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and deliberately scheme for “independence” and provocation, which is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan is part of China. The mainland's coast guard and other departments conduct law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters to maintain normal navigation and operating order and to safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the strait. This is legitimate and lawful, and it has been welcomed by fishermen on both sides of the strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that recently a junior high school student in New Taipei City posted a five-star red flag on campus, wrote phrases such as “Long live China” and “Unify Taiwan,” and shouted slogans in the classroom. The New Taipei City Education Bureau said the school had removed the postings, that this was an individual student's behavior, that the school had followed up with the student and provided…","Realizing the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation is the shared aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. More and more Taiwan compatriots, including young people, recognize that the two sides must and will unify. This is a historical trend that the DPP authorities cannot stop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-08","Zhu Fenglian","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Reportedly, KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun is expected to travel to Beijing on the 9th. Please have the spokesperson introduce the itinerary in Beijing. Will General Secretary Xi Jinping meet with Cheng Li-wun on the 10th? What is the current progress of the arrangements?","We attach great importance to the visit of KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun and the KMT delegation. We will properly arrange the activities for the delegation's itinerary in Jiangsu, Shanghai, and Beijing.\nToday's press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260408_12759515.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-04-09","Zhang Xiaogang","","近期全球最大货运无人机“长鹰-8”首飞成功，岛内舆论称这可能成为解放军新的“反航母利器”。此外岛内广泛关注解放军无人作战体系建设成果，认为这将提升震慑与打击“台独”的能力。请问对此有何评论？","","","http://eng.chinamil.com.cn/2025xb/V_251452/16455038.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16454112.html",0,3,1,""],[0,"2026-04-10","Mao Ning","NHK","The Japanese government published its annual diplomatic bluebook today. Compared with last year, its description of China has changed from one of the most important bilateral relations to an important neighbor. How does the foreign ministry view this change in the wording?","The root cause for the current situation in China-Japan relations is that Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi made the erroneous remarks on Taiwan and breached Japan’s commitments, which erodes the political foundation of China-Japan relations and challenges the postwar international order. The Japanese side needs to abide by the four political documents between China and Japan and its own commitments, reflect on and correct its wrongdoings, and take concrete actions to uphold the political foundation of China-Japan relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260410_11890053.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260410_11889948.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-04-14","Guo Jiakun","China News Service","The spokesperson for the ROK foreign ministry said this afternoon that the ROK government has consistently reaffirmed its respect for the 1992 joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the ROK and the subsequent joint communiqués, in which the government promised to respect the Chinese position that there is only one China and Taiwan is part of China, and the ROK government…","We would like to reiterate that the joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the ROK explicitly states that the government of the Republic of Korea recognizes the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China, and respects China’s position that there is but one China and Taiwan is part of China. ROK President Lee Jae Myung clearly expressed his respect for the one-China position in his interview with Chinese media during his state visit to China early this year.\nTaiwan is part of China. It is only right to list it as “China (Taiwan).” China’s position on the Taiwan question is clear and consistent. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is also the political foundation for all countries, including the ROK, and for relevant international organizations to establish and develop relations with China. We hope the ROK government fully recognize that the Taiwan question bears on the national sentiment of over 1.4 billion Chinese people, uphold the spirit of the joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and the ROK, adhere to the one-China principle, oppose “Taiwan independence” in any form, and work with China to promote the sound and steady development of China-ROK relations through concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260414_11891740.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260414_11891610.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 15, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","On April 10, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Cheng Li-wun, Chair of the Kuomintang, in Beijing and delivered an important speech. Please explain the spirit of the speech. How will the Taiwan Affairs Office implement it?","On April 10, General Secretary Xi Jinping of the Communist Party of China met in Beijing with a delegation of the Kuomintang of China led by KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun and delivered an important speech on advancing relations between the two parties and cross-Strait relations. This was the first meeting between the leaders of the two parties in 10 years, opening a new chapter in exchanges between the KMT and the CPC and carrying significant meaning. General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech takes into account the overall strategic situation of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and the once-in-a-century changes unfolding across the world, grasps the trends of history and of global development, and focuses on the overall interests and long-term development of the Chinese nation. It is lofty in vision, rich in content, and filled with deep feeling. It has further pointed out the direction for the development of cross-Strait relations, and is the fundamental guideline and action plan for doing well the work concerning Taiwan in the new era.\nIn his speech, General Secretary Xi Jinping put forward four opinions on the development of cross-Strait relations, profoundly explaining the major guidelines and policies for promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the great cause of national reunification under the new circumstances. He revealed the great significance of the fact that compatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and are all Chinese, inheriting and promoting Chinese culture, strengthening correct identity, and promoting heartfelt bonds among compatriots. He revealed that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and expressed our firm determination to resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” secession and external interference, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and safeguard the common homeland of the Chinese nation. He demonstrated our sincerity and goodwill in continuing to uphold the concept of cross-Strait families being one family, promoting cross-Strait exchanges and integration, and enhancing the people’s livelihood and well-being of compatriots. He inspired compatriots on both sides of the Strait to unite and strive together, and to join hands to create a beautiful future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nGeneral Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech links history, the present, and the future, demonstrates the vision, breadth of mind, and bearing of a world-class leader, and embodies the mission, sentiment, and historical responsibility of seeking peace for both sides of the Strait, seeking well-being for compatriots, and seeking national rejuvenation. It is filled with care and concern for Taiwan compatriots and deep affection, has aroused strong resonance among Chinese people at home and abroad and enthusiastic responses from the international community, and will certainly have a major and far-reaching impact on the development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech, adhere to the “1992 Consensus,” broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” secession and external interference, promote peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will follow the trend of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, and join us in firmly safeguarding the common homeland of the Chinese nation, jointly creating lasting well-being for the Chinese nation, and sharing the great glory of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760808.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun has led a KMT delegation on a visit to the mainland that has drawn great attention. How do you evaluate this visit by Cheng Li-wun and her delegation? What results were achieved? What impact will it have on the future development of cross-Strait relations?","At the invitation of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and General Secretary Xi Jinping, KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun led a KMT delegation to visit Jiangsu, Shanghai, and Beijing from April 7 to 12. On the morning of the 10th, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Chairperson Cheng in Beijing and delivered an important speech, which pointed out the direction for the development of party relations and cross-strait relations and has had a major and far-reaching impact on the Taiwan Strait and the international community. The leaders of the KMT and the CPC meeting again after 10 years is of great significance to the development of party relations and cross-strait relations.\nTo promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee, in consultation with relevant departments and under authorization, issued ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchange and cooperation, which have been widely praised and warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” the KMT and the CPC have strengthened exchanges and dialogue and maintained positive interaction. They adhere to promoting spiritual affinity through correct identity, to safeguarding our common home through peaceful development, to enhancing the well-being of the people through exchange and integration, and to achieving the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through unity and struggle. This conforms to the historical trend, the common voice of compatriots on both sides, and the overall interests of the Chinese nation. It is conducive to pursuing peace for the two sides, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation, and it firmly keeps the future of cross-strait relations in the hands of the Chinese people themselves. No matter how the international situation and the situation in the Taiwan Strait change, the general direction of human development and progress will not change, the major trend of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation will not change, and the great tide of compatriots on both sides growing closer and coming together will not change. This is a law of history, and we have full confidence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760807.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月潭天”新媒体记者","On April 12, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office, under authorization, released ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchange and cooperation, which were welcomed and affirmed by all sectors in Taiwan. Please provide further explanation of the ten policy measures from the spokesperson. Measures such as allowing Taiwan agricultural and fishery products that meet inspection and quarantine standards to be…","We adhere to the concept that “Cross-Strait Are One Family,” insist on promoting people's well-being through exchange and integration, and aim to let compatriots on both sides live better lives. Focusing on the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots, we have introduced ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. The ten policy measures cover cross-Strait party-to-party exchanges, youth exchanges, and areas such as the economy, livelihood, and culture and tourism. They are another important step in our efforts to promote cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and to enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots. They accord with the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides for peace, development, exchange and cooperation, and they respond to the enthusiastic expectations of the people on the island.\nNext, we will work with relevant departments and localities to carry out the implementation of the relevant policy measures in detail, so that compatriots on both sides will soon benefit and share in the advantages. We hope the DPP authorities will heed the will of the people on the island and respond to the appeals of industry. We hope they will lift all kinds of artificial restrictions as soon as possible and remove obstacles to normalizing and routinizing cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760805.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the mainland's release of ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, the DPP authorities said that several of these measures amount to “united front coercion tactics that instrumentalize exchanges and weaponize economics and trade.” What is your comment?","Whenever the mainland introduces measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, the DPP authorities smear all of them; whatever is beneficial to enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they strongly oppose. This approach has been mocked by Taiwan media as a “knee-jerk reaction,” a conditioned reflex, and has drawn widespread criticism and opposition from all sectors of Taiwan society. We advise the DPP authorities to listen more closely to public opinion on the island, to do more things that promote cross-strait exchange and cooperation, rather than acting as enemies of the people and blocking the people from benefiting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760801.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","At earlier press conferences, the spokespersons of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office explained respectively that, among the “seven betters” for Taiwan after peaceful reunification, “energy and resource security will be better” and “infrastructure construction will be better,” which drew great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. What explanation does the spokesperson have regarding…","Developing cross-Strait relations and achieving the reunification of the motherland has as one of its main goals allowing compatriots on both sides of the Strait to live better lives. We have consistently upheld the concept that across the Strait we are one family, and have actively done real things, good things and difficult things for Taiwan compatriots. Peaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development, will bring tangible benefits to the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and will open up a better future for cross-Strait relations.\nDuring the 14th Five-Year Plan period, the mainland's livelihood guarantees became solid and stable. We won the battle against poverty, historically resolving the problem of absolute poverty, and the goal of building a moderately prosperous society in all respects was achieved on schedule. Newly added urban employment remained stable at over 12 million per year, residents' income growth kept pace with economic growth, and the world's largest education, healthcare and social security systems were built. The people's sense of gain has continued to grow, and common prosperity for all people is advancing steadily. During the 15th Five-Year Plan period, we will increase efforts to ensure and improve people's livelihoods, steadily advance common prosperity for all people, and take new and solid steps in promoting high-quality full employment and improving the income distribution system.\nAfter peaceful reunification, in terms of livelihoods, we will promote the sharing of public services and public resources across the Strait, providing more convenience for Taiwan compatriots, so that the supply of daily necessities in Taiwan will be more ample and diverse, and the public can enjoy better-quality, lower-priced products, further reducing production and living costs. In addition, with a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan will not need to spend huge sums on defense, and fiscal tax revenue can be used fully to improve people's livelihoods and to enrich funding for pensions, national health insurance, labor insurance and other programs, so that the levels of medical care, science, education, culture, sports and social welfare for Taiwan compatriots will be higher and their protection better.\nIn terms of employment, we will further introduce and implement policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises, create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to study, work and live on the mainland, and enable Taiwan compatriots and enterprises to further share in the opportunities arising from the rapid development of new industries and new business forms on the mainland, gaining more employment choices than they would have on the island. Taiwan's advantageous industries such as integrated circuits and precision machinery can complement mainland industries, “earning money for the whole world together,” and traditional industries such as agriculture, fisheries and tourism will regain new vitality and fully drive employment on the island.\nIn terms of housing, we will actively take measures to assist urban renewal and the upgrading and renovation of old housing in Taiwan, help address housing difficulties faced by young people, vulnerable groups and others, gradually narrow the wealth gap, promote common prosperity, and make the living environment of Taiwan compatriots more comfortable.\nIn terms of emergency relief, we will fully support Taiwan in improving its capacity to prevent and respond to disasters, mitigate disasters, and carry out relief, and will improve disaster early-warning and response mechanisms. When Taiwan encounters major natural disasters or sudden emergencies such as earthquakes, windstorms and tsunamis, we will provide disaster relief assistance at the first opportunity. The powerful emergency rescue capabilities of the mainland can all be put to use for Taiwan compatriots. With a strong motherland as its backing, Taiwan's security and development interests will be fully protected, and Taiwan compatriots will have greater sense of security, gain and happiness.\nIn short, national reunification is both a great righteous cause and a great benefit. We hope that compatriots on both sides will uphold the great righteousness of the nation, recognize the great benefits of reunification, and actively take part in the righteous cause of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760803.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","The civil aviation authorities announced that, through the liaison channel between the Cross-Strait Air Transport Exchange Committee and the Taipei Air Transport Business Association, they once again urged the Taiwan side to fully restore normal cross-Strait direct air passenger flights. What is the spokesperson's comment?","Cross-Strait direct air links have greatly facilitated travel between people on both sides and have played an important role in enhancing the well-being of compatriots on both sides. At present, cross-Strait routes are subject to interference from the DPP authorities, and destinations and flights have not fully returned to normal. The mainland has 15 destinations in 14 cities, with more than 300 passenger flights operated weekly (round trips counted as one flight). Compared with the 61 mainland destinations and the peak of 890 passenger flights per week before 2020, there is still a large gap, which seriously affects travel between compatriots on both sides. In 2025, more than 5.78 million passengers traveled between the two sides on direct air passenger flights, and the average load factor on cross-Strait routes currently exceeds 80%. People on both sides strongly call for the full resumption of all cross-Strait direct destinations.\nWe have no policy restrictions on the full resumption of cross-Strait direct air destinations; the root obstacle lies entirely with the DPP authorities. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion and lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport as soon as possible, so that cross-Strait airlines can arrange flight schedules independently based on market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760800.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, when meeting with certain US senators, Lai Ching-te said, “Taiwan is willing to engage in exchanges, but no exchange can come at the cost of democracy, freedom, and national interests.” What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of official exchange between diplomatic allies and the Taiwan region of China, and we firmly oppose foreign politicians colluding with “Taiwan independence” forces. Since Lai Ching-te took office, he has implemented “green authoritarian” dictatorial rule on the island, trampling on democracy and harming freedom. He is scheming to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence by relying on foreign powers,” escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait, which has already aroused strong dissatisfaction among Taiwan residents.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun recently visited the mainland. Raymond Greene, Director of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) Taipei Office, said: The United States' consistent position is to hope that cross-strait exchanges remain stable, and to expect the mainland to maintain communication channels with all Taiwan political parties, especially the “democratically elected government.” He further…","Both sides of the Strait belong to one China. As long as they recognize the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” there are no obstacles to our exchanges with any political party or group in Taiwan.\nThe DPP authorities' collusion with external forces and constant plotting of “independence” and provocations are the root cause of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. Certain people on the US side jump around, repeatedly rehashing the so-called “mainland threat or military pressure.” This completely inverts black and white and is driven by sinister intent. It must be stressed that the Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and outsiders have no right to interfere. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760792.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Although the DPP authorities have done their utmost to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, data released by the National Immigration Administration show that in the first quarter of this year, the number of Taiwan compatriot permit applications processed rose 11.8% year on year, and the number of entries into the mainland by Taiwan compatriots rose 27.6% year on year. What comment do you have on this?","Facts have repeatedly proven that wanting peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. The DPP authorities disregard public opinion and act against the tide, and they are destined to fail.\nWe will continue to uphold the concept that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. Guided by the principles of “greater openness, maximum convenience, and greater safety,” we will actively promote personal exchanges across the Strait and exchange and cooperation in all fields, create better conditions and provide more convenience for compatriots in Taiwan who come to the mainland for tourism, business, visits and exchanges, study and internships, and work and life. We warmly welcome compatriots in Taiwan, especially young friends, to take a “go-when-you-think-of-it” trip, to enjoy the magnificent scenery of the motherland, and to personally experience the mainland's development and progress and the affection and warmth that are everywhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760798.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Cross-Strait exchange activities have been vigorously carried out recently, with rich content. Please introduce the relevant situation.","With spring flowers in bloom, cross-Strait exchange activities across various regions continue to be lively. I will briefly introduce several events. The 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Micro-Drama Competition recently launched in Hengdian, Dongyang, Zhejiang, under the theme “Dreaming in Zhejiang, Connecting Both Sides Through Drama.” Focusing on six major themes—cross-Strait memories, youth together, life like a song, Chinese cultural heritage, rebirth in dreams, and AI dancing together—it is soliciting micro-dramas and scripts from both sides of the Strait. The submission deadline is May 15, and creators of cross-Strait micro-dramas are welcome to enthusiastically sign up and compete.\nThe 3rd “Colorful Taiwan in Beijing” cross-Strait youth short film call for submissions recently launched. In addition to four sections—Daily Light and Shadow, Future Vision, Cultural Imprint and Walking Scroll—this session adds a special AI section, “My Family Memories,” encouraging young people on both sides of the Strait to use technology to record colorful lives through the lens and showcase the beautiful moments of Beijing–Taiwan integration and personal family memories. The submission deadline is May 20, and young people from both sides of the Strait are welcome to pay attention and submit works.\nThe “Wen Tong Yuan · Ge Tong Diao” Jingtai Cultural Exchange Special Concert was held on April 11 in Nanjing County, Zhangzhou, Fujian. Using Hokkien as the medium, the concert invited 22 artists from Penghu County to perform on the same stage, presenting a grand gathering of familiar Hokkien songs, using local dialect to link hometown sentiments and friendship, and using song to convey the shared longing of common roots and origins.\nThe 2026 Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Folk Culture Festival Baosheng Cijii Cultural Activities launched today (April 15) at the Baosheng Cijigong temple in Qingjiao, Haicang District, Xiamen. Representatives of temples and believers from both sides of the Strait, more than 500 people in total, gathered in Haicang to jointly promote folk culture. During the event, supporting activities will also be held, including the Haicang District Biomedical Industry Exchange and Matchmaking Meeting, “Technology Empowerment, Local Charm United” visit and exchange, and the Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Folk Culture Festival Concert, broadening channels of technology empowerment for Taiwan compatriots participating in cross-Strait medical and health exchange and cooperation, and building a bridge of cultural integration.\nFrom April 15 to 20, the “2026 Jiangsu·Nanjing Taiwan Week” was held in Nanjing, including more than 20 exchange activities covering folk culture, cultural and sports interaction, and economic and trade cooperation, attracting nearly 1,000 compatriots from both sides of the Strait to participate.\nOn April 19 (the third day of the third lunar month), the Bingwu Year Yellow Emperor Hometown Ancestor Worship Ceremony, co-sponsored by the Henan Provincial People’s Government, the Henan Provincial Committee of the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, the All-China Federation of Returned Overseas Chinese, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, and the Chinese Association for the Study of Yan and Huang Culture, will be solemnly held in Xinzheng, Henan. Under the theme “Sharing the Same Roots and Ancestry, Peace, Harmony and Concord,” the ceremony will use nine ancient ritual procedures to jointly commemorate the deeds of our ancestors and pray together for national rejuvenation. More than 600 representatives from all walks of life in Taiwan will travel to Xinzheng to take part in the ceremony, and joint worship activities will continue to be held on the island. During the period, the 2026 “Chinese Cultural Origins Central Plains Tour” series of exchange activities will also be held, using archaeological study tours, intangible cultural heritage experiences, academic seminars and economic and trade inspections to let Taiwan compatriots from all sectors learn about Henan’s profound historical and cultural heritage and the vibrant momentum of its economic and social development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","湖南日报记者","The 2026 Cross-Strait (Hunan) Youth Exchange and Development Conference is about to be held, attracting the attention of young people on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The opening ceremony of the 2026 Cross-Strait (Hunan) Youth Exchange and Development Conference will be held in Changsha on April 16. Themed “Friendly Hunan, Youthful ‘Xiang’ Rendezvous,” the conference relies on Hunan's policy dividends for building a province friendly to young people, its complete industrial base, good business environment, profound cultural heritage, and its regional advantages of “low-cost entrepreneurship and high-quality living” to further promote youth exchanges between Hunan and Taiwan and deepen exchanges and integration in all fields in both places. During the conference, there will be activities including the 2026 Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Joining Hands with Youth for Innovation and Entrepreneurship Exchange, the “Spring on the Xiang River” Hunan-Taiwan Cross-Strait Art Exchange Week, and the Cross-Strait Youth E-sports and Music Trend Culture Exchange Camp. It will also promote relevant policy measures supporting Taiwan youth to study, live, work and start businesses in Hunan, providing all-round support for the broad number of Taiwan youth who come to Hunan to study, intern, work and start businesses.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Xiamen City in Fujian launched the “Xiamen Service Package for First-Time Taiwan Compatriot Visitors,” which has drawn attention from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To actively explore new paths for integrated development across the Taiwan Strait and to fully build the “first stop” of the first home for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises landing on the mainland, Xiamen in Fujian has recently launched the innovative “First-Visit Taiwan Compatriot Service Package in Xiamen.” It includes three service measures: providing first-time Taiwan compatriots with free rides on Xiamen's city buses, subway, BRT and the Gulangyu tourist ferry for 7 natural days; free admission to 15 scenic spots and tourist projects, including Gulangyu and “Seeing Kinmen from the Sea”; and discounted accommodation at 26 Xiamen state-owned enterprise hotels. The “service package” adopts a distribution model in which first-time Taiwan compatriots “receive it upon arrival in Xiamen and use it immediately.” Upon entering Xiamen, they may go to the “Near and Convenient” Taiwan compatriot service zone beside the Wutong Passenger Terminal, or to the “One-Stop Comprehensive Service Center for Overseas Guests” in the arrivals hall of Terminal T3 at Gaoqi International Airport to collect it. We welcome more and more Taiwan compatriots to come to Xiamen for sightseeing, exchanges and experiences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Lai Ching-te recently posted that the “Taiwan Relations Act” and the U.S. “Six Assurances” toward Taiwan are key cornerstones of stability and security in the Indo-Pacific region, that peace must rely on strength, and that strength must rely on long-term investment, and he demanded that Taiwan’s legislative bodies pass the special defense budget as soon as possible. What comment do you have on this?","The so-called “Taiwan Relations Act” and “Six Assurances” put forward by the US seriously violate the One-China Principle and the provisions of the three China–US joint communiqués, and seriously violate the basic norms of international relations. They are entirely wrong, illegal, and null and void. We have always firmly opposed them.\nThe Lai Qingde authorities constantly cater to the “Indo-Pacific” concept hyped up by the US and take the initiative to act as the US's pawn in “using Taiwan to contain China.” Their so-called “investment in strength” is in fact “investment in war” and “seeking independence through military force.” Faced with our powerful capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, no matter how many budgets the Lai Qingde authorities allocate or how many weapons they buy, it is like an egg striking a rock. It is overreaching and futile, and it cannot change—and will even accelerate—the inevitable downfall of “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Four Taiwanese films have been released in mainland cinemas since late March, sparking a small upsurge in cross-strait film and television exchanges. The upcoming 16th Beijing International Film Festival has also drawn attention from media on the island. Some public opinion on the island points out that multiple Taiwanese films being screened on the mainland shows the value placed on Taiwan's humanistic…","Cross-Strait filmmakers create film and television works from different perspectives and in diverse ways, showcasing the profound heritage of Chinese culture and the humanistic care of the Chinese nation. This is the inheritance, promotion, innovation, and creation of Chinese culture.\nWe will implement the ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation that our office was recently authorized to release, promote the screening and broadcasting on both sides of the Strait of film and television works that showcase cross-Strait kinship and a good life, enhance mutual understanding and comprehension among compatriots on both sides, and welcome more excellent Taiwan film and television works to share market opportunities on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","香港大公文汇传媒集团记者","Regarding this meeting between the leaders of the KMT and the CPC, a U.S. State Department spokesperson said: Meaningful cross-strait exchanges should focus on dialogue without preconditions between the mainland and Taiwan's “democratically elected government,” including interaction with all Taiwan political parties. The United States opposes any unilateral change to the status quo by either side, urges the…","We have just held a significant dialogue with the Kuomintang of China. The political foundation, or premise, for interaction between both sides is adherence to the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” On this common political foundation, we are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, enhance mutual trust, and jointly work for peace across the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation.\nThere is only one China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately hold to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to carry out provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” They are the disruptors of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and the instigators of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait situation.\nThe US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, handle Taiwan-related issues with prudence, and stop passing judgment on them all day long and interfering in China's internal affairs.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Regarding KMT Chair Cheng Li-wun leading a delegation to visit the mainland, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council Minister Chiu Chui-cheng said that party exchanges cannot replace official mechanisms, and that only by communicating with the “Taiwan government” can cross-Strait relations develop in a healthy way. What is your comment?","Adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” is the foundation for communication and dialogue across the Strait. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the position of “Taiwan independence” and constantly engage in “Taiwan independence” provocations, which is the greatest real threat to cross-Strait relations and peace in the Taiwan Strait. They talk about communication but in fact provoke, a typical case of saying one thing and meaning another, with a double-faced approach.\nWe are willing, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to work together with Taiwan's political parties, groups and social sectors, including the Chinese Kuomintang, to strengthen exchanges and dialogue, seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots and national rejuvenation for the Chinese nation, and firmly hold the future of cross-Strait relations in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Some on the island have noted that Cheng Li-wun has publicly expressed willingness to meet with Lai Ching-te before and after her visit to the mainland and sincerely awaits his invitation, but has received no positive response from Lai Ching-te. What is your comment?","Chairperson Cheng Li-wun led a Chinese Kuomintang delegation to visit the mainland, in keeping with the mainstream public opinion on the island that calls for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. It has positive and important significance for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and safeguarding the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Yet the Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and have deliberately schemed to obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They go against public opinion and greatly lose popular support.\nPeace and war, dialogue and confrontation, cooperation and strife are two entirely different paths. Therefore, I will answer your question with a famous saying from the Analects of Confucius: “道不同，不相为谋” (those whose paths differ do not make plans together).","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","According to Taiwan media, since March 2024 Denmark has changed the nationality and birthplace registration on the residence permits of Taiwan residents living in Denmark from Taiwan to China. Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities recently said that they have cancelled certain courtesies extended to Danish representatives in Taiwan, and called for a solution to be proposed as soon as possible. What comment do you…","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a broad consensus of the international community; it is the will of the people and the trend of the times. No matter how the DPP authorities scheme and make small moves, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot shake the basic framework of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The sixth of the ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchange and cooperation is: “Study the construction, in qualified regions, of wharves and berths to serve Taiwan-region distant-water fishing vessels in mooring and landing distant-water catches.” Does “regions” here refer to ports in mainland China, or would it include ports overseas? The mainland has already established several overseas distant-water…","The ten policy measures we have introduced to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation aim to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and to enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides. Studying the construction, in qualifying areas, of wharves and berths to serve the docking of Taiwan-area distant-water fishing vessels and the landing of their distant-water catches is a concrete arrangement we have made to do practical things for Taiwan's fishermen and to solve their problems. We care about the production and livelihoods of Taiwan's fishermen, and we will continue to advance cross-Strait fisheries cooperation to create better conditions for Taiwan's fishermen to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Recently, US President Trump threatened to blockade the Strait of Hormuz, plunging global energy supply into tension. CNN reported that if Taiwan were blockaded by the PLA, its electricity, water, and chip supplies would fall into full-scale crisis. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no outsider may meddle. Relevant reports create panic over a “China threat” and peddle cross-strait crisis anxiety with ulterior motives. It must be stressed that the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and constantly collude with external forces to scheme for “independence” and provoke confrontation. This is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait, and it also makes them the “troublemakers” for regional peace and stability.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang, recently said during a visit to Shanghai, “Across the Strait must shoulder the mission of creating peace and maintaining stability in the entire region,” and “What should fly in the sky is birds, not bullets; peace is the best gift I bring back to Taiwan.” What comment do you have on this?","Peace is a common value of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the shared expectation of compatriots on both sides. We are willing to work hand in hand with all parties, groups, and far-sighted individuals on the island, on the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. “Taiwan independence” is the chief culprit undermining peace in the Taiwan Strait, and we will absolutely not appease it or tolerate it. Only by firmly opposing the “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme and curbing “Taiwan independence” separatist conduct can compatriots on both sides jointly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Recently, Hunan Satellite TV's program “Ride the Wind 2026” has sparked heated discussion among viewers on both sides of the Strait, and the appearances of several senior Taiwan entertainers on stage have drawn particular attention. What is your comment?","Several variety shows from Hunan Television and Mango TV are deeply loved by Taiwan audiences. I have noted that from the earlier *Sisters Who Make Waves* (《乘风破浪的姐姐》) to the current *Sisters Who Make Waves 2026* (《乘风2026》), this program, which showcases women's charm and promotes cultural exchange at its core, has featured Taiwan entertainers in every season. They compete on stage and create together with mainland entertainers. This has both stirred up the youthful memories of many people on both sides of the Strait and, through the program's broadcast influence, made them known to and loved by even more young people across the Strait. We are glad to see programs like this, which convey emotion through sound and connect hearts through art. We welcome more Taiwan entertainers to come to the mainland to take part in program recordings, literary and artistic performances, and other cultural activities, contributing to cultural resonance and a shared bond between compatriots on both sides. We also wish the “Taiwan sisters” participating this season smooth sailing and excellent results.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260415_12760796.htm"],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that a mainland man who applied last year to travel to Taiwan was denied entry for two years by the DPP authorities after being reported for posting travel videos on social media that referred to “Chinese Taiwan” and included the five-star red flag, which the authorities deemed “maliciously disparaging Taiwan’s dignity.” His appeal was recently rejected. What comment do you have on this?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and “Chinese Taiwan” is a completely correct designation. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and unreasonably suppress this mainland resident, which is entirely a politically motivated manipulation. We firmly oppose any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activity. The DPP authorities should correct their mistakes and stop using improper pretexts to obstruct normal personnel exchanges and cooperation across the Strait.\nMainland residents traveling to Taiwan must hold dedicated documents, namely the “Mainland Residents Travel Permit to Taiwan” and its endorsement. We hope everyone will abide by the relevant regulations to avoid harm to their personal rights and interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Reportedly, Lai Ching-te will lead a delegation to visit Eswatini from April 22 to 27. What is your comment?","We have consistently handled Taiwan’s external exchanges in accordance with the one-China principle, and we firmly oppose any act that attempts to create “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” internationally. We hope the relevant countries will recognize the trend of the times, promptly correct their mistakes, and stand on the right side of history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Question one: Regarding the tenth of the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, “promote the resumption of individual tourism pilot programs for residents of Shanghai Municipality and Fujian Province to Taiwan (main island).” Will residents of Beijing and Jiangsu, where Chairperson Cheng Li-wun visited during this trip, be treated the same way and be allowed to travel to Taiwan for…","First question. Regarding whether Beijing, Jiangsu and other provinces and cities will follow suit in opening tourism to Taiwan, there is currently no further news. We hope the Taiwan side will take practical measures to create conditions for the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges.\nSecond question. The introduction of ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation fully reflects our position of promoting people's well-being through exchange and integration. The aim is to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and dialogue with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang of China, and advance related work. We believe that sharing peace, pursuing development together and promoting prosperity together across the Taiwan Strait is a blessing for compatriots on both sides, and it will certainly win widespread support from the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Regarding Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun’s visit to the mainland with a delegation, a DPP politician said that current laws and regulations on the island do not cover party chairpersons traveling to the mainland, and that the law should be “amended” so that they are treated like civil servants, who must obtain approval from the Joint Review Committee before traveling to the mainland. The Mainland Affairs…","The DPP authorities seek to control and obstruct political party leaders on the island from exchanging and visiting the mainland. Their aim is to undermine cross-Strait relations and to carry out “Taiwan independence dictatorship” and “green terror” on the island. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nPeace, development, exchanges and cooperation are the wishes of the people on both sides of the Strait, and no one can stop the surging tide of cross-Strait exchanges and dialogue. On the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all sectors of society, enhance mutual trust, and work together to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots and rejuvenation for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that robots previously hyped by Green camp media as “Taiwan-developed” and “capable of real-world application” were in fact mainland-made products relabeled and disguised, sparking skepticism and ridicule on the island. What is your comment?","The mainland is the world's largest robot manufacturing base, with a continually expanding industrial scale, steadily rising innovation capacity, and comprehensively broadened application scenarios. Mainland robot products are widely welcomed by consumers worldwide. We are also glad to see Taiwan residents using good mainland products, and to see Taiwan-funded enterprises sharing the opportunities of the mainland's robotics industry development. Through Chairperson Zheng Liwen's visit itinerary, everyone can feel the rapid development of the mainland's robotics industry, humanoid robots, and embodied intelligence, and their world-class level.\nDriven by the narrow interests of one party, the DPP authorities have engaged in extensive political manipulation and pushed for “decoupling and severing chains” across the Strait, obstructing exchange and cooperation in cross-Strait economy and trade. But these self-deceiving approaches cannot hide the truth forever. Their hypocritical face has been seen through by more and more Taiwan residents, and it has met with opposition and rejection across Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office being authorized to release ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said, “The mainland's economic and trade concessions are merely sugar-coated poison packaged as a gift bag.” What is your comment?","Whenever the mainland introduces measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots, the DPP authorities smear and disparage them; whatever is beneficial to enhancing the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, they strongly oppose. Taiwan society has grown accustomed to this practice. The DPP authorities should ask the workers and businesses across all trades in Taiwan whether these ten measures are good and whether they should be adopted, rather than smearing and slandering them. We advise the DPP authorities to say less empty talk and do more practical things.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-15","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","The Dalian Maritime Safety Administration recently announced live-fire shooting in some waters of the northern Yellow Sea. A DPP spokesperson said, “The peace seeds sown by Cheng Li-wun have not yet sprouted before being slapped in the face by the CCP's shells.” What is your comment?","Dragging in irrelevant matters, forcing far-fetched connections, fabricating stories, and switching concepts are the deceptive tricks commonly used by DPP politicians. Their aim is to attack political rivals who work for peace across the Strait and for the well-being of compatriots. Taiwan's public sees this very clearly.\nThe press conference is concluded here. Thank you.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260415_12760779.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-04-17","Guo Jiakun","China-Arab TV","The Chinese embassy in Japan has received several terrorist threats. Only one week after the break-in incident, an individual claiming to be a reserve member of the Self-Defense Forces issued an online threat to the embassy, claiming that a remotely controlled bomb had been planted inside the premises. Discriminatory cases targeting Chinese nationals in Japan have also increased. What is China’s response?","Recent years have seen incessant harassment and provocations targeting Chinese missions in Japan, most notably the string of grave offenses that happened recently, including the break-in of the embassy by a sitting SDF officer carrying a knife. The recurrence of this kind of egregious incidents reveals multiple deep-seated issues in today’s Japan: the worsening right-wing impact and the suppression of objective and rational voices, the toxicity of the Japanese government’s erroneous policies on vital issues concerning China-Japan relations such as history and Taiwan, the serious lack of education on true history, the pervasive erroneous historical views, the ongoing push for a more offensive, expansionist and dangerous defense policy and failure in supervising the SDF and maintaining discipline inside the forces.\nHow to fundamentally address the issue and remove its breeding ground in the Japanese society deserves serious pondering by those with insights in Japan. Soft-pedaling such incidents and even distracting attention from them or spreading disinformation will only lead to more such incidents with even more dreadful consequences, and put more Japanese people under its harmful impact. The malevolent emergence of neo-militarism in Japan could also threaten peace and stability in the region. We once again urge the Japanese side to reflect on and correct its policy and behavior, conduct a thorough probe and take full responsibility for the incident.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260417_11894293.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260417_11894119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-04-17","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","Today, a Japanese Maritime Self-Defense Force vessel entered the Taiwan Strait. What’s China’s comment?","The Chinese military has handled the entry of the Japanese SDF vessel in accordance with laws and regulations. Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have already severely impacted China-Japan relations. The Japanese side is compounding the wrongdoing by sending the Self-Defense Force vessel into the Taiwan Strait to flex its muscles and deliberately provoke China. It exposes the dangerous attempts of certain people in Japan to conduct armed intervention and undermine the peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. This action severely undermines the political foundation of China-Japan relations and threatens China’s sovereignty and security. China firmly opposes it and has lodged strong protest against Japan.\nThe Taiwan question bears on China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and the political foundation of China-Japan relations. It is a red line that must not be crossed. China urges the Japanese side to do serious soul-searching on its wrongdoings, return to the right track at once, exercise prudence in its words and actions, and stop going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260417_11894293.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260417_11894119.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-04-17","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reporter: On April 17, a Japan Self-Defense Forces vessel transited the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?","Zhang Xiaogang: The Japanese destroyer ‘Lei’ transited the Taiwan Strait. The Eastern Theater Command organized sea and air forces to conduct full-course shadowing and effective monitoring and control. We have lodged stern representations with the Japanese side and expressed strong protest. This Japanese move is a deliberate provocation, and it is one mistake after another. What does Japan intend? Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi has made erroneous remarks concerning Taiwan and has not repented to this day. Japan's Self-Defense Force vessels stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait send a wrong signal to ‘Taiwan independence’ separatist forces. This will only arouse greater indignation among the Chinese people and further strengthen China's resolve to counter Japan's playing with fire and provocations. We urge the Japanese side to turn back from the path of error, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and not go further down the wrong path. The Chinese military always maintains a high state of alert, firmly counters all foreign interference schemes, and defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/qwfb/16455741.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-04-20","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","I early had a question about the annual Balikatan military drills, but I will just add on another question to that. Last week, Japan’s destroyer, the Ikazuchi, which sailed through the Taiwan Strait was heading to these drills. I was just wondering, given that destroyer went through the Taiwan Strait, does China have any other comment to add regarding Japan’s active participation in this year’s drills?","The Chinese side has made clear its solemn position regarding the transit of a vessel of the Japanese Self-Defence Forces through the Taiwan Strait. As to your question, we need to stress that Japan bears grave historical responsibilities for Southeast Asian countries, including the Philippines, due to its aggression and colonial rule during WWII. Japan needs to seriously reflect on its history of aggression, and exercise prudence both in words and actions in military and security areas, rather than flexing muscles around and undermining stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260420_11895636.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260420_11895519.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-04-22","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It is reported that, one day after making ritual offerings to the Yasukuni war shrine, Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi made a monetary offering to the shrine today. Minoru Kiuchi, Japan’s Economic Growth Strategy Minister, Haruko Arimura, head of the Liberal Democratic Party’s General Council, and several other cabinet members visited the shrine. What’s China’s comment?","We’ve made China’s serious position clear yesterday. Japan’s negative moves related to the Yasukuni war shrine constitute a blatant provocation against international justice and an affront to human conscience. China is strongly indignant and severely condemns it.\nDuring World War II, Japanese militarists committed innumerable crimes, inflicting immense suffering on Asian countries including China, and the rest of the world. The Yasukuni war shrine is a spiritual tool and symbol of Japanese militarists’ war of aggression. It is in fact a shrine for war criminals, as it honors convicted Class-A war criminals responsible for the war of aggression in WWII, including Hideki Tojo, No.1 war criminal and warmonger; Kenji Doihara, major culprit of aggression against China; Iwane Matsui, top perpetrator of the Nanjing Massacre; Osami Nagano, order-giver of the Pearl Harbor attack; and Kuniaki Koiso, mass murderer on the Korean Peninsula. They are all major war criminals responsible for atrocities against the people in Asia and the rest of the world.\nThe nature of the issue concerning the Yasukuni war shrine is whether Japan is able to rightly perceive and deeply reflect on its history of militarist aggression, and whether it can learn lessons from history and avoid a repeat of that part of history. This bears on the political foundation of China-Japan relations, on Japan’s credibility as a nation, and on the postwar international order as well as peace and justice in the world. The negative moves concerning the Yasukuni war shrine show that Japan, in total disregard of international concerns and just voices from both inside Japan and the world, has all along refused to acknowledge its history of aggression during WWII, attempted to change the verdict on its war of aggression and the Class-A war criminals, and even gone further to challenge the judgment of the Tokyo trials and postwar international order. Lately there has been a marked increase in the Japanese government’s negative moves and reckless provocative acts on issues concerning China’s Taiwan region and the history of WWII as well as military and security issues. Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan have had a grave impact on China-Japan relations. In the face of strong criticism and opposition from China as well as at home and abroad, some Japanese politicians and right-wing forces chose to go down the wrong path, rather than reflect on and correct their wrongdoings. The Chinese people, people in other countries that suffered under Japanese aggression, and all peace-loving forces for justice in the world will never allow this.\nThis year marks the 80th anniversary of the beginning of the Tokyo trials. The trials found Japanese militarism and militarists guilty of launching and executing the war of aggression and related crimes, thus upholding historical truth, international justice and human dignity. Today, 80 years later, Japanese neo-militarism is rearing its ugly head and gaining strength, threatening to cast a shadow on world peace and security. The international community must respond resolutely to prevent any possible resurgence of Japanese militarism.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260422_11897589.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260422_11897449.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-04-22","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan said Lai Ching-te had to cancel his visit to Eswatini, as three African countries denied his overflight access. Taiwan said the countries Seychelles, Mauritius and Madagascar were under economic coercion from China to do so. What is China’s response to that? Did China reach out to those countries about the airspace access? And did China reach out to other African countries too?","All African countries, with the sole exception of Eswatini, have established diplomatic ties with China. These 53 countries together with the African Union have adopted the Beijing Declaration at the 2024 FOCAC Summit. They have reiterated on many occasions that they firmly uphold the one-China principle, there is but one China in the world, Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China, and they firmly support all efforts by the Chinese government to achieve national reunification. China highly commends relevant countries’ commitment to the one-China principle which is fully consistent with international law and basic norms governing international relations. It’s very clear that there’s no longer a so-called “ROC president” in the world anymore. Anyone who wears that false title is acting against history and will only invite disgrace upon themselves. The one-China principle is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends, and to uphold it is the right thing to do. No one can ever stop the eventual reunification of China. The separatist attempts aimed at “Taiwan independence” are just futile and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260422_11897589.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260422_11897449.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 22, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","Recently, the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce gathered representatives of seven major island industries, including travel, hotels, and food, to hold a press conference titled “Industry's Views on the Mainland's Recent Preferential Policies for Taiwan.” It called on the DPP authorities to put people's livelihoods first, not to politicize economic issues affecting livelihoods, and not to sacrifice the living space of…","The voice expressed by the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce and relevant industry circles fully reflects that the ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation that we recently released meet the needs of the island's industrial recovery and help resolve economic and livelihood pain points. The DPP authorities disregard public opinion on the island and disregard the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. Toward the goodwill and sincerity released by the mainland side and the policy measures it has introduced to benefit Taiwan and its people, they only engage in blanket smearing and attacks, and take the opportunity to engage in political manipulation. They fantasize about resuming cross-Strait consultations and dialogue without acknowledging the “1992 Consensus.” These habitual tricks cannot fool anyone and will not succeed. They will only put them increasingly on the opposite side of mainstream public opinion on the island.\nExchange and integration are the aspiration and the source of well-being for compatriots on both sides. The great tide of compatriots on both sides drawing closer, getting nearer and coming together cannot be stopped by anyone. The DPP authorities should stop political manipulation, follow the will of the people and the trend of the times, and change their attitude toward promoting cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762146.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said, “Peace is not achieved through compromise and concession of sovereignty, and placing Taiwan within a one-China framework can achieve it. Packaging unification as peace not only violates public opinion but will also bring endless disasters to Taiwan.” What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. It has never been a country and can never become one, and there is no so-called “sovereignty” at all. China is the common homeland of the Chinese nation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait must safeguard and build this common homeland well. The fundamental way to do so is to uphold the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” and the core is to recognize that both sides of the Strait belong to one China.\nPeace is the common value of compatriots on both sides, and maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the shared hope of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities, defying mainstream public opinion, stubbornly cling to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, constantly manipulate “using force to seek independence,” and scheme to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They are the chief culprits undermining peace in the Taiwan Strait and the instigators of tension and turmoil in the Strait.\nThe future of Taiwan and the security, well-being, and interests of Taiwan compatriots have always been tied to peaceful cross-Strait development and the reunification of the motherland. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to see that the Lai Ching-te authorities' pursuit of “independence” will only provoke conflict and destroy Taiwan. They firmly oppose the separatism of “Taiwan independence” and external interference, and actively seek peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762142.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","Regarding the ten policy measures the mainland has introduced to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said, “All ten policy measures involve core national security and the exercise of government public authority, and must be formally consulted between the two governments before appropriate arrangements are made.” What comment do you have on…","Since the release of the ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, they have been welcomed by all sectors on the island. People have expressed their eager anticipation for the implementation of these policy measures, believing they are important steps to revitalize relevant industries in Taiwan and inject vitality into the economy.\nIn the face of the public's eager expectations, the DPP authorities can only smear and talk down the measures, pour cold water on them, and put up obstacles. This approach—disregarding people's livelihoods for the sake of party interests—has been widely criticized and opposed by the island's public and industry. We advise the DPP authorities to heed public opinion on the island and respond to the calls of industry, and to do more to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation.\nAs long as we uphold the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to work together with all parties, groups, and sectors of society in Taiwan to pursue peace across the Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun returned to Taiwan from her visit to the mainland, the Taiwan “Democratic Culture and Education Foundation” released its latest poll on cross-Strait issues showing that more than half of respondents agree that Taiwan should proactively face and discuss the question of cross-Strait unification, and nearly 70% of the public support strengthening cross-Strait contact and…","Relevant public opinion polls show that Chairperson Cheng Li-wun's visit to the mainland with the Chinese Kuomintang delegation responded to the mainstream public opinion on the island calling for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, and conformed to the broad trend of compatriots on both sides drawing closer and coming together. It plays an important role in promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and safeguarding the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots.\nReunification is Taiwan's only future and is tied to the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end that will only bring profound disaster to the Taiwan Strait. We hope that more Taiwan compatriots will follow the trend of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, recognize the great benefits of reunification, and actively join the just cause of promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762145.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, a poll on the island released by Taiwan’s “Democratic Culture and Education Foundation” showed that, in the event of a military conflict across the Strait, 54.4% of respondents believe the United States definitely or probably will not send troops unconditionally to defend Taiwan, while only 28.6% believe it will. What comment do you have on this?","Relevant polls once again show that more and more Taiwan compatriots recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders are unreliable, and recognize that in the eyes of the United States, Taiwan is merely a “pawn” used to contain the mainland's development, and also a “discarded pawn” that can be abandoned at any time.\nIt must be stressed that the Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is tolerated. The DPP authorities' stubborn “relying on the United States to seek independence” cannot bring security or peace; it will only harm the present and burden future generations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Regarding Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang, leading a delegation to visit the mainland, the head of Taiwan’s security agencies said that cross-Strait exchanges should be led by the Taiwan authorities and should not be decided party-to-party, and that new measures the mainland has introduced toward Taiwan may constitute “election interference,” intended to influence the island’s elections. What comment…","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” which has led to a standstill in cross-Strait dialogue and consultations. They also deliberately smear, attack and suppress normal exchanges between other political parties, groups and all sectors of society on the island and the mainland. We have introduced ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Social sectors on the island and broad Taiwan compatriots all applaud and support them and want to benefit from them early, but only the DPP authorities have jumped out to attack, smear and oppose them.\nThis once again fully exposes the DPP authorities' true face of plotting “Taiwan independence” and their evil nature of undermining cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, harming the well-being of the people, and working against the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762143.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, the civil aviation authorities announced that they again urge the Taiwan side to fully restore normal cross-Strait direct air passenger services. The DPP authorities said that the actual demand for cross-Strait direct flights at this stage is not as high as imagined, and that the flights currently in operation can meet current demand. What comment do you have on this?","Cross-strait air direct flights are an aerial link that facilitates personal exchanges across the Taiwan Strait and smooths economic and cultural exchange and cooperation, carrying the urgent need of the public for frequent contact. How high is the demand? The data speak for themselves. In 2025, cross-strait air flights totaled 31,973 sorties, carrying 5.7828 million passengers. In the first quarter of this year alone, there were 8,079 sorties, carrying 1.4672 million passengers, with passenger numbers up by double digits year on year and load factors exceeding 80%. These concrete data confirm the robust demand in the cross-strait air direct flight market and the strong desire and intention of people on both sides to travel back and forth. It is understood that mainland airlines have basically used up their capacity quotas on cross-strait routes.\nUnder the existing cross-strait air transport arrangements, cross-strait airlines may operate no more than 890 passenger flights per week in total between 61 airports on the mainland and 10 airports in Taiwan. This is an existing arrangement that had been in operation for a long time before 2020. The Cross-Strait Air Transport Exchange Committee has repeatedly urged the Taiwan side to fully restore the normalization of cross-strait air direct flights. This is a positive step in response to the calls of people on both sides and in promoting the full resumption of flights.\nCross-strait air direct flights are a bridge for communication, not a political bargaining chip. The DPP authorities should face the market demand squarely, stop political manipulation, and stop obstructing personal exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, so that cross-strait air direct flights return to their essence of serving people's livelihoods and promoting exchange, and give compatriots on both sides a smooth, convenient, and efficient air route.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","The 18th West Lake–Sun Moon Lake “Two Lakes Forum” was held today at Sun Moon Lake in Nantou, Taiwan. What is your comment?","Since 2009, Hangzhou City and Nantou County have alternately hosted the “West Lake · Sun Moon Lake” Two Lakes Forum, which has been held 17 times to date. The forum has become an important platform for deepening exchanges and cooperation between the two places, has achieved a series of positive results, and has enhanced the well-being of people in both places. We wish this session of the forum great success!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, exchanges and interactions between people on both sides of the Strait have become increasingly warm. From a chicken hotpot restaurant owner in Foshan, Guangdong, who warmly called out to Taiwanese diners, “Chinese people must stand united, and the motherland is a strong backing,” to a young tour guide in Xinjiang who told Taiwanese tourists about the Tianshan Victory Tunnel, saying, “It is not easy to…","Whether it is the owner of a chicken claypot restaurant in Guangdong using plain words to tell Taiwanese diners about his feelings for the nation and homeland, or the young female tour guide from Xinjiang whose heartfelt explanations struck an emotional chord with Taiwanese tourists, these warm and moving moments are a vivid epitome of “both sides of the Strait are one family,” demonstrating that compatriots on both sides share a common national identity and blood ties.\nWe are glad to see, and believe, that such cross-Strait exchange activities will become more numerous. Through food and scenery, they bring each other closer, deepen understanding and identification through exchange, and promote heart-to-heart connection with sincerity. No one can stop the tide of compatriots on both sides drawing closer, coming together. Compatriots on both sides, united and friendly, will surely join hands to create a better future for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Regarding Kuomintang Chairperson Cheng Li-wun’s visit to the mainland with a delegation, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said, “Cheng Li-wun taking the ‘1992 Consensus’ as the premise for cross-Strait dialogue is endorsing the mainland’s elimination of the ‘Republic of China’ on its behalf. This is a poison for annexation, not a cure for peace.” What comment do you have on this?","Out of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities openly peddle the “two-state theory.” They have no willingness to seek peace in the Taiwan Strait, no ability to handle cross-Strait relations well, and have repeatedly and deliberately undermined cross-Strait relations and escalated tensions in the Taiwan Strait. They are the “poison” that harms Taiwan and its people.\nPeace is not difficult, and making Taiwan prosperous is not difficult either. As long as we adhere to the “1992 Consensus” and oppose “Taiwan independence,” cross-Strait relations can develop peacefully, the Taiwan Strait can remain peaceful and stable, and compatriots on both sides can live good lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762144.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Cross-Strait exchange activities have taken diverse forms recently. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Recently, cross-Strait exchange activities have been vibrant. I will introduce several of them.\nFujian has held a series of cross-Strait exchange activities. The 7th “Cross-Strait Hearts, Tea and Tourism Integration” tea-picking exchange event was held on April 11 in Taining, Sanming, Fujian. Using tea as the medium, the event traced the historical lineage of the shared origins of Fujian and Taiwan tea culture, effectively promoting in-depth exchange and integrated development among tea-producing areas of Fujian and Taiwan. The 2026 Rong-Tai Gateball Invitational Tournament was held in Fuzhou from the 13th to the 17th, with 8 Taiwan teams participating. Players from both sides of the Strait bonded through the game, exchanged skills and deepened friendship. The 12th “Cross-Strait Affection, Shared Roots” Baosheng Dadi cultural exchange event concluded on the 16th in Pinghe, Zhangzhou. Nearly 200 Taiwan Lai clan representatives crossed the sea to gather with local relatives, sharing friendship. The 2026 Haicang–Tainan Industrial Deep Integration Exchange Week was held in Haicang, Xiamen from the 16th to the 20th, featuring forms such as a Taiwan business roundtable to deepen industrial alignment and integrated development between the two places. The “Fu Seeds United, Loving China” 13th Fujian Province “March Third” She Ethnic Culture Week was held in Shanghang, Longyan from the 18th to the 19th, including genealogy exchanges and themed evening galas. Guests of all ethnic groups from both sides of the Strait shared the sentiment that across the Strait we are one family and sang together of the bond between Chinese people. From the 19th to the 22nd, the “Seeking Roots, Uniting in Culture” cross-Strait university student field research and short drama event was held in the Zhangzhou Taiwan Investment Zone, attracting nearly 130 university students and short drama actors from both sides to exchange skills and learn from each other.\nOn April 16, the 2026 “Chinese Family Under One Roof” Guangxi–Taiwan Ethnic Groups Celebrate the “Guangxi March Third” Grand Gathering was held in Nanning, with more than 500 compatriots from Guangxi and Taiwan enthusiastically participating. On the same day, Wenzhou, Zhejiang held the “Gathering in Wenzhou, Heading to the Mountains and Seas” cross-Strait media and online influencer field research event. Participants held exchanges and discussions on co-producing cross-Strait short dramas, co-creating film and television IP, and disseminating new media content, and established a Wenzhou–Taiwan New Media Exchange and Cooperation Base, helping more cross-Strait film and television cooperation projects take root.\nIn addition, the five-episode micro-short drama “Tongmai Shixin—Exploring Henan in Taiwan’s Textbooks,” created by Henan’s “Daxiang News,” was selected as a recommended title for the first batch of the National Radio and Television Administration’s 2026 “Micro-Drama+” action plan, and won the Outstanding Work Award at the 2nd International Micro-Drama Competition thanks to its profound cultural core and innovative narrative. The drama helps young people on both sides of the Strait appreciate the depth of Chinese history through poetry and lyrics, and feel the warmth of the times through technological innovation.\nThe 10th Cross-Strait Nezha Folk Culture Exchange Event will be held in Jiangyou, Sichuan from April 28 to May 3, centering on Li Bai culture, Nezha culture, Chinese fortune culture and other themes, and carrying out a series of activities including a cultural and creative competition and economic, trade and cultural exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中新社记者","The DPP authorities announced yesterday that Lai Ching-te's originally planned visit to Eswatini has been canceled because relevant countries refused to grant flight permits for his chartered plane. What is your comment?","We appreciate the position and practice of the relevant countries in adhering to the one-China principle. Those who act justly gain much support; those who do not gain little. Facts have once again proven that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a broad consensus of the international community, and it is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260422_12762141.htm"],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Hunan) Youth Exchange and Development Conference was successfully held in Hunan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From April 10 to 18, the main events of the 2026 Cross-Strait (Hunan) Youth Exchange and Development Conference were successfully held in Hunan, with more than 500 youth representatives, entrepreneurs, and innovation and entrepreneurship teams from both sides of the Strait taking part.\nThe events earnestly implemented the spirit of the important speech General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered when he met with Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China. They included art performances, youth dialogues and on-site visits, and released relevant policy measures and internship and employment opportunities. They showcased from multiple dimensions Hunan's active efforts to build a province friendly to young people. Through implementing the “four friendlies” actions of employment-friendly, entrepreneurship-friendly, life-friendly and growth-friendly, Hunan provides a development environment of “low-cost entrepreneurship and high-quality living” for cross-Strait youth, and it welcomes more Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to exchange and develop.\nAfter the main events, Hunan will also hold a series of Xiang-Taiwan youth exchange activities, covering cultural tracing, sports events, medical and health care, and internships and employment. These aim to promote exchanges and interactions between Hunan and Taiwan and to promote heart-to-heart connection between cross-Strait youth.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Regarding the mainland's push to resume the pilot program for individual tourism by residents of Shanghai Municipality and Fujian Province to Taiwan (main island), Liang Wen-chieh, Deputy Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that whether the mainland opens free independent travel or group tours, “small two-association” consultations are unavoidable, which has caused concern in the island's tourism…","Promoting the resumption of pilot programs for individual tourism to the island by residents of Shanghai and Fujian is a positive measure that conforms to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society calling for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and promotes the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.\nThe DPP authorities should face the voices of the island's tourism industry and residents, stop political manipulation, lift the various unreasonable restrictions on mainland residents traveling to Taiwan for tourism, and adopt pragmatic measures to create favorable conditions for normalizing personnel exchanges across the Strait. Instead of repeatedly setting up barriers with various untenable excuses, being hostile to the people, and blocking people from benefiting.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, while taking part in a tabletop simulation of the island’s so-called “Han Kuang 42” exercise, said, “The exercise should take actual combat as the standard, and combine it with the whole society’s defense resilience and asymmetric warfare thinking, continuously enhancing the armed forces’ ability to respond and overall deterrence. Peace is not achieved by a piece of paper; it must rely on…","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, attempting to “seek independence by relying on foreign powers” and “seek independence by force,” which is the root cause of the tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Their willingness to tie Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” war chariot will ultimately only harm the security and well-being of Taiwan residents.\nNo matter how many “war-game tabletop exercises” or “drills” the DPP authorities stage, they are like a mantis trying to stop a chariot. They cannot change the fate that “Taiwan independence” is bound to fail, and they cannot block the historical trend toward national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, Brazil's “representative in Taiwan” told Taiwan media in an exclusive interview that “Taiwan is part of China.” The Taiwan authorities' foreign affairs department claimed his remarks and conduct were “untrue and inappropriate,” expressed strong dissatisfaction, and lodged a stern protest. What is your comment?","The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community; it is the trend of the times and the righteous course. The DPP authorities' emotional meltdown precisely exposes their fierce appearance masking inner weakness, adding only to their own ridicule.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Bipartisan U.S. senators in Congress recently sent a letter to Taiwan’s legislature urging the swift passage of Taiwan’s “special defense budget” to strengthen Taiwan’s defense capabilities and accelerate procurement of U.S. weapons. Some lawmakers have also called on the U.S. executive branch to continue advancing the process of U.S. arms sales to Taiwan. What comment do you have on this?","We note that for some time, some people in the United States have repeatedly expressed concern about, and even publicly pressured, Taiwan's budget, attempting to play the “Taiwan card” and “use Taiwan to contain China,” and obstruct China's reunification. We firmly oppose this. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe DPP authorities, scheming to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on foreign powers,” and willing to serve as the “ATM” of American arms dealers, will ultimately only turn the island into a “powder keg” and an “ammunition depot,” harming and ruining Taiwan and bringing about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, bipartisan U.S. federal senators once again introduced the “Taiwan Relations Reinforcement Act,” which aims to comprehensively upgrade U.S.-Taiwan relations, ensure that U.S. policy supports “Taiwan’s democracy and international participation,” and urges Taiwan to increase investment in combat capability and asymmetric defense strategies. What comment do you have on this?","A U.S. congressional member has introduced erroneous Taiwan-related bills that encourage Taiwan to procure weapons and prepare for war, seriously violating the one-China principle and brutally interfering in China's internal affairs.\nWe firmly oppose any act of creating “two Chinas,” “one China, one Taiwan,” or “Taiwan independence” internationally under any pretext, and we firmly oppose any form of military ties between diplomatic partners and the Taiwan region of China. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, immediately stop advancing the relevant bills, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, a Japanese Self-Defense Forces vessel entered and operated in the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and an uncrossable red line. Japan has sent Self-Defense Forces vessels into the Taiwan Strait to deliberately provoke, which seriously damages the political foundation of China-Japan relations, seriously threatens China's sovereignty and security, and once again exposes the sinister scheme of some in Japan to forcibly intervene in the Taiwan Strait and undermine its peace and stability. We firmly oppose this. Japan should deeply reflect on history, draw lessons from history, earnestly reflect on and correct its mistakes, abide by the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and stop all erroneous words and actions concerning Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Regarding the ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchange and cooperation, which measures can the mainland advance unilaterally and implement immediately? Which still require consultation and cooperation with the Taiwan side to be implemented? Regarding the matters that Taiwan residents care about, such as resuming mainland tourists' travel to Taiwan, normalizing cross-strait direct flights, and…","We adhere to the concept that “Cross-Strait Are One Family,” insist on promoting people's well-being through exchange and integration, and aim to let compatriots on both sides live better lives. Focusing on the actual needs of Taiwan compatriots, we have introduced ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. The ten policy measures cover cross-Strait party-to-party exchanges, youth exchanges, and areas such as the economy, livelihood, and culture and tourism. They are another important step in our efforts to promote cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and to enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots. They accord with the mainstream public opinion and common aspirations of compatriots on both sides for peace, development, exchange and cooperation, and they respond to the earnest expectations of the people on the island.\nNext, we will work with relevant departments and localities to implement the relevant policy measures on the ground, in detail and in full, so that compatriots on both sides will soon benefit and share in the good results. We hope the DPP authorities will heed the will of the people on the island and respond to the appeals of industry. We hope they will lift all kinds of artificial restrictions and remove obstacles to normalizing and routinizing cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question. Regarding Lai Ching-te’s cancellation of his trip to Eswatini, the Lai authorities have pointed the finger at the mainland for suppression. We believe the mainland side will continue to struggle against the Lai authorities, and the mainland side has also made clear that this targets the “Taiwan independence” forces and not the broad Taiwan public. However, Lai Ching-te is, after all, the…","First, I must emphasize that there is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called \"president.\"\nFirst question. The One-China Principle is a widely recognized basic norm of international relations. We consistently apply the One-China Principle in handling Taiwan's external exchanges, and firmly oppose any attempt to create \"two Chinas\" or \"one China, one Taiwan\" in the international arena. Lai Ching-te attempts to spread separatist \"Taiwan independence\" fallacies abroad, incite \"anti-China and resist China\" sentiment, collude with external forces to seek \"independence\" and provoke confrontation, escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and harm the interests of the people on the island. He will certainly be opposed and will fail.\nOn the basis of the One-China Principle, issues concerning Taiwan's external exchanges can be properly resolved through cross-Strait consultations. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. As long as we speak frankly and consult each other on matters, there are no contradictions or differences that cannot be resolved.\nSecond question. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion on the island. The Kuomintang and the Communist Party, on the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" have strengthened exchanges and interactions among party members at all levels, and promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is of great significance for safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and enhancing the family affection and well-being of compatriots. The DPP authorities oppress and suppress \"opposition\" forces, obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and will stop at nothing. Their record is full of misdeeds; they are creating a \"green terror,\" going against the mainstream public opinion on the island, and are unpopular.\nThird question. We have always supported and encouraged film and cultural works that showcase cross-Strait family affection and a good life to be screened and broadcast on both sides of the Strait, promoting the protection, inheritance, innovation, and development of Chinese culture. I have a set of data on films to share with everyone. In 2024, a total of 9 Taiwanese films were released on the mainland, with combined box office revenue of approximately 742 million yuan; in 2025, 8 Taiwanese films were released on the mainland, with combined box office revenue of approximately 88,105,700 yuan. As of this year, 6 Taiwanese films have been released on the mainland. It can be said that as long as Taiwanese films apply through the proper procedures and their content meets mainland market demand, the channel for their release on the mainland is smooth, and their box office performance is evident to all. On the contrary, the Taiwan side has long implemented a quota system for mainland films, which seriously does not meet the expectations of the industry and Taiwanese audiences, affects cross-Strait film exchange and cooperation, and urgently needs review and improvement.\nFourth question. Recently, mainland TV dramas such as \"Zhu Yu\" have been hit in both sides of the Strait, and the lead actors have therefore attracted attention and affection from audiences on the island. The remarks made by young members of the Kuomintang's visiting delegation expressed the sincere hopes of Taiwanese youth for cross-Strait film and television exchange and cooperation and for the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, vividly illustrating the unique role of film and cultural exchange in bringing the psychological distance between compatriots on both sides closer. We have consistently supported \"two-way engagement\" between the film and television and cultural circles on both sides, and we welcome mainland artists traveling to Taiwan for exchanges and meeting people on the island.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture, and cultural resonance is the most natural bond connecting hearts. We will continue to create convenient conditions for cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation, support more cultural workers and young people from both sides in frequent visits, and use culture as a bridge to deepen mutual understanding and promote heart-to-heart connection.\nFifth question. The DPP authorities disregard public opinion and ignore people's livelihoods, and farmers and fishermen have long lost hope in them. We attach great importance to the wishes of Taiwanese farmer friends to open up the mainland market, and we actively cooperate. On the basis of comprehensive assessment of relevant rectification measures and compliance with mainland inspection and quarantine standards, we have gradually resumed imports of Taiwanese agricultural products such as sugar apples and pomelos.\nWe will continue to work with relevant parties on the island to establish a communication mechanism on the political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" actively advance the implementation of the ten measures, including agricultural products, in a thorough manner, provide assistance for importing Taiwanese agricultural and fishery products into the mainland on the premise of meeting inspection and quarantine standards, and strive to do practical things, good deeds, and solve difficulties for Taiwanese compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Question one: Regarding Lai Ching-te's cancellation of his trip to Eswatini, the DPP authorities said the reason was that “the mainland, through economic coercion, forcefully pressured three countries into temporarily canceling flight permits.” Please confirm this.\nQuestion two: On April 16, a Taiwanese fishing boat caught fire and sank near the Diaoyu Islands. On the 17th, the mainland coast guard said it was…","First question. The DPP authorities, trying to change tactics to achieve a “breakthrough” and failing, have fabricated the fallacy of so-called “economic coercion.” This is entirely deceptive, self-deluding, fabricated, and smearing talk, merely an attempt to conceal their own predicament.\nIt must be stressed that the historical course of the Taiwan question is clear, and the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China is plain. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory, and they cannot stop the inevitable trend toward the motherland's reunification. We hope broad Taiwan compatriots will recognize the ambitions and selfish desires of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatist actions.\nSecond question. It is understood that the mainland coast guard recently rescued a Taiwan fishing vessel that caught fire in the sea area northeast of Huangweiyu. It actively took part in firefighting and searched for Taiwan fishermen who fell into the water, rescuing 6 people.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding the facts and even taking the opportunity to smear and attack the mainland, not only desecrate the spirit of humanitarianism but also show indifference to the life and property safety of the Taiwan people.\nThe mainland has always promptly rescued distressed Taiwan vessels, demonstrating the brotherly bond of compatriots on both sides, whose blood is thicker than water and who look out for one another. This reflects the spirit of humanitarian rescue and is also an inevitable requirement of the mainland's consistent adherence to the principle that the lives of the people come first.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","Question one: Regarding the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce's statement that it hopes the mainland's ten policy measures will not be suspended for political reasons, and that cross-Strait economic and trade stability should be maintained in an institutionalized and normalized manner so that Taiwan's residents can view cross-Strait relations pragmatically, what is your comment?\nQuestion two: Regarding Lai Ching-te's…","First question. The current situation in cross-Strait relations remains complex and grave. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, colluding with external forces, plot “independence” and provoke confrontation, deliberately creating hostility and antagonism between the two sides and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This is the threat facing the Strait.\nWanting peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. We have always upheld the concept that compatriots across the Strait are one family, we adhere to promoting people's well-being through exchange and integration, and we actively do real, good, and problem-solving work for Taiwan compatriots. We are willing to strengthen exchange and dialogue with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all sectors of society on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and to advance the implementation of relevant policy measures. We hope all sectors in Taiwan will firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, work with us to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and help create a favorable atmosphere and conducive conditions for normalizing and routinizing personnel exchanges across the Strait and cooperation in all fields.\nSecond question. No matter how the DPP authorities collude with external forces or pursue so-called “diplomatic breakthroughs” in any form in service of the aim of “Taiwan independence,” it is all in vain. None of it can change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, nor can it shake the international community's universal consensus and basic framework of adhering to the One China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-22","Zhang Han","台湾TVBS电视台记者","Will the mainland side continue to use various means to block Lai Ching-te's “overseas trip”?","Our position is very clear. Those who act justly gain much support; those who do not gain little. Facts prove that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a broad consensus of the international community, and it is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people.\nToday’s press conference is concluded here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260422_12762160.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-04-23","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The U.S. State Department criticized China for influencing three African nations to not let Lai Ching-te fly through their airspace. Does the Foreign Ministry have a response or comment?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing consensus in the world. It is where the public opinion trends and the arc of history bends, and the right thing to do. It is fully just for China to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and for relevant countries to safeguard the one-China principle. The U.S.’s irresponsible accusations are nothing but a mischaracterization of the facts and truth. China firmly opposes it and will never accept it. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop using the Taiwan question to interfere in China’s internal affairs, stop supporting and consolidating the so-called “diplomatic allies” of Taiwan region, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260423_11898587.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260423_11898539.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-04-24","Guo Jiakun","CGTN","We’ve noted an alarming surge of neo-militarism in Japan over the recent month: A sitting SDF officer broke into the Chinese embassy in Japan carrying a knife; a Japanese destroyer transited the Taiwan Strait; the SDF for the first time officially participated in the joint military drill between the U.S. and the Philippines; the Japanese cabinet greatly eased controls on weapons export; and Sanae Takaichi sent…","This once again shows that the rampant and dangerous spread of neo-militarism in Japan is already a reality and poses real threats.\nBack in history, Japanese militarists have waged wars of aggression by fabricating “external threats,” stoking up nationalist sensation, and kidnapping state power. During the aggression, they committed horrendous crimes and brought profound sufferings to the people in the Asia Pacific. Today, rather than deeply reflecting on their history of aggression, Japanese right-wing forces have pushed for more offensive and expansionist defense policies and attempted to accelerate Japan’s remilitarization by rehabilitating its military-industrial complex.\nBesides, Japan has been lobbying around, peddling narratives with distorted facts in an attempt to prop up Japan’s image as a “peace-loving country”, which is already in tatters. However, the world is not easily beguiled. When a country seeks to revise its pacifist Constitution, eases restrictions on export of lethal weapons, deploys offensive missiles, and significantly increases military expenditure, its real intention is to pave the way for military expansion, no matter what it says. Japan has also been interacting frequently with NATO, in an effort to bring the non-regional military organization into the Asia Pacific. Its agenda of provoking confrontation is as clear as day.\nThe lessons of that dark history not far away must be remembered. Countries in the region including China must stay on high alert and jointly defend the outcomes of the victory of WWII. We must not allow Japanese militarism to be revived. We must not allow the tragedies of history to be repeated. We must not allow anyone or any force to undermine peace and sow disaster in our region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260424_11899448.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260424_11899403.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on April 29, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues across the Taiwan Strait.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The spokespersons of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office had previously explained three of the “seven betters” for Taiwan after peaceful reunification, which drew great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. What explanation does the spokesperson have regarding “After peaceful reunification, with a strong motherland as backing, Taiwan’s economic development will be better”?","During the “14th Five-Year Plan” period, the mainland’s total economic output reached a new level, with gross domestic product climbing to the 140-trillion-yuan mark, growing at an average annual rate of 5.4%, ranking among the top of the world’s major economies. Breakthroughs were achieved in technological and industrial innovation, new steps were taken in reform and opening up, and people’s livelihood and well-being reached a new level. The Outline of the “15th Five-Year Plan” makes strategic deployments in areas such as building a modern industrial system, accelerating high-level scientific and technological self-reliance and self-strengthening, building a strong domestic market, accelerating the construction of a high-level socialist market economy system, and expanding high-level opening to the outside world. This year marks the opening year of the “15th Five-Year Plan.” Although the external environment has become more complex and severe, the mainland’s economy got off to a good start in the first quarter, with gross domestic product (GDP) growing 5.0%, continuing to rank at the forefront among the world’s major economies. Growth rates of major macroeconomic indicators have rebounded, new growth drivers have grown rapidly, and new quality productive forces have developed steadily. The mainland’s economic development has strong momentum and abundant vitality, and its fundamental trend of stable progress and long-term improvement has not changed and will not change.\nAfter peaceful unification, drawing on the mainland’s advantages of a vast market and large economic scale, and combining Taiwan’s own technological strengths and talent advantages, Taiwan’s economy will regain new vitality, and Taiwan compatriots will receive tangible benefits. Cross-Strait trade will further unleash new growth momentum, and the mainland market of over 1.4 billion people will become a strong pillar for the steady growth of Taiwan’s economy. Cross-Strait industrial chains and supply chains will be deeply integrated, further activating the internal driving force of Taiwan’s industrial development. In upgrading traditional industries, Taiwan enterprises can achieve digital transformation and intelligent upgrading through collaborative innovation with upstream and downstream partners across the Strait, and bring vigorous momentum to high-end, intelligent, and green development. In growing emerging industries, Taiwan enterprises can develop new technologies, new products, and new application scenarios, enter more new fields and new tracks, and move up toward the high end of industrial and value chains. In deploying future industries, Taiwan enterprises can make good use of the mainland’s science and technology industry resources, actively integrate into the innovation ecosystem, and gain greater room for development. In addition, both sides will achieve interconnection and seamless access, and the flow of logistics, people, capital, and information will become smoother, providing more employment and entrepreneurship opportunities for the Taiwan public.\nPeaceful unification will inject greater certainty and growth potential into Taiwan’s investment and business environments, and is an unprecedented good opportunity and the greatest source of confidence for Taiwan’s economic development. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will join hands with mainland compatriots to promote peaceful unification of the two sides, share in the achievements of Chinese-style modernization, and create a bright future of sustained development and common prosperity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260429_12763396.htm"],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","April 23 marks the 77th anniversary of the founding of the People's Navy. During Navy Day, open-day activities for People's Navy vessels were held in Qingdao and other places, attracting Taiwan media reporters, several Taiwan commentators and internet celebrities, and many Taiwan residents. They praised the achievements of People's Navy development and said that with the People's Liberation Army protecting Taiwan…","Since the new era, the People's Navy has been striving for strength and heading toward the deep blue. This year's Navy Day open-house activities displayed the new achievements and new look of the People's Navy's development and demonstrated the People's Navy's firm resolve, strong determination, and formidable capabilities in defending territorial waters, airspace, and national sovereignty. The heartfelt exclamations of Taiwan's residents after their visit expressed the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait: only a first-class military and a strong national defense are the most reassuring backing for Chinese people at home and abroad, and the sharp sword that thwarts any scheme to split China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260429_12763390.htm"],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan's “Democratic Culture and Education Foundation” released the island's latest public opinion poll, which shows that 55.2% of residents believe it has become very difficult for Taiwan to “continue to maintain the status quo,” and 61.6% agree that “rather than waiting for the mainland to decide Taiwan's fate, it is better for Taiwan to take the initiative to participate in negotiations and propose…","Relevant opinion polls show that more and more Taiwan compatriots recognize that the historical trend toward the motherland's eventual and inevitable reunification is rolling forward and cannot be stopped. Under the premise of safeguarding national sovereignty, security, and development interests, after peaceful reunification, Taiwan's social system and way of life will be fully respected, and Taiwan compatriots' private property, religious beliefs, and legitimate rights and interests will be fully protected. Peaceful reunification will create enormous opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development, bring tangible benefits to the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots, and make Taiwan's future even brighter.\nOn the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to conduct extensive and in-depth consultations with people from Taiwan's political parties, sectors, and social strata on cross-Strait relations and national reunification, and to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the process of peaceful reunification of the motherland. We welcome broad Taiwan compatriots to actively offer suggestions and ideas toward realizing the prospect of peaceful reunification of the motherland, and to keep Taiwan's future and destiny firmly in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260429_12763394.htm"],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Taiwan media reported that after the so-called “US-Taiwan Reciprocal Trade Agreement” (ART) was signed, Taiwan lowered its inspection and quarantine standards for US potatoes, allowing sprouted potatoes to be imported into Taiwan. This has sparked food safety concerns and panic among the island's public. What is your comment?","We have noted relevant reports and are highly concerned about the health of Taiwan compatriots. Facing the United States using the so-called “U.S.-Taiwan reciprocal trade agreement” to carry out economic bullying and product dumping, the DPP authorities, defying the wishes of Taiwan's residents, have stubbornly persisted and openly abandoned the food safety bottom line. After resuming imports of Ractopamine-treated pork (“Lai pork”), they have now put “toxic potatoes” on the dinner tables of ordinary Taiwan people. Once again, they have made sacrificing the public's lives and health a “pledge of loyalty” to curry favor with the United States, in exchange for external forces' support for their “independence” schemes. Harming Taiwan and its people, they will surely be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","The mainland's Gaode Maps app recently launched a “traffic light countdown” feature in Taiwan, which has drawn praise from island residents, who say the navigation countdown is almost “zero error,” convenient and efficient. Some people in the DPP have claimed there are security concerns, and the DPP authorities have also said that once security concerns are confirmed, they will first require public agencies to…","The mainland possesses world-leading digital map, navigation and location service technologies. Several applications have been widely used for years in the mainland and in some countries and regions, meeting people's practical needs and making travel faster and more convenient and daily life more convenient and rich. This is a concrete embodiment of technological development benefiting humankind. Apart from Amap (Gaode Map), the mainland also has many innovative, high-quality products and advanced, cutting-edge technologies. Compatriots on both sides are one family, and we are glad to let Taiwan compatriots share them first.\nIn pursuit of “Taiwan independence,” the DPP authorities have gone so far in “anti-China” sentiment as to be anti-intelligence and anti-technology. Since the DPP came to power, a strange phenomenon has emerged in Taiwan society in which thought is shackled and speech is restrained. The most typical example is that one cannot say “no” to the US or say that the mainland is “good.” Simply because the mainland's technologies and products are good and Taiwan people like to use them, they block Taiwan people from using them. This is truly jumping at shadows (“treating a bow's reflection in a cup as a snake”), absurd and laughable. This practice is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260429_12763391.htm"],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Please have the spokesperson introduce what cross-Strait exchange activities have taken place recently.","This month, exchange activities in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have flourished and grown more vibrant. On the 8th, the Cross-Strait Cultural and Creative Industry Exchange and Cooperation Symposium was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. Experts, scholars, cultural and creative entrepreneurs, designers, and representatives of cultural institutions from both sides conducted in-depth exchanges on topics including the inheritance of Chinese culture, development of cultural and creative IP, and industrial cooperation and transformation, jointly exploring new avenues for cross-Strait cooperation in cultural and creative industries.\nFujian is separated from Taiwan by only a strip of water and is the province with the most frequent and active exchanges with Taiwan. The \"Fuyun Luoyuan, Shanhai Mingzhu\" (Fujian Luoyuan: Bright Pearl of Mountains and Sea) living heritage event for the Sanyue San (Third Month Third) folk culture of the She ethnic group was held on the 18th in Luoyuan County, Fuzhou City. Taiwan's Hualien Indigenous Dance Troupe performed alongside local She ethnic youth, deepening friendship between ethnic minority compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The 6th \"Handmade Qingcun\" Cross-Strait Youth Rural Creative Study Camp opened on the 19th in Jimei District, Xiamen, where more than 50 college students from both sides focused on five major themes, \"Family Affection, Neighborly Affection, Romantic Love, Hometown Affection, and Brotherly Affection,\" to explore the cultural origins between Fujian and Taiwan and create short plays about the story of integrated development across the Strait. The Ming-Tai Agricultural Specialty Industry Matchmaking Event, themed \"Drinking Together with One Heart, Ming-Tai Prosperity Together,\" was held on the 19th in Yong'an City, Sanming City. More than 60 Taiwanese young entrepreneurs, agricultural experts, and university scholars joined local residents in in-depth exchanges on agriculture and cultural tourism. The 2nd Two-Way Matching Conference for Employment, Internship, and Trainee Positions for Taiwan Students at Universities, themed \"Let Your Career Lead You, Build Dreams in Huli,\" was held in Huli District, Xiamen, from the 24th to the 26th. 92 quality enterprises offered 1,163 employment, internship, and trainee positions, providing two-way matching for more than 280 Taiwanese students from 66 cross-Strait universities. The \"Tea Harmony Symbiosis, Hearts Connected\" ecological and low-carbon tea exchange series was held on the 25th in the renowned tea-growing county of Anxi, where more than 100 tea practitioners from both sides exchanged techniques and sought common development. The 2026 Jinmen Family Study Camp, \"Xiamen-Kinmen Joy Fun Ocean,\" was held in Xiamen from the 25th to the 26th. 60 parent-child families from Kinmen and Xiamen together explored the mysteries of the ocean and experienced the appeal of marine technology.\n\"Huafeng Fashion — 2026 Chinese Aesthetics Fashion Development Conference\" was held in Shanghai on the 25th. Based on the shared inheritance and promotion of Chinese culture by both sides of the Strait, the conference used Chinese aesthetics to empower industrial development and promoted in-depth cross-Strait exchanges in diverse fields such as fashion design and cultural creativity. More than 300 industry representatives, designers, and youth representatives from both sides attended.\nFrom the 26th to the 30th, the Straits Exchange Foundation's Cross-Strait Exchange Fund and Beijing Normal University co-hosted the Cross-Strait Young Filmmakers Exchange Workshop. Activities included lectures by experts, scholars, and renowned film producers from mainland film and television industries, exchange seminars on creative work by young filmmakers from both sides, screenings of outstanding works by Taiwanese young filmmakers in recent years, and visits to the China Film Museum, among other activities.\nThe \"WAY! Come to Shenzhen\" 2026 Internship and Employment Program for Taiwanese Youth in Shenzhen has officially launched, offering 1,920 internship positions and 2,492 employment positions for Taiwanese youth, including Global Fortune 500 companies and industry leaders such as Tencent, Ping An, and the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, covering diverse fields including technology, finance, law, and healthcare. We welcome Taiwanese youth to pay close attention. From April 29 to May 3, the launch ceremony and cycling event series for the 2nd Cross-Strait Folk Sports Festival was held in Luhe County, Guangdong, where 300 Taiwanese young cyclists competed alongside mainland cyclists in the Hill Climbing King Challenge, the Guangdong Provincial Bicycle Greenway League, and other events.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and they should frequently visit each other and draw closer. Continuous action brings promising prospects. Each event and each gathering will surely turn the Strait from a barrier into a bridge, and ensure that family members no longer grow distant. The mainland of our motherland has magnificent mountains and rivers, a long cultural heritage, and ever-renewing developments. We warmly welcome our Taiwanese compatriots to visit and see for themselves more often. We are not afraid of you looking; we are only afraid of you not looking. We believe that compatriots who come to the mainland will find their trip worthwhile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","The “Fujian Provincial City Football League” (“Min Super League”) is currently being held in full swing, and the participation of players from both sides of the Strait in the same matches has drawn attention. What comment do you have on this? Will the mainland side, relying on Fujian’s geographic advantage vis-à-vis Taiwan, support more such civil sporting events and exchange activities in the future, providing a…","The “Min Super League” kicked off this year and is drawing huge crowds. The opening match alone attracted more than 51,000 spectators, setting a record for on-site attendance at a single sporting event in Fujian Province. The event rules explicitly welcome Taiwan compatriots who work and live in Fujian to join city representative teams. According to information, both the Pingtan representative team and its cheering squad include Taiwan compatriots, making the “Min Super League” an event with distinctive cross-Strait integration characteristics.\nBuilding a platform for exchange through sports events, allowing compatriots on both sides to deepen understanding and advance together through competition on the same field, is an innovative measure that Fujian has continuously pursued based on its unique advantages in dealing with Taiwan. It demonstrates the unique role of sports in fostering heartfelt connection among compatriots across the Strait and in advancing the construction of the cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone. In 2024, Fujian formed the Fujian Haishark baseball team through a “Fujian-Taiwan joint team” format to take part in mainland baseball leagues, the National Games, and other events.\nNext, Fujian will continue to hold nearly 100 cross-Strait civil sports events and exchange activities, providing a platform for young people on both sides to exchange ideas, compete, and deepen friendship. Young people from Taiwan are warmly welcome to take part actively.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding mainland coast guard and maritime safety enforcement patrols in Kinmen waters, Taiwan's coast guard department said it will record the entire process on video to gather evidence, and will inform other countries of “how the mainland uses gray-zone tactics to harass the Kinmen and Matsu areas.” What is your comment?","Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu are all sacred territory of China. The relevant mainland authorities’ law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters, which safeguard normal navigation and operational order and protect the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, are proper and lawful. The DPP authorities distort the facts and maliciously hype so-called “gray-zone harassment,” attempting to incite cross-Strait confrontation and “rely on outside forces to seek independence.” They will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Regarding the mainland's push, when conditions permit, to connect Kinmen and Matsu with water, electricity, gas, and bridges in order to enhance the well-being of residents of Kinmen and Matsu, Kinmen County recently formed a delegation to inspect Xiamen. Originally, Kinmen County Deputy Magistrate Li Wen-liang and Council Speaker Hung Yun-tien were to lead the delegation, but because the Mainland Affairs Council…","Promoting, where conditions permit, water, electricity, gas, and bridge connections between coastal areas of Fujian and Kinmen and Matsu, and supporting Kinmen's shared use of Xiamen's new airport, are positive measures we have taken to respond to the expectations of Kinmen and Matsu compatriots, enhance the interests and well-being of residents in both places, and promote development in the Kinmen and Matsu areas. The Kinmen delegation visiting Xiamen was deliberately held up by review, which fully exposes the true face of the DPP authorities in placing political self-interest above people's well-being. Their conduct goes against public opinion and does not win popular support, and it has already drawn strong opposition from Kinmen and Matsu residents and widespread criticism from Taiwan's public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Taiwan media reported that under the terms of the “U.S.-Taiwan Agreement on Reciprocal Trade” (ART), U.S. peanuts will enter Taiwan duty-free, and public opinion on the island worries this may lead to dumping of U.S. peanuts. Taiwan’s agriculture authorities said they are prepared to assist industrial transformation and to enhance the added value of Taiwan peanuts. What comment do you have on this?","The DPP authorities, relying on external forces, are unprincipled in fawning on foreigners and bottomlessly selling out Taiwan in trade negotiations with the United States, letting the US take whatever it demands. If the reports that US agricultural products will enter Taiwan with zero tariffs are true, they will inevitably have a serious impact on the development of Taiwan's agriculture and squeeze the survival space of farmers on the island. The DPP authorities' rhetoric of “industrial transformation and value-added upgrading” is nothing more than an empty statement meant to divert attention, placate the public and cover up losses. It cannot at all resolve the actual impact of dumping of imported agricultural products. Their one-sided opening of the market to the US and giving up profits to curry favor, while disregarding the livelihood and well-being of grassroots people at home, harms the interests of Taiwan's people and sacrifices the future of Taiwan's agriculture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Regarding Lai Ching-te's cancellation of his visit to Eswatini, some public opinion holds that more and more countries will regard adherence to the one-China principle as a rational decision, and that Taiwan will find it even harder to so-called “make friends” in the international community. Other public opinion holds that the Lai authorities are using this incident to extensively hype “mainland suppression,”…","Our position on Taiwan's external contacts has been consistent and clear: they must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The one-China principle is what the hearts of the people desire, the trend of the times, and the righteous cause. Anyone who tries to challenge the one-China principle in the international community will only meet with rebuffs everywhere.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the position of “Taiwan independence” and are the instigators of the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. The Lai Ching-te authorities tried to achieve so-called “diplomatic breakthroughs” through “outward forays,” and after being rejected by the relevant countries, they not only refuse to repent, but also openly distort the facts and fabricate a so-called “victim” narrative to deceive the people on the island. The DPP has brought this on itself and courted humiliation. Its habitual tricks have long been seen through by the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202604/t20260429_12763392.htm"],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Regarding the traffic accident involving Taiwanese travelers in Gansu, the Mainland Affairs Council said it immediately contacted the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) to understand the situation through the Straits Exchange Foundation's contacts with the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS). Under the cross-strait agreement mechanisms, did the mainland proactively make a…","First question. As is well known, because the DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, the communication mechanism between the two sides’ two associations has long been suspended. We hope the DPP authorities will stop deceiving Taiwan compatriots on this issue.\nRegarding the accident involving Taiwan compatriots in Gansu, the Taiwan Affairs Office and governments at all levels in Gansu Province immediately activated emergency mechanisms, made every effort to provide medical assistance to the injured Taiwan compatriots, initiated the claims process for travel accident insurance, and assisted the families in handling the aftermath. We mourn the Taiwan compatriot who died in the misfortune and extend sympathy to the family and the injured Taiwan compatriots. We hope cross-Strait tourism exchanges can resume as soon as possible, carried out safely and in an orderly manner. The DPP authorities should promptly cancel the “group travel ban” and other unpopular restrictive measures, and create favorable conditions for restoring normal cross-Strait tourism exchanges.\nTaiwan compatriots are our family and kin. The mainland side has always attached great importance to protecting the lives and property of Taiwan compatriots, and has taken practical and effective measures to safeguard their legitimate rights and interests. It was so in the past, and it will be so in the future.\nSecond question. April 23 this year marked the 77th anniversary of the founding of the PLA Navy. On that day, the Navy opened six warships to the public in Qingdao, Shandong. Many Taiwan compatriots took part in the open-day activities, boarded the warships, exchanged views with Navy officers and sailors, and experienced firsthand on site the great strength and fine conduct of the People’s Navy. The mission of the People’s Navy is to defend the country and protect the people, which naturally includes Taiwan compatriots. The remarks made by Taiwan compatriots expressed sincere national sentiment and won praise from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same language and ancestry, and share weal and woe; they should firmly identify with the Chinese nation, Chinese culture, and the great motherland, and strengthen the resolve, spirit, and confidence to be upright and proud Chinese.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding facts, infringe on freedom of speech, intimidate and suppress people who participate in cross-Strait exchanges and dare to speak out for justice, and vigorously engage in “green terror” and “Taiwan independence authoritarianism.” Those who commit many unrighteous acts will inevitably bring about their own downfall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: regarding the traffic accident involving a Taiwan compatriot tour group in Gansu, what was the cause of the accident? Second question: among the ten measures benefiting Taiwan proposed by the mainland, which can be promoted unilaterally by the mainland side without needing to consult the Taiwan side? Is there a specific timetable for implementation?","First question. Following the cross-Strait traffic safety accident involving Taiwan compatriots in Xiahe County, Gansu Province, on April 24, relevant departments in Gansu Province attached great importance to the matter and made every effort to treat the injured Taiwan compatriots. Most of the injured have now been discharged from hospital and are expected to return to Taiwan soon. Relevant parties have also actively assisted the families of the Taiwan compatriot who died in the accident with the aftermath, and the families have already returned to Taiwan. Regarding the cause of the accident, relevant departments are conducting a further investigation, and any conclusions will be announced in a timely manner.\nSecond question. The introduction of the ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation fully reflects our position of promoting people's well-being through exchange and integration. The aim is to advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots on both sides. The Central Taiwan Work Office and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office will coordinate relevant departments and localities to promote thorough implementation of these policy measures. At the same time, on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchange and dialogue with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all sectors of society, and to work together to advance related work. We believe that sharing peace, pursuing development, and achieving prosperity together across the Strait is a blessing for compatriots on both sides, and it will certainly win broad support from the Taiwan public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Taiwan's defense authorities recently said they have signed multiple arms procurement contracts with the US, including six items such as anti-armor missiles and the joint production of large-caliber ammunition. What is your comment?","We firmly oppose any form of military ties between the United States and the Taiwan region of China. The US side should abide by the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, especially the “August 17 Communiqué,” and immediately stop selling weapons to Taiwan and stop arming Taiwan.\nThe DPP authorities, to seek the political self-interest of “Taiwan independence,” are willing to serve as the “ATM” of the US military-industrial complex and beg for “protection” from external forces that cannot be relied upon. This will only plunge Taiwan into an even more dangerous situation and bring profound disaster to Taiwan compatriots. We warn the DPP authorities: the reunification of the motherland is irresistible. No matter how many weapons they buy, it is like a mantis trying to stop a chariot. They cannot change the inevitable defeat of “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Regarding the full restoration of normalized cross-strait air passenger direct flights, the Mainland Affairs Council said that airlines will apply if they believe there is profit to be made. Taiwan's transportation authorities said that cross-strait direct flights currently have 15 open scheduled flight points and 13 open charter flight points, covering nearly all points estimated to have regular…","First question. The cross-Strait air direct flights agreement is an important cooperative arrangement reached by both sides on the principles of equality, mutual benefit, and benefiting the people’s livelihood, and it should be jointly upheld and faithfully implemented by both parties. The DPP authorities have unilaterally undermined the agreement and arbitrarily adjusted the policy on destinations, changing regular scheduled direct-flight points into charter-only points with cumbersome procedures and harsh conditions in violation of the agreement. Even when airlines apply, they are blocked through “dissuasion” or “refusal to accept,” artificially creating barriers to civil aviation exchanges. This not only increases the operating costs and organizational difficulty for cross-Strait airlines, but also makes travel between the two sides cumbersome and inconvenient for broad compatriots on both sides, seriously damaging the lawful rights and interests of the industry. It is tantamount to turning cross-Strait air direct flights backward.\nIn the face of market demand and public calls, the DPP authorities, on the one hand, restrict destinations and dissuade acceptance of applications, and on the other hand use the pretext that airlines are “unprofitable” and unwilling to fly. Such tactics are despicable. This practice, which violates market rules, disregards the spirit of contracts, and ignores people’s livelihood needs, precisely shows that they are not failing to do the economic math but are only doing the political-manipulation math. What they care about is by no means the development of the cross-Strait civil aviation industry and the interests of the people, but a party’s political self-interest.\nSecond question. In February this year, the mainland side announced that residents of Shanghai would be allowed to travel to Kinmen and Matsu again. This reconnaissance trip is the follow-up implementation of the outcomes of the KMT-CPC think tank forum. We welcome Shanghai tourism operators visiting Kinmen for on-site inspection and holding discussions and exchanges with Taiwan operators. The Shanghai reconnaissance group arrived in Kinmen smoothly, fully demonstrating our sincerity in practicing the concept of cross-Strait families being one family and in advancing the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We hope relevant parties in Taiwan will heed public opinion, remove obstacles, and take pragmatic measures to promote normalization of personnel exchanges between the two sides and the regularization of exchanges in all fields. After the reconnaissance group’s itinerary concludes, relevant follow-up matters will be announced to the public.\nThird question. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and are one family. Cross-Strait affairs are household matters of compatriots on both sides and should of course be discussed and handled within the family. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait are fully wise and capable of resolving their own affairs and safeguarding and building their own homeland.\nAt the same time, I must emphasize that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. We urge the U.S. side to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and handle Taiwan-related issues appropriately.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-04-29","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","More and more Taiwan residents are traveling to the mainland. How will the mainland side protect the rights and safety of Taiwan tourists in the mainland? Will both sides consider restoring existing communication mechanisms or establishing new communication channels for this purpose?","Before the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities imposed restrictions such as the “group travel ban” and “orange alert” on travel to the mainland, Taiwan compatriots had been traveling to the mainland for many years, and overall it went very smoothly. The cross-strait tourism industries have also always maintained very smooth channels, including emergency coordination channels after accidents, which have operated effectively and been recognized by compatriots on both sides.\nBelow, I will announce the situation of the 11th Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz event.\nOn April 13, the WeChat official account of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council released the questions for the 11th “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz,” and netizens enthusiastically took part. As of April 27, the top ten netizens with correct answers and the most message likes, in order, were: “归舟映月,” “潮汐同心,” “爱台海,” “柒妤,” “好好吃饭,” “后尘,” “莫尘,” “冬日暖阳,” “小呆呆,” and “云博.” We congratulate these ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite commemorative gift, the shell carving “Treasure Island Taiwan.” We hope netizens will continue to care about Taiwan-related work and actively take part in promoting the peaceful development of cross-strait relations.\nOn May 11, the WeChat official account of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will release the questions for the 12th “Taiwan-related Knowledge Quiz.” Everyone is welcome to participate enthusiastically!\nToday's press conference ends here.\nAs the “May Day” holiday approaches, I wish the hardworking journalist friends a happy holiday and a healthy, harmonious family. Thank you all!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202604/t20260429_12763382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-04-30","Lin Jian","Hubei Media Group","It’s reported that the Nonpartisan Parliamentary Association for Reconsidering Human Rights Diplomacy convened a meeting at the Diet to discuss the blockade of Lai Ching-te’s trip to Africa and planned to submit a statement to the Japanese government. The statement pointed out that the diplomatic independence of any country shall not be undermined by any coercion. It also demands that the Japanese government play…","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community. China highly commends relevant countries’ concrete actions in upholding the one-China principle and opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, which are fully consistent with international law and basic norms governing international relations.\nThe Japanese side must not forget that the 1972 Sino-Japanese Joint Statement states that “The Government of Japan recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China. The Government of the People’s Republic of China reiterates that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The Government of Japan fully understands and respects this stand of the Government of the People’s Republic of China, and it firmly maintains its stand under Article 8 of the Potsdam Proclamation.” The 1978 Treaty of Peace and Friendship Between China and Japan, ratified by the two countries’ legislatures, affirmed that the principles set out in the 1972 Joint Statement should be strictly observed. Since the two countries normalized relations, the Japanese government has stated on many occasions that the Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. These are legal obligations Japan must fulfill and political commitments it must honor.\nAs to issues related to foreign policy independence, democracy and human rights, I notice that many people with insight in Japan are reflecting on Japan’s domestic and foreign policies. There are also many discussions on “comfort women,” forced war labor, and other issues left from history, as well as indigenous peoples and minority rights in Japan. Yet some politicians in Japan either keep silent and play deaf to those issues or point fingers on Taiwan which is inherently part of China. Guess they are the only ones who know what its hidden objective is.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202604/t20260430_11903597.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202604/t20260430_11903286.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-05-02","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked that Lai Qingde's previous visit to Swaziland was frustrated because the relevant country refused to issue a charter flight permit. According to reports, Lai Qingde secretly got into Swaziland's plane and arrived in Swaziland on May 2. Any comment on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to inquiries that Lai Qingde's previous attempt to visit Swaziland on a chartered flight was canceled because the relevant countries adhered to the one-China principle. However, he was unwilling to fail and even ignored his face and sneaked to Swaziland in a sneaky way. Currently, the island is experiencing an earthquake, but Lai Qingde is ignoring it. This shows that he is cold-blooded and ruthless towards the people on the island, has a stubborn stance on \"Taiwan independence\", and is a complete \"troublemaker\".\nAdhering to the one-China principle is the aspiration of the people of the international community, the general trend and the great cause of justice. Lai Qingde's dirty behavior is like a rat crossing the street and will be ridiculed by the international community. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and living a stable and prosperous life are the aspirations of the people on the island. Lai Qingde disregarded the safety of the people and wantonly deceived the people, and will be spurned by the majority of Taiwan compatriots. The so-called \"diplomatic results\" that Lai Qingde worked so hard to concoct are nothing but tricks and make the world laugh. The inevitable trend of reunification of the motherland is rolling forward and unstoppable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260502_12763833.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-06","Lin Jian","China Daily","Lai Ching-te sneaked into Eswatini on its plane. While in Eswatini, he spoke about “diplomatic independence.” Yet the international community and people in Taiwan described his action as “thief-like” and an “international joke.” What is your response?","Even though there was widespread opposition, Lai Ching-te sneaked onto a foreign plane and cheated himself into Eswatini by concealing passenger information with the country. On his return flight, after use of airspace was rejected by relevant countries, Lai again slipped onto the plane and forced his way through these countries’ skies. The whole thing showed the world how little Lai respects relevant countries’ airspace and sovereignty and cares for the opinion of the world. What he did was extremely dangerous and outrageous. The fact that he would smuggle himself in and out of the country shows exactly “Taiwan independence” separatism is just shady business and unacceptable to the international community. His act was nothing but a scandalous stunt.\nSome politicians in Eswatini who are kept in Taiwan’s pay have been wrongly providing space for “Taiwan independence.” China strongly condemns it. In recent years, we’ve heard people from various sectors in so-called Taiwan’s “diplomatic allies” strongly call on their countries to grow ties with China. Which is the right thing to do? To see where the arc of history bends and follow their people’s will, or to continue serving as a political prop and keeping up the appearances for Lai Ching-te and his kind? The politicians in these countries need to come to the wise decision and stop going further down the doomed path.\nThere’s but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is an international consensus that has solid support and is simply unshakable. The pursuit of “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and its days are numbered. Any new attempt Lai Ching-te makes to advance his separatist agenda will only box himself further in. We urge those separatists to turn back from the wrong path and mend their ways sooner rather than later.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260506_11905648.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260506_11905572.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-06","Lin Jian","Reuters","I have two questions. The first one is a follow-up to Taiwan leader Lai Ching-te’s return flight from Eswatini. Based on the flight route that we’ve seen, he has taken a rather long flight path back to Taiwan. So we wanted to know if China has spoken or made any requests to countries such as Madagascar and Mauritius about letting his flight through their airspace? Also, we noted that on his way back, he did fly…","Whether to open a country’s airspace falls within the country’s sovereignty. Relevant countries, in upholding the one-China principle, have refused to issue flight permits for Lai Ching-te’s visit. This just act is fully consistent with international law and basic norms in international relations, and fully proves that the one-China principle is where the arc of history bends and that “Taiwan independence” separatist moves have no support.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260506_11905648.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260506_11905572.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-05-06","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The company where Yan Wenqun, the nephew of the \"Taiwan independence\" die-hard Liu Shifang, works, issued a statement yesterday severing Yan Wenqun from all positions in the Taiwan head office and the mainland branch. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to inquiries that \"Taiwan independence\" undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and harms the interests of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. It is a dead end. \"Taiwan independence\" harms others and ourselves and must be punished. We will never allow \"Taiwan independence\" die-hards and their relatives to invest and do business in the mainland for profit, and we will never allow those who support \"Taiwan independence\" and undermine cross-Strait relations to make money on the mainland while supporting \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. Our measures to punish \"independence\" only target a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" elements and do not involve the vast number of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese companies. We will, as always, welcome and support the broad masses of Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese companies to take root in the development of the motherland, share the opportunities and achievements of Chinese-style modernization development, and give Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese companies a greater sense of happiness and gain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260506_12764333.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-07","Lin Jian","CCTV","With the China-U.S. presidential meeting approaching, there is speculation that Taiwan tops Beijing’s agenda for the summit. What’s your comment?","The Taiwan question is at the very core of China’s core interests, and the bedrock of the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. Abiding by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and honoring the commitments made by U.S. administrations on the Taiwan question is the U.S.’s due international obligation and the prerequisite for a steady, sound and sustainable China-U.S. relationship. China has unwavering resolve in safeguarding national unity and territorial integrity. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, there must be unequivocal opposition to “Taiwan independence.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260507_11906405.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260507_11906358.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-07","Lin Jian","TV Tokyo","Responding at the Diet on November 7 last year, Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi said that a Taiwan emergency involving the use of military vessels and military force from the Chinese mainland could constitute a “survival-threatening situation” for Japan. It has been six months since then. I wonder if you have any comment today?","We have made clear China’s solemn position on multiple occasions. The root cause of the serious difficulties in bilateral relations lies in Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. The responsibility rests solely with the Japanese side. Genuine exchange and dialogue is only possible when there is respect and consensus is honored. If the Japanese side truly hopes to improve relations with China, it should abide by the four political documents between the two countries and the commitments it made to China, retract its erroneous remarks, and safeguard the political foundation for bilateral relations with concrete actions. We urge the Japanese authorities to face up to the root cause of the issue, do soul-searching, rectify their wrongdoings, and create necessary conditions for normal exchanges between China and Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260507_11906405.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260507_11906358.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-07","Lin Jian","EFE","Paraguay’s president Santiago Peña is right now visiting Taiwan with a delegation of business leaders, reaffirming ties between the two sides. How does China respond to this visit?","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. On the basis of this principle, a total of 183 countries have established diplomatic relations with China. We urge the Paraguayan authorities to come to the right side of history as soon as possible, and make the right decision to recognize the one-China principle and sever so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260507_11906405.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260507_11906358.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-07","Lin Jian","Asahi Shimbun","Exchanges between Japan and China have been dwindling. Does the Chinese side hope to see people-to-people exchange between the two countries restored?","As I pointed out just now, the root cause of the serious difficulties in bilateral relations lies in Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. The responsibility rests solely with the Japanese side. If the Japanese side truly hopes to improve relations with China, it should abide by the four political documents between the two countries and the commitments it made to China, retract its erroneous remarks, safeguard the political foundation for bilateral relations with concrete actions, and create necessary conditions for normal exchanges with China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260507_11906405.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260507_11906358.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-08","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","Honduras’ new president said his government needs to review his predecessor’s agreements with China. He also said that equipment from Huawei will be part of the review, and Honduras is in talks with the U.S. on using tech from Cisco. Does the foreign ministry have any comments on this?","The report puts headline-grabbing sensationalism before journalistic ethics of reporting the truth, taking things out of context, misrepresenting facts and sowing discord. Let me stress, there is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm governing international relations. It is the political foundation and prerequisite for the development of China-Honduras ties and bilateral cooperation. There is not the slightest room for ambiguity here. Since the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Honduras, the two sides have engaged in practical cooperation across various fields in the principle of mutual respect and equal consultation, delivering win-win outcomes that greatly benefit the two peoples and gaining popular support in both countries. Facts fully prove that upholding the one-China principle is the right choice that accords with the trend of history and our times, and serves the fundamental interests of Honduras and its people. The separatist attempts of “Taiwan independence” forces find no support and are doomed to fail.\nAs to the agreements between China and Honduras that you mentioned, I would like to stress that China-Honduras cooperation does not target any third party and should be free from disruptions from any third party. The legitimate and lawful rights and interests of the Chinese side must be fully respected.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260508_11907266.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260508_11907163.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-08","Lin Jian","AFP","The Paraguay president got a red carpet welcome in Taiwan today and met the Taiwan leader. What is China’s comment?","I answered a related question yesterday. Let me reiterate, the one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. On the basis of this principle, a total of 183 countries have established diplomatic relations with China. We urge the Paraguayan authorities to come to the right side of history as soon as possible, and make the right decision to recognize the one-China principle and sever so-called “diplomatic ties” with the Taiwan authorities.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260508_11907266.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260508_11907163.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-05-09","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the PLA recently dispatched naval and air forces to conduct joint combat-readiness patrols around the Taiwan Island, while sending a task force of main battleshipsto waters southwest of Penghu. Some analysts believe that the increased number of PLA vessels and aircraft crossing the so-called median line of the Taiwan Strait may be related to the recent overseas visit by Taiwan's leadership.…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory , and there is no so-called \"median line\" of the Taiwan Strait. Military operations carried out by the PLA in relevant areas are completely legitimate and justified. \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces are the root cause of tensions and the primary source of instability in the Taiwan Strait, whichwe will never tolerate or condone. The PLA will continue to take concrete actions to resolutely safeguard China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, and firmly uphold peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16460455.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16459588.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-05-11","Guo Jiakun","Phoenix TV","The 79th World Health Assembly (WHA) will open on May 18. Taiwan has not yet been invited to attend. Does the Chinese government have any comment on that?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. China’s position on the Taiwan region’s participation in the activities of international organizations, including the WHO, is consistent and clear. That is, this must be handled in line with the one-China principle, which is also a fundamental principle recognized by UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1.\nChina’s Taiwan region, unless given approval by the Central Government, has no basis, reason or right to participate in the WHA. Due to the DPP authorities’ persistent separatist stance, the political foundation for the Taiwan region to participate in the WHA no longer exists. To uphold the one-China principle as well as the sanctity and authority of relevant UNGA and WHA resolutions, China has decided not to approve the Taiwan region’s participation in this year’s WHA. Any attempt to play the “Taiwan card” for political manipulation in defiance of the one-China principle is doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260511_11908438.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260511_11908352.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-12","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It is reported that President of Paraguay Santiago Peña visited Taiwan from May 7 to 10. He met with Lai Ching-te on May 8 in Taipei and signed several so-called “cooperation documents.” President Peña claimed that Paraguay supported Taiwan’s “participation in international multilateral systems,” “the international community should recognize Taiwan,” and Taiwan does not need to worry about changes in their…","China firmly opposes and condemns such moves made by the Paraguayan side. There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The one-China principle is a basic norm governing international relations and a prevailing consensus in the international community. Over the years, we have heard time and again the strong call of people from various sectors in Paraguay to develop relations with China. According to a poll in Paraguay, nearly 90 percent of the respondents supported establishing diplomatic ties with China. This fully demonstrates that establishing diplomatic relations with China serves the fundamental and long-term interests of the Paraguayan people, and that colluding with the Taiwan authorities wins no support. Relevant Paraguayan political figures not only turn a blind eye to it, but also blatantly visit Taiwan to endorse Lai Ching-te and his like in defiance of global criticism and willingly serve as chess pieces for “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. It’s apparent for all whether it is truly for the benefit of the Paraguayan people or for some ulterior motive.\nWe urge the Paraguayan government to change course at an early date, see where the arc of history bends, follow their people’s will, and make the right political decision to recognize the one-China principle. The wheels of history wait for no one. Rejecting the one-China principle will only isolate oneself from the international community.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260512_11909099.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260512_11909048.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-12","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","U.S. President Trump said yesterday that he would discuss with the Chinese side the U.S. arms sales to Taiwan and about Jimmy Lai’s case. Is China prepared to engage on these topics with Trump?","During President Trump’s visit to China, the two heads of state will have an in-depth exchange of views on major issues concerning China-U.S. relations and world peace and development.\nChina’s firm opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear. As to the Lai Chee-ying case, China has made its position clear more than once.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260512_11909099.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260512_11909048.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-12","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi remains unwilling to retract what she said on Taiwan last November. We see that China has been amplifying criticism of Japan’s neo-militarism. Meanwhile, Sanae Takaichi and other Japanese officials have visited many countries in a short period of time to explain Japan’s “peaceful” stance, while easing restrictions on export of lethal weapons and planning to revise its…","Japanese militarism inflicted untold suffering on people in the Asia Pacific. The prosperity enjoyed by Asia-Pacific countries rests on the peaceful foundation laid down by the post-WWII international order. But the reality that must not be ignored is that Japan’s right-wing forces are gearing up with an actual roadmap to tear apart that order and foundation, and the action has already begun. The “gray rhino” of Japan’s remilitarization is charging towards us. Many international experts, scholars and media reports have pointed to Japan’s abandonment of pacifism and most dangerous shift in military and security policy since WWII, which threatens peace and stability in the region and beyond. History shall not be forgotten. Reality shall not go unchecked. All Asia-Pacific countries need to stay clear-eyed and jointly reject Japanese neo-militarism to safeguard the order of peace on which all countries rely to live and thrive.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260512_11909099.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260512_11909048.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-13","Guo Jiakun","Phoenix TV","It is reported that Lai Ching-te addressed the Copenhagen Democracy Summit 2026 via video. The Summit is hosted by an NGO in Denmark. Lai said that the Taiwanese people have every right to engage with the international community. The people of Taiwan have never backed down in the face of mounting external challenges. Taiwan is a “ sovereign independent nation.” What’s your comment?","The Copenhagen Democracy Summit you mentioned is filled with ideological bias. The summit deliberately invited “Taiwan independence” separatists to broadcast their nefarious proposition. This is a severe violation of the one-China principle. China firmly opposes it and urges relevant parties to adhere to the one-China principle and stop offering platforms for “Taiwan independence” forces.\nTaiwan is part of China. It has never been a country and will never be a country. The one-China principle is an international consensus that has solid support and is simply unshakable. Lai Ching-te and his kind chant so-called “democracy” in defiance of mainstream public opinion in Taiwan for peaceful development of cross-Strait ties, peddle their “Taiwan independence” separatist narrative, spread disinformation and incite antagonism and confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. Such moves once again expose their reckless, provocative and diehard stance of pursuing “Taiwan independence.” Whatever Lai Ching-te says or does, it does not change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, evidenced by both history and law, nor will it ever undermine international commitment to the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260513_11909838.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260513_11909783.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on May 13, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning! Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. I would like to ask your questions below.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","新华社记者","The third Cross-Strait Chinese Cultural Summit opened in Beijing on May 11. Please introduce the main situation and results of this summit.","In order to thoroughly implement Xi Jinping's cultural thoughts and the spirit of the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping when he met with Chinese Kuomintang Chairman Zheng Liwen, further promote cross-strait cultural exchanges, and jointly promote Chinese culture, relevant institutions and cultural groups on both sides of the strait will hold the third Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit in Beijing from May 11 to 13. A total of about 2,000 guests from both sides of the Taiwan Strait attended the conference, including about 1,000 Taiwanese guests, cultural representatives, youth and grassroots representatives.\nThe Cross-Strait Chinese Culture Summit has the permanent theme of \"Inheritance, Promotion, and Development\". This summit takes \"Connected by Blood and Connected Cultures\" as its annual theme. It holds an opening ceremony, a main forum, sub-forums on literature, cultural creativity, film and television, drama, traditional culture, and a cross-Strait media summit. It also holds summit special exhibitions, symphony concerts, Peking Opera performances and other performances, and organizes cross-Strait clans, \"Taiwanese Youth Watch Beijing\" and other societies and youth cultural exchange activities. The holding of these activities will definitely further promote the spiritual unity of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits and work together to promote Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765378.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has explained four of the \"seven better things\" for Taiwan after peaceful reunification at previous press conferences, which has attracted great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's explanation for \"After peaceful reunification, with the backing of a strong motherland, Taiwan's spiritual and…","\"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" are the best way to achieve national reunification and best serve the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. After reunification, in the embrace of a strong motherland, the spiritual and cultural lives of Taiwan compatriots will be better protected, developed further, and improved faster.\nFirst, the cultural roots return to the true spiritual home. Chinese culture is the root and origin of the souls of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits. After peaceful reunification, China's excellent traditional culture, historical memory, and national spirit will be better inherited and promoted in Taiwan, and the Taiwanese people will no longer be in a state of ambiguous cultural identity and confused historical understanding. From Minnan culture and Hakka culture to folk beliefs, literature and art, they can all shine brighter when nourished by the roots of Chinese culture. Taiwan compatriots who were born as Chinese will have a more fulfilling spiritual world and a stronger sense of belonging.\nSecond, the space for cultural development will be greatly expanded, and cultural undertakings will become more prosperous. After peaceful reunification, the cultural creativity of Taiwanese society will be fully unleashed. Taiwanese literature, film and television, music, publishing and other works can easily enter the huge mainland market and receive policy and resource support in cultural undertakings, cultural industries, talent training, intangible inheritance and other aspects. People in the relevant industry can achieve better development on a larger platform and more opportunities, and gain more development opportunities internationally. Cross-Strait cultural exchanges are booming, and Taiwan's cultural characteristics will shine brightly in the overall prosperity of Chinese culture.\nThe third is to get rid of political manipulation, and the spiritual world will be clearer and more peaceful. For a long time, the spiritual culture of Taiwanese society has been seriously disturbed by political party disputes and ideological confrontations, and education, media, and public opinion have been deliberately distorted and fiercely opposed. After peaceful reunification, political manipulation was corrected, and the society on the island turned from confusion and anxiety to calmness and calmness, with people's hearts being stable and society being harmonious. The people's needs for spiritual and cultural life will be better met, and they can live with peace of mind, focus on development, and pursue happiness, and will no longer be trapped in confrontation and tearing.\nFourth, the national dignity has been improved and the ambition and confidence have been strengthened. After peaceful reunification, Taiwan compatriots have strong backing from the powerful motherland no matter where they are in the world. They are no longer \"chess pieces\" in international games, and no longer fear being looked down upon by outsiders. Instead, they are Chinese people who hold their heads high and are upright. They will be the masters of the great motherland, their national self-confidence and pride will be comprehensively enhanced, and they will gain the most fundamental and lasting spiritual enrichment.\nThe extensive and profound Chinese culture is the common \"root\" and \"soul\" of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits, and is our common heirloom. Standing at the historical tide of national rejuvenation, only by joining hands and moving toward each other can compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait deepen the cultural integration and strengthen the friendship between our compatriots, so that every Taiwan compatriot can reap stable happiness and rejuvenate with a new spirit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765377.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te delivered a video speech at the \"Copenhagen Democracy Summit\", claiming that \"Taiwan is a sovereign and independent country\", spreading the narrative of \"democracy versus authoritarianism\", and advocating unity and cooperation to protect \"democracy\". What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a historical and legal fact that cannot be denied or denied. Taiwan has never been a country. It has not been in the past and it will definitely not be in the future. Lai Qingde's lie is still a lie even if it is told a thousand times, and it will never become true.\nThe Lai Ching-tak authorities are accustomed to bluffing in the international arena under the guise of \"democracy\", wooing anti-China forces in certain countries, using the so-called \"summit\" to spread the false narrative of \"democracy versus authoritarianism\", inciting cross-strait confrontation, and engaging in acts of separatism. It is a complete political farce that has long been seen through by the world and will only be spurned by all Chinese people. Lai Qingde's poor performance cannot conceal his despicable behavior and authoritarian nature of constantly cracking down on political dissidents and suppressing speech on the island. \"Democracy\" is false, but seeking \"independence\" is true.\nOur will to oppose \"Taiwan independence\" is as solid as a rock, and our ability to crush \"Taiwan independence\" is indestructible. Relevant agencies should fully recognize the high sensitivity of the Taiwan issue and the serious harm of supporting \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, abide by the one-China principle, and stop providing convenience and a stage for the DPP authorities to seek \"independence\" internationally.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765376.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, an inter-provincial working meeting on building a cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone was held in Beijing. What is the current status of the implementation of the \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian to Explore a New Road for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Build a Cross-Strait Integrated Development…","Since the release of the \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring New Roads for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone\" in September 2023, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the National Development and Reform Commission, together with relevant departments of the central and state agencies and Fujian Province, have resolutely implemented the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee, comprehensively promoted the implementation of the key tasks of the \"Opinions\" and effectively promoted the deepening and solidification of the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone. In the past three years, the demonstration effect of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone on Taiwan has gradually emerged and its influence has been increasingly expanded. It has become more convenient for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese companies to land in their first home, economic and trade exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan have continued to be vigorous, Fujian has maintained a good momentum of deepening cross-Strait integrated development, Fujian and Taiwan have continued to deepen humanistic and social exchanges, and the construction of the demonstration zone has made significant progress.\nIn the next step, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the National Development and Reform Commission will work with relevant departments of the central and state agencies and Fujian Province to thoroughly implement General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important expositions on Taiwan work and the Party Central Committee’s decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work, closely focusing on the goal of building a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone tasks, strengthen responsibility, strengthen planning and advancement, support Fujian in continuously exploring new paths and new models for cross-Strait integrated development, launch more innovative measures, deepen the integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan in various fields, and accumulate replicable and promoteable experience for deepening cross-Strait integrated development on a larger scale.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765375.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the dismissal of Yan Wenqun, the nephew of the \"Taiwan independence\" die-hard Liu Shifang, from his Taiwanese company, Liu Shifang said, \"Taiwanese people must be careful when going to the mainland, otherwise their personal safety and property safety will be threatened.\" The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said it \"will study countermeasures,\" and the Straits Exchange Foundation also reminded Taiwanese…","Liu Shifang's pursuit of \"Taiwan independence\" is a criminal act of splitting the country and inciting secession. Yan Wenqun has long been benefiting from the mainland, but has provided Liu with political donations. The two men were punished in accordance with the law and deserved their punishment. Liu Shifang has no intention of repenting and rehabilitating herself, but she fabricates lies in an attempt to sway the Taiwanese people and create a \"chilling effect\", which is disgraceful. In recent years, Taiwanese compatriots have continued to come to the mainland more enthusiastically without fear of obstruction and intimidation from the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. The proportion of Taiwanese young people among them has continued to increase, which shows that Liu Shifang and his like have not succeeded and will not succeed in their attempts to intimidate the Taiwanese people.\nOur attitude is consistent. Punishing \"independence\" in accordance with the law and hanging a sharp sword are aimed at a very small number of \"Taiwan independence\" die-hards and do not involve the vast number of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese companies. As long as Taiwan compatriots are willing to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and do not engage in separatist activities, we welcome them to come to the mainland for sightseeing, exchanges, study, life, employment, and entrepreneurship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765374.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, the State Council announced the \"Regulations on Industrial Chain and Supply Chain Security.\" Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council stated that this has put pressure on foreign investors and Taiwanese businessmen in mainland China to comply with the law, and they are trapped in the dilemma of \"complying with relevant US bans will violate mainland Chinese laws, and ignoring the bans will result in US…","The \"Regulations on Industrial Chain and Supply Chain Security\" focuses on promoting high-level opening up to the outside world and promoting the stability and smoothness of global industrial and supply chains. It fills the mainland's legislative gaps in related fields and protects Taiwan-funded enterprises operating legally and compliantly in the mainland. The sanctions involved are aimed at implementing or assisting in the implementation of behaviors that endanger the safety of the mainland's supply chain, and do not target companies that operate legally and compliantly. As for the so-called \"increased personal safety risks for businessmen in mainland China and Taiwan\", it is pure nonsense and a common tactic used by the DPP authorities to discredit the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","According to reports, in order to implement the so-called \"U.S.-Taiwan Reciprocal Trade Agreement\" (ART), the Democratic Progressive Party authorities will massively relax pesticide residue standards for 174 U.S. agricultural products following the \"poisonous potatoes\", including pesticides that are even listed as having \"carcinogenic potential\" by the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. This has frequently…","Food safety is the bottom line of people's livelihood. If the reports are true, the DPP authorities will add another evil act of catering to the needs of the United States without a bottom line, constantly trampling on food safety red lines, and disregarding the lives and health of the people on the island after opening the \"Laizhu\" containing clenbuterol and releasing the germinated \"poison potatoes\". The DPP authorities blindly pursue \"independence\" and ignore people's livelihood, which brings disaster to the people and is bound to be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the Shanghai Municipal Bureau of Culture and Tourism issued an announcement announcing that Shanghai residents can sign up for group and individual tours to Kinmen and Matsu through travel agencies with relevant qualifications in Shanghai and Fujian Province. How is the current progress of the relevant situation? When will Shanghai residents be able to travel to Taiwan?","On April 29, the Shanghai Municipal Bureau of Culture and Tourism made arrangements for Shanghai residents to travel to Kinmen and Matsu. This is the concrete implementation of the results of the think tank forum between the Kuomintang and the Communist Party in February this year. Recently, the tourism industry on both sides of the Taiwan Strait has begun mutual visits and inspections, paving the way for subsequent cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation. We have announced the resumption of the pilot program for individual travel to Taiwan (main island) for residents of Shanghai and Fujian Province. We hope that relevant parties in Taiwan will comply with public opinion and open the door as soon as possible to create conditions for the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and normalized exchanges in various fields.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","The mainland tourism market is booming during this year's May Day holiday. The \"small three links\" between Xiamen and Jinmen are full of passengers, making Kinmen a popular destination for mainland tourists. Industry insiders on the island have called on the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to reopen cross-strait tourism as soon as possible to attract mainland tourists to Taiwan. Any comment on this?","According to incomplete statistics, during this year's May Day holiday, the cross-strait \"mini-three links\" passenger routes carried a total of about 32,900 passengers, a year-on-year increase of 10.57%. The Xiamen-Jinmen \"Mini Three Links\" passenger route also ushered in a peak passenger flow, with a passenger occupancy rate exceeding 95%. Among them, nearly 5,000 mainland residents traveled to Kinmen, fully reflecting the deep friendship and exchange needs of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe mainland has always actively promoted the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and normalized exchanges in various fields, and has taken the lead in launching a series of convenient measures, demonstrating sincerity and goodwill. The tourism industry on the island has repeatedly called on the DPP authorities to comply with public opinion and lift restrictions on cross-strait tourism exchanges as soon as possible. The DPP authorities should face up to the voices of the industry and the needs of the people on the island, abandon political manipulation, remove artificial obstacles as soon as possible, and promote cross-strait tourism exchanges to return to normal as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765372.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the island's public opinion organization passed the \"Special Regulations on Military Purchase\" that lowered the upper limit from NT$1.25 trillion to NT$780 billion. The Democratic Progressive Party said in response that it was regrettable that the \"opposition parties\" turned a deaf ear to reminders from the United States and the international community, which may cause gaps in future defense security.…","We firmly oppose military collusion between Taiwan and the United States. The so-called \"defense and security\" of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities contains all kinds of evil intentions of \"seeking independence by force\" and \"rejecting reunification by force.\" It squanders the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people and is willing to act as a \"cash machine\" for the United States, harming the vital interests of the Taiwanese people and undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nOur determination to resolve the Taiwan issue and achieve national reunification is rock-solid, and our capabilities are indestructible. I am telling the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that the reunification of the motherland is unstoppable. No matter how many weapons we buy, it will only be a mantis mantis. It will only accelerate the defeat of \"Taiwan independence\" and be judged by history and justice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","According to reports, the \"Triple Forum New Party Roundtable\" was held in Taipei recently. This meeting focused on cross-strait issues such as Taiwan's prospects and peaceful reunification, and attracted public attention. Any comment on this?","The reunification of the motherland is a historical trend that is rolling forward and unstoppable. The sooner reunification is achieved, the better it will be for Taiwan's development and the better it will be for Taiwanese people to live a better life. More and more Taiwan compatriots see this clearly. We welcome all political parties, groups, and people of insight from all walks of life in Taiwan, including the New Party, to provide suggestions and suggestions for peace across the Taiwan Strait, the well-being of our compatriots, national reunification, and national rejuvenation. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait must jointly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advance the great cause of motherland reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Recent polls on the island show that nearly a quarter of the people accept \"peaceful reunification and one country, two systems.\" Some commentators said that this shows that the people on the island are gradually increasing their recognition of \"one country, two systems\" and their calls for peaceful reunification are getting louder. Any comment on this?","Unification is an unstoppable historical trend. \"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" is our basic policy for solving the Taiwan issue. It is the best way to achieve the reunification of the motherland and is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the Chinese nation. More and more Taiwan compatriots have begun to discuss the specific content of the \"one country, two systems\" Taiwan plan, imagine the prospects for Taiwan after reunification, and realize that peaceful reunification will create huge opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development and will bring tangible benefits to the majority of Taiwan compatriots. We will work with our Taiwan compatriots to create the great cause of motherland reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260513_12765373.htm"],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan's retired major captain Lui Lishi participated in the opening of naval ships in Qingdao to celebrate the 77th anniversary of the founding of the People's Navy, and said, \"I feel that the motherland is stronger, which means Taiwan is safer.\" In response, Taiwan's \"Retirement Association\" established a task force to launch an administrative investigation into Lui Shi. Any comment on this?","Mr. Lu Lishi's speech came from the heart and aroused strong resonance among compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities' intention to intimidate and punish not only exposes their lies about the so-called \"freedom of speech\" they advertise, but also exposes their fear of facing the powerful power of the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","During this year’s May Day holiday, mainland Chinese people made 1.517 billion trips, a record high. The consumption was full of enthusiasm, which once again reflected the momentum and vitality of the mainland’s economic and social development, and attracted the attention and praise of netizens on the island. Any comments on this?","During the May Day holiday, the cross-regional movement of people across mainland China reached 1.517 billion, a year-on-year increase of 3.49%, a record high for the same period in history; domestic travel was 325 million, a year-on-year increase of 3.6%, with a total expenditure of 185.492 billion yuan, a year-on-year increase of 2.9%; holiday consumption-related industry sales increased by 14.3% year-on-year, comprehensive retail sales revenue increased by 12.4% year-on-year; movie box office exceeded 750 million yuan. A holiday picture with active people traveling, strong consumer demand, and a prosperous cultural and tourism industry fully demonstrates the vitality of China. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take a walk, see the magnificent rivers and mountains, experience the friendship between compatriots, and feel the prosperity of the great motherland in the warm and rising human fireworks.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Please introduce the recent cross-Strait cultural exchange activities.","Recently, cross-strait cultural exchange activities have continued to flourish.\nOn May 12, the Taiwan League Central Committee, together with the Ministry of Natural Resources and the All-China Taiwan Federation, held the 2026 Cross-Strait Marine Cultural Exchange Platform home event in the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone in Fujian Province. Nearly 300 guests from both sides of the Taiwan Strait who participated in the event focused on the \"origin\" and \"flow\" of the Austronesian language group. Through keynote speeches, roundtable dialogues, cultural carnivals, etc., they elaborated that Taiwan's ethnic minorities are an important part of the diverse unity of the Chinese nation. They called on compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to adhere to correct identification, inherit and carry forward the roots of Chinese culture, firmly build a sense of community for the Chinese nation, and protect the common home of the Chinese nation.\nFujian Province has recently held more than 10 cultural and sports exchange activities between Fujian and Taiwan. Among them, Haicang District of Xiamen City held the 9th Cross-Strait (Xiamen Haicang) Children's Swimming League. Sanming City held the 2026 Mingtai Hand in Hand Senior Training and Age Creation Research Symposium and the 2026 Hakka Culture Study Camp. A series of activities to commemorate the 1066th anniversary of Mazu's birth were held on Meizhou Island in Putian City. Nearly 50 Taiwanese Mazu temples and more than 400 Mazu believers and ancestral temple believers visited Mazu and shared peace. Taiwan's county and city Taoist churches led an exchange group of 45 people to visit Wutong Palace in Xiage Town, Zhao'an County, Zhangzhou City. Believers from both sides of the Taiwan Strait jointly paid homage to Emperor Wu Xian, talked about their hometown, and passed on their faith and customs. Quanzhou City held three Quanzhou-Taiwan exchange activities including the first Cross-Strait (Quanzhou) Youth Basketball Carnival, \"Come to Nan'an and Meet Success\". Longyan City held the 13th Cross-Strait College Students Creative Culture Festival.\nIn addition, the Suixi Lion Dance Troupe from Zhanjiang, Guangdong recently went to Chaotian Palace in Beigang, Yunlin, Taiwan to perform an intangible cultural heritage lion dance performance. The fourth \"Colorful Clouds\" series of activities for overseas Taiwan compatriots to travel to Yunnan were held in Kunming, Dali, Lijiang, Yuxi, Honghe and other places. More than 350 compatriots from both sides of the Taiwan Strait and overseas Taiwan compatriots participated in the launching ceremony. The rich and colorful series of activities allowed everyone to personally experience \"there is a life called Yunnan.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","According to reports, Hainan University recently established a Taiwan Studies Center, with the main consideration being to connect with the advantages of the free trade port system and provide decision-making reference for exchanges with Taiwan. According to incomplete statistics, more than 10 universities in mainland China have established research institutions on Taiwan. Any comment on this? How do these…","The Hainan Free Trade Port will launch island-wide customs closure operations on December 18, 2025. A series of innovative measures in the Free Trade Port will bring more opportunities and benefits to Taiwanese compatriots and enterprises. Hainan University established the Taiwan Research Center to provide theoretical support for better serving the integrated development of both sides of the Taiwan Strait based on the characteristics of the free trade port.\nIn recent years, mainland Taiwan-related research has developed steadily, forming a number of influential research institutions and talent teams, which have played a positive role in promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations. We sincerely welcome Taiwanese academics and mainland research institutions to conduct academic exchanges, enhance mutual understanding, and work together to develop cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council stated that in the past two years, it has received numerous cases of people missing contact and suspected of having their personal freedoms restricted while traveling to the mainland. It once again stated that the risks of traveling to the mainland remain high, and reminded the public to avoid non-essential travel. Any comments on this?","Mainland China's good social security environment is recognized around the world. It is a fact that all Taiwanese compatriots have a safe, comfortable, convenient and comfortable travel experience when traveling on the mainland to visit relatives and friends. The DPP authorities have been deliberately smearing and fabricating so-called \"risks\" in order to create panic, obstruct and disrupt cross-Strait exchanges and personnel exchanges, and escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. I would like to reiterate that as long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots can travel happily and return safely to the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","According to reports, an advisory member of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said that cross-strait religious exchanges are actually a tool for the mainland's \"united front\" operation against Taiwan. The mainland has long used \"united front\" propaganda images such as ancestral temples and \"same roots and same origin\" to weaken Taiwan's religious and cultural autonomy. Any comment on this?","The DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and discredited cross-Strait religious and cultural exchanges, which is unpopular. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots, culture and ethnicity. Most of the religions and folk beliefs in Taiwan originate from the mainland of the motherland. It is natural for Taiwanese compatriots to go to mainland China to offer incense and worship in ancestral temples and pray for a better life. The essence of what the DPP authorities say and do is to promote \"cultural Taiwan independence\" and \"de-Chinaization\", which goes against public opinion and will not succeed.\nWe welcome Taiwanese compatriots to visit the mainland and explore historical and cultural imprints in ancestral temples and ancestral halls. We will continue to support extensive exchanges and exchanges between temples, groups and religious figures on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and build a platform and create conditions for compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to jointly inherit China's excellent traditional culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","Taiwan's public opinion agency recently reviewed a draft amendment to some provisions of the relevant security law, and plans to severely punish words and deeds such as \"advocating military reunification\". Public opinion representatives of the Kuomintang questioned Taiwan's administrative department's suppression of freedom of speech. A Taiwanese Internet celebrity said, \"The DPP wants to restrict the freedom of…","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and ignore the mainstream public opinion that Taiwan wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. It deliberately and unscrupulously undermines cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, incites \"anti-China resistance\", continues to aggravate tensions across the Taiwan Strait, and intensifies to create a \"chilling effect.\" Its various evil deeds of \"Taiwan independence and dictatorship\" and \"green dictatorship\" are unpopular and doomed to failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Recently, President Enrique Peña Nieto of Paraguay, Taiwan's so-called \"ally\", visited Taiwan. Any comment on this?","The one-China principle is the basic norm of international relations and the general consensus of the international community. 183 countries around the world have established diplomatic relations with China on the basis of adhering to the one-China principle. We advise relevant countries to make correct decisions that conform to the general trend of history. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' provocation for \"independence\" goes against the trend of history, and complete failure is bound to happen sooner or later.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question, US Secretary of State Rubio said in a recent interview that US President Trump will discuss Taiwan issues with President Xi Jinping during his visit to China, and US policy remains unchanged. Any comment on this? The second question is that the United States is dissatisfied with the NT$780 billion special defense budget passed by Taiwan's legislative body recently, and hopes that the remaining…","The first question. The Taiwan issue is at the core of China's core interests. It is the international obligation of the United States to abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiqués, and abide by the commitments made by successive US governments on the Taiwan issue. China is unswervingly determined to safeguard national unity and territorial integrity.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and are willing to act as a \"chess piece\" for their own selfish interests. In the end, they cannot escape the fate of becoming an \"abandoned pawn\". To maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, we must oppose \"Taiwan independence.\"\nSecond question. The Taiwan issue is purely China's internal affair and does not tolerate any external interference. We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and China's Taiwan region. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiques, handle the Taiwan issue prudently, stop selling arms to Taiwan, and avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾TVBS电视台记者","First question, regarding the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, what specific responses does the mainland hope the United States will give on the Taiwan issue? Will the United States be required to make clearer commitments on arms sales to Taiwan or related policies? The second question is that the 2026 APEC event will be hosted by the mainland. Taiwan’s “Executive Yuan Political…","The first question. The Taiwan issue is China's internal affair. We firmly oppose the sale of weapons to China's Taiwan region by countries that have diplomatic relations with us. This position is consistent and clear.\nSecond question. Relevant departments have recently released relevant information regarding the upcoming APEC Trade Ministers’ Meeting in Suzhou. As the host of this year's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) events, we will handle Taiwan's participation in the event in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions and practices of APEC's relevant memorandum of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","The first question is: Zheng Liwen, Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, is expected to start a two-week visit to the United States on June 1. How does the mainland view it? Second question: Chinese KMT Chairman Cheng Li-wun recently proposed the concept of a \"Chain of Peace and Prosperity\" in an exclusive interview with CNN. Regarding the KMT's attempt to play the role of a \"regional peace connector\" in…","The first question. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese and one family. Cross-strait affairs are family affairs of compatriots on both sides of the strait, and of course they should be handled through consultation among family members. Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are fully intelligent and capable of solving their own affairs, protecting and building their own homes. On the basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\", we are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, organizations and people from all walks of life, including the Chinese Kuomintang, to jointly seek peace across the Taiwan Strait, welfare for our compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.\nSecond question. The root cause of the current tension and turmoil across the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to a separatist stance, wantonly spread separatist remarks about \"Taiwan independence\", continue to seek \"independence\" and provoke, and attempt to seek \"independence\" by relying on foreign countries and using force. Only by adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" embodying the one-China principle and resolutely opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference can we promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and effectively safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nThe third question. Recently, many mainland film and television dramas have been popular on the island, and some actors in the dramas are deeply loved by Taiwanese audiences. We are happy to hear this and support relevant Taiwanese groups in inviting mainland artists to Taiwan for exchanges and meetings with audiences on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question is that Taiwan's legislative body recently passed a special defense budget of NT$780 billion. When the heads of state of China and the United States meet, will the mainland negotiate with or put pressure on the United States regarding its arms sales to Taiwan? Second question, it has been a month since the mainland released ten policies and measures. In addition to inter-party exchanges between…","The first question. The Taiwan issue is China's internal affairs, and its resolution is a matter for the Chinese people themselves. We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and Taiwan, China, and the sale of weapons by the United States to Taiwan, China. This position is consistent and clear. To maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, we must oppose \"Taiwan independence.\"\nSecond question. Since the release of the ten policy measures, we have adhered to the concept of one family on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, focused on the people's livelihood needs on the island, and on the basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" on the common political basis, we have actively worked with relevant departments and local governments to promote the implementation of relevant policies, persisted in improving people's livelihood and well-being through exchanges and integration, and strived to allow compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to benefit from and share in the benefits. The DPP authorities should comply with the public opinion on the island and respond to the calls of the industry, remove various artificial restrictions, and remove obstacles to the normalization and normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in various fields.\nThe third question. We have always spared no effort to actively promote the restoration of cross-strait routes and destinations. China Eastern Airlines plans to resume direct flights from Chengdu to Taichung from July 1, which is a concrete measure taken by the mainland to actively respond to the travel needs of Taiwanese compatriots. In April this year, a total of 3,140 direct air passenger flights were carried out across the Taiwan Strait, transporting 641,000 passengers. The number of passengers increased by 14% compared with the same period last year. The average passenger load factor of cross-strait airlines exceeds 85%. These data clearly show that people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have strong demand for exchanges, and there is a strong call for exchanges and the resumption of air routes and flights. The DPP authorities should comply with public opinion, face the laws of the market, and meet the travel needs of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","英国独立电视新闻记者","In the upcoming meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, the Taiwan issue and arms sales may be discussed. Does the mainland believe that U.S. arms sales to Taiwan should be banned or restricted?","The Taiwan issue is China's internal affair. We firmly oppose the sale of weapons to China's Taiwan region by countries that have diplomatic relations with us. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","First question, Taiwanese media reported that Li Yanhe, the editor-in-chief of \"Eight Banners Culture\", was released from prison in May. Please tell us the specific time of his release from prison and the time of his departure. Will he have to serve an additional year in the mainland? The second question is that the Mainland Affairs Council said today that it is clarifying whether Taiwan's retired major captain…","The first question. The criminal facts of Li Yanhe's case are clear. The judicial authorities will hold a public hearing in accordance with the law and the punishment will be carried out in accordance with the law. Certain media outlets on the island have repeatedly hyped up judicial cases, slandered and discredited the mainland's judicial system, with ulterior motives.\nSecond question. This is another evil act of the DPP authorities to engage in \"green terror\" and create a \"chilling effect\" on the island. For a long time, the DPP authorities have suppressed Taiwanese people who threaten to participate in cross-strait exchanges out of self-interest for \"independence\". They have tried to restrict and block cross-strait exchanges, and even obstructed and disrupted the close relations between compatriots on both sides of the strait at the expense of the interests and well-being of the Taiwanese people. This is unpopular.\nThe compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family. The mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society that wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation cannot be suppressed or stopped. The deep friendship between the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, which has the same origin, culture, race and blood connection, cannot be severed. We will uphold the concept of one family across the Taiwan Straits and continue to provide more convenience and create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland for sightseeing, business negotiations, exchange visits, study and internship, and work and life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-13","Zhang Han","台湾东森电视台记者","Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council spokesman Liang Wenjie said, \"Two Taiwanese civil servants visited the mainland and were interrogated by national security officers late at night. Do you have any comment on this?","We have always encouraged and supported cross-Strait exchanges in various fields, including tourism, and protected the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. In 2025, Taiwan compatriots will visit the mainland nearly 5 million times. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots do not have to worry about anything when traveling to the mainland. They can come happily and return safely. Out of political self-interest, the DPP authorities have maliciously hyped and spread rumors to smear the mainland in an attempt to create a \"chilling effect.\" The purpose is to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260513_12765382.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-14","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Two questions going back to President Xi’s meeting with Trump. President Xi talked about a new positioning in ties with the U.S. and also he said both leaders agree that building a constructive and strategically stable relation will guide ties in the next three years and beyond. Could you elaborate on that as well? My second question is, President Xi also said if Taiwan issue was handled poorly, then bilateral…","On your first question, President Xi Jinping and President Trump held talks this morning. Both sides agreed on a new vision of building a constructive China-U.S. relationship of strategic stability. This will provide strategic guidance for China-U.S. relations over the next three years and beyond. “Constructive strategic stability” means positive stability with cooperation as the mainstay, healthy stability with competition within proper limits, constant stability with manageable differences, and lasting stability with expectable peace. China stands ready to work with the U.S. to translate the new vision into actions in the same direction and jointly work for a steady, sound and sustainable development of China-U.S. relations.\nOn your second question, as President Xi Jinping noted during the talks with President Trump, the Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-U.S. relations. If it is handled properly, the bilateral relationship will enjoy overall stability. Otherwise, the two countries will have clashes and even conflicts, putting the entire relationship in great jeopardy. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. Safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the biggest common denominator between China and the U.S. The U.S. side must exercise extra caution in handling the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260514_11910614.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260514_11910530.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-14","Guo Jiakun","The New York Times","Did the two leaders specifically discuss American arms sales to Taiwan?","China’s opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260514_11910614.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260514_11910530.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-18","Guo Jiakun","China-Arab TV","Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi lost no time in securing a phone call with U.S. President Donald Trump to reaffirm the importance of their alliance, as the latter was on the way home after the visit to China. The Japanese side will collect information on interactions between the United States and China, including their possible impact on Japan, and respond appropriately. How would you comment on this?","During President Trump’s visit, the two heads of state had in-depth exchanges on regional issues of mutual interest. More than eighty years ago, China and the U.S., along with the other members of the Allied Forces, jointly defeated Japanese militarists and fascists and built the postwar international order—the bedrock for peace and development in the Asia Pacific. Today, Japan’s right-wing forces are seeking to challenge this order, which threatens to shake the very foundation of regional peace and has raised global concerns. Japan should first and foremost address its wrongful rhetoric and action on Taiwan, halt its reckless remilitarization drive, return to the right track of good neighborliness, friendship and peaceful development, and earn trust from its Asian neighbors and the world with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260518_11912625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260518_11912522.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-18","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","There are media reports saying that Taiwan’s Lin Chia-lung is in Geneva to attend events that coincide with the World Health Assembly (WHA). Has China reached out to Switzerland about such participation by the Taiwan side around this WHA event?","We have already made our position clear. There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. When handling issues related to the Taiwan region, WHO and other international organizations must follow the one-China principle, which is also a fundamental principle as demonstrated by the UNGA Resolution 2758 and WHA Resolution 25.1. China firmly opposes any official exchanges in any forms between countries having diplomatic ties with China and the Taiwan region, and firmly opposes any attempts to offer platforms for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. The Taiwan authorities’ practice of sending representatives to various meetings to seek attention is nothing but political theatrics and doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260518_11912625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260518_11912522.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-18","Guo Jiakun","Shenzhen TV","U.S. President Trump said in an exclusive interview aired on May 15 that the U.S. policy on Taiwan remains unchanged. He said, “I don’t like to see anybody going independent. I’m not looking to have somebody say, let’s go independent because the United States is backing us.” The United States has no intention of seeking war and he hopes both sides across the Taiwan Strait will remain calm, he added. The Taiwan…","We have noted President Trump’s remarks. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. It is never a country, not in the past, and never in the future. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To seek “Taiwan independence” by soliciting external support is a dead end. Cross-Strait reunification is the only bright path forward. The DPP authorities should recognize the overwhelming trend, stop burying their heads in the sand, and stop going further down the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260518_11912625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260518_11912522.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-18","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Taiwan’s leader Lai Ching-te said on Sunday that Taiwan will never be traded away as he pressed the United States to keep selling weapons to them. He said arms sales from the United States to Taiwan were an element in maintaining regional peace and stability. What is the foreign ministry’s comment on this?","China’s firm opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260518_11912625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260518_11912522.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-18","Guo Jiakun","Phoenix TV","It is reported that, on the evening of May 17, in response to President Trump’s remarks that the U.S. is against “Taiwan independence” after his visit to China, Lai Ching-te posted on social media that Taiwan has always been a firm defender of the status quo on both sides of the Strait; Taiwan, the Republic of China, is a sovereign and independent democratic country; and there is no “Taiwan independence” issue.…","Lai Ching-te’s latest act is just self-defeating, which once again lays bare his separatist stance and intent to advance “Taiwan independence.”\nThere is but one China in the world. Taiwan is never a country, not in the past, and never in the future. The Chinese mainland and Taiwan belong to one and the same China. This constitutes the real status quo in the Taiwan Strait. By colluding with external forces to seek independence and attempting to make the Taiwan question an international issue, the Lai Ching-te authorities are the biggest destroyer of the status quo and the biggest source of disruption to peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace and stability are as irreconcilable as fire and water. To uphold the one-China principle, one must oppose “Taiwan independence.” Any attempts to seek independence with external forces’ backing or by force are delusional.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260518_11912625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260518_11912522.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-05-18","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, the DPP authorities officially unveiled a new version of the special defense budget, claiming that it meets the urgent need for arms purchases from the United States. However, the budget has been significantly scaled back and remains incomplete. What is your comment on this?","The massive arms purchases are nothing but a \"blood-sucking bill\" for the DPP authorities to fleece the public and undermine people's wellbeing. In total disregard of the hardships of the people and the reality that young people on the island are unwilling to fight on the battlefield for \"Taiwan independence\", the DPP authorities insist on using the people's hard-earned money to fawn on external forces, reducing themselves to an \"ATM\" for foreign arms dealers. They even clamor that \"the more money spent, the safer it is\". Such retrogressive moves are extremely unpopular.\nBuying foreign weapons cannot guarantee Taiwan's security. Those willingly serving as a \"pawn\" will only be sucked dry and thrown away. Taiwan's true security lies on reunification and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. The further the DPP authorities go down the path of seeking \"Taiwan independence\" by force and by soliciting external support, the faster they will court their own demise.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16463707.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16461760.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2026-05-18","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked that the 79th World Health Assembly once again decided not to include Taiwan-related proposals on the agenda of the assembly. Any comment on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said in response to inquiries that this is the 10th consecutive year that the World Health Assembly has rejected so-called Taiwan-related proposals put forward by individual countries. The relevant decision once again shows that adhering to the one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community. It is the aspiration of the people, the trend of the times, and the great cause of justice. The basic pattern of the international community's insistence on the one-China principle cannot be challenged and cannot be shaken. It also shows once again that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and do not recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle. They attempt to take a different approach and make a so-called \"breakthrough\" on the issue of Taiwan's participation in the World Health Assembly. This road will not work and will be frustrated.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan, and Taiwan compatriots are our relatives and family members. We always have the health and well-being of our Taiwan compatriots at heart. While Taiwan has not participated in the World Health Assembly, we have made appropriate arrangements for Taiwan's participation in global health on the basis of the one-China principle. In the past year, Taiwanese medical technology experts participated in a total of 18 WHO technical activities. Under the framework of the International Health Regulations, any information on public health emergencies reported by the WHO to various places can be obtained in a timely manner by the Taiwan region and can be reported to the WHO in a timely manner. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait also have a smooth information reporting mechanism for infectious disease epidemics, and have held hospital director forums and other activities. This fully demonstrates that we are serious about addressing the health issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots, that Taiwan has fully open channels to participate in WHO technical communication and cooperation, and to obtain information and support on various public health emergencies, and that the health rights of Taiwan compatriots are effectively protected.\nFor some time, the DPP authorities have colluded with external forces and have continued to make a fuss about participating in the World Health Assembly, deliberately distorting and challenging the fundamental principles confirmed by United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758 and World Health Assembly Resolution 25.1. This is not only a political maneuver for \"independence\" under the guise of health and a challenge to China's sovereignty and territorial integrity, it is also a challenge to the post-World War II international order, international justice and universal consensus. No matter what tricks the DPP authorities play, they can't deceive people, they can't achieve anything, they can't change the doomed outcome of seeking \"independence\", and they can't stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260518_12766265.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-19","Guo Jiakun","Beijing Daily","The 79th World Health Assembly (WHA) decided to reject the so-called proposal on Taiwan. This has been the 10th year in a row that the WHA has rejected the so-called proposal concerning Taiwan. What’s your comment?","The WHA has rejected the so-called proposal on Taiwan for 10 consecutive years, which fully shows that the international commitment to the one-China principle is unshakable, and the authority of the UNGA Resolution 2758 is indisputable. The rejection of the proposal over the past decade shows that the DPP authorities’ “Taiwan independence” separatist stance is doomed to fail. It’s time for the DPP authorities to put to rest their political stunts for “Taiwan independence.” China will achieve complete reunification. Taiwan must return to the motherland.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260519_11913636.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260519_11913599.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-19","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The Philippines’ President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. said his country would likely be involved in any conflict over Taiwan due to his country’s proximity to the island. To quote him, we do not have a choice because Taiwan is so close to the Philippines, and we have almost 200,000 Filipino nationals living and working in Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have any comment?","China noted that the Philippine leader reiterates his commitment to the one-China policy and non-interference in China’s internal affairs. It should be emphasized that, “large number of Filipinos living and working” on the Taiwan island and “geopolitical proximity” should not serve as the excuse for one country to interfere in another country’s internal and sovereign affairs. We hope the Philippines could honor its commitments, match its words with actions, and abide by the one-China principle with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260519_11913636.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260519_11913599.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-20","Guo Jiakun","Asahi Shimbun","Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te expressed his hope to continue U.S. arms purchases, and said that if he had the opportunity to have a phone call with President Trump, he had a responsibility to express the voice of Taiwanese society. He added that Taiwan is an “independent sovereign country.” What’s China’s comment?","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. It has never been a country and will never be a country. The Lai Ching-te authorities have developed a conditioned response of making every attempt to grab attention, which only time and again revealed their true nature as provocateurs and saboteurs of peace. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. Soliciting external support and pursuing military buildup to seek “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail. China’s firm opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear. The U.S. needs to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and take concrete actions to uphold the overall China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260520_11914528.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260520_11914508.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-20","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Taiwan’s leader Lai Ching-te said today in a speech that foreign forces cannot decide the future of Taiwan, nor can Taiwan be held hostage by fear, division or short-term interest. What is the foreign ministry’s reaction to these comments and Lai’s speech today?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. The two sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China, and this is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. “Taiwan independence” and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water. “Taiwan independence” separatist forces constitute the biggest destroyer of the status quo across the Strait and the biggest source of disruption to peace and stability in the region. To safeguard peace and stability across the Strait, one must firmly follow the one-China principle and stand against “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. Leaders and political figures from the overwhelming majority of countries in the international community have reaffirmed their commitment to the one-China principle through various ways. Facts show that opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and supporting China’s reunification is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends.\nLai Ching-te’s persistent separatist stance and his true agenda of seeking “Taiwan independence” under the cover of so-called democracy has proved himself as a saboteur of peace, creator of crisis and troublemaker. No matter what “Taiwan independence” separatist forces say or do, the people in the Taiwan region will not be misled; the fundamental reality that the Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair will not be changed; the international commitment to the one-China principle will not be shaken; and the historical trend that China will and must achieve reunification will not be stopped.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260520_11914528.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260520_11914508.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-05-20","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that on May 20, Lai Ching-te gave a speech claiming that maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is Taiwan’s “strategic goal,” agitated for strengthening asymmetric combat capabilities, and for enhancing “whole-of-society defense resilience.” What is your comment on this?","Faced with the inevitable trend of national reunification and the reality of profound adjustments in the international landscape, Lai Ching-te still indulges in the illusion of “seeking independence by relying on outside forces.” Under the guise of so-called “peace,” he peddles “Taiwan independence” fallacies on a large scale, incites “using force to seek independence and resisting reunification,” and attempts to change the fundamental status quo that Taiwan belongs to China. Placing his ambition for “independence” above the well-being of the Taiwan people is nothing but self-deception and a miscalculation.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities have disregarded national righteousness and the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan, colluded with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, which is the root cause of the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. Clinging to the obsession with “Taiwan independence,” which can never be realized, they have further gone to great lengths to use the hard-earned money of ordinary people to curry favor with foreign powers and pledge loyalty, forcibly binding the Taiwan people to the chariot of “Taiwan independence” and step by step pushing Taiwan toward the perilous brink of war. We solemnly warn the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that no matter how much money they spend or how many weapons they buy, it will be like a mantis trying to stop a chariot or an egg striking a stone. “Seeking independence by force” is a dead end, and national reunification is the only bright road.\nNational territory cannot be divided, and the nation cannot be split. “Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. The People's Liberation Army remains on high alert at all times, and resolutely thwarts any “Taiwan independence” provocations and firmly defends national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16462417.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on May 20, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Welcome to today's press conference, and I'll take your questions now.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","President Xi Jinping emphasized at the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States on May 14 that the Taiwan issue is the most important issue in Sino-US relations, and the United States must handle the Taiwan issue with caution. Please interpret its important meaning.","The Taiwan issue is one of the important topics at this meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States. President Xi Jinping emphasized that the Taiwan issue is the most important issue in Sino-US relations. If handled well, the relationship between the two countries can maintain overall stability. If it is not handled well, the two countries will collide or even conflict, pushing the entire Sino-US relationship into a very dangerous situation. \"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States. The United States must handle the Taiwan issue with caution. This provides us with a fundamental basis for our work in Taiwan.\nThe Taiwan issue is China's internal affair. It has been a fact since ancient times that the mainland and Taiwan belong to the same China. It is the true status quo of the Taiwan Strait and an important part of the international order after World War II. Solving the Taiwan issue and realizing the complete reunification of the country is the common aspiration of all Chinese people and is also the fundamental interest of the Chinese nation.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and continue to collude with external forces to carry out \"independence\" provocations, which is the root cause of peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States. The prerequisite for achieving this is that we must not support or condone \"Taiwan independence.\" We hope that the U.S. will abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiques, handle the Taiwan issue with caution and prudence, avoid sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and take practical actions to safeguard the stable development of Sino-U.S. relations and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766746.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","The Shanghai Municipal Bureau of Culture and Tourism recently announced that Shanghai residents can apply to travel to Kinmen. The first batch of Shanghai tourists arrived in Kinmen on the 11th and returned to Shanghai on the 13th. Taiwanese media reported that this ushered in the \"Spring Swallow\" for the local tourism industry. The Kinmen County Government stated that it plans to hold four Kinmen tourism…","We are happy to see the positive response to the resumption of Shanghai residents' travel to Kinmen, Matsu and Kinmen. This fully demonstrates the eager expectation of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially those in Kinmen, for the normalization of cross-Strait personnel exchanges and normalized exchanges and cooperation.\nWe are willing to actively promote anything that is conducive to enhancing the well-being and exchanges of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and will take active measures to support and encourage people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to strengthen interaction and exchanges. Relevant parties in Taiwan should comply with public opinion, face up to the calls of the island's tourism industry and people, lift unreasonable restrictions as soon as possible, and promote cross-strait tourism exchanges to return to normal.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766738.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","According to reports, many mainland airlines plan to resume direct cross-strait air passenger routes in the near future. What is the spokesperson's comment on this?","Direct air flights across the Taiwan Strait have greatly facilitated the exchanges between people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and played an important role in improving the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We have been actively promoting the full resumption of normalization of direct air passenger flights across the Taiwan Strait. It is understood that China Eastern Airlines, Spring Airlines, and Shandong Airlines plan to resume direct flights from Chengdu to Taichung, Ningbo to Kaohsiung, and Qingdao to Taichung respectively from July this year. These are concrete measures taken by Continental Airlines to actively respond to the needs of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. They are a good thing to facilitate cross-Strait personnel exchanges and promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We strongly support them.\nIt is hoped that Taiwan will comply with public opinion and resume cross-strait flights in Urumqi, Xi'an, Harbin, Kunming, Lanzhou and other cities as soon as possible, and then comprehensively lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-strait air transport, allowing cross-strait airlines to independently arrange flight plans according to market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","According to reports, Taiwan Electric Power Company recently spent nearly one million New Taiwan dollars to replace its corporate logo, replacing the old version of the logo that had been in use for more than 70 years and was inscribed by the famous calligrapher Yu Youren. Public opinion on the island has criticized it for spending money on \"de-Sinicization\" despite years of losses and rising electricity prices…","The actions of the DPP authorities reveal their disregard for people's livelihood and their use of all possible means to sever the historical and cultural ties between the two sides of the Taiwan Straits. The relevant tactics are both shameless and incompetent. These small moves by the DPP authorities are in vain. No one can erase the Chinese national identity and Chinese cultural identity of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Two years after Lai Ching-te came to power, the latest polls on the island show that Taiwanese people are more dissatisfied with Lai Ching-te's governance than satisfied, with 51% of the people having no confidence in his future performance. Any comment on this?","Relevant polls have fully shown that what Lai Qingde has done in the two years since he took office is contrary to the interests and well-being of the Taiwanese people and has become increasingly unpopular. The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to the stance of \"Taiwan independence\", wantonly peddle fallacies of separatism, deliberately obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and intensify efforts to create \"green terror\"; under the guise of so-called \"democracy\" and \"peace\", they concoct false narratives of \"democracy versus authoritarianism\" to incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation; and serve one party and one self. They are selfish, ignore people's livelihood and well-being, ignore economic laws, and seek to \"decouple\" cross-Strait economic and trade and \"disconnect\" industries; they abuse the judiciary to suppress and persecute political dissidents, continue to manipulate and provoke vicious political fights; they ignore the people's livelihood and wantonly squander the people's wealth and money, flatter and surrender to external forces, and attempt to \"rely on external forces\" and \"use force to seek independence.\" The various perverse actions of the Lai Ching-te administration have seriously violated the mainstream public opinion of Taiwanese society for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, seriously undermined peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and brought Taiwan into the dangerous situation of war. They have fully exposed their stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" nature, and are fully convinced that they are a \"destroyer of cross-Strait peace,\" a \"crisis creator in the Taiwan Strait,\" and a \"betrayer of Taiwan's public opinion.\"\n\"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and confrontation has no way out. The reunification of the motherland is a historical trend that no one or any force can stop. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus\", unite broadly with Taiwan compatriots, resolutely fight against \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, oppose interference from external forces, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and promote the great cause of reunification of the motherland. We hope that our compatriots in Taiwan will follow the general trend of history, uphold national justice, work with us to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, protect the common home of the Chinese nation, and jointly create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766743.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","A poll recently released by the Chinese Kuomintang think tank showed that 80.3% of the people on the island believe that cross-strait issues should be resolved peacefully through consultation, and 65% of the people agree to establish a \"chain of peace and prosperity\" to replace regional confrontation. Any comment on this?","Wanting peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society. The DPP authorities seek \"independence\" to provoke provocations, \"rely on external forces to seek independence\" and incite confrontation, which completely goes against public opinion and is unpopular. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and cross-Strait affairs are family matters of the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and should be discussed and handled by the family members. On the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to engage in dialogue and consultation with people from all political parties, all walks of life, and all walks of life in Taiwan on the development of cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, to jointly maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the process of the peaceful reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The 79th World Health Assembly was held in Geneva on May 18. Taiwan was unable to attend the meeting for the 10th consecutive year. The head of Taiwan's health department and the head of the foreign affairs department held activities outside the WHO in the form of a \"dual ministerial meeting\". Any comments on this?","The DPP authorities are hyping up issues related to the World Health Assembly, using the guise of health services to engage in political manipulation for \"independence\". They are not caring about the interests and well-being of the Taiwanese people at all, but are using the meeting to enhance their presence, make political articles, and deceive the people on the island. The result will only be self-humiliation and will not change the fate of \"independence\" provocations that are destined to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-strait exchange activities.","Recently, various parts of the mainland have been actively organizing a variety of cross-Strait exchange activities, inviting people from all walks of life on both sides to participate, and actively promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.\nIn terms of economic and trade exchanges, from May 14 to 17, the 2026 Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation Zone Construction Promotion Conference was held in Jinan, Shandong Province, focusing on the development direction of new productive forces, striving to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in the fields of intelligent manufacturing, food and medicine, and helping Taiwanese businesses and enterprises share development opportunities. On the 15th, the Cross-Strait Tea Industry Exchange Association, the Taiwan Tea Society and many other tea industry groups from both sides of the Taiwan Strait held the seventh International Tea Day themed event \"Tea to Honor Mazu and Harmonize the World\" in Putian, Fujian Province. Nearly 200 representatives of tea industry groups and tea people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait jointly issued the \"Cross-Strait Tea People Initiative\", calling for the promotion of Chinese tea culture, deepening cross-strait emotional identification, and promoting the high-quality development of the tea industry. On the 19th, the 2026 \"Work-Assisted Revitalization\" Zhangtai Employees \"Cooking God Competition\" skills competition was held in Zhangzhou, Fujian. More than 60 contestants from 30 teams from Zhangzhou and Taiwan competed on the same stage and exchanged cooking skills.\nIn terms of cultural exchanges, the 4th \"Love Connects Cross-Strait, Yunnan and Taiwan Walk Together\" and Taiwan New Media People's Lincang Exchange Event, \"Water Ripples Concentric · Cross-Strait Songs\" - Yuntai Youth 2026 Water Splashing Festival cultural exchange event was held in Yunnan, with more than 90 Taiwanese self-media Tiren and young people from Taiwanese ethnic minorities visited Lincang, Yunnan, and participated in a water-splashing carnival with tens of thousands of people. They immersed themselves in the ethnic customs and landscapes of the Wa, Lahu and Dai people, and went deep into the tea and coffee gardens to experience the charm of the tea and coffee aromas of Awa Mountain and Ali Mountain. From May 13 to 16, Master Yanjue, President of the Buddhist Association of China, led a delegation to Taiwan to attend a series of commemorative events for the 60th anniversary of the founding of Fo Guang Shan, and conducted in-depth exchanges on cross-strait Buddhist culture and education with the Taiwan Federation of Chinese Humanistic Buddhism and other major Buddhist organizations and monasteries in Taiwan. On the 14th, the 2026 China Jigong Cultural Festival was held on the rooftop of Zhejiang. More than 800 Jigong believers from both sides of the Taiwan Strait and overseas gathered together to spread the Jigong spirit and share the nostalgia of our compatriots. On the 15th, the 2026 Bashu Culture and Art Season was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. More than 100 artists, cultural scholars, teachers and students from colleges and universities from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, etc., focused on \"Wuhou Qianqiu Rhythm, Cross-Strait Love\" and conducted in-depth exchanges on the charm of Bashu culture through a series of activities such as academic seminars and exhibitions of original art works by teachers and students from Sichuan and Taiwan.\nIn terms of youth exchanges, on the 19th, the 8th Cross-Strait (Hubei) Youth East Lake Exchange Season was held in Wuhan. About 300 youths from both sides of the Taiwan Strait met in Jiangcheng to discuss youth friendship and show the power of youth through keynote exchanges, young teacher exchange meetings, traditional sports carnivals, literary evenings, and the \"Thousands of Posts to Welcome Taiwan Youth\" special job fair. From the 19th to the 31st, the Xiamen-Taoyuan Autonomous Cycling Exchange Event \"Riding to Gather Landscapes and Connecting Two Places\" was held in Fujian. More than 80 cyclists from Xiamen and Taoyuan, Taiwan, set off from Wuyi Mountain and cycled about 600 kilometers. They will arrive at Jimei, Xiamen on the 31st, and enjoy cycling while enjoying the beautiful scenery of Fujian.\nTwo events are previewed here. From May 20th to 27th, the 20th Cross-Strait Media Tour to Jingchu was held in Hubei. More than 20 cross-Strait and Hong Kong news media reporters and self-media people went to Tianmen, Qianjiang, Xiantao and other places for interviews and exchanges to fully experience the cultural heritage, industrial vitality and new urban appearance of Jingchu. On May 26, the 2026 Zhejiang Taiwan Cooperation Week event co-sponsored by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Zhejiang Provincial People's Government will be held in Hangzhou. With the theme of \"Gathering together to innovate and draw a vivid picture together,\" this year's event will focus on exchanges and docking cooperation in the fields of artificial intelligence, high-end manufacturing, biomedicine, cultural tourism, etc. About 600 people, including heads of relevant industry associations and industrial and commercial groups on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and business representatives, will participate in relevant activities. Media friends are welcome to pay attention and report.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Taiwan's public opinion organization voted on the \"Lai Qingde impeachment case\" on the 19th. Any comment on this?","In the two years since he came to power, Lai Ching-te has stubbornly adhered to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", disregarded the livelihood and well-being of the people on the island, pursued political selfishness, incited cross-strait confrontation, undermined cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, betrayed Taiwan without a bottom line, abused the judiciary to suppress and persecute political dissidents, trampled on democracy wantonly, engaged in \"green terror\" and created a \"chilling effect\". It can be said that he is incompetent in governance and incompetent, and his actions seriously deviate from the mainstream public opinion on the island. The relevant \"impeachment case\" fully expressed the Taiwanese people's strong dissatisfaction and condemnation of Lai Qingde's actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","In order to promote the implementation of ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, Fujian Province has recently issued measures to benefit Taiwan such as the \"Fujian-Taiwan Entry Fujian Tourist Route\". Please introduce the relevant situation.","Fujian Province is based on the origins of the same culture, customs, clans and tastes between Fujian and Taiwan, and meets the needs of Taiwanese people in returning to their hometowns to find their roots, trace their cultural origins, visit ancestral temples, socialize with relatives, and experience delicious food. It selects southern Fujian culture, folk beliefs and customs, ancestral temples, and Fujian cuisine. We will create five 6- to 7-day exclusive inbound tourism itineraries for Taiwanese compatriots based on the five major themes that highlight the historical and cultural symbols of Fujian and Taiwan, deeply presenting the cultural charm of the same roots in Fujian and Taiwan, and providing Taiwanese compatriots with more personalized and optional inbound tourism itineraries in Fujian. At the same time, we have launched multiple Easter egg gift packs and other heart-warming measures to benefit Taiwan's \"Solo people\" traveling to Fujian, as well as measures such as Shanghai residents visiting Fujian and Jinma boutique tourist routes.\nThese measures are warm and powerful. They not only allow Taiwanese compatriots, especially those from Taiwan who come to the mainland for the first time, to fully feel the intimacy of \"home\" in Fujian, but also allow them to get a better cultural and tourism experience in Fujian through real discounts and conveniences. This is a vivid embodiment of \"the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and Fujian and Taiwan are close relatives.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","After the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, U.S. President Trump made it clear in an interview that he did not want Taiwan to be \"independent.\" How does the mainland interpret the signal released by the United States? Do you call on the DPP authorities to return to dialogue based on the \"1992 Consensus\"?","President Xi Jinping pointed out in his meeting with President Trump that the Taiwan issue is the most important issue in Sino-US relations. If it is handled well, the relationship between the two countries can maintain overall stability. If it is not handled well, the two countries will collide or even conflict, pushing the entire Sino-US relationship into a very dangerous situation. \"Taiwan independence\" is incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States. The United States understands China's position and takes China's concerns seriously. Like the international community, it does not agree with or accept Taiwan's move toward \"independence.\"\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle. This is the biggest source of chaos for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It will surely reap the consequences and be spurned by history and the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","The mainland film \"A Love Letter to Grandma\" has recently attracted widespread attention from both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The \"love and justice\" and \"feelings of family and country\" conveyed in the film have strongly resonated with audiences on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Any comment on this?","The movie \"A Love Letter to Grandma\" uses overseas Chinese batches as a carrier and uses delicate and simple lenses to tell a story of the overseas Chinese in Chaoshan who have watched over the mountains and seas for more than half a century. Chaoshan area and Taiwan area have many similarities in language and customs. Taiwanese people who have watched the film were particularly touched by the large number of Chaoshan dialects, the core of integrity and friendship, and the strong feelings of family and country in the film. The sound \"grandma\" is the local pronunciation of the same origin on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and the phrase \"you must be affectionate and righteous\" is the root soul of both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe Taiwanese people love this movie, which fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have a common inheritance and strong resonance with Chinese culture. As of the end of May this year, 9 Taiwanese films have been released in mainland theaters and attracted the attention of mainland audiences. We are also happy to see more Taiwanese compatriots pay attention to and watch excellent mainland movies. We hope that more mainland movies can be released in Taiwan, so that more Taiwanese people can deeply experience the profound heritage and innovative development of Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766736.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Foreign media recently reported that Taiwanese society is setting off a wave of \"exodus\" to apply for a \"second passport\" and move assets abroad. Some media on the island claimed that the DPP authorities used the fear of war as a tool for electoral mobilization and political struggle, and constantly strengthened the \"anti-China card\" and \"sense of national subjugation\" to reap political benefits. The result was a…","Relevant reports indicate that under the bad governance of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities seeking \"independence\" and provocations, more and more Taiwanese people are worried that \"Taiwan independence\" will trigger a war, and are worried that their life and property safety and development rights will not be protected, and they are forced to make plans to leave their country and find another way out. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities place one-party political self-interest above the people's immediate well-being and industrial development interests. They continue to resort to \"relying on foreign countries to seek independence\" and \"using force to seek independence\", creating war anxiety on the island, and cooperating with external forces to hollow out Taiwan's advantageous industries. What he has done not only betrays Taiwan and harms it, but also causes chaos and harms Taiwan. It has made Taiwan increasingly war-torn and dangerous, and people in panic.\nWe hope that the majority of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the harm and danger of the DPP authorities' promotion of \"Taiwan independence\", consciously draw a clear line with the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities, and work with us to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, and protect the common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766739.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","After the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, U.S. President Trump once again named Taiwan's chip industry to set up factories in the United States. He said that \"Taiwan stole the U.S. chip industry\" and asked Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co., Ltd. and other Taiwanese technology companies to invest in Arizona. Now that TSMC has increased investment in Arizona, will the…","The DPP authorities ignore the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the interests of the industry and continue to \"sacrifice\" the island's semiconductor industry and enterprises as bargaining chips for political gain. Their despicable behavior has long been seen and despised by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Expanding cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development are the right choices to promote the sustainable development of Taiwan's high-tech industry.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Democratic Progressive Party recently recruited Shen Boyang to run for mayor of Taipei. Public opinion on the island questioned that Shen, apart from being good at cognitive warfare and conducting so-called \"reverse infiltration\" cognitive attack and defense, has no concern for people's livelihood issues. Any comment on this?","Shen Boyang, a die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" activist, vigorously promoted the separatist fallacy of \"Taiwan independence\" and engaged in criminal activities to split the country. He was punished in accordance with the law and held accountable for life. I believe that the majority of Taiwan compatriots will draw a clear line with them, resolutely safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and resolutely protect their own interests and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Jay Chou and other Taiwanese singers held concerts in many places on the mainland this year, attracting a large number of fans to travel across the city. Faced with the ensuing consumer demand for accommodation, catering and travel, cultural and tourism departments in various places have taken measures to not only escort performing arts activities, but also promote local cultural tourism, achieving a two-way…","Since the beginning of this year, the performance market in mainland China has continued to grow explosively. Taiwanese entertainers have held solo concerts in many cities on the mainland, attracting fans from both sides of the Taiwan Strait to watch performances across the city. Various localities have actively implemented policies to optimize traffic flow, standardize market prices, and strengthen cultural tourism service guarantees. At the same time, they have taken advantage of the trend to launch cultural tourism themed routes, issue consumer coupons, and promote urban cultural tourism resources, achieving a mutually beneficial and win-win situation between the safe and orderly holding of performing arts activities and the diversion of local cultural tourism revenue.\nThe two sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots and cultural background, and pop music is one of the most friendly and down-to-earth carriers of cross-Strait cross-Strait folk exchanges. We have always supported cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in the fields of culture, performing arts, tourism and other fields, and are happy to see more warm and popular cross-Strait cultural exchange activities to promote two-way flows of people, consumption and culture. We welcome Taiwanese entertainers to come to the mainland to hold concerts or participate in various cultural performances. We also welcome fans and friends on the island to take advantage of the increasingly convenient entry and exit policies for Taiwanese compatriots to come to various parts of the mainland to watch various cultural performances and experience the wonderful cultural and tourism life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766737.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","On May 17, Lai Ching-te published the so-called \"5-point statement\" on Facebook, declaring that \"Taiwan is the defender of the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait and the region; the mainland is the source of regional instability and changes in the status quo\"; he once again advocated \"non-affiliation\" between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. Any comment on this?","Lai Ching-te's so-called remarks were full of lies and deception, hostility and confrontation, paranoia and arrogance. He ignored the international community's stance against \"Taiwan independence\", deceived the people of Taiwan and deceived international public opinion with bluff, which fully exposed his ruthless, cunning and despicable nature. Since taking office, Lai Ching-te has stubbornly adhered to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", clamored for the so-called \"non-subordination\" of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, incited cross-Strait confrontation, and continued provocations for \"independence\". He is a destroyer of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the biggest source of chaos for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. While vigorously advocating the separatist fallacy of \"Taiwan independence\", he is doing his best to obstruct and undermine cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. These evil actions have been firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the international community, and are doomed to failure.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan's future can only and must be jointly decided by the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including 23 million Taiwan compatriots. No matter what Lai Qingde says or does, it cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China's territory, nor can it stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766740.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Polls in Taiwan show that among young people aged 20 to 29 on the island, the proportion of those who favor \"Taiwan independence\" has declined in recent years, while the proportion of those who support cross-strait reunification continues to rise, showing a development trend in which the younger generation increasingly disagrees with \"Taiwan independence\" and is more inclined to support reunification. Any comment…","Since coming to power, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have been peddling the separatist fallacy of \"Taiwan independence\", deliberately manipulating \"de-Chinaization\", restricting cross-strait exchanges, and creating an \"information cocoon\" in an attempt to deceive and mislead the Taiwanese people, especially the younger generation, and create confusion in historical memory and distortion of national identity. What they do deviates from history and facts, becomes increasingly unpopular, and is destined to fail.\nYouth are the hope of the country and the future of the nation. The future of cross-Strait relations rests on the youth of both sides of the Taiwan Strait. More and more Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, are actively participating in cross-Strait exchanges, learning from each other, and understanding each other. They are increasingly realizing that reunification is the general trend and the future. We welcome and support more young people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait to come and go frequently to strengthen their ambition, strength and confidence to be Chinese, and to work together for national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766741.htm"],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Zhuo Rongtai said on the 19th that the People's Liberation Army's military exercises are \"the biggest source of unrest and destabilization in the entire region\" and hoped that \"healthy and orderly exchanges, equal and dignified dialogue\" can be carried out between the two sides. Any comment on this?","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and wantonly collude with external forces to pursue \"independence\" provocations. This is the root cause of chaos that undermines peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We will never tolerate or condone any separatist activities seeking \"Taiwan independence.\" The relevant military actions of the People's Liberation Army are a stern warning to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and external interference forces, and are a necessary and just move to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nOn the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to strengthen exchanges and dialogues with Taiwan's political parties, organizations and people from all walks of life to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, seek peace across the Taiwan Strait, benefit our compatriots, and seek rejuvenation for the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The first question is that Taiwanese leader Lai Ching-te delivered a speech this morning on the second anniversary of his inauguration. Do you have any comment on the content related to cross-strait relations?\nThe second question is that the cross-Strait official communication mechanism has been suspended for ten years since 2016. As a result, many cross-Strait people's livelihood, economic and trade issues…","The first question. No matter what Lai Ching-te says or does, it cannot conceal his stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" essence, change Taiwan's status as a part of China, break the historical and legal connection that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and cannot block the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will be reunified.\nRegarding cross-strait relations. The fundamental reason why the deadlock in cross-Strait relations is difficult to thaw and the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism has been suspended is that the DPP authorities ignore the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle. The fundamental reason why the Taiwanese people are anxious and worried about the situation across the Taiwan Strait is that the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and blindly engage in \"relying on foreign countries to seek independence\" and \"using force to seek independence\", inciting cross-strait confrontation and constantly escalating tensions in the Taiwan Strait.\nOn the basis of the one-China principle, there will be no obstacles for any political party or group in Taiwan to interact with us. As long as we return to the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and recognizing the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same country and nation, the cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanism can be restarted, and cross-Strait relations can return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Regarding Lai Ching-te's recent Facebook post stating that \"there is no issue of Taiwan independence in defense of the status quo of the Republic of China,\" former Chairman of the People's Party Ko Wenzhe said that the DPP is fully aware that the \"Taiwan Independence Party Platform\" will not work in international reality, so it can only keep changing concepts and say that the \"Constitution of the Republic of…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an unquestionable historical and legal fact, and it is also the status quo across the Taiwan Strait that cannot be changed. Since Lai Ching-te came to power, he has wantonly colluded with external forces to pursue \"independence\" provocations, severely damaged cross-strait relations, and severely damaged the security and well-being of the Taiwanese people. Everyone can see clearly what he has done, and any sophistry is of no avail. \"Taiwan independence\" is incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait. We will never condone or tolerate \"Taiwan independence\". If the DPP authorities really do not have a \"Taiwan independence\" issue, they should immediately abandon the \"Taiwan independence party platform\", stop \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities, recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle, and take practical actions to improve cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, Shen Boyang, who is running for mayor of Taipei, said, \"Holding the 'Twin Cities Forum' is extremely ineffective. Don't do things that are ineffective.\" The Taipei City Government stated that \"the results of the 'Twin Cities Forum' can be seen in all aspects.\" Shen should listen more to citizens and have more contact with the municipal government. Any comment on this?","The remarks made by Shen Boyang, a die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" activist, completely ignore the facts and are malicious slanders. The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been held for 16 consecutive years. It has reached many consensuses on issues such as economy, culture, technology, society, sports, and urban management, and achieved fruitful results. It has been widely recognized by citizens of the two cities and compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and has become an important platform for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Shen Boyang is accustomed to spreading rumors, slandering, attacking and undermining cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. His bad behavior will be condemned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","The first question is that U.S. President Trump recently stated that he \"does not want Taiwan to be independent.\" U.S. Ambassador to China Pang Dewei also said that when Trump met with President Xi Jinping, he said that he did not support \"Taiwan independence\" and that the U.S. policy toward Taiwan remains unchanged and hopes that cross-strait issues will be resolved peacefully. Any comment on this?\nSecond…","The first question. President Xi Jinping pointed out in his meeting with President Trump that the Taiwan issue is the most important issue in Sino-US relations. If it is handled well, the relationship between the two countries can maintain overall stability. If it is not handled well, the two countries will collide or even conflict, pushing the entire Sino-US relationship into a very dangerous situation. \"Taiwan independence\" is incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States. The United States understands China's position and takes China's concerns seriously. Like the international community, it does not agree with or accept Taiwan's move toward \"independence.\"\nWe hope that the United States will abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiques, never support or condone \"Taiwan independence\", and take practical actions to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nSecond question. We have taken note of President Trump’s relevant remarks. The DPP authorities are servile and militaristic, fully exposing their evil nature of seeking \"independence\" and their cowardice of relying on others. \"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. \"Relying on external forces to seek independence\" and \"using force to seek independence\" are wishful thinking and a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question is that after the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, the two countries reached a new positioning of \"China-US constructive strategic and stable relations.\" Will this affect mainland China's work with Taiwan? What new prospects does the mainland have for cross-strait relations in the future?\nSecond question: After the meeting between the heads of state of China…","The first question. President Xi Jinping and President Trump have taken \"China-US constructive strategic and stable relationship\" as the new positioning of the relationship between the two countries, providing strategic guidance for China-US relations in the next three years and beyond. This has been welcomed by the people of the two countries and the international community, and has also pointed out the direction for China and the United States to properly manage differences on the Taiwan issue. \"China-US constructive strategic and stable relations\" is not a slogan, it is a goal that both sides adhere to and actions they take together.\nThe Taiwan issue is the core of China's core interests and the most important issue in Sino-US relations, affecting the whole country. To grasp the new positioning of Sino-US relations, we must resolutely safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, which is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States. \"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible, and the United States must handle the Taiwan issue cautiously. We hope that the United States will abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiques, never support or condone \"Taiwan independence\", and take practical actions to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\nWe will thoroughly implement the spirit of President Xi Jinping's important speeches, firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus\", resolutely combat \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and promote the great cause of the reunification of the motherland. We hope that the majority of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the Lai Ching-te administration's pursuit of \"independence\" and triggering war, and work with us to firmly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and create a bright future for the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation.\nSecond question. There is only one China in the world. Mainland China and Taiwan belong to the same China. Taiwan has never been a country. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people. It is the general trend, the great cause, and the aspiration of the people. No one or any force can stop it!\nOn the one hand, the DPP authorities refuse to recognize that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", and continue to pursue \"independence\" provocations. On the other hand, they play word games to deceive the people on the island and the international community, trying to cover up and deceive themselves and others.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. Only by completely giving up the \"Taiwan independence\" stance, stopping provocations for \"independence\", and returning to the political basis of the \"1992 Consensus\" can the DPP authorities truly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and improve and develop cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","After the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, U.S. President Trump said that arms sales to Taiwan were a good bargaining chip, but he decided to shelve the decision for the time being. Did China and the United States mention the issue of U.S. arms sales to Taiwan this time? What do you think of Trump’s statement? In addition, Trump also said that before confirming the arms sales…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, China, and the sale of arms by the United States to Taiwan, China. This position is consistent and clear.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","The first question is that Lai Qingde recently claimed that there is currently no \"Taiwan independence\" issue. After the meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States, is it possible for the two sides to ease relations and promote more exchanges and cooperation by \"putting aside disputes\"?\nSecond question: Shi Chongliang, the head of Taiwan’s health department, recently said that when a…","The first question. Lai Ching-te stubbornly adheres to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", constantly invents new tricks to hype the \"new two-nation theory\", and does his best to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. He is a \"destroyer of cross-Strait peace\", a \"creator of crisis in the Taiwan Strait\" and a \"betrayer of Taiwan's public opinion.\"\nRegarding cross-Strait exchanges, our attitude is very clear. We are willing to strengthen exchanges and dialogue with various political parties, groups and people from all walks of life in Taiwan to share the results of cooperation on the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence.\"\nSecond question. We follow the one-China principle to handle Taiwan's participation in international organizations and their activities, including the WHO. This position is consistent and clear. The DPP stubbornly adheres to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and refuses to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle. This is the fundamental reason why Taiwan cannot participate in the conference.\nThe DPP authorities are hyping up issues related to the World Health Assembly and engaging in political manipulation for \"independence\". They do not care about the interests and well-being of the Taiwanese people at all. Instead, they use the meeting to enhance their presence, make political articles, and deceive the people on the island. The result is only self-humiliation and cannot change the fate of \"independence\" provocations that are destined to fail.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260520_12766733.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-20","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","On the 20th, Chen Binhua, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the 20th that in the \"May 20\" speech by Taiwan leaders and in answering reporters' questions about cross-strait relations:\nLai Ching-te's speech today was full of lies and deception, hostility and confrontation. He stubbornly adhered to the wrong position of \"Taiwan independence\", promoted the so-called fallacies of \"sovereign independence\" and \"non-subordination\", exaggerated the \"mainland threat\", escalated cross-Strait confrontation, deliberately \"sought independence by force\" and \"relying on external forces\", undermined the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait, and once again proved to be an out-and-out \"cross-Strait peace destroyer\" and \"Taiwan Strait crisis creator\". While continuing to advocate \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and manipulating \"anti-China resistance\", it falsely claims to promote cross-strait dialogue and exchanges in an attempt to deceive the Taiwanese people and deceive international public opinion. These common tactics have been seen through by more and more people in Taiwan. Their deceptive and provocative behaviors will be firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the international community, and are destined to fail.\nTaiwan is China's Taiwan. It has never been a country. It has not been in the past and it will definitely not be in the future. The Taiwan issue is a legacy of China's civil war in the 1940s. No matter how Taiwan is elected or who is elected after 1949, it cannot change Taiwan's status as a part of China. It cannot sever the historical and legal connection that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. It cannot break the iron law that Taiwan's future can only be determined by all the Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. Defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity is the firm will of all Chinese people. We will never allow anyone or any force to carry out separatist plots for \"Taiwan independence\" under any pretense.\n\"Taiwan independence\" is incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait and is the main culprit undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. We will adhere to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus\", unite broadly with Taiwan compatriots, resolutely combat \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The motherland will eventually be reunified, and the tide of reunification will surely roll forward unstoppably!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260520_12766685.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-21","Guo Jiakun","AFP","U.S. President Donald Trump said on Wednesday he would speak with Taiwan’s leader Lai Ching-te about a possible arms sale. Lai also said on Thursday he would be “happy” to talk to Trump. Can the foreign ministry comment on this?","China’s opposition to any official exchanges between the U.S. and China’s Taiwan region, and the U.S.’s arms sales to Taiwan is consistent, clear and rock-firm. China urges the U.S. to implement the important common understandings between our two leaders, honor its commitments and statements, exercise extra caution in handling the Taiwan question, stop sending any wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as the momentum of steady development of China-U.S. relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260521_11915471.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260521_11915149.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-21","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","The Financial Times has reported that the under-secretary of defense for policy in the U.S. has discussed a summer visit to Beijing with Chinese officials. It cites people familiar with the talks. However, the FT reports that China has signaled that it cannot approve a visit until President Trump decides how he will proceed with the arms package. And this is referring to the 14 billion weapons package to Taiwan.…","China’s opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent and clear. As to your specific question, I would refer you to the Ministry of National Defense.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260521_11915471.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260521_11915149.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-22","Guo Jiakun","AFP","The acting U.S. navy secretary said Thursday that arm sales to Taiwan had been put on pause to ensure that the American military had sufficient munitions for its Iran operations. Taiwan said Friday that there was no information indicating that the U.S. intends to make any adjustments to this arms sale. What is the Chinese foreign ministry’s comment on this?","China’s opposition to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region is consistent, clear and firm.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260522_11916315.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260522_11916126.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-22","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Taiwanese prosecutors are investigating three people for allegedly smuggling Nvidia AI chips to China in violation of U.S. export controls. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","It is not a question about foreign affairs. I’m not aware of that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260522_11916315.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260522_11916126.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-25","Mao Ning","DPA","A multiparty delegation of lawmakers from Germany is starting a visit to Taiwan. A member of the delegation said that “Taiwan is a very important partner for Germany.” The delegation is set to meet with Lai Ching-te. What is the foreign ministry’s comment?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The one-China principle is a well-recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is also the political foundation for China-Germany relations. We urge certain people from Germany to abide by the one-China principle, and stop sending wrong messages to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. The DPP authorities’ attempt to solicit external support for their “independence” agenda will surely end in failure.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260525_11917325.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260525_11917239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-25","Mao Ning","Reuters","China has stopped exporting to Japan several heavy rare earths and other materials for at least four months, according to the Chinese customs data. The timing coincides with the dispute between China and Japan over Taiwan. Can we confirm if Beijing has effectively stopped these exports in response to Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi’s remarks on Taiwan?","For anything specific, I’d refer you to competent authorities. Let me say that China banned the export of dual-use items to Japanese military users and for military purposes in accordance with laws and regulations to contain Japan’s remilitarization and its attempt to possess nuclear weapons.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260525_11917325.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260525_11917239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-25","Mao Ning","AFP","Taiwanese authorities claim that the Chinese mainland deployed more than 100 vessels to the region last week from the Yellow Sea to the South China Sea. So some are located near South Korea, Japan and the Philippines, according to the map they provided. What is your response to this claim by the Taiwanese authorities?","The remarks of “Taiwan independence” separatists are not worth commenting. Let me say that the Chinese military carries out activities in accordance with international law and international practice. China is always a constructive force for peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260525_11917325.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260525_11917239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-05-26","Chen Binhua","Not specified (spokesperson statement)","","The Fujian Coast Guard carried out law enforcement inspections in accordance with the law in the waters near Kinmen on May 26. Chen Binhua, spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, said on the same day that Taiwan, Penghu, Jin, and Malaysia are all part of China. The mainland coast guard department’s law enforcement and patrol operations in relevant waters are reasonable and legal, which is conducive to maintaining the order of maritime operations and ensuring the safety of fishermen on both sides of the strait. We firmly support this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260526_12767624.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on May 27, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Hello fellow journalists, welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Please ask questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Regarding the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council's refutation of Lai Ching-te's fallacy in promoting \"Taiwan independence\" in his speech on the second anniversary of his inauguration, Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council stated that \"Taiwan has never been ruled by the People's Republic of China and is not part of it. It is an objective fact and is also the status quo of the Taiwan Strait.\" It hopes that the…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an unquestionable historical and legal fact, and it is also the current status of the Taiwan Strait that cannot be changed. As the only legal government of the whole of China and the only legal representative internationally, the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China fully enjoys and exercises China's sovereignty as a matter of course, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The DPP authorities misrepresented the special state of long-term political confrontation between the two sides of the Taiwan Straits caused by China's civil war and interference from external forces as \"mutual non-subordination.\" This is a separatist proposition that ignores the facts and is a complete lie. No matter what the DPP authorities say or do, they can't change the fact that Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory, and they can't stop the inevitable reunification of the motherland.\nWanting peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society. We are willing to work with all political parties, organizations and people from all walks of life in Taiwan to strengthen exchanges and dialogue on the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" to seek peace for both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the welfare of our compatriots, and the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767892.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Regarding Lai Ching-te's speech on the second anniversary of his inauguration, public opinion on the island pointed out that the DPP's current strategy has gradually shifted from plotting \"de jure Taiwanese independence\" to \"substantial Taiwanese independence based on identity and culture.\" Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a historical and legal fact that no one can shake, and it is also a general consensus of the international community. Taiwan has never been a country, and it will never become one in the future. Out of their \"independence\" nature and political self-interest, the DPP authorities are vigorously promoting \"cultural Taiwan independence\" and \"de-Sinicization\" in an attempt to distort the national identity of Taiwan compatriots, forgetting their ancestors and betraying the nation, and will surely be liquidated by history. We will never tolerate or tolerate any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. No matter what tricks Lai Ching-te and the DPP try, they are all in vain. They cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, cannot cut off the blood ties of Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, cannot erase the imprint of Chinese culture on Taiwanese society and Taiwan compatriots, and cannot stop the historical trend of the eventual reunification of the motherland.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. We hope that the majority of Taiwan compatriots will see clearly the true face and sinister intentions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' \"Taiwan independence\" campaign, strengthen their identification with the Chinese nation, Chinese culture, and the great motherland, strengthen their ambition and backbone to be upright Chinese, and work with us to resolutely oppose all kinds of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities and protect the common homeland of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767891.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","In response to Lai Ching-te's recent Facebook post stating that he \"defends the status quo of the Republic of China and has no Taiwan independence issue,\" public opinion on the island called for the DPP to delete the \"Taiwan Independence Party Platform\" as soon as possible. Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an unquestionable historical and legal fact, and it is also the current situation across the Taiwan Strait. As we all know, the Democratic Progressive Party is a \"Taiwan independence\" party that has long advocated splitting Taiwan from China. In October 1991, the Democratic Progressive Party revised its party platform and wrote the establishment of a \"sovereign and independent Republic of Taiwan and the formulation of a new constitution\" into the party constitution. This is what everyone calls the \"Taiwan Independence Party Platform.\" Although the party passed several \"resolutions\" later, although they made some disguises in their expressions, they never gave up the idea of ​​splitting the country. During each period when the Democratic Progressive Party was in power in Taiwan, it always deliberately sought to promote \"Taiwan independence\" separatism in an attempt to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait in which both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. Lai Ching-te's \"Taiwan independence\" stance is stubborn, he has made constant provocations for \"independence\", and now he has changed his rhetoric in an attempt to mislead public opinion and deceive the people. He is a complete \"Taiwan independence liar.\"\n\"Taiwan independence\" is incompatible with peace across the Taiwan Strait. It is the greatest danger to Taiwan's development and a dead end. The DPP should recognize the situation clearly, comply with public opinion, immediately abandon the \"Taiwan Independence Party Platform\", stop \"Taiwan Independence\" separatist activities, recognize that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and stop obstructing and undermining cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767890.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","As for the 10-year suspension of the contact mechanism between the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait and the Taiwan Straits Exchange Foundation, the Mainland Affairs Council said, \"The reason for the suspension is that the mainland set unacceptable political preconditions and it was the other party's decision to suspend it.\" Any comment on this?","In 1992, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits and the Taiwan Strait Foundation reached the \"1992 Consensus\" embodying the one-China principle and clearly defined the nature of cross-strait relations. It was on this political basis that the two sessions launched negotiations and signed a series of agreements, benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\", and unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. This is the root cause of the suspension of dialogue and consultation between the two sessions, and the source of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767888.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","On May 24, the Shenzhou 23 manned spacecraft was successfully launched. The first Hong Kong astronaut participated in the national manned space mission, triggering heated discussions among people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Some public opinion on the island hopes that Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwanese youth, can participate in the motherland's aerospace industry in the future. Any comment on this?","Developing the aerospace industry and building a powerful aerospace nation is the aerospace dream pursued unremittingly by the Chinese nation. The Shenzhou 23 manned spacecraft launch mission was a complete success, which is the common pride and glory of all Chinese people. We extend warm congratulations to Dr. Lai Jiaying for becoming the first Hong Kong astronaut and the fourth Chinese female astronaut! Her space journey and spirit of courage to challenge and never give up will inspire Hong Kong teenagers to love and join the national aerospace industry and realize that with the support of the great motherland, everyone can shine their own glory. The stars and rivers are vast, chasing dreams in the sky. We look forward to our Taiwan compatriots working with our mainland compatriots to explore the vast universe and turn their dreams into reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767887.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the song \"Happy Breakup on May 20\" written by netizens to commemorate the second anniversary of Lai Qingde's coming to power has become popular on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Many netizens said that the lyrics in the lyrics, such as \"Hard days are lived every day, happy breakup, goodbye Qingde\", express the unspeakable feelings of the people on the island towards Lai Qingde's rebellious behavior in…","I have listened to this song and noticed the \"complaint-style\" adaptation by netizens. The lyrics are vivid and vivid, which fully reflects netizens' strong dissatisfaction and opposition to Lai Qingde's actions in the two years since he came to power, and has resonated with many Taiwanese people. I hope Lai Qingde will pay more attention to people's livelihood and welfare and less political manipulation and self-interest calculations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","DPP spokesperson Wu Zheng recently said that he was \"bored to death\" because he couldn't stand the criticism of Lai Qingde by the spokesman for the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council every week. This triggered discussion among netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, who believed that this statement was an emotional loss caused by his understanding that \"Taiwan independence\" would not work. Any…","The more you debate the truth, the clearer it becomes. Only when the truth is distorted will you be at a loss for words. The emotional expression of the spokesperson of the Democratic Progressive Party fully exposed his lack of integrity. The Lai Ching-te administration stubbornly adheres to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", and its various perverse actions seriously violate the mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society and severely undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. It will surely be strongly criticized and firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the international community, and its pursuit of \"Taiwan independence\" will eventually be ruined.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Fuzhou launched the \"Third Batch of Pilot Policies to Create a \"City Life Circle\" in Fuzhou\", which attracted the attention of the people on the island. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On May 22, Fuzhou City, following the release of two batches of 20 pilot policies to create Fuzhou-Mazhou \"Intra-city Living Circle\" at the 26th and 27th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Fairs and achieved remarkable results, focused on areas where Taiwan compatriots and Matsu residents have loud voices, wide needs, and high urgency, and promoted The more valuable \"Third Batch of Pilot Policies for Building a \"City Life Circle\" in Fuma\" was released at the 28th China International Maritime Fair, which includes 10 specific measures in three aspects: optimizing the Taiwan-related business environment, deepening scientific and technological exchanges and cooperation between Rong and Taiwan, and improving the convenience of Fuma's \"small three links\".\nAfter the policy was released, it was widely praised and welcomed by the Taiwan compatriots in Rong and Matsu residents. The third batch of policies will further promote the development of Taiwan-funded enterprises in Rong, make Fuma's \"same-city living circle\" more convenient, provide more support for Taiwan compatriots and Matsu residents in implementing equal treatment, improving the convenience of living in the same city, expanding the mainland market, and integrating into the mainland's industrial chain and supply chain. It will further deepen Rong-Taiwan fishery cooperation, common cross-strait standards and promote the development of Taiwan-related parks, which will help accelerate urbanization and promote the spiritual harmony and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","The \"Holy Land of Confucianism, Hospitality in Shandong\" tourism promotion exhibition recently opened at the 2026 Kaohsiung Summer Travel Fair. Many Taiwanese people expressed at the event that they learned about Shandong through movies and TV dramas and yearned to travel to the mainland. Any comment on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait share the same roots, culture and race. Cultural exchanges are an important bridge to promote spiritual unity among compatriots. Film and television works are an important channel to enhance mutual understanding and emotional connection between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe land of Qilu has a long history. As the birthplace of Chinese civilization and Confucian culture, sages such as Confucius and Mencius were born here, accumulating a profound cultural heritage. Shandong has beautiful and diverse landscapes. Mount Tai is the top of the Five Mountains, and Mount Laoshan and Yimeng Mountain are breathtaking. The Yellow and Bohai Seas are vast and long, and the Yellow River rushes into the sea to create a rare intersection of yellow and blue. The ancient charm of the Grand Canal is spread, the springs in Jinan are beautiful and beautiful, and the mountains, seas, rivers and lakes have their own customs. The folk customs here are wonderful, the intangible cultural heritage skills have a long history, and the seasonal festivals are lively. Shandong cuisine, which ranks first among the eight major cuisines, has an authentic flavor. Specialties such as Zibo Barbeque and Dezhou Braised Chicken are fresh and attractive. The mountains, rivers, humanities, scenery and delicious food are integrated, showing the unique charm of Shandong. Hearing is worth seeing. We welcome more Taiwanese compatriots to come to Shandong and the mainland to visit and discover the beauty of the mainland with their own eyes.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, the \"Happy Island Alliance\", an \"urgent independence\" political party on the island, issued an open letter expressing its willingness to adjust the party's fundamental position under the condition that \"Taiwanese rule Taiwan and a high degree of autonomy\" obtain clear legal commitments, consider incorporating it into the governance framework of the People's Republic of China, and participate in the…","The two sides of the Taiwan Strait will eventually be reunified and will be reunified. On the basis of the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to engage in dialogue and consultation with people from various political parties, groups, sectors, and classes in Taiwan on the development of cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, and jointly promote the process of the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, the second Cross-Strait Industrial Development Conference was held in Fuzhou. The conference released the \"Initiative for Strengthening Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation\", which attracted attention and praise from the industries on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On May 21, the second Cross-Strait Industrial Development Conference with the theme of \"Cross-Strait Industrial Chain, Join Hands for Shared Prosperity\" was held in Fuzhou. The China Federation of Industrial Economics and other ten mainland industrial federations (associations) jointly released the \"Initiative for Strengthening Cross-Strait Industrial Cooperation\" focusing on five aspects: technological innovation, green and low carbon, digital and intelligent empowerment, opening up overseas markets, and giving full play to the role of industry associations. The \"Initiative\" proposes that at a time when global economic growth is slowing down, tariff increases and trade policies are full of uncertainty, industrial and supply chains are deeply restructured, and market competition is fierce, the industrial circles on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should adhere to the concept of \"complementary advantages, mutual benefit and win-win, and joint development\", actively promote dialogue and exchanges, and promote the common development of cross-strait industrial and supply chains. We encourage and support the industries on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to seize the development opportunities of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\", deepen the complementary advantages of cross-Strait industries and achieve mutual benefit and win-win results, jointly build a more resilient and safer cross-Strait industrial chain and supply chain, and jointly promote the vigorous development of cross-Strait industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","According to reports, after the signing of the \"U.S.-Taiwan Reciprocal Trade Agreement\", the import tariffs on agricultural products such as American oranges were reduced from 35% to 10%, which caused dissatisfaction among the island's industry. Some public opinion believed that the DPP authorities did not communicate with the island's farmers before and after the event, and they were simply \"selling agriculture…","The so-called \"reciprocal agreement\" is actually a list of the United States' bullying of Taiwan's economy and industry. It is a betrayal contract for the DPP authorities to kneel to the United States without a bottom line. In order to \"rely on the United States and seek independence\", the DPP authorities ignore the well-being of the Taiwanese people and turn Taiwan into a dumping ground for American products. This despicable behavior goes against the mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society, harms Taiwan's industry and the vital interests of the people, and will inevitably be counterattacked.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767885.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-strait exchange activities.","Recently, a variety of cross-strait exchange activities have been held across the mainland.\nEconomic and trade exchanges. The 28th Cross-Strait Economic and Trade Fair was held in Fuzhou, Fujian. It set up three major platforms: \"result display and release, economic and trade industry docking, and Fuma's first trial\". It held more than 10 exchange activities and released the third batch of Fuma's \"same-city living circle\" pilot policies. The scale of the event and the number of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese businessmen participating in the event reached new highs. The 22nd China (Shenzhen) International Cultural Industry Expo and Trade Fair was held in Shenzhen. In addition to setting up a Taiwan Pavilion at the main venue and inviting 18 high-quality Taiwanese cultural and creative brand manufacturers to participate in the exhibition, it also set up branch venues and held activities such as the theme salon of \"Design Co-shaping·Digital Intelligence Rebirth\" to build an interactive platform for makers from both sides of the Taiwan Strait and help Taiwanese youth pursue and realize their dreams in Shenzhen. On May 20, Shenzhen held a financial assistance event for Taiwan. Nearly 100 Taiwanese businessmen, including representatives from Taiwanese enterprises, Taiwanese financial institutions, and the Shenzhen Taiwanese Business Association, met with Shenzhen securities firms to discuss building a tripartite collaborative cooperation channel between cross-Strait governments, banks, and enterprises to help Taiwanese companies better leverage the mainland capital market to achieve high-quality development.\nCultural exchange. On May 23, the 36th National Day for Disabled Persons, the \"Full Protection, Integration and Blooming\" Lutai Disabled Persons Art Exchange Performance was held in Xiamen, Fujian Province, showcasing the artistic talents and self-improvement spirit of disabled compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. In mid-May, the 2026 Southern Fujian Poetry Festival was held at Fujian Minnan Normal University, and the Shoutai North Road Opera exchange event was held in Shouning County, Ningde, Fujian. Taiwanese Beiguan Opera was invited to return to their hometown for the first time for exchanges, to jointly inherit China's excellent traditional culture and enhance the friendship between folks on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nYouth exchange. The 14th Straits Youth Gathering and Lutai Youth Together Event was held in Xiamen. Youth from both sides of the Taiwan Strait conducted exchanges and discussions around Southern Fujian culture and intangible cultural heritage skills. \"Integrating Haicang to Create a Future Together\" Taiwan Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Sharing Forum was held in Haicang District, Xiamen City. Through the form of \"enterprise visits + employment guidance + experience sharing\", it provided more opportunities and convenience for Taiwanese youth to find employment and entrepreneurship in Haicang. On May 24, the 2026 Zhangtai \"Basketball Association Longjia Cup\" Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament and Sports Cultural Exchange Event was held in Zhangzhou. More than 300 young players from both sides of the Taiwan Strait competed competitively while also carrying out social activities such as campus interaction and Southern Fujian cultural experience.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, when asked whether he would have a phone call with Lai Ching-te before making a decision on U.S. arms sales to Taiwan, U.S. President Trump said he would \"talk\" with him. Lai Ching-te said that if there is an opportunity for dialogue, he will emphasize that the purchase of US troops is a necessary means to safeguard Taiwan's security and maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. Any comment…","We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between the United States and Taiwan, China, and the sale of weapons to Taiwan by the United States. We urge the U.S. to implement the important consensus reached at the China-U.S. Presidential Meeting, abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiques, handle the Taiwan issue with caution and prudence, stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, and take practical actions to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the steady development of China-U.S. relations.\nThe DPP authorities deliberately \"rely on the United States to seek independence\" and \"use force to seek independence,\" escalate cross-Strait confrontation and undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. They are out-and-out \"cross-Strait peace destroyers\" and \"Taiwan Strait crisis creators.\" I am warning the Democratic Progressive Party authorities that the reunification of the motherland is unstoppable. No matter how many weapons we buy, it will only be a mantis' attempt to do the trick and will only accelerate the defeat of \"Taiwan independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767886.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","According to reports, the Taiwan military spent more than NT$980 million to purchase multiple self-made drone countermeasures systems, and received \"zero points\" on both inspections. Some public opinion on the island has questioned that the DPP authorities are using drones to feed \"green friends\". Do you have any comment on this?","Out of their \"Taiwan independence\" nature and political self-interest, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities invested hard-earned money that could have been used to improve the livelihood and well-being of the Taiwanese people into a bottomless pit of meaningless arms purchases. The Taiwanese people clearly see how many ulterior interests are involved in sharing the spoils and lining their own pockets.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","According to reports, the acting secretary of the U.S. Navy recently stated that the United States is suspending an arms sales to Taiwan worth approximately US$14 billion. The DPP authorities said they would continue to fight. Any comment on this?","Our position of firmly opposing the US arms sales to China's Taiwan region is consistent, clear and firm. The DPP authorities' attempts to \"rely on the United States for independence\" and \"reject reunification with force\" are doomed to lead to their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","The Nauru government recently issued an announcement stating that it has adopted internal norms on the one-China principle, requiring public officials to strictly abide by the one-China principle in all official activities. The DPP authorities made groundless accusations. Any comment on this?","We express our appreciation for the stance and practices of relevant countries in adhering to the one-China principle. If you gain the right path, you will get a lot of help, but if you get the wrong path, you will get little help. Facts have once again proved that the one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community and the basic norm of international relations. It is the general trend, the great cause and the aspiration of the people. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and go against the historical trend, which will only cause obstacles in the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","In his speech on the second anniversary of his inauguration, Lai Ching-te said that direct democratic elections 30 years ago not only represented that \"sovereignty rests with the people\", but also demonstrated that Taiwan is already a \"sovereign and independent country.\" Any comment on this?","Lai Qingde fabricated lies and fabricated legal principles in an attempt to package the \"new two-nation theory\" under the guise of \"elections\" and \"democracy.\" This was pure self-deception. Taiwan is part of China. It has never been a country and will never become one. There is no so-called \"sovereignty\" at all.\nNo matter how many lies you tell, they will never become true. The more Lai Qingde tells him, the more he proves his guilty conscience. Taiwan is China's Taiwan. No matter how the Taiwan region elects or who is elected, it cannot change Taiwan's status as a part of China. It cannot sever the historical and legal connection that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. It cannot break the iron law that Taiwan's future can only be determined by all the Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202605/t20260527_12767889.htm"],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Regarding the joint statement signed by China and Russia reaffirming the one-China principle, Taiwan's foreign affairs department stated that \"the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are not subordinate to each other, and any statement intended to distort Taiwan's sovereign status is an act of bullying that undermines international peace and stability.\" Any comment on this?","This joint statement is the most important political outcome document reached at the meeting between the heads of state of China and Russia. Facts have once again proved that the one-China principle is the basic norm of international relations and the general consensus of the international community. It is the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times. Taiwan is part of China, and there is no so-called \"sovereignty\" at all. No matter how the DPP authorities spread fallacies, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and they cannot shake the international community's basic pattern of adhering to the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","The Taipei office of the American Institute in Taiwan (AIT) recently stated that the Kuomintang echoes the mainland's position on some diplomatic and security issues and ignores Taiwan's traditional allies such as the United States and Japan. During Cheng Li-wun's visit to the United States, she may be asked whether she will change her past political line. Any comment on this?","The Taiwan issue is China's internal affairs. Solving the Taiwan issue is a matter for the Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and no outsiders can comment on it. For some time, relevant institutions have frequently made irresponsible remarks on cross-Strait affairs, which we firmly oppose. The United States should abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-US joint communiques, and be cautious in its words and deeds on the Taiwan issue. Our position on Taiwan's foreign exchanges is consistent and clear, that is, it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Shenzhou 23 was launched successfully a few days ago, and there were also Kuomintang members leading Taiwanese young students to visit the site. We also noticed that when the spokesperson came in today, he had the Shenzhou 23 logo badge pinned on the collar of his suit jacket, which was very shiny. What are the spokesperson’s expectations for Taiwan’s young people to participate in the space program in the…","The first question. As I just said, the Shenzhou 23 manned spacecraft launch mission was a complete success, which is the common pride and glory of all Chinese people, so I especially wear the logo of this mission today. In addition, I have noticed that many Taiwanese compatriots are also proud and honored. The Chinese nation’s space dream belongs to our compatriots on the mainland, Hong Kong and Macao, and overseas Chinese, as well as our compatriots in Taiwan. We believe that in the near future, Taiwan compatriots will be able to explore the vast universe together with their mainland compatriots and turn their dreams into reality.\nSecond question. We have always encouraged and supported cross-Strait exchanges in all fields and protected the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots do not have to have any concerns when traveling to the mainland. Out of political self-interest, the DPP authorities maliciously hyped and spread rumors to smear the mainland in an attempt to create a \"chilling effect\", obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. This is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","The list of new directors recently announced by Taiwan's \"Center for Cultural Affairs\" includes Taiwanese artist Lin Chi-ling, which has attracted public attention on the island. Lin recently stated that he decided to resign from the position \"in order to avoid more untrue speculations and misunderstandings.\" Any comment on this?","In recent years, the \"Cultural Content Initiative\" has instigated and financed the filming of many film and television dramas such as \"Zero Day Attack\" that distorted history and exaggerated the \"mainland threat\". It is a political tool for the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to promote \"cultural Taiwan independence\" and instigate \"resistance to China and Taiwan.\" It is a wise decision for people in Taiwan’s literary and artistic circles to see clearly its essence and draw a clear line with it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question is that the recent mining disaster in Shanxi caused heavy casualties. Lai Qingde expressed his condolences and condolences. What is the mainland's comment on its condolences? Do you think it is showing goodwill to the mainland? If Taiwan’s rescue team can go to the mainland to assist in further disaster relief, will the mainland accept it?\nSecond question: Li Hongyuan, vice chairman of the KMT…","The first question. Recently, a gas explosion occurred underground in a coal mine in Qinyuan County, Changzhi City, Shanxi Province, causing heavy casualties. Relevant parties have made every effort to carry out the treatment of the wounded and on-site rescue. People from all walks of life on the island also expressed their concern and condolences through various forms.\nSecond question. Exchanges and integration are where the aspirations and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait lie. We have always actively supported cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in all fields, supported compatriots on both sides of the Strait to enhance mutual understanding, achieve mutual benefit and win-win results, work together to develop cross-Strait relations, and build and protect our common home.\nThe third question. Whether there is a big demand for restoring cross-strait destinations or not, data will tell. We have previously published relevant data. No matter what the DPP authorities say, it cannot change the fact that there is strong demand in the cross-strait direct air flight market and people's strong desire for exchanges. We have always been actively promoting the full resumption of normalization of direct cross-Strait air passenger flights. It is hoped that the DPP authorities will face up to the demand, comply with public opinion, and lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-strait air transport as soon as possible, allowing cross-strait airlines to independently arrange flight plans based on market demand. The DPP authorities have always claimed that the so-called 13 \"charter points\" that have been opened have complicated application procedures and harsh conditions, which the aviation industry \"can see but cannot eat.\" If it is true that it \"fully considers the needs of industry and travel companies\", it should restore the so-called \"charter points\" to regular flight points to facilitate cross-strait personnel exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","广东广播电视台“粤TV”记者","Recently, the Taipei International Tourism Expo opened, but Taiwan's tourism department required tourism operators on the island not to post advertisements and copywriting for travel to the mainland, causing dissatisfaction and criticism from the tourism industry on the island. Any comment on this?","The DPP authorities deliberately obstruct cross-Strait tourism exchanges, which not only violates the laws of the market, but also harms the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and tourism operators. Facts have once again shown that the crux and obstacle of cross-strait tourism issues lies in the interference and obstruction of the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities should comply with public opinion and remove unreasonable restrictions such as the \"ban on group travel\" to the mainland as soon as possible to create favorable conditions for cross-strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","The Taiwanese novel \"Taiwan Odyssey\" recently won the 2026 International Booker Prize. According to Agence France-Presse, author Yang Shuangzi said, \"I hope this novel can be published in China in the future and promote dialogue about what the Taiwanese people want for the future.\" What are the conditions for mainland bookstores to introduce this work or publish its simplified version? When Taiwanese books enter…","I want to emphasize that Taiwanese books are not published in \"China\" but in mainland China.\nWriters on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should take a firm national stance, respect historical facts, face up to and deeply understand the huge harm caused by Japan's aggressive war and fascism to the Chinese people and the people of the world, and promote the spiritual harmony of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait with responsible and high-quality works.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-05-27","Chen Binhua","台湾TVBS电视台记者","The Ma Ying-jeou Foundation has long promoted cross-Strait youth exchanges. Will the mainland worry about the internal strife affecting the credibility of cross-Strait non-governmental exchanges? Will the future interaction between mainland China and the foundation be affected by this matter?","We have taken note of the relevant reports. In recent years, the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation has carried out a series of cross-strait exchange activities to promote exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the strait, especially young people. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits are all Chinese and one family. The general trend of getting closer and coming together cannot be changed by any force.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202605/t20260527_12767895.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-05-28","Mao Ning","Reuters","The International Institute for Strategic Studies has come out with its strategic assessment report. It says that a major conflict between the U.S. and China over Taiwan could risk escalation, potentially to a nuclear level, and both sides could target each other’s commands and communication hubs. How does the ministry view this assessment?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that brooks no external interference. To keep the Taiwan Strait peaceful and stable, it is absolutely essential to unequivocally oppose “Taiwan independence.” The U.S. side should earnestly implement the important common understandings between the two presidents in their meetings and exercise extra caution in handling the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260528_11919951.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260528_11919928.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-05-28","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say that during his visit to China, U.S. President Trump said that he \"is not looking to have somebody go independent\", nor is he looking to \"travel 9,500 miles to fight a war\" for Taiwan. In response, Lai Ching-te disingenuously claimed that Taiwan will never become a \"bargaining chip,\" while defending the status quo of the \"Republic of China\", and asserted that there is \"no question of Taiwan…","\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are mutually incompatible. Safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait represents the greatest common ground between China and the United States.\nLai Ching-te once blatantly labeled himself a \"pragmatic worker for Taiwan independence\". Now, he is hypocritically claiming that \"there is no Taiwan independence issue\"— a mere repackaging of his rhetoric after being harshly confronted by reality. This only shows that the pursuit of \"Taiwan independence\" has reached a dead end, and the illusion of seeking U.S. support for \"Taiwan independence\" is bound to be shattered.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16467353.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16466689.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-05-28","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, it was reported that President Xi Jinping met with Pakistani Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif during his visit to China. Additionally, General Zhang Shengmin, Vice Chairman of the Central Military Commission, met with Field Marshal Syed Asim Munir, Chief of Defense Forces and Chief of the Army Staff of the Pakistan Armed Forces, who visited China concurrently with the Prime Minister.…","On your first question, China and Pakistan are good neighbors connected by the same mountains and rivers, good friends bound by trust, good partners watching out for each other, and good brothers sharing weal and woe. Since the establishment of diplomatic relations 75 years ago, the friendship between our two nations has stood the test of shifting international landscapes. It has grown stronger over time and taken deep root in the hearts of our peoples. Pakistani friends often describe China-Pakistan friendship as \"higher than mountain, deeper than sea, and sweeter than honey\", while the Chinese people affectionately refer to Pakistan as an \"iron-clad brother\".\nChina and Pakistan enjoy close military-to-military relationship. Fruitful outcomes have been witnessed in practical cooperation across areas such as strategic communication, joint exercises and training, personnel training, and equipment and technology. A series of flagship joint exercises—such as Exercise Warrior for the armies, Exercise Sea Guardian for the navies, and Exercise Shaheen for the air forces—have become signature programs for bilateral cooperation. We stand ready to work with Pakistan to follow the strategic guidance of our leaders, carry forward traditional friendship, strengthen strategic communication, enhance practical cooperation, firmly support each other on issues involving our core interests, so as to elevate our military-to-military relations to a higher level and jointly contribute to the building of an even closer China-Pakistan community with a shared future in the new era, as well as to global development and security.\nOn your second question, China advocates that defense and security cooperation between countries must not target any third party or harm the interests of any third party, still less undermine regional peace and stability. Japan's right-wing forces continue to take dangerous strides and engage in provocations in the military and security sphere. Its resurgent neo-militarism is poised to become a source of turmoil for East Asia. All peace-loving people should reject Japan's regressive course, preventing it from damaging regional peace and bring catastrophe upon the wider world once again.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16467353.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16466689.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-05-28","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The U.S. Acting Secretary of the Navy recently stated publicly that Washington is deferring a planned arms sale package to the Taiwan region worth approximately USD 14 billion, drawing close attention from observers on the island. Meanwhile, the U.S. House of Representatives has unveiled some contents of the Fiscal Year 2027 National Defense Authorization Act, which includes the \"Taiwan Security Cooperation…","China's position is consistent and unequivocal: we firmly oppose U.S. arms sales to China's Taiwan region. The U.S. side must abide by the one-China principle and the stipulations of the three China-U.S. Joint Communiqués, especially the August 17 Communiqué, faithfully implement the important common understandings reached between the two presidents, honor its commitments and public statements to China, and handle the Taiwan question with the utmost prudence. It should take concrete actions to keep bilateral and military-to-military relations on a stable, sound and sustainable track.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16467353.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16466689.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-05-29","Mao Ning","Reuters","There have been reports that a Canadian warship transited the Taiwan Strait. Is the foreign ministry able to confirm this and do you have any comment?","China respects the right of navigation that all countries are entitled to under international law, but firmly opposes acts that undermine China’s sovereignty and security in the name of freedom of navigation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260529_11921368.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260529_11921244.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-05-29","Mao Ning","CCTV","Yesterday during the Philippine President’s visit to Japan, the two countries issued a joint statement announcing the start of talks on the delimitation of exclusive economic zone and continental shelf between Japan and the Philippines. What’s China’s comment?","The area the two countries announced they will delimit is east of China’s Taiwan island. According to China’s domestic law and international law including UNCLOS, China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in this area. Japan and the Philippines’ so-called maritime delimitation talks constitute a severe violation of China’s maritime rights and interests, UNCLOS and other international law and basic norms governing international relations. China strongly deplores and firmly opposes that and has lodged serious protests with both countries.\nThe so-called delimitation talks are completely illegal, null and void, and will have no effect on China’s claims to rights in the area east of the Taiwan island or exercise of China’s lawful rights. China urges Japan and the Philippines to immediately stop any violation of China’s maritime rights and interests and take concrete actions to uphold regional peace and stability.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202605/t20260529_11921368.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202605/t20260529_11921244.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-01","Lin Jian","TV Asahi","According to the New York Times, one of its journalists was deported. What’s your comment?","The New York Times provided platform for Taiwan authorities to peddle separatist rhetoric for “Taiwan independence,” and blatantly called China’s Taiwan region a “country.” This grossly violates the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and sends a gravely wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces. China firmly opposes it. The New York Times should correct its wrongdoings rather than continue down the wrong path.\nDuring the time the journalist you mentioned was stationed in China, she had a track record of deceiving people into unknowingly taking interviews, and violated the Regulations of the People’s Republic of China on News Coverage by Permanent Offices of Foreign Media Organizations and Foreign Journalists. Her residence permit was thus revoked as dictated by laws and regulations. The U.S. side, out of so-called “reciprocity,” is engaged in political suppression against journalists from Xinhua News Agency working legally in the United States. China firmly opposes this.\nThe facts and merits of the issue of media between China and the U.S. are clear. The root cause is the U.S. side’s unilaterally stirring up trouble, and politicizing issues related to media. China always provides facilitation for foreign journalists as they report and live in China. In recent years, China has shown flexibility and provided visa facilitation for quite a few U.S. journalists coming to China to do reporting, whereas Chinese journalists’ applications for reporting in the United States have rarely been approved. The U.S. side should earnestly implement the understanding reached with China on media issues and take concrete actions to ensure the legitimate rights and interests of Chinese journalists who work and stay in the United States.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260601_11922642.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260601_11922615.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-02","Mao Ning","Shenzhen TV","On May 31, in response to the Foreign Ministry Spokesperson’s remarks on Japan-Philippines announcement of maritime delimitation talks, Taiwan’s “foreign affairs department” commended Japan and the Philippines and questioned Chinese mainland’s sovereign rights over relevant waters. What is your comment?","China has made clear its position on the announced maritime delimitation talks between Japan and the Philippines. Let me reiterate that the area involved in their planned talks is east of China’s Taiwan island. According to China’s domestic law and international law including UNCLOS, China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in this area. As per UNCLOS, the delimitation of the exclusive economic zone and the continental shelf between States with opposite or adjacent coasts shall be effected by the States concerned by agreement on the basis of equity. Any delimitation concerning waters to the east of Taiwan must have China as a party to the talks. Japan and the Philippines’ attempt to bypass China and initiate the so-called maritime delimitation talks constitutes a severe violation of UNCLOS and other international laws and basic norms governing international relations. It also seriously infringes on China’s maritime rights and interests. China will not allow this.\nThe two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China. To uphold national sovereignty and maritime rights and interests is the shared responsibility of all Chinese people on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities, in pursuing selfish political gains, have gone so far as to put the Chinese nation’s vital interest up for sale, a move that betrays ancestors and breaches all moral boundaries. This once again shows that these separatists have completely forfeited the national stance and degenerated into traitors to the nation. What awaits them is contempt from Chinese on both sides of the Strait and the judgement of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260602_11923474.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260602_11923344.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-02","Mao Ning","Nippon TV","Cheng Li-wen is visiting the U.S. Does the foreign ministry have any comment on this?","Issues related to external exchanges of China’s Taiwan region should be handled in line with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260602_11923474.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260602_11923344.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-03","Mao Ning","Hubei Media Group","According to media in Africa and the Taiwan region, before and after Lai Ching-te’s visit to Eswatini, the DPP authorities provided the country with 25 billion or so New Taiwan dollars worth of funding, and pledged that the income of related project belongs entirely to the king and the royal family. Taiwan’s representatives in Eswatini will also profit from that. What’s your comment?","Those reports are yet another example of how far the Lai Ching-te authorities would go to selfishly advance their “Taiwan independence” agenda. Their expensive dollar diplomacy—a combination of corruption, fraudulence, bribery and money for abuse of power—has cost dearly the people in Taiwan, equivalent to collecting more than NT$1,000 from every person in Taiwan. Having Eswatini as a “diplomatic ally” is not about delivering real benefits for the people, but to line the pockets of the very few people who profit from it. This is political theatrics steeped in greed and graft.\nThe one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus, and a basic norm governing international relations. This year, China has extended zero-tariff treatment to all 53 African countries having diplomatic relations with China. This is a fresh opportunity for African countries to expand exports to China and grow their economies. It has delivered tangible benefits to Chinese and Africans. Eswatini is the only country left in Africa with so-called “diplomatic ties” to Taiwan. Betting on “Taiwan independence” has no future. It will only cost them opportunities for development and lead to international isolation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260603_11936890.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260603_11924150.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on June 3, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Let’s start asking questions now.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Please introduce the preparations for the 18th Straits Forum.","The 18th Straits Forum will be held in Fujian in mid-June, and the forum conference will be held on June 13. The main venue of the forum is located in Xiamen, and relevant activities will be held in the Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone of Fujian's districted cities. This forum adheres to the positioning of \"non-governmental, grassroots and extensive\" and continues the theme of \"expanding non-governmental exchanges and deepening integrated development\". It has set up 58 activities in four major sections: grassroots exchanges, youth exchanges, cultural exchanges and economic exchanges. Representatives of Taiwan's relevant political parties and representatives from trade unions, youth, women, folk beliefs, agriculture, fishery, water conservancy, culture and tourism, health, industry, commerce and finance will be invited to participate.\nAt present, the preparations for the forum are advancing steadily and progressing smoothly. The Forum News Center will issue an application notice for reporters, and all media reporters are welcome to interview and report.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769130.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities.","From May to June, cross-strait exchange activities in various fields continued to be vigorous. Gatherings time after time have brought compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait closer to each other, and events after events have made the Chinese culture of the same roots deeply rooted in the hearts of the people.\nOn May 22, Huacan·College Industry-Education Integration Exchange Event was held in Nanchang, Jiangxi. More than 100 young designer representatives from more than 60 universities and industry organizations on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and overseas gathered together to share experiences and discuss development. On May 29, the launching ceremony of the third series of cultural exchange activities between Buddhist platforms was held in Foshan, Guangdong. Nearly 500 people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait participated. The event focused on sports exchanges. In addition to traditional folk cultural sports such as martial arts, dragon boating, and lion dance, it also added fashionable sports such as pickleball, slow pitch, and roller skating that are popular among young people to create a multi-dimensional and normalized youth exchange platform for Buddhist platforms. From May 29th to 31st, the 21st Straits Tourism Expo was held in Xiamen, Fujian Province. The expo focused on creating an urban weekend micro-vacation destination and attracted 55 Taiwanese companies to participate. On June 2, the 2026 Third Season Xiangtai Cultural Exchange Event was held in Xiang'an District, Xiamen, Fujian. More than 300 guests from both sides of the Taiwan Strait passed on and carried forward the excellent traditional culture of southern Fujian through the exchange of Minnan songs.\nTwo events are previewed here. On June 11, the \"World Chinese Yandi Hometown Root-Seeking Festival in the Year of Bingwu\" will be held in Suizhou, Hubei. More than 130 Taiwanese cultural circles, youth and grassroots representatives will participate in the ceremony to pay homage to Yandi Shennong and inherit the millennium cultural heritage. From June 12 to 16, the second Cross-Strait Youth E-Sports Carnival will be held in Suzhou, Jiangsu Province. 150 young people from both sides of the strait will jointly carry out e-Sports exhibitions, base camps, technology experiences and other exchange activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","In recent times, \"Provincial Super League\" has been held in full swing across the mainland. In particular, the \"Fujian Super League\" has launched a series of special activities against Taiwan, which has attracted enthusiastic attention from the majority of Taiwanese compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","As you can see, this summer, the \"Suzhou Super League\"'s outing, the \"Fujian Super League\"'s cross-strait love, the \"Guangdong Super League's\" cheerleaders, the \"Sichuan Super League's\" roar, and the \"Northeast Super League's\" fireworks ignited the passion and blood of fans on both sides of the Taiwan Strait every weekend.\nIn order to support the construction of cross-strait integrated development demonstration zones, \"Minchao\" has recently innovatively launched three series of special activities against Taiwan. The first is to \"call you to participate\", opening up exclusive quotas for Taiwanese compatriots, and each Fujian Super League participating team can add 2 new Taiwanese compatriots players. The second is to \"invite you to watch the game.\" Each major competition area invites Taiwanese compatriots to go to Fujian to watch the game, launches a short video collection campaign for \"Fans on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to cheer in the same frame\", and invites Kinmen and Matsu specialty cheerleaders to perform on the same stage as the Fujian cheerleaders. The third is \"Invite you to come and communicate.\" Each competition area will take the initiative to connect with teams from Taiwan, Hong Kong, Macao and overseas Chinese, and carry out friendly exchange matches on a regular basis. Xiamen, Pingtan and other places will hold at least one special exchange match between a Fujian Super League team and a team from a city in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769122.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Among the ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, \"Taiwanese entrepreneurs can participate in the creation of mainland micro-short dramas in various ways\" has attracted attention. What are the ways and means for Taiwanese compatriots to participate in the creation of micro-short dramas?","Micro-short plays are new popular literature and art in the Internet era. They are deeply loved by young people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and have become a new growth point in the cultural industry. On April 12, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China was authorized to issue ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. The ninth item included \"Taiwanese industry operators can participate in the creation of mainland micro-short dramas in various ways.\" This provides strong policy support for promoting cross-strait micro-short drama exchanges and cooperation.\nCurrently, there are three main ways for Taiwanese industry players to participate in the creation of mainland micro-short dramas.\nFirst, you can invest in and establish radio and television program production and operation companies in Fujian. The \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone\" clearly states that \"a pilot program will allow Taiwanese businesses to invest in and establish radio and television program production and operating companies in Fujian.\" Currently, 18 Taiwan-funded enterprises in Fujian have obtained radio and television program production and operation licenses and are producing micro-short dramas.\nSecond, we can co-produce and create micro-short dramas with mainland industry players. The creative teams on both sides of the Taiwan Strait can jointly create, leverage their respective strengths in production coordination, participation in publicity, shooting execution, and picture design, and develop together.\nThird, you can participate in micro-short drama performances. Taiwanese entertainers can participate in the filming of various types of short dramas. Taiwanese industry professionals who have dreams and love to work hard are welcome to seize the opportunity and actively participate in the creation of micro-short dramas to jointly promote the inheritance, protection, innovation and development of Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769126.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said in a conversation with high school students on the island that the impact of TikTok and Xiaohongshu on Taiwan's young generation has reached a security crisis. Over time, Taiwan may not have the will to protect democracy and will regard \"China\" as a good guy; it will require the education and cultural departments to handle it properly. Any comment on this?","To our Taiwan compatriots, compatriots on the mainland are not only good people, but also relatives and family members. Taiwanese compatriots, especially Taiwanese youth, are increasingly fond of using mainland social software because they can use these social software to enjoy more life experiences and opportunities for free expression. When they share delicious food and beautiful scenery, they will receive enthusiastic interactions that fill the screen with \"I want to go see it\"; when they post about looking for relatives, many mainland netizens will enthusiastically respond and provide clues; when they want to communicate and learn, they will encounter various note-taking tutorials and even \"hand-in-hand\" remote teaching... All the warm moments of intersection are \"two-way rushes\" of \"sharing and co-creation\" by netizens on both sides of the strait, and are a vivid embodiment of \"one family on both sides of the strait\".\nMainland social software helps Taiwanese youth grow, develop, and realize their dreams, but the Lai Ching-te authorities continue to smear it and even intimidate and threaten Taiwanese youth, which shows their guilt and cowardice. No matter how deliberately the Lai authorities try to undermine cross-Strait exchanges and integration, they will never succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769128.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","The 2026 joint interview event for journalists from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, \"Meet in the Central Plains and See the Wonders in Henan\", was recently held in Henan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From May 27 to June 2, the 2026 joint interview event for journalists from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, \"Meet in the Central Plains and See the Wonders in Henan\", was successfully held. More than 40 journalists from both sides of the Taiwan Strait and Hong Kong, as well as Taiwanese youth self-media people, participated in the event and went to Zhengzhou, Luoyang, Kaifeng and other places to interview companies, cultural and museum institutions, etc., and reported on Henan's development in rural revitalization, advanced manufacturing, cultural tourism and other aspects from all aspects and angles, and experienced the rich heritage and vitality of the Central Plains on the ground.\nThe cross-Strait reporter joint interview event is jointly organized by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the China Journalists Association. It has been held for 24 times since 2000. Journalists from both sides of the Taiwan Strait traveled to various parts of the mainland to conduct in-depth interviews and reports, playing a positive role in promoting cross-Strait media exchanges and enhancing mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides. More journalists are welcome to have the opportunity to participate in this brand activity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","The United States recently announced that the non-semiconductor 232 tariff preferential measures for Taiwan specified in the Taiwan-US Investment MOU will take effect from May 1, including auto parts and logs, timber and wood derivatives with a tax rate of no more than 15%. Taiwan's administrative department stated that the preferential treatment received by Taiwan is consistent with that of the European Union,…","The DPP authorities have bowed to the United States and lost faith, betrayed Taiwan's core industries, sacrificed Taiwan's industrial development prospects, and harmed the interests and well-being of the Taiwanese people. The US$500 billion investment in the United States and the implementation of \"zero tariffs\" on 4,885 industrial products and 1,482 agricultural products in the United States and other bloody concessions were only exchanged for symbolic tax concessions. The DPP authorities actually have the nerve to take credit for this and claim it as their own \"merit\", which is completely deceiving themselves and others. Such perverse actions will not deceive Taiwan's industry and people. They will only reap the consequences and become a laughing stock.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769127.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Taiwanese Internet celebrity \"curators\" recently visited Sichuan and Chongqing live, checking in to the Chongqing Anti-Japanese War Relics Museum, visiting Zhang Xue Motorcycle Factory, watching Sichuan Opera Changing Faces and Giant Pandas, and Taiwanese Internet celebrities climbed 178 meters to overlook the Xiamen-Jinjiang Bridge, and went to Yichang to measure the Three Gorges Dam with their feet. These have…","During this period, we have seen many Taiwanese Internet celebrity friends visit and broadcast live in Chongqing, Sichuan, Fujian, Hubei and other places, sharing with the people on the island the beautiful scenery, tasting delicious food, exploring museums and major projects in various parts of the mainland, learning about history, experiencing unique culture, integrating into the daily life of mainland compatriots, and interacting with mainland entrepreneurial youth and entrepreneurs, and talking about cooperation scenes and feelings. Many netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, especially Taiwanese netizens, responded enthusiastically and expressed the hope that there would be more similar kind-hearted interactions and objective recommendations.\nHearing a hundred times is better than seeing it, and meeting it makes you fall in love. We welcome Taiwanese compatriots, including Taiwanese internet celebrities, to visit the mainland, learn about the mainland in various ways, introduce the mainland, and share their real experiences and development opportunities in the mainland with more friends.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769121.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","The Taiwan Film Festival of the 17th Cross-Strait Film Festival was recently held in Ya'an, Sichuan, and the Mainland Film Festival will also meet with Taiwanese audiences in the near future. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The Cross-Strait Film Exhibition is a brand event for cross-Strait film and television exchanges. The 17th Taiwan Film Festival of the Cross-Strait Film Festival was held in Ya'an, Sichuan from May 30 to June 3. Seven Taiwanese films including \"96 Minutes: The Train Bombing\", \"Girls\", and \"Our Unexpected Courage\" were screened in Ya'an. Filmmakers from both sides of the Taiwan Strait conducted discussions on the theme of \"Story and Emotion: Film Expression of China's Excellent Traditional Culture\". The Taiwanese film delegation not only brought the exhibited works to enthusiastically share and interact with mainland audiences at the post-screening exchange site, but also went to the Ya'an Tea Factory and the Ya'an Base of the China Giant Panda Conservation and Research Center for interviews and exchanges, and deeply experienced the charm of Ya'an as a natural film location and fertile ground for film and television development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, the leaders of Japan and the Philippines issued a joint statement, which emphasized the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and announced the launch of the so-called \"maritime delimitation negotiations.\" The DPP authorities echoed this. Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of China's Taiwan Island. Their so-called \"delimitation negotiations\" seriously infringe on China's maritime rights and interests, seriously violate international law and basic norms of international relations, and are completely illegal and invalid.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the Chinese nation and should stand firm on their national stance, uphold national justice, jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation. If the DPP authorities dare to rely on external forces and betray national interests, they will be spurned by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769124.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the Fujian Coast Guard carried out law enforcement inspections in the waters near Kinmen in accordance with the law. The Taiwan Coast Guard said the mainland coast guard \"attempted to create the illusion that it has jurisdiction over Kinmen waters.\" Any comment on this?","Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Malaysia are all part of China. The mainland coast guard department carries out law enforcement inspections in relevant sea areas in accordance with the law to maintain the order of maritime operations and protect the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, which is a normal performance of their duties.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769123.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","NVIDIA founder Huang Jen-Hsun recently said, \"Taiwan needs more electricity.\" Some public opinion on the island pointed out that this statement highlighted concerns about Taiwan's power supply capacity, but the DPP has always dared not face the energy issue that is the lifeline of the industry. Any comment on this?","The DPP authorities are obsessed with pursuing \"Taiwan independence\" and have neither the will nor the ability to solve the structural problems facing the island's economic and social development. \"Lack of electricity\" has become the Achilles heel of Taiwan's sustainable economic and social development, which is obvious to all. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have highly politicized the energy issue. Instead of solving it head-on, they use it as a tool to suppress dissenters and suppress opponents, exposing their self-interest and disregard for Taiwan's people's livelihood and future development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the 2026 Shangri-La Dialogue was held in Singapore. Some public opinion noticed that US Secretary of Defense Hegseth rarely mentioned Taiwan in his keynote speech, but highly affirmed the series of results achieved by President Trump's recent visit to China. Any comment on this?","The Taiwan issue is China's internal affair and does not tolerate any external interference. Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator between China and the United States.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Australia's Lowy Institute recently released a report, \"After Annexation: China's Plan to Rule Taiwan,\" stating that China's strategy toward Taiwan has shifted from its past emphasis on \"peaceful reunification and a high degree of autonomy\" to a \"high-pressure model\" of \"first suppression, then governance.\" Any comment on this?","The Taiwan issue is China's internal affair. The reunification of the motherland is a matter for the Chinese people and a just cause to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The so-called \"annexation\" and \"suppression\" completely confuse right and wrong. The relevant report deliberately spreads the fallacy of the \"China threat\" and peddles panic about the Taiwan Strait crisis, which is unpopular.\nWe would like to emphasize again that \"peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" are our basic policy for solving the Taiwan issue and the best way to achieve national reunification. The specific implementation form of \"one country, two systems\" in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan's actual situation, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions from all walks of life on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and fully take into account the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots. On the premise of ensuring national sovereignty, security, and development interests, after peaceful reunification, Taiwan's social system and way of life will be fully respected, and the desire of Taiwan compatriots to be the masters of the country will be fully protected in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, the so-called \"Taiwan-U.S. Defense Industry Forum\" was held in Taiwan. Huang Zhifang, chairman of the Taiwan Foreign Trade Association, said that Taiwan's industry is ready to work with the United States to jointly create a more reliable \"defense technology ecosystem\" for the Indo-Pacific region. Any comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and China's Taiwan region. The so-called \"defense science and technology ecosystem\" embodies the DPP authorities' evil intentions of \"relying on foreign countries to seek independence\", \"using force to seek independence\" and becoming a \"chess piece\" of the United States' \"use Taiwan to contain China\". It will only put Taiwan into a more dangerous situation and bring serious disasters to Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities continue to collude with external forces to pursue \"independence\" provocations, overestimating their own capabilities and hitting stones with eggs, which will only accelerate the inevitable defeat of \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","In recent days, governments and political figures from many countries including Russia, Canada, and Thailand have continued to speak out, emphasizing their adherence to the one-China stance. Any comment on this?","We express our appreciation for the stance and practices of relevant countries in adhering to the one-China principle and supporting China's reunification cause. Facts have repeatedly proved that the one-China principle is the basic norm of international relations and the general consensus of the international community. It is the aspiration of the people and the trend of the times.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities stated that four mainland-developed applications, including Amap, Bilibili, iQiyi and BIMOBIMO, all have risks such as real-time behavior monitoring, system information acquisition, data transmission and sharing, and reminded Taiwanese people to be more vigilant to ensure their digital security. Any comment on this?","In recent years, more and more mainland applications have been welcomed by Taiwanese compatriots, who believe that these applications are technologically advanced, practical and easy to use. For example, a video \"Teaching you step-by-step to book high-speed rail tickets at 12306\" has recently become popular on the Taiwanese Internet. Many Taiwanese people are searching online for tips on traveling to the mainland and downloading mainland apps to facilitate their various experiences in the mainland. Mainland China's innovative, high-quality products and high-end cutting-edge technologies are constantly meeting the needs of Taiwanese people and becoming a good helper for them to enjoy a better and more convenient life.\nOut of the sinister intention of \"anti-China\", the Democratic Progressive Party authorities continue to maliciously smear and slander mainland technology products and application software, and obstruct the use of Taiwanese people in every possible way. To the point of being anti-technology and anti-era, it will only make more and more Taiwanese people disgusted and despised.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Many Taiwanese media reported that Lai Qingde visited Swaziland by \"smuggling\" in early May, and the price he paid for this was as high as NT$25 billion. The investment plan signed by both parties shows that Taiwan will invest NT$25 billion to build a fuel storage facility in Swaziland, and all profits after completion will belong to the Swaziland royal family. Any comment on this?","In order to pursue \"independence\" political self-interest, the Lai Qingde authorities ignored the livelihood and well-being of the people on the island and squandered the people's hard-earned money. They are out-and-out \"gold and dollar diplomacy\" and \"unscrupulous politicians.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Shen Youzhong, deputy chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that polls show that the majority of Taiwanese people are unwilling to accept \"one country, two systems\" and do not agree with \"the Chinese Communist Party's suppression of Taiwan.\" He insists that Taiwan's future should be jointly decided by the 23 million Taiwanese people. Any comment on this?","Taiwan is China's Taiwan, and Taiwan's future can only and must be jointly decided by the more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. \"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" are the best way to achieve national reunification and are in the best interest of the Chinese nation, including Taiwan compatriots. It is also the best choice to maintain the existing social system and way of life of Taiwan compatriots. Out of the separatist plot of \"Taiwan independence\", the DPP authorities deliberately reject peaceful reunification and discredit \"one country, two systems\" in an attempt to mislead public opinion and deceive the Taiwanese people. They will not succeed.\nWhat needs to be emphasized is that different systems are not an obstacle to unification, nor an excuse for division. More and more insightful people in Taiwan are no longer coerced and deceived by the DPP authorities, support peaceful cross-strait reunification, gradually understand and think about the benefits of \"one country, two systems\", and provide advice and suggestions for the \"two systems\" Taiwan plan through various methods. We believe that more Taiwan compatriots will fully understand the superiority of \"one country, two systems\" and that the \"two systems\" Taiwan plan will be more fully discussed and demonstrated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769129.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Taiwan's public opinion agency reviewed a new batch of nearly NT$300 billion in special budget for US military purchases. Several political parties and groups on the island protested against the DPP authorities' blind purchase of US troops and called for strengthening cross-strait dialogue and sharing the dividends of peace. Any comment on this?","In order to seek political self-interest for \"Taiwan independence\", the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have resorted to militarism and \"prepared for war to seek independence.\" They have intensified their efforts to squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people. They are willing to serve as a \"cash machine\" for the US military-industrial complex. They do not hesitate to turn Taiwan into a \"powder keg\" and coerce the people to serve as \"Taiwan independence\" cannon fodder. They have pushed the majority of Taiwan compatriots into the danger of war. All walks of life in Taiwan have expressed strong dissatisfaction and firm opposition to this.\nThe future of Taiwan and the security, security, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots depend on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. We hope that the majority of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the extreme danger and harm of the DPP authorities' stubborn insistence on the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist line, resolutely oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, work with us to bring cross-Strait relations back to the right track of peaceful development, and effectively safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait as well as their own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260603_12769125.htm"],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently stated that the United States and China continue to \"fight without breaking up\" to strive for bargaining chips and space for strategic adjustment. Taiwan must continue to strengthen relations between Taiwan, the United States and Taiwan and Japan, and consolidate the trust of \"friends and alliances\". Any comment on this?","The relevant remarks exposed the DPP authorities' stubborn persistence in separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and their attempt to collude with external forces for \"independence\" provocations. \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and outsiders cannot be trusted. \"Relying on foreign countries to seek independence\" will only make Taiwan a \"chess piece\" of external forces, and it will inevitably become an \"abandoned piece\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","U.S. President Trump has said that arms sales to Taiwan are an important bargaining chip in the hands of the United States. U.S. Secretary of State Rubio recently stated that the U.S. policy toward Taiwan has not changed and that the current US$14 billion in arms sales to Taiwan are still under review. Any comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and China's Taiwan region. \"Taiwan independence by force\" is a dead end. It cannot change the inevitable defeat of \"Taiwan independence\" and cannot stop the general trend of the motherland's unification. We urge the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiques, handle the Taiwan issue prudently, and stop sending wrong signals to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","In recent years, the mainland has vigorously supported Fujian in building a cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone, but Lai Qingde recently said that the mainland's \"united front penetration\" into Taiwan has five major aspects, including opening an \"integrated development demonstration zone\" to conduct united front work for Taiwanese businessmen and Taiwanese young people. He also said that he has…","We support Fujian in exploring new paths for cross-Strait integrated development and building cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zones in order to deepen cross-Strait integrated development in various fields, allow Taiwan compatriots to share development opportunities on the mainland, and enhance the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. This is a real move to benefit the majority of Taiwan compatriots.\n\"Central Committee of the Communist Party of China\" Since the State Council’s Opinions on Supporting Fujian in Exploring New Roads for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zones” was released in 2023, relevant departments and Fujian Province have issued a series of supporting documents and policy measures, and Fujian Province has also formulated and issued policies to promote Regulations on common standards across the Taiwan Strait have been introduced. Xiamen City has issued several regulations for the direct recognition of professional qualifications in Taiwan. For three consecutive years, Fuzhou City has issued three batches of 30 pilot policies to create a \"city living circle\" in Fuma, taking concrete actions to support the development of Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese companies in Fujian. The number of Taiwan compatriots visiting Fujian will increase from 573,000 in 2023 to 1.042 million in 2025. The number of newly established Taiwanese companies in Fujian will increase from 2,117 in 2023 to 2,612 in 2025. The popularity of exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan continues to rise, and exchanges and cooperation will become closer. It is the general trend and the people's will for compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to get closer.\nOut of one-party political self-interest and ignoring the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises, the Lai Ching-te administration has slandered and smeared the construction of the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone in every possible way, and even attempted to create a chilling effect and restrict cross-Strait exchanges through so-called \"amendments to the law.\" This is reversing the course of history. Its bad behavior deprives Taiwan compatriots of their right to pursue a better life and seriously damages the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots. It is unpopular and will inevitably fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question, regarding the so-called \"maritime delimitation negotiations\" launched by Japan and the Philippines involving the waters east of Taiwan, does the mainland know about the progress of the negotiations between Japan and the Philippines? If negotiations advance in the future, will the mainland carry out regular law enforcement patrols or take other actions near Taiwan's eastern waters? Taiwan's foreign…","The first question. The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of China's Taiwan Island. Their so-called \"delimitation negotiations\" seriously infringe on China's maritime rights and interests, seriously violate international law and basic norms of international relations, and are completely illegal and invalid.\nThe mainland coast guard department carries out law enforcement inspections in relevant sea areas in accordance with the law to maintain the order of maritime operations and protect the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, which is a normal performance of their duties. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the Chinese nation and should stand firm on their national stance, uphold national justice, jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation.\nSecond question. There is only one China in the world, and the mainland and Taiwan belong to the same China. This is the true status quo of the Taiwan issue. Although the two sides of the Taiwan Strait have not yet been completely reunified, China's sovereignty and territory have never been divided, and the fact that the mainland and Taiwan belong to the same China has never changed. No matter how the international situation and the situation across the Taiwan Strait change, the general trend of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation will not change, and the general trend of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits getting closer and coming together will not change.\nAchieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese people. It is the general trend, the great cause and the aspiration of the people. No one or any force can stop it. We firmly believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots will have a profound understanding that Taiwan's development future lies in a strong motherland and that the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots depend on the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We have full confidence in uniting our Taiwan compatriots to jointly open up new prospects for cross-Strait relations and create a bright future of national rejuvenation and motherland reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-03","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","Garbage was thrown at a comedy club in Taipei during a recent rehearsal. The police arrested two suspects. The outside world is concerned about whether this is related to the stand-up comedians who have ridiculed the mainland, but the suspects have denied it. In addition, this year, paint was thrown at the studios of Taiwanese and Hong Kong residents and \"anti-extradition activists\", triggering discussions on…","I don't know the specific situation you mentioned. Two points need to be pointed out: First, \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end. People despise, spit on, and abandon it. This is an expression of public opinion. The so-called \"cross-border suppression\" is completely nonsense, a clumsy trick to divert attention, and a deliberate smear campaign with ulterior motives. Second, the main axis of cross-Strait exchanges is the sincere interaction based on \"one family on both sides of the Strait\", which is the aspiration of the people and the general trend. We deepen cross-Strait integrated development in order to promote mutual understanding and joint development between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nNow I will announce the status of the twelfth Taiwan-related knowledge prize-winning Q&A event.\nOn May 11, the WeChat public account of the \"Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council\" released the titles of the 12th \"Taiwan-related Questions and Answers\" activity, and netizens actively participated in answering the questions. As of June 1st, the top ten netizens with correct answers and the most likes were: \"Qingshan Luotuo\", \"Oreo\", \"Yiwei Crossing the Gorge\", \"Alishan Moon\", \"Spring\", \"Guiyan Zhidu\", \"Little Dot\", \"ASUS Choice\", \"Tide Frequency\", and \"Jeronimos Titon\". Congratulations to the above ten netizens, who will receive the exquisite shell carving \"Treasure Island of Taiwan\" designed by a national first-class technician and handmade by primary school students in Pingtan, Fujian.\nFrom June 2025 to May 2026, the \"Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council\" public account launched 12 consecutive Taiwan-related knowledge Q&A activities. Nearly 190,000 netizens from both sides of the Taiwan Strait actively participated in the interaction, and learned about the central government's policies on Taiwan and various aspects of improving the well-being of compatriots through Q&A. policy initiative, the 12,000 comments in the comment area were sincere, with the sentence \"More exchanges will bring reunion closer\", which expresses the deep friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits who have the same roots, culture and race, and expresses the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait's firm belief and deep expectation for the reunification of the motherland.\nWe hope that netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will pay more attention to Taiwan affairs, actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various fields, and contribute to promoting the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations and promoting the reunification process of the motherland.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260603_12769117.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-06-04","Mao Ning","AP","First, what was the reason China banned four New Zealand lawmakers from traveling for one year and demanded an apology after they traveled to Taiwan, if you can explain a little bit more? Secondly, intelligence agencies from the so-called Five-Eyes Alliance including the U.S. and the UK said that Chinese spies are using online job platforms to recruit people. What would you say about that?","On your first question, several individual New Zealand lawmakers visited China’s Taiwan region in disregard of the grave concern and firm opposition of the Chinese side. Their action violates the one-China principle and interferes in China’s internal affairs. In accordance with relevant laws of the People’s Republic of China, the Chinese side has decided to take measures including an entry ban.\nI need to stress that the one-China principle, a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations, is also the political cornerstone of China-New Zealand relations. We urge the individuals concerned to earnestly respect China’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and strictly abide by the one-China principle. Anyone who tramples on the red line and oversteps on the Taiwan question must pay the price.\nOn the second question, as the world’s largest intelligence cooperation network, the “Five Eyes” has long engaged in massive systemic espionage all over the world. It is ironic that such an organization is accusing China of “spy threat.”","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260604_11937670.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260604_11937631.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-04","Mao Ning","DPA","About the last question on New Zealand, some German lawmakers also visited Taiwan in May. Will China ban lawmakers from Germany and other countries that have visited Taiwan from entering China?","Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. Anyone who crosses the red line on the Taiwan question must pay the price.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260604_11937670.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260604_11937631.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-05","Mao Ning","CCTV","The city of Nagasaki reportedly plans to conclude work to update exhibition panels at the Nagasaki Atomic Bomb Museum by the end of this year. There have been reports that regarding the Nanjing Massacre, the wording on the explanatory panel “massacre” will no longer be used and will be changed to “the Nanjing Incident in which numerous civilians and prisoners were killed.” Can I have your comment on that?","There is abundant evidence for the Nanjing Massacre—a horrendous war crime of Japanese militarists that shall never be erased. The Tokyo Trials ruled in black and white that the wartime atrocities of the Japanese army in Nanjing were a “massacre”, not a mere “incident”. The Judgement of the International Military Tribunal for the Far East dedicated a special chapter to detail “the Rape of Nanking”. With numerous survivors’ testimonies, records of third-country witnesses and Japanese army files, the judgement, in the form of the ruling of international justice, made it very clear that the Japanese army who invaded China committed the heinous crime of the Nanjing Massacre. The Massacre’s chief perpetrator Iwane Matsui was sentenced to death by hanging as a class-A war criminal.\nThe verdict of history must not be overturned. I noted that many survivors of the atomic bombs in Japan, Nagasaki citizen groups and people with insights have called for fully and accurately depicting the crimes and history of Japanese militarists as victimizers. We urge the Japanese side to deeply reflect on its war crimes and make a clean break with militarism.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260605_11938443.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260605_11938293.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-09","Lin Jian","TV Asahi","According to reports, China Coast Guard vessels sailed in the “exclusive economic zone” near Yonaguni Island of the Okinawa Prefecture earlier this month. In response to Japan Coast Guard’s call, the Chinese side claimed that they were conducting routine patrol in areas under China’s jurisdiction. Can you confirm this?","China Coast Guard (CCG) has released information on the law enforcement patrols of the CCG vessel formation in waters east of China’s Taiwan island in accordance with the law. Let me reiterate that China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in this area. Japan and the Philippines bypassing China to initiate the so-called maritime delimitation talks constitutes a severe violation of UNCLOS and other international laws and basic norms governing international relations. It also seriously infringes on China’s maritime rights and interests. China will by no means accept this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260609_11940743.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260609_11940686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-09","Lin Jian","Yonhap News Agency","Taiwan’s “foreign ministry” said that on June 8, three ROK lawmakers met with Taiwan’s Deputy Foreign Minister. The two sides exchanged views on addressing geopolitical challenges and the development of the semiconductor and AI industries. What is your comment?","Taiwan is part of China. There is no such thing as “foreign ministry” of Taiwan. China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic relations with China. The 1992 joint communiqué on China-ROK diplomatic ties clearly stipulates that the ROK recognizes the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government representing China and respects China’s position that there is but one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. Since early this year, the ROK has publicly reiterated on multiple occasions that its commitment to the one-China principle remains unchanged. China has lodged serious representations with the ROK over the matter you mentioned. We urge the ROK side to bear in mind the bigger picture of our bilateral relationship, honor its commitments and earnestly adhere to the one-China principle. The ROK side should refrain from any form of official interactions with the Taiwan region, avoid being exploited by “Taiwan independence” separatists, send no wrong signals to them, and maintain the sound and steady growth of our bilateral ties with real actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260609_11940743.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260609_11940686.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-06-09","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Soon after Japan and the Philippines unilaterally announced initiating maritime delimitation negotiations on the waters east of China's Taiwan Island, the China Coast Guard was reportedly conducted law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters, and the Ministry of Transport later carried out a special law enforcement action on maritime traffic. What is your comment on this?","Regarding the announcement by Japan and the Philippines to bypass China and initiate the so-called \"maritime delimitation negotiations\" on the waters east of China's Taiwan Island, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated China's solemn position of firm opposition many times. We urge Japan and the Philippines to immediately stop their illegal rights-violating and provocative acts. If they choose to persist in their wrong course, they will only be hoisted by their own petard. The Chinese side will take resolute and effective measures to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16471276.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16466352.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-06-09","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It's reported that the head of Taiwan's defense department stated that although the U.S.defense secretary did not mention Taiwan in his keynote speech at the Shangri-LaDialogue, Taiwan would continue to strengthen its \"self-defense\" capabilities, maintain close military cooperation with America, and uphold its \"responsibility and capability to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait\".What is your…","\"Taiwan independence\" and cross-Strait peace are as irreconcilable as fire and water, and safeguarding peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait serves as the greatest common denominator between China and America. Recent statements made by the the U.S. side regarding Taiwan show that America now better understands and attaches greater importance to China's position and concerns on the Taiwan question. There is growing evidence that the prevailing trend of China's reunification is unstoppable. Any plot to \"seek independence by relying on foreign support\" or \"seek independence by force\" is doomed to failure. Those forces that stubbornly cling to their wrong course and move against the historical trend will eventually be overwhelmed by the torrent of history.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16471276.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16466352.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on June 10, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Please ask questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","新华社记者","The 18th Straits Forum is about to be held. Please introduce the relevant preparation progress. Which Taiwanese guests will attend this Straits Forum?","The 18th Straits Forum Conference will be held in Xiamen on June 13. Vice Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang Zhang Ronggong and other representatives from all walks of life in Taiwan will attend the conference. At present, all preparatory work for the forum is basically in place. A series of forum activities have been carried out in various parts of Fujian. Four events have been held, including the Taiwan Talents Xiamen Matchmaking Conference, the Straits People Forum, the Cross-Strait Dragon Boat Races, and the Common Home Forum, with nearly a thousand Taiwanese compatriots actively participating.\nThis forum continues to pay attention to and serve grassroots and youth groups, so that the results of cross-strait integrated development can benefit more compatriots on both sides of the strait. The activities cover diverse fields such as grassroots governance, marriage and family, social welfare, sports events, folk beliefs, singing and dancing arts, financial technology, rural revitalization, agricultural and fishery cooperation, new media creation, etc., innovatively promote the docking of education, e-commerce, biomedicine and small and medium-sized enterprises across the Taiwan Strait, protect the growth of young children, and help Taiwanese youth expand employment and entrepreneurship tracks. We warmly welcome compatriots from all walks of life in Taiwan to gather across the sea to rekindle friendship, share opportunities, seek common development and create a better future.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770186.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","The 18th Straits Forum will be held soon. The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said that \"the Straits Forum is a united front platform for mainland China\" and further expanded restrictions this year, requiring county, city and public officials not to attend relevant activities. Public opinion on the island believes that banning communication based on a single official document makes people feel very threatened.…","The Straits Forum is a cross-Strait non-governmental exchange platform that adheres to the principle of \"non-governmental, grassroots and extensive\". It has played an important and positive role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various fields and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots. It is generally welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nOut of its stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" stance, the DPP authorities ignore the will of the people and local development needs, and have neither the will nor the ability to properly handle cross-strait relations. For its own political self-interest, it smeared and slandered the Straits Forum, undermined cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, restricted the movement and freedom of speech of the Taiwanese people, and seriously harmed the interests and well-being of compatriots on the island. What he did fully exposed his \"fake democracy, true dictatorship\" nature. What I want to emphasize is that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and no force can stop the trend of getting closer and coming together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770185.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has explained five of the \"seven better things\" for Taiwan after peaceful reunification at previous press conferences, which has attracted great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's explanation for \"After peaceful reunification, with the backing of a strong motherland, Taiwan's security will…","After peaceful reunification, with the backing of a strong motherland, the people of Taiwan will be safer. The risk of war brought about by \"Taiwan independence\" will be eliminated from its roots. The Taiwanese people will no longer be used as \"cannon fodder\" by \"Taiwan independence\". The people's hard-earned money will no longer be squandered to purchase arms, and ammunition will not be hoarded in private houses and temples. The black hands of external forces interfering in the internal affairs of the Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will be completely cut off. Taiwan will no longer be a \"chess piece\" of external forces. It will no longer be the \"powder keg\", \"mine island\" and \"hell scene\" that the DPP authorities colluded with external forces to create. It will escape the fate of being ruined by \"Taiwan independence\" and external forces at any time. Taiwan's economy will develop sustainably and stably, and its industrial and supply chains will be more autonomous, controllable, safe and reliable, achieving a healthy combination of high-quality development and high-level security. The legitimate rights and interests of Taiwanese fishermen operating in the waters surrounding Taiwan Island will be promptly and effectively protected by national maritime forces.\nAfter peaceful reunification, Taiwan will become an island of peace, security and prosperity, guarded by all the sons and daughters of the Chinese nation. Taiwan compatriots can truly live a good life of peace and contentment in a peaceful and tranquil environment, and fully enjoy the peaceful years of the reunification of the motherland and the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770184.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","人民政协报记者","A recent poll by Taiwan's \"Democratic Culture and Education Foundation\" showed that nearly 60% of Taiwanese people support proactive peace negotiations with the mainland, and nearly 70% of Taiwanese people believe that cross-strait relations should be improved and peace should be strived for. Some public opinion on the island believes that when the cross-strait issue shifts from reunification and \"independence\"…","The mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society, which wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, cannot be suppressed. Relevant polls have once again proved that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese and one family. They all look forward to peace and tranquility across the Taiwan Strait, the improvement and development of cross-Strait relations, and a better life.\nThe future of the motherland and the nation rests on its young people. More and more Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, realize that Taiwan's development and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots depend on the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, the reunification of the motherland, and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We welcome and support more young people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait to visit each other frequently, enhance understanding, and work together to keep the future of cross-Strait relations firmly in the hands of the Chinese people themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770183.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan's public opinion representative Gao Jin Sumei and his assistant were prosecuted by the Taipei District Prosecutor's Office for corruption and other crimes. They were sentenced to 12 years and 6 months in prison and 16 years in prison respectively. Some public opinion on the island believes that this is the Democratic Progressive Party authorities choosing specific candidates to deal with, and the…","The DPP authorities have used judicial means to crack down on and persecute political dissidents and engage in \"green terror\", which has aroused strong dissatisfaction among the people on the island. The DPP authorities act arbitrarily and recklessly, and their perverse actions will inevitably be counterattacked by public opinion, and they will eventually suffer the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","中新社记者","A recent survey by Taiwan's \"Tianxia\" magazine pointed out that Taiwan's AI-related industries are growing rapidly, but a large number of traditional industries are becoming marginalized. Some public opinion believes that one of the important reasons for Taiwan's traditional industries to maintain competitiveness in the past was the cross-strait division of labor; if traditional industries want to save…","At present, Taiwan's industry can be described as \"one industry thrives while all industries decline.\" The problem of an overly single industrial structure has become increasingly obvious, and the vulnerability of economic development has become more prominent. Traditional industries are in a difficult situation and their development space is shrinking. The income of most residents is far less than the median, and their unpaid leave is getting longer and longer. The people on the island are strongly dissatisfied with this. The DPP authorities not only fail to face up to the outstanding problems and serious hidden dangers of the island's industry and find a way out for the industry, but instead repeatedly promote the \"decoupling and breaking of links\" between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait and obstruct the division of labor and cooperation between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nMainland China's \"15th Five-Year Plan\" outline proposes \"building a modern industrial system\" and \"optimizing and upgrading traditional industries.\" Traditional industries are highly related to the development of people's livelihood. With the strong support of the industrial chain, supply chain and market, innovative development can be achieved through intelligence, greenness and integration. We will, as always, actively support cross-Strait industrial cooperation and support Taiwanese enterprises, including those in traditional industries, to give full play to their own advantages, seize the development opportunities of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\", and achieve better and greater development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770181.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","上海东方卫视记者","According to the 2024 Shanghai-Taipei Urban Forum cooperation memorandum between the two parties, two red pandas from the Shanghai Zoo were exchanged with black-footed penguins from the Taipei Zoo. On June 5 this year, a red panda handover ceremony was held at the Shanghai Zoo, which attracted attention and praise from netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Some DPP politicians claimed that the Twin Cities…","As an important institutionalized exchange platform between the two cities, the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has played a positive role in promoting exchanges and cooperation between the two places in various fields. We have also noticed the enthusiastic comments from netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, such as \"Cute animals serve as bridges across the sea, and warmth rides the wind across the strait\" and \"Using animal conservation as an exchange, there is no confrontation, only warmth. The more such activities, the better.\" More movement and more exchanges are the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We will continue to support exchanges and cooperation in various fields including cross-strait city exchanges, continue to enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and promote the spiritual harmony of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe \"Taiwan independence\" forces frequently use the so-called \"infiltration gap\" to discredit cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. This time they are making a political fuss about the red panda, which is ridiculous.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","In response to Japan and the Philippines announcing the launch of the so-called \"maritime delimitation negotiations,\" the mainland emphasized the one-China principle and that both sides of the Taiwan Strait should jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities falsely claimed that \"the two sides of the Taiwan Strait are not subordinate to each other,…","The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of Taiwan Island. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the above-mentioned waters. Japan and the Philippines launched the so-called \"delimitation negotiations\" without authorization, bypassing China, seriously infringing on China's maritime rights and interests, seriously violating international law and basic norms of international relations, and is completely illegal and invalid.\nThe DPP authorities have kowtowed to cater to external forces and have become complete national scum. Faced with the unanimous condemnation of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the DPP authorities changed their face again and spread the fallacy of \"Taiwan independence\" in an attempt to shift the focus and deceive the people. I am telling the DPP authorities that anyone who forgets their ancestors and betrays the nation will be nailed to the pillar of shame in history without exception.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770179.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said in an exclusive interview that he \"resisted China's pressure\" and made a \"surprise visit\" to Swaziland. He also said that Taiwanese people are unwilling to accept \"Chinese rule\" and hope to continue to live a life of \"freedom, democracy, and human rights.\" Any comment on this?","Lai Ching-te squandered the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people, engaged in \"gold-dollar diplomacy\", and spent huge sums of money to buy \"smuggling\" people. He became the laughing stock of the international community and the island. However, he was not ashamed but proud of it, which fully exposed his \"Taiwan independence\" nature and paranoid despicability.\nThe DPP authorities have been shouting \"freedom\" on the island, but they have long controlled the media, supported cyber troops, suppressed public opinion, and obstructed and restricted cross-strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in various fields; they flaunted \"democracy\" but engaged in \"green terror\", abused justice, and Administrative and other means are used to suppress and persecute political dissidents, and they continue to manipulate and provoke political fights; they talk about \"human rights\" but ignore the interests and well-being of the people on the island. They repeatedly discriminate and make things difficult for mainland-based groups, and label and slap relevant people on the island, which has completely lost people's hearts.\nDifferent social systems are not an excuse for separatism. As long as we agree on the one-China principle, promote the reunification of the motherland, speak things out well, and discuss matters easily, there will be no conflicts and differences that cannot be resolved. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will have a correct understanding of the mainland's social system and development path, see clearly the true face and sinister intentions of the DPP authorities seeking \"independence\" under the guise of \"democracy\", draw a clear line with the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces and their activities, and work with us to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770182.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities said that on June 5, a mainland coast guard ship entered the \"restricted waters\" of the Dongsha Islands, and a confrontation broke out between the ships of the two sides. Any comment on this?","China has sovereignty over the South China Sea Islands, including the Dongsha Islands and their adjacent waters, and it is normal for the mainland coast guard to perform law enforcement and inspections in relevant waters. If the DPP authorities dare to make provocations, they must bear all the consequences.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260610_12770180.htm"],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, Su Jiaquan, chairman of the Straits Exchange Foundation, said that mainland China's selective \"reading\" and \"returning\" without institutional regulations can easily damage the protection of the rights of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Any comment on this?","As we all know, because the DPP authorities refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle, the cross-strait communication mechanism between the two conferences has been suspended. What really damages the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait is the DPP authorities' stubborn insistence on the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","Recently, the United States stated that it would impose an additional 10% tariff on goods from 14 economies, including Taiwan, after investigating so-called \"forced labor practices.\" The Democratic Progressive Party authorities claim that Taiwan has achieved good results in terms of industry and tariffs. Any comment on this?","Regarding the U.S.'s imposition of additional tariffs, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not only did not dare to express protest, but instead boasted about the so-called \"good results\". This is really flattering and shameless.\nFacts have repeatedly proved that Taiwan's future lies in national reunification and the well-being of Taiwan compatriots depends on national rejuvenation. There is no way out for the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) authorities in their attempt to \"rely on foreign countries to seek independence\". They try to please outsiders by sacrificing Taiwan's industrial foundation and people's livelihood. This is a miscalculation that will inevitably lead to backlash.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Recently, with the advent of summer and high temperatures, people on the island have increased their electricity consumption for air conditioners, freezers, etc. However, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have raised electricity prices for people's livelihood, which is the most expensive in history. Many stores complained that the average monthly electricity bill increased by more than 30%. People…","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities often falsely claim that \"power supply is safe,\" but the fact is that Taiwanese people have already endured too many power outages and power rations. Now that electricity prices have hit a new high in summer, not only stores are suffering, but the interests of many employees and consumers are also being harmed. This once again proves that the DPP authorities are bent on seeking \"independence\" and are indifferent to people's livelihood, disregarding people's livelihood, and harming people's interests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, relevant agencies in Kinmen County and Xiamen City made an appointment to simultaneously release a total of 5.61 million fish and shellfish in the waters of Xiamen and Jinmen, demonstrating the loving kindness of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to protect marine resources. However, because the Democratic Progressive Party authorities require Taiwanese ships not to approach mainland ships,…","Xiamen and Jinjiang are separated by a strip of water. The two places work together to release and conserve marine fishery resources. This is a good thing that benefits the people's livelihood in both places and is a good story of the people-to-people ties on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities have artificially set up restrictions, imposed arbitrary obstructions, and used political barriers to harm the friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits, exposing their true nature of being anti-peace, anti-exchange, seeking division, and engaging in confrontation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Quanzhou, Fujian Province held an event to commemorate the 20th anniversary of the opening of the Quanjin “Small Three Links” passenger route. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On June 8, a commemorative event for the 20th anniversary of the opening of the Quanjin \"Mini Three Links\" passenger route was held at the Quanjin Passenger Terminal in Shijing Town, Nan'an, Quanzhou. More than 100 compatriots from both sides of the Taiwan Strait attended. With the theme of \"Twenty Years of Quanjin Passenger Transport Route and Setting Sail to Start a New Journey\", the event reviewed the process of the Quanjin Passenger Transport Route from its opening to vigorous development, and vividly explained the role and significance of the \"golden channel\" of this strait. Not only were the participants, promoters, and witnesses of the route telling warm stories and development changes since the launch of the route with their personal experiences, but there were also food tastings, calligraphy exchanges, Nanyin performances, cross-strait home book exhibitions, and handicraft experiences between Quanjin and Quanzhou. It is worth mentioning that the event officially launched the selection of dishes for the Kinmen Wuzhou Banquet. It is a special food selection activity carried out by the mainland for Kinmen, using food as a link to bring the food culture of the two sides closer together.\nThe \"Little Three Links\" passenger route is one of the most important and convenient channels for people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait to communicate with each other, especially those from Fujian and Taiwan. Since the Quanjin \"Small Three Links\" passenger route was put into operation on June 8, 2006, it has safely and stably transported more than 1.6 million passengers. Relying on the advantages of short-distance shipping, the route uses low-cost and short-distance maritime connectivity to continuously bring the hearts of the people of Quanjin closer. People on both sides of the Taiwan Strait use the Quanjin route to visit relatives and friends, trace their roots and ancestors, find jobs and start businesses, and travel and exchange. They are getting closer and closer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities.","Cross-Strait exchange activities continue to be lively and exciting. Let me introduce several recent activities.\nFrom June 2 to 3, the 13th Cross-Strait (Nanjing) New Display Industry Matchmaking Conference was held in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province. More than 400 cross-strait entrepreneurs, industry experts, representatives of universities and research institutes conducted exchanges and discussions around the theme of \"Display to Intelligence, AI to Innovation, and Industry to Integration\".\nFrom June 11 to 15, the Putian-Taiwan youth cultural exchange event \"Youth Together, Youth Go Together\" will be held in Putian, Fujian. Young people from Putian and Taiwan will gather in Mazu's hometown to experience Mazu's belief culture. During the same period, Putian will also hold Putian-Taiwan fishery breeding exchange activities. Fisheries colleagues in Putian and Taiwan will exchange breeding experiences and sign cooperation agreements to jointly promote the common advancement of fishery technology, resource sharing, industrial prosperity, and market expansion.\nOn June 14, the 2026 \"Meet Zhuhai, Meet Youth\" cross-strait youth dragon boat culture and \"Village BA\" basketball friendly match exchange event will be held in Zhuhai. Youth from both sides of the strait will watch the dragon boat race, taste intangible cultural heritage delicacies, make rice dumplings together, and experience the charm of Lingnan folk customs and the heritage of Chinese culture.\nOn June 16, the second cross-strait folk culture and sports event - Maoming Xian Fu Folk Culture Exchange was held in Maoming, Guangdong. The event was themed \"Continuing Intangible Cultural Heritage and Inheriting the Spirit of Xian Yi\" and focused on the \"good-hearted spirit\" of safeguarding the reunification of the motherland and national unity. Nearly 500 Taiwanese compatriots participated in the exchange activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","It is understood that the 3rd Shaanxi-Taiwan Culture Week and Cross-Strait Youth Han and Tang Culture Summer Camp will be held in Shaanxi. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From June to October, \"Meet in Chang'an, Walk with Youth\" - the 3rd Shaanxi-Taiwan Culture Week and the Han and Tang Culture Summer Camp for Cross-Strait Youth will be held in Xi'an, Shaanxi and other places. More than 40 sub-activities will be held. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait will conduct interactive exchanges in more than 10 fields such as culture, science and technology, and education.\nShaanxi is an important birthplace of Chinese civilization and carries the important spiritual code of Chinese civilization. Xi'an is one of the four ancient capitals in my country. As the summer vacation is approaching, Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, are welcome to visit the land of Sanqin, explore the beginning of Chinese civilization in front of the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum, experience the splendid brilliance of Eastern culture in the Terracotta Warriors and Horses Pit, and gaze at the gold inscriptions on the Duhu Talisman at the Shaanxi History Museum. Look up at the Big Wild Goose Pagoda and reminisce about Xuanzang's perseverance in his journey to the west; take a night tour in the Evernight City of the Tang Dynasty and feel the bright lights of Chang'an Night; climb to the top of Huashan Mountain and visit the \"Sword Discourse Platform\" written by Jin Yong; visit the Hukou Falls in person to witness the majestic power of the Yellow River.\nIn Shaanxi, in addition to experiencing the rich history and culture and beautiful natural scenery, you can also go to a feast in the \"Carbohydrate Capital\", eat a bowl of biangbiang noodles, eat a bite of meat buns, taste various snacks such as gourd heads, golden thread oil towers, squid and fish, and experience the infinite charm of the Qin and Han Dynasties and the grand scenery of the Tang Dynasty through the delicious food on the tip of your tongue.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","The \"Fujian Super League\" football league has launched a series of special activities against Taiwan. The Mainland Affairs Council said that in recent years, the mainland has used various sports exchange activities as a package to strengthen the attraction of Taiwanese sports talents and united front propaganda. Taiwanese people who go to the mainland to engage in sports exchanges \"should not accept any…","Fujian and Taiwan are geographically close, related by blood, and culturally related. It is natural for people from Fujian and Taiwan to have close exchanges. Compatriots from Taiwan go to the mainland to participate in football leagues and other sports exchange activities, which will help compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait enhance understanding and achieve harmony and progress together. The DPP authorities have made irresponsible remarks and slandered the non-governmental events and exchange activities loved by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, which only proves that they are afraid of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait getting closer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","Taiwanese media reported that the island’s travel industry associations have recently stated that there is a clear demand for tourism to the mainland on the island, calling on the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to lift the “ban on group travel” and the so-called “orange alert” to mainland China, so that the people and industry can work together to improve the tourism market. Do you have any comments on…","Relevant reports fully reflect the strong desire of the island's industry to resume cross-strait tourism exchanges, and indicate that the restrictive measures such as the \"ban on group travel\" to mainland China implemented by the DPP authorities are unpopular.\nAccording to statistics, there will be as many as 4.89 million Taiwanese residents coming to the mainland in 2025. Out of self-interest for \"independence\" politics, the DPP authorities turned a deaf ear to the calls of the island's industry and people. This not only harmed the livelihoods of Taiwan's tourism industry, but also deprived Taiwanese youth of the opportunity to understand the true face of the mainland.\nWe have always upheld the concept of one family on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, promoted the resumption of travel for mainland residents to Taiwan and continued to express goodwill. Since 2024, we have resumed travel to Kinmen and Matsu for residents of Fujian and Shanghai. It is hoped that the DPP authorities will face up to public opinion, remove political barriers, and create favorable conditions for the normalization of cross-strait personnel exchanges and tourism exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Regarding the recent special maritime traffic law enforcement operations carried out by the mainland in the waters east of Taiwan, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council stated that the mainland’s official ships have affected foreign merchant ships in this area. “This violates international law and international conventions and undermines regional peace and stability.” Any comment on this? Does the mainland have a…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of Taiwan Island. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the above-mentioned waters. Japan and the Philippines launched the so-called \"delimitation negotiations\" without authorization, bypassing China, seriously infringing on China's maritime rights and interests, seriously violating international law and basic norms of international relations, and is completely illegal and invalid.\nThe Chinese Coast Guard carries out law enforcement patrols in the waters east of Taiwan Island in accordance with the law. This is a necessary action taken against Japan and the Philippines for seriously infringing on China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. It will continue to strengthen the control of relevant waters. The DPP authorities confuse right and wrong and confuse right and wrong, which cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China.\nThe relevant mainland departments carry out law enforcement inspections in relevant sea areas in accordance with the law, which is a just move to safeguard the country's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and is conducive to ensuring the safety of Taiwan's fishermen's lives and property. The DPP authorities are distorting facts and maliciously hyping up the situation in an attempt to provoke cross-strait confrontation and \"rely on external forces to seek independence.\" They will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","台湾《旺报》记者","Recently, some Taiwanese people have reported that when participating in cross-strait exchange activities or related communities, they encountered criminals using false identities to commit emotional or investment fraud, which has affected the trust in cross-strait people-to-people exchanges. Does the mainland know the relevant situation? What specific measures will be taken in the future to combat this kind of…","I don't know the specific situation you are talking about. Fraud is a crime deeply abhorred by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and it is also a target that mainland judicial authorities crack down on in accordance with the law. If Taiwan compatriots encounter illegal abuse in the mainland, please report it to the public security organs in time. The relevant departments will do their best to protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","First question, it is reported that Li Yanhe, editor-in-chief of Taiwan's \"Eight Banners Culture\", has been released from prison, but cannot leave the country due to an additional one-year sentence. Please explain the situation. Second question: On the 6th, the Ministry of Transport of China announced a special maritime traffic law enforcement operation in the eastern waters of Taiwan. The Democratic Progressive…","The first question. Regarding Li Yanhe's case, the relevant departments have always handled it in accordance with the law and at the same time protected the legitimate rights and interests of the parties concerned in accordance with the law.\nSecond question. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. There is no so-called \"sovereignty\". Relevant mainland departments carry out law enforcement inspections in relevant sea areas in accordance with the law, which is a just act to safeguard national sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.\nI have noticed that many Taiwanese people and netizens are applauding the decisiveness and toughness of the mainland. They praise the relevant actions as supporting Taiwanese fishermen. At the same time, they express strong dissatisfaction and opposition to the DPP authorities' self-indulgence and groveling.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","First question, the Taiwan Strait Foundation said on the 5th that Taiwanese Taoist priests have been detained in the mainland in the past two weeks. Can you explain the specific reasons? Second question, Shen Boyang, the Taipei mayoral candidate of the Democratic Progressive Party, said in an interview that \"the Twin Cities Forum has not been beneficial so far.\" He also said that he does not exclude exchanges on…","The first question. We have always encouraged and supported cross-Strait exchanges in all fields and protected the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots do not have to have any concerns when traveling to the mainland. Out of political self-interest, the DPP authorities maliciously hyped, smeared and spread rumors, and attacked the mainland in an attempt to create a \"chilling effect\", obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. This is unpopular and will not succeed.\nThe second question is that the Shanghai-Taipei City Forum, as an important institutionalized exchange platform between Shanghai and Taipei, has played a positive role in promoting exchanges and cooperation between the two cities in various fields, and the results are obvious to all. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are Chinese and one family. They should visit each other frequently and become closer as we go more and more. We treat all Taiwan compatriots equally and welcome them as long as they are willing to participate in cross-strait exchanges and cooperation and do not engage in separatist activities.\nShen Boyang is a die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" person on the list, a black sheep who undermines exchanges, family ties and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. He constantly promotes separatist ideas, harbors the evil intentions of \"Taiwan independence\", exaggerates his own self-esteem and grandstands, and is not worthy of comment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-10","Zhang Han","台湾东森新闻记者","Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council has explicitly banned local government personnel from participating in this year’s Straits Forum. Taitung County Magistrate Rao Qingling’s application to go to the mainland was also rejected. What do you think of this?","The Straits Forum is a cross-Strait non-governmental exchange platform that adheres to the principle of \"non-governmental, grassroots and extensive\". It has played an important and positive role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in various fields and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots. It is generally welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nOut of its stubborn \"Taiwan independence\" stance, the DPP authorities ignore the will of the people and local development needs, and have neither the will nor the ability to properly handle cross-strait relations. For its own political self-interest, it smeared and slandered the Straits Forum, undermined cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, restricted the movement and freedom of speech of the Taiwanese people, and seriously harmed the interests and well-being of compatriots on the island. What he did fully exposed the essence of \"fake democracy and true dictatorship\". Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and no force can stop the trend of getting closer and coming together.\nWe are willing to work with all political parties, organizations, counties, cities and people from all walks of life in Taiwan to jointly oppose the DPP authorities' provocations and disruptions in pursuit of \"independence\" on the political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\", and promote cross-strait exchanges, cooperation and personnel exchanges in all fields to benefit compatriots on both sides.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260610_12770189.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-06-16","Lin Jian","Xinhua News Agency","Foreign Minister Wang Yi just concluded his visit to Mongolia. Can you share more details?","At the invitation of Minister of Foreign Affairs of Mongolia Battsetseg Batmunkh, Foreign Minister Wang Yi visited Mongolia from June 13 to 15. During the visit, Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Mongolian President Khurelsukh Ukhnaa and Prime Minister Uchral Nyam-Osor respectively, held large and small group talks with Foreign Minister Battsetseg Batmunkh, and issued a joint press communiqué. Foreign Minister Wang Yi also, together with senior Mongolian officials, attended the water-flow commissioning ceremony of the Ulaanbaatar Central Wastewater Treatment Plant, a project funded under China’s preferential buyer’s credit.\nBoth sides agree that, connected by mountains and rivers and with a shared future, China and Mongolia are natural neighbors and comprehensive strategic partners. Both sides always respect each other’s independence, sovereignty, and territorial integrity, and any attempts by third countries to utilize the territory to harm the other’s sovereignty and security will not be allowed. These are the important safeguards of the sound development of China-Mongolia relations. Both sides agree, under the important common understandings between the two heads of state, to strengthen strategic mutual trust, deepen practical cooperation, foster people-to-people connectivity, and make continuous efforts to jointly build a bilateral community with a shared future characterized by peaceful coexistence, mutual assistance, and win-win cooperation.\nThe Mongolian side said that developing friendly relations with China is a top priority of Mongolia’s foreign policy, and Mongolia will not do anything that harms China’s interests, regardless of its relations with other countries. It emphasized that the Mongolian side understands and respects China’s positions and concerns, and is firmly committed to the one-China principle. It regards Taiwan as an inalienable part of China’s territory, does not support any form of “Taiwan independence” activity, and supports China’s national reunification. The Mongolian side reiterated its support on the vision of building a community with a shared future for humanity and the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative, the Global Civilization Initiative and the Global Governance Initiative.\nForeign Minister Wang Yi stated that China’s policy toward Mongolia remains consistent and stable, and that China has always placed the development of its relations with Mongolia in an important position in its neighborhood diplomacy. China has both the will and the capability to be a neighbor that Mongolia can rely on, a trustworthy friend, and a partner for accelerated development. China supports Mongolia in developing its economy and improving people’s livelihoods, and stands ready to strengthen the synergy of development strategies with Mongolia, pursue high‑quality Belt and Road cooperation and follow modernization paths suited to our respective national conditions.\nBoth sides have issued a joint press communiqué of the foreign ministers’ talks and established that the important common understandings between the two heads of state shall serve as the guidance for advancing China-Mongolia comprehensive strategic partnership. The two sides should respect each other’s independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity, and not interfere in each other’s internal affairs. Any attempts by third countries to utilize the territory to harm the other’s sovereignty and security should not be allowed. The Mongolian side reiterated that as its natural neighbor, China is a top priority of Mongolia’s foreign policy. It opposes “Taiwan independence” and believes that Xizang-related issues are China’s internal affairs. Both sides condemn fascism and militarism in any form and do not support any attempt to revive them.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260616_11946864.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260616_11946785.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-06-16","Chen Xi","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Japan and the Philippines unilaterally announced the launch of \"maritime boundary delimitation negotiations\" in waters east of Taiwan Island, China Coast Guard vessels carried out law enforcement operations in the relevant waters, and Taiwan's defense authorities called this a \"provocative act\" and \"cognitive warfare.\" What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the sea east of Taiwan island, and China Coast Guard law enforcement patrol operations are justified, necessary, and not to be disturbed. Both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and jointly defending national sovereignty and maritime rights and interests is an inescapable responsibility of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities not only respond passively, but also reverse right and wrong and act perversely. They have abandoned their national standpoint, and such conduct of forgetting one's roots and ancestors is despicable.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16467725.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-06-17","Lin Jian","Global Times","It is reported that regarding the case in which Kodai Murata, a sitting officer of Japan’s Self-Defense Forces, illegally entered the Chinese embassy in Japan with a knife, the Tokyo District Public Prosecutors Office has decided to prolong his detention period for psychiatric assessment to determine whether he is criminally responsible for his actions. What is your comment?","Nearly three months have passed since Kodai Murata, a sitting officer of Japan’s Self-Defense Forces, illegally broke into the Chinese Embassy in Japan armed with a knife. The Japanese side’s investigation and handling of the case have been proceeding slowly, while vicious incidents threatening the security of Chinese diplomatic missions in Japan continue to occur. China deplores this and has lodged protests against the Japanese side on many occasions.\nThe incident again reveals multiple deep-seated issues in Japan: the worsening right-wing impact and the suppression of objective and rational voices, the toxicity of the Japanese government’s erroneous policies on vital issues concerning China-Japan relations such as history and Taiwan, the serious lack of education on true history, the pervasive erroneous historical views, the ongoing push for a more offensive and expansionist defense policy and failure in supervising the SDF and maintaining discipline inside the forces. We notice that, for some time, many people with insight in Japan have asked the Japanese government to make an apology to China. Some have urged the government to reflect on itself and take corrective actions concerning the supervision of SDF, the education on history, and Japan’s policy towards China so as to fundamentally address the issue and remove its breeding ground in the Japanese society. We once again urge the Japanese side to do serious soul-searching, correct its wrongdoings, conduct a thorough probe and take full responsibility for the incident.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260617_11947701.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260617_11947482.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on June 17, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Dear journalists, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Please ask questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The 18th Straits Forum has attracted public attention from both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Could the speaker introduce the results of this Straits Forum?","The 18th Straits Forum was held in Xiamen on the morning of June 13. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended the forum and delivered a speech. Before the conference, he met with Taiwanese guests and representatives attending the forum. This forum adheres to the positioning of \"non-governmental, grassroots and extensive\", continues the theme of \"expanding non-governmental exchanges and deepening integrated development\", and organizes a series of colorful grassroots, youth, cultural and economic exchange activities. So far, more than 30 activities have been held, and more than 6,000 Taiwanese compatriots, especially \"Shou Lai\" and Taiwanese youth, have participated enthusiastically without fear of interference from the DPP authorities. This fully proves that the general trend of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits getting closer and coming together will not change. The DPP authorities’ interference and sabotage are unpopular and will not succeed.\nThis forum insists on improving people's livelihood and well-being through exchanges and integration, and promotes the release, signing, and implementation of a series of policies, measures, cooperation projects, and phased progress during the forum, visually demonstrating the solid results of the \"small four links\" and the bright prospects of the \"new four links\", and comprehensively showing the actual construction of Fujian as the first home for Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese companies. A signing meeting for the docking of ten policies and measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation was held on June 13. A number of intention purchase agreements were signed in the agricultural and fishery industries on both sides of the Strait. Fujian Province implemented five measures to deepen cross-Strait film and television cultural exchanges, took the lead in introducing Taiwanese TV series to be broadcast on satellite TV during prime time, and established a cross-Strait audio-visual copyright exchange center. The Straits Financial Forum and the Taiwan Enterprise Development Forum released the mainland banking industry’s first group standard for financial services to Taiwan. The Cross-Strait Maritime Cultural Exchange Event released 5 work measures to promote the high-quality development of cross-Strait shipping. The Straits Science and Technology Expert Forum facilitated the signing of 6 cross-Strait science and technology exchange and cooperation projects, providing more development opportunities and convenience for Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises to participate in Chinese-style modernization.\nThis forum effectively promotes exchanges and integration between young people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The Straits Youth Forum has established a cross-Strait youth association cooperation mechanism, released 23 cross-Strait association cooperation projects, and 19 groups of cross-Strait youth associations have united to co-build and sign cooperation contracts. The Straits Women's Forum helped pair up 10 families of the same origin. Dozens of Taiwanese young people took to the podium at the forum and a series of events to share their experiences of crossing the Taiwan Strait, finding their roots, and integrating into the life and development of the mainland. More than 100 college students from both sides of the Taiwan Strait formed a co-creation team to hold a short play competition, using the lens to tell vivid stories of Fujian and Taiwan sharing the same roots and helping each other. In his performance at the forum, young mainland actor Zhang Linghe expressed his sincere hope that more Taiwanese compatriots would cross the Taiwan Strait and come to the mainland for a visit. His sentence \"The distance across the Taiwan Strait cannot stop our compatriots from getting closer and closer to each other\" resonated with the audience. When Taiwanese guests from all walks of life participated in the forum activities, they all called for cross-Strait relations to return to the track of peaceful development as soon as possible. They looked forward to expanding exchanges and cooperation between the two sides and working together to create a bright future for national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771509.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Please introduce the situation of the special promotion meeting for the construction of cross-strait integrated development demonstration zones. Since the promulgation of the \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Road for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration…","The special promotion meeting for the construction of cross-strait integrated development demonstration zones was held in Xiamen, Fujian Province on June 13. Wang Huning, member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, attended and delivered a speech. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, the National Development and Reform Commission and other relevant central and state departments as well as relevant responsible comrades from Fujian Province attended the meeting.\nThis meeting summarized the work results since the release of the \"Opinions of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council on Supporting Fujian to Explore a New Road for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Build a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone\" (hereinafter referred to as the \"Opinions\"), exchanged work experience, proposed next-step work plans, and laid a solid foundation for the high-quality construction of a cross-Strait integrated development demonstration zone. The meeting made it clear that it is necessary to implement the requirements of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" to build the demonstration zone for cross-strait integrated development, and to adhere to high-quality development throughout the entire process of the construction of the demonstration zone. It is necessary to focus on the key tasks of building cross-strait integrated development demonstration zones, increase policy and institutional innovation, and promote pilot demonstration zones to provide experience. It is necessary to improve policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, optimize the business environment, strengthen industrial cooperation, and expand the benefits and sense of gain for Taiwan compatriots and enterprises. It is necessary to intensify cross-Strait cultural exchanges, strengthen the role of Chinese cultural ties, and enhance Taiwan compatriots' recognition of the Chinese nation, Chinese culture, and our great motherland. It is necessary to unblock the channels for Taiwanese youth to come to the mainland for development, guide Taiwanese youth to participate in the mainland's high-quality development and modernization, and enhance family well-being and spiritual harmony through exchanges and interactions.\nSince the release of the \"Opinions\" in 2023, relevant departments of the central and state agencies have formulated and issued a series of supporting policy documents. Fujian has issued 5 batches of 74 policy measures to promote the integration of Fujian and Taiwan, implemented a batch of key projects for the integrated development of Fujian and Taiwan on a rolling basis, and publicly released the first batch of With 17 landmark achievements, the demonstration zone's demonstration effect on Taiwan has gradually emerged and its influence has been expanding. It has become more convenient for Taiwanese compatriots and Taiwanese companies to land in their first home. Economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan have continued to deepen. The integrated development of Fujian has maintained a good momentum. The construction of the demonstration zone has made phased progress. In 2025, 2,612 new Taiwan-funded enterprises will be established in Fujian, a year-on-year increase of 6.8%. From January to May this year, 518,000 Taiwan compatriots entered the country through Fujian ports, an increase of 29.7% year-on-year, and 939,000 tourists traveled between the two sides of the \"mini three links\", an increase of 25.6%.\nIn the next step, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the National Development and Reform Commission will work with relevant central and state departments and Fujian Province to implement the deployment of this meeting, adhere to the goal of integrating people's hearts, use institutional innovation as the starting point, and use key areas as the engine, use more practical measures, greater efforts, high standards, and high quality to promote the construction of demonstration zones, strive to create a \"Fujian model\" for cross-Strait integrated development, and promote cross-Strait integrated development to achieve greater results during the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771508.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《中国新闻》记者","During the Straits Forum, a signing meeting for the docking of ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation was held, which was welcomed and praised by people on both sides of the strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","A signing meeting for the docking of ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation was held in Xiamen on the 13th. Mainland enterprises have signed contracts with enterprises and chambers of commerce and associations from many places in Taiwan to purchase agricultural and fishery products such as pineapple custard apples, pomelos, and tea from counties and cities in Taitung, Yunlin, and Nantou in Taiwan. More than 120 guests from both sides of the Taiwan Strait attended the matchmaking meeting. Taitung County Mayor Rao Qingling and Su Qingquan, chairman of the Pingtung County Party Committee of the Chinese Kuomintang, sent congratulations via video.\nSong Tao, director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the signing meeting and delivered a speech, introducing the positive progress and phased results achieved in the implementation of the ten measures, emphasizing that only by adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\", opposing \"Taiwan independence\", and recognizing that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully, only peace and tranquility exist in the Taiwan Strait, and only the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait can be guaranteed. Zhang Ronggong, Vice Chairman of the Chinese Kuomintang, said in his speech that cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation are the best channels to promote mutual understanding and enhance the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The Chinese Kuomintang will be committed to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and insisting on seeking peace across the Taiwan Strait and improving people's livelihood. Taiwanese industry players who participated in the signing meeting said that the ten measures will allow farmers and fishermen on the island to obtain tangible cross-strait peace dividends. They hope that the two sides will continue to promote more and better results through good-faith dialogue and communication.\nIn the future, we will further promote the implementation of the ten measures, insist on improving people's livelihood and well-being through exchanges and integration, and strive to allow more compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to benefit from and share the benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771507.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Regarding the active participation of people from all walks of life on the island in this Straits Forum, the Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council said, \"The Straits Forum is an out-and-out platform for the mainland's united front against Taiwan. It is impossible to watch the mainland use exchanges to cover up the united front, infiltration and division.\" Public opinion on the island pointed out that the DPP cannot…","Since its establishment 18 years ago, the Straits Forum has always adhered to the positioning of being \"civilian, grassroots, and broad-based.\" It has so far held more than 800 colorful cross-strait exchange activities covering grassroots, youth, culture, and economy, attracting the enthusiastic participation of more than 100,000 Taiwanese compatriots. The active participation of Taiwan compatriots is a full affirmation of the effectiveness of the Straits Forum, and is also a source of confidence and motivation for relevant institutions on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to continue to successfully run the forum. In recent years, relevant activities of the Straits Forum have become more and more relevant to the needs of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, with continuous innovation in the form and content of the activities and fruitful results, which are fully recognized by all walks of life on both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nThe peaceful development of cross-Strait relations is a historical trend. The strong desire and forward pace of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to communicate and cooperate cannot be stopped by anyone or any force. Out of political self-interest, the DPP authorities come out to smear and attack every year. This year, they have tightened restrictions and obstructed people from all walks of life on the island from participating in the Strait Forum. However, the more they cause trouble, the more they fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Taiwan's security department recently stated that it has completed the construction of the so-called \"Chinese Public Contact Window\" website as a channel for mainland people to provide intelligence. Any comment on this?","The DPP authorities blatantly targeted the mainland for intelligence theft and infiltration and sabotage activities, escalating cross-Strait antagonism and damaging cross-Strait relations, fully exposing their stubborn stance on \"Taiwan independence\" and their obsession with confrontational thinking. We strongly condemn this and will resolutely counterattack.\nIn accordance with relevant laws and regulations, Chinese citizens, political parties and people's organizations, enterprises, institutions and other social organizations all have the responsibility and obligation to maintain security. For those who provide intelligence to Taiwan's intelligence agencies and constitute a crime, the relevant departments will pursue their legal responsibilities in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771504.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, actor Zhang Linghe participated in the 18th Straits Forum and talked about his youth experience across the strait. He also responded to the call of young friends on the island to come to Taiwan for exchanges, which attracted attention on the island. Any comment on this? What is your response to Zhang Linghe’s exchange in Taiwan?","At the 18th Strait Forum Conference, Mr. Zhang Linghe told the story of his youth across the Taiwan Strait, echoing the expectations of young people on the island for close communication and dialogue. He showed the sincere feelings of mainland youth who care about cross-strait development and are willing to contribute to cross-strait exchanges. He received attention and praise from public opinion on both sides of the strait. We always support the \"two-way travel\" of young people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and are happy to see well-known mainland actors, singers and other literary and artistic workers go to Taiwan to meet and communicate with the people and young people on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771506.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","A few days ago, a signing meeting for the docking of ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation was held in Xiamen, including the purchase of some agricultural and fishery products from Taiwan. Due to the obstruction of the DPP authorities, Taitung County Mayor Rao Qingling could only participate in the video speech. However, there are still DPP politicians who claimed that they…","The signing of the contract will make it easier for agricultural and fishery products such as pineapples and sugar apples from some counties and cities in Taiwan to be imported into the mainland, which will open up sales channels and increase income for farmers and fishermen in central and southern Taiwan. For such a good thing, the DPP authorities are speaking out against it. Are they going against Taiwan's farmers and fishermen friends? Is it legitimate to threaten to \"settle accounts\" with county mayors who work for fruit farmers to make a living? If you don't do any real things or do bad things yourself, but don't let others do good things, this is called \"green terror\" and evil people are in power. In this regard, I have only one comment, that is, those who do too much injustice will be punished by themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771503.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","The head of the Mainland Affairs Council said at a symposium on the island recently that \"China continues to exert pressure on Taiwan. It is not Taiwan that really changes the status quo, but China; Taiwan has always maintained the status quo.\" Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an unquestionable historical and legal fact, and it is also the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\nNo matter what pretext the DPP authorities use, they cannot conceal the \"Taiwan independence\" nature of their attempt to separate Taiwan from China. What the DPP authorities want to \"maintain\" is their imagined \"divisive status quo.\" To this end, it has engaged in provocations for \"independence\", exaggerated the \"mainland threat\", and manipulated \"anti-China resistance\". It is a destroyer of the status quo in the Taiwan Strait and the biggest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. We will never leave any space for any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. The DPP authorities should completely abandon the \"Taiwan independence\" stance, stop provocations for \"independence\", return to the political basis of the \"1992 Consensus\", and use practical actions to maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771505.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The public memorial ceremony for Fuxi, the founder of Chinese humanity, will be held in Gansu in 2026 (Bingwu). Please introduce the relevant situation.","On June 21, the 2026 (Bingwu) public memorial ceremony for Fuxi, the founder of Chinese humanity, co-sponsored by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council, and the Gansu Provincial People's Government, will be held grandly at the Fuxi Temple in Tianshui City, Gansu Province. On the same day, the 13th Cross-Strait Ceremony to Commemorate Fu Xi will be held simultaneously in Taiwan. During the public memorial event, many activities such as a root-seeking and ancestor worship tour for Xihuang compatriots from Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan, and overseas Chinese, and the 2026 Fuxi Cultural Forum will also be held.\nThe third Longtai Cultural Exchange Month event will also open in Tianshui on the same day. More than 1,000 people including Taiwanese college students and scientific and technological workers will participate in more than 20 activities such as commemorating Fuxi, sports events, and cultural studies.\nGansu is not only the hometown of Emperor Xi, but also the core area of ​​the Silk Road and the golden corridor connecting Europe and Asia. Summer is approaching. We welcome Taiwanese compatriots, especially young friends, to cross the mountains and seas and come to Longyuan for a spiritual journey of cultural roots and visual feast. Go to Tianshui Fuxi Temple to experience the virtues of the ancestors of humanity, visit the Maijishan Grottoes to gaze at the warmth of the \"Oriental Smile\", and go to Dunhuang Mogao Grottoes to witness the thousand-year-old murals. You can sit by the Crescent Moon Spring in the Mingsha Mountain and listen to the distant echo of the camel bells along the Silk Road. You can dream back to the Jiayuguan Gate Tower and recall the pride of the frontier fortress. You can watch Zhangye Danxia and marvel at the uncanny craftsmanship of nature. You can ride in Gannan to encounter the green grass of the Sangke Prairie. You can climb Kongtong Mountain to appreciate the profound artistic conception of Taoism and nature.\nIn Gansu, you can also go to a carnival of \"Noodle Paradise\" and \"Cattle and Sheep Feast\". Eat a bowl of authentic Lanzhou noodles, taste a delicious hand-caught mutton dish, try stuffed skin, gray beans, water noodles, milk and egg fermented glutinous rice and various special snacks. Let this hearty taste on the tip of your tongue take you to relive the glory of the Han and Tang Dynasties and witness the rapid changes in Gansu today.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, a Taiwanese artist posted a video saying that searching the island's TV channels did not include the World Cup football match. Related topics sparked heated discussions among netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Mainland netizens have shouted to Taiwan compatriots, \"It's free to watch in mainland China\" and \"Come to the mainland to watch, and watch whichever of the 104 games you want to watch.\"…","The Football World Cup is the world's top event and a sports feast for fans. Relying on its huge market size and the institutional advantages of \"concentrating its efforts on big things\", the mainland negotiated with FIFA and signed a broadcast contract, and obtained the exclusive all-media rights and media sub-licensing rights for this World Cup in mainland China. It covers all channels such as open-circuit TV, pay TV, the Internet and mobile devices, and is provided to all people free of charge, truly realizing \"all people share\".\nWe welcome compatriots on the island to use the mainland network, APP, etc. to watch the live broadcast of the event, or come to the mainland to watch football and games, enjoy the passion of greenery with the mainland compatriots, and at the same time experience the mainland's convenient life services and vigorous development vitality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that many kindergartens on the island have selected mainland songs such as \"Snow Dragon Song\" and \"Light the Future\" as graduation songs or songs for daily singing and dancing activities. They have been smeared by the Green Camp. Many kindergarten teachers have spoken out and begged strange netizens to stop bullying. Any comment on this?","These two songs have beautiful melodies and positive contents. One praises the spirit of hard work and progress, and the other hopes that children will have a bright heart and grow up toward the sun. Regarding these two popular songs that are widely sung and popular, the green camp cyber forces and flankers on the island are smearing them for no reason. They extend their black hands into pure kindergartens and bully and attack the preschool teachers who sing the songs. It is disgusting.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities and the \"Taiwan independence\" forces \"will oppose China when encountering China and soften when encountering the United States.\" They regard mainland pop culture as a scourge. They go crazy when they see simplified Chinese characters. They get violent online when they hear someone saying that mainland China is good. They claim to be engaged in \"united front\" whenever there are cross-strait exchange activities. Weird things happen one after another, fully exposing the fragility and darkness in their hearts. Regarding these unbelievable phenomena, all walks of life in Taiwan should uphold justice and condemn them with one voice.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771498.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities in various fields.","Cross-Strait exchange activities continue to be lively and exciting. Let me introduce several recent activities.\nFrom June 1st to 7th, an agricultural exchange delegation from Dehua County, Fujian Province went to Taiwan to carry out industry-specific exchanges. They went deep into Taiwan's grassroots farmers' associations, tea associations, well-known tea companies, and boutique tea gardens. They exchanged views on the coordinated development of modern agriculture and the quality and upgrading of specialty industries, and reached a number of cooperations such as the co-creation of tea and porcelain cultural creation, tea tree variety improvement, and tea-making technology research.\nFrom June 9 to 13, the second cross-strait coffee cultural exchange event \"Coffee on the Cloud·Fragrant Cross-Strait\" was held in Baoshan City, Yunnan Province. Nearly 200 coffee industry representatives, experts and scholars from both sides of the Taiwan Strait conducted exchanges and discussions around cross-strait coffee cultural exchanges, coffee industry cooperation, talent training and introduction, etc., and reached a number of cooperation. The event also launched the first cross-strait co-branded coffee product - \"Shanhai Coffee\".\nOn June 10, the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition was launched in Jiangsu. Focusing on the development of new productivity, five major tracks were set up, including high-end manufacturing, electronic information, new energy and new materials, synthetic biology, and cultural and creative services. High-quality innovation and entrepreneurship projects from both sides of the Taiwan Strait were invited to participate. The registration deadline is July 15th. Young entrepreneurs from both sides of the Taiwan Strait are welcome to log on to the \"Jiangsu and Taiwan\" website or related WeChat public accounts to register for the competition.\nFrom June 12 to 16, the second Cross-Strait Youth E-Sports Carnival, \"Two Competing for Beauty and Seeing Yangcheng,\" was held in Suzhou, Jiangsu. 150 youths from both sides of the strait competed on the same stage and further enhanced friendship through e-Sports exhibitions, base camps, technology experiences and other activities.\nOn June 13, on the occasion of the 23rd World Blood Donor Day, Zhuhai held a voluntary blood donation charity event called \"Blood Relations, Zhuhai and Taiwan\". Nearly 50 compatriots from both sides of the Taiwan Strait successfully donated blood, demonstrating the deep friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Blood is thicker than water and they are one family.\nFrom June 15th to 19th, the 2026 Zhaotai calligraphy and painting art exchange event \"Mo Yuan Zhaotai has the same origin and common veins\" was held in Zhao'an County, Fujian Province, the \"Hometown of Chinese Painting and Calligraphy\". More than 60 calligraphers and painters from both sides of the Taiwan Strait used pen to make friends and express emotions with ink, and jointly witnessed the opening of the Zhaotai Calligraphy and Painting Art Integration Hall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that the mainland has begun to rectify the chaos of some people on the island taking advantage of cross-strait exchanges for profit, promote the \"direct reporting and direct review\" model, bypass intermediaries and directly connect with relevant groups and societies on the island, and clarify the public welfare nature of exchange activities. Public opinion on the island pointed out that a…","Frequent visits and exchanges will help compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits enhance understanding, promote cooperation and deepen friendship. We have always actively promoted cross-Strait exchanges and integration, and are committed to creating a more open, convenient, and safe communication environment for compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, so that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait can have heart-to-heart conversations, increase trust in exchanges, and promote spiritual harmony. We actively support relevant institutions and individuals on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in accordance with the law and regulations, but we will never allow illegal intermediaries to use cross-Strait exchanges to seek improper benefits. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots to participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, share the economic and social development opportunities of the mainland, enjoy the magnificent mountains and rivers of the motherland, contribute to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and help realize life dreams.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that the peanut harvest price in Yunlin County, the island's largest peanut producer, has recently fallen due to the impact of the zero-tariff import of American peanuts. Although the head of Taiwan's agricultural department said that \"the U.S.-Taiwan trade agreement has not yet come into effect and American peanuts have not been imported,\" it still caused widespread concern among local…","Yunlin County is the most important peanut production area in Taiwan, accounting for more than 70% of Taiwan's planting area and output. Once American peanuts are imported to Taiwan with zero tariff, Yunlin peanuts will face dumping of cheap American peanuts, and local farmers will be in deep trouble to survive. The DPP authorities ignored farmers' anxiety and industrial difficulties, responded perfunctorily, and were unable to do anything. This fully exposes his incompetence in governance and once again proves that \"kneeling to the United States will inevitably betray Taiwan.\" The so-called trade agreement between the United States and Taiwan will only harm the interests of all walks of life in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, the official website of a higher vocational school in Yunlin County, Taiwan published the latest \"2027 School Youth Service Mobilization Preparation Classification Plan\" promulgated by the education department of the Democratic Progressive Party. The content includes how to organize and mobilize students to cooperate with the military to strengthen vigilance. After the news was exposed, the island…","\"Vote for the Democratic Progressive Party, young people go to the battlefield.\" Since coming to power, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have deliberately undermined peace across the Taiwan Strait, continuously instigated \"resistance to China and safeguard Taiwan\" and stepped up \"preparations for war and independence\", causing panic in Taiwanese society and uneasiness among parents. Only by resolutely opposing \"Taiwan independence\" can peace across the Taiwan Strait be effectively guaranteed, the Taiwanese people be able to feel at ease, and Taiwan's youth be free from the worry of being \"mobilized for war.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","According to Bloomberg, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are considering implementing strict controls on the sales of artificial intelligence chips to the mainland and intend to criminalize unauthorized exports. Public opinion on the island believes that this is a \"letter of surrender\" submitted by the Lai Ching-te administration to the United States. If it insists on doing so, Taiwan's semiconductor…","If the report is true, it will further prove that the DPP authorities are \"relying on the United States and seeking independence\" and are frantic in promoting the \"decoupling and disconnection\" of cross-strait industries. The abuse of justice to destroy cross-strait industrial and supply chains violates the laws of market economy and suppresses the development space of Taiwan's semiconductor industry. In the end, it will only shoot itself in the foot, leading to an accelerated loss of Taiwan's core industrial advantages.\nMainland China is accelerating high-quality development and continues to make new breakthroughs in fields such as chips and artificial intelligence. Large-scale domestic models lead the global open source ecosystem. Brain-computer interfaces have achieved a critical leap from \"laboratory theoretical exploration\" to \"preliminary clinical applications.\" New productive forces are developing rapidly. Intelligent, green, and integrated industries are developing at a rapid pace, opening up a broader space for the two sides of the Taiwan Strait to complement each other's advantages and achieve win-win cooperation in related fields. We welcome Taiwanese companies to come to the mainland, embrace the certainty of development, seize the initiative in development, and achieve greater and better development in a stable, open, and innovative environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Taiwanese media reported that the DPP authorities have compiled a defense budget of nearly NT$950 billion in 2026, an increase of approximately three times compared with 2016 when the DPP came to power. Public opinion on the island criticized this as squandering huge amounts of money that should be used to improve people's livelihood on meaningless armaments. Any comment on this?","Since coming to power, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have stubbornly adhered to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and continued to collude with external forces to carry out \"independence\" provocations. For the political selfish interests of one party, they have intensified their efforts to squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people. They are willing to pay \"protection fees\" to external forces and run on the evil path of militarism.\n\"Taiwan independence\" and peace across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. \"Protection fees\" cannot buy protection, and \"seeking independence through force\" will only lead Taiwan step by step into the abyss of disaster, turning the Taiwanese people into cannon fodder for \"Taiwan independence\" efforts. The future of Taiwan and the safety, security, interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots have always been tied to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the reunification of the motherland. Only by opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism can peace and tranquility be achieved across the Taiwan Strait. Only by realizing the complete reunification of the motherland can Taiwan maintain peace forever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771500.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Recently, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have said that Taiwan's economic data are impressive, but some public opinion points out that the island's economic growth has not benefited most ordinary people. Faced with difficulties such as employment difficulties and rising prices, the \"pain index\" of Taiwan's people's livelihood is soaring. Any comment on this?","The purpose of economic development should be to improve people's livelihood and allow people to live a better life. However, the DPP authorities have kowtowed to the outside world, allowing outsiders to take whatever they want from advantageous industries to market opening. They also exploited internally, from customizing subsidies to selling land at low prices, to enrich a specific group of \"green friends\". Under the economic data promoted by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, commodity prices and electricity prices on the island have continued to rise. The gap between the rich and the poor has widened. The difficulties faced by traditional manufacturing, service industries, agriculture and fishery have intensified. People's wages have risen slowly. The \"sense of deprivation\" of ordinary people has increased day by day. The \"misery index\" has continued to soar. It has become a general public consensus that the island's social economy has \"no sense of recovery\".\nFaced with various facts and public dissatisfaction, the DPP authorities did not face the problem and focus on solving the immediate pain of the industry and people's livelihood. Instead, they boasted, which fully proved that they only have political self-interest in mind and no people's livelihood and well-being. They will surely lose the hearts of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260617_12771501.htm"],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, some public opinion on the island has questioned that in Taiwan's defense department's 2026 budget, the budget for the \"Taiwan-US Defense Department Joint Cooperation Assessment Plan\" has soared from US$410,000 last year to US$5 million. This is a clever excuse to send \"protection money\" to the United States, or to use it for \"lobbying expenses\" against the US Congress. Any comment on this?","In order to \"seek independence and reject reunification,\" the DPP authorities use unscrupulous means and use money to pave the way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Mainland actor Zhang Linghe recently encouraged Taiwanese people to visit the mainland in his speech at the Straits Forum. Taiwanese public opinion representative Chen Yuzhen also invited him to visit Kinmen. Do you currently know Zhang Linghe’s application arrangements for traveling to Taiwan? Will there be a specific mechanism to help high-traffic mainland artists, including Zhang Linghe, go to Taiwan to…","We are happy to see mainland entertainers come to Taiwan for exchanges, and are willing to provide strong support for exchanges between cultural and artistic workers on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Currently, the main obstacle for mainland entertainers to come to Taiwan is the obstruction and restrictions imposed by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. The DPP authorities should comply with the public opinion on the island, remove artificial barriers, and create conditions for normal cross-strait exchanges. The so-called \"cultural united front\" is pure nonsense and ridiculous.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","On the first question, the mainland proposed to “actively support Taiwanese businesses in rectification and further promote the import of Taiwanese pomelo into the mainland.” The harvesting and marketing time of Taiwan's Wendan pomelo must follow the solar terms. This year's Wendan pomelo harvesting will take place 10 days before and after the white dew on September 7. I would like to ask whether the mainland has…","The first question. We have always adhered to the concept of \"one family on both sides of the Taiwan Strait\", and have done our best to do practical things, do good things, and solve problems for Taiwan compatriots, and are working with relevant parties in Taiwan to promote relevant industries to make rectifications. As long as we adhere to the \"1992 Consensus\" and oppose \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to work together with relevant parties on the island to continue to provide help in expanding the sales of Taiwan's agricultural products in the mainland on the premise of complying with the relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations.\nSecond question. We have introduced ten policies and measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, with the aim of promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and enhancing the family well-being of our compatriots. Through the joint efforts of relevant parties on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, the implementation of the ten measures has achieved positive progress and phased results, and Taiwan's farmers, fishermen, film and television industries and other groups have benefited from them. On the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to strengthen exchanges and dialogue with Taiwan's political parties, groups and people from all walks of life, including the Chinese Kuomintang, and continue to promote the implementation of the ten measures. We believe that sharing peace, seeking common development, and jointly promoting prosperity on both sides of the Taiwan Strait is the wish and blessing of our compatriots, and will surely receive universal support from the Taiwanese people. Whoever is an enemy of the people and stands in the way of their gains will be spurned by the people and backlashed by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Regarding the mainland's special maritime traffic law enforcement operations in the waters east of Taiwan, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities said, \"The mainland has no right to claim law enforcement rights in the waters east of Taiwan. It takes the opportunity to expand its jurisdictional claims in the waters surrounding Taiwan and infringe on ships in surrounding waters. The international community…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of Taiwan Island. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the above-mentioned waters. Japan and the Philippines launched the so-called \"demarcation negotiations\" without authorization, bypassing China, which seriously violated international law and basic norms of international relations, seriously infringed on China's maritime rights and interests, and was completely illegal and invalid.\nThe mainland coast guard has carried out law enforcement inspections in the waters east of Taiwan Island in accordance with the law. This is a necessary action taken in response to Japan and the Philippines' serious infringement of China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and will continue to strengthen the control of relevant waters. The DPP authorities have bowed to the serious violations committed by Japan and the Philippines, betrayed national interests, and become a national scum. They have been opposed and spurned by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, including Taiwan compatriots. Its actions and statements in an attempt to escalate cross-strait antagonism are nothing more than diverting pressure and deceiving the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwanese media recently reported that for the first time this year, Taiwan’s Military Intelligence Bureau has stationed US troops, presumably to cooperate in monitoring the mainland. Any comment on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between the United States and China's Taiwan region. The DPP authorities deliberately escalate cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. The further they go on the evil path of \"relying on foreign countries to seek independence\" and \"using force to seek independence,\" the more they will lead to their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, the island announced the 2026 brochure for the joint recruitment of mainland students for master's and doctoral programs in Taiwan's universities and colleges. Only mainland students who have already studied in Taiwan can apply for master's and doctoral programs. The overall number of places has been slightly reduced from last year, but analysts believe that this number is still far greater than the…","While the DPP authorities are talking about \"welcoming mainland students\", they are constantly tightening the threshold and creating unfair treatment. The so-called \"number of places is greater than the actual demand\" is essentially the result of artificial suppression and political manipulation by the DPP authorities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, after a large-scale power outage occurred in Taichung City on the island, affecting more than 140,000 residents, an unexpected power outage also occurred in Changhua County, affecting nearly 4,000 residents. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have repeatedly claimed that there will be no power shortage problem before 2034. Any comment on this?","The DPP authorities are talking empty words and deceiving themselves, which cannot convince the people at all. Frequent power outages and rising electricity prices are daily issues faced by Taiwan's industry and people. If the Democratic Progressive Party authorities do not change their wrong energy policies, the island's \"power shortage\" problem will only get worse.\nMainland China has built the world's largest power supply system and clean power generation system. Cross-Strait power supply cooperation can optimize Taiwan's energy structure and power supply system and solve the island's power shortage problem.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","台湾“中央社”记者","A 10-year tracking poll released by the Taoyuan City Development Education Foundation on the 15th pointed out that although the majority of Taiwanese people still support cross-strait political negotiations, it has dropped from a peak of 77.7% in 2018 to 61.6% this year. How does the mainland view such poll results? Will it enhance its appeal to the Taiwanese people in addition to the economy? What are the…","We have noticed that a number of recent polls on the island show that the majority of the people believe that the status quo is unsustainable and that Taiwan should actively seek to negotiate cross-strait reunification with the mainland. The development history of cross-Strait relations proves that only by replacing confrontation with dialogue, replacing struggle with cooperation, and replacing zero-sum with win-win can cross-Strait relations achieve steady and long-term development. On the common political basis of adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to work with Taiwan's political parties, organizations and people from all walks of life to strengthen exchanges and dialogues, promote political negotiations, and conduct extensive and in-depth democratic consultations on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation.\nIn recent years, the DPP authorities and their flankers have been able to badmouth the mainland's economy and slander the mainland's development, creating excuses for them to promote cross-strait \"decoupling and disconnection\" and escalate cross-strait antagonism and confrontation. But no matter what they say or say, they cannot cover up the fundamentals of mainland China's stable economic foundation, many advantages, strong resilience, great potential, long-term improvement, and stability. They cannot change the objective fact that the strength of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait is increasingly disparate, and they cannot stop the general trend of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait getting closer and coming together.\nPeaceful reunification will create huge opportunities for Taiwan's economic and social development and bring tangible benefits to Taiwan compatriots. This is the biggest attraction. The earlier reunification is achieved, the better it will be for Taiwan's development and the better life for Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-17","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question is that during this year’s Straits Forum, many Taiwanese people visited Xiamen Xiang’an International Airport, which will be opened by the end of the year. Although the mainland supports Kinmen to share this airport, it is still difficult to achieve. The most direct impact at present is that the distance between Xiang'an Airport and Kinmen Shangyi Airport is too close, and the flight areas are…","The first question. As a world-class modern aviation hub, Xiamen Xiang'an Airport will further benefit Xiamen and Kinmen after it is put into operation, facilitate people's travel, promote regional development, and is a good thing to enhance the interests and well-being of the people of Kinmen. During the Straits Forum, many people from Kinmen visited the construction site of Xiamen Xiang'an Airport, hoping that Xiang'an Airport could be put into use as soon as possible. We support Kinmen’s sharing of Xiamen Xiang’an Airport, which will bring benefits to the people of Kinmen.\nSecond question. The one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community and the basic norm of international relations. It is the general trend, the great cause and the aspiration of the people.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", blatantly distort the facts, maliciously hype, escalate cross-strait antagonism and confrontation, and attempt to challenge the one-China principle in the international community. They are bound to encounter opposition and failure.\nThis concludes today’s press conference, thank you all. I wish everyone a healthy Dragon Boat Festival!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260617_12771495.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-06-18","Lin Jian","Reuters","Taiwanese leader Lai Ching-te stated today that Taiwan “is not part of the People’s Republic of China,” and that Taiwan’s future can only be decided by democratic elections by the Taiwanese people. However, he also said that Taiwan’s refusal to accept the rule of the Chinese Communist Party should not be seen as a provocation to the Chinese mainland or a regional trouble maker. He also said that Taiwan hopes the…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The future of Taiwan can only be decided by the over 1.4 billion Chinese people, including our Taiwan compatriots. The fact that Lai Ching-te keeps peddling around “Taiwan independence” narratives only reveals his nervousness and unsureness, for seeking “independence” with U.S. support and military buildup will only lead to a dead end. No words or deeds of the DPP authorities or Lai Ching-te himself will ever change the fundamental nature of the Taiwan question, which is purely China’s internal affair. Nor will they ever waver the international commitment to one China or stop the inevitability of China’s reunification.\nChina’s opposition to U.S. arms sales to Taiwan is consistent and clear.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260618_11948720.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260618_11948460.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on June 24, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held a regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters' questions on recent cross-strait hot issues.","Dear journalist friends, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council. Please ask questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","The spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council explained at a previous press conference six of the \"seven better things\" for Taiwan after peaceful reunification, which attracted great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. What is the spokesperson's explanation for \"After peaceful reunification, Taiwan's foreign exchanges will be better with the backing of a strong…","As a permanent member of the United Nations Security Council, China has proposed global development initiatives, global security initiatives, global civilization initiatives, and global governance initiatives, and its international influence, charisma, and shaping power have significantly increased. At present, China has established diplomatic relations with 183 countries, and the number of partnerships with various countries and regional organizations has increased to 153; China is already a major trading partner of more than 160 countries and regions, has signed 24 free trade agreements with 31 countries and regions, has joined almost all universal intergovernmental international organizations, and participated in more than 600 international conventions and amendments; China has promoted the creation of multilateral mechanisms such as the BRICS New Development Bank, the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank, the World Internet Conference International Organization, and the International Mediation Court. Our \"circle of friends\" continues to grow and is a builder of world peace, a contributor to global development, a defender of the international order, and a provider of public goods.\nAfter the peaceful reunification of the two sides of the Taiwan Strait, with the backing of a strong motherland, Taiwan compatriots will join with their mainland compatriots to share the dignity and glory of a great country. They will be stronger and more confident internationally, safer and more dignified, and enjoy unprecedented development opportunities. Taiwan's channels for external exchanges will be comprehensively expanded, and Taiwanese compatriots will participate in international affairs as masters; Taiwanese businessmen and enterprises will be deeply integrated into the global supply chain industry chain, with greater room for development and stronger competitiveness in the global market; Taiwanese compatriots will be able to receive support and help from their motherland more conveniently and smoothly overseas.\nAchieving peaceful cross-Strait reunification is not only a blessing for the Chinese nation and people, but also a blessing for the international community and people around the world. China's reunification will not harm the legitimate interests of any country, including its economic interests in Taiwan. It will only bring more benefits to Taiwan compatriots, bring more development opportunities to all countries, inject more positive energy into the prosperity and stability of the Asia-Pacific region and the world, and make greater contributions to building a community with a shared future for mankind, world peace, development, and human progress.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772490.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently stated that \"Taiwan's sovereignty belongs to the people, and the Republic of China and the People's Republic of China are not affiliated with each other.\" \"Only 23 million people can decide Taiwan's future.\" He declared that \"Taiwan is willing to cooperate with the international community to maintain the status quo across the Taiwan Strait.\" Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, Taiwan is part of China, and Taiwan belongs to all Chinese people. Taiwan's future can only be decided jointly by more than 1.4 billion Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. No matter what Lai Qingde says or does, it cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan is part of China's territory, nor can it stop the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and will be reunified.\nThe one-China principle is the general consensus of the international community and the basic norm of international relations. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and attempt to change the status quo of the Taiwan Strait that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. This is a denial of the results of the victory in World War II and a challenge to the post-war international order. The international community adheres to the one-China principle, opposes the general consensus of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and the mainstream public opinion on the island that wants peace, development, exchanges and cooperation. This fully proves that \"Taiwan independence\" separatism has no way out and \"anti-China and anti-China\" efforts are doomed to fail. Lai Ching-te's frequent clamor to the outside world has exposed his inner anxiety and uneasiness, confirming that \"Taiwan independence\" is increasingly reaching its end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772488.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the 4th Chain Expo opened in Beijing, with digital technology, advanced manufacturing, green agriculture and other companies actively participating. Many Taiwanese companies said that the cross-strait industries can complement each other's advantages and become bigger and stronger by deepening supply chain cooperation. Any comment on this?","The development history and fruitful results of cross-Strait cooperation have fully proved that the industrial advantages of the two sides of the Strait are complementary, deepening cross-Strait industrial chain supply chain cooperation, and promoting industrial integrated development are a bright road to mutual benefit and win-win results. During the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period, the mainland will adhere to the direction of intelligence, greenness, and integration, build a modern industrial system with advanced manufacturing as the backbone, steadily develop new productive forces, and move toward new and better high-quality development. This will certainly open up a broader space for the two sides to complement each other's advantages in related fields and achieve win-win cooperation. We welcome Taiwanese companies to come to the mainland to seize the development opportunities of the 15th Five-Year Plan, work with mainland companies to build a more resilient and safer cross-strait industrial and supply chain, and jointly strengthen the Chinese national economy.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Qiu Chuizheng, chairman of Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that the agricultural department will be asked to investigate and deal with five agricultural and fishery groups from Hualien and other places that went to the Straits Forum to sign agricultural and fishery product docking contracts, triggering widespread criticism from public opinion on the island. Any comment on this?","The mainland has always been an important export destination for Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products. We uphold the concept of \"Two sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family\" and have taken a series of measures to work with relevant groups and enthusiasts on the island to help Taiwan's farmers and fishermen expand the mainland market, find ways to expand sales and stabilize profits for Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products, which is well received by the Taiwanese people. The DPP authorities have blocked this effort and even threatened to investigate and deal with relevant businesses. They are arrogant and domineering. The strong indignation of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery circles and the condemnation of public opinion on the island show that the actions of the DPP authorities are unpopular and reprehensible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772487.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Regarding the mainland’s announcement during the Straits Forum to purchase agricultural and fishery products such as Taitung pineapple custard apples and Pingtung grouper, Qiu Chuizheng, chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the mainland has long used agricultural products as a “united front” tool against Taiwan and affects the market through political conditions. When there are political…","We have always adhered to the concept of \"two sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family\", insisted on improving people's livelihood and well-being through exchanges and integration, and tried every means to help Taiwan's grassroots farmers and fishermen open up the mainland market, striving to make compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait live a better life. The DPP authorities frequently attack and smear the mainland and use people's livelihood issues for political manipulation, which once again exposes their bad nature of being an enemy of the people and \"revolting whenever they encounter China.\" Who is thinking about Taiwan’s farmer friends and who is harming their interests? Taiwan’s farmer friends have a clear idea in their minds. We advise the DPP authorities to comply with the mainstream public opinion on the island, respond to the calls of the industry, and do more to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, rather than acting as enemies of the people and blocking their gains.\n\"United Front\" is the abbreviation of United Front, and \"Great Unity and Great Alliance\" is the eternal theme of the United Front. After the Japanese invasion of China broke out, the Anti-Japanese National United Front was formally formed and made great contributions to the great victory of the Anti-Japanese War. Now the main meaning of the united front is still \"unity\", or gathering people's hearts and gathering strength. The DPP authorities have repeatedly \"stigmatized\" the United Front and used it to discredit the mainland's policies to benefit Taiwan and the people, cross-strait exchange activities, etc., with sinister intentions. We hope that our compatriots in Taiwan will clarify the origin and original meaning of \"united front\" and stop being fooled and deceived by it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772486.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","The Sixth Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum will be held in Guangdong, attracting the attention of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","This year marks the 160th anniversary of the birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen. Mr. Sun Yat-sen was a great patriot and a great pioneer of China's democratic revolution. His spirit and feelings are the common spiritual wealth of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Guangdong has a glorious and long revolutionary tradition. It is the birthplace of the modern Chinese revolution and the hometown of Dr. Sun Yat-sen. From June 27th to 29th, the 6th Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum will be held in Zhongshan, Guangdong. The forum has the theme of \"Carrying forward Dr. Sun Yat-sen's fighting spirit and working together to pursue the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\" The activities include nine activities, including the opening ceremony, sub-forums, Taiwan's high-level talent exchange tour in the Bay Area, and the \"Dr. Sun Yat-sen and Taiwan\" archives and historical materials exhibition.\nThe land of Lingnan is the first to develop a trend. Guangdong is the vanguard, pioneer and experimental zone of mainland China's reform and opening up. Its economic aggregate has ranked first in the country for 37 consecutive years, its regional innovation capability has ranked first in the country for nine consecutive years, and the \"Shenzhen-Hong Kong-Guangzhou\" urban innovation cluster has ranked first in the world. Emerging industries such as new energy vehicles, low-altitude economy, and artificial intelligence are booming, and \"Made in Guangdong\" is renowned around the world.\nLingnan has thick soil and a cultural heritage that has been passed down for thousands of years. There is not only the ever-changing innovative vitality here, but also a cultural warmth that has lasted for thousands of years. In Guangdong, you can enjoy the night view of the Guangdong Pearl River and the carved eaves of the Chen Clan Ancestral Hall, experience the Shenzhen Bay light show and the innovation cluster of Nanshan Science and Technology Park, stroll the arcades of Shantou Small Park and the blue sea and silver beach of Nan'ao Island, and visit the Meizhou Hakka Dragon House and the thousand-year-old cypresses of Lingguang Temple.\nLingnan has charm, and fireworks also have flavor. Speak a word of Cantonese, watch a Teochew opera, sing a Hakka folk song, watch a movie \"Love Letter to Grandma\", the operatic accents and local accents reveal the memories of Lingnan. Go to a morning tea appointment, have a bowl of Cantonese-style sugar water, and unlock the market flavors such as rice rolls, rice noodles, thin rice cakes, and fish rolls. You can enjoy Lingnan specialties with a tea and a meal.\nThere is love in Lingnan, and Guangdong and Taiwan are closely connected. Guangdong is a gathering place for Taiwanese investment. A total of more than 30,000 Taiwanese-funded enterprises have taken root in Guangdong and become bigger and stronger. Policies that benefit Taiwan and people continue to be implemented, giving Taiwan youth a broad stage for entrepreneurship and enterprise transformation. We warmly welcome Taiwanese compatriots, especially young Taiwanese friends, to come to Guangdong to visit the cultural heritage of Zhongshan, go to the coastal area, encounter Hakka customs, experience authentic fireworks, seize development opportunities, and realize their life ideals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772485.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, a young Taiwanese actor posted a root-searching video on a short video platform. He held a family tree and asked mainland netizens for help, saying, \"I want to go back and find my roots.\" Netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and local people enthusiastically helped and helped him find his ancestral home in Shantou, Guangdong in less than two days. During the Dragon Boat Festival, he returned to…","Once the Taiwanese actor's video of searching for his roots in Shantou was released, it quickly attracted attention on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and received heartwarming messages of \"Welcome home\" filling the screen. A piece of yellowed genealogy is connected across the sea, and the dream of finding the roots of thousands of miles is finally fulfilled. The words \"Grandpa and Grandma, I'm home\" brought tears to the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait who were looking forward to reunion. On the occasion of the Dragon Boat Festival, we made the unique salty and sweet rice dumplings of our hometown with our clan members and shared a family dinner, allowing the clansmen on both sides of the Taiwan Strait to renew their century-old friendship.\nIt is a fine tradition of the Chinese nation to pursue the past with caution, to respect one's clan and to live in harmony with one's clan. In recent years, more and more Taiwanese young people have returned to their ancestral homeland on the mainland to trace their roots. This fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Straits share the same roots, culture and race, and are a community with a shared future, connected by blood and sharing weal and woe. We welcome more Taiwanese folks to come to the mainland to look for ancestral halls, look at their family’s genealogy, feel the warmth of home, pass on family affection, and work with our mainland compatriots to protect and build the common home of the Chinese nation. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and Taiwan Affairs Offices at all levels are willing to provide necessary support and assistance for this purpose.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772483.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","An article in the US \"Foreign Policy\" pointed out that in recent years, Taiwan has excessively bet on the support of the United States for its security and strategic future, but it has ignored the reality that \"no major power will always support the other side unconditionally.\" Public opinion on the island pointed out that while the United States is actively engaging with mainland China, the DPP authorities still…","Solving the Taiwan issue is a matter for the Chinese people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. We hope that the international community will understand clearly the nature and serious harm of the Taiwan Democratic Progressive Party's \"Taiwan independence\" campaign, understand and support the Chinese government and the Chinese people's just cause of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and completing national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Lai Ching-te recently said, \"I call on China to give up its military expansion in the South China Sea, East China Sea and Taiwan Strait, and also give up using force to attack Taiwan.\" He also said that Taiwan is \"willing to engage in exchanges and cooperation with China under the principle of reciprocity and dignity to promote peace and common prosperity.\" Any comment on this?","Currently, the situation in the South China Sea and East China Sea remains generally stable. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and attempt to \"rely on foreign countries to seek independence\" and \"use force to seek independence.\" This is the source of tension and instability in the Taiwan Strait and a \"troublemaker\" for regional peace and stability.\nWhat I want to emphasize is that we are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the greatest sincerity and our best efforts, but we will never promise to give up the use of force, and we will never leave any space for any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities. Only if the DPP authorities recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle and stop the separatist behavior of \"Taiwan independence\" can cross-Strait consultation and dialogue be restored, and cross-Strait relations return to the right track of peaceful development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772484.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Lai Qingde recently stated that \"China's non-coastal countries have no right to intervene in Japan-Philippines exclusive economic zone negotiations,\" adding that \"gray harassment by China's Coast Guard and others has caused regional unrest, and China's expansion attempts in the Western Pacific have become increasingly obvious.\" Any comment on this?","The proposed delimitation area announced by Japan and the Philippines is located east of Taiwan Island. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the above-mentioned waters. Japan and the Philippines bypassed China and initiated so-called maritime delimitation negotiations without authorization, seriously violating international law and basic norms of international relations, including the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, and seriously infringing on China's maritime rights and interests. It is legitimate and necessary for the relevant mainland departments to carry out law enforcement inspections in relevant sea areas in accordance with the law. It is a just act to safeguard national sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.\nThe DPP authorities have turned a blind eye to the abuses committed by Japan and the Philippines, but they have taken the opportunity to spread the separatist fallacy of \"Taiwan independence\" and incited \"anti-China resistance\". They have become an accomplice of external forces that infringe on the overall interests of the Chinese nation. They are despicable and shameless and must be liquidated.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","A recent poll on the island showed that in terms of maintaining peace across the Taiwan Strait, the proportion of people who chose \"showing goodwill to the mainland\" was much higher than \"deepening cooperation with the United States.\" Any comment on this?","Wanting peace, development, exchanges and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwanese society. In line with the mainstream public opinion on the island, we have always been committed to maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and continuing to introduce policies and measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. This fully reflects our commitment to safeguarding the overall interests of the Chinese nation and our goodwill and sincerity in doing good things for the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We have been widely recognized and welcomed by all walks of life in Taiwan.\nOut of their nature to pursue \"independence\", the DPP authorities ignored the mainstream public opinion on the island, deliberately escalated cross-strait antagonism and confrontation, constantly obstructed cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, turned a blind eye to the island's economic and people's livelihood issues, turned a deaf ear to the voices of the island's businesses and people, and allowed external forces to drive Taiwan into a dangerous situation of war. More and more Taiwan compatriots are dissatisfied with this and have condemned it.\nTaiwan's future and destiny depend on the great rejuvenation of the nation and the unity and prosperity of the country. Only by adhering to the \"1992 Consensus\", opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and recognizing that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China can cross-Strait relations develop peacefully, peace and tranquility can be found across the Taiwan Strait, and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots can be fundamentally guaranteed. We hope that our compatriots in Taiwan will follow the general trend, uphold justice, and work with us to safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and protect the common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202606/t20260624_12772489.htm"],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Regarding Taitung County Magistrate Rao Qingling’s video participation in the signing meeting for the purchase of agricultural and fishery products on the island during the Straits Forum, Mainland Affairs Council Chairman Qiu Chuizheng said that Rao Qingling has previously had relevant violation records and will ask the competent authorities to conduct administrative investigations and punishments in accordance…","County Mayor Rao Qingling participated in a signing ceremony for ten policies and measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation through a pre-recorded video to promote Taitung's agricultural products and benefit the local people, which received widespread support and recognition. Out of self-interest for \"independence\", the DPP authorities have repeatedly obstructed and sabotaged relevant activities and set up numerous obstacles for related activities. Now they want to \"settle accounts later\". They are basically abusing their power and specifically working against the people of Taiwan. They do bad things themselves and prevent others from doing good things. They are opposed by more and more Taiwanese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Just as the mainland is actively expanding sales of agricultural and fishery products such as pineapples and custard apples from some counties and cities in Taiwan, Liang Wenjie, spokesperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that \"Taiwanese people hardly eat pineapples and custard apples. It can be said that they are completely dependent on the mainland for agricultural products.\" This triggered an…","The DPP authorities have always been indifferent to people's livelihoods and harmed people's interests. They not only do not care about, do not care about, and do not solve the livelihood problems of grassroots farmers and fishermen on the island, they also mock, despise, and belittle the fruits of labor of farmers and fishermen, and attack, slander, and discredit the good intentions of the mainland. Justice lies in the hearts of the people, but his outrageous behavior has aroused public resentment on the island. If the DPP authorities do not stop political manipulation and stop restricting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, they will surely face a greater backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic, trade and exchange activities in various fields.","Recently, cross-Strait exchange activities in various fields have continued to flourish. Let me introduce some of them.\nIn June, Fujian held a series of cross-strait exchange activities. From the 10th to the 14th, the Zhangzhou Intangible Cultural Heritage Theater Exchange Troupe went to New Taipei, Miaoli and other counties and cities in Taiwan for exchange performances. The performances of Gezi Opera (Xiang Opera) and puppet show with strong Fujian and Taiwan characteristics vividly interpreted the saying that \"cross-strait families are close, and Fujian and Taiwan are close relatives.\" On the 19th, the 20th Fujian-Taiwan Crossing Cultural Festival and the Kaijiang Water Splashing Festival were held in Quanzhou. More than a hundred Taiwanese compatriots celebrated the Dragon Boat Festival with local folks. From the 23rd to the 27th, the 14th Strait Youth Gathering and the 4th Cross-Strait Youth \"Creating the Future\" Science Popularization Summer Camp was held in Fuzhou. From the 26th to the 29th, the 2026 Ninth Jimei District Cross-Strait Characteristic Temple Fair and Jimei Cross-Strait Concentric Integrated Consumption Season will be held in Jimei, Xiamen. Representatives of relevant enterprises and youth from both sides of the Taiwan Strait will conduct in-depth exchanges and docking around leisure, tourism, residence and employment. On the 27th, the 35th Cross-Strait (Dongshan, Fujian) Guandi Cultural Tourism Festival will be held in Dongshan, Zhangzhou. Nearly a thousand Taiwanese believers will experience the cultural charm of Guandi's loyalty and righteousness together with local folks.\nFrom June 16th to 21st, more than 80 Taiwanese night market stall owners were invited to Tongzhou District, Beijing, where they made, displayed and sold Taiwanese night market specialties such as Shihlin Sausage, Shenkeng Stinky Tofu, Liuhe Iron Plate Small Tubes, and Ximending Oyster Noodles. They were welcomed and loved by more than 100,000 mainland people.\nFrom June 21st to 25th, the 2026 \"China Good Anchors\" Cross-Strait Youth Livestreaming E-commerce Entrepreneurship Exchange Conference was held in Yiwu, Zhejiang, the \"World Capital of Small Commodities\". It included a series of activities such as a livestreaming e-commerce training camp, Yiwu International Trade City research, special salons, and resource docking. More than 500 youths from both sides of the Taiwan Strait participated.\nFrom June 22 to July 1, the first batch of \"Ecology and Humanities\" study camp for outstanding youths from both sides of the Taiwan Strait was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. It focused on topics such as ecological protection and the inheritance of China's excellent traditional culture, and included academic lectures, learning about pastures in Tibetan areas and intangible cultural heritage, and interviews with herders.\nFrom June 24 to 27, Chongqing will hold the 2026 \"Taiwanese Businessmen and Taiwan Youth Chongqing Tour\" event. More than 250 Taiwanese businessmen and Taiwanese youth will participate in the exchange and discussion on promoting the financial empowerment industry to help Taiwanese businesses and enterprises develop high-quality development and better integrate into Chongqing's modern manufacturing cluster system.\nIn addition, during the Dragon Boat Festival, China Central Radio and Television broadcast the Dragon Boat Festival special program \"Hundreds of Couples Competing to Praise the Dragon Boat Festival\", which received widespread attention from netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. One of the short films, \"Lan Zhi Weixin\", tells the story of the two Quyuan Palaces in Zhangzhou and Taipei facing each other across the sea for more than 300 years, and the blood and family ties of the same origin. It resonated with netizens on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. They left messages saying, \"One palace is across the strait, and one root connects the two sides of the Taiwan Strait\", \"We are one family\", etc.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that Taiwan’s military is conducting a so-called “immediate war preparation exercise”, claiming that “this exercise focuses on verifying the resilience and joint combat capabilities of each combat zone when the mainland takes action.” Any comment on this?","The so-called \"drill\" conceals the evil intention of the DPP authorities to \"seek independence through force,\" which fully proves that it is the root cause of incitement to cross-Strait confrontation and tension and instability across the Taiwan Strait. In the face of the powerful people's army, the pretentiousness of the DPP authorities is completely in vain and will only harm Taiwan and destroy itself.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","According to reports, Lai Ching-te recently said that \"Taiwan is not part of the People's Republic of China,\" hoping that the United States will approve an arms sale worth US$14 billion as soon as possible, and declared that \"rejecting reunification, Taiwan's future can only be determined by the Taiwanese people.\" Any comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a historical and legal fact that no one can change or shake, and it is also a general consensus of the international community. Our position of firmly opposing the United States' arms sales to China's Taiwan region is consistent and clear. The U.S. is urged to abide by the one-China principle and the three Sino-U.S. joint communiqués and handle the Taiwan issue prudently.\nNo matter what fallacies Lai Ching-te spreads or how many weapons he buys, they will not change Taiwan's status as part of China, nor will it change the iron law that Taiwan's future can only be determined by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. It will not change the inevitable demise of \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","After the island's public opinion organizations passed the \"abridged version\" of the defense budget, Lai Qingde recently said that he will not give up increasing defense expenditures and will propose special regulations or use additional budgets to ensure the smooth progress of defense equipment procurement. Any comment on this?","For the sake of one-party political self-interest, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are trying to \"seek independence through force.\" They continue to squander the hard-earned money of the Taiwanese people to engage in militarization, and engage in \"all people as soldiers\" in an attempt to tie the Taiwanese people to the \"Taiwan independence\" chariot. This will only push Taiwan into a more dangerous situation. \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end, and outsiders cannot be trusted. We have the firm will, strong determination, and strong capabilities to smash all separatist plots for \"Taiwan independence\" and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nReporter of Shenzhen Satellite TV's \"Direct News\"\n: Taiwan's administrative agency recently passed the so-called \"Special Regulations on the Procurement of Defense Autonomous Unmanned Vehicles\" draft, planning to allocate NT$210 billion from 2026 to 2031 to purchase independent defense unmanned vehicle equipment to build the so-called \"immediate detection and strike\" asymmetric combat capability. Any comment on this?\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\" and attempt to \"seek independence by force\", which will only put Taiwan into danger and bring serious disasters to Taiwan compatriots. The wheel of history of the reunification of the motherland is rolling forward. No matter how many weapons the DPP authorities buy, it will be like a mantis trying to pull a chariot, and it cannot change the inevitable defeat of \"Taiwan independence\".","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question, Taiwan media reported that the mainland's \"Xiangyanghong 22\" scientific research vessel was driven away by the Taiwan Coast Guard in the eastern waters of Taiwan. Taiwan claimed that the ship entered the relevant waters without permission. I would like to ask if the ship's scientific research route in eastern Taiwan has been adjusted compared to the past? Due to the current lack of communication…","The first question. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. In order to comprehensively understand the natural ecological conditions of sea areas under national jurisdiction and support and serve marine ecological protection, the Ministry of Natural Resources conducted a marine environmental survey in the sea east of Taiwan Island from June 16 to 18. The operations of mainland China's marine scientific research vessels in relevant waters are completely legitimate and legal. The DPP authorities' interference with normal scientific examination operations is political manipulation with ulterior motives. If we continue to use this to cause trouble and provocation and escalate cross-strait antagonism and confrontation, we will definitely be defeated.\nSecond question. I want to reiterate that there is only one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Relevant mainland departments have carried out law enforcement inspections in the waters under their jurisdiction in accordance with the law. This is a necessary action in response to Japan and the Philippines' serious infringement of China's territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and will continue to strengthen the control of relevant waters.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of \"Taiwan independence\", confuse right and wrong, and confuse right and wrong. On the one hand, they endorse the serious violations committed by Japan and the Philippines and sell out national interests. On the other hand, they attempt to provoke cross-strait confrontation. Their evil deeds have been firmly opposed by compatriots on both sides of the strait and will surely be punished by history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","The first question is that Liang Wenjie, deputy chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that \"pineapples and custard apples are an agricultural product that Taiwanese people hardly eat and rely entirely on the mainland.\" Some comments pointed out that if you just shout \"anti-Taiwan independence\" and promote the export of agricultural products to the mainland, you will be banned, cross-strait…","The first question. DPP politicians are arrogant and self-righteous and ignorant of the suffering of the people. An apology cannot calm the anger of farmers and fishermen, nor can it restore the lost hearts and minds. What the DPP authorities should apologize for most is that they went against the mainstream public opinion on the island and blocked cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. What they should most change are their separatist stance on \"Taiwan independence\" and their provocative actions seeking \"independence.\"\nSecond question. Pineapple and custard apples on both sides of the Taiwan Strait have their own characteristics. The mainland has a very large market that can fully accommodate agricultural products from Taiwan. We will uphold the concept of \"Two sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family\" and continue to help Taiwanese farmers and fishermen expand the mainland market and effectively increase their income.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-06-24","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question is that the recent topic of mainland importing Taitung pineapple and custard apples has triggered controversy on the island. Taipei Mayor Chiang Wanan, in addition to supporting pineapple custard apples, also called on the mainland to establish stable and sustainable institutional practices such as reasonable quarantine and tax rates when importing Taiwanese agricultural products. Any comment…","The first question. As we have repeatedly emphasized, we have always adhered to the concept of \"one family across the Taiwan Straits\", and we have done our best to do practical things, do good things, and solve problems for Taiwan compatriots. We have introduced a series of policies and measures that benefit Taiwan's farmers, fishermen, and enterprises, help Taiwan's farmers and friends expand the mainland market, and effectively enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. I believe everyone can clearly see who is helping Taiwanese farmers and who is harming Taiwanese farmers. We will, as always, actively promote cross-Strait agricultural cooperation to solve problems for Taiwanese farmers and fishermen. We also welcome more Taiwanese farmers and Taiwanese enterprises to invest and start business in the mainland to share opportunities and seek common development.\nSecond question. Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to the same country, and the compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are all Chinese and one family. Cross-strait affairs are family affairs of compatriots on both sides of the strait, and of course they should be handled through consultation among family members.\n\"Taiwan independence\" is the culprit that undermines peace across the Taiwan Strait. To seek peace across the Taiwan Strait, we must resolutely oppose all kinds of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist actions, strive to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and firmly protect the common home of the Chinese nation.\nThis concludes today's press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202606/t20260624_12772496.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-06-25","Guo Jiakun","Hubei Media Group","It is reported that Taiwan’s so-called “deputy foreign minister” said that the Taiwan authorities are in dialogue and consultation with political figures and social communities in Honduras regarding the restoration of “diplomatic ties” between China’s Taiwan region and Honduras. However, not long ago, the Foreign Ministry of Honduras clarifies on social media that Honduras is not engaged in any official talks or…","We note that the government of Honduras has made clarifications on the DPP authorities’ lies. Apparently, upholding the one-China principle is recognized internationally as the right thing to do. It is where the arc of history bends and public opinion trends. The “Taiwan independence” forces and the DPP authorities’ unjust pursuit have little support and will end up in failure.\nSince the two countries established diplomatic ties, China-Honduras ties which were built on the basis of the one-China principle have grown rapidly, and the economic and social development of Honduras has benefited from the practical cooperation it has had with China in various fields. It is quite clear that China-Honduras diplomatic ties serve the fundamental and long-term interests of both countries and peoples. China is committed to further advancing ties with Honduras on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260625_11952387.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260625_11952304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-25","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Chinese embassies and consulates in the United States have reportedly contacted U.S. local government offices and private firms to discourage engagement with Taiwan, while mischaracterizing U.S. policy. This is according to letters sent by U.S. government departments to governors’ offices and business leaders in the U.S. How does the ministry respond to these allegations?","China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between China’s Taiwan region and the U.S., including its federal and state governments. To only maintain unofficial relations with Taiwan is a commitment made by the U.S. side in the Joint Communiqué on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations. China urges the U.S. to earnestly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stick to the statements and commitments President Trump has made to China, prudently handle the Taiwan question, and not to have any official interactions with the Taiwan region under any pretext or send any wrong signal to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260625_11952387.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260625_11952304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-25","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","The United States, Britain, France, and Germany have expressed concern that recent Chinese activities off Taiwan’s east coast, where China has deployed Coast Guard patrols, threaten regional stability, freedom of navigation, and the safety of international shipping. How does the ministry view these concerns?","According to China’s domestic law and international law including UNCLOS, China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in waters east of China’s Taiwan island. Chinese authorities’ law enforcement and patrol activities in these waters are legitimate actions to exercise China’s jurisdiction, safeguard regional stability and uphold order at sea in accordance with the law. These actions are also a necessary response to Japan and the Philippines’ manipulation of their delimitation agenda and violation of China’s maritime rights and interests. Relevant countries need to respect China’s sovereignty, territorial integrity and maritime rights and interests, and stop mischaracterizing facts and truth. Relevant institutions should not make statements unsuited to their identity.\nThe DPP authorities are playing deaf to the infringement of Japan and the Philippines and even joining with external forces to vilify the Central Government’s effort to safeguard rights, and peddle their separatist narratives. It once again exposes the DPP authorities’ separatist nature and betrayal of the overriding interest of the Chinese nation. What awaits them is contempt from the people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait and the judgment of history.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260625_11952387.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260625_11952304.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Lai Ching-te, leader of the Taiwan region, recently said that regarding the defense special budget that was substantially cut by the Taiwan “Legislative Yuan,” he will not give up on raising defense spending, and will propose a separate special act or support the Taiwan military through supplementary budgets. The Taiwan executive branch subsequently passed the draft “Special Act on Procurement of Defense…","The DPP authorities are increasingly squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people, pouring it into a bottomless pit of meaningless arms purchases, and accelerating the push of Taiwan toward a dangerous situation of war and calamity. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: the trend toward unification is unstoppable, and \"seeking independence through force\" will surely lead to self-destruction.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say the U.S. House Appropriations Committee released a draft of the “FY2027 Defense Appropriations Act,” in which $2 billion is for providing weapons, equipment, and services to Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","Regarding this draft, what I want to say is: force cannot buy peace, and reckless militarism only overdraws the future. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and tolerates no external interference. “Using Taiwan to contain China” is bound to fail, and “using arms to aid independence” will only intensify tensions in the Taiwan Strait, ultimately bringing disaster upon oneself and reaping one's own bitter fruit. We demand that the US side adhere to the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, earnestly implement the important consensus reached at the meeting between the leaders of China and the US, stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait through concrete actions.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","As the Taiwan military launched a five-day “immediate combat readiness drill” on the 22nd, Taiwan's “Ministry of National Defense” said on the evening of the 23rd that the PLA aircraft carrier Fujian transited the Taiwan Strait that day and again released aerial footage. It said the Taiwan military closely monitored it using joint intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance means. Taiwan's “Minister of…","Taiwan is part of China. Where is there any “Minister of National Defense”? This is a routine training conducted by the Fujian aircraft carrier, and we will continue to organize such training in the future.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say Lai Ching-te stated that promoting the drone industry is a major policy of Taiwan, that drones can create a “hellish scene,” and that their deterrent effect is enormous. What is your comment?","Lai Ching-te always wants to push the people of Taiwan into the fire pit. He vigorously pursues \"independence,\" provokes war, and stirs up cross-Strait confrontation. Do we want peace or war? Do we want everyday life with its ordinary warmth, or a \"hellscape\"? We believe that the people of Taiwan have their own choice. We hope that Taiwan compatriots will see clearly Lai Ching-te's evil face as a \"war maker\" and a \"destroyer of peace,\" hold fast to righteousness, follow the trend of the times, and join us in opposing \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and safeguarding our common Chinese homeland.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to reports, after China rebutted Japan’s hype about China’s defense spending in March this year, the Japanese Minister of Defense recently again publicly questioned the transparency of China’s defense spending, while claiming that “Japan will invest transparently in new combat means such as drones and artificial intelligence to adapt to the changing nature of conflict.” What…","First, to answer your first question. China’s national defense expenditure is open and transparent. Each year, in accordance with the law, it publicly discloses the total amount of its national defense expenditure budget along with information on its scale, structure, and uses. It actively participates in the UN military expenditure reporting system and, since 2008, has submitted a report on its military expenditure for the previous fiscal year to the United Nations every year. China’s national defense spending has consistently adhered to being reasonable, moderate, and restrained, and its share of GDP has long remained below 1.5%. By contrast, Japan, as a defeated country in World War II, has seen its defense budget grow rapidly for 14 consecutive years, with its defense spending as a share of GDP soaring to 2% and even planned to rise further to 3.5%. Its per capita defense spending is more than three times that of China. Those who are clean remain clean, and those who are muddy remain muddy. Japan uses “conspiracy theories” to smear China’s defense spending, attempting to divert attention, mislead public opinion, and conceal its ambitions and moves toward “re-militarization.” What the world really needs to be told clearly is about Japan: “neo-militarism” is gaining momentum and becoming a menace. What does it intend to do?\nNow, to answer your second question: the Taiwan Affairs Office has already responded to this. I will send the DPP authorities one more line: overly clever scheming ends up costing you your own life.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say Taiwan's defense authorities stated that PLA aircraft entered airspace southwest of Taiwan and the Western Pacific for “long-range far-sea deployments,” and publicly released high-definition footage of the PLA's 无侦-10 unmanned reconnaissance aircraft flying around Taiwan, claiming “close monitoring and appropriate response.” What comments do you have on this?","“Taiwan independence” armed forces blowing whistles to boost their courage is purely self-deception. Taiwan is an inseparable part of China’s territory, and the PLA’s training and exercises around the island are reasonable, lawful and aboveboard.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The US and Japan are conducting large-scale “Valiant Shield” military exercises, and Taiwan's military is simultaneously holding combat readiness drills. The timing of the two sides' exercises highly overlaps, and they carry a strong implication targeting the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities deliberately create tension and escalate cross-Strait confrontation, which does not win popular support. Relying on military drills to embolden themselves cannot bring real security. Whoever treats confrontation as the norm and puts political self-interest ahead of people's livelihood and well-being will ultimately pay the corresponding price. The People's Liberation Army remains on high alert at all times and resolutely thwarts any “Taiwan independence” provocations.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, according to reports, the Japanese city of Nagasaki plans to complete the update of the exhibition panels at the Nagasaki Atomic Bomb Museum within fiscal year 2026. The planned panel text about the Nanjing Massacre in the museum will no longer use “massacre,” and will instead read “the Nanjing Incident, in which many civilians and prisoners were killed.” Nagasaki atomic bomb…","First, let me answer your first question. The Nanjing Massacre was a brutal crime committed by Japanese militarism. The iron-clad evidence is as solid as a mountain and cannot be altered. The Tokyo Trial clearly determined that the atrocities committed by the Japanese army in Nanjing were a “massacre” and not a so-called “incident.” The Judgment of the International Military Tribunal for the Far East has a dedicated chapter discussing this, and by way of an international judicial judgment, it determined the monstrous crimes of the Japanese army in Nanjing. Matsui Iwane, the chief perpetrator of the Nanjing Massacre, was sentenced to hanging as a Class A war criminal.\nAs a defeated nation in World War II, Japan to this day still denies, distorts, and even glorifies its history of aggression. Japanese right-wing forces visit the Yasukuni Shrine, revise history textbooks, deny the Nanjing Massacre, and forcibly recruit “comfort women”; these crimes and historical facts constitute a challenge to the post-war international order, a challenge to human conscience, and a challenge to the people of all victorious nations. We urge the Japanese side to face up to the voices of justice and reason, completely sever ties with militarism, and sincerely apologize and repent. Only in this way can it truly earn the respect of its Asian neighbors and the international community.\nNow let me answer your second question. We have released information on the Liaoning carrier group's far-seas combat-realistic training, and have made public video footage of the Japanese aircraft and vessels approaching to harass the scene. Who is the threat and who is the provocateur? It is perfectly clear. We urge the Japanese side to stop its dangerous conduct of interfering with the normal exercises and training activities of the Chinese side.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Japan and the Philippines have launched negotiations on an exclusive economic zone, and China has carried out law enforcement operations in the waters east of Taiwan island. Offices of the United States, the United Kingdom, France, and Germany in Taiwan have stated that China’s actions threaten regional stability, freedom of navigation, and international maritime shipping security, and aggravate tensions. What…","The waters for which Japan and the Philippines announced a proposed delimitation lie east of Taiwan Island, China, where China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf. Japan and the Philippines unilaterally launched so-called maritime delimitation negotiations, bypassing China. This seriously violates international law, including the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, and the basic norms of international relations, and seriously infringes on China's maritime rights and interests. Our law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters are legitimate and necessary, and a just action to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests. The standard for judging right and wrong is not who shouts the loudest. On this issue, the party infringing and provoking is Japan and the Philippines, and forming cliques to pressure China will not work.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-06-25","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","When meeting with foreign media, Lai Ching-te said that Taiwan's “rejection of ‘one country, two systems’ and Communist Party of China rule” should not be interpreted as provocation, and called on the mainland to abandon the use of force against Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","“Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question. It is the best way to realize the reunification of the motherland and the most beneficial outcome for compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation. At present, the Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and constantly provoke to seek “independence,” which is the root cause of the threat to Taiwan’s security. We will never allow “Taiwan independence” separatist forces to split Taiwan from China in any name or by any means. Any force or act that splits the motherland will surely be met with a head-on blow from the entire Chinese people.","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzh_246940/16469695.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-06-26","Guo Jiakun","NHK","Several Japanese economic delegations are visiting China to attend the China International Supply Chain Expo. How does China assess non-governmental exchanges between the two countries and what does China expect to achieve in the future? Besides, the delegation of Japan’s Association for the Promotion of International Trade also visited China’s Foreign Ministry and met with Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Hua…","On your first question, the Fourth China International Supply Chain Expo (CISCE) that kicked off this Monday attracted active participation of companies and organizations across the world. We’ve learned that many Japanese companies and economic groups also registered for the event, which represents the urgent call from Japan’s business sector for improving China-Japan relations and having cooperation with China. It’s hoped that those running the Japanese government can heed the call, face up to the root cause of problems, do serious soul-searching, correct the wrongdoings, show the sincerity of improving ties with China with concrete actions and create necessary conditions for normal exchanges between the two countries.\nOn your second question, Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs Hua Chunying on Monday met with the delegation led by Gaku Hashimoto, acting chief of the Japanese Association for the Promotion of International Trade (JAPIT), who traveled to China for the CISCE. The Chinese side expressed condolences over the passing of Yohei Kono, the president of JAPIT, and stated its consistent position on China-Japan relations and Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous remarks on Taiwan. The Chinese side expressed the hope that the Japanese business sector can help foster a right view of history in the country and improve bilateral relations between China and Japan.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260626_11953253.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260626_11953047.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-06-29","Guo Jiakun","Bloomberg","Tokyo’s top government spokesman has said that China Coast Guard ’s activity in Japan’s exclusive economic zone south of Yonaguni Island and territorial claims on those waters are unacceptable. What is the foreign ministry’s comment?","China has made its position clear on many occasions. Let me reiterate that China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in waters east of China’s Taiwan island. It is fully legitimate, lawful and justified for Chinese authorities to carry out relevant activities in these waters. Japan and the Philippines’ attempt to bypass China and initiate the so-called maritime delimitation talks constitutes a severe violation of UNCLOS and other international laws and basic norms governing international relations. It also seriously infringes on China’s maritime rights and interests. China will not allow this.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202606/t20260629_11954304.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202606/t20260629_11954266.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-01","Guo Jiakun","The Paper","It’s reported that regarding Honduran foreign ministry’s recent statement that it did not discuss “resuming diplomatic ties” with Taiwan and China’s response over the matter, the so-called spokesperson for Taiwan’s “foreign affairs office” said that Taiwan is open to “restoring ties” with Honduras without preconditions. What is China’s comment?","We notice that the government of Honduras has made clarifications on relevant issues, laying bare the DPP authorities’ deception-based diplomacy. Let me stress that the “Taiwan independence” separatism, running counter to the overwhelming trend, wins no public support and is doomed to fail. China is ready to promote China-Honduras relations and bring more benefits to our two peoples on the basis of the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260701_11955939.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260701_11955763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-01","Guo Jiakun","Jiji Press","I have three questions on China-Japan relations. First, regarding the Japanese citizens who were placed under compulsory measures in Dalian, what is the current status of the case? Have the individuals been formally arrested? Second, concerning the export control regulations, apart from the Dalian case, are there any other law-enforcement operations involving Japanese companies or citizens? Third, certain actions…","On your first question, the case is being handled in accordance with the law.\nOn your second question, the competent Chinese authorities deal with illegal acts and criminal offences in accordance with the law. The Japanese side should remind its nationals and businesses in China to comply with Chinese laws and regulations.\nOn China-Japan economic and trade relations, I’d refer you to the competent authorities. In fact, the competent authorities have made China’s position clear on many occasions. What you just said is not the truth. China has said more than once that the root cause of the serious difficulties in bilateral relations lies in the Japanese authorities’ erroneous remarks and actions on Taiwan and in the fields of military and security. The responsibility rests solely with the Japanese side. Why not ask those running the Japanese government whether they will respect China’s core interests and stop interfering in China’s internal affairs; whether they will honor the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan and safeguard the political foundation of China-Japan relations and foster an enabling environment for economic and trade cooperation; and whether they will do serious soul-searching and demonstrate the sincerity to bring the bilateral relations back to the right track with real actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260701_11955939.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260701_11955763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-01","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Paraguay’s foreign minister said yesterday that the country is open to trade with China, as long as it does not have to sever ties with Taiwan. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","China has made its position clear on relevant issues on many occasions. The government and leadership of Paraguay need to ask themselves what the people want, what best serves Paraguay’s fundamental and long-term interest and where the arc of history bends, and decide whether they should stop being on the wrong side of history and join the overwhelming majority of countries instead.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260701_11955939.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260701_11955763.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-02","Guo Jiakun","AFP","Taiwan said on Thursday that prosecutors had detained two employees of U.S. company Supermicro Computer after expanding a probe into the alleged smuggling of Nvidia AI chips to China. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this？","It is not a question about foreign affairs. I’m not familiar with that.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260702_11963957.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260702_11956618.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 2, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to today's press conference. Please begin asking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","On July 1, the grand meeting celebrating the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China was held in Beijing, and General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech. The content concerning Taiwan has drawn the attention of Taiwan compatriots. Please provide an interpretation.","General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the meeting celebrating the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, pointing out that our Party has developed into the world's largest ruling party with major global influence, enjoys the sincere support and backing of the people, and is the strong leadership core of the cause of socialism with Chinese characteristics. Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the unwavering historic mission of our Party and the shared aspiration of all Chinese people. General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech emphasized upholding the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” demonstrating sincerity and goodwill toward uniting the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and deepening cross-strait exchange, cooperation, and integrated development. It expressed our firm resolve to crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and oppose interference by external forces, and showed our strong determination to firmly advance the great cause of national reunification.\nIn the 105 years since the founding of the Communist Party of China, the Party has always been concerned with the future and fate of Taiwan and the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and has tirelessly struggled to resolve the Taiwan question and achieve the complete reunification of the motherland. At this important moment, when the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China is being celebrated and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation shows unprecedented bright prospects, General Secretary Xi Jinping has profoundly grasped the historical trend and the situation in the Taiwan Strait, and clearly expounded the general principles and policies for Taiwan work. He has further pointed the way for the development of cross-strait relations, and provides the fundamental guidance and action plan for doing Taiwan work in the new era. We will study and comprehend in depth, and fully implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech. We will thoroughly implement the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, and work together to advance the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations and create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774063.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Summit opened in Beijing on July 2 and has drawn close attention from cross-Strait youth. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Summit was held in Beijing from July 2 to 6. The summit was co-hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the Ministry of Education, the All-China Youth Federation, and the Beijing Municipal People's Government, under the theme “Joining Hands to Paint Youth, Striving Forward in the New Era.” The opening ceremony and main forum were held on July 2, followed by nine main events, including the Beijing-Taiwan College Students' Dragon Boat Race, the Young Scientists Forum, the Workers' Exchange Week of Hundreds of Trades and Professions, the Classical Poetry and Couplet Exchange Meeting, and the Youth Spark Thought-Sharing Session. Cultural research camps, sports exchange competitions, audio-visual experience tours, and 30 other series of activities will continue until the end of August. About 5,000 cross-Strait youths will take part in the summit's series of activities, learning from and drawing on each other in sports competitions, visits and study, and intangible cultural heritage experiences, deepening their friendship. We welcome more Taiwan youths to come to Beijing to take part in these activities, to personally experience the warmth and friendliness of compatriots on the mainland, to deeply experience China's excellent traditional culture, to keep this youthful appointment together, to share kinship ties, and to discuss a bright future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774062.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The 6th Straits Forum on Cross-Strait Zhongshan was held in Zhongshan, Guangdong, and compatriots on both sides of the Strait participated enthusiastically. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From June 27 to 29, the Sixth Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum was held in Zhongshan City, Guangdong Province, with about 2,000 participants from all walks of life across the Taiwan Strait, Hong Kong and Macao. Centered on commemorating the 160th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen, under the theme \"Carry forward Mr. Zhongshan's spirit of struggle and jointly pursue the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation,\" the forum held 1 main forum, 2 sub-forums and 9 exchange activities. Its scale, the participation of Taiwan compatriots and the proportion of young participants all reached new highs. The forum brought together forces from all sectors, industries and youth on both sides of the Strait, built consensus on jointly inheriting and carrying forward Sun Yat-sen's spirit, conveyed the shared aspiration for peace, development, exchange and cooperation, continued to deepen cross-Strait integration and development, and inspired compatriots on both sides to strive together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.\nDuring the forum, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Enterprises and the Zhongshan Municipal People's Government renewed their strategic cooperation framework agreement and held a signing ceremony for relevant industrial cooperation projects. The total signed amount reached over 30 billion yuan, of which Taiwan-funded projects accounted for 10.8 billion yuan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Please, spokesperson, introduce the situation of recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Recently, various cross-strait exchange activities have continued to heat up. Here are a few highlights.\nOn June 24, two Jiangsu-Taiwan industry matchmaking events were held in Jiangsu Province. One was a special matchmaking event for central state-owned enterprises and Taiwan-funded enterprises held in Nanjing, with 16 central state-owned enterprises and 35 Taiwan-funded enterprises, about 120 people in total, participating. It promoted complementary advantages between central enterprise resources in equipment manufacturing and electronic information and the technological strengths of Taiwan enterprises, helping deepen Jiangsu-Taiwan industrial integration and two-way empowerment and development. The other was an integrated circuit industry chain matchmaking event held in Wuxi, with nearly 70 enterprises from both sides and more than 100 industry professionals participating, providing a platform for precise matching and efficient connection for the cross-strait integrated circuit industry.\nFrom June 26 to 28, the 2026 Xiamen-Kinmen Bay Paddleboard Exchange Competition was held in Xiamen, Fujian Province. More than 100 paddleboard enthusiasts from both sides gathered on Dadeng Island in Xiang'an, Xiamen, competing on the same field and making friends through competition. They also visited the former site of the Kinmen County Government in Dadeng for the Wind Lion God Culture Market, youth exchange camps and other related activities, jointly experiencing the charm of Southern Fujian culture. From June 27 to July 1, the Fourth Xiamen-Taiwan Youth Music Study and Exchange Activity was also held in Xiamen. Over 500 cross-strait young people used folk music as a medium to exchange skills and deepen emotional bonds, including 120 teachers and students from four Taiwan campus folk music bands participating in the study and exchange activity.\nOn June 26, the awards ceremony for the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Micro-Drama Competition was held in Dongyang, Zhejiang Province. Themed \"Dreams Within Zhejiang, Drama Connecting Both Sides,\" the competition received a total of 1,070 works from both sides, including 125 works from Taiwan. Nine categories of awards were selected, including the \"Golden Camellia Award\" for Best Micro-Drama and the Best Script Award. More than 600 people from the film and television industries, youth, journalists and self-media practitioners from both sides attended the awards ceremony. During the competition, a series of activities were also held, including a micro-drama themed salon, a micro-drama on-site filming training camp and visits to micro-drama production bases, providing a platform for young people on both sides to deeply participate in micro-drama creation and share experiences.\nFrom July 3 to 9, the Fifth Cross-Strait Emei Martial Arts Cultural Exchange Activity will be held in Leshan, Sichuan Province, with nearly 200 Chinese martial arts enthusiasts and experts and scholars from both sides participating. Martial arts enthusiasts from both sides will exchange skills on the same stage, jointly inherit the spirit of Chinese martial arts, and visit the Leshan Giant Buddha, Emei Golden Summit, the Palace Museum Relics Southward Migration Exhibition Hall, and the giant panda base, experiencing the charm of Sichuan's cultural tourism and its development achievements.\nIn addition, from July to August, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots will hold the 23rd Taiwan Compatriot Youth Thousand-Person Summer Camp, themed \"Dragon Veins Passed Down, Youth for China,\" carrying out study and exchange activities on topics including the achievements of Chinese-style modernization, scientific and technological innovation, China's outstanding traditional culture, and cross-strait integration and development. From July 3 to 6, the main camp's visit and exchange activities will be held in Wuhan, Hubei Province, with about 330 Taiwan compatriot youth participating. Afterward, branch camp activities will be held one after another across mainland China, covering 30 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities, with about 1,300 Taiwan youth participating.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","June 28 this year marks the 15th anniversary of the launch of individual tourism to Taiwan by mainland residents. Some public opinion holds that tourism is a “touching” experience without language barriers, and is also the best way for both sides to achieve mutual benefit; close-range interaction can resolve differences, and individual travel will bring business opportunities and expand Taiwan's market demand.…","Travel is the encounter between people and scenery, and the meeting of people with one another. Group tours and individual travel to Taiwan both bring customers to Taiwan’s cultural and tourism industries, revitalize the island’s consumer market, and promote mutual understanding among compatriots on both sides of the Strait. This is a mutually beneficial and win-win development, and the industry on the island looks forward to it with great anticipation.\nWe warmly welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait to visit one another and travel together. In the mainland, you can climb the Great Wall to experience the grandeur of the mountains and rivers, walk through the Beijing Palace Museum to feel the history and culture, and stroll around West Lake in Hangzhou to savor the charm of Jiangnan. In Taiwan, you can climb Alishan, paddle on Sun Moon Lake, visit the Guguan Green Tunnel, travel through the Huadong Longitudinal Valley, and fully enjoy the coastal scenery. The mountains and rivers on both sides of the Strait are interconnected and share the same cultural roots. We look forward to more compatriots on both sides of the Strait crossing the strait to visit and exchange, continuously strengthening the friendship among compatriots and narrowing the psychological distance between us.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","As summer vacation approaches, many students on the island have expressed interest in coming to the mainland to take part in study tour activities. Please introduce what study tour activities Taiwan youth and students can take part in on the mainland, and through what channels they can participate.","Carrying out study-tour exchanges helps young people broaden their horizons and gain knowledge. Science and technology on the mainland are developing with each passing day, Chinese culture has a long history, sports and folk activities are colorful and varied, and study resources are very rich. We welcome Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to take part in a wide variety of study activities, and we will provide good services and guarantees. Here I would like to introduce three categories of study activities for our Taiwan young friends.\nFirst, science and technology innovation study tours. Taiwan youth interested in science and technology innovation may come to Shanghai to visit the Science and Technology Museum, the Maritime Museum, the Lingang Super Factory, and so on; to Shenzhen to experience AI autonomous driving and leading drone light-show enterprises, and so on; and to Hangzhou to learn about the City Brain operations command center, the metaverse experience hall, and so on.\nSecond, history and culture study tours. Taiwan youth interested in history and culture may come to Beijing to visit the Forbidden City, the Great Wall, the National Museum, and so on; to Henan to visit the Longmen Grottoes, Yinxu, the Erlitou Xia Capital Site, the China Museum of Chinese Characters, and so on; and to Shandong to climb Mount Tai, visit the Confucius Temple, and experience Qilu culture, and so on.\nThird, sports and folk custom study tours. Taiwan youth who want both to exercise their bodies and to experience excitement may come to Guizhou to take part in the Village BA basketball games and try spinning tops, bamboo-pole dancing, and so on; to Inner Mongolia to learn intangible cultural heritage skills such as Mongolian leather carving and wool felt handicrafts; and to Heilongjiang to learn intangible cultural heritage skills such as Hezhe fish-skin picture crafts, and so on.\nWe welcome Taiwan compatriots, Taiwan youth and students, to come to study in various parts of the mainland, find what they love, learn what they enjoy, and determine their own space for development and future goals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774056.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Regarding the mainland coast guard's recent law enforcement patrol activities in the waters east of Taiwan, Lai Ching-te said, “Recent Chinese maritime actions are carried out under the guise of law enforcement, in fact pursuing expansion, undermining the security and peace and stability of the Indo-Pacific region and the status quo, and also undermining the rules-based international order.” What is your comment…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the waters east of Taiwan Island. Japan and the Philippines bypassed China and unilaterally started delimitation negotiations in relevant waters. This seriously violates international law and the basic norms of international relations, seriously infringes on China's maritime rights and interests, and is completely illegal and null and void. The mainland coast guard conducts law enforcement patrols in relevant waters in accordance with the law to exercise jurisdiction. This is a just act to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and it is also a necessary action taken against Japan and the Philippines unilaterally starting delimitation negotiations in these waters while bypassing China and infringing on China's maritime rights and interests.\nThe DPP authorities turn a deaf ear and a blind eye to the infringing acts of Japan and the Philippines, and ignore the damage to the interests of people on the island. Yet they take the opportunity to spread “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies on a large scale and incite “anti-China and resistance to China.” They have become accomplices of external forces that harm the overall interests of the Chinese nation. Such despicable conduct will certainly be condemned by compatriots on both sides of the strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774052.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, Zhang Xue, founder of “Zhang Xue Motorcycles,” had a video call with the first motorcycle owner on the island. When the owner exclaimed, “Your industrial technology is really advanced,” Zhang Xue warmly replied, “It’s us.” This sparked wide emotional resonance among netizens on both sides of the Strait. What comments do you have on this?","This kind of dialogue reminds me of a song, “We Are All One Family”: “In the past we were one family, and now we are still one family.” Because we are one family, Chinese on both sides of the Strait take pride in the innovation and development achievements of a large number of mainland industries and technologies, such as “Zhang Xue Motorcycles.” Because we are one family, mainland compatriots are willing to take the lead in sharing with Taiwan compatriots the opportunities of Chinese-style modernization and jointly creating the great cause of national rejuvenation. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often to travel and see for themselves, to personally experience the ever-changing development of the mainland, to actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, and to join hands in creating a better future for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","The summer vacation is about to begin, and some places on the mainland have successively released internship positions for Taiwan youth and students, which have been welcomed. How can we make it more convenient for an increasing number of Taiwan youth and students to intern and work on the mainland?","The summer internship positions for Taiwan youth launched across various regions are ample and diverse, and they are welcomed by a broad range of Taiwan youth and students. This fully demonstrates that the mainland's high-quality development holds vast opportunities, and that exchange and integration between young people on both sides of the Strait is the will of the people. The steady advancement of Chinese modernization will provide enormous space for the development of Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan's young people, and Taiwan's young people can achieve much in the broad expanse of the motherland mainland. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams. We will continue to create better conditions and more opportunities for this, and we look forward to more Taiwan youth taking the lead at the forefront of the times, actively coming to the mainland for internships and employment, accumulating job experience, improving professional skills, expanding their development space, and realizing their life ambitions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","According to media reports, the United States, the United Kingdom, France, and Germany expressed concern about mainland coast guard vessels conducting law enforcement patrols in waters east of Taiwan island, claiming that such law enforcement actions threaten regional stability, freedom of navigation, and the safety of international shipping. Taiwan's external affairs authorities have hyped this. What is your…","Taiwan is part of China, and China has an exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in the sea east of Taiwan Island. The mainland coast guard conducting law enforcement patrols in relevant waters is exercising jurisdiction in accordance with the law. It is a righteous act to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and is also a righteous action taken against Japan and the Philippines, which bypassed China and unilaterally launched delimitation negotiations in the area, infringing upon China's maritime rights and interests.\nOur actions are lawful and legitimate, appropriate and necessary. They are conducive to safeguarding the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to safeguarding regional stability and maritime order, and to ensuring the safety of life and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait. Relevant countries should respect China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and maritime rights and interests, rather than confusing right and wrong and turning black into white. The DPP authorities not only make concessions to Japan and the Philippines, but also echo the infringing acts of external forces, serving \"relying on external forces to seek independence\" that harms the overall interests of the Chinese nation and the vital interests of Taiwan fishermen. They have become a disgrace to the nation, have been spurned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and will inevitably face historical reckoning.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the Mainland Film Exhibition of the 17th Cross-Strait Film Festival was held in Taiwan and was well received by audiences on the island. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The mainland film showcase of the 17th Cross-Strait Film Festival was held in Taipei from June 22 to 27, with eight mainland films of diverse styles, including “Ri Gua Zhong Tian,” “Dongji Island,” and “The Lychee of Chang'an,” screened collectively, bringing a feast of light and shadow to island audiences. During the festival, several mainland filmmakers traveled to Taiwan to attend multiple post-screening talks and industry exchange events aimed at audiences, interacting warmly with Taiwan audiences and sharing their creative experiences. We support and hope that cross-Strait film and television exchange activities will be held more often and do better, promoting mutual understanding and deepening friendship between people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of the Mainland Affairs Council, said in an interview recently that the DPP authorities' consistent policy is “maintaining the status quo,” and that at this stage cross-Strait relations have no “Taiwan independence” issue, only the issue of being “forcibly unified” by the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities define the status quo across the Strait with the “new two-state theory,” which completely violates legal principles, history, and reality, and is an out-and-out separatist fallacy of “Taiwan independence.” Their pursuit of “independence” and provocations, inciting “anti-China and resistance to China” on the island, escalating cross-Strait hostility and confrontation, and undermining cross-Strait relations, make them the destroyers of the status quo across the Strait and the source of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable, and it runs counter to the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan. If the DPP truly believes there is no “Taiwan independence” issue, it should immediately abolish the “Taiwan independence party platform,” stop “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, and improve cross-Strait relations through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Recently, the 6th Cross-Strait Zhongshan Forum was successfully held in Guangdong. Regarding the enthusiastic participation of Taiwan youth in this forum, MAC Chairperson Chiu Chui-cheng said, “Low prices, on-the-ground hosting or full subsidies clearly carry United Front suspicions.” What comment do you have?","It is a good thing for young people from both sides of the Strait to gather to commemorate Mr. Sun Yat-sen and discuss national rejuvenation together. The DPP authorities, out of political self-interest, are politically manipulating such exchange activities, attempting to create a “green terror” and deter Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland. They are afraid that the “information cocoons” they painstakingly fabricated will be pierced, and afraid that their lies demonizing the mainland and inciting cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation will be exposed. We warn the DPP authorities: compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. The great tide of visiting relatives, drawing closer, and coming together will not change, and no scheme to divide the two sides and seek “independence” through confrontation will succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","Regarding the DPP authorities' rejection of applications by tourism operators from Shanghai and Fujian for pre-trip inspection visits to the island, tourism groups and operators on the island have spoken out in opposition, calling on the DPP authorities to engage in less political manipulation, let tourism go first, and leave room for easing cross-Strait relations. What is your comment?","Promoting the resumption of tourism to Taiwan by residents of Shanghai and Fujian is a positive measure that conforms to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan and promotes the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. A site inspection trip (“踩线”) is a routine industry practice, aimed at arranging meals, lodging, attractions and reception procedures, and it is purely civilian, purely business exchange. However, the DPP authorities have unilaterally put forward “must first be consulted through the tourism ‘mini two associations’” as a precondition, and directly rejected the entry applications of site inspection groups. This is typical political manipulation and artificial obstruction. The industry's appeal, “Less political manipulation, let tourism go first,” fully reflects the tourism industry's dissatisfaction with and opposition to the DPP authorities' deliberate politicization of cross-Strait tourism, which disregards the survival difficulties of tourism operators on the island and the livelihood demands of ordinary people.\nWe have always upheld the concept that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We have promoted the resumption of tourism to Taiwan by mainland residents and have continued to extend goodwill. Since 2024, we have successively resumed tourism to Kinmen and Matsu by residents of Fujian and Shanghai. If the DPP authorities truly care about the livelihoods of operators, they should lift the restrictions on mainland residents' tourism to Taiwan as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774053.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, public opinion on the island has pointed out that, against the backdrop of both the United States and China striving to establish communication and reduce risks, the DPP authorities must face the reality that peace in the Taiwan Strait requires political mutual trust. The issue of the DPP's “Taiwan independence party platform” is no longer merely an intra-party matter for the DPP, but an important…","The DPP stubbornly holds to its “Taiwan independence” stance. The “Taiwan independence party platform” is clear proof that it has deliberately pursued “Taiwan independence” and sought to split Taiwan from China. Since taking power, the DPP authorities have extensively colluded with external forces to pursue “independence” and provoke, seriously undermining cross-Strait relations, threatening peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and seriously harming the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan. They have met with opposition and condemnation from broad sections of Taiwan's compatriots.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. “Relying on outsiders to seek independence” cannot bring security and peace, and “seeking independence by force” will only lead Taiwan step by step into an abyss of disaster. Taiwan's future, the security and well-being of Taiwan's compatriots, and their interests have always been tied to the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. Only if the DPP abandons the “Taiwan independence party platform,” stops “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, and acknowledges the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, can it truly improve cross-Strait relations and ensure peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. On the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, and to work together for peace across the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and the rejuvenation of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774060.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te, while attending an exchange event on the island, said that the award received by “Taiwan Travelogue” shows that “Taiwan literature continues to be read, understood, and affirmed by the world,” and declared that he will continue to keep the cultural budget generous, “making Taiwan’s literature and culture an irreplaceable force internationally.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. The origin of Taiwan’s culture is Chinese culture; it is both an important component of Chinese culture and enriches its connotations. Any remarks that promote the “Taiwan independence view of history” and disregard historical facts will inevitably be unanimously condemned by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities attempt to use culture as a pretext to smuggle the “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy into the international community. This runs counter to the trend of history and will only hit a wall everywhere in the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, the director of the Taipei Office of the “American Institute in Taiwan” told island media in an exclusive interview that 70% of Taiwan’s public supports “maintaining the status quo,” which can serve as the basis for dialogue between Taiwan’s leader and the mainland; that the mainland’s attempts to create division in Taiwan will not achieve the result it wants; and that US policy toward Taiwan is…","The Sino-US heads-of-state meeting reached important consensus and achieved fruitful results. Some people are making a fuss, saying one thing and doing another regarding President Trump's remarks on Taiwan, creating discordant noise on the Taiwan question, and slandering and smearing the mainland's policy toward Taiwan. Their intentions are sinister, and we firmly oppose this.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the real status quo of the Taiwan Strait. Any attempt by any person or force to change this status quo will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","The Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress has formally taken effect. Some DPP politicians claim that by holding overseas organizations and individuals accountable, the regulation creates a “chilling effect” on Taiwan’s academia, media, and friends of Taiwan, and uses legal tools to expand “transnational repression.” What is your comment?","As a promotional law that safeguards the fundamental and overall interests of the Chinese nation, the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress, upon its formal implementation, will provide a solid legal safeguard for the steady and far-reaching cause of ethnic unity and progress, and will gather mighty strength for all ethnic groups across the country to jointly advance the cause of building a strong nation and national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the Chinese nation, and all are Chinese. All ethnic groups, including compatriots in Taiwan, jointly forged a unified multi-ethnic nation, jointly wrote the glorious history of China, and jointly created splendid Chinese culture. They have come together as a community of shared destiny, bound by blood ties, shared beliefs, cultural connections, economic interdependence, and mutual affection. The implementation of the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress is conducive to further promoting cross-Strait economic and cultural exchanges and cooperation, deepening integrated development of cross-Strait relations in all fields, and promoting compatriots on both sides of the Strait to jointly inherit and promote Chinese culture, enhancing Taiwan compatriots’ sense of belonging, identity, and honor toward the Chinese nation.\nThe DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. Out of political self-interest, they have repeatedly commented on this law, spread rumors and smears, and fabricated lies, deliberately confusing the public, with the aim of inciting cross-Strait opposition and confrontation and intimidating the people of Taiwan. Their intentions are sinister, and they will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774061.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, Taiwan entertainer Tseng Pei-tzu won the championship on Hunan Television's “Riding the Wind 2026” program, and a Taiwan compatriot player successfully scored a goal in the Min Super League. Many Taiwan compatriots have found broad platforms on the mainland in various fields to showcase their talents, personally confirming that the mainland offers enormous development opportunities. What comment do you…","As everyone has seen, the five “Taiwan sisters” who took part in *Ride the Wind 2026* not only brought audiences distinctive stage performances, but also won over audiences on both sides of the Strait with their courage to break through their own limits. At the Fujian Min Super League matches, 12 Taiwan compatriot players have already joined teams and are fighting side by side with mainland teammates, with excellent coordination; they have scored goals many times and won enthusiastic support from fans on both sides of the Strait. The facts prove that with passion and perseverance, one can earn applause on an ever-larger stage.\nThe greatness of the mainland lies in its vast stage and abundant opportunities. The development of the economy, culture, education, science and technology, sports, health, and other fields provides a great stage for Taiwan compatriots to display their talents and realize their dreams, and creates great opportunities. We warmly welcome the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to develop, pursue their dreams, keep pace with the times, and move forward with the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","According to the milk market price ranking recently released by the Global Statistics Database, Taiwan’s milk price, at US$3.07 per liter, ranks first in the world. In the face of complaints from island residents, the DPP authorities have deliberately steered the topic toward “resisting China.” What is your comment on this?","Speaking of milk, I would like to share a set of data: In 2025, the Mainland produced 40.91 million tons of milk annually. In May this year, the average retail price of urban fresh milk was 11.5 yuan per liter, only about half the price of milk in Taiwan. Diversified dairy products meet diverse market demands. During the 14th Five-Year Plan period, the average height of boys aged 6 to 17 increased by 2.1 centimeters, and that of girls increased by 2.2 centimeters. It can be said that the Mainland’s supply of fresh raw milk is stable, of excellent quality, and offers high cost-effectiveness, and that cooperation between the two sides in the dairy products field has enormous potential.\nUnfortunately, the DPP authorities are indifferent to livelihood issues that directly affect the vital interests of the people on the island. They care only about political self-interest and are focused solely on political manipulation. On the one hand, they unilaterally restrict the import of Mainland agricultural products into Taiwan, obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, choose a roundabout path while there is a nearby option, spend money lavishly, and willingly serve as an “ATM” for external forces. On the other hand, they rely on stirring up antagonism to divert public attention. Whenever their governance fails and their shortcomings are exposed, they immediately “blame the Mainland.” This trick has long been seen through by compatriots on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Taiwan's “Beautiful Island Electronic Journal” recently released its latest opinion poll, showing that 47.6% of the public is dissatisfied with Lai Ching-te's governance, an increase of 2.7 percentage points from May, while satisfaction decreased by 1.7 percentage points from May, resulting in a “death cross.” Some commentary on the island has also criticized the Lai Ching-te authorities for having no concrete…","Relevant public opinion polls and public opinion on the island show that the Lai Ching-te authorities have been concerned only with their own political interests, have ignored people's livelihood and well-being, have deviated from public opinion, and have lost popular support.\nFor some time, the Lai Ching-te authorities have vigorously peddled “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies, continuously provoked for independence, racked their brains to manipulate “anti-China and resist-China” sentiment, and obstructed and undermined cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They have suppressed and persecuted political opponents and carried out a “green terror.” For their own private interests, they have not hesitated to tie the ordinary people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot and push Taiwan toward the danger of war. They have shamelessly kowtowed to foreign powers and obstinately “relied on outsiders to seek independence” and “sought independence by force.” The island's public is no longer buying the political tricks of the Lai Ching-te authorities, and increasingly sees clearly that they are the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of calamity for the people's livelihood and well-being in Taiwan. Only by resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be effectively safeguarded, and only then can the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan's development prospects be effectively guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","The Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress has been formally implemented. May I ask: how will the Mainland side define the legal boundary between undermining ethnic unity and legitimate cross-Strait civil exchanges? Is there concern that, under such a relatively “vague” definition, there is a risk of overturning the dividends of past cross-Strait civil exchanges? If Taiwan residents traveling to the Mainland…","The Mainland Affairs Council’s statements about the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress are completely fabricated slander and smears. It deliberately confuses people, invents so-called “risks,” intimidates the people of Taiwan, and creates a “chilling effect.” The door to cross-Strait exchanges has always been open. We have always welcomed compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople from across the Strait to come to the mainland for exchanges and cooperation in all fields. Coming to the mainland is convenient and easy for compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople, who need not have any concerns. We also consistently safeguard, in accordance with the law, the lives, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides, including those in Taiwan, while consistently cracking down on all kinds of illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law. If “Taiwan independence” forces carry out acts of splitting the nation and undermining ethnic unity for the purpose of seeking “independence,” they will certainly be punished in accordance with the law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","Lai Qingde recently said, “China is weaponizing agricultural products, attempting to use agriculture to coerce politics, including by using import bans and raising tariffs as pretexts; the United States and Japan have become Taiwan's top two export markets for agricultural products.” What is your comment?","The mainland has always been an important export destination for Taiwan's agricultural products. Adhering to the concept that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, we are making every effort to do practical things, good deeds and solve difficult problems for Taiwan compatriots. We have taken a series of measures to help Taiwan farmers and fishermen expand the mainland market, find outlets for Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products, expand sales channels, and secure stable returns, so that more and more Taiwan farmers and fishermen can enjoy the dividends of Chinese modernization and lead better lives.\nThe DPP authorities not only have for a long time unilaterally restricted the import of mainland agricultural products into Taiwan (including more than a thousand agricultural products), obstructing normal cross-Strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, and threatening to punish county and city magistrates and relevant fishery and agricultural associations that actively promote the export of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products to the mainland; they also kowtow to the United States and sell out Taiwan's core industries, implementing “zero tariffs” on 4,885 industrial products and 1,482 agricultural products from the United States, seriously harming the interests of Taiwan's related industries and the well-being of its people.\nWhoever sincerely works for the benefit of the people, and whoever arbitrarily blocks the people from profiting, Taiwan's farmers and fishermen have a clear account in their hearts. Taiwan's grassroots operators are deeply worried, and harbor great indignation at the DPP authorities, which not only fail to help farmers and fishermen solve practical problems, but also vigorously obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and attempt to curry favor with outsiders by sacrificing the island's industries and people's livelihoods. We advise the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation and do more things that benefit the interests and well-being of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260702_12774059.htm"],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Ching-te said at the joint graduation ceremony of Taiwan's military academies, “Facing China's military operations around the Taiwan Strait, Taiwan will continue to strengthen its self-defense, work with democratic allies to play a deterrent role, and achieve peace through strength. The National Armed Forces must establish a clear sense of friend and foe, resist threats and temptations, and defend…","Lai Ching-te's remarks further expose his stubborn “Taiwan independence” stance and his sinister intent of “seeking independence by force” and “relying on foreign forces to seek independence.” Disregarding the mainstream public opinion on the island that wants peace, development, exchange and cooperation, he loudly peddles separatist fallacies and hypes the so-called “mainland threat,” deliberately escalating cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism and undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. This will only push Taiwan into the perilous situation of war and calamity, making him an out-and-out “wrecker of cross-Strait peace,” a “creator of Taiwan Strait crises,” and a “war instigator.”\nThe trend toward the reunification of the motherland is vast and surging forward. Any conduct that defies this trend is doomed to fail, and any scheme to split the country will inevitably go bankrupt.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question. Regarding the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress, the Mainland Affairs Council and the DPP said that “this law is far too subjective.” May I ask how the mainland side responds to doubts that the law “criminalizes vaguely” or forces a choice between “unification or independence”? Can it be clearly defined?\nSecond question. The 16th anniversary of the signing of the ECFA has arrived. The…","Question one. There is absolutely no so-called issue of “vague criminalization” or “either unification or independence.” The relevant claims by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are complete slander and smears, deliberately confusing public perception, fabricating so-called “risks,” and intimidating the Taiwan public. We have always welcomed Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople to come to the mainland for exchanges and cooperation in all fields; traveling to the mainland for Taiwan compatriots and businesspeople is both convenient and easy. We have also consistently safeguarded, in accordance with the law, the lives, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, and we adhere to cracking down on all types of illegal and criminal activities in accordance with the law.\nQuestion two. Since the DPP authorities came to power, on the one hand, they have obstinately insisted on the “Taiwan independence” stance, advocated “decoupling and severing chains” in cross-Strait economic and trade relations, and implemented more discriminatory trade restriction policies against the mainland; on the other hand, they have colluded with external forces and sold out Taiwan’s core industries, harming the interests of most Taiwan industries and people. This despicable scheme will only let compatriots on both sides of the Strait see more clearly the selfishness of the DPP authorities, and see more clearly the risk that the DPP authorities are aggravating Taiwan’s structural economic problems.\nQuestion three. From January to May this year, cross-Strait trade totaled US$150.837 billion, up 22% year on year. Among this, the mainland’s exports to Taiwan were US$41.874 billion, up 30.6% year on year, and imports from Taiwan were US$108.963 billion, up 19.1% year on year. These figures show that cross-Strait economic ties have not weakened but have strengthened.\nThe problems that have emerged in cross-Strait economic and trade relations are entirely because the DPP authorities have disregarded the objective facts that the economies of the two sides are highly complementary and inseparable, and have deliberately and persistently sought to undermine cross-Strait industrial and supply chains and artificially restrict and interfere with Taiwan businesses’ investment layout. On the one hand, they forcefully push cross-Strait “decoupling and severing chains,” and on the other hand, they strenuously hype up the so-called “non-red supply chain.” This is a reckless act that places political self-interest above economic laws; what it undermines is the long-term foundation of Taiwan’s industrial development, and what it harms is the immediate interests of the broad Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises.\nStrengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development is a righteous path in line with the common interests of compatriots and enterprises on both sides of the Strait. The mainland’s economy has strong resilience, great potential, a sound foundation, and broad room for development, and its prospects are bright; it has always been the best choice for the broad Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises to invest and set up businesses. No matter how the winds and clouds change, the trend of close cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepened integrated development cannot be stopped.\nQuestion four. In June 2010, on the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus,” the two sides signed the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA). Over the years, we have earnestly fulfilled our commitments, promoted and ensured the entry into force and implementation of ECFA, and brought tangible benefits to relevant enterprises and people on the island, especially the broad small and medium-sized enterprises and farmers and fishermen.\nBefore taking office, the DPP attacked ECFA; after taking office, it has seriously obstructed the implementation of ECFA. It has not only failed to take substantive measures to lift discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, but has also continuously gone to greater extremes by modifying rules and setting up obstacles, maliciously obstructing and undermining normal cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation. This has led relevant mainland departments to have to suspend the tariff reductions for some ECFA products. The responsibility lies entirely with the DPP authorities.\nThe key to safeguarding and enhancing the interests and well-being of the broad Taiwan compatriots lies in compatriots on both sides of the Strait uniting, resolutely opposing “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, eliminating the root of “Taiwan independence,” and jointly safeguarding the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. On the basis of the “1992 Consensus,” any issue related to ECFA can be properly resolved through cross-Strait consultation. But if the DPP authorities disregard public opinion and even create more problems, they will certainly be hitting their own feet with a rock they lift themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-02","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Regarding the 16th anniversary of the signing of ECFA, the Mainland Affairs Council said that “cross-Strait economic and trade relations have undergone structural changes.” How do you comment on the phenomenon of Taiwan's economy and trade being “de-mainlandized” while Taiwan's economy is rising?","Taiwan's economy and trade can never be “de-mainlandized.”\nTwo points need to be emphasized. First, the Economic Cooperation Framework Agreement (ECFA) is an important institutionalized economic cooperation achievement that the two sides signed on the political basis of the “1992 Consensus.” Since ECFA's implementation, it has brought tangible benefits to both sides of the Strait, especially to relevant enterprises and people in Taiwan. However, the DPP authorities, obstinately adhering to the “Taiwan independence” position and refusing to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” not only refuse to implement the cross-Strait Trade in Services Agreement under ECFA, but also refuse to take measures to lift trade restrictions on the mainland, seriously undermining the basis for cross-Strait consultation and the implementation of ECFA. The full responsibility for ECFA failing to benefit more Taiwanese businesses and people lies with the DPP authorities.\nSecond, we uphold the concept that both sides of the Strait are one family, actively deepen cross-Strait integrated development, and enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides. In 2025, cross-Strait trade reached US$314.33 billion, maintaining a high growth rate of 7.3% against the backdrop of a slowdown in global trade growth. The mainland newly established 8,132 Taiwan-invested enterprises, showing that cross-Strait industrial cooperation is increasingly close and economic and trade exchanges continue to be vibrant. The development course and rich achievements of cross-Strait economic and trade relations fully demonstrate that the Chinese mainland has always been a strong backing for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises and the best choice for investment and business, and that deepening cross-Strait integrated development is the necessary path to benefit the livelihoods and well-being of compatriots on both sides.\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260702_12774050.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-07-03","Guo Jiakun","China News Service","It is reported that Taiwan’s so-called “Ministry of Foreign Affairs” said recently that Taiwan is in contact with Honduras for restoring their diplomatic relations. President of Paraguay Peña, when visiting Taiwan, said that he strongly encourage Honduras to look at the partnership that Paraguay and Taiwan have. However, Honduras’ Foreign Minister Agüero said that Honduras has already refuted claims of alleged…","We commend Foreign Minister Agüero’s remarks on China. The one-China principle is a prevailing international consensus and a basic norm in international relations. It is what the greater national interests entail and where global opinion trends and the arc of history bends. The Taiwan authorities are going against the overwhelming tide. All separatist acts aimed at “Taiwan independence” are doomed to fail and will bring nothing but shame.\nSince diplomatic ties were established between China and Honduras in 2023, bilateral relations have grown rapidly on the basis of the one-China principle, with fruitful outcomes in practical cooperation. Facts have fully proven that the establishment of diplomatic relations serves the fundamental and long-term interests of both countries and peoples. On the basis of the one-China principle, China stands ready to advance relations with Honduras for the greater benefit of both peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260703_11974685.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260703_11974639.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 8, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Taiwan’s defense authority recently stated that, in view of the “mainland’s military threat against Taiwan” rising ever higher, and in order for soldiers to understand the mission of “why fight and for whom to fight,” the “patriotic education and political training course” for military academy graduates has been renamed and restored to “Anti-Communist Patriotic Education.” What is your comment on this?","The Communist Party of China is the vanguard of the Chinese people and the Chinese nation. Over the 105 years since its founding, it has led the people through unremitting struggle to thoroughly end the history of old China’s internal turmoil and foreign aggression, its poverty and weakness, and its decline into a semi-colonial and semi-feudal society. It established the New China in which the people are masters of their own country, and in just a few decades completed an industrialization process that developed countries took several centuries to complete. It has created two miracles, rapid economic development and long-term social stability, and has achieved historic accomplishments recognized worldwide, writing the most magnificent epic in the thousands of years of Chinese nation’s history. The Communist Party of China has always held fast to its original aspiration and mission of seeking happiness for the Chinese people and seeking rejuvenation for the Chinese nation, has always maintained its flesh-and-blood ties with the masses, and has always won the sincere support and backing of the people. It is the leadership core of contemporary China.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have tried to instill “anti-communist” ideas in graduates of Taiwan’s military academies and to incite them to fight for “Taiwan independence” and fight for the Democratic Progressive Party. This is a great step backward in history and a deliberate escalation of cross-Strait opposition and confrontation.\n“Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and “seeking independence by force” is a path to certain destruction. We hope that broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the malicious intentions and harm of the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, refuse to become sacrificial pawns and cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence,” stand on the right side of history and the side of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, and join us in promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the great cause of national reunification, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775133.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan, regarding so-called “how to distinguish normal cross-Strait exchanges from united front activities,” said that normal cross-Strait exchanges are not a problem, but any activity hosted by the mainland's Taiwan Affairs Office that declares a stance on unification with Taiwan has a clearly united front nature. It will strengthen the review of cross-Strait exchanges,…","We would like to ask the DPP authorities: Do you know what united front work is? Do you know the origin and original meaning of the united front? “United front” is short for “united front work,” and its essence is great unity and broad alliance. It is about uniting people’s hearts and gathering strength. On the basis of common interests, common goals, common emotions and a common future, it unites all forces that can be united and mobilizes all positive factors that can be mobilized to work together for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. United front work has been carried out for many years and is open and aboveboard.\nOur work on Taiwan has always been mindful of the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation and the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We have always upheld uniting broad Taiwan compatriots, fully understanding the special historical experiences of Taiwan compatriots, fully considering the realities in the Taiwan region, and fully taking into account the interests and feelings of all strata and groups in Taiwan. We are willing to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups and people from all walks of life on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence.” We will continue to uphold the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” consistently implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots, introduce policies and measures that benefit Taiwan and its people, smooth the channels for cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and personnel exchanges, facilitate Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in sharing the development opportunities on the mainland, and continuously enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities have repeatedly “stigmatized” united front work and used it to smear the mainland’s policies that benefit Taiwan and its people and cross-Strait exchange activities, and to intimidate and suppress Taiwan compatriots who take part in cross-Strait exchanges. In their eyes, is there any normal cross-Strait exchange left? We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will see through their sinister intentions and despicable conduct, stand with us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, jointly promote cross-Strait exchanges and integration, continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, and together create a bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775132.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Raymond Greene, Director of the Taipei Office of the “American Institute in Taiwan” (AIT), recently said that nothing is more effective at deterring conflict than turning Taiwan into a “beehive” filled with aerial, surface, and underwater drones. Raymond Greene and Lin Chia-lung also invited representatives in Taiwan of several so-called “diplomatic allies” and reiterated the “commitment” to Taiwan. What is your…","The Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-US relations and one of the key topics of the May meeting between the heads of state of China and the United States. After the meeting, President Trump publicly stated that he does not want to see anyone pursuing “independence,” does not want U.S. forces to travel 9,500 miles to fight a war, will not serve as a “backer” of “Taiwan independence,” and will not readily promise arms sales to Taiwan. The Chinese side takes the political statements and actions of the U.S. side seriously.\nFor some time, 谷立言 has behaved as if he were a “Grand Emperor,” constantly making remarks about Taiwan's domestic political situation and attempting to suppress political forces that oppose “Taiwan independence” and uphold peace in the Taiwan Strait. He has repeatedly stirred up trouble in the Taiwan Strait, supported the DPP authorities' “independence” schemes and provocations, deliberately distorted the cross-Strait “status quo,” and spread the fallacy of so-called “unconditional dialogue” to provide cover for the “Taiwan independence” line. He has persistently spread “porcupine” rhetoric and fabricated the “beehive” concept, pressured Taiwan's domestic legislative bodies to pass a “special defense budget,” advocated helping Taiwan build “asymmetric combat capabilities,” handed “Taiwan independence” separatist forces a “knife,” and continuously incited cross-Strait confrontation, attempting to turn Taiwan into a “powder keg” and a “landmine island.”\n谷立言's words and deeds violate the solemn statements made by President Trump, undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and attempt to steer China-US relations and cross-Strait relations in an extremely dangerous direction. The U.S. side should abide by the one-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, and demand that relevant agencies and personnel stop spreading erroneous remarks, stop stirring up trouble in the Taiwan Strait region, stop colluding to advocate for “Taiwan independence,” and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775131.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","This year marks the 89th anniversary of the 'July 7th War of Resistance'. Communities on both sides of the Strait have held commemorative activities in various forms. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","On July 7, 1937, the “Lugouqiao Incident” broke out, and Japanese militarism launched a full-scale war of aggression against China. At a time of national peril, the Kuomintang and the Communist Party of China cooperated to establish an anti-Japanese national united front, and all Chinese people, regardless of party affiliation, united as one, fought strong enemies with unbending backbone, and built a Great Wall with their flesh and blood. They won the first complete victory in resisting foreign aggression in modern times, brought the treasured island of Taiwan, which had been occupied by Japanese imperialism for as long as 50 years, back into the embrace of the motherland, and made major contributions to saving human civilization and defending world peace.\nThough the mountains and rivers remain intact, the years speak. During the arduous and extraordinary War of Resistance, compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait shared the same breath and common destiny, standing shoulder to shoulder against external aggression and vowing to defend the nation and home to the death. Large numbers of Taiwan compatriots, holding the conviction that “to save Taiwan, one must first save the motherland,” resolutely crossed the Strait back to the Chinese mainland, joined the anti-Japanese torrent and the national salvation cause, demonstrating the iron-hearted patriotism of loving the country and loving the nation. We will forever remember the heroic anti-Japanese spirit of Taiwan compatriots and their efforts for the liberation cause of the Chinese nation. We hope that broad Taiwan compatriots will carry forward the glorious patriotic tradition, uphold a correct view of history, nation, and state, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, and join mainland compatriots in pursuing the bright future of national reunification and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775130.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress has taken effect. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council said the law is a “unification law” disguised as ethnic unity, linking “national reunification” with “ethnic unity,” and that it reflects the CCP's shift in its Taiwan policy from “opposing Taiwan independence” to a new stage of legal warfare of “forced unification.” What is your comment on this?","The Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress clearly stipulates that legal means be used to resist all kinds of illegal acts in ethnic-related fields. It is grounded in national conditions, conforms to legal principles, and is consistent with international practice. It is a just and necessary measure to safeguard national sovereignty, unity, and territorial integrity.\nThe DPP authorities, out of their independence-seeking nature and political self-interest, seek to erase and distort the Chinese national identity of Taiwan compatriots. They have repeatedly launched unreasonable attacks and fabricated smears against this law, with the aim of creating pretexts for betraying the nation, splitting the country, undermining cross-strait relations, and restricting cross-strait exchanges.\nNo matter what tricks the DPP authorities play, they cannot change the fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China. They cannot sever the blood ties of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, cannot erase the imprint of Chinese culture on Taiwan society and its compatriots, and cannot block the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and certainly will be. If “Taiwan independence” forces dare to carry out acts that split the nation and undermine national unity, we will resolutely punish them in accordance with law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775129.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","In response to the implementation of the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress, Taiwan's administrative authorities established a so-called “Cross-Border Suppression Inter-Agency Coordination Platform.” The Mainland Affairs Council said that specific countermeasures are under study and that cross-Strait exchange reviews will be strengthened. What is your comment?","The Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress is a promotional law that safeguards the fundamental and overall interests of the Chinese nation. Its formal implementation will provide solid legal safeguards for steady and far-reaching progress in ethnic unity and progress, and will gather tremendous strength among all ethnic groups nationwide to jointly advance a strong nation through Chinese-style modernization and the great cause of national rejuvenation.\nResolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. Reunification is a historical conclusion, the trend of the times, the justice of the cause, and the will of the people. No matter how many tricks the DPP authorities collude with external forces to play, they cannot stop the historical trend that the motherland will be reunified and will certainly be reunified. Through the joint efforts of compatriots on both sides, the complete reunification of the motherland must be achieved, and it certainly can be achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775128.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","On July 6, one of the Navy's strategic nuclear submarines successfully launched a submarine-launched strategic missile carrying a training simulated warhead. In response, the DPP authorities said: “The mainland is raising tensions in the surrounding area and undermining regional peace and stability. Taiwan will firmly defend its sovereignty, security, and regional peace and stability, and calls on the…","The spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense has already provided an explanation. This missile test firing was a routine arrangement of annual military training. Relevant countries were notified in advance, it conforms to international law and international practice, and it is not directed at any specific country or target.\nWe have firm will, strong determination, and powerful capability to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist schemes and to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. The DPP authorities’ excessive reaction to this missile test fully exposes their provocative “independence” schemes as outwardly fierce but inwardly timid.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775125.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, the Kuomintang has stated that peace across the Taiwan Strait is the most fundamental interest of the Taiwanese people. To avoid conflict across the Strait, one cannot rely on slogans, nor engage in confrontation, and certainly not engage in dangerous political maneuvers like the DPP's pushing Taiwan to the edge of war. Peace across the Strait requires a common political foundation and institutionalized…","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion of Taiwan society and the common voice of compatriots on both sides. When family members get along, as long as they speak well and consult each other on matters, conflicts and confrontation can be avoided, differences can be resolved, and mutual trust can be consolidated. On the common political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we are willing to strengthen communication with Taiwan’s political parties, groups, and people from all walks of life, including the Kuomintang, to deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, and to work together for peace in the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775127.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Recently, the book 'Cross-Strait Relations Development and the Benefits of Unification' was officially published and released, and has drawn attention. Please introduce the relevant situation.","I believe everyone saw this booklet when entering the press conference venue.\nIn October 2025, Xinhua News Agency published articles under the byline “Zhong Taiwen” on three consecutive days, titled “The Origin and Nature of the Taiwan Question,” “Favorable Conditions for the Development of Cross-Strait Relations and Unification,” and “The Motherland's Unification Is Inevitable and Irresistible,” which drew close attention from compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Recently, the book “Favorable Conditions for the Development of Cross-Strait Relations and Unification,” with the three bylined articles as its core, was officially published and released by Jiuzhou Press. The book is a compilation in both simplified and traditional Chinese characters, accompanied by color illustrations, combining text and images for ease of reading. We hope compatriots on both sides of the Strait will, through this book, further understand the historical development of the Taiwan question, the course of cross-Strait relations, and the bright prospects after the motherland's reunification. We hope they will better understand and support the central government's policies on Taiwan, more actively participate in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and make new and greater contributions to the early realization of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","This June marks the tenth anniversary of the unified China-Europe Railway Express brand. It is understood that many Taiwanese enterprises in Chongqing, Fujian, Jiangsu and other places have shipped their products to Europe via the China-Europe Railway Express, significantly reducing costs and increasing efficiency and expanding Belt and Road markets, and some Taiwanese enterprises have also used Fujian's sea-rail…","With its advantages of speed, low cost, and wide coverage, the China-Europe Railway Express has increasingly become an important channel for mainland Taiwan-invested enterprises to expand into Europe and markets along the Belt and Road. Taiwan enterprises can use the China-Europe Railway Express to achieve efficient end-to-end connections for raw material imports, component distribution, and finished product exports, making order delivery more stable, turnover more efficient, and market expansion faster. For example, Taiwan-invested companies in Chongqing such as Quanta and Inventec used this international logistics corridor to ship goods, reducing the freight time to Europe from nearly two months to 25 days. Taiwan-invested company Compal Group in Fujian used the \"COSCO Star\" ro-ro ship to transport computer components from Taichung Port to Xiamen, and then shipped them to Europe and other places via the \"Taiwan-Xiamen-Chengdu-Europe\" train. This became the first sea-rail intermodal shipment of Taiwan goods in the country, reducing the 40 to 45 days needed for traditional sea transport to 18 days, greatly improving logistics efficiency and saving time costs. As of the end of June this year, the China-Europe Railway Express (Xiamen) had undertaken Taiwan cargo via sea-rail intermodal transport, totaling 418 standard containers equivalent, with a transported value of RMB 224 million.\nGoing forward, we will continue to optimize relevant service guarantees, strengthen customs clearance facilitation, multimodal transport, and customized logistics support, and provide more reliable, economical, and efficient international logistics solutions for Taiwan-invested enterprises. We will empower industries through channels and promote cooperation through openness, help Taiwan enterprise products expand into emerging foreign trade markets, and continuously promote the integration and high-quality development of cross-Strait industries.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","According to reports, TSMC will inject US$20 billion of capital into its US subsidiary to build a 12-inch wafer fab and an advanced packaging plant. This is the sixth time that Taiwan’s economic authorities have approved an investment case by TSMC in its US subsidiary, and so far the cumulative approved investment by TSMC in the United States has reached US$44 billion. This has once again heightened concern on…","The DPP authorities treat TSMC's investment in the United States as a “pledge of allegiance” for “seeking independence by relying on the US,” shamelessly clinging to the US, actively cooperating with the US to seize Taiwan's advantageous industries, and exchanging the abandonment of industrial foundations and the sacrifice of industrial interests for so-called “support.” The further they go down the wrong path, the more the concerns of the Taiwan people will become reality.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","In the first half of this year, the overall market value of Taiwan-invested companies listed on the mainland performed well, drawing attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the listing of Taiwan-invested companies on the mainland.","The Outline of the 15th Five-Year Plan clearly proposes “encouraging Taiwan-invested enterprises that meet the conditions to list on the mainland,” and Taiwan-invested enterprises listing on the mainland already enjoy treatment equal to that of mainland enterprises. In recent years, more and more Taiwan-invested enterprises have chosen to list on the mainland and take root and develop there. The mainland stock market has become an important channel for Taiwan-invested enterprises to conduct direct financing, expand their scale, and enhance their brand image. As of now, 67 Taiwan-related enterprises have listed on the mainland. We will, as always, provide good services for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises. We hope that Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises will fully seize the new opportunities of the mainland capital market, deeply cultivate the mainland market, and achieve a dual enhancement of their own scale and competitiveness.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”和“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, the Mainland dance drama “Only This Blue-Green” (《只此青绿》) was performed in Taiwan and was warmly welcomed by Taiwan audiences. What comments do you have?","From July 2 to 5, the dance drama “Only Such Blue-Green” by China Oriental Performing Arts Group was staged in Taipei. We understand that two performances were added on a temporary basis, bringing the total from five to seven shows. Every show sold out as soon as tickets went on sale, the venue was filled with spectators throughout, the applause was thunderous at the curtain call, and the reviews after viewing were overwhelmingly positive. Taiwan audiences repeatedly praised the production as stunningly beautiful and fully showcasing the depth of Chinese culture. Many audience members were moved to tears, saying, “cultural exchange is excellent” and “you must come back to perform in Taiwan.” I believe everyone has seen many similar videos on social media.\n“Only Such Blue-Green” is drawn from the classic Chinese painting “A Thousand Li of Rivers and Mountains.” Through beautiful, fluid dance and a dreamlike stage presentation, it recreates traditional Chinese aesthetics and revitalizes thousand-year-old Chinese culture. The show has not a single line of dialogue, yet its great sound is silent, reaching hearts directly. This fully demonstrates that Chinese culture is the deepest and most enduring strength of the Chinese nation, and the most empathetic and resonant spiritual bond for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. It fully confirms the words, “We are born as Chinese, and what is most fundamental is that we have the unique spiritual world of the Chinese people.” We hope such cultural exchanges across the Strait will become increasingly frequent, and we are willing to promote more quality performing troupes to visit Taiwan so that compatriots on the island can enjoy world-class performances.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Regarding mainland coast guard ships conducting law enforcement patrols in waters around Taiwan island, the Taiwan Coast Guard Administration said it has advised Taiwanese vessels not to respond to questions from mainland coast guard ships, to report to the coast guard immediately, and to move toward Taiwan coast guard vessels. If the situation becomes urgent, the coast guard will position itself between the two…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. The relevant mainland departments carry out law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters in accordance with the law, which is a just and necessary measure to safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and has been welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan's fishermen. The DPP authorities, out of their political self-interest in seeking independence, are selling out the national interest and disregarding the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan's people, attempting to maliciously hype this up and stir up cross-Strait opposition and confrontation. They will not succeed. If the DPP authorities dare to provoke and stir up trouble, they must bear all the consequences arising from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","According to statistics, as of early July, Fujian had supplied a cumulative total of more than 50 million tons of water to Kinmen, with a 100% water quality compliance rate, which has drawn praise from netizens on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","We have consistently attached great importance to and actively supported the economic and social development of Kinmen, and have continuously taken measures to enhance the interests and well-being of Kinmen compatriots. The Fujian coastal area water supply project to Kinmen officially began supplying water on August 5, 2018, and has been supplying water for nearly 8 years. As of July 1 this year, the Fujian coastal area has cumulatively supplied over 50 million tons of water to Kinmen, accounting for 87% of Kinmen's total daily water supply from its water treatment plants, and the water quality qualification rate has remained stably at 100% year-round. At present, the Fujian coastal area supplies Kinmen with an average of about 22,000 tons of water per day, continuously meeting the water needs of Kinmen compatriots and effectively conserving Kinmen's groundwater. It has relieved urgent needs and eliminated worries for Kinmen's livelihood, security and development, and has been warmly welcomed by Kinmen compatriots. \"Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, sharing the water of one river\": the Fujian coastal area water supply project to Kinmen has become a model of cooperation in cross-Strait livelihood. In the future, we will continue to deliver safe, high-quality and clean water sources to Kinmen, using this river of living water as a bond to bring benefits to cross-Strait livelihoods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","In the first half of this year, the Fuzhou–Matsu “Small Three Links” route saw over 62,000 person-times of entries and exits, a year-on-year increase of over 40%, of which over 55,000 person-times were Taiwan compatriots, a year-on-year increase of 39%. However, requests by Kinmen and Matsu to add flights have consistently not been approved by the DPP authorities. What comments do you have on this?","\"Small Three Links\" passenger shipping routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges and contacts across the Taiwan Strait, especially between the people of Fujian and Taiwan. As of June 30, 2026, the \"Small Three Links\" have safely carried more than 27 million passenger trips. In the first half of this year, the passenger volume on the Fuzhou-Matsu \"Small Three Links\" route was approximately 63,000 trips, an increase of over 40% year on year. The passenger volume on the Xiamen-Kinmen \"Small Three Links\" route exceeded 1 million trips, setting the fastest record for this route to reach the one-million-passenger mark. Compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family, and we welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland via the \"Small Three Links\" routes to take a look around, seek their roots and pay respects to ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchanges and cooperation. The DPP authorities should put the well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait first, lift all artificial restrictions as soon as possible, and increase \"Small Three Links\" flights in line with the travel and exchange needs of people on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic and trade activities.","To implement the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchange and cooperation that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee was authorized to issue, from July 2 to 4 the Shenzhen Taiwan Investors Association organized more than 10 Taiwan-invested businesses to exhibit at the 2026 High-End Food and Quality Agricultural Products (Shenzhen) Expo. They displayed Taiwan’s distinctive fresh seafood, traditional pastries, Nangang special baozhong tea, Taiwanese snacks and meals, and more than 20 product categories such as wax apples and pineapple sugar apples, helping Taiwan agricultural and fishery products expand sales channels on the mainland.\nFrom July 7 to 12, the 14th Yunnan-Taiwan Economic, Trade and Cultural Exchange and Cooperation Symposium was held in Kunming, Yunnan Province, and other places. This session of the “Yun-Tai Meeting” took “Sharing RCEP New Opportunities, Creating a New Situation for Integrated Development of Yunnan and Taiwan” as its theme. It aims to give full play to Yunnan’s advantages in resources, location, and openness, continuously guide Taiwan-invested businesses to make full and good use of the RCEP policy dividends, and deepen economic, trade, and cultural exchange and cooperation between Yunnan and Taiwan. About 900 people attended, including more than 600 Taiwan guests.\nAt the same time, the 17th Tianjin-Taiwan Investment and Cooperation Negotiation Conference was held in Tianjin. This session of the “Jin-Tai Meeting” took “Gathering Wisdom for New Development, Sharing New Opportunities” as its theme. It aims to continuously promote economic and trade exchange and cooperation between Tianjin and Taiwan, and deepen the economic and social integrated development of Tianjin and Taiwan. Its program included an opening ceremony, a Tianjin-Taiwan artificial intelligence industry cooperation and exchange meeting, a Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Taiwan health industry exchange meeting, and industry matchmaking and site visits. About 350 people attended, including cross-Strait entrepreneurs, political and business figures, and Taiwan youth, among whom about 280 were Taiwan guests.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","As summer arrives, cross-Strait exchanges are becoming increasingly active.\nFujian has long been at the forefront of cross-Strait exchanges. From June 29 to July 3, the Fifth Anniversary of the Two National Standards for Taiwanese-Style Oolong Tea and the Zhangzhou-Taiwan Tea Farmers Vocational Skills Competition were held in Pinghe, Longyan. More than 60 tea experts and tea enterprise representatives from both sides of the Strait conducted in-depth exchanges on the implementation results of common standards for the cross-Strait tea industry and paths for integrated development. From July 1 to 9, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Yong'an) Youth Basketball Series was held in Yong'an, Sanming. More than 200 Taiwanese young people competed in basketball with local peers and took part in activities including the Fujian-Taiwan family “Seeking Flavors in Yan City” and practical study tours. From July 3 to 5, more than 600 Taiwan compatriots came to Meizhou Island in Putian to carry out the activity of walking around the island's 15 Meizhou Mazu temples to pay respects to the ancestor and burn incense. From July 3 to 9, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Jianyang) Youth Tea Bowl Culture Exchange Event was held in Jianyang, Nanping. More than 230 cross-Strait tea bowl industry representatives and young people conducted in-depth exchanges on topics including establishing industry alliances and jointly cultivating talent. During the same period, the 14th Straits Youth Gathering · 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Sports Study Tour was held in Mawei, Fuzhou. More than 200 cross-Strait young people visited study bases including the Shipbuilding Museum and the thousand-year-old Min'an Ancient Town, and took part in sports competitions, cultural visits, themed study tours and other activities. On July 3, the 2nd “Ming-Taiwan Cup” Cross-Strait Youth Baseball Tournament began in Ninghua, Sanming. More than 70 cross-Strait young baseball players competed on the same field, made friends through the game, and savored Hakka cultural heritage during study tours in the Hakka ancestral homeland. On July 6, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Zhangzhou) Summer Youth Exchange Season was launched in Zhangzhou. Nearly 1,000 Taiwanese young people were invited to take part in 17 colorful summer youth study activities. From July 8 to 12, the 2026 Cross-Strait Persons with Disabilities Exchange Carnival, co-hosted by the China Disabled Persons' Federation together with the Fujian Provincial Disabled Persons' Federation and others, was held in Xiamen and other places. It included a series of activities such as the cross-Strait “Co-Creating Technology for Welfare” exchange and sharing session, cultural and sports exchanges for persons with disabilities, and rehabilitation exchanges. During this period, the Several Measures of the China Disabled Persons' Federation on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for the Integrated Development of Cross-Strait Disability Affairs will be released. It comprises 13 measures in 3 areas, to support Fujian in leveraging its unique advantages toward Taiwan and its pioneering, pilot and demonstration role; to implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots with disabilities in Fujian; and to promote substantive progress in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in rehabilitation services, the assistive device industry, technology for assisting persons with disabilities, cultural and sports affairs, and volunteer services.\nOn July 3, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Anhui) Youth Exchange Season opened in Hefei. Thirteen exchange events will be held at multiple locations across Anhui Province, including a Hui Culture Summer Camp, an e-sports carnival, baseball games, and a lighting design roadshow. More than 500 representatives of cross-Strait youth and various sectors took part.\nOn July 4, the two-week “Same Source Notes — Sea Gathering Training Camp” opened in Shanghai. It covers baseball, e-sports, performing arts, creativity, and skills modules, and includes the Cross-Strait Baseball Culture Festival, the Cross-Strait E-sports Culture Festival, the Cross-Strait Original Ecological Arts Festival, and the “Magic City Experience Tour.” More than 500 Taiwanese young people took part. On the same day, the 2026 Poetry City Fengjie Chongqing-Taiwan Youth Poetry Gathering was held in Fengjie, Chongqing. Nearly 400 cross-Strait young people went together to the summit of the Three Gorges, visited Baidi City, revisited classic poems by masters such as Li Bai and Du Fu, and jointly experienced the charm of Chinese classical poetry.\nFrom July 4 to 12, the 2nd Qingdao Taiwan Food and Creative Culture Carnival was held in Qingdao, Shandong. Using food and creative culture as its vehicle, it linked cultural experiences, youth interaction and the integration of culture and tourism, and used the warmth of everyday life to deepen the friendship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. On July 6, the “Hand in Hand, Set Sail, Dreaming of the Deep Blue” Straits Cross-Strait Youth Sailing Experience Camp opened in Qingdao. More than 400 Taiwanese young people took part, sailed together with mainland youth, experienced sailing, and appreciated the unique charm of the “Sailing Capital” and the “Beer City.”\nOn July 7, the “Moon City” Cross-Strait (Yangzhou) Youth Cultural and Creative Week opened in Yangzhou, Jiangsu. More than 380 young cultural and artistic workers from Taiwan joined local youth in taking part in the Same Source Notes Yangzhou-Taiwan Youth Lawn Concert, the Straits Cross-Strait (Yangzhou) Youth Cultural and Creative Selected Exhibition, the “Sharing This Bright Moon, Seeing Artists Through It” Yangzhou-Taiwan Contemporary Art Joint Exhibition, the “Same Source Gathering” cross-Strait artists' painting gathering, and the Yangzhou Intangible Cultural Heritage Experience Tour, among other activities.\nOn July 10, the 2026 Henan Province Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Month and the Straits Cross-Strait Youth Taekwondo Exchange Competition will be launched in Zhengzhou. More than 500 youth representatives from various sectors in Taiwan will carry out taekwondo competitions, pickleball exchanges, cultural study, vocational education and other activities with local youth, visit the Four Ancient Capitals, tour modern enterprises, and take part in study and internship programs. On the same day, the 20th Hubei · Wuhan Taiwan Week opened, and will host more than ten events, including the Cross-Strait (Wuhan) New Energy and Intelligent Connected Vehicle Industry Integration Development Exchange Conference, the Straits Cross-Strait (Hubei) College Students' Jingchu Culture Tour, and the Hubei-Taiwan Workers and Family Culture Exchange.\nIn addition, cross-Strait exchanges between universities are also heating up with the arrival of summer vacation. Shandong University, Chang'an University, the Xi'an Academy of Fine Arts and many other universities have each launched the 2nd “Straits Art Rhythm · Youth Chord” Cross-Strait Youth Art Workshop and similar activities, inviting Taiwanese young students to come together.\n“Learning alone without friends leads to isolation and little knowledge.” We believe that deep exchange and mutual learning among cross-Strait youth will surely lead to common growth and mutual achievement. Though the mountains and seas are far apart, where one is determined to go, one will surely arrive. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots to visit and exchange in the mainland, to admire the magnificent landscapes of our rivers and mountains, witness the new face of China, and feel the warmth of mainland compatriots, as warm as summer.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","南方日报、南方+记者","According to Reuters, the DPP authorities recently held a so-called “whole-of-society defense resilience exercise” in Nantou County, testing whether mountainous counties and cities could still maintain normal operations if attacked by the mainland. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately persist in their “Taiwan independence” stance. To collude with external forces in plotting “independence” and provoking confrontation, they incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation, and they are the chief culprits behind tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. Their large-scale push for “everyone a soldier” and their willingness to tie Taiwan residents to the “Taiwan independence” chariot seriously harm the safety and well-being of Taiwan residents. Before the powerful People's Liberation Army, no matter how many drills the DPP authorities stage, they are only putting on a show and their efforts are futile. They cannot change the fate of “Taiwan independence” being doomed to fail, and they cannot stop the historical trend of the motherland's inevitable reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视记者","Taiwan’s foreign affairs authorities recently said they have amended the so-called “Measures for Encouraging Businesses to Invest in Countries with Diplomatic Relations,” broadening the scope of subsidies, raising the airfare subsidy for visiting “allies” to NT$100,000, and substantially increasing the maximum cumulative subsidy within seven years from NT$20 million to NT$60 million. What is your comment on this?","Previously, Lai Ching-te, disregarding face, made a furtive visit to Eswatini in exchange for a 25 billion New Taiwan dollar investment pledge and exorbitant travel expenses. The Lai authorities, acting as a “money-scattering boy” externally, have given large amounts of Taiwan’s hard-earned money away to so-called “diplomatic allies,” while domestically disregarding the economic and livelihood welfare of the island’s people. They have no real intention or ability to solve the island’s economic and livelihood problems, and now they are even disguisedly mobilizing businesses to hollow out Taiwan further. This thoroughgoing “sugar daddy diplomacy” harms Taiwan and its people, is a laughingstock, and is despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Former Japanese media figure Akio Yaita was recently attacked in Taichung by a Hong Kong person, who has been arrested. Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council and foreign affairs departments said, “This is the first cross-border suppression case since the Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress took effect, and it is suspected that foreign forces are exploiting the convenience of Hong Kong people’s…","First question. This Hong Kong man acted out of righteous indignation, and the incident was an accidental, ordinary public-order case. The DPP authorities took the opportunity to engage in political manipulation, forcibly linking and distorting the Ethnic Unity and Progress Promotion Law, with the aim of stirring up cross-Strait confrontation and misleading and intimidating the Taiwan public. Their despicable conduct is not even endorsed by the people on the island. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities not to infringe on this Hong Kong man's legitimate rights and interests, and they must ensure his personal and property safety is protected from harm.\nSecond question. When governance is stable, public sentiment is stable, and people cannot be driven away even if one tries. When governance is chaotic, public sentiment is chaotic, and people cannot be kept even if one tries. Since taking office, the DPP authorities have continuously pursued “independence” and provoked confrontation, escalated their suppression and persecution of dissenters, plunged Taiwan's society into division and confrontation, and placed Taiwan's compatriots under “green terror.” As a result, the Taiwan Strait has become dangerous and war-prone, and Taiwan's people live in anxiety. Some Taiwan residents have chosen to emigrate or move their assets abroad. This is a normal risk-avoidance step and reflects their deep concern about the “Taiwan independence” provocations.\n“Taiwan independence” not eliminated, Taiwan will not be at peace. We hope the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the essence and harm of the DPP authorities' pursuit of “independence.” Starting from their own safety, interests and well-being, they should resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and work to maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260708_12775126.htm"],[2,"2026-07-08","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”记者","First question: US President Donald Trump recently mentioned Taiwan's semiconductors again, saying that Taiwan has taken almost 100% of America's chip business and that “Taiwan's situation is somewhat fragile.” He threatened that before leaving office he would let the United States hold 40% to 60% of chip production capacity. The island is worried that the Taiwan Strait situation is being manipulated and that…","First question. The DPP authorities, with no bottom line, shamelessly curry favor with the United States and sell out Taiwan. What they receive in return is nothing but the United States pushing for more and squeezing Taiwan dry. If TSMC becomes “US-TSMC,” it will lead to the wholesale relocation abroad of talent, technology, and capital across upstream and downstream sectors. That would become “the last straw that breaks the camel’s back” for Taiwan’s industry, and it is the broad masses of Taiwan residents who would be harmed.\nSecond question. The so-called claim that “some of the precursor raw materials mainly come from the mainland” is pure nonsense. The DPP authorities’ incompetence in governance has led to rampant drugs on the island, yet they keep shifting blame and evading responsibility. Their intentions are sinister and utterly shameless.\nI want to stress that the country firmly cracks down on drug crimes, especially drug crimes involving the two sides of the Strait. We will severely punish drug criminals and will absolutely not show leniency or softness.\nToday’s press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260708_12775135.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-07-09","Mao Ning","AFP","Media outlets in Taiwan are reporting that China’s recent long-range submarine launch missile test was actually fired from the sea surface south of Guangdong rather than from underwater. Does the foreign ministry have a comment on this?","We have stated our position on the test launch on multiple occasions. I don’t have anything further to add.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260709_11978719.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260709_11978521.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-07-09","Chen Xi","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, while attending the graduation ceremony of a Taiwan military academy, Lai Ching-te said Taiwan will continue to strengthen foreign arms procurement and defense self-reliance. Recently, Taiwan's navy also adjusted and formed the “Coastal Operations Command.” What comments do you have on this?","Lai Ching-te has been clamoring for “seeking independence through force” and “seeking independence by relying on external forces,” once again exposing his true face as a “destroyer of peace” and an “instigator of war.” No matter what Lai says or does, it cannot change the military balance across the Taiwan Strait, nor can it stop the historical trend toward the inevitable reunification of the motherland. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; reunification is the right path. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will clearly see the extreme danger and harmfulness of the DPP authorities’ stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist line, and join us in resolutely combating “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, opposing interference by external forces, and jointly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477740.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 15, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first announced the holding of the 9th Straits Youth Development Forum and the 6th Straits Youth Culture Month, and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear journalist friends, good day everyone. Welcome to the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/closing)","","First, two announcements.\nThe 9th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum will be held from July 17 to 21 in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, and other locations. On the morning of July 17, the forum's opening ceremony and the launch ceremony of the Zhejiang-Taiwan Youth Exchange Season will be held in Hangzhou. Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang of China and chairperson of the Chinese Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, has been invited to attend the forum. Guests from relevant parties on both sides of the Strait and youth representatives from all sectors, about 1,000 people in total, will take part in the forum's related activities. Media reporters are welcome to visit and report.\nThe 6th Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month opened on July 15 in Suzhou, Jiangsu. Under the theme “Together in Unity, the Power of Youth,” with “new expressions of traditional culture” as the main thread, this Culture Month builds an interactive and experiential exchange platform for young people on both sides of the Strait, promoting exchange, interaction, and integration among cross-Strait youth. The activities will run from mid-July to late September. During this period, more than 40 main-venue supporting events and more than 30 branch-venue events will be held, covering culture and arts, technological innovation, sports competitions, intangible cultural heritage study tours, and more. These include the Cross-Strait Film and Television Development Exchange Conference, the “Guofeng Hanfeng” Chinese cultural series of exchange activities, the Cross-Strait Mei Lanfang Art and Culture Week, and the Huang Gongwang-themed Cross-Strait Cultural and Creative Competition, creating a cultural carnival belonging to cross-Strait youth. We warmly welcome young people from both sides of the Strait to participate actively, to appreciate the timeless charm of excellent traditional Chinese culture together, and to gain joy, friendship, and rich rewards through mutual exchange and learning.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776670.htm https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776672.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Reports say a youth exchange delegation of the Taiwan People’s Party arrived in Shanghai on the 14th for a visit and exchange. Which places will this delegation visit during this trip? What is the Taiwan Affairs Office’s comment on the delegation’s visit to the mainland?","From July 14 to 17, a youth exchange delegation of the Taiwan People’s Party visited Shanghai for exchanges. The delegation toured the Yangshan Port, the 12345 Citizen Service Hotline Operation Center, and the Sihang Warehouse Anti-Japanese War Memorial, and held a discussion with young teachers and students of Shanghai Jiao Tong University. We welcome the delegation’s visit, will make appropriate arrangements for related activities, and will provide the necessary convenience.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture, and are one family with blood ties. They should naturally visit each other often and draw closer to one another. We warmly welcome compatriots in Taiwan, especially young people from Taiwan, to visit the mainland more often to see and experience it for themselves, to appreciate its magnificent landscapes, to feel its cultural heritage, to experience its trendy lifestyle, and to join us for a youthful appointment and create a better future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776669.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Counting the third geng day after the summer solstice marks the first fu period, and today is the first day of the fu period. During the midsummer season, cross-Strait youth exchange activities are diverse and colorful.\nFirst, sports exchange activities allow cross-Strait youth to fully release their energy. From July 7 to 11, the Fuzhou-Taiwan Inter-School Youth Football Friendly Exchange Event was held in Fuzhou, with more than 150 teachers and students from six middle schools in Fuzhou and Taiwan participating. Most of the Taiwanese players were young members of ethnic minorities who were coming to the mainland for the first time. From July 9 to 14, the 14th Straits Youth Gathering 'Ice and Snow Bond' 2026 Cross-Strait (Fujian) Youth Land Curling Summer Camp and the 11th Cross-Strait (Fujian) Youth Rugby Exchange Tournament were successively held in Fuzhou, with more than 300 cross-Strait youths making friends through sports and engaging in in-depth exchanges. On July 9, the 6th Taekwondo Competition of the 2026 Longyan Municipal Mass Fitness Sports Games and the Longyan-Taiwan Taekwondo Exchange Event were held in Longyan, with 111 cross-Strait youth athletes competing on the same stage and making friends through martial arts. From July 13 to 26, the 2026 Straits (Putian) Sports Series was held in Putian, covering multiple events including youth football, basketball, taekwondo, and wushu. Among them, the university basketball competition featured 16 cross-Strait university basketball teams.\nSecond, music and dance exchange activities bring more beautiful enjoyment to cross-Strait youth. From July 11 to 13, the 2nd Straits Cross-Strait Folk Culture and Sports Gathering, 'Drum Rhythms Spread Across the Four Seas, Chaozhou Sentiments Unite Both Sides of the Strait,' Chaozhou Drum Music Cultural Exchange Event was held in Chaozhou, Guangdong. More than 160 Taiwanese youths and mainland drum music enthusiasts jointly held drum music flash mobs and performances, and also experienced folk culture from the Chaoshan region, including the Yinggeh dance. From July 19 to 20, the '2026 Zhangzhou-Taiwan Youth Study and Practice Exchange Event, Dance Rhythms United in Heart, Feelings Connect Both Sides of the Strait,' will be held in Zhangzhou City, Fujian, inviting more than 60 Taiwanese youths to Zhangzhou for singing and dancing performances and exchanges with local peers of the same age. From July 20 to 25, Wenzhou, Zhejiang, will host the Cross-Strait Banpingshan Southern Min Music Season, including a Southern Min music gathering, a short video competition, performances by Taiwanese young musicians, and a cross-Strait youth experience camp. More than 400 Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese youths will participate, jointly inheriting and promoting Southern Min culture.\nThird, food and short video exchange activities let cross-Strait youth experience more good things. On July 12, Zhuhai held the first 'Taiwan Connection, Zhuhai Affection' Taiwanese Food Carnival, with more than 600 cross-Strait compatriots participating. Classic Taiwanese snacks such as braised pork rice, oyster noodles, and large intestine wrapped in small intestine were gathered on site, and a Zhuhai Taiwanese Food Map was released, allowing cross-Strait compatriots to fully experience the taste memories that share the same roots. Those who go to Zhuhai can follow the map and check in at the 17 Taiwanese food restaurants listed on it one by one. From July 14 to 17, the grand final of the 8th 'Fun in Guangdong' Cross-Strait Youth Creative Short Film Competition was held in Zhongshan, Guangdong. Themed around commemorating the 160th anniversary of the birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen, the competition received more than 800 works, and 20 cross-Strait teams advanced to the final, including 10 Taiwanese teams, helping cross-Strait youth passionate about creative film and television engage in in-depth exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic and trade activities.","From July to August, a series of 2026 Qiong-Tai Cooperation Week activities will be held in Haikou, Hainan Province, and other locations. Themed “Two Islands with One Heart and Moving Forward Together, Qiong-Tai Integrating and Winning Together,” the events will include a launch ceremony, the Qiong-Tai Economic and Trade Cooperation and Exchange Meeting, the Cross-Strait Leisure Agriculture Development (Hainan) Seminar, Qiong-Tai youth employment and entrepreneurship exchange activities, Qiong-Tai in-law ties, and 10 sub-events in total. Around 600 people, including Taiwan business leaders, heads of key Taiwan-funded enterprises, and representatives of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth, will take part. The activities will help deepen integrated development across Qiong-Tai fields and help Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises share the development dividends of Hainan's free trade port.\nFrom July 12 to 15, the 2026 Guizhou-Taiwan Economic and Trade Exchange and Cooperation Forum will be held in Guiyang, Guizhou. Themed “Seize New Opportunities of Integration, Create a New Future for Industries,” this edition of the “Qian-Tai Meeting” will feature a series of targeted industrial matchmaking activities, youth innovation and entrepreneurship exchange activities, and characteristic cultural activities. More than 200 Taiwan entrepreneurs, industry experts, and young elites will visit Guizhou for exchanges. The activities aim to build an integrated platform for industrial matchmaking, youth interaction, and cultural fellowship, and to improve the quality and efficiency of economic and trade cooperation and grassroots exchanges between the two places, bringing them forward in a practical and substantive way.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Although the DPP authorities have tried in various ways to intimidate Taiwan residents into not coming to the mainland, the willingness of Taiwan residents to come to the mainland for exchanges has continued to rise in the first half of this year. The number of participants in many cross-strait exchange activities has repeatedly hit record highs, and many Taiwan youths are discussing whether “coming to the…","Visits by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland have indeed become increasingly popular. According to statistics from the National Immigration Administration, from January to June this year, cross-Strait personnel exchanges totaled 3.119 million person-times, an increase of 22.1% year on year, of which Taiwan compatriots visiting the mainland accounted for 2.85 million person-times, an increase of 24.9% year on year.\nThese data fully demonstrate that wanting peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The lie fabricated deliberately by the DPP authorities that “the mainland is dangerous” has long since collapsed on its own. More and more Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, have already planned or are planning to travel or exchange on the mainland, measuring the vast and magnificent rivers and mountains with their feet, feeling the brilliant and splendid Chinese civilization with their hearts, observing the thriving economy and technology with their eyes, and experiencing the fraternal affection of mainland people and the everyday warmth found everywhere with their emotions.\nSeeing is believing. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for exchanges and visits, study tours and internships, employment and entrepreneurship, sightseeing and tourism, and business inspections, and we will provide more convenience and create better conditions for this. With summer vacation arriving, Taiwan compatriots, especially young students, can head to various parts of the mainland: riding horses across the grasslands of the frontier to take in the emerald sky where “when the wind blows, the grass bends low, revealing cattle and sheep,” strolling through the water towns of Jiangnan to savor the cultural codes of “a thousand li of orioles singing, green set off by red,” traveling thousands of li across the Gobi of the northwest to feel the majestic grandeur of “the bright moon rising over the Tianshan Mountains,” and cooling off on the black soil of Northeast China to experience the northern scenery of “clouds cool and breeze clear, summer heat naturally subsides.” A trip to the mainland is not only worthwhile, but more than worth it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776667.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","The State Administration for Market Regulation recently announced that over the past two years or so, both sides of the Strait have jointly developed and implemented 378 cross-Strait common standards, involving multiple fields including characteristic agricultural products, modern service industries, food, new energy, and culture and tourism. These have fully played the role of “soft connectivity” of relevant…","In September 2023, Xinhua News Agency was authorized to publish the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” (hereinafter the “Opinions”), which comprehensively deployed support for Fujian's construction of a cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone. Since the release of the “Opinions,” the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission, together with the State Administration for Market Regulation and other relevant central and state organs, have steadily promoted the implementation of the key tasks of the “Opinions” in detail, and achieved interim progress in supporting Fujian in building a cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone with high quality.\nCross-strait standards that are mutually compatible and effective promote the integration of cross-strait industries, markets and talent, and are an important component of building the cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone. In 2023, the State Administration for Market Regulation took the lead in issuing special support measures, focusing on “soft connectivity” of standards, supporting Fujian in systematically carrying out cross-strait standards compatibility in building the cross-strait integrated development demonstration zone, exploring new models and mechanisms for cross-strait standards compatibility, and forming a pattern of integrated development of “joint standard development, shared markets, and interconnected talent.”\nFirst, it pioneered a working mechanism of “four joints and three adoptions,” namely jointly selecting topics, jointly comparing, jointly developing, and jointly using compatible standards: mainland advanced standards are adopted by Taiwan, Taiwan advanced standards are adopted by the mainland, and standards in blank fields are jointly developed by both sides across the Strait and adopted. This removes technical barriers in the circulation of goods and technical cooperation.\nSecond, it innovatively launched cross-strait standards compatibility pilot projects, promoting 75 pilot projects in fields such as machinery manufacturing, modern services, and folk culture, of which 11 pilots, including architectural design, dragon fruit cultivation, and tea-industry study tours, have achieved application results in Taiwan.\nThird, it supported the issuance of the “Fujian Province Regulations on Promoting Cross-Strait Standards Compatibility,” building a comprehensive, full-chain legal system for standardization related to Taiwan.\nFourth, it built a cross-strait standards compatibility service platform, which contains 6,047 pieces of comparative information on cross-strait terminology standards, providing “one-stop” services for cross-strait industry, academia, research institutions and enterprises.\nSince the release of the “Opinions,” the results of cross-strait standards compatibility have continued to expand. Industry, academia and research institutions on both sides of the Strait have jointly developed and implemented 378 compatible standards, the standard system continues to improve, and application scenarios have extended to multiple dimensions such as industry, trade and culture, playing a positive role in promoting social integration, economic integration and emotional integration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, the head of Taiwan's economic department said that, as the geopolitical situation changes, “non-red supply chains” have become an international trend. He hopes to promote the “de-redding” of five major industries on the island, establish closer supply chain links with global democracies, and even form an ecosystem to strengthen resilience. What is your comment on this?","The so-called “non-Red supply chain” is a political manipulation that some countries draw lines based on ideology. It seriously violates economic and market laws, undermines the stability of the world economy, disrupts normal international trade, and also harms the island’s economic development. Driven by its nature of seeking “independence,” the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have tagged along with the noise and actively cooperated. On the one hand, they have tried hard to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation; on the other hand, they have groveled before external forces, selling off Taiwan’s advantageous industries and handing over their economic development autonomy. But what they have done has only brought ever more unscrupulous extraction and plunder from their “foreign masters,” and what is harmed is the interests and future of Taiwan’s enterprises and people.\nThe mainland has a complete industrial system, an open, super-large market, abundant innovation resources, and a resilient supply chain network. It is the main engine of global economic growth, a focal point for global capital investment, and a fertile ground where Taiwan businesspeople can invest, develop, and grow. According to statistics from the General Administration of Customs, from January to June 2026, total cross-Strait import and export trade was about US$185.03 billion, up 25.3% year on year. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$51.884 billion, up 32.9% year on year, and mainland imports from Taiwan were US$133.154 billion, up 22.5% year on year. This fully proves that cross-Strait industrial and supply chain cooperation continues to deepen, and that cross-Strait economic integration and development continue to strengthen. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are stubbornly pushing for cross-Strait “decoupling and supply chain cutoff.” Their reckless actions will only lift a rock only to drop it on their own feet.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776660.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","A DPP politician claimed that the mainland is changing the status quo across the Taiwan Strait through various military and non-military actions, and that the international community should closely watch the mainland's actions, otherwise the current status quo across the Strait will gradually disappear. What is your comment?","The claims made by DPP politicians completely distort the facts and are purely malicious hype. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities' use of the “new two-state theory” to define the so-called “status quo across the Taiwan Strait” completely violates law, history, and reality, and is an outright “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacy. Their obstinate insistence on the “Taiwan independence” position, refusal to recognize the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the One-China Principle, and continual collusion with external forces to provoke “independence” are a destruction of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the greatest source of chaos for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace in the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. Only by resolutely cracking down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and opposing foreign interference can we deter the risk of “Taiwan independence” adventurism, truly safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and uphold the common interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776668.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, Guangxi, Hubei, Gansu and other places have suffered wind and flood disasters. Have Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises been affected? Could you introduce the relevant situation?","Recently, Guangxi, Hubei, Gansu and other places have been hit by extreme weather such as heavy rainfall and strong winds, triggering floods and geological disasters that have caused major casualties and economic losses. General Secretary Xi Jinping issued important instructions on flood control and disaster relief work, and relevant departments and localities have thoroughly implemented the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important instructions and are fully engaged in emergency rescue and disaster relief work.\nWe attach great importance to flood control and disaster relief work for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland. We immediately surveyed the disaster situation of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in the affected areas, and simultaneously launched various efforts including emergency rescue, resettlement, relief, and support. According to our understanding, Taiwan compatriots in Guangxi, Hubei, and Gansu are all safe, and some Taiwan-funded enterprises in Guangxi have suffered economic losses to varying degrees. The Taiwan Affairs Office is working with the Guangxi authorities to actively help affected Taiwan-funded enterprises overcome difficulties and resume production and operations as soon as possible.\nWe note that, affected by Typhoon \"Bavi,\" residents in many parts of Taiwan have been hit by the disaster. We extend our condolences to the affected compatriots in Taiwan and sincerely hope they will quickly restore normal production and daily life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776658.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, KMT Chairperson Cheng Li-wun said in Penghu County that Penghu has outstanding natural landscapes and cultural heritage, but its development has been restricted in recent years. She called for a full restart of the “Mini Three Links” so that Penghu, like Kinmen and Matsu, can welcome mainland tourists, which she said is the key to reviving tourism. What is your comment?","The 'Small Three Links' (Xiao San Tong) is the livelihood channel and kinship route connecting people on both sides of the Strait. As of June 30, 2026, the 'Small Three Links' has safely transported more than 27 million passenger trips in total, including more than 1.15 million passenger trips in the first half of this year alone, injecting strong momentum into the development of Taiwan's tourism industry.\nTourism is an important carrier of a good life and a natural bridge promoting exchanges. We have carefully listened to the opinions and suggestions of all sectors in Taiwan and actively promoted the resumption of tourism to Kinmen and Matsu by residents of Shanghai and Fujian, which has been warmly welcomed by the Taiwan public. As of now, the cumulative number of tourist trips to Kinmen and Matsu by residents of Shanghai and Fujian has exceeded 300,000.\nWhen Penghu is mentioned, everyone thinks of 'Grandma's Penghu Bay,' the Shuangxin Stone Fish Weirs of Qimei Island, and the Penghu Tianhou Temple. Mainland residents are very willing to travel throughout Taiwan, including Penghu. The main obstacle now is that the DPP authorities, on various untenable pretexts, interfere with and obstruct mainland residents' tourism to Taiwan, artificially blocking the channel for the recovery of the cross-Strait tourism market. We advise the DPP authorities to put the interests of people on both sides of the Strait first and lift restrictions on mainland residents' tourism to Taiwan as soon as possible.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776662.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, it was revealed on the island that soybean salad oil was found to exceed the limit for the carcinogen “benzo[a]pyrene,” which has raised concerns in Taiwan society about food safety regulation and other issues. What is your comment?","Food concerns people's livelihood, and food safety is the bottom line of people's wellbeing. “Benzo(a)pyrene” has been listed by the World Health Organization as a Group 1 carcinogen, and more than 3,900 tons of problematic oil have flowed onto the dining tables of numerous households, schools and restaurants, seriously endangering the lives and health of the people of Taiwan. Faced with such a major food safety incident, the DPP authorities have delayed handling it and attempted to “cover up” and conceal information, which fully exposes their ugly face of disregard for people's livelihoods.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776661.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The Ministry of Culture and Tourism recently issued the “15th Five-Year Plan for Building a Tourism Powerhouse,” stating that it will promote tourism exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and strengthen exchanges among young people on both sides. What steps will be taken next to promote cross-Strait tourism cooperation?","The 《Plan for Building a Strong Tourism Nation during the 15th Five-Year Plan Period》 proposes to advance tourism exchange and cooperation across the Taiwan Strait and to strengthen youth exchanges between the two sides. This points the way for upgrading the cultural tourism industry in the new era and provides a solid basis for deepening cultural tourism exchange and cooperation across the Strait.\nMountains and seas as the medium, culture and tourism as the bridge. Tourism is a natural bond that connects the hearts of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Through mutual visits and exchanges, compatriots on both sides personally experience shared culture, common roots and beautiful scenery. Tourism also concerns economic livelihood: cross-Strait tourism exchange can fully drive income growth in Taiwan's catering, transportation, cultural and creative industries, relieve the operating difficulties of practitioners on the island, and enhance the well-being of the industry and the public.\nWe will continue to promote cross-Strait tourism cooperation, open two-way tourism channels across the Strait, use tourism to bring compatriots closer emotionally, and cultivate cultural identity across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that, due to the mainland's “cultural and military intimidation” of Taiwan in recent years, the Taiwan military this week held its first “joint defense exercise,” simulating “threat scenarios such as detecting enemy takeoffs and entry into territorial waters” to respond to possible potential threats. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities, attempting to “use military force to seek independence” and escalate cross-Strait confrontation, are the chief culprits behind the tension and turbulence in the Taiwan Strait. In the face of the powerful People’s Liberation Army, no matter how many drills the DPP authorities hold, they are merely putting on a show and their efforts are futile. They cannot change the doomed fate of “Taiwan independence,” nor can they stop the historical trend toward the inevitable reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776657.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, the European Parliament passed a report on the geopolitical situation in East Asia, stating its opposition to any conduct that unilaterally changes the status quo through coercion. Taiwan's foreign affairs department expressed gratitude for this. What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The relevant report by the European Parliament crudely interferes in China's internal affairs, and we firmly oppose it. We urge the European Parliament to immediately correct its erroneous words and actions on Taiwan and to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.\nThe DPP authorities' attempt to win over external forces to endorse their provocative acts of seeking “independence” is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Reference News published an article titled “Silicon Valley Senses ‘Winds of a New Cross-Strait Situation Rising,’” pointing out that the Taiwan Strait issue is becoming a hot topic in Silicon Valley and attracting attention. Some Silicon Valley investors have said that China and the US have no reason to go to war, and that Taiwan will be gradually unified by the mainland within 10 to 20 years. The…","Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all sons and daughters of China. The motherland must be reunified and will inevitably be reunified; this is a historical trend that no person or force can stop. Cross-Strait reunification is not only an inevitable requirement for the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, but will also surely provide more reliable guarantees for the peaceful development of the world and inject stronger momentum into global economic and trade cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, the foreign ministers of the United States, Japan and South Korea met and stressed the importance of maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and “expressed concern over increasingly frequent acts around Taiwan that undermine stability.” They encouraged the peaceful resolution of cross-Strait issues and opposed any attempt to unilaterally change the status quo. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no outside interference is permitted. There is only one China, and the mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China; this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The relevant actions carried out by mainland authorities around the island of Taiwan are just measures to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity and the overall interests of the Chinese nation. Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle, stop making remarks on the Taiwan question, and stop sending any wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Reportedly, Zhang Xue, chairman of Zhang Xue Motorcycles, said in an interview that he very much wants to open a store in Taiwan, no later than next year. He promised that his future Taiwan motorcycle owners will enjoy exactly the same after-sales service as mainland owners, and expressed his desire to ride around the island of Taiwan. What Zhang said has been well received by netizens on both sides of the…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We are willing to share good mainland products with compatriots in Taiwan, and to support two-way investment and cooperation between enterprises on both sides for win-win outcomes. We hope industries on both sides will fully leverage their respective strengths, deepen exchanges and cooperation, better serve the people on both sides, and ensure that people on both sides can buy and use good-quality products at reasonable prices.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Lai Ching-te recently said, “According to statistics from 2024 through the end of June this year, 374 Taiwan residents have gone missing, been detained for questioning, or had their personal freedom restricted after going to China. People should avoid going to China if there is no necessity.” What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated lies and maliciously hyped issues, attempting to create a “chilling effect” and intimidate Taiwan’s public. This fully exposes their sinister intention of deliberately obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel in order to pursue “independence.”\nWe have consistently encouraged and supported cross-Strait exchanges in all fields, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. Since 2024, more and more Taiwan compatriots have come to the mainland for exchange visits, study and employment, sightseeing, business inspection and other purposes, totaling over 11.7 million person-trips. The facts fully demonstrate that as long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots can come to the mainland happily and return safely. They also prove that the lies and schemes of the DPP authorities are being seen through by more and more Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","During the 2026 U.S.-Canada-Mexico World Cup, several cinemas in Fujian launched live broadcast services for World Cup matches, attracting many Taiwan compatriots to come and watch the games alongside mainland football fans. Public opinion points out that this move gave Taiwan fans an excellent experience and has also made civil exchanges across the Strait increasingly warm and vivid. What is your comment on this?","The 2026 FIFA World Cup is a festive feast for football fans around the world. The World Cup has now entered the semifinals, and the tournament is in its final sprint. We welcome Taiwan compatriot football fans to come to the mainland to watch matches. In the mainland, they can watch live broadcasts anytime and anywhere using mainland television, internet, apps and other platforms. They can also go to cinemas showing live World Cup broadcasts to experience the passion of the football field together with mainland compatriots, and enjoy the convenient life services and vibrant development of the mainland. After the World Cup, Taiwan compatriot friends can also watch in person the Min Super League, Su Super League, Yue Super League, Northeast Super League and Chuan Super League, fully experiencing the charm of football and the wonderful cultural tourism of various localities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260715_12776659.htm"],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question. The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that within the past ten days, 10 Taiwan residents went missing after traveling to the mainland. May I ask whether the Taiwan Affairs Office and relevant mainland departments know the specific whereabouts of these 10 Taiwan residents? Could it involve telecommunications fraud, criminal offenses, or simply missing-person cases? In addition, the Mainland…","First question. The Mainland Affairs Council fabricated and deliberately spread false information in an attempt to mislead Taiwan’s public. This is completely untenable. Media friends have no need to make unfounded speculation about it.\nIt is an undeniable fact that compatriots in Taiwan enjoy safe, comfortable, convenient and pleasant travel experiences when they tour the mainland and visit relatives and friends. The DPP authorities deliberately smear, intending to create panic, obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and personnel exchanges, and escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation. Their conduct is despicable, and their intentions are deserving of condemnation.\nSecond question. Cross-Strait direct air links are an important air bridge connecting the kinship of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and facilitating economic, trade and cultural exchanges, carrying the urgent needs of people’s exchanges. In the first half of this year, 3.1378 million passenger trips were made across the Strait on direct air passenger flights, a year-on-year increase of 15%. This fully confirms the strong demand of the cross-Strait direct flight market and the strong desire of people on both sides to visit each other.\nWe actively promote the full restoration of normal cross-Strait direct air links. This position is consistent and clear. We hope the Taiwan side will face up to the actual demand for cross-Strait direct air passenger links, heed the wishes of the people, and promptly lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport, so that cross-Strait airlines can arrange flight schedules independently according to market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-15","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Taiwan recently exposed a toxic oil problem, and now there are suspicions of a “toxic apple” issue. The DPP authorities plan to relax the fipronil residue standard for apples by six times, and the island has questioned whether this is linked to the United States. Taiwan's Food and Drug Administration responded that it has nothing to do with the United States. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities have completely disregarded the health and well-being of the Taiwan public and openly abandoned the bottom line of food safety. From opening the market to “Lai pork,” “Lai beef,” “poisonous potatoes,” and “poisonous apples,” they have time and again used the lives and health of the public as a “pledge of loyalty” to curry favor with the US, attempting to exchange support from external forces for their “seeking independence” conduct. The DPP authorities’ reckless and wanton conduct is unpopular and will surely be despised.\nThe press conference is now over. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260715_12776655.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-07-20","Lin Jian","Shenzhen TV","It is reported that on July 17, Taiwan’s “foreign affairs office” decided to remove Cambodia from visa facilitation programs, saying that Cambodia had failed to reciprocate Taiwan’s goodwill and instead echoed China in supporting the one-China policy. Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation responded that Cambodia viewed Taiwan as a province of China. Its commitment to the one-China…","Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is a prevailing consensus in the international community. By exploiting people-to-people facilitation measures to coerce other countries, the DPP authorities’ moves constitute a blatant challenge to the one-China principle, a basic norm in international relations, and once again lay bare the malignant nature of their “Taiwan independence” separatist agenda. The firm commitment of the Cambodian government to the one-China principle fully proves that the DPP authorities’ separatist playbook finds no support and will lead nowhere.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260720_11986625.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260720_11986571.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-21","Lin Jian","Beijing Youth Daily","Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul concluded his official visit to China. Can you share more details on his visit?","From July 16 to 20, Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul paid an official visit to China and attended the 2026 World AI Conference. President Xi Jinping held a meeting with Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul. Premier Li Qiang and Chairman Zhao Leji held talks and met with him respectively. The two sides had in-depth exchanges of views on China-Thailand relations and international and regional issues of mutual interest, and reached wide consensus. During his visit, the two sides released the Joint Statement between the Government of the People’s Republic of China and the Government of the Kingdom of Thailand towards a China-Thailand Community with a Shared Prosperous Future. There are three highlights of the visit.\nFirst, firming up mutual support. The two sides agreed to speed up the establishment of a China-Thailand community with a shared future for enhanced stability, prosperity, and sustainability, and make full use of the China-Thailand 2+2 strategic dialogue mechanism co-chaired by foreign ministers and defense ministers to elevate strategic coordination to new heights. China supports the new government of Thailand in its governance. Thailand reaffirms the unwavering commitment to the one-China policy, firmly supports China’s peaceful reunification and will not support any call for the independence of Taiwan.\nSecond, deepening mutually beneficial cooperation. Thailand welcomes China’s initiative to establish the World AI Cooperation Organization and stands ready to work with China to strengthen international cooperation and global governance on AI. The two sides agreed to advance high-quality Belt and Road Initiative, speed up the construction of the China-Thailand high-speed railway and other key projects, expand cooperation in emerging areas such as aerospace, new energy vehicles, and clean energy and resolutely crack down on cross-border crimes including online gambling and telecom fraud. Prime Minister Anutin also traveled to Sichuan province to attend the China-Thailand Investment and Economic Forum and the Inauguration Ceremony of the Thailand Board of Investment of the Thailand’s Consulate General in Chengdu. The two sides have also signed 10-plus cooperation documents on science and technology, AI education and combating cross-border crimes.\nThird, carrying out closer multilateral coordination. Thailand appreciates and welcomes the four global initiatives put forward by President Xi Jinping, as the initiatives demonstrate China’s commitment to multilateralism. Both sides will firmly safeguard the UN-centered international system and the international order underpinned by international law, and strengthen coordination and collaboration under multilateral mechanisms such as the UN, APEC, China-ASEAN cooperation and the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation.\nThrough the visit, China is ready to deepen strategic communication with Thailand, strengthen synergy of our development strategies, and expand practical cooperation so as to produce more outcomes in developing China-Thailand relations and better benefit the two countries and two peoples.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260721_11989141.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260721_11989097.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 22, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Please begin asking your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","人民日报社记者","During the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month activities, Song Tao, Director of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, announced the launch of the “Taiwan Youth e-Home” platform, which provides Taiwan youth with information on internships, study, employment, entrepreneurship and other opportunities on the mainland. It has drawn wide attention and praise from Taiwan youth and public opinion on the island. Please…","To clear and smooth the channels through which Taiwanese youth come to the mainland for exchange, study, internships, and employment, and to better serve the integrated development of cross-Strait youth, the “Taiwan Youth e-Home” service platform was officially launched on July 15 on the China Taiwan Network. Focusing on the needs of Taiwanese youth, the platform sets up four sections: Internships, Job Search, Exchanges, and School Selection. It also sets up special zones for provincial and municipal information, policy information, exchange activities, life guides, and experience sharing by Taiwanese youth, providing one-stop services for Taiwanese youth.\nAmong them, the “Internships” and “Job Search” sections compile information on internship and employment positions offered by the mainland to Taiwanese youth, consolidated and updated in real time, so that Taiwanese youth can search online and apply with one click, efficiently connecting with the employment needs of all parties. The “Exchanges” section centrally publishes information on cross-Strait youth study programs, visits, social practice, entrepreneurship training, and other exchange activities, making it convenient for Taiwanese youth to sign up promptly. The “School Selection” section integrates information such as admission policies for Taiwan students at key mainland universities, application channels, and introductions to majors, providing guidance for Taiwanese youth who aspire to pursue higher education on the mainland. The “Experience Sharing by Taiwanese Youth” zone includes real cases, practical insights, and life-sharing from Taiwanese youth studying, interning, working, and starting businesses on the mainland, directly showing the development environment on the mainland from the perspective of Taiwanese youth, and answering questions and providing reference for Taiwanese youth.\nWe welcome broad numbers of Taiwanese youth to regularly use and make good use of the “Taiwan Youth e-Home” service platform to learn about internship and employment positions, cross-Strait exchange activities, and university admissions information, to draw on the growth experiences of Taiwanese youth on the mainland, and to actively seize the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization, eagerly coming to the mainland to study, pursue internships and employment, and put down roots to develop. In the future, we will continue to enrich the platform's resource supply and iteratively optimize its functions, continuously improving the refinement and convenience of services, supporting more frequent exchanges and deeper integration between young people on both sides of the Strait, jointly promoting cross-Strait integrated development in greater depth and substance, so that more young Taiwanese can benefit from it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778249.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the 9th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum was held in Zhejiang. Please introduce the relevant results.","From July 17 to 21, the 9th Straits Forum for Youth Development across the Taiwan Strait was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province. Song Tao, Director of the Central Taiwan Work Office of the Communist Party of China and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Wang Hao, Secretary of the Zhejiang Provincial Committee of the Communist Party of China and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Zhejiang Provincial People's Congress; and Hung Hsiu-chu, former Chairperson of the Kuomintang and Chairperson of the Chinese Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, attended the opening ceremony of the forum and delivered speeches. More than 1,000 guests from both sides of the Strait and youth representatives from all sectors gathered together. Centered on the forum theme “Growing Up Together in Youth, Building the Future with One Heart,” they exchanged views, built consensus, and achieved positive results.\nThe number of Taiwan youth participating in this forum reached a record high. The forum carried out study camps and other activities in Ningbo, Wenzhou, Huzhou, and other places. Youth from both sides learned from and inspired each other, walked hand in hand with a shared heart, went into cities and villages, schools and communities, explored the poetic and picturesque scenery of Jiangnan and its green waters and green mountains, touched cutting-edge technologies such as AI and robotics, deepened understanding and friendship, and together encouraged each other on national missions, shared youthful ideals, and created a better future.\nWe will continue to thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's congratulatory letter to the sixth Straits Forum for Youth Development across the Taiwan Strait, continue to successfully hold the Straits Forum for Youth Development across the Taiwan Strait and other exchange activities, provide more opportunities for the growth and success of youth on both sides of the Strait, encourage youth on both sides to bravely shoulder the responsibilities of the times and become firm promoters of exchange and integration, steadfast guardians of our common home, and resolute advancers of national rejuvenation, and inject more youthful strength into promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778250.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, cross-Strait youth exchange activities such as the Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month and the Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum have been held one after another. Summer is precisely the busy season for youth exchange activities and for internships and employment of Taiwan youth and students. Please introduce the positive measures the mainland has taken to promote exchanges and interaction between young…","For a long time, we have practiced the concept of “Cross-Strait Families Are One Family,” and have continuously improved policy measures to benefit the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. We provide greater convenience for Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, to study, live, work, and start businesses on the mainland, helping Taiwan youth pursue, build, and realize their dreams on the mainland. In April this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office was authorized to issue ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. On July 15, Director Song Tao attended the activities of the 6th Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month and announced that the nationwide unified online service platform for Taiwan youth, “Taiqing e-Jia” (台青e家), has gone live. It provides full-chain information services for Taiwan youth friends in areas such as exchange, study, internships, and employment. As of now, many Taiwan youth have visited and registered, and we hope everyone will make good use of the “Taiqing e-Jia” service platform to better take root and develop on the mainland.\nAt present, the mainland is comprehensively implementing the 15th Five-Year Plan and actively advancing the building of Chinese-style modernization. The broad land holds great potential, and now is the right time to work and build. More and more Taiwan youth friends are crossing the Strait and coming to the mainland to strive hard for their dreams. We warmly welcome more Taiwan youth friends to come to the mainland for exchanges and development, to find their life direction, and to realize their life ideals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","新华社记者","The DPP held its National Congress on July 19. Lai Ching-te, leader of the Taiwan region who also serves concurrently as DPP chairperson, once again advocated separatist remarks such as cross-Strait “mutual non-subordination” at the congress, loudly exaggerated the mainland's “threat” to Taiwan, and clamored that he would never allow “democratic Taiwan” to become “Chinese Taiwan.” May the spokesperson please…","Lai Ching-te made outrageous and boastful remarks at the Democratic Progressive Party's National Congress. His entire speech was filled with hostility and conflict, lies and slander, obstinacy and arrogance, once again exposing that his \"Taiwan independence\" stance is intransigent, that he is provocative with radical and risky actions, and that he is stubbornly bent on harming and destroying Taiwan. This fully proves that Lai Ching-te and the Democratic Progressive Party are the root of trouble undermining the stability of cross-Strait relations and social peace in Taiwan, the source of turmoil threatening peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and in the region, and are unmistakably \"peace wreckers,\" \"war instigators,\" and \"troublemakers.\"\nShortly after its founding, the Democratic Progressive Party embarked on the wrong path of \"Taiwan independence\" separatism. In the decades that followed, it deliberately plotted \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, attempting to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait in which both sides belong to one China. It is a thoroughgoing \"Taiwan independence party.\" In the past decade, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have become even more single-minded in \"seeking independence by relying on foreign powers\" and \"seeking independence through force,\" causing the situation across the Taiwan Strait to become increasingly tense and turbulent. In this speech, Lai Ching-te once again propagated the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist fallacy, advocated \"mutual non-subordination between the two sides of the Strait,\" and recklessly challenged the one-China principle, thoroughly tearing off his so-called disguise of \"there is no 'Taiwan independence' issue\" and revealing his true face as a \"Taiwan independence worker.\" Since taking office, Lai Ching-te has vigorously pursued a \"green terror,\" strenuously curbed freedom of speech, abused the judiciary to suppress political opponents, arbitrarily persecuted forces supporting the development of cross-Strait relations, and brutally violated the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan's people in participating in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. A person who tramples on democracy, undermines freedom, and damages the rule of law is so shameless as to boast about democracy and freedom and clamor about \"democracy versus authoritarianism\"; it is truly shameless. In short, Lai Ching-te has become a \"scourge of Taiwan,\" and the Democratic Progressive Party has become the greatest \"group harming Taiwan,\" which has aroused strong dissatisfaction among the people on the island.\nTaiwan is Taiwan of China and has never been a country; it was not in the past and it will absolutely not be in the future. The Taiwan question is a legacy of the Chinese Civil War of the 1940s. No matter how the election in the Taiwan region is conducted or whom it elects, it cannot change Taiwan's status as part of China, cannot sever the historical and legal connection that both sides of the Strait belong to one China, and cannot break the iron rule that Taiwan's future can only be decided jointly by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. We uphold the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, resolutely combat \"Taiwan independence\" separatism, and safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. The great trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland is vast and irresistible!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778251.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, a youth exchange delegation of the Taiwan People’s Party visited and exchanged views in Shanghai. It was the party’s first formal delegation to the mainland since its founding, and it stated that it hopes to use exchange to build goodwill and to replace confrontation with dialogue. What is your comment on this?","From July 14 to 17, a youth exchange delegation of the Taiwan People’s Party visited Shanghai for exchanges. The delegation toured economic development projects, historical venues, technology companies, and youth innovation and entrepreneurship bases, and held a discussion with teachers and students of Shanghai Jiao Tong University. The delegation was warmly received and welcomed by the relevant parties.\nPeace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots across the Strait are one family with blood ties, and they should visit each other often and draw closer to one another. This is the general trend of history, and no force can stop it. Compatriots on both sides should join hands, follow the trend of history, strengthen exchanges and cooperation in all fields, advance the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, and jointly create a bright future for cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Recently, Chu Jung-tai, head of the Taiwan region's executive authorities, said at an event of the “Asia Taiwan Chambers of Commerce General Federation” that Taiwan has revised its past dependence on the “Chinese single market,” shifting toward Europe, the United States, and Southbound countries. He also said a support platform has been set up for Taiwanese businesses investing around the world. What is your comment?","In the first half of 2026, cross-Strait trade reached US$185 billion, of which mainland imports from Taiwan were US$133.1 billion, a year-on-year increase of 22.5%, and mainland exports to Taiwan were US$51.9 billion, a year-on-year increase of 32.9%. This fully demonstrates that the industrial structures on both sides of the Strait are complementary and that cooperation prospects are broad. Strengthening cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and deepening cross-Strait integrated development accords with the common interests of compatriots and enterprises on both sides, and is also the result of economic laws and market principles acting together. Cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and mutual benefit and win-win outcomes cannot be stopped by anyone.\nIn order to “rely on outsiders to seek independence,” the DPP authorities shamelessly sell out Taiwan, fawn on external forces, and pledge allegiance, catering to outside forces in hollowing out Taiwan’s advantageous industries. This is an out-and-out act of harming Taiwan and bringing disaster upon it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778247.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, a Taiwan compatriot was involved in a traffic accident near Irkutsk Oblast, Russia. After learning of it, the Chinese Consulate General in Irkutsk immediately assisted the injured in going to a local hospital for treatment, and visited and comforted the injured Taiwan compatriot. What is your comment on this?","It is understood that recently, a tour group of compatriots from Taiwan was involved in a traffic accident near Irkutsk Oblast, Russia. After receiving a request for help from Taiwan compatriots late at night, the Consulate General of the People’s Republic of China in Irkutsk immediately coordinated with local hospitals to dispatch ambulances to provide assistance, and visited and expressed condolences to the Taiwan compatriots who were seriously injured. At present, the condition of the injured Taiwan compatriots is stable.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. Providing consular protection and assistance to Chinese citizens abroad, including Taiwan compatriots, is our responsibility. Wherever compatriots have expectations and needs, the care and protection of the motherland will follow. We will continue to shield our compatriots from wind and rain and help them resolve their difficulties, so that every Chinese person can feel the warmth and strength of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778248.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that it will regularly publish data on residents who go missing or are detained on the mainland, reminding the public to carefully assess before traveling to the mainland and to “not go if they don't have to.” What is your comment on this?","According to statistics from the National Immigration Agency, from January to June this year, cross-Strait personnel exchanges totaled 3.119 million person-trips, up 22.1% year on year, of which trips by Taiwan compatriots to the mainland totaled 2.85 million, up 24.9% year on year. More and more compatriots from Taiwan are coming to the mainland for exchanges and visits, study and employment, and tourism and sightseeing. We lawfully protect the life, property, and legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland, so that compatriots from Taiwan can travel safely and smoothly between the two sides of the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities disregard the facts and fabricate lies, repeatedly rehashing so-called data on missing persons in an attempt to create a “chilling effect,” deceiving and intimidating the Taiwan public, in order to restrict cross-Strait exchanges and sever the family ties between compatriots on both sides. Their conduct is shameful and their intentions are wicked.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778246.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, the Papua New Guinea government announced the closure of the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Office in Papua New Guinea.” Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities expressed protest. What is your comment?","We express high appreciation for the relevant measures taken by the government of Papua New Guinea. Facts have repeatedly proven that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and that adhering to the one-China principle is what justice requires and what the trend of the times demands. Those who have the right way have much help; those who lack the right way have little help. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, going against the tide of history, and will only find themselves hitting walls everywhere in the international community.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778245.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","Regarding the Philippines’ recent deliberate provocation at Ren’ai Jiao, violently attacking Chinese law enforcement personnel, and then distorting and hyping the incident afterward, Taiwan’s foreign affairs authority actually echoed this, saying it “condemns the mainland for using force to injure people,” and opposes any attempt or action to unilaterally change the status quo through force, coercion, or…","Regarding the Philippines’ deliberate provocation and attack on China Coast Guard law enforcement personnel at Ren’ai Jiao, the relevant departments clarified the facts at the first opportunity, released on-site footage, and made solemn representations to the Philippine side.\nRen’ai Jiao is part of China’s Nansha Islands and is Chinese territory. The DPP authorities have abandoned their national standpoint, echoed external forces in confusing right and wrong, and attacked and smeared the mainland. Once again, this has exposed their evil nature of forgetting their roots and ancestors and “seeking independence by relying on external support.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778243.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the Cross-Strait Artificial Intelligence Integrated Development and Innovation Forum was held during the 2026 World Artificial Intelligence Conference, attracting attention from industry on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 2026 World Artificial Intelligence Conference Cross-Strait Artificial Intelligence Integrated Development and Innovation Forum and exhibition activities will be held in Shanghai from July 17 to 20. This series of activities is co-hosted by the Straits Economic and Technological Cooperation Center and other units, with the theme “Leading the New Journey with Intelligence, Integrating and Innovating for the Future.” It centrally showcases the achievements of cross-Strait AI cooperation and deeply explores paths for integrated development.\nAmong them, the cross-Strait forum invites about 150 representatives from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait to take part in thematic dialogues focusing on AI empowering advanced manufacturing and healthcare, and jointly promoting technological breakthroughs, industrial synergy and ecosystem co-building. The cross-Strait exhibition area invites more than 20 representative AI enterprises from both sides of the Strait to exhibit, centrally showcasing the development achievements and cutting-edge technological breakthroughs in key links of the cross-Strait AI industrial chain. We warmly welcome Taiwan businesspeople to take part in similar activities, to embrace broader development opportunities on the mainland as they integrate into the new development pattern.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Regarding the Taiwan People’s Party’s first group visit to the mainland, the Mainland Affairs Council said: “We do not oppose political parties engaging in exchanges on the mainland, but they should maintain equal dignity and not echo the CCP’s narratives or propositions. The Taiwan Affairs Office did not emphasize ‘the 1992 Consensus and opposition to Taiwan independence’ during the TPP’s visit to the mainland…","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" and strive to obstruct dialogue and communication across all sectors of cross-Strait society and exchanges and interactions in all fields. They are completely on the opposite side of the historical trend and mainstream public opinion, and will inevitably be scorned and fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Reports say TSMC will increase its investment in Arizona, USA by US$100 billion, and is expected to build four more wafer fabs and an advanced packaging plant. This has again triggered concerns on the island that TSMC is becoming “TSMC America” and that Taiwan's semiconductor industry will be hollowed out. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities' “relying on the US to seek independence” and “kneeling to the US and selling out Taiwan” are the chief culprits behind the damage to Taiwan's economy and the gradual loss of Taiwan's advantages. For their political self-interest, they sell out the interests of industry and hollow out the economic foundations of Taiwan. Those harmed include not only the future of industry but also the livelihoods of the broad Taiwanese public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Regarding the “Zhang Xue motorcycles” hoping to open a store in Taiwan, Taiwan’s Ministry of Economic Affairs said that under the current customs import tariff rules, motorcycles (complete vehicles) made in mainland China fall under the “mainland goods not permitted for import” category and, by law, cannot be imported into Taiwan. What is your comment?","As “Zhang Xue” motorcycles continue to achieve excellent results in professional events around the world, more and more compatriots in Taiwan have expressed their wish to ride “Zhang Xue” motorcycles and personally experience the progress of mainland technology. We are pleased to see Taiwan compatriots using good products from the mainland and sharing the development achievements of Chinese-style modernization.\nWe urge the DPP authorities to heed public opinion, lift unreasonable restrictive measures as soon as possible, and do more practical and good deeds that benefit the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Recently, cross-Strait exchange activities have been colorful and varied.\nIn youth exchanges: From July 8 to 12, the 7th Cross-Strait Youth Mazu Culture Study Camp was held in Putian, Fujian. From July 12 to 15, the 4th Rong-Taiwan Youth Handball Exchange Event was held in Fuzhou, Fujian, with cross-Strait teenagers forming 10 handball teams to compete and exchange. From July 13 to 20, the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Medical Culture Exchange Summer Camp was held in Jiangsu, Zhejiang and Shanghai. From July 14 to 17, the 2026 Rong-Taiwan Youth Study Tour Camp was held in Fuzhou, Fujian. From July 18 to 25, the 2026 Cross-Strait College Students' Basketball Competition was held in Putian, Fujian. On July 22, the 3rd “Rong Guotuan Cup” Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao Youth Table Tennis Exchange Event was held in Zhuhai, Guangdong, with about 300 young people from across the Taiwan Strait and the Hong Kong and Macao regions participating.\nIn economic and trade exchanges and cooperation: From July 15 to 18, the first “Lan-Taiwan Intellectual Property Special Exchange Event: Wisdom Connects Lan-Taiwan to Create the Future, Intellectual Property Builds a Bridge for Integration” was held in Pingtan, Fujian. On July 19, the 12th Strait Tea Gathering and the Cross-Strait Beauty Tea Culture Exchange Event was held in Sanming, Fujian.\nIn cultural and sports exchanges: On July 12, the “Silk Road Strings, Yellow River Music — Gansu-Shanghai-Taiwan Concert of 100 Young People” was held in Lanzhou, Gansu. More than 500 Taiwan youths, 12 visiting delegations and young students from 8 universities in Lanzhou gathered on the banks of the Yellow River and played the harmonious movement of “Cross-Strait Family Ties.” From July 12 to 16, the 22nd Cross-Strait Book Fair was held in Taipei, with 60 mainland book publishers and library collection units attending and exhibiting about 20,000 mainland books. On July 11, the opening ceremony of the 2026 Cross-Strait Inter-University Alliance Basketball Competition (Lanzhou Stop) was held in Lanzhou, Gansu. On July 12, the 2nd Hang-Taiwan Genealogy Airing Day was held in Shanghang, Longyan, Fujian. Nearly 100 cross-Strait surname culture inheritors, genealogy researchers and clan representatives exchanged views and discussed deepening cross-Strait exchange on Hakka genealogy culture. On July 16, the 2026 Cross-Strait Chinese Character Culture Series of Activities was held in Xiamen, promoting the inheritance and innovative integration of Chinese character culture. From July 19 to 22, the 2nd Cross-Strait (Jiaocheng) Harmonica Culture Week was held in Ningde, inviting nearly 300 Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwanese harmonica world champions, well-known bands and harmonica enthusiasts.\nIn grassroots exchanges: From July 2 to 8, the “Enjoy the Mountains and Seas, Meet in Hunan” Cross-Strait Grassroots Exchange Event was held in Loudi, Hunan. It included the 3rd Cross-Strait Ethnic Minority Music Festival and several other distinctive activities, and more than 300 compatriots from Taiwan came to take part.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The 2026 Taipei Summer Travel Fair recently opened. The Taipei Office of the Cross-Strait Tourism Exchange Association exhibited under the dual themes “Travel Following Cultural Relics” and “Travel Following Gourmet Food,” which was welcomed by the Taiwan public. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From July 17 to 20, 2026, the Taipei Office of the Straits Tourism Exchange Association participated in the 2026 Taipei Summer Travel Fair. Under two concentrated themed exhibition areas, “Travel Following Cultural Relics” and “Travel Following Gourmet Food,” it showcased new mainland formats of cultural and tourism integration, creating an atmosphere with culture as its soul and everyday life as its charm. This exhibition area promoted resources such as cultural relic derivatives and local specialty foods, showing Taiwan compatriots the new immersive, everyday style of mainland tourism, and allowing them to experience up close the new charm of mainland travel, where “cultural relics lend depth and food lends warmth.”\nThe Taipei Office, together with the National Museum of China, launched the “Travel Following Cultural Relics” themed exhibition area, displaying more than 50 cultural and creative products across 9 major themed series, including the “National Museum Yanyi” Haiyan Heqing Zun series and the Four-Ram Square Zun series. Relying on the Chinese cultural lineage, these products highlight that cross-Strait compatriots share the same roots, culture, and ancestry. Together with the Anhui Provincial Department of Culture and Tourism, the Taipei Office launched the “Travel Following Gourmet Food” themed exhibition area. It recreated a Huizhou-style ancient architectural scene, used realistic food models to restore Huizhou cuisine banquets, and paired these with a display of the Huizhou fish lantern intangible cultural heritage. Through the cross-disciplinary integration of “architecture + food + intangible cultural heritage,” it lets Taiwan compatriots understand the regional culture behind the food and immersively experience the everyday charm of mainland cultural tourism.\nAt the same time, the Taipei Office also set up a mainland cultural tourism resources area, a Hanfu experience area, a mainland aviation area, a consultation area for Taiwan compatriot permit applications, and a stage promotion area. It invited nine mainland airlines, including Air China, China Eastern, and China Southern, as well as the Straits Friendship Travel Agency and the magazine “Travel Reader” to exhibit, so that Taiwan compatriots can obtain comprehensive, multi-level information and services for traveling to the mainland.\nCultural relics carry the cultural lineage of cross-Strait common roots and shared culture and ancestry, and food links the everyday warmth of compatriots on both sides who are bound by blood. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland and personally experience its upgraded travel offerings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan's “Central Election Commission” stated, regarding candidate eligibility for the “nine-in-one” elections, that if former residents of the mainland apply to register as candidates, it will check whether they have submitted proof of loss of original nationality annotation, and whether they have been registered as residents in Taiwan for 10 years. Commentators on the island point out that this is a…","The mainland and Taiwan belong to one China, and compatriots on both sides are one family. There is fundamentally no so-called “nationality” issue. Mainland spouses are relatives of Taiwan compatriots and builders and contributors to Taiwan society, and they should rightly be recognized and respected.\nOut of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have for a long time arbitrarily suppressed and bullied the mainland spouse community, and have increasingly restricted their political participation rights in Taiwan. This is unpopular and will inevitably meet with unanimous opposition from compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","According to reports, the “Cross-Strait Young Teachers' Northern Frontier Tour” activity has drawn attention on the island after being accused of involving “united front” work. The island's education authority said it has repeatedly sent letters reminding schools that they must not violate relevant regulations, that it will strictly vet the activity, and that it will continue to supervise schools to pay attention…","The DPP authorities routinely pin labels on normal cross-strait educational exchanges and put up obstacles, and in recent years they have grown increasingly extreme. These measures include prohibiting Taiwan institutions from exchanging and cooperating with Jinan University, Beihang University, and 8 other schools on the mainland, and requiring Taiwan institutions to report on their faculty and students’ exchanges to the mainland, among others. All of these actions aim to manipulate “anti-China resistance” and create “green terror.”\nWhy is the DPP authorities so afraid of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland for exchanges? Simply put, they fear that people will learn about the mainland’s real development and expose the false narratives they have deliberately fabricated, and break the information cocoons they have laboriously built.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently said that one active-duty police officer and one retired police officer, during a trip to Fujian in June this year, were forcibly taken away from their guesthouse by mainland national security personnel for isolated interrogation, and were pressed about Taiwan's critical infrastructure and their past work. After returning to Taiwan, the two asked the Mainland Affairs Council…","We have consistently encouraged and supported exchanges and interactions across all fields between the two sides of the Strait, including tourism, and we protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law. Taiwan compatriots have been coming to the mainland for sightseeing and travel, exchange visits, study and employment, and business inspection. Since 2024, the cumulative total has reached more than 11.7 million person-times.\nThe DPP authorities, for their own political self-interest, have consistently and maliciously hyped up, fabricated rumors about, and smeared the mainland, attempting to create a “chilling effect.” Their aim is to obstruct cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and escalate cross-Strait confrontation. This does not win popular support and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Reportedly, the head of Taiwan's defense department recently said that he calls for the passage through the executive branch of the draft drone regulations to drive the development of related industries and form a \"non-red supply chain\" that does not rely on the mainland. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” stance, deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation, continuously obstruct and undermine cross-Strait economic exchanges and cooperation, and fabricate various pretexts to forcibly “decouple and break supply chains” with the mainland. Their aim is to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on foreign powers.” More and more Taiwan compatriots have recognized the essence of the DPP authorities' “Taiwan independence” and its serious harm, and they refuse to pay for “Taiwan independence” actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","The Taiwan newspaper Liberty Times reported that regarding the review of drone regulations by Taiwan’s legislative body, there are rumors that the mainland is “pulling strings” for the blue and white camps on the island. What is your comment?","This green media outlet has long recklessly fabricated rumors and smeared the Mainland. In cooperation with the DPP authorities, it suppresses dissenters and incites confrontation, and it has no credibility whatsoever.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","The Taiwan authorities said that because Cambodia voiced support for One China, they canceled the so-called “visa” convenience measures for Cambodia. In response, the Cambodian government said that Cambodia has always regarded Taiwan as a province of China and will not change its position of adhering to the One China principle. What comments do you have on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. The firm stance of the Cambodian government conforms to the trend of history and the wishes of its own people, and once again shows that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities' attempt to coerce relevant countries into providing space for “Taiwan independence” is overestimating their own strength and miscalculating. Their base scheme is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260722_12778244.htm"],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, Hong Kong police conducted searches of certain bookstores in accordance with the law. Lai Ching-te posted on social media, “No country should fear people reading, nor should it suppress freedom of speech in this manner. Continue to pay attention to Hong Kong, and express support for anyone who supports freedom of speech and defends democracy.” What is your comment on this?","The relevant departments of the Hong Kong SAR government have already issued an explanation on this matter. The persons concerned violated Hong Kong law. The SAR government's taking action against them is legitimate, lawful, and entirely justified.\nSince the Hong Kong National Security Law took effect, under high-level security protection, Hong Kong's social order has been restored and its spirit of the rule of law has been upheld. The rights and freedoms that Hong Kong residents enjoy under the law have been fully protected, and the strong vitality and superiority of “One Country, Two Systems” have been fully demonstrated. The relevant laws and regulations target only a very small number of criminals who endanger national security. Safeguarding national security is safeguarding Hong Kong's democracy and freedoms, and safeguarding the human rights and well-being of all Hong Kong citizens. Any scheme that undermines the process by which Hong Kong moves from order to prosperity, or that aims to create chaos in Hong Kong and contain China, is doomed to fail.\nThe DPP authorities are vigorously carrying out a “green terror” on the island, a “fake democracy, real dictatorship,” which has already aroused strong public dissatisfaction. Yet out of their nature of seeking “independence,” they still, under the banner of so-called “democracy and freedom,” twist black and white, maliciously attack and smear Hong Kong's rule of law, and threaten and intimidate the people of Taiwan. Their real aim is to incite “anti-China” and “resist-China” sentiment and to undermine cross-Strait relations. Their intentions are sinister, and their conduct is despicable and shameless.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","Recently, bookstores in Hong Kong were investigated by law enforcement authorities. In recent years, the mainland side has repeatedly stressed its hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will jointly promote Chinese culture. Some Taiwanese public opinion has questioned whether “the right to define Chinese culture” and how it is promoted are limited to what the mainland’s official authorities determine?","The issue you raised has no connection with Chinese culture, and inciting division and turmoil has never been advocated by Chinese culture. On the contrary, Chinese civilization has outstanding unity; Chinese people at home and abroad, including compatriots on both sides of the Strait, have firmly forged the shared conviction that the territory cannot be divided, the country cannot be in chaos, the nation cannot be scattered, and civilization cannot be broken.\nHong Kong is a society governed by the rule of law, where laws must be observed and violations must be prosecuted. Relevant persons violated relevant laws of Hong Kong, and the Hong Kong SAR government took action against them, which is legitimate, lawful, and a matter of course. Since the implementation of the Hong Kong National Security Law, under high-level security protection, Hong Kong society’s order has been restored and the spirit of the rule of law has been upheld. The rights and freedoms enjoyed by Hong Kong residents in accordance with law have been fully protected, and the strong vitality and superiority of “one country, two systems” have been fully demonstrated.\nOut of its nature of pursuing “independence,” the DPP authorities have repeatedly colluded with those who disrupt Hong Kong, maliciously attacking and smearing the rule of law in Hong Kong, with the aim of inciting “anti-China and resist-China” and undermining cross-Strait relations. Their intentions are sinister.\nWhat I want to emphasize is that the successful practice of “one country, two systems” in Hong Kong must not be subject to rumor-mongering and sabotage by any force, and no evil acts of disrupting Hong Kong or pursuing “independence” will succeed. We sincerely hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will work together in harmony, move forward hand in hand, jointly promote cross-Strait integration and exchanges, and jointly advance the complete reunification of the motherland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","According to reports, a serving police officer and a retired police officer from Taiwan were questioned by mainland national security personnel while traveling in Fujian in June. Earlier, a Taiwan judge, while traveling in North China, was questioned at his hotel by public security personnel about work matters, including differences between the cross-Strait judicial systems. What is your comment on whether…","I must emphasize that we adhere to governing the country according to law, attach great importance to the building of the rule of law, protect the various rights and freedoms enjoyed by the people in accordance with the law, and safeguard the lives, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots, in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have absolutely no need to have any concerns about coming to the mainland. Since 2024, the cumulative number of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland for sightseeing, exchange visits, study and employment, and business inspections has exceeded 11.7 million person-times. Among them were judicial and police personnel who came to travel, visit relatives and friends, and all of them, as long as they abided by the rules and laws, came happily and returned safely.\nDriven by political self-interest, the DPP authorities have consistently and maliciously hyped up, fabricated rumors, and defamed the mainland, creating a “chilling effect.” The aim is to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions and to escalate cross-Strait confrontation. This does not win popular support and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Regarding the visit to Shanghai by the Youth Exchange Delegation of the Taiwan People's Party, Li Wei-hua, Chairperson of the TPP Central Evaluation Committee who led the delegation, said during the visit: “I hope today is the starting point of understanding and the beginning of more cooperation in the future.” This coincides with the Taiwan Affairs Office's emphasis that “family members should visit each other…","From July 14 to 17, a youth exchange delegation of the Taiwan People's Party visited Shanghai for exchanges. The schedule was tight and the content was rich. They visited economic construction projects, historical venues, technology companies, and youth innovation and entrepreneurship bases, and also engaged in in-depth exchanges with teachers and students of Shanghai Jiao Tong University, discussing youth and responsibility together. We believe that all members of the delegation gained a great deal and that the trip was worthwhile.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and are a family united by blood. Frequent visits and exchanges, and getting closer to one another, are natural and a trend of the times that no force can stop. In the face of the complex and grave situation in the Taiwan Strait, cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation must not stop, must not be cut off, and must not diminish. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should join hands, work together to overcome interference and remove obstacles, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the well-being of compatriots and kinship, and jointly create a bright future for cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Regarding the list of Taiwan residents reported missing after traveling to the mainland, which the Mainland Affairs Council recently published, as of now, have the Straits Exchange Foundation, the Mainland Affairs Council, or the relevant police system formally transferred the so-called “missing persons” list and related police report materials to the relevant mainland authorities through existing…","Question one. As is widely known, the DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” and refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, which has seriously affected the implementation of the cross-strait agreements between the two associations. Recently, the DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated so-called missing-person data without presenting specific evidence. The purpose is to mislead public perception and deceive and intimidate Taiwan residents. We have always, in accordance with the law, safeguarded the lives, property, and lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots. The statistics on Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland in the first half of this year are sufficient to prove that the scheming of the DPP authorities has not succeeded.\nQuestion two. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” stance, continuously escalate discriminatory trade restrictions against the mainland, go to ever greater lengths to set up obstacles, and maliciously obstruct and undermine the normal exchanges and cooperation in cross-strait economic and trade relations. Taiwan’s traditional industries and small and medium-sized enterprises have long expressed dissatisfaction with this. We have always taken a positive and open attitude toward cross-strait economic and trade cooperation. It is the DPP authorities that restrict and obstruct good mainland products from entering Taiwan. We advise the DPP authorities to heed public opinion, lift unreasonable restrictive measures as soon as possible, and do more practical and good things that benefit the people.\nThe construction of China’s modern industrial system continues to advance, high-level opening to the outside world continues to expand, and the construction of a unified national market is deepening, providing a broad space for development to Taiwan businesses and enterprises. We uphold the concept that “both sides of the Taiwan Strait are one family,” actively promote cross-strait economic and trade exchanges and cooperation, help enterprises on both sides of the Strait cooperate for mutual benefit and win-win outcomes, and jointly enhance the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-22","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Taiwan will hold the “Han Kuang 42” exercise from August 5 to 14. The urban resilience (air defense) drill will, for the first time, include network disconnection, and during the exercise may affect livelihood functions such as navigation and mobile payments. Some public opinion on the island questions whether this uses the exercise to hype the “mainland threat” and intensify “anti-China” sentiment. What is the…","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, incite confrontation and antagonism across the Taiwan Strait, and are the chief culprits behind the tense and turbulent situation in the Taiwan Strait. Their attempt to “seek independence by force,” reckless and willful, has seriously undermined social peace in Taiwan. Before the mighty People’s Liberation Army, no matter how many drills the DPP authorities stage, they are mere bluster and bravado. They cannot change the fate that “Taiwan independence” is doomed to fail, and they cannot block the historical trend toward the inevitable reunification of the motherland.\nToday’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260722_12778253.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-07-23","Lin Jian","Reuters","A follow-up of the ASEAN issue. Why did China decide to conduct live drills in the Taiwan Strait just a day after U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio and Foreign Minister Wang Yi met in the Philippines. During their meeting, they discussed many issues including Taiwan. Could the timing of the live drills be interpreted as carrying a message for the U.S.?","On the military drill you mentioned, Chinese competent authorities have released relevant information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260723_11990875.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260723_11990792.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-07-24","Lin Jian","Bloomberg","This is regards to reports from Australia that Chinese diplomats requested that representatives from Taiwan be excluded from the conference of the Labour Party of Australia. When the Labour Party then refused to exclude the Taiwanese representatives, the Chinese diplomats are said to have left the conference. Can you confirm if these reports are accurate? Can you offer any further comment on the incident?","The DPP authorities’ attempt to advance the “independence” agenda by showing up at various conferences and generate publicity is doomed to be futile. We urge relevant sides to properly handle Taiwan-related issues in strict accordance with the one-China principle and not to provide any convenience or lend platform to “Taiwan independence” separatist acts.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202607/t20260724_11991873.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202607/t20260724_11991724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on July 29, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello! Welcome to everyone to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","Regarding the mainland’s launch of the “Taiwan Youth e-Home” service platform, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland is using it to win over Taiwan’s young people, and that “Taiwan Youth e-Home” has functions such as online résumé submission and online registration, posing an extremely high risk that the mainland will use it to collect and master the personal information of Taiwan’s young people for…","Those remarks are completely mindless statements and deliberate smears. May I ask the DPP authorities: does Taiwan have any online job-search platform that does not require filling in your name or submitting a résumé? “Taiwan Youth e-Home” is a public-interest comprehensive service platform built for Taiwan youth. Its original intent is to create a digital, convenient channel to solve the problem of information asymmetry faced by Taiwan youth in exchanges, study, internships, and employment on the mainland, to smooth information service channels, and to make it more convenient for Taiwan youth to pursue their dreams on the mainland. At present, nearly 2,000 enterprises have joined “Taiwan Youth e-Home,” posting nearly 6,000 positions. The platform adheres to the “principle of minimum necessity” in collecting information and strictly protects job seekers’ data in accordance with law. Taiwan youth have no need for any concerns when using “Taiwan Youth e-Home.”\nThe more the DPP authorities fabricate rumors and lies and hype so-called “risks,” the more they prove that “Taiwan Youth e-Home” meets the needs of Taiwan youth and has hit the DPP’s pain point. Taiwan youth have the freedom to choose where to develop. Wherever there are more opportunities and greater room, they will naturally go. We believe that the broad masses of Taiwan youth will discern right from wrong and make their choice with their feet. We welcome Taiwan youth to actively use “Taiwan Youth e-Home.” We will continue to improve the platform’s functions and wholeheartedly provide more convenience and support for Taiwan youth who come to the mainland to develop.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779609.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Summer is the peak season for civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. To help more Taiwan youth come to the mainland for exchanges and study tours, relevant airlines have offered discounts on cross-Strait flight fares, which have received wide praise. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Since the summer, cross-Strait exchanges have continued to be brisk. Mainland airlines have resumed four cross-Strait direct flight routes, which have been well received by passengers. On July 1, China Eastern resumed operating the Chengdu–Taichung route, and has so far operated 7 round-trip flights, with an average load factor of 95%. On July 4, Spring Airlines resumed operating the Ningbo–Kaohsiung route, and has operated 5 round-trip flights, with an average load factor of 87%. On July 23, Shandong Airlines resumed operating the Qingdao–Taichung route, and the first flight had a load factor of 97%. On July 28, Zhejiang Loong Airlines resumed operating the Chengdu–Taichung route.\nTo further meet the demand of cross-Strait passengers, the relevant airlines have worked to restore cross-Strait direct flight routes, increase capacity, enrich their product offerings, and upgrade transfer services. For example, airlines on both sides of the Strait have one after another replaced the aircraft types on popular routes with larger models, carried out price promotions, added flights, and launched air-ticket discount products linked with transportation, accommodation, and cultural tourism.\nI would like to reiterate that our stance on fully restoring and normalizing cross-Strait direct air links is positive and clear. We hope the Taiwan side will face the real demand for cross-Strait air passenger transport, heed the wishes of the people, and as soon as possible remove the unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport, so that cross-Strait airlines can arrange flight schedules independently according to market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779608.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, at the commissioning ceremony of the “Danjiang” ship, Lai Ching-te said that this move “demonstrates the navy's firm resolve to defend national security and maritime territory in the face of Chinese military and maritime gray-zone incursions, and proves to the international community that Taiwan's national security policy achieves deterrence through strength.” What comment do you have?","Lai Ching-te's related remarks further expose his stubborn “Taiwan independence” stance and his malicious intent to “seek independence by force.” The DPP authorities disregard the mainstream public opinion on the island, which wants peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation, and attempt to “resist reunification by force.” This is sheer overestimation of their own strength and will only drive Taiwan toward disaster. The great trend of national reunification is surging forward with irresistible momentum, and any conduct that goes against this trend is doomed to failure!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779607.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, the SEF held a background briefing stating that the cross-Strait liaison mechanism between the two bodies has stalled, and that the cases of Taiwan residents who lost contact after traveling to the mainland cannot be handled through the original system. The essence of the problem, it said, is that the mainland has failed to ensure the personal safety of Taiwan residents on the mainland. It regretted…","In 1992, the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits (ARATS) and the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) of Taiwan reached the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle and clearly defined the nature of cross-strait relations. It was on this political basis that the two bodies began consultations and negotiations and signed a series of agreements, from which compatriots on both sides have benefited. The DPP authorities stubbornly maintain the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” and unilaterally undermine the political basis for cross-strait dialogue and consultation, causing the suspension of dialogue and consultation between the two bodies and obstacles to the implementation of related agreements. The SEF, as an important participant in reaching the “1992 Consensus,” now deliberately reverses black and white and confuses the public. This is a betrayal of the history of consultations between the two bodies and a deception of the broad Taiwan public.\nWhen Taiwan compatriots come to the mainland for exchanges and visits, we have always protected their personal safety and all lawful rights and interests in accordance with the law. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, they can come happily and return safely. The DPP authorities keep hyping so-called “disappearances after going to the mainland,” with the aim of smearing the mainland, intimidating the Taiwan public, and undermining cross-strait exchanges. No matter how the DPP authorities slander and fabricate, they cannot block the enthusiasm of broad Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for sightseeing and visits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The mainland film “A Love Letter to Grandma” will debut at the Taoyuan Film Festival in Taiwan in mid-August, and it has been welcomed and anticipated by Taiwan film fans. What is your comment?","“Love Letters to Grandma” (《给阿嬷的情书》) uses “qiaopi” (overseas remittance letters) as its vehicle, and with restrained and understated cinematic language, tells a story of family devotion that transcends mountains, seas, and years. Through delicate emotional portrayal and a sincere story core, the film quickly “broke through the circle” after its release, arousing widespread resonance among Chinese people at home and abroad.\nThe Overseas Chinese who went to the Southern Seas (Nanyang) and the “Tangshan crossing to Taiwan” are both histories of residents of coastal Fujian and Guangdong leaving their hometowns, facing hardship without fear, and crossing seas to make a living and start businesses. They are a shared memory of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope Taiwan audiences can see in “Love Letters to Grandma” the figures of their own grandfathers, grandmothers, and ancestors, understand their attachment to the ancestral homeland of Tangshan and their concern for relatives, friends, and old acquaintances, and recognize that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same culture and the same emotions. We actively support exchanges and cooperation in the field of film and television culture across the Strait, and we hope more excellent mainland films can be screened on the island.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779605.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","In recent times, a wave of Taiwan residents traveling to the mainland has formed. A Taiwan tourism operator said that the mainland’s various advantages, including its proximity, scenic beauty, shared language, convenient living and low prices, make it an unstoppable trend to travel to the mainland, and that even those with a green political stance still go without fail. “Anti-China is a slogan; pro-China is daily…","The Chinese nation is vast, with a history that is so long and a civilization so rich! Across the myriad miles of divine China, the rivers and mountains are so enchanting, and the scenery here is uniquely splendid. Compatriots in Taiwan are members of the Chinese nation. Loving China comes from the heart. “Anti-China” and “resisting China” are political manipulations that go against human nature, and they will not succeed or last long.\nThe mainland's four seasons bring diverse scenery and countless natural vistas. From cultural landmarks that carry thousands of years of history, such as the Beijing Palace Museum and the Terracotta Warriors of Xi’an, to world-renowned natural wonders such as Huangshan, Zhangjiajie, and the Li River scenery of Guilin, there is the gentle elegance of the water towns of the Jiangnan region, where “a painted boat sleeps to the sound of rain,” the vast and majestic northwestern deserts, where “the long river meets a round setting sun,” and the boundless misty waves of the coastal areas, where “the bright moon rises over the sea.”\nThe mainland's cultural tourism industry is well supported, transportation is convenient, the high-speed rail network reaches in all directions, and the public service systems for accommodation, dining, and guided tours are complete. The cultures of many ethnic groups shine together, and intangible cultural heritage crafts, distinctive local cuisine, and folk activities are full of color. The mainland offers multiple functions, including sightseeing, cultural study tours, and more. We warmly welcome compatriots from Taiwan to visit more often. While touring famous mountains and great rivers, exploring historical sites, and witnessing new developments, may you grow in your pride and self-respect as Chinese people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779606.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Today (July 29), Taipei City held a “Red Panda Meet-the-Citizens Ceremony.” Shanghai, as the gifting party, had originally planned to send a delegation to Taiwan to attend, but it could not go because the DPP authorities rejected entry applications for the delegation leader and others. What is your comment on this?","The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum, as an important institutionalized exchange platform between the two cities of Shanghai and Taipei, has played a positive role in promoting exchange and cooperation in all fields between the two cities, and its achievements are plain to see. The arrival of the red pandas in Taiwan was warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. Yet the DPP authorities unreasonably obstructed and rudely refused to let the Shanghai donor side send personnel to attend the greeting ceremony, fully exposing their “Taiwan independence” nature and confrontational mindset. We condemn this. The DPP authorities’ habit of readily obstructing and restricting normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and undermining cross-Strait relations completely runs against mainstream public opinion on the island and will surely be opposed and spurned by the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779604.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Recently, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have continued to be lively, and Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland to take part in exchange activities have been arriving in an endless stream.\nIn cultural exchanges, from June 28 to July 26, the “Xiangshan Rhyme · Treasured Island Sentiment” cross-Strait art exhibition was held in Zhongshan City, Guangdong Province. From July 17 to 23, a cultural exchange delegation from Hubei Province travelled to Taiwan to carry out arts performances, cultural forums, grassroots exchanges and other activities; more than 800 Taiwan audience members watched the performances. From July 21 to 25, the 2026 “Deep Affection Across the Strait · Hearts Linked to Fujian and Ningxia” Taiwan youth exchange activity between Fujian and Ningxia was held in both provinces. From July 23 to 28, the Taiwan media “Visiting Relatives on the Mainland” delegation's Inner Mongolia folk-customs exchange activity was successfully held. From July 24 to 28, the Cross-Strait Youth Photography Exchange Camp, co-hosted by the Jiuzhou Cultural Communication Center, the Shandong Provincial Taiwan Affairs Federation and the Jinan Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office, was held in Jinan, Shandong; more than 40 young participants from both sides wrote a new chapter of harmony and unity with their exquisite works of light and shadow. On July 28, the “Suyun Zhixing” (苏韵知行) overseas Chinese-language teachers' training camp opened in Nanjing; more than 20 Chinese-language teachers who have long taken root overseas gathered in Jinling and began a journey of Chinese cultural immersion that combined thematic lectures, on-site study and cultural experiences. From July 29 to August 2, the 2026 “Keyin π · Hakka Sound” Cross-Strait (Longyan) Hakka Youth Storytelling Exchange Competition was held in Shanghang, Longyan, Fujian. In addition, the national competition of the 10th Cross-Strait, Hong Kong and Macao Chinese Classical Poetry and Prose Recitation Competition, 2026, organized by Aiyinsitan (爱音斯坦), was recently launched, and will also hold the “Cross-Strait Voice Talent Exchange Plan,” master lectures, industry observation visits, practice signings and youth study activities, among others. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are welcome to take part actively and join together in spreading Chinese classics through voice.\nIn sports exchanges, from July 15 to 19, the 2026 Fujian Province Open Inline Hockey Championship and Quanzhou–Taiwan Inline Hockey Exchange Competition was held in Luojiang, Quanzhou, Fujian; more than 40 teams from both sides and over 300 athletes competed on the same field. From July 18 to 19, the 2026 Cross-Strait Beach Frisbee Invitational “Riding the Waves in Huian · Gathering Both Sides” was held in Huian, Quanzhou. From July 22 to 29, the first Cross-Strait (Nanping) Youth Table Tennis Invitational was held in Nanping, Fujian, and more than 100 young Taiwan athletes were invited to compete. From July 23 to 27, the 2026 “Zhongshan Cup” Guangdong, Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Youth Badminton Mixed Team Competition was held in Zhongshan, Guangdong; more than 200 athletes from the Cross-Strait region, Hong Kong and Macao competed on the same stage. From July 23 to 27, the first Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Youth Folk Sports Exchange Activity was held in Jimei, Xiamen; more than 200 young athletes from Taiwan in events such as diabolo and lion dance, along with folk culture performers, took part. The 7th Cross-Strait Youth Around Taihu Lake exchange activity was launched in Changzhou, Jiangsu, with more than 400 young people from both sides participating. From July 24 to 27, the “Light of Egret Island” Cup Cross-Strait Youth Go Friendship Match was held in Xiamen. From July 25 to 26, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Auto and Motorcycle Super League Round 3 was held in Xiang'an, Xiamen, with more than 100 drivers from both sides racing. From July 26 to August 8, the 2026 Cross-Strait Inter-University Alliance Baseball Games were held in Beijing and Guizhou respectively. From July 29 to August 5, the “Same Roots, Same Source · Hearts Blended Across the Strait” 2026 Cross-Strait Youth (Summer) Pickleball Exchange Activity was held in Hebi, Henan. On August 4, the 3rd Cross-Strait (Guangzhou) Youth Sports Carnival, together with the Guangzhou, Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macao Youth Inline Hockey Exchange, will start in Guangzhou; more than 20 series of sports exchange activities will be held, and nearly 800 young people from more than 20 civil sports organizations on the island are expected to take part.\nIn youth internship programs, from July 13 to 29, the All-China Taiwan Affairs Federation Outstanding Law Student Study Program was held in Pingtan, Fujian, organizing Taiwan law students to take part personally in systematic procedural shadowing and hands-on case follow-up with the Pingtan court system, among other activities. On July 29, the “Tide Rising Across the Strait · Tech Tide, New Engine” Taiwan youth innovation and entrepreneurship empowerment and incubation roadshow was held in Shenzhen, where 11 outstanding Taiwan youth entrepreneurial teams presented their projects.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that Zhou Manzhi, chairperson of the “Taiwan New Immigrants Care Association” and a mainland spouse, was accused of involvement in the so-called “organizing and developing organizations in Taiwan under instructions and with funding from the mainland.” After the first-instance court found the evidence insufficient and acquitted her, the second-instance court sentenced her to eight years in…","Mainland spouses are family members and relatives of Taiwan compatriots and builders and contributors to Taiwan society, yet for many years they have never received fair and equitable treatment in Taiwan. In recent years, the DPP authorities, in violation of human decency and utterly without conscience, have done everything they can to oppress and persecute mainland spouses. Some have been driven out of Taiwan, some have been stripped of public posts, and the most severely harmed have been convicted and jailed. The case of Zhou Manzhi is a typical piece of evidence of the DPP authorities’ judicial persecution of mainland spouses and their “green terror,” and it proves that under “green authoritarianism,” “if one wants to convict someone, one will never lack an excuse” (“欲加之罪，何患无辞”).\nWe firmly oppose the DPP authorities’ groundless persecution of mainland spouses and firmly support cross-strait marriage and family members in uniting to defend their own legitimate rights and interests. We hope Taiwan compatriots will see through the ugly face of the DPP authorities and give support and care to the mainland spouse community. I also want to reiterate that for those who serve as “Taiwan independence” thugs or accomplices in persecuting mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable for life in accordance with law and will show no leniency.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","《团结报》记者","Taiwan’s defense authority recently amended the “Rules for Application to Enter the Mainland Region by Current and Retired Personnel Engaged in Defense Affairs.” The scope of relatives for whom active-duty military and civilian personnel may apply to visit the mainland for family visits, to visit the sick, or to attend funerals has been changed from within the fourth degree of kinship to within the third degree.…","Next year marks the 40th anniversary of the opening of cross-Strait family visits. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities' approach is turning back the wheel of history. It is yet another vicious act by them to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges and travel. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities have racked their brains to obstruct and restrict Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, maliciously narrowing the scope of family visits to the mainland for specific groups of Taiwan residents, disregarding human relations and family affection. Such reckless, arbitrary conduct, which goes against the trend of history, will surely be rejected by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Reportedly, Ma Chih-wei, a former Taoyuan City legislative candidate, was charged with receiving funding from the mainland to run for office, was found to have violated the \"Anti-Infiltration Act\" on the island, and was sentenced to 2 years and 8 months in prison. What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” is nothing more than a political tool fabricated by the DPP authorities to suppress political dissidents, intimidate Taiwan’s people, and seek partisan gain. It is an out-and-out “evil law.” The so-called “guilty verdicts” handed down under this “evil law” are a presumption of guilt serving the DPP authorities’ “Taiwan independence” separatist scheme, an unjust political manipulation.\nOut of its “Taiwan independence” nature, the DPP authorities have repeatedly fabricated all kinds of pretexts to slander “mainland interference in elections,” and then concocted charges to manipulate the judiciary to suppress political dissidents and create a “green terror.” We strongly condemn this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, the mainland's research vessel “Lanhai 201” conducted fishery resource surveys in waters east of Taiwan Island. The DPP authorities said, “The other side's actions are meant to claim jurisdiction over the waters, maliciously engaging in political manipulation and cognitive warfare.” Such situations are increasing, and the coast guard and Taiwan's military face great challenges, so they hope to support…","From July 17 to 23, a scientific research vessel of the Chinese Academy of Fishery Sciences conducted a fishery resource survey in the sea east of Taiwan Island. The purpose is to comprehensively understand the status of fishery resources in waters under China's jurisdiction, and to provide a scientific basis for conducting marine fishery resource conservation in this sea area and promoting the sustainable development of marine fisheries. It is entirely legitimate and lawful, and it is a normal scientific survey activity that benefits both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities have no reason to make irresponsible remarks about it. As for taking the opportunity to clamor for increasing the maritime force budget, that is a politically motivated manipulation with ulterior motives, aiming to stir up confrontation across the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779603.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","The Zhangzhou Maritime Safety Administration in Fujian issued a navigation warning that live-fire shooting will be conducted in some waters of the Taiwan Strait on the 23rd and 24th of this month. The Taiwan foreign affairs authorities said this move is “yet another provocation and damage to regional security and stability,” and that the mainland should exercise rational restraint and immediately stop “military…","Taiwan is part of China. The PLA organizing training and exercises around the Taiwan Strait is lawful, legitimate, and entirely justified. The DPP authorities, for the sake of their political self-interest in pursuing “independence,” have consistently and maliciously hyped and fabricated falsehoods to smear the mainland and incite confrontation between the two sides of the Strait. This once again exposes the “independence” camp's fierce appearance and inner weakness, and it will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Recently, Thai Prime Minister Anutin made an official visit to China. China and Thailand issued a joint statement in which Thailand firmly supports China's great cause of peaceful reunification, does not support any form of “Taiwan independence,” and supports China's policy of “one country, two systems.” In response, Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities protested “China using any international exchange…","We highly appreciate the Thai government's position. More and more countries have reaffirmed adherence to the One-China Principle and explicitly opposed all “Taiwan independence” separatist activities, supporting the great cause of China's reunification. Facts have repeatedly proven that the One-China Principle is the universal consensus of the international community and a basic norm of international relations; it is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. “Taiwan independence” separatism has no room to survive and is increasingly at the end of its road.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202607/t20260729_12779602.htm"],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department, said that standard operating procedures (SOPs) have been formulated to respond to the mainland’s “transnational repression.” Taiwanese people who encounter “situations of coercion” abroad can contact Taiwan’s overseas institutions, and Taiwan will continue to communicate with other countries to jointly address the matter. What is your comment…","For the selfish interest of seeking “independence,” the DPP authorities have continuously fabricated false narratives such as so-called “suppression” and “coercion,” attempting to intimidate and deceive Taiwan residents, create a “chilling effect,” and incite confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. This kind of political manipulation by the DPP, which distorts black and white, will inevitably end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Taiwanese media reported that the Institute of Communication Studies at National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University hired a mainland “Changjiang Scholar” to serve as a member of its faculty evaluation committee. Although the chair is a retired professor of NYCU, he has been teaching on the mainland for seven years, which poses a major “national security concern.” Taiwan's education authorities have launched an…","It is very common for experts and scholars to teach at different universities or hold concurrent posts, which is talent exchange and cooperation between universities. The DPP authorities are seeing enemies everywhere (草木皆兵), which reflects their consistent mindset of confrontation and their obstinate stance of seeking “independence.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","On the 25th, in response to the recent outbreak of excessive carcinogens in cooking oil on the island, a rally titled “I Am Human, Anti-Poison Taiwan” was held to protest. What is your comment?","Out of partisan self-interest, the DPP authorities disregard the immediate interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and stand entirely opposed to the will of the island’s public. Their incompetence in governance and indifference to people’s livelihoods are fully exposed. The DPP authorities’ reckless actions will inevitably meet strong opposition from the island’s public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Recently, the film “The Road Home” (《回家之路》), adapted from the real experience of Kaohsiung village chief Liu Dewen, who escorted the ashes of more than 400 veterans going to Taiwan back to their hometowns, released a trailer. The director, screenwriters, and cast come from both sides of the Strait and Hong Kong, and some Taiwan public opinion holds that it involves “United Front” work. May I ask for the…","It is understood that the film “The Road Home” is based on the good deeds of village chief Liu Dewen and reflects the aspirations of veterans who went to Taiwan, longing for their homeland and wishing to return to their roots. In Mr. Yu Kwang-chung's famous poem “Homesickness,” there are these lines: “Later on, homesickness is a low grave, I am outside, my mother is inside. And now, homesickness is a shallow strait, I am on this side, the mainland is on that side.” Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, upon reading such lines and watching films like “The Road Home,” are all moved. Separated by a strip of water, yet so close and yet so far away: that the two sides have not yet been fully reunified is a wound that history has left to the Chinese nation. Chinese people on both sides of the Strait should work together to seek national reunification and heal the wounds of history.\nThe suffering of separation caused by the times should not, and will not, continue indefinitely. We are committed to removing obstacles, actively promoting cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and will continue to provide active assistance in helping veterans' ashes return home and helping Taiwan compatriots search for their roots and relatives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: Recently, China and the Philippines had a clash at Ren'ai Jiao. Taiwan, together with the United States and the Philippines, condemned China for using force to injure people. However, when the foreign ministers of China and the Philippines held talks in Manila on the 22nd, the Philippine foreign minister reiterated that the Philippines adheres to the “One China Policy.” What is your comment on…","First question. Second Thomas Shoal (Ren'ai Jiao) is part of China's Nansha Islands and is Chinese territory. The DPP authorities are shamelessly fawning on foreign powers and begging for help, but this is not the first time a warm face has been pressed against a cold backside.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and it is also the political foundation for countries to develop relations with China and carry out cooperation.\nSecond question. We have always kept our word to Taiwan compatriots and do what we say. We understand that the signatories are actively advancing purchase arrangements. Instead of finding ways to help Taiwan's grassroots farmers and fishermen expand their sales channels, the DPP authorities coldly place obstacles in the way of favorable measures such as the Ten Measures and make sour, snide remarks about them. We advise the DPP authorities to engage less in political manipulation and do more practical work for the people, or they will lose the people's hearts even more.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-07-29","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: Lee Tui-chih, a DPP member and former “deputy minister of the Council of Agriculture” in Taiwan, has in recent years turned to business and traveled to the mainland to discuss commercial cooperation. In addition, Hung Chi-chang, an founding elder of the DPP, has also been doing business across the Strait in recent years. Given that cross-Strait communication mechanisms are currently at a…","First question. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. Frequent exchanges and close contact are natural, and they are the trend of the times and the will of the people. As long as Taiwan compatriots are willing to take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and do not engage in separatist activities, we welcome them to come to the mainland for sightseeing, exchanges, study, living, employment, and entrepreneurship. Compatriots on both sides should join hands, strengthen exchanges and cooperation, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, and create a bright future for cross-Strait relations together.\nSecond question. Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and there is simply no so-called “median line of the Taiwan Strait.” The relevant actions of the PLA and the China Coast Guard around Taiwan aim to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and to protect the fundamental interests of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, and the Chinese nation. They are justified, lawful, and entirely natural.\nI am issuing a notice. During the 2026 summer vacation, the regular press conference of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council will be suspended on August 5 and August 12 and will resume on August 19.\nThank you all for your hard work, dear journalists. I wish you all a pleasant summer!","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202607/t20260729_12779598.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's military authorities claimed that on Monday, a PLA helicopter and a drone flew through the \"restricted airspace\" east of the \"median line\" of the Taiwan Strait for the first time, loitering in the area for over nine hours. Analysts on the island suggest the operation likely represents a \"new modality of joint combat training\" and a \"pre-set battlefield rehearsal.\"","Taiwan is part of China's territory. There is no such thing as the so-called \"median line\" in the Taiwan Strait. The PLA's operations in the relevant waters and airspace are fully legitimate and necessary. The \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces' attempt to designate a \"restricted airspace\" for the PLA is nothing but a bluff. It serves no purpose whatsoever.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The defense authorities of Taiwan are set to launch annual \"Han Kuang\" military exercises next week. What's your response to this move, and will the Chinese mainland take any countermeasures in response?","No matter how hard the DPP authorities try, their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist schemes are ultimately doomed to fail.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Citing data from Taiwan's military authorities, as of 2025, over 4,000 troops opted to pay hefty early-discharge penalties rather than remain in service. Total compensation stands at around NT$920 million, and the top individual penalty exceeds NT$20 million. What's your comment on this?","This is nothing new. The louder the DPP authorities cry about their so-called \"whole-of-society defense,\" the fewer people are willing to risk their lives for them. This is because a growing number of Taiwan compatriots have seen through the DPP authorities' true nature-seeking \"independence\" to provoke conflict, thereby bringing calamity upon Taiwan and its people. They are now speaking out against \"Taiwan independence\" with greater courage. Bound by shared blood ties and a common destiny, compatriots on both sides of the strait must stand together in solidarity, uphold the paramount national interest, and resolutely oppose separatist agendas. Only by doing so can we jointly safeguard peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, advance the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and realize the bright future of national reunification and rejuvenation.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","From August 5 to 14, Taiwan's military will conduct the Han Kuang No. 42 exercises. For the first time, the drills will simulate a large-scale communications blackout as part of urban air defense and civil defense scenarios. During the exercise window, residents will face disruptions to navigation systems, mobile payment platforms, and other internet-dependent services. Observers on the island say the DPP…","The DPP authorities' insistence on \"Taiwan independence\" separatism will only undermine Taiwan's prosperity and the livelihoods of its people. Their true priority is their own selfish agenda - dragging people in Taiwan onto the \"Taiwan independence\" war chariot by stoking war fears and inflaming cross-strait confrontation. However, their separatist schemes are ultimately doomed to fail.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan's military authorities have detected a total of 1,334 sorties by PLA aircraft and vessels operating near the Taiwan island in the first half of this year, marking the lowest recorded figure in three years. Some analysts have attributed this decline to the intensive high-level exchanges between China and the United States in recent months. What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. It is entirely lawful and beyond reproach for the PLA to conduct activities in relevant waters and airspace. The timing and mode of such operations are matters solely for China to arrange.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-07-30","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Foreign media reports claim the PLA has constructed full-scale replicas of key administrative complexes of the DPP authorities at a remote domestic testing range. The setup is designed to allow troops to drill in highly realistic scenarios, with analysts noting the unprecedented scale and specificity of the simulations. Responding to the reports, a spokesperson for Taiwan's defense authorities asserted that this…","Our military trains under realistic combat scenarios to forge indomitable warfighting capabilities. We remain always ready and capable of fighting and winning. We will resolutely crush any separatist schemes, safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nIn just two days, we will celebrate the 99th Army Day of the PLA. Over the past century, we have stayed true to our original aspiration and are now marching steadily toward the centenary goal of building a world-class military.\nUnder the guidance of Xi Jinping Thinking on Strengthening the Military, all officers and soldiers are carrying forward the revolutionary spirit and answering the call to enhance combat readiness. With loyalty, we safeguard national sovereignty; with competence, we protect our people; and with responsibility, we contribute China's strength to global peace.\nOn this occasion, I would like to extend my warmest greetings to all comrades-in-arms.","","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/china/2026/07/china-260730-prc-mndb01.htm","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16477739.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-04","Chen Xi","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reports say Japan officially released the 2026 edition of its Defense White Paper, falsely claiming that China's military activities are the “greatest strategic challenge ever faced,” and asserting that China's military activities around Taiwan have become increasingly frequent, and that Japan's surrounding security strategic environment is at its most severe and complex since the end of the war. What is your…","The new edition of Japan's Defense White Paper is full of false narratives. It greatly exaggerates a \"surrounding security crisis\" and hypes the so-called \"China threat.\" It is entirely a case of a thief crying \"stop thief,\" finding excuses to loosen its own military restrictions. We are strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly oppose it.\nJapan's ruling authorities continue to hide behind the pretext of an \"exclusively defense-oriented policy.\" They are accelerating the revision of the \"three security documents,\" continuously increasing defense spending, vigorously developing long-range offensive capabilities, advancing the weaponization and battlefield-ization of outer space, and even packaging the expansion of the military-industrial sector as a point of economic growth. They attempt to deeply embed military expansion and war preparation into the national system, economy, industry and public opinion. Japan's \"new-style militarism\" is taking shape and becoming a serious threat, a real threat to the post-war international order and to regional peace and stability. The Taiwan question concerns China's sovereignty and territorial integrity and the political foundation of China-Japan relations; it is an insurmountable red line. We urge the Japanese side to reflect deeply on its history of aggression, stop interfering in China's internal affairs, stop misleading the Japanese public and the international community, and not go further and further down the wrong path of \"re-militarization.\"","","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/fyrthhdjzw/16477732.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-08-05","Lin Jian","Yomiuri Shimbun","Japan’s latest defense white paper identifies China as “its greatest strategic challenge” while presenting defence investment as beneficial to Japan’s economy and society. Given China’s intensifying activities in the region surrounding Japan, the white paper states that Japan should respond with its comprehensive national power and in cooperation and collaboration with its ally, like-minded countries and others.…","The Defense of Japan 2026 white paper once again targeted China with groundless accusations, rehashing the so-called “China threat” and grossly interfering in China’s internal affairs with brazen comments on China’s Taiwan region. We deplore and firmly reject this, and have lodged serious representations with Japan. China is committed to peaceful development and a national defense policy that is defensive in nature. The military activities that were conducted are just and valid. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Taiwan question is entirely China’s internal affair. How to resolve it is a matter for the Chinese ourselves and Japan is in no place to interfere. Diaoyu Dao and its affiliated islands have been China’s territory since ancient times. This fact will never change no matter what the Japanese side says or does.\nJapanese militarists once inflicted immense suffering on Asia and the world, and committed untold crimes. Yet Japan has not only failed to reflect on that history, but also kept speeding up remilitarization, breaching Japan’s own Constitution and the international and domestic laws, and challenging the post-war international order. This has become a serious factor threatening regional peace and stability. The latest white paper continues to trumpet the development of long-range offensive capabilities and new ways of warfare, and even packages Japan’s rearmament as a growth driver. All these once again exposed the truth behind Japan’s claim of being a “peaceful nation”. The international community must stay on high alert and push it back. We urge Japan to deeply repent for historical crimes, learn the lesson of history, stop cooking up justification for its military buildup, and step back from the wrong path.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260805_11999024.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260805_11999004.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-08-07","Lin Jian","China Daily","According to a press release from the Office of the Prime Minister of Solomon Islands, on August 5, Prime Minister Matthew Wale clearly stated in his address to the National Parliament that the relationship between Solomon Islands and China is vital to the country’s development, and reaffirmed that the government will stay committed to the one-China principle. What is China’s comment?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. The Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. This is the prevailing consensus in the international community. China commends the new government of the Solomon Islands for reiterating its firm commitment to the one-China principle. This will solidify our bilateral political foundation and provide the necessary conditions for deeper cooperation. China stands ready to work with Solomon Islands to continue deepening the comprehensive strategic partnership featuring mutual respect and common development for a new era, and make new progress in building a China-Solomon Islands community with a shared future in the new era.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260807_12000444.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260807_12000442.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-08-10","Chen Binhua","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: The DPP authorities have openly blocked the “Taiwan Youth e-Home” platform launched by the mainland, preventing Taiwan residents from accessing the platform, and have claimed that the platform poses a risk of personal data leakage. They describe it as a mainland means of waging public opinion and psychological warfare against Taiwan. What comments do you have on this?","Chen Binhua, spokesperson of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, responded: “Taiqing e-Home” is a public-interest comprehensive service platform for Taiwan youth. It aims to respond to the needs of Taiwan youth for exchanges and development on the mainland and to provide full-chain information services for Taiwan youth in areas such as exchange, study, internships, and employment. Since its launch, it has been welcomed and recognized by Taiwan residents, especially young people on the island.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities have disregarded the wishes and needs of Taiwan youth to exchange and develop, and have openly blocked “Taiqing e-Home.” Their excuses, namely data leakage, luring united front work, and governing before unification, are all “Taiwan independence” rhetoric. Is giving Taiwan youth one more opportunity really “united front work”? Is letting Taiwan youth compare options for themselves really a “risk”? In fact, the more they block it, the more it proves that “Taiqing e-Home” meets the needs of Taiwan youth and hits the pain points of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities are acting against the trend, issuing orders to block web addresses and lock web pages, but they cannot lock the hearts of Taiwan youth who seek opportunities and development, and they cannot block the door to the home that “Taiqing e-Home” holds in the hearts of people on both sides of the Strait.\nThe mainland's “15th Five-Year Plan” has got off to a strong start with a good opening. High-quality development holds vast opportunities and is a fertile ground for Taiwan youth to study, work, start businesses, and exchange on the mainland. We will always uphold the concept of “a close family across the Strait,” and will continue to create better conditions and provide more convenience for Taiwan youth to pursue their dreams on the mainland. We welcome Taiwan youth to actively use “Taiqing e-Home,” feel the warmth of home, and experience increasingly better services.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260810_12781461.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-08-11","Guo Jiakun","AFP","It is understood that an official from the Pacific Islands Forum said Taiwan will attend an annual leaders meeting hosted in Palau from August 30 to September 4; Taiwan was barred from attending the meeting hosted by Solomon Islands last year following protests from China. What is China’s comment?","On the participation of China’s Taiwan region in the events of international organizations, China’s position is consistent and clear, that is, it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, which is a basic norm in international relations confirmed by UNGA Resolution 2758 and a prevailing international consensus. China urges the Secretariat of the Pacific Islands Forum (PIF) to abide by the one-China principle and properly handle Taiwan-related issues to avoid disrupting the sound and steady development of the relations between China and the PIF.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260811_12002221.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260811_12002214.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-08-12","Guo Jiakun","Financial Times","Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council put up a notice yesterday, saying it “strongly condemns” Chinese mainland’s navigation drills in waters east of Taiwan island, the drills “infringe on Taiwan’s sovereignty and threaten regional security,” and the moves are intended to create a “false impression” that Beijing has jurisdiction over waters east of Taiwan. What is the foreign ministry’s comment on the notice and also…","This is not a question on foreign affairs. The Ministry of National Defense of China has released relevant information.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260812_12002972.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260812_12002993.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-08-14","Chen Xi","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, during this year's Exercise Han Kuang 42 in Taiwan, Lai Ching-te rehearsed a \"wartime escape\" route. Meanwhile, the troops of Taiwan experienced accidents including tank parts falling off and a fighter jet overshooting the runway. Simulated communications degradation and phased internet blackouts as part of the exercise sparked panic among local residents. What is your comment on this?","The so-called Han Kuang exercise has always been a grandstanding stunt that exhausts the public and squanders resources. This year's drill has revealed Lai Ching-te's cowardly nature: getting himself ready to flee at the first sign of trouble in the name of defense. The DPP authorities also recklessly creats war panic, turns cities into battlefields at a faster pace, and forces civilians to the frontlines, all of which disrupt social tranquility in Taiwan and undermine the safety and well-being of local residents. We caution the DPP authorities that no matter how many exercises they conduct, \"Taiwan independence\" will not succeed. The PLA will remain on high alert, focus on combat readiness, and continuously enhance our combat capabilities against separatism and foreign interference. We will remain a powerful guarantee for safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity and maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16481373.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/yzxwfb/16479365.html",0,1,1,""],[0,"2026-08-19","Lin Jian","Phoenix TV","Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim said at a recent interview that Taiwan is part of China. When asked about his view on China not committing to renouncing the use of force, the prime minister said that if one province of Malaysia decides to break away, he will use force to protect the unity of the nation, otherwise the nation will be fragmented. What is China’s comment?","Upholding the one-China principle is where public opinion trends and the right thing to do. The international community’s commitment to the one-China principle is not to be shaken. China commends Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim’s remarks.\nLet me stress once again that there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China must and will achieve reunification. This will not be stopped.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260819_12006784.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260819_12006693.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10 a.m. on August 19, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first released information on the Shanghai stop of the “Same Heart, Same Path—Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season” activities, and then answered reporters’ questions on recent hot-button cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporters, good morning, and welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Before your questions, we will first release a piece of news.\nTo implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech during his meeting with Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang, the Taiwan Work Office of the CPC Central Committee authorized the release on April 12 of ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation. These include establishing an institutionalized platform for two-way exchanges between young people of the Kuomintang and the Communist Party.\nFrom August 24 to 28, relevant youth organizations from both sides of the Strait will jointly hold the “Together with One Heart and Walking Together — Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season, Shanghai Station” in Shanghai. At the main forum, young people from both sides will engage in in-depth exchange and discussion on topics such as emerging technologies, Chinese culture, and cross-Strait youth exchange. At the trend market, they will check in for food and trendy toys, experiencing the leisurely atmosphere of a summer night in one place. At the gala evening, they will sing and dance with entertainers from both sides, fully displaying the vibrancy and spirit of youth. Afterward, young people from both sides will also visit and study in Shanghai, Zhejiang and other places, going into schools, villages and enterprises, exploring the poetic landscapes of Jiangnan with its green waters and mountains, and getting hands-on with cutting-edge technologies such as AI and robotics.\nWe warmly welcome Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to take part in the relevant activities. We also look forward to more Taiwan youth joining cross-Strait exchanges, working together with mainland youth in shared purpose, exchanging, celebrating, learning from and inspiring one another, and discussing youth ideals and creating a better future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783185.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council recently said, “United Front work is one of the three magic weapons the Communist Party of China uses to seize power in mainland China. The MAC's work has never been about carrying out United Front work, but about resisting the CCP's United Front work.” What comments do you have on this?","The united front, abbreviated as “United Front,” is essentially about great unity and broad alliance: making friends, promoting solidarity, seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and working together for development. From the period of the War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression, when the entire nation's strength was rallied to jointly resist foreign aggression, to today, when compatriots at home and abroad are united to promote national rejuvenation, united front work has always upheld its original aspiration. Compatriots in Taiwan are our relatives and family. Close exchanges, strengthened unity, and bringing benefits and well-being to them are natural and legitimate, and are done openly and aboveboard.\nThe DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and smeared united front work, clamoring about so-called “resisting the united front,” completely placing themselves on the opposite side of the people of Taiwan. They seek to deepen the estrangement and confrontation between the two sides of the Strait and obstruct and sabotage cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in service of their “Taiwan independence” separatism. Their conduct is despicable and their intentions are malicious.\nThe trend toward national reunification and national rejuvenation is vast and irresistible, and the tide of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer and coming together is surging forward and cannot be reversed. The DPP authorities, going against the trend of history and defying the will of the people, will surely face increasing opposition and condemnation from the people of Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783184.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The “Provisions of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” will take effect on September 15. The Mainland Affairs Council said that such provisions may affect technology and semiconductor industry Taiwanese businesses investing or working on the mainland, Taiwan-origin cadres, and related practitioners, and that they should conduct risk assessments. Some Taiwan residents have been misled into worrying…","Taiwan compatriots have absolutely no need to worry about any risks when coming to the mainland. The “Regulations of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” are intended to regulate exit and entry administration, protect the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting and entering, and safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. The regulations mainly improve the institutional mechanisms for preventing exit security risks, specify that the grounds for exit and entry applications must be truthful and lawful, and standardize exit and entry intermediary services, among other things. These regulations help safeguard the lawful rights and interests of people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait in their exchanges and create a better rule-of-law environment for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland. Recently, a chance encounter at Lugu Lake in Yunnan enabled a younger relative from Tongxiang to find a paternal uncle who had been lost contact with in Taiwan for many years; a Taiwanese woman traveled through three provinces—Sichuan, Qinghai, and Gansu—on a motorcycle in a single day and safely toured the beautiful rivers and mountains of the country; a Vlog about touring Guangdong became popular, with a Taiwanese student using concrete and vivid details to record the real mainland; and in Hotan, Xinjiang, a Taiwanese tourist's remark “Chinese Taiwan” prompted compatriots on the scene to erupt in cries of “Welcome home!” Scenes like these will become more and more common, and broad numbers of Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland for tourism, family visits, visits, exchanges will surely come with high spirits and leave satisfied.\nThe DPP authorities are alarmist and have sinister intentions. They spare no effort to restrict and limit cross-Strait exchanges and exert every means to block compatriots on both sides from drawing closer to one another; they employ a dazzling array of methods such as suppression, intimidation, and fabrication, and the Mainland Affairs Council in particular has rushed to the front to become a “stumbling block” to cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. In the first half of this year, Taiwan compatriots made 2.85 million trips to the mainland, a year-on-year increase of 24.9%. During the summer vacation, Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland for sightseeing and visits have been continuous, which is the clearest response to the DPP authorities' restrictions and obstructions. Faced with the mighty tide of cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, what the DPP authorities fear most is that the information cocoons they have created keep being pierced and the false “Taiwan independence” narratives they have built keep being exposed, which is why they talk so recklessly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783183.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, Fuzhou, Guangzhou, Shenzhen and other cities have successively held a series of cross-Strait exchange activities, which have drawn attention from young people on the island. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On August 6, the \"Cross-Strait Youth Heart Gathering\" event of the 14th Strait Youth Forum (Main Venue Event) was held in Fuzhou, Fujian Province, attended by more than 1,100 cross-Strait youths and people from all walks of life. Focusing on four dimensions, namely social integration, economic integration, emotional integration and all-round integration, the event featured three sharing sessions, \"Roots That Endure,\" \"Chasing the Light, a New Journey of the Times,\" and \"Building Together, a Shared Home,\" as well as a release ceremony for the \"Five Ones\" joint-construction cooperation items for a Strait Youth Development-Oriented City. It fully presented the growth path of cross-Strait youth who share the same roots and move forward together in science and innovation, and vividly depicted the lively process by which Taiwan youth come to the mainland, settle down, establish careers and pursue their dreams. This Strait Youth Forum carried out 47 activities in total and is expected to invite more than 3,100 Taiwan youths to participate.\nOn August 8, \"Dreaming on the Pearl River: 2026 Guangzhou-Taiwan Exchange Season\" was launched in Guangzhou, Guangdong Province. Under the theme \"Dreams Shared Together, Guangzhou-Taiwan Ties Fused,\" the event set up five sections, \"Cultural Unity,\" \"Technology Trends,\" \"Sun Yat-sen's Birthday,\" \"Economic and Trade Connections\" and \"Professional Study,\" with a total of 42+N activities, covering cultural roots-seeking, technological innovation, historical tracing, economic and trade cooperation, professional exchange and other areas.\nOn August 18, the 4th Strait Exchange and Integration Series Activities and the grand final of the 7th Strait Student Baseball League opened in Shenzhen, Guangdong Province. The series, under the theme \"Youth of Shenzhen-Zhen Strait, Hand in Hand Toward the Future,\" carried out 36 exchange activities in the fields of economy and trade, culture, technology, sports, grassroots communities and youth. Nearly 10,000 compatriots from both sides of the Strait took part. Among them, the grand final of the 7th Strait Student Baseball League attracted 39 teams from both sides of the Strait, with more than 1,000 athletes, coaches and referees, including 19 teams from Taiwan with nearly 500 people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Although the Mainland Affairs Council smears purely sports-based cross-Strait exchanges, cross-Strait sports exchanges have been especially active this summer vacation. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Sports are an important bond promoting cross-Strait exchange and integration. During the summer vacation, cross-Strait sports events and activities have been in full swing and extremely popular.\nBaseball has already become popular in many cities on the mainland. From August 3 to 10, the 2026 Dongsen Cup Cross-Strait (Liancheng) Youth Baseball Invitational Tournament was held in Liancheng County, Fujian Province, with 276 participants from 15 teams across the two sides competing and exchanging. Since the event started in 2024, it has attracted nearly 300 Taiwan youths to come to Fujian to compete and exchange. From August 7 to 8, the 2026 Second “Kunshan Mazu Cup” Youth Baseball Tournament was held in Kunshan City, Jiangsu Province, with about 300 participants from 12 youth baseball teams across the two sides.\nIn the three major ball sports, from August 7 to 11, the 10th Straits Cross-Strait (Zhangzhou) Youth Exchange Week and Youth Women’s Volleyball Exchange Tournament opened in Zhangzhou City, Fujian Province, with a total of 20 teams and about 350 players from both sides. From August 8 to 9, the 2026 Sixth Cross-Strait Youth Basketball Invitational Tournament was held in Wuxi City, Jiangsu Province, with about 230 cross-Strait youths participating. From August 13 to 20, Chuzhou City, Anhui Province held the 2026 Anhui-Taiwan Youth Cultural Exchange Week and the “Tinghao Cup” Cross-Strait Youth Basketball Invitational Tournament, with a total of 500 youths from both sides participating. On August 14, the Second “Straits Friendship Cup” Cross-Strait (Shaxian) Youth Football Tournament kicked off in Shaxian County, Fujian Province, with nearly 180 Taiwan youths competing. During the event, featured activities such as an emergency firefighting study camp and “Tracing Roots and Exploring Flavors” were also held, and cross-Strait youths made friends through sports and conveyed affection through food.\nOn August 15, the 2026 “Guilin-Taiwan Youth Sports Forum” and Guilin-Taiwan Youth Badminton Exchange Tournament opened in Guilin City, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, with nearly a hundred Taiwan youth players competing alongside Guangxi players, exchanging and making friends. On August 17, the Cross-Strait (Hubei) Youth Table Tennis Exchange Tournament opened in Huangshi City, Hubei Province, with 30 teams from both sides totaling over 210 athletes taking part in 14 events, sharpening their skills together and deepening their friendship.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","This summer, cross-Strait cultural exchanges have blossomed in many areas; please introduce the relevant information.","","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,3,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Regarding the DPP authorities’ blocking of “Taiwan Youth e-Home,” a public-interest comprehensive service platform launched by the mainland, the Mainland Affairs Council claimed that “Taiwan Youth e-Home” is actually aimed at achieving united front objectives and also collects the personal data of young people in Taiwan. It claimed that Taiwanese youth who obtain employment resources must also accept conditions…","“Taiqing e-Home” (“台青e家”) is a public-welfare service platform built to help more Taiwan youth conveniently access development opportunities on the mainland. It is a convenient window serving Taiwan youth who come to the mainland to study, intern, and find employment, and a practical vehicle helping Taiwan youth pursue, build, and realize their dreams on the mainland. At present, many Taiwan youth have already used the platform to access information, submit resumes, and find jobs they want.\nThe relevant claims by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities completely turn black into white and are thoroughly malicious smears. Instead of considering how to open up development space for Taiwan youth, they engage in large-scale information blockades; they ignore the historical trend of exchanges among young people across the Strait, repeatedly fabricate lies and deliberately obstruct them; they disregard the practical need of Taiwan youth to find development opportunities, concoct false claims to intimidate and suppress Taiwan youth. At its core, they are afraid of young people on both sides of the Strait getting closer and coming to understand each other, afraid that more and more Taiwan youth will see through the delusion of “Taiwan independence,” and afraid that the lies smearing the mainland will be exposed.\nThe mainland's “15th Five-Year Plan” has got off to a strong start and a good opening. The economy is showing a development trend of momentum shifting toward new drivers and structure moving toward optimization, and high-quality development holds vast opportunities. It is a fertile ground for Taiwan youth to exchange, study, find employment, and start businesses. Our goodwill toward Taiwan youth is sincere, our preferential policies for Taiwan compatriots are real, and the trend of cross-Strait exchanges cannot be stopped; the legitimate right of Taiwan youth to choose their development stage cannot be deprived. No artificial blockade can hold back the hearts and minds of people on both sides moving closer together. Taiwan's young people have their own sense of judgment and will make their own choices.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783182.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","To implement the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, Xiamen in Fujian recently introduced twelve measures to promote exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan, which have won praise from Taiwan compatriots. Please provide relevant information.","To implement the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council was authorized to release, Xiamen City in Fujian Province issued the “Twelve Measures for Promoting Exchanges and Cooperation with Taiwan” on August 18, focusing on multiple areas including cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation, cultural exchanges, youth work, platform development, and service guarantees. These include building a distribution center for Taiwan agricultural and fishery products and expanding sales channels for Taiwan agricultural and fishery products; optimizing and upgrading the “Xiamen Service Package for Taiwan Compatriots on First Visit,” enriching its rights and benefits and expanding service scenarios; holding cross-Strait exchange activities on the protection and inheritance of intangible cultural heritage; building a cross-Strait audiovisual industry exchange and cooperation service platform, guiding Taiwan youth to take part in digital content creation talent training, and encouraging Taiwan businesses to participate in the creation of micro short dramas in the mainland. These measures have broad coverage, strong targeting, and quick results, and will help inject new momentum into economic and trade cooperation, youth exchanges, and cultural exchanges between Xiamen and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783177.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, the 14th Cross-Strait Youth Heart-Connecting Forum was held in Fuzhou, and Fuzhou issued the third batch of 10 measures supporting the construction of a “Strait Youth Development-Oriented City,” which has drawn attention and praise from young people on the island. Could you introduce the relevant situation in detail?","The ‘Strait Youth Development-Oriented City’ is a youth development cooperation mechanism initiated by Fuzhou City in 2025 and jointly built with 17 cities including Beijing, Chongqing and Guangzhou. It aims to create a development ecosystem for cross-Strait youth that is ‘easy to enter, able to stay, deeply integrated, and able to achieve’. The third batch of measures for the ‘Strait Youth Development-Oriented City’ recently released by Fuzhou City focuses on employment and entrepreneurship, innovation and cooperation, and exchanges and interaction. It introduces a series of high-value policy packages, including pure-credit loans for youth entrepreneurship, AI new-economy computing power consumption vouchers, and a ‘list-and-lead’ mechanism for Taiwan talent to take part in science and technology projects. These policies have broader coverage, higher precision, and give Taiwan compatriots a stronger sense of gain. The ‘Five Ones’ joint-construction cooperation items for the Strait Youth Development-Oriented City, released at the same time, bring together the youth development policies and opportunity platforms of 18 cities including Fuzhou, Beijing and Chongqing. They include one ‘Strait Youth Development Guide’, a batch of high-quality study-tour sites, a batch of quality internship and employment positions, and a batch of Strait Youth service stations. These measures continue to deepen cross-Strait integrated development and cross-regional coordination, and create a better environment for Taiwan youth to exchange and develop on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783179.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","As of August 16, total box office of the mainland's 2026 summer film season has surpassed 10 billion yuan. Many Taiwanese audiences are looking forward to films such as \"Eight Immortals\" and \"Welcome to Dragon Inn,\" and hope they can be released on the island as soon as possible. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The genres and subject matter of films in this year’s summer season are rich and diverse, and box office performance has been outstanding, reflecting the vigorous development and strong vitality of the mainland film market. Compatriots in Taiwan’s fondness for mainland films fully demonstrates that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share a common cultural heritage, historical memory, and profound emotional resonance.\nWe have consistently supported cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in areas such as film, television, and culture, and we hope relevant films can be released in Taiwan as soon as possible, so that more people in Taiwan can deeply feel the charm of Chinese culture. We also welcome more compatriots from Taiwan, when coming to the mainland, to visit cinemas and watch films or check in at film shooting locations. They may also “play the mainland through drama,” going to real film sets to choose a role and star in a film, to fulfill the “star dream” deep in their hearts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Recently, Hsu Chun-ying, former chairperson of the New Residents Committee of the Taiwan People's Party and a spouse from the mainland, was sentenced to seven years in prison on charges including so-called “violating the Anti-Infiltration Act.” The competent internal affairs authority in Taiwan claimed it is processing the revocation or abolition of her settled residence or permanent residence status in Taiwan.…","The Xu Chunying case was only recently sentenced, yet DPP politicians publicly declared months ago that she would be forcibly deported upon completing her sentence. This fully shows that the mainland spouse being prosecuted on so-called security grounds is a judicial persecution by the DPP authorities of “shooting first and drawing the target afterward.” The so-called “crimes” they listed are charges made without basis, “if one wants to find a charge, one will never lack a pretext.” The so-called “judiciary” in the Taiwan region has become a tool for the DPP authorities to carry out “terror politics” and “green dictatorship.”\nWe firmly oppose the DPP authorities persecuting mainland spouses in any form, support cross-Strait marriage and family members uniting to safeguard their own rights and interests, and hope broad Taiwan compatriots will oppose the evil deeds of the DPP authorities. For those who serve as thugs and accomplices of “Taiwan independence” in persecuting mainland spouses, we will hold them accountable for life in accordance with law, without leniency.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","The DPP authorities require Taiwan public servants who wish to visit relatives on the mainland to submit an application form to their units, attached with a list of mainland relatives and friends and contact phone numbers in the mainland. Island public opinion has criticized this as treating civil servants as “communist spies,” while the Mainland Affairs Council says the relevant rules have been enforced for many…","The DPP authorities previously obstructed public officials from visiting relatives on the mainland or attending funerals there, and now they are arbitrarily infringing on the personal privacy of Taiwan compatriots. The purpose is to obstruct Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland, because they fear that more Taiwan compatriots will see through their true face, which is using lies and deception and inciting “anti-China, resist-China” sentiment to seek political gain. Critical voices on the island have already shown the strong dissatisfaction of the broad Taiwanese public.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","Recently, the British weekly \"The Economist\" published its latest commentary on Taiwan's political situation, rarely naming and criticizing Lai Ching-te directly as \"stubborn\" for refusing to negotiate with moderates in the Kuomintang, and describing Taiwan's political situation as \"holding Taiwan's democracy hostage.\" What is your comment on this?","Since taking office, Lai Ching-te has obstinately clung to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and has been arrogant, domineering, and abusive of power and misgovernment. In order to realize “Taiwan independence dictatorship,” he has disregarded public opinion and people's livelihood on the island, continuously stirred up political bloodbaths, arbitrarily suppressed dissenters, created “green terror” and a “chilling effect,” and aggravated internal strife and division within Taiwanese society. Lai is “fake democracy, real dictatorship,” and his notoriety has long been widespread.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783181.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","According to Taiwanese media, Taiwan’s outbound tourism deficit in the first half of this year reached 6.36 million trips. Island industry analysts attribute the gap mainly to mainland tourists being unable to visit Taiwan normally, and have called on the DPP authorities to open up mainland tourist visits to Taiwan as soon as possible. What is your comment?","We have consistently upheld the concept that “cross-strait compatriots are one family” and have actively promoted personnel exchanges across the Strait. The DPP authorities, stubbornly insisting on the “Taiwan independence” position, have long refused to open Taiwan to tourism by mainland residents. This artificially splits the cross-strait tourism market and only causes them to miss out on the huge dividend of mainland tourist sources. We advise the DPP authorities to face the livelihood demands of the island's industries, and to stop obstructing mainland residents from traveling to Taiwan under various pretexts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783178.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","August 15 this year marks the 81st anniversary of Japan's announcement of unconditional surrender. Several civil groups on the island have recently held multiple events to commemorate the victory in the War of Resistance and Taiwan's return to the embrace of the motherland. They protested the DPP authorities' downplaying of the history of the War of Resistance and their severing of the shared historical memory of…","Taiwan's pro-unification groups have commemorated the victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan through various means, including holding seminars and forums and staging rallies. They oppose the DPP authorities' downplaying of the history of the War of Resistance and glorification of Japan's colonial rule, protest Japan's renewed intervention in the Taiwan question, and call on Taiwan people to oppose and stop “Taiwan independence” forces from colluding with Japan to obstruct the reunification of the motherland and undermine peace in the Taiwan Strait. We highly appreciate these righteous actions and strongly condemn the DPP authorities' ugly conduct of betraying the nation and betraying history.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, Wu Zhaoxie (吴钊燮) accepted a media interview. Regarding the law enforcement and rights-protection operations the mainland has carried out around Taiwan island over the past two years, he falsely claimed that he is “most worried that Taiwanese people will become numb and let Chinese jurisdiction become a fact.” What is your comment on this?","Taiwan is part of China. This is an unquestionable and unchallengeable historical and legal fact. Relevant authorities carrying out law enforcement and rights-protection operations in the waters around Taiwan island in accordance with the law is a just and righteous act to defend national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, to ensure the safety of the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, and to maintain normal navigation and operational order in the relevant waters. The DPP authorities distort facts and maliciously hype the issue, attempting to manipulate “resisting China and protecting Taiwan” to seek political private gain. This is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, the mainland's Maritime Safety Administration issued a notice that, due to the impact of Typhoon “Bai Haitun,” it would impose traffic control on vessels heading north through the southern entrance of the Taiwan Strait. The Mainland Affairs Council responded: “The CCP is falsely invoking the typhoon as a pretext to declare control over the relevant waters, in violation of international norms such as the…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. China has sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. Under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and China’s domestic law, the waters of the Taiwan Strait are divided into China’s internal waters, territorial sea, contiguous zone, and exclusive economic zone. The mainland’s maritime administration agencies perform their duties in accordance with the law, and during typhoon periods, they implement necessary traffic management in the Taiwan Strait, aiming to ensure maritime traffic safety. On the one hand, the DPP authorities maliciously hype this issue, using it as an opportunity to smear and attack the mainland. On the other hand, they strive to echo external forces that sell out Taiwan’s interests, abandon their national standpoint, and harbor “Taiwan independence” malicious intent. They will surely reap what they sow.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, the DPP authorities held the so-called “Han Kuang 42 Exercise,” which for the first time included drills for throttling mobile phone networks. Society on the island has questioned whether such “network shutdown” drills, which left people unable to order takeout or use payment cards, affected normal life. What comment do you have?","The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position and vigorously promote “seeking independence through force.” They abuse power and act recklessly, which has seriously disrupted Taiwan's social tranquility and affected the daily lives and well-being of Taiwan people. So-called “drills” will only let Taiwan people further see clearly that “Taiwan independence” separatism is the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and the greatest scourge to the well-being of Taiwan people. Only by adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence” can peace and tranquility be safeguarded and people be able to live and work in peace and contentment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan media reported that Hsu Shu-po, chairman of the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce, said that to win back more cross-Strait direct flight points, he has consulted with the Mainland Affairs Council and is pushing in the direction of “charter flights first, direct flights later,” and has submitted the charter flight demand between Xi'an and Taiwan to Taiwan's civil aviation authorities for review. Are you aware of…","Relevant parties and public-spirited people in Taiwan have been running around and calling for the restoration of more direct cross-Strait links, fully reflecting the common wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait for the full normalization of direct cross-Strait air passenger services.\nThe Civil Aviation Administration of China accepted Eastern Airlines' charter flight application for Xi'an to Taoyuan. However, it is understood that Taiwan's civil aviation authority has rejected this charter application on the grounds that it does not fall within the scope of holiday charter flights. This once again proves that the so-called “charter points” that the DPP authorities have long claimed to have opened have stringent application conditions, so that the public and operators “can see them, but cannot touch them, and cannot even eat them.” The DPP authorities should face the real demand for direct cross-Strait air passenger services, follow the popular will, and promptly remove unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport, returning to compatriots on both sides of the Strait a smooth, convenient and efficient air route.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Taiwan media reported that some Taiwan businesses dismantled mainland “Chang Xue” motorcycles into components, shipped them to Taiwan in batches, and then assembled them into motorcycles, and were then seized by Taiwan’s economic authorities during an inspection. What is your comment?","Consumers hope to use high-quality products, and merchants do their best to meet this demand; this is the natural law of the market. Regarding the seizure in Taiwan of the first “Zhang Xue motorcycle” assembled by a member of the public from parts purchased by themselves, one incisive online comment reads: “The mainland is staging a myth, while Taiwan is making a fool of itself.” Out of its inherent nature of plotting “independence,” the DPP authorities obstruct and restrict the entry of high-quality mainland products into Taiwan, harming consumers’ rights and interests. Their high-handed conduct is unpopular and will only undermine and worsen Taiwan’s business environment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260819_12783180.htm"],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中国日报记者","Taiwan media reported that Taiwan’s executive authority will propose a 16% increase in the 2027 defense budget, which would push the island’s defense budget past NT$1 trillion for the first time. What is your comment?","Since taking office, the DPP authorities have stubbornly upheld a “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, going further and further in squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people and rushing down the evil path of militarism. This not only crowds out spending on the island's livelihood and social welfare and harms the immediate interests of Taiwan's people, but also steers Taiwan step by step toward the abyss of disaster, and it will certainly be repudiated by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Reports say that the DPP authorities have continued to restrict cross-Strait educational exchanges. Taiwan's education authorities have required schools to provide the daily itineraries, course topics, and visit locations of mainland trainees in Taiwan, and plan to tighten the review of applications by mainland trainees and teachers to visit Taiwan. Many programs for mainland trainees to Taiwan have been forced…","This is yet another vile act by the DPP authorities to obstruct and ban normal cross-Strait exchanges. The reciprocal dispatch of research trainees between cross-Strait universities has been practiced for many years and is an important component of cross-Strait educational exchanges. It helps promote mutual learning and exchange of academic achievements across the Strait and promotes the common development of cross-Strait education. The DPP authorities abuse power recklessly, ignoring the strong desire and practical needs of island universities to participate in cross-Strait exchanges. They frequently extend their “black hand” into cross-Strait educational exchanges, forcibly restrict Mainland students from studying in Taiwan, and coerce and lure Taiwan's education sector. This seriously harms cross-Strait educational exchanges and the legitimate rights and interests of students, and is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","The controversy over carcinogenic oil on the island continues to escalate. The DPP authorities deliberately shielded Taiwan Sugar Corporation, a state-owned enterprise involved in the case, by narrowing its reporting obligations for the problem oil it failed to report, which has sparked strong suspicion among island residents. Recent polls on the island show that nearly 60% of respondents said they are…","The carcinogenic oil issue has not been resolved to this day, which fully exposes the ugly nature of the DPP authorities: disregarding people's livelihoods, evading responsibility, and incompetent governance. It is entirely understandable that the people of Taiwan are strongly dissatisfied.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Recently, when some Taiwan residents entered Uganda, their “Taiwan passports” were confiscated and they were required to exchange them for mainland passports. Previously, some countries, including Cuba, also did not recognize “Taiwan passports.” What comments do you have on this? For Taiwan residents who have travel needs to relevant countries in the future, or who encounter similar problems…","First question: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We do not object to civil-nature economic and cultural exchanges between the Taiwan region of China and foreign countries. The DPP authorities keep exploiting convenience measures for personnel exchanges to coerce other countries and openly challenge the one-China principle, and what is ultimately harmed is the vital interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nTaiwan compatriots are citizens of China. We have always attached great importance to safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots overseas. If any Taiwan compatriot needs assistance, they may contact the Chinese embassy or consulate in the local area at any time, or call the consular protection hotline 12308.\nSecond question: From September 22 to 27 this year, the 48th WorldSkills Competition will be held in Shanghai. We look forward to brilliant performances by competitors from both sides of the Strait, and we wish them good results. Regarding matters concerning the participation of relevant personnel from the Taiwan region in the competition and related activities, we will handle them in accordance with the one-China principle and the relevant memorandum of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan region Vice President Hsiao Bi-khim told foreign media, “China's intention to seize Taiwan has long been no secret. China is adopting a two-pronged strategy: on the one hand, military intimidation, and on the other, declaring that the people of Taiwan are part of the big family of the Chinese nation.” She claimed Taiwan's strategy is to “strengthen self-defense, raise the threshold for resorting…","These remarks confuse right and wrong and harbor malicious intent. They are yet another clumsy performance by the DPP authorities aimed at misleading public opinion and deceiving the public, and they fully expose their true face as “destroyers of peace across the Strait” and “creators of the Taiwan Strait crisis.” The DPP authorities refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and stubbornly “rely on foreign forces to seek independence” and “use force to seek independence,” which will only push Taiwan further into the perilous situation of war and danger. No matter what they say or do, they cannot stop the historical trend of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nThe broad masses of Taiwan compatriots are all Chinese and members of the Chinese nation. We have always adhered to the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” actively promoting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields, and enhancing the interests and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We are willing to create broad space for peaceful reunification and strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-19","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: August 15 is the anniversary of Japan's surrender. In response to Japanese Minister of Defense Koizumi Shinjiro and others visiting the Yasukuni Shrine, the Taiwan side claimed to \"respect\" it. What comments do you have on this?\nSecond question: US President Trump, in order to promote a meeting with Kim Jong Un, has significantly reduced the scale of the US-South Korea joint military exercises.…","On the first question: regarding Japanese politicians' visits to the \"war criminal shrine,\" the relevant departments have already expressed a solemn position. Japan, as a country bearing historical responsibility on the Taiwan question, should deeply reflect on history, earnestly reflect and correct its mistakes, adhere to the one-China principle and the spirit of the four China-Japan political documents, and be prudent in its words and deeds on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities are \"fawning on Japan and nostalgic for colonialism,\" once again letting the world see their ugly face of betraying history and betraying the nation.\nOn the second question: the United States always follows \"America First,\" caring only about \"American interests.\" In the eyes of Americans, Taiwan's true value is as \"fat meat\" and an \"ATM,\" and as a pawn for containing the mainland and a tool serving the United States. For political self-interest, the Lai Ching-te authorities kowtow and cater to external forces, sucking up to and pleasing them; their subservience to and kneeling before the United States is without principle, and their selling out and harming Taiwan is without bottom line. This has already met with growing opposition from the Taiwan public, who do not want to see Taiwan go from a \"chess piece\" of the United States to an \"abandoned piece.\"\nThe press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260819_12783169.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on August 26, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Please introduce the activities of the Shanghai station of the “Together on the Same Journey: Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season.” What other activities are planned this year on the institutionalized two-way exchange platform for youth of the KMT and the CPC?","On August 25, the Shanghai stop of the “Together in Heart and Action — Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season” opened in Shanghai. The event is a concrete measure to implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech when he met with Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, and to establish an institutionalized platform for two-way exchanges between the youth of the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang. It was jointly hosted by the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, the All-China Youth Federation, the Shanghai Municipal People’s Government, the Youth Affairs Development Committee of the Kuomintang of China, the Zhonghua Qingyan Peace Education Foundation, the Youth Group of the Industrial and Commercial Construction Research Association, the Cross-Strait Peace Development Foundation, and others. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Gong Zheng, Deputy Secretary of the Shanghai Municipal Party Committee and Mayor of Shanghai; A Dong, First Secretary of the Secretariat of the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League of China; Chang Jung-kung, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China; and Lien Sheng-wu, Chairman of the Youth Affairs Development Committee of the Kuomintang of China, attended the event and delivered speeches. About 1000 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait and youth representatives attended. At the main forum, young people from both sides conducted in-depth exchanges and discussions on topics such as emerging technologies, Chinese culture, and cross-strait youth exchanges. They will also visit and study in Shanghai, Zhejiang, and other places, fully demonstrating the positive and upward-looking spirit of young people across the Strait working hand in hand. The event will continue until August 28.\nGoing forward, through the institutionalized platform for two-way exchanges between the Communist Party and the Kuomintang, we will invite more delegations to visit and exchange views on the mainland, with rich and varied content. We also sincerely invite young Taiwan friends to come to the mainland to take a look and see for themselves. We hope that young people on both sides of the Strait will work hand in hand to continuously gather youthful strength for promoting the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784589.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","The New Party held its 33rd anniversary celebration on August 22, stating that the New Party will uphold its stance and firmly promote the unification of the Chinese nation. In addition, the event was originally planned to be held at CPC Corporation, Taiwan. Reports say that due to DPP suppression, CPC Corporation breached its contract at the last minute, and the event had to be urgently moved to another venue.…","Resolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the common aspiration of all Chinese sons and daughters. The motherland must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified. More and more Taiwan compatriots, including those in the New Party, have come to recognize that cross-strait reunification is a historical trend that no person or force can stop. On the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to continue working with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals, including the New Party, to jointly promote the peaceful development of cross-strait relations, jointly create the historic cause of reunifying the motherland, and jointly share the great glory of national rejuvenation.\nThe DPP authorities are defying the trend of history and obstinately holding to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position. By any means, they are attacking and persecuting political opponents, including unificationists on the island, and vigorously carrying out “green terror.” This fully exposes their vile essence of fake democracy and real dictatorship, and of pretending to protect Taiwan while actually harming it. They will inevitably be spurned by history and by the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784588.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Recently, at the “8·23 Artillery Battle 68th Anniversary” event in Kinmen, Lai Ching-te again rehashed the “new two-state theory” and clamored for “resisting unification by force,” saying the island should “support national defense, defend the nation, and safeguard democracy.” What is your comment on this?","Lai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” constantly spreads “Taiwan independence” fallacies and heretical theories, deliberately distorts history, vigorously hypes the so-called “China threat,” and continuously incites “anti-China and resisting China,” attempting to “resist unification by force” and “seek independence by force,” pushing Taiwan step by step into the perilous situation of war. He is, without any exaggeration, a “destroyer of peace across the Taiwan Strait” and a “creator of the Taiwan Strait crisis.”\nWe solemnly warn Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities: the trend toward unification is irresistible, and “seeking independence by force” will only hasten their own destruction. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the deceptiveness and harmfulness of Lai Ching-te’s provocations to seek independence, join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism, and with concrete actions safeguard their own security and well-being and the peace and stability of the Taiwan Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784587.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","香港经济导报记者","Recently, the Taiwan Industrial Association released the “2026 TIA White Paper,” whose cross-Strait policy is themed “Confident and Steady, Building a New Pattern for Cross-Strait Development.” It recommends that the DPP authorities simplify the review process for mainland professionals visiting Taiwan, and hopes to create more stable cross-Strait relations through civil exchanges. What comments do you have on this?","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family and should frequently visit and draw close to one another. Taiwan's business and industrial circles hope for smooth and active cross-Strait exchanges, which is the will of the people and the trend of the times. For a long time, we have adhered to the concept of “cross-Strait families are one,” actively promoted exchanges and cooperation between the two sides in all fields, and continuously taken measures to provide convenience for exchanges between people on both sides. We hope the DPP authorities will listen to the voices of the business community and, as soon as possible, cancel unreasonable restrictive measures that hinder cross-Strait exchanges, so as to facilitate cross-Strait exchange and integration.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784583.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","The Ministry of Public Security's “Measures for Supervision and Inspection of Cyberspace Security by Public Security Organs,” will take effect on October 1. The DPP authorities said that the mainland is building an “authoritarian legal toolchain that is strict and tight from the inside out,” and that Taiwanese people going to the mainland must carefully assess whether it is necessary and must not underestimate…","Recently, the Ministry of Public Security issued the departmental rule “Measures for the Supervision and Inspection of Cyberspace Security by Public Security Organs.” These Measures apply to public security organs carrying out supervision and inspection in accordance with law of how network operators, data processors, and personal information processors perform their data security obligations, and they standardize public security law enforcement conduct. Formulating these Measures helps supervise network operators, data processors, personal information processors, and others, strengthens security protection of networks, data, and personal information, jointly guards against telecommunications network fraud and other illegal and criminal acts, and safeguards national security and public social interests.\nThe relevant remarks by the DPP authorities are complete fabrication and slander, aimed at muddying the waters. It is precisely the DPP authorities who have extended the “black hand” into people’s lives and are the greatest culprit. They repeatedly rehash the false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism,” deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation, and obstruct, restrict, and undermine cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. On the island, they wantonly trample democracy, undermine the rule of law, restrict freedoms, and vigorously carry out a “green terror.” Recently, they have repeatedly demanded that Taiwan civil servants who wish to visit relatives on the mainland provide data such as lists of relatives and friends and phone numbers, and required schools on the island that wish to engage in exchanges on the mainland to register on the website of the Mainland Affairs Council, and so on. Such wanton infringement of the personal privacy of Taiwan residents: what qualifications and face do the DPP authorities have to talk so lightly about “information security”?","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784584.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, Liu Shih-fang, head of Taiwan’s competent authority for internal affairs, said that since the restrictions on the Xiaohongshu app last December, the number of fraud cases has dropped by 80% and the amount of fraud has dropped by 55%, which is very effective. Now, in accordance with procedures, a registered letter is being sent to Xiaohongshu again, and if it still ignores this, it will likely be blocked…","The data you mentioned were self-written and self-directed by the DPP authorities, with the aim of fabricating pretexts to ban mainland social media platforms and incite antagonism and confrontation across the Strait. The DPP authorities brazenly deprive the people of Taiwan, especially young people, of their right to know and their freedom to use social media platforms, and brazenly obstruct communication between young people on both sides of the Strait, which is completely unpopular. Their perverse actions cannot stop the enthusiasm of Taiwan people to communicate through mainland social media platforms, nor can they stop the popular trend of people on both sides of the Strait drawing closer together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","The 30th Lu-Tai Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference will be held soon; please introduce the relevant information.","From August 31 to September 3, the 30th Shandong-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference will be held in Weifang and other places in Shandong. The conference is co-hosted by the Shandong Provincial People’s Government and the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office, with the theme “Seizing the Momentum to Forge Ahead in the ‘15th Five-Year Plan’; Shandong and Taiwan Jointly Paint a New Picture.” The main venue will be set up in Weifang City, hosting the opening ceremony and theme event of the Cross-Strait Conference on High-Quality Development of Industrial Integration, as well as thematic events on modern agriculture, green chemicals, marine health, intelligent manufacturing, youth entrepreneurship, vocational education, and more. Concurrently, sub-venues will be set up in Zibo, Jining, Dezhou, Heze and other cities to hold a series of cross-Strait exchange activities. The aim is to promote economic, trade, and cultural exchange and cooperation between Shandong and Taiwan, and to build a new landscape of integrated development between Shandong and Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","The first Cross-Strait Film Exchange Conference was recently held in Beijing and was welcomed by film and television practitioners on both sides. A Taiwanese creator said that cross-Strait film and television exchanges had been interrupted for many years, and that they look forward to resuming exchanges and dialogue through formal platforms, bringing more cooperation possibilities to cross-Strait film and…","To implement the ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, which were authorized for release by the Central Taiwan Work Office, the first Cross-Strait Film Exchange Conference was held in Beijing on August 20–21. It was guided by the National Film Administration and sponsored by the Cross-Strait Exchange Fund of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits, and it drew attention from the film circles on both sides. Under the theme “Sailing Together in Light and Shadow,” the event held sub-events including a cross-Strait film project pitching conference, a cross-Strait film and television industry forum, and a master class lecture for cross-Strait filmmakers. More than 170 representatives from the cross-Strait film and television industries attended. Fourteen original cross-Strait co-produced film projects were presented and promoted, and the “Cross-Strait Film Project Sailing Together Award” was selected from them. This is also the first award established for cross-Strait cooperative co-produced film projects.\nWe have consistently supported cross-Strait film exchanges. The long-running flagship project, the “Cross-Strait Film Festival,” is very popular on the island. Cross-Strait film and television exchange activities built on mainland film festivals and film awards have been held continuously, such as the Golden Rooster Awards, which set up a Taiwan film showcase segment; the Shanghai International Film Festival, which screened cross-Strait co-created films; and the Silk Road International Film Festival, which set up a cross-Strait film exchange section.\nThe DPP authorities have disregarded the calls of the industry and the public, obstructed cross-Strait film exchanges, and engaged in political manipulation. To this day they still impose various unreasonable restrictions on the public screening of mainland films in Taiwan. The DPP authorities should promptly lift these restrictions and stop obstructing cross-Strait film and television cultural exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784585.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan's education authorities said that, in cooperation with the Mainland Affairs Council, they have established a “registration platform,” and schools on the island that go to the mainland for exchanges must report information on this platform. If the reported information is false, they will consider deducting future exchange subsidies or activity equipment for schools. This move has again caused some…","The DPP authorities have left no stone unturned in undermining normal cross-Strait exchanges in education and among young students. This fully exposes their sinister intention to obstruct personnel exchanges and all other forms of cross-Strait exchange and cooperation, and to escalate confrontation and antagonism across the Strait.\nFacts have repeatedly proven that the DPP authorities are the greatest obstacle to cross-Strait exchanges and interactions and the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Wanting peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion on the island. The desire of compatriots on both sides to draw closer and the trend toward cross-Strait exchange and cooperation are irresistible. Any act that turns back the wheel of history and defies the will of the people will ultimately be rejected by public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784582.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","上海东方卫视记者","The Shanghai leg of the Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season opened yesterday (August 25). The Mainland Affairs Council said, “Exchanges are exchanges; do not go along with the CCP's narratives and propositions,” and said it will continue to monitor this event. What is your comment?","Strengthening cooperation and exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait is an irresistible historical trend, and it also accords with mainstream public opinion on the island. In particular, young people on both sides shoulder the hopes of the nation and the future of the Chinese people. Letting them strengthen exchanges and deepen mutual understanding is a “hope project” that benefits the present and will be remembered for generations, serving the nation’s prosperity and rejuvenation. We advise the DPP authorities to listen more to the mainstream public opinion on the island, do more things that benefit cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and do less to undermine and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, district prosecutors' offices across Taiwan have successively mailed election inspection and advocacy letters to village chief candidates in their jurisdictions. The letters include content such as “mainland interference in elections” and “must not violate the Anti-Infiltration Act.” Public opinion on the island holds that this is “using fake advocacy as a cover for intimidation,” while the Mainland…","Every time there is an island-wide election, the DPP deliberately manipulates “resisting China and defending Taiwan” and slanders “mainland interference in the election” in order to seek political gain. This time, it went so far as to deploy prosecutorial and judicial organs to threaten and intimidate the public and extensively create a “green terror.” This despicable practice of the DPP is being seen through and spurned by more and more Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the General Administration of Customs website announced the addition of a batch of registrations for Taiwan pomelo packing plants and orchards. Please explain the relevant situation.","We have consistently upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” and have made our utmost efforts to do practical good deeds, help, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. Since the Central Taiwan Affairs Office was authorized to announce ten measures to promote cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in April this year, relevant parties on both sides have, on the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” promoted the detailed implementation of various measures and achieved positive results. On the premise of complying with relevant Mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we welcome more high-quality Taiwan products to be sold to the Mainland, so that compatriots on both sides can share the dividends of the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202608/t20260826_12784586.htm"],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Regarding the Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson’s criticism of the DPP authorities for forcibly restricting mainland students from studying and conducting research in Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council responded that Taiwan’s policy on mainland research trainees has been consistent, that this is not a problem at all, and that what Taiwan lacks is degree students. It is the mainland side that does not allow…","This claim is a sheer distortion of right and wrong. In recent years, the Democratic Progressive Party authorities have obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and have disregarded the strong desire of Taiwan's education community and young students to participate in cross-Strait exchanges. They have gone to great lengths to suppress and restrict cross-Strait education exchanges and cooperation. As everyone knows, they have banned higher education institutions on the island from exchanges and cooperation with 10 mainland schools, including Jinan University and Beijing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics, and have used various pretexts to obstruct cross-Strait education exchanges and cooperation at the primary, secondary and tertiary levels. They have imposed a range of unreasonable measures and restrictions on mainland students studying in Taiwan, including in scholarships, internships and national health insurance, and have subjected them to many unfair treatments, seriously harming the rights and interests of mainland students studying in Taiwan.\nThe actions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities are the fundamental obstacle affecting mainland students' study in Taiwan. Their bans, restrictions and blockade of cross-Strait education exchanges have drawn widespread opposition from the island's education community. We advise the Democratic Progressive Party authorities to stop political manipulation as soon as possible, genuinely protect the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan, and restore normal cross-Strait education exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Recently, Xiamen in Fujian announced new measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, including advancing construction of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Xiamen section), striving for the main sea route to open to traffic by the end of this year, and simultaneously advancing research on the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Kinmen section) plan. The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that the issue of linking…","Building the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge is the shared call and urgent wish of the people of Xiamen and Kinmen. The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Integrated Development across the Taiwan Strait and Building a Demonstration Zone for Integrated Cross-Strait Development,” issued in 2023, clearly proposed to “explore a model of joint Xiamen-Kinmen cooperation in building infrastructure and accelerate the connection of Kinmen to electricity, gas, and bridges.” Among these, the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge (Xiamen section) project began construction in October 2023 and is currently advancing in an orderly manner. Once the full Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge opens to traffic, it will bring convenience to people traveling between the two places, add impetus to Kinmen's economic development and improvement of people's livelihoods, and the two places of Xiamen and Kinmen will become a closer “one-city living circle.” After the bridge is completed, water, electricity, and natural gas can be delivered to Kinmen through pipelines in the bridge, improving Kinmen's development environment. It will also complement the maritime “Mini Three Links” and other sea routes, adding passage routes between Xiamen and Kinmen. The DPP authorities should face up to the interests and demands of Kinmen compatriots, stop political calculations, genuinely act for the people's benefit, and support the early completion and opening of the Xiamen-Kinmen Bridge.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","To remedy the decline of Penghu’s tourism market, the Penghu County Tourism Association recently visited the MAC and hoped to restart the Penghu “Mini Three Links.” The DPP authorities responded that, given security concerns and the continued harassment of Taiwan by mainland military aircraft and vessels, there are currently no plans to open the Penghu “Mini Three Links.” What is your comment on this?","The “small three links” routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between the two sides, especially between the people of Fujian and Taiwan. They are livelihood channels and kinship routes connecting the people on both sides, and have played an important role in deepening cross-Strait integrated development and advancing the well-being of the people. We have actively promoted the resumption of tourism by residents of Shanghai and Fujian to Kinmen and Matsu, which has been warmly welcomed by Taiwan residents. Since August 2024, residents of Shanghai and Fujian have traveled to Kinmen and Matsu via the “small three links” routes, totaling about 350,000 person-times.\nThe mainland side has always upheld the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” and has made continuous efforts to promote personnel exchanges across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities disregard the will of the people and engage in political manipulation, which lacks popular support.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Recently, exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait have continued to be lively.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, from August 13 to 15, the 15th Cross-Strait Hospital Directors Forum was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, to explore a path for coordinated and innovative development of cross-Strait medical care. More than 650 people from both sides attended, including 250 Taiwan compatriots from over 100 relevant associations and institutions. From August 17 to 19, the 2nd Cross-Strait Forum on the Development of the Three Teas was held in Xiamen, Fujian, attended by over 200 experts and scholars from both sides, tea enterprise representatives, and intangible cultural heritage inheritors. From August 18 to 20, the 5th Cross-Strait (Sanming) Rural Integration Development Forum was held in Sanming, Fujian. About 600 Taiwan compatriots were invited to attend, and 27 Mainland-Taiwan cooperation achievements in seven fields were released. From August 20 to 23, the 2026 Henan-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference and Cross-Strait Intelligent Equipment Manufacturing Matchmaking Event was held in Hebi, Henan. Industry representatives from both sides held seminars, exchanges, and cooperation matchmaking. From August 26 to September 1, the 2nd Guizhou-Taiwan Youth Big Data Industry Development Exchange Week, themed “Data Showcases Guizhou’s Colors · Jointly Promoting Integration,” was held in Guizhou.\nIn cultural exchanges, from August 15 to 19, the 2nd Cross-Strait Folk Customs and Sports Exchange on the South China Sea (Yangjiang) Fishing Season Folk Culture Exchange event was held in Yangjiang, Guangdong. More than 600 guests and youth representatives from both sides attended. From August 16 to 20, the Cross-Strait (Zherong) Mazu Faith Culture Activity Week was held in Ningde, Fujian. More than 100 Taiwan compatriots took part, including Taiwan experts and scholars, Taoist temples, and believers. From August 18 to 21, the 5th Cross-Strait Poetry and Couplet Culture Exchange event was held in Putian, Fujian. More than 200 people from poetry circles on both sides gathered on Meizhou Island. On August 20, the 4th Cross-Strait Youth Grand Canal Culture Exchange event opened in Tianjin. From August 20 to 27, the “Music Moves Haicang” 2026 Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Chinese Folk Music Exchange Series was held in Haicang, Xiamen. From August 21 to 23, the 9th Nan’an Zheng Chenggong Culture Week was held in Nan’an, Quanzhou, Fujian, the hometown of Zheng Chenggong. More than 400 Taiwan guests were invited. During the same period, the 3rd “Minnan Soul” Minnan Dialect Choral Art Performance was held in Zhangzhou, Fujian. Six Taiwan choirs, with more than 200 Taiwan compatriots, performed classic Minnan dialect songs in choral form together with 20 local choirs. From August 21 to 27, the “Father’s Grassland, Mother’s River” music collection activity by compatriots on both sides was held in Inner Mongolia. From August 22 to 27, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Fujian) Academy Culture Exchange, themed “Seeking Roots in Minnan · Books Connecting Both Sides,” was held in Xiamen, Fujian.\nIn youth exchanges, on August 20, the Cross-Strait Youth Thematic Exchange Camp “Realizing Dreams in the Greater Bay Area · Integrating to Create the Future” was launched in Shenzhen. More than 120 youth representatives from both sides took part and immersively learned about the Greater Bay Area’s achievements in information technology, artificial intelligence, cultural creativity, and other fields. From August 21 to 28, the “Visiting Wuhu, Feeling Hometown Affection” summer camp for Taiwan youth was held in Wuhu, Anhui. From August 26 to 29, the “Qing Wang Qin Hao · Walking Together with Heartfelt Care” cross-Strait youth volunteer service exchange activity was held in Suqian, Jiangsu.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中国网记者","The 2026 Cross-Strait Relations Seminar opened in Wuhan on the 20th, and several Taiwan scholars were invited to attend. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 2026 Cross-Strait Relations Symposium was held in Wuhan, Hubei Province, from August 20 to 21. More than 160 people from both sides of the Taiwan Strait, including relevant personnel, experts and scholars, attended this important academic exchange across the Strait.\nThe symposium took “Upholding National Righteousness and Jointly Pursuing the Great Cause of National Rejuvenation” as its theme. Participants conducted in-depth discussions around topics such as “Firmly Holding Correct Identity and Safeguarding Our Common Home” and “Deepening Exchange and Integration and Cultivating Kinship and Well-Being.” Many participants said that General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech at the celebration of the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China points the way for the development of cross-Strait relations. They said that the mainland has successfully charted a path of Chinese-style modernization, whose economic development has strong momentum and abundant vitality, opening broad prospects for the development of cross-Strait relations and the rejuvenation of the nation. They held that compatriots on both sides are members of one family and should work together for national rejuvenation and national reunification. They stressed that compatriots on both sides should firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism, expand exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, continuously enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, maintain peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and well safeguard the common great home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Recently, the concert “Echoes of Mountains and Seas, Songs Through the Seasons — Classic Cross-Strait Folk Song Concert” was held in Beijing, and the audience response was enthusiastic. Please introduce the relevant details.","The concert “Echoes of Mountains and Seas, Songs Across Four Seasons: Classic Voices of Cross-Strait Folk Songs,” co-hosted by the Movie Channel, China Foreign Culture Group Co., Ltd., and Phoenix Television, was successfully held in Beijing recently. Centered on the narrative of “One Mountain and River, Songs Across Four Seasons,” the concert was jointly created by professional teams from both sides of the Strait, and more than 20 well-known artists from both sides and nearly 300 members of choirs and symphony orchestras from both sides took part in the performance. Everyone joined hands to sing classic melodies together and sing of the brocade-like rivers and mountains of the Chinese land and the changing of the four seasons, expressing the theme of “letting Chinese culture shine in the hearts of Chinese people on both sides of the Strait.” It paid tribute to the spirit of the Taiwan folk song movement 50 years ago, “singing our own Chinese songs,” and enhanced the shared memories and emotional resonance of compatriots on both sides. The concert will be produced and broadcast; stay tuned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar recently said in an interview that Taiwan is part of China, and that if a Malaysian state insists on splitting away, he will also defend the sanctity and unity of the nation. The Taiwan foreign affairs authorities responded that this remark demeans Taiwan’s “sovereignty” and may adversely affect the confidence of Taiwan businesses investing in Malaysia. What is your comment on this?","We appreciate the position of the relevant countries in adhering to the one-China principle.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. Taiwan has no “sovereignty” whatsoever. The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” position and spread “Taiwan independence” fallacies everywhere; at the slightest provocation they use economic, trade and investment pressure against relevant countries, which precisely exposes the essence of their “seeking independence through economics.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","The Mainland Affairs Council recently released its latest poll showing that 70% of Taiwanese people believe the mainland’s dispatch of coast guard ships to patrol the waters off eastern Taiwan is “malicious.” Although the mainland has said that the relevant law enforcement is a countermeasure against Japan and the Philippines’ “maritime delimitation” behavior, the Taiwan side says this is a way to advance “gray…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Mainland coast guard enforcement patrols in the relevant waters, exercising jurisdiction in accordance with the law, are a just and righteous act to defend national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, to safeguard the lives and property of fishermen on both sides of the Strait, and to maintain normal navigation and operational order in the relevant waters.\nThe DPP authorities designed and released this public opinion poll with malicious intent. The DPP authorities habitually use so-called “gray zone harassment” to attack and smear the mainland, deliberately exaggerate the “mainland threat,” incite “anti-China” sentiment, and stir up confrontation across the Strait. People on both sides of the Strait express strong dissatisfaction with the DPP authorities’ despicable conduct of abandoning their own stance and selling out the interests of the nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-08-26","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","On the first question: following the claims that “mainlanders can't afford tea eggs” and “China's high-speed rail has no backrest,” a program on the island recently featured someone claiming that “Beijing doesn't even have refrigerators” and that “Beijingers don't drink cold beverages.” What comments does the spokesperson have on this? Does this reflect the significant gap between the perceptions of some people…","On the first question: Statements that depart from facts will only become a laughingstock. The DPP authorities have deliberately banned and obstructed cross-Strait exchanges and contacts, deliberately created information cocoons on the island, and attempted to block Taiwan residents from understanding the mainland, with sinister intent. We welcome Taiwan residents to break through the barriers, come to the mainland more often to look and see, and understand the real and lovable mainland.\nOn the second question: During this year's Straits Forum, we held a signing ceremony for the matching of ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, to help Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products expand their market on the mainland, so that Taiwan farmers and fishermen can truly share the dividends of peaceful development across the Strait. After the signing ceremony, relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” actively promoted the steady implementation of the signed matters. Recently, the General Administration of Customs newly announced the registration of a batch of pomelo orchards and packaging plants in Taiwan, making it more convenient for more Taiwan businesses to sell pomelos to the mainland. We will continue to implement the ten measures to benefit and bring good fortune to compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nThis press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202608/t20260826_12784575.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-08-27","Lin Jian","NHK","We have learned that a group of Japanese lawmakers visiting China met today with an official of the International Department of the CPC Central Committee. Could you provide more details about the meeting? Does the foreign ministry have any comment on it?","Chinese competent authorities will release information on the meeting in due course. The root cause of the serious difficulties in bilateral relations lies in the erroneous remarks and actions on Taiwan and in the fields of military and security made by those running the Japanese government. They should heed and value the voice of reason in Japan, do serious soul-searching, correct the wrongdoings, abide by the four political documents, and safeguard the political foundation of China-Japan relations with concrete actions.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202608/t20260827_12011637.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202608/t20260827_12011623.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, the Taiwan administrative agency on August 20 passed the fiscal year 2027 general budget proposal. The DPP authorities in the Taiwan region have pegged overall so-called defense spending at NT$1.1225 trillion, up NT$173 billion from fiscal year 2026, an increase of 18.2% — the first time the figure has crossed the NT$1 trillion threshold and set a record high. The so-called defense…","Peace, development, exchanges and cooperation represent the mainstream public will in Taiwan society. The Lai Ching-te authorities, driven by the partisan and personal interests of the DPP alone, act against the tide—vainly currying favor with and pandering to external forces, recklessly squandering the people's hard-earned wealth, and rushing headlong down the reactionary path of arms expansion. This gravely undermines the livelihood and well-being of our compatriots on the island, will ultimately drain Taiwan's coffers, and the DPP authorities are bound to be spurned by the public and meet their defeat.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media outlets in Taiwan, China and Indonesia have carried out maritime exercises in waters to the east of Taiwan Island, which is a political manipulation to expand presence under the pretext of exercise. A US State Department spokesperson claimed that relevant countries should seek a peaceful resolution of the Taiwan question, instead of peddling narratives that the mainland may undermine peace and…","Taiwan is part of China. China has an exclusive economic zone and a continental shelf in waters to the east of Taiwan Island. The exercise conducted by the navies of China and Indonesia in the waters is completely justified, lawful, and necessary. It further enhances integrated combat capabilities and promotes pragmatic cooperation, which is conducive to maintaining regional peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. Firstly, it was reported that Chinese Defense Minister Dong Jun recently paid a visit to Timor-Leste and went to Indonesia to attend the Second Ministerial Meeting of China-Indonesia Joint Foreign and Defense Ministerial Dialogue. Please share more information with us. Secondly, on August 23rd, Lai Ching-te claimed that the DPP authorities will not yield an inch of Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen,…","On your first question, upon invitation, Defense Minister Dong Jun recently visited Timor-Leste and went to Indonesia for the Second Ministerial Meeting of China-Indonesia Joint Foreign and Defense Ministerial Dialogue. These are concrete steps implementing the important consensus between the leaders of China and Timor-Leste, and China and Indonesia. The visits will further deepen mutual trust on security and defense cooperation, and contribute to building a community with a shared future with neighboring countries.\nThe relationship between China and Timor-Leste is stronger than ever before. During this first Chinese defense minister's visit to Timor-Leste, Minister Dong Jun held separate meetings with the President and the Prime Minister of Timor-Leste. The two sides had in-depth exchanges on bilateral relations and military-to-military ties, the international and regional situation, and other issues of shared interest. They agreed to further deepen defense cooperation in both bilateral and multilateral formats, and elevate the military-to-military relationship to a higher level.\nIn recent years, bilateral defense cooperation between China and Indonesia has improved in both quality and efficiency, setting an example for new-type defense cooperation among the Global South and major developing countries. China will work with Indonesia to advance cooperation in defense and military development from a strategic perspective, further tap the potential of defense cooperation, and promote regular and institutionalized cooperation on defense equipment and technology, joint exercises and training, personnel training, and maritime security. The two sides will continue these efforts to provide solid security safeguards for their respective development, play a key role in regional stability, and inject more stability, certainty, and constructive factors into a world marked by transformation and disruption.\nOn your second question, there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu are all parts of China. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te's deliberate distortion of history and his attempts to stir up cross-strait confrontation and antagonism go against the will of the people and will find no support. We hope that our fellow compatriots in the Taiwan region will join hands with us to oppose and strike the \"Taiwan independence separatist forces, firmly oppose interference by external forces, resolutely advance the great cause of national reunification, and work together for peace across the Taiwan Strait and for the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to media reports, several Japanese politicians visited the Yasukuni Shrine, which enshrines Class-A war criminals, on August 15th, the anniversary of Japan's surrender. Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi offered a ritual offering fee. Rather than condemning the move, the DPP authorities in Taiwan went so far as to claim that they respect the diverse views in Japanese society on historical issues. What's your…","The Yasukuni Shrine is a veritable shrine for war criminals and a house for summoning the soul of militarism. Japanese politicians' repeated collective \"worship of the dead\" tramples wantonly on the feelings of people across the Asia-Pacific, grossly profanes historical justice, and lays bare the true nature of Japan's right-wing forces, who cling to the obsession of reviving militarism and the inherent instinct for external aggression and expansion. The international community must heighten its vigilance and firmly check such moves.\nBeyond the 14 convicted Class A war criminals, the shrine also honors war criminals such as Rikichi Ando and Nogi Maresuke, whose hands were stained with the blood of our compatriots in Taiwan. The DPP authorities in the Taiwan region, by fawning over Japan and worshipping the colonizer while treating the aggressor as kin, have sunk to a despicable low. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will stand as upright Chinese nationals, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" separatism and external interference, and actively join the just cause of the motherland's peaceful reunification.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to data published by Taiwan's defense authorities, their troops have detected 1,334 sorties of PLA military aircraft in the first half of this year. The number has fallen by more than half year-on-year. During this period, the PLA has not carried out any large military exercises around the island. But the Chinese government vessels have stepped up their operations in the waters around Taiwan. Some…","China's national reunification is an overwhelming historical trend. As we build a great country and advance national rejuvenation, we will enhance our capability to resolve the Taiwan question and have stronger capabilities and more reliable means at our disposal. No matter how many exercises they carry out, the doomed fate of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces can never be changed. The PLA will temper and sharpen its combat capabilities, serve as a powerful guarantee for national reunification, resolutely smash any \"Taiwan independence\" separatist plot, and firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[1,"2026-08-27","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to Taiwan media, the first two single-seat fighters from the 66 brand-new F-16V Block 70 jets the DPP authorities in the Taiwan region bought from the US under the so-called \"Feng Xiang Project\" are about to be handed over to the Taiwan side. What's your comment on that?","China firmly opposes US arms sales to China's Taiwan region. This position is consistent and unequivocal. \"Taiwan independence\" is utterly incompatible with peace in the Taiwan Strait. Arming Taiwan to abet \"Taiwan independence\" separatists will only lead to playing with fire and getting burned, and leave them to taste the bitter fruit of their own making. We urge the US side to honor the one-China principle and the provisions of the three China-US joint communiqués, particularly the August 17th Communiqué of 1982, stop arming Taiwan in whatever form, and stop disrupting cross-Strait peace and stability.","","http://eng.mod.gov.cn/2025xb/P/16483651.html","http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/xwfyr/lxjzhzt/2026lxjzh/2026n8y/16481856.html",0,1,1,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 2, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Recently, the 30th Lu-Taiwan Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference was held in Shandong, and Taiwan businesses and enterprises actively participated. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On August 31, the 30th Lu-Tai Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference, co-hosted by the People's Government of Shandong Province and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, opened in Weifang, Shandong. Around 800 people from all sectors across the Strait attended, including Zhang Ping, vice chairman on the mainland side of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit; Song Tao, director of the Central Taiwan Work Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Lin Wu, Party Secretary of Shandong Province; Hsiao Hsu-tsen, vice chairman of the Kuomintang; Mao Zhiguo, vice chairman on the Taiwan side of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit; Li Zhenghong, president of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises; Hsu Shu-po, chairman of the Taiwan Chamber of Commerce; and Lei Hongyi, chairman of the Taiwan Industrial and Commercial Construction Research Association.\nSince 1994 the Lu-Tai Economic and Trade Negotiation Conference has been held 30 times, making it one of the longest-running cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities. This session carried out six thematic matchmaking sessions in fields including modern agriculture, green chemicals, the marine economy, intelligent manufacturing, youth entrepreneurship and vocational education, and organized multiple exchange activities at sub-venues in Zibo, Jining, Dezhou, Heze and other places, producing a series of cooperation results. Enterprises, associations and universities from both sides signed seven cooperation agreements or memoranda in areas such as park construction, joint ventures and technological cooperation, and unveiled one school-enterprise innovation practice base.\nDuring the event, Shandong also introduced 11 policy measures for the “15th Five-Year Plan” period to support Taiwan businesses and enterprises in developing in Shandong. They cover project investment, agricultural cooperation, technological innovation, financial services and other areas, so that Taiwan businesses and enterprises can better integrate into Shandong's economic and social development, achieve greater and better development of their own, and open a new chapter of Lu-Tai economic and trade cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","On August 26, a mudslide occurred on the Nepali side, causing casualties and missing persons at the Jilong Port in Rikaze City, Xizang. After the disaster, Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Chinese Nationalist Party, people from all walks of life in Taiwan, and Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises on the mainland all expressed concern and sympathy, and donated money to the affected areas and people.…","After the debris flow disaster in Jilong County, Rikaze City, Xizang, General Secretary Xi Jinping attached great importance to it and issued important instructions, and Premier Li Qiang went to the disaster area on the General Secretary's behalf to guide the rescue and disaster relief work. We have launched a Level II national disaster relief emergency response, and all parties are fully mobilized for rescue efforts to do their utmost to protect the lives and property of the people.\nIt is understood that, as of now, no Taiwan compatriots have been killed, injured or reported missing due to the disaster. We will continue to follow the situation of Taiwan compatriots in the area and provide necessary assistance in a timely manner. People from all sectors in Taiwan, as well as Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-invested enterprises on the mainland, have expressed their concern and condolences through various forms, reflecting the fraternal bond between both sides of the Strait, where blood is thicker than water and they look out for one another. We express our sincere thanks for this.\nRecently, southern Taiwan has suffered several consecutive heavy rainfalls, seriously affecting the production and daily life of local residents. We extend our condolences to the compatriots affected by the disaster and are willing to provide help, and we hope they will quickly restore normal order in production and daily life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785959.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, Xiamen, Fujian, established the first batch of “Taiwan Compatriot Financial Service Centers” to facilitate financial business for Taiwan compatriots, which has been welcomed by local Taiwan compatriots. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To implement the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone,” Xiamen, relying on bank outlets, has established “Taiwan Compatriot Financial Service Centers.” The first batch of 10 outlets is located at airports and ports, tourist attractions, major commercial districts, government service centers, Taiwan business associations' halls, and other places frequently visited by Taiwan compatriots. Centered on the practical needs of Taiwan compatriots for tourism, sightseeing, and settling down to live and work, the service centers provide integrated services and standardized procedures to facilitate Taiwan compatriots in handling all kinds of financial business, including opening accounts, currency exchange, mobile payment, fund transfers, home purchase and property investment, and wealth management and entrepreneurship. This better meets Taiwan compatriots' financial needs for living and developing in Xiamen, and builds a financial service home exclusively for Taiwan compatriots, with proactive outreach, one-stop integration, standard procedures, and services that are tangible and accessible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, the General Administration of Customs website announced the registration of a batch of new packaging plants and orchards for Taiwan pomelo, which drew attention on the island. Will more Taiwan counties and cities' pomelos be approved for import to the mainland?","In April this year, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office was authorized to announce ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, including facilitating the import of Taiwanese agricultural and fishery products that meet inspection and quarantine standards into the mainland. During this year's Straits Forum, we held a signing event to connect with the ten policy measures promoting cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, creating a platform to open up mainland markets for Taiwan's distinctive agricultural and fishery products. Following the announcement on August 25 of a batch of registrations for Taiwan pomelo packaging plants and orchards, the General Administration of Customs announced on September 1 a new batch of registrations for Taiwan pomelo orchards and packaging plants, providing convenience for more Taiwan businesses to sell pomelos to the mainland.\nWe will do our utmost to do practical things, good things, and things that solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. On the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” and on the premise of complying with relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we will work together with relevant parties on the island to help more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products and quality products enter households across the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785960.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, MAC Deputy Minister Shen Yu-chung said that the mainland has recently issued regulations on online and entry-exit management, among others, whose enforcement standards are vague, and that it cannot rule out more negative impacts on cross-Strait exchanges. He called for cross-Strait exchanges to be “depoliticized, de-risked, and healthy and orderly.” What is your comment on this?","The relevant regulations have a legal basis and are open and transparent. The formulation of measures for supervision and inspection of cyberspace security helps strengthen the security protection of networks, data, and personal information, jointly prevent telecom network fraud and other illegal crimes, and safeguard national security and public social interests. The provisions on exit and entry administration are intended to standardize the mainland's exit and entry administration, protect the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting and entering, and safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. They also create a better rule-of-law environment for Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland.\nThe various claims of the DPP authorities are entirely deliberate misleading and intentional smears. Frequent visits and exchanges help compatriots on both sides of the Strait understand each other and promote cooperation, and civilian exchanges across the Strait have strong internal momentum. The DPP authorities should follow the will and sentiment of the people and not use various means to interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation or incite confrontation and antagonism between the two sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785958.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Recently, the Lai Ching-te authorities declared that Taiwan’s 2027 defense budget will break through NT$1 trillion for the first time. “We must turn all defense resources into reliable defensive combat capability,” and must not let the mainland misjudge “Taiwan’s determination to defend itself.” What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities of Lai Ching-te have obstinately adhered to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position and disregarded the mainstream public opinion on the island, which calls for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation. They have persistently incited confrontation and antagonism between the two sides, lavishly squandered public funds, and attempted to “resist unification through force” and “pursue independence through force.” This is purely an overestimation of their own capabilities, and it will only bring profound disaster to the people of Taiwan.\nOur determination to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity is firm and unwavering, and our capacity to do so is immensely strong. We will never leave any room for any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. We hope that the broad masses of compatriots in Taiwan will clearly recognize the extreme harm and danger of “Taiwan independence” separatism, resolutely oppose the conduct of “Taiwan independence” separatism, and firmly safeguard our common homeland of the Chinese nation and our own security and well-being.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785961.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, the 2nd World Humanoid Robot Games were held in Beijing, attracting widespread global attention. Public opinion on the island has praised the mainland's robotics technology for taking major strides toward being more refined, more intelligent, and more practical, noting that the speed of multiple technological iterations is astonishing, and holds that cross-Strait industrial cooperation in related fields…","Mainland humanoid robots have progressed from hopping and bouncing on the Spring Festival Gala stage, to repeatedly setting new records at sports events, to entering application scenarios in production and daily life. This is a microcosm of the deep integration and rapid development of mainland technological and industrial innovation. The 15th Five-Year Plan forward-looks to deploy future industries such as embodied intelligence and brain-computer interfaces. Relying on its complete industrial system, solid industrial foundation, and rich application scenarios, the mainland will create broad development space for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises. We welcome Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises to come to the mainland to innovate and start businesses, take part in high-quality development, and jointly grow the economy of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785956.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","Regarding the General Administration of Customs’ announcement of a new batch of Taiwan wendan pomelo orchards and packing plants, the Mainland Affairs Council said that only those who meet political prerequisites and conditions can obtain registration, and that this approach is united front propaganda. It also said that quarantine of cross-strait agricultural products involves matters of public authority and must…","Importing Taiwanese pomelos into the mainland helps expand sales channels for the island's agricultural products and improves the well-being of Taiwan compatriots. This is a good thing and a real benefit for grassroots operators on the island. The DPP neither wishes nor is able to help more grassroots people increase their benefits and well-being. Instead, it persistently spreads rumors and smears, fully exposing that it disregards the people's livelihoods and has only its own selfish interests in mind, and it will certainly be opposed by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Recently, exchanges between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait in various fields have remained active.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, from September 2 to 5, the “Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Taiwanese Businesses Visit Jilin” event was held in Changchun, Jilin and other places. Themed “Gathering New Momentum in Circles, Jilin-Taiwan Looking to the Future,” it included on-site observation, industry promotion and economic and trade negotiations, helping Taiwanese businesspeople and enterprises seize opportunities in the revitalization and development of Northeast China. From September 3 to 6, the 17th Dongguan Taiwan Famous Products Expo will be held in Dongguan, Guangdong. The Taiwan Special Exhibition Hall will bring together 22 counties and cities from across the island, displaying machinery and equipment, agricultural and fishery specialties and more. From September 6 to 10, the 18th “Chongqing·Taiwan Week” will be held in Chongqing, including a series of activities such as the Cross-Strait Information and Communication Cooperation and Development Seminar and the Cross-Strait Youth Pursue Dreams in Chongqing Employment and Entrepreneurship Seminar.\nIn cultural exchanges, from August 23 to September 2, the first Sichuan Tea Horse Ancient Road Photography Journey Experience Camp was held in Ya'an, Garze and other places in Sichuan. Photography enthusiasts from both sides of the Taiwan Strait used their lenses as a medium to embark together on a photographic creative journey of walking and seeking roots. From August 29 to 31, the 8th Cross-Strait Humanities Forum was held in Xiamen, Fujian, with scholars and experts in philosophy, literature, history and other fields from both sides of the Taiwan Strait attending.\nIn youth exchanges, from August 20 to 27, the 14th Strait Youth Gathering and the 2nd Cross-Strait (Fuzhou) Sports Protection and Rehabilitation Exchange Activity, along with the “Feather Dance Youth, Bonded by the Strait” Fujian-Taiwan Youth Badminton Exchange Series, were held in Fuzhou, Fujian. On August 26, the “Youth Quajiang, Zhelí Huacan, Dancing Youth” Cross-Strait Street Dance Youth Cultural Exchange Event and the 3rd Cross-Strait Youth Street Dance Competition opened in Quzhou, Zhejiang. From August 26 to September 1, the “Tiangong Kaiwu·Intangible Cultural Heritage Appointment” 2026 Cross-Strait (Xinyu) Youth Exchange Activity was held in Xinyu, Jiangxi. On August 28, the 16th Cross-Strait (Binzhou) Youth Students' Sun Tzu Art of War Friendship Debate Competition kicked off in Huimin, Shandong. From September 3 to 9, the 2026 4th Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival·Youth Filmmakers Training Camp will be held in Xiamen, Fujian.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","Recently, the mainland-gifted giant panda “Yuan Yuan” (圆圆) celebrated her 22nd birthday, and the Taipei Zoo held a celebration for “Yuan Yuan,” which drew attention from netizens on both sides of the Strait, who sent their blessings. What is your comment on this?","Giant pandas are deeply loved by people on both sides of the Strait and are the embodiment of peace and friendship. In 2008, giant pandas “Tuan Tuan” and “Yuan Yuan” went to Taiwan to make their home there, and during their stay they successfully gave birth to cubs “Yuan Zai” and “Yuan Bao.” Over the years, they have brought joy to compatriots in Taiwan. Recently, “Yuan Yuan” celebrated her 22nd birthday. Here we extend our sincere birthday wishes to “Yuan Yuan,” and we also wish the two panda cubs healthy growth, so that this warm family affection across the Strait may continue endlessly.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","Taiwanese media reported that netizens on the island are widely discussing the growing number of young people who like to travel independently to the mainland. Data show that since this summer vacation, passenger traffic on the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” route has continued to run at a high level, and on August 23, passenger traffic set a new record since the route resumed operation. Please introduce the…","The “Mini Three Links” passenger shipping routes are among the most important and convenient channels for exchanges between the two sides of the Strait, especially between Fujian and Taiwan. Since this summer, demand on the cross-strait “Mini Three Links” passenger routes has continued to rise, and passenger flow has remained at a high level. Among them, the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” route has operated a cumulative 1,550 trips, carrying 386,400 passengers, up 11.4% and 24.1% year on year, respectively. On August 23, the single-day passenger flow on the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” route exceeded 7,900 passengers, setting a single-day record since the route resumed operation in 2023.\nTo meet summer passenger flow, relevant authorities on the mainland have closely coordinated to improve support capacity and better meet travelers' needs. Starting August 1, the Xiamen-Kinmen “Mini Three Links” route implemented temporary additional summer trips and appropriately extended its operating hours. At the same time, they have optimized customs clearance procedures, strengthened maritime safety supervision, improved passenger services, and achieved efficient and smooth customs clearance through an intelligent system. The “Mini Three Links” routes have operated overall safely and smoothly, with good order.\nThe busy operation of the “Mini Three Links” routes this summer is a vivid expression of compatriots on both sides of the Strait visiting and getting closer to each other. We welcome more fellow Taiwanese to come to the mainland via the “Mini Three Links” routes to seek their roots and ancestors, visit relatives and friends, and engage in exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785957.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, some Green Camp politicians claimed that the Taiwanese civil group “Xiaoyizi Hanfu” filmed videos against the backdrop of the Confucius Temple during the Dragon Boat Festival under the name of “promoting Confucianism and Hanfu culture,” and that it is suspected of having united-front overtones. Shen Yu-chung, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, said in response that culture should be…","Chinese culture is the shared spiritual home of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. Civil groups on the island are dedicated to inheriting and promoting Chinese culture and actively take part in cross-Strait exchange activities, which precisely proves that both sides share the same roots and origins, the same culture, and the same ethnicity. We will work with compatriots in Taiwan to continue advancing cross-Strait cultural exchange and cooperation, jointly promote Chinese culture, and be guardians, inheritors, and promoters of Chinese culture.\nThe essence of united front work is broad unity and wide alliance: making friends, promoting solidarity, seeking common ground while setting aside differences, and working together for development. The DPP authorities deliberately distort the true meaning and essence of united front work, smear cross-Strait exchange activities, and intimidate and suppress compatriots in Taiwan who take part in cross-Strait exchange activities, with sinister intent.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260902_12785955.htm"],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan's legislature passed the so-called “Drone Industry Development Plan.” Some public opinion on the island worries that drones have also become an important project for expanding Taiwan's armaments. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities want to militarize civilian industries and attempt to turn drones into a tool for “seeking independence and resisting reunification,” which is purely a waste of effort. The reunification of the motherland is unstoppable; no matter how many drones the DPP authorities produce, it will be in vain.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾“中央社”记者","Hung Shen-han, head of Taiwan’s Ministry of Labor, will travel to Nanjing in late September to attend the APEC meeting. The Taiwan side said this is in accordance with the existing norms and model of APEC, under which members participate on an equal basis. What are your views on this? Does the mainland believe this trip will help increase cross-Strait exchanges and interaction and create some new possibilities…","As the host of this year's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) activities, we handle the matter of the Taiwan region's participation in meetings in accordance with the one-China principle, the relevant memorandum of understanding of APEC, and established practice, including the issue you mentioned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","The first question: Taiwan authorities recently said that since December 2025, more than 300 person-times from 25 departments and units in Taiwan have come to the mainland to attend various APEC meetings, and the process has been smooth without any incidents. Will the mainland side, in accordance with past patterns of interaction, ensure that Hong Shen-han, head of Taiwan’s labor department, who will travel to…","First question. Our position on Chinese Taipei-related issues at APEC is consistent and clear: participation by the Taiwan region must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle, the relevant APEC memorandum of understanding, and established practice.\nSecond question. This organization has willingly served as a pawn for international anti-China forces, has repeatedly sowed discord and fabricated smears against the mainland, and has been firmly boycotted by the international community. It is entirely reasonable and lawful for border inspection authorities to review certain individuals who once worked for this organization.\nIn 2025, Taiwan compatriots made more than 4.89 million trips to the mainland, and in the first half of this year, Taiwan compatriots made 2.85 million trips to the mainland. As long as they abide by the rules and laws, Taiwan compatriots come with joy and leave with satisfaction. The Democratic Progressive Party authorities ignore the above facts, yet they spread rumors about certain individuals who once worked for an anti-China organization. This is entirely a confusion of right and wrong and a reversal of black and white, with the aim of intimidating the people on the island and interfering with and obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and contacts. Their despicable conduct will certainly be condemned and opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question. Recently, a man operating a computer on the platform of the Taipei Main Station MRT displayed simplified Chinese characters including “Second War Zone” on the screen. Some Taiwan residents initially questioned whether mainland personnel had been sent to Taiwan to search for intelligence, but it turned out to be a farce. What is the mainland’s response? Second question. The mainland’s new entry and…","First question. Public information online has already shown that this is a farcical comedy of errors. Certain individuals on the island always seize on such matters to stir up cross-strait opposition and confrontation, and their intentions are sinister.\nSecond question. We have repeatedly stressed that we lawfully protect the life and property safety and legitimate rights and interests of cross-strait compatriots, including Taiwan compatriots. The relevant regulations have a legal basis and are open and transparent. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have no need whatsoever to worry about coming to the mainland. The DPP authorities loudly peddle so-called “risks” of coming to the mainland and even deceive and intimidate the people of Taiwan, merely to obstruct Taiwan’s people from coming to the mainland for exchanges and visits. The historical trend of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer cannot be stopped. Their carefully woven information cocoons will inevitably be punctured by facts, and their despicable tricks will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾东森电视台记者","Taiwanese entertainer Chou Tzu-yu debuted as a member of the Korean girl group TWICE. Recently, news emerged that after her contract with her Korean agency expires, mainland China has actively sought to bring her over to switch tracks, and it has been reported that her political stance was offered as a condition in exchange for entertainment resources. Can the spokesperson confirm this?","I am not aware of the specific situation you mentioned. We have consistently and actively supported cross-Strait cultural exchanges and welcome Taiwan entertainers to develop in the mainland. We support more Taiwan entertainers sharing opportunities in the development of the mainland's cultural industry, realizing their dreams, and jointly promoting the prosperity and development of cross-Strait cultural undertakings. Of course, we will never permit or condone the practice of making money in the mainland while supporting “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. This is our consistent and clear position.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress recently adopted the newly revised National Defense Mobilization Law, which will take effect on October 1. The law stipulates that, in light of development and interest needs, the disposal of civilian resources may be expanded from “requisition” to “expropriation.” Could the Taiwan Affairs Office clarify whether the “expropriation” provisions of the new law…","The newly revised National Defense Mobilization Law adheres to the overall national security concept and clarifies, under the new system, the functional roles of the military and civilian sectors in national defense mobilization, the operational mechanisms, and key tasks. It will play an important role in standardizing and strengthening national defense mobilization work, safeguarding national security and development interests. It must be emphasized that whether deciding to implement national defense mobilization or requisitioning and expropriating civilian resources during national defense mobilization, there are clear legal requirements and statutory procedures, and the state lawfully protects the lawful rights and interests of organizations and individuals participating in national defense mobilization activities.\nWe will uphold the concept that ‘compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,’ support the development of Taiwanese businesses and enterprises on the mainland, and help more Taiwanese businesspeople and compatriots participate equally, integrate actively, and share in building and advancing the process of Chinese-style modernization. Taiwanese businesses and enterprises need have no concerns about long-term investment and lawful, compliant operations on the mainland. There will only be more opportunities, broader space, and better protection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-02","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The Gwangju Biennale in South Korea restored the name “Taiwan Pavilion,” and mainland artists collectively withdrew their works on the eve of the opening. The organizers said that “politics should not interfere with art.” Outsiders are worried that similar occasions or exhibitions in the future may evolve into a situation of “you or me” across the Strait. What comments do you have on this? Second…","First question: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Taiwan's participation in international activities must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle.\nThe DPP authorities use cultural exchanges, conferences, exhibitions and other occasions to engage in political manipulation and disrupt the normal order of the relevant events, which is despicable. No matter what tricks the DPP authorities play, they cannot change the destined failure of their provocations to seek independence.\nSecond question: The so-called “antagonistic sentiment” was entirely deliberately stirred up by the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities disregard the development demands of the island's industry and scheme to attach political labels to performing artists, attempting to use political manipulation to obstruct normal cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao cultural exchanges and commercial performances through bans and restrictions. This completely goes against mainstream public opinion on the island and seriously harms the interests of Taiwan businesses and the public. It is unpopular and will not succeed.\nToday's press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260902_12785940.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-09-03","Guo Jiakun","AFP","The coast guard of Taiwan said today that it deployed vessels to monitor two Chinese ships operating in waters to its east, saying it firmly rejects China’s campaign of “law enforcement in name, jurisdictional expansion in practice.” Does the Chinese foreign ministry have a reaction to this?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.\n**************************************************","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260903_12015816.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260903_12015775.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-09-03","Guo Jiakun","The following question was raised after the press conference","The Chinese exhibition team announced it will withdraw from the Gwangju Biennale in the ROK in strong protest against the organizer’s wrongful practice related to Taiwan. The Chinese embassy in the ROK has made a statement on that. What’s your comment?","The China-ROK joint communiqué on the establishment of diplomatic relations states clearly that “the government of the Republic of Korea recognizes the government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal government of China and respects China’s position that there is only one China and Taiwan is part of China.” The ROK side also clearly stated on many occasions this year that its commitment to the one-China position remains unchanged.\nThe organizer of the ROK Gwangju Biennale, however, has stubbornly clung to the wrongful practice, allowing China’s Taiwan region to participate under a designation that is completely incompatible with its status. This is a grave violation of the one-China principle. China is firmly opposed to this and has lodged serious representations with the ROK side, demanding that the relevant party immediately correct its wrongdoings. We hope that the ROK government will honor its political commitments, earnestly shoulder its responsibilities, and uphold the one-China principle with concrete actions.\nIt’s despicable for the DPP authorities to exploit occasions such as cultural exchanges, conferences and exhibitions to engage in political manipulation and make “Taiwan independence” provocations. Their political schemes are doomed to fail.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260903_12015816.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260903_12015775.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-09-04","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, Taiwan’s defense authorities submitted the “2026 Report on Mainland China’s Military Power” and the “Five-Year Force Building and Governance Plan Report of the Taiwan Military” to the island’s legislative body, playing up the “mainland threat,” pointing out that the PLA routinely sends ships and aircraft around Taiwan to conduct combat readiness patrols and “harassment” operations, and emphasizing the…","The relevant report confuses right and wrong and reverses black and white. It is merely a pretext the DPP authorities use to peddle war anxiety and “seek independence through force.” Taiwan is an inseparable part of China's territory. The PLA's routine combat readiness patrols around the island and its anti-secession and anti-interference operations are to safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and are a mission and responsibility. The trend toward national reunification is irresistible, and any attempt to “seek independence through force” is doomed to fail.","","http://www.81.mil.cn/yw_208727/16483607.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-09-07","Mao Ning","China News Service","According to the Solomon Star, Taiwan increased its annual aid to Palau from US$18 million last year to US$25 million this year, apparently in an effort to secure political backing at the Pacific Islands Forum. The Taiwan authorities also allocated nearly US$281,000 in direct cash gifts for Palau’s former president, incumbent political figures, and individual lawmakers. The report commented that Taiwan’s…","The report is yet another example of the Lai Ching-te authorities’ expensive dollar diplomacy using the hard-earned money of the people in Taiwan—a combination of corruption, fraudulence, bribery and power-for-money deals—to serve “Taiwan independence” separatism and their personal political agenda. For certain countries like Palau, having Taiwan as a “diplomatic ally” is not about delivering for the country and the people, but to line the pockets of the very few people who profit from it.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260907_12017650.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260907_12017452.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-09-08","Mao Ning","China Daily","It’s reported that Lai Ching-te claimed at an event that China is contorting UNGA Resolution 2758. Taiwan is a “sovereign independent nation.” The resolution only addresses the People’s Republic of China’s representation at the UN and has nothing to do with Taiwan. What is China’s comment on this?","There is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. This is an unshakable fact grounded in both history and law. The Cairo Declaration issued by China, the U.S. and the UK in 1943 stated in explicit terms that Taiwan is a territory that Japan had stolen and shall be restored to China. The Potsdam Proclamation in 1945 reaffirmed that the terms of the Cairo Declaration shall be carried out. This series of instruments with legal effect under international law have all clearly affirmed China’s sovereignty over Taiwan. UNGA Resolution 2758 solemnly reaffirmed the one-China principle, which “decides to restore all its rights to the People’s Republic of China and to recognize the representatives of its Government as the only legitimate representatives of China to the United Nations.” From political, legal and procedural aspects, the resolution resolved once and for all the question of the representation of the whole of China, including Taiwan, in the UN. It made clear that there is only one seat of China in the United Nations, and there is no such thing as “two Chinas” or “one China, one Taiwan.”\nTaiwan has never been a country and will never be a country. The Lai Ching-te authorities’ deliberate distortion of UNGA Resolution 2758 once again revealed their separatist nature for “Taiwan independence.” Their rhetoric will not change the historical and legal fact that the two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one and the same China, nor will it undermine the international community’s steadfast commitment to one China.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260908_12018516.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260908_12018501.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 9, the Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporters, good day. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","The “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” are about to mark three years since their release and implementation. Please introduce what important progress has been made in building the demonstration zone, and how it will be further…","In September 2023, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Supporting Fujian in Exploring a New Path for Cross-Strait Integrated Development and Building a Cross-Strait Integrated Development Demonstration Zone” was issued and implemented. Over the past three years, the central government and relevant departments of state organs have formulated and issued a series of supporting policy documents. Fujian has successively issued 74 policy measures promoting Fujian-Taiwan integration in five batches, and has organized the implementation of 206 key Fujian-Taiwan integrated development projects, with total investment exceeding 1.3 trillion yuan.\nAfter three years of efforts, the construction of the demonstration zone has made phased progress. The convenience of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises landing in the first homeland has become greater, economic exchanges and cooperation between Fujian and Taiwan have remained vibrant, Fujian's overall integrated development has maintained good momentum, and people-to-people and social exchanges between Fujian and Taiwan have continued to deepen. From January to August this year, 2.0874 million passenger trips were made between Fujian and Taiwan, a year-on-year increase of 20.64%; 857,500 Taiwan compatriots entered through Fujian ports, a year-on-year increase of 27.94%; and 1.5836 million cross-Strait passengers traveled through the “mini three links,” a year-on-year increase of 25.34%.\nNext, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the National Development and Reform Commission will, together with relevant departments of the central government and state organs and Fujian Province, build on the start of the 15th Five-Year Plan, continue to push forward the implementation of the “Opinions” in detail, highlight promoting integration through connectivity, through benefits, and through emotional bonds, further promote institutional innovation, industrial coordination, people-to-people exchanges, and livelihood security, and run the high-quality development requirements through the entire process of demonstration zone construction. We will take greater steps in exploring a new path for cross-Strait integrated development, continuously promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787267.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","A associate professor at Changhua University of Education in Taiwan has published three consecutive articles on social media platforms about the Taiwan plan of “One Country, Two Systems,” attracting attention and heated discussion from readers on both sides of the Strait. Some view this as “a rare icebreaking text.” What is your comment on this? How do you view the new trend of civilian discussion across the…","“Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems” is the best way to realize the reunification of the motherland. It embodies the Chinese wisdom of embracing all rivers and having great tolerance. It fully takes into account Taiwan’s actual situation and is conducive to the long-term stability and prosperity of Taiwan after reunification. The specific form of realizing “one country, two systems” in Taiwan will fully take into account Taiwan’s actual situation, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of all sectors on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nReunification of the motherland is an unstoppable historical trend. For Taiwan compatriots, it is not an optional question but a compulsory one. We are pleased to see more and more Taiwan compatriots face reunification squarely and begin to understand and discuss the specific content of the “one country, two systems” plan for Taiwan, offering suggestions and ideas for the “two systems” plan for Taiwan through various channels. In this process, it is normal for compatriots on both sides of the Strait to have differences and debates. We believe that more Taiwan compatriots will break through the ideological confinement and information cocoons created by the DPP authorities, and will increasingly recognize the superiority of “one country, two systems” and the inclusiveness of the “two systems” plan for Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787266.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","September 3 is the Commemoration Day of the Chinese People's War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War Victory. Far-sighted people from all walks of life on the island have spoken out, calling on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to remember their shared history of resistance, defend the fruits of victory in the War of Resistance, and oppose the separatist acts of…","This year marks the 81st anniversary of the victory of the Chinese people's War of Resistance against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War. Taiwan compatriots have a glorious tradition of patriotism. During the heroic years of the War of Resistance, tens of thousands of Taiwan compatriots selflessly crossed the Strait and joined the nation-wide torrent of resistance, contributing to the defeat of Japanese fascism and the restoration of Taiwan. The victory of the War of Resistance is a great triumph forged by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, through fearless, unyielding, and bloody struggle. It is also a shared historical memory of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nTo forget history is to betray it. The DPP authorities deliberately downplay and wantonly distort the history of the War of Resistance. This is a betrayal of history and a desecration of the martyrs, and it is paving the way for their betrayal of the nation and division of the country. We believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities' false historical narrative and sinister intent of “de-Sinicization,” hold fast to national righteousness and correct historical views, and join hands with compatriots on the mainland to carry forward and promote the great spirit of the War of Resistance, and jointly contribute to the great cause of national reunification and a bright future of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787263.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","It is understood that the 6th “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams: Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar Event” will be held in Urumqi, Xinjiang, attracting attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams -- Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” has been held for five consecutive sessions since 2021 and has become an important brand for cross-Strait exchanges. The sixth session will be held in Urumqi, Xinjiang, from September 11 to 12. Relevant parties from both sides of the Strait, heads of parties and groups, and representative personages will conduct in-depth discussions on topics such as the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and jointly pursuing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, to build broad consensus.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","July and August are the peak season for cross-Strait youth exchanges, and cross-Strait youth exchange activities have been colorful and continuously lively. Please introduce the highlights and characteristics of the summer youth exchange activities. What is your comment?","This summer, the enthusiasm for youth exchanges across the Taiwan Strait has continued to climb, and activities in various places have followed one after another, each more exciting than the last. Tens of thousands of young people from Taiwan have crossed the sea to interact with their peers on the mainland, gaining a great deal.\nFirst, branded activities have released powerful momentum. The launch of the \"Together with One Heart — Cross-Strait Youth Exchange Season, Shanghai Stop\" was an instant hit, with more than a thousand young people from both sides gathering in Shanghai to explore trendy technology and culture, vividly illustrating the mutual pursuit and joint progress of the new generation across the Strait. The 14th Strait Youth Gathering focused on social, economic, emotional and comprehensive integration, and launched the third batch of measures for the \"Strait Youth Development-Oriented City,\" attracting wave after wave of young people from Taiwan to Fujian for exchange and development. The 24th Strait Youth Forum, the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Summit, the 9th Cross-Strait Youth Development Forum and other activities have continued to grow in influence, drawing Taiwan youth in an endless stream.\nSecond, cultural exchange activities continue to attract participants. The 6th Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month, centered on the theme \"New Expressions of Traditional Culture,\" built a cultural carnival belonging to young people on both sides. The 3rd Shaanxi-Taiwan Cultural Exchange Week and the Cross-Strait Youth Han-Tang Culture Summer Camp, under the theme \"Carry Forward Chinese Culture and Write a Brilliant Chapter of Youth,\" promoted in-depth exchange and cooperation in culture and other fields across the Strait. Young people from both sides sang mountain songs together in Longyan, Fujian, and Meizhou, Guangdong, promoting Hakka culture, and used music to express their feelings in Jinan, Shandong, and Lanzhou, Gansu, singing together the youthful songs of both sides of the Strait.\nThird, sports exchange activities are the most exciting and popular. The Cross-Strait Inter-School Alliance baseball games held in Beijing and Guizhou, the beach frisbee invitational tournament held in Fujian, the \"Tinghao Cup\" Cross-Strait Youth Basketball Invitational Tournament held in Anhui, the youth table tennis exchange tournament held in Hubei, the Guangdong-Taiwan-Hong Kong-Macao Youth Roller Hockey Exchange Tournament held in Guangdong, the summer pickleball exchange event held in Henan, and the Guangxi-Taiwan Youth Badminton Exchange Tournament held in Guangxi, among other events, all attracted large numbers of Taiwan youth. Young people from both sides competed on the same field, achieved good results, and made good friends.\nFourth, the activities are geographically broad and the exchanges are deep. From the desert wonder of \"mountain springs coexisting, sand and water living together\" in Dunhuang, Gansu, to the Mazu temples on Meizhou Island in Putian; from the vast and majestic landscapes of the Longjiang region to the scenery of Guilin's mountains and rivers, which is unmatched under heaven, young people from both sides have measured the country's splendid landscapes with their feet and felt the history and culture of the Chinese nation with their hearts.\nThe mainland is also the home of the vast number of Taiwan compatriots. Not only in summer, but at any time, we sincerely welcome Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to visit, see for themselves, and take part in cross-Strait exchanges, to exchange and learn from mainland youth on equal footing, discuss youthful ideals together, and create a better future together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787256.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","北京日报记者","According to reports, the Straits Exchange Foundation recently published a 2027 budget of over NT$350 million, about NT$10 million more than in 2026, used to increase personnel costs. Its specific task is to promote safety concerns about travel to the mainland at major tourism expos and remind island residents to carefully assess the risks. What is your comment on this?","In 2025, Taiwan compatriots visited the mainland nearly 4.9 million person-times, and in the first half of this year, 2.85 million person-times. The personal safety and various lawful rights and interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots during their stay on the mainland are guaranteed in accordance with law, so that they come happily and return safely.\nThe purpose of the Straits Exchange Foundation is to be “Chinese, well-intentioned, and service-oriented,” and when it was founded, it was positioned as taking on the mission of “being a bridge, not a wall.” Yet today it has fallen to becoming a pawn of the DPP authorities in obstructing and undermining cross-Strait exchange and cooperation and inciting cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation. This is truly lamentable. Regarding the Foundation’s recent remarks, I have eight words of advice: “Don’t forget the original intent, and do more real work.”","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","Recently, the DPP authorities have loudly stirred up talk that Taiwan residents going to the mainland face so-called “risks,” and have fabricated and smeared four supposed risks, including that the “Regulations of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” have “inconsistent standards.” What is your comment?","The “Regulations of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” are intended to standardize exit and entry administration, protect the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting and entering, and safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. The relevant regulations help further protect the lawful rights and interests of all persons entering and exiting, including Taiwan compatriots.\nIn order to obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, the DPP authorities have continuously distorted facts and smeared the mainland. Recently, they have also manipulated cyber troops and flank forces to fabricate rumors, slander, and maliciously defame specific individuals, which is shameful.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, Taiwan’s transportation and tourism authority sent a letter to travel agencies requiring operators, when organizing exchange and travel to the mainland, to assist travelers group by group in completing pre-departure registration for travel to the mainland and to fill in relevant notes. Although the MAC said it is “not forcing” anyone, this has still caused concern among people on the island about the…","This is yet another despicable tactic by the DPP authorities to threaten and intimidate Taiwan compatriots who come to the mainland, and to interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel. It has already provoked resentment and dissatisfaction among Taiwan compatriots and the industry. The desire of compatriots on both sides to visit and draw closer to each other, and the trend toward cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, cannot be stopped. Any act that turns back the wheel of history and runs counter to the will of the people will inevitably face a backlash from public opinion.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, the urban workplace drama “Early Spring Sunshine,” directed by a Taiwanese director and starring mainland actors, has sparked a binge-watching craze on the island. Many Taiwanese media outlets have run special reports on it, and many viewers on the island have been urging updates on online platforms. What is your comment?","We welcome more film and television works co-produced by cross-Strait filmmakers that showcase cross-Strait kinship and a good life being broadcast on both sides of the Strait, realizing a “two-way journey” of emotions and exchanges between the peoples on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Recently, cross-Strait exchange activities have remained active.\nFrom August 25 to 29, the 2026 Straits Hakka “Kejing·Gaozuo” (客青·搞作) short video creation competition for Taiwan Hakka descendants visiting their ancestral homeland was held in Longyan City, Fujian Province. Forty Taiwan Hakka youths created short videos on Hakka culture and the landscapes of their ancestral homeland, recording what they saw and felt from fresh perspectives.\nFrom August 29 to September 2, the Fujian–Taiwan (Mingxi) Traditional Chinese Medicine Culture Exchange Event was held in Sanming City, Fujian Province. Nearly 70 people from both sides of the Strait, including traditional Chinese medicine experts and scholars, industry associations, and traditional Chinese medicine enterprises, attended, reached a number of substantive cooperation agreements, and continued to deepen multi-dimensional cooperation in traditional Chinese medicine between Fujian and Taiwan.\nOn September 2, the opening ceremony of the “2026 Cross-Strait Youth Study Camp: Exploring the Code of Chinese Civilization Together” was held at Qiannan Normal University for Nationalities in Guizhou. Through close contact, young people from both sides of the Strait immersed themselves in experiencing Guizhou’s development and Chinese civilization.\nOn the same day, the launch ceremony of the first season of the young musician SEEK project, “Cuobian Huixiang · Liang’an Tongsheng” (厝边回响 两岸同声), was held in Zhangzhou. More than 150 participants, including well-known musicians and artists from both sides of the Strait and young Taiwan people, attended. Using joint music creation by young people across the Strait as its vehicle, the event will organize field trips and music creation, hold dedicated performances and exchange activities, simultaneously run promotion competitions, and incubate young musical talent.\nOn September 3, the closing ceremony of the 2026 Taiwan Youth Lingnan Tour was held at the Guangzhou Xinghai Conservatory of Music. Young people from both sides of the Strait shared their reflections on the Lingnan tour exchange and performed together, demonstrating a spirit of working hard together and realizing dreams together.\nFrom September 3 to 9, the 2026 4th Straits Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival · Youth Filmmaker Training Camp was held in Xiamen City. Young people from both sides of the Strait used images as a medium to connect shared emotions and exchange creative insights.\nFrom September 9 to 12, the 6th Pingtan IM Cross-Strait Youth Film Festival will be held in Pingtan, Fujian. The work submission scope of the event covers 410 universities, and more than 3,500 Taiwan young people are participating. The number of submitted films and the scale of participating institutions both reached record highs for the festival. Under the theme “If the Wind Had Colors,” this year’s festival will hold a number of activities, including a “Youth Film Night,” and more than 700 people from all sectors, including well-known filmmakers, industry representatives, and university teachers and students, will attend in person.\nFrom September 9 to 12, the 14th Anhui–Taiwan Science and Technology Forum and the 18th Straits Cross-Strait Science Popularization Forum will be held in Bengbu, Anhui. Nearly 60 experts, scholars, and youth representatives from both sides of the Strait will hold extensive exchanges and discussions in fields such as electronic information and biotechnology.\nFrom September 9 to 15, the 2026 Straits Cross-Strait (Nanchang) Youth Maker Camp will be held in Nanchang, Jiujiang, Jingdezhen, and other places in Jiangxi Province.\nFrom September 14 to 18, the first Straits Cross-Strait (Jiaocheng) Yandi Shennong Culture Week will be held in Ningde, Fujian. Nearly 200 representatives of Taiwan temples and believers will come to Ningde to carry out ceremonial rites, interactive experiences of agricultural culture and traditional Chinese medicine, and free clinics by cross-Strait Chinese medicine practitioners, among other activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Taiwanese media reported that, catalyzed by the DPP authorities' “anti-China” policies, the Green camp on the island has recently repeatedly staged “espionage hunts,” engaging in suspicious and blundering farces. They have even grown increasingly sensitive and uneasy about “Mainland accents,” “simplified characters,” and “Mainland terminology,” and are increasingly rejecting them. What is your comment?","The Democratic Progressive Party authorities and “Taiwan independence” forces have become increasingly “bewitched” in “opposing everything from the mainland” and “opposing and resisting China.” From treating the use of “mainland terms” by Taiwan residents as a major threat, to imagining individual simplified Chinese characters as espionage infiltration, they are as jumpy as someone who mistakes a bow's reflection for a snake. The actions of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities not only further damage cross-Strait mutual trust, but also aggravate a “green terror” in society on the island, and they will surely be opposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","The 81st session of the UN General Assembly opened on the 8th. Recently, Lai Ching-te declared that the mainland is misapplying UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, which only resolves the question of the representation of the People’s Republic of China at the United Nations and has nothing to do with Taiwan at all. Taiwan’s foreign affairs department claimed that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 does not…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is an indisputable historical and legal fact and the true status quo of the Taiwan Strait. In 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly, by an overwhelming majority, adopted Resolution 2758, deciding to restore all the rights of the People’s Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the representatives of the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legitimate representatives of China at the United Nations. This thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the issue of representation of all of China at the United Nations, including Taiwan.\nLai Qingde and the DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, attempting to challenge the one-China principle generally recognized by the international community. This will only bring humiliation upon themselves and is bound to fail. No matter how hard they scheme, they cannot change the legal fact that Taiwan is part of China, cannot shake the firm pattern of the international community’s adherence to the one-China principle, and cannot block the historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and certainly will be.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787259.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, the mainland coast guard announced that a “Putuoshan” vessel formation will conduct routine law enforcement patrols in waters east of Taiwan island. Taiwan’s coast guard authorities said this move is “fake law enforcement, real expansion of power” and “attempts to create the illusion of having jurisdiction.” What comment do you have?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The mainland coast guard carried out law enforcement and rights-protection operations in its jurisdictional waters in accordance with the law, effectively ensuring normal navigation and operational order and earnestly safeguarding the lawful and legitimate rights and interests as well as the lives and property of Chinese citizens, including Taiwan compatriots. This is a legitimate and just act to defend national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.\nThe DPP authorities, stubbornly clinging to their “Taiwan independence” separatist stance, distorting facts and maliciously hyping the issue, are doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, Kyrgyzstan and Egypt each issued joint statements with China, both emphasizing adherence to the one-China principle and support for achieving China's unification. Taiwan's foreign affairs authorities falsely claimed that the mainland is “improperly manipulating” matters internationally, that Taiwan is a “sovereign independent state,” and that the two sides “are not subordinate to each other.” What is…","We appreciate the position of relevant countries that adhere to the one-China principle and support China’s reunification. Facts have once again proven that the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community. It is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the aspiration of the people.\nThere is only one China in the world. Taiwan is part of China and has never been a country, nor will it ever possibly become one. There is simply no so-called “sovereignty.” No matter how the DPP authorities talk wildly and hype the “new two-state theory,” they cannot change the historical and legal fact that Taiwan belongs to China. They cannot change the outcome that “Taiwan independence” is at the end of its road and doomed to failure, and they cannot stop the trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified and certainly will be reunified.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, the DPP authorities claimed that in 2025, Taiwanese business investment in the mainland fell 59 percent from the previous year, and in the first half of 2026 it fell another 30 percent, and that the mainland's economic development has fallen into difficulty, so Taiwanese businesses should be cautious about investing in the mainland. What is your comment on this?","According to statistics from the relevant authorities, from January to July this year, cross-Strait trade reached US$221.8 billion, up 26.5% year on year. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$62.17 billion, up 31.6% year on year, and mainland imports from Taiwan were US$159.63 billion, up 24.7% year on year. This fully demonstrates that the economic ties across the Strait are close, the foundation of shared interests is solid, and the industrial and supply chains across the Strait are stable and resilient.\nThis year, we have effectively responded to changes in the external environment, such as geopolitical conflicts and trade frictions. We have maintained an overall stable development trend that is moving toward new and better directions. The economy has shown vigor and strong resilience, injecting powerful momentum and rare certainty into the world economy, and continuously providing new opportunities and new room for strengthening cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepening integrated development. The mainland has always been the best choice for broad Taiwan compatriots and Taiwanese enterprises to invest and start businesses, a profound fertile ground for innovation and development, and a strong reliance for resisting risks. The DPP authorities’ smears and predictions of decline have already been proven futile, and will continue to be proven futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260909_12787262.htm"],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: The Mainland Affairs Council says that Taiwan's Minister of Labor Hung Shen-han, who is traveling to Nanjing to attend the APEC meeting, may enter the mainland with an APEC invitation letter and does not need to apply for a Taiwan Compatriot Permit. Please confirm this. Have the relevant arrangements been finalized? Second question: The Tourism Administration of Taiwan previously issued a letter…","First question: Since 1991, when Taiwan's side has participated in APEC meetings and activities, they have been handled in accordance with the one-China principle, the relevant APEC memorandum of understanding, and established practice, and this year is no different.\nSecond question: The DPP authorities' despicable tricks have triggered resentment and dissatisfaction among the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and the island's tourism industry, and they were ultimately forced to backtrack. This precisely illustrates the saying: \"There is nothing in the world to worry about, but fools worry themselves into trouble.\"\nThird question: We have consistently upheld the concept that \"cross-Strait compatriots are one family,\" and we are making every effort to do practical things, good things, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. On the basis of comprehensively evaluating the relevant rectification measures and in conformity with the relevant mainland inspection and quarantine regulations, we support more Taiwan pomelo packaging plants and orchards in registering on the mainland. We will further promote the implementation, in detail and in full, of the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, continue to facilitate the import of Taiwan agricultural and fishery products into the mainland, and let the farmers and fishermen on the island gain tangible benefits.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-09","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The family of Beijing lawyer Wang Xiahong is stranded in Taiwan seeking resettlement. The MAC has publicly confirmed this sudden incident and set the tone of “humanitarian first” in providing resettlement. May I ask whether you can confirm Wang Xiahong's departure from the mainland and flight situation?\nSecond question: Recently, some Taiwan residents noticed that the mainland brand Luckin Coffee…","Question one: Regarding issues of lawyer practice management, please inquire with the relevant competent authorities. There are corresponding management regulations for mainland residents traveling to Taiwan, and relevant departments will handle these matters in accordance with law and regulations.\nQuestion two: We are pleased to see Taiwan compatriots using high-quality mainland products, and we support two-way investment and win-win cooperation between cross-Strait enterprises. The DPP authorities, for the sake of narrow party interests, deliberately obstruct and restrict mainland investment and product entry into the island, worsen the island's business environment and harm the vital interests of Taiwan's people. This is an unpopular political manipulation.\nQuestion three: The DPP authorities' vile tactics aim to threaten and intimidate Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland and to disrupt and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and personnel travel. These tactics are unpopular and have already triggered strong resentment and dissatisfaction among the broad public and the tourism industry on the island. These vile tactics cannot stop the wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to draw closer together, nor can they stop the trend of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. They are turning back the wheel of history and going against the tide.\nWe have always adhered to the concept of “cross-Strait families are one family” and lawfully protect the legitimate rights and interests of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots, including tourists. According to the “Tourism Law of the People's Republic of China,” Taiwan compatriots traveling on the mainland enjoy the same legal protection as mainland residents. If the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots are infringed, they may, in accordance with the “Measures for Handling Tourism Complaints,” file a complaint with the county-level or higher tourism complaint handling agency at the location of the tourism operator, the place where the tourism contract was signed, or the place where the tourism dispute occurred. They may also call the 12345 government service hotline or contact local Taiwan Affairs Offices for assistance.\nOur press conference ends here. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260909_12787252.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-09-11","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Taiwanese official Hsiao Bi-khim is in Italy. Does China have a response to this?","China has lodged serious protests with Italy and the EU side on the “Taiwan independence” politicians’ attendance at the conference in Italy. The DPP authorities and individual politicians from Taiwan are making every attempt to grab attention and solicit external support for their separatist agenda under the pretext of “democracy” and “freedom.” Their moves are truly despicable and simply futile. Let me reiterate that there is but one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes official interactions of any form between China’s Taiwan region and countries having diplomatic ties with China. The one-China principle is a widely-recognized norm in international relations and a prevailing international consensus. It is also the political foundation of China-Italy relations and China-EU relations. We urge relevant parties to honor the one-China principle with real action.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260911_12020880.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260911_12020879.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-09-14","Guo Jiakun","China Daily","It’s reported that some Panamanian lawmakers recently set up a so-called “Panama-Taiwan parliamentary exchange group.” U.S. lawmakers attended the launch of the group via video link. Regarding this, Panamanian President José Raúl Mulino stated that the Panamanian government reiterates that “foreign relations are directed by the Executive,” and engagements of the parliamentarians with Taiwan “do not mean that the…","There is but one China in the world and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. China firmly opposes official interactions and engagements of any form between the Taiwan authorities and countries having diplomatic ties with China, and does not allow interference in China’s internal affairs by any external forces. We urge those few politicians to see the real picture. To cross the line on the Taiwan question will lead to serious consequences.\nThe establishment of this so-called “parliamentary exchange group” seriously violates the one-China principle upheld by Panama. We noted the statement of the Panamanian government and hopes that Panama will honor its commitment to the one-China principle with real actions to uphold the political foundation of China-Panama relations. China urges the U.S. to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, stop sending the wrong message to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and stop disrupting and sabotaging China-Panama relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260914_12021997.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260914_12021744.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-09-15","Guo Jiakun","Kyodo News","The cross-party Japan-China Friendship Parliamentarians’ Union had a meeting with Assistant Foreign Minister Liu Bin yesterday. Can you share more details and how does China view the significance of this talk?","On September 14, Assistant Foreign Minister Liu Bin met with the delegation of young Japanese lawmakers from the Japan-China Friendship Parliamentarians’ Union, who was on a visit to China. China stressed that the crux of the serious difficulties in China-Japan relations lies in Prime Minister of Japan Sanae Takaichi’s erroneous words and deeds on Taiwan. The Japanese side should honor the spirit of the four political documents, learn the lesson of history, and earn trust from its Asian neighbors and the rest of the world with concrete actions. We hope that the Japan-China Friendship Parliamentarians’ Union will carry forward its tradition of goodwill toward China, step up to its responsibility, and create conditions and a sound environment for bringing the bilateral relations back to the right track.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260915_12022885.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260915_12022859.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-09-16","Guo Jiakun","Global Times","It is reported that Lin Chia-lung, head of the “foreign affairs” department of the Taiwan authorities, in a recent interview confirmed the plan to set up a “representative’s office” in the central Philippine province of Cebu, which will serve as a platform to deepen ties through the “Taiwan-Philippines economic corridor.” What’s your comment?","Let me stress again, no matter how the DPP authorities collude with external forces to seek “diplomatic breakthroughs” and advance their separatist agenda in whatever form, such attempts will be all in vain and doomed to fail. We also urge the Philippine side to abide by the one-China principle with concrete actions, and refrain from taking any steps that could harm China-Philippines relations.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260916_12023728.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260916_12023724.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 16, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Welcome everyone to the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. We will now begin taking questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","The 6th “Joining Hands to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar” was recently held in Xinjiang and has drawn high attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant details.","From September 11 to 12, the 6th “Hand in Hand to Realize Dreams — Cross-Strait Compatriots Exchange and Seminar Event” was successfully held in Urumqi, Xinjiang. Officials, party and group leaders, and representatives from relevant parties and groups on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, along with more than 120 experts, scholars, and representatives of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan youth, attended the event.\nSong Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the opening ceremony and delivered a speech. He called on compatriots on both sides of the Strait to work steadfastly toward the great cause of national reunification, to strive persistently for our common well-being, and to strengthen themselves unceasingly for the rejuvenation of the nation. Chen Xiaojiang, Party Secretary of the CPC Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region Committee, introduced in his speech the major achievements of Xinjiang's economic and social development, guided by the Party's strategy for governing Xinjiang in the new era. He stated that Xinjiang will continue to deepen exchanges and cooperation with Taiwan in all fields and contribute to the integrated development of both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nAround the theme of “Peaceful Development, Safeguarding Our Homeland, United Struggle, and Working Together for Rejuvenation,” the participants held in-depth exchanges and discussions and reached five important consensuses. These include: upholding the great righteousness of the nation and promoting spiritual connection among compatriots; opposing separatism and interference and firmly safeguarding our common homeland; sharing broad opportunities and deepening cross-Strait integration and development; pooling the strength of compatriots and uniting to jointly pursue national rejuvenation; and consciously shouldering responsibility and writing a youthful chapter in the great cause of rejuvenation. These consensuses reflect the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, who are united in advancing national reunification and jointly creating a bright future of national rejuvenation.\nThe participants visited the thematic achievement exhibition marking the 70th anniversary of the founding of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region and toured world-leading wind power equipment manufacturers, among other sites. They personally witnessed Xinjiang's favorable situation of social stability and harmony, strong momentum for development, ethnic unity and progress, harmonious and amicable religious relations, flourishing cultural development, and people living and working in peace and contentment. They each called for adhering to the principle that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, opposing “Taiwan independence” and separatism, and for compatriots on both sides to work together to promote reunification and jointly pursue rejuvenation. They strongly demanded that the DPP authorities lift the restrictions and obstacles to cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, fully restore normal cross-Strait passenger air direct flights, and resume cross-Strait flights to cities such as Urumqi as soon as possible. These demands have resonated in Taiwan society.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788691.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson’s remarks welcoming public discussion after an associate professor at National Changhua University of Education in Taiwan proposed exploring a “one country, two systems” plan for Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland would not agree to a single one of the several conditions raised in the article. What is your comment on this?","The trend of national reunification is moving forward irresistibly. Achieving peaceful reunification across the Strait is a blessing for the Chinese nation. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to express their views freely and pool their wisdom, and to offer specific opinions and suggestions on the “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan. The earlier and more fully Taiwan compatriots discuss the specific content of the “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan, the more opportunities it will bring for Taiwan’s economic and social development, and the more benefits it will bring to themselves.\nOut of its “Taiwan independence” separatist nature, the DPP authorities place political self-interest above the pursuit of interests and well-being by Taiwan compatriots. They obstruct people on both sides of the Strait from exchanging views on the future of cross-Strait relations. Their intentions are sinister, and they have lost the support of the people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788688.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","On September 16, the Pinglu Canal was officially completed and opened to navigation, drawing attention from cross-Strait industry circles. What conveniences has it brought to Taiwan-invested enterprises along the canal?","On September 16, the Pingyu Canal officially opened to navigation. The Pingyu Canal is a key project of the New International Land-Sea Trade Corridor in western mainland China. It will open a river-sea intermodal channel linking the Xijiang River directly to the Beibu Gulf ports, radiating to western regions including Chongqing, Sichuan, Guizhou, and Yunnan, and closely connecting the western inland hinterland with the ASEAN market. Cargo from western regions going to sea via the Pingyu Canal can shorten the voyage by more than 560 kilometers, and logistics costs can be reduced by 18%–30%.\nThe opening of navigation of the Pingyu Canal has drawn wide attention from industry circles on both sides of the Strait. Taiwanese businesspeople generally believe that the Pingyu Canal will facilitate Taiwanese enterprises in linking up with resources in western mainland cities, and that rail-river-sea intermodal transport can effectively reduce import and export logistics costs, forming an industrial chain of “western raw material processing — Guangxi river-sea transshipment — ASEAN market sales,” which creates new opportunities for Taiwan-funded enterprises to open up the ASEAN market. We welcome Taiwanese businesspeople and enterprises to share the opportunities of the New International Land-Sea Trade Corridor in western China, and to take root on the mainland to achieve better development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788685.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, the 2026 China International Fair for Trade in Services (CIFTIS) was held in Beijing from the 9th to the 13th, and the Taiwan image exhibition was well received there. Please provide relevant information.","From September 9 to 13, 2026, the China International Fair for Trade in Services (CIFTIS) was held in Beijing. Adhering to the concept of “Global Services, Mutual Benefit and Shared Results,” the fair closely followed the demands for expanding capacity and improving the quality of service industry development, and adhered to its direction of holding the fair with “professionalism, internationalization, distinctiveness, and marketization.” More than 1,830 enterprises exhibited on-site, and more than 5,300 enterprises exhibited online.\nDuring the fair, the Taiwan Image Exhibition was widely welcomed. Themed “Integrated Development of Services, Shared National Future,” the Taiwan Image Exhibition featured more than 40 cross-Strait business associations and Taiwan-invested enterprises. During the fair, the Fourth Cross-Strait Service Trade Promotion Conference was held, the “Research on Cross-Strait Service Trade Development” was released, the “Framework Agreement on Promoting Cross-Strait Agricultural Product Trade Cooperation” and the “Framework Agreement on Cooperation in Taiwan Agricultural Product Procurement” were signed, and the Beijing Branch of the Bank of China and the Beijing Taiwan-Invested Enterprises Association signed a financial services cooperation agreement, providing credit lines of RMB 2 billion for Taiwanese enterprises in Beijing, effectively converting policy dividends into enterprise development momentum.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","The 26th China International Fair for Investment and Trade (CIFIT) opened in Xiamen on September 8. It is understood that this year’s CIFIT has comprehensively upgraded the cross-Strait integrated development zone, building an exchange platform for cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan compatriot businesses and enterprises at this year’s fair.","From September 8 to 11, the 26th China International Fair for Investment and Trade (CIFIT) was held in Xiamen, Fujian. CIFIT has the permanent theme “Expanding Two-Way Investment, Jointly Promoting Global Development,” and features an exhibition and negotiation area of 200,000 square meters and 14 planned professional exhibition zones, dedicated to building an investment event for global open cooperation.\nDuring CIFIT, the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Zone, under the theme “Linking Both Sides of the Strait, Sharing New Opportunities,” set up three major functional areas: the Taiwan-funded enterprise showcase area, the cross-strait industrial park matching area, and the roadshow promotion area. It is dedicated to creating a new cooperation scenario that integrates achievement display, industrial exchange and project matching, and to building a precise exchange and cooperation platform for cross-strait industrial coordination and for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises developing on the mainland. Building on its debut in 2025, the zone has undergone comprehensive expansion and quality improvement: its exhibition area has been expanded from 500 square meters to 1,000 square meters, its industry coverage has become more diverse, focusing on integrated circuits, precision machinery, biopharmaceuticals, financial services, consumer food and other fields. The Taiwan-funded enterprise showcase area displays new achievements and applications of 18 Taiwan-funded enterprises in technological innovation, product development and industrial integration. The cross-strait industrial park matching area presents park policies, implementation procedures and benchmark cases, and provides on-site investment matching, policy consultation and other services. The roadshow promotion area is equipped with professional large screens and negotiation space, and hosts new product launches, project promotions, specialty product experiences and other activities.\nIt is understood that the Cross-Strait Integrated Development Zone will be a permanent fixture at CIFIT, providing further support for cross-strait economic and trade integrated development and promoting exchanges and cooperation between enterprises on both sides in more fields and at deeper levels.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","The DPP authorities have long pushed “de-Sinicization” in education on the island, cutting numerous excellent classical Chinese essays from the curriculum, causing confusion in Taiwanese students' historical understanding. Some students even understood “the Oath of the Peach Garden” to mean an alliance in Taoyuan City, Taiwan, which has caused concern among academics on the island. What is your comment on this?","Relevant circumstances show that the DPP authorities' long-term “de-Sinicization” education and “cultural Taiwan independence” have already caused serious consequences, which is regrettable and lamentable. Chinese culture is the spiritual homeland of Taiwan compatriots and the spiritual driving force behind Taiwan's economic and social development. When the roots of Chinese culture are severed on the island, and when classic texts refined over centuries are torn away, Taiwan's children have no opportunity to learn from textbooks classic essays such as “Record of Yueyang Tower,” “Record of the Pavilion of the Drunken Old Man,” and “Exhortation to Learning,” and they do not know historical figures such as Zhuge Liang, Yue Fei, and Wen Tianxiang, nor the 72 martyrs of Huanghuagang, nor the Nanjing Massacre... This is not the ignorance of children, but the crime of the “Taiwan independence” forces.\nIf “Taiwan independence” education is allowed to continue being tampered with in this way, Taiwan compatriots cut off from the nourishment of Chinese culture will become duckweed without roots, and Taiwan society without the nourishment of Chinese culture will become a barren desert. Various sectors on the island are deeply worried about this, and more and more Taiwan compatriots oppose “cultural Taiwan independence” and “de-Sinicization” education. They hope that things can be set right, that there can be a correct curriculum that passes on the excellent traditional Chinese culture, and that the spiritual homeland of Taiwan compatriots can be defended.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788687.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","河南广电“大象新闻”记者","With the Mid-Autumn Festival approaching, various places have successively held Mid-Autumn celebration activities for compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On September 16, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Kunshan) Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival lighting ceremony and the closing ceremony of the 6th Cross-Strait Youth Culture Month were held in Kunshan City, Jiangsu Province. The Kunshan Mid-Autumn Lantern Festival has been held for 12 consecutive years; this edition will continue until October 31, and during this period, featured lantern-viewing activities, cross-Strait art exhibitions, a hundred-performance garden fair, the “Moonlit Elegant Gathering” in the forest, and many other activities will take place. The two types of lanterns you see today in the release hall: the larger one is the gold-award work by a Taiwanese youth in the 7th Kunshan Mazu Cup Youth Mid-Autumn Lantern Design Competition, and the smaller one draws on the painting “Tangshan Crossing to Taiwan,” depicting the story of early settlers from the mainland who crossed the sea to Taiwan to open up and build the land. Both lanterns express the hope of compatriots on both sides of the Strait that they share the same roots, the same blood, and jointly pray for reunion.\nOn September 16, the 2026 Yuntai Mid-Autumn Tea Gathering was held in Kunming City, Yunnan Province, attended by more than 300 people, including representatives of the Kaohsiung Elite Volunteer Delegation from Taiwan and representatives of Taiwan compatriots living in Yunnan. Activities included a Taiwan food exhibition, sharing by Taiwanese youth on entrepreneurship, and artistic singing and dance performances. Compatriots on both sides gathered together to celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival and to share kinship and friendship.\nReporter from China Media Group's “Ri Yue Tan Tian” new media program:\nTaiwan media reported that the defense budget and special budget for fiscal year 2027 approved by the Taiwan administrative authorities amount to nearly 4% of GDP, and Hsiao Bi-khim reiterated Lai Ching-te's promise to raise defense spending to 5% of GDP. What is your comment on this?\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities, for the sake of their party's political self-interest, seek to “use force to pursue independence” and “rely on the United States to pursue independence,” and they have gone further, squandering the hard-earned money of the Taiwan people and racing down the dead-end road of militarism. This not only crowds out domestic spending on livelihood and social welfare, harming the immediate interests of the Taiwan people, but also pushes Taiwan step by step into a more dangerous situation, turning the Taiwan people into cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence.” This conduct, which harms Taiwan and destroys it and brings about its own downfall, will certainly meet with strong opposition from the Taiwan people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788689.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","福建东南卫视记者","Recently, cultural exchange activities in cross-Strait film, television, music, fine arts and other fields have been lively. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On September 8, “Sound” Gathers Both Sides of the Strait Because of You: The Jingtai Youth Talent Concert was held in Zhangzhou, Fujian Province, with more than 100 Taiwan compatriots taking part. The activities covered a range of genres, including Minnan-language hometown songs, original programs by Taiwan youth, solo dance, and traditional opera, vividly showcasing the cultural heritage that shares common roots and origins on both sides of the Strait and the upbeat spirit of young people across the Strait.\nOn September 12, the 17th Cross-Strait Children and Youth Art Exhibition opened in Taipei. Themed “Trust” (信), roughly 200 works by young people from the Chinese mainland, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macao were displayed together, and the theme for the next round of submissions, “Seeing” (看见), was announced. The exhibition was warmly received and widely praised by all walks of life on the island. For the convenience of viewers who could not attend in person, an online exhibition was launched for the first time. The Taipei exhibition runs through September 17, and after it concludes, it will tour Beijing, Kaohsiung, and other cities.\nFrom September 16 to 20, the 12th “Golden Swallow” Cross-Strait Micro-Film and Micro-Video Competition Carnival was held in Wuhan. Themed “Gazing · Tide” (望·潮), the competition received nearly 500 entries from both sides of the Strait, about half of them from the island. After selection by experts from both sides, 61 outstanding works were shortlisted, covering subjects such as everyday life on both sides of the Strait, youth growth, family ties and nostalgia for home, cross-disciplinary AI, and cultural inheritance. Youth from both sides attending the carnival will also take part in activities including Jingchu intangible cultural heritage experiences, an AI creation academic salon, a visit to a micro-short-drama industry base, and a Chinese-style red carpet show.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, the ancient-costume micro-drama 'Emperor Jiaqing Tours Taiwan' went online and began airing, drawing attention from viewers on the island. Please introduce the relevant situation.","To actively implement the ten policy measures promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation that the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee was authorized to release, the Beijing Municipal Taiwan Affairs Office guided the government new media account “Jingcai Taiwan” in producing the ancient-costume micro-drama *Emperor Jiaqing Visits Taiwan*, which held its premiere ceremony in Beijing on September 11. The drama draws on Taiwanese folk legends and glove-puppetry elements, blending regional culture with distinctive local opera styles. Several Taiwanese actors took part in the performances and in the Southern Min (Hokkien) dubbing for this ancient-costume micro-drama. All 70 episodes have gone online on the “Jingcai Taiwan” WeChat Channels account and will be released gradually on mainstream platforms at home and abroad in the near future. We welcome and support more Taiwanese businesses in creating micro-dramas for the mainland. Taiwanese businesses may establish broadcast and television program production and operation companies in Fujian, may co-produce micro-dramas with mainland businesses, and may take part directly in performances of all kinds of micro-dramas. We hope people on both sides of the Strait will see more fine micro-drama works featuring Taiwanese businesses.\nFrom September 15, Dongnan Satellite TV will broadcast the seven-episode Taiwanese TV drama *Fairy Tale Stories, Part II*, opening a new chapter in making cross-Strait film and television cultural exchanges more substantive and deeper. Everyone is welcome to watch.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","The DPP recently said that it is the mainland that is undermining peace across the Taiwan Strait, that Taiwan does not accept the one-China principle set by the mainland, and that the mainland has therefore unilaterally suspended institutionalized cross-Strait consultations, halted individual tourism by mainland residents to Taiwan, and blocked mainland students and mainland tourists from traveling to Taiwan.…","The DPP is accustomed to turning black into white, shifting blame, and playing the victim. The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. This is a historical fact and a legal reality. It is precisely on the basis of the 1992 Consensus, which embodies the one-China principle, that the two sides have been able to conduct consultations and negotiations and reach a series of outcomes that benefit compatriots on both sides. After the DPP took office, it stubbornly adhered to its “Taiwan independence” stance, refused to acknowledge the 1992 Consensus that embodies the one-China principle, and unilaterally undermined the political foundation for cross-strait consultations. This has caused the institutionalized cross-strait consultation and negotiation mechanisms and communication channels to stall, continuously eroded the achievements of peaceful development of cross-strait relations, and constantly threatened peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities have also gone further in obstructing and restricting personnel exchanges and exchanges and cooperation in all fields across the Strait, seriously harming the tangible interests of Taiwan compatriots, and this has drawn opposition and criticism from all sectors of society on the island.\nWe advise the DPP authorities to stop political manipulation, listen more to the voices of the public and industry on the island, and do more things that are conducive to the development of cross-strait relations and the well-being of compatriots on both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait economic and trade exchange activities.","On September 11, the 20th Gan-Taiwan (Lushan) Economic, Trade and Cultural Cooperation and Exchange Conference opened in Lushan, Jiangxi. The exchange conference was co-hosted by the People's Government of Jiangxi Province and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, and supported by the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriot Enterprises, the Chinese National Federation of Industries, and others. Themed 'Cross-Strait Hands in Hand with One Heart, Gan-Taiwan Integrated Development,' the conference focuses on four key areas: economic and trade matchmaking, industrial cooperation, cultural tourism integration, and youth exchanges. Supporting special activities include promotions on electronic information and equipment manufacturing, modern agriculture, and cultural tourism cooperation, as well as an award ceremony for the Gan-Taiwan Youth Short Video Competition.\nFrom September 19 to 21, the 29th Beijing-Taiwan Science and Technology Forum will be held in Beijing. Themed 'Science and Technology Lead Industrial Integration, Digital Intelligence Empowers a Healthy Future,' the forum adopts a '1+4+N' model, holding 1 main forum, 4 parallel forums, and N series of activities. The forum will invite heads of Taiwan business and industry groups, including the Taiwan side of the Cross-Strait Entrepreneurs Summit, the Electrical and Electronic Manufacturers' Association, the Chinese National Federation of Industries, the General Chamber of Commerce, the Industrial and Commercial Association, and the Three-Three Enterprise Exchange Association, as well as industry, commerce, and technology figures on the island and representatives of Taiwan businesspeople on both sides of the Strait.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairman of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the mainland is pursuing a strategy of “exercising jurisdiction before unification” through four major means: “internalizing administrative and judicial jurisdiction, making the international system’s one-China principle a matter of course, granting Taiwan residents national treatment, and integrating offshore islands with mainland…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of Chinese territory. The historical and legal facts that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China cannot be changed. The historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified, cannot be stopped, and the future and destiny of Taiwan can and must only be jointly decided by all 1.4 billion-plus Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, refuse to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” that embodies the one-China principle, and scheme to interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges. This completely goes against the mainstream public opinion on both sides of the Strait that calls for peace, development, exchanges and cooperation, and it has met with joint opposition from people on both sides of the Strait.\nOur policies toward Taiwan are clear and consistent. We will firmly uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and integrated development, enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and firmly advance the process of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788690.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the cross-Strait espionage drama “Clash” was broadcast and has drawn attention and discussion from audiences on both sides of the Strait. Liang Wen-chieh, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the drama is part of the mainland's efforts to promote national security education and publicity among the entire population. What is your comment on this?","We have noted the approval of the TV drama *Confrontation* by audiences on both sides of the Strait. This drama reflects the steadfastness and sacrifice of the unsung heroes on the covert front, and shows that safeguarding national security is the responsibility and obligation of every citizen.\nWe will adhere to the holistic approach to national security and resolutely carry out the struggle against separatism, subversion, infiltration, and espionage theft, effectively safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and protect national security and development interests. It must be emphasized that the future of Taiwan and the security, interests, and well-being of Taiwan compatriots lie in the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and national reunification. Opposing “Taiwan independence” accords with the fundamental interests and immediate well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We hope the broad Taiwan compatriots will join us in firmly guarding against the sabotage of peaceful cross-Strait development and the interference in the process of national reunification by the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and hostile external forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788684.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, Grandma Chu from Taiwan sent 62 train tickets from “Zhuifen Station” to “Chenggong Station” in Taichung City to senior-year students at Shenzhen No. 7 High School, expressing her blessings for their success in the college entrance examination. Fifty students handwrote replies to Grandma Chu. This story has moved many people on both sides of the Strait. What is your comment?","Sixty-two train tickets carried the sincere goodwill and blessings of a Taiwanese grandmother for her juniors. Fifty handwritten letters conveyed the gratitude of a Shenzhen teenager toward elders. This is a vivid expression of “cross-strait families are one.” There are many similar stories, such as a Taiwanese man who posted online asking for help, and mainland internet users who in turn helped his father travel in Shenyang. Or a Taiwanese village chief who went back and forth across the strait to help hundreds of veterans who went to Taiwan return home to their roots, allowing cross-strait families to be reunited......\nThe goodwill and sincerity of two-way exchanges between people on both sides of the strait deeply confirm the profound friendship between compatriots on both sides, as close as blood and bone, and interpret the Chinese cultural virtues of respecting the elderly and caring for the young. This is the inexhaustible driving force of cross-strait civilian exchanges and the strong bond of cross-strait kinship. We wish that all third-year students at No. 7 High School will reach the admission cutoff score as Grandma Chu hoped. We also welcome Grandma Chu and more Taiwan friends to bring the blessings of the 50 students to Shenzhen and other places on the mainland to see and experience them for themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","Recently, the Panama National Assembly established a “cross-party parliamentary exchange group” with Taiwan's legislative body, and the DPP authorities welcomed this. What is your comment?","The relevant departments have already stated their solemn position on this. There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. We urge the Pakistani side to immediately correct the relevant wrong practices and implement the One-China Principle in practice. No matter what banner the DPP authorities fly while “relying on outside forces to seek independence,” they are doomed to a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, a cross-Strait tourism industry symposium was held in Lushan, Jiangxi. Please introduce the relevant information.","On September 11, a cross-Strait tourism industry symposium was held at Mount Lushan in Jiangxi. Representatives of the tourism industry from Jiangxi, Shanghai, Fujian, and Taiwan, more than 60 people in total, attended. They conducted in-depth exchanges on matters related to cross-Strait tourism, including jointly building cultural and tourism products and mutually sending tourist sources, to promote deeper and more substantive cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation.\nTaiwan tourism industry representatives attending the meeting said that the Taiwan tourism industry sincerely hopes cross-Strait tourism exchanges can return to normal as soon as possible, and that mainland residents can travel to Taiwan island as soon as possible. The Taiwan tourism industry is willing to actively work toward this and jointly promote the prosperous development of the cross-Strait tourism industry. Industry representatives from both sides unanimously agreed that tourism is a direct and vivid carrier of civil exchanges across the Taiwan Strait, that cross-Strait cultural and tourism resources are rich and each has its own characteristics, and that there is a solid foundation for cooperation. They hope to further open channels for industry connection, strengthen business exchanges, tap cooperation potential, and develop distinctive tourism routes that suit the needs of people on both sides, so as to bring compatriots on both sides closer in spirit.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","The “Regulations of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” took effect on September 15. The DPP authorities have continuously smeared and attacked these regulations. The Mainland Affairs Council has even warned that “five categories of people” on the island should pay attention to exit and entry risks when traveling to the mainland. What is your comment?","The promulgation and implementation of the “Regulations of the State Council on Exit and Entry Administration” are intended to standardize exit and entry administration, safeguard the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting and entering, and safeguard national sovereignty, security, and development interests. The Regulations mainly improve the institutional safeguards against exit security risks, stipulate that the grounds for exit and entry applications must be truthful and lawful, and standardize exit and entry intermediary services. These Regulations are conducive to safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of people traveling across the Taiwan Strait, and create a better rule-of-law environment for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. Broad Taiwan compatriots who travel to the mainland lawfully and in compliance with regulations for tourism, family visits, visits, and exchanges will surely come with joy and leave with satisfaction.\nThe DPP authorities are alarmist, fabricate rumors, smear and mislead the public, with sinister intentions. They have deliberately sought to restrict and prohibit cross-Strait exchanges and travel, and use suppression, intimidation, rumors, and other means to block compatriots on both sides from getting closer to each other, because they fear that the information cocoons they have created will keep being pierced and the false “Taiwan independence” narrative they have built will keep being exposed. From January to June this year, 2.85 million Taiwan compatriot visits to the mainland were recorded, a year-on-year increase of 24.9%. Taiwan compatriots continue to travel back and forth across the Strait without end, which, through the clearest actions, proves how absurd and laughable the DPP authorities’ restrictions and obstructions are.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260916_12788686.htm"],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Recently, multiple cross-party pro-Taiwan Japanese politicians formed a delegation to sneak into Taiwan, saying that “a Taiwan contingency is a Japanese contingency,” and advocated that Japan refer to the United States in drafting a “Taiwan Relations Act” and intervene in Taiwan Strait affairs. What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. Japanese lawmakers' visit to the Taiwan region and clamor for so-called “defense cooperation” violate the one-China principle and the spirit of the four political documents between China and Japan, and we firmly oppose this.\nThe DPP authorities, in seeking political self-interest and attempting to “curry favor with Japan to seek independence” and “seek independence through force,” will only harm and ruin Taiwan and bring about their own destruction.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Taiwan media reported that the DPP authorities’ cyber force, the “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command,” plans to spend NT$95.93 million in its 2027 defense budget to form a so-called “cyber hunting team,” claiming it must “proactively detect and eliminate mainland hackers who have long lurked and are continuously sabotaging.” What is your comment?","The DPP authorities have manipulated the “Information, Communications and Electronic Force Command” (资通电军) to frequently attack and sabotage mainland network facilities, disrupting social order and harming the interests of the public. Since June 2025, mainland public security organs have carried out concentrated crackdowns on its organized cyber illegal and criminal activities. They have jumped out to provoke trouble, which is purely overestimating themselves.\nPublic security organs will firmly safeguard national security and the lawful rights and interests of relevant enterprises and the people, and will take effective measures in accordance with law to crack down on the relevant illegal and criminal acts.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan's sports authority revised and issued the “Cross-Strait Sports Exchange Handling Guidelines,” requiring that Taiwan residents not serve as athletes on mainland national representative teams competing in international events, indicating the policy bottom line for cross-Strait sports exchanges. What comments do you have on this?","Sports are an important bridge and link between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and have always played a unique role in promoting cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation and deepening friendship among compatriots on both sides. Strengthening cross-Strait sports exchanges and cooperation is a common wish of sports circles on both sides and is in line with the overall interests of Taiwan’s sports circles.\nAny act that attempts to interfere with or obstruct cross-Strait sports exchanges or politicize sports will ultimately harm the interests and well-being of Taiwan’s sports practitioners and the public. It is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Some commentary on the island analyzes that this year's G7 summit once again stressed the importance of peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, opposed any unilateral change to the status quo, and advocated resolving issues through peaceful dialogue, showing that Western countries refuse to give Taiwan a “blank check” to change the status quo. What is your comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair. It tolerates no external interference and no one pointing fingers. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese people themselves. The root cause of undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and causing tension is the DPP authorities’ stubborn adherence to the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, their refusal to acknowledge the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and their continued provocations to seek “independence.” Maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait requires resolute opposition to “Taiwan independence” separatism. We hope relevant countries will strictly adhere to the one-China principle and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe true status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Only if the DPP authorities abandon their “Taiwan independence” separatist ambitions, stop provoking to seek “independence,” and acknowledge the “1992 Consensus” can cross-Strait communication and contact resume, and only then will there be a basic guarantee for peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, a number of discussions have appeared online in Taiwan about the growing appeal of mainland social media platforms to young people in Taiwan. Many netizens said that mainland social platforms offer rich and in-depth information, and that even for obscure knowledge one can find instructional videos there. The interactive experience of “danmu” (bullet comments) can also provide emotional value. What is…","Many social media platforms on the mainland are indeed good channels for learning and self-improvement. Many Taiwanese netizens regard mainland social media platforms as a “second classroom.” They can not only conveniently obtain rich and diverse information and knowledge, but also interact with like-minded netizens through danmaku, comments, and other means, make good friends, and achieve cooperation. We welcome more Taiwanese netizens to obtain information and broaden their horizons through mainland social media platforms, make friends, accumulate positive energy, and take part in cross-Strait exchanges in various ways.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","The first question: this year’s Shanghai-Taipei City Forum will be held in Taipei. The Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office deputy director was originally scheduled to lead a delegation to Taiwan for a preparatory visit, but the Mainland Affairs Council blocked the trip and only approved personnel at the division-chief level to travel to Taiwan. Outside observers are concerned that the level of Shanghai’s participation…","First question. The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been held for 16 consecutive years. Through discussions on multiple topics including economy, culture, technology, society, sports, and urban management, it has reached many areas of consensus and achieved fruitful results. It has won general recognition from residents of both cities and compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait, and has become an important platform for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The DPP authorities have unreasonably obstructed and hindered the preparations for the forum, going against mainstream public opinion on the island and losing popular support.\nSecond question. The One-China Principle is a general consensus of the international community, and the trend toward national reunification is unstoppable. The diehard “Taiwan independence” elements are at the end of their rope, like birds startled by a bow. For the “Taiwan independence” diehards on the list, we will show no leniency, and we will take all necessary measures to punish them in accordance with the law and hold them accountable for life.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《旺报》记者","Recently, the wife of Taipei Mayor Jiang Wan'an introduced herself as “Chinese Taipei” while participating in an APEC event, and some public opinion holds that this name is problematic. Taiwan's “Minister of Labor” Hong Shenhan said that “Chinese Taipei” is indeed Taiwan's official name in APEC. What is your comment?","Under the One-China Principle, Taiwan participates in APEC and its activities as a regional economy under the name “Chinese Taipei.” This is an important political precondition for Taiwan’s participation in APEC, and all parties must abide by the provisions and practices of APEC’s relevant memoranda of understanding.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Regarding Shen Boyang's recent appearance on a Japanese street wearing a bulletproof vest, in which he claimed that he is wanted by the mainland and that, because he is running for Taipei mayor, he must pay special attention to his personal safety. What is your comment on this?","A handful of stubborn “Taiwan independence” diehards repeatedly stage absurd farces and seek notoriety, fully exposing their essence of being fierce in appearance but weak at heart. Those who remain obstinate and unrepentant will certainly not escape severe punishment under national law.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","Last year, after Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an attended the “Twin Cities Forum,” the Mainland side announced military drills against Taiwan one day later. Under these circumstances, what substantive role does the “Twin Cities Forum” play in peaceful cross-Strait exchanges? How can the Mainland side make Taiwan's people believe that cross-Strait exchanges can cool tensions in the Taiwan Strait and bring cross-Strait…","It is meaningless to link these two matters.\nThe Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been held for 16 consecutive years. It has reached many points of consensus on issues including economy, culture, technology, society, sports, and urban management, and has achieved fruitful results. It is widely recognized by residents of both cities and by compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and has become an important platform for cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. We hope this platform can continue to play its due role.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-16","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森电视台记者","First question: Shen Boyang, a candidate for Taipei mayor, recently said that if elected mayor, he would dare to attend the “Twin Cities Forum.” What is your comment on this? Second question: Ashin (Chen Xinhong) of the Taiwanese band Mayday recently attended an Apple product launch event. When someone on site introduced him as coming from China, staff reminded him, “Do not mention this topic.” Does the mainland…","On the first question: People like Shen Boyang repeatedly stage absurd farces and seek cheap publicity. He has also previously said, “Everyone thinks military service is a waste of time.” People of this kind, on the one hand, peddle “Taiwan independence” propositions to the Taiwan public, especially young people, advocating “resisting unification by force” and “everyone a soldier,” and urging other people's children to go to the battlefield as cannon fodder; on the other hand, they hide behind others and are even ready to slip away at any moment. This hypocritical face and ugly conduct are despicable, and they fully prove that “Taiwan independence” cannot succeed.\nOn the second question: Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. This is the historical and legal fact across the Strait and the broad consensus of the international community.\nMore and more Taiwan performing artists are expressing, in various ways, their identification with Chinese culture and with the idea that “both sides of the Strait are one family.” This is a natural and genuine outpouring of feeling. We hope that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will jointly safeguard a good atmosphere for cross-Strait cultural exchanges and do more things that help build mutual trust and bring hearts closer.\nThis press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260916_12788699.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-09-21","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","The New Zealand Defence Force said today that two of its naval ships have transited the Taiwan Strait. The New Zealand PM called this a routine activity and said he was not expecting any backlash from China. Does China have any comment on this event?","China’s position on foreign military vessels’ transit through the Taiwan Strait is consistent.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260921_12027763.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260921_12027748.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 23, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian first announced the holding of the “Moon Full Over Beijing, Hearts Linked Across the Strait — 2026 Cross-Strait Compatriots Mid-Autumn Festival Gathering,” and then answered reporters' questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Welcome everyone to the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office press conference.\nOn September 23, the “Moon Full Over Beijing, Cross-Strait Hearts Connected — 2026 Cross-Strait Compatriots Mid-Autumn Festival Gathering” was held at Yanqi Lake in Beijing. More than 400 guests from both sides of the Strait attended, including more than 300 Taiwan guests, among them representatives of relevant sectors on the island, well-known entrepreneurs, and Taiwan compatriots in Beijing. Activities included a Mid-Autumn tea gathering for compatriots on both sides, the “e起绽放吧” (“Let’s Bloom Together”) Strait Song Gathering, and more. Compatriots from both sides admired the bright moon together, shared their feelings for their hometowns, looked forward to the future together, and celebrated the traditional Chinese festival together.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","As the Mid-Autumn Festival approaches, Taiwan pomelos are being put on shelves in many places on the mainland. On September 22, the “Taste Taiwan Pomelo, Celebrate the Full Moon Mid-Autumn Festival” event was held in Shenzhen. Please introduce the relevant situation.","In April of this year, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office was authorized to issue ten policy measures to promote cross-strait exchanges and cooperation. On the political foundation of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” relevant parties on both sides of the Strait have jointly worked to put these policies into effect, helping more island farmers and fishermen open up the mainland market, with positive results. Many Taiwanese packaging plants, orchards, and food enterprises have registered in the mainland, customs clearance efficiency has continued to improve, and logistics and transportation have become more convenient.\nIt is worth mentioning that, thanks to the joint efforts of all parties, Taiwan’s wendan pomelo has appeared at trade fairs in many places on the mainland and has been put on sale in supermarkets, farmers’ markets, and e-commerce platforms, where it has been welcomed by a wide range of consumers. During the Mid-Autumn Festival and National Day holidays, more Taiwanese wendan pomelo will enter households across the mainland, more mainland consumers will be able to taste high-quality Taiwanese fruit, and more grassroots Taiwanese fruit growers will be able to share in the vast opportunities of the mainland market. This two-way effort presents a vivid picture of integrated development and mutual benefit. We will continue to uphold the concept that “across the Strait, we are one family,” actively promote economic exchanges and cooperation across the Strait, and let compatriots on both sides share the dividends of peaceful development and integrated development of cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814587.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","With the Mid-Autumn Festival approaching, what activities are being held in various localities for cross-Strait compatriots to celebrate the festival together?","The Mid-Autumn Festival will arrive the day after tomorrow. We extend Mid-Autumn greetings to compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait: may flowers bloom and the moon is full, families reunite, and mutual understanding and companionship bring prosperity in all things. (In Hokkien) Wishing our kinsfolk on both sides of the Strait a happy Mid-Autumn Festival and a peaceful reunion. (In Hakka) Whether at home or away from home, whether eating sweet or savory mooncakes, everyone can enjoy the moon with family and share a cup of tea. We also welcome our Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to take part in the rich and colorful Mid-Autumn friendship activities.\nOn September 19, the Shandong Provincial Association of Taiwan Compatriots' Relatives and the Taiwan Shandong Fellow Villagers Association jointly held the 2026 Shandong Cross-Strait Fellow Villagers Mid-Autumn Friendship Gathering via video link in Jinan and Taipei, titled “Cross-Strait Shandong Melodies Form a Cloud Bridge, Talking About Reunion at the Mid-Autumn Festival of the Bing-Wu Year.” Nearly 200 representatives took part: Taiwan businesspeople, Taiwan youth and Taiwan compatriots' relatives in Jinan, and Shandong fellow villagers from various sectors in Taipei. Compatriots on both sides exchanged holiday greetings across the screen and jointly watched wonderful arts performances from both places in a joyful and harmonious atmosphere.\nFrom September 22 to 26, Hebei Province held a series of Mid-Autumn welcoming friendship activities for Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan youth titled “Youth Rendezvous, Chasing Dreams in Yan-Zhao.” More than 120 people, including representatives of the Taiwan-based cultural tourism industry association, Taiwan youth representatives, and representatives of the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei Taiwan Business Association, gathered in Shijiazhuang. They carried out enterprise visits, promotion of the investment environment of the province and cities, cultural tourism industry inspections, cross-strait softball exchanges and other activities, and conducted on-site inspections of key industries and distinctive cultural tourism resources in Zhengding, Zhao County, Luquan and the High-tech Zone.\nFrom September 19 to 23, Zhangzhou, Quanzhou and other places in Fujian Province held multiple Mid-Autumn friendship activities. On the 19th, the 2nd Cross-Strait (Zhangzhou) Women and Family Carnival · Cross-Strait Marriage and Family Mid-Autumn Festival Friendship Activity was held in Zhangzhou. A hundred representatives of cross-strait marriage families and of Taiwan compatriots and relatives of Taiwan compatriots in Zhangzhou took part, sharing stories of harmonious family life and experiencing Fujian-Taiwan specialty snacks, Mid-Autumn lantern making, and a dragon dance parade through century-old tulou.\nOn the 23rd, the “The Moon Shines Brightest in Our Hometown — 2026 Cross-Strait (Zhangzhou) Mid-Autumn Gala” was held in Zhangzhou. More than 150 representatives of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople from all sectors, and overseas Chinese compatriot representatives, attended. The gala explored shared cross-strait memories such as qiaopi, taipi, and Minnan culture, and presented distinctive programs including scenic dramatizations of qiaopi and taipi, Gezai opera, original Minnan songs, and a Lin Yutang musical, vividly portraying the moving stories of compatriots on both sides of the Strait who share the same roots and origins and integrate their development.\nOn the 23rd, the “Full Moon over Fengshan, Upholding Loyalty and Filial Piety · Celebrating the Mid-Autumn Festival from a Common Origin” Fujian-Taiwan Guangze Zunwang Mid-Autumn Reunion Friendship Activity was held in Quanzhou. Representatives of Guangze Zunwang branch temples in 22 counties and cities in Taiwan, along with believers, totaling more than one hundred people, returned to Nan'an to pay respects to ancestors and celebrate the festival. Through live-action dramas they learned about the filial-piety legends of Guangze Zunwang, and they experienced traditional folk customs such as the bobing dice game and solving lantern riddles.\nOn September 23, the 2026 “Meet Taiwan in Henan · Full Moon, Blooming Flowers” Henan-Taiwan Workers’ Mid-Autumn Friendship Gala was held in Zhengzhou, Henan Province. Worker representatives from both places gathered together and took part in intangible cultural heritage experiences such as crochet, dough figurine making, and cloth tiger sachet making. They celebrated the Mid-Autumn holiday together and shared the joy of reunion.\nOn September 24, the 2026 Hefei Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala will be held at the Qingfeng Pavilion in Baogong Park, Hefei, Anhui, a cross-strait exchange base. Closely following the main theme of “Poetry · Reunion · Family and Nation,” about 300 compatriots from both sides of the Strait will admire the bright moon together and recite timeless poems together. At the gala, the “Hefei Welcomes You” first-visit welfare package for Taiwan compatriots will also be released.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","《参考消息》记者","A recent island “Annual Survey on Cross-Strait Relations” showed that public support exceeds 60% for three measures: continuing to hold cross-Strait exchange platforms, supporting expanded cross-Strait tourist travel, and supporting expanded cross-Strait civilian exchanges in film, television, art, and sports. The support rates are 63%, 67%, and 62%, respectively. What comments do you have on this?","Facts have proven that the desire for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and the collective consensus of all sectors on the island. We will always adhere to the concept of “cross-Strait compatriots as one family,” continue to introduce more policies that benefit Taiwan and its people, constantly strengthen institutional support for cross-Strait exchange and integration, and actively promote personnel exchanges and cooperation across all fields between the two sides. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to take part in cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in various ways, join the process of cross-Strait integrated development, and share the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814577.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities held in various localities.","Over the past week, a range of exchange activities were held across both sides of the Taiwan Strait.\nFrom September 13 to 18, the 4th Cross-Strait Chinese Photography Award and the 7th Cross-Strait Image Culture Week were held in Zhejiang Province, with the theme “Beautiful Countryside — Two-Way Engagement of Cross-Strait Photographers.” More than 300 people from the photography circles on both sides took part, visiting Ningbo, Huzhou, Lishui and other places for site visits and creative work. The activities deepened cultural exchange across the Strait and showcased the new opportunities for Chinese-style modernization in the “15th Five-Year Plan” period.\nOn September 15, the awards ceremony of the 5th Cross-Strait Online Literature Competition was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province. More than 200 guests from both sides, literary creators, enthusiasts, and media reporters attended. The competition received 903 entries from both sides and selected 28 award-winning works. During the event, several well-known writers from both sides delivered keynote speeches, several online literature IP adaptation works were released, and a cross-Strait salon on literary exchange and integrated development was held, effectively promoting exchange and cooperation among online literature enthusiasts on both sides.\nOn September 19–20, the Taipei stop of the “Black Myth: Wukong” Global Concert was held in Taipei City. Singers and musicians from both sides jointly performed theme songs including “Yellow Wind Rising,” “Sounds from the Cloud Palace,” and “May I Ask Where the Road Lies,” and the theater, which seats a thousand, was filled to capacity. Game and music fans from both sides expressed their love for and admiration of national music, and also voiced their hopes for the next game, “Black Myth: Zhong Kui.”\nOn September 23, the “Century Splendor — Cross-Strait National Music Concert Commemorating the 160th Anniversary of the Birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen” was held in Nanjing City, Jiangsu Province. It was co-hosted by the Cross-Strait Exchange Foundation of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Strait and the relevant departments of Jiangsu Province and Nanjing City. Hundreds of outstanding musicians and art groups from both sides will perform national music, symphonic works, and choral pieces, jointly expressing the patriotic sentiments of Chinese people and their fond hopes for unity.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan’s Liberty Times has hyped up claims by some Taiwan businesspeople that their rights and interests were harmed when they invested on the mainland many years ago, accusing the mainland of “lacking protection of the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","We have always attached great importance to and actively safeguarded the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. We have thoroughly implemented the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, incorporated the protection of Taiwan compatriots’ rights and interests into the overall picture of socialist modernization with Chinese characteristics and the building of a country under the rule of law, and continuously improved systems and policies to promote the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The overall framework of comprehensively governing the country according to law has basically taken shape, and a first-class business environment that is market-oriented, rule-of-law-based, and internationalized has continued to improve, providing a fundamental institutional foundation for safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nGovernments and competent authorities at all levels on the mainland empathize with the difficulties and problems encountered by Taiwan compatriots, actively understand their demands, keep their needs in mind, strive to relieve their troubles and difficulties, and improve their well-being through concrete actions. The total number of disputes involving Taiwan affairs accepted by the Taiwan Affairs Office system has been declining year by year, the proportion of cases involving litigation has dropped significantly, and the satisfaction and recognition of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots with the mainland’s legal and business environments have continued to rise.\nIn terms of communication mechanisms for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots across the Taiwan Strait, in 2005 the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and relevant institutions of the Kuomintang established a platform for work on protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan businesspeople. It later developed into a work platform for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots jointly run by the Communist Party of China and the Kuomintang, and has continued to operate to this day. Relying on this platform, relevant parties on both sides of the Strait have conducted extensive and in-depth exchanges on issues of concern to Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and have also resolved many urgent problems that Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises have long hoped to see solved, which is highly recognized by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises. For reasons that are well known, the cross-Strait investment dispute coordination mechanism is currently stalled. However, our commitment to protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will not change. The Taiwan Compatriot Investment Protection Law and its Implementation Rules remain in effect, and the Communist Party of China and Kuomintang platform for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots also remains in effect.\nAs for the claims by individual Taiwan businesspeople you mentioned that their “rights and interests have been harmed,” our understanding is that the relevant cases have already been decided by mainland arbitration and a final ruling by the Supreme People’s Court, and the facts are clear and definitive. We care about and show concern for Taiwan compatriots and safeguard their lawful rights and interests. We also hope that the relevant Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises will respect the facts and the law, safeguard their lawful rights and interests in accordance with laws and regulations, and not be exploited by people with ulterior motives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814584.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Lai Ching-te recently declared that “in the face of highly changing international circumstances and continuously intensifying Chinese threats,” his responsibility is to make Taiwan better prepared and stronger to maintain the status quo, and to not allow peace to be undermined by unilateral provocations. He reiterated that Taiwan's defense budget is expected to reach 5% of GDP by 2030, defending peace with…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The Lai Ching-te authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist “Taiwan independence” position, deliberately escalate cross-Strait opposition and confrontation, and attempt to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on external powers.” They are the chief culprits undermining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and undermining the status quo. For their own political gain, they repeatedly advocate raising defense budgets, squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people on warmongering. This runs counter to mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society and will only accelerate pushing Taiwan into peril. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities: no matter how many budgets they draw up or how many weapons they buy, they cannot change the inevitable demise of “Taiwan independence,” nor can they stop the inevitable trend of the motherland's reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814586.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","As the Mid-Autumn Festival and National Day holidays approach, many compatriots from Taiwan hope to restore more cross-Strait direct air passenger routes. Are there any new arrangements or plans for cross-Strait direct air passenger flight routes and destinations during this holiday?","“The moon is brightest at the Mid-Autumn Festival.” In the hearts of Chinese people, the full moon of the Mid-Autumn Festival symbolizes reunion and fulfillment. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland to celebrate the festival with their families. At present, due to obstruction and interference by the Democratic Progressive Party authorities, cross-Strait air routes, destinations and flights have not fully returned to normal. The mainland has 15 destinations in 14 cities, with more than 300 passenger flights operated per week, which is a far cry from the situation before 2020, when the mainland had 61 destinations and a weekly peak of 890 passenger flights. This seriously affects travel between compatriots on both sides. Residents on both sides of the Strait strongly call for the full resumption of direct cross-Strait flights to all destinations. According to our understanding, among the 15 destinations where direct flights have resumed, mainland airlines have essentially used up the capacity quotas for cross-Strait flights.\nThe crux of the obstacle to fully restoring cross-Strait direct air service to all destinations lies with the Democratic Progressive Party authorities. We hope the Taiwan side will heed public opinion, promptly lift unreasonable restrictions on cross-Strait air transport, and allow airlines on both sides to arrange flight schedules independently based on market demand.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814576.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the DPP authorities held the so-called “2026 Whole-of-Society Defense Resilience International Forum,” focusing on topics such as “integration of military and civilian resources, gray-zone threats, cybersecurity and protection of critical infrastructure,” with participants from the United States, Japan, the Philippines and other countries. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” collude with external forces to seek “independence” and provoke confrontation, and do not hesitate to tie the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, seriously endangering the security and well-being of the Taiwan people. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end, and no matter how many so-called “defense resilience” measures they pursue, it will be in vain. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a universal consensus of the international community. Relevant countries should abide by the one-China principle and not send wrong signals to the “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Taiwan's “Black Bear Academy” advocated that counties and cities in Taiwan should break away from traditional disaster prevention thinking, incorporate “war disasters” into local disaster preparedness, and agitated for county and city mayoral candidates to put forward so-called concrete “resilience platforms,” in order to build a more comprehensive whole-of-society defense system. What is your comment?","The remarks about “Black Bear Academy” are entirely heretical theories that incite Taiwan to become a battlefield, and they will certainly be opposed by the Taiwan public. On the one hand, they go to every extreme to hype up a war atmosphere and cultivate “seeds of violence” in the island's society, openly engaging in “Taiwan independence” separatist activities. They are a bona fide “Taiwan independence” base. On the other hand, under the guise of “lectures,” “training,” “outdoor drills,” and the like, they buy low and sell high to profit from the price difference, and collude with external forces to swindle money. They are veritable “Taiwan independence profiteers.” Their ugly conduct and despicable record deserve contempt, and “Taiwan independence” separatist acts will certainly be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814551.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Sichuan-Chongqing) Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From September 13 to 22, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Sichuan-Chongqing) Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. More than 200 people attended, including heads of Taiwan compatriot associations in multiple places, leaders of Taiwan youth entrepreneurship parks, and young Taiwanese businesspeople. The exchange conference included activities such as introductions to the business environment and entrepreneurship policies in the Sichuan-Chongqing region, sharing of entrepreneurship stories by Taiwan youth representatives, release of internship and employment positions for Taiwan youth, and pitch presentations of outstanding Taiwan youth entrepreneurship projects. It also presented certificates titled 'Guides for Taiwan Youth Internship, Employment, and Entrepreneurship in Sichuan' to more than 10 enthusiastic Taiwan compatriots who have long been dedicated to serving the growth of Taiwan youth and promoting cross-Strait youth exchanges, and presented awards to the winning teams of the 13th Rongtai Cross-Strait Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition.\nThe Cross-Strait (Sichuan-Chongqing) Youth Employment and Entrepreneurship Development Exchange Conference has been held five times. Many Taiwan youth friends have found a stage for their life struggles through the exchange conference, writing moving stories of sincere cooperation. We warmly welcome Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to pursue, build, and realize their dreams. We will continue to create better conditions and more opportunities, and we look forward to more Taiwan youth friends seizing the opportunity to come to the mainland for internships and employment, expanding their development space, and realizing their life ideals.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Taiwan media recently reported that the DPP authorities have designated many civilian facilities as so-called “wartime emergency response centers,” including even a “Children's Future Museum.” This has caused an uproar on the island, with many questioning whether children will be made to block bullets. What comments do you have on this?","The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” coerce the people of Taiwan for political self-interest into serving as “cannon fodder for Taiwan independence,” and have even gone so far as to attempt, in a fiendish manner, to use children as “shields for Taiwan independence.” This seriously threatens the safety and well-being of Taiwan compatriots and will inevitably be strongly condemned and opposed by the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814575.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","中新社记者","Recently, the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF) said that a delegation including the heads of the Shandong and Shanxi working areas of the Mainland Taiwan Enterprises Association and others proposed to the SEF applications for charter flights during next year’s Spring Festival, flight planning, and related matters for the Jinan route. What is the mainland side’s attitude?","Cross-strait direct air links are an important aerial bridge connecting the kinship of compatriots on both sides and facilitating economic, trade, and cultural exchanges, and they carry the urgent needs of people on both sides to travel. From January to August this year, passengers traveling between the two sides on scheduled direct air passenger flights totaled 4.221 million, up 12.9% year on year. This fully demonstrates the strong demand in the cross-strait direct flight market and the strong desire of people on both sides to travel. We are actively promoting the full restoration of normal cross-strait direct air links, and this position has been consistent and clear. From calls to restore routes and add flights to applications for charter flights, this reflects the eager expectation of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan compatriots for the full resumption of cross-strait direct routes. We hope the DPP authorities will stop political manipulation, respond to the voices of the public, and fully restore normal cross-strait direct air passenger services as soon as possible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","Taiwan media reported that a decommissioned Taiwanese coast guard ship donated to the Philippines was recently found to have been converted into a Philippine law enforcement vessel. Taiwan's Coast Guard Administration said, “This case is handled in accordance with precedent,” and that Taiwan has signed fisheries agreements with the Philippines and others and established consultation mechanisms, and will continue…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Both sides of the Strait should jointly safeguard national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and safeguard the overall and fundamental interests of the Chinese nation.\nThe DPP authorities turned a deaf ear to the infringing conduct of Japan and the Philippines in announcing the launch of maritime delimitation negotiations for the waters east of Taiwan Island. Not only do they fail to do their utmost to protect the interests of the people on the island, they instead aid and abet wrongdoing, increase the risk of harm to the rights and interests of Taiwan's fishermen, and abandon the national standpoint, which is contemptible.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814552.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs authority, said that Taiwan will establish an office in Cebu, the Philippines. Public opinion on the island questions whether the negotiation to set up an “office” is taking place during the so-called “maritime boundary delimitation negotiations” between Japan and the Philippines, and whether it comes at the cost of Taiwan's interests. What is your comment?","The relevant authorities have already expressed a solemn position on this. We firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have established diplomatic relations with China and the Taiwan region of China. The Philippines should abide by the one-China principle and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nThe DPP authorities’ stubborn “seeking independence by relying on external support” cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China, and cannot shake the international community’s common consensus and basic framework of adhering to the one-China principle. It will only end in failure.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","香港经济导报记者","On September 22, the 48th WorldSkills Competition opened in Shanghai. Please introduce the participation of the Taiwan region.","From September 22 to 27, the 48th WorldSkills Competition was held in Shanghai. The Chinese Taipei delegation sent 53 contestants to compete in 47 events, including industrial mechanics, mobile application development, and automotive technology. We look forward to outstanding performances by contestants from both sides of the Strait, and wish them good results in advance.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","上海“澎湃新闻”记者","Recently, Chu Jung-tai, head of Taiwan's executive department, claimed that \"Taiwan now faces cultural aggression from external sources such as Xiaohongshu and Douyin, and the government will use its power to protect the local cultural industry.\" What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “foreign cultural aggression” is pure nonsense. The source of Taiwan’s culture is Chinese culture. Taiwan culture is both an important component of Chinese culture and an enrichment of it. Taiwan compatriots, especially Taiwan youth, use mainland social media platforms to engage in cultural exchanges with mainland compatriots, learn from one another, deepen mutual understanding, and at the same time showcase their talents and enrich their cultural lives on mainland social media. This is a vivid manifestation of Chinese culture taking root among the Taiwan people, and a rich channel for civil exchanges across the Strait.\nThe DPP authorities, disregarding facts and acting against the tide, have politicized and stigmatized normal cross-strait cultural exchanges, engaged in large-scale political manipulation, and attempted to build a “cultural wall” between compatriots on both sides to sever the blood ties across the Strait. This is unpopular and doomed to be futile.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260923_12814582.htm"],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《中国时报》记者","Taiwan scholar Chang Ya-chung recently published an article after attending the Beijing Xiangshan Forum, arguing that the mainland now treats “one country, two systems” as a toast and “armed unification” as a punishment wine, and that these contents are more like a disposition plan for “after being unified.” He suggested that the mainland explore “harmony before unification,” first answer how the two sides can…","\"Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems\" is the basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and also the best way to achieve national reunification. It embodies the Chinese wisdom of embracing all rivers, where tolerance makes greatness. It fully takes into account the realities of Taiwan and is also conducive to the long-term stability and security of Taiwan after reunification. The specific form of realizing the \"two systems\" Taiwan plan in Taiwan will fully take into account the realities of Taiwan, fully absorb the opinions and suggestions of people on both sides of the Strait, and fully take care of the interests and feelings of Taiwan compatriots.\nOn the common political basis of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" we are willing to conduct extensive and in-depth democratic consultations with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals on cross-Strait relations and the future of the nation, and to work together to promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We also welcome Taiwan compatriots to offer suggestions and ideas for advancing the cause of national reunification. The earlier and the more Taiwan compatriots discuss matters related to reunification, the more opportunities they will bring to Taiwan's economic and social development, and the more real benefits they will bring to themselves.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: Reuters reports that during President Xi Jinping’s visit to the United States, he may raise the “August 17 Communiqué” signed by China and the US in 1982, and demand that US President Donald Trump halt arms sales to Taiwan on that basis. What comments do you have on this? Second question: Shen Yu-chung, Deputy Minister of the Mainland Affairs Council, recently said that after the meeting between…","Question one: Taiwan is Taiwan of China. The Taiwan question is China's internal affair, and no external force is allowed to interfere. We firmly oppose the US selling arms to China's Taiwan region. This position is consistent and clear.\nQuestion two: There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference is permitted. The historical and legal fact that both sides of the Strait belong to one China cannot be changed by any person or force. The motherland must be reunified, and it will certainly be reunified.\nQuestion three: The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the 'Taiwan independence' separatist position, collude with external forces to provoke 'independence,' and are the root cause of peril to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. No matter what fallacies the DPP authorities spread, they cannot change the fact that Taiwan is part of China.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The deputy director of the Shanghai Taiwan Affairs Office was blocked twice by the Mainland Affairs Council (MAC) during his trip to Taiwan for an advance site visit. The MAC stated that this is a response principle to the mainland's “22 measures for punishing 'Taiwan independence',” which prohibit directors and deputy directors of local Taiwan Affairs Offices on the mainland from coming to…","First question. The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum is an important urban exchange platform between the two sides of the Taiwan Strait. To hold this year's “Twin Cities Forum” well, so that compatriots on both sides can continue to benefit from it, the two cities have maintained communication on matters related to holding the forum. The Shanghai side's trip to Taipei for a site reconnaissance was in keeping with customary practice. The DPP authorities, obstinately holding to the “Taiwan independence” position and, for political self-interest, deliberately setting all kinds of obstacles to the forum, unreasonably making things difficult, and obstructing and undermining cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, do not win popular support.\nSecond question. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We support and actively promote all cross-strait exchanges and cooperation, including the “Twin Cities Forum.” The “Twin Cities Forum” has been held for 16 consecutive years and has formed certain conventions and practices. We are glad to see it and believe that this year it will certainly be held smoothly in accordance with convention.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《旺报》记者","In June this year, Mainland actor Zhang Linghe attended the Straits Forum and drew attention from young people on both sides of the Strait. Recently, the Mainland TV drama *Clear Early Spring* has been a hit in Taiwan, and its lead actors Jing Boran and Sun Qian have also drawn attention from Taiwan viewers. Will the two lead actors have opportunities to take part in cross-Strait youth exchange activities and…","The three actors you mentioned are themselves young people, so their participation in cross-Strait youth exchange activities is only natural. We hope that in the future there will be more opportunities for young performing artists from the mainland and young people from Taiwan to engage in exchanges and cooperation in various ways, join the process of cross-Strait integration and development together, and share in the development opportunities of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","First question: The APEC Human Resources Development Ministerial Meeting concluded in Nanjing on the 22nd, and Taiwan's representatives attended smoothly, with the process going well. Does the mainland side believe that this experience has added mutual trust across the Strait and laid a foundation for future interactions? During the meeting, did responsible persons from relevant parties on both sides of the…","First question. As the host of this year’s APEC activities, we handle matters concerning Chinese Taipei’s participation in accordance with the one-China principle and the relevant APEC memorandum of understanding and practices.\nSecond question. The DPP authorities have long claimed they have opened so-called “charter flight points,” but the application conditions are extremely harsh, leaving the public and industry “able to see them, unable to touch them, and unable to even eat them.” The DPP authorities should face the real demand for cross-strait direct air passenger services, heed the wishes of the people, and promptly lift the unreasonable restrictions on cross-strait air transportation, returning to cross-strait compatriots a smooth, convenient, and efficient air route.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-23","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: Taiwan’s “Minister of Labor” Hung Shen-han attended the APEC meeting in Nanjing, with a desk placard reading “Chinese Taipei.” By comparison, when Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an’s wife once described herself as from “Chinese Taipei,” some people on the island criticized it as “self-demeaning,” but there has been no such voice in Hung Shen-han’s case. How do you view this double standard within Taiwan?…","On the first question: under the one-China principle, Taiwan participates in APEC and related activities under the name “Chinese Taipei” and the identity of a regional economy. All parties must abide by the relevant memorandums of understanding and practices of APEC.\nOn the second question: Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland need not have groundless worries or concerns. As long as they comply with the law and regulations, they can certainly come happily and return safely.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260923_12814547.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: according to reports, the New Zealand frigate “Te Mana” and the replenishment ship “Aotearoa” recently transited the Taiwan Strait. What comments do you have? Second question: according to reports, the Japanese government plans to establish a new legal entity closely related to defense in fiscal year 2027. This entity will coordinate the export of defense equipment, cultivate…","On the first question, the Chinese military, in accordance with law and regulations, organized sea and air forces to conduct full-process monitoring and vigilance over the New Zealand warship transiting the Taiwan Strait, and effectively responded and handled the situation. We urge the New Zealand side to abide by the one-China principle and not send wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.\nOn the second question, a series of documents with international legal force, including the Cairo Declaration, the Potsdam Proclamation and the Instrument of Japanese Surrender, clearly stipulate that Japan must be completely disarmed and must not maintain industries that could enable it to rearm. This is an important component of the post-war international order and an important barrier for the international community to prevent the resurgence of Japanese militarism. In recent years, Japan's military budget has continued to surge, it has vigorously developed offensive capabilities, and it has even engaged in large-scale expansion of its military industry under the guise of developing the economy. How similar this is to the signs before Japan launched its foreign aggression in the past. The international community should remain highly vigilant about this and firmly curb Japan's “new-type militarism” from wreaking havoc on the world.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, recently, the China Coast Guard's Sanzhou'ao vessel carried out a rights-protection law enforcement operation in waters near China's Xianbin Reef in the Nansha Islands in accordance with the law. Philippine vessel No. 3015 ignored China's repeated solemn warnings, deliberately changed course, suddenly accelerated, and cut diagonally across the bow of our Coast Guard vessel, causing a…","On the first question, the China Coast Guard has already introduced the relevant situation. The facts are clear and the evidence conclusive, leaving no room for Philippine sophistry and hype. Philippine government vessels provoked trouble in the sea area near Sabina Shoal (Xianbin Jiao) in China's Nansha Islands, adopting dangerous maneuvers similar to 'changing lanes to cut off other vehicles,' and deliberately rammed Chinese coast guard ships. This seriously threatened the safety of Chinese personnel and vessels and seriously violated international law and the basic norms of international relations. The Philippine side has repeatedly played the victim and spread false narratives, but this cannot change the essence of its infringement and provocation. China will continue to take effective measures to firmly defend its territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests, and to firmly uphold peace and stability in the South China Sea.\nOn the second question, for the sake of its 'Taiwan independence' separatist scheme, the DPP authorities, disregarding the tragedy of Philippine coast guard shooting Taiwanese fishermen, have actively cozied up and colluded with the Philippines. They attempt to use naval vessel assistance as a tool to expand so-called 'official contacts,' selling out national dignity and interests, which has earned the scorn of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. We urge the Philippine side to abide by the one-China principle, not to conduct any form of official exchanges or military ties with the Taiwan region of China, and to stop sending wrong signals to 'Taiwan independence' separatist forces.\"","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: President Xi Jinping is currently on a state visit to the United States. Under the strategic guidance of the leaders of both countries, the two sides are working to build a constructive China-US strategic stability relationship. Recently, the two militaries have also had some interactions. After the theater commander meeting last month, the US side raised the level of its…","Regarding the first question, head-of-state diplomacy has an irreplaceable strategic guiding role for China-U.S. military-to-military relations. We are willing to work with the U.S. side to implement the important consensus reached by the two heads of state on military affairs, strengthen communication and dialogue, carry out pragmatic cooperation, appropriately manage differences, maintain the stable, healthy, and sustainable development of military-to-military relations, and play a positive role in building a constructive China-U.S. strategic stability relationship.\nRegarding the second question, for information about President Xi's visit to the United States, please follow official news reports. It must be emphasized that the Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-U.S. relations, and safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator for both sides. We hope the U.S. side will handle the Taiwan question with extreme caution.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question: This year marks the 95th anniversary of the September 18 Incident. Around the anniversary, some Japanese politicians continue to hype the Taiwan Strait as Japan's so-called “survival-threatening situation.” Meanwhile, the United States, Japan and Australia are holding the “Orient Shield 26” military exercise at multiple locations in Japan, and Japan continues to advance…","On the first question: In that year, Japanese militarists deliberately staged the September 18 Incident, launched the war of aggression against China, and committed countless crimes against Asian neighbors, including China, and against the people of the world. To this day, Japan not only has failed to reflect on its responsibility for its history of aggression, but instead is repeating its old tricks, accelerating “re-militarization” under the pretext of a so-called “survival-threatening situation,” threatening regional peace and stability. The international community should remain highly vigilant and firmly curb Japan's reckless moves of “new-style militarism.”\nOn the second question: A country without defense cannot stand, and a people without defense cannot be secure. The “National Defense Education Month” activities are carried out every September and have become an important vehicle for strengthening national defense education for the whole people and raising the national defense literacy of the whole people. This year, the military and local authorities have centered on the theme “Carry Forward the Great Spirit of the Long March, Jointly Building a Strong National Defense with One Heart,” and have organized a rich variety of educational activities in a concentrated manner. The military has deepened the military camp open-day activities, scientifically organized military training for students, and widely carried out mass educational activities, actively exploring, gathering, and using resources to support participation in national defense education for the whole people. At the army camp open-day activity and “Accompanying the Army, Youth in Position” live-streamed national defense education scene class held at the “former unit of Yang Gensi,” the topic reached 520 million views. Multi-platform media programs such as “National Defense Open Class,” “Building National Defense Together,” and “Sunshine Military Recruitment, We Walk Together” reached more than 100 million people in total across media. A total of 464 teams from 201 military and local colleges and universities across the country registered to participate in the second National Youth Intelligent Unmanned Systems Application Competition, and more than 400,000 young people registered for the National Youth National Defense Literacy Competition, creating an innovative and leading national defense education brand, effectively cultivating young people's ideology of valuing culture and martial prowess and their sense of responsibility for strengthening the country and the military. Various localities have also widely carried out activities such as “Our August 1st, Our First Lesson in National Defense” and “Military Training, Youth in Its Prime,” gathering the strength of will of society as a whole to care about, love, build, and defend national defense.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","A US think tank recently released a report recommending that the US government not get involved in the Taiwan Strait conflict, calling for the immediate withdrawal of US military training personnel stationed in Taiwan, and also for an end to informal verbal commitments. What is China's comment?","The Taiwan question is purely China’s internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. More and more people recognize that supporting “Taiwan independence” is of no benefit and only harms the US. Complying with the historical trend of China’s reunification and resolutely opposing the DPP authorities’ provocations to seek “independence” is the wise choice.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Recently, calls for discussing the “one country, two systems” Taiwan plan and the question of reunification have been growing on the island, and the voices of island residents hoping for peaceful reunification are also rising. What is your comment?","This demonstrates that the reunification of the motherland is the trend of the times and the desire of the people. “Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems” is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to realize the reunification of the motherland. Reunification will eradicate the root and source of “Taiwan independence” troubles, eliminate the hidden danger of war in the Taiwan Strait, build a solid security barrier for Taiwan compatriots, and provide strong support for the prosperity and development of Taiwan's society. All Chinese people will further join hands and work together to create a peaceful era of national reunion and family harmony, and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","According to reports, two F-16V fighter jets that the Taiwan military purchased and were originally scheduled for delivery turned back mid-flight recently and are still stranded in Hawaii, with no delivery date specified. This batch of arms sales, totaling 66 aircraft, has been repeatedly delayed since the contract was signed. The U.S. has repeatedly engaged in “taking the money without delivering the goods” in…","To serve the private interests of one party, the DPP authorities are squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people on “Kaizi” arms purchases. This cannot buy security; it will only further hollow out Taiwan and harm its people.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-09-24","Jiang Bin","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have three questions. First, fighting has recently escalated near the Bab el-Mandeb Strait. Is the PLA base in Djibouti affected? Some research institutions, based on satellite image analysis, have found that the base has added antennas, satellite communication equipment and other facilities, which has enhanced its monitoring capability over military activities in the Middle East and Africa. Can the…","Regarding the first question, the Chinese base in Djibouti is operating normally. I am not aware of the specific situation you mentioned.\nRegarding the second question, according to the “Law of the People's Republic of China on Reserve Servicemen,” reserve personnel are members of the national armed forces and shall participate in military training as prescribed and meet the training requirements stipulated in the military training syllabus. This is both a legal obligation and a necessary measure to strengthen the building of the reserve personnel force.\nRegarding the third question, the National Defense Mobilization Law is a foundational law in the field of national defense mobilization. Its main function is to regulate national defense mobilization work, clarify the rights and obligations of citizens and organizations in national defense mobilization, and provide legal safeguards for building and consolidating national defense. This is not fundamentally different from national defense mobilization laws and regulations promulgated by most countries in the world. China's current National Defense Mobilization Law was formally implemented in July 2010. After more than a decade of practice, some provisions of the law no longer suit the new situation, tasks, and requirements of national defense mobilization. This revision of the law is necessary to implement the decisions and arrangements of the Party Central Committee, improve the national defense legal and regulatory system, and carry out national defense mobilization work in accordance with the law. The relevant provisions clearly stipulate that national defense mobilization adheres to the strategic guidelines of military strategy in the new era, namely the principles of defense, self-defense, and striking only after the enemy has struck, implementing “active defense.” Relevant parties need not over-interpret this.","","http://www.81.cn/fyr/jdt_208546/16489558.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-09-29","Guo Jiakun","CCTV","Today marks the 54th anniversary of the issuance of the China-Japan Joint Statement. As China-Japan relations face grave difficulties, how does China see the historical significance of the four political documents between the two countries, including the joint statement, and how are they still relevant today?","Today 54 years ago, the older generation of Chinese and Japanese leaders, with extraordinary political vision and courage, signed and issued the China-Japan Joint Statement, which marked the normalization of relations between the two countries. In the joint statement, Japan explicitly noted that it is “keenly conscious of” and “deeply reproaches itself” over its responsibility for war and that it “recognizes the Government of the People’s Republic of China as the sole legal Government of China.” The statement also notes that the Government of Japan “fully understands and respects” the position of the Chinese government that Taiwan is an inalienable part of the territory of the People’s Republic of China. The four political documents between China and Japan, including the joint statement, laid the political and legal foundation for China-Japan relations, and established the rules for properly settling major issues of principle, including history and Taiwan. There should be no distortion or regression, still less sabotage, regarding these principles.\nToday, more than half a century later, China-Japan relations once again face a severe situation. The root cause is that the political foundation of the bilateral relations has been gravely undermined. The incumbent leader of Japan not only refuses to reflect on the history of aggression, but also claims that a contingency in Taiwan will constitute a “survival threatening” situation for Japan. This is a blatant challenge to China’s state sovereignty and against the aspiration demonstrated by the normalization of China-Japan relations and the political commitments Japan made to China. Japan keeps peddling the so-called “external threat” narrative, using it as a pretext to speed up remilitarization. The move poses a challenge to the postwar international order and threatens regional peace and stability.\nHistory has repeatedly shown that only by staying true to the spirit of the four political documents can China and Japan keep the relationship on the right course. Just as Foreign Minister Wang Yi noted in the meeting yesterday with Takeshi Iwaya, head of the Japanese Association for the Promotion of International Trade, the pressing priority for Japan is to correct Japanese leader’s erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question. Japan should adopt a correct attitude on historical issues, and form an objective and rational perception on China. On this day of historic significance, we once again urge those running the government of Japan to seriously reflect on and correct their wrongdoings, and take real actions to return to the purpose and mission of the four political documents.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202609/t20260929_12033413.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202609/t20260929_12033332.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on September 30, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot cross-Strait issues.","Dear reporters, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","新华社记者","On September 24, President Xi Jinping, in talks with U.S. President Trump, stated China’s principled position on the Taiwan question, which has drawn great attention from public opinion on both sides of the Strait. Please interpret this.","The Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-U.S. relations. President Xi Jinping has stressed that China's position on safeguarding national unification and territorial integrity is very clear. We hope the U.S. side will uphold its correct position of opposing “Taiwan independence,” handle the Taiwan question with prudence, and lay a solid foundation for China-U.S. strategic cooperation and the development of bilateral relations.\nThe Taiwan question is China's internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for Chinese on both sides of the Strait to decide themselves. Realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is the shared aspiration of all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots; it is the historical trend, the righteous cause, and the will of the people. More and more Taiwan compatriots have come to recognize that “Taiwan independence” is a dead end and that outsiders cannot be relied upon. We have the determination and capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We hope the broad mass of Taiwan compatriots will join us in firmly opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, and actively take part in the righteous cause of promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the reunification of the motherland.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait are as incompatible as fire and water. Maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is the greatest common denominator for China and the U.S., and it is also an inherent requirement of a constructive China-U.S. strategic stability relationship. We hope the U.S. side will abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, uphold its correct position of opposing “Taiwan independence,” handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, avoid sending wrong signals to separatist forces for “Taiwan independence,” and uphold the constructive China-U.S. strategic stability relationship through concrete actions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815879.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the 2026 Cross-Strait Compatriots Mid-Autumn Festival Reunion event was held in Beijing, where compatriots from both sides of the Strait admired the bright moon together, talked about their home ties together, and shared visions of the future together. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On September 23, more than 400 compatriots from both sides of the Strait gathered at Huairou Yanqi Lake in Beijing to jointly attend the “Moon Full over Beijing, Feelings Linking Both Sides of the Strait” — 2026 Cross-Strait Compatriots' Mid-Autumn Festival Friendship Event. The event was co-hosted by the Beijing Cross-Strait Civil Exchange Promotion Association and the People's Government of Huairou District. Activities included a Mid-Autumn tea gathering for compatriots from both sides of the Strait, and the “Let's Blossom Together” Cross-Strait Song Festival. Compatriots from both sides of the Strait together admired the bright moon, shared hometown sentiments, and talked about the future, expressing their joy in welcoming the traditional Chinese festival and their fond hopes for cross-Strait reunion.\nSong Tao, Director of the Taiwan Work Office of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, attended the Mid-Autumn tea gathering. He said that this April, General Secretary Xi Jinping met with Cheng Li-wun, Chairperson of the Kuomintang of China, and delivered an important speech, pointing the way for the development of cross-Strait relations. We will thoroughly implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” broadly unite Taiwan compatriots, deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation, and integrated development, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and foreign interference, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nLi Qianlong, Vice Chairman and Secretary-General of the Kuomintang of China, along with more than 300 Taiwan guests, including guest representatives from the island, Taiwanese entrepreneurs, and Taiwan compatriots in Beijing, attended the event. Taiwan guests attending said that for Chinese people on both sides of the Strait, the Mid-Autumn Festival is not just a holiday but a bond of feeling; the Mid-Autumn moon is a cultural imprint shared by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nAttendees also jointly watched the “Let's Blossom Together” Cross-Strait Song Festival produced by China Media Group. Performance guests and youth representatives from both sides of the Strait, through co-creating, co-singing, co-performing, and co-integrating, presented a warm and sincere music festival that showcased a vivid picture of compatriots on both sides of the Strait walking side by side and hand in hand toward the future. The song festival was broadcast on September 29 on the CMG CCTV Variety Channel and CMG new media platforms, and everyone is welcome to watch it through CMG's “Watch Taiwan Strait” new media matrix.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815878.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Recently, New Party Vice Chairman Li Shengfeng gave a media interview setting out the New Party’s views on the “two systems” Taiwan plan. The 9th “National Reunification and National Rejuvenation” think tank dialogue, held in Hubei, has also drawn public attention. What is your comment?","National reunification is an irresistible historical trend. \"Peaceful reunification and one country, two systems\" is our basic policy for resolving the Taiwan question and the best way to achieve national reunification, and it is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation. An increasing number of Taiwan residents, including those in the New Party, have begun discussing the specific content of the \"two systems\" Taiwan plan, envisioning a bright future after reunification, considering the enormous opportunities that reunification will bring to Taiwan's economic and social development, and the tangible benefits it will bring to broad Taiwan compatriots.\nOn September 28, the 9th \"National Reunification and National Rejuvenation\" Think Tank Dialogue was held in Enshi, Hubei Province, with more than 100 experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong, and Macao in attendance. Centering on the theme \"Pursue peace across the Strait, pursue well-being for compatriots, pursue rejuvenation for the nation,\" the experts and scholars actively explored effective paths to advance the process of national reunification, envisioned the bright prospects of national rejuvenation, and injected new wisdom and strength into the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations.\nWe welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait to pool ideas and offer more opinions and suggestions on the \"two systems\" Taiwan plan, jointly create the historic cause of national reunification, and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815876.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Lai Qingde declared that next year he will allocate a defense budget of over NT$1.3 trillion for military procurement, international cooperation and defense self-reliance, especially for strengthening industries such as drones and robotics. What is your comment?","The Lai Ching-te authorities stubbornly adhere to the “Taiwan independence” separatist stance and attempt to “seek independence through force” and “rely on external forces to seek independence.” They are squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan’s people even more recklessly. Huge defense spending not only squeezes out expenditures on people’s livelihood and social welfare on the island, harming the immediate interests of Taiwan residents, but also pushes Taiwan step by step into an even more dangerous situation, coercing Taiwan residents to become cannon fodder for “Taiwan independence.” This vicious conduct of harming and destroying Taiwan and seeking self-destruction will surely be strongly opposed. No matter how large a budget Lai Ching-te allocates or how many weapons he shuffles around, none of it can change the inevitable fate of “Taiwan independence” as a path to defeat.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815874.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, the mainland TV series “Lan Xiang Ru Gu” premiered in Taiwan and immediately became a hit. Some Taiwan media called it a “2026 dark-horse divine drama,” and netizens on the island even sparked discussions focusing on life in the Ming Dynasty depicted in the series. What is your comment?","Watching a TV drama together, singing a song together, savoring a meal together, and visiting a city together are increasingly becoming popular ways of life among people on both sides of the Strait, especially young people. Compatriots on both sides share the same roots and origins, the same writing and the same ethnicity, and it is easy for them to form cultural consensus and emotional resonance through various exchanges. This is a powerful endogenous driving force for promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. We hope more Taiwan compatriots will take part in cross-Strait exchanges and jointly promote integrated development across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities.","Cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields continue to be vibrant and diverse.\nFrom September 18 to 23, the cultural exchange activities \"Tianjin Rhythm of Mazu: Praying for Centuries of Blessings\" and the 2026 series of cross-Strait \"Mazu Bond\" cultural exchange activities were held in Tianjin. Forty-eight Taiwan temples and more than 700 Mazu devotees took part together in activities including the blessing ceremony marking the 700th anniversary of the imperially sanctioned Tianjin Tianhou Palace.\nFrom September 20 to 25, Sichuan held the cross-Strait grassroots community education exchange activity \"Working Together for Education, Good Governance Hand in Hand,\" in which Taiwan youth teachers and students entered communities and campuses to appreciate the institutional advantages and governance effectiveness of grassroots social governance on the mainland in the new era.\nFrom September 21 to 27, Guizhou held the 2nd Taiwan Youth Student Guizhou Yangming Studies Inheritance Camp. Youth from both sides of the Strait explored the roots of the cultural lineage of the Chinese nation and further strengthened cultural identity.\nFrom September 24 to 28, the 2026 3rd Taiwan Youth Shenzhen Longgang Science and Technology Innovation Camp was held, in which 70 Taiwan youths experienced at close range the vitality of cutting-edge technology and the cultural charm of Shenzhen.\nFrom September 24 to 30, Zhuzhou, Hunan held the cross-Strait youth ceramic culture and art exchange activity \"Same Culture Origin, Youth Walking Together,\" which expanded space for cooperation and deepened friendship between compatriots through mutual learning.\nFrom September 25 to 28, the 3rd Cross-Strait (Shenzhen) Street Dance League was held, attracting thousands of dancers from both sides of the Strait, Hong Kong and Macao to compete on the same stage, including nearly 200 youth dancers from the island.\nFrom September 28 to 30, the first \"Cross-Strait Innovation and Development Week\" was held in Shanghai under the theme \"New Vision, Winning the Future.\" Adopting a \"1+5+N\" model, it included 1 main seminar and 5 parallel exchange seminars, and more than 1,000 people attended, including important industry and commerce groups from both sides of the Strait, enterprise leaders and youth representatives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","成都商报“红星新闻”记者","Recently, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, wrote in a Japanese media outlet that the rules-based international order is facing challenges from authoritarian states. “China is deliberately distorting UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 in an attempt to obstruct Taiwan's participation in international organizations. If the international community does not stop this, such rhetoric could be…","Those remarks are purely distortions of facts and a reversal of right and wrong. The Charter of the United Nations laid the cornerstone of the post-war international order, established an international system centered on the United Nations, and adherence to the UN Charter has become the greatest common denominator of the post-war international community.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. In 1971, the 26th session of the United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority, deciding to restore all the rights of the People's Republic of China in the United Nations and recognizing the representatives of the government of the People's Republic of China as the only legitimate representatives of China in the United Nations. The opening statement of General Assembly Resolution 2758 clearly states: “The restoration of the lawful rights of the People's Republic of China is essential both to the maintenance of the United Nations Charter and to the work that the United Nations has to do in consequence of the Charter,” solemnly clarifying the clear position of upholding the authority of the United Nations. This resolution thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all China in the United Nations, including Taiwan.\nThe historical record is clear, and the legal facts are plain. The DPP authorities have repeatedly distorted and attacked UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, attempting to challenge the authority of the United Nations and the post-war international order, but this is absolutely impossible to achieve.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815873.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","四川日报“封面新闻”记者","Recently, US Secretary of State Rubio said that selling weapons to Taiwan “means we no longer have them,” and that US arms sales to Taiwan must take into account many factors, including the defense needs of the United States itself. What comments do you have on this?","We firmly oppose any form of military contact between diplomatic allies and the Taiwan region of China. The DPP authorities, attempting to “rely on foreign powers to seek independence” and “use military force to seek independence,” will only harm and destroy Taiwan and bring about their own downfall.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Recently, the People's Daily published an article pointing out that the one-China principle is the political foundation of China-US relations, that “Taiwan independence” is a common enemy of China and the United States, and that managing “Taiwan independence” is a key link in building a constructive strategic stability relationship between China and the United States. This has sparked heated discussion in public…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. Adhering to the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a general consensus of the international community, and it is the foundation of the foundations of the political basis of China-US relations. The Taiwan question is the core of China's core interests and the most important issue in China-US relations. If handled well, the relationship between the two countries can maintain overall stability; if handled poorly, the two countries will collide or even clash, pushing the entire China-US relationship into a very dangerous situation.\nThe Lai Ching-te authorities, stubbornly holding to the \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist position, refusing to acknowledge the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, and continually engaging in provocations to seek independence, are the chief culprits undermining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. Firmly opposing \"Taiwan independence\" secession and maintaining peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait is in the common interest of both China and the United States. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the extreme harm and danger of the Lai Ching-te authorities' obstinate pursuit of independence, firmly oppose \"Taiwan independence\" secessionist acts, and join us in firmly safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait and advancing the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815877.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng, Chairperson of Taiwan’s Mainland Affairs Council, said in an exclusive media interview that after the mainland released the “22 measures for punishing ‘independence’,” the Taiwan side in principle prohibits directors and deputy directors of local mainland Taiwan Affairs Offices from visiting Taiwan. The exception is that they may be allowed after review if recommended by a local Taiwan…","The specific measures by judicial authorities to punish, in accordance with the law, the crimes of splitting the country and inciting the splitting of the country are a righteous action in response to the wishes of people on both sides of the Strait to safeguard unity and oppose “Taiwan independence.”\nThe DPP authorities, out of their “independence”-seeking nature and political self-interest, are obstructing and banning cross-Strait exchanges. This completely goes against the mainstream public opinion and the common voice of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, who call for peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation. It will inevitably be opposed by Taiwan compatriots, and it cannot stop the trend of compatriots on both sides of the Strait drawing closer to each other.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","From September 22 to 27, the 48th WorldSkills Competition was successfully held in Shanghai. Please introduce the awards won by contestants from the Taiwan region.","From September 22 to 27, the 48th WorldSkills Competition was held in Shanghai. More than 1,300 contestants from 68 countries and regions took part. The Chinese Taipei delegation sent 53 contestants to compete, winning 3 gold medals, 3 silver medals, 7 bronze medals, and 30 Medallions for Excellence. We extend our congratulations.\nIn this major event in the skills field, compatriots on both sides of the Strait exchanged skills, deepened friendship, and interpreted the competition theme, “Skills Change the World, Skills Light the Future,” with the spirit of craftsmanship. We look forward to compatriots on both sides of the Strait working together and learning from each other in the field of vocational skills, continuously strengthening friendship among compatriots and jointly realizing their life aspirations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait film, television and music exchange activities.","Highlights of cross-strait cultural exchanges continue.\nOn September 23, the grand final and awards ceremony of the 2026 Cross-Strait Minnan Dialect “Village Song” Competition was held in Xiamen, Fujian. The event set up a Taiwan division for the first time, attracting 170 Taiwan compatriots from the island who entered original songs in Minnan dialect.\nOn the evening of September 24, the “Moon of a Thousand Autumns” Mid-Autumn Symphony Concert was held in Beijing. Co-hosted by the Central Committee of the Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League and the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, the concert used elegant traditional music to recount shared roots and kinship and to pray for national reunion on the Mid-Autumn night of family reunion. It was broadcast live online and attracted nearly 300,000 viewers.\nOn September 25, the “Crossing the Sea” episode of the cross-strait micro-drama series “Wait for Me, Come Home” went online. Created jointly by teams from both sides of the Strait and based on real people and events in Taiwan, the series was released at the Mid-Autumn reunion. It tells the moving story of protagonist Wen Xiuming, who voluntarily escorted the ashes of three veterans back to the mainland.\nFrom September 26 to 27, the Kunshan Contemporary Kunqu Opera Theatre of Jiangsu went to Taiwan for the “Kunqu Fragrance Spreads, Kun and Taiwan Share Kindred Spirit” Kunqu cultural exchange activity. Together with the Taipei New Theatre, it staged two special Peking-Kunqu performances, attracting about 600 Taiwan audience members on site.\nOn September 29, the “Qin Shen Tells of Love for the Motherland” 2026 Fujian-Taiwan Art Youth Concert was held in Zhangzhou, Fujian. About 40 young artists from both sides of the Strait performed together, mainly with Minnan songs, blending traditional music and dance with contemporary youthful interpretation to sound the shared dialect of both sides.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","The US think tank Chicago Council on Global Affairs recently released a poll showing that 57% of Americans support friendly cooperation with China. The proportion of Americans who support US forces protecting Taiwan in the event of cross-Strait conflict (38%) has fallen by 14% compared with five years ago. Some commentary on the island believes that Taiwan should “understand the wind direction” and try to “stay…","Maintaining a constructive strategic stability relationship between China and the US is in the common interest of both sides. The DPP authorities’ attempt to “rely on the US to seek independence” is an illusion. We believe that more and more Taiwan residents have fully recognized that the actions of the DPP authorities will only lead Taiwan step by step into an abyss of disaster.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","As the National Day holiday approaches, please introduce the convenience measures the Mainland has for Taiwan compatriots, especially “first-time visitors” (首来族), for tourism and exchanges on the Mainland.","We continue to create better conditions for Taiwan compatriots traveling to the mainland. At present, “first-time visitors” from Taiwan are exempt from the certificate fee when applying for a Taiwan Compatriot Permit. The number of ports that can issue a one-time-valid Taiwan Compatriot Permit has increased to 100. Most of the mainland's Class A and higher scenic spots waive admission fees for Taiwan “first-time visitors.” Taiwan compatriots are enjoying more and more convenient services. With the National Day “Golden Week” holiday approaching, we welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come for a free and enjoyable trip to the mainland, to appreciate its scenery, experience its culture, witness its development, and experience the warmth and friendliness of compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202609/t20260930_12815875.htm"],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, Wang Tao, deputy captain of the Navy’s Fujian ship, received paintings created by three Taiwanese children expressing respect for the officers and sailors of the Fujian ship. After receiving the paintings, Wang Tao said, “After the reunification of the motherland, we welcome these three children and more Taiwanese children to visit the Fujian ship, and we will give them explanations at that time.” This…","At present, there are more and more such heartwarming interactions across the Strait, expressing the common wish of compatriots on both sides for family reunion. This year marks the 77th anniversary of the founding of the People’s Navy. During the ship open-day activities marking the anniversary, many Taiwan compatriots boarded active-duty warships open to the public and visited the Navy Museum. We will continue to create conditions so that more Taiwan compatriots can understand the construction and development of the People’s Navy and share the pride and glory of being Chinese.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","南方日报、南方+记者","According to U.S. media reports, U.S. government officials have asked Taiwan officials to reduce their visits to Washington, as the U.S. does not want Taiwan to become a “stumbling block” to advancing U.S.-China relations. What is your comment?","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” separatist position, attempting to challenge the one-China principle in the international community, and they will only run into walls everywhere.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: After the meeting between the leaders of China and the United States, outside attention continues to focus on the impact of US-China interaction on the situation in the Taiwan Strait. Zheng Liwen, Chairwoman of the Kuomintang, said that the DPP authorities should proactively propose specific plans to reduce risks in the Taiwan Strait and restore cross-Strait communication. Under the current state…","First question. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" attempting to \"use force to seek independence\" and \"rely on foreign forces to seek independence,\" and are the principal culprits leading to tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait situation. Only by returning to the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" can the dialogue and communication mechanism across the Taiwan Strait be restarted. We are willing, on the common political foundation of upholding the \"1992 Consensus\" and opposing \"Taiwan independence,\" to strengthen exchanges and communication with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and people from all sectors, to jointly consult and resolve issues of concern to compatriots on both sides of the Strait, to seek peace for the Taiwan Strait, well-being for compatriots, and rejuvenation for the nation.\nSecond question. President Xi Jinping and President Trump engaged in candid and in-depth exchanges of views, in a friendly atmosphere of mutual respect, on strategic and overall issues concerning China-US relations and the trends of the world. President Xi Jinping clarified China's principled position on the Taiwan question, stressed that China firmly safeguards national unification and territorial integrity, urged the US side to adhere to the correct position of opposing \"Taiwan independence\" and to handle the Taiwan question with prudence, and to remove interference for China-US strategic cooperation and the development of bilateral relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Recently, the leaders of China and the United States reviewed the history of the two countries fighting side by side during World War II. Taiwan's Mainland Affairs Council and foreign affairs departments have said this distorts the facts and “de-ROCs” history. What is your comment on this? Second question: Although some public opinion in Taiwan holds that the DPP authorities are downplaying the…","First question. This year marks the 81st anniversary of the victory of the Chinese People’s War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression and the World Anti-Fascist War, and also the 81st anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration. The victory of the War of Resistance is a great triumph forged by all Chinese sons and daughters, who fearlessly confronted brutal aggression, refused to yield despite repeated setbacks, and fought bloody battles. It is also a shared historical memory of compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. In their meeting, the heads of state of China and the United States mentioned on several occasions that China and the United States were allies in World War II, and that the two peoples joined hands to win the war. In their struggle against Japanese fascism, the Chinese and American peoples stood shoulder to shoulder in common hatred of the enemy, withstood the test of blood and fire, and forged a deep friendship.\nThe DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” attempt to switch concepts, confuse national sovereignty, distort the history of World War II, and deliberately create confrontation across the Taiwan Strait. No matter what fallacies the DPP authorities spread, they cannot shake the international community’s one-China framework or block the historical trend of the inevitable reunification of the motherland.\nSecond question. There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory. On October 1, 1949, the Central People’s Government of the People’s Republic of China was proclaimed, replacing the Government of the Republic of China as the sole legal government representing all of China. This was a change of regime in which China, as a subject of international law, underwent no change. China’s sovereignty and its inherent territory and borders did not change, and the government of the People’s Republic of China naturally fully enjoys and exercises China’s sovereignty, including sovereignty over Taiwan. This is also the consensus of the international community.\nThe DPP authorities deliberately distort the history of the War of Resistance and repeatedly peddle the “Taiwan independence” view of history in an attempt to split the country. This is a betrayal of history, a desecration of the martyrs, and a betrayal of the nation. We believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots will see through the DPP authorities’ false historical narrative and their sinister intent of “de-Sinicization,” will uphold the great righteousness of the nation and the correct view of history, and will join mainland compatriots in carrying forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance, working together for the great cause of national reunification for generations to come, and creating a bright future of national rejuvenation.\nThird question. The victory of the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan are a great victory of the entire nation and a shared glory of the Chinese people and the Chinese nation. During the War of Resistance, the Communist Party of China raised high the banner of the anti-Japanese national united front, adhered to the line of all-out resistance, formulated correct strategies and tactics, opened vast guerrilla battlefields behind enemy lines, and became the mainstay in persisting with the war of resistance. The guerrilla battlefields led by the Communist Party of China and the frontal battlefields led by the Kuomintang coordinated with each other to attack the enemy from both sides, forming a strategic posture of jointly resisting Japanese aggression. The Communist Party of China clearly put forward the proposal to recover Taiwan, and guided and helped Taiwan compatriots organize anti-Japanese armed forces such as the Taiwan Volunteer Corps, supporting and promoting the Taiwan restoration movement.\nThe victory of the War of Resistance is a victory of the entire nation and an important component of the victory of the World Anti-Fascist War, and is worth remembering and commemorating together by compatriots on both sides of the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities’ deliberate distortion of history and their schemes to incite opposition and confrontation across the Strait are unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","During the War of Resistance, both the Kuomintang and the Communist Party made sacrifices. In the future, when the mainland holds commemorative activities for World War II or the War of Resistance, will it faithfully and fully present the historical facts of the frontal battlefield, so as to win greater recognition among Taiwan's young people of this period of anti-Japanese history?","Victory in the War of Resistance is a victory for the entire nation and an important component of the global victory in the anti-fascist war. For national liberation and the restoration of Taiwan, and to defeat Japanese fascism, all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, made enormous sacrifices and important contributions. We hold relevant commemorative activities and invite representatives from all sectors of Taiwan to attend. This helps both sides of the Strait remember history, mourn the martyrs, carry forward the great spirit of the War of Resistance, and jointly work toward the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","The Mainland Affairs Council of Taiwan said that recently four new cases have emerged of Taiwan public employees being interrogated during visits to the mainland. Does the Taiwan Affairs Office have knowledge of the relevant situation? Will Taiwan public employees traveling to the mainland be subject to questioning based on their occupation or the agency they work for?","We uphold, in accordance with the law, the life and property safety and the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, including Taiwan compatriots. As long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, Taiwan compatriots have no need for any concern when coming to the mainland. In the first half of this year, Taiwan compatriots made 2.85 million trips to the mainland, covering people from all walks of life, including quite a few public officials.\nThe DPP authorities previously required public officials to submit private information such as lists of relatives and friends before visiting relatives on the mainland or attending funerals there. Now they have repeatedly and maliciously hyped the so-called topic of “being interrogated when going to the mainland.” The aim is to intimidate people on the island and disrupt cross-Strait exchanges and interactions. This is unpopular and will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-09-30","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","First question: The Ministry of State Security recently announced a case in which a mainland exchange student was infiltrated by a female Taiwanese intelligence officer and handed over relevant materials. Cross-Strait relations are already making youth exchanges very difficult, so why does the mainland side choose to announce this individual case of a mainland student being turned in Taiwan now? What are the…","First question. Providing a normal learning and living environment for mainland students studying in Taiwan is the responsibility the Taiwan side should bear. The subversion and recruitment activities of Taiwan’s espionage and intelligence agencies seriously endanger the safety and healthy growth of young students and seriously interfere with cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation in education.\nThe relevant authorities’ lawful crackdown on criminal acts that endanger national security is to safeguard national security, maintain the normal order of cross-Strait exchanges and interactions, and protect the lawful rights and interests of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nSecond question. Our policies toward Taiwan are consistent and clear. We will firmly adhere to the One-China Principle and the “1992 Consensus,” firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and interference by external forces, continue to promote cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, and enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots. The historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified, cannot be stopped.\nAgainst “Taiwan independence” separatists and external hostile forces, we will uphold the overall national security concept, resolutely carry out the struggle against separatism, subversion, infiltration and espionage, effectively safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard national security and development interests. This also accords with the fundamental interests and vital well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nWishing everyone a happy National Day holiday. Today’s press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202609/t20260930_12815886.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-10-06","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","U.S. officials believe the likelihood of China “invading” Taiwan before 2028 is getting increasingly low. What’s the foreign ministry’s response?","The Taiwan question is China’s internal affair. Resolving the Taiwan question is a matter for the Chinese ourselves that brooks no external interference. The U.S. side needs to implement the important common understandings reached at the meeting between the two presidents, abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, and act prudently on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261006_12035790.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261006_12035789.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-06","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","Taiwan recently received two F-16V fighter jets purchased from the United States and plans to receive another 64 within the year. What is the foreign ministry’s response? (Also raised by AFP)","China’s position is clear. We remain firmly opposed to U.S. arms sales to China’s Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261006_12035790.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261006_12035789.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-06","Guo Jiakun","Reuters","U.S. authorities arrested a California woman on Sunday and accused her of spying on a son of Taiwan’s Lai Ching-te at the behest of Chinese officials, the FBI said. Does the foreign ministry have any comment? (Also raised by AFP, NBC and The Wall Street Journal)","I am not familiar with what you mentioned. China opposes vilifying China by peddling the so-called “Chinese spy” narrative.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261006_12035790.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261006_12035789.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-10-10","Zhang Han","Not specified (reporter question, outlet not named)","A reporter asked: Lai Ching-te today delivered a so-called “Double Ten” speech in Taipei. What comments does the spokesperson have on the content of the speech concerning cross-Strait relations?","Spokesperson Zhang Han of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council responded to questions: Lai Ching-te's speech disregards facts, reverses right and wrong, misleads the public, and has sinister intent. It is his “true-colors performance” as a “pragmatic Taiwan independence worker.” In his speech, he stubbornly clings to “Taiwan independence” separatist thinking, plays up the “mainland threat,” peddles the false narrative of “democracy against authoritarianism,” attempts to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence by relying on external forces,” stirs up cross-Strait confrontation, and undermines peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common consensus of the international community, and an important component of the post-World War II international order. Taiwan's future can and must only be decided jointly by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots.\nWe will uphold the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” broadly unite compatriots from all walks of life in Taiwan, resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, and safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. We will uphold the concept that “cross-Strait compatriots are one family,” deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, and advance the great cause of national reunification and the great endeavor of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261010_12817230.htm","",1,5,2,""],[1,"2026-10-11","Chen Xi","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Reportedly, Lai Qingde recently delivered a so-called “Double Ten” speech, hyping up the mainland's continued use of military action to pressure and change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait, calling for increased defense investment, and strengthening “whole-of-society defense resilience.” What is your comment?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the true status quo of the Taiwan Strait. Lai Ching-te stubbornly insists on the “Taiwan independence” position, distorts right and wrong, exaggerates the so-called “military threat from the mainland,” incites confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and attempts to “seek independence through force” and “seek independence by relying on foreign powers.” This once again exposes his true nature as a “calamity for Taiwan” and a “disaster for peace.”\nIn recent years, the DPP authorities, for the sake of their own party, have pursued “independence” and rejected unification on a large scale, and have groveled to foreign powers. They have forcefully promoted the so-called “whole-people military” and “whole-Taiwan battlefield,” tying the people of Taiwan to the “Taiwan independence” chariot, undermining stability across the Taiwan Strait, and sacrificing Taiwan’s future. The PLA’s regular training and exercises around Taiwan are aimed at deterring “Taiwan independence” reckless actions and the schemes of foreign interference, and at safeguarding the security and well-being of the people of Taiwan. This is entirely justified and beyond reproach.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace across the Taiwan Strait are irreconcilable. National reunification is the trend of the times, the righteous cause, and the wish of the people. We hope that compatriots in Taiwan will recognize the extreme danger and harm of Lai Ching-te authorities’ stubborn pursuit of “independence,” join us in resolutely cracking down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, jointly protect our peaceful and tranquil beautiful home, and jointly share the well-being and glory of national rejuvenation.","","http://m.cyol.com/gb/news/articles/2026-10/11/content_lbQzg8UWog.html","",0,5,1,""],[0,"2026-10-12","Mao Ning","Beijing Daily","Today, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs put on its website the decision to take countermeasures against Paraguay’s Minister of Information and Communication Technologies Gustavo Emigdio Villate Samaniego and Belize Minister of Foreign Affairs and Foreign Trade Francis Fonseca. Could you share more information on that?","The Taiwan question is a major issue of principle bearing on China’s sovereignty and national reunification. It is at the core of China’s core interests. Certain politicians in Paraguay and Belize willingly serve as chess pieces for the DPP authorities in their pursuit of independence by soliciting external support. Their visits to Taiwan and reception of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces in their countries constitute severe interference in China’s internal affairs. They also attacked and smeared China by spreading the “Chinese cyber attack” disinformation, causing egregious impact in the world.\nIn response to these moves and in accordance with the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law of the People’s Republic of China, China announced in the form of MFA decree countermeasures as an action of warning and deterrence.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261012_12038810.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261012_12038772.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-12","Mao Ning","Reuters","The U.S. State Department last week said China’s maritime activities off Taiwan’s east coast are “deeply destabilizing.” What is the foreign ministry’s comment on that?","China has on multiple occasions made clear its position on this. China has exclusive economic zone and continental shelf in waters east of the Taiwan island. It is fully within China’s sovereign rights and jurisdiction, therefore legitimate, lawful and beyond reproach, for China to carry out activities in these waters. The party that instigates troubles and disrupts stability in this part of waters has never been the Chinese side.\nThe Taiwan question is China’s internal affair that brooks no external interference. The U.S. needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question prudently, and take concrete actions to uphold the overall China-U.S. relations and peace and stability in the region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261012_12038810.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261012_12038772.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-12","Mao Ning","Xinhua News Agency","On October 10, leader of the Taiwan region Lai Ching-te made a speech in which he again solicited external support for “Taiwan independence,” and smeared Chinese mainland. What’s your comment?","There is but one China in the world. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China’s territory, and the Government of the People’s Republic of China is the sole legal government representing the whole of China. To uphold the one-China principle, reject “Taiwan independence” separatist activities and support China’s reunification is where international public opinion trends.\nLai Ching-te’s so-called “democracy” cannot hide his “Taiwan independence” separatist nature. Taiwan’s return to China is an integral part of the outcome of WWII victory and the postwar international order. The real status quo across the Taiwan Strait is that both sides of the Strait belong to one and the same China. Whatever Lai Ching-te says or does, it does not change the fact backed by history and law that Taiwan belongs to China or the doomed failure of “Taiwan independence,” and will by no means stop China’s ultimate reunification.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261012_12038810.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261012_12038772.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-12","Mao Ning","Reuters","Regarding China’s sanctions on the Paraguay and Belize ministers, would this be first of such measures against ministers from countries that maintain ties with Taiwan?","For diehard supporters of “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, China will take all necessary punitive measures to firmly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity. We urge the very few countries left which still have so-called “diplomatic ties” with China’s Taiwan region to avoid being repeatedly manipulated and used by separatist forces for “Taiwan independence.” Betting on “Taiwan independence” has no future. It will only cost them opportunities for development and lead to international isolation.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261012_12038810.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261012_12038772.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-12","Mao Ning","Global Times","Following his recent visit to China, former Japanese Foreign Minister and head of the Japanese Association for the Promotion of International Trade Mr. Takeshi Iwaya said that the deterioration in China-Japan relations was caused by the Japanese side and that the Japanese government should seek ways to improve the bilateral ties. There are voices in Japan criticizing the evasion of historical responsibility for…","China commends these remarks, which reflect reason and conscience among those with insight in Japan. As they have pointed out, the real issue lies in the distorted and erroneous views toward history and China held by those running the Japanese government, which has severely undermined the political foundation of China-Japan relations. The situation does not serve the two countries’ interests, and the responsibility rests fully with Japan. To bring China-Japan relations back to the right track, the ball is, apparently, in Japan’s court.\nWe urge those running the Japanese government to heed and take seriously the just voice at home, face up to the root causes of the problem, abide by the four political documents between China and Japan, and genuinely reflect on and correct wrongdoings on such issues as Taiwan, the history, and their China perception.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261012_12038810.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261012_12038772.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-13","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Trump administration via the U.S. State Department recently said that it opposes “coercion and aggression” by China against countries for exercising their sovereign rights. It said this in response to Beijing sanctioning ministers from Belize and Paraguay over their ties to Taiwan. Do you have any comment?","The one-China principle is a basic norm in international relations and prevailing international consensus. It is also the political foundation of China-U.S. relations. The U.S. needs to abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question prudently, and stop sending wrong signals to “Taiwan independence” separatist forces.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261013_12039583.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261013_12039483.shtml",0,1,0,""],[0,"2026-10-14","Mao Ning","AFP","The Taiwanese authorities said today they will inject up to US$ 4.4 billion into a U.S. pipeline project in Alaska. Given the huge amount of this investment, I wonder if the foreign ministry has any comment or any view on the deal.","External exchanges of China’s Taiwan region must be handled in line with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities will not succeed in seeking “Taiwan independence” in the name of trade and investment.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261014_12040329.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261014_12040283.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 14, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","On September 30, General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered an important speech at the reception celebrating the 77th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China, stressing the need to deepen cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, oppose interference by external forces, promote the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and…","Resolving the Taiwan question and achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the unwavering historical mission of the Communist Party of China, and an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech demonstrates the sincerity and goodwill toward uniting broad Taiwan compatriots, deepening cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and promoting peaceful development of cross-Strait relations. It expresses the firm resolve to crack down resolutely on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces and oppose interference by external forces, and it demonstrates the confidence and determination to steadfastly advance the great cause of reunifying the motherland.\nWe will thoroughly study, fully understand, and comprehensively implement the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping’s important speech, thoroughly implement the Party’s overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, adhere to the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” unite broad Taiwan compatriots, deepen cross-Strait exchanges, cooperation and integrated development, resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatist forces, and jointly create a bright future of reunifying the motherland and rejuvenating the nation. We hope Taiwan compatriots will conform to the trend of history, uphold our shared national righteousness, and join us in safeguarding our common home of the Chinese nation and creating enduring well-being for the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817984.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","The Chinese-U.S. leaders' meeting on September 24 included the history of China and the United States as WWII allies in its list of outcomes. The DPP authorities claimed this “conveys a wrong historical narrative,” and Lai Ching-te, in his so-called “Double Ten” speech, falsely asserted that “we will never allow distortion of WWII history.” Public opinion on the island has criticized that after coming to power…","During President Xi Jinping's state visit to the United States, the heads of state of China and the United States repeatedly mentioned that China and the United States were allies in World War II, fought side by side, and won the war, and this was included in the list of consensus outcomes. This is a commemoration of the world's anti-fascist forces fighting for human justice during World War II, and a firm defense of the fruits of victory in World War II.\nThe victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan are great victories forged by all Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots, who fought fearlessly against brutal aggression and fought bloody battles. Taiwan's liberation from the shackles of Japanese colonial rule and its return to the embrace of the motherland were a major achievement of China's victory in the War of Resistance, an important component of the postwar international order, and a historical memory that compatriots on both sides of the Strait will never forget.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities stubbornly cling to the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" arbitrarily distort history, peddle the \"Taiwan independence\" view of history, and curry favor with Japan while longing for colonial rule. They are sinners against history. History is a mirror that reveals the true nature of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities: they fabricate the \"Taiwan independence\" view of history, distort national identity, and sever the historical ties across the Strait. It also reveals their true face of inciting confrontation between the two sides of the Strait, \"anti-China and resist-China,\" and their detestable face of forgetting their ancestors and betraying the nation. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots will recognize the deceptive nature and harm of the Democratic Progressive Party authorities' provocations to seek independence, stand on the right side of history, uphold the great righteousness of the nation, hold to correct views of history, nation, and state, resolutely oppose the separatist acts of \"Taiwan independence,\" firmly maintain peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, and work to advance the great cause of national reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817983.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","It is understood that the Taiwan Affairs Office has long attached great importance to coordinating and resolving Taiwan-related investment disputes, and many Taiwanese businesses, after receiving help, have written letters to the Taiwan Affairs Office to express thanks and presented it with silk banners. Could the spokesperson introduce the work the mainland has done in recent years to protect the rights and…","We have always attached great importance to protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. We protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with law, improve the systems and policies that promote the well-being of Taiwan compatriots, and regions and departments across the country work to do practical things, good deeds, and solve difficulties for Taiwan compatriots. We have actively issued relevant laws, regulations and policies, and established and improved the institutional system for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. The state has successively issued the 《Law on the Protection of Investment by Taiwan Compatriots》 and its implementing rules, and various localities have successively formulated regulations on the protection of Taiwan compatriots' investment or measures for implementing the 《Investment Protection Law》, effectively safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots.\nOver the years, the Central Taiwan Affairs Office and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council have actively advanced the rule-of-law process for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots, and have promoted relevant departments to take many measures in legislation, law enforcement and judicial work, with notable results. The main manifestations are: the legal system for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots has continued to improve, forming a legal norm system led by the 《Anti-Secession Law》, with the 《Investment Protection Law》 and its implementing rules as the main body, and composed of relevant laws, administrative regulations, local regulations, normative documents, judicial interpretations and the agreements of the two associations; the enforcement mechanism for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots has continued to improve, and a complaint coordination mechanism that takes into account both sides of the Strait has basically been established; the judicial mechanism for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots has continued to innovate, and a diversified dispute resolution mechanism that organically combines arbitration, mediation and judicial adjudication has basically been established; the legal service means for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots have continued to be enriched, and Taiwan-related legal services such as lawyers, notarization, mediation, assistance, consultation, publicity and training are widely carried out, providing thoughtful services for Taiwan compatriots to “resolve disputes,” so that Taiwan compatriots can personally feel, in their own surroundings and in individual cases, fairness and justice, a good business environment, and the achievements of comprehensively governing the country according to law.\nThe TAO system nationwide has always attached great importance to protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. The Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council formally established a Complaints Coordination Bureau in 2005, and local Taiwan Affairs Offices at all levels have correspondingly set up complaint coordination divisions or Taiwan compatriot service centers. At the time, this measure drew a strong response from Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesses, who praised it: “Setting up a dedicated agency to protect the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses is unique in the world, and fully demonstrates the mainland's high regard for Taiwan businesses.” This mechanism has continued to operate effectively in accordance with laws and regulations. In addition, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council has also established a platform for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan businesses with the Kuomintang's Mainland Taiwan Business Service Liaison Center, which has helped resolve related disputes. Many Taiwan businesses that received assistance have expressed thanks to our office through various means.\nI must emphasize again that everyone is equal before the law, and no one has privileges above the law. What we protect in accordance with law are the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. We hope that the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan enterprises will operate on the mainland in compliance with the law and legally, and protect their own rights and interests in accordance with laws and regulations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817982.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","In his so-called “Double Ten” speech, Lai Ching-te claimed that he will continue to promote defense reform and investment and strengthen asymmetric combat capabilities, which is to deter war and ensure that dialogue can take place on the basis of equality and dignity. What is your comment on this?","In his so-called “Double Ten” speech, Lai Qingde on the one hand clamored for reckless militarism and “using force to seek independence,” and on the other hand once again sang the high note of “dialogue.” This is a typical two-faced tactic to deceive the world and mislead the people, and even more an act of a mantis trying to stop a chariot, overestimating its own strength.\nOnly by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and ceasing “Taiwan independence” separatist actions, can cross-Strait consultations and dialogue be resumed, and only then will there be a fundamental guarantee of peace across the Taiwan Strait and security for Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817981.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","《参考消息》记者","The DPP authorities recently claimed: “The CCP has long carried out compound pressure against Taiwan in an attempt to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Taiwan will continue to uphold sovereignty and our way of life of democracy, freedom, and the rule of law, and is committed to maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.” In his National Day speech, Lai Ching-te also claimed that “we…","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China; this is the true status quo across the Taiwan Strait. Under the guise of so-called “freedom and democracy,” the DPP authorities keep peddling “Taiwan independence” fallacies, slandering and attacking the mainland, hyping so-called “pressure and threats,” and fabricating a false narrative of “democracy versus authoritarianism.” They incite cross-Strait antagonism and confrontation and attempt to “seek independence by force” and “seek independence by relying on external forces.” This will only drive Taiwan further into danger and bring profound disaster to Taiwan’s people. We believe that more and more Taiwan compatriots will recognize the hypocrisy of the DPP authorities’ so-called “maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait,” and the danger and harm of their stubborn schemes for independence and provocations. They will firmly oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and safeguard their own interests and well-being and the common home of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817980.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson's criticism that Lai Ching-te's “October 10” speech was a “Taiwan independence” performance, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland should face the differences in the systems and status quo on both sides of the Strait and stop “coercion and pressure” against Taiwan. What is your comment on this?","The two sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China, and Taiwan is part of China. Differences in system are not an obstacle to unification, and they are certainly not a pretext for separation. Out of its “independence” nature, the DPP authorities spread the so-called false narrative of “mainland coercion and pressure,” continuously carry out all kinds of “Taiwan independence” provocations, and attempt to intimidate and deceive Taiwan residents and incite confrontation and antagonism across the Taiwan Strait. This kind of political manipulation, which twists black and white and harbors sinister intent, is bound to fail. As long as “Taiwan independence” provocations continue, the crackdown on them will not stop for a moment.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","Recently, some media reported that “Taiwan independence” diehard Shen Boyang, while clamoring for “resisting China and protecting Taiwan,” is trying every means, together with his father, to evade mainland sanctions and make money on the mainland. What is your response to this?","In June 2025, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council announced sanctions against Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., headed by Shen Tu-cheng, father of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figure Shen Boyang. Investigation found that, to evade sanctions, Shen Tu-cheng has continued trade and business cooperation with relevant mainland enterprises under the name of another company, VWAY, profiting from these dealings. While Shen Boyang clamors for “anti-China and resist China” and obstructs cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, he and his relatives are doing everything they can to make money on the mainland. This ugly conduct is deplorable. The mainland will never allow affiliated companies of die-hard “Taiwan independence” figures to profit on the mainland, and has decided to take necessary measures against VWAY, prohibiting it from conducting any transactions or cooperation with mainland organizations, enterprises, and individuals.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817979.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","During this year’s National Day holiday, the “Small Three Links” passenger routes welcomed a surge of cross-Strait compatriots visiting relatives and friends and traveling. Please introduce the relevant situation.","During the 2026 National Day holiday, passenger flows on the four “mini three links” passenger routes—Xiamen to Kinmen, Quanzhou to Kinmen, Fuzhou Mawei to Matsu, and Huangqi to Matsu—continued to surge. Over 250 sailings were operated, carrying about 42,000 passenger trips. Visiting relatives, family reunions, and leisure travel became the mainstream of travel, fully reflecting the continued warming of exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nRelevant departments have fully guaranteed travel demand on the “mini three links.” The Xiamen–Kinmen route added 4 extra sailings per day during key peak passenger periods. On the first day of the National Day holiday, the Fuzhou Huangqi–Matsu route was adjusted from its usual “two inbound and two outbound” to “four inbound and four outbound,” effectively meeting Taiwan compatriots’ travel needs for visiting relatives and tourism. Ports and shipping companies have refined safety measures, optimized clearance procedures, and shortened inspection waiting times. On site, various performances such as dance, face-changing, and songs were arranged, along with flash mobs, fun “bobing” dice games, and themed photo spots, allowing cross-strait passengers to experience family affection and warmth while traveling efficiently and conveniently.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","上海东方卫视记者","Recently, the younger brother of “Taiwan independence” hardliner Tsao Hsing-cheng tried to sneak into the Mainland and was refused entry at the airport. What comments do you have?","Cao Hsing-cheng has been placed on the list of die-hard “Taiwan independence” elements and subjected to sanctions, and he and his family members are prohibited from entering the mainland and the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions. We welcome compatriots on both sides to come and go frequently, but we will never show leniency toward “Taiwan independence” separatist acts. “Taiwan independence” die-hards who undermine cross-Strait relations and harm the interests of compatriots, whose conduct harms both others and themselves, will surely be severely punished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","Taiwan media, citing U.S. media reports, said the U.S. Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) arrested a U.S. woman who is suspected of surveilling Lai Ching-te’s son at the instruction of mainland officials. The DPP authorities said this is a typical “transnational repression” and that they have actively drafted amendments to the so-called “Anti-Infiltration Act” in response. What comments do you have on this?","I am not aware of the situation you mentioned. We firmly oppose the DPP authorities colluding with external forces to talk nonsense and make things up, manipulating “anti-China and resist-China” rhetoric, stirring up cross-Strait confrontation, and seeking political gain. This sinister scheme and despicable practice cannot deceive Taiwan residents and will only be despised.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, during her trip to the United States, Tsai Ing-wen spoke about cross-Strait relations, claiming that the Taiwanese public has formed a view of maintaining the cross-Strait status quo and avoiding unnecessary provocations, and expressing the consensus that Taiwan will protect its own democracy and security. She said, “Restraint should not be mistaken for weakness. Its purpose is to avoid miscalculation,…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. This is the real status quo across the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence,” and under the guise of “democracy” and “peace,” collude with external forces to engage in provocations aimed at seeking “independence.” They deliberately escalate cross-Strait confrontation and opposition. They are the destroyers of the status quo across the Taiwan Strait and the source of trouble for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait.\n“Taiwan independence” and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait are incompatible. Only by abandoning the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” and acknowledging the one-China principle and the “1992 Consensus,” can peace across the Taiwan Strait and tranquility for Taiwan be guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","During this year's “National Day” holiday, the Mainland's cultural and tourism market continued to boom. Taiwan's tourism industry, which has lost Mainland tourist markets due to DPP obstruction, is recovering slowly. Tourism operators on the island have repeatedly said that Mainland tourists used to bring huge benefits when visiting Taiwan, but now they are “able to see but not eat.” What is your comment?","According to statistics, during this year's National Day holiday, domestic travel reached 826 million person-trips, with total spending of 738.375 billion yuan, up 6.3% and 4.3% respectively over the same period last year.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family. We have consistently and actively promoted cross-Strait tourism exchanges and cooperation, and we hope that compatriots on both sides will visit each other often, stay in close contact, and deepen their friendship. Mainland residents traveling to Taiwan once greatly boosted the development of Taiwan's tourism-related industries, advanced the interests and well-being of grassroots residents and industry in Taiwan, and promoted mutual understanding and recognition between compatriots on both sides of the Strait, strengthening their bonds. However, for some time now, the DPP authorities have placed their political self-interest above people's livelihood and well-being. They have completely disregarded the voices and demands of Taiwan's tourism operators and the broad public, and have deliberately set up barriers and restrictions to obstruct cross-Strait tourism exchanges. As a result, the recovery of Taiwan's tourism industry has been sluggish, and the interests of relevant industries and the public have been seriously harmed.\nThe DPP authorities should change course and heed public opinion. They should remove the obstructive restrictions on cross-Strait personal exchanges and tourism exchanges and cooperation, and resume mainland residents' travel to Taiwan as soon as possible. Otherwise, they will only face growing opposition and condemnation from Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817976.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中新社记者","Taiwanese entertainer Cai Kangyong appeared at the founding conference of the campaign headquarters of Shen Boyang, the DPP candidate for Taipei mayor. What comments does the spokesperson have on this?","Taiwan is an inseparable part of China. Adhering to the one-China principle is a general consensus of the international community and the common political foundation of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. The conduct of \"Taiwan independence\" diehard Shen Boyang is well known to all, and any form of \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activity seriously harms the fundamental interests of the Chinese nation, and we resolutely oppose all of it.\nWe have always respected and safeguarded the legitimate freedoms of speech and expression of Taiwan compatriots, but on matters of major principle, there is no room for ambiguity. Upholding unification and opposing \"Taiwan independence\" is the common will of the entire Chinese people. No person or force may profit from the mainland's development dividends while colluding with \"Taiwan independence\" separatist forces, playing \"two-faced\" games.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817978.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Exchanges in all fields across the Taiwan Strait continue to be lively. I will introduce recent cross-Strait economic and trade, youth, and cultural exchanges.\nIn economic and trade exchanges, the 7th Cross-Strait (Shaanxi) Economic, Trade and Science and Technology Cooperation Conference, co-hosted by the Shaanxi Provincial People’s Government and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, will open in Xi’an on October 15. It will include the opening ceremony, the Cross-Strait Machinery Industry Exchange Meeting, the Shaanxi-Taiwan Women Entrepreneurs Cooperation and Exchange Symposium, the Taiwan Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Exchange Meeting and Shaanxi-Taiwan Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition, the Shaanxi-Taiwan Agricultural Cooperation Forum, and other activities. The aim is to promote the expansion of Shaanxi-Taiwan economic and trade cooperation into broader and deeper areas.\nIn youth exchanges, Xiamen, Fujian held the “Cross-Strait Encounter at Yonghua Lane, Youthful Celebration of the Full Moon and Anniversary” youth exchange event and the “Island · Shadow” Gulangyu Youth Song Festival. Zhangzhou held the “Echoes from Neighbors, One Voice Across the Strait” Youth Musician SEEK Plan (Season 1) and the Double Fish Island Music Carnival. Quanzhou held the 2026 Cross-Strait (Quanzhou) Street Dance Competition Grand Final. Ningde held the “Ning-Tai One Family” table tennis invitational tournament. Youth from both sides deepened their friendship through interactive exchanges. On October 11, the Taiwan division of the 3rd World Minnan Youth Singers Competition, titled “Ocean Voices · Youth in Full Bloom,” concluded. Six contestants stood out and will take part in the advancement competition in November. From October 12 to 21, Hubei held the 10th “Taiwan Youth Look at Wuhan · Charming River City Snapshot” event, in which youth from both sides captured the scenery of the river city through their lenses. From October 14 to 20, Henan held the “Central Plains Cultural Experience Camp,” in which youth from both sides immersively experienced the roots of Chinese civilization and historical and cultural heritage through visits and exchanges. From September 16 to 25, the “Taiwan Youth Look at Xinjiang — Charming Silk Road Snapshot” event was held in Xinjiang, in which invited Taiwan youth recorded and shared, through their lenses, the magnificent scenery, prosperity and development, and the beauty of ethnic integration in Xinjiang.\nIn cultural exchanges, the “Huangmei Opera Expressing Feelings, Anhui Charm Lasting Fragrance — Classic Huangmei Opera Showcase” cultural exchange performance was held in Taiwan in September. Taiwan audiences had close-up enjoyment of classic Huangmei opera pieces in their original authentic style. The series “Guarding Our Spiritual Home — The 12th Cross-Strait Intangible Cultural Heritage Month” was held in Taiwan from September to October, featuring exhibitions, performances, and craft demonstrations on Hainan intangible cultural heritage themes, and was warmly welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. From September 27 to October 1, the 4th Zhejiang-Taiwan Literature Week, themed “Feel Poetic Zhejiang, Tell Chinese Stories Well,” was held in Quzhou City, Zhejiang Province, with more than 150 writers, poets, and literature enthusiasts from both sides attending. On September 23, the result announcement ceremony of the 2026 Cross-Strait WE Short Drama Competition was held in Quanzhou, Fujian. More than 700 representatives of cross-Strait micro short drama production organizations, online platforms, and micro short drama creators used micro short dramas, a new cultural carrier, to promote cross-Strait cultural exchange. On October 18, the dance drama “Mazu” will premiere at the Fujian Grand Theatre. Produced jointly by the Fujian Provincial Song and Dance Drama Theatre, the China Oriental Song and Dance Troupe, and the Youth Troupe of the Beijing Dance Academy, the drama uses the language of modern dance to transform classic legends such as “Rescuing Kin from the Air” and “Burning the House to Guide the Ship” into delicate and moving stage narratives, shaping the image of Mazu as an ordinary person with warmth and integrity. Everyone is welcome to follow it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","人民政协报记者","During the National Day holiday, several Taiwan entertainers posted messages blessing the motherland, and the Mainland Affairs Council proposed so-called “two red lines” in response. Well-known Taiwan entertainer Wu Qilong was also removed from a public event on the island because he expressed blessings for the motherland at Tiananmen Square. What comment do you have on this?","Taiwan is part of China, and it is only natural for Taiwan compatriots to spontaneously express their patriotic sentiments. Taiwan entertainers offering blessings to the motherland and expressing patriotic feelings on the occasion of National Day is a genuine outpouring from the heart, and we fully affirm this.\nThe DPP authorities have repeatedly threatened and intimidated Taiwan entertainers, and have staged a “green terror.” This seriously hurts the national sentiments of Taiwan compatriots and is unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261014_12817977.htm"],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","香港经济导报记者","Recently, Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan’s foreign affairs department, made an unofficial visit to Arizona, USA, to unveil the plaque of the “Taipei Economic and Cultural Office in Phoenix.” What is your comment?","The DPP authorities stubbornly “rely on the US to seek independence” and “kowtow to the US and sell out Taiwan,” disregarding the well-being of Taiwan compatriots and the interests of the industrial sector. They treat the island’s advantageous industries as tools for seeking “independence” and as tribute for currying favor with foreigners. This is selling out, harming and destroying Taiwan.\nWe firmly oppose any form of official exchanges between countries that have diplomatic relations with us and the Taiwan region of China. The relevant departments have made serious representations to the US side. We urge the US side to abide by the One-China principle and the three China-US joint communiqués, stop official US-Taiwan exchanges, and stop condoning or supporting the “Taiwan independence” forces and their separatist activities in any form.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","福建东南卫视记者","Taiwan’s coast guard authorities recently said, “Two mainland fishing vessels that crossed into the waters of Dongsha were expelled in accordance with the law,” and one of them refused to raise its anchor and was driven back with water cannon. Cho Jung-tai, head of the Executive Yuan, said, “Firing water cannon is something we had to do. If sovereignty is violated, law enforcement personnel must defend national…","China has indisputable sovereignty over the South China Sea Islands, including the Dongsha Islands, and their adjacent waters. Mainland vessels operating in the relevant waters are entirely lawful and legitimate, and we resolutely safeguard the lives and property of the people. The DPP authorities obstinately adhere to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence,” treat mainland vessels roughly in a dangerous manner, endanger the lives and property of the personnel involved, and maliciously stir up cross-Strait confrontation. They must bear all consequences arising from this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“看台海”新媒体记者","According to a Reuters report, some US officials analyze that the possibility of mainland China attacking Taiwan before 2028 has decreased. In response, the DPP authorities said that the mainland’s intention to “annex” Taiwan by force has never changed and will never be abandoned because of who is in “power.” What is your comment on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The DPP authorities' obstinate insistence on the separatist stance of “Taiwan independence” is the root cause of tension and turmoil in the Taiwan Strait. The motherland must be reunified, and it will be reunified; this is a historical trend that no one and no force can stop.\n福","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, the European Parliament released a report on EU-China political relations, clamoring for refusing Chinese pressure on international organizations and restricting Taiwan's participation in international exchanges, and emphasizing that the EU takes the “One China Policy” as the guiding framework for its Taiwan policy and has never endorsed the one-China principle. Taiwan's foreign affairs department…","The relevant departments have already expressed a solemn position on this.\nWe firmly oppose the European Parliament's commenting on the Taiwan question and its brutal interference in China's internal affairs. We urge the European side to abide by the one-China principle and to handle Taiwan-related issues prudently and appropriately.\nRegarding the Taiwan region's participation in international organizations and their activities, our position is consistent and clear: it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. The DPP authorities' attempt to win over external forces to endorse their vile provocations aimed at seeking “independence” will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Regarding the incident involving Taiwan entertainer Cai Kangyong, Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an publicly called on the mainland to respect Taiwan's free and democratic way of life. The differences in values between the two sides of the Strait cannot be made to disappear by merely shouting the slogan “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” Taiwan needs to understand the mainland's insistence. Is it…","The mainland and Taiwan both belong to one China. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and culture, and are bound by blood. We are all Chinese, we are all one family. “Compatriots on both sides are one family” is not an empty slogan but an indisputable fact. We respect the social system and way of life chosen by compatriots in Taiwan, and compatriots in Taiwan should also respect the development path chosen by compatriots on the mainland and respect the current judicial system on the mainland. Differences in social systems are not an excuse for separatism, let alone an obstacle to reunification, and should not become tools for inciting cross-strait confrontation or distorting national identity. When family members get along, as long as they speak frankly and consult each other on matters, there are no contradictions or differences that cannot be resolved.\nWe have always respected, cared for, and united with compatriots in Taiwan, and we are willing to listen to the voices of compatriots in Taiwan. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait should engage in mutual learning and dialogue with tolerance, put themselves in others' shoes, deepen mutual understanding, and enhance mutual trust and recognition. On the basis of the one-China principle, we are willing to hold dialogues and exchanges with Taiwan's political parties, groups, and individuals on cross-strait political issues and matters related to advancing the process of national reunification, broadly exchange views, and seek social consensus. Compatriots in Taiwan may fully express their opinions and actively participate in the design of the political and social systems after reunification.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: In his “Double Ten” speech, Lai Ching-te, on the one hand, stressed that Taiwan will not give up freedom, and on the other hand expressed the hope of maintaining peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. What is your comment on this? Second question: TSMC recently reached a 2 billion US dollar cooperation agreement with the American foundry GlobalFoundries, further strengthening the US AI chip…","First question. The Office has already responded on October 10 to Lai Ching-te's speech. This speech is full of deception. It uses the lie of so-called defense of “democracy and freedom” to conceal its sinister intent of seeking “Taiwan independence,” peddles “Taiwan independence” separatist fallacies under the banner of “safeguarding peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait,” hypes up the so-called “mainland threat,” incites confrontation between the two sides of the Strait, and seeks to confuse people and mislead public opinion. The DPP authorities' deceptive tactics of saying one thing and doing another have long been seen through by compatriots on both sides of the Strait.\nOnly by acknowledging the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle, and halting provocations for “Taiwan independence,” can cross-Strait dialogue and consultation resume and can peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait be fundamentally guaranteed.\nSecond question. In pursuit of “relying on the US to seek independence,” the DPP authorities have blindly kowtowed to and pandered to the US and sold out Taiwan. They have cooperated with US pressure on TSMC to shift production capacity to the US, resulting in leakage of technology, outflow of talent and relocation of industries. The DPP authorities' conduct can only bring disaster to Taiwan and ruin it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Last year, the mainland sanctioned companies affiliated with Shen Po-yang's father. How were the related companies of Shen's father able to complete several transactions within half a year and smoothly clear customs for export? Some public opinion in Taiwan holds that the timing of this disclosure is sensitive and may involve “election interference,” which would benefit the Green camp in reverse-manipulating…","We punish “Taiwan independence” diehards and their affiliated companies in accordance with the law. We always adhere to facts as the basis and law as the standard, acting righteously and in accordance with the law. Whenever we find a case, we investigate and deal with it, and we will show no leniency or softness. The attempts of “Taiwan independence” diehards and their affiliated companies to hide from public view and evade sanctions are entirely futile. They precisely expose their panic over the sword of punishment for “independence” hanging overhead, and they highlight their ugly faces of being fierce in appearance but timid within, and driven by profit.\n“Taiwan independence” diehards who split the country, undermine cross-strait relations and harm the interests and well-being of compatriots are punished according to law and held accountable for life. They harm others and themselves, and it is entirely self-inflicted. Our punishment of an extremely small number of illegal and criminal “Taiwan independence” diehards is a righteous act and does not involve the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","First, regarding reports on Shen Boyang, he recently said that every time they respond to these groundless accusations, it inevitably gives the relevant claims more volume. What comment does the Taiwan Affairs Office have? Second, Shen Boyang, a candidate for Taipei mayor, said in May this year that the “Twin City Forum” has extremely low benefit and that “things without benefit should not be done.” Recently he…","On the first question: The relevant departments adhere to the principles of basing their handling of “Taiwan independence” diehards and their affiliated enterprises on facts and applying the law as the standard, and we believe that the relevant media reports have already fulfilled their responsibility to verify facts and be objective and fair. The person you mention has consistently been inconsistent, changing positions faster than turning pages. What he should do now is clear his name and give a responsible account to Taiwan society.\nOn the second question: The Shanghai-Taipei City Forum has been held for 16 consecutive years, and it has reached many points of consensus on topics including the economy, culture, technology, society, sports, and urban management. It is of great significance for promoting exchanges and cooperation between the two cities, enhancing the well-being of residents of both cities, and advancing the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations, and it has been widely recognized and welcomed by compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the common aspirations of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. “Taiwan independence” diehards have long advocated “Taiwan independence” secessionist positions, stirred up confrontation across the Strait, and undermined peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. They have no qualifications whatsoever to speak of cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-14","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","Pursuant to the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced sanctions against two incumbent ministers of Paraguay and Belize. Some public opinion in Taiwan says this is the first time the mainland authorities have extended the application of domestic law to incumbent officials of Taiwan's “diplomatic allies.” Will this practice become routine in the future? Will this kind of…","I do not think that resolutely cracking down on “Taiwan independence” separatist acts, resolutely opposing interference by external forces, and winning the hearts of the Taiwan people are contradictory. The clearer and more resolute our position and actions in safeguarding national unification and peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait, the more compatriots in Taiwan will support and back us.\nRegarding the specific cases of implementing the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law that you mentioned, the relevant departments have already expressed a solemn position on this. I suggest you review the relevant provisions of the Anti-Foreign Sanctions Law, which clearly set out the rules for the relevant situations and have clear boundaries.\nThere is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China. Taiwan has never been a country and has no qualifications to establish or maintain any so-called “diplomatic relations” with any country. Certain politicians in Paraguay and Belize have colluded with “Taiwan independence” elements, seriously interfered in China's internal affairs, and caused a bad influence. We have taken countermeasures in accordance with relevant laws, which is reasonable and lawful. The DPP, in pursuit of its private interests in “independence,” has continuously fabricated false narratives, attempted to incite confrontation across the Taiwan Strait, and challenged the one-China principle recognized by the international community. It will not succeed and is doomed to fail.\nToday's press conference is concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261014_12817974.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-10-19","Mao Ning","AFP","On the South China Sea. Authorities in Taiwan said yesterday that they had driven away 16 mainland Chinese Coast Guard, research and fishing vessels in coordinated operations around Taiwan’s main island and Pratas, also known as the Dongsha Islands. Does the foreign ministry have any more information or comments on this?","This is not a question about foreign affairs.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261019_12042922.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261019_12042878.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 21, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Zhang Han answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, good morning. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now, please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","新华社记者","Recently, the National Health and Wellness Conference was held in Beijing. General Secretary Xi Jinping attended the conference and delivered an important speech, emphasizing the need to actively promote building a community of shared health for mankind and to work hand in hand to meet major challenges in the fields of health and wellness. Please introduce the exchanges and cooperation between the two sides of…","General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech at the National Health and Health Conference has pointed the way and provided the fundamental guideline for advancing cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in the fields of health and wellness.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese and are one family. We have always upheld the concept of “compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family,” and actively promoted cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in the fields of health and wellness, striving to enhance the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. On the one hand, we support cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in the fields of health and wellness in various forms, including supporting the holding of activities such as the Straits Forum – Health and Wellness Sub-forum, the Cross-Strait Hospital Directors Forum, and the Cross-Strait Hospital Pharmacy Conference, to build high-level dialogue platforms for the cross-Strait medical community. We support the holding of cross-Strait medical youth summer camps, young physician exchange visits, and public welfare training activities for grassroots free clinics, to promote mutual understanding, exchange and mutual learning between the cross-Strait medical community, especially young physicians and medical students.\nOn the other hand, we continuously improve policy measures that benefit Taiwan compatriots in the fields of health and wellness, effectively resolve issues faced by Taiwan compatriots in seeking medical care, studying medicine, practicing medicine and running medical institutions on the Chinese mainland, and deepen the integrated development of cross-Strait health and wellness. In terms of seeking medical care, Taiwan compatriots holding a Taiwan Compatriot Permit or residence permit can enjoy medical services in various places, and some provinces and cities can provide agency services for National Health Insurance reimbursement. In terms of studying medicine, Taiwan compatriots who obtain a medical degree on the Chinese mainland can take the physician qualification examination after completing one year of internship. In terms of practicing medicine, Taiwan compatriots can participate in medical services on the Chinese mainland through three pathways: examination, certification, or short-term practice. In terms of running medical institutions, Taiwan-funded enterprises can establish wholly foreign-owned hospitals in some provinces and cities.\nNext, we will thoroughly implement the Party Central Committee's decisions and arrangements on Taiwan work and the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speech on health and wellness work, continuously advance cross-Strait exchange and cooperation in the fields of health and wellness, expand coverage, focus on key areas, and more fully and effectively transform exchange achievements into health dividends benefiting compatriots on both sides of the Strait, continuously enhance the health and well-being of compatriots on both sides of the Strait, and lay a foundation for the prosperity of the nation and the strength of the country.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819207.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","人民日报记者","Recently, the “Opinions of the CPC Central Committee and the State Council on Developing New Quality Productive Forces” was released, drawing high attention from industry circles on both sides of the Strait. What opportunities will this bring to Taiwanese businesses and enterprises developing on the mainland? How will it help mainland Taiwanese businesses and enterprises seize opportunities and achieve greater…","This year is the opening year of the “15th Five-Year Plan”. During the “15th Five-Year Plan” period, we will place the development of new quality productive forces, tailored to local conditions, in a more prominent strategic position. On October 9, the CPC Central Committee and the State Council issued the “Opinions on Developing New Quality Productive Forces”, which deploys 19 key measures across five areas: vigorously promoting scientific and technological innovation, promoting deep integration of scientific-technological innovation and industrial innovation, strongly advancing innovation in development methods, solidly advancing institutional and mechanism innovation, and deepening innovation in talent work mechanisms. These measures will accelerate the formation of production relations better suited to new quality productive forces, create a favorable development ecosystem conducive to the deep integration of scientific-technological innovation and industrial innovation, and better support high-quality development.\nThe “Opinions” set a benchmark for unifying thinking and action in developing new quality productive forces, and also provide guidance for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to seize opportunities and achieve better development of their own. A series of measures, such as “strengthening the supply of inclusive incentive policies”, “promoting the opening of supply chains from large enterprises to small and medium-sized enterprises”, and “improving an efficient technology market for transforming achievements”, will provide broader development space for Taiwan businesses and enterprises to consolidate and enhance their existing undertakings and explore and expand emerging ventures. We will continue to implement equal treatment for Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, continuously improve institutions and policies that benefit Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises, and support Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises in seizing the opportunities of developing new quality productive forces, integrating into the new development pattern, and participating in high-quality development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819206.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","福建厦门卫视记者","October 25 marks the 81st anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration and the first anniversary of the state establishing Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. Will there be commemorative activities?","This year marks the 81st anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, and also the first anniversary of the establishment of the national Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. The relevant parties will hold commemorative activities to jointly review the history of all Chinese sons and daughters who, generation after generation and fighting bloodily, achieved victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan, and to rally the strength to advance the complete reunification of the motherland and the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation. We will release information on the relevant activities in a timely manner.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","香港中评社记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the mainland will hold “commemorative activities for the 160th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen” in November, using this to conduct propaganda on “opposing independence and promoting reunification.” Those who apply for permission to travel to the mainland will be denied permission, including county and city heads and other officials, who are all…","This year marks the 160th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen. We solemnly commemorate Mr. Sun Yat-sen in order to carry forward his lofty spirit of safeguarding national unity and devoting himself to national revitalization, to unite all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots, to resolutely combat “Taiwan independence” separatism, oppose foreign interference, promote cross-Strait exchange and integration, and jointly strive for the realization of national reunification and national rejuvenation.\nThe DPP authorities are willing to use every means, and have calculatedly obstructed and restricted cross-Strait exchanges and intimidated and suppressed Taiwan compatriots. This fully exposes their treacherous intent to betray the nation, betray history, plot to split the country, and escalate cross-Strait confrontation and antagonism, and they will inevitably be opposed and reviled by all Chinese descendants.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","《参考消息》记者","Recently, island polls have shown that about 60% of Taiwan’s youth believe Taiwan cannot rely on the US, and support actively engaging in dialogue and negotiations with the mainland. This stands in sharp contrast to the “anti-China” atmosphere that the DPP authorities have long incited. What is your comment?","Peace, development, exchange, and cooperation are the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. The DPP authorities stubbornly maintain a separatist “Taiwan independence” position, kowtow and fawn on external forces, pander to and kneel before the United States without principle, and sell out and harm Taiwan without bottom line. They are doing everything they can to obstruct cross-strait exchange and cooperation and to incite cross-strait opposition and confrontation. Broad sections of Taiwan compatriots, including Taiwan’s young people, see this more and more clearly and increasingly oppose the reckless conduct of the DPP authorities.\nWe are willing, on the common political basis of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” to strengthen exchanges and cooperation with people from all walks of life in Taiwan, to promote the peaceful and integrated development of cross-strait relations, to enhance the kinship and well-being of compatriots, and to jointly create a better future for cross-strait relations.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819200.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","福建东南卫视记者","According to statistics released by Taiwan's finance authority, in September this year Taiwan exported US$20.62 billion to the mainland and imported US$13.5 billion from the mainland, up 30.2% and 59.1% year on year, respectively. Some public opinion holds that although the DPP authorities keep clamoring for cross-Strait “decoupling and supply chain breaking,” cross-Strait economic and trade data shatter their…","The mainland has an extremely large domestic market and the most complete industrial system, and it is the most stable driving force of global economic growth. It is also a fertile ground for Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises to invest, develop, and grow bigger and stronger. According to the General Administration of Customs, from January to September this year, cross-Strait trade reached US$301.18 billion, up 30.3% year on year, with strong momentum. Among this, mainland exports to Taiwan were US$84.9 billion, up 37.3% year on year, and mainland imports from Taiwan were US$216.28 billion, up 27.8% year on year.\nThese data fully demonstrate that cross-Strait industrial and supply chains remain stable, that the two economies cannot be decoupled and industries cannot be cut off from their chains, and that cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation, mutual benefit and win-win results, and integrated development are the trend of the times and the aspiration of the people. The DPP authorities, out of their inherent nature of seeking “independence,” strenuously obstruct cross-Strait economic exchange and cooperation and cater to external forces that push to “decouple and cut off chains” across the Strait. This is doomed to fail.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819204.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","环球时报、环球网记者","It is understood that mainland entertainer Zhang Linghe recently applied to visit Taiwan to hold fan meetings and other exchange activities, but the DPP authorities rejected his application. What is your comment?","Mainland performing artists traveling to Taiwan for cultural exchanges are a form of people-to-people contact that people on both sides of the Strait welcome and look forward to, and it helps enhance mutual understanding between compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities, for political purposes, have disregarded the wishes of the people on the island, especially Taiwan's youth, and refused to approve the exchange visits of Mainland performing artists to Taiwan. This undermines cross-Strait cultural exchanges and runs counter to the wishes of the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots. We urge the DPP authorities to heed the common wish of compatriots on both sides of the Strait to strengthen exchanges and contacts, abandon political manipulation, lift unreasonable restrictions, and provide convenience for cross-Strait cultural exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819202.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","香港凤凰卫视记者","In response to the Taiwan Affairs Office's announcement that it would impose punishment on companies linked to the hardline \"Taiwan independence\" separatist Shen Boyang, Shen has repeatedly tried to rationalize his conduct, and the Mainland Affairs Council said, \"This is an attempt to coerce Taiwan society and interfere with elections.\" What comments do you have on this?","After the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council announced sanctions in June 2025 against Zhaoyi Co., Ltd., headed by Shen Tu-cheng, father of the die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" figure Shen Boyang, Shen Tu-cheng continued to purchase goods from the mainland and sell them to foreign countries under the name of another company under his name, VWAY, profiting from the price difference. The facts are clear and the evidence is conclusive. Shen Boyang has made countless excuses and confused the public, attempting to divert attention. This fully exposes his guilty conscience and base character.\nWe protect the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots in accordance with the law, but we will never tolerate die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" elements and their affiliated enterprises that undermine the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. The DPP authorities colluded with die-hard \"Taiwan independence\" elements, working hand in glove, attacking and smearing the mainland for their own political gain. This is despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819201.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","After the DPP took office, the cross-Strait investment dispute consultation mechanism was suspended. The Kuomintang-CPC work platform for protecting the rights of Taiwan compatriots has become an important platform for safeguarding the legitimate rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople in accordance with the law. What achievements has this platform made in protecting the legitimate…","In April 2005, during a visit led by Mr. Lien Chan, Chairman of the Kuomintang of China, formal talks were held between the KMT and the CPC, producing a number of outcomes, including the “establishment of a platform for exchange and communication between the two parties.” On this basis, and on the common political foundation of upholding the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” in the second half of 2005 the relevant bureau of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and relevant parties of the KMT established a working platform for protecting the lawful rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots. In the second half of 2016, relevant parties of the KMT and the CPC agreed to use the KMT-CPC working platform for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots as the main channel for communication on protecting those rights and interests.\nOver the years, the KMT-CPC working platform for protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots has carried out exchanges and cooperation through regular meetings, case referrals, and other means. It has operated continuously and effectively, and has played an important role in cross-Strait exchanges and in protecting the rights and interests of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan businesspeople. The scope of rights protection under this mechanism has continuously expanded, and it has become an important channel for people on both sides of the Strait to lodge complaints and petitions, seek consultation and assistance, and safeguard their own lawful rights and interests. In particular, since the beginning of this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and relevant parties of the KMT have held multiple consultations on strengthening the operational quality and effectiveness of the KMT-CPC working platform, and have reached consensus. The two sides will continue to strengthen regular communication and timely feedback, provide professional legal services to Taiwan compatriots through the platform mechanism, and play a greater role in assisting Taiwan compatriots who encounter temporary difficulties, in family and person searches, and in providing humanitarian care.\nThe cross-Strait investment dispute coordination mechanism you mentioned just now was established in 2012 under the “Agreement on Investment Protection and Promotion across the Taiwan Strait.” After May 2016, its operation was suspended because the DPP authorities refused to recognize the “1992 Consensus,” which embodies the one-China principle. As long as the DPP authorities recognize the “1992 Consensus,” we are willing to hold dialogue on resuming the operation of the cross-Strait investment dispute coordination mechanism.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819205.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","Exchange activities across all fields between the two sides of the Strait continue to be active. I will introduce recent exchanges in youth and culture between the two sides.\nIn youth exchanges: From October 12 to 16, the “Partnering Self-Media, Building Dreams in the Greater Bay Area” Taiwan Youth Bay Area Tour was held in Guangdong, where young people from both sides immersively experienced the development pulse of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area and the charm of Chinese culture during visits and exchanges. On October 13, the exhibition of results of the “Love in Lingnan, Guarding Together” cross-Strait marriage and family series activities and the 5th Guangdong Cross-Strait Marriage and Family Bay Area Tour were held in Dongguan, with about 600 people from all walks of life, including cross-Strait marriage representatives, attending. From October 15 to 20, the 2026 Cross-Strait Da Yu (Yu the Great) Cultural Exchange Activity was held in Dezhou, Shandong, where young representatives from both sides gathered in Dezhou to study Da Yu culture together and share fraternal bonds. From October 16 to 20, the 2026 Cross-Strait Emergency Management Industry-Education Integration Academic Forum was held at Henan Polytechnic University. From October 17 to 18, the “Porcelain Charm, Tea Fragrance, Meeting Across the Strait” — First Cross-Strait Red Oolong Tea Master Competition was held in Quanzhou, Fujian. On October 18, the Cross-Strait and Hong Kong-Macao Film Industry Dialogue, held as part of the Yangtze River Delta International Youth Film Week, took place in Ningbo, Zhejiang.\nIn cultural exchanges: On October 16, the 3rd Taiwan-Benefiting Music Event was held in Huizhou, Guangdong. From October 17 to 18, the 2nd Cross-Strait Opera Culture Exchange Activity was held in Xiamen, Fujian, where nearly 500 famous opera performers and opera fans from both sides gathered in Xiamen to sing the elegant tunes of the Pear Garden together. On October 17, the Cross-Strait Hanfu Carnival, an exchange on the inheritance of Hanfu culture and industrial development, was held in Xiamen, Fujian, where about 200 cross-Strait Hanfu culture practitioners and corporate representatives exchanged ideas. From October 21 to 26, the ICH study activity commemorating the 896th anniversary of the birth of Zhu Xi, focused on Zhu Xi culture, was held at the Nanxi Academy in Youxi, Sanming, Fujian, attended by more than 50 representatives, including representatives from the Yannan Academy in Kinmen. On October 15, the “Henan–Taiwan Common Origin: Crossing the Strait to Trace Roots” micro-documentary series, jointly produced by the Henan Provincial Taiwan Affairs Office and Henan Radio and Television, was released on relevant platforms. Using the six major surnames of Chen, Lin, Huang, Zheng, Cai, and Lai as its thread, the series shows six Taiwan youths coming to their ancestral homeland in the Central Plains, asking about their origins amid the thousand-year cultural lineage, and witnessing the deep connections of compatriots on both sides of the Strait who share common roots and origins.\nIn folk beliefs: From October 11 to 18, the 2026 “Passing on Incense, Forging Bonds, Caring for Both Sides of the Strait” — Kunshan Mazu Pilgrimage to Taiwan activity held island-entry parades, visiting temples in New Taipei, Taipei, Taichung, and other places. During this time, Kunshan Taiwan businesspeople and enterprises purchased Taiwan pomelo along the parade route and presented them to temples and relatives across Taiwan, conveying the good wish of “Safe and Sound with Precious Pomelos.” On October 18 and 19, the commemorative activity for the ascension of Mazu and the folk custom of the Golden Body Patrol for Safety was held on Meizhou Island in Putian, Fujian, where more than 100 Taiwan Mazu temples and over 600 believers joined local residents in attending. On October 18, the Cross-Strait Joint Ceremony Commemorating the Yellow Emperor, Bingwu (2026) Year, was held in Jinyun, Lishui, Zhejiang, with more than 300 representatives from both sides of the Strait, overseas compatriots, and all walks of life attending. From October 18 to 24, the 2026 (Bingwu) Cross-Strait Yan Emperor Shennong Cultural Exchange Conference was held in Zhuzhou, Hunan. Young people from both sides of the Strait jointly worshipped Emperor Yan Shennong, deepening emotional bonds among compatriots and strengthening identification with common ancestry and forebears.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","中新社记者","Although the DPP authorities maintain an “orange” travel alert for travel to the mainland and constantly warn the public that there are “risks” in traveling to the mainland, the number of trips to the mainland has still surged. According to Taiwan's statistics, from January to August this year, Taiwan residents made a cumulative 2.492 million trips to the mainland, up 19.63% year on year. What is your comment on…","The facts fully prove that the DPP authorities' obstruction of Taiwan residents from coming to the mainland is absurd and futile.\nFrom January to June of this year, the number of Taiwan compatriot visits to the mainland increased by 24.9% year-on-year. Yesterday, the National Immigration Administration released data on entries and exits in the first three quarters, including data for residents of Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan. “Unboxing the mainland” is increasingly becoming a lifestyle trend for Taiwan residents, especially Taiwan youth. We welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland for all kinds of “unboxing experiences,” from traditional sightseeing such as climbing the Great Wall and seeing giant pandas, to enjoying performances by intelligent robots and drones and visiting smart new energy vehicle factories; from joining group tours to riding high-speed rail and self-guided cycling trips; from savoring local food and browsing markets to experiencing short dramas produced in an immersive way and short-term training courses to learn new skills. Taiwan residents deeply “unbox” a rich and colorful way of life on the mainland and experience the happiness of being Chinese.\nThe DPP authorities should face squarely the demands of the island's industry and public, and stop deliberately obstructing cross-Strait exchanges and contacts by all kinds of means.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261021_12819203.htm"],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","Recently, at an event, the host referred to Jay Chou as a “Chinese singer.” Jay Chou himself reposted and liked the related video on social media, which was well received by netizens on both sides of the Strait. They believe that over many years he has created a large body of Chinese-style music that has become a shared cultural memory for young people on both sides. However, the Green camp on the island…","Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are all Chinese. For Taiwan entertainers to identify as “Chinese singers” is a sincere expression of their wish to be Chinese with dignity and integrity. “Taiwan independence” forces cannot bear to see compatriots on both sides of the Strait feel emotionally connected and draw closer together. They attach labels and attack entertainers, attempting to use political means to restrict the legitimate expression of Taiwan compatriots. Their intentions are sinister and unpopular.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","北京日报记者","Recently, the academic seminar on 'UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and the Taiwan Question' was held in Beijing. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On October 14, the academic symposium \"UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 and the Taiwan Question,\" hosted by the Cross-Strait Law Exchange Promotion Association of the China Law Society, was held in Beijing. Nearly 100 legal experts and scholars from research institutions on Taiwan-related affairs, universities, and research institutions in Hong Kong and Macau attended the meeting. Focusing on the theme of the meeting, the experts and scholars systematically studied the historical original context and legal binding force of UN General Assembly Resolution 2758, and held in-depth exchanges and discussions on consolidating the international law foundation of the one-China principle and on strengthening the use of the rule of law to advance the process of national reunification.\nThe symposium clarified the facts and emphasized that UN General Assembly Resolution 2758 thoroughly resolved, politically, legally, and procedurally, the question of representation of all of China, including Taiwan, at the United Nations; its legitimacy, validity, and authority cannot be challenged. Resolution 2758 fully reflects and solemnly confirms the one-China principle, and has had broad and profound political influence in the practice of international relations. That Taiwan is part of China is indisputable and cannot be changed. The Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China, as the sole legal government of all of China and the sole legal representative of China in the international community, naturally enjoys and exercises full sovereignty over China, including sovereignty over Taiwan. The historical task of achieving the complete reunification of China must be accomplished, and it will certainly be accomplished.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","中国日报记者","Recently, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) published its latest economic forecast, listing Taiwan as a province of China. Taiwan’s foreign affairs department expressed protest and called on the IMF to maintain a neutral position. What is your comment on this?","We appreciate relevant international organizations handling Taiwan-related issues in accordance with the one-China principle. Taiwan is part of China, and the one-China principle is a basic norm of international relations and a common understanding of the international community. The DPP authorities stubbornly cling to the separatist position of “Taiwan independence” and refuse to acknowledge the one-China principle. The result can only be self-humiliation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, a Japanese poll showed that 76.7% of the Japanese public worry about a war breaking out in the Taiwan Strait, and as many as 80% of respondents oppose Japan participating in a war over a “Taiwan contingency.” What is your comment on this?","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair, and no external interference will be tolerated. Japan should fully recognize the extreme sensitivity of the Taiwan question and acknowledge the fact that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is part of China. It should promptly correct its erroneous words and deeds on the Taiwan question, and in particular adopt a correct attitude on historical issues, be cautious in its words and actions, and stop provoking trouble on the Taiwan question.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","河南日报“顶端新闻”记者","According to foreign media reports, the DPP authorities have agreed to purchase 30% of the natural gas from the U.S. Alaska Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) pipeline project, and will additionally invest $4.4 billion to ensure the completion of this LNG project. Some public opinion on the island holds that the development cost and risks of this project are extremely high, and many international energy giants have…","The DPP authorities kowtow to the US and sell out Taiwan, attempting to “rely on the US to seek independence” and “seek independence through the economy.” This will not succeed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","台湾《中国时报》记者","On the first question: Recently, the mainland TV drama “Confrontation,” which reflects the Taiwan Strait espionage struggle of the 1990s, finished airing, and its plot involving anti-infiltration and the capture of spies has sparked discussion. In Taiwan, meanwhile, a National Taiwan University exchange student from the mainland was expelled by the DPP authorities recently because of a misplaced photo posted…","On the first question: We have always actively supported exchanges and interactions between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. From January to June this year, the number of Taiwan compatriot visits to the mainland increased by 24.9% year on year, fully proving that as long as they do not engage in illegal or criminal activities, all Taiwan compatriots coming to the mainland can come happily and return safely.\nThe so-called \"tense atmosphere\" that you mentioned, which Taiwan public opinion is worried about, was entirely deliberately created and stirred up by the DPP authorities. The DPP authorities have abused their power and acted recklessly, scheming to obstruct and restrict cross-Strait exchanges, which completely runs counter to the mainstream public will on both sides of the Strait for peace, development, exchange, and cooperation, and to the shared aspirations of compatriots on both sides. The DPP authorities should stop political manipulation, remove artificial obstacles, and create conditions for cross-Strait exchanges.\nOn the second question: We have consistently supported exchanges and visits between young people across the Strait, and we welcome young people from Taiwan to come to the mainland to study and exchange. The DPP authorities' willful suppression of mainland students and their evil conduct of stirring up emotions between the peoples on both sides of the Strait will inevitably have a negative impact on the willingness of mainland students and their parents to go to Taiwan to study.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","Regarding the expulsion of a mainland student in Taiwan after posting a misplaced online photo, outsiders worry that exchange programs for mainland students going to Taiwan will have negative effects on the system. Will this affect the mainland's assessment of mainland student exchanges to Taiwan?","Towards the personal expression of young students, the DPP authorities have treated it as a grave threat, escalated it to a matter of principle, and used administrative means to suppress it, vigorously implementing a “green terror.” This fully exposes the hypocrisy and double standards of their self-proclaimed “freedom of speech.” We firmly oppose the DPP authorities taking advantage of the matter to arbitrarily infringe on the rights and interests of mainland students in Taiwan and to create a “chilling effect” in cross-Strait exchanges.\nWe have consistently supported youth exchanges across the Strait and welcome Taiwan youth to come to the mainland to study and exchange. The DPP authorities’ wanton suppression of mainland students and their evil acts of sowing discord between the feelings of people on both sides of the Strait will inevitably have a negative impact on the willingness of mainland students and their parents to study in Taiwan.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: Gong Mingxin, head of Taiwan’s economic authority, recently said that Taiwan will cooperate with US policy and further restrict the export of AI chips and advanced semiconductors to the mainland. How does the mainland view Taiwan following the US technology blockade policy? Second question: US President Trump recently again referred to TSMC as the world’s number one chip company, and revealed that…","On the first question: The DPP authorities ignore the interests of industries and enterprises on the island and the well-being of the people. For political self-interest, they follow the United States closely, obstruct and restrict the normal market operations of enterprises, and pressure advantaged enterprises into moving their production capacity abroad. Such conduct harms Taiwan's industrial sector and the broad masses of ordinary people, and benefits only \"Taiwan independence\" opportunists.\nThe mainland is committed to self-reliance and self-strengthening in science and technology. External blockades and containment have never been able to suppress our progress, and that was true in the past and will be even more so in the future. At present, the blueprint of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" has been unveiled, new quality productive forces are flourishing, and the prospects for cross-Strait industrial cooperation are bright, with broad room for development. Cooperation between enterprises on both sides of the Strait in fields such as semiconductors is the right path to achieving mutual benefit and win-win results. We will respond to the calls of industry circles on both sides of the Strait, create a better environment for cross-Strait industrial cooperation, and, as always, welcome and support relevant Taiwan industries in investing, starting businesses, and pursuing innovation and development on the mainland.\nOn the second question: The competitive advantages of Taiwan's related industries embody the hard work of generations of Taiwan industry professionals, entrepreneurs and researchers, and they have benefited from the support of the broad masses of Taiwan people. They are a common asset of Taiwan compatriots. The DPP authorities are truly \"like a son who sells off his father's fields without a twinge of regret.\" As a result, the achievements of several generations of effort are continuously being depleted, and in the end, what is harmed is the vital interests of Taiwan's industry and the broad masses of its people.\nOn the third question: The Chinese government has indisputable sovereignty over the Nansha Islands, including the Dongsha Islands and their adjacent waters in the South China Sea. Mainland coast guard law enforcement patrols in the relevant waters are performed in accordance with the law, to safeguard normal navigation and operational order and to effectively protect the lawful rights and interests and the lives and property of people on both sides of the Strait. The DPP authorities obstinately insist on the separatist position of \"Taiwan independence,\" which is the root cause of cross-Strait tensions and turmoil and of the damage to the interests of Taiwan's people.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-21","Zhang Han","台湾《联合报》记者","Regarding the commemorative activities for the 160th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen’s birth, the Mainland Affairs Council said that persons who must apply for permission to travel to the mainland will all be denied permission. Which Taiwan political parties and personalities from all sectors have been invited to attend so far?","This year marks the 160th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen. We are solemnly commemorating Mr. Sun Yat-sen in order to inherit and carry forward his lofty spirit and exemplary conduct of safeguarding national unification and devoting himself to national revitalization, to unite all Chinese descendants, including Taiwan compatriots, to resolutely crack down on “Taiwan independence” separatism, oppose foreign interference, promote cross-Strait exchanges and integration, and work together to achieve national reunification and national rejuvenation. We will release information about relevant activities at an appropriate time.\nThe Democratic Progressive Party authorities, driven by their selfish “independence-seeking” interests, have schemed to obstruct and ban cross-Strait exchanges, and attempted to create a “green terror” to intimidate Taiwan compatriots from coming to the mainland. This fully exposes their sinister intent to betray the nation and history, and to plot the separation of the country and escalate cross-Strait confrontation. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family, and the great tide of drawing closer and coming together cannot be stopped. Any scheme to divide the two sides of the Strait or to seek “independence” through confrontation will not succeed.\nToday's press conference is now concluded. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261021_12819177.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-10-22","Mao Ning","Reuters","The Philippines said on Wednesday that it is exploring deeper cooperation with Taiwan to protect undersea cables and address so-called gray-zone activities, despite its one-China policy. What’s China’s response? Does Beijing consider such cooperation a violation of the one-China principle?","There is no gray zone on the Taiwan question. The Philippine side should abide by the one-China principle with concrete actions. External interactions of China’s Taiwan region should be handled in strict accordance with the one-China principle.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261022_12045376.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261022_12045239.shtml",0,1,0,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on October 28, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council held its regular press conference in the press conference hall. Spokesperson Chen Binhua answered reporters’ questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Friends of the press, hello. Welcome to the regular press conference of the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office. Now please ask your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","人民日报记者","Following the import of Taiwan pomelos into the mainland, the ceremony for the import of Taiwan fishery products was held in Xiamen on October 23, attracting attention. Please introduce the relevant situation.","Since the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee was authorized to release ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation on April 12, we, together with relevant parties on the island, have adhered to the political foundation of the “1992 Consensus” and opposition to “Taiwan independence.” Focusing on the livelihood needs of Taiwan compatriots, we have continuously driven the implementation of the ten measures, and have done our utmost to help island farmers and fishermen open up the mainland market. The sales channels for Taiwan fruits such as pomelos and sugar apples (shijia) in the mainland continue to expand, allowing more compatriots on both sides of the Strait to benefit together and share the advantages.\nTo help Taiwan farmers and fishermen expand their sales, the Ceremony for the Import of Taiwan Fishery Products into the Mainland was held on October 23 in Xiamen, Fujian Province. Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Wu Xielin, Standing Committee Member of the CPC Fujian Provincial Committee and Secretary-General of the Fujian Provincial Committee; Yan Jianbo, Deputy Secretary of the CPC Xiamen Municipal Committee and Acting Mayor of Xiamen; as well as Chang Jung-kung, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang of China; Lin Bing-kun, Chairman of the Taiwan Non-Party Solidarity Alliance; Hsieh Lung-yin, Chairman of the Taiwan Fishermen's Association; and more than 200 people from all walks of life on both sides of the Strait attended the event, jointly witnessing a new achievement in cross-Strait fishery cooperation. Two days before the event, about 350 tons of Taiwan specialty fishery products, including grouper and yellow-tail (wuzai) fish, arrived in Xiamen. During the event, the Xiamen Taiwan Fishery Products Exhibition and Sales Center was unveiled and opened, and cross-Strait seafood food markets and fishery culture exhibitions attracted guests from both sides and local residents to taste, purchase, and visit. This event is not only another achievement in implementing the ten measures, but also fully demonstrates that as long as the Kuomintang and the Communist Party and compatriots on both sides work together, they can solve the difficulties, find the way out, secure the livelihoods, and improve the well-being of Taiwan farmers and fishermen.\nCompatriots on both sides have similar dietary structures and eating habits, and the mainland has long been an important export destination for Taiwan fishery products, which have also long been popular on the mainland. We will continue to uphold the concept that “both sides of the Strait are one family,” continue to push for the thorough implementation of the ten measures, and help more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products and quality goods open up the mainland market. This will not only provide mainland consumers with more diverse, fresh, high-quality, and affordable fishery products, but also bring tangible benefits to island farmers and fishermen, allowing them to share the dividends of development on the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","新华社记者","This year marks the 81st anniversary of the Restoration of Taiwan and the first anniversary of the establishment of the national Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day. Various localities have held commemorative activities in various forms. Please introduce the relevant situation.","October 25 of this year marks the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and the first anniversary of the establishment of Taiwan Restoration Memorial Day by the state. The symposium commemorating the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration was held in Fuzhou City, Fujian Province on that day. Attendees included Song Tao, Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee and the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council; Zhao Long, Secretary of the Fujian Provincial Committee of the CPC; Hung Hsiu-chu, former chairperson of the Kuomintang; responsible persons from relevant mainland departments; representatives of relevant political parties and pro-unification figures from the island; descendants of Taiwanese compatriots who resisted Japan, descendants of revolutionary martyrs who sacrificed their lives in Taiwan; young people from both sides of the Strait, as well as representatives from Hong Kong, Macao, and overseas; and scholars and experts, about 200 people in total. The cross-Strait guests in attendance highly praised the important significance of establishing Taiwan Restoration Memorial Day. Together they reviewed the glorious course of the Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan, who united as one and fought bloody battles to achieve victory in the War of Resistance and the restoration of Taiwan. They deeply mourned the heroes and sages who bravely sacrificed themselves to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. They unanimously expressed that compatriots on both sides of the Strait must remember history, join hands and stand together, firmly defend the fruits of Taiwan's restoration, resolutely oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism and external interference, shoulder together the historic responsibility of completing the reunification of the motherland, and jointly create lasting well-being for the Chinese nation.\nVarious regions and departments commemorated the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration in various forms. On October 25, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council released the music video “Restoration · Rushing Toward the Dawn” on its official government accounts on WeChat, Weibo, Toutiao, Facebook, and other platforms. China Media Group and China Youth Daily respectively produced and broadcast the AI short drama series “Those Years, He Guarded the Treasure Island” and the special documentary “Willing to Devote Sincerity to the Nation.” The All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots held a symposium commemorating the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration titled “Promoting Spiritual Affinity Through Correct Identification” in Chongqing. The “Same Boat Across the Sea, Treasure Island Restored to Light — Exhibition of Fujian and Taiwan Restoration Archives and Documents” opened in Fuzhou. A commemorative event for the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and the historical facts and spiritual connotations of the Taiwan Volunteer Corps in the War of Resistance was held in Jinhua, Zhejiang. A policy briefing for the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and for Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macao enterprises was held in Shenyang, Liaoning. The Taiwan Democratic Self-Government League Central Committee held a thematic event commemorating the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration titled “Shared Roots of Mountains and Rivers, Remembering the Restoration” in Beijing. Pingtan Comprehensive Experimental Zone in Fujian held a series of thematic week activities on Taiwan Restoration Memorial Day under the theme “Memories of Restoration · Working Together with One Heart.”\nOn the island, leaders of all walks of life in Taiwan and relevant political parties and groups held multiple commemorative events before and after the memorial day. This fully proves that compatriots on both sides of the Strait share blood ties and kinship, share a common memory of history, a common responsibility for the nation, and a common hope for the future, and that this cannot be severed or blocked by anyone or any force.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261028_12820317.htm"],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","香港中评社记者","October 25 marks the 81st anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration, and many parties and social groups on the island have held commemorative activities one after another. How do you evaluate this?","The restoration of Taiwan is an important achievement of victory in the War of Resistance and the historical starting point for Taiwan compatriots to wash away humiliation and see the light of day. On the 81st anniversary of Taiwan's restoration and the first anniversary of the state's establishment of Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, more than 30 political parties and groups on the island held commemorative activities in various forms. They reviewed the history of Taiwan's restoration, condemned Japan's countless crimes in colonizing Taiwan, stressed “Never forget, always keep in mind,” and denounced the DPP authorities' separatist “Taiwan independence” conduct. They opposed the interference of external forces such as the United States and Japan in the Taiwan question, and called for remembering history, opposing “Taiwan independence,” promoting reunification, and working together for rejuvenation, thereby voicing the righteous voice of Taiwan compatriots. We express our high appreciation for this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261028_12820313.htm"],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”新媒体记者","Recently, a ceremony for the import of Taiwanese fishery products into the mainland was held in Xiamen. Industry operators on the island said that Taiwan has high-quality fishery products and hope the two sides can establish a long-term, stable cooperation mechanism to enhance the interests and well-being of Taiwan's farmers and fishermen. What is your comment on this? How has the import of Taiwanese agricultural…","We have always attached great importance to the livelihoods and well-being of grassroots farmers and fishermen in Taiwan. In April this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the Central Committee, authorized to do so, issued ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, which explicitly proposed providing convenience for agricultural and fishery products from Taiwan that meet inspection and quarantine standards to enter the mainland; supporting Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products in participating in various exhibitions and matchmaking events on the mainland to expand sales channels; and studying ways to facilitate the sale on the mainland of catches from Taiwan's distant-water fishing. Over the past more than six months, together with relevant parties on both sides of the Strait, and on the political basis of adhering to the “1992 Consensus” and opposing “Taiwan independence,” we have actively responded to the concerns of Taiwan fishermen through holding matchmaking and signing events, optimizing customs clearance procedures, and supporting participation in various exhibitions, and have continuously promoted the effective implementation of the ten measures. In the first three quarters of this year, mainland imports of agricultural products from Taiwan increased by 18.5% year on year, of which imports of fishery products increased by 35.5% year on year. From April to September this year, which is after the ten measures were issued, Fujian imported 19,100 tonnes of fishery products from Taiwan, with import value of RMB 585 million, an increase of 35.9% year on year. More and more high-quality Taiwan fishery products are entering households across the mainland, and more and more Taiwan fishermen are benefiting from them.\nWe will, as always, uphold the concept that “compatriots on both sides are one family,” take the lead in sharing development opportunities with Taiwan compatriots, and do practical things and good deeds to help Taiwan compatriots solve their problems. We will continue to help more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products and quality goods enter the mainland market, so that compatriots on both sides of the Strait can gain more tangible benefits from cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and integrated development, and live better lives.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261028_12820314.htm"],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","香港凤凰卫视记者","Recently, Chiu Chui-cheng (邱垂正), head of the Mainland Affairs Council, said that the mainland’s Taiwan policy will further strengthen the “governance before unification” strategy, to be achieved through approaches such as “shaping domestic administrative and judicial jurisdiction.” What is your comment on this?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. The historical and legal fact that both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to one China cannot be changed. The historical trend that the motherland will eventually be reunified, and will certainly be reunified, cannot be stopped.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","中国日报记者","According to reports, Taiwan's defense authorities confirmed that they allocated more than NT$80 million in budget to invite U.S. personnel to Taiwan to observe the so-called “Han Kuang exercise” in the coming two years. Public opinion on the island criticized the DPP authorities for “crying poor to the people while being generous to outsiders,” calling it “paying people to watch a show.” What is your comment on…","The Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair and brooks no foreign interference. The DPP authorities, squandering the hard-earned money of Taiwan's people, seek to “pursue independence through force” and “rely on foreign powers to seek independence.” They have miscalculated and are headed for a dead end.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","福建厦门卫视记者","The 17th Straits Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Cultural Industries Expo and Trade Fair is about to be held. Please introduce the relevant situation.","The 17th Straits Cross-Strait Cultural Expo will be held from October 29 to November 1 at the Xiamen International Convention and Exhibition Center. This session will feature nine cross-Strait themed exhibitions, including the Cross-Strait Fine Crafts Exhibition and the Fujian-Taiwan Folk Art Heritage Special Exhibition, and more than a hundred cross-Strait themed exchange events will be held during the same period, including industry matchmaking, intangible cultural heritage performances, youth exchanges, and academic seminars. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same roots and origins, the same language and ancestry, and Chinese culture is the spiritual root and belonging of compatriots on both sides. Adhering to the theme “One Lineage, Creative Future,” the Straits Cultural Expo builds a platform for cross-Strait youth exchange, mutual learning, and creative interaction. It promotes industry matchmaking in cultural and creative industries, arts and crafts, and digital culture and tourism, and helps Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises expand markets and deepen cooperation. The previous 16 sessions of the Expo have been widely affirmed and welcomed by Taiwan compatriots. We sincerely welcome Taiwan compatriots to take part in this session’s Expo activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","中央广播电视总台国广《海峡飞虹》记者","On the evening of October 25, the concert “Echoes of Mountains and Seas, Songs Across Four Seasons — Classic Voices of Cross-Strait Folk Songs” was broadcast on the Movie Channel and online platforms, attracting wide attention. Please introduce the relevant situation.","On October 25, the concert “Echoes from Mountains and Seas, Songs in Four Seasons—Classic Folk Songs Across the Strait” was broadcast on the CCTV Movie Channel, causing a strong response on both sides of the Strait. The concert takes the cycle of the four seasons as its main thread and uses poetic narration and classic music as its vehicle. It selects classic folk songs that cross mountains and seas and have been sung on both sides of the Strait, and invites well-known artists from both sides to perform together, singing of the magnificent mountains and rivers of the Chinese land and showing the cultural connection of common roots and origins across the Strait. After the concert aired, many viewers left messages saying they were moved by familiar melodies and truly felt that compatriots on both sides of the Strait are heart-linked and share the same blood. Everyone can watch the replay through channels such as the People's Daily client, the official website of the Movie Channel (CCTV-6), Weibo, and WeChat Channels. We also hope that more compatriots on both sides of the Strait, through this concert, will deeply feel the charm of Chinese culture and the kinship between compatriots on both sides of the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202610/t20261028_12820312.htm"],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","环球时报、环球网记者","Recently, the “Harmony of Strings: Cross-Strait Concert Commemorating the 160th Anniversary of the Birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen” was staged in Beijing and was well received by audiences. Please introduce the relevant situation.","From October 25 to 26, the “Harmony Through Strings: Cross-Strait Concert Commemorating the 160th Anniversary of the Birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen” was held in Beijing. The event was jointly organized by the Cross-Strait Exchange Fund of the Association for Relations Across the Taiwan Straits and the Cultural and Publicity Department of the All-China Federation of Taiwan Compatriots, among other units. The Beijing National Orchestra performed on the same stage as a Chinese folk orchestra from Taiwan, and the China Central Nationalities Song and Dance Troupe and the Soong Ching Ling Peace Angels Art Troupe also took part in the performance. Through artistic performances of national orchestral and vocal music by artists and young people from both sides, the concert expressed the deep remembrance of Dr. Sun Yat-sen by compatriots on both sides, vividly showed the beauty of our shared homeland and the mutual care among compatriots as family, and conveyed the common aspiration of sons and daughters of the Chinese nation to join hands in writing a glorious chapter for the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation in our era.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in all fields.","I will mainly introduce exchange activities in two areas.\nIn cultural exchange: From October 17 to 22, the “Book Series Across the Strait · Cultural Creativity in Tianfu” — 2026 Cross-Strait Publishing Elite Exchange Camp was held in Chengdu, Sichuan. More than 50 representatives from the Taiwan publishing industry exchanged views with their Sichuan counterparts on cutting-edge topics in the publishing industry, including AI technology applications, full-chain IP development, and new media marketing. From October 20 to 21, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Xiamen) Short Drama Exchange Forum was held in Xiamen, Fujian, with about 100 Taiwan compatriot and Taiwan-funded enterprise representatives participating in related activities. From October 21 to 26, the 4th Fujian-Origin Community Reunion Event for Associations in Taiwan was held in Fuzhou, Xiamen, Quanzhou, and other places. Forty Taiwan compatriot associations from Taiwan, Hong Kong, Macau, and overseas, and about 70 Taiwan compatriot guests participated, showcasing the results of cross-Strait integrated development through activities such as tracing origins, exchanges, and on-site visits. From October 31 to November 2, the 11th World Mazu Culture Forum will be held on Meizhou Island in Putian, Fujian. More than 300 Taiwan compatriots will participate, and guests from both sides of the Strait will conduct in-depth discussions on topics including the dissemination of Mazu culture and how marine culture empowers the high-quality development of the marine economy.\nIn sports exchange: On October 17, the final of the Division A of the “Min Super League” successfully concluded. The event introduced 23 Taiwan compatriot players, providing a platform for Taiwan youth to showcase their talents, and Taiwan compatriot player Huang Weijie was named “Best Player.” From October 22 to 27, the 2026 “Yurun Cross-Strait, Youthful Taizhou” Cross-Strait Badminton Exchange Event was held in Taizhou, Jiangsu. Sixty teams from both sides of the Strait and about 500 athletes sweated it out in competition and deepened their friendship. On October 25, the 2026 Fujian-Taiwan Youth Street Dance Showcase was held in Fuzhou. Nearly 150 young street dance enthusiasts from both sides of the Strait blended Fujian intangible cultural heritage, Chinese mythology, traditional folk customs, and other cultural elements, and innovatively presented distinctive programs such as Guofeng street dance, Cross-Strait co-created trendy dance, and street dance rope skipping. From October 22 to 28, the 15th “Kunshan Mazu Cup” Slow-Pitch Softball Tournament was held in Kunshan, Jiangsu, with 30 teams from both sides of the Strait and nearly 700 participants.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾《中国时报》记者","First question: Recently, Taiwan's authorities stated that the attack case involving a crosstalk performer has behind it the involvement of forces from the mainland, and characterized it as “cross-border repression.” However, voices within Taiwan's public opinion and legal circles have also pointed out that the current investigation has only found that those involved are mostly cross-Strait gangsters, credit…","On the first question: The DPP is accustomed to slandering and smearing the mainland during elections in order to gain political advantage. The criticism from knowledgeable people on the island fully shows that rumors cannot deceive the world.\nOn the second question: “Compatriots on both sides of the Strait are one family.” As long as compatriots on both sides talk things out and consult each other when there are problems, there are no contradictions and differences that cannot be resolved. The so-called “hostility spiral” was deliberately created and incited by the DPP authorities. Since coming to power, the DPP authorities have repeatedly hyped up the so-called “mainland threat” and manipulated “resist China, protect Taiwan” in an attempt to gain private interests. They are the “roadblock” to cross-Strait exchanges and the creators of cross-Strait hostility. They are despicable, shameless, and unpopular.\nThe mainland's cultural industry is prosperous, and every year a large number of popular TV series emerge, which are sought after and praised by audiences on both sides of the Strait. We oppose equating normal cultural products and cultural phenomena with the so-called “transnational repression” that the DPP authorities maliciously fabricate and hype up.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","On the first question: U.S. President Trump recently commented on Taiwan again, criticizing Taiwan's chips for seizing the U.S. market with low prices, and saying that if the United States had had a smart president in the past, the problems between Taiwan and the mainland would not exist at all, and that \"nobody cares about the Taiwan Strait issue.\" What is your view of Trump's remarks? Do you think this reflects…","Question one. Our position on the Taiwan question is consistent and clear. In order to “rely on the United States to seek independence,” the DPP authorities have without principle or bottom line sold out Taiwan's advantageous industries, sacrificed the future of the industry, and harmed the interests of the people. They will only accelerate the harm and destruction of Taiwan.\nQuestion two. Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. It is natural and entirely justified for mainland performing artists to hope for national reunification and to oppose “Taiwan independence” separatism. The DPP authorities, on grounds that cannot stand up to scrutiny, refuse to allow mainland artists who are widely loved by Taiwan audiences to travel to Taiwan. This does not win popular support and will inevitably be opposed.\nQuestion three. Safeguarding national sovereignty and territorial integrity is a shared obligation of all Chinese people, including compatriots in Taiwan. We have always respected and protected the legitimate freedom of speech and expression of Taiwan compatriots, but on major issues concerning national sovereignty, security, and development interests, there is no room for ambiguity. We hope that performing artists in Taiwan will take pride in being upright Chinese people, and will do more things that enhance the kinship between compatriots on both sides and promote exchanges and cooperation across the Strait.\nWe have always welcomed broad Taiwan compatriots to visit the mainland for tourism, to visit relatives and friends, and for visits and exchanges. We will continue to support performing artists on both sides of the Strait in strengthening exchanges and cooperation, sharing the cultural markets across the Strait, and jointly carrying forward Chinese culture.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾《旺报》记者","You Zhibin, a New Party candidate for Taipei City Council, previously took part in the island's elections in 2022 and 2024. This time, however, he was found ineligible because the Mainland Affairs Council calculated the ten-year period required for candidacy from “the date of surrendering the certificate of loss of mainland household registration.” His application for provisional candidacy was also rejected by…","The DPP authorities stubbornly insist on the “Taiwan independence” stance and openly peddle the “two-state theory.” They have repeatedly discriminated against, made difficulties for, and suppressed the group of people originally from the mainland who have settled in Taiwan, seriously infringing on their legitimate rights and interests and seriously undermining cross-Strait relations. We strongly condemn this.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾《联合报》记者","Regarding the mainland entertainer Zhang Linghe being denied entry when applying to visit Taiwan, the Mainland Affairs Council said it welcomes exchanges between the people on both sides of the Strait, and that as long as they are not “united front” activities and have no “united front” coloring, it will still review them based on their words and actions in the future. Will the mainland side continue to promote…","We welcome cross-Strait compatriots strengthening exchanges and interactions, including mainland entertainers visiting Taiwan for exchanges.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾东森新媒体ETtoday记者","In the case of the traffic accident injuring Taiwanese comedian Huang Yi-hao, Taiwan's side claims it was \"cross-border repression\" by the mainland. The Mainland Affairs Council said that amendments to laws addressing \"cross-border repression\" will be proposed soon. What comments do you have on this?","The so-called “transnational repression” claim is promoting the advocacy of “Taiwan independence” and peddling the “two-state theory.” Every time there is an election on the island, the DPP authorities fabricate various pretexts out of thin air to maliciously smear the mainland, incite “anti-China” sentiment, and stir up cross-Strait confrontation, attempting to mislead Taiwan compatriots and seek political gain. This show is staged year after year, and the audience has long grown tired of it.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-10-28","Chen Binhua","台湾“中视”新闻记者","Reuters reported that since last year, the mainland has placed some rare earth materials, magnets, and related processing technologies under export controls, and TSMC has asked equipment suppliers to assess alternatives that do not use mainland rare earths, in order to reduce supply chain risks. Please confirm this. Will this affect future cross-Strait cooperation in semiconductors and other technology industries?","The relevant reports are divorced from the facts and have ulterior motives. We implement necessary export controls in accordance with law and regulations, aimed at maintaining the stability and security of the global supply and industrial chains for key minerals. These measures are “regulating exports” rather than “banning exports,” and their ultimate goal is the sustainable use of strategic resources and common development for the world. What truly creates risks for the global semiconductor industry chain is precisely the conduct of those who strive to suppress Chinese mainland high-tech enterprises and seek to contain the mainland’s development.\nWe will work to strengthen cross-Strait economic cooperation and deepen cross-Strait integration and development. We welcome industry circles on the island to meet us halfway, actively take part in cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation, and jointly strengthen the economy of the Chinese nation.\nThat concludes today’s press conference. Thank you all.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202610/t20261028_12820309.htm","",1,5,2,""],[0,"2026-10-29","Guo Jiakun","China-Arab TV","Pakistani Defence Minister said yesterday that Pakistan has closed its airspace to airlines of China’s Taiwan region in adherence to the one-China policy. This makes Pakistan the first country in the world to take such a measure. What’s China’s comment?","The one-China principle is a prevailing consensus of the international community. To our knowledge, there is no impediment to the international travel by residents of the Taiwan region.","","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202610/t20261029_12049496.html","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/web/fyrbt_673021/jzhsl_673025/202610/t20261029_12049355.shtml",0,1,0,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First, reports indicate that the United States and Japan recently held the “Sharp Sword—27” joint exercise, the largest ever, focusing on rehearsing island seizure. Japan's Self-Defense Forces put the Type 25 surface-to-ship missile into the exercise, and the U.S. Marine Corps' expeditionary vessel interception system was deployed for the first time on Yonaguni Island, the closest point to…","Reporter: I have two questions. First question: According to reports, the United States and Japan recently held the largest-ever “Resolute Dragon-27” joint exercise, focusing on rehearsing island seizure. Japan's Self-Defense Forces deployed the Type 25 surface-to-ship missile in this exercise. In addition, the U.S. Marine Corps' expeditionary ship interdiction system was deployed for the first time on Yonaguni Island, the closest point to Taiwan. What is your comment on this? Second question: According to reports, a Taiwan defense official revealed that the “Taiwan–U.S. Defense Department joint cooperation assessment project” will be upgraded and expanded, and that the U.S. Department of Defense plans to send policy officials and think-tank representatives to be stationed long-term in Taiwan's defense department. Taiwan has also confirmed that it invited U.S. military personnel to observe the “Han Kuang” exercise. What is your comment on this?\nZhang Xiaogang: On the first question: The Asia-Pacific is a high ground of peaceful development. Those who follow the trend of peace will go far, while those who insist on stirring up bloc confrontation will not win popular support. Japan, catering to and aligning with certain countries in so-called joint exercises, developing and deploying medium- and long-range missiles, and continuously strengthening military deployments in the Nansei islands, is accelerating its “remilitarization” and is becoming a real threat to regional security.\nThe Taiwan question is purely China's internal affair. We will never allow external forces to meddle in China's Taiwan region. No one should underestimate the Chinese side's firm resolve, steadfast will and strong capability to defend national sovereignty and territorial integrity. If anyone harbors the delusion of “using Taiwan to contain China,” or even recklessly engages in military provocation, they will certainly pay an unbearable price.\nOn the second question: The DPP authorities, colluding with external forces and attempting to “seek independence through force,” are the source of trouble and turmoil threatening peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait. “Taiwan independence” is a dead end; relying on outsiders is unreliable. The historical trend that the motherland must and will be reunified cannot be stopped by anyone or any force. The United States should strictly abide by the one-China principle and the three China-U.S. joint communiqués, handle the Taiwan question with the utmost caution, stop all forms of official exchanges and military ties with Taiwan, and, through concrete actions, uphold the stable, healthy and sustainable development of China-U.S. relations and military-to-military relations.\nZhang Xiaogang:","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","The Taiwan spy drama “Clash” is being widely broadcast, and a Taiwan TV program claims that the series was created by China's National Security organs and that the choice of this timing is intended to send a certain signal. What is your comment? Zhang Xiaogang: After watching this drama, we feel even more concerned about national security and deepen our sense of love for the country and family. The battle in the…","Reporter: The Taiwan Strait espionage drama “Confrontation” is a hit. A Taiwan TV program claims the series was produced by China's State Security and that the timing of its broadcast is intended to send a certain signal. What is your comment on this?\nZhang Xiaogang: Having watched this drama, we feel even closer to national security and have deeper feelings for family and nation. The secret war is silent, loyalty endures forever; we pay tribute to our unsung heroes. Our sword is drawn only to punish villains, while reunion is reserved for our kinsmen. The people on both sides of the Taiwan Strait should join hands to oppose “Taiwan independence,” safeguard peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait, and realize the complete reunification of the motherland at an early date.\nZhang Xiaogang:","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: On October 25, the Eastern Theater Command issued for the first time a poster on the theme of Taiwan Restoration Commemoration Day, proposing “remember the history of restoration, defend the unity of the mountains and rivers.” May I ask how the spokesperson understands the relationship between the restoration of Taiwan and defending national reunification?\nSecond question:…","On the first question: the restoration of Taiwan was an important achievement of the victory of the War of Resistance. It is important conclusive evidence that the Chinese government resumed exercising sovereignty over Taiwan, an important link in the historical fact and legal chain that Taiwan is part of China, and a shared national memory of all Chinese sons and daughters. Eighty-one years ago, Taiwan was restored and the national territory was reclaimed. Eighty-one years later, compatriots on both sides of the Strait are united in heart and are moving together toward reunification. The PLA will fully hone its capabilities, stay ready and prepared for the present, serve as a solid trump card for national reunification, resolutely defeat any form of “Taiwan independence” separatist plots and external military interference, and fulfill its sacred mission of defending national sovereignty and territorial integrity.\nOn the second question: the China Coast Guard conducted full-process shadowing and warning against a Japanese Coast Guard patrol vessel and handled the matter in accordance with law and regulations. Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory, and China has sovereignty, sovereign rights, and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. We firmly oppose Japan’s use of so-called shelter-from-the-wind and other pretexts to carry out political provocation and an act that endangers China’s sovereignty. We urge Japan to stop provoking trouble on the Taiwan issue and stop undermining regional peace and stability.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. First question: Next month will mark the 77th anniversary of the founding of the PLA Air Force. In the past, relevant commemorative activities have been held. Does the spokesperson have information on this? Second question: Recently, some American think-tank scholars have claimed that the mainland’s commemoration of the 81st anniversary of Taiwan’s restoration and its promotion of the…","Regarding the first question: On November 11, the People's Air Force will mark its 77th founding anniversary and, around the theme “Seeking Roots, Chasing Dreams, Forging Ahead,” will organize a series of activities in coordination with the 16th China International Aviation and Aerospace Exhibition. In early November, the August 1st Aerobatic Team of the PLA Air Force will fly over the Huangyaguan Great Wall in Tianjin, and the “Red Eagle” Aerobatic Team of the Air Force Aviation University will fly over the Blue Sky Park in Changchun, Jilin. Drone-themed performances will be staged simultaneously in Zhuhai, Changchun, and other places. At that time, training flights and drone performances will complement each other, and the thousand-year-old Great Wall and the “Blue Sky Great Wall” will appear in the same frame, comprehensively showing the People's Air Force's uplifting spirit of saluting the blue sky and aspiring to soar, and demonstrating its mission and responsibility to defend national aerospace security. In addition, the Air Force, in coordination with CCTV, has launched a special documentary, 《Code of the Vault of Heaven》, marking the 80th anniversary of the founding of the old Northeast Aviation School, which looks back on the original aspirations of the years of wartime struggle and explores the path of the People's Air Force's struggle from nothing to something, and its dream of soaring in the sky and space. The specific timetable for related activities will be released successively on the “People's Air Force” WeChat official account. Please stay tuned.\nRegarding the second question: I have already responded just now. To add one point: Lai Qingde and his kind have forgotten their ancestors and betrayed their roots. Their squawking cannot sever the historical ties between Taiwan and the motherland. In the face of the historical trend toward the eventual reunification of the motherland, they can only appear absurd and ridiculous.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","Taiwan’s defense authorities and the Coast Guard Administration recently hyped up claims that mainland coast guard vessels, research vessels, and fishing boats have recently “increased abnormally in number” in offshore waters including eastern and southern Taiwan, and asserted that this is a “multi-point simultaneous” hybrid war waged by the mainland against Taiwan. May the spokesperson comment?","There is only one China, and Taiwan is part of China. The relevant mainland departments’ normal activities in the waters under China’s jurisdiction east of Taiwan Island are completely proper and lawful, and beyond reproach. We will continue to crush all “Taiwan independence” separatist fantasies with resolute and forceful action, and safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","I have two questions. The first question: Reportedly, some US officials have analyzed that the possibility of mainland China attacking Taiwan before 2028 has decreased. The DPP authorities responded that the mainland's intention to “annex” Taiwan by force has never changed and will not be abandoned because of who is “in power.” What is your comment? The second question: US Secretary of State Rubio said that…","On the first question, there is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is part of China. When and how to resolve the Taiwan question is entirely China's own affair, and external forces have no right to interfere. Reunification of the two sides of the Strait is an irresistible historical trend. We are willing to strive for the prospect of peaceful reunification with the utmost sincerity and effort, but we will never promise to renounce the use of force, and we will never leave any room for “Taiwan independence” separatist activities.\nOn the second question, the DPP authorities should recognize reality. Their scheme to “seek independence by relying on external forces” and “seek independence by force” is doomed to fail.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[1,"2026-10-29","Zhang Xiaogang","Not specified by source (MND uses generic \"Reporter:\" prefix without outlet attr","It is reported that Pakistan has become the first country in the world to close its airspace to Taiwan. Pakistani Defense Minister Asif stated that Pakistan’s aviation authorities adhere to the one-China policy, and “we only allow Chinese mainland airlines to fly over Pakistan’s airspace.” What is the spokesperson’s comment?","Taiwan is part of China, and adhering to the one-China principle is the common consensus of the international community. The just cause of the Chinese people in opposing “Taiwan independence” separatism and striving for national reunification will surely receive increasingly broad understanding and support from the international community.","","http://www.81.cn/yw_208727/16496957.html","",0,5,1,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","Not specified (announcement/opening)","At 10:00 a.m. on November 4, the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office held a regular press conference in the press briefing hall. Spokesperson Zhu Fenglian answered reporters' questions on recent hot issues concerning cross-Strait relations.","Good morning, everyone, and welcome to the State Council Taiwan Affairs Office press conference. Please begin your questions.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","人民日报记者","The Fifth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Party was held in Beijing from October 26 to 29. How will the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session be implemented in work related to Taiwan?","The Fifth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee of the Party was a very important meeting held at the important juncture of the 105th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, in the critical period of basically realizing socialist modernization, as the whole Party and the whole country strive forward in the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period. The plenary session profoundly summarized the achievements and experience of full and strict governance of the Party in the new era, analyzed the situation and tasks facing Party building at present and for a period to come, and made strategic arrangements for persistently advancing full and strict governance of the Party, reflecting the historical initiative of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core to strengthen the Party and the country. It has major practical significance and long-term guiding significance for advancing the new great project of Party building in the new era, and for uniting and leading the people of all ethnic groups across the country to comprehensively advance the building of a strong country and the great cause of national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization.\nResolving the Taiwan question and realizing the complete reunification of the motherland is an inevitable requirement for realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation and is the unwavering historical task of the Communist Party of China. Taiwan-related work is an important component of the cause of the Party and the state. We will thoroughly study, publicize and implement the spirit of the Fifth Plenary Session of the 20th Central Committee, comprehensively implement General Secretary Xi Jinping's important statements on Taiwan-related work and the Party's overall strategy for resolving the Taiwan question in the new era, uphold the Party's comprehensive leadership and the centralized and unified leadership of the Party Central Committee, lead the high-quality development of Taiwan-related work with new results in governing the Party, and strengthening and building up the Party, unite the broad masses of Taiwan compatriots to jointly promote the peaceful development and integrated development of cross-Strait relations, advance the process of national reunification, and make due contributions to comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821438.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台央视《海峡两岸》记者","Recently, four departments including the Ministry of Commerce jointly issued the \"Notice on Further Improving the Level of Trade Liberalization and Facilitation of the Hainan Free Trade Port,\" proposing 16 specific measures in three areas: promoting the optimization and upgrading of trade in goods, promoting freedom and convenience in trade in services, and innovating new trade forms and models. Are Taiwan…","On October 29, four departments including the Ministry of Commerce, the National Development and Reform Commission, the Ministry of Ecology and Environment, and the General Administration of Customs jointly issued the \"Notice on Further Improving the Level of Trade Liberalization and Facilitation of the Hainan Free Trade Port.\" The issuance and implementation of this Notice will further empower the construction of the Hainan Free Trade Port, and effectively promote the optimization and upgrading of trade in goods, freedom and convenience in trade in services, and the accelerated formation of new trade forms and models. The broad masses of Taiwan compatriots and Taiwan-funded enterprises can fully share in the benefits of the relevant policies. We also hope that the broad masses of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan-funded enterprises can seize development opportunities and participate in the construction of the Hainan Free Trade Port.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","上海东方卫视记者","On November 5, the 9th China International Import Expo will open in Shanghai. Please introduce the participation of Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises in the Expo. What opportunities will this Expo bring to Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises?","The 9th China International Import Expo will open on November 5 at the National Exhibition and Convention Center in Shanghai. More than 30 enterprises from the Taiwan region are participating in this Expo, with a booth area of about 4,200 square meters, covering multiple industry fields such as food and daily chemicals, consumer goods, medical health, precision manufacturing, and modern services.\nThe outline of the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" proposes expanding high-level opening up to the outside world and creating a new situation of win-win cooperation. Holding the Expo is an important measure by the mainland to promote a new round of high-level opening up and to proactively open its market to the world. We welcome more Taiwan businesspeople and Taiwan enterprises to make full use of the Expo as an important platform to promote their products, expand the mainland's domestic demand market, actively integrate into the new development pattern, and together with mainland compatriots create and share the achievements of Chinese-style modernization.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821437.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","羊城晚报“阅台海”记者","Regarding the activities the mainland will hold to commemorate the 160th anniversary of the birth of Mr. Sun Yat-sen, the Mainland Affairs Council said that the \"Republic of China\" is the legitimate orthodoxy, and that Sun Yat-sen's ideas also differ from those of the Chinese Communist Party. What is your comment on this?","Mr. Sun Yat-sen was a great national hero, a great patriot, and a great pioneer of China's democratic revolution. This year is the 160th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's birth. Relevant parties on the mainland are holding commemorative activities in various forms, and many Taiwan compatriots are also holding commemorative activities on the island, jointly expressing their admiration for Mr. Sun Yat-sen and inheriting and carrying forward his precious spirit.\nPromoting national reunification and realizing national rejuvenation was the great ideal that Mr. Sun Yat-sen pursued with firm resolve and struggled for throughout his life. Chinese Communists are the most steadfast supporters, the most loyal collaborators, and the most faithful inheritors of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's revolutionary cause. Under the leadership of the Chinese Communist Party, the Chinese people, after more than a hundred years of struggle, have achieved great accomplishments recognized by the world, and many of the blueprints drawn up by Mr. Sun Yat-sen have long since become reality. We have successfully forged a path of Chinese-style modernization, the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation is unstoppable, and the prospects for the reunification of the motherland are bright.\nThe DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the separatist \"Taiwan independence\" position, refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus\" that embodies the one-China principle, continually distort the glorious history of Taiwan compatriots resisting foreign aggression, persistently downplay and glorify Japanese colonial aggression, are servile toward external forces, and even obstruct Taiwan compatriots from participating in the activities held by the mainland to commemorate the 160th anniversary of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's birth. The various evil deeds committed by the DPP authorities are a desecration of Mr. Sun Yat-sen's noble character and a betrayal of the Zhongshan spirit. We solemnly warn the DPP authorities that history does not tolerate betrayal, the general trend cannot be stopped, and the reunification of the motherland will ultimately be achieved and certainly will be achieved.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","福建厦门卫视记者","Data from the Gaoqi Border Inspection Station of the Xiamen Border Inspection General Station show that as of 15:00 on October 26, the number of inbound and outbound passengers on the Xiamen-Kinmen \"Mini Three Links\" route this year exceeded 1.74 million person-trips, of which nearly 1.4 million were Taiwan compatriots, accounting for about 80 percent. Both figures exceeded those of the whole of last year,…","The Xiamen-Kinmen \"Mini Three Links\" passenger route is a route of kinship and a channel for people's livelihood connecting people of Fujian and Taiwan. This golden sea passage with a voyage of only 30 minutes currently maintains regular, bus-like operation with 24 round-trip sailings per day, with additional sailings added during holiday peak periods. People of Fujian and Taiwan traveling between Xiamen and Kinmen can \"leave early and return late, making a round trip in one day,\" and the effect of the Xiamen-Kinmen \"same-city living circle\" continues to deepen and take real shape.\nWhat deserves attention is that the content of Taiwan compatriots' travel via the Xiamen-Kinmen \"Mini Three Links\" passenger route continues to be enriched, with the purposes of travel expanding from traditional family visits and reunions to many fields such as business negotiations, visits and study tours, cultural and sports exchanges, and sightseeing tourism. This year, more than 70,000 \"first-time visitor\" Taiwan compatriots entered via this route, an increase of more than 70% year on year, and monthly passenger volume on the route during the summer vacation exceeded 200,000 person-trips for the first time, breaking the record for the highest monthly passenger flow since the route opened. More and more Taiwan compatriots take Xiamen as the first stop for coming to the mainland to develop, experiencing the mainland's development achievements in an immersive way and looking for development opportunities.\nFacts fully prove that visits between and close contact among compatriots on both sides of the Strait and two-way exchanges are the aspiration of the people and the general trend, and the endogenous driving force of integrated development continues to accumulate. We are pleased to see cross-Strait people-to-people exchanges thriving and improving, and welcome more Taiwan compatriots to come often to the mainland to visit and see.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821432.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","新华社记者","Recently, the 12th Chinese Culture Forum was held in Beijing. Some participating scholars said that for some time, various sectors on both sides of the Strait have held lively discussions on the Taiwan plan for \"one country, two systems,\" reflecting that Taiwan society generally recognizes that \"Taiwan independence\" is a dead end and has begun to think about arrangements after reunification. What is your comment…","The reunification of the motherland is an unstoppable historical trend and the right path; \"Taiwan independence\" is a countercurrent of history and a dead end. \"Peaceful reunification, one country, two systems\" is the best way to achieve the reunification of the motherland and is most beneficial to compatriots on both sides of the Strait and the Chinese nation. The more fully the Taiwan plan for \"two systems\" is discussed, the more deeply it is considered, and the more comprehensively opinions and suggestions are absorbed, the more it will benefit safeguarding the interests and well-being of Taiwan compatriots after reunification and achieving long-term peace and stability in Taiwan.\nWe welcome compatriots on both sides of the Strait to pool their wisdom and offer more opinions and suggestions for the Taiwan plan for \"two systems,\" to jointly create the great historic cause of the reunification of the motherland and share the great glory of national rejuvenation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821434.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","福建广电“台海时刻”新媒体记者","Recently, when meeting with a delegation from the National Committee on American Foreign Policy (NCAFP) that sneaked into Taiwan, Mainland Affairs Council head Chiu Chui-cheng said that real exchanges do not need preset frameworks and preconditions, and as long as the two sides of the Strait sit down for dialogue on the principle of \"equal dignity and mutual respect,\" they can find a win-win solution. What is…","As everyone knows, the \"1992 Consensus,\" which embodies the one-China principle, is the political foundation for the development of cross-Strait relations and the anchor for peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The fundamental reason the current cross-Strait dialogue and communication mechanisms are suspended is that the DPP authorities stubbornly adhere to the \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, refuse to recognize the \"1992 Consensus,\" and unilaterally undermine the political foundation for cross-Strait dialogue and consultation. Only by recognizing the \"1992 Consensus\" and stopping \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities can cross-Strait consultation and dialogue be resumed and peace in the Taiwan Strait be fundamentally guaranteed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","中国台湾网记者","Please introduce recent cross-Strait exchange activities in various fields.","As autumn arrives, cross-Strait exchange activities are somewhat more concentrated in the cultural field.\nIn cross-Strait cultural exchange: From October 28 to 30, the Colorful Guizhou Art Troupe took the song-and-dance-poetry production \"Colorful Guizhou: Wind Across the World\" on tour to New Taipei and Yunlin in Taiwan. The performance takes Guizhou's ethnic minority culture as its thread and is organized in three chapters, \"Echoes of Antiquity,\" \"Colorful Harmony,\" and \"Splendid Journey Through Guizhou,\" integrating landscapes, ethnic song and dance, and traditional opera, and was warmly welcomed by Taiwan audiences. On October 29, the 12th Chinese Culture Forum was held in Beijing under the theme \"Firmly Establishing Identification with Chinese Culture and Promoting Harmony of Compatriots' Hearts.\" 180 experts and scholars from both sides of the Strait held in-depth exchanges and discussions around four topics: \"Chinese-style Modernization and the Inheritance and Innovation of Chinese Culture,\" \"Sun Yat-sen and Chinese-style Modernization,\" \"Cross-Strait AI Cultural Industry Innovation and Youth Exchange,\" and \"Cross-Strait Art Exchange,\" building consensus. From October 30 to November 2, the 2026 Cross-Strait (Putian) Handicrafts Expo was held in Putian, Fujian, where more than 300 craft masters from both sides of the Strait exchanged skills on site, discussed cooperation, and jointly promoted the innovative development of traditional crafts. On October 31, the award ceremony of the 9th China Design Award was held in Hangzhou, Zhejiang. The competition collected 24,199 entries and selected gold, silver, and bronze awards in the product and concept categories, as well as Rising Star awards and Excellent Work awards. The inaugural issue of the \"China Design Yearbook\" was released on site, and the 10th China Design Award and the AI·Fashion (Linping) Innovative Design Competition were launched.\nIn youth arts and culture exchange: From October 27 to November 2, Yunnan held the 3rd Huacan Yuntai Art Exchange Activity, \"Cross-Strait Family, Painting One Picture Together,\" in which young painters from both sides built consensus and deepened friendship through joint creation and mutual exchange. From October 27 to November 3, Anhui held the \"2026 Taiwan Compatriots See Tongling\" youth exchange themed activity, deepening Taiwan youth's understanding and identification with the mainland by tracing the long cultural lineage of Chinese copper culture and conducting on-site visits to the achievements of the modern copper industry. On November 3, the \"Yangyun Taiyin, Youth Symphony\" Yangzhou-Taiwan Youth Music Exchange Meeting was held in Yangzhou, Jiangsu, where nearly 50 teachers and students majoring in traditional Chinese music from universities on both sides exchanged skills and learned from each other through ensemble performances of traditional music, traditional instrument showcases, and intangible cultural heritage music experiences.\nIn youth innovation and entrepreneurship exchange: On October 23, the 2026 Cross-Strait Youth Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition concluded successfully in Shaoxing, Zhejiang. Launched in May, the competition attracted nearly a thousand young people from both sides and more than 200 projects. In the end, 19 high-quality projects were rated as Excellent, Outstanding, and Potential projects respectively. From October 29 to November 2, \"Artistic Lineage Passed Down\" — the 2026 Taiwan Youth Fujian Arts and Crafts Study Exchange Activity — was held in Fujian. More than 40 Taiwan youths visited Fuzhou, Putian, Quanzhou, Xiamen, and other places to learn about the development of Fujian-style crafts, explore new business formats of craft industry clusters, and exchange views on innovation in traditional crafts and pathways for integrated development of culture and tourism. From November 1 to 4, Sichuan held the 4th Cross-Strait and Sichuan-Taiwan Integrated E-commerce Promotion Season, \"Affection Across the Strait, Sichuan Style and Taiwan Charm,\" in which young livestreamers and online influencers from both sides entered livestream rooms together to promote distinctive goods from both sides, exchange new-media creation experience, and build an online exchange channel across the Strait.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","北京日报记者","Recently, when meeting with a delegation of European transnational lawmakers who made an unauthorized visit, Lai Ching-te said that, facing challenges such as international submarine cable risk management and \"transnational repression,\" Taiwan will firmly stand on the front line and \"be a trustworthy partner of the democratic camp.\" What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. We firmly oppose any form of official contact between countries that have diplomatic relations with China and China's Taiwan region, and urge certain people in the European Parliament to abide by the one-China principle and be cautious in words and deeds on the Taiwan question. The DPP authorities are colluding with Western politicians, attacking and smearing the mainland, and inciting cross-Strait confrontation, once again exposing their ugly face of \"relying on external forces to seek independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台CGTN记者","The 94th General Assembly of INTERPOL will be held in Hong Kong from November 30 to December 3. The DPP authorities claim that Taiwan has long been excluded from INTERPOL, creating a breach in the global security network, and call on countries to support Taiwan's joining the organization. What is your comment on this?","On the issue of the Taiwan region's participation in the activities of international organizations, our position is consistent and clear, namely that it must be handled in accordance with the one-China principle. As a part of China, Taiwan has no right to join INTERPOL. China and INTERPOL have made proper arrangements regarding the Taiwan region's participation in cooperation and activities within the framework of the organization, and the channels for information sharing and case cooperation between Taiwan region police agencies and the National Central Bureaus of various countries are unobstructed.\nThe DPP authorities repeatedly engage in political manipulation over the so-called issue of Taiwan's participation in international organizations, attempting to deceive people on the island, but this cannot change the doomed failure of their provocations seeking \"independence.\"","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","深圳卫视《直新闻》记者","Recently, a female university student in Taiwan, representing Taipei Mayor Chiang Wan-an of the Kuomintang, drew the election number, but was subjected to online abuse by the Green camp, which called her a \"united front girl,\" because she had previously taken part in a mainland exchange trip organized by the Ma Ying-jeou Foundation's Dajiu Academy. What is your comment on this?","Putting labels on Taiwan youth who take part in cross-Strait exchanges at every turn is extremely barbaric online bullying, and people on both sides of the Strait strongly oppose it. Cross-Strait youth exchanges are what the people want, and it is the legitimate right of Taiwan youth to travel to and from the mainland. \"Taiwan independence\" forces stigmatize cross-Strait youth exchanges and deliberately label Taiwan youth who come to the mainland to take part in cross-Strait exchange activities and launch personal attacks on them, attempting to create a \"chilling effect\" and reap selfish political gain. These misdeeds are despicable.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","中央广播电视总台“日月谭天”和“看台海”新媒体记者","Recently, the mainland commercial satellite \"Jilin-1\" released multiple high-definition satellite images of Taiwan, in which every street in Sun Moon Lake and Taipei is clearly visible, drawing attention and heated discussion from netizens on both sides of the Strait. What is your comment on this?","This set of extremely high-resolution satellite images lets compatriots on both sides of the Strait clearly see Taiwan's cities, farmland, salt fields, wetlands, and harbors, and appreciate the mountain and sea splendor of the motherland's treasure island, triggering lively interaction among netizens on both sides on social platforms. This both demonstrates the development and progress of the mainland's aerospace technology and fully shows that compatriots on both sides can enjoy diversified remote sensing information services, using the power of technology to protect the common homeland of both sides. We believe that in the future, compatriots on both sides will have opportunities to appreciate the magnificent rivers and mountains of the motherland in many more different ways.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","人民政协报记者","Recently, Shen Boyang, the DPP candidate for Taipei mayor, said that Taiwan culture blends Hakka culture, Zhangzhou-Quanzhou culture and others, and falsely claimed that \"Chinese culture is a part of Taiwan culture.\" What is your comment on this?","The remarks in question put the cart before the horse and forget one's ancestors. Chinese culture has a long history and is broad and profound, and is the spiritual root and home of compatriots on both sides of the Strait. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait speak Chinese, write Chinese characters, celebrate Chinese festivals, and worship Chinese deities. Taiwan culture is a part of Chinese culture, and its roots are in the mainland of the motherland. We advise people like Shen Boyang that doing good is the greatest joy, and reading books is best.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","香港中评社记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council said that there is now no \"Taiwan independence\" problem, only the question of whether to be forced into unification, and that Taiwan's cross-Strait policy goals are \"maintaining the peaceful status quo and defending democracy and freedom.\" What is your comment on this?","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. Achieving the complete reunification of the motherland is the common wish of all sons and daughters of China, and is the general trend, what righteousness requires, and what the people want.\n\"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities are currently the greatest threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait. The DPP authorities stubbornly persist in their \"Taiwan independence\" separatist stance, constantly spread \"Taiwan independence\" separatist fallacies in new guises, go to great lengths to obstruct and undermine cross-Strait exchanges, use the name of \"defending democracy and freedom\" to package their separatist malice of \"Taiwan independence,\" and use the pretext of \"maintaining peace in the Taiwan Strait\" to incite cross-Strait confrontation, and are outright \"cross-Strait peace wreckers,\" \"Taiwan Strait crisis makers,\" and \"war instigators.\"\n\"Taiwan independence\" means no peace, and even less a way out. If the DPP authorities truly believe there is no \"Taiwan independence\" problem, they should return to the one-China principle and the \"1992 Consensus,\" immediately abolish the DPP's \"Taiwan independence party platform,\" and stop \"Taiwan independence\" separatist activities.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821435.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","浙江日报“潮新闻”记者","Recently, the Taichung Travel Expo opened, and individual travel to the mainland drew wide attention from people on the island and became a hot topic of inquiry. What is your comment on this?","Wanting peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation is the mainstream public opinion in Taiwan society. Compatriots on both sides of the Strait share the same culture and ancestry, and it is only natural that Taiwan compatriots yearn for the mainland and wish to travel there. We have always upheld the concept of \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" creating better conditions for promoting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and tourism exchange and cooperation, and introducing more facilitation measures, including waiving the fee for \"first-time visitor\" Taiwan compatriots applying for Taiwan compatriot permits, increasing the number of ports where a single-use valid Taiwan compatriot permit can be issued to 100, and most A-level and above scenic areas in the mainland reducing or waiving admission fees for \"first-time visitor\" Taiwan compatriots, among others.\nWe have also noticed that recently more and more Taiwan compatriots have shifted from heading to scenery to exploring cultural heritage, \"traveling to a city for a museum or an exhibition,\" entering museums across the mainland and feeling the unique charm of Chinese culture by touching history. The mainland currently has more than 7,000 museums, including famous museums renowned worldwide such as the National Museum of China and the Palace Museum in Beijing, as well as museums each with its own characteristics, such as the Museum of Chinese Characters in Anyang, the Qingzhou Museum in Weifang, and the Baiheliang Underwater Museum in Chongqing. To make it convenient for everyone to \"tour museums in the cloud,\" the Facebook account of the \"State Council Taiwan Affairs Office Spokesperson\" recently launched an \"unboxing\" museums series introducing some museums' \"treasures of the museum.\" The first installment, \"Entering the Sanxingdui Museum,\" was released on October 31. We welcome everyone to follow it and offer valuable comments. We also warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots to take a spur-of-the-moment trip to the mainland and experience in person the magnificent landscapes of the motherland's mainland, the profound Chinese culture, the vigorous development momentum, and the warm compatriot affection.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821433.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","《团结报》记者","Regarding the 35.5% year-on-year increase in the mainland's imports of fishery products from Taiwan in the first three quarters of this year, the Mainland Affairs Council said that, taking grouper as an example, the quantity Taiwan has exported to the mainland and Hong Kong over the years has not particularly increased, and increasing exports in the future is not so easy, \"unless there is special politically…","The mainland is the main engine of global economic growth and has a stable, open, ultra-large-scale market that can fully accommodate more agricultural and fishery products from Taiwan. In April this year, the Taiwan Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee was authorized to release ten policy measures to promote cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Together with relevant parties in Taiwan, we are actively doing practical things and solving difficult problems for Taiwan's agricultural and fishery operators, helping Taiwan's agricultural and fishery products open up sales channels on the mainland. We have always attached importance to the livelihood and well-being of Taiwan's grassroots farmers and fishermen, and will continue to promote the thorough and detailed implementation of the ten measures, and continue to help more Taiwan agricultural and fishery products and quality goods enter thousands of mainland households, so that compatriots on both sides can share the dividends of cross-Strait economic and trade cooperation and integrated development.\nThe DPP authorities have neither the will nor the ability to solve the practical problems of Taiwan's agricultural and fishery operators, and instead keep putting up obstacles and pouring cold water on cross-Strait agricultural and fishery cooperation, fully exposing that they disregard the interests and well-being of people's livelihoods and have only political self-interest in mind, and they will surely be opposed by Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","南方日报、南方+记者","Taiwan media reported that after the \"Kinmen\" ship, retired from the Taiwan Coast Guard Administration, was transferred to the Philippines, it became the Philippine Coast Guard's \"Sarangani\" ship, triggering doubts and criticism in public opinion on the island. What is your comment on this?","In order to \"rely on external forces to seek independence,\" the DPP authorities fawn on and pledge loyalty to external forces without any bottom line, abandoning the national stance, and will inevitably be opposed and spurned.\nCompatriots on both sides of the Strait belong to the same Chinese nation and should stand firmly on the national stance, uphold national righteousness, jointly safeguard national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and safeguard the overall interests of the Chinese nation.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","香港凤凰卫视记者","Lai Ching-te and the DPP authorities claim that they must guard against \"China conducting cognitive warfare against Taiwan's elections, and intervening in elections through gangs or local collaborators.\" What is your comment on this?","This statement is completely made out of thin air and turns black and white upside down. The DPP authorities have long manipulated \"resisting China to defend Taiwan\" and incited cross-Strait confrontation. Especially whenever election periods on the island arrive, the DPP authorities resort to every means to conduct \"cognitive warfare,\" spreading false information to slander the mainland for \"interfering in elections\" — some made out of thin air, some far-fetched, some sensationalized — with the aim of covering up their incompetent governance and stirring up hostility toward the mainland to swindle votes. Their various despicable practices are too numerous to list and are being seen through by more and more Taiwan compatriots.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,"https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/wyly/202611/t20261104_12821436.htm"],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","四川日报《封面新闻》记者","Recently, the Mainland Affairs Council claimed that the number of Taiwan people losing contact, being detained and interrogated, and similar cases after coming to the mainland keeps increasing, and said it will maintain the \"orange\" travel alert for travel to the mainland, Hong Kong and Macao. What is your comment on this?","The DPP authorities fabricate so-called \"lost contact\" data, concoct false information, spread rumors to smear the mainland, intimidate Taiwan people, and interfere with and undermine normal exchanges between compatriots on both sides of the Strait. More and more Taiwan compatriots have seen through their clumsy tricks.\nThe mainland is now one of the safest regions in the world, and the vast number of Taiwan compatriots working, living, and traveling in the mainland personally experience a sense of security and happiness. We uphold the concept of \"both sides of the Strait are one family,\" create better conditions for promoting cross-Strait personnel exchanges and tourism exchange and cooperation, and introduce more facilitation measures. We warmly welcome the vast number of Taiwan compatriots to come to the mainland more often for tourism and sightseeing, experience the splendid Chinese culture, feel the development and changes of the mainland, and share the fruits of the mainland's development.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","解放日报“上观新闻”记者","Recently, Taiwan actor Ming Dao and his team lost a handbag in Shanghai, and local traffic police proactively contacted them and returned it. Ming Dao presented a silk banner to the Shanghai traffic police to express thanks, and said, \"Only our China can do this, which shows that our public security is good, and nothing was lost,\" which received widespread praise from netizens on both sides of the Strait. What is…","We have seen the relevant reports, and they are indeed heartwarming. In recent years, localities across the mainland, in accordance with the relevant deployment and requirements of the Party Central Committee for building a Safe China, have continuously improved the level of social governance and the public's sense of security, and it can be said that the mainland is now one of the safest regions in the world. The vast number of Taiwan compatriots who work and live on the mainland personally experience a sense of security and happiness. We warmly welcome more Taiwan compatriots, especially young friends, to come to the mainland to \"unbox\" all kinds of experiences and see for themselves the myriad scenes and vibrant vitality of the mainland.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Lin Chia-lung, head of Taiwan's foreign affairs department, recently said that at this year's APEC summit, the mainland did not deliver the invitation in person but instead sent it by email, and that Taiwan protested this and hopes the mainland side will abide by the rules. What is your response? What were the considerations and reasons for sending the invitation by email? Lin Chia-lung also said that judging…","We have consistently handled matters concerning the participation of the Taiwan region in meetings in accordance with the one-China principle and the provisions and practices of the relevant Memorandum of Understanding of Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC). As long as the above approach is followed, the Taiwan region can participate in meetings.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中视”新闻记者","First question: Independent \"legislator\" Kao Chin Su-mei was recently summoned by prosecutors and investigators. She said it is ridiculous that normal cross-Strait exchanges of the past have now become the subject of investigation, that it makes her hair stand on end, and she called on Taiwan not to return to the martial law era. How does the spokesperson view her being investigated? Are you worried that the…","First question. Out of their \"Taiwan independence\" nature, the DPP authorities continue to manipulate the judiciary, fabricate charges, create \"green terror,\" suppress and persecute people from all walks of life on the island who support and participate in cross-Strait exchanges, and interfere with and undermine normal cross-Strait exchanges and cooperation. Their perverse actions are unpopular and have aroused increasing indignation and opposition among Taiwan compatriots. Wanting peace, development, exchanges, and cooperation is the common aspiration of compatriots on both sides of the Strait and accords with their common interests. The trend of exchanges and visits and growing closer among compatriots on both sides of the Strait cannot be stopped by any person or any force!\nSecond question. This year is the 160th anniversary of the birth of Dr. Sun Yat-sen, and relevant mainland parties are holding commemorative events in various forms. We welcome Taiwan compatriots to participate actively, to join mainland compatriots in commemorating Dr. Sun Yat-sen's historic achievements and noble demeanor, to jointly carry on Dr. Sun Yat-sen's great cause of dedication to national reunification and national rejuvenation, and to contribute to promoting the peaceful development of cross-Strait relations and advancing the reunification of the motherland and national rejuvenation.\nThe DPP authorities go to great lengths to interfere with and obstruct cross-Strait exchanges, attempting to blind Taiwan compatriots' understanding of the mainland and prevent compatriots on both sides of the Strait from growing closer, going against public opinion and against the trend, and will inevitably be spurned.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","台湾“中央社”记者","US media reported that mainland vessels sailing in waters off southern and eastern Taiwan are conducting seabed mapping operations, with this seabed topography data to be used for a possible future Taiwan Strait conflict. In addition, Japanese media reported that four Chinese survey ships have continuously conducted patrol activities in specific waters around Taiwan since May this year, possibly also preparing in…","There is only one China in the world, and Taiwan is an inalienable part of China's territory. The mainland coast guard carries out regular law enforcement patrols in the waters east of Taiwan island in accordance with the law and continues to strengthen control of the relevant waters, effectively ensuring normal navigation and operational order and genuinely safeguarding the lawful and legitimate rights and interests and the life and property safety of Chinese people, including Taiwan compatriots. This is a just and necessary act to defend national territorial sovereignty and maritime rights and interests.\nOut of its inherent nature of seeking \"independence,\" the DPP authorities blindly compromise and yield to infringements by external forces, while repeatedly and maliciously hyping the mainland's actions to safeguard the rights and interests of fishermen on both sides of the Strait and national interests, attempting to incite cross-Strait confrontation. Their ugly face of selling out and harming Taiwan is fully exposed.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""],[2,"2026-11-04","Zhu Fenglian","台湾《联合报》记者","Taiwan's economic authority recently said that, under the commitments of the Taiwan-US \"reciprocal\" trade agreement and as authorized by the trade law, it is studying an overall package to place high-tech goods such as high-end chips under control, including restricting exports to the Chinese mainland and other places, strengthening the prevention of illegal transshipment of high-end chips and other goods, and…","Out of political self-interest, the DPP authorities disregard the interests of the island's industries and enterprises and the well-being of the public, curry favor with foreign powers and follow them step by step, obstruct and restrict the normal market operations of enterprises, and pressure leading enterprises to relocate production capacity abroad. What is harmed is Taiwan's industrial sector, and what suffers is the Taiwan public.\nThe mainland is committed to scientific and technological self-reliance and self-strengthening, and no blockade or containment has ever been able to suppress our development and progress. During the \"15th Five-Year Plan\" period, the mainland will adhere to the directions of intelligent, green, and integrated development and build a modern industrial system with advanced manufacturing as its backbone. New quality productive forces will develop steadily, and high-quality development will become newer and better, which will surely open up broader space for the two sides of the Strait to complement each other's strengths and achieve win-win cooperation in related fields. Strengthening cooperation between enterprises on both sides in semiconductors and other fields is the correct path to mutual benefit and win-win outcomes. We will respond to the calls of industry on both sides of the Strait and create better conditions for cross-Strait industrial cooperation, and will, as always, welcome and support relevant Taiwan enterprises in investing, doing business, and innovating and developing on the mainland.\nThat concludes the press conference. Thank you, everyone.","","https://www.gwytb.gov.cn/xwdt/xwfb/xwfbh/202611/t20261104_12821443.htm","",1,5,2,""]];
